अ|अं|अः
अ The first letter of the alphabet; अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि Bg. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अः|अ|अं
अ + .{@अः@} [अवति, अतति सातत्येन तिष्ठतीति वा; अव्-अत्- वा, ड Tv.]<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu, the first of the three sounds constituting the sacred<BR> syllable ओम्; अकारो विष्णुरुद्दिष्ट उकारस्तु महेश्वरः । मकारस्तु स्मृतो<BR> ब्रह्मा प्रणवस्तु त्रयात्मकः ॥ For more explanations of the three<BR> syllables अ, उ, म् see ओम्.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva, Brahmā, Vāyu, or Vaiśvānara. −[अः कृष्णः शंकरो<BR> ब्रह्मा शक्रः सोमोऽनिलोऽनलः । सूर्यः प्राणो यमः कालो वसन्तः प्रणवः<BR> सुखी ॥ Enm. अः स्याद् ब्रह्मणि विष्ण्वीशकूर्माणङ्करणेषु च । गौरवेऽन्तःपुरे<BR> हेतौ भूषणेऽङ्घ्रावुमेज्ययोः ॥ Nm. अः शिखायां सिद्धमन्त्रे प्रग्राहेऽर्के<BR> रथार्वणि । चक्रे कुक्कुटमूर्ध्नीन्दुबिम्बे ब्रह्मेशविष्णुषु ॥ ibid. Thus<BR> अः means Kṛṣṇa, Śiva, Brahmā, Indra, Soma, Vāyu, Agni, the<BR> Sun, the life-breath, Yama, Kāla, Vasanta, Praṇava, a happy man, a tortoise,<BR> a courtyard, a battle, greatness, a female apartment in a palace, an object<BR> or a cause, an ornament, a foot, Umā, sacrifice, a flame, a particularly<BR> efficacious mantra, reins, the horse of a chariot, a wheel, the head of<BR> a cock, the disc of the moon];<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A prefix corresponding to Latin <i>in</i>, Eng. <i>in</i> or <i>un</i>, Gr.<BR> <i>a</i> or <i>an</i>, and joined to nouns, adjectives, indeclinables (or rarely<BR> even to verbs) as a substitute for the negative particle नञ्, and<BR> changed to अन् before vowels (except in the word अ-ऋणिन्). The<BR> senses of न usually enumerated are six:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) सादृश्य ‘likeness’ or ‘resemblance’; अब्राह्मणः one like<BR> a Brāhmaṇa (wearing the sacred thread &c.), but not a Brāhmaṇa; a<BR> Kṣatriya, or a Vaiśya; अनिक्षुः a reed appearing like इक्षु, but<BR> not a true इक्षु.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) अभाव ‘absence’, ‘negation’, ‘want’, ‘privation’; अज्ञानम्<BR> absence of knowledge, ignorance; अक्रोधः, अनङ्गः, अकण्टकः, अघटः &c.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) अन्यत्व ‘difference’ or ‘distinction’; अपटः not a cloth,<BR> something different from, or other than, a cloth.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) अल्पता ‘smallness’, ‘diminution’, used as a diminutive particle;<BR> अनुदरा having a slender waist (कृशोदरी or तनुमध्यमा).<BR>——(<i>e</i>) अप्राशस्त्य ‘badness’, ‘unfitness’, having a depreciative<BR> sense; अकालः wrong or improper time; अकार्यम् not fit to be done,<BR> improper, unworthy, bad act.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) विरोध ‘opposition’, ‘contrariety’; अनीतिः the opposite<BR> of morality, immorality; असित not white, black; असुर not a god,<BR> a demon &c. These senses are put together in the following verse:− तत्सादृश्यमभावश्च<BR> तदन्यत्वं तदल्पता । अप्राशस्त्यं विरोधश्च नञर्थाः षट् प्रकीर्तिताः ॥<BR> See न also. With verbal derivatives, such as gerunds, infinitives,<BR> participles, it has usually the sense of ‘not’; अदग्ध्वा not having<BR> burnt; अपश्यन् not seeing; so असकृत् not once; अमृषा, अकस्मात्<BR> &c. Sometimes in बहुव्रीहि अ does not affect the sense of the second<BR> member; अ-पश्चिम that which has no last, <i>i. e.</i> best, topmost;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> विपश्चितामपश्चिमः cf. also R. 19. 1. अनुत्तम having<BR> no superior, unsurpassed, most excellent: (for examples see these words).<BR>—2 An interjection of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Pity (ah!) अ अवद्यं P. I. 1. 14. Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Reproach, censure (fie, shame); अपचसि त्वं जाल्म P. VI. 3. 73. Vārt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">Page0001-2</a>]<BR> See अकरणि, अजीवनि also.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Used in addressing; अ अनन्त.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) It is also used as a particle of prohibition.<BR>—3 The augment prefixed to the root in the formation of the Imperfect,<BR> Aorist and Conditional Tenses. <i>N. B.</i>:− The application of this privative<BR> prefix is practically unlimited; to give every possible case would almost<BR> amount to a dictionary itself. No attempt will, therefore, be made to<BR> give <i>every possible</i> combination of this prefix with a following word;<BR> only such words as require a special explanation, or such as most frequently<BR> occur in literature and enter into compounds with other words, will be<BR> given; others will be found self-explaining when the English ‘in’, ‘un’,<BR> or ‘not’, is substituted for अ or अन् before the meaning of the<BR> second word, or the sense may be expressed by ‘less’, ‘free from’, ‘devoid or destitute of’<BR> &c.; अकथ्य unspeakable; अदर्प without pride,<BR> or freedom from pride; अप्रगल्भ not bold; अभग unfortunate;<BR> अवित्त destitute of wealth &c. In many cases such compounds will be<BR> found explained under the second member. Most compounds beginning with<BR> अ or अन् are either Tatpuruṣa or Bahuvrīhi (to be determined<BR> by the sense) and should be so dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अऋणिन्
अऋणिन् <i>a.</i> (epic.) (ऋ being here regarded as a consonant) Not<BR> a debtor, free from debt; दिवसस्याष्टमे भागे शाकं पचति यो नरः ।<BR> अऋणी चाप्रवासी च स वारिचर मोदते ॥ Mb. The normal form अनृणिन्<BR> also occurs in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्
अंश् €10 U. अंशयति-ते also अंशापयति To divide, distribute, share among.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशः|अंश
अंशः [अंश्-अच्]<BR>—1 A share, part, portion, division; member; सकृदंशो निपतति Ms. 9. 47;<BR> तुर्यांशः a fourth part; षष्ठ˚; ममैवांशो जीवलोके जीवभूतः<BR> सनातनः Bg. 15. 7; भुवमंशाविव धर्मयोर्गतौ R. 8. 16; अंशेन<BR> दर्शितानुकूलता K. 159 partly.<BR>—2 A share in property, inheritance; स्वतोंऽशतः Ms. 8. 408; अनंशौ<BR> क्लीबपतितौ 9. 201; पत्न्यः कार्याः समांशिकाः Y. 2. 115.<BR>—3 the numerator of a fraction; अन्योन्यहाराभिहतौ हरांशौ Līlā.;<BR> sometimes used for fraction itself.<BR>—4 A degree of latitude (or longitude); अक्षस्यांशाः समाख्याताः षष्ट्युत्तरशतत्रयम्;<BR> स च अंशः षष्टिकलात्मकः, कला तु षष्टिविकलात्मिका.<BR>—5 The shoulder (more correctly written as अंस, q. v.).<BR>—6 N. of one of the Ādityas; Mb. 1. 227. 25; cf. also the beginning of<BR> T. Ār. The senses of ‘party’, ‘a share of booty’, ‘earnest money’, which<BR> are said to occur in the Veda are traceable to 1 above.<BR>—7 The vital note in a Rāga.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अंशांशः, अंशांशि, अंशावतारः, अंशावतरणम्, अंशकुण्डली, अंशभाज्, अंशहर, अंशहारिन्, अंशविवर्तिन्, अंशसवर्णनम्, अंशस्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांशः|अंशांश
अंशः + -अंशः [ष˚ त˚] a secondary incarnation; part of a portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांशि
अंशः + -अंशि <i>adv.</i> share by share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशावतारः|अंशावतार
अंशः + -अवतारः, -अवतरणम् [ष˚ त˚] descent (on earth) of parts<BR> of deities, partial incarnation; ˚तार इव धर्मस्य Dk. 153; ˚रमिव<BR> कृतान्तस्य K. 31; ˚उच्चैःश्रवसः 79; so अंशावतीर्णमिव 108;<BR> N. of a sub-parvan covering Adhyāyas 64-67 of Ādiparvan of Mb. Even<BR> without the compound<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">Page0002-1</a>]<BR> अंश means partial incarnation. अंश, आवेश, and अवतार are<BR> the three kinds of Lordʼs manifestations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशावतरणम्
अंशः + -अवतारः, -अवतरणम् [ष˚ त˚] descent (on earth) of parts<BR> of deities, partial incarnation; ˚तार इव धर्मस्य Dk. 153; ˚रमिव<BR> कृतान्तस्य K. 31; ˚उच्चैःश्रवसः 79; so अंशावतीर्णमिव 108;<BR> N. of a sub-parvan covering Adhyāyas 64-67 of Ādiparvan of Mb. Even<BR> without the compound<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">Page0002-1</a>]<BR> अंश means partial incarnation. अंश, आवेश, and अवतार are<BR> the three kinds of Lordʼs manifestations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशकुण्डली
अंशः + -कुण्डली (= नवांशकुण्डली) the horoscope prepared by taking<BR> into consideration the nine zodiacal divisions. (¹⁄₁₀₈th of a राशि =<BR> नवांश or नवमांश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशभाज्
अंशः + -भाज्, -हर, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> [उप˚ समास] one who takes<BR> or has a share, one entitled to a share in the ancestral property, an<BR> heir, a co-heir; पिण्डदोंऽशहरश्चैषां पूर्वाभावे परः परः Y. 2. 132;<BR> जातोऽपि दास्यां शूद्रेण कामतोंऽशहरो भवेत् 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहर
अंशः + -भाज्, -हर, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> [उप˚ समास] one who takes<BR> or has a share, one entitled to a share in the ancestral property, an<BR> heir, a co-heir; पिण्डदोंऽशहरश्चैषां पूर्वाभावे परः परः Y. 2. 132;<BR> जातोऽपि दास्यां शूद्रेण कामतोंऽशहरो भवेत् 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहारिन्
अंशः + -भाज्, -हर, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> [उप˚ समास] one who takes<BR> or has a share, one entitled to a share in the ancestral property, an<BR> heir, a co-heir; पिण्डदोंऽशहरश्चैषां पूर्वाभावे परः परः Y. 2. 132;<BR> जातोऽपि दास्यां शूद्रेण कामतोंऽशहरो भवेत् 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशविवर्तिन्
अंशः + -विवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> [स˚ त˚] slightly turned away, or turned<BR> away towards the shoulder; मुखसंशविवर्ति पक्ष्मलाक्ष्याः Ś. 3. 24.<BR> v. l. for अंसविवर्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशसवर्णनम्
अंशः + -सवर्णनम् [ष˚ त˚] reduction of fractions to the same<BR> denominator (अतुल्यच्छेदयो राश्योः समच्छेदकरणम्) अन्योन्यहाराभिहतौ<BR> हरांशौ राश्योः समच्छेदविधानमेवम् Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशस्वरः|अंशस्वर
अंशः + -स्वरः the keynote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशकः|अंशक|अंशकं
अंशकः [अंश्-ण्वुल्; अंशिका <i>f.</i>]<BR>—1 One having a share, a co-parcener, relative.<BR>—2 (स्वार्थे कन्) A share, portion, division; त्रिंशांशकस्तथा राशेर्भाग<BR> इत्यभिधीयते; द्विभर्तृका मेषनवांशके स्यात्, वृषांशके सा पशुशीलयुक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशकम्
अंशकः + .{@-कम्@} A solar day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितव्य
अंशयितव्य [अंश्-तव्यच्] <i>a.</i> Fit to be divided into parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशल|अंशलः
अंशल <i>a.</i> [अंशं लाति, ला-क]<BR>—1 Having, or entitled to a share (अंशग्राहक).<BR>—2 अंसल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशनम्
अंशनम् [अंश्-ल्युट्] Act of dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितृ
अंशयितृ <i>m.</i> (अंश्-तृच्) A divider, sharer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशिन्
अंशिन् <i>m.</i> [अंश-इनि]<BR>—1 A sharer, co-parcener; (पुनर्विभागकरणे) सर्वे वा स्युः समांशिनः<BR> Y. 2. 114 (entitled to the same share.)<BR>—2 Having parts or members (अवयविन्); अंशिनः स्वांशगात्यन्ताभावं<BR> प्रति मृषात्मतां -Ved. Paribhāṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्य
अंश्य <i>a.</i> [अंश्-कर्मणि यत्] Divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुः|अंशु
अंशुः [अंश्-मृग˚ कु.]<BR>—1 A ray, beam of light; चण्ड˚, घर्म˚ hot-rayed, the sun; सूर्याशुभिर्भिन्नमिवाराविन्दम्<BR> Ku. 1. 32; lustre, brilliance चण्डांशुकिरणाभाश्च हाराः Rām. 5. 9. 48;<BR> Śi. 1. 9. रत्न˚, नख˚ &c.<BR>—2 A point or end.<BR>—3 A small or minute particle.<BR>—4 End of a thread.<BR>—5 A filament, especially of the Soma plant (Ved.)<BR>—6 Garment; decoration.<BR>—7 N. of a sage or of a prince.<BR>—8 Speed, velocity (वेग).<BR>—9 Fine thread<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अंशूदकम्, अंशुजालम्, अंशुधरः, अंशुपतिः, अंशुभृत्, अंशुबाणः, अंशुभर्तृ, अंशुस्वामिन्, अंशुपट्टम्, अंशुमाला, अंशुमालिन्, अंशुहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशूदकम्
अंशुः + -उदकम् dew-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुजालम्
अंशुः + -जालम् a collection of rays, a blaze or halo of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुधरः|अंशुधर
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुपतिः|अंशुपति
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुभृत्
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुबाणः|अंशुबाण
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुभर्तृ|अंशुभर्त्तृ
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुस्वामिन्
अंशुः + -धरः, -पतिः, -भृत्, -बाणः, -भर्तृ, -स्वामिन् the sun, (bearer or lord of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुपट्टम्
अंशुः + -पट्टम् a kind of silken cloth (अंशुना सूक्ष्मसूत्रेणयुक्तं पट्टम्);<BR> सश्रीफलैरंशुपट्टम् Y. 1. 186; श्रीफलैरंशुपट्टानां Ms. 5. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमाला
अंशुः + -माला a garland of light, halo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमालिन्
अंशुः + -मालिन् <i>m.</i> [अंशवो मालेव, ततः अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 the sun (wreathed with, surrounded by, rays).<BR>—2 the number twelve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुहस्तः|अंशुहस्त
अंशुः + -हस्तः [अंशुः हस्त इव यस्य] the sun (who draws up water<BR> from the earth by means of his 1000 hands in the form of rays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्|अंशुमन्त्
अंशुमत् <i>a.</i> [अंशु-अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्]<BR>—1 Luminous, radiant; ज्योतिषां रविरंशुमान् Bg. 10. 21.<BR>—2 Pointed.<BR>—3 Fibrous, abounding in filaments (Ved.) <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमान्
अंशुमत् + (˚मान्)<BR>—1 The sun; वालखिल्यैरिवांशुमान् R. 15. 10; अंशुमानिव तन्वभ्रपटलच्छन्नविग्रहः<BR> Ki. 11. 6; जलाधारोष्विवांशुमान् Y. 3. 144; rarely the moon also; ततः<BR> स मध्यंगतमंशुमन्तं Rām. 5. 5. 1.<BR>—2 N. of the grandson of Sagara, son of Asamañjasa and father of Dilīpa.<BR>—3 N. of a mountain;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्फला
अंशुमत् + ˚मत्फला N. of a plant, कदली Musa sapientum<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">Page0002-2</a>]<BR> or Paradisiaca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमती
अंशुमत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 N. of a plant सालपणीं (Mar. डवला, सालवण) Desmodium Gangeticum.<BR>—2 N. of the river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुकम्
अंशुकम् [अंशवः सूत्राणि विषयो यस्य; अंशु ऋश्यादि˚ क]<BR>—1 A cloth, garment in general; सितांशुका मङ्गलमात्रभूषणा V. 3. 12;<BR> यत्रांशुकाक्षेपविलज्जितानां Ku. 1. 14; चीनांशुकमिव केतोः<BR> Ś. 1. 33; स्तन˚ a breast-cloth.<BR>—2 A fine or white cloth; धुन्वन् कल्पद्रुमकिसलयान्यंशुकानीव वातैः<BR> Me. 64; usually silken or muslin.<BR>—3 An upper garment; a mantle.<BR>—4 An under garment; कररुद्धनीविगलदंशुकाः स्त्रियः Śi. 13. 31.<BR>—5 A leaf.<BR>—6 Mild or gentle blaze of light (नातिदीप्ति) (कः also; स्वार्थे कन्.)<BR>—7 The string of a churning stick. cf. अंशुकं नेत्रवस्त्रयोः । cf.<BR> also अंशुकं सूक्ष्मवस्त्रे स्यात् परिधानोत्तरीययोः । किरणानां समूहे<BR> च मुखवस्त्रे तदिष्यते ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुल|अंशुलः
अंशुल <i>a.</i> Radiant, luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुलः|अंशुल
अंशुल + .{@-लः@} [अंशुं प्रभां बुद्धिप्रतिभां लाति, or अंशुरस्य अस्तीति<BR> ला-क] N. of Cāṇakya; of any sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस्
अंस् अंसयति अंसापयति. See अंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसः|अंस
अंसः [अंस् कर्मभावादौ अच्]<BR>—1 A part, portion; see अंशः.<BR>—2 The shoulder, shoulder-blade; यदयं रथसंक्षोभादंसेनांसो रथोपमश्रोण्याः V. 1. 13.<BR>—3 N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसौ
अंसः + .({@-सौ@}) The two angles of an altar [cf. Goth. <i>amsa</i>; L. <i>ansa</i>,<BR> <i>humerus</i>; Gr. <i>omor</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अंसकूटः, अंसत्रम्, अंसफलकः, अंसभारः, अंसभारिक, अंसविवर्तिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसकूटः|अंसकूट
अंसः + -कूटः [अंसः कूट इव वृहत्त्वात्] a bullʼs hump, the protuberance<BR> between the shoulders; राजन्योच्चांसकूटक्रथनपटुरटद्घोरधारः कुठारः Prab. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसत्रम्
अंसः + -त्रम् [उप˚ स˚]<BR>—1 an armour to protect the shoulders.<BR>—2 a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसफलकः|अंसफलक
अंसः + -फलकः the upper part of the spine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसभारः|अंसभार
अंसः + -भारः (अंसे˚) [अंसे धृतो भारः शाक˚ त˚ वा अलुक्]<BR> a burden or yoke put upon the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसभारिक
अंसः + -भारिक, -भारिन् <i>a.</i> (अंसे˚) [भस्त्रादिगण, अंस(से)भारेण<BR> हरति; ष्ठन्] bearing a yoke or burden on the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसविवर्तिन्
अंसः + -विवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> [उप˚ स˚] turned towards the shoulders;<BR> मुखमंसविवर्ति पक्ष्मलाक्ष्याः Ś. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसल|अंसलः
अंसल <i>a.</i> [अंस लच्, बलवति इत्यर्थे; P. V. 2. 98] Strong,<BR> lusty, powerful, having strong shoulders; युवा युगव्यायतबाहुरंसलः<BR> R. 3. 34; भुजेन रक्षापरिघेण भूमेरुपैतु योगं पुनरंसलेन 16. 84;<BR> ˚पुरुषप्रयत्नदुश्चलं Dk. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस्य
अंस्य <i>a.</i> [अंसे भवः अंस-यत्.] Belonging to the shoulder;<BR> ये अंस्या ये अङ्ग्याः सूचीकाः Rv. 1. 191. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्
अंह् €1 Ā. अंहते, अंहितुं To go; approach; set out; Bk. 3. 25, 46,<BR> आनंहे चान्तिकं पितुः 14. 51, 4. 4 &c. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To send; तमाञ्जिहन्मैथिलयज्ञभूमिं Bk. 2. 40, 15. 75.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR>—3 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहुर
अंहुर <i>a.</i> [अंह्-मद्गुरादि उरच्] Moving (गतियुक्त); तासामेकामिदभ्यंहुरो<BR> गात् Rv. 10. 5. 6; distressed, straitened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहूरण
अंहूरण <i>a.</i> (Ved.) distressing, troublesome; sinful; straitened; Rv. 6. 47. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहूरणम्
अंहूरण + .{@-णम्@} A sin, distress; Rv. 1. 105. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहोयु
अंहोयु <i>a.</i> Troublesome, threatening; Rv. 5. 15 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहतिः|अंहति
अंहतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [हन्-अति, अंहादेशश्च; हन्तेरतिः स्यादंहादेशश्च<BR> धातोः Uṇ. 4. 62; हन्ति दुरितमनया इति दानम्]<BR>—1 A gift.<BR>—2 Anxiety, trouble, care, distress, illness (Ved.); Rv. 1. 94. 2, 8. 75. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहती
अंहतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [हन्-अति, अंहादेशश्च; हन्तेरतिः स्यादंहादेशश्च<BR> धातोः Uṇ. 4. 62; हन्ति दुरितमनया इति दानम्]<BR>—1 A gift.<BR>—2 Anxiety, trouble, care, distress, illness (Ved.); Rv. 1. 94. 2, 8. 75. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहस्
अंहस् <i>n.</i> अंहः, ˚हसी &c. [अम् असुन् हुक् च Uṇ. 4. 212,<BR> अमति गच्छति प्रायाश्चित्तेन]<BR>—1 A sin; सहसा संहतिमंहसां विहन्तुम् … अलं Ki. 5. 17; कृतः<BR> कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29; leaving oneʼs religion or duty<BR> (स्वधर्मत्याग); लोभोऽनृतं चौर्यमनार्यमंहः Bhāg. 1. 17. 32.<BR>—2 Trouble, anxiety, care; युयोतन नो अंहसः Rv. 8. 18. 10 [<i>cf.</i><BR> अघ, आगस्; Gr. <i>akhos</i>.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहः|अंह
अंहस् <i>n.</i> अंहः, ˚हसी &c. [अम् असुन् हुक् च Uṇ. 4. 212,<BR> अमति गच्छति प्रायाश्चित्तेन]<BR>—1 A sin; सहसा संहतिमंहसां विहन्तुम् … अलं Ki. 5. 17; कृतः<BR> कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29; leaving oneʼs religion or duty<BR> (स्वधर्मत्याग); लोभोऽनृतं चौर्यमनार्यमंहः Bhāg. 1. 17. 32.<BR>—2 Trouble, anxiety, care; युयोतन नो अंहसः Rv. 8. 18. 10 [<i>cf.</i><BR> अघ, आगस्; Gr. <i>akhos</i>.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहसी
अंहस् <i>n.</i> अंहः, ˚हसी &c. [अम् असुन् हुक् च Uṇ. 4. 212,<BR> अमति गच्छति प्रायाश्चित्तेन]<BR>—1 A sin; सहसा संहतिमंहसां विहन्तुम् … अलं Ki. 5. 17; कृतः<BR> कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29; leaving oneʼs religion or duty<BR> (स्वधर्मत्याग); लोभोऽनृतं चौर्यमनार्यमंहः Bhāg. 1. 17. 32.<BR>—2 Trouble, anxiety, care; युयोतन नो अंहसः Rv. 8. 18. 10 [<i>cf.</i><BR> अघ, आगस्; Gr. <i>akhos</i>.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहोमुच्
अंहस् + ˚मुच् <i>a.</i> freeing from distress;<BR> अंहोमुचे प्रभरे Yv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहसस्पतिः|अंहसस्पति
अंहसस्पतिः (Ved.) The intercalary month (Lord of distress or perplexity ?). Vāj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहस्वत्
अंहस्वत् <i>a.</i> Sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहितिः|अंहिति
अंहितिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [अंह् क्तिन् ग्रहादित्वात् इट् Tv.] A gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहिती
अंहितिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [अंह् क्तिन् ग्रहादित्वात् इट् Tv.] A gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहु
अंहु <i>a.</i> [अंह् मृग˚ कु] (Ved.) Sinful, wicked, injurious (पापकारिन्,<BR> हननशील); strait, narrow (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहु
अंहु + .{@-हु@} <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Anxiety, distress; sin, crime (?).<BR>—2 Pudendum Muliebre (?). [cf. L. <i>angustus, anxius</i>, Goth. <i>aggvus</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहुभेद
अंहु + .{@-भेद, -दी@} having a narrow slit; having the pudendum divided (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहुभेदी
अंहु + .{@-भेद, -दी@} having a narrow slit; having the pudendum divided (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिः|अंह्रि
अंह्रिः [अंह् वंक्रपादि क्रिन्, अंहते गच्छत्यनेन]<BR>—1 A foot.<BR>—2 The root of a tree, cf. अङ्घ्रि.<BR>—3 The number four.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अंह्रिपः, अंह्रिस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिपः|अंह्रिप
अंह्रिः + -पः ‘foot-drinker’, a tree (मूलेन पिबति सिक्ततोयम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिस्कन्धः|अंह्रिस्कन्ध|अंह्रिस्कंध
अंह्रिः + -स्कन्धः [अंह्रेः स्कन्ध इव] the upper part of the sole of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्
अक् €1 P. (अकति) To go, move tortuously like a serpent [cf. L.<BR> <i>angulus</i>, Gr. <i>agkai</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक <i>a.</i> Moving tortuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्
अकम् [न कं सुखम्] Absence of happiness; pain, misery (as in<BR> नाकं, न अकं दुःखं यत्र), sin नास्ति कं सुखं यस्मात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकच|अकचः
अकच <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Bald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकचः|अकच
अकच + .{@-चः@} N. of Ketu (the descending node), who is represented as a<BR> headless trunk. Tv. explains it thus: अकाय दुःखाय चायते; चाय्-ड;<BR> केतुग्रहस्य उदयेन लोकोपप्लवस्य शास्त्रप्रसिद्धिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकडमम्
अकडमम्, अकथहम्, ˚चक्रम् N. of a mystical circle (चक्र)<BR> or diagram with the letters of the alphabet, such as अ, क, ड, म;<BR> अ, क, थ, ह &c. written therein and used in determining the auspicious<BR> or inauspicious stars of a person; (ग्राह्यगोपालमन्त्रस्य तन्त्रोक्तमन्त्रग्रहणार्थं<BR> तत्तन्मन्त्राणां शुभाशुभविचारोपयोगी चक्रभेदः Tv.) (Mar. अवकहडाचक्र<BR> given in पञ्चाङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथहम्
अकडमम्, अकथहम्, ˚चक्रम् N. of a mystical circle (चक्र)<BR> or diagram with the letters of the alphabet, such as अ, क, ड, म;<BR> अ, क, थ, ह &c. written therein and used in determining the auspicious<BR> or inauspicious stars of a person; (ग्राह्यगोपालमन्त्रस्य तन्त्रोक्तमन्त्रग्रहणार्थं<BR> तत्तन्मन्त्राणां शुभाशुभविचारोपयोगी चक्रभेदः Tv.) (Mar. अवकहडाचक्र<BR> given in पञ्चाङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकडमचक्रम्
अकडमम्, अकथहम्, ˚चक्रम् N. of a mystical circle (चक्र)<BR> or diagram with the letters of the alphabet, such as अ, क, ड, म;<BR> अ, क, थ, ह &c. written therein and used in determining the auspicious<BR> or inauspicious stars of a person; (ग्राह्यगोपालमन्त्रस्य तन्त्रोक्तमन्त्रग्रहणार्थं<BR> तत्तन्मन्त्राणां शुभाशुभविचारोपयोगी चक्रभेदः Tv.) (Mar. अवकहडाचक्र<BR> given in पञ्चाङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथनीय
अकथनीय <i>a.</i> Not fit to be mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथित
अकथित <i>a.</i> ‘Not told’, not otherwise mentioned by way of any<BR> of the other case-relations, such as अपादान &c.; a name given to the<BR> indirect (गौण) object governed by verbs like दुह्, याच् &c. cf.<BR> अनभिहितम् अकथितं कर्म and ‘अकथितं च’ P. I. 4. 51. In the<BR> sentence ‘गां पयः दोग्धि’ गाम् is the indirect (गौण) object,<BR> and it could have taken the ablative ending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथ्य|अकथ्यः
अकथ्य <i>a.</i> Not fit to be mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठ|अकनिष्ठः
अकनिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Not the youngest (such as eldest, middle); elder, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठः|अकनिष्ठ
अकनिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@} N. of Buddha Gautama; of a deified Buddhist saint (pl. in<BR> this latter sense.) cf. बहूनि शतसहस्राणि यावदकनिष्ठानां संनिपतितान्यभूवन् । Lv.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकनिष्ठपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठपः|अकनिष्ठप
अकनिष्ठ + -पः + ({@-गः@} also) [अकनिष्ठान् बुद्धान् पातीति; पा-क.]<BR> N. of Buddha, lord of Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठगः|अकनिष्ठग
अकनिष्ठ + -पः + ({@-गः@} also) [अकनिष्ठान् बुद्धान् पातीति; पा-क.]<BR> N. of Buddha, lord of Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकन्या
अकन्या [न˚ त˚] No virgin, a maid who is not so any longer;<BR> अकन्येति तु यः कन्यां ब्रूयाद् द्वेषेण मानवः Ms. 8. 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पन|अकम्पनः
अकम्पन <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पनः|अकम्पन
अकम्पन + .{@-नः@} N. of a Rāksasa; Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पित|अकंपित|अकम्पितः
अकम्पित <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Unshaken, firm, resolute; not tremulous;<BR> असंदिग्धान् स्वरान् ब्रूयादविकृष्टानकम्पितान् । Rv. Pr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पितः|अकम्पित|अकंपित
अकम्पित + .{@-तः@} N. of a Jaina, or Buddhist saint, a pupil of the last Tīrthaṅkara<BR> (कम्पितं बुद्धिवृत्तेश्चालनं तन्नास्ति यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर
अकर <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Handless, maimed.<BR>—2 Exempt from tax or duty.<BR>—3 [न˚ त˚] Not doing or acting; not disposed to work, ceasing from work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरा
अकर + .{@-रा@} N. of a plant आमलकी, Emblic Myrobalan, Phyllanthus Emblica<BR> (Mar. आंवळा) (अकं दुःखं सेवनात् लोकानां राति गृह्णाति नाशयतीति; रा-क Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणम्
अकरणम् [कृ-भावे ल्युट्, न˚ त˚] Not doing, absence of action;<BR> अकरणान्मन्दकरणं श्रेयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरण|अकरणं
अकरणम् + .{@-ण@} <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not artificial, natural.<BR>—2 Devoid of all organs, (epithet of the Supreme Spirit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणिः|अकरणि
अकरणिः <i>f.</i> [नञ्-कृ-आक्रोशे अनिः; P. III. 3. 112.] Failure,<BR> disappointment, non-accomplishment, mostly used in imprecations; तस्याकरणिरेवास्तु<BR> Sk. may he be disappointed, or experience a failure! अकरणिर्ह ते वृषल<BR> Mbh. 6. 1. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण|अकर्णः|अकर्ण्ण
अकर्ण <i>a.</i> [न स्तः कर्णौ यस्य]<BR>—1 Devoid of ears; deaf.<BR>—2 Destitute of Karṇa: अनर्जुनमकर्णं वा जगदद्येति निश्चितः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्णः|अकर्ण|अकर्ण्ण
अकर्ण + .{@-र्णः@} A serpent (तस्य चक्षुषैव श्रवणात्, hence also called<BR> चक्षुःश्रवाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण्य
अकर्ण्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not fit for the ears; not in the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तः|अकर्त
अकर्तः [कृत्] Identity; absence of difference; सध्र्यङ् नियम्य<BR> यतयो यमर्तहेतिं Bhāg. 2. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तन|अकर्त्तन|अकर्त्तनः
अकर्तन <i>a.</i> [कृत्-भावे ल्युट्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not cutting.<BR>—2 Dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तृ|अकर्त्तृ
अकर्तृ <i>m.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not an agent; अकर्तरि च कारके<BR> P. III. 3. 19; actionless; चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः ।<BR> तस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्धपकर्तारमव्ययम् ॥ Bg. 4. 13. पुरुषोऽकर्ता<BR> भोक्ता Sāṅkhya; a subordinate agent;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकर्तृभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तृत्वम्
अकर्तृ + ˚त्वम्, -ता an inferior or subordinate position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तृता
अकर्तृ + ˚त्वम्, -ता an inferior or subordinate position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तृभावः|अकर्तृभाव
अकर्तृ + -भावः the state of non-agent; द्रष्टृत्वमकर्तृभावश्च ।<BR> Sāṅ. K. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मन्|अकर्म्मन्
अकर्मन् <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Without work, idle; inefficient.<BR>—2 Disqualified for performing the necessary rites, wicked, degraded;<BR> अकर्मा दस्युरभि नो Rv. 10. 22. 8.<BR>—3 (Gram.) intransitive, generally in this sense अकर्मक. ━<i>n.</i><BR> (र्म) [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Absence of work; absence of necessary observances; neglect of essential<BR> observances; inaction; अकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः Bg. 4. 17, 18.<BR>—2 An improper act; crime, sin.<BR>—3 Not doing (= अकरणम्), non-performance; प्रतिषेधादकर्म MS. 10. 8. 10.<BR>—4 What should not be done; अकर्म वा कृतदूषा स्यात् । MS. 12. 1. 10<BR> (where शबर explains अकर्म by न वा कर्तव्या दार्शिकी वेदिः ।).<BR>—5 Non-act, non-activity; अन्यद्धि कर्म भक्षणं प्रतिषिध्यमानम् अन्यद्<BR> अकर्म मानसः संकल्पः । ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 19.<BR>—6 Not doing, violation. तदकर्मणि च दोषः MS. 6. 3. 3(where तदकर्मणि<BR> is explained as प्रधानातिक्रमे by शबर); अकर्मणि चाप्रत्यवायात् ।<BR> MS. 6. 3. 10.<BR>—7 A wrong act, an improper act. अकर्म च दारक्रिया या आधानोत्तरकाले ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 14; अकर्म<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">Page0004-1</a>]<BR> चोर्ध्वमाधानात्˚ । MS. 6. 8. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकर्मान्वित, अकर्मकृत्, अकर्मभोगः, अकर्मशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मान्वित|अकर्म्मान्वितः
अकर्मन् + -अन्वित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 unengaged, unoccupied, idle.<BR>—2 criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मकृत्|अकर्म्मकृत्
अकर्मन् + -कृत् <i>a.</i> free from action; न हि कश्चित् क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत् ।<BR> Bg. 3. 5 doing an improper act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मभोगः|अकर्मभोग
अकर्मन् + -भोगः<BR>—1 enjoyment of freedom from the fruits of action.<BR>—2 renunciation of self-righteousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मशील
अकर्मन् + -शील <i>a.</i> lazy, indolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मक|अकर्म्मक
अकर्मक <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कर्म यस्य ब˚ कप्] Intransitive;<BR> फलव्यापारयोरेकनिष्ठतायामकर्मकः Bhartṛhari. {@अकर्मिका@}<BR> <i>f.</i> प्रसिद्धेरविवक्षातः कर्मणोऽकर्मिका क्रिया <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्यं
अकर्मण्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unable to work, inefficient, unfit for work.<BR>—2 Unfit to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल
अकल <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कला अवयवो यस्य] Not in parts, without<BR> parts, epithet of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकलङ्क|अकलङ्कः
अकलङ्क <i>a.</i> Without stains or spots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकलङ्कः|अकलङ्क
अकलङ्क + .{@-कः@} N. of a Jaina author, also called भट्ट अकलङ्कदेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्क
अकल्क <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कल्को यत्र]<BR>—1 Free from sediment, pure.<BR>—2 sinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्का
अकल्क + .{@-ल्का@} Moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कता
अकल्कता Honesty, integrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कन|अकल्कनः
अकल्कन, -क <i>a.</i><BR> [नास्ति कल्कनं दम्भः, कल्को वा यस्मिन्] Free from<BR> pride; humble, modest; honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कक
अकल्कन, -क <i>a.</i><BR> [नास्ति कल्कनं दम्भः, कल्को वा यस्मिन्] Free from<BR> pride; humble, modest; honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्प|अकल्पः
अकल्प <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Uncontrolled, not subject to control or rules, unrestrained, unfettered.<BR>—2 Weak, unable.<BR>—3 Incomparable.<BR>—4 Incapable, unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्पः|अकल्प
अकल्प + .{@-ल्पः@} A patient; Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्पनम्
अकल्पनम् Freedom from desires; absolution; बुद्धीन्द्रियमनःप्राणाञ्जनानामसृजत्प्रभुः ।<BR> मात्रार्थं च भवार्थं च आत्मनेऽकल्पनाय च ॥ Bhāg. 10. 87. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्पित|अकल्पितः
अकल्पित <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not artificial or manufactured;<BR> natural, genuine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्माष
अकल्माष<BR>—1 Name of the son of the fourth Manu; Hariv.<BR>—2 Without sin or stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्य|अकल्यः
अकल्य <i>a.</i> [कलासु साधुः कल्यः निरामयः, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unwell, ill, indisposed.<BR>—2 [कल्यते इतिं कल्-यत् कल्यं मिथ्याभूतम्; न˚ त˚] True; (तम्)<BR> अनीनयदकल्यसन्धो वन्धनागारं Dk. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्यशरीर
अकल्य + .{@-शरीर@} <i>a.</i> not in sound health; Pratimā 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्याण|अकल्याणं
अकल्याण <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Inauspicious, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्याणम्
अकल्याण + .{@-णम्@} Inauspiciousness, ill, evil, adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकव
अकव, -वा <i>a.</i> [न कव्यते वर्ण्यते कव्-आ, न˚ त˚] Indescribable<BR> (अवर्णनीय); not contemptible, not bad;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकवा
अकव, -वा <i>a.</i> [न कव्यते वर्ण्यते कव्-आ, न˚ त˚] Indescribable<BR> (अवर्णनीय); not contemptible, not bad;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकवारिः|अकवारि
अकव, -वा + ˚अरिः = कुत्सिता अरयो यस्य<BR> स कवारिः; न कवारिः अ˚; or यस्य शत्रवोऽप्यकुत्सिता वृत्रादयः;<BR> or अकुत्सितम् इयर्ति ऐश्वर्यं प्राप्नोति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकवि
अकवि <i>a.</i> (Ved.) Unwise, foolish; अयं कविरकविषु Rv. 7. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकस्मात्
अकस्मात् <i>ind.</i> [न कस्मात् किंचित्कारणाधीनत्वं यत्र, अलुक् स˚]<BR>—1 Accidentally, suddenly, unexpectedly, all of a sudden; अकस्मादागन्तुना<BR> सह विश्वासो न युक्तः H. 1; coming by chance, an accidental visitor.<BR>—2 Without cause or ground, causelessly, in vain; नाकस्माच्छाण्डिलीमाता<BR> विक्रीणाति तिलैस्तिलान् Pt. 2. 65; न ह्यकस्मात् प्रशंसा स्यात् । MS. 5. 3. 42;<BR> अकस्मादेव भर्तृद्वेष्यतां गतासि Dk. 135; नाकस्मादप्रियं<BR> वदेत् Y. 1. 132; अथ तु रिंपुरकस्माद् द्वेष्टि नः पुत्रभाण्डे Mv. 2. 44;<BR> कथं त्वां त्यजेदकस्मात्पतिरार्यवृत्तः R. 14. 55, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्ड|अकांड
अकाण्ड <i>a.</i> [नास्ति काण्डम् अवसरः उचितकालः यस्य]<BR>—1 Accidental, untoward, unexpected, sudden; अकाण्डपाण्डरघनप्रस्पर्धि<BR> Mv. 5. 39 -(v. l. अकालपाण्डुर) out of season; पुनंरकाण्डविवर्तनदारुणः<BR> U. 4. 15; ˚प्रचण्डकलहयोः U. 6; पततु शिरस्यकाण्डयमदण्ड<BR> इवैष भुजः Māl. 5. 31; ˚भङ्गुरतां संसारसुखानां K. 172.<BR>—2 Destitute of stem or stock.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकाण्डजात, अकाण्डताण्डवम्, अकाण्डपातः, अकाण्डपातजात, अकाण्डशूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डजात
अकाण्ड + -जात <i>a.</i> suddenly born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डताण्डवम्
अकाण्ड + -ताण्डवम् irrelevant display of erudition, indignation etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डपातः|अकाण्डपात
अकाण्ड + -पातः unexpected occurrence; ˚उपनता कं न लक्ष्मीर्विमोहयेत् Ks. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डपातजात
अकाण्ड + -पातजात <i>a.</i> dying as soon as born; perishing soon after birth; H. 4. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डशूलम्
अकाण्ड + -शूलम् a sudden attack of colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डे|अकांडे
अकाण्डे <i>adv.</i> Unexpectedly, all of a sudden; दर्भाङ्कुरेण चरणः<BR> क्षत इत्यकाण्डे तन्वी स्थिता Ś. 2. 12; उन्मथ्य मन्थरविवेकमकाण्ड<BR> एव Māl. 1. 18; तातस्तु तमकाण्ड एव प्राणहरमप्रतीकारमुपप्लवमुपनतमालोक्य K. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाम
अकाम <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कामो यस्य]<BR>—1 Free from desire, affection, love; अकामस्य क्रिया काचिद् दृश्यते नेह<BR> कर्हिचित् Ms. 2. 4 everything is an act of his will.<BR>—2 Reluctant, unwilling; योऽकामां दूषयेत्कन्यां स सद्यो वधमर्हति ।<BR> Ms. 8. 364; also नाकामो दातुमर्हति.<BR>—3 Uninfluenced by, not subject to, love; भयादकामापि हि दृष्टिविभ्रमं Ś. 1. 23.<BR>—4 Unconscious, unintentional; अकामोपनतेनेव साधोर्हृदयमेनसा R. 10. 39<BR> unconsciously committed.<BR>—5 The Sandhi which causes the dropping of a final र् before a following र्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकामकर्शन, अकामहत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकामकर्शन
अकाम + -कर्शन <i>a.</i> Ved. not frustrating desire; शिक्षानरः प्रदिवो<BR> अकामकर्शनः Rv. 1. 53. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकामहत
अकाम + -हत <i>a.</i> not smitten with desire or affection, free from desire, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकामतः
अकामतः <i>adv.</i> [अकाम-पञ्चम्यास्तसिल्] Unwillingly, reluctantly,<BR> unintentionally, unconsciously; इतरे कृतवन्तस्तु पापान्येतान्यकामतः<BR> Ms. 9. 242; अकामतः कृते पापे प्रायश्चित्तं विदुर्बुधाः 11. 45; अकामतः<BR> कृतं पापं वेदाभ्यासेन शुध्यति 11. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकामता
अकामता Absence of desire; न चैवेहास्त्यकामता Ms. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाय|अकायः
अकाय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कायो यस्य] Without body, incorporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकायः|अकाय
अकाय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Rāhu, who is represented as having no body, but only a head.<BR>—2 Epithet of the Supreme Spirit (without body, parts &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार|अकारः
अकार <i>a.</i> [करोतीति कारः कृ-घञ् अण् वा, न˚ त˚] Not doing<BR> or acting, void of action (क्रियारहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारः|अकार
अकार + .{@-रः@} The letter अ; अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि Bg. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारण|अकारणं
अकारण <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Causeless, groundless, spontaneous;<BR> ˚मित्राणि सतां चेतांसि K. 37 disinterested friends; ईदृशो मां प्रत्यमीषाम्<BR> ˚स्नेहः U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणम्
अकारण + .{@-णम्@} Absence of a cause, motive, or ground;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणाद्
अकारण + .{@-अकारणाद्, -रणम्, -णे@} causelessly, without cause or ground; किमकारणमेव<BR> दर्शनं विलपन्त्यै रतये न दीयते Ku. 4. 7; ˚परित्यक्ता मातापित्रोर्गुरोस्तथा<BR> Ms. 3. 157; अकारणात् परित्यज्य K. 167; त्यक्तो वा स्यादकारणात्<BR> Ms. 9. 177; किमकारणे कुप्यसि, अकारणे आत्मानमायासयसि Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणम्
अकारण + .{@-अकारणाद्, -रणम्, -णे@} causelessly, without cause or ground; किमकारणमेव<BR> दर्शनं विलपन्त्यै रतये न दीयते Ku. 4. 7; ˚परित्यक्ता मातापित्रोर्गुरोस्तथा<BR> Ms. 3. 157; अकारणात् परित्यज्य K. 167; त्यक्तो वा स्यादकारणात्<BR> Ms. 9. 177; किमकारणे कुप्यसि, अकारणे आत्मानमायासयसि Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणे
अकारण + .{@-अकारणाद्, -रणम्, -णे@} causelessly, without cause or ground; किमकारणमेव<BR> दर्शनं विलपन्त्यै रतये न दीयते Ku. 4. 7; ˚परित्यक्ता मातापित्रोर्गुरोस्तथा<BR> Ms. 3. 157; अकारणात् परित्यज्य K. 167; त्यक्तो वा स्यादकारणात्<BR> Ms. 9. 177; किमकारणे कुप्यसि, अकारणे आत्मानमायासयसि Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्णवेष्टकिक
अकार्णवेष्टकिक <i>a.</i> Face not adapted for ear-rings (Kāśi. VI. 2. 155).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्पण्य|अकार्पण्यं
अकार्पण्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Got without meanness; अकार्पण्यमशनं Bh. 3. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्य|अकार्य्य|अकार्य्यं
अकार्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Improper, not fit to be done.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">Page0005-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्यम्
अकार्य + .{@-र्यम्@} An improper, unworthy or bad act, a criminal or sinful action;<BR> मा नाम वैक्लव्यादकार्यं कुर्यात् Mk. 3. (आत्मघातादिरूपम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकार्यकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्यकारिन्
अकार्य + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> —1 an evil-doer, one who commits a misdeed; महापातकिनश्चैव<BR> शेषाश्चाकार्यकारिणः Ms. 11. 239 one that neglects oneʼs duty; दानेनाकार्यकारिणः<BR> (शुध्यन्ति) 5. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाल|अकालः
अकाल <i>a.</i> [नास्ति उचितः कालो यस्य]<BR>—1 Untimely, premature, inopportune, unseasonable, out of season; न<BR> प्रजासु ˚मृत्युश्चरति U. 2; न ह्यकालभवो मृत्युरिक्ष्वाकुपदमस्पृशत् ॥<BR> R. 15. 44; अकालमृत्युहरणं सर्वव्याधिविनाशनम् । सूर्यपादोदकं<BR> तीर्थं जठरे धारयाम्यहम् ॥ (सूर्यनमस्कारसंकल्पः); ˚वातावली Ratn. 3.<BR>—2 [न कालः] Not black, white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालः|अकाल
अकाल + .{@-लः@} [न˚ त˚] Wrong, inauspicious or unseasonable time,<BR> not the proper time (for anything); unholy time in a year calculated and<BR> shown in Indian almanacs. ˚लः स्वबलप्रधानविरोधस्य Ve. 3; ˚लः<BR> कुलजनस्य निवर्तितुं Mu. 7; अकाले बोधितो भ्राता R. 12. 81 (at an<BR> improper time); अत्यारूढो हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः 12. 33 takes<BR> no account of proper or improper time; अकाले वीक्षितो विष्णुर्हन्ति पुण्यं<BR> पुराकृतम्; नाकाले म्रियते कश्चित् प्राप्ते काले न जीवति; नाकाले म्रियते<BR> जन्तुः H. 1. 17 does not die a premature death; काले प्राप्तस्त्वकाले<BR> वा नास्यानश्नन् गृहे वसेत् Ms. 3. 105 in time or late.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकालकुसुमम्, अकालपुष्पम्, अकालकूष्माण्डः, अकालज, अकालोत्पन्न, अकालजात, अकालजलदः, अकालजलदोदयः, अकालमेघोदयः, अकालज्ञ, अकालवेला, अकालसह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालकुसुमम्
अकाल + -कुसुमम्, -पुष्पम् a flower blossoming out of season; ˚कुसुमानीव<BR> भयं संजनयन्ति हि H. 3. 23, (a bad omen boding some evil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालपुष्पम्
अकाल + -कुसुमम्, -पुष्पम् a flower blossoming out of season; ˚कुसुमानीव<BR> भयं संजनयन्ति हि H. 3. 23, (a bad omen boding some evil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालकूष्माण्डः|अकालकूष्माण्ड
अकाल + -कूष्माण्डः a pumpkin produced out of season; (fig.) of a useless birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालज|अकालजः
अकाल + -ज, -उत्पन्न, -जात <i>a.</i> produced out of season; premature; unseasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालोत्पन्न
अकाल + -ज, -उत्पन्न, -जात <i>a.</i> produced out of season; premature; unseasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालजात
अकाल + -ज, -उत्पन्न, -जात <i>a.</i> produced out of season; premature; unseasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालजलदः|अकालजलद
अकाल + -जलदः —1 an untimely cloud. —2 N. of the great-grandfather of<BR> the poet Rājaśekhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालजलदोदयः|अकालजलदोदय
अकाल + -जलदोदयः, -मेघोदयः<BR>—1 an unseasonable rise or gathering of clouds; बालातपमिवाब्जानामकालजलदोदयः R. 4. 61.<BR>—2 mist or fog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालमेघोदयः|अकालमेघोदय
अकाल + -जलदोदयः, -मेघोदयः<BR>—1 an unseasonable rise or gathering of clouds; बालातपमिवाब्जानामकालजलदोदयः R. 4. 61.<BR>—2 mist or fog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालज्ञ
अकाल + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> taking no account of proper or improper time; अत्यारूढो<BR> हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः R. 12. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालवेला
अकाल + -वेला unseasonable or improper time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालसह
अकाल + -सह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not enduring delay or loss of time, impatient, not biding oneʼs time.<BR>—2 not able to hold out (for a long time), unable to stand a protracted<BR> siege (as a दुर्ग); H. 3. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालिकम्
अकालिकम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 All of a sudden; अकालिकं कुरवो नाभविष्यन् Mb. 5. 32. 30.<BR>—2 Soon; यत्ते कार्यं सुपुत्रस्य क्रियतां तदकालिकम् Mb. 5. 57. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकासारः|अकासार
अकासारः Name of a teacher; Bhav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचन|अकिञ्चन|अकिञ्चनः
अकिंचन <i>a.</i> [नास्ति किंचन यस्य] Without anything, quite<BR> poor, utterly destitute, indigent, penniless; अकिंचनः सन् प्रभवः<BR> स संपदां Ku. 5. 77; न द्वन्द्वदुःखमिह किंचिदकिंचनोपि Śi. 4. 64<BR> disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचनम्
अकिंचन + .{@-नम्@} That which is worth nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचनता|अकिञ्चनता
अकिंचनता Renunciation of everything, voluntary poverty (संन्यासाङ्गयमविशेषः);<BR> व्रतं दानं परिव्रज्या तपस्या नियमस्थितिः । अहिंसासूयतास्तेयब्रह्माकिंचनता<BR> यमाः ॥ ˚त्वम् Poverty; अकिंचनत्वं मखजं व्यनक्ति R. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचनिमन्|अकिञ्चनिमन्
अकिंचनिमन् <i>m.</i> [पृथ्वादिगण] Poverty, utter destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचिज्ज्ञ
अकिंचिज्ज्ञ <i>a.</i> Not knowing anything, quite ignorant; यदाऽकिंचिज्ज्ञोऽहं<BR> द्विप इव मदान्धः समभवम् Bh. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिंचित्कर
अकिंचित्कर <i>a.</i> Not productive of anything, useless, immaterial;<BR> ˚रोऽन्यत्र पञ्चशरोऽपि स एव K. 242 powerless to do anything; परतन्त्रमिदमकिञ्चित्करं च Ve. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिल्बिष
अकिल्बिष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] sinless; न मां दोषेण सुग्रीव<BR> हन्तुमर्हस्यकिल्बिषम् । Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकीर्तिः|अकीर्ति|अकीर्त्ति|अकीर्त्तिः
अकीर्तिः <i>f.</i> [अप्रशस्ता कीर्तिः, न˚ त˚] Infamy, ill-repute,<BR> disgrace; अकीर्ति चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम् । संभावितस्य चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते ॥<BR> Bg. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुण्ठ|अकुंठ
अकुण्ठ <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not blunted, unobstructed; आशस्त्रग्रहणादकुण्ठपरशोः Ve. 2. 2.<BR>—2 Vigorous, able to work.<BR>—3 Fixed;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुण्ठधिष्ण्यम्
अकुण्ठ + ˚धिष्ण्यम् Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुण्ठित|अकुंठित
अकुण्ठित <i>a.</i> Not blunted; शास्त्रेष्वकुण्ठिता बुद्धिः R. 1. 19<BR> penetrating all sciences; बिभ्रतोऽस्त्रमचलेऽप्यकुण्ठितं 11. 74 taking<BR> effect on, prevailing against even mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुतः
अकुतः <i>adv.</i> [न कुतः, न˚ त˚] Not from anywhere (in comp. only).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकुतश्चलः, अकुतोभय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुतश्चलः|अकुतश्चल
अकुतः + -चलः N. of Śiva (not movable from any cause).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुतोभय|अकुतोभयः
अकुतः + -भय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कुतोऽपि भयं यस्य] secure, not threatened<BR> from any quarter, free from danger or fear, safe; मादृशानामपि ˚यः<BR> संचारो जातः U. 2; यानि त्रीण्यकुतोभयानि च पदान्यासन्खरायोधने<BR> <i>v. l.</i> for अपराङ्मुखाणि 5. 34. (अकुतश्चिद्भय also in the same sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुध्र्यञ्च्|अकुध्र्यंच्
अकुध्र्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> (Ved.) Fruitless, worthless (etym. doubtful); माकुध्र्यगिन्द्र<BR> शूर वस्वीरस्मे Rv. 10. 22. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुप्यम्
अकुप्यम् [न कुप्यम्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not a base metal, gold or silver; अकुप्यं वसु Ki. 1. 35 gold or silver.<BR>—2 Any base metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुल|अकुलः
अकुल <i>a.</i> [अप्रशस्तं कुलं यस्य] Low, mean, of a low family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलः|अकुल
अकुल + .{@-लः, -लम्@} N. of Śiva; अकुलं शिव इत्युक्तः कुलं शक्तिः प्रकीर्तिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलम्
अकुल + .{@-लः, -लम्@} N. of Śiva; अकुलं शिव इत्युक्तः कुलं शक्तिः प्रकीर्तिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुला
अकुल + .{@-ला@} N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलीन
अकुलीन <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Low-born, of no high descent.<BR>—2 Not belonging to the earth, not earthly; दिव्ययोषितमिवाकुलीनां<BR> K. 11 (a pun on the word; न कौ पृथ्व्यां लीना स्थिता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुशल
अकुशल <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Inauspicious, evil; unlucky, unfortunate.<BR>—2 Not clever or skilful.<BR>—3 Unpleasant, unwelcome; न द्वेष्ट्यकुशलं कर्म Bg. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुशलम्
अकुशल + .{@-लम्@} Evil; स स्निग्धो ऽकुशलान्निवारयति यः H. 2. 141 guards from evils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुह
अकुह <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] One who does not cheat, an honest<BR> man; अकुहः श्रद्दधानः सन् Rām. 2. 109. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूज
अकूज <i>a.</i> Silent; तमकूजमभिज्ञाय जनौघं सर्वशस्तदा Mb. 1. 126. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूपार|अकूपारः
अकूपार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Resulting in good, having a good issue.<BR>—2 Unlimited, unbounded; अकूपारस्य दावने Rv. 5. 39. 2<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूपारः|अकूपार
अकूपार + .{@-रः@} [न कुं पृथ्वीं पिपर्ति; पॄ-अण् बा˚ दीर्घः; न क्वापि पारं<BR> पूरणं वा गन्तव्यदेशो यस्य वा, पृषो. दीर्घः]<BR>—1 The sea, the receptacle of waters; अकूपारः सलिलो मातरिश्वा Rv. 10. 109. 1<BR> (समुद्रोऽप्यकूपार उच्यते अकूपारो भवति महापारः Nir.); न<BR> ह्यकूपारवत्कूपा वर्धन्ते विधुकान्तिभिः H.; अकूपारमिवापारं पारयिष्यामहे<BR> कथम् । Śiva B. 31. 44.<BR>—2 The sun (आदित्योऽप्यकूपार उच्यते अकूपारो भवति दूरपारः Nir.).<BR>—3 A tortoise in general (न कूपमृच्छति).<BR>—4 King of tortoises sustaining the world.<BR>—5 A stone or rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूवार
अकूवार = अकूपार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूर्च|अकूर्चः|अकूर्च्च|अकूर्च्चः
अकूर्च <i>a.</i> [नास्ति कूर्चं यस्य]<BR>—1 Not deceitful.<BR>—2 Bald; beardless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूर्चः|अकूर्च|अकूर्च्च|अकूर्च्चः
अकूर्च + .{@-र्चः@} Buddha; a deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृच्छ्र
अकृच्छ्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Free from difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृच्छ्रम्
अकृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्@} Absence of difficulty; ease, facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत|अकृतं
अकृत <i>a.</i> [कृ-कर्मणि क्तः, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not done, undone, unperformed; सर्वान् बलकृतानर्थानकृतान् मनुरब्रवीत्<BR> Ms. 8. 168; कृतं चाप्यकृतं भवेत् 8. 117.<BR>—2 Wrongly or differently done; कृताकृतावेक्षणादौ ब्रह्मा ऋत्विङ् नियुज्यते<BR> इति याज्ञिकाः.<BR>—3 Incomplete, not ready (as food); अकृतं च कृतात्क्षेत्रात् (अदोषवत्)<BR> Ms. 10. 114 not cultivated (अनुप्तशस्यम् Kull.); कृतान्नं चाकृतान्नेन<BR> (निर्मतव्यम्) 10. 94 (सिद्धान्नं चामान्नेन Kull.)<BR>—4 Uncreated.<BR>—5 One who has done no work.<BR>—6 Not developed or perfected, unripe, immature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृता
अकृत + .{@-ता@} One not legally regarded as a daughter and placed on a level<BR> with sons, (पुत्रिकात्वेन अकल्पिता); अकृता वा कृता वापि यं विन्देत्सदृशात्सुतम्<BR> Ms. 9. 136; according to some, a daughter who is not by a formal declaration<BR> but only mentally appointed to supply an heir for her father (अभिसंधिमात्रकृता<BR> वाग्व्यवहारेण कृता; कृता = यदपत्यं भवेदस्यां तन्मम स्यात्स्वधाकरम्<BR> इत्यभिधाय कन्यादानकाले वरानुमत्या या क्रियते Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतम्
अकृत + .{@-तम्@} An unperformed act; non-performance of an act; an unheard-of<BR> deed; अकृतं वै प्रजापतिः करोति Ait. Br.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकृतार्थ, अकृतास्त्र, अकृतात्मन्, अकृतोद्वाह, अकृतैनस्, अकृतकारम्, अकृतज्ञ, अकृतधी, अकृतबुद्धि, अकृतव्रणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतार्थ
अकृत + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> unsuccessful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतास्त्र
अकृत + -अस्त्र <i>a.</i> unpractised in arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतात्मन्
अकृत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ignorant, foolish, having an uncontrolled mind.<BR>—2 not identified with Brahma or the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतोद्वाह
अकृत + -उद्वाह <i>a.</i> unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतैनस्
अकृत + -एनस् <i>a.</i> not sinful or guilty, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतकारम्
अकृत + -कारम् <i>adv.</i> as has not been done before; ˚रं करोति Kāśi. III. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञ|अकृतज्ञः
अकृत + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> ungrateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतधी
अकृत + -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> ignorant; पश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति<BR> दुर्मतिः Bg. 18. 16.<BR> through unrefined understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतबुद्धि
अकृत + -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> ignorant; पश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति<BR> दुर्मतिः Bg. 18. 16.<BR> through unrefined understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतव्रणः|अकृतव्रण
अकृत + -व्रणः<BR>—1 N. of a commentator on the Purāṇas; V. P.; of a companion of Rāma<BR> Jāmadagnya; Mb.<BR>—2 not wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतिन्
अकृतिन् <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not skilful or clever, clumsy, awkward;<BR> unfit for doing anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्य
अकृत्य <i>a.</i> Unfit to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्यम्
अकृत्य + .{@-त्यम्@}<BR>—1 A crime, an improper act.<BR>—2 That which cannot be done; न हि वचनस्य किंचिदकृत्यमस्ति ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्त
अकृत्त <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Uncut, undiminished or unimpaired;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्तरुच्
अकृत्त + ˚रुच् of unimpaired splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्रिम|अकृत्रिमं
अकृत्रिम <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Natural, not man-made.<BR>—2 Spontaneous.<BR>—3 Valid, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्वा
अकृत्वा <i>ind.</i> Without doing; अकृत्वा परसंतापमगत्वा खलनम्रताम् । Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृप|अकृपः
अकृप <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Pitiless, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृपण|अकृपणः
अकृपण <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not wretched, not miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृश
अकृश <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not slender or weak, full, entire, strong.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकृशाश्वः, अकृशलक्ष्मी, अकृशलक्ष्मीः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृशाश्वः|अकृशाश्व
अकृश + -अश्वः N. of a king of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृशलक्ष्मी
अकृश + -लक्ष्मी <i>a.</i> endowed with full prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृशलक्ष्मीः
अकृश + -लक्ष्मीः great splendour or property; अकृशमकृशलक्ष्मीश्चेतसा<BR> शंसितं सः Ki. 5. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्ट
अकृष्ट <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not tilled; not drawn.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकृष्टपच्य, अकृष्टपच्या, अकृष्टरोहिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्टपच्य
अकृष्ट + -पच्य <i>a.</i> [अकृष्टे क्षेत्रे पच्यते] growing or ripening<BR> in unploughed land, growing exuberant or wild: ˚च्या इव सस्यसंपदः<BR> Ki. 1. 17; so ˚च्या ओषधयः; ˚च्यम् अशनं धान्यम्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्टपच्या
अकृष्ट + -पच्या (applied especially to) the earth yielding food grains,<BR> fruit etc. without being tilled; very fertile; अकृष्टपच्या पृथिवी विबभौ<BR> चैत्यमालिनी Mb. Crit. Ed. 12. 29. 21, 12. 216. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्टरोहिन्
अकृष्ट + -रोहिन् = ˚पच्य; बीजं च बालेयमकृष्टरोहि R. 14. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्टपच्य
अकृष्ट + -रोहिन् = ˚पच्य; बीजं च बालेयमकृष्टरोहि R. 14. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्ण|अकृष्णः
अकृष्ण <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not black, white, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्णः|अकृष्ण
अकृष्ण + .{@-ष्णः@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">Page0006-2</a>]<BR> [नास्ति कृष्णं मले यस्य]<BR>—1 The spotless moon; चन्द्रमा वै ब्रह्मा ऽकृष्णः इति श्रुतिः<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अकृष्णकर्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्णकर्मन्|अकृष्णकर्म्मन्
अकृष्ण + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> virtuous, free from black deeds, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेतु
अकेतु <i>a.</i> [नास्ति केतुश्चिह्नं यस्य] Unconscious (अज्ञान);<BR> केतुं कृण्वन्नकेतवे Rv. 1. 6. 3. (अज्ञानाय); shapeless (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेश|अकेशः
अकेश <i>a.</i> [अविद्यमानाः अल्पाः अप्रशस्ता वा केशा यस्य] Hairless,<BR> bald; having very few or very bad hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोटः|अकोट
अकोटः [न कृटति वक्रीभवति स्कन्धादिषु] The betel-nut palm,<BR> Areca (Mar. सुपारी) (without a कोट or bend, as it grows with<BR> a straight stem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्कः|अक्क
अक्कः A corner of a house; अक्के चेन्मधु विन्देत किमर्थं पर्वतं व्रजेत् ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्का
अक्का [अक्-क, अच्यते इत्यक्, अञ्च् क्विप् गतिः तस्यै कायति, कै-क वा<BR> Tv.] A mother. (Voc. अक्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त See under अञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ता
अक्ता <i>f.</i> (Ved.) Night; कृष्णेभिरक्तोषाः Rv. 1. 62. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तु|अक्तुः
अक्तु <i>m. f.</i> (Ved.) [अञ्ज् गतौ-क्तु]<BR>—1 Night; darkness, gloom.<BR>—2 Light, ray.<BR>—3 Ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त्रम्
अक्त्रम् [अञ्ज्-बा˚ क्त्र] An armour (वर्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्र|अक्रः
अक्र <i>a.</i> (Ved.) [अञ्च् गतौ-रक्]<BR>—1 Inactive, steady, firm (स्थिर).<BR>—2 Bootless, profitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रः|अक्र
अक्र + .{@-क्रः@} A fortification or rampart (प्राकार); banner (?); Nir. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रतु
अक्रतु <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्रतुर्यस्य]<BR>—1 Without sacrifices.<BR>—2 Devoid of energy, powerless; unwise.<BR>—3 Devoid of will or volition (संकल्परहित), epithet of God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रम|अक्रमः
अक्रम <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्रमः पादः क्रमणं वा यस्य]<BR>—1 Devoid of order, confused. —2 Without the power of going or moving (पादशून्य,<BR> आक्रमणशून्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रमः|अक्रम
अक्रम + .{@-मः@} —1 Want of order, confusion, irregularity (क्रमाभावः);<BR> एह्येहि पुत्र, अयमक्रमः Pañc. 1.<BR>—2 Absence of motion or movement.<BR>—3 Breach of propriety or decorum; कमक्रमं कर्तुमभूदपेक्षा वैलक्ष्यभाजां<BR> न महीपतीनाम् Vikr. 10. 3; कन्यान्तःपुरमक्रमात् प्रविशता Mv. 2. 50<BR> indecently, immodestly; वलीमुखचक्रमक्रममुच्चलितं Mv. 6 in disorder.<BR>—4 N. of a concept in kashmir Śaivism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्त|अक्रांत
अक्रान्त <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Unsurpassed; unconquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्ता
अक्रान्त + .{@-ता@} [न क्रम्यते कण्टकावृतत्वात् क्रम्-क्त, न˚ त˚] The<BR> egg plant (बृहती), Solanum Melongena (Mar. डोरलें वांगें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिय|अक्रियः
अक्रिय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्रिया यस्य न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Inactive, dull, torpid.<BR>—2 Without essential works.<BR>—3 Abstaining from religious rites.<BR>—4 Without action of any kind, epithet of God.<BR>—5 Worthless, good-for-nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिया
अक्रिय + .{@-या@} [न˚ त˚] Inactivity; neglect of duty; प्रधानस्याक्रिया<BR> यत्र साङ्गं तत्क्रियते पुनः । तदङ्गस्याक्रियायां तु नावृत्तिर्न च तत्क्रिया ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूर|अक्रूरः
अक्रूर <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूरः|अक्रूर
अक्रूर + .{@-रः@} N. of a Yādava, a friend and uncle of Kṛṣṇa. [It was<BR> he who induced Balarāma and Kṛṣṇa to go to Mathurā and kill Kaṃsa.<BR> He told the two brothers how their father Ānakadundubhi, the princess<BR> Devakī and even his own father Ugrasena had been insulted by the iniquitous<BR> demon Kaṃsa, and told them why he had been despatched to them. Kṛṣṇa<BR> consented to go and promised to slay the demon within 3 nights, which<BR> he succeeded in doing.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोध|अक्रोधः
अक्रोध <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्रोधो यस्य न˚ ब˚] Free from anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोधः|अक्रोध
अक्रोध + .{@-धः@} [न˚ त˚] Absence or suppression of anger; अक्रोधस्तपसः<BR> (विभूषणम्) Bh. 2. 80; अक्रोधेन जयेत् क्रुद्धं Mb. 5. 15. 18 regarded<BR> as one of the ten duties of an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोधन|अक्रोधनः
अक्रोधन <i>a.</i> Free from anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोधनः|अक्रोधन
अक्रोधन + .{@-नः@} N. of a prince, son of Ayutāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लान्त|अक्लान्तः
अक्लान्त <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Tireless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिका
अक्लिका The Indigo plant (Mar. नीळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिन्न
अक्लिन्न <i>a.</i> Not wet or moist;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिन्नवर्त्मन्
अक्लिन्न + ˚वर्त्मन् a sort of disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्ट
अक्लिष्ट <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unwearied, untroubled, not annoyed, undisturbed, indefatigable.<BR>—2 Not marred, unimpaired; इदमुपनतमेवं रूपमक्लिष्टकान्ति Ś. 5. 19<BR> of unimpaired or unblemished beauty; अन्यथा कथमियम् ˚ता लावण्यस्य<BR> K. 12 unmarred state, perfection.<BR>—3 Not laboured or elaborate.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्लिष्टकर्मन्, अक्लिष्टकारिन्, अक्लिष्टवर्ण, अक्लिष्टव्रत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्टकर्मन्
अक्लिष्ट + -कर्मन्, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> unwearied in actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्टकारिन्
अक्लिष्ट + -कर्मन्, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> unwearied in actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्टवर्ण
अक्लिष्ट + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> not confused, distinct; ˚र्णां गमनाभ्यनुज्ञां<BR> K. 293 given in plain, distinct terms; of unfaded colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्टव्रत
अक्लिष्ट + -व्रत <i>a.</i> not swerving from religious vows, unwearied in observing them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लीब
अक्लीब <i>a.</i> True, real; इदं वचनमक्लीबं Rām. 7. 83. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लीबम्
अक्लीब + .{@-बम्@} <i>ind.</i> Fearlessly; पितुर्वचनमक्लीबं करिष्यामि पितुर्हितम्<BR> Rām. 2. 21. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेश|अक्लेशं|अक्लेशः
अक्लेश <i>a.</i> Without trouble, easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेशम्
अक्लेश + .{@-शम्@} <i>n.</i> Want of trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्
अक्ष् €1. €5. P. [अक्षति, अक्ष्णोति, आनक्ष, अक्षिष्यति-अक्ष्यति, आक्षीत्, अक्षितुम्-अष्टुम्<BR> अक्षित्वा-अष्ट्वा, अष्ट]<BR>—1 To reach.<BR>—2 To pass through, pervade, penetrate (mostly Ved. in these senses);<BR> मक्षू ता त इन्द्र दानाप्नस आक्षाणे शूर वज्रिवः । Rv. 10. 22. 11.<BR>—3 To accumulate, increase. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षः|अक्ष|अक्षं
अक्षः [अश्-सः]<BR>—1 An axis, axle, pivot; अक्षभङ्गे च यानस्य … न दण्डं मनुरब्रवीत्<BR> Ms. 8. 291, 292; दृढधूः अक्षः Kāśi. V. 4. 74; Śi. 12. 2, 18. 7;<BR> ज्योतिश्चक्राक्षदण्डः Dk. 1 Axle-pole.<BR>—2 The pole of a cart.<BR>—3 A cart, car; also a wheel.<BR>—4 The beam of a balance.<BR>—5 Terrestrial latitude.<BR>—6 A die for playing with; cube; यानाक्षमधिकृत्य ब्रूत इति गम्यते<BR> न तु विदेवनाक्षमिति । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 35.<BR>—7 The seed of which rosaries are made.<BR>—8 A weight equal to 16 māṣas and called कर्ष.<BR>—9 N. of the plant Terminalia Belerica (विभीतक- Mar. बेहडा)<BR> the seed of which is used as a die; also the nut of this plant; यथा<BR> वै द्वे वामलके द्वे वा कोले द्वौ वाक्षौ मुष्टिरनुभवति Ch. Up.; so<BR> धाराभिरक्षमात्राभिः.<BR>—10 A shrub producing the rosary seed, Eleocarpus Ganitrus (रुद्राक्ष);<BR> the seed of this plant, as also of another plant (इन्द्राक्ष).<BR>—11 A serpent; hence a curve.<BR>—12 Garuḍa.<BR>—13 N. of a son of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—14 The soul.<BR>—15 Knowledge (usually, sacred).<BR>—16 Law; a lawsuit; legal procedure.<BR>—17 A person born blind.<BR>—18 The lower part of the temples (कर्णनेत्रयोर्मध्ये शङ्खादधोभागः).<BR>—19 The base of a column; अथवाक्षं नवांशोच्चं जन्म चैकेन कारयेत् । Māna. 14. 17.<BR>—20 The window-like part of a swing, a hammock, a palanquin, an axle of<BR> a chariot; पार्श्वयोर्वारणं कुर्यात् तस्याधोऽक्षं सुसंयुतम् ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-2" target="_blank">Page0007-2</a>]<BR> Māna. 50. 165, 166. 21 Gambling (in general). cf. अक्षो द्यूते वरूथाङ्गे<BR> नयवादौ बिभीतके । कर्षे व्याप्तौ कृषे (?) चक्रे आधारव्यवहारयोः । आत्मजे<BR> पाशके दैत्यभेदे चेन्द्रियवालयोः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षम्
अक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@} (अश्नुते व्याप्नोति विषयान् स्ववृत्त्या संयोगेन वा) —1 An<BR> organ of sense; निरोधाच्चेतसोऽक्षाणि निरुद्धान्यखिलान्यपि Pt. 2. 154;<BR> संयताक्षो विनीतः Mātaṅga L. 12. 1. (The word संयताक्ष here<BR> means ‘having control over his senses’, but ‘having eyes closed’ MW.);<BR> <i>m.</i> also नियच्छेद्विषयेभ्योऽक्षान् Bhāg.; an object of sense.<BR>—2 The eye, (only at the end of comp.; जलजाक्ष, कमलाक्ष, &c.)<BR>—3 Sachal salt, sea-salt.<BR>—4 Blue vitriol (from its crystallized shape) (Mar. मोरचूद) [cf.<BR> L. <i>axis</i>; Gr. <i>akshon</i> or <i>axon</i>, Old Germ. <i>ahsa</i>; Germ. <i>achse</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्षांशः, अक्षाग्रम्, अक्षाग्रकीलः, अक्षाग्रकीलकः, अक्षावपनम्, अक्षावलिः, अक्षावापः, अक्षोपकरणम्, अक्षकर्णः, अक्षकुशल, अक्षशौण्ड, अक्षकूटः, अक्षकोविद, अक्षक्षेत्रम्, अक्षग्लहः, अक्षचक्रम्, अक्षजम्, अक्षजः, अक्षतत्त्वम्, अक्षविद्या, अक्षदण्डः, अक्षदर्शकः, अक्षदृश्, अक्षदृक्कर्मन्, अक्षदेविन्, अक्षद्यूतम्, अक्षद्यूतिकम्, अक्षद्रुग्ध, अक्षधरः, अक्षधूः, अक्षधूर्तः, अक्षधूर्तिलः, अक्षपटलः, अक्षपटलाधिकृतः, अक्षपरि, अक्षपाटः, अक्षपाटकः, अक्षपातः, अक्षपादः, अक्षपीडा, अक्षभागः, अक्षभारः, अक्षमदः, अक्षमात्रम्, अक्षमाला, अक्षसूत्रम्, अक्षराजः, अक्षवामः, अक्षवाटः, अक्षविद्, अक्षवृत्त, अक्षवृत्तम्, अक्षशालिन्, अक्षस्तुषः, अक्षहृदयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षांशः|अक्षांश
अक्षः + -अंशः the degree of latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्रम्
अक्षः + -अग्रम् the axle or its end; the anterior end of the axle or its<BR> end; the anterior end of the pole of a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्रकीलः|अक्षाग्रकील
