अक्षर + -चञ्चुः, -चञ्चुम्, -चणः, -चनः<BR> [अक्षरेण वर्णविन्यासलिप्या वित्तः अक्षर-चणप्<BR> or चु(ञ्चुं)ञ्चुप् तेन वित्तश्चुञ्चुप् चणपौ; P. V. 2. 26.]<BR> a scribe, writer, copyist; so ˚जीवकः, -जीवी, अक्षरेण जीवति; जीव् णिनि<BR> or ण्वुल्; also ˚जीविकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजीवी
अक्षर + -चञ्चुः, -चञ्चुम्, -चणः, -चनः<BR> [अक्षरेण वर्णविन्यासलिप्या वित्तः अक्षर-चणप्<BR> or चु(ञ्चुं)ञ्चुप् तेन वित्तश्चुञ्चुप् चणपौ; P. V. 2. 26.]<BR> a scribe, writer, copyist; so ˚जीवकः, -जीवी, अक्षरेण जीवति; जीव् णिनि<BR> or ण्वुल्; also ˚जीविकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजीविकः|अक्षरजीविक
अक्षर + -चञ्चुः, -चञ्चुम्, -चणः, -चनः<BR> [अक्षरेण वर्णविन्यासलिप्या वित्तः अक्षर-चणप्<BR> or चु(ञ्चुं)ञ्चुप् तेन वित्तश्चुञ्चुप् चणपौ; P. V. 2. 26.]<BR> a scribe, writer, copyist; so ˚जीवकः, -जीवी, अक्षरेण जीवति; जीव् णिनि<BR> or ण्वुल्; also ˚जीविकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरच्युतकम्
अक्षर + -च्युतकम् [अक्षरं च्युतं लुप्तं यत्र; ब˚ कप्] getting out<BR> a different meaning by the omission of a letter (<i>e. g.</i> कुर्वन् दिवाकरश्लेषं<BR> दधच्चरणडम्बरम् । देव यौष्माकसेनयोः करेणुः प्रसरत्यसौ where<BR> another meaning may be got by omitting क in करेणुः <i>i. e.</i><BR> by taking रेणुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरच्छन्दस्|अक्षरच्छंदस्|अक्षरछन्दस्
अक्षर + -छन्दस् <i>n.</i>, {@-वृत्तम्@}<BR> a metre regulated by the number of syllables it contains;<BR> छन्दस्तु द्विविधं प्रोक्तं वृत्तं जातिरिति द्विधा । वृत्तमक्षरसंख्यातं<BR> जातिर्मात्राकृता भवेत् ॥ unshaken resolve, resolute (अक्षरं निश्चिलं<BR> छन्दोऽभिप्रायो यस्य);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजननी
अक्षर + -जननी, -तूलिका [अक्षराणां जननीव; तल्लिपिलेखानां तूलिकेव<BR> वा साधनत्वात्] a reed or pen. -जीवकः or -जीविन् <i>m.</i> ‘One who lives by writing’<BR>, a scribe. {@-(वि)न्यासः@} [ष˚ त˚ भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 writing, arrangement of letters; भूर्जपत्रगतो ˚सः V. 2.<BR>—2 the alphabet.<BR>—3 scripture. —4 हृदयाद्याधारस्पर्शपूर्वकं तदक्षराणां स्मरणोच्चारणरूपस्तन्त्रप्रसिद्धो वर्णन्यासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरतूलिका
अक्षर + -जननी, -तूलिका [अक्षराणां जननीव; तल्लिपिलेखानां तूलिकेव<BR> वा साधनत्वात्] a reed or pen. -जीवकः or -जीविन् <i>m.</i> ‘One who lives by writing’<BR>, a scribe. {@-(वि)न्यासः@} [ष˚ त˚ भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 writing, arrangement of letters; भूर्जपत्रगतो ˚सः V. 2.<BR>—2 the alphabet.<BR>—3 scripture. —4 हृदयाद्याधारस्पर्शपूर्वकं तदक्षराणां स्मरणोच्चारणरूपस्तन्त्रप्रसिद्धो वर्णन्यासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरपङ्क्ति
अक्षर + -पङ्क्ति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having 5 syllables (पङ्क्ति = Gr. <i>pentas</i>-five) सु मत् पद्<BR> वग दे इत्येष वै यज्ञोऽक्षरपङ्क्तिः Ait. Br. (तान्योतान्यक्षराणि होतृजपादौ<BR> प्रयोक्तव्यानि).<BR>—2 N. of metre of four lines (द्विपदा विराज्) each having five syllables<BR> (one dactyl and one spondee).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरभाज्
अक्षर + -भाज् <i>a.</i> having a share in the syllables (of a prayer ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरभूमिका
अक्षर + -भूमिका tablet; न्यस्ताक्षरामक्षरभूमिकायाम् R. 18. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरमुखः|अक्षरमुख
अक्षर + -मुखः [अक्षराणि तन्मयानि शास्त्राणि वा मुखे यस्य] a scholar, student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरमुखम्
अक्षर + -मुखम् [ष˚ त˚] the beginning of the alphabet; the letter अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरमुष्टिका
अक्षर + -मुष्टिका ‘finger-speech’, speaking by means of finger-signs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरवर्जित
अक्षर + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> unlettered, illiterate, not knowing how to read<BR> or write. <i>a.</i> of an epithet of परमात्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरव्यक्तिः|अक्षरव्यक्ति
अक्षर + -व्यक्तिः <i>f.</i> [ष˚ त˚] distinct articulation of syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरशिक्षा
अक्षर + -शिक्षा [ष˚ त˚] the science of (mystic) syllables; theory<BR> of ब्रह्म (ब्रह्मतत्त्व); मह्यं ˚क्षां विधाय Dk. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरसंस्थानम्
अक्षर + -संस्थानम् [अक्षराणां संस्थानं यत्र] arrangement of letters,<BR> writing, alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरकम्
अक्षरकम् [स्वार्थे कन्] A vowel, a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरशः
अक्षरशः <i>adv.</i> [अक्षरमक्षरमिति वीप्सार्थकारके शस्]<BR>—1 Syllable by syllable.<BR>—2 To the very letter; literally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षर्य
अक्षर्य <i>a.</i> [गवादिगण] Relating to letters or syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरी
अक्षरी [अश्नुते गगनाभोगं मेघैः; अश् सरन्, गौरा˚ ङीष्] The rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षानह्
अक्षानह् See under अक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षान्तिः|अक्षान्ति|अक्षांति|अक्षांतिः
अक्षान्तिः <i>f.</i> [न˚ त˚] Intolerance, non-forbearance; envy,<BR> jealousy, anger, impatience; अक्षान्तिसारसर्वस्वं दुर्वाससमवेहि माम् V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षार|अक्षारः
अक्षार <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्षारं यत्र] Free from artificial salt<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षारः|अक्षार
अक्षार + .{@-रः@} Natural salt गोक्षीरं गोघृतं चैव धान्यमुद्रास्तिला यवाः ।<BR> सामुद्रसैन्धवं चैव अक्षारंलवणं स्मृतम् ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्षारलवणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षारलवणम्
अक्षार + -लवणम् (-रा˚) [क्षारेण ऊषरमृत्तिकया निर्वृत्तं-अण् क्षारं<BR> कृत्रिमं लवणं; न˚ त˚] natural salt; मुन्यन्नानि पयः सोमो<BR> मांसं यच्चानुपस्कृतम् । अक्षारलवणं चैव प्रकृत्या हविरुच्यते ॥<BR> Ms. 3. 257 (अकृत्रिमलवणं सैन्धवादि); ˚लवणान्नाः स्युः 5. 73;<BR> चतुर्थकालमश्नीयादक्षारलवणं मितम् 11. 109; sometimes used for<BR> food that may be eaten at times unfit for the performance of religious<BR> duties; a class of objects such as cowʼs milk, ghee, rice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षि
अक्षि <i>n.</i> [अश्नुते विषयान्; अश्-क्सि, अशेर्णित् Uṇ. 3. 155-6] अक्षिणी,<BR> अक्षीणि, अक्ष्णा, अक्ष्णः &c.<BR>—1 The eye (which grasps or sees objects); changed to अक्ष at the<BR> end of Bahuvrīhi comp.; <i>f.</i> ˚क्षी when a limb of the body is indicated,<BR> as जलजाक्षी, otherwise दीर्घाक्षा वेणुयष्टिः; in Avyayī. comp.<BR> also it is changed to अक्ष, (समक्षम्, परोक्षम् &c.).<BR>—2 The number two; (-क्षिणी) the sun and moon. [cf. L. <i>oculus</i>;<BR> Ger. <i>auge</i>; Gr. <i>okos, okkos</i>, Zend. <i>ashi</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्ष्यामयः, अक्षिकम्पः, अक्षिकूटः, अक्षिकूटकः, अक्षिगोलः, अक्षितारा, अक्षिगत, अक्षिजाहः, अक्षिपक्ष्मन्, अक्षिलोमन्, अक्षिपटलम्, अक्षिपत्, अक्षिभू, अक्षिभेषजम्, अक्षिजः, अक्षिभ्रुवम्, अक्षिविकूणितम्, अक्षिविकूशितम्, अक्षिश्रवस्, अक्षिसंवित्, अक्षिसूत्रम्, अक्षिस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्यामयः|अक्ष्यामय
अक्षि + -आमयः an eye-disease; यथा अक्ष्यामये मुद्गौदनं निवातशय्या<BR> चेति नित्यं शय्यासनं भोजनं च विकरोति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 32 and 10. 6-81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकम्पः|अक्षिकम्प
अक्षि + -कम्पः twinkling; नाक्षिकम्पं व्यतिष्ठत R. 15. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकूटः|अक्षिकूट
अक्षि + -कूटः, -कूटकः, -गोलः, -तारा [ष˚ त˚] the eyeball, pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकूटकः|अक्षिकूटक
अक्षि + -कूटः, -कूटकः, -गोलः, -तारा [ष˚ त˚] the eyeball, pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगोलः|अक्षिगोल
अक्षि + -कूटः, -कूटकः, -गोलः, -तारा [ष˚ त˚] the eyeball, pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितारा
अक्षि + -कूटः, -कूटकः, -गोलः, -तारा [ष˚ त˚] the eyeball, pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगत|अक्षिगतः
अक्षि + -गत <i>a.</i> [अक्ष्णि गतः सर्वदा भावनावशात् अक्ष्यसन्निकृष्टोऽपि उपस्थित इव]<BR>—1 visible, present; न विभावयत्यनिशमक्षिगतामपि मां भवानतिसमीपतया Śi. 9. 81.<BR>—2 rankling in the eye, an eye-sore,<BR> being a thorn in the eye, hated; ˚तोहमस्य हास्यो जातः Dk. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिजाहः|अक्षिजाह
अक्षि + -जाहः [ष˚ त˚] the root of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपक्ष्मन्
अक्षि + -पक्ष्मन्, -लोमन् <i>n.</i> [ष˚ त˚] the eyelash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिलोमन्
अक्षि + -पक्ष्मन्, -लोमन् <i>n.</i> [ष˚ त˚] the eyelash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपटलम्
अक्षि + -पटलम् [ष˚ त˚].<BR>—1 a coat of the eye.<BR>—2 a disease of the eye pertaining to this coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपत्
अक्षि + -पत् <i>a.</i> Ved. falling into the eye, hence hurtful. न हि<BR> मे अक्षिपच्चनाऽच्छान्त्सुः पञ्च कृष्टयः Rv. 10. 119. 6. <i>adv.</i> a little,<BR> as much as a mote (as much as could fall into the eye).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिभू
अक्षि + -भू <i>a.</i> [अक्ष्णो भूर्विषयः] visible, perceptible, manifest;<BR> (hence) true, real.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिभेषजम्
अक्षि + -भेषजम् [ष˚ त˚] collyrium, a kind of balm (for the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिजः|अक्षिज
अक्षि + -जः (-जम् also) N. of a plant (पट्टिकालोध्रवृक्ष) used<BR> to heal some varieties of the eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिभ्रुवम्
अक्षि + -भ्रुवम् [समाहारद्वन्द्व] the eye and the eyebrows taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिविकूणितम्
अक्षि + -विकूणितम्, -विकूशितम् [अक्ष्णः विकूणितम् लज्जादिना सम्यक् प्रसाराभावात्<BR> संकोचो यत्र] a side-look, leer, a look with the eyelids partially closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिविकूशितम्
अक्षि + -विकूणितम्, -विकूशितम् [अक्ष्णः विकूणितम् लज्जादिना सम्यक् प्रसाराभावात्<BR> संकोचो यत्र] a side-look, leer, a look with the eyelids partially closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिश्रवस्
अक्षि + -श्रवस् serpent बभुरक्षिश्रवसो मुखे विशालाः Śi. 20. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिसंवित्
अक्षि + -संवित् perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिसूत्रम्
अक्षि + -सूत्रम् the line of the eyes (with reference to idols). अक्षिसूत्रावसानं<BR> च तस्याधस्तात्पदान्तकम् Māna. 9. 2. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिस्पन्दनम्
अक्षि + -स्पन्दनम् eye twitching; Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकः|अक्षिक
अक्षिकः [अक्षाय चक्रावयवाय हितः -ठन्] N. of a tree (रञ्जनद्रुम<BR> Mar. थोरराळेचा वृक्ष). अक्षीक; also see अक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिणी
अक्षिणी One of the 8 conditions or privileges attached to landed property (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षित
अक्षित <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Undecayed, permanent, uniniured,<BR> undecaying, unfailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितम्
अक्षित + .{@-तम@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 100000 millions.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्षितोति, अक्षितवसु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितोति
अक्षित + -ऊति, -वसु (ता˚) N. of Indra, giving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">Page0010-2</a>]<BR> permanent help, or having unfailing wealth (?) उग्रं न वीरं नमसोप<BR> सेदिम विभूतिमक्षितावसुम् Rv. 8. 49. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितवसु
अक्षित + -ऊति, -वसु (ता˚) N. of Indra, giving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">Page0010-2</a>]<BR> permanent help, or having unfailing wealth (?) उग्रं न वीरं नमसोप<BR> सेदिम विभूतिमक्षितावसुम् Rv. 8. 49. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितरम्
अक्षितरम् [अक्षीव तरति; तृ-अच् Tv.] Water (निर्मलत्वान्नेत्रतुल्यत्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिति|अक्षितिः
अक्षिति <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितिः|अक्षिति
अक्षिति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Imperishable nature; यो वैषामक्षिति वेद सोऽन्नमिति<BR> प्रतीकेन Bṛ. Ār. Up. 1. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षियत्|अक्षियन्त्
अक्षियत् <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Not decreasing in wealth; destitute<BR> of a dwelling, unsettled (?); क्षियन्तं त्वमक्षियन्तं कृणोति Rv. 4. 17. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिवः|अक्षिव
अक्षिवः [अक्षि वाति प्रीणाति अञ्जनेन; वा˚ क.] N. of a plant,<BR> शोभाञ्जनवृक्ष Guilandina or Hyperanthera Moringa [Mar. शेवगा].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिवम्
अक्षिवः + .{@-वम्@} Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीक|अक्षीकः
अक्षीक See अक्षक or अक्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीव|अक्षीवं|अक्षीवः
अक्षीव (ब) <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीब|अक्षीबः
अक्षीव (ब) <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीवः|अक्षीव|अक्षीवं
अक्षीव (ब) + .{@-वः@} [न क्षीवते माद्यति, क्षीव्-क क्त वा, न˚ त˚]<BR> N. of the tree शोभाञ्जन (Mar. शेवगा, शेगट) Hyperanthera moringa;<BR> cf विडङ्गा-क्षीबकुल्माष-माषगोधूमसंस्कृतम् । मोदकार्थं महीपाल पिष्टमाढकमिष्यते ॥<BR> Mātaṅga L. 21. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीवम्
अक्षीव (ब) + .{@-वम्@} Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षु
अक्षु <i>a.</i> Ved. [अक्ष्-उ] Quick (शीघ्र); according to others<BR> (क्षुः) a kind of net. जूर्णो वामक्षुरंहसो यजत्राः Rv. 1. 180. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुण्ण|अक्षुण्णः
अक्षुण्ण <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unbroken, uncurtailed.<BR>—2 Not conquered or defeated, successful; अक्षुण्णोऽनुनयः Ve. 1. 2.<BR>—3 Not trodden or beaten, unusual, strange; अभीक्ष्णमक्षुण्णतयातिदुर्गमम्<BR> Śi. 1. 32 being not practised or experienced.<BR>—4 Inexperienced, not expert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुद्र|अक्षुद्रः
अक्षुद्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not small or insignificant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुद्रः|अक्षुद्र
अक्षुद्र + .{@-द्रः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुध्
अक्षुध् <i>f.</i> [न˚ त˚] Absence of hunger, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुध्य
अक्षुध्य <i>a.</i> [अक्षुधे हितं; अक्षुध्-यत्.] Ved.<BR>—1 That which tends to cause absence of hunger (क्षुधाभावसाधनं द्रव्यम्).<BR>—2 Not liable to hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षेत्र
अक्षेत्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Destitute of fields; uncultivated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षेत्रम्
अक्षेत्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 A bad field (अप्रशस्तम् क्षेत्रम्); अक्षेत्रे बीजमुत्सृष्टमन्तरैव<BR> विनश्यति Ms. 10. 71.<BR>—2 Not a good geometrical figure.<BR>—3 (fig.) A bad pupil, unworthy recipient or receptacle (of anything).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्षेत्रविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षेत्रविद्
अक्षेत्र + -विद् <i>a.</i> [क्षेत्रं देहतत्त्वं तत्त्वतो न जानाति; विद्-क्विप्]<BR> destitute of spiritual knowledge; not knowing the true nature of the क्षेत्र<BR> or body (क्षेत्रतत्त्वानभिज्ञः आत्मत्वेन देहाभिमानी जीवः); So अक्षेत्रज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षेत्रिन्
अक्षेत्रिन् <i>a.</i> [क्षेत्रं शस्योत्पत्तिस्थानं कलत्रं वा; मत्वर्थे<BR> इनि, न˚ त˚] Having no field, not the master of a field, येऽक्षेत्रिणो<BR> बीजवन्तः परक्षेत्रप्रवापिणः Ms. 9. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोटः|अक्षोट
अक्षोटः [अक्ष्-ओट; अक्षस्य बिभीतकस्येव उटानि पर्णान्यस्य वा Tv.]<BR>—1 N. of a tree पर्वतीयपीलु (Mar. डोंगरी अक्रोड).<BR>—2 A walnut; a tree bearing an oily nut. also अक्षोटक; … आम्रैरक्षोटकैस्तदा<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोडः|अक्षोड
अक्षोडः [अक्ष् ओड; अक्षः बिभीतकः इव ओडति पत्रैः संहन्यते;<BR> उड्-अच् वा Tv.] also written as अक्षोट, -ड, -डक, -आक्षोट, आखोड, आखोडक &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ|अक्षोभः
अक्षोभ <i>a.</i> [नास्ति क्षोभो यस्य] Not agitated, unmoved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभः|अक्षोभ
अक्षोभ + .{@-भः@}<BR>—1 Absence of agitation.<BR>—2 The tying post of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ्य|अक्षोभ्यः
अक्षोभ्य <i>a.</i> [क्षोभ्यते विचाल्यते; क्षुभ्-णिच् कर्माणि यत्, न˚ त˚]<BR> Immovable, imperturbable; अक्षोभ्यः स नवोप्यासीत् R. 17. 44.<BR> was unassailable<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ्यः|अक्षोभ्य
अक्षोभ्य + .{@-भ्यः@}<BR>—1 A particular sage (तन्त्रोक्तो द्वितीयविद्योपासकः तद्देवतायाः शिरसि<BR> नागरूपेण स्थितः ऋषिभेदः; अक्षोभ्योस्या ऋषिः प्रोक्तः Tv.).<BR>—2 N. of a Buddha.<BR>—3 An immense number, said by Buddhists to be 100 विवर.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्षोभ्यकवचम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ्यकवचम्
अक्षोभ्य + -कवचम् [अक्षोभाय हितम् अक्षोभ्यम्] a sort of कवच or<BR> armour referred to in Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षौरिमम्
अक्षौरिमम् (astrol.) A star on which it is considered inauspicious to get shaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षौहिणी
अक्षौहिणी [ऊहः समूहः संविकल्पज्ञानं वा सोऽस्यामस्ति इनि, अक्षाणां<BR> रथानां सर्वेषामिन्द्रियाणां वा ऊहिनी; णत्वं वृद्धिश्च P. VI. 1. 89. Vārt.]<BR> A large army consisting of 21870 chariots, as many elephants, 65610 horse,<BR> and 109350 foot. अक्षौहिणी = 10 अनीकिन्यः. अनीक्रिनी = 3 चम्वः.<BR> चमूः = 3 पृतनाः. पृतना = 3 वाहिन्यः. वाहिनी = 3 गणाः.<BR> गण = 3 गुल्माः. गुल्मः = 3 सेनामुखानि. सेनामुखम् = 3 पत्तयः.<BR> पत्तिः = १ रथः + १ हस्ती + ३ अश्वाः + ५ पदातयः.<BR> cf. एकेभैकरथा त्र्यश्वा पत्तिः पञ्चपदातिका । पत्त्यङ्गैस्त्रिगुणैः<BR> सर्वैः क्रमादाख्या यथोत्तरम् ॥ सेनामुखं गुल्मगणौ वाहिनी पृतना चमूः ।<BR> अनीकिनी दशानीकिन्यक्षौहिणी … … ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्ण|अक्ष्णं
अक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> [अश्नुते व्याप्नोति अश्-क्स्न; Uṇ. 3. 17] Unbroken (अखण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णम्
अक्ष्ण + .{@-क्ष्णम्@} Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णा
अक्ष्णा A part स यद्यनेन किञ्चिदक्ष्णयावृतं भवति Bṛ. Ār. Up. 1. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णया
अक्ष्णया <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Tortuously, circuitously, in a crooked way; तानक्ष्णया संतृन्दन्ति.<BR> Śat. Br. (वक्रमार्गेण, कौटिल्येन).<BR>—2 Wrongly;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अक्ष्णयारज्जुः, अक्ष्णयास्तोमीया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णयाद्रुह्
अक्ष्णया + ˚द्रुह् Ved. seeking to hurt in a wrongful way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णयारज्जुः|अक्ष्णयारज्जु
अक्ष्णया + -रज्जुः <i>f.</i> diagonal line; Śulba. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णयास्तोमीया
अक्ष्णया + -स्तोमीया Name of an Iṣṭakā, Ts.; Śat. Br. अक्ष्णयाध्रुक् Rv. 1. 122. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्णयावन्
अक्ष्णयावन् <i>a.</i> Going through, penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखट्टः|अखट्ट
अखट्टः [खट्ट्-अच्, न˚ त˚] N. of a tree (प्रियाल) Buchanania<BR> Latifolia. [Mar. चारोळी]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखट्टिः|अखट्टि
अखट्टिः <i>m. f.</i> [खट्ट्-इ, न˚ त˚ वा डीप्] Bad conduct<BR> (अशिष्टव्यवहार); a childish freak or whim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्ड|अखंड|अखण्डः
अखण्ड <i>a.</i> [खण्ड्-घञ्, न˚ त˚] Unbroken, whole, entire,<BR> complete; अखण्डं पुण्यानां फलमिव Ś. 2. 10; अखण्डकलः शशी<BR> Māl. 2. 2; with undiminished orb, full; निर्जिगाय मुखमिन्दुमखण्डम्<BR> Ki. 9. 38; अखण्डेन तपसा 10. 63; undisturbed; सुन्दस्त्रीदमनेप्यखण्डयशसः<BR> U. 5. 34 v. l.; of untarnished, unsullied fame;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डद्वादशी
अखण्ड + ˚द्वादशी the 12th<BR> day of the bright half of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डम्
अखण्ड + .{@-ण्डम्@} <i>adv.</i> Uninterruptedly; अखण्डमाखण्डलतुल्यधामभिश्चिरं<BR> धृता Ki. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डन|अखंडन|अखण्डनः
अखण्डन <i>a.</i> [न खण्ड्यते निरवयवत्वात्; खण्ड्-ल्युट्; न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unbroken, not capable of being broken or divided, epithet of परमात्मन्.<BR>—2 Full, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डनम्
अखण्डन + .{@-नम्@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not breaking, leaving entire.<BR>—2 Non-refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डनः|अखण्डन|अखंडन
अखण्डन + .{@-नः@} Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डित|अखंडित
अखण्डित <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unbroken, undivided.<BR>—2 Uninterrupted, perpetual, undisturbed, continuous; ˚ता मे वाणिज्या<BR> Mu. 1; अखण्डितं प्रेम लभस्व पत्युः Ku. 7. 28 everlasting, unbroken.<BR>—3 Unimpaired; unrefuted &c.; भट्टिन्या अखण्डितात् प्रणयात् M. 3 never<BR> disappoinied; शतमखं तमखण्डितपौरुषम् R. 9. 13 whose prowess<BR> knows no repulse or defeat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अखण्डितोत्सव, अखण्डितर्तुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डितोत्सव
अखण्डित + -उत्सव <i>a.</i> always festive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डितर्तुः|अखण्डितर्तु|अखण्डितर्त्तु|अखण्डितर्त्तुः
अखण्डित + -ऋतुः [अखण्डितः ऋतुः तत्संपत् पुष्पादिप्रसवरूपा यत्र]<BR> time or season which yields its usual produce of flowers &c. ━(<i>a.</i>) fruitful,<BR> bearing fruit in due season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखर्व
अखर्व <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not dwarfish, short or stunted; not<BR> small; great; अखर्वेण गर्वेण विराजमानः Dk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखलः|अखल
अखलः A good physician. Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखात|अखातं|अखातः
अखात <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not dug; not buried. अखाते च तडागे<BR> च प्रविष्टो मकरः कथम् । Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखातः|अखात|अखातं
अखात + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A natural lake or pool of water; a bay; especially a<BR> pool before a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखातम्
अखात + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A natural lake or pool of water; a bay; especially a<BR> pool before a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखाद्य|अखाद्यं
अखाद्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिद्र
अखिद्र <i>a.</i> Ved. [खिद्-रक्, न˚ त˚] Unwearied; यातेमखिद्रयामभिः<BR> Rv. 1. 38. 11 unwearied in their course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिन्न
अखिन्न <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not fatigued or wearied.<BR>—2 Not involving fatigue. मखेष्वखिन्नोऽनुमतः Ki. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिल|अखिलं
अखिल <i>a.</i> [नास्ति खिलम् अवशिष्टं यस्य Tv.]<BR>—1 Whole, entire, complete; oft. with सर्व. एतद्धि मत्तोऽधिजगे<BR> सर्वमेषोऽखिलं मुनिः Ms. 1. 59; ˚लेन entirely.<BR>—2 Not uncultivated or fallow, ploughed (land);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिलात्मन्
अखिला + ˚आत्मन् the universal spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिलिका
अखिलिका [वनस्पतिवि˚] Momordaica Charantia (Mar. कारली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखेटिकः|अखेटिक
अखेटिकः [न खेटत्यस्मात्; खिट् भये षिकन् Tv.]<BR>—1 A tree in general.<BR>—2 (आखेटिक) A dog trained to the chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखेदिन्
अखेदिन् <i>a.</i> Not wearisome, not fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखेदित्वम्
अखेदिन् + ˚त्वम् continuous flow<BR> of speech regarded as one of the वाग्गुणs of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्खल
अख्खल <i>ind.</i> An exclamation of joy;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्खलीकृ
अख्खल + ˚लीकृ to utter this exclamation.<BR> अख्खलीकृत्या पितरं न पुत्रो अन्यो अन्यमुपवदन्तमेति । Rv. 7. 103. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्यातिः|अख्याति
अख्यातिः <i>f.</i> Infamy, ill-repute;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्यातिकर
अख्यातिः + ˚कर <i>a.</i> disgraceful, disreputable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्
अग् €1 P. (अङ्गति, आगीत्, अगिष्यति, अगितुम्)<BR>—1 To wind, curl, move tortuously, or in a zigzag way.<BR>—2 To go (अङ्गति, अङ्गीत् &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग|अगः
अग <i>a.</i> [न गच्छतीति; गम्-ड. न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unable to walk, not going, not in a position to go; अगो वृषलः शीतेन<BR> P. VI. 3. 77. Sk. अगजगदोकसामखिलशक्त्यवबोधक ते Bhāg. 10. 87. 14.<BR>—2 Unapproachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगः|अग
अग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 A tree; सदानतो येन विषाणिनाऽगः Śi. 4. 63.<BR>—2 A mountain; ध्वनिरगविवरेषु नूपुराणाम् Ki. 10. 4 also a stone;<BR> प्रत्यापगं प्रत्यगम् Mahānāṭaka.<BR>—3 A snake.<BR>—4 The sun (न गच्छति वक्रगत्या पश्चिमम्, तस्य हि वक्रगत्यभावो<BR> ज्योतिषप्रसिद्धः; or, ‘not going’ the earth by its diurnal rotation causing<BR> day and night).<BR>—5 A water-jar, as in अगस्त्य (कुम्भस्त्यान).<BR>—6 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">Page0012-1</a>]<BR> number seven (from the seven कुलाचलs). cf. … अथ पन्नगे । नगाः<BR> अगाः पर्वतेऽर्के पादपे स्यात् … । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगात्मजा, अगौकस्, अगज, अगजा, अगजानिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगात्मजा
अग + -आत्मजा ‘the daughter of the mountain’, N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगौकस्
अग + -ओकस् <i>m.</i> [अगः पर्वतः ओको यस्य]<BR>—1 a mountain-dweller.<BR>—2 a bird (वृक्षवासी).<BR>—3 the animal शरभ supposed to have 8 legs.<BR>—4 a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगज|अगजं
अग + -ज <i>a.</i> (अगात् पर्वतशिलातो जायते; जन्-ड), produced on<BR> a mountain or from a tree; roaming or wandering through mountains, wild<BR> (गिरिचर); कचाचितौ विष्वगिवागजौ गजौ Ki. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगजम्
अग + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) bitumen. [शिलाजित]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगजा
अग + -जा Born From the mountain, Pārvatī. अगजाननपद्मार्कं गजाननमहर्निशम् ।<BR> अनेकदं तं भक्तानामेकदन्तमुपास्महे ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगजानिः
अग + -जानिः Śiva. सर्वं तद्भगवन् त्वदीयमगजाजाने समस्तार्तिहन् ।<BR> चोलचम्पूकाव्य p. 9, Verse 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगच्छ|अगच्छः|अगछ
अगच्छ <i>a.</i> [गम् बाहु˚ श, न˚ त˚] Not going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगच्छः|अगच्छ|अगछ
अगच्छ + .{@-च्छः@} A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगण्डः
अगण्डः A trunk without hands and feet,<BR> … (कुम्भकर्णः) … अगण्डभूतो विवृतो दावदग्ध इव द्रुमः Rām. 6. 68. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगण्य|अगण्यं
अगण्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Countless, immense; ˚पण्यविस्तारितमणि Dk. 1.<BR>—2 Not deserving to be counted (अर्हे यत्); worthless, immaterial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगतिः|अगति
अगतिः <i>f.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Want of resort or recourse; necessity.<BR>—2 Want of access (lit. & fig.); अगतिस्तत्र रामस्य यत्र गमिष्यामि<BR> विहायसा Rām.; मनोरथानामगतिर्न विद्यते Ku. 5. 64. See under गति.<BR>—3 Evil path; अगतिश्च गतिश्चैव लोकस्य विदिता तव Mb. 12. 16. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगतिक
अगति(ती)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Helpless, without any resort or resource; बालमेनमगतिमादाय<BR> Dk. 9; दण्डस्त्वगतिका गतिः Y. 1. 346.<BR>—2 The last resource or shift; अगतिका गतिर्ह्येषा पापा राजोपसेविनाम् ।<BR> v. l. अगतीकगतीनस्मान्नष्टार्थानर्थसिद्धये Mb. 12. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगतीक
अगति(ती)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Helpless, without any resort or resource; बालमेनमगतिमादाय<BR> Dk. 9; दण्डस्त्वगतिका गतिः Y. 1. 346.<BR>—2 The last resource or shift; अगतिका गतिर्ह्येषा पापा राजोपसेविनाम् ।<BR> v. l. अगतीकगतीनस्मान्नष्टार्थानर्थसिद्धये Mb. 12. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगद|अगदः
अगद <i>a.</i> [नास्ति गदो रोगो यस्य]<BR>—1 Healthy, sound, free from disease, in good health नरोऽगदः Ms. 8. 107.<BR>—2 (गद् भाषणे-अच्, न˚ त˚) Not speaking or telling.<BR>—3 Free from judicial affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदः|अगद
अगद + .{@-दः@} [नास्ति गदो रोगो यस्मात्]<BR>—1 A medicine, a medicinal drug; इति चिन्ताविषघ्नोऽयमगदः किं न पीयते<BR> H. Pr. 29; विषघ्नैरगदैश्चास्य सर्वद्रव्याणि योजयेत् Ms. 7. 218.<BR>—2 Health, freedom from disease; औषधान्यगदो विद्या देवी च विविधा स्थितिः ।<BR> तपसैव प्रसिध्यन्ति तपस्तेषां हि साधनम् ॥ Ms. 11. 237. (अगदः<BR> गदाभावः नैरुज्यमिति यावत् Kull.)<BR>—3 The science of antidotes; one of the 8 parts of medical science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदराजः|अगदराज
अगद + .{@-राजः@} good medicine; श्रेयस्तनोत्यगदराज इवोपयुक्तः Bhāg. 10. 47. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदंकारः|अगदङ्कार|अगदंकार|अगदङ्कारः
अगदंकारः [अगदं करोति; अगद कृ-अण् मुमागमश्च; कारे सत्यागदस्य;<BR> P. VI. 3. 70] A physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगद्यति
अगद्यति Den. P. To have good health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम|अगमः
अगम <i>a.</i> = अग q. v. बभूवुरगमाः सर्वे मारुतेन विनिर्धुताः<BR> Rām. 5. 14. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्य|अगम्यं
अगम्य <i>a.</i> [न गन्तुमर्हति गम्-यत्; न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not fit to be walked in or approached, unapproachable, inaccessible<BR> (lit. & fig.); योगिनामप्यगम्यः &c.<BR>—2 Inconceivable, incomprehensible; मनसोऽगम्य ईश्वरः God transcends<BR> mind (conception or thought); याः सम्पदस्ता मनसोऽप्यगम्याः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">Page0012-2</a>]<BR> Śi. 3. 59; see under गम्य also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगम्यरूप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यरूप
अगम्य + -रूप <i>a.</i> of unsurpassed or inconceivable nature, form, &c.<BR> ˚रूपां पदवीं प्रपित्सुना Ki. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्या
अगम्या A woman not deserving to be approached (for cohabitation),<BR> one of the low castes; ˚म्यां च स्त्रियं गत्वा, ˚गमनं चैव जातिभ्रंशकराणि वा &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगम्यागमनम्, अगम्यागामिन्, अगम्यागमनीय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यागमनम्
अगम्या + -गमनम् illicit intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यागामिन्
अगम्या + -गामिन् <i>a.</i> practising illicit intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यागमनीय
अगम्या + -गमनीय <i>a.</i> relating to illicit intercourse; ˚नीये तु<BR> (पापम्) व्रतैरेभिरपानुदेत् Ms. 11. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरी
अगरी [नास्ति गरो विषं यस्याः; प˚ ब˚ गौर˚ ङीष्]<BR>—1 A kind of grass or plant (देवताड वृक्ष) commonly called Deotar,<BR> Andropogon Serratus. It is said to be an antidote against the poison of rats and mice.<BR>—2 Any substance that removes poison (विषहारिद्रव्यमात्रम्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरु
अगरु <i>n.</i> [न गिरति; गॄ-उ. न˚ त˚] Agallochum,<BR> Amyris Agallocha. a kind of चन्दन; also अगुरु; संचारिते चागुरुसारयोनौ<BR> धूपे समुत्सर्पति वैजयन्तीः R. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगर्दभः
अगर्दभः A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगव्यूति
अगव्यूति <i>a.</i> Ved. Without good pasture grounds for cattle, barren<BR> (क्षेत्रम्) अगव्यूति क्षेत्रमागन्म देवाः Rv. 6. 47. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्ति|अगस्तिः
अगस्ति [विन्ध्याख्यम् अगम् अस्यति; अस्-क्तिच् शकन्ध्वादि˚, Uṇ. 4. 179,<BR> or अगं विन्ध्याचलं स्त्यायति स्तभ्नाति, स्त्यै-क; or अगः कुम्भः<BR> तत्र स्त्यानः संहतः इत्यगस्त्यः]<BR>—1 ‘Pitcher-born’, N. of a celebrated Ṛṣi or sage.<BR>—2 N. of the star Canopus, of which Agastya is the regent.<BR>—3 N. of a plant (बकवृक्ष) Sesbana (or AEschynomene) Grandiflora<BR> [Mar. रुईमंदार]. [The sage Agastya is a very reputed personage in<BR> Hindu mythology. In the Ṛgveda he and Vasiṣṭha are said to be the<BR> off-springs of Mitra and Varuṇa, whose seed fell from them at the sight<BR> of the lovely nymph Urvaśī at a sacrificial session. Part of the seed<BR> fell into a jar and part into water; from the former arose Agastya, who<BR> is, therefore, called Kumbhayoni, Kumbhajanman, Ghaṭodbhava, Kalaśayoni<BR> &c.; from the latter Vasiṣṭha. From his parentage Agastya is also called<BR> Maitrāvaruṇi, Aurvaśeya, and, as he was very small when he was born,<BR> he is also called Mānya. He is represented to have humbled the Vindhya<BR> mountains by making them prostrate themselves before him when they tried<BR> to rise higher and higher till they wellnigh occupied the sunʼs disc and<BR> obstructed his path. See Vindhya. (This fable is supposed by some, to<BR> typify the progress of the Āryas towards the south in their conquest and<BR> civilization of India, the humbling of the mountain standing metaphorically<BR> for the removal of physical obstacles in their way). He is also known<BR> by the names of Pītābdhi, Samudra-chuluka &c.; from another fable according<BR> to which he drank up the ocean because it had offended him and because<BR> he wished to help Indra and the gods in their wars with a class of demons<BR> called Kāleyas who had did themselves in the waters and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">Page0013-1</a>]<BR> oppressed the three worlds in various ways. His wife was Lopāmudrā.<BR> She was also called Kauṣītakī and Varapradā. She bore him two sons,<BR> Dṛḍhāsya and Dṛḍhāsyu. In the Rāmāyaṇa Agastya plays a distinguished<BR> part. He dwelt in a hermitage on mount Kunjara to the south of the Vindhya<BR> and was chief of the hermits of the south. He kept under control the evil<BR> spirits who infested the south and a legend relates how he once ate up<BR> a Rākṣasa named Vātāpi, who had assumed the form of a ram, and destroyed<BR> by a flash of his eye the Rākṣasaʼs brother who attempted to avenge<BR> him. In the course of his wanderings Rāma with his wife and brother came<BR> to the hermitage of Agastya who received him with the greatest kindness<BR> and became his friend, adviser and protector. He gave Rāma the bow of<BR> Viṣṇu and accompanied him to Ayodhyā when he was restored to his kingdom<BR> after his exile of 14 years. The superhuman power which the sage possessed,<BR> is also represented by another legend, according to which he turned king<BR> Nahuṣa into a serpent and afterwards restored him to his proper form.<BR> In the south he is usually regarded as the first teacher of science and<BR> literature to the primitive Dravidian tribes, and his era is placed by<BR> Dr. Caldwell in the 7th or 6th century B. C. The Purāṇas represent<BR> Agastya as the son of Pulastya (the sage from whom the Rākṣasas sprang)<BR> and Havirbhuvā the daughter of Kardama. Several ‘hymn-seers’ are mentioned<BR> in his family, such as his two sons, Indrabāhu, Mayobhuva and Mahendra,<BR> also others who served to perpetuate the family. The sage is represented<BR> as a great philosopher, benevolent and kind-hearted, unsurpassed in the<BR> science of archery and to have taken a principal part in the colonization<BR> of the south; निर्जितासि मया भद्रे शत्रुहस्तादमर्षिणा । अगस्त्येन दुराधर्षा<BR> मुनिना दक्षिणेव दिक् ॥ Rām.; अगस्त्याचरितामाशाम् R. 4. 44; cf. also;<BR> अगस्त्यो दक्षिणामाशामाश्रित्य नभसि स्थितः । वरुणस्यात्मजो योगी विन्ध्यवातापिमर्दनः ॥<BR> and R. 6. 61; Mv. 7. 14.] अगस्तितुल्या हि घृताब्धिशोषणे । Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0012-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्ती
अगस्ती A female descendant of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यः|अगस्त्य
अगस्त्यः<BR>—1 = अगस्ति See above.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगस्त्योदयः, अगस्त्यगीता, अगस्त्यचारः, अगस्त्यतीर्थम्, अगस्त्यवटः, अगस्त्यसंहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्योदयः|अगस्त्योदय
अगस्त्यः + -उदयः<BR>—1 the rise of Canopus which takes place about the end of Bhādra; with<BR> the rise of this star the waters become clear; cf. प्रससादोदयादम्भः<BR> कुम्भयोनेर्महौजसः. R. 4. 21.<BR>—2 the 7th day of the dark half of Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यगीता
अगस्त्यः + -गीता [अगस्त्येन गीता विद्याभेदः] N. of a sort of विद्या<BR> mentioned in the Mb. Śāntiparvan; (pl.) Agastyaʼs hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यचारः|अगस्त्यचार
अगस्त्यः + -चारः [ष˚ त˚] the course of Canopus, the time of its<BR> rise which ushers the Śarad season and then every thing on earth assumes<BR> a lovely appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यतीर्थम्
अगस्त्यः + -तीर्थम् N. of a celebrated Tīrtha in the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यवटः|अगस्त्यवट
अगस्त्यः + -वटः N. of a holy place on the Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्यसंहिता
अगस्त्यः + -संहिता Agastyaʼs collection of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगा
अगा <i>a.</i> Ved. Not going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाध|अगाधं|अगाधः
अगाध <i>a.</i> [गाध्-प्रतिष्ठायां घञ्; न˚ ब˚] Unfathomable,<BR> very deep, bottomless; अगाधसलिलात्समुद्रात् H. 1. 52; (fig.) profound,<BR> sound, very deep, यस्य ज्ञानदयासिन्धोरगाधस्यानघा गुणाः Ak. unfathomable,<BR> incomprehensible, inscrutable, Not learned; अगाधाश्चाप्रतिष्ठाश्च गतिमन्तश्च<BR> नारद Mb. 12. 286. 7 Not established, well-known; अगाधजन्मामरणं<BR> च राजन् Mb. 12. 308. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधः|अगाध|अगाधं
अगाध + .{@-धः, -धम्@} a deep hole or chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधम्
अगाध + .{@-धः, -धम्@} a deep hole or chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधः|अगाध|अगाधं
अगाध + .{@-धः@} N. of one of the 5 fires at the स्वाहाकार [cf. Gr. <i>agathos</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगाधजलः, अगाधसत्त्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधजलः|अगाधजल
अगाध + -जलः [अगाधं जलं यत्र] a deep pool or pond, deep lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधसत्त्व
अगाध + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> possessing profound inherent power. द्विजमुख्यतमः<BR> कविर्बभूव प्रथितः शूद्रक इत्यगाधसत्त्वः ॥ Mk. 1. 3, अगाधसत्त्वो<BR> मगधप्रतिष्ठः । R. 6. 21;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधज्ञानम्
अगाध + -सत्त्व + ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः <i>a.</i> so ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः; great; as ˚भयम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधबुद्धिः|अगाधबुद्धि
अगाध + -सत्त्व + ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः <i>a.</i> so ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः; great; as ˚भयम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधभयम्
अगाध + -सत्त्व + ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः <i>a.</i> so ˚ज्ञानम्, ˚बुद्धिः; great; as ˚भयम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगारम्
अगारम् [अगं न गच्छन्तम् ऋच्छति प्राप्नोति अग-ऋ-अण् Tv.] A house;<BR> शून्यानि चाप्यगाराणि Ms. 9. 265;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगारम्
अगारम् + ˚दाहिन् an incendiary अगारदाही<BR> गरदः 3. 158. See आगार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिरः|अगिर
अगिरः (नः ?) [न गीर्यते दुःखेन; गॄ- बा˚ क.<BR> न˚ त˚ Tv.]<BR>—1 Heaven.<BR>—2 The sun or fire ?<BR>—3 A Rākṣasa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगिरौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिनः|अगिन
अगिरः (नः ?) [न गीर्यते दुःखेन; गॄ- बा˚ क.<BR> न˚ त˚ Tv.]<BR>—1 Heaven.<BR>—2 The sun or fire ?<BR>—3 A Rākṣasa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगिरौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिरौकस्
अगिरः + -ओकस् <i>a.</i> [अगिरः स्वर्गः ओको वासस्थानं यस्य] dwelling<BR> in the heaven (as a god); जीराश्चिदगिरौकसः Rv. 1. 135. 9; not to<BR> be stopped by threatening shouts (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगु|अगुः
अगु <i>a.</i> [नास्ति गौर्यस्य] Ved.<BR>—1 Destitute of cows or rays; poor. उक्थं चन शस्यमानमगोः Rv. 8. 2. 14.<BR>—2 Wicked (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुः|अगु
अगु + .{@-गुः@}<BR>—1 N. of Rāhu.<BR>—2 Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुण|अगुणः
अगुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Destitute of attributes (referring to God).<BR>—2 Having no good qualities, worthless; अगुणो ऽयमकोशः M. 3, गुणयुक्तो<BR> दरिद्रोऽपि नेश्वरैरगुणैः समः ॥ Mk. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणः|अगुण
अगुण + .{@-णः@} [न˚ त˚] A fault, defect, demerit, vice; तद्वः<BR> सर्वं प्रवक्ष्यामि प्रसवे च गुणागुणान् Ms. 3. 22; गुणागुणज्ञ knowing<BR> merit and demerit; लोभश्चेदगुणेन किम् Bh. 2. 55; अगुणेषु तस्य<BR> धियमस्तवतः Ki. 6. 21 vices;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणम्
अगुण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Absolution (मोक्ष, कैवल्य); धर्मादयः किमगुणेन च काङ्क्षितेन<BR> Bhāg. 7. 6. 25.<BR>—2 Supreme Being (परब्रह्म).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगुणवादिन्, अगुणशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणवादिन्
अगुण + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> fault-finding, censorious, not appreciating merits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणशील
अगुण + -शील <i>a.</i> of a worthless character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरु|अगुरुः
अगुरु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not heavy, light.<BR>—2 (In prosody) Short.<BR>—3 Having no teacher.<BR>—4 One different from a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरु|अगुरुः
अगुरु + .{@-रु@} <i>n.</i> (<i>m.</i> also) [न गुरुर्यस्मात्]<BR>—1 The fragrant aloe wood and tree; Aquiluria Agallocha.<BR>—2 That which yields Bdellium, Amyris Agallocha.<BR>—3 The Śiśu tree (शिंशपा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अगुरुशिंशपा, अगुरुसारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरुशिंशपा
