अग्रवातः
अग्र + -वातः fresh breeze; अग्रवातमासेवमाना M. 1<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रशोभा
अग्र + -शोभा towering beauty or the beauty of the peaks; कैलासशैलस्य<BR> यदग्रशोभाम् । Bu. C. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसंधानी|अग्रसन्धानी
अग्र + -संधानी [अग्रे फलोत्पत्तेः प्राक् संधीयते ज्ञायते ऽनया कार्यम्<BR> Tv.] the register of human actions kept by Yama (यत्र हि प्राणिवर्गस्य<BR> प्राग्भवीयकर्मानुसारेण शुभाशुभसूचकं सर्वं लिख्यते सा यमपञ्जिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसन्ध्या|अग्रसंध्या
अग्र + -सन्ध्या early dawn; कर्कन्धूनामुपरि तुहिनं रञ्जयत्यग्रसन्ध्या Ś. 4, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसर|अग्रसरः
अग्र + -सर = यायिन् taking the lead; आयोधनाग्रसरतां त्वयि वीर<BR> याते R. 5. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसारा
अग्र + -सारा [अग्रं शीर्षमात्रं सारो यस्याः सा]<BR>—1 a sprout which has tips without fruits.<BR>—2 a short method of counting immense numbers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहर
अग्र + -हर <i>a.</i> [अग्रे ह्रियते दीयतेऽसौ; हृ-अच्]<BR>—1 that which must be given first.<BR>—2 = अग्रहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहस्त|अग्रहस्तः
अग्र + -हस्त (˚कर; ˚पाणिः), the forepart of the hand or arm; अग्रहस्तेन<BR> गृहीत्वा प्रसादयैनाम् Ratn. 3; forepart of the trunk (of an elephant);<BR> often used for a finger or fingers taken collectively; शीतलस्ते ˚स्तः<BR> Mk. 3; अतिसाध्वसेन वेपते मे ˚स्तः Ratn. 1; कुसुमित इव ते ˚स्तः<BR> प्रतिभाति M. 1; प्रसारिते ˚स्ते M. 4; ˚हस्तात्प्रभ्रष्टं पुष्पभाजनम्<BR> Ś. 4 slipped from the fingers; also the right hand; अथ ˚हस्ते मुकुलीकृताङ्गुलौ<BR> Ku. 5. 63. (अग्रश्चासौ हस्तश्च Malli.). Ki. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रकर|अग्रकरः
अग्र + -हस्त (˚कर; ˚पाणिः), the forepart of the hand or arm; अग्रहस्तेन<BR> गृहीत्वा प्रसादयैनाम् Ratn. 3; forepart of the trunk (of an elephant);<BR> often used for a finger or fingers taken collectively; शीतलस्ते ˚स्तः<BR> Mk. 3; अतिसाध्वसेन वेपते मे ˚स्तः Ratn. 1; कुसुमित इव ते ˚स्तः<BR> प्रतिभाति M. 1; प्रसारिते ˚स्ते M. 4; ˚हस्तात्प्रभ्रष्टं पुष्पभाजनम्<BR> Ś. 4 slipped from the fingers; also the right hand; अथ ˚हस्ते मुकुलीकृताङ्गुलौ<BR> Ku. 5. 63. (अग्रश्चासौ हस्तश्च Malli.). Ki. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपाणिः|अग्रपाणि
अग्र + -हस्त (˚कर; ˚पाणिः), the forepart of the hand or arm; अग्रहस्तेन<BR> गृहीत्वा प्रसादयैनाम् Ratn. 3; forepart of the trunk (of an elephant);<BR> often used for a finger or fingers taken collectively; शीतलस्ते ˚स्तः<BR> Mk. 3; अतिसाध्वसेन वेपते मे ˚स्तः Ratn. 1; कुसुमित इव ते ˚स्तः<BR> प्रतिभाति M. 1; प्रसारिते ˚स्ते M. 4; ˚हस्तात्प्रभ्रष्टं पुष्पभाजनम्<BR> Ś. 4 slipped from the fingers; also the right hand; अथ ˚हस्ते मुकुलीकृताङ्गुलौ<BR> Ku. 5. 63. (अग्रश्चासौ हस्तश्च Malli.). Ki. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहायनः|अग्रहायन
अग्र + -हायनः (णः) [अग्रः श्रेष्ठः हायनो व्रीहिः अत्र, णत्वम्]<BR> the beginning of the year; N. of the month मार्गशीर्ष; (मासानां<BR> मार्गशीर्षोऽहम् Bg. 10. 35); ˚इष्टिः नवशस्येष्टिर्यागभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहारः|अग्रहार
अग्र + -हारः<BR>—1 a grant of land given by kings (to Brāhmaṇas) for sustenance (अग्रं<BR> ब्राह्मणभोजनं, तदर्थं ह्रियन्ते राजधनात् पृथक् क्रियन्ते ते क्षेत्रादयः<BR> नीलकण्ठ; क्षेत्रोत्पन्नशस्यादुद्धृत्य ब्राह्मणोद्देशेन स्थाप्यं धान्यादि,<BR> गुरुकुलादावृत्तब्रह्मचारिणे देयं क्षेत्रादि, ग्रामभेदश्च Tv.); अग्रहारांश्च<BR> दास्यामि ग्रामं नगरसंमितम् Mb. 3. 64. 4. कस्मिंश्चिदग्रहारे Dk. 8. 9.<BR>—2 the first offering in वैश्वदेव Mb. 3. 234. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतः
अग्रतः <i>adv.</i> [अग्रे अग्राद्वा, अग्र-तसिल्] (with gen.)<BR>—1 Before (opp. पृष्टतः), in front of, at the head of; forward; अग्रतश्चतुरो<BR> वेदान् पृष्टतः सशरं घनुः । इदं ब्राह्ममिदं क्षात्रं शापादपि शरादपि ॥<BR> Subhāṣ. न गणस्याग्रतो गच्छेत् H. 1. 29. गच्छाग्रतः lead<BR> the way; ˚तो विलोक्य seeing before him.<BR>—2 In the presence of; मेघनादस्य˚ Pt. 1; अमात्यस्याग्रतः Mu. 5;<BR> धनुर्भृतामग्रत एव रक्षिणाम् R. 3. 39 in the very presence of.<BR>—3 First; पुरुषं जातमग्रतः Rv. 10. 20. 7; अग्रतः कृ to give<BR> precedence to, consider most important; to put in front or at the head<BR> of पुरस्तात्प्रथमे प्राच्यां पुरोऽर्थेऽग्रत इत्यपि Nm. 4. From; तदग्रतः<BR> स्वकर्मस्थं स्मृत्वा Rām. 6. 79. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अग्रतःसर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतःसर|अग्रतःसरः
अग्रतः + -सर <i>a.</i> [अग्रतः सरति; सृ-ट] going in front, taking the lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतःसरः|अग्रतःसर
अग्रतः + -सर + .({@-रः@}) a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिम|अग्रिमः
अग्रिम <i>a.</i> [अग्रे भवः; अग्र-डिमच् P. IV. 3. 23. Vārt.]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">Page0020-2</a>]<BR>—1 First (in order, rank &c.); foremost, best, excellent, preferable,<BR> superior; वीराणामग्रिमो भूत्वा युयुधे पार्थिवैः सह Mb.<BR>—2 Prior, preceding.<BR>—3 Elder, eldest.<BR>—4 Furthest, advanced, first ripe. —5 Further.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिमः|अग्रिम
अग्रिम + .{@-मः@} An elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिमा
अग्रिम + .{@-मा@} A kind of fruit, Annona Reticulata. (Mar. रामफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिय|अग्रियं|अग्रियः
अग्रिय <i>a.</i> [अग्रे भवः; अग्र-घ] Foremost, best &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रियः|अग्रिय|अग्रियं
अग्रिय + .{@-यः@} An elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रियम्
अग्रिय + .{@-यम्@} The first fruits; the best part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रीय|अग्रीयं
अग्रीय <i>a.</i> [अग्रे-भवः; अग्र-छ] Foremost, best &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रे
अग्रे <i>adv.</i><BR>—1 In front of, before (in time or space); अग्रे यान्ति रथस्य रेणुपदवीं … घनाः<BR> V. 1. 5, 2. 7; R. 2. 56; Bh. 3. 36.<BR>—2 In the presence of, before; ममाग्रे स्तुवन्ति H. 1; तं मे त्वमग्रहीरग्रे<BR> वृणोमि त्वामहं ततः Mb. 1. 81. 21.<BR>—3 At the head, ahead; बलाग्रे तिष्ठते वीरो नलः Rām.<BR>—4 Further on, subsequently, in the sequel; एवमग्रे वक्ष्यते, एवमग्रेऽपि<BR> द्रष्टव्यम् &c.<BR>—5 In the beginning; at first, first; प्रतापोऽग्रे ततः शब्दः परागस्तदनंतरम्<BR> R. 4. 30; आत्मैवेदमग्र आसीत् Bṛ. Ār. Up. 4. 1. 1; Ms. 2. 169.<BR>—6 First, in preference to others; सवर्णाग्रे द्विजातीनां प्रशस्ता दारकर्मणि<BR> Ms. 3. 12. अतिथिभ्योऽग्र एवैतान् भोजयेत् 3. 114.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अग्रेगः, अग्रेगाः, अग्रेगूः, अग्रेदिधिषुः, अग्रेदिधिषूः, अग्रेपाः, अग्रेपूः, अग्रेवनम्, अग्रेणम्, अग्रेसर, अग्रेसरिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगः|अग्रेग
अग्रे + -गः a leader; सेनाग्रगः Rām. 7. 35. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगाः
अग्रे + -गाः going in front or before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगूः
अग्रे + -गूः Going in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषुः|अग्रेदिधिषु
अग्रे + -दिधिषुः, -दिधिषूः a man (of one of the first three castes) who marries<BR> a wife married before (पुनर्भूविवाहकारी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषूः
अग्रे + -दिधिषुः, -दिधिषूः + .({@-षूः@}) <i>f.</i> a married woman whose elder sister is still unmarried<BR> (ज्येष्टायां यद्यनूढायां कन्यायामुह्यतेऽनुजा । सा चाग्रेदिधिषूर्ज्ञेया पूर्वा<BR> च दिधिषूः स्मृता); ˚पतिः the husband of such a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषूः
अग्रे + -दिधिषुः, -दिधिषूः + .({@-षूः@}) <i>f.</i> a married woman whose elder sister is still unmarried<BR> (ज्येष्टायां यद्यनूढायां कन्यायामुह्यतेऽनुजा । सा चाग्रेदिधिषूर्ज्ञेया पूर्वा<BR> च दिधिषूः स्मृता); ˚पतिः the husband of such a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषुपतिः|अग्रेदिधिषुपति
अग्रे + -दिधिषुः, -दिधिषूः + .({@-षूः@}) <i>f.</i> a married woman whose elder sister is still unmarried<BR> (ज्येष्टायां यद्यनूढायां कन्यायामुह्यतेऽनुजा । सा चाग्रेदिधिषूर्ज्ञेया पूर्वा<BR> च दिधिषूः स्मृता); ˚पतिः the husband of such a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषूपतिः|अग्रेदिधिषूपति
अग्रे + -दिधिषुः, -दिधिषूः + .({@-षूः@}) <i>f.</i> a married woman whose elder sister is still unmarried<BR> (ज्येष्टायां यद्यनूढायां कन्यायामुह्यतेऽनुजा । सा चाग्रेदिधिषूर्ज्ञेया पूर्वा<BR> च दिधिषूः स्मृता); ˚पतिः the husband of such a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेपाः
अग्रे + -पाः [अग्रे स्थित्वा पाति, अलुक्] first to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेपूः
अग्रे + -पूः [अग्रे पूयते, पू-क्विप्] purifying in oneʼs presence; having<BR> precedence in drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेवनम्
अग्रे + -वनम्, -णम् [वनस्याग्रं राजदन्ता˚ पूर्वनिपातः; अलुक् णत्वम्<BR> P. VIII. 4. 4.] the border or skirt of a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेणम्
अग्रे + -वनम्, -णम् [वनस्याग्रं राजदन्ता˚ पूर्वनिपातः; अलुक् णत्वम्<BR> P. VIII. 4. 4.] the border or skirt of a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसर|अग्रेसरः
अग्रे + -सर <i>a.</i> [अग्रमग्रेणाग्रे वा सरति सृ. ट. अलुक्-पुरोऽग्रतोऽग्रेषु<BR> सर्त्तेः । P. III. 2. 18.] going in front, taking the lead, a leader,<BR> foremost, first; निरपत्रपाणाम् अग्रेसरीकृतास्मि K. 169; मरण˚रो<BR> भवामि Pt. 1; Māl. 9 first to die; मानमहतामग्रेसरः केसरी Bh. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसरिकः|अग्रेसरिक
अग्रे + -सरिकः [अग्रेसरे अग्रगतौ प्रसृतः ठन्]<BR>—1 a servant (who precedes his master).<BR>—2 a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्य|अग्र्यः
अग्र्य <i>a.</i> [अग्रे जातः, अग्र-यत्] —1 Foremost, best, choicest,<BR> most essential or important, highest, pre-eminent, first; तदङ्गमग्र्यं<BR> मघवन् महाक्रतोः R. 3. 46; ˚महिषी 10. 66; उपेयुषः स्वामपि<BR> मूर्तिमग्त्याम् 6. 73, 8. 28, 14. 19, 18. 39; Ku. 7. 78; Ms. 5. 166, 12. 30;<BR> अद्याहं पुत्रिणामग्र्यः V. 5. 14: also with loc.; अग्त्याःसर्वेषु<BR> वेदेषु Ms. 3. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्यः|अग्र्य
अग्र्य + .{@-ग्र्यः@} An elder brother<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्यम्
अग्र्य + .{@-ग्र्यम्@} The roof of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्या
अग्र्य + .{@-ग्र्या@} The tree myrobalans (Mar. त्रिफळा or a mixture of हिरडा,<BR> बेहडा, आंवळकाठी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अग्र्यतपस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्यतपस्
अग्र्य + -तपस् N. of a muni; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभण
अग्रभण <i>a.</i> Ved. Having nothing acceptable; अनारम्भणे तदवीरयेथामनास्थाने<BR> अग्रभणे समुद्रे । Rv. 1. 116. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रह|अग्रहः
अग्रह <i>a.</i> Without any escort, retinue etc. A vānaprastha etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राम्य
अग्राम्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not rustic or rural, town-made; अग्राम्यशब्दाभिधानमौदार्यम् Kau. A. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Not tame, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0020-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राह्य|अग्राह्यं
अग्राह्य <i>a.</i> Not acceptable, that which ought not to be taken or<BR> accepted as a gift, present &c.; ˚ह्यम् शिवनिर्माल्यं पत्रं पुष्पं फलं<BR> जलम्; not to be perceived, admitted or trusted; not to be considered<BR> or taken into account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राह्या
अग्राह्य + .{@-ह्या@} N. of the clay or मृत्तिका which ought not to be taken<BR> for purposes of purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रुः|अग्रु
अग्रुः, -ग्रूः <i>f.</i><BR> [अङ्ग-क्रु नलोपः वा ऊङ्] Ved.<BR>—1 A finger.<BR>—2 A river; सप्त स्वसारो अग्रुवः Rv. 1. 191. 14. (according to others)<BR> single, unmarried (as a young woman); Rv. 5. 44. 7, 7. 96. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रूः
अग्रुः, -ग्रूः <i>f.</i><BR> [अङ्ग-क्रु नलोपः वा ऊङ्] Ved.<BR>—1 A finger.<BR>—2 A river; सप्त स्वसारो अग्रुवः Rv. 1. 191. 14. (according to others)<BR> single, unmarried (as a young woman); Rv. 5. 44. 7, 7. 96. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्
अघ् = अङ्घ् q. v. ━(€10 U.) To wrong, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ|अघं|अघः
अघ <i>a.</i> [अघ्-कर्तरि अच्] —1 Bad, sinful, evil, wicked; अघायुरिन्द्रियारामो<BR> मोघं पार्थ स जीवति Bg. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघम्
अघ + .{@-घम्@} [अघ् भावे अच्]<BR>—1 Sin; अघं स केवलं भुङ्क्ते यः पचत्यात्मकारणात् Ms. 3. 118; Bg. 3. 13;<BR> अघौघविध्वंसविधौ पटीयसीः Śi. 1. 18, हरत्यघं सम्प्रति<BR> हेतुरेष्यतः 26; ˚मर्षण &c.; misdeed, fault, crime; श्रेयान् द्विजातिरिव<BR> हन्तुमघानि दक्षम् Śi. 4. 37 sins and griefs also.<BR>—2 An evil, mishap, misfortune, accident, injury, harm; न वधूष्वघानि<BR> विमृशन्ति धियः Ki. 6. 45 do not think of doing harm or evil; क्रियादघानां<BR> मघवा विघातम् 3. 52; अघोपघातं मघवा विभूत्यै 11. 80; प्रजानां<BR> तमघावहम् R. 15. 51, 19. 52; see अनघ.<BR>—3 Impurity (अशौचम्); अनुरुन्ध्यादघं त्र्यहम् Ms. 5. 63; न वर्धयेदघाहानि 84.<BR> न राज्ञामघदोषोऽस्ति 93;<BR>—4 Pain, suffering, grief, distress; उपप्लुतमघौघेन नात्मानमवबुद्धयसे<BR> Rām. 2. 7. 14; Mb. 3. 237. 19; Bhāg. 1. 14. 20. दयालुमनघस्पृष्टम्<BR> R. 10. 19 not subject to grief.<BR>—5 Passion. cf. अंहोदुःखव्यसनेष्वघम् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघः|अघ|अघं
अघ + .{@-घः@} N. of a demon, brother of Baka and Pūtanā and commander-in-chief<BR> of Kaṃsa. [Being sent by Kaṃsa to Gokula to kill Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma<BR> he assumed the form of a huge serpent 4 yojanas long, and spread himself<BR> on the way of the cowherds, keeping his horrid mouth open. The cowherds<BR> mistook it for a mountain cavern and entered it, cows and all. But Kṛṣṇa<BR> saw it, and having entered the mouth so stretched himself that he tore<BR> it to pieces and rescued his companions.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघा
अघ + .{@-घा@} The Goddess of sin; (pl.) the constellation usually called Maghā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अघासुरः, अघाहः, अघायुस्, अघकृत्, अघघ्नः, अघनाश, अघनाशन, अघभोजिन्, अघमर्षण, अघमार, अघरुद्, अघविषः, अघशंसः, अघशंसिन्, अघहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघासुरः|अघासुर
अघ + -असुरः See अघ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघाहः|अघाह
अघ + -अहः (अहन्) a day of impurity (अशौ चदिनम्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघायुस्
अघ + -आयुस् <i>a.</i> leading a wicked life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघकृत्
अघ + -कृत् <i>a.</i> sinful, wicked, evil-doer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघघ्नः|अघघ्न
अघ + -घ्नः = ˚नाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशनः|अघनाशन
अघ + -घ्नः = ˚नाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाश
अघ + -नाश, -नाशन <i>a.</i> [अघं नाशयति] expiatory, destroying<BR> sin (such as gifts, muttering holy prayers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशनः|अघनाशन
अघ + -नाश, -नाशन + .({@-नः@}) destroyer of the demon अघ; N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशन|अघनाशनः
अघ + -नाश, -नाशन <i>a.</i> [अघं नाशयति] expiatory, destroying<BR> sin (such as gifts, muttering holy prayers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघभोजिन्
अघ + -भोजिन् <i>a.</i> [अघं पापफलकं भुङ्क्ते] a sinful eater (one<BR> who cooks and eats for his own sake and not for Gods, Manes guests &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमर्षण|अघमर्षणं
अघ + -मर्षण <i>a.</i> [अघं मृष्यते उत्पन्नत्वेऽपि नाशनेन कर्माक्षमत्वात्<BR> सह्यते अनेन मृष्-ल्युट्] expiatory, removing or destroying sin, usually<BR> applied to a prayer (सन्ध्या) repeated by Brāhmaṇas (the 190th hymn<BR> of Rv. 10.); सर्वैनसामपध्वंसि जप्यं त्रिष्वघमर्षणं Ak.; यथाश्वमेधः<BR> क्रतुराट् सर्वपापापनोदनः । तथाघमर्षणं सूक्तं सर्वपापप्रणाशनम् ॥<BR> The most heinous crimes, such as illicit intercourse with a preceptorʼs<BR> wife, oneʼs own mother, sister, daughter-in-law &c. are said to be expiated<BR> by repeating this<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">Page0021-2</a>]<BR> सूक्त thrice in water; पवित्राण्यघमर्षणानि जपन्त्याम् K. 179, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमार
अघ + -मार <i>a.</i> [अघं मारयति नाशयति; मृ णिच्-अण्] destroying<BR> sin, an epithet of Gods (यमो मृत्युरघमारो निरृतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघरुद्
अघ + -रुद् <i>a.</i> [अघं रोदिति स्वकर्माक्षमतया यस्मात्, रुद्-अपादाने क्विप्]<BR>—1 ‘making sin weep and fly’, N. of a Mantra which destroys sin; fearfully howling (?).<BR>—2 [अघे व्यसने रोदिति न तत्प्रतीकाराय घटते, क्विप्] one who only<BR> weeps in times of calamity, but does not try to get over them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघविषः|अघविष
अघ + -विषः [अघं व्यसनकारि विषं यस्य] a serpent; fearfully venomous (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघशंसः|अघशंस
अघ + -शंसः [अघस्य शंसः; शंस् भावे अच्]<BR>—1 indication or reporting of sin.<BR>—2 [अघम् अनिष्टं शंसति इच्छति; शंस्-अण्] a wicked man, such as a thief.<BR>—3 wicked; sin-destroying (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघशंसिन्
अघ + -शंसिन् <i>a.</i> reporting or telling oneʼs sin or guilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघहारः|अघहार
अघ + -हारः a noted robber; rumour of guilt (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघन
अघन <i>a.</i> Not solid, a hollow moulding; घनं वाप्यघनं वापि<BR> कुर्यात्तु शिल्पवित्तमः Māna. 62. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनमानम्
अघन + .{@-मानम्@} Measurement by the interior of a structure; एवं तद्<BR> घनमानमुक्तमघनमानं वक्ष्यतेऽधुना Māna. 33. 331-35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघल
अघल <i>a.</i> [अघं लाति नाशयति ला-क] Destroying sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघायति
अघायति Den. P. To sin, to be malicious; to threaten with ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघायु
अघायु <i>a.</i> Malicious, wicked, sinful, harmful, injurious; अघायुरिन्द्रियारामो<BR> मोघं पार्थ स जीवति Bg. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघारिन्
अघारिन् <i>a.</i> [अघं व्यसनम् ऋच्छति; ऋ-णिनि] Suffering from evil<BR> or calamity (व्यसनयुक्त) not anointing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्म|अघर्म्म
अघर्म <i>a.</i> Not hot, cold;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्मांशु
अघर्म + {@˚अंशु, ˚धामन्@} the moon whose rays are cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्मधामन्|अघर्म्मधामन्
{Circular ref 274.004}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोर|अघोरः
अघोर <i>a.</i> Not terrific or fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरः|अघोर
अघोर + .{@-रः@} [नास्ति घोरो यस्मात्]<BR>—1 N. of Śiva or of one of his forms, (ईशानाघोरनामानौ वामदेवस्ततः<BR> परम् । सद्योजात इति प्रोक्तः क्रमशोऽर्चनकर्मणि ॥)<BR>—2 A worshipper of Śiva and Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरा
अघोर + .{@-रा@} [अघोरः शिवः उपास्यत्वेन अस्यां सा, अघोर-अच्] The fourteenth<BR> day of the dark half of Bhādra sacred to Śiva (भाद्रमास्यसिते पक्षे<BR> ह्यघोराख्या चतुर्दशी । तस्यामाराधितः स्थाणुर्नयेच्छिवपुरं ध्रुवम् ॥).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अघोरघोररूपः, अघोरपथः, अघोरमार्गः, अघोरप्रमाणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरघोररूपः|अघोरघोररूप
अघोर + -घोररूपः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरपथः|अघोरपथ
अघोर + -पथः, -मार्गः a follower of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरमार्गः|अघोरमार्ग
अघोर + -पथः, -मार्गः a follower of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरप्रमाणम्
अघोर + -प्रमाणम् a terrific oath or ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोष|अघोषः
अघोष <i>a.</i> [नास्ति घोषो यस्य यत्र वा]<BR>—1 Hard-sounding. See below.<BR>—2 Devoid of cow-herds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोषः|अघोष
अघोष + .{@-षः@} The hard sound of a consonant, hollowness of sound with which<BR> all hard consonants and the Visarga are pronounced (one of the 11 kinds<BR> of बाह्यप्रयत्न. See P. VIII. 2. 1.) or the consonants so pronounced<BR> (खयां यमाः खयः Zक-Vपौ विसर्गः शर एव च । एते श्वासानुप्रदाना<BR> अघोषाश्च विवृण्वते ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोस्
अघोस् <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle, another form अघवन् (Ved.) P. VIII. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्न्य|अघ्न्यः
अघ्न्य <i>a.</i> Not to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्न्यः|अघ्न्य
अघ्न्य + .{@-घ्न्यः@} [न हन्ति सृष्टिकर्तृत्वात् न हन्-यक् निपातः Tv.]<BR>—1 Brahmā (अघ्न्यः प्रजापतिः Uṇ. 4. 111.)<BR>—2 A Bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्न्या
अघ्न्य + .{@-घ्न्या@} [न हन्यते स्त्रीहत्यायाः निषिद्धत्वात्] A cow; त्रिः<BR> सप्त नामाघ्न्या बिभर्ति Rv. 7. 87. 4; Mb. 12. 262. 47; अघ्न्यः इति गवां<BR> नाम क एतां हन्तुमर्हति cf. ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0021-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्रेय
अघ्रेय <i>a.</i> Not fit to be smelt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्रेयम्
अघ्रेय + .{@-यम्@} Liquor (मद्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क्|अंक्
अङ्क्^1 €1 Ā. (अङ्कते) To move in a curve. €10 U. (अङ्कयति-ते अङ्कयितुम्)<BR>—1 To mark, stamp; हेमपादाङ्कितायां पीठिकायाम् K. 192; स्वनामधेयाङ्कित<BR> Ś. 4 stamped with his name; नयनोदबिन्दुभिः अङ्कितं स्तनांशुकम्<BR> V. 4. 7 so भुजे शचीपत्रविशेषकाङ्किते R. 3. 55, 68.<BR>—2 To enumerate, count.<BR>—3 To brand, stain, stigmatize; तत्को नाम गुणो भवेत्सुगुणिनां यो दुर्जनैर्नाङ्कितः<BR> Bh. 2. 54 branded, censured, condemned; वस्त्रेण वेष्टयित्वा ˚तं शिरः<BR> Ks. 13. 152 branded head.<BR>—4 To walk, stalk, go.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: missing virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कः|अङ्क|अंक|अंकः
अङ्कः [अङ्क् कर्तरि करणे वा अच्]<BR>—1 The lap (<i>n.</i> also); अङ्काद्ययावङ्कमुदीरिताशीः Ku. 7. 5 passed<BR> from lap to lap.<BR>—2 A mark, sign; अलक्तकाङ्कां पदवीं ततान R. 7. 7; पदपङ्क्तिरलक्ताङ्का<BR> Rām.; रतिवलयपदाङ्के कण्ठे Ku. 2. 64 marked with the signs or<BR> traces &c.; मद्गोत्राङ्कं गेयम् Me. 86, a stain, spot, stigma, brand;<BR> इन्दोः किरणेष्विवाङ्कः Ku. 1. 3; कट्यां कृताङ्को निवस्यिः Ms. 8. 281.<BR>—3 A numerical figure; a number; the number 9.<BR>—4 A side flank; proximity, reach (connected with 1 above); समुत्सुकेवाङ्कमुपैति<BR> सिद्धिः Ki. 3. 40; प्रेम्णोपकण्ठं मुहुरङ्कभाजो रत्नावलीरम्बुधिराबबन्ध<BR> Śi. 3. 36; सिंहो जम्बुकमङ्कमागतमपि त्यक्त्वा निहन्ति द्विपम् Bh. 2. 30;<BR> Ki. 17. 64; see -आगत below.<BR>—5 An act of a drama, for its nature &c.; see S. D. 278.<BR>—6 A hook or curved instrument.<BR>—7 A species of dramatic composition, one of the ten varieties of रूपक. See S. D. 519.<BR>—8 An ornament (भूषा).<BR>—9 A sham fight, military show (चित्रयुद्ध).<BR>—10 A coefficient.<BR>—11 A place; नानाङ्कचिह्नैर्नवहेमभाण्डैः (तुरङ्गैः) Bu. C. 2. 4.<BR>—12 A sin, misdeed.<BR>—13 A line, curved line; a curve or bend generally, the bend in the arm.<BR>—14 The body.<BR>—15 A mountain. अङ्कः स्थानान्तिकक्रोडभूषणोत्संगलक्ष्मसु । मन्तो नाटकविच्छेदे<BR> चित्रयुद्धे च रूपके ॥ Nm. [cf. L. <i>uncus</i>; Gr. <i>ogkos</i>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्काङ्कम्, अङ्कावतारः, अङ्कागत, अङ्कगत, अङ्ककरणम्, अङ्कतन्त्रम्, अङ्कधारणम्, अङ्कधरणा, अङ्कपरिवर्तः, अङ्कपादव्रतम्, अङ्कपालिः, अङ्कपाली, अङ्कपाशः, अङ्कपूरणम्, अङ्कबन्धः, अङ्कभाज्, अङ्कमुखम्, अङ्कलोड्यः, अङ्कलोपः, अङ्कविध्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्काङ्कम्
अङ्कः + -अङ्कम् [अङ्के मध्ये अङ्काः शतपत्रादिचिह्नानि यस्य Tv.] water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कावतारः|अङ्कावतार|अंकावतार
अङ्कः + -अवतारः when an act, hinted by persons at the end of the preceding<BR> act, is brought in continuity with the latter, it is called अङ्कावतार<BR> (descent of an act), as the sixth act of Śākuntala or second of Mālavikāgnimitra<BR> (अङ्कान्ते सूचितः पात्रैस्तदङ्कस्याविभागतः । यत्राङ्कोवतरत्येषोऽङ्कावतार<BR> इति स्मृतः S. D. 311). The Daśarūpa defines it differently; अङ्कावतारस्त्वङ्कान्ते<BR> पातोऽङ्कस्याविभागतः । एभिः संसूचयेत्सूच्यं दृश्यमङ्कैः प्रदर्शयेत् 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कागत
अङ्कः + -आगत, -गत <i>a.</i> [द्वि˚ त˚] come within the grasp;<BR> सिंहत्वं ˚सत्त्ववृत्तिः R. 2. 18; श्रियं युवाप्यङ्कगतामभोक्ता R. 13. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कगत
अङ्कः + -आगत, -गत <i>a.</i> [द्वि˚ त˚] come within the grasp;<BR> सिंहत्वं ˚सत्त्ववृत्तिः R. 2. 18; श्रियं युवाप्यङ्कगतामभोक्ता R. 13. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ककरणम्
अङ्कः + -करणम् marking, branding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कतन्त्रम्
अङ्कः + -तन्त्रम् the science of numbers (arithmetical or algebraical).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कधारणम्
अङ्कः + -धारणम्, -धरणा<BR>—1 bearing or having marks, such as those on the body of a Vaiṣṇava.<BR>—2 manner of holding the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कधरणा
अङ्कः + -धारणम्, -धरणा<BR>—1 bearing or having marks, such as those on the body of a Vaiṣṇava.<BR>—2 manner of holding the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपरिवर्तः|अङ्कपरिवर्त|अंकपरिवर्त
अङ्कः + -परिवर्तः [स˚ त˚]<BR>—1 turning on the other side.<BR>—2 rolling or dallying in the lap or on the person; अपि कर्णजाहविनिवेशिताननः<BR> प्रियया तदङ्कपरिवर्तमाप्नुयाम् Māl. 5. 8. (an occasion for) embrace<BR> (अङ्के क्रोडे सर्वतोभावेन वर्तनं हृदयालिङ्गनम् इत्यर्थः जगद्धर);<BR> so ˚परिवर्तिन्; भर्तुः ˚नी भव M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपरिवर्तिन्
अङ्कः + -परिवर्तः [स˚ त˚]<BR>—1 turning on the other side.<BR>—2 rolling or dallying in the lap or on the person; अपि कर्णजाहविनिवेशिताननः<BR> प्रियया तदङ्कपरिवर्तमाप्नुयाम् Māl. 5. 8. (an occasion for) embrace<BR> (अङ्के क्रोडे सर्वतोभावेन वर्तनं हृदयालिङ्गनम् इत्यर्थः जगद्धर);<BR> so ˚परिवर्तिन्; भर्तुः ˚नी भव M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपादव्रतम्
अङ्कः + -पादव्रतम् N. of a Vrata; title<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">Page0022-2</a>]<BR> of a chapter in the भविष्योत्तरपुराण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपालिः|अङ्कपालि|अंकपालि
अङ्कः + -पालिः, -पाली [पा-अलि ष˚ त˚ वा. ङीप्]<BR>—1 the extremity of region of the lap (क्रोडप्रान्त or प्रदेश);<BR> a seat in the lap; hence, an embrace; तावद्गाढं वितर सकृदप्यङ्कपालीं<BR> प्रसीद Māl. 8. 2. स्पृश हस्तेन मे हस्तमेहि देह्यङ्कपालिकाम् ।<BR> Śiva B. 21. 33.<BR>—2 [अङ्केन पालयति पाल्-इ. तृ˚ त˚] a nurse.<BR>—3<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाली|अंकपाली
अङ्कः + -पालिः, -पाली + ({@-ली@})<BR> a variety of plant, Piring or Medicago Esculenta; (Mar.<BR> धोत्रा निघण्टुरत्नाकर) [वेदिकाख्यगन्धद्रव्यम्]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाली|अंकपाली
अङ्कः + -पालिः, -पाली [पा-अलि ष˚ त˚ वा. ङीप्]<BR>—1 the extremity of region of the lap (क्रोडप्रान्त or प्रदेश);<BR> a seat in the lap; hence, an embrace; तावद्गाढं वितर सकृदप्यङ्कपालीं<BR> प्रसीद Māl. 8. 2. स्पृश हस्तेन मे हस्तमेहि देह्यङ्कपालिकाम् ।<BR> Śiva B. 21. 33.<BR>—2 [अङ्केन पालयति पाल्-इ. तृ˚ त˚] a nurse.<BR>—3<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाशः|अङ्कपाश|अंकपाश
अङ्कः + -पाशः [अङ्कः पाश इव बन्धनेनेव पातनहेतुर्यत्र Tv.] an<BR> operation in arithmetic by which a peculiar concatenation or chain of<BR> numbers is formed by making the figures 1, 2 &c. exchange places (स्थानान्तमेकादिचयाङ्कघातः<BR> संख्याविभेदा नियतैः स्युरङ्कैः । भक्तोऽङ्कमित्याङ्कसमासनिघ्नः स्थानेषु<BR> युक्तो मितिसंयुतिः स्यात् ॥ See Līlā. 240); (न गुणो न हरो न कृतिर्न<BR> घनः पृष्टस्तथापि दुष्टानाम् । गर्वितगणकवहूनां स्यात् पातोऽवश्यमङ्कपाशेऽस्मिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपूरणम्
अङ्कः + -पूरणम् multiplication of numbers of figures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कबन्धः|अङ्कबन्ध
अङ्कः + -बन्धः forming the lap, bending the thighs into a curve and<BR> squatting down.<BR>—2 branding with a mark that resembles a headless trunk (अशिरःपुरुषाकारोऽङ्कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कभाज्|अंकभाज्
अङ्कः + -भाज् [अङ्कं भजते उप˚ स˚]<BR>—1 seated in the lap or carried on the hip, as an infant.<BR>—2 being within easy reach, drawing near, soon to be obtained; अविरहितमनेकेनाङ्कभाजा<BR> फलेन Ki. 5. 52.<BR>—3 premature, early ripe, forced fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कमुखम्
अङ्कः + -मुखम् (or आस्यम्) that part of an act, wherein the subject<BR> of all the acts is intimated, is called अङ्कमुख, which suggests the<BR> <i>germ</i> as well as the <i>end</i>; <i>e. g.</i> in Māl. 1 कामन्दकी and<BR> अवलोकिता hint the parts to be played by भूरिवसु and others and<BR> give the arrangement of the plot in brief (यत्र स्यादङ्क एकस्मिन्नङ्कानां<BR> सूचनाखिला । तदङ्कमुखमित्याहुर्बीजार्थख्यापकं च तत् ॥ S. D. 322.)<BR> The Daśarūpa defines it thus: अङ्कान्तपौत्ररङ्कास्यं छिन्नाङ्कस्यार्थसूचनात् ।<BR> <i>i. e.</i> where a character at the end of an act cuts short the story<BR> and introduces the beginning of another act; as in the second of Mv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कलोड्यः|अङ्कलोड्य
अङ्कः + -लोड्यः [अङ्केन लोड्यते असौ] a kind of tree (Mar. चिंचोट), ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कलोपः|अङ्कलोप
अङ्कः + -लोपः subtraction of numbers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कविध्या
अङ्कः + -विध्या the science of numbers, arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कनम्
अङ्कनम् [अङ्क-करणे भावे वा ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A mark, token; स्नेहाङ्कनानि Māl. 9. 46; marks of love.<BR>—2 Act of marking.<BR>—3 Means of marking, stamping, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कसम्
अङ्कसम् [अङ्कोऽस्मिन्नस्ति-अच्] Having marks, trappings (?) (वस्त्रम्<BR> आप्रपदिकम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्किन्|अंकिन्
अङ्किन् <i>m. n.</i> [अङ्कः आलिङ्गनस्थानत्वेन अस्यास्ति, अङ्क-इनि]<BR> A sort of drum or tabor (अङ्केनालिङ्ग्य वादनीयो मृदङ्गादिवाद्यभेदः क्रीडाविशिष्टश्च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्किनी
अङ्किन् + .{@-नी@} [अङ्कानां समूहः; खलादि˚ इनि ङीप्]<BR>—1 A number of marks or signs.<BR>—2 A woman having marks (of branding &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क्य|अंक्य|अङ्क्यः
अङ्क्य <i>a.</i> [अङ्क्-ण्यत्] Fit to be branded, marked or counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क्यः|अङ्क्य|अंक्य
अङ्क्य + .{@-क्यः@} [अङ्के क्रोडे स्थापयित्वा वाद्यते असौ, यत्, or अङ्के सावुः,<BR> अङ्क्-य] A sort of drum or tabor (सार्धतालत्रयायामश्च चतुर्दशाङ्गुलाननः ।<BR> हरीतक्याकृतिर्यः स्यादङ्क्योङ्के स हि वाद्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कतिः|अङ्कति|अंकति|अंकतिः
अङ्कतिः [अञ्च्-गतौ अति कुत्वं; अञ्चेः को वा Uṇ. 4. 61; अङ्कतिः अञ्चतिर्वा]<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 Brahmā.<BR>—4 A Brāhmaṇa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">Page0023-1</a>]<BR> who keeps the sacred fire, अग्निहोत्रिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कतिः|अङ्कति|अंकति|अंकतिः
अङ्कतिः + .{@-तिः, -ती@} <i>f.</i> Going; one who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कती
अङ्कतिः + .{@-तिः, -ती@} <i>f.</i> Going; one who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0022-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कस्|अंकस्
अङ्कस् <i>n.</i> [अञ्च्-असुन् कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 A mark.<BR>—2 The body.<BR>—3 a curve or bend; पथामङ्कांस्यन्वापनीफणत् Rv. 4. 40. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कित|अङ्कितः
अङ्कित <i>a.</i> marked, branded; स्वाहास्वधावषट्कारैरङ्कितं मेषवाहनम्<BR> numbered, calculated, counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुटः|अङ्कुट|अंकुट|अंकुटः
अङ्कुटः (ety. ?) A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुपम्
अङ्कुपम् Ved. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरः|अङ्कुर|अंकुर|अंकुरं|अंकुरः
अङ्कुरः, -रम्<BR> [अङ्क्-ऊर्च् Uṇ. 1. 38]<BR>—1 A sprout, shoot, blade; दर्भाङ्कुरेण चरणः क्षतः Ś. 2. 12;<BR> ‘a little bloomed flower’; स नानाकुसुमैः कीर्णः कपिः साङ्कुरकोरकैः<BR> Rām. 5. 1. 49. oft. in comp. in the sense of ‘pointed’, ‘sharp’ &c.;<BR> मकरवक्त्रदंष्ट्राङ्कुरात् Bh. 2. 4 pointed jaws; नृसिंहस्य नखाङ्कुरा<BR> इव K. 4 pointed nails; कुरण्टकविपाण्डुरं दधति धाम दीपाङ्कुराः<BR> Vb. 4. 1; पतङ्गपवनव्यालोलदीपाङ्कुरच्छायाचञ्चलम् Bh. 3. 68 unsteady<BR> like the pointed flame of a lamp; (fig.) scion, offspring, progeny; अनेन<BR> कस्यापि कुलाङ्कुरेण Ś. 7. 19 sprout or child of some one; अन्वयाङ्कुरम् Dk. 6<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 Blood.<BR>—4 A hair.<BR>—5 A tumour, swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरम्
अङ्कुरः, -रम्<BR> [अङ्क्-ऊर्च् Uṇ. 1. 38]<BR>—1 A sprout, shoot, blade; दर्भाङ्कुरेण चरणः क्षतः Ś. 2. 12;<BR> ‘a little bloomed flower’; स नानाकुसुमैः कीर्णः कपिः साङ्कुरकोरकैः<BR> Rām. 5. 1. 49. oft. in comp. in the sense of ‘pointed’, ‘sharp’ &c.;<BR> मकरवक्त्रदंष्ट्राङ्कुरात् Bh. 2. 4 pointed jaws; नृसिंहस्य नखाङ्कुरा<BR> इव K. 4 pointed nails; कुरण्टकविपाण्डुरं दधति धाम दीपाङ्कुराः<BR> Vb. 4. 1; पतङ्गपवनव्यालोलदीपाङ्कुरच्छायाचञ्चलम् Bh. 3. 68 unsteady<BR> like the pointed flame of a lamp; (fig.) scion, offspring, progeny; अनेन<BR> कस्यापि कुलाङ्कुरेण Ś. 7. 19 sprout or child of some one; अन्वयाङ्कुरम् Dk. 6<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 Blood.<BR>—4 A hair.<BR>—5 A tumour, swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरित|अंकुरित
अङ्कुरित (अङ्कूरित) <i>a.</i> [अङ्कुरा अस्य सञ्जाताः, तारका˚ इतच्]<BR>—1 Having sprouts; ˚तं मनसिजेनेव V. 1. 13 as if Love has put forth sprouts.<BR>—2 Blotched, having boils on the skin; निद्रालुरङ्कूरितहस्तलक्ष्यः<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 2; ˚घर्मसलिलः Dk. 125 with drops of perspiration<BR> bursting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूरित
अङ्कुरित (अङ्कूरित) <i>a.</i> [अङ्कुरा अस्य सञ्जाताः, तारका˚ इतच्]<BR>—1 Having sprouts; ˚तं मनसिजेनेव V. 1. 13 as if Love has put forth sprouts.<BR>—2 Blotched, having boils on the skin; निद्रालुरङ्कूरितहस्तलक्ष्यः<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 2; ˚घर्मसलिलः Dk. 125 with drops of perspiration<BR> bursting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरकः|अङ्कुरक|अंकुरकः
अङ्कुरकः [अङ्क्यते तृणादिना संचीयतेऽसौ; अञ्च्-घुरच् ततः क]<BR> An abode of birds, animals; a nest (of birds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशः|अङ्कुश|अंकुश|अंकुशः
अङ्कुशः [अङ्क्-लक्षणे उशच् Uṇ. 4. 107] A hook, a goad; Proverb:<BR> विक्रीते करिणि किमङ्कुशे विवादः why higgle about a trifling thing<BR> when the whole bargain (of which it forms part) has been struck; the goad<BR> ought to follow the elephant; संनिवेश्य कुशावत्यां रिपुनागाङ्कुशं कुशम्<BR> R. 15. 97; (fig.) one who checks, a corrector, governor, director; त्यजति<BR> तु यदा मोहान्मार्गं तदा गुरुरङ्कुशः Mu. 3. 6; कुशं द्विषामङ्कुशम्<BR> R. 16. 81; (= Preventor) सिद्धेः पूर्वोऽङ्कुशस्त्रिविधा Sāṅ. K. 51.<BR> a restraint or check; निरङ्कुशाः कवयः poets have free license or<BR> are unfettered; pinching; पादावकर्षसन्धानैस्तोमराङ्कुशलासनैः Mb. 7. 142. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशी
अङ्कुशः + .{@-शी@} one of the 24 Jaina Goddesses. [cf. Germ. <i>angel</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्कुशग्रहः, अङ्कुशदुर्धरः, अङ्कुशधारिन्, अङ्कुशमुद्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशग्रहः|अङ्कुशग्रह|अंकुशग्रह
अङ्कुशः + -ग्रहः an elephant-driver; अन्वेतुकामोऽवमताङ्कुशग्रहः Śi. 12. 16<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशदुर्धरः|अङ्कुशदुर्धर|अंकुशदुर्धर
अङ्कुशः + -दुर्धरः [तृ˚ त˚ अङ्कुशेन दुःखेन धार्यते] a restive elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशधारिन्
अङ्कुशः + -धारिन् <i>m.</i> a keeper of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशमुद्रा
अङ्कुशः + -मुद्रा [अङ्कुशाकारा मुद्रा] a mark resembling a goad in form<BR> (ऋज्वीं च मध्यमां कृत्वा तन्मध्यं पर्वमूलतः । तर्जनीं किञ्चिदाकुञ्चेत्<BR> सा मुद्राङ्कुशसंज्ञिता ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशित
अङ्कुशित <i>a.</i> [इतच्] Urged on by a hook, goaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशिन्|अंकुशिन्
अङ्कुशिन् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे इनि] Having a hook or goad; laying hold<BR> of with a hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूयत्|अंकूयत्|अङ्कूयन्त्
अङ्कूयत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Moving tortuously to escape यमङ्कूयन्तमानयन्<BR> Rv. 6. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूरः|अङ्कूर|अंकूर|अंकूरः
अङ्कूरः [अङ्क्-खर्जूरादित्वात् ऊरच्] A sprout. See अङ्कुर; दशरथकुलाङ्कूरमाद्यम् Mv. 6. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूषः|अङ्कूष|अंकूष|अंकूषः
अङ्कूषः [अङ्क्-ऊषच्] = अङ्कुश q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोटः|अङ्कोट|अंकोट|अंकोटः
अङ्कोटः, -ठः, -लः<BR> [अङ्क्यते लक्ष्यते कीलाकारकण्टैः; अङ्क् ओट-ठ -ल]<BR> N. of a tree (Mar. पिस्ता), Alangium Hexapetalum; अङ्कोलाश्च कुरण्टाश्च<BR> Rām. 4. 1. 80. Walnut (Mar. अक्रोड); अङ्कोलैर्भव्यतिनिशैः Rām. 2. 99. 8.<BR> so अङ्कोलकः, स्वार्थे कन्; अङ्कोलिका.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्कोटसार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोठः|अङ्कोठ|अंकोठ
अङ्कोटः, -ठः, -लः<BR> [अङ्क्यते लक्ष्यते कीलाकारकण्टैः; अङ्क् ओट-ठ -ल]<BR> N. of a tree (Mar. पिस्ता), Alangium Hexapetalum; अङ्कोलाश्च कुरण्टाश्च<BR> Rām. 4. 1. 80. Walnut (Mar. अक्रोड); अङ्कोलैर्भव्यतिनिशैः Rām. 2. 99. 8.<BR> so अङ्कोलकः, स्वार्थे कन्; अङ्कोलिका.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्कोटसार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोलः|अङ्कोल|अंकोल
अङ्कोटः, -ठः, -लः<BR> [अङ्क्यते लक्ष्यते कीलाकारकण्टैः; अङ्क् ओट-ठ -ल]<BR> N. of a tree (Mar. पिस्ता), Alangium Hexapetalum; अङ्कोलाश्च कुरण्टाश्च<BR> Rām. 4. 1. 80. Walnut (Mar. अक्रोड); अङ्कोलैर्भव्यतिनिशैः Rām. 2. 99. 8.<BR> so अङ्कोलकः, स्वार्थे कन्; अङ्कोलिका.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्कोटसार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोटसार
अङ्कोटः + -सार a sort of poison prepared from the Aṅkola plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोलिका|अंकोलिका
अङ्कोलिका (probably a corruption of अङ्कपालिका) An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ख्|अंख्
अङ्ख् €10 P. (अङ्गयति)<BR>—1 To crawl.<BR>—2 To cling.<BR>—3 To check, hold back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग्|अंग्
अङ्ग् €1 P. (अङ्गति, आङ्ग, अङ्गितुम्) To go, walk.<BR> €10 P.<BR>—1 To walk, go round.<BR>—2 To mark (cf. अङ्क्). ━<i>With</i> {@परि (पलि)@} to stir up. ━{@विपलि@}<BR> to envelop, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle meaning ‘well’, ‘well, sir’, ‘indeed’,<BR> ‘true’; ‘assent’ (as in अङ्गीकृ); अङ्ग कच्चित्कुशली तातः K. 221;<BR> प्रभुरपि जनकानामङ्ग भो याचकस्ते Mv. 3. 5; अङ्ग अस्ति कश्चिद्विमर्दको<BR> नामात्रभवतः Dk. 59; अङ्ग कुरु, अङ्ग पच P. VIII. 1. 33. Sk.;<BR> अङ्गाधीष्व भक्तं तव दास्यामि P. VIII. 2. 96 Sk; समनद्ध किमङ्ग<BR> भूपतिः Śi. 16. 34, 2. 12; यदि मनसि शमः किमङ्गचापम् Ki. 10. 55, 13. 65;<BR> used with किम् in the sense of ‘how much less’, or ‘how much more’<BR>; शक्तिरस्ति कस्यचिद्विदेहराजस्य छायामप्यवस्कन्दितुं किमङ्ग<BR> जामातरम् Mv. 3; तृणेन कार्यं भवतीश्वराणां किमङ्ग वाघस्तवता<BR> नरेण Pt. 1. 71. Lexicographers give the following senses of अङ्गः-क्षिप्रे<BR> च पुनरर्थे च सङ्गमासूययोस्तथा । हर्षे संबोधने चैव ह्यङ्गशब्दः<BR> प्रयुज्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गम्
अङ्गम् [अम् गत्यादौ बा˚ गन्; according to Nir. अङ्ग, अङ्गनात् अञ्चनात् वा]<BR>—1 The body.<BR>—2 A limb or member of the body; शेषाङ्गनिर्माणविधौ विधातुः Ku. 1. 33;<BR> क्लेशस्याङ्गमदत्वा Pt. 5. 32 without undergoing troubles; इति<BR> स्वप्नोपमान्मत्वा कामान्मा गास्तदङ्गताम् । Ki. 11. 34 do not be influenced<BR> or swayed by them (do not be subject to them)<BR>—3 (<i>a</i>) A division or department (of anything), a part or portion,<BR> as of a whole; as सप्ताङ्गम् राज्यम्, चतुरङ्गम् बलम्, चतुःषष्ट्यङ्गम्<BR> ज्योतिःशास्त्रम् see the words; गीताङ्गानाम् Pt. 5. 56; यज्ञश्चेत्प्रतिरुद्धःस्यादेकेनाङ्गेन<BR> यज्वनः Ms. 11. 11. (Hence) (<i>b</i>) A supplementary or auxiliary portion,<BR> supplement; षडङ्ग or साङ्ग वेदः A peculiar use of the word<BR> अङ्ग in masculine gender may here be noted वेदांश्चैव तु वेदाङ्गान्<BR> वेदान्तानि तथा स्मृतीः । अधीत्य ब्राह्मणः पूर्वं शक्तितोऽन्यांश्च संपठेत्<BR> Bṛhadyogiyājñavalkya Smṛti 12. 34. (<i>c</i>) A constituent part, essential<BR> requisite or component; सर्वैर्बलाङ्गैः R. 7. 59; तदङ्गमग्र्यं<BR> मघवन् महाक्रतो R. 3. 46. (<i>d</i>) An attributive or secondary part;<BR> secondary, auxiliary or dependent member (serving to help the principal<BR> one) (opp. प्रधान or अङ्गिन्); अङ्गी रौद्ररसस्तत्र सर्वेऽङ्गानि<BR> रसाः पुनः S. D. 517; अत्र स्वभावोक्तिरुत्प्रेक्षांङ्गम् Malli. on Ki. 8. 26.<BR> (<i>e</i>) An auxiliary means or expedient (प्रधानोपयोगी उपायः<BR> or उपकरणम्); सर्वकार्यशरीरेषु मुक्त्वाङ्गस्कन्धपञ्चकम् । मन्त्रो<BR> योध इवाधीर सर्वाङ्गैः संबृतैरपि ॥ Śi. 2. 28-29; see अङ्गाङ्गि,<BR> पञ्चाङ्ग also (<i>the angas</i> of the several sciences<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">Page0024-1</a>]<BR> or departments of knowledge will be given under those words).<BR>—4 (Gram.). A name for the base of a word; यस्मात्प्रत्ययविधिस्तदादिप्रत्यये<BR> अङ्गम् P. I. 4. 13; यः प्रत्ययो यस्मात्क्रियते तदादिशब्दस्वरूपं तस्मिन्प्रत्यये<BR> परे अङ्गसंज्ञं स्यात् Sk. The अङ्ग terminations are those of the<BR> nominative, and accusative singular and dual.<BR>—5 (Drama) (<i>a</i>) One of the sub-divisions of the five joints or sandhis<BR> in dramas; the मुख has 12, प्रतिमुख 13, गर्भ 12, विमर्ष 13<BR> and उपसंहार 14, the total number of the <i>angas</i> being thus 64;<BR> for details see the words. (<i>b</i>) The whole body of subordinate characters.<BR>—6 (astr.) A name for the position of stars (लग्न). See अङ्गाधीश.<BR>—7 A symbolical expression for the number six (derived from the six Vedāngas).<BR>—8 The mind; हिरण्यगर्भाङ्गभुवं मुनिं हरिः Śi. 1. 1; see अङ्गज also.<BR>—9 N. of the chief sacred texts of the jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गः|अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं
अङ्गम् + .{@-ङ्गः@} (pl.) N. of a country and the people inhabiting it, the<BR> country about the modern Bhāgalpur in Bengal. [It lay on the south of<BR> Kauśikī Kaccha and on the right bank of the Ganges. Its capital was<BR> Champā, sometimes called Aṅgapurī, Lomapādapurī, Karṇapurī or Mālinī.<BR> According to Daṇḍin (अङ्गेषु गङ्गातटे बहिश्चम्पायाः) and Hiouen<BR> Thsang it stood on the Ganges about 24 miles west of a rocky island. General<BR> Cunningham has shown that this description applies to the hill opposite<BR> Pātharghāṭā, that it is 24 miles east of Bhāgalpur, and that there<BR> are villages called Champanagar and Champapura adjoining the last. According<BR> to Sanskrit poets the country of the Aṅgas lay to the east of Girivraja,<BR> the capital of Magadha and to the north-east or south-east of Mithilā.<BR> The country was in ancient times ruled by Karṇa] cf. अङ्गं गात्रान्तिकोपाय<BR> प्रतीकेष्वप्रधानके । देशभेदे तु पुंसि स्यात् … ॥ Nm. <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Contiguous.<BR>—2 Having members or divisions.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्गाङ्गि, अङ्गाधिपः, अङ्गाधीशः, अङ्गापूर्वम, अङ्गकर्मन्, अङ्गक्रमः, अङ्गग्रहः, अङ्गज, अङ्गजात, अङ्गज्वरः, अङ्गदूषणम्, अङ्गद्वीपः, अङ्गन्यासः, अङ्गपालिः, अङ्गपालिका, अङ्गप्रायाश्चित्तम्, अङ्गभूः, अङ्गभङ्गः, अङ्गमन्त्रः, अङ्गमर्दः, अङ्गमर्षः, अङ्गयज्ञः, अङ्गयागः, अङ्गरक्तः, अङ्गरक्तम्, अङ्गरक्षकः, अङ्गरक्षणी, अङ्गरागः, अङ्गरुहम्, अङ्गलिपिः, अङ्गलेपः, अङ्गलोड्यः, अङ्गवस्त्रोत्था, अङ्गविकल, अङ्गविकृतिः, अङ्गविकारः, अङ्गविक्षेपः, अङ्गविद्या, अङ्गविधिः, अङ्गवीरः, अङ्गवैकृतम्, अङ्गवैगुण्यम्, अङ्गसंस्कारः, अङ्गसंस्क्रिया, अङ्गसंहतिः, अङ्गसंहिता, अङ्गसङ्गः, अङ्गसुप्तिः, अङ्गसेवकः, अङ्गस्कन्धः, अङ्गस्पर्शः, अङ्गहानिः, अङ्गहारः, अङ्गहारिः, अङ्गहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाङ्गि|अंगांगि
अङ्गम् + -अङ्गि, [अङ्गीभावः -अङ्गस्य अङ्गिनो भावः] the relation<BR> of a limb to the body, of the subordinate to the principal, or of that<BR> which is helped or fed to the helper or feeder (गौणमुख्यभावः, उपकार्योपकारकभावश्च);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> प्रयाज and other rites are to दर्श as its <i>angas</i>,<BR> while दर्श is to them the <i>aṅgi</i>; अङ्गाङ्गिभावमज्ञात्वा कथं<BR> सामर्थ्यनिर्णयः । पश्य टिट्टिभमात्रेण समुद्रो व्याकुलीकृतः ॥ H. 2. 138;<BR> अत्र वाक्ये समासगतयोरुपमयोः साध्यसाधनभावात् ˚वेन सम्बन्धः<BR> Malli. on Ki. 6. 2; अविश्रान्तिजुषामात्मन्यङ्गाङ्गित्वं तु संकरः K. P. 10.<BR> (अनुग्राह्यानुग्राहकत्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाधिपः|अङ्गाधिप|अंगाधिप
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाधीशः|अङ्गाधीश
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराजः|अङ्गराज|अंगराज
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपतिः|अङ्गपति
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गेश्वरः|अङ्गेश्वर|अंगेश्वर
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाधीश्वरः|अङ्गाधीश्वर
अङ्गम् + -अधिपः, -अधीशः<BR>—1 ‘lord of the Aṅgas’, N. of Karṇa (cf. ˚राजः, ˚पतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚अधीश्वरः).<BR>—2 ‘lord of a लग्न’, the planet presiding over it; (अङ्गाधिपे बलिनि<BR> सर्वविभूतिसम्पत्; अङ्गाधीशः स्वगेहे बुधगुरुकविभिः संयुतो वीक्षितो वा Jyotiṣa.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गापूर्वम
अङ्गम् + -अपूर्वम effect of a secondary sacrificial act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गकर्मन्|अङ्गकर्म्मन्
अङ्गम् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-क्रिया@}<BR>—1 besmearing the body with fragrant cosmetics, rubbing it &c. Dk. 39.<BR>—2 a supplementary sacrificial act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गक्रमः|अङ्गक्रम
अङ्गम् + -क्रमः the order of the performance with reference to the अङ्गs.<BR> The rule in this connection is that the अङ्गकम must conform to the<BR> मुख्यक्रम. cf. MS. 5. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गग्रहः|अङ्गग्रह
अङ्गम् + -ग्रहः spasm; seizure of the body with some<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">Page0024-2</a>]<BR> illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गज|अंगज|अङ्गजं|अङ्गजः
अङ्गम् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> [अङ्गात् जायते जन्-ड.]<BR>—1 produced from or on the body, being in or on the body, bodily; ˚जं<BR> रजः, ˚जाः अलङ्काराः &c.<BR>—2 produced by a supplementary rite.<BR>—3 beautiful, ornamental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गजात
अङ्गम् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> [अङ्गात् जायते जन्-ड.]<BR>—1 produced from or on the body, being in or on the body, bodily; ˚जं<BR> रजः, ˚जाः अलङ्काराः &c.<BR>—2 produced by a supplementary rite.<BR>—3 beautiful, ornamental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गजः|अङ्गज|अंगज|अङ्गजं
अङ्गम् + -ज, -जात + .({@-जः@}) {@-जनुस्@} also<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 hair of the body (<i>n.</i> also); तवोत्तरीयं करिचर्म साङ्गजम् Ki. 18. 32.<BR>—3 love, cupid (अङ्गं मनः तस्माज्जातः); intoxicating passion; अङ्गजरागदीपनात् Dk. 161.<BR>—4 drunkenness, intoxication.<BR>—5 a disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गजा|अंगजा
अङ्गम् + -ज, -जात + .({@-जा@}) a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गजम्
अङ्गम् + -ज, -जात + .({@-जम्@}) blood, अङ्गजं रुधिरेऽनङ्गे केशे पुत्रे मदे पुमान् । नागरे<BR> नखरेऽपि स्यात् … । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गज्वरः|अङ्गज्वर
अङ्गम् + -ज्वरः [अङ्गमङ्गम् अधिकृत्य ज्वरः] the disease called राजयक्ष्मा,<BR> a sort of consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गदूषणम्
अङ्गम् + -दूषणम्<BR>—1 the defects of the limbs; the penalties of a defective construction; Māna.<BR>—2 name of the 79th chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गद्वीपः|अङ्गद्वीप|अंगद्वीप
अङ्गम् + -द्वीपः one of the six minor Dvīpas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन्यासः|अङ्गन्यास|अंगन्यास
अङ्गम् + -न्यासः [अङ्गेषु मन्त्रभेदस्य न्यासः] touching the limbs<BR> of the body with the hand accompanied by appropriate Mantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपालिः|अङ्गपालि|अंगपालि
अङ्गम् + -पालिः <i>f.</i> [अङ्गं पाल्यते सम्बध्यतेऽत्र, अङ्ग-पाल्-इ] an<BR> embrace (probably a corruption of अङ्कपालि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपालिका|अंगपालिका
अङ्गम् + -पालिका = अङ्कपालि q. v. {@प्रत्यङ्गम्@} [समा˚ द्वन्द्व]<BR> every limb, large and small; ˚गानि पाणिना स्पृष्ट्वा K. 167, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गप्रायाश्चित्तम्
अङ्गम् + -प्रायाश्चित्तम् [अङ्गस्य शुद्धयर्थ प्रायश्चित्तम्] expiation<BR> of bodily impurity, such as that caused by the death of a relative, consisting<BR> in making presents (पञ्चसूनाजन्यदुरितक्षयार्थं कार्यं दानरूपं प्रायश्चित्तम् Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गभू|अंगभू
अङ्गम् + -भू^1 <i>a.</i> [अङ्गात् मनसो वा भवति; भू-क्विप्] born from the body or mind.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गभूः
अङ्गम् + -भूः + .({@-भूः@})<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 Cupid.<BR>—3 [अङ्गानाम् अङ्गमन्त्राणां भूः स्थानम्] one who has touched and purified,<BR> and then restrained, his limbs by repeating the Mantras pertaining to<BR> those limbs; ब्रह्माङ्गभूर्ब्रह्मणि योजितात्मा Ku. 3. 15 (सद्योजातादिमन्त्राणाम्<BR> अङ्गानां हृदयादिमन्त्राणां भूः स्थानं, कृतमन्त्रन्यासः Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गभङ्गः|अङ्गभङ्ग|अंगभंग
अङ्गम् + -भङ्गः<BR>—1 palsy or paralysis of limbs; ˚विकल इव भूत्वा स्थास्यामि Ś. 2.<BR>—2 twisting or stretching out of the limbs (as is done by a man just after<BR> he rises from sleep); साङ्गभङ्गमुत्थाय Vb.; जृम्भितैः साङ्गभङ्गैः<BR> Mu. 3. 21; K. 85.<BR>—3 The middle part of the anus and testicles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमन्त्रः|अङ्गमन्त्र
अङ्गम् + -मन्त्रः N. of a Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्दः|अङ्गमर्द|अंगमर्द|अङ्गमर्द्द|अङ्गमर्द्दः
अङ्गम् + -मर्दः [अङ्गं मर्दयति; मृद्-णिच्]<BR>—1 one who shampoos his masterʼs body.<BR>—2 [भावे घञ्] act of shampooing;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्दका
अङ्गम् + ˚मर्दका or ˚मर्दिन् (मृद्-णिच्<BR> ण्वुल् or णिनि) one who shampoos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्दः|अङ्गमर्द|अंगमर्द|अङ्गमर्द्द|अङ्गमर्द्दः
अङ्गम् + ˚मर्दका or ˚मर्दिन् (मृद्-णिच्<BR> ण्वुल् or णिनि) one who shampoos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्षः|अङ्गमर्ष|अंगमर्ष
अङ्गम् + -मर्षः [ष˚ त˚] rheumatism; ˚प्रशमनम् the curing<BR> of this disease. ˚मेजयत्वम् subtle throbbing of the body; Pātañjala S. 1. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गयज्ञः|अङ्गयज्ञ
अङ्गम् + -यज्ञः, -यागः [अङ्गीभूतः यज्ञः] a subordinate sacrificial<BR> act which is of 5 sorts: समिधो यजति, तनूनपातं यजति, इडो यजति,<BR> बर्हिर्यजति, स्वाहाकारं यजति इति पञ्चविधाः । एतेषां सकृदनुष्टानेनैव<BR> तन्त्रन्यायेन प्रधानयागानामाग्नेयादीनामुपकारितेति मीमांसा Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गयागः|अङ्गयाग
अङ्गम् + -यज्ञः, -यागः [अङ्गीभूतः यज्ञः] a subordinate sacrificial<BR> act which is of 5 sorts: समिधो यजति, तनूनपातं यजति, इडो यजति,<BR> बर्हिर्यजति, स्वाहाकारं यजति इति पञ्चविधाः । एतेषां सकृदनुष्टानेनैव<BR> तन्त्रन्यायेन प्रधानयागानामाग्नेयादीनामुपकारितेति मीमांसा Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्तः|अङ्गरक्त
अङ्गम् + -रक्तः, -रक्तम् [अङ्गे अवयवे रक्तः] N. of a plant गुडारोचनी<BR> found in काम्पिल्य country and having red powder (रक्ताङ्गलोचनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्तम्
अङ्गम् + -रक्तः, -रक्तम् [अङ्गे अवयवे रक्तः] N. of a plant गुडारोचनी<BR> found in काम्पिल्य country and having red powder (रक्ताङ्गलोचनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षकः|अङ्गरक्षक
अङ्गम् + -रक्षकः [अङ्गं रक्षति; रक्ष्-ण्वुल्] a body-guard, personal<BR> attendant Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षणी|अंगरक्षणी
अङ्गम् + -रक्षणी [अङ्गं रक्ष्यते अनया] a coat of mail, or a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षणम्
अङ्गम् + -रक्षणी + .({@-णम्@}) protection of person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरागः|अङ्गराग|अंगराग
अङ्गम् + -रागः [अङ्गं रज्यते अनेन करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 a scented cosmetic, application of perfumed unguents to the body, fragrant<BR> unguent; पुष्पगन्धेन अङ्गरागेण R. 12. 27, 6. 60, स्तनाङ्गरागात् Ku. 5. 11.<BR>—2 [भावे ल्युट्] act of anointing the body with unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरुहम्
अङ्गम् + -रुहम् [अङ्गे रोहति;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">Page0025-1</a>]<BR> रुह्-क स˚ त˚ P. III. 9. 135.] hair; मम वर्णो मणिनिभो मृदून्यङ्गरुहाणि<BR> च Rām. 6. 48. 12. विहङ्गराजाङ्गरुहैरिवायतैः Śi. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलिपिः|अङ्गलिपि
अङ्गम् + -लिपिः <i>f.</i> written character of the Aṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलेपः|अङ्गलेप
अङ्गम् + -लेपः [अङ्गं लिप्यते अनेन; लिप्-करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 a scented cosmetic.<BR>—2 [भावे घञ्] act of anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलोड्यः|अङ्गलोड्य
अङ्गम् + -लोड्यः (लोड ण्यत्) a kind of grass, ginger or its root, Amomum Zingiber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवस्त्रोत्था
अङ्गम् + -वस्त्रोत्था <i>f.</i> A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविकल
अङ्गम् + -विकल <i>a.</i> [तृ˚ त˚]<BR>—1 maimed, paralysed.<BR>—2 fainting, swooning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविकृतिः|अङ्गविकृति|अंगविकृति
अङ्गम् + -विकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 change of bodily appearance; collapse.<BR>—2 [अङ्गस्य विकृतिश्चालनादिर्यस्मात् प˚ ब˚] an apoplectic fit,<BR> swooning, apoplexy (अपस्मार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविकारः|अङ्गविकार
अङ्गम् + -विकारः a bodily defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविक्षेपः|अङ्गविक्षेप|अंगविक्षेप
अङ्गम् + -विक्षेपः<BR>—1 movement of the limbs; gesticulation.<BR>—2 a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविद्या|अंगविद्या
अङ्गम् + -विद्या [अङ्गरूपा व्याकरणादिशास्त्ररूपा विद्या ज्ञानसाधनम्]<BR>—1 the science of grammar &c. contributing to knowledge.<BR>—2 the science of foretelling good or evil by the movements of limbs.<BR> Kau. A. 1. 12; N. of chapter 51 of Bṛhat Saṃhitā which gives full details<BR> of this science; न नक्षत्राङ्गविद्यया … भिक्षां लिप्सेत कर्हिचित् Ms. 6. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविधिः|अङ्गविधि
अङ्गम् + -विधिः [अङ्गस्य प्रधानोपकारिणः विधिः विधानम्] a subordinate<BR> or subsidiary act subservient to a knowledge of the principal one (प्रधानविधिविधेयकर्मणोऽङ्गबोधकतया अङ्गविधिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवीरः|अङ्गवीर
अङ्गम् + -वीरः chief or principal hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवैकृतम्
अङ्गम् + -वैकृतम् [अङ्गेन अङ्गचेष्टया वैकृतं हृदयभावो ज्ञाप्यते यत्र बहु.]<BR>—1 a sign, gesture or expression of the face leading to a knowledge of<BR> internal thoughts (आकार)<BR>—2 a nod, wink.<BR>—3 changed bodily appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवैगुण्यम्
अङ्गम् + -वैगुण्यम् a defect or flaw in the performance of some subordinate<BR> or subsidiary act which may be expiated by thinking of Viṣṇu; (श्राद्धादिपद्धतौ<BR> कर्मान्ते यत्किञ्चिदङ्गवैगुण्यं जातं तद्दोषप्रशमनाय विष्णुस्मरणमहं<BR> करिष्ये इत्यभिलापवाक्यम् Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंस्कारः|अङ्गसंस्कार|अंगसंस्कार
अङ्गम् + -संस्कारः, -संस्क्रिया [अङ्गं संस्क्रियते अनेन; कृ-करणे<BR> or भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 embellishment of person, personal decoration, doing whatever secures<BR> a fine personal appearance, such as bathing, rubbing the body, perfuming<BR> it with cosmetics &c.<BR>—2 [कर्त्रर्थे अण्] one who decorates or embellishes the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंस्क्रिया|अंगसंस्क्रिया
अङ्गम् + -संस्कारः, -संस्क्रिया [अङ्गं संस्क्रियते अनेन; कृ-करणे<BR> or भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 embellishment of person, personal decoration, doing whatever secures<BR> a fine personal appearance, such as bathing, rubbing the body, perfuming<BR> it with cosmetics &c.<BR>—2 [कर्त्रर्थे अण्] one who decorates or embellishes the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंहतिः|अङ्गसंहति|अंगसंहति
अङ्गम् + -संहतिः <i>f.</i> compactness, symmetry; body; स्थेयसीं दधतमङ्गसंहतिम्<BR> Ki. 13. 50; or strength of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंहिता
अङ्गम् + -संहिता The phonetic relation between consonants and vowels in<BR> the body of a word Ts. Prāt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसङ्गः|अङ्गसङ्ग|अङ्गसंग|अंगसंग
अङ्गम् + -सङ्गः bodily contact, union; coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसुप्तिः
अङ्गम् + -सुप्तिः <i>f.</i> Benumbing of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसेवकः|अङ्गसेवक
अङ्गम् + -सेवकः a personal attendant, body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गस्कन्धः|अङ्गस्कन्ध
अङ्गम् + -स्कन्धः [कर्मधा.] a subdivision of a science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गस्पर्शः|अङ्गस्पर्श
अङ्गम् + -स्पर्शः fitness or qualification for bodily contact or being<BR> touched by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहानिः|अङ्गहानि
अङ्गम् + -हानिः <i>f.</i> —1 a defect or flaw in the performance of a secondary<BR> or subsidiary act (= ˚वैगुण्यम्); दैवाद् भ्रमात् प्रमादाच्चेदङ्गहानिः<BR> प्रजायते । स्मरणादेव तद्विष्णोः संपूर्णं स्यादिति श्रुतिः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहारः|अङ्गहार|अंगहार
अङ्गम् + -हारः [अङ्गं ह्रियते इतस्ततः चाल्यते यत्र, हृ-आधारे or भावे घञ्]<BR> gesticulation, movements of the limbs, a dance; अङ्गहारैस्तथैवान्या<BR> कोमलैर्नृत्यशालिनी Rām. 5. 10. 36. संसक्तैरगुरुवनेषु साङ्गहारम्<BR> Ki. 7. 37; Ku. 7. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहारिः|अङ्गहारि
अङ्गम् + -हारिः [अङ्गं ह्रियतेऽत्र; हृ-बा˚ णि]<BR>—1 gesticulation.<BR>—2 stage; dancing hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहीन|अंगहीन|अङ्गहीनः
अङ्गम् + -हीन <i>a.</i> [तृ˚ त˚] —1 mutilated, deprived of some defective<BR> limb (अङ्गं हीनं यथोचितप्रमाणात् अल्पं यस्य) according to Suśruta<BR> a man is so born, if the motherʼs दोहद has not been duly fulfilled<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">Page0025-2</a>]<BR> (सा प्राप्तदौर्हृदा पुत्रं जनयेत गुणान्वितम् । अलब्धदौर्हृदा गर्भे लभेतात्मनि<BR> वा भयम् ॥ येषु योष्विन्द्रियार्थेषु दौर्हृदे वै विमानना । जायते तत्सुतस्यार्तिस्तस्मिंस्तस्मिंस्तथेन्द्रिये ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गकम्
अङ्गकम् [अङ्गमेव अङ्गकं स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>—1 A limb; अकृत मधुरैरम्बानां मे कुतूहलमङ्गकैः U. 1. 20, 24.<BR>—2 The body; हरन्ति रतये रहः प्रियतमाङ्गकादम्बरम् Śi. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिका|अंगिका
अङ्गिका [अङ्गम् आच्छादयति अङ्ग्-इनि स्वार्थे कन्, स्त्रियां टाप्] A bodice or jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिन्|अंगिन्
अङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> [अङ्ग्-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 Corporeal, having limb, embodied, incarnate; धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामवतार<BR> इवाङ्गवान् v. l. -भाक् R. 10. 84. अङ्गिनां तमसेवोभौ गुणौ 38.<BR> one who has a body; येनाङ्गविकारः P. II. 3. 23 येनाङ्गेन विकृतेनाङ्गिनो<BR> विकारस्तस्मात् तृतीया Sk. व्यायामे वृद्धिरङ्गिनाम् Śi. 2. 94.<BR>—2 Having subordinate parts; chief, principal; ये रसस्याङ्गिनो धर्माः,<BR> एक एव भवेदङ्गी शृङ्गारो वीर एव वा, अङ्गी अत्र करुणः, रसस्याङ्गित्वमाप्तस्य<BR> धर्माः शौर्यादयो यथा S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीय|अंगीय
अङ्गीय <i>a.</i> [अङ्ग-छ]<BR>—1 Belonging to the body.<BR>—2 Referring to the Aṅga country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग्य|अंग्य
अङ्ग्य <i>a.</i> [अङ्ग-यत्] Belonging to or connected with the body, corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गणम्
अङ्गणम् = अङ्गनम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गतिः|अङ्गति|अंगति|अंगतिः
अङ्गतिः [अङ्गति यात्यनेन, अङ्ग् करणे अति]<BR>—1 A conveyance, vehicle (<i>f.</i> also).<BR>—2 [अङ्ग्यते गम्यते सेवादिना कर्मणि अति] Fire.<BR>—3 Brahmā.<BR>—4 [कर्तरि अति] A Brāhmaṇa who maintains the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गदम्
अङ्गदम् [अङ्गं दायति शोधयति भूषयति, अङ्गं द्यति वा, दै or दो-क.]<BR> An ornament, bracelet &c. worn on the upper arm, an armlet;<BR> तप्तचामीकराङ्गदः V. 1. 15. संघट्टयन्नङ्गदमङ्गदेन R. 6. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गदा
अङ्गदम् + .{@-दा@}<BR>—1 The female elephant of the south (?).<BR>—2 A woman who offers her person for use (अङ्गं ददाति अर्पयति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गदः|अङ्गद|अंगद|अंगदं|अङ्गदं
अङ्गदम् + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 N. of a son of Vāli, monkey-king of Kiṣkindhā. cf. अङ्गदो वालिनन्दने,<BR> नपुंसि बाहुवलये … । Nm. [He was born of Tārā, Vālīʼs wife,<BR> and is supposed to have been an incarnation of Bṛhaspati to aid the cause<BR> of Rāma (and hence noted for his eloquence). When, after the abduction<BR> of Sītā by Rāvaṇa, Rāma sent monkeys in all quarters to search for<BR> her, Aṅgada was made chief of a monkey-troop proceeding to the south.<BR> For one month he got no information, and, when consequently he determined<BR> to cast off his life, he was told by Sampāti that Sītā could be found<BR> in Laṅkā. He sent Māruti to the island and, on the latterʼs return<BR> with definite information, they joined Rāma at Kiṣkindhā. Afterwards<BR> when the whole host of Rāma went to Laṅkā Aṅgada was despatched to<BR> Rāvaṇa as a messenger of peace to give him a chance of saving himself<BR> in time. But Rāvaṇa scornfully rejected his advice and met his doom.<BR> After Sugrīva Aṅgada became king of Kiṣkindhā. In common parlance<BR> a man is said to act the part of Aṅgada when he endeavours to mediate<BR> between two contending parties, but without<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">Page0026-1</a>]<BR> any success.]<BR>—2 N. of a son of Lakṣmaṇa by Urmilā (अङ्गदं चन्द्रकेतुं च लक्ष्मणोऽप्यात्मसंभवौ ।<BR> शासनाद्रघुनाथस्य चक्रे कारापथेश्वरौ ॥ R. 15. 90), his capital<BR> being called Aṅgadīyā.<BR>—3 N. of a warrior on the side of Duryodhana.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्गदनिर्यूहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गदनिर्यूहः
अङ्गदम् + -निर्यूहः the crest-like forepart of the Aṅgada ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनम्
अङ्गनम्, -णम्<BR> [अङ्ग्यते गृहान्निःसृत्य गम्यते अत्र; अङ्ग-ल्युट्, वा णत्वम्<BR> Tv.] —1 A place to walk in, a courtyard, an area, yard, court; गृह˚, गगन˚ the wide firmament; केसरवृक्षस्य v. l. बालबकुलस्य Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गणम्
अङ्गनम्, -णम्<BR> [अङ्ग्यते गृहान्निःसृत्य गम्यते अत्र; अङ्ग-ल्युट्, वा णत्वम्<BR> Tv.] —1 A place to walk in, a courtyard, an area, yard, court; गृह˚, गगन˚ the wide firmament; केसरवृक्षस्य v. l. बालबकुलस्य Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनभुवः
अङ्गनम्, -णम् + ˚भुवः<BR>—1 situated or being in the courtyard.<BR>—2 [करणे ल्युट्] A conveyance.<BR>—3 [भावे ल्युट्] Going, walking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गणभुवः
अङ्गनम्, -णम् + ˚भुवः<BR>—1 situated or being in the courtyard.<BR>—2 [करणे ल्युट्] A conveyance.<BR>—3 [भावे ल्युट्] Going, walking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गना|अंगना
अङ्गना [प्रशस्तम् अङ्गं यस्याः सा; अङ्गात् कल्याणे नः P. V. 2. 100.]<BR>—1 A woman or female in general; नृप˚, गज˚, हरिण˚ &c.<BR>—2 A woman with well-rounded limbs, a beautiful woman.<BR>—3 (Astr.) Virgo. कन्याराशिः<BR>—4 The female elephant of the north.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अङ्गनाजनः, अङ्गनाप्रिय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाजनः|अङ्गनाजन
अङ्गना + -जनः<BR>—1 the female sex, woman-kind.<BR>—2 woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाप्रिय|अंगनाप्रिय|अङ्गनाप्रियः
अङ्गना + -प्रिय <i>a.</i> beloved of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाप्रियः|अङ्गनाप्रिय|अंगनाप्रिय
अङ्गना + -प्रिय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 N. of a plant (अशोक) Jonesia Aśoka, for women are fond of decking<BR> their persons with Aśoka flowers.<BR>—2 Name of a medicinal fragrant plant प्रियङ्गु (Mar. गव्हला).<BR> It is a small plant used in perfumed oils and ointments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गभः|अङ्गभ
अङ्गभः A kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवम्
अङ्गवम् [अङ्गे स्वावयवे वाति अन्तर्भवति अतिशोषणात् संकुचिताङ्गमिव<BR> भवति, वा-ड Tv.] Dried fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गस्|अंगस्
अङ्गस् <i>m.</i> [अञ्ज्-असुन् कुत्वम्] A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारः|अङ्गार|अंगार|अंगारं|अंगारः
अङ्गारः, -रम्<BR> [अङ्ग्-आरन् Uṇ. 3. 134] —1 Charcoal (whether heated or<BR> not); घृतकुम्भसमा नारी तप्ताङ्गारसमः पुमान्; उष्णो दहति चाङ्गारः<BR> शीतः कृष्णायते करम् H. 1. 80; नालास्त्रार्थाग्निचूर्णे तु गन्धाङ्गारौ तु<BR> पूर्ववत् Śukra. 4. 1035. त्वया स्वहस्तेनाङ्गाराः कर्षिताः Pt.<BR>—1 you have ruined yourself with your own hands; cf. "to dig a mine under<BR> oneʼs feet." कुरुकुलाङ्गार Ve. 6 destroyer or pest of the Kuru family.<BR>—2 The planet Mars.<BR>—3 A plant हितावली, ˚कुष्टकःहितावली.<BR>—4 N. of a prince who fought with king Māndhāṭr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

