अङ्गारपर्णः|अङ्गारपर्ण|अङ्गारपर्ण्ण
अङ्गारः + -पर्णम् + .({@-र्णः@}) [अस्त्यर्थे अच्] N. of Citraratha, king of the Gandharvas.<BR> [On one occasion, while he was sporting with his wife, he saw Kuntī with<BR> her five sons proceeding to the capital of Pāñcāla in disguise. He<BR> accosted them and asked<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-2" target="_blank">Page0026-2</a>]<BR> them to tell him where they were going, or to fight. Arjuna accepted the<BR> challenge; but Aṅgāraparṇa finding Arjuna to be a very skilful warrior<BR> gave him a secret lore called Cākṣuṣī (enabling one to see the smallest<BR> things) and took from him in return a lore called Agniśirāstra and became<BR> a friend of the Pāṇḍavas.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0026-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

