अच्युत|अच्युतः
अच्युत <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚ स्वरूपसामर्थ्यात् न च्युतः च्यवते<BR> वा-कालसामान्ये कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Not fallen, firm, fixed; not giving way, solid; गरुडमूर्तिरिव अच्युतस्थितिरमणीया<BR> K. 52 (अच्युत meaning ‘Viṣṇu’ and ‘firm’, ‘fixed’); ˚क्षित् having solid ground.<BR>—2 Imperishable, permanent; ˚रुष् inveterate enmity.<BR>—3 [न च्योतति क्षरति; च्युत्-क. न˚ त˚] Not melting away<BR> or perishing, not leaking or dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युतः|अच्युत
अच्युत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu; of the Almighty Being;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">Page0030-2</a>]<BR> यस्मान्न च्युतपूर्वोऽहमच्युतस्तेन कर्मणा Bhāg.<BR>—2 गच्छाम्यच्युतदशनेन K. P. 5. (where अ˚ also means ‘one who is firm, does not yield to passions’<BR>)<BR>—3 N. of a plant, Morinda Tinctoria. (Mar. बारातोंडी, शिर्दोली).<BR>—4 A sort of poetical composition containing 12 cantos.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अच्युताग्रजः, अच्युताङ्गजः, अच्युतपुत्रः, अच्युतात्मजः, अच्युतावासः, अच्युतवासः, अच्युतजः, अच्युतजल्लकिन्, अच्युतस्थलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

