अज्
अज् €1 P. (optionally replaced by the root वी in non-conjugational<BR> tenses; अजति, आजीत्, अजितुम्)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To drive, lead.<BR>—3 To throw, cast (used with prepositions found only in Vedic literature).<BR> [cf. L. <i>ago</i>; Gr. <i>ago</i>; Zend. <i>az</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज <i>a.</i> [न जायते; जन्-ड. न˚ त˚] Unborn, existing<BR> from all eternity; यो मामजमनादिं च वेत्ति लोकमहेश्वरम् Bg. 10. 3;<BR> अजस्य गृह्णतो जन्म R. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजः|अज
अज + .{@-जः@}<BR>—1 The ‘unborn’, epithet of the Almighty Being; न हि जातो न जायेऽहं<BR> न जनिष्ये कदाचन । क्षेत्रज्ञः सर्वभूतानां तस्मादहमजः स्मृतः ॥<BR> Mb.; also a N. of Viṣṇu, Śiva or Brahmā.<BR>—2 The (individual) soul (जीवः) अजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो न<BR> हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे Bg. 2. 20.<BR>—3 A ram, he-goat [अजेन ब्रह्मणा दक्षयज्ञभङ्गसमये मेषरूपग्रहणेन<BR> पलायमानत्वात् अजाधिष्टितरूपवत्त्वात् मेषस्य उपचारात् अजत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—4 The sign Aries.<BR>—5 A sort of corn or grain; अजैर्यष्टव्यं तत्राजा व्रीहयः Pt. 3.<BR>—6 Mover, leader (Ved.), said of Indra, Maruts, &c.; a drove.<BR>—7 N. of a mineral substance (माक्षिकधातु).<BR>—8 N. of the Moon or Kāmadeva (आत् विष्णोर्जायते इति; cf. चन्द्रमा<BR> मनसो जातः).<BR>—9 A vehicle of the sun.<BR>—10 N. of the father of Daśaratha and grand-father of Rāma; so called<BR> because he was born on the Brāhma Muhūrta.<BR>—11 N. of a Ṛṣi. cf. अजो हरौ हरे कामे विधौ छागे रघोः सुते । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजादः, अजादनी, अजान्त्री, अजाविकम्, अजाश्वम्, अजैकपाद्, अजदः, अजैडकम्, अजकर्णः, अजकर्णकः, अजगन्धा, अजगन्धिका, अजगन्धिनी, अजगरः, अजगल, अजगल्लिका, अजजीवः, अजजीविकः, अजदण्डी, अजदेवता, अजनामकः, अजनाशनः, अजपतिः, अजपथः, अजपदः, अजपाद्, अजपादः, अजभक्षः, अजमायु, अजमारः, अजमीढः, अजमुख, अजमोदा, अजमोदिका, अजलम्बनम्, अजलोमन्, अजलोमी, अजलोमा, अजवस्तिः, अजवीथिः, अजवीथी, अजशृङ्गी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजादः|अजाद
अज + -अदः [अजम् अत्तीति; अद्-कर्मण्यण् P. III. 2. 9.] N. of the<BR> ancestor of a warrior tribe, P. IV. 1. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजादनी
अज + -अदनी [अजैः तृप्त्या अन्यैः दुःखस्पर्शत्वेऽपि अद्यतेः अद् कर्मणि<BR> ल्युट्] a kind of prickly nightshade, दुरालभा (Mar. धमासा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजान्त्री
अज + -अन्त्री [अजस्य अन्त्रमिव अन्त्रं तदाकारवती मञ्जरी यस्याः]<BR> N. of a potherb Convolvulus Argenteus, नीलबुह्ना. (Mar. शंखवेल ?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाविकम्
अज + -अविकम् [अजाश्चावयश्च तेषां समाहारः द्वन्द्व] goats and<BR> sheep; small cattle; अजाविके तु संरुद्धे Ms. 8. 235. खरोष्ट्रमहिषीश्चैव<BR> यच्च किञ्चिदजाविकम् Mb. 1. 113. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाश्वम्
अज + -अश्वम् goats and horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाश्वः|अजाश्व
अज + -अश्वम् + .({@-श्वः@}) the Sun or Pūṣan, who has goats for the horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैकपाद्
अज + -एकपाद्, -दः [अजस्य छागस्य एकः पाद इव पादो यस्य] N. of<BR> one of the 11 Rudras, or of the asterism पूर्वाभाद्रपदा presided over by that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजदः
अज + -एकपाद्, -दः [अजस्य छागस्य एकः पाद इव पादो यस्य] N. of<BR> one of the 11 Rudras, or of the asterism पूर्वाभाद्रपदा presided over by that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैडकम्
अज + -एडकम् [अजाश्च एडकाश्च तेषां समाहारः] goats and rams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्णः|अजकर्ण
अज + -कर्णः, -कर्णकः [अजस्य कर्णम् इव पर्णं यस्य-स्वार्थे कन्]<BR> N. of the plant असनवृक्ष Terminalia Alata Tomentosa; of another<BR> tree साल Shorea Robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्णकः|अजकर्णक|अजकर्ण्णक
अज + -कर्णः, -कर्णकः [अजस्य कर्णम् इव पर्णं यस्य-स्वार्थे कन्]<BR> N. of the plant असनवृक्ष Terminalia Alata Tomentosa; of another<BR> tree साल Shorea Robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धा
अज + -गन्धा [अजस्य गन्ध इव गन्धो यस्याः सा] the shrubby basil,<BR> वनयामानी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिका
अज + -गन्धिका a kind of वर्वरीशाक (Mar. तिलवणी, कानफोडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिनी
अज + -गन्धिनी = अजशृङ्गी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगरः|अजगर
अज + -गरः [अजं छागं गिरति भक्षयति; गॄ-अच्] a huge serpent<BR> (boa-constrictor) who is said to swallow goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगरी
अज + -गरः + .({@-री@}) N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगल
अज + -गल See अजागल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगल्लिका
अज + -गल्लिका [अजस्य गल्ल इव] an infantile disease (Mentagra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजजीवः
अज + -जीवः, -जीविकः [अजैस्तच्चारणेन जीवति; अजा एव जीविका यस्य<BR> वा] a goat-herd; so -˚पः, -˚पालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजजीविकः|अजजीविक
अज + -जीवः, -जीविकः [अजैस्तच्चारणेन जीवति; अजा एव जीविका यस्य<BR> वा] a goat-herd; so -˚पः, -˚पालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजदण्डी
अज + -दण्डी [अजस्य ब्रह्मणो दण्डो यस्याः सा] ब्रह्मदण्डी a<BR> kind of plant (ब्रह्मणो यज्ञार्थदण्डस्य तदीयकाष्टेन करणात् तथात्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजदेवता
अज + -देवता<BR>—1 N. of the 25th asterism. पूर्वाभाद्रपदा.<BR>—2 fire, the presiding deity of goats (रौद्री धेनुर्विनिर्दिष्टा छाग आग्नेय उच्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनामकः|अजनामक
अज + -नामकः [अजः नाम यस्य सः कप्] a mineral substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनाशनः|अजनाशन
अज + -नाशनः A wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपतिः|अजपति
अज + -पतिः<BR>—1 the best of goats.<BR>—2 N. of Mars; lord of the sign Aries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपथः|अजपथ
अज + -पथः = अजवीथिः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपदः|अजपद
अज + -पदः, -पाद्, -पादः N. of a Rudra; see अजैकपाद above. {@बन्धुः@}<BR> [अजस्य बन्धुरिव मूर्खत्वात्] a fool (silly like the goat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपाद्
अज + -पदः, -पाद्, -पादः N. of a Rudra; see अजैकपाद above. {@बन्धुः@}<BR> [अजस्य बन्धुरिव मूर्खत्वात्] a fool (silly like the goat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपादः|अजपाद
अज + -पदः, -पाद्, -पादः N. of a Rudra; see अजैकपाद above. {@बन्धुः@}<BR> [अजस्य बन्धुरिव मूर्खत्वात्] a fool (silly like the goat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजभक्षः|अजभक्ष
अज + -भक्षः [अजैर्भक्ष्यते असौ भक्ष्-कर्मणि घञ्] N. of the वर्वरी<BR> plant (तिळवण the leaves of which are very dear to goats).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमायु
अज + -मायु <i>a.</i> Ved. bleating like a goat (a frog) गोमायुरेक अजमायुरेकः<BR> Rv. 7. 103. 6, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमारः|अजमार
अज + -मारः [अजं मारयति विक्रयार्थ; मृ-णिच्-अण्]<BR>—1 a butcher.<BR>—2 N. of a country (the modern Ajmeer, which, it is supposed, formerly<BR> abounded in butchers).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-1" target="_blank">Page0031-1</a>]<BR>—3 N. of a tribe (गण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमीढः|अजमीढ
अज + -मीढः [अजो मीढो यज्ञे सिक्तो यत्र ब˚]<BR>—1 N. of the place called Ajmeer.<BR>—2 N. of the eldest son of Hasti, born in the family of Puru, son of Yayāti.<BR>—3 N. of a son of सुहोत्र and author of some Vedic hyms like Rv. 4. 43.<BR>—4 surname of Yudhisṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमुख
अज + -मुख <i>a.</i> goat-faced. ({@खः@}) N. of a Prajāpati (Dakṣa).<BR> When Dakṣa reviled Śiva at his sacrificial session, Vīrabhadra pulled<BR> out his face, and afterwards at the request of Śiva himself he put up<BR> a goatʼs face in place of the original human one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमुखी
अज + -मुख + .({@-खी@}) N. of a Rākṣasī kept to watch over Sītā in the Aśoka<BR> garden at Laṅkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

