अजगवम्
अजगवम् [अजगो विष्णुः शरत्वेन अस्त्यस्य अजग-व P. V. 2. 110]<BR> Śivaʼs bow, Pināka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगावः|अजगाव|अजगावं
अजगावः [अजगं विष्णुम् अवति अव्-अण्]<BR>—1 Śivaʼs bow.<BR>—2 The southern portion of the path of the sun, moon and planets.<BR>—3 N. of a snake-priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजटा
अजटा [नास्ति जटा शिफा यस्याः सा] N. of a plant भूम्यालकी<BR> or कपिकच्छू. See अज्झटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजड
अजड <i>a.</i> Not stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजडा
अजड + .{@-डा@} N. of the plant अजटा, कपिकच्छू (अजडयति स्पर्शमात्रात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजथ्या
अजथ्या [अजाय हिता अजथ्या; अज्-थ्यन् P. V. 1. 8]<BR>—1 N. of the yellow jasmine यूथिका (Mar. पिवळी जाई).<BR>—2 A flock of goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अजन <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Destitute of men, tenantless, desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनः|अजन|अजनं
अजन + .{@-नः@} [कुत्सितार्थे नञ्] A bad or insignificant person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननिः|अजननि
अजननिः <i>f.</i> [नञ् जन्-आकोशे अनि P. III. 3. 112] Cessation<BR> of existence; तस्याजननिरेवास्तु जननीक्लेशकारिणः Śi. 2. 45 may<BR> he not be born, may he cease to exist!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनयोनिजः|अजनयोनिज
अजनयोनिजः Dakṣa Prajāpati (Bhāg. 4. 30. 48).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनाभम्
अजनाभम् An ancient name of Bhāratavarṣa; (Bhāg. 11. 2. 24).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्मन्
अजन्मन् <i>a.</i> Unborn, epithet of the Unborn Being, the Eternal being;<BR> पुरुषस्य पदेष्वजन्मनः R. 8. 78. ━<i>m.</i> [नास्ति जन्म यत्र]<BR> Final beatitude, absolution; तस्मात्स योगादधिगम्य योगमजन्मनेऽकल्पत<BR> जन्मभीरुः R. 18. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्य|अजन्यं
अजन्य <i>a.</i> Not fit to be produced; not favourable to mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्यम्
अजन्य + .{@-न्यम्@} [लौकिकंहेतुभिर्न जन्यते; जन्-णिच्-यत्] A portentous<BR> phenomenon, inauspicious to mankind, such as earth-quake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपः|अजप
अजपः [अस्पष्टं जपति निन्दार्थे नञ्, जप्-अच्] A Brāhmaṇa who<BR> does not (properly) repeat his prayers (कुपाठक); अजपा ब्राह्मणास्तात<BR> शूद्रा जपपरायणाः । भविष्यन्ति कलौ Mb.; one who reads heretical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपा
अजपः + .{@-पा@} [प्रयत्नेन न जप्या अप्रयत्नोच्चारितत्वात्; कर्मणि अच्]<BR> N. of a Mantra called हंस, which consists of a number of inhalations<BR> and exhalations (श्वासप्रश्वासयोः वहिर्गमनागमनाभ्याम् अक्षरनिष्पादनरूपो<BR> जपः स च हंसः सोऽहम् इत्याकार एव उच्छ्वासैरेव निश्वासैर्हंस इत्यक्षरद्वयम् ।<BR> तस्मात्प्राणश्च हंसाख्य आत्माकारेण संस्थितः ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजम्भ|अजंभ|अजम्भः
अजम्भ <i>a.</i> [नास्ति जम्भो दन्तो यस्य] Toothless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजम्भः|अजम्भ|अजंभ
अजम्भ + .{@-भः@}<BR>—1 A frog.<BR>—2 The sun. —3 Toothless state (of a child.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अजय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति परैर्जयो यस्य] Invincible, unsurpassed unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजयः|अजय
अजय + .{@-यः@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 A defeat; सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ Bg. 2. 38.<BR>—2 N. of Agni (अजेन छागेन याति; या-क); or of Viṣṇu (according<BR> to some); of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजया
अजय + .{@-या@} [नास्ति जयो मादकत्वेन अस्याम्]<BR>—1 Hemp or भाङ्ग.<BR>—2 N. of a friend of Durgā<BR>—3 Māyā or illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय्य|अजय्यं
अजय्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Invincible; सख्युस्ते स किल शतकतोरजग्यः Ś. 6. 30. राज्ञामजय्यः R. 18. 8.<BR>—2 Not proper to be win at play; ˚य्यं जिगाय तान्, Bopadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अजर <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not subject to old age or decay; ever young अजरं वृद्धत्वम् K. 103;<BR> cf. वृद्धत्वं जरया विना R. 1. 23<BR>—2 Undecaying, imperishable; पुराणमजरं विदुः R. 10. 19; अनन्तमजरं<BR> ब्रह्म Bh. 3. 69; H. Pr. 3; Pt. 1. 151; Ms. 2. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरः|अजर
अजर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A god (who is not subject to old age). अजरामरवत्प्राज्ञो विद्यामर्थं<BR> च चिन्तयेत् H.<BR>—2 N. of a plant वृद्धदारक or जीर्णफंजी (Mar. काळी वरधारा).<BR> (˚रा also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजरद्रुमः, अजररा, अजररम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरा
अजर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A god (who is not subject to old age). अजरामरवत्प्राज्ञो विद्यामर्थं<BR> च चिन्तयेत् H.<BR>—2 N. of a plant वृद्धदारक or जीर्णफंजी (Mar. काळी वरधारा).<BR> (˚रा also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजरद्रुमः, अजररा, अजररम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरद्रुमः
अजर + -द्रुमः The name of Kalpavṛkṣa. Śāhendra. 2. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजररा
अजर + -रा<BR>—1 N. of a plant गृहकन्या or घृतकुमारा Also Perfoliote. (Mar. कोरफड).<BR>—2 A house-lizard (गोधालिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजररम्
अजर + -रम् [जीर्यते क्षीयते जॄ-अच्] The Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरकः|अजरक
अजरकः (कम्) Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरकम्
अजरकः (कम्) Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य|अजर्य्य|अजर्य्यं
अजर्य <i>a.</i> [न जीर्यति; ज कर्तरि यत् P. III. 1. 105.]<BR>—1 Not digestible.<BR>—2 Not decaying, imperishable, everlasting perpetual. तेन संगतमार्येण<BR> रामाजर्यं कुरु द्रुतम् । Bk. 6. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्यम्
अजर्य + .{@-र्यम@} (with संगतम् expressed or understood) Friendship;<BR> मृगैरजर्यं जरसोपदिष्टम् R. 18. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरत्|अजरन्त्
अजरत् -रयु-रस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not old. अजरयू अयातम् Rv. 1. 116. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजवस्
अजवस् <i>a.</i> [जु-असुन्] Not quick, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्तुन्दम्
अजस्तुन्दम् [अजस्य इव तुन्दम् अस्य सुट् निपातोऽयम्] N. of a town, P. VI. 1. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र <i>a.</i> [न जस्-र P. III. 2. 167; जसिर्नञ्पूर्वः क्रियासातत्ये<BR> वर्तते Sk.] Not ceasing, constant, perpetual; ˚दीक्षाप्रयतस्य R. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्रम्
अजस्र + .{@-स्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Ever, constantly, perpetually; वृथैव संकल्पशतैरजस्रम्<BR> Ś. 3. 5. तच्च धूनोत्यजस्रम् U. 4. 26. अजस्रमास्फालित … । Śi. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्स्वार्था
अजहत्स्वार्था [न जहत् स्वार्थोऽत्र, हा-शतृ न˚ ब˚] A kind<BR> of लक्षणा, in which the primary or original sense of a word (which<BR> is used elliptically) does not disappear; as कुन्ताः प्रविशन्ति = कुन्तधारिणः<BR> पुरुषाः; श्वेतो धावति = श्वेतवर्णोऽश्वो धावति; also called उपादानलक्षणा<BR> q. v.; स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः; कुन्ताः प्रविशन्ति, यष्टयः प्रविशन्ति<BR> इत्यादौ कुन्तादिभिरात्मनः प्रवेशसिद्धपर्थ स्वसंयोगिनः पुरुषा आक्षिप्यन्ते<BR> K. P. 2. Adhyātma Rām. 7. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्स्वार्थवृत्ति
अजहत्स्वार्थवृत्ति <i>a.</i> Functioning without entirely surrendering<BR> oneʼs own connotation; उत्पलशब्दसंनिधाने तदपेक्षा नीलशब्दस्तेनैकवाक्यतामभ्युपगच्छन्नजहत्स्वार्थवृत्तिरुत्पलविशेषाभिधानपर<BR> उच्चार्यमाणः सम्बन्धमभ्युपैति । ŚB. on MS. 3. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहल्लिङ्गम्
अजहल्लिङ्गम्^1 [न जहत् लिङ्गं यं; हा-शतृ] A noun which does<BR> not change its original gender, even when used like an adjective; <i>e. g.</i><BR> वेदः or श्रुतिः प्रमाणम् (not प्रमाणः or ˚णा).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: missing virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहा
अजहा [न जहाति शूकान् हा-श.] N. of a plant, cowage, Carpopogon<BR> Pruriens. (Mar. कुहिली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागर|अजागरः
अजागर <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Not wakeful, not requiring keeping up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागरः|अजागर
अजागर + .{@-रः@} [जागरयतीति जागरः न जागरो यस्मात्] A plant, Verbesina<BR> Prostrata (भृङ्गराजवृक्ष) (सेवनेन निद्राराहित्यकारकः, यदपेक्षया<BR> अन्यस्मिन् जागरणकर्तृत्वं नास्ति.) (Mar. माका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजिः|अजाजि
अजाजिः, -जी <i>f.</i><BR> [अजेन छागेन वीयते गन्धोत्कटत्वात् त्यज्यते, अज्-इन्<BR> वीभावाभावः] Cumin seed (श्वेतजीरक); कृष्णजीरक Nigella Indica;<BR> (Mar. कार्ळें, पांढरें जिरें). काकोदुम्बरिका Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR> (Mar. धेडौंबर). कृष्णाजाजी विडश्चैव शीतपाकी तथैव च Mb. 13. 91. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजी
अजाजिः, -जी <i>f.</i><BR> [अजेन छागेन वीयते गन्धोत्कटत्वात् त्यज्यते, अज्-इन्<BR> वीभावाभावः] Cumin seed (श्वेतजीरक); कृष्णजीरक Nigella Indica;<BR> (Mar. कार्ळें, पांढरें जिरें). काकोदुम्बरिका Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR> (Mar. धेडौंबर). कृष्णाजाजी विडश्चैव शीतपाकी तथैव च Mb. 13. 91. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात [न˚ त˚] Unborn; अजातमृतमूर्खेभ्यो मृताजातौ सुतौ<BR> वरम् Pt. 1; not yet born, produced, or fully developed; ˚ककुद्, ˚पक्ष &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजातारि, अजातशत्रु, अजातककुत्, अजातककुद्, अजातदन्त, अजातपक्ष, अजातव्यञ्जन, अजातव्यवहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातारि|अजातारिः
अजात + -अरि, -शत्रु <i>a.</i> [न जातः शत्रुः अस्य; जातस्य जन्तुमात्रस्य<BR> न शत्रुः] having no enemy or adversary, not an enemy of any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातशत्रु|अजातशत्रुः
अजात + -अरि, -शत्रु <i>a.</i> [न जातः शत्रुः अस्य; जातस्य जन्तुमात्रस्य<BR> न शत्रुः] having no enemy or adversary, not an enemy of any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातारिः|अजातारि
अजात + -अरि, -शत्रु + .({@-रिः, -त्रुः@}) epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira; हन्त जातमजातारेः प्रथमेन<BR> त्वयारिणा Śi. 2. 802; न द्वेक्षि यज्जनमतस्त्वमजातशत्रुः Ve. 3. 15;<BR> also of Śiva and various other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातशत्रुः|अजातशत्रु
अजात + -अरि, -शत्रु + .({@-रिः, -त्रुः@}) epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira; हन्त जातमजातारेः प्रथमेन<BR> त्वयारिणा Śi. 2. 802; न द्वेक्षि यज्जनमतस्त्वमजातशत्रुः Ve. 3. 15;<BR> also of Śiva and various other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातककुत्
अजात + -ककुत्, -ककुद् <i>m.</i> (ब˚) a young bull whose hump is not yet<BR> fully developed, P. V. 4. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातककुद्
अजात + -अरि, -शत्रु + .({@-रिः, -त्रुः@}) epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira; हन्त जातमजातारेः प्रथमेन<BR> त्वयारिणा Śi. 2. 802; न द्वेक्षि यज्जनमतस्त्वमजातशत्रुः Ve. 3. 15;<BR> also of Śiva and various other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातदन्त
अजात + -दन्त <i>a.</i> [न जाता दन्ता यस्य यस्मिन् वयसि वा] one without<BR> teeth, or (a state) in which one has got no teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातपक्ष
अजात + -पक्ष <i>a.</i> having undeveloped or unfledged wings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातव्यञ्जन|अजातव्यंजन
अजात + -व्यञ्जन <i>a.</i> having no distinctive marks or features (as a beard.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातव्यवहारः|अजातव्यवहार
अजात + -व्यवहारः a minor (who has not attained his majority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाति|अजातिः
अजाति <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Having no caste, race &c.<BR>—2 Eternal, not produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातिः|अजाति
अजाति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Non-production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजादिः|अजादि
अजादिः a gaṇa of pāṇini (IV. 1. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानिः|अजानि
अजानिः [नास्ति जाया यस्य] Without a wife; a widower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानिक
अजानिक <i>a.</i> [अजेन तद्विक्रयपालनादिना आनो जीवनम् अस्त्यस्य;<BR> ठन् Tv.] A goat-herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानेय|अजानेयः
अजानेय <i>a.</i> Of high breed, powerful, fearless, undaunted (as a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानेयः|अजानेय
अजानेय + .{@-यः@} A horse of high breed. See आजानेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजापक्वम्
अजापक्वम् N. of a sort of medicinal preparation of ghee (used as<BR> a remedy against cough, asthma, consumption &c.) (अजादुग्धादिभ्यो जातम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजामि
अजामि <i>a.</i> Ved. [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not of kin or related; यत्र जामयः कृणवन्नजामि Rv. 10. 10. 10<BR> (अजामिकर्माणि भ्रातॄणाम् अजामियोग्यानि मैथुनसम्बधानि कर्माणि करिष्यन्ति Nir.)<BR>—2 Not parallel or correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजि|अजिः
अजि <i>a.</i> [अजति; अज्-इ Uṇ. 4. 139] Going, moving; as पदाजि<BR> walking on foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिः|अजि
अजि + .{@-जिः@} <i>f.</i> [भावे इन्]<BR>—1 Motion, going.<BR>—2 Throwing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजित|अजितं|अजितः
अजित <i>a.</i> —1 Invincible, unconquerable, irresistible, ˚तं पुण्यं … महः U. 5. 27.<BR>—2 Not conquered or won<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">Page0033-1</a>]<BR> (as a country &c.); not restrained, curbed, controlled, ˚आत्मन्; ˚इन्द्रिय<BR> of uncontrolled soul or passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितः|अजित|अजितं
अजित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu or Śiva or of Buddha.<BR>—2 N. of a powerful antidote, or a poisonous sort of rat. ━(pl.) A class<BR> of deities in the first Manvantara cf. परमात्मन्यात्मनि च त्रिषु स्यादस्फुटेऽजितः ।<BR> अपराजितविष्ण्वीशपरमात्मसु कथ्यते ॥ Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजितापीडः, अजितकेशकम्बलः, अजितबला, अजितविक्रमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितापीडः|अजितापीड
अजित + -आपीडः having an invincible crown; N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितकेशकम्बलः|अजितकेशकम्बल
अजित + -केशकम्बलः Name of one of the six chief heretical teachers.<BR> (mentioned in Buddhist texts as contemporaries of Buddha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितबला
अजित + -बला N. of a Jain deity who acts under orders from the Arhat Ajita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजितविक्रमः|अजितविक्रम
अजित + -विक्रमः ‘of unsubdued power’, N. of Chandragupta II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनम्
अजिनम् [अजति क्षिपति रज आदि आवरणेन; अज्-इनच्, अजेरज च<BR> Uṇ. 2. 48, वीभावबाधनार्थम्]<BR>—1 the (hairy) skin of a tiger, lion, elephant &c., especially of a black<BR> antelope (used as a seat, garment &c.); अथाजिनाषाढधरः Ku. 5. 30,<BR> गजाजिनं शोणितबिन्दुवर्षि च 67; Ki. 11. 15; ऐणेयेनाजिनेन ब्राह्मणं<BR> रौरवेण क्षत्रियम् अजिनेन वैश्यम् Āśval.<BR>—2 A sort of leather bag or bellows.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजिनपत्रा, अजिनपत्री, अजिनत्रिका, अजिनफला, अजिनयोनिः, अजिनवासिन्, अजिनसन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनपत्रा
अजिनम् + -पत्रा, -पत्री, -त्रिका [अजिनं चर्म इव सुश्लिष्टं पत्रं पक्षो<BR> यस्याः सा, गौरा˚ ङीष् स्वार्थे कन्] a bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनपत्री
अजिनम् + -पत्रा, -पत्री, -त्रिका [अजिनं चर्म इव सुश्लिष्टं पत्रं पक्षो<BR> यस्याः सा, गौरा˚ ङीष् स्वार्थे कन्] a bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनत्रिका
अजिनम् + -पत्रा, -पत्री, -त्रिका [अजिनं चर्म इव सुश्लिष्टं पत्रं पक्षो<BR> यस्याः सा, गौरा˚ ङीष् स्वार्थे कन्] a bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनफला
अजिनम् + -फला [अजिनं भस्त्रेव फलं यस्याः सा] N. of a plant (भस्त्राकारफलो वृक्षः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनयोनिः|अजिनयोनि
अजिनम् + -योनिः [अजिनस्य योनिः प्रभवः] a deer, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनवासिन्
अजिनम् + -वासिन् <i>a.</i> [अजिनं वस्ते, वस्णिनि] clad in an antelope-hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनसन्धः|अजिनसन्ध|अजिनसंध
अजिनम् + -सन्धः [अजिनं सन्दधाति] a furrier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर^1 <i>a.</i> [अज् गतौ किरन् वीभावाभावः Uṇ. 1. 53.] Quick,<BR> swift (शीघ्र)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरः|अजिर|अजिरं
अजिरः + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A sort of mouse, hairy mole.<BR>—2 A kind of ceremony in pronouncing curses<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरम्
अजिरः + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A court-yard, an enclosed space, arena; उटजाजिरप्रकीर्ण K. 39,<BR> आस्थाननिकेतनाजिरम् Ki. 1. 16; so रण˚ सावित्र इति विख्यातः प्रविवेश<BR> रणाजिरम् Rām. 7. 27. 34 गृह˚ &c.<BR>—2 The body.<BR>—3 Any object of sense.<BR>—4 The wind, air.<BR>—5 A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरा
अजिरः + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 N. of a river.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरः|अजिर|अजिरं
अजिरः + .{@-रः@} N. of a snake-priest.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजिराधिराज, अजिरशोचिस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिराधिराज
अजिरः + -आधिराज [कर्म˚] Ved. ‘a quick emperor’, epithet of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरशोचिस्
अजिरः + -शोचिस् <i>a.</i> [अजिरं शोचिर्यस्य] glittering, having tremulous<BR> or flashing light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरीय
अजिरीय <i>a.</i> [अजिरम् उत्करा˚ छ] Connected with a court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अजिह्म <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Straight.<BR>—2 Upright, straightforward, honest; अजिह्मामशठां शुद्धां जीवेत् ब्राह्मणजीविकाम्<BR> Ms. 4. 11, 7. 32; ˚गामिभिः Śi. 1. 63 straight and honest, 3. 57, 9. 62<BR> cf. अजिह्मः सत्कृतावृजौ । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मः|अजिह्म|अजिह्मं
अजिह्म + .{@-ह्मः@}<BR>—1 A frog.<BR>—2 A fish (probably a corruption of अजिह्व below).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजिह्मग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मग|अजिह्मगः
अजिह्म + -ग <i>a.</i> [उप˚ स˚] going straight on; व्रजेद्दिशमजिह्मगः Ms. 6. 31<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मगः|अजिह्मग
अजिह्म + -ग + .({@-गः@}) an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्वः|अजिह्व
अजिह्वः [न˚ ब˚] A frog (which is supposed to have been<BR> deprived of its tongue by the curse of Agni whom frogs had offended.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीकवम्
अजीकवम् [अज्या शरक्षेपणेन कं ब्रह्माणं वाति प्रीणाति बा-क] Śivaʼs bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्तः|अजीगर्त|अजीगर्त्त
अजीगर्तः [अज्यै गमनाय गर्तम् अस्य]<BR>—1 (One that has a hole to go into) a serpent.<BR>—2 N. of a Brāhmaṇa in the family of भृगु and father of शुनःशेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीत
अजीत <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not faded or withered, not faint.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अजीतपुनर्वर्ण्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीतपुनर्वर्ण्यम्
अजीत + -पुनर्वर्ण्यम् N. of a two-fold rite to be performed by Kṣatriyas<BR> (अप्राप्तप्राप्तिकरणार्थो विधिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीतिः|अजीति
अजीतिः <i>f.</i> Prosperity, freedom from decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण <i>a.</i> Undigested; undecomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्णम्
अजीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्, -र्णिः@} <i>f.</i> —1 Indigestion; अजीर्णे भेषजं वारि जीर्णे<BR> वारि बलप्रदम्, अजीर्णे भोजनं विषम्; कैरजीर्णभयांद् भ्रातर्भोजनं परिहीयते<BR> H. 2. 57; Ms. 4. 121. —2 Vigour, energy, absence of decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्णिः|अजीर्णि
अजीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्, -र्णिः@} <i>f.</i> —1 Indigestion; अजीर्णे भेषजं वारि जीर्णे<BR> वारि बलप्रदम्, अजीर्णे भोजनं विषम्; कैरजीर्णभयांद् भ्रातर्भोजनं परिहीयते<BR> H. 2. 57; Ms. 4. 121. —2 Vigour, energy, absence of decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीव|अजीवः
अजीव <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Devoid of life; lifeless, as a jar<BR> or a dead person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवः|अजीव
अजीव + .{@-वः@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Non-existence, death.<BR>—2 (With Jainas) All that is not a living soul, <i>i. e.</i> the whole of<BR> जड or inanimate and unsentient substance (opp. जीव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवन
अजीवन <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Devoid of livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनम्
अजीवन + .{@-नम्@} Non-existence, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनिः|अजीवनि
अजीवनिः <i>f.</i> [न-जीव्-अनि P. III. 3. 112] —1 Death, non-existence<BR> (used as an imprecation); अजीवनिस्ते शठ भूयात् Sk. may death seize<BR> thee, rogue! mayest thou cease to live! cf. also अभावे भवतां योऽस्मिन्<BR> जीवेत्तस्यास्त्वजीवनिः । Bk. 7. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुर
अजुर, -र्य <i>a.</i><BR> [अज्-कुरच् न व्यादेशः] Ved. Not subject to decay<BR> or old age; strong, very swift or speedy. अवकक्षिणं वृषभं यथाऽजुरम् Rv. 8. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुर्य
अजुर, -र्य <i>a.</i><BR> [अज्-कुरच् न व्यादेशः] Ved. Not subject to decay<BR> or old age; strong, very swift or speedy. अवकक्षिणं वृषभं यथाऽजुरम् Rv. 8. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुष्टि|अजुष्टिः
अजुष्टि <i>f.</i> Non-enjoyment; feeling of dissatisfaction or disappointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेय|अजेयः
अजेय <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not fit to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेयम्
अजेय + .{@-यम्@} A sort of medicinal preparation of ghee said to serve as<BR> an antidote; पिबेत् घृतमजेयाख्यम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजोष
अजोष <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not gratified or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जु(ज्जू)का [अर्जयति या सा, अर्ज्-ऊक, पृषो रकारस्य जत्वम्<BR> Tv.] A courtezan (used only in dramas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जूका
अज्जु(ज्जू)का [अर्जयति या सा, अर्ज्-ऊक, पृषो रकारस्य जत्वम्<BR> Tv.] A courtezan (used only in dramas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जम्
अज्जम् (see अज्झलम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झटा
अज्झटा [Said to be fr. अज्] N. of a plant भूम्यामलकी Flacourtia<BR> Cataphracta. (Mar. भुईआंबळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झलम्
अज्झलम्<BR>—1 A shield.<BR>—2 A live coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञ|अज्ञः
अज्ञ <i>a.</i> [न जानाति, ज्ञा-क. न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not knowing, unaware of, unconscious, devoid of knowledge or experience;<BR> अज्ञो भवति वै बालः Ms. 2. 153; ज्ञाज्ञौ (ज्ञः ईश्वरः अज्ञः जीवः)<BR> the knowing and unknowing, supreme and individual soul.<BR>—2 Ignorant, unwise, foolish, silly, stupid (said of men as well as animals);<BR> अज्ञः सुखमाराध्यः Bh. 1. 3; Pt. 2. 3.<BR>—3 Inanimate; not endowed with the power of understanding (अचेतन..)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञका
अज्ञका [स्वार्थे कन्] An ignorant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात
अज्ञात <i>a.</i> Unknown, unexpected, unconscious, unaware; ˚भुक्त,<BR> संवत्सरस्यैकमपि चरेत्कृच्छ्रं द्विजोत्तमः । अज्ञातभुक्तशुद्धयर्थ ज्ञातस्य<BR> तु विशेषतः ॥ Ms. 5. 21 eaten unconsciously or unawares; ˚कुलशीलस्य<BR> whose family and character are unknown; ˚पातं सलिले ममज्ज R. 16. 72.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अज्ञातकेत, अज्ञातवस्तुशास्त्रम्, अज्ञातचर्या, अज्ञातवासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातकेत
अज्ञात + -केत <i>a.</i> [ब˚] Ved. of secret designs. अज्ञातकेता वृजिना<BR> अभूवन् Rv. 5. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातवस्तुशास्त्रम्
अज्ञात + -वस्तुशास्त्रम् Agnoiology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातचर्या
अज्ञात + -चर्या, -वासः remaining <i>incognito</i> (said of the Pāṇḍavas);<BR> हंसाः संप्रति पाण्डवा इव वनादज्ञातचर्यां गताः Mk. 5. 6; Mb. 3. 185. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातवासः|अज्ञातवास
अज्ञात + -चर्या, -वासः remaining <i>incognito</i> (said of the Pāṇḍavas);<BR> हंसाः संप्रति पाण्डवा इव वनादज्ञातचर्यां गताः Mk. 5. 6; Mb. 3. 185. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातिः|अज्ञाति
अज्ञातिः [न˚ त˚] Not a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञान|अज्ञानं
अज्ञान <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Ignorant, unwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानम्
अज्ञान + .{@-नम्@} [न˚ त˚] Ignorance, unconsciousness; especially,<BR> spirtual ignorance (अविद्या) which makes one consider his self as distinct<BR> from the Supreme spirit and the material world as a reality. According<BR> to the Vedāntins, अज्ञान is not merely a negative principle (ज्ञानस्य<BR> अभावः), but a distinct positive principle; oft. identified with माया,<BR> प्रकृति &c. See अविद्या also In compounds अज्ञान may be translated<BR> by ‘unawares’, ‘inadvertently’, ‘unconsciously’; ˚आचरित, ˚उच्चारित<BR> &c.;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानतः
अज्ञान + .{@-नम्@} + ˚नतः, ˚नेन, ˚नात् unawares, inadvertently, unconsciously,<BR> unwillingly ˚तः स्वचरितं नृपतिः शशंस R. 9. 77 committed unintentionally<BR> or unconsciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानेन
अज्ञान + .{@-नम्@} + ˚नतः, ˚नेन, ˚नात् unawares, inadvertently, unconsciously,<BR> unwillingly ˚तः स्वचरितं नृपतिः शशंस R. 9. 77 committed unintentionally<BR> or unconsciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानात्
अज्ञान + .{@-नम्@} + ˚नतः, ˚नेन, ˚नात् unawares, inadvertently, unconsciously,<BR> unwillingly ˚तः स्वचरितं नृपतिः शशंस R. 9. 77 committed unintentionally<BR> or unconsciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानपरीक्षा
अज्ञान + .{@-परीक्षा@} See अज्ञातवस्तुशास्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानिन्
अज्ञानिन् = अज्ञ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञेय
अज्ञेय <i>a.</i> unknowable, unfit to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञेय
अज्ञेय + ˚वादः Agnosticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्मन्
अज्मन् <i>f.</i> [अजति गच्छति स्वर्गं दानेन अनया, अज्-करणे मनिन्<BR> न वीभावः] A cow. ━<i>n.</i> Career, passage; battle; house (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्येष्ठ
अज्येष्ठ <i>a.</i> Not the eldest or best, having no elder brothers;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्येष्ठवृत्ति|अज्येष्ठवृत्तिः
अज्येष्ठ + ˚वृत्ति not acting like the elder brothers; or acting like one who has<BR> no elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र|अज्रः
अज्र <i>a.</i> [fr. अज् to go] Ved. Agile, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्रः|अज्र
अज्र + .{@-ज्रः@} A field, plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र|अज्रः
अज्र + .{@-ज्र@} <i>a.</i> Being in or connected with a field or plain; समज्या<BR> पर्वत्या वसूनि Rv. 10. 69. 6. [cf. L. <i>ager</i>; Gr. <i>agros</i>.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्विन्
अज्विन् <i>a.</i> Ved. [fr. अज्] Quick, agile, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च्|अंच्
अञ्च् €1 U. (अञ्चु) (अञ्चति-ते, आनञ्च-ञ्चे, अञ्चितुम्, अच्यात् or अञ्च्यात्, अक्त or अञ्चित)<BR>—1 To bend, incline, curl, curve; शिरोऽञ्चित्वा Bk. 9. 40.<BR>—2 To go, move, tend towards; स्वतन्त्रा कथमञ्चसि Bk. 4. 22; also<BR> in अवाञ्च्; tending downward, प्राञ्च्, उदञ्च्; विश्वगञ्चति, सहाञ्चति,<BR> तिरोऽञ्चति &c.; तस्मिन्नद्य रसालशाखिनि दशां दैवात् कृशामञ्चति<BR> Bv. 1. 48 having gone, being reduced to, &c.; त्वं चेदञ्चसि लोभम् 46,<BR> art greedy; संकोचमञ्चति सरः 17.<BR>—3 To worship, honour, reverence; भीमोऽयं शिरसाञ्चति Ve. 5. 28.<BR> salutes; to adorn, grace; see अञ्चित below.<BR>—4 To request, ask or call for, desire.<BR>—5 To murmur, speak indistinctly. ━<i>Caus.</i> or €10 U. To manifest,<BR> unfold; मुदमञ्चय Gīt. 10. [cf. Zend. <i>anku</i>; Gr. <i>ankulos</i>;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">Page0034-2</a>]<BR> L. <i>uncus</i>.] ━<i>With</i> {@अप@} to put away, drive away; (intr.) to run away.<BR>━{@आ@} to bend; दक्षिणं जान्वाच्य; जान्वाक with bent knees.<BR>━{@उप@} to draw or raise (water).<BR>━{@परि@} to cause to revolve, whirl, twist.<BR>━{@वि@} to draw or bend asunder; to extend, stretch out.<BR>━{@सम्@} to crowd or drive together, to bend together. See समक्न<BR> also; to go properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चित|अंचित|अञ्चितः
अञ्चित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Curved, bent; ˚उचित Dk. 125, bent and raised; किंचिदञ्चितां<BR> दृष्टिं संचारयन्ती 143, bent or oblique look; दोलींलाञ्चितचन्द्रशेखरधनुः<BR> Mv. 1. 54 bent; ˚सव्यजानुः R. 18. 51. अञ्चितदक्षिणोरुः Bk. 2. 31, 9. 40;<BR> ˚लाङ्गूलः (कपिः), ˚स्कन्धः (वृक्षः).<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Arched and handsome (as eyebrows); ˚अक्षिपक्ष्मन् R. 5. 76;<BR> crisped, curled (as hair); स्वसिताञ्चितमूर्धजा Mb.<BR>—2 Gone.<BR>—3 Honoured; adorned, graced, graceful, handsome, दोर्दण्डाञ्चितमहिमा<BR> अञ्चितामादधानः Mv. 7. 8 graced, adorned; गतेषु लीलाञ्चितविक्रमेषु<BR> Ku. 1. 34. cf. also कनकाचलसंकाशदेवतायतनाञ्चिते Śiva B. 9. 53.<BR> sportively handsome; ˚ताभ्यां गताभ्याम् R. 2. 18, लीलाञ्चितभ्रूलता<BR> Dk. 124, 151; समधुरं मधुरञ्चितविकमः R. 9. 24 of esteemed or<BR> a adorable prowess; (अङ्गानि) रोमाञ्चमञ्चिततरं बिभराम्बभूवुः Ki. 15. 53.<BR>—4 Sewn or woven, arranged; अर्धाञ्चिता सत्वरमुत्थितायाः (रशना)<BR> R. 7. 10 half-strung or woven (गुम्फित Malli.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्चितपत्रम्, अञ्चितभ्रूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चितपत्रम्
अञ्चित + -पत्रम् [ब˚] a lotus with curved leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चितभ्रूः
अञ्चित + -भ्रूः a woman having arched or handsome eyebrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चतिः|अञ्चति|अंचतिः
अञ्चतिः [अञ्च्-गतौ कर्तरि अति]<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 One who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चलः|अञ्चल|अंचलं|अंचलः
अञ्चलः, -लम्<BR> [अञ्चति प्रान्तम्; अञ्च्-अलच्]<BR>—1 The border or end (of a garment), skirt or hem (Mar. पदर); क्षीणाञ्चलमिव<BR> पीनस्तनजघनायाः Udb. विमुञ्च ममाञ्चलम् Bv. 2. 21.<BR>—2 Corner or outer angle (as of the eye); दृगञ्चलैः पश्यति केवलं<BR> मनाक् <i>ibid.</i>; यदि चलाञ्चले लोचने Mv. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चलम्
अञ्चलः, -लम्<BR> [अञ्चति प्रान्तम्; अञ्च्-अलच्]<BR>—1 The border or end (of a garment), skirt or hem (Mar. पदर); क्षीणाञ्चलमिव<BR> पीनस्तनजघनायाः Udb. विमुञ्च ममाञ्चलम् Bv. 2. 21.<BR>—2 Corner or outer angle (as of the eye); दृगञ्चलैः पश्यति केवलं<BR> मनाक् <i>ibid.</i>; यदि चलाञ्चले लोचने Mv. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्ज्|अंज्
अञ्ज् €7 P. (rarely Ā.) (अनक्ति or अङ्क्ते, आनञ्ज, अञ्जिष्यति-अङ्क्ष्यति,<BR> अञ्जित्वा-अङ्क्त्वा-अक्त्वा, अञ्जितुम्, अङ्क्तुम्, अक्त)<BR>—1 To anoint, smear with, bedaub.<BR>—2 To make clear, show, represent, characterize; मा नाञ्जी राक्षसीर्मायाः Bk. 9. 49.<BR>—3 To go.<BR>—4 To shine, be beautiful.<BR>—5 To honour, celebrate.<BR>—6 To decorate. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To smear with, नाञ्जयन्ती स्वके नेत्रे Ms. 4. 44.<BR>—2 To speak or shine.<BR>—3 To cause to go. [cf. Zend. <i>anj</i>; L. <i>unctum, ungo</i>.] ━<i>With</i> {@अधि@}<BR> to fit out, equip, furnish.<BR>━{@आ@}<BR>—1 to anoint, smear.<BR>—2 to smooth, polish, prepare.<BR>—3 to honour, respect.<BR>━{@नि@}<BR>—1 to smear.<BR>—2 to conceal or hide oneself.<BR>━{@प्रति@}<BR>—1 to smear.<BR>—2 to adorn, decorate.<BR>━{@सम्@}<BR>—1 to smear.<BR>—2 to fit out, equip, harness.<BR>—3 to honour.<BR>—4 to join together, to consume, devour; to adorn, decorate, beautify<BR> (mostly Ved. in these senses).<BR>—5 to unite, to put together, compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनः|अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अंजनः
अञ्जनः<BR>—1 A kind of lizard.<BR>—2 N. of a tree or mountain.<BR>—3 N. of the guardian elephant (of the west or s. w.) तस्य चान्येऽपि<BR> दिङ्नागा बभूवुरनुयायिनः । अञ्जनो वामनश्चैव महापद्मश्च सुप्रभः ॥ Mb. 6. 64. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनम्
अञ्जनः + .{@-नम्@} [अज्यते अनेन; अञ्ज्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">Page0035-1</a>]<BR> ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Anointing, smearing with, दन्तधावनमञ्जनं पूर्वाह्व एव कुर्वीत<BR> Ms. 4. 152; mixing; unfolding, manifesting.<BR>—2 Collyrium or black pigment used to paint the eyelashes; विलोचनं<BR> दक्षिणमञ्जनेन संभाव्य R. 7. 8 salve; अमृत ˚कोऽयं दृशोरमृताञ्जनम्<BR> U. 4. 18 ambrosial salve; कुर्वन् ˚मेचका इव दिशो मेघः समुत्तिष्ठते<BR> Mk. 5. 8, 1. 34; (fig. also) अज्ञानान्धस्य लोकस्य ज्ञानाञ्जनशलाकया ।<BR> चक्षुरुन्मीलितं येन तस्मै पाणिनये नमः ॥ Śik. 45; पटुतरविवेकाञ्जनजुषाम्<BR> Bh. 3. 84; cf. also दारिद्र्यं परमाञ्जनम्; (fig.) impurity, as in<BR> निरञ्जन, q. v.<BR>—3 Paint, a cosmetic ointment.<BR>—4 Magic ointment.<BR>—5 A special kind of material of the black pigment, such as antimony (used<BR> as collyrium, lamp-black &c.) (सौवीर).<BR>—6 Ink.<BR>—7 Fire.<BR>—8 Night.<BR>—9 (नम्, ना) (Rhet.) A suggested meaning; also the process by which<BR> such meaning is suggested. It is the power of suggestion (founded on अभिधा<BR> or लक्षणा denotation or indication), by which something else is understood<BR> from a word which, though having more meanings than one, has been restricted<BR> to a single meaning by relations of conjunction, disjunction &c. (संयोग,<BR> विप्रयोग, साहचर्य, विरोधिता &c.), or, briefly, the use of a word<BR> of several meanings in a special sense determined by the context; <i>e. g.</i><BR> सशङ्घचक्रो हरिः the adjective restricts Hari to mean ‘Viṣṇu’<BR> alone, and not a ‘lion’ or ‘monkey’; so रामलक्ष्मणौ दाशरथी, रामार्जुनौ<BR> भार्गवकार्तवीर्यौ &c.; cf. अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्य वाचकत्वे नियन्त्रिते ।<BR> संयोगाद्यैरवाच्यार्थधीकृद् व्यापृतिरञ्जनम् ॥ K. P. 2.; S. D. 23-6;<BR> See व्यञ्जना also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्जनाधिका, अञ्जनाद्रिः, अञ्जनगिरिः, अञ्जनाम्भस्, अञ्जनकेशी, अञ्जनत्रितयम्, अञ्जननामका, अञ्जनमूलकः, अञ्जनशलाका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाधिका
अञ्जनः + -अधिका [अञ्जनादधिका कृष्णत्वात्] a kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाद्रिः|अञ्जनाद्रि
अञ्जनः + -अद्रिः, -गिरिः (कर्म˚) [अञ्जनमिव कृष्णः गिरिः] N. of<BR> a mountain. See नीलगिरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनगिरिः|अञ्जनगिरि
अञ्जनः + -अद्रिः, -गिरिः (कर्म˚) [अञ्जनमिव कृष्णः गिरिः] N. of<BR> a mountain. See नीलगिरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाम्भस्
अञ्जनः + -अम्भस् <i>n.</i> eye-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनकेशी
अञ्जनः + -केशी [अञ्जनमिव केशो यस्याः] N. of a vegetable perfume (हट्टविलासिनीनामकं<BR> गन्धद्रव्यं यत्संयोगात्केशस्यातीव कृष्णत्वम्) (Mar. नखला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनत्रितयम्
अञ्जनः + -त्रितयम् (Āyurveda) पुष्पाञ्जन, रसाञ्जन and कोलाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जननामका
अञ्जनः + -नामका [ष˚ त˚] a swelling of the eye-lid, sty (Mar.<BR> रांजणवाडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनमूलकः|अञ्जनमूलक
अञ्जनः + -मूलकः A variety of an inferior gem, deep-dark in colour. Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनशलाका
अञ्जनः + -शलाका a stick or pencil for the application of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जकः|अञ्जक
अञ्जकः N. of the son of Viprachitti; V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनकः|अञ्जनक|अंजनकः
अञ्जनकः A portion of the Vedas containing the word अञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनकी
अञ्जनकः + .{@-की@} N. of a medicinal plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनता
अञ्जनता Identity. (Pātaṅjala Yogadarśana, I. 41).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जना|अंजना
अञ्जना<BR>—1 N. of the female elephant of the north.<BR>—2 N. of the mother of Māruti or Hanūmat. [She was the daughter of a<BR> monkey named Kuñjara and wife of Kesarin, another monkey. She was in<BR> a former birth a celestial nymph by name Puñjikasthali and was born on<BR> earth owing to a curse. One day while she was seated on the summit of<BR> a mountain, her garment was slightly displaced, and the God of Wind being<BR> enamoured of her beauty assumed a visible form, and asked her to yield<BR> to his desires. She requested him not to violate her chastity, to which<BR> he consented; but he told her that she would conceive a son equal to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">Page0035-2</a>]<BR> himself in strength and lustre by virtue of his amorous desire fixed on<BR> her, and then disappeared. In course of time Añjanā conceived and brought<BR> forth a son who was called Māruti being the son of Marut.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनावती|अंजनावती
अञ्जनावती [अञ्जनं विद्यते अस्याः अधिककृष्णवर्णत्वात्]<BR>—1 N. of the female elephant of the north-east quarter.<BR>—2 N. of a tree कालाञ्जनवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनिका|अंजनिका
अञ्जनिका [अञ्जना स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>—1 A species of lizard; a small mouse.<BR>—2 N. of the mate of the elephant सुप्रतीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनी|अंजनी
अञ्जनी [अज्यते चन्दनकुङ्कुमादिभिरसौ, अञ्ज्-कर्मणि-ल्युट् डीप्]<BR>—1 A woman decorated with the application of pigments, ointments, sandal<BR> &c., or one fit for such application.<BR>—2 [करणे-ल्युट्] N. of two plants कटुकावृक्ष and कालाञ्जनवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिः|अञ्जलि|अंजलिः
अञ्जलिः <i>m.</i> [अञ्ज्-अलि Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>—1 A cavity formed by folding and joining the open hands together, the<BR> hollow of the hands; hence, a cavity. full of anything (changed to अञ्जल<BR> or ˚लि after द्वि and त्रि in द्विगु comp., P. V. 4. 102);<BR> न वार्यञ्जलिना पिबेत् Ms. 4. 63; सुपूरो मूषिकाञ्जलिः Pt. 1. 25;<BR> अरण्यबीजाञ्जलिदानलालिताः Ku. 5. 15; प्रकीर्णः पुष्पाणां हरिचरणयोरञ्जलिस्यम्<BR> Ve. 1. 1 a cavity-ful of flowers; so जलस्याञ्जलयो दश Y. 3. 105. 10<BR> cavity-fuls or libations of water; श्रवणाञ्जलिपुटपेयम् Ve. 1. 4.<BR> to be drunk by the cavity of the ear; अञ्जलिं रच्, बन्ध्, कृ or आधा<BR> fold the hands together and raise them to the head in supplication<BR> or salutation; बद्धः, कातर्यादरविन्दकुड्मलनिभो मुग्धः प्रणामाञ्जलिः U. 3. 37.<BR>—2 Hence {sic} a mark of respect or salutation; कः शक्रेण कृतं नेच्छेदधिमूर्धानमञ्जलिम्<BR> Bk. 8. 84; बध्यतामभययाचनाञ्जलिः R. 11. 78.<BR>—3 A measure of corn = कुडव; another measure = प्रसृत, or one-half<BR> of a मानिका.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्जलिकर्मन्, अञ्जलिकारिका, अञ्जलिपुटः, अञ्जलिपुटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकर्मन्|अञ्जलिकर्म्मन्
अञ्जलिः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> folding the hands, respectful salutation; लुब्धमर्थेन गृह्वीयात् क्रुद्धं चाञ्जलिकर्मणा Cāṇ. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकारिका
अञ्जलिः + -कारिका<BR>—1 an earthen doll making the अञ्जलि (?).<BR>—2 N. of a plant, Mimosa Pudica (लज्जालु) (Mar. लाजाळू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिपुटः|अञ्जलिपुट
अञ्जलिः + -पुटः, -पुटम् the cavity formed by joining the hands together; hollowed<BR> palms of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिपुटम्
अञ्जलिः + -पुटः, -पुटम् the cavity formed by joining the hands together; hollowed<BR> palms of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिका|अंजलिका
अञ्जलिका [अञ्जलिरिव कायते प्रकाशते; कै-क टाप् Tv.].<BR>—1 A small mouse.<BR>—2 The sensitive plant of Mimosa Pudica (Mar. लाजाळू).<BR>—3 An insect of the spider tribe (Mar. कांतीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकः|अञ्जलिक
अञ्जलिका + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of one of Arjunaʼs arrows.<BR>—2 अञ्जल्याकारमुख (mouse-mouthed) arrow भल्लैरञ्जलिकैरपि Rām. 6. 45. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकावेध
अञ्जलिका + .{@-वेध@} a fighting stratagem जानन्नञ्जलिकावेधं नापाक्रामत पाण्डवः Mb. 7. 26. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस्|अंजस्
अञ्जस् <i>n.</i> (-जः) [अनक्ति गच्छति मिश्रयति वा अनेन;<BR> अञ्ज् गतौ मिश्रणे च-असन्] Speed, velocity, strength; fitness, propriety;<BR> ointment, preparation (?).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्जःपा, अञ्जःसवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जः|अञ्ज
अञ्जस् <i>n.</i> (-जः) [अनक्ति गच्छति मिश्रयति वा अनेन;<BR> अञ्ज् गतौ मिश्रणे च-असन्] Speed, velocity, strength; fitness, propriety;<BR> ointment, preparation (?).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्जःपा, अञ्जःसवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जःपा
अञ्जस् + -पा drinking instantly इममञ्जस्पामुभये अकृण्वत Rv. 10. 92. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जःसवः|अञ्जःसव
अञ्जस् + -सवः rapid preparation of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस|अंजस|अञ्जसः
अञ्जस <i>a.</i> [अञ्ज्-असच्] Not crooked, straight; honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसा|अंजसा
अञ्जसा <i>adv.</i> (instr. of अञ्जस्)<BR>—1 Straight on.<BR>—2 Truly, correctly, accurately, properly, justly; साक्षाद् दृष्टोऽसि न<BR> पुनर्विद्मस्त्वां वयमञ्जसा Ku. 6. 22 we do not know you rightly or<BR> correctly; विद्म हे शठ पलायनच्छलान्यञ्जसा R. 19. 31, न हि कश्चित्प्रियः<BR> स्त्रीणामञ्जसा Subhāṣ.; सर्वमेवाञ्जसा वद Ms. 8. 101.<BR>—3 Directly (साक्षात्),<BR>—4 Soon, quickly, instantly; स गच्छत्यञ्जसा विप्रो ब्रह्मणः सद्म<BR> शाश्वतम् Ms. 2. 244. … अञ्जसा तत्त्वतूर्णयोः । Nm. वशमानेतुमञ्जसा ।<BR> Śiva B. 25. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अञ्जसायन, अञ्जसाकृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0036-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसायन
अञ्जसा + -अयन <i>a.</i> going straight on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0036-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसाकृत
अञ्जसा + -कृत <i>a.</i> [तृ. अलुक्] done rightly or justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0036-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसीन|अंजसीन
