अण्
अण् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sound.<BR>—2 (€4 Ā.) To breathe, live (for अन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0037-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणक|अणकः
अण(न)क <i>a.</i> [अणति यथेच्छं नदति, अण्-अच् कुत्सायां कन् च]<BR> Very small, contemptible, mean, insignificant, wretched; पापाणके कुत्सितैः<BR> P. II. 1. 54; oft. in comp. in the sense of deterioration or contempt;<BR> ˚कुलालः Sk. a contemptible potter. cf. also मृतेऽपि त्वयि जीवन्त्या<BR> किं मयाणकभार्यया Bk. 14. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0037-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अण(न)क <i>a.</i> [अणति यथेच्छं नदति, अण्-अच् कुत्सायां कन् च]<BR> Very small, contemptible, mean, insignificant, wretched; पापाणके कुत्सितैः<BR> P. II. 1. 54; oft. in comp. in the sense of deterioration or contempt;<BR> ˚कुलालः Sk. a contemptible potter. cf. also मृतेऽपि त्वयि जीवन्त्या<BR> किं मयाणकभार्यया Bk. 14. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0037-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

