अण्डालुः [अण्डः अस्ति अस्य; अण्ड-आलुच्] A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डीरः|अण्डीर|अंडीरः
अण्डीरः [अण्डः अस्ति अस्य; अण्ड-ईरच् P. V. 2. 3.] A full-grown<BR> or full-developed man, a strong or powerful person; चिरादण्डीरेण त्वयि<BR> तदपि रामेण गुणितम् A. R. 4. See आण्डीर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्|अन्त्|अंत्
अत् €1 P. (अति), अतति, अतितुम्, अत्त-अतित<BR>—1 To go, walk; wander, to go constantly.<BR>—2 To obtain (mostly Ved.)<BR>—3 To bind.<BR>—4 (अन्तति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतकः|अतक
अतकः [अतति सततं गच्छति; अत्-कन्] A wanderer, a passer-by, traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनम्
अतनम् [अत्-ल्युट्] Going, wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनः|अतन|अतनं
अतनम् + .{@-नः@} A wanderer, a passer-by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतज्ज्ञ
अतज्ज्ञ <i>a.</i> [न तत्-जानाति] Not knowing that (तत् i. e. Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतट|अतटः
अतट <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Having no shore or beach; precipitate, steep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतटः|अतट
अतट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A precipice, a steep crag.<BR>—2 N. of a hill.<BR>—3 The lower part of the earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतटप्रपातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतटप्रपातः|अतटप्रपात
अतट + -प्रपातः a steep precipice; a fall headlong from a precipice; a precipitate fall; मनोरथानामतटप्रपातः Ś. 6. 10 of my hopes<BR> there is a precipitate fall. (Some read the line as मनोरथा नाम तटप्रपातः<BR> and take it to mean ‘verily our desires are like the crumblings of river banks’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथा
अतथा <i>ind.</i> Not so;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथा
अतथा + ˚उचित <i>a.</i> not deserving that, not<BR> used to such things; क्लेशानामतथोचितः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतदर्हम्
अतदर्हम् <i>ind.</i> Unjustly, undeservedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतद्गुणः|अतद्गुण
अतद्गुणः (Rhet.) The ‘non-borrower’, N. of a figure of speech in<BR> which the thing in question does not assume the quality of another, though<BR> there is a reason for it; परगुणाननुहारस्त्वस्य तत्स्यादतद्गृणः;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> धवलो ऽसि यद्यपि सुन्दर तथापि त्वया मम रञ्जितं हृदयम् ।<BR> रागपूरितेऽपि हृदये सुभग निहितो न रक्तोऽसि ॥ K. P. 10; or संगतान्यगुणानङ्गीकारमाहुरतद्गुणम् ।<BR> चिरं रागिणि मच्चित्ते निहितोऽपि न रज्यसि ॥ Kuval.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतद्गुणसंविज्ञानः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतद्गुणसंविज्ञानः|अतद्गुणसंविज्ञान
अतद्गुणः + -संविज्ञानः N. of a variety of Bahuvrīhi; <i>e. g.</i> दृष्टसमुद्रमानय;<BR> अत्र गुणीभूतस्य समुद्रस्य नानयनेऽन्वयः इति न˚ बहुव्रीहिः; लम्बकर्णमानय<BR> इति तु तद्गुणसंविज्ञानः. Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्त्र|अतंत्र
अतन्त्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Having no ropes or musical strings (as a musical instrument); नातन्त्री<BR> वाद्यते वीणा Rām.<BR>—2 Unrestrained; not necessarily binding; not being the object of the<BR> rule under consideration; ह्रस्वग्रहणमतन्त्रम्, क्लीबत्वं ˚न्त्रम्<BR> Sk. Something which is not intended; on which there is no emphasis or stress<BR> (वार्त्तिक 2. 2. 34. 1).<BR>—3 Without formulas or empirical actions.<BR>—4 Not (having the binding force of) a scientific statement; तत्राविज्ञातग्रहणमतन्त्रमिति<BR> कल्प्येत । ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्त्रत्वम्
अतन्त्र + .{@-त्वम्@} meaninglessness, superfluity, superfluous nature. किं<BR> तु इतरस्मिन् पक्षे बाध्यतेतरां श्रुतिः । ऐन्द्रशब्दस्यातन्त्रत्वात् । ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्र|अतंद्र
अतन्द्र, -न्द्रित, -न्, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Alert, unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतन्द्रिता<BR> सा स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14; R. 17. 39; H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रित|अतंद्रित
अतन्द्र, -न्द्रित, -न्, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Alert, unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतन्द्रिता<BR> सा स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14; R. 17. 39; H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रिन्|अतंद्रिन्
अतन्द्र, -न्द्रित, -न्, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Alert, unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतन्द्रिता<BR> सा स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14; R. 17. 39; H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रिल
अतन्द्र, -न्द्रित, -न्, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Alert, unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतन्द्रिता<BR> सा स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14; R. 17. 39; H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनु
अतनु <i>a.</i> More वीतप्रभावतनुरप्यतनुप्रभावः Ki. 16. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप
अतप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not excited, cool.<BR>—2 Unostentatious.<BR>—3 Unemployed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपाः
अतप + .{@-पाः@} (pl.) N. of a class of deities among Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्
अतपस्, -स्क<BR> [न˚ ब˚] One who neglects his religious austerities;<BR> अतपास्त्वनधीयानः Ms. 4. 190; an irreligious or impious man; इदं<BR> ते नातपस्काय Bg. 18. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्क
अतपस्, -स्क<BR> [न˚ ब˚] One who neglects his religious austerities;<BR> अतपास्त्वनधीयानः Ms. 4. 190; an irreligious or impious man; इदं<BR> ते नातपस्काय Bg. 18. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्त
अतप्त <i>a.</i> Not heated &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतप्ततनु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्ततनु
अतप्त + -तनु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One whose body is not marked (with red mudrās &c.).<BR>—2 who has not fully mortified his body by penance. अतप्ततनूर्न तदामो<BR> अश्नुते Rv. 9. 83. 1.<BR>—3 whose body or mass is cool (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क|अतर्कः
अतर्क <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Illogical, void of reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कः|अतर्क
अतर्क + .{@-र्कः@}<BR>—1 Absence of argument or reasoning, bad logic.<BR>—2 An illogical reasoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कित
अतर्कित <i>a.</i> Unthought of, unexpected सममेव गतोऽस्यतर्कितां<BR> गतिमङ्गेन च जीवितेन च Ku. 4. 22; Bh. 3. 137. ˚गमनेन Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कितम्
अतर्कित + .{@-तम्@} <i>adv.</i> Unexpectedly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतर्कितागत, अतर्कितोपनत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कितागत
अतर्कित + -आगत, -उपनत <i>a.</i> occuring or befalling unexpectedly, quite<BR> accidental, sudden; ˚दर्शनोल्लासितलोचनया अनया Māl. 3; ˚उपपन्नं<BR> दर्शनम् Ku. 6. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कितोपनत
अतर्कित + -आगत, -उपनत <i>a.</i> occuring or befalling unexpectedly, quite<BR> accidental, sudden; ˚दर्शनोल्लासितलोचनया अनया Māl. 3; ˚उपपन्नं<BR> दर्शनम् Ku. 6. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अतर्क्य <i>a.</i> Inconceivable; baffling thought or reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अतल <i>a.</i> Bottomless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलम्
अतल + .{@-लम्@} [अस्य भूखण्डस्य तलं पृषो˚ इदमोऽत्वम्] N. of a पाताल<BR> or lower region, one of the 7 Pātālas, being the first among them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलः|अतल|अतलं
अतल + .{@-लः@} N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतलस्पृश्, अतलस्पर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पृश्
अतल + -स्पृश्, -स्पर्श <i>a.</i> [न तले स्पृश्यते कर्मणि क्विप्; न<BR> तलस्य स्पर्शो यत्र] bottomless, very deep, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पर्श|अतलस्पर्शः
अतल + -स्पृश्, -स्पर्श <i>a.</i> [न तले स्पृश्यते कर्मणि क्विप्; न<BR> तलस्य स्पर्शो यत्र] bottomless, very deep, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतव्यस्
अतव्यस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not very strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस् <i>ind.</i> [इदं-तसिल्]<BR>—1 Than this; from this (having a comparative force); अतो देवा अवन्तु<BR> नो यतो विष्णुर्विचक्रमे Rv. 1. 22. 16; किमु परमतो नर्तयसि माम्<BR> Bh. 3. 6; अतोऽन्यथा Ms. 5. 31.<BR>—2 From this or that cause, hence, consequenty, so, therefore (corr. to<BR> यत्, यस्मात् or हि, expressed or understood); अन्तर्गतं प्राणभृतां<BR> हि वेद सर्वं भवान्भावमतोऽभिधास्ये R. 2. 43, 3. 50; Ku. 2. 5; अथातो<BR> ब्रह्मजिज्ञासा Ś. B. now therefore &c.<BR>—3 Hence, from this place; henceforth (of time or place); (-परम्, -ऊर्ध्वम्), afterwards.<BR>—4 Then (corr. of यदि-यद्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतोर्थम्, अतोनिमित्तम्, अतएव, अतऊर्ध्वम्, अतःपरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोर्थम्
अतस् + -अर्थम्, -निमित्तम् on this account, hence, for this reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोनिमित्तम्
अतस् + -अर्थम्, -निमित्तम् on this account, hence, for this reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतएव
अतस् + -एव for this very reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतऊर्ध्वम्
अतस् + -ऊर्ध्वम् henceforth; afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतःपरम्
अतस् + -परम्<BR>——(<i>a</i>) further on, any longer (with abl.); hereafter; निवसिष्यसि<BR> मग्येव अत ऊर्ध्वम् Bg. 12. 8.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) beyond this, further than this; भाग्यायत्तमतःपरम् Ś. 4. 16<BR> more than this; अतःपरं नास्ति ममोत्तरम् V. 2 <i>now</i> I have<BR> nothing more to say;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसः|अतस
अतसः [अतति गच्छति इत्यतसः अत्-असच् Uṇ. 3. 117]<BR>—1 Wind, air.<BR>—2 The soul.<BR>—3 A garment made of the fibre of flax (˚सं generally).<BR>—4 A weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसिः|अतसि
अतसिः Ved. [अत्-असिच्] A wandering mendicant. कन्नव्यो अतसीनां<BR> तुरो गृणीत मर्त्यः Rv. 8. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसिका
अतसिका Flax; Bhāg. 3. 28. 24; see अतसी 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसी
अतसी<BR>—1 Common flax.<BR>—2 Hemp.<BR>—3 Linseed. (Mar. अळशी) अतसीपुष्पसंकाशम् Mb. 12. 47. 90<BR>—4 A thicket, copse (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति <i>ind.</i> [अत्-इ]<BR>—1 A prefix used with adjectives and adverbs, meaning ‘very’, ‘too’, ‘exceedingly’,<BR> ‘excessively’, ‘very much’, and showing उत्कर्ष; Surpassing, superior<BR> अत्याश्रमानयं सर्वान् Mb. 12. 12. 6. नातिदूरे not very far from;<BR> ˚कृश very lean; ˚भृशम् very much; also with verbs or verbal forms;<BR> ˚सिक्तमेव भवता Sk.; स्वभावो ह्यतिरिच्यते &c.<BR>—2 (With verbs) Over, beyond; अति-इ go beyond, overstep; so ˚क्रम्<BR> ˚चर्, ˚वह् &c. In this case अति is regarded as a preposition उपसर्ग.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) (With nouns or pronouns) Beyond, past, surpassing, superior to,<BR> eminent, respectable, distinguished, higher, above, (used with acc. as<BR> a कर्मप्रवचनीय, or as first member of Bah. or Tat. comp. ज्याशब्दस्तावुभौ<BR> शब्दावति रामस्य शुश्रुवे Rām. 6. 75. 37 in which last case it has<BR> usually the sense of eminence or higher degree; अतिगो, ˚गार्ग्यः = प्रशस्ता<BR> गौः, शोभनो गार्ग्यः; ˚राजन् an excellent king; or the sense of अतिक्रान्त<BR> must be understood with the latter member which will then stand in the<BR> accusative case; अतिमर्त्यः = मर्त्यमतिक्रान्तः; ˚मालः, अतिक्रान्तो मालाम्;<BR> so अतिकाय, ˚केशर, q. v.); अत्यादित्यं हुतवहमुखे संभृतं तद्धि<BR> तेजः Me. 1. 45. Surpassing the sun. अति देवान् कृष्णः Sk.; मानुषानतिगन्धर्वान्<BR> सर्वान्गन्धर्व लक्षये Mb.; ˚मानुषं कर्म a deed which is beyond<BR> human power, i. e. a superhuman action; ˚कशः past the whip (as a<BR> horse), unmanageable; ˚त्यद् surpassing that; ˚त्वाम्, ˚त्वान् him<BR> or them that surpasses or surpass thee, so ˚मां, ˚यूयं &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) (With nouns derived from roots) Extravagant, exaggerated, inordinate,<BR> excessive, extraordinary; <i>e. g.</i> ˚आदरः excessive regard; ˚आशा<BR> extravagant hope; so ˚भयं, ˚तृष्णा, ˚आनन्दः &c. &c.; अतिदानाद्<BR> बलिर्बद्धो नष्टो मानात्सुयोधनः । विनष्टो रावणो लौल्यादति सर्वत्र वर्जयेत् ॥<BR> cf. ‘extremes are ever bad’.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Unfit, idle, improper, in the sense of असंप्रति or क्षेप<BR> ‘censure’; अतिनिद्रम् = निद्रा सम्प्रति न युज्यते Sk. The गणरत्नमहोदधि<BR> gives the following senses of अतिः:− विक्रमातिक्रमाबुद्धिभृशार्थातिशयेष्वति<BR> <i>e. g.</i> अतिरथः रथाधिकं विक्रमवान्; ˚मतिः बुद्धपतिक्रमः;<BR> ˚गहनं बुद्धेरविषयः; ˚तप्तं भृशतप्तं; ˚वेगः अतिशयितो वेगः.<BR> Cf. also प्रकर्षे लङ्घनेऽप्यति Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथा
अतिकथा<BR>—1 An exaggerated tale.<BR>—2 Idle or meaningless talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथ|अतिकथः
अतिकथा + .{@-थ@} <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Exaggerated, incredible (अश्रद्धेय).<BR>—2 Unfit to be told.<BR>—3 Past narration or mention, dead, lost.<BR>—4 Swerving from oneʼs caste traditions &c.; lawless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकन्दकः|अतिकन्दक|अतिकंदकः
अतिकन्दकः [अतिरिक्तः कन्दो यस्य] N. of a tree हस्तिकन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकर्षणम्
अतिकर्षणम् <i>n.</i> Afflicting very much, excessive exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकल्यम्
अतिकल्यम् early morning नातिकल्यं नातिसायं नातिमध्यन्दिने स्थिते ।<BR> गच्छेत् … Ms. 4. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकश
अतिकश <i>a.</i> Beyond the whip, unmanageable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकामुकः|अतिकामुक
अतिकामुकः A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकाय|अतिकायः
अतिकाय <i>a.</i> [अत्युत्कटः कायो यस्य]. Of an extraordinary size, gigantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकायः|अतिकाय
अतिकाय + .{@-यः@} N. of a Rākṣasa, son ofRāvaṇa, who was killed by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्र|अतिकृच्छ्रः
अतिकृच्छ्र [प्रादि˚ स˚] <i>a.</i> Very difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्रम्
अतिकृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्, -च्छ्रः@} [अतिक्रान्तं कृच्छ्रं प्राजापत्यम्] Extraordinary<BR> hardship, a kind of severe penance to be finished in 12 nights एकैकं<BR> ग्रासमश्नीयात् त्र्यहाणि त्रीणि पूर्ववत् । त्र्यहं चोपवसेदन्त्यमतिकृच्छ्रं<BR> चरन् द्विजः ॥ Ms. 11. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्रः|अतिकृच्छ्र
अतिकृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्, -च्छ्रः@} [अतिक्रान्तं कृच्छ्रं प्राजापत्यम्] Extraordinary<BR> hardship, a kind of severe penance to be finished in 12 nights एकैकं<BR> ग्रासमश्नीयात् त्र्यहाणि त्रीणि पूर्ववत् । त्र्यहं चोपवसेदन्त्यमतिकृच्छ्रं<BR> चरन् द्विजः ॥ Ms. 11. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृतम्
अतिकृतम् Overdone, done too much, excess; सर्वत्रातिकृतं लोके<BR> व्यसनायोपकल्पते Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृतिः|अतिकृति
अतिकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Overdoing.<BR>—2 N. of a metre of 4 lines, each line containing 25 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकेशरः|अतिकेशर
अतिकेशरः [अतिरिक्तानि केशराणि यस्य] N. of an aquatic plant<BR> कुब्जक Trapa Bīpinosa. (Mar. शिंगाडा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकोप
अतिकोप <i>a.</i> Free from anger, calm, तेन चैवातिकोपेन स यज्ञः<BR> सन्धितस्तदा Mb. 7. 202. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम्
अतिक्रम् €1 U., €4 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To step or pass beyond, get accross, go over, cross यत्कथयितुं<BR> प्रवृत्तस्तत्परित्यज्य अतिदूरमतिक्रान्तोऽस्मि K. 346 led far away from<BR> my story, rambled, made a great digression; सप्त कक्षान्तराण्यतिक्रम्य 92;<BR> निमिषमात्रेणातिदूरमतिक्रामति 120; समीपेऽप्यक्रामन्ती M. 1.<BR> going so near; अतिक्रम्य तांस्तान् विशेषान् Me. 57.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To pass over, pass by, walk past, go beyond; सेनानिवेशदेशमतिक्रम्य<BR> Dk. 4. 10; कथमतिक्रान्तमगस्त्याश्रमपदम् Mv. 7 is it passed or<BR> left behind; तस्मिन्नतिक्रामति Ś. 7. 31. इदं कदलीगृहमतिक्रम्य<BR> दृश्यते Ratn. 3 beyond the plantain-bower; तच्चातिक्रम्य कैलासगिरिः<BR> K. 121; जम्बुद्वीपमतिक्रम्य शिशिरो नाम पर्वतः Rām.; अतिक्रामत्ययम्<BR> K. 85 is going or departing.<BR>—2 To excel, surpass; exceed (in number, strength &c.); इरावतीमतिक्रामन्ती<BR> भव M. 4. अतिक्रामन्तीमिवेरावतीं प्रेक्षे M. 1; वृद्धिर्नातिक्रामति<BR> पञ्चताम् Ms. 8. 151; कर्णीसुतमप्यतिक्रान्तः Dk. 74; कलासु रूपे<BR> चाप्सरसोऽप्यतिक्रान्ता 78; surpassing, superior to; शक्तिमनतिक्रम्य<BR> यथाशक्ति Sk.<BR>—3 To transgress, violate, go beyond, overstep; जनकाग्रजन्मनोः शासनमतिक्रम्य<BR> Dk. 2; नालं पुरुषो नियतिलिखितां लेखामतिक्रमितुम् 61; एवमतिक्रान्तमर्यादे<BR> त्वयि Ve. 1, अये वात्सल्यादतिक्रामति प्रसङ्गः Māl. 6. Oh, the event<BR> through excessive affection transgresses all due limits; अतिक्रम्य सदाचारम् K. 160, 181.<BR>—4 To exclude, pass by, neglect, set aside, leave; अतिक्रामेत्प्रमत्तं<BR> या मत्तं रोगार्तमेव वा Ms. 9. 78. किं वा परिजनमतिक्रम्य भवान्<BR> संदिष्टः M. 4. प्रथितयशसां प्रबन्धानतिक्रम्य M. 1 to the exclusion of.<BR>—5 To go or pass away, elapse, roll on (as time); सा निशा अतिचक्राम<BR> Pt. 1; यथा यथा यौवनमतिचक्राम K. 59; शैशवम् 74; भवतामप्यतिक्रामति<BR> देवार्चनविधिवेला 47; is passing away (is being violated); अतिक्रान्ते<BR> दशाहे Ms. 5. 76; also trans. allow to pass; द्वित्राणि दिनान्यतिक्रम्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">Page0040-1</a>]<BR> Dk. 100; अत्यक्राममिमान्मासांस्तद्वधं परिचिन्तयन् Rām.; नाहारवेलातिक्रमणीया K. 266.<BR>—6 To overcome. overpower, seize; व्यालद्विप इवास्माभिरतिक्रम्यैव दम्यसे<BR> Mv. 3. 31 by seizing or falling upon, by main force; केनापि सत्त्वेन<BR> अतिक्रम्य Ś. 6.<BR>—7 To lose; स हि स्वाम्यादतिक्रामेत् ऋतूनां प्रतिरोधनात् Ms. 9. 93. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To let pass, allow to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0039-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमः|अतिक्रम
अतिक्रमः<BR>—1 Act of overstepping, going beyond &c.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Breach of decorum or duty; अहो अतिक्रमः Māl. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Transgression, violation; उपचार˚ केवलमुपचारातिक्रमं प्रमार्ष्टुमस्माक्रमयमारम्भः M. 4. 5.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Trespass; disrespect, injury, opposition; ब्राह्मण˚ त्यागो भवतामेव<BR> भूतये Mv. 2. 10 refraining from all trespass against Brāhmaṇas;<BR> दिशत्यपायं हि सतामतिक्रमः Ki. 14. 9; कुलान्यकुलतां यान्ति ब्राह्मणातिक्रमेण<BR> च Ms. 3. 63; एतस्मिन्नतिक्रमे परवतीयम् M. 3; गुरुजनातिक्रमात्<BR> K. 160; शशिनो ज्येष्टातिक्रमः 56 transgression (passing through);<BR> मर्षणीयोऽयमारोहणातिक्रमः 81; वात्सल्यादतिक्रमोऽपि Mv. 1 violation<BR> (of due limits or propriety); Mv. 4. 25.<BR>—3 Lapse, passing away (of time); अनेकसंवत्सरातिक्रमेऽपि U. 4; वेला˚<BR> मं कृत्वा आगतः Pt. 1; उचितवेलातिक्रमे M. 2; सन्ध्या˚ Rām.<BR>—4 Overcoming, conquering, surpassing; mostly with दुर्; स्वजातिर्दुरतिक्रमा,<BR> स्वभावो दुरतिक्रमः &c.<BR>—5 Neglect, omission, disregard; क्रामतो रेतसः सेकं व्रतस्थस्य द्विजन्मनः ।<BR> अतिक्रमं व्रतस्याहुर्धर्मज्ञा ब्रह्मवादिनः ॥ Ms. 11. 120.<BR>—6 A vigorous attack, determined onset (= अभिक्रम q. v.).<BR>—7 Excess.<BR>—8 Abuse, misapplication.<BR>—9 Imposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्त|अतिक्रांत|अतिक्रान्तः
अतिक्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Exceeded, surpassed, gone beyond &c.; सोतिक्रान्तः श्रवणविषयम्<BR> Me. 103; सुदूरमतिक्रान्तः K. 35 departed, gone; मनोरथ ˚दर्शना<BR> Māl. 10 beyond the reach even of desire; विचारातिक्रान्तः Mu. 5. 4<BR> past the stage of thought; चक्षुर्विषयातिक्रान्तेषु पक्षिषु H. 1.<BR>—2 Past, gone by; ˚कुनृपति K. 5, past, former; 169; Pt. 1. 333; Pt. 2,<BR> Bh. 3. 32; ˚पार्थिवगुणान् Mu. 1 former kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्तम्
अतिक्रान्त + .{@-तम्@} A past thing, thing of the past, the past; ˚तं भगवती<BR> कथयति M. 5 your ladyship is speaking of the past; ˚ते धैर्यमवलम्ब्यताम्<BR> U. 3; किं ˚उपालम्भेन H. 1; cf. ‘let bygones be bygones’ ˚योगिन्<BR> <i>a.</i> with the moon in conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्ता
अतिक्रान्ता N. of the sixth stage of the elephantʼs must; अतिक्रान्तावस्थो<BR> गजपतिरिदं स्थावरचरम्, जगत्सर्वं हन्तुं समभिलषति क्रोधकलुषः ।<BR> Mātaṅga L. 9. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्तिः|अतिक्रान्ति
अतिक्रान्तिः Transgression; स्थित्यतिक्रान्तिभीरूणि … तोयानि Ki. 11. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमणम्
अतिक्रमणम् Overstepping, spending of time, excess; fault, offence;<BR> तेनातिक्रमणेन दुःखयति नः Mv. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमणीय
अतिक्रमणीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be transgressed or violated, to be disregarded,<BR> passed by, neglected or avoided; ˚यं मे सुहृद्वाक्यम् Ś. 2. इतस्तपस्विकार्यमितो<BR> गुरुजनाज्ञा । द्वयमप्यनतिक्रमणीयम् । 3, 6, 7; अनतिक्रमणीयस्य<BR> जन्ममृत्योरिवागमम् H. 4. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रुद्ध|अतिक्रुद्धः
अतिक्रुद्ध <i>a.</i> Very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रुद्धः|अतिक्रुद्ध
अतिक्रुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} [प्रा˚ स˚] N. of a Mantra mentioned in Tantras;<BR> (अष्टाविंशत्यक्षरो य एकत्रिंशदथापि वा । अतिक्रुद्धः स विज्ञेयो निन्दितः<BR> सर्वकर्मसु ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रूर|अतिक्रूरः
अतिक्रूर <i>a.</i> Very cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रूरः|अतिक्रूर
अतिक्रूर + .{@-रः@} [प्रा˚ स˚]<BR>—1 A malignant planet such as Saturn, Mars &c. (क्रूरा वका अतिक्रूराः).<BR>—2 N. of a Mantra in Tantras (त्रिंशदक्षरको मन्त्रस्त्रयस्त्रिंशदथापि<BR> वा । अतिक्रूरः स विज्ञेयो निन्दितः सर्वकर्मसु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्षिप्त
अतिक्षिप्त <i>a.</i> [क्षिप्-क्त] Thrown beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्षिप्तम्
अतिक्षिप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} A kind of sprain or dislocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिखट्व
अतिखट्व <i>a.</i> Without a bedstead, able to dispense with a bed-stead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगम्
अतिगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To pass, elapse, pass away (as time); दशाहेऽतिगते Rām.<BR>—2 To overcome, exceed, excel. See अतिग.<BR>—3 To pass over, pass by, neglect.<BR>—4 To pass away, die.<BR>—5 To escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग
अतिग <i>a.</i> [गम्-ड] (in comp.) Exceeding, going beyond, transcending,<BR> excelling, surpassing; सर्वलोक˚ Mu. 1. 2; किमौषधपथातिगैरुपहतो<BR> महाव्याधिभिः Mu. 6. 16 by diseases defying the powers of medicine,<BR> past the stage of physicking; बाणैर्देहातिगैः R. 12. 48 piercing through<BR> their bodies; वयो˚ Ms. 7. 149 advanced in years, aged; संख्यातिगाः<BR> संपदः Bh. 3. 132; वपुःप्रकर्षेण जनातिगेन Ki. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगण्डः|अतिगण्ड|अतिगंडः
अतिगण्डः<BR>—1 N. of star of the 6th lunar asterism.<BR>—2 A large cheek or temple.<BR>—3 One who has large cheeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्ध|अतिगंध|अतिगन्धः
अतिगन्ध <i>a.</i> Having an excessive or overpowering smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्धः|अतिगन्ध|अतिगंध
अतिगन्ध + .{@-न्धः@}<BR>—1 Sulphur.<BR>—2 N. of various plants: चम्पक, भूततृण lemon-grass & मुद्गर.<BR> (Mar. सुगंधी रोहिस गवत, सोनचांफा, बटमोगरा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्धालु|अतिगंधालु|अतिगन्धालुः
अतिगन्धालु N. of the plant पुत्रदात्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्धिका
अतिगन्धिका (= अतिगन्धालु) (Mar. पिठवण डवला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगव
अतिगव <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तो गाम्]<BR>—1 Very foolish, quite stupid.<BR>—2 Inexpressible, indescribable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगहन
अतिगहन, -गव्हर <i>a.</i><BR> Very deep, impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगव्हर
अतिगहन, -गव्हर <i>a.</i><BR> Very deep, impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुण|अतिगुणः
अतिगुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having excellent or superior qualities.<BR>—2 Devoid of merits, worthless [गुणमतिक्रान्तः].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुणः|अतिगुण
अतिगुण + .{@-णः@} Excellent merits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुरु|अतिगुरुः
अतिगुरु <i>a.</i> Very heavy (such as mercury &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुरुः|अतिगुरु
अतिगुरु + .{@-रुः@} A very respectable person, such as a father, mother &c. (त्रयः<BR> पुरुषस्य अतिगुरवो भवन्ति पिता माता आचार्यश्च)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुहा
अतिगुहा [अतिक्रान्ता गुहां मध्यावकाशेन] N. of the plant पृश्निपर्णी.<BR> (Mar. सालवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगृहकम्
अतिगृहकम् A lofty house, a terrace भूमीगृहांश्चैत्यगृहान्गृहातिगृहकानपि<BR> Rām. 5. 12. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्रह्
अतिग्रह् €9 P. To take beyond the usual measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्रह|अतिग्रहः
अतिग्रह <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तो ग्रहम्] Difficult to be comprehended,<BR> incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्रहः|अतिग्रह
अतिग्रह + .{@-हः, -ग्राहः@}<BR>—1 Object of an apprehensive organ, such as स्पर्श ‘touch’ the object<BR> of त्वच्, रस of जिह्वा &c. The <i>Grahas</i> are eight<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">Page0041-1</a>]<BR> in number; प्राण, वाच्, जिह्वा, चक्षुस्, श्रोत्र, मनस्, हस्तौ & त्वच्;<BR> the corresponding atigrāhas being अपान, नामन्, रस, रूप, शब्द,<BR> काम, कर्मन् & स्पर्श. अथ हैनं जारत्कारव आर्तभागः पप्रच्छ<BR> याज्ञवल्क्येति होवाच कति ग्रहाः कत्यतिग्रहा इति । अष्टौ ग्रहा अष्टावतिग्रहा<BR> इति Bṛ. Up. 3. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Right knowledge, correct apprehension.<BR>—3 Act of overtaking, surpassing &c.<BR>—4 One who siezes or takes to a very great extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राहः|अतिग्राह
अतिग्रह + .{@-हः, -ग्राहः@}<BR>—1 Object of an apprehensive organ, such as स्पर्श ‘touch’ the object<BR> of त्वच्, रस of जिह्वा &c. The <i>Grahas</i> are eight<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">Page0041-1</a>]<BR> in number; प्राण, वाच्, जिह्वा, चक्षुस्, श्रोत्र, मनस्, हस्तौ & त्वच्;<BR> the corresponding atigrāhas being अपान, नामन्, रस, रूप, शब्द,<BR> काम, कर्मन् & स्पर्श. अथ हैनं जारत्कारव आर्तभागः पप्रच्छ<BR> याज्ञवल्क्येति होवाच कति ग्रहाः कत्यतिग्रहा इति । अष्टौ ग्रहा अष्टावतिग्रहा<BR> इति Bṛ. Up. 3. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Right knowledge, correct apprehension.<BR>—3 Act of overtaking, surpassing &c.<BR>—4 One who siezes or takes to a very great extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0040-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राह्य|अतिग्राह्यः
अतिग्राह्य <i>a.</i> To be held in check, to be controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राह्यः|अतिग्राह्य
अतिग्राह्य + .{@-ह्यः@} N. the of three libations made at the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ
अतिघ [अतिशयेन हन्ति; हन्-टक्]<BR>—1 A weapon.<BR>—2 Wrath^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/ap90/issues/issue26 readme_althw_2.txt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ्न
अतिघ्न <i>a.</i> Very destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ्नी
अतिघ्न + .{@-घ्नी@} [अतिशयेन हन्ति दुःखम्; हन्-टक्] A happy state of complete<BR> oblivion which drowns all thought of whatever is disagreeable in the past;<BR> अतिघ्नीमानन्दस्य गत्वा Bṛ. Ār. Up. 2. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचमू
अतिचमू <i>a.</i> [चमूमतिक्रान्तः] Victorious over armies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर्
अतिचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To transgress, violate; be unfaithful to, offend (as a wife &c.); स्वं<BR> स्वमाचारमत्यचारिषुः Dk. 162; यथा चाहं नातिचरे पतीन्; पुत्राः पितॄनत्यचरन्नार्यश्चात्यचरन्<BR> पतीन् Mb.; धर्मे चार्थे च कामे च नातिचरामि-विवाहमन्त्र.<BR>—2 To pass by, neglect, omit.<BR>—3 To overtake, overcome; surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर
अतिचर <i>a.</i> Very changeable, transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचरा
अतिचर + .{@-रा@} [अतिक्रम्य स्वस्थानं सरोऽन्तरं गच्छति] N. of the shrub<BR> Hibiscus Mutabilis (पद्मिनी, स्थलपद्मिनी or पद्मचारिणीलता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचरणम्
अतिचरणम् Excessive practice, overdoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचारः|अतिचार
अतिचारः<BR>—1 Transgression.<BR>—2 Excelling,<BR>—3 Overtaking &c.<BR>—4 Accelerated motion of planets (कुजादिपञ्चग्रहाणां स्वस्वाक्रान्तराशिषु<BR> भोगकालमुल्लङ्घ्य राश्यन्तरगमनम्); passage from one zodiacal sign to another.<BR>—5 Violation of justice Kau. A. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचारिन्
अतिचारिन् <i>a.</i> Transgressing, surpassing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचिरम्
अतिचिरम् <i>adv.</i> Very long; ˚रं मया कृतं Ratn. 1. I have<BR> been very late; नातिचिरं गतायां च तस्याम् K. 178 she had not long left when &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रः|अतिच्छत्र|अतिछत्र
अतिच्छत्रः, -त्रा, -च्छत्रका<BR> [अतिक्रान्तः छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom,<BR> anise, principally Anesum or Anethum Sowa (Mar. शोपा) N. of another<BR> plant, Barleria Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara to be जलतृणभेदः)<BR> (Mar. शेतगवत); and ˚त्रा = शतपुष्पा (Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रा|अतिछत्रा
अतिच्छत्रः, -त्रा, -च्छत्रका<BR> [अतिक्रान्तः छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom,<BR> anise, principally Anesum or Anethum Sowa (Mar. शोपा) N. of another<BR> plant, Barleria Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara to be जलतृणभेदः)<BR> (Mar. शेतगवत); and ˚त्रा = शतपुष्पा (Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रका
अतिच्छत्रः, -त्रा, -च्छत्रका<BR> [अतिक्रान्तः छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom,<BR> anise, principally Anesum or Anethum Sowa (Mar. शोपा) N. of another<BR> plant, Barleria Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara to be जलतृणभेदः)<BR> (Mar. शेतगवत); and ˚त्रा = शतपुष्पा (Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छेदः|अतिच्छेद
अतिच्छेदः (v. l. अतिच्छन्दः) Great disparity अतिच्छेदातिवादाभ्यां<BR> स्मयोऽयं समुपागतः Mb. 13. 120. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छन्दः|अतिच्छन्द|अतिच्छंदः
अतिच्छन्दः, -दस् <i>a.</i><BR> [अतिक्रान्तः छन्दः -न्दं वा]<BR>—1 Free from worldly desires.<BR>—2 Exceeding thought or will.<BR>—3 One who violates Vedic traditions of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छन्दस्|अतिच्छंदस्
अतिच्छन्दः, -दस् <i>a.</i><BR> [अतिक्रान्तः छन्दः -न्दं वा]<BR>—1 Free from worldly desires.<BR>—2 Exceeding thought or will.<BR>—3 One who violates Vedic traditions of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छन्दस्|अतिच्छंदस्
अतिच्छन्दः, -दस् + .{@-स्@} <i>f. n.</i><BR>—1 N. of two classes of metres (अतिक्रान्ता छन्दः वृत्तानुसारिवर्णविन्यासभेदम्)<BR>—2 Fondness, inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजगती
अतिजगती [अतिक्रान्ता जगतीं द्वादशाक्षरपादाम् एकाक्षराधिक्यात्]<BR> N. of a class of metres belonging to the अतिच्छन्दस् class, with 13<BR> letters in each line (प्रथमाऽतिजगत्यासां सा द्विपञ्चाशदक्षरा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजन
अतिजन <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तो जनम्] Not tenanted or inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजागर|अतिजागरः
अतिजागर <i>a.</i> Always wakeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजागरः|अतिजागर
अतिजागर + .{@-रः@} The black Curlew (नीलबक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजात
अतिजात <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तो जातं-जातिं जनकं वा] (opp. अपजात)<BR> Superior to his parentage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजित
अतिजित <i>a.</i> Completely defeated, लोकं ह्यतिजितं कृत्वा ह्यावां<BR> हन्तुमिहेच्छति Rām. 3. 70. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0041-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीव्
