अतीसारिन्
अति(ती)सारिन् <i>m.</i> [अत्यन्तं सारयति मलम्] The disease called<BR> अतिसार. {@-अतिसारकिन्@} <i>a.</i><BR> [अतिसारो यस्यास्ति, इनि कुक् च P. V. 2. 129.] Affected<BR> by, afflicted with, dysentery; सातिसारोऽतिसारकी Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृज्
अतिसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To give, present, bestow, grant; अतिसृष्टो राज्यार्धविभागः Mu. 2;<BR> पुरा नारायणेनेयमतिसृष्टा मरुत्वते V. 1. 17; राघवाय तनयां<BR> … अतिसृष्टवान् R. 11. 48; अनसूयातिसृष्टेन 12. 27.<BR>—2 To dismiss, abandon, part with.<BR>—3 To permit, allow.<BR>—4 To remit, forgive (as fine &c.).<BR>—5 To leave as a remnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्गः|अतिसर्ग
अतिसर्गः<BR>—1 Granting (of a wish); giving; स्रष्टुर्वरातिसर्गात्तु मया तस्य दुरात्मनः R. 10. 42.<BR>—2 Granting permission (to do what one likes कामचारानुज्ञा) P. III. 3. 163,<BR> one of the senses of the Potential अतिसर्गाच्च पटवो दृष्ट्वा<BR> Rām. 5. 62. 7.<BR>—3 Dismissal, discharge, parting with; giving away; स्त्रीणां दानविकयातिसर्गा<BR> विद्यन्ते न पुंसः Nir.<BR>—4 Favour; तवातिसर्गाद्देवेश प्राजापत्यमिदं पदम् । Mb. 8. 34. 2.<BR>━<i>a.</i> [सर्गं सृष्टिमतिक्रान्तः] Ever-lasting, permanent (नित्य);<BR> emancipated (मुक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्जनम्
अतिसर्जनम्<BR>—1 Giving, granting; consigning विधुरां ज्वलनातिसर्जनात् Ku. 4. 32,<BR> consigning to the flames; दीयतामिति वचोऽतिसर्जने Śi. 14. 48; तत्तदीयविशिखातिसर्जनात्<BR> Ki. 13. 57 giving back.<BR>—2 Liberality, munificence.<BR>—3 Killing.<BR>—4 Deception.<BR>—5 Separation from, parting with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृष्टि
अतिसृष्टि Superior creation सैषा ब्रह्मणोऽतिसृष्टिः Bṛ. Ār. Up. 1. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौरभ|अतिसौरभः
अतिसौरभ <i>a.</i> Very fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौरभम्
अतिसौरभ + .{@-भम्@} Great fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौरभः|अतिसौरभ
अतिसौरभ + .{@-भः@} The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौहित्यम्
अतिसौहित्यम् Stuffing oneself with food; न ˚त्यमाचरेत् Ms. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्पर्श|अतिस्पर्शः
अतिस्पर्श <i>a.</i> Not liberal, niggardly, mean-spirited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्पर्शः|अतिस्पर्श
अतिस्पर्श + .{@-र्शः@} Slight contact or absence of contact of the tongue and palate<BR> in pronunciation; epithet of the semivowels and vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्नेहः|अतिस्नेह
अतिस्नेहः Over-affection, ˚हः कार्यदर्शी V. 2 sees or finds<BR> what is to be done; ˚हः पापशङ्की Ś. 4 is apt to suspect evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहस्तयति
अतिहस्तयति Den. P. [अतिहस्त-णि]<BR>—1 To stretch out the hands (हस्तौ निरस्यति).<BR>—2 [हस्तिना अतिक्रामति] To overtake (one) on an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अती
अती [अति-इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To go beyond, pass on, over or beyond, cross (time or space); स्तोकमन्तरमतीत्य<BR> Ś. 1; जवादतीये हिमवानधोमुखैः Ki. 14. 54 was gone to or reached;<BR> स्थातव्यं ते नयनविषयं यावदत्येति भानुः Me. 36 passes out of<BR> sight; अतीत्यैकादशाहं तु नामकर्म तथाऽकरोत् Rām. after 11 days;<BR> गृहपङ्क्तयश्चिरमतायिरे जनैः Śi. 13. 53.<BR>—2 To enter, step over; अद्वारेण च नातीयात् ग्रामं वा वेश्म वा वृतम् Ms. 4. 73.<BR>—3 To excel, surpass, outstrip, be more than a match for; त्रिस्रोतसः<BR> कान्तिमतीत्य तस्थौ Ku. 7. 15;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-2" target="_blank">Page0048-2</a>]<BR> सत्यमतीत्य हरितो हरींश्च वर्तन्ते वाजिनः Ś. 1; अग्निस्त्विषा<BR> नात्येति पूषणम् Śi. 2. 23; to exceed, go beyond, transcend; कुसीदवृद्धिर्द्वैगुण्यं<BR> नात्येति Ms. 8. 151 does not exceed; अतीत्य वाचां मनसां च गोचरं<BR> स्थिताय Ki. 18. 41, अपराधशतक्षमं नृपः क्षमयात्येति भवन्तमेकया Śi. 16. 48.<BR>—4 To overcome, subdue, vanquish, get the better of; न प्रदीप इव<BR> वायुमत्यगात् R. 19. 53 did not overcome, outlive or survive; to overtake, out-do<BR>—5 To walk by, walk past, pass by, leave behind; स्रोतोवहां पथि निकामजलामतीत्य<BR> Ś. 6. 16; सोऽत्यगाद् आश्रमम् R. 15. 37.<BR>—6 To omit, neglect, disregard, violate, transgress, overstep; न दिष्टमर्थमत्येतुमीशो<BR> मर्त्यः कथंचन Mb. avoid; अतीत्य हि गुणान् सर्वान् स्वभावो मूर्ध्नि<BR> वर्तते H. 1. 18 देशं कालं च योऽतीयात् Y. 2. 195; अतीयात्सागरो<BR> वेलां न प्रतिज्ञामहं पितुः Rām.; भूतान्यत्येति पञ्च वै Ms. 12. 90<BR> oversteps the five elements (मोक्षं प्राप्नोति Kull.); अत्येति तत्सर्वमिदं<BR> विदित्वा Bg. 8. 28, 14. 20.<BR>—7 (Intrans.) To pass, elapse (time); अत्येति रजनी या तु सा न प्रतिनिवर्तते<BR> Rām.; अतीते दक्षिणायने &c.<BR>—8 To overflow, be redundant, be in excess.<BR>—9 To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत|अतीतं|अतीतः
अतीत <i>p. p.</i> [इ-क्त.]<BR>—1 Gone beyond, crossed.<BR>—2 (Used actively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) exceeding, going beyond, avoiding, overstepping, having passed<BR> over or neglected &c., with acc. or in comp.; परिच्छेदातीतः Māl. 1. 30<BR> beyond or past definition; संख्यामतीत or संख्यातीत beyond<BR> enumeration, innumerable; तामतीतस्य ते Me. 29; यमुनामतीतमथ<BR> शुश्रुवानमुम् Śi. 13. 1; वयोतीतः Ki. 11. 2 past youth, advanced<BR> in years; सर्वारम्भपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते Bg. 14. 25; कैर्लिङ्गैस्त्रीन्<BR> गुणानेतानतीतो भवति प्रभो 14. 21; बाणपथमतीतः कव्यभोजनः<BR> V. 5 gone beyond the reach of arrows, past bowshot; अतीतनौकेऽतिनु<BR> Ak. who has left the boat, i. e. landed, disembarked.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Gone by, passed away, past (as time &c.); अतीते निशान्ते<BR> Dk. 11; असन्निवृत्त्यै तदतीतमेव Ś. 6. 10; ˚अनागतवर्तमानवेदिना<BR> Pt. 1; अतीते वर्षुके काले Bk. 7. 18; ˚शैशवाः Ms. 8. 27; अतीते<BR> कार्यशेषज्ञः शत्रुभिर्नाभिभूयते Ms. 7. 179; ˚लाभस्य च रक्षणार्थम्<BR> Pt. 2. 182 of past gains; वेत्ति जन्मान्तराण्यतीतानि K. 46.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Dead, deceased; सब्रह्मचारिण्येकाहमतीते क्षपणं स्मृतम<BR> Ms. 5. 71; अप्रजायामतीतायां भर्तुरेव तदिष्यते 9. 196, 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीतम्
अतीत + .{@-तम्@} The past, past time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययः|अत्यय
अत्ययः [इ-अच्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Passing away, lapse; काल˚ आधिश्चोपनिधिश्चोभौ न कालात्ययमर्हतः Ms. 8. 145.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) End, conclusion, termination, absence, disappearance; तपात्यये<BR> Ku. 4. 44, 5. 23; शिशिरात्ययस्य पुष्पोच्चयः 3. 61; आतप˚ R. 1. 52.<BR>—2 Complete disappearance, death, destruction, passing away, perishing;<BR> पितुरत्ययात् Dk. 64.<BR>—3 Danger, risk, harm, injury, evil; जीवितात्ययमापन्नः Ms. 10. 104<BR> the life being in danger or jeopardy; प्राणानामेव चात्यये 5. 27; प्राणात्यये<BR> च संप्राप्ते Y. 1. 179; Ms. 6. 68, 8. 69; पुत्रदारात्ययं प्राप्तः 10. 99<BR> (Kull. क्षुदवसन्नपुत्रकलत्रः).<BR>—4 Suffering, misery, difficulty, distress.<BR>—5 Guilt, fault, offence, transgression; क्षत्रियस्यात्यये दण्डो भागाद्दशगुणो<BR> भवेत Ms. 8. 243; दाप्योऽष्टगुणमत्ययं 8. 400 should be made to<BR> pay as a fine for his offence.<BR>—6 Attack, assault<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">Page0049-1</a>]<BR> साहसस्तेयपारुष्यगोऽभिशापात्यये Y. 2. 12.<BR>—7 Overcoming, mastering mentally, comprehending; बुद्धिश्च ते लोकैरपि<BR> दुरत्यया Rām.<BR>—8 Overstepping; क्षुरस्य धारा निशिता दुरत्यया Ken.<BR>—9 A class kind. cf. अशुभे चापदि स्मृतः । अत्ययो ऽतिक्रमे कृच्छ्रे दोषे<BR> दण्डविनाशयोः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिक
अत्ययिक = आत्ययिक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययित
अत्ययित^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Exceeded, surpassed.<BR>—2 Violated, outraged.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिन्
अत्ययिन् <i>a.</i> [इ-इनि P. III. 2. 157] Exceeding surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतीन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्त इन्द्रियम्] Beyond the cognizance (reach)<BR> of the senses; अतीन्द्रियेष्वप्युपपन्नदर्शनः R. 3. 41; यत्तत्सूक्ष्ममतीन्द्रियं<BR> ज्ञानं यन्निर्विकल्पाख्यं तदतीन्द्रियमुच्यते; ˚ज्ञाननिधिः Śi. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रियः|अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं
अतीन्द्रिय + .{@-यः@} The Soul or Puruṣa, (in Sāṅkhya Phil.); the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रियम्
अतीन्द्रिय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Pradhāna or Nature (in Sāṅkhya Phil.).<BR>—2 The mind (in Vedānta) योऽसावतीन्द्रियग्राह्यः सूक्ष्मोऽव्यक्तः सनातनः<BR> Ms. 1. 7 (Kull. इन्द्रियमतीत्य वर्तते इति ˚यं मनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव [अति-इव] <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Exceedingly, excessively, very, very much, quite, too; ˚पीडित, ˚हृष्ट &c.<BR>—2 Surpassing, superior to (acc.); अतीवान्यान् भविष्यावः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुन्द|अतुंद
अतुन्द <i>a.</i> Not bulky, lean, lank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर <i>a.</i> Ved. Not rich or liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अतुल^1 <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Unequalled, unsurpassed, matchless,<BR> peerless, incomparable, very great; भयमतुलं गुरुलोकात् Pt. 5. 31;<BR> so ˚पराक्रम, ˚रूप &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: missing vowel diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुलः|अतुल
अतुल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 The sesamum seed and plant (तिलकवृक्ष).<BR>—2 Cough Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल्य|अतुल्यं
अतुल्य <i>a.</i> Unequalled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुषार
अतुषार <i>a.</i> Not cold.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतुषारकरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुषारकरः|अतुषारकर
अतुषार + -करः The Sun; so अतुहिनकर, ˚रश्मि, ˚धामन्, ˚रुचि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूतुजि
अतूतुजि <i>a.</i> [न तुज्-कि द्वित्वदीर्घे]<BR>—1 Not a donor or giver, not liberal (अदातृ)<BR>—2 Not quick, slow; अतूतुजिं चित् तूतुजिरशिश्नत् Rv. 7. 28. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्त|अतूर्त्त
अतूर्त <i>a.</i> [न तूर्यते, तूर-हिंसायाम्] Ved. Not obstructed<BR> or stopped or injured, unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्तम्
अतूर्त + .{@-र्तम्@} The unlimited space, sky. अतूर्ते बद्धं सविता समुद्रम्<BR> Rv. 10. 149. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अतूर्तदक्ष, अतूर्तपथिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्तदक्ष
अतूर्त + -दक्ष <i>a.</i> Ved. whose plans cannot be obstructed or are unhurt.<BR> अतूर्तदक्षा वृषणा वृषण्वसु Rv. 8. 26. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्तपथिन्
अतूर्त + -पथिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. whose path cannot be obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृणादः|अतृणाद
अतृणादः [न तृणम् अत्ति, अद्-अण्] ‘Not eating grass’, a new-born<BR> calf; Śat. Br. 14. अथ वत्सं जातमाहुरतृणाद इति Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृण्या
अतृण्या [न˚ त˚] A small quantity of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृदिल
अतृदिल <i>a.</i> [न तृद्यते वध्यते, तृद्-किलच्] Ved. Not assailable,<BR> immovable, solid, firm (as a mountain); तृदिला अतृदिलासः Rv. 10. 94. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस् <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not bright, dim.<BR>—2 Weak, feeble.<BR>—3 Insignificant; so अतेजस्क, अतेजस्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस् + .{@-स्@} <i>n.</i> Dimness, shadow, darkness; absence of vigour, feebleness, dullness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्कः|अत्क
अत्कः [अतति गच्छति सततं विकृतिं, पन्थानं &c. अत्-कन् कित्त्वम् Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>—1 A traveller.<BR>—2 A limb or member (of the body).<BR>—3 (Ved.) Water, lightning, garment, armour (?).<BR>—4 Corner of a house (See अक्क above)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्कीलः|अत्कील
अत्कीलः N. of the author of some Vedic hymns, a descendant of Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता <i>f.</i> [अतति सततं संबध्नाति; अत्-तक् इडभावः-टाप्]<BR>—1 A mother.<BR>—2 An elder sister.<BR>—3 A mother-in-law; (rarely) motherʼs sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तिः|अत्ति
अत्तिः <i>f.</i>, अत्तिका [अत्यते सर्वदा संबध्यते, कर्मणि क्तिन्]<BR> An elder sister &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ &c. See under अद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नम्
अत्नम् [अतति जयपराजयौ अत्र, अत्-न] A battle, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नः|अत्न|अत्नं
अत्नः [अतति सततं गच्छति; अत्-न Uṇ. 3. 6.]<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 A traveller. Written also as अत्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यः|अत्य
अत्यः [अतति शीघ्रं गच्छति, अत् कर्तरि यत्] A courser, steed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंहस्
अत्यंहस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Emancipated from sin or evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्नि|अत्यग्निः
अत्यग्नि <i>a.</i> Surpassing fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्निः|अत्यग्नि
अत्यग्नि + .{@-ग्निः@} Morbidly rapid digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्निष्टोमः|अत्यग्निष्टोम
अत्यग्निष्टोमः [अतिक्रान्तोऽग्निष्टोमम् अधिकफलदत्वात्] The optional<BR> second part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यङ्कुश|अत्यंकुश
अत्यङ्कुश <i>a.</i> [अङ्कुशमतिक्रान्तः] Past the goad, uncontrollable,<BR> unmanageable; अत्यङ्कुशमिवोद्दामं गजं मदजलोद्धतम् । प्रधावितमहं<BR> दैवं पौरुषेण निवर्तये ॥ Rām. 2. 23. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यच्छ
अत्यच्छ <i>a.</i> Of a chaste conduct, Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यध्वन्
अत्यध्वन् <i>m.</i> A long or wearisome travelling; a long journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तः अन्तं सीमां नाशम्]<BR>—1 Excessive, much, very great or strong; ˚वैरम् great enmity; ˚मैत्री;<BR> ˚हिमोत्किरानिलाः Ku. 5. 26.<BR>—2 Complete, perfect, absolute; ˚अभावः absolute non-existence; see below.<BR>—3 Endless, perpetual, permanent, everlasting, uninterrupted, unbroken;<BR> किं वा तवात्यन्तवियोगमोघे हतजीविते R. 14. 65; भवत्यजरमत्यन्तम्<BR> Pt. 1. 151; यो बन्धनवधक्लेशान् प्राणिनां न चिकीर्षति । स सर्वस्य<BR> हितप्रेप्सुः सुखमत्यन्तमश्नुते ॥ Ms. 5. 46; Bg. 6. 28; कस्यात्यन्तं<BR> सुखमुपनतम् Me. 111. नायमत्यन्तसंवासो लम्यते येन केनचित् H. 4. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तम्
अत्यन्त + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Exceedingly, excessively, very much, to the highest degree; स्थायीभवति<BR> चात्यन्तं रङ्गः शुक्लपटे यथा Pt. 1. 33; स्तनंधयोऽत्यन्तशिशुः<BR> स्तनादिव Mu. 4. 14 very young.<BR>—2 For ever, to the end (of life), through life; अत्यन्तमात्मसदृशेक्षणवल्लभाभिराहो<BR> निवत्स्यति Ś. 1. 26. For all time, in perpetuity; सा चात्यन्तमदर्शनं<BR> नयनयोर्याता<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">Page0050-1</a>]<BR> V. 4. 9; oft. in comp.; ˚गता See below; प्रियमत्यन्तविलुप्तदर्शनम्<BR> Ku. 4. 2. For ever lost to view; R. 14. 39.<BR>—3 Absolutely, perfectly, completely.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अत्यन्तापह्नवः, अत्यन्ताभावः, अत्यन्तग, अत्यन्तगत, अत्यन्तगति, अत्यन्तगामिन्, अत्यन्तनिवृत्तिः, अत्यन्तवासिन्, अत्यन्तसहचरित, अत्यन्तसंयोगः, अत्यन्तसंपर्कः, अत्यन्तसुकुमार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तापह्नवः|अत्यन्तापह्नव
अत्यन्त + -अपह्नवः A flat, categorical or total denial; a denial nipping<BR> the accusation in the bud (P. वार्त्तिक III. 2. 115.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्ताभावः|अत्यन्ताभाव
अत्यन्त + -अभावः absolute or complete non-existence, absolute non-entity,<BR> a thing which does not exist at any one of the three periods of time,<BR> or does not exist for all time; त्रैकालिकसंसर्गावाच्छिन्नप्रतियोगिकः<BR> (This is considered to be नित्य or eternal and different from the<BR> other kinds of अभाव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तग
अत्यन्त + -ग <i>a.</i> going or walking too much or too fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगत
अत्यन्त + -गत <i>a.</i> —1 gone or departed forever, gone never to return; कथमत्यन्तगतां न मां दहेः R. 8. 56.<BR>—2 always applicable, perfectly intimate or pertinent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगति
अत्यन्त + -गति <i>f.</i> —1 sense of ‘completely’; अनत्यन्तगतौ क्तात् P. V. 4. 4.<BR> completion, accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगामिन्
अत्यन्त + -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going or walking very much, going too fast or quickly.<BR>—2 excessive, much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तनिवृत्तिः|अत्यन्तनिवृत्ति
अत्यन्त + -निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> complete disappearance, absolute cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तवासिन्
अत्यन्त + -वासिन् <i>m.</i> [वस्-णिनि] one who constantly stays with his<BR> preceptor, as a student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसहचरित
अत्यन्त + -सहचरित <i>a.</i> going together invariably (P. वार्त्तिक VIII. 1. 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसंयोगः|अत्यन्तसंयोग
अत्यन्त + -संयोगः<BR>—1 close proximity, uninterrupted continuity; कालाध्वनोरत्यन्तसंयोगे P. II. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Inseparable co-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसंपर्कः|अत्यन्तसम्पर्क|अत्यन्तसंपर्क
अत्यन्त + -संपर्कः excessive sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसुकुमार|अत्यन्तसुकुमारः
अत्यन्त + -सुकुमार <i>a.</i> very tender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसुकुमारः|अत्यन्तसुकुमार
अत्यन्त + -सुकुमार + .({@-रः@}) a kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्ताय
अत्यन्ताय <i>adv.</i> For good, totally; तत्र अत्यन्ताय स्वार्थः परित्यक्तो<BR> भवति । ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यन्तिक <i>a.</i> [अत्यन्तं गच्छति; अत्यन्त-ठन्]<BR>—1 Going too much or too fast.<BR>—2 Very near.<BR>—3 Not near, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिकम्
अत्यन्तिक + .{@-कम्@} [अतिशयितम् अन्तिकं नैकट्यम्]<BR>—1 Close proximity, immediate neighbourhood or being in close proximity.<BR>—2 [अतिक्रान्तम् अन्तिक्रम्] Great distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तीन|अत्यंतीन|अत्यन्तीनः
अत्यन्तीन <i>a.</i> [अत्यन्तं गामी अत्यन्तीनः, भृशं गन्ता; अत्यन्त-ख P. V. 2. 11.]<BR>—1 Going or walking too much, going too fast (अत्यन्तगमनशील);<BR> लक्ष्मीं परम्परीणां त्वमत्यन्तीनत्वमुन्नय Bk.<BR>—2 the state of lasting for a long time. पानशौण्डः श्रियं नेता नात्यन्तीनत्वमुन्मनाः Bk. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं|अत्यम्लः
अत्यम्ल <i>a.</i> [अतिशयितोऽम्लो रसः फलपत्रादौ यस्य] Very acid or sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्लः|अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं
अत्यम्ल + .{@-म्लः@} N. of a tree, Spondias Mangifera. (Mar. अंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ला
अत्यम्ल + .{@-म्ला, ˚पर्णी@} A species of citron (वनबीजपूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्लपर्णी|अत्यम्लपर्ण्णी
अत्यम्ल + .{@-म्ला, ˚पर्णी@} A species of citron (वनबीजपूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय, अत्ययिक &c. See under अती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिक
अत्यय, अत्ययिक &c. See under अती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तः अर्थम् अनुरूपस्वरूपम्] Beyond the proper<BR> worth or measure, excessive, very great, intense, exorbitant; ˚तापात् M. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थम्
अत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@} <i>adv.</i> Very much, exceedingly, excessively; अत्यर्थं<BR> परदास्यमेत्य निपुणं नीतौ मनो दीयते Mu. 2. 5; प्रियो हि ज्ञानिनोत्यर्थमहं<BR> स च मम प्रियः Bg. 7. 17; oft. in comp.;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थवेदनः|अत्यर्थवेदन
अत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@} + ˚वेदनः A type of the<BR> elephant having extreme sensibility; प्राजनाङ्कुशदण्डेभ्यो दूरादुद्विजते<BR> हि यः । स्पृष्टो वा व्यथतेऽत्यर्थं स गजोऽत्यर्थवेदनः ॥<BR> Mātaṅga L. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थसंपीडितः|अत्यर्थसम्पीडित
अत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@} + ˚संपीडितः Ś. 7. 11 excessively pinched; ˚क्रुद्ध, ˚तृषित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थक्रुद्ध
अत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@} + ˚क्रुद्ध, ˚तृषित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थतृषित
अत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@} + ˚क्रुद्ध, ˚तृषित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यवि
अत्यवि <i>a.</i> Ved. Passing over or through the sieve or strainer<BR> (epithet of Soma.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टिः|अत्यष्टि
अत्यष्टिः <i>f.</i> [अतिक्रान्ता अष्टिं षोडशाक्षरपादां वृत्तिम् एकाक्षराधिक्यात्]<BR> A metre of 4 lines, each containing 17 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यस्त
अत्यस्त <i>a.</i> (p. p. अति + अस् €4 P.) cast, tossed, thrown over<BR> or beyond (P. II. 1. 24, तरङ्गात्यस्तः -काशिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यह्न
अत्यह्न <i>a.</i> [अतिक्रान्तमहः] Exceeding a day in duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकारः|अत्याकार
अत्याकारः [अतिशयितः आकारः तिरस्कारः]<BR>—1 Contempt, blame, censure; गोजचरणाच्श्लाघात्याकारतदवेतेषु P. V. 1. 134.<BR>—2 Bigness of person, a very large body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याक्रम्
अत्याक्रम् = आक्रम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार <i>a.</i> [आचारमतिक्रान्तः] Deviating from established<BR> usages or customs, negligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचारः|अत्याचार|अत्याचारं
अत्याचार + .{@-रः@} Performance of works not sanctioned by usage (अनुचिताचरणम्);<BR> irreligious conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादित्य
अत्यादित्य <i>a.</i> Surpassing the (lustre of the) sun; अत्यादित्यं<BR> हुतवहमुखे संभृतं तद्धि तेजः Me. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यानन्दा|अत्यानंदा
अत्यानन्दा <i>f.^1</i> Morbid indifference to the pleasures of sexual union.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याधानम्
अत्याधानम्<BR>—1 Laying on, imposition.<BR>—2 Transgression.<BR>—3 Violation of आधान, not keeping the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याय|अत्यायः
अत्याय <i>a.</i> [इ or अय्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Transgressing.<BR>—2 Past going time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यायः|अत्याय
अत्याय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Transgression, violation.<BR>—2 Excess. P. III. 1. 141.<BR>—3 Great gain or profit (अतिशयितो लाभः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यायु
अत्यायु <i>n.</i> [अति-आ-या-कु] A kind of sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यारूढ
अत्यारूढ <i>a.</i> Grown to excess; ˚ढो हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः R. 12. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यारूढम्
अत्यारूढ + .{@-ढम्, -ढिः@} <i>f.</i> A very high position, great elevation or rise;<BR> अत्यारूढिंर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4, v. l.; अत्यारूढं<BR> रिपोः सोढं चन्दनेनेव भोगिनः R. 10. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यारूढिः|अत्यारूढि
अत्यारूढ + .{@-ढम्, -ढिः@} <i>f.</i> A very high position, great elevation or rise;<BR> अत्यारूढिंर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4, v. l.; अत्यारूढं<BR> रिपोः सोढं चन्दनेनेव भोगिनः R. 10. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यालः|अत्याल
अत्यालः [अतिशयेन समन्तात् अलति पर्याप्नोति; अति-आ-अल् -अच्] N.<BR> of a plant रक्तचित्रक Plumbago Rosea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याश्रमः|अत्याश्रम
अत्याश्रमः Saṃnyāsa, Renunciation. (-श्रमिन्) Saṃnyāsa. (Śvet. Up. 6. 21.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यासः|अत्यास
अत्यासः [अति-अस्-घञ्] Allowing to pass, only in acc. sing. as<BR> णमुल्; द्वयहात्यासं or द्वपहमत्यासं गाः पाययति P. III. 4. 57<BR> after an interval of 2 days (अद्य पाययित्वा द्वपहमतिक्रम्य पुनः पाययति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहारयमाण
अत्याहारयमाण <i>a.</i> Making exactions from. लोभादैलश्चातुर्वर्ण्यमत्याहारयमाणः<BR> (विननाश) Kau. A. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहितम्
अत्याहितम् [आधा-आधारे क्त, अत्यन्तमाधीयते तन्निवारणार्थं मनो<BR> दीयते यस्मिन् Tv.]<BR>—1 A great calamity, danger or evil, misfortune, mishap, accident; न<BR> किमप्यत्याहितं Ś. 1. किम् अत्याहितं सीतादेव्याः; न केवलं ˚तं<BR> सापवादमपि U. 2; मया ˚तमुपलब्धं V. 4; किमिदमुच्चैरत्याहितम्<BR> Mv. 6; श्रुतमत्याहितम् M. 4 evil or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">Page0051-1</a>]<BR> evil news; oft. as an exclamation, ‘Ah, me!’ ‘alas! alas!’, ‘how bad it is!’<BR> Māl. 3. 7; V. 5.<BR>—2 A rash or daring deed (जीवानपेक्षि कर्म); अत्याहितं किमपि राक्षसकर्म<BR> कुर्यात् Mv. 4. 49 rash and demoniacal deed; पाण्डुपुत्रैर्न किमप्यत्याहितमाचेष्टितं भवेत् Ve. 2.<BR>—3 Great fear; अराजके धनं नास्ति नास्ति भार्याप्यराजके । इदमत्याहितं<BR> चान्यत्कुतः सत्यमराजके ॥ Rām. 2. 67. 11 <i>cf.</i> अत्याहितं महाभीतौ<BR> कर्म जीवानपेक्षि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ता
अत्युक्ता, -क्था<BR> [उक्ता-क्था एकाक्षरपादा वृत्तिः, ताम् अतिक्रान्ता] N. of a<BR> class of metres of 4 lines, each of 2 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्था
अत्युक्ता, -क्था<BR> [उक्ता-क्था एकाक्षरपादा वृत्तिः, ताम् अतिक्रान्ता] N. of a<BR> class of metres of 4 lines, each of 2 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्तिः|अत्युक्ति
अत्युक्तिः <i>f.</i> Exaggeration, hyperbole, over-drawn or coloured description;<BR> अत्युक्तौ न यदि प्रकुप्यसि मृषावादं च नो मन्यसे । Udb. See<BR> अतिशयोक्ति also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युग्र
अत्युग्र <i>a.</i> Very fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युग्रम्
अत्युग्र + .{@-ग्रम्@} Asafoetida. (Mar. हिंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युपध
अत्युपध <i>a.</i> [उपधाम् अतिक्रान्तः] Above guiles, trustworthy,<BR> tried; अमात्ये चात्युपधे Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूमशा
अत्यूमशा <i>ind.</i> [ऊर्यादिगण] A particle of abuse, occurring<BR> in comp. with कृ, भू or अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूर्मि
अत्यूर्मि <i>a.</i> Ved. Overflowing or bubbling over. अत्यूर्मिर्मत्सरो<BR> मदः सोमः पवित्रे अर्षति Rv. 9. 17. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूहः|अत्यूह
अत्यूहः [अतिशयेन ऊहः तर्कः]<BR>—1 Close or deep meditation or thinking; earnest reasoning.<BR>—2 [अतिशयेन ऊहते शब्दायते; अति-ऊह्-अच्] A gallinule (दात्यूह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूहा
अत्यूहः + .{@-हा@} A plant (नीलिका) Nyctanthes Tristis, or Jasminum Villosum.<BR> (Mar. निर्गुडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र (अत्रा Ved.) <i>ind.</i> [अस्मिन् एतास्मिन् वा, इदं-एतद् वा सप्तम्याः<BR> त्रल् प्रकृतेः अश्भावश्च Tv.]<BR>—1 In this place, here; अपि संनिहितोऽत्र कुलपतिः Ś. 1; अत्र<BR> गृह्यते अत्र गृह्यते K. 119 here-here <i>i. e.</i> just now.<BR>—2 In this respect, matter, or case; as to this, (serving the purpose<BR> of अस्मिन् विषये or of the forms अस्मिन् or एतस्मिन्, अस्याम्, &c.<BR> with a substantive or adjectival force); अहिंसा परमो धर्म इत्यत्र<BR> एकमत्यम् H. 1; अलं प्रयत्नेन तवात्र R. 3. 50; भवन्तमेवात्र<BR> गुरुलाघवं पृच्छामि Ś. 5; तदत्र परिगतार्थं कृत्वा Ś. 6 informing<BR> him of this matter.<BR>—3 There, in that direction.<BR>—4 Then, at that time (Ved.); कः कोऽत्र भोः who is there? which of<BR> the servants is in attendance? who waits there? (used in calling out to<BR> oneʼs servants &c.; cf. Hindustāni <i>Kaun hai</i>).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अत्रान्तरे, अत्रदघ्न, अत्रभवत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रा
अत्र (अत्रा Ved.) <i>ind.</i> [अस्मिन् एतास्मिन् वा, इदं-एतद् वा सप्तम्याः<BR> त्रल् प्रकृतेः अश्भावश्च Tv.]<BR>—1 In this place, here; अपि संनिहितोऽत्र कुलपतिः Ś. 1; अत्र<BR> गृह्यते अत्र गृह्यते K. 119 here-here <i>i. e.</i> just now.<BR>—2 In this respect, matter, or case; as to this, (serving the purpose<BR> of अस्मिन् विषये or of the forms अस्मिन् or एतस्मिन्, अस्याम्, &c.<BR> with a substantive or adjectival force); अहिंसा परमो धर्म इत्यत्र<BR> एकमत्यम् H. 1; अलं प्रयत्नेन तवात्र R. 3. 50; भवन्तमेवात्र<BR> गुरुलाघवं पृच्छामि Ś. 5; तदत्र परिगतार्थं कृत्वा Ś. 6 informing<BR> him of this matter.<BR>—3 There, in that direction.<BR>—4 Then, at that time (Ved.); कः कोऽत्र भोः who is there? which of<BR> the servants is in attendance? who waits there? (used in calling out to<BR> oneʼs servants &c.; cf. Hindustāni <i>Kaun hai</i>).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अत्रान्तरे, अत्रदघ्न, अत्रभवत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रान्तरे
अत्र + -अन्तरे <i>adv.</i> in the meanwhile, meantime. अत्रान्तरे श्रवणकातरतां<BR> गतोऽस्मि Ś. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रदघ्न
अत्र + -दघ्न <i>a.</i> (-घ्नी <i>f.</i>) reaching so far up; as tall as this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रभवत्|अत्रभवन्त्
अत्र + -भवत् (<i>m.</i> {@-भवान्@}) an honorific epithet meaning ‘worthy’,<BR> ‘revered’, ‘honourable’, ‘your or his honour’, and referring to a person<BR> that is present or near the speaker, (opp. तत्रभवत्); ˚भवती<BR> <i>f.</i> ‘your or her lady-ship’ (पूज्ये तत्रभवानत्रभवांश्च भगवानपि);<BR> अत्रभवान् प्रकृतिमापन्नः Ś. 2; वृक्षसेचनादेव परिश्रान्तामत्रभवतीं<BR> लक्षये Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रत्य
अत्रत्य <i>a.</i> [अत्र भवो जातः एतत्स्थानसंबद्धो वा; अत्र-त्यप्]<BR>—1 Belonging to, or connected with, this place; दौरात्म्याद्रक्षसस्तां<BR> तु नात्रत्याः श्रद्दधुः प्रजाः R. 15. 72.<BR>—2 Produced or found here, of this place; local.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Not giving or enjoying protection. Bṛ. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रः|अत्र
अत्र + .{@-त्रः@} Ved. [अद्-त्रन्] An eater, devourer; a demon, Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रम्
अत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} Food. अत्राण्यस्मै षड्भिः संभरन्ति Rv. 10. 79. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Shameless, impudent, immodest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रपु
अत्रपु <i>a.</i> Not tinned. Maitrāyaṇī, Kāṭhaka and Kāpiṣṭhala Saṃhitās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रवस्
अत्रवस् <i>ind.</i> The year before last (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रस्त
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, -त्रस्नु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not afraid,<BR> fearless; जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रास
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, -त्रस्नु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not afraid,<BR> fearless; जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रस्नु
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, -त्रस्नु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not afraid,<BR> fearless; जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि <i>a.</i> [properly अत्त्यि, Uṇ. 4. 68, अदेस्त्रिनिश्च, अद्-त्रिन्]<BR> Devourer; अत्रिमनु स्वराज्यमग्निम् Rv. 2. 8. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिः|अत्रि
अत्रि + .{@-त्रिः@} N. of a celebrated sage and author of many Vedic hymns.<BR> [He appears in the Vedas in hymns addressed to Agni, Indra, the Aśvins<BR> and the Viśvedevas. In the Svāyambhuva Manvantara, he appears as one<BR> of the ten Prajāpatis or mind-born sons of Brahmā, being born from his<BR> eye. These sons having died by the curse of Śiva, Brahmā performed a<BR> sacrifice, at the beginning of the present Vaivasvata Manvantara, and<BR> Atri was born from the flames of Agni. Anasūyā was his wife in both lives.<BR> In the first, she bore him three sons, Datta, Durvāsas and Soma; in the<BR> second, she had two additional children, a son by name Aryaman and a daughter<BR> called Amalā. In the Rāmāyaṇa an account is given of the visit paid<BR> by Rāma and Sītā to Atri and Anasūyā in their hermitage, when they<BR> both received them most kindly. (See Anasūyā.) As a Riṣi or sage he<BR> is one of the seven sages who were all sons of Brahmā, and represents<BR> in Astronomy one of the stars of the Great Bear situated in the north.<BR> He is also the author of a code of laws known as अत्रिस्मृति or अत्रिसंहिता.<BR> In the Purāṇas he is said to have produced the moon from his eye, while<BR> he was practising austere penance, the moon being in consequence called<BR> अत्रिज, -जात, -दृग्ज, अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत, -˚प्रभव, ˚भव &c.; cf.<BR> also अथ नयनसमुत्थं ज्योतिरत्रेरिव द्यौः R. 2. 75 and अत्रेरिवेन्दुः<BR> V. 5. 21.] ━(pl.) descendants of Atri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्री
अत्रि + .{@-अत्री@} wife of अत्रि; अत्रिरत्र्या नमस्कर्ता Mb. 13. 17. 38.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अत्रिचतुरहः, अत्रिजातः, अत्रिभारद्वाजिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिचतुरहः|अत्रिचतुरह
अत्रि + -चतुरहः N. of a Sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजातः|अत्रिजात
अत्रि + -जातः<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Datta. —3 Durvāsas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिभारद्वाजिका
अत्रि + -भारद्वाजिका Marriage of descendants of Atri with those of Bhāradvāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजात|अत्रिजातः
अत्रिजात <i>a.</i> A man belonging to one of the three classes (= द्विज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन् <i>m.</i> A devourer, a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्वक्क
अत्वक्क <i>a.</i> Skinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्सरुकः|अत्सरुक
अत्सरुकः [नास्ति त्सरुर्यस्य] N. of a sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ (Ved. अथा) <i>ind.</i> [अर्थ्-ड, पृषोद˚ रलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 A particle used at the beginning (of works) mostly as a sign of auspiciousness,<BR> and translated by ‘here’, ‘now’ (begins) (मङ्गल, आरम्भ, अधिकार).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">Page0052-1</a>]<BR> (Properly speaking ‘auspiciousness’ or मङ्गल is not the sense of<BR> अथ, but the very utterance or hearing of the word is considered to<BR> be indicative of auspiciousness, as the word is supposed to have emanated<BR> from the throat of Brahmā; ओंकारश्चाथशब्दश्च द्वावेतौ ब्रह्मणः पुरा ।<BR> कण्ठं भित्त्वा विनिर्यातौ तेन माङ्गलिकावुभौ ॥ and therefore we find<BR> in Śāṅkara Bhāṣya अर्थान्तरप्रयुक्तः अथशब्दः श्रुत्या मङ्गलमारचयति);<BR> अथ निर्वचनम्; अथ योगानुशासनम्; अथेदं प्रारभ्यते द्वितीयं तन्त्रम्<BR> Pt. 2. (usually followed by इति at the end, इति प्रथमोऽङ्कः here ends &c.).<BR>—2 Then, afterwards (आनन्तर्य) अथ प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते R. 2. 1;<BR> often as a correlative of यदि or चेत्; न चेन्मुनिकुमारोऽयम्<BR> अथ कोऽस्य व्यपदेशः Ś. 7; मुहूर्तादुपरि उपाध्यायश्चेदागच्छेत् अथ<BR> त्वं छन्दोऽधीष्व P. III. 3. 9. Sk.<BR>—3 If, supposing, now if, in case, but if (पक्षान्तर); अथ कौतुकमावेदयामि<BR> K. 144, अथ तु वेत्सि शुचि व्रतमात्मनः पतिकुले तव दास्यमपि क्षमम् ॥<BR> Ś. 5. 27; अथ मरणमवश्यमेव जन्तोः किमिति मुधा मलिनं यशः<BR> कुरुध्वे Ve. 3. 6. अथ गृह्णाति Ś. 7; Ku. 5. 45; Mu. 3. 25; Ki. 1. 44;<BR> अथ चास्तमिता त्वमात्मना R. 8. 51 while, but, on the other hand;<BR> oft. followed by ततः or तथापि, Bg. 2. 26, 12. 9, 11; अथ<BR> चेत् but if Bg. 2. 33, 18. 58.<BR>—4 And, so also, likewise (समुच्चय); गणितमथ कलां वैशिकीम्<BR> Mk. 1. मातृष्वसा मातुलानी श्वश्रूरथ पितृष्वसा । संपूज्या गुरुपत्नीवत्<BR> समास्ता गुरुभार्यया ॥ Ms. 2. 1. 31; भीमोऽथार्जुनः G. M.<BR>—5 Used in asking or introducing questions (प्रश्न) oft. with the<BR> interrogative word itself; अथ सा तत्रभवती किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः पत्नी<BR> Ś. 7; अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः । अथ भगवाँल्लोकानुग्रहाय कुशली<BR> काश्यपः Ś. 5; अथ शक्नोषि भोक्तुम् G. M.; अथात्रभवती कथमित्थंभूता<BR> M. 5; अथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः । Bg. 3. 36; अथ<BR> भवन्तमन्तरेण कीदृशोऽस्या दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2; अथ माढव्यं प्रति<BR> किमेवं प्रयुक्तम् Ś. 6 (अथ may in these two sentences mean ‘but’).<BR>—6 Totality, entirety (कार्त्स्न्य); अथ धर्मं व्याख्यास्यामः G. M.<BR> we shall explain the whole धर्म (धर्म in all its details.) Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—7 Doubt, uncertainty (संशय, विकल्प); शब्दो नित्यो ऽथानित्यः<BR> G. M. The senses of अथ usually given by lexicographers are:− अथोऽथ<BR> स्यातां समुच्चये । मङ्गले संशयारम्भाधिकारानन्तरेषु च । अन्वादेशे<BR> प्रतिज्ञायां प्रश्नसाकल्ययोरपि ॥ Some of these senses are indentical<BR> with those in (1), while some are not in general use.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अथातः, अथानन्तरम्, अथापि, अथकिम्, अथकिमु, अथतु, अथवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथा
अथ (Ved. अथा) <i>ind.</i> [अर्थ्-ड, पृषोद˚ रलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 A particle used at the beginning (of works) mostly as a sign of auspiciousness,<BR> and translated by ‘here’, ‘now’ (begins) (मङ्गल, आरम्भ, अधिकार).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">Page0052-1</a>]<BR> (Properly speaking ‘auspiciousness’ or मङ्गल is not the sense of<BR> अथ, but the very utterance or hearing of the word is considered to<BR> be indicative of auspiciousness, as the word is supposed to have emanated<BR> from the throat of Brahmā; ओंकारश्चाथशब्दश्च द्वावेतौ ब्रह्मणः पुरा ।<BR> कण्ठं भित्त्वा विनिर्यातौ तेन माङ्गलिकावुभौ ॥ and therefore we find<BR> in Śāṅkara Bhāṣya अर्थान्तरप्रयुक्तः अथशब्दः श्रुत्या मङ्गलमारचयति);<BR> अथ निर्वचनम्; अथ योगानुशासनम्; अथेदं प्रारभ्यते द्वितीयं तन्त्रम्<BR> Pt. 2. (usually followed by इति at the end, इति प्रथमोऽङ्कः here ends &c.).<BR>—2 Then, afterwards (आनन्तर्य) अथ प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते R. 2. 1;<BR> often as a correlative of यदि or चेत्; न चेन्मुनिकुमारोऽयम्<BR> अथ कोऽस्य व्यपदेशः Ś. 7; मुहूर्तादुपरि उपाध्यायश्चेदागच्छेत् अथ<BR> त्वं छन्दोऽधीष्व P. III. 3. 9. Sk.<BR>—3 If, supposing, now if, in case, but if (पक्षान्तर); अथ कौतुकमावेदयामि<BR> K. 144, अथ तु वेत्सि शुचि व्रतमात्मनः पतिकुले तव दास्यमपि क्षमम् ॥<BR> Ś. 5. 27; अथ मरणमवश्यमेव जन्तोः किमिति मुधा मलिनं यशः<BR> कुरुध्वे Ve. 3. 6. अथ गृह्णाति Ś. 7; Ku. 5. 45; Mu. 3. 25; Ki. 1. 44;<BR> अथ चास्तमिता त्वमात्मना R. 8. 51 while, but, on the other hand;<BR> oft. followed by ततः or तथापि, Bg. 2. 26, 12. 9, 11; अथ<BR> चेत् but if Bg. 2. 33, 18. 58.<BR>—4 And, so also, likewise (समुच्चय); गणितमथ कलां वैशिकीम्<BR> Mk. 1. मातृष्वसा मातुलानी श्वश्रूरथ पितृष्वसा । संपूज्या गुरुपत्नीवत्<BR> समास्ता गुरुभार्यया ॥ Ms. 2. 1. 31; भीमोऽथार्जुनः G. M.<BR>—5 Used in asking or introducing questions (प्रश्न) oft. with the<BR> interrogative word itself; अथ सा तत्रभवती किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः पत्नी<BR> Ś. 7; अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः । अथ भगवाँल्लोकानुग्रहाय कुशली<BR> काश्यपः Ś. 5; अथ शक्नोषि भोक्तुम् G. M.; अथात्रभवती कथमित्थंभूता<BR> M. 5; अथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः । Bg. 3. 36; अथ<BR> भवन्तमन्तरेण कीदृशोऽस्या दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2; अथ माढव्यं प्रति<BR> किमेवं प्रयुक्तम् Ś. 6 (अथ may in these two sentences mean ‘but’).<BR>—6 Totality, entirety (कार्त्स्न्य); अथ धर्मं व्याख्यास्यामः G. M.<BR> we shall explain the whole धर्म (धर्म in all its details.) Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—7 Doubt, uncertainty (संशय, विकल्प); शब्दो नित्यो ऽथानित्यः<BR> G. M. The senses of अथ usually given by lexicographers are:− अथोऽथ<BR> स्यातां समुच्चये । मङ्गले संशयारम्भाधिकारानन्तरेषु च । अन्वादेशे<BR> प्रतिज्ञायां प्रश्नसाकल्ययोरपि ॥ Some of these senses are indentical<BR> with those in (1), while some are not in general use.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अथातः, अथानन्तरम्, अथापि, अथकिम्, अथकिमु, अथतु, अथवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0051-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथातः
अथ + -अतः, -अनन्तरम् now, therefore; अथाऽतो धर्मजिज्ञासा Ms. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथानन्तरम्
अथ + -अतः, -अनन्तरम् now, therefore; अथाऽतो धर्मजिज्ञासा Ms. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथापि
अथ + -अपि moreover, and again &c. (= अथ in most cases); ˚च<BR> likewise, also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिम्
अथ + -किम् what else, yes, exactly so, quite so, certainly; सर्वथा<BR> अप्सरःसंभवैषा । अथ किम् Ś. 1; अपि वृषलमनुरक्ताः प्रकृतयः<BR> अथ किम् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिमु
अथ + -किमु how much more, so much more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथतु
अथ + -तु but, on the contrary. अथ तु वेत्सि शुचि व्रतमात्मनः । Ś. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथ + -वा<BR>—1 or (used like the English disjunctive conjunction ‘<i>or</i>’ and occupying<BR> the same place); व्यवहारं परिज्ञाय वध्यः पूज्योऽथवा भवेत् H. 1. 55;<BR> समस्तैरथवा पृथक् Ms. 7. 198; अथवा-अथवा either━or; ▪<BR> वाथ is often used in the same sense with वा; कार्तिके वाथ चैत्रे<BR> वा Pt. 3. 38; साम्ना दानेन भेदेन समस्तैरथवा पृथक् । विजेतुं प्रयतेतारीन्न<BR> युद्धेन कदाचन ॥ Ms. 7. 182; अथापि वा also used in the same sense;<BR> एतदेव व्रतं कुर्युश्चान्द्रायणमथापि वा 11. 117, 8. 287.<BR>—2 or rather, or why,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">Page0052-2</a>]<BR> or perhaps, is it not so (correcting or modifying a previous statement);<BR> why should there be any thought or hesitation about it, or it is no wonder;<BR> अपि नाम कुलपतेरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् । अथवा कृतं सन्देहेन<BR> Ś. 1. 1, 16; गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम् … अथवा कृतवाग्द्वारे वंशेऽस्मिन्<BR> R. 1. 3-4; अथवा मृदु वस्तु हिंसितुम् R. 8. 45; दीर्ये किं न सहस्रधाहमथवा<BR> रामेण किं दुष्करम् U. 6. 40; अधोधो गङ्गेयं पदमुपगता स्तोकमथवा ।<BR> विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनिपातः शतमुखः Bh. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो = अथ in most senses; अथो वयस्यां परिपार्श्ववर्तिनीं … ऐक्षत<BR> Ku. 5. 51; स्त्रियो रत्नान्यथो विद्या Ms. 2. 240, 3. 202,<BR> Bg. 4. 35; Ki. 5. 16, 6. 1. cf. मङ्गलानन्तरारम्भप्रश्नकार्त्स्न्येष्वथो<BR> अथ । कथमादौ तथाप्यन्ते यत्ने गौरवबाढयोः ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथरिः|अथरि
अथरिः, -री Ved. <i>m., f.</i><BR> A finger; finger-like or pointed flame (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथरी
अथरिः, -री Ved. <i>m., f.</i><BR> A finger; finger-like or pointed flame (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्यति
अथर्यति Den. P. To go constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्य
अथर्य, -र्यु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Moving constantly, tremulous (गमनशील)<BR> दूरेदृशं गृहपतिमथर्युम् (अग्निम्) Rv. 7. 1. 1; pointed like<BR> a lance, lambent (?) उषर्बुधमथर्यः Rv. 4. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्यु
अथर्य, -र्यु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Moving constantly, tremulous (गमनशील)<BR> दूरेदृशं गृहपतिमथर्युम् (अग्निम्) Rv. 7. 1. 1; pointed like<BR> a lance, lambent (?) उषर्बुधमथर्यः Rv. 4. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वः|अथर्व|अथर्व्व
अथर्वः = अथर्वन् See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वणः|अथर्वण|अथर्व्वण|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्वणः [अथर्वा तदुक्तविद्या अस्त्यस्य ज्ञातृत्वात् अच् न टिलोपः]<BR>—1 Śiva.<BR>—2 N. of the Atharvaveda. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वन्|अथर्व्वन्
अथर्वन् <i>m.</i> [अथ-ऋ-वनिप् शकन्ध्वादि˚ Tv.; probably connected<BR> with some word like <i>athar</i> fire]<BR>—1 A priest who has to worship fire and Soma.<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 N. of the priest who is said to have first brought down fire from the<BR> heaven, offered Soma and recited prayers. [He is represented as the eldest<BR> son of Brahmā sprung from his mouth; as a Prajāpati appointed by Brahmā<BR> to create and protect subordinate beings, who first learnt from Brahmā<BR> and then taught the Brahmavidyā and is considered to be the author of<BR> the Veda called after him. His wife was Śānti, daughter of Kardama Prajāpati.<BR> He had also another wife called Citti; he is also considered identical<BR> with Aṅgiras and father of Agni.]<BR>—4 Epithet of Śiva, Vasiṣṭha. वृतपदपङ्क्तिरथर्वणेव वेदः Ki. 10. 10.<BR>━(pl.) Descendants of Atharvan; hymns of this Veda; जिष्णुं जैत्रैरथर्वभिः R. 17. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वा|अथर्व्वा
अथर्वन् + .{@-र्वा, -र्व@} <i>m. n.</i>, ˚वेदः The Atharvaveda, regarded as the<BR> fourth Veda. [It contains many forms of imprecations for the destruction<BR> of enemies and also contains a great number of prayers for safety and<BR> averting mishaps, evils, sins or calamities, and a number of hymns, as<BR> in the other Vedas, addressed to the gods with prayers to be used at religious<BR> and solemn rites; cf. Mv. 2. 24. मूर्तिमभिरामघोरां बिभ्रदिवाथर्वणो<BR> निगमः. It has nine Śākhās and five Kalpas, and is comprised in 20<BR> Kāṇḍas. The most important Brāhmaṇa belonging to this Veda is the<BR> Gopatha-Brāhmaṇa, and the Upaniṣads pertaining to it are stated to<BR> be 52, or, according to another account 31.] [cf. Zend. <i>atharvan</i>, Pers.<BR> <i>āturbān</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अथर्वाधिपः, अथर्वनिधिः, अथर्वविद्, अथर्वभूताः, अथर्वशिखा, अथर्वशिरसू, अथर्वसंहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व|अथर्वः|अथर्व्व
अथर्वन् + .{@-र्वा, -र्व@} <i>m. n.</i>, ˚वेदः The Atharvaveda, regarded as the<BR> fourth Veda. [It contains many forms of imprecations for the destruction<BR> of enemies and also contains a great number of prayers for safety and<BR> averting mishaps, evils, sins or calamities, and a number of hymns, as<BR> in the other Vedas, addressed to the gods with prayers to be used at religious<BR> and solemn rites; cf. Mv. 2. 24. मूर्तिमभिरामघोरां बिभ्रदिवाथर्वणो<BR> निगमः. It has nine Śākhās and five Kalpas, and is comprised in 20<BR> Kāṇḍas. The most important Brāhmaṇa belonging to this Veda is the<BR> Gopatha-Brāhmaṇa, and the Upaniṣads pertaining to it are stated to<BR> be 52, or, according to another account 31.] [cf. Zend. <i>atharvan</i>, Pers.<BR> <i>āturbān</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अथर्वाधिपः, अथर्वनिधिः, अथर्वविद्, अथर्वभूताः, अथर्वशिखा, अथर्वशिरसू, अथर्वसंहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्ववेदः|अथर्ववेद
अथर्वन् + .{@-र्वा, -र्व@} <i>m. n.</i>, ˚वेदः The Atharvaveda, regarded as the<BR> fourth Veda. [It contains many forms of imprecations for the destruction<BR> of enemies and also contains a great number of prayers for safety and<BR> averting mishaps, evils, sins or calamities, and a number of hymns, as<BR> in the other Vedas, addressed to the gods with prayers to be used at religious<BR> and solemn rites; cf. Mv. 2. 24. मूर्तिमभिरामघोरां बिभ्रदिवाथर्वणो<BR> निगमः. It has nine Śākhās and five Kalpas, and is comprised in 20<BR> Kāṇḍas. The most important Brāhmaṇa belonging to this Veda is the<BR> Gopatha-Brāhmaṇa, and the Upaniṣads pertaining to it are stated to<BR> be 52, or, according to another account 31.] [cf. Zend. <i>atharvan</i>, Pers.<BR> <i>āturbān</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अथर्वाधिपः, अथर्वनिधिः, अथर्वविद्, अथर्वभूताः, अथर्वशिखा, अथर्वशिरसू, अथर्वसंहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0052-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाधिपः|अथर्वाधिप
अथर्वन् + -अधिपः N. of बुध Mercury (सामवेदाधिपो भौमः शशिजोऽथर्ववेदराट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वनिधिः|अथर्वनिधि
अथर्वन् + -निधिः, -विद् <i>m.</i> receptacle of the (knowledge of) Atharvaveda,<BR> or conversant with it; गुरुणाऽथर्वविदा कृतक्रियः R. 8. 4, 1. 59;<BR> (अथर्वविधिपदेन दुरितोपशमननिमित्तशान्तिकपौष्टिकप्रवीणत्वं पौरोहित्योचितत्वं<BR> द्योत्यते Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वविद्
अथर्वन् + -निधिः, -विद् <i>m.</i> receptacle of the (knowledge of) Atharvaveda,<BR> or conversant with it; गुरुणाऽथर्वविदा कृतक्रियः R. 8. 4, 1. 59;<BR> (अथर्वविधिपदेन दुरितोपशमननिमित्तशान्तिकपौष्टिकप्रवीणत्वं पौरोहित्योचितत्वं<BR> द्योत्यते Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वभूताः
अथर्वन् + -भूताः (pl.) those who have become Atharvans, Names of the 12 Maharṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वशिखा
अथर्वन् + -शिखा, -शिरसू <i>n.</i> (अथर्वणो वेदस्य शिखा शिर इव वा ब्रह्मविद्याप्रतिपादकत्वेन<BR> श्रेष्ठत्वात्) N. of an Upaniṣad dealing with Brahmavidyā. अथर्वशिरसोऽध्येता<BR> ब्रह्मचारी यतव्रतः Mb. 13. 90. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वशिरसू
अथर्वन् + -शिखा, -शिरसू <i>n.</i> (अथर्वणो वेदस्य शिखा शिर इव वा ब्रह्मविद्याप्रतिपादकत्वेन<BR> श्रेष्ठत्वात्) N. of an Upaniṣad dealing with Brahmavidyā. अथर्वशिरसोऽध्येता<BR> ब्रह्मचारी यतव्रतः Mb. 13. 90. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वसंहिता
अथर्वन् + -संहिता A text of collection of hymns of अथर्ववेद. अथर्वसंहितायाजी<BR> विदधे विधिवद्धुतम् Bm. 1. 869.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वणिः|अथर्वणि|अथर्व्वणि|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्वणिः [अथर्वणि तदुक्तशान्त्यादौ वा कुशलः, इस् सित्वेन भत्वाभावात्<BR> न टिलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa versed in this Veda; or skilled in the performance of<BR> the rites enjoined by it.<BR>—2 A family priest (पुरोधस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरस्|अथर्वांगिरस्
अथर्वाङ्गिरस् <i>m.</i> A member of the class of this name. ━(pl.)<BR>—1 Descendants of Atharvan and of Aṅgiras.<BR>—2 Names of the hymns of the Atharvaveda; दण्डनीत्यां च कुशलमथर्वाङ्गिरसे<BR> तथा Y. 1. 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरस|अथर्वांगिरस|अथर्वाङ्गिरसः
अथर्वाङ्गिरस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Connected with अथर्वाङ्गिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरसम्
अथर्वाङ्गिरस + .{@-सम्@} Office of this person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरसाः
अथर्वाङ्गिरस + .{@-साः@} Hymns of this Veda. श्रुतीरथर्वाङ्गिरसीः प्रकुर्यादविचारयन् Ms. 11. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाणम्
अथर्वाणम् Ritual of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाणः|अथर्वाण|अथर्वाणं
अथर्वाणम् + .{@-णः, -˚विद्@} One studying or versed in this Veda or the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाणविद्
अथर्वाणम् + .{@-णः, -˚विद्@} One studying or versed in this Veda or the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वी
अथर्वी <i>a.</i> Ved. [न थुर्व्-अच्, पृषो˚ उलोपः गौरा˚ -ङीष् Tv.]<BR> Not injuring or hurting, not destructive; pierced by a lance (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथवा, अथो See under अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथवा, अथो See under अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद् €2 P. [अत्ति, आद, -जघास, अघसत्. अत्स्यति, अत्तुम्, अन्न-जग्ध, जग्ध्वा]<BR>—1 To eat, devour.<BR>—2 To destroy.<BR>—3 = अन्द्, q. v. ━<i>Caus.</i> to feed with, cause to eat; आदयत्यन्नं<BR> वटुना Sk. ━<i>Desid.</i> जिघत्सति To wish to eat. [cf. L. <i>edo</i>,<BR> Gr. <i>edo</i>, Germ. <i>essen</i>, Eng. <i>eat</i>; Lith. <i>edmi</i>, Sans. <i>admi</i>,<BR> Goth. <i>at</i>, Zend. <i>ad</i>] ━<i>With</i> {@अव@} to satisfy by food, get rid of<BR> with feeding; (fig.) stop the mouth of. ━{@आ@} to eat &c. ━{@प्र-सम्@}<BR> to use up, consume, devour; समदन्त्यामिषं खगाः Bk. 18. 12.<BR>━{@वि@} to gnaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ <i>a.</i> [अद्-तृच्] One who eats; अरक्षितारमत्तारं नृपं<BR> विद्यादधोगतिम्. Ms. 8. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद्, -द <i>a.</i><BR> (at the end of comp.) Eating, devouring; मांसाद<BR> carnivorous, feeding on flesh; so मत्स्य˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद|अदः
अद्, -द <i>a.</i><BR> (at the end of comp.) Eating, devouring; मांसाद<BR> carnivorous, feeding on flesh; so मत्स्य˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदन
आदन Food. Rv. 6. 54. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंष्ट्र|अदंष्ट्रः
अदंष्ट्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Toothless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंष्ट्रः|अदंष्ट्र
अदंष्ट्र + .{@-ष्ट्रः@} A serpent without teeth; one whose fangs have been taken out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अदक्षिण <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not right, left.<BR>—2 [न˚ ब˚] Not bringing in Dakṣiṇā to the priests; without<BR> any gifts (as a sacrifice); अदक्षिणास अच्युता दुधुक्षन् Rv. 10. 61. 10<BR> मृतो यज्ञस्त्वदक्षिणः Pt. 2. 94.<BR>—3 Simple, weak-minded, silly; मेनेऽथ सत्यमेवेति परिहासमदक्षिणा Rām.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">Page0053-2</a>]<BR>—4 Not handy, skilful or clever; awkward.<BR>—5 Unfavourable Bhāg. 10. 82. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिणीय
अदक्षिणीय, -दक्षिण्य <i>a.</i><BR> Not deserving Dakṣinā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण्य
अदक्षिणीय, -दक्षिण्य <i>a.</i><BR> Not deserving Dakṣinā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदग्ध
अदग्ध <i>a.</i> Not burnt; not burnt according to the rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड|अदंड
अदण्ड <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Free or exempt from punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड्य|अदंड्य
अदण्ड्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not deserving punishment; अदण्ड्यान् दण्डयन् राजा दण्ड्याश्चैवाप्यदण्डयन् Y. 2.<BR>—2 Exempt or free from punishment; नादण्ड्यो नाम राज्ञोऽस्ति यः स्वधर्मे<BR> न तिष्टति Ms. 8. 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्|अदन्त्
अदत् <i>a.</i> Toothless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त|अदत्तं
अदत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not given. अदत्तान्युपभुञ्जानः Ms. 4. 202.<BR>—2 Unjustly or improperly given.<BR>—3 Not given in marriage.<BR>—4 Not having given any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्ता
अदत्त + .{@-त्ता@} An unmarried girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्तम्
अदत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} A gift which is null and void (having been given under particular<BR> circumstances which make it revocable).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदत्तादायिन्, अदत्तपूर्वा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्तादायिन्
अदत्त + -आदायिन् <i>a.</i> the receiver of such a gift; one who takes what<BR> has not been given away, such as a thief; अदत्तादायिनो हस्ताल्लिप्सेत<BR> ब्राह्मणो धनं । याजनाध्यापनेनापि यथा स्तेनस्तथैव सः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्तपूर्वा
अदत्त + -पूर्वा not affianced or betrothed before; अदत्तपूर्वेत्याशङ्क्यते Māl. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्र
अदत्र <i>a.</i> [अद्-बा˚ अत्रन्] Ved. Fit to be eaten; अदत्रया<BR> दयते वार्याणि Rv. 5. 49. 3. (= अदनीयानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदध्र्यञ्च्
अदध्र्यञ्च् [अमुम् अञ्चति अदस्-अञ्च् क्विप् अध्र्यागमः P. VIII. 2. 80-81.]<BR> Going to that, tending to that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त|अदंत|अदन्तः
अदन्त <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Toothless.<BR>—2 Not yet having the teeth formed or grown (said of young ones of men<BR> or animals before the teething time).<BR>—3 Ending in अत् or अ. P. VIII. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्तः|अदन्त|अदंत
अदन्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A leech.<BR>—2 N. of Pūṣan, one of the 12 Ādityas, he having lost his teeth at<BR> the destruction of Dakṣaʼs sacrifice by Vīrabhadra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त्य|अदंत्य
अदन्त्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not dental.<BR>—2 Not fit for the teeth; injurious to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्ध
अदब्ध, -दम्भ <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Unbroken or unimpaired, unhurt,<BR> uninjured; pure, true;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्भ|अदंभ|अदम्भः
अदब्ध, -दम्भ <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Unbroken or unimpaired, unhurt,<BR> uninjured; pure, true;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्धासु
अदब्ध, -दम्भ + ˚असु or ˚आयुः having uninjured or pure<BR> life; leaving uninjured the man who sacrifices;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्धायुः|अदब्धायु
अदब्ध, -दम्भ + ˚असु or ˚आयुः having uninjured or pure<BR> life; leaving uninjured the man who sacrifices;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्धधीति
अदब्ध, -दम्भ + ˚धीति, ˚व्रत whose<BR> works or religious observances are unimpaired. अर्यमणं भगमदब्धधीतीनच्छ Rv. 6. 51. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्धव्रत
अदब्ध, -दम्भ + ˚धीति, ˚व्रत whose<BR> works or religious observances are unimpaired. अर्यमणं भगमदब्धधीतीनच्छ Rv. 6. 51. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदभ्र|अदभ्रः
अदभ्र <i>a.</i> [दम्भ्-रक्, न˚ त˚] Not scanty, plentiful,<BR> copious; अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य स स्थलीम् Ki. 1. 38; ˚अभ्रनिर्घोष Dk. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्भ|अदंभ|अदम्भः
अदम्भ <i>a.</i> Honest, undeceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्भः|अदम्भ|अदंभ
अदम्भ + .{@-भः@}<BR>—1 Honesty, absence of deceit.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदय
अदय [न˚ ब˚] Merciless, unkind, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदयम्
अदय + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Mercilessly; ardently; fervently, closely (as an<BR> embrace) इच्छामि चैनमदयं परिरब्धुमङ्गैः V. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शः|अदर्श
अदर्शः<BR>—1 Day of new moon.<BR>—2 A mirror (= आदर्श).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0053-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शनम्
अदर्शनम् —1 Not seeing, non-vision; absence, not being seen; तमाहितौत्सुक्यमदर्शनेन<BR> R. 2. 73; अन्तर्धौ येनादर्शनमिच्छति P. I. 4. 28 the person whose<BR> sight one wishes to avoid; ˚नं गतः Pt. 2; ˚नीभूतः Pt. 1<BR> become invisible; अस्य ˚नं गत्वा Pt. 2 going out of his sight,<BR> beyond the reach of vision; सा चात्यन्तमदर्शनं नयनयोर्याता V. 4. 9.<BR> lost to view, become invisible.<BR>—2 Neglect, or failure to see; ब्राह्मणादर्शनेन च Ms. 10. 43.<BR>—3 (Gram.) Disappearance, elision, omission; अदर्शनं लोपः P. I. 1. 60.<BR>—4 Non-mention, non-assertion; दर्शनादर्शनयोश्च दर्शनं प्रमाणम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 7. 36.<BR>—5 Ignorance; अदर्शनादापतिताः पुनश्चादर्शनं गताः Mb. 11. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदल|अदलः
अदल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Leafless.<BR>—2 Without parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदलः|अदल
अदल + .{@-लः@} A plant (हिज्जल) Eugenia or Barringtonia Acutangula.<BR> (Mar. समुद्रफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदला
अदल + .{@-ला@} A plant (घृतकुमारी) Aloe Indica Royle. (Mar. कोरफड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्
अदस् <i>pron. a.</i> [न दस्यते उत्क्षिप्यते अङ्गुलिर्यत्र इदंतया<BR> निर्द्धारणाय पुरोवर्तिनि एवाङ्गुलिनिर्देशः संभवति नापुरोवर्तिनि, न-दस्-क्विप्<BR> Tv.] (असौ <i>m., f.</i> अदः <i>n.</i>). That, (referring to a person<BR> or thing not present or near the speaker) (विप्रकृष्ट or परोक्ष);<BR> इदमस्तु सन्निकृष्टं समीपतरवर्ति चैतदो रूपम् । अदसस्तु विप्रकृष्टं<BR> तदिति परोक्षे विजानीयात् ॥ अमुष्य विद्या रसनाग्रनर्तकी N. 1. 5; असौ<BR> नामाऽहमस्मीति स्वनाम परिकीर्तयेत् Ms. 2. 122. I am that person, so<BR> and so (giving the name); असावहमिति ब्रूयात् 130, 216; Y. 1. 26. अदस्<BR> is, however, often used with reference to प्रत्यक्ष or सन्निकृष्ट<BR> objects &c. in the sense of ‘this here’, ‘yonder’; असौ शरण्यः शरणोन्मुखानाम्<BR> R. 6. 21. (असाविति पुरोवर्तिनो निर्देशः Malli.); अमी रथ्याः Ś. 1. 8;<BR> अमी वह्नयः 4. 18, 7. 11. It is often used in the sense of<BR> तत् as a correlative of यत्; हिंसारतश्च यो नित्यं नेहासौ सुखमेधते<BR> Ms. 4. 170. He, who &c. But when it immediately follows the relative pronoun<BR> (योऽसौ, ये अमी &c.) it conveys the sense of प्रसिद्ध ‘well-known’,<BR> ‘celebrated’, ‘renowned’; योऽसावतीन्द्रियग्राह्यः सूक्ष्मोऽव्यक्तः सनातनः<BR> Ms. 1. 7; योऽसौ कुमारसेवको नाम Mu. 3; योऽसौ चोरः Dk. 68;<BR> sometimes अदस् used by itself conveys this sense; विधुरपि विधियोगाद्<BR> ग्रस्यते राहुणाऽसौ that (so well-known to us all) moon too. See the<BR> word तद् also and the quotations from K. P. ━<i>ind.</i> There, at that<BR> time, then, thus, ever; correlative to some pronominal forms; यदादः,<BR> यत्रादः whenever, whereever &c. By अदोऽनुपदेशे P. I. 4. 70. अदस्<BR> has the force of a (गति) preposition when no direction to another<BR> is implied; अदःकृत्य अदःकृतम्; । परं प्रत्युपदेशे तु अदःकृत्वा अदःकुरु । Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदसीय
अदसीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to this or that, Śāhendra. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्यति
अदस्यति Den. P. To become that P. VIII. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदातृ
अदातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not giving, miserly; आदाननित्याच्चादातुः Ms. 11. 15 not liberal<BR>—2 Not giving (a daughter) in marriage; कालेऽदाता पिता वाच्यः Ms. 9. 4.<BR>—3 Not liable to payment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदादि
अदादि <i>a.</i> Having अद् at the head, a term used to mark roots<BR> of the second conjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान
अदान <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not giving, miserly.<BR>—2 Without rut (or not charitable); सदादानः परिक्षीणः शस्त एव करीश्वरः ।<BR> अदानः पीनगात्रोऽपि निन्द्य एव हि गर्दभः ॥ Pt. 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान्य
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान्य
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिन्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदामन्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाशु
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाशुरि
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाश्वस्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्, अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not giving, miserly, poor; irreligious, impious, जघन्वाँ इन्द्र मित्रेरूञ्चोदप्रवृद्धो<BR> हरिवो अदाशून् Rv. 1. 174. 6. यस्ते देवाँ अदाशुरिः प्रममर्ष मघत्तये Rv. 8. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाभ्य|अदाभ्यः
अदाभ्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Faithful, trusty.<BR>—2 Uninjured, unhurt; अदाभ्यः पुरएता विशाम् Rv. 3. 11. 5.<BR>—3 Pure, undefiled.<BR>—4 Unapproachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाभ्यः|अदाभ्य
अदाभ्य + .{@-भ्यः@} N. of a soma-offering in the ज्योतिष्टोम Sacrifice; अदाभ्येन प्रचरति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाय
अदाय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति दायो यस्य] Not entitled to a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायाद
अदायाद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not entitled to be an heir; पुमान्दायादोऽदायादा स्त्री Nir.; कानीनश्च<BR> सहोढश्च कीतः पौनर्भवस्तथा । स्वयंदत्तश्च शौद्रश्च षडदायादबान्धवाः ॥<BR> Ms. 9. 160.<BR>—2 Destitute of heirs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिक
अदायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दायमर्हति दाय-ठक् न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 That which is not claimed by an heir; destitute of heirs; अदायिकं<BR> धनं राजगामि Kāty.<BR>—2 Not relating to inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदारः|अदार
अदारः [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 One who has no wife, a widower or bachelor.<BR>—2 [न˚ त˚] Not injuring or tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदारिका
अदारिका N. of a plant. (Mar. वृक्षकमळ)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदासः|अदास
अदासः A free man; Ms. 10. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाह्य
अदाह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Incombustible.<BR>—2 Not fit to be burnt on the funeral fire. —3 Not capable of being burnt,<BR> epithet of परमात्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिक्क
अदिक्क <i>a.</i> Ved. Having no direction or region of the world for<BR> oneself; banished from beneath the sky. Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
अदिति <i>a.</i> [न दीयते खण्ड्यते बध्यते बृहत्त्वात्; दो-क्तिच्]<BR> Free, not tied. आदित्यासो अदितयः स्याम Rv. 7. 52. 1 boundless, unlimited,<BR> inexhaustible; entire, unbroken; happy, pious (mostly Ved. in all these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिः|अदिति
अदिति + .{@-तिः@} [अत्ति प्राणिजातम्; अदितिच्]<BR>—1 Devourer <i>i. e.</i> death; यद्यदेवासृजत तत्तदत्तुमाध्रियत, सर्वं<BR> वा अत्तीति तददितेरदितित्वम् Bṛ. Ār. Up. 1. 2. 5.<BR>—2 An epithet of God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिः|अदिति
अदिति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> [न दातुं शक्तिः]<BR>—1 Inability to give, poverty.<BR>—2 [दातुं छेत्तुम् अयोग्या]<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The earth.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The goddess Aditi, mother of the Ādityas, in mythology represented<BR> as the mother of gods; see further on.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Freedom, security; boundlessness, immensity of space (opp. to the earth).<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Inexhaustible abundance, perfection.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) The lunar mansion called पुनर्वसु.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) Speech; या प्राणेन संभवत्यदितिर्देवतामयी (शब्दादीनाम्<BR> अदनात् अदितिः Śaṅkara.).<BR>——(<i>g</i>) A cow. cf. ŚB. on MS. 10. 3-49.<BR>——(<i>h</i>) Milk; wife (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिती
अदिति + .{@-ती@} (<i>dual</i>) Heaven and earth. [अदिति literally means ‘unbounded’,<BR> ‘the boundless Heaven’, or according to others, ‘the visible infinite, the endless expanse beyond the earth, beyond the clouds, beyond the sky’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">Page0055-1</a>]<BR>. According to Yāska अदितिरदीना देवमाता,<BR> and the verse beginning with अदितिर्द्यैः &c. Rv. 1. 89. 16 he interprets<BR> by taking अदिति to mean अदीन <i>i. e.</i> अनुपक्षीण, न ह्येषां<BR> क्षयोऽस्ति इति. In the Ṛgveda Aditi is frequently implored ‘for blessings on children and cattle, for protection and for forgiveness’<BR>. She is called<BR> ‘Devamātā’ being strangely enough represented both as mother and daughter<BR> of Dakṣa. She had 8 sons; she approached the gods with 7 and cast away<BR> the 8th (Mārtaṇḍa, the sun.) In another place Aditi is addressed as<BR> ‘supporter of the sky, sustainer of the earth, sovereign of this world, wife of Viṣṇu’<BR>, but in the Mahābhārata, Rāmāyaṇa and Purāṇas,<BR> Viṣṇu is said to be the son of Aditi, one of the several daughters of<BR> Dakṣa and given in marriage to Kaśyapa by whom she was the mother of<BR> Viṣṇu in his dwarf incarnation, and also of Indra, and she is called<BR> mother of gods and the gods her sons, ‘Aditinandanas’; see Dakṣa and Kaśyapa also].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदितिजः, अदितिनन्दनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0054-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिजः|अदितिज
अदिति + -जः, -नन्दनः a god, divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिनन्दनः|अदितिनन्दन|अदितिनंदन
अदिति + -जः, -नन्दनः a god, divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीन
अदीन <i>a.</i> Not low or depressed, high-spirited; mighty, not poor; rich, happy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदीनात्मन्, अदीनवृत्ति, अदीनसत्त्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीनात्मन्
अदीन + -आत्मन्, -वृत्ति, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> not depressed in spirit, high-spirited, high-mettled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीनवृत्ति
अदीन + -आत्मन्, -वृत्ति, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> not depressed in spirit, high-spirited, high-mettled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीनसत्त्व
अदीन + -आत्मन्, -वृत्ति, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> not depressed in spirit, high-spirited, high-mettled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घ
अदीर्घ <i>a.</i> Not long.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदीर्घसूत्र, अदीर्घसूत्रिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घसूत्र
अदीर्घ + -सूत्र, -सूत्रिन् <i>a.</i> [न दीर्घं सूत्रं सूत्रवत् विस्तारो यस्य]<BR> quick, prompt in action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घसूत्रिन्
अदीर्घ + -सूत्र, -सूत्रिन् <i>a.</i> [न दीर्घं सूत्रं सूत्रवत् विस्तारो यस्य]<BR> quick, prompt in action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुःख
अदुःख <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Free from evil, propitious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदुःखनवमी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुःखनवमी
अदुःख + -नवमी the propitious 9th day in the bright half of भाद्रपद<BR> when women worship Devī to avert evil for the ensuing year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुच्छुन|अदुछुन
अदुच्छुन <i>a.</i> Ved. Free from evil, propitious. पवमानस्य ते<BR> रसो मदो राजन्नदुच्छुनः Rv. 9. 61. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुपध
अदुपध <i>a.</i> A word with अ as the Penultimate letter (P. III. 1. 98.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुर्ग
अदुर्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not inaccessible, not difficult of access.<BR>—2 Destitute of forts;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुर्ग
अदुर्ग + ˚विषयः an unfortified country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुर्मुख
अदुर्मुख <i>a.</i> Ved. Unremitting, zealous, cheerful; यस्याजुषन्नमस्विनः<BR> शमीमदुर्मुखस्य वा Rv. 8. 75. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदू
अदू <i>a.</i> Ved. Not zealous, dilatory; not worshipping; आदुवः Rv. 7. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूर
अदूर <i>a.</i> Not distant, near (in time or space); ˚वर्तिनीं सिद्धिं<BR> राजन् विगणयात्मनः R. 1. 87; ˚उज्झितवर्त्मसु मृगद्वन्द्वेषु 1. 40;<BR> ˚त्रिंशाः Sk. not far from 30, i. e. nearly 30; ˚कोपा हि मुनिजनप्रकृतिः<BR> K. 142 easily provoked, irascible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूरम्
अदूर + .{@-रम्@} Proximity, vicinity; वसन्नदूरे किल चन्द्रमौलेः R. 6. 34;<BR> त्रिंशतोऽदूरे वर्तन्ते इति अदूरत्रिंशाः Sk.; अदूरे, -रम्,<BR> -रेण, -रतः -रात् (with gen. or abl.) not far from, at no great distance<BR> from; अदूरे प्रियासमागमं ते प्रेक्षे V. 3 not far distant, very near.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदूरभव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूरभव
अदूर + -भव <i>a.</i> not being far off, being near. (P. IV. 2. 70).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषित
अदूषित <i>a.</i> Not vitiated, uncorrupted, unspotted, irreproachable;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषितधी
अदूषित + ˚धी possessing an uncorrupted soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृप्त
अदृप्त <i>a.</i> Not proud, not vain;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृप्तक्रतु
अदृप्त + ˚क्रतु not proud-minded, sober, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्
अदृश् <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Sightless, blind.<BR>—2 Not seeing, not perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्य|अदृश्यं
अदृश्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invisible; किमपि भूतमदृअश्यरूपम् Ku. 4. 45.<BR>—2 Not capable of being seen. epithet of परमेश्वर.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदृश्यकरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्यकरणम्
अदृश्य + -करणम् rendering invisible, a part of a conjurerʼs legerdemain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं|अदृष्टः
अदृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invisible, not seen; ˚पूर्व not seen before.<BR>—2 Not known or experienced, not felt; ˚विरहव्यथम् H. 1. 125.<BR>—3 Unforeseen, not observed or thought of; unknown, unobserved. तस्माददृष्टं<BR> त्वां भयमागमिष्यति Mb. 1. 3. 9.<BR>—4 Not permitted or sanctioned, illegal; न चादृष्टां (वृद्धिं)<BR> पुनर्हरेत् Ms. 8. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टः|अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं
अदृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} N. of some venomous substance or vermin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टम्
अदृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 The invisible one.<BR>—2 Destiny, fate, luck (good or bad); दैवमिति यदपि कथयसि पुरुषगुणः<BR> सोऽप्यदृष्टाख्यः Pt. 5. 30.<BR>—3 Virtue or vice as the eventual cause of pleasure or pain. (Fate is<BR> supposed to be the result of good or bad actions done in one state of existence<BR> and experienced in another, the performance of good deeds being rewarded<BR> with residence in Heaven, and of bad deeds, visited with condemnation<BR> to Hell; धर्माधर्मावदृष्टं स्यात् धर्मः स्वर्गादिसाधनम … अधर्मो<BR> नरकादीनां हेतुर्निन्दितकर्मजः Bhāṣā P. 161-2. The Vedāntins do<BR> not recognize अदृष्ट or luck; तैर्हि कर्मणः सूक्ष्मावस्थापन्नसंस्कारविशेष<BR> एव अदृष्टस्थानीयत्वेनाङ्गीक्रियते; अदृष्ठम् आत्मधर्म इति नैयायिका वैशेषिकादयश्च,<BR> सांख्यपातञ्जलास्तु बुद्धिधर्म इत्यभ्युपगच्छन्ति Tv.)<BR>—4 An unforeseen calamity or danger (such as from fire, water &c.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदृष्टार्थ, अदृष्टकर्मन्, अदृष्टकल्पना, अदृष्टनरः, अदृष्टपुरुषः, अदृष्टफल, अदृष्टहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टार्थ
अदृष्ट + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> [ब˚] having a metaphysical or occult meaning,<BR> metaphysical; having an object not evident to the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टकर्मन्
अदृष्ट + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> one who has had no practice or practical experience,<BR> not practical, inexperienced; कर्मस्वदृष्टकर्मा यः शास्त्रज्ञोऽपि<BR> विमुह्यति H. 3. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टकल्पना
अदृष्ट + -कल्पना Supposition of an invisible object or idea. दृष्टे<BR> सत्यदृष्टकल्पनाऽन्याय्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टनरः|अदृष्टनर
अदृष्ट + -नरः, -पुरुषः one of the 20 ways of peace-making, in which<BR> no third person is seen, said of a treaty concluded by the parties themselves<BR> without a mediator यत्र शत्रुः पणं कुर्यात्सोऽदृष्टपुरुषः स्मृतः H. 4. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपुरुषः|अदृष्टपुरुष
अदृष्ट + -नरः, -पुरुषः one of the 20 ways of peace-making, in which<BR> no third person is seen, said of a treaty concluded by the parties themselves<BR> without a mediator यत्र शत्रुः पणं कुर्यात्सोऽदृष्टपुरुषः स्मृतः H. 4. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टफल
अदृष्ट + -फल <i>a.</i> [ब˚] that of which the consequences are not<BR> yet visible. ({@लम्@}) the (future) result of good or bad actions;<BR> the result or consequence hidden in the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टहन्
अदृष्ट + -हन् <i>a.</i> destroying poisonous vermin (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टिः|अदृष्टि
अदृष्टिः <i>f.</i> [विरुद्धा दृष्टिः]<BR>—1 An evil or malicious eye, evil look, an angry or envious look.<BR>—2 Not being seen. ━<i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Blind, sightless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेय
अदेय <i>a.</i> Not to be given; what cannot or ought not to be given<BR> away; अदेयमासीत्त्रयमेव भूपतेः R. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेयम्
अदेय + .{@-यम्@} That which it is not right or necessary to give━ wife,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">Page0056-1</a>]<BR> sons, deposits, and a few other things belong to this class. अन्वाहितं<BR> याचितकमाधिः साधारणं च यत् । निक्षेपः पुत्रदाराश्च सर्वस्वं चान्वये<BR> सति ॥ आपत्स्वपि च कष्टासु वर्तमानेन देहिना । अदेयान्याहुराचार्या यच्चान्यस्मै<BR> प्रतिश्रुतम् ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदेयदानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0055-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेयदानम्
अदेय + -दानम् an unlawful gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेव|अदेवः
अदेव <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not god-like or divine, not pertaining to a deity.<BR>—2 Godless, impious, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवः|अदेव
अदेव + .{@-वः@} [न˚ त˚] One who is not a god.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदेवत्र, अदेवमातृक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवत्र
अदेव + -त्र <i>a.</i> [न देवाः त्रायन्ते प्रीयन्ते अनेन, त्रै-करणे क]<BR> not gratifying the gods, such as food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवमातृक|अदेवमातृकः
अदेव + -मातृक <i>a.</i> [न देवो मेघो माता वृष्टिकारकः यस्य] not<BR> rained upon; (lit.) not having the god of rain as mother to suckle or water;<BR> hence (artificially) supplied with the water of rivers, canals &c., irrigated;<BR> वितन्वति क्षेममदेवमातृकाश्चिराय तस्मिन्कुरवश्चकासते Ki. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवयत्|अदेवयन्त्
अदेवयत्, -यु <i>a.</i> [न देवं याति प्राप्नोति] Not reaching the<BR> gods by prayers, impious, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवयु
अदेवयत्, -यु <i>a.</i> [न देवं याति प्राप्नोति] Not reaching the<BR> gods by prayers, impious, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेशः|अदेश
अदेशः [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 A wrong place, not oneʼs proper place or strong position; ˚स्थो हि<BR> रिपुणा स्वल्पकेनापि हन्यते H. 4. 45; स्त्रियं स्पृशेददेशे यः Ms. 8. 358;<BR> नादेशे तर्पणं कुर्यात् &c.<BR>—2 A bad country; The Smṛtis mention several places of this description:−<BR> म्लेच्छ, आनर्तक, अङ्ग, मगध, सुराष्ट्र, दक्षिणापथ, वङ्ग, कलिङ्ग &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अदेशकालः, अदेशस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेशकालः|अदेशकाल
अदेशः + -कालः wrong place and time; अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च<BR> दीयते । Bg. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेशस्थ
अदेशः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> [स˚ त˚] in the wrong place, out of place;<BR> absent from oneʼs country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश्य
अदेश्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚ न देष्टुं योग्यः]<BR>—1 Not fit to be ordered, advised, indicated or pointed out; अदेश्यं<BR> यश्च दिशति Ms. 8. 53.<BR>—2 Not on the spot or pertaining to the place or occasion referred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रेश्य
अद्रेश्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Invisible (अदृश्य). Muṇḍ. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैन्य
अदैन्य <i>a.</i> Involving no humiliation or self-degradation Bh. 3. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैव
अदैव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Not predestined or predetermined (by Gods or by Fate).<BR>—2 Not connected with the Gods or their action, not divine; अदैवं भोजयेच्छ्राद्धम्<BR> Ms. 3. 247 (Kull. वैश्वदेवब्राह्मणभोजनरहितम्).<BR>—3 Unfortunate, ill-fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोग्धृ
अदोग्धृ <i>a.</i> Not exacting; considerate (as a king.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमद
अदोमद, -ध <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not causing inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमध
अदोमद, -ध <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not causing inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोहः|अदोह
अदोहः<BR>—1 The time when milking is not practicable.<BR>—2 Not milking; अदोहं चादिशद्गवाम् R. 17. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोष|अदोषः
अदोष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Free from faults, demerits &c.; innocent; जायामदोषामुत संत्यजामि R. 14. 34.<BR>—2 Free from the faults of composition, such as अश्लीलता, ग्राम्यता<BR> &c.; see दोष; अदोषौ शब्दार्थौ K. P. 1; अदोषं गुणवत् काव्यम् Sar. K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोषः|अदोष
अदोष + .{@-षः@} Not a fault; किमित्यदोषेण तिरस्कृता वयम् Ki. 14. 11<BR> though not at fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्गः|अद्ग
अद्गः [अद्यते देवैः, अद्-कर्मणि गन् Uṇ. 1. 120, = पुरोडाश]<BR> A sacrificial oblation called पुरोडाश, q. v. Av. 1. 27. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धा
अद्धा <i>ind.</i> [अत्यते अत् तं सन्ततं गमनं ज्ञानं वा दधाति क्विप् Tv.]<BR>—1 Truly, clearly, surely, undoubtedly, in truth, really, certainly, indeed;<BR> को अद्धा वेद Rv. 10. 129. 6. अद्धा श्रियं पालितसङ्गराय प्रत्यर्पयिष्यति R. 13. 65.<BR>—2 Manifestly, clearly; व्यालाधिपं च यतते परिरब्धुमद्धा Bv. 1. 95.<BR>—3 in this way, thus; ˚कृ = साक्षात्कृ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्धापुरुष, अद्धाबोधेयाः, अद्धालोहकर्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धापुरुष
अद्धा + -पुरुष a right or true man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धाबोधेयाः
अद्धा + -बोधेयाः (pl.) N. of a school of the Śukla Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धालोहकर्ण
अद्धा + -लोहकर्ण <i>a.</i> having ears clearly or quite red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धातिः|अद्धाति
अद्धातिः Ved. A wise man, seer. अथैकं चकं यद्गुहा तदद्धातय<BR> इद्विदुः Rv. 10. 85. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 5. 1 अदि भुवो डुतच्; according to Nir. न<BR> भूतम् the like of which did not take place before.]<BR>—1 Wonderful, marvellous; ˚कर्मन् of wonderful deeds; ˚गन्ध having<BR> wonderful smell; ˚दर्शन, ˚रूप; prodigious; extraordinary, transcendental, supernatural.<BR>—2 Ved. Unobserved, invisible (opp. दृश्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतम्
अद्भुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A wonder, a wonderful thing or occurrence, a prodigy, miracle; देव<BR> अद्भुतं खलु संवृत्तम् Ś. 5 a wonderful or unexpected occurrence; आकालिकमनध्यायं<BR> विद्यात्सर्वाद्भुतेषु च Ms. 4. 118.<BR>—2 Surprise, astonishment, wonder (<i>m.</i>) also; ˚उद्भ्रान्तदेवासुराणि<BR> विकान्तचरितानि U. 6 lost in wonder.<BR>—3 One of the five proportions of the measurement of height; in this measurement<BR> height is twice the breadth; हीनं तु द्वयं तद्द्विगुणं चाद्भुतं कथितम्<BR> Māna. 11. 20. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतः|अद्भुत|अद्भुतं
अद्भुत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 One of the 8 or 9 <i>Rasas</i>, the marvellous sentiment; जगति जनितात्यद्भुतरसः U. 3. 44.<BR>—2 N. of the Indra of the 9th Manvantara.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्भुतोत्तरकाण्डम्, अद्भुतैनस्, अद्भुतधर्मः, अद्भुतब्राह्मणम्, अद्भुतरामायणम्, अद्भुतशान्तिः, अद्भुतसंकाश, अद्भुतसारः, अद्भुतस्वन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतोत्तरकाण्डम्
अद्भुत + -उत्तरकाण्डम् N. of a work, an appendix to or imitation of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतैनस्
अद्भुत + -एनस् <i>a.</i> Ved. in whom no sin is visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतधर्मः|अद्भुतधर्म
अद्भुत + -धर्मः a system of prodigies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतब्राह्मणम्
अद्भुत + -ब्राह्मणम् N. of a portion of a Brāhmaṇa belonging to the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतरामायणम्
अद्भुत + -रामायणम् N. of a work ascribed to Vāmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतशान्तिः|अद्भुतशान्ति
अद्भुत + -शान्तिः <i>f.</i> N. of the Sixtyseventh Pariśiṣṭa of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतसंकाश
अद्भुत + -संकाश <i>a.</i> resembling a marvel; so ˚उपम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतसारः|अद्भुतसार
अद्भुत + -सारः the wonderful resin (of the खदिर or Catechu plant)<BR> (Mar. खैराची राळ); Mimosa Catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतस्वन|अद्भुतस्वनः
अद्भुत + -स्वन <i>a.</i> having a wonderful sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतस्वनः|अद्भुतस्वन
अद्भुत + -स्वन + .({@-नः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मन्
अद्मन् <i>n.</i> Ved. Eating, a meal; a house (?) आ स्वमद्म युवमानो<BR> अजरस्तृष्वविष्यन्नतसेषु तिष्टति Rv. 1. 58. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मसद्
अद्मन् + .{@-सद्@} <i>m.</i> (also {@-सद्वन्@}) <i>a.</i><BR> companion at a meal; अद्मा हि सूनो अद्मसद्वा Rv. VI. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मनिः|अद्मनि
अद्मनिः [अत्ति सर्वान्; उद्-मनिन् Uṇ. 2. 104 अदेर्मुट् च] Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मर|अद्मरः
अद्मर <i>a.</i> [अत्तुं शीलमस्य; अद्-कर्तरि क्मरच्] Voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य <i>a.</i> Eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यम्
अद्य + .{@-द्यम्@} Food, anything eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य <i>ind.</i> [अस्मिन्नहनि इदंशद्वस्य निपातः सप्तम्यर्थे; अस्मिन्<BR> द्यवि अहनि वा Nir.]<BR>—1 Today, this day; अद्य त्वां त्वरयति दारुणः कृतान्तः Māl. 5. 25;<BR> ˚रात्रौ to-night, this night; ˚प्रातरेव this very morning;<BR> oft. in comp. with दिन,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">Page0057-1</a>]<BR> दिवस &c., ˚दिवसनक्षत्रं of this day, to-dayʼs; अद्यैव<BR> this very day; अद्यैव वा मरणमस्तु युगान्तरे वा Bh. 2. 74.<BR>—2 Now; अद्य गच्छ गता रात्रिः Ks. 4. 68.<BR>—3 At present, now-a-days. [cf. L. <i>ho-die</i>.].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्यापि, अद्यावधि, अद्यपूर्वम्, अद्यप्रभृति, अद्यश्वीन, अद्यसुत्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0056-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यापि
अद्य + -अपि still, yet, even now, to this day, down to the present time<BR> or moment; अद्यापि नूनं हरकोपवह्निः Ś. 3. 3; अद्यापि ते मन्युविषयः<BR> U. 3; अद्यापि नोच्छ्वसिति <i>ibid.</i>; न˚ not yet; गुरुः खेदं<BR> खिन्ने मयि भजति नाद्यापि कुरुषु Ve. 1. 11; (every one of the 50 stanzas<BR> of C. P. begins with अद्यापि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यावधि
अद्य + -अवधि<BR>—1 from to-day; ˚धि भवद्भयो भिन्नोऽहं Ve. 1.<BR>—2 till to-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यपूर्वम्
अद्य + -पूर्वम् before now; अद्यपूर्वोच्चरित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यप्रभृति
अद्य + -प्रभृति <i>ind.</i> from to-day, this day forward, henceforth; अद्यप्रभृत्यवनताङ्गि<BR> तवास्मि दासः Ku. 5. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यश्वीन|अद्यश्वीनं
अद्य + -श्वीन <i>a.</i> [अद्य श्वः परदिने वा जनिष्यते प्रसोष्यते वा,<BR> अद्य-श्वस्-ख टिलोपः अद्यश्वानीवष्टब्धे P. V. 2. 13] likely to happen<BR> to-day or tomorrow, imminent; ˚नम् मरणम्, ˚नः वियोगः Sk. (= आसन्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यश्वीना
अद्य + -श्वीन + .({@-ना@}) a female near delivery (आसन्नप्रसवा); अद्य श्वो वा<BR> विजायते इति अद्यश्वीना वडवा Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यसुत्या
अद्य + -सुत्या extraction and consecration of Soma juice on the same day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f</i>)<BR> [अद्य भवः; अद्य टपु तुडागमश्च]<BR>—1 Pertaining or referring to, extending over, to-day; ˚दिवस, ˚काल<BR> &c. आ न्याय्यादुत्थानादा न्याय्याच्च संवेशनात् । एषोऽद्यतनः कालः । अपरे<BR> पुनराहुरुभयतोऽर्द्धरात्रम् अद्यतनः कालः । Kāśi., कलोपसर्जनेच तुल्यम्.<BR>—2 Current, now-a-days, prevalent at present, modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनः|अद्यतन
अद्यतन + .{@-नः@} The current or this day, period of the current day (Kāśi.<BR> on P. I. 2. 57); see अनद्यतन also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनी
अद्यतन + .{@-नी@} (<i>scil.</i> वृत्तिः) A name given to the Aorist tense, as<BR> it denotes an action done to-day or on the same day (= ˚भूतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनीय
अद्यतनीय = अद्यतन<BR>—1 Of to-day; ˚हिमपातो व्यर्थतां नीयते Pt. 3.<BR>—2 Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यु
अद्यु <i>a.</i> Ved. Blunt, not sharp or harmful; अद्युं कृणोत शंसं<BR> निनित्सोः Rv. 7. 34. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्युत्
अद्युत् <i>a.</i> Not bright, अद्यं द्योतयदद्युतः Rv. 6. 39. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यूत्य
अद्यूत्य <i>a.</i> [न द्यूतलब्धं, न˚ त˚] Not obtained by gambling, honestly got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यूत्यम्
अद्यूत्य + .{@-अद्यूत्यम्@}<BR>—1 Unlucky gambling;<BR>—2 The watch just before the dawn (?) अद्यूत्येऽवसे नि ह्वये Rv. 1. 112. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव|अद्रवः
अद्रव <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not liquid, not of the nature of a liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रवः|अद्रव
अद्रव + .{@-वः@} Not a liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्यम्
अद्रव्यम् [न˚ त˚] A worthless thing, an object which is<BR> good for nothing; नाद्रव्ये विहिता काचित् क्रिया फलवती भवेत् H. Pr. 43;<BR> hence, a worthless or bad pupil or recipient of instruction; विनेतुरद्रव्यपरिग्रह<BR> एव बुद्धिलाघवं प्रकाशयति M. 1; अद्रव्यमेत्य भुवि शुद्धनयोऽपि<BR> मन्त्री Mu. 7. 14. क्रिया हि द्रव्यं विनयति नाद्रव्यम् Kau. A. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिः|अद्रि
अद्रिः [अद्-किन् Uṇ. 4. 65; according to Nir. fr. दॄ to tear<BR> or अद् to eat.]<BR>—1 A mountain.<BR>—2 A stone, especially one for pounding Soma with or grinding it on.<BR>—3 A thunderbolt (आदृणाति येन Nir.).<BR>—4 A tree.<BR>—5 The sun. cf. अद्रिः शैलेऽर्कवृक्षयोः । Nm.<BR>—6 A mass of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">Page0057-2</a>]<BR> clouds (probably so called from its resemblance to a mountain); a cloud<BR> (आदरयितव्यो भवति ह्यसौ उदकार्थं Nir.) mostly Ved.<BR>—7 A kind of measure.<BR>—8 The number<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्रीशः, अद्रिपतिः, अद्रिनाथः, अद्रिकटक, अद्रिकर्णी, अद्रिकीला, अद्रिकुक्षिः, अद्रिज, अद्रिजात, अद्रिजूत, अद्रिदुग्ध, अद्रितनया, अद्रिनन्दिनी, अद्रिद्विष्, अद्रिभिद्, अद्रिहन्, अद्रिद्रोणि, अद्रिणी, अद्रिपतिः, अद्रिराजः, अद्रिबर्हस्, अद्रिबुध्न, अद्रिभू, अद्रिमातृ, अद्रिवह्निः, अद्रिशय्यः, अद्रिशृङ्गम्, अद्रिसानु, अद्रिसुत, अद्रिसारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रीशः|अद्रीश
अद्रिः + -ईशः, -पतिः, -नाथः &c.<BR>—1 the lord of mountains, the Himālaya.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva (Lord of Kailāsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिपतिः|अद्रिपति
अद्रिः + -ईशः, -पतिः, -नाथः &c.<BR>—1 the lord of mountains, the Himālaya.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva (Lord of Kailāsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिनाथः|अद्रिनाथ
अद्रिः + -ईशः, -पतिः, -नाथः &c.<BR>—1 the lord of mountains, the Himālaya.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva (Lord of Kailāsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकटक
अद्रिः + -कटक the ridge of mountain; नितम्बः पश्चिमश्रोणीभागेऽद्रिकटकेऽपि च । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकर्णी|अद्रिकर्ण्णी
अद्रिः + -कर्णी <i>a.</i> plant (अपराजिता) Clitoria Ternatea Lin. (Mar.<BR> पांढरी गोकर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकीला
अद्रिः + -कीला [अद्रयः कुलपर्वताः कीलाः शङ्कव इव यस्याः] the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकीलः|अद्रिकील
अद्रिः + -कीला + .({@-लः@}) N. of the mountain विष्कुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकुक्षिः|अद्रिकुक्षि
अद्रिः + -कुक्षिः a mountain cave, mountain side अस्मिन्नहमद्रिकुक्षौ व्यापारितः R. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिज|अद्रिजं
अद्रिः + -ज <i>a.</i> [अद्रौ जायते; जन्-ड] produced from, or found among<BR> mountains, mountain-born. अब्जा गोजा ऋतजा अद्रिजा ऋतम् Rv. 4. 41. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिजा
अद्रिः + -ज + .({@-जा@})<BR>—1 a plant (सैंहली). (Mar. सिंहपिंपळी).<BR>—2 {@-कन्या, -तनया, -सुता@} &c. Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिजम्
अद्रिः + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) red chalk (शिलाजतु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिजात|अद्रिजातः
अद्रिः + -जात <i>a.</i> mountain-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिजातः|अद्रिजात
अद्रिः + -जात + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 forest conflagration.<BR>—2 the ‘Sun-born’, Haṃsa or Swan.<BR>—3 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिजूत
अद्रिः + -जूत, -दुग्ध Ved. [तृ˚ त˚] expressed or extracted by<BR> means of stones. रथो ह वामृतजा अद्रिजूतः Rv. 3. 58. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिदुग्ध
अद्रिः + -जात + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 forest conflagration.<BR>—2 the ‘Sun-born’, Haṃsa or Swan.<BR>—3 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रितनया
अद्रिः + -तनया, -नन्दिनी<BR>—1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—2 N. of a metre of 4 lines, each having 23 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिनन्दिनी
अद्रिः + -तनया, -नन्दिनी<BR>—1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—2 N. of a metre of 4 lines, each having 23 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिद्विष्
अद्रिः + -द्विष्, -भिद्, -हन् <i>m.</i> [अद्रिं द्वेष्टि भिनात्ति वा, द्विष्-भिद्-हन्-क्विप्]<BR> the enemy or splitter of mountains (or clouds personified), epithet of<BR> Indra अहनद्वज्रेणाद्रीनिवाद्रिहा Mb. 8. 20. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभिद्
अद्रिः + -द्विष्, -भिद्, -हन् <i>m.</i> [अद्रिं द्वेष्टि भिनात्ति वा, द्विष्-भिद्-हन्-क्विप्]<BR> the enemy or splitter of mountains (or clouds personified), epithet of<BR> Indra अहनद्वज्रेणाद्रीनिवाद्रिहा Mb. 8. 20. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिहन्
अद्रिः + -द्विष्, -भिद्, -हन् <i>m.</i> [अद्रिं द्वेष्टि भिनात्ति वा, द्विष्-भिद्-हन्-क्विप्]<BR> the enemy or splitter of mountains (or clouds personified), epithet of<BR> Indra अहनद्वज्रेणाद्रीनिवाद्रिहा Mb. 8. 20. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिद्रोणि
अद्रिः + -द्रोणि, -णी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a mountain valley. Dk. 2. 8.<BR>—2 a river taking its rise in a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिणी
अद्रिः + -द्रोणि, -णी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a mountain valley. Dk. 2. 8.<BR>—2 a river taking its rise in a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिपतिः|अद्रिपति
अद्रिः + -पतिः, -राजः &c. See ˚ईश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिराजः|अद्रिराज
अद्रिः + -पतिः, -राजः &c. See ˚ईश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिबर्हस्
अद्रिः + -बर्हस् <i>a.</i> Ved. [अद्रेर्बर्ह इव बर्हो यस्य] as strong<BR> or hard as a mountain; mountain-high (?); पीयूषं द्यौरदितिरद्रिबर्हाः Rv. 10. 63. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिबुध्न
अद्रिः + -बुध्न <i>a.</i> [अद्रेर्बुध्न इव बुध्नो यस्य] rooted in a mountain<BR> or rock; as hard as a stone or mountain. अयं निधिः सरमे अद्रिबुध्नः<BR> Rv. 10. 108. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभू
अद्रिः + -भू <i>a.</i> [अद्रौ भवति जायते] mountain-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभूः
अद्रिः + -भू + .({@-भूः@}) N. of a plant (आखुकर्णी or अपराजिता. Mar. उंदिरकानी, गोकर्णी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिमातृ
अद्रिः + -मातृ Ved. [अद्रि मेघः तज्जलं मिमीते, अद्रेर्माता वा मा-तृच्]<BR> producing water from clouds (मेघजलनिर्मातृ); having a mountain for<BR> the mother (?). कोशं दिवोऽद्रिमातरम् Rv. 9. 86. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिवह्निः|अद्रिवह्नि
अद्रिः + -वह्निः forest conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिशय्यः|अद्रिशय्य
अद्रिः + -शय्यः (having the mountain कैलास for his bed) N. of Śiva;<BR> cf. ˚ईश, ˚इन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिशृङ्गम्
अद्रिः + -शृङ्गम्, -सानु mountain peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसानु
अद्रिः + -शृङ्गम्, -सानु mountain peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिषुत
अद्रिः + -सुत (˚षुत), {@-संहत@} <i>a.</i><BR> prepared or expressed by means of stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसंहत
अद्रिः + -सुत (˚षुत), {@-संहत@} <i>a.</i><BR> prepared or expressed by means of stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसारः|अद्रिसार
अद्रिः + -सारः [अद्रेः सार इव ष˚ त˚] ‘the essence of mountains’,<BR> iron. ━<i>a.</i> hard like a mountain;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसारमय
अद्रिः + -सारः + ˚मय made of iron or very hard<BR> ततः सुबाहुस्त्रिंशद्भिरद्रिसारमयैः शरैः Mb. 7. 18. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिवत्|अद्रिवन्त्
अद्रिवत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Armed with, or having stones or thunderbolts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुह्
अद्रुह्^1, -द्रुह्वन् <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Free from malice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुह्वन्
अद्रुह्^1, -द्रुह्वन् <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Free from malice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रेश्य
अद्रेश्य <i>a.</i> Invisible अदृश्य; Muṇḍ. 1. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघ
अद्रोघ <i>a.</i> Ved. [द्रुह्-घञ् वेदे घत्वं न˚ ब˚] True, not<BR> false, free from malice;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघवाच्
अद्रोघ + ˚वाच् speaking the truth;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघावित
अद्रोघ + ˚अवित guarding from malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघम्
अद्रोघ + .{@-घम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without malice or falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0057-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोहः|अद्रोह
अद्रोहः Absence of malice or ill-feeling; moderation, mildness, अद्रोहेणैव<BR> भूतानामल्पद्रोहेण वा पुनः । या वृत्तिस्तां समास्थाप्य विप्रो जीवेदनापदि ॥ Ms. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वन्द्व
अद्वन्द्व <i>a.</i> Without duality or enmity; असमस्तपदवृत्तिमिव<BR> अद्वन्द्वां K. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अद्वय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति द्वयं यस्य]<BR>—1 Not two.<BR>—2 Without a second, unique; sole; अद्वयं ब्रह्म Ved. Sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयः|अद्वय
अद्वय + .{@-यः@} [अद्वयं विज्ञानाभेदः पदार्थानाम् अस्त्यस्य वादकत्वेन अस्त्यर्थे<BR> अच्] N. of Buddha<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयम्
अद्वय + .{@-यम्@} [न˚ त˚] Non-duality, unity, identity; especially<BR> of Brahman and the universe, or of spirit and matter; the highest truth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्वयानन्दः, अद्वयवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयानन्दः|अद्वयानन्द
अद्वय + -आनन्दः = अद्वैतानन्दः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयवादिन्
अद्वय + -वादिन् (= अद्वैत˚) —1 one who propounds the identity of spirit<BR> and matter or of Brahman and the universe (सर्वमेव वस्तु चित्स्वरूपं<BR> नान्यदतो द्वितीयमस्ति इति यः प्रतिपादयति) —2 Buddha; Jina; षडभिज्ञो<BR> दशबलोऽद्वयवादी विनायकः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयत्|अद्वयन्त्
अद्वयत्, अद्वयस् <i>a.</i><BR> Ved. Having no second; सखा सुशेवो अद्वयाः<BR> Rv. 1. 187. 3 (द्वयरहित); free from duplicity, true, sincere (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयस्
अद्वयत्, अद्वयस् <i>a.</i><BR> Ved. Having no second; सखा सुशेवो अद्वयाः<BR> Rv. 1. 187. 3 (द्वयरहित); free from duplicity, true, sincere (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयाविन्
अद्वयाविन् <i>a.</i> [अद्वयम् अस्त्यर्थे विनि छन्दसि दीर्घः] Not having<BR> two ways (देवपितृयानरूपमार्गद्वयरहित); पुत्रस्य पाथः पदमद्वयाविनः Rv. 1. 159. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयु
अद्वयु <i>a.</i> [द्वयं द्विप्रकारोऽस्त्यस्य बा˚ उ, न˚ ब˚]<BR> Free from duplicity, the same internally or externally (अन्तर्बाह्यैकरूप).<BR> उपद्वयुं चाद्वयुं च वसवः Rv. 8. 18. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वारम्
अद्वारम् Not a door, any passage or entrance which is not intended<BR> to serve as a regular door; अद्वारेण न चातीयाद् ग्रामं वा वेश्म वा पुरम्<BR> Ms. 4. 73; नाद्वारेण विशेत् Y. 1. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वारासङ्गः|अद्वारासङ्ग
अद्वारासङ्गः Absence of forming a queue at the door; कार्यार्थिनामद्वारासङ्गं<BR> कारयेत् Kau. A. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीय|अद्वितीयः
अद्वितीय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति द्वितीयं यस्य]<BR>—1 Without a second, matchless, peerless; न केवलं रूपे शिल्पेऽप्यद्वितीया<BR> मालविका M. 2; किमुर्वशी अद्वितीया रूपेण V. 2.<BR>—2 Without a companion, alone. —3 Sole, only, unique, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीयम्
अद्वितीय + .{@-यम्@} Brahman; एकं ˚यं ब्रह्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्विषेण्य
अद्विषेण्य [न˚ त˚] Not malevolent, not to be disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष|अद्वेषः
अद्वेष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Free from hatred or malevolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषः|अद्वेष
अद्वेष + .{@-षः@} Freedom from hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषस्
अद्वेषस् <i>a.</i> [द्विष्-असुन्. न˚ त˚] Friendly, not hating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not dual; of one or uniform nature, equable, unchanging; ˚तं सुखदुःखयोः U. 1. 39.<BR>—2 Matchless, peerless, sole, only, unique.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतम्
अद्वैत + .{@-तम्@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Non-duality, identity; especially that of Brahman with the universe<BR> or with the soul, or of soul and matter; see अद्वय also.<BR>—2 The supreme or highest truth or Brahman itself.<BR>—3 N. of an Upaniṣad; अद्वैतेन solely, without any duplicity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अद्वैतानन्दः, अद्वैतवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतानन्दः|अद्वैतानन्द
अद्वैत + -आनन्दः (अद्वय˚)<BR>—1 the joy arising from a knowledge of the identity of the universe and<BR> the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 N. of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">Page0058-2</a>]<BR> author and Founder of the Vaiṣṇava sect in Bengal, flourished at the<BR> close of the 15th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतवादिन्
अद्वैत + -वादिन् = अद्वयवादिन् q. v. above; a Vedāntin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैध
अद्वैध <i>a.</i> Not divided or disunited; free from malice. यद्यप्येषभवेद्भर्ता<BR> अनार्यो वृत्तिवर्जितः । अद्वैधमत्र वर्तव्यम् Rām. 2. 118. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध|अधः
अध, अधा <i>ind.</i> Ved. Used like अथ as an inceptive<BR> particle in the sense of ‘now’, ‘then’, ‘afterwards’, ‘moreover’, ‘and’,<BR> ‘partly’, ‘so much the more’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधा
अध, अधा <i>ind.</i> Ved. Used like अथ as an inceptive<BR> particle in the sense of ‘now’, ‘then’, ‘afterwards’, ‘moreover’, ‘and’,<BR> ‘partly’, ‘so much the more’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन
अधन <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Without wealth, poor. कृत्वा नृशंसं ह्यधने धिगस्त्वधनतामिह Mb. 12. 8. 11.<BR>—2 Not entitled or competent to possess independent property (in law);<BR> भार्या पुत्रश्च दासश्च त्रय एवाधनाः स्मृताः । यत्ते समधिगच्छन्ति<BR> यस्य ते तस्य तद्धनम् ॥ Ms. 8. 416.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन्य
अधन्य <i>a.</i> Unhappy, wretched, miserable; हन्त धिङ् मामधन्यम् U. 1. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम <i>a.</i> ‘one who does not blow’. cf. अधमः कुत्सिते न्यूने<BR> अधःस्थाध्मानयोरपि Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम <i>a.</i> [अव्-अम; अवतेः अमः, वस्य पक्षे धः Uṇ. 5. 54.]<BR> The lowest, vilest, meanest; very bad, or low, or vile (in quality, worth,<BR> position &c.) (opp. उत्तम); अधममध्यमोत्तमाः or उत्तमाधममध्यमाः<BR> &c.; शस्त्रावपाते गर्भस्य पातनेचोत्तमो दमः । उत्तमो वाधमो वापि<BR> पुरुषस्त्रीप्रमापणे ॥ Y. 2. 277. oft. at the end of comp.; नर˚,<BR> द्विज˚; चाण्डालश्चाधमो नृणाम् Ms. 10. 12 lowest in position; अधम˚<BR> the vilest of the vile, the meanest wretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमः|अधम
अधम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 An unblushing sensualist (भयदयालज्जाशून्यः कामकीडाविषये कर्तव्याकर्तव्याविचारकः<BR> Śabdak.); वापीं स्नातुमितो गतासि न पुनस्तस्याधमस्यान्तिक्रम् K. P. 1.<BR>—2 A sort of योग or conjunction of planets (नृणां वित्तज्ञानादिषु<BR> अधमत्वसूचकः रविचन्द्रयोः स्थितिविशेषरूपो योगभेदः Tv.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमा
अधम + .{@-मा@} A bad mistress (हितकारिप्रियतमेऽहितकारिणी). [cf. L. <i>infimus</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधमाङ्गम्, अधमार्धम्, अधमार्ध्य, अधमाचार, अधमर्णः, अधमर्णिकः, अधमभृतः, अधमभृतकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमाङ्गम्
अधम + -अङ्गम् [कर्म˚] the foot (opp. उत्तमाङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमार्धम्
अधम + -अर्धम् [कर्म˚] the lower half of the body (below navel)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमार्ध्य
अधम + -अर्ध्य <i>a.</i> [अधमार्धे भवः] connected with the lower part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमाचार|अधमाचारः
अधम + -आचार <i>a.</i> [ब˚] of the vilest conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमाचारः|अधमाचार
अधम + -आचार + ({@-रः@})<BR> (कर्म˚) the meanest conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णः|अधमर्ण
अधम + -ऋणः, -ऋणिकः [अधमः अधमावस्थां प्राप्तः ऋणेन, ततः ठन्]<BR> a debtor (opp. उत्तमर्णः) (lit. reduced to a low position by his<BR> incurring debt). मन्येऽधमर्णप्रतिमेन भर्त्रे प्रत्यर्पितोऽभूदशितो धनौघः ।<BR> Śiva B. 23. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिकः|अधमर्णिक
अधम + -ऋणः, -ऋणिकः [अधमः अधमावस्थां प्राप्तः ऋणेन, ततः ठन्]<BR> a debtor (opp. उत्तमर्णः) (lit. reduced to a low position by his<BR> incurring debt). मन्येऽधमर्णप्रतिमेन भर्त्रे प्रत्यर्पितोऽभूदशितो धनौघः ।<BR> Śiva B. 23. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमभृतः|अधमभृत
अधम + -भृतः, -भृतकः [कर्म˚] a porter, groom, a servant of the<BR> lowest class, one of the 3 kinds of servants; उत्तमस्त्वायुधीयोत्र मध्यमस्तु<BR> कृषीवलः । अधमो भारवाही स्यादित्येवं विविधो भृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमभृतकः|अधमभृतक
अधम + -भृतः, -भृतकः [कर्म˚] a porter, groom, a servant of the<BR> lowest class, one of the 3 kinds of servants; उत्तमस्त्वायुधीयोत्र मध्यमस्तु<BR> कृषीवलः । अधमो भारवाही स्यादित्येवं विविधो भृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर <i>a.</i> [न ध्रियते; धृ-अच्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Lower (opp. उत्तर), (lit. not held up); tending downwards; under,<BR> nether, downwards; ˚वासः under garment; असितमधरवासो बिभ्रतः<BR> Ki. 4. 38; cf. अम्बर; सुवर्णसूत्राकलिताधराम्बराम् Śi. 1. 6; ˚ओष्ठ<BR> lower or nether lip, see below. (In this sense अधर partakes of the<BR> character of a pronoun).<BR>—2 Low, mean, vile; ˚उत्तरम् See below; lower in quality,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">Page0059-1</a>]<BR> inferior.<BR>—3 Silenced, worsted, not able to speak; see हीन, हीनवादिन्.<BR>—4 Previous, preceding as in अधरेद्युः, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरः|अधर|अधरं
अधर + .{@-रः@} The nether (or sometimes the upper) lip; in general ˚पत्रम्.<BR> प्रवेपमानाधरपत्रशोभिना Ku. 5. 27 leaf-like lower lip; बिम्बाधरालक्तकः<BR> M. 3. 5; पक्वबिम्बाधरोष्ठी Me. 84; पिबसि रतिसर्वस्वमधरम्<BR> Ś. 1. 21, 1. 23, 3. 23; cf. अधरं खलु बिम्बनामकं फलमाभ्यामिति<BR> भव्यमन्वयम् । लभतेऽधरबिम्ब इत्यदः पदमस्या रदनच्छदे वदत् ॥ N. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरा
अधर + .{@-रा@} The nadir; (अधोदिश्) or the southern direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरम्
अधर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The lower part (of the body); पृष्टवंशाधरे त्रिकम् Ak.<BR>—2 Pudendum Muliebre (also <i>m.</i>). —3 Address, speech (opp. उत्तर);<BR> statement, sometimes used for reply also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधरोत्तर, अधरौष्ठः, अधरौष्ठः, अधरकंटकः, अधरकंटिका, अधरकण्ठः, अधरकायः, अधरपानम्, अधरमधु, अधरामृतम्, अधरस्वस्तिकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0058-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरोत्तर
अधर + -उत्तर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 higher and lower, inferior and superior, worse and better; राज्ञः<BR> समक्षमेवावयोः ˚व्यक्तिर्भविष्यति M. 1; व्यत्यये कर्मणां साम्यं<BR> पूर्ववच्चाधरोत्तरम् Y. 1. 96.<BR>—2 former; prior and later; sooner and later; यश्चाधरोत्तरानर्थान् विगीतान्नावबुध्यते Ms. 8. 53.<BR>—3 in a contrary way, topsy-turvy, upside down (the natural order of things<BR> being inverted); श्रुतं भवट्भिरधरोत्तरम् Ś. 5 you have (certainly)<BR> learnt in a contrary way, <i>i. e.</i> to consider good as bad and <i>vice</i><BR> <i>versa</i>; (it might perhaps also mean “have you, i. e. the members of the<BR> Kingʼs court”, heard this mean or base reply अधरं च तदुत्तरम्);<BR> (यदि न प्रणयेद्राजा दण्डं) स्वाम्यं च न स्यात्कस्मिंश्चित् प्रवर्तेताधरोत्तरम्<BR> Ms. 7. 21 (अधरम् = शूद्रादि, उत्तरम् = प्रधानम्); अधर्मेण जितो<BR> धर्मः प्रवृत्तमधरोत्तरम् Mb.<BR>—4 nearer and further.<BR>—5 question and answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरौष्ठः|अधरौष्ठ
अधर + -ओष्ठः, -औष्ठः P. वार्त्तिक ओत्वोष्टदोःसमासे वा. the lower<BR> lip; अङ्गुलिसंवृत˚ Ś. 3. 24; Me. 84<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरौष्ठम्
अधर + -ओष्ठः, -औष्ठः + .({@-ष्ठम्@}) the lower and upper lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरौष्ठः|अधरौष्ठ
अधर + -ओष्ठः, -औष्ठः P. वार्त्तिक ओत्वोष्टदोःसमासे वा. the lower<BR> lip; अङ्गुलिसंवृत˚ Ś. 3. 24; Me. 84<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरकंटकः|अधरकण्टक
अधर + -कंटकः a prickly plant; Hedysarum Alhagi (धमासा Mar.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरकंटिका
अधर + -कंटिका a plant, Asparagus racemosus (Mar. लघुशतावरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरकण्ठः|अधरकण्ठ
अधर + -कण्ठः the lower part of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरकायः|अधरकाय
अधर + -कायः [अधरं कायस्य] the lower part of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरपानम्
अधर + -पानम् kissing, lit. drinking the lower lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरमधु
अधर + -मधु, -अमृतम् the nectar of the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरामृतम्
अधर + -मधु, -अमृतम् the nectar of the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्वस्तिकम्
अधर + -स्वस्तिकम् the nadir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीकृ
अधरीकृ €8 U., अधरयति Den. P. To surpass, excel, beat down,<BR> worst; शोकं किञ्चिदधरीकृत्य Dk. 6 lessening, forgetting; to defeat,<BR> vanquish; भवता धीरतयाऽधरीकृतः Ki. 2. 40, 6. 21; चरितैर्मुनीनधरयञ्<BR> शुचिभिः Ki. 6. 24 exceling; अधरीकृतसर्वस्रेहेन अपत्यप्रेम्णा K. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीभू
अधरीभू €1 P. To be worsted (in a law suit); to be invalidated; साक्षिषूभयतः<BR> सत्सु साक्षिणः पूर्ववादिनः । पूर्वपक्षेऽधरीभूते भवन्त्युत्तरवादिनः ॥ Y. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीण|अधरीणः
अधरीण <i>a.</i> [अधरे भवः अधर-ख]<BR>—1 Lower.<BR>—2 Traduced, vilified, reproached; अधरीणः परिणंस्यते A R. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेद्युः|अधरेद्यु
अधरेद्युः <i>ind.</i> [अधरे दिने; अधर-एद्युस्]<BR>—1 On a previous day.<BR>—2 The day before yesterday; the other day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्मात्
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतः
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्तात्
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरात्
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतात्
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेण
अधरस्मात्, -रतः, -स्तात्, -रात्, -तात्, -रेण <i>ind.</i><BR> Below, beneath, in the lower regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराञ्च्|अधरांच्
अधराञ्च् <i>a.</i> [अधरां दक्षिणां दिशम् अञ्चति अञ्च् क्विन् P. III. 2. 59]<BR> Southward; tending downwards, to the nadir or lower region; tending to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराञ्ची
अधराञ्च् + .{@-ञ्ची@} the southern direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराक्
अधराञ्च् + .{@-क्@} <i>ind.</i> Beneath,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराचीन
अधराचीन, -च्य <i>a.</i><BR> [अधराचि भवः; अधराच् ख यत् वा] Tending downwards;<BR> situated in the region below; being downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराच्य
अधराचीन, -च्य <i>a.</i><BR> [अधराचि भवः; अधराच् ख यत् वा] Tending downwards;<BR> situated in the region below; being downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मः|अधर्म|अधर्म्म|अधर्म्मः
अधर्मः [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unrighteousness, irreligion, impiousness, wickedness, injustice; ˚दण्डनम्<BR> Ms. 8. 127 unjust punishment; अधर्मेण unjustly, in an improper way;<BR> यश्चाधर्मेण पृच्छति Ms. 2. 111; an unjust act; a guilty or wicked<BR> deed; sin; ˚चारिन् committing unjust or unrighteous deeds; so ˚आत्मन्<BR> of an irreligious spirit; तदा कथम्˚भीरुः Ś. 5; ˚मय full of<BR> wickedness or sin; for definitions &c. of धर्म and अधर्म See<BR> Tarka K. P. 19. (धर्म and अधर्म are two of the 24 qualities<BR> mentioned in Nyāya, and they pertain only to the soul. They are the peculiar<BR> causes of pleasure and pain respectively. They are imperceptible, but<BR> inferred from reasoning and from transmigration.)<BR>—2 N. of a Praiāpati or of an attendant of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मा
अधर्मः + .{@-र्मा@} Unrighteousness personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मम्
अधर्मः + .{@-र्मम्@} Devoid of attributes, an epithet of ब्रह्मन.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधर्मास्तिकायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मास्तिकायः|अधर्मास्तिकाय|अधर्म्मास्तिकाय
अधर्मः + -अस्तिकायः the category of अधर्म. See अस्तिकाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मिन्|अधर्म्मिन्
अधर्मिन् <i>a.</i> Impious, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्य
अधर्म्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wicked, impious.<BR>—2 Illegal, unlawful; पञ्चानां तु त्रयो धर्म्या द्वावधर्म्यौ स्मृताविह Ms. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधवा
अधवा [अविद्यमानो धवो भर्ता यस्याः] A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस्, अधः <i>ind.</i> [अधर-असि, अधरशब्दस्थाने अध् आदेशः P. V. 3. 39.]<BR>—1 Below, down; पतत्यधो धाम विसारि सर्वतः Śi. 1. 2; in lower<BR> region, to the infernal regions or hell; व्यसन्यधोऽधो व्रजति स्वर्यात्यव्यसनी<BR> मृतः Ms. 7. 53. (According to the context अधः may have the sense<BR> of the nominative, ˚अङ्कुशः &c.; ablative, अधो वृक्षात् पतति;<BR> or locative, अधो गृहे शेते).<BR>—2 Beneath, under, used like a preposition with gen.; तरूणाम्˚ Ś. 1. 14;<BR> rarely with abl. also; वाहित्थं तु ततोऽप्यधः Hem.;<BR> (when repeated) lower and lower, down and down; अधोधः पश्यतः कस्य<BR> महिमा नोपचीयते H. 2. 2; यात्यधोधोव्रजत्युच्चैर्नरः स्वैरेव कर्मभिः<BR> H. 2. 47; अधोधो गङ्गेयं पदमुपगता स्तोकं Bh. 2. 10; from under,<BR> just below (with acc.); नवानधोऽधो बृहतः पयोधरान् Śi. 1. 4. In<BR> comp. with nouns अधः has the sense of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) lower, under, as ˚भुवनं, ˚लोकः the lower world; ˚वासः<BR> or ˚अंशुकम् an under-garment; or<BR>——(<i>b</i>) the lower part; ˚कायः the lower part of the body; अधःकृ<BR> means to surpass, eclipse, overcome, vanquish, despise, scorn; तपः<BR> शरीरैः कठिनैरुपार्जितं तपस्विनां दरमधश्चकार सा Ku. 5. 29; अधःकृताशेषान्तःपुरेण<BR> K. 177; ˚कृतकुसुमायुधं 179; Śi. 1. 35; क्षितिप्रतिष्ठोऽपि मुखारविन्दैर्वधूजनश्चन्द्रमधश्चकार 3. 52;<BR> ˚कृतैनसः Śi. 16. 8 dispelled.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) अधस्, अधस्तात् -Pudendum muliebre.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधोक्ष, अधोक्षजः, अधोधस्, अधउपासनम्, अधोङ्गम्, अधोद्वारम्, अधोमर्म, अधःकरः, अधःकरणम्, अधःखननम्, अधोगतिः, अधोगन्तृ, अधोगण्टा, अधोघण्टा, अधश्चरः, अधोजानु, अधोजिह्विका, अधस्तलम्, अधोदिश्, अधोदृष्टि, अधःपदं, अधःपातः, अधःपुष्पी, अधःप्रस्तरः, अधोभक्तम्, अधोभागः, अधोभूः, अधोमुख, अधोवदन, अधोयन्त्रम्, अधोरक्तपित्तम्, अधोराम, अधोलम्बः, अधोवर्चस्, अधोवशः, अधोवायुः, अधोवेदः, अधःशय, अधःशय्य, अधःशिरस्, अधःस्थ, अधःस्थित, अधःस्वस्तिकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधः|अध
अधस्, अधः <i>ind.</i> [अधर-असि, अधरशब्दस्थाने अध् आदेशः P. V. 3. 39.]<BR>—1 Below, down; पतत्यधो धाम विसारि सर्वतः Śi. 1. 2; in lower<BR> region, to the infernal regions or hell; व्यसन्यधोऽधो व्रजति स्वर्यात्यव्यसनी<BR> मृतः Ms. 7. 53. (According to the context अधः may have the sense<BR> of the nominative, ˚अङ्कुशः &c.; ablative, अधो वृक्षात् पतति;<BR> or locative, अधो गृहे शेते).<BR>—2 Beneath, under, used like a preposition with gen.; तरूणाम्˚ Ś. 1. 14;<BR> rarely with abl. also; वाहित्थं तु ततोऽप्यधः Hem.;<BR> (when repeated) lower and lower, down and down; अधोधः पश्यतः कस्य<BR> महिमा नोपचीयते H. 2. 2; यात्यधोधोव्रजत्युच्चैर्नरः स्वैरेव कर्मभिः<BR> H. 2. 47; अधोधो गङ्गेयं पदमुपगता स्तोकं Bh. 2. 10; from under,<BR> just below (with acc.); नवानधोऽधो बृहतः पयोधरान् Śi. 1. 4. In<BR> comp. with nouns अधः has the sense of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) lower, under, as ˚भुवनं, ˚लोकः the lower world; ˚वासः<BR> or ˚अंशुकम् an under-garment; or<BR>——(<i>b</i>) the lower part; ˚कायः the lower part of the body; अधःकृ<BR> means to surpass, eclipse, overcome, vanquish, despise, scorn; तपः<BR> शरीरैः कठिनैरुपार्जितं तपस्विनां दरमधश्चकार सा Ku. 5. 29; अधःकृताशेषान्तःपुरेण<BR> K. 177; ˚कृतकुसुमायुधं 179; Śi. 1. 35; क्षितिप्रतिष्ठोऽपि मुखारविन्दैर्वधूजनश्चन्द्रमधश्चकार 3. 52;<BR> ˚कृतैनसः Śi. 16. 8 dispelled.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) अधस्, अधस्तात् -Pudendum muliebre.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधोक्ष, अधोक्षजः, अधोधस्, अधउपासनम्, अधोङ्गम्, अधोद्वारम्, अधोमर्म, अधःकरः, अधःकरणम्, अधःखननम्, अधोगतिः, अधोगन्तृ, अधोगण्टा, अधोघण्टा, अधश्चरः, अधोजानु, अधोजिह्विका, अधस्तलम्, अधोदिश्, अधोदृष्टि, अधःपदं, अधःपातः, अधःपुष्पी, अधःप्रस्तरः, अधोभक्तम्, अधोभागः, अधोभूः, अधोमुख, अधोवदन, अधोयन्त्रम्, अधोरक्तपित्तम्, अधोराम, अधोलम्बः, अधोवर्चस्, अधोवशः, अधोवायुः, अधोवेदः, अधःशय, अधःशय्य, अधःशिरस्, अधःस्थ, अधःस्थित, अधःस्वस्तिकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्ष
अधस् + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> situated below the axle or car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षम्
अधस् + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षम्@}) <i>adv.</i> below the car, under the axle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षजः|अधोक्षज
अधस् + -अक्षजः [अक्षात् इन्द्रियाज्जायते इति अक्षजं प्रत्यक्षज्ञानम्,<BR> तदधरं ग्राहकत्वाभावात् हीनं यस्य सः Tv.; अधःकृतम् अक्षजम् इन्द्रियज्ञानं<BR> येन Malli.] N. of Viṣṇu; other etymologies of the name are also found:−<BR> (1) अधो न क्षीयते जातु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">Page0060-1</a>]<BR> यस्मात्तस्मादधोक्षजः; (2) द्यौरक्षं पृथिवी चाधस्तयोर्यस्मादजायत ।<BR> मध्ये वैराजरूपेण ततोऽधोक्षज इष्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0059-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोधस्
अधस् + -अधस् See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधउपासनम्
अधस् + -उपासनम् sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोङ्गम्
अधस् + -अङ्गम्, -द्वारम्, -मर्म the anus; Pudendum Muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोद्वारम्
अधस् + -अङ्गम्, -द्वारम्, -मर्म the anus; Pudendum Muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमर्म|अधोमर्म्म
अधस् + -अङ्गम्, -द्वारम्, -मर्म the anus; Pudendum Muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकरः|अधःकर
अधस् + -करः the lower part of the hand (करभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकरणम्
अधस् + -करणम् excelling, defeating, degradation; K. 202; so ˚क्रिया;<BR> सहते न जनोप्यधःक्रियाम् Ki. 2. 47 degradation, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःक्रिया
अधस् + -करणम् excelling, defeating, degradation; K. 202; so ˚क्रिया;<BR> सहते न जनोप्यधःक्रियाम् Ki. 2. 47 degradation, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःखननम्
अधस् + -खननम् undermining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगतिः|अधोगति
अधस् + -गतिः <i>f.</i>, {@गमनम्, -पातः@}<BR>—1 a downward fall or motion, descent; going downwards.<BR>—2 degradation, downfall, going to perdition or hell; मूलानामधोगतिः<BR> K. 41 (where ˚ति has both senses); ˚तिम् आयाति Pt. 1. 150 sinks,<BR> comes down (feels dishonoured); Ms. 3. 17; अरक्षितारमत्तारं नृपं<BR> विद्यादधोगतिम् 8. 309 destined to go to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगन्तृ|अधोगंतृ
अधस् + -गन्तृ <i>m.</i> one who digs downwards, a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगण्टा
अधस् + -गण्टा, -घण्टा [अधरात् अधस्तादारभ्य घण्टेव तदाकारफलत्वात्]<BR> a plant Achyranthes Aspera (अपामार्ग. Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोघण्टा
अधस् + -गण्टा, -घण्टा [अधरात् अधस्तादारभ्य घण्टेव तदाकारफलत्वात्]<BR> a plant Achyranthes Aspera (अपामार्ग. Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधश्चरः|अधश्चर
अधस् + -चरः [अधः खनित्वा चरति-अच्]<BR>—1 thief.<BR>—2 one who goes downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोजानु
अधस् + -जानु <i>n.</i> the lower part of the knee. ━<i>ind.</i> below the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोजिह्विका
अधस् + -जिह्विका [अल्पा जिह्वा जिह्विका, अधरा जिह्विका] the uvula (Mar. पडजीभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तलम्
अधस् + -तलम् the lower part or surface; शय्या˚, खट्वा˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोदिश्
अधस् + -दिश् <i>f.</i> the lower region, the nadir; the southern direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोदृष्टि|अधोदृष्टिः
अधस् + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> casting a downward look; a posture in Yoga; करणान्यबहिष्कृत्य<BR> स्थाणुवन्निश्चलात्मकः । आत्मानं हृदये ध्यायेत् नासाग्रन्यस्तलोचनः ॥<BR> इति योगसारे. cf. also Ku. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोदृष्टिः|अधोदृष्टि
अधस् + -दृष्टि + .({@-ष्टिः@}) a downward look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपदं|अधःपद
अधस् + -पदं [अधोवृत्ति पदं, पादस्याधःस्थानं वा] the place under<BR> the foot, a lower place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपातः|अधःपात
अधस् + -पातः = ˚गति q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपुष्पी
अधस् + -पुष्पी [अधोमुखानि पुष्पाणि यस्याः] Names of two plants अवाक्पुष्पी<BR> (Pimpinella Anisum) and गोजिह्वा (Elephantopus Scaber).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःप्रस्तरः|अधःप्रस्तर
अधस् + -प्रस्तरः a seat of grass for persons in mourning to sit upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभक्तम्
अधस् + -भक्तम् [अधरं भक्तं यस्मात्] a dose of water, medicine &c.<BR> to be taken after meals &c. (भोजनान्ते पीयमानं जलादिकम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभागः|अधोभाग
अधस् + -भागः<BR>—1 the lower part (of the body); पूर्वभागो गुरुः पुंसामधोभागस्तु योषितां<BR> Suśr. 2 the lower part of any thing, the region below, down below; ˚व्यवस्थितं<BR> किंचित्पुरमालोकितं Pt. 1 situated down below. See पाताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभूः
अधस् + -भूः <i>f.</i> lower ground, land at the foot of a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुख|अधोमुखः
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> having the face downwards; ˚खी तिष्ठति;<BR> ˚खैः पत्रिभिः R. 3. 57.<BR>—2 head-long, precipitate, flying downwards.<BR>—3 upside down, topsy-turvy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवदन
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> having the face downwards; ˚खी तिष्ठति;<BR> ˚खैः पत्रिभिः R. 3. 57.<BR>—2 head-long, precipitate, flying downwards.<BR>—3 upside down, topsy-turvy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुखः|अधोमुख
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन + .({@-खः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुखा
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन + .({@-खा, -खी@}) N. of a plant गोजिह्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुखी
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन + .({@-खा, -खी@}) N. of a plant गोजिह्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुखम्
अधस् + -मुख, -वदन + .({@-खम्@}) (नक्षत्रम्)<BR>—1 flying downwards, having a downward motion; these <i>nakṣatras</i> are:−<BR> मूलाश्लेषा कृत्तिका च विशाखा भरणी तथा । मघा पूर्वात्रयं चैव अधोमुखगणः<BR> स्मृतः ॥ Jyotiṣa.<BR>—2 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोयन्त्रम्
अधस् + -यन्त्रम् a still.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोरक्तपित्तम्
अधस् + -रक्तपित्तम् discharge of blood from the anus and urethra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोराम
अधस् + -राम <i>a.</i> [अधोभागे रामः शुक्लः, दृष्टितर्पकत्वात् तस्य रामत्वम्]<BR> having a white colour or white marks on the lower part of the body (said of a goat);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोलम्बः|अधोलम्ब
अधस् + -लम्बः<BR>—1 a plummet.<BR>—2 a perpendicular.<BR>—3 the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवर्चस्
अधस् + -वर्चस् <i>a.</i> strong in the lower regions; whose lustre penetrates downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवशः|अधोवश
अधस् + -वशः Pudendum Muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवायुः|अधोवायु
अधस् + -वायुः [अधोगामी वायुः शाक˚ त˚] breaking wind, flatulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवेदः
अधस् + -वेदः to marry a second wife when the first is alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःशय
अधस् + -शय, -शय्य <i>a.</i> sleeping<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">Page0060-2</a>]<BR> on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःशय्या
अधस् + -शय, -शय्य + .({@-य्या@}) sleeping on the ground; अग्नीन्धनं भैक्षचर्यामधःशय्यां<BR> गुरोर्हितम । आसमावर्तनात् कुर्यात्कृतोपनयनो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःशय्य
अधस् + -शय, -शय्य <i>a.</i> sleeping<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">Page0060-2</a>]<BR> on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःशिरस्
अधस् + -शिरस् <i>a.</i>, {@-मुख@} (<i>n.</i>)<BR> N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःस्थ
अधस् + -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> situated below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःस्थित
अधस् + -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> situated below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःस्वस्तिकम्
अधस् + -स्वस्तिकम् the nadir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोपः|अधिरोप
अधिरोपः Accusation; पक्षपाताधिरोपस्य कारणानि च पञ्च वै Śukra. 4. 528.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेत्तव्या
अधिवेत्तव्या (-वेद्या)<BR> A woman fit to be married as a second wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेद्या
अधिवेत्तव्या (-वेद्या)<BR> A woman fit to be married as a second wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रित
अधिश्रित <i>a.</i> Heated; Bhāg. 10. 9. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोपहासः|अधोपहास
अधोपहासः [अधः अधोभागस्य योन्याः उपहासः छान्दसः सन्धिः, स्त्रीणामधोभागस्य<BR> उपहसनम् Tv.] Ved. Sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तन
अधस्तन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अधोभवः अधस्-टपु तुट् च]<BR>—1 Lower, situated beneath.<BR>—2 Prior, previous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तराम्
अधस्तरा(मा)म् <i>ind.</i> [अतिशयेनाधः] Very low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तमाम्
अधस्तरा(मा)म् <i>ind.</i> [अतिशयेनाधः] Very low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तात्
अधस्तात् <i>adv.</i> or <i>prep.</i> [अधर-अस्ताति, अध् आदेशः P. V. 3. 39-40.]<BR> Down, below, under, beneath, underneath &c. (with gen.). See<BR> अधः, अधस्तान्नोपदध्याच्च Ms. 4. 54; धर्मेण गमनमूर्ध्वं गमनमधस्ताद्भवत्यधर्मेण<BR> Sāṅ. K.; ˚तादागतः Pt. 3; तस्याधस्ताद्वयमपि रतास्तेषु पर्णोटजेषु<BR> U. 2. 25; यस्य सर्वमेवाधस्ताद् गतं K. 289; gone to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधामार्गवः|अधामार्गव
अधामार्गवः [न धीयते अधाः, तादृशं मार्गम्; वाति वा-क Tv.]<BR> = अपामार्ग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधारणक
अधारणक <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not profitable; ˚कं ममैतत्स्थानं Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिः|अधि
अधिः [आधीयते दुःखमनेन आधा कि वा. पृ˚ ह्रस्वः]<BR>—1 Mental pain or agony. See आधिः<BR>—2 A woman in her courses. (= अवि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 (As a prefix to verbs) over, above; (अधिकार); ˚स्था to stand<BR> over; ˚कृ to place over or at the head of; ˚रुह् to grow over or<BR> above; over and above, besides, in addition to (आधिक्य); fully, completely<BR> (अतिशय, विशेष), to get something in addition to another; अधिगत्य<BR> जगत्यधीश्वरात् having obtained fully, अधि intensifying the meaning<BR> of the root; इतो वा सातिमीमहे दिवो वा पार्थिवादधि Rv. 1. 6. 10; (अधीमहे<BR> आधिक्येन याचामहे).<BR>—2 (As a separable adverb) Over, above, from above (mostly Vedic); षष्टिर्वीरासो<BR> अधि षट् Rv. 7. 18. 14.<BR>—3 (As a preposition) with acc.<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Above, over, upon, in (उपरि); यं दन्तमधिजायते नाडी<BR> तं दन्तमुद्धरेत् Suśr. अध्यधि Just above; लोकानुपर्युपर्यास्तेऽधोऽधोऽध्यधि<BR> च माधवः Bopadeva; with gen. also; ये नाकस्याधि रोचने दिवि Rv. 1. 19. 6<BR> above the sun; ˚विटपि Śi. 7. 35; ˚त्वत् 7. 41; ˚रजनि<BR> at night. अधिरजनि जगाम धाम तस्याः 52.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) with reference to, concerning, in the case of, on the subject<BR> of (अधिकृत्य) (mostly in adverbial compounds in this sense); हरौ<BR> इति अधिहरि; so अधिस्त्रि; कृष्णमधिकृत्य प्रवृत्ता कथा अधिकृष्णम्;<BR> so ˚ज्योतिषम्, ˚लोकम्, ˚दैवम्, ˚दैवतम् treating of stars &c.; ˚पुरन्ध्रि<BR> Śi. 6. 32 in the case of women.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) (With abl.) Just over, more than (अधिक); सत्त्वादधि महानात्मा<BR> Kaṭh.; अविदितादधि<BR>——(<i>d</i>) (With loc.) Over, on or upon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-1" target="_blank">Page0061-1</a>]<BR> above (showing lordship or sovereignty over something) (ऐश्वर्य);<BR> अधिरीश्वरे P. I. 4. 97; अधि भुवि रामः P. II. 3. 9. Sk. Rāma rules<BR> over the earth; the country ruled over may be used with loc. of ‘ruler’;<BR> अधि रामे भूः <i>ibid.</i>; प्रहारवर्मण्यधि विदेहा जाताः Dk. 77<BR> subject to, under the government of, become the property or possession<BR> of (अधि denoting स्वत्वं in this case); under, inferior to (हीन);<BR> अधि हरौ सुराः (Bopadeva) the gods are under Hari.<BR>—4 (As first member of Tatpuruṣa compounds)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Chief, supreme, principal, presiding; ˚देवता presiding deity;<BR> ˚राजः supreme or sovereign ruler; ˚पतिः supreme lord &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Redundant, superfluous (growing over another); ˚दन्तः = अध्यारूढः<BR> (दन्तस्योपरि जातः) दन्तः P. VI. 2. 188.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Over, excessive; ˚अधिक्षेपः high censure. According to G. M.<BR> अधि has these senses. अधिरध्ययनैश्वर्यवशित्वस्मरणाधिके ।<BR> <i>e. g.</i>; उपाध्यायादधीते; इङोऽध्ययनार्थकत्वस्य अधिद्योतकः; अधिपतिः<BR> (ऐश्वर्ये); अधीनः (वशित्वे) अधिगतः इनं; मातुरध्येति<BR> (स्मरणे); अधिकम् (अधिके).<BR>—5 Instead of; इदमग्ने सुधितं दुर्धितादधि प्रियादु चिन्मन्मनः प्रेय<BR> अस्तु ते Rv. 1. 140. 11. In the Veda अधि is supposed by B. and R.<BR> to have the senses of ‘out of’, ‘from’, ‘of’, ‘among’, ‘before’, ‘beforehand’,<BR> ‘for’, ‘in favour of’, ‘in’, ‘at’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0060-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक|अधिकं|अधिकः
अधिक <i>a.</i> [abbreviation of अध्यारूढ; अध्यारूढशब्दात् कन् उत्तरपदलोपश्च P. V. 2. 73].<BR>—1 More, additional, greater (opp. ऊन or सम); तदस्मिन्नधिकम्<BR> P. V. 2. 45. (In comp. with numerals) plus, greater by; अष्टाधिकं शतम् 100<BR> plus 8 = 108; चत्वारिंशतोऽधिकाः = ˚चत्वारिंशाः more than 40;<BR> नवाधिकां नवतिम् R. 3. 69; एकाधिकं हरेज्ज्येष्ठः Ms. 9. 117.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Surpassing in quantity, more numerous, copious, excessive, abundant;<BR> in comp. or with instr.; श्वासः प्रमाणाधिकः Ś. 1. 29 more than<BR> the usual measure.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Inordinate, grown, increased, become greater; abounding in, full<BR> of; strong in; ˚क्रोध R. 12. 90; वयोऽधिकः Ms. 4. 141 senior in<BR> years; शिशुरधिकवयाः Ve. 3. 32 old, advanced in years; भवनेषु<BR> रसाधिकेषु v. l. (सुधासितेषु) पूर्वं Ś. 7. 20; करोति रागं<BR> हृदि कौतुकाधिकं K. 2; रसाधिके मनसि Śi. 17. 48 abounding in.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) More, greater, stronger, mightier, more violent or intense; अधिकां<BR> कुरु देवि गुरुभक्तिम् K. 62; ऊनं न सत्त्वेष्वधिको बबाधे R. 2. 14<BR> the stronger animal did not prey on the weaker; पुमान्पुंसोऽधिके शुके<BR> स्त्री भवत्यधिके स्त्रियाः Ms. 3. 49; अधिकं मेनिरे विष्णुम् Rām.;<BR> अधिकं मित्रम् Pt. 2; यवीयान्गुणतोऽधिकः Ms. 11. 185, 9. 154.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Superior to, better than; higher than (with abl. or in comp.);<BR> प्रमाणादधिकस्यापि मत्तदन्तिनः Pt. 1. 327; सेनाशतेभ्योऽधिका बुद्धिः<BR> Mu. 1. 27 surpassing, more than a match for &c.; विधेरधिकसंभारः<BR> R. 15. 62 more than what was sanctioned by rules; तपस्विभ्योऽधिको योगी<BR> Bg. 6. 46; ब्रह्म प्रदानेभ्योऽधिकम् Y. 1. 212; अश्वाधिको राजा H. 3. 77<BR> strong in cavalry; धनधान्याधिको वैश्यः H. 4. 21 excels in,<BR> is superior by reason of; लोकाधिकं तेजः Mu. 4. 10 superior to; sometimes<BR> with gen.; पञ्चदशानां भ्रातणामधिको गुणैः K. 136.<BR>—4 Later, subsequent, further than (of time); राजन्यबन्धोर्द्वाविंशे<BR> (केशान्तो विधीयते) वैश्यस्य द्वपधिके ततः Ms. 2. 65.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">Page0061-2</a>]<BR> 2 years later i. e. in the 24th year; sometimes with gen.; ममाधिका वा<BR> तुल्या वा Rām.<BR>—5 Eminent, uncommon, special, peculiar (असाधारण); विद्या नाम<BR> नरस्य रूपमधिकम् Bh. 2. 20 superior or uncommon form or beauty; धर्मो<BR> हि तेषामधिको विशेषः H. Pr. 25; इज्याध्ययनदानानि वैश्यस्य क्षत्रियस्य<BR> च । प्रतिग्रहोऽधिको विप्रे याजनाध्यापने तथा ॥ Y. 1. 118; sometimes<BR> used in the comparative in the above senses; क्लेशोऽधिकतरस्तेषाम्<BR> Bg. 12. 5; ˚तरमिदानीं राजते राजलक्ष्मीः V. 5. 22; स्वर्गादधिकतरं<BR> निर्वृत्तिस्थानम् Ś. 7.<BR>—6 Redundant, superfluous; ˚अङ्ग having a redundant limb; नोद्वहेत्कपिलां<BR> कन्यां नाधिकाङ्गीं न रोगिणीम् Ms. 3. 8.<BR>—7 Intercalated, intercalary (as a month &c.)<BR>—8 Inferior, secondary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकम्
अधिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Surplus, excess, more; लाभोऽधिकं फलम् Ak.<BR>—2 Abundance, redundancy, superfluity. —3 A figure of speech equivalent<BR> to hyperbole; आश्रयाश्रयिणोरेकस्याधिक्येऽधिकमुच्यते । किमधिकमस्य<BR> ब्रूमो महिमानं वारिधेर्हरिर्यत्र । अज्ञात एव शेते कुक्षौ निक्षिप्य भुवनानि<BR> ॥ अत्र आश्रयस्याधिक्यम् । युगान्तकालप्रतिसंहृतात्मनो जगन्ति यस्यां<BR> सविकाशमासत । तनौ ममुस्तत्र न कैटभद्विषस्तपोधनाभ्यागमसंभृता<BR> मुदः ॥ S. D.; महतोर्यन्महीयांसावाश्रिताश्रययोः क्रमात् । आश्रयाश्रयिणौ<BR> स्यातां तनुत्वेऽप्यधिकं तु तत् ॥ K. P. 10. ━<i>adv.</i><BR>—1 More, in a greater degree; स राज्यं गुरुणा दत्तं प्रतिपद्याधिकं<BR> बभौ R. 4. 1; shone the more; 3. 18; यस्मिन्नैवाधिकं चक्षुरारोपयति<BR> पार्थिवः Pt. 1. 243; oft. in comp.; इयमधिकमनोज्ञा Ś. 1. 20;<BR> ˚सुरभि Me. 21.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, too much.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिकाङ्ग, अधिकाधिक, अधिकार्थ, अधिकर्द्धि, अधिकतिथिः, अधिकदन्तः, अधिकमांसार्मन्, अधिकवाक्योक्तिः, अधिकषाष्टिकसाप्ततिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाङ्ग|अधिकाङ्गं
अधिक + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> (-ङ्गी <i>f.</i>) having a redundant limb. Ms. 3. 8.<BR> (see above 6)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाङ्गम्
अधिक + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गम्@}) [अधिकोऽङ्गात्] a sash, girdle or belt worn over the mail coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाधिक
अधिक + -अधिक <i>a.</i> more and more, out-doing one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार्थ
अधिक + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> exaggerated;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार्थवचनम्
अधिक + -अर्थ + ˚वचनम् exaggeration, an exaggerated<BR> statement or assertion (whether of praise or of censure); कृत्यैरधिकार्थवचने<BR> P. II. 1. 33; (˚नम् = स्तुतिनिन्दा फलकमर्थवादवचनम्; e. g. वातच्छेद्यं<BR> तृणम् i. e. so light and weak; काकपेया नदी so deep and full).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्द्धि
अधिक + -ऋद्धि <i>a.</i> abundant, prosperous; ऋद्धिमन्तमधिकर्द्धिरुत्तरः<BR> पूर्वमुत्सवमपोहदुत्सवः R. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकतिथिः|अधिकतिथि
अधिक + -तिथिः, <i>f.</i>, {@-दिनं, -दिवसः@}<BR> an intercalated day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकदन्तः|अधिकदन्त
अधिक + -दन्तः = अधिदन्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकमांसार्मन्
अधिक + -मांसार्मन् = अधिमांस q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकवाक्योक्तिः|अधिकवाक्योक्ति
अधिक + -वाक्योक्तिः <i>f.</i> exaggeration, hyperbole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकषाष्टिकसाप्ततिक
अधिक + -षाष्टिकसाप्ततिक <i>a.</i> containing or costing more than 60 or 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाम|अधिकामः
अधिकाम <i>a.</i> [अधिकः कामो यस्य] Of vehement desires, impassioned, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकामः|अधिकाम
अधिकाम + .{@-मः@} [कर्म˚] Strong desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृ
अधिकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To authorize, qualify for the discharge of some duty; be entitled to,<BR> have a right to; नैवाध्यकारिष्महि वेदवृत्ते Bk. 2. 34; गुणाः प्रियत्वेधिकृता<BR> न संस्तवः Ki. 4. 25 merits are calculated to produce liking, not mere intimacy.<BR>—2 To place at the head of, appoint, set; पाण्डवेन ह्यहं तात अश्वेष्वधिकृतः<BR> पुरा Mb.; दृप्तविनयाधिकृतः R. 9. 62 appointed to humble the proud;<BR> शिथिलीकृतेऽधिकृतकृत्यविधौ Ki. 6. 30 set or appointed to duty; देवाः<BR> प्रसह्य तमधिकुर्युः Mv. 2 set on, incite or appoint as their chief.<BR>—3 To aim at, allude or refer to, make the subject of; अधिकृत्य कृते<BR> ग्रन्थे P. IV. 3. 87; किरातार्जुनौ अधिकृत्य कृतं काव्यं किरातार्जुनीयम्<BR> Sk.; नाटकं प्रयोगेण अधिक्रियताम् Ś. 1 should be made the subject<BR> of representation, should be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">Page0062-1</a>]<BR> represented on the stage.<BR>—4 To be used as the head or governing rule; समर्थानां प्रथमाद्वा<BR> P. IV. 1. 82; इदं पदत्रयमधिक्रियते Sk.<BR>—5 To superintend, be at the head.<BR>—6 (Ā.) To bear, endure or overpower, be superior to; शत्रुमधिकुरुते<BR> Sk.; अधिचक्रे न यं हरिः Bk. 8. 20.<BR>—7 To feel, enjoy; भवादृशाश्चेदधिकुर्वते रतिं निराश्रया हन्त हता<BR> मनस्विता Ki. 1. 43.<BR>—8 To refrain or desist from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणम्
अधिकरणम् [कृ ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Placing at the head of, appointing &c.<BR>—2 Relation, reference, connection; रामाधिकरणाः कथाः Rām. referring to.<BR>—3 (In gram.) Agreement, concord, government or grammatical relation (as<BR> of subject and predicate &c.); तत्पुरुषः समानाधिकरणः कर्मधारयः<BR> P. I. 2. 42 having the members (of the compound) in the same relation<BR> or apposition; समानाधिकरणो or व्यधिकरणो बहुव्रीहिः; पीताम्बरः,<BR> चकपाणिः &c.<BR>—4 A receptacle or subject, technically substratum; ज्ञानाधिकरणम् आत्मा<BR> T. S. the soul is the substratum of knowledge.<BR>—5 Location, place, the sense of the locative case; आधारोधिकरणम्<BR> P. I. 4. 45; कर्तृकर्मव्यवहितामसाक्षाद्धारयत् क्रियाम् । उपकुर्वत् क्रियासिद्धौ<BR> शास्त्रेधिकरणं स्मृतम् ॥ Hariv.; as गेहे स्थाल्यामन्नं पचति.<BR>—6 A topic, subject; section, article or paragraph; a complete argument<BR> treating of one subject; A chapter in Kauṭilīya Arthaśāstra.<BR> <i>e. g.</i> प्रथमाधिकरणम्. the Sūtras of Vyāsa and Jaimini are divided<BR> into Adhyāyas, the Adhyāyas into Pādas and the Pādas into Adhikaraṇas<BR> or sections. (According to the Mīmāṃsakas a complete Adhikaraṇa consists<BR> of five members:− विषय the subject or matter to be explained, विशय<BR> or संशय the doubt or question arising upon that matter, पूर्वपक्ष<BR> the first side or <i>prima facie</i> argument concerning it, उत्तर<BR> or उत्तरपक्ष or सिद्धान्त the answer or demonstrated conclusion,<BR> and संगति pertinency or relevancy, or according to others निर्णय<BR> the final conclusion; विषयो विशयश्चैव पूर्वपक्षस्तथोत्तरम् । निर्णयश्चेति<BR> सिद्धान्तः शास्त्रेऽधिकरणं स्मृतम् ॥ The Vedāntins put संगति<BR> in the 3rd place, and सिद्धान्त last; तत्र एकैकमधिकरणं पञ्चावयवम्,<BR> विषयः संदेहः संगतिः पूर्वपक्षः सिद्धान्तश्च. Generally speaking,<BR> the five members may be विषय, संशय, पूर्वपक्ष, उत्तरपक्ष and<BR> सिद्धान्त or राद्धान्त).<BR>—7 Court of justice, court, tribunal; स्वान्दोषान् कथयन्ति नाधिकरणे<BR> Mk. 9. 3; ˚रणे च साधनम् Dk. 40.<BR>—8 Stuff, material; विप्रतिषिद्धं चानधिकरणवाचि P. II. 4. 13 (अद्रव्यवाचि);<BR> अधिकरणै ˚एतावत्त्वे च P. II. 4. 15 fixed number of things, as दश<BR> दन्तोष्टाः Sk.<BR>—9 A claim. Bhāg. 5. 1. 16.<BR>—10 Supremacy.<BR>—11 A government department; सर्वाधिकरणरक्षणम् Kau. A. 4.<BR>—12 A gathering place प्रत्यक्षाश्च परोक्षाश्च सर्वाधिकरणेष्वथ । वृत्तेर्भरतशार्दूल<BR> नित्यं चैवान्ववेक्षणम् ॥ Mb. 12. 59. 68.<BR>—13 A department; अश्वागारान् गजागारान् बलाधिकरणानि च Mb. 12. 69. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणी
अधिकरणम् + .{@-णी@} One who superintends.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिकरणभोजकः, अधिकरणमण्डपः, अधिकरणलेखकः, अधिकरणविचालः, अधिकरणसिद्धान्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणभोजकः|अधिकरणभोजक
अधिकरणम् + -भोजकः a court-dignitary, a judge, भीतभीता अधिकरणभोजकाः Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणमण्डपः|अधिकरणमण्डप
अधिकरणम् + -मण्डपः court or hall of justice. अधिकरणमण्डपस्य मार्गमादेशय Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणलेखकः|अधिकरणलेखक
अधिकरणम् + -लेखकः <i>m.^1</i> official recorder or scribe, who drew up sale-deeds<BR> and other documents after getting the land measured in his presence; RT. VI. 38.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणविचालः|अधिकरणविचाल
अधिकरणम् + -विचालः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">Page0062-2</a>]<BR> [अधिकरणस्य विचालः अन्यथाकरणम्] changing the quantity of any<BR> thing, increasing or decreasing it so many times; ˚विचाले च P. V. 3. 43;<BR> द्रव्यस्य संख्यान्तरापादने संख्याया धा स्यात्; एकं राशिं पञ्चधा कुरु Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणसिद्धान्तः|अधिकरणसिद्धान्त
अधिकरणम् + -सिद्धान्तः a conclusion which involves others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणिकः|अधिकरणिक
अधिकरणिकः [अधिकरणम् आश्रयतया अस्त्यस्य ठन्]<BR>—1 A judge, magistrate. अहो व्यवहारपराधीनतया दुष्करं खलु परचित्तग्रहणमधिकरणिकैः Mk. 9.<BR>—2 A government official.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण्यम्
अधिकरण्यम् Authority, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मन्|अधिकर्म्मन्
अधिकर्मन् <i>n.</i> [अधिकं कर्मं]<BR>—1 A higher or superior act.<BR>—2 Superintendence. ━<i>m.</i> One who is charged with superintendence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिकर्मकरः, अधिकर्मकृत्, अधिकर्मकृतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मकरः|अधिकर्मकर|अधिकर्म्मकर
अधिकर्मन् + -करः, -कृत् a sort of servant, overseer of workmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मकृत्
अधिकर्मन् + -करः, -कृत् a sort of servant, overseer of workmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मकृतः|अधिकर्मकृत|अधिकर्म्मकृत
अधिकर्मन् + -कृतः [अधिकर्म कृतं येन निष्ठान्तस्य परनिपातः] one appointed<BR> to superintend an institution or establishment; सर्वेष्वधिकृतो यः स्यात्<BR> कुटुम्बस्य तथोपरि । सोऽधिकर्मकृतो ज्ञेयः स च कौटुम्बिकः स्मृतः ॥<BR> In families he is the head or <i>pater familias</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मिकः|अधिकर्मिक|अधिकर्म्मिक|अधिकर्म्मिकः
अधिकर्मिकः [अधिकृत्य कर्मणे अलम्, अधिकर्म ठन्] The overseer<BR> of a market whose duty is to recover toll or duties from the traders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारः|अधिकार
अधिकारः —1 Superintendence, watching over; स्त्रीषु कष्टोऽधिकारः<BR> V. 3. 1; यः पौरवेण राज्ञा धर्माधिकारे नियुक्तः Ś. 1<BR> superintendence of religious matters;<BR>—2 Duty, office, charge; power, post of authority; authority; मन्त्राधिकारः<BR> Kau. A. 1 निर्णयाधिकारे ब्रवीमि M. 1. I say this in the capacity of<BR> a judge; अविश्रमोऽयं लोकतन्त्राधिकारः Ś. 5; द्वीपिनस्ताम्बूलाधिकारो<BR> दत्तः Pt. 1, तुल्योद्योगस्तव दिनकृतश्चाधिकारो मतो नः V. 2. 1;<BR> अर्थ˚ administration of pecuniary matters स्वाधिकारात् प्रमत्तः<BR> Me. 1; अधिकारे मम पुत्रको नियुक्तः M. 5; यः सर्वाधिकारे नियुक्तः<BR> प्रधानमन्त्री स करोतु, अनुजीविना पर˚ चर्चा न कर्तव्या H. 2; शिल्पाधिकारे<BR> योग्येयं दारिका M. 1 fit to be initiated in to the fine arts.<BR>—3 Sovereignty, government or administration, jurisdiction, rule; स्वाधिकारभूमौ<BR> वर्तिष्यते Ś. 7 seat of government or jurisdiction, ˚खेदं निरूप्य Ś. 5.<BR>—4 Position, dignity, rank; हृताधिकारां मलिनाम् Y. 1. 70 deprived<BR> of the position or rights or privileges of a wife.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Right, authority, privilege, claim, title (as to wealth, property<BR> &c.); right of ownership or possession; अधिकारः फले स्वाम्यमधिकारी<BR> च तत्प्रभुः S. D. 296; वत्सेऽधिकारः स्थितः Mv. 4. 38 it now belongs to the child.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Qualification or authority to perform certain specified duties,<BR> civil, sacrificial, religious &c.; as the अधिकार of a king to rule<BR> and protect, of a Brāhmaṇa to sacrifice, of a Vaiśya to till or trade<BR> &c.; शूद्रोऽधिकारहीनोऽपि Y. 3. 262; with loc.; निषेकाद्रिस्मशानान्तो<BR> मन्त्रैर्यस्योदितो विधिः । तस्य शास्त्रेऽधिकारोऽस्मिन् ज्ञेयो नान्यस्य कस्यचित्<BR> Ms. 2. 16; श्राद्धाधिकारसम्पदस्तु इति भवन्तो ब्रुवन्तु (repeated in<BR> Śrāddha ceremonies).<BR>—6 Prerogative of a king.<BR>—7 Effort, exertion; कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन Bg. 2. 47<BR> your business is with action alone &c.<BR>—8 Relation, reference; स राघवस्तत्र तदा प्रलापाञ् शुश्राव लोकस्य<BR> समागतस्य । आत्माधिकारा विविधाश्च वाचः Rām. 2. 17. 43.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">Page0063-1</a>]<BR> कथा विचित्राः पृतनाधिकाराः Mb.<BR>—9 Place = अधिकरण; महत्खलु पुरुषाधिकारं ज्योतिः M. 1.<BR>—10 A topic, paragraph or section; प्रायश्चित्त˚ Mit.; see अधिकरण.<BR>—11 Counting, enumeration, occasion for counting; संसत्सु जाते पुरुषाधिकारे<BR> Ki. 3. 51 (गणनाप्रस्तावे).<BR>—12 (In gram.) A head or governing rule, which exerts a directing or governing<BR> influence over other rules; <i>e. g.</i> सर्वस्य द्वे P. VIII. 1. 1;<BR> समर्थानां प्रथमाद्वा; प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् IV. 1. 82-3; तत्पुरुषः II. 1. 22;<BR> अधिकारोऽयं Sk. (This अधिकार is of three kinds; सिंहावलोकितं<BR> चैव मण्डूकप्लुतमेव च । गङ्गाप्रवाहवच्चापि अधिकारस्त्रिधा मतः ॥.)<BR> अधिकार also means a word or sūtra extending over in the following<BR> सूत्रs up to a particular limit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिकारविधिः, अधिकारस्थ, अधिकाराढ्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारविधिः|अधिकारविधि
अधिकारः + -विधिः determination or statement of qualifications to do particular<BR> acts; as राजा राजसूयेन यजेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारस्थ
अधिकारः + -स्थ, -आढ्य <i>a.</i> possessed of authority, invested with office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाराढ्य
अधिकारः + -स्थ, -आढ्य <i>a.</i> possessed of authority, invested with office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिन्
अधिकारिन्, अधिकारवत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे इनि मतुप् वा]<BR>—1 Possessed of authority, having power; निःस्पृहो नाधिकारी स्यात् Pt. 1. 164;<BR> सन्धिविग्रहकार्य˚, कार्य˚ H. 3.<BR>—2 Entitled to, having a right to; सर्वे स्युरधिकारिणः; so उत्तराधिकारिन्<BR> heir; धनग्रहण˚ &c.; तपस्यनधिकारित्वात् R. 15. 51 not qualified or authorised.<BR>—3 Belonging to, owned by.<BR>—4 Fit for. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारवत्|अधिकारवन्त्
अधिकारिन्, अधिकारवत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे इनि मतुप् वा]<BR>—1 Possessed of authority, having power; निःस्पृहो नाधिकारी स्यात् Pt. 1. 164;<BR> सन्धिविग्रहकार्य˚, कार्य˚ H. 3.<BR>—2 Entitled to, having a right to; सर्वे स्युरधिकारिणः; so उत्तराधिकारिन्<BR> heir; धनग्रहण˚ &c.; तपस्यनधिकारित्वात् R. 15. 51 not qualified or authorised.<BR>—3 Belonging to, owned by.<BR>—4 Fit for. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारी
अधिकारिन्, अधिकारवत् + ({@-री, -वान्@})<BR>—1 An official, officer; न निष्प्रयोजनम् अधिकारवन्तः प्रभुभिराहूयन्ते<BR> Mu. 3; a functionary, superintendent, head, director, governor.<BR>—2 A rightful claimant, proprietor, master, owner.<BR>—3 One qualified to sacrifice or perform sacred works.<BR>—4 Man as the lord of creation.<BR>—5 One well versed in the Vedānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारवान्
अधिकारिन्, अधिकारवत् + ({@-री, -वान्@})<BR>—1 An official, officer; न निष्प्रयोजनम् अधिकारवन्तः प्रभुभिराहूयन्ते<BR> Mu. 3; a functionary, superintendent, head, director, governor.<BR>—2 A rightful claimant, proprietor, master, owner.<BR>—3 One qualified to sacrifice or perform sacred works.<BR>—4 Man as the lord of creation.<BR>—5 One well versed in the Vedānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिता
अधिकारिता, -त्वम्<BR> Authority, rightful claim, qualification &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारित्वम्
अधिकारिता, -त्वम्<BR> Authority, rightful claim, qualification &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत|अधिकृतः
अधिकृत <i>p. p.</i> [कृ-क्त] Authorised, appointed &c.; one possessed<BR> of authorised qualification, &c.; राज्ञश्चाधिकृतो विद्वान् ब्राह्मणः<BR> Ms. 8. 11; पात्राणि नाट्येऽधिकृताः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृतः|अधिकृत
अधिकृत + .{@-तः@} An officer, official, functionary, superintendent, head,<BR> one in charge of any thing; संभावना ह्यधिकृतस्य तनोति तेजः Ki. 6. 46;<BR> प्रासाद˚ Mu. 3; Pt. 1. 424; राष्ट्र˚ Y. 1. 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृतिः|अधिकृति
अधिकृतिः <i>f.</i> Right, privilege, ownership. See अधिकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत्य
अधिकृत्य <i>ind.</i> With reference to, regarding, concerning; ग्रीष्मसमयमधिकृत्य<BR> गीयताम् Ś. 1; शकुन्तलामधिकृत्य ब्रवीमि Ś. 2. I refer to, speak<BR> of Śakuntalā; 3. 4; शान्तिमधिकृत्य कृत्यवित् अन्वयुङ्क्त गुरुम् R. 11. 62.<BR> See अधिकृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रम्
अधिक्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To ascend, mount upon.<BR>—2 To attack, scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रमः|अधिक्रम
अधिक्रमः, -क्रमणम्<BR> An attack, invasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रमणम्
अधिक्रमः, -क्रमणम्<BR> An attack, invasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षित्
अधिक्षित् <i>m.</i> [अधिक्षि भावे कर्तरि वा क्विप् तुक् च Tv.] Decay<BR> or one that causes decay; a lord or ruler (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षिप्
अधिक्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To insult, abuse, asperse, vilify, traduce, censure; किं मां संभृतदोषैरधिक्षिपथ<BR> Ś. 5 heap accusations on me; नृपतावधिक्षिपति शौरिम् Śi. 15. 44;<BR> न मे पादरजसा तुल्य इत्यधिक्षिप्तः M. 1.<BR>—2 To throw or lay upon, bespatter.<BR>—3 To superinduce (disease).<BR>—4 To surpass. cf. अधिक्षिपदब्जनेत्र <i>a.</i> Having eyes which eclipse the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षेपः|अधिक्षेप
अधिक्षेपः<BR>—1 Abuse, insulting, insult; प्रज्ञा˚ Dk. 52 insult to, reflection<BR> on, the understanding; भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनं Ki. 1. 28.<BR>—2 Laying upon; fixing; throwing.<BR>—3 Dismissal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम्
अधिगम् €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To acquire, obtain, get, attain, secure; आज्ञाकरत्वमधिगम्य<BR> V. 3. 19; अधिगच्छति महिमानं चन्द्रोऽपि निशापरिगृहीतः M. 1. 13;<BR> भर्तारमधिगच्छेत् Ms. 9. 91 marry; श्रेयांसि सर्वाण्यधिजग्मुषस्ते R. 5. 34.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To find, meet with, fall in with, see, discover.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To accomplish; अर्थं सप्रतिबन्धं प्रभुरधिगन्तुं सहायवानेव<BR> M. 1. 9; न मे बुद्धिर्निश्चयमधिगच्छति Mu. 5 is not able to decide; for<BR>——(<i>a</i>) see also Ms. 2. 218; Bg. 2. 64; R. 2. 66.<BR>—2 To approach, reach, go towards or near; गुणालयोऽप्यसन्मन्त्री नृपतिर्नाधिगम्यते<BR> Pt. 1. 384; तस्यान्तं नांधिगच्छति does not reach or go to the end.<BR>—3 To study, learn; know; तेभ्योऽधिगन्तुं निगमान्तविद्याम् U. 2. 3;<BR> श्रुतमप्यधिगम्य Ki. 2. 41, 6. 38; Ms. 7. 39; धर्मेणाधिगतो यैस्तु 12. 109;<BR> वेदार्थानधिगच्छेत् Y. 1. 99; Bk. 7. 37.<BR>—4 To cohabit with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगत
अधिगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Acquired, obtained &c.; ˚परमार्थान्पण्डितान्मावमंस्थाः Bh. 2. 13.<BR>—2 Studied, known, learnt, mastered; किमित्येवं पृच्छस्यनधिगतरामायण<BR> इव U. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगमः|अधिगम
अधिगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Acquisition, obtaining, getting, finding &c.; (इच्छामि.) श्रोतुं<BR> च सीताधिगमे प्रयत्नम् Rām. 5. 64. 32; दुरधिगमः परभागः Pt. 5. 34;<BR> वंशस्थितेरधिगमात् V. 5. 15; दाराधिगमनम् Ms. 1. 112 marriage.<BR>—2 Mastery, knowledge; असच्छास्त्राधिगमनम् Ms. 11. 65.<BR>—3 Mercantile return, profit; acquiring property; निध्यादेः प्राप्तिः<BR> Mit. or धनप्राप्तिः; स्थापयन्ति तु यां वृद्धिं स तत्राधिगमं प्रति Ms. 8. 157.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 Intercourse.<BR>—6 Seeing, looking; अपनेष्यामि संतापं तवाधिगमशासनात् Rām. 5. 35. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगमनम्
अधिगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Acquisition, obtaining, getting, finding &c.; (इच्छामि.) श्रोतुं<BR> च सीताधिगमे प्रयत्नम् Rām. 5. 64. 32; दुरधिगमः परभागः Pt. 5. 34;<BR> वंशस्थितेरधिगमात् V. 5. 15; दाराधिगमनम् Ms. 1. 112 marriage.<BR>—2 Mastery, knowledge; असच्छास्त्राधिगमनम् Ms. 11. 65.<BR>—3 Mercantile return, profit; acquiring property; निध्यादेः प्राप्तिः<BR> Mit. or धनप्राप्तिः; स्थापयन्ति तु यां वृद्धिं स तत्राधिगमं प्रति Ms. 8. 157.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 Intercourse.<BR>—6 Seeing, looking; अपनेष्यामि संतापं तवाधिगमशासनात् Rām. 5. 35. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम्य
अधिगम्य, -गमनीय, -गन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Attainable. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगमनीय
अधिगम्य, -गमनीय, -गन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Attainable. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगन्तव्य|अधिगंतव्य
अधिगम्य, -गमनीय, -गन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Attainable. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगन्तृ|अधिगंतृ
अधिगन्तृ <i>a.</i> [गम्-तृच्] One who attains or acquires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगव
अधिगव <i>a.</i> or <i>adv.</i> [गवि इत्यधिगवम् अव्ययी˚ स˚] Found<BR> in or derived from a cow; स्वादीयो यदधिगवं क्षीरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगुण|अधिगुणः
अधिगुण <i>a.</i> [अधिका गुणा यस्य]<BR>—1 Possessing superior qualities, worthy, meritorious; याच्ञा मोघा वरमधिगुणे<BR> नाधमे लब्धकामा Me. 6.<BR>—2 [अधिगतो गुणो ज्या येन] well strung (as a bow); ˚शरासनं जनाः Ki. 12. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगुणः|अधिगुण
अधिगुण + .{@-णः@} A superior or eminent merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिचर्
अधिचर् €1 P. To walk or move over or on something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिचरणम्
अधिचरणम् Act of walking over something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजननम्
अधिजननम् Birth; मातुरग्रेऽधिजननम् Ms. 2. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्वः|अधिजिह्व
अधिजिह्वः [अधिका जिह्वा यस्य] A serpent (who has a forked tongue).<BR> This arose from the attempt of the serpents to lick the nectar placed<BR> on a bed of Kuśa grass, the sharp points of which pricked the tongue and<BR> split it into two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्वा
अधिजिह्वः + .{@-ह्वा, -जिह्विका@} [अधिरूढा जिह्वा, स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>—1 The uvula.<BR>—2 A sort of swelling of the tongue or epiglottis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्विका
अधिजिह्वः + .{@-ह्वा, -जिह्विका@} [अधिरूढा जिह्वा, स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>—1 The uvula.<BR>—2 A sort of swelling of the tongue or epiglottis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्य
अधिज्य <i>a.</i> [अध्यारूढा ज्या यत्र, अधिगतं ज्यां वा] Having the<BR> bow-string stretched, well strung (as a bow).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिज्यधन्वन्, अधिज्यकार्मुक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्यधन्वन्
अधिज्य + -धन्वन्, -कार्मुक <i>a.</i> having the bow strung; अधिज्यधन्वा<BR> विचचार दावम् R. 2. 8. त्वयि चाधिज्यकार्मुके Ś. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्यकार्मुक
अधिज्य + -धन्वन्, -कार्मुक <i>a.</i> having the bow strung; अधिज्यधन्वा<BR> विचचार दावम् R. 2. 8. त्वयि चाधिज्यकार्मुके Ś. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्यता
अधिज्यता —1 The state of being strung; ˚तां नी to string; लीलयैव<BR> धनुषी अधिज्यताम् R. 11. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधित्यका
अधित्यका [अधि-त्यकन् P. V. 2. 34; पर्वतस्य आरूढस्थलमधित्यका<BR> Sk.] A table-land, highland; स्थाणुं तपस्यन्तमधित्यकायां Ku. 3. 17;<BR> अधित्यकायामिव धातुमग्याम् R. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधित्वत्
अधित्वत् <i>ind.</i> In you; अधिकमधित्वदनेन निपाति Śi. 7. 41. (see अधि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदण्डनेतृ|अधिदंडनेतृ
अधिदण्डनेतृ <i>m.</i> N. of Yama; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदन्तः|अधिदन्त|अधिदंतः
अधिदन्तः [अध्यारूढो दन्तः] A redundant tooth growing over another.<BR> P. VI. 2. 188; also Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदार्व
अधिदार्व <i>a.</i> Wooden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदीधिति
अधिदीधिति <i>a.</i> Of superior or transcendental lustre; निदाघधामानमिवाधिदीतिम् Śi. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेवः|अधिदेव
अधिदेवः, -वता<BR> [अधिष्ठाता-त्री देवः देवता वा]<BR>—1 A presiding or tutelary deity; ययाचे पादुके पश्चात्कर्तुं राज्याधिदेवते<BR> R. 12. 17, 13. 68, 16. 9; (सा) नैवापयाति हृदयाधिदेवतेव Bv. 3. 3;<BR> सा रामणीयकनिधेरधिदेवता वा Māl. 1. 21. (The eleven organs<BR> of sense are said to have each a presiding deity: श्रोत्रस्य दिक्, त्वचो<BR> वातः, नेत्रस्य अर्कः, रसनाया वरुणः, घ्राणस्य अश्विनौ, वागिन्द्रियस्य<BR> वह्निः, हस्तस्य इन्द्रः, पादस्य उपेन्द्रः, पायोः मित्रः, उपस्थस्य प्रजापतिः,<BR> मनसः चन्द्रश्च.)<BR>—2 [अधिकृतो देवो येन गुणातिशयात्] The supreme or highest god, Almighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेवता
अधिदेवः, -वता<BR> [अधिष्ठाता-त्री देवः देवता वा]<BR>—1 A presiding or tutelary deity; ययाचे पादुके पश्चात्कर्तुं राज्याधिदेवते<BR> R. 12. 17, 13. 68, 16. 9; (सा) नैवापयाति हृदयाधिदेवतेव Bv. 3. 3;<BR> सा रामणीयकनिधेरधिदेवता वा Māl. 1. 21. (The eleven organs<BR> of sense are said to have each a presiding deity: श्रोत्रस्य दिक्, त्वचो<BR> वातः, नेत्रस्य अर्कः, रसनाया वरुणः, घ्राणस्य अश्विनौ, वागिन्द्रियस्य<BR> वह्निः, हस्तस्य इन्द्रः, पादस्य उपेन्द्रः, पायोः मित्रः, उपस्थस्य प्रजापतिः,<BR> मनसः चन्द्रश्च.)<BR>—2 [अधिकृतो देवो येन गुणातिशयात्] The supreme or highest god, Almighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेवनम्
अधिदेवनम् Gambling table, board for gambling (अधि उपरि दीव्यते यत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदैवम्
अधिदैवम्, -दैवतम्<BR> [अधिष्ठातृ दैवम्-दैवतम् वा]<BR>—1 The presiding god or deity; अधिदैवं किमुच्यते Bg. 8. 1. पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम्<BR> Bg. 8. 4, 7. 30; शिवाधिदैवतं ध्यायेत् वह्निप्रत्यधिदैवतम्; तमभिनन्दन्ति …<BR> यः अधिदैवतमिव स्तौति K. 109.<BR>—2 The supreme deity or the divine agent operating in material objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदैवतम्
अधिदैवम्, -दैवतम्<BR> [अधिष्ठातृ दैवम्-दैवतम् वा]<BR>—1 The presiding god or deity; अधिदैवं किमुच्यते Bg. 8. 1. पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम्<BR> Bg. 8. 4, 7. 30; शिवाधिदैवतं ध्यायेत् वह्निप्रत्यधिदैवतम्; तमभिनन्दन्ति …<BR> यः अधिदैवतमिव स्तौति K. 109.<BR>—2 The supreme deity or the divine agent operating in material objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिनाथः|अधिनाथ
अधिनाथः [अधिको नाथः] The Supreme lord; a chieftain or lord;<BR> N. of the author of कालयोगशास्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिनी
अधिनी €1 P. To lead away from, to enhance, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिनायः|अधिनाय
अधिनायः [नी-घञ्, -अधिनीयते वायुना] Fragrance, odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिनिर्णिज्
अधिनिर्णिज् <i>a.</i> Veiled; यः श्वेताँअधिनिर्णिजश्चक्रे कृष्णाँ अनुव्रता Rv. 8. 41. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपः|अधिप
अधिपः [अधिपाति, अधि-पा-क] A lord, ruler, king, sovereign, head;<BR> अथ प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते R. 2. 1; mostly in comp.; नराधिपः<BR> lord of men, king; गज˚ a lordly elephant &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपतिः|अधिपति
अधिपतिः [अधिकः पतिः]<BR>—1 = अधिपः.<BR>—2 A part of the head where the wound proves immediately fatal; (मस्तकाभ्यन्तरोपरिष्टात्<BR> शिरासन्धिसन्निपातो रोमावर्तोऽधिपतिः, तत्रापि सद्यो मरणम् Suśr.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपत्नी
अधिपत्नी Ved. A female ruler, mistress (स्वामिनी) नक्षत्राणामधिपत्नी<BR> विशाखे T. Br. 3. 1. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपाः
अधिपाः [अधिपाति-पा क्विप्] A king, ruler, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपांशुल
अधिपांशुल <i>a.</i> Dusty from above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपुरुषः|अधिपुरुष
अधिपु(पू)रुषः [अधिकः पु(पू)रुषः] The Supreme Being; तस्माद्<BR> विराळजायत विराजो अधिपूरुषः Rv. 10. 90. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपूरुषः|अधिपूरुष
अधिपु(पू)रुषः [अधिकः पु(पू)रुषः] The Supreme Being; तस्माद्<BR> विराळजायत विराजो अधिपूरुषः Rv. 10. 90. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपुष्पलिका
अधिपुष्पलिका A betel-nut tree,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपेषणम्
अधिपेषणम् [पिष्-ल्युट्] Pounding or grinding upon, serving to pound or grind upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रज
अधिप्रज <i>a.</i> [अधिका प्रजा यस्य] Having many children (as<BR> a man, woman &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रजम्
अधिप्रज + .{@-जम्@} <i>adv.</i> [प्रजामधिकृत्य] Regarding creation (of the<BR> world) as a means of preserving the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रष्टियुगम्
अधिप्रष्टियुगम् [प्रष्टौ निहितं युगम्] A yoke laid on the प्रष्टि<BR> or foremost of the three horses, used on certain sacrificial occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रष्टियुगः|अधिप्रष्टियुग|अधिप्रष्टियुगं
अधिप्रष्टियुगम् + .{@-गः@} The fourth horse thus attached (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिबलम्
अधिबलम् An interlocution of high words in mutual defiance; S. D. 526.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूः
अधिभूः [अधिभवति स्वामीभवति; भू-क्विप्] A master, superior; foremost;<BR> राक्षसानामधिभुवि Mv. 6. 47; रघूणामधिभुवा 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूतम्
अधिभूतम्^1 [अधिष्ठायिभूतं or भूतं प्राणिमात्रमधिकृत्य वर्तमानम्]<BR> The highest being; the Supreme Spirit or its all-pervading influence;<BR> the whole inanimate creation; अधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तं Bg. 8. 1; अधिभूतं<BR> क्षरो भावः 8. 4 ‘अधिभूत is all perishable things’.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost diacritics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभोजनम्
अधिभोजनम् [अधिकं भोजनम्]<BR>—1 Excess in eating.<BR>—2 [अधिकं भोजनं धनं मूल्यं वा यस्य] Very costly or valuable;<BR> दश वस्त्राधिभोजना Rv. 6. 47. 23; a supplementary or additional gift (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमखः|अधिमख
अधिमखः The presiding deity of a sacrifice; तस्मै नमो भगवतेऽभिमखाय<BR> तुभ्यम् (Bhāg. 3. 9. 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमन्थः|अधिमन्थ|अधिमंथः
अधिमन्थः [अधिकं मथ्यते अनेन; मन्थ् करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 Severe ophthalmia; उत्पाट्यत इवात्यर्थं नेत्रं निर्मथ्यते तथा ।<BR> शिरसोऽर्धं तु तं विद्यादधिमन्थं स्वलक्षणैः.<BR>—2 = अधिमन्थनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमन्थनम्
अधिमन्थनम् [मन्थ्-भावे करणे वा ल्युट्] Rubbing together for producing<BR> fire; suitable for such friction (as wood). अस्तीदमधिमन्थनम् Rv. 3. 29. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमन्थित|अधिमंथित
अधिमन्थित <i>a.</i> [अधिमन्थोऽस्य संजातः इतच्] Suffering from eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमर्म
अधिमर्म <i>ind.</i> In the vital parts. (See अधि) अथ तीक्ष्णायसैर्बाणैरधिमर्म<BR> रघूत्तमौ Bk. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसः|अधिमांस
अधिमांसः [अधिकं मांसं यत्र] A sort of disease in the white<BR> of the eye, a sort of cancer or protuberance of flesh; विस्तीर्णं मृदु<BR> बहुलं यकृत्प्रकाशं श्यावं वा तदधिमांसजार्म विद्यात् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसकः|अधिमांसक
अधिमांसकः [अधिकं मांसं यत्र] A sort of cancer in the back<BR> of the gums; हनूस्थे पश्चिमे दन्ते महाशोथो महारुजः । लालास्रावी<BR> (कालास्नायी) कफकृतो विज्ञेयः सोऽधिमांसकः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमात्र
अधिमात्र <i>a.</i> [अधिका मात्रा यस्य] Beyond measure, excessive, inordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमात्रम्
अधिमात्र + .{@-त्रम्@} On the subject of prosody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमासः|अधिमास
अधिमासः [अधिको रविमासात् अतिरिक्तः शुक्लप्रतिपदादिदर्शान्तश्चान्द्रो<BR> मासः] An intercalary (lunar) month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुक्तकः|अधिमुक्तक
अधिमुक्तकः Jasmin Sambal मधुमाधवी (Mar. मोगरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुक्तिः|अधिमुक्ति
अधिमुक्तिः <i>f.</i> Trust, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुक्तिका
अधिमुक्तिका A pearl-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुह्यः|अधिमुह्य
अधिमुह्यः N. of Buddha in one of his 34 former births.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियज्ञ|अधियज्ञः
अधियज्ञ <i>a.</i> Pertaining to a sacrifice; ˚ज्ञं ब्रह्म जपेत् Ms. 6. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियज्ञः|अधियज्ञ
अधियज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञः@} Principal sacrifice; the agency effecting or causing such<BR> sacrifice; ˚ज्ञोहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर Bg. 8. 4 the अधियज्ञ<BR> is I myself in this body (i. e. Kṛṣṇa); अत्रास्मिन्देहे अन्तर्यामित्वेन<BR> स्थितोऽहमधियज्ञः यज्ञादिकर्मप्रवर्तकस्तत्फलदाता चेति श्रीधरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियज्ञम्
अधियज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञम्@} <i>adv.</i> on the subject of sacrifices; so अधियाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियाङ्ग|अधियांग
अधियाङ्ग = अधिकाङ्ग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियोगः|अधियोग
अधियोगः [अधिको योगः] An auspicious conjunction of stars for<BR> departure, expedition &c. (ज्योतिषप्रसिद्धो यात्रिकशुभयोगः); योगे<BR> क्षेममथाधियोगगमने क्षेमं रिपूणां वधः Muhūrtachintāmaṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियोधः|अधियोध
अधियोधः [आधिक्येन युध्यते; युध्-अच्] The foremost hero or warrior<BR> (in fighting); न हि कोपपरीतानि हर्षवीर्योत्सुकानि च । भवन्ति अधियोधानां<BR> मुखानि निहते पतौ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरज्जु
अधिरज्जु <i>a.</i> Ved. [अधिगता रज्जुर्येन] Fastening, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथ|अधिरथः
अधिरथ <i>a.</i> [अध्यारूढो रथं रथिनं वा] Being on or over a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथः|अधिरथ
अधिरथ + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 A charioteer, driver.<BR>—2 N. of a charioteer who was king of Aṅga and foster-father of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथम्
अधिरथ + .{@-थम्@} Ved. A cart-load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्
अधिराज् <i>m.</i>, -जः<BR> [अधिराजते; राज्-क्विप्, राजन्-टच्-वा] A sovereign or supreme<BR> ruler, an emperor; प्रायोपविष्टो गङ्गायामनादृत्याधिराट् श्रियम् Bhāg.;<BR> अद्यास्तमेतु भुवनेष्वधिराजशब्दः U. 6. 16; king, head, lord (of men,<BR> animals &c.); हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; so मृग˚, नाग˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्ः
अधिराज् <i>m.</i>, -जः<BR> [अधिराजते; राज्-क्विप्, राजन्-टच्-वा] A sovereign or supreme<BR> ruler, an emperor; प्रायोपविष्टो गङ्गायामनादृत्याधिराट् श्रियम् Bhāg.;<BR> अद्यास्तमेतु भुवनेष्वधिराजशब्दः U. 6. 16; king, head, lord (of men,<BR> animals &c.); हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; so मृग˚, नाग˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्यम्
अधिराज्यम्, -ष्ट्रम्<BR> [अधिकृतं राज्यं राष्ट्रम् अत्र]<BR>—1 Imperial or sovereign sway, supremacy, sole sovereignty, imperial dignity, an empire.<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराष्ट्रम्
अधिराज्यम्, -ष्ट्रम्<BR> [अधिकृतं राज्यं राष्ट्रम् अत्र]<BR>—1 Imperial or sovereign sway, supremacy, sole sovereignty, imperial dignity, an empire.<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुक्म
अधिरुक्म <i>a.</i> [अधिगतं रुक्मम् आभरणं येन] Having ornaments (of gold &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधिरुह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To ascend, mount (a throne, hill &c.); go up to, find access to, sit<BR> in or on (acc.); पादाहतं यदुत्थाय मूर्धानमधिरोहति Śi. 2. 46;<BR> पुराधिरूढः शयनं महाधनं Ki. 1. 38 lying on; तुरगाधिरूढं<BR> R. 7. 37 riding a horse; विमानरत्नाधिरूढः 12. 104; बन्धुजनाधिरूढैर्गजानां वृन्दैः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">Page0065-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 7. 52 mounted or seated on; योगाधिरूढाः R. 13. 52; engaged or<BR> lost in contemplation; so Pt. 1; सद्यः परस्परतुलामधिरोहतां द्वे<BR> R. 5. 68 bear or acquire; प्रतिज्ञाम्˚ enter on; कीर्तिर्द्यामधिरोहति<BR> Śi. 2. 52; सर्वमनोरथानामग्रमिवाधिरूढा K. 158 mounted on the summit<BR> or pinnacle; त्वां धूरियं योग्यतयाधिरूढा Ki. 3. 50 this responsibility<BR> lies on your shoulders.<BR>—2 To string; अधिरोहति गाण्डीवं महेषौ Ki. 13. 16.<BR>—3 (Intrans.) To rise or grow over or above. ━<i>Caus.</i> [रोह(प)यति]<BR>—1 To raise, place, seat, cause to mount or ascend; ताः स्वमङ्कमधिरोप्य<BR> R. 19. 44 having placed or seated; जनः समेनैव पथाधिरोहति Śi. 12. 46.<BR>—2 To restore, give back; पुराणशोभामधिरोपितायां (वसतौ) R. 16. 42<BR> restored to its former grandeur.<BR>—3 To string (as a bow); कार्मुकं च बलिनाधिरोपितम् R. 11. 81.<BR>—4 To give, confer &c.; उदारक इति प्रीतलोकाधिरोपितापरश्लाघ्यनामनि Dk. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधिरुह् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Growing on; धरणिरुहाधिरुहो<BR> लतायाः Śi. 7. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढ
अधिरूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mounted, ascended &c.<BR>—2 Increased;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढसमाधियोगः|अधिरूढसमाधियोग
अधिरूढ + ˚समाधियोगः engaged in profound meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूषित
अधिरूषित <i>a.</i> Besmeared with sandal paste &c. मुखमधिरूषितपाण्डुगण्डलेखम् Ki. 10. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोपणम्
अधिरोपणम् Act of raising, exalting or causing to mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहः|अधिरोह
अधिरोहः An elephant rider; गजपतिमधिरोहः पक्षकव्यत्ययेन Śi. 11. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहणम्
अधिरोहणम् Ascending, mounting; चिता˚ R. 8. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहणी
अधिरोहणम् + .{@-णी@} [अधिरुह्यते अनया, रुह् करणे ल्युट्] A ladder, flight of<BR> steps (of wood &c. Mar. शिडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहिन्
अधिरोहिन् <i>a.</i> Ascending, mounting, rising above &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहिणी
अधिरोहिन् + .{@-णी@} [अधिरोहः साधनत्वेन अस्त्यस्याः] A ladder, flight of steps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवच्
अधिवच् €2 P. To speak in favour of, advocate, side with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवक्तृ
अधिवक्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who advocates a particular cause (पक्षपातेन वक्तृ), an advocate.<BR>—2 An orator.<BR>—3 A comforter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवचनम्
अधिवचनम्<BR>—1 Advocacy, speaking in favour of (पक्षपातेन कथनं वचनम्).<BR>—2 A name, epithet, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवाकः|अधिवाक
अधिवाकः [वच्-घञ्] Advocacy; तमिद्धनेषु हितेष्वधिवाकाय हवन्ते<BR> Rv. 8. 16. 5 (पक्षपातवचनाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवस्
अधिवस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To inhabit, fix oneʼs abode or residence in, settle, dwell or reside<BR> in (with acc. of place); गिरिमधिवसेस्तत्र विश्रामहेतोः Me. 25; यानि<BR> प्रियासहचरश्चिरमध्यवात्सम् U. 3. 8; बाल्यात्परामिव दशां मदनोऽध्युवास<BR> R. 5. 63, 11. 61, 13. 79; Śi. 3. 59; Bk. 1. 3, 5. 6; माऽधिवात्सीर्भुवम् 8. 79.<BR>—2 To settle, alight or perch on.<BR>—3 (€2 Ā.) To put on (clothes)<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to stay overnight.<BR>—2 To consecrate, set up (as an image).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवस्त्र
अधिवस्त्र <i>a.</i> [अध्यावृतं वस्त्रं येन] Clad, veiled; अधिवस्त्रा<BR> वधूरिव Rv. 8. 26. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासः|अधिवास
अधिवासः<BR>—1 Abode, residence; dwelling; सतत ˚सुभगार्पितस्तनम् Māl. 5. 8;<BR> तस्यापि स एवं गिरिरधिवासः K. 137; लक्ष्मीभृतोऽम्भोधितटाधिवासान्<BR> Śi. 3. 71 situated on; settlement, habitation. वसन्ति मन्नियोगेन<BR> अधिवासं च राक्षसाः Rām. 3. 36. 4.<BR>—2 An inhabitant, neighbour.<BR>—3 Obstinate pertinacity in making a demand, sitting without food before<BR> a personʼs house till he ceases to oppose or refuse it (Mar. धरर्णे).<BR>—4 [अधिवासयति देवता अनेन, करणे घञ्] Consecration of an image<BR> especially before the commencement of a sacrificial rite; see अधिवासनम्<BR> also. शुद्धाधिवासाश्च विशुद्धसत्त्वाः Bu. C. 1. 39.<BR>—5 A garment, mantle (अधीवासः also).<BR>—6 A birth-place; जातिश्रेण्यधिवासानां कुलधर्मांश्च सर्वतः । वर्जयन्ति<BR> च ये धर्मं तेषां धर्मो न विद्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 36. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित <i>p. p.</i> Inhabited, resorted to; विद्याधराध्युषितचारुशिलातलानि<BR> स्थानानि Bh. 2. 70; बलैरध्युषितास्तस्य R. 4. 46, 9. 25, 14. 30;<BR> सप्तर्षिमण्डल˚ K. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवास्
अधिवास् €10 P. To scent, perfume; कर्पूरपल्लवरसेन अधिवासय<BR> गन्धपात्राणि K. 184; मन्दारपुष्पैरधिवासितायाम् V. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासः|अधिवास
अधिवासः Application of perfumes or fragrant cosmetics; scenting,<BR> perfuming; fragrance, scent, fragrant odour itself; अधिवासस्पृहयेव<BR> मारुतः R. 8. 34; Śi. 2. 20, 5. 42; K. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासनम्
अधिवासनम् [वस्-णिच्, or वास् ल्युट्.]<BR>—1 Scenting with perfumes or odorous substances (संस्कारो गन्धमाल्याद्यैः Ak.).<BR>—2 [वस्-णिच्-ल्युट्] Preliminary consecration (प्रतिष्टा) of an image,<BR> its invocation and worship by suitable Mantras &c. before the commencement<BR> of a sacrifice; (यज्ञारम्भात्प्राक् देवताद्यावाहनपूर्वकः पूजनादिकर्मभेदः);<BR> Making a divinity assume its abode in an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासिन्
अधिवासिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inhabiting, dwelling or siting in.<BR>—2 Scenting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासित
अधिवासित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Invested or clothed with.<BR>—2 Scented, perfumed. कदम्बसर्जार्जुनकेतकीवनं विकम्पयंस्तत्कुसुमाधिवासितः<BR> Ṛs. 2. 17. अमरचन्द्रʼs commentary says, ‘कुसुमैः पुष्पैः अधिवासितः सुगन्धीकृतः ।’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवाहनम्
अधिवाहनम् Taking up, carrying over, conveying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविकर्तनम्
अधिविकर्तनम् The act of cutting off or cutting through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविद्
अधिविद् €6 U. To marry in addition to, supersede (as a wife) (said<BR> also of wives); वन्ध्याष्टमेऽधिवेद्या Ms. 9. 81; अधिविविदुरमात्यैराहृतास्तस्य<BR> यूनः प्रथमपरिगृहीते श्रीभुवौ राजकन्याः R. 18. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविन्ना
अधिविन्ना [विद्-क्त] A superseded wife, one whose husband has married<BR> again; अधिविन्ना तु भर्तव्या Y. 1. 74; अधिविन्ना तु या नारी निर्गच्छेद्रुषिता<BR> गृहात् । सा सद्यः सन्निरोद्धव्या त्याज्या वा कुलसन्निधौ ॥ Ms. 9. 83.<BR> [According to Hindu<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">Page0066-2</a>]<BR> Śāstras a wife may be superseded for any one of these 8 defects:− सुरापी<BR> व्याधिता धूर्ता वन्ध्यार्थध्न्यप्रियंवदा । स्त्रीप्रसूश्चाधिवेत्तव्या पुरुषद्वेषिणी<BR> तथा Y. 1. 73, 74; Ms. 9. 80-83.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेत्तृ
अधिवेत्तृ <i>m.</i> [विट्-कर्त्तरि तृच्] A husband who supersedes his first wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदः|अधिवेद
अधिवेदः Marrying an additional wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदम्
अधिवेदः + .{@-दम्@} <i>adv.</i> concerning the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदनम्
अधिवेदनम् [भावे ल्युट्] = अधिवेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिशी
अधिशी €2 Ā. To lie or sleep upon, sleep in, rest or recline upon;<BR> (with acc. of place); अध्यशेरत बृहद्भुजान्तरम् R. 19. 32; अमुम् … अधिशेते 13. 6, 16. 49;<BR> शिलापट्टमधिशयाना Ś. 3; अध्यशयिष्ट गाम् Bk. 15. 114;<BR> चन्द्रापीडः शयनतलमधिशिश्ये K. 98, 206; Ki. 1. 38; Dk. 112;<BR> to dwell, inhabit लङ्कावनं सिंहसमोऽधिशेते Bk. 10. 36; to<BR> sit in; अथाधिशिश्ये प्रयतः प्रदोषे रथम् R. 5. 28.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to sleep on; दर्भशम्यामधिशाय्य Dk. 105 placing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिशयित
अधिशयित <i>p. p.</i> Reclining upon, used for reclining upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रि
अधिश्रि €1 U.<BR>—1 To sleep on, ascend, mount, resort to; विलोचने बिभ्रदधिश्रितश्रिणी<BR> Śi. 1. 24 possessed of beauty; अधिश्रयन्तीर्गजताः 12. 50.<BR>—2 To place over.<BR>—3 (अधिश्री also) To put on fire, make hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयः|अधिश्रय
अधिश्रयः [श्रि-भावे अच्]<BR>—1 A receptacle.<BR>—2 [श्री-अच्] Boiling, making hot (by putting on fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयणम्
अधिश्रयणम्, -पणम्<BR> [श्रि-श्री-भावे-ल्युट्] Placing a kettle on fire; warming, boiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रपणम्
अधिश्रयणम्, -पणम्<BR> [श्रि-श्री-भावे-ल्युट्] Placing a kettle on fire; warming, boiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयणी
अधिश्रयणम्, -पणम् + .{@-णी@} [अधिश्रीयते पच्यतेऽत्र, आधारे ल्युट् डीप्] An oven, a fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्री
अधिश्री <i>a.</i> [अधिका श्रीर्यस्य] Of exalted dignity, supreme;<BR> very rich, sovereign lord; इयं महेन्द्रप्रभृतीनधिश्रियश्चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य<BR> मानिनी Ku. 5. 53; R. 7. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिषवणम्
अधिषवणम् [अधिषूयते सोमोऽत्र; अधिसु-आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A contrivance (like a hand-press) of leather &c. to extract and strain<BR> the Soma juice, or (<i>a.</i>) used for the act of straining &c.<BR>—2 [भावे-ल्युट्] Straining Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिषवण्या
अधिषवण्या [अधिषवणाय हिता, यत्] The board or wooden plank<BR> (फलक) used in the act of extracting Soma juice. यत्र द्वाविव<BR> जघनाधिषवण्या कृता Rv. 1. 28. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठा
अधिष्ठा €1 P. (used with acc. P. I. 4. 46.)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To stand on or upon, to sit in or upon, occupy (as a seat &c.),<BR> resort to; अर्धासनं गोत्रभिदोऽधितष्ठौ R. 6. 73; शाखिनः केचिदध्यष्ठुः<BR> Bk. 15. 31; प्रतनुबलान्यधितिष्ठतस्तपांसि Ki. 10. 16 practising;<BR> मामधिष्ठाय Rām. depending on me.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To stand, be; अध्यतिष्ठदङ्गुष्ठेन शतं समाः Mb.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To stand over, mount.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To stand by, be near; आश्रमबहिर्वृक्षमूलमधितिष्टति U. 4.<BR>—2 To be in, dwell in, inhabit, reside, stay; भुजङ्गपिहितद्वारं पातालमधितिष्ठति<BR> R. 1. 80; माधिष्ठा निर्जनं वनम् Bk. 8. 79; श्रीजयदेवभणितमधितिष्ठतु<BR> कण्ठतटीमविरतम् Gīt. 11.<BR>—3 To make oneself master of, seize, take possession of, overpower, conquer;<BR> संग्रामे तानधिष्ठास्यन् Bk. 9. 72; त्वमधिष्ठास्यसि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-1" target="_blank">Page0067-1</a>]<BR> द्विषः 16. 40; स सदा फलशालिनीं क्रियां शरदं लोक इवाधितिष्ठति<BR> Ki. 2. 31 obtains; अधितिष्ठति लोकमोजसा स विवस्वानिव मेदिनीपतिः 2. 38;<BR> यक्षः कुतश्चिदधिष्टाय वालचन्द्रिकां निवसति Dk. 18.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To lead, conduct as head or chief; महाराजदशरथस्य दारानधिष्ठाय<BR> वसिष्ठः प्राप्तः U. 4; see अधिष्टित also.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To be at the head of, govern, direct, preside over, rule, superintend;<BR> प्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय Bg. 4. 6 governing, controlling; श्रोत्रं चक्षुः<BR> स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च । अधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते 15. 9<BR> presiding over and thus turning to use.<BR>—5 To use, employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठित
अधिष्ठित <i>p. p.</i> [अधिष्ठा-क्त]<BR>—1 (Used actively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Standing, being; दन्तान्तरमधिष्टितम् Ms. 5. 141; (oft. with<BR> अ dropped; ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य धिष्ठितम् Bg. 13. 17.);<BR> वीरलोकमधिष्ठितस्तातः Mv. 5 gone to; राजप्रसाद˚<BR> Pt. 1 being in or enjoying royal favour.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Possessed of, dependent on.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Directing, presiding over; धर्माधिकरणाधिष्ठितपुरुषैः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 (Passively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Inhabited or resorted to by, occupied, possessed by; दनुकबन्धाधिष्ठितो<BR> दण्डकारण्यभागः U. 1; लोकेशाधिष्ठितो राजा Ms. 5. 97; अचिराधिष्ठितराज्यः<BR> शत्रुः M. 1. 8 an enemy who has newly (not long ago) ascended the throne,<BR> a newly established king; अचिर˚ अधिकारः Dk. 64 newly established;<BR> so ग्रहेण possessed by; मयूर˚ K. 97; ˚पुरोभागाम् K. 10, 130, 147, 152.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Full of, seized with, taken possession of, smitten, affected,<BR> overpowered; अनेनाधिष्ठितानां कामिनीनां K. 236, 161, 194; कामाधिष्ठितचेतसा<BR> H. 1; Śi. 13. 39.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Watched over, guarded, superintended; रक्षापुरुषाधिष्ठिते प्रासादे<BR> Pt. 1; आर्यारुन्धतीवसिष्ठाधिष्ठितेषु रघुकुलकदम्बकेषु U. 2; प्रनष्टाधिगतं<BR> द्रव्यं तिष्ठेद्युक्तैरधिष्ठितम् Ms. 8. 34.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Led, conducted, commanded by, presided over; साङ्ख्यमिव कपिलाधिष्ठितम्<BR> K. 40; अनेनाधिष्ठितं भुवनतलम् 43, 44, 228; वसिष्ठाधिष्ठिता देव्यो<BR> गता राघवमातरः U. 1. 3; तव प्रतापाधिष्ठितेन उपायेन H. 4 aided<BR> or supported; ताताधिष्ठितानामपि बलानाम् Ve. 3; स्वामिनाधिष्ठितः श्वापि H. 3. 129.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Ridden, mounted upon; मूषकाधिष्ठितं तमवलोक्य Pt. 2 with<BR> the mouse seated upon him; विलोक्य वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया Ku. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठातृ
अधिष्ठातृ [स्था-तृच्] Superintending, watching over, presiding over,<BR> guiding, governing; हनूमांश्चाप्यधिष्ठाता Rām. 5. 63. 22; tutelary<BR> guardian; as ˚त्री देवता a guardian or presiding deity. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठातृता
अधिष्ठातृ + ({@-ता@})<BR> A superintendent, head, chief, protector, controller, regulator,<BR> ruler; सर्वेन्द्रियाधिष्ठाता Bhāṣā P.; especially with reference to<BR> the Almighty who is the ruler of the universe. See अधिदेव also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठानम्
अधिष्ठानम् [अधि-स्था-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Standing or being near, being at hand, approach (सन्निधि); अत्राधिष्ठानं<BR> कुरु take a seat here.<BR>—2 Resting upon, occupying, inhabiting, dwelling in, locating oneself<BR> in; प्राणाधिष्टानं देहस्य &c.<BR>—3 A position, site, basis, seat; त्र्यधिष्ठानस्य देहिनः Ms. 12. 4;<BR> इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते Bg. 3. 40, 18. 14 the seat<BR> (of that desire.)<BR>—4 Residence, abode; नगरं राजाधिष्ठानम् Pt. 1; so धर्म˚; a<BR> place, locality, town; सर्वाविनयाधिष्ठानतां गच्छन्ति K. 106;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">Page0067-2</a>]<BR> कस्मिंश्चिदधिष्टाने in a certain place.<BR>—5 Authority, power, power of control, presiding over; अनधिष्ठानम्<BR> H. 3. 83 loss of position, dimissal from a post (of authority); समर्थस्त्वमिमं<BR> जेतुमधिष्ठानपराक्रमैः Rām.; यथेह अश्वैर्युक्तो रथः सारथिनाऽधिष्ठितः<BR> प्रवर्तते तथा आत्माधिष्ठानाच्छरीरम् Gaudapāda; महाश्वेताकृताच्च सत्याधिष्ठानात्<BR> K. 346 appeal or reference to truth.<BR>—6 Government, dominion.<BR>—7 A wheel (of a car &c.) अधिष्ठानं मनश्चासीत्परिरथ्या सरस्वती<BR> Mb. 8. 34. 34, 5. 178. 74.<BR>—8 A precedent, prescribed rule.<BR>—9 A benediction. cf. अधिष्टानं चकपुरप्रभावाध्यासनेष्वपि । Nm.<BR>—10 Destruction (?); अमित्राणामधिष्ठानाद्वधाद् दुर्योधनस्य च । भीम<BR> दिष्ट्या पृथिव्यां ते प्रथितं सुमहद्यशः ॥ Mb. 9. 61. 14.<BR>—11 Couch, seat, bed; साधिष्ठानानि सर्वशः Rām. 6. 75. 19.<BR>—12 A butt (for an allurement.) तस्माद् बाह्यमधिष्ठानं कृत्वा कार्ये चतुर्विधे ।<BR> Kau. A. 1. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधिष्ठानाधिकरणम्, अधिष्ठानशरीरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठानाधिकरणम्
अधिष्ठानम् + -अधिकरणम् Municipal Board. (अधिष्ठान = city; अधिकरण<BR> = court and office of administration) EI. XV, p. 143, XVII. p. 193 f, XX, pp. 61 ff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठानशरीरम्
अधिष्ठानम् + -शरीरम् A body which forms the medium between the subtle and the gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्त्रि
अधिस्त्रि <i>ind.</i> [स्त्रियमधिकृत्य] Concerning a woman or wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्त्री
अधिस्त्रि + .{@-स्त्री@} [अधिका स्त्री] A superior or distinguished woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्यन्दम्
अधिस्यन्दम् <i>ind.</i> [अधिकः स्यन्दो वेगो यथा स्यात्तथा] More quickly;<BR> अधिस्यन्दं प्रववृतिरे चमूचराः Śi. 17. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधी
अधी [अधिं-इ] €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To study, learn (by heart), read; (with abl. of person) learn from;<BR> आख्यातोपयोगे P. I. 4. 29. उपाध्यायादधीते Sk.; सोऽध्यैष्ट वेदान् Bk. 1. 2.<BR>—2 (P.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To remember, think of, long or care for, mind, (with regret)<BR> with gen.; रामस्य दयमानोऽसावध्येति तव लक्ष्मणः Bk. 8. 119, 18. 38;<BR> ममैवाध्येति नृपतिस्तृप्यन्निव जलाञ्जलेः Ki. 11. 74 thinks of me only.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To know or learn by heart, study, learn; गच्छाधीहि गुरोर्मुखात् Mb.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To teach, declare.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To notice, observe, understand.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) To meet with, obtain; तेन दीर्घममरत्वमध्यगुः । Śi. 14. 31<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> [अध्यापयति] to teach, instruct (in); with acc. of the<BR> agent of the verb in the primitive sense; (तौ) साङ्गं च वेदमध्याप्य<BR> R. 15. 33; विद्यामथैनं विजयां जयां च … अध्यापिपद् गाधिसुतो यथावत्<BR> Bk. 2. 21, 7. 34; अध्यापितस्योशनसापि नीतिम् Ku. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीत|अधीतः
अधीत <i>p. p.</i> Learnt, studied, read, remembered, attained &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अधीतविद्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतविद्य
अधीत + -विद्य <i>a.</i> who has studied the Vedas or finished his studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिः|अधीति
अधीतिः <i>f.</i> [इ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Study, perusal; ˚बोधाचरणप्रचारणैः N. 1. 4.<BR>—2 Remembrance, recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिन्
अधीतिन् <i>a.</i> [अधीतमनेन; अधीत-इनि] Well-read, proficient<BR> in (with loc.) अधीती चतुर्ष्वाम्रायेषु Dk. 120; वेदे, व्याकरणे &c.;<BR> त्वगुत्तरासङ्गवतीमधीतिनीम् Ku. 5. 16 muttering holy prayers, engaged<BR> in repeating sacred texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीयानः|अधीयान
अधीयानः <i>pres. p.</i> A student, one who goes over the Vedas यो<BR> वै युवाप्यधीयानः Ms. 2. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0067-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोनिबन्धः|अधोनिबन्ध
अधोनिबन्धः The third stage of must of an elephant; Mātaṅga L. 9. 14.<BR> The stage is callad अधोनिबन्धिनी in Somadevaʼs Yaśastilakachampū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययः|अध्यय
अध्ययः [इ-भावे अच्]<BR>—1 Learning, study; remembrance.<BR>—2 = अध्याय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनम्
अध्ययनम्<BR>—1 [इ-ल्युट्] Learning, study, reading (especially the Vedas); one of<BR> the six duties of a Brāhmaṇa. The study of the Vedas is allowed to the<BR> first 3 classes, but not to a Śūdra Ms. 1. 88, 91. अध्ययनं च अक्षरमात्रपाठ<BR> इति वैदिकाः, सार्थाक्षरग्रहणमिति मीमांसकाः; the latter view is obviously<BR> correct; cf. यथा पशुर्भारवाही न तस्य भजते फलम् । द्विजस्तथार्थानभिज्ञो<BR> न वेदफलमश्नुते ॥ or better still Yāskaʼs Nirukta: स्थाणुरयं<BR> भारहारः किलाभूदधीत्य वेदं न विजानाति योऽर्थम् । योऽर्थज्ञ इत् (अर्थविद्)<BR> सकलं भद्रमश्नुते नाकमेति ज्ञानविधूतपाप्मा ॥ See also under अनग्नि.<BR>—2 Muttering प्रणव mantra; वीतरागा महाप्रज्ञा ध्यानाध्ययनसम्पदा<BR> Mb. 12. 300. 49. (अध्ययनं प्रणवजपः इति टीका)<BR>—3 Teaching; कृत्वा चाध्ययनं तेषां शिष्याणां शतमुत्तमम् Mb. 12. 318. 17<BR> see अध्यापनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापकः|अध्यापक
अध्यापकः [अधि-इ-णिच्-ण्वुल्] A teacher, preceptor, instructor especially<BR> of the Vedas; व्याकरण˚, न्याय˚ professor or teacher of grammar,<BR> logic &c.; भृतक˚ a hired teacher, mercenary teacher; ˚उदितः<BR> styled a professor. According to Viṣṇu-Smṛti an <i>adhyāpaka</i> is of 2<BR> kinds: he is either an <i>Acārya</i> i. e. one who invests a boy with<BR> the sacred thread and initiates him into the Vedas, or he is an <i>Upādhyāya</i><BR> i. e. one who teaches for livelihood (वृत्त्यर्थम्) See Ms. 2. 140-141.<BR> and the two words. [उपनीय तु यः शिष्यं वेदमध्यापयेद्द्विजः । सकल्पं<BR> सरहस्यं च तमाचार्यं प्रचक्षते ॥ एकदेशं तु वेदस्य वेदाङ्गान्यपि<BR> वा पुनः । योऽध्यापयति वृत्त्यर्थमुपाध्यायः स उच्यते ॥]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापनम्
अध्यापनम् [इ-णिच्, भावे-ल्युट्] Teaching, instructing, lecturing,<BR> especially on sacred knowledge; one of the six duties of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> According to Indian lawgivers अध्यापन is of three kinds: (1) undertaken<BR> for charity, (2) for wages and (3) in consideration of services rendered;<BR> cf. Hārīta: अध्यापनं च त्रिविधं धर्मार्थमृक्थकारणम् । शुश्रूषाकरणं<BR> चेति त्रिविधं परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापयितृ
अध्यापयितृ <i>m.</i> [इ-णिच्-तृच्] A teacher, instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्याय <i>a.</i> [इ-घञ् P. III. 3. 21] (At the end of comp.) A reader,<BR> student, one who studies; वेदाध्यायः a student of the Vedas; so मन्त्र˚<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यायः|अध्याय
अध्याय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Reading, learning, study, especially of the Vedas; प्रशान्ताध्यायसत्कथा<BR> (नगरी) Rām.<BR>—2 Proper time for reading or for a lesson; ˚ज्ञाः प्रचक्षते Ms. 4. 102,<BR> see अनध्याय also.<BR>—3 A lesson, lecture; अधीयतेऽस्मिन् अध्यायः P. III. 3. 122; so स्वाध्यायोऽध्येतव्यः.<BR>—4 A chapter, a large division of a work, such as of the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR> Mahābhārata, Manusmṛti, Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras &c. The following are some<BR> of the names used by Sanskrit writers to denote chapters or divisions<BR> of works:− सर्गो वर्गः परिच्छेदोद्घाताध्यायाङ्कसंग्रहाः । उच्छ्वासः परिवर्तश्च<BR> पटलः काण्डमाननम् । स्थानं प्रकरणं चैव पर्वोल्लासाह्निकानि च । स्कन्धांशौ<BR> तु पुराणादौ प्रायशः परिकीर्तितौ ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यायिन्
अध्यायिन् <i>a.</i> [इ-णिनि] Studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतृ
अध्येतृ <i>m.</i>, -त्री <i>f.</i><BR> A student, learner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येत्री
अध्येतृ <i>m.</i>, -त्री <i>f.</i><BR> A student, learner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीकारः|अधीकार
अधीकारः [कृ-घञ् उपसर्गदीर्घत्वम्] = अधिकार q. v.; स्वागतं<BR> स्वानधीकारानवलम्ब्य Ku. 2. 18; सर्वाकरेष्वधीकारः Ms. 11. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीन|अधीनः
अधीन <i>a.</i> [अधि-ख P. V. 4. 7; अधिगतः इनं प्रभुं वा]<BR> Subject to, subservient, dependent on; usually in comp.; स्थाने प्राणाः<BR> कामिनां दूत्यधीनाः M. 3. 14; त्वदधीनं खलु देहिनां सुखम् Ku. 4. 10;<BR> इक्ष्वाकूणां दुरापेऽर्थे त्वदधीना हि सिद्धयः R. 1. 72; केन निमित्तेन<BR> भवदधीनो जातः Dk. 7 consigned to your care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीमन्थ|अधीमंथ
अधीमन्थ = अधिमन्थ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीर|अधीरः
अधीर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bold, timid.<BR>—2 Confused, lacking self-command, excited, excitable.<BR>—3 Fitful, capricious.<BR>—4 Unsteady, not fixed, tremulous, rolling; ˚विप्रेक्षितमायताक्ष्याः<BR> Ku. 1. 46; ˚लोचनः Śi. 1. 53; ˚तडिन्नयना 6. 25.<BR>—5 Querulous, foolish, weak-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीरा
अधीर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Lightning.<BR>—2 A capricious or quarrelsome mistress; see under नायिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीवासः|अधीवास
अधीवासः [वस् अच्छादने करणे घञ्] A long coat or mantle covering<BR> the whole person (उपरिष्टादावरकं वासः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीशः|अधीश
अधीशः [अधिकः ईशः] Lord, supreme lord or master, sovereign<BR> ruler, अङ्ग˚, मृग˚, मनुज˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश्वरः|अधीश्वर
अधीश्वरः [अधिकः ईश्वरः]<BR>—1 A supreme lord or an employer.<BR>—2 An Arhat (among Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीष्ट|अधीष्टः
अधीष्ट <i>a.</i> [अधि-इष् दिवादि-क्त] Honorary, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीष्टः|अधीष्ट
अधीष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} [भावे-क्त] Honorary office or duty; one of the cases<BR> in which लिड् or the Potential may be used; P. III. 3. 161 (अधीष्टः<BR> = सत्कारपूर्वको व्यापारः Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुना
अधुना <i>ind.</i> [अस्मिन् काले; इदमः इदंशब्दस्य सप्तम्यन्तात्कालवाचिनः<BR> स्वार्थे अधुनाप्रत्ययः स्यात् P. V. 3. 17. Sk.] Now, at this time; प्रमदानामधुना<BR> विडम्बना Ku. 4. 12. अधुना हरणे कुचौ यतेते दयिते ते करिशावकुम्भलक्ष्म्याः Bv. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुनातन|अधुनातनं
अधुनातन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अधुना भवार्थे टपुल् तुट्च] Belonging to the<BR> present times, modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुर
अधुर <i>a.</i> [नास्ति धूः चिन्ताभारो वा यस्य] Not laden, free from<BR> the burden of cares &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधूः
अधुर + .{@-धूः@} [न˚ त˚] Absence of burden or cares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधूमकः|अधूमक
अधूमकः [न˚ ब˚] ‘Smokeless’, burning or blazing fire.<BR> अङ्गुष्टमात्रः पुरुषो ज्योतिरिवाधूमकः Ken. 2. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृत|अधृतः
अधृत <i>a.</i> Not held or controlled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृतः|अधृत
अधृत + .{@-तः@} One of the 1000 names of Viṣṇu (सर्वेषां धारकत्वेन<BR> केनापि न धृतः स्वप्रतिष्ठितः परमेश्वरः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृतिः|अधृति
अधृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Want of firmness or control, looseness.<BR>—2 Incontinence.<BR>—3 Unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अधृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bold, modest, shy.<BR>—2 invincible, irresistible; unhurt; हूतासो वसवोऽघृष्टाः Rv. 6. 50. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्य|अधृष्यः
अधृष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invincible, unassailable; मनसाप्यधृष्यम् Ku. 3. 51 unassailable<BR> even in thought; unapproachable (opp. अभिगम्य); अधृष्यश्चाभिगम्यश्च<BR> यादोरत्नैरिवार्णवः R. 1. 16.<BR>—2 Modest, shy.<BR>—3 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0068-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्या
अधृष्या N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधेनु|अधेनुः
अधेनु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] (A cow) not yielding milk. अधेनुं<BR> दस्रा स्तर्यं विषक्ताम् Rv. 1. 117. 20; not nourishing अधेन्वा चरति<BR> मायया Rv. 10. 71. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य|अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य्यः
अधैर्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Without self-possession, courage<BR> &c., swayed by excitement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्यम्
अधैर्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Absence of courage, firmness or control; excitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्ष
अधोऽक्ष, अधोऽक्षज, अधोंऽशुक See under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षज|अधोक्षजः
अधोऽक्ष, अधोऽक्षज, अधोंऽशुक See under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोंशुक|अधोंशुकं
अधोऽक्ष, अधोऽक्षज, अधोंऽशुक See under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्ष|अध्यक्षः
अध्यक्ष <i>a.</i> [अधिगतः अक्षम् इन्द्रियं व्यवहारं वा]<BR>—1 Perceptible to the senses, visible; यैरध्यक्षैरथ निजसखं नीरदं<BR> स्मारयद्भिः Bv. 4. 17.<BR>—2 One who exercises supervision, presiding over. cf. प्रत्यक्षेऽधिकृतेऽध्यक्षः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षः|अध्यक्ष
अध्यक्ष + .{@-क्षः@}<BR>—1 A superintendent, president, head, lord, master, controller, ruler.<BR> ततो राज्ञः कलत्राणि भ्रातॄणां चास्य सर्वतः । वाहनेषु समारोप्य अध्यक्षाः<BR> प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥ Mb. 9. 29. 94. मयाऽध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिः सूयते सचराचरम्<BR> Bg. 9. 10; यदध्यक्षेण जगतां वयमारोपितास्त्वया Ku. 6. 17; इत्यध्यक्षप्रचारो<BR> द्वितीयमधिकरणम् । Kau. A. 2 oft. in comp.; गज˚, सेना˚, ग्राम˚, द्वार˚.<BR>—2 An eye-witness (Ved.)<BR>—3 N. of a plant (क्षीरिका) Mimusops Kauki. (Mar. दुधी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षरम्
अध्यक्षरम् <i>ind.</i> On the subject of syllables; above all syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षरम्
अध्यक्षरम् + .{@-रम्@} The mystic syllable ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यग्नि
अध्यग्नि <i>ind.</i> [अग्नौ अग्निसमीपे वा] Over, by or near the nuptial<BR> fire. <i>n.</i> (-ग्नि) One of the six kinds of स्त्रीधन (womanʼs property)<BR> mentioned in Ms. 9. 194 (अध्यग्न्यध्यावाहनिकं दत्तं च प्रीतिकर्मणि ।<BR> भ्रातृमातृपितृप्राप्तं षड्विधं स्त्रीधनं स्मृतम् ॥); a gift made to<BR> a woman at the time of marriage: विवाहकाले यत्स्त्रीभ्यो दीयते ह्यग्निसन्निधौ ।<BR> तदध्यग्निकृतं सद्भिः स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम् ॥ So अध्यग्निकृतम्<BR> अध्यग्न्युपागतम्; पितृमातृपतिभ्रातृदत्तमध्यग्न्युपागतम् । आधिवेदनिकाद्यं<BR> च स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यञ्च्|अध्यंच्
अध्यञ्च् [अधि -अञ्च्-क्विन्]<BR>—1 Tending upwards; superior, eminent; अध्यङ् शस्त्रभृतां रामः । Bk. 5. 36.<BR>—2 One who obtains or acquires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यण्डा|अध्यंडा
अध्यण्डा [अधिकमण्डमिव बीजं यस्याः सा] Names of two plants<BR> (अजशृङ्गी) Carpopogon Pruriens (Mar. मेढशिंगी), and भूम्यामलकी<BR> Flacourtia Cataphracta (Mar. भुई आंवळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधि
अध्यधि <i>ind.</i> On high (acc.); ˚धि लोकम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधिक्षेपः|अध्यधिक्षेप
अध्यधिक्षेपः [अधिकः अधिक्षेपः] Excessive abuse or censure, gross<BR> abuse; गुरूणामध्यधिक्षेपो वेदनिन्दा सुहृद्वधः । ब्रह्महत्यासमं ज्ञेयमधीतस्य<BR> च नाशनम् ॥ Y. 3. 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधीन
अध्यधीन <i>a.</i> [आधिक्येन अधीनः] Completely subject or dependent,<BR> as a slave; नाध्यधीनो न वक्तव्यो न दस्युर्न विकर्मकृत् । Ms. 8. 66<BR> (Kull. अत्यन्तपरतन्त्रो गर्भदासः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यय|अध्ययः
अध्यय, अध्ययनम् &c. See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनम्
अध्यय, अध्ययनम् &c. See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्ध|अध्यर्धः
अध्यर्ध <i>a.</i> [अधिकमर्धं यस्य] Having an additional half;<BR> अध्यर्धयोजनं गत्वा सरय्वा दक्षिणे तटे Rām. 1. 22. 11; Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 1.<BR> एकाधिकं हरेज्ज्येष्ठः पुत्रोऽध्यर्धं ततोऽनुजः Ms. 9. 117;<BR> शतमध्यर्धमायता Mb., i. e. 150; ˚योजनशतात् Pt. 2. 18. (in<BR> comp. with a following noun) Amounting to or worth one and a half; ˚कंस<BR> amounting to one<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">Page0069-2</a>]<BR> and a half Kaṃsa; so ˚काकिणीक, कार्षापण-णिक, ˚खारीक, ˚पण्य, ˚पाद्य,<BR> ˚प्रतिक, ˚भाष्य, ˚विंशतिकीन, ˚शत, -त्य, ˚श(शा)तमान, ˚शाण, ˚शाण्य,<BR> ˚शूर्प, ˚सहस्त्र, ˚सौवर्ण &c. (P. V. 1. 28-35.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्धः|अध्यर्ध
अध्यर्ध + .{@-र्धः@} Wind (यदस्मिन इदं सर्वम् अध्यार्ध्नोत् अधिकमवर्धयत्<BR> तेन अध्यर्धः पवनः इति स्थितम् Bṛ. Up.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्बुदम्
अध्यर्बुदम् [अधिकम् or अधिजातम् अर्बुदम्] A tumour, goitre;<BR> यज्जायतेऽन्यत्खलु पूर्वजाते ज्ञेयं तदध्यर्बुदमर्बुदज्ञैः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसो
अध्यवसो €4 P.<BR>—1 To determine, resolve; कथमिदानीं दुर्जनवचनादेवम् अध्यवसितं<BR> देवेन U. 1; अदुर्लभं मरणमध्यवसितम् K. 171; किमध्यवस्यन्ति<BR> गुरवः Ve. 1; अभिधातुमध्यवससौ न गिरा Śi. 9. 76; resolve or mean to do.<BR>—2 To attempt, exert, undertake; मा साहसम् अध्यवस्यः Dk. 123; व्रतं<BR> दुष्करमध्यवसितम् H. 1.<BR>—3 To grapple with.<BR>—4 To conceive, apprehend, think; अकार्यं कार्यवदध्यवस्य Dk. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसानम्
अध्यवसानम् [भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Effort, determination &c. See अध्यवसाय.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) Identification of two things (प्रकृत and अप्रकृत)<BR> in such a manner that the one is completely absorbed into the other; निगीर्याध्यवसानं<BR> तु प्रकृतस्य परेण यत् K. P. 10; on such identification is founded<BR> the figure called अतिशयोक्ति, and the लक्षणा called साध्यवसाना. See K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायः|अध्यवसाय
अध्यवसायः<BR>—1 An attempt, effort, exertion; न स्वल्पमप्यध्यवसायभीरोः करोति<BR> विज्ञाननिधिर्गुणं हि H. 1, v. l.; ˚सहचरेषु साहसेषु Dk. 161.<BR>—2 Determination, resolution; mental effort or apprehension; संभावनं<BR> नाम अस्तित्वाध्यवसायः P. VI. 2. 21. cf. also प्रतिविषयाध्यवसायो<BR> दृष्टम् । Sāṅ. K. 5.<BR>—3 Perseverance, diligence, energy, constancy; तत्कोऽयं पदे पदे महाननध्यवसायः<BR> U. 4 absence of energy or resolution, drooping of spirits; (with महानध्यवसायः<BR> as the reading, the meaning would be ‘why this effort on your part <i>i. e.</i> to determine whether you should go or not, hesitation’<BR>.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायिन्
अध्यवसायिन् <i>a.</i> [सो-णिनि] Attempting; resolute, persevering, energetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसित
अध्यवसित <i>p. p.</i> Attempted, mentally apprehended, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसिन्
अध्यवसिन् <i>a.</i> One who observes a vow, धर्माश्रमेऽध्यवसिनां<BR> ब्राह्मणानां युधिष्टिरः Mb. 12. 64. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवहननम्
अध्यवहननम् [अधि उपरि अवहननम्] Beating again what is being<BR> threshed and peeled (पूर्वावघातेन वितुषीकरणेऽपि पुनरवघातः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशनम्
अध्यशनम् [अधिकमशनम्] Excessive eating, eating again before<BR> the last meal is digested; साजीर्णे भुज्यते यत्तु तदध्यशनमुच्यते Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्थि
अध्यस्थि <i>n.</i> [अधिरूढमस्थि] A bone growing over another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्
अध्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To place upon another, add or append to.<BR>—2 (In Phil) To attribute or ascribe falsely, attribute the nature of<BR> one thing to another; सर्वो हि पुरोऽवस्थिते विषये विषयान्तरमध्यस्यति,<BR> बाह्यधर्मानात्मन्यध्यस्यति Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0069-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्त|अध्यस्तं
अध्यस्त <i>p. p.</i> [अस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Placed upon or over.<BR>—2 Attributed, wrongly ascribed or supposed; as शुक्तौ रजतमध्यस्तम्,<BR> ब्रह्मणि जगदध्यस्तम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासः|अध्यास
अध्यासः [अस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 False attribution, wrong supposition (मिथ्याज्ञानम्, अतस्मिस्तद्बुद्धिः<BR> or अयथार्थानुभवः); स्मृतिरूपः परत्र पूर्वदृष्टावभासः; for<BR> full explanation see Ś. B. 8-22 and अध्यारोप also.<BR>—2 An appendage.<BR>—3 Putting down upon; पादाध्यासे शतं दमः Y. 2. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याक्रम्
अध्याक्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To fix upon, to occupy.<BR>—2 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याक्रान्त
अध्याक्रान्त <i>a.</i> Taken possession of, occupied; ˚ता वसतिरमुना Ś. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याचरित
अध्याचरित <i>a.</i> used शय्यासनेऽध्याचरिते श्रेयसा न समाविशेत् Ms. 2. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्म
अध्यात्म <i>a.</i> [आत्मनः संबद्धं, आत्मनि अधिकृतं वा] Belonging<BR> to self or person; concerning an individual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मम्
अध्यात्म + .{@-त्मम्@} <i>ind.</i> [आत्मानमधिकृत्य] Concerning self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मम्
अध्यात्म + .{@-त्मम्@} The supreme spirit (manifested as the individual self) or<BR> the relation between the supreme and the individual soul; अक्षरं ब्रह्म<BR> परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते Bg. 8. 3 (स्वस्यैव ब्रह्मण एवांशतया<BR> जीवस्वरूपेण भावो भवनं स एव आत्मानं देहमधिकृत्य भोक्तृत्वेन वर्तमानोऽध्यात्मशब्देनोच्यते<BR> Śrīdhara) ‘Brahman is the supreme, the indestructible; its manifestation (as an individual self) is अध्यात्म’<BR> -Telangʼs Bhagavadgītā;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मन्
अध्यात्म + .{@-त्मन्@}<BR>—1 Egotism; कर्माण्यध्यात्मना रुद्रे यदहं ममता क्रिया Bhāg. 7. 12. 29.<BR>—2 Wind; स्पर्शमध्यात्मनि त्वचम् Bhāg. 7. 12. 27. ˚चेतसा Bg. 3. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्यात्मज्ञानम्, अध्यात्मविद्या, अध्यात्मदृश्, अध्यात्मविद्, अध्यात्मयोगः, अध्यात्मरति, अध्यात्मरामायणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मज्ञानम्
अध्यात्म + -ज्ञानम्, -विद्या knowledge of the supreme spirit or आत्मन्, theosophical<BR> or metaphysical knowledge (the doctrines taught by the Upaniṣads &c.);<BR> ˚विद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम् Bg. 10. 32 (अध्यात्मविद्या न्यायवैशोषिकमते<BR> देहभिन्नत्वेन, सांख्यादिमते प्रकृतिभिन्नत्वेन आत्मनः स्वरूपादिप्रतिपादिका,<BR> वेदान्तिमते तु ब्रह्माभिन्नत्वेन इति भेदः; सर्वेषां मतेऽपि आत्मतत्त्वज्ञानरूपत्वात्तस्या<BR> अध्यात्मविद्यात्वम्.). त्रयी विग्रहवत्येव सममध्यात्मविद्यया M. 1. 14;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मविद्या
अध्यात्म + -ज्ञानम्, -विद्या knowledge of the supreme spirit or आत्मन्, theosophical<BR> or metaphysical knowledge (the doctrines taught by the Upaniṣads &c.);<BR> ˚विद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम् Bg. 10. 32 (अध्यात्मविद्या न्यायवैशोषिकमते<BR> देहभिन्नत्वेन, सांख्यादिमते प्रकृतिभिन्नत्वेन आत्मनः स्वरूपादिप्रतिपादिका,<BR> वेदान्तिमते तु ब्रह्माभिन्नत्वेन इति भेदः; सर्वेषां मतेऽपि आत्मतत्त्वज्ञानरूपत्वात्तस्या<BR> अध्यात्मविद्यात्वम्.). त्रयी विग्रहवत्येव सममध्यात्मविद्यया M. 1. 14;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मदृश्
अध्यात्म + -दृश्, -विद् <i>n.</i> [अध्यात्मं पश्यति वेत्ति वा] one proficient<BR> in this knowledge; न ह्यनध्यात्मवित्कश्चित् क्रियाफलमुपाश्नुते Ms. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मविद्
अध्यात्म + -दृश्, -विद् <i>n.</i> [अध्यात्मं पश्यति वेत्ति वा] one proficient<BR> in this knowledge; न ह्यनध्यात्मवित्कश्चित् क्रियाफलमुपाश्नुते Ms. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मयोगः|अध्यात्मयोग
अध्यात्म + -योगः [आत्मानं क्षेत्रज्ञमधिकृत्य योगः] concentration of<BR> the mind on the Ātman drawing it off from all objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मरति
अध्यात्म + -रति <i>a.</i> [स˚ ब˚] one who delights in the contemplation<BR> of the supreme spirit; अध्यात्मरतिरासीनो निरपेक्षो निरामिषः । आत्मनैव<BR> सहायेन सुखार्थी विचरेदिह ॥ Ms. 6. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मरामायणम्
अध्यात्म + -रामायणम् N. of a Rāmāyaṇa which treats of the relation between<BR> the supreme and the individual soul, while it narrates Rāmaʼs story.<BR> It forms part of the Brahmāṇḍa Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मिक
अध्यात्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to अध्यात्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापक|अध्यापकः
अध्यापक, -पनम्, अध्याय<BR> See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापनम्
अध्यापक, -पनम्, अध्याय<BR> See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्यापक, -पनम्, अध्याय<BR> See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारुह्
अध्यारुह् €1 P. —1 to ascend, mount; विष्णुपदं द्वितीयमध्यारुरोहेव<BR> रजश्छलेन R. 16. 28; (fig.) to gain ascendancy over, domineer or lord<BR> it over; लतेव विटपकानध्यारोहति K. 105; बुद्धिहीनोऽत्युच्छ्रितोऽपि<BR> भूभृत् परैरध्यारुह्यमाणमात्मानं न चेतयते Dk. 154. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> [-रोहयति]<BR>—1 To cause to ascend, mount<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">Page0070-2</a>]<BR> or sit in.<BR>—2 (रोपयति)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To place one in, entrust or appoint to; to cause, produce, bring<BR> about; कुसुमायुधस्य दुर्जयतामध्यारोपयन्ती K. 148; कस्य न बन्धुत्वमध्यारोपयसि 202.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To attribute falsely; दोषानपि गुणपक्षमध्यारोपयद्भिः K. 108<BR> (falsely) representing even vices as virtues.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To overdo, exaggerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारूढ|अध्यारूढः
अध्यारूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mounted, ascended.<BR>—2 Raised above, elevated.<BR>—3 Above, superior to, more than (with instr.); below, inferior; ततोऽध्यारूढानां<BR> पदमसुजनद्वेषजननम् Mu. 5. 12 of those in high office; आयुधपरिग्रहं<BR> यावदध्यारूढो दुर्योगः U. 6 my insolence went the length of taking up arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपः|अध्यारोप
अध्यारोपः<BR>—1 Raising, elevating &c.<BR>—2 (In Vedānta Phil.) Act of attributing falsely or through mistake;<BR> erroneously attributing the properties of one thing to another; considering<BR> through mistake a rope (which is not really a serpent) to be a serpent,<BR> or considering Brahman (which is not really the material world) to be<BR> the material world; असर्पभूतरज्जौ सर्पारोपवत्, अजगद्रूपे ब्रह्मणि<BR> जगद्रूपारोपवत्, वस्तुनि अवस्त्वारोपोऽध्यारोपः Vedāntasāra.<BR>—3 Erroneous knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपणम्
अध्यारोपणम्<BR>—1 Raising &c.; अलीक˚ K. 222, 108.<BR>—2 Sowing (seed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपित
अध्यारोपित <i>p. p.</i> Falsely attributed or supposed; hyperbolical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावापः|अध्यावाप
अध्यावापः [अधि-आ-वप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Act of sowing or scattering (seed &c.)<BR>—2 [आधारे घञ्] A field wherein seed &c. is sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिकम्
अध्यावाहनिकम् [अध्यावाहनं पितृगृहात्पतिगृहगमनम्, तत्काले लब्धम्;<BR> लब्धार्थे ठन्] One of the six kinds of स्त्रीधन or womanʼs property,<BR> the property which she receives when leaving her fatherʼs house for her<BR> husbandʼs; Ms. 9. 194. यत् पुनर्लभते नारी नीयमाना तु पैतृकात् (गृहात्) ।<BR> अध्यावाहनिकं नाम स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याशयः|अध्याशय
अध्याशयः (उत्कृष्टः आशयः कर्णिकाख्यः) the pericarp; अध्याशयो<BR> वा स्फुटपुण्डरीकं पुराधिराजं तदलञ्चकार । Bu. C. 1. 9, the commentator<BR> explains the word also as ‘Jīva’ अधि प्रधानभूत आशेते निवसति शरीर<BR> इत्यध्याशयो जीवः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास्
अध्यास् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 ——(<i>a</i>) To lie down, settle upon; occupy, dwell in (as a seat or habitation);<BR> seat oneself in or upon, enter upon, get into (as a path &c.) (with acc.<BR> of place); त्वरिततरमध्यास्यतामियं वनस्थली K. 28, 36, 40; पर्णशालामध्यास्य<BR> R. 1. 95; द्वितीयमाश्रममध्यासितुं समयः V. 5; द्वारदेशमध्यास्ते<BR> Dk. 3 is waiting at the door; R. 2. 17, 4. 74, 6. 10, 12. 85, 13. 22, 76, 15. 93;<BR> Me. 78; Bk. 1. 5; Ms. 7. 77; अये सिंहासनमध्यास्ते वृषलः<BR> Mu. 3; भगवत्या प्राश्निकपदमध्यासितव्यम् M. 1.<BR> occupy the seat of judge, accept the office of judge.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To take possession of, grasp, seize; धेन्वा तदध्यासितकातराक्ष्या<BR> R. 2. 52 with eyes tremulous on account of her being seized by him (अध्यासितम् = आक्रमणम्).<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To resort to,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">Page0071-1</a>]<BR> inhabit; यदध्यासितमर्हद्भिस्तद्धि तीर्थं प्रचक्षते Ku. 6. 56.<BR>—2 To live in conjugal relation; cohabit with.<BR>—3 To be directed or fixed upon.<BR>—4 To rule, govern, influence; affect, concern (mostly Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To cause one to sit down upon; भवन्तमध्यासयन्नासनम् Bk. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0070-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासनम्
अध्यासनम्<BR>—1 Sitting down upon, occupying, presiding over.<BR>—2 A seat, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासित
अध्यासित <i>a.</i> Seated down, upon, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासितम्
अध्यासित + .{@-तम्@} Sitting upon; धेन्वा तदध्यासितकातराक्ष्या निरीक्ष्यमाणः R. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासः|अध्यास
अध्यासः See under अध्यस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहारः|अध्याहार
अध्याहारः A mode of interpreting a sentence. According to this mode,<BR> an incomplete sentence is made to yield complete sense by supplying some<BR> extra word or words therein. अध्याहार should be clearly distinguished<BR> from अनुषङ्ग which also is a mode of interpreting an incomplete sentence;<BR> परिपूर्णमेवेदं वाक्यं नाध्याहारमर्हति विप्रलम्भकर्तृकम् ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 10<BR> (see अनुषङ्ग). cf. also अपरिपूर्णं यद् वाक्यं<BR> तदध्याहारेण वा पूर्येत व्यवहितकल्पनया वा । तत्राध्याहाराद् व्यवहितकल्पना<BR> ज्यायसी । अध्याहारे हि अश्रुतः कल्प्येत । इतरत्र श्रुतेन सम्बन्धः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 7. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहारः|अध्याहार
अध्याहारः, -हरणम्<BR>—1 Supplying an ellipsis (आकाङ्क्षाविषयपदानुसंधानम्).<BR>—2 Arguing; inferring; new supposition; inference or conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरणम्
अध्याहारः, -हरणम्<BR>—1 Supplying an ellipsis (आकाङ्क्षाविषयपदानुसंधानम्).<BR>—2 Arguing; inferring; new supposition; inference or conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित <i>a.</i> Inhabited, occupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषिते
अध्युषिते <i>ind.</i> At day-break; उवाच राजन्संग्रामेऽध्युषिते पर्युपस्थिते Mb. 8. 36. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट|अध्युष्टः
अध्युष्ट <i>a.</i> (Ety. ?) Coiled up three and a half times;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्टवलयः|अध्युष्टवलय
अध्युष्ट + ˚वलयः<BR> a snake forming a ring coiled up three and a half times; अवाप्य स्वां<BR> भूमिं भुजगनिभमध्युष्टवलयं स्वमात्मानं कृत्वा Ā. L. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट्रः|अध्युष्ट्र
अध्युष्ट्रः [अधिगतः उष्ट्रं वाहनत्वेन] A carriage drawn or borne by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्यूढ <i>a.</i> [अधि उपरि ऊढः]<BR>—1 Raised, exalted, elevated, hanging over. एतस्यामृच्यध्यूढँ साम तस्मादृच्यध्यूढँ<BR> साम गीयते Ch. Up. 1. 6. 1.<BR>—2 Abundant, increased, copious.<BR>—3 Rich, affluent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढः|अध्यूढ
अध्यूढ + .{@-ढः@}<BR>—1 Śiva.<BR>—2 The son of a woman pregnant before marriage; अध्यूढश्च तथाऽपरः Mb. 13. 49. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढा
अध्यूढ + .{@-ढा@} A wife whose husband has married another wife and thus superseded<BR> her (= अधिविन्ना q. v.). अध्यूढायाश्च यद् दुःखं साक्षिभिर्विहितस्य<BR> च Mb. 2. 68. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूध्नी
अध्यूध्नी [अधिकम् ऊधो यस्याः अनङ् ङीप् च]<BR>—1 A cow with full and fat udders.<BR>—2 The vessel (in the body) above the udder or above the scrotum; perhaps urethra (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूह्
अध्यूह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To overlay, place on or upon.<BR>—2 To raise above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूहनम्
अध्यूहनम् Putting of a layer (of ashes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषणम्
अध्येषणम् [अधि-इष् प्रैरणे-ल्युट्] Causing one to do a thing, especially<BR> a preceptor &c. as an honorific duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषणा
अध्येषणम् + .{@-णा@} [अधिका एषणा प्रार्थना] Solicitation, entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रि
अध्रि <i>a.</i> [न-धृ-कि] Not restrained, irresistible.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्रिगु, अध्रिगू, अध्रिगुः, अध्रिपुष्पलिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रिगु|अध्रिगुः
अध्रि + -गु, -गू <i>a.</i> [अधि-गम्-कू-डित् ऊङादेशो वा] of irresistible<BR> motion or course (अधृतगमन), impetuous; यदभ्रिगावो अंध्रिगू इदा<BR> चिदह्नो अश्विना Rv. 8. 22. 11 also तुभ्यं श्चोतन्ति अध्रिगो Ait. Br. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रिगू
अध्रि + -गु, -गू <i>a.</i> [अधि-गम्-कू-डित् ऊङादेशो वा] of irresistible<BR> motion or course (अधृतगमन), impetuous; यदभ्रिगावो अंध्रिगू इदा<BR> चिदह्नो अश्विना Rv. 8. 22. 11 also तुभ्यं श्चोतन्ति अध्रिगो Ait. Br. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रिगुः|अध्रिगु
अध्रि + -गुः N. of a heavenly killer of sacrificial victims, or the name<BR> formula itself ending with an invocation of Agni. -ज <i>a.</i> [अध्रिं<BR> जनयति, जन्-ड] making irresistible. इति चिन्मन्युमध्रिजः Rv. 5. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रिपुष्पलिका
अध्रि + -पुष्पलिका the betelnut plant. (Mar. पानबेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रियमाण
अध्रियमाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not held, not to be got hold of; not forthcoming.<BR>—2 Not surviving, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अध्रुव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uncertain, doubtful.<BR>—2 Unsteady, moving, not fixed or permanent; स्वाङ्गेऽध्रुवे P. III. 4. 54;<BR> separable (which can be severed or detached without fatal or disastrous<BR> effects) (येन विना न जीवनं सोऽध्रुवः Sk.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुवम्
अध्रुव + .{@-वम्@} An uncertainty; यो ध्रुवाणि परित्यज्य अध्रुवाणि निषेवते ।<BR> ध्रुवाणि तस्य नश्यन्ति अध्रुवं नष्टमेव च H. 1. 184. cf. the English<BR> phrase ‘A bird in the hand is worth two in the bush’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुषः|अध्रुष
अध्रुषः Quinsy; a kind of disease attended with fever arising from<BR> the affection of blood; शोथः स्थूलस्तोददाहप्रकाशो रक्ताज्ज्ञेयः सोऽध्रुषो<BR> रुग्ज्वराढ्यः Suśr. (Mar. गळसटें, घटसर्प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्
अध्वन् <i>m.</i> [अत्ति बलं; अद्-क्वनिप् धादेशः Uṇ. 4. 115; perhaps<BR> from अत् also]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A way, road; passage, orbit (of planets &c.); मुक्ताध्वानं ये<BR> लङ्घयेयुर्भवन्तम् Me. 54.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Distance, space (traversed or to be traversed); पञ्चदशयोजनमात्रमध्वानं<BR> जगाम K. 119, 120; क्रियत्यध्वनि सा उज्जयिनी 207; Dk. 13; अपि<BR> लङ्घितमध्वानं बुबुधे न बुधोपमः R. 1. 47; उल्लङ्घिताध्वा Me. 45;<BR> कालाध्वनोरत्यन्तसंयोगे &c.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Journey, travel, course, march; नैकः प्रपद्येताध्वानम् Ms. 4. 60<BR> undertake a journey; अध्वसु त्रिषु विसृष्टमैथिलः R. 11. 57 after<BR> three marches; परिक्लान्तः किलाध्वना Ki. 11. 2 way-worn; अध्वश्रमपरिगतम्<BR> Me. 17, 40; अध्वा वर्णकंफस्थौल्यसौकुमार्यविनाशनः Suśr.<BR>—2 A recension of the Vedas and the school upholding it (शाखा, अवयव)<BR> एकविंशत्यध्वयुक्तमृग्वेदमृषयो विदुः । सहस्राध्वा सामवेदो यजुरेकशताध्वकम्<BR> ॥ अध्वा देवगतिः शाखा इति पर्यायवाचकाः ।<BR>—3 Time (Kāla), time personified, (being the eater of all) दुर्मरं<BR> पुरुषेणेह मन्ये ह्यध्वन्यनागते Mb. 14. 80. 24.<BR>—4 Air; sky, atmosphere.<BR>—5 Place. प्रस्थितं दीर्घमध्वानं स्वबन्धुमिव बान्धवाः Rām. 5. 1. 45.<BR>—6 Means, resource; method.<BR>—7 Attack (अधिकदुरारोहणम्). अध्वन् is changed to अध्व after<BR> prepositions; प्राध्वः, व्यध्वः &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्वातिः, अध्वाधिपः, अध्वेशः, अध्वायनम्, अध्वगः, अध्वगत्, अध्वगत्यन्तः, अध्वगन्तव्यः, अध्वजा, अध्वपतिः, अध्वरथः, अध्वशल्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वातिः|अध्वाति
अध्वन् + -अतिः [अध्वानमतति, अत्-इ]<BR>—1 a traveller. —2 an intelligent person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वाधिपः|अध्वाधिप
अध्वन् + -अधिपः, -ईशः [ष˚ त˚] an officer in charge of the public roads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वेशः|अध्वेश
अध्वन् + -अधिपः, -ईशः [ष˚ त˚] an officer in charge of the public roads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वायनम्
अध्वन् + -अयनम् [अध्वन्ययनम्] journey, travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगः|अध्वग
अध्वन् + -गः —1 one who travels; a traveller, way-farer; Av. 13. 1. 36.<BR> सन्तानकतरुच्छायासुप्तविद्याधराध्वगम् Ku. 6. 46 (˚गामिन्).<BR>—2 a camel.<BR>—3 a mule.<BR>—4 the sun;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगः|अध्वग
अध्वन् + -गः + ˚भोग्यः N. of a tree, Spondias Mangifera (आम्रातकवृक्ष)<BR> अध्वगैः अयत्नलभ्यफलत्वात् भोग्यः (Mar. आंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगा
अध्वन् + -गः + .({@-गा@}) the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगत्
अध्वन् + -गत् <i>m.</i> [अध्वानं गच्छति; गम्-क्विप् P. VI. 4. 40] a traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगत्यन्तः|अध्वगत्यन्त
अध्वन् + -गत्यन्तः, -गन्तव्यः [ष˚ त˚] measure of length applicable<BR> to roads; कालभावाध्वगन्तव्यः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">Page0072-1</a>]<BR> Mbh. Vārt. on P. I. 4. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगन्तव्यः|अध्वगन्तव्य
अध्वन् + -गत्यन्तः, -गन्तव्यः [ष˚ त˚] measure of length applicable<BR> to roads; कालभावाध्वगन्तव्यः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">Page0072-1</a>]<BR> Mbh. Vārt. on P. I. 4. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0071-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वजा
अध्वन् + -जा [अध्वनि जायते; जन्-ड] A plant (स्वर्णुली or स्वर्णपुष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वपतिः|अध्वपति
अध्वन् + -पतिः<BR>—1 the sun (दिवैव पथिकानां गमनात् रात्रौ च गमननिषेधात् सूर्यस्य<BR> अध्वपालकत्वम् or अध्वनः आकाशस्य पतिः).<BR>—2 inspector of the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरथः|अध्वरथ
अध्वन् + -रथः [अध्वने हितः पर्याप्तो रथः शाक˚ त˚]<BR>—1 a travelling coach.<BR>—2 [अध्वैव रथो यस्य] a messenger skilled in travelling (पथि प्रज्ञो दूतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वशल्यः|अध्वशल्य
अध्वन् + -शल्यः [अध्वनि शल्यमिव आचरतीति क्विपच् Tv.] N. of a tree<BR> (अपामार्ग) (अध्वगानां पादवस्त्रादौ शल्यवद्वेधकारकत्वात् तथात्वम्)<BR> (Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीन|अध्वनीनः
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य <i>a.</i> [अध्वानम् अलं गच्छति; अध्वन्-ख-यत् वा;<BR> अध्वनो यत्खौ P. V. 2. 16] Able to undertake a journey,<BR> speeding on a journey; क्षिप्रं ततोऽध्वन्यतुरङ्गयायी Bk. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्य|अध्वन्यः
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य <i>a.</i> [अध्वानम् अलं गच्छति; अध्वन्-ख-यत् वा;<BR> अध्वनो यत्खौ P. V. 2. 16] Able to undertake a journey,<BR> speeding on a journey; क्षिप्रं ततोऽध्वन्यतुरङ्गयायी Bk. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीनः|अध्वनीन
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य + .{@-नः, -न्यः@} A traveller going fast, way-farer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्यः|अध्वन्य
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य + .{@-नः, -न्यः@} A traveller going fast, way-farer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर|अध्वरः
अध्वर <i>a.</i> [न ध्वरति कुटिलो न भवति ध्वृ-अच्, न˚ त˚;<BR> ध्वरतिर्हिंसाकर्मा तत्प्रतिषेधो निपातः अहिंस्रः Nir.]<BR>—1 Not crooked, not broken, uninterrupted; इमं यज्ञमवतामध्वरं<BR> नः Yv. 27. 17 (अध्वरम् = अकुटिलं शास्त्रोक्तम्).<BR>—2 Intent, attentive.<BR>—3 Durable, sound.<BR>—4 Not injuring; ततोऽध्वरजटः स्थाणुर्वेदाध्वरपतिः शिवः Mb. 12. 256. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरः|अध्वर
अध्वर + .{@-रः@} [अध्वानं सत्पथं राति ददाति फलत्वेन, रा-क] A sacrifice,<BR> a religious ceremony; also a Soma sacrifice; तमध्वरे विश्वजिति R. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरः|अध्वर
अध्वर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Sky or air (आकाश).<BR>—2 The second of the 8 Vasus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्वरकल्पा, अध्वरकाण्डम्, अध्वरग, अध्वरदीक्षणीया, अध्वरमीमांसा, अध्वरश्रीः, अध्वरसमिष्टयजुः, अध्वरस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरम्
अध्वर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Sky or air (आकाश).<BR>—2 The second of the 8 Vasus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्वरकल्पा, अध्वरकाण्डम्, अध्वरग, अध्वरदीक्षणीया, अध्वरमीमांसा, अध्वरश्रीः, अध्वरसमिष्टयजुः, अध्वरस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरकल्पा
अध्वर + -कल्पा an optional sacrifice (काम्येष्टि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरकाण्डम्
अध्वर + -काण्डम् [ष˚ त˚] part of the शतपथब्राह्मण which<BR> treats of sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरग
अध्वर + -ग [अध्वरं गच्छति] intended for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरदीक्षणीया
अध्वर + -दीक्षणीया [ष˚ त˚] consecration connected with an Adhvara;<BR> so ˚प्रायश्चित्तिः an expiation &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरमीमांसा
अध्वर + -मीमांसा [ष˚ त˚] N. of Jaiminiʼs Pūrvamīmāṃsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरश्रीः
अध्वर + -श्रीः [ष˚ त˚] glory of the Adhvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरसमिष्टयजुः
अध्वर + -समिष्टयजुः <i>n.</i> N. of an aggregate of libations connected<BR> with a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरस्थ
अध्वर + -स्थ <i>a.</i> Engaged in a sacrifice; य उदृचि यज्ञे अध्वरेष्टाः ।<BR> Rv. 10. 77. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरीयति
अध्वरीयति, अध्वर्यति Den. P. To desire to have a sacrifice<BR> performed; or to perform one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्यति
अध्वरीयति, अध्वर्यति Den. P. To desire to have a sacrifice<BR> performed; or to perform one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्युः [अध्वरमधीते Nir.; अध्वर-क्यच्-युच् ततोऽन्त्याकारलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 Any officiating priest, technically distinguished from होतृ, उद्रातृ<BR> and ब्रह्मन्. His duty was “to measure the ground, build the altar,<BR> prepare sacrificial vessels, to fetch wood and water, to light the fire,<BR> to bring the animal and immolate it”, and while doing this to repeat the<BR> Yajurveda; होता प्रथमं शंसति तमध्वर्युः प्रोत्साहयति Sk. See<BR> अच्छावाक also.<BR>—2 The Yajurveda itself. ━pl. Adherents of that Veda.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्वर्युकाण्डमं, अध्वर्युकतुः, अध्वर्युवेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्युकाण्डमं
अध्वर्युः + -काण्डमं N. of a book of mantras or prayers intended for Adhvaryu priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्युकतुः
अध्वर्युः + -कतुः Sacrificial act performed by the Adhvaryu (Pāṇini II. 4. 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्युवेदः|अध्वर्युवेद
अध्वर्युः + -वेदः Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वस्मन्
अध्वस्मन् <i>a.</i> [ध्वंस् मनिन् किच्च, न˚ त˚] Imperishable; bright (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान
अध्वान <i>a.</i> (न˚ ब˚) Dumb, taciturn; अक्षद्यूतजितो युधिष्टिर<BR> इवाध्वानं गतः कोकिलः Mk. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्तम्
अध्वान्तम् [न˚ त˚] Twilight, gloom, slight darkness, shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्तः|अध्वान्त|अध्वांतं
अध्वान्तम् + .{@-न्तः@} [ष˚ त˚] End of the journey.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अध्वान्तशात्रवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्तशात्रवः|अध्वान्तशात्रव
अध्वान्तम् + -शात्रवः [अध्वान्तस्य मार्गसीमायाः शात्रव इव Tv.] A plant<BR> (श्चोनाक) Cassia Fistula or Bignonia Indica (blossoming in shade).<BR> (Mar. बाहवा, पाडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् €2 P. [अनिति, आन(नी)त्, आन, अनितुम्, अनित]<BR>—1 To breathe; आनीदवातं स्वधया तदेकम् Rv. 10. 129. 2.<BR>—2 To move, go about, live; को ह्येवान्यात् यद्येष आकाश आनन्दो न स्यात् T. Up.<BR>—3 To gasp, pant with thirst (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i> आनयति; <i>desid.</i> अनिनिषति.<BR> €4 Ā. To live.<BR> €10 P. आनयति. also €1 P. अनति, to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् <i>m.</i> [क्विप्] The soul; विश्वे चनेदना Rv. 4. 30. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनः|अन
अनः [अन्-अच्] Breath, respiration; प्राणोऽपानो व्यान उदानः<BR> समानोऽनः इत्येतत्सर्वं प्राण इति Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 3. [cf. L. <i>animus</i>,<BR> Gr. <i>anemos</i>]. अनः प्राणयुतेऽपि स्यात् । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननम्
अननम् [अन् ल्युट्] Act of breathing, living &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंश
अनंश <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not entitled to a share in the inheritance; ˚शौ क्लीबपतितौ जात्यन्धबधिरौ<BR> तथा । उन्मत्तजडमूकाश्च ये च केचिन्निरिन्द्रियाः ॥ Ms. 9. 201. Other<BR> persons are also mentioned by Devala, Baudhāyana, Kātyāyana and Nārada.<BR>—2 Without parts, undivided, portionless; an epithet of the sky or the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंशुमत्फला
अनंशुमत्फला [न अंशुमत् मोचकाभ्यन्तरस्थत्वात् फलं यस्याः]<BR> The plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्
अनक् <i>a.</i> Blind. व्यनगचष्ट Rv. 2. 15. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अनक <i>a.</i> Mean, base; see अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष्
अनक्ष् <i>a.</i> [न अक्ष्णोति व्याप्नोति विषयमिन्द्रियेण, अक्ष्-क्विप् न˚ त˚]<BR> Without sight, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष|अनक्षः
अनक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without an axle-tree.<BR>—2 Sightless, blind. यस्यानक्षा दुहिता Rv. 10. 27. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकदुन्दुभिः|अनकदुन्दुभि|अनकदुंदुभिः
अनकदुन्दुभिः = आनकदुन्दुभि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकस्मात्
अनकस्मात् <i>ind.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not causelessly, not suddenly<BR> or accidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षर|अनक्षरं
अनक्षर <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Unable to speak, mute, dumb, unlettered; मुखमनक्षरं स्वाकृतेः Bh. 2. 56.<BR>—2 Unfit to be uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षरम्
अनक्षर + .{@-रम्@} [अप्रशस्तान्यक्षराणि यत्र] Abusive language, foul or<BR> abusive words, censure. ━<i>adv.</i> Without the use of words, not expressed<BR> by words, mutely, dumbly; ˚रं पप्रच्छ K. 219, 143; ˚व्यञ्जितदौर्हृदेन R. 14. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षि
अनक्षि <i>n.</i> [अप्रशस्तम् अक्षि] A bad eye, weak eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगार|अनगारः
अनगार <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Houseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगारः|अनगार
अनगार + .{@-रः@} A vagrant ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगारिका
अनगारिका The houseless state of a vagrant ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नि|अनग्निः
अनग्नि [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Non-fire, substance other than fire; यदधीतमविज्ञातं निगदेनैव<BR> शब्द्यते । अनग्नाविव शुष्कैधो न तज्ज्वलति कर्हिचित् Nir.<BR>—2 Absence of fire. <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not requiring fire, dispensing with fire, without the use of fire;<BR> विदधे विधिमस्य नैष्टिकं यतिभिः सार्धमनग्निमग्निचित् R. 8. 25; said<BR> of a sacrifice also (अग्निचयनरहितो यज्ञः).<BR>—2 Not maintaining the sacred fire; अनग्निरनिकेतः स्यान्मुनिर्मूलफलाशनः Ms. 6. 25, 43;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">Page0073-1</a>]<BR> irreligious, impious.<BR>—3 Dyspeptic.<BR>—4 Unmarried.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनग्नित्र, अनग्नित्रा, अनग्निदग्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नित्र
अनग्नि + -त्र, -त्रा <i>a.</i> Ved. not maintaining the sacred fire, sinful,<BR> irreligious अग्ने त्वमस्मद् युयोध्यमीवा अनग्नित्रा अभ्यमन्त कृष्टीः Rv. 1. 189. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नित्रा
अनग्नि + -त्र, -त्रा <i>a.</i> Ved. not maintaining the sacred fire, sinful,<BR> irreligious अग्ने त्वमस्मद् युयोध्यमीवा अनग्नित्रा अभ्यमन्त कृष्टीः Rv. 1. 189. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्निदग्ध
अनग्नि + -दग्ध <i>a.</i> Not burnt with fire or on the funeral pile, ये<BR> अग्निदग्धा ये अनग्निदग्धा मध्ये दिवः स्वधया मादयन्ते Rv. 10. 15. 14<BR> (श्मशानकर्म न प्राप्ताः); a class of Manes Ms. 3. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघ|अनघः
अनघ <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Sinless, innocent; अवैमि चैनामनघेति R. 14. 40.<BR>—2 Free from blame, faultless, handsome; अखण्डं पुण्यानां फलमिव च<BR> तद् रूपमनघम् Ś. 2. 10; यस्य ज्ञानदयासिन्धोरगाधस्यानघा गुणाः<BR> Ak.; ˚सर्वगात्री Dk. 123.<BR>—3 Without mishap or accident, free from danger, calamity &c.; safe, unhurt;<BR> यास्त्वामनघमद्राक्ष्म Dk. 108; कच्चिन्मृगीणामनघा प्रसूतिः R. 5. 7;<BR> मृगवधूर्यदा अनघप्रसवा भवति Ś. 4 safely delivered or brought<BR> to bed; ˚प्रसूतेः R. 14. 75.<BR>—4 Without grief or sorrow; दयालुमनघस्पृष्टम् R. 10. 19.<BR>—5 Free from dirt, impurities &c., pure, spotless; R. 10. 80, 13. 65; Śi. 3. 31.<BR>—6 Tireless, not exhausted; Bhāg. 2. 7. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघः|अनघ
अनघ + .{@-घः@}<BR>—1 White mustard.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu; अनघो विजयो जेता; V. Sah. 16; also of Śiva and<BR> of several other persons, a Gandharva, Sādhya &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनघाष्टमी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघाष्टमी
अनघ + -अष्टमी N. of the eighth day (spoken of in the fifty-fifth Adhyāya<BR> of Bhaviṣyottara Purāṇa)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्कुश|अनंकुश
अनङ्कुश <i>a.</i> [अङ्कुशेन न-वश्यः]<BR>—1 Ungovernable, unruly.<BR>—2 Taking license (as a poet.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनङ्ग <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Bodiless, without a body; formless, incorporeal; त्वमनङ्गः कथमक्षता<BR> रतिः Ku. 4. 9.<BR>—2 Different from the body.<BR>—3 Without a supplement or auxiliary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गः|अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं
अनङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः@}<BR>—1 Cupid (the bodiless one; so called from his having been reduced to<BR> ashes by Śiva with the fire of his third eye, when he tried to seduce<BR> the Godʼs mind towards Pārvatī for the birth of a deliverer of the Gods from Tāraka.)<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 A goblin.<BR>—4 A shadow, cf. अनङ्गे मन्मथे वायौ पिशाचच्छाययोरपि Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गम्
अनङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गम्@}<BR>—1 Sky, air, ether.<BR>—2 The mind (आकाशस्य निरवयवत्वात् न्यायवैशेषिकमते चित्तस्य अगुणत्वेन<BR> तस्य तथात्वम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनङ्गापीडः, अनङ्गकीडा, अनङ्गद, अनङ्गदेवी, अनङ्गद्वादशी, अनङ्गपालः, अनङ्गलेखः, अनङ्गरङ्गः, अनङ्गलेखा, अनङ्गशत्रुः, अनङ्गासुहृत्, अनङ्गशेखरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गापीडः|अनङ्गापीड
अनङ्ग + -आपीडः N. of a king of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गकीडा
अनङ्ग + -कीडा [तृ˚ त˚]<BR>—1 amorous sports.<BR>—2 N. of a metre of two lines, the first with 16 long, and second with 32<BR> short, syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गद
अनङ्ग + -द <i>a.</i> [उप˚ स˚] inspiring love; ˚दे तनुभूते ते<BR> भुजलते K. 220. (also without Aṅgada); बाह्वोरनङ्गदत्वस्य बाले<BR> ते कारणे उभे Bhār. C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गदेवी
अनङ्ग + -देवी N. of a queen of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गद्वादशी
अनङ्ग + -द्वादशी N. of the 83rd chapter of भविष्योत्तरपुराण; ˚त्रयोदशीव्रतम्,<BR> see under व्रत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गपालः|अनङ्गपाल
अनङ्ग + -पालः N. of a kingʼs chamberlain at Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गलेखः|अनङ्गलेख|अनंगलेख
अनङ्ग + -लेखः (मदनलेखः) a love letter; ˚लेखक्रिययोपयोगं<BR> (व्रजन्ति) Ku. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गरङ्गः|अनङ्गरङ्ग
अनङ्ग + -रङ्गः N. of an erotic work describing the several postures (आसन)<BR> pertaining to sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गलेखा
अनङ्ग + -लेखा<BR>—1 A love letter.<BR>—2 N. of a queen of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गशत्रुः|अनङ्गशत्रु
अनङ्ग + -शत्रुः, -असुहृत् &c. N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गासुहृत्|अनंगासुहृत्
अनङ्ग + -शत्रुः, -असुहृत् &c. N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गशेखरः|अनङ्गशेखर
अनङ्ग + -शेखरः N. of a metre of four lines, each with 15 iambic feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गकम्
अनङ्गकम् The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गुरि|अनंगुरि
अनङ्गुरि, -लि <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Destitute of fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गुलि
अनङ्गुरि, -लि <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Destitute of fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनच्छ|अनच्छः
अनच्छ <i>a.</i> Not clear, dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनजका
अनजका, अनजिका [अप्रशस्ता अजा] A miserable or small goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनजिका
अनजका, अनजिका [अप्रशस्ता अजा] A miserable or small goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनञ्जन|अनंजन|अनञ्जनं
अनञ्जन <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Without collyrium, pigment or paint; नेत्रे दूरमनञ्जने S. D.<BR>—2 Faultless, taintless.<BR>—3 Without any connection (निःसम्बन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनञ्जनम्
अनञ्जन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The sky, atmosphere.<BR>—2 The Supreme Spirit (परब्रह्म), Viṣṇu or Nārāyaṇa. यदा<BR> विसृष्टस्त्वमनञ्जनेन वै बलं प्रविष्टोऽजितदैत्यदानवम् Bhāg. 9. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह्
अनडुह् <i>m.</i> [अनः शकटं वहति] (अनड्वान्, ˚ड्वाहौ, ˚डुद्भ्याम् &c.)<BR>—1 An ox, bull.<BR>—2 The sign Taurus. वृषभराशि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुही
अनडुह् + .{@-ही@} or अनड्वाही A cow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनडुग्जिहृ, अनडुग्द<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुग्जिहृ
अनडुह् + -जिहृ [अनडुहो जिह्वेव पत्राणि यस्याः सा] a plant (गोजिह्वा, अनन्तमूल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुग्द
अनडुह् + -द <i>a.</i> [उप˚ स˚] a giver of oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुत्क
अनडुत्क <i>a.</i> Having oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुहः|अनडुह
अनडुहः N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणु|अनणुः
अनणु <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not small or minute or fine, coarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणुः|अनणु
अनणु + .{@-णुः@} Coarse grain, peas &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनति
अनति <i>ind.</i> Not very much; compounds beginning with अनति<BR> may be analysed by referring to अति; e. g. अनतिक्रमः moderation;<BR> अनतिक्रमणीय not to be transgressed, inviolable; अनतिदृश्य opaque;<BR> अनतिद्भुत unsurpassed, real, true, proper, ब्रह्मा त इन्द्र गिर्वणः<BR> क्रियन्ते अनतिद्भुता Rv. 8. 90. 3. अनतिव्याध्य invulnerable; अनत्यन्तगति<BR> P. V. 4. 4 sense of diminutive words; अनत्यय imperishable, undecaying<BR> &c.; अनतिप्रश्न not to be asked to excess; अनतिविलम्बिता absence<BR> of delay; fluency as a speakerʼs qualification, one of the 35 Vāgguṇas, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्धा
अनद्धा <i>ind.</i> [न˚ त˚] Ved. Not truly or clearly, not<BR> certainly or definitely.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनद्धापुरुषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्धापुरुषः|अनद्धापुरुष
अनद्धा + -पुरुषः not a true man; one who is not of use, either to gods,<BR> men or the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यः|अनद्य
अनद्यः [न अद्यः भक्ष्यः अप्राशस्त्ये नञ्] White mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यतन|अनद्यतनः
अनद्यतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [न˚ त˚] Not pertaining to this or the current<BR> day; a term used by Pāṇini to denote the sense of the Imperfect or the<BR> Periphrastic future P. III. 2. 111, III. 3. 15; ˚भूते लङ्-अपचत्; ˚ने<BR> भविष्यति लुट्-पक्ता; परोक्षानद्यतने लिट्-पपाच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यतनः|अनद्यतन
अनद्यतन + .{@-नः@} Not the current day; अतीतायाः रात्रेः पश्चार्धेन आगामिन्या<BR> रात्रेः पूर्वार्धेन सहितो दिवसोऽद्यतनः Sk., तद्भिन्नः कालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिक
अनधिक <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not more or excessive.<BR>—2 Boundless; perfect.<BR>—3 Not capable of being enlarged or surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारः|अनधिकार
अनधिकारः [न˚ त˚] Absence of authority, right, claim &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनधिकारचर्चा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारचर्चा|अनधिकारचर्च्चा
अनधिकारः + -चर्चा intermeddling, officiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारिन्
अनधिकारिन् <i>a.</i> Not entitled to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगत|अनधिगतः
अनधिगत <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Not obtained, acquired or studied.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनधिगतमनोरथ, अनधिगतशास्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगतमनोरथ
अनधिगत + -मनोरथ <i>a.</i> foiled in oneʼs expectations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगतशास्त्र
अनधिगत + -शास्त्र <i>a.</i> who has not learnt the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीन|अनधीनः
अनधीन <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीनः|अनधीन
अनधीन + .{@-नः, -नकः@} [संज्ञायां कन्] An independent carpenter working<BR> on his own account (कौटतक्षः); स हि कुट्यां वसन् न कस्यचिदधीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीनकः|अनधीनक
अनधीन + .{@-नः, -नकः@} [संज्ञायां कन्] An independent carpenter working<BR> on his own account (कौटतक्षः); स हि कुट्यां वसन् न कस्यचिदधीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यक्ष|अनध्यक्षः
अनध्यक्ष <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not perceptible or observable, invisible; मनोऽपि न तथाज्ञानादनध्यक्षं<BR> तदा भवेत् । Bhāṣā P.<BR>—2 Without controller or ruler &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यायः|अनध्याय
अनध्यायः अनध्ययनम् [न˚ त˚] Not studying, intermission<BR> of study; the time when there is or ought to be such intermission, a holiday<BR> (˚दिवसः); अद्य शिष्टानध्यायः U. 4 a holiday (given) in honour<BR> of distinguished guests. See Ms. 2. 105-6, 4. 103-4, 105-8, 117-8, 126 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभावुक
अननुभावुक <i>a.</i> Unable to comprehend;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभावुक
अननुभावुक + ˚ता non-comprehension,<BR> unintelligibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभाषणम्
अननुभाषणम्<BR>—1 Not repeating a statement or proposition.<BR>—2 Tacit assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अनन्त <i>a.</i> [नास्ति अन्तो यस्य] Endless, infinite, eternal,<BR> boundless, inexhaustible; ˚रत्नप्रभवस्य यस्य Ku. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तः|अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं
अनन्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu; गन्धर्वाप्सरसः सिद्धाः किन्नरोरगचारणाः । नान्तं<BR> गुणानां जानन्ति (नास्यान्तमधिगच्छन्ति) तेनानन्तोऽयमुच्यते ॥;<BR> also of Viṣṇuʼs couch, the serpent Śeṣa; of Kṛṣṇa and his brother;<BR> of Śiva, the 14th Arhat; Vāsuki, the lord of serpents अनन्तश्चास्मि<BR> नागानाम् Bg. 10. 29.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 Talc.<BR>—4 N. of a plant (सिन्दुवार) Vitex Trifolia (Mar. निरगुडी).<BR>—5 The asterism श्रवण.<BR>—6 A silken cord with 14 knots tied round the right arm on the अनन्तचतुर्दशी day.<BR>—7 The letter आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ता
अनन्त + .{@-न्ता@}<BR>—1 The earth (the endless).<BR>—2 The number one.<BR>—3 Names of various females; N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—4 Names of various plants; शारिवा, अनन्तमूल (a very medicinal plant)<BR> दूर्वा, आमलकी, गुडूची, अग्निमन्थ, कणा, लाङ्गली, दुरालभा, हरीतकी,<BR> अग्निशिखा, श्यामलता, पिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ती
अनन्त + .{@-न्ती@} A small silken cord tied round the left arm of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तम्
अनन्त + .{@-न्तम्@}<BR>—1 The sky, atmosphere.<BR>—2 Infinity, eternity.<BR>—3 Absolution, final beatitude; तदनन्ताय कल्पते Pt. 2. 72.<BR>—4 The Supreme Spirit, Brahman (परब्रह्म); सत्यं ज्ञानमनन्तं<BR> ब्रह्मेति श्रुतिः । न व्यापित्वाद्देशतोऽन्तो नित्यत्वान्नापि कालतः । न वस्तुतोऽपि<BR> सर्वात्म्यादानन्त्यं ब्रह्मणि त्रिधा ॥<BR>—5 A sloping and a projecting member of the entablature representing a<BR> continued pent-roof; अनन्तं चान्तरिक्षं च प्रस्तरं चाष्टधा लुपाः<BR> Māna. 18. 174-175. cf. अनन्तः शेषविष्ण्वोश्चानवधौ क्लीबमम्बरे ।<BR> स्त्रियां स्याच्छारिवादूर्वाविशल्यालाङ्गलीषु च । हैमवत्यां गळूच्यां च … । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनन्तात्मन्, अनन्तकर, अनन्तग, अनन्तगुण, अनन्तचतुर्दशी, अनन्तव्रतम्, अनन्तचरित्रः, अनन्तजित्, अनन्ततान, अनन्ततीर्थकृत्, अनन्ततृतीया, अनन्तदृष्टिः, अनन्तदेवः, अनन्तनेमिः, अनन्तपार, अनन्तपालः, अनन्तमतिः, अनन्तमायिन्, अनन्तमूलः, अनन्तराशिः, अनन्तरूप, अनन्तवातः, अनन्तविकमिन्, अनन्तविजयः, अनन्तवीर्यः, अनन्तव्रतम्, अनन्तशक्ति, अनन्तशयनम्, अनन्तशीर्ष, अनन्तशुष्म, अनन्तश्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तात्मन्
अनन्त + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the Supreme Spirit;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तकर
अनन्त + -कर <i>a.</i> magnifying to any extent; P. III. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तग
अनन्त + -ग <i>a.</i> moving forever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तगुण
अनन्त + -गुण <i>a.</i> possessed of endless merits; of countless or infinite<BR> number; प्लवङ्गानामनन्तगुणतैधते Mv. 6. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तचतुर्दशी|अनन्तचतुर्द्दशी
अनन्त + -चतुर्दशी, -व्रतम् [अनन्तस्य आराधनं यस्यां सा चतुर्दशी]<BR> the 14th day of the bright half of Bhādrapada when Ananta is worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तव्रतम्
अनन्त + -चतुर्दशी, -व्रतम् [अनन्तस्य आराधनं यस्यां सा चतुर्दशी]<BR> the 14th day of the bright half of Bhādrapada when Ananta is worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तचरित्रः
अनन्त + -चरित्रः N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तजित्
अनन्त + -जित् (अनन्तानि भूतानि जितवान्)<BR>—1 N. of Vāsudeva, the conqueror<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">Page0074-2</a>]<BR> of all.<BR>—2 N. of an Arhat deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ततान
अनन्त + -तान <i>a.</i> of endless width, extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ततीर्थकृत्
अनन्त + -तीर्थकृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 one who visits many places of pilgrimage.<BR>—2 a Jaina deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ततृतीया
अनन्त + -तृतीया the third day of the bright half of भाद्रपद, मार्गशीर्ष<BR> or वैशाख; नभस्ये वाथ वैशाखे मार्गशीर्षेऽथवा पुनः । शुक्लपक्षतृतीयायां …<BR> उक्तानन्ततृतीयैषा सुतानन्दफलप्रदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तदृष्टिः|अनन्तदृष्टि
अनन्त + -दृष्टिः [अनन्ता दृष्टयो नेत्राणि यस्य] N. of Śiva, or of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तदेवः|अनन्तदेव
अनन्त + -देवः [अनन्तो देव इव]<BR>—1 the serpent Śeṣa.<BR>—2 [अनन्ते दीव्यति; दिव्-अच्] N. of Nārāyaṇa who sleeps on Śeṣa.<BR>—3 N. of the king of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तनेमिः|अनन्तनेमि
अनन्त + -नेमिः N. of the king of Mālava, a contemporary of शाक्यमुनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तपार
अनन्त + -पार <i>a.</i> of endless width, boundless; ˚रं किल शब्दशास्त्रम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तपालः|अनन्तपाल
अनन्त + -पालः N. of a warrior-chief in Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तमतिः|अनन्तमति
अनन्त + -मतिः N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तमायिन्
अनन्त + -मायिन् <i>a.</i> of endless tricks, endlessly deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तमूलः|अनन्तमूल
अनन्त + -मूलः a medicinal plant (शारिवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तराशिः|अनन्तराशि
अनन्त + -राशिः an infinite quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरूप
अनन्त + -रूप <i>a.</i> of innumerable forms or shapes; epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवातः|अनन्तवात
अनन्त + -वातः a disease of the head, resembling tetanus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तविकमिन्
अनन्त + -विकमिन् N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तविजयः|अनन्तविजय
अनन्त + -विजयः [अनन्तान् विजयते ध्वनिद्वारा अनेन] N. of Yudhiṣṭhiraʼs<BR> conchshell. अनन्तविजयं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्टिरः Bg. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवीर्यः|अनन्तवीर्य|अनन्तवीर्य्य|अनन्तवीर्य्यः
अनन्त + -वीर्यः N. of the 23rd Jaina Arhat of a future age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तव्रतम्
अनन्त + -व्रतम्<BR>—1 See अनन्तचतुर्दशी above.<BR>—2 N. of the 102nd Adhyāya of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशक्ति
अनन्त + -शक्ति <i>a.</i> of boundless power, omnipotent, epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशयनम्
अनन्त + -शयनम् Travancore; Śrīraṅgapaṭṭaṇa (because there are<BR> temples of Viṣṇu reclining on अनन्त Serpent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशीर्ष
अनन्त + -शीर्ष N. of Viṣṇu or the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशीर्षा
अनन्त + -शीर्ष + .({@-र्षा@}) N. of the wife of Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशुष्म
अनन्त + -शुष्म <i>a.</i> Ved. possessing endless strength; endlessly blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तश्री
अनन्त + -श्री <i>a.</i> of boundless magnificence, an epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तक|अनंतक
अनन्तक <i>a.</i> [स्वार्थे कन्] Endless, eternal &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तकम्
अनन्तक + .{@-कम्@} The Eternal or Infinite (among the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त्य|अनंत्य
अनन्त्य <i>a.</i> [अनन्तस्य इदं-यत्] Endless, eternal, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त्यम्
अनन्त्य + .{@-न्त्यम्@}<BR>—1 Eternity, infinity.<BR>—2 The foot of हिरण्यगर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवत्|अनंतवत्|अनन्तवन्त्
अनन्तवत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्] Endless, eternal. ━<i>m.</i> One<BR> of Brahmanʼs four feet; earth, intermediate region, heaven, and ocean.<BR> पृथिवी कलान्तरिक्षं कला द्यौः कला समुद्रः कलैष वै सोम्य चतुष्कलः<BR> पादो ब्रह्मणोऽनन्तवान्नाम । Ch. Up. 4. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर|अनंतर|अनन्तरं
अनन्तर <i>a.</i> [नास्ति अन्तरं व्यवधानं, मध्यः; अवकाशः &c. यस्य]<BR>—1 Having no interior or interior space, limitless; तदेतत् ब्रह्म अपूर्वमनन्तरम्<BR> अबाह्यम् Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 19.<BR>—2 Having no interval or interstice of pause (of space or time); compact,<BR> close; हलोऽनन्तराः संयोगः P. I. 1. 7; see संयोग.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Contiguous, neighbouring, adjoining; Rām. 4. 21. 14; अनयत्<BR> प्रभुशक्तिसंपदा वशमेको नृपतीननन्तरान् R. 8. 19; भारतवर्षादुत्तरेण<BR> अनन्तरे किंपुरुषनाम्नि वर्षे K. 136; immediately adjoining; Ki. 2. 53,<BR> R. 7. 21; not distant from (with abl.); आत्मनोऽनन्तरममात्यपदं<BR> ग्राहितः Mu. 4; ब्रह्मावर्तादनन्तरः Ms. 2. 19 (Kull. अनन्तरः<BR> किंचिदूनः); अरेः अनन्तरं मित्रम् 7. 158; or in comp.; विषयानन्तरो<BR> राजा शत्रुः Ak. who is an immediate neighbour.<BR>—4 Immediately before or after; Rām. 4. 29. 31.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">Page0075-1</a>]<BR> तदिदं क्रियतामनन्तरं भवता बन्धुजनप्रयोजनम् Ku. 4. 32<BR> soon after, just afterwards; अनन्तरोदीरितलक्ष्मभाजौ पादौ यदीयावुपजातयस्ताः<BR> Chand. M. having characteristics mentioned just before.<BR>—5 Following, coming close upon (in comp.); शङ्खस्वनानन्तरपुष्पवृष्टि<BR> Ku. 1. 23, 2. 53; ˚करणीयम् Ś. 4 the next duty, what should be done next.<BR>—6 Belonging to the caste immediately following; पुत्रा येऽनन्तरस्त्रीजाः Ms. 10. 14.<BR>—7 Uninterrupted, unbroken, continuous. सुखदुःखावृते लोके नेहास्त्येकमनन्तरम्<BR> Mb. 12. 153. 89.<BR>—8 Straight, direct (साक्षात्). अथवाऽनन्तरकृतं किंचिदेव निदर्शनम्<BR> Mb. 12. 305. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरम्
अनन्तर + .{@-रम्@} [न˚ त˚] —1 Contiguity, proximity; अनन्तरविहिते<BR> चास्यासने K. 93. —2 Brahman, the supreme soul (as being of one entire essence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरम्
अनन्तर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> [Strictly it is acc. of time कालात्यन्तसंयोगः;<BR> नास्ति अन्तरं यथा स्यात्तथा]<BR>—1 Immediately after, afterwards.<BR>—2 (with a prepositional force) After (with abl.); पुराणपत्त्रापगमादनन्तरम्<BR> R. 3. 7; त्यागाच्छान्तिरनन्तरम् Bg. 12. 12; गोदानविधेरनन्तरम्<BR> R. 3. 33, 36, 2. 71; स्वामिनोऽनन्तरं भृत्याः Pt. 1; rarely with gen.;<BR> अङ्गदं चाधिरूढस्तु लक्ष्मणोऽनन्तरं मम Rām.; or in comp.; घनोदयाः<BR> प्राक् तदनन्तरं पयः Ś. 7. 30; R. 4. 2; Ms. 3. 252; Y. 2. 41;<BR> वचनानन्तरमेव K. 78 immediately after those words.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनन्तरजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरजः|अनन्तरज
अनन्तर + -जः or {@जा@} [अनन्तरस्या अनन्तरवर्णाया मातुः जायते]<BR>—1 the child of a Kṣatriyā or Vaiśyā mother, by a father belonging<BR> to the caste immediately above the motherʼs, स्त्रीष्वनन्तरजातासु द्विजैरुत्पादितान्सुतान् ।<BR> सदृशानेव तानाहुर्मातृदोषविगर्हितान् ॥ Ms. 10. 6.<BR>—2 born immediately before or after; a younger or elder brother. Legitimate<BR> son (औरसः); आत्मा पुत्रश्च विज्ञेयस्तस्यानन्तरजश्च यः Mb. 13. 49. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरजा
अनन्तर + -जः or {@जा@} [अनन्तरस्या अनन्तरवर्णाया मातुः जायते]<BR>—1 the child of a Kṣatriyā or Vaiśyā mother, by a father belonging<BR> to the caste immediately above the motherʼs, स्त्रीष्वनन्तरजातासु द्विजैरुत्पादितान्सुतान् ।<BR> सदृशानेव तानाहुर्मातृदोषविगर्हितान् ॥ Ms. 10. 6.<BR>—2 born immediately before or after; a younger or elder brother. Legitimate<BR> son (औरसः); आत्मा पुत्रश्च विज्ञेयस्तस्यानन्तरजश्च यः Mb. 13. 49. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरजा
अनन्तर + -जः + .({@-जा@}) a younger or elder sister; अनुष्टितानन्तरजाविवाहः<BR> R. 7. 32; so ˚जात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरजात
अनन्तर + -जः + .({@-जा@}) a younger or elder sister; अनुष्टितानन्तरजाविवाहः<BR> R. 7. 32; so ˚जात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरीय|अनंतरीय
अनन्तरीय <i>a.</i> Next in succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरयः|अनन्तरय|अनंतरयः
अनन्तरयः [अन्तरयः दूरीकरणं, न˚ त˚] Not leaving,<BR> non-abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तराय
अनन्तराय <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Uninterrupted, without a break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर्गर्भिन्
अनन्तर्गर्भिन् <i>m.</i> [अनन्तर्गर्भो यस्य; अस्त्यर्थे इनि, न˚ त˚]<BR> N. of Kuśa grass used for the पवित्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्द|अनंद|अनन्दः
अनन्द <i>a.</i> [न नन्दयति; नन्द्-णिच् अच्] Joyless, cheerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्दः|अनन्द|अनंद
अनन्द + .{@-न्दः@} N. of a purgatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्नम्
अनन्नम् Not food, that which is undeserving of being eaten. अनद्यमानो<BR> यदनन्नमत्ति Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अनन्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not different, identical, same, not other than, self; अनन्या राघवस्याहं<BR> भास्करस्य प्रभा यथा । सा हि सत्याभिसन्धाना तथानन्या च भर्तरि Rām.<BR> cf. Rām. 5. 21. 15.<BR>—2 Sole, unique, without a second.<BR>—3 [नास्ति अन्यः विषयो यस्य] Undivided, undistracted (mind &c.);<BR> having no other object or person to think of &c.; अनन्याश्चिन्तयन्तो मां<BR> ये जनाः पर्युपासते Bg. 9. 22. In comp. अनन्य may be translated<BR> by ‘not by another’, ‘directed or devoted to no one else’, ‘having no other object’.<BR>—4 unopposed; अनन्यां पृथिवीं भुङ्क्ते सर्वभूतहिते रतः Kau. A.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनन्यार्थ, अनन्याश्रित, अनन्यगतिः, अनन्यगतिक, अनन्यगुरु, अनन्यचित्त, अनन्यचिन्त, अनन्यचेतस्, अनन्यमनस्, अनन्यमानस, अनन्यहृदय, अनन्यजः, अनन्यजन्मन्, अनन्यदृष्टि, अनन्यदेव, अनन्यपरता, अनन्यपरायण, अनन्यपूर्वः, अनन्यभाज्, अनन्यविषय, अनन्यवृत्ति, अनन्यशासन, अनन्यसामान्य, अनन्यसाधारण, अनन्यसद्द्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यार्थ
अनन्य + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> not subservient to any other object, principal.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">Page0075-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्याश्रित
अनन्य + -आश्रित <i>a.</i> independent, not resorting to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्याश्रितम्
अनन्य + -आश्रित + .({@-तम्@}) unencumbered estate (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगतिः|अनन्यगति
अनन्य + -गतिः <i>f.</i> sole resort or resource.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगतिक|अनन्यगतिकः
अनन्य + -गतिक <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] having no other resource or help,<BR> having no other resource left; अनन्यगतिके जने विगतपातके चातके Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगुरु
अनन्य + -गुरु <i>a.</i> than which nothing is greater. अनन्यगुर्वास्तव<BR> केन केवलः पुराणमूर्तेर्महिमावगम्यते Śi. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यचित्त
अनन्य + -चित्त, -चिन्त, -चेतस्, -मनस्, -मानस, -हृदय <i>a.</i> giving<BR> oneʼs undivided thought or attention to, with undivided mind; विचिन्तयन्ती<BR> यमनन्यमानसा Ś. 4. 1; K. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

