अनवेक्षा
अनवेक्ष, -क्षा<BR> = अनपेक्ष-क्षा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षणम्
अनवेक्षणम्<BR>—1 Carelessness, inattention; अनवेक्षणादपि कृषिः Pt. 1. 169.<BR>—2 Want of supervision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनव्रत|अनव्रतः
अनव्रत <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Not altogether destitute of holy<BR> or ascetic performances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनव्रतः|अनव्रत
अनव्रत + .{@-तः@} A Jaina devotee who is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशनम्
अनशनम् Fasting, abstinence from food, fasting oneself to death;<BR> कृशामनशनेन च Rām. 5. 15. 23. ˚नं च शाययित्वा Dk. 156 making<BR> him fast; ˚नात् उत्तिष्ठति Pt. 4. <i>a.</i> Without food, fasting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशनाय
अनशनाय <i>a.</i> Ved. Not hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्नत्|अनश्नन्त्
अनश्नत् <i>a.</i> Not eating; अनश्नन्नन्यो अभि चाकशीति Rv. 1. 164. 20;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्नत्साङ्गमनः
अनश्नत् + ˚साङ्गमनः the sacrificial fire in the sabhā which is approached<BR> before eating or breakfast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्व|अनश्वः
अनश्व <i>a.</i> Having no horse or horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वः|अनश्व
अनश्व + .{@-श्वः@} Something that is not a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वन्
अनश्वन् <i>m.</i> N. of Parikṣitʼs father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वर|अनश्वरं
अनश्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) Imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्
अनस् <i>n.</i> [अनिति शब्दायते अन-असुन्]<BR>—1 A cart; तद्यथानः सुसमाहितमुत्सर्जद्यायादेवमेवायं शारीर आत्मा<BR> Bṛ. Ār. Up. 3. 35. उद्राता चाप्यनः क्रये Ms. 8. 209; मुसलोलूरवलाऽनसाम्<BR> (प्रोक्षणम्) Y. 1. 184, 3. 269; Śi. 12. 26.<BR>—2 [अनिति जीवत्यनेन] Food, boiled rice.<BR>—3 Birth.<BR>—4 A living being.<BR>—5 A kitchen.<BR>—6 A parent (father or mother); said to be <i>f.</i> in these two senses.<BR> At the end of Avyayībhāva comp. अनस् is changed to अनस; as<BR> अध्यनसम् &c.; also at the end of Tat. comp.; महानसम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूय
अनसूय, -यक <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ ब˚] Free from malice, not envious,<BR> not spiteful; श्रद्दधानोऽनसूयश्च Ms. 4. 158; श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च<BR> शृणुयादपि यो नरः । Bg. 18. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अनसूय, -यक <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ ब˚] Free from malice, not envious,<BR> not spiteful; श्रद्दधानोऽनसूयश्च Ms. 4. 158; श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च<BR> शृणुयादपि यो नरः । Bg. 18. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूया
अनसूय, -यक + .{@-या@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Absence of envy, charity of disposition, freedom from spite or illwill;<BR> न गुणान् गुणिनो हन्ति स्तौति चान्यगुणानपि । न हसेच्चान्यदोषांश्च सानसूया प्रकीर्तिता.<BR>—2 N. of a friend of Śakuntalā.<BR>—3 N. of a daughter of Dakṣa.<BR>—4 N. of Atriʼs wife, the highest type of chastity and wifely devotion.<BR> [She was very pious and given to austere devotion by virtue of which she<BR> had obtained miraculous powers. Several stories are told to illustrate<BR> them. When the earth was devastated by a terrible drought which lasted<BR> for 10 years, Anasūyā created water, fruits, roots &c. by means of her<BR> ascetic powers and saved many lives. On one occasion when the sage Māṇḍavya<BR> was about to be impaled, the wife of a sage happened to touch the stake<BR> as she passed by, whereupon Māṇḍavya cursed her that she would become<BR> a widow at sunrise. She, however, prevented the sun from rising, and all<BR> actions of men being consequently stopped, the gods, sages &c. went to<BR> Anasūyā, her friend, who, by the force of her penance, made<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">Page0080-1</a>]<BR> the sun rise without, at the same time, bringing widowhood on her friend.<BR> Another legend is also told in which Anasūyā changed Brahmā, Viṣṇu<BR> and Maheśa into infants, when, at the instigation of their wives, they<BR> attempted to test her chastity, but restored them to their former shapes<BR> at the importunities of their humbled consorts. She is also said to have<BR> caused the three-streamed Ganges to flow down on the earth near the hermitage<BR> of her husband for the ablutions of sages; see R. 13. 51. In the Rāmāyaṇa<BR> she is represented as having been very kind and attentive to Sītā whom<BR> she favoured with sound motherly advice on the virtues of chastity, and<BR> at the time of her departure gave her an unguent (See R. 12. 27, 14. 14)<BR> which was to keep her beautiful for ever and to guard her person from<BR> the attempts of rapacious beasts, demons &c. She was the mother of the<BR> irascible sage Durvāsas]. सा त्वेवमुक्ता वैदेही त्वनसूयानसूयया Rām. 2. 18. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयु
अनसूयु <i>a.</i> = अनसूय; इदं तु ते गुह्यतमं प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे Bg. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थ|अनस्थः
अनस्थ, -स्थिक<BR> [न˚ ब˚] Boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थिक
अनस्थ, -स्थिक<BR> [न˚ ब˚] Boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थः|अनस्थ
अनस्थ, -स्थिक + .{@-स्थः@}<BR>—1 A boneless limb or member.<BR>—2 Without parts, epithet of प्रधान of the Sāṅkhyas or ईश्वरमाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहंवादिन्
अनहंवादिन् <i>a.</i> Prideless, modest; मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी …<BR> (सात्त्विक उच्यते) Bg. 18. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहन्
अनहन् <i>n.</i> [न अहः अप्रशस्तमहः] A bad or unlucky day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अना
अना <i>ind.</i> Ved. Thus, hereby, indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकार
अनाकार <i>a.</i> Formless, shapeless, epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकालः|अनाकाल
अनाकालः [न˚ त˚ निपातः]<BR>—1 Inopportune time.<BR>—2 [आ सम्यक् अन्नादिसंपन्नः कालः आकालः, न˚ त˚ Tv.] Famine<BR> (perhaps an irregular form for अन्नाकाल).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाकालभृतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकालभृतः|अनाकालभृत
अनाकालः + -भृतः one who, to save himself from starvation in a famine, voluntarily<BR> becomes a slave of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाश|अनाकाशः
अनाकाश <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Opaque, not transparent.<BR>—2 Having no transparent atmosphere; differing from it. अपश्यत्कृतमाकाशमनाकाशं<BR> जनार्दनैः Mb. 10. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाशः|अनाकाश
अनाकाश + .{@-शः, -शम्@} Not an atmosphere, one undeserving of its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाशम्
अनाकाश + .{@-शः, -शम्@} Not an atmosphere, one undeserving of its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अनाकुल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not perplexed or confused, calm, collected, self-possessed.<BR>—2 Regular, consistent. अनाकुलान्यब्जसमुद्रतानि (पदानि सप्त) Bu. C. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकृत
अनाकृत <i>a.</i> Not prevented (अनिवारित); unreclaimed ह्वारो<BR> न वक्वा जरणा अनाकृतः Rv. 1. 141. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रन्द
अनाक्रन्द <i>a.</i> Maddened with pain; इति लोकमनाक्रन्दं मोहशोकपरिप्लुतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 331. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रान्त|अनाक्रांत
अनाक्रान्त <i>a.</i> Unassailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रान्ता
अनाक्रान्त + .{@-ता@} [आक्रमितुमयोग्या सर्वतः कण्टकावृतत्वात्, न˚ त˚]<BR> Prickly nightshade, Solanum Jacquini (कण्टकारिवृक्ष) (Mar. रिंगणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षित्
अनाक्षित् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाग
अनाग <i>a.</i> [न आ सम्यग् गच्छति स्वर्गम् अनेन नागः अधर्मः;<BR> न˚ ब˚ Tv.] Sinless; अनागान् सविता देवो वरुणाय वोचत् Rv. 10. 12. 8.<BR> (अनागान् = अपापान्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागा
अनाग + .{@-गा@} N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागत|अनागतं
अनागत <i>a.</i> [न आगतः, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not come or arrived; तावद्भयस्य भेतव्यं यावद्भयमनागतम् H. 1. 54.<BR>—2 Not got or obtained; वर्धिष्णुमाश्रयमनागतमभ्युपैति Śi. 5. 14;<BR> so ˚आर्तव.<BR>—3 Future, to come; see compounds below.<BR>—4 Not learnt or attained, unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतम्
अनागत + .{@-तम्@} The future time, future; ˚तं यः कुरुते स शोभते Pt. 3. 164<BR> he shines (thrives, prospers) who provides for the future; अनागतवतीं<BR> चिन्तामसंभाव्यां करोति यः Pt. 5. 71.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनागतावेक्षणम्, अनागताबाधः, अनागतार्तवा, अनागतविधातृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतावेक्षणम्
अनागत + -अवेक्षणम् looking to the future, provident thought, foresight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागताबाधः|अनागताबाध
अनागत + -आबाधः [अनागतः आबाधः दुःखम्] future (physical) trouble<BR> or calamities, illness &c. affecting the body in times to come;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागताबाधप्रतिषेधनीयम्
अनागत + -आबाधः + ˚प्रतिषेधनीयम्<BR> N. of chapter 24 of the चिकित्सास्थान in Suśruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतार्तवा|अनागतार्त्तवा
अनागत + -आर्तवा [स्त्रीपुष्पविकासनम् आर्तवम्, न आगतमार्तवं यस्याः]<BR> a maiden who has not yet arrived at puberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतविधातृ
अनागत + -विधातृ <i>m.</i> [अनागतम् उद्दिश्य विदधाति] one who provides<BR> for the future, provident, prudent (used as the name of a fish in Pt. 1. 318;<BR> H. 4. 6); अनागतविधाता च प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिस्तथा । द्वावेतौ सुखमेधेते<BR> यद्भविष्यो विनश्यति ॥ (where Dr. Peterson translates the three names<BR> by ‘Mr. Provider-against-a-future-evil’, ‘Mr. Cool-head’, and ‘Mr. what-will-be-will-be’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतिः|अनागति
अनागतिः <i>f.</i> Non-arrival, non-attainment, non-access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अनागम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not come, not present.<BR>—2 [न˚ ब˚] (In law) Without the title-deed or document of possession<BR> (such as purchase deed &c.), anything possessed from time immemorial and<BR> without any documentary proof;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागमोपभोगः|अनागमोपभोग
अनागम + ˚उपभोगः enjoyment of property without such a deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागमः|अनागम
अनागम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Non-arrival.<BR>—2 Non-attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम्य
अनागम्य <i>a.</i> Unapproachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामिन्
अनागामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not coming, not arriving.<BR>—2 Not future, not likely to return. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of the third among<BR> the 4 Buddhist orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामुक
अनागामुक <i>a.</i> Not likely to return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागन्धित
अनागन्धित <i>a.</i> Not smelt; (fig.) not touched or affected; सर्वदोषानागन्धितं<BR> प्रतिवचनमाह Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागस्
अनागस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Innocent, blameless; आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि Ś. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Conferring bliss or happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार|अनाचारः
अनाचार <i>a.</i> Devoid of customary observances or duties, improper<BR> in behaviour, unprincipled, regardless of custom, law or propriety &c.;<BR> also अनाचारिन् in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचारः|अनाचार
अनाचार + .{@-रः, -अनाचरणम्@} Absence of due observances or customary duties,<BR> improper conduct, departure from established usage or principle; अनाचार<BR> is of two kinds विहितस्य अननुष्ठानं निषिद्धस्य चानुष्टानम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचरणम्
अनाचार + .{@-रः, -अनाचरणम्@} Absence of due observances or customary duties,<BR> improper conduct, departure from established usage or principle; अनाचार<BR> is of two kinds विहितस्य अननुष्ठानं निषिद्धस्य चानुष्टानम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाज्ञात
अनाज्ञात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unknown, not properly known.<BR>—2 Surpassing all that has yet been known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अनातप <i>a.</i> Free from or devoid of heat or the blaze of the sun,<BR> not exposed to heat, cool, shady; वाञ्छन्देशमनातपं विधिवशात्तालस्य<BR> मूलं गतः Bh. 2. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातपः|अनातप
अनातप + .{@-पः@} Coolness, shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अनातुर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not eager, indifferent; अनातुरोत्कण्ठितयोः प्रसिध्यता समागमेनापि<BR> रतिर्व मां प्रति । v. l. for अनादर M. 3. 15.<BR>—2 Not fatigued, unwearied; भेजे धर्ममनातुरः R. 1. 21.<BR>—3 Not ill or diseased, well, healthy, in good health; अनातुरः सप्तरात्रमवकीर्णिव्रतं<BR> चरेत् Ms. 2. 187, 4. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मन्
अनात्मन् <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Destitute of spirit or mind.<BR>—2 Not spiritual, corporeal.<BR>—3 One who has not restrained his self; अनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैवशत्रुवत्<BR> Bg. 6. 6. ━<i>m.</i> [अप्रशस्तो भिन्नो वा आत्मा, न˚ त˚] Not self,<BR> another, something different from आत्मन् (spirit or soul) <i>i. e.</i><BR> the perishable body; अप्राप्तः प्राप्यते योऽयमत्यन्तं त्यज्यतेऽथवा ।<BR> जानीयात्तमनात्मानं बुद्धयन्तं वपुरादिकम् ॥ अनात्मन्यात्मबुद्धिर्या साऽविद्या<BR> परिकीर्तिता ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनात्मज्ञा, अनात्मवेदिन्, अनात्मप्रत्यवेक्षा, अनात्मसंपन्न<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मज्ञा
अनात्मन् + -ज्ञा, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devoid of spiritual knowledge or true wisdom.<BR>—2 not knowing oneself, foolish, silly; मा तावदनात्मज्ञे Ś. 6; कथं<BR> कार्यविनिमयेन व्यवहरति मयि ˚ज्ञः M. 1; स्फुटमापदां पदमनात्मवेदिता Śi. 15. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मवेदिन्
अनात्मन् + -ज्ञा, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devoid of spiritual knowledge or true wisdom.<BR>—2 not knowing oneself, foolish, silly; मा तावदनात्मज्ञे Ś. 6; कथं<BR> कार्यविनिमयेन व्यवहरति मयि ˚ज्ञः M. 1; स्फुटमापदां पदमनात्मवेदिता Śi. 15. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मप्रत्यवेक्षा
अनात्मन् + -प्रत्यवेक्षा reflection that there is no spirit or soul (with Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मसंपन्न
अनात्मन् + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> foolish, destitute of qualities (of the soul)<BR> not self-possessed; न त्वेवानात्मसंपन्नाद् वृत्तिमीहेत पण्डितः Pt. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मक
अनात्मक <i>a.</i> [नास्ति आत्मा स्थिरो यत्र] Unreal, transitory,<BR> of an unenduring character, an epithet (with Buddhists) for the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मनीन
अनात्मनीन <i>a.</i> Not adapted to, or for the benefit of, self; disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मवत्|अनात्मवन्त्
अनात्मवत् <i>a.</i> [आत्मा वश्यत्वेन नास्त्यस्य] Not self-possessed;<BR> having no control over the senses; अनात्मवन्तः पशुवद् भुञ्जते येऽप्रमाणतः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्म्य
अनात्म्य <i>a.</i> [आत्मनः इदम् आत्म्यं शरीरम् न˚ ब˚] Impersonal,<BR> incorporeal (अशरीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्म्यम्
अनात्म्य + .{@-त्म्यम्@} Want of affection for oneʼs own family. Pride of the possession<BR> of body &c. ते यद्यनुत्पादितदोषदृष्टयो बलीयसानात्म्यमदेन मन्युना<BR> Bhāg. 4. 3. 16, 4. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्यन्तिक|अनात्यंतिक
अनात्यन्तिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not constant or perpetual, not final.<BR>—2 Intermittent, recurrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अनाथ <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Helpless, poor, forlorn, parentless,<BR> orphan (as a child); widowed (as a wife); having no master or natural<BR> protector, without a protector in general; नाथवन्तस्त्वया लोकास्त्वमनाथा<BR> विपत्स्यसे U. 1. 43; R. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथम्
अनाथ + .{@-थम्@} Ved. Helplessness. किं भ्रातासद्यदनाथं भवाति । Rv. 10. 10. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाथपिण्डदः, अनाथपिण्डिकः, अनाथसमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथपिण्डदः|अनाथपिण्डद
अनाथ + -पिण्डदः, -पिण्डिकः ‘giver of food to the poor’, N. of a merchant<BR> in whose garden Buddha Gautama used to instruct his pupils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथपिण्डिकः|अनाथपिण्डिक
अनाथ + -पिण्डदः, -पिण्डिकः ‘giver of food to the poor’, N. of a merchant<BR> in whose garden Buddha Gautama used to instruct his pupils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथसमा
अनाथ + -समा a poor-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अनादर <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Showing no respect, indifferent,<BR> calm, regardless; M. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरः|अनादर
अनादर + .{@-रः@} [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Disregard,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">Page0081-2</a>]<BR> disrespect, disdain, contempt; षष्टी चानादरे P. II. 3. 38, मन्यकर्मण्यनादरे<BR> विभाषाऽप्राणिषु 17.<BR>—2 Ease, facility (one of the senses of आदर being ‘effort or care’,<BR> see the word); ˚खण्डितशङ्करशरासनः U. 1 (perhaps also ‘without any respect for the bow of the great god’<BR>); अनादरोपात्तघृतैकसायकम् Ki. 14. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरणम्
अनादरणम् Disrespectful conduct, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरिन्
अनादरिन् <i>a.</i> Disrespectful, irreverent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादि|अनादिः
अनादि <i>a.</i> [आदिः कारणं पूर्वकालो वा नास्ति यस्य सः] Having<BR> no beginning, eternal, existing from eternity, epithet of परमेश्वर;<BR> जगदादिरनादिस्त्वम् Ku. 2. 9; अनादिरादिर्गोविन्दः सर्वकारणकारणम्;<BR> also of हिरण्यगर्भ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाद्यनन्त, अनाद्यन्त, अनादिनिधन, अनादिमध्यान्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्यनन्त|अनाद्यनन्तः
अनादि + -अनन्त, -अन्त <i>a.</i> without beginning and end; eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्यनन्तः|अनाद्यनन्त
अनादि + -अनन्त, -अन्त + .({@-अन्तः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्यन्त
अनादि + -अनन्त, -अन्त <i>a.</i> without beginning and end; eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिनिधन
अनादि + -निधन <i>a.</i> having neither beginning nor end, eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिमध्यान्त
अनादि + -मध्यान्त <i>a.</i> having no beginning, middle or end; eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिता
अनादिता, -त्वम्<BR> State of having no beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादित्वम्
अनादिता, -त्वम्<BR> State of having no beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिमत्|अनादिमन्त्
अनादिमत् <i>a.</i> Not produced or effected, having no beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादीनव
अनादीनव <i>a.</i> Faultless; यद्वासुदेवेनादीनमनादीनवमीरितम् Śi. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अनादृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disrespected, despised; अनादृतास्तु यस्यैते सर्वास्तस्याफलाः क्रियाः<BR> Ms. 2. 234; ˚सत्कार not accepting the hospitality.<BR>—2 Not careful, regardless of, indifferent to; अनादृतस्यामरसायकेष्वपि Ki. 14. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृतम्
अनादृत + .{@-तम्@} Disrespect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेय
अनादेय <i>a.</i> Not fit to be taken, unacceptable; inadmissible; अनादेयस्य<BR> चादानादादेयस्य च वर्जनात् Ms. 8. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेशः|अनादेश
अनादेशः Absence of direction or command.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनादेशकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेशकर
अनादेशः + -कर <i>a.</i> doing what is not commanded; or (अन्-आ-देशकर)<BR> not doing what is ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्य
अनाद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 = अनादि q. v.<BR>—2 Not eatable; what ought not to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधार
अनाधार <i>a.</i> Without support, an epithet applicable, according<BR> to the Naiyāyikas, to eternal objects only (such as sky), or to Brahman<BR> according to the Vedāntins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधि
अनाधि <i>a.</i> —1 Without mental pain or anxiety; धनुरधिज्यमनाधिरुपाददे R. 9. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्
अनाधृष् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not checking or not being checked. Av. 6. 21. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्ट
अनाधृष्ट, -ष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invincible, unchecked, irresistible. तमादित्यमिवोद्यन्तमनाघृष्यं<BR> महाबलम् Mb. 5. 179. 11.<BR>—2 Perfect, unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्य
अनाधृष्ट, -ष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invincible, unchecked, irresistible. तमादित्यमिवोद्यन्तमनाघृष्यं<BR> महाबलम् Mb. 5. 179. 11.<BR>—2 Perfect, unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुकृत्य
अनानुकृत्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Inimitable, unparalleled; अनानुकृत्यमपुनश्चकार<BR> Rv. 10. 68. 10, 112. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुद
अनानुद <i>a.</i> Ved. [अनु ददाति; दा-क, न˚ त˚, पृ˚ दीर्घः]<BR> Unsurpassed in giving (अतुल्यदातृ). अनानुदो वृषभो Rv. 2. 23. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुपूर्व्यम्
अनानुपूर्व्यम्<BR>—1 Separation of the different members of compounds by the intervention of others.<BR>—2 Not coming in regular order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुभूतिः|अनानुभूति
अनानुभूतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Neglect, absence of experience or observation,<BR> inattention. ━(pl.) Neglectful, irreligious people; अनानुभूतीरः वधून्वानः<BR> पूर्वीरिन्द्रः शरदस्तर्तरीति Rv. 6. 47. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापद्
अनापद् <i>f.</i> Absence of calamity or misfortune; या वृत्तिस्तां समास्थाय<BR> विप्रो जीवेदनापदि Ms. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापि
अनापि <i>a.</i> [आप्यते-आप् कर्मणि इन् आपिः आप्तो बन्धुश्च, न˚ ब˚<BR> Tv.] Without friends or kindreds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अनाप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not obtained.<BR>—2 Not reaching or attaining, unsuccessful in the attempt to get.<BR>—3 Unfit, not apt, unskilful; युग्यस्थाः प्राजकेऽनाप्ते सर्वे दण्ड्याः<BR> शतं शतम् Ms. 8. 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्तः|अनाप्त
अनाप्त + .{@-प्तः@} A stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्तिः|अनाप्ति
अनाप्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्तृ
अनाप्तृ <i>a.</i> Not getting &c.; अनाप्तुरेनसाम् Śi. 16. 38 not touched by sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभयिन्
अनाभयिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. [आबिभेति आभी-उणा-इनि, आभयिन्, न˚ त˚]<BR> Not at all afraid, fearless, undaunted; अनाभयिन् ररिमा ते Rv. 8. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभू
अनाभू <i>a.</i> Ved. [आभिमुख्येन भवतीत्याभूः स्तोता, न˚ त˚]<BR> Not praising or worshipping, irreligious (अस्तोतृ); not coming in front.<BR> Neglectful, disobliging; इन्द्रः श्नथयन्ननाभुवः Rv. 1. 51. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अनामन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Nameless.<BR>—2 Infamous. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 ‘The nameless’ month, an intercalary month.<BR>—2 The ring-finger; see अनामिका below. ━<i>n.</i> [अननमनः, अनं<BR> जीवनम् अमयति रुजति, अम्-कनिन् Tv.] Piles (अर्शोरोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामक|अनामकं|अनामकः
अनामक <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚ स्वार्थे कन्] Nameless, infamous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामकः|अनामक|अनामकं
अनामक + .{@-कः, -कम@} = अनामन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामकम्
अनामक + .{@-कः, -कम@} = अनामन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामा
अनामा, अनामिका [नास्ति नाम अन्याङ्गुलिवत् यस्याः, स्वार्थे<BR> कन्] The ring-finger; so called because it has no name like the other<BR> fingers; Śat. Br. 14. cf. Tv. तया हि शिवेन ब्रह्मशिरश्छिन्नं, तेन<BR> तस्या अपवित्रजातीयता; अत एव तस्याः पवित्रीकरणार्थं यज्ञादौ पवित्रनामककुशधारणं<BR> तत्र क्रियते । अनामिकाघृता दर्भा ह्येकानामिकयापि वा । द्वाभ्यामनामिकाभ्यां<BR> तु धार्ये दर्भपवित्रके ॥; also पुरा कवीनां गणनाप्रसङ्गे कनिष्ठिकाधिष्ठितकालिदासाः ।<BR> अध्यापि तत्तुल्यकवेरभावादनामिका सार्थवती बभूव ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिका
अनामा, अनामिका [नास्ति नाम अन्याङ्गुलिवत् यस्याः, स्वार्थे<BR> कन्] The ring-finger; so called because it has no name like the other<BR> fingers; Śat. Br. 14. cf. Tv. तया हि शिवेन ब्रह्मशिरश्छिन्नं, तेन<BR> तस्या अपवित्रजातीयता; अत एव तस्याः पवित्रीकरणार्थं यज्ञादौ पवित्रनामककुशधारणं<BR> तत्र क्रियते । अनामिकाघृता दर्भा ह्येकानामिकयापि वा । द्वाभ्यामनामिकाभ्यां<BR> तु धार्ये दर्भपवित्रके ॥; also पुरा कवीनां गणनाप्रसङ्गे कनिष्ठिकाधिष्ठितकालिदासाः ।<BR> अध्यापि तत्तुल्यकवेरभावादनामिका सार्थवती बभूव ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अनामय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति आमयः रोगो यस्य] Free from disease, healthy,<BR> sound; तदन्नमपि भोक्तव्यं जीर्यते यदनामयम् Rām. 3. 50. 18 not<BR> breeding disease; जन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम् Bg. 2. 51<BR> where there is no unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयः|अनामय|अनामयं
अनामय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Good or sound health; health, well-being, welfare;<BR> स भवन्तमनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकमाह Ś. 5; महाश्वेता कादम्बरीमनामयं<BR> पप्रच्छ K. 192 inquired about her health; अप्यनामयं राज्ञः Mv. 1<BR> how does the king do? ब्राह्मणं कुशलं पृच्छेत्क्षत्रबन्धुमनामयम् ।<BR> वैश्यं क्षेमं समागम्य शूद्रमारोग्यमेव च Ms. 2. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयम्
अनामय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Good or sound health; health, well-being, welfare;<BR> स भवन्तमनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकमाह Ś. 5; महाश्वेता कादम्बरीमनामयं<BR> पप्रच्छ K. 192 inquired about her health; अप्यनामयं राज्ञः Mv. 1<BR> how does the king do? ब्राह्मणं कुशलं पृच्छेत्क्षत्रबन्धुमनामयम् ।<BR> वैश्यं क्षेमं समागम्य शूद्रमारोग्यमेव च Ms. 2. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयः|अनामय|अनामयं
अनामय + .{@-यः@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">Page0082-2</a>]<BR> [नास्ति आमयः यस्मात्]<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu (or Śiva according to some); पुण्यकीर्तिरनामयः;<BR> विष्णुर्हि बाह्याभ्यन्तरपीडां निवारयति तस्मादनामयः.<BR>—2 Final release (= मोक्षः) नियतं यातुमनामयाय कालः Bu. C. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयत्|अनामयन्त्
अनामयत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not causing pain or hurt, not hurting. ━<i>n.</i> Health (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयित्नु
अनामयित्नु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not injuring or paining; हस्ताभ्यामनामयित्नुभ्याम् Rv. 10. 137. 7.<BR>—2 Salubrious, curative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिष
अनामिष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without flesh or any bait<BR>—2 bootless, profitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृण
अनामृण <i>a.</i> [आमृणाति हिनस्ति आमृण् क. न˚ ब˚] Having<BR> no injurer or an enemy that can injure (हिंसकरहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृत
अनामृत <i>a.</i> Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायक
अनायक <i>a.</i> Without a leader, disorderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत
अनायत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unrestrained, unchecked.<BR>—2 Not propped or supported.<BR>—3 Not long, of short duration; अनायतस्वभावभङ्गुराणि सुखानि K. 175.<BR>—4 Continuous, close, unseparated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त <i>a.</i> Not dependent; ˚त्तो रोषस्य K. 45 not swayed<BR> by; uncontrolled, independent; एतावज्जन्मसाफल्यं यदनायत्तवृत्तिता<BR> H. 2. 22 freedom, independent livelihood, independence of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायन
अनायन <i>a.</i> [न आयनं चालनं यत्र] Invariable (एकान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास <i>a.</i> Not troublesome or difficult, easy; ममाप्येकस्मिन्<BR> ˚से कर्मणि त्वया सहायेन भवितव्यम् Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासः|अनायास
अनायास + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 Facility, ease, absence of difficulty or exertion; शरीरं पीड्यते<BR> येन शुभेनाप्यशुभेन वा । अत्यन्तं तन्न कुर्वीत अनायासः स उच्यते ॥<BR>—2 Idleness, neglect;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनायासकृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासएन
अनायास + .{@-सः@} + ˚सेन easily, without difficulty, readily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासकृत|अनायासकृतं
अनायास + -कृत <i>a.</i> done easily or readily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासकृतम्
अनायास + -कृत + .({@-तम्@}) an infusion prepared without effort or exertion (prepared<BR> extemporaneously) अनायासकृतं फाण्टं Ak. 2. 94. See फाण्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुष्य
अनायुष्य <i>a.</i> [आयुषे न हितम्, न˚ त˚] Not giving long<BR> life, fatal to long life (such as excessive food, sexual union &c.); अनारोग्यमनायुष्यमस्वर्ग्य<BR> चातिभोजनम् Ms. 2. 57 नहीदृशमनायुष्यं लोके किञ्चन विद्यते । यादृशं<BR> पुरुषस्येह परदारोपसेवनम् ॥ 4. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावर
अनावर <i>a.</i> One without a covering for the head; तथा नौसाधनपरान्<BR> मल्लवाराननावरान् Śiva B. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not ceasing or stopping, continuous, uninterrupted.<BR>—2 Eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारतम्
अनारत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Continuity.<BR>—2 Absolute non-entity (अत्यन्ताभाव). ━<i>adv.</i> Continuously, always;<BR> eternally; अनारतं तेन पदेषु लम्भिताः Ki. 1. 15, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारभ्य
अनारभ्य <i>a.</i> Unfit to be commenced or undertaken. ━<i>ind.</i><BR> Without commencing; without reference to any particular thing <i>e. g.</i> ˚वादः<BR>—1 detached remark (upon sacrifices &c.); किञ्चित्कर्मारभ्य उद्यते उच्यते<BR> इत्यारभ्यवादः न आरभ्यवादः<BR>—2 A statement without any specific reference to any particular thing<BR> or act, न वानारभ्यवादात् । MS. 6. 6. 3, A statement having no definite context.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनारभ्याधीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारभ्याधीत
अनारभ्य + -अधीत <i>a.</i> [न आरभ्य किञ्चिदधीतः] studied or taught or<BR> read without reference to any particular subject (not as part of a regular<BR> or authoritative work); learnt as a detached subject; येषां मन्त्राणां<BR> कर्मविशेषे विनियोगो नोक्तः तेषां मन्त्राणाम् अनारभ्याधीतत्वात् ब्रह्मयज्ञे<BR> एव विनियोग इति मीमांसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भः|अनारम्भ|अनारंभः
अनारम्भः Non-commencement, not undertaking; विकारं खलु परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वा<BR> ˚म्भः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 3; ˚म्भो हि कार्याणां प्रथमं बुद्धिलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भण|अनारंभण
अनारम्भण <i>a.</i> Having no support (for अनालम्बन); also written<BR> अनारम्बण. यदिदमन्तरिक्षमनारम्बणमिव केनाक्रमेण यजमानः<BR> स्वर्गं लोकमाक्रमत Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्य
अनारोग्य <i>a.</i> [नास्ति आरोग्यं यस्मात् न˚ ब˚] Unwholesome,<BR> not conducive to good health, fatal to health; अनायुष्यमनारोग्यमस्वर्ग्यं<BR> चातिभोजनम् Ms. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्यम्
अनारोग्य + .{@-ग्यम्@} Sickness, indisposition;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्यकर
अनारोग्य + .{@-ग्यम्@}˚कर unhealthy, unwholesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव <i>a.</i> Crooked; dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जवम्
अनार्जव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Crookedness (moral also), fraud, insincerity कामिन्यः श्रदधुरनार्जवं<BR> नरेषु Śi. 8. 11.<BR>—2 [नास्ति आर्जवं सारल्यं स्वाच्छन्द्यं वा यस्मिन्] Disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्तव|अनार्त्तव
अनार्तव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>) Unseasonable, inopportune, premature<BR> (as a flower blossoming out of season).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्तवा
अनार्तव + .{@-वा@} A girl who has not attained to puberty (the menstruation period).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य <i>a.</i> Not respectable (not deserving to be styled आर्य),<BR> not polite or decent; vulgar; not belonging to an Arya, unworthy, vile,<BR> base, mean, wretched; अनार्यानार्यलिङ्गिनः Ms. 9. 260; अनार्यायां<BR> समुत्पन्नो ब्राह्मणात् 10. 66; H. 4. 22; कीकटा नाम देशोऽनार्यनिवासः<BR> Nir. void of Āryas; शकुन्तलायामनार्यमाचरितं तेन राज्ञा Ś. 4<BR> the king has behaved basely or unworthily towards Śakuntalā; कदाचिदस्मिन्नप्यनार्योऽनार्यमाचरिष्यति<BR> Ve. 4. न मां कामेष्वनार्येषु प्रचारयितुमर्हसि । Bu. C. 4. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यः|अनार्य|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य + .{@-र्यः@}<BR>—1 One who is not an Ārya.<BR>—2 A country not inhabited by the Āryas.<BR>—3 A Śūdra.<BR>—4 A Mleccha.<BR>—5 An ignoble person.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनार्यकर्मिन्, अनार्यज, अनार्यजुष्ट, अनार्यता, अनार्यतिक्तः, अनार्यसमाचारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यकर्मिन्
अनार्य + -कर्मिन् <i>a.</i> doing work unbecoming an Ārya or becoming only a non-Ārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यज|अनार्य्यज|अनार्य्यजं
अनार्य + -ज <i>a.</i> of vile or base origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यजम्
अनार्य + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) [अनार्यदेशे जातम्] agallochum (being produced in the<BR> country of the Mlecchas &c.). (Mar. अगरु)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यजुष्ट
अनार्य + -जुष्ट <i>a.</i> discarded by the good, not practised or observed<BR> by the Āryas or respectable people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यता|अनार्य्यता
अनार्य + -ता Vileness, unworthiness; अनार्यता निष्टुरता क्रूरता निष्क्रियात्मता ।<BR> पुरुषं व्यञ्जयन्तीह लोके कलुषयोनिजम् ॥ Ms. 10. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यतिक्तः|अनार्यतिक्त|अनार्य्यतिक्त|अनार्य्यतिक्तः
अनार्य + -तिक्तः [अनार्यप्रियः तिक्तः शाक˚ त˚] N. of the plant<BR> Gentiana Cherayta Rox. (Mar. किराईत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यसमाचारः|अनार्यसमाचार
अनार्य + -समाचारः bad conduct; न चानार्यसमाचारः कश्चित् तत्र भविष्यति ।<BR> Mb. 3. 239. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यकम्
अनार्यकम् [अनार्यदेशे भवम् अनार्यकम्] Agallochum or aloe wood.<BR> (Mar. अगरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्ष
अनार्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not belonging to the Ṛṣis, not Vedic; not belonging to the text<BR> of a Vedic hymn (as इति used in the Padapāṭha with certain words<BR> not followed in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">Page0083-2</a>]<BR> the Saṃhitā by इति); सम्बुद्धौ शाकल्यस्येतावनार्षे P. I. 1. 16<BR> (= अवैदिके Sk.).<BR>—2 Not added to a Ṛṣiʼs name (as an affix); P. IV. 1. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्षेय
अनार्षेय = अनार्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्ब|अनालंब|अनालम्बः
अनालम्ब <i>a.</i> Without support or stay; कथंकारमनालम्बा कीर्तिर्द्यामधिरोहति Śi. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्बः|अनालम्ब|अनालंब
अनालम्ब + .{@-म्बः@} Want of support; despondency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्बी
अनालम्ब + .{@-म्बी@} Śivaʼs lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्बुका|अनालंबुका
अनालम्बु(म्भु)का A woman during menstruation (रजस्वला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्भुका|अनालंभुका
अनालम्बु(म्भु)का A woman during menstruation (रजस्वला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालाप|अनालापः
अनालाप <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Reserved, taciturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालापः|अनालाप
अनालाप + .{@-पः@} Reserve, taciturnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालोकः|अनालोक
अनालोकः Absence of light, darkness; अनालोकमयं लोकम् । Śiva B. 28. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालोचित|अनालोचितः
अनालोचित <i>a.</i> Unseen, unheeded, unconsidered, unexpected, not<BR> well considered or examined, rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावया
अनावया <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not yielding or desisting.<BR>—2 (अनावयस्) Not having the power of causing conception; Av. 7. 90. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावर्तिः|अनावर्ति|अनावर्त्ति
अनावर्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-return (to birth), final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावर्तिन्
अनावर्तिन् <i>a.</i> Not recurring or returning; ˚र्ती कालो व्रजति<BR> स वृथा तन्न गणितम् Bh. 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावाप
अनावाप <i>a.</i> One who dose not acquire anything new; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविद्ध
अनाविद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pierced or wounded; unperforated; ˚द्धं रत्नम् Ś. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Unhurt, uninjured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविल|अनाविलः
अनाविल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not turbid or muddy, pure, clear, pleasant (प्रसन्न); व्यकसद्विकसद्विलोचनेभ्यो<BR> दददालोकमनाविलं बलेभ्यः Śi. 20. 38.<BR>—2 Not marshy, wholesome, salubrious, as a country Ms. 7. 69 (रोगोपसर्गाद्यैरनाकुल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्त
अनावृत्त <i>a.</i> Not returning, not repeated, being for the first<BR> time; मलमासेप्यनावृत्तां तीर्थयात्रां विवर्जयेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्तिः|अनावृत्ति
अनावृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-return, absence of repetition or recurrence.<BR>—2 Non-return (to birth), final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृष्टिः|अनावृष्टि
अनावृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Drought, one of the kinds of ईति q. v. तेन<BR> द्वादशवार्षिक्यामनावृष्टयां महात्मना । वृष्टं सस्यविवृद्धयर्थं मिषतो<BR> वज्रपाणिनः ॥ Mb. 3. 126. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाव्रस्कः|अनाव्रस्क
अनाव्रस्कः Uninjured condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश
अनाश <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚ नास्ति आशा यस्य]<BR>—1 Hopeless, despondent.<BR>—2 [नास्ति नाशो यस्य] Imperishable, living, undestroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशक
अनाशक <i>a.</i> [न आ सम्यक् यथेच्छम् आशः अशनं यस्य, न नाशो<BR> यस्य वा, न˚ ब˚ कप्] Devoid of full enjoyment or indestructible, not hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशकम्
अनाशक + .{@-कम्@} Fast, abstaining from eating even to death; यज्ञेन दानेन<BR> तपसाऽनाशकेनैतमेव विदित्वा मुनिर्भवति Bṛ. Ār. Up. 4. 4. 22; Y. 3. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशकायनम्
अनाशकायनम् [न नश्यति अनाशकः आत्मा तस्यायनं प्राप्त्युपायः]<BR> The state of ब्रह्मचर्य, unmarried or studentʼs life, devoted to<BR> contemplation and knowledge of the soul; अथ यदनाशकायनमित्या चक्षते<BR> ब्रह्मचर्यमेव तत् । एष ह्यात्मा न नश्यति यं ब्रह्मचर्येणानुविन्दते<BR> Ch. Up. 8. 5. 3; a course of fasting as a penance (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशस्त
अनाशस्त <i>a.</i> Not praised. यत् चिद्धि सत्य सोमपा अनाशस्ता इव<BR> स्मसि । Rv. 1. 29. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशिन्
अनाशिन् <i>a.</i> [न नश्यति or न कर्मफलमश्नुते; न˚ त˚]<BR> Imperishable, indestructible, as the Soul or Supreme Being; अनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य<BR> Bg. 2. 14. (ईश्वरस्य कर्मफलभोक्तृत्वाभावात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशु
अनाशु <i>a.</i> [नश् उण्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Imperishable, indestructible.<BR>—2 [अश्, उण्. न˚ त˚] Not pervading or occupying.<BR>—3 [न-आशु] Not quick, slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रमिन्
अनाश्रमिन् <i>m.</i> One who does not belong to, or follow, any of the 4<BR> orders of life (गृहस्थाद्याश्रमशून्य); अनाश्रमी न तिष्टेत्तु क्षणमेकमपि<BR> द्विजः; अनाश्रम(मे)वासः not dwelling in any Āśrama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रय|अनाश्रयः
अनाश्रय <i>a.</i> Defenceless, unprotected, isolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रयः|अनाश्रय
अनाश्रय + .{@-यः@} Self-dependence, isolation, absence of support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रव
अनाश्रव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not listening to, obstinate, turning a deaf ear to; तथानुशिष्टापि<BR> अनाश्रवैवासीत् Dk. 57; K. 350; भिषजामनाश्रवः R. 19. 49.<BR>—2 Free from worldly torment or pain; सवितर्कविचारमवाप शान्तं प्रथमं<BR> ध्यानमनाश्रवप्रकारम् । Bu. C. 5. 10<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रित
अनाश्रित <i>a.</i> Not connected with, or dependent on, independent,<BR> detached; non-inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्वस्
अनाश्वस् <i>a.</i> [अश् भोजने क्वसु निपातः इडभावश्च, न˚ त˚<BR> P. III. 2. 109] Not having eaten or enjoyed, fasting; घृतजयघृतेरनाशुषः<BR> Ki. 12. 2; Śi. 14. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्वास
अनाश्वास <i>a.</i> Unfit to depend upon; कर्मण्यस्मिन्ननाश्वासे धूमधूम्रात्मनां<BR> भवान् Bhāg. 1. 18. 12. ━<i>ind.</i> Without rest; A. Rām. 4. 5. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्
अनास् <i>a.</i> [आस्यते निरास्यते ष्टीवनमनेन इति आः मुखं, तन्नास्ति<BR> साधनत्वेन अस्य] Without mouth or face; अनासो दस्यूँरमृणो वधेन<BR> Rv. 5. 29. 10. (Names of demons.) Without the power of speech (आस्यव्यापारशब्दरहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास
अनास, अनासिका <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासिका
अनास, अनासिका <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादित
अनासादित <i>a.</i> Not obtained, not found or met with; not encountered<BR> or attacked; not occurred or having happened, non-existent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनासादितविग्रह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादितविग्रह
अनासादित + -विग्रह <i>a.</i> unused to war, having had no occasion to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्था
अनास्था<BR>—1 Indifference, unconcern, want of consideration; अनास्था बाह्यवस्तुषु<BR> Ku. 6. 63; पिण्डेष्वनास्था खलु भौतिकेषु R. 2. 57; स्त्री पुमानित्यनास्थैषा<BR> वृत्तं हि महितं सताम् Ku. 6. 12 a male or female is no consideration<BR> &c.; Ki. 4. 34.<BR>—2 Want of faith or confidence, want of devotedness, disrespect; अत्यद्भुतैर्मम<BR> हृतस्य तथाप्यनास्था Mv. 2. 39 diffidence. ━<i>a.</i> (-स्थ) Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्थान
अनास्थान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no fixed seat or site.<BR>—2 having or yielding no basis or fulcrum, unfit for a fixed seat (as<BR> water); अनारम्भणे तदवीरयेथामनास्थाने अग्रभणे समुद्रे Rv. 1. 116. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्वाद|अनास्वादः
अनास्वाद <i>a.</i> Without taste, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्वादः|अनास्वाद
अनास्वाद + .{@-दः@} Insipidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्वादित
अनास्वादित <i>a.</i> Untasted; मधु नवमनास्वादितरसम्; Ś. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्राव
अनास्राव <i>a.</i> Without injury or hurt (क्लेशरहित). तेषामसि<BR> त्वमुत्तममनास्रावमरोगणम् Av. 2. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहत|अनाहतं|अनाहतः
अनाहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unbeaten, unwounded, intact.<BR>—2 [आहतं छेदो भोगो वा तन्नास्ति यस्य] New and unbleached (as cloth)<BR> (Mar. कोरें).<BR>—3 Not produced by beating (as sound).<BR>—4 Not multiplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहतम्
अनाहत + .{@-तम्, -तः@} The 4th of the mystical Cakras in the body, (तन्त्रशास्त्रे<BR> प्रसिद्धं ह्रदयस्थितं सुषुम्णामध्यस्थं द्वादशदलपद्मम्); शब्दो<BR> ब्रह्ममयः शब्दोऽनाहतो यत्र दृश्यते । अनाहताख्यं तत् पद्मं मुनिभिः<BR> परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाहतनादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहतः|अनाहत|अनाहतं
अनाहत + .{@-तम्, -तः@} The 4th of the mystical Cakras in the body, (तन्त्रशास्त्रे<BR> प्रसिद्धं ह्रदयस्थितं सुषुम्णामध्यस्थं द्वादशदलपद्मम्); शब्दो<BR> ब्रह्ममयः शब्दोऽनाहतो यत्र दृश्यते । अनाहताख्यं तत् पद्मं मुनिभिः<BR> परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाहतनादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहतनादः|अनाहतनाद
अनाहत + -नादः Sound ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार|अनाहारः
अनाहार <i>a.</i> Abstaining from food, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहारः|अनाहार
अनाहार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Abstinence from food, fasting; अनाहारेणात्मानं व्यापादयिष्यामि H. 1.<BR>—2 Non-production.<BR>—3 Non-seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहारिन्
अनाहारिन् <i>a.</i> Fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार्य|अनाहार्य्य
अनाहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not artificial, natural, not producible.<BR>—2 Not eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहुतिः|अनाहुति
अनाहुतिः <i>f.</i> Not sacrificing; a sacrifice not worthy of that name;<BR> also an improper oblation; तेनास्मद्विश्वामनिरामनाहुतिमपामीवामप<BR> दुष्वप्न्यं सुव Rv. 10. 37. 4 and अपामीवामप विश्वामनाहुतिम् 63. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूत|अनाहूतः
अनाहूत <i>a.</i> Not called, uninvited.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनाहूतोपजल्पिन्, अनाहूतोपविष्ट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूतोपजल्पिन्
अनाहूत + -उपजल्पिन् an uncalled for speaker or boaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूतोपविष्ट
अनाहूत + -उपविष्ट <i>a.</i> seated as an uninvited guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिकेत
अनिकेत <i>a.</i> Houseless, vagrant; having no fixed abode (as a recluse);<BR> अनग्निरनिकेतः स्यान्मुनिर्मूलफलाशनः Ms. 6. 25, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिक्षिप्तधूरः|अनिक्षिप्तधूर
अनिक्षिप्तधूरः N. of a Bodhisattva or deified Buddhist saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिक्षुः|अनिक्षु
अनिक्षुः [न इक्षुः सादृश्ये अप्राशस्त्ये वा नञ्] Not (true) sugarcane,<BR> a sort of long grass or reed producing coarse sugar; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR> (Mar. बोरू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्ण|अनिगीर्णः|अनिगीर्ण्ण
अनिगीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not swallowed.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) Not hidden or concealed, present, not to be supplied (अनपह्नुतभेद);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> in अश्वः श्वेतो धावति, the श्वेतत्व of the horse is<BR> not निगीर्ण or hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रह|अनिग्रहः
अनिग्रह <i>a.</i> Unrestrained, invincible, unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रहः|अनिग्रह
अनिग्रह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 Non-restraint.<BR>—2 Non-refutation.<BR>—3 Not admitting oneʼs defeat in argument;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रहस्थानम्
अनिग्रह + .{@-हः@} + ˚स्थानम् occasion of non-refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिङ्ग्य|अनिंग्य
अनिङ्ग्य <i>a.</i> Not divisible, a word not divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छ
अनिच्छ, -च्छक, -च्छु, -च्छुक, -च्छत् <i>a.</i><BR> Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR> reluctant; अनिच्छन्तमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छक
अनिच्छ, -च्छक, -च्छु, -च्छुक, -च्छत् <i>a.</i><BR> Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR> reluctant; अनिच्छन्तमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छु|अनिच्छुः|अनिछु
अनिच्छ, -च्छक, -च्छु, -च्छुक, -च्छत् <i>a.</i><BR> Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR> reluctant; अनिच्छन्तमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छुक
अनिच्छ, -च्छक, -च्छु, -च्छुक, -च्छत् <i>a.</i><BR> Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR> reluctant; अनिच्छन्तमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छत्|अनिच्छन्त्
अनिच्छ, -च्छक, -च्छु, -च्छुक, -च्छत् <i>a.</i><BR> Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR> reluctant; अनिच्छन्तमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छा
अनिच्छा Unwillingness, indifference, reluctance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित
अनित <i>a.</i> [अन्-इत] Not gone with, unattended, destitute of;<BR> वनितयाऽनितया रजनीवधूः R. 9. 38; पृथु निरन्तरमिष्टभुजान्तरं<BR> वनितयाऽनितया न विषेहिरे Śi. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनितभा
अनित + ˚भा<BR>—1 having no splendour.<BR>—2 N. of a river; मा वो रसानितभा कुभा कुमुर्मा वः सिन्धुर्निरीरमत्<BR> Rv. 5. 53. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अनित्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not eternal or everlasting, transient, non-eternal, perishable (नश्वर)<BR> (opp. नित्य); गन्धवती पृथ्वी सा द्विविधा नित्याऽनित्या च T. S. 9<BR> (अनित्या = कार्यरूपा); see नित्य; यदि नित्यमनित्येन निर्मलं मलवाहिना ।<BR> यशः कायेन लभ्येत तन्न लब्धं भवेन्नु किम् ॥ H. 1. 45; रजस्वलमनित्यं<BR> च भूतावासमिमं त्यजेत् Ms. 6. 77; धर्मोऽनित्यः सुखदुःखेऽप्यनित्ये<BR> जीवोऽनित्यो हेतुरस्याप्यनित्यः Mb.<BR>—2 Occasional, temporary, casual; not peremptory or obligatory as a rule &c., special.<BR>—3 Unusual, extraordinary; वर्णे चानित्ये P. V. 4. 31 (लोहितकः<BR> कोपेन, अन्यथा तु श्वेतवर्ण इति भावः); आनाय्योऽनित्ये III. 1. 127<BR> (स हि गार्हपत्यादानीयतेऽनित्यश्च सततमप्रज्वलनात् Sk.) See VI. 1. 147.<BR>—4 Unsteady, fickle, not permanent; अनित्यं यौवनं रूपम् H. 4. 68;<BR> ˚हृदया हि ताः Rām.<BR>—5 Uncertain, doubtful; अनित्यो विजयो यस्माद् दृश्यते युध्यमानयोः<BR> Ms. 7. 199; विजयस्य ह्यनित्यत्वात् Pt. 3. 22.<BR>—6 (in grammar) A rule or operation which is not invariable or compulsory; optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यम्
अनित्य + .{@-त्यम्@} <i>adv.</i> Occasionally, not permanently, incidentally, casually;<BR> अनित्यं हि स्थितो यस्मात् Ms. 3. 102.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनित्यकर्मन्, अनित्यक्रिया, अनित्यदत्तः, अनित्यदत्तकः, अनित्यदत्रिमः, अनित्यप्रत्यवेक्षा, अनित्यभावः, अनित्यसमः, अनित्यसमासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यकर्मन्
अनित्य + -कर्मन्, -क्रिया an occasional act, such as a sacrifice for a special<BR> purpose, a voluntary and occasional act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यक्रिया
अनित्य + -कर्मन्, -क्रिया an occasional act, such as a sacrifice for a special<BR> purpose, a voluntary and occasional act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्तः|अनित्यदत्त
अनित्य + -दत्तः, -दत्तकः, -दत्रिमः a son given by his parents to another<BR> temporarily (for temporary or preliminary adoption).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्तकः|अनित्यदत्तक
अनित्य + -दत्तः, -दत्तकः, -दत्रिमः a son given by his parents to another<BR> temporarily (for temporary or preliminary adoption).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्रिमः|अनित्यदत्रिम
अनित्य + -दत्तः, -दत्तकः, -दत्रिमः a son given by his parents to another<BR> temporarily (for temporary or preliminary adoption).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यप्रत्यवेक्षा
अनित्य + -प्रत्यवेक्षा (with Buddhists) the consciousness that everything<BR> is perishable and is passing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यभावः|अनित्यभाव
अनित्य + -भावः transitoriness, transient, state, limited nature or existence;<BR> so अनित्यता-त्वम् frailty, instability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यसमः|अनित्यसम
अनित्य + -समः a sophism or fallacious reasoning which generalizes what<BR> is exceptional (as अनित्यत्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यसमासः|अनित्यसमास
अनित्य + -समासः a compound which it is not obligatory to form in every<BR> case (the sense of which may be equally expressed by resolving it into<BR> its constituent members.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद
अनिद <i>a.</i> That which cannot be seen; इत्यभिष्टूय पुरुषं यद्रूपमनिदं<BR> यथा Bhāg. 10. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद्र
अनिद्र <i>a.</i> Sleepless, awake; (fig.) vigilant, watchful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद्रा
अनिद्र + .{@-द्रा@} sleeplessness, vigilance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिधृष्ट
अनिधृष्ट <i>a.</i> Unchecked, unsubdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन
अनिन <i>a.</i> Ved. Having no master or lord (इन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्र|अनिंद्र
अनिन्द्र <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Dispensing with or disregarding<BR> Indra or his worship; (इन्द्रोपासनाशून्य); मामनिन्द्राः कृणवन्ननुक्थाः Rv. 5. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्रियम्
अनिन्द्रियम्<BR>—1 Reason (that which is not the senses).<BR>—2 Not an organ of sense, the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपद्यमान
अनिपद्यमान <i>a.</i> Not falling down (to sleep), untiring; अपश्यं<BR> गोपामनिपद्यमानमा च परा च पथिभिश्चरन्तम् Rv. 1. 164. 31 and 10. 177. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपातः|अनिपात
अनिपातः Not a fall, continuance of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबद्ध
अनिबद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bound अनायतो अनिबद्धः कथायं न्यङ्गुत्तानो अवपद्यते न Rv. 4. 13. 5.<BR>—2 incoherent;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबद्धप्रलापिन्
अनिबद्ध + ˚प्रलापिन् prattling (talking incoherently).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबाध|अनिबाधः
अनिबाध <i>a.</i> Unobstructed; उरौ महाँ अनिबाधे नवर्धापो अग्निम् Rv. 3. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबाधः|अनिबाध
अनिबाध + .{@-धः@} Liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृत
अनिभृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not private or reserved, public, open, not hidden.<BR>—2 Immodest, bold. कामिनामनिभृतान्यपि रम्भास्तम्भकोमलतलेषु नखानि Śi. 10. 66.<BR>—3 Unsteady, not firm, tremulous; ˚करेष्वाक्षिपत्सु प्रियेषु Me. 70;<BR> ˚वेलावीचिबाहुः Ki. 3. 60, 13. 66; असौ सन्ध्याशङ्खध्वनिरनिभृतः<BR> खे विचरति Māl. 2. 12 not hidden, loud; see निमृत also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृष्ट
अनिभृष्ट <i>a.</i> [नि-भ्रंश्-क्त, निपातः न˚ त˚] Unobstructed,<BR> unimpaired, unabated; अनिभृष्टतविषिर्हन्त्योजसा Rv. 2. 25. 4, अनिभृष्टस्तन्वं<BR> वावृधस्व 10. 116. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभ्य
अनिभ्य <i>a.</i> Not wealthy (इभ्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमकः|अनिमक
अनिमकः [अन्-जीवने शब्दे च, भावे बाहु˚ इमन् इत्यनिमः जीवनं,<BR> तेन कायति प्रकाशते, कै-क. Tv.]<BR>—1 A frog (तस्य मरणेपि पुनरुज्जीवनात्).<BR>—2 A cuckoo.<BR>—3 A bee (उभयोरपि तयोः मधुरशब्देन प्रकाशमानत्वात्).<BR>—4 The filament of a lotus, पद्मकेशर.<BR>—5 N. of the tree मधूक Med. (Mar. मोहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमान
अनिमान <i>a.</i> Unbounded, immense (अपरिच्छिन्न); ˚नो धूमकेतुः Rv. 1. 27. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्त
अनिमित्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causeless, groundless; casual, incidental; आलक्ष्यदन्तमुकुलाननिमित्तहासैः<BR> Ś. 7. 17; ˚त्तं मित्रम् disinterested, Dk. 25; ˚उत्कण्ठा M. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्तम्
अनिमित्त + .{@-त्तम्@} Absence of an adequate cause or occasion, causelessness,<BR> groundlessness.<BR>—2 A bad omen, ill-omen; चारुदत्तस्यैव दर्शनमनिमित्तं प्रमार्जयिष्यति<BR> Mk. 6; ममानिमित्तानि हि खेदयन्ति 9. 10; शमनार्थम् अनिमित्तस्य Ve. 2. 3.<BR>—3 Not a valid means of knowledge अनिमित्तं विद्यमानोपलम्भनात् MS. 1. 1. 4.<BR>━<i>adv.</i>, {@-˚तः@}<BR> Groundlessly, causelessly, without any adequate cause; अनिमित्तमिन्दुवदने<BR> किमत्रभवतः पराङ्मुखीभवसि M. 1. 18; अनातुरः स्वानि रवानि न<BR> स्पृशेदनिमित्ततः Ms. 4. 144.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिमित्तनिराक्रिया, अनिमित्तलिङ्गनाशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्तनिराक्रिया
अनिमित्त + -निराक्रिया averting ill omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्तलिङ्गनाशः|अनिमित्तलिङ्गनाश
अनिमित्त + -लिङ्गनाशः a kind of ophthalmic disease ending in total darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषम्
अनिमिषम्^1, -षा, -मेषम् <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR> Without winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR> नेमा आपो अनिमिषं चरन्तीः Rv. 1. 24. 6; अनिमेषं रक्षमाणस्तव<BR> व्रते Rv. 1. 31. 12 and 164. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषा
अनिमिषम्^1, -षा, -मेषम् <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR> Without winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR> नेमा आपो अनिमिषं चरन्तीः Rv. 1. 24. 6; अनिमेषं रक्षमाणस्तव<BR> व्रते Rv. 1. 31. 12 and 164. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेषम्
अनिमिषम्^1, -षा, -मेषम् <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR> Without winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR> नेमा आपो अनिमिषं चरन्तीः Rv. 1. 24. 6; अनिमेषं रक्षमाणस्तव<BR> व्रते Rv. 1. 31. 12 and 164. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिष|अनिमिषं|अनिमिषः
अनिमि(मे)ष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not winking, steadfastly or intently fixed; ˚लोचनं सुचिरमालोक्य<BR> K. 102; ˚पक्ष्मणा 131; शतैस्तमक्ष्णामनिमेषवृत्तिभिः R. 3. 43;<BR> ˚दर्शनरमणीयैः K. 50 (Pun) fish and twinkleless glances.<BR>—2 Vigilant.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">Page0086-1</a>]<BR> watchful.<BR>—3 Open (as eyes, flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमि(मे)ष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not winking, steadfastly or intently fixed; ˚लोचनं सुचिरमालोक्य<BR> K. 102; ˚पक्ष्मणा 131; शतैस्तमक्ष्णामनिमेषवृत्तिभिः R. 3. 43;<BR> ˚दर्शनरमणीयैः K. 50 (Pun) fish and twinkleless glances.<BR>—2 Vigilant.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">Page0086-1</a>]<BR> watchful.<BR>—3 Open (as eyes, flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषः|अनिमिष|अनिमिषं
अनिमि(मे)ष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 A god (for the eyes of gods do not twinkle); देवैरिवानिमिषदृष्टिभिरीक्ष्यमाणः Śi. 5. 57.<BR>—2 A fish. cf. सुरे मत्स्ये चानिमिषः … Nm. यथा चानिमिषाः स्थूला<BR> जालं छित्वा पुनर्जलम् Mb. 12. 300. 12.<BR>—3 Viṣṇu Bhāg. 1. 1. 4.<BR>—4 N. of Mahākāla.<BR>—5 A particular mode of sexual intercourse.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिमिषाचार्यः, अनिमिषदृष्टि, अनिमिषनयन, अनिमिषलोचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषाचार्यः|अनिमिषाचार्य|अनिमिषाचार्य्य|अनिमिषाचार्य्यः
अनिमिष + -आचार्यः Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषदृष्टि
अनिमिष + -दृष्टि, -नयन, -लोचन <i>a.</i> looking steadfastly or with a<BR> fixed gaze, gazing intently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषनयन
अनिमिष + -दृष्टि, -नयन, -लोचन <i>a.</i> looking steadfastly or with a<BR> fixed gaze, gazing intently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषलोचन
अनिमिष + -दृष्टि, -नयन, -लोचन <i>a.</i> looking steadfastly or with a<BR> fixed gaze, gazing intently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषीय
अनिमिषीय <i>a.</i> Relating to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियत|अनियतं
अनियत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uncontrolled, unrestricted.<BR>—2 Indefinite, uncertain, not fixed; irregular (forms also); ˚वेलम्<BR> आहारोऽश्यते Ś. 2 at irregular hours.<BR>—3 Causeless, casual, incidental, occasional; ˚रुदितस्मितम् (वदनकमलकम्)<BR> U. 4. 4; Māl. 10. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनियताङ्कः, अनियतात्मन्, अनियतपुंस्का, अनियतवृत्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियताङ्कः|अनियताङ्क|अनियतांक
अनियत + -अङ्कः an indeterminate digit (in Math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियतात्मन्
अनियत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> not self-possessed, whose soul is not properly controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियतपुंस्का
अनियत + -पुंस्का a woman loose in conduct, unchaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियतवृत्ति
अनियत + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having no regular or fixed employment or application (as a word).<BR>—2 having no regular income.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियन्त्रण
अनियन्त्रण <i>a.</i> Unrestrained, uncontrolled, free; ˚अनुयोगो<BR> नाम तपस्विजनः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियमः|अनियम
अनियमः<BR>—1 Absence of rule, control, regulation or fixed order; no settled rule<BR> or direction; प्रामाण्यबुद्धिर्वेदेषु साधनानामनेकता । उपास्यानामनियम<BR> एतद्धर्मस्य लक्षणम् ॥ Lok. Tilak. पञ्चमं लघु सर्वत्र सप्तमं<BR> द्विचतुर्थयोः । षष्ठे पादे गुरु ज्ञेयं शेषेष्वनियमो मतः ॥ Chand. M.<BR>—2 Irregularity, uncertainty. indefiniteness, vagueness, doubt.<BR>—3 Improper conduct, अनियामित <i>a.</i> Irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियुक्त|अनियुक्तः
अनियुक्त <i>a.</i> Not appointed or authoritative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियुक्तः|अनियुक्त
अनियुक्त + .{@-क्तः@} An assessor at a court who has not been formally appointed<BR> and who is not entitled to vote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर
अनिर <i>a.</i> [न ईरयितुं शक्यते, ईर्-क पृ˚ ह्रस्वः] That cannot<BR> be propelled or driven along; अप त्या अस्थुरनिरा Rv. 8. 48. 11 (प्रेरयितुमशक्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरा
अनिर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Want of food; utter destitution (अन्नरहितदारिद्र्यम्); युयुतमस्मदनिराममीवाम् Rv. 7. 71. 2.<BR>—2 [नास्ति इरा अन्नं यस्याः पं˚ ब˚] A calamity such as अतिवृष्टि,<BR> अनावृष्टि (= ईति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरवसित
अनिरवसित <i>a.</i> [p. p. of निर् + अव + सो €4 P.] Śūdras who<BR> are not expelled (from dish), <i>i. e.</i> those Śūdras who are not regarded<BR> so low as to defile the plates and vessels permanently in which they might<BR> have taken their meal. cf. पात्रादनिरवसितानाम् । यैर्मुक्ते पात्रं संस्कारेण<BR> शुध्यति ते अनिरवसिताः । यैर्भुक्ते पात्रं संस्कारेणापि न शुध्यति ते निरवसिताः<BR> शूद्राणामनिरवसितानाम्; (P. II. 4. 10. Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिराकरणम्
अनिराकरणम् Not obstructing or warding off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिराकृत|अनिराकृतः
अनिराकृत <i>a.</i> Unobstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरिण
अनिरिण <i>a.</i> even, without any ups and downs; तस्मिन्देशे त्वनिरिणे<BR> ते तु युद्धमरोचयन् Mb. 9. 55. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुक्त
अनिरुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not articulated or clearly spoken.<BR>—2 Not clearly stated or explained, vague, not plain or well-defined;<BR> ˚क्तप्रातःसवनः प्रथमः Kāty.; एतास्मिन्नदृश्येऽनात्म्येऽनिरुक्ते Ait. Br.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिरुक्तगानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुक्तगानम्
अनिरुक्त + -गानम् indistinct singing or humming, a particular mode of chanting<BR> the सामवेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्ध|अनिरुद्धं|अनिरुद्धः
अनिरुद्ध <i>a.</i> Unobstructed, free, uncontrolled, self-willed, unruly, ungovernable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धः|अनिरुद्ध|अनिरुद्धं
अनिरुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}<BR>—1 A spy, secret emissary.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Pradyumna. [Aniruddha was the son of Kāma and grandson<BR> of Kṛṣṇa. Uṣā, the daughter of a demon named Bāṇa, fell in love<BR> with him and had him brought by magic influence to her apartments in her<BR> fatherʼs city of Śoṇitapura. Bāṇa sent some guards to seize him, but<BR> the brave youth slew his assailants with only an iron club. At last, however,<BR> he was secured by means of magic powers. On discovering where Aniruddha<BR> had been carried, Kṛṣṇa, Balarāma and Kāma went to rescue him and<BR> a great battle was fought. Bāṇa, though aided by Śiva and Skanda, was<BR> vanquished, but his life was spared at the intercession of Śiva, and<BR> Aniruddha was carried home to Dvārakā with Uṣā as his wife. He had<BR> also another wife Rochanā, grand-daughter of king Rukmin of Vidarbha,<BR> who bore him a son named Vajra.].<BR>—3 Also N. of Viṣṇu; and of Śiva; of an Arhat, a contemporary of Buddha.<BR> (अनिरुद्धो हि लोकेषु महानात्मेति कथ्यते Mb. 12. 340. 30.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धम्
अनिरुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} A cord or rope (for fastening cattle).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिरुद्धपथम्, अनिरुद्धभाविनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धपथम्
अनिरुद्ध + -पथम् [न निरुद्धः पन्था यत्र ब˚]<BR>—1 unobstructed path.<BR>—2 the sky, atmosphere (तत्र कस्यापि गतिरोधनाभावात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धभाविनी
अनिरुद्ध + -भाविनी Aniruddhaʼs wife Uṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णयः|अनिर्णय
अनिर्णयः Uncertainty, indecision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दश
अनिर्दश, अनिर्दशाह <i>a.</i> [न निर्गतानि दशाहानि यस्य]<BR> Within the 10 days of impurity caused either by childbirth or death; विगतं<BR> तु विदेशस्थं शृणुयाद्यो ह्यनिर्दशम् Ms. 5. 75; अनिर्दशाया गोः क्षीरम् 5. 8, 5. 79, 4. 212, 217;<BR> not ten days old; अनिर्दशाहां गां सूताम् Ms. 8. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दशाह
अनिर्दश, अनिर्दशाह <i>a.</i> [न निर्गतानि दशाहानि यस्य]<BR> Within the 10 days of impurity caused either by childbirth or death; विगतं<BR> तु विदेशस्थं शृणुयाद्यो ह्यनिर्दशम् Ms. 5. 75; अनिर्दशाया गोः क्षीरम् 5. 8, 5. 79, 4. 212, 217;<BR> not ten days old; अनिर्दशाहां गां सूताम् Ms. 8. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दिष्ट
अनिर्दिष्ट <i>a.</i> Undefined, not specified; क्व ˚कारणं गम्यते<BR> V. 2 without a definite aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देशः|अनिर्देश
अनिर्देशः Absence of positive rule or direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश्य|अनिर्द्देश्य
अनिर्देश्य <i>a.</i> Undefinable, ineffable, indescribable, inexplicable,<BR> incomparable; ˚सुखः खर्गः कस्तं विस्मारयिष्यति V. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश्यम्
अनिर्देश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} An epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्धारित|अनिर्धारितः
अनिर्धारित <i>a.</i> Not determined or ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्मल|अनिर्म्मल|अनिर्म्मलः
अनिर्मल <i>a.</i> Dirty, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्माल्या|अनिर्म्माल्या
अनिर्माल्या N. of a medicinal plant, पिण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनम्
अनिर्वचनम् Silence, not uttering (anything) loudly; देवतायास्त्वनिर्वचनम्<BR> &c. MS. 10. 8. 52(where Śabara explains अनिर्वचनम् as तूष्णीभावः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीय|अनिर्व्वचनीयः
अनिर्वचनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unutterable, indescribable, undefinable, epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR>—2 Improper to be mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीयम्
अनिर्वचनीय + .{@-यम्@} (In Vedānta)<BR>—1 Māyā or illusion,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">Page0087-1</a>]<BR> ignorance.<BR>—2 The world.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिर्वचनीयसर्वस्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीयसर्वस्वम्
अनिर्वचनीय + -सर्वस्वम् N. of a work by Śrīharṣa, also called खण्डनखण्डखाद्य;<BR> तत्र सर्वेषां पदार्थानाम् इदंतया निर्वक्तुमशक्यता दर्शिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वाण
अनिर्वाण <i>a.</i> Unwashed; unbathed; अरुंतुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य<BR> दन्तिनः R. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वाहः|अनिर्वाह|अनिर्व्वाह|अनिर्व्वाहः
अनिर्वाहः<BR>—1 Non-completion; non-accomplishment.<BR>—2 Inconclusiveness.<BR>—3 Insufficiency of income, being straitened in means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्विद|अनिर्व्विद
अनिर्विद <i>a.</i> Not fatigued or tired; अनिर्विदाया विदधे विधात्रा Śi. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्विण्ण|अनिर्व्विण्ण|अनिर्व्विण्णः
अनिर्विण्ण <i>a.</i> Not depressed or fatigued; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वेदः|अनिर्वेद
अनिर्वेदः Non-depression, absence of dejection or despondency; self-reliance,<BR> plucking up courage; अनिर्वेदः श्रियो मूलमनिर्वदः परं सुखम् । अनिर्वेदो<BR> हि सततं सर्वार्थेष्वनुवर्तते Rām. 5. 12. 10. अनिर्वेदप्राप्याणि<BR> श्रेयांसि V. 4; cf. ‘Faint heart never won fair lady’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृत|अनिर्व्वृत
अनिर्वृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ill at ease, uneasy, discomposed, unhappy.<BR>—2 Unaccomplished, unfulfilled (अनिर्वृत्त also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृतिः|अनिर्वृति|अनिर्व्वृति
अनिर्वृतिः, -त्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Uneasiness, anxiety, disquietude.<BR>—2 Poverty, destitution; अनिर्वृतिनिशाचरी मम गृहान्तरालं गता Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृत्तिः|अनिर्वृत्ति
अनिर्वृतिः, -त्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Uneasiness, anxiety, disquietude.<BR>—2 Poverty, destitution; अनिर्वृतिनिशाचरी मम गृहान्तरालं गता Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वेश
अनिर्वेश <i>a.</i> Destitute of employment, wretched, miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलः|अनिल
अनिलः [अनिति जीवति अनेन, अन् इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54]<BR>—1 Wind; वायुरनिलममृतमथेदम् Īśop. 17. प्राणानामनिलेन वृत्तिरुचिता<BR> Ś. 7. 12; स सखा दीप इवानिलाहतः Ku. 4. 30. (The number of winds<BR> is 7:− आवहो निवहश्चैव उद्वहः संवहस्तथा । विवहः प्रवहश्चैव<BR> परिवाहस्तथैव च ॥ and these are again subdivided into 7 divisions,<BR> the total number being 49).<BR>—2 The god of wind.<BR>—3 One of the subordinate deities, 49 of whom form the class of winds.<BR>—4 N. of one of the 8 Vasus, <i>i. e.</i> the fifth.<BR>—5 The wind in the body, one of the humours; ˚हन्, ˚हृत्, ˚घ्न.<BR>—6 Rheumatism or any disease referred to disorder of the wind.<BR>—7 The letter य्.<BR>—8 Symbolical expression for the number 49.<BR>—9 N. of the lunar asterism स्वाति.<BR>—10 N. of Viṣṇu (तस्य प्राणात्मना सर्वदेहधारणात् तथात्वम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिलायनम्, अनिलाशन, अनिलाशिन्, अनिलान्तकः, अनिलात्मजः, अनिलामयः, अनिलघ्न, अनिलहन्, अनिलहृत्, अनिलघ्नकः, अनिलपर्यायः, अनिलप्रकृति, अनिलभद्रकः, अनिलव्याधिः, अनिलसखः, अनिलसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलायनम्
अनिलः + -अयनम् way or course of the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलाशन
अनिलः + -अशन, -आशिन् <i>a.</i> [अनिलमश्नातीति]<BR>—1 feeding on the wind, fasting.<BR>—2 a serpent. आर्जवेन विजानामि नासौ देवोऽनिलाशन Mb. 12. 360. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलाशिन्
अनिलः + -अशन, -आशिन् <i>a.</i> [अनिलमश्नातीति]<BR>—1 feeding on the wind, fasting.<BR>—2 a serpent. आर्जवेन विजानामि नासौ देवोऽनिलाशन Mb. 12. 360. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलान्तकः|अनिलान्तक
अनिलः + -अन्तकः (wind-destroying) N. of a plant (Iṅgudī) or अङ्गारपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलात्मजः|अनिलात्मज
अनिलः + -आत्मजः son of the wind, epithet of Bhīma and Hanūmat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलामयः|अनिलामय
अनिलः + -आमयः [अनिलकृतः आमयः शाक˚ त˚]<BR>—1 flatulence.<BR>—2 rheumatism (वातरोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलघ्न
अनिलः + -घ्न, -हन्, -हृत् <i>a.</i> curing disorders from wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलहन्
अनिलः + -घ्न, -हन्, -हृत् <i>a.</i> curing disorders from wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलहृत्
अनिलः + -घ्न, -हन्, -हृत् <i>a.</i> curing disorders from wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलघ्नकः|अनिलघ्नक
अनिलः + -घ्नकः a large tree (बिभीतक) Terminalia Belerica. (Mar. बेहडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलपर्यायः|अनिलपर्याय
अनिलः + -पर्यायः pain and swelling of the eyelids and outer parts of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलप्रकृति|अनिलप्रकृतिः
अनिलः + -प्रकृति <i>a.</i> of a windy nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलप्रकृतिः|अनिलप्रकृति
अनिलः + -प्रकृति + .({@-तिः@}) N. of the planet Saturn.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">Page0087-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलभद्रकः|अनिलभद्रक
अनिलः + -भद्रकः a kind of chariot. With regard to shape the chariots<BR> are divided into seven classes:− नभस्वद्भद्रक, प्रभञ्जनभद्रक,<BR> निवातभद्रक, पवनभद्रक, परिषद्भद्रक, इन्द्रकभद्रक, and अनिलभद्रक<BR> Māna. 43. 112-115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलव्याधिः|अनिलव्याधि
अनिलः + -व्याधिः derangement of the bodily (internal) wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलसखः|अनिलसख
अनिलः + -सखः, -सारथिः fire (the friend of wind); जनमेजयस्य वो<BR> यज्ञे धक्ष्यत्यनिलसारथिः Mb. 1. 15. 1; so ˚बन्धुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलसारथिः|अनिलसारथि
अनिलः + -सखः, -सारथिः fire (the friend of wind); जनमेजयस्य वो<BR> यज्ञे धक्ष्यत्यनिलसारथिः Mb. 1. 15. 1; so ˚बन्धुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलबन्धुः|अनिलबन्धु
अनिलः + -सखः, -सारथिः fire (the friend of wind); जनमेजयस्य वो<BR> यज्ञे धक्ष्यत्यनिलसारथिः Mb. 1. 15. 1; so ˚बन्धुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोडित
अनिलोडित <i>a.</i> Inexperienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलम्भसमाधिः|अनिलम्भसमाधि
अनिलम्भसमाधिः unsupported meditation; Name of a peculiar kind<BR> of meditation (Buddh.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्लोडित
अनिर्लोडित <i>a.</i> Not well considered; not-examined thoroughly. ˚कार्यस्य<BR> वाग्जालं वाग्मिनो वृथा Śi. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवर्तन|अनिवर्त्तन
अनिवर्तन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not turning away, firm, steadfast.<BR>—2 Right, not fit to be abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवर्तिन्|अनिवर्त्तिन्
अनिवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Brave, not retreating; also an epithet of Viṣṇu and the Almighty God.<BR>—2 Not returning; यौवनमनिवर्ति यातं तु K. P. 10.<BR>—3 Non-recurring (account); आवर्तकोऽनिवर्ती च व्ययायौ तु पृथग् द्विधा<BR> Śukra. 2. 339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिविशमान
अनिविशमान <i>a.</i> Not sitting down or retiring to rest, ever going,<BR> restless; पुनाना यन्त्यनिविशमानाः Rv. 7. 49. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवेशन
अनिवेशन <i>a.</i> Ved. Having no place of rest. अतिष्टन्तीनामनिवेशनानां<BR> काष्ठानां मध्ये निहितं शरीरम् Rv. 1. 32. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिविष्ट
अनिविष्ट <i>a.</i> Not married; कलत्रं स्वयमनिविष्टः Avimāraka, I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश|अनिशं
अनिश <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Nightless, <i>i. e.</i> uninterrupted, incessant (निशा तद्धेतुकतेनोपचारात्<BR> चेष्टाविनाशः सा नास्ति यस्य).<BR>—2 Ever afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिशम्
अनिश + .{@-शम्@} <i>ind.</i> Incessantly, ceaselessly; अनिशमपि मकरकेतुर्मनसो<BR> रुजमावहन्नभिमतो मे Ś. 3, 4; Bv. 2. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिशित
अनिशित <i>a.</i> Ved. Not resting or reposing, incessant; याद्राध्यं<BR> वरुणो योनिमप्यमनिशितं निमिषि जर्भुराणः Rv. 2. 38. 8, and 9. 96. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिशितसर्ग
अनिशित + ˚सर्ग incessantly flowing; Rv. 10. 89. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषिद्ध
अनिषिद्ध, अनिषेध्र Ved. <i>a.</i> Unforbidden, unchecked, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषेध्र
अनिषिद्ध, अनिषेध्र Ved. <i>a.</i> Unforbidden, unchecked, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्कृत
अनिष्कृत <i>a.</i> Unfinished, not settled.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिष्कृतैनस्, अनिष्कृतपाप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्कृतैनस्
अनिष्कृत + -एनस्, -पाप having the guilt not settled, <i>i. e.</i> unexpiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्कृतपाप
अनिष्कृत + -एनस्, -पाप having the guilt not settled, <i>i. e.</i> unexpiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ट|अनिष्टः
अनिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unwished, undesirable; unfavourable, disagreeable, ill (with gen.);<BR> ध्यायत्यनिष्टं यत्किञ्चित्पाणिग्राहस्य चेतसा Ms. 9. 21 whatever ill<BR> she thinks of her husband.<BR>—2 Evil, forbidden.<BR>—3 Bad, unlucky, ominous.<BR>—4 Not honoured with a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टम्
अनिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} An evil, mishap, misfortune, calamity, disadvantage; a crime,<BR> offence, wrong, unwelcome thing; ˚एकबुद्धि Māl. 8. 12; भवत्यनिष्टादपि<BR> नाम दुःसहान्मनस्विनीनां प्रतिपत्तिरीदृशी Ku. 5. 42; ill-omen; प्रातरेव<BR> ˚दर्शनं जातम् H. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिष्टानुबन्धिन्, अनिष्टापत्तिः, अनिष्टाशंसिन्, अनिष्टग्रहः, अनिष्टदुष्टधी, अनिष्टप्रसङ्गः, अनिष्टफलम्, अनिष्टशङ्का, अनिष्टहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टानुबन्धिन्
अनिष्ट + -अनुबन्धिन् <i>a.</i> followed by or attended with calamities; विषयोपभोगेषु<BR> ˚बन्धिषु यः सुखबुद्धिमारोपयति K. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टापत्तिः|अनिष्टापत्ति
अनिष्ट + -आपत्तिः <i>f.</i>, {@-आपादनम्@}<BR> getting what is not desired, an undesired occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टाशंसिन्
अनिष्ट + -आशंसिन् <i>a.</i> (˚सूचक)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">Page0088-1</a>]<BR> indicating or boding ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टग्रहः|अनिष्टग्रह
अनिष्ट + -ग्रहः an evil or malignant planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टदुष्टधी
अनिष्ट + -दुष्टधी <i>a.</i> having an evil and corrupt mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टप्रसङ्गः|अनिष्टप्रसङ्ग|अनिष्टप्रसंग
अनिष्ट + -प्रसङ्गः<BR>—1 an undesired occurrence.<BR>—2 connection with a wrong object, argument or rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टफलम्
अनिष्ट + -फलम् an evil result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टशङ्का|अनिष्टशंका
अनिष्ट + -शङ्का fear of evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टहेतुः|अनिष्टहेतु
अनिष्ट + -हेतुः an evil omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टिन्
अनिष्टिन् <i>a.</i> One who has not sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टृत
अनिष्टृत <i>a.</i> Ved. Unhurt; य उग्रः सन्ननिष्टृतः स्थिरो रणाय<BR> संस्कृतः Rv. 8. 33. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टा
अनिष्टा Unsteadfastness, unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ठुर
अनिष्ठुर <i>a.</i> Not harsh on cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ण
अनिष्ण <i>a.</i> Not skilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पत्तिः|अनिष्पत्ति
अनिष्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-accomplishment, non-completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पत्रम्
अनिष्पत्रम् <i>ind.</i> [निःसृतं पत्रं पक्षो यत्र तादृशं न भवति]<BR> So that the arrow (the feathery portion of it) does not come out on the<BR> other side; <i>i. e.</i> not with great force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिसर्ग
अनिसर्ग <i>a.</i> Unnatural, affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्ण
अनिस्तीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not crossed, set aside or got rid of<BR>—2 Unanswered, unrefuted (as a charge).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनिस्तीर्णाभियोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्णाभियोगः|अनिस्तीर्णाभियोग
अनिस्तीर्ण + -अभियोगः a defendant who has not cleared himself of a charge<BR> (by refuting it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकः|अनीक|अनीकं
अनीकः, -कम<BR> [अनिति जीवत्यनेन; अन्-ईकन् Uṇ. 4. 16-17]<BR>—1 Army, forces; troop, host; दृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवानीकम् Bg. 1. 2. महारथानां<BR> प्रतिदन्त्यनीकम् Ki. 16. 14. पदातीश्च महीपालः पुरोऽनीकस्य योजयेत् H. 3. 73.<BR>—2 A collection, group, mass; नवाम्बुदानीकमुहूर्तलाञ्छने R. 3. 53.<BR>—3 Battle, fight, combat.<BR>—4 A row, line, marching column.<BR>—5 Front, head; chief; रथेषु नोऽनीकेष्वधिश्रियः Rv. 8. 20. 12. (सेनामुखेषु);<BR> अग्निर्वै देवानामनीकम् Śat. Br.; अग्निमनीकं कृत्वा. cf. अनीकस्तु<BR> रणे सैन्ये सन्देहेऽपि च कथ्यते Nm.<BR>—6 Face, countenance, <i>ibid.</i> (मुखम्) (तस्य प्राणवायुनिस्सारणात्<BR> तथात्वम्); splendour; brilliance; form (तेजस्); स्वनीक Rv. 7. 1. 23, 3. 6<BR> (mostly Ved. in these two senses)<BR>—7 Edge, point.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनीकस्थः, अनीकस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकम
अनीकः, -कम<BR> [अनिति जीवत्यनेन; अन्-ईकन् Uṇ. 4. 16-17]<BR>—1 Army, forces; troop, host; दृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवानीकम् Bg. 1. 2. महारथानां<BR> प्रतिदन्त्यनीकम् Ki. 16. 14. पदातीश्च महीपालः पुरोऽनीकस्य योजयेत् H. 3. 73.<BR>—2 A collection, group, mass; नवाम्बुदानीकमुहूर्तलाञ्छने R. 3. 53.<BR>—3 Battle, fight, combat.<BR>—4 A row, line, marching column.<BR>—5 Front, head; chief; रथेषु नोऽनीकेष्वधिश्रियः Rv. 8. 20. 12. (सेनामुखेषु);<BR> अग्निर्वै देवानामनीकम् Śat. Br.; अग्निमनीकं कृत्वा. cf. अनीकस्तु<BR> रणे सैन्ये सन्देहेऽपि च कथ्यते Nm.<BR>—6 Face, countenance, <i>ibid.</i> (मुखम्) (तस्य प्राणवायुनिस्सारणात्<BR> तथात्वम्); splendour; brilliance; form (तेजस्); स्वनीक Rv. 7. 1. 23, 3. 6<BR> (mostly Ved. in these two senses)<BR>—7 Edge, point.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनीकस्थः, अनीकस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकस्थः|अनीकस्थ
अनीकः + -स्थः<BR>—1 a warrior, combatant.<BR>—2 a sentinel, (armed) watch. अभिचक्राम भर्तारमनीकस्थः कृताञ्जलिः<BR> Rām. 6. 32. 34.<BR>—3 an elephant-driver, or its trainer (द्राविडी ‘अने’ = हत्ती); अनीकस्थप्रमाणैः<BR> प्रशस्तव्यञ्जनाचारान् हस्तिनो गृह्णीयुः Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>—4 a war-drum or trumpet.<BR>—5 a signal, mark; sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकस्थानम्
अनीकः + -स्थानम् a military station; Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकवत्|अनीकवन्त्
अनीकवत् <i>a.</i> Ved. forming the face or front rank; occupying the<BR> foremost rank. अग्नयेऽनीकवते पुरोडाशम् T. S. 1. 8. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकशः
अनीकशः <i>adv.</i> In rows or columns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकिनी
अनीकिनी [अनीकानां सङ्घः; अनीकं युद्धं प्रयोजनतया अस्त्यस्याः<BR> इति वा, अनीक-इनि]<BR>—1 An army, host, forces.<BR>—2 Three chamūs or one-tenth of a complete army (अक्षौहिणी); 10935<BR> foot, 6561 horse, 2187 elephants and as many chariots. चमूस्तु पृतनास्तिस्रस्तिस्रश्चम्वस्त्वनीकिनी ।<BR> अनीकिनी दशगुणा प्राहुरक्षौहिणीं बुधाः ॥ Mb. 1. 2. 22<BR>—3 A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीच
अनीच <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not low or vile, decent, respectable.<BR>—2 Not pronounced with the अनुदात्त accent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनीचानुवर्तिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचानुवर्तिन्|अनीचानुवर्त्तिन्
अनीच + -अनुवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> not associating with low or vile persons. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR> a faithful husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिचिदर्शिन्
अनिचिदर्शिन् <i>m.</i> A form of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीड
अनीड <i>a.</i> Having no abode (body), incorporeal, epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीतिः|अनीति
अनीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Impropriety, immorality; injustice, wrong act; indiscretion, foolish conduct.<BR>—2 (न ईतिः) Freedom from calamity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनीतिज्ञ, अनीतिविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीतिज्ञ
अनीतिः + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i> impolite, not discreet, not conversant with policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीतिविद्
अनीतिः + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i> impolite, not discreet, not conversant with policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीप्सित
अनीप्सित <i>a.</i> Not desired (<i>p. p.</i> from the desiderative of आप्)<BR> तथायुक्तंचानीप्सितम्; (cf. P. I. 4. 50).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीर्षु
अनीर्षु <i>a.</i> Not envious, not conceiving malice; मृतपुत्रा भृतामात्या<BR> भृतदारा ह्यनीर्षवः Mb. 12. 221. 31 (Poona Critical Edition, B. O. R. I.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनील
अनील <i>a.</i> Not blue, white &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीलवाजिन्
अनील + ˚वाजिन् <i>m.</i> ‘white-horsed’;<BR> N. of Arjuna; इतीरिताकूतमनीलवाजिनम् Ki. 14. 26, 42<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश|अनीशः
अनीश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no lord or superior, paramount, supreme, without a controller,<BR> uncontrolled; सर्वप्रभुरनीशस्त्वम् R. 10. 20.<BR>—2 Not a master or lord, having no mastery or control over; not master<BR> of (with gen.); powerless; गात्राणामनीशोऽस्मि संवृत्तः Ś. 2; अनीशया<BR> शरीरस्य हृदयं स्ववशं मयि न्यस्तम् V. 2. 19; उर्ध्वं पितुश्च मातुश्च<BR> समेत्य भ्रातरः समम् । भजेरन् पैतृकं रिक्थमनीशास्ते हि जीवतोः ॥ Ms. 9. 104.<BR>—3 Not oneʼs own master, not independent (अस्वतन्त्र); एको ह्यनीशः सर्वत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीशः|अनीश
अनीश + .{@-शः@} N. of Viṣṇu (सर्वनियन्ता अनन्यस्वामिको हि सः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीशा
अनीश + .{@-शा@} Helplessness (दीनभाव); समाने वृक्षे पुरुषो निमग्नोऽनीशया<BR> शोचति मुह्यमानः Muṇḍ. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वर
अनीश्वर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no superior, uncontrolled.<BR>—2 Unable; शयिता सविधेप्यनीश्वरा सफलीकर्तुमहो मनोरथान् Bv. 2. 182.<BR>—3 Not relating to God; ध्यानेनानीश्वरान् गुणान् (दहेत्) Ms. 6. 72.<BR>—4 Not acknowledging God, atheistical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरम्
अनीश्वर + .{@-रम्@} The godless one (with Sāṅkhyas), epithet of the world;<BR> जगदाहुरनीश्वरम्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनीश्वरवादः, अनीश्वरवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरवादः|अनीश्वरवाद
अनीश्वर + -वादः atheism, not acknowledging God as the Supreme Ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरवादिन्
अनीश्वर + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> one who maintains the doctrine of no god or atheism, an atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीह|अनीहः
अनीह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Indifferent, listless. एकान्तेन ह्यनीहोऽयं पराभवति पूरुषः Mb. 3. 32. 39.<BR>—2 Not industrious, lazy; ऋणं धारयमाणस्य कुतः सुखमनीहया Mb. 5. 107. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहः|अनीह
अनीह + .{@-हः@} N. of a king of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहा
अनीह + .{@-हा@} Disregard, apathy, indifference, disinclination; अनीहया<BR> Ki. 2. 10 carelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहित
अनीहित <i>a.</i> Undesired, disagreeable, unpleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहितम्
अनीहित + .{@-तम्@} Displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु <i>ind.</i> (Either used with nouns to form adverbial compounds,<BR> or as a prefix to verbs and verbal derivatives, or as a separable preposition<BR> with acc. and regarded<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-1" target="_blank">Page0089-1</a>]<BR> as a कर्मप्रवचनीय).<BR>—1 After, behind, along after (पश्चात्); सर्वे नारदमनु उपविशन्ति<BR> V. 5; प्रमदामनु संस्थितः शुचा नृपतिः सन् R. 8. 72; तं गच्छन्त्यनु<BR> ये विपत्तिषु सदा ते तत्प्रतिष्ठाशया Mu. 1. 14; असौ कुमारस्तमजोनुजातः<BR> R. 6. 78; रत्या च साशङ्कमनुप्रयातः Ku. 3. 23; क्रमेण सुप्तामनु<BR> संविवेश सुप्तोत्थितां प्रातरनूदतिष्ठत् R. 2. 24; अनुविष्णु = विष्णोः<BR> पश्चात् P. II. 4. 18. Sk.; तदनु कथयेर्माधवीयामवास्थाम् Māl. 9. 26<BR> afterwards.<BR>—2 Along, alongside, by the side of, lengthwise यस्यचायामः P. II. 1. 16<BR> जलानि सा तीरनिखातयूपा वहत्ययोध्यामनु राजधानीम् R. 13. 61;<BR> सोऽश्वमेधशतेनेष्ट्वा यमुनामनु वीर्यवान् । त्रिशताश्वान् सरस्वत्यां<BR> गङ्गामनु चतुःशतान् Mb.; अनुगङ्गं वाराणसी = गङ्गामन्वायतम् (गङ्गादैर्ध्यसदृशदैर्ध्योपलक्षिता)<BR> situated alongside the Gaṅgā. P. II. 1. 16. Sk.; आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः<BR> कन्दलीश्चानुकच्छम् Me. 21; गिरिरिव अनुतटपुष्पितकर्णिकारयष्टिः<BR> V. 3. 3 along the sides or slopes.<BR>—3 After, in consequence of, being indicated by; जपमनु प्रावर्षत्<BR> P. II. 3. 8. Sk. (हेतुभूतजपोपलक्षितं वर्षणम्); so वृक्षमनु विद्योतते विद्युत्.<BR>—4 With, along with (सहार्थे); connected with; नदीमन्वसिता सेना<BR> P. I. 4. 85. Sk. (नद्या सह सम्बद्धा) उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु प्रवृद्धः<BR> Ku. 7. 24 along with, contemporaneously; Śi. 8. 56; दिवसोऽनुमित्रमगमद्विलयम् 9. 17.<BR>—5 Inferior or subordinate to, (मित्रलाभमनु लाभसम्पदः Ki. 13. 52<BR> inferior, lower in value or importance; अनु हरिं सुराः = हरेर्हीनाः<BR> हीने); P. I. 4. 86. Sk.<BR>—6 In a particular relation or state (इत्थंभूताख्याने प्रकारविशेषनिरूपणे);<BR> भक्तो विष्णुमनु Sk. (विष्णोरित्थंभूतः, भक्तिविशेषयुक्तः) an<BR> ardent devotee of Viṣṇu; यस्त्वां द्वेष्टि स मां द्वेष्टि यस्त्वामनु स<BR> मामनु Rām. favourably inclined or devoted to.<BR>—7 Having a part or share, participation; or one that claims a share of<BR> (भागे); भागोऽस्यास्ति इति भागस्वामी; लक्ष्मीर्हरिमनु (हरेर्भागः)<BR> Sk., हरिस्वामिकभागवतीत्यर्थः.<BR>—8 Repetition, in a distributive sense, mostly in comp. (वीप्सार्थे, विषयतायाम्);<BR> अनुदिवसम् day by day, every day; अनुक्षणम् every moment; ˚वेलम्<BR> every time, frequently; वृक्षम् वृक्षमनु सिञ्चति Sk. waters tree after,<BR> tree, <i>i. e.</i> every tree (यावद्वृक्षव्यापकः सेकः).<BR>—9 Towards, in the direction of, near, to, at (अनुर्यत्समया P. II. 1. 15);<BR> अनुवनमशनिर्गतः Sk.; ˚नदि Śi. 7. 24 near the river;<BR> प्रजिघाय कान्तमनु मुग्धतरः 9. 55 to (प्रति); on or in, with<BR> the force of the locative; यदेतदस्यानुतटं विभाति 4. 39, 7. 1;<BR> तस्माद्गच्छेरनुकनखलं शैलराजावतीर्णाम् (जह्नोः कन्याम्) Me. 52.<BR>—10 In orderly succession, according to; अनुक्रमम् in regular order;<BR> अनुज्येष्टम् = ज्येष्ठस्यानुपूर्व्येण in order of seniority; ˚पूर्वम्;<BR> अनुरूपम् = रूपस्य योग्यम् Sk.<BR>—11 Corresponding with, like, in imitation of; सर्वं मामनु ते प्रियाविरहजां<BR> त्वं तु व्यथां मानुभूः V. 4. 47; so अनुगर्ज् to roar after or in imitation of.<BR>—12 Following, conformable to (अनुगत); तथैव सोऽभूदन्वर्थो राजा<BR> प्रकृतिरञ्जनात् R. 4. 12. (अनुगतोऽर्थो यस्य).<BR>—13 With regard to, towards, in respect of; अर्ध्यदानमनु चोदितो वचः<BR> Śi. 14. 53; साधुर्देवदत्तो मातरमनु;<BR>—14 On account of, by reason of (with abl.); समस्तो बत लोकोऽयं भजते<BR> कारणादनु । त्वं तु निष्कारणादेव प्रीयसे वरवर्णिनि ॥ Rām. As a<BR> separable adverb अनु is used only in the Vedas and means after, afterwards,<BR> later on, now, at this time, again, once more, then, and further. (The<BR> senses of अनु as given by G. M. are:−<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">Page0089-2</a>]<BR> अनु वेदाध्ययनानुष्ठानसामीप्यपश्चाद्भावानुबन्धनसाम्याभिमुखहीनविसर्गलक्षणेषु;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> वेदे अनुवाकः; अनुष्ठाने अनुतिष्टति; सामीप्ये अनुमेघं वर्षति;<BR> पश्चाद्भावे तदनु; अनुबन्धने अनुशेते; साम्ये अनुकरोति; आभिमुख्ये मातरमनुधावति<BR> वत्सः; हीने अनुहरिं सुराः; विसर्गे अनुजानीते; लक्षणे अनुवनमशनिर्गतः.)<BR> The senses of अनु may be thus expressed in verse:− आयामेऽपरभावे<BR> च (पश्चादर्थे) वीप्सायां सन्निधौ तथा । इत्थंभूते लक्षणे च भागसादृश्ययोरपि<BR> ॥ योग्यतायां तथा हीने तृतीयार्थे ह्यनुक्रमे । अर्थेष्वेतेषु बहुशो ह्यनुशब्दः<BR> प्रयुज्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुः|अनु
अनुः Ved.<BR>—1 A man.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Yayāti.<BR>—3 An ancient tribe in India; अनुत्वाहिघ्ने अध देव देवा Rv. 6. 18. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनुक <i>a.</i> [अनु-कन् P. V. 2. 74, अनुकामयते इति अनुकः कमिता Sk.]<BR>—1 Greedy; desirous.<BR>—2 Libidinous, lustful (as a lover).<BR>—3 Sloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकच्छम्
अनुकच्छम् Along or near the marshy ground; आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः<BR> कन्दलीश्चानुकच्छम् (Me. 21).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथ्
अनुकथ् €10 P.<BR> To relate after (some one else), mention subsequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथनम्
अनुकथनम्<BR>—1 Subsequent mention; आदेशः कथनम्, अन्वादेशोऽनुकथनम् Kāśi.<BR> on P. II. 4. 32.<BR>—2 Relation, narration; discourse, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकनीयस्
अनुकनीयस् <i>a.</i> The next youngest. P. VI. 2. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्|अनुकंप्
अनुकम्प् €1 Ā. To take pity or compassion on, sympathize with, pity<BR> (with acc.); किमुज्जिहानजीवितां वराकीं नानुकम्पसे Māl. 10; कथं<BR> ब्राह्मणी मामनुकम्पते Mk. 3; कम्पसे नानुकम्पसे 4. 8; with loc.<BR> also; सौहृदेन तथा प्रेम्णा सदा मथ्यनुकम्पसे Mb. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To pity &c.; शफरीं प्रथमा वृष्टिरिवान्वकम्पयत् Ku. 4. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पक|अनुकंपक
अनुकम्पक <i>a.</i> Pitying, taking compassion on, sympathizing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पन|अनुकंपन
अनुकम्पन <i>a.</i> One who pities, kind-hearted, compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पनम्
अनुकम्पन + .{@-नम्@} Compassion, pity, tenderness, sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पा|अनुकंपा
अनुकम्पा [कम्प्-अङ्] Compassion, commiseration, pity; with gen.;<BR> तेषामेवानुकम्पार्थम् Bg. 10. 11; or with loc.; भक्त्या गुरौ मय्यनुकम्पया<BR> च R. 2. 63; or in comp.; भूतानुकम्पा तव चेत् R. 2. 48; अनुकम्पायां<BR> कन् P. V. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पित|अनुकंपित
अनुकम्पित <i>p. p.</i> Pitied;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पितात्मन्
अनुकम्पित + ˚आत्मन् having a compassionate spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पिन्|अनुकंपिन्
अनुकम्पिन् <i>a.</i> Pitying (in comp.); sympathizing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्य|अनुकंप्य|अनुकम्प्यः
अनुकम्प्य <i>pot. p.</i> Pitiable, worthy of sympathy; किं तन्न येनासि<BR> ममानुकम्प्या R. 14. 74; दुहितरमनुकम्प्यामद्रिरादाय दोर्भ्याम् Ku. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्यः|अनुकम्प्य|अनुकंप्य
अनुकम्प्य + .{@-म्प्यः@}<BR>—1 A courier, express messenger.<BR>—2 An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकल्पः|अनुकल्प
अनुकल्पः An alternative, a second alternative, a make-shift, अभावे<BR> हि श्रुतस्य अनुकम्पः प्रतिनिधिः । ŚB. on MS. 6. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाङ्क्षा|अनुकांक्षा
अनुकाङ्क्षा Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाम|अनुकामं|अनुकामः
अनुकाम <i>a.</i> [कामस्य सदृशः अनुरूपो वा]<BR>—1 Agreeable to, according to oneʼs desire.<BR>—2 [अनुकामयते कम्-अच्] Desirous, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामम्
अनुकाम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i> At will, according to desire or wish, as desired, at pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामः|अनुकाम|अनुकामं
अनुकाम + .{@-मः@} [अनुरूपः कामः] Proper or worthy desire; desire;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामकृत्
अनुकाम + .{@-मः@} + ˚कृत्<BR> fulfilling oneʼs desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामीन|अनुकामीनः
अनुकामीन <i>a.</i> [कामस्य सदृशम् अनुकामम्; ख प्रत्ययः; अनुकामं<BR> गामी यथेष्टं गन्ता इत्यर्थः P. V. 2. 11. Sk.] Going at will or pleasure;<BR> one who acts as he pleases; अनुकामीनतां त्यज Bk. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाल
अनुकाल <i>a.</i> [कालस्य योग्यः] Opportune, timely, adapted or<BR> suited to the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकालम्
अनुकाल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Opportunely, on a proper occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकीर्तनम्
अनुकीर्तनम् Act of proclaiming or publishing. असदाचरिते मार्गे<BR> कथं स्यादनुकीर्तनम् Mb. 3. 233. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूल|अनुकूलः
अनुकूल <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः कूलं तटं स्नेहादिबन्धनं वा]<BR>—1 Favourable, agreeable (lit. following the bank or slope, according<BR> to the current, with the grain); as wind, fate &c.; मन्दं मन्दं नुदति<BR> पवनश्चानुकूलो यथा त्वाम् Me. 9; शान्त ˚पवनश्च Ś. 4. 11; ˚परिणामा<BR> संवृत्ता Ś. 7; बाणास्त एव मदनस्य ममानुकूलाः V. 3. 20.<BR>—2 Friendly, kind, well or kindly disposed.<BR>—3 Conformable to; pleasing, agreeable or favourable to, conducing to,<BR> capable of; oft. in comp.; स्पर्शानुकूला इव सूर्यकान्ताः Ś. 2. 7;<BR> अननुकूलोऽभिमानस्य K. 45 not inclined to pride; दर्शनानुकूलाहमस्य<BR> न वेति 197; कुशलविरचितानुकूलवेशः R. 5. 76 befitting, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलः|अनुकूल
अनुकूल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A faithful or kind husband, (एकरतिः S. D. or एकनिरतः एकस्यामेव<BR> नायिकायाम् आसक्तः), a variety of नायक.<BR>—2 ‘Favourable to all’, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूला
अनुकूल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 N. of a tree (दन्ती) Croton Polyandrum.<BR>—2 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलम्
अनुकूल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Favour, kindness; नारीणामनुकूलमाचरति चेत् K. P. 9.<BR>—2 (Rhet.) A figure in which unfavourableness turns into kindness; अनुकूलं<BR> प्रातिकूल्यमानुकूल्यानुबन्धि चेत् S. D.; कुपितासि यदा तन्वि निधाय करजक्षतम् ।<BR> बधान भुजपाशाभ्यां कण्ठमस्य दृढं तदा ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलता
अनुकूलता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Favour, conformity, kindness, good will; पवनस्यानुकूलत्वात् R. 1. 42<BR> the wind being favourable.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलत्वम्
अनुकूलता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Favour, conformity, kindness, good will; पवनस्यानुकूलत्वात् R. 1. 42<BR> the wind being favourable.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलयति
अनुकूलयति^1 Den. P. To conciliate, propitiate, act in a friendly<BR> way towards; (तम्) अनुकूलयतीन्द्रोऽपि कल्पद्रुमविभूषणैः Ku. 2. 39;<BR> अस्यानुकूलय मतिं मतिमन्ननेन Ki. 13. 71; Śi. 7. 11.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost diacritics; see quotations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलित
अनुकूलित <i>a.</i> One who is honoured or well received; मन्त्रिणो<BR> नैगमाश्चैव यथार्हमनुकूलिताः Rām. 7. 74. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृ
अनुकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To do after or afterwards; follow; especially to imitate, do after<BR> or in imitation of, resemble, equal, copy (with gen.); ततोऽनुकुर्याद्विशदस्य<BR> तस्याः … स्मितस्य Ku. 1. 44; श्यामतया हरेरिवानुकुर्वतीम्<BR> K. 10; अनुकरोति भगवतो नारायणस्य 6, 282; ननु कलभेन यूथपतेरनुकृतम्<BR> M. 5; (also with acc.); सर्वाभिरन्याभिः कलाभिरनुचकार तं वैशम्पायनः<BR> K. 76; शैलाधिपस्यानुचकार लक्ष्मीम् Bk. 2. 8; बहुतरं भवन्तमनुकरोति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">Page0090-2</a>]<BR> V. 5; Ms. 2. 199.<BR>—2 To requite, recompense.<BR>—3 To try on, adjust, adapt; बन्धं ततोऽनुकुर्वीत Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर|अनुकरः
अनुकर <i>a.</i> Imitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरः|अनुकर
अनुकर + .{@-रः@} An assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरणम्
अनुकरणम्, -कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Imitation; त्वदीयसुचरितैकदेशस्यानुकरणं किलैतत् Mu. 7.<BR>—2 Copy, resemblance, similarity; शब्दानुकरणम् onomatopoeia; अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात<BR> इतौ P. VI. 1. 98, V. 4. 57, I. 4. 62; धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणाः Me. 71.<BR>—3 Compliance; ओमित्येतदनुकृति ह स्म वै T. Up. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृतिः|अनुकृति
अनुकरणम्, -कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Imitation; त्वदीयसुचरितैकदेशस्यानुकरणं किलैतत् Mu. 7.<BR>—2 Copy, resemblance, similarity; शब्दानुकरणम् onomatopoeia; अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात<BR> इतौ P. VI. 1. 98, V. 4. 57, I. 4. 62; धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणाः Me. 71.<BR>—3 Compliance; ओमित्येतदनुकृति ह स्म वै T. Up. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्तृ
अनुकर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An imitator.<BR>—2 Actor, performer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्मन्|अनुकर्म्मन्
अनुकर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Imitation.<BR>—2 [पश्चात्कृतं कर्म] A subsequent rite. ━<i>m.</i> N. of one of the Viśvedevas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारः|अनुकार
अनुकारः [कृ-घञ्] Imitation, resemblance; सुलभानुकारः खलु<BR> जगति वेधसो निर्माणसंनिवेशः Māl. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारिन्
अनुकारिन् <i>a.</i> Imitating, resembling (with gen. or in comp.); प्रियायाः<BR> किञ्चिदनुकारिणीषु लतासु दृष्टिं विलोभयामि Ś. 6; अनुकारिणि पूर्वेषां<BR> युक्तरूपमिदं त्वयि Ś. 2. 17, 1. 21; R. 1. 43. कपिलानुकारिणा 3. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकार्य|अनुकार्य्य
अनुकार्य, -करणीय, -कर्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Fit to be imitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरणीय
अनुकार्य, -करणीय, -कर्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Fit to be imitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्तव्य
अनुकार्य, -करणीय, -कर्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> Fit to be imitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकार्यम्
अनुकार्य, -करणीय, -कर्तव्य + .{@-र्यम्, -अनुक्रिया@} A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रिया
अनुकार्य, -करणीय, -कर्तव्य + .{@-र्यम्, -अनुक्रिया@} A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रीः
अनुक्रीः [अनु-कृ उणा˚ वा. ई. किच्च Tv.] A kind of sacrificial<BR> rite called साद्यस्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकीर्ण
अनुकीर्ण <i>a.</i> Filled, Pervaded; अनुकीर्णं महारण्यं ब्राह्मणैः<BR> समपद्यत Mb. 3. 26. 1. Crowded, crammed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृत
अनुकृत <i>a.</i> Imitated, made like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृतम्
अनुकृत + .{@-तम्@} <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Return.<BR>—2 Defence; जघ्नतुस्तौ तदान्योन्यं कृतानुकृतकारिणौ Rām. 6. 107. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृपायते
अनुकृपायते Den. Ā. to sympathize or condole with. अनुकृष् To<BR> mourn for, long; अनु पूर्वाः कृपते वावशाना Rv. 1. 113. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृष्
अनुकृष् €1 P. To drag after oneself, to attract (in gram.); see अनुकर्ष<BR> below. ━<i>Caus.</i> To subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षः|अनुकर्ष
अनुकर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR>—1 Dragging after, drawing along; attraction in general.<BR>—2 Summoning or invoking (by means of spells).<BR>—3 Grammatical attraction, application or attraction of a word in a preceding<BR> rule to a subsequent rule, word &c.; नायमनुकर्षणार्थश्चकारः Mbh.<BR> on P. II. 2. 4; see also Sk. on P. VI. 1. 127.<BR>—4 [अनुकृष्यते स्वसम्बद्धेन चक्रेण] The axle-tree or bottom of a carriage.<BR>—5 Delayed performance of a duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षणम्
अनुकर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR>—1 Dragging after, drawing along; attraction in general.<BR>—2 Summoning or invoking (by means of spells).<BR>—3 Grammatical attraction, application or attraction of a word in a preceding<BR> rule to a subsequent rule, word &c.; नायमनुकर्षणार्थश्चकारः Mbh.<BR> on P. II. 2. 4; see also Sk. on P. VI. 1. 127.<BR>—4 [अनुकृष्यते स्वसम्बद्धेन चक्रेण] The axle-tree or bottom of a carriage.<BR>—5 Delayed performance of a duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षन्
अनुकर्षन् <i>m.</i> The bottom of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृष्ट
अनुकृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drawn after, attracted.<BR>—2 Implied; included.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकॢप्
अनुकॢप् €1 Ā. To follow duly. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause others to follow duly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकल्पः|अनुकल्प
अनुकल्पः [अनुगतः मुख्यं कल्पम्]<BR>—1 A secondary direction or precept, a substitute or alternative to be<BR> used in times of necessity when the primary one (प्रथमकल्प) is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">Page0091-1</a>]<BR> not possible; as the direction to use गोधूम or तण्डुल in the<BR> absence of यव; प्रभुः प्रथमकल्पस्य योऽनुकल्पेन वर्तते Ms. 11. 30, 3. 147.<BR>—2 A work connected with Kalpa (one of the six auxiliaries of the Vedas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्त
अनुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unuttered, unsaid (in gram.) = अनभिहित q. v. under अभिधा.<BR>—2 Unheard of, extraordinary.<BR>—3 Not told; असावनुक्तोऽपि सहाय एव Ku. 3. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्थ
अनुक्थ <i>a.</i> Without hymns or songs of praise; किं मामनिन्द्राः<BR> कृणवन्ननुक्थाः Rv. 5. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रकच
अनुक्रकच <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः ककचम्] Serrated, dentated like a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रन्द्|अनुक्रंद्
अनुक्रन्द् €1 P. To cry after, reply to the sound; यं क्षोणीरनुचकदे<BR> Rv. 8. 3. 10. वीरुन्नीडकपोतकूजितमनुक्रन्दन्त्यमी कुक्कुटाः Māl. 9. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रन्दनम्
अनुक्रन्दनम् A cry in reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम्
अनुक्रम् €1 U., €4 P.<BR>—1 To go after, follow (fig. also); महर्षिभिरनुक्रान्तं धर्मपन्थानमास्थितः<BR> Rām.; to betake oneself to; तीर्थयात्रामनुक्रामन् Mb.; व्यवसायमनुक्रान्ता<BR> क्रान्ते त्वमतिशोभनम् Rām.<BR>—2 To count up, enumerate, state or go through in order; यच्चानुक्रान्तं<BR> यच्चानुक्रंस्यते Mbh. on P. I. 1. 72; give a table of contents, used<BR> frequently in the Nirukta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम|अनुक्रमः
अनुक्रम <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः क्रमम्] In due order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमः|अनुक्रम
अनुक्रम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Succession, order, sequence, arrangement, method, due order; प्रचक्रमे<BR> वक्तुमनुक्रमज्ञा R. 6. 70; श्वश्रूजनं सर्वमनुक्रमेण 14. 60;<BR> गृहीतानुक्रमाद्दाप्यो Y. 2. 41.<BR>—2 A table of contents, index, such as that of the Vedic Saṃhitās.<BR>—3 Routine order, daily practice; मानेन रक्ष्यते धान्यमश्वान् रक्षत्यनुक्रमः<BR> Mb. 5. 34. 40. (अनुक्रमः व्यायामशिक्षादिः इति भाष्यकारः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणम्
अनुक्रमणम्<BR>—1 Proceeding in order.<BR>—2 Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणी
अनुक्रमणम् + .{@-णी, -णिका@} [स्वार्थे कन्] A table of contents, an index showing<BR> the successive contents of a work. उभे सन्ध्ये जपन्किञ्चित् सद्यो मुच्येत<BR> किल्बिषात् । अनुक्रमण्या यावत्स्यादह्ना रात्र्या च सञ्चितम् ॥ Mb. 1. 1. 263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणिका
अनुक्रमणम् + .{@-णी, -णिका@} [स्वार्थे कन्] A table of contents, an index showing<BR> the successive contents of a work. उभे सन्ध्ये जपन्किञ्चित् सद्यो मुच्येत<BR> किल्बिषात् । अनुक्रमण्या यावत्स्यादह्ना रात्र्या च सञ्चितम् ॥ Mb. 1. 1. 263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रुश्
अनुक्रुश् €1 P. To shout at or after. ━<i>Caus.</i> To join in lamenting,<BR> condole with, show sympathy. तावदिमान् बालवृक्षान् उदकप्रदानेन अनुक्रोशयिष्यामि ।<BR> Pratimā 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रोशः|अनुक्रोश
अनुक्रोशः<BR>—1 Pity, compassion, tenderness (with loc.); भगवन्कामदेव न ते मय्यनुक्रोशः<BR> Ś. 3; Me. 117; किमपि सानुक्रोशः कृतः made to relent Ś. 4; न<BR> ते मां प्रति अनुक्रोशः Ś. 3.<BR>—2 One who has gone over a krośa (2 miles) (अनुगतः क्रोशम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षणम्
अनुक्षणम् <i>ind.</i> Every instant, constantly, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षत्तृ
अनुक्षत्तृ <i>m.</i>, (-त्ता)<BR> The attendant of a door-keeper or charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षत्ता
अनुक्षत्तृ <i>m.</i>, (-त्ता)<BR> The attendant of a door-keeper or charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षपम्
अनुक्षपम् <i>ind.</i> Night after night; Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षेत्रम्
अनुक्षेत्रम् Stipend given to certain temple-worshippers in Orissa<BR> in commutation of the proceeds of an endowment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्या
अनुख्या €2 P. Ved. To descry, see from a distance; अनु पूर्वाणि चख्यथुर्युगानि Rv. 7. 70. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्यातिः|अनुख्याति
अनुख्यातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Descrying.<BR>—2 Reporting, revealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्यातृ
अनुख्यातृ <i>m.</i> (-ता)<BR> A discoverer; reporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्याता
अनुख्यातृ <i>m.</i> (-ता)<BR> A discoverer; reporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम्
अनुगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go after, follow, attend, accompany; अनभिज्ञो गुणानां यो न भृत्यैरनुगम्यते<BR> Pt. 1. 73; ओदकान्तात्स्रिग्धो जनोऽनुगन्तव्यः Ś. 4; केकारवैरनुगम्यमानो<BR> भूषणनिनादः K. 84; मार्गं मनुष्येश्वरधर्मपत्नी श्रुतेरिवार्थ स्मृतिरन्वगच्छत्<BR> R. 2. 2; छायेव तां भूपतिरन्वगच्छत् 6; Ms. 12. 115;<BR>—2 To follow, practise, observe, obey, act up to; प्रतिशब्दक इव राजवचनमनुगच्छति<BR> जनो भयात् K. 104; पूर्वैरयमभिप्रेतो गतो मार्गोऽनुगम्यते Rām.;<BR> विपत्तौ च महाँल्लोके धीरतामनुगच्छति H. 3. 37.<BR>—3 To seek, wander through; काननं वापि शैलं वा यं रामोऽनुगमिष्यति<BR> Rām.; कृत्स्नां पृथ्वीमनुगच्छत <i>ibid.</i> go in quest of.<BR>—4 To come, arrive, approach, present oneself (as time); काले त्वनुगते Bhāg.<BR>—5 To answer or respond to; correspond with, be suitable to; imitate,<BR> resemble; धनुःश्रियं गोत्रभिदोऽनुगच्छति Ki. 4. 326; आस्फालितं यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैर्भृदङ्गधीरध्वनिमन्वगच्छत्<BR> R. 16. 13; न चापि कादम्बरीं लक्ष्मीरनुगन्तुमलम् K. 203.<BR>—6 To go or die out, be extinguished; यद्येष उख्योऽग्निरनुगच्छेत् Śat. Br.<BR>—7 To enter into. ━<i>Caus.</i> [गमयति] To cause to follow, follow;<BR> उद्ग्रीवैरनुगमितस्य पुष्करस्य M. 1. 21 followed or accompanied in sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग|अनुगः
अनुग <i>a.</i> [अनुगच्छतीति, गम्-ड] (In comp.) Following, going<BR> after; corresponding or tallying with, adequate to; सदा पृष्ठानुगः<BR> पुरे Pt. 1. 59; गीतानुगं वारि मृदङ्गवाद्यम् R. 16. 64; Me. 47; कामक्रोधवशानुगम्<BR> Ms. 2. 214; गोत्ररिक्थानुगः पिण्डः 9. 142 governed or regulated by; 8. 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगः|अनुग
अनुग + .{@-गः@} A follower, (obedient) servant, companion; तद्भूतनाथानुग<BR> R. 2. 58, 9. 82; बल˚ followed by an army, being the head of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगत|अनुगतः
अनुगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 (Used passively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Followed (lit. & fig.), attended; अनुगतमलिवृन्दैर्गण्डभित्तीर्विहाय<BR> R. 12. 102; M. 3. 9; मद्यानुगतभोजनं मलावहम् Ms. 11. 70.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Full of, filled with; दारिद्र्येणाभिभूतेन त्वत्स्नेहानुगतेन<BR> च Mk. 4. 5; वर्षधरकलमूकानुगतेन परिजनेन K. 159 consisting<BR> or made up of; चिन्तानुगतसर्वात्मन् Mb.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Covered, as by a dress hanging behind; शिवमिवानुगतं गजचर्मणा<BR> Ki. 5. 2 (पश्चाद्व्याप्तम्).<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Extinguished &c.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Acquired, obtained.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) Overtakan; कालेनानुगतो ह्यसि Rām. 7. 68. 6.<BR>—2 (Used actively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Following, obeying; observing; स्वमतमनुगतः Mu. 5. 19;<BR> विभवानुगता भार्या Mk. 3. 28; दिग्विजयप्रसङ्गेनानुगतो भूमिमिमाम्<BR> K. 191 come to; Ms. 9. 267; K. 166; Mu. 6. 5; H. 2. 55; R. 15. 9.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Corresponding or tallying with, adapted or answering to, in harmony<BR> with; सूत्रेणानुगतं भवति Ś. B.; पादन्यासो लयमनुगतः M. 2. 8<BR> in accompaniment to the musical time; मृदङ्ग ˚तः सङ्गीतमधुरः<BR> Ratn. 1; ˚वीणैः Śi. 11. 10.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Adequate or suitable to, fit for; प्रस्तावानुगतं पृष्टः Pt. 5.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Imitating; परितुष्टोऽस्मि यत्पितरमनुगतो वत्सः M. 5. I<BR> am glad that the boy takes after his father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगतम्
अनुगत + .{@-तम्@} Moderate time im music.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुगतार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगतार्थ
अनुगत + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> having a corresponding or easily discoverable sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगतिः|अनुगति
अनुगतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Following; बलस्य चतुरङ्गस्य नायकानुगतिर्नयः Rām.; गतानुगतिको<BR> लोकः Pt. 1. 342 following, imitating; see under गत.<BR>—2 Consent, approval; अकाम˚ forced consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमः|अनुगम
अनुगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Following; आत्मानुगमनेन गां प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88; बृहतेर्धातोरर्थानुगमात् Ś. B.<BR>—2 Comprehending, grasping (as a sense); रसाद्यनुगतः S. D.<BR>—3 Following in death, post-cremation, self-immolation of a widow on her<BR> husbandʼs funeral pile.<BR>—4 Imitating; approaching.<BR>—5 Conformity, accordance; श्रुत्यनुगमाच्च Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमनम्
अनुगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Following; आत्मानुगमनेन गां प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88; बृहतेर्धातोरर्थानुगमात् Ś. B.<BR>—2 Comprehending, grasping (as a sense); रसाद्यनुगतः S. D.<BR>—3 Following in death, post-cremation, self-immolation of a widow on her<BR> husbandʼs funeral pile.<BR>—4 Imitating; approaching.<BR>—5 Conformity, accordance; श्रुत्यनुगमाच्च Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामिन्
अनुगामिन् <i>a.</i> Following. ━<i>m.</i> A follower = अनुग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामुक
अनुगामुक <i>a.</i> Habitually or constantly following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगर्ज्
अनुगर्ज् €1 P. To roar after or in imitation of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगर्जित
अनुगर्जित <i>p. p.</i> Roared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगर्जितम्
अनुगर्जित + .{@-तम्@} A roaring echo, अनुगर्जितसन्दिग्धाः करणैर्मुरजखनाः Ku. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगव
अनुगव <i>a.</i> [गोः सदृशः आयामः, अच्] Suiting (the length of) the oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगवीनः|अनुगवीन
अनुगवीनः [अनुगु गोः पश्चात्पर्याप्तं यथा गच्छति सोऽनुगवीनः<BR> गोपालः; अनुगु ख P. V. 2. 15. Sk.] A cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगादिन्
अनुगादिन् <i>a.</i> [गद्-णिनि] Repeating, following in speaking,<BR> echoing. (P. V. 4. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगिरम्
अनुगिरम् <i>ind.</i> By the mountain-side अयं सुजातोऽनुगिरं तमालः R. 13. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीता
अनुगीता <i>f.</i> An after-song. N. of a part of the fourteenth book<BR> of the Mb. (Chs. 16-92).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीति|अनुगीतिः
अनुगीति See under अनुगै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुण|अनुगुणः
अनुगुण <i>a.</i> [अनुकूलो गुणो यस्य] Having similar qualities,<BR> of the same nature; कान्तारतापसाविक्षू वंशकानुगुणौ स्मृतौ Suśr.;<BR> conformable to, favourable or agreeable to, suitable, according to; मनोरथस्यानुगुणं<BR> सर्वदा यस्य चेष्टितम् Mv. 7. 7 obedient to the will 7. 38; गुणसम्पदानुगुणतां<BR> गमितः Ki. 6. 33, 10. 13; congenial, suitable, fit; ˚अन्नलाभात्<BR> Dk. 64, 94; अननुगुणदाराणाम् Dk. 130 not having wives worthy of themselves;<BR> (विणा) उत्कण्ठितस्य हृदयानुगुणा वयस्या Mk. 3. 3 agreeable or<BR> pleasing to the heart, exactly after the heart (Tv. here takes ˚णा<BR> mean तन्त्रीयुक्तवीणा itself); अत्र द्वावप्युपध्मानीयावेव न शान्तानुगुणौ<BR> R. G.; रसानुगुणतामेति S. D.; ˚णं सर्वास्ववस्थासु यत् U. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणः|अनुगुण
अनुगुण + .{@-णः@} A natural peculiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणम्
अनुगुण + .{@-णम्@} <i>adv.</i><BR>—1 Favourably, conformably to oneʼs desires; चिरेणानुगुणं प्रोक्ता प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुखी Bk. 8. 95.<BR>—2 Agreeably or conformably to (in comp.); तदादेशानुगुणं भवदागमनमभूत् Dk. 11.<BR>—3 Naturally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणत्वम्
अनुगुणत्वम् Favourableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणयति
अनुगुणयति Den. P. To make favourable, conciliate; bring about,<BR> secure; सम्पदोऽनुगुणयन् सुखैषिणाम् Ki. 13. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुप्त
अनुगुप्त <i>a.</i> Covered, sheltered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगै
अनुगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To sing after (a person), sing to (a tune); follow in singing; अनुगायति<BR> काचिदुदञ्चितपञ्चमरागम् Gīt. 1; अनुजगुरथ दिव्यं दुन्दुभिध्वानमाशाः<BR> Ki. 3. 60 sent back, echoed.<BR>—2 To sing; to celebrate in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीतम्
अनुगीतम् Singing in response to; झङ्कारस्यानुगीतैरनुरणनमिवारभ्यते<BR> भृङ्गसार्थैः Ratn. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीतिः|अनुगीति
अनुगीतिः <i>f.</i> N. of a metre of two lines, the first having 27 and<BR> the second 32 mātrās, a species of the Āryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगृहम्
अनुगृहम् The roof of a house; कर्णकीलायसम्बन्धोऽनुऋगृहं सेतुः<BR> (cf. Kau. A. ch. 65.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रह्
अनुग्रह् €9 P. (Ved. -गृभ्णाति).<BR>—1 To favour, oblige, treat with kindness; शिलातलैकदेशमनुगृह्णातु<BR> वयस्यः Ś. 3 our friend will be so good as to, or kindly, take a seat<BR> on the stone; अयं विष्टरोऽनुगृह्यताम् V. 5 be pleased to sit down<BR> &c.; महेन्द्रेण पुनरनुगृहीता V. 3 favoured (by modifying the curse);<BR> with instr. or abl. of that which is an obligation; अनुगृहीतोऽहमनया<BR> मघवतः सम्भावनया Ś. 6; कतरत्कुलमनुगृहीतं भगवत्या जन्मना<BR> K. 135; अनुगृहीतोऽस्मि अहमुपदेशाद्भवतः V. 4. I am much obliged<BR> to you &c. (अनुगृहीत is oft. used by itself in the sense of ‘much obliged’<BR>, ‘many thanks’, ‘I thank you’, ‘I esteem it as a favour’.)<BR>—2 To foster, cherish, protect, maintain (as fire); अग्निर्नित्यानुगृहीतः<BR> स्यात् Āśval.<BR>—3 To receive, welcome.<BR>—4 To hold up, support, uphold. त्रिभिस्तीक्ष्णैर्महावेगैरन्वगृह्णाच्छिरः<BR> शरैः Mb. 6. 120. 45.<BR>—5 To follow in robbing, seizing or depriving.<BR>—6 To keep to, conform or correspond to, follow, take after; आकृतिमनुगृह्णन्ति<BR> गुणाः Vb. 2; क्षात्रधर्मश्चानुगृहीतो भवति U. 5. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To cause to favour, or to favour; आर्यस्य दर्शनेनात्मानमनुग्राहयितुम् Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहः|अनुग्रह
अनुग्रहः, -हणम्<BR>—1 A favour, kindness, obligation; showing favour, obliging, rewarding<BR> (opp. निग्रह); निग्रहानुग्रहकर्ता Pt. 1; पादार्पणानुग्रहपूतपृष्टम्<BR> R. 2. 35; अनुग्रह इवेयमभ्यर्थना Ś. 1; अनुग्रहं संस्मरणप्रवृत्तम् Ku. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Assistance, help (shown to the poor in feeding them &c. दरिद्रादिपोषणम्).<BR>—3 Facilitating by spells.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 Rear-guard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुग्रहकातर, अनुग्रहसर्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहणम्
अनुग्रहः, -हणम्<BR>—1 A favour, kindness, obligation; showing favour, obliging, rewarding<BR> (opp. निग्रह); निग्रहानुग्रहकर्ता Pt. 1; पादार्पणानुग्रहपूतपृष्टम्<BR> R. 2. 35; अनुग्रह इवेयमभ्यर्थना Ś. 1; अनुग्रहं संस्मरणप्रवृत्तम् Ku. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Assistance, help (shown to the poor in feeding them &c. दरिद्रादिपोषणम्).<BR>—3 Facilitating by spells.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 Rear-guard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुग्रहकातर, अनुग्रहसर्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहकातर
अनुग्रहः + -कातर <i>a.</i> anxious to please or for favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहसर्गः|अनुग्रहसर्ग
अनुग्रहः + -सर्गः creation of feelings or mental conditions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राह्य
अनुग्राह्य <i>pot. p.</i> Fit to be favoured or obliged; ततः कथनेनात्मानमनुग्राह्यमिच्छामि<BR> K. 134; न वयमनुग्राह्याः प्रायो देवतानाम् 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राहक
अनुग्राहक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Favouring, furthering, promoting.<BR>—2 Gracious, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रासकः|अनुग्रासक
अनुग्रासकः A mouthful; the equivalent of a mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुघटनम्
अनुघटनम् Linking together with; क्षिप्ता कथानुघटनाय मयापि वाणी K. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुघट्ट्
अनुघट्ट् To stroke, to rub lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर्
अनुचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To follow, pursue, go after; to serve, attend or wait upon; पित्रोः<BR> पादाननुचरन् K. 368 serving.<BR>—2 To traverse, seek after, go through, wander.<BR>—3 To conduct oneself, behave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरः|अनुचर
अनुचरः<BR>—1 A companion, follower, attendant, servant; तेनानुचरेण धेनोः R. 2. 4;<BR> आत्मानुचरस्य भावं जिज्ञासमाना 26, 52; Me. 3; विबुधानुचराः<BR> Ms. 12. 47. In comp. attended or followed by; वानर˚, राक्षस˚ &c.<BR>—2 Following a spy (चरमनुगतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरा
अनुचरः + .{@-रा, -री@}<BR>—1 A female attendant.<BR>—2 A logical or due strophe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरी
अनुचरः + .{@-रा, -री@}<BR>—1 A female attendant.<BR>—2 A logical or due strophe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरित
अनुचरित <i>p. p.</i> Followed &c. attended, विद्याधरानुचरितं<BR> किन्नरीभिस्तथैव च Mb. 3. 158. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरितम्
अनुचरित + .{@-तम्@} Walk; walk in life; conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचारकः|अनुचारक
अनुचारकः A follower, servant &c. सहचरस्तु स्यादनुचारे सहाशने । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचारिका
अनुचारकः + .{@-रिका@} A female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर्चिः|अनुचर्चि
अनुचर्चिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Repeating (in a chorus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचित
अनुचित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wrong, improper.<BR>—2 Unusual; unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचितार्थः|अनुचितार्थ
अनुचित + .{@-अर्थः@} An unusual meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्त्|अनुचिंत्
अनुचिन्त् €10 P. To consider, think of, call to mind; धातुर्विभुत्वमनुचिन्त्य<BR> वपुश्च तस्याः Ś. 2. 10; परमं पुरुषं दिव्यं याति पार्थानुचिन्तयन्<BR> Bg. 8. 8; धर्मार्थौ चानुचिन्तयेत् Ms. 4. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्ता|अनुचिंता
अनुचिन्ता, अनुचिन्तनम्<BR>—1 Calling to mind, thinking of, meditating upon.<BR>—2 Recalling, recollecting.<BR>—3 Constant thinking, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्तनम्
अनुचिन्ता, अनुचिन्तनम्<BR>—1 Calling to mind, thinking of, meditating upon.<BR>—2 Recalling, recollecting.<BR>—3 Constant thinking, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छादः|अनुच्छाद|अनुछाद
अनुच्छादः The part of a manʼs under-garment which is allowed to hang<BR> down in front from the waist to the feet (Mar. नित्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छित्तिः|अनुच्छित्ति
अनुच्छित्तिः <i>f.</i>, अनुच्छेदः Non-extirpation; non-destruction;<BR> indestructibility. अविनाशी वा अरे अयमात्मा अनुच्छित्तिधर्मा । Bṛ. Up. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिष्ट|अनुच्छिष्टः
अनुच्छिष्ट <i>a.</i> Not rejected; pure, holy; fresh, unused; ˚यौवना Dk. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्
अनुजन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born after, arise or be produced after, to follow in being born,<BR> arising &c.; पुत्रिकायां कृतायां तु यदि पुत्रोऽनुजायते Ms. 9. 134;<BR> अथवा जायमानस्य यच्छीलमनुजायते Mb.<BR>—2 To take after (oneʼs parents); to be born similar to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज|अनुजं|अनुजः
अनुज, -जात <i>p. p.</i><BR> Born after, later, younger; राममनुजातः<BR> P. III. 4. 72; असौ कुमारस्तमजोऽनुजातः R. 6. 78; पुमांसमनुरुध्य<BR> जाता पुमनुजा Sk.; so स्त्र्यनुजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजात|अनुजातः
अनुज, -जात <i>p. p.</i><BR> Born after, later, younger; राममनुजातः<BR> P. III. 4. 72; असौ कुमारस्तमजोऽनुजातः R. 6. 78; पुमांसमनुरुध्य<BR> जाता पुमनुजा Sk.; so स्त्र्यनुजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजः|अनुज|अनुजं
अनुज, -जात + .{@-जः, -जातः@}<BR>—1 A younger brother; दन्तजातेऽनुजाते च कृतचूडे च संस्थिते । अशुद्धा<BR> बान्धवाः सर्वे सूतके च तथोच्यते ॥ Some interpret the word अनुजात<BR> there to mean ‘a child which has not, cut teeth’. Ms. 5. 58.<BR>—2 A cadet; born again, after born, younger, later.<BR>—3 Taking after. अनुजातो हि मां सर्वैर्गुणैः श्रेष्ठो ममात्मजः Rām. 2. 2. 11.<BR>—4 Born again, invested with the sacred thread.<BR>—5 Equal, resembling; एकस्त्वमनुजातोऽसि पितरं बलवत्तरम् Rām. 6. 76. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजातः|अनुजात
अनुज, -जात + .{@-जः, -जातः@}<BR>—1 A younger brother; दन्तजातेऽनुजाते च कृतचूडे च संस्थिते । अशुद्धा<BR> बान्धवाः सर्वे सूतके च तथोच्यते ॥ Some interpret the word अनुजात<BR> there to mean ‘a child which has not, cut teeth’. Ms. 5. 58.<BR>—2 A cadet; born again, after born, younger, later.<BR>—3 Taking after. अनुजातो हि मां सर्वैर्गुणैः श्रेष्ठो ममात्मजः Rām. 2. 2. 11.<BR>—4 Born again, invested with the sacred thread.<BR>—5 Equal, resembling; एकस्त्वमनुजातोऽसि पितरं बलवत्तरम् Rām. 6. 76. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजा
अनुज, -जात + .{@-जा, -जाता@}<BR>—1 younger sister.<BR>—2 N. of a plant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">Page0093-2</a>]<BR> (त्रायमाणालता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजाता
अनुज, -जात + .{@-जा, -जाता@}<BR>—1 younger sister.<BR>—2 N. of a plant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">Page0093-2</a>]<BR> (त्रायमाणालता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजम्
अनुज, -जात + .{@-जम्@} N. of a palnt (प्रपौण्डरीक; Mar. पुण्डरीक),<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुजावर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजावर
अनुज + -अवर <i>a.</i> lower than the younger, youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजनः|अनुजन
अनुजनः Attendants, followers. Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्मन्
अनुजन्मन् <i>m.</i> [अनु जन्म यस्य] A younger brother; जननाथ<BR> तवानुजन्मनाम् Ki. 2. 17; Śi. 13. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्
अनुजीव् €1 P.<BR>—1 To depend upon for subsistence, hang on, live by or upon (something);<BR> ये च त्वामनुजीवन्ति नाहं तेषां न ते मम Rām.; स तु तस्याः<BR> पाणिग्राहकमनुजीविष्यति Dk. 112 hang or depend on, live (submissively)<BR> under, live as a subordinate to.<BR>—2 To see without envy; यां तां श्रियमसूयामः पुरा दृष्ट्वा युधिष्टिरे ।<BR> अद्य तामनुजीवामः Mb.<BR>—3 To live for any one.<BR>—4 To follow or imitate in living; प्रेमदत्तवदनानिलः पिबन्नन्वजीवदमरालकेश्वरौ<BR> R. 19. 15 v. l. (अत्यजीवत्).<BR>—5 To survive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविन्
अनुजीविन् <i>a.</i> Dependent, living on or upon. ━<i>m.</i> A dependent,<BR> servant, follower; अवञ्चनीयाः प्रभवोऽनुजीविभिः Ki. 1. 4, 10; भर्तुश्चिन्तानुवर्तित्वं<BR> सुवृत्तं चानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविवृत्तम्
अनुजीविन् + ˚वृत्तम् conduct of a courtier; Kau. A. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्य
अनुजीव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be served (as a master).<BR>—2 To be followed in living; आचार्यो गुरवो वृद्धा वृथा वां पर्युपासिताः ।<BR> सारं यद्राजशास्त्राणामनुजीव्यं न गृह्यते ॥ Rām. 6. 29. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To permit, allow (a person or thing); assent or consent to, approve;<BR> authorise, sanction; तदनुजानीहि मां गमनाय U. 3 so let me go;<BR> सेयं याति शकुन्तला पतिगृहं सर्वैरनुज्ञायताम् Ś. 4. 9 permitted<BR> to go; ततोऽनुजज्ञे गमनं सुतस्य Bk. 1. 23; M. 1. 19; तन्मया<BR> प्रीतिमताऽनुज्ञातम् Ś. 5 approved, agreed to.<BR>—2 To betroth, affiance; मां जातमात्रां धनमित्रनाम्नेऽन्वजानाद्भार्यां<BR> मे पिता Dk. 50.<BR>—3 To excuse, forgive; अनुप्रवेशे यद्वीर कृतवांस्त्वं ममाप्रियम् ।<BR> सर्वं तदनुजानामि Mb.<BR>—4 To repent, be sorry for.<BR>—5 To request, entreat, beg; त्वां साहमनुजानामि न गन्तव्यमितो वनम् Rām.<BR>—6 To treat or behave kindly, favour; ते मां वीर्येण यशसा …<BR> अस्त्रैश्चाप्यन्वजानत Mb.<BR>—7 To dismiss, bid farewell (usually in caus.).<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> (-ज्ञापयति)<BR>—1 To ask or beg for, request.<BR>—2 To ask permission, ask for leave; take leave of, bid adieu to; सोऽपि<BR> तत् श्रुत्वा … वानरमनुज्ञाप्य स्वाश्रयं गतः Pt. 4; तं चकधरमनुज्ञाप्य<BR> स्वगृहं गतः 5; अतिथिं चाननुज्ञाप्य Ms. 4. 122, 9. 82; स मातरमनुज्ञाप्य<BR> तपस्येव मनो दधे । जग्मतुश्च यथाकाममनुज्ञाप्य परस्परम् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा, -ज्ञानम्<BR> [ज्ञा-अङ् -ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Permission, consent, sanction; गुरोरनुज्ञामधिगम्य मातः (v. l.<BR> ऋषेरनुज्ञाम्) R. 2. 66.<BR>—2 Permission or leave to depart.<BR>—3 Excusing, forgiving, allowance made for faults.<BR>—4 An order, command.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुज्ञैषणा, अनुज्ञाप्रार्थना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञानम्
अनुज्ञा, -ज्ञानम्<BR> [ज्ञा-अङ् -ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Permission, consent, sanction; गुरोरनुज्ञामधिगम्य मातः (v. l.<BR> ऋषेरनुज्ञाम्) R. 2. 66.<BR>—2 Permission or leave to depart.<BR>—3 Excusing, forgiving, allowance made for faults.<BR>—4 An order, command.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुज्ञैषणा, अनुज्ञाप्रार्थना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञैषणा
अनुज्ञा + -एषणा, -प्रार्थना requesting permission, taking leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञाप्रार्थना
अनुज्ञा + -एषणा, -प्रार्थना requesting permission, taking leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञात
अनुज्ञात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Permitted, allowed, ब्रह्म यस्त्वननुज्ञातमधीयानादवाप्नुयात् । स<BR> ब्रह्मस्तेयसंयुक्तो नरकं प्रतिपद्यते ॥ Ms. 2. 116.<BR>—2 assented to, granted, honoured, favoured.<BR>—3 authorised.<BR>—4 dismissed.<BR>—5 Taught; शिष्याणामखिलं कृत्स्नमनुज्ञातं ससंग्रहम् Mb. 12. 318. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापकः|अनुज्ञापक
अनुज्ञापकः One who commands or orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापनम्
अनुज्ञापनम्, -ज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Authorising.<BR>—2 Issuing an order or command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञप्तिः|अनुज्ञप्ति
अनुज्ञापनम्, -ज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Authorising.<BR>—2 Issuing an order or command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्येष्ठ
अनुज्येष्ठ <i>a.</i> [अनुगतो ज्येष्टम्] Next to the eldest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्येष्ठम्
अनुज्येष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@} <i>adv.</i> According to seniority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्
अनुतप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To heat; vex, annoy (fig.).<BR>—2 (€4 Ā. or <i>pass.</i>) To repent, grieve, be sorry for, be stung with<BR> remorse; विविधैरनुतप्यन्ते दयितानुनयैर्मनस्विन्यः V. 3. 5 (v. l.<BR> for निर्भृतैर्व्यपत्रपन्ते &c.); तेनानिमित्तेन तथा न पार्थस्तयोर्यंथा<BR> रिक्ततयानुतेपे Ki. 17. 40. ━<i>Caus.</i> To pain, afflict, distress<BR> विरहः किमिवानुतापयेद्वद बाह्यैर्विषयैर्विपश्चितम् R. 8. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्त
अनुतप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated.<BR>—2 Filled with regret, repentant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापः|अनुताप
अनुतापः<BR>—1 Repentance, remorse, contrition, subsequent regret or sorrow; जातानुतापेव<BR> सा V. 4. 67 stung with remorse; ख्यापनेनानुतापेन (पापकृन्मुच्यते<BR> पापात्) Ms. 11. 228.<BR>—2 Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापन
अनुतापन <i>a.</i> Causing distress or regret or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापिन्
अनुतापिन् <i>a.</i> Repentant, sorry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनुतर See under अनुतॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षः|अनुतर्ष
अनुतर्षः [तृष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Thirst, desire to drink; सोपचारमुपशान्तविचारं सानुतर्षमनुतर्षपदेन<BR> Śi. 10. 2 (thirst and liquor).<BR>—2 Wish, desire.<BR>—3 Drinking spirituous liquors.<BR>—4 A drinking vessel (used in drinking spirituous liquors).<BR>—5 Liquor itself, Śi. 10. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षणम्
अनुतर्षणम् = अनुतर्ष 3 and 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिल
अनुतिल <i>a.</i> Following तिल (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिलम्
अनुतिल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Grain after grain, <i>i. e.</i> by grains or very minutely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतुन्न
अनुतुन्न <i>a.</i> Ved. Depressed or repressed (in sound), unruffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतूलयति
अनुतूलयति Den. P. To rub (as the point or end of grass) with cotton; P. III. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतूलनम्
अनुतूलनम् Rubbing in this manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतॄ
अनुतॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To go across or to the end.<BR>—2 To stretch lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतरम्
अनुतरम् [अनुतीर्यते अनेन; तॄ-करणे अप्] Fare, freight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्क
अनुत्क <i>a.</i> Not over-anxious, not repentant or regretful; self-complacent<BR> अपरः कोकिलोऽनुत्को यं प्रतिश्रुत्य कूजति । Bu. C. 4. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्कट
अनुत्कट <i>a.</i> Short, small; Hc. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्त
अनुत्त <i>a.</i> Ved. [उन्द्-क्त, न˚ त˚ P. VIII. 2. 61]<BR>—1 Not moistened or wet; तुभ्यमिदद्रिवोऽनुत्तम् Rv. 1. 80. 7.<BR>—2 Not set, driven forth or urged (अप्रेरित); invincible (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम <i>a.</i> [न उत्तमो यस्मात्]<BR>—1 Than which there is nothing better, having no superior or better, unsurpassed,<BR> the very best or highest, incomparably or pre-eminently the best; सर्वद्रव्येषु<BR> विद्यैव द्रव्यमाहुरनुत्तमम् H. Pr. 4; काङ्क्षन् गतिमनुत्तमाम् Ms. 2. 242;<BR> Y. 1. 87;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">Page0094-2</a>]<BR> अदस्त्वया नुन्नमनुत्तमं तमः Śi. 1. 27 all-pervading; Bg. 7. 18;<BR> Ms. 2. 9, 5. 158, 8. 81.<BR>—2 Not the best.<BR>—3 (in gram.) Not used in the उत्तम or first person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तमः|अनुत्तम
अनुत्तम + .{@-मः@} N. of Śiva or Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुत्तमाम्भस्, अनुत्तमाम्भसिकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तमाम्भस्
अनुत्तम + -अम्भस्, -अम्भसिकम् a term in Sāṅkhya Philosophy, said to mean<BR> ‘indifference to and abstinence from sensual enjoyment, as fatiguing or involving injury to external objects’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तमाम्भसिकम्
अनुत्तम + -अम्भस्, -अम्भसिकम् a term in Sāṅkhya Philosophy, said to mean<BR> ‘indifference to and abstinence from sensual enjoyment, as fatiguing or involving injury to external objects’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तर|अनुत्तरं
अनुत्तर <i>a.</i> [नास्ति उत्तरो यस्मात्]<BR>—1 Principal, chief.<BR>—2 Best, excellent; अनुत्तराणि विलसितानि Dk. 162 unsurpassed. शरीरसौख्यार्थमनुत्तरस्य<BR> निपेततुर्मूर्धनि तस्य सौम्ये । Bu. C. 1. 35.<BR>—3 [नास्ति उत्तरं यस्य] Without a reply, silent, unable to answer;<BR> भवत्यवज्ञा च भवत्यनुत्तरात् Naiṣadha.<BR>—4 Fixed, firm (न उत्तरति चलति). अर्थ्यं तथ्यं हितं वाक्यं<BR> लघुयुक्तमनुत्तरम् Mb. 2. 2. 5.<BR>—5 Low, inferior, base, mean.<BR>—6 Southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरम्
अनुत्तर + .{@-रम्@} [न˚ त˚] No reply, a reply which, being evasive,<BR> is considered to be no reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तराः
अनुत्तर + .{@-राः@} (pl.) A class of gods among Jainas (˚उपपातिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरोपपातिकदशाः
अनुत्तर + .{@-उपपातिकदशाः@} <i>f.</i> Title of the ninth aṅga of the Jainas<BR> treating of those gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरा
अनुत्तर + .{@-रा@} The south<BR> … अनुत्तरः । नोदीच्यां नोपरि श्रेष्ठे … । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुत्तरयोगतन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरयोगतन्त्रम्
अनुत्तर + -योगतन्त्रम् Title of the last of the four Bauddhatantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरङ्ग
अनुत्तरङ्ग <i>a.</i> Steady, not ruffled (by waves); अपामिवाधारमनुत्तरङ्गम् Ku. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तालः|अनुत्ताल
अनुत्तालः A melodious note; Hc. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्थानम्
अनुत्थानम् Absence of exertion. अनुत्थाने ध्रुवो नाशः Kau. A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिः|अनुत्पत्ति
अनुत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> Failure, non-production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिक
अनुत्पत्तिः + .{@-त्तिक@} <i>a.</i> Not yet produced.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुत्पत्तिधर्मक्षान्तिः, अनुत्पत्तिसमः, अनुत्पत्तिसमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिधर्मक्षान्तिः|अनुत्पत्तिधर्मक्षान्ति
अनुत्पत्तिः + -धर्मक्षान्तिः preparation for a future state, acquiescence in<BR> the state and moral condition which is yet to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिसमः|अनुत्पत्तिसम
अनुत्पत्तिः + -समः, -समा a method of arguing against a thing by attempting<BR> to prove that nothing exists from which it could spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिसमा
अनुत्पत्तिः + -समः, -समा a method of arguing against a thing by attempting<BR> to prove that nothing exists from which it could spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पन्न
अनुत्पन्न <i>a.</i> Not produced or born, unborn, unproduced &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पादः|अनुत्पाद
अनुत्पादः Not coming into existence, not taking effect.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुत्पादक्षान्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पादक्षान्ति
अनुत्पादः + -क्षान्ति see अनुत्पत्तिधर्मक्षान्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्साह|अनुत्साहः
अनुत्साह <i>a.</i> Destitute of energy or determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्साहः|अनुत्साह
अनुत्साह + .{@-हः@} Want of determination, energy &c.; listlessness, languor, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सुक
अनुत्सुक <i>a.</i> Moderate, not overeager, retiring, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सूत्र
अनुत्सूत्र <i>a.</i> Not deviating from the Sūtra (of Pāṇini or of<BR> morality); not anomalous or irregular; ˚पदन्यासा सद्वृत्तिः सन्निबन्धना Śi. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेकः|अनुत्सेक
अनुत्सेकः Absence of haughtiness or pride; ˚को लक्ष्म्याम् Bh. 2. 64;<BR> modesty; ˚कः खलु विकमालङ्कारः V. 1; cf. "Modesty is the handmaid of heroism".<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेकिन्
अनुत्सेकिन् <i>a.</i> Not puffed up, not proud or arrogant; भाग्येषु<BR> ˚नी भव Ś. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद
अनुद <i>a.</i> [न नुदति or अनुददाति तुल्यं ददाति, दा-क]<BR> Ved. Not urging or driving onward; or, emulating others in giving (तुल्यरूपदातृ);<BR> see अनानुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदक
अनुदक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Waterless (as a desert). याः प्रवतो निवत उद्वत उदन्वतीरनुदकाश्च<BR> याः Rv. 7. 50. 4.<BR>—2 Having very little water (as a puddle).<BR>—3 Devoid of the libations of water (a sort of श्राद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदग्र|अनुदग्रः
अनुदग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not lofty, low.<BR>—2 Soft, tender; weak, not sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर
अनुदर <i>a.</i> —1 Having a slender waist; thin, lank; ˚राजकन्या<BR> Sk. (अल्पार्थे नञ्, see अ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदा
अनुदा €3 U. To give back, restore; to yield, grant, remit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेयी
अनुदेयी<BR>—1 Restoration.<BR>—2 A female companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्त|अनुदात्तः
अनुदात्त <i>a.</i> Grave (accent); not elevated or raised (not pronounced<BR> with the Udātta accent); उच्चैरुदात्तः नीचैरनुदात्तः; accentless,<BR> having the neutral, general tone; उदात्तश्चानुदात्तश्च स्वरितश्च त्रयः<BR> स्वराः uttered with the grave accent (as a vowel); प्रयत्नप्रेरितो<BR> वायुर्यदोर्ध्वभागे प्रतिहतोऽचं निष्पादयति स उदात्तः; एवमधोनिष्पन्नोऽच्<BR> अनुदात्तः; ताल्वादिषु सभागेषु स्थानेषु नीचभागे निष्पन्नोऽच् अनुदात्तः;<BR> ˚त्तं पदमेकवर्जम् Sk. (The term अनुदात्त is used by Pāṇini for<BR> the grave accent which immediately precedes the Udātta, and also for<BR> the general accentless tone neither high nor low, termed एकश्रुति,<BR> the one monotonous intonation belonging to the generality of syllables in a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्तः|अनुदात्त
अनुदात्त + .{@-त्तः@} The grave accent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुदात्तादिः, अनुदात्तेत्, अनुदात्तोदयम्, अनुदात्ततर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्तादिः|अनुदात्तादि
अनुदात्त + -आदिः a nominal base of which the first syllable is अनुदात्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्तेत्
अनुदात्त + -इत् a verbal root having for its अनुबन्ध the grave accent<BR> (denoting that it takes the Ātm. terminations only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्तोदयम्
अनुदात्त + -उदयम् a syllable followed (immediately) by the grave accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्ततर
अनुदात्त + -तर <i>a.</i> more than अनुदात्त; still lower or graver accent,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> that which immediately precedes a syllable having the उदात्त<BR> or स्वरित accent and is thus more depressed than the ordinary अनुदात्त accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not liberal, niggardly; not high or noble.<BR>—2 Having none more liberal, very liberal, or great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार <i>a.</i> (अनुगतो दारान्) —1 Adhering to or followed by a<BR> wife; यस्मिन्प्रसीदसि पुनः स भवत्युदारोऽनुदारश्च K. P. 4. (used in sense<BR>—1 also).<BR>—2 Having a suitable or worthy wife (अनुरूपाः दाराः यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
अनुदित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unsaid, not uttered.<BR>—2 Not risen or appeared forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिनम्
अनुदिनम्, -दिवसम् <i>ind.</i><BR> Daily, day after day; पारावतः खलु शिलाकणमात्रभोजी<BR> कामी भवेदनुदिनं वद कोऽत्र हेतुः Udb.; अनुदिवसं परिहीयसेऽङ्गैः Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिवसम्
अनुदिनम्, -दिवसम् <i>ind.</i><BR> Daily, day after day; पारावतः खलु शिलाकणमात्रभोजी<BR> कामी भवेदनुदिनं वद कोऽत्र हेतुः Udb.; अनुदिवसं परिहीयसेऽङ्गैः Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिश्
अनुदिश् €6 P. To point out, assign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिशम्
अनुदिश् + .{@-अनुदिशम्@} <i>ind.</i> In every quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेशः|अनुदेश
अनुदेशः<BR>—1 Pointing back; rule or direction which refers or points back to a previous<BR> rule; यथासङ्ख्यमनुदेशः समानाम् P. I. 3. 10; subsequent mention<BR> of things (words, suffixes &c.) in the order of things previously mentioned;<BR> respective enumeration or statement,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">Page0095-2</a>]<BR> first for first, second for second; as in समूलाकृतजीवेषु हन्कृञ्ग्रहः P. III. 4. 36.<BR>—2 Direction, order, injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेशिन्
अनुदेशिन् <i>a.</i> Pointing or referring back; being the object of an अनुदेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृश्
अनुदृश् €1 P. To survey, behold; to keep in view or mind, see in prospect;<BR> पूर्वेषां पन्थामनुदृश्य धीराः Rv. 10. 130. 7. न च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि<BR> हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे Bg. 1. 31; न संसारोत्पन्नं चरितमनुपश्यामि<BR> कुशलम् Bh. 3. 3. ━<i>Caus.</i> To show, tell, inform as follows; सेनापतिः<BR> पुत्रमग्निमित्रं परिष्वज्य अनुदर्शयति M. 5 writes or informs as follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर्शनम्
अनुदर्शनम् Inspection, survey; उत्थितश्चाप्रमत्तश्च बलानामनुदर्शने<BR> Rām.; consideration, regard; जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम्<BR> Bg. 13. 8 perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृष्टि|अनुदृष्टिः
अनुदृष्टि <i>a.</i> Having a favourable look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृष्टिः|अनुदृष्टि
अनुदृष्टि + .{@-ष्टिः@} <i>f.</i> A favourable look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रष्टृ
अनुद्रष्टृ <i>a.</i> Benefactor; अनसूयुरनुद्रष्टा सत्कृतस्ते पुरोहितः<BR> Rām. 2. 100. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदैर्घ्य
अनुदैर्घ्य <i>a.</i> [दैर्ध्यमनुगतः] Longitudinal, lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धत
अनुद्धत <i>a.</i> Not raised or puffed up; ˚ताः सत्पुरुषाः समृद्धिभिः<BR> Ś. 5. 12; humble; modest; unsurpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धरणम्
अनुद्धरणम्<BR>—1 Not removing or taking away.<BR>—2 Not offering, establishing or proving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धात
अनुद्धात <i>a.</i> Even, without ups and downs स्थेनानुद्धातस्तिमितगतिना<BR> तिर्णजलधिः Ś. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धारः|अनुद्धार
अनुद्धारः<BR>—1 Non-partition; not taking a share (र्विशोद्धारशून्यो विभागः).<BR>—2 Non-removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृत
अनुद्धृत <i>a.</i> Undivided, unremoved, uninjured, unharmed, undestroyed,<BR> unoffered or established &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुद्धृताभ्यस्तमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृताभ्यस्तमयः|अनुद्धृताभ्यस्तमय
अनुद्धृत + -अभ्यस्तमयः taking place of sunset, while the आहवनीय<BR> fire continues to be unremoved from the गार्हपत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्भट
अनुद्भट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bold; soft, mild.<BR>—2 Not exalted or lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्य
अनुद्य <i>a.</i> unutterable; P. III. 1. 101. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यत
अनुद्यत, अनुद्यम <i>a.</i> Not diligent, idle, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यम
अनुद्यत, अनुद्यम <i>a.</i> Not diligent, idle, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यूतम्
अनुद्यूतम् Repeated playing or gambling; N. of a part of the Sabhāparvan (Chap. 70-79).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योग|अनुद्योगः
अनुद्योग <i>a.</i> Lazy, not industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योगः|अनुद्योग
अनुद्योग + .{@-गः@} Idleness, inactivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रु
अनुद्रु €1 P.<BR>—1 To run after, follow, accompany. अश्वेति विद्रुतमनुद्रवताश्वमन्यम् Śi. 5. 59.<BR>—2 To chase, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रुत|अनुद्रुतं
अनुद्रुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Followed, pursued; धनुर्धरं राजसुतैरनुद्रुतम् R. 3. 38, 12. 67, 16. 25;<BR> Śi. 1. 52; (sometimes used actively).<BR>—2 Sent or brought back (as sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रुतम्
अनुद्रुत + .{@-तम्@} A measure of time in music = half <i>druta</i>, or one-fourth<BR> of a Mātrā (or of the time taken to utter a short vowel); अर्धमात्रं<BR> द्रुतं ज्ञेयं द्रुतार्घं चाप्यनुद्रुतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वाहः|अनुद्वाह
अनुद्वाहः Non-marriage, celibacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्विग्न
अनुद्विग्न <i>a.</i> Easy in mind, secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वेग|अनुद्वेगः
अनुद्वेग <i>a.</i> Free from anxiety or apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वेगः|अनुद्वेग
अनुद्वेग + .{@-गः@} Security or freedom from fear. अदैन्यमनुदीर्णत्वमनुद्वेगो<BR> व्यवस्थितिः Mb. 12. 274. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधाव्
अनुधाव् €1 P.<BR>—1 To run after; follow; ऋषीणां पुनराद्यानां वाचमर्थोऽनुधावति U. 1. 10<BR> the sense follows the words (the words being not uttered with a<BR> view to a particular sense); स्वरुचिं निश्चयतोऽनुधावति Śi. 16. 44<BR> follows his own will.<BR>—2 To run up to, approach.<BR>—3 To cleanse, wash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावनम्
अनुधावनम्<BR>—1 Going or running after, following, pursuing; तुरग ˚कण्डितसन्धेः Ś. 2.<BR>—2 Close pursuit of an object (for the knowledge of truth); research, investigation.<BR>—3 Seeking a mistress, though unattainable.<BR>—4 Cleansing, purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधूपित
अनुधूपित <i>a.</i> Puffed up, proud, ज्योगभूवन्ननुधूपितासो हत्वी<BR> तेंषामा भरा नो वसूनि Rv. 2. 30. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यै
अनुध्यै €1 P.<BR>—1 To think of, muse, consider attentively.<BR>—2 To wish well of, to bless, favour; प्रजानिषेकं मयि वर्तमानं सूनोरनुध्यायत<BR> चेतसेति R. 14. 60 bless; अनुदध्युरनुध्येयं सांनिध्यैः प्रतिमागतैः 17. 36<BR> favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्या
अनुध्या [ध्यै-अङ्]<BR>—1 Thinking or wishing well of, favouring, attachment. यदनुध्यासिना<BR> युक्ताः कर्मग्रन्थिनिबन्धनम् Bhāg. 1. 2. 15.<BR>—2 Sorrow; प्रेतो यन्तु व्याधः प्रानुध्याः Av. 7. 114. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यान
अनुध्यान <i>p. p.</i> Mused, thought of &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यातम्
अनुध्यान + .{@-तम्, -नम्@} [ध्यै-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Thought; अनुध्यानानन्तरमेव K. 262; meditation, religious contemplation.<BR>—2 Thinking of, remembrance; या नः प्रीतिर्विरूपाक्ष त्वदनुध्यानसम्भवा Ku. 6. 21.<BR>—3 Wishing well of, affectionate solicitude for; अनुध्यानैरुपेतव्यं<BR> वत्सयोर्भद्रमस्तु वः (v. l. अनुध्यातै) U. 7. 11; सा त्वमम्ब<BR> स्नुषायामरुन्धतीव सीतायां शिवानुध्यानपरां भव U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यानम्
अनुध्यान + .{@-तम्, -नम्@} [ध्यै-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Thought; अनुध्यानानन्तरमेव K. 262; meditation, religious contemplation.<BR>—2 Thinking of, remembrance; या नः प्रीतिर्विरूपाक्ष त्वदनुध्यानसम्भवा Ku. 6. 21.<BR>—3 Wishing well of, affectionate solicitude for; अनुध्यानैरुपेतव्यं<BR> वत्सयोर्भद्रमस्तु वः (v. l. अनुध्यातै) U. 7. 11; सा त्वमम्ब<BR> स्नुषायामरुन्धतीव सीतायां शिवानुध्यानपरां भव U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यायः|अनुध्याय
अनुध्यायः [ध्यै कर्तरि घञ्] One who wishes well of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्येय
अनुध्येय <i>a.</i> To be favoured or wished well of; अनुदध्युरनुध्येयम् R. 17. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनद्
अनुनद् €1 P. To sound towards or at (with acc.).<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to sound, make resonant, fill with echo; पृथिवीं<BR> चान्तरिक्षं च सागरांश्चानुनादयन्; साधु साध्विति नादेन पृथिवीमन्वनादयन्;<BR> विहङ्गैरनुनादितम् Mb. made musical or resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनादः|अनुनाद
अनुनादः [अनुरूपो नादः] Sound, noise; गुरुतरकलनूपुरानुनादम्<BR> Śi. 7. 18; reverberation, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनादिन्
अनुनादिन् <i>a.</i> Echoing, sounding, resonant. तस्यास्फोटितशब्देन<BR> महता चानुनादिना । पेतुर्विहङ्गा गगनादुच्चैश्चेदमघोषयन् ॥ Rām. 5. 42. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनन्द्
अनुनन्द् €1 P. To enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय, -नायिका<BR> See under अनुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायिका
अनुनय, -नायिका<BR> See under अनुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिक
अनुनासिक <i>a.</i> [अनुगतो नासिकाम्]<BR>—1 Nasal, pronounced through the nose; मुखसहितनासिकया उच्चार्यमाणो<BR> वर्णोऽनुनासिकसंज्ञः स्यात् Sk.; मुखनासिकावचनोऽनुनासिकः P. I. 1. 8;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">Page0096-2</a>]<BR> अमोऽनुनासिका न ह्रौ Śik.; अनुनासिक being a name for the 5<BR> nasal consonants, the vowels or the consonants य्, व्, ल् (under certain<BR> circumstances); <i>i. e.</i> the letters included in the प्रत्याहार अम्<BR> except ह् and र्.<BR>—2 The sign used to mark the nasalization in the case of य्, व् or ल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिकम्
अनुनासिक + .{@-कम्@} The nasal twang.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुनासिकादिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिकादिः|अनुनासिकादि
अनुनासिक + -आदिः a conjunct consonant beginning with a nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्देशः|अनुनिर्देश
अनुनिर्देशः Description or relation following the previous order<BR> or sequence; भूयसामुपदिष्टानां क्रियाणामथ कर्मणाम् । क्रमशो योऽनुनिर्देशो<BR> यथासङ्ख्यं तदुच्यते S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्वापः|अनुनिर्वाप
अनुनिर्वापः Subsequent libation (with clarified butter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्वाप्या
अनुनिर्वाप्या A ceremony connected with this libation<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिशीथम्
अनुनिशीथम् <i>ind.</i> At midnight; Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनी
अनुनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To conciliate, win over, induce, persuade, prevail upon; request, supplicate,<BR> entreat, propitiate, pacify, appease (anger &c.); स चानुनीतः प्रणतेन<BR> पश्चात् R. 5. 54; विग्रहाच्च शयने पराङ्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स तत्वरे 19. 38, 43;<BR> Bk. 5. 46, 6. 137; त्वत्सङ्गमेन मम तत्तदिवानुनीतम्<BR> V. 3. 20 pacified, made favourable or agreeable; Ki. 13. 67; M. 5; K. 168, 178;<BR> Dk. 3, 4, 7.<BR>—2 To cherish love; विद्विषोप्यनुनय Bh. 2. 77; cf. Shakespeare "Cherish<BR> those hearts that hate thee".<BR>—3 To bring near to (with dat. of reason).<BR>—4 To train, discipline.<BR>—5 To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय <i>a.</i> [नी-अच्] Kind, conciliatory, pacifying (as words).<BR> तुल्यदुःखोऽब्रवीद्भ्राता लक्ष्मणोऽनुनयं वचः Rām. 4. 27. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयः|अनुनय
अनुनय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Conciliation, propitiation, pacification (of anger), friendly persuasion;<BR> कथं नु शक्योऽनुनयो महर्षेर्विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनाम् R. 2. 54;<BR> कथं वा तेषामनुनयः कृतः H. 4; प्रकृतिवक्रः स कस्यानुनयं<BR> प्रतिगृह्णाति Ś. 4.<BR>—2 Courtesy, civility, courteous or polite behaviour, modesty, modest<BR> or respectful deportment, conciliatory act (such as salutation); showing<BR> respect (to a guest, deity &c.); विविधैरनुतप्यन्ते दयितानुनयैर्मनस्विन्यः<BR> V. 3. 5; दयितजन˚ 2. 22; वाक्यैः स्निग्धैरनुनयो भवेदर्थस्य साधनम् S. D. 458.<BR>—3 An humble supplication or entreaty, a request in oeneral; भद्र प्रियं<BR> नःकिंतु त्वदभिप्रायापरिज्ञानान्तरितोऽयमस्मदनुनयः Mu. 2; R. 6. 2;<BR> निषेधवाक्यालङ्कारजिज्ञासानुनये खलु Ak; ˚आमन्त्रणम् conciliatory address.<BR>—4 Discipline, training, regulation of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयम्
अनुनय + .{@-यम्@} <i>adv.</i> Fitly, suitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयिन्
अनुनयिन् <i>a.</i> Courteous, polite, humble, supplicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनीतिः|अनुनीति
अनुनीतिः = अनुनय q. v.; सानुनीतिश्च सीतायै नाकुध्यत् Bk. 8. 75<BR> adopting a conciliatory tone; भजते कुपितोऽप्युदारधीरनुनीतिं<BR> नतिमात्रकेण सः Śi. 16. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायक
अनुनायक <i>a.</i> Submissive, humble, supplicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायिक
अनुनायिक <i>a.</i> Conciliating; प्रियतमेषु वधूरनुनायिका Śi. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायिका
अनुनायिक + .{@-का@} A female character subordinate to the Nāyikā or leading<BR> character, such as a friend, nurse, maid-servant &c.; सखी प्रव्रजिता<BR> दासी प्रेष्या धात्रेयिका तथा । अन्याश्च शिल्पकारिण्यो विज्ञेया ह्यनुनायिकाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनेय
अनुनेय (-नीय)<BR> <i>a.</i> Favourable; अनुनेयानि जल्पन्तम् Mb. 7. 85. 25<BR> To be conciliated; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनीय
अनुनेय (-नीय)<BR> <i>a.</i> Favourable; अनुनेयानि जल्पन्तम् Mb. 7. 85. 25<BR> To be conciliated; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्नत
अनुन्नत <i>a.</i> Not raised or elevated, not lifted up.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुन्नतानत, अनुन्नतगात्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्नतानत
अनुन्नत + -आनत <i>a.</i> level (neither raised nor lowered).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्नतगात्र
अनुन्नत + -गात्र <i>a.</i> having limbs not stout or prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्माद
अनुन्माद, अनुन्मत्त <i>a.</i><BR> Not mad or frantic, sober, calm, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्मत्त
अनुन्माद, अनुन्मत्त <i>a.</i><BR> Not mad or frantic, sober, calm, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप
अनुप = अनूप, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकारिन्
अनुपकारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not obliging, ungrateful, not making a return for benefits received.<BR>—2 Worthless, useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपक्षित
अनुपक्षित <i>p. p.</i> Not injured or destroyed (अनुपक्षीण). द्युमदग्ने<BR> सूवीर्यं वर्षिष्ठमनुपक्षितम् Rv. 3. 13. 7; Av. 6. 78. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपगीत
अनुपगीत <i>a.</i> Not praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपगीतम्
अनुपगीत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> So that no other person accompanies in singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपघातः|अनुपघात
अनुपघातः Absence of damage or detriment;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपघातार्जित
अनुपघातः + ˚अर्जित obtained without<BR> any detriment (to the paternal estate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपजीवनीय
अनुपजीवनीय <i>a.</i> Not yielding or granting livelihood, having no livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठ्
अनुपठ् €1 P. To say after, repeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठित
अनुपठित <i>p. p.</i> Read through, repeated in imitation of the teacherʼs instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठितिन्
अनुपठितिन् <i>a.</i> Who has read through, proficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपत्
अनुपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly to or towards.<BR>—2 To fly or run after, follow (fig. also); pursue, chase; मुहुरनुपतति<BR> स्यन्दने दत्तदृष्टिः Ś. 1. 7; कथमनुपतत एव मे प्रयत्नप्रेक्षणीयः<BR> संवृत्तः Ś. 1; न यत्र प्रत्याशामनुपतति नो वा रहयति (चेतः)<BR> Māl. 9. 8 does not run after (cherish), hope or leave it; यस्यैवं<BR> भवन्तः कुटुम्बवृत्तिमनुपतिताः Mv. 1; अनुपतति रजनीं पूर्वसन्ध्या Śi. 11. 40.<BR>—3 To fall upon, attack; प्राग्वीराननुपत्य Māl. 8. 9.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fly to.<BR>—2 To throw another down along with oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतनम्
अनुपतनम्, -पातः<BR>—1 Falling upon, alighting upon in succession.<BR>—2 Following, going after, pursuit; उपवनपवनानुपातदक्षैः Śi. 7. 27.<BR>—3 Going or proceeding in order or as a consequence.<BR>—4 [अनुरूपः त्रैराशिकेन पातः] Proportion.<BR>—5 Rule of three.<BR>—6 A degree of latitude, opposite to one given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातः|अनुपात
अनुपतनम्, -पातः<BR>—1 Falling upon, alighting upon in succession.<BR>—2 Following, going after, pursuit; उपवनपवनानुपातदक्षैः Śi. 7. 27.<BR>—3 Going or proceeding in order or as a consequence.<BR>—4 [अनुरूपः त्रैराशिकेन पातः] Proportion.<BR>—5 Rule of three.<BR>—6 A degree of latitude, opposite to one given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातम्
अनुपतनम्, -पातः + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> (regarded as ending in <i>namul</i> from पत्) Following<BR> in succession, going after; लतानुपातं कुसुमान्यगृह्णात् Bk. 2. 11<BR> (लतां लतामनुपात्य going to creeper after creeper, or after bending the creepers.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातिन्
अनुपातिन् <i>a.</i> Following as a result. ━<i>m.</i> A follower; मदनुपातिनामेष<BR> पन्थाः Dk. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपथ|अनुपथः
अनुपथ <i>a.</i> [पन्थानमनुगतः] Following the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपथः|अनुपथ
अनुपथ + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 A road, favourable road; अन्तस्पथा अनुपथाः Rv. 5. 52. 10<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">Page0097-2</a>]<BR> (अनुकूलमार्गाः)<BR>—2 an attendant; क एतेऽनुपथा ये ते एकादश महाभटाः Bhāg. 4. 25. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपथम्
अनुपथ + .{@-थम्@} <i>adv.</i> Along the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद्
अनुपद् €4 Ā. (P. in epic poetry)<BR>—1 To go after, follow, attend.<BR>—2 To be fond of, be attached to (as a wife); उतथ्यस्य यवीयांस्तु ममतामन्वपद्यत Mb.<BR>—3 To enter, go to or into.<BR>—4 To fall down, come down (to the earth); वसुधामन्वपद्येतां वातनुन्नाविव द्रुमौ Mb.<BR>—5 To enter upon, betake oneself to; जितमित्येव तानक्षान्पुनरेवान्वपद्यत,<BR> ध्यानमेवान्वपद्यत Rām.; पुत्रौ दृष्ट्वा सुसंभ्रान्ता नान्वपद्यत<BR> किंचन Mb. did not do anything else.<BR>—6 To find, discover, see, notice; दीर्घं दध्यौ … निमित्तं सोऽन्वपद्यत Bhāg.<BR>—7 To lose (with abl.) महत्त्वान्नान्वपद्येताम् Mb.<BR>—8 To handle.<BR>—9 To fall to the share of (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद्
अनुपद् <i>a.</i> [पद्-क्विप्] Ved. Coming to pass. ━<i>f.</i> Food (got<BR> every day) (अनुदिनलभ्यमन्नम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद|अनुपदं|अनुपदः
अनुपद <i>a.</i> [पदान्यनुगतः]<BR>—1 Following the feet closely.<BR>—2 Following every word;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदसूत्रम्
अनुपद + ˚सूत्रम् a commentary (of a Brāhmaṇa) explaining<BR> the text word for word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदः|अनुपद|अनुपदं
अनुपद + .{@-दः@} N. of a man or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदम्
अनुपद + .{@-दम्@} A chorus, burden of a song or words sung again at regular<BR> intervals. ━<i>ind.</i> [पदानां पश्चात्]<BR>—1 Along the feet, near the feet; अनुपदं बद्धा अनुपदीना Sk.<BR>—2 Step by step, at every step; स्खलिताभिरप्यनुपदं प्रमदाः प्रणयातिभूमिमगमन्गतिभिः Śi. 9. 78.<BR>—3 Word for word.<BR>—4 On the heels of, close behind or after, immediately after (of time<BR> or space); अनुपदमन्वेष्टा अनुपदी Sk.; गच्छतां पुरो भवन्तौ । अहमप्यनुपदमागत<BR> एव Ś. 3 I shall be close behind you, just follow you; ˚दमुच्चलित<BR> एव K. 263, 264; oft. with gen. or in comp. in this sense; लक्ष्मीवाननुपदमस्य<BR> संप्रतस्थे Ki. 12. 54; (तौ) आशिषामनुपदं समस्पृशत् पाणिना<BR> R. 11. 31; अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णन्तावर्ध्यानुपदमाशिषः 1. 44, 14. 81;<BR> दर्शनानुपदमेव Śi. 14. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिक
अनुपदिक <i>a.</i> [अनुपदमस्त्यस्य गन्तृत्वेन, ठन्] Following, gone after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिन्
अनुपदिन् <i>a.</i> [अनुपद्-इनि P. V. 2. 90] Following, seeking after<BR> or for a searcher, inquirer; अनुपदमन्वेष्टा गवामनुपदी Sk.; क्षणदाकरेऽनुपदिभिः<BR> प्रयये Śi. 9. 70; मृगस्यानुपदी रामो जगाम गजविकमः Bk. 5. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदीना
अनुपदीना [आयामार्थे अनु, पदस्यायामतुल्यायामः, तेन बद्धा ख]<BR> A shoe (boot, buskin, or slippers) of the length of the foot (अनुपदं<BR> बद्धा अनुपदीना उपानत् P. V. 2. 9. Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदवी
अनुपदवी A way, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपधः|अनुपध
अनुपधः ‘Having no उपधा or penultimate’, a letter or syllable<BR> not preceded by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपधि
अनुपधि <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Guileless, without fraud; रहस्यं<BR> साधूनामनुपधि विशुद्धं विजयते U. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यासः|अनुपन्यास
अनुपन्यासः<BR>—1 Not mentioning; non-statement.<BR>—2 Uncertainty, doubt, failure of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपत्तिः|अनुपपत्ति
अनुपपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Failure, failing to be; लक्षणा शक्यसंबन्धस्तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः<BR> Bhāṣā P. 82 (तात्पर्य˚ being the failure of the meaning aimed<BR> at, or of any connected meaning).<BR>—2 Inapplicability, not being applicable.<BR>—3 Inconclusive reasoning; absence of reasonable grounds (युक्त्यभाव);<BR>—4 Penury, adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपन्न
अनुपपन्न <i>a.</i> Improper, impossible, inapplicable, impracticable,<BR> inconclusive, irrelevant. पीनो देवदत्तो दिवा न भुङ्क्ते इत्यत्र दिवाऽभोजिनः<BR> पीनत्वं रात्रिभोजनं विनानुपपन्नम् see अर्थापत्ति also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपादकाः
अनुपपादकाः ‘Having no material parent’. N. of a class of Buddhas,<BR> called Dhyānibuddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपम|अनुपमः
अनुपम <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Incomparable, matchless, peerless,<BR> best, most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपममतिः|अनुपममति
अनुपम + .{@-मतिः@} N. of a contemporary of Śākya muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमा
अनुपम + .{@-मा@} The female elephant of the south-west (mate of कुमुद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमेय
अनुपमेय, -मित <i>a.</i><BR> Matchless, incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमित
अनुपमेय, -मित <i>a.</i><BR> Matchless, incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमर्दनम्
अनुपमर्दनम् Non-refutation of a charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयुक्त
अनुपयुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not used (as food).<BR>—2 Unsuited, unfit, improper, useless, unserviceable; सत्क्रियाविशेषादनुपयुक्तमिवात्मानं<BR> समर्थये Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयोग|अनुपयोगः
अनुपयोग <i>a.</i> Useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयोगः|अनुपयोग
अनुपयोग + .{@-गः@} Uselessness, not being used (as food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपरत
अनुपरत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not dead.<BR>—2 Not stopped, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्ध
अनुपलब्ध <i>a.</i> Unobserved, unperceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्धि|अनुपलब्धिः
अनुपलब्धि <i>f.</i> Non-recognition, non-perception (प्रत्यक्षाद्यभाव);<BR> नास्ति घटोऽनुपलब्धेः (the knowledge of घटाभाव is possible because<BR> the प्रतियोगी or counter-entity is not found with the non-entity or<BR> अभाव, that is, there being no उपलब्धि or knowledge of the घट);<BR> one of the instruments of knowledge according to the Mīmāṃsakas, but<BR> not according to the Naiyāyikas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुपलब्धिसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्धिसमः|अनुपलब्धिसम
अनुपलब्धि + -समः a fallacy, trying to establish a fact (say, the eternity<BR> of sound) from the impossibility of seeing the non-perception of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलम्भः|अनुपलम्भ|अनुपलंभः
अनुपलम्भः Want of apprehension; non-perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपवीतिन्
अनुपवीतिन् <i>m.</i> One who does not wear the sacred thread (belonging to his caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपशयः|अनुपशय
अनुपशयः Any thing or circumstance that aggravates a malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपश्य
अनुपश्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Following with his looks, keeping in view.<BR>—2 One who sees; Pātañjala Yogadarśana 2. 21; P. III. 1. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसंहारिन्
अनुपसंहारिन् <i>m.</i> A kind of हेत्वाभास or fallacy in Nyāya,<BR> a subdivision of the अनैकान्तिकहेत्वाभास; वस्तुमात्रपक्षकोऽनुपसंहारी<BR> that is, that which includes every known thing in the पक्ष and thus<BR> prevents the corroboration of a general rule of causation by illustrations,<BR> positive or negative; as सर्वं नित्यं प्रमेयत्वात्; अत्र सर्वस्यैव<BR> पक्षत्वात् प्रमेयत्वं हेतुरनुपसंहारी अन्वये व्यतिरेके वा दृष्टान्ताभावात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसर्गः|अनुपसर्ग
अनुपसर्गः<BR>—1 A word (particle &c.) that is not, or has not the force of, an <i>Upasarga</i>.<BR>—2 That which has no Upasarga.<BR>—3 That which needs no additions (as a divine being).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसर्जन
अनुपसर्जन <i>a.</i> An independent word, i. e. a word which is not<BR> relegated to a subordinate position (by entering into a compound formation) P. IV. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसेचन
अनुपसेचन <i>a.</i> Having no उपसेचन i. e. some condiment,<BR> sauce, curds &c. to moisten food with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कृत
अनुपस्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unpolished (as silver).<BR>—2 Genuine, blameless.<BR>—3 Not cooked or dressed (as food).<BR>—4 Not requiring any evident object.<BR>—5 Without any doubt in mind; तस्मात्स्वधर्ममास्थाय सुव्रताः सत्यवादिनः ।<BR> लोकस्य गुरवो भूत्वा ते भवन्त्यनुपस्कृताः ॥ Mb. 12. 11. 25.<BR>—6 Selfless, without greed or motive; देहत्यागोऽनुपस्कृतः Ms. 10. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कार
अनुपस्कार <i>a.</i> Not elliptical (अध्याहारदोषरहित) Ki. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थानम्
अनुपस्थानम् Absence, not being at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापनम्
अनुपस्थापनम्^1 Not placing, offering or producing, not having ready or at hand.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापित
अनुपस्थापित <i>a.</i> Not ready or at hand, not offered or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थायिन्
अनुपस्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Not present, absent, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थित
अनुपस्थित <i>a.</i> Not present, absent, not at hand or near; not current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थितम्
अनुपस्थित + .{@-तम्@} A word that is not उपस्थित q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थितिः|अनुपस्थिति
अनुपस्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Absence; मम ˚तिं क्षमन्तां भवन्तः your honour will be pleased<BR> to excuse my absence.<BR>—2 Inability to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपहत
अनुपहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not injured, unimpaired, unvitiated.<BR>—2 Not used, unbleached, new (as cloth); ˚तं दुकूलयुगलम् K. 110, 229.<BR> See अनाहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपा
अनुपा €2 P.<BR>—1 To drink after (a person or thing), drink along with; (मधु पीत्वा) …<BR> अनुपास्यसि बाष्पदूषितं जलाञ्जलिम् R. 8. 68; कल्माषान्भक्षयन्मधु<BR> चानुपिबेत् Suśr.; (चूर्णं) लीढ्वानुपीत्वा च पयोऽग्निशक्त्या कामं<BR> निकामं पुरुषो निषेवेत् । Bṛ. S. 76. 6.<BR>—2 To follow in drinking.<BR>—3 (€2 P.) = अनुपाल् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानम्
अनुपानम्<BR>—1 A drink taken with or after medicine (अनु भेषजेन सह पश्चाद्वा<BR> यत् किञ्चिन्मधुक्षीरादि पीयते तत्); a fluid vehicle in medicine.<BR>—2 A drink close at hand. हन्तानुपानमित्युच्छिष्टं वै मे पीत्ँ स्यादिति<BR> होवाच Ch. Up. 1. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानीय
अनुपानीय <i>a.</i> Serving as a liquid vehicle of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानीयम्
अनुपानीय + .{@-यम्@} An after-drink, what is fit to be drunk after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपा
अनुपा €2 P., -पाल् €10 P.<BR>—1 To guard, watch over, protect, defend; बालदायादिकं रिक्थं तावद्राजानुपालयेत्<BR> Ms. 8. 27 keep in custody.<BR>—2 To conform to, obey, observe; दशरथवचनमनुपालयन् K. 21;<BR> सत्येऽनुपालयेत्सत्यम् H. 4. 23; so प्रतिज्ञाम्, धर्मम्, मार्गम् &c.;<BR> keep, preserve; अनुपालयतां प्रभुशक्तिम् Ki. 2. 10 watching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाल्
अनुपा €2 P., -पाल् €10 P.<BR>—1 To guard, watch over, protect, defend; बालदायादिकं रिक्थं तावद्राजानुपालयेत्<BR> Ms. 8. 27 keep in custody.<BR>—2 To conform to, obey, observe; दशरथवचनमनुपालयन् K. 21;<BR> सत्येऽनुपालयेत्सत्यम् H. 4. 23; so प्रतिज्ञाम्, धर्मम्, मार्गम् &c.;<BR> keep, preserve; अनुपालयतां प्रभुशक्तिम् Ki. 2. 10 watching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपालनम्
अनुपालनम् Preserving, keeping up, obeying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाकृत
अनुपाकृत <i>a.</i> Not rendered fit for or consecrated for sacrificial purposes.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुपाकृतमांसम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाकृतमांसम्
अनुपाकृत + -मांसम् flesh of an animal not prepared for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाख्य
अनुपाख्य <i>a.</i> What is not directly perceived, hence something which<BR> is only inferable (= अनुमेय Kāśi.); P. VI. 3. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपात|अनुपातः
अनुपात, -तिन्<BR> see under अनुपत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातिन्
अनुपात, -तिन्<BR> see under अनुपत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातम्
अनुपातम् <i>ind.</i> In regular succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातकम्
अनुपातकम् [पातकं ब्रह्महत्यादि तत्सदृशम्] A heinous crime<BR> such as theft, murder, adultery &c. 35 such sins are enumerated in Viṣṇusmṛti;<BR> Manu mentions 30 kinds; see 11. 54-58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपात्ययः|अनुपात्यय
अनुपात्ययः<BR>—1 Not to violate a turn or succession.<BR>—2 To do something by turn.<BR>—3 Turn, succession. कमप्राप्तस्यानतिपातोऽनुपात्ययः, परिपाटी ।<BR> Kāśi. on. P. III. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानत्क
अनुपानत्क <i>a.</i> Shoeless; Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपालः|अनुपाल
अनुपालः A keeper (of horses &c.). कुशलैस्तरुणैर्दक्षैरनुपालैः ।<BR> शालिहोत्र of भोज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपालुः|अनुपालु
अनुपालुः [वनस्पतिवि˚] Erum Indicum. (Mar. रान आळू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपार्श्व
अनुपार्श्व <i>a.</i> Lateral, along or by the side. ━(pl.) N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपावृत्त
अनुपावृत्त <i>a.</i> Ved. Western. ━(pl.) N. of a people; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुरुषः|अनुपुरुष
अनुपुरुषः [अनुगतः अन्यं पुरुषम्] A follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुष्पः|अनुपुष्प
अनुपुष्पः [अनुगतः पुष्पं तद्विकारम्] A kind of reed (शरवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व|अनुपूर्वं|अनुपूर्व्व
अनुपूर्व <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः पूर्वं परिपाटीं क्रमं वा]<BR>—1 Regular, having a suitable measure, regularly shaped, symmetrical;<BR> वृत्तानुपूर्वे च न चातिदीर्घे Ku. 1. 35; ततोनुपूर्वायतवृत्तबाहुः<BR> Ki. 17. 50 (गोपुच्छाकार Malli.); जङ्घे अनुपूर्ववृत्ते Dk. 131;<BR> ˚ताम्राङ्गुली वाहुलते <i>ibid.</i>; ˚केश who has regular hair; ˚गात्र<BR> having regularly shaped limbs; so ˚दंष्ट्र, ˚नाभि, ˚पाणि.<BR>—2 Orderly, successive, in due order or succession; coming in order, following.<BR>—3 The lowest (निकृष्टप्रमाण); अनुपूर्वा इतरे Kāty.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुपूर्वज, अनुपूर्ववत्सा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्वज
अनुपूर्व + -ज <i>a.</i> descended in a regular line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्ववत्सा
अनुपूर्व + -वत्सा a cow that calves regularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्वशः
अनुपूर्वशः, -पूर्वेण <i>adv.</i><BR> In regular order, one by one, successively,<BR> from above, downwards; from the beginning or first; वर्णानामनुपूर्वशः<BR> Ms. 8. 142, 3. 39, 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्वेण
अनुपूर्वशः, -पूर्वेण <i>adv.</i><BR> In regular order, one by one, successively,<BR> from above, downwards; from the beginning or first; वर्णानामनुपूर्वशः<BR> Ms. 8. 142, 3. 39, 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

