अनुप्रवचनम्
अनुप्रवचनम् Repetition or reproduction of what has been said by<BR> the teacher;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवचनादि
अनुप्रवचनम् + ˚आदि a class of words given in P. V. 1. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवण
अनुप्रवण <i>a.</i> Agreeable, pleasant; प्रायश्चित्तकथा ह्येषा भक्ष्याभक्ष्यविवर्जिता ।<BR> कौतूहलानुप्रवणा हर्षं जनयतीव मे ॥ Mb. 12. 37. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवादः|अनुप्रवाद
अनुप्रवादः Rumour. Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रविश्
अनुप्रविश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To enter into, join; पथिकसार्थं विदिशागामिनमनुप्रविष्टः M. 5;<BR> (fig. also); विश्रम्य लौकिकाः संस्त्यायमनुप्रविशन्ति Mv. I enter<BR> into familiar talk or conversation.<BR>—2 To accommodate or adapt oneself to; यस्य यस्य हि यो भावस्तस्य<BR> तस्य हि तं नरः । अनुप्रविश्य मेधावी क्षिप्रमात्मवशं नयेत् Pt. 1. 68;<BR> सखे वामदेव त्वमपि गाधिनन्दनमनुप्रविष्टोऽसि A. R. 1 you<BR> too share in his opinion, or think with him.<BR>—3 To follow in entering; sleep with.<BR>—4 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवेश|अनुप्रवेशः
अनुप्रवेश<BR>—1 Entrance into; पुपोष वृद्धिं हरिदश्वदीधितेरनुप्रवेशादिव बालचन्द्रमाः<BR> R. 3. 22, 10. 51.<BR>—2 Adapting oneself to the will of; बलवताभिभूतस्य विदेशगमनं<BR> तदनुप्रवेशो वा नीतिः Pt. 1; भजते विदेशमधिकेन जितस्तदनुप्रवेशमथवा<BR> कुशलः Śi. 9. 48.<BR>—3 Imitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रश्नः|अनुप्रश्न
अनुप्रश्नः A subsequent question (having reference to what the teacher<BR> has previously said).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसक्तिः|अनुप्रसक्ति
अनुप्रसक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Very close attachment.<BR>—2 Very close logical connection (of words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसद्
अनुप्रसद् <i>Caus.</i> To propitiate, conciliate; रोहिणीमृगलाञ्छनं<BR> साक्षीकृत्य आर्यपुत्रमनुप्रसादयामि V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसादनम्
अनुप्रसादनम् Propitiation, conciliation; प्रिय ˚नं नाम व्रतम् V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रस्थ
अनुप्रस्थ <i>a.</i> Latitudinal, following the breadth or latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रहित
अनुप्रहित <i>a.</i> Fixed; प्रियैषिणानुप्रहिताः शिवेन Ki. 17. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राण्
अनुप्राण् €2 P. To breathe after. ━<i>Caus.</i> To animate, support,<BR> feed, help; mostly used in the statement of Alankāras in a sentence;<BR> उत्प्रेक्षानुप्राणिता स्वभावोक्तिः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राणनम्
अनुप्राणनम् Breathing after, animation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्
अनुप्राप् €5 P.<BR>—1 To get, obtain.<BR>—2 To reach, go to, overtake; गङ्गानदीमनुप्राप्ताः Mb.<BR>—3 To imitate; लीलाखेलमनुप्रापुर्महोक्षास्तस्य विकमम् R. 4. 22.<BR>—4 To arrive, come (intrans); कथमिमां भूमिमनुप्राप्तः K. 132; Ve. 6.<BR>—5 To get back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्त
अनुप्राप्त <i>p. p.</i> Reached, got, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्तिः|अनुप्राप्ति
अनुप्राप्तिः <i>f.</i> Getting to, reaching, arriving &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रासः|अनुप्रास
अनुप्रासः [अनुगतः रसाद्यनुगुणं प्रकृष्टमासं वर्णन्यासं समवर्णरचनां<BR> समवर्णोच्चारणं वा] Alliteration, repetition of similar letters, syllables<BR> or sounds; वर्णसाम्यमनुप्रासः K. P. 9; (स्वरवैसादृश्येऽपि व्यञ्जनसदृशत्वं<BR> वर्णसाम्यं रसाद्यनुगतः प्रकृष्टो न्यासः; अनुप्रासः शब्दसाम्यं वैषम्येऽपि<BR> स्वरस्य यत् S. D. 633.) अनुप्रास is of 5 kinds;<BR>——(<i>a</i>) छेक˚ or single alliteration; बकुलगन्धानन्धीकुर्वन्,<BR> कावेरीवारिपावनः पवनः; मूर्ध्नामुद्वृत्तकृत्ताविरलगरल &c. K. P. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) वृत्ति˚ or harmonious. उदा˚ उन्मीलन्मधुगन्धलुब्धमधुपव्याधूतचूताङ्कुरक्रीडत्कोकिलकाकलीकलकलैरुद्गीर्णकर्णज्वराः ।<BR> नीयन्ते पथिकैः कथंकथमपि ध्यानावधानक्षणप्राप्तप्राणसमासमागमरसोल्लासैरमी वासराः ॥<BR>——(<i>c</i>) श्रुति˚ or melodious. उदा˚ दृशा दग्धं मनसिजं जीवयन्ति<BR> दृशैव याः । विरूपाक्षस्य जयिनीस्ताः स्तुमो वामलोचनाः ॥<BR>——(<i>d</i>) अन्त्य˚ or final; as मन्दं हसन्तः पुलकं वहन्तः.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) लाट˚; स्मेरराजीवनयने नयने किं निमीलिते । पश्य निर्जितकन्दर्पे<BR> कन्दर्पवशगं प्रियम् ॥ For definitions and examples see S. D. 633-38<BR> and K. P. 9th Ullāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लु
अनुप्लु €1 Ā. To run after, follow; इदमन्यतो वानरद्वयम् आर्यस्य<BR> पार्ष्णिग्राहमिव संश्रयादनुप्लवते A. R. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लवः|अनुप्लव
अनुप्लवः A follower, servant; सानुप्लवः प्रभुरपि क्षणदाचराणाम्<BR> R. 13. 75; सानुप्लवाः क्वापि यातास्त्रिमूर्धखरदूषणाः । Mv. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध्|अनुबंध्
अनुबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind or fasten to, attach, tie, connect; सीमन्तं निजमनुबध्नती<BR> कराभ्याम् Śi. 8. 69 forming, arranging; उभयोरपि राजेन्द्र संबन्धेनानुबध्यतां<BR> (इक्ष्वाकुकुलम्) Rām.; सखीजनानुबद्धां कथाम् Dk. 114 connected with.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To have in the train (fig. also); न शिष्याननुबध्नीत Bhāg.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To bring about, cause, lead to, result in, produce as a consequence;<BR> नानुबध्नाति कुशलम् Mb.; हे वृषल ते तथा विक्षेपोऽस्तु यथा हिंसामनुबध्नाति<BR>—3 To press, importune, urge, request; पुनः पुनश्चानुबध्यमाना K. 69, 133, 207, 233.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To attend or follow closely, follow at the heels of, follow;<BR> को नु खल्वयमनुबध्यमानस्तपखिनीभ्यामबालसत्त्वो बालः Ś. 7; मधुकरकुलैरनुबध्यमानम्<BR> K. 139; दिष्ट्या तावदयमनङ्गो मामिव तमप्यनुबध्नाति K. 158, 194, 319, 347;<BR> Ki. 6. 8; Mv. 7. 18; Śi. 5. 26.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To chase, pursue; तच्चानुबध्यमानम् K. 120; अनुबध्नता<BR> तुरगमुखमिथुनम् 132.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To adhere or stick to, cling to; धन्या चित्रलेखा यामनुबध्नाति<BR> देवीप्रसादः K. 221.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To continue, take up; तदेवानुबध्यतां तपः 322; तान्येव<BR> चिरपरिचितान्यक्षराणि मामनुबध्नन्ति U. 3 v. l. for अनुरुन्धन्ति;<BR> वैशम्पायनागमनालापमेवानुबध्य K. 262.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) To follow, succeed, come close upon; सत्योऽयं जनप्रवादो<BR> यद्विपद्विपदं संपत्सं -पदमनुबध्नातीति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-2" target="_blank">Page0100-2</a>]<BR> K. 73; see अनुबन्धि below.<BR>—5 To foster, cherish, entertain, harbour; तेषु किं भवतः स्नेहमनुबध्नाति<BR> मानसम् Mārk. P.<BR>—6 To bear, endure; अन्येद्युश्चानुबध्नत्या राज्ञ्या राजा स यत्नतः Ks. 49. 47.<BR>—7 Not to burst or break loose, hold or keep together; भङ्गेऽपि हि मृणालानामनुबध्नन्ति<BR> तन्तवः H. 1. 91. ━<i>pass.</i> To be related to or connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबद्ध
अनुबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, attached, tied to.<BR>—2 Following in the train, coming as a consequence; अनुबद्धार्थानर्थसंशयान्<BR> विचार्य Dk. 41.<BR>—3 Connected with, related to, relating or belonging to.<BR>—4 Constantly sticking to, being in; continued, continuous; नित्यानुबद्धकुलवैरः<BR> Ve. 1; ˚मुग्धकाकलीहसितम् U. 3; ˚विजृम्भकम् K. 66; ˚बिन्दुभिरश्रुभिः 135<BR> constantly flowing.<BR>—5 Fixed upon, directed towards; कलहंस ˚वक्त्रायाः Dk. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धः|अनुबन्ध|अनुबंधः
अनुबन्धः<BR>—1 Binding or fastening on, connection, attachment, tie (lit. & fig.);<BR> यस्यां मनश्चक्षुषोरनुबन्धस्तस्यामृद्धिः Māl. 2; एतस्येदृशेन<BR> दर्शनेन कीदृशो मे हृदयानुबन्धः इति न जानासि U. 3 state of feeling; K. 257.<BR>—2 Uninterrupted succession, unbroken sequence, continuous flow, continuity;<BR> series, chain; बाष्पं कुरु स्थिरतया विरतानुबन्धम् Ś. 4. 15; मरण˚<BR> K. 236 following up death, desire for dying; अनुबन्धाद्विरमेद्वा K. 280;<BR> यदा नात्याक्षीदेवानुबन्धम् 309 (persistence in) following me, 317;<BR> वैर˚, मत्सर˚, Dk. 63, 161; मुच्यतां देवि शोकानुबन्धः K. 63<BR> continuous sorrow; दुर्लभजनप्रार्थना˚ Ratn. 1; विरम विरम<BR> वह्ने मुञ्च धूमानुबन्धम् 4. 16; सानुबन्धाः कथं न स्युः संपदो<BR> मे निरापदः R. 1. 64 continuous, uninterrupted; परिवृद्धरागमनुबन्धसेवया<BR> R. 9. 69 continuous enjoyment; अयं सोऽर्थोऽनर्थानुबन्धः संवृत्तः<BR> V. 5 giving rise to a chain of evils.<BR>—3 Descendants, posterity; सानुबन्धा हता ह्यसि Rām. relation, भूमेः<BR> सुतां भूमिभृतोऽनुबन्धात् Viś. Guṇā. 475.<BR>—4 Consequence, result (good or bad); आत्मदोषानुबन्धेन K. 319 in<BR> consequence of; यदग्रे चानुबन्धे च सुखम् Bg. 18. 39, 25; अनुबन्धमजानन्तः<BR> कर्मणामविचक्षणाः Rām. 3. 51. 26; नार्थानां प्रकृतिं वेत्सि नानुबन्धमवेक्षसे Mb. 4. 49. 1.<BR>—5 Intention; design, motive, cause; अनुबन्धानपेक्षेत सानुबन्धेषु<BR> कर्मसु Mb. 5. 34. 8. अनुबन्धं परिज्ञाय देशकालौ च तत्त्वतः । सारापराधौ<BR> चालोक्य दण्डं दण्डपेषु पातयेत् Ms. 8. 126; पाप˚ of evil designs.<BR>—6 An adjunct of a thing, a secondary member (मुख्यानुयायि, अप्रधानम्);<BR> (उल्का) दृश्यते सानुबन्धा च Rām. 5. 1. 63 a secondary symptom,<BR> symptomatic affection, attendant on the principal disease (वातपित्तादिदोषाणामप्राधान्यम्);<BR> मूर्छानुवन्धा विषमज्वराः Suśr.<BR>—7 Connecting link or adjunct of a subject or topic; theme, matter of<BR> discussion; introductory reasons; (विषयप्रयोजनाधिकारिसंबन्धः अनुबन्धः)<BR> (an indispensable element of the Vedānta).<BR>—8 (Gram.) An indicatory syllable or letter intended to denote some peculiarity<BR> in the inflection, accent &c. of the word to which it is attached; as<BR> the ऌ in गमॢ, ण् in इण्; रिपुराप पराभवाय मध्यं प्रकृतिप्रत्यययोरिवानुबन्धः Ki. 13. 19.<BR>—9 Offence, fault.<BR>—10 An obstacle, impediment; also the clog or encumbrance of a family;<BR> domestic ties or attachment.<BR>—11 A child or pupil who follows the example set by his parent or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">Page0101-1</a>]<BR> teacher (मुख्यानुयायी शिशुः).<BR>—12 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—13 Repeated application or devotion (पौनःपुन्येन अभिनिवेशः).<BR>—14 Course, pursuit.<BR>—15 A small bit or part, a trifle.<BR>—16 The junction of a fraction (with an integer), as भागानुबन्धपूर्णाङ्कः.<BR>—17 Base, stem (प्रकृति). cf. अनुबन्धः प्रकृत्यादौ दोषोत्पादे विनश्वरे ।<BR> मुख्यानुयायिनि शिशौ प्रकृतस्यानुवर्तने । अनुबन्धेऽपि हिक्कायां भ्रष्टायामपि<BR> कथ्यते । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धी
अनुबन्धः + .{@-धी@} [अनुबध्यते अतिश्वासेन व्याप्रियते अनया]<BR>—1 Thirst.<BR>—2 Hickup. अनुबन्धी तु हिक्कायां तृष्णायामपि योषिति Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धक|अनुबंधक
अनुबन्धक <i>a.</i> Connected, related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धनम्
अनुबन्धनम् Connection, succession, series &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धिका
अनुबन्धिका <i>f.</i> Pain in the joint; अनुबद्धमनुबन्धिकाभिः Hc. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धिन्|अनुबंधिन्
अनुबन्धिन् <i>a.</i> (oft. at the end of comp.)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Connected with, attached or related to; अहो सरसरमणीयानुबन्धिनी<BR> स्त्रीजनकथा Māl. 1 having for its contents or subject-matter &c.;<BR> परिचर्यानुबन्धी Dk. 101 continuing.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Mixed or blended with; नीलकण्ठकलकेकानुबन्धिना मन्द्रहुङ्कृतेन<BR> मामनुमन्यते Māl. 9.<BR>—2 Followed by, accompanied with; having in its train, resulting in having<BR> as a consequence; तदियमापत्समन्ततोऽनर्थानुबन्धिनी Dk. 60; अयमर्थोऽर्थानुबन्धी 67;<BR> शास्त्रं शास्त्रान्तरानुबन्धि 156; दुःखं दुःखानुबन्धि V. 4 one<BR> misfortune closely follows another, or misfortunes never come single;<BR> K. 349; महोदयैस्तस्य हितानुबन्धिभिः Ki. 1. 20; कर्मानुबन्धीनि<BR> मनुष्यलोके Bg. 15. 2; गुणा गुणानुबन्धित्वात्तस्य सप्रसवा इव R. 1. 22<BR> being associated with.<BR>—5 Lasting, thriving, prosperous, growing apace, continuous; uninterrupted;<BR> अपि त्वदावर्जितवारिसंभृतं प्रवालमासामनुबन्धि वीरुधाम् Ku. 5. 34;<BR> ऊर्ध्वं गतं यस्य न चानुबन्धि R. 6. 77 continuous uninterrupted<BR> or all pervading; K. 246, 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध्य|अनुबंध्य
अनुबन्ध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Principal, chief, primary (which may receive an adjunct, as a root,<BR> a disease &c.).<BR>—2 [वधार्थं बन्धः अनुबन्धः कर्मणि ण्यत्] To be killed (as a bull),<BR> one of the three principal sacrificial animals at the ज्योतिष्टोम sacrifice;<BR> गारनुबन्ध्यः K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबलम्
अनुबलम् [अनु पश्चात्स्थितं बलम्] A rearguard, an auxiliary army<BR> following another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबुध्
अनुबुध् €4 Ā. To awake, to recollect; learn, obtain information of,<BR> know, be aware of; न सत्यमनुबुध्यते K. 104 does not perceive or<BR> recognise. ━<i>Caus.</i> —1 To remind, put in mind of; अये सम्यगनुबोधितोऽस्मि Ś. 1<BR> well reminded.<BR>—2 To advise, inform; इति शिष्येण किलान्वबोधयत् R. 8. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधः|अनुबोध
अनुबोधः<BR>—1 An after-thought, recollection.<BR>—2 Reviving the scent of faded perfumes, replacing them when removed by bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधनम्
अनुबोधनम् Recollection, reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणम्
अनुब्राह्मणम्<BR>—1 A work resembling a Brāhmaṇa (ब्राह्मणसदृशो ग्रन्थः P. IV. 2. 62. Sk.).<BR>—2 <i>ind.</i> According to the Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणिन्
अनुब्राह्मणिन्, -क <i>a.</i><BR> [तदधीते वेद वा इति इनिप्रत्ययः] One who learns<BR> or knows an अनुब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणिक
अनुब्राह्मणिन्, -क <i>a.</i><BR> [तदधीते वेद वा इति इनिप्रत्ययः] One who learns<BR> or knows an अनुब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभव|अनुभवः
अनुभव, -भाव &c.<BR> See under अनुभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाव|अनुभावः
अनुभव, -भाव &c.<BR> See under अनुभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाजित
अनुभाजित <i>a.</i> Worshipped नानुबध्येत तद्वाक्यैर्विभ्रमैश्चानुभाजितः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 47. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाषणम्
अनुभाषणम्<BR>—1 Repetition of an assertion to refute it.<BR>—2 Repeating what has been said.<BR>—3 Conversation, dialogue (अनु सह भाषणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाषितृ
अनुभाषितृ <i>a.</i> Speaking in reply; श्लाघ्यो भवान्स्वजन इत्यनुभाषितारम्<BR> (क्षितीशम्) R. 16. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभासः|अनुभास
अनुभासः A kind of crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभुज्
अनुभुज् €7 Ā. To enjoy, experience (good or bad things), suffer (as<BR> the due consequences of oneʼs deeds); मेघमुक्तविशदां स चन्द्रिकाम्<BR> अन्वभुङ्क्त R. 19. 39; सा मण्डनान्मण्डनमन्वभुङ्क्त Ku. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभोगः|अनुभोग
अनुभोगः<BR>—1 Enjoyment.<BR>—2 A grant of a land in perpetuity for service done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभू
अनुभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To enjoy; taste, experience, feel, have experience or knowledge of,<BR> notice, perceive (by the senses &c.); to suffer, bear, undergo (as misery<BR> &c.); अन्वभवं च मधुकर इव नवमालिकामार्द्रसुमनसम् Dk. 121;<BR> असक्तः सुखमन्बभूत् R. 1. 21; भुवनालोकनप्रीतिः स्वर्गिभिर्नानुभूयते<BR> Ku. 2. 45; R. 7. 28; आत्मकृतानां हि दोषाणामनुभवितव्यं फलमात्मनैव<BR> K. 121; अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णम् Ś. 5. 7; Ku. 4. 41;<BR> संवत्सरमात्रं प्रेष्यभावमनुभूय M. 5 undergoing the state of a<BR> servant; षष्ठमनुभवन् वर्षम् K. 77 being in the sixth year, six years old.<BR>—2 To learn, hear, understand; वेदान्नानुभवसि Ch. Up.<BR>—3 To try, test, put to the test; न त्वं तेनान्वभाविष्ठा नान्वभावि त्वयाप्यसौ ।<BR> अनुभूता मया चासौ तेन चान्वभविष्यहम् ॥ Bk. 5. 35.<BR>—4 To comprise, include, grasp; द्वे वामलके अनुभवति Ch. Up.<BR>—5 To come up with, arrive at, get, obtain (mostly Ved. in these senses).<BR>—6 To turn or incline to; यत् त्वा भवतो रोदसी अनु Rv. 10. 147. 1.<BR>—7 To act favourably; य एवैतमनुभवति यो वै तमनुभार्यान् बुभूर्षति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 18. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to enjoy, feel, or experience; अनुभावयितुं मन्ये यत्नः<BR> संप्रति मां विधेः Mu. 6. 15; स्नानभोजनादिकमनुभावितोऽस्मि Dk. 125;<BR> आमोदो न हि कस्तूर्याः शपथेनानुभाव्यते Bv. 1. 120.<BR>—2 To reflect on, meditate, think of; मनसा तमेव वृत्तान्तमन्वभावयत् K. 176, 279.<BR>—3 To infer, know; तस्मात्परोक्षवृत्तीनां फलैः कर्मानुभाव्यते H. 4. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभवः|अनुभव
अनुभवः<BR>—1 Direct perception or cognition, knowledge derived from personal observation<BR> or experiment, notion, apprehension, the impression on the mind not derived<BR> from memory, one of the kinds of knowledge; सर्वव्यवहारहेतुर्ज्ञानं<BR> बुद्धिः । सा द्विविधा स्सृतिरनुभवश्च । संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं स्मृतिः ।<BR> तद्भिन्नं ज्ञानमनुभवः which again is यथार्थ right & अयथार्थ<BR> wrong. See T. S. 34. (The Naiyāyikas recognize प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान,<BR> उपमान and शाब्द as the four sources of knowledge; the Vedāntins<BR> and Mīmāṃsakas<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">Page0102-1</a>]<BR> add two more अर्थापत्ति and अनुपलब्धि; the Vaiśeṣikas and Bauddhas<BR> admit the first two only, the Sāṅkhyas exclude उपमान, while the<BR> Cārvākas admit प्रत्यक्ष only. Other sections of philosophical<BR> schools add three more to the six sources of knowledge recognised by the<BR> Mīmāṃsakas:− संभव ‘equivalence’; ऐतिह्य ‘fallible testimony’,<BR> and चेष्टा ‘gesture’.)<BR>—2 Experience; अनुभवं वचसा सखि लुम्पसि N. 4. 105.<BR>—3 Understanding.<BR>—4 Result, consequence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुभवसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभवसिद्ध
अनुभवः + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> established by experience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावः|अनुभाव
अनुभावः<BR>—1 Dignity, consequence or dignity of person, majestic lustre, splendour,<BR> might, power, authority. (परिमेयपुरःसरौ) अनुभावविशेषात्तु सेनापरिवृताविव<BR> R. 1. 37; संभावनीयानुभावा अस्याकृतिः Ś. 7; अनुभावसौभाग्यमात्रपरिशेषधूसरश्रीः<BR> U. 1, 3, 6. 20, 41, 4. 22; K. 108, 240; V. 1; तवानुभावोऽयमवेदि यन्मया<BR> Ki. 1. 6; Dk. 29, 113; दिव्यौषध्या जयति महिमा कोऽप्यचिन्त्यानुभावः<BR> Mv. 6. 53; अहो महानुभावः पार्थिवो दुष्यन्तः Ś. 3 of great might<BR> or power; जाने वो रक्षसाकान्तावनुभावपराक्रमौ R. 10. 38, 2. 75 greatness<BR> (dignity) &c., valour; न निहन्ति धैर्यमनुभावगुणः Ki. 6. 28; महानुभावप्रकृतिः<BR> कापि तत एवागतवती Māl. 1 very noble or dignified.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) An external manifestation or indication of a feeling (भाव)<BR> by appropriate symptoms, such as by look, gesture &c., called by some<BR> <i>ensuant</i> (भावबोधक-न); भावं मनोगतं साक्षात् स्वगतं व्यञ्जयन्ति<BR> ये । तेऽनुभावा इति ख्याताः; यथा भ्रूभङ्गः कोपस्य व्यञ्जकः; उद्बुद्धं<BR> कारणं स्वैः स्वैर्बहिर्भावं प्रकाशयन् । लोके यः कार्यरूपः सोऽनुभावः<BR> काव्यनाट्ययोः ॥ S. D. 162, 163 &c.; धिगेव रमणीयतां त्वदनुभावभावादृते Māl. 9. 35.<BR>—3 Firm opinion or resolution, determination, belief; अनुभावांश्च जानासि<BR> ब्राह्मणानां न संशयः Mb. 3. 24. 8. अनुभाववता गुरुस्थिरत्वात्<BR> Ki. 13. 15. cf. अनुभावः प्रभावे च सतां च मतिनिश्चये Ak. also Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावक
अनुभावक <i>a.</i> Causing to understand, making one apprehend, indicative;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावकता
अनुभावक + ˚ता understanding, knowledge; यत्पदेन विना यस्याननुभावकता भवेत्<BR> Bhāṣā P. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावनम्
अनुभावनम् Indication of feelings by signs, gestures &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावित
अनुभावित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Experienced; एकभक्त्यानुभाविते Bhāg. 3. 24. 43.<BR>—2 greatly empowered; मह्यमाख्याह्यनुभाविताः Bhāg. 11. 16. 5.<BR>—3 protected; वयं च सर्वे भवतानुभाविता; Bhāg. 10. 63. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाविन्
अनुभाविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Perceiving, knowing, showing signs of feeling.<BR>—2 An eye-witness; अनुभावी तु यः कश्चित्कुर्यात्साक्ष्यं विवादिनाम् Ms. 8. 69.<BR>—3 Being or coming after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभू
अनुभू <i>a.</i> [भू-क्विप्] Perceiving, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूः
अनुभू + .{@-भूः@} <i>f.</i> Experience, direct knowledge or perception; अयमात्मा<BR> सर्वानुभूः Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूतिः|अनुभूति
अनुभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Perception, apprehension, experience.<BR>—2 (In Nyāya) knowledge derived from four sources: namely direct perception,<BR> inference, comparison, and verbal knowledge; see Bhāṣā P. 51, 52.<BR>—3 Dignity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">Page0102-2</a>]<BR> consequence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुभूतिप्रकाशः, अनुभूतिस्वरूपाचार्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूतिप्रकाशः|अनुभूतिप्रकाश
अनुभूतिः + -प्रकाशः N. of the metrical gloss or paraphrase of the principal<BR> Upanisads by Mādhavācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूतिस्वरूपाचार्यः|अनुभूतिस्वरूपाचार्य
अनुभूतिः + -स्वरूपाचार्यः N. of the author of the grammar Sārasvata-prakriyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभृ
अनुभृ €1. €3. P.<BR>—1 To praise conformably; to throw or commit into.<BR>—2 To insert, enter; आ अनुभृतमनर्वा Rv. 10. 61. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभर्तृ
अनुभर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Praising conformably, imitating.<BR>—2 Supporting, strengthening.<BR>—3 Penetrating, एषा स्या वो मरुतोऽनुभर्त्री प्रति ष्टोभति वाघतो न वाणी Rv. 1. 88. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभ्रातृ
अनुभ्रातृ <i>m.</i> A younger brother (अनुगतो भ्रातरम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमद्
अनुमद् €1 P. Ved. To rejoice over, gladden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत्त
अनुमत्त <i>p. p.</i> Intoxicated with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमाद्य
अनुमाद्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be praised in succession, to be granted with praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्
अनुमन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To agree or consent to, comply with, approve, sanction, grant; to permit,<BR> allow; किं महार्हशयनोपेते न वासमनुमन्यसे Rām. 5. 24. 2. तत्र<BR> नाहमनुमन्तुमुत्सहे मोघवृत्ति कलभस्य चेष्टितम् R. 11. 39; राजन्यान्<BR> स्वपुरनिवृत्तयेऽनुमेने R. 4. 87; कैलासनाथोद्वहनाय पुष्पकमन्वमंस्त 14. 20;<BR> शुश्रूषमाणां गिरिशोनुमेने Ku. 1. 59, 5. 68; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR> सुताम् Ś. 5. 20; इमां स्वसारं च यवीयसीं मे कुमुद्वतीं नार्हसि<BR> नानुमन्तुम् R. 16. 85 be pleased not to reject or refuse; अविनयमनुमन्तुं<BR> नोत्सहे दुर्जनानाम् Bh. 3. 22.<BR>—2 To follow, have recourse to; धर्मार्थावभिसन्त्यज्य संरभं योनुमन्यते Mb.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To ask for leave or permission; ask the consent of; अनुमान्यतां महाराजः<BR> V. 2 ask for leave to go; take counsel with; भूयोऽपि सखीजनमनुमानयिष्यामि Ś. 3.<BR>—2 To ask for, request or beg; अन्नमादाय तृप्ताः स्थ शेषं चैवानुमान्य<BR> च (विकिरंत्) Y. 1. 241.<BR>—3 To honour.<BR>—4 To put to account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत|अनुमतः
अनुमत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Approved, assented to, agreed to, permitted, allowed, granted &c. द्वारे<BR> नियुक्तपुरुषानुमतप्रवेशः M. 1. 12. भ्रूक्षेपमात्रानुमतप्रवेशाम्<BR> Ku. 3. 60. कृतमनुमतं दृष्ठं वा यैरिदं गुरुपातकम् Ve. 3. 24;<BR> ˚गमना Ś. 4. 10 allowed to depart; अनुमतो गृहाय R. 5. 10; उभय˚तः<BR> साक्षी Y. 2. 72 admitted by both parties &c.<BR>—2 Liked, beloved, pleasant, loved, agreeable, desired by, dear to; वृष्टिं<BR> च कर्षकजनानुमतां करोति Bṛ. S. 5. 72.<BR>—3 Being of one opinion, agreeing or concurring with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमतः|अनुमत
अनुमत + .{@-तः@} A lover; घनमतो नमतोनुमतान् प्रियाः Śi. 6. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमतम्
अनुमत + .{@-तम्@} Consent, approval, permission; प्रथमं कस्यानुमते चोरितमेतत्त्वया<BR> हृदयम् V. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमतिः|अनुमति
अनुमतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Permission, consent, approval, assent.<BR>—2 The 15th day of the moonʼs age on which she rises one digit less than<BR> full, when the gods and manes receive oblations with favour; personified<BR> as a goddess or worshipped in the Rājasūya sacrifice (कलाहीनचन्द्रवती<BR> शुक्लचतुर्दशीयुतपूर्णिमातिथिः); अनुमत्यै हविरष्टाकपालं पुरोडाशं<BR> निर्वपति Śat. Br.; Ms. 3. 86-87.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुमतिपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमतिपत्रम्
अनुमतिः + -पत्रम् a deed expressing assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमननम्
अनुमननम्<BR>—1 Assent; sufferance.<BR>—2 Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्तृ|अनुमंतृ
अनुमन्तृ <i>a.</i> Consenting to, permitting, allowing, suffering (opp.<BR> to active agent); उपद्रष्टाऽनुमन्ता च भर्ता भोक्ता महेश्वरः Bg. 13. 22;<BR> Ms. 5. 51 adviser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्त्र्|अनुमंत्र्
अनुमन्त्र् €10 Ā. To consecrate or accompany with sacred hymns or magical<BR> formulas; to dismiss with sacred and auspicious words, dismiss with a<BR> blessing; विसृष्टश्च वामदेवानुमन्त्रितोऽश्वः U. 2. (v. l. for अभिमन्त्रित);<BR> रथमारोप्य कृष्णेन यत्र कर्णोऽनुमन्त्रितः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्त्रः|अनुमन्त्र
अनुमन्त्रः A favourable speech; रहोनुमन्त्रैरपकृष्टचेतनः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 27. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्त्रणम्
अनुमन्त्रणम् Consecration by hymns and prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्त्रित
अनुमन्त्रित <i>a.</i> Consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरणम्
अनुमरणम् See under अनुमृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरुः|अनुमरु
अनुमरुः A country next to a desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा €3 Ā., €2 P.<BR>—1 To infer, (as from some signs, premises &c.); अलिङ्गां प्रकृतिं त्वाहुलिंङ्गैरनुमिमीमहे<BR> Mb.; conclude, guess, conjecture; धूमादग्निमनुमाय T. S. 41; पर्याकुलत्वान्मरुतां<BR> वेगभङ्गोऽनुमीयते Ku. 2. 25; अन्वमीयत शुद्धेति शान्तेन वपुषैव<BR> सा R. 15. 77, 17. 11; तेजोविशेषानुमितां दधानः 2. 7, 68, 5. 12;<BR> इह मदस्नपितैरनुमीयते सुरगणस्य गतं हरिचन्दनैः Ki. 5. 47.<BR>—2 To reconcile, equal. ━<i>Caus.</i> (-मापयति) To lead one to<BR> infer or guess, bespeak, indicate; आकृतिरेवानुमापयत्यमानुषताम् K. 132, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा [मा-अङ्] Inference, conclusion from given premises; see अनुमिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमातृ
अनुमातृ <i>a.</i> One who infers; न हि करिणि दृष्टे चीत्कारेण तमनुमिमतेऽनुमातारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमात्रा
अनुमात्रा Determination, resolution; तत्रेयमनुमात्रा मे भीमसेन<BR> विवक्षिता । नैकान्तसिद्धिर्वक्तव्या शत्रुभिः सह संयुगे ॥ Mb. 5. 77. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमानम्
अनुमानम्<BR>—1 Inferring as the instrument of an अनुमिति, conclusion; from given<BR> premises; an inference, conclusion, one of the four means of obtaining<BR> knowledge according to the Nyāya system; (अनुमितिकरणमनुमानं तच्च<BR> धूमो वह्निव्याप्य इति व्याप्तिज्ञानम्. It is of two kinds स्वार्थानुमानम्<BR> & परार्थानुमानम्); प्रत्यक्षं चानुमानं च शास्त्रं च विविधागमम् ।<BR> त्रयं सुविदितं कार्यं धर्मशुद्धिमभीप्सता ॥ Ms. 12. 105.<BR>—2 A guess, conjecture, sign to know; इङ्गितैरनुमानैश्च मया ज्ञेया भविष्यति Rām.<BR>—3 Analogy, similarity; आत्मनो हृदयानुमानेन प्रेक्षसे Ś. 5 you judge<BR> (of others) by the analogy of your own heart; स्वानुमानात्कादम्बरीमुत्प्रेक्ष्य K. 305.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.) A figure which consists in a notion, expressed in a peculiarly<BR> striking manner, of a thing established by proof; S. D. 711; यत्र पतत्यबलानां<BR> दृष्टिर्निशिंताः पतन्ति तत्र शराः । तच्चापरोपितशरो धावत्यासां पुरः<BR> स्मरो मन्ये ॥ अनुमानं तदुक्तं यत्साध्यसाधनयोर्वचः K. P. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुमानोक्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमानोक्ति|अनुमानोक्तिः
अनुमानम् + -उक्ति <i>f.</i> reasoning; logical inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमापक
अनुमापक <i>a.</i> (-पिका <i>f.</i>) Causing an inference as an<BR> effect, being the ground of an inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमितिः|अनुमिति
अनुमितिः <i>f.</i> Inference from given premises; the knowledge obtained<BR> by means of अनुमान; लिङ्गपरामर्शजन्यं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">Page0103-2</a>]<BR> ज्ञानमनुमितिः the knowledge that arises from deduction or syllogistic reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमित्सा
अनुमित्सा Desire of inferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमेय
अनुमेय <i>pot. p.</i> Inferable, to be inferred; फलानुमेयाः प्रारम्भाः R. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमार्गम्
अनुमार्गम् <i>adv.</i> Along the way, according to a (particular) way,<BR> on or in the way; अनुमार्गागतया K. 100 come by this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमाषम्
अनुमाषम् <i>adv.</i> Like a kidney bean or in a kidney bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमासः|अनुमास|अनुमासं
अनुमासः [अनुगतो मासः] The following month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमासम्
अनुमासः + .{@-सम्@} <i>ind.</i> Every month, month after month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमुद्
अनुमुद् €1 Ā. (P. in epic poetry)<BR>—1 To rejoice with, join in rejoicing or sympathizing with; मुदितामनुमोदते Bhāg.<BR>—2 To express approval; तदेव राममातृभिरनुमोदितम् U. 2; approve,<BR> second, applaud; निषेद्धुमासीदनुमोदितुं वा R. 14. 43; to allow with<BR> pleasure, permit; अनुमोदितमाचार्यैः K. 77; अननुमोदिता मात्रा 160.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To gladden, delight, favour, permit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदः|अनुमोद
अनुमोदः<BR>—1 The feeling of pleasure arising from sympathy, subsequent pleasure.<BR>—2 = अनुमोदनम् see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदनम्
अनुमोदनम्<BR>—1 Approval, assent, seconding, acceptance, compliance.<BR>—2 Causing pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमृ
अनुमृ €6 Ā. To follow in death; रुदता कुत एव सा पुनर्भवता नानुमृतापि<BR> लभ्यते R. 8. 85 followed in death by you; गतिविभ्रमसादनीरवा न<BR> शुचा नानुमृतेव लक्ष्यते 58 (used actively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरणम्
अनुमरणम् Following in death; तन्मरणे चानुमरणं करिष्यामीति<BR> मे निश्चयः H. 3; post-cremation of a widow (अनुमरणं हि भर्तुर्देशान्तरादिमरणे<BR> देहाद्यलाभ एव); देशान्तरमृते पत्यौ साध्वी तत्पादुकाद्वयम् । निधायोरसि<BR> संशुद्धा प्रविशेज्जातवेदसम् ॥ This is allowed to Kṣatriya, Vaiśya<BR> and other women, but not to Brāhmaṇa women; पृथक् चितां समारुह्य<BR> न विप्रा गन्तुमर्हति. Bāṇa severely condemns this practice; see K. 173-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयवम्
अनुयवम् <i>adv.</i> In the grains of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुया
अनुया €2 P.<BR>—1 To follow, go after (fig. also); अनुयाहि साधुपदवीम् Bh. 2. 77;<BR> अनुयास्यन्मुनितनयाम् Ś. 1. 28; त्वामनुयामि यद्यपि Ku. 4. 21.<BR>—2 To imitate, equal; न किलानुययुस्तस्य राजानो रक्षितुर्यशः R. 1. 27, 9. 6;<BR> अनुयातलीलः 16. 71; गुणैर्नृपाः शार्ङ्गिणमन्वयासिषुः<BR> Śi. 12. 3 followed and imitated.<BR>—3 To attend, accompany; इयं मुसलमनुयाति कलेन हुङ्कृतेन Mu. 1. 4;<BR> अनुयातारुन्धतीको वसिष्ठः U. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुया
अनुया <i>a.</i> Following; अनुया रात्र्या रात्रीं जिन्व Vāj. 15. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयाः
अनुया + .{@-याः@} Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयातृ
अनुयातृ <i>m.</i> A follower, companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रम्
अनुयात्रम्, -त्रा<BR> Retinue, train; attendance upon; following; त्यक्तभोगस्य<BR> मे राजन् वने वन्येन जीवतः । किं कार्यमनुयात्रेण Rām. सखिभिश्चित्रकथैः<BR> कृतानुयात्रः । Bu. C. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रा
अनुयात्रम्, -त्रा<BR> Retinue, train; attendance upon; following; त्यक्तभोगस्य<BR> मे राजन् वने वन्येन जीवतः । किं कार्यमनुयात्रेण Rām. सखिभिश्चित्रकथैः<BR> कृतानुयात्रः । Bu. C. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रम्
अनुयात्रम्, -त्रा + .{@-त्रम्@} <i>adv.</i> In or after a procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रिकः|अनुयात्रिक
अनुयात्रिकः [अनुयात्रा अनुगमनमस्त्यस्य ठन्] A follower, attendant;<BR> यावदनुयात्रिकान्समेत्य निवेशयेयम् Ś. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयानम्
अनुयानम् Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायिन्
अनुयायिन् <i>a.</i> [P. III. 2. 78]<BR>—1 Following; attending, consequent. तत् त्रिकालहितं वाक्यं धर्म्यमर्थानुयायि<BR> च Rām. 5. 51. 21. वसिष्ठधेनोरनुयायिनं तमावर्तमानं वनिता वनान्तात् R. 2. 19.<BR>—2 Like, similar.<BR>—3 Following a principal person as a teacher (मुख्यस्य अनुगन्ता शिशुः)<BR>━<i>m.</i> A follower (lit. & fig.); रामानुजानुयायिनः followers of the<BR> doctrines of R.; a dependent or attendant; न्यषेधि शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः R. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयाजः|अनुयाज
अनुयाजः [यज्-घञ्, कुत्वाभावः P. VII. 3. 62] A part of a sacrificial<BR> ceremony (यज्ञाङ्गम्); secondary or supplementary sacrificial rite;<BR> usually written अनूयाज q. v.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुयाजप्रसवः, अनुयाजप्रैषाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयाजप्रसवः|अनुयाजप्रसव
अनुयाजः + -प्रसवः permission to perform an Anuyāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयाजप्रैषाः
अनुयाजः + -प्रैषाः the formulae belonging to the Anuyāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुज्
अनुयुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To ask, question; किं वस्तु विद्वन्गुरवे प्रदेयं त्वया कियद्वेति<BR> तमन्वयुङ्क्त R. 5. 18; अन्वयुङ्क्त गुरुमीश्वरः क्षितेः 11. 62; स्वजनस्य<BR> वार्तमयमन्वयुङ्क्त च Śi. 13. 68.<BR>—2 To examine (as an accused), put on trial; प्राड्विवाकोऽनुयुञ्जीत विधिनानेन<BR> सान्त्वयन् Ms. 8. 79, 259.<BR>—3 To impart or give, as instruction.<BR>—4 To order, enjoin.<BR>—5 To select as husband.<BR>—6 To request, beg; धार्तराष्ट्रं सहामात्यं स्वयं समनुयुङ्क्ष्महे Mb. 5. 72. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्त|अनुयुक्तः
अनुयुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Asked, questioned, examined, ordered &c.<BR>—2 Censured, reproached.<BR>—3 Learning from a hired teacher (भृतकाध्येता). See अनुयोक्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्तिन्
अनुयुक्तिन् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे इनि] One who has ordered, examined;<BR> cf. गृहीतिन्, अधीतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुगम्
अनुयुगम् <i>ind.</i> According to the Yuga; फलन्त्यनुयुगं लोके प्रभावश्च<BR> शरीरिणाम् Ms. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुञ्जक
अनुयुञ्जक <i>a.</i> Jealous यथैषां वक्तुमिच्छन्ति नैर्गुण्यमनुयुञ्जकाः<BR> Mb. 12. 299. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोक्तृ
अनुयोक्तृ <i>m.</i> An examiner, interrogator; inquirer; a teacher, especially<BR> hired or mercenary (भृतकाध्यापक). अनुयोक्ता च यो विप्रो अनुयुक्तश्च<BR> भारत Mb. 13. 23. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगः|अनुयोग
अनुयोगः<BR>—1 A question, inquiry, examination; याऽस्मि साऽस्म्यनुयोगो मे न कर्तव्यः<BR> कथञ्चन Mb. 13. 93. 82. अनियन्त्रणानुयोगस्तपस्विजनः Ś. 1;<BR> निगृह्यानुयोगे P. VIII. 2. 94; वार्ता˚ मधुराक्षरया च वाचा R. 13. 71.<BR>—2 Censure, reproof, punishment; नानुयोगा ब्राह्मणानां भवन्ति Mb. 3. 192. 56.<BR>—3 Solicitation.<BR>—4 Exertion, effort; अनुयोगं विना तैलं तिलानां नोपजायते Pt. 2. 140.<BR>—5 Religious meditation; spiritual union.<BR>—6 Comment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुयोगकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगकृत्
अनुयोगः + -कृत्<BR>—1 an interrogator.<BR>—2 a teacher, spiritual preceptor (अनुयोगं कृन्तति प्रश्नविषयसंशयं छिनत्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगिन्
अनुयोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 What combines or unites; connected with, situated in or on.<BR>—2 Examining, questioning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोज्य|अनुयोज्यं|अनुयोज्यः
अनुयोज्य <i>pot. p.</i> Fit to be questioned, asked; asked with a reproof.<BR> ममेदमिति यो ब्रूयात्सोऽनुयोज्यो यथाविधि Ms. 8. 31.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">Page0104-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोज्यः|अनुयोज्य|अनुयोज्यं
अनुयोज्य + .{@-ज्यः@} A servant; obedient and humble servant; उभाभ्यामपि वासवानुयोज्यो<BR> दुष्यन्तः प्रणमति Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोजनम्
अनुयोजनम् A question, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्ज्|अनुरंज्
अनुरञ्ज् €4 U.<BR>—1 To be red; भृशमन्वरज्यदतुषारकरः Śi. 9. 7. (became red or attached).<BR>—2 To be delighted, find pleasure; तव प्रकीर्त्या जगत्प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते<BR> च Bg. 11. 36.<BR>—3 To be attached or devoted to, be fond of, love, like (with acc. or<BR> loc.); समस्थमनुरज्यन्ति विषमस्थं त्यजन्ति च Rām.; अशुद्धप्रकृतौ<BR> राज्ञि जनता नानुरज्यते Pt. 1. 301; भ्रातुर्मृतस्य भार्यायां योऽनुरज्येत<BR> कामतः Ms. 3. 173.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To make red, redden, dye, colour; सरसकिसलयानुरञ्जितैर्वा Śi. 7. 64, 8. 17, 12. 68;<BR> Dk. 168; Ki. 4. 27, 12. 23.<BR>—2 To attach oneself to, please, gratify, conciliate, keep contented or<BR> satisfied; अनुरक्तः प्रजाभिश्च प्रजाश्चाप्यन्वरञ्जयत् Rām.; कष्टं<BR> जनः कुलधनैरनुरञ्जनीयः U. 1. 14; शिष्यगुणानुरञ्जितमनसम<BR> Pt. 1 pleased, gratified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्त|अनुरक्तः
अनुरक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Reddened, dyed, coloured; सन्ध्यानुरक्ते जलदे दीप्ता विद्युदिवोज्ज्वला<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 88. कुण्डलमणिप्रभानुरक्तगण्डस्थलः K. 170.<BR>—2 Pleased, contented; loved, beloved; loyal, loyally devoted; अनुरक्तः<BR> शुचिर्दक्षः Ms. 7. 64; गुणानुरक्तामनुरक्तसाधनः Ki. 1. 31 having<BR> all means favourable to him;<BR>—3 Glowing; तापानुरक्तमधुना कमलं ध्रुवमीहते जेतुम् । Nāg. 3. 10.<BR> ˚प्रजः, -लोकः beloved by people; attached or devoted to, fond<BR> of (with loc. or acc.); अपि वृषलमनुरक्ताः प्रकृतयः━अथ किम्━चन्द्रगुप्ते<BR> दृढमनुरक्ताः प्रकृतयः Mu. 1; कथं वसन्तसेना आर्यचारुदत्तमनुरक्ता<BR> Mk. 1; एषा भवन्तमनुरक्ता Ś. 6. 19; अलभ्यमनुरक्तवान् कथय<BR> किंनु नारीजनम् Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्तिः|अनुरक्ति
अनुरक्तिः <i>f.</i> Love, attachment, devotion, affection. Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जक|अनुरंजक
अनुरञ्जक <i>a.</i> Gratifying, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जनम्
अनुरञ्जनम् Conciliating, satisfying, gratifying, pleasing, keeping<BR> contented; युक्तः प्रजानामनुरञ्जने स्याः U. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जित|अनुरंजित
अनुरञ्जित <i>p. p.</i> Pleased, conciliated, kept contented &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराग|अनुरागः
अनुराग <i>a.</i> Become red, reddened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागः|अनुराग
अनुराग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Redness.<BR>—2 Devotion, attachment, contentment, loyalty (opp. अपरागः); love,<BR> affection, passion (with loc. or in comp.); आविर्भूतानुरागाः Mu. 4. 21;<BR> कण्टकितेन प्रथयति मय्यनुरागं कपोलेन Ś. 3. 14; R. 3. 10;<BR> बहलानुरागकुरुविन्ददलप्रतिबद्धमध्यमिव दिग्वलयम् Śi. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागेङ्गितम्
अनुराग + .{@-गः@} + ˚इङ्गितम् a gesture or external sign expressive of love; प्रसादस्तु<BR> शब्दः स्यादनुरागजः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिन्
अनुरागिन्, अनुरागवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attached, enamoured, impassioned, inspired with love; स वृद्धस्तस्यामतीवानुरागवान्<BR> H. 1; सा केनापि वणिक्पुत्रेण सहानुरागवती बभूव <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 Causing or inspiring love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागवत्|अनुरागवन्त्
अनुरागिन्, अनुरागवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attached, enamoured, impassioned, inspired with love; स वृद्धस्तस्यामतीवानुरागवान्<BR> H. 1; सा केनापि वणिक्पुत्रेण सहानुरागवती बभूव <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 Causing or inspiring love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिणी
अनुरागिन्, अनुरागवत् + .{@-णी@} Personification of a musical note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरणनम्
अनुरणनम्<BR>—1 Sounding conformably to; a continuous tinkling echo produced by the<BR> sounds of bells, anklets &c.<BR>—2 The power of words called व्यञ्जन q. v.; the meaning suggested<BR> by what is actually stated; कमलक्ष्यत्वादेवानुरणनरूपो यो व्यङ्ग्यः S. D. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरतिः|अनुरति
अनुरतिः <i>f.</i> Love, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरथम्
अनुरथम् <i>ind.</i> Behind the carriage; P. II. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरथ्या
अनुरथ्या [रथ्यामन्वायतं स्थिता] A foot-path, a by-road, the<BR> margin of a street, (a path along the margin of a road); प्रकाशीकरणार्थं<BR> च निशागमनशङ्कया । दीपवृक्षांस्तथा चकुरनु रथ्यासु सर्वशः Rām. 2. 6. 18;<BR> Mb. 3. 15. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसित|अनुरसितं
अनुरसित <i>a.</i> Sounding, echoing; उद्ग्रीवैरनुरसितस्य पुष्करस्य<BR> M. 1. 21 accompanied in sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसः|अनुरस
अनुरसः, -रसितम्<BR> Echo, reverberation;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसितम्
अनुरसः, -रसितम्<BR> Echo, reverberation;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसितगुरु
अनुरसः, -रसितम् + ˚गुरु magnified by echo; अनुरसितगुरूणि<BR> स्त्यानमम्बूकृतानि U. 2. 21; (this same verse occurs in). Māl. 9. 6; Mv. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसः|अनुरस
अनुरसः [अनुगतो रसम्]<BR>—1 A secondary feeling (in Rhet.).<BR>—2 A secondary flavour; लवण˚ saltish taste; मधुरानुरसं रूक्षं<BR> लवणानुरसं लघु । नार्यास्तु मधुरं स्तन्यं कषायानुरसं हिमम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरहस
अनुरहस <i>a.</i> [अनुगतम् रहः] Secret, solitary, private.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरहसम्
अनुरहस + .{@-सम्@} <i>adv.</i> In secret, apart, privately; अनुरहसमनायि नायकेन Śi. 7. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरात्र
अनुरात्र <i>a.</i> Following the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरात्रम्
अनुरात्र + .{@-त्रम्@} <i>adv.</i> In the night; every night, night after night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराद्ध
अनुराद्ध <i>a.</i> Accomplished, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराध|अनुराधः
अनुराध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing welfare; also written as अनूराध; इन्द्रं वयमनूराधं हवामहे Av.<BR>—2 Born under the asterism अनुराधा P. IV. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधः|अनुराध
अनुराध + .{@-धः@} N. of a Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधा
अनुराध + .{@-धा@} [अनुगता राधां विशाखाम्] N. of the 17th of the 27 lunar<BR> mansions or asterisms (so called because it follows राधा or विशाखा).<BR> It consists of four stars.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुराधग्रामः, अनुराधपुरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधग्रामः|अनुराधग्राम
अनुराध + -ग्रामः, -पुरम् the ancient capital of Laṅkā or Ceylon; founded<BR> by अनुराध. Also called अनुरोधपुर, described by Rājaśekhara<BR> as full of curiosities. It is a large town in the north of Ceylon “with 1600<BR> square granite pillars which supported the floor of an enormous monastery<BR> called ‘The Great Brazen Palace’ said to have been built in 161 B. C.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधपुरम्
अनुराध + -ग्रामः, -पुरम् the ancient capital of Laṅkā or Ceylon; founded<BR> by अनुराध. Also called अनुरोधपुर, described by Rājaśekhara<BR> as full of curiosities. It is a large town in the north of Ceylon “with 1600<BR> square granite pillars which supported the floor of an enormous monastery<BR> called ‘The Great Brazen Palace’ said to have been built in 161 B. C.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुद्
अनुरुद् €2 P. To weep along with, condole with, sympathize; गुरुशोकामनुरोदितीव<BR> माम् Ku. 4. 15; अनुरोदितीव करुणेन पत्रिणाम् Śi. 4. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोदनम्
अनुरोदनम् Condolence, sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुध्
अनुरुध् €7 U.<BR>—1 To obstruct, block up; शिलाभिर्ये मार्गमनुरुन्धन्ति Mb.; to surround,<BR> hem in; रुद्रानुचरैर्मखो महान् … अन्वरुध्यत Bhāg.<BR>—2 To bind, fasten.<BR>—3 To stick or adhere to, follow closely, observe, practise; अनुरुध्यादघं<BR> त्र्यहम् Ms. 5. 63 should observe impurity (be in mourning); पुमांसमनुरुध्य<BR> जाता पुमनुजा P. III. 2. 100. Sk. born immediately after a male.<BR>—4 To love, be fond of, or devoted to, attach oneself to. समस्थमनुरुध्यन्ते<BR> विषमस्थं त्यजन्ति च Rām.; सद्वृत्तिमनुरुध्यन्तां भवन्तः Mv. 2<BR> follow or adopt; स्वधर्ममनुरुन्धन्ते नातिक्रमम् Ki. 11. 78; नानुरोत्स्ये<BR> जगल्लक्ष्मीम् Bk. 16. 23 love, like.<BR>—5 To conform to, obey, follow, adapt oneself to, act up to; नियतिं लोक<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">Page0105-2</a>]<BR> इवानुरुध्यते Ki. 2. 12; हन्त तिर्यञ्चोऽपि परिचयमनुरुध्यन्ते<BR> U. 3 remember or cherish (act up to it); मद्वचनमनुरुव्यते वा भवान्<BR> K. 181, 298; वात्सल्यमनुरुध्यन्ते महात्मनः Mv. 6 feel the force<BR> of compassion; तेनापि रावणे मैत्रीमनुरुध्य व्यपेक्ष्यते Mv. 5. 34 following<BR> up; यदि गुरुष्वनुरुध्यसे Mv. 3 regard with respect, obey; अनुरुध्यस्व<BR> भगवतो वसिष्ठस्यादेशम् U. 4; चन्द्रकेतोर्वचनम् U. 5.<BR>—6 To coax, gratify, flatter, soothe; इत्यादिभिः प्रियशतरैनुरुध्य मुग्धाम्<BR> U. 3. 26; अभिनवसेवकजनेऽपि एवमनुरुध्यते K. 207 please by carefully<BR> attending to &c., show regard for; 248.<BR>—7 To urge, press, entreat, request; आगमनाय अनुरुध्यमानः K. 277;<BR> तया चाहमनुरुध्यमानस्तां बकुलमालां दत्तवान् Māl. 1; सा च<BR> भीमधन्वना बलवदनुरुद्धा Dk. 122 courted, wooed.<BR>—8 To assent or agree to, approve; like, comply with; प्रकृतयो न मे<BR> व्यसनमनुरुध्यन्ते Dk. 106; यदि भगवाननुरुध्यते Mv. 4 agree with me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुद्ध
अनुरुद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Checked.<BR>—2 Opposed.<BR>—3 Pacified, soothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुध्
अनुरुध् <i>a.</i> [रुध-क्विप्]<BR>—1 One who obeys, conforms to &c.<BR>—2 Obeyed, observed, wanted (अपेक्षित), written as अनूरुध्; आक्षित्<BR> पूर्वास्वपरा अनूरुत् Rv. 3. 55. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधः|अनुरोध
अनुरोधः, -धनम्<BR>—1 Compliance, gratification, fulfilling oneʼs wishes &c.<BR>—2 Conformity, accordance, obedience, regard, consideration; धर्मानुरोधात्<BR> K. 160, 180, 192; अत्र नानुरोधं तर्कये Mv. 7 pleasure or gratification;<BR> आधारानुरोधात् Mu. 1. 2 out of regard for; कविश्रमानुरोधाद्वा Ve. 1<BR> in consideration of; दत्तोत्सेकः प्रलपति मया याज्ञवल्क्यानुरोधात्<BR> Mv. 3. 28, 5. तदनुरोधात्-धेन accordingly, in accordance with it;<BR> वदेद्विपश्चिन्महतोनुरोधात् Pt. 1. 100 after great consideration; humouring;<BR> प्राप्तार्थग्रहणं द्रव्यपरीवर्तोनुरोधनम् H. 2. 101; reference (of a rule.)<BR>—3 Pressing, urging, coaxing; entreaty, solicitation, request; क इवात्रानुरोधः<BR> K. 209; तदनुरोधात् 135; विनानुरोधात्स्वहितेच्छयैव Ś. 20. 81.<BR>—4 Bearing of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधनम्
अनुरोधः, -धनम्<BR>—1 Compliance, gratification, fulfilling oneʼs wishes &c.<BR>—2 Conformity, accordance, obedience, regard, consideration; धर्मानुरोधात्<BR> K. 160, 180, 192; अत्र नानुरोधं तर्कये Mv. 7 pleasure or gratification;<BR> आधारानुरोधात् Mu. 1. 2 out of regard for; कविश्रमानुरोधाद्वा Ve. 1<BR> in consideration of; दत्तोत्सेकः प्रलपति मया याज्ञवल्क्यानुरोधात्<BR> Mv. 3. 28, 5. तदनुरोधात्-धेन accordingly, in accordance with it;<BR> वदेद्विपश्चिन्महतोनुरोधात् Pt. 1. 100 after great consideration; humouring;<BR> प्राप्तार्थग्रहणं द्रव्यपरीवर्तोनुरोधनम् H. 2. 101; reference (of a rule.)<BR>—3 Pressing, urging, coaxing; entreaty, solicitation, request; क इवात्रानुरोधः<BR> K. 209; तदनुरोधात् 135; विनानुरोधात्स्वहितेच्छयैव Ś. 20. 81.<BR>—4 Bearing of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधिन्
अनुरोधिन्, -धक <i>a.</i><BR> Compliant, complying with, obeying or conforming<BR> to, having regard to, caring for; पतिव्रतानां समयानुरोधिनी Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधक
अनुरोधिन्, -धक <i>a.</i><BR> Compliant, complying with, obeying or conforming<BR> to, having regard to, caring for; पतिव्रतानां समयानुरोधिनी Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुह्
अनुरुह् P. To ascend, mount; पञ्च पदानि रुपो अन्वरोहम् Rv. 10. 13. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूप|अनुरूपः
अनुरूप <i>a.</i> [रूपस्य सदृशः योग्यो वा]<BR>—1 Like, resembling, corresponding to; शब्दानुरूपेण पराक्रमेण भवितव्यम्<BR> Pt. 1; worthy of; आत्मानुरूपं वरम् Ś. 1; रूपानुरूप K. 192, 203.<BR>—2 Suitable or fit, adapted to, according to, with gen. or in comp.; नैतदनुरूपं<BR> भवतः K. 146, 158; भव पितुरनुरूपस्त्वं गुणैर्लेककान्तैः V. 5. 21;<BR> काममननुरूपमस्या वपुषो वल्कलम् Ś. 1; स्वप्रमाणानुरूपैः<BR> सेचनघटैः <i>ibid.</i>; सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत<BR> Bg. 17. 3; R. 1. 33; Me. 13<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपम्
अनुरूप + .{@-पम्@}<BR>—1 Resemblance, likeness, conformity.<BR>—2 Suitability, fitness; अपि जनकसुतायास्तच्च तच्चानुरूपम् U. 6. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपः|अनुरूप
अनुरूप + .{@-पः@} The antistrophe, having the same metre as the स्तोत्रिय<BR> or strophe; the second of the three verses (तृच) recited together,<BR> the other two being स्तोत्रिय and पर्यासः एकस्तोत्रियेष्वहस्सु योऽन्योऽनन्तरः<BR> सोऽनुरूपः Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपतः
अनुरूपतः, -पेण, -पशः <i>adv.</i><BR> Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपेण
अनुरूपतः, -पेण, -पशः <i>adv.</i><BR> Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपशः
अनुरूपतः, -पेण, -पशः <i>adv.</i><BR> Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलग्न
अनुलग्न <i>a.</i> Attached to, intent on, seeking or pursuing after;<BR> येन आर्यायाः सुस्निग्धा दृष्टिरनुलग्ना Mk. 4 intently fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलापः|अनुलाप
अनुलापः Repetition, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलालित
अनुलालित <i>a.</i> Entertained कुशिकसुतवचोनुलालिताभ्यां सुखमिव<BR> सा विबाभौ विभावरी Rām. 1. 23. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलासः|अनुलास
अनुलासः, -स्यः<BR> [लस्-नर्तने-घञ्] A peacock; hence metaphorically ‘a corner’<BR> as in वास्तुच्छिद्रानुलासः Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलास्यः|अनुलास्य
अनुलासः, -स्यः<BR> [लस्-नर्तने-घञ्] A peacock; hence metaphorically ‘a corner’<BR> as in वास्तुच्छिद्रानुलासः Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलिप्
अनुलिप् €6 P. To anoint, besmear (with perfumes &c. after bathing);<BR> smear, daub, cover over; वपुरन्वलिप्त न वधूः Śi. 9. 51, 9. 15;<BR> प्रभानुलिप्तश्रीवत्सम् R. 10. 10 covered with; तच्छायानुलिप्तभूतलाम्<BR> K. 131; हरिभिरचिरभासा तेजसा चानुलिप्तैः Ś. 7. 7; so स्नातानुलिप्तः;<BR> तिमिरानुलिप्त enveloped in darkness; स्नापितोऽनुलेपितश्च Dk. 71<BR> besmeared with perfumes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपः|अनुलेप
अनुलेपः, -लेपनम्<BR>—1 Unction, anointing, smearing.<BR>—2 Ointment, unguent such as sandal juice, oil &c.; any emollient or oily<BR> application; ˚आर्द्रमृदङ्गध्वनि K. 28 rubbed with paste; सुरभिकुसुमधूपानुलेपनानि K. 324.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपनम्
अनुलेपः, -लेपनम्<BR>—1 Unction, anointing, smearing.<BR>—2 Ointment, unguent such as sandal juice, oil &c.; any emollient or oily<BR> application; ˚आर्द्रमृदङ्गध्वनि K. 28 rubbed with paste; सुरभिकुसुमधूपानुलेपनानि K. 324.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपक
अनुलेपक, -लेपिन् <i>a.</i><BR> One who anoints (the body) with unguents &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपिन्
अनुलेपक, -लेपिन् <i>a.</i><BR> One who anoints (the body) with unguents &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलीन
अनुलीन <i>a.</i> Hidden, clinging to, attached; स्कन्धं सुगन्धिमनुलीनवता<BR> नगस्य Śi. 5. 46; जनादनुलीनः Dk. 104 concealed from the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोम|अनुलोमः
अनुलोम <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः लोम P. V. 4. 75.]<BR>—1 ‘With the hair’, regular, in natural order, successive (opp. प्रतिलोम);<BR> hence favourable, agreeable; ˚सुखो वायुरनुसारयतीव माम् Rām.;<BR> त्रिरेनामनुलोमामनुमार्ष्टि Śat. Br.; ˚कृष्टं क्षेत्रं प्रतिलोमं कर्षति<BR> Sk. ploughed in the regular direction.<BR>—2 Mixed as a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमा
अनुलोम + .{@-मा@} A woman of the lower caste than that of the manʼs whom she<BR> marries; सकामास्वनुलोमासु न दोषस्त्वन्यथा दमः Y. 2. 288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमम्
अनुलोम + .{@-मम्@} <i>adv.</i> In regular or natural order; प्रतिलोममालिम्पेन्नानुलोमम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमाः
अनुलोम + .{@-माः@} (pl.) Mixed castes.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुलोमाय, अनुलोमार्थ, अनुलोमकल्पः, अनुलोमग, अनुलोमज, अनुलोमजन्मन्, अनुलोमपरिणीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमाय
अनुलोम + -अय <i>a.</i> having fortune favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमार्थ
अनुलोम + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> speaking in favour of; जडानप्यनुलोमार्थान् प्रवाचः<BR> कृतिनां गिरः Śi. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमकल्पः|अनुलोमकल्प
अनुलोम + -कल्पः the thirty-fourth of the Atharvaveda Pariśiṣṭas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमग
अनुलोम + -ग <i>a.</i> straight going; प्रदक्षिणा ग्रहाश्चापि भविष्यन्त्यनुलोमगाः<BR> Mb. 3. 190. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमज|अनुलोमजः
अनुलोम + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> born in due gradation, offspring of a mother<BR> inferior in caste to the father; said of the mixed tribes; संकीर्णयोनयो<BR> ये तु प्रतिलोमानुलोमजाः Ms. 10. 25; Y. 1. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमजन्मन्
अनुलोम + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> born in due gradation, offspring of a mother<BR> inferior in caste to the father; said of the mixed tribes; संकीर्णयोनयो<BR> ये तु प्रतिलोमानुलोमजाः Ms. 10. 25; Y. 1. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमपरिणीत
अनुलोम + -परिणीत <i>a.</i> married in regular gradation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमनम्
अनुलोमनम्<BR>—1 Regular gradation, sending or putting in the right direction.<BR>—2 (In medicine) Carrying off by the regular channels, such as purging; alleviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमयति
अनुलोमयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To stroke or rub with the hair or with the grain, go with the grain;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">Page0106-2</a>]<BR> तत्र प्रतिलोममनुलोमयेत् Suśr.<BR>—2 To evacuate, purge, carry off by the regular channels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुल्वण
अनुल्वण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not excessive, neither more nor less (अनतिरिक्त, अन्यूनाधिक);<BR> smoothed, free from disturbing circumstances (?).<BR>—2 Not clear or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवंशः|अनुवंश
अनुवंशः [वंशमनुगतो वृत्तान्तः]<BR>—1 A genealogical table; तत्रानुवंशो रुद्रस्य तं निबोध युधिष्ठिर<BR> Mb. 3. 114. 10. यत्रानुवंशं भगवान् जामदग्न्यस्तथा जगौ Mb.<BR>—2 Modern race or species; new family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवंशम्
अनुवंशः + .{@-शम्@} <i>ind.</i> अत्रानुवंशं पठतः शृणु मे कुरुनन्दन Mb. 3. 129. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवंश्य
अनुवंश्य <i>a.</i> [अनुवंशे भवः यत्] Relating to a genealogical table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवक्र
अनुवक्र <i>a.</i> [अनुकमेण वक्रः] Very crooked; somewhat crooked<BR> or oblique;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवक्रग
अनुवक्र + ˚ग moving somewhat obliquely or retrogressively (said of planets).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवच्
अनुवच् €2 P.<BR>—1 To say or speak after or for one; येषां द्विजानां सावित्री नानूच्येत<BR> यथाविधि Ms. 11. 191.<BR>—2 To repeat, recite, reiterate; शतमनूच्यमायुष्कामस्य Ait. Br.;<BR> learn, study; परोवरं यज्ञोऽनूच्यते Śat. Br.; वेदमनूच्याचार्योन्तेवासिनमनुशास्ति<BR> T. Up. 1. 10. अरण्येऽनूच्यमानत्वादारण्यकम् Sāy., see अनूचान below.<BR>—3 To concede the point, assent to, yield.<BR>—4 To name, call. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to recite; to read to oneself<BR> (before reading aloud); oft. used in dramas; उभे नाम मुद्राक्षराण्यनुवाच्य<BR> परस्परमवलोकयतः Ś. 1; अनुवाचय तावत् यद्यविरुद्धं श्रोष्यामि<BR> V. 2; Mu. 1; अनुवाचितलेखममात्यमवलोक्य M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवक्तृ
अनुवक्तृ <i>m.</i> Repeating, reciting (गुरुमुखोच्चारितानुरूपपाठक); replying &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवचनम्
अनुवचनम्<BR>—1 Repetition, recitation; teaching, instruction, lecture, वेदानुवचनं<BR> यज्ञो ब्रह्मचर्यं तपो दमः । श्रद्धोपवासः स्वातन्त्र्यमात्मनो ज्ञानहेतवः ॥<BR> Y. 3. 190. तमेतं वेदानुवचनेन ब्राह्मणा विविदिषन्ति Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 22.<BR>—2 A chapter, section, lesson, division.<BR>—3 Repetition of Mantras or texts in conformity with प्रैष or injunction<BR> said by other priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाकः|अनुवाक
अनुवाकः [अनूच्यते इति, वच् घञ् कुत्वम् P. II. 4. 29. Vārt.]<BR>—1 Repeating, reciting reading. अनुवाकहताबुद्धिः Mb. 5. 132. 6.<BR>—2 A subdivision of the Vedas, section, chapter; जेतुं जैत्रानथ खलु<BR> जपन्सूक्तसामानुवाकान् Mv. 3. 23.<BR>—3 Chapter or section referring to a compilation from the Ṛgveda or<BR> Yajurveda (ऋग्यजुःसमूह).<BR>—4 A statement in the ब्राह्मणs illustrating the mantrās; यं वाकेष्वनुवाकेषु<BR> निषत्सूपनिषत्सु च Mb. 12. 47. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुवाकानुक्रमणी, अनुवाकसङ्ख्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाकानुक्रमणी
अनुवाकः + -अनुक्रमणी N. of a table of contents, referring to the Ṛgveda,<BR> attributed to Śaunaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाकसङ्ख्या
अनुवाकः + -सङ्ख्या the fourth of the eighteen Pariśiṣṭas of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक्या
अनुवाक्या [वच्-ण्यत्-कुत्वम्] A verse recited by the Hotṛ priest,<BR> in which the god is invoked to accept the offering prepared for him, or<BR> a sort of priest;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">Page0107-1</a>]<BR> वाक्यलक्षणविदोऽनुवाक्यया Śi. 14. 20 (प्रशास्तृपाठ्या तदभावे होतृपाठ्या<BR> देवताह्वानी ऋक् Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाच्
अनुवाच् <i>f.</i> [वच्-णिच्-क्विप्] Repetition, recitation &c. See अनुवचनम्.<BR>━<i>m.</i> A lecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाचनम्
अनुवाचनम्<BR>—1 Recitation of passages of the Ṛgveda by the Hotṛ priest in obedience<BR> to the injunction (प्रैष) of the अध्वर्यु priest.<BR>—2 Causing to recite, teaching, instructing.<BR>—3 Reading to oneself; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्त
अनूक्त <i>p. p.</i> Repeated, recited after; occurring in the text studied.<BR> यथा वेदो वाननूक्तोऽन्यद्वा कर्माकृतम् Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्तम्
अनूक्त + .{@-क्तम्, -क्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Subsequent mention; repetition by way of explanation or illustration.<BR>—2 Study of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्तिः|अनूक्ति
अनूक्त + .{@-क्तम्, -क्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Subsequent mention; repetition by way of explanation or illustration.<BR>—2 Study of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूचान <i>a.</i> or -नः<BR> [अनुवच्-कानच् निपातः P. III. 2. 109; वेदस्य अनुवचनं<BR> कृतवान् अनूचानः Sk.]<BR>—1 One devoted to study, learned; especially one well-versed in the Vedas<BR> with their Aṅgas so as to be able to repeat, read and teach them; योऽनूचानः<BR> स नो महान् Mb. 9. 51. 50; Ms. 2. 154, 5. 82; Y. 3. 24; इदमूचुरनूचानाः<BR> Ku. 6. 15. दृप्तबालाकिर्हानूचानो गार्ग्य आस Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Modest, unassuming; humble, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचानः|अनूचान
अनूचान <i>a.</i> or -नः<BR> [अनुवच्-कानच् निपातः P. III. 2. 109; वेदस्य अनुवचनं<BR> कृतवान् अनूचानः Sk.]<BR>—1 One devoted to study, learned; especially one well-versed in the Vedas<BR> with their Aṅgas so as to be able to repeat, read and teach them; योऽनूचानः<BR> स नो महान् Mb. 9. 51. 50; Ms. 2. 154, 5. 82; Y. 3. 24; इदमूचुरनूचानाः<BR> Ku. 6. 15. दृप्तबालाकिर्हानूचानो गार्ग्य आस Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Modest, unassuming; humble, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवत्सरः|अनुवत्सर|अनुवत्सरं
अनुवत्सरः [अनुकूलो वत्सरो दानादिविशेषाय]<BR>—1 A year.<BR>—2 The 4th year in the 5 yearsʼ cycle; or the 5th of 5 cycles of 12 years<BR> in the Bṛhaspati cycle. वायुमेव तदनुवत्सरमाप्नोति T. Br. 1. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवद्
अनुवद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To imitate in speaking, mock (with acc.); गिरं नः … अनुवदति<BR> शुकस्ते मञ्जुवाक् पञ्जरस्थः R. 5. 74 repeat; उक्तमनुवदति Sk.;<BR> (P. & Ā.) to resound, echo; अनुवदति बीणा P. I. 3. 49. Sk. अनुवदते<BR> कठः कलापस्य <i>ibid.</i>; सभाभित्तिप्रतिध्वानैर्भयादन्ववदन्निव<BR> Śi. 2. 67 echoed and approved also; घोषस्यान्ववदिष्टेव लङ्का पूतकतोः<BR> पुरः Bk. 8. 29.<BR>—2 To repeat or say again by way of explanation, illustration or corroboration;<BR> see Kull. on Ms. 1. 74, 2. 6.<BR>—3 To repeat, tell, say (generally); निजमनोरथमनुवदन्त्या Dk. 21.<BR>—4 To abuse, rail at. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to resound or echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादः|अनुवाद
अनुवादः<BR>—1 Repetition (in general); गुण˚ K. 206.<BR>—2 Repetition by way of explanation, illustration or corroboration; अनुवादे<BR> चरणानाम् P. II. 4. 3 (सिद्धस्योपन्यासे Sk.)<BR>—3 Explanatory repetition or reference to what is already mentioned, such<BR> as paraphrase or free translation; particularly, any portion of the Brāhmaṇas<BR> which comments on, illustrates, or explains a <i>Vidhi</i> or direction previously<BR> laid down and which does not itself lay down any directions; a supplementary<BR> repetition, opp. to विधि ‘authoritative or direct injunction’; विधिविहितस्य<BR> अनुवचनमनुवादः । नानुवादपुनरुक्तयोः विशेषः शब्दाभ्यासोपपत्तेः<BR> Nyāya S.; cf. also विध्यनुवादयोर्विधिर्ज्यायान्, अपूर्वार्थप्रकल्पत्वादिति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 3. It is of 3 kinds:− भूतार्थ˚ (सदेव सौम्येदमग्र<BR> आसीत्); स्तुत्यर्थ˚ (वायुर्वै क्षेपिष्ठा देवता) and गुण˚ (अग्निहोत्रं<BR> जुहोति इत्युक्ते दध्ना जुहोति इति गुणविधानात्);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">Page0107-2</a>]<BR> see अर्थवाद also.<BR>—4 Corroboration, confirmation.<BR>—5 Slander, abuse, reviling.<BR>—6 Advertisement, notice; report, rumour.<BR>—7 Commencement of speech (वाचारम्भणमात्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादक
अनुवादक, -वादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Explanatory, corroborative, repeating with comment, explanation or<BR> illustration; आरम्भश्च साहसानुवादी Dk. 95 bespeaks.<BR>—2 Conformable to, in harmony with, like; युक्तगीतानुवादिना Rām.;<BR> तदनुवादिगुणः कुसुमोद्गमः R. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादिन्
अनुवादक, -वादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Explanatory, corroborative, repeating with comment, explanation or<BR> illustration; आरम्भश्च साहसानुवादी Dk. 95 bespeaks.<BR>—2 Conformable to, in harmony with, like; युक्तगीतानुवादिना Rām.;<BR> तदनुवादिगुणः कुसुमोद्गमः R. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादिन्
अनुवादक, -वादिन् + .{@-न्@} <i>m.</i> N. of any one of the three notes of the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be explained or illustrated.<BR>—2 (In gram.) To be made the subject of an assertion (in a sentence),<BR> opposed to विधेय which affirms or denies something about the subject.<BR> In a sentence the अनुवाद्य or subject which is supposed to be already<BR> known is repeated to mark its connection with the विधेय or predicate<BR> and should be placed first; अनुवाद्यमनुक्त्वैव न विधेयमुदीरयेत्;<BR> in वृद्धिरादैच्, P. I. 1. 1 आदैच् should have been placed first,<BR> though the construction is defended by Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तन|अनुवर्तनं|अनुवर्त्तन|अनुवर्त्तनं
अनुवर्तन, -वर्तिन् &c.<BR> see अनुवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तिन्|अनुवर्त्तिन्
अनुवर्तन, -वर्तिन् &c.<BR> see अनुवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्त्मन्
अनुवर्त्मन् <i>m.</i> A follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवश|अनुवशः
अनुवश <i>a.</i> [वशमनुगतः] Subject to the will of another, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवशः|अनुवश
अनुवश + .{@-शः@} Subjection, obedience (to the will of another). भरतानुवशात्सोऽपि<BR> शत्रुघ्नस्तत्समं गतः Rām. 2. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवस्
अनुवस् To clothe, cover; सोमस्त्वा राजा अमृतेनानु वस्ताम् Rv. 6. 75. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवस्
अनुवस् €1 P. To dwell near to or along with (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासिन्
अनुवासिन् <i>a.</i> One who dwells near; resident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवसित
अनुवसित <i>a.</i> [वस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Dressed, clothed, wrapped up.<BR>—2 Fastened, or bound to, attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवहः|अनुवह
अनुवहः One of the 7 tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवातः|अनुवात
अनुवातः [अनुगतो वातः] The windward direction; the wind which<BR> blows from the pupil to the preceptor &c.; प्रतिवातेऽनुवाते च नासीत<BR> गुरुणा सह Ms. 2. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवारम्
अनुवारम् <i>ind.</i> Time after time, repeatedly, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास्
अनुवास् €10 P.<BR>—1 To scent, perfume.<BR>—2 To use the oily enema (see the next word); treat by using such enema;<BR> अवश्यं स्थापनीयाश्च नानुवास्याः कथञ्चन Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासः|अनुवास
अनुवासः, -सनम्<BR>—1 Perfuming or scenting (in general) with incense &c.<BR>—2 Perfuming clothes by dipping the ends.<BR>—3 (˚नः also) A syringe, clyster-pipe (Mar. पिचकारी); an oily<BR> enema or the operation itself; असाध्यता विकाराणां स्यादेषामनुवासनात्<BR> Suśr.; द्विधा बस्तिः परिज्ञेयो निरूहश्चानुवासनम् । कषायाद्यैर्निरूहः<BR> स्यात् स्नेहाद्यैरनुवासनम् ॥ (अनुवसति अनुवासरं वा दीयते अनुवसन्नपि<BR> न दुष्यति अनुदिवसं वा दीयते इति अनुवासनः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासनम्
अनुवासः, -सनम्<BR>—1 Perfuming or scenting (in general) with incense &c.<BR>—2 Perfuming clothes by dipping the ends.<BR>—3 (˚नः also) A syringe, clyster-pipe (Mar. पिचकारी); an oily<BR> enema or the operation itself; असाध्यता विकाराणां स्यादेषामनुवासनात्<BR> Suśr.; द्विधा बस्तिः परिज्ञेयो निरूहश्चानुवासनम् । कषायाद्यैर्निरूहः<BR> स्यात् स्नेहाद्यैरनुवासनम् ॥ (अनुवसति अनुवासरं वा दीयते अनुवसन्नपि<BR> न दुष्यति अनुदिवसं वा दीयते इति अनुवासनः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासित
अनुवासित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fumigated, perfumed.<BR>—2 Administered as an enama; treated by this operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्
अनुविद् €6 U.<BR>—1 To find, discover, see, obtain.<BR>—2 To deem, consider.<BR>—3 To marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवित्त
अनुवित्त <i>a.</i> Found, obtained; यस्यानुवित्तः प्रतिबुद्ध आत्माऽस्मि<BR> सन्देह्ये गहने प्रविष्टः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 13. अयं पन्था अनुवित्तः<BR> पुराणः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवित्तिः|अनुवित्ति
अनुवित्तिः <i>f.</i> Finding, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविध
अनुविध <i>a.</i> One who imitates, a devotee दृतय इव श्वसन्त्यसुभृतां<BR> यदि तेऽनुविधा Bhāg. 10. 87. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध See under अनुव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधा
अनुविधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To lay down a rule, regulate.<BR>—2 To obey, act up to, follow, conform to; see अनुविधायिन्; पदमनुविधेयं<BR> च महताम् Bh. 2. 28 the foot-steps of the great have to be trodden in.<BR>—3 To resemble, imitate. ━<i>pass.</i> To be trained to follow rules; obey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधानम्
अनुविधानम्<BR>—1 Obedience.<BR>—2 Acting in conformity to (orders &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधायिन्
अनुविधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obedient, submissive, compliant, conforming to orders; सा स्त्री याऽनुविधायिनी<BR> H. 2. 130; भवितव्यानुविधायीनीन्द्रियाणि V. 3.<BR>—2 Resembling; निजवधूश्वसितानुविधायिनि Śi. 6. 23, 15. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविहित
अनुविहित <i>a.</i> Obedient; तस्यानुविहितोऽनाथा Bhāg. 1. 9. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविनश्
अनुविनश् €4 P. To disappear, vanish or perish after or along with<BR> another. विज्ञानघन एव एतेभ्यो भूतेभ्यः समुत्थाय, तान्येवानुविनश्यति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 4 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविनाशः|अनुविनाश
अनुविनाशः Perishing after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविश्
अनुविश् €6 P. To enter or go after, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेशः|अनुवेश
अनुवेशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Following, entering after.<BR>—2 Marriage of a younger brother before the elder is married; (ज्येष्ठातिक्रमेण<BR> कनिष्ठस्य विवाहः); यवीयसोऽनुवेशो हि ज्येष्टस्य विधिलोपकः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेशनम्
अनुवेशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Following, entering after.<BR>—2 Marriage of a younger brother before the elder is married; (ज्येष्ठातिक्रमेण<BR> कनिष्ठस्य विवाहः); यवीयसोऽनुवेशो हि ज्येष्टस्य विधिलोपकः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेश्य
अनुवेश्य <i>a.</i> [अनुकमेण वेशमर्हति, यत्] A next-door neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविश्वः|अनुविश्व
अनुविश्वः (pl.) N. of a people in the north-east. Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविषयः|अनुविषय
अनुविषयः Taste; अपश्यन्तोऽनुविषयं भुञ्जते विघसाशिनः Mb. 12. 287. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविष्टम्भः|अनुविष्टम्भ|अनुविष्टंभः
अनुविष्टम्भः Being obstructed in consequence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्
अनुवृत् €1 Ā. (sometimes P. also)<BR>—1 (Transitively used)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go or roll after, follow, pursue; (fig.) to follow, conform<BR> to, act according to, obey, adapt oneself to, be guided by; humour; अहं<BR> तावत्स्वामिनश्चित्तवृत्तिमनुवर्तिष्ये Ś. 2; तेऽपि परिचयमनुवर्तन्ते<BR> K. 289; किमत्र चित्रं यदि विशाखे शशाङ्कलेखामनुवर्तेते Ś. 3 approve<BR> of her choice; लौकिकानां हि साधूनामर्थं वागनुवर्तते U. 1. 10 words<BR> conform to the sense; न कुलकममनुवर्तते K. 104 follow; मधु<BR> द्विरेफः कुसुमैकपात्रे पपौ प्रियां स्वामनुवर्तमानः Ku. 3. 36 followed<BR> his mate in drinking, drank after her; (जननीम्)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">Page0108-2</a>]<BR> अत्यन्तशुद्धहृदयामनुवर्तमानाम् Bh. 2. 110; मम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते<BR> मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः Bg. 3. 23; Dk. 80, 96, 126; कृतज्ञतामनुवर्तमानेन<BR> Mu. 3 following the path of gratitude; प्रभुचित्तमेव हि जनोऽनुवर्तते<BR> Śi. 15. 41; Māl. 3. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To imitate, resemble; equal; तेऽन्ववर्तन् पितॄन्सर्वे यशसा<BR> च बलेन च Mb.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To gratify, humour, please; Dk. 65.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To serve, worship; पञ्चवर्षसहस्राणि सूर्यं चैवान्ववर्तत<BR> Rām. 7. 10. 8.<BR>—2 (Intransitively used)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To follow, come after; संग्राह्य इत्यनुवर्तते H. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To continue, endure.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To act towards, behave.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) (In gram.) To be repeated or supplied from a preceding rule,<BR> Sūtra or assertion (said of a word or rule which continues to exercise<BR> influence on what follows); <i>e. g.</i> in भक्तिः P. IV. 3. 95; सोऽस्य<BR> (occurring in Sūtra 89 before) इत्यनुवर्तते Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to revolve, turn round; एवं प्रवर्तितं चकं नानुवर्तयतीह<BR> यः Bg. 3. 16.<BR>—2 To act up to, follow, obey; तथापि लोकयात्रानुवर्तनीया Mv. 7;<BR> पुत्रैः पितरो लोकद्वयेप्यनुवर्तनीयाः Ve. 3; K. 367.<BR>—3 To favour, oblige; comply with oneʼs request; विधिनापि भवतेव वयमनुवर्तिताः<BR> K. 73; यथाचित्तमनुवर्तनीयः Māl. 7.<BR>—4 To put in, carry out.<BR>—5 To repeat or supply from a preceding Sūtra; केचित्तु विजायते इति<BR> नानुवर्तयन्ति P. V. 2. 13. Sk.<BR>—6 To use, employ.<BR>—7 To lead one to, attach to.<BR>—8 To speak in favour of, speak for; to approve.<BR>—9 To imitate, do after one; सतां चरितान्यनुवर्तितानि नेन्द्रियाणि K. 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तनम्
अनुवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Following (fig. also); attending, compliance, obedience, conformity;<BR> प्रकृतस्यानुवर्तने Ak.; इदमाश्चर्यमथवा लोकस्थित्यनुवर्तनम्<BR> Mv. 7. 4; दाक्षिण्य˚ Dk. 161.<BR>—2 Gratifying, obliging.<BR>—3 Approval of, concurrence in.<BR>—4 Continuance; result, consequence.<BR>—5 Supplying from a preceding Sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तिन्|अनुवर्त्तिन्
अनुवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Following, obeying, conforming to, with acc. or in comp.; कश्च लक्ष्मणमुक्तानां<BR> रामकोपानुवर्तिनाम् । शराणामग्रतः स्थातुं शक्तो देवासुरेष्वपि ॥ Rām. 5. 51. 19.<BR> राक्षसाश्चापि गृह्यन्ते नित्यं छन्दानुवर्तिभिः Pt. 1. 69;<BR> नराधिपा नीचजनानुवर्तिनः 1. 383.<BR>—2 Guided by, following the advice of; obedient, faithful, compliant;<BR> अनुवर्तिनि कलत्रे Pt. 1. 101, भृत्यानामनुवर्तिनाम् 298.<BR>—3 Like, resembling, worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्त्मन्
अनुवर्त्मन् <i>a.</i> [अनुगतो वर्त्म] Following, attending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्त
अनुवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obeying, following &c. स मेरुमनुवृत्तः स पुनर्गच्छति पाण्डव<BR> Mb. 3. 163. 31.<BR>—2 Uninterrupted, continuously kept up, continued; अनुवृत्तस्त्वया भगीरथगृहे<BR> प्रसादः U. 7.<BR>—3 Rounded off; taperingly round (कमशः वर्तुलाकार); सुपत्रमनुवृत्ताङ्गं<BR> सुपर्वाणं सुसंस्थितम् Rām. 6. 90. 65. दीर्घानुवृत्तपीनबाहुना K. 179.<BR>—4 Supplied from a preceding rule &c.<BR>—5 Conforming to the character (शीलानुगत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्तम्
अनुवृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} Obedience, conformity, compliance; मूर्खं छन्दोऽनुवृत्तेन<BR> (गृह्णीयात्) Cāṇ. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्तिः|अनुवृत्ति
अनुवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Assenting to, approval; तवानुवृत्तिं न च कर्तुमुत्सहे Ku. 5. 65.<BR>—2 Obedience, conformity, following, continuance in (opp. व्यावृत्ति);<BR> taking up; continuity; ज्येष्ठानुवृत्तिजटिलम् R. 13. 78 by following<BR> the example of;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">Page0109-1</a>]<BR> अनुवृत्त्या प्रमार्ष्टुमागतः Dk. 100 service; cf. also वाचानुवृत्तिः<BR> खलु अतिथिसत्कारः Pratimā 5. ततान वह्निः पवनानुवृत्त्या Ki. 16. 52<BR> in consequence of.<BR>—3 Acting according or suitably to, compliance, acquiescence; gratifying,<BR> pleasing; कान्ता˚चातुर्यमपि शिक्षितं वत्सेन U. 3; Māl. 9; Śi. 9. 58;<BR> K. 265; M. 2. 9; राज्यं हि नाम राजधर्म˚ परस्य नृपतेर्महदप्रीतिस्थानम्<BR> Mu. 3 who conforms to or is true to the duties of kings; (previous) compliant<BR> or obedient spirit, previous course of conduct; U. 7. 5.<BR>—4 Remembrance आसेदुषां गोत्रभिदोऽनुवृत्त्या Ki. 18. 18.<BR>—5 (Gram.) Being supplied or repeated in a following rule; continued influence<BR> of a preceding on a following rule.<BR>—6 Imitating, resembling &c.<BR>—7 Repetition; वर्णानामनुवृत्तिरनुप्रासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृद्धि
अनुवृद्धि <i>a.</i> Ved. Increasing in regular ratio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेलम्
अनुवेलम् <i>ind.</i> Ever and anon, constantly; इति स्म पृच्छत्यनुवेलमादृतः<BR> R. 3. 5; Śi. 3. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेल्लित
अनुवेल्लित <i>a.</i> [वेल्ल्-क्तम्] Bent in conformity with; bent under.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेल्लितम्
अनुवेल्लित + .{@-तम्@} Securing with bandages, bandaging, a sort of bandage (व्रणलेपनबन्धभेदः)<BR> one of the 14 kinds mentioned by Suśruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्य
अनुव्य <i>a.</i> [अनुव्ययति अनुगच्छति व्ये-क] Following (अनुगत);<BR> ˚व्यमिवासुः Kāty. (न्यग्भूमिं प्राप्ता इव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यञ्जनम्
अनुव्यञ्जनम् A secondary token.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यध्
अनुव्यध् €4 P.<BR>—1 To hit or pierce again; विद्धमनुविध्यतः Ms. 9. 43.<BR>—2 To wound, pierce; कामशरानुविद्धः &c.<BR>—3 To fill or mix with, blend with, see अनुविद्ध below.<BR>—4 To impel, urge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pierced, bored; कीटानुविद्धरत्नादिसाधारण्येन काव्यता S. D.<BR>—2 Overspread, intertwined; surrounded, full of; pervaded by, replete<BR> or filled with, abounding in, mixed or blended with, intermixed; सरसिजमनुविद्धं<BR> शैवलेनापि रम्यम् Ś. 1. 20; क्वचित्प्रभालेपिभिरिन्द्रनीलैर्मुक्तामयी<BR> यष्टिरिवानुविद्धा R. 13. 54 interwoven with emeralds; 16. 48, 6. 18;<BR> अलके बालकुन्दानुविद्धम् Me. 67; सौरभ्य˚ Mk. 1; कोपानुविद्धां<BR> चिन्तां नाटयन् Mu. 3; Ku. 3. 35; पाण्डुतानुविद्धेव देहच्छविः Dk. 112, 137;<BR> Māl. 1.<BR>—3 Connected with, relating to; adhering to; देशवार्तानुविद्धा संकथा<BR> Dk. 117, 124; उद्गूर्णलोष्टलगुडैः परितोऽनुविद्धम् Śi. 5. 25 chased,<BR> closely followed or pursued.<BR>—4 Set, inlaid; variegated; रत्नानुविद्धार्णवमेखलाया दिशः सपत्नी<BR> भव दक्षिणस्याः R. 6. 63, 14; Śi. 4. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेधः|अनुवेध
अनुवेधः, -व्याधः<BR>—1 Hurting, piercing, perforating; न हि कीटानुवेधादयो रत्नस्य रत्नत्वं<BR> व्याहन्तुमीशाः S. D. 1.<BR>—2 Contact, union; मुखामोदं मदिरया कृतानुव्या कृतमुद्वमन् Śi. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Blending, mixture; fusion.<BR>—4 Obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याधः|अनुव्याध
अनुवेधः, -व्याधः<BR>—1 Hurting, piercing, perforating; न हि कीटानुवेधादयो रत्नस्य रत्नत्वं<BR> व्याहन्तुमीशाः S. D. 1.<BR>—2 Contact, union; मुखामोदं मदिरया कृतानुव्या कृतमुद्वमन् Śi. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Blending, mixture; fusion.<BR>—4 Obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यवसायः|अनुव्यवसाय
अनुव्यवसायः (In Nyāya) Consciousness of the perception; (in Vedānta<BR> Phil.) perception of a sentiment or judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याख्यानम्
अनुव्याख्यानम् [अनुरूपं व्याख्यानम्] That which comments on and<BR> explains Mantras, Sūtras &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">Page0109-2</a>]<BR> (मन्त्रविवरणम्); especially, that portion of a Brāhmaṇa which<BR> explains difficult Sūtras, texts &c. occurring in another place (मन्त्रादीनामनुरूपार्थप्रकाशकं व्याख्यानम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहरणम्
अनुव्याहरणम्, -व्याहारः<BR>—1 Repetition, repeated utterance; mentioning, along with something else.<BR>—2 A curse, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहारः|अनुव्याहार
अनुव्याहरणम्, -व्याहारः<BR>—1 Repetition, repeated utterance; mentioning, along with something else.<BR>—2 A curse, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहारिन्
अनुव्याहारिन् <i>a.</i> Cursing; execrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रज्
अनुव्रज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To follow, go after; तां व्रजन्तीमनुवव्राज K. 132, 210; attend<BR> especially a departing guest (as far as the bank of water, lake, &c.)<BR> as a mark of respect; अतिथिं श्रोत्रियं तृप्तमासीमान्तमनुव्रजेत् Y. 1. 113;<BR> तं मातरो देवमनुव्रजन्त्यः Ku. 7. 38; यमिच्छेत्पुनरायान्तं<BR> नैनं दूरमनुव्रजेत् Rām. 2. 40. 50.<BR>—2 To visit in order, seek.<BR>—3 To go to or near; betake oneself to; मृगा मृगैः सङ्गमनुव्रजन्ति<BR> Pt. 1. 282 deer herd or associate with deer.<BR>—4 To obey, to do homage to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रजनम्
अनुव्रजनम्, -व्रज्या<BR> Following, going after, especially a departing guest;<BR> आसनावसथौ शय्यामनुव्रज्यामुपासनाम् Ms. 3. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रज्या
अनुव्रजनम्, -व्रज्या<BR> Following, going after, especially a departing guest;<BR> आसनावसथौ शय्यामनुव्रज्यामुपासनाम् Ms. 3. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्राज्य
अनुव्राज्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be followed as by the relatives of a dead<BR> person to the cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रत|अनुव्रतः
अनुव्रत <i>a.</i> [अनुकूलं व्रतं कर्म यस्य]<BR>—1 Devoted or faithful to, राजानो राजपुत्राश्च धृतराष्ट्रमनुव्रताः<BR> Mb. 3. 35. 30 attached to (with acc. or gen.); अभ्यगच्छददीनात्मा दमयन्तीमनुव्रतः<BR> Mb. 3. 54. 27. प्रियतमा का अनुव्रता Bh. 2. 103; वैश्याः क्षत्रमनुव्रताः Rām.<BR>—2 Duly performing the vows or duties prescribed (opp. अपव्रत) Bhāg. 8. 15. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रतः|अनुव्रत
अनुव्रत + .{@-तः@} A class of Jaina ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रता
अनुव्रत + .{@-ता@} A devoted virtuous wife (पतिव्रता); रक्ते भटे रणमुखे<BR> रुधिरेण तस्मिन् रक्ता भवत्यमरयोषिदनुव्रतेन; विश्वगुणादर्शचम्पू 379.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशतिक
अनुशतिक <i>a.</i> Accompanied with, or bought for, a hundred; तथाविधोनुशतिकः<BR> शतानीकस्य साधकः । जानाति युद्धसंभारं कार्ययोग्यं च सैनिकम् Śukra. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशतिकादिः|अनुशतिकादि
अनुशतिक + ˚आदिः a class of words or गण mentioned in P. VII. 3. 20,<BR> where both members undergo Vṛddhi. अनुशतिकादीनां च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशय|अनुशयः
अनुशय, -शयिन् &c.<BR> See under अनुशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशय, -शयिन् &c.<BR> See under अनुशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशरः|अनुशर
अनुशरः [अनु-शृणाति. शॄ-अच्] A sort of evil-spirit, Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशस्त्रम्
अनुशस्त्रम् [अनुगतं शस्त्रं शस्त्रार्थे प्रयुक्तम्] Anything used<BR> (for the time being) instead of a regular instrument, such as a finger-nail;<BR> a secondary weapon or instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशाला
अनुशाला An ante-chamber, a special kind of hall; अनुशाला च मध्ये<BR> च चैकभागेन भद्रकम् Māna. 26. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्
अनुशास् €2 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To advise, persuade, prevail upon, address; इति ध्रुवेच्छामनुशासती<BR> सुतां शशाक मेना न नियन्तुमुद्यमात् Ku. 5. 5; पूर्वानुशिष्टां निजगाद<BR> भोज्याम् R. 6. 59.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To direct, tell, order, enjoin, to teach, instruct (how to act);<BR> दशरथप्रभवानुशिष्टः R. 13. 75; वत्से त्वमधुनाऽनुशासनीयासि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">Page0110-1</a>]<BR> Ś. 4; राजपत्नीनियोगस्थमनुशाधि पुरीजनम् Bk. 20. 17; को नु खलु<BR> मामेवमनुशास्ति V. 4 tells, directs; मघवा वनगमनाय कृतबुद्धिं<BR> भवन्तमनुशास्ति V. 5 tells, directs; माणवकं धर्ममनुशास्ति Sk.; Ms. 6. 86.<BR>—2 To rule, govern.<BR>—3 To chastise, punish, correct; इयमेव तावत्प्रथममनुशासनीया<BR> Ve. 2; अरिकुलमनुशासनीयम् 3; स्वकर्म ख्यापयन्ब्रूयान्मां भवाननुशास्त्विति<BR> Ms. 11. 99, 9. 233.<BR>—4 To praise, extol.<BR>—5 To accomplish, perform, execute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासक
अनुशासक, -शासिन्, -शास्तृ or शासितृ <i>a.</i><BR> One who directs, instructs,<BR> governs or punishes; कविं पुराणमनुशासितारम् Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष<BR> चोरानुशासी राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासिन्
अनुशासक, -शासिन्, -शास्तृ or शासितृ <i>a.</i><BR> One who directs, instructs,<BR> governs or punishes; कविं पुराणमनुशासितारम् Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष<BR> चोरानुशासी राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्तृ
अनुशासक, -शासिन्, -शास्तृ or शासितृ <i>a.</i><BR> One who directs, instructs,<BR> governs or punishes; कविं पुराणमनुशासितारम् Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष<BR> चोरानुशासी राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासितृ
अनुशासक, -शासिन्, -शास्तृ or शासितृ <i>a.</i><BR> One who directs, instructs,<BR> governs or punishes; कविं पुराणमनुशासितारम् Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष<BR> चोरानुशासी राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासनम्
अनुशासनम् Advice, persuasion, direction, order. command; instruction,<BR> laying down rules or precepts; a law, rule, precept; treatment (of a subject),<BR> (with the object in comp. or with gen., the agent, if expressed, being<BR> put in the instr. or gen.); एतद्वै भद्रमनुशासनस्य Rv. 10. 32. 7.<BR> एतदनुशासनम् T. Up. 7. 9. 7. भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनम्<BR> Ki. 1. 28 words of advice; तन्मनोरनुशासनम् Ms. 8. 139, 6. 50, 2. 159;<BR> यौवन˚ K. 146; नामलिङ्ग˚ laying down rules on the gender<BR> of nouns, explanation of gender &c.; शब्दानुशासनम् Sk.; शब्दानामनुशासनमाचार्यस्य<BR> आचार्येण वा P. II. 3. 66. Sk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुशासनपर, अनुशासनपर्वन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासनपर
अनुशासनम् + -पर <i>a.</i> obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासनपर्वन्
अनुशासनम् + -पर्वन् N. of the 13th book of the Mahābhārata (so called because<BR> it lays down precepts of advice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्तिः|अनुशास्ति
अनुशास्तिः <i>f.</i> Advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिष्ट
अनुशिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 educated; स प्रैति क्षेत्रविदानुशिष्टः Rv. 10. 32. 7; Bhāg. 5. 9. 4;<BR> तस्मात् पुत्रमनुशिष्टं लोक्यमाहुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 17.<BR>—2 questioned इति तेनानुशिष्टस्तु वाचं मन्दमुदीरयत् Rām. 6. 30. 4.<BR>—3 Directed; एष धर्मानुशिष्टो वो यतीनां नियतात्मनाम् Ms. 7. 86, 9. 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिष्टिः|अनुशिष्टि
अनुशिष्टिः <i>f.</i> Instruction, teaching; order, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिक्षिन्
अनुशिक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Practising, learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिशुः|अनुशिशु
अनुशिशुः <i>f.</i> [अनुगता शिशुना] An animal followed by its young one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशी
अनुशी €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To lie or sleep with, sleep along with; lie upon, close or along; lay<BR> oneself down; to adhere to or follow closely, cling or stick to; शयानं<BR> चानुशेते हि तिष्ठन्तमनुतिष्टति । अनुधावति धावन्तं कर्म पूर्वकृतं<BR> नरम् ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 To repent, grieve for; दत्तमिष्टमपि नान्वशेत सः Śi. 14. 45;<BR> पुरानुशेते तव चञ्चलं मनः Ki. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयः|अनुशय
अनुशयः [शी-अच्]<BR>—1 Repentance, remorse; regret, sorrow; नन्वनुशयस्थानमेतत् Māl. 8;<BR> कुतस्तेऽनुशयः M. 3 why should you be sorry; बाष्पं प्रमृज्य<BR> विगतानुशयो भवेयम् Ś. 7. 25; इतो गतस्यानुशयो मा भूदिति V. 4;<BR> ततः सपत्नापनयस्मरणानुशयस्फुरा Śi. 2. 14.<BR>—2 Intense enmity or anger; शिशुपालोऽनुशयं परं गतः Śi. 16. 2;<BR> यस्मिन्नमुक्तानुशया सदैव जागर्ति भुजङ्गी Māl. 6. 1.<BR>—3 Hatred.<BR>—4 Close connection, as with a consequence; close attachment (to any object).<BR> अयं त्वन्यो गुणः श्रेष्ठश्च्युतानां स्वर्गतो मुने । शुभानुशययोगेन मनुष्येषूपजायते ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">Page0110-2</a>]<BR> Mb. 3. 261. 33.<BR>—5 (In Vedānta Phil.) The result or consequence of bad deeds which very<BR> closely clings to them and makes the soul enter other bodies after enjoying<BR> temporary freedom from recurring births; (स्वर्गार्थकर्मणो भुक्तफलस्य<BR> अवशेषः कश्चिदनुशयो नाम भाण्डानुसारिस्नेहवत्, यथा हि स्नेहभाण्डं<BR> विरिच्यमानं सर्वात्मना न विरिच्यते भाण्डानुसार्येव कश्चित् स्नेहशेषोऽवतिष्ठते<BR> तथानुशयोऽपि Tv.).<BR>—6 Regret in the case of purchases, technically called rescission; कीत्वा<BR> विकीय वा किञ्चिद्यस्येहानुशयो भवेत् Ms. 8. 222; see कीतानुशय. cf.<BR> … अनुशयो द्वेषे पश्चात्तापानुबन्धयोः and<BR> … अनुशयो दीर्घद्वेषानुतापयोः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयी
अनुशयः + .{@-यी@} A disease of the feet, a sort of boil or abscess on the upper part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयान
अनुशयान <i>a.</i> Regretting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयाना
अनुशयान + .{@-ना@} A variety of heroine (परकीयनायिकाभेदः); one who is<BR> sad and dejected, being apprehensive of the loss of her lover (इष्टहानिजनितानुतापवती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशयिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devotedly attached to, faithful.<BR>—2 Repentant, penitent, regretful, sorry.<BR>—3 Hating intensely.<BR>—4 Connected as with a consequence.<BR>—5 Enjoying the fruits of deeds; epithet of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशायिन्
अनुशायिन् <i>a.</i> Lying or extending along. ━<i>m.</i> Life; यश्चानुशायिनां<BR> स्वर्गः पाखण्डस्य च संभवः Bhāg. 2. 8. 22. See अनुशयिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीतम्
अनुशीतम् <i>ind.</i> In cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलनम्
अनुशीलनम् Intent or assiduous application, constant pursuit or exercise,<BR> constant or repeated practice or study; विज्ञातसाराण्यनुशीलनेन Ki. 16. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलित
अनुशीलित <i>a.</i> Assiduously practised, repeatedly done, carefully<BR> attended to or studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुच्
अनुशुच् €1 P. To bewail, mourn over, regret; गतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति<BR> पण्डिताः Bg. 2. 11. कथं तमेव चौरहतकमनुशोचसि Mk. 3; नष्टं<BR> मृतमतिक्रान्तं नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः Pt. 1. 333; शैशवं ते स्मृत्वात्मानमनुशोचामि<BR> K. 333; विराजमानौ शोकेऽपि तनयाननुशोचतम् Ve. 5. 4 condole with,<BR> weep with. ━<i>Caus.</i> To mourn over, deplore, grieve for, regret;<BR> तृणमिव वने शून्ये त्यक्ता न वाप्यनुशोचिता U. 3. 32 nor was she (her<BR> loss) regretted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुचिका
अनुशुचिका A ceremony enjoined by the Vedas (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोकः|अनुशोक
अनुशोकः, -शोचनम्<BR> Sorrow, repentance; regret; अनुशु(शो)चितम्<BR> in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचनम्
अनुशोकः, -शोचनम्<BR> Sorrow, repentance; regret; अनुशु(शो)चितम्<BR> in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचक
अनुशोचक, -शोचिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Regretful, penitent<BR>—2 Causing regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचिन्
अनुशोचक, -शोचिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Regretful, penitent<BR>—2 Causing regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्रु
अनुश्रु €5 P.<BR>—1 To hear (= श्रु) नानुशुश्रुम जात्वेतत् Ms. 9. 100;<BR> तद्यथानुश्रूयते Pt. 1 heard, related.<BR>—2 To hear repeatedly as from a sacred authority, hand down as by Vedic tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्रवः|अनुश्रव
अनुश्रवः Vedic or sacred tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्रविक
अनुश्रविक <i>a.</i> Known from the Śāstras; (Pātañjala Yogadarśana 1. 15)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्लोकम्
अनुश्लोकम् [अनुश्लोक्यते गीयते, श्लोक्, कर्मणि अच्] A Kind of Sāma<BR> (महाव्रतगेयः सामभेदः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषञ्ज्|अनुषंज्
अनुषञ्ज् (˚सञ्ज्) €1 P. To adhere or cling to, follow closely. ━<i>pass.</i> (-षज्यते)<BR>—1 To stick, cling, adhere to, be attached to (fig. also); धर्मपूते<BR> च मनसि नभसीव न जातु रजोऽनुषज्यते Dk. 43; sometimes occurring<BR> as अनुषज्जते (from सस्ज् also); यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते<BR> Bg. 6. 4, 18. 10,<BR>—2 To be supplied from a preceding rule or statement. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fasten or attach (something) to.<BR>—2 To supply (as an elliptical expression); इति पदमत्रानुषञ्जनीयम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषक्
अनुषक्, -ट् <i>adv.</i><BR> In continuous or close order, one after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषट्
अनुषक्, -ट् <i>adv.</i><BR> In continuous or close order, one after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषक्त
अनुषक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Connected with, closely related or attached to; नित्य˚क्तः प्रकृतिकोपः<BR> Mv. 2 constant, ever-arising.<BR>—2 Clinging or adhering to (actively used); मृत्युर्जरा च व्याधिश्च दुःखं<BR> चानेककारणम् । अनुषक्तं सदा देहे Mb.; हृदि नित्यानुषक्तेन सीताशोकेन<BR> तप्यते U. 4. 2 constantly preying on the heart; ˚मन्दाकिनीपवित्रमेखलम् Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गः|अनुषङ्ग|अनुषंग|अनुषंगः
अनुषङ्गः<BR>—1 Close adherence or attendance; connection, conjunction, association;<BR> तस्य वैरानुषङ्गस्य गन्ताऽस्म्यन्तं सुदुर्गमम् Mb. 5. 162. 35. सानुषङ्गाणि<BR> कल्याणानि U. 7 good things closely follow one another (come close upon one another).<BR>—2 Coalition, commixture.<BR>—3 Connection of word with word.<BR>—4 A word or words repeated from the context to supply an ellipsis. cf.<BR> अनुषङ्गश्च फलवचनमभविष्यत् ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 5.<BR>—5 Necessary consequence, inevitable result.<BR>—6 Connection of a subsequent with a previous act.<BR>—7 Incidental mention or relation (प्रसङ्ग).<BR>—8 Yearning, eager longing.<BR>—9 Compassion, pity, tenderness.<BR>—10 (In Nyāya) Connecting together the उपनय or application and<BR> निगमन or conclusion by the use of the pronoun इदं (उपनयवाक्यस्थस्य<BR> अयमिति पदस्य निगमनवाक्ये आकर्षणम्).<BR>—11 The nasals connected with certain roots ending in consonants; P. VII. 1. 59. Sk.<BR>—12 An ellipsis. A mode of interpreting an incomplete sentence by supplying<BR> the required word or words from the immediate context. This mode is admissible<BR> only if there is no break (व्यवाय). This corresponds to the principle<BR> known as अनुवृत्ति (in grammar) on which a word or expression from<BR> a preceding सूत्र is read in the succeeding सूत्र or सूत्रs.<BR> नानुषङ्गः प्राप्नुयात् । कुतः । व्यवायात् । ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिक|अनुषंगिक
अनुषङ्गिक <i>a.</i> Following as a necessary result, consequent; concomitant,<BR> adhering to, connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिन्|अनुषंगिन्
अनुषङ्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Connected with, adhering or sticking to; अनीकजे रजसि मुखानुषङ्गिणि Śi. 17. 57.<BR>—2 Following as a necessary consequence; यस्यानुषङ्गिण इमे भोगादयो<BR> भवन्ति Bh. 3. 76.<BR>—3 Related or applicable to, common, prevailing (अनुक्षणं प्रसक्त);<BR> सप्तकस्यास्य वर्गस्य सर्वत्रैवानुषङ्गिणः Ms. 7. 52; विभुतानुषङ्गि<BR> भयमेति जनः Ki. 6. 35 connected<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">Page0111-2</a>]<BR> with, natural to, greatness.<BR>—4 Addicted to, devoted or attached to, fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषञ्जनम्
अनुषञ्जनम् Concord, grammatical connection or agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषत्य
अनुषत्य <i>a.</i> Being conformable to truth; हविष्मन्तो अनुषत्यं<BR> स्वर्विदम् Rv. 3. 26. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषेकः|अनुषेक
अनुषेकः, -सेचनम्<BR> Rewatering, sprinkling over again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसेचनम्
अनुषेकः, -सेचनम्<BR> Rewatering, sprinkling over again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुतिः|अनुष्टुति
अनुष्टुतिः <i>f.</i> Praise (in due order).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ् €1 P. (˚स्तुभ्) To praise after, follow in praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ् <i>f.</i> [अनु निरन्तरम् स्तुभ्यतेऽनया अनुष्टुप् वाक्]<BR>—1 Following in praise; speech.<BR>—2 Sarasvatī.<BR>—3 N. of a class of metres consisting of four Pādas of 8 syllables each,<BR> the whole stanza consisting of 32 syllables (so called because it follows<BR> with its praise <i>i. e.</i> अनुष्टोभति the Gāyatrī, which has 3 Pādas),<BR> अनुष्टोभनादनुष्टुप्. In later metrical systems it stands as a general<BR> name for all metres which have 8 syllables in each foot (the highest possible<BR> number being computed to be 256); पञ्चमं लघु सर्वत्र सप्तमं द्विचतुर्थयोः ।<BR> गुरु षष्ठं च पादानां शेषेष्वनियमो मतः ॥ which rule is sometimes<BR> violated. अनुष्टुभा सोम उक्थैर्महस्वान् Rv. 10. 130. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठा
अनुष्ठा €1 U. (˚स्था) —1 To do, perform or carry out, execute, attend<BR> to (order, duty &c.); bring about, effect, accomplish (business); अनुतिष्ठसि<BR> धर्मेण ये चान्ये विदितास्त्वया Mb. 3. 267. 11. विवाहदीक्षाविधिमन्वतिष्ठत्<BR> Ku. 7. 1, 1. 17; किमनुतिष्ठति भगवान् मारीचः Ś. 7; आज्ञापयतु<BR> आर्यः को नियोगोऽनुष्ठीयतामिति Ś. 1; ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति<BR> मानवाः Bg. 3. 31 follow; गुरोर्वचनमनुतिष्ठ V. 5 do as your papa<BR> orders; अनुतिष्टस्वात्मनो नियोगम् M. 1<BR> look or attend to your own duty, do your business.<BR>—2 To follow, practise, observe (धर्म, व्रत &c.); commit (a sin).<BR>—3 To rule, govern, superintend; appoint.<BR>—4 To stand by or near (with loc.); तिष्ठन्तीष्वनुतिष्ठेत्तु व्रजन्तीष्वप्यनुव्रजेत्<BR> Ms. 11. 112; sit on; occupy; अनुष्ठास्यति रामस्य सीता प्रकृतमासनम् Rām.<BR>—5 To follow, go after (lit.); स्वकान्तामनुतिष्ठति Rām.; नाराजके<BR> पतिं भार्या यथावदनुतिष्ठति Subhāṣ.; follow, obey.<BR>—6 To imitate, tread in; पदं चेहानुतिष्ठन्ति पूर्वेषां पूर्वजैः कृतम् Bhāg.<BR>—7 (Intrans.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To place or put oneself on, be in a position, present oneself.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To remain, continue.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To be engaged in religious ceremonies (muttering prayers &c.);<BR> अनुतिष्ठतां ब्राह्मणानाम् M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठ
अनुष्ठ <i>a.</i> [स्था-क-षत्वम्] Standing after or in succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठा
अनुष्ठा <i>a.</i> Standing after, in succession; अभीमिन्द्रो नद्यो वव्रिणा<BR> हिता विश्वा अनुष्ठाः प्रवणेषु जिघ्नते Rv. 1. 54. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातृ
अनुष्ठातृ, -ष्ठायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Doing, performing, executing &c.; one who undertakes or begins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठायिन्
अनुष्ठातृ, -ष्ठायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Doing, performing, executing &c.; one who undertakes or begins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठानम्
अनुष्ठानम्<BR>—1 Doing, performance, practice, execution, accomplishment &c.; obeying,<BR> acting in conformity to; उपरुध्यते तपोऽनुष्ठानम् Ś. 4 practice<BR> of religious austerities; कोऽपि वधोपायश्चिन्त्यो यस्यानुष्ठानेन Pt. 1;<BR> नानुष्ठानैर्विहीनाः स्युः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">Page0112-1</a>]<BR> कुलजा विधवा इव Pt. 2. 95; धर्मे स्वयमनुष्ठानं कस्यचित्तु महात्मनः<BR> H. 1. 99; शास्त्रानुष्ठानं वा Kau. A. 1. 6.<BR>—2 Commencing, undertaking, engaging in; यदि समुद्रेण सह वैरानुष्ठानं<BR> कार्यम् Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Commencement or course of conduct, procedure, course of action; कथं<BR> न्याग्यमनुष्ठानं मादृशः प्रतिषेधतु U. 5. 21.<BR>—4 Practice of religious rites or ceremonies, any religious rite or ceremony;<BR> किंत्वनुष्ठाननित्यत्वं स्वातन्त्र्यमपकर्षति U. 1. 8; Mv. 4. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठानी
अनुष्ठानम् + .{@-नी@} Performance, doing &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुष्ठानशरीरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठानशरीरम्
अनुष्ठानम् + -शरीरम् ‘the body of action’; (according to the Sāṅkhya doctrine)<BR> the intermediate body between the सूक्ष्म or subtle and the स्थूल or gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठापक
अनुष्ठापक <i>a.</i> Causing to perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठापनम्
अनुष्ठापनम् Causing to do an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठायिन्
अनुष्ठायिन् <i>a.</i> Doing, performing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठित
अनुष्ठित <i>p. p.</i> Done, performed, accomplished &c.; practised,<BR> followed, &c.; वीराश्च नियतोत्साहा राजशास्त्रमनुष्ठिताः Rām. 1. 7. 12.<BR> विक्रियायै न कल्पन्ते संबन्धाः सदनुष्टिताः Ku. 6. 29 brought<BR> about; तथानुष्ठिते that being done, thereupon; begun, undertaken; न<BR> युक्तं हि त्यक्तुं कार्यमनुष्टितम् Rām. (used actively) following, practising; Ms. 10. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठिः|अनुष्ठि
अनुष्ठिः, -ष्ठुः <i>f.</i><BR> [स्था-कु] Proper order, succession (used only<BR> in instr.); ˚ष्ठु, अनुष्ठया, अनुष्टुया in proper order, duly, immediately,<BR> properly; immediate, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठुः|अनुष्ठु
अनुष्ठिः, -ष्ठुः <i>f.</i><BR> [स्था-कु] Proper order, succession (used only<BR> in instr.); ˚ष्ठु, अनुष्ठया, अनुष्टुया in proper order, duly, immediately,<BR> properly; immediate, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठेय
अनुष्ठेय, -ष्ठातव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be effected, performed; followed, done<BR> conformably to; विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयम् M. 5 what to do with. कस्मिंश्चिदाप्तजनानुष्ठेये<BR> कर्मणि त्वां व्यापारयितुमिच्छामि Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातव्य
अनुष्ठेय, -ष्ठातव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be effected, performed; followed, done<BR> conformably to; विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयम् M. 5 what to do with. कस्मिंश्चिदाप्तजनानुष्ठेये<BR> कर्मणि त्वां व्यापारयितुमिच्छामि Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ण|अनुष्णं|अनुष्णः
अनुष्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not hot, cold, chilly; अनुष्णैरानन्दाश्रुबिन्दुभिः R. 12. 62.<BR>—2 Apathetic; lazy, sluggish (अलस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णः|अनुष्ण|अनुष्णं
अनुष्ण + .{@-ष्णः@} Cold touch or sensation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णा
अनुष्ण + .{@-ष्णा@} N. of a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णम्
अनुष्ण + .{@-ष्णम्@} A water-lily, blue lotus (उत्पल).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनुष्णाशीत, अनुष्णगुः, अनुष्णवल्लिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णाशीत
अनुष्ण + -अशीत <i>a.</i> Neither hot nor cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णगुः|अनुष्णगु
अनुष्ण + -गुः + ({@-गो@} ray) having cold rays, the moon, also camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णगो
अनुष्ण + -गुः + ({@-गो@} ray) having cold rays, the moon, also camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्णवल्लिका
अनुष्ण + -वल्लिका N. of a plant नीलदूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्वध
अनुष्वध <i>a.</i> [स्वधामनु, स्वधया सहितः] Accompanied by food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्वधम्
अनुष्वध + .{@-धम्@} <i>adv.</i><BR>—1 Through or after food. —2 According to food; after every sacrifice.<BR>—3 Voluntarily, according to oneʼs will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्यन्दः|अनुष्यन्द|अनुष्यंदः
अनुष्यन्दः A hind wheel. Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंवरणम्
अनुसंवरणम् Concealing in order or succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंचर्|अनुसञ्चर्
अनुसंचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To walk alongside, follow, join.<BR>—2 To pursue, seek after.<BR>—3 To visit, go towards or to.<BR>—4 To penetrate, cross, traverse.<BR>—5 To become assimilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंचरणम्|अनुसञ्चरणम्
अनुसंचरणम् Following, pursuing. ━<i>adv.</i> At every occasion of coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंतन्|अनुसन्तन्
अनुसंतन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To extend everywhere; to diffuse, spread about, overspread. अधश्च<BR> मूलान्यनुसंततानि कर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके Bg. 15. 2.<BR>—2 To continue, join in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंततिः|अनुसन्तति
अनुसंततिः <i>f.</i> Continued succession, continuity; अनुसंततिपातिनः पटुताम् Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधा|अनुसन्धा
अनुसंधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To search into or after, look after, inquire into, investigate, explore,<BR> examine, ascertain; प्रसवयोग्यं स्थानमनुसंधीयताम् H. 3; यस्तर्केणानुसंधत्ते<BR> स धर्मं वेद नेतरः Ms. 12. 106.<BR>—2 To calm, compose, quiet; आत्मानमनुसंधेहि शोकचर्चां च परिहर H. 4.<BR>—3 To think of, aim at, refer or allude to, consider, deliberate; यथाकर्तव्यमनुसंधीयताम्<BR> H. 3; नैतदनुसंधाय मयोक्तम् Mv. 6 after deliberation, or because<BR> I aimed at it; अलमनेनातीतोपालम्भेन प्रस्तुतमनुसंधीयताम् H. 3<BR> let us consider what is before us, (turn to the matter in hand); अत्र …<BR> इति पुरावृत्तकथानुऽसंधेया Malli. on Ku. 1. 21 should be sought or referred to.<BR>—4 To plan, arrange; prepare, set in order; सारसत्वं दुर्गमनुसंधेहि,<BR> दुर्गशोधनमनुसंधातव्यम् H. 3.<BR>—5 To follow, go after, attend, accompany; चरेण अनुसंधीयमानः<BR> Mu. 6; कस्ते निर्बन्धः पदे पदे मामनुसंधातुम् Mk. 1; एतौ तौ मामनुसंधत्तः<BR> Mk. 2 are after me.<BR>—6 To take up, follow, continue; तच्छेषमात्मवचसाऽप्यनुसंदधानः<BR> K. 240 following, making up the unfinished portion &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधानम्
अनुसंधानम्<BR>—1 Inquiry, investigation; close inspection or scrutiny, examination; Mv. 7.<BR>—2 Aiming at. H.<BR>—3 Planning, arranging, getting ready &c.; दुर्गानुसंधाने को नियुज्यताम्<BR> H. 3 equipping with the necessary materials.<BR>—4 A plan, scheme.<BR>—5 Suitable connection.<BR>—6 (In the Vaiś. Phil.) The 4th step in a syllogism, the उपनय or application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधानिन्|अनुसन्धानिन्
अनुसंधानिन्, -संधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Investigating, looking after; skilful in concerting plans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधायिन्|अनुसन्धायिन्
अनुसंधानिन्, -संधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Investigating, looking after; skilful in concerting plans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंहित
अनुसंहित <i>p. p.</i> Inquired into, investigated; connected with,<BR> in accordance or union with, conformable to; अहिंसा सर्वधर्मानुसंहिता<BR> Mb.; अर्थधर्मानुसंहितं वाक्यम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंहितम्
अनुसंहित + .{@-तम्@} <i>adv.</i> In the Saṃhitā text; according to this text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमापनम्
अनुसमापनम् Regular completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमि
अनुसमि €2 P. (˚इ)<BR>—1 To go to or visit successively or in order.<BR>—2 To join in following or being guided by.<BR>—3 To join, become assimilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमयः|अनुसमय
अनुसमयः<BR>—1 Regular or proper connection, as of words.<BR>—2 Doing several details with reference to several things or persons.<BR> This can be done in more ways than one and hence we have three varieties<BR> of अनुसमय<BR>——(<i>a</i>) पदार्थानुसमय i. e. doing one thing with reference to all,<BR> then doing the second in the same way and so on.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) काण्डानुसमय i. e. doing the whole mass of details with<BR> reference to one thing first, then doing the same with the second and so<BR> on. This is also known as एकजातीयानुसमय.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) समुदायानुसमय i. e. doing a group of details forming a<BR> composite whole (समुदाय) with reference to one, then doing it with<BR> reference to the second and so on. It may be noted that when several details<BR> are to be performed with reference to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0113-1" target="_blank">Page0113-1</a>]<BR> one thing or person, the details are in close proximity with the प्रधान<BR> and hence the problem of अङ्गप्रधानप्रत्यासत्ति does not arise in<BR> such cases. But when several things are to be performed with respect to<BR> several things or persons, this अङ्गप्रधानप्रत्यासत्ति can be achieved<BR> by following the पदार्थानुसमय, which, therefore, is to be preferred<BR> to the other two words. (This is known as the पदार्थानुसमयन्याय.)<BR> But when पदार्थानुसमय is found not practicable, the second mode<BR> i. e. the काण्डानुसमय or एकजातीयानुसमय should be adopted,<BR> provided that among the details to be performed, there are none which<BR> together form a composite whole. (This is known as काण्डानुसमयन्याय.)<BR> If, however, there are among the details to be performed some details<BR> which form one or more composite wholes, they should be performed together<BR> with the first thing or person, then with the second, and so on. Thus<BR> in such cases the समुदायानुसमय should be adopted. (This is known<BR> as समुदायानुसमयन्याय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंबद्ध|अनुसम्बद्ध
अनुसंबद्ध <i>a.</i> Connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंसृतिः|अनुसंसृति
