अनुस्मृ
अनुस्मृ €1 P. To remember, think of, call to mind, recollect (with<BR> acc. or gen.); वरप्रार्थनामनुस्मृत्य Ś. 1; यदैव अनुस्मृतं देवेन<BR> Ś. 7. तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु मामनुस्मर युध्य च Bg. 8. 7; व्यपगतमदरागस्यानुसस्मार<BR> लक्ष्मीम् Ki. 4. 38.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To remind (painfully), cause to remember with regret; मुहुरनुस्मरयन्तमनुक्षपं<BR> त्रिपुरदाहमुमापतिसेविनः Ki. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्मरणम्
अनुस्मरणम्<BR>—1 Recollection, remembering.<BR>—2 Repeated recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्मृतिः|अनुस्मृति
अनुस्मृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cherished recollection; thinking of; अनुस्मृतेर्बादरिः Ś. B. 1. 2. 30.<BR>—2 Thinking of one thing to the exclusion of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्यूत
अनुस्यूत <i>a.</i> [सिव्-क्त-ऊठ्]<BR>—1 Woven together regularly and uninterruptedly.<BR>—2 Sewn on, fastened to.<BR>—3 Closely attached or linked to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वानः|अनुस्वान
अनुस्वानः<BR>—1 Sounding conformably to.<BR>—2 An after-sound; echo; see अनुरणन and K. P. 4 (36).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वारः|अनुस्वार
अनुस्वारः [स्वृ-अप् स्वराः; स्वरवर्णा एव स्वाराः, अनुगतः स्वारान्<BR> Tv.] The nasal sound which is marked by a dot above the line (.) and which<BR> always belongs to a preceding vowel; अनुनासिकात्परोऽनुस्वारः P. VIII. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वारव्यवायः|अनुस्वारव्यवाय
अनुस्वारः + .{@-व्यवायः@} Separation between two sounds caused by an अनुस्वार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहवः|अनुहव
अनुहवः Inviting, stirring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहुङ्कृ|अनुहुंकृ
अनुहुङ्कृ €8 U. To roar in imitation of, reply to; अनुहुङ्कुरुते घनध्वनिं<BR> न हि गोमायुरुतानि केसरी Śi. 16. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहुङ्कारः|अनुहुङ्कार
अनुहुङ्कारः Roaring in imitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहृ
अनुहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To imitate, resemble; देहबन्धेन स्वरेण च रामभद्रमनुहरति<BR> U. 4; व्रीडितस्य ललितं युवतीनां क्षीबता बहुगुणैरनुजह्ने Ki. 9. 67,<BR> sometimes with gen. of person; मातुरनुहरति Sk.; see below.<BR>—2 To take after (oneʼs parents), to always imitate their nature (Ā. in<BR> this sense) (गतताच्छील्ये); पैतृकमश्वा अनुहरन्ते मातृकं गावः<BR> P. I. 3. 21. Vārt.; (गतं प्रकारः, पितुर्मातुश्चागतं प्रकारं सततं<BR> परिशीलयन्ति Sk.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहरणम्
अनुहरणम्, -हारः<BR> Imitation, resemblance, similarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहारः|अनुहार
अनुहरणम्, -हारः<BR> Imitation, resemblance, similarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार्य|अनुहार्यः|अनुहार्य्य
अनुहार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be imitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार्यः|अनुहार्य|अनुहार्य्य
अनुहार्य + .{@-र्यः@} Monthly obsequies on the Darśa or new moon day (cf. अन्वाहार्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहोडः|अनुहोड
अनुहोडः A cart (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूकः|अनूक|अनूकं
अनूकः, -कम्<BR> [अनु-उच् समवाये क निपातः कुत्वम्; or fr. अञ्च् with अनु]<BR>—1 the back-bone, spine (वङ्कयाधारः आयतः पृष्ठास्थिविशेषः); सदं<BR> चानूकं च गृहपतेः Ait. Br. (where<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">Page0114-2</a>]<BR> Sāy. remarks अनूकं मूत्रवास्तिः स्यात् सास्नेत्येके वदन्ति च).<BR>—2 A kind of sacrificial vessel; according to some, the back part of the<BR> altar; अयुग्मागणमध्यमानूके.<BR>—3 Former birth or state of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूकम्
अनूकः, -कम्<BR> [अनु-उच् समवाये क निपातः कुत्वम्; or fr. अञ्च् with अनु]<BR>—1 the back-bone, spine (वङ्कयाधारः आयतः पृष्ठास्थिविशेषः); सदं<BR> चानूकं च गृहपतेः Ait. Br. (where<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">Page0114-2</a>]<BR> Sāy. remarks अनूकं मूत्रवास्तिः स्यात् सास्नेत्येके वदन्ति च).<BR>—2 A kind of sacrificial vessel; according to some, the back part of the<BR> altar; अयुग्मागणमध्यमानूके.<BR>—3 Former birth or state of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूकम्
अनूकः, -कम् + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Family, race.<BR>—2 Disposition, temperament; character, peculiarity of race; व्याधर्क्षनकुलानूकैः<BR> पैत्तिका हि नराः स्मृताः Suśr. cf. अनूकमस्त्रियां वंशे शीले च गतजन्मनि Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूका
अनूकः, -कम् + .{@-का@} <i>f.</i> N. of an Apsaras; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्यम्
अनूक्यम् Backbone; ग्रीवाभ्यस्त उष्णिहाभ्यः कीकसाभ्यो अनूक्यात् Rv. 10. 163. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूकाशः|अनूकाश
अनूकाशः [अनु-काश्-घञ् उपसर्गस्य दीर्घत्वम्]<BR>—1 Reflection (of light).<BR>—2 Regard, reference, illustration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्ति|अनूक्तिः
अनूक्ति, अनूचान &c. See under अनुवच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूक्ति, अनूचान &c. See under अनुवच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचीन
अनूचीन <i>a.</i> [अन्वञ्च्-ख] Ved. Coming after, successive; अनूचीना<BR> जीविता मानुषेभ्यः Rv. 4. 54. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचीनाहम्
अनूचीन + ˚अहम् day after day, on the following<BR> day;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचीनगर्भ
अनूचीन + ˚गर्भ (गो) born in successive order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्यम्
अनूच्यम् The plank or board on the side of a bed (दक्षिणोत्तरयोर्दीर्घे<BR> खट्वाङ्गे अनूच्यसंज्ञे Śaṅkara.); अरत्निमात्राणि शीर्षण्यान्यनूच्यानि<BR> Ait. Br.; (अनूच्ये = पार्श्वद्वयवर्तिनी फलके Sāy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूज्जि
अनूज्जि Ved. To be victorious after अग्नीषोमयोरुज्जितिमनूज्जेषम् Vāj. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढ|अनूढः
अनूढ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not borne or carried.<BR>—2 Unmarried; परिवेत्तानुजोऽनूढे ज्येष्ठे दारपरिग्रहात् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढा
अनूढ + .{@-ढा@} An unmarried woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनूढमान, अनूढागमनम्, अनूढाभ्रातृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढमान
अनूढ + -मान <i>a.</i> bashful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढागमनम्
अनूढ + -गमनम् (˚ढा˚) Fornication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढाभ्रातृ
अनूढ + -भ्रातृ <i>m.</i> (˚ढा˚)<BR>—1 the brother of an unmarried woman<BR>—2 the brother of the concubine of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूतिः|अनूति
अनूतिः <i>f.</i> [वे-क्तिन्, न˚ त˚] Not coming or going (to<BR> aid) (अनागमनम्) अनूती हिरिशिप्रः सत्वा Rv. 6. 29. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदकम्
अनूदकम् Want of water; drought, aridity यथा वर्षमनूदके Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्देशः|अनूद्देश
अनूद्देशः Describing, mentioning according to or conformably with.<BR> S. D. X. 79. यथासङ्ख्यमनूद्देश उद्दिष्टांना कमेण यत् S. D. 732.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्य|अनूद्यं
अनूद्य, अनूदित &c. See under अनुवद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदित
अनूद्य, अनूदित &c. See under अनुवद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनून|अनूनं
अनून <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not inferior, not less (with abl. expressed or understood); not wanting<BR> or lacking in (with instr.); वृन्दावने चैत्ररथादनूने R. 6. 50; अनूनसारं<BR> निषधान्नगेन्द्रात् 18. 1; आकृतिप्रत्ययादेनामनूनवस्तुकां संभावयामि<BR> M. 1 of no inferior stuff; इमामनूनां सुरभेरवेहि R. 2. 54; गुणैरनूनाम् 6. 37;<BR> किंचिदूनमनूनर्धेः R. 10. 1.<BR>—2 Full, whole, entire; large; महर्षभस्कन्धमनूनकन्धरम् Ki. 14. 40;<BR> great; Śi. 4. 11; (before adjectives) very; ˚गुरुर्नितम्बः S. D.<BR> excessively big or heavy.<BR>—3 Having full power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप|अनूपं|अनूपः
अनूप <i>a.</i> [अनु-अप् ऊदनोर्देशे P. VI. 3. 98, अनुगताः आपः<BR> यास्मिन्] Situated near water, watery, rich or abounding in water, wet,<BR> marshy. जलप्रायमनूपं स्यात्पुंसि कच्छस्तथाविधः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">Page0115-1</a>]<BR> Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपः|अनूप|अनूपं
अनूप + .{@-पः, -पम्@}<BR>—1 A watery place or country; स्यन्दनाश्वैः समे युध्येदनूपे नौद्विपैस्तथा<BR> Ms. 7. 192; Y. 3. 42; शौरेरूपानूपमपाहरन्मनः Śi. 12. 44. नानाद्रुमलतावीरुन्निर्झरप्रांतशीतलैः ।<BR> वनैर्व्याप्तमनूपं तत्सस्यैर्व्रीहियवादिभिः<BR>—2 N. of a particular country<BR>.(-पाः pl.); तामग्रतः अनूपराजस्य विधाय R. 6. 37.<BR>—3 A marsh, bog.<BR>—4 A pond or tank of water.<BR>—5 Bank or side (of a river, mountain); सागरात्पर्वतानूपात् Rām.;<BR> नदीं गोयुतानूपाम् अतरत् <i>ibid.</i><BR>—6 A buffalo.<BR>—7 A frog.<BR>—8 A kind of partridge.<BR>—9 An elephant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनूपजम्, अनूपप्राय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपम्
अनूप + .{@-पः, -पम्@}<BR>—1 A watery place or country; स्यन्दनाश्वैः समे युध्येदनूपे नौद्विपैस्तथा<BR> Ms. 7. 192; Y. 3. 42; शौरेरूपानूपमपाहरन्मनः Śi. 12. 44. नानाद्रुमलतावीरुन्निर्झरप्रांतशीतलैः ।<BR> वनैर्व्याप्तमनूपं तत्सस्यैर्व्रीहियवादिभिः<BR>—2 N. of a particular country<BR>.(-पाः pl.); तामग्रतः अनूपराजस्य विधाय R. 6. 37.<BR>—3 A marsh, bog.<BR>—4 A pond or tank of water.<BR>—5 Bank or side (of a river, mountain); सागरात्पर्वतानूपात् Rām.;<BR> नदीं गोयुतानूपाम् अतरत् <i>ibid.</i><BR>—6 A buffalo.<BR>—7 A frog.<BR>—8 A kind of partridge.<BR>—9 An elephant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनूपजम्, अनूपप्राय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपजम्
अनूप + -जम् moist ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपप्राय
अनूप + -प्राय <i>a.</i> marshy, boggy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप्य
अनूप्य <i>a.</i> [अनूपे देशे भवः, यत्] Being in a pond or bog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूबन्ध्य|अनूबंध्य
अनूबन्ध्य <i>a.</i> Ved. To be fastened as a sacrificial animal; वशामनुबन्ध्यामालभेत<BR> Śat. Br.; अनुबन्ध्ययेष्ट्वा Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूयाज
अनूयाज, अनूराध = अनुयाज, अनुराध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूराध
अनूयाज, अनूराध = अनुयाज, अनुराध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरु|अनूरुः
अनूरु <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Thighless. अपूर्णाण्डाविनिर्भेदादनूरुररुणो<BR> ऽभवत् Bm. 1. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरुः|अनूरु
अनूरु + .{@-रुः@} Aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun (who is represented as<BR> having no thighs); the dawn; see अरुण.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनूरुसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरुसारथिः|अनूरुसारथि
अनूरु + -सारथिः the sun (having अनूरु for his charioteer); गतं<BR> तिरश्चीनमनूरुसारथेः Śi. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्जित
अनूर्जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not strong, weak, powerless.<BR>—2 Free from pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्ध्व
अनूर्ध्व <i>a.</i> Not high, low;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्ध्वभास्
अनूर्ध्व + ˚भास् Ved. whose splendour does<BR> not rise, who lights no (sacred) fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्मि
अनूर्मि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not waving, unruffled by waves, not fluctuating.<BR>—2 Inviolable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूला
अनूला N. of a river in Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूवृज्
अनूवृज् <i>m.</i> Ved. A part of the body near the ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूषर
अनूषर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Saline, the same as ऊषर; cf. उत्तम and अनुत्तम.<BR>—2 Not saline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूह
अनूह <i>a.</i> Thoughtless, careless. बलिं हरन्तोऽन्नमदन्त्यनूहाः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृक्क
अनृक्क <i>a.</i> See अनृच् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृक्षर
अनृक्षर <i>a.</i> Ved. Thornless (as a path or couch). अनृक्षरा ऋजवः<BR> सन्तु पन्थाः Rv. 10. 85. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृच्
अनृच्, -च <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Without a hymn, not containing a verse from the Ṛgveda; अनृक् साम<BR> P. V. 4. 74. Sk.<BR>—2 [नास्ति ऋक् अभ्यस्ततया यस्य अच् समासः] Not conversant with, not<BR> studying the Ṛgveda, one not invested with the sacred thread and hence<BR> not yet entitled to study the Vedas (as a body); द्विवेदाश्चैकवेदाश्चाप्यनृचश्च<BR> तथापरे Mb. 3. 149. 28. यथा चाज्ञेऽफलं दानं तथा विप्रो ऽनृचोऽफलः<BR> Ms. 2. 158; अनृचो माणवकः Mugdha. (In this case the form should<BR> properly be अनृच; अनृचबह्वृचावध्येतर्येव Sk.; but sometimes अनृच्<BR> also in the same sense; cf. तथाऽनृचे हविर्दत्वा न दाता लभते फलम्<BR> Ms. 3. 142; सहस्रं हि सहस्राणामनृचां यत्र भुञ्जते 131); अनृक्क<BR> also in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृच
अनृच्, -च <i>a.</i><BR> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Without a hymn, not containing a verse from the Ṛgveda; अनृक् साम<BR> P. V. 4. 74. Sk.<BR>—2 [नास्ति ऋक् अभ्यस्ततया यस्य अच् समासः] Not conversant with, not<BR> studying the Ṛgveda, one not invested with the sacred thread and hence<BR> not yet entitled to study the Vedas (as a body); द्विवेदाश्चैकवेदाश्चाप्यनृचश्च<BR> तथापरे Mb. 3. 149. 28. यथा चाज्ञेऽफलं दानं तथा विप्रो ऽनृचोऽफलः<BR> Ms. 2. 158; अनृचो माणवकः Mugdha. (In this case the form should<BR> properly be अनृच; अनृचबह्वृचावध्येतर्येव Sk.; but sometimes अनृच्<BR> also in the same sense; cf. तथाऽनृचे हविर्दत्वा न दाता लभते फलम्<BR> Ms. 3. 142; सहस्रं हि सहस्राणामनृचां यत्र भुञ्जते 131); अनृक्क<BR> also in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृजु|अनृजुः
अनृजु <i>a.</i> Not straight, crooked; (fig.) unfair, wicked, dishonest;<BR> न पाणिपादचपलो न नेत्रचपलोऽनृजुः Ms. 4. 177; P. V. 2. 75. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृण
अनृण <i>a.</i> Free from debt, who has paid off the debt (due to another)<BR> with gen. of person or thing; एनामनृणां करोमि Ś. 1; तत्रानृणास्मि<BR> U. 7; प्राणैर्दशरथप्रीतेरनृणम् (गृध्रम्) R. 12. 54; Mv. 5. 58;<BR> पितॄणामनृणः Ms. 9. 106, 6. 94. Every one that is born has three<BR> debts to pay off:− to Sages, Gods, and the Manes; cf. जायमानो वै ब्राह्मणस्त्रिभिरृणैर्वा<BR> जायते ब्रह्मचर्येणार्षिभ्यः, यज्ञेन देवेभ्यः, प्रजया पितृभ्यः; he,<BR> therefore, who learns the Vedas, offers sacrifices to Gods, and begets<BR> a son, becomes अनृण (free form debt); एष वानृणः यः पुत्री यज्वा<BR> ब्रह्मचारीवासी; cf. also ऋषिदेवगणस्वधाभुजां श्रुतयागप्रसवैः स<BR> पार्थिवः । अनृणत्वमुपेयिवान्बभौ परिधेर्मुक्त इवोष्णदीधितिः ॥ R. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृणता
अनृणता, आनृण्यम्<BR> Freedom from debt; ˚ताकृत्येनापकारं करिष्यामि Pt. 5<BR> do harm by way of retaliation or injury; भर्तृप्रियः प्रियैर्भर्तुरानृण्यमसुभिर्गतः<BR> M. 5. 11; येन स्वामिप्रसादस्य अनृणतां गच्छामः Pt. 1 repay or requite<BR> the favour of our lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्यम्
अनृणता, आनृण्यम्<BR> Freedom from debt; ˚ताकृत्येनापकारं करिष्यामि Pt. 5<BR> do harm by way of retaliation or injury; भर्तृप्रियः प्रियैर्भर्तुरानृण्यमसुभिर्गतः<BR> M. 5. 11; येन स्वामिप्रसादस्य अनृणतां गच्छामः Pt. 1 repay or requite<BR> the favour of our lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृणिन्
अनृणिन् <i>a.</i> = अनृण; एकमप्यक्षरं यस्तु गुरुः शिष्ये निवेदयेत् ।<BR> पृथिव्यां नास्ति तद् द्रव्यं यद् दत्वा सोऽनृणी भवेत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृत|अनृतं
अनृत <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Not true, false (words); ˚तं धनम् Ms. 4. 170 wrongly got; प्रियं<BR> च नानृतं ब्रूयात् 4. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतम्
अनृत + .{@-तम्@} Falsehood, lying, cheating; deception, fraud; सत्यानृते<BR> अवपश्यञ्जनानाम् Rv. 7. 49. 3; अनृतं जीवितस्यार्थे वदन्न स्पृश्यतेऽनृतैः<BR> Mb. 7. 190. 47, 1. 74. 105, 8. 69. 65. ऋतानृते Ms. 1. 29; साक्ष्येऽनृतं<BR> वदन् 8. 97; oft. in comp.; पशु˚, भूमि˚, गो˚, पुरुष˚ giving false<BR> evidence in the matter of &c.; Ms. 9. 71; cf. also: पञ्च कन्यानृते<BR> हन्ति दश हन्ति गवानृते । शतमश्वानृते हन्ति सहस्रं पुरुषानृते ॥<BR> Pt. 3. 108. अनृत personified is the son of अधर्म and हिंसा,<BR> husband and brother of निकृति, father of भय, नरक, माया and<BR> वेदना. V. P.<BR>—2 Agriculture ‘सेवाश्ववृत्तिरनृतं कृषिः’ इति कोशात्; आमिषं यच्च पूर्वेषां<BR> राजसं च मलं भृशम् । अनृतं नाम तद् भूतं क्षिप्तेन पृथिवीतले ॥<BR> Rām. 7. 74. 16. (opp. सत्य); Occupation of a Vaiśya (वाणिज्य);<BR> सत्यानृतं तु वाणिज्यं तेन चैवापि जीव्यते Ms. 4. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनृतदेव, अनृतवदनम्, अनृतभाषणम्, अनृताख्यानम्, अनृतवादिन्, अनृतवाच्, अनृतव्रत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतदेव
अनृत + -देव <i>a.</i> whose gods are not true (Sāy.); यदि वाहमनृतदेव<BR> आस Rv. 7. 104. 14; not playing fairly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवदनम्
अनृत + -वदनम्, -भाषणम्, -आख्यानम् lying, falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतभाषणम्
अनृत + -वदनम्, -भाषणम्, -आख्यानम् lying, falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृताख्यानम्
अनृत + -वदनम्, -भाषणम्, -आख्यानम् lying, falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवादिन्
अनृत + -वादिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> a liar. उद्विजन्ते यथा सर्पान्नरादनृतवादिनः<BR> Rām. 2. 109. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवाच्
अनृत + -वादिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> a liar. उद्विजन्ते यथा सर्पान्नरादनृतवादिनः<BR> Rām. 2. 109. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतव्रत
अनृत + -व्रत <i>a.</i> false to oneʼs vows or promises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतक
अनृत(ति)क, अनृतिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Lying, a liar. नैवाव्रतो नानृतिको न हिंस्रः Bu. C. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतिक
अनृत(ति)क, अनृतिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Lying, a liar. नैवाव्रतो नानृतिको न हिंस्रः Bu. C. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतिन्
अनृत(ति)क, अनृतिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Lying, a liar. नैवाव्रतो नानृतिको न हिंस्रः Bu. C. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतुः|अनृतु
अनृतुः [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unfit season, improper or premature time; अनृतौ चाभ्रदर्शने Ms. 4. 104.<BR>—2 Time before menstruation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनृतुकन्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतुकन्या
अनृतुः + -कन्या a girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेक|अनेकं
अनेक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not one; more than one, many; अनेकपितृकाणां तु पितृतो भागकल्पना<BR> Y. 2. 120, अनेकराजन्यरथाश्वसंकुलम् Ki. 1. 16; several, various;<BR> तथात्मैकोऽप्यनेकश्च Y. 3. 144.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">Page0116-1</a>]<BR>—2 Separated; divided; oft. in comp.; ˚आकार having many shapes or<BR> forms; diverse, multiform; ˚कालम् -वारम् several times, many a time<BR> and oft.; ˚भार्य having more wives than one.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनेकाक्षर, अनेकाच्, अनेकाग्र, अनेकान्त, अनेकार्थ, अनेकाल्, अनेकाश्रय, अनेकाश्रित, अनेककृत्, अनेकगुण, अनेकगुप्तः, अनेकगोत्र, अनेकचर, अनेकचित्त, अनेकज, अनेकपः, अनेकपद, अनेकभार्य, अनेकमुख, अनेकमूर्तिः, अनेकयुद्धविजयिन्, अनेकविजयिन्, अनेकरूप, अनेकलोचनः, अनेकवचनम्, अनेकवर्ण, अनेकविध, अनेकशफ, अनेकशब्द, अनेकसाधारण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाक्षर
अनेक + -अक्षर, -अच् <i>a.</i> having more than one vowel or syllable; polysyllabic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाच्
अनेक + -अक्षर, -अच् <i>a.</i> having more than one vowel or syllable; polysyllabic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाग्र
अनेक + -अग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 engaged in several pursuits.<BR>—2 not concentrated or fixed on one object.<BR>—3 Agitated, perplexed^1; स त्वनेकाग्रहृदयो द्वास्थं प्रत्यर्च्य तं जनम्<BR> Rām. 2. 41. 34.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकान्त|अनेकान्तः
अनेक + -अन्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 [न˚ ब˚] not alone so as to exclude all others, uncertain,<BR> doubtful, variable; स्यादित्यव्ययमनेकान्तवाचकम्<BR>—2 = अनैकान्तिक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकान्तः|अनेकान्त
अनेक + -अन्त + ({@-न्तः@})<BR>—1 unsettled condition, absence of permanence.<BR>—2 uncertainty, doubtfulness.<BR>—3 an unessential part, as the several <i>anubandhas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकान्तवादः|अनेकान्तवाद
अनेक + -अन्त + ˚वादः scepticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकान्तवादिन्
अनेक + -अन्त + ˚वादिन् <i>m.</i> a sceptic, a Jaina or an Arhat of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकार्थ|अनेकार्थः
अनेक + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having many (more than one) meanings, homonymous; as the words गो,<BR> अमृत, अक्ष &c.; ˚त्वम् Capacity to express more senses than one;<BR> अनेकार्थत्वमन्याय्यम् ŚB. on MS. 7. 3. 55. अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्य K. P. 2.<BR>—2 having the sense of the word अनेक.<BR>—3 having many objects or purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकार्थः|अनेकार्थ
अनेक + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@}) multiplicity of objects, topics &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाल्
अनेक + -अल् <i>a.</i> having more than one अल् (letter) P. I. 1. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाश्रय
अनेक + -आश्रय, -आश्रित <i>a.</i> (in Vaiś. Phil.) dwelling or abiding<BR> in more than one (such as संयोग, सामान्य); एतेऽनेकाश्रिता गुणाः<BR> Bhāṣā P.; dependence upon more than one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाश्रित
अनेक + -आश्रय, -आश्रित <i>a.</i> (in Vaiś. Phil.) dwelling or abiding<BR> in more than one (such as संयोग, सामान्य); एतेऽनेकाश्रिता गुणाः<BR> Bhāṣā P.; dependence upon more than one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेककृत्
अनेक + -कृत् <i>m.</i> ‘doing much’, N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकगुण
अनेक + -गुण <i>a.</i> of many kinds, manifold, diverse; विगणय्य कारणमनेकगुणम् Ki. 6. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकगुप्तः
अनेक + -गुप्तः N. of a king; ˚अर्चितपादपङ्कजः K. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकगोत्र
अनेक + -गोत्र <i>a.</i> belonging to two families (such as a boy when adopted)<BR> <i>i. e.</i> that of his own, and that of his adoptive father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकचर
अनेक + -चर <i>a.</i> gregarious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकचित्त
अनेक + -चित्त <i>a.</i> not of one mind, fickle-minded; कच्चिन्नानेकचित्तानां<BR> तेषां त्वं वशमागतः Rām. 6. 24. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकचित्तमन्त्रः|अनेकचित्तमन्त्र
अनेक + -चित्त + ˚मन्त्रः not following the<BR> counsels of one; H. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकज|अनेकजः
अनेक + -ज <i>a.</i> born more than once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकजः|अनेकज
अनेक + -ज + .({@-जः@}) a bird (गर्भाण्डाभ्यां जातत्वात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकपः|अनेकप
अनेक + -पः an elephant (so called because he drinks with his trunk and<BR> mouth); cf. द्विप; वन्येतरानेकपदर्शनेन R. 5. 47; Śi. 5. 35, 12. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकपद
अनेक + -पद <i>a.</i> multi-numbered; having many component members (as<BR> in a Bahuvrīhi compound). e. g. बृहद् अस्य रथन्तरसाम इति बृहद्रथन्तरसामा<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकभार्य
अनेक + -भार्य <i>a.</i> Having more wives than one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकमुख
अनेक + -मुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 having many faces, many-faced.<BR>—2 scattered, dispersed, going in various directions, taking to various<BR> ways; (बलानि) जगाहिरेऽनेकमुखानि मार्गान् Bk. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकमूर्तिः|अनेकमूर्ति|अनेकमूर्त्ति
अनेक + -मूर्तिः ‘having many forms’, N. of Viṣṇu who assumed various<BR> forms to deliver the earth from calamities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकयुद्धविजयिन्
अनेक + -युद्धविजयिन्, -विजयिन् <i>a.</i> victorious in many battles; Pt. 3. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकविजयिन्
अनेक + -युद्धविजयिन्, -विजयिन् <i>a.</i> victorious in many battles; Pt. 3. 9, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकरूप|अनेकरूपः
अनेक + -रूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of various forms, multiform.<BR>—2 of various kinds or sorts.<BR>—3 fickle, changeable, of a varying nature; वेश्याङ्गनेव नृपनीतिरनेकरूपा Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकरूपः|अनेकरूप
अनेक + -रूप + .({@-पः@}) epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकलोचनः|अनेकलोचन
अनेक + -लोचनः N. of Śiva; also of Indra, and of the Supreme Being,<BR> he being said to be सहस्राक्षः सहस्रपात् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवचनम्
अनेक + -वचनम् the plural number; dual also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवर्ण
अनेक + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> involving more than one (unknown) quantity<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">Page0116-2</a>]<BR> (the unknown quantities <i>x</i>. <i>y</i>. <i>z</i>. &c. being represented in Sanskrit<BR> by colours नील, काल &c.);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवर्णसमीकरणम्
अनेक + -वर्ण + ˚समीकरणम् simultaneous equation;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवर्णगुणनम्
अनेक + -वर्ण + ˚गुणनम्, ˚व्यवकलनम्, ˚हारः multiplication, subtraction or division<BR> of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवर्णव्यकलनम्
अनेक + -वर्ण + ˚गुणनम्, ˚व्यवकलनम्, ˚हारः multiplication, subtraction or division<BR> of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकवर्णहारः|अनेकवर्णहार
अनेक + -वर्ण + ˚गुणनम्, ˚व्यवकलनम्, ˚हारः multiplication, subtraction or division<BR> of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकविध
अनेक + -विध <i>a.</i> various, different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकशफ
अनेक + -शफ <i>a.</i> cloven-hoofed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकशब्द
अनेक + -शब्द <i>a.</i> synonymous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकसाधारण
अनेक + -साधारण <i>a.</i> common to many, the common property of many persons Dk. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकधा
अनेकधा <i>ind.</i> In various ways, variously; जगत्कृत्स्नं प्रविभक्तमनेकधा Bg. 11. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकशः|अनेकश
अनेकशः <i>ind.</i> [वीप्सार्थे कारके शस्]<BR>—1 Several or many times, frequently; अनेकशो निर्जितराजकस्त्वम् Bk. 2. 52.<BR>—2 In various ways or manners.<BR>—3 In large numbers or quantities; पुत्रा अनेकशो मृता दाराश्च H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाकिन्
अनेकाकिन् <i>a.</i> Not alone, accompanied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेजत्|अनेजन्त्
अनेजत् <i>a.</i> [न एजत्] Not moving, immovable; of the same form,<BR> epithet of Brahman or the Supreme Soul (सर्वदैकरूपं ब्रह्म) अनेजदेकं<BR> मनसो जवीयः Īśop. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकीकृ
अनेकीकृ or भू To make or be manifold; to divide or be divided into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकीभू
अनेकीकृ or भू To make or be manifold; to divide or be divided into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेडः|अनेड
अनेडः A foolish or stupid person, dolt, fool.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अनेडमूक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेडमूक|अनेडमूकः
अनेडः + -मूक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deaf and dumb; ˚मूकताद्यैश्च द्यतु दोषैरसंमतान् K. P. 7.<BR>—2 blind. cf. अन्धेऽप्यनेडमूकः स्यात् Nm.<BR>—3 dishonest, fraudulent, wicked, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेद्य
अनेद्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not to be blamed; praiseworthy, chief (प्रशस्त, प्रधान).<BR>—2 Not near; infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेन|अनेनः
अनेन <i>a.</i> Sinless, faultless (Sāy.); without a variegated set<BR> (of horses); अनेनो वो मरुतो यामो अस्तु Rv. 6. 66. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनस्
अनेनस् <i>a.</i> Sinless, blameless; not liable to error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनः|अनेन
अनेनः ‘One who has no superior’, a sovereign or paramount lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेमन्
अनेमन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेव
अनेव <i>ind.</i> Otherwise; एवानेवाव सा गरत् Av. 16. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेहस्
अनेहस् <i>a.</i> [न हन्यते, हन्-असि, धातोः एहादेशः नञि हन् एह<BR> च Uṇ. 4. 223] (lit.) Not killed or destroyed or obstructed; Ved. without<BR> a rival, incomparable, unattainable, inaccessible; unobstructed, not liable<BR> to be hurt or injured; शंभुवं मन्त्रं देवा अनेहसम् Rv. 1. 40. 6, 4, 6. 50. 3.<BR>━<i>m.</i> (हा-हसौ &c.) Time (not being liable to be<BR> destroyed). cf. तस्मादनेहसं कंचित्प्रतीक्षस्व महाभुज Śiva B. 9. 18<BR> also 5. 11, 59. कुसुमबाणसखेन सुखासितं विपिनमापि न मानमनेहसा<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त|अनैकांत
अनैकान्त <i>a.</i> Variable, uncertain, unsteady; occasional, casual<BR> (as a cause not invariably attended by the same effects.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्तिक|अनैकांतिक
अनैकान्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Unsteady, uncertain; not to the point, not very important; भृत्योऽभृत्य<BR> इति ˚कमेतत् Pt. 1.<BR>—2 (in Logic) Name of one of the five main divisions of हेत्वाभास<BR> (fallacies), otherwise called<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">Page0117-1</a>]<BR> सव्यभिचार. It is of three kinds:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) साधारण, where the हेतु is found both in the सपक्ष,<BR> and विपक्ष, the argument being therefore too general.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) असाधारण where the हेतु is in the पक्ष alone, the<BR> argument being not general enough.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) अनुपसंहारी which embraces every known thing in the पक्ष,<BR> the argument being non-conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैक्यम्
अनैक्यम्<BR>—1 Existence of many; absence of one, plurality.<BR>—2 Want of union, confusion, disorder, anarchy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त्यम्
अनैकान्त्यम् Variable nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैतिह्यम्
अनैतिह्यम् Absence of traditional sanction or authority, or that which<BR> is without such sanction; अनागतमनैतिह्यं कथं ब्रह्माधिगच्छति Mb. 12. 239. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनो
अनो <i>ind.</i> No, not; अभावे न ह्यनो नापि Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकशायिन्
अनोकशायिन् <i>m.</i> (-यी) Not sleeping in house, a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकह|अनोकहः
अनोकह <i>a.</i> [अन्-ओकस्-हा] Not leaving the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकहः|अनोकह
अनोकह + .{@-हः@} [अनसः शकटस्य अकं गतिं हन्ति, हन्, -ड] A tree;<BR> अनोकहाकम्पितपुष्पगन्धी R. 2. 13, 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोङ्कृत|अनोंकृत
अनोङ्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not attended with the sacred syllable ओम्. ब्रह्मणः प्रणवं<BR> कुर्यादादावन्ते च सवदा । स्रवत्यनोङ्कृतं पूर्वं परस्ताच्च विशीर्यति ॥<BR> Ms. 2. 74.<BR>—2 Not accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोदन
अनोदन <i>a.</i> Without food (as a व्रत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोवाह्य
अनोवाह्य <i>a.</i> To be carried in a carriage (अनसा वाह्यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौचित्यम्
अनौचित्यम् Unfitness, impropriety; अनौचित्यादृते नान्यद्रसभङ्गस्य<BR> कारणम् K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौजस्यम्
अनौजस्यम् Want of vigour, energy, or strength; S. D. thus defines<BR> it; दौर्गत्याद्यैरनौजस्यं दैन्यं मलिनतादिकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौद्धत्यम्
अनौद्धत्यम्<BR>—1 Freedom from pride, modesty, humility.<BR>—2 Tranquility, placidity, calmness; नदीरनौद्धत्यमपङ्कता महीम् Ki. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौरस
अनौरस <i>a.</i> Not legitimate, not oneʼs own, adopted (as a son).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्|अत्|अंत्
अन्त् €1 P. (अन्तति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त <i>a.</i> [अम्-तन् Uṇ. 3. 86]<BR>—1 Near.<BR>—2 Last.<BR>—3 Handsome, lovely; Me. 23; दन्तोज्ज्वलासु विमलोपलमेखलान्ताः Śi. 4. 40,<BR> (where, however, the ordinary sense of ‘border’ or ‘skirt’ may<BR> do as well, though Malli. renders अन्त by रम्य, quoting the authority<BR> of शब्दार्णव− ‘मृताववसिते रम्ये समाप्तावन्त इष्यते’).<BR>—4 Lowest, worst. —5 Youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तः|अन्त|अंत|अन्तं
अन्त + .{@-तः@} (<i>n.</i> in some senses)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) End, limit, boundary (in time or space); final limit, last or<BR> extreme point; स सागरान्तां पृथिवीं प्रशास्ति H. 4. 50 bounded by<BR> the ocean, as far as the sea; अपाङ्गौ नेत्रयोरन्तौ Ak.; उद्युक्तो विद्यान्तमधिगच्छति<BR> H. 3. 114 goes to the end of, masters completely; श्रुतस्य यायादयमन्तमर्भकस्तथा<BR> परेषां युधि चेति पार्थिवः (where अन्त also means end or destruction);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-2" target="_blank">Page0117-2</a>]<BR> जीवलोकसुखानामन्तं ययौ K. 59 enjoyed all worldly pleasures; आलोकितः<BR> खलु रमणीयानामन्तः K. 124 end, furthest extremity; दिगन्ते श्रूयन्ते Bv. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Skirt, border, edge, precinct; a place or ground in general; यत्र<BR> रम्यो वनान्तः U. 2. 25 forest ground, skirts of the forest; ओदकान्तात्<BR> स्निग्धो जनोऽनुगन्तव्यः Ś. 4; उपवनान्तलताः R. 9. 35 as far as<BR> the borders or skirts; वृत्तः स नौ संगतयोर्वनान्ते R. 2. 58, 2. 19;<BR> Me. 23. Upper part (शिरोभाग); महार्हमुक्तामणिभूषितान्तम्<BR> Rām. 5. 4. 30.<BR>—3 End of a texture, edge, skirt, fringe or hem of a garment; वस्त्र˚;<BR> पवनप्रनर्तितान्तदेशे दुकूले K. 9 (by itself in Veda).<BR>—4 Vicinity, proximity, neighbourhood, presence; नाधीयीत श्मशानान्ते<BR> ग्रामान्ते Ms. 4. 116; Y. 2. 162; जलान्ते छन्दसां कुर्यादुत्सर्गं विधिवद्<BR> बहिः 1. 143; गङ्गाप्रपातान्तविरूढशष्पम् (गह्वरम्) R. 2. 26;<BR> पुंसो यमान्तं व्रजतः Pt. 2. 115 going into the vicinity or presence<BR> of Yama; अन्योन्यामन्त्रणं यत्स्याज्जनान्ते तज्जनान्तिकम् S. D.; यां<BR> तु कुमारस्यान्ते वाचमभाषथास्तां मे ब्रूहिं Śat. Br. (These four senses are allied).<BR>—5 End, conclusion, termination (opp. आरम्भ or आदि); सेकान्ते<BR> R. 1. 51; दिनान्ते निहितम् R. 4. 1; मासान्ते, पक्षान्ते, दशाहान्ते<BR> &c.; एकस्य दुःखस्य न यावदन्तं गच्छाम्यहं पारमिवार्णवस्य Pt. 2. 175;<BR> व्यसनानि दुरन्तानि Ms. 7. 45; दशान्तमुपेयिवान् R. 12. 1<BR> going to the end of the period of life (end of the wick); व्यसनं<BR> वर्धयत्येव तस्यान्तं नाधिगच्छति Pt. 2. 180; oft. in comp. in this<BR> sense, and meaning ‘ending in or with’, ‘ceasing to exist with’, ‘reaching to the end’<BR>; तदन्तं तस्य जीवितम् H. 1. 91 ends in it; कलहान्तानि<BR> हर्म्याणि कुवाक्यान्तं च सौहृदम् । कुराजान्तानि राष्ट्राणि कुकर्मान्तं यशो<BR> नृणाम् ॥ Pt. 5. 76; विशाखान्ता गता मेघा प्रसूत्यन्तं च यौवनम् ।<BR> प्रणामान्तः सतां कोपो याचनान्तंहि गौरवम् ॥ Subhāṣ. फलोदयान्ताय<BR> तपःसमाधये Ku. 5. 6 ending with (lasting till) the attainment of<BR> fruit; यौवनान्तं वयो यस्मिन् Ku. 6. 44; R. 11. 62, 14. 41; विपदन्ता<BR> ह्यविनीतसंपदः Ki. 2. 52; युगसहस्रान्तं ब्राह्मं पुण्यमहर्विदुः<BR> Ms. 1. 73 at the end of 1000 Yugas; प्राणान्तं दण्डम् Ms. 8. 359 capital<BR> punishment (such as would put an end to life).<BR>—6 Death, destruction; end or close of life; धरा गच्छत्यन्तं Bh. 3. 71<BR> goes down to destruction; योगेनान्ते तनुत्यजाम् R. 1. 8; एका<BR> भवेत्स्वस्तिमती त्वदन्ते 2. 48, 12. 75; ममाप्यन्ते Ś. 6; अद्य<BR> कान्तः कृतान्तो वा दुःखस्यान्तं करिष्यति Udb.; औषध्यः फलपाकान्ताः<BR> Ms. 1. 46; अन्तं या To be destroyed, perish, be ruined.<BR>—7 (In gram.) A final syllable or letter of a word; अजन्त ending<BR> in a vowel; so हलन्त, सुबन्त, तिङन्त &c.<BR>—8 The last word in a compound.<BR>—9 Ascertainment, or settlement (of a question); definite or final settlement;<BR> pause, final determination, as in सिद्धान्त; न चैव रावणस्यान्तो दृश्यते<BR> जीवितक्षये Rām. 6. 107. 58 उभयोरपि दृष्टोन्तस्त्त्वनयोस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः<BR> Bg. 2. 16 (सदसतोः इत्यर्थः).<BR>—10 The last portion or the remainder (<i>n.</i> also); निशान्तः, वेदान्तः<BR> &c. वेदांश्चैव तु वेदाङ्गान् वेदान्तानि तथा स्मृतीः । अधीत्य ब्राह्मणः<BR> पूर्वं शक्तितोऽन्यांश्च संपठेत् ॥ Bṛhadyogiyājñavalkya Smṛti 12. 34.<BR>—11 Underneath, inside, inner part; युष्मदीयं च जलान्ते गृहम् Pt. 4<BR> in water, underneath water; सुप्रयुक्तस्य दम्भस्य ब्रह्माप्यन्तं न<BR> गच्छति Pt. 1. 202 does not penetrate or dive<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">Page0118-1</a>]<BR> into, sound, fathom; आशङ्कितस्यान्तं गच्छामि M. 3 shall dive deep<BR> into, fully satisfy, my doubts.<BR>—12 Total amount, whole number or quantity.<BR>—13 A large number.<BR>—14 Nature, condition; sort, species; मम मोक्षस्य कोऽन्तो वै ब्रह्मन्ध्यायस्व<BR> वै प्रभो Mb. 12. 282. 32. एतदन्तास्तु गतयो ब्रह्माद्याः समुदाहृताः Ms. 1. 50.<BR>—15 Disposition; essence; शुद्धान्तः<BR>—16 Division (विभाग); तेऽनया कात्यायन्याऽन्तं करवाणीति Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 1.<BR> [cf. Goth. <i>andeis, andja</i>; Germ. <i>ende</i> and <i>ent</i>; also<BR> Gr. <i>anti</i>; L. <i>ante</i>]. cf. अन्तस्तु भागेऽवसिते रचनायां च तत्परे ।<BR> मृतौ निषेवणे रम्ये समाप्तावग्रमध्ययोः ॥ स्वरूपे च समीपे च पुंलिङ्गेऽपि<BR> प्रकीर्तितः । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तावशायिन्, अन्तावसायिन्, अन्तोदात्त, अन्तौष्ठः, अन्तकर, अन्तकरण, अन्तकारिन्, अन्तकर्मन्, अन्तकालः, अन्तवेला, अन्तकृत्, अन्तकृद्दशाः, अन्तग, अन्तगति, अन्तगामिन्, अन्तगमनम्, अन्तचक्रम्, अन्तचर, अन्तज, अन्तदीपकम्, अन्तपरिच्छदः, अन्तपालः, अन्तभव, अन्तभाज्, अन्तलीन, अन्तलोपः, अन्तवासिन्, अन्तवेला, अन्तव्यापत्तिः, अन्तशय्या, अन्तसंश्लेषः, अन्तसत्क्रिया, अन्तसद्, अन्तस्वरितः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तावशायिन्
अन्त + -अवशायिन् <i>m.</i> [अन्ते पर्यन्तदेशे अवशेते] a cāṇḍāla^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: also changed 6 more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तावसायिन्
अन्त + -अवसायिन् [नखकेशानामन्तम् अवसातुं छेत्तुं शीलमस्य, सो-णिनि]<BR>—1 a barber.<BR>—2 a cāṇḍāla^1, low-caste.<BR>—3 N. of a sage, see अन्त्यावसायिन् (अन्ते पश्चिमे वयसि अवस्यति<BR> तत्त्वं निश्चिनोति).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तोदात्त|अन्तोदात्तः
अन्त + -उदात्त <i>a.</i> having the acute accent on the last syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तोदात्तः|अन्तोदात्त
अन्त + -उदात्त + .({@-त्तः@}) the acute accent on the last syllable; P. VI. 1. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तौष्ठः
अन्त + -ओष्ठः The lower lip (अधरोष्ठ); रुधिरं न व्यतिक्रामदन्तोष्ठादम्ब<BR> मा शुचः Mb. 11. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर
अन्त + -कर, -करण, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> causing death or destruction, fatal,<BR> mortal, destructive; क्षत्रियान्तकरणोऽपि विकमः R. 11. 75 causing<BR> the destruction of; राज्यान्तकरणावेतौ द्वौ दोषौ पृथिवीक्षिताम् Ms. 9. 221;<BR> अहमन्तकरो नूनं ध्वान्तस्येव दिवाकरः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकरण
अन्त + -कर, -करण, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> causing death or destruction, fatal,<BR> mortal, destructive; क्षत्रियान्तकरणोऽपि विकमः R. 11. 75 causing<BR> the destruction of; राज्यान्तकरणावेतौ द्वौ दोषौ पृथिवीक्षिताम् Ms. 9. 221;<BR> अहमन्तकरो नूनं ध्वान्तस्येव दिवाकरः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकारिन्
अन्त + -कर, -करण, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> causing death or destruction, fatal,<BR> mortal, destructive; क्षत्रियान्तकरणोऽपि विकमः R. 11. 75 causing<BR> the destruction of; राज्यान्तकरणावेतौ द्वौ दोषौ पृथिवीक्षिताम् Ms. 9. 221;<BR> अहमन्तकरो नूनं ध्वान्तस्येव दिवाकरः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर्मन्|अन्तकर्म्मन्
अन्त + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> death, destruction; षो अन्तकर्मणि Dhātupāṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकालः|अन्तकाल
अन्त + -कालः, -वेला time or hour of death; स्थित्वा स्यामन्तकालेऽपि<BR> ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति Bg. 2. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवेला
अन्त + -कालः, -वेला time or hour of death; स्थित्वा स्यामन्तकालेऽपि<BR> ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति Bg. 2. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकृत्
अन्त + -कृत् <i>m.</i> death; वर्जयेदन्तकृन्मर्त्यं वर्जयेदनिलोऽनलम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकृद्दशाः
अन्त + -कृद्दशाः N. of the eighth of the twelve sacred Aṅga texts of<BR> the Jainas (containing ten chapters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तग|अन्तगः
अन्त + -ग <i>a.</i> having gone to the end of, thoroughly conversant or<BR> familiar with, (in comp.); शाखान्तगमथाध्वर्युम् Ms. 3. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तगति
अन्त + -गति, -गामिन् <i>a.</i> perishing. प्राप्तोऽन्तगामी विपरीतबुद्धिः<BR> Rām. 6. 59. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तगामिन्
अन्त + -गति, -गामिन् <i>a.</i> perishing. प्राप्तोऽन्तगामी विपरीतबुद्धिः<BR> Rām. 6. 59. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तगमनम्
अन्त + -गमनम्<BR>—1 going to the end, finishing, completing; प्रारब्धस्य ˚नं द्वितीयं<BR> बुद्धिलक्षणम्<BR>—2 death, perishing, dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तचक्रम्
अन्त + -चक्रम् Reading of omens and augury; Kau. A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तचर
अन्त + -चर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 walking about, going to the borders or frontiers.<BR>—2 completing or finishing (as a business &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तज
अन्त + -ज <i>a.</i> last born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तदीपकम्
अन्त + -दीपकम् a figure of speech (in Rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तपरिच्छदः
अन्त + -परिच्छदः a cover, covering utensil. राजतान्तपरिच्छदां दिव्यपायससंपूर्णां<BR> पात्रीम् Rām. 1. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तपालः|अन्तपाल
अन्त + -पालः<BR>—1 a frontier-guard, guarding the frontiers; विनीतैरन्तपालैश्च रक्षोभिश्च<BR> सुरक्षितम् Rām. 5. 6. 9. ˚दुर्गे M. 1; त्वदीयेनान्तपालेनावस्कन्द्य<BR> गृहीतः <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 a door-keeper (rare). सुद्युम्नस्त्वन्तपालेभ्यः श्रुत्वा लिखितमागतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 23. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तभव
अन्त + -भव, -भाज् <i>a.</i> being at the end, last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तभाज्
अन्त + -भव, -भाज् <i>a.</i> being at the end, last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तलीन
अन्त + -लीन <i>a.</i> hidden, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तलोपः|अन्तलोप
अन्त + -लोपः dropping of the final of a word. (न्ते˚)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवासिन्
अन्त + -वासिन् <i>a.</i> dwelling near the frontiers, dwelling close by.<BR>━<i>m.</i> [अन्ते गुरुसमीपे वस्तुं शीलं यस्य]<BR>—1 a pupil (who always dwells near his master to receive instruction);<BR> P. IV. 3. 104, VI. 2. 36; Ms. 4. 33.<BR>—2 a cāṇḍāla (who dwells at the extremity of a village).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवेला
अन्त + -वेला = ˚कालः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तव्यापत्तिः|अन्तव्यापत्ति
अन्त + -व्यापत्तिः <i>f.</i> change of the final syllable, as in मेघ<BR> from मिह् Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तशय्या
अन्त + -शय्या<BR>—1 a bed on the ground.<BR>—2 the last bed, death-bed; hence death itself,<BR>—3 a place for burial or burning.<BR>—4 a bier or funeral<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">Page0118-2</a>]<BR> pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तसंश्लेषः|अन्तसंश्लेष
अन्त + -संश्लेषः union (सन्धि), joint; सुखदुःखान्तसंश्लेषम्<BR> (कालचक्रम्) Mb. 14. 45. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तसत्क्रिया
अन्त + -सत्क्रिया last rites, funeral ceremonies, obsequies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तसद्
अन्त + -सद् <i>m.</i> a pupil; तमुपासते गुरुमिवान्तसदः Ki. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तस्वरितः|अन्तस्वरित
अन्त + -स्वरितः the <i>svarita</i> accent on the last syllable of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक <i>a.</i> [अन्तयति, अन्तं करोति, ण्वुल्] Causing death, making<BR> an end of, destroying; सूर्यकान्त इव ताडकान्तकः R. 11. 21; क्रोधान्धस्तस्य<BR> तस्य स्वयमिह जगतामन्तकस्यान्तकोहम् Ve. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकः|अन्तक|अंतक
अन्तक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Death. तदिदं पाण्डवेयानामन्तकायाभिसंहितम् Mb. 10. 15. 17.<BR>—2 Death personified, the destroyer; Yama, the god of death; नान्तकः<BR> सर्वभूतानां तृप्यति Pt. 1. 137; ऋषिप्रभावान्मयि नान्तकोऽपि प्रभुः<BR> प्रहर्तुम् R. 2. 62.<BR>—3 A border, boundary.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तकद्रुह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकद्रुह्
अन्तक + -द्रुह् Ved. provoking death; मूर्धा रथस्य चाकन् नैतावतैनसान्तकध्रुक्<BR> Rv. 10. 132. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ततः|अन्तत
अन्ततः <i>ind.</i> [अन्त-तसिल्]<BR>—1 From the end.<BR>—2 At last, finally; at length, lastly. नलं सर्वगुणैर्युक्तं मन्ये<BR> बाहुकमन्ततः Mb. 3. 71. 33.<BR>—3 In part, partly.<BR>—4 Inside, within.<BR>—5 In the lowest way; (opp. मुख्यतः, मध्यतः); (अन्ततः may<BR> have all the senses of अन्त).<BR>—6 In fact; हा हन्तौदनमन्ततः शुचितमं तद् दृष्टमाशु त्यजेत् Viś. Guṇā. 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवत्|अंतवत्|अन्तवन्त्
अन्तवत् <i>a.</i> [अन्त अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्]<BR>—1 Having an end; limited; perishable; अन्तवन्त इमे देहा नित्यस्योक्ताः<BR> शरीरिणः Bg. 2. 18. स हैतानन्तवत उपास्तेऽन्तवतः स लोकाञ्जयति Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR>—2 <i>m.</i> The god^1 of the space or atmosphere (दिगन्तानामीश्वरः); वसु<BR> ददातु अन्तवान् Mb. 3. 197. 5.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ते
अन्ते <i>ind.</i> (loc. of अन्त; oft. used adverbially)<BR>—1 In the end, at last, at length, lastly, finally.<BR>—2 Inside.<BR>—3 In the presence of, near, close by.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तेवसायिन्, अन्तेवसायी, अन्तेवासः, अन्तेवासि, अन्तेवासिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवसायिन्
अन्ते + -वसायिन्, -वसायी a Cāṇḍāla (अन्त्यज) अशौचमनृतं<BR> स्तेयं नास्तिक्यं शुल्कविग्रहः । कामः क्रोधश्च तर्षश्च स्वभावोऽन्तेवसायिनाम्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 17. 20, 7. 11. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवसायी
अन्ते + -वसायिन्, -वसायी a Cāṇḍāla (अन्त्यज) अशौचमनृतं<BR> स्तेयं नास्तिक्यं शुल्कविग्रहः । कामः क्रोधश्च तर्षश्च स्वभावोऽन्तेवसायिनाम्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 17. 20, 7. 11. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासः|अन्तेवास
अन्ते + -वासः<BR>—1 a neighbour; companion; तव वा इमेऽन्तेवासास्त्वमेवैभिः संपिबस्व Ait. Br.<BR>—2 a pupil; आचार्योऽन्तेवासिनमनुशास्ति T. Up. 1. 9. रुतानि शृण्वन्वयसां<BR> गणोऽन्तेवासित्वमाप स्फुटमङ्गनानाम् Śi. 3. 55; Ve. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासि
अन्ते + -वासि <i>ind.</i> in a state of pupilage, (<i>in statu pupillari^1</i>).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासिन्
अन्ते + -वासिन् = अन्तवासिन् q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तम|अंतम
अन्तम <i>a.</i> Ved. Nearest, next; शिक्षा अन्तमस्य Rv. 1. 27. 5;<BR> तनूपा अन्तमो भव 6. 46. 10; intimate, very close or familiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर् <i>ind.</i> [अम्-अरन्-तुडागमश्च Uṇ. 5. 60, अमेस्तुट् च]<BR>—1 (Used as a prefix to verbs and regarded as a preposition or गति)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) In the middle, between; in, into, inside; ˚हन्, ˚धा, ˚गम्,<BR> ˚भू, ˚इ, ˚ली &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Under.<BR>—2 (Used adverbially)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Between, betwixt, amongst, within; in the middle or interior,<BR> inside (opp. बहिः); अदह्यतान्तः R. 2. 32 burnt within himself,<BR> at heart; अन्तरेव विहरन् दिवानिशम् R. 19. 6 in the palace, in the<BR> harem; so ˚भिन्नं भ्रमति हृदयम् Māl. 5. 20; अन्तर्विभेद Dk. 13;<BR> यदन्तस्तन्न जिह्वायाम् Pt. 4. 88; अन्तर्यश्च मृग्यते V. 1. 1<BR> internally, in the mind.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) By way of seizing or holding; अन्तर्हत्वा गतः (हतं परिगृह्य).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">Page0119-1</a>]<BR>—3 (As a separable preposition)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) In, into, between, in the middle, inside, within, (with loc.);<BR> निवसन्नन्तर्दारुणि लङ्घ्यो वह्निः Pt. 1. 31; अन्तरादित्ये Ch. Up.;<BR> अन्तर्वेश्मनि Ms. 7. 223; Y. 3. 301; अप्स्वन्तरमृतमप्सु Rv. 1. 23. 19.<BR> अप्सु मे सोमोऽब्रवीदन्तर् विश्वानि भेषजा <i>ibid.</i><BR>——(<i>b</i>) Between (with acc.) Ved. अन्तर्मही बृहती रोदसीमे Rv. 7. 87. 2;<BR> अन्तर्देवान् मर्त्यांश्च 8. 2. 4; हिरण्मय्योर्ह कुश्योरन्तरवहित<BR> आस Śat. Br.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) In, into, inside, in the interior, in the midst (with gen.);<BR> प्रतिबलजलधेरन्तरौर्वायमाणे Ve. 3. 7; अन्तःकञ्चुकिकञ्चुकस्य<BR> Ratn. 2. 3; बहिरन्तश्च भूतानाम् Bg. 13. 15; त्वमग्ने सर्वभूतानामन्तश्चरसि<BR> साक्षिवत् Y. 2. 104; लघुवृत्तितया भिदां गतं बहिरन्तश्च नृपस्य<BR> मण्डलम् Ki. 2. 53; अन्तरीपं यदन्तर्वारिणस्तटम् Ak.; oft. in<BR> comp. at the end; कूपान्तः पतितः Pt. 5; सभान्तः साक्षिणः प्राप्तान्<BR> Ms. 8. 79; दन्तान्तरधिष्ठितम् Ms. 5. 141 between the teeth; उत्पित्सवोऽन्तर्नदभर्तुः<BR> Śi. 3. 77; also in compound with a following word; अहं सदा शरीरान्तर्वासिनी<BR> ते सरस्वती Ks. 4. 11.<BR>—4 It is frequently used as the first member of compounds in the sense<BR> of ‘internally’, ‘inside’, ‘within’, ‘in the interior’, ‘having in the interior’<BR>, ‘filled with’, ‘having concealed within’, or in the sense of<BR> ‘inward’, ‘internal’, ‘secret’, ‘hidden’ &c., forming Adverbial, Bahuvrīhi<BR> or Tatpuruṣa compounds; कुन्दमन्तस्तुषारम् (Bah. comp.) Ś. 5. 19<BR> filled with dew; ˚स्तोयम् (Bah. comp.) Me. 66; अन्तर्गिरि (Adv. comp.)<BR> Ki. 1. 34; ज्वलयति तनूमन्तर्दाहः (Tat. comp.) U. 3. 31;<BR> so ˚कोपः, ˚कोणः, ˚आकूतम् &c.<BR>—5 It is also supposed to be a particle of assent (स्वीकारार्थक).<BR> (<i>Note</i>. In comp. the र् of अन्तर् is changed to a visarga before<BR> hard consonants, as अन्तःकरणम्, अन्तःस्थ &c.). [cf. L. <i>inter</i>;<BR> Zend. <i>antare</i>; Goth. <i>undar</i>; Pers. <i>andar</i>; Gr. <i>entos</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरंसः, अन्तरग्निः, अन्तरङ्ग, अन्तरवयव, अन्तराकाशः, अन्तराकूतम्, अन्तरागमः, अन्तरागारम्, अन्तरात्मन्, अन्तरापणः, अन्तराय, अन्तराल, अन्तराराम, अन्तरिन्द्रियम्, अन्तरुष्यम्, अन्तःकरणम्, अन्तःकल्पः, अन्तःकुटिल, अन्तःकृमिः, अन्तःक्रिमिः, अन्तःकोटरपुष्पी, अन्तःकोपः, अन्तःकोशम्, अन्तर्गङ्गा, अन्तर्गडु, अन्तर्गम्, अन्तर्गत, अन्तर्गर्भ, अन्तर्गिरम्, अन्तर्गिरि, अन्तर्गुदवलयः^1, अन्तर्गूढ, अन्तर्गृहम्, अन्तर्गेहम्, अन्तर्भवनम्, अन्तर्घणः, अन्तर्घणम्, अन्तर्घातः, अन्तश्चर, अन्तर्ज, अन्तर्जठरम्, अन्तर्जम्भः, अन्तर्जात, अन्तर्जानु, अन्तर्जानुशयः, अन्तर्ज्ञानम्, अन्तर्ज्योतिस्, अन्तर्ज्वलनम्, अन्तस्ताप, अन्तर्दधनम्, अन्तर्दशा, अन्तर्दशाहम्, अन्तर्दहनम्, अन्तर्दाहः, अन्तर्दुःख, अन्तर्दुष्ट, अन्तर्दृष्टिः, अन्तर्देशः, अन्तर्द्वारम्, अन्तर्धा, अन्तर्धि, अन्तर्हित, अन्तर्नगरम्, अन्तर्निवेशनम्, अन्तर्निहित, अन्तर्निष्ठ, अन्तःपटः, अन्तःपटम्, अन्तःपथ, अन्तःपदम्, अन्तःपदवी, अन्तःपरिधानम्, अन्तःपर्शव्य, अन्तःपवित्रः, अन्तःपशुः, अन्तःपातः, अन्तःपात्यः, अन्तःपातित, अन्तःपातिन्, अन्तःपात्रम्, अन्तःपालः, अन्तःपुरम्, अन्तःपुरचर, अन्तःपुराध्यक्षः, अन्तःपुररक्षकः, अन्तःपुरवर्ती, अन्तःपुरिकः, अन्तःपुष्पम्, अन्तःपूय, अन्तःपेयम्, अन्तःप्रकृतिः, अन्तःप्रकोपनम्, अन्तःप्रज्ञ, अन्तःप्रतिष्ठानम्, अन्तर्बाष्प, अन्तर्भावः, अन्तर्भावना, अन्तर्भिन्न, अन्तर्भूमिः, अन्तर्भेदः, अन्तर्भौम, अन्तर्मदावस्थ, अन्तर्मनस्, अन्तर्मुख, अन्तर्मातृका, अन्तर्मुद्र, अन्तर्मृत, अन्तर्यागः, अन्तर्यामः, अन्तर्यामिन्, अन्तर्योगः, अन्तर्लम्ब, अन्तर्लीन, अन्तर्लोम, अन्तर्वंशः, अन्तर्वंशिकः, अन्तर्वासिकः, अन्तर्वण, अन्तर्वत्, अन्तर्वती, अन्तर्वमिः, अन्तर्वर्तिन्, अन्तर्वासिन्, अन्तर्वसुः, अन्तर्वस्त्रम्, अन्तर्वासस्, अन्तर्वा, अन्तर्वाणि, अन्तर्विगाहः, अन्तर्विगाहनम्, अन्तर्विद्वस्, अन्तर्वेगः, अन्तर्वेदि, अन्तर्वेश्मन्, अन्तर्वेश्मिकः, अन्तर्वैशिकः, अन्तःशरः, अन्तःशरीरम्, अन्तःशल्य, अन्तःशिला, अन्तःश्लेषः, अन्तःश्लेषणम्, अन्तःसंज्ञ, अन्तःसत्त्व, अन्तःसन्तापः, अन्तःसरल, अन्तःसलिल, अन्तःसार, अन्तःसुख, अन्तःसेनम्, अन्तःस्थ, अन्तःस्था, अन्तःस्वेदः, अन्तर्हणनम्, अन्तर्हननम्, अन्तर्हस्तम्, अन्तर्हस्तीन, अन्तर्हासः, अन्तर्हदयम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरंसः|अन्तरंस
अन्तर् + -अंसः the breast (= अंतरा-अंस q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरग्निः|अन्तरग्नि
अन्तर् + -अग्निः inward fire, the fire which stimulates digestion; दीप्तान्तरग्निपरिशुद्धकोष्टः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरङ्ग|अन्तरंग|अन्तरङ्गः
अन्तर् + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inward, internal, comprehended, included (with abl.); त्रयमन्तरङ्गं<BR> पूर्वेभ्यः Pātañjala S..<BR>—2 proximate, related to, essential to or referring to the essential part<BR> of the अङ्ग or base of a word (opp. बहिरङ्ग); धातूपसर्गयोः<BR> कार्यमन्तरङ्गम् P. VIII. 3. 74. Sk.<BR>—3 dear, most beloved (अत्यन्तप्रिय); स्वपिति सुखमिदानीमन्तरङ्गः<BR> कुरङ्गः Ś. 4, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरङ्गम्
अन्तर् + -अङ्ग + ({@-अङ्गम्@})<BR>—1 the inmost limb or organ, the heart, mind; सन्तुष्टान्तरङ्गः Dk. 11;<BR> ˚वृत्ति 21; the interior.<BR>—2 an intimate friend, near or confidential person (forming, as it were,<BR> part of oneself); मदन्तरङ्गभूताम् Dk. 81, 93, 101; राजान्तरङ्गभावेन 135;<BR> अन्तरङ्गेषु राज्यभारं समर्प्य 159.<BR>—3 an essential or indispensable part, as श्रवण, मनन & निदिध्यासन<BR> in realizing Brahman.<BR>—4 What is intimately connected or related; अन्तरङ्गबहिरङ्गयोरन्तरङ्गं<BR> बलीयः ŚB. on MS. 12. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरवयव
अन्तर् + -अवयव an inner part; P. V. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराकाशः|अन्तराकाश
अन्तर् + -आकाशः the ether or Brahman that resides in the heart of man<BR> (a term often occurring in the Upaniṣads).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराकूतम्
अन्तर् + -आकूतम् secret or hidden intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरागमः|अन्तरागम
अन्तर् + -आगमः an additional augment between two letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरागारम्
अन्तर् + -आगारम् the interior of a house; स्त्रीनक्तमन्तरागारबहिःशत्रुकृतांस्तथा Y. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरात्मन्
अन्तर् + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> (त्मा)<BR>—1 the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">Page0119-2</a>]<BR> inmost spirit or soul, the soul or mind; also the internal feelings, the<BR> heart, अङ्गुष्टमात्रपुरुषोन्तरात्मा Śvet. Up.; नास्य प्रत्यकरोद्वीर्यं<BR> विक्लवेनान्तरात्मना Rām. 6. 103. 28. गतिमस्यान्तरात्मनः Ms. 6. 73;<BR> जीवसंज्ञोन्तरात्मान्यः सहजः सर्वदेहिनाम् 12. 13; मद्गतेनान्तरात्मना<BR> Bg. 6. 47 with the heart fixed on me; जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामं …<BR> अन्तरात्मा Ś. 4. 22; U. 3. 38, प्रायः सर्वो भवति करुणावृत्तिरार्द्रान्तरात्मा Me. 95.<BR>—2 (In phil) the inherent supreme spirit or soul (residing in the interior<BR> of man); अन्तरात्मासि देहिनाम् Ku. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरापणः|अन्तरापण
अन्तर् + -आपणः a market in the heart (inside) of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराय|अंतरायः|अन्तरायः
अन्तर् + -आय, -आल See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराल|अंतरालं|अन्तरालं
अन्तर् + -आय, -आल See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराराम
अन्तर् + -आराम <i>a.</i> rejoicing in oneself, finding pleasure in his soul<BR> or heart; योऽन्तःसुखोन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव सः Bg. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिन्द्रियम्
अन्तर् + -इन्द्रियम् an internal organ or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरुष्यम्
अन्तर् + -उष्यम् Ved. a secret abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकरणम्
अन्तर् + -करणम् the internal organ; the heart, soul; the seat of thought<BR> and feeling, thinking faculty, mind, conscience; प्रमाणं ˚प्रवृत्तयः<BR> Ś. 1. 22; सबाह्य ˚णः अन्तरात्मा V. 4 the soul in all its senses<BR> external and internal, the inner and outer man; दयार्द्रभावमाख्यातमन्तःकरणैर्विशङ्कैः<BR> R. 2. 11. According to the Vedānta अन्तःकरण is of four kinds:−<BR> मनो बुद्धिरहङ्कारश्चित्तं करणमान्तरम् । संशयो निश्चयो गर्वः स्मरणं<BR> विषया इमे ॥ अन्तःकरणं त्रिविधम् Sāṅ. K. 33, i. e. बुद्ध्यहङ्कारमनांसि;<BR> सान्तःकरणा बुद्धिः 35, i. e. अहङ्कारमनःसहिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकल्पः|अन्तःकल्प
अन्तर् + -कल्पः a certain number of years (with Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकुटिल|अन्तःकुटिलः
अन्तर् + -कुटिल <i>a.</i> inwardly crooked (fig. also); fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकुटिलः|अन्तःकुटिल
अन्तर् + -कुटिल + .({@-लः@}) a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकृमिः|अन्तःकृमि
अन्तर् + -कृमिः, -क्रिमिः a disease of worms in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःक्रिमिः
