अन्तर् + -निवेशनम् inner part of the house; यथा चारोपितो वृक्षो जातश्चान्तर्निवेशने<BR> Rām. 6. 128. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्निहित
अन्तर् + -निहित <i>a.</i> being concealed within; अङ्गैरन्तर्निहितवचनैः<BR> सूचितः सम्यगर्थः M. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्निष्ठ
अन्तर् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> engaged in internal meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपटः|अन्तःपट
अन्तर् + -पटः, -पटम् a screen of cloth held between two persons who are<BR> to be united (as a bride and bridegroom, or pupil and preceptor) until<BR> the actual time of union arrives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपटम्
अन्तर् + -पटः, -पटम् a screen of cloth held between two persons who are<BR> to be united (as a bride and bridegroom, or pupil and preceptor) until<BR> the actual time of union arrives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपथ
अन्तर् + -पथ <i>a.</i> Ved. being on the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपदम्
अन्तर् + -पदम् <i>ind.</i> in the interior of an inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपदवी
अन्तर् + -पदवी = सुषुम्णामध्यगतः पन्थाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपरिधानम्
अन्तर् + -परिधानम् the innermost garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपर्शव्य
अन्तर् + -पर्शव्य <i>a.</i> being between the ribs (as flesh).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपवित्रः|अन्तःपवित्र
अन्तर् + -पवित्रः the Soma when in the straining vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपशुः|अन्तःपशु
अन्तर् + -पशुः [अन्तर्ग्राममध्ये पशवो यत्र] the time when the cattle<BR> are in the village or stables (from sunset to sunrise); अन्तःपशौ पशुकामस्य<BR> सायं प्रातः Kāty.; (सायं पशुषु ग्राममध्ये आगतेषु प्रातश्च ग्रामादनिःसृतेषु com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपातः|अन्तःपात
अन्तर् + -पातः, -पात्यः<BR>—1 insertion of a letter (in Gram.)<BR>—2 a post fixed in the middle of the sacrificial ground (used in ritual<BR> works); अन्तःपूर्वेण यूपं परीत्यान्तःपात्यदेशे स्थापयति Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपात्यः|अन्तःपात्य
अन्तर् + -पातः, -पात्यः<BR>—1 insertion of a letter (in Gram.)<BR>—2 a post fixed in the middle of the sacrificial ground (used in ritual<BR> works); अन्तःपूर्वेण यूपं परीत्यान्तःपात्यदेशे स्थापयति Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपातित
अन्तर् + -पातित, -पातिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inserted. —2 included or comprised in; falling within; दन्डकारण्य˚<BR> ति आश्रमपदम् K. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपातिन्
अन्तर् + -पातित, -पातिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inserted. —2 included or comprised in; falling within; दन्डकारण्य˚<BR> ति आश्रमपदम् K. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपात्रम्
अन्तर् + -पात्रम् Ved. interior of a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपालः|अन्तःपाल
अन्तर् + -पालः one who watches over the inner apartments of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरम्
अन्तर् + -पुरम् [अन्तः अभ्यन्तरं पुरं गृहम्, or पुरस्यान्तःस्थितम्]<BR>—1 inner apartment of a palace (set apart for women); female or womenʼs<BR> apartments, seraglio, harem (so called from their being situated <i>in</i><BR> <i>the heart of the town</i>, for purposes of safety); व्यायम्याप्लुत्य मध्याह्ने<BR> भोक्तुमन्तःपुरं विशेत् Ms. 7. 216, 221, 224; कन्यान्तःपुरे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">Page0120-2</a>]<BR> कश्चित्प्रविशति Pt. 1.<BR>—2 inmates of the female apartments, a queen or queens, the ladies taken<BR> collectively; अन्तःपुराणि सर्वाणि रुदमानानि सत्वरम् Rām. 6. 111. 111.<BR> ˚विरहपर्युत्सुकस्य राजर्षेः Ś. 3; K. 58; ततो राजा सान्तःपुरः<BR> स्वगृहमानीयाभ्यर्चितः Pt. 1; कस्यचिद्राज्ञोऽन्तःपुरं जलक्रीडां कुरुते<BR> <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरप्रचारः|अन्तःपुरप्रचार
अन्तर् + -पुरम् + ˚प्रचारः gossip of the harem Ms. 7. 153;<BR>˚समागतः<BR> Ś. 4; also in pl.; कदाचिदस्मत्प्रार्थनामन्तःपुरेभ्यः कथयेत् Ś. 2;<BR> न ददाति वाचमुचितामन्तःपुरेभ्यो यदा Ś. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरजन
अन्तर् + -पुरम् + ˚जन women<BR> of the palace; inmates of the female apartments;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरचर|अन्तःपुरचरः
अन्तर् + -पुरचर, -पुराध्यक्षः, -पुररक्षकः, -पुरवर्ती guardian or superintendent of the harem,<BR> chamberlain; वृद्धः कुलोद्गतः शक्तः पितृपैतामहः शुचिः । राज्ञामन्तःपुराध्यक्षो<BR> विनीतश्च तथेष्यते ॥ (of these five sorts are mentioned:− वामनक,<BR> जघन्य, कुब्ज, मण्डलक and सामिन् see Bṛ. S.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुराध्यक्षः|अन्तःपुराध्यक्ष
अन्तर् + -पुरचर, -पुराध्यक्षः, -पुररक्षकः, -पुरवर्ती guardian or superintendent of the harem,<BR> chamberlain; वृद्धः कुलोद्गतः शक्तः पितृपैतामहः शुचिः । राज्ञामन्तःपुराध्यक्षो<BR> विनीतश्च तथेष्यते ॥ (of these five sorts are mentioned:− वामनक,<BR> जघन्य, कुब्ज, मण्डलक and सामिन् see Bṛ. S.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुररक्षकः|अन्तःपुररक्षक
अन्तर् + -पुरचर, -पुराध्यक्षः, -पुररक्षकः, -पुरवर्ती guardian or superintendent of the harem,<BR> chamberlain; वृद्धः कुलोद्गतः शक्तः पितृपैतामहः शुचिः । राज्ञामन्तःपुराध्यक्षो<BR> विनीतश्च तथेष्यते ॥ (of these five sorts are mentioned:− वामनक,<BR> जघन्य, कुब्ज, मण्डलक and सामिन् see Bṛ. S.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरवर्ती
अन्तर् + -पुरचर, -पुराध्यक्षः, -पुररक्षकः, -पुरवर्ती guardian or superintendent of the harem,<BR> chamberlain; वृद्धः कुलोद्गतः शक्तः पितृपैतामहः शुचिः । राज्ञामन्तःपुराध्यक्षो<BR> विनीतश्च तथेष्यते ॥ (of these five sorts are mentioned:− वामनक,<BR> जघन्य, कुब्ज, मण्डलक and सामिन् see Bṛ. S.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरसहायः|अन्तःपुरसहाय
अन्तर् + -पुरम् + ˚सहायः one<BR> belonging to the harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरिकः|अन्तःपुरिक
अन्तर् + -पुरिकः [अन्तःपुरे नियुक्तः, ठक्] a chamberlain = ˚चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरचरः|अन्तःपुरचर
अन्तर् + -पुरिकः [अन्तःपुरे नियुक्तः, ठक्] a chamberlain = ˚चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरिकः|अन्तःपुरिक
अन्तर् + -पुरिकः + .({@-कः, -का@}) a woman in the harem; अस्मत्प्रार्थनामन्तःपुरिके<BR> (का) भ्यो निवेदय Caṇḍ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुरिका
अन्तर् + -पुरिकः + .({@-कः, -का@}) a woman in the harem; अस्मत्प्रार्थनामन्तःपुरिके<BR> (का) भ्यो निवेदय Caṇḍ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुष्पम्
अन्तर् + -पुष्पम् [कर्म˚] the menstrual matter of women, before it<BR> regularly begins to flow every month; वर्षद्वादशकादूर्ध्वं यदि पुष्पं<BR> बहिर्न हि । अन्तःपुष्पं भवत्येव पनसोदुम्बरादिवत् Kāśyapa; ˚ष्पम्<BR> is therefore the age between 12 and the menstruation period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपूय
अन्तर् + -पूय <i>a.</i> ulcerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपेयम्
अन्तर् + -पेयम् Ved. drinking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रकृतिः|अन्तःप्रकृति
अन्तर् + -प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the internal nature or constitution of man.<BR>—2 the ministry or body of ministers of a king.<BR>—3 heart or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रकृतिप्रकोपः
अन्तर् + -प्रकृतिः + ˚प्रकोपः internal dissensions or disaffection;<BR> अणुरप्युपहन्ति विग्रहः प्रभुमन्तःप्रकृतिप्रकोपजः Ki. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रकोपनम्
अन्तर् + -प्रकोपनम् sowing internal dissensions, causing internal revolts;<BR> अन्तःप्रकोपनं कार्यमभियोक्तुः स्थिरात्मनः H. 3. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रज्ञ
अन्तर् + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing oneself, with an enlightened soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रतिष्ठानम्
अन्तर् + -प्रतिष्ठानम् residence in the interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्बाष्प|अन्तर्बाष्पः
अन्तर् + -बाष्प <i>a.</i><BR>—1 with suppressed tears; अन्तर्बाष्पश्चिरमनुचरो राजराजस्य दध्यौ Me. 3.<BR>—2 with tears gushing up inside, bedimmed with tears; कोपात्˚ष्पे स्मरयति मां लोचने तस्याः V. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्बाष्पः|अन्तर्बाष्प
अन्तर् + -बाष्प + .({@-ष्पः@}) suppressed tears, inward tears; निगृह्य ˚ष्पम् Bh. 3. 6; Māl. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावः|अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः
अन्तर् + -भावः, -भावना see under अन्तर्भू separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावना|अंतर्भावना
अन्तर् + -भावः, -भावना see under अन्तर्भू separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भिन्न
अन्तर् + -भिन्न <i>a.</i> split or broken inside, perforated, bored (said<BR> of a pearl) Pt. 4 (also torn by dissensions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूमिः|अन्तर्भूमि
अन्तर् + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> interior of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भेदः|अन्तर्भेद
अन्तर् + -भेदः discord, internal dissensions; ˚जर्जरं राजकुलम्<BR> Mk. 4 torn by internal dissensions; अन्तर्भेदाकुलं गेहं न चिराद्विनशिष्यति<BR> ‘a house divided against itself cannot stand long’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भौम
अन्तर् + -भौम <i>a.</i> subterranean, underground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मदावस्थ
अन्तर् + -मदावस्थ <i>a.</i> having the rutting state concealed within; आसीदनाविष्कृतदानराजिरन्तर्मदावस्थ<BR> इव द्विपेन्द्रः R. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मनस्
अन्तर् + -मनस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 sad, disconsolate, dejected, distracted.<BR>—2 one who has concentrated and turned his mind inward, lost in abstract meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मुख
अन्तर् + -मुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 going into the mouth, pointing or turned inward; प्रचण्डपरिपिण्डितः<BR> स्तिमितवृत्तिरन्तर्मुखः Mv. 5. 26.<BR>—2 having an inward entrance or opening (बाह्यवस्तुपरिहारेण परमात्मविषयकतया<BR> प्रवेशयुक्तं चित्तादि).<BR>—3 an epithet of the soul called प्राज्ञ, when it is enjoying the sweet<BR> bliss of sleep (आनन्दभुक् चेतोमुखः प्राज्ञः इति श्रुतेः).<BR>—4 Spiritual minded, looking inwardly into the soul; ‘अन्तर्मुखाः सततमात्मविदो महान्तः’<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मुखम्
अन्तर् + -मुख + .({@-खम्@}) a sort of surgical scissors (having an opening inside),<BR> one of the 20 instruments mentioned by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">Page0121-1</a>]<BR> Suśruta in chapter 8 of Sūtrasthāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मातृका
अन्तर् + -मातृका [अन्तःस्थाः षट्चकस्थाः मातृकाः अकारादिवर्णाः] a name<BR> given in the Tantras for the letters of the alphabet assigned to the six<BR> lotuses (पद्म) of the body;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मातृकान्यासः|अन्तर्मातृकान्यास
अन्तर् + -मातृका + ˚न्यासः a term used in Tantra literature<BR> for the mental assignment of the several letters of the alphabet to the<BR> different parts of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मुद्र
अन्तर् + -मुद्र <i>a.</i> sealed inside; N. of a form of devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मृत
अन्तर् + -मृत <i>a.</i> still-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यागः|अन्तर्याग
अन्तर् + -यागः mental sacrifice or worship, a mode of worship referred<BR> to in the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामः|अन्तर्याम
अन्तर् + -यामः<BR>—1 suppression of the breath and voice.<BR>—2 ˚पात्रम्, a sacrificial vessel (ग्रहरूपं सामापराख्यं यज्ञियपात्रम्);<BR> according to others, a Soma libation made during the suppression of breath<BR> and voice; सुहवा सूर्यायान्तर्याममनुमन्त्रयेत् Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामिन्
अन्तर् + -यामिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 regulating the soul or internal feelings, soul; Providence, Supreme<BR> Spirit as guiding and regulating mankind, Brahman; (according to the Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR> अन्तर्यामिन् ‘the internal check’ is the Supreme Being and<BR> not the individual soul; who standing in the earth is other than the earth,<BR> whom the earth knows not, whose body the earth is, who internally restrains<BR> and governs the earth; the same is <i>thy</i> soul and mind, the internal<BR> check अन्तर्यामिन्, &c. &c.); अन्तराविश्य भूतानि यो बिभर्त्यात्मकेतुभिः ।<BR> अन्तर्यामीश्वरः साक्षाद्भवेत् &c. —2 wind;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामिब्राह्मणम्
अन्तर् + -यामिन् + ˚ब्राह्मणम् N. of a Brāhmaṇa<BR> included in the Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्योगः|अन्तर्योग
अन्तर् + -योगः deep meditation, abstraction<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लम्ब|अन्तर्लम्बः
अन्तर् + -लम्ब <i>a.</i> acute-angular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लम्बः|अन्तर्लम्ब
अन्तर् + -लम्ब + .({@-बः@}) an acute-angled triangle (opp. बहिर्लम्ब) (the perpendicular<BR> from the vertex or लम्ब falling within अन्तर् the triangle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लीन
अन्तर् + -लीन <i>a.</i> —1 latent, hidden, concealed inside; ˚नस्य दुःखाग्नेः<BR> U. 3. 9; ˚भुजङ्गमम् Pt. 1.<BR>—2 inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लोम
अन्तर् + -लोम <i>a.</i> (P. V. 4. 117) covered with hair on the inside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लोमम्
अन्तर् + -लोम + .({@-मम्@}) [अन्तर्गतमाच्छाद्यं लोम अच्] the hair to be covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वंशः|अन्तर्वंश
अन्तर् + -वंशः = ˚पुरम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वंशिकः|अन्तर्वंशिक
अन्तर् + -वंशिकः, -वासिकः [अन्तर्वंशे वासे नियुक्तः ठक्] a superintendent<BR> of the womenʼs apartments; Pt. 3; K. 93; Ak. 2. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वासिकः|अन्तर्वासिक
अन्तर् + -वंशिकः, -वासिकः [अन्तर्वंशे वासे नियुक्तः ठक्] a superintendent<BR> of the womenʼs apartments; Pt. 3; K. 93; Ak. 2. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वण
अन्तर् + -वण (वन) <i>a.</i> situated in a forest; ˚णो देशः P. VI. 2. 179. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वणम्
अन्तर् + -वण + .({@-णम्@}) <i>ind.</i> within a forest P. VIII. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वत्|अन्तर्वन्त्
अन्तर् + -वत् <i>a.</i> being in the interior; having something in the interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वती
अन्तर् + -वती (वत्नी) Ved. [अन्तरस्त्यस्यां गर्भः] a pregnant<BR> woman; अन्तर्वत्नी प्रजावती R. 15. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वमिः|अन्तर्वमि|अन्तर्व्वमिः
अन्तर् + -वमिः [अन्तः स्थित एव उद्गारशब्दं कारयति, वम्-इन्] indigestion,<BR> flatulence; belching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वर्तिन्|अन्तर्वर्त्तिन्
अन्तर् + -वर्तिन्, -वासिन् <i>a.</i> being or dwelling inside, included or comprised in<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वासिन्
अन्तर् + -वर्तिन्, -वासिन् <i>a.</i> being or dwelling inside, included or comprised in<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वसुः|अन्तर्वसु
अन्तर् + -वसुः N. of a Soma sacrifice (for राज्यकाम and पशुकाम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वस्त्रम्
अन्तर् + -वस्त्रम्, -वासस् <i>n.</i> an undergarment; गृहीत्वा तत्र तस्यान्तर्वस्त्राण्याभरणानि<BR> च । चेलखण्डं तमेकं च दत्वान्तर्वाससः कृते ॥ Ks. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वासस्
अन्तर् + -वस्त्रम्, -वासस् <i>n.</i> an undergarment; गृहीत्वा तत्र तस्यान्तर्वस्त्राण्याभरणानि<BR> च । चेलखण्डं तमेकं च दत्वान्तर्वाससः कृते ॥ Ks. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वा
अन्तर् + -वा <i>a.</i> [अन्तः अन्तरङ्गभावम् अन्तःकरणं वा वाति गच्छति<BR> स्निग्धत्वेन, वा-विच् Tv.] forming part of oneself such as children, cattle<BR> &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वावत्|अन्तर्वावन्त्
अन्तर् + -वा + ˚वत् <i>a.</i> (अस्त्यर्थे मतुप् मस्य वः) having progeny, cattle<BR> &c.; अन्तर्वावत्क्षयं दधे Rv. 1. 40. 7; abounding with precious things<BR> inside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वा
अन्तर् + -वा ━<i>adv.</i> inwardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वाणि|अन्तर्व्वाणि|अन्तर्व्वाणिः
अन्तर् + -वाणि <i>a.</i> [अन्तःस्थिता शास्त्रवाक्यात्मिका वाणी यस्य] skilled<BR> or versed in scriptures, very learned (शास्त्रविद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्विगाहः|अन्तर्विगाह
अन्तर् + -विगाहः, -विगाहनम्^1 entering within, penetration.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">Page0121-2</a>]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्विगाहनम्
अन्तर् + -विगाहः, -विगाहनम्^1 entering within, penetration.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">Page0121-2</a>]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्विद्वस्
अन्तर् + -विद्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved. (विदुषी <i>f.</i>) knowing correctly<BR> or exactly (knowing the paths between heaven and earth) Rv. 1. 72. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेगः|अन्तर्वेग
अन्तर् + -वेगः inward uneasiness or anxiety, inward fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेदि|अन्तर्वेदिः
अन्तर् + -वेदि <i>a.</i> pertaining to the inside of the sacrificial ground.<BR>━<i>adv.</i> within this ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेदिः|अन्तर्वेदि
अन्तर् + -वेदि + .({@-दिः, -दी@} <i>f.</i>) [अन्तर्गता वेदिर्यत्र देशे] the tract of<BR> land (the Doab) between the rivers Gaṅgā and Yamunā, regarded as a<BR> sacred region and the principal seat of Āryan Brāhmaṇas; cf. एते भगवत्यौ<BR> भूमिदेवानां मूलमायतनमन्तर्वेदिपूर्वेण कलिन्दकन्यामन्दाकिन्यौ संगच्छेते<BR> A. R. 7; it is supposed to have extended from Prayāga to Haradvāra and<BR> is also known by the names of शशस्थली and ब्रह्मावर्त. ━<i>m.</i><BR> (pl.) inhabitants of this land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेदी|अन्तर्व्वेदी
अन्तर् + -वेदि + .({@-दिः, -दी@} <i>f.</i>) [अन्तर्गता वेदिर्यत्र देशे] the tract of<BR> land (the Doab) between the rivers Gaṅgā and Yamunā, regarded as a<BR> sacred region and the principal seat of Āryan Brāhmaṇas; cf. एते भगवत्यौ<BR> भूमिदेवानां मूलमायतनमन्तर्वेदिपूर्वेण कलिन्दकन्यामन्दाकिन्यौ संगच्छेते<BR> A. R. 7; it is supposed to have extended from Prayāga to Haradvāra and<BR> is also known by the names of शशस्थली and ब्रह्मावर्त. ━<i>m.</i><BR> (pl.) inhabitants of this land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेश्मन्
अन्तर् + -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> the inner apartments, interior of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेश्मिकः|अन्तर्वेश्मिक
अन्तर् + -वेश्मिकः a chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वैशिकः|अन्तर्वैशिक
अन्तर् + -वैशिकः Officer in charge of the harem. समुद्रमुपकरणमन्तर्वैशिकहस्तादादाय<BR> परिचरेयुः Kau. A. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशरः|अन्तःशर
अन्तर् + -शरः internal arrow or disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशरीरम्
अन्तर् + -शरीरम् internal and spiritual part of man; the interior of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशल्य
अन्तर् + -शल्य <i>a.</i> having in the interior an arrow, pin or any such<BR> extraneous matter; rankling inside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशिला
अन्तर् + -शिला N. of a river rising from the Vindhya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःश्लेषः|अन्तःश्लेष
अन्तर् + -श्लेषः, -श्लेषणम् Ved. internal support (scaffolding &c.) एतानि<BR> ह वै वेदानामन्तः -श्लेषणानि यदेता व्याहृतयः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःश्लेषणम्
अन्तर् + -श्लेषः, -श्लेषणम् Ved. internal support (scaffolding &c.) एतानि<BR> ह वै वेदानामन्तः -श्लेषणानि यदेता व्याहृतयः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसंज्ञ|अन्तःसञ्ज्ञ
अन्तर् + -संज्ञ <i>a.</i> inwardly conscious (said of trees &c.); ˚ज्ञा<BR> भवन्त्येते सुखदुःखसमान्विताः Ms. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसत्त्व
अन्तर् + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> having inward strength &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसत्त्वा
अन्तर् + -सत्त्व + ({@˚त्त्वा@})<BR>—1 a pregnant woman.<BR>—2 the marking nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसन्तापः|अन्तःसन्ताप|अन्तःसंताप
अन्तर् + -सन्तापः internal pain, sorrow, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसरल
अन्तर् + -सरल <i>a.</i> upright at heart, or having Sarala trees inside; K. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसलिल
अन्तर् + -सलिल <i>a.</i> with water (flowing) underground; नदीमिवान्तःसलिलां<BR> सरस्वतीम् R. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसार|अन्तःसारः
अन्तर् + -सार <i>a.</i> having inward strength and vigour, full or strong^1<BR> inside; powerful, strong, heavy or ponderous; ˚रैर्मन्त्रिभिर्घार्यते राज्यं<BR> सुस्तम्भैरिव मन्दिरम् Pt. 1. 126; ˚साराणि इन्धनानि Dk. 132; ˚रं<BR> घन तुलयितुं नानिलः शक्ष्यति त्वाम् Me. 20.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसारः|अन्तःसार
अन्तर् + -सार + .({@-रः@}) internal treasure or store, inner store or contents; वमन्त्युच्चैरन्तःसारम्<BR> H. 2. 103 internal matter or essence (and pus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसुख
अन्तर् + -सुख <i>a.</i> whose delight is in self, inwardly happy योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामः Bg. 5. 24<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसेनम्
अन्तर् + -सेनम् <i>ind.</i> into the midst of armies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्थ|अन्तःस्थः
अन्तर् + -स्थ <i>a.</i>^1 being between or in the midst.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: phrase removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्थः|अन्तःस्थ
अन्तर् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः, -स्था@}) a term applied to the semivowels, य्, र्, ल्, व्<BR> as standing between vowels and consonants and being formed by a slight<BR> contact of the vocal organs (ईषत्स्पृष्टम् अन्तस्थानाम्); or they are<BR> so called because they stand between स्पर्श (क-म) letters and<BR> ऊष्मन् (श, ष, स, ह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्था
अन्तर् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः, -स्था@}) a term applied to the semivowels, य्, र्, ल्, व्<BR> as standing between vowels and consonants and being formed by a slight<BR> contact of the vocal organs (ईषत्स्पृष्टम् अन्तस्थानाम्); or they are<BR> so called because they stand between स्पर्श (क-म) letters and<BR> ऊष्मन् (श, ष, स, ह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्था
अन्तर् + -स्था<BR>—1 a deity of the vital organs.<BR>—2 N. of one of the Ṛgveda^1 hymns.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: 5 other also changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्थमुद्गरः|अन्तःस्थमुद्गर
अन्तर् + -स्था + ˚मुद्गरः the malleus of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्वेदः|अन्तःस्वेद
अन्तर् + -स्वेदः [अन्तः खेदो मदजलस्यन्दनं यस्य] an elephant (in rut).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हणनम्
अन्तर् + -हणनम् striking in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हननम्
अन्तर् + -हननम् N. of a country बाहीक P. VIII. 4. 24. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हस्तम्
अन्तर् + -हस्तम् <i>ind.</i> in the hand, within reach of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हस्तीन
अन्तर् + -हस्तीन <i>a.</i> being in the hand or within reach of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हासः|अन्तर्हास
अन्तर् + -हासः laughing inwardly (in the sleeves), a secret or suppressed<BR> laugh; सान्तर्हासं कथितम् Me. 113<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0122-1" target="_blank">Page0122-1</a>]<BR> with a suppressed laugh, with a gentle smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हदयम्
अन्तर् + -हदयम् the interior of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर <i>a.</i> [अन्तं राति ददाति, रा-क]<BR>—1 Being in the inside, interior, inward, internal (opp. बाह्य); योन्तरो<BR> यमयति Śat. Br.; ˚र आत्मा T. Up.; कश्चनान्तरो धर्मः<BR> S. D. अन्तरापणवीथ्यश्च नानापण्योपशोभिताः अनुगच्छन्तु Rām. 7. 64. 3.<BR>—2 Near, proximate (आसन्न); कृष्वा युजश्चिदन्तरम् Rv. 1. 10. 9.<BR>—3 Related, intimate, dear, closely connected (आत्मीय) (opp. पर);<BR> तदेतत्प्रेयः पुत्रात् … प्रेयोऽन्यस्मात्सर्वस्मादन्तरतरं यदयमात्मा<BR> Śat. Br.; अयमत्यन्तरो मम Bharata.<BR>—4 Similar (also अन्तरतम) (of sounds and words); स्थानेऽन्तरतमः<BR> P. I. 1. 50; हकारस्य घकारोन्तरतमः Śabdak.; सर्वस्य पदस्य<BR> स्थाने शब्दतोऽर्थतश्चान्तरतमे द्वे शब्दस्वरूपे भवतः P. VIII. 1. 1. Com.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Different from, other than (with abl.); योऽप्सु तिष्ठन्नद्भ्योऽन्तरः<BR> Bṛ. Ār. Up.; आत्मा स्वभावोऽन्तरोऽन्यो यस्य स आत्मान्तरः अन्यस्वभावः<BR> व्यवसायिनोऽन्तरम् P. VI. 2. 166. Sk. ततोऽन्तराणि सत्त्वानि स्वादते<BR> स महाबलः Rām. 7. 62. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The other; उदधेरन्तरं पारम् Rām. 6 Exterior, outer, situated<BR> outside, or to be worn outside (अन्तरं बहिर्योगोपसंव्यानयोः P. I. 1. 36)<BR> (In this sense it is declined optionally like सर्व in nom.<BR> pl. and abl. and loc. sing.) अन्तरे-रा वा गृहाः वाह्या इत्यर्थः (चण्डालादिगृहाः);<BR> अन्तरे-रा वा शाटकाः परिधानीया इत्यर्थः Sk.; so अन्तरायां पुरि,<BR> अन्तरायै नगर्यै, नमोऽन्तरस्मै अमेधसाम् Vop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरम्
अन्तर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The interior, inside; ततान्तरं सान्तरवारिशीकरैः Ki. 4. 29, 5. 5;<BR> जालान्तरगते भानौ Ms. 8. 132; विमानान्तरलम्बिनीनाम्<BR> R. 13. 33; Mk. 8. 5; Ku. 7. 62; अपि वनान्तरं श्रयति V. 4. 24; लीयन्ते<BR> मुकुलान्तरेषु Ratn. 1. 26; Ki. 3. 58; अन्तरात् from inside, from<BR> out of; प्राकारपरिखान्तरान्निर्ययुः Rām.; अन्तरे in, into; वन˚,<BR> कानन˚, प्रविश्यान्तरे &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Hence, the interior of any thing, contents; purport, tenor; अत्रान्तरं<BR> ब्रह्मविदो विदित्वा Śvet. Up.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) A hole, an opening; तस्य बाणान्तरेभ्यस्तु बहु सुस्राव शोणितम्.<BR>—2 Soul, heart; mind; सततमसुतरं वर्णयन्त्यन्तरम् Ki. 5. 18<BR> the inmost or secret nature (lit. middle space or region); लब्धप्रतिष्ठान्तरैः<BR> भृत्यैः Mu. 3. 13 having entered the heart; सदृशं पुरुषान्तरविदो<BR> महेन्द्रस्य V. 3.<BR>—3 The Supreme Soul.<BR>—4 Interval, intermediate time or space, distance; रम्यान्तरः Ś. 4. 11;<BR> किंचिदन्तरमगमम् Dk. 6; अल्पकुचान्तरा V. 4. 49; कोशान्तरेन<BR> पथि स्थिताः H. 4 at the distance of; बृहद् भुजान्तरम् R. 3. 54;<BR> अन्तरे oft. translated by between, betwixt; गीतान्तरेषु Ku. 3. 38<BR> in the intervals of singing; मरणजीवितयोरन्तरे वर्ते betwixt<BR> life and death; अस्त्रयोगान्तरेषु Rām.; तन्मुहूर्तकं बाष्पसलिलान्तरेषु<BR> प्रेक्षे तावदार्यपुत्रम् U. 3 in the intervals of weeping; बाष्पविश्रामोऽप्यन्तरे<BR> कर्तव्य एव U. 4 at intervals; स्मर्तव्योस्मि कथान्तरेषु भवता<BR> Mk. 7. 7 in the course of conversation; कालान्तरावर्तिशुभाशुभानि H. 1.<BR> v. l. See कालान्तरम्; सरस्वतीदृषद्वत्योर्यदन्तरम् Ms. 2. 17, 22;<BR> द्यावापृथिव्योरिदमन्तरं हि व्याप्तं त्वयैकेन Bg. 11. 20; न<BR> मृणालसूत्रं रचितं स्तनान्तरे Ś. 6. 18 between the breasts; Bg. 5. 27;<BR> अस्य खलु ते बाणपथवर्तिनः कृष्णसारस्यान्तरे तपस्विन उपस्थिताः<BR> Ś. 1; तदन्तरे सा विरराज धेनुः R. 2. 20, 12. 29.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Intervention (व्यवधान) oft. in the sense of ‘through’;<BR> मेघान्तरालक्ष्यमिवेन्दुबिम्बम् R. 13. 38 through the clouds; वस्त्रम्<BR> अन्तरं व्यवधायकं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0122-2" target="_blank">Page0122-2</a>]<BR> यस्य स वस्त्रान्तरः P. VI. 2. 166. Sk.; महानद्यन्तरं यत्र तद्देशान्तरमुच्यते;<BR> जालान्तरप्रेषितदृष्टिः R. 7. 9 peeping through a window; विटपान्तरेण<BR> अवलोकयामि Ś. 1; क्षणमपि विलम्बमन्तरीकर्तुमक्षमा K. 306<BR> to allow to come between or intervene; कियच्चिरं वा मेघान्तरेण पूर्णिमाचन्द्रस्य<BR> दर्शनम् U. 3.<BR>—5 Room, place, space in general; मृणालसूत्रान्तरमप्यलभ्यम् Ku. 1. 40;<BR> न ह्यविद्धं तयोर्गात्रे बभूवाङ्गुलमन्तरम् Rām.; मूषिकैः<BR> कृतेऽन्तरे Y. 1. 147; गुणाः कृतान्तराः K. 4 finding or making room<BR> for themselves; न यस्य कस्यचिदन्तरं दातव्यम् K. 266; देहि दर्शनान्तरम् 84.<BR> room; पौरुषं श्रय शोकस्य नान्तरं दातुमर्हसि Rām. do not<BR> give way to sorrow; तस्यान्तरं मार्गते Mk. 7. 2 waits till it finds<BR> room; अन्तरम् अन्तरम् Mk. 2 make way, make way.<BR>—6 Access, entrance, admission, footing; लेभेन्तरं चेतसि नोपदेशः<BR> R. 6. 66 found no admission into (was not impressed on) the mind; 17. 75;<BR> लब्धान्तरा सावरणेऽपि गेहे 16. 7.<BR>—7 Period (of time), term; मासान्तरे देयम् Ak.; सप्तैते मनवः ।<BR> स्वे स्वेन्तरे सर्वमिदमुत्पाद्यापुश्चराचरम् Ms. 1. 63, see मन्वन्तरम्;<BR> इति तौ विरहान्तरक्षमौ R. 8. 56 the term or period of separation; क्षणान्तरे<BR> -रात् within the period of a moment.<BR>—8 Opportunity, occasion, time; देवी चित्रलेखामवलोकयन्ती तिष्टति ।<BR> तस्मिन्नन्तरे भर्तोपस्थितः M. 1. अत्रान्तरे प्रणम्याग्रे समुपविष्टः;<BR> Pt. 1 on that occasion, at that time; अस्मिन्नन्तरे Dk. 164; केन<BR> पुनरुपायेन मरणनिर्वाणस्यान्तरं संभावयिष्ये Māl. 6; कृतकृत्यता<BR> लब्धान्तरा भेत्स्यति Mu. 2. 22 getting an opportunity; 2. 9; यावत्त्वामिन्द्रगुरवे<BR> निवेदयितुम् अन्तरान्वेषी भवामि Ś. 7 find a fit or opportune time;<BR> शक्तेनापि सता जनेन विदुषा कालान्तरप्रेक्षिणा वस्तव्यम् Pt. 3. 12;<BR> waiting for a suitable opportunity or time; सारणस्यान्तरं दृष्ट्वा<BR> शुको रावणमब्रवीत् Rām.<BR>—9 Difference (between two things), (with gen. or in comp.) शरीरस्य<BR> गुणानां च दूरमत्यन्तमन्तरम् H. 1. 46; उभयोः पश्यतान्तरम् H. 1. 64,<BR> नारीपुरुषतोयानामन्तरं महदन्तरम् 2. 39; तव मम च<BR> समुद्रपल्वलयोरिवान्तरम् M. 1; Bg. 13. 34; यदन्तरं सर्षपशैलराजयोर्यदन्तरं<BR> वायसवैनतेययोः Rām.; द्रुमसानुमतां किमन्तरम् R. 8. 90, 18. 15;<BR> rarely with instr., त्वया समुद्रेण च महदन्तरम् H. 2; स्वामिनि<BR> गुणान्तरज्ञे Pt. 1. 101; difference; सैव विशिनष्टि पुनः प्रधानपुरषान्तरं<BR> सूक्ष्मम् Sāṅ. K.<BR>—10 (Math.) Difference, remainder also subtraction, cf. योगोन्तरेणोनयुतोऽर्धितस्तौ<BR> राशी स्मृतौ संकमणाख्यमेतत् ॥ Līlā.<BR>—11<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Different, another, other, changed, altered (manner, kind, way<BR> &c.); [Note that in this sense अन्तर always forms the latter part<BR> of a compound and its gender remains unaffected i. e. neuter, whatever<BR> be the gender of the noun forming the first part; कन्यान्तरम् (अन्या<BR> कन्या), राजान्तरम् (अन्यो राजा), गृहान्तरम् (अन्यद् गृहम्);<BR> in most cases it may be rendered by the English word ‘another’.]; इदमवस्थान्तरमारोपिता<BR> Ś. 3 changed condition; K. 154; Mu. 5; शुभाशुभफलं सद्यो नृपाद्देवाद्भवान्तरे<BR> Pt. 1. 121; जननान्तरसौहृदानि Ś. 5. 2 friendships of another (former)<BR> existence; नैवं वारान्तरं विधास्यते H. 3 I shall not do so again;<BR> आमोदान् हरिदन्तराणि नेतुम् Bv. 1. 15, so दिगन्तराणि; पक्षान्तरे<BR> in the other case; देश˚, राज˚, क्रिया˚ &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Various, different, manifold (used in pl.); लोको नियम्यत<BR> इवात्मदशान्तरेषु Ś. 4. 2; मन्निमित्तान्यवस्थान्तराण्यवर्णयत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">Page0123-1</a>]<BR> Dk. 118 various or different states; 160; sometimes used pleonastically<BR> with अन्यत् &c.; अन्यत्स्थानान्तरं गत्वा Pt. 1.<BR>—12 Distance (in space); व्यामो बाह्वोः सकरयोस्ततयोस्तिर्यगन्तरम्<BR> Ak.; प्रयातस्य कथंचिद् दूरमन्तरम् Ks. 5. 80.<BR>—13 Absence; तासामन्तरमासाद्य राक्षसीनां वराङ्गना Rām.; तस्यान्तरं<BR> च विदित्वा <i>ibid.</i><BR>—14 Intermediate member, remove, step, gradation (of a generation &c.);<BR> एकान्तरम् Ms. 10. 13; द्वषेकान्तरासु जातानाम् 7; एकान्तरमामन्त्रितम्<BR> P. VIII. 1. 55; तत्स्रष्टुरेकान्तरम् Ś. 7. 27 separated by one remove,<BR> See एकान्तर also.<BR>—15 Peculiarity, peculiar or characteristic possession or property; a<BR> (peculiar) sort, variety, or kind; व्रीह्यन्तरेप्यणुः Trik.; मीनो<BR> राश्यन्तरे, वेणुर्नृपान्तरे <i>ibid.</i>; प्रासङ्गो युगान्तरम् cf. also<BR> प्रधानपुरुषान्तरं सूक्ष्मम् Sāṅ. K. 37. &c.<BR>—16 Weakness, weak or vulnerable point; a failing, defect, or defective<BR> point; प्रहरेदन्तरे रिपुम्, Śabdak. सुजयः खलु तादृगन्तरे<BR> Ki. 2. 52; असहद्भिर्माममित्रैर्नित्यमन्तरदर्शिभिः Rām.; परस्यान्तरदर्शिना<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; कीटकेनेवान्तरं मार्गयमाणेन प्राप्तं मया महदन्तरम्<BR> Mk. 9; अथास्य द्वादशे वर्षे ददर्श कलिरन्तरम् Nala. 7. 2; हनूमतो<BR> वेत्ति न राक्षसोऽन्तरं न मारुतिस्तस्य च राक्षसोऽन्तरम् Rām.<BR>—17 Surety, guarantee, security; तेन तव विरूपकरणे सुकृतमन्तरे<BR> धृतम् Pt. 4 he has pledged his honour that he will not harm you; आत्मानमन्तरेऽर्पितवान्<BR> K. 247; अन्तरे च तयोर्यः स्यात् Y. 2. 239; भुवः संज्ञान्तरयोः<BR> P. III. 2. 179; धनिकाधमर्णयोरन्तरे यस्तिष्ठति विश्वासार्थं स प्रतिभूः Sk.<BR>—18 Regard, reference, account; न चैतदिष्टं माता मे यदवोचन्मदन्तरम्<BR> Rām. with reference to me; त्वदन्तरेण ऋणमेतत्.<BR>—19 Excellence, as in गुणान्तरं व्रजति शिल्पमाधातुः M. 1. 6 (this<BR> meaning may be deduced from 11).<BR>—20 A garment (परिधान).<BR>—21 Purpose, object, (तादर्थ्य) तौ वृषाविव नर्दन्तौ बलिनौ वासितान्तरे<BR> Mb. 1. 102. 41; (Malli. on R. 16. 82).<BR>—22 Concealment, hiding; पर्वतान्तरितो रविः (this sense properly<BR> belongs to अन्तरि q. v.).<BR>—23 Representative, substitution. क्षात्रमाचरतो मार्गमपि बन्धोस्त्वदन्तरे Mb. 12. 10. 3.<BR>—24 Destitution, being without (विना) which belongs to अन्तरेण.<BR> (अन्तरमवकाशावधिपरिधानान्तर्धिभेदतादर्थ्ये । छिद्रात्मीयविनावहिरवसरमध्येन्तरात्मनि<BR> च Ak.) [cf. L. <i>alter</i>]<BR>—25 Space (अवकाश); प्रेक्षतामृषिसङ्घानां बभूव न तदान्तरम्<BR> Rām. 7. 14. 19.<BR>—26 Separation (वियोग); भार्यापत्योरन्तरम् Mb. 5. 35. 43.<BR>—27 A move or skilful play in wrestling; अन्योन्यस्थान्तरप्रेप्सू प्रचकातेऽन्तरं<BR> प्रति Mb. 9. 57. 11.<BR>—28 A moulding of the pedestal and the base; षडंशं चान्तरे कर्णे<BR> उत्तरांशं तदूर्ध्वके । Māna. 13. 121; cf. स्थानात्मीयान्यतादर्थ्यरन्ध्रान्तर्धिषु<BR> चान्तरम् । परिधानेऽवधौ मध्येऽन्तरात्मनि नपुंसके । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरापत्या, अन्तरचक्रम्, अन्तरज्ञ, अन्तरतत्, अन्तरद, अन्तरदिशा, अन्तरदृश्, अन्तरपुरुषः, अन्तरपूरुषः, अन्तरपूजा, अन्तरप्रभवः, अन्तरप्रश्नः, अन्तरशायिन्, अन्तरस्थ, अन्तरस्थायिन्, अन्तरस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरापत्या
अन्तर + -अपत्या a pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरचक्रम्
अन्तर + -चक्रम् a technical term in augury Bṛ. S. chap. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरज्ञ
अन्तर + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the interior, prudent, wise, foreseeing; नान्तरज्ञाः<BR> श्रियो जातु प्रियैरासां न भूयते Ki. 11. 24 not knowing the difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतत्
अन्तर + -तत् <i>a.</i> spreading havoc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरद
अन्तर + -द <i>a.</i> cutting the interior or heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरदिशा
अन्तर + -दिशा, {@अन्तरा दिक्@} intermediate region or quarter of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरदृश्
अन्तर + -दृश् <i>a.</i> realizing the Supreme Soul (परमात्मानुसंधायिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरपुरुषः|अन्तरपुरुष
अन्तर + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः the internal man, soul (the deity<BR> that resides in man and witnesses all his deeds); तांस्तु देवाः प्रपश्यन्ति<BR> स्वस्यैवान्तरपूरुषः; Ms. 8. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरपूरुषः|अन्तरपूरुष
अन्तर + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः the internal man, soul (the deity<BR> that resides in man and witnesses all his deeds); तांस्तु देवाः प्रपश्यन्ति<BR> स्वस्यैवान्तरपूरुषः; Ms. 8. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरपूजा
अन्तर + -पूजा = अन्तर्-पूजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरप्रभवः|अन्तरप्रभव
अन्तर + -प्रभवः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">Page0123-2</a>]<BR> [अन्तराभ्यां भिन्नवर्णमातापितृभ्यां प्रभवति] one of a mixed origin<BR> or caste. (अम्बष्ठ, क्षत्तृ, करण, इ˚); अन्तरप्रभवाणां च धर्मान्नो<BR> वक्तुमर्हसि Ms. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरप्रश्नः|अन्तरप्रश्न
अन्तर + -प्रश्नः an inner question, one contained in and arising out of<BR> what has been previously mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरशायिन्
अन्तर + -शायिन्, -स्थ, -स्थायिन्, -स्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inward, internal, inherent; ˚स्थैर्गुणैः शुभ्रैर्लक्ष्यते नैव केन चित् Pt. 1. 221.<BR>—2 interposed, intervening, separate.<BR>—3 seated in the heart, an epithet of जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरस्थ
अन्तर + -शायिन्, -स्थ, -स्थायिन्, -स्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inward, internal, inherent; ˚स्थैर्गुणैः शुभ्रैर्लक्ष्यते नैव केन चित् Pt. 1. 221.<BR>—2 interposed, intervening, separate.<BR>—3 seated in the heart, an epithet of जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरस्थायिन्
अन्तर + -शायिन्, -स्थ, -स्थायिन्, -स्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inward, internal, inherent; ˚स्थैर्गुणैः शुभ्रैर्लक्ष्यते नैव केन चित् Pt. 1. 221.<BR>—2 interposed, intervening, separate.<BR>—3 seated in the heart, an epithet of जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरस्थित
अन्तर + -शायिन्, -स्थ, -स्थायिन्, -स्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inward, internal, inherent; ˚स्थैर्गुणैः शुभ्रैर्लक्ष्यते नैव केन चित् Pt. 1. 221.<BR>—2 interposed, intervening, separate.<BR>—3 seated in the heart, an epithet of जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतः|अन्तरत|अंतरतः
अन्तरतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In the interior; internally, between or betwixt; तृणमन्तरतः कृत्वा<BR> तमुवाच निशाचरम् Mb. 3. 281. 17.<BR>—2 Within (prep. with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतम|अंतरतम|अन्तरतमः
अन्तरतम <i>a.</i> Nearest, internal, most immediate, most intimate<BR> or related; like, analogous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतमः|अन्तरतम|अंतरतम
अन्तरतम + .{@-मः@} A letter of the same class; for ex. see under अन्तर <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीयम्
अन्तरीयम् [अन्तरे भवम् छ] An under garment; अतिश्लिष्टचीनांशुकान्तरीयम्<BR> Dk. 69; संजज्ञे युतकमिवान्तरीयमूर्वोः Ki. 7. 14, 9. 48; नाभौ<BR> धृतं च यद्वस्त्रमाच्छादयति जानुनी । अन्तरीयं प्रशस्तं तदच्छिन्नमुभयान्तयोः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरे|अंतरे
अन्तरे Between, amidst, amongst &c.; see अन्तर (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्य|अंतर्य|अन्तर्य्य
अन्तर्य <i>a.</i> Interior, internal; being within, in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरयति
अन्तरयति Den. P.<BR>—1 to cause to intervene, divert, put off; सर्वमेवान्यदन्तरयति<BR> K. 338; भवतु तावदन्तरयामि U. 6 well, I shall change the topic,<BR> divert the course of conversation.<BR>—2 To oppose, prevent; नैनमन्धकारराशिरन्तरयति K. 243.<BR>—3 To remove (to a distance), push after; भुवो बलैरन्तरयाम्बभूविरे<BR> Śi. 12. 29; सर्वानन्तरायानन्तरयन् K. 161; जलान्तराणीव महार्णवौघः<BR> शब्दान्तराण्यन्तरयाञ्चकार Śi. 3. 24 drowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरा|अंतरा
अन्तरा <i>ind.</i> (fr. अन्तर)<BR>—1 (Used adverbially)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) In the interior, inside, within, inwardly; भवाद्भिरन्तरा प्रोत्साह्य<BR> कोपितो वृषलः Mu. 3 inwardly, secretly.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) In the middle, between; त्रिशङ्कुरिवान्तरा तिष्ठ Ś. 2 stay<BR> between the two or in the mid-air; मैनमन्तरा प्रतिबध्नीत Ś. 6<BR> do not interrupt him (in the middle); अक्षेत्रे बीजमुत्सृष्टमन्तरैव<BR> विनश्यति Ms. 10. 71 therein; पशुमण्डूकमार्जारश्वसर्पनकुलाखुभिः ।<BR> अन्तरा गमने 4. 126; अन्तरा शकलीकृतः R. 15. 20; लाटी तु<BR> रीतिर्वैदर्भीपाञ्चाल्योरन्तरास्थिता S. D. 629; ˚रा स्था to oppose, to<BR> stand to oppose; तत्र यद्यन्तरा मृत्युर्यदि सेन्द्रा दिवौकसः । स्थास्यन्ति<BR> तानपि रणे काकुत्स्थो विहनिष्यति ॥ Rām.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) On the way, <i>en route</i>, midway; विलम्बेथां च मान्तरा Mv. 7. 28;<BR> अन्तरा चारणेभ्यस्त्वदीयं जयोदाहरणं श्रुत्वा त्वामिहस्थमुपागताः<BR> V. 1; अन्तरा दृष्टा देवी Ś. 6; अन्तरोपलभ्य Dk. 52; K. 267, 304-5;<BR> कुमारो ममाप्यन्तिकमुपागच्छन्नन्तरा त्वदीयेनान्तपालेन अवस्कन्द्य<BR> गृहीतः M. 1, अन्तरा पतिते पिण्डे सन्देहे वा पुनर्हरेत् Y. 2. 107<BR>——(<i>d</i>) In the neighbourhood, near, at hand; approaching, resembling;<BR> न द्रक्ष्यामः पुनर्जातु धार्मिकं राममन्तरा Rām. approaching or<BR> resembling Rāma.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Nearly, almost.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) In the mean time; नाद्याच्चैव तथान्तरा Ms. 2. 56; Y. 3. 20.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) At intervals, here and there; now and then, for sometime, now-now<BR> (when repeated);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">Page0124-1</a>]<BR> अन्तरा पितृसक्तमन्तरा मातृसंबद्धमन्तरा शुकनासमयं कुर्वन्नालापम्<BR> K. 118; अन्तरान्तरा निपतित here and there, at intervals; 121, 127;<BR> प्रजानुरागहेतोश्चान्तरान्तरा दर्शनं ददौ 58; Dk. 49.<BR>—2 (Used as a preposition with acc. P. II. 3. 4.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Between; पञ्चालास्त इमे … कलिन्दतनयां त्रिस्रोतसं<BR> चान्तरा B. R. 10. 86; यन्दतरा पितरं मातरं च Bṛ. Ār. Up.;<BR> ते (नामरूपे) यदन्तरा तद् ब्रह्म Ch. Up.; अन्तरा त्वां<BR> च मां च मां च कमण्डलुः Mbh.; rarely with loc.; सुमन्त्रस्य बभूवात्मा<BR> चकयोरिव चान्तरा Rām.; पादयोः शकटं चक्रुरन्तरोरावुलूखलम् Rām.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Through; तिरस्कारिणमन्तरा <i>ibid.</i><BR>——(<i>c</i>) During; अन्तरा कथाम् S. D. <i>d</i> Without, except; न च<BR> प्रयोजनमन्तरा चाणक्यः स्वप्नेऽपि चेष्टते Mu. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरांसः, अन्तरागर्भिणीन्यायः, अन्तराभवदेहः, अन्तराभवसत्त्वम्, अन्तरादिश्, अन्तराभरः, अन्तरावेदिः, अन्तरावेदी, अन्तराशृङ्गम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरांसः|अन्तरांस
अन्तरा + -अंसः the space between the shoulders, breast; अथ ˚से अभिमृश्य<BR> जपति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरागर्भिणीन्यायः|अन्तरागर्भिणीन्याय
अन्तरा + -गर्भिणीन्यायः a position similar to the foetus which resides<BR> in the womb of a female; a topic within a topic; an अधिकरण within<BR> an अधिकरण (which is not a very desirable or acceptable situation<BR> in the explanation of a ग्रन्थ); तत्र एवमन्तरागर्भिणीन्यायो भवतीति<BR> अन्यथा सूत्रं वर्ण्यते । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 62, 9. 3. 2 + 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराभवदेहः|अन्तराभवदेह
अन्तरा + -भवदेहः, -भवसत्त्वम् the soul or embodied soul existing between<BR> the two stages of death and birth (यो मरणजननयोरन्तराले स्थितः<BR> प्राणी सोऽन्तराभवसत्त्वः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराभवसत्त्वम्
अन्तरा + -भवदेहः, -भवसत्त्वम् the soul or embodied soul existing between<BR> the two stages of death and birth (यो मरणजननयोरन्तराले स्थितः<BR> प्राणी सोऽन्तराभवसत्त्वः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरादिश्
अन्तरा + -दिश् see अन्तरदिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराभरः|अन्तराभर
अन्तरा + -भरः Ved. bringing into the midst or procuring स नः शक्रश्चिदा<BR> शकद् दानवाँ अन्तराभरः Rv. 8. 32. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरावेदिः|अन्तरावेदि
अन्तरा + -वेदिः, -वेदी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a veranda resting on columns, porch, portico.<BR>—2 a kind of wall जयश्रीरन्तरावेदिर्मत्तवारणयोरिव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरावेदी
अन्तरा + -वेदिः, -वेदी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a veranda resting on columns, porch, portico.<BR>—2 a kind of wall जयश्रीरन्तरावेदिर्मत्तवारणयोरिव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराशृङ्गम्|अन्तराशृंगम्
अन्तरा + -शृङ्गम् <i>ind.</i> between the horns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरेण <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 (Used as a preposition with acc. P. II. 3. 4 अन्तरान्तरेण युक्ते)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Except, without, leaving; हरिमन्तरेण न सुखम् Sk.; क<BR> इदानीं सहकारमन्तरेण पल्लवितामतिमुक्तलतां सहते Ś. 3; क्रियान्तरान्तरायमन्तरेण<BR> आर्यं द्रष्टुमिच्छामि Mu. 3 without interfering with any other duty; न<BR> राजापराधमन्तरेण प्रजास्वकालमृत्युश्चरति U. 2; मार्भिकः को मरन्दानामन्तरेण<BR> मधुव्रतम् Bv. 1. 117.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) With regard or reference to, with respect to, about, towards,<BR> on account of; अथ भवन्तमन्तरेण कीदृशोऽस्या दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2; तदस्या<BR> देवीं वसुमतीमन्तरेण महदुपालम्भनं गतोऽस्मि Ś. 5; किं नु खलु<BR> मामन्तरेण चिन्तयति वैशंपायनः K. 178; छलितं नाम नाट्यमन्तरेण<BR> कीदृशी मालविका M. 2 how M. is faring or progressing in the dance &c.;<BR> ततस्तया भवतोऽविनयमन्तरेण परिगृहीतार्था कृता देवी M. 4.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Within, inside, into (मध्ये).<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Between, (उभयोर्मध्ये); त्वां मां चान्तरेणकमण्डलुः<BR> Mbh.; अन्तरेण हवनीयं गार्हपत्यं च Śat. Br.; अन्तरेण स्तनौ<BR> वा भ्रुवौ वा विमृज्यात् <i>ibid.</i>; Śi. 3. 3.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) During, amidst.<BR>—2 (Used as an adverb)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) between, amidst; यावद्वा मक्षिकायाः पत्त्रं तावानन्तरेणावकाशः Śat. Br.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) At heart, अन्तरेण सुस्निग्धा एषा Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरालम्
अन्तरालम्, अन्तरालकम् [अन्तरं व्यवधानसीमाम् आराति गृह्णाति,<BR> आरा-क, रस्य लत्वम्]<BR>—1 Intermediate space or region or time, interval; दंष्ट्रान्तराललग्न<BR> K. 30; आस्यान्तरालनिःसृतेन Dk. 143; दिङ्नामान्यन्तराले P. II. 2. 26;<BR> दक्षिणस्याः पूर्वस्याश्च दिशोरन्तरालं दक्षिणपूर्वा Sk.; Śi. 9. 2;<BR> पयोधरान्तरालम् K. 83; रागलज्जान्तरालवर्तिभिरीक्षणविशेषैः<BR> Dk. 17, 143 half way betwixt love and bashfulness; प्रतिमानं प्रतिच्छाया<BR> गजदन्तान्तरालयोः Trik.; oft. used for ‘room’ or ‘space’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">Page0124-2</a>]<BR> in general; त्रस्तजनदत्तान्तरालया राजवीथ्या Dk. 150; भुवनान्तरालविप्रकीर्णेन<BR> शाखासञ्चयेन K. 23, 162; अन्तराले in midway; in the middle; or midst;^1<BR> in the interval; बाष्पाम्भःपरिपतनोद्गमान्तराले in the interval<BR> between the dropping down and starting up of tears; U. 1. 31; Māl. 9. 14;<BR> अहमागच्छन्नन्तराले महता सिंहेन अभिहितः Pt. 1; कंचित्पुरुषमन्तराल<BR> एवावलम्ब्य Dk. 15; न मयान्येन वान्तराले दृष्टा Dk. 123.<BR>—2 Interior, inside, inner or middle part; छिद्रीकृतान्तरालम् Dk. 148;<BR> विषमीकृतान्तरालया K. 223.<BR>—3 Mixed tribe or caste (संकीर्णवर्ण); वर्णानां सान्तरालानां स<BR> सदाचार इष्यते.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरालदिश्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरालकम्
अन्तरालम्, अन्तरालकम् [अन्तरं व्यवधानसीमाम् आराति गृह्णाति,<BR> आरा-क, रस्य लत्वम्]<BR>—1 Intermediate space or region or time, interval; दंष्ट्रान्तराललग्न<BR> K. 30; आस्यान्तरालनिःसृतेन Dk. 143; दिङ्नामान्यन्तराले P. II. 2. 26;<BR> दक्षिणस्याः पूर्वस्याश्च दिशोरन्तरालं दक्षिणपूर्वा Sk.; Śi. 9. 2;<BR> पयोधरान्तरालम् K. 83; रागलज्जान्तरालवर्तिभिरीक्षणविशेषैः<BR> Dk. 17, 143 half way betwixt love and bashfulness; प्रतिमानं प्रतिच्छाया<BR> गजदन्तान्तरालयोः Trik.; oft. used for ‘room’ or ‘space’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">Page0124-2</a>]<BR> in general; त्रस्तजनदत्तान्तरालया राजवीथ्या Dk. 150; भुवनान्तरालविप्रकीर्णेन<BR> शाखासञ्चयेन K. 23, 162; अन्तराले in midway; in the middle; or midst;^1<BR> in the interval; बाष्पाम्भःपरिपतनोद्गमान्तराले in the interval<BR> between the dropping down and starting up of tears; U. 1. 31; Māl. 9. 14;<BR> अहमागच्छन्नन्तराले महता सिंहेन अभिहितः Pt. 1; कंचित्पुरुषमन्तराल<BR> एवावलम्ब्य Dk. 15; न मयान्येन वान्तराले दृष्टा Dk. 123.<BR>—2 Interior, inside, inner or middle part; छिद्रीकृतान्तरालम् Dk. 148;<BR> विषमीकृतान्तरालया K. 223.<BR>—3 Mixed tribe or caste (संकीर्णवर्ण); वर्णानां सान्तरालानां स<BR> सदाचार इष्यते.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरालदिश्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरालदिश्
अन्तरालम् + -दिश् <i>f.</i> the intermediate point of the compass, such as, north-east &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरि|अंतरि
अन्तरि €2 P. (अन्तर् + इ)<BR>—1 To go between, to stand in oneʼs way, intervene to separate; रात्रेरेनं<BR> तदन्तरियात् Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To exclude from, to pass over, omit.<BR>—3 To disappear, see अन्तरित below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरयति
अन्तरि + .({@-अयति@}) To come or step between, interpose; दर्दुरक उपसृत्य<BR> अन्तरयति Mk. 2 (it may also mean, ‘separates the two’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरयः|अन्तरय|अंतरयः
अन्तरयः, -रायः<BR>—1 An impediment, obstacle, hindrance, what stands in the<BR> way; स चेत् त्वमन्तरायो भवसि च्युतो विधिः R. 3. 45, 14. 65; वह्वन्तराययुक्तस्य<BR> धर्मस्य त्वरिता गतिः Pt. 3. 101; अस्य ते बाणपथवर्तिनः कृष्णसारस्य<BR> अन्तरायौ तपास्विनौ संवृत्तौ Ś. 1.<BR> v. l. standing in the way.<BR>—2 (In Vedānta) Hindrance to the concentration of mind which is said<BR> to be of four kinds, लय, विक्षेप, कषाय and रसास्वाद.<BR>—3 An intervention, a covering, screen; दाहप्रेम्ह्णा सरसबिसिनीपत्रमात्रान्तरायः Māl. 3. 12.<BR>—4 (With the Jainas) Interference or obstruction offered to those who<BR> are engaged in seeking deliverance, and consequent prevention of their<BR> accomplishment of it; one of the 8 classes of <i>karman</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरायः|अन्तराय|अंतरायः
अन्तरयः, -रायः<BR>—1 An impediment, obstacle, hindrance, what stands in the<BR> way; स चेत् त्वमन्तरायो भवसि च्युतो विधिः R. 3. 45, 14. 65; वह्वन्तराययुक्तस्य<BR> धर्मस्य त्वरिता गतिः Pt. 3. 101; अस्य ते बाणपथवर्तिनः कृष्णसारस्य<BR> अन्तरायौ तपास्विनौ संवृत्तौ Ś. 1.<BR> v. l. standing in the way.<BR>—2 (In Vedānta) Hindrance to the concentration of mind which is said<BR> to be of four kinds, लय, विक्षेप, कषाय and रसास्वाद.<BR>—3 An intervention, a covering, screen; दाहप्रेम्ह्णा सरसबिसिनीपत्रमात्रान्तरायः Māl. 3. 12.<BR>—4 (With the Jainas) Interference or obstruction offered to those who<BR> are engaged in seeking deliverance, and consequent prevention of their<BR> accomplishment of it; one of the 8 classes of <i>karman</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरित|अंतरित|अन्तरितं
अन्तरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone between, intervening.<BR>—2 Gone within, hidden, concealed, covered, screened, shielded, protected<BR> (from view) by something; पादपान्तरित एव विश्वस्तामेनां पश्यामि<BR> Ś. 1 hid behind a creeper; सारसेन स्वदेहान्तरितो राजा H. 3 screened;<BR> विटपान्तरितस्तिष्ठ Ś. 3; नलिनीपत्रान्तरितं प्रियसहचरमपश्यन्ती<BR> Ś. 4; शार्दूलचर्मान्तरितोरुपृष्टम् Ku. 7. 37 covered; Dk. 21, 146;<BR> K. 28, 152, 200; पर्वतान्तरितो रविः set. Ak.; त्वगन्तरिततृतीयलोचनम्<BR> K. 108; R. 10. 8; उन्मादमोहान्तरितोऽपि Māl. 9; तल्पमन्तरितभूमिभिः<BR> कुथैः R. 19. 2.<BR>—3 Gone in, reflected; स्फटिकभित्त्यन्तरितान् मृगशावकान् reflected<BR> in the crystal wall.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Concealed, made dormant, impeded, hindered, prevented; त्वदभिप्रायापरिज्ञानान्तरित<BR> एवायमनुनयः Mu. 2 prevented from being made; त्वद्वाञ्छान्तरितानि<BR> साध्यानि Mu. 4. 15 prevened from being actually effected &c.; द्विषत्प्रतापान्तरितोरुतेजाः<BR> Ki. 3. 45 obscured; नोपालभ्यः पुमांस्तत्र दैवान्तरितपौरुषः Pt. 2. 133.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Separated, lost to view, made invisible by interposition; मुहूर्तान्तरितमाधवा<BR> दुर्मनायमाना Māl. 8; भर्तुरेतान्यक्षराणि बिम्बान्तरितानि M. 3;<BR> धनमित्राख्ययान्तरितः Dk. 36; चन्द्रापीडनामान्तरितस्य चन्द्रमसः<BR> K. 338; प्रतिनिवर्तमानयात्राजनसंकुलेन अन्तरिते तस्मिन् Māl. 2;<BR> क्रियतां कथमन्त्यमण्डनं परलोकान्तरितस्य ते मया Ku. 4. 22 separated<BR> (from me) by the next<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">Page0125-1</a>]<BR> world, i. e. dead, deceased; मेघैरन्तरितः प्रिये तव मुखच्छायानुकारी शशी S. D.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Drowned, obscured removed, eclipsed; परलोकभयमैहिकदुःखेनान्तरितम्<BR> Dk. 82 drowned, eclipsed, obscured; वीरलोकसाधुवादेनान्तरितः समरतूर्यरवः<BR> Ve. 4 drowned; विस्मयान्तरितशोकवृत्तान्ता K. 322; कार्यान्तरितोत्कण्ठम्<BR> V. 3. 4 forgotten, removed; इन्दुप्रकाशान्तरितोडुतुल्याः R. 16. 65 obscured by moon-light.<BR>—5 Disappeared, vanished, departed, retired, withdrawn; (महामृगः)<BR> आश्रमान्तरितः शीघ्रं प्लवमानो महाजवः Mb. 3. 311. 9. अन्तरिते<BR> तस्मिञ्शबरसेनापतौ K. 33; नाथदेहस्पर्शेन अन्तरित एव सन्तापः<BR> U. 6 has disappeared, has been removed.<BR>—6 Passed over, omitted; अये मध्यमाम्बावृत्तान्तोऽन्तरित एवार्येण U. 1;<BR> कथान्तरेणान्तरितमिदम् M. 5 put off, delayed.<BR>—7 Slighted, despised.<BR>—8 (In Math.) That which remains, the remainder<BR>—9 A technical term in architecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षम्
अन्तरि(री)क्षम्<BR> [अन्तः स्वर्गपृथिव्योर्मध्ये ईक्ष्यते, ईक्ष् कर्मणि घञ्,<BR> अन्तः ऋक्षाणि अस्य वा पृषो ˚पक्षे ह्रस्वः ऋकारस्य रित्वं वा Tv., according<BR> to Nir. अन्तरा द्यावापृथिव्योः क्षान्तम् अवस्थितं भवति, or अन्तरा<BR> इमे द्यावापृथिव्यौ क्षयति निवसति; or शरीरेष्वन्तः अक्षयं न पृथिव्यादिवत् क्षीयते]<BR>—1 The intermediate region between heaven and earth; the air, atmosphere,<BR> sky (अन्तरा द्यावापृथिव्योर्मध्ये ईक्ष्यमाणं व्योम Sāy.) दिवं च<BR> पृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षमथो स्वः Sandhyā Mantra; योऽन्तरेणाकाश आसीत्तदन्तरिक्षमभवदीक्षं<BR> हैतन्नाम ततः पुरान्तरा वा इदमीक्षमभूदिति तस्मादन्तरिक्षं Śat. Br.<BR> दिव्यन्तरिक्षे भूमौ च घोरमुत्पातजं भयम् Rām. 2. 1. 43<BR>—2 The middle of the three spheres or regions of life.<BR>—3 Talc. (Mar. अभ्रक)<BR>—4 A synonym of a pent-roof. Māna. 18. 174-75.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरिक्षोदर, अन्तरिक्षकान्तः, अन्तरिक्षक्षित्, अन्तरिक्षसद्, अन्तरिक्षगः, अन्तरिक्षचरः, अन्तरिक्षगत, अन्तरिक्षजलम्, अन्तरिक्षप्रा, अन्तरिक्षप्रुत्, अन्तरिक्षलोकः, अन्तरिक्षशंसित, अन्तरिक्षसद्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीक्षम्
अन्तरि(री)क्षम्<BR> [अन्तः स्वर्गपृथिव्योर्मध्ये ईक्ष्यते, ईक्ष् कर्मणि घञ्,<BR> अन्तः ऋक्षाणि अस्य वा पृषो ˚पक्षे ह्रस्वः ऋकारस्य रित्वं वा Tv., according<BR> to Nir. अन्तरा द्यावापृथिव्योः क्षान्तम् अवस्थितं भवति, or अन्तरा<BR> इमे द्यावापृथिव्यौ क्षयति निवसति; or शरीरेष्वन्तः अक्षयं न पृथिव्यादिवत् क्षीयते]<BR>—1 The intermediate region between heaven and earth; the air, atmosphere,<BR> sky (अन्तरा द्यावापृथिव्योर्मध्ये ईक्ष्यमाणं व्योम Sāy.) दिवं च<BR> पृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षमथो स्वः Sandhyā Mantra; योऽन्तरेणाकाश आसीत्तदन्तरिक्षमभवदीक्षं<BR> हैतन्नाम ततः पुरान्तरा वा इदमीक्षमभूदिति तस्मादन्तरिक्षं Śat. Br.<BR> दिव्यन्तरिक्षे भूमौ च घोरमुत्पातजं भयम् Rām. 2. 1. 43<BR>—2 The middle of the three spheres or regions of life.<BR>—3 Talc. (Mar. अभ्रक)<BR>—4 A synonym of a pent-roof. Māna. 18. 174-75.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तरिक्षोदर, अन्तरिक्षकान्तः, अन्तरिक्षक्षित्, अन्तरिक्षसद्, अन्तरिक्षगः, अन्तरिक्षचरः, अन्तरिक्षगत, अन्तरिक्षजलम्, अन्तरिक्षप्रा, अन्तरिक्षप्रुत्, अन्तरिक्षलोकः, अन्तरिक्षशंसित, अन्तरिक्षसद्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षोदर
अन्तरिक्षम् + -उदर <i>a.</i> whose inside is as wide as the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षोदरम्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -उदर + .({@-रम्@}) the interior of the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षकान्तः|अन्तरिक्षकान्त
अन्तरिक्षम् + -कान्तः a class of ten-storeyed buildings. Māna. 28. 14-15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षक्षित्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -क्षित्, -सद् <i>a.</i> dwelling in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षसद्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -क्षित्, -सद् <i>a.</i> dwelling in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षगः|अन्तरिक्षग
अन्तरिक्षम् + -गः, -चरः a bird (moving through the atmosphere). ततोऽन्तरिक्षगो<BR> वाचं व्याजहार नलं तदा Mb. 3. 53. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षचरः|अन्तरिक्षचर
अन्तरिक्षम् + -गः, -चरः a bird (moving through the atmosphere). ततोऽन्तरिक्षगो<BR> वाचं व्याजहार नलं तदा Mb. 3. 53. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षगत
अन्तरिक्षम् + -गत <i>a.</i> moving in air; अब्रवीच्च तदा वाक्यं जातक्रोधो विभीषणः ।<BR> अन्तरिक्षगतः Rām. 6. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षजलम्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -जलम् water of the atmosphere, dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षप्रा
अन्तरिक्षम् + -प्रा <i>a.</i> [अन्तरिक्षं प्राति पूरयति, प्रा-विच्] filling the<BR> atmosphere; illuminating the sky, travelling through the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षप्रुत्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -प्रुत् <i>a.</i> [अन्तरिक्षं प्रवते गच्छति, प्रु क्विप्] floating<BR> over the atmosphere, sweeping or going through it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षलोकः|अन्तरिक्षलोक
अन्तरिक्षम् + -लोकः the intermediate region, regarded as a distinct world;<BR> त्रयो लोका एत एव वागेवायं लोकः (earth) मनोन्तरिक्षलोकः, प्राणोऽसौ<BR> लोकः (heaven) Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षशंसित
अन्तरिक्षम् + -शंसित <i>a.</i> sharpened in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्षसद्यम्
अन्तरिक्षम् + -सद्यम् [अन्तरिक्षे सद्यं सदनं, सद् भावे यत्] dwelling<BR> or residence in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष्य
अन्तरि(री)क्ष्य <i>a.</i><BR> [भवार्थे यत्] Aerial, atmospheric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीक्ष्य
अन्तरि(री)क्ष्य <i>a.</i><BR> [भवार्थे यत्] Aerial, atmospheric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीपः|अन्तरीप|अन्तरीपं|अंतरीपः
अन्तरीपः [अन्तः मध्ये गता आपो यस्य बहु. अ P. V. 4. 74.<BR> अप ईत् द्वयन्तरुपसर्गेभ्योऽपईन्; P. VI. 3. 97] A portion of land<BR> stretching out into the sea, promontory; an island (being situated in and<BR> surrounded on all sides by, water). सान्तरीपश्च सागरः Śiva B. 18. 13;<BR> दृष्ट्वा तानि ध्रुवमुपगतः सैन्धवादन्तरीपात् । Rām. Ch. 4. 96<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरे|अंतरे
अन्तरे, -रेण<BR> See under अन्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरे, -रेण<BR> See under अन्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गम्|अंतर्गम्
अन्तर्गम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go between, interpose, intervene (so as to exclude).<BR>—2 To be included or comprised in.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear (mostly used in past part. only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गत|अंतर्गत|अन्तर्गतं
अन्तर्गत <i>p. p.</i>, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gone into or between, crept into (as a bad word &c.).<BR>—2 Being or seated in, included in or by, existing in, belonging to; ˚शवे<BR> ग्रामे Ms. 4. 108; लघुद्वीपा जम्बूद्वीपान्तर्गता एव H. 3; पार्थिवानि<BR> च भूतानि सागरान्तर्गतानि च Rām.<BR>—3 Being in the interior, hidden, concealed, internal, inward, secret,<BR> suppressed; अन्तर्गतमपास्तं मे रजसोऽपि परं तमः Ku. 6. 60 inward;<BR> सौमित्रिरन्तर्गतबाष्पकण्ठः R. 14. 53 with suppressed tears; K. 60;<BR> ˚तां हृदयशुद्धिम् 135 inward; अन्तर्गतं प्राणाभृतां हि वेद सर्वं<BR> भवान्भावम् R. 2. 43 internal, seated in the breast or heart; ˚फलारम्भाः 10. 59;<BR> ˚तो हृदयाभिलाषः K. 143; ˚तेन चन्द्रापीडेन 198; नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च<BR> लक्ष्यतेऽन्तर्गतं मनः inward or secret motives of the mind Pt. 1. 44;<BR> बाह्यैर्विभावयेल्लिङ्गैर्भावमन्तर्गतं नृणाम् Ms. 8. 25; ˚गतप्रार्थनम्<BR> Ś. 7. 2 inwardly longing (for the same).<BR>—4 Slipped out of memory, forgotten.<BR>—5 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>—6 Destroyed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तर्गतोपमा, अन्तर्गतमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गामिन्
अन्तर्गत <i>p. p.</i>, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gone into or between, crept into (as a bad word &c.).<BR>—2 Being or seated in, included in or by, existing in, belonging to; ˚शवे<BR> ग्रामे Ms. 4. 108; लघुद्वीपा जम्बूद्वीपान्तर्गता एव H. 3; पार्थिवानि<BR> च भूतानि सागरान्तर्गतानि च Rām.<BR>—3 Being in the interior, hidden, concealed, internal, inward, secret,<BR> suppressed; अन्तर्गतमपास्तं मे रजसोऽपि परं तमः Ku. 6. 60 inward;<BR> सौमित्रिरन्तर्गतबाष्पकण्ठः R. 14. 53 with suppressed tears; K. 60;<BR> ˚तां हृदयशुद्धिम् 135 inward; अन्तर्गतं प्राणाभृतां हि वेद सर्वं<BR> भवान्भावम् R. 2. 43 internal, seated in the breast or heart; ˚फलारम्भाः 10. 59;<BR> ˚तो हृदयाभिलाषः K. 143; ˚तेन चन्द्रापीडेन 198; नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च<BR> लक्ष्यतेऽन्तर्गतं मनः inward or secret motives of the mind Pt. 1. 44;<BR> बाह्यैर्विभावयेल्लिङ्गैर्भावमन्तर्गतं नृणाम् Ms. 8. 25; ˚गतप्रार्थनम्<BR> Ś. 7. 2 inwardly longing (for the same).<BR>—4 Slipped out of memory, forgotten.<BR>—5 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>—6 Destroyed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तर्गतोपमा, अन्तर्गतमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गतोपमा
अन्तर्गत + -उपमा a concealed simile (the particle of comparison being omitted.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गतमनस्
अन्तर्गत + -मनस् = अन्तर्मनस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धा|अंतर्धा
अन्तर्धा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place or keep within, deposit; उदुम्बरशाखामन्तर्धाय अभिषिञ्चति Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To receive within or into oneself, admit, take in; तथा विश्वंभरे<BR> देवि मामन्तर्धातुमर्हसि R. 15. 81; contain, comprise, include; (शास्त्रमेतत्)<BR> अन्तर्धास्यति तत्सर्वमेतद्वः कथितं मया Mb.<BR>—3 To indicate, exhibit, display.<BR>—4 To hide or conceal oneself from, avoid the sight of, (with abl. and<BR> used in <i>Ātm.</i>); उपाध्यायादन्तर्धत्ते P. I. 4. 28. Com. अन्तर्धत्स्व<BR> रघुव्याघ्रात् Bk. 5. 32; मत्तो मान्तर्धिथाः सीते 6. 15. अन्तर्दधानां<BR> रक्षोभ्यः 8. 71;<BR>—5 To cover up, conceal from view, hide, obscure, envelope, wrap up, veil;<BR> सध्वजं सरथं साश्वं भीष्ममन्तर्दधे शरैः Mb. 6. 118. 37 eclipse<BR> (fig.); अनृतेनात्मानमन्तर्धाय Ch. Up.; भौमं (रजः) अन्तर्दधे<BR> लोकमावृत्य सवितुः प्रभां Rām. enveloped, covered; पितुरन्तर्दधे<BR> कीर्तिं शीलवृत्तिसमाधिभिः Mb. obscured or eclipsed. ━<i>pass.</i> —1 To<BR> be received within, be absorbed; to be covered up or concealed, be obscured<BR> or rendered invisible, become invisible; to vanish, disappear, cease to<BR> exist; इषुभिर्व्यतिसर्पद्भिरादित्योऽन्तरधीयत Mb.; ते चान्तर्दधिरे<BR> नागाः <i>ibid.</i>; रात्रिरादित्योदयेऽन्तर्धीयते Nir. disappears; आत्मन्यन्तर्दधे,<BR> तत्रैवान्तरधीयत &c.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> (-धापयति) To render invisible, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धा|अंतर्धा
अन्तर्धा [धा भावे अङ्] Covering, concealment &c.; अन्तर्धामुपययुरुत्पलावलीषु Śi. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धानम्
अन्तर्धानम् [धा-ल्युट्] Being invisible, disappearance, passing<BR> out of sight; ˚व्यसनरसिका रात्रिकापालिकीयम् K. P. 10; ˚गम् or इ<BR> to become invisible, disappear.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तर्धानगत, अन्तर्धानचर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धानगत
अन्तर्धानम् + -गत <i>a.</i> disappeared, invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धानचर
अन्तर्धानम् + -चर <i>a.</i> moving invisibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धायक|अंतर्धायक
अन्तर्धायक <i>a.</i> Concealing, rendering invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0125-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धिः|अन्तर्धि|अन्तर्द्धिः|अंतर्धिः
अन्तर्धिः <i>f.</i> [धा-कि] Disappearance, concealment; hiding oneself<BR> from (another); अन्तर्धौ येनादर्शनमिच्छति P. I. 4. 28; अन्तर्धिं<BR> द्रुतमिव कर्तुमश्रुवर्षैः Śi. 8. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हित|अंतर्हित|अन्तर्हितं
अन्तर्हित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed between, separated, rendered invisible by interposition, hidden,<BR> concealed; अब्रुवन्ब्राह्मणाः सिद्धा भूतान्यन्तर्हितानि च Mb. 3. 37. 21.<BR> अन्तर्हिता शकुन्तला वनराज्या Ś. 4; covered (with something else);<BR> अन्तर्हिताशापथो जलदकाल इव K. 293; शेष्वानन्तर्हितायां त्वं भूमौ<BR> Rām. uncovered or bare ground; पात्रेषु दर्भान्तर्हितेषु अप आसिच्य<BR> Āśval.; अन्तर्हिते आवाम् V. 2; अन्तर्हिता यदि भवेद्वनिता न वेति<BR> Mk. 3. 4 a disguised male, a female in male dress.<BR>—2 Disappeared, vanished, become invisible; इति मन्त्रयमाणः स्वयमन्तर्हितः<BR> Ś. 4 withdrew from sight, became invisible; अन्तर्हिते शशिनि Ś. 4. 2;<BR> तस्यायमन्तर्हितसौधभाजः R. 13. 40 dwelling in a palace hidden<BR> under (the waters).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तर्हितात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हितात्मन्
अन्तर्हित + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भू|अंतर्भू
अन्तर्भू €1 P. To be contained, comprised or included in; be inherent<BR> or implied in; कदा न्वन्तर्वरुणे भुवानि Rv. 7. 86. 2. केचिदन्तर्भवन्त्येषु<BR> K. P. 8; गुणाश्चिरन्तनैरुक्ता ओजस्यन्तर्भवन्ति ते S. D.; अन्तर्भूय<BR> रहस्येषु तैर्वशीक्रियते हि सः Ks. 34. 204; वैदिके कर्मयोगे तु सर्वाण्येतान्यशेषतः ।<BR> अन्तर्भवन्ति कमशस्तस्मिंस्तस्मिन्क्रियाविधौ ॥ Ms. 12. 87.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To contain, include, imply, involve; अन्तर्भावितण्यर्थोऽत्र<BR> नमिः P. III. 1. 88. Sk. involving a causal sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भव|अंतर्भव
अन्तर्भव <i>a.</i> Inward, internal, inwardly situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावः|अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः
अन्तर्भावः<BR>—1 being included or comprised in, inclusion; तेषां गुणानामोजस्यन्तर्भावः K. P. 8.<BR>—2 Inherent or natural condition or disposition.<BR>—3 Disappearance, becoming invisible; सर्वे अन्तर्भावं गताः Dk. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावना|अंतर्भावना
अन्तर्भावना<BR>—1 Inclusion.<BR>—2 Inward meditation or anxiety.<BR>—3 A technical term in arithmetic, rectification of numbers by the differences<BR> of the products.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूत|अंतर्भूत|अन्तर्भूतः
अन्तर्भूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Included or contained in; कालभावाध्वदेशानामन्तर्भूतक्रियान्तरैः ।<BR> सर्वैरकर्मकैर्योगे कर्मत्वमुपजायते ॥ Hariv.<BR>—2 Inward, internal, internally situated; एष वै भगवान् विष्णुरन्तर्भूतः सनातनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्य|अंतर्य|अन्तर्य्य
अन्तर्य <i>a.</i> Inner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तस्त्यम्
अन्तस्त्यम् Intestines; Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तार
अन्तार <i>a.</i> [अन्त ऋ अण्] A cowherd; Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ति|अंति|अन्तिः
अन्ति <i>ind.</i> [अन्त-इ] Ved.<BR>—1 Near, before, in the presence of; न ही नु वो मरुतो अन्त्यस्मे Rv. 1. 167. 9, 1. 79. 11.<BR>—2 (Prep.) To, in the vicinity of (with gen.); मुग्धप्रभीतवदुपेयतुरन्ति<BR> मात्रोः Bhāg. 10. 8. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिः|अन्ति|अंति
अन्ति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> An elder sister (in dramas).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्त्यूति, अन्तिगृहम्, अन्तिदेव, अन्तिमित्र, अन्तिवाम, अन्तिषुम्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यूति|अन्त्यूतिः
अन्ति + -ऊति <i>a.</i> ready with help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यूतिः|अन्त्यूति
अन्ति + -ऊति + .({@-तिः@} <i>f.</i>) protection of what is near (आसन्नरक्षण);<BR> अर्चामि सुम्नयन्नहमन्त्यूतिं मयांभुवम् Rv. 1. 138. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिगृहम्
अन्ति + -गृहम् a house near oneʼs own dwelling, the neighbourhood of the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिदेव
अन्ति + -देव <i>a.</i> being near the god; an adversary (at dice); पाथो<BR> हि ष्मा वृषणाअन्तिदेवम् Rv. 1. 180. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिमित्र
अन्ति + -मित्र, -वाम, -षुम्ण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">Page0126-2</a>]<BR>. <i>a.</i> near or at hand with help, wealth, or kindness;<BR> अन्तिवामा दूरे Rv. 7. 77. 4 (निकटस्थधना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिवाम
अन्ति + -मित्र, -वाम, -षुम्ण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">Page0126-2</a>]<BR>. <i>a.</i> near or at hand with help, wealth, or kindness;<BR> अन्तिवामा दूरे Rv. 7. 77. 4 (निकटस्थधना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिषुम्ण
अन्ति + -मित्र, -वाम, -षुम्ण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">Page0126-2</a>]<BR>. <i>a.</i> near or at hand with help, wealth, or kindness;<BR> अन्तिवामा दूरे Rv. 7. 77. 4 (निकटस्थधना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिका|अंतिका
अन्तिका<BR>—1 An elder sister.<BR>—2 An oven, fire-place.<BR>—3 N. of a plant (सा(शा)तलाख्यौषधिः; Mar. शिकेकाई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक <i>a.</i> [अन्तः सामीप्यम् अस्यास्तीति मत्वथींयः ठन्; according<BR> to Nir. from आ-नी; अन्तिकं कस्मात् आनीतं भवति सन्निकृष्टत्वात्]<BR>—1 Near, proximate (with gen. or abl. P. II. 3. 34). वैरमन्तिकमासाद्य<BR> यः प्रीतिं कर्तुमिच्छति । मृन्मयस्येव भग्नस्य यथा सन्धिर्न विद्यते ।<BR> Mb. 12. 139. 69.<BR>—2 Reaching to the end of, reaching to; नासान्तिक Ms. 2. 46.<BR>—3 Lasting till, until; as far as, up to; षट्त्रिंशदाब्दिकं चर्यं गुरौ<BR> त्रैवेदिकं व्रतम् Ms. 3. 1; ग्रहणान्तिकम् Y. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकम्
अन्तिक + .{@-कम्@} Nearness, proximity, vicinity, presence; न त्यजन्ति ममान्तिकम्<BR> H. 1. 43; oft. in comp.; ˚न्यस्त R. 2. 24; कर्ण-, ˚चरः Ś. 1. 23;<BR> सिंहासनान्तिकचरेण सहोपसर्पन् M. 1. 12 a servant in attendance<BR> upon the throne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकः|अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं
अन्तिक + .{@-कः@} A class of two storeyed buildings; Māna. 20. 94. 26-27.<BR>━<i>adv.</i> (with abl. or gen. or as last member of comp.) Near (to), in<BR> the vicinity; अन्तिकं ग्रामात्-ग्रामस्य वा Sk.; into the presence or<BR> proximity of; दूरस्थस्यैत्य चान्तिकम् Ms. 2. 197; प्रविष्टे पितुरन्तिकम्<BR> Rām.; so जनान्तिकम्, मृगान्तिकम्; अन्तिकेन near (with gen.) अन्तेकन<BR> ग्रामस्य P. II. 3. 35; अन्तिकात् near, closely, within the presence<BR> of; from the proximity of, from near, from (abl. or gen. or acc.); ˚कादागतः<BR> P. VI. 2. 49; रजःकणैःस्पृशद्भिर्गात्रमन्तिकात् Rām.; कीणीयाद्यस्त्वपत्यार्थं<BR> मातापित्रोर्यमन्तिकात् Ms. 9. 174 from; so नैव प्रवृत्तिं शृणुमस्तयोः<BR> कस्यचिदन्तिकात् Rām.; अन्तिके near, closely, in the presence of<BR> or proximity of; दूरस्थं चान्तिके च तत् Bg. 13. 15; दमयन्त्यास्तदान्तिके<BR> निपेतुः Nala. 1. 22; ˚के स्त्रियाः Ms. 2. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तिकाश्रयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकाश्रयः|अन्तिकाश्रय
अन्तिक + -आश्रयः resorting to what is near, contiguous support (that given<BR> by a tree to a creeper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तितः|अन्तित|अंतितः
अन्तितः <i>ind.</i> Ved. Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
अन्तिम <i>a.</i> [अन्ते भवः, अन्त डिमच्]<BR>—1 Immediately following.<BR>—2 Last, final, ultimate; अजातमृतमूर्खाणां वरमाद्यौ न चान्तिमः H. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्तिमाङ्कः, अन्तिमाङ्गुलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिमाङ्कः|अन्तिमाङ्क|अंतिमांक
अन्तिम + -अङ्कः the last digit, the number nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिमाङ्गुलिः|अन्तिमाङ्गुलि|अंतिमांगुलि
अन्तिम + -अङ्गुलिः the little finger (कनिष्ठिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ती|अंती
अन्ती An oven, fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अन्त्य <i>a.</i> [अन्ते भवति वसति &c., अन्ताय हितः; अन्त-यत्]<BR>—1 Last, final (as a letter, word &c.); last (in time, order or place)<BR> P. I. 1. 47; as ह of letters, Revatī of asterisms, Mīna of the<BR> zodiacal signs. &c.; अन्त्ये वयसि in old age R. 9. 79; अन्त्यम् ऋणम्<BR> R. 1. 71 last debt; ˚मण्डनम् 8. 71 last funeral decoration, Ku. 4. 22.<BR>—2 Immediately following (in comp.); अष्टम˚ ninth.<BR>—3 perishable, transitory; देहाद्यपार्थमसदन्यमभिज्ञमात्रं (विन्देत)<BR> Bhāg. 12. 8. 44.<BR>—4 Lowest (in rank, degree or position), undermost, worst, inferior, base,<BR> vile, wretched; ˚अवस्थां गतः Pt. 4. 110 reduced to the worst plight;<BR> अन्त्यासु दशासु Pt. 1. 336 at perilous (critical) times; belonging<BR> to the lowest caste; चण्डाल ˚स्त्रियः Ms. 11. 175; ˚स्त्रीनिषेविणः 12. 59;<BR> अन्त्यादपि वरं रत्नं स्त्रीरत्नं दुष्कुलादपि;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">Page0127-1</a>]<BR> शूद्राश्च सन्तः शूद्राणामन्त्यानामन्त्ययोनयः (साक्ष्यं कुर्युः) 8. 68, 3. 9, 4. 79;<BR> Y. 1. 148, 2. 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यः|अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं
अन्त्य + .{@-न्त्यः@}<BR>—1 A man of the lowest caste; see above.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (मुस्ता Mar. नागरमोथा) (<i>f.</i> also) (the roots<BR> of which are prescribed for colic).<BR>—3 The last syllable of a word.<BR>—4 The last lunar month i. e. Phālguna.<BR>—5 A Mleccha^1, foreigner, barbarian. अन्त्येषु स विनिक्षिप्य पुत्रान् यदुपुरोगमान् Mb. 1. 86. 12.<BR>—6 (In Vaiśeṣika Phil.) A name for the category विशेष; अन्त्यो नित्यद्रव्यवृत्तिर्विशेषः<BR> परिकीर्तितः Bhāṣā P.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्या
अन्त्य + .{@-न्त्या@}<BR>—1 A technical name for त्रिज्या in astronomy.<BR>—2 A woman of the lowest tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यम्|अंत्यम्
अन्त्य + .{@-न्त्यम्@}<BR>—1 A measure of number; 1000 trillions (1000,000,000,000,000)^1.<BR>—2 The 12th sign of the zodiac.<BR>—3 The last member or term of a progression (series), the last figure;<BR> स्थाप्योन्तवर्गो द्विगुणान्त्यनिघ्नः Līlā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्त्यानुप्रासः, अन्त्यावसायिन्, अन्त्याश्रमिन्, अन्त्याहुतिः, अन्त्येष्टिः, अन्त्यर्णम्, अन्त्यगमनम्, अन्त्यज, अन्त्यजन्मन्, अन्त्यजाति, अन्त्यजातीय, अन्त्यधनम्, अन्त्यपदम्, अन्त्यमूलम्, अन्त्यभम्, अन्त्ययुगम्, अन्त्ययोनि, अन्त्यलोपः, अन्त्यवर्णः, अन्त्यवर्णा, अन्त्यविपुला<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0126-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यानुप्रासः|अन्त्यानुप्रास
अन्त्य + -अनुप्रासः see under अनुप्रास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायिन्
अन्त्य + -अवसायिन् <i>m., f.</i> ({@˚यी, ˚यिनी@}) a man or woman of the<BR> lowest caste, begotten by a cāṇḍāla on a Niṣādī woman; निषादस्त्री<BR> तु चाण्डालात्पुत्रमन्त्यावसायितम् । स्मशानगोचरं सूते बाह्यानामपि गर्हितम् ॥<BR> Ms. 10. 39; the following 7 are regarded as belonging to this class;<BR> चाण्डालः श्वपचः क्षत्ता सूतो वैदेहकस्तथा । मागधायोगवौ चैव सप्तैतेऽन्त्यावसायिनः<BR> ॥ सोऽहमन्त्यावसायानां हराम्येनां प्रतिगृहात् Mb. 12. 141. 41; see अन्तेवसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायी
अन्त्य + -अवसायिन् <i>m., f.</i> ({@˚यी, ˚यिनी@}) a man or woman of the<BR> lowest caste, begotten by a cāṇḍāla on a Niṣādī woman; निषादस्त्री<BR> तु चाण्डालात्पुत्रमन्त्यावसायितम् । स्मशानगोचरं सूते बाह्यानामपि गर्हितम् ॥<BR> Ms. 10. 39; the following 7 are regarded as belonging to this class;<BR> चाण्डालः श्वपचः क्षत्ता सूतो वैदेहकस्तथा । मागधायोगवौ चैव सप्तैतेऽन्त्यावसायिनः<BR> ॥ सोऽहमन्त्यावसायानां हराम्येनां प्रतिगृहात् Mb. 12. 141. 41; see अन्तेवसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायिनी
अन्त्य + -अवसायिन् <i>m., f.</i> ({@˚यी, ˚यिनी@}) a man or woman of the<BR> lowest caste, begotten by a cāṇḍāla on a Niṣādī woman; निषादस्त्री<BR> तु चाण्डालात्पुत्रमन्त्यावसायितम् । स्मशानगोचरं सूते बाह्यानामपि गर्हितम् ॥<BR> Ms. 10. 39; the following 7 are regarded as belonging to this class;<BR> चाण्डालः श्वपचः क्षत्ता सूतो वैदेहकस्तथा । मागधायोगवौ चैव सप्तैतेऽन्त्यावसायिनः<BR> ॥ सोऽहमन्त्यावसायानां हराम्येनां प्रतिगृहात् Mb. 12. 141. 41; see अन्तेवसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्याश्रमिन्
अन्त्य + -आश्रमिन् <i>m.</i> one who belongs to the last or mendicant order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्याहुतिः|अन्त्याहुति
अन्त्य + -आहुतिः, -इष्टिः <i>f.</i>, {@-कर्मन्, -क्रिया@}<BR> last or funeral oblations, sacrifices or rites;<BR> ˚कर्म Ms. 11. 197, 5. 168; अन्त्याहुतिं हावयितुं सविप्राः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्येष्टिः|अन्त्येष्टि
अन्त्य + -आहुतिः, -इष्टिः <i>f.</i>, {@-कर्मन्, -क्रिया@}<BR> last or funeral oblations, sacrifices or rites;<BR> ˚कर्म Ms. 11. 197, 5. 168; अन्त्याहुतिं हावयितुं सविप्राः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यर्णम्
अन्त्य + -ऋणम् the last of the three debts which every one has to pay,<BR> i. e. begetting children; see अनृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यगमनम्
अन्त्य + -गमनम् intercourse by a woman of the higher caste with a man<BR> of the lowest caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यज|अन्त्यजः
अन्त्य + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 latest born, younger<BR>—2 belonging to the lowest caste; ˚जैर्नृभिः Ms. 4. 61; ˚स्त्री 8. 385.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजः|अन्त्यज
अन्त्य + -ज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a śūdra (अन्त्यः सन् जायते, वर्णमध्ये शेषभवत्वात्).<BR>—2 one of the 7 inferior tribes; cāṇḍāla &c.; रजकश्चर्मकारश्च<BR> नटो वरुड एव च । कैवर्तमेदभिल्लाश्च सप्तैते चान्त्यजाः स्मृताः ॥<BR> Yama Smṛti; also Ms. 8. 279; Y. 1. 273.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजा
अन्त्य + -ज + .({@-जा@}) a woman of the lowest caste; Ms. 11. 59, 171; Y. 3. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजन्मन्
अन्त्य + -जन्मन्, -जाति, -जातीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one belonging to the lowest caste; प्रतिग्रहस्तु क्रियते शूद्रादप्यन्त्यजन्मनः Ms. 10. 110.<BR>—2 a Śūdra; ˚तिता Ms. 12. 9.<BR>—3 a cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजाति|अन्त्यजातिः
अन्त्य + -ज + .({@-जा@}) a woman of the lowest caste; Ms. 11. 59, 171; Y. 3. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजातीय
अन्त्य + -ज + .({@-जा@}) a woman of the lowest caste; Ms. 11. 59, 171; Y. 3. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यधनम्
अन्त्य + -धनम् the last term of a progression or series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यपदम्
अन्त्य + -पदम्, -मूलम् the last or greatest root (in a square).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यमूलम्
अन्त्य + -पदम्, -मूलम् the last or greatest root (in a square).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यभम्
अन्त्य + -भम्<BR>—1 the last lunar mansion रेवती.<BR>—2 the last sign of the Zodiac; मीन Pisces..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्ययुगम्
अन्त्य + -युगम् the last or Kali age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्ययोनि|अन्त्ययोनिः
अन्त्य + -योनि <i>a.</i> of the lowest origin; अन्त्यानामन्त्ययोनयः<BR> (साक्ष्यम्) Ms. 8. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्ययोनिः|अन्त्ययोनि
अन्त्य + -योनि + .({@-निः@}) the lowest source or origin<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यलोपः|अन्त्यलोप
अन्त्य + -लोपः dropping of the last letter or syllable of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यवर्णः|अन्त्यवर्ण|अन्त्यवर्ण्ण
अन्त्य + -वर्णः, -वर्णा a man or woman of the lowest caste, a śūdra male or female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यवर्णा
अन्त्य + -वर्णः, -वर्णा a man or woman of the lowest caste, a śūdra male or female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यविपुला
अन्त्य + -विपुला N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यकः|अन्त्यक|अंत्यकः
अन्त्यकः A man of the lowest tribe. See अन्त्यज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रम्
अन्त्रम् [अन्त्यते बध्यते देहोऽनेन, अन्त्-करणे ष्ट्रन्; according<BR> to Uṇ. 4. 163 अम्-क्त्र] An entrail, intestine; अन्त्रभेदनं क्रियते<BR> प्रश्रयश्च Mv. 3 the vitals of the heart are rent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">Page0127-2</a>]<BR> (मर्मभिदः वाचः उच्यन्ते इत्यर्थः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्री
अन्त्रम् + .{@-न्त्री@} N. of a plant [used against colic or wind in the stomach<BR> (Mar. वरधारा); cf. अजान्त्री, छगलान्त्री].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्त्रादः, अन्त्रकूजः, अन्त्रकूजनम्, अन्त्रविकूजनम्, अन्त्रपाचक, अन्त्रमांसम्, अन्त्रवृद्धिः, अन्त्रशिला, अन्त्रस्रज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रादः|अन्त्राद
अन्त्रम् + -आदः a worm in the intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रकूजः|अन्त्रकूज
अन्त्रम् + -कूजः, -कूजनम्, -विकूजनम् the rumbling noise in the bowels;<BR> पक्वाशयस्थोन्त्रकूजं शूलं नाभौ करोति वा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रकूजनम्
अन्त्रम् + -कूजः, -कूजनम्, -विकूजनम् the rumbling noise in the bowels;<BR> पक्वाशयस्थोन्त्रकूजं शूलं नाभौ करोति वा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रविकूजनम्
अन्त्रम् + -कूजः, -कूजनम्, -विकूजनम् the rumbling noise in the bowels;<BR> पक्वाशयस्थोन्त्रकूजं शूलं नाभौ करोति वा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रपाचक
अन्त्रम् + -पाचक [अन्त्रस्थं दोषं पाचयति] N. of a medicinal plant<BR> AEschynomene Grandiflora. (सं. वसन; Mar. तमालपत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रमांसम्
अन्त्रम् + -मांसम् a kind of roasted flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रवृद्धिः|अन्त्रवृद्धि
अन्त्रम् + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> inguinal hernia, rupture, swelling of the scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रशिला
अन्त्रम् + -शिला N. of a river rising from the Vindhya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रस्रज्
अन्त्रम् + -स्रज् <i>f.</i> a garland of intestines (worn by नृसिंह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रंधमिः|अन्त्रन्धमि|अन्त्रंधमि|अंत्रंधमिः
अन्त्रंधमिः <i>f.</i> Indigestion, inflammation of bowels; flatulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्द्|अंद्
अन्द् €1 P. To bind, fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दः|अन्द|अंदः
अन्दः Binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दुः|अन्दु|अंदुः
अन्दुः, -न्दूः <i>f.</i><BR> [अन्द्यते बध्यते अनेन, अन्द्-कू, कूप्रत्ययान्तः<BR> निपातः Uṇ. 1. 93] also अन्दुकः, अन्दूकः<BR>—1 A chain or fetter.<BR>—2 A chain for the elephantʼs feet; गजमन्दूरिव निश्चलं चकार<BR> Śi. 20. 51; ˚निनादः 11. 7.<BR>—3 A sort of ornament worn round the ankles; cf. नूपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दूः
अन्दुः, -न्दूः <i>f.</i><BR> [अन्द्यते बध्यते अनेन, अन्द्-कू, कूप्रत्ययान्तः<BR> निपातः Uṇ. 1. 93] also अन्दुकः, अन्दूकः<BR>—1 A chain or fetter.<BR>—2 A chain for the elephantʼs feet; गजमन्दूरिव निश्चलं चकार<BR> Śi. 20. 51; ˚निनादः 11. 7.<BR>—3 A sort of ornament worn round the ankles; cf. नूपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दिका|अंदिका
अन्दिका<BR>—1 An oven, fire-place.<BR>—2 An elder sister (cf. अन्तिका^1).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलयति
अन्दोलयति Den. P. To swing, agitate, rock to and fro, oscillate. See आन्दोल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलनम्
अन्दोलनम् Swinging, oscillating, waving; द्राक् चामरान्दोलनात्<BR> Udb. See आन्दोलनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्|अंध्
अन्ध् €10 U.<BR>—1 To make blind, blind; अन्धयन् भृङ्गमालाः Śi. 11. 19; तिमिरे<BR> जनस्य दृशमन्धयति 9. 21.<BR>—2 To be or become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blind (lit. and fig.); devoid of sight, unable to see (at particular<BR> times); दिवान्धाः प्राणिनः कोचिद्रात्रावन्धास्तथापरे; D. Bhāg. made<BR> blind, blinded; स्रजमपि शिरस्यन्धः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्यहिशङ्कया Ś. 7. 24;<BR> मदान्धः blinded by intoxication; so दर्पान्धः, क्रोधान्धः;<BR> काम˚, लोभ˚, अज्ञान˚; अज्ञानान्धस्य दीपस्य ज्ञानाञ्जनशलाकया । चक्षुरुन्मीलितं<BR> येन तस्मै श्रीगुरवे नमः ॥; सहजान्धदृशः स्वदुर्नये Śi. 16. 29<BR> blind to his own wicked acts.<BR>—2 Making blind, preventing the sight; utter, pitchy; complete, thick<BR> (darkness) प्रधर्षितायां वैदेह्यां बभूव सचराचरम् । जगत्सर्वममर्यादं<BR> तमसान्धेन संवृतम् ॥ Rām. 3. 52. 9; Ms. 8. 94; सीदन्नन्धे तमसि<BR> U. 3. 33; Māl. 9. 8. 20; see ˚कूप, ˚तामसम् <i>infra</i>.<BR>—3 Afflicted. आर्यः पर्युषितं तु नाभ्यवहरत्यन्धः क्षुधान्धोऽप्यसौ<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 101.<BR>—4 Soiled, tarnished; निःश्वासान्ध इवादर्शश्चन्द्रमा न प्रकाशते Rām. 3. 16. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धम्
अन्ध + .{@-न्धम्@}<BR>—1 Darkness. अन्धः स्यादन्धवेलायां बाधिर्यमपि चाश्रयेत् Mb. 1. 140. 12.<BR>—2 Spiritual ignorance; अज्ञान or अविद्या q. v.<BR>—3 Water; also, turbid water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धः|अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं
अन्ध + .{@-धः@}<BR>—1 A kind of mendicant (परिव्राजक) who has completely controlled<BR> his organs; तिष्ठतो व्रजतो वापि यस्य चक्षुर्न दूरगम् । चतुष्पदां<BR> भुवं मुक्त्वा परिव्राडन्ध उच्यते ॥<BR>—2 An epithet of the zodiacal signs at particular periods; (नष्टद्रव्यलाभालाभोपयोगयुक्तो राशिभेदः);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">Page0128-1</a>]<BR> मेषो वृषा मृगेन्द्रश्च रात्रावन्धाः प्रकीर्तिताः । नृयुक्कर्कटकन्याश्च<BR> दिवान्धाः परिकीर्तिताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न्धाः
अन्ध + .{@-न्धाः@} (pl.) N. of a people; see अन्ध्र.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्धालजी, अन्धाहिः, अन्धाहिकः, अन्धकारः, अन्धकूपः, अन्धतमसम्, अन्धतामसम्, अन्धन्धातमसम्, अन्धतामिस्रः, अन्धतामिश्रः, अन्धधी, अन्धपूतना, अन्धमूषा, अन्धमूषिका, अन्धरात्री, अन्धवर्त्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0127-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धालजी
अन्ध + -अलजी a blind boil or abscess in the eyes (one that does not<BR> open or suppurate). (Ved. अलजि. विसल्पस्य विद्रधस्य वातीकारस्य<BR> वालजेः Av. 9. 8. 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहिः|अन्धाहि
अन्ध + -अहिः, -अहिकः a blind serpent, i. e. one that is not poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहिकः|अन्धाहिक
अन्ध + -अहिः, -अहिकः a blind serpent, i. e. one that is not poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहिः|अन्धाहि
अन्ध + -अहिः, -अहिकः + .({@-हिः, -हिकः@}) N. of a fish (कुचिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहिकः|अन्धाहिक
अन्ध + -अहिः, -अहिकः + .({@-हिः, -हिकः@}) N. of a fish (कुचिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकारः|अन्धकार
अन्ध + -कारः [अन्धं करोति] darkness (lit. and fig.); लीनं दिवाभीतमिवान्धकारम्<BR> Ku. 1. 12; काम˚, मदन˚; अन्धकारतामुपयाति चक्षुः K. 36 grows dim;<BR> बाष्पजलधारान्धकारितमुखी K. 161, 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकूपः|अन्धकूप
अन्ध + -कूपः [अन्धयतीत्यन्धः, अन्धः कूपः]<BR>—1 a well, the mouth of which is hidden; a well overgrown with plants &c.<BR>—2 [अन्धस्य दृष्ट्यभावस्य कूप इव] mental darkness, infatuation.<BR>—3 N. of a hell, to which those who tease and kill harmless creatures are condemned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतमसम्
अन्ध + -तमसम् (P. V. 4. 79.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामसम्
अन्ध + -तामसम्, -न्धातमसम् deep or complete darkness; लोकमन्धतमसात्क्रमोदितौ<BR> R. 11. 24; अन्धतमसमिव प्रविशामि U. 7 the gloom of hell; प्रध्वंसितान्धतमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं<BR> रविः Śi. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामसा
अन्ध + -तामसम्, -न्धातमसम् + .({@-सा@}) night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धन्धातमसम्
अन्ध + -तामसम्, -न्धातमसम् deep or complete darkness; लोकमन्धतमसात्क्रमोदितौ<BR> R. 11. 24; अन्धतमसमिव प्रविशामि U. 7 the gloom of hell; प्रध्वंसितान्धतमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं<BR> रविः Śi. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिस्रः|अन्धतामिस्र|अन्धतामिस्रं
अन्ध + -तामिस्रः, -तामिश्रः + .({@-स्रम्@} also)<BR>—1 complete or deep darkness (especially of the soul); तामिस्रोष्टदशधा<BR> तथा भवत्यन्धतामिस्रः Sāṅ. K. 48 (भयविशेषविषयकोऽभिनिवेशः);<BR> तस्यामन्धतामिस्रमभ्यध्यायत् Mv. 1.<BR>—2 spiritual ignorance (देहे नष्टे अहमेव नष्टः इति रूपमज्ञानम्);<BR> enveloped in utter darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिश्रः|अन्धतामिश्र
अन्ध + -तामिस्रः, -तामिश्रः + .({@-स्रम्@} also)<BR>—1 complete or deep darkness (especially of the soul); तामिस्रोष्टदशधा<BR> तथा भवत्यन्धतामिस्रः Sāṅ. K. 48 (भयविशेषविषयकोऽभिनिवेशः);<BR> तस्यामन्धतामिस्रमभ्यध्यायत् Mv. 1.<BR>—2 spiritual ignorance (देहे नष्टे अहमेव नष्टः इति रूपमज्ञानम्);<BR> enveloped in utter darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिस्रम्
अन्ध + -तामिस्रः, -तामिश्रः + .({@-स्रम्@} also)<BR>—1 complete or deep darkness (especially of the soul); तामिस्रोष्टदशधा<BR> तथा भवत्यन्धतामिस्रः Sāṅ. K. 48 (भयविशेषविषयकोऽभिनिवेशः);<BR> तस्यामन्धतामिस्रमभ्यध्यायत् Mv. 1.<BR>—2 spiritual ignorance (देहे नष्टे अहमेव नष्टः इति रूपमज्ञानम्);<BR> enveloped in utter darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिस्रः|अन्धतामिस्र|अन्धतामिस्रं
अन्ध + -तामिस्रः, -तामिश्रः + .({@-स्रः, -स्रम्@})<BR>—1 N. of a division of Tartarus or infernal regions, the second of the 21<BR> hells to which those who seduce the wives of others and enjoy them<BR> are condemned. According to Bhavabhūti persons committing suicide were<BR> condemned to this hell; cf. अन्धतामिस्रा ह्यसूर्या नाम ते लोकास्तेभ्यः<BR> प्रतिविधीयन्ते य आत्मघतिन इत्येवमृषयो मन्यन्ते U. 4; तामिस्रमन्धतामिस्रं<BR> महारौरवरौरवौ । नरकं कालसूत्रं च महानरकमेव च ॥ Ms. 4. 88, 197;<BR> Y. 3. 224; doctrine of annihilation after death.<BR>—2 Death मोहोऽप्रकाशस्तामिस्रमन्धतामिस्रसंज्ञितम् । मरणं चान्धतामिस्रं<BR> तामिस्रं क्रोध उच्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 313. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिस्रम्
अन्ध + -तामिस्रः, -तामिश्रः + .({@-स्रः, -स्रम्@})<BR>—1 N. of a division of Tartarus or infernal regions, the second of the 21<BR> hells to which those who seduce the wives of others and enjoy them<BR> are condemned. According to Bhavabhūti persons committing suicide were<BR> condemned to this hell; cf. अन्धतामिस्रा ह्यसूर्या नाम ते लोकास्तेभ्यः<BR> प्रतिविधीयन्ते य आत्मघतिन इत्येवमृषयो मन्यन्ते U. 4; तामिस्रमन्धतामिस्रं<BR> महारौरवरौरवौ । नरकं कालसूत्रं च महानरकमेव च ॥ Ms. 4. 88, 197;<BR> Y. 3. 224; doctrine of annihilation after death.<BR>—2 Death मोहोऽप्रकाशस्तामिस्रमन्धतामिस्रसंज्ञितम् । मरणं चान्धतामिस्रं<BR> तामिस्रं क्रोध उच्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 313. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धधी
अन्ध + -धी <i>a.</i> mentally blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धपूतना
अन्ध + -पूतना a demoness supposed to cause diseases in children; यो<BR> द्वेष्टि स्तनमतिसारकासहिक्काछर्दीभिर्ज्वरसहिताभिरर्द्यमानः । दुर्वर्णः<BR> सततमधःशयोऽम्लगन्धिस्तं ब्रूयुर्वरभिषजोन्धपूतनार्तम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषा
अन्ध + -मूषा a small covered crucible with a hole in the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषिका
अन्ध + -मूषिका [अन्धं दृष्ट्यभावं मुष्णाति, भुष्-ण्वुल्] N. of a plant<BR> or grass देवताड (तत्सेवनेन चक्षुष्मत्ता भवतीति वैद्यकप्रसिद्धिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धरात्री
अन्ध + -रात्री dark night (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धवर्त्मन्
अन्ध + -वर्त्मन् <i>m.</i> [अन्धं सूर्यप्रकाशराहित्याद्वर्त्म यत्र] the<BR> seventh skandha or region of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धङ्करण|अंधंकरण|अन्धंकरण
अन्धङ्करण <i>a.</i> Making blind (P. III. 2. 56).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धंभविष्णु|अन्धम्भविष्णु|अंधंभविष्णु
अन्धंभविष्णु, -भावुक <i>a.</i><BR> Becoming blind (P. III. 2. 57).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धंभावुक|अन्धम्भावुक|अंधंभावुक
अन्धंभविष्णु, -भावुक <i>a.</i><BR> Becoming blind (P. III. 2. 57).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धक|अंधक|अन्धकः
अन्धक <i>a.</i> [अन्ध्-कन्] Blind; अन्धकः कुब्जकश्चैव Pt. 5. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकः|अन्धक|अंधक
अन्धक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of an Asura, son of Kaśyapa and Diti and killed by Śiva. [He is<BR> represented as a demon with 1000 arms and heads, 2000 eyes and feet, and<BR> called <i>Andhaka</i>, because he walked like a blind man, though he could<BR> see very well; स व्रजत्यन्धवद्यस्मादनन्धोऽपि हि भारत । तमन्धकोऽयं<BR> नाम्नेति प्रोचुस्तत्र निवासिनः ॥ He was slain by Śiva when he attempted<BR> to carry off the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">Page0128-2</a>]<BR> Pārijāta tree from heaven; whence Śiva is called <i>Andhakaripu, -ari, -dviṣ</i><BR> &c. According to the Matsya Purāṇa <i>Andhaka</i> was admitted<BR> to the class of Gaṇas by Śiva, at his importunities and humble supplication,<BR> when he was about to be killed by the god for having attempted to carry<BR> off his wife Pārvatī].<BR>—2 N. of a descendant of Yadu and ancestor of Kṛṣṇa and his descendants,<BR> a grandson of Kroṣṭu, son of Yudhājit who, together with his brother<BR> Vṛṣṇi is the ancestor of the celebrated family of Andhakavṛṣṇis;<BR> P. IV. 1. 114, VI. 2. 34.<BR>—3 N. of a sage, son of Mamatā and of Utathya, elder brother of Bṛhaspati.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्धकारिः, अन्धकरिपुः, अन्धकशत्रुः, अन्धकघाति, अन्धकासुहृद्, अन्धकवर्तः, अन्धकवृष्णि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकारिः|अन्धकारि
अन्धक + -अरिः, -रिपुः, -शत्रुः, -घाति, -असुहृद् &c. slayer of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकरिपुः|अन्धकरिपु
अन्धक + -अरिः, -रिपुः, -शत्रुः, -घाति, -असुहृद् &c. slayer of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकशत्रुः|अन्धकशत्रु
अन्धक + -अरिः, -रिपुः, -शत्रुः, -घाति, -असुहृद् &c. slayer of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकघाति
अन्धक + -अरिः, -रिपुः, -शत्रुः, -घाति, -असुहृद् &c. slayer of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकासुहृद्
अन्धक + -अरिः, -रिपुः, -शत्रुः, -घाति, -असुहृद् &c. slayer of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकवर्तः|अन्धकवर्त
अन्धक + -वर्तः N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकवृष्णि
अन्धक + -वृष्णि <i>m.</i> <i>pl.</i> descendants of अन्धक and वृष्णि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धिका|अंधिका
अन्धिका [अन्ध्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 A kind of game or sport, probably blindmanʼs buff; gambling (तया<BR> हि जनः अन्ध इव विवेकशून्यः क्रियते Tv.).<BR>—3 A woman of a particular character, one of the classes of women.<BR>—4 A disease of the eye.<BR>—5 = सर्षपी, = सिद्धा q. v. (अस्या अत्यन्तसेवनात् दृष्टिक्षयो जायते<BR> इति वैद्यकप्रसिद्धिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीकृ|अंधीकृ
अन्धीकृ €8 U. To make blind, blind;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीकृतात्मा
अन्धीकृ + ˚कृतात्मा blinded in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीभू|अंधीभू
अन्धीभू To become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
अन्धस् <i>n.</i> [अद्-असुन् नुम् धश्च; अदेर्नुम्धौ च Uṇ. 4. 205]<BR>—1 Food; द्विजातिशेषेण यदेतदन्धसा Ki. 1. 39; सशेष एवान्धसि<BR> असावतृप्यत् Dk. 133, 157; Viś. Guṇā. 101; Mb. 3. 193. 34. (supposed<BR> to have in the Veda the senses of Soma, the herb itself, or its juice;<BR> juice, ghee or boiled rice, but usually taken to mean ‘food’ only by Indian<BR> lexicographers and commentators.)<BR>—2 Grassy ground उभे यत्ते महिना शुभ्रे अन्धसी अधिक्षियन्ति पूरवः<BR> Rv. 7. 96. 2. [cf. Gr. <i>andhos</i>.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धुः|अन्धु|अंधुः
अन्धुः [fr. अम् Uṇ. 1. 27]<BR>—1 A well; आपीनोऽन्धुः P. VI. 1. 28; Sk. cf. also ‘मन्यमानः … … बन्धूनन्धूनिवासौ …’<BR> चोलचम्पूकाव्य p. 9, Verse 13.<BR>—2 The male organ of generation; वाक्पाणिपादपाय्वन्धुसंज्ञान्याहुर्मनीषिणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धुलः|अन्धुल|अंधुलः
अन्धुलः [अन्ध्-उलच्] A kind of tree, Acacia Sirissa (शिरीष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्रः|अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अंध्रः
अन्ध्रः (<i>pl.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of a people and the country inhabited by them. [The country of the<BR> Āndhras is said to be the modern Telingana. But the limits were probably<BR> confined to the Ghats on the West and the rivers Godāvarī and Kṛṣṇā<BR> on the North and South. It bordered on Kalinga (See Dk. 7th Ullāsa),<BR> and its capital Andhranagara is probably the old town of Vengi or Vegi.<BR> According to Daṇḍin, there was near it a lake ‘like the ocean and crested with cranes’<BR> which description can only refer to the lake Colair which<BR> has an area of over 150 miles; जगन्नाथादूर्ध्वभागादर्वाक् श्रीभ्रमरात्मकात् ।<BR> तावदन्ध्राभिधो देशः].<BR>—2 N. of a dynasty of kings.<BR>—3 A man of a mixed (low) caste, being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">Page0129-1</a>]<BR> born of a Vaideha father and Kārāvara mother, who lives by killing game;<BR> कारावरो निषादात्तु चर्मकारः प्रसूयते । वैदेहकादन्ध्रमेदौ बहिर्ग्रामप्रतिश्रयौ ॥ Ms. 10. 36.<BR>—4 A kind of fowler.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्ध्रजातिः, अन्ध्रभृत्याः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0128-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्रजातिः|अन्ध्रजाति
अन्ध्रः + -जातिः the Andhra tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्रभृत्याः
अन्ध्रः + -भृत्याः N. of a dynasty of kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नम्
अन्नम् [अद्-क्त; अनित्यनेन, अन्-नन्; according to Yāska, from<BR> अद्, अद्यते अत्ति च भूतानि; or from आ-नम्, आ आभिमुख्येन ह्येतन्नतं<BR> प्रह्वीभूतं भवति भोजनाय भूतानाम्]<BR>—1 Food (in general); अद्यतेऽत्ति च भूतानि तस्मादन्नं तदुत्त्यते<BR> T. Up.; मेदोऽसृङ्मांसमज्जास्थि वदन्त्यन्नं मनीषिणः Ms. 3. 8. 182;<BR> अहमन्नं भवान् भोक्ता H. 1. 51. I am your prey &c.; चराणामन्नमचराः Ms. 5. 29.<BR>—2 Food as representing the lowest form in which the Supreme Soul is manifested,<BR> being the coarsest and last of the 5 vestures (कोश) in which the<BR> soul is clothed and passes from body to body in the long process of metempsychosis<BR> −“the nutrimentitious vesture or visible body in the world of sense”<BR> (स्थूलशरीर called अन्नमयकोश).<BR>—3 Boiled rice; अन्नेन व्यञ्जनम् P. II. 1. 34.<BR>—4 Corn (bread corn); ता (आपः) अन्नमसृजन्त तस्माद्यत्र क्व<BR> च वर्षति तदेव भूयिष्ठमन्नं भवति Ch. Up. 6. 2. 4; आदित्याज्जायते<BR> वृष्टिर्वृष्टेरन्नं ततः प्रजाः Ms. 3. 76; कृत˚ 9. 219, 10. 86, 12. 65.<BR>—5 Water.<BR>—6 Earth (पृथिव्या अन्नहेतुत्वादन्नशब्दवाच्यता). —7 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नः|अन्न|अन्नं
अन्नम् + .{@-न्नः@} The sun (स हि अन्नहेतुवृष्टिहेतुः).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्नाकालः, अन्नात्तृ, अन्नादिन्, अन्नाहारिन्, अन्नाद, अन्नाद्यम्, अन्नाच्छादनम्, अन्नवस्त्रम्, अन्नायुः, अन्नकाम, अन्नकालः, अन्नकिट्टः, अन्नकूटः, अन्नकोष्ठकः, अन्नगतिः, अन्नगन्धिः, अन्नज, अन्नजात, अन्नजम्, अन्नजा, अन्नजलम्, अन्नतेजस्, अन्नद, अन्नदातृ, अन्नदायिन्, अन्नप्रद, अन्नदा, अन्नदासः, अन्नदेवता, अन्नदोषः, अन्नद्वेषः, अन्नपतिः, अन्नपाकः, अन्नपू, अन्नपूर्ण, अन्नपेयम्, अन्नप्रलय, अन्नप्राशः, अन्नप्राशनम्, अन्नब्रह्मन्, अन्नात्मन्, अन्नभक्त, अन्नभुज्, अन्नमय, अन्नमलम्, अन्नरक्षा, अन्नरसः, अन्नवत्, अन्नवस्त्रम्, अन्नविकारः, अन्नविद्, अन्नव्यवहारः, अन्नशेषः, अन्नसंस्कारः, अन्नहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाकालः|अन्नाकाल
अन्नम् + -अकालः = अनाकाल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नात्तृ
अन्नम् + -अत्तृ, -आदिन्, -आहारिन् eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नादिन्
अन्नम् + -अत्तृ, -आदिन्, -आहारिन् eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाहारिन्
अन्नम् + -अत्तृ, -आदिन्, -आहारिन् eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद|अन्नादः
अन्नम् + -अद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 eating food.<BR>—2 having a good appetite (दीप्ताग्नि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नादः|अन्नाद
अन्नम् + -अद + .({@-दः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद्यम्
अन्नम् + -अद्यम् proper food, food in general; कुर्यादहरहः श्राद्धमन्नाद्येनोदकेन<BR> वा Ms. 3. 82, 4. 112, 11. 144. अन्नाद्येन प्रजापतिः (तृप्तः)<BR> Mb. 3. 200. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाच्छादनम्
अन्नम् + -आच्छादनम्, -वस्त्रम् food and clothing, food and raiment, the<BR> bare necessaries of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नवस्त्रम्
अन्नम् + -आच्छादनम्, -वस्त्रम् food and clothing, food and raiment, the<BR> bare necessaries of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नायुः|अन्नायु
अन्नम् + -आयुः (अन्नायु) consisting of, living by, food; desirous of<BR> food (अन्नबन्धनः, अन्नजीवनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकाम
अन्नम् + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of food; स इद्भोजो यो गृहवे ददात्यन्नकामाय<BR> Rv. 10. 117. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकालः|अन्नकाल
अन्नम् + -कालः hour of dinner; meal-time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकिट्टः|अन्नकिट्ट
अन्नम् + -किट्टः = ˚मल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकूटः|अन्नकूट
अन्नम् + -कूटः a large heap of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकोष्ठकः|अन्नकोष्ठक
अन्नम् + -कोष्ठकः<BR>—1 a cupboard; granary.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नगतिः|अन्नगति
अन्नम् + -गतिः <i>f.</i> the passage of food, gullet (cf. वाहिस्रोतस्^1).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260215. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/112. note: Seen in other dictionaries. vAhisrotas means oesophagus..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नगन्धिः|अन्नगन्धि
अन्नम् + -गन्धिः dysentery, diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नज
अन्नम् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> produced from food as the primitive substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजात
अन्नम् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> produced from food as the primitive substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजम्
अन्नम् + -जम् rice-gruel of three days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजा
अन्नम् + -जा <i>f.</i> a hiccup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजलम्
अन्नम् + -जलम् food and water, bare subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नतेजस्
अन्नम् + -तेजस् <i>a.</i> having the vigour caused by food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद
अन्नम् + -द, -दातृ, -दायिन्, -प्रद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 giving food; वारिदस्तृप्तिमाप्नोति सुखमक्षय्यमन्नदः Ms. 4. 229.<BR>—2 epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदातृ
अन्नम् + -द, -दातृ, -दायिन्, -प्रद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 giving food; वारिदस्तृप्तिमाप्नोति सुखमक्षय्यमन्नदः Ms. 4. 229.<BR>—2 epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदायिन्
अन्नम् + -द, -दातृ, -दायिन्, -प्रद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 giving food; वारिदस्तृप्तिमाप्नोति सुखमक्षय्यमन्नदः Ms. 4. 229.<BR>—2 epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्रद
अन्नम् + -द, -दातृ, -दायिन्, -प्रद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 giving food; वारिदस्तृप्तिमाप्नोति सुखमक्षय्यमन्नदः Ms. 4. 229.<BR>—2 epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदा
अन्नम् + -दा N. of Durgā or Annapūrṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदासः|अन्नदास
अन्नम् + -दासः [अन्नेन पालितो दासः शाक˚ त˚] a servant who works<BR> for food only, one who becomes a servant or slave by getting food only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदेवता
अन्नम् + -देवता the deity supposed to preside over articles of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदोषः|अन्नदोष
अन्नम् + -दोषः<BR>—1 sin arising from eating prohibited food; Ms. 5. 4.<BR>—2 a defect in the food eaten; derangement of food or the humours of the<BR> body; आलस्यादन्नदोषाच्च मृत्युर्विप्राञ् जिघांसति Ms. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद्वेषः|अन्नद्वेष
अन्नम् + -द्वेषः dislike of food, loss of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपतिः|अन्नपति
अन्नम् + -पतिः lord or possessor of food, epithet of Savitṛ, Agni, and<BR> Śiva. अन्नपतेऽन्नस्य नो देहि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">Page0129-2</a>]<BR> Ts. 11. 83, 34. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपाकः|अन्नपाक
अन्नम् + -पाकः cooking of food; digestion of food; (by the fire in the stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपू
अन्नम् + -पू <i>a.</i> purifying food, epithet of the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्ण
अन्नम् + -पूर्ण <i>a.</i> filled with, possessed of, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्णा|अन्नपूर्ण्णा
अन्नम् + -पूर्ण + .({@-र्णा@}) a form of Durgā (the goddess of plenty);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्णेश्वरी|अन्नपूर्ण्णेश्वरी
अन्नम् + -पूर्ण + .({@-र्णा@}) + ˚ईश्वरी<BR> N. of Durgā or a form of Bhairavī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपेयम्
अन्नम् + -पेयम् = वाजपेयम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्रलय
अन्नम् + -प्रलय <i>a.</i> being dissolved into food after death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्राशः|अन्नप्राश
अन्नम् + -प्राशः, -प्राशनम् the ceremony of giving a new-born child food<BR> to eat for the first time, one of the 16 <i>Saṃskāras</i> performed between<BR> the 5th and 8th month (usually in the sixth, Ms. 2. 34) with preliminary<BR> oblations to fire (Mar. उष्टावण); षष्टेऽन्नप्राशनं मासि Ms. 2. 34;<BR> Y. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्राशनम्
अन्नम् + -प्राशः, -प्राशनम् the ceremony of giving a new-born child food<BR> to eat for the first time, one of the 16 <i>Saṃskāras</i> performed between<BR> the 5th and 8th month (usually in the sixth, Ms. 2. 34) with preliminary<BR> oblations to fire (Mar. उष्टावण); षष्टेऽन्नप्राशनं मासि Ms. 2. 34;<BR> Y. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नब्रह्मन्
अन्नम् + -ब्रह्मन्, -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> Brahman as represented by food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नात्मन्
अन्नम् + -ब्रह्मन्, -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> Brahman as represented by food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नभक्त
अन्नम् + -भक्त <i>a.</i> [अन्नार्थं भक्तः दासः] = अन्नदास q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नभुज्
अन्नम् + -भुज् <i>a.</i> eating food, epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नम् + -मय <i>a.</i> see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमलम्
अन्नम् + -मलम्<BR>—1 excrement, faeces; P. VI. 1. 148. Sk.<BR>—2 spirituous liquor; सुरा वै मलमन्नानाम् Ms. 11. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नरक्षा
अन्नम् + -रक्षा precautions as to eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नरसः|अन्नरस
अन्नम् + -रसः essence of food, chyle; food and drink, nutriment; नानाविधानन्नरसान्<BR> वन्यमूलफलाश्रयान् । तेभ्यो ददौ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नवत्|अन्नवन्त्
अन्नम् + -वत् <i>a.</i> possessed of food; अन्नवान्त्सन् रफितायोपजग्मुषे<BR> Rv. 10. 117. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नवस्त्रम्
अन्नम् + -वस्त्रम् = ˚आच्छादनम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाच्छादनम्
अन्नम् + -वस्त्रम् = ˚आच्छादनम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नविकारः|अन्नविकार
अन्नम् + -विकारः<BR>—1 transformation of food, assimilation.<BR>—2 disorder of the stomach caused by indigestion.<BR>—3 seminal discharge (of man); semen itself; cf. अन्नाद्रेतः संभवति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नविद्
अन्नम् + -विद् <i>a.</i> acquiring food; कार्षीवणा अन्नविदो न विद्यया Av. 6. 116. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नव्यवहारः|अन्नव्यवहार
अन्नम् + -व्यवहारः the law or custom relating to food, <i>i. e.</i> the<BR> custom of eating together or not with other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नशेषः|अन्नशेष
अन्नम् + -शेषः leavings of food, offal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नसंस्कारः|अन्नसंस्कार
अन्नम् + -संस्कारः consecration of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नहोमः|अन्नहोम
अन्नम् + -होमः a sacrifice (with 10 materials) connected with the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Consisting or made of food, composed of or containing<BR> boiled rice;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमयकोशः|अन्नमयकोश
अन्नमय + ˚कोशः -षः the gross material body, the स्थूलशरीर,<BR> which is sustained by food and which is the fifth or last vesture or wrapper<BR> of the soul; see अन्न (2) above and also कोश; hence, also the<BR> material world, the coarsest or lowest form in which Brahman is considered<BR> as manifesting itself in the worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमयकोषः|अन्नमयकोष
अन्नमय + ˚कोशः -षः the gross material body, the स्थूलशरीर,<BR> which is sustained by food and which is the fifth or last vesture or wrapper<BR> of the soul; see अन्न (2) above and also कोश; hence, also the<BR> material world, the coarsest or lowest form in which Brahman is considered<BR> as manifesting itself in the worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमयम्
अन्नमय + .{@-यम्@} Plenty of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद|अन्नादः
अन्नाद <i>a.</i> eater of food; अहमन्नादः T. Up. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नावृध्
अन्नावृध् [अन्नं वर्धते अनेन वृध्-करणे क्विप्, पूर्वपददीर्घः]<BR> Increasing food; त्वा पितृभृतो जनित्रीः अन्नावृधं प्रति चरन्ति अन्नैः Rv. 10. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नंभट्टः|अन्नम्भट्ट|अन्नंभट्ट
अन्नंभट्टः N. of the author of the Tarkasaṅgraha. cf. काशीगमनमात्रेण<BR> नान्नंभट्टायते द्विजः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य <i>a.</i> [अन् अघ्न्यादि˚ य; अन्यः, न्यस्मै, ˚स्मात्; <i>n.</i> अन्यत् &c.]<BR>—1 Another, different, other (भिन्न); another, other (generally);<BR> स एव त्वन्यः क्षणेन भवतीति विचित्रमेतत् Bh. 2. 40; अन्यदेव<BR> भागधेयमेते निर्वपन्ति Ś. 2; सर्वमन्यत् everything else; किमुतान्यहिंस्राः<BR> R. 2. 62; changed, altered; संप्रत्यन्ये वयम् Bh. 3. 66 quite different<BR> persons; oft. in comp. अन्यसङ्गात्, अनन्यपरायण, अनन्यसाधारण &c.<BR>—2 Other than, different from, else than (with abl. or as last member<BR> of comp.); नास्ति जीवितादन्यदभिमततरमिह सर्वजन्तूनाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">Page0130-1</a>]<BR> K. 35; कोऽस्ति धन्यो मदन्यः Bv. 4. 37; उत्थितं ददृशेऽन्यच्च कबन्धेभ्यो<BR> न किंचन R. 12. 49; किमन्यदस्याः परिषदः श्रुतिप्रसादनतः<BR> Ś. 1; oft. used in addition to ऋते or विना; ऋते समुद्रादन्यः को<BR> बिभर्ति वडवानलम् Pt. 5. 35; किं नु खलु मे प्रियादर्शनादृते शरणमन्यत् Ś. 3.<BR>—3 Another person, one different from self (opp. स्व, आत्मीय); वासश्च<BR> धृतमन्यैर्न धारयेत् Ms. 4. 66.<BR>—4 Strange, unusual, extraordinary; अन्य एव स प्रकारः K. 168; अन्या<BR> जगद्धितमयी मनसः प्रवृत्तिः Bv. 1. 69; धन्या मृदन्यैव सा S. D.<BR>—5 Ordinary, any one; निरातङ्कः कन्यामन्योऽपि याचते Mv. 1. 31; cf. इतर.<BR>—6 Additional, new, more; अन्यान् दशसुवर्णान्प्रयच्छ Mk. 2 another<BR> ten (coins); अन्यदन्यन्नलिनदलशयनम् K. 157 new and new (changing<BR> every now and then); अन्यस्मिन् दिवसे another day; one of a number<BR> (with gen.); अन्यच्च moreover, besides, and again (used to connect<BR> sentences together); एक━अन्य the one━the other; एकः सख्यास्तव<BR> सह मया वामपादाभिलाषी । काङ्क्षन्त्यन्यो वदनमदिरां दौहृदच्छद्मनास्याः<BR> Me. 80; see under एक also; अन्य━अन्य one-another; अन्यः करोति<BR> अन्यो भुङ्क्ते one does, another suffers; अन्यन्मुखे अन्यन्निर्वहणे<BR> Mu. 5; अन्यदुप्तं जातमन्यत् Ms. 9. 40, 99, 8. 204; कर्णे लगति<BR> चान्यस्य प्राणैरन्यो वियुज्यते Pt. 1. 305; अन्यदुच्छृङ्खलं सत्त्वमन्यच्छास्त्रनियन्त्रितम्<BR> Śi. 2. 62; अन्य━अन्य━अन्य &c. one, another, third, fourth &c.,<BR> जल्पन्ति सार्धमन्येन पश्यन्त्यन्यं सविभ्रमाः । हृद्गतं चिन्तयन्त्यन्यं<BR> प्रियः को नाम योषिताम् Pt. 1. 135; मनस्यन्यद्ववचस्यन्यत् कार्यमन्यद्<BR> दुरात्मनाम् H. 1. 97; (in pl.) केचित्━अन्ये some━others; एके━अन्ये━तथान्ये<BR> (बीजमेके प्रशंसन्ति क्षेत्रमन्ये मनीषिणः । बीजक्षेत्रे तथैवान्ये तत्रेयं<BR> तु व्यवस्थितिः ॥) Ms. 10. 70, 4. 9, 12. 123. [cf. L. <i>alius</i>; Gr. <i>allos</i><BR> for <i>aljos</i>, Zend. <i>anya</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यार्थ, अन्यासाधारण, अन्याश्रयण, अन्योदर्य, अन्योढा, अन्यकारुका, अन्यक्षेत्रम्, अन्यग, अन्यगामिन्, अन्यगोत्र, अन्यचित्त, अन्यज, अन्यजात, अन्यजन्मन्, अन्यदुर्वह, अन्यदेवत, अन्यदेवत्य, अन्यदैवत्य, अन्यधर्मन्, अन्यधी, अन्यनाभि, अन्यपदार्थः, अन्यपर, अन्यपुष्टा, अन्यभृता, अन्यपूर्वा, अन्यबीज, अन्यबीजसमुद्भव, अन्यसमुत्पन्न, अन्यभृत्, अन्यमनस्, अन्यमनस्क, अन्यमानस, अन्यमातृजः, अन्यरङ्गः, अन्यराजन्, अन्यराष्ट्रीय, अन्यरूप, अन्यलिङ्ग, अन्यलिङ्गक, अन्यवादिन्, अन्यवापः, अन्यविवर्धित, अन्यव्रत, अन्यशाखः, अन्यशाखकः, अन्यसंक्रान्त, अन्यसंगमः, अन्यसाधारण, अन्यस्त्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0129-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यार्थ
अन्य + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> having a different meaning, sense, or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यासाधारण
अन्य + -असाधारण <i>a.</i> not common to others, peculiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याश्रयण
अन्य + -आश्रयण <i>a.</i> going or passing over to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्य|अन्योदर्यः|अन्योदर्य्य|अन्योदर्य्यः
अन्य + -उदर्य <i>a.</i> born from another; नहि ग्रभायारणः सुशेवोऽन्योदर्यो<BR> मनसा मन्तवा उ Rv. 7. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्यः|अन्योदर्य|अन्योदर्य्य|अन्योदर्य्यः
अन्य + -उदर्य + .({@-र्यः@}) a step-motherʼs son, a half brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्या
अन्य + -उदर्य + .({@-र्या@}) a half sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योढा
अन्य + -ऊढा <i>a.</i> married to another; anotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यकारुका
अन्य + -कारुका a worm bred in excrement (शकृत्कीटः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यक्षेत्रम्
अन्य + -क्षेत्रम्<BR>—1 another field.<BR>—2 another or foreign territory. अन्यक्षेत्रे कृतं पापं पुण्यक्षेत्रे<BR> विनश्यति । पुण्यक्षेत्रे कृतं पापं वज्रलेपो भविष्यति ॥<BR>—3 anotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यग
अन्य + -ग, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going to another.<BR>—2 adulterous, unchaste; वणिजां तु कुलस्त्रीव स्थिरा लक्ष्मीरनन्यगा<BR> Ks. 21. 56, 19. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यगामिन्
अन्य + -ग, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going to another.<BR>—2 adulterous, unchaste; वणिजां तु कुलस्त्रीव स्थिरा लक्ष्मीरनन्यगा<BR> Ks. 21. 56, 19. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यगोत्र
अन्य + -गोत्र <i>a.</i> of a different family or lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यचित्त
अन्य + -चित्त <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on something or some one else;<BR> see ˚मनस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यज
अन्य + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> of a different origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यजात
अन्य + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i> of a different origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यजन्मन्
अन्य + -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> another life or existence, regeneration, metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदुर्वह
अन्य + -दुर्वह <i>a.</i> difficult to be borne by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदेवत
अन्य + -देवत, -देवत्य, -दैवत्य <i>a.</i> addressed or referring to another<BR> deity (as a Vedic Mantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदेवत्य
अन्य + -देवत, -देवत्य, -दैवत्य <i>a.</i> addressed or referring to another<BR> deity (as a Vedic Mantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदैवत्य
अन्य + -देवत, -देवत्य, -दैवत्य <i>a.</i> addressed or referring to another<BR> deity (as a Vedic Mantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यधर्मन्
अन्य + -धर्मन् <i>a.</i> having another or different property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यधर्मः|अन्यधर्म
अन्य + -धर्मन् + .({@-र्मः@}) different property or characteristic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यधी
अन्य + -धी <i>a.</i> whose mind is turned away from God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यनाभि
अन्य + -नाभि <i>a.</i> belonging to another family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपदार्थः|अन्यपदार्थ
अन्य + -पदार्थः<BR>—1 another substance.<BR>—2 the sense of another word; ˚प्रधानो बहुव्रीहिः the Bahuvrīhi compound<BR> essentially depends on the sense of another word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपर
अन्य + -पर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devoted to another or something else.<BR>—2 expressing or referring to something<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">Page0130-2</a>]<BR> else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपुष्टा
अन्य + -पुष्टा, -भृता ‘reared by another’, epithet of the cuckoo, which<BR> is supposed to be reared by the crow (called अन्यभृत्); अप्यन्यपुष्टा<BR> प्रतिकूलशब्दा Ku. 1. 45; कलमन्यभृतासु भाषितम् R. 8. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृता
अन्य + -पुष्टा, -भृता ‘reared by another’, epithet of the cuckoo, which<BR> is supposed to be reared by the crow (called अन्यभृत्); अप्यन्यपुष्टा<BR> प्रतिकूलशब्दा Ku. 1. 45; कलमन्यभृतासु भाषितम् R. 8. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपूर्वा|अन्यपूर्व्वा
अन्य + -पूर्वा [अन्यः पतिः पूर्वो यस्याः]<BR>—1 a woman already promised or betrothed to another.<BR>—2 a remarried widow (पुनर्भू) see अनन्यपूर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यबीज
अन्य + -बीज, -बीजसमुद्भव, -समुत्पन्न an adopted son (born from other<BR> parents), one who may be adopted as a son for want of legitimate issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यबीजसमुद्भव
अन्य + -बीज, -बीजसमुद्भव, -समुत्पन्न an adopted son (born from other<BR> parents), one who may be adopted as a son for want of legitimate issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यसमुत्पन्न
अन्य + -बीज, -बीजसमुद्भव, -समुत्पन्न an adopted son (born from other<BR> parents), one who may be adopted as a son for want of legitimate issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृत्
अन्य + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a crow (rearing another, it being supposed to sit<BR> on the eggs of the cuckoo and to rear its young ones), cf. Ś. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्
अन्य + -मनस्, -मनस्क, -मानस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the mind fixed on something else; inattentive.<BR>—2 fickle, versatile, unsteady; अन्यमनसः स्त्रियः H. 1. 111 absent-minded;<BR> possessed by a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्क|अन्यमनस्कः
अन्य + -मनस्, -मनस्क, -मानस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the mind fixed on something else; inattentive.<BR>—2 fickle, versatile, unsteady; अन्यमनसः स्त्रियः H. 1. 111 absent-minded;<BR> possessed by a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमानस
अन्य + -मनस्, -मनस्क, -मानस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the mind fixed on something else; inattentive.<BR>—2 fickle, versatile, unsteady; अन्यमनसः स्त्रियः H. 1. 111 absent-minded;<BR> possessed by a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमातृजः|अन्यमातृज
अन्य + -मातृजः a half-brother (born of another mother) असंसृष्ट्यपि<BR> वाऽऽदद्यात्संसृष्टो नान्यमातृजः Y. 2. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरङ्गः|अन्यरङ्ग
अन्य + -रङ्गः the second court or theatre or a compound; Māna. 21. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यराजन्
अन्य + -राजन्, -राष्ट्रीय <i>a.</i> subject to another king or kingdom (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यराष्ट्रीय
अन्य + -राजन्, -राष्ट्रीय <i>a.</i> subject to another king or kingdom (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरूप
अन्य + -रूप <i>a.</i> having another form, changed, altered; पद्मिनीं<BR> वान्यरूपाम् Me. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरूपम्
अन्य + -रूप + .({@-पम्@}) another or changed form;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यरूपेण
अन्य + -रूप + .({@-पम्@}) + ˚पेण in another form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यलिङ्ग|अन्यलिंग
अन्य + -लिङ्ग, -लिङ्गक <i>a.</i> following the gender of another word (i. e.<BR> the substantive), an adjective; ऊषवानूषरो द्वावप्यन्यलिङ्गौ Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यलिङ्गक|अन्यलिंगक
अन्य + -रूप + .({@-पम्@}) + ˚पेण in another form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवादिन्
अन्य + -वादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 giving false evidence.<BR>—2 a defendant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवापः|अन्यवाप
अन्य + -वापः the cuckoo leaving the eggs in the nests of other birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यविवर्धित
अन्य + -विवर्धित <i>a.</i> = पुष्ट a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यव्रत
अन्य + -व्रत <i>a.</i> following other (than Vedic) observances, devoted<BR> to other gods, infidel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यशाखः|अन्यशाख
अन्य + -शाखः, -शाखकः a Brāhmaṇa who has gone over to another school<BR> (of religion &c.); an apostate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यशाखकः|अन्यशाखक
अन्य + -शाखः, -शाखकः a Brāhmaṇa who has gone over to another school<BR> (of religion &c.); an apostate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यसंक्रान्त
अन्य + -संक्रान्त <i>a.</i> fixed on or transferred to another (woman); ˚हृदयः<BR> आर्यपुत्रः M. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यसंगमः|अन्यसङ्गम|अन्यसंगम
अन्य + -संगमः intercourse with another; illicit intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यसाधारण
अन्य + -साधारण <i>a.</i> common to many others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यस्त्री
अन्य + -स्त्री anotherʼs wife, a woman not oneʼs own. [In Rhetoric she<BR> is considered as one of three chief female characters in a poetical composition,<BR> the other two being स्वीया and साधारणी स्त्री. अन्या may be either<BR> a damsel or anotherʼs wife. The ‘damsel’ is one not yet married, who is<BR> bashful and arrived at the age of puberty. As "anotherʼs wife" she is<BR> fond of festivals and similar occasions of amusement, who is a disgrace<BR> to her family and utterly destitute of modesty, see S. D. 108-110].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यस्त्रीगः|अन्यस्त्रीग
अन्य + -स्त्री + ˚गः<BR> an adulterer. यस्य स्तेनः पुरे नास्ति नान्यस्त्रीगो न दुष्टवाक् …<BR> स राजा शक्रलोकभाक्; Ms. 8. 386. [Note: Some compounds under अन्य<BR> will be found under अनन्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यक
अन्यक <i>a.</i> Another, other (= अन्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्
अन्यत् <i>a.</i> (अन्य <i>n.</i>) Another &c. नैवास्ति लिखितादन्यत्<BR> स्मारकं व्यवहारिणाम् Sulhā. ━<i>ind.</i> Again, moreover, besides &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यदर्थ, अन्यदाशा, अन्यदाशिस्, अन्यदास्था, अन्यदुत्सुक, अन्यद्रागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदर्थ|अन्यदर्थः
अन्यत् + -अर्थ<BR>—1 having a different meaning.<BR>—2 referring to or expressing another sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदर्थः|अन्यदर्थ
अन्यत् + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@}) a different meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदाशा
अन्यत् + -आशा desire of something else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदाशिस्
अन्यत् + -आशिस् <i>f.</i> anotherʼs blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदास्था
अन्यत् + -आस्था devotion or attachment to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदुत्सुक
अन्यत् + -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> longing for another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यद्रागः|अन्यद्राग
अन्यत् + -रागः attachment to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0130-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतम|अन्यतमः
अन्यतम <i>a.</i> [अन्य-डतम] (declined like a noun and not<BR> a pronoun) One of many, any one out of a large number (with gen. or in<BR> comp.); (जपन्वान्यतमं वेदम् Ms. 11. 75, 6. 32, 32 4; Y. 2. 22, 3. 253;<BR> अन्यतरान्यतमशब्दौ अव्युत्पन्ने प्रातिपदिके इति कैयटः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतर|अन्यतरः
अन्यतर <i>a.</i> (declined like a pronoun) One of the two (persons<BR> or things), either of the two (with gen.); तयोर्मुनिकुमारयोरन्यतरः<BR> K. 151; सन्तः परीक्ष्यान्यतरद् भजन्ते M. 1. 2 the one or the other;<BR> अन्यतरा युवयोरागच्छतु Ś. 3; Ms. 2. 111, 9. 171; other, different;<BR> अन्यतर━अन्यतर the one━the other; अन्यतरस्याम् (loc. of<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरा
अन्यतर + ˚रा) either way, in both ways, optionally; frequently used by Pāṇini<BR> in his Sūtras in the sense of वा or विभाषा; हृकोरन्यतरस्याम्,<BR> आत्मनेपदेष्वन्यतरस्याम् &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरतः
अन्यतरतः <i>adv.</i> One one of the two sides;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरदन्त
अन्यतरतः + ˚दन्त having<BR> teeth on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरेद्युः
अन्यतरेद्युः <i>adv.</i> [अन्यतरस्मिन्नहनि -एद्युस्] One either<BR> of the two days, on one day or on another, P. V. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतः
अन्यतः <i>adv.</i><BR>—1 From another; न चान्यतस्तस्य शरीररक्षा R. 2. 4; तीर्थोदकं<BR> च वह्निश्च नान्यतः शुद्धिमर्हतः U. 1. 13.<BR>—2 One one side; अन्यतः━अन्यतः, एकतः -अन्यतः on the one side,<BR> on the other side; तपनमण्डलदीपितमेकतः सततनैशतमोवृतमन्यतः<BR> Ki. 5. 2; एकवस्तु सकलानि निमित्तान्यन्यतो हि मनसः प्रतिपत्तिः Nīti.<BR>—3 To another place, towards some other person or direction; गन्तव्यं<BR> वा ततोऽन्यतः Ms. 2. 200; अन्यतोऽपि नयने प्रेरयन्त्या Ś. 2. 2;<BR> आर्ये व्रजामोऽन्यतः R. 6. 82.<BR>—4 From another ground or motive.<BR>—5 On the other side; on the contrary.<BR>—6 Otherwise; in another place, elsewhere.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यतोरण्यम्, अन्यतएत, अन्यतएतस्, अन्यतएनी, अन्यतोघातिन्, अन्यतोवात<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतोरण्यम्
अन्यतः + -अरण्यम् Ved. a land which is woody here and there. Vāj. 30. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतएत
अन्यतः + -एत, -एतस्, -एनी Ved. variegated or spotted on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतएतस्
अन्यतः + -एत, -एतस्, -एनी Ved. variegated or spotted on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतएनी
अन्यतः + -एत, -एतस्, -एनी Ved. variegated or spotted on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतोघातिन्
अन्यतः + -घातिन् <i>a.</i> striking in one direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतोवात|अन्यतोवातः
अन्यतः + -वात <i>a.</i> suffering occasional wind (rheumatism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतोवातः|अन्यतोवात
अन्यतः + -वात + .({@-तः@}) a sort of eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्त्यः|अन्यतस्त्य
अन्यतस्त्यः [अन्यतो भवः, त्यप्] An enemy, adversary. स य<BR> एतमेवमुपास्ते जिष्णुर्हापराजिष्णुर्भवत्यन्यतस्त्यजायी Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यतस्त्यजयिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्त्यजयिन्
अन्यतस्त्यः + -जयिन् <i>a.</i> overwhelming adversaries. Śat. Br. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र <i>adv.</i> [अन्य-त्रल्] (oft. = अन्यस्मिन् with a subst. or adj. force)<BR>—1 Elsewhere, in another place (with abl.); अपत्याधिकारादन्यत्र लौकिकमपत्यमात्रं<BR> गोत्रम् P. IV. 2. 39 Com.; sometimes with विना; विना मलयमन्यत्र<BR> चन्दनं न प्ररोहति Pt. 1. 41; (with verbs of motion) to another place.<BR>—2 On another occasion, at another time than; oft. (in comp.); मधुपर्के<BR> च यज्ञे च पितुर्दैवतकर्मणि । अत्रैव पशवो हिंस्यान्नान्यत्रेत्यब्रवीन्मनुः Ms. 5. 41.<BR>—3 Except, without, other than; यथा फलानां जातानां नान्यत्र पतनाद्भयम् ।<BR> एवं नरस्य जातस्य नान्यत्र मरणाद्भयम् ॥ Rām. 2. 105. 17; Mv. 6. 8;<BR> R. 14. 32; Bg. 3. 9; Y. 1. 215; अन्यत्र नैमिषेयसत्रात् V. 5,<BR> Ms. 4. 164; oft. with the force of the nom. case; देवा अन्यत्रैवाश्विभ्यां<BR> सत्त्रं निषेदुः Kauṣ. Br. (अन्यत्र = अन्ये).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">Page0131-2</a>]<BR>—4 Otherwise, in another way, in the other case, in the other sense; सुराज्ञि<BR> देशे राजन्वान् स्यात्ततोऽन्यत्र राजवान् Ak.; राजन्वती भूः, राजवान्<BR> अन्यत्र; चर्मण्वती नदी चर्मवती अन्यत्र P. VIII. 2. 12, 14. Sk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यत्रमनस्, अन्यत्रचित्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्रमनस्
अन्यत्र + -मनस्, -चित्त <i>a.</i> whose mind is directed to something else,<BR> inattentive. Śat. Br. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्रचित्त
अन्यत्र + -मनस्, -चित्त <i>a.</i> whose mind is directed to something else,<BR> inattentive. Śat. Br. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा <i>ind.</i> [अन्य-प्रकारार्थे था]<BR>—1 Otherwise, in another way or manner, in a different manner; यदभावि<BR> न तद्भावि भावि चेन्न तदन्यथा H. प्रस्ताविका 24; with अतः, इतः<BR> or ततः otherwise than, in a manner different from; अतोऽन्यथा प्रवृत्तिस्तु<BR> राक्षसो विधिरुच्यते Ms. 5. 31; एतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोऽन्यथा<BR> Bg. 13. 11. अन्यथा━अन्यथा in one way, in another (different) way;<BR> योऽन्यथा सन्तमात्मानमन्यथा भाषते Ms. 4. 255; सत्त्वभङ्गभयाद्राज्ञां<BR> कथयन्त्यन्यथा पुरः । अन्यथा विवृतार्थेषु स्वैरालापेषु मन्त्रिणः Mu. 4. 8.<BR> अन्यथा कृ<BR>——(<i>a</i>) to do otherwise, change or alter; न हि दैवं शक्यमन्यथा<BR> कर्तुमभियुक्तेनापि K. 62; न स्वभावोऽत्र मर्त्यानां शक्यते कर्तुमन्यथा<BR> Pt. 1. 258; Ś. 6. 14;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) to act otherwise, violate, transgress, go against; त्वया कदाचिदपि<BR> मम वचनं नान्यथा कृतम् Pt. 4;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) to destroy, undo, frustrate, baffle, defeat (hope, plan &c.),<BR> कर्तुमकर्तुमन्यथाकर्तुं समर्थ ईश्वरः; ममेच्छां मान्यथा कृथाः<BR> Ks. 22. 51; लाभं कुर्याच्च योऽन्यथा Y. 2. 195;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) to make false, falsify; ख्यातो लोकप्रवादोऽयं भरतेनान्यथा<BR> कृतः Rām.; अमात्यः प्राड्विवाको वा यत्कुर्युः कार्यमन्यथा Ms. 9. 234<BR> to do wrongly; ˚ग्रह्, -मन्, -संभावय्, -समर्थय्, -विकल्पय्<BR> &c. to take or think to be otherwise, to misunderstand, understand wrongly;<BR> अलमन्यथा गृहीत्वा न खलु मन-स्विनि मया प्रयुक्तमिदम् M. 1. 20;<BR> अलमस्मानन्यथा संभाव्य Ś. 1; किं मामन्यथा संभावयसि K. 147;<BR> Ś. 3. 19; जनोऽन्यथा भर्तृमतीं विशङ्कते Ś. 5. 17 suspects to be<BR> otherwise (than chaste), ˚भू or या to be otherwise, be changed<BR> or altered, be falsified; न मे वचनमन्यथा भवितुमर्हति Ś. 4;<BR> शोकार्तस्य प्रवृत्तो मे श्लोको भवतु नान्यथा Rām.; तयोर्महात्मनोर्वाक्यं<BR> नान्यथा याति सांप्रतम् Rām.<BR>—2 Otherwise, or else, in the contrary case; व्यक्तं नास्ति कथमन्यथा<BR> वासन्त्यपि तां न पश्येत् U. 3; स्तेनोऽन्यथा भवेत् Ms. 8. 144; Y. 1. 86, 2. 288;<BR> on the other hand, on the contrary.<BR>—3 Falsely, untruly; किमन्यथा भट्टिनी मया विज्ञापितपूर्वा V. 2; किमन्यथा<BR> भट्टिन्यै विज्ञापितम् M. 4; न खल्वन्यथा ब्राह्मणस्य वचनम् V. 3;<BR> यो न्यायमन्यथा ब्रूते स याति नरकं नरः Pt. 3. 107; H. 3. 15; Ms. 8. 90.<BR>—4 Wrongly, erroneously, badly, as in अन्यथासिद्ध q. v. below; see<BR> under (1) also.<BR>—5 From another motive, cause, or ground; दुर्वाससः शापादियं त्वया<BR> प्रत्यादिष्टा नान्यथा Ś. 7. [cf. L. <i>aliuta</i>.].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यथानुपपत्तिः, अन्यथाकारः, अन्यथाख्यातिः, अन्यथाभावः, अन्यथावादिन्, अन्यथावृत्ति, अन्यथासिद्ध, अन्यथासिद्धम्, अन्यथासिद्धिः, अन्यथास्तोत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथानुपपत्तिः|अन्यथानुपपत्ति
अन्यथा + -अनुपपत्तिः <i>f.</i> see अर्थापत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाकारः|अन्यथाकार
अन्यथा + -कारः changing, altering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाकारम्
अन्यथा + -कारः + .({@-रम्@}) <i>adv.</i> in a different manner, differently P. III. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाख्यातिः|अन्यथाख्याति
अन्यथा + -ख्यातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 erroneous conception of the Spirit.<BR>—2 Name of a philosophical work.<BR>—3 wrong conception in general (in phil.). In Sāṅkhya philosophy it<BR> means the assertion that something is not really what it appears to be<BR> according to sensual perception; title of a philosophical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाभावः|अन्यथाभाव
अन्यथा + -भावः alteration, change, being otherwise, difference; एकस्या<BR> व्यक्तेः सर्वावयवावच्छेदेनान्यथाभावः कार्त्स्न्यम् P. V. 4. 53; Sk. change<BR> of view or mind; मयि ˚भावो न कर्तव्यः Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथावादिन्
अन्यथा + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking differently or falsely; speaking<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">Page0132-1</a>]<BR> falsely or inconsistently; (in law) a prevaricator, prevaricating witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0131-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथावृत्ति
अन्यथा + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 changed, altered.<BR>—2 affected, perturbed; disturbed by strong emotions; मेघालोके भवति<BR> सुखिनोप्यन्यथावृत्ति चेतः Me. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्ध
अन्यथा + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> proved or demonstrated wrongly; (in Nyāya) said<BR> of a cause (कारण) which is not the true one, but only refers to accidental<BR> and remote circumstances (as the ass employed to fetch clay &c. in the<BR> case of a घट or jar) which do not invariably contribute to the result,<BR> see कारण; this अन्यथा˚ is said to be of 3 kinds in Tarka K.,<BR> but 5 are mentioned in Bhāṣā P. 19-22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धम्
अन्यथा + -सिद्धम्, -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> wrong demonstration; one in which arguments<BR> not being true causes are advanced; an unessential cause, an accidental<BR> or concomitant circumstance. Bhāṣā P. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धिः|अन्यथासिद्धि
अन्यथा + -सिद्धम्, -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> wrong demonstration; one in which arguments<BR> not being true causes are advanced; an unessential cause, an accidental<BR> or concomitant circumstance. Bhāṣā P. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथास्तोत्रम्
अन्यथा + -स्तोत्रम् satire, irony; सत्यासत्यान्यथास्तोत्रैर्न्यूनाङ्गेन्द्रियरोगिणाम्<BR> (क्षेपं करोति) cf. यत्र विकृताकृतिरेव दर्शनीयस्त्वमसीत्युच्यते<BR> तदन्यथास्तोत्रम् । Mit. Y. 2. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथयति
अन्यथयति Den. P. To change, alter, to change into something totally<BR> different; धर्मश्च कर्तुमकर्तुमन्यथयितुमीश्वरस्य शिवस्य आज्ञानुल्लङ्घनम् ।<BR> चोलचम्पू p. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 At another time, on another occasion, in any other case; अन्यदा भूषणं<BR> पुंसां क्षमा लज्जेव योषिताम् Śi. 2. 44; R. 11. 73.<BR>—2 Once, one day, at one time, once upon a time. अन्यदा भृशमुद्विग्नमना<BR> नष्टद्रविण इव कृपणः कश्मलं महदभिरम्भित इति होवाच Bhāg. 5. 8. 15.<BR>—3 Sometimes, now and then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीय
अन्यदीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to another.<BR>—2 Being or existing in another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यर्हि
अन्यर्हि <i>ind.</i> At another time (= अन्यदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृक्ष
अन्यादृक्ष^1, -श्, -श <i>a.</i><BR> [अन्य इव पश्यति, अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स,<BR> क्विन्, कञ् वा P. III. 2. 60]<BR>—1 Of another kind, like another.<BR>—2 Changed, unusual, strange; यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवन्तमवधारयामि<BR> Māl. 1; अन्यादृशमेव भगवत्या वचनम् 2; being different or otherwise;<BR> न खलु अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवन्ति 4; अन्यादृश्येव<BR> क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106; K. 309; अन्यादृशी रचना कस्यापि वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश्
अन्यादृक्ष^1, -श्, -श <i>a.</i><BR> [अन्य इव पश्यति, अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स,<BR> क्विन्, कञ् वा P. III. 2. 60]<BR>—1 Of another kind, like another.<BR>—2 Changed, unusual, strange; यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवन्तमवधारयामि<BR> Māl. 1; अन्यादृशमेव भगवत्या वचनम् 2; being different or otherwise;<BR> न खलु अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवन्ति 4; अन्यादृश्येव<BR> क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106; K. 309; अन्यादृशी रचना कस्यापि वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश|अन्यादृशः
अन्यादृक्ष^1, -श्, -श <i>a.</i><BR> [अन्य इव पश्यति, अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स,<BR> क्विन्, कञ् वा P. III. 2. 60]<BR>—1 Of another kind, like another.<BR>—2 Changed, unusual, strange; यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवन्तमवधारयामि<BR> Māl. 1; अन्यादृशमेव भगवत्या वचनम् 2; being different or otherwise;<BR> न खलु अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवन्ति 4; अन्यादृश्येव<BR> क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106; K. 309; अन्यादृशी रचना कस्यापि वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यान्य
अन्यान्य <i>a.</i> See अन्योन्य; अन्यान्याश्चैव तनवो यथेष्टं प्रतिपद्यते<BR> Mb. 14. 19. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युः|अन्येद्यु
अन्येद्युः <i>ind.</i> [अन्य-एद्युस् P. V. 3. 22]<BR>—1 On the other or following day; अन्येद्युरात्मानुचरस्य भावं जिज्ञासमाना R. 2. 26.<BR>—2 one day, once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युष्क|अन्येद्युष्कः
अन्येद्युष्क <i>a.</i> [अन्येद्युर्भवः, कन्] Occurring every day, daily,<BR> diurnal; अन्येद्युष्कमहोरात्रादेककालं प्रवर्तते Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युष्कः|अन्येद्युष्क
अन्येद्युष्क + .{@-ष्कः@} A quotidian fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य <i>a.</i> [अन्य-कर्मव्यतिहारे द्वित्वं, पूर्वपदे सुश्च]<BR> One another, each other, mutual (treated like a pronoun). In many cases<BR> the use of this word corresponds to the use of the word ‘each other’ or<BR> ‘one another’ in English; अन्योन्यं ताडयतः Mk. 9 they strike each other<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">Page0132-2</a>]<BR> (अन्यः अन्यं ताडयति). Thus अन्यः may be regarded as the subject<BR> and अन्यम् as the object of the verb, as in English. The second अन्य<BR> may, therefore, in many cases stand in the instr., gen., or loc. cases;<BR> अन्योन्यैराहताः सन्तः सस्वनुर्भीमनिःस्वनाः Rām.; अन्योन्यस्य व्यतिलुनन्ति<BR> P. I. 3. 16. Sk. But there are several instances, especially when अन्योन्य<BR> enters into compound, in which the first अन्य loses all its nominative<BR> force and becomes a sort of oblique case, or an irregular compound of<BR> अन्य and अन्य, see P. VIII. 1. 12. Sk.; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारः<BR> Ms. 9. 101; oft. in comp. and translated by ‘mutual’, ‘reciprocal’, ‘mutually’;<BR> ˚शोभाजननात् Ku. 1. 42; so ˚कलह, ˚दर्शन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यम्
अन्योन्य + .{@-न्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Mutually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यम्
अन्योन्य + .{@-न्यम्@} (In Rhet.) A figure of speech, the ‘Reciprocal’, in which<BR> two things do the same act to each other; अन्योन्यमुभयोरेकक्रियायाः<BR> करणं मिथः । त्वया सा शोभते तन्वी तया त्वमपि शोभसे ॥ रजन्या शोभते<BR> चन्द्रश्चन्द्रेणापि निशीथिनी । S. D. 724.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्योन्याध्यासः, अन्योन्यापहृत, अन्योन्याभावः, अन्योन्याश्रय, अन्योन्योक्तिः, अन्योन्यकार्यम्, अन्योन्यपक्षनयनम्, अन्योन्यभेदः, अन्योन्यमिथुनम्, अन्योन्यविभागः, अन्योन्यवृत्तिः, अन्योन्यव्यतिकरः, अन्योन्यसंश्रयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याध्यासः|अन्योन्याध्यास
अन्योन्य + -अध्यासः reciprocal attribution of identity (अन्योन्यतादात्म्यारोपः);<BR> जलव्योम्ना घटाकाशो यथा सर्वस्तिरोहितः । तथा जीवे च कूटस्थः सोऽन्योन्याध्यास उच्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यापहृत
अन्योन्य + -अपहृत <i>a.</i> taken from one another, taken secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याभावः|अन्योन्याभाव
अन्योन्य + -अभावः mutual non-existence or negation; one of the two main<BR> kinds of अभाव; it is reciprocal negation of identity, essence, or<BR> respective peculiarity, and is equivalent to difference (भेद); तादात्म्यसंबन्धावच्छिन्नप्रतियोगिकोऽन्योन्याभावः,<BR> as घटः पटो न भवति; it exists between two notions which have<BR> no property in common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याश्रय|अन्योन्याश्रयः
अन्योन्य + -आश्रय <i>a.</i> mutually dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याश्रयः|अन्योन्याश्रय
अन्योन्य + -आश्रय + .({@-यः@}) mutual or reciprocal dependence, support, or connection;<BR> reciprocal relation of cause and effect (a term in Nyāya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्योक्तिः|अन्योन्योक्ति
अन्योन्य + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यकार्यम्
अन्योन्य + -कार्यम् Sexual intercourse (मैथुन); अन्योन्यकार्याणि यथा<BR> तथैव न पापमात्रेण कृतं हिनस्ति Mb. 12. 141. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यपक्षनयनम्
अन्योन्य + -पक्षनयनम् transposition of numbers from one side to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यभेदः|अन्योन्यभेद
अन्योन्य + -भेदः mutual dissension or enmity; so ˚कलह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यकलह
अन्योन्य + -भेदः mutual dissension or enmity; so ˚कलह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यमिथुनम्
अन्योन्य + -मिथुनम् mutual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यविभागः|अन्योन्यविभाग
अन्योन्य + -विभागः mutual partition of an inheritance made by the sharers<BR> (without the presence of any other party).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यवृत्तिः|अन्योन्यवृत्ति
अन्योन्य + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> mutual effect of one thing upon another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यव्यतिकरः|अन्योन्यव्यतिकर
अन्योन्य + -व्यतिकरः, -संश्रयः reciprocal action or influence; mutual<BR> relation of cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यसंश्रयः|अन्योन्यसंश्रय
अन्योन्य + -व्यतिकरः, -संश्रयः reciprocal action or influence; mutual<BR> relation of cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यङ्ग|अन्यंग
अन्यङ्ग <i>a.</i> Ved. Spotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्या
अन्या <i>a.</i> Ved. Not drying up, inexhaustible; इन्द्रं धेनुं सुदुघामन्याम् Rv. 8. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Unjust, improper;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायदण्डः|अन्यायदण्ड
अन्याय + ˚दण्डः unjust punishment;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायः|अन्याय
अन्याय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Any unjust or unlawful action; see न्याय; नरेष्वन्यायवर्तिषु Ms. 7. 16<BR> acting unjustly, following evil courses; अन्यायेन unjustly,<BR> improperly; नापृष्टः कस्यचिद् ब्रूयान्न चान्यायेन पृच्छतः Ms. 2. 110.<BR>—2 Injustice, impropriety.<BR>—3 Irregularity, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अन्यायिन् <i>a.</i> Unjust, improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्य|अन्याय्यः
अन्याय्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unjust, unlawful. अन्याय्यः परदारपृच्छाव्यवहारः Ś. 5.<BR>—2 Improper, unbecoming, indecorous,<BR>—3 Not authoritative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0132-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून <i>a.</i> Not defective or deficient, complete, whole, entire;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्यूनाङ्ग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनाधिक
अन्यून + ˚अधिक neither deficient nor superfluous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनाङ्ग|अन्यूनांग
अन्यून + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> not having a defective limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योकस्
अन्योकस् <i>a.</i> Not residing in oneʼs own house (dwelling in anotherʼs), Av.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्ष|अन्वक्षः
अन्वक्ष <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः अक्षम् इन्द्रियं गति समा.]<BR>—1 Visible, perceptible.<BR>—2 Following, close on the heels of, immediately following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्षम्
अन्वक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Afterwards, after; आरोह त्वं … सीतां चारोपयान्वक्षम् Rām. 2. 52. 75.<BR>—2 Immediately after, forthwith, directly; हतानां नृपगोविप्रैरन्वक्षं<BR> चात्मधातिनाम् Y. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्षरसन्धिः|अन्वक्षरसन्धि|अन्वक्षरसंधि|अन्वक्षरसंधिः
अन्वक्षरसन्धिः A kind of Vedic Sandhi, that of a vowel and consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वञ्च्|अन्वंच्
अन्वञ्च् <i>a.</i> [अनु-अञ्च्-क्विप्; nom. अन्वङ् <i>m.</i>, अन्वक्<BR> <i>n.</i> अनूची <i>f.</i>]<BR>—1 Going after, following; तस्मादिमे अन्वञ्चो मासा यन्ति Śat. Br.;<BR> त्वामन्वञ्चो वयं स्मसि Ait. Br.<BR>—2 Lying lengthwise, horizontal; {@अनूचि@} <i>adv.</i> in the rear or<BR> behind, from behind; आगच्छतोऽनूचि गजस्य घण्टयोः Śi. 12. 34 (पृष्ठदेशे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्
अन्वक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Afterwards; बालेन निष्कर्षयताऽन्वगुलूखलं तद्दामोदरेण तरसोऽत्कलिताङ्घ्रिबन्धौ<BR> Bhāg. 10. 10. 27.<BR>—2 from behind; पिदधानमन्वगुपगम्य दृशौ Śi. 9. 76.<BR>—3 Friendly disposed, favourably; अन्वग्भूत्वा, -भावं, -आस्ते becoming<BR> friendly disposed P. III. 4. 64. Sk. (अग्रतः पार्श्वतः पृष्ठतो वानुकूलो<BR> भूत्वा आस्ते; अन्वग्भूत्वा तिष्ठति = पृष्ठतो भूत्वा) cf. अन्वग्भावं रघुवृषभयोर्वानरेन्द्रो<BR> विराजन् Bk. 6. 143.<BR>—4 (with acc.) After; तां … अन्वग्ययौ मध्यमलोकपालः R. 2. 16<BR> went after or followed her; तमन्वगिन्द्रप्रमुखाश्च देवाः Ku. 7. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वन्
अन्वन् <i>a.</i> [अन्-वनिप्] Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वन्तः|अन्वन्त
अन्वन्तः A raised platform or a couch; Māna. 16. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय See under अन्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्तितृ
अन्वर्तितृ <i>m.</i> Ved. An inviter, a wooer; अन्वर्तिता वरुणो मित्र<BR> आसीत् Rv. 10. 109. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थ
अन्वर्थ <i>a.</i> [अनुगतः अर्थम्] Having the meaning clear or intelligible,<BR> having a meaning easily deducible from the etymology of the word; hence,<BR> true to the sense, significant; तथैव सोऽभूदन्वर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरञ्जनात्<BR> R. 4. 12; अन्वर्था तैर्वसुन्धरा Ki. 11. 64; अन्वर्थसंज्ञैव परं<BR> त्रिमार्गगा Śi. 12. 23; अन्वर्थ एवायमधुना प्रलापो वर्तते U. 3;<BR> अन्वर्थतोऽपि ननु राक्षस राक्षसोऽसि Mu. 5. 7 in the true sense of<BR> the word, properly so called.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वर्थग्रहणम्, अन्वर्थसंज्ञा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थग्रहणम्
अन्वर्थ + -ग्रहणम् literal acceptation of the meaning of a word (opp. to<BR> रूढ or conventional).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थसंज्ञा
अन्वर्थ + -संज्ञा<BR>—1 an appropriate name, a technical term which directly conveys its own<BR> meaning; <i>e. g.</i> भविष्यन्ती a name for ‘future’ is an अन्वर्थसंज्ञा<BR> compared with ऌट्.<BR>—2 a proper name the meaning of which is obvious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववकिरणम्
अन्ववकिरणम् Scattering about successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववचारः|अन्ववचार
अन्ववचारः Descending and following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसर्गः|अन्ववसर्ग
अन्ववसर्गः [सृज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Slackening, letting loose (opp. आयाम).<BR>—2 Permission to do as one likes (कामचारानुज्ञा), one of the senses<BR> of अपि P. I. 4. 96; see अपि.<BR>—3 Following oneʼs own will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसित
अन्ववसित <i>a.</i> Connected with, bound or fastened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववायः|अन्ववाय
अन्ववायः A race, family, lineage; तस्यान्ववाये राजानः क्रमाद्येनाभिषेचिताः<BR> Rām. 6. 128. 65; अन्ववायमवदातमाकृतिः Ki. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्षा
अन्ववेक्षा Regard, consideration. तस्यै स प्रददौ मन्त्रमापद्धर्मान्ववेक्षया Mb. 1. 111. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका [अनुगतोऽष्टकाम्] The 9th day of the dark half of, the<BR> three months following the full moon in मार्गशीर्ष, i. e. पौष,<BR> माघ and फाल्गुन; पितॄंश्चैवाष्टकास्वर्चेन्नित्यमन्वष्टकासु च Ms. 4. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टक्यम्
अन्वष्टक्यम् A Śrāddha or any such ceremony performed on the अन्वष्टका days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टमदिशम्
अन्वष्टमदिशम् <i>ind.</i> Towards the north-east direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वस्त
अन्वस्त <i>a.</i> [fr. अस् to throw] Shot or hurled along, shot;<BR> interwoven (as in silk); chequered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम् <i>ind.</i> Day after day, every day. आभ्यः कुर्याद् देवताभ्यो<BR> ब्राह्मणो होममन्वहम् Ms. 3. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्या
अन्वाख्या €2 P. To repeat in succession, enumerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्यानम्
अन्वाख्यानम्<BR>—1 Subsequent mention or enumeration; an explanation referring to what<BR> is mentioned before.<BR>—2 Section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वागम्
अन्वागम् €1 P. To follow, come after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वागत
अन्वागत <i>a.</i> Attached; स यत्तत्र किंचित्पश्यत्यनन्वागतस्तेन<BR> भवत्यसङ्गः Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचयः|अन्वाचय
अन्वाचयः [प्रधानस्य पश्चादन्यः आचीयते बोध्यते यत्र, चिअच्]<BR>—1 Statement of a secondary (गौण) rite or action after the mention<BR> of a primary (प्रधान) one; adding an object of secondary importance<BR> to the main object, one of the senses of the particle च; चान्वाचये<BR> समाहारे Ak.; अन्यतरस्यानुषङ्गिकत्वेऽन्वाचयः; as भो भिक्षामट<BR> गां चानय where going out to beg is enjoined to the beggar as his principal<BR> object, and the bringing of a cow (if he can see any) is tacked on to<BR> it as a secondary object.<BR>—2 Such an object itself.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वाचयशिष्ट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचयशिष्ट
अन्वाचयः + -शिष्ट <i>a.</i> propounded as a rule or matter of secondary importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचित
अन्वाचित <i>a.</i> Secondary, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाजे
अन्वाजे <i>ind.</i> [अनु आजयत्यनेन, अनु आजि-डे Tv.] (Used like<BR> उपाजे only with कृ) So as to assist or support the weak (दुर्बलस्य<BR> बलाधाने); optionally regarded as a preposition; ˚कृत्य or ˚कृत्वा<BR> supporting, assisting (a weak person); दुर्बलस्य बलमाधाय P. I. 4. 73. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिश्
अन्वादिश् €6 P. To name or mention again; to mention or refer to in<BR> a subsequent place, employ again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0133-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिष्ट
अन्वादिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mentioned after or according to; employed again; अन्वादिष्टः पुरुषः<BR> अनुपुरुषः P. VI. 2. 190. Sk.<BR>—2 (Hence) Inferior, of secondary importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादेशः|अन्वादेश
अन्वादेशः<BR>—1 Subsequent or repeated mention, referring to what has been previously<BR> mentioned; re-employment of the same word in a subsequent part of a sentence,<BR> or of the same thing to perform a subsequent operation; आदेशः कथनम्<BR> अन्वादेशः अनुकथनम् Kāśi. on P. II. 4. 32. (इदम् and एतद्<BR> are said to assume the forms एने, एनौ, एनान् &c. in the sense of अन्वादेश;<BR> किंचित्कार्यं विधातुमुपात्तस्य कार्यान्तरं विधातुं पुनरुपादानम् अन्वादेशः;<BR> e. g. अनेन व्याकरणमधीतम् एनं छन्दोऽध्यापय; अनयोः पवित्रं कुलम्<BR> एनयोः प्रभूतं स्वम् Sk.).<BR>—2 An additional statement, a supplement; शूद्रश्च न देय इत्यन्वादेशः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधानम्
अन्वाधानम् [अग्निस्थापनस्य पश्चादाधानम्] Putting on or depositing<BR> fuel on the sacred fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधिः|अन्वाधि
अन्वाधिः [अनु पश्चादाधीयते, धा-कि] (In civil law)<BR>—1 A bail, deposit or security delivered to a third person to be handed<BR> over ultimately to the right owner; अर्थमार्गणकार्येषु अन्यस्मिन्वचनान्मम ।<BR> दद्यास्त्वमिति यो दत्तः स इहान्वाधिरुच्यते ॥.<BR>—2 A second deposit.<BR>—3 [अनुगतः सन्ततः आधिः] Constant anxiety, remorse, repentance,<BR> regret (after the committal of a bad act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयम्
अन्वाधेयम्, -यकम्<BR> A sort of स्त्रीधन or womanʼs property, presented to<BR> her after marriage by her husbandʼs or fatherʼs family, or by her own<BR> relatives; विवाहात्परतो यच्च लब्धं भर्तृकुलात् स्त्रिया । अन्वाधेयं तु<BR> तद् द्रव्यं लब्धं पितृ (v. l. बन्धु-) कुलात्तथा ॥ Kāty. quoted<BR> by Kull. on Ms. 9. 195; बन्धुदत्तं तथा शुल्कमन्वाधेयकमेव च Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयकम्
अन्वाधेयम्, -यकम्<BR> A sort of स्त्रीधन or womanʼs property, presented to<BR> her after marriage by her husbandʼs or fatherʼs family, or by her own<BR> relatives; विवाहात्परतो यच्च लब्धं भर्तृकुलात् स्त्रिया । अन्वाधेयं तु<BR> तद् द्रव्यं लब्धं पितृ (v. l. बन्धु-) कुलात्तथा ॥ Kāty. quoted<BR> by Kull. on Ms. 9. 195; बन्धुदत्तं तथा शुल्कमन्वाधेयकमेव च Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित = अन्वाधि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाध्यः|अन्वाध्य
अन्वाध्यः A class of divinities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वान्त्र्य|अन्वांत्र्य
अन्वान्त्र्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Being in the entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतन
अन्वायतन <i>a.</i> Latitudinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतनम्
अन्वायतन + .{@-नम्@} <i>ind.</i> In the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायत्त
अन्वायत्त <i>a.</i> Ved. In accordance with (अनुगत &c.); following after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायात्या
अन्वायात्या A deity invoked by the verb अन्वाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्
अन्वारभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To begin, commence.<BR>—2 To touch; अंसेऽध्वर्युमन्वारभते Āśval. यदि मां संस्पृशेद्रामः<BR> सकृदन्वारभेत वा । धनं वा यौवराज्यं वा जीवेयमिति मे मतिः ॥ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारब्ध
अन्वारब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Touched on the back or on any part of the body; विष्णोः कर्माणीति<BR> वाचयति रूपमन्वारब्धमिति Kāty.<BR>—2 That which has touched or has been placed on the body (as the hand).<BR>—3 Followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्य
अन्वारभ्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be touched along with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भः|अन्वारम्भ|अन्वारंभः
अन्वारम्भः, -म्भणम्<BR> Touching, contact, especially touching the यजमान<BR> (the performer of a sacrifice) to make him entitled to the fruits and<BR> merits of the holy rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भणम्
अन्वारम्भः, -म्भणम्<BR> Touching, contact, especially touching the यजमान<BR> (the performer of a sacrifice) to make him entitled to the fruits and<BR> merits of the holy rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भणीया|अन्वारंभणीया
अन्वारम्भणीया<BR>—1 An initiatory or preliminary ceremony.<BR>—2 A sacrificial rite to be performed before दर्शपूर्णमास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारुह्
अन्वारुह् €1 P. To follow in ascending, especially the funeral pile;<BR> to ascend, climb, mount; अन्वारोहच्च सुग्रीवः (गिरिम्) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहः|अन्वारोह
अन्वारोहः N. of certain Japas uttered at the soma-libations. Ts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहणम्
अन्वारोहणम्^1 A womanʼs ascending the funeral pile after or with the<BR> body of her husband.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: missing virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वास्
अन्वास् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To be seated near or round; सखायमन्वास्ते Mb.; to wait upon,<BR> serve, attend upon; सखीभ्यामन्वास्यते Ś. 3; अन्वासितमरुन्धत्या<BR> स्वाहयेव हविर्भुजम् R. 1. 56; to sit after one (acc. of person); ताम्<BR> अन्वास्य R. 2. 24.<BR>—2 To perform, as a religious ceremony; सन्ध्यामन्वास्य पश्चिमाम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासनम्
अन्वासनम्<BR>—1 Service, attendance, waiting upon, worship.<BR>—2 Taking a seat after another.<BR>—3 Regret, sorrow.<BR>—4 A place of industry, manufactory, workshop &c.<BR>—5 An oily or cooling enema.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासीन
अन्वासीन <i>pres. p.</i> Sitting down after, seated along side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य <i>a.</i> To be performed later, following (duty); अन्वाहार्यं<BR> महाराज पितॄणां श्राद्धमुच्यते Mb. 13. 87. 6. ˚त्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्यः (also -र्यम्) -र्यकम्<BR> [अनु मासि मासि आह्रियते, कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 A sacrificial gift or offering presented to the priests (Sāy. अन्वाहरति<BR> यज्ञसंबन्धि दोषजातं परिहरत्यनेन इत्यन्वाहार्यो नाम ऋत्विग्भ्यो देय ओदनः)<BR>—2 The monthly Śrāddha performed in honour of the manes on the day of<BR> new moon; पितॄणां मासिकं श्राद्धमन्वाहार्यं विदुर्बुधाः Ms. 3. 123.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वाहार्यपचनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यम्
अन्वाहार्यः (also -र्यम्) -र्यकम्<BR> [अनु मासि मासि आह्रियते, कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 A sacrificial gift or offering presented to the priests (Sāy. अन्वाहरति<BR> यज्ञसंबन्धि दोषजातं परिहरत्यनेन इत्यन्वाहार्यो नाम ऋत्विग्भ्यो देय ओदनः)<BR>—2 The monthly Śrāddha performed in honour of the manes on the day of<BR> new moon; पितॄणां मासिकं श्राद्धमन्वाहार्यं विदुर्बुधाः Ms. 3. 123.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वाहार्यपचनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यकम्
अन्वाहार्यः (also -र्यम्) -र्यकम्<BR> [अनु मासि मासि आह्रियते, कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 A sacrificial gift or offering presented to the priests (Sāy. अन्वाहरति<BR> यज्ञसंबन्धि दोषजातं परिहरत्यनेन इत्यन्वाहार्यो नाम ऋत्विग्भ्यो देय ओदनः)<BR>—2 The monthly Śrāddha performed in honour of the manes on the day of<BR> new moon; पितॄणां मासिकं श्राद्धमन्वाहार्यं विदुर्बुधाः Ms. 3. 123.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वाहार्यपचनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यपचनः|अन्वाहार्यपचन|अन्वाहार्य्यपचन
अन्वाहार्यः + -पचनः the southern sacrificial fire used in the अन्वाहार्य<BR> sacrifice. अन्वाहार्यपचनं यजुरन्तरिक्षम् T. Ār. अथान्वाहार्यपचनादुत्थितो<BR> घोरदर्शनः Bhāg. 6. 9. 12; Ch. Up. 4. 12. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Daily, diurnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित = अन्वाधेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वि
अन्वि €2 P. [अनु-इ]<BR>—1 To follow, come or go after, succeed; ऋतस्य पन्थामन्वेतवै Rv. 7. 44. 5.<BR> गच्छतः पृष्टतोऽन्वियात् Ms. 4. 154; एनां … प्रयता<BR> प्रातरन्वेतु R. 1. 90; शुनीमन्वेति श्वा Bh. 3. 18; attend, accompany,<BR> accrue to; कर्मफलं कर्तारमन्वेति.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To follow (in grammar or construction); be connected or construed<BR> with; धातुरादेशमन्वेति Mb. See अन्वय below.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To obey, conform to, be guided by; यश्चित्तमन्वेति परस्य Mb.<BR>—3 To seek; to fall to oneʼs lot (Ved.). मा पितुर्गोतमादन्वियाय Rv. 4. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयः|अन्वय
अन्वयः [इकर्तरि भावे वा अच्]<BR>—1 Going after, following; follower, retinue, attendants; का त्वमेकाकिनी<BR> भीरु निरन्वयजने वने Bk. 5. 66.<BR>—2 Association, connection, relation; गन्धः कटुकान्वयः = कटुकान्वितः.<BR>—3 The natural<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">Page0135-1</a>]<BR> order or connection of words in a sentence, construing grammatical order<BR> or relation; पदानां परस्पराकाङ्क्षा योग्यता च, or शब्दानां परस्परमर्थानुगमनम्;<BR> तात्पर्याख्यां वृत्तिमाहुः पदार्थान्वयबोधने S. D.; logical connection<BR> of words, अत्र (in the ex. तिष्ठतु सर्पिः) सर्पिःशब्दस्य स्थितिक्रियायामन्वयः<BR> P. VIII. 3. 44 Sk; परस्परनिरपेक्षस्यानेकस्य एकस्मिन्नन्वयः समुच्चयः<BR> P. II. 2. 29. Sk.<BR>—4 Drift, tenor, purport.<BR>—5 Race, family, lineage; रघूणामन्वयं वक्षये R. 1. 9, 12, 3. 27, 12. 33;<BR> अन्वयगुणः Mv. 4. 22 virtue of my race.<BR>—6 Descendants, posterity; ताभ्य ऋते अन्वयः Y. 2. 117; स˚ along<BR> with the family or descendants; Ms. 2. 168; जातस्तु गण्यते सोऽत्र यः<BR> स्फुरत्यन्वयाधिकम् Pt. 1. 27.<BR>—7 Logical connection of cause and effect, logical continuance; जन्माद्यस्य<BR> यतोऽन्वयादितरतः Bhāg. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—8 Being seen (प्रत्यक्ष); स्यात्साहसं त्वन्वयवत् प्रसभं कर्म<BR> यत्कृतम् । निरन्वयं भवेत्स्तेयम् … Ms. 8. 332.<BR>—9 (In Nyāya) Statement of the constant and invariable concomitance of<BR> the हेतु (middle term) and the साध्य (major term) of an Indian<BR> syllogism (हेतुसाध्ययोर्व्याप्तिरन्वयः). In the familiar instance पर्वतो<BR> वह्निमान् धूमवत्त्वात् the relation यत्र यत्र धूमस्तत्र तत्र वह्निः<BR> (wherever there is smoke there is fire) is called अन्वय or अन्वयव्याप्ति.<BR> अन्वय, in fact, corresponds to the universal proposition of European<BR> logic ‘All A is B’. The ‘व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति’ means an assertion of the<BR> concomitance of the absence of साध्य and the absence of हेतु (तदभावयोः<BR> हेत्वभावसाध्याभावयोः व्याप्तिः) and corresponds to the converted A proposition<BR> ‘All not-B is not-A’; or in Sanskrit यत्र यत्र वह्निर्नास्ति तत्र तत्र<BR> धूमोऽपि नास्ति; and a cause or हेतु is said to be connected with<BR> its effect by अन्वयव्यतिरेकव्याप्ति when both the affirmative and negative<BR> relations between the thing to be proved and the cause that proves can<BR> be equally asserted; such a <i>Hetu</i> alone makes the argument perfectly<BR> sound and incapable of refutation. This process of arriving at the Vyāpti<BR> or universal proposition corresponds to the methods of Agreement and Difference<BR> in Millʼs Logic; साध्ये निश्चितमन्वयेन घटितम् Mu. 5. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वयागत, अन्वयज्ञः, अन्वयव्यतिरेक, अन्वयव्याप्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयागत
अन्वयः + -आगत <i>a.</i> hereditary; Pt. 1, 3; ˚तं वैरम् Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयज्ञः|अन्वयज्ञ
अन्वयः + -ज्ञः a genealogist; अथ स्तुते बन्दिभिरन्वयज्ञैः R. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयव्यतिरेकौ
अन्वयः + -व्यतिरेक (˚कौ or ˚कम्)<BR>—1 positive and negative assertion; agreement and contrariety or difference; see above.<BR>—2 rule and exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयव्यतिरेकम्
अन्वयः + -व्यतिरेक (˚कौ or ˚कम्)<BR>—1 positive and negative assertion; agreement and contrariety or difference; see above.<BR>—2 rule and exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयव्याप्तिः|अन्वयव्याप्ति
अन्वयः + -व्याप्तिः <i>f.</i> affirmative assertion or agreement, affirmative universal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयवत्|अन्वयवन्त्
अन्वयवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a connection or consequence, following.<BR>—2 Belonging to a race or family; born of a noble family, noble, high-born;<BR> सत्यपि अन्वयवति अवरोधजने K. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयायिन्
अन्वयायिन् <i>a.</i> Descendent, belonging to the family; इतीमे काशयो<BR> भूपाः क्षत्रवृद्धान्वयायिनः Bhāg. 9. 17. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन् <i>a.</i> Connected as with a consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्वित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Followed or attended by, in company with, joined by; अमात्यपुत्रैः<BR> सवयोभिरन्वितः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">Page0135-2</a>]<BR> R. 3. 28.<BR>—2 Possessed of, having, possessing, endowed with; full of, seized or<BR> struck with, overpowered by; with instr. or in compound; कुलान्वितं कुकुलजा<BR> निन्दन्ति Pt. 1. 415; धैर्य˚; गुण˚, वित्त˚; विस्मय˚ struck with<BR> wonder; भय˚, क्रोध˚, लोभ˚ &c. &c.<BR>—3 Connected with, linked to, following (as a consequence).<BR>—4 Connected grammatically; वर्णाः पदं प्रयोगार्हानन्वितैकार्थबोधकाः S. D. 9.<BR>—5 Understood, reached by the mind.<BR>—6 Suitable, befitting; तपसा चान्वितो वेषस्त्वं राममहिषी ध्रुवम्<BR> Rām. 5. 33. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अन्वितार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वितार्थ
अन्वित + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> having a meaning which is easily understood from<BR> the context.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वितार्थवादः|अन्वितार्थवाद
अन्वित + -अर्थ + ˚वादः -अभिधानवादः a doctrine of the Mīmāṃsakas that<BR> words in a sentence convey meanings not independently or generally, but<BR> as connected with one another in that particular sentence; see अभिहितान्वयवादिन्<BR> under अभिधा and K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विति|अन्वितिः
अन्विति <i>a.</i> Won over or favourably disposed by means of a salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वितिः|अन्विति
अन्विति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Following.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्
अन्विष् €6 P. To desire, seek, search for or after, look out for, seek<BR> to get; अतः सिद्धिसमेताभ्यामुभाभ्यामन्वियेष सः R. 17. 47. ━(€4 P.)<BR> To seek, search, look out for &c.; न रत्नमन्विष्यति मृग्यते हि तत्<BR> Ku. 5. 45; अन्वेष्टव्यो यदसि भुवने भूतनाथः शरण्यः U. 2. 13; to<BR> inquire, investigate; किं वृथा तर्केण अन्विष्यते Ś. 5.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To seek, search &c.; यामन्वेषयतां प्रयान्ति सततं सर्वे<BR> समाप्तिं गुणाः Bh. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्ट|अन्विष्टः
अन्विष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Desired, sought, searched; यद्वायुरन्विष्टमृगैः<BR> किरातैः Ku. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषः|अन्वेष
अन्वेषः, -षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Search after, seeking for, inquiry into or after,<BR> looking out for, watching; वयं तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हताः Ś. 1. 23;<BR> न्याय ˚णतत्परौ Pt. 3. 91; रन्ध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां द्विषाम् R. 12. 11;<BR> अस्यैवान्वेषणा वर्तते V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0135-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

