 N. of Varuṇa; अपांपित्तम् fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप <i>ind.</i> [न पाति रक्षति पतनात् पा-ड Tv.]<BR>—1 (As a prefix to verbs it means)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Away, away from, denoting वियोग; अपयाति, अपनयति;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) deterioration (विकृति); अपकरोति does wrongly or badly;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) opposition, negation, contradiction (विपरीत); अपकर्षति, अपचिनोति;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) direction or mention or illustration (निदर्शन); अपदिशति;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) exclusion (वर्जन); अपवह्, अपसृ <i>Caus.</i>; (<i>f</i>)<BR> joy, merriment or laughter (आनन्द); अपहसति;<BR>——(<i>g</i>) concealment or denial (चौर्य); अपलपति, अपवदते.<BR>—2 As first member of Tat. or Bahuvrīhi comp. it has all the above senses;<BR> अपयानम्, अपकर्म, अपपाठः; अपशब्दः a bad or corrupt word; ˚भी<BR> fearless; ˚कल्मष stainless; अपरागः discontent (opp. to अनुराग);<BR> ˚मेघोदयं वर्षम् Ku. 6. 54 &c. In most cases अप may be translated<BR> by ‘bad’, ‘inferior’, ‘corrupt’, ‘wrong’, ‘unworthy’ &c. It also means<BR> ‘going downwards’ as in अपानः.<BR>—3 As a separable preposition (with a noun in the abl.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) away from; यत्संप्रत्यप लोकेभ्यो लङ्कायां वसतिर्भयात् Rām.;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) without, on the outside of; अप हरेः संसारः Sk.;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) with the exception of, excepting; अप त्रिगर्तेभ्यो वृष्टो देवः<BR> Sk. on the outside of, with the exception of. In these senses अप<BR> may form adverbial compounds also (P. II. 1. 12); ˚विष्णु संसारः Sk.<BR> without Viṣṇu; ˚त्रिगर्तं वृष्टो देवः excepting त्रिगर्त &c.<BR> It also implies negation, contradiction &c.; ˚कामम्, ˚शङ्कम्. The<BR> senses of this word as given by G. M. may be thus put in verse; वर्जने<BR> विकृतौ चौर्ये विपरीतवियोगयोः । अपकृष्टे च निर्देशे हर्षे चापः प्रयुज्यते.<BR> [cf. L. <i>ab</i>; Gr. <i>apo</i>; Goth. <i>af</i>; Eng. <i>of</i> or <i>off</i>; Zend. <i>apa</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरुण
अपकरुण <i>a.</i> Cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलङ्कः|अपकलङ्क|अपकलंक|अपकलंकः
अपकलङ्कः^1 A deep, indelible stain.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: Not sure. cf mw, ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकामः|अपकाम
अपकामः Ved. Abhorrence, aversion, abominableness; absence of what<BR> is dear. धनुः शत्रोरपकामं करोति Rv. 6. 75. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकामम्
अपकामः + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i> Unwillingly, against oneʼs will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकीर्तिः|अपकीर्ति|अपकीर्त्ति
अपकीर्तिः Infamy, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकुञ्जः|अपकुञ्ज
अपकुञ्जः N. of the younger brother of the serpent-king Śeṣa, Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृ
अपकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To carry or bear away, remove, drag away, insult by dragging away;<BR> योऽपचक्रे वनात् सीताम् Bk. 8. 20 bore forcibly away.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, wrong, harm, do harm or injury to (usually with gen.<BR> of person); आपदि येनापकृतम् Pt. 4. 16; Śi. 14. 78; न किंचिन्मया<BR> तस्यापकर्तुं शक्यम् Pt. 1; किं तस्या मयापकृतम् 4 what harm have<BR> I done to her? किं च राक्षसराजस्य रामेणापकृतं पुरा Rām.; sometimes<BR> with acc. or loc. also; अथ वा सैनिकाः केचिदपकुर्युर्युधिष्ठिरम् Mb.;<BR> किमिव बत नात्मन्यपकृतं Bh. 3. 115; न परेषु महौजसश्छलादपकुर्वन्ति<BR> मलिम्लुचा इव Śi. 16. 52. ━<i>Caus.</i> To harm, injure &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरणम्
अपकरणम्<BR>—1 Acting improperly.<BR>—2 Doing wrong, injuring; ill-treating, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अपकर्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Injurious, doing harm or injury, offensive.<BR>—2 Hostile, inimical. ━<i>m.</i> An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्मन्|अपकर्म्मन्
अपकर्मन् <i>a.</i> [बहु˚ स˚] Of bad or degraded actions,<BR> corrupted, depraved. ━<i>n.</i> (˚र्म)<BR>—1 Discharge, paying off (of a debt); दत्तस्यानपकर्म च Ms. 8. 4.<BR>—2 An improper or unworthy act; evil doing, conduct, or course; any degrading or impure act.<BR>—3 Wickedness, violence, oppression.<BR>—4 Incompetence, laziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारः|अपकार
अपकारः<BR>—1 Harm, wrong; injury, hurt, offence, misdeed, wrong deed (opp. उपकार);<BR> स्वल्पेनाप्यपकारेण ब्राह्मण्यमिव दुष्यति Pt. 1. 66; उपकर्त्रारिणा<BR> सन्धिर्न मित्रेणापकारिणा । उपकारापकारौ हि लक्ष्यं लक्षणमेतयोः<BR> Śi. 2. 37; अपकारोप्युपकारायैव संवृत्तः &c.<BR>—2 Thinking ill of, desire to offend or hurt (अनिष्टचिन्ता).<BR>—3 Wickedness, violence, oppression, enmity.<BR>—4 A mean or degraded action.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपकारार्थिन्, अपकारगिर्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारार्थिन्
अपकारः + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> meaning to harm, malevolent, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारगीः
अपकारः + -गिर् + ({@-गीः@}), {@-शब्दः@}<BR> abusive words, menacing or insulting speech; भर्त्सनं<BR> त्वपकारगीः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अपकारक, -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Injuring, doing harm or wrong to, mischievous, offending,<BR> harmful, hurtful, injurious; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या सापकारिणी<BR> Pt. 1. 95; Śi. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारक, -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Injuring, doing harm or wrong to, mischievous, offending,<BR> harmful, hurtful, injurious; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या सापकारिणी<BR> Pt. 1. 95; Śi. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारकः|अपकारक
अपकारक, -कारिन् + .{@-कः, -री@} An evil-doer (opp. उपकारी), enemy; अपकारिषु<BR> यः साधुः स साधुः सद्भिरुच्यते H. 1; अन्˚ harmless, not harmful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारी
अपकारक, -कारिन् + .{@-कः, -री@} An evil-doer (opp. उपकारी), enemy; अपकारिषु<BR> यः साधुः स साधुः सद्भिरुच्यते H. 1; अन्˚ harmless, not harmful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत
अपकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Injured, wronged, wickedly or maliciously committed &c. निरीक्ष्य<BR> कृष्णाऽपकृतं गुरोः सुतम् Bhāg. 1. 7. 42.<BR>—2 Done or practised as a degrading or impure act, as funeral rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृतम्
अपकृत + .{@-तम्@} An injury, harm, offence. कर्मणः फलनिर्वृत्तिं स्वयमश्नाति<BR> कारकः । प्रत्यक्षं दृश्यते लोके कृतस्यापकृतस्य च ॥ Mb. 13. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0136-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृतिः|अपकृति
अपकृतिः <i>f.</i> अपकृत्यम्<BR>—1 harm, injury, hurt, damage, offence.<BR>—2 Opposition, enmity.<BR>—3 A degrading or impure act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत्यम्
अपकृतिः <i>f.</i> अपकृत्यम्<BR>—1 harm, injury, hurt, damage, offence.<BR>—2 Opposition, enmity.<BR>—3 A degrading or impure act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया<BR>—1 Hurt, injury, disservice; fault, wrong or faulty deed, misdeed; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये<BR> तु शत्रौ (v. l. रिपौ) सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54; मा कृथाः<BR> पुनरमूमपक्रियाम् Ki. 13. 64 fault.<BR>—2 Paying or clearing off (debts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्
अपकृष् €1 P., €6 U.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To draw back or away, draw off or aside, drag down, drag away,<BR> take or carry off, take or draw out, extract; आनायिभिस्तामपकृष्टनक्राम्<BR> R. 16. 55 drawn out; दन्ताग्रभिन्नमपकृष्य निरीक्षते च Ṛs. 4. 13<BR> pulling off or back.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To take or carry away, remove; धैर्यं शोकोऽपकर्षति Rām.;<BR> किं त्वनुष्ठाननित्यत्वं स्वातन्त्र्यमपकर्षति U. 1. 8; Mv. 4. 33 prevents<BR> or interferes with freedom of action; क्षात्रं तेजोऽपकर्षति Mv. 1. 32<BR> destroys, robs one of.<BR>—2 To diminish, decrease, omit; अपकर्षेदेवं यावत्पञ्चदश Suśr.<BR>—3 To bend (as a bow); धनुःश्रेष्ठमपकृष्य Mb.<BR>—4 To lower or debase, dishonour, detract from, lessen the value of, disparage;<BR> पीडयन् भृत्यवर्गं हि आत्मानमपकर्षति Mb.<BR>—5 To bring or draw backwards; anticipate (as a word in a sentence) what<BR> occurs later on; अग्रिमसूत्रस्थं सर्वत्रग्रहणमिहापकृष्यते P. IV. 1. 17<BR> Com. ━<i>Caus.</i> To remove, take away, lessen, diminish, detract from;<BR> काव्यस्यात्मभूतं रसमपकर्षयन्तः काव्यस्यापकर्षकाः (दोषाः)<BR> उच्यन्ते S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षः|अपकर्ष
अपकर्षः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Drawing off or down; diminution, decrease, reduction; मेदोऽपकर्षात्<BR> Dk. 160; loss, decay, decline, destruction; तेजोऽपकर्षः Ve. 1; deterioration,<BR> inferiority; उत्कर्षापकर्षविहीनो मध्यः Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Dishonour, degradation, lowering (of esteem), infamy, disgrace<BR> (opp. उत्कर्ष in all senses); तपोबीजप्रभावैस्तु ते गच्छन्ति युगे<BR> युगे । उत्कर्षं चापकर्षं च मनुष्येष्विह जन्मतः ॥ Ms. 10. 42; मूल्योत्कर्ष˚<BR> rise and fall in price, increase and decrease.<BR>—2 Anticipated performance of a duty, as of a Śrāddha, anticipation<BR> (of some detail or details at a विकृतियाग), i. e. performing them<BR> at an earlier stage. (see उत्कर्ष).<BR>—3 Anticipation of a word occurring later on (in gram., poetry or Mīmāṃsā &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपकर्षसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षसमः|अपकर्षसम
अपकर्षः + -समः a sort of fallacy; <i>e. g.</i> sound has not the quality<BR> of shape, as a jar, so sound and a jar have no qualities in common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षक
अपकर्षक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drawing or taking off or down, removing.<BR>—2 Lessening, diminishing, detracting from; दोषास्तस्य (काव्यस्य)<BR> अपकर्षकाः S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षण
अपकर्षण <i>a.</i> Taking or drawing away, removing, diminishing (opp.<BR> वर्धक); न चास्ति सदृशं तेन किंचित्स्थौल्यापकर्षणम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षणम्
अपकर्षण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Removing, taking away; drawing away or down, depriving (one) of, drawing<BR> out, extracting.<BR>—2 Lessening, making inferior, detraction.<BR>—3 Superseding.<BR>—4 Denying; abolishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drawn or taken away, removed; अपकृष्टश्चाणक्याच्चन्द्रगुप्तः Mu. 4<BR> severed, alienated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">Page0137-2</a>]<BR> estranged, cut off; so नृपोऽपकृष्टः सचिवात् 4. 14; extracted, drawn<BR> out, dragged, lost, diminished, brought down, depressed, lowered &c.<BR>—2 Drawn or attracted by; सर्वं दैवापकृष्टं मन्यते युधिष्ठिरः Ve. 5,<BR> dependent on, or the work of, Fate.<BR>—3 Low, vile, base, inferior, mean (opp. उत्कृष्ट); न कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोऽपि<BR> भजते Ś. 5. 10; पतिं हित्वाऽपकृष्टं स्वमुत्कृष्टं या निषेवते<BR> Ms. 5. 163, 8. 281, 9. 24; सहापकृष्टैर्महतां न सङ्गतम् Ki. 14. 22.<BR>—4 Forbidden, prohibited; चारित्रेण महाबाहुरपकृष्टः स लक्ष्मणः<BR> Rām. 4. 33. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टः|अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं
अपकृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} A crow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपकृष्टचेतन, अपकृष्टजाति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टचेतन
अपकृष्ट + -चेतन <i>a.</i> mentally debased or corrupted, low-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टजाति
अपकृष्ट + -जाति <i>a.</i> of a low tribe or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकॄ
अपकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To scatter, spout out (water); अपकिरति कुसुमम्; गजोऽपकिरति Sk.<BR>—2 To scrape with the feet (for food &c.) through joy, said of quadrupeds<BR> and birds, (changed to अपस्कृ Ā. in this sense अपाच्चतुष्पाच्छकुनिष्वालेखने-सुट्<BR> P. VI. 1. 142) अपस्किरते वृषो हृष्टः कुक्कुटो भक्षार्थी, श्वा आश्रयार्थी<BR> च Sk; शृङ्गैरपस्कीर्णमहत्तटीभुवाम् Śi. 12. 74 scratched, छायापस्किरमाणविष्किर. U. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकिरणम्
अपकिरणम् Scattering about &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकोष
अपकोष <i>a.</i> Something without cover or sheath; मृदुभ्यामपकोषाभ्यां<BR> पदाभ्यामपसर्पति Śiva B. 22. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकौशली
अपकौशली News, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्तिः|अपक्ति
अपक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Unripenness, immaturity.<BR>—2 Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अपक्व <i>a.</i> Unripe, immature, undigested (as food); uncooked, raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम्
अपक्रम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go away, run away, fly, escape, flee away, leave, retreat, retire<BR> (from); नगरादपक्रान्तः Mu. 1; राक्षसोऽपक्रामन्नुपेक्षितः 3 while escaping.<BR>—2 To glide away, pass away (as time).<BR>—3 To measure off by step or by pacing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमः|अपक्रम
अपक्रमः<BR>—1 Going away, flight, escape, retreat.<BR>—2 The place or limit to which one may retreat; विक्षिपत्येष विक्षेपं<BR> चन्द्रादीनामपक्रमात् Sūrya S.<BR>—3 Gliding or passing away (of time). ━<i>a.</i> [अपगतः क्रमो यस्मात्]<BR>—1 Without order.<BR>—2 Irregular, in wrong order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमणम्
अपक्रमणम्, -क्रामः<BR> Retreat, retiring, flight, escape &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रामः|अपक्राम
अपक्रमणम्, -क्रामः<BR> Retreat, retiring, flight, escape &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमिन्
अपक्रमिन् <i>a.</i> Going forth or away; not going fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोशः|अपक्रोश
अपक्रोशः Abuse, reviling; न तु शक्यमपक्रोशं पृथिव्यां दातुमात्मनः<BR> Rām. 3. 56. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ष
अपक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without wings or the power of flight. अपक्षो हि कथं पक्षी कर्म<BR> किंचित्समाचरेत् Rām. 4. 59. 23.<BR>—2 Not belonging to the same side or party.<BR>—3 Having no adherents or friends.<BR>—4 Opposed to, adverse.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपक्षपातः, अपक्षपातिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षपातः|अपक्षपात
अपक्ष + -पातः impartiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षपातिन्
अपक्ष + -पातिन् <i>a.</i> impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षि
अपक्षि €1. €5. €9 P. To bring to an end, destroy; annihilate. ━<i>pass.</i><BR> To decline, decay, waste away; wane (as the moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0137-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षयः|अपक्षय
अपक्षयः<BR>—1 Decline, decay, wane.<BR>—2 Dark fortnight; द्रव्यसूक्ष्मविपाकश्च धूमो रात्रिरपक्षयः Bhāg. 7. 15. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षीण
अपक्षीण <i>p. p.</i> Declined, wasted, waned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षीयमाणपक्षः|अपक्षीयमाणपक्ष
अपक्षीयमाणपक्षः Dark fortnight. रात्रेरपक्षीयमाणपक्षमपक्षीयमाणपक्षाद्यान्षण्मासान्<BR> (Bṛ. Ār. Up. 6. 2. 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षिप्
अपक्षिप् €6 P. To throw away or down, take away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षेपः|अपक्षेप
अपक्षेपः, -क्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Casting away or throwing down.<BR>—2 Throwing or putting down, one of the 5 kinds of कर्मन् in the Vaiśeṣika<BR> Phil., see कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षेपणम्
अपक्षेपः, -क्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Casting away or throwing down.<BR>—2 Throwing or putting down, one of the 5 kinds of कर्मन् in the Vaiśeṣika<BR> Phil., see कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगण्डः|अपगण्ड|अपगंडः
अपगण्डः One who has attained his majority; see अपोगण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम्
अपगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go away, depart; pass away, elapse (as time); K. 73; तन्मुखाच्छायापगता<BR> H. 3; संपदो नापगच्छन्ति Pt. 3. 8.<BR>—2 To fall off or down; go away, vanish, disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपग
अपग <i>a.</i> Going, turning away. Av. 1. 34. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगा
अपग + .{@-गा@} A river (wrongly for आपगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगत|अपगतः
अपगत <i>q. v.</i><BR>—1 Gone away, departed, passed away, gone off; being remote; oft. as first<BR> member of comp. in the sense of ‘free from’, ‘devoid of’; ˚अन्यव्यापाराः<BR> K. 43 having no other duties; ˚मत्सर 45, 47, 157, 164, 207, 211;<BR> ˚निमेषेण चक्षुषा 154 devoid of twinkling or winking; ˚मले मनसि 102.<BR>—2 Dead, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगमः|अपगम
अपगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Going away or off, departure, separation; समागमाः सापगमाः H. 4. 65.<BR>—2 Falling off, going away, removal, disappearance; निमित्तमुद्दिश्य<BR> हि यः प्रकुप्यति ध्रुवं स तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति ॥ Pt. 1. 283; त्वत्संरोधापगमविशदैश्चन्द्रपादैः<BR> Me. 72; पुराणपत्रापगमादनन्तरम् R. 3. 7; lapse, passing away;<BR> कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 66, 193.<BR>—3 Death, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगमनम्
अपगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Going away or off, departure, separation; समागमाः सापगमाः H. 4. 65.<BR>—2 Falling off, going away, removal, disappearance; निमित्तमुद्दिश्य<BR> हि यः प्रकुप्यति ध्रुवं स तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति ॥ Pt. 1. 283; त्वत्संरोधापगमविशदैश्चन्द्रपादैः<BR> Me. 72; पुराणपत्रापगमादनन्तरम् R. 3. 7; lapse, passing away;<BR> कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 66, 193.<BR>—3 Death, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगतिः|अपगति
अपगतिः <i>f.</i> A bad fate (going to hell &c.); येन चापगतिर्भवेत् Pt. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगरः|अपगर
अपगरः [अप-निन्दार्थे गॄ भावे अप्]<BR>—1 Censure, reviling (निन्दा); अभिगरापगरौ Kāty.<BR>—2 One who reviles or says what is disagreeable, reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगर्जित
अपगर्जित <i>a.</i> Thunderless (as a cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोपुर
अपगोपुर <i>a.</i> Deprived of its gateways (as a town).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगल्भ
अपगल्भ <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Wanting in boldness, abortive.<BR>—2 Being on the side, lateral.<BR>—3 Separated from the oldest by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुणः|अपगुण
अपगुणः<BR>—1 A demerit, fault.<BR>—2 Devoid of all qualities (merits and demerits) निर्गुणः; सकलैर्वपुः<BR> सकलदोषसमुदितमिदं गुणैस्तव । व्यक्तमपगुण गुणत्रितयत्यजनप्रयासमुपयासि<BR> किं मुधा ॥ Śi. 15. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुर्
अपगुर् €6 Ā.<BR>—1 To disapprove, reject.<BR>—2 To threaten, menace; revile, censure, reproach, rail at; इन्द्रो अपगूर्या<BR> जघान Rv. 5. 32. 6.<BR>—3 To deprive of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगारम्
अपगारम्, -गोरम् <i>ind.</i><BR> Having raised or lifted up; अस्यपगोरम्-गारम्<BR> युध्यन्ते अपगुरो णमुलि P. VI. 1. 53. Sk. lifting their swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोरम्
अपगारम्, -गोरम् <i>ind.</i><BR> Having raised or lifted up; अस्यपगोरम्-गारम्<BR> युध्यन्ते अपगुरो णमुलि P. VI. 1. 53. Sk. lifting their swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुह्
अपगुह् €1 U. (अपगूहति-ते) To hide, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोहः|अपगोह
अपगोहः Ved. A hiding place, disappearance, concealment; स विद्वाँ<BR> अपगोहं कनीनामाविर्भवन्नुदतिष्ठत् परावृक् । Rv. 2. 15. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघनः|अपघन
अपघनः [अपहन्यते संहत्य कर्म कृत्वा वियुज्यते, हन्-अप्-घनादेशः<BR> P. III. 3. 77]. A limb or member of the body, as a hand or foot (cf. अङ्ग<BR> प्रतीकोऽवयवोऽपघनोऽथ कलेवरम् ।) (अपघनोऽङ्गम् III. 3. 81;<BR> अङ्गं शरीरावयवः स च न सर्वं किं तु पाणिः पादश्चेत्याहुः Sk.<BR> and Kāśi.); but it is also used in the sense of ‘the body’; लौहोद्घनघनस्कन्धा<BR> ललितापघनां स्त्रियम् Bk. 7. 62 (where the commentators take अपघन<BR> to mean the body itself). ━<i>a.</i> Free from the obstruction of clouds; cloudless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातः|अपघात
अपघातः<BR>—1 Striking or cutting off, warding off, preventing; वात्सल्यात्सर्वभूतेभ्यो<BR> वाच्याः श्रोत्रसुखा गिरः । परितापोऽपघातश्च पारुष्यं चात्र गर्हितम् ।<BR> Mb. 12. 191. 14.<BR>—2 Killing.<BR>—3 A violent death, any evil accident proving fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातक
अपघातक <i>a.</i> Destroying. जिज्ञासा तदपघातके हेतौ Sāṅ. K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिन्
अपघातिन् <i>a.</i> Killing, murdering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचः|अपच
अपचः [पक्तुमशक्तः Sk.]<BR>—1 Unable to cook, or one who does not cook for himself.<BR>—2 A bad cook, a term of abuse (आक्रोशे); अपचो जाल्मः P. VI. 2. 157-8. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचर्
अपचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To depart.<BR>—2 To go astray, transgress; offend, commit a fault, act wrongly; यो<BR> यस्तेषामपचरेत्तमाचक्षीत वै द्विजः Mb.; तदङ्गनास्वपाचरन्नरेन्द्रः<BR> Dk. 162 outraged; ते ह्येनमपचरन्तमपि न त्यजन्ति Kau. A. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचरित
अपचरित <i>p. p.</i> Gone away, departed; deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचरितम्
अपचरित + .{@-तम्@} A fault, wrong or wicked deed, misdeed; आहोस्वित्प्रसवो<BR> ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो वीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारः|अपचार
अपचारः<BR>—1 Departure; death; सिंहघोषश्च कान्तकापचारं निर्भिद्य Dk. 72.<BR>—2 Want, absence.<BR>—3 A fault; offence, misdeed, improper conduct, crime; शिष्यो गुराविव<BR> कृतप्रथमापचारः Mv. 4. 20; न राजापचारमन्तरेण U. 2 (v. l.<BR> for ˚अपराधम्); राजन्प्रजासु ते कश्चिदपचारः प्रवर्तते R. 15. 47.<BR>—4 Injurious or hurtful conduct, injury, Ve. 4. 10. (v. l. अपहार ?).<BR>—5 A defect, flaw, failure, deficiency; नापचारमगमन् क्वचित्क्रियाः<BR> Śi. 14. 32; mistake, omission (to do a thing) (लोप); महाध्वरे<BR> विध्यपचारदोषः Ki. 16. 48.<BR>—6 Unwholesome or improper regimen (अपथ्य); कृतापचारोऽपि परैरनाविष्कृतविक्रियः ।<BR> असाध्यः कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा ॥ Śi. 2. 84 (where अ˚<BR> also means hurt or injury).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् <i>a.</i> Offending, doing wrong; wicked, bad; भार्यापचारिणी<BR> Ms. 8. 317 a faithless wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0138-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचाय्
अपचाय् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To fear.<BR>—2 To respect, honour, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायित|अपचायितः
अपचायित <i>a.</i> Feared, honoured. P. VII. 2. 30 (Com.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायिन्
अपचायिन् <i>a.</i> Not rendering due respect. Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचि
अपचि €3 P.<BR>—1 To honour, respect.<BR>—2 To invite respectfully.<BR>—3 (€5 U.) To gather, collect. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be reduced in strength or bulk, sink, waste away; अपचितमपि<BR> गात्रं व्यायतत्वादलक्ष्यम् Ś. 2. 4 reduced in bulk, emaciated, lean;<BR> to wane, decline, diminish, grow less; राजहंस तव सैव शुभ्रता चीयते<BR> न च न चापचीयते K. P. 10.<BR>—2 To fall away from, be deprived of, lose (with abl.); प्रकृतिः सूयते<BR> तद्वदानन्त्यान्नापचीयते Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचयः|अपचय
अपचयः<BR>—1 Diminution, decrease, decay, decline, fall (fig. also.); कफापचयः<BR> Dk. 160; तेनास्यापचयं यान्ति व्याधेर्मूलान्यशेषतः Suśr. येषां<BR> राज्ञा सह स्यातामुच्चयापचयौ ध्रुवम् H. 3. 126. शिवस्योपचयं वीक्ष्य<BR> तथापचयमात्मनः Śiva B. 25. 32.<BR>—2 Loss, privation, failure, defect; H. 3. 126.<BR>—3 N. of several planetary mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित|अपचितः
अपचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Reduced in bulk, decreased, wasted, expended &c.; emaciated, thin, lean. Ś. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Honoured, respected, saluted सर्वाजमीढोऽपचितं नरेन्द्रम् Mb. 3. 139. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचितम्
अपचित + .{@-तम्@} Honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचितिः|अपचिति
अपचितिः <i>f.</i> (P. VII. 2. 30. Vārt.)<BR>—1 Loss, decay, decline, destruction; न वैनतेयो गरुडः प्रशंसति<BR> महाजनम् । दृष्ट्वासुपर्णोऽपचितिं महत्या अपि भारत ॥ Mb. 6. 3. 84.<BR>—2 Expense.<BR>—3 Atonement, amends; निहत्य पितृहन्तारं यास्याम्यपचितिं पितुः Bhāg. 10. 66. 27.<BR> Compensation, expiation of sin.<BR>—4 Exclusion.<BR>—5 Punishing.<BR>—6 N. of a daughter of Marīci^1.<BR>—7 Honouring, worshipping, showing reverence, worship; अहं त्वपचितिं<BR> भ्रातुः पितुश्च सकलामिमाम् (करिष्यामि) Rām. 2. 74. 30; विहितापचितिर्महीभृता<BR> Śi. 16. 9, 1. 17; (where it also means loss, destruction हानि), अस्य<BR> वनशुन इवापचितिः 15. 34; देवतोचितामपचितिं संपाद्य K. 324;<BR> Ki. 6. 46, 11. 9. cf. स्त्री पूजायामपचितिर्द्वयोश्च स्यात्क्षयार्चयोः Nm.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: also 5 others changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित्
अपचित् <i>f.</i> A noxious flying insect; that which causes decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपची
अपची [अपकृष्टं पच्यते असौ, पच् कर्मकर्तरि अच् गौरा˚ ङीष्]<BR> A disease in which the glands of the neck are enlarged and swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छत्र
अपच्छत्र <i>a.</i> Without a parasol or umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय <i>a.</i> [अपगता छाया यस्मात्]<BR>—1 Shadowless.<BR>—2 Having a bad or unlucky shadow.<BR>—3 Devoid of brightness, dim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छायः|अपच्छाय
अपच्छाय + .{@-यः@} One that has no shadow, i. e. a god; cf. N. 14. 21; श्रियं<BR> भजन्तां क्रियदस्य देवाश्छाया नलस्यास्ति तथापि नैषाम् । इतीरयन्तीव तया<BR> निरैक्षि सा (छाया) नैषधे न त्रिदशेषु तेषु N. 14. 23 ||<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाया
अपच्छाय + .{@-या@} An unlucky shadow, apparition, phantom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदः|अपच्छेद
अपच्छेदः, -दनम<BR>—1 Cutting off or away.<BR>—2 loss.<BR>—3 Interruption.<BR>—4 Break; संयुक्तस्य हि पृथग्भावोऽपच्छेदः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">Page0139-2</a>]<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 5. 50.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपच्छेदन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदनम
अपच्छेदः, -दनम<BR>—1 Cutting off or away.<BR>—2 loss.<BR>—3 Interruption.<BR>—4 Break; संयुक्तस्य हि पृथग्भावोऽपच्छेदः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">Page0139-2</a>]<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 5. 50.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपच्छेदन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदन्यायः
अपच्छेदः + -न्यायः the maxim concerning अपच्छेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्यु
अपच्यु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To fall off, go away or off, withdraw, desert; इहैवैधि माप<BR> च्योष्टाः Rv. 10. 173. 2.<BR>—2 To perish, die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्यवः|अपच्यव
अपच्यवः Going or coming out (निर्गम); यत्र नार्यपच्यवमुपच्यवं<BR> च शिक्षते Rv. 1. 28. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्युत
अपच्युत <i>p. p.</i> Fallen off; departed, perished; melted away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजातः|अपजात
अपजातः A bad son who has turned out ill; one inferior to his parents<BR> in qualities; मातृतुल्यगुणो जातस्त्वनुजातः पितुः समः । अतिजातोऽधिकस्तस्मादपजातोऽधमाघमः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजर्गुराण
अपजर्गुराण <i>a.</i> [अपगॄ-यङ्लुक् चानश्] Ved. Accustomed to take<BR> off or remove the covering &c. (आच्छादनादिमोचनशील) जिगर्तिमिन्द्रो<BR> अपजर्गुराणः प्रति श्वसन्तमव दानवं हन् Rv. 5. 29. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजि
अपजि €1 P. To defeat, conquer; turn off or away, avert, ward or keep<BR> off; येन मृत्युमपजयति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजयः|अपजय
अपजयः Defeat, overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपज्ञा
अपज्ञा €9 Ā. To deny, disown, repudiate, dissemble, conceal; शतमपजानीते<BR> P. I. 3. 44. Sk. (अपलपति); आत्मानमपजानानः शशमात्रोऽनयद्दिनम्<BR> Bk. 8. 26 concealing himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपज्ञानम्
अपज्ञानम् Denying, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपञ्चीकृतम्
अपञ्चीकृतम् A simple elementary substance not made of the five (पञ्च)<BR> gross elements; the five subtle elements; पञ्चप्राणमनोबुद्धिदशेन्द्रियसमन्वितम् ।<BR> अपञ्चीकृतभूतोत्थं सूक्ष्माङ्गं भोगसाधनम् ॥ Vedānta P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटान्तर|अपटांतर|अपटान्तरं
अपटान्तर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not separated (by a curtain or screen).<BR>—2 Adjoining, contiguous (= अपदान्तर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी [अल्पः पटः पटी, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 A screen or wall of cloth, particularly the screen or <i>kanāt</i> surrounding a tent.<BR>—2 A curtain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपटीक्षेपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक्षेपः|अपटीक्षेप
अपटी + -क्षेपः (अपटक्षेपः) tossing aside the curtain;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक्षेपण
अपटी + ˚क्षेपेण<BR> (= अकस्मात्) ‘with a (hurried) toss of the curtain’, frequently occurring<BR> as a stage direction and denoting precipitate entrance on the stage which<BR> arises from fear, hurry, agitation &c., as when a character tossing up<BR> the curtain suddenly enters without the usual introduction ततः प्रविशति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक
अपटीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has no knowledge of commentaries, अपटीको जडो माघे भृशं<BR> जाड्येन ताड्यते Śi.<BR>—2 one who has no covering garment (अ-पटीक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटु|अपटुः
अपटु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not clever or skilful, slow, dull, awkward, uncouth.<BR>—2 Ineloquent (as a speaker).<BR>—3 Sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपठ
अपठ <i>a.</i> Unable to read; not reading; a bad reader; cf. अपच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डित|अपंडित
अपण्डित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not learned or wise, foolish, ignorant; आत्मनः कर्मदोषाणि न विजानात्यपण्डितः<BR> Mb. 3. 209. 6. विभूषणं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">Page0140-1</a>]<BR> मौनमपण्डितानाम् Bh. 2. 7.<BR>—2 Wanting in skill, taste, appreciation &c. cf. अपण्डितास्ते पुरुषा<BR> मता मे ये स्त्रीषु च श्रीषु च विश्वसन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0139-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्य
अपण्य <i>a.</i> Not saleable (the Smṛtis name several things which<BR> ought not to be sold by particular persons and on particular occasions);<BR> जीविकार्थे चापण्ये P. V. 3. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतन्त्रकः|अपतन्त्रक|अपतंत्रकः
अपतन्त्रकः [अपगतं तन्त्रं भिषजामधीनता यत्र कप् Tv.]<BR> A kind of वातरोग, spasmodic contraction of the body or stomach; अपतन्त्रकातुरं<BR> नापतर्पयेत् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानकः|अपतानक
अपतानकः [अपकम्य अन्तरान्तरा तनुते तन् कर्तरि ण्वुल्] Spasmodic<BR> contraction with occasional convulsive fits; सोऽपतानकसंज्ञो यः पातयत्यन्तरान्तरा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानकिन्
अपतानकिन् <i>a.</i> Affected with spasmodic contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपति|अपतिः
अपति, -तिक <i>a.</i><BR> Without a master; without a husband, unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिक
अपति, -तिक <i>a.</i><BR> Without a master; without a husband, unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिः|अपति
अपति, -तिक + .{@-तिः@} Ved. Not a master or husband; अव भेषज पादय य इमां<BR> संविवृत्सत्यपतिः स्वपतिं स्त्रियम् Av. 8. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नी
अपत्नी Unmarried, without a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नीक
अपत्नीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without a wife (when she is either absent or dead).<BR>—2 To be performed without the company of a wife; अपत्नीकः पितृयज्ञः Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतीर्थ
अपतीर्थ A bad Tīrtha or place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतृप्
अपतृप् €10 P. To cause to fast or starve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पणम्
अपतर्पणम्<BR>—1 Fasting (in sickness).<BR>—2 Absence of satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यम्
अपत्यम् [न पतन्ति पितरोऽनेन, पत् बाहु˚ करणे यत्, न˚ त˚;<BR> some derive it from अप, the termination त्य being added to it,<BR> as in तत्रत्य, अत्रत्य, sprung from a stock; Yāska gives two etymologies:−<BR> अपत्यं कस्मात् अपततं भवति पितुः सकाशादेत्य पृथगिव ततं भवति,<BR> अनेन जातेन सता पिता नरके न पततीति वा]<BR>—1 Offspring, child, progeny, issue (of animals and men); offspring in<BR> general (male or female); sons or grandsons and other later generations<BR> of a Gotra; अपत्यं पौत्रप्रभृति गोत्रम् P. IV. 1. 162; अपत्यैरिव<BR> नीवारभागधेयो. चितैर्मृगैः R. 1. 50. (Bhavabhūti calls <i>apatya</i><BR> ‘a knot for tying parents together’ अन्योन्यसंश्लेषणम् पित्रोः; अन्तःकरणतत्त्वस्य<BR> दम्पत्योः स्नेहसंश्रयात् । आनन्दग्रन्थिरेकोऽयमपत्यमिति बध्यते ॥ U. 3. 17).<BR>—2 A patronymic affix; स्त्रीपुंसयोरपत्यान्ताः Ak.; ˚अधिकारप्रकरणम् Sk.;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपत्यकाम, अपत्यजीवः, अपत्यद, अपत्यता, अपत्यपथः, अपत्यप्रत्ययः, अपत्यविक्रयिन्, अपत्यशत्रुः, अपत्यसाच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यकाम
अपत्यम् + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यजीवः|अपत्यजीव
अपत्यम् + -जीवः N. of a plant (Mar. पुत्रजीवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यद
अपत्यम् + -द <i>a.</i> giving offspring (as a Mantra &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यता
अपत्यम् + -ता State of childhood; शूद्रावेदी पतति … तदपत्यतया<BR> भृगोः Ms. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यतादा
अपत्यम् + -ता + .({@-दा@}) N. of a plant (गर्भदात्रीवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यपथः|अपत्यपथ
अपत्यम् + -पथः the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यप्रत्ययः|अपत्यप्रत्यय
अपत्यम् + -प्रत्ययः a patronymic affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यविक्रयिन्
अपत्यम् + -विक्रयिन् <i>m.</i> a seller of his children, a father who sells<BR> his girl for money to a bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यशत्रुः|अपत्यशत्रु
अपत्यम् + -शत्रुः [अपत्यं शत्रुर्गर्भभेदनेन नाशकं यस्याः सा]<BR>—1 ‘having the child for its enemy’, a crab (said to die in producing young).<BR>—2 a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यसाच्
अपत्यम् + -साच् <i>a.</i> Ved. accompanied with offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्त्र
अपत्त्र <i>a.</i> Leafless, without wings &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्त्रः|अपत्र
अपत्त्र + .{@-त्त्रः@}<BR>—1 The shoot of bamboo; a sprout in general (तदवस्थायां तयोः पत्रशून्यतयोत्पत्तेस्तथात्वम्).<BR>—2 A tree the leaves of which have fallen off.<BR>—3 A bird without wings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्त्रा
अपत्त्र + .{@-त्त्रा@} N. of a plant (Mar. नेबती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप्
अपत्रप् €1 Ā. To be ashamed, be bashful, hang down the face through<BR> shame; (with instr. of person or thing); येनापत्रपते साधुरसाधुस्तेन<BR> तुष्यति Mb.; य आत्मनापत्रपते भृशं नरः स सर्वलोकस्य गुरुर्भवत्युत<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; तस्माद्बलैरपत्रेपे Bk. 14. 84 turned away from with shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप|अपत्रपः
अपत्रप <i>a.</i> Shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपा
अपत्रप + .{@-पा, -पणम्@}<BR>—1 Shame, bashfulness.<BR>—2 Embarrassment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपणम्
अपत्रप + .{@-पा, -पणम्@}<BR>—1 Shame, bashfulness.<BR>—2 Embarrassment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपिष्णु|अपत्रपिष्णुः
अपत्रपिष्णु <i>a.</i> [अपत्रप्-इष्णुच्] Bashful; लोलाक्षे सुरतगुरावपत्रपिष्णोः Śi. 8. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रस्
अपत्रस् To flee in terror from; अप स्मत् तरसन्ती न भुज्युः Rv. 10. 95. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रस्त
अपत्रस्त <i>p. p.</i> Afraid of, deterred from; तरङ्गापत्रस्तः<BR> (slightly) afraid of waves; P. II. 1. 38. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ <i>a.</i> [नास्ति पन्था यत्र] Pathless, roadless; ˚थो देशः,<BR> ˚था नगरी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथम्
अपथ + .{@-थम्, -थः@} (also अपन्थाः P. V. 4. 72, II. 4. 30)<BR>—1 Not a way, absence of a way or road, pathless state; a bad or wrong<BR> road (lit.); अपन्थानं तु गच्छन्तं सोदरोऽपि विमुञ्चति Rām. (fig.).<BR> irregularity, deviation, a moral irregularity or deviation, a wrong road,<BR> bad or evil course; अपथे पदमर्पयन्ति हि श्रुतवन्तोऽपि रजोनिमीलिताः<BR> R. 9. 74, 17. 54; न कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोऽपि भजते Ś. 5. 10<BR> follows evil ways; कारितस्त्वमपथे पदं मया Ki. 13. 45, 64.<BR>—2 Heresy, heterodoxy (in opinions).<BR>—3 The vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथः|अपथ|अपथं
अपथ + .{@-थम्, -थः@} (also अपन्थाः P. V. 4. 72, II. 4. 30)<BR>—1 Not a way, absence of a way or road, pathless state; a bad or wrong<BR> road (lit.); अपन्थानं तु गच्छन्तं सोदरोऽपि विमुञ्चति Rām. (fig.).<BR> irregularity, deviation, a moral irregularity or deviation, a wrong road,<BR> bad or evil course; अपथे पदमर्पयन्ति हि श्रुतवन्तोऽपि रजोनिमीलिताः<BR> R. 9. 74, 17. 54; न कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोऽपि भजते Ś. 5. 10<BR> follows evil ways; कारितस्त्वमपथे पदं मया Ki. 13. 45, 64.<BR>—2 Heresy, heterodoxy (in opinions).<BR>—3 The vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथा
अपथ + .{@-था@} Name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथम्
अपथ + .{@-थम्@} <i>ind.</i> By or in the wrong way, astray; अपथं वर्तते Sk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपथगामिन्, अपथप्रपन्न<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथगामिन्
अपथ + -गामिन् <i>a.</i> pursuing evil courses; heretical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथप्रपन्न
अपथ + -प्रपन्न <i>a.</i> taking to evil ways (as man); spent or used out<BR> of place, misapplied, misspent (as money &c.); यः काकिनीमप्यपथप्रपन्नां<BR> समुद्धरेन्निष्कसहस्रतुल्याम् H. 3. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अपथ्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Unfit, unsuited, improper, inconsistent, obnoxious; अकार्यं कार्यसंकाशमपथ्यं<BR> पथ्यसंमितम् Rām.<BR>—2 (In medicine) Unwholesome, unsalutary (as food, regimen &c.); सन्तापयन्ति<BR> कमपथ्यभुजं न रोगाः H. 3. 110; भवति पुरुषस्य व्याधिर्मरणं<BR> सेविते अपथ्ये, राजापथ्ये पुनः सेविते सकलकुलं नश्यति Mu. 6.<BR>—3 Bad, unlucky.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपथ्याशिन्, अपथ्यकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्याशिन्
अपथ्य + -अशिन् <i>a.</i> One taking an unwholesome food; शत्रवो नीतिहीनानां<BR> यथापथ्याशिनां गदाः Śukra. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्यकारिन्
अपथ्य + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> an offender; एवमपथ्यकारिषु तीक्ष्णदण्डो राजा;<BR> राज ˚री क्षपणकः; अनुभव राजापथ्यकारित्वस्य फलम् Mu. 1 an enemy<BR> or traitor to the king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्
अपद्, -पाद <i>a.</i> (पदी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [न पद्यते ज्ञायते पद्-क्विप्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Incomprehensible, unknowable.<BR>—2 Having no feet, footless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाद
अपद्, -पाद <i>a.</i> (पदी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [न पद्यते ज्ञायते पद्-क्विप्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Incomprehensible, unknowable.<BR>—2 Having no feet, footless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Footless. —2 Having no office or post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदः|अपद
अपद + .{@-दः@} A reptile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदम्
अपद + .{@-दम्@} No place or abode.<BR>—2 A wrong or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">Page0141-1</a>]<BR> bad place or abode; wrong timer चिरमपदे शङ्कितोऽस्मि M. 1 my doubts<BR> were out of place, ill-founded; प्रेम पश्यति भयान्यपदेऽपि Ki. 9. 70<BR> unreasonably.<BR>—3 A word which is not a <i>pada</i> or an inflected word.<BR>—4 Ether.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपदान्तर, अपदरुहा, अपदरोहिणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0140-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तर|अपदान्तरः
अपद + -अन्तर <i>a.</i> adjoining, contiguous, very near. धर्मराजमिदं<BR> वाक्यमपदान्तरमब्रवीत् Mb. 7. 17. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तरम्
अपद + -अन्तर + .({@-रम्@}) proximity, contiguity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदरुहा
अपद + -रुहा, -रोहिणी N. of a parasitical plant; (Mar. बादांगुळ, बांडगूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदरोहिणी
अपद + -रुहा, -रोहिणी N. of a parasitical plant; (Mar. बादांगुळ, बांडगूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदक्षिणम्
अपदक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> To the left side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदम
अपदम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without self-restraint.<BR>—2 Of wavering fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदव
अपदव <i>a.</i> Free from forest fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदश
अपदश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Far from ten.<BR>—2 Without a fringe (दशा) as a garment; तथानान्यधृतं धार्यं न<BR> चापदशमेव च Mb. 13. 104. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानम्
अपदानम्, -दानकम्<BR> [अपदायति परिशुध्यति येन कर्मणा, दै करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Pure conduct, approved course of life; (परिशुद्धाचरणम्).<BR>—2 A great or noble work, excellent work दृष्टापदाना विक्रान्तास्त्वया सत्कृत्य<BR> मानिताः Rām. 2. 100. 31. (perhaps for अवदानम् q. v.).<BR>—3 A work well or completely done, an accomplished work; कथितेषु जनैरमुष्य<BR> राजन् अपदानेषु विशिष्य कौतुकं नः Rām. Ch. 2. 18.<BR>—4 A legend treating of former and future births of men and exhibiting<BR> the consequences of their good and evil actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानकम्
अपदानम्, -दानकम्<BR> [अपदायति परिशुध्यति येन कर्मणा, दै करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Pure conduct, approved course of life; (परिशुद्धाचरणम्).<BR>—2 A great or noble work, excellent work दृष्टापदाना विक्रान्तास्त्वया सत्कृत्य<BR> मानिताः Rām. 2. 100. 31. (perhaps for अवदानम् q. v.).<BR>—3 A work well or completely done, an accomplished work; कथितेषु जनैरमुष्य<BR> राजन् अपदानेषु विशिष्य कौतुकं नः Rām. Ch. 2. 18.<BR>—4 A legend treating of former and future births of men and exhibiting<BR> the consequences of their good and evil actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदार्थः|अपदार्थ
अपदार्थः<BR>—1 Nothing, non-entity.<BR>—2 Not the meaning of words actually used in a sentence; अपदार्थोऽपि<BR> वाक्यार्थः समुल्लसति K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश्
अपदिश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To point out, indicate, show; तदागतित्वेनाहमपदेश्यः Dk. 60; assign, allot.<BR>—2 To declare, put forward, adduce, communicate; announce, say, tell;<BR> inform against, accuse; अपदिश्यापदेश्यं च Ms. 8. 54.<BR>—3 To feign, pretend, hold out or plead as a pretext or excuse; मित्रकृत्यमपदिश्य<BR> R. 19. 31, 32, 54; शिरःशूलस्पर्शनमपदिशन् Dk. 56 pleading head-ache as an excuse.<BR>—4 To refer to, have reference to; रहसि भर्त्रा मद्गोत्रापदिष्टा Dk. 102<BR> referred to, called by the name of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिष्ट
अपदिष्ट <i>a.</i> Assigned as a reason or pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेशः|अपदेश
अपदेशः<BR>—1 Statement, adducing (उपदेश); pointing out, mentioning the name<BR> of; अपदेशो मे जनकान्नोत्पत्तिर्वसुधातलात् Rām. 6. 116. 16. नैष<BR> न्यायो यद्दातुरपदेशः Dk. 60; हेत्वपदेशात् प्रतिज्ञायाः पुनर्वचनं<BR> निगमनम् Nyāya S.; दीक्षाया अपदेशात् Kāty.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A pretext, pretence, plea, excuse; contrivance; अवेक्ष्यमाणा<BR> शनकैर्जगाम कृत्वाग्निहोत्रस्य तदापदेशम् Mb. 3. 111. 18 केनापदेशेन<BR> पुनराश्रमं गच्छामः Ś. 2; रक्षापदेशान्मुनिहोमधेनोः R. 2. 8;<BR> व्रतापदेशोज्झितगर्ववृत्तिना V. 3. 12.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Guise, disguise, form; विकटदुष्टश्वापदापदेशकालगोचरं<BR> गता Māl. 7; मन्त्रिपदापदेशं यौवराज्यम् Dk. 101.<BR>—3 Statement of the reason, adducing a cause, the second (हेतु) of<BR> the five members of an Indian syllogism (according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">Page0141-2</a>]<BR> the Vaiśeṣikas).<BR>—4 A butt, mark (लक्ष्य).<BR>—5 A place, quarter.<BR>—6 Refusal, rejection.<BR>—7 Fame, reputation.<BR>—8 Deceit.<BR>—9 (अपकृष्टो देशः) A bad or wrong place.<BR>—10 Danger or peril. cf. अपदेशः पदे लक्ष्ये स्यात् प्रसिद्धनिमित्तयोः ।<BR> औदार्यशौर्यधैर्येषु निःसीमव्यपदेशयोः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेशिन्
अपदेशिन् <i>a.</i> Pretending to be, assuming the appearance of (in comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश्य
अपदेश्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be feigned, adduced &c.<BR>—2 Being in a wrong place.<BR>—3 To be indicated or stated; अपदिश्यापदेश्यं च Ms. 8. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिशम्
अपदिशम् <i>ind.</i> Half a point between two regions of the compass<BR> (दिशयोर्मध्ये), in an intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेवता
अपदेवता A goblin, evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्यम्
अपद्रव्यम् A bad thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रुतम्
अपद्रुतम् To run away in a bent posture; Rām. 6. 40. 25. (परस्परजान्वादिग्रहायावनतकायया<BR> धावनम् इति टीका)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्वारम्
अपद्वारम् A side door or entrance, an entrance other than the proper<BR> door; अपद्वारैर्वीक्षते निर्यियासुः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधा
अपधा Ved. Shutting up, hiding (वारणार्थं निरोधः) यो गा उदाजपधा<BR> वलस्य Rv. 2. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधाव्
अपधाव् €1 P. To prevaricate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधावनम्
अपधावनम् Prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधूम
अपधूम <i>a.</i> Free from smoke;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधूमत्व
अपधूम + ˚त्व Smokelessness; कृशानुरपधूमत्वात्प्रसन्नत्वात्प्रभाकरः<BR> (विशुद्धशुचौ) R. 10. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यै
अपध्यै €1 P. To think ill of, have evil thoughts about, curse mentally;<BR> अपध्याता च विप्रेण न्यपतद्धरणीतले Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यानम्
अपध्यानम्<BR>—1 Evil thoughts, thinking ill of, cursing mentally; तदपध्यानात् पिशाचतामुपगतम् K. 29.<BR>—2 Meditation upon things which are not to be thought of. (Jain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंस्
अपध्वंस् €1 Ā. (rarely P.)<BR>—1 To pack off, clear out; अपध्वंसेति बहुशो वदन्<BR> क्रोधसमन्वितः Hariv. आः अपध्वंस Dūtavākyam 1.<BR>—2 To abuse, revile, scold; न चाप्यन्यमपध्वंसेत्कदाचित्कोपसंयुतः<BR> Mb. ━<i>Caus.</i> To free from dust; blow away (as dust &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसः|अपध्वंस
अपध्वंसः<BR>—1 Degradation, falling off or from, disgrace.<BR>—2 Concealment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपध्वंसजः, अपध्वंसजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसजः|अपध्वंसज
अपध्वंसः + -जः, -जा a person of a mixed, degraded and impure caste (where<BR> the mother belongs to a higher caste than the fatherʼs) एको विड्वर्ण<BR> एवाथ तथाऽत्रैवोपलक्षितः । षडपध्वंसजास्ते हि … Mb. 13. 49. 8.<BR> अपध्वंसजाः स्मृताः Ms. 10. 41. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसजा
अपध्वंसः + -जः, -जा a person of a mixed, degraded and impure caste (where<BR> the mother belongs to a higher caste than the fatherʼs) एको विड्वर्ण<BR> एवाथ तथाऽत्रैवोपलक्षितः । षडपध्वंसजास्ते हि … Mb. 13. 49. 8.<BR> अपध्वंसजाः स्मृताः Ms. 10. 41. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसिन्
अपध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i> Destroying, removing; सर्वैनसामपध्वंसि जप्यं<BR> त्रिष्वघमर्षणम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Reviled, cursed, accursed, contemptible, to be disdained. अपध्वस्ता<BR> दस्युभूता भवन्ति ये ब्राह्मणान्क्षत्रियाः सन्त्यजन्ति Mb. 12. 73. 10.<BR>—2 Pounded badly or imperfectly (अवचूर्णित).<BR>—3 Abandoned. शरैरपध्वस्त-विनीतवेषम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">Page0142-1</a>]<BR> Rām. 7. 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्तः|अपध्वस्त
अपध्वस्त + .{@-स्तः@} A vile wretch, lost to all sense of right and virtue; मूर्ख<BR> अपध्वस्तोऽसि Mk. 8. cf. अपध्वस्तः परित्यक्ते निन्दितेष्वथ चूर्णिते । Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वान्त|अपध्वांत
अपध्वान्त <i>a.</i> Sounding wrongly. अपध्वान्तं वरुणस्य Ch. Up. 2. 22. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वान्तम्
अपध्वान्त + .{@-न्तम्@} A wrong or harsh sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनस
अपनस <i>a.</i> Without a nose; असिं कौक्षेयमुद्यम्य चकारापनसं मुखम् Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनामन्
अपनामन् Having a bad name.<BR>━<i>n.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनाम
अपनामन् + ({@-म@}) A bad name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनिधि
अपनिधि <i>a.</i> poor, without pelf; आचार्योऽपनिधिश्चैव भर्त्स्यते<BR> तदनन्तरम् Mb. 3. 190. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनी
अपनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To lead or carry away, carry or lead off; cause to retire; तमप्यपनयेत् Ms. 3. 242.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To remove (in all senses), destroy, take away; आर्तानां भयमपनेतुमात्तधन्वा<BR> Ś. 6. 27; शत्रूनपनेष्यामि Bk. 16. 30; so तृष्णाम्, भयम्, भ्रमम्,<BR> दोषम्, संशयम् &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To rob, steal, take away, carry away or off; त्वं रक्षसा भीरु<BR> यतोऽपनीता R. 13. 24.<BR>—3 To extract, take or draw out from (dart, oil &c.); अपनीताशेषशल्यम्<BR> Dk. 31; दिष्टया शल्यं मे हृदयादपनीतमिव V. 5.<BR>—4 To put off or away, take or pull off (dress, ornaments, fetters &c.);<BR> अपनीताशेषराजचिह्ना K. 206; एषां बन्धनान्यपनय H. 1; चरणान्निगडमपनय<BR> Mk. 6; अपनयन्तु भवत्यो मृगयावेषम् Ś. 2; R. 4. 64.<BR>—5 To deny; नैतन्मया निर्दिष्टमित्यपनयति Kull. on Ms. 8. 53.<BR>—6 To except, exclude from a rule.<BR>—7 To behave wrongly, immorally; शत्रौ हि साहसं यत्तत्किमिवात्रापनीयते<BR> Rām. 6. 64. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयः|अपनय
अपनयः<BR>—1 Taking away, removing; refuting (as an assertion); स्वमतात्प्रच्यावनमपनयो<BR> निग्रहः P. VIII. 2. 94 Com. बुभुक्षापनयं दत्त्वा चन्द्रार्कौ मम<BR> वासव Rām. 7. 35. 34.<BR>—2 A bad policy or conduct.<BR>—3 Injury, offence (अपकार); ततः सपत्नापनयस्मरणानुशयस्फुरा Śi. 2. 14.<BR>—4 Immorality (अनीति); ममापनयजं दुःखं विक्रमेण समीकुरु<BR> Rām. 6. 63. 25.<BR>—5 Injustice; स मामपनयो राजन् भ्रंशयामास वै श्रियः Mb. 3. 181. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयनम्
अपनयनम्<BR>—1 Taking away, removing, extracting &c. गण्डस्वेद˚ Me. 26; नातिश्रमापनयनाय Ś. 5. 6.<BR>—2 Healing, destroying, curing (disease &c.); रोगाच्चापनयने P. V. 4. 49.<BR>—3 Discharge or acquittance of a debt or obligation.<BR>—4 Subtraction, deduction.<BR>—5 Injustice; शृणु राजन् स्थिरो भूत्वा तवापनयनो महान् Mb. 6. 49. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीत
अपनीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Taken away; removed, pulled off, &c.<BR>—2 Removed from deviating from, opposed to, contradictory; तत्त्वधर्मापनीतस्य<BR> दृश्यते कर्मणः फलम् Rām.<BR>—3 Badly done or executed, spoiled; अपनीतं सुनीतेन योऽर्थं प्रत्यानिनीषते Mb.<BR>—4 Paid off, discharged.<BR>—5 Of bad behaviour; स बन्धुर्योऽपनीतेषु साहाय्यायोपकल्पते Rām. 6. 63. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीतम्
अपनीत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Bad conduct.<BR>—2 Cheating, fraud; अवश्यमपनीतेन जहतामेव जीवितम् Rām. 6. 8. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुद्
अपनुद् €6 P. To remove, take or drive away, destroy; नारीणामपनुनुदुर्न<BR> देहखेदान् Bk. 10. 13; न हि प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्यात् यच्छोकम् Bg. 2. 8<BR> expiate, atone for (as sin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्तिः|अपनुत्ति
अपनुत्तिः <i>f.</i>, -नोदः, -नोदनम्<BR> Removing, taking away, removal, destroying, driving<BR> away; सुखायान्यापनुत्तये Bhāg. 7. 13. 25 expiation, atonement (as<BR> of a sin); पापानामपनुत्तये Ms. 11. 209, 139, 92; Y. 3. 305; गुरुतल्प˚<BR> Ms. 11. 106; ब्रह्महत्यापनोदाय 11. 75; कृच्छ्रोऽयं सर्वपापापनोदनः 11. 215, 252, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदः|अपनोद
अपनुत्तिः <i>f.</i>, -नोदः, -नोदनम्<BR> Removing, taking away, removal, destroying, driving<BR> away; सुखायान्यापनुत्तये Bhāg. 7. 13. 25 expiation, atonement (as<BR> of a sin); पापानामपनुत्तये Ms. 11. 209, 139, 92; Y. 3. 305; गुरुतल्प˚<BR> Ms. 11. 106; ब्रह्महत्यापनोदाय 11. 75; कृच्छ्रोऽयं सर्वपापापनोदनः 11. 215, 252, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदनम्
अपनुत्तिः <i>f.</i>, -नोदः, -नोदनम्<BR> Removing, taking away, removal, destroying, driving<BR> away; सुखायान्यापनुत्तये Bhāg. 7. 13. 25 expiation, atonement (as<BR> of a sin); पापानामपनुत्तये Ms. 11. 209, 139, 92; Y. 3. 305; गुरुतल्प˚<BR> Ms. 11. 106; ब्रह्महत्यापनोदाय 11. 75; कृच्छ्रोऽयं सर्वपापापनोदनः 11. 215, 252, 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपन्न
अपन्न <i>a.</i> Ved. Not going down, not fallen or sunk, indestructible.<BR> अग्नेर्वोऽपन्नगृहस्य सदसि सादयामि Vāj. 6. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपयस्
अपपयस् <i>a.</i> Waterless, dry: (ससुरचापम्) अपपयोविशदम् Ki. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपाठः|अपपाठ
अपपाठः A wrong or bad reading (in a text); mistake in reading;<BR> द्वादशापपाठा अस्य जाताः P. IV. 4. 64. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अपपात्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deprived of the use of common vessels; using separate vessels (from<BR> which no one else will eat); अपपात्राश्च कर्तव्याः Ms. 10. 51.<BR>—2 Of low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्रितः|अपपात्रित
अपपात्रितः [पात्रभोजनात् बहिष्कृतः] One who has lost his caste<BR> through some great sin or offence, and who is, therefore, not allowed<BR> by his relatives to eat or drink from a common vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपाद
अपपाद <i>a.</i> Having bad feet; ˚त्र having no shoe, shoeless; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपानम्
अपपानम् A bad drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपित्वम्
अपपित्वम् Ved. Separation. भरतस्य पुत्राः अपपित्वं चिकितुर्न<BR> प्रपित्वम् Rv. 3. 53. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपूत
अपपूत <i>a.</i> Having badly formed hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपूतौ
अपपूत + .{@-तौ@} Badly formed hips; P. VI. 2. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रजाता
अपप्रजाता A female that has suffered a miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रदानम्
अपप्रदानम् A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रोषितम्
अपप्रोषितम् Ved. Fault or evil caused by wrong departure (प्रवासदोष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपबर्हिस्
अपबर्हिस् <i>a.</i> Not having the use of <i>Barhis</i> (बर्हिर्होमरहित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपबाहुकः|अपबाहुक
अपबाहुकः A bad arm; stiffness in the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभय
अपभय <i>a.</i> Free from fear, fearless, undaunted; ततः प्रहस्यापभयः<BR> पुरन्दरं पुनर्बभाषे तुरगस्य रक्षिता R. 3. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभरणी
अपभरणी See भरणी. So called in Yv. Ts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभर्तृ|अपभर्त्तृ
अपभर्तृ <i>a.</i> Ved. Taking away, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाष्
अपभाष् €1 Ā. To abuse, revile, defame, libel; न केवलं यो महतोऽपभाषते<BR> शृणोति तस्मादपि यः स पापभाक् Ku. 5. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाषणम्
अपभाषणम् Reviling, defamation, libel, calumny, vituperation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभू
अपभू €1 P. To be away, be absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभूतिः|अपभूति
अपभूतिः <i>f.</i> Defect, damage: Rv. 5. 8. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश्
अपभ्रंश् €1 Ā. To fall away or off.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To dismiss, discharge; अपभ्रंशितोऽधिकारात् चाणक्यहतकः Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंशः|अपभ्रंश
अपभ्रंशः<BR>—1 Falling down or away, a fall; अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा<BR> Ś. 4 v. l. ending in a (precipitate) fall.<BR>—2 A corrupted word, corruption; घर is an अपभ्रंश or corruption<BR> of गृह; (hence) an incorrect word whether formed against the rules<BR> of grammar or used in a sense not strictly Sanskrit; see अपशब्द.<BR>—3 A corrupt language, one of the lowest forms of the Prākṛta dialect<BR> used by cow-herds &c. (in kāvyas); (in Śāstras) any language other<BR> than Sanskrit; आभीरादिगिरः काव्येष्वपभ्रंश इति स्मृताः । शास्त्रेषु संस्कृतादन्यदपभ्रंशतयोदितम् ॥ Kāv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रष्ट
अपभ्रष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Fallen away, corrupted (as a dialect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपम|अपमः
अपम <i>a.</i> [अपकृष्टं मीयते, मा बाहु˚ क] Ved. The most distant<BR> or remote, the last, lowest in caste, most degraded (जात्यातिनिकृष्ट)<BR> युवं भगोऽनाशोश्चिदवितारापमस्य चित् । Rv. 10. 39. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमः|अपम
अपम + .{@-मः@} (In astr.) Declination. (कलन, क्रान्ति, गति) the ecliptic<BR> (क्रान्तिवृत्त); परिसरतां गगनसदां चलनं किंचिद् भवेदपमः Sid. Śir.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपमज्या, अपममण्डलम्, अपमवृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमज्या
अपम + -ज्या the line of the ecliptic; see क्रान्तिज्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपममण्डलम्
अपम + -मण्डलम्, -वृत्तम् the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमवृत्तम्
अपम + -मण्डलम्, -वृत्तम् the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्दः|अपमर्द|अपमर्द्द
अपमर्दः What is swept away, dust, dirt; हयहस्तिकरीषाभ्यामपमर्दः<BR> कृतो महान् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्शः|अपमर्श
अपमर्शः Touching, grazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमन्
अपमन् <i>Caus.</i> To disrespect, dishonour, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमन्यु
अपमन्यु <i>a.</i> Free from grief; लोकास्त्वासन् यथापूर्वं दृष्टास्तेनापमन्युना Mb. 7. 54. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानः|अपमान|अपमानं
अपमानः Disrespect, dishonour, disgrace; despising, slighting; contempt;<BR> लभते बुद्धयवज्ञानमपमानं च पुष्कलम् Pt. 1. 63; समुद्रेण<BR> मम भृत्यस्याण्डान्यपहृत्य मेऽपमानस्थानं कृतम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानिन्
अपमानिन् <i>a.</i> Dishonouring, disrespecting, slighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्गः|अपमार्ग
अपमार्गः<BR>—1 A by-path, side-way; a bad way.<BR>—2 Shampooing, rubbing &c. of the body (अङ्गपरिमार्जनम्) अमृतद्रवैर्विदधदब्जदृशामपमार्गमोषधिपतिः<BR> स्म करैः Śi. 9. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्य
अपमित्य Ved. To be thrown away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्यम्
अपमित्य + .{@-त्यम्, -त्यकम्@} Debt. Av. 6. 117. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्यकम्
अपमित्य + .{@-त्यम्, -त्यकम्@} Debt. Av. 6. 117. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमुख
अपमुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having the face averted.<BR>—2 Ill-favoured, ill-looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमुखम्
अपमुख + .{@-खम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमूर्धन्
अपमूर्धन् <i>a.</i> Headless; ˚कलेवरम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृज्
अपमृज् €2 P., €10 P. To wipe off, efface, blot or wipe out, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्जनम्
अपमार्जनम्<BR>—1 Wiping away, cleansing, purifying.<BR>—2 Shaving, paring.<BR>—3 Chips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्युः|अपमृत्यु
अपमृत्युः [अपकृष्टो दुष्टहेतुजन्यत्वेन मृत्युः]<BR>—1 Sudden or untimely death, accidental or unnatural death; भर्तृसक्तोऽपमृत्युस्तस्य<BR> संचरति Pt. 4.<BR>—2 Any great danger, illness &c. from which a person, hopelessly given<BR> up for lost, recovers, quite contrary to expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृषित
अपमृषित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unintelligible, obscure as a वाक्य or speech.<BR>—2 Unbearable, borne or liked (असोढ, अतितिक्षित); विहितं मयाद्य<BR> सदसीदमपमृषितमच्युतार्चनम् । यस्य &c. Śi. 15. 46. (For the formation<BR> of the word see Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अपयशस् <i>n.</i> (-शः)<BR> Infamy, disgrace, ill-repute; अपयशो यद्यस्ति किं मृत्युना Bh. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशः
अपयशस् <i>n.</i> (-शः)<BR> Infamy, disgrace, ill-repute; अपयशो यद्यस्ति किं मृत्युना Bh. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपया
अपया €2 P. To depart, go away, retire, withdraw, fall off or away,<BR> disappear; अपयातमेव हि विमानमण्डलैः U. 6. 4; शोको दिनेषु गच्छत्सु<BR> वर्धतामपयाति किम् H. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयानम्
अपयानम्<BR>—1 Going away, departure, retreat, flight, escape. भग्नापयानेष्वनभिज्ञदोषः Pañc. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Disregard (उपेक्षा); न वै शक्यं विहितस्यापयानम् Mb. 1. 198. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयानकम्
अपयानकम् A war manoeuvre of retreat; आकुञ्चनं तथा यानं प्रयाणमपयानकम्<BR> Śukra. 4. 1100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर <i>a.</i> (treated as a pronoun in some senses)<BR>—1 Having nothing higher or superior, unrivalled. matchless; without rival<BR> or second (नास्ति परो यस्मात्); स्रीरत्नसृष्टिरपरा प्रतिभाति सा<BR> मे Ś. 2. 10; cf. अनुत्तम, अनुत्तर.<BR>—2 [न पृणाति संतोषयति पॄ अच्]<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Another, other (used as adj. or subst.). वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा<BR> विहाय नवानि गृह्णीति नरोऽपराणि Bg. 2. 22.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) More, additional; कृतदारोऽपरान् दारान् Ms. 11. 5.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Second, another Pt. 4. 37; खं केशवोऽपर इवाक्रमितुं प्रवृत्तः<BR> Mk. 5. 2 like another (rival) Keśava.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Different; other; अन्ये कृतयुगे धर्मास्त्रेतायां द्वापरेऽपरे<BR> Ms. 1. 85; Ks. 26. 235; Pt. 4. 6 (with gen.).<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Ordinary, of the middle sort (मध्यम); परितप्तोऽप्यपरः<BR> सुसंवृतिः Śi. 16. 23.<BR>—3 Belonging to another, not oneʼs own (opp. स्व); यदि स्वाश्चापराश्चैव<BR> विन्देरन् योषितो द्विजाः Ms. 9. 85 of another caste.<BR>—4 Hinder, posterior, latter, later, (in time space) (opp. पूर्व);<BR> the last; पूर्वां सन्ध्यां जपंस्तिष्ठेत्स्वकाले चापरां चिरम् Ms. 4. 93;<BR> रात्रेरपरः कालः Nir.; oft. used as first member of a genitive<BR> Tatpuruṣa comp. meaning ‘the hind part’, ‘latter part or half’; ˚पक्षः<BR> the latter half of a month; ˚हेमन्तः latter half of a winter; ˚कायः<BR> hind part of the body &c.; ˚वर्षा, ˚शरद् latter part of the rains, autumn &c.<BR>—5 Following, the next.<BR>—6 Western; पयसि प्रपित्सुरपराम्बुनिधेः Śi. 9. 1. पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी<BR> वगाह्य Ku. 1. 1; Mu. 4. 21<BR>—7 Inferior, lower (निकृष्टः); अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि<BR> मे पराम् Bg. 7. 5.<BR>—8 (In Nyāya) Non-extensive, not covering too much, one of the two kinds<BR> of सामान्य, see Bhāṣā P. 8. (परं = अधिकवृत्ति higher अपरम्<BR> = न्यूनवृत्ति lower or अधिकदेशवृत्तित्वं परं, अल्पदेशवृत्तित्वम्<BR> अपरम् Muktā.)<BR>—9 Distant; opposite. When अपर is used in the singular as a correlative<BR> to एक the one, former, it means the other, the latter; एको ययौ<BR> चैत्ररथप्रदेशान् सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R. 5. 60; when used in<BR> pl. it means ‘others’, ‘and others’, and the words generally used as its<BR> correlatives are एके, केचित्-काश्चित् &c., अपरे, अन्ये; केचिद् रक्तपटीकृताश्च<BR> जटिलाः कापालिकाश्चापरे Pt. 4. 34; एके समूहुर्बलरेणुसंहतिं शिरोभिराज्ञामपरे<BR> महीभृतः Śi. 12. 45 some━others; शाखिनः केचिदध्यष्ठुर्न्यमाङ्क्षुरपरेऽम्बुधौ । अन्ये<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">Page0144-1</a>]<BR> त्वलङ्घिषुः शैलान् गुहास्त्वन्ये न्यलेषत ॥ केचिदासिषत स्तब्धा भयात्केचिदघूर्णिषुः ।<BR> उदतारिषुरम्भोधिं वानराः सेतुनापरे Bk. 15. 31. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरः|अपर|अपरं
अपर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 the hind foot of an elephant; बद्धापराणि परितो निगडान्यलावीत्<BR> Śi. 5. 48 (Malli. चरमपादाग्राणि).<BR>—2 An enemy (न पृणाति सन्तोषयति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरा
अपर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Western direction, the west अपरां च दिशं प्राप्तो वालिना समभिद्रुतः<BR> Rām. 4. 46. 18.<BR>—2 The hind part of an elephant.<BR>—3 Sacred learning, learning the four Vedas with the 6 Aṅgas.<BR>—4 The womb; the outer skin of the embryo.<BR>—5 Suppressed menstruation in pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरी
अपर + .{@-री@} Ved. The future, future times; उतापरीभ्यो मघवा विजिग्ये Rv. 1. 32. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरम्
अपर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The future, any thing to be done in future (कार्य); तदेतद्ब्रह्मापूर्वमपरमनन्तम्<BR> Bṛ. Ār. Up. (नास्ति अपरं कार्यं यस्य).<BR>—2 The hind quarter of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरम्
अपर + .{@-रम्@} <i>adv.</i> Again, moreover, in future, for the future; अपरं<BR> च moreover; अपरेण behind, west of, to the west of (with gen.<BR> or acc.). [cf. Goth. <i>afar</i>; Germ. <i>aber</i>, as in aberglauben].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपराग्नि, अपराङ्गम्, अपरान्त, अपरान्तकः, अपरापराः, अपरापरे, अपरापराणि, अपरापरम्, अपरार्धम्, अपराह्ण, अपरेतरा, अपरकान्यकुब्ज, अपरकालः, अपरगात्रम्, अपरगोदानम्, अपरज, अपरजनः, अपरदक्षिणम्, अपरपक्षः, अपरपञ्चालाः, अपरपर, अपरपाणिनीयाः, अपरप्रणेय, अपरभावः, अपररात्रः, अपरलोकः, अपरवक्त्रा, अपरवक्त्रम्, अपरवैराग्यम्, अपरसक्थम्, अपरस्वस्तिकम्, अपरहैमन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0143-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग्नि
अपर + -अग्नि (अग्नी dual)<BR>—1 the southern and western fires (दक्षिण and गार्हपत्य).<BR>—2 the last fire i. e. used at the funeral ceremony (˚ग्निः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराङ्गम्
अपर + -अङ्गम् one of the 8 divisions of गुणीभूतव्यङ्ग्य (the second<BR> kind of काव्य) mentioned in K. P. 5. In this the व्यङ्ग्य or suggested<BR> sense is subordinate to something else; अगूढमपरस्याङ्गम्; अपरस्य<BR> रसादेर्वाच्यस्य वा (वाक्यार्थीभूतस्य) अङ्गं रसादि अनुरणनरूपं<BR> वा; e. g. अयं स रसनोत्कर्षी पीनस्तनविमर्दनः । नाभ्यूरुजघनस्पर्शी<BR> नीविविस्रंसनः करः ॥ where शृङ्गार is subordinate to करुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्त|अपरान्तः
अपर + -अन्त <i>a.</i> living at the western borders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्तः|अपरान्त
अपर + -अन्त + .({@-न्तः@})<BR>—1 the western border or extremity, the extreme end or term; the western shore.<BR>—2 (pl.) the country or inhabitants of the western borders near the Sahya<BR> mountain; अपरान्तजयोद्यतैः (अनीकैः) R. 4. 53 Western people.<BR> दशार्णाश्चापरान्ताश्च द्विपानां मध्यमा मताः Kau. A. 1. 2.<BR>—3 the kings of this country.<BR>—4 death, Pātañjala Yogadarśana 3. 22. ˚ज्ञानम् anticipation of oneʼs end.<BR>—5 the hind foot of an elephant; मृदुचलदपरान्तोदीरितान्दूनिनादम्<BR> Śi. 11. 7, 18. 32.<BR>—6 Islander, inhabitant of an island (द्वीपवासिन्) कोट्यापरान्ताः<BR> सामुद्रा रत्नान्युपहरन्तु ते Rām. 2. 82. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्तकः|अपरान्तक
अपर + -अन्तकः<BR>—1 = ˚अन्तः pl.<BR>—2 N. of a song; अपरान्तकमुल्लोप्यं मद्रकं प्रकरीं तथा । औवेणकं<BR> सरोबिन्दुमुत्तरं गीतकानि च ॥ Y. 3. 113; ˚अन्तिका N. of a metre<BR> consisting of 64 mātrās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापराः
अपर + -अपराः, -अपरे, -अपराणि another and another, several, various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापरे
अपर + -अपराः, -अपरे, -अपराणि another and another, several, various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापराणि
अपर + -अपराः, -अपरे, -अपराणि another and another, several, various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापरम्
अपर + -अपरम् <i>ind.</i> Further and further (उत्तरोत्तरम्); अहं<BR> हि वचनं त्वत्तः शुश्रूषुरपरापरम् Mb. 5. 136. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरार्धम्
अपर + -अर्धम् the latter or second half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपर + -अह्ण [fr. अहन् changed to अह्न P. II. 4. 29, V. 4. 88.]<BR> the latter part of the day, the afternoon, closing or last watch of the<BR> day; Ms. 3. 278; अपराह्णशीतलतरेण शनैरनिलेन Śi. 9. 4; ˚तन,<BR> ˚ह्णेतन belonging to this time; ˚कृतं P. II. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेतरा
अपर + -इतरा the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरकान्यकुब्ज
अपर + -कान्यकुब्ज <i>a.</i> situated in or belonging to the western part<BR> of Kānyakubja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरकालः|अपरकाल
अपर + -कालः later period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरगात्रम्
अपर + -गात्रम् a minor limb (hand, foot etc.); कोपप्रसादापरगात्रहस्तः<BR> (सुप्तः क्षितौ) रावणगन्धहस्ती Rām. 6. 109. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरगोदानम्
अपर + -गोदानम् (also गोडनि or गोडानि) N. of a country to the<BR> west of Mahāmeru (according to Buddhistic ideas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरज|अपरजः
अपर + -ज <i>a.</i> born later or at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">Page0144-2</a>]<BR> the end of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरजः|अपरज
अपर + -ज + .({@-जः@}) the destroying fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरजनः|अपरजन
अपर + -जनः an inhabitant of the west, the western people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरदक्षिणम्
अपर + -दक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> in the south-west (belonging to the तिष्ठद्गु class).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपक्षः|अपरपक्ष
अपर + -पक्षः<BR>—1 the second or dark half of the month.<BR>—2 the other or opposite side; a defendant (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपञ्चालाः
अपर + -पञ्चालाः the western Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपर
अपर + -पर <i>a.</i> one and the other, several, various; अपरपराः<BR> सार्थाः गच्छन्ति P. VI. 1. 144. Sk. several caravans go; (अपरे च<BR> परे च सकृदेव गच्छन्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपाणिनीयाः
अपर + -पाणिनीयाः the pupils of Pāṇini living in the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरप्रणेय
अपर + -प्रणेय <i>a.</i> easily led or influenced by others, docile, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरभावः|अपरभाव
अपर + -भावः<BR>—1 being another or different, difference.<BR>—2 succession, continuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपररात्रः|अपररात्र
अपर + -रात्रः [अपरं रात्रेः] the latter or closing part of night,<BR> the last watch of night (P. V. 4. 87); उत्थायापररात्रान्ते प्रयताः सुसमाहिताः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 4. 24. ˚कृतम् P. II. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरलोकः|अपरलोक
अपर + -लोकः the other world, the next world. Paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवक्त्रा
अपर + -वक्त्रा, -वक्त्रम् N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवक्त्रम्
अपर + -वक्त्रा, -वक्त्रम् N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवैराग्यम्
अपर + -वैराग्यम् a kind of Vairāgya mentioned by Patañjali (दुष्टानुश्राविकविषयवितृष्णस्य<BR> वशीकारसंज्ञं वैराग्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरसक्थम्
अपर + -सक्थम् the hind thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्वस्तिकम्
अपर + -स्वस्तिकम् the western point in the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरहैमन
अपर + -हैमन <i>a.</i> belonging to the latter half of winter (P. VII. 3. 11).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरता
अपरता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Being another or different (one of the 24 Guṇas); difference, opposition,<BR> contrariety, relativeness.<BR>—2 Nearness.<BR>—3 Distance, posteriority (in time or space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्वम्
अपरता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Being another or different (one of the 24 Guṇas); difference, opposition,<BR> contrariety, relativeness.<BR>—2 Nearness.<BR>—3 Distance, posteriority (in time or space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्र
अपरत्र <i>adv.</i> In another place, elsewhere; एकत्र or क्वचित्-अपरत्र<BR> in one place-in another place; in the first case-in the second case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरथा
अपरथा <i>ind.</i> In another manner; जलदकालमबोधकृतं दिशामपरथाप<BR> रथावयवायुधः Śi. 6. 41 ध्रुवं ज्ञाने दोषः कथमपरथा दुर्व्यवहृतिः Mv. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवत्|अपरवन्त्
अपरवत् <i>ind.^1</i> Like what follows.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर <i>a.</i> [अपर-पर]<BR>—1 One after another, uninterrupted, continued (as applied to an action);<BR> अपरस्पराः क्रियासातत्ये P. VI. 1. 144; सुट् निपात्यते; ˚राः सार्था<BR> गच्छन्ति, सततमविच्छेदेन गच्छन्तीत्यर्थः Sk.<BR>—2 One another (अन्योन्य); अपरस्परसंभूतं किमन्यत्कामहैतुकम् Bg. 16. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेद्युः
अपरेद्युः <i>adv.</i> On the following day अथापरेद्युः संप्राप्ते हताशिष्टाः<BR> जनास्तदा Mb. 3. 65. 35; Ms. 3. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरञ्ज्|अपरंज्
अपरञ्ज् (Used in pass. only) To be disaffected or discontented (with<BR> abl.); नयहीनादपरज्यते जनः Ki. 2. 49; K. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरक्त
अपरक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Colourless, bloodless, pale; श्वासापरक्ताधरः Ś. 6. 6.<BR>—2 Discontented, dissatisfied, disaffected; चन्द्रगुप्तादपरक्ताः Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरागः|अपराग
अपरागः<BR>—1 Discontent, dissatisfaction, disaffection; ˚हेतून् ज्ञातुमिच्छामि<BR> Mu. 3; अपरागसमीरणेरितः Ki. 2. 50; K. 329.<BR>—2 Apathy, enmity. यथा त्वं गुणविद्वेषादपरागं चिकीर्षसि Mb. 5. 168. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0144-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरतिः|अपरति
अपरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cessation (= उपरति^1 q. v.);<BR>—2 Dissatisfaction.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवः|अपरव
अपरवः<BR>—1 Contest, dispute (about the enjoyment of property); ˚उज्झित uncontested,<BR> undisputed (as possession of any thing).<BR>—2 Ill-repute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर <i>a.</i> [अ-परस्पर] Not reciprocal, not mutual; असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं<BR> ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम् । अपरस्परसंभूतं किमन्यत्कामहैतुकम् ॥ Bg. 16. 8<BR> (Mr. Telang renders ˚र by ‘produced by union of male and female’,<BR> caused by lust, where अपरस्पर must be supposed to be connected<BR> with उपरस्पर under अपर q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराक्
अपराक् <i>ind.</i> In (or to) the western direction. शयीत नापराक्<BR> नान्यैर्न नग्ना न च सन्ध्ययोः Bhāg. 6. 18. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराञ्च्
अपराञ्च् <i>a.</i> [˚राङ्, ˚राची, ˚राक्] Not averted, fronting, facing,<BR> in front. ━<i>ind.</i> In front of.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपराञ्ङ्मुख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराञ्ङ्मुख
अपराञ्च् + -मुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 not turning away the face; with unaverted face.<BR>—2 presenting a bold front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित <i>a.</i> Unconquered, invincible, unsurpassed; ˚ता दिक्<BR> the north-east direction, (ऐशानी) so called because the Gods were<BR> not defeated there; ते (देवासुराः) उदीच्यां प्राच्यां दिश्ययतन्त<BR> ते ततो न पराजयन्त सैषा दिगपराजिता Ait. Br., अपराजितां वास्थाय<BR> व्रजेद्दिशमजिह्मगः Ms. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजितः|अपराजित
अपराजित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A sort of poisonous insect.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu; N. of Śiva. अपराजित-अप्रतिहत-जयन्त-वैजयन्त-कोष्ठकान् …<BR> पुरमध्ये कारयेत् Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR>—3 One of the 11 Rudras.<BR>—4 A class of divinities forming a portion of the अनुत्तर divinities<BR> of the Jainas. —5 N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजिता
अपराजित + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 N. of Durgā, to be worshipped on the Vijayādaśamī or <i>Dasarā</i><BR> day; तिष्ठ देवि शिखाबन्धे चामुण्डे ह्यपराजिते Sandhyā.; दशम्यां<BR> च नरैः सम्यक् पूजनीयाऽपराजिता । … ददाति विजयं देवी पूजिता<BR> जयवर्धिनी Skanda P.<BR>—2 N. of several plants; दूर्वा, शेफालिका, जयन्ती, असन, शङ्खिनी, हपुषा, असनपर्णी.<BR>—3 A kind of plant (or ओषधि) fastened round the wrist and serving<BR> as a charm or amulet; see Ś. 7. (In Vikramorvaśīyam Act 2, Kālidāsa<BR> uses अपराजिता in the sense of a spell or विद्या; ननु भगवता देवगुरुणा<BR> अपराजितां नाम शिखाबन्धनविद्यामुपदिशता त्रिदशपरिपक्षस्यालङ्घनीये कृते स्वः).<BR>—4 The north-east quarter; see under ˚त above.<BR>—5 A kind of metre, 4 lines with 14 syllables in each<BR>—6 A sort of Yoginī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजिष्णु
अपराजिष्णु, -पराजेय <i>a.</i><BR> Invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजेय
अपराजिष्णु, -पराजेय <i>a.</i><BR> Invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध्
अपराध् €4. €5 P.<BR>—1 To offend, wrong, sin against, commit an offence against; (with gen.<BR> or loc. of person or thing); यौवनमत्रापराध्यति Mk. 9 is to blame;<BR> यस्मिन्कस्मिन्नपि पूजार्हेऽपराद्धा शकुन्तला Ś. 4; अपराद्धोऽस्मि<BR> तत्रभवतः कण्वस्य Ś. 7; महतां योऽपराध्येत दूरस्थोऽस्मीति नाश्वसेत्<BR> Pt. 1. 307; V. 2; किं पुनरसुरावलेपेन भवतीनामपराद्धम् V. 1;<BR> sometimes with dat. also; न दूये सात्वतीसूनुर्यन्मह्यमपराध्यति Śi. 2. 11.<BR> सति च कुलविरोधे नापराध्यन्ति बालाः Pañc. 3. 4.<BR>—2 To annoy, disturb.<BR>—3 To prohibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अपराद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sinned, offended, having committed an offence, guilty, an offender,<BR> criminal (used in an active sense); कृतवत्यसि नावधीरणामपरद्धेऽपि<BR> यदा चिरं मयि R. 8. 48; प्रोवाच कोशलपतिः प्रथमापराद्धः 9. 79<BR> the first to offend.<BR>—2 Missed, not hitting the mark (as an arrow) मृगदेहापराद्धैर्नामेषुमोक्षणैः<BR> Dk. 163; ˚इषुः or ˚पृषत्कः an archer whose arrows always miss<BR> the mark, an unskilful archer; निमित्तादपराद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येव वल्गितम् Śi. 2. 27.<BR>—3 Violated, transgressed; अपराद्धा अभिषेकवेलोपाध्यायस्य V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धम्
अपराद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} [भावे क्तः] An offence, crime, injury; न तु ग्रीष्मस्यैवं<BR> सुभगमपराद्धं युवतिषु Ś. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धिः|अपराद्धि
अपराद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Fault, mistake, offence.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधः|अपराध
अपराधः An offence, a fault, guilt, crime, sin, mistake, error;<BR> (32 kinds are usually stated in Śāstras); कमपराधलवं मयि पश्यसि<BR> V. 4. 29; यथापराधदण्डानाम् R. 1. 6; सर्वापराधेषु अवध्याः खलु<BR> दूताः Abhiṣeka. 1. यथेन्द्रशत्रुः स्वरतोऽपराधात् Śik. 52 mistake<BR> or error in accent; sometimes with gen. or loc. of person; अदः सुरेन्द्रस्य<BR> कृतापराधान् दैत्यान् V. 1. 20; कृतापराधमिव त्वय्यात्मानमवगच्छति K. 203.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपराधक्षमापनस्तोत्रम्, अपराधभञ्जनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधक्षमापनस्तोत्रम्
अपराधः + -क्षमापनस्तोत्रम् A panegyric to Devī (देवीस्तोत्र) by a later<BR> Śaṅkarācārya^1 in which there is a striking and melodious ending at<BR> the end of each verse as कुपुत्रो जायेत क्वचिदपि कुमाता न भवति ।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: 12 others also changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधभञ्जनः|अपराधभञ्जन
अपराधः + -भञ्जनः the destroyer of sins, epithet of Śiva; ˚स्तोत्रम्<BR> a short poem by Śaṅkarācārya in praise of Śiva, the fourth line<BR> of the verses being usually क्षन्तव्यो मेऽपराधः शिव शिव शिव भोः श्रीमहादेव शम्भो ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अपराधिन् <i>a.</i> Offending, guilty, offender, criminal; अपराधी<BR> नामाहं प्रसीद रम्भोरु V. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापरण
अपरापरण <i>a.</i> Destitute of descendants or offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरामृष्ट
अपरामृष्ट <i>a.</i> In no way connected; Pātañjala Yogadarśana 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरार्कः|अपरार्क
अपरार्कः The oldest known commentator of याज्ञवल्क्यस्मृति^1. The<BR> name of his com. is अपरार्कचन्द्रिका.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्रम
अपरिक्रम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unable to walk round. जानन्नपि च किं कुर्यादशक्तश्चापरिक्रमः<BR> Rām. 2. 63. 42.<BR>—2 Not diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्लेशः|अपरिक्लेश
अपरिक्लेशः Welfare; Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह <i>a.</i> Without possessions or belongings, attendants &c.;<BR> Without a wife; तदाप्रभृत्येव विमुक्तसङ्गः पतिः पशूनामपरिग्रहोऽभूत<BR> Ku. 1. 53 quite destitute, as in निराशीरपरिग्रहः Bg. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रहः|अपरिग्रह
अपरिग्रह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 Non-acceptance, rejection, renunciation, one of the several kinds of<BR> <i>yamas</i> (mental restraints) stated in Yogaśāstra by Patañjali.<BR>—2 Destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचयिन्
अपरिचयिन्, -परिचेय <i>a.</i><BR> Having no acquaintance; unsocial, misanthropic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचेय
अपरिचयिन्, -परिचेय <i>a.</i><BR> Having no acquaintance; unsocial, misanthropic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छद
अपरिच्छद <i>a.</i> Poor, destitute. पुमांसश्चापरिच्छदाः Ms. 8. 405.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छिन्न|अपरिच्छिन्नं
अपरिच्छिन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undiscerned, undistinguished.<BR>—2 Continuous, connected, without interval or separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0145-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेदः|अपरिच्छेद
अपरिच्छेदः<BR>—1 Want of distinction or division.<BR>—2 Want of order or arrangement.<BR>—3 Want of judgment.<BR>—4 Continuance, connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिज्यानिः|अपरिज्यानि
अपरिज्यानिः <i>f.</i> Not losing; not growing old or decaying; इष्टापूर्तस्य˚<BR> N. of a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणयः|अपरिणय
अपरिणयः Celibacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणीता
अपरिणीता An unmarried girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणामः|अपरिणाम
अपरिणामः Unchangeableness; ˚दर्शिन् not prudent, improvident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपर
अपरिपर <i>a.</i> Ved. Not going by a tortuous course. Av. 18. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिनिष्ठित
अपरिनिष्ठित <i>a.</i> Not properly placed or established; ˚तस्योपदेशस्यान्याय्यं<BR> प्रकाशनम् M. 1 not properly grounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमाण
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय <i>a.</i> Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमित|अपरिमितं
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय <i>a.</i> Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमेय
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय <i>a.</i> Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिम्लान|अपरिम्लानः
अपरिम्लान <i>a.</i> Not fading, withering, or decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिम्लानः|अपरिम्लान
अपरिम्लान + .{@-नः@} N. of a plant (महासहावृक्ष). Gomphrena Globosa. (Mar.<BR> आंबोली, रानौडीद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरियाणि
अपरियाणि [अ-परि˚] Not walking about (used in curses only);<BR> see अप्रयाणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिविष्ट
अपरिविष्ट <i>a.</i> Ved. Not covered or enclosed (अव्याप्त, वेष्टनशून्य).<BR> ऊर्जयन्त्या अपरिविष्टमास्यम् Rv. 2. 13. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवृत
अपरिवृत <i>a.</i> Not enclosed or fenced on all sides (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिशेष|अपरिशेषः
अपरिशेष <i>a.</i> Not leaving a remainder; all-surrounding, all-pervading;<BR> ˚षं ज्ञानम् Sāṅ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिशेषः|अपरिशेष
अपरिशेष + .{@-षः@} Absence of remainder or limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कारः|अपरिष्कार
अपरिष्कारः^1 Want of polish or refinement (moral or physical); coarseness,<BR> rudeness, unrefined state.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कृत|अपरिष्कृतं
अपरिष्कृत <i>a.</i> Unpolished, unrefined, rude, coarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्टिः|अपरिष्टि
अपरिष्टिः <i>f.</i> [रिष्टेहिंसाया अभावः] Worship (पूजाया हिंसाहेतुकद्वेषशून्यत्वात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसर|अपरिसरः
अपरिसर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not near, distant.<BR>—2 Not extensive, not current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसरः|अपरिसर
अपरिसर + .{@-रः@} Absence of extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसंख्यानम्
अपरिसंख्यानम् Infinity, innumerableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसंस्थित
अपरिसंस्थित <i>a.</i> One who is not steady anywhere; काननानि च<BR> वेगेन भ्रमत्यपरिसंस्थितः Rām. 3. 60. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिस्कन्द|अपरिस्कंद
अपरिस्कन्द <i>a.</i> Motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहरणीय
अपरिहरणीय, अपरिहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inevitable.<BR>—2 Not to be abandoned.<BR>—3 Not to be degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहार्य|अपरिहार्य्य|अपरिहार्य्यं
अपरिहरणीय, अपरिहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inevitable.<BR>—2 Not to be abandoned.<BR>—3 Not to be degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिह्वृत
अपरिह्वृत <i>a.</i> Ved. Not endangered or afflicted; straightforward.<BR> cf. अपरिह्वृताश्च P. VII. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षित
अपरीक्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unexamined एतच्चापरीक्षितक्रयविषयम् Mit.; untried, untested, unproved.<BR>—2 Ill-considered,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">Page0146-2</a>]<BR> foolish, thoughtless (of person or thing); ˚कारकं नाम पञ्चमं तन्त्रम्<BR> Pt. 5 ‘the inconsiderate doer’.<BR>—3 Not clearly proved or established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीत|अपरीतः
अपरीत <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not surrounded or encircled, not approached (अनभिगत).<BR>—2 Unobstructed, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीतः|अपरीत
अपरीत + .{@-तः@} N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरुष्
अपरुष् <i>a.</i> Free from anger; अपरुषा परुषाक्षरमीरिता R. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अपरूप <i>a.</i> (-पा, -पी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Ugly, deformed, odd-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूपम्
अपरूप + .{@-पम्@}<BR>—1 Deformity, monstrosity.<BR>—2 Delight, wonder (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्ष
अपरोक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not invisible, perceptible to the senses, visible.<BR>—2 Not distant or remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षम्
अपरोक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} <i>adv.</i> In the presence of (with gen.) अपरोक्षात् perceptibly,<BR> visibly, manifestly, openly,<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपरोक्षानुभूतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षानुभूतिः|अपरोक्षानुभूति
अपरोक्ष + -अनुभूतिः <i>f.</i> direct cognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षयति
अपरोक्षयति Den. P. To make perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोधः|अपरोध
अपरोधः Exclusion, prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोपः|अपरोप
अपरोपः Extermination, dethronement; श्रुत्वा स्वाम्यपरोपरौद्रविषमानाघाततूर्यस्वनान् Mu. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्ण
अपर्ण <i>a.</i> Leafless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्णा|अपर्ण्णा
अपर्ण + .{@-र्णा@} N. of Durgā or Pārvatī; Kālidāsa thus accounts for the<BR> name:− स्वयंविशीर्णद्रुमपर्णवृत्तिता परा हि काष्ठा तपसस्तया पुनः ।<BR> तदप्यपाकीर्णमिति प्रियंवदां वदन्त्यपर्णेति च तां पुराविदः ॥<BR> Ku. 5. 28; cf. Śiva P. चतुर्थे त्यक्तपर्णा च अपर्णाख्यामवाप सा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्तु|अपर्तुः|अपर्त्तु
अपर्तु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untimely. Av. 3. 28. 1; अपर्तावपि भद्रं ते उपावर्तेत मे विभो<BR> Bhāg. 4. 18. 11.<BR>—2 Past menstruation time (निवृत्तरजस्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्तुः|अपर्तु|अपर्त्तु
अपर्तु + .{@-र्तुः@} Improper time, not the right time or season; प्रविष्टानां<BR> महारण्यमपर्तौ सुमहद् द्विज Bhāg. 10. 80. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्यन्त|अपर्यंत|अपर्य्यन्त
अपर्यन्त <i>a.</i> Unlimited, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्तं
अपर्याप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not sufficient or enough, incomplete, insufficient.<BR>—2 Unlimited.<BR>—3 Unable (to do its work), incompetent; अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं<BR> भीष्माभिरक्षितम् Bg. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्तवत्|अपर्याप्तवन्त्
अपर्याप्तवत् <i>a.</i> Not competent to; तस्य प्रयातस्य वरूथिनीनां<BR> पीडामपर्याप्तवतीव सोढुम् (वसुन्धरा) R. 16. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्तिः|अपर्याप्ति|अपर्य्याप्ति
अपर्याप्तिः <i>f.</i> Insufficiency; अमात्यभूरिवसोरात्मजेत्यपर्याप्तिर्बहुमानस्य Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याय|अपर्यायः|अपर्य्याय
अपर्याय <i>a.</i> Without order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्यायः|अपर्याय|अपर्य्याय
अपर्याय + .{@-यः@} Want of order or method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्युषित|अपर्य्युषित|अपर्य्युषितं
अपर्युषित <i>a.</i> Not standing over-night, fresh, new (as a flower);<BR> not standing over till the next day; ˚प्रतिज्ञे मारुतौ Ve. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्वन्
अपर्वन् <i>a.</i> Without a joint. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 No joint or point of conjunction.<BR>—2 A day which is not a पर्वन् i. e. not the proper time or season<BR> (the Parva days being अमावास्या, पौर्णिमा, अष्टमी, चतुर्दशी &c.);<BR> अपर्वणि ग्रहकलुषेन्दुमण्डला विभावरी कथय कथं भविष्यति M. 4. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपर्वदण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्वदण्डः|अपर्वदण्ड|अपर्व्वदण्डः
अपर्वन् + -दण्डः a sort of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0146-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल|अपलं
अपल <i>a.</i> Without flesh (पलशून्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलम्
अपल + .{@-लम्@} A pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलप्
अपलप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To deny, disown; राजदेयमपलपितम् Kull. on Ms. 8. 400; refuse;<BR> शतमपलपति P. I. 3. 44. Sk.<BR>—2 To conceal, hide.<BR>—3 To detract from, slander.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To outwit, overreach, deceive; अपलापयमानस्य शत्रूंस्तस्याभवन्मतिः Bk. 8. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलपनम्
अपलपनम्, अपलापः<BR>—1 Concealing, hiding; कृततिग्मद्युतिमण्डलापलापैः Śi. 20. 28.<BR>—2 Concealment or denial of knowledge, evasion; न हि प्रत्यक्षसिद्धस्यापलापः<BR> कर्तुं शक्यते Ś. B.<BR>—3 Detraction, concealment of truth, thoughts, feelings &c.; उन्मुखदर्शनापलपनैः<BR> पिण्डार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>—4 Affection, regard.<BR>—5 (In medicine) The part between the shoulder and the ribs.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपलपनदण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापः|अपलाप
अपलपनम्, अपलापः<BR>—1 Concealing, hiding; कृततिग्मद्युतिमण्डलापलापैः Śi. 20. 28.<BR>—2 Concealment or denial of knowledge, evasion; न हि प्रत्यक्षसिद्धस्यापलापः<BR> कर्तुं शक्यते Ś. B.<BR>—3 Detraction, concealment of truth, thoughts, feelings &c.; उन्मुखदर्शनापलपनैः<BR> पिण्डार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>—4 Affection, regard.<BR>—5 (In medicine) The part between the shoulder and the ribs.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपलपनदण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलपनदण्डः
अपलपनम् + -दण्डः (in law) a fine laid on one who denies the charge on which<BR> he is convicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापिन्
अपलापिन् <i>a.</i> One who denies, disowns, hides, conceals &c.; concealing;<BR> जयन्ति महतां संस्तुतापलापिन्यः कल्याणिन्यो नीतयः Māl. 10; साधारणस्यापलापिन् Y. 2. 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिका
अपलाषिका [लाषिका पर्यायेण इच्छा, तद्विपरीता इच्छा] Excessive<BR> thirst or desire (अतिशयलालसा); (अपलासिका is sometimes used<BR> in the same sense, but regarded as an incorrect word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिन्
अपलाषिन्, -लाषुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thirsty (P. III. 2. 144.).<BR>—2 Free from thirst or desire; प्रलापिनो भविष्यन्ति कदा न्वेतेऽपलाषुकाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषुक
अपलाषिन्, -लाषुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thirsty (P. III. 2. 144.).<BR>—2 Free from thirst or desire; प्रलापिनो भविष्यन्ति कदा न्वेतेऽपलाषुकाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलीन
अपलीन <i>a.</i> Concealed; औषसातपभयादपलीनम् Ki. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल्यूलनम्
अपल्यूलनम् Not cleansing or washing; यदिदं स्नानवस्त्रं विहितमपल्यूलनं<BR> कृतं भवति Śat. Br. (क्षारद्रव्यसंयोगादिनाऽधौतम्); not cleansed<BR> or washed by cleaning substances (as by a washerman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवक्तृ
अपवक्तृ <i>m.</i> Ved. Speaking away, warning off, averting, preventing.<BR> अपदे पादा प्रतिधातवेऽकरुतापवक्ता हृदयाविधाश्चित् Rv. 1. 24. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवचनम्
अपवचनम् Speaking ill; Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाचनम्
अपवाचनम् Act of speaking away or warning off, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवत्स
अपवत्स <i>a.</i> Without a calf; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवत्सय्
अपवत्सय् (Denominative from अपवत्स) “To behave as towards<BR> a weaned calf” with cautious watchfulness; neither too much love, nor too<BR> much apathy. ये सपत्नाः सपत्नानां सर्वांस्तानपवत्सयेत् v. l. सर्वांस्तानुपसेवयेत्<BR> Mb. 12. 139. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवद्
अपवद् €1 U.<BR>—1 To revile, abuse, censure, reproach; परानमी यदपवदन्त आत्मनः<BR> Śi. 17. 19; नार्तोऽप्यपवदेद्विप्रान् Ms. 4. 236; स्वं पुत्रम् अपवदति-ते<BR> वा P. I. 3. 77. Sk. (क्रियाफलस्य कर्तृगामित्वे द्योतिते वा स्यात्);<BR> नृभ्योऽपवदमानस्य Bk. 8. 45 reviling or abusing men.<BR>—2 To disown, deny (Ā.); न्यायमपवदते P. I. 3. 73. Sk.<BR>—3 To argue out, refute, contradict; अपवदेयुस्तानितिहासैः पुरातनैः Y. 3. 7.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To blame, censure.<BR>—2 To oppose or contradict as unadvisable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादः|अपवाद
अपवादः<BR>—1 Censuring, reviling; censure, reproach, blame, abuse; आः तातापवावभिन्नमर्याद<BR> U. 5; लोकापवादो बलवान्मतो मे R. 14. 40; लोकापवादाद्भयम् Bh. 2. 62;<BR> scandal, evil report; चिरकालान्मया श्रुतस्तवापवादः Pt. 1;<BR> Ki. 11. 25, 14. 12; Mk. 9. 3; U. 1; Pt. 4; Y. 2. 207; देव्यामपि हि वैदेह्यां<BR> सापवादो यतो जनः U. 1. 6 spreading or indulging in scandals about;<BR> न केवलमत्याहितं सापवादमपि U. 2; सापवादम् censuringly Māl. 9.<BR>—2 An exception, a special rule that restricts or sets aside a general<BR> rule (opp. उत्सर्ग); मा हिंस्यात्सर्वभूतानि इति उत्सर्गः; वायव्यं<BR> श्वेतमालभेत इत्यपवादः; अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः कृतव्यावृत्तयः परैः<BR> Ku. 2. 27; R. 15. 7; ˚प्रत्ययः exceptional suffix; ˚स्थलम् a case<BR> for a special rule.<BR>—3 An order, command; ततोऽपवादेन पताकिनीपतेश्चचाल निर्ह्रादवती<BR> महाचमूः Ki. 14. 27. cf.<BR> … अपवादस्तु निन्दने । आज्ञायां स्यात् … । Nm.<BR>—4 Refutation; (in Vedānta Phil.) refutation as of a wrong imputation<BR> or belief; रज्जुविवर्तस्य सर्पस्य रज्जुमात्रत्ववत्, वस्तुभूतब्रह्मणो<BR> विवर्तस्य प्रपञ्चादेः वस्तुभूतरूपतोऽपदेशः अपवादः Tv.; अध्यारोपापवादाभ्यां<BR> वस्तुतत्त्वविनिश्चयः Vedānta; hence also, a means of refutation.<BR>—5 Confidence, trust.<BR>—6 Love; familiarity.<BR>—7 A small bell or other instrument sounded to decoy deer; मधुकरैरपवादकरैरिव<BR> Śi. 6. 9; (˚करैः = व्याधैः; अपवादं मृगवञ्चनाय घण्टादिकुत्सितवाद्यं<BR> कुर्वन्ति तैः Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादक
अपवादक, अपवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blaming, censuring, reviling, traducing, defaming; मृगयापवादिना<BR> माढव्येन Ś. 2.<BR>—2 Opposing; contradicting, excepting, setting aside, excluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादिन्
अपवादक, अपवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blaming, censuring, reviling, traducing, defaming; मृगयापवादिना<BR> माढव्येन Ś. 2.<BR>—2 Opposing; contradicting, excepting, setting aside, excluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवन|अपवनं
अपवन <i>a.</i> Without wind or air, sheltered from wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवनम्
अपवन + .{@-नम्@} [अपकृष्टं कृत्रिमत्वात्स्वल्पत्वाच्च वनम्] A grove, a<BR> garden or park planted near a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरक|अपवरकः
अपवरक, -वारक See under अपवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारक|अपवारकः
अपवरक, -वारक See under अपवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग &c. See under अपवृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त|अपवर्तः|अपवर्त्त
अपवर्त &c. See under अपवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवल्गित
अपवल्गित <i>a.</i> Suspended or hung; अपवल्गिता गवाक्षेषु वातं<BR> गृह्णन्ति सलिलगर्गर्यः Mk. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवह्
अपवह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To carry off or away, bear off or away; अपोवाह च वासोऽस्या मारुतः<BR> Mb. (प्रद्युम्नं) अपोवाह रणात्सूतः Bhāg. 10. 76. 27.<BR>—2 To drive away, disperse, dispel, remove, take away; अमी जनस्थानमपोढविघ्नं<BR> मत्वा R. 13. 22 freed from obstacles; अथानपोढार्गलमप्यगारम् (प्रविष्टाम्) 16. 6<BR> the bolts of which were not removed or unchained; तदुच्छिष्टमपोह्य Dk. 133.<BR>—3 To give up, relinquish, leave, abandon, cast off; शमिततापमपोढमहीरजः<BR> Śi. 6. 33; संभ्रमोऽभवदपोढकर्मणाम् (ऋत्विजाम्) R. 11. 25; तद्भक्त्यपोढपितृराज्यमहाभिषेके<BR> (मूर्धनि) 13. 70, thrown away; Dk. 67; दिव्येन शून्यं वलयेन बाहुमपोढनेपथ्यविधिर्ददर्श<BR> R. 16. 73 before he had commenced his toilet.<BR>—4 To deduct, subtract.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To carry off, remove, carry or draw to a distance, take away; मलयकेतुरपवाहितः<BR> Mu. 1, 3; कलत्रम् 2; इमां मया सार्धमपवाह्य M. 5; अपवाह्य<BR> च्छलाद् वीरौ किमर्थं मामिहाऽहरः Bk. 8. 86.<BR>—2 To chase or drive away, expel; हृतसर्वस्वतया<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">Page0148-1</a>]<BR> अपवाहितः Dk. 47, 59.<BR>—3 To reduce to powder, pulverize.<BR>—4 To cause to carry the yoke; गामिव नासिकां विद्ध्वापवाहयति Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0147-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहः|अपवाह
अपवाहः, -हनम्<BR>—1 Taking or carrying away, removal; Dk. 41; स्वराष्ट्रं वासयेद्राजा<BR> परदेशापवाहनात् H. 3, v. l. bearing away men from other countries;<BR> See अभिष्यन्द.<BR>—2 Deduction, subtraction (as of fractions).<BR>—3 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहनम्
अपवाहः, -हनम्<BR>—1 Taking or carrying away, removal; Dk. 41; स्वराष्ट्रं वासयेद्राजा<BR> परदेशापवाहनात् H. 3, v. l. bearing away men from other countries;<BR> See अभिष्यन्द.<BR>—2 Deduction, subtraction (as of fractions).<BR>—3 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवोढृ
अपवोढृ <i>a.</i> One who carries away or removes; कश्चिच्छस्त्रापातमूढोऽपवोढुर्लब्धा<BR> भूयश्चेतनामाहवाय Śi. 18. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ <i>p. p.</i> Carried away, removed &c. See अपवह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवासः|अपवास
अपवासः [अपसृत्य वासः] Ved.<BR>—1 Disappearance, vanishing, retreat; Av. 3. 7. 7.<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविक्षत
अपविक्षत <i>a.</i> Uninjured, unhurt, unviolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविघ्न
अपविघ्न <i>a.</i> Unobstructed, uninterrupted; शतं कतूनामपविघ्नमाप<BR> सः R. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध &c. See under अपव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्या
अपविद्या Ignorance, spiritual ignorance, Māyā or illusion (अविद्या);<BR> तत्त्वस्य संवित्तिरिवापविद्याम् Ki. 16. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविष
अपविष <i>a.</i> Free from poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविषा
अपविष + .{@-षा@} A sort of grass with aromatic roots; Kyllingia Monocephala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवीण
अपवीण <i>a.</i> Having no lute, or having a bad lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवीणा
अपवीण + .{@-णा@} A bad lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृ
अपवृ €5 U. To open, uncover, disclose, exhibit.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> or €10 P. To cover, wrap, envelop, screen, conceal; बाहुबन्धनापवारितपयोधरोद्गमाम्<BR> Māl. 7 covered, or concealed; विटपेनापवारितशरीरा भूत्वा Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरकः|अपवरक
अपवरकः, -का<BR> [वृ-संज्ञायां वुन्]<BR>—1 An inner apartment; the lying-in chamber.<BR>—2 An air-hole, aperture; ततश्चैकस्मादपवरकात् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरका
अपवरकः, -का<BR> [वृ-संज्ञायां वुन्]<BR>—1 An inner apartment; the lying-in chamber.<BR>—2 An air-hole, aperture; ततश्चैकस्मादपवरकात् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरणम्
अपवरणम्<BR>—1 Covering, screening.<BR>—2 A garment, cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारकः|अपवारक
अपवारकः<BR>—1 Covering &c.<BR>—2 An enclosed or screened place (जवनिका); ˚के प्रविश्य एकान्ते तिष्ठ Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारणम्
अपवारणम् Covering, concealment, disappearance.<BR> … छादने त्वपवारणम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारित|अपवारितं
अपवारित <i>p. p.</i> Covered, concealed; ˚तं प्रवहणं तिष्ठति<BR> Mk. 6 covered; vanished, disappeared;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितम्
अपवारित + .{@-तम्, अपवारितकम्@} Concealed or secret manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितकम्
अपवारित + .{@-तम्, अपवारितकम्@} Concealed or secret manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितम्
अपवारित + .{@-तम्, अपवारितकेन, अपवार्य@} <i>ind.</i> Frequently occurring in<BR> dramas in the sense of ‘apart’, ‘aside to another’ (opp. प्रकाशम्);<BR> it is speaking in such a way that only the person addressed may hear it;<BR> तद्भवेदपवारितम् । रहस्यं तु यदन्यस्य परावृत्त्य प्रकाश्यते ।<BR> त्रिपताककरेणान्यमपवार्यान्तरा कथाम् S. D. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितकेन
अपवारित + .{@-तम्, अपवारितकेन, अपवार्य@} <i>ind.</i> Frequently occurring in<BR> dramas in the sense of ‘apart’, ‘aside to another’ (opp. प्रकाशम्);<BR> it is speaking in such a way that only the person addressed may hear it;<BR> तद्भवेदपवारितम् । रहस्यं तु यदन्यस्य परावृत्त्य प्रकाश्यते ।<BR> त्रिपताककरेणान्यमपवार्यान्तरा कथाम् S. D. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवार्य|अपवार्य्य
अपवारित + .{@-तम्, अपवारितकेन, अपवार्य@} <i>ind.</i> Frequently occurring in<BR> dramas in the sense of ‘apart’, ‘aside to another’ (opp. प्रकाशम्);<BR> it is speaking in such a way that only the person addressed may hear it;<BR> तद्भवेदपवारितम् । रहस्यं तु यदन्यस्य परावृत्त्य प्रकाश्यते ।<BR> त्रिपताककरेणान्यमपवार्यान्तरा कथाम् S. D. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृतिः|अपवृति
अपवृतिः <i>f.</i> Opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृज्
अपवृज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To avert, destroy, dissipate; तमः, शत्रुम् &c.<BR>—2 To tear off, pull out, take out. —3 To conclude, finish, absolve.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To leave, quit, abandon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">Page0148-2</a>]<BR> avoid; दूरापवर्जितच्छत्रैः शिरोभिः R. 17. 79 keeping the umbrellas<BR> at a (great) distance; त्वयात्महस्तेन मही मदच्युता मतङ्गजेन स्रगिवापवर्जिता<BR> Ki. 1. 29 abandoned, left, lost.<BR>—2 To let go, drop down, throw, pour; सुमनसो दिव्याः खेचरैरपवर्जिता<BR> Bhāg.; करयुग्मपद्ममुकुलापवर्जितैः Śi. 13. 37.<BR>—3 To abandon, release, discharge, pay off (as debt &c.); absolve oneself<BR> from, fulfil, make good (as a promise).<BR>—4 To sever, separate, cut off; भल्लापवर्जितैस्तेषां शिरोभिः (महीं<BR> तस्तार) R. 4. 63; Ki. 17. 58 severed or cut off by arrows; इमान्यमूनीत्यपवर्जिते<BR> शनैः Ki. 8. 20 plucked.<BR>—5 To overturn; empty; घटेऽपवर्जिते Y. 3. 300.<BR>—6 To honour, respect, esteem.<BR>—7 To give, bestow, grant, present; अपवर्जितं कोशजातम् Dk. 36;<BR> दक्षिणामपवर्ज्य Mb.; अपवर्जितौ वरौ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्गः|अपवर्ग
अपवर्गः<BR>—1 Completion, end, fufilment or accomplishment of an action; अपवर्गे<BR> तृतीया P. II. 3. 6, III. 4. 60; (अपवर्गः = क्रियाप्राप्तिः or समाप्तिः<BR> Sk.) तेषां चैवापवर्गाय मार्गं पश्यामि नाण्डज Mb. 5. 113. 17. क्रियापवर्गेष्वनुजीविसात्कृताः<BR> Ki. 1. 14; अपवर्गे तृतीयेति भणतः पाणिनेरपि N. 17. 68; Ki. 16. 49;<BR> पञ्च˚ coming to an end in 5 days.<BR>—2 An exception, special rule; अभिव्याप्यापकर्षणमपवर्गः Suśr.<BR>—3 Absolution, final beatitude; अपवर्गमहोदयार्थयोर्भुवमंशाविव<BR> धर्मयोर्गतौ R. 8. 16; ज्ञानेन चापवर्गः Sāṅkhya K. 44.<BR>—4 A gift, donation.<BR>—5 Abandonment. आत्मदोषापवर्गेण तद्याच्ञा जनमोहिनी Bhāg. 10. 23. 46;<BR>—6 Throwing, discharge (as of arrows); मुष्टेरसंभेद इवापवर्गे Ki. 16. 20.<BR>—7 Cessation, end; क्रियाणामर्थशेषत्वात् प्रत्यक्षतस्तन्निवृत्त्या अपवर्गः<BR> स्यात् । Ms. 11. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जनम्
अपवर्जनम्<BR>—1 Leaving, abandonment; making good, fulfilling (as promise); discharging (debt &c.).<BR>—2 A gift or donation; spending.<BR>—3 Final beatitude, salvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जित|अपवर्ज्जित
अपवर्जित <i>p. p.</i> Left, abandoned; fulfilled; see above; oft.<BR> in comp. in the sense of ‘free from’, ‘being without’, ‘destitute of’,<BR> or with instr.; षड्भिरपवर्जिताशीतिः Bṛ. S. 53. 7; 80 minus 6,<BR> अपवर्जितविप्लवे शुचौ Ki. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृक्त
अपवृक्त <i>p. p.</i> Finished, ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृक्तिः|अपवृक्ति
अपवृक्तिः <i>f.</i> Fulfilment, accomplishment, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्
अपवृत् €1 Ā.<BR> To turn back, turn away, depart; तस्मादपावर्तत दूरकृष्टा<BR> R. 6. 58; तस्मादपावर्तत कुण्डिनेशः 7. 33.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> —1 To turn back or away, turn aside, bend; व्यपोढपार्श्वैरपवर्तितत्रिकाः<BR> Ki. 4. 15; आसक्ततिर्यगपवर्तितदृष्टि वक्त्रम् (वहन्ती) Māl. 1. 40.<BR>—2 (Math.) To divide (as by a common measure) without remainder; समेन<BR> केनाप्यपवर्त्यहारभाज्यौ भजेद्वा सति संभवे तु Līlā.<BR>—3 To reduce to a common measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तः|अपवर्त|अपवर्त्त
अपवर्तः<BR>—1 Taking away, removing.<BR>—2 (Math.) The (common) divisor which is applied to both or either of<BR> the quantities of an equation.<BR>—3 Reduction to a common measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तकः|अपवर्तक
अपवर्तकः<BR>—1 A common measure.<BR>—2 A necklace of pearls and gold-globules alternately put; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तनम्
अपवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Removal, transferring from one place to another; स्थान˚.<BR>—2 Taking away, depriving one of; न त्यागोऽस्ति द्विषन्त्याश्च न च दायापवर्तनम् Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—3 Abridging, abbreviation.<BR>—4 Reducing a fraction to its lowest terms; division without remainder,<BR> or the divisor itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्त
अपवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Turned away, reversed, inverted, overturned; agitated, disturbed; मुकुटेनापवृत्तेन<BR> कुण्डलोज्ज्वलिताननम् Rām. 5. 10. 25; ˚जठरशफरी Ki. 12. 49.<BR>—2 With downward face; व्याकीर्णस्फुरदपवृत्तरुण्डखण्डः Māl. 3. 17.<BR>—3 Ended, finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्तम्
अपवृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} The ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्तिः|अपवृत्ति
अपवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> End.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्यध्
अपव्यध् €4 P.<BR>—1 To pierce (badly); अपविद्धः शरैर्भृशम् Mb.<BR>—2 To throw or cast in general, throw or cast off, toss away; प्रेङ्खयन्<BR> परिजनापविद्धया (दोलया) R. 19. 44 left, let go; भुजस्तम्भापविद्ध<BR> Mv. 2. 33 thrown, or wielded; अपविद्धसर्वस्वा Dk. 61 given or spent<BR> away; Ki. 5. 30; Śi. 8. 37; हृदयमशरणं मे पक्ष्मलाक्ष्याः कटाक्षैरपहृतमपविद्धं<BR> पीतमुन्मूलितं च Māl. 1. 28 pierced through, distracted, overcome.<BR>—3 To abandon, leave, desert, cast off (as a child, ornaments &c.); पुरा<BR> श्मशाने स्रगिवापविध्यते Mb.; Ms. 11. 41; Dk. 98. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cast or thrown off, thrown or cast away, abandoned, forsaken; तेनाहमपविद्धश्च<BR> हृतदारश्च राघव Rām. 4. 10. 27 dismissed, rejected, neglected,<BR> removed; oft. used in the sense of ‘freed from’, ‘devoid of’; रक्षोविप्रकृतावास्तामपविद्धशुचाविव R. 10. 74.<BR>—2 Abject, mean. शव इवापविद्धः Bhāg. 5. 14. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्धः|अपविद्ध
अपविद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}, ˚पुत्रः A son that is abandoned by the father or mother<BR> or by both, and adopted by a stranger; one of the 12 kinds of sons among<BR> Hindus; मातापितृभ्यामुत्सृष्टं तयोरन्यतरेण वा । यं पुत्रं परिगृह्णीयादपविद्धः<BR> स उच्यते ॥ Ms. 9. 171; उत्सृष्टो गृह्यते यस्तु सोऽपविद्धो भवेत्सुतः Y. 2. 132.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपविद्धलोक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्धलोक
अपविद्ध + -लोक <i>a.</i> dead, departed from this world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेधः|अपवेध
अपवेधः Piercing through (a pearl, ruby &c.) wrongly, or in the<BR> wrong direction (and thus spoiling it). मणीनामपवेधे च दण्डः प्रथमसाहसः Ms. 9. 286.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययः|अपव्यय
अपव्ययः [अपकृष्टः मर्यादामुल्लङ्घ्य कृतः व्ययः] Extravagant<BR> expenditure, prodigality, lavishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययिन्
अपव्ययिन्, -व्ययमान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Squandering, spending lavishly; prodigal.<BR>—2 Denying a debt; अर्थेऽपव्ययमानं तु करणेन विभावितम् Ms. 8. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययमान
अपव्ययिन्, -व्ययमान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Squandering, spending lavishly; prodigal.<BR>—2 Denying a debt; अर्थेऽपव्ययमानं तु करणेन विभावितम् Ms. 8. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्रत
अपव्रत <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Swerving from religious observances, irreligious, impious; अनुव्रताय<BR> रन्धयन्नपव्रतानाभूभिरिन्द्रः Rv. 1. 51. 9; देवहेलनान्यपव्रतानि<BR> Bhāg. 5. 6. 10.<BR>—2 Disobedient, unfaithful.<BR>—3 Perverse. गूळ्हं सूर्यं तमसापव्रतेन तुरीयेण ब्रह्मणाविन्ददत्रिः Rv. 5. 40. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशकुनम्
अपशकुनम् A bad omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशङ्क|अपशंक
अपशङ्क <i>a.</i> Free from fear or hesitation, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशङ्कम्|अपशंकम्
अपशङ्क + .{@-ङ्कम्@} <i>adv.</i> Fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशदः|अपशद
अपशदः = अपसद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशब्दः|अपशब्द
अपशब्दः<BR>—1 A bad or ungrammatical word, a corrupted word (in form or meaning);<BR> त एव शक्तिवैकल्यप्रमादालसतादिभिः । अन्यथोच्चारिताः शब्दा अपशब्दा<BR> इतीरिताः ॥; दूरतश्चापशब्दं त्यक्त्वा Bh. 3. 134 (where ˚ब्दम् has<BR> also sense 4); अपशब्दशतं माघे Subhāṣ. cf. also वैयाकरणकिरातादपशब्दमृगाः<BR> क्व यान्ति संत्रस्ताः । Udb. and Kau. A. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Vulgar speech.<BR>—3 A form of language not Sanskrit; ungrammatical language.<BR>—4 A reproachful word, offensive expression, censure; प्रापाक्ष्णोर्गलदपशब्दमञ्जनाम्भः Śi. 8. 43.<BR>—5 Words not in standard use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशमः|अपशम
अपशमः Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशव्य
अपशव्य <i>a.</i> Not tending to the growth of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशिरस्
अपशिरस्, -शीर्ष, -र्षन् <i>a.</i><BR> Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशीर्ष
अपशिरस्, -शीर्ष, -र्षन् <i>a.</i><BR> Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशीर्षन्
अपशिरस्, -शीर्ष, -र्षन् <i>a.</i><BR> Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशु|अपशुः
अपशु <i>a.</i> Without cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुः|अपशु
अपशु + .{@-शुः@} Not cattle; a bad animal; any animal other than a cow and<BR> horse; अपशवो वा अन्ये गोऽश्वेभ्यः Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुच्
अपशुच् <i>a.</i> Without sorrow. ━<i>m.</i> (Without sorrow) The soul;<BR> क उत्तमः श्लोकगुणानुवादात् पुमान् विरज्येत विनापशुग्घ्नात् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशूद्रः|अपशूद्र
अपशूद्रः A man of any of the first three वर्णs; one who is<BR> not a शूद्र; अपि वा वेदनिर्देशादपशूद्राणां प्रतीयेत । MS. 6. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक <i>a.</i> Without sorrow or grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोकः|अपशोक
अपशोक + .{@-कः@} The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्चिम
अपश्चिम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 What is not followed by any other, having not other in the rear, last<BR> (used much in the same sense as पश्चिम; cf. उत्तम and अनुत्तम,<BR> उत्तर and अनुत्तर); अयमत्र ते जन्मन्यपश्चिमः पश्चिमावस्थाप्रार्थितो<BR> मकरन्दबाहुपरिष्वङ्गः Māl. 9; अयमपश्चिमस्ते रामस्य शिरसि<BR> पादपङ्कजस्पर्शः U. 1. (v. l. for पश्चिम); प्रसीदतु महाराजो<BR> ममानेनापश्चिमेन प्रणयेन Ve. 6; प्रणमापश्चिमस्य पितुः पादयोः<BR> Mu. 7; तात अम्ब मेऽपश्चिमः प्रणामः Nāg. 5; हा कथमपश्चिममस्य<BR> वचनम् । Nāg. 4; अपश्चिमं कुरु वचनम् Ve. 141.<BR>—2 Not last, first, foremost; श्रुतवतामपश्चिमः R. 19. 1. cf. also<BR> विपश्चितामपश्चिमः ।<BR>—3 Extreme; अपश्चिमामिमां कष्टामापदं प्राप्तवत्यहम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्य
अपश्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्रयः|अपश्रय
अपश्रयः A bolster, pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्री
अपश्री <i>a.</i> Deprived of beauty; कुमुदवनमपश्रि श्रीमदम्भोजषण्डम् Śi. 11. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्वासः|अपश्वास
अपश्वासः = अपान q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठम्
अपष्ठम् [अप-स्था, -क सस्य षत्वम् P. VIII. 3. 97] The point<BR> of the goad of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु <i>a.</i> [अप-स्था कु Uṇ. 1. 25; P. VIII. 3. 98]<BR>—1 Contrary, opposite.<BR>—2 Unfavourable, adverse, perverse.<BR>—3 Left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु + .{@-ष्ठु@} <i>adv.</i><BR>—1 Contrary, on the contrary<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">Page0150-1</a>]<BR> or opposite way or direction.<BR>—2 Falsely, untruly, wrongly; तव धर्मराज इति नाम कथमिदमपष्ठु<BR> पठ्यते Śi. 15. 17; अपष्ठु पठतः पाठ्यमधिगोष्ठि शठस्य ते N.<BR>—3 Faultlessly. —4 Well, properly, handsomely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुः|अपष्ठु
अपष्ठु + .{@-ष्ठुः@} Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुर|अपष्ठुरं
अपष्ठुर, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Contrary, opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुल|अपष्ठुलं
अपष्ठुर, -ल <i>a.</i><BR> Contrary, opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्
अपस् <i>n.</i> [आप् असुन् ह्रस्वश्च; आपः कर्माख्यायां ह्रस्वो नुट् च<BR> वा स्यात् Uṇ. 4. 207. अप्नः, अपः]<BR>—1 Work, action; अपसा सन्तु नेमे Rv. 1. 54. 8.<BR>—2 Sacred act or rite, sacrificial work.<BR>—3 Water. ━<i>a.</i> (अपाः)<BR>—1 Active, engaged in any act (कर्मयुक्त).<BR>—2 Got or obtained. According to B. and R. अपसः <i>f.</i> pl. stands<BR> in the Veda for (1) the hands and fingers busy in kindling the sacred<BR> fire and performing the sacrificial rites; (2) the three goddesses of sacred<BR> speech or the three divinties, fire, wind and sun; and (3) the active<BR> or running waters. [cf. L. <i>opus</i>.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्तम
अपस्तम <i>a.</i> Most active or rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्य
अपस्य <i>a.</i> [अपसि कर्मणि साधुः यत्] Ved. Active, fit for<BR> an act, skilful in doing any thing (साधुकर्मकारिन्); सिध्मा यद् वनधितिरपस्यात्<BR> Rv. 1. 121. 7; Yv. 10. 7; flowing, watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्या
अपस्य + .{@-स्या@}<BR>—1 Activity यादृश्मिन् धायि तमपस्यया विदद् Rv. 5. 44. 8.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 A sort of brick used in preparing the sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यति
अपस्यति Den. P. To be active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यु
अपस्यु <i>a.</i> [अपस्-क्यच्-उ] Active, busily engaged, desirous of working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसदः|अपसद
अपसदः [अपकृष्टो नीच इव सीदति, सद-अच्]<BR>—1 An outcast, a low man; usually at the end of comp. in the sense of<BR> ‘vile’, ‘wretched’, ‘accursed’; कापालिक˚ Māl. 5; रे रे क्षत्रियापसदाः<BR> Ve. 3; नर˚, ब्राह्मण˚ &c.<BR>—2 N. for the children of six degrading connections, i. e. of men of the<BR> first three castes with women of the castes inferior to their own; विप्रस्य<BR> त्रिषु वर्णेषु नृपतेर्वर्णयोर्द्वयोः । वैश्यस्य वर्णे चैकस्मिन् षडेतेऽपसदाः<BR> स्मृताः ॥ Ms. 10. 10. See अपध्वंसः.<BR>—3 प्रतिलोमजः contrary to अनुलोमजः (परवर्णासु अनुलोमजाः<BR> षडपध्वंसजाः विलोमजा अपसदाः षडिति ज्ञेयम्) cf. Mb. 13. 49. 6-8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसमम्
अपसमम् <i>ind.</i> Last year; at the end of the year (वर्षात्यये).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर|अपसरः
अपसर, -सर्प &c.<BR> See under अपसृ, अपसृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर, -सर्प &c.<BR> See under अपसृ, अपसृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्जनम्
अपसर्जनम् [सृज्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A gift or donation,<BR>—2 Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसल
अपसल = अपसव्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसलवि
अपसलवि <i>ind.</i> [अप-सल् बा˚ अविं]<BR>—1 To the left (opp. प्रसलवि); ˚वि सृष्टया रज्ज्वा Kāty. (अप्रादक्षिण्येन).<BR>—2 (The space) Between the thumb and the forefinger, supposed to be sacred<BR> to the Manes, as water &c. in ceremonies like तर्पण is offered to<BR> them being poured down through that space; प्रदेशिन्यङ्गुष्ठयोरन्तरा<BR> अपसलवि अपसव्यं वा तेन पितृभ्यो निदधाति Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अपसव्य, -सव्यक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not on the left, right; मण्डलान्यपसव्यानि खगाश्चकू रथं प्रति<BR> Rām. 6. 57. 34 अपसव्येन हस्तेन Ms. 3. 214.<BR>—2 Contrary, opposite यद्येतदपसव्यं ते वचो मम भविष्यति Mb. 5. 138. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यक
अपसव्य, -सव्यक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not on the left, right; मण्डलान्यपसव्यानि खगाश्चकू रथं प्रति<BR> Rām. 6. 57. 34 अपसव्येन हस्तेन Ms. 3. 214.<BR>—2 Contrary, opposite यद्येतदपसव्यं ते वचो मम भविष्यति Mb. 5. 138. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यम्
अपसव्य, -सव्यक + .{@-व्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> To the right, making the sacred thread hang down<BR> towards the left part of the body over the right shoulder (opp. सव्यम्<BR> when it hangs over the left); a position of the thread in Śrāddha or<BR> other religious ceremonies at particular times of those ceremonies (the<BR> three positions being सव्य, निवीत & अपसव्य); प्राचीनावीतिना<BR> सम्यगपसव्यमतन्द्रिणा । पित्र्यमानिधनात्कार्यं विधिवद्दर्भपाणिना ॥<BR> Ms. 3. 279; ˚व्यं कृ to go round one so as to keep the right side<BR> towards him; to make the sacred thread hang over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यवत्|अपसव्यवन्त्
अपसव्यवत् <i>a.</i> Wearing the sacred thread over the right sholder;<BR> आवाहनाग्नौकरणरहितं ह्यपसव्यवत् Y. 1. 251.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसिद्धान्तः|अपसिद्धान्त|अपसिद्धांतः
अपसिद्धान्तः A wrong or erroneous conclusion; सिद्धान्तमभ्युपेत्यानियमात्<BR> कथाप्रसङ्गोऽपसिद्धान्तः Gaut. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृ
अपसृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To walk off, go or get away, depart; अपसर इतः begone,<BR> avaunt hence, get you gone; अपसराग्रतः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To withdraw, retire, retreat, turn back; यदपसरति मेषः कारणं<BR> तत्प्रहर्तुम् Pt. 3. 43.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear; यस्यानुष्ठानेन मे सन्ततिविनाशदुःखमपसरति Pt. 1.<BR>—4 To escape, elude the sight.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To make (a thing or person) go away or retire, take or put<BR> away, remove, drive away or off, throw aside; अपसारय घनसारम् K. P. 9;<BR> अपसार्यतां वेत्रलता Pt. 1 put aside, take away; Ms. 7. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरः|अपसर
अपसरः<BR>—1 Departure, retreat.<BR>—2 A proper excuse or apology, valid reason (for possession of a thing,<BR> such as buying &c.) Ms. 8. 198.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरणम्
अपसरणम्<BR>—1 Going away, retreating, escape; तत्ते युक्तं कर्तुमपसरणम् Pt. 3.<BR>—2 Egress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारः|अपसार
अपसारः<BR>—1 Going out, retreating.<BR>—2 An outlet, egress (opp. प्रवेश); Pt. 3. 120; अनपसारमार्गाः<BR> Dk. 163; H. 3. 53; Śi. 18. 40.<BR>—3 Escaping, fleeing; सनिगडचरणत्वात्सावशेषापसारः Mk. 7. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपसारभूमिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारभूमिः
अपसारः + -भूमिः A strong-hold; Kau. A. 1. 16 (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारणम्
अपसारणम्, -णा<BR> Removing to a distance, driving, expelling; किमर्थमपसारणा<BR> क्रियते Mu. 4, making room (cf. Mar. बाजू, बाजू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारणा
अपसारणम्, -णा<BR> Removing to a distance, driving, expelling; किमर्थमपसारणा<BR> क्रियते Mu. 4, making room (cf. Mar. बाजू, बाजू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृत
अपसृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone away, retreated &c.; dropped or fallen down; अपसृतपाण्डुपत्रा<BR> मुञ्चन्त्यश्रूणीव लताः Ś. 4. 15.<BR>—2 Extended, held out, stretched; Ś. 6.<BR>—3 Discharged; अपसृतमिव शस्त्रम् Mv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृज्
अपसृज् €6 P. To leave, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृष्ट
अपसृष्ट <i>a.</i> One who has left. समहोदरधूम्राक्षा अपसृष्टा रणाजिरात्<BR> Rām. 7. 32. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृप्
अपसृप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To glide or move gently along, glide away or off.<BR>—2 To withdraw, retire, go away; अपसर्पन्तु ते भूता ये भूता भूमिंसंस्थिताः<BR> Sandhyā; त्वरितमनन तरुगहनेनापसर्पत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">Page0151-1</a>]<BR> U. 4; उत्प्रेक्षितविकारः अपसर्पेत Mv. 4 retire, go into voluntary exile.<BR>—3 To observe closely (as a spy); शुद्धान्तचारी दुर्मुखः स मया पौरजानपदानपसर्पितुं<BR> प्रयुक्तः U. 1. ━<i>Caus.</i> To drive away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पः|अपसर्प
अपसर्पः, -र्पकः<BR> A secret agent or emissary, spy; सोपसर्पैर्जजागार<BR> यथाकालं स्वपन्नपि R. 17. 51; R. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पकः|अपसर्पक
अपसर्पः, -र्पकः<BR> A secret agent or emissary, spy; सोपसर्पैर्जजागार<BR> यथाकालं स्वपन्नपि R. 17. 51; R. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पणम्
अपसर्पणम् Going back, retreating; observing as a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृप्तिः|अपसृप्ति
अपसृप्तिः <i>f.</i> Going away or forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कम्भः|अपस्कम्भ|अपस्कंभः
अपस्कम्भः Fastening, making firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्करः|अपस्कर
अपस्करः [अप-कॄ अप्-सुट् रथाङ्गे निपातः अपस्करो रथाङ्गम् P. VI. 1. 149]<BR>—1 Any part of a carriage, except the wheel (˚रम् also); उरगध्वजदुर्घर्षं<BR> सुवरूथं स्वपस्करम् Rām. 6. 57. 26; cf. स्याद्रथाङ्गमपस्करः ।<BR> Ak. अपस्करमधिष्ठाने हिमवान् विन्ध्यपर्वतः Mb.<BR>—2 Excrement.<BR>—3 Vulva.<BR>—4 Anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कारः|अपस्कार
अपस्कारः The root or underpart of the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्खलः|अपस्खल
अपस्खलः Leaping or jumping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्तम्भः|अपस्तम्भ|अपस्तंभः
अपस्तम्भः A vessel in the side of the breast containing vital air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नात|अपस्नातः
अपस्नात <i>a.</i> [अपकृष्टं स्नातः] One who has bathed after death<BR> or mourning or upon the death of a relation, preparatory to other ceremonies;<BR> अपस्नात इवारिष्टं प्रविवेश गृहोत्तमम् Rām. 2. 42. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नानम्
अपस्नानम्<BR>—1 Bathing as after mourning or upon the death of a relative; funeral bathing.<BR>—2 Impure bathing, bathing in water in which a person has previously washed<BR> himself (स्नानशिष्टं जलम्) Ms. 4. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पतिः|अपस्पति
अपस्पतिः N. of a son of Uttānapāda; V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पश
अपस्पश <i>a.</i> Devoid of spies; शब्दविद्येव नो भाति राजनीतिरपस्पशा<BR> Śi. 2. 112 (where ˚शा also means without पस्पशा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पृश्
अपस्पृश् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not letting oneself be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पर्श
अपस्पर्श^1 <i>a.</i> Insensible.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: under root apaspfS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फिग
अपस्फिग <i>a.</i> Having badly formed hips; (P. VI. 2. 187).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फुर्
अपस्फुर् (-स्फूः), -र, -रत्<BR> <i>a.</i> Injured (Sāy.); swelling, increasing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फुर
अपस्फुर् (-स्फूः), -र, -रत्<BR> <i>a.</i> Injured (Sāy.); swelling, increasing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फुरत्|अपस्फुरन्त्
अपस्फुर् (-स्फूः), -र, -रत्<BR> <i>a.</i> Injured (Sāy.); swelling, increasing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारः|अपस्मार
अपस्मारः, -स्मृतिः <i>f.</i><BR> [अपस्मारयति स्मरणं विलोपयति, स्मृ-णिच्, कर्तरि<BR> अच्, or अपगतः स्मारः स्मरणं यतः]<BR>—1 Forgetfulness, loss of memory; स्मर˚ Bh. 1. 89.<BR>—2 Epilepsy, falling sickness; Suśr. thus derives it; स्मृतिर्भूतार्थविज्ञानमपश्च<BR> परिवर्जने । अपस्मार इति प्रोक्तस्ततोऽयं व्याधिरन्तकृत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मृतिः|अपस्मृति
अपस्मारः, -स्मृतिः <i>f.</i><BR> [अपस्मारयति स्मरणं विलोपयति, स्मृ-णिच्, कर्तरि<BR> अच्, or अपगतः स्मारः स्मरणं यतः]<BR>—1 Forgetfulness, loss of memory; स्मर˚ Bh. 1. 89.<BR>—2 Epilepsy, falling sickness; Suśr. thus derives it; स्मृतिर्भूतार्थविज्ञानमपश्च<BR> परिवर्जने । अपस्मार इति प्रोक्तस्ततोऽयं व्याधिरन्तकृत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मरणम्
अपस्मरणम् Reminding (?); सकृद्वचनेन ज्ञातस्य पुनर्वचनेन<BR> प्रयोजनमस्तीति । उच्यते । भवति उपस्मरणमपि प्रयोजनमित्युक्तम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 1. (If the word is अप्रस्मरण it would mean ‘absence of forgetting’<BR> प्र + स्मृ is used by Śabara<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">Page0151-2</a>]<BR> in the sense ‘to forget’. It is, therefore, likely that the reading here<BR> is अप्रस्मरण instead of अपस्मरण which does not appear in<BR> शबरʼs भाष्य elsewhere.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारिन्
अपस्मारिन् <i>a.</i> Epileptic, having an epileptic fit; Ms. 3. 7; फेनायमानं<BR> पतिमापगानामसावपस्मारिणमाशशङ्के Śi. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मृत
अपस्मृत <i>a.</i> Absentminded, unconscious; मुखाद्वमन् रुधिरमपस्मृतोऽसुरः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 18. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मृति|अपस्मृतिः
अपस्मृति <i>a.</i> Forgetful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्य
अपस्य, -स्यु &c.<BR> See under अपस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यु
अपस्य, -स्यु &c.<BR> See under अपस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्वरः|अपस्वर
अपस्वरः An unmusical sound or note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्वानः|अपस्वान
अपस्वानः A hurricane; Āpast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहन्
अपहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To ward or beat off, repel, destroy, kill, take away, remove; अपघ्नन्तो<BR> दुरितं हव्यगन्धैः Ś. 4. 8; न तु खलु तयोर्ज्ञाने शक्तिं करोत्यपहन्ति<BR> वा U. 2. 4 takes away; Ms. 6. 96; अपहतपाप्मानं सवितारमुपतिष्ठस्व U. 3.<BR>—2 To attack, affect, seize (as disease &c.).<BR>—3 To husk out, take off the shell or husk (as rice).<BR>—4 To shoot out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह
अपह <i>a.</i> [अप्-हन्-ड] (At the end of comp.) Warding or<BR> keeping off, taking away, removing, destroying, repelling &c.; न दंशमशकापहम्<BR> Pt. 3. 97; स्रगियं यदि जीवितापहा R. 8. 46; परकर्मापहः सोऽभूत् 17. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहतिः|अपहति
अपहतिः <i>f.</i> Removing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहननम्
अपहननम् Warding off, repelling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहल
अपहल <i>a.</i> Having a bad plough. P. VI. 2. 187<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्
अपहस् €1 P. To mock or scoff at, ridicule, deride; साहसापहसितकुमारेण<BR> Dk. 9 scoffed at, i. e. excelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहसितम्
अपहसितम्, -हासः<BR> Silly or causeless laughter; often laughter with tearful<BR> eyes (नीचानामपहसितम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहासः|अपहास
अपहसितम्, -हासः<BR> Silly or causeless laughter; often laughter with tearful<BR> eyes (नीचानामपहसितम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तः|अपहस्त
अपहस्तः [अपसारणार्थो हस्तः]<BR>—1 The hand placed on the neck to drive out a person (गलहस्त);<BR> one that is so driven out; सारथिं चास्य दयितमपहस्तेन जघ्निवान्<BR> Mb. 1. 129. 36, 3. 12. 85.<BR>—2 Throwing away or off, taking away असिहस्तापहस्ताभ्यां तेषां गात्राण्यकृन्तत Mb. 6. 90. 45.<BR>—3 Stealing, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तयति
अपहस्तयति Den. P. To seize by the neck and drive out; hence throw<BR> away, abandon, leave, discard, reject (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तित
अपहस्तित <i>p. p.</i> Thrown away, discarded, abandoned, cast off,<BR> given up; ˚सकलसखीजनं त्वयि विश्वसिति मे हृदयम् K. 233, 202;<BR> ˚बान्धवे त्वया Māl. 9. 19; अयं मम ˚लज्जो व्यवसायः V. 2;<BR> मानिनीभिरपहास्तितधैर्यः Ki. 9. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहा
अपहा €3^1 P.<BR>—1 To leave, abandon; साक्षात्प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वम् Ś. 6. 15.<BR> विललाप स बाष्पगद्गदं सहजामप्यपहाय धीरताम् R. 8. 43.<BR>—2 To discharge, pay off; ऋणान्यनपहाय Mb. 12. 7. 18. ━<i>pass.</i><BR> To waste away, wane.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: class of root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानम्
अपहानम् Leaving, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानिः|अपहानि
अपहानिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Leaving, abandonment; stopping.<BR>—2 Ceasing, vanishing.<BR>—3 Exception, exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहाय
अपहाय <i>ind.</i> Leaving, abandoning, except, without, excepting<BR> (used with the force of a preposition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृ
अपहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 ——(<i>a</i>) To take off, bear or snatch away, carry off; पश्चात्पुत्रैरपहृतभरः V. 3. 1<BR> relieved of the burden; तन्त्रादचिरापहृतः पटः brought; तन्त्रादचिरापहृते<BR> P. V. 2. 70. Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To avert, turn away; वदनमपहरन्तीम् (गौरीम्) Ku. 7. 95<BR> averting or turning away her face.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To rob, plunder, steal.<BR>—2 To sever, separate, cut off; R. 15. 52, v. l.<BR>—3 To overpower, overcome, subdue; attract, ravish, captivate; affect,<BR> influence (in a good or bad sense); अपह्रिये खलु परिश्रमजनितया<BR> निद्रया U. 1 overpowered; उत्सवापहृतचेतोभिः Ratn. 1; यथा नापह्रियसे<BR> सुखेन K. 109 seduced, led away, 277; न … प्रियतमा यतमानमपाहरत्<BR> R. 9. 7 did not subdue i. e. did not divert his mind.<BR>—4 To remove, take away, destroy, annihilate, deprive (one) of; कीर्ति˚<BR> R. 11. 74; प्रिया मे दत्ता वाक् पुनर्मेऽपहृता Dk. 52.<BR>—5 To take back, resume; देयं प्रतिश्रुतं चैव दत्त्वा नापहरेत्पुनः Y. 2. 176.<BR>—6 To subtract, deduct.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To cause (others) to take away; परैस्त्वदन्यः क इवापहारयेन्मनोरमाम् Ki. 1. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरणम्
अपहरणम्<BR>—1 Taking or carrying away, removing.<BR>—2 Stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहर्तृ|अपहर्त्तृ
अपहर्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One that takes or carries away, steals, removes, destroys &c.<BR>—2 Removing, expiating; स्तेयदोषापहर्तॄणां व्रतनाम् Ms. 11. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारः|अपहार
अपहारः<BR>—1 Taking or carrying away, stealing, plundering, removing, killing, destroying;<BR> कर्णनासापहारेण भगिनी मे विरूपिता Rām. by the cutting of ears<BR> and nose; निद्रापहार, विष˚.<BR>—2 Concealing, dissembling; कथमात्मापहारं करोमि Ś. 1 how shall<BR> I dissemble myself, conceal my real name and character; see अपहारक below.<BR>—3 Spending or using anotherʼs property.<BR>—4 Loss, damage.<BR>—5 Bringing in, obtaining; समित्कुशकुसुमापहारसंमार्जनलब्धविश्रमाः<BR> (वानप्रस्थाः) Mb. 12. 192. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारक|अपहारकः
अपहारक, -हारिन् <i>a.</i><BR> One who or that which takes away, steals, removes,<BR> destroys, conceals &c. (usually in comp.); जालापहारिणः H. 1; परद्रव्य˚<BR> plunderer, thief; परवित्त˚; वागपहारकः Ms. 11. 51; Y. 3. 210;<BR> Ms. 4. 255, 2. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारिन्
अपहारक, -हारिन् <i>a.</i><BR> One who or that which takes away, steals, removes,<BR> destroys, conceals &c. (usually in comp.); जालापहारिणः H. 1; परद्रव्य˚<BR> plunderer, thief; परवित्त˚; वागपहारकः Ms. 11. 51; Y. 3. 210;<BR> Ms. 4. 255, 2. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारकः|अपहारक
अपहारक, -हारिन् + .{@-कः@} A robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृत
अपहृत <i>p. p.</i> Taken away, carried off &c.; तस्मिन्नहनि राजर्षिर्निद्रयापहृतो<BR> भृशम् Rām. 7. 55. 15 destitute of, free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नवः|अपह्नव
अपह्नवः<BR>—1 Concealment, hiding; concealment of oneʼs knowledge, feelings &c. स<BR> कदाचिदुपासीन आत्मापह्नवमात्मनः Bhāg. 9. 6. 49.<BR>—2 Denial or disowning of the truth, dissimulation; ˚वे ज्ञः P. I. 3. 44;<BR> ज्ञातं मया ते हृदयं सखे माऽपह्नवं कृथाः Ks. 10. 92.<BR>—3 Appeasing, satisfying.<BR>—4 Love, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नु
अपह्नु €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To conceal, hide, disguise; अदेश्यं यश्च दिशति निर्दिश्यापह्नुते<BR> च यः Ms. 8. 53; कामदेवव्यपदेशेन सखीपुरतोऽपह्नुतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">Page0152-2</a>]<BR> Ratn. 2 was passed off as Cupid upon her friend<BR>—2 To deny, disown; गुणांश्चापह्नुषेऽस्माकम् Bk. 5. 44; अपह्नुवानस्य<BR> जनाय यन्निजाम् (अधीरताम्) N. 1. 49.<BR>—3 To exculpate, excuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुतिः|अपह्नुति
अपह्नुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Concealment of knowledge, denial.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech, in which the real character of the thing<BR> in question is denied and that of another (alien or imaginary) object<BR> is ascribed to, or superimposed upon, it; प्रकृतं यन्निषिध्यान्यत्साध्यते<BR> सा त्वपह्नुतिः K. P. 10; (उपमेयमसत्यं कृत्वा उपमानं सत्यतया<BR> यत्स्थाप्यते साऽपह्नुतिः) <i>e. g.</i> नेदं नभोमण्डलमम्बुराशिर्नैताश्च<BR> तारा नवफेनभङ्गाः । नायं शशी कुण्डलितः फणीन्द्रो नासौ कलङ्कः शयितो<BR> मुरारिः ॥ see also K. P. 10 and S. D. 683-84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्रासः|अपह्रास
अपह्रासः Reduction, diminution<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्
अपाक् <i>ind.</i> See अपाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक|अपाकः
अपाक <i>a.</i> Ved, [fr. अञ्च् with अप]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Situated aside or behind.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Remote, distant.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Coming from a distant place.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Unequalled, incomparable, very great (अनल्प Sāy.); ˚चक्षस्^1<BR> of unequalled brightness; ˚कात्-का aside, distant; ˚केस्थ standing behind.<BR>—2 Raw, unripe.<BR>—3 Not matured, undigested.<BR>—4 (पाकः पक्तव्यप्रज्ञः मूर्खः तद्विलक्षणः Of matured intellect,<BR> wise) Rv. 1. 110. 2, 6. 12. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकः|अपाक
अपाक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Indigestion (of food &c.).<BR>—2 Immaturity, not being ripe^1 or cooked.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपाकज, अपाकशाकम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकज
अपाक + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not produced by cooking or ripening.<BR>—2 natural, original; Bhāṣā P. 42, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकशाकम्
अपाक + -शाकम् ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृ
अपाकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To drive away, dispel, remove, destroy; keep, put, or take away; तन्नैशं<BR> तिमिरमपाकरोति चन्द्रः Ś. 6. 30; स्फुटता न पदैरपाकृता Ki. 2. 27;<BR> पापमपाकरोति Bh. 2. 23; गुहोऽपि येषां प्रथमात्मजन्मनां<BR> न पुत्रवात्सल्यमपाकरिष्यति Ku. 5. 14 remove, reduce, lessen; Māl. 6. 4;<BR> R. 6. 57; Śi. 8. 61.<BR>—2 To cast off, reject (also an opinion), leave, give up, throw away,<BR> drop; हंसैर्यियासुभिरपाकृतमुन्मनस्कैः Mk. 5. 1; शिवा भुजच्छेदमपाचकार R. 7. 50.<BR>—3 To discharge, liquidate (as debt &c.) ऋणानि त्रीण्यपाकृत्य मनो मोक्षे<BR> निवशयेत् Ms. 6. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरणम्
अपाकरणम्, अपाकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Driving away, removal.<BR>—2 Rejection, refutation; तदपाकरणायाह Praśna. Up.<BR>—3 Payment, liquidation; ऋणत्रयापाकरणान्नास्त्यपवर्गः Nyāya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृतिः|अपाकृति
अपाकरणम्, अपाकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Driving away, removal.<BR>—2 Rejection, refutation; तदपाकरणायाह Praśna. Up.<BR>—3 Payment, liquidation; ऋणत्रयापाकरणान्नास्त्यपवर्गः Nyāya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकर्मन्|अपाकर्म्मन्
अपाकर्मन् <i>n.</i> (˚र्म) Payment, liquidation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरिष्णु
अपाकरिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Driving away, removing.<BR>—2 Excelling, eclipsing; वर्णः स्वर्णापाकरिष्णुः Bh. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृत
अपाकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Removed, destroyed, dispelled, paid &c.<BR>—2 Devoid or destitute of, free from; कृतमिदमपाकृते गुणैः Śi. 15. 33;<BR> यत्स्वयमभियोगदुःखैरपाकृतं तदेव राज्यं सुखयति Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृतिः|अपाकृति
अपाकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Rejection, removal &c. विदा देवा अघानाआदित्यासो अपाकृतिम् Rv. 8. 47. 2.<BR>—2 Emotion resulting from anger, fear &c. निशम्य सिद्धिं द्विषतामपाकृतीः Ki. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकीर्ण
अपाकीर्ण <i>a.</i> Rejected, discarded; कुन्त्या त्वहमपाकीर्णो यथा<BR> न कुशलं तथा Mb. 5. 141. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष <i>a.</i> [अपनतः अक्षमिन्द्रियम्]<BR>—1 Present, perceptible.<BR>—2 [अपगते अपकृष्टे वा अक्षिणी यस्य] Eyeless; having bad eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त|अपांक्त
अपाङ्क्त, -पाङ्क्तेय, -पाङ्क्त्य <i>a.</i><BR> ‘Not in the same row or line’; especially<BR> one who is not allowed by his caste-men to sit in the same row with them<BR> at meals; degraded, excommunicated, excluded from or inadmissible into<BR> society, an outcast; ˚उपहत defiled by the presence of excommunicated<BR> or impious persons. एतान्विगर्हिताचारानपाङ्क्तेयान्द्विजाधमान् (विवर्जयेत्) Ms. 3. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्तेय|अपांक्तेय
अपाङ्क्त, -पाङ्क्तेय, -पाङ्क्त्य <i>a.</i><BR> ‘Not in the same row or line’; especially<BR> one who is not allowed by his caste-men to sit in the same row with them<BR> at meals; degraded, excommunicated, excluded from or inadmissible into<BR> society, an outcast; ˚उपहत defiled by the presence of excommunicated<BR> or impious persons. एतान्विगर्हिताचारानपाङ्क्तेयान्द्विजाधमान् (विवर्जयेत्) Ms. 3. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त्य|अपांक्त्य
अपाङ्क्त, -पाङ्क्तेय, -पाङ्क्त्य <i>a.</i><BR> ‘Not in the same row or line’; especially<BR> one who is not allowed by his caste-men to sit in the same row with them<BR> at meals; degraded, excommunicated, excluded from or inadmissible into<BR> society, an outcast; ˚उपहत defiled by the presence of excommunicated<BR> or impious persons. एतान्विगर्हिताचारानपाङ्क्तेयान्द्विजाधमान् (विवर्जयेत्) Ms. 3. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्ग|अपांग|अपाङ्गः
अपाङ्ग, -ङ्गक <i>a.</i><BR> [अपगतम् अङ्गं यस्य]<BR>—1 Wanting or deformed in some limb of the body. —2 Maimed, crippled<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गक|अपांगक|अपाङ्गकः
अपाङ्ग, -ङ्गक <i>a.</i><BR> [अपगतम् अङ्गं यस्य]<BR>—1 Wanting or deformed in some limb of the body. —2 Maimed, crippled<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गः|अपाङ्ग|अपांग
अपाङ्ग, -ङ्गक + .{@-ङ्गः, -ङ्गकः@} [अपाङ्गति तिर्यक् चलति नेत्रं यत्र, अप-अङ्ग-घञ्]<BR>—1 The outer corner or angle of the eye; चलापाङ्गां दृष्टिम् Ś. 1. 24;<BR> अम्महे अपाङ्गकः स्फुरति किमपि वामकः M. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>—3 Cupid, the god of love.<BR>—4 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग Mar. आघाडा) &c. अपाङ्गो नेत्रयोरन्ते<BR> तिलकाङ्गविहीनयोः Nm.<BR>—5 End; अथेमां सागरापाङ्गीं गाम् (अध्यतिष्ठत्) Mb. 1. 64. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपाङ्गदर्शनम्, अपाङ्गदृष्टिः, अपाङ्गदेशः, अपाङ्गनेत्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गकः|अपाङ्गक|अपांगक
अपाङ्ग, -ङ्गक + .{@-ङ्गः, -ङ्गकः@} [अपाङ्गति तिर्यक् चलति नेत्रं यत्र, अप-अङ्ग-घञ्]<BR>—1 The outer corner or angle of the eye; चलापाङ्गां दृष्टिम् Ś. 1. 24;<BR> अम्महे अपाङ्गकः स्फुरति किमपि वामकः M. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>—3 Cupid, the god of love.<BR>—4 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग Mar. आघाडा) &c. अपाङ्गो नेत्रयोरन्ते<BR> तिलकाङ्गविहीनयोः Nm.<BR>—5 End; अथेमां सागरापाङ्गीं गाम् (अध्यतिष्ठत्) Mb. 1. 64. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपाङ्गदर्शनम्, अपाङ्गदृष्टिः, अपाङ्गदेशः, अपाङ्गनेत्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गदर्शनम्
अपाङ्ग + -दर्शनम्, -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i>, -विलोकितम्, -वीक्षणम् &c.<BR> a side-glance, side-long look, wink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गदृष्टिः|अपाङ्गदृष्टि
अपाङ्ग + -दर्शनम्, -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i>, -विलोकितम्, -वीक्षणम् &c.<BR> a side-glance, side-long look, wink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गदेशः|अपाङ्गदेश
अपाङ्ग + -देशः the place of the corner of the eye; the corner itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गनेत्र
अपाङ्ग + -नेत्र <i>a.</i> (said of a lady) having eyes with beautiful (or<BR> long) outer corners; यदियं पुनरप्यपाङ्गनेत्रा परिवृत्तार्धमुखी मयाद्य<BR> दृष्टा V. 1. 19. (a better interpretation would however be ‘with the eyes turned towards the corners’<BR> अपाङ्गयोः प्रेरिते नेत्रे यया <i>i. e.</i><BR> casting sidelong looks.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्
अपाच्, अपाञ्च् (<i>m.</i> ङ्, <i>f.</i> ची, <i>n.</i> क्) [अपाञ्चति, अञ्च् क्विप्]<BR>—1 Going or situated backwards, behind.<BR>—2 Not open or clear (अप्रकाश).<BR>—3 Western.<BR>—4 Southern (opp. उदञ्च्); probably for अवाञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाञ्च्|अपांच्
अपाच्, अपाञ्च् (<i>m.</i> ङ्, <i>f.</i> ची, <i>n.</i> क्) [अपाञ्चति, अञ्च् क्विप्]<BR>—1 Going or situated backwards, behind.<BR>—2 Not open or clear (अप्रकाश).<BR>—3 Western.<BR>—4 Southern (opp. उदञ्च्); probably for अवाञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्
अपाच्, अपाञ्च् + .{@-क्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Behind, backwards.<BR>—2 Westward or southward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाची
अपाची The south or west; cf. Śiva B. 4. 64 and 5. 29. ˚इतरा<BR> the north (other than south).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाचीन|अपाचीनं
अपाचीन <i>a.</i> [अपाच्यां भवः ख]<BR>—1 Situated backwards or behind, turned backwards.<BR>—2 Not visible, imperceptible; यो अपाचीने तमसि मदन्तीःप्राचीश्चकार<BR> नृऽतमः शचीभिः Rv. 7. 6. 4.<BR>—3 Southern.<BR>—4 Western.<BR>—5 Opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्य|अपाच्यं
अपाच्य <i>a.</i> [अपाच्-यत्] Western or southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाटव|अपाटवं
अपाटव <i>a.</i> Unskilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाटवम्
अपाटव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Unskilfulness.<BR>—2 Sickness, illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाठ्य
अपाठ्य <i>a.</i> Illegible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिग्रहणम्
अपाणिग्रहणम् Celibacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिनीय
अपाणिनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not taught by Pāṇini in his works (as a rule &c.).<BR>—2 (पाणिनीयम् अष्टाध्यायीरूपं ग्रन्थं यो नाधीते) One who does not (properly)<BR> study Pāṇiniʼs grammar; <i>i. e.</i> a superficial scholar, smatterer of Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रम्
अपात्रम्<BR>—1 A worthless vessel or utensil.<BR>—2 (fig.) An unworthy or undeserving person, unfit receptacle or recipient.<BR>—3 One unfit or disqualified to receive gifts; अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च<BR> दीयते Bg. 17. 22; Ks. 24. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपात्रकृत्या, अपात्रीकरणम्, अपात्रदायिन्, अपात्रभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रकृत्या
अपात्रम् + -कृत्या, अपात्रीकरणम् doing degrading or unworthy acts; disqualification,<BR> any action which makes a man unworthy; four disqualifications for a Brāhmaṇa<BR> are mentioned in Ms. 11. 70. निन्दितेभ्यो धनादानं वाणिज्यं शूद्रसेवनम् ।<BR> अपात्रीकरणं ज्ञेयमसत्यस्य च भाषणम् ॥; see also संकरापात्रकृत्यासु<BR> मासं शोधनमैन्दवम् 11. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रीकरणम्
अपात्रम् + -कृत्या, अपात्रीकरणम् doing degrading or unworthy acts; disqualification,<BR> any action which makes a man unworthy; four disqualifications for a Brāhmaṇa<BR> are mentioned in Ms. 11. 70. निन्दितेभ्यो धनादानं वाणिज्यं शूद्रसेवनम् ।<BR> अपात्रीकरणं ज्ञेयमसत्यस्य च भाषणम् ॥; see also संकरापात्रकृत्यासु<BR> मासं शोधनमैन्दवम् 11. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रदायिन्
अपात्रम् + -दायिन् <i>a.</i> giving to unworthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रभृत्
अपात्रम् + -भृत् <i>a.</i> supporting the unworthy or worthless; प्रायेणापात्रभृद्भवति राजा Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाद
अपाद्^1अ = अपद् q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादा
अपादा €3 Ā. To take off or away, to remove; तत्पाप्मानमपादत्ते;<BR> मृत्पिण्डमपादाय महावीरं करोति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादानम्
अपादानम्<BR>—1 Taking away, removal; ablation; a thing from which another is removed.<BR>—2 (in gram.) The sense of the ablative case; ध्रुवमपायेऽपादानम्<BR> P. I. 4. 24; अपादाने पञ्चमी II. 3. 28; अपाये यदुदासीनं चलं वा<BR> यदि वाऽचलम् । ध्रुवमेव तदावेशात्तदपादानमुच्यते ॥ Hariv.; अपादान<BR> is of three kinds:− निर्दिष्टविषयं किंचिदुपात्तविषयं तथा । अपेक्षितक्रियं<BR> चेति त्रिधापादानमिष्यते ॥ <i>e. g.</i> वृक्षात् पत्रं पतति, मेघाद्विद्योतते<BR> विद्युत्, & कुतो भवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्त
अपात्त <i>a.</i> acquired, Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाध्वन्
अपाध्वन् <i>n.</i> A bad way; P. VI. 2. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्
अपान् €2 P. [अप-अन्]<BR>—1 To breathe out, respire; यद्वै प्राणिति स प्राणो यदपानिति सोऽपानः Ch. Up.<BR>—2 To expire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानः|अपान|अपानं
अपानः Breathing out, respiration (opp. प्राण); प्राणापानौ समौ<BR> कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ Bg. 5. 27; one of the five life-winds in the<BR> body which goes downwards and out at the anus (अपनयनान्मूत्रपुरीषादेरपानोऽधोवृत्तिर्वायुर्नाभिस्थानः)<BR> मूत्रशुक्रवहो वायुरपान इति कीर्त्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानः|अपान|अपानं
अपानः + .{@-नः, -नम्@} The anus (आधारे घञ्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपानदा, अपानद्वारम्, अपानपवनः, अपानवायुः, अपानभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानम्
अपानः + .{@-नः, -नम्@} The anus (आधारे घञ्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपानदा, अपानद्वारम्, अपानपवनः, अपानवायुः, अपानभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानदा
अपानः + -दा giving Apāna. Vāj. 17. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानद्वारम्
अपानः + -द्वारम् the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानपवनः|अपानपवन
अपानः + -पवनः, -वायुः<BR>—1 the life-wind called अपान.<BR>—2 ventris crepitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानवायुः|अपानवायु
अपानः + -पवनः, -वायुः<BR>—1 the life-wind called अपान.<BR>—2 ventris crepitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानभृत्
अपानः + -भृत् <i>f.</i> a sort of brick (cherishing the life-wind अपान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाननम्
अपाननम्<BR>—1 Respiration.<BR>—2 Taking downwards, urine, excrement &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानृत
अपानृत <i>a.</i> Free from falsehood, true. अपानृतकथं पुत्र पितरं<BR> कर्तुमिच्छसि Rām. 2. 34. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्तरतमा
अपान्तरतमा <i>m.</i> The name of an ancient sage or of Vyāsa in his<BR> previous birth. सरस्वतीमुच्चचार तत्र सारस्वतोऽभवत् । अपान्तरतमा<BR> नाम सुतो वाक्संभवः प्रभुः ॥ Mb. 12. 349. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाप|अपापः
अपाप, -पिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Sinless, guiltless, pure, virtuous; अपापानां कुले<BR> जाते मयि पापं न विद्यते । यदि संभाव्यते पापमपापेन च किं मया ॥ Mk. 9. 37.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपापकाशिन्, अपापवस्यसम्, अपापविद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपापिन्
अपाप, -पिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Sinless, guiltless, pure, virtuous; अपापानां कुले<BR> जाते मयि पापं न विद्यते । यदि संभाव्यते पापमपापेन च किं मया ॥ Mk. 9. 37.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपापकाशिन्, अपापवस्यसम्, अपापविद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपापकाशिन्
अपाप + -काशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not ill-looking.<BR>—2 not revealing evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपापवस्यसम्
अपाप + -वस्यसम् Ved. well-being, welfare, sound health, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपापविद्ध
अपाप + -विद्ध <i>a.</i> Not afflicted with evil; शुद्धमपापविद्धम् (ब्रह्मन्) Vāj. 40. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांपित्त|अपाम्पित्त|अपांपित्तं|अपाम्पित्तं
अपांपित्त ˚नपात् &c. &c. see under अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्गः|अपामार्ग
अपामार्गः [अपमृज्यते व्याध्यादिरनेन इत्यपामार्गः, मृज् करणे घञ्<BR> कुत्वं दीर्घश्च P. III. 3. 121. Sk.] N. of a plant Achyranthes Aspera<BR> (Mar. आघाडा) largely used in medicine, washing teeth, sacrificial<BR> and other religious purposes and in incantations; अपामार्ग त्वया वयं<BR> सर्वं तदपमृज्महे; अपामार्ग ओषधीनां सर्वासामेक इद्वशी । Av.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपामार्गक्षारतैलम्, अपामार्गतैलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्गक्षारतैलम्
अपामार्गः + -क्षारतैलम्, -तैलम् N. of two medicated oils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्गतैलम्
अपामार्गः + -क्षारतैलम्, -तैलम् N. of two medicated oils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्जनम्
अपामार्जनम् Cleansing, purifying, removing (diseases, evils &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाय|अपायः
अपाय, -यिन्<BR> See under अपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपाय, -यिन्<BR> See under अपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shoreless.<BR>—2 Boundless, unbounded, unlimited; अपारस्याप्रमेयस्य परं पारमुपाश्रिते<BR> Rām. unfathomable, of great length.<BR>—3 Inexhaustible, immense, great (अधिक); अपारो वो महिमा Rv. 5. 87. 6.<BR>—4 Out of reach.<BR>—5 Difficult to be crossed; difficult to be surmounted or overcome (as<BR> an enemy); रावणश्च महाशत्रुरपारः प्रतिभाति मे । Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारः|अपार|अपारं
अपार + .{@-रः@} An ocean; कर्णधार इवापारे भगवान्पारदर्शकः Bhāg. 1. 13. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारम्
अपार + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A kind of mental satisfaction or acquiescence; or, reverse of mental<BR> acquiescence, non-acquiescence.<BR>—2 The opposite bank of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारा
अपार + .{@-रा@} The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार + .{@-पार@} <i>a.</i> Carrying over the boundless sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारक
अपारक <i>a.</i> Unable, incompetent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारवार
अपारवार <i>a.</i> Boundless; अपारवारमक्षोभ्यं गाम्भीर्यात्सागरोपमम्<BR> Rām. 5. 38. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्ण
अपार्ण <i>a.</i> [अप-अर्द्-क्त निपातः]<BR>—1 Distant, remote, far.<BR>—2 Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थ
अपार्थ [अप-अर्थ], अपार्थक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Useless, unprofitable, worthless; सर्वमेतदपार्थं ते क्षिप्रं तौ<BR> संप्रसादय Mb.<BR>—2 Meaningless, unmeaning, senseless; अपार्थं बहु भाषते Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थक
अपार्थ [अप-अर्थ], अपार्थक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Useless, unprofitable, worthless; सर्वमेतदपार्थं ते क्षिप्रं तौ<BR> संप्रसादय Mb.<BR>—2 Meaningless, unmeaning, senseless; अपार्थं बहु भाषते Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थम्
अपार्थ [अप-अर्थ], अपार्थक + .{@-र्थम्@}<BR>—1 Senseless or incoherent talk or argument (regarded as one of the faults<BR> of composition in rhetoric); योग्यतासत्त्याकाङ्क्षाशून्यं वाक्यम् Gaut. S.;<BR> पौर्वापर्यायोगादप्रतिबन्धार्थमपार्थकम्; cf. also Kāv. 3. 128; समुदायार्थशून्यं<BR> यत्तदपार्थमितीष्यते ।<BR>—2 uselessness; तेषां श्रमो ह्यपार्थाय यदात्मा नादृतः स्वयम् Bhāg. 3. 13. 13.<BR>━<i>ind.</i> In vain, unprofitably; स्वयं सधर्मा अपि शोचन्त्यपार्थम्<BR> Bhāg. 7. 2. 37.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपार्थकरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थकरणम्
अपार्थ + -करणम् advancing a false plea in a law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थिव
अपार्थिव <i>a.</i> Not earthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपालङ्कः|अपालङ्क|अपालंकः
अपालङ्कः N. of a plant, Cassia Fistula. आरग्वध (Mar. बाहवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपालम्बः|अपालम्ब|अपालंबः
अपालम्बः Ved. The hinder part of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृ
अपावृ €5 P.<BR>—1 To open, lay bare or open, unveil, uncover; expose, display, reveal;<BR> (शयनम्) तस्य विभ्रमरतान्यपावृणोत् R. 19. 25.<BR>—2 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत|अपावृतं
अपावृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Opened, laid bare or open; राधो विश्वायु शवसे अपावृतम् Rv. 1. 57. 1.<BR> स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतम् Bg. 2. 32.<BR>—2 Covered, concealed; enclosed.<BR>—3 Free, unrestrained, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृतिः|अपावृति
अपावृतिः <i>f.</i>, अपावरणम्<BR>—1 Opening, laying bare or open.<BR>—2 Covering, enclosing, surrounding.<BR>—3 Concealing, hiding, screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावरणम्
अपावृतिः <i>f.</i>, अपावरणम्<BR>—1 Opening, laying bare or open.<BR>—2 Covering, enclosing, surrounding.<BR>—3 Concealing, hiding, screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्
अपावृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn away, return, turn back; to turn away from, abstain or desist from.<BR>—2 To come to nothing.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To send back, turn back; to reject, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावर्तनम्
अपावर्तनम्, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Turning away or from, retreating, retiring; repulse, rejection.<BR>—2 Revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्तिः|अपावृत्ति
अपावर्तनम्, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Turning away or from, retreating, retiring; repulse, rejection.<BR>—2 Revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्त|अपावृत्तं
अपावृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 (With abl.) Turned away from, averted, reversed, repelled, driven back,<BR> defeated; कथं द्रक्ष्याम्यपावृत्तां परैरिव हतां चमूम् Rām. 2. 12. 64.<BR>—2 (Actively used) Dismissing, scorning, rejecting with contempt; प्रतिग्रहादपावृत्तः<BR> सन्तुष्टो येन केन चित् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्तम्
अपावृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@}<BR>—1 Rolling on the ground (of a horse).<BR>—2 Moving aside (a war manoeuvre); परावृत्तमपावृत्तमपद्रुतमवप्लवम्<BR> Rām. 6. 40. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्या
अपाश्या Not a large number of snares, <i>i. e.</i> a few snares; ययतोश्चातदर्थे<BR> P. VI. 2. 156. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रि
अपाश्रि €1 U.<BR>—1 To resort to, betake oneself to; परस्परं केचिदपाश्रयन्ते Rām.<BR>—2 To use, practise, employ; आहारमनपाश्रित्य शरीरस्येव धारणम् Mb.<BR>—3 To rest on, lie on (intrans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रय|अपाश्रयः
अपाश्रय <i>a.</i> Without support or refuge, helpless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रयः|अपाश्रय
अपाश्रय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Refuge, recourse, that to which recourse is had for refuge; कर्णे<BR> कृतापाश्रयः Ve. 5. 1.<BR>—2 An awning or canopy spread over a courtyard.<BR>—3 Head; त्वदङ्कापाश्रयां ताम् Dk. 34, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रित
अपाश्रित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 (Passively used)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Resorted to^1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Girt round, fastened.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Inhabited by.<BR>—2 (Actively used) Resting or reposing on, resorting to, entering on or<BR> into, being in or under.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाष्टिः|अपाष्टि
अपाष्टिः <i>f.</i> Ved. The heel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाष्ठः|अपाष्ठ
अपाष्ठः [स्था-क; सस्य षत्वम्] Ved. The barb or point of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाष्ठम्
अपाष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठम्@} The remainder of the Soma plant after it has been pressed<BR> out; ˚वत् barbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्
अपास् [अप्-अस्] €4 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To throw or fling away, cast away or off, leave, keep or put<BR> aside, reject, discard (opinion also); सारं ततो ग्राह्यमपास्य फल्गु<BR> Pt. 1. 5; किमित्यपास्याभरणानि यौवने धृतं त्वया वार्धकशोभि वल्कलम्<BR> Ku. 5. 44; निरस्तगाम्भीर्यमपास्तपुष्पकम् Śi. 1. 55; इत्यादीनामपि<BR> काव्यलक्षणत्वमपास्तम् S. D. rejected, discarded.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To leave, abandon, desert, quit, retire or withdraw from; यदि<BR> समरमपास्य नास्ति मृत्योर्भयम् Ve. 3. 5.<BR>—2 To scare, disperse, drive away; अपास्य चास्य यन्तारम् Mb.<BR>—3 To leave behind, leave in a deserted condition; to disregard, take<BR> no notice of, condemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासनम्
अपासनम्<BR>—1 Throwing away, discarding.<BR>—2 Quitting.<BR>—3 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासित
अपासित <i>p. p.</i> (fr. caus.) Thrown away, discarded &c.; injured,<BR> destroyed, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्त|अपास्तं
अपास्त <i>a.</i> Discarded, thrown away, abandoned. किं त्यक्तापास्तदेवत्वमानुष्यकपरिग्रहैः Ki. 15. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासङ्गः|अपासङ्ग|अपासंग|अपासंगः
अपासङ्गः [सञ्ज्-घञ्-कुत्वम्] A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासरणम्
अपासरणम् <i>n.</i> Departure, retreat, removal; see अपसरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासु
अपासु <i>a.</i> Lifeless, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाहा
अपाहा €3 P. = अपहा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपि
अपि <i>ind.</i> (Sometimes with the अ dropped according to the opinion<BR> of Bhāguri; वष्टि भागुरिरल्लेपमवाप्योरुपसर्गयोः; पिधा, पिधान &c.)<BR>—1 (Used with roots and nouns in the sense of) Placing near or over, taking<BR> towards, uniting with; reaching or going up to, proximity, nearness &c.<BR> [cf. Gr. <i>epi</i>, Zend. <i>api</i>, Germ. and Eng. <i>be</i>]. (Note:− अपि,<BR> as a prefix to roots, occurs mostly in Veda, its place being taken by<BR> अभि in classical literature).<BR>—2 (As a separable adverb or conjunction) And, also, too, moreover, besides,<BR> in addition, having a cumulative force (समुच्चय); अस्ति मे सोदरस्नेहोऽप्येतेषु;<BR> Ś. 1 on oneʼs part, in oneʼs turn; विष्णुशर्मणाऽपि राजपुत्राः पाठिताः<BR> Pt. 1; राजाऽपि मुनिवाक्यमङ्गीकृत्यातिष्ठत् Dk. 2; अपि-अपि or अपि<BR> च as well as, and also; अपि स्तुहि, अपि सिञ्च P. I. 4. 46. Sk., न<BR> नापि━न चैव, न वाऽपि, नापि वा चापि neither━nor; न चापि काव्यं<BR> नवमित्यवद्यम् M. 1. 2 nor; वाऽपि or; अल्पोऽप्येवं महान् वाऽपि<BR> Ms. 3. 53 whether small or great.<BR>—3 It is often used to express emphasis in the sense of ‘too’, ‘even’,<BR> ‘very’; विधुरपि विधियोगाद् ग्रस्यते राहुणाऽसौ H. 1. 19 the very moon;<BR> यूयमप्यनेन कर्मणा परिश्रान्ताः Ś. 1 even you, you also; अन्यदपि<BR> also another; अद्यापि even, yet, still, even now; इदानीमपि even<BR> now; मुहूर्तमपि even for a moment, for one moment at least; नाद्यापि<BR> not yet; यद्यपि though, although, even if; तथापि still, यद्यपि<BR> बहु नाधीषे तथापि पठ पुत्र व्याकरणम्; nevertheless, notwithstanding,<BR> yet; sometimes यद्यपि is understood, तथाऽपि only being used;<BR> as in भवादृशेषु प्रमदाजनोदितं भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनम् । तथाऽपि<BR> वक्तुं व्यवसाययन्ति मां निरस्तनारीसमया दुराधयः Ki. 1. 28.<BR>—4 Though (oft. translatable by ‘even’, ‘even if’); सरसिजमनुविद्धं<BR> शैवलेनापि रम्यम् Ś. 1. 20 though over-spread &c.; इयमधिकमनोज्ञा<BR> वल्कलेनापि तन्वी <i>ibid.</i> though in her bark dress; बलवदपि शिक्षितानाम् 1. 2<BR> though ever so learned. In this sense अपि is most frequently<BR> used by writers to show real or imaginary opposition (विरोध); कृष्णमपि<BR> असुदर्शनम्, पुष्पवत्यपि पवित्रा &c.<BR>—5 But however.<BR>—6 Used at the beginning of sentences अपि introduces a question; अपि<BR> सन्निहितोऽत्र कुलपतिः Ś. 1; अपि क्रियार्थं सुलभं समित्कुशं … अपि<BR> स्वशक्त्या तपसि प्रवर्तसे Ku. 5. 33, 34, 35; अप्यग्रणीर्मन्त्रकृतामृषीणां<BR> कुशाग्रबुद्धे कुशली गुरुस्ते R. 5. 4.<BR>—7 Hope, expectation (usually with the potential mood); कृतं रामसदृशं<BR> कर्म । अपि जीवेत्स ब्राह्मणशिशुः U. 2 I hope the Brāhmaṇa boy comes<BR> to life, Note━ In this sense अपि is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-2" target="_blank">Page0155-2</a>]<BR> frequently used with नाम and has the sense of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) ‘is it likely’, ‘may it be’;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) ‘perhaps’, ‘in all probability’ or<BR>——(<i>c</i>) ‘would that’, ‘I wish or hope that’; अपि नाम कुलपतेरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा<BR> स्यात् Ś. 1; Ś. 7; तदपि नाम मनागवतीर्णोऽसि रतिरमणबाणगोचरम्<BR> Māl. 1 perhaps, in all probability; अपि नाम तयोः कल्याणिनोः अभिमतः<BR> पाणिग्रहः स्यात् <i>ibid.</i>; अपि नाम रामभद्रः पुनरपीदं वनमलङ्कुर्यात्<BR> U. 2; ‘is it likely’, ‘I wish’; यथा वनज्योत्स्नानुरूपेण पादपेन संगता<BR> अपि नाम एवमहमप्यात्मनोऽनुरूपं वरं लभेयेति Ś. 1 would that;<BR> अपि नामाहं पुरूरवा भवेयम् V. 2 I wish I were P.<BR>—8 Affixed to interrogative words, अपि makes the sense indefinite,<BR> ‘any’, ‘some’; कोऽपि some one; किमपि something; कुत्रापि somewhere;<BR> कदाऽपि at any time; कथमपि any how &c. केऽपि एते प्रवयसः<BR> त्वां दिदृक्षवः U. 4 some people. It may often be translated by ‘unknown’,<BR> ‘indescribable’, ‘inexpressible’ (अनिर्वाच्य); व्यतिषजति पदार्थानान्तरः<BR> कोऽपि हेतुः U. 6. 12. तत्तस्य किमपि द्रव्यं यो हि यस्य प्रियो जनः 2. 19;<BR> Mu. 3. 22; K. 143; कोऽपि महिमा स्यात् U. 6, 6. 11, 7. 12; Māl. 1. 26;<BR> R. 1. 46.<BR>—9 After words expressing number, अपि has the sense of ‘totality’,<BR> ‘all’; चतुर्णामपि वर्णानाम् of all the 4 castes; सर्वैरपि राज्ञां<BR> प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1.<BR>—10 It sometimes expresses ‘doubt’ or ‘uncertainty’, ‘fear’ (शङ्का);<BR> अपि चोरो भवेत् G. M. there is perhaps a thief.<BR>—11 (with pot. mood) It has the sense of संभावना ‘possibility’,<BR> ‘supposition’; P. I. 4. 96, III. 3. 154; अपि स्तुयाद्विष्णुम्, अपि स्तुयाद्राजानम्,<BR> अपि गिरिं शिरसा भिन्द्यात् Sk.; सोऽयमपि सिञ्चेत्सहस्रं द्राक्षाणां क्षणेनैकेन Dk. 127.<BR>—12 Contempt, censure, or reproof; P. I. 4. 96, III. 3. 142; धिग्देवदत्तमपि<BR> स्तुयाद् वृषलम्; धिग्जाल्मं देवदत्तमपि सिञ्चेत् पलाण्डुम्; अपि जायां त्यजसि<BR> जातु गणिकामाधत्से गर्हितमेतत् Sk. shame to &c. or fie upon, Devadatta &c.<BR>—13 It is also used with the Imperative mood to mark ‘indifference on the part of the speaker’<BR>, where he permits another to do as he likes, (अन्ववसर्ग<BR> or कामचारानुज्ञा, the imperative being softened); अपि स्तुहि Sk.<BR> you may praise (if you like); अपि स्तुह्यपि सेधाऽस्मांस्तथ्यमुक्तं नराशन Bk. 8. 92.<BR>—14 अपि is sometimes used as a particle of exclamation,<BR>—15 Rarely in the sense of ‘therefore’, ‘hence’ (अत एव).<BR>—16 Used as a separable preposition with gen. it is said to express the<BR> sense of a word understood (पदार्थ), and is treated as a कर्मप्रवचनीय<BR> P. I. 4. 96; the example usually given is सर्पिषोऽपि स्यात् where some<BR> word like बिन्दुरपि ‘a drop’, ‘a little’ &c. has to be understood,<BR> ‘there may perhaps be a drop of ghee’, ‘I presume there may be at least a drop’<BR> &c. अपि संभावनाप्रश्नशङ्कागर्हासमुच्चये । तथायुक्तपदार्थेषु<BR> कामचारक्रियासु च ॥ Viśva.; अपिः पदार्थसंभावनान्ववसर्गगर्हासमुच्चयेषु<BR> P. I. 4. 96; G. M. adds the senses of आशिस् ‘blessing’, (भद्रमपि),<BR> मृति ‘death’ (मरणमपि) and भूषा ‘decoration’ (अपि नह्यति<BR> हारं). cf. also<BR> … अपिः प्रश्नविरोधयोः । संभावनायां गर्हायां समुच्चयवितर्कयोः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकक्षः|अपिकक्ष
अपिकक्षः Ved. The region of the arm-pits and shoulder-blades, especially<BR> in animals. उत स्य वाजी क्षिपणिं तुरण्यति ग्रीवायां बद्धो अपिकक्ष<BR> आसनि Rv. 4. 40. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकक्षम्
अपिकक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@} <i>ind.</i> In the arm-pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकक्ष्य
अपिकक्ष्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to this region (Sāy. on Rv. I. 117. 22<BR> says ˚क्ष्यं छिन्नस्य यज्ञशिरसः कक्षप्रदेशेन सन्धानभूतं प्रवर्ग्यविद्याख्यं रहस्यम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकर्णम्
अपिकर्णम् The region of ears; near (समीप) ते अपिकर्ण आघृणे Rv. 6. 48, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिगीर्ण|अपिगीर्णं
अपिगीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praised, celebrated,<BR>—2 Told, described.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच्छिल|अपिच्छिलः
अपिच्छिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not muddy, clear, free from sediment.<BR>—2 Deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिज|अपिजः
अपिज <i>a.</i> Born after or again, epithet of several deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिजः|अपिज
अपिज + .{@-जः@} [अपि अप्सु जायते, अलुक् वेदे अप्शब्दस्यैकवचनत्वमपि]<BR> N. of the month of Jyeṣṭha (जलक्रीडारतिसाधनत्वात्तथात्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्
अपित् <i>a.</i> [आपः इतो गता यस्य, वेदे]<BR>—1 Dry, waterless, as a river.<BR>—2 Not having the इत् or अनुबन्ध प्. सार्वधातुकमपित् P. I. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितृक
अपितृक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fatherless.<BR>—2 Not ancestral or paternal, not inherited (अपैतृक also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्र्य
अपित्र्य <i>a.</i> Not ancestral. अविद्यानां तु सर्वेषामीहातश्चेद्धनं<BR> भवेत् । समस्तत्र विभागः स्यादपित्र्य इतिधारणा ॥ Ms. 9. 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्वम्
अपित्वम् Ved. [अपित्वरते अस्मै, त्वर् बा˚ ड] A part, portion, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्विन्
अपित्विन् <i>a.</i> Having a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधा
अपिधा €3 U. To shut, close, cover, conceal. चक्षूंष्याश्वपिधध्वं<BR> वो विधास्ये क्षेममञ्जसा Bhāg. 10. 30. 22;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधानम्
अपिधानम्, (also पिधानम्)<BR>—1 Covering, concealing, concealment.<BR>—2 A cover, lid, covering (fig. also); अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा; नैकजलदच्छत्रापिधानं<BR> जगत् Mk. 5. 24; a cloth for covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधानम्
अपिधानम्, (also पिधानम्)<BR>—1 Covering, concealing, concealment.<BR>—2 A cover, lid, covering (fig. also); अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा; नैकजलदच्छत्रापिधानं<BR> जगत् Mk. 5. 24; a cloth for covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधिः|अपिधि
अपिधिः <i>f.</i> Concealment, covering;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधिः|अपिधि
अपिधिः + .{@-धिः@} What is given to anotherʼs entire satisfaction तृप्तिपर्यन्तदत्त.<BR> प्रियाँ अपिधीँर्वनिषीष्ट मेधिर Rv. 1. 127. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिहित
अपिहित, -पिहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shut, closed, covered, concealed (fig. also); बाष्पापिहित covered with tears.<BR>—2 Not concealed, plain, clear; अर्थो गिरामपिहितः पिहितश्च किंचित्,<BR> सत्यं चकास्ति मरहट्टवधूस्तनाभः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिहित
अपिहित, -पिहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shut, closed, covered, concealed (fig. also); बाष्पापिहित covered with tears.<BR>—2 Not concealed, plain, clear; अर्थो गिरामपिहितः पिहितश्च किंचित्,<BR> सत्यं चकास्ति मरहट्टवधूस्तनाभः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिहितम्
अपिहित, -पिहित + .{@-तम्@} <i>adv.</i> Visibly, openly; भुजङ्गवृन्दापिहितात्तवातम् Bu. C. I. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिनद्ध|अपिनद्धं
अपिनद्ध <i>a.</i> Closed, concealed; अश्नापिनद्धं मधु पर्यपश्यन् Rv. 10. 68. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिपरिक्लिष्ट
अपिपरिक्लिष्ट <i>a.</i> Excessively harassed अपि चापिपरिक्लिष्टं<BR> चिराद्दारैः समागतम् । आत्मकार्यगरीयस्त्वाद्वक्तुं नेच्छामि वानरम् ॥<BR> Rām. 4. 28. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिप्राण
अपिप्राण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Always animating or vivifying (सर्वदा चेष्टमान)<BR> अपिप्राणी च सदनी च भूयाः Rv. 1. 186. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिभाग
अपिभाग <i>a.</i> Ved. Sharing or partaking in, having a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिव्रत
अपिव्रत <i>a.</i> Sharing in the same religious acts or other works;<BR> connected by blood; अपिव्रताश्चान्वारभन्ते यजमानम् Kāty. (संसृष्टं<BR> साधारणकर्म येषां ते अपिव्रताः अविभक्ता दायादाः, ते हि एकेनापि कृष्यादिकर्म<BR> कृतं सर्वे उपजीवन्ति Com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशर्वर|अपिशर्व्वर
अपिशर्वर <i>a.</i> Ved. Close to the night, being at the beginning<BR> (or end) of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशर्वरम्
अपिशर्वर + .{@-रम्@} Early or untimely morning, evening (or morning) time (प्रदोषमुखम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशलाः
अपिशलाः (pl. of आपिशल)^1 descendants or pupils of आपिशलि.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशस्
अपिशस् <i>a.</i> Ripping up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिस्वित्
अपिस्वित् <i>ind.</i> Interrogative; अपिस्वित्पर्यभुङ्क्थास्त्वं सम्भोज्यान्वृद्धबालकान्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 14. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपी
अपी [अपि-इ] €2 P. (Mostly Vedic)<BR>—1 To go in or near, enter into or upon, approach.<BR>—2 To have a share in, partake of, suffer; जरामृत्युं पुनरेवापियन्ति<BR> Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 7.<BR>—3 To join, flow, flow into, dissolve, be resolved into; स्वमपीतो भवति<BR> तस्मादेनं स्वपितीत्याचक्षते Ch. Up.<BR>—4 To die.<BR>—5 To pour out (as a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीत|अपीतः
अपीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gone into, entered; Śat. Br. 10.<BR>—2 Lost; लोकानपीतान्ददृशे स्वदेहे Bhāg. 3. 8. 12.<BR>—3 Dead; कंसः सहानुगोऽपीतो Bhāg. 10. 57. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीतिः|अपीति
अपीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Entering into, approaching. पुरा यत् सूरस्तमसो अपीते Rv. 1. 121. 10.<BR>—2 Dissolution, destruction, loss.<BR>—3 Destruction of the world (प्रलय); अपीतौ तद्वत् प्रसङ्गादसमञ्जसम्<BR> Br. Sūt. 2. 1. 8.<BR>—4 Encountering, joining in battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्ययः|अप्यय
अप्ययः<BR>—1 Approaching, meeting, joining, juncture.<BR>—2 Pouring out (of rivers).<BR>—3 Entrance into, vanishing, disappearance; absorption, dissolution into<BR> oneself, destruction; सर्गस्थित्यप्ययेशस्य गुणकर्मानुवर्णनम् Bhāg. 7. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्ययनम्
अप्ययनम्<BR>—1 Union, junction.<BR>—2 Copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीच्य
अपीच्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very handsome or beautiful (अतिसुन्दर) अपीच्यदर्शनं श्यामं<BR> तडिद्वाससमच्युतम् Bhāg. 1. 12. 8.<BR>—2 Secret, concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीजु
अपीजु <i>a.</i> Ved. Impelling, stirring up. (MW. अपीजू) उषासानक्ता<BR> जगतामपीजुवा Rv. 2. 31. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीनसः|अपीनस|अपीनसं
अपीनसः [अपीनाय, अपीनत्वाय सीयते कल्पते कर्मकर्तरि क<BR> Tv.] Dryness of the nose; cold (in the head), rheum, catarrh; see पीनस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीव्य|अपीव्यं
अपीव्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Very handsome; अपीव्यदर्शनं शश्वत् सर्वलोकनमस्कृतम्<BR> Bhāg. See अपीच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्
अपुंस् <i>m.</i> (˚पुमान्) Not a man, a eunuch; पुमान्पुंसोऽधिके<BR> शुक्रे स्त्री भवत्यधिके स्त्रियाः । समेऽपुमान्पुंस्त्रियौ वा क्षीणेऽल्पे च विपर्ययः ॥<BR> Ms. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुमान्
अपुंस् <i>m.</i> (˚पुमान्) Not a man, a eunuch; पुमान्पुंसोऽधिके<BR> शुक्रे स्त्री भवत्यधिके स्त्रियाः । समेऽपुमान्पुंस्त्रियौ वा क्षीणेऽल्पे च विपर्ययः ॥<BR> Ms. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्त्वम्
अपुंस्त्वम् The state of a eunuch, impotent state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्का
अपुंस्का <i>f.</i> A woman without a husband; नापुंस्कासीति मे मतिः Bk. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुच्छ
अपुच्छ <i>a.</i> Without tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुच्छा
अपुच्छ + .{@-च्छा@} N. of a tree (Mar. शीसु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्य
अपुण्य <i>a.</i> Not virtuous or holy, wicked, bad; ˚कृत् one who<BR> does not perform meritorious deeds, or who commits unrighteous deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रः|अपुत्र
अपुत्रः Not a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रकः|अपुत्रक
अपुत्रः + .{@-पुत्रकः@} <i>a.</i> (˚त्रिका <i>f.</i>) Having no son or heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रिका
अपुत्रिका The daughter of a sonless father, who herself has no male<BR> child; one who is not appointed by her father to beget male issue for<BR> him on failure of a son; cf. अकृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रिकः|अपुत्रिक
अपुत्रिका + .{@-कः@} The father of such a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनर्
अपुनर् <i>ind.</i> Not again, once for all, forever.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपुनरन्वय, अपुनरादानम्, अपुनरावृत्तिः, अपुनःप्राप्य, अपुनर्भवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनरन्वय
अपुनर् + -अन्वय <i>a.</i> not returning; dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनरादानम्
अपुनर् + -आदानम् not taking back or again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनरावृत्तिः|अपुनरावृत्ति
अपुनर् + -आवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 ‘non-return’, exemption of the soul from further transmigration, final beatitude.<BR>—2 Death; नयाम्यपुनरावृत्तिं यदि तिष्ठेर्ममाग्रतः Bhāg. 10. 77. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनःप्राप्य
अपुनर् + -प्राप्य <i>a.</i> irrecoverable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनर्भवः|अपुनर्भव
अपुनर् + -भवः<BR>—1 not being born again (of diseases also).<BR>—2 final beatitude; तुलयाम लवेनापि न स्वर्गं नापुनर्भवम् Bhāg. 1. 18. 13.<BR>—3 knowledge of the Supreme Soul which tends to this step.<BR>—4 a person released from metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुराण
अपुराण <i>a.</i> Not old; modern, new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुरुष
अपुरुष <i>a.</i> Not manlike, unmanly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपुरुषार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुरुषार्थ
अपुरुष + -अर्थ<BR>—1 a rite or ceremony which is not in the interests of the doer.<BR>—2 not the principal object of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्कल
अपुष्कल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not much.<BR>—2 Mean, low, base. Ve. 4; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्ट
अपुष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not nourished or fed, lean, not fat.<BR>—2 Not loud or violent, soft, low (as sound).<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Not feeding or assisting (the meaning), irrelevant (मुख्यानुपकारिन्),<BR> regarded as one of the <i>arthadoṣas</i> (faults of the sense or meaning);<BR> as in the instance given under S. D. 576 विलोक्य वितते व्योम्नि विधुं<BR> मुञ्च रुषं प्रिये, the adjective वितत ‘expanded’, as applied,<BR> to the sky, does not in any way help the cessation of anger and is, therefore, irrelevant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्प|अपुष्पः
अपुष्प <i>a.</i> Flowerless, not flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पः|अपुष्प
अपुष्प + .{@-ष्पः@} The glomerous fig-tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपुष्पफल, अपुष्पफलद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफल|अपुष्पफलः
अपुष्प + -फल, -फलद bearing having neither fruits nor flowers; fruits without flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफलद|अपुष्पफलदः
अपुष्प + -फल, -फलद bearing having neither fruits nor flowers; fruits without flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफलः|अपुष्पफल
अपुष्प + -फल, -फलद + .({@-लः, -दः@})<BR>—1 the jack tree (Mar. फणस). Artocarpus Integrifolia.<BR>—2 the glomerous fig-tree (उदुम्बर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफलदः|अपुष्पफलद
अपुष्प + -फल, -फलद + .({@-लः, -दः@})<BR>—1 the jack tree (Mar. फणस). Artocarpus Integrifolia.<BR>—2 the glomerous fig-tree (उदुम्बर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुस्
अपुस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Shape, body = वपुस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजक
अपूजक <i>a.</i> Irreligious, irreverent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजा
अपूजा Disrespect, irreverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपः|अपूप
अपूपः [न पूयते विशीर्यते, पू-प. न˚ त˚ Tv.]<BR>—1 A small round cake of flour, meal &c. (Mar. वडा, घारगा, अनरसा<BR> &c.), thicker than ordinary cakes and mixed with sugar and spices; कृसरसंयावं<BR> पायसापूपमेव Ms. 5. 7.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">Page0157-2</a>]<BR> भीमेनातिबलेन मत्स्यभवनेऽपूपा न संघट्टिताः Pt. 3. 172; अपूपं गुरवे<BR> तं च सामृतं स न्यवेदयत् । Bm. 1. 38.<BR>—2 Wheat.<BR>—3 Honeycomb. आदित्यो देवमंधु … अन्तरिक्षमपूपो Ch. Up. 3. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपशाला
अपूपः + .{@-शाला@} a Sweetmeat shop; सभाप्रपापूपशाला Ms. 9. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपीय
अपूपीय, -अपूप्य<BR> [अपूपाय हितं, छ यत् च] Belonging to, intended for, अपूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप्य|अपूप्यः
अपूपीय, -अपूप्य<BR> [अपूपाय हितं, छ यत् च] Belonging to, intended for, अपूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप्यम्
अपूपीय, -अपूप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} Flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरणी
अपूरणी The silk cotton tree (शाल्मली). Bombax. Heptaphyllum<BR> (Mar. सांवरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरुष
अपूरुष<BR>—1 Lifeless, inanimate (as wood &c.) अदो यद् दारु प्लवते सिन्धोः पारे<BR> अपूरुषम् Rv. 10. 155. 3<BR>—2 Soulless.<BR>—3 Unpeopled, untenanted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ण
अपूर्ण <i>a.</i> Not full or completed, incomplete, deficient, imperfect;<BR> अपूर्णमेकेन शतक्रतूनाम् R. 3. 38; अपूर्ण एव पञ्चरात्रे दोहदस्य M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णम्
अपूर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} Incomplete number or fraction.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपूर्णकाल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकाल|अपूर्णकालः
अपूर्ण + -काल <i>a.</i> premature, untimely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकालः|अपूर्णकाल
अपूर्ण + -काल + .({@-लः@}) premature or incomplete time; ˚ज abortive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्तिः|अपूर्ति
अपूर्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व|अपूर्वः|अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व्वं
अपूर्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not preceded, not having existed before, like of which did not exist<BR> before, quite new; ˚र्वं नाटकम् Ś. 1; ˚र्वं राजकुलम् M. 5; K. 191;<BR>—2 Strange, extraordinary, wonderful; अपूर्वः कोऽपि बहुमानहेतुर्गुरुषु<BR> U. 4; अपूर्वो दृश्यते वह्निः कामिन्याः स्तनमण्डले । दूरतो दहतीवाङ्गं<BR> हृदि लग्नस्तु शीतलः ॥ Ś. Til. 17; singular, unexampled, unprecedented;<BR> अपूर्व एष विरहमार्गः Ś. 6; अपूर्वरूपा दारिका M. 1; अतोऽपूर्वः<BR> खलु वो ऽनुग्रहः Ś. 7; अपूर्वकर्मचाण्डालमयि मुग्धे विमुञ्च माम्<BR> U. 1. 46 committing an unparalleled atrocity.<BR>—3 Unknown, unacquainted, stranger; अपूर्वोऽप्यथवा विद्वान् Mb. 13. 22. 8;<BR> विदितेऽप्यपूर्व इव Ki. 6. 39.<BR>—4 Not first.<BR>—5 Preceded by अ or आ.<BR>—6 (In phil.) ‘That unseen virtue which is a relation superinduced, not before possessed, unseen but efficacious to connect the consequence with its past and remote cause and to bring about at a distant period or in another world the relative effect’<BR>. -Colebrooke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वम्
अपूर्व + .{@-र्वम्@}<BR>—1 The remote consequence of an act (as the acquisition of heaven which<BR> is the result of good deeds), (Mīmāṃsā).<BR>—2 Virtue and vice (पापपुण्यम्) as the eventual cause of future happiness or misery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वः|अपूर्व|अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व्वं
अपूर्व + .{@-र्वः@} The Supreme Soul (परब्रह्म).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपूर्वकर्मन्, अपूर्वपतिः, अपूर्ववादः, अपूर्वविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वकर्मन्
अपूर्व + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> religious rites the power of which on the future<BR> is not seen before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वपतिः|अपूर्वपति|अपूर्व्वपति
अपूर्व + -पतिः <i>f.</i> one who has had no husband before, a virgin; ˚तिः कुमारी Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ववादः|अपूर्ववाद|अपूर्व्ववाद
अपूर्व + -वादः discussion or talk about the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वविधिः|अपूर्वविधि|अपूर्व्वविधि
अपूर्व + -विधिः an authoritative direction or injunction which is quite<BR> new; it is of four kinds; कर्मविधि, गुणविधि, विनियोगविधि and प्रयोगविधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वता|अपूर्व्वता
अपूर्वता, -त्वम्<BR> Not having existed before, incomparableness, unparalleled<BR> or extraordinary nature; अपूर्वत्वात्प्रबन्धस्य Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वत्वम्
अपूर्वता, -त्वम्<BR> Not having existed before, incomparableness, unparalleled<BR> or extraordinary nature; अपूर्वत्वात्प्रबन्धस्य Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ववत्|अपूर्व्ववत्
अपूर्ववत् <i>ind.</i> Singularly, unlike anything else; दृष्टोऽपि<BR> शैलः स मुहुर्मुरारेरपूर्ववद्विस्मयमाततान Śi. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0157-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्विन्
अपूर्विन् <i>a.</i> Having not enjoyed the married life with a wife before.<BR> अपूर्वी भार्यया चार्थी तरुणः^1 Rām. 3. 18. 4.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वीय
अपूर्वीय <i>a.</i> Relating to the remote consequence of an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वेण
अपूर्वेण <i>adv.</i> Never before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्य|अपूर्व्व्य
अपूर्व्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unpreceded, first.<BR>—2 Incomparable, unheard of before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृक्त|अपृक्तः
अपृक्त <i>a.</i> Not united, uncombined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृक्तः|अपृक्त
अपृक्त + .{@-क्तः@}<BR>—1 (In gram.) An affix (or a word) consisting of a single letter; अपृक्त<BR> एकाल्प्रत्ययः P. I. 2. 41; एकवर्णपदमपृक्तम् Sk.<BR>—2 (In the Prātiśākhyas) The preposition आ and the particle उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृणत्|अपृणन्त्
अपृणत् <i>a.</i> Not filling; stingy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथक्
अपृथक् <i>ind.</i> Not separately, together with, collectively.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपृथग्धर्मशील, अपृथग्धी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथग्धर्मशील|अपृथग्धर्म्मशील
अपृथक् + -धर्मशील of the same religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथग्धी
अपृथक् + -धी <i>a.</i> maintaining the doctrine of pantheism; regarding God in all things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथक्त्विन्
अपृथक्त्विन् <i>a.</i> One who cannot distinguish (between the पुरुष<BR> and the प्रकृति). वर्णाश्रमपृथक्त्वे च दृष्टार्थस्यापृथक्त्विनः ।<BR> नान्यदन्यदिति ज्ञात्वा नान्यदन्यत्प्रवर्तते ॥ Mb. 12. 308. 177 Critical<BR> Edition. ‘पृथक्त्वं पुंप्रकृत्योर्विवेकः, तदस्यास्तीति पृथक्त्वी, तदन्यस्य’ -नीलकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपे
अपे [अप-इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To go away, depart, withdraw, retire, run away, escape; {@अपोहि@}<BR> begone, avaunt, away, hence, get you gone; to disappear, vanish, pass<BR> away; die or perish also; धर्मश्चापैति Ms. 1. 82; हृदयात्प्रत्यादेशव्यलीकमपैतु<BR> ते Ś. 7. 24; रम्या नवद्युतिरपैति न शाद्वलेभ्यः Ki. 5. 37 does not leave.<BR>—2 To be wanting, be omitted, be deprived of, be free from.<BR>—3 To start (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायः|अपाय
अपायः [इ-अच्]<BR>—1 Going away, departure.<BR>—2 Separation; ध्रुवमपायेऽपादानम् P. I. 4. 24 (अपायो विश्लेषः<BR> Sk.); येन जातं प्रियापाये कद्वदं हंसकोकिलम् Bk. 6. 75.<BR>—3 Disappearance, vanishing, absence; सूर्यापाये Me. 82 at the time<BR> of sunset; क्षणदापायशशाङ्कदर्शनः R. 8. 74 close of night; जलापायविपाण्डुराणि<BR> Śi. 4. 5, 4. 54, 18. 1.<BR>—4 Destruction, loss, death, annihilation; करणापायविभिन्नवर्णया<BR> R. 8. 42 loss, 83; मालत्यपायमधिगम्य Māl. 10. 9 death or disappearance of M.<BR>—5 An evil, ill, misfortune, risk, calamity, danger (oft. opp. उपाय);<BR> तदपि मरणापायचकितः Bh. 3. 9; तदनेन पापबुद्धिनोपायश्चिन्तितो<BR> नापायः Pt. 1 not the danger (resulting from the plan); उपायं चिन्तयेत्प्राज्ञस्तथापायं<BR> च चिन्तयेत् Pt. 1. 406; अपायसंदर्शनजां विपत्तिमुपायसंदर्शनजां<BR> च सिद्धिम् 1. 61; बह्वपाये वने Pt. 1 exposed to many dangers, dangerous;<BR> कायः संनिहितापायः H. 4. 65 exposed to dangers or calamities; सत्येऽप्यपायमपेक्षते<BR> H. 4. 102; Ki. 14. 19.<BR>—6 Loss, detriment, injury.<BR>—7 The end (of a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपायिन् <i>a.</i> Departing, transient; perishable; see अनपायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेत
अपेत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone away, disappeared; अपेतयुद्धाभिनिवेशसौम्यः Śi. 3. 1.<BR>—2 Departing or deviating from, swerving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">Page0158-2</a>]<BR> from, contrary (with abl.); अर्थादनपेतमर्थ्यम्^1 P. IV. 4. 92. Sk.<BR> (धर्मपथ्यर्थन्यायादनपेते); स्मृत्यपेतादिकारिणः Y. 2. 4.<BR>—3 Free from, devoid of, deprived of (with abl. or in comp.); सुखादपेतः<BR> Sk.; उदवहदनवद्यां तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70 faultless; ˚भीः<BR> Ms. 7. 197; भर्तर्यपेततमसि प्रभुता तवैव Ś. 7. 32 free from<BR> (mental) darkness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपेतराक्षसी<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेतराक्षसी
अपेत + -राक्षसी N. of a plant, Ocimum Sanctum (तुलसी) (अस्याः राक्षसतुल्यपापादिहरणात्तन्नामत्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्
अपेक्ष् [अप्-ईक्ष्] €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To look round or about for something, to look or hope for, expect.<BR>—2 To wait for, await; सज्जो रथो भर्तुर्विजयप्रस्थानमपेक्षते Ś. 2<BR> awaits; क्षणमपेक्षस्व U. 7; K. 84; न कालमपेक्षते स्नेहः<BR> Mk. 7. न स्वयं दैवमादत्ते पुरुषार्थमपेक्षते H. Pr. 30; पादेन<BR> नापैक्षत सुन्दरीणां संपर्कमासिञ्जितनूपुरेण Ku. 3. 26.<BR>—3 To require, want, stand in need of; wish or desire for; शब्दार्थौ<BR> सत्कविरिव द्वयं विद्वानपेक्षते Śi. 2. 86; न शालेः स्तम्बकरिता<BR> वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3; प्रभुता रमणेषु योषितां न हि भावस्खलितान्यपेक्षते<BR> V. 4. 26; Ku. 3. 18; Pt. 2. 26.<BR>—4 To have regard to, look to, have in view, have an eye to; किमपेक्ष्य<BR> फलं पयोधरान् ध्वनतः प्रार्थयते मृगाधिपः Ki. 2. 21; यतः शब्दोऽयं<BR> व्यञ्जकत्वेऽर्थान्तरमपेक्षते S. D.<BR>—5 To take into account or consideration, consider, think of, respect,<BR> care for; उपकृतमपि नापेक्षते K. 35, 197, 257, 315; नूनमस्यायमनपेक्षितास्मदवस्थो<BR> व्यापारः Māl. 9; अनलेष्विष्टवान् कस्मान्न त्वयाऽपेक्षितः पिता Bk. 6. 128;<BR> Ś. 5. 16; Ms. 8. 309; with न not to like, not to care for;<BR> अनपेक्षितराजराजम् Mu. 3. 18; तदानपेक्ष्य स्वशरीरमार्दवम् Ku. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षा
अपेक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR>—1 Expectation, hope, desire.<BR>—2 Need, requirement, necessity; निरपेक्ष without hope or need, regardless<BR> of; निर्विशङ्का निरुद्विग्ना निरपेक्षा च भैथिली Rām. 6. 47. 9. द्रोणस्तथोक्तः<BR> कर्णेन सापेक्षः फाल्गुनं प्रति (उवाच) Mb. 12. 2. 12. सापेक्षत्वेऽपि<BR> गमकत्वात्सभासः; अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्षः Bg. 12. 16; or in comp.; स्फुलिङ्गावस्थया<BR> वह्निरेधापेक्ष इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15 awaiting kindling.<BR>—3 Consideration, reference, regard, with the obj. in loc. case; more<BR> usually in comp.; मध्यभङ्गानपेक्षम् Ratn. 1. 15 regardless of; the<BR> instr. and sometimes loc. of this word frequently occur in comp. meaning<BR> ‘with reference to’, ‘out of regard for’, ‘with a view to’, ‘for the sake of’<BR>; साऽपि कार्यकरणापेक्षया क्षुरमेकमादाय तस्याभिमुखं प्रेषयामास<BR> Pt. 1; नियमापेक्षया R. 1. 94; वृषलापेक्षया Mu. 1; पौरजनापेक्षया 2<BR> ‘out of regard for’ किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षया 3 with a view<BR> to gain some object; प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया Me. 17; दण्डं शक्त्यपेक्षम्<BR> Y. 2. 26, in proportion to, in accordance with; अत्र व्यङ्ग्यं गुणीभूतं<BR> तदपेक्षया वाच्यस्यैव चमत्कारिकत्वात् K. P. 1 as compared with it.<BR>—4 Connection, relation, dependence as of cause with effect or of individual<BR> with species; शरीरसाधनापेक्षं नित्यं यत्कर्म तद्यमः Ak.<BR>—5 Care, attention, heed; देशाऽपेक्षास्तथा यूयं यातादायाङ्गुलीयकम् Bk. 7. 49.<BR>—6 respect, reference.<BR>—7 (In gram.) = आकाङ्क्षा q. v.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपेक्षाबुद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणम्
अपेक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR>—1 Expectation, hope, desire.<BR>—2 Need, requirement, necessity; निरपेक्ष without hope or need, regardless<BR> of; निर्विशङ्का निरुद्विग्ना निरपेक्षा च भैथिली Rām. 6. 47. 9. द्रोणस्तथोक्तः<BR> कर्णेन सापेक्षः फाल्गुनं प्रति (उवाच) Mb. 12. 2. 12. सापेक्षत्वेऽपि<BR> गमकत्वात्सभासः; अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्षः Bg. 12. 16; or in comp.; स्फुलिङ्गावस्थया<BR> वह्निरेधापेक्ष इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15 awaiting kindling.<BR>—3 Consideration, reference, regard, with the obj. in loc. case; more<BR> usually in comp.; मध्यभङ्गानपेक्षम् Ratn. 1. 15 regardless of; the<BR> instr. and sometimes loc. of this word frequently occur in comp. meaning<BR> ‘with reference to’, ‘out of regard for’, ‘with a view to’, ‘for the sake of’<BR>; साऽपि कार्यकरणापेक्षया क्षुरमेकमादाय तस्याभिमुखं प्रेषयामास<BR> Pt. 1; नियमापेक्षया R. 1. 94; वृषलापेक्षया Mu. 1; पौरजनापेक्षया 2<BR> ‘out of regard for’ किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षया 3 with a view<BR> to gain some object; प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया Me. 17; दण्डं शक्त्यपेक्षम्<BR> Y. 2. 26, in proportion to, in accordance with; अत्र व्यङ्ग्यं गुणीभूतं<BR> तदपेक्षया वाच्यस्यैव चमत्कारिकत्वात् K. P. 1 as compared with it.<BR>—4 Connection, relation, dependence as of cause with effect or of individual<BR> with species; शरीरसाधनापेक्षं नित्यं यत्कर्म तद्यमः Ak.<BR>—5 Care, attention, heed; देशाऽपेक्षास्तथा यूयं यातादायाङ्गुलीयकम् Bk. 7. 49.<BR>—6 respect, reference.<BR>—7 (In gram.) = आकाङ्क्षा q. v.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपेक्षाबुद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षाबुद्धिः|अपेक्षाबुद्धि
अपेक्षा + -बुद्धिः (In Vaiśeṣika Phil.) the distinguishing perception by<BR> which we apprehend ‘this is one’, ‘this is one’ &c. and which gives rise<BR> to the notion of duality; see Sarva. S. chap. 10 where अपेक्षाबुद्धिः = विनाशकविनाशप्रति-योगिनी बुद्धिः;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">Page0159-1</a>]<BR> cf. Bhāṣā P. द्वित्वादयः परार्धान्ता अपेक्षाबुद्धिजा मताः । अनेकाश्रयपर्याप्ता<BR> एते तु परिकीर्तिताः ॥ अपेक्षाबुद्धिनाशाच्च नाशस्तेषां निरूपितः । 107-8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0158-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्य
अपेक्ष्य, -क्षितव्य, -क्षणीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR> expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितव्य
अपेक्ष्य, -क्षितव्य, -क्षणीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR> expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणीय|अपेक्षणीयं
अपेक्ष्य, -क्षितव्य, -क्षणीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR> expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षित
अपेक्षित <i>p. p.</i> Looked for, expected; wanted, desired, required;<BR> considered, referred to &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितम्
अपेक्षित + .{@-तम्@} Desire, wish; regard, reference, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षिन्
अपेक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Hoping, waiting for, wishing or desiring for, wanting;<BR> considering, caring; usually as last member of comp.; गुरुर्विधिबलापेक्षी<BR> R. 15. 85; प्रयोजनापेक्षितया Ku. 3. 1 according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेय|अपेयं
अपेय <i>a.</i> Not fit to be drunk; अपेयेषु तडागेषु बहुतरमुदकं<BR> भवति Mk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेहि
अपेहि (Imper. 2nd sing.) Used as the first member of some compounds<BR> (belonging to the class मयूरव्यंसकादि P. II. 1. 72); ˚कटा^1,<BR> ˚द्वितीया, ˚प्रघसा^2, ˚वाणिजा, ˚स्वागता where it has the sense of ‘excluding’,<BR> ‘expelling’, ‘refusing admission to’; <i>e. g.</i> ˚वाणिजा a ceremony<BR> where merchants are excluded; so ˚द्वितीया &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अपेहिवाता<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: cf. pwg.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेहिवाता
अपेहि + -वाता N. of a plant which expels wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्डः|अपोगण्ड|अपोगंडः
अपोगण्डः, -अपौगण्ड<BR> [अ-पोगण्डः, or अपसि (वैध) कर्मणि<BR> गण्डः त्याज्यः Tv.]<BR>—1 Having a limb too many or too few (redundant or deficient).<BR>—2 Not under 16 years of age; बाल आषोडशाद्वर्षात्पोगण्डश्चापि संज्ञितः ।<BR> Nārada; अजडश्चेदपौगण्डो विषये चास्य भुज्यते । Ms. 8. 148;<BR> पोगण्डः पञ्चमादब्दादर्वाक् च दशमाब्दतः ।<BR>—3 A child or infant (किशोर, शिशु).<BR>—4 Very timid;<BR>—5 Wrinkled, flaccid.<BR>—6 One past 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौगण्ड
अपोगण्डः, -अपौगण्ड<BR> [अ-पोगण्डः, or अपसि (वैध) कर्मणि<BR> गण्डः त्याज्यः Tv.]<BR>—1 Having a limb too many or too few (redundant or deficient).<BR>—2 Not under 16 years of age; बाल आषोडशाद्वर्षात्पोगण्डश्चापि संज्ञितः ।<BR> Nārada; अजडश्चेदपौगण्डो विषये चास्य भुज्यते । Ms. 8. 148;<BR> पोगण्डः पञ्चमादब्दादर्वाक् च दशमाब्दतः ।<BR>—3 A child or infant (किशोर, शिशु).<BR>—4 Very timid;<BR>—5 Wrinkled, flaccid.<BR>—6 One past 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ see under अप-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदक
अपोदक <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Waterless; water-tight (नौः Rv. 1. 116. 3.).<BR>—2 Not watery, not fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदकम्
अपोदक + .{@-कम्@} [अपकृष्टमुदकं यस्मात्] Poison &c. that removes water<BR> (जलापकर्षहेतु विषादि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिका
अपोदिका, -की^1 <i>f.</i><BR> A sort of pot-herb (अपनद्धमुदकं यस्याः, तत्फलेषूदकवत्त्यात्तथात्वम्).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिकी
अपोदिका, -की^1 <i>f.</i><BR> A sort of pot-herb (अपनद्धमुदकं यस्याः, तत्फलेषूदकवत्त्यात्तथात्वम्).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिकी
अपोदिका, -की + .{@-की@} see उपोदकी. Bassella Lucida or Rubra (Mar. थोरमयाळ)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्
अपोह् €1 U.<BR> [अप-उह् or ऊह्] —1 To remove, drive or push away, dispel, take<BR> away, destroy; स हि विघ्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; कुसुमानि … प्रभवन्त्यायुरपोहितुं<BR> यदि R. 8. 44, 54; पूर्वमुत्सवमपौहदुत्सवः (उत्तरः) 19. 5<BR> pushed away, displaced, supplanted; मनसिजरुजं सा वा दिव्या ममालमपोहितुम्<BR> V. 3. 10; अकिञ्चिदपि कुर्वाणः सौख्यैर्दुःखान्यपोहति U. 2. 19 Removes;<BR> Bk. 17. 83, 15. 119; Ms. 8. 414, 11. 108; कल्पनाया अपोढः कल्पनापोढः<BR> P. II. 1. 38. Sk. removed from, or beyond imagination<BR>—2 To heal, cure (as illness).<BR>—3 To avoid, give up, leave; सर्वान् रसानपोहेत Ms. 10. 86; पञ्चवट्यां<BR> ततो रामः … अनपोढस्थितिस्तस्थौ R. 12. 31 not leaving (the path of) propriety.<BR>—4 To deny; स्थाप्यतेऽपोह्यते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">Page0159-2</a>]<BR> वा चेत् S. D. 730.<BR>—5 To reason, argue by way of opposing a statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहः|अपोह
अपोहः<BR>—1 Removing, driving away, healing &c.<BR>—2 Removal of doubt by the excercise of the reasoning faculty.<BR>—3 Reasoning, arguing; reasoning faculty.<BR>—4 Negative reasoning (opp. ऊह) (अपरतर्कनिरासाय कृतो विपरीतस्तर्कः),<BR> one of the <i>dhīguṇas</i> q. v. स्वयमूहापोहासमर्थः; इमे मनुष्या दृश्यन्ते<BR> ऊहापोहविशारदाः Mb. 13. 145. 43. ऊहापोहमिमं सरोजनयना यावद्विधत्तेतराम्<BR> Bv. 2. 74; hence ऊहापोह = complete discussion of a question.<BR>—5 Excluding all things not coming under the category in point; तद्वानपोहो<BR> वा शब्दार्थः (where Maheśvara paraphrases अपोह by अतद्व्यावृत्ति<BR> <i>i. e.</i> तद्भिन्नत्यागः),<BR>—6 A superfluous member attached to a structure of some construction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहनम्
अपोहनम्<BR>—1 Removal &c. = अपोह above.<BR>—2 Reasoning faculty; मत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च Bg. 15. 15<BR> (Mr. Telang translates अ˚ by removal; Lok. Tilak translates as नाश.)<BR> ततो धर्मस्ततो ज्ञानं यावत्स्मृतिरपोहनम् Bhāg. 11. 13. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहित
अपोहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Removed; न च सामर्थ्यमपोहितं क्वचित् Ki. 2. 27.<BR>—2 Denied (in disputation, opp. to स्थापित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्य
अपोह्य, -अपोहनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be removed, taken away; मृत्युर्बुद्धिमतापोह्यो<BR> यावद् बुद्धिबलोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 1. 48 expiated (as sin); to be established by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहनीय
अपोह्य, -अपोहनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be removed, taken away; मृत्युर्बुद्धिमतापोह्यो<BR> यावद् बुद्धिबलोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 1. 48 expiated (as sin); to be established by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुष
अपौरुष, -पौरुषेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unmanly, cowardly, timid.<BR>—2 Superhuman, not of the authorship of man, of divine origin; अपौरुषेया<BR> वेदाः; अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठः सुवर्णबिन्दुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9 not set<BR> up by (the hand of) man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुषेय
अपौरुष, -पौरुषेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unmanly, cowardly, timid.<BR>—2 Superhuman, not of the authorship of man, of divine origin; अपौरुषेया<BR> वेदाः; अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठः सुवर्णबिन्दुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9 not set<BR> up by (the hand of) man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुषम्
अपौरुष, -पौरुषेय + .{@-षम्, -षेयम्@}<BR>—1 Cowardice, pusillanimity.<BR>—2 Superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुषेयम्
अपौरुष, -पौरुषेय + .{@-षम्, -षेयम्@}<BR>—1 Cowardice, pusillanimity.<BR>—2 Superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्त|अप्तः
अप्त <i>a.</i> Ved. Obtained; watery; cf. Rv. 9. 16. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तस्
अप्तस् <i>n.</i> A sacrificial act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु <i>a.</i> Ved. Busy, active, industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तुः|अप्तु
अप्तु + .{@-प्तुः@} (or <i>n.</i> Uṇ. 1. 74)<BR>—1 The body.<BR>—2 Soma (सूक्ष्मरूपसोम).<BR>—3 A sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तुर्
अप्तुर् <i>m.</i> [अद्भ्यः जलदानाय तुतोर्ति, जलानि प्रेरयति, तुर् क्विप् Tv.]<BR>—1 Active, busy, giving water, flowing as water; an epithet of Indra (Sāy.<BR> अपां प्रेरक इन्द्रः).<BR>—2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु, -प्तू -र्यम्<BR> [अप्तुरो भावः बाहु˚ वेदे यत्] Sending down water<BR> (वृष्टिप्रेरकत्वम्), giving of water; zeal, activity युवोरप्तूर्यं<BR> हितम् Rv. 3. 12. 8, 51. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तू
अप्तु, -प्तू -र्यम्<BR> [अप्तुरो भावः बाहु˚ वेदे यत्] Sending down water<BR> (वृष्टिप्रेरकत्वम्), giving of water; zeal, activity युवोरप्तूर्यं<BR> हितम् Rv. 3. 12. 8, 51. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तूर्यम्
अप्तु, -प्तू -र्यम्<BR> [अप्तुरो भावः बाहु˚ वेदे यत्] Sending down water<BR> (वृष्टिप्रेरकत्वम्), giving of water; zeal, activity युवोरप्तूर्यं<BR> हितम् Rv. 3. 12. 8, 51. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तोर्यामः|अप्तोर्याम
अप्तोर्यामः, -मन् <i>m.</i><BR> N. of a sacrifice and of a verse of the Sāma Veda<BR> closing that rite; the last or 7th part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तोर्यामन्
अप्तोर्यामः, -मन् <i>m.</i><BR> N. of a sacrifice and of a verse of the Sāma Veda<BR> closing that rite; the last or 7th part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्त्य
अप्त्य <i>a.</i> [अप्तुनि देहे भवः यत् वेदे टिलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 Engaged in an act, active (देहकर्मणि स्थित).<BR>—2 Offspring (अपत्य Nir.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नः|अप्न
अप्नः, -अप्नस् <i>n.</i><BR> [आप्-असुन् नुट् ह्रस्वश्च, Uṇ. 4. 207]<BR>—1 Possession, property.<BR>—2 Work, sacrificial act or rite,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">Page0160-1</a>]<BR> any act.<BR>—3 Offspring.<BR>—4 Form, shape.<BR>—5 To be obtained (used actively); [cf. L. <i>ops</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्नस्थ, अप्नराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्
अप्नः, -अप्नस् <i>n.</i><BR> [आप्-असुन् नुट् ह्रस्वश्च, Uṇ. 4. 207]<BR>—1 Possession, property.<BR>—2 Work, sacrificial act or rite,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">Page0160-1</a>]<BR> any act.<BR>—3 Offspring.<BR>—4 Form, shape.<BR>—5 To be obtained (used actively); [cf. L. <i>ops</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्नस्थ, अप्नराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0159-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्थ
अप्नः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> superintending work (कर्मण्यधिकृत); (or <i>m.</i>)<BR> proprietor of an estate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नराजः|अप्नराज
अप्नः + -राजः lord of wealth or property, illustrious by means of works;<BR> directing works to be done (कर्मप्रेरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नवान|अप्नवानः
अप्नवान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having progeny.<BR>—2 Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नवानः|अप्नवान
अप्नवान + .{@-नः@} [अप्नसे आदायकर्मणे वानं यस्य पृषो˚ सलोप Tv.]<BR>—1 The arm.<BR>—2 N. of a Ṛṣi in the family of or connected with Bhṛgu. यमप्नवानो<BR> भृगवो विरुरुचुः Rv. 4. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्वत्|अप्नस्वन्त्
अप्नस्वत् <i>a.</i> Having (sacrificial) acts or works; productive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पति|अप्पतिः
अप्पति, -अप्पित्तम्<BR> see under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पित्तम्
अप्पति, -अप्पित्तम्<BR> see under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्य
अप्य <i>a.</i> [अपाम् इदं तत्र साधु संस्कृतम् वा यत्; अद्भिः संस्कृतम् P. IV. 4. 134]<BR>—1 Connected with or coming from water. त्वया हितमप्यमप्सु भागम्<BR> Rv. 2. 38. 7; watery; स ईं मृगो अप्यो वनर्गुरुप 1. 145. 5 consisting<BR> of, consecrated with, water (as हविः.)<BR>—2 Obtainable.<BR>—3 Active, connected with sacrificial acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यदीक्षितः|अप्यदीक्षित
अप्यदीक्षितः N. of a celebrated Draviḍa writer, author of works<BR> on Alaṅkāra and other subjects and a contemporary of Pandit Jagannātha<BR> who lived in the 17th century (written also as अप्पयादीक्षित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यञ्च्
अप्यञ्च् [fr. अञ्च्] Gone into, reaching, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यय|अप्ययः
अप्यय &c. see under अपी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यर्धम्
अप्यर्धम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Near, in the neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकट|अप्रकटः
अप्रकट <i>a.</i> Unmanifested, unapparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकम्प|अप्रकंप
अप्रकम्प <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unshaken (fig. also), firm, steady.<BR>—2 Unanswerable (as argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकर
अप्रकर <i>a.</i> Not acting well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकरणम्
अप्रकरणम् Not the main or principal topic, incidental or irrelevant matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकल्पक
अप्रकल्पक <i>a.</i> Not explicitly enjoining, not prescribing as obligatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाण्ड|अप्रकांड|अप्रकाण्डः
अप्रकाण्ड <i>a.</i> Stemless (small).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाण्डः|अप्रकाण्ड|अप्रकांड
अप्रकाण्ड + .{@-ण्डः@} A bush, a shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश|अप्रकाशः
अप्रकाश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not shining or bright, dark, wanting in brightness (fig. also); प्रकाशश्चाप्रकाशश्च<BR> लोकालोक इवाचलः R. 1. 68.<BR>—2 Self-illuminated.<BR>—3 Hidden, secret, concealed; सीमायामप्रकाशानि कारयेत् Ms. 8. 251, 9. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशम्
अप्रकाश + .{@-शम्, -शे@} <i>ind.</i> In secret, secretly; अहमप्रकाशे तिष्ठामि<BR> M. 4; सत्यवत्या हस्तेऽप्रकाशं निक्षिप्तः V. 5 secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशे
अप्रकाश + .{@-शम्, -शे@} <i>ind.</i> In secret, secretly; अहमप्रकाशे तिष्ठामि<BR> M. 4; सत्यवत्या हस्तेऽप्रकाशं निक्षिप्तः V. 5 secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशः|अप्रकाश
अप्रकाश + .{@-शः@} Indistinctness, secrecy; a secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशक
अप्रकाशक <i>a.</i> Making dark; not disclosing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश्य
अप्रकाश्य <i>a.</i> Not to be disclosed, to be kept secret (one of 9<BR> such things); जन्मर्क्षं मैथुनं मन्त्रो गृहच्छिद्रं च वञ्चनम् । आयुर्धनापमानं<BR> स्त्री न प्रकाश्यानि सर्वथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृत|अप्रकृतः
अप्रकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not principal or chief, incidental, occasional.<BR>—2 Not relevant to the subject under discussion, not to the point, irrelevant;<BR> see प्रकृत, प्रस्तुत; अप्रकृतम् अनुसन्धा ‘to beat about the bush’,<BR> not to come to the point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृतम्
अप्रकृत + .{@-तम्@} (In Rhet.) उपमान <i>i. e.</i> the standard of comparison<BR> (opp. प्रकृत or उपमेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृतः|अप्रकृत
अप्रकृत + .{@-तः@} An insane person (cf. Dānasāgara.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृतिः|अप्रकृति
अप्रकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Not the inherent or natural property, accidental property or nature;<BR> an accident (विकृति).<BR>—2 Spiritual being; the Puruṣa of the Sāṅkhyas.<BR>—3 Not the original word; such as a termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृष्ट|अप्रकृष्टः
अप्रकृष्ट <i>a.</i> Not excelled, low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृष्टः|अप्रकृष्ट
अप्रकृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रक्षित
अप्रक्षित <i>a.</i> Undecayed, undiminished, inexhaustible; अप्रक्षितं<BR> वसु बिभर्षि Rv. 1. 55. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रख्यता
अप्रख्यता Infamy; अक्षमा ह्रीपरित्यागः श्रीनाशो धर्मसंक्षयः ।<BR> अभिध्याऽप्रख्यता चैव सर्वं लोभात्प्रवर्तते Mb. 12. 158. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगम
अप्रगम <i>a.</i> Going too fast to be followed by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगल्भ
अप्रगल्भ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bold, bashful, modest (opp. धृष्ट); धृष्टः पार्श्वे वसति<BR> नियतं दूरतश्चाप्रगल्भः H. 2. 26.<BR>—2 Coward, fearful; (विहगा जलचारिणः) नावगाहन्ति सलिलमप्रगल्भा<BR> इवाहवम् Rām. 3. 16. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगुण|अप्रगुणः
अप्रगुण <i>a.</i> Perplexed, confounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रग्राह
अप्रग्राह <i>a.</i> Unrestrained, unbridled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचङ्कश|अप्रचंकश
अप्रचङ्कश <i>a.</i> Ved. Without the power of seeing; Av. 8. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचेतस्
अप्रचेतस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Deficient in understanding, foolish, stupid;<BR> Av. 20. 128. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचोदित
अप्रचोदित <i>a.</i> unasked, undesired; (भिक्षां) पुरस्तादप्रचोदितां … ग्राह्याम् Ms. 4. 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्छेद्य
अप्रच्छेद्य <i>a.</i> Inscrutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्युत
अप्रच्युत <i>a.</i> Unmoved; पर्वते न श्रितान्यप्रच्युतानि Rv. 2. 28. 8.<BR> not swerving from, following, observing (with abl.); अस्मादप्रच्युतो<BR> विप्रः प्राप्नोति परमां गतिम् Ms. 12. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रज
अप्रज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without progeny, childless; अप्रजाः सन्तु अत्रिणः Rv. 1. 21. 5<BR> शोच्यं मैथुनमप्रजम् Cāṇ. 57. अप्रजः सुप्रजतमो Bhāg. 4. 23. 33.<BR>—2 Unborn.<BR>—3 Unpeopled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजा
अप्रज + .{@-जा@} Having no child, not giving birth to children, not prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजस्
अप्रजस्, अप्रजात <i>a.</i> Childless, having no issue or progeny;<BR> अतीतायामप्रजसि बान्धवास्तदवाप्नुयुः Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजात
अप्रजस्, अप्रजात <i>a.</i> Childless, having no issue or progeny;<BR> अतीतायामप्रजसि बान्धवास्तदवाप्नुयुः Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजस्ता
अप्रजस्, अप्रजात + .{@-ता@} A woman who has borne no child, a barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजज्ञि
अप्रजज्ञि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Inexperienced, unskilful.<BR>—2 Childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रज्ञात
अप्रज्ञात <i>a.</i> Not known, अतीन्द्रिय; आसीदिदं तमोभूतमप्रज्ञातमलक्षणम् Ms. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणीत
अप्रणीत <i>a.</i> Unconsecrated, vulgar, profane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणीतम्
अप्रणीत + .{@-तम्@} Frying clarified butter without consecrated water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0160-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतर्क्य
अप्रतर्क्य <i>a.</i> Incomprehensible by reason or inference, undefinable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रता
अप्रता <i>a.</i> Ved. Very great or extensive, affluent; न सोमो अप्रता<BR> पपे Rv. 8. 32. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतापः|अप्रताप
अप्रतापः<BR>—1 Want of lustre, dullness, dimness.<BR>—2 Meanness, want of dignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रति
अप्रति <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Without opponents or foes, irresistible; य एक इदप्रतिर्मन्यमानः<BR> Rv. 5. 32. 3; ˚वीर्य of irresistible prowess.<BR>—2 Unsurpassed, unequalled. ━<i>adv.</i> Irresistibly तदुग्रवेगं दिशि<BR> दिश्युपर्यधो विसर्पदुत्सर्पदसह्यमप्रति Bhāg. 8. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर|अप्रतिकरः
अप्रतिकर <i>a.</i> Trusting, trusty, confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर्मन्|अप्रतिकर्म्मन्
अप्रतिकर्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of unequalled deeds or achievements.<BR>—2 Irresistible, irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकार|अप्रतिकारः
अप्रति(ती)कार <i>a.</i> Irremediable, helpless, that cannot be remedied<BR> or helped; ˚रेयमापदुपस्थिता K. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीकार
अप्रति(ती)कार <i>a.</i> Irremediable, helpless, that cannot be remedied<BR> or helped; ˚रेयमापदुपस्थिता K. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकारः|अप्रतिकार
अप्रति(ती)कार + .{@-रः@} Not remedying, non-requital, non-retaliation. यदि मामप्रतीकारम् । Bg. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिगृह्य
अप्रतिगृह्य <i>a.</i> One from whom one must not accept any thing as a gift &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राहक
अप्रतिग्राहक <i>a.</i> Not accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राह्य
अप्रतिग्राह्य <i>a.</i> Unacceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिघ
अप्रतिघ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be vanquished, invincible.<BR>—2 Not to be warded or kept off; यत्तु दुःखसमायुक्तमप्रीतिकरमात्मनः ।<BR> तद्रजोऽप्रतिपं (घं) विद्यात् Ms. 12. 28.<BR>—3 Not angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिद्वन्द्व|अप्रतिद्वंद्व
अप्रतिद्वन्द्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no adversary in battle, irresistible.<BR>—2 Unsurpassed, unrivalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिधुर
अप्रतिधुर <i>a.</i> Without the fellow-horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपक्ष|अप्रतिपक्षः
अप्रतिपक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without a rival or opponent.<BR>—2 Unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपत्तिः|अप्रतिपत्ति
अप्रतिपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-performance, non-acceptance.<BR>—2 Neglect, omission, disregard.<BR>—3 Want of understanding.<BR>—4 Absence of determination (what to do), perplexity; ˚विह्वल &c.<BR> K. 159; (अप्रतिपत्तिर्जडता स्यादिष्टानिष्टदर्शनश्रुतिभिः); ˚त्तिसाध्वसजडा<BR> K. 240; ययुः क्षणादप्रतिपत्तिमूढताम् Ki. 14. 43.<BR>—5 (Hence) absence of mind or ready wit (स्फूर्त्यभाव); उत्तरस्याप्रतिपत्तिरप्रतिभा Gaut. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपद्
अप्रतिपद् <i>a.</i> Not going (विकल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबन्ध|अप्रतिबंध
अप्रतिबन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>—2 Direct, undisputed; (in law) got by birth without any obstruction,<BR> not collateral (as inheritance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबल
अप्रतिबल <i>a.</i> of irresistible might, of unequalled power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभ|अप्रतिभः
अप्रतिभ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Modest, bashful.<BR>—2 Not ready-witted, dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभा
अप्रतिभ + .{@-भा@} Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभट|अप्रतिभटः
अप्रतिभट <i>a.</i> Unrivalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभटः|अप्रतिभट
अप्रतिभट + .{@-टः@} An unrivalled warrior; आत्मानं ˚टं मन्यमानः Dk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिम
अप्रतिम, -मान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without an equal or parallel, incomparable, matchless, unrivalled;<BR> त्वं ह त्यदप्रतिमानमोजो Rv. 8. 96. 17. रामस्य पश्याप्रतिमानमोजः<BR> Mv. 1. 62; ˚रूपत्वम्; ˚वीर्य, ˚बुद्धि &c.<BR>—2 Improper; तस्मात्त्वया समारब्धं कर्म ह्यप्रतिमं परैः Rām. 6. 12. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिमान
अप्रतिम, -मान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without an equal or parallel, incomparable, matchless, unrivalled;<BR> त्वं ह त्यदप्रतिमानमोजो Rv. 8. 96. 17. रामस्य पश्याप्रतिमानमोजः<BR> Mv. 1. 62; ˚रूपत्वम्; ˚वीर्य, ˚बुद्धि &c.<BR>—2 Improper; तस्मात्त्वया समारब्धं कर्म ह्यप्रतिमं परैः Rām. 6. 12. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिमानुष
अप्रतिमानुष <i>a.</i> Extra-ordinary; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्नः|अप्रतियत्न
अप्रतियत्नः Natural or spontaneous state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियोगिन्
अप्रतियोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without an adversary.<BR>—2 Having no opposite or counterpart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं|अप्रतिरथः
अप्रतिरथ <i>a.</i> or -थः<BR>—1 (A hero) who has no प्रतिरथ or rival warrior, a matchless or<BR> unrivalled warrior; दौष्यांतिमप्रतिरथं तनयं निवेश्य Ś. 4. 20; Ś. 7, 7. 33.<BR>—2 Matchless; अप्रतिहतैस्तेजोभिः एकैकस्य योग्यता Mv. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथः|अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं
अप्रतिरथ <i>a.</i> or -थः<BR>—1 (A hero) who has no प्रतिरथ or rival warrior, a matchless or<BR> unrivalled warrior; दौष्यांतिमप्रतिरथं तनयं निवेश्य Ś. 4. 20; Ś. 7, 7. 33.<BR>—2 Matchless; अप्रतिहतैस्तेजोभिः एकैकस्य योग्यता Mv. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथः|अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं
अप्रतिरथ <i>a.</i> or -थः + .{@-थः@} N. of a Ṛṣi (Composer of the hymn Rv. 10. 103); N. of<BR> a son of Rantināra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथः|अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं
अप्रतिरथ <i>a.</i> or -थः + .{@-थः, -थम्@} N. of a hymn composed by अ˚; यद्यात्रामङ्गलं साम<BR> तदप्रतिरथं विदुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथम्
अप्रतिरथ <i>a.</i> or -थः + .{@-थः, -थम्@} N. of a hymn composed by अ˚; यद्यात्रामङ्गलं साम<BR> तदप्रतिरथं विदुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरव
अप्रतिरव <i>a.</i> Uncontested, undisputed; वर्षशताधिकभोगः सन्ततोऽप्रतिरवः<BR> स्वत्वं गमयति Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूप
अप्रतिरूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not corresponding with, unfit; वाक्यमप्रतिरूपं तु न चित्रं स्त्रीषु<BR> मैथिलि Rām. 3. 45. 29.<BR>—2 Of unequalled form.<BR>—3 Incomparable (in a good or bad sense).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रतिरूपकथा, अप्रतिरूपवीर्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूपकथा
अप्रतिरूप + -कथा incomparable talk (संगणिका), उत्तरवाक्यरहिता वाक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूपवीर्यम्
अप्रतिरूप + -वीर्यम् irresistible power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिवीर्य|अप्रतिवीर्य्य
अप्रतिवीर्य <i>a.</i> Of incomparable prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिशासन
अप्रतिशासन <i>a.</i> Having no rival ruler, subject to one rule; कृतवानप्रतिशासनं<BR> जगत् R. 8. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिषेधः|अप्रतिषेध
अप्रतिषेधः A meaningless prohibition, an invalid objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठ|अप्रतिष्ठः
अप्रतिष्ठ^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not stable or firmly fixed, fluctuating, not made permanent; अप्रतिष्ठे<BR> रघुज्येष्ठे का प्रतिष्ठा कुलस्य नः U. 5. 25.<BR>—2 Thrown away, unprofitable, useless; अप्रतिष्ठं तु वार्धुषौ Ms. 3. 180.<BR>—3 Disreputable, infamous.<BR>—4 Without support, adjustment; असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम् Bg. 16. 8.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठः|अप्रतिष्ठ
अप्रतिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@} N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठा
अप्रतिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठा@} Instability, ill-fame, ill-repute, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठम्
अप्रतिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@} Brahman (स्वधामप्रतिष्ठितं ब्रह्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठान
अप्रतिष्ठान <i>a.</i> Ved. Not firm, having no solid ground. Av. 11. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठानम्
अप्रतिष्ठान + .{@-नम्@} Instability, want of solidity or firmness (fig. also); तर्काप्रतिष्ठानादप्यन्यथानुमेयम् Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठित|अप्रतिष्ठितः
अप्रतिष्ठित <i>a.</i> Unsettled, unfixed, uncelebrated, obscure; unconsecrated, unholy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठितः|अप्रतिष्ठित
अप्रतिष्ठित + .{@-तः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिसंक्रम|अप्रतिसङ्क्रम
अप्रतिसंक्रम <i>a.</i> Having no intermixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिसंख्य|अप्रतिसङ्ख्य
अप्रतिसंख्य <i>a.</i> Unobserved, unnoticed; ˚ख्य(ख्या)निरोधः<BR> unobserved nullity, annihilation of an object;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">Page0162-1</a>]<BR> one of the three topics included by the Buddhas under the category of<BR> निरूप, the other two being प्रतिसंख्यानिरोध wilful destruction,<BR> as of a jar by a mallet, and आकाश the ethereal element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहत
अप्रतिहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not obstructed or impeded, irresistible; ˚हतान् पुत्रान् K. 62; अस्मद्गृहे<BR> ˚गतिः Pt. 1 free to move; तोयस्येवाप्रतिहतरयः U. 3. 36; जृम्भतामप्रतिहतप्रसरमार्यस्य<BR> क्रोधज्योतिः Ve. 1.<BR>—2 Unimpaired, unmarred, unrepulsed, unaffected, at home in every respect;<BR> सा बुद्धिरप्रतिहता Bh. 2. 40; Pt. 5. 26; so ˚चित्त, ˚मनस्.<BR>—3 Not disappointed.<BR>—4 A kind of deity; अपराजित-अप्रतिहत-जयन्त-वैजयन्त-कोष्ठकान् …<BR> पुरमध्ये कारयेत् Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रतिहतनेत्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहतनेत्र|अप्रतिहतनेत्रः
अप्रतिहत + -नेत्र <i>a.</i> of unimpaired eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहतनेत्रः|अप्रतिहतनेत्र
अप्रतिहत + -नेत्र + .({@-त्रः@}) N. of a Buddhist deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीक
अप्रतीक <i>a.</i> Without parts or body, epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीत
अप्रतीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pleased or delighted; को न्वनेनाप्रतीतेन (संप्रीयेत)<BR> Rām. 2. 48. 20.<BR>—2 Unapproached; unassailable. Av. 7. 25. 1.<BR>—3 Unopposed.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.) Not understood or clearly intelligible (as a word), one<BR> of the defects of a word (शब्ददोष); अप्रतीतं यत्केवले शास्त्रे<BR> प्रसिद्धम् K. P. 7, <i>i. e.</i> a word is said to be अप्रतीत if it<BR> be used in a sense which it has in particular classes of works only (and<BR> not in general or popular use); <i>e. g.</i> सम्यग्ज्ञानमहाज्योतिर्दलिताशयताजुषः<BR> (where आशय = वासना occurs in Yogaśāstra only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीतिः|अप्रतीति
अप्रतीतिः <i>f.</i> Unintelligibleness; mistrust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतुलः|अप्रतुल|अप्रतुलं
अप्रतुलः<BR>—1 Want of weight.<BR>—2 Want, necessity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्त
अप्रत्त (˚प्रदत्त) Not given away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदत्त
अप्रत्त (˚प्रदत्त) Not given away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्ता
अप्रत्त (˚प्रदत्त) + .{@-त्ता@} A girl, one not given away in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्ष|अप्रत्यक्षः
अप्रत्यक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>—2 Unknown. —3 Absent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रत्यक्षशिष्ट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्षशिष्ट
अप्रत्यक्ष + -शिष्ट <i>a.</i> not distinctly taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यय|अप्रत्ययः
अप्रत्यय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Diffident, distrustful (with loc.); बलवदपि शिक्षितानामात्मन्यप्रत्ययं<BR> चेतः Ś. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Having no knowledge.<BR>—3 (In gram.) Having no affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्ययः|अप्रत्यय
अप्रत्यय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Diffidence, distrust, disbelief, doubt; क्षेत्रमप्रत्ययानाम् Pt. 1. 191.<BR>—2 Not being understood.<BR>—3 Not an affix; अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकम् P. I. 2. 45.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रत्ययस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्ययस्थ
अप्रत्यय + -स्थ <i>a.</i> (in gram.) not pertaining to an affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यृत
अप्रत्यृत <i>a.</i> Not attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदक्षिणम्
अप्रदक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the left to the right.<BR>—2 unfavourable; निमित्तानि च भूयिष्ठं यानि प्रादुर्भवन्ति नः । तेषु<BR> तेष्वभिपन्नेषु लक्षयाम्यप्रदक्षिणम् ॥ Rām. 6. 104. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदुग्ध
अप्रदुग्ध <i>a.</i> Ved. Not milked completely. आ धेनवो अप्रदुग्धाः Rv. 3. 55. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधान|अप्रधानं
अप्रधान <i>a.</i> Subordinate, secondary, inferior; आवां तावदप्रधानौ H. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधानम्
अप्रधान + .{@-नम्@} (˚ता, ˚त्वम्)<BR>—1 Subordinate or secondary state, inferiority.<BR>—2 A secondary or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">Page0162-2</a>]<BR> subordinate act. (The word अप्रधान usually occurs in the neuter gender<BR> either by itself, or as an attribute to a noun, or as last member of comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधृष्य
अप्रधृष्य <i>a.</i> Unconquerable, invincible; यदाश्रौषं भीष्ममत्यंतशूरं<BR> हतं पार्थेनाहवेष्वप्रधृष्यम् Mb.; यस्याप्रधृष्यः प्रभवस्त्वमुच्चैः M. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रपदनम्
अप्रपदनम् Ved. A bad place of refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभ
अप्रभ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obscure, dull.<BR>—2 Mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभु
अप्रभु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wanting power, not powerful.<BR>—2 Having no power or control over, unable, incompetent; with gen. or<BR> loc.; आशताऽत्राकर्तमव पदात्यप्रभुः Rv. 9. 73. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभूतिः|अप्रभूति
अप्रभूतिः <i>f.</i> Little effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमत्त|अप्रमत्तः
अप्रमत्त <i>a.</i> Not careless or inattentive, careful, attentive,<BR> vigilant, watchful; अप्रमत्तो बले कोशे दुर्गे जनपदे तथा (भवेथाः)<BR> Rām. 2. 52. 72, 3. 33. 20; युक्तश्चैवाप्रमत्तश्र परिरक्षेदिमाः प्रजाः Ms. 7. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमद
अप्रमद <i>a.</i> Devoid of festivities, sad, joyless; Bk. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाद|अप्रमादः
अप्रमाद <i>a.</i> Careful, vigilant, cautious, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादः|अप्रमाद
अप्रमाद + .{@-दः@} Care, attention, vigilance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादम्
अप्रमाद + .{@-दम्@} <i>ind.</i> Carefully, attentively, uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादता
अप्रमाद + .{@-ता@} The state of being cautious; शौचाक्रोधाप्रमादता Y. 3. 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादिन्
अप्रमाद + .{@-दिन्@} <i>a.</i> careful; तस्मै मां ब्रूहि विप्राय निधिपायाप्रमादिने Ms. 2. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमय
अप्रमय <i>a.</i> Imperishable; unlimited (अप्रमेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमा
अप्रमा Incorrect knowledge (opp. प्रमा q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाण
अप्रमाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unlimited, immeasurable, boundless.<BR>—2 Without authority, proof or weight, unauthorized.<BR>—3 Not regarded as an authority, not trustworthy; आजन्मनः शाठ्यमशिक्षितो<BR> यस्तस्याप्रमाणं वचनं जनस्य Ś. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाणम्
अप्रमाण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 That which cannot be taken as authority in actions; <i>i. e.</i> a rule,<BR> direction &c. which cannot be accepted as obligatory.<BR>—2 Irrelevancy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रमाणाभः, अप्रमाणशुभः, अप्रमाणविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाणाभः|अप्रमाणाभ
अप्रमाण + -आभः, -शुभः (pl.) ‘of unlimited lusture’, N. of a class of deities<BR> (with Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाणशुभः|अप्रमाणशुभ
अप्रमाण + -आभः, -शुभः (pl.) ‘of unlimited lusture’, N. of a class of deities<BR> (with Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाणविद्
अप्रमाण + -विद् <i>a.</i> not conversant with evidence, or incapable of weighing evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमायुक
अप्रमायुक <i>a.</i> [प्र-मि-उण् आत्त्वे युच्, स्वार्थे कन् Tv.] Not dying<BR> suddenly, very long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमित
अप्रमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not measured, unlimited.<BR>—2 Not proved or established by authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमूर
अप्रमूर (Ved.), अप्रमूर्च्छित <i>a.</i> Not foolish, prudent,<BR> wise; ते अप्रमूरा महोभिः Rv. 1. 90. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमूर्च्छित
अप्रमूर (Ved.), अप्रमूर्च्छित <i>a.</i> Not foolish, prudent,<BR> wise; ते अप्रमूरा महोभिः Rv. 1. 90. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमृष्य
अप्रमृष्य <i>a.</i> Indestructible, unassailable (अबाध्य); सुदामन्<BR> तद् रेक्णो अप्रमृष्यम् Rv. 6. 20. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेय
अप्रमेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Immeasurable, unbounded, boundless; ˚महिमा; येषां वेद इवाप्रमेयमहिमा<BR> धर्मे वसिष्ठो गुरुः Mv. 4. 30.<BR>—2 That which cannot be properly ascertained, understood. &c.; inscrutable,<BR> unfathomable (of person or thing);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">Page0163-1</a>]<BR> अचिन्त्यस्याप्रमेयस्य कार्यतत्त्वार्थवित्प्रभुः Ms. 1. 3, 12. 94.<BR>—3 Not to be proved or demonstrated (as Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेयम्
अप्रमेय + .{@-यम्@} Brahman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रमेयानुभाव, अप्रमेयात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेयानुभाव
अप्रमेय + -अनुभाव <i>a.</i> of unlimited might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेयात्मन्
अप्रमेय + -आत्मन् ‘of inscrutable spirit’ epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमोदः|अप्रमोद|अप्रमोदं
अप्रमोदः, -दम्<BR>—1 Inability to remove pain.<BR>—2 Absence of delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमोदम्
अप्रमोदः, -दम्<BR>—1 Inability to remove pain.<BR>—2 Absence of delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्न|अप्रयत्नः
अप्रयत्न <i>a.</i> Not energetic or diligent, indifferent, apathetic,<BR> not zealously devoted to (with loc.); ˚त्नः सुखार्थेषु Ms. 6. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्नः|अप्रयत्न
अप्रयत्न + .{@-त्नः@} Absence of effort or exertion, indifference, apathy, laziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयाणिः|अप्रयाणि
अप्रयाणिः <i>f.</i> [अ-प्रया-अनि P. III. 3. 112, न changed<BR> to ण by P. VIII. 4. 29] Not going or progressing (used only in uttering<BR> imprecations); अप्रयाणिस्ते शठ भूयात् Sk. mayest thou not move onward<BR> or progress! See अजीवनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयापणि
अप्रयापणि, -निः <i>f.</i><BR> Not allowing to go on or progress आक्रोशे नत्र्यनिः<BR> (P. III. 3. 112, VIII. 4. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयापनिः
अप्रयापणि, -निः <i>f.</i><BR> Not allowing to go on or progress आक्रोशे नत्र्यनिः<BR> (P. III. 3. 112, VIII. 4. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयावम्
अप्रयावम् <i>adv.</i> Without interruption, attentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुच्छत्|अप्रयुच्छन्त्|अप्रयुछत्
अप्रयुच्छत्^1, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Unceasing, continual,<BR> not separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुत
अप्रयुच्छत्^1, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Unceasing, continual,<BR> not separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुत्वन्
अप्रयुच्छत्^1, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Unceasing, continual,<BR> not separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुक्त
अप्रयुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not used or employed, not applied.<BR>—2 Wrongly used, as a word.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Rare, unusual (as a word when used in a particular sense<BR> or gender though that sense or gender be sanctioned by lexicographers);<BR> अप्रयुक्तं तथाम्नातमपि कविभिर्नादृतम्; तथा मन्ये दैवतोऽस्य पिशाचो<BR> राक्षसोऽथवा । where the mas. gender of दैवत, though sanctioned<BR> (by Amara), is not used by poets and is, therefore, अप्रयुक्त. सन्त्यप्रयुक्ताः Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयोगः|अप्रयोग
अप्रयोगः Non-application or bad application, non-employment. अप्रयोगः<BR> प्रयोगान्यत्वात् Mbh. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रलम्ब|अप्रलंब|अप्रलम्बं
अप्रलम्ब <i>a.</i> Prompt, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तक|अप्रवर्त्तक
अप्रवर्तक, अप्रवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not exciting or stimulating to action, inert, abstaining from action;<BR> पूर्णमप्रवतीति वा अहमेतमुपास इति Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 5.<BR>—2 Continuous, unbroken, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तिन्|अप्रवर्त्तिन्
अप्रवर्तक, अप्रवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not exciting or stimulating to action, inert, abstaining from action;<BR> पूर्णमप्रवतीति वा अहमेतमुपास इति Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 5.<BR>—2 Continuous, unbroken, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तनम्
अप्रवर्तनम् Not engaging in, not exciting to any action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृत्त
अप्रवृत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not acting, not engaged in.<BR>—2 Not instigated.<BR>—3 Not proper; अप्रवृत्तं सुदुर्बुद्धे यस्मादेतत्त्वया कृतम् Mb. 5. 192. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृत्तिः|अप्रवृत्ति
अप्रवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Not engaging in action or proceeding, not taking place.<BR>—2 Inertia, inactivity, non-excitement, absence of incentive or stimulus.<BR>—3 (In medic.) Suppression of the natural evacuations, constipation. ischuria &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीत
अप्रवीत <i>a.</i> Ved. Not approached; यदप्रवीता दधते ह गर्भम् Rv. 4. 7. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीता
अप्रवीत + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 Not loved (अकामिता).<BR>—2 Not impregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवेद
अप्रवेद <i>a.</i> Difficult to be found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not praiseworthy, worthless, contemptible.<BR>—2 Not approved, forbidden.<BR>—3 (Ved.) Disobedient.<BR>—4 Less, deficient, decayed (क्षीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्त
अप्रसक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not attached or addicted, moderate, temperate.<BR>—2 Unconnected.<BR>—3 unobstructed; विवेश गां तोयमिवाप्रसक्ता Mb. 9. 17. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्तिः|अप्रसक्ति
अप्रसक्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-attachment, moderation. विषयेष्वप्रसक्तिश्च<BR> क्षत्रियस्य समासतः Ms. 1. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसङ्गः|अप्रसङ्ग|अप्रसंग|अप्रसंगः
अप्रसङ्गः<BR>—1 Want of attachment.<BR>—2 Want of connection.<BR>—3 Inopportune time or occasion; अप्रसङ्गाभिधाने च श्रोतुः श्रद्धा न जायते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्न|अप्रसन्नं
अप्रसन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pleased.<BR>—2 Turbid, muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्नम्
अप्रसन्न + .{@-न्नम्@} The milk of a cow milked after the 7th day of delivery. Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसादः|अप्रसाद
अप्रसादः Disfavour, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसव|अप्रसवः
अप्रसव <i>a.</i> Not being prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसवः|अप्रसव
अप्रसव + .{@-वः@} Not being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसूत
अप्रसूत <i>a.</i> Barren, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसहिष्णु
अप्रसहिष्णु <i>a.</i> quite unable (to); जगत्प्रभोरप्रसहिष्णु वैष्णवम्<BR> (चक्रम्) Ku. 1. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाह
अप्रसाह <i>a.</i> Not being affected by evils or ill omens; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्ध|अप्रसिद्धं
अप्रसिद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unknown, unimportant, insignificant अप्यप्रसिद्धं यशसे हि पुंसाम् Ku. 3. 19.<BR>—2 Unusual, uncommon; ˚पदम् an obsolete word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्धिः|अप्रसिद्धि
अप्रसिद्धिः <i>f.</i> Obscurity, insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्ताविक
अप्रस्ताविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Not belonging to the subject-matter, irrelevant (=<BR> अप्रास्ताविक q. v.); Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unsuitable to the time or subject, not to the point, irrelevant.<BR>—2 Absurd, nonsensical; रे गोरम्भ किमप्रस्तुतं लपसि Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Accidental or extraneous.<BR>—4 Not ready.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा
अप्रस्तुत + -प्रशंसा a figure of speech which, by describing the अप्रस्तुत<BR> (what is not the subject-matter) conveys a reference to the प्रस्तुत<BR> or subject-matter; अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव प्रस्तुताश्रया K. P. 10.<BR> It is of 5 kinds:− कार्ये निमित्ते सामान्ये विशेषे प्रस्तुते सति ।<BR> तदन्यस्य वचस्तुल्ये तुल्यस्येति च पञ्चधा ॥ <i>i. e.</i> when the subject-matter is viewed<BR>——(<i>a</i>) as an effect, information of which is conveyed by stating the cause;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) when viewed as a cause by stating the effect;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) when viewed as a general assertion by stating a particular instance;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) when viewed as a particular instance by stating a general assertion; and<BR>——(<i>e</i>) when viewed as similar by stating what is similar to it. See<BR> K. P. 10 and S. D. 706 for examples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहत|अप्रहतं
अप्रहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unhurt, intact.<BR>—2 Waste, unploughed, K. 326.<BR>—3 New and unbleached (as cloth); ईषद्धौतं नवं श्वेतं सदशं यन्त्रधारितम् ।<BR> निर्णेजकाक्षालितं चाप्रहतं वास उच्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0163-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहन्
अप्रहन् <i>a.</i> Not destroying, favouring, aiding (अनुग्राहक)<BR> त्यमूं वो अप्रहनं गृणीषे Rv. 6. 44. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहित
अप्रहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not sent out; Av. 6. 29. 2.<BR>—2 Unattacked by foes.<BR>—3 Not stirred up, इत ऊती वो अजरं प्रहेतारमप्रहितम् Rv. 8. 99. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकरणिक
अप्राकरणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Not belonging to the subject-matter; अप्राकरणिकस्याभिधानेन<BR> प्राकरणिकस्याक्षेपो ऽप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकृत
अप्राकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not vulgar.<BR>—2 Not original.<BR>—3 Not ordinary, extraordinary; ˚आकृतीनाम् K. 174, अप्राकृतेषु पात्रेषु<BR> यत्र वीरः स्थितो रसः Mv. 1. 3.<BR>—4 Special.<BR>—5 Not belonging to प्राकृत language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राग्र्य|अप्राग्र्यं
अप्राग्र्य <i>a.</i> Secondary, subordinate, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राचीन|अप्राचीनं
अप्राचीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Modern.<BR>—2 Not eastern, western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञ
अप्राज्ञ <i>a.</i> Ignorant, unlearned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञता
अप्राज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञता@} Ignorance; दुःखं सुमहदाप्नोति प्रेत्याप्राज्ञतया नरः Ms. 4. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रादेशिक
अप्रादेशिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pointing to, or suggestive of; Nir. 1. 13.<BR>—2 Non-provincial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राधान्य
अप्राधान्य <i>a.</i> Subordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राण|अप्राणः
अप्राण <i>a.</i> Lifeless; inanimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राणः|अप्राण
अप्राण + .{@-णः@} The Almighty Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्त|अप्राप्तः
अप्राप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not obtained or got; अप्राप्तयोस्तु या प्राप्तिः सैव संयोग ईरितः । Bhāṣā P.<BR>—2 Not arrived or come, unaccomplished; अप्राप्तव्यवहारम् Y. 2. 243.<BR>—3 Not authorised or following, as a rule.<BR>—4 Not come to or reached; राघवो रथमप्राप्तां तामाशां च सुरद्विषाम्<BR> (चिच्छेद) R. 12. 96.<BR>—5 Not of a marriageable age; Ms. 9. 88.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्राप्तकाल, अप्राप्तप्रापक, अप्राप्तयौवन, अप्राप्तव्यवहार, अप्राप्तवयस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तकाल
अप्राप्त + -काल<BR>—1 inopportune, ill-timed, unseasonable; ˚लं वचनं बृहस्पतिरपि ब्रुवन् । लभते बुद्धपवज्ञानमपमानं च पुष्कलम् Pt. 1. 63.<BR>—2 under age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तकालम्
अप्राप्त + -काल + .({@-लम्@}) an irregular discussion (of any subject).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तप्रापक
अप्राप्त + -प्रापक <i>a.</i> —1 conveying (the sense of) what is not otherwise<BR> specified, such as the use of the Potential mood in स्वर्गकामो यजेत.<BR>—2 not yet tamed (as a young calf)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तयौवन
अप्राप्त + -यौवन <i>a.</i> not arrived at puberty or who has not reached his<BR> youth; शिशुमप्राप्तयौवनम् R. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तव्यवहार
अप्राप्त + -व्यवहार, -वयस् <i>a.</i> (in law) under age, not old enough to<BR> engage in public business on his own responsibility, a minor (a boy before<BR> he reaches his 16th year); अप्राप्तव्यवहारोऽसौ यावत् षोडशवार्षिकः Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तवयस्
अप्राप्त + -व्यवहार, -वयस् <i>a.</i> (in law) under age, not old enough to<BR> engage in public business on his own responsibility, a minor (a boy before<BR> he reaches his 16th year); अप्राप्तव्यवहारोऽसौ यावत् षोडशवार्षिकः Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तिः|अप्राप्ति
अप्राप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-acquisition; तदप्राप्तिमहादुःखविलीनाशेषपातका K. P. 4.<BR>—2 Not being proved or established by a rule before; विधिरत्यन्तमप्राप्तौ<BR> नियमः पाक्षिके सति Mīm.<BR>—3 Not taking place or occurring.<BR>—4 Not being applicable = अनुपपत्ति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाणिक|अप्रामाणिकः
अप्रामाणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Unauthoritative, unwarranted; इदं वचनमप्रामाणिकम्.<BR>—2 Untrustworthy, unreliable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामि
अप्रामि <i>a.</i> Ved. Unhurt, unimpaired, Rv. 8. 61. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायत्यम्
अप्रायत्यम् Ved.<BR>—1 Impurity.<BR>—2 Ungovernableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायु
अप्रायु <i>a.</i> Ved. Not going forth (अगन्तृ); अप्रायुवो रक्षितारो<BR> दिवेदिवे Rv. 1. 89. 1; unceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायुस्
अप्रायुस् <i>a.</i> Ved. With undiminished or unimpaired life or vigour;<BR> अप्रायुषे दिवातरात् Rv. 1. 127. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अप्रिय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disliked, disagreeable, unpleasant, offensive अप्रियस्य च पथ्यस्य<BR> वक्ता श्रोता च दुर्लभः Rām.; Ms. 4. 138; अतः समीपे परिणेतुरिष्यते<BR> तदप्रियापि प्रमदा स्वबन्धुभिः Ś. 5. 17; hated, distasteful.<BR>—2 Unkind, unfriendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियः|अप्रिय|अप्रियं
अप्रिय + .{@-यः@} A foe, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिया
अप्रिय + .{@-या@} A sort of fish (शृङ्गीमत्स्यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियम्
अप्रिय + .{@-यम्@} An unfriendly or offensive act; पाणिग्राहस्य साध्वी स्त्री …<BR> नाचरेत्किञ्चिदप्रियम् Ms. 5. 156.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रियकर, अप्रियकारिन्, अप्रियकारक, अप्रियभागिन्, अप्रियवद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियकर
अप्रिय + -कर, -कारिन्, -कारक <i>a.</i> unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियकारिन्
अप्रिय + -कर, -कारिन्, -कारक <i>a.</i> unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियकारक
अप्रिय + -कर, -कारिन्, -कारक <i>a.</i> unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियभागिन्
अप्रिय + -भागिन् <i>a.</i> ill-fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियवद
अप्रिय + -वद, (˚यम्˚), {@-वादिन्@} <i>a.</i><BR> speaking unkind or harsh words; वन्ध्यार्थघ्न्यप्रियंवदा<BR> Y. 1. 73; माता यस्य गृहे नास्ति भार्या चाप्रियवादिनी Cāṇ. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीतिः|अप्रीति
अप्रीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Dislike, aversion.<BR>—2 Unfriendly feeling, enmity.<BR>—3 Pain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्रीतिकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीतिकर
अप्रीतिः + -कर<BR>.(-री <i>f.</i>).<BR>—1 unkind; unfavourable.<BR>—2 disagreeable, disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेतराक्षसी
अप्रेतराक्षसी = अपेतराक्षसी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेमन्
अप्रेमन् <i>a.</i> Disliking, unfriendly. <i>n.</i> Dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रोक्षित
अप्रोक्षित <i>a.</i> Not sprinkled, not consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रोटः|अप्रोट
अप्रोटः A kind of bird (Mar. कुकुडकुंभा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढ
अप्रौढ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not arrogant.<BR>—2 Timid, gentle, not bold.<BR>—3 Not full-grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढा
अप्रौढ + .{@-ढा@}<BR>—1 An unmarried girl.<BR>—2 A girl very recently married and not arrived at puberty or womanhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लव
अप्लव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without a ship, Av. 19. 50. 31.<BR>—2 Not swimming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लुत
अप्लुत <i>a.</i> Not protracted (as a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्व
अप्व <i>a.</i> [आप् बाहु˚ व, पृषो˚ ह्रस्वः] Attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्वा
अप्व + .{@-प्वा@} Disease, danger; गृहाणाङ्गान्यप्वे परेहि Rv. 10. 103. 12.<BR> the region of the throat or neck. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सः|अप्स
अप्सः, -प्सा <i>m.</i> ▪.(-प्साः Ved.)<BR> [अपःसनोति, सन्-ड]<BR>—1 Giving or yielding water; forming the essential portion of water (अपां<BR> सारभूतो रसः).<BR>—2 not destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सा
अप्सः, -प्सा <i>m.</i> ▪.(-प्साः Ved.)<BR> [अपःसनोति, सन्-ड]<BR>—1 Giving or yielding water; forming the essential portion of water (अपां<BR> सारभूतो रसः).<BR>—2 not destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सम्
अप्सः, -प्सा <i>m.</i> ▪.(-प्साः Ved.) + .{@-प्सम्@} Form, see अप्सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरः|अप्सर
अप्सरः [अप्-सृ-अच्] Any aquatic animal (moving in water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस् <i>f.</i> (-राः, -रा)<BR> [अदूभ्यः सरन्ति उद्गच्छन्ति, सृ-असुन् Uṇ. 4. 236;<BR> cf. Rām. अप्सु निर्मथनादेव रसात्तस्माद्वरस्त्रियः । उत्पेतुर्मनुजश्रेष्ठ<BR> तस्मादप्सरसोऽभवन् ॥]<BR>—1 A class of female divinities or celestial damsels who reside in the<BR> sky and are regarded as the wives of the Gandharvas. They are very fond<BR> of bathing, can change their shapes, and are endowed with superhuman power<BR> (प्रभाव).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">Page0165-1</a>]<BR> They are called स्वर्वेश्याः and are usually described as the servants<BR> of Indra, who, when alarmed by the rigorous austerities of some mighty<BR> sage, sends down one of them to disturb his penance, and her mission is<BR> generally successful; मेनकाऽप्सरसां श्रेष्ठा महर्षीणां पिता च ते<BR> Mb. 1. 74. 75. cf. या तपोविशेषपरिशाङ्कितस्य सुकुमारं प्रहरणं<BR> महेन्द्रस्य V. 1. They are also said to covet heroes who die gloriously<BR> on the battle-field; cf. परस्परेण क्षतयोः प्रहर्त्रेरुत्कान्तवाथ्वोः<BR> समकालमेव । अमर्त्यभावेऽपि कयोश्चिदासीदेकाप्सरः प्रार्थितयोर्विवादः ॥<BR> R. 7. 53. Bāṇa mentions 14 different families of these nymphs (see<BR> K. 136) The word is usually said to be in pl. (स्त्रियां बहुष्वप्सरसः)<BR> but the singular, as also the form अप्सरा, sometimes occurs; नियमविघ्नकारिणी<BR> मेनका नाम अप्सराः प्रेषिता Ś. 1; एकाप्सरः &c. R. 7. 53 and see<BR> Malli. thereon; अनप्सरेव प्रतिभासि V. 1.<BR>—2 Direction or the intermediate point of the compass (दिक् च उपदिक् च).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्सरस्तीर्थम्, अप्सरःपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरा
अप्सरस् <i>f.</i> (-राः, -रा)<BR> [अदूभ्यः सरन्ति उद्गच्छन्ति, सृ-असुन् Uṇ. 4. 236;<BR> cf. Rām. अप्सु निर्मथनादेव रसात्तस्माद्वरस्त्रियः । उत्पेतुर्मनुजश्रेष्ठ<BR> तस्मादप्सरसोऽभवन् ॥]<BR>—1 A class of female divinities or celestial damsels who reside in the<BR> sky and are regarded as the wives of the Gandharvas. They are very fond<BR> of bathing, can change their shapes, and are endowed with superhuman power<BR> (प्रभाव).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">Page0165-1</a>]<BR> They are called स्वर्वेश्याः and are usually described as the servants<BR> of Indra, who, when alarmed by the rigorous austerities of some mighty<BR> sage, sends down one of them to disturb his penance, and her mission is<BR> generally successful; मेनकाऽप्सरसां श्रेष्ठा महर्षीणां पिता च ते<BR> Mb. 1. 74. 75. cf. या तपोविशेषपरिशाङ्कितस्य सुकुमारं प्रहरणं<BR> महेन्द्रस्य V. 1. They are also said to covet heroes who die gloriously<BR> on the battle-field; cf. परस्परेण क्षतयोः प्रहर्त्रेरुत्कान्तवाथ्वोः<BR> समकालमेव । अमर्त्यभावेऽपि कयोश्चिदासीदेकाप्सरः प्रार्थितयोर्विवादः ॥<BR> R. 7. 53. Bāṇa mentions 14 different families of these nymphs (see<BR> K. 136) The word is usually said to be in pl. (स्त्रियां बहुष्वप्सरसः)<BR> but the singular, as also the form अप्सरा, sometimes occurs; नियमविघ्नकारिणी<BR> मेनका नाम अप्सराः प्रेषिता Ś. 1; एकाप्सरः &c. R. 7. 53 and see<BR> Malli. thereon; अनप्सरेव प्रतिभासि V. 1.<BR>—2 Direction or the intermediate point of the compass (दिक् च उपदिक् च).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अप्सरस्तीर्थम्, अप्सरःपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0164-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्तीर्थम्
अप्सरस् + -तीर्थम् N. of a sacred pool in which the Apsarasas bathe; probably<BR> it is the name of a place, see Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरःपतिः|अप्सरःपति
अप्सरस् + -पतिः lord of the Apsarasas, epithet of Indra. N. of the Gandharva<BR> शिखण्डिन्; Av. 4. 37. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव
अप्सव <i>a.</i> [अप्सं जलरसं वाति हिनस्ति, वा-क]<BR>—1 Devoid of the essence (freshness) of water;<BR>—2 possessed of form or shape; giving water (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव्य
अप्सव्य <i>a.</i> [अप्सु भवः यत्] Being in, or fit for, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सस्
अप्सस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Form, beauty; or one possessed of beauty; cheek (?).<BR> उषा हस्रेव नि रिणीते अप्सः Rv. 1. 124. 7^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सु
अप्सु <i>a.</i> [नास्ति प्सु रूपं यस्य Nir.]<BR>—1 Formless, shapeless.<BR>—2 Not beautiful. Note:− -अप्सु forms the first member of several compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुक्षित्
अप्सु + .{@-क्षित्@} a god (dwelling within the clouds); अप्सुक्षितो महिनैकादश<BR> स्थ Rv. 1. 139. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुचर
अप्सु + .{@-चर@} <i>a.</i> aquatic; moving in waters. P. VI. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुज
अप्सु + .{@-ज, -जा@} <i>a.</i> born in the waters or in the atmosphere; यदग्ने<BR> दिविजा अस्यप्सुजा वा सहस्कृत Rv. 8. 43. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुजाः
अप्सु + .{@-ज, -जा@} + .({@-जाः@}), {@-योनिः@}<BR>—1 a horse.<BR>—2 a cane or reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुजा
अप्सु + .{@-ज, -जा@} <i>a.</i> born in the waters or in the atmosphere; यदग्ने<BR> दिविजा अस्यप्सुजा वा सहस्कृत Rv. 8. 43. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुजित्
अप्सु + .{@-जित्@} vanquishing the aerial Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुमत्|अप्सुमन्त्
अप्सु + .{@-मत्@} <i>a.</i> possessed of what is in water; not losing oneʼs nature<BR> in water (as lightning); getting sufficient water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सुयोनि
अप्सु + .{@-योनि@} <i>a.</i> born from the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अफल <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Unfruitful, fruitless, barren (lit. & fig.); याः फलिनीर्या अफलाः<BR> Rv. 10. 97. 15. ˚ला ओषधयः, ˚लं कार्यम् &c.<BR>—2 Unproductive, useless, vain; यथा षण्ढोऽफलः स्त्रीषु यथा गौर्गवि<BR> चाफला । यथा चाज्ञेऽफलं दानं तथा विप्रोऽनृचोऽफलः Ms. 2. 158.<BR>—3 Deprived of virility, castrated; emasculated; अफलोऽहं कृतस्तेन<BR> क्रोधात्सा च निराकृता Rām. 1. 49. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलः|अफल
अफल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 N. of a plant (Mar. झाबुक) Tamarix Indica<BR>—2 A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफला
अफल + .{@-ला@} The Aloe plant (Mar. घृतकुमारी कोरफड); another plant<BR> (Mar. भूम्यामलकी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अफलाकाङ्क्षिन्, अफलप्रेप्सु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलाकाङ्क्षिन्|अफलाकांक्षिन्
अफल + -आकाङ्क्षिन्, -प्रेप्सु <i>a.</i> one who desires no reward (for his labours),<BR> disinterested; अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञः क्रियते ब्रह्मवादिभिः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलप्रेप्सु
अफल + -आकाङ्क्षिन्, -प्रेप्सु <i>a.</i> one who desires no reward (for his labours),<BR> disinterested; अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञः क्रियते ब्रह्मवादिभिः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल्गु
अफल्गु <i>a.</i> Productive, profitable; तरीषु तत्रत्यमफल्गु भाण्डम् Śi. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन <i>a.</i> Frothless, without scum or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेनम्
अफेन + .{@-नम्@} Opium (perhaps a corruption of अहिफेन; अ has here a<BR> depreciative force).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्
अब्^1 = अम्ब्^2 q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: Verbs acc. to correspondence with AP90 etc..<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: Verbs acc. to correspondence with AP90 etc..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अबद्ध, -द्धक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 At liberty; not bound or restrained.<BR>—2 Unmeaning, nonsensical, absurd, contradictory; <i>e. g.</i> यावज्जीवमहं<BR> मौनी ब्रह्मचारी च मे पिता । माता तु मम वन्ध्यासीदपुत्रश्च पितामहः ॥<BR> (contradictory); जरद्गवः कम्बलपादुकाभ्यां द्वारि स्थितो गायति<BR> मङ्गलानि (v. l. मत्तकानि) । तं ब्राह्मणी पृच्छति पुत्रकामा राजनगर्यां<BR> लवणस्य कोऽर्घः ॥ Rāyamukuṭa on Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धक|अबद्धकं
अबद्ध, -द्धक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 At liberty; not bound or restrained.<BR>—2 Unmeaning, nonsensical, absurd, contradictory; <i>e. g.</i> यावज्जीवमहं<BR> मौनी ब्रह्मचारी च मे पिता । माता तु मम वन्ध्यासीदपुत्रश्च पितामहः ॥<BR> (contradictory); जरद्गवः कम्बलपादुकाभ्यां द्वारि स्थितो गायति<BR> मङ्गलानि (v. l. मत्तकानि) । तं ब्राह्मणी पृच्छति पुत्रकामा राजनगर्यां<BR> लवणस्य कोऽर्घः ॥ Rāyamukuṭa on Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धः|अबद्ध|अबद्धं
अबद्ध, -द्धक + .{@-द्धः@} Improper, impossible thing; नापध्यायेन्न स्पृहयेन्नाबद्धंचिन्तयेदसत्<BR> Mb. 12. 215. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबद्धमुख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धमुख|अबद्धमुखः
अबद्ध + -मुख <i>a.</i> foul-mouthed, abusive, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धवत्|अबद्धवन्त्
अबद्धवत् <i>a.</i> Unmeaning, ungrammatical; यस्मिन्प्रतिश्लोकमबद्धवत्यपि<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध
अबध, -ध्य<BR> See अवध-ध्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्य|अबध्यं
अबध, -ध्य<BR> See अवध-ध्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबधा
अबधा <i>f.</i> Segment of the basis of a triangle. See अबाधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धक|अबंधक
अबन्धक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not binding.<BR>—2 Without any pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धन|अबंधन
अबन्धन <i>a.</i> Free, without bonds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्र|अबंध्र
अबन्ध्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Without ligatures; falling asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धु|अबंधु
अबन्धु, -बान्धव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Friendless, lonely. त्वमेताञ्जनराज्ञो द्विर्दशाऽबन्धुना सुश्रवसोपजग्मुषः Rv. 1. 53. 9<BR>—2 Unowned.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबन्धुकृत्, अबन्धुकृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अबन्धु, -बान्धव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Friendless, lonely. त्वमेताञ्जनराज्ञो द्विर्दशाऽबन्धुना सुश्रवसोपजग्मुषः Rv. 1. 53. 9<BR>—2 Unowned.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबन्धुकृत्, अबन्धुकृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धुकृत्
अबन्धु + -कृत् <i>a.</i> causing want of companions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धुकृत
अबन्धु + -कृत <i>a.</i> not brought about by relatives, growing spontaneously;<BR> त्वय्यस्याः कथमप्यबान्धवकृतां स्नेहप्रवृत्तिं च ताम् Ś. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अबल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Weak, feeble, unprotected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलः|अबल|अबलं
अबल + .{@-लः@} N. of a plant Crataeva Roxburghii (वरुणवृक्ष) (Mar. वायवर्णा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबला
अबल + .{@-ला@} —1 A woman (as belonging to the weaker sex); नूनं हि ते<BR> कविवरा विपरीतबोधा ये नित्यमाहुरबला इति कामिनीनाम् । याभिर्विलोलतरतारकदृष्टिपातैः<BR> शक्रादयोऽपि विजितास्त्वबलाः कथं ताः ॥ Bh. 1. 10; compare also:− हृदये<BR> वहसि गिरीन्द्रौ त्रिभुवनजयिनी कटाक्षेण । अबला त्वं यदि मन्ये के<BR> बलवन्तो न जानीमः ॥ Udb. ˚जनः a woman^1; इष्टप्रवासजनितान्यबलाजनस्य<BR> दुःखानि … Ś. 4. 3; R. 9. 46.<BR>—2 One of the ten earths according to the Buddhists.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: 'a. italics' means 'a' here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलम्
अबल + .{@-लम्@} Weakness, want of strength; see बलाबलम् also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबलाबलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलाबलः|अबलाबल
अबल + -अबलः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलास
अबलास <i>a.</i> Not consumptive; Av. 8. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल्यम्
अबल्यम्<BR>—1 Weakness. स यत्रायमात्माऽबल्यं न्येत्य संमोहमिव Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 1.<BR>—2 Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अबाध <i>a.</i> Unrestrained, unobstructed.<BR>—2 Free from pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधा
अबाध + .{@-धा@} The segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधः|अबाध|अबाधं
अबाध + .{@-धः@}<BR>—1 Non-obstruction.<BR>—2 Non-refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधित
अबाधित <i>a.</i> Unimpeded, unrestricted, unrefuted; सहुरिः स्तन्नबाधितः Rv. 10. 92. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाल
अबाल, -अबालिश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not childish, youth; Nir. 9. 10^1.<BR>—2 Not young, full (as the moon).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबालिश
अबाल, -अबालिश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not childish, youth; Nir. 9. 10^1.<BR>—2 Not young, full (as the moon).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0165-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाह्य
अबाह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not exterior, internal; राज्ञः शिवं सावरजस्य भूयादित्याशशंसे<BR> करणैरबाह्यैः R. 14. 50;<BR>—2 (fig.) Familiar or intimately acquainted with, conversant with; गीतनृत्यवाद्यादिष्वबाह्यः Dk. 155.<BR>—3 Without an exterior; तदेतद् ब्रह्मापूर्वमनपरमनन्तरमबाह्यम्<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिन्धनः|अबिन्धन|अबिंधनः
अबिन्धनः [आपः एव इन्धनं यस्य] The submarine fire (that feeds<BR> on the waters of the ocean); अबिन्धनं वह्निमसौ बिभर्ति R. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिभीवस्
अबिभीवस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Fearless; इन्द्रेण सं हि दृक्षसे सञ्जग्मानो<BR> अविभ्युषा Rv. 1. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीज|अबीजः
अबीज (-जक)<BR> <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impotent, seedless; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—2 Causeless;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीजक
अबीज (-जक)<BR> <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impotent, seedless; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—2 Causeless;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीजः|अबीज
अबीज (-जक) + .{@-जः@} Victory over the mind;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीजा
अबीज (-जक) + .{@-जा@} a kind of grape (Mar. बेदाणा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीजम्
अबीज (-जक) + .{@-जम्@} An unproductive seed; अबीजविक्रयी Ms. 9. 291.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्ध|अबुद्धः
अबुद्ध <i>a.</i> Foolish, unwise; अपवादमात्रमबुद्धानाम् Sāṅ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धः|अबुद्ध
अबुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} The individual soul (जीवात्मा); अथ बुद्धमथाबुद्धमिमं<BR> गुणनिधिं शृणु Mb. 12. 308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धम्
अबुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 Inanimate, lifeless matter (जड); बुद्ध्यमानं महाप्राज्ञमबुद्धपरिवर्जनात्<BR> Mb. 12. 305. 31.<BR>—2 Ignorance (अज्ञान); एवमप्रतिबुद्धत्वादबुद्धमनुवर्तते Mb. 12. 303. 1.<BR> <i>ind.</i> Inadvertantly; न बुद्धिपूर्वं नाबुद्धं स्मरामीह<BR> कदाचन Rām. 2. 22. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिः|अबुद्धि
अबुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Want of understanding (अविद्या); अबुद्धिरज्ञानकृता प्रबुद्ध्या<BR> कृष्यते मनः Mb. 12. 204. 4.<BR>—2 Ignorance, stupidity; ˚मत् foolish, ignorant. <i>a.</i> Ignorant,<BR> dull-witted, stupid.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबुद्धिपूर्व, अबुद्धिपूर्वक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिपूर्व
अबुद्धिः + -पूर्व, -पूर्वक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not preceded by knowledge or consciousness; not wanton or intentional.<BR>—2 beginning with non-intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिपूर्वक|अबुद्धिपूर्व्वक
अबुद्धिः + -पूर्व, -पूर्वक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not preceded by knowledge or consciousness; not wanton or intentional.<BR>—2 beginning with non-intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिपूर्वम्
अबुद्धिः + -पूर्व, -पूर्वक + .({@-र्वम्, -र्वकम्@}) <i>adv.</i> unconsciously, ignorantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धीपूर्वकम्
अबुद्धिः + -पूर्व, -पूर्वक + .({@-र्वम्, -र्वकम्@}) <i>adv.</i> unconsciously, ignorantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्
अबुध्, -बुध <i>a.</i><BR> Foolish, stupid; (पुत्रस्नेहशुचातुरौ) पितरावन्वतप्येतां<BR> पुत्रयोरबुधौ बलम् Bhāg. 10. 44. 17. ━<i>m.</i> A fool. <i>f.</i> (अभुत्)<BR> Ignorance, want of intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध
अबुध्, -बुध <i>a.</i><BR> Foolish, stupid; (पुत्रस्नेहशुचातुरौ) पितरावन्वतप्येतां<BR> पुत्रयोरबुधौ बलम् Bhāg. 10. 44. 17. ━<i>m.</i> A fool. <i>f.</i> (अभुत्)<BR> Ignorance, want of intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्य
अबुध्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not to be perceived or awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अबोध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ignorant, foolish, stupid. —2 Perplexed, puzzled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधः|अबोध
अबोध + .{@-धः@} —1 Ignorance, stupidity, want of understanding; ˚धोपहताश्चान्ये<BR> Bh. 3. 2; निसर्गदुर्बोधमबोधविक्लवाः क्व भूपतीनां चरितं क्व जन्तवः Ki. 1. 6.<BR>—2 Not knowing or being aware of. जलदकालमबोधकृतं दिशामप रथाप<BR> रथावयवायुधः Śi. 6. 41<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अबोधगम्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधगम्य
अबोध + -गम्य <i>a.</i> incomprehensible, inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध्य
अबोध्य, अबोधनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unintelligible.<BR>—2 Not to be awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधनीय
अबोध्य, अबोधनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unintelligible.<BR>—2 Not to be awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्न
अबुध्न <i>a.</i> Having no bottom or root, bottomless. अबुध्ने राजा<BR> वरुणो वनस्य ऊर्ध्वं स्तूपं ददते पूतदक्षः Rv. 1. 24. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0166-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

