अभयंकर|अभयङ्कर
अभयंकर, -कृत्^1 <i>a.</i><BR> [अ-भय-कृ with the insertion of खच् मेघर्तिभयेषु<BR> कृञ्ः P. III. 2. 43].<BR>—1 Not dreadful.<BR>—2 Causing security. यत इन्द्र भयामहे ततो नो अभयं कृधि । Rv. 8. 61. 13<BR> सोमपा अभयंकरः Rv. 10. 152. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: anusvara placement wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयंकृत्|अभयङ्कृत्
अभयंकर, -कृत्^1 <i>a.</i><BR> [अ-भय-कृ with the insertion of खच् मेघर्तिभयेषु<BR> कृञ्ः P. III. 2. 43].<BR>—1 Not dreadful.<BR>—2 Causing security. यत इन्द्र भयामहे ततो नो अभयं कृधि । Rv. 8. 61. 13<BR> सोमपा अभयंकरः Rv. 10. 152. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: anusvara placement wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभर्तृका
अभर्तृका<BR>—1 A widow.<BR>—2 An unmarried woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवः|अभव
अभवः<BR>—1 Non-existence; मत्त एव भवाभवौ Mb.<BR>—2 Absolution, final beatitude; प्राप्तुमभवमभिवाञ्छति वा Ki. 12. 30, 18. 27.<BR>—3 End or destruction; अद्यैव सर्वभूतानां रक्षसामभवाय च Rām. 3. 64. 56.<BR> सुखं च दुःखं च भवाभवात्मकम् Mb. 3. 295. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवत्
अभवत् <i>a.</i> Not existing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभवन्मतयोगः, अभवन्मतसंयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवन्मतयोगः|अभवन्मतयोग
अभवत् + अभवन्मतयोगः, अभवन्मतसंयोगः (in Rhet.) a defect in composition;<BR> अभवन् असंभवन्नपि मतः इष्टः योगः सम्बन्धः यत्र K. P. 7; the<BR> ‘failure of an intended connection’, or want of harmony between the ideas<BR> to be expressed and the words expressing them; <i>e. g.</i> ईक्षसे यत्कटाक्षेण<BR> तदा धन्वी मनोभवः, here the word यत् can have no <i>Correlation</i><BR> with तदा though intended by the poet. The proper reading would be<BR> ईक्षसे चेत् &c.; for other examples see S. D. 575 <i>ad loc.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवन्मतसंयोगः
अभवत् + अभवन्मतयोगः, अभवन्मतसंयोगः (in Rhet.) a defect in composition;<BR> अभवन् असंभवन्नपि मतः इष्टः योगः सम्बन्धः यत्र K. P. 7; the<BR> ‘failure of an intended connection’, or want of harmony between the ideas<BR> to be expressed and the words expressing them; <i>e. g.</i> ईक्षसे यत्कटाक्षेण<BR> तदा धन्वी मनोभवः, here the word यत् can have no <i>Correlation</i><BR> with तदा though intended by the poet. The proper reading would be<BR> ईक्षसे चेत् &c.; for other examples see S. D. 575 <i>ad loc.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवनिः|अभवनि
अभवनिः Non-birth; Hariv. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव्य
अभव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be, not predestined;<BR>—2 Improper.<BR>—3 unfortunate; उपगतमवधीरयन्त्यभव्याः Ki. 10. 51.<BR>—4 uncivil, rude; अभव्यो भव्यरूपेण Rām. 4. 17. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्रका
अभस्त्रका, अभस्त्रिका also अभस्त्राका<BR> [{@अ-भस्त्रा@} P. VII. 3. 47.]<BR>—1 A badly made or inferior pair of bellows.<BR>—2 A young woman who has no bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0168-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्रिका
