अभिख्या
अभिख्या + .{@-ख्या@} [ख्या-अङ्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Splendour, beauty, lustre; काप्यभिख्या तयोरासीद् व्रजतोः शुद्धवेषयोः<BR> R. 1. 46; सूर्यापाये न खलु कमलं पुष्यति स्वामभिख्याम् Me. 82; Ku. 1. 43, 7. 18.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A gracious look; अभिख्यानो मघवन्नाधमानान् Rv. 10. 112. 10.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Look, view, appearance, aspect (Ved.).<BR>—2 Telling, declaring.<BR>—3 Calling, addressing.<BR>—4 A name, appellation.<BR>—5 A word, synonym.<BR>—6 Fame, glory; notoriety (in a bad sense); greatness (माहात्म्यम्).<BR>—7 Intellect (Nir.). अभिख्या-कीर्ति-माहात्म्यनामशोभास्वपि स्त्रियाम् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यात
अभिख्यात <i>p. p.</i> Become or made known; celebrated; ˚दोषः Y. 3. 300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यातृ
अभिख्यातृ <i>a.</i> Ved. Looking, supervising, Superintending; Rv. 4. 17. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यानम्
अभिख्यानम् Fame, Glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्
अभिगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go to, go near to, approach (with acc.); एनमभिजग्मुर्महर्षयः<BR> R. 15. 59; Ki. 10. 21; मनुमेकाग्रमासीनमभिगम्य महर्षयः Ms. 1. 1, 11. 100.<BR>—2 To follow; go after; अनुरागाद्वने रामं दिष्ट्या त्वमभिगच्छसि Rām.<BR>—3 To find; meet with (casually or by chance).<BR>—4 To cohabit; have sexual intercourse (with man or woman); अभिगन्तास्मि<BR> भगिनीं मातरं वा तवेति ह Y. 2. 205; अभ्यगच्छः पतिं यत्त्वं भजमानम् Mb.<BR>—5 To take to, undertake, betake oneself to.<BR>—6 To get, to share in; be subject to; निद्रामभिगतः Rām.<BR>—7 To conceive, apprehend, understand, comprehend.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to go to or approach; take, convey; send; Dk. 102.<BR>—2 To cause to apprehend; explain, teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगन्तृ|अभिगंतृ
अभिगन्तृ <i>a.</i> One who approaches or has intercourse (with a woman);<BR> one who understands &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमः|अभिगम
अभिगमः, -गमनम<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Approaching^1, going or coming to visit, arrival; तवार्हतो नाभिगमेन<BR> तृप्तम् R. 5. 11, 17. 72; ज्येष्ठाभिगमनात्पूर्वं तेनाप्यनभिनन्दिता 12. 35,<BR> K. 158; Pt. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Finding out; enjoying; कृत्वा तासामभिगममपाम् Me. 51. (सेवनम् Malli.).<BR>—2 Sexual intercourse (with a man or woman); परदाराभिगमनम् K. 107;<BR> प्रसह्य दास्यभिगमे Y. 2. 291; Pt. 1; वरं क्लैब्यं पुंसां<BR> न च परकलत्राभिगमनम् H. 1. 116; नीच˚ Y. 3. 297, 2. 294.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमनम
अभिगमः, -गमनम<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Approaching^1, going or coming to visit, arrival; तवार्हतो नाभिगमेन<BR> तृप्तम् R. 5. 11, 17. 72; ज्येष्ठाभिगमनात्पूर्वं तेनाप्यनभिनन्दिता 12. 35,<BR> K. 158; Pt. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Finding out; enjoying; कृत्वा तासामभिगममपाम् Me. 51. (सेवनम् Malli.).<BR>—2 Sexual intercourse (with a man or woman); परदाराभिगमनम् K. 107;<BR> प्रसह्य दास्यभिगमे Y. 2. 291; Pt. 1; वरं क्लैब्यं पुंसां<BR> न च परकलत्राभिगमनम् H. 1. 116; नीच˚ Y. 3. 297, 2. 294.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्य
अभिगम्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be approached, visited or sought; अद्यप्रभृति भूतानामधिगम्योऽस्मि<BR> शुद्धये Ku. 6. 56.<BR>—2 Accessible, that can be approached without fear, inviting; तथाप्यनभिगमनीयो<BR> लोकस्य Mk. 4; भीमकान्तैर्नृपगुणैः … अधृष्यश्चाभिगम्यश्च R. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभिगामिन् <i>a.</i> Approaching, having intercourse with; ऋतुकालाभिगामी<BR> स्यात् स्वदारनिरतः सदा Ms. 3. 45; Y. 2. 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामुक
अभिगामुक <i>a.</i> Inviting, leading one to approach (as qualities).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्ज्
अभिगर्ज् €1 P. To roar or bawl at, to raise wild or ferocious cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्जनम्
अभिगर्जनम्, अभिगर्जितम् A wild, savage or ferocious roar; up-roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्जितम्
अभिगर्जनम्, अभिगर्जितम् A wild, savage or ferocious roar; up-roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगा
अभिगा = अभी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगाह्
अभिगाह् To penetrate into; अभि गोत्राणि सहसा गाहमानः Rv. 10. 103. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुप्
अभिगुप् €10 P.<BR>—1 To guard, protect, defend; लङ्कायामभिगुप्तायां सागरेण समन्ततः Rām.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुप्तिः|अभिगुप्ति
अभिगुप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Guarding, protecting.<BR>—2 Self-denial, self-control; तपो दमः सत्यमात्माभिगुप्तिः Mb. 12. 299. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगोप्तृ
अभिगोप्तृ <i>m.</i> Protector, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुर्
अभिगुर् €6 U. To assent or agree to, approve of (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगूर्त|अभिगूर्त्त
अभिगूर्त <i>p. p.</i> Approved of; destined for an offering; uttered<BR> (with praise). इष्टं वीतम् अभिगूर्तं वषट्कृतम् Rv. 1. 162. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगूर्तिः|अभिगूर्ति|अभिगूर्त्ति
अभिगूर्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Song of praise; constant desire or thought; तेषामभिगूर्तिर्न इन्वतु Rv. 1. 162. 6.<BR>—2 Effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगृध्न
अभिगृध्न <i>a.</i> One with a longing, covetous Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगॄ
अभिगॄ €9 U. Ved.<BR>—1 To call to or address approvingly, join in, welcome, praise.<BR>—2 To accept propitiously, allow, approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगरः|अभिगर
अभिगरः [गॄ-अप्] Song of praise; praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगै
अभिगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To call to, sing to.<BR>—2 To fill with song, make noisy with songs; भृङ्गराजाभिगीतानि (वनानि) Rām.<BR>—3 To sing, celebrate in song; तदप्येष श्लोकोऽभिगीतः Ait. Br.<BR>—4 To approve, allow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगीत
अभिगीत <i>p. p.</i> Sung, chanted, celebrated in song &c. <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sung, chanted well; अभिगीतमिदं गीतं सर्वगीतिषु कोविदौ Rām. 1. 4. 27.<BR>—2 Addressed, praised in song; अपघ्नन्नेषि पवमान शत्रून् प्रियां न<BR> जारो अभिगीत इन्दुः Rv. 9. 96. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगेष्ण
अभिगेष्ण, -ष्णु <i>a.</i><BR> [गै-इष्णुच्] Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगेष्णु
अभिगेष्ण, -ष्णु <i>a.</i><BR> [गै-इष्णुच्] Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रह्
अभिग्रह् (Ved. -ग्रभ्) €9 U.<BR>—1 To take or seize, catch, catch hold of, seize forcibly, attack; रिपुणाभिगृह्य<BR> Dk. 5, 98, 103.<BR>—2 To accept, take.<BR>—3 To receive (as a guest).<BR>—4 To fold, lay or bring together (as the hands).<BR>—5 To set, show or bring forth (as blossom, fruit &c.).<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To catch or surprise one in the very act, to let oneself be<BR> so caught; अर्यवर्यस्य कस्यचिद् गृहे चोरयित्वा रूपाभिग्राहितो बद्धः Dk. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रभ्
अभिग्रह् (Ved. -ग्रभ्) €9 U.<BR>—1 To take or seize, catch, catch hold of, seize forcibly, attack; रिपुणाभिगृह्य<BR> Dk. 5, 98, 103.<BR>—2 To accept, take.<BR>—3 To receive (as a guest).<BR>—4 To fold, lay or bring together (as the hands).<BR>—5 To set, show or bring forth (as blossom, fruit &c.).<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To catch or surprise one in the very act, to let oneself be<BR> so caught; अर्यवर्यस्य कस्यचिद् गृहे चोरयित्वा रूपाभिग्राहितो बद्धः Dk. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहः|अभिग्रह
अभिग्रहः<BR>—1 Seizing, robbing, plundering शङ्कारूपकर्माभिग्रहः Kau. A. 4.<BR>—2 Attack, assault, onset. यातव्यामित्रयोरभिग्रहचिन्ता Kau. A. 7.<BR>—3 Challenge.<BR>—4 Complaint.<BR>—5 Authority, power, weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहणम्
अभिग्रहणम् Robbing, seizing in the presence of the owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगृहीत
अभिगृहीत <i>a.</i> Taken hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगृहीतपाणि
अभिगृहीत + .{@-पाणि@} <i>a.</i> Having the hands joined; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघर्षणम्
अभिघर्षणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>—2 Possession by an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभिघात, -घातक, -तकिन् &c.<BR> See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातक|अभिघातकः
अभिघात, -घातक, -तकिन् &c.<BR> See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातकिन्
अभिघात, -घातक, -तकिन् &c.<BR> See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघृ
अभिघृ (Used only in <i>caus.</i>)<BR>—1 To cause to trickle down, let fall down by drops; तां (वपां)<BR> आध्वर्युः स्रुवेणाभिघारयन्नाह Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To sprinkle with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघारः|अभिघार
अभिघारः [घृ-णिच्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>—2 Dropping down ghee upon offerings at sacrifices; प्रणीतपृषदाज्याभिघारघोरस्तनूनपात् Mv. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघारणम्
अभिघारणम् Act of sprinkling (with ghee), besprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघ्रा
अभिघ्रा €1 P. To smell at, snuffle; to bring the nose close to anotherʼs<BR> forehead (as in caressing, kissing &c. as a token of affection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघ्राणम्
अभिघ्राणम् Smelling at or touching the forehead with the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचक्ष्
अभिचक्ष् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To look at, view, perceive, see; अभि यो विश्वा भुवनानि चष्टे (सूर्यः) Rv. 7. 61. 1.<BR>—2 To call to or address.<BR>—3 To address sharply, to assail with sharp words. यो मा पाकेन मनसा<BR> चरन्तमभिचष्टे अनृतेभिर्वचोभिः Rv. 7. 104. 8.<BR>—4 To name, call.<BR>—5 To look graciously upon; कदा चिकित्वो अभिचक्षसे नो Rv. 5. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचक्षणम्
अभिचक्षणम् Ved. Means of defence; (magical) remedy; Av. 6. 127. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचक्षणा
अभिचक्षणम् + .{@-णा@} Viewing, indicating; Av. 9 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचर्
अभिचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To act wrongly towards any one, offend, trespass; तत्र विराधदनुकबन्धप्रभृतयः<BR> केऽप्यभिचरन्तीति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">Page0171-1</a>]<BR> श्रुतम् Mv. 2.<BR>—2 To be faithless (as wife or husband) पतिं या नाभिचरति मनोवाग्देहसंयता<BR> Ms. 5. 165, 9. 102.<BR>—3 To charm, conjure, exorcise (by spell or incantations), employ spells<BR> for magical purposes &c. Rv. 10. 34. 14; वृष्टयायुःपुष्टिकामो वा तथैवाभिचरन्नपि<BR> Y. 1. 295, 3. 288.<BR>—4 to possess, occupy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0170-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरः|अभिचर
अभिचरः A follower, servant, attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरणम्
अभिचरणम् Enchanting, exorcising, employment of spells for malevolent<BR> purposes (such as श्येनयाग); कौटिल्यः कोपनोऽपि स्वयमभिचरणे<BR> ज्ञातदुःखः प्रतिज्ञाम् Mu. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरणीय
अभिचरणीय <i>a.</i> Fit for exorcising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरितुः|अभिचरितु
अभिचरितुः <i>f.</i> Ved. Enchanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारः|अभिचार
अभिचारः<BR>—1 Exorcising, enchanting, employment of magical spells for malevolent<BR> purposes; magic itself (being regarded as one of the Upapātakas or minor<BR> sins); दिग्गजैर्दन्दशूकैश्च अभिचारावपातनैः Bhāg. 7. 5. 43; अभिचारेषु<BR> सर्वेषु कर्तव्यो द्विशतो दमः Ms. 9. 290, 11. 63. 197; K. 109; ब्रह्मद्विषो<BR> ह्येष निहन्ति सर्वानाथर्वणस्तीव्र इवाभिचारः Mv. 1. 62.<BR>—2 Killing गतः क्रियां मन्त्र इवाभिचारिकीम् Ki. 3. 56.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिचारकल्पः, अभिचारज्वरः, अभिचारमन्त्रः, अभिचारयज्ञः, अभिचारहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारकल्पः|अभिचारकल्प
अभिचारः + -कल्पः N. of a work on incantations regarded as part of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारज्वरः|अभिचारज्वर
अभिचारः + -ज्वरः a fever caused by magical spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारमन्त्रः|अभिचारमन्त्र
अभिचारः + -मन्त्रः a magical formula, an incantation or formula for working<BR> a charm; स्फुटमिदमभिचारमन्य एक Śi. 7. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारयज्ञः|अभिचारयज्ञ
अभिचारः + -यज्ञः, -होमः a sacrifice made for magical purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारहोमः|अभिचारहोम
अभिचारः + -यज्ञः, -होमः a sacrifice made for magical purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारक|अभिचारकः
अभिचारक, -चारिन् (˚रिकी, ˚रिणी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Conjuring, enchanting,<BR> using magical spells for evil purposes; magical. Ki. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिन्
अभिचारक, -चारिन् (˚रिकी, ˚रिणी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Conjuring, enchanting,<BR> using magical spells for evil purposes; magical. Ki. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारकः|अभिचारक
अभिचारक, -चारिन् + .{@-कः, -री@} A conjurer, magician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारी
अभिचारक, -चारिन् + .{@-कः, -री@} A conjurer, magician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिच्छाय
अभिच्छाय <i>a.</i> Being in shade or turned towards the shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिच्छायम्
अभिच्छाय + .{@-यम्@} <i>adv.</i> In shade or darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजन्
अभिजन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born to or for (a person or thing), to win, to claim as oneʼs<BR> birth-right; स महीमभिजायते Mb. 5. 129. 33; see also under अभिजात (1) below.<BR>—2 be born or produced, arise, spring from; कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते Bg. 2. 62;<BR> स्वाभाविकं तु यन्मित्रं भाग्येनैवाभिजायते H. 1. 178.<BR>—3 To be born or produced again; शुचीनां श्रीमतां गेहे योगभ्रष्टोऽभिजायते<BR> Bg. 6. 41, 13. 23.<BR>—4 To be, become, be turned into; तस्याः स्पृष्ट्वैव सलिलं नरः शैलोऽभिजायते Rām.<BR>—5 To be born of a high family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज
अभिज <i>a.</i> Born or produced all round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनः|अभिजन
अभिजनः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A family, race, lineage; कलहंसकादभिजनं ज्ञात्वा Māl. 8;<BR> नाभिजनमीक्षते K. 104; पतिं त्यक्त्वा देवं भुवनपतिमुच्चैराभिजनम्<BR> Mu. 6. 6; Ms. 4. 18; Dk. 135, 170; U. 4.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Birth, extraction, descent; तुल्याभिजनेषु भूमिभरेषु (धरेषु ?)<BR> राज्ञां वृत्तिः M. 1; Ms. 1. 100; Y. 1. 123.<BR>—2 High or noble descent, noble birth or family; तान्गुणान्संप्रधार्याहमग्र्यं<BR> चाभिजनं तव Rām. 4. 17. 20; स्तुतं तन्माहात्म्यं यदभिजनतो यच्च<BR> गुणतः Māl. 2. 13; शीलं शैलतटात्पतत्वभिजनः संदह्यतां वह्निना<BR> Bh. 2. 39; M. 5.<BR>—3 Fore-fathers, ancestors; अभिजनाः पूर्वे बान्धवाः Kāśi. on P. IV. 3. 90;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">Page0171-2</a>]<BR> also descendants.<BR>—4 Native country, motherland, ancestral abode (opp. निवास); cf.<BR> Sk. on P. IV. 3. 90 यत्र स्वयं वसति स निवासः (यत्र संप्रति<BR> उष्यते Mbh.); यत्र पूर्वैरुषितं सोऽभिजनः इति विवेकः<BR>—5 Fame, celebrity.<BR>—6 The head or ornament of family; यद्विद्वानपि तादृशेऽप्यभिजने धर्म्यात्पथो<BR> विच्युतः Mv. 1. 33.<BR>—7 Attendants, retinue (परिजन q. v.); वयसा शास्त्रतो धैर्यात्<BR> कुलेनाभिजनेन च Mb. 5. 12. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनन
अभिजनन (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Becoming oneʼs high birth; Mv. 5. 18. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनवत्|अभिजनवन्त्
अभिजनवत् <i>a.</i> Of noble descent, nobly born; ˚तीम् मालविकाम्<BR> M. 5; ˚वतो भर्तुः श्लाघ्ये स्थिता गृहिणीपदे Ś. 4. 19; आढपोऽभिजनवानस्मि Bg. 16. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनितुः|अभिजनितु
अभिजनितुः <i>f.</i> Ved. Being born or produced (Ved.); ˚तोः to produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजात|अभिजातः
अभिजात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Born to or for; भवन्ति संपदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत Bg. 16. 3, 4, 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Produced all around.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Born in consequence of.<BR>—2 Inbred, inborn.<BR>—3 Born, produced; अजातपक्षामभिजातकण्ठीम् Rām. सर्वे तुल्याभिजातीया<BR> यथा देवास्तथा वयम् Mb. 12. 166. 29.<BR>—4 Noble, nobly or well born, of noble descent; तेऽभिजाता महेष्वासाः<BR> Mb. 6. 77. 62; जात्यस्तेनाभिजातेन शूरः शौर्यवता कुशः R. 17. 4;<BR> Māl. 4; courteous, polite; अभिजातं खल्वस्य वचनम् V. 1; K. 102,<BR> M. 3; Māl. 7; अनभिजाते Mu. 2.<BR>—5 Fit, proper, worthy.<BR>—6 Sweet, agreeable; प्रजल्पितायामभिजातवाचि Ku. 1. 45.<BR>—7 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>—8 Learned, wise; distinguished; संकीर्णं नाभिजातेषु नाप्रबुद्धेषु संस्कृतम्<BR> (वदेत्); अभिजातः कुलजे बुधे Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजातम्
अभिजात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Nobility, noble birth.<BR>—2 Birth ceremony (जातकर्मन्); यथा हि सूत्यामभिजातकोविदाः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 6. 1. ━<i>adv.</i> Nobly, politely, courteously; ˚तं खलु एष<BR> वारितः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजातिः|अभिजाति
अभिजातिः <i>f.</i> Noble birth. Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजि
अभिजि €1 P.<BR>—1 To conquer completely.<BR>—2 To acquire by conquest. ━<i>Desid.</i> To desire to win or conquer, acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजयः|अभिजय
अभिजयः Conquest; complete victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजित्
अभिजित् <i>a.</i> [अभि-जि-क्विप्]<BR>—1 Victorious, conquering completely. पराभिजिद्गन्धनगन्धवाहः Rām. 6. 109. 12.<BR>—2 Helping in conquering completely.<BR>—3 Born under the constellation अभिजित् P. IV. 3. 36, see अभिजित. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of a sacrifice, part of the great sacrifice called गवामयन;<BR> (यजेत) अभिजिद्विश्वजिद्भ्यां वा Ms. 11. 75, also used for अतिरात्र q. v.<BR>—3 N. of a star; N. of one of the lunar mansions.<BR>—4 Name of a son (Hariv.) or the father (V. P.) of Punarvasu. <i>n.</i><BR>—1 The 8th Muhūrta of the day, mid-day (fit for a Śrāddha ceremony).<BR>—2 N. of a लग्न favourable to setting out.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिजिन्मुहूर्तः, अभिजिद्विश्वजितौ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजिन्मुहूर्तः|अभिजिन्मुहूर्त
अभिजित् + -मुहूर्तः The 8th Muhūrta or period comprising 24 minutes before<BR> and 24 minutes after noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजिद्विश्वजितौ
अभिजित् + -विश्वजितौ the two Soma-sacrifices Abhijit and Viśvajit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0171-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजितः|अभिजित
अभिजितः N. of an asterism or the Muhūrta indicated by it; मुहूर्तेऽभिजिते<BR> प्राप्ते सार्धरात्रे विभूषिते । देवक्यजनयद्विष्णुं यशोदा तां तु कन्यकाम् ॥ V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजितिः|अभिजिति
अभिजितिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Victory, conquest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजुष्
अभिजुष् €6 Ā. (or Ved. P.)<BR>—1 To visit, frequent, call upon; श्रियाभिजुष्टः Mb.<BR>—2 To be pleased or contented with, like, be fond of (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजुष्ट
अभिजुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Visited, frequented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञा
अभिज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To recognize, discern; (सा) नाभ्यजानान्नलं नृपम् Mb.<BR>—2 To know, understand, be acquainted with, be aware of, perceive; अहं<BR> हि नाभिजानामि भवेदेवं न वेति वा Mb.; Bg. 18. 55, 4. 14, 7. 13; भवदभिज्ञातं<BR> कथयतु Dk. 3, 78.<BR>—3 To look upon, consider or regard as, know to be.<BR>—4 To admit, own, acknowledge; न पुत्रमभिजानामि त्वयि जातम् Mb. 5<BR> To remember; recollect; used with the Future instead of the Imperfect.<BR> Imperfect with यत्, or both when interdependence of two actions is<BR> denoted, P. III. 2. 112, 114; cf. Bk. 6. 138, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञ|अभिज्ञः
अभिज्ञ <i>a.</i> [ज्ञा-क]<BR>—1 Knowing, aware of, one who understands or is acquainted with, experiencing<BR> or having had experience of (with gen. or loc. in comp.); कान्तारवनदुर्गाणामभिज्ञा<BR> Rām. 4. 39. 28. यद्वा कौशलमिन्द्रसूनुदमने तत्राप्यभिज्ञो जनः<BR> U. 5. 34; अभिज्ञाच्छेदपातानां क्रियन्ते नन्दनद्रुमाः Ku. 2. 41; Me. 16;<BR> R. 7. 64; अनभिज्ञो भवान्सेवाधर्मस्य Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Skilled in, conversant with, proficient, skilful, clever; यदि त्वमीदृशः<BR> कथायामभिज्ञः U. 4., see अनभिज्ञ also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञः|अभिज्ञ
अभिज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञः@} Brahmā, The Almighty; देहाद्यपार्थमसदन्त्यमभिज्ञमात्रं<BR> विन्देत ते तर्हि सर्वमनीषितार्थम् Bhāg. 12. 8. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञा
अभिज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञा@}<BR>—1 Recognition.<BR>—2 Remembrance, recollection; अभिज्ञावचने लृट् P. III. 2. 112.<BR>—3 A supernatural faculty or power of which five kinds are usually mentioned:−<BR> (1) taking any form at will; (2) hearing to any distance; (3) seeing to<BR> any distance; (4) penetrating menʼs thoughts; (5) knowing their state<BR> and antecedents. Monier Williams. cf. नामस्मृत्योरभिज्ञा स्यात् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञता
अभिज्ञता, -त्वम्<BR> the knowledge of; शङ्खस्वनाभिज्ञतया निवृत्ताः R. 7. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञत्वम्
अभिज्ञता, -त्वम्<BR> the knowledge of; शङ्खस्वनाभिज्ञतया निवृत्ताः R. 7. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञात
अभिज्ञात <i>a.</i> One who knows, understands; महात्मा रजनीचरः<BR> अभिज्ञातस्य मायानाम् Rām. 6. 85. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानम्
अभिज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Recognition; तदभिज्ञानहेतोर्हि दत्तं तेन महात्मना Rām. (आभिज्ञान<BR> is a combination of अनुभव or direct perception and स्मृति or<BR> recollection; a sort of direct perception assisted by the memory; as when<BR> we say ‘this is the same man I saw yesterday’ सोऽयं ह्यो दृष्टो नरः,<BR> अनुभव or direct perception leading to the identification expressed<BR> by अयम् and the memory leading to the reference to past action expressed by सः).<BR>—2 Remembrance, recollection; knowledge, ascertainment.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A sign or token of recognition (person or thing); वत्स योगिन्यस्मि<BR> मालत्यभिज्ञानं च धारयामि Māl. 9; Bk. 8. 118, 124; R. 12. 62;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">Page0172-2</a>]<BR> Me. 114; उपपन्नेराभिज्ञानैर्दूतं तमवगच्छत Rām.<BR>—4 The dark portion in the disc of the moon. cf. आभिज्ञानं स्मृतावपि ।<BR> गर्वे ज्ञाने च हिंसायां प्रणवे च समीरितम् Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिज्ञानाभरणम्, अभिज्ञानपत्रम्, अभिज्ञानशकुन्तलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानाभरणम्
अभिज्ञानम् + -आभरणम् a recognition-ornament, a token-ring. अभिज्ञानाभरणदर्शनेन<BR> शापो निवर्तिष्यते Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानपत्रम्
अभिज्ञानम् + -पत्रम् a certificate, letter of recommendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानशकुन्तलम्
अभिज्ञानम् + -शकुन्तलम्^1 N. of a celebrated drama by Kālidāsa in seven acts,<BR> in which king Duṣyanta marries Kaṇvaʼs foster daughter Śakuntalā by<BR> the Gāndharva form of marriage, forgets all about her owing to the curse<BR> of Durvāsas, but ultimately recollects, at the sight of the token-ring<BR> (अभिज्ञान) that he had duly married her; अभिज्ञानेन स्मृता शकुन्तला<BR> अभिज्ञानशकुन्तला; तामधिकृत्य कृतं नाटकं˚ शाकुन्तलम्; (the reading<BR> ˚शाकुन्तलम् is grammatically indefensible).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञापक
अभिज्ञापक <i>a.</i> Making known, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञु
अभिज्ञु <i>n.</i> Ved. [अभिगते जानुनी येन] On the knees, kneeling<BR> up to the knees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिडीनम्
अभिडीनम् Flying towards; अभिडीनं महाडीनम् Mb. 8. 41. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितड्
अभितड् €10 P.<BR>—1 To beat, knock, thump, hit, smite, strike (fig. also); to wound; वाक्शरैरभिताडितः Rām.<BR>—2 (Astr.) To eclipse the greater part of the disc; उल्काभिताडितशिखः<BR> शिखी शिवः Bṛ. S. 11. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताडनम्
अभिताडनम् Beating, thumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्
अभितप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To irradiate with heat, heat, inflame, अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते<BR> कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43, 19. 56.<BR>—2 To pain, distress, wound, afflict. ━<i>pass.</i> To suffer intensely, be afflicted.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To pain, distress, afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्त
अभितप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated, inflamed, scorched, burnt.<BR>—2 Distressed, grieving or lamenting for (actively used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितापः|अभिताप
अभितापः Extreme heat, whether of body or mind; agitation, affliction,<BR> great distress or pain; Śi. 9. 1; Ki. 9. 4; बलवान्पुनर्मे मनसोऽभितापः V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितराम्
अभितराम्^1 <i>ind.</i> Nearer to.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितस्
अभितस् <i>ind.</i> (Used as an adverb or preposition with acc.)<BR>—1 Near to, to, towards; अभितस्तं पृथासूनुः स्नेहेन परितस्तरे Ki. 11. 8.<BR> संनद्धा निर्ययुस्तूर्णं राक्षसानभितः पुरान् Rām. 7. 27. 22.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Near, hard by, close by, in the proximity of; ततो राजाब्रवीद्वाक्यं<BR> सुमन्त्रमभितः स्थितम् Rām.; sometimes with gen.; निषसादाभितस्तस्य <i>ibid.</i><BR>——(<i>b</i>) Before, in the presence of; तन्वन्तमिद्धमभितो गुरुमंशुजालम् Ki. 2. 59.<BR>—3 Opposite to, facing, in front of; त्रिपथगामभितः Ki. 6. 1, 5. 14.<BR>—4 On both sides; चूडाचुम्बितकङ्कपत्रमभितस्तूणीद्वयं पृष्ठतः<BR> U. 4, 20; Mv. 1. 18; पादपैः पुष्पपत्राणि सृजद्भिरभितो नदीम् Rām.<BR> Ś. 6. 17; Bk. 9. 137.<BR>—5 Before and after.<BR>—6 On all sides, कीर्त्याभितः सुरभितः Dk. 1; round, round about (with<BR> acc. or gen.); परिजनो यथाव्यापारं राजानमभितः स्थितः M. 1; Ś. 7;<BR> यस्याभितः U. 6. 36; everywhere; Ki. 8. 10.<BR>—7 Entirely, thoroughly,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">Page0173-1</a>]<BR> completely, throughout.<BR>—8 Quickly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभितोस्थि, अभितोभाविन्, अभितोरात्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितोस्थि
अभितस् + -अस्थि <i>a.</i> surrounded by bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितोभाविन्
अभितस् + -भाविन् <i>a.</i> being all round, surrounding; P. VI. 2. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितोरात्रम्
अभितस् + -रात्रम् Ved. near the night; just at the beginning or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताम्र
अभिताम्र <i>a.</i> Very red, dark red; अथ धूमाभिताम्राक्षम् R. 15. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितृप्
अभितृप् €10 P.<BR>—1 To satiate, satisfy.<BR>—2 To refresh; उर्वी पयसाभितर्पयद्भिः Bṛ. S. 19. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभित्वरमाणकः
अभित्वरमाणकः A messenger (EI. IV. 250, XVII. 321).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितर्पणम्
अभितर्पणम् Satiation, refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदक्षिणम्
अभिदक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> To or towards the right (= प्रदक्षिणम् q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदापनम्
अभिदापनम् The Being trodden under the foot by elephants (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदृश्
अभिदृश् €1 P. To look at, behold. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To show, point out.<BR>—2 To show oneself to, appear before. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be seen, be visible, appear.<BR>—2 To be considered or thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदर्शनम्
अभिदर्शनम्<BR>—1 Seeing.<BR>—2 Becoming visible; appearance. पथि मोषाभिदर्शने शक्तितो नाभिधावन्तो Ms. 9. 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदेवनम्
अभिदेवनम् A board for playing at dice; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्यु|अभिद्युः
अभिद्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Directed to heaven, tending or going to heaven, heavenward.<BR>—2 Heavenly.<BR>—3 Bright, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्युः|अभिद्यु
अभिद्यु + .{@-द्युः@} A half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रु
अभिद्रु €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To run up to, run near; पयस्यभिद्रवति भुवं युगावधौ Śi. 17. 40.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To invade, march against, fall upon, attack, assail; मकरन्देन<BR> प्रतिहतो जामाता बलात्कारेण अभिद्रवन् Māl. 7 laying violent hands<BR> on; गजा इवान्योऽन्यमभिद्रवन्तः (वारिधराः) Mk. 5. 21; Ve. 3.<BR>—2 To overrun; infest, harass, afflict; जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिवेदनाभिरभिद्रुतम्<BR> (देहम्) Mb.<BR>—3 To come over, pass or run over.<BR>—4 To befall. ━<i>Caus.</i> To rout, put to flight; पुररक्षानभिद्राव्य Dk. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुत
अभिद्रुत <i>p. p.</i> Attacked, overrun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रवः|अभिद्रव
अभिद्रवः, -वणम्<BR> An attack; a manouvre in battle; अभिद्रवणमप्लावमवस्थानं<BR> सविग्रहम् । परावृत्तमपावृत्तमपद्रुतमवप्लुतम् Rām. 6. 40. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रवणम्
अभिद्रवः, -वणम्<BR> An attack; a manouvre in battle; अभिद्रवणमप्लावमवस्थानं<BR> सविग्रहम् । परावृत्तमपावृत्तमपद्रुतमवप्लुतम् Rām. 6. 40. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुह्
अभिद्रुह् €4 P. (Ā. in epic poetry) To hate, seek to injure or maliciously<BR> assail, plot againt (with acc.); नित्यमस्मच्छरीरमभिद्रोग्धुं यतते<BR> Mu. 1, 2; क्रूरमभिद्रुह्यति Sk. (sometimes with dat. also); मया<BR> पुनरेभ्य एवाभिद्रुग्धमज्ञेन U. 6; नाभिद्रुह्यति भूतेभ्यः Bhāg.; Mu. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुग्ध
अभिद्रुग्ध a<BR>—1 Injured, oppressed; Bhāg.<BR>—2 Injuring, oppressing; Mbh. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुह्
अभिद्रुह् <i>a.</i> Ved. Seeking to injure, inimical. जनो यो मित्रावरुणावभिध्रुक्<BR> Rv. 1. 122. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रोहः|अभिद्रोह
अभिद्रोहः<BR>—1 Injuring, plotting against, harm, cruelty, oppression; स परत्रान्धकूपे<BR> तदभिद्रोहेण निपतति Bhāg. 5. 26. 17; Ki. 11. 21.<BR>—2 Abuse; censure. नामजातिग्रहं त्वेषामभिद्रोहेण कुर्वतः Ms. 8. 271.<BR>—3 Sorrow, misery; संस्थायां यस्त्वभिद्रोहो दुःसहश्चेतनापहः (यूयं<BR> न जानीथ) Bhāg. 6. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधर्मः|अभिधर्म
अभिधर्मः The supreme truth or Metaphysics according to Buddhistic dogmas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिधर्मपिटकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधर्मपिटकः|अभिधर्मपिटक
अभिधर्मः + -पिटकः ‘basket of Metaphysics’, one of the three sections (पिटक)<BR> of Buddhist holy writings which treat of अभिधर्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधर्षणम्
अभिधर्षणम्<BR>—1 Possession by evil spirits, demons &c.<BR>—2 Oppressing.<BR>—3 Striking against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा €3 U.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To say, speak, tell (with acc. rarely with dat.); सा तथ्यमेवाभिहिता<BR> भवेन Ku. 3. 63; Ms. 1. 42; Bk. 7. 78. य इदं परमं गुह्यं मद्भक्तेष्वभिधास्यति Bg. 18. 68.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To denote, express or convey directly or primarily (as sense<BR> &c.); state, mention, set forth; साक्षात्संकेतितं योऽर्थमभिधत्ते स<BR> वाचकः K. P. 2; तन्नाम येनाभिदधाति सत्त्वम्.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To speak or say to, address.<BR>—2 To name, call, designate; usually in <i>pass.</i> (-धीयते); इदं<BR> शरीरं कौन्तेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते Bg. 13. 1.<BR>—3 To lay or put on, fasten, bind; to overlay, load; assail; receive,<BR> comprehend, include; to draw oneself towards, hold, support (mostly Ved.<BR> in these senses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा <i>a.</i> Ved. Naming; praised, invoked. अभिधा असि भुवनमसि<BR> यन्तासि धर्ता Vāj. 22. 3. <i>n.</i><BR>—1 A name, appellation; oft. in comp.; कुसुमवसन्ताद्यभिधः S. D.<BR>—2 A word, sound.<BR>—3 The literal power or sense of a word, <i>denotation</i>, one of the three<BR> powers of a word; वाच्योऽर्थोऽभिधया बोध्यः S. D. 2. “the expressed<BR> meaning is that which is conveyed to the understanding by the wordʼs denotation”,<BR> for it is this अभिधा that conveys to the understanding the meaning<BR> which belongs to the word by common consent or convention (संकेत)<BR> (which primarily made it a word at all); स मुख्योऽर्थस्तत्र मुख्यो यो<BR> व्यापारोऽस्याभिधोच्यते K. P. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिधाध्वंसिन्, अभिधामूल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधाध्वंसिन्
अभिधा + -ध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i> losing oneʼs name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधामूल
अभिधा + -मूल <i>a.</i> founded on a wordʼs denotation or literal meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानम्
अभिधानम्<BR>—1 Telling, mentioning, speaking, naming, denotation; एतावतामर्थानामिदमभिधानम्<BR> Nir.; गोशब्दस्य वाहीकार्थाभिधानम् S. D.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Asserting or predicating something of another, as the subject<BR> of an assertion, (which then can be put in the nom. case only); predication,<BR> assertion; see P. II. 3. 2. Sk.<BR>—3 A name, appellation, title, designation; अभिधानं तु पश्चात्तस्याहमश्रौषम्<BR> K. 32; तवाभिधानाद् व्यथते नताननः Ki. 1. 24; (at the end of comp.)<BR> called, named; ऋणाभिधानाद् बन्धनात् R. 3. 20.<BR>—4 An expression, word.<BR>—5 Speech, discourse महत्तमानामभिधानयोगः Bhāg. 1. 18. 18.<BR>—6 A dictionary, vocabulary (of words), lexicon (in these last 4 senses<BR> said to be also <i>m.</i>)<BR>—7 A song, षट्पादतन्त्रीमधुराभिधानम् Rām. 4. 28. 36.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिधानचिन्तामाणिः, अभिधानमाला, अभिधानरत्नमाला, अभिधानविप्रतिपत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानचिन्तामाणिः
अभिधानम् + -चिन्तामाणिः N. of a celebrated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">Page0174-1</a>]<BR> vocabulary of synonyms by Hemacandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0173-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानमाला
अभिधानम् + -माला a dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानरत्नमाला
अभिधानम् + -रत्नमाला N. of a vocabulary of words by Halāyudha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानविप्रतिपत्तिः
अभिधानम् + -विप्रतिपत्तिः Incongruence of the word and the sense intended<BR> to be conveyed thereby; केयमभिधानविप्रतिपत्तिर्नाम । यदन्यथाभिधानमन्यथाभिधेयम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 9. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानकम्
अभिधानकम् A sound, voice, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायक
अभिधायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), अभिधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Naming, expressing, denoting; एतेषामभिधायकानि क्लीबे स्युः Sk.;<BR> कर्षूः कुल्याभिधायिनी Ak. denotes, means, has the sense of.<BR>—2 Saying, speaking, telling; तेनाहमुक्तः प्रेक्ष्यैवं घोरशापाभिधायिना<BR> Rām. 3. 71. 4; लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे Amaru. 27; वाच्याभिधायी<BR> पुरुषः पृष्ठमांसाद उच्यते Trik.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिका
अभिधायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), अभिधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Naming, expressing, denoting; एतेषामभिधायकानि क्लीबे स्युः Sk.;<BR> कर्षूः कुल्याभिधायिनी Ak. denotes, means, has the sense of.<BR>—2 Saying, speaking, telling; तेनाहमुक्तः प्रेक्ष्यैवं घोरशापाभिधायिना<BR> Rām. 3. 71. 4; लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे Amaru. 27; वाच्याभिधायी<BR> पुरुषः पृष्ठमांसाद उच्यते Trik.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिन्
अभिधायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), अभिधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Naming, expressing, denoting; एतेषामभिधायकानि क्लीबे स्युः Sk.;<BR> कर्षूः कुल्याभिधायिनी Ak. denotes, means, has the sense of.<BR>—2 Saying, speaking, telling; तेनाहमुक्तः प्रेक्ष्यैवं घोरशापाभिधायिना<BR> Rām. 3. 71. 4; लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे Amaru. 27; वाच्याभिधायी<BR> पुरुषः पृष्ठमांसाद उच्यते Trik.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेय|अभिधेयं
अभिधेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be named, mentioned, expressed &c.; वागेव मे नाभिधेयविषयमवतरति<BR> त्रपया K. 151 words refuse, through shame, to express what I have to say.<BR>—2 Nameable, as a category or predicament (in logic); अभिधेयाः पदार्थाः,<BR> अभिधेयत्वं पदार्थसामान्यलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेयम्
अभिधेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Signification, meaning, sense, import; P. I. 1. 34. Sk.; स्तुवन्ति<BR> गुर्वीमाभिधेयसंपदम् Ki. 14. 5.<BR>—2 A substance;<BR>—3 The subject-matter; इहाभिधेयं सप्रयोजनम् K. P. 1; इति प्रयोजनाभिधेयसंबन्धाः Mugdha.<BR>—4 The primary or literal sense of a word (= अभिधा); अभिधेयाविनाभूतप्रतीतिर्लक्षणोच्यते K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Said, declared, spoken, mentioned; मयाभिहितम्, तेनाभिहितम् &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Predicated, asserted; अनभिहिते कर्मणि द्वितीया P. II. 3. 1-2.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Spoken to, addressed, called, named.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Whispered, prompted to say; determined.<BR>—2 Fastened, placed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितम्
अभिहित + .{@-तम्@} A name, expression, word; हरन्ति स्मरतश्चित्तं गोविन्दाभिहितानि<BR> च Bhāg. 1. 15. 27. ˚त्वम् being said or spoken to, a declaration;<BR> authority, test.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिहितान्वयवादः, अभिहितवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितान्वयवादः|अभिहितान्वयवाद
अभिहित + -अन्वयवादः, -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a particular doctrine (or the follower<BR> of that doctrine) on the import of words, as opposed to अन्विताभिधानवाद,<BR> -वादिन्. The <i>anvitābhidhānavādins</i> (the Mīmāṃsakas, the followers<BR> of Prabhākara) hold that words only express a meaning (अभिधान) as<BR> parts of a sentence and grammatically connected with one another (अन्वित);<BR> that they, in fact, only imply an action or something connected with an<BR> action; <i>e. g.</i> घटम् in घटम् आनय means not merely ‘jar’,<BR> but ‘jar’ as connected with the action of ‘bringing’ expressed by the<BR> verb. The <i>abhihitānvayavādins</i> (the Bhāṭṭas or the followers<BR> of Kumārilabhaṭṭa who hold the doctrine) on the other hand hold that<BR> words by themselves can express their own independent meanings which are<BR> afterwards combined into a sentence expressing one connected idea; that,<BR> in other words, it is the logical connection between the words of a sentence,<BR> and not the sense of the words themselves, that suggests the import or<BR> purport of that sentence; they thus believe in a <i>tātparyārtha</i><BR> as distinguished<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">Page0174-2</a>]<BR> from <i>vācyārtha^1</i>; see K. P. 2 and Maheśvaraʼs commentary<BR> <i>ad hoc</i>. ˚तिः <i>f.</i> Naming, speaking &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितवादिन्
अभिहित + -अन्वयवादः, -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a particular doctrine (or the follower<BR> of that doctrine) on the import of words, as opposed to अन्विताभिधानवाद,<BR> -वादिन्. The <i>anvitābhidhānavādins</i> (the Mīmāṃsakas, the followers<BR> of Prabhākara) hold that words only express a meaning (अभिधान) as<BR> parts of a sentence and grammatically connected with one another (अन्वित);<BR> that they, in fact, only imply an action or something connected with an<BR> action; <i>e. g.</i> घटम् in घटम् आनय means not merely ‘jar’,<BR> but ‘jar’ as connected with the action of ‘bringing’ expressed by the<BR> verb. The <i>abhihitānvayavādins</i> (the Bhāṭṭas or the followers<BR> of Kumārilabhaṭṭa who hold the doctrine) on the other hand hold that<BR> words by themselves can express their own independent meanings which are<BR> afterwards combined into a sentence expressing one connected idea; that,<BR> in other words, it is the logical connection between the words of a sentence,<BR> and not the sense of the words themselves, that suggests the import or<BR> purport of that sentence; they thus believe in a <i>tātparyārtha</i><BR> as distinguished<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">Page0174-2</a>]<BR> from <i>vācyārtha^1</i>; see K. P. 2 and Maheśvaraʼs commentary<BR> <i>ad hoc</i>. ˚तिः <i>f.</i> Naming, speaking &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानी
अभिधानी Ved. A halter, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधाव्
अभिधाव् €1 P.<BR>—1 To run up towards, fly at or towards.<BR>—2 To rush upon, attack, assail; तं सीताघातिनं मत्वा हन्तुं रामोऽभ्यधावत Bk. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावक|अभिधावकः
अभिधावक <i>a.</i> Assailing, rushing upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावकः|अभिधावक
अभिधावक + .{@-कः@} An assailant; विक्रुष्टे नाभिधावकः Y. 2. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावनम्
अभिधावनम् Assault, pursuit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधृष्णु
अभिधृष्णु <i>a.</i> Ved. Overpowering, subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यै
अभिध्यै €1 P. (epic. €2 P.)<BR>—1 To meditate upon, reflect, consider, think of; यदभिध्याम्यहं शश्वच्छुभं<BR> वा यदि वाऽशुभम् Mb.<BR>—2 To covet, wish or desire for; परद्रव्याण्यभिध्यायन् Y. 3. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्या
अभिध्या [ध्यै-अङ्]<BR>—1 Coveting anotherʼs property. न चाचिकीर्षीत् परवस्त्वभिध्याम् Bu. C. 2. 44.<BR>—2 Longing, wish; desire in general; अभिध्योपदेशात् Br. Sūt.<BR>—3 Desire of taking (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यानम्
अभिध्यानम्<BR>—1 Desiring or longing for, coveting; a wish or desire; परद्रव्येष्वभिध्यानम् Ms. 12. 5.<BR>—2 Meditation, profound thought.<BR>—3 Anxiety; अभिध्याऽप्रख्यता चैव सर्वं लोभात्प्रवर्तते Mb. 12. 158. 5.<BR>—4 Censure, reviling; सोऽभिध्यानाद् ब्राह्मणस्य पराभूयादसंशयम् Mb. 12. 327. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्द्|अभिनंद्
अभिनन्द् €1 P. (rarely Ā.)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To rejoice at or in, exult over, be glad or satisfied; आत्मविडम्बनामभिनन्दन्ति<BR> K. 108; Dk. 75.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To celebrate (with rejoicings &c.); महोत्सवेन मज्जन्माभिनन्दितवान्<BR> K. 137; नाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि Bg. 2. 57.<BR>—2 To congratulate, hail with joy, welcome; greet; एनां परिष्वज्य तातकाश्यपेनैवम्<BR> अभिनन्दितम् Ś. 4; तापसीभिरभिनन्द्यमाना शकुन्तला तिष्ठति <i>ibid.</i> 5, 6, 7;<BR> अभिनन्दितागमनेषु समीरेषु K. 49, 63; अभिनन्द्य ब्रवीति<BR> Mv. 2 says (writes) after compliments; प्रविश्य पौरैराभिनन्द्यमानः<BR> R. 2. 74, 3. 68, 7. 69, 71, 11. 30, 16. 64, 17. 15, 60; आशीर्भिरभिनन्दितः Y. 1. 332.<BR>—3 To rejoice at, approve, praise, applaud, commend; यो रत्नराशीनपि<BR> विहाय अभिनन्द्यते Ś. 2; अतस्ते वचो नाभिनन्दामि <i>ibid.</i> do not<BR> approve; तद्युक्तमस्या अभिलाषोऽभिनन्दितुम् Ś. 3; श्रूयन्ते परिणीतास्ताः<BR> (कन्यकाः) पितृभिश्चाभिनन्दिताः 3. 22; नाम यस्याभिनन्दन्ति द्विषोऽपि<BR> स पुमान्पुमान् Ki. 11. 73, 4. 4; with न reject; R. 12. 35.<BR>—4 To care for, like, desire or wish for, respect, delight in (usually<BR> with न in this sense); नाभिनन्दन्ति केलिकलाः Māl. 3; नाहारमभिनन्दति<BR> K. 61; Dk. 159; आर्यपुत्रस्यैव मनोरथसंपत्तिमभिनन्दामि Ve. 2.<BR> wish or desire नाभिनन्देत मरणं नाभिनन्देत जीवितम् Ms. 6. 45; H. 4. 4.<BR>—5 To bless, grant success to, त्वां मैत्रावरुणोऽभिनन्दतु U. 5. 27.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To gladden, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्द|अभिनंद|अभिनन्दः
अभिनन्द <i>a.</i> That which delights, encourages, praises &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दः|अभिनन्द|अभिनंद
अभिनन्द + .{@-न्दः@}<BR>—1 Rejoicing, delighting, joy, delight. Bṛ. Up. 6. 2. 13.<BR>—2 Praising, applauding, approving, greeting, congratulating.<BR>—3 Wish, desire.<BR>—4 Encouraging, inciting to action.<BR>—5 Very little happiness (सुखलव).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">Page0175-1</a>]<BR>—6 An epithet of परमात्मन् the Supreme Being.<BR>—7 N. of a commentator on the अमरकोश.<BR>—8 N. of the author of the योगवासिष्ठसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दा
अभिनन्द + .{@-न्दा@} Delight; wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0174-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दनम्
अभिनन्दनम्<BR>—1 Rejoicing at, greeting, welcoming.<BR>—2 Praising, approving.<BR>—3 Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दनीय|अभिनंदनीय
अभिनन्दनीय, -नन्द्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be rejoiced at, praised, or applauded;<BR> काममेतदभिनन्दनीयम् Ś. 5; (जनस्य) द्वावप्यभूतामभिनन्द्यसत्त्वौ R. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्द्य|अभिनंद्य
अभिनन्दनीय, -नन्द्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be rejoiced at, praised, or applauded;<BR> काममेतदभिनन्दनीयम् Ś. 5; (जनस्य) द्वावप्यभूतामभिनन्द्यसत्त्वौ R. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दिन्|अभिनंदिन्
अभिनन्दिन् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Rejoicing at, approving, praising &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनभः
अभिनभः, -नभ्यम् <i>adv.</i> Ved.<BR> Towards the clouds or heaven; अहमस्मि<BR> महामहोऽभिनभ्यमुदीषितः Rv. 10. 119. 12; गुरुकाव्यानुगां बिभ्रच्चान्द्रीमभिनभः<BR> श्रियम् Śi. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनभ्यम्
अभिनभः, -नभ्यम् <i>adv.</i> Ved.<BR> Towards the clouds or heaven; अहमस्मि<BR> महामहोऽभिनभ्यमुदीषितः Rv. 10. 119. 12; गुरुकाव्यानुगां बिभ्रच्चान्द्रीमभिनभः<BR> श्रियम् Śi. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनम्
अभिनम् €1 P. To bow, to bend, to turn towards a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनम्र
अभिनम्र <i>a.</i> Bent, deeply bowed or bent; स्तनाभिरामस्तबकाभिनम्राम् R. 13. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनव|अभिनवः
अभिनव <i>a.</i> [आधिक्येन नवः, भृशार्थे अभिरत्र]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Quite new or fresh (in all senses); पदपङ्क्तिर्दृश्यतेऽभिनवा<BR> Ś. 3. 7, 5. 1; ˚कण्ठशोणित 6. 27; Me. 100; R. 9. 29; ˚वा वधूः<BR> K. 2 newly married.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Quite young or fresh, blooming, youthful (as body, age &c.);<BR> वपुरभिनवमस्याः पुष्यति स्वां न शोभाम् Ś. 1. 19; U. 5. 12; the<BR> younger; ˚शाकटायनः; ˚भोजः &c.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Fresh, recent.<BR>—2 Very young, not having experience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवः|अभिनव
अभिनव + .{@-वः@} [अभिनु अप्] Praise to win over, flattery.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिनवोद्भिद्, अभिनवोद्भिदः, अभिनवकालिदासः, अभिनवगुप्तः, अभिनवचन्द्रार्घविधिः, अभिनवतामरसम्, अभिनवयौवन, अभिनववयस्क, अभिनववैयाकरणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवोद्भिद्
अभिनव + -उद्भिद्, -उद्भिदः a new shoot or bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवोद्भिदः|अभिनवोद्भिद
अभिनव + -उद्भिद्, -उद्भिदः a new shoot or bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवकालिदासः|अभिनवकालिदास
अभिनव + -कालिदासः The modern Kālidāsa, i. e. Mādhavācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवगुप्तः|अभिनवगुप्त
अभिनव + -गुप्तः N. of a well-known author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवचन्द्रार्घविधिः|अभिनवचन्द्रार्घविधि
अभिनव + -चन्द्रार्घविधिः<BR>—1 a ceremony performed at the time of the new moon.<BR>—2 N. of the 114th chapter in the Bhaviṣya Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवतामरसम्
अभिनव + -तामरसम्<BR>—1 a fresh-blown lotus.<BR>—2 a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवयौवन
अभिनव + -यौवन, -वयस्क <i>a.</i> youthful, very young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनववयस्क
अभिनव + -यौवन, -वयस्क <i>a.</i> youthful, very young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनववैयाकरणः|अभिनववैयाकरण
अभिनव + -वैयाकरणः one who has newly begun his study of grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनह्
अभिनह् €4 P. To bind up (as the eyes), to bind, tie, fasten; स्तनयोः<BR> समयेन याङ्गनानामभिनद्धारसमा न सा रसेन । परिरम्भरुचिं ततिर्जलानामाभिनद्धा<BR> रसमानसारसेन ॥ Śi. 6. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनहनम्
अभिनहनम्<BR>—1 A bandage (over the eyes); तस्य यथाभिनहनं प्रमुच्य प्रब्रूयात्<BR> Ch. Up. 6. 14. 2.<BR>—2 a blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिधन|अभिनिधनं
अभिनिधन <i>a.</i> [अभिगतो निधनं मरणम्] About to perish, approaching oneʼs doom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिधनम्
अभिनिधन + .{@-नम्@} N. of certain verses of the Sāmaveda repeated at this time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिधानम्
अभिनिधानम्<BR>—1 Putting on, setting up.<BR>—2 Euphonic, suppression, weakening in the pronunciation of words, especially<BR> the supression of an initial अ after ए or ओ; cf. अवग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनियुक्त
अभिनियुक्त <i>a.</i> Occupied in, busy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनियोगः
अभिनियोगः Close application, attention or intentness, absorption;<BR> कार्य˚ Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्तः|अभिनिर्म्मुक्त
अभिनिर्मुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Left or quitted (by the sun when it sets).<BR>—2 One asleep at sunset and thus not doing the duties to be then performed.<BR> सूर्येणाभ्युदितो यश्च ब्रह्मचारी भवत्युत । तथा सूर्याभिनिर्मुक्तः कुनखी<BR> श्यावदन्नपि ॥ Mb. 12. 34. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्याणम्
अभिनिर्याणम्<BR>—1 A march.<BR>—2 Invasion, marching against an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्वृत्तिः|अभिनिर्वृत्ति
अभिनिर्वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Accomplishment, completion. यस्य ह्यर्थाभिनिर्वृत्तौ<BR> स भवन्त्याप्ययिताः परे Mb. 5. 134. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवर्तः|अभिनिवर्त|अभिनिवर्त्त
अभिनिवर्तः Turning towards, turning again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविश्
अभिनिविश् €6 Ā. अभिनिविशश्च (P. I. 4. 47) —1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To enter into, be settled in; to occupy, set foot in.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To take possession of, resort to, be attached to (with acc.);<BR> अभिनिविशते सन्मार्गम् Sk. takes to, follows, a good path; सैव धन्या<BR> गणिकादारिका यामेवं भवन्मनोऽमिनिविशते Dk. 57; Mu. 5. 12; Bk. 8. 80.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To make one enter or occupy, lead, carry or conduct<BR> to; (fig.) apply, direct or turn (as mind, heart &c.) towards something;<BR> प्रतिबन्धवत्स्वपि विषयेषु आभिनिवेश्य M. 3; Śi. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्ट
अभिनिविष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Intent on, engrossed in, engaged in or occupied with, applying oneself<BR> to; माधवापकारं प्रति अभिनिविष्टा भवामि Māl. 6.<BR>—2 Firmly or steadily fixed, uncontrollably fixed, steady, attentive,<BR> intent; अत्यभिनिविष्टवित्तदर्पस्य Dk. 29; Māl. 1.<BR>—3 Endowed with, possessed of; गुरुभिरभिनिविष्टम् (गर्भम्) लोकपालानुभावैः R. 2. 75.<BR>—4 Determined, resolute, persevering.<BR>—5 (In a bad sense) Obstinate, perverse; अथवाभिनिविष्टबुद्धिषु व्रजति<BR> व्यर्थकतां सुभाषितम् Śi. 16. 43; Ki. 17. 11.<BR>—6 Well-versed or proficient in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्टम्
अभिनिविष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्टता
अभिनिविष्टता Resoluteness, determination of purpose; निन्दाक्षेपापमानादेरमर्षोऽभिनिविष्टता<BR> S. D. <i>i. e.</i> adhering to oneʼs purpose; not minding censure, abuse, dishonour &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशः|अभिनिवेश
अभिनिवेशः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Devotion, attachment, intentness, being occupied with, adherence<BR> to close application, with loc. or in comp.; कतमस्मिंस्ते भावाभिनिवेशः<BR> V. 3; अहो निरर्थकव्यापारेष्वभिनिवेशः K. 120, 146; Dk. 81; Māl. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Firm attachment, love, fondness, affection; बलीयान् खलु मेऽभिनिवेशः<BR> Ś. 3; अनुरूपोऽस्या ˚शः <i>ibid.</i>, V. 2; असत्यभूते वस्तुन्यभिनिवेशः Mit.<BR>—2 Earnest desire, ardent longing or expectation; wish, desire; Māl. 5. 27.<BR>—3 Resolution, determined resolve, determination of purpose, firmness<BR> of resolve, perseverance; जनकात्मजायां नितान्तरूक्षाभिनिवेशमीशम्<BR> R. 14. 43; अनुरूप˚ शतोषिणा Ku. 5. 7; Śi. 3. 1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Idea, thought; Ms. 12. 5; Y. 3. 155.<BR>—4 (In Yoga Phil.) A sort of ignorance causing fear of death; instinctive<BR> clinging to worldly life and bodily enjoyments and the fear that one might<BR> be cut off from all of them by death; अविद्यास्मितारागद्वेषाभिनिवेशाः<BR> पञ्चक्लेशाः Yoga S.; cf. also Sāṅkhya<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">Page0176-1</a>]<BR> K. 150 and Malli. on Śi. 4. 55.<BR>—5 Pride; भयं द्वितीयाभिनिवेशतः स्यात् Bhāg. 11. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0175-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशिन्
अभिनिवेशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devoted to, intent on, adhering or clinging to; वितथाभिनिवेशी च<BR> जायतेऽन्त्यासु योनिषु Y. 3. 134; कल्याणाभिनिवेशिनः K. 136 of blessed<BR> or noble resolve, 191.<BR>—2 Fixing on, directing or turning (the mind) to; गुणेष्वभिविवेशिनो<BR> भर्तुरपि प्रिया M. 3; अहो नु खलु दुर्लभ ˚शी मदनः V. 1; Dk. 57.<BR>—3 Determined, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्कारिन्
अभिनिष्कारिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Doing completely.<BR>—2 Injuring, thinking ill of; Av. 10. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रमणम्
अभिनिष्क्रमणम्<BR>—1 Going out or forth.<BR>—2 (With Buddhists) Leaving the house to become an anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्टानः|अभिनिष्टान
अभिनिष्टानः [स्तन्-घञ्, सस्य च षत्वम् अभिनिशः स्तनः शब्दसंज्ञायां<BR> P. VIII. 3. 86]<BR>—1 A sound which dies away; विसर्जनीयोऽभिनिष्टानः.<BR>—2 A letter of the alphabet (˚नो वर्णः).<BR>—3 The Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्
अभिनिष्पत् €1 P. To rush out, issue, sally, go forth; to spring or<BR> shoot forth; गवाक्षजालैरभिनिष्पतन्त्यः Bk. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पतनम्
अभिनिष्पतनम् Sallying, issuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पद्
अभिनिष्पद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go or come to.<BR>—2 To enter into, become.<BR>—3 To appear, become visible. ━<i>Caus.</i> To bring to, help to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्तिः|अभिनिष्पत्ति
अभिनिष्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> Completion, end, accomplishment, fulfilment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्यन्दः|अभिनिष्यन्द
अभिनिष्यन्दः Trickling; यस्याः पयोभिनिष्यन्दात्क्षीरोदो नाम सागरः<BR> Rām. 7. 23. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिह्नवः|अभिनिह्नव
अभिनिह्नवः Denial, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनी
अभिनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring near, conduct or lead towards, carry to; तटाभिनीतेनाम्भसा<BR> Ki. 8. 32; अमात्यस्य गृहजनं स्वगृहमभिनीय रक्षसि Mu. 1, 5, 6. 15;<BR> दृष्ट्वा शरं ज्यामभिनीयमानम् Mb. being fitted to the bow.<BR>—2 To act, represent or exhibit dramatically, gesticulate; mostly occurring<BR> in stage-directions; श्रुतिमभिनीय Ś. 3 acting as if he heard something;<BR> Mu. 1. 2, 3. 30; M. 2. 5.<BR>—3 To quote, adduce, introduce.<BR>—4 To allow to elapse<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनयः|अभिनय
अभिनयः<BR>—1 Acting, gesticulation, any theatrical action (expressive of some sentiment,<BR> passion &c.); नृत्याभिनयाक्रियाच्युतम् Ku. 5. 79; अभिनयान् परिचेतुमिवोद्यता<BR> R. 9. 33; नर्तकीरभिनयातिलङ्घिनीः 19. 14; Ki. 10. 42.<BR>—2 Dramatic representation, exhibition on the stage; ललिताभिनयं तमद्य<BR> भर्ता मरुतां द्रष्टुमनाः सलोकपालः V. 2. 18; S. D. thus defines and<BR> classifies अभिनय:− भवेदभिनयोऽवस्थानुकारः स चतुर्विधः । आङ्गिको<BR> वाचिकश्चैवमाहार्यः सात्त्विकस्तथा ॥ 274, ‘acting is the imitation of condition’<BR>, it is of four kinds:− (1) <i>gestural</i>, conveyed by bodily<BR> actions; (2) <i>vocal</i>, conveyed by words; (3) <i>extraneous</i>, conveyed<BR> by dress, ornaments, decoration &c.; (4) <i>internal</i>, conveyed by the<BR> manifestation of internal feeling such as perspiration,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">Page0176-2</a>]<BR> thrilling &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिनयाचार्यः, अभिनयविद्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनयाचार्यः|अभिनयाचार्य
अभिनयः + -आचार्यः a dancing preceptor; उभावभिनयाचार्यौ त्वां द्रष्टुमिच्छतः M. 1. 10<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनयविद्या
अभिनयः + -विद्या science of acting or dramatic representation; art of dancing;<BR> मया तीर्थादभिनयविद्या शिक्षिता M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीत|अभिनीतः
अभिनीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Brought near, conveyed.<BR>—2 Performed, represented dramatically.<BR>—3 Highly finished or polished, most excellent.<BR>—4 Highly ornamented or decorated.<BR>—5 Fit, proper, suitable (योग्य); अभिनीततरं वाक्यमित्युवाच युधिष्ठिरः Mb.<BR>—6 Patient, forgiving, even-minded.<BR>—7 Angry (युक्तेऽतिसंस्कृतेमर्षिण्यभिनीतः Ak. where the word may be<BR> अमर्षिणि as well while Nm. reads युक्ते तु संस्कृतेऽमर्षिण्यभिनीतः<BR> प्रचक्ष्यते).<BR>—8 Kind, friendly.<BR>—9 Acknowledged, agreed (प्रतिज्ञात); मित्रार्थमभिनीतार्थं यथावत्<BR> कर्तुमर्हति Rām. 4. 29. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीतिः|अभिनीति
अभिनीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Gesture, expressive gesticulation.<BR>—2 Kindness, friendship, patience; सान्त्वपूर्वमभिनीतिहेतुकम् Ki. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेय
अभिनेय, -नेतव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be acted or dramatically represented &c.<BR> दृश्यं तत्राभिनेयं तद्रूपारोपात्तु रूपकम् S. D. 273; M. 1; तस्य<BR> (प्रबन्धस्य) एकदेशः अभिनेयार्थः कृतः U. 4 a part of it has<BR> been adapted to the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतव्य
अभिनेय, -नेतव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be acted or dramatically represented &c.<BR> दृश्यं तत्राभिनेयं तद्रूपारोपात्तु रूपकम् S. D. 273; M. 1; तस्य<BR> (प्रबन्धस्य) एकदेशः अभिनेयार्थः कृतः U. 4 a part of it has<BR> been adapted to the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतृ
अभिनेतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who brings near; वस्वो राशिमभिनेतासि भूरिम् Rv. 4. 20. 8.<BR>—2 An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेत्री
अभिनेतृ + .{@-त्री@} An actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनुन्न
अभिनुन्न <i>a.</i> Agitated, full of woe; दण्डकाष्ठाभिनुन्नाङ्गी चचाल<BR> भृशमाकुला Mb. 14. 58. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्न
अभिन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not broken or cut, unbroken; not split; अभिन्नपुटोत्तरान् R. 17. 12.<BR>—2 Unaffected; क्लेशलेशैरभिन्नम् Ś. 2. 4.<BR>—3 Not changed or altered, unchanged; ˚गतयः Ś. 1. 14 with their<BR> gait unchanged.<BR>—4 Not different from, the same, identical (with abl.); जगन्मिथोभिन्नमभिन्नमीश्वरात् Prab.<BR>—5 Undivided, whole, one (as number).<BR>—6 Holding together, continuous.<BR>—7 Uninterrupted; अभिन्ने खिल्ये निदधाति देवयुम् Rv. 6. 28. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्यासः|अभिन्यास
अभिन्यासः A kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपत्
अभिपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly near, go or hasten near, approach; हन्तुमभिपतति पाण्डुसुतम्<BR> Ki. 12. 36; अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1; Dk. 72, 128; Mk. 9. 12;<BR> Ki. 10. 42.<BR>—2 To fall upon, attack, assail; यन्ता गजस्याभ्यपतद्गजस्थम् R. 7. 37;<BR> Dk. 62, 70, 96; Ki. 7. 19.<BR>—3 To fall down; fall (as tears).<BR>—4 To fall into, enter or come into.<BR>—5 To overtake in flying.<BR>—6 To pass over, traverse.<BR>—7 To get back, withdraw, retire; अभिपतितुमना लघुत्वभीतेः Śi. 7. 51;<BR> Ki. 10. 54,<BR>—8 (€4 Ā.) To be lord or master of (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i> To throw upon,<BR> throw down into; ज्वलनमभिपातयामि Ve. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपतनम्
अभिपतनम्<BR>—1 Approaching.<BR>—2 Falling upon, assault, attack.<BR>—3 Going forth, departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपद्
अभिपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go to, draw near, approach (with acc.); रावणावरजा तत्र राघवं<BR> मदनातुरा । अभिपेदे निदाघार्ता<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">Page0177-1</a>]<BR> व्यालीव मलयद्रुमम् ॥ R. 12. 32, 19. 11; Dk. 166; K. 265; to enter<BR> (into) Śi. 3. 25 sometimes with loc. also.<BR>—2 To look upon, consider, regard; to take or know to be; क्षणमभ्यपद्यत<BR> जनैर्न मृषा गगनं गणाधिपतिमूर्तिरिति Śi. 9. 27.<BR>—3 To help, assist; मयाऽभिपन्नं तं चापि न सर्पो धर्षयिष्यति Mb. 1. 50. 20.<BR>—4 To seize, catch hold of; overpower, attack, subdue, take possession<BR> of, overcome, afflict; सर्वतश्चाभिपन्नैषा धार्तराष्ट्री महाचमूः । चण्डवाताभिपन्नानामुदधीनामिव<BR> स्वनः Mb.; see अभिपन्न also.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To take, assume; स्वानि स्वान्यभिपद्यन्ते यथा कर्माणि देहिनः Ms. 1. 30<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To accept, receive; निरास्वाद्यतमं शून्यं (राज्यं)<BR> भरतो नाभिपत्स्यते Rām.<BR>—6 To apply or devote oneself to, undertake, fall to, observe; स चिन्तामभ्यपद्यत Rām.<BR>—7 To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपत्तिः|अभिपत्ति
अभिपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approaching, drawing near.<BR>—2 Completion.<BR>—3 Protection; त्वमेव धर्मार्थदुघाभिपत्तये Bhāg. 4. 6. 44.<BR>—4 See उपपत्तिः; अथाभिपत्तिर्लोकस्य कर्तव्या पुण्यपापयोः Mb. 12. 32. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपन्न|अभिपन्नः
अभिपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone or come near, approached, run towards, gone to (a state &c.);<BR> त्वमन्यमाकारमिवाभिपन्नः Ki. 3. 46.<BR>—2 Fled, fugitive, seeking refuge with.<BR>—3 Subdued, overpowered, afflicted, seized &c.; कालाधिपन्नाः सीदन्ति<BR> सिकतासेतवो यथा Rām. सीता वितत्रास यथा वनान्ते सिंहाभिपन्ना गजराजकन्या<BR> Rām. 5. 28. 1. यदिदं सर्वं मृत्युनाभिपन्नम् Śat. Br.; दोष˚,<BR> कश्मल˚, व्याघ्र˚ &c.<BR>—4 Unfortunate, fallen into difficulties &c.<BR>—5 Accepted; Rām. 6. 63. 24.<BR>—6 Guilty; अभिपन्नाऽस्मि पाञ्चालि याज्ञसेनि क्षमस्व मे Mb. 3. 233. 61.<BR>—7 Removed to a distance.<BR>—8 Dead.<BR>—9 Endowed see उपपन्न; अभिपन्नमिदं लोके राज्ञामुद्यतदण्डनम् Mb. 12. 32. 20.<BR>—10 Protected; मयाऽभिपन्नं तं चापि न सर्पो धर्षयिष्यति Mb. 1. 50. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपद्म
अभिपद्म <i>a.</i> Very beautiful; पञ्चाभिपद्मानिव वारणेन्द्रान् Mb. 1. 187. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपरिप्लुत
अभिपरिप्लुत^1 <i>a.</i> Overflowed, filled with, inundated; (fig.) overwhelmed,<BR> affected; attacked; shaken; शोकेन, मन्युना &c. Mb. 3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: print vague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपाण्डु
अभिपाण्डु <i>a.</i> Faded, pale; मनोभुवा तप्त इवाभिपाण्डुताम् Ki. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपातः|अभिपात
अभिपातः<BR>—1 moving, walking about; वियदभिपातलाघवेन Ki. 7. 21.<BR>—2 Fall, ruin; नूनं प्रियाया मम नाभिपातः Rām. 3. 63. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपित्वम्
अभिपित्वम् <i>n.</i>^1 or <i>s.</i> Ved. [पा भावे कित्वन्]<BR>—1 Come, approaching (अभिप्राप्त).<BR>—2 Visiting, putting up (for the night at an inn &c.); the time of coming.<BR>—3 Approaching time.<BR>—4 Close or departure of day, evening.<BR>—5 Dawn sacrifice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपुष्प
अभिपुष्प <i>a.</i> [अभितः पुष्पाण्यस्य] Covered over with flowers (as a tree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपुष्पम्
अभिपुष्प + .{@-ष्पम्@} An excellent flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूज्
अभिपूज् €10 P.<BR>—1 To adorn, worship.<BR>—2 To honour, approve, assent to; तथेति भरतो वाक्यं वसिष्ठस्याभिपूज्य<BR> तत् Rām. अभिपूजितलाभैश्च यतिर्मुक्तोऽपि बध्यते Ms. 6. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूजनम्
अभिपूजनम् Honouring; approving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूर्वम्
अभिपूर्वम् <i>ind.</i> One after another, successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपॄ
अभिपॄ €3. €9 P. To fill. ━<i>Pass.</i> To become full. <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fill, make full.<BR>—2 To load with (as animals); cover with.<BR>—3 To present with.<BR>—4 To overwhelm, overpower, master completely; शोको मामभ्यपूरयत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूरणम्
अभिपूरणम् Filling, overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूर्तम्
अभिपूर्तम् That which has been fulfilled; Av. 9. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रज्ञा
अभिप्रज्ञा Thinking constantly of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणी
अभिप्रणी €1 P. To lead to, bring towards; उत प्रणेष्यभि वस्यो अस्मान्<BR> Rv. 1. 31. 18 consecrate; जज्वाल लोकस्थितये स राजा यथाध्वरे वह्निरभिप्रणीतः Bk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणयः|अभिप्रणय
अभिप्रणयः Affection, favour, propitiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणयनम्
अभिप्रणयनम् Consecrating by sacred hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रतप्त
अभिप्रतप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intensely heated.<BR>—2 Dried up.<BR>—3 Exhausted with pain, fever &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रथनम्
अभिप्रथनम् Spreading or extending over, throwing over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रदक्षिणम्
अभिप्रदक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> Towards the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रपद्
अभिप्रपद् = प्रपद् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रमुर्
अभिप्रमुर् <i>f.</i> The tongue of fire (जुहू); Completely raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवृत्
अभिप्रवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To advance up to, approach, go up to.<BR>—2 To fall or flow into; यत्र भागिरथीं गङ्गां यमुनाऽभिप्रवर्तते Rām.<BR>—3 To become conversant with. ━<i>Caus.</i> To roll onward or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवर्तनम्
अभिप्रवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Advancing up to.<BR>—2 Proceeding, acting.<BR>—3 Flowing, coming forth, as of sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवृत्त
अभिप्रवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Advancing, going up to.<BR>—2 Occurring.<BR>—3 Engaged or occupied in (with loc.); कर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किंचित्करोति<BR> सः Bg. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रश्निन्
अभिप्रश्निन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Desirous of asking many questions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राणनम्
अभिप्राणनम् Exhaling (opp. अपाननम्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राप्
अभिप्राप्, -प्तिः &c.<BR> = प्राप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राप्तिः|अभिप्राप्ति
अभिप्राप्, -प्तिः &c.<BR> = प्राप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रीतिः|अभिप्रीति
अभिप्रीतिः <i>f.</i> Wish; rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रे
अभिप्रे [अभिप्र-इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To go to or near, approach; कर्मणा यमभिप्रैति स संप्रदानम् P. I. 4. 32.<BR>—2 To intend, aim at, think of, mean; cf. अभिप्रेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राय|अभिप्रायः
अभिप्राय <i>a.</i> [इ -अच्] Going near, approaching; aiming at, intending,<BR> meaning, accruing to; स्वरितञितः कर्त्रभिप्राये क्रियाफले P. I. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रायः|अभिप्राय
अभिप्राय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Aim, purpose, object, intention, wish, desire; अभिप्राया न सिद्धयन्ति<BR> तेनेदं वर्तते जगत् Pt. 1. 158; साभिप्रायाणि वचांसि Pt. 2 earnest words;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">Page0178-1</a>]<BR> भावः कवेरभिप्रायः.<BR>—2 Meaning, sense, import, implied sense of a word, passage &c.; तेषामयमभिप्रायः<BR> such is the meaning intended, import (of the passage &c.).<BR>—3 Opinion, belief. तेषां स्वं स्वमभिप्रायमुपलभ्य पृथक् पृथक् Ms. 7. 57.<BR>—4 Relation, reference.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत|अभिप्रेतं
अभिप्रेत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Meant, aimed at, intended; designed; अत्रायमर्थोऽभिप्रेतः; किमभिप्रेतमनया<BR> Bh. 3. 67; निवेदयाभिप्रेतम् Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Wished, desired; यथाभिप्रेतमनुष्ठीयताम् H. 1.<BR>—3 Approved, accepted; पूर्वैरयमभिप्रेतो गतो मार्गोऽनुगम्यते Rām.<BR>—4 Dear or agreeable to, favourite with, beloved; धर्मस्तवाभिप्रेतः Dk. 42; Ś. 6.<BR>—5 Wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेतम्
अभिप्रेत + .{@-तम्@} Intellectual nature (बुद्धिवृत्तिः); त्वं प्रभास्त्वमभिप्रेतम् Mb. 1. 23. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रोक्षणम्
अभिप्रोक्षणम् Sprinkling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लु
अभिप्लु €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go up to, jump or leap towards.<BR>—2 To overflow; (fig.) affect, fill with, overwhelm; तमसाभिप्लुते लोके<BR> रजसा च Mb.; रजसाभिप्लुतां नारीम् Ms. 4. 41 being in her courses;<BR> व्यसनाभिप्लुतेऽपि वा Y. 2. 50.<BR>—3 To spring to or over, spring upon. ━<i>Caus.</i> To wash or ripple against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लवः|अभिप्लव
अभिप्लवः<BR>—1 Affliction, disturbance.<BR>—2 Inundation, overflowing.<BR>—3 N. of a religious ceremony performed as part of the sacrifice गवामयन.<BR>—4 N. of the Prājāpatya Āditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लुत
अभिप्लुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overwhelmed; तमसाऽभिप्लुते लोके Mb. 4. 33. 1.<BR>—2 Affected; रजसाभिप्लुतां नारीं नरस्य ह्युपगच्छतः Ms. 4. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिबलम्
अभिबलम् A technical term in Rhetoric; अभिबलमभिसन्धिश्छलेन<BR> यः S. D. 375 ‘an inquiry or examination by an artifice’. See Ratn. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिबुद्धिः|अभिबुद्धि
अभिबुद्धिः <i>f.</i> An organ of apprehension, a बुद्धीन्द्रिय or ज्ञानेन्द्रिय<BR> (opp. कर्मेन्द्रिय); these are the eye, tongue, ear, nose, and skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभङ्गः|अभिभङ्ग|अभिभंगः
अभिभङ्गः<BR>—1 Breaking down.<BR>—2 One who breaks down or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभर्त्सित
अभिभर्त्सित <i>a.</i> Derided Mb. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभा
अभिभा €2 P. To glitter or shine; दिवि स्थितः सूर्य इवाभिभाति Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभा
अभिभा Ved. [अभिभा-अङ्]<BR>—1 Apparition, phenomenon; an inauspicious omen. मा त्वा का चिदभिभा<BR> विश्व्या विदत् Rv. 2. 42. 1.<BR>—2 A calamity, state of being overpowered.<BR>—3 Superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभार
अभिभार <i>a.</i> Very heavy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाष्
अभिभाष् €1 Ā. (P. in epic poetry)<BR>—1 To speak to, address; talk or converse with<BR> (with acc.); भोभवत्पूर्वकं त्वेनमभिभाषेत धर्मवित् Ms. 2. 128;<BR> नोदक्यामभिभाषेत Ms. 4. 57 sometimes with instr. also;<BR>—2 To speak, say (as वाणीम्, वचः &c.); इति अभिभाषन्ते so they say.<BR>—3 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">Page0178-2</a>]<BR> relate, narrate, speak of.<BR>—4 To proclaim, announce, confess; गुरुतल्प्यभिभाष्यैनस्तप्ते स्वप्यादयोमये Ms. 11. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषणम्
अभिभाषणम् Speaking to, addressing, conversing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषिन्
अभिभाषिन् <i>a.</i> Addressing, speaking to; speaking, talking; स्मितपूर्वाभिभाषिणम्<BR> R. 17. 31 whose words are preceded by a smile, speaking with a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभू
अभिभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To overcome, subdue, conquer, vanquish (of persons or things);<BR> prevail over, predominate, defeat; (hence) excel, surpass; अभिभवति<BR> मनः कदम्बवायौ Ki. 10. 23; अभिभूय विभूतिमार्तवीम् R. 8. 36, 4. 56, 6. 29, 16. 10;<BR> K. 52, 53; Mu. 3. 20; Ms. 7. 5; धर्मे नष्टे कुलं<BR> कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत Bg. 1. 40 predominates over, overpowers; so<BR> शोकाभिभूत, विपद्˚, काम˚ &c.<BR>—2 To attack, seize or fall upon, assail; विपदोऽभिभवन्त्यविक्रमम्<BR> Ki. 2. 14; अभ्यभावि भरताग्रजस्तया R. 11. 16, 84; Bṛ. S. 33. 30;<BR> ममापि सत्त्वैरभिभूयन्ते गृहाः Ś. 6 infested; परित्रायध्वं मामनेन<BR> मधुकरेणाभिभूयमानाम् Ś. 1 attacked, troubled; अभ्यभून्निलयं भ्रातुः Bk. 6. 117.<BR>—3 To humiliate, mortify, insult, disrespect; अण्डभङ्गाभिभूता Pt. 1.<BR>—4 To go up to, turn to or towards (Ved.); अभी षु णः सखीनामविता जरितॄणाम् ।<BR> शतं भवास्यूतिभिः Rv. 4. 31. 3.<BR>—5 To be victorious or prosperous; पुष्यात् क्षेमे अभि योगे भवात्युभे<BR> Rv. 5. 37. 5. ━<i>Caus.</i> To overpower, surpass, defeat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवः|अभिभव
अभिभवः<BR>—1 Defeat, subjugation, subjection, overpowering; इतरेतरानभिभवेन<BR> मृगास्तमुपासते गुरुमिवान्तसदः Ki. 6. 34 (cf. K. 45 and the Bible<BR> “The wolf shall also dwell with the lamb” &c.); 8. 28; स्पर्शानुकूला इव<BR> सूर्यकान्तास्तदन्यतेजोऽभिभवाद्वमन्ति^1 Ś. 2. 7 when assailed, opposed,<BR> overpowered by another energy; अभिभवः कुत एव सपत्नजः R. 9. 4, 4. 21.<BR>—2 Being overpowered जराभिभवविच्छायम् K. 346; being attacked or<BR> affected, stupefied (by fever &c.); न रोगशान्तिर्न चाभिभवः Suśr.<BR>—3 Contempt, disrespect; निरभिभवसाराः परकथाः Bh. 2. 64.<BR>—4 Humiliation, mortification (of pride); अलभ्यशोकाभिभवेयमाकृतिः<BR> Ku. 5. 43; K. 195.<BR>—5 Predominance, prevalence, rise, spread; अधर्माभिभवात्कृष्ण प्रदुष्यन्ति<BR> कुलस्त्रियः Bg. 1. 41; Ki. 2. 37.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: add ' (avagraha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवनम्
अभिभवनम् Overpowering, overcoming, being subjected to or overpowered<BR> by; जरया चाभिभवनम् Ms. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावनम्
अभिभावनम् Making victorious, overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाविन्
अभिभाविन्, -भाव(वु)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overpowering, defeating, conquering; शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता<BR> K. 170 fear which conquered grief.<BR>—2 Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोऽभिभाविना R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>—3 Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>—4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावक
अभिभाविन्, -भाव(वु)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overpowering, defeating, conquering; शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता<BR> K. 170 fear which conquered grief.<BR>—2 Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोऽभिभाविना R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>—3 Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>—4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावुक
अभिभाविन्, -भाव(वु)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overpowering, defeating, conquering; शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता<BR> K. 170 fear which conquered grief.<BR>—2 Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोऽभिभाविना R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>—3 Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>—4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभुः|अभिभु
अभिभुः, -भूः Ved.<BR>—1 One who surpasses or prevails over, a superior.<BR>—2 Pride (अहंकार); त्वं महानभिभूः Mb. 1. 23. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूः
अभिभुः, -भूः Ved.<BR>—1 One who surpasses or prevails over, a superior.<BR>—2 Pride (अहंकार); त्वं महानभिभूः Mb. 1. 23. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति <i>a.</i> That which defeats, conquers &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूतिः|अभिभूति
अभिभूति + .{@-तिः@}<BR>—1 Predominance, prevalence, excessive or superior power; जूतिं कृष्टिप्रो<BR> अभिभूतिमाशोः Rv. 4. 38. 9.<BR>—2 Conquering,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">Page0179-1</a>]<BR> defeat, subjugation; अभिभूतिभयादसूनतः सुखमुज्झन्ति न धाम मानिनः Ki. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Disrespect, disgrace, humiliation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिभूत्योजस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूत्योजस्
अभिभूति + -ओजस् <i>a.</i> of superior or predominant power. <i>n.</i> superior power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूयम्
अभिभूयम् Ved. Superiority; Av. 19. 37. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूवन्
अभिभूवन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Prevailing or victorious over; surpassing; Rv. 10. 159. 5-6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमद्
अभिमद् €4 P. Ved. To gladden, exhilarate, inebriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमादः|अभिमाद
अभिमादः Intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद्यत्क
अभिमाद्यत्क <i>a.</i> Half drunk, partially intoxicated, stammering<BR> (like a drunkard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्
अभिमन् €4 Ā. (P. epic.)<BR>—1 To wish or desire, long for, covet, like; न त्वेवं ज्यायसीं वृत्तिमभिमन्येत<BR> कर्हिचित् Ms. 10. 95; see अभिमत below.<BR>—2 To assent to, approve of, allow, admit; give a grant (to any one, dat.).<BR>—3 To think, fancy, imagine, consider, believe, regard; तामार्यामसावन्यथाऽभ्यमन्यत<BR> Dk. 164; Bk. 5. 71; U. 5.<BR>—4 To injure, threaten (Ved.)<BR>—5 (€8 Ā.) To think of self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Desired, wished, liked, dear, beloved, favourite (person or thing);<BR> agreeable, desirable; नास्ति जीवितादन्यदभिमततरमिह जगति सर्वजन्तूनाम्<BR> K. 35, 58; अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bk. 1. 27; यद्येवमभिमतम्<BR> Pt. 1 if you like to do so; तयोरभिमतं वद Mv. 6. 21 choose which<BR> you will; इक्ष्वाकुवंशोऽभिमतः प्रजानाम् U. 1. 44; Ś. 3. 5; Ku. 3. 23,<BR> Pt. 1. 70; Me. 51; Mu. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Agreed or assented to, liked, approved, accepted, admitted; न किल<BR> भवतां स्थानं देव्या गृहेऽभिमतं ततः U. 3. 32; प्रसिद्धमाहात्म्याभिमतानामपि<BR> कपिलकणभुक्प्रभृतीनाम् Ś. B. honoured, respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतम्
अभिमत + .{@-तम्@} Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतः|अभिमत|अभिमतं
अभिमत + .{@-तः@} A beloved person, lover; अभिमतमभितः कृताङ्गभङ्गा<BR> Śi. 7. 72, 8. 68, 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतिः|अभिमति
अभिमतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Desire.<BR>—2 Pride; न विक्रिया विश्वसुहृत्सखस्य साम्येन वीताभिमतेस्तवापि Bhāg. 5. 10. 25.<BR>—3 Respect, regard, see अभिमान below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनस्
अभिमनस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intent on, desirous of; युद्धाभिमनसः सर्वे Rām. 5. 42. 26.<BR>—2 anxious, longing for; भवतोऽभिमनाः समीहते सरुषः कर्तुमुपेत्य<BR> माननाम् Śi. 16. 2 (where अ˚ also means undaunted, of fearless mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनायते
अभिमनायते Den. Ā. To have life, be full of life and joy, be pleased<BR> or delighted, to long for; अभ्यमनायिष्ट चान्तरात्मा Dk. 111, 119;<BR> कान्तिं (विलोक्य) नाभिमनायेत को वा स्थाणुसमोऽपि ते Bk. 5. 73<BR> (Com. = सचेताः or प्रीतमनाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तुः|अभिमन्तु|अभिमंतुः
अभिमन्तुः <i>f.</i> Ved. Injuring, harming, destroying; ˚न्तोः to<BR> destroy; to claim as oneʼs own, pretending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तृ|अभिमंतृ
अभिमन्तृ <i>a.</i> Longing for; self-conceited, referring all objects<BR> to self; Ms. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानः|अभिमान
अभिमानः<BR>—1 Pride (in a good sense), self-respect, honourable or worthy feeling;<BR> सदाभिमानैकधना हि मानिनः Śi. 1. 67; त्यक्त्वा जातिकुलाभिमानमुचितम्<BR> Bh. 3. 5. अभिमानधनस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">Page0179-2</a>]<BR> गत्वरैः Ki. 2. 19; संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतम् Ku. 3. 24.<BR>—2 Self-conceit, pride, arrogance, haughtiness, egotism, high opinion<BR> of oneself; शिथिल˚ नाः संवृत्ताः M. 2; Bh. 3. 46; Bg. 16. 4; (अतिमानः<BR> is another reading) ˚वत् proud, conceited.<BR>—3 Referring all objects to self, the act of अहंकार, personality,<BR> misconception (मिथ्याज्ञानम्), see अहंकार.<BR>—4 Conceit, conception; supposition, belief, opinion; मुनिरस्मि निरागसः<BR> कुतो मे भयमित्येष न भूतयेऽभिमानः Ki. 13. 7.<BR>—5 Knowledge, consciousness (बुद्धि, ज्ञान); साधारण्याभिमानतः S. D.<BR>—6 Affection, love.<BR>—7 Desire, wishing for.<BR>—8 Laying claim to.<BR>—9 Injury, Killing, seeking to injure.<BR>—10 A sort of state occasioned by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानम्
अभिमानः + .{@-नम्@} Authority (प्रमाण); ये चरन्त्यभिमानानि सृष्टार्थमनुषङ्गिणः<BR> Mb. 12. 168. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिमानशालिन्, अभिमानशून्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानशालिन्
अभिमानः + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानशून्य
अभिमानः + -शून्य <i>a.</i> void of pride or arrogance, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानितम्
अभिमानितम्<BR>—1 Egotism.<BR>—2 Love; copulation, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of self-respect; Ki. 1. 31; K. 212.<BR>—2 Having a high opinion of oneself, proud, arrogant, conceited.<BR>—3 Regarding all objects as referring to oneʼs own self; अभिमानिव्यपदेशस्तु<BR> विशेषानुगतिभ्याम् Br. Sūt. 2. 1. 5.<BR>—4 Fancying, pretending, or regarding oneself to be; नरेन्द्र˚ Dk. 51;<BR> K. 194. ━<i>m.</i> A form of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानुक
अभिमानुक <i>a.</i> Ved. [मन् बाहु˚ उकच्] Striving to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्र्|अभिमंत्र्
अभिमन्त्र् €10 Ā. (P. also)<BR>—1 To consecrate or accompany with sacred hymns; पशुरसौ योऽभिमन्त्र्य<BR> कतौहतः Ak.; वामदेवाभिमन्त्रितोऽश्वः U. 2; गायत्र्या चाभिमन्त्रयेत्<BR> Y. 3. 325, 2. 102, 3. 278.<BR>—2 To consecrate with magical formulas, charm, enchant, invoke or invite<BR> by means of charms; तदभिमन्त्रितेन चरणेन Dk. 138; पानीयैरभिमन्त्रितैः Mb.<BR>—3 To speak to, address, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रणम्
अभिमन्त्रणम्<BR>—1 Consecrating, hallowing, making sacred by repetition of special formulas<BR> or Mantras; दत्त्वान्नं पृथिवीपात्रमिति पात्राभिमन्त्रणम् (कृत्वा)<BR> Y. 1. 238; मन्त्रमुच्चारयन्नेव मन्त्रार्थत्वेन संस्मरेत् । शेषिणं<BR> तन्मना भूत्वा स्यादेतदभिमन्त्रणम् ॥ Mīm.<BR>—2 Charming, enchanting.<BR>—3 Addressing, inviting, advising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्थः|अभिमन्थ|अभिमंथः
अभिमन्थः^1 = अधिमन्थः q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: Also, aDimanT -> aDimanTaH.  This is a m. noun, not a present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यमान
अभिमन्यमान <i>a.</i> Making a lascivious attempt on. ब्राह्मणकन्यामभिमन्यमानः<BR> भोजः Kau. A. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्युः|अभिमन्यु
अभिमन्युः<BR>—1 N. of a son of Arjuna by his wife Subhadrā, sister of Kṛṣṇa and<BR> Balarāma; also known by the metronymic Saubhadra. [He was called <i>Abhimanyu</i><BR> because at his very birth he appeared to be heroic, long-armed and very<BR> fiery (अभिवृद्धः मन्युर्यस्य). When the Kauravas at the advice of<BR> Droṇa formed the peculiar battle-array called ‘Cakravyūha’ hoping that,<BR> as Arjuna was away, none of the Pāṇḍavas<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">Page0180-1</a>]<BR> would be able to break through it, Abhimanyu assured his uncles that he<BR> was ready to try, if they only assisted him. He accordingly entered the<BR> Vyūha, killed many warriors on the Kaurava side, and was for a time more<BR> than a match even for such veteran and elderly heroes as Droṇa, Karṇa,<BR> Duryodhana &c. He could not, however, hold out long against fearful odds,<BR> and was at last overpowered and slain. He was very handsome. He had two<BR> wives, Vatsalā daughter of Balarāma and Uttarā daughter of the king<BR> of Virāṭa. Uttarā was pregnant when he was slain and gave birth to<BR> a son named Parīkṣita who succeeded to the throne of Hastināpura.]<BR>—2 Name of a son of Manu Cākṣuṣa.<BR>—3 Name of two kings of Kāśmīra; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्युपुरम्
अभिमन्युः + .{@-पुरम्@} -Name of a town. Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमरः|अभिमर
अभिमरः [मृ-अच्]<BR>—1 Killing, destruction, slaughter.<BR>—2 War, combat.<BR>—3 Treachery in oneʼs own camp; danger from oneʼs own men or party.<BR>—4 Binding, confinement; a tie or fetter.<BR>—5 Oneʼs own party or army.<BR>—6 One who desperately goes to fight with tigers, elephants &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाति|अभिमातिः
अभिमाति <i>a.</i> [मे कर्तरि क्तिन् न इत्त्वम्]<BR>—1 Insidious; स हि ष्मा विश्वचर्षणिरभिमाति सहो दधे Rv. 5. 23. 4.<BR>—2 Striving or seeking to injure, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमातिः|अभिमाति
अभिमाति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Seeking to injure, hurting, plotting against.<BR>—2 An enemy, a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमातिन्
अभिमातिन् <i>a.</i> [मे-क्त, इष्टादिभ्यः इन्]<BR>—1 Insidious; बाधन्ते विश्वमभिमातिनम् Rv. 1. 85. 3.<BR>—2 One who hurts or injures, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाय|अभिमायः
अभिमाय <i>a.</i> [अभिगतो मायामविद्याम्] Bewildered (इतिकर्तव्यतामूढ);<BR> ignorant, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमिह्य
अभिमि(मे)ह्य <i>a.</i> Ved. To be wetted (by making water upon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमेह्य
अभिमि(मे)ह्य <i>a.</i> Ved. To be wetted (by making water upon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिगतं मुखं यस्य अभेर्मुखम् P. VI. 2. 185]<BR>—1 With the face turned or directed towards, in the direction of, towards,<BR> turned towards, facing; अभिमुखे मयि संहृतमीक्षितम् Ś. 2. 12. ˚खा<BR> शाला Sk.; गच्छन्नभिमुखो वह्नौ नाशं याति पतङ्गवत् Pt. 1. 237;<BR> with the acc.; राजानमेवाभिमुखा निषेदुः; पम्पामभिमुखो ययौ Rām.;<BR> Bg. 11. 28; K. 264; sometimes with dat., or gen. or loc.; आश्रमायाभिमुखा<BR> बभूवुः Mb.; यस्ते तिष्ठेदभिमुखे रणे Rām.; मथ्यभिमुखीभूय<BR> Dk. 124; also in comp. शकुन्तलाभिमुखो भूत्वा Ś. 1<BR> turning towards Ś.; Ku. 3. 75, 7. 9.<BR>—2 Coming or going near, approaching, near or close at hand; अभिमुखीष्विव<BR> वाञ्छितसिद्धिषु व्रजति निर्वृतिमेकपदे मनः V. 2. 9; यौवनाभिमुखी<BR> संजज्ञे Pt. 4; R. 17. 40.<BR>—3 Disposed or intending to, inclined to; ready for, about (to do something),<BR> in comp.; चन्द्रापीडाभिमुखहृदया K. 198, 233; अस्ताभिमुखे सूर्ये<BR> Mu. 4. 19; प्रसादाभिमुखो वेधाः प्रत्युवाच दिवौकसः Ku. 2. 16, 5. 60;<BR> U. 7. 4; Māl. 10. 13; कर्मण्यभिमुखेन स्थेयम् Dk. 89; अनभिमुखः<BR> सुखानाम् K. 45; प्रातः प्रयाणाभिमुखाय तस्मै R. 5. 29; निद्रा चिरेण<BR> नयनाभिमुखी बभूव 5. 64; sometimes as first member of comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">Page0180-2</a>]<BR> in this sense; फलमभिमुखपाकं राजजम्बूद्रुमस्य; V. 4. 27.<BR>—4 Favourable, friendly or favourably disposed; आनीय झटिति घटयति<BR> विधिरभिमतमभिमुखीभूतः Ratn. 1. 5.<BR>—5 Taking oneʼs part, nearly related to.<BR>—6 With the face turned upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखः|अभिमुख|अभिमुखं
अभिमुख + .{@-खः@} Forepart (अग्र); तस्येषुपाताभिभुखं (विसृज्य)<BR> Bhāg. 9. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखी
अभिमुख + .{@-खी@} One of the 10 earths according to Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखम्
अभिमुख + .{@-खम्, -खे@} <i>ind.</i> Towards, in the direction of, facing, in front<BR> or presence of, near to; with acc., gen. or in comp. or by itself; स<BR> दीप्त इव कालाग्निर्जज्वालाभिमुखं खगम् Rām. 5. 67. 12. आसीताभिमुखं<BR> गुरोः Ms. 2. 193; तिष्ठन्मुनेरभिमुखं स विकीर्णधाम्नः Ki. 2. 59;<BR> Śi. 13. 2; Ki. 6. 46; नेपथ्याभिमुखमवलोक्य Ś. 1; स पुराभिमुखं<BR> प्रतस्थे Pt. 3; Me. 70; कर्णं ददात्यभिमुखं मयि भाषमाणे Ś. 1. 30;<BR> also at the beginning of comp.; अभिमुखनिहतस्य Bh. 2. 112<BR> killed in the front ranks of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखे
अभिमुख + .{@-खम्, -खे@} <i>ind.</i> Towards, in the direction of, facing, in front<BR> or presence of, near to; with acc., gen. or in comp. or by itself; स<BR> दीप्त इव कालाग्निर्जज्वालाभिमुखं खगम् Rām. 5. 67. 12. आसीताभिमुखं<BR> गुरोः Ms. 2. 193; तिष्ठन्मुनेरभिमुखं स विकीर्णधाम्नः Ki. 2. 59;<BR> Śi. 13. 2; Ki. 6. 46; नेपथ्याभिमुखमवलोक्य Ś. 1; स पुराभिमुखं<BR> प्रतस्थे Pt. 3; Me. 70; कर्णं ददात्यभिमुखं मयि भाषमाणे Ś. 1. 30;<BR> also at the beginning of comp.; अभिमुखनिहतस्य Bh. 2. 112<BR> killed in the front ranks of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखता
अभिमुखता<BR>—1 Presence, proximity.<BR>—2 Favourableness; ˚तां नी to win over. मुनिमभिमुखतां निनीषवो<BR> याः समुपययुः कमनीयतागुणेन Ki. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीकृ
अभिमुखीकृ, -मुखयति<BR> To propitiate, win over; अथ भूतभव्यभवदीशमभिमुखयितुं<BR> कृतस्तवाः Ki. 12. 19; K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखयति
अभिमुखीकृ, -मुखयति<BR> To propitiate, win over; अथ भूतभव्यभवदीशमभिमुखयितुं<BR> कृतस्तवाः Ki. 12. 19; K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीकरणम्
अभिमुखीकरणम् Causing (one) to turn the face towards; speaking to,<BR> addressing (in gram.); संबोधनमभिसुखीकरणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमूर्छित
अभिमूर्छित <i>a.</i> Utterly confused, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृद्
अभिमृद् P.<BR>—1 To crush by standing, tread under foot, trample down; oppress, devastate<BR> (as a country).<BR>—2 (In astr.) To contend against, oppose, be in opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द|अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्दः<BR>—1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>—2 Crushing down, trampling down; कृतोऽभिमर्दः कुरुभिः प्रसह्य Mb. 3. 269. 8.<BR>—3 Ravage, devastation of a country (by an enemy).<BR>—4 War, battle. कथं शक्ष्यामहे ब्रह्मन् दानवैरभिमर्दनम् Mb. 12. 209. 12.<BR>—5 Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दन|अभिमर्द्दन
अभिमर्दन <i>a.</i> Crushing down, oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दनम्
अभिमर्दन + .{@-नम्@} Crushing, oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृश्
अभिमृश् €6 P. To touch (in all senses); come in contact with; strike<BR> or rub gently; अभि प्रियाणि मर्मृशत् पराणि Rv. 3. 38. 1; पदाभिमृष्ट,<BR> वचसा˚, पादतल˚, गदा˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शः|अभिमर्श
अभिमर्शः, -र्शनम्, -मर्षः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Touch, contact; उष्णांशुकराभिमर्षात् Śi. 4. 16.<BR>—2 Assault; violence, attack; सर्वतः समुपेतस्य तव तेनाभिमर्षणम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 8.<BR>—3 Outraging, touching carnally, sexual intercourse; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR> Ś. 5. 20 carnally touched or embraced, seduced, outraged; पराभिमर्शो<BR> न तवास्ति Ku. 5. 43 (Malli. = परधर्षणम्); परदाराभिमर्शेषु<BR> प्रवृत्तान् Ms. 8. 352; Y. 2. 284. (v. l. अवमर्शनम्). cf. also आत्मानं<BR> मृगमुद्दिश्य भ्रातृदाराभिमर्शनम् । Abhiṣeka. 1. 20. तस्य दाराभिमर्शेन<BR> कथं दण्ड्योऽस्मि राघव । Abhiṣeka. 1. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शनम्
अभिमर्शः, -र्शनम्, -मर्षः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Touch, contact; उष्णांशुकराभिमर्षात् Śi. 4. 16.<BR>—2 Assault; violence, attack; सर्वतः समुपेतस्य तव तेनाभिमर्षणम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 8.<BR>—3 Outraging, touching carnally, sexual intercourse; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR> Ś. 5. 20 carnally touched or embraced, seduced, outraged; पराभिमर्शो<BR> न तवास्ति Ku. 5. 43 (Malli. = परधर्षणम्); परदाराभिमर्शेषु<BR> प्रवृत्तान् Ms. 8. 352; Y. 2. 284. (v. l. अवमर्शनम्). cf. also आत्मानं<BR> मृगमुद्दिश्य भ्रातृदाराभिमर्शनम् । Abhiṣeka. 1. 20. तस्य दाराभिमर्शेन<BR> कथं दण्ड्योऽस्मि राघव । Abhiṣeka. 1. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षः|अभिमर्ष
अभिमर्शः, -र्शनम्, -मर्षः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Touch, contact; उष्णांशुकराभिमर्षात् Śi. 4. 16.<BR>—2 Assault; violence, attack; सर्वतः समुपेतस्य तव तेनाभिमर्षणम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 8.<BR>—3 Outraging, touching carnally, sexual intercourse; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR> Ś. 5. 20 carnally touched or embraced, seduced, outraged; पराभिमर्शो<BR> न तवास्ति Ku. 5. 43 (Malli. = परधर्षणम्); परदाराभिमर्शेषु<BR> प्रवृत्तान् Ms. 8. 352; Y. 2. 284. (v. l. अवमर्शनम्). cf. also आत्मानं<BR> मृगमुद्दिश्य भ्रातृदाराभिमर्शनम् । Abhiṣeka. 1. 20. तस्य दाराभिमर्शेन<BR> कथं दण्ड्योऽस्मि राघव । Abhiṣeka. 1. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षणम्
अभिमर्शः, -र्शनम्, -मर्षः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Touch, contact; उष्णांशुकराभिमर्षात् Śi. 4. 16.<BR>—2 Assault; violence, attack; सर्वतः समुपेतस्य तव तेनाभिमर्षणम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 8.<BR>—3 Outraging, touching carnally, sexual intercourse; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR> Ś. 5. 20 carnally touched or embraced, seduced, outraged; पराभिमर्शो<BR> न तवास्ति Ku. 5. 43 (Malli. = परधर्षणम्); परदाराभिमर्शेषु<BR> प्रवृत्तान् Ms. 8. 352; Y. 2. 284. (v. l. अवमर्शनम्). cf. also आत्मानं<BR> मृगमुद्दिश्य भ्रातृदाराभिमर्शनम् । Abhiṣeka. 1. 20. तस्य दाराभिमर्शेन<BR> कथं दण्ड्योऽस्मि राघव । Abhiṣeka. 1. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शक
अभिमर्शक, -र्षक, -मर्शिन्, -र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Touching, coming in contact with.<BR>—2 Outraging; assaulting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">Page0181-1</a>]<BR> परस्वहरणे युक्तं परदाराभिमर्शकं त्याज्यमाहुः Rām. 6. 87. 22.<BR> त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्षी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः Dk. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षक
अभिमर्शक, -र्षक, -मर्शिन्, -र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Touching, coming in contact with.<BR>—2 Outraging; assaulting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">Page0181-1</a>]<BR> परस्वहरणे युक्तं परदाराभिमर्शकं त्याज्यमाहुः Rām. 6. 87. 22.<BR> त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्षी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः Dk. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शिन्
अभिमर्शक, -र्षक, -मर्शिन्, -र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Touching, coming in contact with.<BR>—2 Outraging; assaulting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">Page0181-1</a>]<BR> परस्वहरणे युक्तं परदाराभिमर्शकं त्याज्यमाहुः Rām. 6. 87. 22.<BR> त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्षी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः Dk. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षिन्
अभिमर्शक, -र्षक, -मर्शिन्, -र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Touching, coming in contact with.<BR>—2 Outraging; assaulting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">Page0181-1</a>]<BR> परस्वहरणे युक्तं परदाराभिमर्शकं त्याज्यमाहुः Rām. 6. 87. 22.<BR> त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्षी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः Dk. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्ट
अभिमृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Touched, rubbed or stroked gently;<BR>—2 Brought close to, grazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमेथिक
अभिमेथिक <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमेथिका
अभिमेथिक + .{@-मेथिका@}<BR>—1 Use of words or language calculated to secure every thing (सर्वप्राप्तिसाधनो वाग्भेदः).<BR>—2 Abusive speech, obscene expression; an imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिम्लात
अभिम्लात, -न <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Altogether faded or withered, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिम्लान
अभिम्लात, -न <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Altogether faded or withered, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियज्ञः
अभियज्ञः A sacrificial act.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभियज्ञगाथा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियज्ञगाथा
अभियज्ञः + -गाथा a sacrificial verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिया
अभिया €2 P.<BR>—1 To go up to, approach, go or repair to; अभिययौ स हिमाचलमुच्छ्रितम्<BR> Ki. 5. 1; R. 9. 27.<BR>—2 To come or draw near (without an object); come (as time).<BR>—3 To march against, attack, assail, encounter; अभि स्पृधो यासिषद् वज्रबाहुः<BR> Rv. 1. 175. 5; कुबेरादभियास्यमानात् R. 5. 30; Dk. 30.<BR>—4 To give or resign oneself to, devote, attach or betake oneself to.<BR>—5 To partake or share in, get, obtain. ━<i>Caus.</i> To send away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिया
अभिया <i>m., f.</i> Going to, approaching, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातृ
अभियातृ, -यातिन् <i>a.</i><BR> approaching, assailing, encountering; assailant;<BR> रामाभियायिनां तेषाम् R. 12. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिन्
अभियातृ, -यातिन् <i>a.</i><BR> approaching, assailing, encountering; assailant;<BR> रामाभियायिनां तेषाम् R. 12. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिः|अभियाति
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायिन्
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायितृ
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायी
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ + .({@-यी, -ता@}) Approaching with hostile intentions, an assailant, enemy, a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिःता
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ + .({@-यी, -ता@}) Approaching with hostile intentions, an assailant, enemy, a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिः|अभियाति
अभियातिः, -यायिन्, -तृ + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियानम्
अभियानम्<BR>—1 Approaching.<BR>—2 Marching against, attack, assault; सीता श्रुत्वाभियानं मे आशामेष्यति<BR> जीविते Rām. 6. 4. 4; असहन्तोऽभियानं तच्छाल्वराजस्य कौरव Mb. 3. 16. 9.<BR> रणाभियानेन Dk. 10 marching out for battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाच्
अभियाच् €1 Ā. To beg, request, ask for, solicit (= याच् q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाचनम्
अभियाचनम्, -याच्ञा<BR> Asking for, request, an entreaty, solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाच्ञा
अभियाचनम्, -याच्ञा<BR> Asking for, request, an entreaty, solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्
अभियुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To apply oneself to, exert oneself, make oneself ready for, prepare,<BR> set about, strive or endeavour (used in <i>passive</i> also in this sense);<BR> तद्यदि न सहते ततः स्वयमभियुज्यस्व । एते स्वकर्मण्यभियुज्यामहे ।<BR> Mu. 3; Dk. 55; K. 300; व्यसनमभियुञ्जानस्य Mu. 4 trying to find<BR> out a weak point.<BR>—2 To attack, assail; भवन्तमभियोक्तुमुद्युङ्क्ते Dk. 3; वृषलमभियोक्तुमुद्यतः<BR> Mu. 1; क इदानीमभियोक्ष्यते U. 3.<BR>—3 To accuse, charge; complain or inform against, prosecute, claim or<BR> demand (as in a law-suit); न तत्र विद्यते किंचिद्यत्परैरवियुज्यते<BR> Ms. 8. 183; विभावितैकदेशेन देयं यदभियुज्यते V. 4. 17 claimed,<BR> asked, or demanded; Y. 2. 9, 28, 100.<BR>—4 To wish or long for, desire, ask for, request.<BR>—5 To say, speak, tell; नाभियोक्तुमनृतं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">Page0181-2</a>]<BR> त्वमिष्यसे Ki. 13. 58, 14. 7.<BR>—6 To appoint to, entrust with (with loc.).<BR>—7 To use with (instr.).<BR>—8 To be working or operative.<BR>—9 To put to; harness; harness repeatedly.<BR>—10 To hurt. ━<i>Caus.</i> To join or unite to, attach oneself to; परकलत्रेषु<BR> सुहृत्त्वेनाभियोज्य Dk. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्त|अभियुक्तः
अभियुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Engaged or occupied or absorbed in, applying oneself to, intent<BR> on; स्वस्वकर्मण्यधिकतरमभियुक्तः परिजनः Mu. 1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Diligent, persevering, resolute, zealous, intent, assiduous,<BR> zealously engaged, attentive, careful; इदं विश्वं पाल्यं विधिवदभियुक्तेन<BR> मनसा U. 3. 30; Mu. 1. 13; Dk. 55; अश्वावेक्षणेऽनभियुक्ते Mu. 3;<BR> भवतु भूयोऽभियुक्तः स्वरव्यक्तिमुपलप्स्ये Mu. 1; तेषां नित्याभियुक्तानां<BR> योगक्षेमं वहाम्यहम् Bg. 9. 22; Kām. 5. 77.<BR>—2 Well-versed or proficient in; शास्त्रार्थेष्वभियुक्तानां पुरुषाणाम् Kumārila.<BR>—3 (Hence) Learned, of acknowledged position; a competent judge, an expert,<BR> connoisseur, a learned person (<i>m.</i> also in this sense); न हि शक्यते<BR> दैवमन्यथाकर्तुमभियुक्तेनापि K. 62; अन्येऽभियुक्ता अपि नैवेदमन्यथा<BR> मन्यन्ते Ve. 2; सूक्तमिदमभियुक्तैः प्रकृतिर्दुस्त्यजेति <i>ibid.</i><BR>—4 Attacked, assailed; अभियुक्तं त्वयैनं ते गन्तारस्त्वामतः परे<BR> Śi. 2. 101; Mu. 3. 25.<BR>—5 Accused, charged, indicted; Mk. 9. 9; prosecuted; a defendant; अभियुक्तोऽभियोगस्य<BR> यदि कुर्यादपह्नवम् Nārada.<BR>—6 Appointed. अभियुक्ताश्च ये यत्र यन्निबन्धं नियोजयेत् Śukra. 4. 545.<BR>—7 Said, spoken.<BR>—8 Proper, just; श्रेयोऽभियुक्तं धर्म्यं च Rām. 7. 11. 38.<BR>—9 Believing, putting faith in; हितेष्वनभियुक्तेन सोऽयमासादितस्त्वया Mb. 6. 63. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुग्वन्
अभियुग्व(ज्व)न् <i>m.</i> One who hurts or attacks; an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्वन्
अभियुग्व(ज्व)न् <i>m.</i> One who hurts or attacks; an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्
अभियुज् <i>f.</i> (-क्, -ग्)<BR>—1 Attacking &c.<BR>—2 An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्
अभियुज् <i>f.</i> (-क्, -ग्)<BR>—1 Attacking &c.<BR>—2 An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुग्
अभियुज् <i>f.</i> (-क्, -ग्)<BR>—1 Attacking &c.<BR>—2 An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तव्य
अभियोक्तव्य, -योज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be rebuked or blamed; to be accused; न<BR> स राज्ञाऽभियोक्तव्यः Ms. 8. 50; assailable, indictable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोज्य
अभियोक्तव्य, -योज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be rebuked or blamed; to be accused; न<BR> स राज्ञाऽभियोक्तव्यः Ms. 8. 50; assailable, indictable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभियोक्तृ <i>a.</i> Assailing, attacking, accusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्ता
अभियोक्तृ + ({@-क्ता@}) ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An enemy, assailant, invader; त्वय्युत्कृष्टबलेऽभियोक्तरि^1 नृपे Mu. 4. 15; H. 3. 86.<BR>—2 (In law) A complainant, plaintiff, accuser, prosecutor; तत्राभियोक्ता<BR> प्राक् पृष्टो ह्यभियुक्तस्त्वनन्तरम् Śukra. 4. 655; Ms. 8. 52, 58; Y. 2. 95.<BR>—3 A pretender, claimant; a stronger party.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगः|अभियोग
अभियोगः<BR>—1 Application or devotion (to something); connection; गुरुचर्यातपस्तन्त्रमन्त्रयोगाभियोगजाम्<BR> Māl. 9. 52; C. P. 11.<BR>—2 Close application, perseverance, zealous intentness, energetic effort,<BR> exertion; ˚भाज् persevering, resolute; निरुत्सुकानामभियोगभाजाम्<BR> Ki. 3. 40; सन्तः स्वयं परहितेषु कृताभियोगाः Bh. 2. 73; Māl. 1. 34;<BR> मत्प्रियाभियोगेन Māl. 1; तदभियोगं प्रति निरुद्योगः Mu. 1;<BR> स्वयमभियोगदुःखैः <i>ibid.</i>; Dk. 41; K. 345; Śi. 7. 63.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Application or devotion to learn something; कस्यां कलायामभियोगो<BR> भवत्योः M. 5 to what art have you applied or devoted yourselves; K. 109.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Learning, scholarship; अभियोगश्च शब्दादेरशिष्टानाम् अभियोगश्चेतरेषाम् ŚB. on MS.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Attack,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">Page0182-1</a>]<BR> assault; invasion (of a town or country); क्षुभितं वनगोचराभियोगात्<BR> Ki. 13. 10, 2. 46; Ku. 7. 50; Ve. 4; Māl. 8; Mu. 2, 1. 7; Mv. 6. 38.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Battle, war, conflict.<BR>—5 (In law) A charge, accusation, plaint, indictment; अभियोगमनिस्तीर्य<BR> नैनं प्रत्यभियोजयेत् Y. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभियोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devoted to, intent on, absorbed in (in comp).<BR>—2 Attacking, assaulting.<BR>—3 Accusing; मिथ्याभियोगी Y. 2. 11. ━<i>m.</i> A plaintiff, complainant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोजनम्
अभियोजनम् Ved. Harnessing (one horse) on to another, re-fastening<BR> to make firm or tight (Sāy. युक्ते पुनर्योजनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्ष्
अभिरक्ष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To protect, preserve, keep, guard, help; भीष्ममेवाभिरक्षन्तु Bg. 1. 10, 11.<BR>—2 To rule over, govern (as earth &c.); command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षा
अभिरक्षा, -रक्षणम्<BR> Universal or complete protection; protection in every<BR> quarter; प्रशान्तबाधं दिशतोऽभिरक्षया Ki. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षणम्
अभिरक्षा, -रक्षणम्<BR> Universal or complete protection; protection in every<BR> quarter; प्रशान्तबाधं दिशतोऽभिरक्षया Ki. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षितृ
अभिरक्षितृ <i>a.</i> Protecting, guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरञ्ज्|अभिरंज्
अभिरञ्ज् <i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be coloured or tinted.<BR>—2 To be flushed or greatly delighted, exult. ━<i>Caus.</i> To tinge, colour, tint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्त
अभिरक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Devoted, intent, attached.<BR>—2 Sweet; सुजातपक्ष्मामभिरक्तकण्ठीम् Rām. 5. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरञ्जनम्
अभिरञ्जनम् Colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरम्
अभिरम् €1 Ā. (rarely P.)<BR>—1 To be pleased or delighted (with loc.); दृष्टिरिहाभिरमते<BR> हृदयं च Mk. 4, 5. 15; न गन्धहरिणो दमनककेदारिकायामभिरमति<BR> Vb. 3; Ratn. 2; Y. 1. 252.<BR>—2 To please or gratify oneself, take pleasure or delight in (with loc.);<BR> विद्यासु विद्वानिव सोऽभिरेमे Bk. 1. 9. ━<i>Caus.</i> To gratify,<BR> please; मत्सपत्नीरभिरमयिष्यसि Dk. 90, 92, 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरत
अभिरत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Glad, delighted, satisfied, (विप्रविसर्जने) अभिरम्यतामिति वदेद्<BR> ब्रूयुस्तेभिरताः स्म ह Y. 1. 252; रेचितं परिजनेन महीयः केवलाभिरतदम्पति<BR> धाम Śi. 10. 55, 89.<BR>—2 Engaged in, devoted or attached to; performing, practising; स्वे स्वे<BR> कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः Bg. 18. 45.<BR>—3 Attentive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरतिः|अभिरति
अभिरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Pleasure, delight, satisfaction; attachment or devotion to; न मृगयाभिरतिर्न<BR> दुरोदरम् (तमपाहरत्) R. 9. 7; Ki. 6. 44.<BR>—2 Practice, occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरमणम्
अभिरमणम् Delighting in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभिराम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pleasing, delightful, sweet, agreeable; लोकाभिरामं रणरङ्गधीरम्<BR> Rāmarakṣā. मनोऽभिरामाः (केकाः) R. 1. 39, 2. 72, 6. 47; अनपेतकालमभिरामकथाः Ki. 6. 30.<BR>—2 Beautiful, lovely, graceful, charming; स्यादस्थानोपगतयमुनासंगमेवाभिरामा<BR> Me. 53; कुमारा माराभिरामाः Dk. 10; ˚त्वं प्रमदवनस्य V. 2;<BR> राम इत्यभिरामेण वपुषा तस्य चोदितः R. 10. 67, 13. 32; K. 145; Mv. 5. 47-8.<BR> Ś. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामः|अभिराम
अभिराम + .{@-मः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामम्
अभिराम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i> —1 Gracefully, beautifully; ग्रीवाभङ्गाभिरामं दत्तदृष्टिः Ś. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Referring to Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरम्भित
अभिरम्भित <i>a.</i> Seized by; कश्मलं महदभिरम्भितः Bhāg. 5. 8. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराज्
अभिराज् <i>a.</i> Reigning everywhere, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराध्
अभिराध् <i>Caus.</i> To propitiate; निरगमदभिराद्धुमादृतानां भवति<BR> महत्सु न निष्फलः प्रयासः Śi. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराधनम्
अभिराधनम् Propitiation; ब्राह्मणस्याभिराधनम् (त्वं कर्तुमर्हसि)<BR> Mb. 3. 303. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराद्ध
अभिराद्ध <i>a.</i> Propitiated, pleased; दशाननादीनभिराद्धदेवता … Śi. 1. 71<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराष्ट्र
अभिराष्ट्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Who has gained dominion or supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुच्
अभिरुच् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine, look finely; धर्मोऽभिरोचते यस्माद्धर्मराजस्ततः स्मृतः Mārk. P.<BR>—2 To like, desire; यदभिरोचते or अभिरुचितं भवते V. 2 ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To be inclined to, have a taste or liking for, long, desire or wish for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचिः|अभिरुचि
अभिरुचिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Desire, taste, liking, relish, delight, pleasure; यशसि चाभिरुचिः<BR> Bh. 2. 63; (v. l. अभिरतिः) परस्पराभिरुचिनिष्पन्नो विवाहः K. 367.<BR>—2 Desire of fame, ambition; splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचित|अभिरुचितः
अभिरुचित <i>p. p.</i> Liked, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचितः|अभिरुचित
अभिरुचित + .{@-तः@} A lover; (वामताम्) तेनिरेऽभिरुचितेषु तरुण्यः Śi. 10. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचिर
अभिरुचिर <i>a.</i> Very pleasant or agreeable, beautiful, splendid,<BR> bright; Rv. 3. 39. 5<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुत
अभिरुत <i>a.</i> Sounded, vocal; cooed (as the voices of birds &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुतम्
अभिरुत + .{@-तम्@} A sound, cry, noise. Rām. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप <i>a.</i> [अभिगतो रूपम्]<BR>—1 Corresponding with, conformable or suitable to, congruous; अभिरूपमस्या<BR> वयसो वल्कलम् Ś. 1, v. l.<BR>—2 Pleasing, delightful, handsome, charming, beautiful, well-formed; अभिरूपेणापि<BR> स्वदारसंतुष्टेन K. 51; उत्कृष्टायाभिरूपाय वराय सदृशाय च (कन्यां<BR> दद्यात्) Ms. 9. 88.<BR>—3 Dear to, beloved or liked by, favourite; यो यः प्रदेशः सख्या मेऽभिरूपः Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Learned, wise, enlightened; अभिरूपभूयिष्ठा परिषदियम् Ś. 1; K. 78;<BR> Ms. 3. 144. cf. प्राप्तरूपाभिरूपौ द्वौ विद्वांसे सुन्दरेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपः|अभिरूप
अभिरूप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR>—3 Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 Cupid,<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिरूपपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपपतिः|अभिरूपपति
अभिरूप + -पतिः ‘having an agreeable husband’, N. of a fast or riteperformed to secure a good husband in the next world; Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपक
अभिरूपक = अभिरूप q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरोरुद
अभिरोरुद <i>a.</i> Ved. Causing tears (of joy or earnest desire); Av. 7. 38. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्षित
अभिलक्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Marked with signs, bearing marks; मुमोच परमेष्वासः षट् शरानभिलक्षितान्<BR> Rām. 3. 28. 26.<BR>—2 Selected; दक्षिणां प्रेषयामास वानरानभिलक्षितान् Rām. 4. 41. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्ष्य
अभिलक्ष्य <i>a.</i> To be marked or noted. हरिस्तस्याभिलक्ष्यस्य मोक्षयंल्लक्ष्यसंग्रहम्<BR> Rām. 5. 48. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्ष्यम्
अभिलक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Towards a mark or aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलङ्घ्|अभिलंघ्
अभिलङ्घ् €1. €10 P.<BR>—1 To jump across or over; (अग्निं) न चैनमभिलङ्घयेत् Ms. 4. 54; Y. 1. 137.<BR>—2 To attack, rush upon or over, fly at; तत्रभवत्या वदनमभिलङ्घति<BR> मधुकरः Ś. 6.<BR>—3 To violate, transgress; to offend, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलङ्घनम्
अभिलङ्घनम् Jumping across or over, flying at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलप्
अभिलप् €1 P. To talk to or address; अभिलपतश्च द्वारनिहितलोचनौ Mk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलापः|अभिलाप
अभिलापः<BR>—1 Expression, word, speech; अनवसितार्थपदाकुलोऽभिलापः Ki. 10. 61.<BR>—2 Declaration, mention, specification; न च स्मार्तमतद्धर्माभिलापात्<BR> Br. Sūt. 1. 2. 19.<BR>—3 Declaration of the object of a vow or religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलम्भनम्
अभिलम्भनम् Acquisition; शशंस पित्रे तत्सर्वं वयोरूपाभिलम्भनम्<BR> Bhāg. 9. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलष्
अभिलष् €1. €4 P. To desire or wish for, long for, covet, crave or<BR> yearn after; तेन दत्तमभिलेषुरङ्गनाः R. 19. 12; मानुषानभिलष्यन्ती Bk. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषणम्
अभिलषणम् Desiring, longing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषित
अभिलषित <i>p. p.</i> Desired, wished, longed for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषितम्
अभिलषित + .{@-तम्@} Desire, wish, will, pleasure; यथाभिलषितम् अनुष्ठीयताम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषः|अभिलाष
अभिलाषः (˚सः sometimes) A desire, wish, longing for, craving<BR> after; affection, longing of a lover, love, (usually with loc. of the<BR> object of desire); अतोऽभिलाषे प्रथमं तथाविधे मनो बबन्ध R. 3. 4;<BR> भव हृदय साभिलाषम् Ś. 1. 27; Me. 112. साभिलाषं निर्वर्ण्य<BR> Ś. 3 casting a coveting or wistful look; न खलु सत्यमेव शकुन्तलायां<BR> ममाभिलाषः Ś. 2; Pt. 5. 67; sometimes with प्रति and acc., or in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलासः|अभिलास
अभिलाषः (˚सः sometimes) A desire, wish, longing for, craving<BR> after; affection, longing of a lover, love, (usually with loc. of the<BR> object of desire); अतोऽभिलाषे प्रथमं तथाविधे मनो बबन्ध R. 3. 4;<BR> भव हृदय साभिलाषम् Ś. 1. 27; Me. 112. साभिलाषं निर्वर्ण्य<BR> Ś. 3 casting a coveting or wistful look; न खलु सत्यमेव शकुन्तलायां<BR> ममाभिलाषः Ś. 2; Pt. 5. 67; sometimes with प्रति and acc., or in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषक
अभिलाषक, -लाषि(सि)न्, -लाषुक <i>a.</i><BR> Wishing or desiring<BR> for (with acc., loc. or in comp.); desirous, covetous, greedy of; यदार्यमस्यामभिलाषि<BR> मे मनः Ś. 1. 22. जलाभिलाषी जलमाददानाम् R. 2. 6, 3. 36; Me. 80;<BR> जयमत्रभवान् नूनमरातिष्वभिलाषुकः Ki. 11. 18; Śi. 15. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

