अभिलेखनम्
अभिलिखित + .{@-तम्, अभिलेखितम्, -नम्@}<BR>—1 Writing, inscribing.<BR>—2 A writing; ज्ञातिबन्धुसाक्ष्यभिलेखितैः Y. 2. 149. A written document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिली
अभिली €4 Ā. To enter into, lurk or lie hid into; कपिलाशवस्य क्रोडमभ्यलीयत Dk. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलीन
अभिलीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Adhering or clinging to, attached to; तिरश्चकार भ्रमराभिलीनयोः<BR> सुजातयोः पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8.<BR>—2 Embracing, shrouding; पश्चादुच्चैर्भुजतरुवनं मण्डलेनाभिलीनः Me. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलुलित
अभिलुलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Agitated, disturbed.<BR>—2 Playful, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलूता
अभिलूता <i>f.</i> A sort of spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवक्तृ
अभिवक्तृ <i>a.</i> One who speaks arrogantly; Mb. 12. 180. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवद्
अभिवद् €1 U.<BR>—1 To speak to, address; परस्त्रियं योऽभिवदेत्तीर्थेऽरण्ये वनेऽपि<BR> वा Ms. 8. 356; Y. 2. 301.<BR>—2 To speak of or with reference to, tell, declare, mention; यत्कर्म<BR> क्रियमाणम् ऋगभिवदति Ait. Br.<BR>—3 To express, utter, signify; यद्वाचाऽनभ्युदितं येन वागभ्युद्यते ।<BR> तदेव ब्रह्म त्वं विद्धि नेदं यदिदमुपासते Ken. 1. 4.<BR>—4 To name, call.<BR>—5 To salute, greet; see <i>caus.</i>; ━<i>caus.</i><BR>—1 To greet or salute respectfully, oft. with the mention of the person<BR> saluted and the person who salutes; तात प्राचेतसान्तेवासी लवोऽभिवादयते<BR> U. 6. भगवन्नभिवादये V. 5; see अभिवाद also.<BR>—2 To cause to salute (with acc. or instr. of agent of action); अभिवादयते<BR> देवं भक्तं भक्तेन वा.<BR>—3 To utter, pronounce.<BR>—4 To play on an instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवदनम्
अभिवदनम्<BR>—1 Addressing &c.<BR>—2 Salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादः|अभिवाद
अभिवादः, -वादनम्<BR>—1 Reverential salutation, respectful obeisance, salutation of a superior<BR> or elder by an inferior or junior, or of a teacher by his disciple. It<BR> consists in (1) rising from oneʼs seat (प्रत्युत्थान^1); (2) clasping<BR> the feet (पादोपसंग्रह), and (3) repeating the form of salutation<BR> (अभिवाद) which includes the name or title of the person addressed,<BR> followed by the mention of the personʼs own name. For the different ways<BR> of performing obeisance and the merit arising therefrom see Ms. 2. 120-126.<BR>—2 Abuse, insulting or scurrilous speech (for अतिवाद).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादनम्
अभिवादः, -वादनम्<BR>—1 Reverential salutation, respectful obeisance, salutation of a superior<BR> or elder by an inferior or junior, or of a teacher by his disciple. It<BR> consists in (1) rising from oneʼs seat (प्रत्युत्थान^1); (2) clasping<BR> the feet (पादोपसंग्रह), and (3) repeating the form of salutation<BR> (अभिवाद) which includes the name or title of the person addressed,<BR> followed by the mention of the personʼs own name. For the different ways<BR> of performing obeisance and the merit arising therefrom see Ms. 2. 120-126.<BR>—2 Abuse, insulting or scurrilous speech (for अतिवाद).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभिवादक <i>a.</i> (-दिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Saluting; saluter<BR>—2 Polite, respectful, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादयितृ
अभिवादयितृ <i>m.</i> A respectful saluter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादिन्
अभिवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Saluting respectfully.<BR>—2 Describing, referring to; तदभिवादिनी एषा ऋग्भवति Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0183-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

