अभिविख्यात
अभिविख्यात <i>a.</i> Universally known, renowned, famous; called, known as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविधिः|अभिविधि
अभिविधिः [अभितो विधिर्व्याप्तिः]<BR>—1 Complete comprehension or inclusion; one of the senses of the particle<BR> आ; आङ् मर्यादाभिविध्योः P. II. 1. 13, the limit <i>inceptive</i> as<BR> opposed to the limit <i>conclusive</i> and translated by ‘from’, ‘commencing with’<BR>, ‘including’; as in आबालं -आबालेभ्यः -हरिभक्तिः (मर्यादा<BR> and अभिविधि are thus distinguished तेन विना मर्यादा, तत्साहितोऽभिविधिः).<BR>—2 Complete pervasion, filling up or occupying completely; अभिविधौ भाव<BR> इनुण् P. III. 3. 44; also V. 4. 53 and Sk. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविनी
अभिविनी €1 U. To teach, instruct (= विनी q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविनीत
अभिविनीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Well behaved, well principled.<BR>—2 Taught, instructed; वृद्धैरभिविनीतश्च Rām. 2. 1. 21; कस्यां<BR> कलायाम् अभिविनीते भवत्यौ M. 5, v. l. for अभियोगः दैवे निमित्ते दण्डनीत्यां<BR> च अभिविनीतम् Kau. A. 1<BR>—3 Pious, pure, devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविमान
अभिविमान <i>a.</i> Of unlimited dimensions, an epithet of the Supreme<BR> Being; यस्त्वेतमेवम् प्रादेशमात्रमभिविमानमात्मानम् वैश्वानरमुपास्ते<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 18. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविश्रुत
अभिविश्रुत <i>a.</i> Widely celebrated, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवीक्ष्
अभिवीक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To look at, view, behold, see, perceive, observe; न चैनं भुवि शक्नोति<BR> कश्चिदप्यभिवीक्षितुम् Ms. 7. 6.<BR>—2 To aim at.<BR>—3 To prove, test, examine. —4 To be affected towards, incline or lean to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवीक्षणम्
अभिवीक्षणम् Perceiving, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवीर
अभिवीर <i>a.</i> [अभिवृतो वीरैः] Surrounded by heroes; Rv. 10. 103. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृत्
अभिवृत्^1 €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go up to, go towards, go or come near, approach; used with or without<BR> any acc.; भरतो मन्त्रिभिः सार्धमभ्यवर्तत राजवत् Rām. 2. 91. 38.<BR> इत एवाभिवर्तन्ते (in dramas) are coming hitherward or in this<BR> direction; श्रावस्तीमभ्यवर्तिषि Dk. 116; तमर्च्यमारादभिवर्तमानम्<BR> R. 2. 10; यतो यतः षट्चरणोऽभिवर्तते Ś. 1. 23 turns.<BR>—2 To attack, assail, rush upon or towards, turn towards (inimically or<BR> to attack); नानाप्रहरणैः क्रुद्धस्तत्सैन्यं सोऽभ्यवर्तत Rām. T. 27. 40;<BR> वदनं मधुकरोऽभिवर्तते Ś. 1; अयमेकचरोऽभिवर्तते<BR> माम् Ki. 13. 3.<BR>—3 To face, encounter, stand opposite to.<BR>—4 To stretch or extend towards; दीर्घारण्यानि दक्षिणां दिशमभिवर्तन्ते U. 2.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To turn up, arise, begin.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To appear, commence; सरय्वाश्चोत्तरे तीरे राज्ञो यज्ञोऽभ्यवर्तत<BR> Rām. 1. 14. 1; break (as day).<BR>—6 To be, exist, chance to be.<BR>—7 To procure for one (dat.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To carry over, transport.<BR>—2 To overcome, to be master of.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: missing virAma on verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्तिन्|अभिवर्त्तिन्
अभिवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> Going towards, approaching, attacking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्तनम्
अभिवर्तनम् Going towards, approaching, attacking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्तः|अभिवर्त
अभिवर्तः Name of a Sāman; Ts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृध्
अभिवृध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To grow, increase, be augmented; हविषा कृष्णवर्त्मेव भूय एवाभिवर्धते Ms. 2. 94.<BR>—2 Thrive, prosper (of men also); दातारो नोऽभिवर्धन्तां वेदाः सन्ततिरेव<BR> च Ms. 3. 259, 7. 27; Y. 1. 245. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To increase, augment, add to; कोशम्, धनम्, प्रीतिम् &c.<BR>—2 To stretch, extend, lengthen.<BR>—3 To bring up, rear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृद्धिः|अभिवृद्धि
अभिवृद्धिः <i>f.</i> Increase, growth, addition; success, prosperity;<BR> राष्ट्र˚; सामदण्डौ प्रशंसन्ति नित्यं राष्ट्राभिवृद्धये Ms. 7. 109;<BR> लाभ˚ धन˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृष्
अभिवृष् €1 P. To rain upon, pour, sprinkle, water, bedew, cover with<BR> (a shower of anything), pour or shower down upon; प्रस्रवेणाभिवर्षन्ती<BR> (भुवम्) R. 1. 84, 10. 48, 15. 58, 99; Ki. 2. 31; बाणैर्मामभिवर्षति<BR> V. 4. ━<i>Caus.</i> To sprinkle or cover with, shower upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृष्ट
अभिवृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Sprinkled; rained upon, showered; मण्डूको यदाभिवृष्टः<BR> कनिष्कन् Rv. 7. 103. 4; स्थली नवाम्भःपृषताभिवृष्टा R. 7. 69, 15. 99;<BR> V. 4. 6; also used actively; V. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्षणम्
अभिवर्षणम् Raining upon, watering, bedewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्षिन्
अभिवर्षिन् <i>a.</i> Raining upon, bedewing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवेगः|अभिवेग
अभिवेगः Ved. Consideration, thought, determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यञ्ज्|अभिव्यंज्
अभिव्यञ्ज् €7 P. (˚अञ्ज्) or <i>Caus.</i> To manifest, make clear;<BR> reveal, disclose, exhibit, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्त
अभिव्यक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Manifested, revealed, declared.<BR>—2 Distinct, plain, clear; तां प्रत्यभिव्यक्तमनोरथानाम् R. 6. 12, 16. 23,<BR> Mu. 1; V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्तम्
अभिव्यक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Clearly, distinctly, plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्तिः|अभिव्यक्ति
अभिव्यक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Manifestation (of a cause as an effect); distinction, exposition, declaration,<BR> revelation, display, exhibition; सर्वाङ्गसौष्ठवाभिव्यक्तये M. 1; दूतीसंप्रेषणैर्नार्या<BR> भावाभिव्यक्तिरिष्यते S. D. 6.<BR>—2 Association, concomitance; P. VIII. 1. 15 (Sk. = साहचर्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यञ्जक|अभिव्यंजक
अभिव्यञ्जक <i>a.</i> Displaying, showing, indicating; गुणाभिव्यञ्जकौ<BR> शब्दार्थौ S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यञ्जनम्
अभिव्यञ्जनम् Manifesting, revealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यादानम्
अभिव्यादानम्<BR>—1 Suppressed sound.<BR>—2 Repetition of the same sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याधिन्
अभिव्याधिन् <i>a.</i> Striking, injuring greatly, hurting much; Av. 1. 91. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्
अभिव्याप् €5 P.<BR>—1 To extend to, include, comprehend; अधिकारोऽयं यूनस्तिः इत्यभिव्याप्य Sk.<BR>—2 To pervade, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यापक
अभिव्यापक, -व्यापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Including, comprehending, pervading.<BR>—2 (In gram.) One of the three kinds of आधार q. v.; ˚कः आधारः<BR> P. II. 3. 36. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यापिन्
अभिव्यापक, -व्यापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Including, comprehending, pervading.<BR>—2 (In gram.) One of the three kinds of आधार q. v.; ˚कः आधारः<BR> P. II. 3. 36. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्तिः|अभिव्याप्ति
अभिव्याप्तिः <i>f.</i> Inclusion, comprehension, universal pervasion, co-extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्य
अभिव्याप्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be included.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्यम्
अभिव्याप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} Validity of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहृ
अभिव्याहृ €1 P. To utter, pronounce; say or express well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहृत
अभिव्याहृत <i>a.</i> Pronounced, spoken, addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहृतम्
अभिव्याहृत + .{@-तम्@} What is spoken, uttered; speech, address; इत्यभिव्याहृतं<BR> तस्या आकर्ण्यासुरपुङ्गवाः Bhāg. 8. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहरणम्
अभिव्याहरणम्, -व्याहारः<BR>—1 Uttering, pronunciation, speaking.<BR>—2 An articulate significant word, a name, appellation; अभिव्याहाराय<BR> वाक् Ch. Up. 8. 12. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहारः|अभिव्याहार
अभिव्याहरणम्, -व्याहारः<BR>—1 Uttering, pronunciation, speaking.<BR>—2 An articulate significant word, a name, appellation; अभिव्याहाराय<BR> वाक् Ch. Up. 8. 12. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहारिन्
अभिव्याहारिन् <i>a.</i> Pronouncing, telling, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्लङ्गः|अभिव्लङ्ग|अभिव्लंगः
अभिव्लङ्गः Ved.<BR>—1 Going towards or against, assault.<BR>—2 Turning off, shaking off; यासां तिस्रः पञ्चाशतोऽभिव्लङ्गैरपावपः Rv. 1. 133. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंस्
अभिशंस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To blame, accuse, charge, calumniate, defame, traduce; महापापोपपापाभ्यां<BR> योऽभिशंसेन्मृषा परम् Y. 3. 285.<BR>—2 To praise, extol; किं नाम कृपणं दैवमशक्तमभिशंससि Rām. 2. 23. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसक
अभिशंसक, -शंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Accusing, charging, calumniating, insulting, abusive;<BR> मिथ्याभिशंसिनो दोषो द्विः समो भूतवादिनः Y. 3. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसिन्
अभिशंसक, -शंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Accusing, charging, calumniating, insulting, abusive;<BR> मिथ्याभिशंसिनो दोषो द्विः समो भूतवादिनः Y. 3. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसनम्
अभिशंसनम् Accusation, charge; (whether true or false); मिथ्या˚<BR> Y. 2. 289; abuse, insult, affront; पंचाशद् ब्राह्मणो दण्ड्यः क्षत्रियस्याभिशंसने Ms. 8. 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Charged, falsely accused, calumniated, abused, insulted; यानि मिथ्याभिशस्तानां<BR> पतन्त्यश्रूणि राघव Rām. 2. 100. 59; Ms. 8. 116, 373; Y. 1. 161, 3. 284.<BR>—2 Hurt, injured, attacked (supposed to be from अभिशस्); देवि केनाभिशस्तासि<BR> केन वासि विमानिता Rām.; अभिशस्तं प्रपश्यन्ति दरिद्रम् पार्श्वतः<BR> स्थितम् Mb. 12. 8. 14; Ms. 11. 112 threatened.<BR>—3 Cursed (for अभिशप्त).<BR>—4 Wicked, sinful, infamous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तम्
अभिशस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} = अभिशस्ति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तक
अभिशस्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Falsely accused, defamed; wicked; Y. 1. 223; a person of bad repute; 2. 70.<BR>—2 Caused by imprecation or curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तिः|अभिशस्ति
अभिशस्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A curse.<BR>—2 Effect of an imprecation, misfortune, evil, calamity.<BR>—3 Censure, calumny, abuse, defamation, charge, insult.<BR>—4 Asking, begging.<BR>—5 What curses or injures; the cause or source of injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्क्|अभिशंक्
अभिशङ्क्^1 €1 Ā. (P. also) To doubt, mistrust, suspect, be suspicious<BR> of (with acc. of person or thing); माभिशङ्कीर्वचो मम Mb. अवस्थामभिशङ्कते<BR> Mk. 9. 8; Ms. 8. 96; also with abl.; be afraid of; Bk. 6. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्का|अभिशंका
अभिशङ्का Doubt, suspicion, apprehension, fear, alarm, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्कित|अभिशंकित
अभिशङ्कित <i>p. p.</i> Doubtful, suspicious, apprehensive; प्रविभयांचकाराऽसौ<BR> काकुत्स्थादभिशङ्कितः Bk. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशप्
अभिशप् €1 U. To curse, execrate; अभिशप्तः फलमेतदन्वभूत् Ku. 4. 41.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To conjure, invoke (as by charms), charm, enchant;<BR> सत्येन माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कम् Y. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपनम्
अभिशपनम्, -शापः<BR>—1 A curse, imprecation.<BR>—2 A serious charge, accusation; नृपार्थेष्वभिशापे च वहेयुः शुचयः<BR> सदा Y. 2. 99; अभिशापः पातकाभियोगः Mit.<BR>—3 Slander, calumny, false charge; असतो दोषस्य अध्याहारोऽभिशापः; अभिशापभयाद्भीतो<BR> भवन्तं नोपसर्पति Mb. 12. 55. 11.<BR>—4 An injury, hurt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिशपनज्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापः|अभिशाप
अभिशपनम्, -शापः<BR>—1 A curse, imprecation.<BR>—2 A serious charge, accusation; नृपार्थेष्वभिशापे च वहेयुः शुचयः<BR> सदा Y. 2. 99; अभिशापः पातकाभियोगः Mit.<BR>—3 Slander, calumny, false charge; असतो दोषस्य अध्याहारोऽभिशापः; अभिशापभयाद्भीतो<BR> भवन्तं नोपसर्पति Mb. 12. 55. 11.<BR>—4 An injury, hurt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिशपनज्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपनज्वरः
अभिशपनम् + -ज्वरः fever caused by the pronunciation of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापनम्
अभिशापनम् Pronouncing a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दित
अभिशब्दित <i>a.</i> Declared, announced, said, named; ध्यानिकं सर्वमेवैतद्यदेतदभिशब्दितम् Ms. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्
अभिशस् €1 P. To hurt, injure, attack (= अभिशंस्^1 q. v.) ━<i>f.</i><BR> Ved. Accusation, charge, imprecation &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त <i>p. p.</i> Hurt, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तृ
अभिशस्तृ <i>m.</i> An enemy, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशिरोग्र
अभिशिरोग्र <i>a.</i> With the top and bottom inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशीत
अभिशीत, -श्यात<BR> [श्यै-क्त] <i>a.</i> Cold, chilly, as wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्यात
अभिशीत, -श्यात<BR> [श्यै-क्त] <i>a.</i> Cold, chilly, as wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशीन
अभिशीन, -श्यान <i>a.</i><BR> Congealed, coagulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्यान
अभिशीन, -श्यान <i>a.</i><BR> Congealed, coagulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोकः|अभिशोक
अभिशोकः<BR>—1 Intense grief.<BR>—2 Warmth; ardour (Ved.); यदि शोको यदि वाऽभिशोको Av. 1. 25. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोच
अभिशोच <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shining, glowing with heat.<BR>—2 Causing great grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोचनम्
अभिशोचनम्<BR>—1 Intense grief or pain, torment.<BR>—2 That which torments; a spirit or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोचयिष्णु
अभिशोचयिष्णु <i>a.</i> Tormenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्यात
अभिश्यात or अभिशीत <i>a.</i> Cold, Chilly; विभाषाभ्यवपूर्वस्य<BR> P. VI. 1. 26. Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशीत
अभिश्यात or अभिशीत <i>a.</i> Cold, Chilly; विभाषाभ्यवपूर्वस्य<BR> P. VI. 1. 26. Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रवणम्
अभिश्रवणम् Repeating Vedic texts, while Brāhmaṇas are sitting<BR> down to a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रावः|अभिश्राव
अभिश्रावः Hearing (a prayer); granting (an answer); अभिश्रावाय<BR> प्रथमं सुमेधाः Rv. 1. 185. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रुत
अभिश्रुत <i>a.</i> Renowned; त्वं वीरुधां श्रेष्ठतमाभिश्रुतास्योषधे Av. 6. 138. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्री
अभिश्री <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Joining, connected with, mixing; attached to; शिवे ते स्तां द्यावापृथिवी<BR> असंतापे अभिश्रियौ Rv. 1. 144. 6; Av. 8. 2. 14;<BR>—2 Combining; arranging.<BR>—3 Approaching, having recourse to.<BR>—4 Worthy.<BR>—5 Shining.<BR>—6 Powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रिष्
अभिश्रिष्, -श्लिष् <i>f.</i> (-ट्) Ved.<BR> A ligature; य ऋते चिदभिश्रिषः Rv. 8. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्लिष्
अभिश्रिष्, -श्लिष् <i>f.</i> (-ट्) Ved.<BR> A ligature; य ऋते चिदभिश्रिषः Rv. 8. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्लेषणम्
अभिश्लेषणम् A bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वस्
अभिश्वस् <i>m.</i> Ved. One who breathes upon or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वसः|अभिश्वस
अभिश्वसः Ved. Breathing forth or upon, eructation (of the stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वासः|अभिश्वास
अभिश्वासः Breathing or blowing upon; blowing into a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वैत्य
अभिश्वैत्य <i>a.</i> (अभितः श्वैत्यं शुद्धचारित्र्यादिर्यस्य) One whose<BR> conduct is chaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषञ्ज्|अभिषंज्
अभिषञ्ज् €1 P. [˚सञ्ज्, स् being changed to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 65]<BR> To be in contact with, touch; attach oneself to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषक्त
अभिषक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed by evil spirits.<BR>—2 Humiliated, defeated.<BR>—3 Reviled, cursed; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषङ्गः|अभिषङ्ग|अभिषंग|अभिषंगः
अभिषङ्गः (also अभिसङ्गः)<BR>—1 Complete contact or union; attachment, connection, association; कन्यका<BR> दुन्वन्ति हृदयं मनुष्याणामीदृशाद् दुरभिसङ्गात् Māl. 7 ill attachment<BR> or union; Māl. 8; मुहुरिति वनविभ्रमाभिषङ्गात् Śi. 7. 68; K. 146, 290.<BR>—2 Defeat, mortification, discomfiture; जाताभिषङ्गो नृपतिः R. 2. 30.<BR>—3 A sudden blow, shock or grief, a sudden calamity or misfortune, unexpected<BR> reverse; ततोऽभिषङ्गानिलविप्रविद्धा R. 14. 54, 77; Ku. 3. 73; ˚जडं<BR> विजज्ञिवान् R. 8. 75.<BR>—4 Possession by devils or evil spirits; अभिघाताभिषङ्गाभ्यामभिचाराभिशापतः Mādh. N.<BR>—5 An oath.<BR>—6 Embracing; copulation.<BR>—7 A curse or imprecation, abuse.<BR>—8 A false charge or accusation, calumny or defamation.<BR>—9 Contempt, disrespect.<BR>—10 The state of being disturbed in mind; उच्चारितं मे मनसोऽभिषङ्गात्<BR> Mb. 5. 30. 1. cf. अभिषङ्गस्तु शपथे शापे सङ्गे पराभवे Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिषङ्गज्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसङ्गः|अभिसङ्ग
अभिषङ्गः (also अभिसङ्गः)<BR>—1 Complete contact or union; attachment, connection, association; कन्यका<BR> दुन्वन्ति हृदयं मनुष्याणामीदृशाद् दुरभिसङ्गात् Māl. 7 ill attachment<BR> or union; Māl. 8; मुहुरिति वनविभ्रमाभिषङ्गात् Śi. 7. 68; K. 146, 290.<BR>—2 Defeat, mortification, discomfiture; जाताभिषङ्गो नृपतिः R. 2. 30.<BR>—3 A sudden blow, shock or grief, a sudden calamity or misfortune, unexpected<BR> reverse; ततोऽभिषङ्गानिलविप्रविद्धा R. 14. 54, 77; Ku. 3. 73; ˚जडं<BR> विजज्ञिवान् R. 8. 75.<BR>—4 Possession by devils or evil spirits; अभिघाताभिषङ्गाभ्यामभिचाराभिशापतः Mādh. N.<BR>—5 An oath.<BR>—6 Embracing; copulation.<BR>—7 A curse or imprecation, abuse.<BR>—8 A false charge or accusation, calumny or defamation.<BR>—9 Contempt, disrespect.<BR>—10 The state of being disturbed in mind; उच्चारितं मे मनसोऽभिषङ्गात्<BR> Mb. 5. 30. 1. cf. अभिषङ्गस्तु शपथे शापे सङ्गे पराभवे Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिषङ्गज्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषङ्गज्वरः|अभिषङ्गज्वर
अभिषङ्गः + -ज्वरः fever caused by the action of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषञ्जनम्
अभिषञ्जनम् = अभिषङ्ग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषव|अभिषवं|अभिषवः
अभिषव see under अभिषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषह्य
अभिषह्य <i>ind.</i> By force, forcibly, violently; insolently; अभिषह्य<BR> तु यः कन्यां कुर्याद्दर्पेण मानवः Ms. 8. 367.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषाच्
अभिषाच् <i>a.</i> [अभि-सच् स्वार्थे णिच् क्विप्] Ved.<BR>—1 Following.<BR>—2 Honouring, devoted.<BR>—3 Defeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषाह्
अभिषाह् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bearing, patient.<BR>—2 Overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषिच्
अभिषिच् €6 U. [˚सिच्, स् changed to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 65]<BR>—1 To sprinkle, pour down upon, water, wet, shower upon (fig. also); स्नान्तीहाभ्यषिचज्जलैः<BR> Bk. 6. 21, 15. 3, 6. 23; सङ्गे पुनर्बहुतराममृताभिषिक्ताम् C. P. 29 v. l.<BR> अथ वपुरभिषेक्तुं तास्तदाम्भोभिरीषुः Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—2 To anoint, consecrate, appoint &c. (by sprinkling water on the head);<BR> to crown, install, inaugurate (with loc. of the post of authority); अग्निवर्णमभिषिच्य<BR> राघवः स्वे पदे R. 19. 1, 17. 13; सोऽटवीराज्येऽभिषिक्तः H. 2; V. 5. 23.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To have another consecrated, inaugurated &c.<BR>—2 To let oneself be crowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषिक्त
अभिषिक्त <i>a.</i> Sprinkled, anointed, installed. cf. मूर्धाभिषिक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकः|अभिषेक
अभिषेकः<BR>—1 Sprinkling, watering, wetting.<BR>—2 Anointing, inaugurating or consecrating by sprinkling water (a king,<BR> idol &c.). ततो हि नः प्रियतरं नान्यात्किंचिद्भविष्यति । यथाभिषेको<BR> रामस्य Rām. 2. 17. 11; अग्निहोत्राभिषेकौ Kau. A. 1. 3.<BR>—3 (Particularly) Coronation, inauguration, installation (of kings); royal<BR> unction; अथाभिषेकं रघुवंशकेतोः R. 14. 7.<BR>—4 The (holy) water required at inauguration, coronation water; अमात्यपरिषदं<BR> ब्रूहि संभ्रियतामायुषो राज्याभिषेक इति V. 5; यौवराज्य˚ <i>ibid.</i>; R. 17. 14.<BR>—5 Bathing; ablution, holy or religious bathing; अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय काश्यपाय<BR> Ś. 4; अत्राभिषेकाय तपोधनानाम् R. 13. 51, 1. 85, 10. 63, 13. 58, 14. 82;<BR> K. 22, 36, 96; Ku. 5. 16, 7. 11; Ś. 7. 12; H. 4. 87.<BR>—6 Bathing or sprinkling with water (of a divinity to whom worship is offered).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिषेकाहः, अभिषेकशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकाहः|अभिषेकाह
अभिषेकः + -अहः day of coronation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकशाला
अभिषेकः + -शाला coronation-hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक्तृ
अभिषेक्तृ <i>a.</i> One who sprinkles, anoints, inaugurates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचनम्
अभिषेचनम्<BR>—1 Sprinkling.<BR>—2 Coronation, inauguration; अनुभूय वशिष्ठसंभृतैः सलिलैस्तेन सहाभिषेचनम् R. 8. 3.<BR>—3 Equipment, paraphernalia of coronation; भरतश्चाभिषिच्येत यदेतदभिषेचनम् ।<BR> त्वदर्थे विहितं राज्ञा तेन सर्वेण राघव ॥ Rām. 2. 18. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचनीय|अभिषेचनीयः
अभिषेचनीय, -षेच्य, -षेक्य<BR>—1 Worthy of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>—2 Belonging to coronation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेच्य
अभिषेचनीय, -षेच्य, -षेक्य<BR>—1 Worthy of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>—2 Belonging to coronation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक्य
अभिषेचनीय, -षेच्य, -षेक्य<BR>—1 Worthy of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>—2 Belonging to coronation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचनीयः|अभिषेचनीय
अभिषेचनीय, -षेच्य, -षेक्य + .{@-यः@} N. of a sacrificial ceremony performed at the coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषु
अभिषु €5 P. (˚सु)<BR>—1 To extract Soma juice or any juice; अभिषुण्वन्त आसते Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To apply water to or press out; यानि चैवाभिषूयन्ते पुष्पमूलफलैः<BR> शुभैः Ms. 5. 10 (Kull. उदकेन संधा).<BR>—3 To moisten, sprinkle; ते विज्ञायाऽभिसोष्यन्तं रक्तै रक्षांसि सव्यथाः Bk. 9. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवः|अभिषव|अभिषवं
अभिषवः [अभि-सु-अप्]<BR>—1 Extracting or pressing out the Soma juice. चक्रुस्ते विधिवद्राजंस्तथैवाभिषवं<BR> द्विजाः Mb. 14. 88. 21.<BR>—2 Distillation or extraction (of liquors &c.).<BR>—3 Religious bathing, ablution preparatory to religious rites.<BR>—4 Bathing or ablution (in general); जपोपवासाभिषवैर्मुनीनाम् Ki. 3. 28.<BR>—5 Drinking the Soma juice.<BR>—6 A sacrifice in general.<BR>—7 Ferment, yeast; any substance producing fermentation.<BR>—8 A finger used in extracting Soma juice (Nir.).<BR>—9 Coronation; रामाभिषवसंयुक्ताश्चक्रुरेव कथा मिथः Rām. 2. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवम्
अभिषवः + .{@-वम्@} Sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवणम्
अभिषवणम्<BR>—1 Bathing; कृतजन्मनोऽभिषवणेन जटाः Ki. 6. 23.<BR>—2 Means of extracting or pressing out Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवणी
अभिषवणी A mechanical contrivance to press out the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषावकः|अभिषावक
अभिषावकः, -षोतृ <i>m.</i><BR> The priest who extracts the the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषोतृ
अभिषावकः, -षोतृ <i>m.</i><BR> The priest who extracts the the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुत|अभिषुतं
अभिषुत <i>p. p.</i> Extracted, pressed out, as Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुतम्
अभिषुत + .{@-तम्@} Sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुकः|अभिषुक
अभिषुकः Name of a plant. Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेण
अभिषेण <i>a.</i> Ved. Approaching (as an enemy) with an army; Rv. 6. 44. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणनम्
अभिषेणनम् Marching against an enemy, encountering a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणयति
अभिषेणयति Den. P. [अभिसेना-णिच् P. III. 1. 25, VIII. 3. 65]<BR> To march against (with an army), to attack, to face or encounter (another)<BR> with an army; कः सिन्धुराजमभिषेणयितुं समर्थः Ve. 2. 26; Śi. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टनः|अभिष्टन
अभिष्टनः [अभि-स्तन्-अप्-षत्वम्] Ved. Roaring, a loud shout (सिंहनाद);<BR> अभिष्टने ते अद्रिवो यत् स्था जगच्च रेजते Rv. 1. 80. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टि|अभिष्टिः
अभि(भी)ष्टि <i>a.</i> (Ved.) To be worshipped by offering sacrifices<BR> (Sāy. अभियष्टव्य); an assistant, a protector, one who is praised<BR> or worshipped as a protector, one who approaches to assist or attack,<BR> one who assails or overpowers an enemy, one who approaches in order to<BR> obtain, desiring, desire (these meanings are given by European scholars).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टि
अभि(भी)ष्टि <i>a.</i> (Ved.) To be worshipped by offering sacrifices<BR> (Sāy. अभियष्टव्य); an assistant, a protector, one who is praised<BR> or worshipped as a protector, one who approaches to assist or attack,<BR> one who assails or overpowers an enemy, one who approaches in order to<BR> obtain, desiring, desire (these meanings are given by European scholars).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टिः|अभिष्टि
अभि(भी)ष्टि + .{@-ष्टिः@} <i>f.</i> Assistance, help, worshipping, praising; a sacrifice;<BR> a hymn; approaching to assist or approaching in general; access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टिमत्|अभिष्टिमन्त्
अभिष्टिमत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टु
अभिष्टु €2 P. (-स्तु)<BR>—1 To praise, laud, extol; अथ इतरामभिष्टुवन्ति U. 5; Śi. 15. 20.<BR>—2 To consecrate, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टुत|अभिष्टुतं
अभिष्टुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praised, commended; अभिगम्य च तत्तुष्ट्या दत्तमाहुरभिष्टुतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 293. 18.<BR>—2 Consecrated; ओङ्काराभिष्टुतं सोमसलिलं पावनं पिबेत् Y. 3. 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टवः|अभिष्टव
अभिष्टवः Praise, eulogy; देवा ब्रह्मादयः सर्वे उपतस्थुरभिष्टवैः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 1. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्द्
अभिष्यन्द् €1 Ā. (स् changed to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 72) —1 To ooze,<BR> flow, trickle; अभिस्य(ष्य)न्दते दुग्धम् Sk.; सततमभिष्यन्दमानमेघमेदुरितनीलिमा (गिरिः) U. 1<BR> raining or pouring down water.<BR>—2 (fig.) To be melted (with pity, love &c.), to overflow with; यदि<BR> त्वामीदृशं रामभद्रः पश्येत् तदास्य हृदयं स्नेहेनाभिष्यन्देत U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दः|अभिष्यन्द|अभिष्यंदः
अभिष्य(स्य)न्दः<BR>—1 Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>—2 Weakness of, or running at, the eyes.<BR>—3 Great increase, or enlargement, surplus, excess, superfluous portion;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिष्यन्दवमनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्यन्दः|अभिस्यन्द|अभिस्यंदः
अभिष्य(स्य)न्दः<BR>—1 Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>—2 Weakness of, or running at, the eyes.<BR>—3 Great increase, or enlargement, surplus, excess, superfluous portion;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिष्यन्दवमनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दवमनम्
अभिष्यन्दः + -वमनम्; स्वर्गाभिष्यन्दवमनं कृत्वेवोपनिवेशितम् (ओषधिप्रस्थम्)<BR> Ku. 6. 37 by drawing off the surplus population <i>i. e.</i> by emigration<BR> (अभिष्यन्दः अतिरेकः अतिरिक्तजन इति यावत् तस्य वमनं निःसारणं<BR> कृत्वा स्थितमिव); cf. also R. 15. 29 Hemacandraʼs remarks thereon.<BR> also स्वदेशाभिष्यन्दवमनम् Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिन्|अभिष्यंदिन्
अभिष्य(स्य)न्दिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Oozing, flowing, trickling,<BR>—2 Laxative, opening the bowels.<BR>—3 Causing defluxions or watery effusion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिष्यन्दिरमणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्यन्दिन्|अभिस्यंदिन्
अभिष्य(स्य)न्दिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Oozing, flowing, trickling,<BR>—2 Laxative, opening the bowels.<BR>—3 Causing defluxions or watery effusion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिष्यन्दिरमणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिरमणम्
अभिष्यन्दिन् + -रमणम् a suburb, smaller city appended to and regarded as part<BR> of a larger one; cf. शाखानगरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्वङ्गः|अभिष्वङ्ग|अभिष्वंग|अभिष्वंगः
अभिष्वङ्गः [स्वञ्ज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Contact; सर्वदोषानभिष्वङ्गादाम्नायसमतां गताः Mv. 1. 38.<BR>—2 Intense attachment, love, affection; विद्यास्वभिष्वङ्गः Dk. 155;<BR> अहो अभिष्वङ्गः Māl. 1; काम˚ <i>ibid.</i> असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः<BR> पुत्रदारगृहादिषु Bg. 13. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंयोगः|अभिसंयोग
