अभिसमापद्
अभिसमापद् €4 Ā. To enter upon; चितामभिसमापेदे Rām. 2. 12. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसमापन्न
अभिसमापन्न <i>a.</i> Facing, one who is in front. (कः कृष्णसर्पम्)<BR> तुदत्यभिसमापन्नमङ्गुल्यग्रेण लीलया Rām. 3. 19. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपत्|अभिसम्पत्
अभिसंपत्^1 €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly towards, hasten, jump upon; महीतलात्केचिदुदीर्णवेगाः पुनर्द्रुमाग्रानभिसंपतन्ति Rām.<BR>—2 To fly along; शस्त्रैश्च दिव्यैरभिसंपतद्भिः Mb.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. note: verb missing virAma,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपातः|अभिसम्पात|अभिसंपात|अभिसम्पातः
अभिसंपातः<BR>—1 Meeting together, concourse, confluence.<BR>—2 War battle, contest.<BR>—3 A curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपद्|अभिसम्पद्
अभिसंपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To become (anything); to be changed to, be similar to, assume the state<BR> of; ब्रह्मलोकमभिसंपद्यते Ch. Up. 8. 15. 1. इष्टकामग्निरभिसंपद्यते Śat. Br.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">Page0188-2</a>]<BR> श्रोत्रे हीमे सर्वे वेदा अभिसंपन्नाः <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 To come or go, arrive at.<BR>—3 To get, to obtain. ━<i>Caus.</i> To make similar to, change into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपत्तिः|अभिसम्पत्ति|अभिसंपत्ति
अभिसंपत्तिः <i>f.</i> Becoming or being effected completely, going<BR> over, transition; being changed into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपद्|अभिसम्पद्
अभिसंपद् <i>f.</i> Becoming complete; complete number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपन्न|अभिसम्पन्न
अभिसंपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Complete, completely effected; वदत्ययमभिसंपन्नमार्षेण संस्कारेण<BR> U. 5 quite in keeping with his holy instruction.<BR>—2 Filled up, covered with; अन्तरिक्षेऽभिसंपन्ने न रूपाणि चकाशिरे<BR> Rām. 6. 89. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपरायः|अभिसम्पराय|अभिसंपराय
अभिसंपरायः Futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबन्ध्|अभिसम्बन्ध्|अभिसंबंध्
अभिसंबन्ध् €9 P. To bind together. ━<i>pass.</i> To be connected with,<BR> to relate or refer to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबन्धः|अभिसम्बन्ध|अभिसंबन्ध|अभिसंबंधः
अभिसंबन्धः —1 Connection, relation; conjunction, contact; शिष्टाञ्शिष्टाभिसंबन्धान्मानिनोऽनवमानिनः<BR> Mb. 12. 57. 23; sexual connection; बैजिकादभिसंबन्धादनुरुन्ध्यादघं<BR> त्र्यहम् Ms. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबाध|अभिसम्बाध
अभिसंबाध <i>a.</i> Very much contracted or confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंमुख|अभिसम्मुख
अभिसंमुख <i>a.</i> Facing, fronting, looking respectfully towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर|अभिसरः
अभिसर, -सर्ग, -सर्जन &c.<BR> See under अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ग|अभिसर्गः
अभिसर, -सर्ग, -सर्जन &c.<BR> See under अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभिसर, -सर्ग, -सर्जन &c.<BR> See under अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्पणम्
अभिसर्पणम् Approaching, drawing near (with hostile intention).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसान्त्व्|अभिसांत्व्
अभिसा(शा)न्त्व् €10 P. To conciliate, propitiate, pacify, comfort, console;<BR> उवाच च तदा रामस्तं गार्ग्यमभिसान्त्वयन् Rām. 2. 32. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशान्त्व्|अभिशांत्व्
अभिसा(शा)न्त्व् €10 P. To conciliate, propitiate, pacify, comfort, console;<BR> उवाच च तदा रामस्तं गार्ग्यमभिसान्त्वयन् Rām. 2. 32. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसान्त्वः|अभिसान्त्व|अभिसांत्वः
अभिसा(शा)न्त्वः, -न्त्वनम् Conciliation, consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशान्त्वः|अभिशान्त्व|अभिशांत्वः
अभिसा(शा)न्त्वः, -न्त्वनम् Conciliation, consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसान्त्वनम्
अभिसा(शा)न्त्वः, -न्त्वनम् Conciliation, consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायः|अभिसाय|अभिसायं
अभिसायः<BR>—1 Destruction, end.<BR>—2 Sunset ‘सायो नाशदिनान्तयोः’ इति विश्वः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायार्कम्
अभिसायः + .{@-अर्कम्@} ━<i>ind.</i> At Sunset; अभिसायार्कमावृत्तां छायामिव Ki. 11. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायम्
अभिसायम् <i>ind.</i> At sunset, about evening; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृ
अभिसृ P.<BR>—1 To go up to, go towards, approach; to go to some place or other,<BR> go or proceed; पुरोभिसस्रे सुरसुन्दरीजनैः Ki. 8. 4.<BR>—2 To attack, assail.<BR>—3 To go or advance to meet (as at an appointed place); सुन्दरीरभिससार<BR> K. 58; Dk. 51, 52, 91; अभिससार न वल्लभमङ्गना Śi. 6. 26. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To visit, approach, go to meet; वल्लभानभिसिसारयिषूणाम् Śi. 10. 20, 21;<BR> S. D. 115; Ki. 9. 38; Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरः|अभिसर
अभिसरः<BR>—1 A follower, an attendant; Dk. 73, 127.<BR>—2 A companion; मन्मथाभिसरा तदागारमभिसरामि Dk. 15; शिवराजस्याभिसराः<BR> प्रसरन्ति पुरः पुरः Śiva B. 24. 39.<BR>—3 N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरणम्
अभिसरणम्<BR>—1 Approaching, going to meet (also with hostile intentions).<BR>—2 Meeting, rendezvous,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">Page0189-1</a>]<BR> assignation or appointment of lovers; त्वदभिसरणरभसेन वलन्ती<BR> पतति पदानि क्रियन्ति चलन्ती Gīt. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरी
अभिसरी (-रिः), <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Following; असुरपुरवधे गच्छन्त्यभिसरीम् Pratimā 3. 7.<BR>—2 Going out to help; गत्वा पूर्वं स्वसैन्यैरभिसरिसमये खं समानैर्विमानैः<BR> Pratimā 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरिः
अभिसरी (-रिः), <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Following; असुरपुरवधे गच्छन्त्यभिसरीम् Pratimā 3. 7.<BR>—2 Going out to help; गत्वा पूर्वं स्वसैन्यैरभिसरिसमये खं समानैर्विमानैः<BR> Pratimā 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्तृ
अभिसर्तृ <i>a.</i> One who attacks; an assailant; शोकायाभिसर्तारम् Vāj. 30. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारः|अभिसार
अभिसारः<BR>—1 Going to meet (as a lovers), appointment, assignation; रतिसुखसारे<BR> गतमभिसारे मदनमनोहरवेशम् Gīt. 5.<BR>—2 The place where lovers meet by appointment, rendezvous; त्वरितमुपैति<BR> न कथमभिसारम् Gīt. 6.<BR>—3 An attack, assault; श्वोऽभिसारः पुरस्य नः Rām.<BR>—4 War, battle.<BR>—5 A follower, companion.<BR>—6 Might, power.<BR>—7 An instrument, means; अभिसारेण सर्वेण तत्र युद्धमवर्तत Mb. 3. 15. 4.<BR>—8 A purificatory rite.<BR>—9 ({@˚राः@} pl.) N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारी
अभिसारः + .{@-री@} N. of a town.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभिसारस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारस्थानम्
अभिसारः + -स्थानम् a place fit for making appointments; see under अभिसारिका below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारणम्
अभिसारणम् Going to meet a lover &c. प्रकुपितमभिसारणेऽनुनेतुं Ki. 10. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभिसारिका A woman who either goes to meet her lover or keeps an appointment<BR> made by him; यत्रौषधिप्रकाशेन नक्तं दर्शितसंचराः । अनभिज्ञास्तमिस्राणां<BR> दुर्दिनेष्वभिसारिकाः Ku. 6. 43; R. 16. 12; अभिसारयते कान्तं या मन्मथवशंवदा ।<BR> स्वयं वाभिसरत्येषा धीरैरुक्ताऽभिसारिका S. D. 115; कान्तार्थिनी तु<BR> या याति संकेतं साभिसारिका Ak. The directions as to dress &c. to be<BR> observed by the different kinds of अभिसारिका are given in S. D. 116.<BR> The S. D. further recommends the following 8 places as eligible spots<BR> for lovers to meet:− (1) a field; (2) a garden; (3) a ruined temple; (4)<BR> the house of a female messenger; (5) forest; (6) caravansary (a place<BR> for pilgrims &c.); (7) a cemetery; and (8) the bank of a river; क्षेत्रं<BR> वाटी भग्नदेवालयो दूतीगृहं वनम् । मालयं च श्मशानं च नद्यादीनां तटी तथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिन्
अभिसारिन् <i>a.</i> Going to meet, visiting; attacking, rushing out,<BR> going forth; युद्धाभिसारिणः U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिणी
अभिसारिन् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 = अभिसारिका see above.<BR>—2 N. of a species of the त्रिष्टुभ् metre in which the Pādas contain 12<BR> instead of 11 syllables, and which is, therefore, said to approach<BR> (अभिसरति) another metre called जगती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृज्
अभिसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To pour out or forth; एते वामभ्यसृक्षत तिरः पवित्रमाशवः Rv. 1. 135. 6.<BR>—2 To make, prepare; तस्य चितेयमभिसृष्टा Mv. 5.<BR>—3 To unloose, untie.<BR>—4 To give, grant; अभिसृज्य वरद्वयम् Rām.<BR>—5 To fall upon, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्गः|अभिसर्ग
अभिसर्गः Creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्जनम्
अभिसर्जनम्<BR>—1 A gift, donation.<BR>—2 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसेवनम्
अभिसेवनम्<BR>—1 Practising, observing.<BR>—2 Cultivating.<BR>—3 Fondness of, indulgence in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्कन्दः|अभिस्कन्द|अभिस्कंदः
अभिस्कन्दः Ved.<BR>—1 An attack, assault.<BR>—2 An assailant, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्कन्दम्
अभिस्कन्दः + .{@-न्दम्@} <i>adv.</i> By attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्नेहः|अभिस्नेह
अभिस्नेहः Attachment, affection; love, desire; यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहः Bg. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्फुरित
अभिस्फुरित <i>a.</i> Expanded to the full, full-grown (as a blossom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्रवन्त
अभिस्रवन्त <i>a.</i> Flowing, bestowing; शंयोरभिस्रवन्ताय अथर्वाय<BR> नमो नमः Mb. 13. 14. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वृ
अभिस्वृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To assent or agree to, approve of.<BR>—2 To praise, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्
अभिस्वर् <i>f.</i> (or <i>n.</i> according to some) [अभितः स्वः स्वरणशब्दो यस्य] Ved.<BR>—1 Invocation, calling into oneʼs presence; अभिस्वरा निषदा गा Rv. 2. 21. 53, 3. 45. 2.<BR>—2 A song or hymn of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वरः|अभिस्वर
अभिस्वरः Urging towards, driving onwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वरे
अभिस्वरः + .{@-रे@} Very close or near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्तृ
अभिस्वर्तृ <i>m.</i> Praising; invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहन्
अभिहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike, smite, beat (fig. also); thump at; अभिहन्ति हन्त कथमेष<BR> माधवम् (स्मरः) Māl. 1. 39; लोष्टैरभिघ्नन्तो नयत U. 4;<BR> कल्लोलमालाभिहतः पोतः Dk. 7.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, kill, destroy.<BR>—3 To drive or beat off, ward off; आलोलपत्राभिहतद्विरेफम् (अरविन्दम्) R. 6. 13.<BR>—4 To strike or beat (as a drum &c.). ततः शङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च पणवानकगोमुखाः ।<BR> सहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त Bg. 1. 13.<BR>—5 To befall, attack; affect, overpower; Dk. 6. ━<i>Caus.</i> To strike &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहत
अभिहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck (fig. also), beaten, smitten, attacked, injured; अज्मनाभिहतः<BR> शयाम् Av. 11. 10. 22; धाराभिरातप इवाभिहतं सरोजम् M. 5. 3; Amaru. 2;<BR> struck against (as sound); Śik. 9.<BR>—2 Struck, affected, overcome; शोक˚, काम˚, दुःख˚, क्षुत्तृषा˚.<BR>—3 Obstructed.<BR>—4 (In math.) Multiplied; अन्योन्यहाराभिहतौ हरांशौ Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहतिः|अभिहति
अभिहतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Striking, beating, hurting &c.<BR>—2 (In Math.) Multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातः|अभिघात
अभिघातः<BR>—1 Striking, (fig. also); beating, smiting, attack, injury, hurt; तटाभिघातादिव<BR> लग्नपङ्के Ku. 7. 49; शीतातपाभिघातान् Ms. 12. 77 attacks of heat<BR> and cold; so दुःख˚, शोक˚ &c.<BR>—2 (In Vaiśeṣika Phil.) Striking against (such as gives rise to sounds<BR> &c.), regarded as a kind of संयोग.<BR>—3 Striking back, driving or warding off.<BR>—4 Extirpation, complete destruction or removal; दुःखत्रयाभिघाताज्जिज्ञासा<BR> तदभिघातके हेतौ Sāṅ. K. 1.<BR>—5 Abrupt or vehement articulation of words (as of Vedic texts); sudden shock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातम्
अभिघातः + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The combination of the 4th letter of any class with the first or third<BR> letter of that class; of the second with the first; and of the third with<BR> the second letter of any class; अभिघातं स्यात्पूर्वं वेदद्वित्र्यादिवर्णाश्चेत् ।<BR> नववर्गाणां नवतो धरणीचन्द्रद्विरामाद्याः Śabdak.<BR>—2 A harsh pronunciation caused by the neglect of <i>Sandhi</i> rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातक|अभिघातकः
अभिघातक <i>a.</i> Striking; keeping or beating back, repelling, extirpating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातकः|अभिघातक
अभिघातक + .{@-कः@} An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0189-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातिन्
अभिघातिन् Striking, hurting. ━<i>m.</i> An enemy; assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहवः|अभिहव
अभिहवः [ह्वे-अप्]<BR>—1 Invocation, calling.<BR>—2 Sacrificing fully or completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहूतिः|अभिहूति
अभिहूतिः <i>f.</i> Calling, invocation; worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहस्य
अभिहस्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहासः|अभिहास
अभिहासः Jest, joke, mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित, -ति<BR> See under अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहिति|अभिहितिः
अभिहित, -ति<BR> See under अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहु
अभिहु €3 P. To make an oblation, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहवः|अभिहव
अभिहवः An oblation, a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहोमः|अभिहोम
अभिहोमः Offering an oblation of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहृ
अभिहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To carry or bear off, snatch away, remove, take away.<BR>—2 To tear off, pull down.<BR>—3 To bring; bring near.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to take away.<BR>—2 To bring on the table, serve up in dishes &c. (as food).<BR>—3 To lay or put on (as a coat).<BR>—4 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरः|अभिहर
अभिहरः Carrying off, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरणम्
अभिहरणम्<BR>—1 Bringing near, fetching; व्यादिदेश गणशोऽथ पार्श्वगान् कार्मुकाभिहरणाय<BR> मैथिलः R. 11. 43.<BR>—2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहर्तृ
अभिहर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who takes away, bears off, or takes by violence.<BR>—2 A ravisher, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहारः|अभिहार
अभिहारः<BR>—1 Carrying away, robbing, stealing.<BR>—2 An attack, assault.<BR>—3 Arming oneself, taking up arms.<BR>—4 Mingling together, mixture.<BR>—5 An effort.<BR>—6 A drunkard; drinker of smoking drinks.<BR>—7 Bringing near; तस्याभिहारं कुर्याच्च Mb. 12. 69. 37. cf. अभिहारोऽभियोगे<BR> च चौर्ये संनहनेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुत्
अभिह्रुत्^1 <i>a.</i> Ved. Bending, causing crookedness, acting injuriously.<BR>━<i>f.</i> Fall; defeat, loss.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुति|अभिह्रुतिः
अभिह्रुति <i>a.</i> Offensive, injurious; acting crookedly;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुतिः|अभिह्रुति
अभिह्रुति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Causing to fall.<BR>—2 Defeat; loss;<BR>—3 Offence, injury; शतभुजिभिस्तमभिह्रुतेरघात् Rv. 1. 166. 8; Av. 6. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वर|अभिह्वरः
अभिह्वर, -ह्वार <i>a.</i><BR> Falling off, crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वार
अभिह्वर, -ह्वार <i>a.</i><BR> Falling off, crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वरः|अभिह्वर
अभिह्वर, -ह्वार + .{@-रः@} Crookedness, sin; नाभिह्वारे पदं निदधाति Av. 6. 76. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी [अभि -इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To approach, come or draw near, go up to (with acc.) अस्मानत्तुमितोऽभ्येति<BR> Bk. 7. 84; Ki. 2. 54.<BR>—2 To go along or after, follow, serve.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go into, enter; Bk. 5. 67; अवाङ्नरकमभ्येति Ms. 8. 75.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To go over to, reach, arrive at; Me. 36 v. l.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) To fall to oneʼs share, come to; नाऽविविदिषुमभ्येति सम्पद्<BR> रुरुदिषुं नरम् Bk. 7. 99.<BR>—4 To get, meet with, fall into, suffer, undergo (said of good or bad<BR> things); कार्यं संसिद्धिमभ्येति Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीतिः|अभीति
अभीतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Approach, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत्वन्
अभीत्वन् <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>), अभीत्वर <i>a.</i><BR> Approaching, attacking, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत्वरी
अभीत्वन् <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>), अभीत्वर <i>a.</i><BR> Approaching, attacking, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत्वर
अभीत्वन् <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>), अभीत्वर <i>a.</i><BR> Approaching, attacking, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ययः|अभ्यय
अभ्ययः<BR>—1 Going over, approach, arrival.<BR>—2 Entering.<BR>—3 Setting (of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी <i>a.</i> Without fear; व्याघ्रानभीरभिमुखोत्पतितान् R. 9. 63, 15. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक <i>a.</i> [For ety. see अभिक]<BR>—1 Longing after, desirous, anxious.<BR>—2 Lustful, libidinous, voluptuous; मेदस्विनः सरभसोपगतानभीकान् Śi. 5. 64.<BR>—3 Fearless.<BR>—4 Gone to (अभिगत).<BR>—5 Dreadful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीकः|अभीक
अभीक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A lover, husband.<BR>—2 A poet.<BR>—3 A master. cf. … अथ क्रूरे च कामुके । भयहीने कवौ पुंस्यादभीकः<BR> प्रोच्यते ततः ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीकम्
अभीक + .{@-कम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 Proximity, nearness. —2 Collision; combat, encounter, opposition; प्रावन्मनुं<BR> दस्यवे करभीकम् Rv. 9. 92. 5. [The form अभीके frequently occurs<BR> in the Vedas in the sense of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) near;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) at the same time or place, at the right time, just in time;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) in a moment, instantaneously, or (used like a preposition with abl.),<BR>——(<i>d</i>) from, out of;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) on account of, with regard to;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) from.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्ण|अभीक्ष्णं
अभीक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> [अभिगतः क्षणं पृषो˚; अभीक्ष्णम् अभिक्षणं भवति<BR> तद्धि क्षणमाभिमुख्येन स्थितं भवति Nir.] Repeated, frequent.<BR>—2 Constant, perpetual.<BR>—3 Excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्णम्
अभीक्ष्ण + .{@-क्ष्णम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Frequently, repeatedly; क्षते प्रहारा निपतन्त्यभीक्ष्णम् Pt. 2. 186.<BR>—2 Constantly,<BR>—3 Very much, exceedingly.<BR>—4 Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्णशः
अभीक्ष्णशः <i>ind.</i> Repeatedly; वृजिनं नार्हति प्राप्तुं पूज्यं<BR> वन्द्यमभीक्ष्णशः Bhāg. 1. 7. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीघात
अभीघात = अभिघात q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीज्य|अभीज्यः
अभीज्य <i>a.</i> [fr. यज्] To be sacrificed to; one to whom a sacrifice is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीज्यः|अभीज्य
अभीज्य + .{@-ज्यः@} A God; नानाभिधाभीज्यगणोपपन्नः Bhāg. 2. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अभीत, -ति <i>a.</i><BR> Not afraid, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीति|अभीतिः
अभीत, -ति <i>a.</i><BR> Not afraid, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीतिः|अभीति
अभीत, -ति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Fearlessness.<BR>—2 Approach, attack, assault; विश्वा अभीतीरपसो युयोधि Rv. 2. 33. 3.<BR>—3 Nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीद्ध
अभीद्ध [इन्ध-क्त] Inflamed, shining; ऋतं च सत्यं चाभीद्धात्<BR> तपसोऽध्यजायत Mahānār. Up. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीपत्
अभीपत् <i>m.</i> [अभि-पत्-क्विप् दीर्घः] One who goes or resorts to<BR> (अभिगमनवान् Sāy.), a pond or any spot in which water collects; a favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सित|अभीप्सितं
अभीप्सित <i>a.</i> Desired, wished; अभीप्सितार्थसिद्ध्यर्थं पूजितो<BR> यः सुरासुरैः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सितम्
अभीप्सित + .{@-तम्@} A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सिन्
अभीप्सिन्, अभीप्सु <i>a.</i> Wishing for, desirous of obtaining; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सु
अभीप्सिन्, अभीप्सु <i>a.</i> Wishing for, desirous of obtaining; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीम|अभीमः
अभीम <i>a.</i> Not causing fear, not terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमः|अभीम
अभीम + .{@-मः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान = अभिमान q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमोदः|अभीमोद
अभीमोदः Joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुद्
अभीमोदः + .{@-मुद्@} Ved. great joy, or <i>a.</i> excessively delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरः|अभीर
अभीरः [अभिमुखीकृत्य ईरयति गाः, ईर्-अच्]<BR>—1 A cowherd<BR>—2 N. of a pastoral people; more usually written<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">Page0191-1</a>]<BR> आभीर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरी
अभीरः + .{@-री@} The language of the अभीर people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरम्
अभीरः + .{@-रम्@} N. of a metre, see आभीर.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभीरपल्ली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0190-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरपल्ली
अभीरः + -पल्ली a hamlet of cowherds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरणी
अभीरणी A kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीराजी
अभीराजी N. of a poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु <i>a.</i> (-रुः, -रू <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fearless.<BR>—2 Unterrific, harmless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुः|अभीरु
अभीरु + .{@-रुः@}<BR>—1 N. of Śiva or Bhairava.<BR>—2 Name of a prince in the Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुः|अभीरु
अभीरु + .{@-रुः@} <i>f.</i>, अभीरुपत्री<BR> N. of a plant (Mar. शतावरी) Asparagus Racemosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु + .{@-रु@} <i>n.</i> A place of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुण
अभीरुण <i>a.</i> Fearless, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुणम्
अभीरुण + .{@-णम्@} <i>ind.</i> Before or in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलम्
अभीलम्<BR>—1 A difficulty, distress.<BR>—2 A dreadful scene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलु
अभीलु, -लुक<BR> = अभीरु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलुक
अभीलु, -लुक<BR> = अभीरु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलापः|अभीलाप
अभीलापः [लप् घञ्-दीर्घः] Discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलापलप्
अभीलापलप् <i>a.</i> (Frequentative, irr. Intensive) Excessively whimpering.<BR> आलापाश्च प्रलापाश्चाभीलापलपश्च ये Av. 11. 8. 25<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्गः|अभीवर्ग
अभीवर्गः Circuit, compass; अहं राष्ट्रस्याभीवर्गे निजो भूयासमुत्तमः Av. 3. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्तः|अभीवर्त|अभीवर्त्त
अभीवर्तः [वृत्-करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 N. of a Sāman, <i>Brahma Sāman</i><BR>—2 N. of a hymn (Rv. 10. 174) recited in attacking the enemy.<BR>—3 A year.<BR>—4 A sort of oblation. (B. and R. take this word to mean ‘existing everywhere’,<BR> ‘attacking successfully’, ‘successful attack or victory’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत्
अभीवृत् <i>a.</i> Existing everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत
अभीवृत <i>a.</i> Covered, surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशापः|अभीशाप
अभीशापः A curse; see अभिशाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशुः|अभीशु
अभीशुः, -षुः<BR> [अभि-अश्-उन्, पृषो˚ अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 A rein, bridle; यैर्गुप्तान्यकुतोभयानि भुवनान्यासन्महाभीशवः Mv. 5. 23;<BR> तेन हि मुच्यन्तामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 A ray of light; प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः Śi. 1. 22; ˚मत्<BR> resplendent, splendid. cf. अभीशुः प्रग्रहरशिमनोः । Nm. ‘अभीशुः प्रग्रहे रश्मौ’ इति शाश्वतः ।<BR>—3 An arm (अभ्यश्नुते कर्माणि Nir.).<BR>—4 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषुः|अभीषु
अभीशुः, -षुः<BR> [अभि-अश्-उन्, पृषो˚ अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 A rein, bridle; यैर्गुप्तान्यकुतोभयानि भुवनान्यासन्महाभीशवः Mv. 5. 23;<BR> तेन हि मुच्यन्तामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 A ray of light; प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः Śi. 1. 22; ˚मत्<BR> resplendent, splendid. cf. अभीशुः प्रग्रहरशिमनोः । Nm. ‘अभीशुः प्रग्रहे रश्मौ’ इति शाश्वतः ।<BR>—3 An arm (अभ्यश्नुते कर्माणि Nir.).<BR>—4 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्
अभीष् €6 P. To wish or desire for, seek for, strive to get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Wished, desired.<BR>—2 Dear, favourite, darling; अनभीष्टदम्पत्योः Pt. 1. 174; oft. with<BR> gen. of person; H. 1. 12.<BR>—3 Optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टः|अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं
अभीष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} A darling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टा
अभीष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@}<BR>—1 A mistress, beloved woman.<BR>—2 Betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टम्
अभीष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 An object of desire.<BR>—2 A desirable object (अभिमत); अन्यस्मै हृदयं देहि नानभीष्टे<BR> घटामहे Bk. 20. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभीष्टदेवता, अभीष्टलाभः, अभीष्टसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टदेवता
अभीष्ट + -देवता favourite deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टलाभः|अभीष्टलाभ
अभीष्ट + -लाभः, -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> gaining a desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टसिद्धिः|अभीष्टसिद्धि
अभीष्ट + -लाभः, -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> gaining a desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषङ्ग|अभीषंग|अभीषङ्गः
अभीषङ्ग = अभिषङ्ग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषया
अभीषया <i>adv.</i> Fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषह्
अभीषह्^1 <i>a.</i> Overpowering; guaranteeing safety from enemies (परेभ्योऽभयदाता;<BR> अभीषहमाणः सपत्नान्, अभिभवति शत्रून् Nir.). ━<i>f.</i> (ट्) Great power.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uneaten, unenjoyed, unused; अभुक्तायां यस्यां क्षणमपि न यातं नृपशतैः Bh. 3. 25.<BR>—2 (Actively used) One who has not eaten, enjoyed, used &c.; cf. पीत.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभुक्तमूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्तमूलम्
अभुक्त + -मूलम् the interval between the closing part of Jyeṣṭhā and<BR> the beginging of Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज्
अभुज् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 One who has not experienced or enjoyed न म आशृणोः किमभुग्वदासि<BR> Rv. 10. 95. 11.<BR>—2 one who does not keep a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुञ्जत्|अभुंजत्|अभुञ्जन्त्
अभुञ्जत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not eating.<BR>—2 Not allowing to enjoy, stingy; अध स्वप्नस्य निर्विदेऽभुञ्जतश्च रेवतः<BR> Rv. 1. 120. 12.<BR>—3 Not protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not bent or crooked, straight,<BR>—2 Well, free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज
अभुज <i>a.</i> Armless, maimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुजिष्या
अभुजिष्या Not a slave or servant, an independent woman; एष स जन<BR> एतामिच्छत्यभुजिष्यां कर्तुम् Mk. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूः
अभूः ‘Unborn’, N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अभूत <i>a.</i> Non-existent, what is not or has not been; not true<BR> or real, false; स्तुवन्ति श्रान्तास्याः क्षितिपतिमभूतैरपि गुणैः Mu. 3. 16,<BR> Ki. 14. 19; Rām. 5. 14. 34.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभूताहरणम्, अभूततद्भावः, अभूतपूर्व, अभूतप्रादुर्भावः, अभूतशत्रु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूताहरणम्
अभूत + -आहरणम् ‘utterance of an unreality’, a covert expression, a<BR> speech founded on fraud, one of the members of <i>garbha</i> S. D. 365.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूततद्भावः|अभूततद्भाव
अभूत + -तद्भावः the becoming or being changed into, or making, that<BR> which it is not before; कृभ्वस्तियोगे संपद्येकर्तरि च्विः P. V. 4. 50;<BR> अभूततद्भावे इति वक्तव्यम्; अकृष्णः कृष्णः संपद्यते तं करोति<BR> कृष्णीकरोति Sk.; cf. पयोधरीभूतचतुःसमुद्राम् R. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतपूर्व
अभूत + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> unprecedented, unsurpassed; अभूत् ˚र्वो राजा चिन्तामणिर्नाम<BR> Vās. 1, कुतोऽद्यसमरोदधेरयमभूतपूर्वः पुरः Ve. 3. 2; Śi. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतप्रादुर्भावः|अभूतप्रादुर्भाव
अभूत + -प्रादुर्भावः becoming manifest of what has not been before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतशत्रु
अभूत + -शत्रु <i>a.</i> having no enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतिः|अभूति
अभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-existence, non-entity.<BR>—2 Want of power.<BR>—3 Poverty.<BR>—4 Destruction; कालोऽयं दारुणः प्राप्तो भरतानामभूतये Mb. 3. 29. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमिः|अभूमि
अभूमिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-earth, anything but earth,<BR>—2 An unfit place or object, no proper object for, beyond the reach or<BR> scope of; अभूमिरियं मालविकायाः M. 3; अभूमिरियमविनयस्य Ś. 7;<BR> स खलु मनोरथानामप्यभूमिर्विसर्जनावसरसत्कारः <i>ibid.</i><BR> far exceeded or transcended my (highest) expectations; Śi. 1. 42; Śānti. 4. 22.<BR> K. 45, 196, 204.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभूमिज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमिज
अभूमिः + -ज<BR>—1 produced in a bad or improper place.<BR>—2 not produced in earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयःसंनिवृत्तिः
अभयःसंनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> No return any more i. e. absolution; त्वय्यावेशितचित्तानां<BR> त्वत्समर्पितकर्मणाम् । गतिस्त्वं वीतरागाणामभूयःसंनिवृत्तये ॥ R. 10. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूरि
अभूरि <i>a.</i> few, some; several; so, अभूमन्, अभूयिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत
अभृत, अभृत्रिम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not hired or paid; कर्म कारयितुं चैव भृतानप्यभृतांस्तथा Mb. 5. 165. 8.<BR> सा स्यात्पालेऽभृते भृतिः Ms. 8. 231.<BR>—2 Not supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत्रिम
अभृत, अभृत्रिम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not hired or paid; कर्म कारयितुं चैव भृतानप्यभृतांस्तथा Mb. 5. 165. 8.<BR> सा स्यात्पालेऽभृते भृतिः Ms. 8. 231.<BR>—2 Not supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृश|अभृशं
अभृश <i>a.</i> Not much, little, few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undivided.<BR>—2 Identical, same, alike; तयोरभेदप्रतिपत्तिरस्ति मे Bh. 3, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेदः|अभेद
अभेद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Absence of difference or distinction, identity, sameness;<BR>—2 unity, oneness; भेदाभेदयोर्भेदो ग्रहीतव्यः । ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 3.<BR> तद्रूपकमभेदो य उपमानोपमेययोः K. P. 10; Śi. 13. 25.<BR>—3 Close union; इच्छतां सह वधूभिरभेदम् Ki. 9. 13. अभेदेन च<BR> युध्येत रक्षेच्चैव परस्परम् H. 3. 72; आशास्महे विग्रहयोरभेदम् Bh. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अभेद्य, अभैदिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be divided, broken or pierced through, impenetrable.<BR>—2 Indivisible<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभैदिक
अभेद्य, अभैदिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be divided, broken or pierced through, impenetrable.<BR>—2 Indivisible<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्यम्
अभेद्य, अभैदिक + .{@-द्यम्@} A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तृ
अभोक्तृ, ˚भोगिन् <i>a.</i> Not using or enjoying, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोगिन्
अभोक्तृ, ˚भोगिन् <i>a.</i> Not using or enjoying, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोगः|अभोग
अभोगः Non-enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्
अभोज् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not sacrificing; not giving food to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजनम्
अभोजनम् Not eating, fasting, abstinence; त्रिरात्रं स्यादभोजनम्<BR> Ms. 11. 166, 203, 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजिन्
अभोजिन् <i>a.</i> Not eating, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य <i>a.</i> Not to be eaten, prohibited as food, impure, unholy;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य + .{@˚अन्न@} <i>a.</i> one whose food is prohibited from being eaten by<BR> others; य एतेऽन्ये त्वभोज्यान्नाः क्रमशः परिकीर्तिताः Ms. 4. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभौतिक
अभौतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Not material, not elemental,<BR> not produced by the gross elements; mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभौम
अभौम = अभूमिज q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्र|अभ्यग्रं
अभ्यग्र <i>a.</i> [अभिमुखम् अग्रं यस्य]<BR>—1 Near, proximate; अभ्यग्रं च प्रपश्यन्ति युद्धमानन्दिनो द्विजाः Mb. 6. 2. 18.<BR>—2 Fresh, new;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्रम्
अभ्यग्र + .{@-ग्रम्@} proximity; vicinity. It is used adverbially also in इदं<BR> शोणितमभ्यग्रं संप्रहारेऽच्युतत् तयोः Bk. 4. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यङ्क|अभ्यंक
अभ्यङ्क <i>a.</i> Recently marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यञ्ज्|अभ्यंज्
अभ्यञ्ज् €7 P.<BR>—1 To smear, anoint as with oily substances.<BR>—2 To decorate, adorn (Ved.).<BR>—3 To defile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यक्त
अभ्यक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Smeared, anointed (with oil, perfumes &c.); अभ्यक्तमिव स्नातः<BR> Ś. 5. 11; Y. 1. 68; Ms. 4. 44.<BR>—2 Decorated; अभ्यक्ताक्ता स्वरंकृता Av. 10. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यङ्गः|अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंग|अभ्यंगः
अभ्यङ्गः<BR>—1 Smearing the body with unctuous or oily substances, smearing with oil;<BR> अभ्यङ्गने पथ्यमलंचकार Ku. 7. 7; स्तन्यदानाभ्यङ्गपोषणादिभिः<BR> पुपोष Pt. 5; Ms. 2. 178.<BR>—2 Smearing in general, inunction.<BR>—3 An unguent, salve, liniment.<BR>—4 cream of milk; (Nigh.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यञ्जनम्
अभ्यञ्जनम्<BR>—1 Smearing the body with oily substances, inunction; भोजनाभ्यञ्जनाद्दानाद्यदन्यत्कुरुते<BR> तिलैः Ms. 10. 91.<BR>—2 Smearing or anointing in general.<BR>—3 Applying collyrium to the eyelashes; Ms. 2. 211. (here the 1 & 2 meaning<BR> can be applicable).<BR>—4 An oily substance; oil, unguent^1.<BR>—5 An ornament, decoration (Ved.).<BR>—6 Cream of milk; (Nigh.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यतीत
अभ्यतीत <i>p. p.</i> Dead, passed away; गुरुषु त्वभ्यतीतेषु Ms. 4. 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक <i>a.</i> —1 More than, exceeding, beyond; सद्यःप्रसूताप्रियापीतादभ्यधिकम् U. 4. 1.<BR> remaining after &c. Pt.<BR>—2 Surpassing, more than in quality or quantity, higher, greater; एष<BR> चाभ्यधिकोऽस्माकं गुणः Rām.; न त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यः<BR> Bg. 11. 43; M. 3. 3; Ms. 7. 177; Y. 2. 295; sometimes with abl. or instr.;<BR> धान्यं दशभ्यः कुम्भेभ्यो हरतोऽभ्यधिकं वधः Ms. 8. 320, 322; Y. 2. 27.<BR> प्रभुः क्षमावान् वीरश्च दाता चाभ्यधिको नृपैः Nala. 21. 13.<BR>—3 More than ordinary, extraordinary, pre-eminent; कृष्णाङ्घ्रिरेण्वभ्यधिकाभ्यनेत्री<BR> Bhāg. 1. 19. 6. पञ्चाभ्यधिकः शरोभव Ś. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिकम्
अभ्यधिक + .{@-कम्@} <i>adv.</i> Very much, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यध्वम्
अभ्यध्वम् <i>adv.</i> Towards the way, on the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यध्वे
अभ्यध्वम् + .{@-ध्वे@} Near the way; ययोरभ्यध्व उत यद् दूरे Av. 4. 28. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To permit, assent or agree to, approve; अतोऽभ्यनुजानातु भवती K. 209; M. 3;<BR>—2 To permit one to go, grant leave to, dismiss. ━<i>Caus.</i> To ask<BR> for leave, to depart, take leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा, -ज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Consent, approval, permission. कृताभ्यनुज्ञा गुरुणा गरीयसा Ku. 5. 7,<BR> R. 2. 69.<BR>—2 Order, command.<BR>—3 Granting leave of absence, dismissing.<BR>—4 Admission of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञानम्
अभ्यनुज्ञा, -ज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Consent, approval, permission. कृताभ्यनुज्ञा गुरुणा गरीयसा Ku. 5. 7,<BR> R. 2. 69.<BR>—2 Order, command.<BR>—3 Granting leave of absence, dismissing.<BR>—4 Admission of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञात
अभ्यनुज्ञात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Assented, approved; हृदयेनाभ्यनुज्ञातो यो धर्मस्तं निबोधत Ms. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Favoured by; Rām. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनूक्त
अभ्यनूक्त <i>a.</i> Said agreeably to what was said before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर <i>a.</i> [अभिगतमन्तरम्]<BR>—1 interior, internal, inner (opp. बाह्य); R. 17. 45; K. 66; कृच्छ्रोऽभ्यन्तरशोणिते Y. 3. 292.<BR>—2 Being included in, one of a group or body; देवीपरिजनाभ्यन्तरः<BR> M. 5; गणाभ्यन्तर एव च Ms. 3. 154; R. 8. 95<BR>—3 Initiated in, skilled or proficient in, familiar or conversant with;<BR> with loc., or sometimes gen., or in comp.; संगीतकेऽभ्यन्तरे स्वः<BR> M. 5. अहो प्रयोगाभ्यन्तरः प्राश्निकः M. 2; अनभ्यन्तरे आवां मदनगतस्य<BR> वृत्तान्तस्य Ś. 3; मन्त्रेष्वभ्यन्तराः के स्युः Rām., see अभ्यन्तरीकृ below.<BR>—4 Nearest, intimate, closely or intimately related; त्यक्ताश्चाभ्यन्तरा<BR> येन Pt. 1. 259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरम्
अभ्यन्तर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The inside or interior, inner or interior part of anything, space<BR> within; प्रविश्याभ्यन्तरं रिपुः (नाशयेत्) Pt. 2. 38; K. 15, 17, 18;<BR> ˚गतः आत्मा M. 5 inmost soul; शमीमिवाभ्यन्तरलीनपावकां<BR> R. 3. 9; Bg. 5. 27; V. 2; Mk. 1. पर्णाभ्यन्तरलीनतां विजहति Ś. 7. 8.<BR>—2 Included space, interval (of time or place); षण्मासाभ्यन्तरे Pt. 4<BR>—3 The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरम्
अभ्यन्तर + .{@-रम्, -रतः@} <i>adv.</i> In the interior, inside, inward.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">Page0193-1</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्यन्तरायामः, अभ्यन्तराराम, अभ्यन्तरकरण, अभ्यन्तरकला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरतः
अभ्यन्तर + .{@-रम्, -रतः@} <i>adv.</i> In the interior, inside, inward.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">Page0193-1</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्यन्तरायामः, अभ्यन्तराराम, अभ्यन्तरकरण, अभ्यन्तरकला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरायामः|अभ्यन्तरायाम
अभ्यन्तर + -आयामः<BR>—1 curvature of the spine by spasm.<BR>—2 emprosthonos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तराराम
अभ्यन्तर + -आराम <i>a.</i> Internally delighted; see अन्तराराम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरकरण
अभ्यन्तर + -करण <i>a.</i> having the organs (concealed) inside, internally<BR> possessed of the powers of perception &c.; ˚णया मया प्रत्यक्षीकृतवृत्तान्तो<BR> महाराजः V. 4<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरकरणम्
अभ्यन्तर + -करण + .({@-णम्@}) the internal organ <i>i. e.</i> अन्तःकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरकला
अभ्यन्तर + -कला the secret art, the art of coquetry or flirtation; Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरकः|अभ्यन्तरक|अभ्यंतरकः
अभ्यन्तरकः An intimate friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरीकृ|अभ्यंतरीकृ
अभ्यन्तरीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To initiate, familiarize with; प्रागल्भ्याद्वक्तुमिच्छन्ति^1 मन्त्रेष्वभ्यन्तरीकृताः Rām.<BR>—2 To admit or introduce to; सर्वविश्रम्भेषु अभ्यन्तरीकरणीया K. 101;<BR> Dk. 159, 162; मुष्टिमर्धमुष्टिं वाभ्यन्तरीकृत्य Dk. 156 throwing<BR> down into (the belly);<BR>—3 To make a near friend of (a person) बाह्याश्चाभ्यन्तरीकृताः Pt. 1. 259.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरीकरणम्
अभ्यन्तरीकरणम् Initiating, introducting &c.; सजीवनिर्जीवासु<BR> च द्यूतकलास्वभ्यन्तरीकरणम् Dk. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यम्
अभ्यम् €1 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To injure, pain, attack; अनग्नित्रा अभ्यमन्त कृष्टीः Rv. 1. 189. 3.<BR>—2 To overcome.<BR>—3 To be angry with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमनम्
अभ्यमनम्<BR>—1 Attack, assault, injury.<BR>—2 Disease; ˚वत् diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित|अभ्यमितः
अभ्यमित, अभ्यान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Diseased, sick.<BR>—2 Injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्त|अभ्यांत
अभ्यमित, अभ्यान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Diseased, sick.<BR>—2 Injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमिन्
अभ्यमिन् <i>a.</i> [अम्-णिनि P. III. 2. 157]<BR>—1 Attacking, inclined to attack.<BR>—2 Diseased, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रम्
अभ्यमित्रम् An attack on an enemy. <i>adv.</i> Towards or against the<BR> enemy; to face the enemy; समुज्झिता योद्धृभिरभ्यमित्रम् Ki. 16. 5;<BR> Mv. 6; Ve. 5. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीणः|अभ्यमित्रीण
अभ्यमित्रीणः, -यः, -मित्र्यः<BR> [अभ्यमित्र -ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं<BR> सुष्ठु गच्छतीत्यर्थः अभ्यमित्राच्छ च P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior who valiantly<BR> encounters his enemy; उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR> Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीयः|अभ्यमित्रीय
अभ्यमित्रीणः, -यः, -मित्र्यः<BR> [अभ्यमित्र -ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं<BR> सुष्ठु गच्छतीत्यर्थः अभ्यमित्राच्छ च P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior who valiantly<BR> encounters his enemy; उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR> Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्र्यः|अभ्यमित्र्य
अभ्यमित्रीणः, -यः, -मित्र्यः<BR> [अभ्यमित्र -ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं<BR> सुष्ठु गच्छतीत्यर्थः अभ्यमित्राच्छ च P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior who valiantly<BR> encounters his enemy; उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR> Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

