अभ्यवस्कन्द्|अभ्यवस्कंद्
अभ्यवस्कन्द्^1 €1 P. To jump up or upon, attack.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: Missing virama on verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्दः|अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कंदः
अभ्यवस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 Vigorously encountering an enemy, impetuous attack, marching against an enemy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">Page0194-1</a>]<BR>—2 Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>—3 A blow in general.<BR>—4 Overtaking, reaching up to.<BR>—5 A fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्दनम्
अभ्यवस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 Vigorously encountering an enemy, impetuous attack, marching against an enemy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">Page0194-1</a>]<BR>—2 Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>—3 A blow in general.<BR>—4 Overtaking, reaching up to.<BR>—5 A fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृ
अभ्यवहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To throw, fling, cast.<BR>—2 To collect, draw in, procure, obtain.<BR>—3 To use as food or drink, eat; सक्तून् पिब धानाः खादेत्यभ्यवहरति<BR> P. III. 4. 5. Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to throw down (in water).<BR>—2 To cause to take or eat (as food), feed (one with something); शक्नोषि<BR> किमनेन शालिप्रस्थेन संपन्नमन्नमस्मानभ्यवहारयितुम् Dk. 131, 72, 132;<BR> to take or eat (oneself).<BR>—3 To lay or put on (snares &c.).<BR>—4 To attack; get one to oppose another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरणम्
अभ्यवहरणम्<BR>—1 Throwing away or down.<BR>—2 Eating, taking food; throwing down the throat (कण्ठादधोनयनम् Mit.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्यवहार <i>a.</i> Fit to eat; शुचीन्यभ्यवहाराणि मूलानि च फलानि<BR> च Rām. 4. 50. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहारः|अभ्यवहार
अभ्यवहारः<BR>—1 Eating, taking food, eating, drinking &c. Śukra. 3. 30.<BR>—2 Food; जम्भशब्दोऽभ्यवहारार्थवाची Kāśi.; ˚संवादापेक्षी M. 4;<BR> V. 2; Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहारमण्डपः|अभ्यवहारमण्डप
अभ्यवहारः + .{@-मण्डपः@} A dining hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्य|अभ्यवहार्य्य
अभ्यवहार्य <i>pot. p.</i> Fit to eat, eatable; कानि चाभ्यवहार्याणि<BR> तत्र तेषां महात्मनाम् Mb. 3. 160. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्यम्
अभ्यवहार्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Food; सर्वत्रौदरिकस्य अभ्यवहार्यमेव विषयः V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवे
अभ्यवे [˚इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To go down, descend, अवभृथमभ्यवैति Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To perceive, understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवायनम्
अभ्यवायनम् Going down, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यश्
अभ्यश् €5 Ā. (P. also in Ved.) —1 To pervade, reach to, get, gain; to<BR> make oneself master of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यशनम्
अभ्यशनम् Pervading, reaching to, gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश <i>a.</i> Near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याशः|अभ्याश
अभ्याश + .{@-शः@}<BR>—1 Reaching to, pervading.<BR>—2 Proximate neighbourhood, vicinity (also written as अभ्यास q. v.);<BR> वायसाभ्याशे समुपविष्टः Pt. 2; सहसाभ्यागतां भैमीमभ्याशपरिवर्तिनीम् Mb.; Dk. 62.<BR>—3 Result, consequence.<BR>—4 Prospect, hope of gaining; hence oft. used in the sense of ‘quickly’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्
अभ्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To practise, exercise; धन्यो वन्यमतङ्गजः परिचयप्रागल्भ्यमभ्यस्यति<BR> Māl. 9. 32; अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारम् R. 13. 67; Ms. 11. 106.<BR>—2 To repeat, perform repeatedly; मृगकुलं रोमन्थमभ्यस्यतु Ś. 2. 6;<BR> अभ्यस्यन्ति तटाघातम् Ku. 2. 50; K. 183.<BR>—3 To learn, study, acquire or learn by practice, recite, read; वेदमेव<BR> सदाभ्यस्येत् Ms. 2. 166, 4. 147, 149; Y. 3. 204; K. 79.<BR>—4 To throw down upon, heap one upon another, accumulate, lay on (Ved.).<BR>—5 To throw or fling at, shoot or aim at (as arrows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसनम्
अभ्यसनम्<BR>—1 Repetition, repeated practice or exercise; ब्रह्मध्यानाभ्यसनविधिना<BR> Bh. 3. 41; स्वाध्यायाभ्यसनम् Bg. 17. 15.<BR>—2 Constant study, close application (to anything); (तां) विद्यामभ्यसनेनेव<BR> प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88; अनभ्यसनशीलस्य विद्येव तनुतां गता Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसनीय
अभ्यसनीय, अभ्यस्य <i>a.</i> <i>pot. p.</i> To be repeated, studied;<BR> fit to be studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्य
अभ्यसनीय, अभ्यस्य <i>a.</i> <i>pot. p.</i> To be repeated, studied;<BR> fit to be studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्यस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Repeated, frequently practised, exercised; नयनयोरभ्यस्तमामीलनम्<BR> Amaru. 97; used or accustomed to; अनभ्यस्तरथचर्याः U. 5; not accustomed<BR> to the use of the chariot; ˚गुणा च वाणी Māl. 3. 11.<BR>—2 Learnt, studied; शैशवेऽभ्यस्तविद्यानाम् R. 1. 8; Bh. 3. 89.<BR>—3 (In Math.) Multiplied; अयुतं दशकृत्वोऽभ्यस्तं नियुतमुच्यते Nir.<BR>—4 (In gram.) Reduplicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तम्
अभ्यस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} Reduplicated base of a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासः|अभ्यास
अभ्यासः<BR>—1 Repetition in general; व्याख्याता व्याख्याता इति पदाभ्यासोऽध्यायपरिसमाप्तिं<BR> द्योतयति Ś. B.; T. 4. 28 नाभ्यासकममीक्षते Pt. 1. 151; Ms. 12. 74;<BR> Y. 3. 322. cf. also अन्यायश्च कृतेऽभ्यासः । MS. 10. 3. 26<BR>—2 Repeated practice or exercise, continued practice or use; अविरतश्रमाभ्यासात्<BR> K. 30; Pt. 1. 133; अभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते Bg. 6. 35, 44<BR> by constant practice (to remain pure and unmodified); 12. 12; योग˚<BR> Y. 3. 51 practice of concentration; hence sometimes used for ‘concentration of mind upon one subject’<BR>; ˚निगृहीतेन मनसा R. 10. 23; so शर˚, अस्त्र˚ &c.<BR>—3 Habit, custom, practice; मिथ्योपपदात् कृञोऽभ्यासे P. I. 3. 71; तद्<BR> यथाभ्यासम् अभिधीयताम् U. 1 therefore address me as is your wont; अमङ्गलाभ्यासरतिम्<BR> Ku. 5. 65; Y. 3. 68.<BR>—4 Discipline in arms, exercise, military discipline.<BR>—5 Reciting, study, repeated reading or learning by heart; काव्यज्ञशिक्षयाभ्यासः<BR> K. P. 1; K. 146, 200; Ms. 5. 4; वेद˚ is of 5 kinds:− वेदस्वीकरणं<BR> पूर्वं विचारोऽभ्यसनं जपः । तद्दानं चैव शिष्येभ्यो वेदाभ्यासो हि पञ्चधा ॥ Dakṣa.<BR>—6 vicinity, proximity, neighbourhood (for अभ्याश); चूतयष्टिरिवाभ्यासे<BR> (शे) मधौ परभृतोन्मुखी Ku. 6. 2; (अभ्यासे-शे मधौ must mean<BR> here speaking to ‘Madhu who was <i>near</i> her’ <i>scil.</i> by having manifested<BR> himself before her, which fully preserves the simile of Pārvatī, herself<BR> silent, speaking to her lover who was near her through her friend); अर्पितेयं<BR> तवाभ्यासे सीता पुण्यव्रता वधूः U. 7. 17 given in your charge; Śi. 3. 40;<BR> अभ्यासा(शा)दागतः P. II. 1. 38. Sk. (regarded as an Aluk Compound).<BR>—7 (In gram.) Reduplication.<BR>—8 The first syllable of a reduplicated base, reduplicative syllable;<BR> पूर्वोऽभ्यासः P. VI. 1. 4; अत्र ये द्वे विहिते तयोः पूर्वोऽभ्याससंज्ञः स्यात् Sk.<BR>—9 (In Math.) Multiplication.<BR>—10 (In poetry) Repetition of the last verses or lines (as of a chorus);<BR> chorus, burden of a song.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्यासगत, अभ्यासपरिवर्तिन्, अभ्यासयोगः, अभ्यासलोपः, अभ्यासव्यवायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासगत
अभ्यासः + -गत <i>a.</i> approached, gone near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासपरिवर्तिन्
अभ्यासः + -परिवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> wandering about or near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासयोगः|अभ्यासयोग
अभ्यासः + -योगः abstraction of mind resulting from continuous deep meditation;<BR> अभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनञ्जय Bg. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासलोपः|अभ्यासलोप
अभ्यासः + -लोपः dropping of the reduplicative syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासव्यवायः|अभ्यासव्यवाय
अभ्यासः + -व्यवायः interval caused by the reduplicative syllable; ˚येऽपि<BR> though separated by this syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासिन्
अभ्यासिन् <i>a.</i> Practising, exercising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयति
अभ्यसूयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To be angry with, bear malice against, envy, be jealous of (with acc.); न च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">Page0195-1</a>]<BR> मां योऽभ्यसूयति Bg. 18. 67; प्रहसन्ति स्म तां केचिदभ्यसूयन्ति चापरे Mb.<BR>—2 Not to like, detract from, calumniate; ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति<BR> मे मतम् Bg. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्यसूय <i>a.</i> Angry, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक <i>a.</i> (-यिका)<BR> Jealous, envious; a detractor; calumniator; मामात्मपरदेहेषु<BR> प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः Bg. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूया
अभ्यसूया Envy, jealousy, disfavour, anger; शुकाभ्यसूयाविनिवृत्तये<BR> यः R. 6. 74; रूपेषु वेशेषु च साभ्यसूयाः 7. 2, 2. 9; Me. 41; Ku. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तम्
अभ्यस्तम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 [अस्तमभि] Towards sunset; ˚गम् -इ, -या to go down or set (as<BR> the sun) during or with reference to some act.<BR>—2 Repeated, again and again; अभ्यस्तं भौतिकं पश्यन् Mb. 12. 278. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमयः|अभ्यस्तमय
अभ्यस्तमयः Setting of the sun during or with reference to some act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमित
अभ्यस्तमित <i>a.</i> One on whom the sun has set while asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकर्षः|अभ्याकर्ष
अभ्याकर्षः Striking the breast with the flat of the hand as a sign<BR> of defiance (as by wrestlers &c.). Mb. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकाङ्क्षितम्
अभ्याकाङ्क्षितम्<BR>—1 A false charge, groundless complaint.<BR>—2 A desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकारम्
अभ्याकारम् <i>adv.</i> By drawing to oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकाशम्
अभ्याकाशम्^1 <i>ind.</i> Coverless (निरावरण) अहःसु सततं तिष्ठेदभ्याकाशं<BR> निशां स्वपन् Mb. 12. 35. 38.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याक्रामम्
अभ्याक्रामम् <i>ind.</i> By or in stepping near or mutually, in stepping rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यात
अभ्याख्यात <i>a.</i> Falsely accused, traduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यानम्
अभ्याख्यानम् A false charge; calumny, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम्
अभ्यागम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go near to, draw near, approach; visit; see अभ्यागत below;<BR> to come, arrive (as time).<BR>—2 To come to, fall into, go to any state; चिन्ताभ्यागतः fell to thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Come near, approached, arrived; भो भवानभ्यागतोऽतिथिः Pt. 4; कमादभ्यागतं<BR> द्रव्यम् Y. 2. 119; तस्मिन्नभ्यागते काले Rām.<BR>—2 Come as a guest; सर्वत्राभ्यागतो गुरुः H. 1. 103; श्रोत्रियाय<BR> अभ्यागताय U. 4; Śi. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागतः|अभ्यागत
अभ्यागत + .{@-तः@} A guest, visitor; ˚क्रियया नियोजितः Pt. 2; K. 280; Śi. 3. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमः|अभ्यागम
अभ्यागमः<BR>—1 Coming or going near, arrival; a visit; तपोधनाभ्यागमसंभवा मुदः<BR> Śi. 1. 23; किं वा मदभ्यागमकारणं ते R. 16. 8; Mv. 2. 22 (v. l.)<BR> वसन्तमास˚ K. 308.<BR>—2 Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR>—3 Arriving at or enjoying a result.<BR>—4 Rising, getting up.<BR>—5 Striking, killing.<BR>—6 Encountering, attacking.<BR>—7 War, battle.<BR>—8 Enmity, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमनम्
अभ्यागमनम् Approach, arrival, visit; हेतुं तदभ्यागमने परीप्सुः Ki. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिकः|अभ्यागारिक
अभ्यागारिकः [अभ्यागारे तत्संबन्धिकर्मणि व्यापृतः ठन्] One who<BR> is diligent in supporting a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघातः|अभ्याघात
अभ्याघातः<BR>—1 An attack, assault, striking.<BR>—2 Persuading to steal; अभ्याघातेषु मध्यस्थान् शिष्याच्चौरानिव द्रुतम् Ms. 9. 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघातिन्
अभ्याघातिन् <i>a.</i> Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याचक्ष्
अभ्याचक्ष्<BR>—1 To look at.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याचर्
अभ्याचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To approach. विशो अदेवीरभ्याचरन्ती Rv. 8. 96. 15.<BR>—2 To use, practise, perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याचारः|अभ्याचार
अभ्याचारः Ved. Approaching (as an enemy); disturbing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याज्ञायः|अभ्याज्ञाय
अभ्याज्ञायः Ved. [ज्ञा-घ]<BR>—1 Recognition.<BR>—2 Order, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यातन्
अभ्यातन् €8 U. To take aim at, shoot or hurl (missiles) against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यातानः|अभ्यातान
अभ्यातानः Spreading over, stretching, expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यात्म
अभ्यात्म <i>a.</i> Directed towards oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यात्मम्
अभ्यात्म + .{@-त्मम्@} <i>adv.</i> Towards oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादा
अभ्यादा €3 Ā.<BR>—1 To take, seize, snatch. न हीनतः परमभ्याददीत Mb. 1. 88. 8.<BR>—2 To put on, wear (garland &c.).<BR>—3 To take up (the conversation), to commence speaking (after another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यात्त
अभ्यात्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obtained, got.<BR>—2 Occupied or pervaded; epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादानम्
अभ्यादानम् Beginning, commencement, first beginning; ओमभ्यादाने<BR> P. VIII. 2. 87 (˚ने = आरम्भे Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याधा
अभ्याधा €3 U. To lay on, add (fuel &c.) to apply, throw under; अभ्यादध्युश्च<BR> काष्ठानि तत्र दह्येत पापकृत् Ms. 8. 372; यथाग्निरभ्याहितं दहति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याधानम्
अभ्याधानम् Laying on, adding (as fuel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहित
अभ्याहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Laid down, put on; यथाद्रैधाग्नेरभ्याहितात्पृथग्धूमा विनिश्चरन्ति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 10. ˚पशुः a sort of gift or present; P. VI. 3. 10. Sk.<BR>—2 Increased, full blown; यथा सौम्य महतोऽभ्याहितस्यैकोऽङ्गारः खद्योतमात्रः<BR> परिशिष्टः स्यात् Ch. Up. 6. 7. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्त|अभ्यांत
अभ्यान्त See under अभ्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यापातः|अभ्यापात
अभ्यापातः A calamity, misfortune, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्दः|अभ्यामर्द|अभ्यामर्द्द
अभ्यामर्दः, -मर्दनम्<BR> War, battle, conflict, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्दनम्
अभ्यामर्दः, -मर्दनम्<BR> War, battle, conflict, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यायम्
अभ्यायम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To stretch, extend, lengthen (sound), draw or pull (as a rudder).<BR>—2 To give.<BR>—3 To aim at.<BR>—4 To restrain.<BR>—5 To approach, visit (= अभ्यागम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यायंसेन्य
अभ्यायंसेन्य <i>a.</i> Ved. One who allows himself to be drawn near<BR> (said of अश्विन् Rv. 1. 34. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारम्
अभ्यारम् <i>adv.</i> Near, at hand; by going near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारुह्
अभ्यारुह् €1 P. —1 To ascend, go up to, reach, get to (mostly Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारूढ
अभ्यारूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ascended, gone up to.<BR>—2 Surpassed, excelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहः|अभ्यारोह
अभ्यारोहः, -रोहणम्<BR>—1 Ascending, mounting, going up to.<BR>—2 Ascending in prayer or devotion, muttering holy prayers; अथातः पवमानानामेवाभ्यारोहः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR>—3 Transition from one place or state to another.<BR>—4 Progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहणम्
अभ्यारोहः, -रोहणम्<BR>—1 Ascending, mounting, going up to.<BR>—2 Ascending in prayer or devotion, muttering holy prayers; अथातः पवमानानामेवाभ्यारोहः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR>—3 Transition from one place or state to another.<BR>—4 Progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहणीयः|अभ्यारोहणीय
अभ्यारोहणीयः N. of a religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्
अभ्यावृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To come up to, approach.<BR>—2 To come again, be repeated. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To come down, approach.<BR>—2 To repeat (as सावित्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्तः|अभ्यावर्त|अभ्यावर्त्त
अभ्यावर्तः<BR>—1 Repetition.<BR>—2 A hymn the verses of which are repeated in singing (आवृत्तिस्तोत्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्तम्
अभ्यावर्तः + .{@-र्तम्@} <i>adv.</i> By repeating, repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्तिन्|अभ्यावर्त्तिन्
अभ्यावर्तिन् <i>a.</i> Recurring; आत्मीयास्ते ये पराञ्चः पुरस्तादभ्यावर्ती<BR> संमुखो यः परोऽसौ Śi. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्त|अभ्यावृत्तः
अभ्यावृत्त <i>p. p.</i> Come near to, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्तः|अभ्यावृत्त
अभ्यावृत्त + .{@-त्तः@} The residue of sacrificial offerings (होमशेषद्रव्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्तिः|अभ्यावृत्ति
अभ्यावृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Repetition, recurrence (so many times); see P. V. 4. 17,<BR> and Sk. thereon; see अनभ्यावृत्ति also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश, -स<BR> see under अभ्यश्-स्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्याश, -स<BR> see under अभ्यश्-स्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासद्
अभ्यासद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To get, obtain, attain; स्वमिव पुरुषकारं शैलमभ्याससाद Ki. 5. 52.<BR>—2 To sit oneself in (acc.). ━<i>Caus.</i> To attack, assail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासादनम्
अभ्यासादनम् Attacking or facing an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहन्
अभ्याहन् €2 P. To strike, smite, wound, injure, kill, destroy; वृक्षस्य<BR> यो मूलेऽभ्याहन्यात् Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहत
अभ्याहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck, beaten.<BR>—2 Affected, smitten; अभ्याहतं कीर्तिविपर्ययेण (हृदयम्) R. 14. 33;<BR> मृत्युना ˚तः &c.<BR>—3 Impeded, obstructed; रक्षोभिरभ्याहतकर्मवृत्तिः Bk. 1. 17.<BR>—4 Faulty, erroneous; अनभ्याहतचित्तः स्यादनभ्याहतवाग्भवेत् Mb. 12. 245. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहननम्
अभ्याहननम्<BR>—1 Striking, hurting, killing.<BR>—2 Impeding, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहृ
अभ्याहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring towards, bring near; to give or hand over; गृहीत्वा<BR> फलमूलं च रामस्याभ्याहरन् बहु Rām. to carry off; पशुरभ्याहृतो<BR> राजन् प्रनष्टस्तव दुर्नयात् Rām. 1. 61. 7.<BR>—2 To rob, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहारः|अभ्याहार
अभ्याहारः<BR>—1 Bringing near or towards, conveying<BR>—2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार्य|अभ्याहार्य्य
अभ्याहार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्त
अभ्युक्त <i>a.</i> Said with reference to some object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्ष्
अभ्युक्ष् €1. €6 U. To sprinkle over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षणम्
अभ्युक्षणम्<BR>—1 Sprinkling over, wetting; परस्पराभ्युक्षणतत्पराणाम् (तासाम्) R. 16. 57.<BR>—2 Consecration by sprinkling; (प्रोक्षण, अभ्युक्षण and अवोक्षण<BR> are thus distinguished; उत्तानेनैव हस्तेन प्रोक्षणं परिकीर्तितम् ।<BR> न्यञ्चताभ्युक्षणं प्रोक्तं तिरश्चावोक्षणं स्मृतम् ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युचित
अभ्युचित^1 <i>a.</i> Usual, customary.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: By alph. order and sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युच्चयः|अभ्युच्चय
अभ्युच्चयः [चि-अच्]<BR>—1 Increase, augmentation, growth.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR>—3 Addition; तथाभ्युच्चयो यदिदमिह भवतीति विज्ञायते अपरमपि भवतीति<BR> विज्ञानम् । ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युच्छ्रित
अभ्युच्छ्रित <i>a.</i> Uplifted, upraised; elevated by, distinguished<BR> for अभ्युच्छ्रिता कर्मभिरप्यवन्ध्यैः R. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रुष्ट
अभ्युत्क्रुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Praised with loud acclamations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रोशनम्
अभ्युत्क्रोशनम् Loud acclamation; ˚मन्त्र a hymn of applause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्था
अभ्युत्था €1 P. To rise for another, rise in honour of, rise to greet;<BR> नाभ्युत्तिष्ठन्ति गुरून् K. 108; Ś. 3; मामियमभ्युत्तिष्ठति देवी<BR> M. 5. 6; Śi. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थानम्
अभ्युत्थानम्<BR>—1 Rising (from a seat) to do honour, rising in honour of; नाभ्युत्थानाक्रिया<BR> यत्र Pt. 2. 62.<BR>—2 Starting, departure, setting out; arrangements for starting; अभ्युत्थानं<BR> त्वमद्यैव कृष्णपक्षचतुर्दशी । कृत्वा निर्याह्यमावास्यां विजयाय बलैर्वृतः ॥<BR> Rām. 6. 92. 62.<BR>—3 Rise (lit. and fig.), elevation, exaltation, prosperity, dignity, a<BR> position of dignity or authority; (तस्य) नवाभ्युत्थानदर्शिन्यो ननन्दुः<BR> सप्रजाः प्रजाः R. 4. 3; यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।<BR> अभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाभ्यहम् Bg. 4. 7 when impiety increases<BR> or is in the ascendant.<BR>—4 Sun-rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थायिन्
अभ्युत्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Rising to greet or in honour of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थित
अभ्युत्थित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Risen, arisen, gone up.<BR>—2 Blazing, flaming (fire); R. 1. 53.<BR>—3 Elevated, exalted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पत्
अभ्युत्पत् €1 P. To fly up to, jump up to, leap upon. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To cause to fly up to (acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पतनम्
अभ्युत्पतनम् Springing or leaping against, sudden spring or leap,<BR> assault; अलक्षिताभ्युत्पतनो नृपेण R. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरणम्
अभ्युदाहरणम् An example or illustration of a thing by its reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदि
अभ्युदि €2 P. [अभि + उद्-इ]<BR>—1 To rise (fig. also); go up (as the sun); एनांस्त्वभ्युदितान्विद्याद् यदा<BR> प्रादुष्कृताग्निषु Ms. 4. 104.<BR>—2 To rise over (one); तं चेदभ्युदियात्सूर्यः शयानं कामचारतः<BR> Ms. 2. 220, 219.<BR>—3 To come into existence, happen, originate.<BR>—4 To engage in combat with (one), encounter, (लोकवीरान्) को जीवितार्थी<BR> समरेऽभ्युदियात् Mb.<BR>—5 To prosper, thrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय <i>a.</i> Rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयः|अभ्युदय
अभ्युदय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Rise (of heavenly bodies); sunrise.<BR>—2 Rise, prosperity, good fortune, elevation, success; स्पृशन्ति नः<BR> स्वामिनमभ्युदयाः Ratn. 1 success; भवो हि लोकाभ्युदयाय तादृशाम्<BR> R. 3. 14; Ms. 3. 254; Bh. 2. 63; R. 12. 3; V. 5.<BR>—3 A festival; any religious or festive celebration, festive occasion;<BR> ˚कालः joyous or festive occasion; Ś. 7; प्रतिषिद्धा पिबेद्या तु<BR> मद्यमभ्युदयेष्वपि Ms. 9. 84.<BR>—4 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—5 Occurrence, happening.<BR>—6 Accomplishment of a desired object (which is the cause of festivity).<BR>—7 The <i>tonsure</i> ceremony.<BR>—8 A Śrāddha performed on account of child-birth (वृद्धिश्राद्धम्)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्युदयार्थकम्, अभ्युदयेष्टिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयार्थकम्
अभ्युदय + -अर्थकम् Śrāddha for prosperity or elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयेष्टिः|अभ्युदयेष्टि
अभ्युदय + -इष्टिः <i>f.</i> N. of a particular expiatory sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयिन्
अभ्युदयिन् <i>a.</i> Rising, going up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
अभ्युदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Risen; occurred.<BR>—2 Elevated, risen to prosperity.<BR>—3 Asleep at sunrise, over whom the sun has risen; सूर्येण ह्यभिनिर्मुक्तः<BR> शयानोऽभ्युदितश्च यः Ms. 2. 221.<BR>—4 Celebrated as a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदिता
अभ्युदित + .{@-ता@} N. of a religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदितम्
अभ्युदित + .{@-तम्@} Rising, sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गम्
अभ्युद्गम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go forth to meet.<BR>—2 To extend, spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्ग
अभ्युद्ग <i>a.</i> Rising, uprisen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गत
अभ्युद्गत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone forth to meet.<BR>—2 Extended, spread; elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गमः|अभ्युद्गम
अभ्युद्गमः, -मनम्, -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going forth to meet or to do honour (to a guest or to a venerable person).<BR>—2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गमनम्
अभ्युद्गमः, -मनम्, -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going forth to meet or to do honour (to a guest or to a venerable person).<BR>—2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गतिः|अभ्युद्गति
अभ्युद्गमः, -मनम्, -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going forth to meet or to do honour (to a guest or to a venerable person).<BR>—2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्दृष्टम्
अभ्युद्दृष्टम् Becoming visible (of a star).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्दृष्टा
अभ्युद्दृष्टम् + .{@-ष्टा@} N. of a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्धृत
अभ्युद्धृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Taken out, taken up; अभ्युद्धृतैर्जलैः Y. 1. 17.<BR>—2 Got without solicitation.<BR>—3 Got after a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यम्
अभ्युद्यम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring, offer.<BR>—2 To lift up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यत
अभ्युद्यत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, lifted up; as ˚आयुध, ˚शस्त्र, ˚कर &c.<BR>—2 Prepared or ready, exerting oneself for (with inf., dat.; loc. or in<BR> comp.); चण्डी चण्डं हन्तुमभ्युद्यता माम् M. 3. 21, प्रहर्तुमभ्युद्यतमात्मयोनिम्<BR> Ku. 3. 70; दिनकररथमार्गविच्छित्तयेऽभ्युद्यतं यच्चलच्छृङ्गम् Bṛ. S. 12. 7;<BR> Me. 59; Ms. 9. 302.<BR>—3 Gone forth, risen, appearing forth or approaching; कुलमभ्युद्यतनूतनेश्वरम् R. 8. 15.<BR>—4 Given or brought unsolicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युन्नत
अभ्युन्नत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Raised, elevated; अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तात् Ś. 3. 7.<BR>—2 Projecting upwards; very high; अभ्युन्नताङ्गुष्ठनखप्रभा Ku. 1, 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युन्नतिः|अभ्युन्नति
अभ्युन्नतिः <i>f.</i> Great elevation or prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम्
अभ्युपगम् €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go to or near, approach; परलोकमभ्युपगते (भर्तरि)<BR> विविशुः Śi. 9. 13.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To come<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">Page0197-2</a>]<BR> to the help of; वयमभ्युपगच्छामः कृष्णेन त्वां प्रधर्षितम् Hariv.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To have recourse to.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To arrive at (a point of time); आषाढीमभ्युपगतो भरतः Rām.<BR>—2 To obtain, get.<BR>—3 To admit, grant, own; अभ्युपगतं तावदस्माभिरेवम् Ś. 5 we admit<BR> all this; Mu. 3.<BR>—4 To assent to, agree to, undertake, promise; Dk. 73. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To induce or cause one to assent to or grant; मामभ्युपगमय्य Dk. 60, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगत|अभ्युपगतः
अभ्युपगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Approached, agreed or assented to; granted; suffered; देव्या मद्वचनात्तथाभ्युपगतः<BR> पत्युर्वियोगस्तदा Ratn. 4. 20; promised &c.<BR>—2 Inferred, probable.<BR>—3 Similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमः|अभ्युपगम
अभ्युपगमः<BR>—1 Approach, arrival.<BR>—2 Granting, admitting, accepting to be true. P. VIII. 3. 74. Sk.; confession<BR> (as of guilt); करिष्याम्येवं नो पुनरिति भवेदभ्युपगमः Ratn. 2. 18.<BR>—3 Undertaking, promising; निर्णय˚ M. 1; a contract, agreement, promise;<BR> क्रियाभ्युपगमात्त्वेतद्बीजार्थंयत्प्रदीयते Ms. 9. 53.<BR>—4 Probable ascertainment, belief; judgment, a view accepted; युष्माकमभ्युपगमाः<BR> प्रमाणं पुण्यपापयोः Mv. 1. 38 supposition, inference.<BR>—5 Analogy, affinity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्युपगमसिद्धान्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमसिद्धान्तः|अभ्युपगमसिद्धान्त
अभ्युपगमः + -सिद्धान्तः an admitted proposition or axiom; Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमित|अभ्युपगमितः
अभ्युपगमित <i>Caus. p. p.</i> Made to consent, obtained by free consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमितः|अभ्युपगमित
अभ्युपगमित + .{@-तः@} A slave for a fixed term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपद्
अभ्युपपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To deliver (from distress), protect; to console, comfort, take compassion<BR> or pity on, pity, favour; स सुहृद्यो विपन्नार्थं दीनमभ्युपपद्यते<BR> Rām. 6. 63. 27; रतिमभ्युपपत्तुमातुरां मधुरात्मानमदर्शयत्पुरः<BR> Ku. 4. 25; (कदा) तपः कृशामभ्युपपत्स्यते सखीं वृषेव सीतां तदवग्रहक्षताम् 5. 61;<BR> U. 2, 3. 7; Māl. 4.<BR>—2 To ask for help, seek protection, submit; अभ्युपपन्नवत्सलः Mk. 7.<BR>—3 To furnish with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्तिः|अभ्युपपत्ति
अभ्युपपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approaching to assist, taking pity or compassion on, favouring; a favour,<BR> kindness; अभ्युपपत्त्या अस्या जीवितमवलम्बस्व Ś. 3; अनयाभ्युपपत्त्या<BR> Ś. 4; मम˚ निमित्तम् Mk. 1.<BR>—2 Consolation.<BR>—3 Protection, defence; ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तौ च शपथे नास्ति पातकम्<BR> Ms. 8. 112, 349, 10. 62; आर्त˚ Dk. 39.<BR>—4 An agreement, assent, promise.<BR>—5 Impregnation of a woman (especially of a brotherʼs widow as an act<BR> of duty); मात्रोरभ्युपपत्तिश्च धर्मोपनिषदं प्रति Mb. 1. 1. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपन्न
अभ्युपपन्न <i>a.</i> Protected, rescued; asked for protection or help;<BR> अभ्युपपन्नवत्सलः खलु तत्रभवानार्यचारुदत्तः श्रूयते Mk. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपादनम्
अभ्युपपादनम् Protection &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपस्थित
अभ्युपस्थित <i>a.</i> Accompanied, assisted; निवासमकरोद्धीमान् सुग्रीवेणाभ्युपस्थितः<BR> Mb. 3. 280. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाकृत
अभ्युपाकृत <i>a.</i> Asked to take part in a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाश्रयः
अभ्युपाश्रयः Shelter, support; कोऽयं कस्य कुतो वापि किं कार्यं<BR> कोऽभ्युपाश्रयः Rām. 5. 48. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपे
अभ्युपे €2 P. [˚उप-इ]<BR>—1 To go near, approach, arrive, enter; व्यतीतकालस्त्वहमभ्युपेतः<BR> R. 5. 14, 16. 22; त्रिरह्नो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">Page0198-1</a>]<BR> ऽभ्युपयन्नपः Ms. 11. 259 entering the water <i>i. e.</i> bathing; Y. 3. 3.<BR>—2 To go to or enter a particular state, attain to; सत्यं न तद्यच्छलमभ्युपैति<BR> H. 3. 54 so ब्राह्मणतां, वैश्यतां, सखित्वम् &c.<BR>—3 To agree, (to do something), accept, promise, undertake; मन्दायन्ते<BR> न खलु सुहृदामभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Me. 40. अस्यै दास्यमभ्युपेतं मया<BR> Dk. 44, 55, 89, 138, 159.<BR>—4 To admit, grant, own, acknowledge, Śi. 11. 67; श्रुत्यैव च तर्कस्याभ्युपेतत्वात्<BR> Ś. B.; Dk. 45.<BR>—5 To approve, agree with, assent to.<BR>—6 To obey, submit to, be faithful to; विरोध्य मोहात्पुनरभ्युपेयुषाम् Ki. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायः|अभ्युपाय
अभ्युपायः<BR>—1 A promise, an engagement, agreement.<BR>—2 A means, an expedient, remedy; अस्मिन्सुराणां विजयाभ्युपाये Ku. 3. 19;<BR> यैरभ्युपायैरेनांसि मानवो व्यपकर्षति Ms. 11. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायनम्
अभ्युपायनम् A complimentary present; inducement, bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत्य
अभ्युपेत्य <i>ind.</i> Having approached; having aggreed or promised.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्युपेत्याशुश्रूषा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत्याशुश्रूषा
अभ्युपेत्य + -अशुश्रूषा one of the 18 titles of Hindu law, breach of contract<BR> or engagement between master and servant (where the servant does not work<BR> having agreed^1 to do so).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषः|अभ्युष
अभ्युषः, अभ्यूषः, अभ्योषः [अभितः उ(ऊ)ष्यते अग्निना दह्यते,<BR> उ(ऊ)ष् बाहु˚ क]<BR>—1 A sort of cake or bread (Mar. पोळी or रोटी) (अर्धस्विन्नयवादेर्घृतादिना<BR> भर्जितयवादेर्वा घृतपक्वान्नस्य ‘पोळी’ इति ख्यातस्य नाम).<BR>—2 Half parched food (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

