अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य, -षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय <i>a.</i> Belonging<BR> to, consisting of, or fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योषीय
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य, -षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय <i>a.</i> Belonging<BR> to, consisting of, or fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषित|अभ्युषितः
अभ्युषित <i>a.</i> [वस्-क्त] Dwelling near or with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषितः|अभ्युषित
अभ्युषित + .{@-तः@} A servant who is in attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूढ
अभ्यूढ <i>a.</i> [वह्-क्त] Brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूह्
अभ्यूह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To cover over, clothe.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To watch for; form a plot against.<BR>—3 To infer, guess.<BR>—4 To reason, argue, think over; Dk. 90.<BR>—5 To supply an ellipsis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूहः|अभ्यूह
अभ्यूहः [ऊह्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Arguing, reasoning, discussion.<BR>—2 Deduction, inference, guess, conjecture; पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि<BR> स्थगयति Māl. 1. 14.<BR>—3 Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>—4 Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येषणम्
अभ्येषणम् [इष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Desiring, wishing.<BR>—2 Going towards, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्
अभ्र् €1 P. [अभ्रति, आनभ्र, अभ्रित] To go, wander about; वनेष्वानभ्र<BR> निर्भयः Bk. 4. 11, 14. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम्
अभ्रम् [अभ्र्-अच्; but more correctly अप्-भृ; अपो बिभर्ति भृ-क;<BR> अभ्रम् अब्भरणात् Nir. being filled with water]<BR>—1 A cloud; अग्निर्वै धूमो जायते धूमादभ्रमभ्राद् वृष्टिः Śat. Br.;<BR> अभ्रं वा अपां भस्म; धूमो भूत्वा अभ्रं भवति अभ्रं भूत्वा मेघो भवति<BR> मेघो भूत्वा प्रवर्षति Ch. Up. 5. 10. 5-6. (these quotations show the<BR> conception of the ancient Ṛṣis about the formation of clouds).<BR>—2 Atmosphere, sky; परितो विपाण्डु दधदभ्रशिरः Śi. 9. 3. See अभ्रंलिह &c.<BR>—3 Talc, mica. (Mar. अभ्रक)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">Page0198-2</a>]<BR>—4 Gold.<BR>—5 Camphor. —6 A kind of reed; Calamus Rotang (वेतस्, वेत्र).<BR>—7 Cyperus Rotundus (मुस्ता). (Mar. नागरमोथा)<BR>—8 (In arith.) A zero or cypher. [cf. L. <i>imbers</i>; Gr. <i>ombros, appros</i>;<BR> Zend. <i>awra</i>, Pers. <i>abr</i>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्रावकाशः, अभ्रावकाशिक, अभ्रावकाशिन्, अभ्रोत्थः, अभ्रकूटम्, अभ्रगङ्गा, अभ्रघनः, अभ्रजा, अभ्रनागः, अभ्रपथः, अभ्रपिशाचः, अभ्रपिशाचकः, अभ्रपुष्पः, अभ्रप्रुष्, अभ्रमांसी, अभ्रमातङ्गः, अभ्रमाला, अभ्रवृन्दम्, अभ्ररोहम्, अभ्रलिप्ती, अभ्रवर्ष, अभ्रवाटिकः, अभ्रवाटिका, अभ्रविलायम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशः|अभ्रावकाश
अभ्रम् + -अवकाशः clouds as the only shelter; fall of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिक
अभ्रम् + -अवकाशिक, -अवकाशिन् <i>a.</i> exposed to the rain (and so practising<BR> penance), not seeking shelter from the rain; अभ्रावकाशा वर्षासु हेमन्ते<BR> जलसंश्रयाः Mb. 12. 244. 10; ग्रीष्मे पञ्चतपास्तु स्याद्वर्षास्वभ्रावकाशिकः Ms. 6. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिन्
अभ्रम् + -अवकाशिक, -अवकाशिन् <i>a.</i> exposed to the rain (and so practising<BR> penance), not seeking shelter from the rain; अभ्रावकाशा वर्षासु हेमन्ते<BR> जलसंश्रयाः Mb. 12. 244. 10; ग्रीष्मे पञ्चतपास्तु स्याद्वर्षास्वभ्रावकाशिकः Ms. 6. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रोत्थः|अभ्रोत्थ|अभ्रोत्थं
अभ्रम् + -उत्थः ‘sky born’, the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रकूटम्
अभ्रम् + -कूटम् a peak of a (mountain-like) cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रगङ्गा
अभ्रम् + -गङ्गा the heavenly river; K. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रघनः|अभ्रघन
अभ्रम् + -घनः a mass of clouds; वर्षात्ययेन रुचमभ्रघनादिवेन्दोः R. 13. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रजा
अभ्रम् + -जा <i>a.</i> Ved. born from clouds, caused by vapours, यो अभ्रजा<BR> वातजा यश्च शुष्मो वनस्पतीन्त्सचतां पर्वतांश्च Av. 1. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रनागः|अभ्रनाग
अभ्रम् + -नागः one of the elephants supporting the globe; N. of Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपथः|अभ्रपथ
अभ्रम् + -पथः<BR>—1 atmosphere.<BR>—2 balloon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाचः|अभ्रपिशाच
अभ्रम् + -पिशाचः, -पिशाचकः ‘sky-demon’, epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाचकः|अभ्रपिशाचक
अभ्रम् + -पिशाचः, -पिशाचकः ‘sky-demon’, epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्पः|अभ्रपुष्प|अभ्रपुष्पं
अभ्रम् + -पुष्पः N. of a cane (Mar. वेत) Calamus Rotang. See अभ्र (6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्पम्
अभ्रम् + -पुष्पः + .({@-ष्पम्@})<BR>—1 water.<BR>—2 ‘a sky flower’, anything impossible, a castle in the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रप्रुष्
अभ्रम् + -प्रुष् (ट्) <i>f.</i> sprinkling of clouds, rain. अभ्रप्रुषो<BR> न वाचा प्रुषा वसु Rv. 10. 77. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमांसी
अभ्रम् + -मांसी N. of a plant (जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमातङ्गः|अभ्रमातङ्ग|अभ्रमातंग
अभ्रम् + -मातङ्गः Indraʼs elephant, Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमाला
अभ्रम् + -माला, -वृन्दम् a line, succession, or mass of clouds; मयूरकेकाभिरिवाभ्रवृन्दम्<BR> R. 7. 69, 13. 76, 16. 25; मुक्ताजालग्रथितमलकं कामिनीवाभ्रवृन्दम् Me. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रवृन्दम्
अभ्रम् + -माला, -वृन्दम् a line, succession, or mass of clouds; मयूरकेकाभिरिवाभ्रवृन्दम्<BR> R. 7. 69, 13. 76, 16. 25; मुक्ताजालग्रथितमलकं कामिनीवाभ्रवृन्दम् Me. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ररोहम्
अभ्रम् + -रोहम् the <i>lapis lazuli</i> (लाजवर्त, आकाशमणि)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रलिप्ती
अभ्रम् + -लिप्ती<BR>—1 sky covered with a few clouds.<BR>—2 a woman smeared with <i>mustā</i> grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रवर्ष|अभ्रवर्षः
अभ्रम् + -वर्ष <i>a.</i> Ved. rained upon, sprinkled with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रवर्षः|अभ्रवर्ष
अभ्रम् + -वर्ष + .({@-र्षः@}) down-pour of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रवाटिकः|अभ्रवाटिक
अभ्रम् + -वाटिकः, -वाटिका N. of a tree (आभ्रातक; Mar. अंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रवाटिका
अभ्रम् + -वाटिकः, -वाटिका N. of a tree (आभ्रातक; Mar. अंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रविलायम्
अभ्रम् + -विलायम् <i>ind.</i> just as clouds melt away; विच्छिन्नाभ्रविलायं<BR> वा विलीये नगमूर्धनि Ki. 11. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह <i>a.</i> [अभ्रं लेढि स्पृशति; खश् मुमागमश्च वहाभ्रेलिहः<BR> P. III. 2. 32] ‘Cloud-licking’, touching or scraping the clouds (very<BR> high); अभ्रंलिहाग्राः प्रासादाः Me. 66; प्रासादमभ्रंलिहमारुरोह<BR> R. 14. 29; K. 270; Śi. 5. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिहः|अभ्रंलिह
अभ्रंलिह + .{@-हः@} Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रकम्
अभ्रकम् [स्वार्थे कन्] Talc, mica; said to be produced from Pārvatīʼs<BR> menstrual discharge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्रकभस्मन्, अभ्रकसत्त्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रकभस्मन्
अभ्रकम् + -भस्मन् <i>n.</i> calx of talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रकसत्त्वम्
अभ्रकम् + -सत्त्वम् steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंकष|अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रंकष <i>a.</i> [अभ्रं कषति पीडयति तुङ्गत्वात्; खच् मुमागमश्च<BR> सर्वकूलाभ्रकरीषेषु लिहः P. III. 2. 42] Touching or scraping the clouds,<BR> very high; आदायाभ्रंकषं प्रायान्मलयं फलशालिनम् Bk.; K. 33; Dk. 110;<BR> Mv. 6. 7. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकष|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रंकष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 Wind, air; अभ्रंकषो वायुः Sk.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रयन्ती
अभ्रयन्ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Forming clouds, bringing rainy weather.<BR>—2 Name of one of the seven Kṛttikās; Yv. Ts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रायते
अभ्रायते Den. Ā. To create clouds, make cloudy; अभ्रं करोति अभ्रायते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रित
अभ्रित <i>a.</i> [अभ्राणि अस्य संजातानि; अभ्र-इतच् तारकादिगण]<BR> Overcast with clouds, clouded; ददर्श काले दिवमभ्रितामिव R. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिय|अभ्रियः
अभ्रिय <i>a.</i> [अभ्रे भवः घञ्] Belonging to or produced from clouds, sky<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रियः|अभ्रिय
अभ्रिय + .{@-यः@} Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रियम्
अभ्रिय + .{@-यम्@} A mass of thunder-clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रयः
अभ्रयः ‘One who is clothed only by the air’, an ascetic who is stark-naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम|अभ्रमः
अभ्रम <i>a.</i> Not mistaking, steady, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमः|अभ्रम
अभ्रम + .{@-मः@} Composure, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुः|अभ्रमु
अभ्रमुः <i>f.</i> The female elephant of the east, the mate of Airāvata,<BR> Indraʼs elephant, सलीलयातानि न भर्तुरभ्रमोर्न (प्रशशंस) Śi. 1. 52.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्रमुप्रियः, अभ्रमुवल्लभः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुप्रियः|अभ्रमुप्रिय
अभ्रमुः + -प्रियः, -वल्लभः Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुवल्लभः|अभ्रमुवल्लभ
अभ्रमुः + -प्रियः, -वल्लभः Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृव्य
अभ्रातृव्य <i>a.</i> Without a rival or enemy, अभ्रातृव्यो अना त्वमनापिरिन्द्र<BR> जनुषा सनादसि Rv. 8. 21. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्त|अभ्रांत|अभ्रान्तः
अभ्रान्त <i>a.</i> Composed, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्तिः|अभ्रान्ति|अभ्रांतिः
अभ्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> Composure, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिः|अभ्रि
अभ्रिः, -भ्री <i>f.</i><BR> [अभ्रति गच्छति मलं यस्मात् or येन, अभ्र-इन्]<BR>—1 A wooden scraper or sharp-pointed stick (for cleaning a boat).<BR>—2 A spade, hoe in general, अभ्रिं कार्ष्णायसीं दद्यात्सर्पं हत्वा द्विजोत्तमः Ms. 11. 134.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्रिखातम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्री
अभ्रिः, -भ्री <i>f.</i><BR> [अभ्रति गच्छति मलं यस्मात् or येन, अभ्र-इन्]<BR>—1 A wooden scraper or sharp-pointed stick (for cleaning a boat).<BR>—2 A spade, hoe in general, अभ्रिं कार्ष्णायसीं दद्यात्सर्पं हत्वा द्विजोत्तमः Ms. 11. 134.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अभ्रिखातम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिखातम्
अभ्रिः + -खातम् ‘dug up with a spade’, a ploughed field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रेषः|अभ्रेष
अभ्रेषः Non-deviation, fitness, propriety. P. III. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्व
अभ्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Huge, large (महत् Nir.).<BR>—2 Mighty strong or powerful. —3 monstrous, immense, terrible; आ यो नो<BR> अभ्व ईषते Rv. 1. 39. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्वम्
अभ्व + .{@-भ्वम्@}<BR>—1 Immense power, immensity.<BR>—2 Monstrosity, hugeness; (the great pervading principle of the universe;<BR> water; a cloud; embarrassed state, calamity; a monster; अरीरमत् पतयत्<BR> कच्चिदभ्वम् Rv. 6. 71. 5; closeness; offspring, given by B. and R.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Quickly.<BR>—2 A little. cf. also अं सुखं कश्मलं दुःखं पूर्णं दूरं गतं वरम् Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् €1 P. [अमति, अमितुम्, अमित Ved. pres. अमिति; अमीति]<BR>—1 To go; to go to or towards.<BR>—2 To serve, honour.<BR>—3 To sound.<BR>—4 To eat.<BR>—5 To be pernicious or dangerous; वराहमिन्द्र एमुषम् Rv. 8. 77. 10.<BR> €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i> (आमयति)<BR>—1 To come upon, attack, afflict with sickness or pain from disease.<BR>—2 To be ill or be afflicted or diseased. ━<i>With</i> {@सम्@} Ved. €1 Ā.<BR>—1 to convince oneself of, ascertain.<BR>—2 to ally or connect oneself with.<BR>—3 To fix or settle oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम <i>a.</i> Unripe (as fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमः|अम|अमं
अम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Going.<BR>—2 Pressure, weight; strength, power (बलम्).<BR>—3 Fright, terror.<BR>—4 Sickness, disease.<BR>—5 A servant, follower, an attendant.<BR>—6 Vital air, life-wind (प्राण).<BR>—7 This self.<BR>—8 Unmeasured state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अम + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 Soul.<BR>—2 Unmeasured state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमवत्|अमवन्त्
अमवत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Violent, strong, stormy (winds); powerful (sound also).<BR>—2 Persevering, constant.<BR>—3 Capable, fit, proper.<BR>—4 Attended by ministers.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">Page0199-2</a>]<BR>—5 Attended by diseases.<BR>—6 Possessed of self. ━<i>ind.</i> Violently, impetuously; य आश्वश्वा<BR> अमवद् वहन्त Rv. 5. 58. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतः|अमत
अमतः [अम्-अतच् Uṇ. 3. 110.]<BR>—1 Sickness, disease.<BR>—2 Death.<BR>—3 Time.<BR>—4 Dust, particle of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिः|अमति
अमतिः [अम्-अति Uṇ. 4. 59.]<BR>—1 Time.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 (Ved.) Form, shape (Nir.).<BR>—4 Want, poverty. <i>a.</i> poor, indigent; अनापिरज्ञा असजात्यामतिः Rv. 10. 39. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतीवन्
अमतिः + .{@-अमतीवन्^1@} <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Evil-minded, wicked (दुष्ट, अप्रशस्तबुद्धिमत् Sāy.).<BR>—2 Poor, indigent; न मे स्तोतामतीवा न दुर्हितः स्यादग्ने न पापया Rv. 8. 19. 26.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
अमङ्गल, -ल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inauspicious, evil, ill; R. 12. 43; ˚अभ्यासरतिम् Ku. 5. 65; अमङ्गल्यं<BR> शीलं तव भवतु नामैकमखिलम् Puṣpadanta.<BR>—2 Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल्य|अमंगल्य|अमङ्गल्यः
अमङ्गल, -ल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inauspicious, evil, ill; R. 12. 43; ˚अभ्यासरतिम् Ku. 5. 65; अमङ्गल्यं<BR> शीलं तव भवतु नामैकमखिलम् Puṣpadanta.<BR>—2 Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गलः|अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं
अमङ्गल, -ल्य + .{@-लः@} The castor-oil tree (एरण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गलम्
अमङ्गल, -ल्य + .{@-लम्@} Inauspiciousness, ill-luck; evil; oft. used in dramatic literature;<BR> शान्तं पापं प्रतिहतममङ्गलम्; cf. God forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्ड|अमंड|अमण्डः
अमण्ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without decoration or ornaments.<BR>—2 Without froth or scum (as boiled rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्डः|अमण्ड|अमंड
अमण्ड + .{@-ण्डः@} The castor oil tree (एरण्ड) Ricinus communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्डित
अमण्डित <i>a.</i> unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत|अमतः
अमत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not felt, not perceptible by the mind, unknown.<BR>—2 Disliked, not agreed to, see under अम् also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमतपरार्थता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतपरार्थता
अमत + -परार्थता ‘an unaccepted second sense’, one of the faults of<BR> a word (शब्ददोष); अमतः प्रकृतविरुद्धः परार्थो यत्र; <i>e. g.</i><BR> in राममन्मथशरेण ताडिता &c. (R. 11. 20) the second sense suggestive<BR> of शृङ्गाररस is opposed to the proper <i>rasa</i> of the passage<BR> which is either वीर or बीभत्स; K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अमति <i>a.</i> Evil-minded, wicked, depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिः|अमति
अमति + .{@-तिः@} A rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिः|अमति
अमति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> —1 Ignorance, unconsciousness, absence of knowledge,<BR> intention, or fore-thought; अमत्यैतानि षड् जग्ध्वा Ms. 5. 20, 4. 222.<BR> For some of the other senses see under अम्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमतिपूर्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिपूर्व|अमतिपूर्व्व
अमति + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> unconscious, unintentional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
अमत्र <i>a.</i> Ved. [अम्-अत्रन् Uṇ. 3. 105.] Overpowering (enemies),<BR> strong or disposed to march on (गमनशील); स्वरिरमत्रो ववक्षे<BR> रणाय Rv. 1. 61. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्रम्
अमत्र + .{@-त्रम, -त्रकम्@} [अमति भुङ्क्ते अन्नमत्र, आधारे अत्रन्]<BR>—1 A pot, vessel, utensil. उत्तार्य गोपी सुशृतं पयः पुनः प्रविश्य<BR> संदृश्य च दध्यमत्रकम् Bhāg. 10. 9. 7. अन्येषां चाप्यमत्राणां<BR> सौवर्णानामनेकशः Śiva B. 29. 59.<BR>—2 Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्रकम्
अमत्र + .{@-त्रम, -त्रकम्@} [अमति भुङ्क्ते अन्नमत्र, आधारे अत्रन्]<BR>—1 A pot, vessel, utensil. उत्तार्य गोपी सुशृतं पयः पुनः प्रविश्य<BR> संदृश्य च दध्यमत्रकम् Bhāg. 10. 9. 7. अन्येषां चाप्यमत्राणां<BR> सौवर्णानामनेकशः Śiva B. 29. 59.<BR>—2 Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्रिन्
अमत्रिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Strong, powerful.<BR>—2 Having a drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्सर|अमत्सरः
अमत्सर <i>a.</i> Unenvious, disinterested; यद्यद्रोचेत विप्रेभ्यस्तत्तद्दद्यादमत्सरः Ms. 3. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमद
अमद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from intoxication, grave, serious.<BR>—2 Sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमदनः|अमदन
अमदनः Name of Śiva. B. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0199-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्त
अमत्त <i>a.</i> Sober, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमधव्य
अमधव्य <i>a.</i> Not sweet, not worthy of the sweetness of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्
अमनस्, -अमनस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without the organ of desire, thought &c.<BR>—2 Devoid of intellect (as a child).<BR>—3 Inattentive, careless.<BR>—4 Having no control over the mind.<BR>—5 Devoid of affection. <i>n.</i><BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमनोगत, अमनोनीत, अमनोज्ञ, अमनोयोगः, अमनोहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्क
अमनस्, -अमनस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without the organ of desire, thought &c.<BR>—2 Devoid of intellect (as a child).<BR>—3 Inattentive, careless.<BR>—4 Having no control over the mind.<BR>—5 Devoid of affection. <i>n.</i><BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमनोगत, अमनोनीत, अमनोज्ञ, अमनोयोगः, अमनोहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनः
अमनस्, -अमनस्क + ({@-नः@})<BR>—1 Not the organ of desire, non-perception.<BR>—2 Inattention. ━<i>m.</i> The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोगत
अमनस् + -गत <i>a.</i> Unknown, unthought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोनीत
अमनस् + -नीत, -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> Disapproved, condemned; reprobate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोज्ञ
अमनस् + -नीत, -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> Disapproved, condemned; reprobate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोगः|अमनोयोग
अमनस् + -योगः Absence of concentration of mind, inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोहर
अमनस् + -हर <i>a.</i> displeasing, disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्विन्
अमनस्विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unintelligent.<BR>—2 Inhuman (as a demon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनिः|अमनि
अमनिः^1 [अम्-अनिः, अमति गच्छत्यत्र Uṇ. 2. 101] Motion (गतिः); way.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: misplaced vowel diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनाक्
अमनाक् <i>ind.</i> Not a little, greatly, very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अमनुष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not human, not manly.<BR>—2 Not frequented by man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्यः|अमनुष्य
अमनुष्य + .{@-ष्यः@}<BR>—1 Not a man; नामनुष्ये भवत्यग्निः Rām. 2. 93. 22.<BR>—2 A demon, fiend (= रक्षःपिशाचादि Sk. on P. II. 4. 23).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्यता
अमनुष्य + .{@-ता@} Unmanliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्तु|अमंतु
अमन्तु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unwise, foolish.<BR>—2 Guiltless, innocent.<BR>—3 Despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्र|अमंत्र
अमन्त्र, -न्त्रक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not accompanied by Vedic verses, not requiring the repetition of Vedic<BR> texts, as a ceremony &c.; सायं त्वन्नस्य सिद्धस्य पत्न्यमन्त्रं बलिं<BR> हरेत् Ms. 3. 121, 2. 66.<BR>—2 Not entitled to Vedic verses, such as a Śūdra, a female &c.; निरिन्द्रिया<BR> ह्यमन्त्राश्च स्त्रियोऽनृतमिति स्थितिः Ms. 9. 18.<BR>—3 Not knowing Vedic texts; अव्रतानाममन्त्राणाम् Ms. 12. 114.<BR>—4 Not accompanied by the use of spells or incantations, as a cure &c.;<BR> अनया कथमन्यथावलीढा न हि जीवन्ति जना मनागमन्त्राः Bv. 1. 111.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमन्त्रज्ञ, अमन्त्रतन्त्र, अमन्त्रविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रक|अमंत्रक
अमन्त्र, -न्त्रक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not accompanied by Vedic verses, not requiring the repetition of Vedic<BR> texts, as a ceremony &c.; सायं त्वन्नस्य सिद्धस्य पत्न्यमन्त्रं बलिं<BR> हरेत् Ms. 3. 121, 2. 66.<BR>—2 Not entitled to Vedic verses, such as a Śūdra, a female &c.; निरिन्द्रिया<BR> ह्यमन्त्राश्च स्त्रियोऽनृतमिति स्थितिः Ms. 9. 18.<BR>—3 Not knowing Vedic texts; अव्रतानाममन्त्राणाम् Ms. 12. 114.<BR>—4 Not accompanied by the use of spells or incantations, as a cure &c.;<BR> अनया कथमन्यथावलीढा न हि जीवन्ति जना मनागमन्त्राः Bv. 1. 111.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमन्त्रज्ञ, अमन्त्रतन्त्र, अमन्त्रविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रज्ञ
अमन्त्र + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> Not knowing Vedic texts or hymns; Ms. 3. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रतन्त्र
अमन्त्र + -तन्त्र <i>a.</i> Without the use of spells or the magical feats<BR> attendant on them, without the use of magical arts; अमन्त्रतन्त्रं वशीकरणम् Pt. 1. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रविद्
अमन्त्र + -विद् <i>a.</i> Not knowing Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्द|अमंद|अमन्दः
अमन्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not slow or dull, active, intelligent; मन्दोऽप्यमन्दतामेति संसर्गेण<BR> विपश्चितः M. 2. 8.<BR>—2 Sharp, strong, violent (wind &c.).<BR>—3 Not little, much, excessive, great, violent; अमन्दमददुर्दिन<BR> U. 5. 5; अमन्दमिलदिन्दिरे निखिलमाधुरी मन्दिरे Bv. 4. 1; ˚दष्टौष्ठकरावधूननम्<BR> Ki. 8. 6 violently bit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्दः|अमन्द|अमंद
अमन्द + .{@-न्दः@} N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्यमान
अमन्यमान <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not understanding; offering no homage; अमन्यमानाँ अभि मन्यमानैः Rv. 1. 33. 9.<BR>—2 Not being aware of; अमन्यमानाच्छर्वा जघान Rv. 2. 12. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्युत
अमन्युत <i>a.</i> Ved. Not bearing ill-will towards another; अमन्युता<BR> नो वीरुधो भवन्तु Av. 12. 3. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम <i>a.</i> Without egotism, without any selfish or worldly attachment,<BR> devoid of personal ties or desires;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">Page0200-2</a>]<BR> शरणेष्वममश्चैव वृक्षमूलनिकेतनः Ms. 6. 26<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममः|अमम
अमम + .{@-मः@} The twelfth Jaina saint of a future उत्सर्पिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममता
अममता, -त्वम्<BR> Indifference, disinterestedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममत्वम्
अममता, -त्वम्<BR> Indifference, disinterestedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम्रि
अमम्रि <i>a.</i> Ved. Immortal; अमम्रिर्भवामृतोऽतिजीवो Av. 8. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर <i>a.</i> [मृ-पचाद्यच्, न˚ त˚] Undying, immortal, imperishable;<BR> अजरामरवत् प्राज्ञो विद्यामर्थं च चिन्तयेत् H. Pr. 3; Ms. 2. 148.<BR> अजरोऽमरोऽमृतः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरः|अमर
अमर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A god, deity.<BR>—2 N. of a Marut.<BR>—3 N. of a plant Euphorbia Tirucalli (स्नुहीवृक्ष; Mar. शेर).<BR> Tiaridium Indicum (हस्तिशुण्ड ?; Mar. भुरुंडी).<BR>—4 Quick-silver.<BR>—5 Gold.<BR>—6 A species of pine.<BR>—7 The number 33. (that being the number of Gods.)<BR>—8 N. of Amarasiṃha, see below; of a mountain.<BR>—9 Mystical signification of the syllable उ.<BR>—10 A heap of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरा
अमर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 The residence of Indra (cf. अमरावती).<BR>—2 The naval string; umbilical cord.<BR>—3 The womb.<BR>—4 A house-post (स्थूणा).<BR>—5 N. of several plants; इन्द्रवारुणी, वटी, महानीली, घृतकुमारी, स्नुही,<BR> गुडूची, दूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

