अमर + -प्रख्य, -प्रभ <i>a.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">Page0201-1</a>]<BR> like an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरप्रभुः|अमरप्रभु
अमर + -प्रभुः one of the 1000 names of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरमाला
अमर + -माला N. of a lexicon. (said to be composed by the same author<BR> as that of Amarakośa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमररत्नम्
अमर + -रत्नम् a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरराजः|अमरराज
अमर + -राजः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोकः|अमरलोक
अमर + -लोकः the world of the gods, heaven; ˚ता heavenly bliss;<BR> तेषु सम्यग्वर्तमानो गच्छत्यमरलोकताम् Ms. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरवल्लरी
अमर + -वल्लरी N. of a plant (आकाशवल्ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरसिंहः|अमरसिंह
अमर + -सिंहः N. of the author of <i>Amarakośa</i>; he was a Jaina<BR> and is said to have been one of the 9 gems that adorned the court of king<BR> Vikramāditya. The dates of many of these ‘gems’ are still doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरस्त्री
अमर + -स्त्री An Apsaras or a nymph of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणम्
अमरणम् Not dying, immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरता
अमरता, -त्वम्<BR> The state of the gods, immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरत्वम्
अमरता, -त्वम्<BR> The state of the gods, immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरावती [अमर-वत्, र being changed to रा by P. VI. 3. 119]<BR>—1 Abode of the gods, residence of Indra (said to be above Meru or the<BR> sunʼs orb; cf. Ki. 7, 2); ससंभ्रमेन्द्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR> भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1.<BR>—2 N. of a modern town in Berar, Amravati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरिष्णु
अमरिष्णु, -अमर्त <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त|अमर्त्त
अमरिष्णु, -अमर्त <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अमर्त्य <i>a.</i> Immortal, divine, imperishable; ˚भावेऽपि R. 7. 53;<BR> ˚भुवनम् heaven; ˚ता immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यः|अमर्त्य
अमर्त्य + .{@-र्त्यः@} A god.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमर्त्यापगा, अमर्त्यभुवनम्, अमर्त्यवधूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यापगा
अमर्त्य + -आपगा the celestial river, epithet of the Ganges; Vikr. 18. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यभुवनम्
अमर्त्य + -भुवनम् The heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यवधूः
अमर्त्य + -वधूः An Apsaras or a nymph of heaven; लेभे परां द्युतिममर्त्यवधूसमूहः Ki. 6. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरी
अमरी A goddess; अमरीकबरीभारभ्रमरीमुखरीकृतम् Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुः|अमरु
अमरुः, -अमरुकः<BR> N. of a king and poet who composed 100 verses which<BR> are usually known by the name अमरुशतक; प्रज्ञानवानमरुकस्य कवेः<BR> प्रसारश्लोकाञ्छतं विवृणुतेऽर्जुनवर्मदेवः Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुकः|अमरुक
अमरुः, -अमरुकः<BR> N. of a king and poet who composed 100 verses which<BR> are usually known by the name अमरुशतक; प्रज्ञानवानमरुकस्य कवेः<BR> प्रसारश्लोकाञ्छतं विवृणुतेऽर्जुनवर्मदेवः Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्दित|अमर्द्दित
अमर्दित <i>a.</i> Unthreshed, untrodden, unsubdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मन्
अमर्मन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not a vital organ or part of the body, having<BR> no joint or vital part. येभिर्वृत्रस्येषितो विवेदामर्मणो मन्यमानस्य<BR> मर्म Rv. 3. 32. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमर्मजात, अमर्मवेधिन्, अमर्मवेधिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मजात
अमर्मन् + -जात <i>a.</i> not produced in a vital organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मवेधिन्
अमर्मन् + -वेधिन् <i>a.</i> not injuring the vital parts; mild, soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मवेधिता
अमर्मन् + -वेधिता <i>f.</i> The state of not inflicting severe injury on others,<BR> absence of acrimony (one of the thirty-five Vāg-guṇas of a Tīrthaṅkara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्याद|अमर्य्याद
अमर्याद <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Exceeding due limits or bounds, transgressing every bound, disrespectful,<BR> improper; मर्यादायाममर्यादाः स्त्रियस्तिष्ठन्ति सर्वदा Pt. 1. 142;<BR> तादृशं त्वममर्यादं कर्म कर्तुं चिकीर्षसि Rām.<BR>—2 Boundless, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्यादा|अमर्य्यादा
अमर्याद + .{@-दा@} Transgression of due limits or bounds, impropriety of conduct,<BR> forwardness, disrespect, violation of due respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अमर्ष <i>a.</i> Not enduring or bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षः|अमर्ष
अमर्ष + .{@-र्षः@}<BR>—1 Non-endurance, tolerance, impatience; अमर्षप्रभवो रोषः सफलो<BR> मे भविष्यति Rām. 5. 62. 33. अमर्षशून्येन जनस्य जन्तुना न जातहार्देन<BR> न विद्विषादरः Ki. 1. 33; jealousy, jealous anger; किं नु भवतस्तातप्रतापोत्कर्षेऽप्यमर्षः<BR> U. 5. In Rhet.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">Page0201-2</a>]<BR> अमर्ष is one of the 33 minor feelings or व्यभिचारिभाव. See S. D.;<BR> R. G. thus defines it: परकृतावज्ञादिनानापराधजन्यो मौनवाक्पारुष्यादिकारणीभूतश्चित्तवृत्तिविशेषोऽमर्षः.<BR>—2 Anger, passion, wrath; पुत्रवधामर्षोद्दीपितेन गाण्डीविना Ve. 2;<BR> हर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैः Bg. 12. 15. सामर्ष angry, indignant; सामर्षम् angrily.<BR>—3 Impetuosity, violence.<BR>—4 Determination of purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षा
अमर्ष + .{@-र्षा@} Intolerance; यत्र सङ्गीतसन्नादैर्नदद्गुहममर्षया Bhāg. 8. 2. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमर्षज, अमर्षहासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षज
अमर्ष + -ज <i>a.</i> arising from anger or impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षहासः|अमर्षहास
अमर्ष + -हासः an angry laugh, sarcastic sneer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अमर्षण, -र्षित, -र्षिन्, -र्षवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving; विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः<BR> आभिमुख्यम् Pt. 1. 326.<BR>—2 Angry, indignant, passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः R. 3. 53;<BR> अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पाण्डुपुत्रैः Ve. 4.<BR>—3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षित
अमर्षण, -र्षित, -र्षिन्, -र्षवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving; विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः<BR> आभिमुख्यम् Pt. 1. 326.<BR>—2 Angry, indignant, passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः R. 3. 53;<BR> अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पाण्डुपुत्रैः Ve. 4.<BR>—3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षिन्
अमर्षण, -र्षित, -र्षिन्, -र्षवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving; विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः<BR> आभिमुख्यम् Pt. 1. 326.<BR>—2 Angry, indignant, passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः R. 3. 53;<BR> अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पाण्डुपुत्रैः Ve. 4.<BR>—3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षवत्
अमर्षण, -र्षित, -र्षिन्, -र्षवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving; विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः<BR> आभिमुख्यम् Pt. 1. 326.<BR>—2 Angry, indignant, passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः R. 3. 53;<BR> अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पाण्डुपुत्रैः Ve. 4.<BR>—3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अमल <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Free from dirt or impurities, pure, undefiled, stainless, spotless;<BR> कपालमेवामलशेखरश्रीः । (बभूव) Ku. 7. 32, 33; लोकानमलान्<BR> प्रतिपद्यते Bg. 14. 14. अमलाः सुहृदः Pt. 2. 171 pure, sincere.<BR>—2 White, bright, shining; कर्णावसक्तामलदन्तपत्रम् Ku. 7. 23; R. 6. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमला
अमल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 N. of the goddess Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 The navel cord.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (Mar. आंवळा) Emblica Officinalis Gaertn; also of<BR> a plant (सातलावृक्ष) also <i>n.</i> in this sense. यथा वै द्वे वामलके<BR> Ch. Up. 7. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलम्
अमल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Purity.<BR>—2 Talc.<BR>—3 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमलात्मन्, अमलगर्भः, अमलपतत्रिन्, अमलरत्नम्, अमलमणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलात्मन्
अमल + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> Of pure or undefiled mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलगर्भः|अमलगर्भ
अमल + -गर्भः N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलपतत्रिन्
अमल + -पतत्रिन् + ({@-त्री@}) <i>m.</i> the wild goose; माधुर्यादमलपतत्रिणां<BR> कुलानि Śi. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलपतत्री
अमल + -पतत्रिन् + ({@-त्री@}) <i>m.</i> the wild goose; माधुर्यादमलपतत्रिणां<BR> कुलानि Śi. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलरत्नम्
अमल + -रत्नम्, -मणिः a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलमणिः|अमलमणि
अमल + -रत्नम्, -मणिः a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलयति
अमलयति Den. P. To make pure or spotless, brighten; अमलयतीह<BR> वनान्तमिन्दुलेखा Ki. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अमलिन <i>a.</i> Clean, spotless, pure (morally also); कुलममलिनं<BR> न त्वेवायं जनो न च जीवितम् Māl. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलानकम्
अमलानकम् Globe-amaranth. (Mar. मखमाल)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमवत्|अमवन्त्
अमवत् See under अम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमविष्णु
अमविष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going in different directions, up and down.<BR>—2 Immovable; अनातुरा अजराः स्थामविष्णवः Rv. 10. 94. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसः|अमस
अमसः [अम्-असच्]<BR>—1 Disease.<BR>—2 Stupidity.<BR>—3 A fool.<BR>—4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसृण
अमसृण <i>a.</i> Not soft or bland, harsh, violent, strong, intense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तु
अमस्तु^1 <i>n.</i> Curds.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: from sense 'curds'. (why not 'without curds'?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा <i>a.</i> [न मा-क] Measureless. ━<i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 At home, in the house; कामश्चरताममाभूत् Rv. 2. 38. 6.<BR>—2 In this world, here below (इहलोके).<BR>—3 With, near, close to; अमैवासां तद्भवति Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 20.<BR>—4 Together with, in conjunction or company with, as in अमात्य, अमावास्या<BR> q. v.; अमाकृ to draw near, have near oneself. अमा सह समीपे च Nm. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 The day of the new moon, the day of the conjunction of the sun and moon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">Page0202-1</a>]<BR> अमायां तु सदा सोम ओषधीः प्रतिपद्यते Vyāsa.<BR>—2 The sixteenth digit of the moon.<BR>—3 The fifteenth digit also. ━<i>m.</i> The soul.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमाक्त, अमान्तः, अमेष्ट, अमाजुर्, अमापर्वन्, अमाहठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाक्त
अमा + -अक्त <i>a.</i> Ved. met, come together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमान्तः|अमान्त
अमा + -अन्तः The end of the day of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेष्ट
अमा + -इष्ट <i>a.</i> Sacrificed at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाजुर्
अमा + -जुर् <i>f.</i> Living at home during life, growing old at home; अमाजुरश्चिद्भवयो<BR> युवं भगो Rv. 10. 39. 3; being without husband in the same dwelling<BR> with her parents, as a maiden (पितृषद्); अमाजूरिव पित्रोः सचा सती Rv. 2. 17. 7<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमापर्वन्
अमा + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> The sacred time of अमा, day of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाहठः|अमाहठ
अमा + -हठः Name of a snake-demon; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांस|अमांसः
अमांस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without flesh, not containing flesh.<BR>—2 Lean, thin, weak, enfeebled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांसम्
अमांस + .{@-सम्@} Not flesh, anything but flesh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमांसौदनिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांसौदनिक
अमांस + -ओदनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Not relating to a preparation of rice with meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्
अमात् <i>ind.</i> Ved. —1 From near, at hand. <i>a.</i> Not measuring, boundless;<BR> प्रमदादमानिव पुरे महीयसि Śi. 13. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृ
अमातृ, -तृक <i>a.</i><BR> Motherless; Dk. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृक
अमातृ, -तृक <i>a.</i><BR> Motherless; Dk. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृभोगीण
अमातृभोगीण <i>a.</i> Not fit for the use of a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्यः|अमात्य
अमात्यः [अमा सह वसति, अमा-त्यप्, अव्ययात्त्यप् P. IV. 2. 104.<BR> Vārt. अमेहक्वतसित्रेभ्य एव]<BR>—1 One living with or near another, an inmate of the same house or family (Ved.).<BR>—2 A companion or follower of a king, minister; तस्यामात्या गुणैरासन्निक्ष्वाकोः<BR> सुमहात्मनः Rām. 1. 7. 1; अमात्याः सर्व एवैते कार्याः स्युर्न तु मन्त्रिणः Kau. A. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्यिका
अमात्यः + .{@-अमात्यिका@} <i>f.</i> Mbh. on P. VII. 3. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमात्योत्पत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्योत्पत्तिः
अमात्यः + -उत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> Creation of ministers Kau. A. 1. 8. अमात्यपुत्रैः<BR> सवयोभिरन्वितः R. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्र|अमात्रः
अमात्र <i>a.</i> [नास्ति मात्रा इयत्ता यस्य]<BR>—1 Boundless, immeasurable; अमात्रं त्वा धिषणा तित्वेषे Rv. 1. 102. 7.<BR>—2 Not whole or entire.<BR>—3 Not elementary.<BR>—4 Having the measure or quantity of the letter अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रम्
अमात्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 Non-measure.<BR>—2 Not a measure or quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रः|अमात्र
अमात्र + .{@-त्रः@} The Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रवत्वम्
अमात्रवत्वम्<BR>—1 Spirit, spiritual essence.<BR>—2 Defect, deficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाननम्
अमाननम्, -ना<BR> Disrespect, insult; disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानना
अमाननम्, -ना<BR> Disrespect, insult; disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानव
अमानव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not human; animal.<BR>—2 Superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानस्यम्
अमानस्यम् Pain (मानसे साधु न भवति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अमानिन् <i>a.</i> Modest, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिता
अमानिता, -त्वम्<BR> Modesty, humility. अमानित्वमदाम्भित्वम् Bg. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानित्वम्
अमानिता, -त्वम्<BR> Modesty, humility. अमानित्वमदाम्भित्वम् Bg. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अमानुष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Not human, not belonging to man, supernatural, unearthly, superhuman;<BR> आकृतिरेवानुमापयत्यमानुषताम् K. 132, ˚आकृतिः K. 131, 132, 258;<BR> ˚शक्तित्वम् 103; ˚गीतध्वनिम् 126 an unearthly melody.<BR>—2 Inhuman, monster-like; ill-disposed towards man.<BR>—3 Tenantless, desolate; ˚षं वनम् 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुषः|अमानुष
अमानुष + .{@-षः, -षी@} One not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">Page0202-2</a>]<BR> a man, an irrational animal; Ms. 9. 284, स्त्रीणामशिक्षितपटुत्वममानुषीषु<BR> संदृश्यते Ś. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुषी
अमानुष + .{@-षः, -षी@} One not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">Page0202-2</a>]<BR> a man, an irrational animal; Ms. 9. 284, स्त्रीणामशिक्षितपटुत्वममानुषीषु<BR> संदृश्यते Ś. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्य
अमानुष्य <i>a.</i> Not human, superhuman &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्यम्
अमानुष्य + .{@-˚ष्यम्@} Inhuman state; अमानुष्यं समापन्नान् दासकर्मण्यवस्थितान्<BR> Mb. 5. 160. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामसी
अमाम(मा)सी = अमावसी or अमावस्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामासी
अमाम(मा)सी = अमावसी or अमावस्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अमाय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not cunning or sagacious, guileless, sincere, honest.<BR>—2 Immeasurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाया
अमाय + .{@-या@}<BR>—1 Absence of fraud or deceit, honesty, sincerity.<BR>—2 (In Vedānta Phil.) Absence of delusion or error, knowledge of the supreme truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायम्
अमाय + .{@-यम्@} The Supreme Spirit (ब्रह्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिक|अमायिकः
अमायिक, -मायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Guileless; honest, sincere, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिन्
अमायिक, -मायिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Guileless; honest, sincere, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमारः|अमार
अमारः Not dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ग|अमार्गः
अमार्ग <i>a.</i> Pathless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्गः|अमार्ग
अमार्ग + .{@-र्गः@} Not a road, absence of road; a bad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसुः|अमावसु
अमावसुः N. of a prince (a descendant of Purūravas); Mb.; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावस्या
अमावस्या, -वास्या, -वसी, -वासी (also written अमामसी, -मासी)<BR> [अमावस्<BR> -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चन्द्रार्कौ अस्यां सा. अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्<BR> P. III. 1. 122. Sk.]<BR>—1 The day of new moon, when the sun and moon dwell together or are in<BR> conjunction; the 15th day of the dark half of every lunar month; सूर्याचन्द्रमसोः<BR> यः परः सन्निकर्षः साऽमावस्या Gobhila; अमावास्यायां दीक्षित्वा Ch. Up. 5. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>—3 The sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्या
अमावस्या, -वास्या, -वसी, -वासी (also written अमामसी, -मासी)<BR> [अमावस्<BR> -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चन्द्रार्कौ अस्यां सा. अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्<BR> P. III. 1. 122. Sk.]<BR>—1 The day of new moon, when the sun and moon dwell together or are in<BR> conjunction; the 15th day of the dark half of every lunar month; सूर्याचन्द्रमसोः<BR> यः परः सन्निकर्षः साऽमावस्या Gobhila; अमावास्यायां दीक्षित्वा Ch. Up. 5. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>—3 The sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसी
अमावस्या, -वास्या, -वसी, -वासी (also written अमामसी, -मासी)<BR> [अमावस्<BR> -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चन्द्रार्कौ अस्यां सा. अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्<BR> P. III. 1. 122. Sk.]<BR>—1 The day of new moon, when the sun and moon dwell together or are in<BR> conjunction; the 15th day of the dark half of every lunar month; सूर्याचन्द्रमसोः<BR> यः परः सन्निकर्षः साऽमावस्या Gobhila; अमावास्यायां दीक्षित्वा Ch. Up. 5. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>—3 The sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

