अमामसी
अमावस्या, -वास्या, -वसी, -वासी (also written अमामसी, -मासी)<BR> [अमावस्<BR> -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चन्द्रार्कौ अस्यां सा. अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्<BR> P. III. 1. 122. Sk.]<BR>—1 The day of new moon, when the sun and moon dwell together or are in<BR> conjunction; the 15th day of the dark half of every lunar month; सूर्याचन्द्रमसोः<BR> यः परः सन्निकर्षः साऽमावस्या Gobhila; अमावास्यायां दीक्षित्वा Ch. Up. 5. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>—3 The sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामासी
अमावस्या, -वास्या, -वसी, -वासी (also written अमामसी, -मासी)<BR> [अमावस्<BR> -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चन्द्रार्कौ अस्यां सा. अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्<BR> P. III. 1. 122. Sk.]<BR>—1 The day of new moon, when the sun and moon dwell together or are in<BR> conjunction; the 15th day of the dark half of every lunar month; सूर्याचन्द्रमसोः<BR> यः परः सन्निकर्षः साऽमावस्या Gobhila; अमावास्यायां दीक्षित्वा Ch. Up. 5. 2. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>—3 The sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्य
अमावास्य, -स्यक <i>a.</i><BR> [अमावस्या, वुन्-अच् अमावास्याया वा P. IV. 3. 30-31;<BR> अमावास्यायां जातः] Born or produced on the night of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्यक
अमावास्य, -स्यक <i>a.</i><BR> [अमावस्या, वुन्-अच् अमावास्याया वा P. IV. 3. 30-31;<BR> अमावास्यायां जातः] Born or produced on the night of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unmeasured, boundless, unlimited, infinite, great, immense; मितं<BR> ददाति हि पिता मितं भ्राता मितं सुतः । अमितस्य हि दातारं भर्तारं<BR> का न पूजयेत् Rām. 2. 37. 30.<BR>—2 Neglected, disregarded.<BR>—3 Unknown.<BR>—4 Unpolished.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमिताक्षर, अमिताशनः, अमिताभ, अमितायुः, अमितौजस्, अमितक्रतु, अमितगतिः, अमिततेजस्, अमितद्युति, अमितध्वजः, अमितरुचिः, अमितविक्रमः, अमितवीर्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिताक्षर
अमित + -अक्षर <i>a.</i> not having a fixed number of syllables; prosaic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिताशनः|अमिताशन
अमित + -अशनः Powerful devourer, epithet of परमेश्वर; of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिताभ|अमिताभः
अमित + -आभ <i>a.</i> Of great lustre, of unbounded splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिताभः|अमिताभ
अमित + -आभ + .({@-भः@}) a class of divinities mentioned in V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितायुः|अमितायु
अमित + -आयुः N. of a Dhyānibuddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितौजस्
अमित + -ओजस् <i>a.</i> of unbounded energy, all-powerful, Almighty; स<BR> तैः पृष्टस्तथा सम्यगमितौजा महात्मभिः Ms. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितक्रतु
अमित + -क्रतु <i>a.</i> of unbounded wisdom or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितगतिः|अमितगति
अमित + -गतिः N. of a Vidyādhara, Ks. N. of a Jaina author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिततेजस्
अमित + -तेजस्, -द्युति <i>a.</i> of unbounded lustre or glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितद्युति
अमित + -तेजस्, -द्युति <i>a.</i> of unbounded lustre or glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितध्वजः|अमितध्वज
अमित + -ध्वजः N. of a son of Dharmadhvaja; V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितरुचिः|अमितरुचि
अमित + -रुचिः N. of a deity (Buddhistic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितविक्रमः|अमितविक्रम
अमित + -विक्रमः<BR>—1 of unbounded valour; अनन्तवीर्यामितविक्रमस्त्वम् Bg. 11. 40.<BR>—2 a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितवीर्य
अमित + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> of immense strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रः|अमित्र
अमित्रः [न मित्रम्; by Uṇ. 4. 173 fr. अम् to go against;<BR> अमेर्द्विषति चित्; अमित्रः शत्रुः] Not a friend, an enemy,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">Page0203-1</a>]<BR> adversary, a foe, rival, opponent; स्याताममित्रौ मित्रे च सहजप्राकृतावपि<BR> Śi. 2. 36; तस्य मित्राण्यमित्रास्ते 101; Dk. 109, 171; M. 1; प्रकृत्यमित्रा<BR> हि सतामसाधवः Ki. 14. 21; Ms. 7. 83, 12. 79, 2. 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रा
अमित्रः + .{@-त्रा@} An enemy; ˚युध् Ved. subduing oneʼs enemies.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमित्रखाद्, अमित्रघात, अमित्रघातिन्, अमित्रघ्न, अमित्रहन्, अमित्रजित्, अमित्रदम्भन, अमित्रसह, अमित्रसाह, अमित्रसेना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0202-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रखाद्
अमित्रः + -खाद् <i>a.</i> Devouring oneʼs enemies, epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रघात
अमित्रः + -घात, -घातिन्, -घ्न, -हन् Killing enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रघातिन्
अमित्रः + -घात, -घातिन्, -घ्न, -हन् Killing enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रघ्न
अमित्रः + -घात, -घातिन्, -घ्न, -हन् Killing enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रहन्
अमित्रः + -घात, -घातिन्, -घ्न, -हन् Killing enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रजित्
अमित्रः + -जित् <i>a.</i> Conquering oneʼs enemies; अमित्रजिन्मित्रजिदोजसा<BR> यत् N. 1. 13; N. of a son of Suvarṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रदम्भन
अमित्रः + -दम्भन <i>a.</i> Ved. hurting oneʼs enemies. बृहस्पते भीमममित्रदम्भनम् Rv. 2. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रसह
अमित्रः + -सह, -साह <i>a.</i> enduring or overpowering oneʼs<BR> enemies, epithet of Indra; शास इत्था महाँ अस्यमित्रसाहो अस्तृतः Av. 1. 20. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रसाह
अमित्रः + -सह, -साह <i>a.</i> enduring or overpowering oneʼs<BR> enemies, epithet of Indra; शास इत्था महाँ अस्यमित्रसाहो अस्तृतः Av. 1. 20. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रसेना
अमित्रः + -सेना a hostile army; अमित्रसेनामभिजञ्जभानो Av. 5. 20. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रकम्
अमित्रकम् An unfriendly act; राजानमिममासाद्य सुहृच्चिह्नममित्रकम्<BR> Rām. 6. 65. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रता
अमित्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Enmity; Pt. 2. 98; तदास्य मित्राण्यपि यान्त्यमित्रताम् Mk. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रत्वम्
अमित्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Enmity; Pt. 2. 98; तदास्य मित्राण्यपि यान्त्यमित्रताम् Mk. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रयति
अमित्रयति Den. P., अमित्रायते Ā. To act like an enemy, act<BR> hostilely towards, hate; हा कष्टं पुरुषस्य जीर्णवयसः पुत्रोऽप्यमित्रायते Bh. 3. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रायते
अमित्रयति Den. P., अमित्रायते Ā. To act like an enemy, act<BR> hostilely towards, hate; हा कष्टं पुरुषस्य जीर्णवयसः पुत्रोऽप्यमित्रायते Bh. 3. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रिन्
अमित्रिन् <i>a.</i> Hostile, inimical; मा कस्मै धातमभ्यमित्रिणे Rv. 1. 120. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रीय
अमित्रीय, -त्र्य <i>a.</i><BR> Hostile, inimical; विश्वा वृत्रममित्रिया शवोभिः Rv. 6. 17. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्र्य
अमित्रीय, -त्र्य <i>a.</i><BR> Hostile, inimical; विश्वा वृत्रममित्रिया शवोभिः Rv. 6. 17. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथित
अमिथित <i>a.</i> Ved. Not reviled, not provoked; को नु मर्या अमिथितः<BR> सखा सखायमब्रवीत् Rv. 8. 45. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथ्या
अमिथ्या <i>adv.</i> Not falsely, truly; तामूचतुस्ते प्रियमप्यमिथ्या R. 14. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन्
अमिन् <i>a.</i> Sick, diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन
अमिन <i>a.</i> Ved. Inviolable (अहिंस्य); immense (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिनत्|अमिनन्त्
अमिनत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not hurting; unhurt.<BR>—2 Unalterable; यजत्रैरमिनती तस्थतुरुक्षमाणे Rv. 4. 56. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिलातकम्
अमिलातकम् Globe-amaranth. See अमलानकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्र
अमिश्र, -श्रित <i>a.</i><BR> Unmixed, unblended; not shared by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रित
अमिश्र, -श्रित <i>a.</i><BR> Unmixed, unblended; not shared by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Free from guile or deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिषम्
अमिष + .{@-षम्@} [अम् भोगे-कर्मणि इषन्]<BR>—1 An object of worldly enjoyment, luxury.<BR>—2 Honesty, absence of fraud or deceit.<BR>—3 Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीत
अमीत <i>a.</i> Unhurt; ˚अर्णाः of unhurt or unextinguishable or<BR> unaltered colour; समना समानीरमीतवर्णा उषसश्चरन्ति Rv. 4. 51. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीवा
अमीवा [अम्-वन्-ईडागमः निपातः] Ved.<BR>—1 Affliction, sickness, disease.<BR>—2 Distress, terror.<BR>—3 A demon, tormenting spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीवः|अमीव|अमीवं
अमीवा + .{@-वः@} An enemy, one who afflicts or torments;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीवम्
अमीवा + .{@-वम्@} —1 Affliction, distress, pain, injury, कच्चिद् बुधः स्वस्त्यनमीव<BR> आस्ते Bhāg. 3. 1. 32. कुठारैश्चिच्छिद्रुः क्रुद्धाः स्मरन्तोऽमीवमस्य तत्<BR> Bhāg. 4. 28. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक <i>pron. a.</i> [अदस्-टेरकच् उत्वमत्त्वे Tv.] A certain person<BR> or thing, so and so (to be used when a person or thing is referred to<BR> without a name); मतं मेऽमुकपुत्रस्य यदत्रोपरिलेखितम् Y. 2. 86-87;<BR> उभयाभ्यर्थितेनैतन्मया ह्यमुकसूनुना । लिखितं ह्यमुकेनेति लेखकोऽन्ते<BR> ततो लिखेत् 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्त|अमुक्तं
अमुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not loosened, not let go.<BR>—2 Not liberated from recurring birth and death, not having got final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तम्
अमुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} A weapon (a knife, sword &c.) that is always grasped and<BR> not thrown. चतुर्विधमायुधम् । मुक्तममुक्तं मुक्तामुक्तं यन्त्रमुक्तं<BR> चेति Dhanur. V. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमुक्तहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तहस्त
अमुक्त + -हस्त <i>a.</i> one whose hand is not open or free (to give), sparing,<BR> stingy (in a bad sense); frugal, economical, prudent (in a good sense);<BR> सदा प्रहृष्टया भाव्यं व्यये चामुक्तहस्तया Ms. 5. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तिः|अमुक्ति
अमुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-liberation.<BR>—2 Want of freedom or liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुच्
अमुच् <i>f.</i> Ved. Non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुची
अमुची <i>f.</i> Ved. Not unbinding, not setting at liberty (said of<BR> an evil spirit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतः
अमुतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From there, there.<BR>—2 From that place, from above, <i>i. e.</i> from the other world or heaven.<BR>—3 Upon this, thereupon; henceforth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र <i>ind.</i> (opp. इह) [अदस्-त्रल्]<BR>—1 There, in that place, therein; अमुत्रासन् यवनाः Dk. 127.<BR>—2 There (in what precedes or has been said), in that case.<BR>—3 There above, in the next world, in the life to come; यावज्जीवं च<BR> तत्कुर्याद्येनामुत्र सुखं वसेत्; यत्तु वाणिजके दत्तं नेह नामुत्र तद्भवेत्<BR> Ms. 3. 181; पार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते Bg. 6. 40.<BR>—4 There; अनेनैवार्भकाः सर्वे नगरेऽमुत्र भक्षिताः Ks.<BR>—5 Thither, that way.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमुत्रभूयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रभूयम्
अमुत्र + -भूयम् Ved. Being in the other world; dying; अमुत्रभूयादधि<BR> यद् यमस्य बृहस्पतेरभिशस्तेरमुञ्चः Av. 7. 53. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रत्य
अमुत्रत्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to a future life, being of the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुथा
अमुथा <i>ind.</i> Thus, in that manner, like that; ˚अस् to be thus,<BR> euphemistically for ‘to fare very ill’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुया
अमुया <i>ind.</i> Ved. In that manner, thus and thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुर्हि
अमुर्हि <i>ind.</i> Then, at that time; यद्वा एतेऽमुर्ह्यघ्रियन्त तदेवाप्यद्य<BR> कुर्वन्ति Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुवत्
अमुवत् <i>ind.</i> Like a person or thing referred to without name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्य
अमुष्य (gen. of अदस्) Of such a one (in comp. only).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमुष्यकुल, अमुष्यपुत्रः, अमुष्यपुत्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यकुल
अमुष्य + -कुल <i>a.</i> [अलुक् स˚] belonging to the family of such a one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यकुलम्
अमुष्य + -कुल + .({@-लम्@}) a well-known family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यपुत्रः|अमुष्यपुत्र
अमुष्य + -पुत्रः, -पुत्री the son or daughter of such a one or of a good or<BR> well-known family or origin; see आमुष्यायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यपुत्री
अमुष्य + -पुत्रः, -पुत्री the son or daughter of such a one or of a good or<BR> well-known family or origin; see आमुष्यायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश्
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष <i>a.</i> (-शी, -क्षी <i>f.</i> cf. अन्यादृश)<BR> Such-like, such a one, of<BR> such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश|अमूदृशः
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष <i>a.</i> (-शी, -क्षी <i>f.</i> cf. अन्यादृश)<BR> Such-like, such a one, of<BR> such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृक्ष
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष <i>a.</i> (-शी, -क्षी <i>f.</i> cf. अन्यादृश)<BR> Such-like, such a one, of<BR> such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0203-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर
अमूर <i>a.</i> Ved. Not perplexed or bewildered, not ignorant, infallible.<BR> अर्धमर्धेन पयसा पृणक्ष्यर्धेन शुष्म वर्धसे अमूर Av. 5. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त <i>a.</i> Formless, shapeless, incorporeal, unembodied (opp.<BR> मूर्त where Muktā. says मूर्तत्वम् = अवच्छिन्नपरिमाणवत्त्वम्)<BR> द्वै वाव ब्रह्मणो रूपे मूर्त चामूर्त च Bṛ. Up. 2. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तः|अमूर्त|अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त + .{@-र्तः@} N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमूर्तगुणः, अमूर्तरजस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तगुणः|अमूर्तगुण|अमूर्त्तगुण
अमूर्त + -गुणः (in Vaiś. Phil.) a quality considered to be अमूर्त<BR> or incorporeal such as धर्म, अधर्म &c.; धर्माधर्मौ भावना च शब्दो<BR> बुद्ध्यादयोऽपि च । एते मूर्तगुणाः सर्वे Bhāṣā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तरजस्
अमूर्त + -रजस् A son of Kuśa (by Vaidarbhī); Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्ति|अमूर्तिः|अमूर्त्ति
अमूर्ति <i>a.</i> Formless, shapeless. कालो मूर्तिरमूर्तिमान् Maitr. Up. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तिः|अमूर्ति|अमूर्त्ति
अमूर्ति + .{@-र्तिः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तिः|अमूर्ति|अमूर्त्ति
अमूर्ति + .{@-र्तिः@} <i>f.</i> Shapelessness; (<i>m.</i> pl.) A class of Manes who<BR> have no definite form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तिमत्|अमूर्तिमन्त्|अमूर्त्तिमत्
अमूर्तिमत् <i>a.</i> Formless &c. ━<i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल, -लक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rootless (lit.); पशवोऽमूला ओषधयो ऽमूलिन्यः Śat. Br.; (fig.);<BR> without basis or support, baseless, groundless.<BR>—2 without authority; not being in the original; इहान्वयमुखेनैव सर्वं<BR> व्याख्यायते मया । नामूलं लिख्यते किंचित् Malli. Introduction of Ṭīkā on R.<BR>—3 without material cause, as the <i>Pradhāna</i> of the Sāṅkhyas; मूलं<BR> मूलाभावादमूलम्.<BR>—4 Not fixed in the earth, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूलक|अमूलकं
अमूल, -लक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rootless (lit.); पशवोऽमूला ओषधयो ऽमूलिन्यः Śat. Br.; (fig.);<BR> without basis or support, baseless, groundless.<BR>—2 without authority; not being in the original; इहान्वयमुखेनैव सर्वं<BR> व्याख्यायते मया । नामूलं लिख्यते किंचित् Malli. Introduction of Ṭīkā on R.<BR>—3 without material cause, as the <i>Pradhāna</i> of the Sāṅkhyas; मूलं<BR> मूलाभावादमूलम्.<BR>—4 Not fixed in the earth, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूला
अमूल, -लक + .{@-ला@} N. of a plant (अग्निशिखा, Mar. कळलावी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य <i>a.</i> Priceless, invaluable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृक्त
अमृक्त <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unhurt, unharmed, safe.<BR>—2 Unwashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृज
अमृज <i>a.</i> without toilet &c.; परिक्लिष्टैकवसनाममृजां राघवप्रियाम्<BR> (ददर्श) Rām. 6. 81. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणालम्
अमृणालम् [सादृश्ये नञ्] The root of a fragrant grass (वीरण,<BR> Mar. काळा वाळा) used for screens &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not dead; अमृते जारजः कुण्डः Ak.<BR>—2 Immortal; अपाम सोममृता अभूम Rv. 8. 48. 3; U. 1. 1. ब्रह्मणो<BR> हि प्रतिष्ठाहममृतस्याव्ययस्य च Bg. 14. 27.<BR>—3 Imperishable, Indestructible, eternal.<BR>—4 Causing immortality.<BR>—5 Beautiful, agreeable, desired. पाञ्चजन्याभिषिक्तश्च राजाऽमृतमुखोऽभवत्<BR> Mb. 12. 40. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतः|अमृत|अमृतं
अमृत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A god, an immortal, deity. आरुरोह यथा देवः सोमोऽमृतमयं रथम्<BR> Mb. 12. 37. 44.<BR>—2 N. of Dhanvantari, physician of the gods; also N. of Indra, of the<BR> sun, of Prajāpati, of the soul, Viṣṇu and Śiva.<BR>—3 N. of a plant (वनमुद्ग, Mar. मटकी)<BR>—4 N. of the root of a plant (वाराहीकन्द, Mar. डुकरकंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृता
अमृत + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—2 N. of various plants; <i>e. g.</i> आमलकी, हरीतकी, गुडूची, मागधी,<BR> तुलसी, इन्द्रवारुणी, ज्योतिष्मती, गोरक्षदुग्धा, अतिविषा, रक्तत्रिवृत्, दूर्वा,<BR> स्थूलमांसहरीतकी.<BR>—3 N. of one of the Nāḍīs in the body; नाडीनामुदयक्रमेण जगतः<BR> पञ्चामृताकर्षणात् Māl. 5. 2.<BR>—5 One of the rays of the sun; सौरीभिरिव नाडीभिरमृताख्याभिरम्मयः R. 10. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतम्
अमृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Immortality, imperishable state; न मृत्युरासीदमृतं न तर्हि<BR> Rv. 10. 129. 2; Ms. 22. 85.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Final beatitude, absolution; तपसा किल्बिषं हन्ति विद्ययामृतमश्नुते Ms. 12. 104;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">Page0204-2</a>]<BR> स श्रिये चामृताय च Ak.<BR>—2 The collective body of immortals.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The world of immortality, Paradise, Heaven; the power of eternity,<BR> immortal light, eternity.<BR>—4 Nectar of immortality, ambrosia, beverage of the gods (opp. विष)<BR> supposed to be churned out of the ocean; देवासुरैरमृतमम्बुनिधिर्ममन्थे<BR> Ki. 5. 30; विषादप्यमृतं ग्राह्यम् Ms. 2. 239; विषमप्यमृतं क्वचिद्भवेदमृतं<BR> वा विषमीश्वरेच्छया R. 8. 46; oft. used in combination with words like<BR> वाच्, वचनम्, वाणी &c.; कुमारजन्मामृतसंमिताक्षरम् R. 3. 16;<BR> आप्यायितोऽसौ वचनामृतेन Mb.; अमृतं शिशिरे वह्निरमृतं क्षीरभोजनम्<BR> Pt. 1. 128 the height of pleasure or gratification.<BR>—5 The Soma juice.<BR>—6 Antidote against poison.<BR>—7 The residue or leavings of a sacrifice (यज्ञशेष); विघसाशी<BR> भवेन्नित्यं नित्यं वाऽमृतभोजनः Ms. 3. 285.<BR>—8 Unsolicited alms, alms got without solicitation; मृतं स्याद्याचितं<BR> भैक्षममृतं स्यादयाचितम् Ms. 4. 4-5.<BR>—9 Water; मथितामृतफेनाभमरजोवस्त्रमुत्तमम् Rām. 5. 18. 24. अमृताध्मातजीमूत<BR> U. 6. 21; अमृतादुन्मथ्यमानात् K. 136; cf. also the formulas अमृतोपस्तरणमसि<BR> स्वाहा and अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा; Mahānār. Up. 7 and 10; repeated<BR> by Brāhmaṇas at the time of sipping water before the commencement and<BR> at the end of meals.<BR>—10 A drug.<BR>—11 Clarified butter; अमृतं नाम यत् सन्तो मन्त्रजिह्वेषु जुह्वति Śi. 2. 107.<BR>—12 Milk; अमृतं च सुधा चैव सुधा चैवामृतं तथा Mb. 13. 67. 12.<BR>—13 Food in general.<BR>—14 Boiled rice.<BR>—15 Anything sweet, anything lovely or charming; a sweetmeat. यथामृतघटं<BR> दंशा मकरा इव चार्णवम् Rām. 7. 7. 3.<BR>—16 Property.<BR>—17 Gold.<BR>—18 Quicksilver.<BR>—19 Poison.<BR>—20 The poison called वत्सनाभ.<BR>—21 The Supreme Spirit (ब्रह्मन्).<BR>—22 N. of sacred place.<BR>—23 N. of particular conjunctions of <i>Nakṣatras</i> (lunar asterisms)<BR> with week days (वारनक्षत्रयोग) or of lunar days with week days<BR> (तिथिवारयोग).<BR>—24 The number four.<BR>—25 splendour, light. [cf. Gr. <i>ambrotos, ambrosia</i>; L. <i>immortalis</i>].<BR> cf. अमृतं वारि सुरयोर्निर्वाणे चातिसुन्दरे । अयाचिते यज्ञशेषे पुंसि<BR> धन्वन्तरेऽपि च । पीयूषे च धृते दीप्तावाचार्ये विबुधेऽपि च । हरीतक्यामामलक्यां<BR> गलूच्यामपि तत्स्त्रियाम् । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमृतांशुः, अमृतकरः, अमृतदीधितिः, अमृतद्युतिः, अमृतरश्मिः, अमृतांशुकः, अमृताक्षर, अमृताग्रभूः, अमृतान्धस्, अमृताशनः, अमृताशिन्, अमृतापिधानम्, अमृतासु, अमृताशः, अमृतासङ्गः, अमृताहरणः, अमृतेष्टका, अमृतेशः, अमृतेश्वरः, अमृतोत्पन्ना, अमृतोपस्तरणम्, अमृतौदनः, अमृतकरः, अमृतकिरणः, अमृतकुण्डम्, अमृतक्षारम्, अमृतगतिः, अमृतगर्भ, अमृतचितिः, अमृतज, अमृतजटा, अमृततरङ्गिणी, अमृततिलका, अमृतद्रव, अमृतधार, अमृतनन्दनः, अमृतनादोपनिषद्, अमृतपः, अमृतपक्षः, अमृतफलः, अमृतबन्धुः, अमृतबिन्दूपनिषद्, अमृतभल्लातकी, अमृतभवनम्, अमृतभुज्, अमृतभू, अमृतमति, अमृतमन्थनम्, अमृतमालिनी, अमृतमूर्तिः, अमृतयोगः, अमृतरसः, अमृतलता, अमृतलतिका, अमृतवाक, अमृतसंयावम्, अमृतसार, अमृतसूः, अमृतसूतिः, अमृतसोदरः, अमृतस्रवः, अमृतस्रुत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतांशुः|अमृतांशु
अमृत + -अंशुः, -करः, -दीधितिः, -द्युतिः, -रश्मिः &c. epithets of the<BR> moon; अमृतदीधितिरेष विदर्भजे N. 4. 104; अमृतांशूद्भव born<BR> from the moon; ‘from whom was born the moon’, N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

