अमृत + -अंशुकः An interior variety of gems having white rays, Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताक्षर
अमृत + -अक्षर <i>a.</i> immortal and imperishable; क्षरं प्रधानममृताक्षरं<BR> हरः Śvet. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताग्रभूः
अमृत + -अग्रभूः N. of the horse of Indra (उच्चैःश्रवस्); अमृताग्रभुवः<BR> पुरेव पुच्छम् Śi. 20. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतान्धस्
अमृत + -अन्धस्, -अशनः, -आशिन् <i>m.</i> ‘one whose food is nectar’; a god, an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताशनः|अमृताशन
अमृत + -अन्धस्, -अशनः, -आशिन् <i>m.</i> ‘one whose food is nectar’; a god, an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताशिन्
अमृत + -अन्धस्, -अशनः, -आशिन् <i>m.</i> ‘one whose food is nectar’; a god, an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतापिधानम्
अमृत + -अपिधानम् Water sipped after eating nectar-like food so as to<BR> overlay it like a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतासु
अमृत + -असु <i>a.</i> whose soul is immortal; अमृतासुर्वर्धमानः सुजन्मा Av. 5. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताशः|अमृताश
अमृत + -आशः<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a god; इदं कार्यममृताशाः शृणोमि Mb. 12. 299. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतासङ्गः|अमृतासङ्ग|अमृतासङ्गं
अमृत + -आसङ्गः a sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताहरणः|अमृताहरण
अमृत + -आहरणः N. of Garuḍa who once stole Amṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतेष्टका
अमृत + -इष्टका a kind of sacrificial brick shaped like the golden head<BR> of men, beasts &c. (पशुशीर्षाणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतेशः|अमृतेश
अमृत + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतेश्वरः|अमृतेश्वर
अमृत + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

