अमृत + -गतिः N. of a metre consisting of 40 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतगर्भ|अमृतगर्भः
अमृत + -गर्भ <i>a.</i> filled with water or nectar; ambrosial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतगर्भः|अमृतगर्भ
अमृत + -गर्भ + .({@-र्भः@})<BR>—1 the individual soul.<BR>—2 the Supreme Soul.<BR>—3 child of immortality (said of sleep); देवानाममृतगर्भोऽसि स्वप्न Av. 6. 46. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतचितिः|अमृतचिति
अमृत + -चितिः <i>f.</i> an arrangement or accumulation of sacrificial bricks<BR> conferring immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतज|अमृतजः
अमृत + -ज <i>a.</i> produced by or from nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतजः|अमृतज
अमृत + -ज + .({@-जः@}) a sort of plant, Yellow Myrobalan (Mar. हिरडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतजटा
अमृत + -जटा N. of a plant (जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृततरङ्गिणी|अमृततरंगिणी
अमृत + -तरङ्गिणी moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृततिलका
अमृत + -तिलका N. of a metre of 4 lines, also called त्वरितगति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतद्रव|अमृतद्रवः
अमृत + -द्रव <i>a.</i> shedding nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतद्रवः|अमृतद्रव
अमृत + -द्रव + .({@-वः@}) flow of nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतधार
अमृत + -धार <i>a.</i> shedding nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतधारा
अमृत + -धार + .({@-रा@})<BR>—1 N. of a metre.<BR>—2 flow of nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतनन्दनः
अमृत + -नन्दनः A pavilion with 58 pillars (Matsya P. 270. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतनादोपनिषद्
अमृत + -नादोपनिषद् <i>f.</i> ‘The sound of immortality’, Name of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतपः|अमृतप
अमृत + -पः<BR>—1 a drinker of nectar’ a god or deity.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 One who drinks wine; ध्रुवममृतपनामवाञ्छयासावधरममुं मधुपस्तवाजिहीते<BR> Śi. 7. 42 (where अ˚ has sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतपक्षः|अमृतपक्ष
अमृत + -पक्षः<BR>—1 having golden or immortal wings, a sort of hawk.<BR>—2 the immortal or golden wings of sacrificial fire.<BR>—3 fire itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतफलः|अमृतफल|अमृतफलं
अमृत + -फलः N. of two trees पटोल and पारावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतफला
अमृत + -फलः + .({@-ला@})<BR>—1 a bunch of grapes, vine plant, a grape (द्राक्षा)<BR>—2 = आमलकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतफलम्
अमृत + -फलः + .({@-लम्@}) a sort of fruit (रुचिफल) found in the country of<BR> the Mudgalas according to Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतबन्धुः|अमृतबन्धु
अमृत + -बन्धुः Ved.<BR>—1 a god or deity in general.<BR>—2 a horse or the moon.<BR>—3 A friend or keeper of immortality; तां देवा अन्वजायन्त भद्रा अमृतबन्धवः Rv. 10. 72. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतबिन्दूपनिषद्
अमृत + -बिन्दूपनिषद् <i>f.</i> ‘drop of nectar’, N. of an Upaniṣad of<BR> the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतभल्लातकी
अमृत + -भल्लातकी a sort of medicinal preparation of ghee mentioned by Cakradatta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतभवनम्
अमृत + -भवनम् N. of a monastery (built by Amṛtaprabhā); Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतभुज्
अमृत + -भुज् <i>m.</i> an immortal, a god, deity; one who tastes the sacrificial residues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतभू
अमृत + -भू <i>a.</i> free from birth and death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमति
अमृत + -मति = ˚गति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमन्थनम्
अमृत + -मन्थनम्<BR>—1 churning (of the ocean) for nectar.<BR>—2 N. of the chapters 17 to 19 of Mb. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमालिनी
अमृत + -मालिनी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमूर्तिः|अमृतमूर्ति
अमृत + -मूर्तिः The moon; आप्याययत्यसौ लोकं वदनामृतमूर्तिना Bhāg. 4. 16. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतयोगः|अमृतयोग
अमृत + -योगः see under अमृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतरसः|अमृतरस
अमृत + -रसः<BR>—1 nectar, ambrosia; काव्यामृतरसास्वादः H. 1; विविधकाव्यामृतरसान्<BR> पिबामः Bh. 3. 40.<BR>—2 the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतरसा
अमृत + -रसः + .({@-सा@})<BR>—1 dark-coloured grapes.<BR>—2 a sort of cake (Mar. अनर्सा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतलता
अमृत + -लता, -लतिका a nectar-giving creeping plant (गुडूची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतलतिका
अमृत + -लता, -लतिका a nectar-giving creeping plant (गुडूची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतवाक
अमृत + -वाक <i>a.</i> producing nectar like sweet words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसंयावम्
अमृत + -संयावम् a sort of dish mentioned in Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसार|अमृतसारः
अमृत + -सार <i>a.</i> ambrosial; ˚राणि प्रज्ञानानि U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसारः|अमृतसार
अमृत + -सार + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 clarified butter.<BR>—2 a sort of अयःपाक. ˚जः raw sugar, molasses (गुड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसूः
अमृत + -सूः, -सूतिः<BR>—1 the moon (distilling nectar).<BR>—2 mother of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसूतिः
अमृत + -सूः, -सूतिः<BR>—1 the moon (distilling nectar).<BR>—2 mother of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसोदरः|अमृतसोदर
अमृत + -सोदरः<BR>—1 ‘brother of nectar’, the horse called उच्चैःश्रवस्.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">Page0205-2</a>]<BR>—2 a horse in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रवः
अमृत + -स्रवः flow of nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रवा
अमृत + -स्रवः + .({@-वा@}) N. of a plant and tree (रुदन्ती-रुद्रवन्ती; Mar. रानहरभरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रुत्
अमृत + -स्रुत् <i>a.</i> shedding or distilling nectar; स्वरेण तस्याममृतस्रुतेव Ku. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतता
अमृतता, -त्वम्<BR> Immortality; उतामृतत्वस्येशानो यदन्नेनातिरोहति Rv. 10. 90. 2;<BR> अहिंसया च भूतानाममृतत्वाय कल्पते Ms. 6. 60; Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतत्वम्
अमृतता, -त्वम्<BR> Immortality; उतामृतत्वस्येशानो यदन्नेनातिरोहति Rv. 10. 90. 2;<BR> अहिंसया च भूतानाममृतत्वाय कल्पते Ms. 6. 60; Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमय
अमृतमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Consisting of nectar, ambrosial, full of nectar. तेजोमयोऽमृतमयः<BR> पुरुषः Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 1.<BR>—2 Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतकम्
अमृतकम् The nectar of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताफलम्
अमृताफलम् The fruit of the Trichosanthes (पटोलफल Mar. पडवळ, चिकार्डें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतायते
अमृतायते Den. Ā. To be like nectar; उत्तिष्ठ वत्सेत्यमृतायमानं<BR> वचो निशम्य R. 2. 61; अमृतायते हि सुतपः सुकर्मणाम् Ki. 12. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतेशयः|अमृतेशय
अमृतेशयः N. of Viṣṇu (sleeping in waters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्यु|अमृत्युः
अमृत्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Immortal; causing immortality. तन्म ऋतवोऽमृत्यव आभरध्वम् Kauś. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्युः|अमृत्यु
अमृत्यु + .{@-त्युः@} Not death, immortality.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृध्र
अमृध्र <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unassailable, invulnerable.<BR>—2 Unremitting, unceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृषा
अमृषा <i>ind.</i> Not falsely, truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृषोद्यम्
अमृषोद्यम् True speech; अमृषोद्यं वदन् रुच्यो जगाहे द्यां निशाचरः Bk. 6. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्ट
अमृष्ट <i>a.</i> Unrubbed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमृष्टभोजिन्, अमृष्टमृज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्टभोजिन्
अमृष्ट + -भोजिन् <i>a.</i> Not eating delicate food or dainties; Rām. 1. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्टमृज
अमृष्ट + -मृज <i>a.</i> of unimpaired purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेदस्क
अमेदस्क <i>a.</i> Fatless, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेधस्
अमेधस् <i>a.</i> [अ-मेधा; नित्यमसिच् P. V. 4. 122] Foolish, stupid, an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अमेध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not able or allowed to sacrifice.<BR>—2 Unfit for a sacrifice; नामेध्यं प्रक्षिपेदग्नौ Ms. 4. 53, 56, 5. 5, 132.<BR>—3 Unholy, filthy, foul, dirty, impure; उच्छिष्टमपि चामेध्यं भोजनं<BR> तामसप्रियम् Bg. 17. 10; Bh. 3. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यम्
अमेध्य + .{@-ध्यम्@}<BR>—1 Excrement, ordure; समुत्सृजेद्राजमार्गे यस्त्वमेध्यमनापदि Ms. 9. 282, 5. 126, 128, 12. 71.<BR>—2 An unlucky or inauspicious omen, अमेध्यं दृष्ट्वा सूर्यमुपतिष्ठेत Kāty.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमेध्यकुणपाशिन्, अमेध्ययुक्त, अमेध्यलिप्त, अमेध्यलेपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यकुणपाशिन्
अमेध्य + -कुणपाशिन् <i>a.</i> feeding on carrion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्ययुक्त
अमेध्य + -युक्त, -लिप्त <i>a.</i> smeared with ordure, foul, defiled, dirty; Ms. 4. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलिप्त
अमेध्य + -युक्त, -लिप्त <i>a.</i> smeared with ordure, foul, defiled, dirty; Ms. 4. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलेपः|अमेध्यलेप
अमेध्य + -लेपः smearing with ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेन
अमेन Ved.<BR>—1 Having no wife, a widower. न हि त्वदिन्द्र वस्यो अन्यदस्त्यमेनाँश्चिज्जनिवतश्चकर्थ Rv. 5. 31. 2.<BR>—2 Not injuring or hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेय
अमेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 immeasurable, boundless, अमेयो मितलोकस्त्वम् R. 10. 18.<BR>—2 Unknowable.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमेयात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेयात्मन्
अमेय + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> possessing an immeasurable soul, magnanimous, large-minded.<BR> ━<i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेष्ट
अमेष्ट <i>a.</i> [अमा-इष्ट] Ved. Sacrificed at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्य
अमोक्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not to be unloosened; सिनात्वेनान्निरृतिर्मृत्योः<BR> पाशैरमोक्यैः Av. 3. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचनम्
अमोचनम् Not loosening or letting go, non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचनीय
अमोचनीय, -अमोच्य <i>a.</i><BR> Not to be liberated; अमोच्यमश्वं यदि मन्यसे<BR> प्रभो R. 3. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोच्य
अमोचनीय, -अमोच्य <i>a.</i><BR> Not to be liberated; अमोच्यमश्वं यदि मन्यसे<BR> प्रभो R. 3. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्ष|अमोक्षः
अमोक्ष <i>a.</i> Not liberated, unloosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्षः|अमोक्ष
अमोक्ष + .{@-क्षः@}<BR>—1 Bondage, confinement.<BR>—2 Non-liberation from worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्षयत्
अमोक्षयत् <i>a.</i> Not liberating; शक्तोऽप्यमोक्षयन्स्वामी Y. 2. 300.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unfailing, reaching the mark; धनुष्यमोघं समधत्त बाणम् Ku. 3. 66;<BR> R. 3. 53, 12. 97; कामिलक्ष्येष्वमोघैः Me. 75.<BR>—2 Unerring, infallible (words, boon &c.); अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णन्तावर्घ्यानुपदमाशिषः<BR> R. 1. 44; युतममोघतया Ki. 6. 40.<BR>—3 Not vain or useless, efficacious, fruitful, productive; यदमोघमपामन्तरुप्तं<BR> बीजमज त्वया Ku. 2. 5; so ˚बलम्, ˚शक्ति, ˚वीर्य, ˚क्रोध &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघः|अमोघ
अमोघ + .{@-घः@}<BR>—1 Not failing or erring, unerringness.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu (or of Śiva according to some).<BR>—3 N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघा
अमोघ + .{@-घा@}<BR>—1 N. of the plant पाटली (Mar. पाडळी) (the trumpet flower).<BR>—2 N. of another plant विडङ्ग (Mar. वावडिंग) the seed of which<BR> is used as a vermifuge, and hence also called कृमिघ्न.<BR>—3 = पथ्या.<BR>—4 N. of a spear or शक्ति.<BR>—5 N. of Śivaʼs wife.<BR>—6 Mystical name of the conjunct consonant क्ष.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अमोघाक्षी, अमोघदण्डः, अमोघदर्शिन्, अमोघदृष्टि, अमोघनन्दिनी, अमोघपाशः, अमोघबल, अमोघभूतिः, अमोघराजः, अमोघवर्षः, अमोघवाच्, अमोघवाञ्छित, अमोघविक्रमः, अमोघसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघाक्षी
अमोघ + -अक्षी <i>f.</i> N. of Dākṣāyaṇī, Matsya P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघदण्डः|अमोघदण्ड
अमोघ + -दण्डः ‘unerring in punishment’, N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघदर्शिन्
अमोघ + -दर्शिन्, -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> ‘of unerring mind or view’, N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघदृष्टि
अमोघ + -दर्शिन्, -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> ‘of unerring mind or view’, N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघनन्दिनी
अमोघ + -नन्दिनी N. of a Śikṣā-text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघपाशः|अमोघपाश
अमोघ + -पाशः N. of a Lokeśvara (Buddhistic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघबल
अमोघ + -बल <i>a.</i> of never-failing strength or vigour. (उच्चैःश्रवस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघभूतिः|अमोघभूति
अमोघ + -भूतिः N. of a king of the Punjab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघराजः|अमोघराज
अमोघ + -राजः N. of a Bhikṣu; L. V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघवर्षः|अमोघवर्ष
अमोघ + -वर्षः N. of a Cālukya^1 prince.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552. note: [-varzaH].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघवाच्
अमोघ + -वाच् <i>f.</i> words not vain or idle, that are sure to be fulfilled<BR> or realized. <i>a.</i> one whose words are not vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघवाञ्छित
अमोघ + -वाञ्छित <i>a.</i> never disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघविक्रमः|अमोघविक्रम
अमोघ + -विक्रमः of neverfailing valour; N. of Siva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघसिद्धिः|अमोघसिद्धि
अमोघ + -सिद्धिः N. of the fifth Dhyānibuddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोत
अमोत <i>a.</i> [अमा-उत] Ved. The hems or skirts of which are not<BR> cut; woven at home, taken care of or protected at home; ˚पुत्रका a<BR> maiden protected at home. cf. Av. 20. 127. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोतकः|अमोतक
अमोतकः<BR>—1 One protected at home (as a child).<BR>—2 A weaver (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमौनम्
अमौनम्<BR>—1 Non-silence.<BR>—2 Knowledge of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्नस्
अम्नस् <i>ind.</i> Ved. (स् being changed to र् by P. VIII. 2. 70)<BR>—1 Unawares, quickly. अम्नो जातान् मारयन्ति Av. 8. 6. 19.<BR>—2 At present.<BR>—3 A little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्|अंब्
अम्ब् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बः|अम्ब|अंब|अंबः
अम्बः<BR>—1 A father.<BR>—2 Sound; the Veda.<BR>—3 One who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बः + .{@-म्बा@} see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बम्
अम्बः + .{@-म्बम्@}<BR>—1 The eye.<BR>—2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब|अंब|अंबः|अम्बः
अम्बः + .{@-म्ब@} <i>ind.</i> A particle of affirmation; ‘well, well now’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बकम्
अम्बकम्<BR>—1 An eye (in त्र्यम्बक).<BR>—2 A father.<BR>—3 Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बया|अंबया
अम्बया Ved. A mother; good woman (as a courteous mode of address).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरम्
अम्बरम् [अम्बः शब्दः तं राति धत्ते, रा-क]<BR>—1 Sky, atmosphere, ether; कैलासनिलयप्रख्यमालिखन्तमिवाम्बरम् Rām. 5. 2. 23.<BR> तावतर्जयदम्बरे R. 12. 41.<BR>—2 Cloth, garment, clothing, apparel, dress; दिव्यमाल्याम्बरधरम्<BR> Bg. 11. 11; R. 3. 9. दिगम्बर; सागराम्बरा मही the sea, girt, earth.<BR>—3 Saffron.<BR>—4 Talc.<BR>—5 A kind of perfume (Ambergris).<BR>—6 Cotton. cf. अंबरं व्योम्नि वाससि । सुगन्धिनि च कार्पासे … ।<BR> Rāghavaʼs Nānārtha.<BR>—7 N. of a people.<BR>—8 Circumference, compass.<BR>—9 Neighbourhood, surrounding country (Nir.) यद् वा स्थो अध्यम्बरे Rv. 8. 8. 14<BR>—10 Lip.<BR>—11 Evil, sin.<BR>—12 Destroyer of elephants (नागभिद् Trik.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अम्बराधिकारिन्, अम्बरान्तः, अम्बरौकस्, अम्बरग, अम्बरदम्, अम्बरमणिः, अम्बरयुगम्, अम्बरलेखिन्, अम्बरशैलः, अम्बरस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बराधिकारिन्
अम्बरम् + -अधिकारिन् Superintendent over the robes (an officer at court). Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरान्तः|अम्बरान्त|अंबरान्त
अम्बरम् + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the end of a garment.<BR>—2 the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरौकस्|अंबरौकस्
अम्बरम् + -ओकस् <i>m.</i> dwelling in heaven, a god; (भस्मरजः) विलिप्यते<BR> मौलिभिरम्बरौकसाम् Ku. 5. 79<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरग
अम्बरम् + -ग <i>a.</i> sky-going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरदम्
अम्बरम् + -दम् cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरमणिः|अम्बरमणि
अम्बरम् + -मणिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरयुगम्
अम्बरम् + -युगम् two principal garments used by men; upper and lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरलेखिन्
अम्बरम् + -लेखिन् <i>a.</i> sky-touching; एतद्गिरेर्माल्यवतः पुरस्तादाविर्भवत्यम्बरलेखि<BR> शृङ्गम् R. 13. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरशैलः|अम्बरशैल
अम्बरम् + -शैलः a high mountain touching the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरस्थली
अम्बरम् + -स्थली the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर्यति
अम्बर्यति Den. P. To bring together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरीषम्
अम्बरीषम् [In some senses अम्बरीषः also; ˚षः only by Uṇ. 4. 29.<BR> क्लीबेम्बरीषं भ्राष्ट्रो ना Ak.]<BR>—1 A frying-pan ‘अम्बरीषो भवेद् भ्राष्ट्र’ इति विश्वः । अम्बरीषोपमम्<BR> दीप्तं विधूम इव पावकः Rām. 4. 67. 7.<BR>—2 Regret, remorse.<BR>—3 War, battle.<BR>—4 One of the hells (Jaina.).<BR>—5 A young animal, colt.<BR>—6 The sun. Rām. 5.<BR>—7 The hog-plum plant (आम्रातकम्, Mar. अंबाडा)<BR>—8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—9 N. of Śiva.<BR>—10 N. of a king of the solar race who was celebrated as a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR>—11 N. of a Vedic king and seer; Rv. 1. 100. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरीषकः|अम्बरीषक
अम्बरीषकः Latent or concealed fire; उदपानाः कुरुश्रेष्ठ तथैवाप्यम्बरीषकाः Mb. 3. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठः|अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अंबष्ठः
अम्बष्ठः<BR>—1 The offspring of a man of the Brāhmaṇa and a woman of the Vaiśya<BR> tribe; ब्राह्मणाद् वैश्यकन्यायामम्बष्ठो नाम जायते Ms. 10. 8, 13. 15;<BR> Y. 1. 91. cf. also अम्बष्ठानां दार्विहोमिको ब्राह्मणः । ŚB. on MS. 8. 4. 2.<BR> (According to Ms. 10. 47 the duty of an अम्बष्ठ is the curing<BR> of diseases; अम्बष्ठानां चिकित्सितम्).<BR>—2 An elephant-driver. अपश्यत्कुवलयापीडं कृष्णोऽम्बष्ठप्रचोदितम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 43. 2. (pl.)<BR>—3 N. of a country and its inhabitants (they seem to have occupied the<BR> country to the east of Tākṣaśilā, comprising the modern district of Lahore.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठा
अम्बष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठा@} N. of several plants:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) गणिका, यूथिका (Mar. जुई);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">Page0207-1</a>]<BR>——(<i>b</i>) पाठा (Mar. पाहाडमूळ).<BR>——(<i>c</i>) चुक्रिका (Mar. चुका);<BR>——(<i>d</i>) another plant (Mar. अंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठा
अम्बष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठा, -ष्ठी@} An Ambaṣṭha woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठी
अम्बष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठा, -ष्ठी@} An Ambaṣṭha woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठकी|अंबष्ठकी
अम्बष्ठकी = अम्बष्ठा (पाठा) see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठिका|अंबष्ठिका
अम्बष्ठिका N. of a plant (ब्राह्मी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बा [अम्ब्-घञ्] (Voc. अम्बे Ved.; अम्ब in later Sanskṛt)<BR>—1 A mother; also used as an affectionate or respectful mode of address;<BR> ‘good woman’, ‘good mother’; किमम्बाभिः प्रेषितः; अम्बानां कार्यं निर्वर्तय<BR> Ś. 2; कृताञ्जलिस्तत्र यदम्ब सत्यात् R. 14. 16.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (अम्बष्ठा <i>d</i>).<BR>—3 N. of Durgā, wife of Śiva.<BR>—4 N. of an Apsaras; of a sister of Pāṇḍuʼs mother, a daughter of Kāśīrāja.<BR> [She and her two sisters were carried off by Bhīṣma to be the wives<BR> of Vicitravīrya who had no issue. Ambā, however, had been previously<BR> betrothed to a king of Śālva and Bhīṣma sent her to him; but the latter<BR> rejected her because she had been in another manʼs house. So she came<BR> back to Bhīṣma and prayed him to accept her; but he could not break his<BR> vow of life-long celibacy, and being enraged she returned to the forest<BR> and practised austere penance to revenge herself on Bhīṣma. Śiva favoured<BR> her and promised her the desired vengeance in another birth. Afterwards<BR> she was born as Śikhaṇḍin^1ī, daughter of Drupada, who came to be called<BR> Śikhaṇḍin^2 and became the cause of Bhīṣmaʼs death.]<BR>—5 A term in astrology to denote the fourth condition. [cf. Dravid. <i>Amma</i>;<BR> Germ. <i>Amme</i>; Old Germ. <i>Amma</i>].<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बाडा|अंबाडा
अम्बाडा (Ved. -ला)<BR> A mother; P. VI. 1. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बाला
अम्बाडा (Ved. -ला)<BR> A mother; P. VI. 1. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बायुः|अम्बायु|अंबायुः
अम्बायुः <i>f.</i> A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बालिका|अंबालिका
अम्बालिका<BR>—1 A mother; good woman (as a term of respect or endearment.)<BR>—2 N. of a plant (Mar. अंबाडा).<BR>—3 N. of the youngest daughter of Kāśīrāja, wife of Vicitravīrya^1.<BR> She became the mother of Pāṇḍu by Vyāsa who was invoked by Satyavatī<BR> to beget a son to Vicitravīrya^2 who had died without issue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: 8 others also changed.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: 8 others also changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिः|अम्बि|अंबिः
अम्बिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Water; woman; nurse; mother; अम्बयो यन्त्यध्वभिर्जामयो<BR> अध्वरीयताम् Rv. 1. 23. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिका|अंबिका
अम्बिका<BR>—1 A mother, good woman, also used like अम्बा as a term of respect<BR> or endearment; अत्तिके अम्बिके शृणु मम विज्ञप्तिम् Mk. 1.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (अम्बा 2); N. of another plant कटुकी.<BR>—3 N. of Pārvatī, wife of Śiva; आशीर्भिरेधयामासुः पुरः पाकाभिरम्बिकाम् Ku. 6. 90.<BR>—4 N. of the middle daughter of Kāśīrāja and the eldest wife of Vicitravīrya.<BR> Like her youngest sister she had no progeny, and Vyāsa begot on her a<BR> son named धृतराष्ट्र.<BR>—5 Name of a Jaina deity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अम्बिकापतिः, अम्बिकाभर्ता, अम्बिकापुत्रः, अम्बिकासुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकापतिः|अम्बिकापति
अम्बिका + -पतिः, -भर्ता N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकाभर्ता
अम्बिका + -पतिः, -भर्ता N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकापुत्रः|अम्बिकापुत्र
अम्बिका + -पुत्रः, -सुतः N. of धृतराष्ट्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकासुतः|अम्बिकासुत
अम्बिका + -पुत्रः, -सुतः N. of धृतराष्ट्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेयः|अम्बिकेय|अंबिकेय|अंबिकेयः
अम्बिकेयः, -यकः<BR> N. of Gaṇeśa, Kārttikeya or Dhṛtarāṣṭra; प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्तप्यमानोऽम्बिकेयः<BR> Mb. 3. 4. 1; more correctly written आम्बिकेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेयकः|अम्बिकेयक|अंबिकेयकः
अम्बिकेयः, -यकः<BR> N. of Gaṇeśa, Kārttikeya or Dhṛtarāṣṭra; प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्तप्यमानोऽम्बिकेयः<BR> Mb. 3. 4. 1; more correctly written आम्बिकेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बु|अंबु
अम्बु <i>n.</i> [अम्ब्-शब्दे उण्]<BR>—1 Water; गाङ्गमम्बु सितमम्बु यामुनम् K. P. 10.<BR>—2 The watery element of the blood (cf. <i>imber</i>).<BR>—3 N. of a metre.<BR>—4 A term in astrology (लग्नावधिकं चतुर्थस्थानम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अम्बुकणः, अम्बुकण्टकः, अम्बुकन्दः, अम्बुकिरातः, अम्बुकीशः, अम्बुकूर्मः, अम्बुकेशरः, अम्बुक्रिया, अम्बुकुक्कुटी, अम्बुग, अम्बुचर, अम्बुचारिन्, अम्बुघनः, अम्बुचत्वरम्, अम्बुचामरम्, अम्बुज, अम्बुजन्मन्, अम्बुतस्करः, अम्बुतालः, अम्बुद, अम्बुदेवम्, अम्बुदैवम्, अम्बुधर, अम्बुधिः, अम्बुधिस्रवा, अम्बुनाथः, अम्बुनामन्, अम्बुनिधिः, अम्बुप, अम्बुपतिः, अम्बुपत्रा, अम्बुपद्धतिः, अम्बुप्रसादः, अम्बुप्रसादनम्, अम्बुभवम्, अम्बुभृत्, अम्बुमात्रज, अम्बुमुच्, अम्बुराजः, अम्बुराशिः, अम्बुरुह्, अम्बुरुहः, अम्बुरुहम्, अम्बुरोहिणी, अम्बुवाची, अम्बुवासिनी, अम्बुवासी, अम्बुवाहः, अम्बुवाहिन्, अम्बुविहारः, अम्बुविस्रवा, अम्बुवेग, अम्बुवेतसः, अम्बुशिरीषिका, अम्बुसरणम्, अम्बुसर्पिणी, अम्बुसेचनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकणः|अम्बुकण
अम्बु + -कणः a drop of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकण्टकः|अम्बुकण्टक
अम्बु + -कण्टकः (short-nosed), alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकन्दः|अम्बुकन्द
अम्बु + -कन्दः An acquatic plant Trapa bispinosa (Mar. शिंगाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकिरातः|अम्बुकिरात
अम्बु + -किरातः alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकीशः|अम्बुकीश
अम्बु + -कीशः, -कूर्मः a tortoise (शिशुमार); particularly Gangetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकूर्मः|अम्बुकूर्म|अम्बुकूर्म्म|अम्बुकूर्म्मः
अम्बु + -कीशः, -कूर्मः a tortoise (शिशुमार); particularly Gangetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकेशरः|अम्बुकेशर
अम्बु + -केशरः lemon-tree (छालङ्गवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

