अयुज
अयुज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no equal or companion. अयुजो असमो नृभिरेकः Rv. 8. 62. 2.<BR>—2 Separate, single, odd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disjoined, detached, not connected.<BR>—2 Uninterrupted, undisturbed. Av. 19. 51. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतम्
अयुत + .{@-तम्@} Ten thousand, a myriad. सूर्याब्धिसंख्यया द्वित्रिसागरैरयुताहतैः<BR> Sūrya S. शाखानामयुतम्<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अयुताध्यापकः, अयुतता, अयुतजित्, अयुतनायिन्, अयुतसिद्ध, अयुतसिद्धिः, अयुतहोम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुताध्यापकः|अयुताध्यापक
अयुत + -अध्यापकः a good teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतता
अयुत + -ता, -जित् Name of a king (son of Sindhudvīpa and father of Ṛtuparṇa)<BR> Bṛ. Up. N. of another king (son of Bhajamāna); V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतजित्
अयुत + -ता, -जित् Name of a king (son of Sindhudvīpa and father of Ṛtuparṇa)<BR> Bṛ. Up. N. of another king (son of Bhajamāna); V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतनायिन्
अयुत + -नायिन् N. of a king in the Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतसिद्ध
अयुत + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> (in Vaiś. Phil.) proved to be inseparable and inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतसिद्धिः|अयुतसिद्धि
अयुत + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> proof that certain things or notions are inseparable and inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुतहोम
अयुत + -होम a kind of sacrifice. B. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अयुद्ध <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not fighting.<BR>—2 Unconquered, irresistible. अयुद्ध इद् युधा वृतम् Rv. 8. 45. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्धम्
अयुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} Absence of fighting or war.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अयुद्धसेन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्धसेन
अयुद्ध + -सेन <i>a.</i> of unconquerable armies (or arrows), irresistible.<BR> अयुद्धसेनो विभ्वा विभिन्दता Rv. 10. 138. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध्वी
अयुद्ध्वी^1 <i>ind.</i> Without fighting.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf. other dictionaries; Vedic..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुधः|अयुध
अयुधः A non-combatant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुध्य
अयुध्य <i>a.</i> Unconquerable, irresistible दुश्च्यवनः पृतनाषाळयुध्यो<BR> Rv. 10. 103. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुव
अयुव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undisturbed, unshaken.<BR>—2 Unconnected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुवमारिन्
अयुवमारिन् <i>a.</i> Where no young people die. Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a vocative particle, or as a kind of gentle address. (= अयि);<BR> अये गौरीनाथ त्रिपुरहर शम्भो त्रिनयन Bh. 3. 123.<BR>—2 An interjection showing<BR>——(<i>a</i>) ‘surprise’ or ‘wonder’ and translated by ‘oh’, ‘ah’, अये मातलिः<BR> Ś. 6; अये कुमारलक्ष्मणः प्राप्तः U. 1; अये मय्येव भ्रुकुटीधरः<BR> संवृत्तः U. 5;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) ‘grief’, ‘dejection’; अये देवपादपद्मोपजीविनोऽवस्थेयम् Mu. 2. (alas!);<BR>——(<i>c</i>) ‘anger’ अये अश्वमेध इति विश्वविजयिनां क्षत्रियाणां महानुत्कर्षनिकषः U. 4;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) ‘fear’, ‘flurry’, ‘agitation’;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) ‘recollection’;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) ‘fear’;<BR>——(<i>g</i>) ‘fatigue’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अयोग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unconnected with.<BR>—2 Indistinctly connected.<BR>—3 Making vigorous efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगः|अयोग
अयोग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Separation, disjunction, interval.<BR>—2 Unfitness, impropriety, incongruity.<BR>—3 An improper conjunction.<BR>—4 Inefficacy of a remedy or medicine (as of a purgative or emetic).<BR>—5 Strong or vigorous effort.<BR>—6 Medical treatment against the symptoms.<BR>—7 Non-application or misapplication of remedies.<BR>—8 A sort of disease (cured by prescribing emetics).<BR>—9 A widower; absent lover or husband (विधुर).<BR>—10 A hammer (for अयोग्र, अयोघन).<BR>—11 Dislike.<BR>—12 A conjunction of two planets (also inauspicious).<BR>—13 Falling from the practice of Yoga; दत्तस्त्वयोगादथ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">Page0213-1</a>]<BR> योगनाथः Bhāg. 6. 8. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अयोगवाहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगवाहः|अयोगवाह
अयोग + -वाहः a term for अनुस्वार, विसर्जनीय, उपध्मानीय, and जिह्वामूलीय<BR> as standing between vowels and consonants; अनुस्वारो विसर्गश्च.<BR> ZकVपौ चैव पराश्रितौ । अयोगवाहा विज्ञेया आश्रयस्थानभागिनः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगवः|अयोगव
अयोगवः (-वा or -वी <i>f.</i>) The son of a Śūdra^1 man<BR> and Vaiśya woman; सैरिध्रं वागुरावृत्तिं सूते दस्युरयोगवे Ms. 10. 32;<BR> see आयोगव; (his business is carpentry).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: And 13 others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगुड|अयोगुडः
अयोगुड, -जाल &c.<BR> see under अयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजाल
अयोगुड, -जाल &c.<BR> see under अयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगूः
अयोगूः A blacksmith; Vāj. 30. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्य
अयोग्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unfit, improper, unsuitable, useless.<BR>—2 Not ascertainable by senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोद्धृ
अयोद्धृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 No warrior, a bad warrior.<BR>—2 One who is not equalled by other warriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्य
अयोध्य <i>a.</i> Not to be warred against, unassailable; irresistible;<BR> अद्यायोध्या महाबाहो अयोध्या प्रतिभाति नः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्या
अयोध्य + .{@-ध्या@} The capital of solar kings, born of the line of Raghu, (the<BR> modern Oudh) situated on the river Śarayū. अलमुपहितशोभां तूर्णमायादयोध्याम् ।<BR> Bk. [It is said to have extended 48 miles in length and 12 miles in<BR> breadth. It was also called Sāketa, and one of its suburbs was Nandi-grāma,<BR> where Bharata lived governing the kingdom during the absence of Rāma.<BR> The town plays an important part in the story of the Rāmāyaṇa; the<BR> second book (अयोध्याकाण्ड) dealing mostly with events that took place<BR> in that city during the youthful days of Rāma.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनि|अयोनिः
अयोनि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without origin or source, eternal; जगद्योनिरयोनिस्त्वम् Ku. 2. 9.<BR>—2 Not born from the womb; born in a manner not approved by law or religion.<BR>—3 Of unknown family; अयोनिं च वियोनिं च न गच्छेत विचक्षणः Mb. 13. 104. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिः|अयोनि
अयोनि + .{@-निः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Not the womb; अयोनौ गच्छतो योषां पुरुषम् Y. 2. 293; Ms. 11. 174.<BR>—2 Not a particular verse of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिः|अयोनि
अयोनि + .{@-निः@}<BR>—1 N. of Brahmā and Śiva.<BR>—2 A pestle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अयोनिज, अयोनिजन्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिज|अयोनिजः
अयोनि + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> not born from the womb, not produced in the<BR> ordinary course of generation; शरीरं द्विविधं योनिजमयोनिजं चेति<BR> T. S.; तनयाम् अयोनिजाम् R. 11. 47, 48; कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म भवतामास्ते Mv. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिजन्मन्
अयोनि + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> not born from the womb, not produced in the<BR> ordinary course of generation; शरीरं द्विविधं योनिजमयोनिजं चेति<BR> T. S.; तनयाम् अयोनिजाम् R. 11. 47, 48; कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म भवतामास्ते Mv. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिजः|अयोनिज
अयोनि + -ज, -जन्मन् + .({@-जः@}) N. of Viṣṇu. ˚ईशः, ईश्वरः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिजा
अयोनि + -ज, -जन्मन् + .({@-जा@}), {@-संभवा@}<BR> N. of Sītā, daughter of Janaka, who was born from a<BR> furrow in a field; राघवाय तनयामयोनिजां पार्थिवः श्रियमिव न्यवेदयत्<BR> R. 11. 47; Mv. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिक
अयोनिक <i>a.</i> Without the words एष ते योनिः Vāj. 23. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगपद्यम्
अयौगपद्यम् Absence of simultaneity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगिक
अयौगिक (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Not etymologically derived (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौक्तिक
अयौक्तिक <i>a.</i> Inconsistent with reason, unreasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर <i>a.</i> [इयर्ति गच्छत्यनेन, ऋ-अच्]<BR>—1 Speedy, swift.<BR>—2 Little. यदा ह्येवैष एतस्मिन्नुदरमन्तरं कुरुते T. Up. 2. 7. 1. 3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">Page0213-2</a>]<BR> Going (at the end of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरः|अर|अरं
अर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The spoke or radius of a wheel; अरा इव रथानाभौ Muṇḍ. 2. 2. 6;<BR> Praśna. 2. 6. (˚रम् also); अरैः संधार्यते नाभिर्नाभौ चाराः प्रतिष्ठिताः<BR> Pt. 1. 81. cf. also अरव्यक्तिर्नष्टा स्थितमिव जवाच्चक्रवलयम् Pratimā 3. 2.<BR>—2 A spoke of the time-wheel; a Jaina division of time.<BR>—3 A corner (कोण) or angle; त्रिपञ्चारे पीठे Śyāmāstava.<BR>—4 Moss (शैवाल).<BR>—5 = पर्पट q. v.<BR>—6 N. of an ocean in Brahmāʼs world; यदरण्यायनमित्याचक्षते ब्रह्मचर्यमेव<BR> तत्तदरश्च ह वैण्यश्चार्णवौ ब्रह्मलोके Ch. Up. 8. 5. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरान्तर, अरघट्टः, अरघट्टकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरान्तर
अर + -अन्तर (pl.) the intervals of the spoke; चक्रभ्रान्तिररान्तरेषु<BR> जनयत्यन्यामिवारावलिम् V. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्टः|अरघट्ट
अर + -घट्टः, -घट्टकः [अरैः घट्टयते रच्यते असौ]<BR>—1 a wheel or machine for raising water from a well (Mar. राहाट).<BR> (It usually consists of a single wheel with spokes on each side serving<BR> as handles to turn it, and a rope with a bucket attached to it passes<BR> over this wheel); ˚ट्टं खेलयमानः Pt. 4 turning this machine; ˚घटी<BR> a bucket so used; कूपमासाद्य ˚टीमार्गेण सर्पस्तेनानीतः Pt. 4.<BR>—2 a deep well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्टकः|अरघट्टक
अर + -घट्टः, -घट्टकः [अरैः घट्टयते रच्यते असौ]<BR>—1 a wheel or machine for raising water from a well (Mar. राहाट).<BR> (It usually consists of a single wheel with spokes on each side serving<BR> as handles to turn it, and a rope with a bucket attached to it passes<BR> over this wheel); ˚ट्टं खेलयमानः Pt. 4 turning this machine; ˚घटी<BR> a bucket so used; कूपमासाद्य ˚टीमार्गेण सर्पस्तेनानीतः Pt. 4.<BR>—2 a deep well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरकः|अरक
अरकः A spoke of a wheel. न नाभिभङ्गे ह्यरका वहन्ति Pt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षस्
अरक्षस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not disturbed by evil spirits.<BR>—2 Harmless, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंकृ|अरङ्कृ
अरंकृ, -गम्<BR> See under अरम् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगम्|अरङ्गम्
अरंकृ, -गम्<BR> See under अरम् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गिन्|अरंगिन्
अरङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> Passionless; ˚सत्त्वः a passionless being; a class<BR> of divinities with Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dustless, clean, pure (fig also); मथितामृतफेनाभमरजोवस्त्रमुत्तमम्<BR> Rām. 5. 18. 24.<BR>—2 Free from passion (रजस्).<BR>—3 Not having the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजाः
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क + .({@-जाः@}) <i>f.</i> A young girl who has not reached the age of puberty; a<BR> girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरज
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dustless, clean, pure (fig also); मथितामृतफेनाभमरजोवस्त्रमुत्तमम्<BR> Rām. 5. 18. 24.<BR>—2 Free from passion (रजस्).<BR>—3 Not having the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्क
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dustless, clean, pure (fig also); मथितामृतफेनाभमरजोवस्त्रमुत्तमम्<BR> Rām. 5. 18. 24.<BR>—2 Free from passion (रजस्).<BR>—3 Not having the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजायते
अरजायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To become dustless or pure.<BR>—2 To lose the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरज्जु
अरज्जु <i>a.</i> Not consisting of or furnished with cords; अरज्जौ<BR> दस्यून् Rv. 2. 13. 9. <i>n.</i> A prison house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरडा
अरडा <i>f.</i> N. of a goddess. Gobhil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण|अरणं
अरण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>) Ved.<BR>—1 Departed, gone away; belonging to others, strange, unusual, foreign;<BR> distant, remote (opp. स्व, नित्य or अमा); (Sāy. grieved, sorry<BR> दुःखित, अरममाण); inimical, hostile, (with whom one is not on speaking terms).<BR>—2 Not fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणम्
अरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Moving, going.<BR>—2 Entering into, being inserted.<BR>—3 A refuge; बिभेति यस्मादरणं ततो नः Bhāg. 6. 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिः|अरणि
अरणिः <i>m., f.</i>, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [ऋ-अनि Uṇ. 2. 101; अरणिः अग्नेर्योनिः] A piece<BR> of wood (of the Śamī tree) used for kindling the sacred fire by attrition,<BR> the fire-producing wooden stick; प्रयच्छन्ति फलं भूमिररणीव हुताशनम् Pt. 1. 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणी
अरणिः <i>m., f.</i>, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [ऋ-अनि Uṇ. 2. 101; अरणिः अग्नेर्योनिः] A piece<BR> of wood (of the Śamī tree) used for kindling the sacred fire by attrition,<BR> the fire-producing wooden stick; प्रयच्छन्ति फलं भूमिररणीव हुताशनम् Pt. 1. 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणी
अरणिः <i>m., f.</i>, -णी <i>f.</i> + .{@-णी@} (dual) The two pieces of wood used in kindling the sacred<BR> fire. धरण्योर्निहितो जातवेदाः Kaṭh. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिः|अरणि
अरणिः <i>m., f.</i>, -णी <i>f.</i> + .{@-णिः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 fire.<BR>—3 Flint.<BR>—4 N. of several fire-producing plants, particularly अग्निमन्थ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">Page0214-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिः|अरणि
अरणिः <i>m., f.</i>, -णी <i>f.</i> + .{@-णिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A path, way.<BR>—2 Ved. Stinginess.<BR>—3 Discomfort; निररणि^1 सविता साविषक् Av. 1. 18. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरणिकेतुः, अरणिसुतः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: cf AV. 1,18,2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिकेतुः
अरणिः + -केतुः = अग्निमन्थ Premna Intergrifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिसुतः
अरणिः + -सुतः<BR>—1 N. of Śuka, a celebrated sage (born from the seed of Vyāsa fallen<BR> upon an <i>Araṇi</i> at the sight of the nymph Ghṛtācī^1); पितुः पादावगृह्णादरणीसुतः<BR> Mb. 12. 327. 31.<BR>—2 Fire, Agni; चितिं कृत्वा प्रवेक्ष्यामि समिद्धमरणीसुतम् Rām. 5. 13. 39.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: and 2 other instances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिमत्|अरणिमन्त्
अरणिमत् <i>a.</i> Related to the two Araṇis; to be produced by them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यम्
अरण्यम् (sometimes) <i>m.</i> also, [अर्यते गम्यते शेषे वयसि ऋ-अर्तेर्निच्च Uṇ. 3. 102]<BR>—1 A land neither cultivated nor grazed, a wilderness, forest, desert;<BR> प्रियानाशे कृत्स्नं किल जगदरण्यं हि भवति U. 6. 30; माता यस्य<BR> गृहे नास्ति भार्या चाप्रियवादिनी । अरण्यं तेन गन्तव्यं यथारण्यं तथा<BR> गृहम् ॥ Cāṇ. 44; तपःश्रद्धे ये ह्युपवसन्त्यरण्ये Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 11<BR> oft. used as first member of comp. in the sense of ‘wild’, ‘grown or produced in forest’<BR>; ˚बीजम् wild seed; ˚कार्पासी^1, ˚कुलत्थिका;<BR> ˚कुसुम्भः &c.; so ˚मार्जारः, ˚मूषकः.<BR>—2 A foreign or distant land; अरण्येषु जर्भुराणा चरन्ति Rv. 1. 163. 11.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यः|अरण्य|अरण्यं
अरण्यम् + .{@-ण्यः@} N. of a plant कट्फल (Mar. कायफळ)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरण्याध्यक्षः, अरण्यायनम्, अरण्ययानम्, अरण्यौकस्, अरण्यसद्, अरण्यकणा, अरण्यकदली, अरण्यकाण्डम्, अरण्यगजः, अरण्यगानम्, अरण्यचटकः, अरण्यचन्द्रिका, अरण्यचर, अरण्यज, अरण्यजीरम्, अरण्यदमनः, अरण्यद्वादशी, अरण्यव्रतम्, अरण्यधर्मः, अरण्यधान्यम्, अरण्यशालिः, अरण्यनृपतिः, अरण्यराज्, अरण्यपण्डितः, अरण्यपर्वन्, अरण्यभव, अरण्यमक्षिका, अरण्यमुद्गकः, अरण्ययानम्, अरण्यरक्षकः, अरण्यराज्यम्, अरण्यरुदितम्, अरण्यवायसः, अरण्यवासः, अरण्यसमाश्रयः, अरण्यवासिन्, अरण्यवास्तुकः, अरण्यवास्तूकः, अरण्यविलपितम्, अरण्यविलापः, अरण्यश्वन्, अरण्यषष्ठी, अरण्यसभा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्याध्यक्षः|अरण्याध्यक्ष
अरण्यम् + -अध्यक्षः headman or superintendent of a forest district; forest<BR> keeper or ranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यायनम्
अरण्यम् + -अयनम्, -यानम् going into the forest, becoming a hermit; अथ<BR> यदरण्यायनामित्याचक्षते ब्रह्मचर्यमेव तद् Ch. Up. 8. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्ययानम्
अरण्यम् + -अयनम्, -यानम् going into the forest, becoming a hermit; अथ<BR> यदरण्यायनामित्याचक्षते ब्रह्मचर्यमेव तद् Ch. Up. 8. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यौकस्
अरण्यम् + -ओकस्, -सद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dwelling in woods, being in a forest; किंतु ˚सदोवयम् अनभ्यस्त<BR> रथचर्याः U. 5; वैक्लव्यं मम तावदीदृशमपि स्नेहादरण्यौकसः Ś. 4. 6.<BR>—2 especially, one who has left his family and become an anchorite, forest-dweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यसद्
अरण्यम् + -ओकस्, -सद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dwelling in woods, being in a forest; किंतु ˚सदोवयम् अनभ्यस्त<BR> रथचर्याः U. 5; वैक्लव्यं मम तावदीदृशमपि स्नेहादरण्यौकसः Ś. 4. 6.<BR>—2 especially, one who has left his family and become an anchorite, forest-dweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकणा
अरण्यम् + -कणा wild cumin seed (Mar. जिरें)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकदली
अरण्यम् + -कदली wild plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकाण्डम्
अरण्यम् + -काण्डम् N. of the third book of the Rāmāyaṇa which embodies<BR> Rāmāʼs exploits in the course of his journey through the forests in<BR> company with Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यगजः|अरण्यगज
अरण्यम् + -गजः a wild elephant (not tamed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यगानम्
अरण्यम् + -गानम् N. of one of the four hymn-books of the Sāmaveda (to be<BR> chanted in the forest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचटकः|अरण्यचटक
अरण्यम् + -चटकः a wild sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचन्द्रिका
अरण्यम् + -चन्द्रिका (lit.) moonlight in a forest; (fig.) an ornament or<BR> decoration which is useless, or does not serve its purpose; just as moonlight<BR> in a forest is useless there being no human beings to view, enjoy and<BR> appreciate it, so is decoration when not viewed and appreciated by those<BR> for whom it is intended; thus Malli. on स्त्रीणां प्रियालोकफलो हि वेषः<BR> Ku. 7. 22 remarks अन्यथाऽरण्यचन्द्रिका स्यादिति भावः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचर
अरण्यम् + -चर (˚ण्येचर also), {@-जीव@} <i>a.</i><BR> wild, living in woods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यज
अरण्यम् + -ज <i>a.</i> wild; ˚आर्द्रका wild ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यजीरम्
अरण्यम् + -जीरम् wild cumin (Mar. कडू जिरें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यदमनः
अरण्यम् + -दमनः N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यद्वादशी
अरण्यम् + -द्वादशी, -व्रतम् N. of a ceremony performed on the 12th day of<BR> Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यव्रतम्
अरण्यम् + -द्वादशी, -व्रतम् N. of a ceremony performed on the 12th day of<BR> Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधर्मः|अरण्यधर्म|अरण्यधर्म्म
अरण्यम् + -धर्मः —1 wild state or usage, wild nature; तथारण्यधर्माद्वियोज्य<BR> ग्राम्यधर्मे नियोजितः Pt. 1<BR>—2 the duties of a Vānaprastha or anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधान्यम्
अरण्यम् + -धान्यम्, -शालिः wild rice (नीवार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यशालिः|अरण्यशालि
अरण्यम् + -धान्यम्, -शालिः wild rice (नीवार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यनृपतिः|अरण्यनृपति
अरण्यम् + -नृपतिः, -राज् (ट्), {@-राजः@}<BR> ‘lord of the woods’, epithet of a lion or a tiger; so अरण्यानां पतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यराज्
अरण्यम् + -नृपतिः, -राज् (ट्), {@-राजः@}<BR> ‘lord of the woods’, epithet of a lion or a tiger; so अरण्यानां पतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यपण्डितः|अरण्यपण्डित
अरण्यम् + -पण्डितः [अरण्ये एव पण्डितः, न तु नगरादिषु जनसमाजेषु]<BR> ‘wise in a forest’;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">Page0214-2</a>]<BR> (fig.) a foolish person (who can display his learning only in a forest<BR> where no one will hear him and correct his errors).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यपर्वन्
अरण्यम् + -पर्वन् N. of the first section of the Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यभव
अरण्यम् + -भव <i>a.</i> growing in a forest, wild; यथा ˚वास्तिलाः Pt. 2. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

