अरण्यम् + -वास्तुकः, -वास्तूकः N. of a plant वनवेतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यविलपितम्
अरण्यम् + -विलपितम्, -विलापः (˚ण्ये) = ˚रुदितम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यविलापः
अरण्यम् + -विलपितम्, -विलापः (˚ण्ये) = ˚रुदितम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यश्वन्
अरण्यम् + -श्वन् <i>m.</i> ‘a wild hound’, wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यषष्ठी
अरण्यम् + -षष्ठी N. of a festival celebrated on the 6th day of the bright<BR> half of Jyeṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यसभा
अरण्यम् + -सभा a forest-court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकम्
अरण्यकम्<BR>—1 Forest-court.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (Mar. बकाणा निंब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानिः|अरण्यानि
अरण्यानिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> [अरण्य-आनुक्, ङीप् च; P. IV. 1. 49; हिमारण्ययोर्महत्त्वे]<BR>—1 A large forest, or desert, vast wilderness; यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरन्तः<BR> Śat. Br.; Mv. 4.<BR>—2 The spirit or presiding deity of the woods and mother of wild animals.<BR> उतो अरण्यानिः सायं शकटीरिव सर्जति Rv. 10. 146. 3. अरण्यानी<BR> महारण्यम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> [अरण्य-आनुक्, ङीप् च; P. IV. 1. 49; हिमारण्ययोर्महत्त्वे]<BR>—1 A large forest, or desert, vast wilderness; यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरन्तः<BR> Śat. Br.; Mv. 4.<BR>—2 The spirit or presiding deity of the woods and mother of wild animals.<BR> उतो अरण्यानिः सायं शकटीरिव सर्जति Rv. 10. 146. 3. अरण्यानी<BR> महारण्यम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यीय
अरण्यीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Containing a forest.<BR>—2 Near a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्येनूच्यः|अरण्येनूच्य
अरण्येऽनूच्यः (<i>scil.</i> पुरोडाश)<BR>—1 A kind of oblation (अरण्ये अनूच्याः पठनीयाः मन्त्रा यस्य).<BR>—2 N. of a Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्येतिलकः|अरण्येतिलक
अरण्येतिलकः [P. II. 1. 44] Wild sesamum yielding no oil; (fig.<BR> anything which does not answer to oneʼs expectation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dull, languid, apathetic.<BR>—2 Dissatisfied, discontented, averse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतम्
अरत + .{@-तम्@} Non-copulation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरतत्रप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतत्रप|अरतत्रपः
अरत + -त्रप <i>a.</i> not ashamed of copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतत्रप|अरतत्रपः
अरत + -त्रप + .({@-प@}) a dog (as copulating even in the streets without shame).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dissatisfied, discontented.<BR>—2 Dull, languid, restless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतिः|अरति
अरति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Absence of pleasure or amusement; अरतिर्जनसंसदि Bg. 13. 10.<BR> regarded as arising from the longings of love, स्वाभीष्टवस्त्वलाभेन<BR> चेतसो याऽनवस्थितिः । अरतिः सा S. D.; one of the ten states of love-lorn<BR> persons (अनङ्गदशा); Mb. 12. 300. 48.<BR>—2 Pain, distress; भृशमरतिमवाप्य तत्र Ki. 10. 49.<BR>—3 Anxiety, regret, uneasiness, agitation; संधत्ते भृशमरतिं हि सद्वियोगः Ki. 5. 51.<BR>—4 Dissatisfaction, discontent.<BR>—5 Languor, dullness.<BR>—6 A bilious disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतिः|अरति
अरति + .{@-तिः@} [ऋ-अति]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">Page0215-1</a>]<BR>—1 Anger, passion.<BR>—2 Ved. Going, moving quickly.<BR>—3 Moving flame.<BR>—4 Occupying, attacking.<BR>—5 Servant, manager, assistant.<BR>—6 A master.<BR>—7 An intelligent being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निः|अरत्नि
अरत्निः (<i>m.</i> or <i>f.</i>) [ऋ-कत्नि रत्निः स नास्ति यत्र]<BR>—1 The elbow; sometimes the fist itself.<BR>—2 A cubit of the middle length, from the elbow to the tip of the little<BR> finger, an ell; अरत्निस्तु निष्कनिष्ठेन मुष्टिना Ak.; मध्याङ्गुलिकूर्परयोर्मध्ये<BR> प्रामाणिकः करः । बद्धमुष्टिकरो रत्निररत्निः स कनिष्ठिकः ॥ Halāy.;<BR> A measure 24 Aṅgulas (fingers); एकविंशतियूपास्ते एकविंशत्यरत्नयः<BR> Rām. 1. 14. 25. पञ्चारत्नयो रथपथः Kau. A. 2. 4. सममरत्नियुगेऽयुगचक्षुषः Ki. 18. 6.<BR>—3 The arm; अरत्निना चाभिहत्य शिरः कायादपाहरत् Mb. 3. 157. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निकः|अरत्निक
अरत्निकः The elbow; चत्वार्यरत्निकास्थीनि (बाह्वोः प्रमाणानि) Y. 3. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथिन्
अरथिन् <i>a.</i> One who does not fight in a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथीः
अरथीः Ved. Not a charioteer; यमजत्यरथीः Rv. 6. 66. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरद
अरद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Toothless (as a child).<BR>—2 Whose teeth are broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरध्र
अरध्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not lazy, not to be subdued, invincible; अरध्रस्य रध्रतुरो बभूव Rv. 6. 18. 4.<BR>—2 Prosperous (समृद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरन्धनम्
अरन्धनम् Absense of cooking (as on सिंह and कन्या संक्रान्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरन्ध्र
अरन्ध्र <i>a.</i> Dense, thick; पयोमुच इवारन्ध्राः Ki. 15. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपस्
अरपस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unhurt, safe. (also अरप); विश्वहारपऽएधते गृहे Vāj. 8. 5;<BR> sinless, pure.<BR>—2 Not hurting, sound; salutary, beneficial, शं वातो वात्वरपा अपस्रिधः Rv. 8. 18. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपचनः|अरपचन
अरपचनः A mystical collective name of the 5 Buddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम्
अरम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. [ऋ-अम्]<BR>—1 Swiftly, near, at hand, present. अरं राजगिरिं याहि पाहि राज्यं<BR> निजं नृप Śiva B. 26. 45.<BR>—2 Readily, fitly, suitably, so as to answer some purpose.<BR>—3 Enough, sufficiently (cf. अलम्); excessively; पुरु वारं पुरु त्मना<BR> Rv. 1. 142. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंकृ|अरङ्कृ
अरंकृ To prepare, make ready, serve; ˚कृत् gratifying, decorating,<BR> adorning, serving as a worshipper; ˚कृतिः<BR>—1 decorating, gratification.<BR>—2 Service; का ते अस्त्यरंकृतिः सूक्तैः Rv. 7. 29. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगम्|अरङ्गम्
अरंगम् To be present, come or go near (to help); become visible, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगमः|अरङ्गम|अरंगम
अरंगमः Coming near or into the presence, becoming visible, being<BR> present to help; अरंगमाय जग्मये Rv. 6. 42. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगरः|अरङ्गर|अरंगर
अरंगरः<BR>—1 Praising readily. Av. 20. 135. 13.<BR>—2 Factitious or made up poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंघुष|अरङ्घुष
अरंघुष <i>a.</i> Praising readily, sounding aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम|अरमः
अरम <i>a.</i> Low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमणस्
अरमणस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Hostile.<BR>—2 Obedient, devoted to the worship of God; निकाममरमणसं येन नवन्तमहिं<BR> सं पिणगृजीषिन् Rv. 6. 17. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमति|अरमतिः
अरमति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not resting, active, going everywhere.<BR>—2 Patient; महीमरमतिं दधन्विरे Rv. 10. 92. 5; अरमतिः सविता<BR> देव आगात् Rv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमतिः|अरमति
अरमति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Splendour.<BR>—2 Readiness to serve, obedience; devotion to God, hence personified in<BR> the Vedas as a Goddess protecting the worshippers of the gods and pious<BR> works in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमिष्
अरमिष् <i>a.</i> Ved. Going near quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमण
अरमण, अरममाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pleasing or gratifying, disagreeable, unpleasant. —2 Unceasing, incessant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरममाण
अरमण, अरममाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pleasing or gratifying, disagreeable, unpleasant. —2 Unceasing, incessant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमुडिः|अरमुडि
अरमुडिः A King of Nepāl; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररम्
अररम् [ऋ-अरन्; अरश्चित् स्यात् Uṇ. 3. 132] The leaf or panel of<BR> a door (कपाटम्), सरभसमरराणि द्रागपावृत्य Mv. 6. 27<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररः|अरर|अररं
अररम् + .({@-रः, -री@} also); चञ्चूकोटिविपाटिताररपुटो यास्याम्यहं पञ्जरात् Bv. 1. 58.<BR>—2 A door.<BR>—3 The sheath of a bamboo shoot (करीरकोष).<BR>—4 A covering or sheath in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररी
अररम् + .({@-रः, -री@} also); चञ्चूकोटिविपाटिताररपुटो यास्याम्यहं पञ्जरात् Bv. 1. 58.<BR>—2 A door.<BR>—3 The sheath of a bamboo shoot (करीरकोष).<BR>—4 A covering or sheath in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररः|अरर|अररं
अररम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 An awl.<BR>—2 A part of a sacrifice.<BR>—3 War, fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररका
अररका <i>f.</i> N. of the ancestress of a celebrated Hindu family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिः|अररि
अररिः The leaf of a door; a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिन्दम्
अररिन्दम् Ved.<BR>—1 Water (अररिं पिपासोपशमं ददाति).<BR>—2 A vessel used in preparing Soma; अधारयदररिन्दानि सुक्रतुः Rv. 1. 139. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिवस्
अररिवस् <i>m., f.</i><BR>—1 Not giving or offering.<BR>—2 Hard, unfriendly, envious, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररु|अररुः
अररु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Moving (गमनस्वभाव), कं चिद् यावीरररुं शूर मत्यम् Rv. 1. 129. 3.<BR>—2 = अररिवस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररुः|अररु
अररु + .{@-रुः@} [अर्तेः अरुः Uṇ. 4. 79].<BR>—1 An enemy.<BR>—2 A weapon.<BR>—3 N. of an Asura; अवेद्यमिमीताररुं यश्चतुष्पात् Rv. 10. 99. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररे
अररे <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle expressive of (1) great haste;<BR> (2) contempt or disdain; अररे महाराजं प्रति कुतः क्षत्रियाः G. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर्यति
अरर्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To work with an awl.<BR>—2 To try, put to the test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरव
अरव <i>a.</i> Noiseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दम्
अरविन्दम् [अरान् चकाङ्गानीव पत्राणि विन्दते विन्द् श P. III. 1. 138. Vārt.]<BR>—1 A lotus (Nymphea stellata) (it is one of the 5 arrows of Cupid; see<BR> under पञ्चबाण); शक्यमरविन्दसुरभिः Ś. 3. 6. It is a sun<BR> lotus; cf. सूर्यांशुभिर्भिन्नमिवारविन्दम् Ku. 1. 32; स्थल˚, चरण˚, मुख˚ &c.<BR>—2 Also a red or blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दः|अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं
अरविन्दम् + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 The (Indian) crane.<BR>—2 Copper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरविन्दाक्ष, अरविन्ददलप्रभम्, अरविन्दनाभिः, अरविन्दनाभः, अरविन्दसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दाक्ष
अरविन्दम् + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed, an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्ददलप्रभम्
अरविन्दम् + -दलप्रभम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दनाभिः|अरविन्दनाभि
अरविन्दम् + -नाभिः, -नाभः N. of Viṣṇu, from whose navel sprang the lotus<BR> which supported Brahmā; हृदये मदीये देवश्चकास्तु भगवानरविन्दनाभः Bv. 4. 8.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">Page0216-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दनाभः|अरविन्दनाभ
अरविन्दम् + -नाभिः, -नाभः N. of Viṣṇu, from whose navel sprang the lotus<BR> which supported Brahmā; हृदये मदीये देवश्चकास्तु भगवानरविन्दनाभः Bv. 4. 8.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">Page0216-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दसद्
अरविन्दम् + -सद् <i>m.</i> N. of Brahmā. आनन्दयिष्यदागम्य कथं त्वामरविन्दसत् Bk. 21. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दिनी|अरविंदिनी
अरविन्दिनी<BR>—1 A lotus plant; प्रपीतमधुका भृङ्गैः सुदिवेवारविन्दिनी Bk. 5. 70.<BR>—2 An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>—3 A place abounding in lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अरस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sapless, not juicy, tasteless, insipid; अरसं नित्यमगन्धवच्च<BR> यत् Kaṭh. 3. 15.<BR>—2 Dull, flat.<BR>—3 Weak, having no strength, inefficacious. वृश्चिकस्यारसं विषमरसं<BR> वृश्चिक ते विषम् Rv. 1. 191. 16.<BR>—4 One who has no sense of appreciation. किमस्या नाम स्यादरसपुरुषानादरशतैः । N.<BR>—5 Unhappy. कृपणं बत यज्जनः स्वयं सन्नरसो व्याधिजराविनाशधर्मा Bu. C. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसः|अरस
अरस + .{@-सः@} No juice, absence of juice.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरसाशः, अरसाशिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसाशः|अरसाश
अरस + -आशः<BR>—1 eating sapless food.<BR>—2 maceration of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसाशिन्
अरस + -आशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 eating sapless food.<BR>—2 macerating the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अरसिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devoid of taste, sapless, insipid, flavourless (of a thing).<BR>—2 Void of feeling or taste, dull, unfeeling, inappreciative, insensible<BR> to the charms (of poetry &c.); अरसिकेषु कवित्वनिवेदनं शिरसि मा<BR> लिख मा लिख मा लिख Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसीठक्कुरः|अरसीठक्कुर
अरसीठक्कुरः N. of a poet (mentioned in Śārṅgadharaʼs anthology).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहस्
अरहस् <i>n.</i> Absence of secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहायते
अरहायते Den. Ā. To become known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराग, -अरागिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Cool, dispassionate; तमहमरागकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं<BR> वन्दे Ve. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिन्
अराग, -अरागिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Cool, dispassionate; तमहमरागकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं<BR> वन्दे Ve. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक <i>a.</i> Having no king, anarchical; नाराजके जनपदे<BR> Rām. 2. 67. 9-28; Ms. 7. 3; अराजके जीवलोके दुर्बला बलवत्तरैः ।<BR> पीड्यन्ते न हि वित्तेषु प्रभुत्वं कस्यचित्तदा ॥ Mb.; शोच्यं राज्यमराजकम् Cāṇ. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्
अराजन् <i>m.</i> Not a king.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अराजभोगीन, अराजस्थापित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजभोगीन
अराजन् + -भोगीन <i>a.</i> not fit for the use of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजस्थापित
अराजन् + -स्थापित <i>a.</i> not established by a king, illegal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजिन्
अराजिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Unchecked, unrestrained, or without splendour;<BR> पर्वताँ अराजिनः Rv. 8. 7. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराटकी
अराटकी Ved. N. of the plant अजशृङ्गी (Mar. मेढशिंगी) एयमगन्नोषधीनां<BR> वीरुधां वीर्यावती । अजशृङ्ग्यराटकी तीक्ष्णशृङ्गी व्यृषतु Av. 4. 37. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरात्
अरात् <i>ind.</i> Immediately; at once; वर्तन्ति यदनीत्या ते तेन<BR> साकं पतन्त्यरात् Śukra. 4. 1266<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिः|अराति
अरातिः [न राति ददाति सुखं, रा-क, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 An enemy, foe; देशः सोऽयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन् ह्रदाः पूरिताः<BR> Ve. 3. 33; अरातिं बह्वमन्यत R. 12. 89. (in the Veda) non-offering<BR> (of sacrifices), stinginess, hardness, malignity, malevolence, failure<BR> or adversity; malignity personified: evil spirit whose aim it was to defeat<BR> the good intentions and disturb the happiness of man (used in <i>f.</i>).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">Page0216-2</a>]<BR>—2 The number six.<BR>—3 The sixth position in (astronomy).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरातिदूषण, अरातिदूषि, अरातिह, अरातिभङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिदूषण
अरातिः + -दूषण, -दूषि, -ह <i>a.</i> Ved. destroying adversities or enemies; Av. 19. 34. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिदूषि
अरातिः + -दूषण, -दूषि, -ह <i>a.</i> Ved. destroying adversities or enemies; Av. 19. 34. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिह
अरातिः + -दूषण, -दूषि, -ह <i>a.</i> Ved. destroying adversities or enemies; Av. 19. 34. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिभङ्गः|अरातिभङ्ग|अरातिभंग
अरातिः + -भङ्गः destruction of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातियति
अराति(ती)यति Den. P. Ved. To desire not to offer; to act like an<BR> enemy, act maliciously; अथो यो नो अरातियात् Av. 4. 36. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयति
अराति(ती)यति Den. P. Ved. To desire not to offer; to act like an<BR> enemy, act maliciously; अथो यो नो अरातियात् Av. 4. 36. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयत्
अरातीयत् <i>a.</i> Not offering, unfriendly, malicious, acting like an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयु
अरातीयु <i>a.</i> Ved. Not accustomed to offer; inimical; अरातीयोर्भ्रातृव्यस्य<BR> दुर्हार्दो द्विषतः शिरः Av. 10. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीवन्
अरातीवन् <i>a.</i> Not offering; unfriendly, malicious, hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराद्धिः|अराद्धि
अराद्धिः <i>f.</i> Transgression, sin, offence; envy. परिविविदानमराद्धया Vāj. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराधस्
अराधस् <i>a.</i> [राधः; धनम्- Nir. न˚ ब˚] Poor, not<BR> able to perform sacrifices, stingy; hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराम
अराम <i>a.</i> Disagreeable, unpopular; एवं प्रव्राजितश्चैव रामोऽरामो<BR> भविष्यति. Rām. 2. 9. 33<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराय|अरायः
अराय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति रा धनं यस्य वेदे षच्समासः]<BR>—1 Devoid of wealth, without sacrificial gifts.<BR>—2 Stingy, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरायः|अराय
अराय + .{@-यः, -यी@} Any malignant or evil spirit; अरायि काणे विकटे Rv. 10. 155. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरायी
अराय + .{@-यः, -यी@} Any malignant or evil spirit; अरायि काणे विकटे Rv. 10. 155. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल <i>a.</i> [ऋ-विच् अरम् आलाति, ला क] Spreading like the spokes<BR> of a wheel, curved, crooked; ‘अरालः कुटिले मतः इति’ मेदिनीकरः;<BR> Māl. 9. 34; पादावरालाङ्गुली M. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरालः|अराल|अरालं
अराल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A bent or crooked arm.<BR>—2 The resin of the plant Shorea Robusta (सर्जरस; Mar. राळ).<BR>—3 An elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराला
अराल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 An unchaste woman, harlot, courtezan.<BR>—2 A modest woman (अधृष्टा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरालकेशी, अरालपक्ष्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरालकेशी
अराल + -केशी a woman with curled hair; भित्त्वा निराकामदरालकेश्याः R. 6. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरालपक्ष्मन्
अराल + -पक्ष्मन् <i>a.</i> having curved eyelashes; करोति लक्ष्यं चिरमस्य<BR> चक्षुषो न वक्त्रमात्मीयमरालपक्ष्मणः Ku. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरावन्
अरावन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not offering, malignant, epithet of evil spirits.<BR> अपघ्नन्तो अराव्णः Rv. 9. 13. 9. यो अस्मभ्यमरावा Rv. 9. 21. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराष्ट्रम्
अराष्ट्रम् Loss of a royal power or sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि <i>a.</i> [ऋ-इन्] Moving, going, reaching; obtaining, aspiring,<BR> devoted to, zealous (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिः|अरि
अरि + .{@-रिः@}<BR>—1 An enemy, foe (cf. Uṇ. 4. 138); (used in the Veda like an adjective<BR> in the sense of ‘ungenerous’, ‘malicious’, ‘not worshipping or devoted’,<BR> ‘hostile’); विजितारिपुरःसरः R. 1. 59, 61, 4. 4.<BR>—2 An enemy of mankind (said of the six feelings which disturb manʼs mind);<BR> कामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभो मदमोहौ च मत्सरः; कृतारिषड्वर्गजयेन Ki. 1. 9.<BR>—3 A species of खदिर or Mimosa (विट्खदिर; Mar. शेण्या खैर).<BR>—4 N. of the number six (from the six enemies).<BR>—5 N. of a condition in astronomy.<BR>—6 Any part of a carriage.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">Page0217-1</a>]<BR>—7 A wheel, also a disk, अन्योऽन्यहस्तकलितैः कति मूर्तिभेदाः, शम्भोर्हरेरिव<BR> गदारिसरोजशङ्खैः Līlā.<BR>—8 A lord, master.<BR>—9 The wind.<BR>—10 A pious or religious man.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरिकर्षण, अरिकुलम्, अरिकेलिः, अरिगूर्त, अरिघ्नः, अरिचिन्तनम्, अरिचिन्ता, अरित्र, अरिधायस्, अरिनन्दन, अरिनिपातः, अरिभद्रः, अरिमर्दः, अरिमर्दन्, अरिमेदः, अरिमेदकः, अरिस्थानकम्, अरिसूदनः, अरिहन्, अरिहिंसकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकर्षण
अरि + -कर्षण <i>a.</i> tamer or subduer of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकुलम्
अरि + -कुलम्<BR>—1 a host of enemies.<BR>—2 an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकेलिः
अरि + -केलिः Sport of a foe, sexual enjoyment cf. अरिकेलिः शत्रुलीला<BR> स्त्रीरत्योश्चापि कीर्तितः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिगूर्त|अरिगूर्त्त
अरि + -गूर्त <i>a.</i> Ved. ready for the destruction of enemies; praised<BR> by devoted men or worshippers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिघ्नः|अरिघ्न
अरि + -घ्नः destroyer of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिचिन्तनम्
अरि + -चिन्तनम्, -चिन्ता schemes directed against enemies; administration<BR> of foreign affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिचिन्ता
अरि + -चिन्तनम्, -चिन्ता schemes directed against enemies; administration<BR> of foreign affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरि + -त्र <i>a.</i> protecting from enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिधायस्
अरि + -धायस् <i>a.</i> possessed by lords only (<i>i. e.</i> very precious)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिनन्दन
अरि + -नन्दन <i>a.</i> "an enemyʼs joy", affording triumph to an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिनिपातः|अरिनिपात
अरि + -निपातः invasion made by enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिभद्रः
अरि + -भद्रः the foremost or most powerful enemy; पप्रच्छ भद्रं<BR> विजितारिभद्रः R. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमर्दः|अरिमर्द|अरिमर्द्द
अरि + -मर्दः ‘crushing enemies’, N. of a plant (काममर्द; Mar. कासविंदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमर्दन्
अरि + -मर्दन् <i>a.</i> crushing or trampling foes, destroying enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमेदः|अरिमेद
अरि + -मेदः N. of a tree (विट्खदिर; Mar. शेण्या खैर); N. of<BR> a country; Bṛ. S. 14. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमेदकः|अरिमेदक
अरि + -मेदकः N. of an insect bred in excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिस्थानकम्
अरि + -स्थानकम् consternation, defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिसूदनः|अरिसूदन
अरि + -सूदनः, -हन्, -हिंसकः destroyer of enemies; पूजार्हावरिसूदन<BR> Bg. 2. 4. हरिहयोऽरिहयोगविचक्षणः R. 9. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिहन्
अरि + -सूदनः, -हन्, -हिंसकः destroyer of enemies; पूजार्हावरिसूदन<BR> Bg. 2. 4. हरिहयोऽरिहयोगविचक्षणः R. 9. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिहिंसकः|अरिहिंसक
अरि + -सूदनः, -हन्, -हिंसकः destroyer of enemies; पूजार्हावरिसूदन<BR> Bg. 2. 4. हरिहयोऽरिहयोगविचक्षणः R. 9. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिंदम|अरिन्दम|अरिन्दमः
अरिंदम <i>a.</i> [अरीन् दाम्यति दमयति वा; खच् मुमागमश्च] Subduer<BR> of enemies, victorious, conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्त
अरिक्त <i>a.</i> Not empty, abundant; तूणावरिक्तौ कवचं च दिव्यम्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज्, अरिक्थीय <i>a.</i> Not entitled to a share in the<BR> ancestral property (as an heir incapacitated by impotence &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीय
अरिक्थभाज्, अरिक्थीय <i>a.</i> Not entitled to a share in the<BR> ancestral property (as an heir incapacitated by impotence &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिणिन्
अरिणिन् <i>m.</i> A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरितृ
अरितृ [ऋ-तृच्-इडागमः] A rower, helmsman (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र <i>a.</i> [गच्छत्यनेन; ऋ-इत्र P. III. 2. 184.] Ved.<BR>—1 Propelling, urging onwards.<BR>—2 Protecting on all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्रम्
अरित्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 An oar; लोलैररित्रैश्चरणैरिवाभितः Śi. 12. 71.<BR>—2 A rudder, helm; नावा चापि यथा प्राज्ञो विभागज्ञः स्वरित्रया Mb. 14. 50. 27.<BR>—3 A ship, boat.<BR>—4 A part of a carriage. —5 A Soma vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्रः|अरित्र|अरित्रं
अरित्र + .{@-त्रः@} A Soma vessel. [cf. L. <i>aratrum</i> Gr. <i>cretmos</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरित्रगाध, अरित्रपरण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्रगाध
अरित्र + -गाध <i>a.</i> ‘oardeep’, shallow (water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्रपरण
अरित्र + -परण <i>a.</i> Ved. crossing by means of oars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिन्
अरिन् <i>n.</i> (-रि) A wheel; discus; नदारिशङ्खाब्जधरम्<BR> Rāmatāpanīya Upaniṣad 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरिन् <i>n.</i> (-रि) A wheel; discus; नदारिशङ्खाब्जधरम्<BR> Rāmatāpanīya Upaniṣad 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिप्र
अरिप्र <i>a.</i> [रिप्रं पापनाम Nir., तन्नास्ति यस्य] Ved.<BR> Sinless, spotless, blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिफित
अरिफित <i>a.</i> Not changed to र् (said of the Visarga) Prātiśākhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषम्
अरिषम् [न रिष्यते विच्छिद्यते] A continuous down-pour of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषः|अरिष|अरिषं
अरिषम् + .{@-षः@} A sort of disease in the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्य
अरिषण्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not harming or injuring, inoffensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्यत्|अरिषण्यन्त्
अरिषण्यत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not being hurt or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unhurt; perfect, complete; imperishable, undecaying, secure, safe;<BR> अरिष्टं गच्छ पन्थानम् Rām. 1. 24. 3; अरिष्टं मार्गमातिष्ठत् पुण्यं<BR> वा तु निषेवितम् Rām.<BR>—2 Auspicious, अक्षताभ्यामरिष्टाभ्यां हतः कर्णो महारथः Mb. 8. 66. 2.<BR>—3 unauspicious; अरिष्टमैन्द्रं निशितम् Rām. 6. 67. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टः|अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं
अरिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@}<BR>—1 A heron (कङ्क).<BR>—2 A raven, crow.<BR>—3 An enemy; अरिष्टस्त्वाष्ट्रस्य Mv. 4. 18.<BR>—4 N. of various plants:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) the soap-berry tree (Mar. रिठा); कुतपानामरिष्टकैः (शुद्धिः) Ms. 5. 120.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) another plant (Mar. निंब) Rām. 2. 94. 9; Bhāg. 8. 2. 12.<BR>—5 Garlic.<BR>—6 A distilled mixture.<BR>—7 N. of a demon killed by Kṛṣṇa; a son of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टा
अरिष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@}<BR>—1 A bandage.<BR>—2 N. of a medical plant (कटुका).<BR>—3 N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and one of the wives of Kaśyapa, and mother<BR> of महाश्वेता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टम्
अरिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Bad or ill luck, evil, misfortune, calamity.<BR>—2 A portentous phenomenon foreboding misfortune, unlucky omen (such as earth-quake).<BR>—3 Unfavourable symptom, especially of approaching death; रोगिणो मरणं<BR> यस्मादवश्यं भावि लक्ष्यते । तल्लक्षणमरिष्टं स्याद्रिष्टमप्यभिधीयते ॥<BR> cf. also Pātañjala Yogadarśana 3. 22.<BR>—4 Good fortune or luck, happiness.<BR>—5 The lying-in-chamber, delivery-room, womenʼs apartments; कर्मारारिष्टशालासु<BR> ज्वलेदग्निः सुरक्षितः Mb. 12. 69. 49; (अन्तःपुरम्); अपस्नात इवारिष्टं<BR> प्रविवेश गृहोत्तमम् Rām.<BR>—6 Butter-milk.<BR>—7 Spirituous liquor; ग्लानिच्छेदी क्षुत्प्रबोधाय पीत्वा रक्तारिष्टम् Śi. 18. 77.<BR> cf. … अरिष्टं सूतिकागृहे । अशुभे निम्बवृक्षे च शुभे तक्राङ्कयोः<BR> पुमान् । काके च फेनिले नीचे व्यसनेऽनर्थलम्बयोः । भाग्यहीने … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरिष्टासु, अरिष्टगातु, अरिष्टगृहम्, अरिष्टग्राम, अरिष्टताति, अरिष्टदुष्टधी, अरिष्टनेमिः, अरिष्टपुरम्, अरिष्टभर्मन्, अरिष्टमथनः, अरिष्टशय्या, अरिष्टसूदनः, अरिष्टहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टासु
अरिष्ट + -असु <i>a.</i> Ved. having oneʼs life unhurt. अरिष्टासु सचेवहि<BR> बृहते वाजसातये Av. 14. 2. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टगातु
अरिष्ट + -गातु <i>a.</i> Ved. dwelling securely चाऽरिष्टगातुः स होता सहोभरिः Rv. 5. 44. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टगृहम्
अरिष्ट + -गृहम् the lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टग्राम
अरिष्ट + -ग्राम <i>a.</i> Ved. of undivided group, having a complete troop;<BR> अरिष्टग्रामाः सुमतिं पिपर्तन Rv. 1. 166. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टताति|अरिष्टतातिः
अरिष्ट + -ताति <i>a.</i> Ved. making fortune or happy, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टतातिः|अरिष्टताति
अरिष्ट + -ताति + .({@-तिः@} <i>f.</i>) safeness, security, succession of good fortune,<BR> continuous happiness (अरिष्टं करोतीति ˚तातिः; अरिष्टस्य भावो वा शिवशमरिष्टस्य<BR> करे P. IV. 4. 143-4. Sk.); तदत्रभवता निष्पन्नाशिषां काममरिष्टतातिमाशास्महे Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टदुष्टधी
अरिष्ट + -दुष्टधी <i>a.</i> apprehensive of death, alarmed at the approach of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टनेमिः|अरिष्टनेमि
अरिष्ट + -नेमिः N. of the 22nd तीर्थंकर of the Jainas; N. of the<BR> brother of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टपुरम्
अरिष्ट + -पुरम् N. of a place; cf. अरिष्टाश्रितपुरम् P. VI. 2. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टभर्मन्
अरिष्ट + -भर्मन् <i>a.</i> granting security; देवेभिर्देव्यदितेऽरिष्टभर्मन्ना<BR> गहि Rv. 8. 18. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टमथनः|अरिष्टमथन
अरिष्ट + -मथनः N. of Śiva or Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टशय्या
अरिष्ट + -शय्या a lying in couch; अरिष्टशय्यां परितो विसारिणा R. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टसूदनः|अरिष्टसूदन
अरिष्ट + -सूदनः, -हन् <i>m.</i> killer of Ariṣṭa, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टहन्
अरिष्ट + -सूदनः, -हन् <i>m.</i> killer of Ariṣṭa, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टकः|अरिष्टक
अरिष्टकः = अरिष्टः The soap-berry tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टिः|अरिष्टि
अरिष्टिः <i>f.</i> Security; safety; स्वाय लोकायारिष्टिमिच्छेत् Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0217-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्यत्|अरिष्यन्त्
अरिष्यत् <i>a.</i> Not hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरीळ्ह
अरीळ्ह <i>a.</i> (= अरीढ) Ved. Not licked; अरीळ्हं वत्सं चरथाय<BR> माता Rv. 4. 18. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुः|अरु
अरुः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (रक्तखदिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुंषिका
अरुंषिका [अरूंषि मर्मस्थानान्यधिकृत्य जाता] Scab on the head<BR> (Mar. खवडे) Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्
अरुच्^1 <i>a.</i> Ved. Lightless, dark; अयं रोचयदरुचो रुचानो Rv. 6. 39. 4.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Vedic. While other dictionaries have 'ruca' and 'ruc' -  they don't have aruca. So assume missing virama..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिः|अरुचि
अरुचिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Aversion, dislike in general; क्व सा भोगानामुपर्यरुचिः K. 146.<BR>—2 Want of appetite, disrelish, disgust; सन्निपातक्षयश्वासकासहिक्कारुचिप्रणुत् Suśr.<BR>—3 Absence of a satisfactory explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिर
अरुचिर, अरुच्य <i>a.</i> Disagreeable, disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्य
अरुचिर, अरुच्य <i>a.</i> Disagreeable, disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज्
अरुज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from disease, sound, healthy. कोऽरुक् कोऽरुक् कोऽरुक् घृतभुङ्<BR> मितभुगशाकभुक्सोऽरुक् Udb.<BR>—2 Not festering^1 (as a boil).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुग्ण
अरुग्ण <i>a.</i> Not broken, not diseased, sound. रुजदरुग्णं वि<BR> वलस्य सानुम् Rv. 6. 39. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज|अरुजः
अरुज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sound, healthy; यावत्स्वस्थमिदं शरीरमरुजम् Bh. 3. 88, v. l.<BR>—2 Not breaking, not suppurating.<BR>—3 That which destroys a disease. विषेभ्यः खलु सर्वेभ्यः कर्णिकामरुजां<BR> स्थिराम् । Suśr.<BR>—4 Painless.<BR>—5 Brisk, gay; त्वत्कृते न हि सर्वं स्यात्प्रशान्तमरुजं जगत् Rām. 7. 84. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुजः|अरुज
अरुज + .{@-जः@} N. of a plant (आरग्वध; Mar. बाहवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण <i>a.</i> (-णा, -णी^1 <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋ-उनन्; cf. Uṇ. 3. 60]<BR>—1 Reddish brown, tawny, red, ruddy (of the colour of the morning as opposed<BR> to the darkness of night); प्रत्याख्यातविशेषकं कुरबकं श्यामावदातारुणम्<BR> M. 3. 5; नयनान्यरुणानि घूर्णयन् Ku. 4. 12.<BR>—2 Perplexed, embarrassed.<BR>—3 Dumb.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणः|अरुण|अरुणं
अरुण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 Red colour, the colour of the dawn or morning twilight.<BR>—2 The dawn personified as the charioteer of the Sun; आविष्कृतारुणपुरःसर<BR> एकतोऽर्कः Ś. 4. 2, 7. 4; विभावरी यद्यरुणाय कल्पते Ku. 5. 44;<BR> R. 5. 71. [Aruṇa is represented as the elder brother of Garuḍa, being<BR> the son of Vinatā by Kaśyapa. Vinatā prematurely hatched the egg and<BR> the child was born without thighs, and hence he is called <i>Anūru</i> ‘thighless’,<BR> or <i>Vipāda</i> ‘footless’. He cursed his mother that since she had brought<BR> him forth before the due season she would be a slave to her rival Kadrū;<BR> but at her earnest entreaties, he modified the curse and said that her<BR> next son would deliver her from bondage. Aruṇa now holds the office of<BR> the charioteer of the Sun. His wife was Śyenī, who bore him two sons<BR> Saṃpāti and Jaṭāyu.]<BR>—3 The Sun; रागेण बालारुणकोमलेन Ku. 3. 30, 5. 8; संसृज्यते<BR> सरसिजैररुणांशुभिन्नैः; R. 5. 69; Ś. 1. 31 अरुणकररुचायतेऽन्तरीक्षे Bu. C. 5. 87.<BR>—4 A kind of leprosy with red spots and insensibility of the skin.<BR>—5 A little poisonous creature Bhāg. 8. 10. 10.<BR>—6 N. of a plant पुंनाग; also a synonym of अर्क q. v.<BR>—7 Molasses<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">Page0218-2</a>]<BR> (गुड).<BR>—8 N. of a peak of the Himālaya situated to the west of Kailāsa.<BR>—9 N. of one of the 12 Ādityas, the one presiding over Maghā.<BR>—10 N. of a sage; उद्दालकोऽरुणात् Bṛ. Up. 6. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणा
अरुण + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 N. of several plants;<BR>——(<i>a</i>) अतिविषा (Mar. अतिविख);<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Madder (मञ्जिष्ठा);<BR>——(<i>c</i>) त्रिवृत् commonly called Teori;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) a black kind of the same (श्यामाका);<BR>——(<i>e</i>) bitter apple (इन्द्रवारुणी);<BR>——(<i>f</i>) the Guñja plant that yields the red and black berry (गुंज)<BR> used as a weight by jewellers &c.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) मुण्डतिक्ता cf. अरुणः कपिले कुष्ठे सन्ध्यारागेऽर्कसारथौ ।<BR> अव्यक्तरागे निःशब्दे द्रव्ये त्रिषु निरूपितः । स्त्रियामतिविषाश्यामामञ्जिष्ठात्रिवृतासु च । Nm.<BR>—2 N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणी
अरुण + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A red cow (Nir.). —2 The early dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणम्
अरुण + .{@-णम्@} —1 Red colour; दिविस्पृश्यात्यरुणानि कृण्वन् Rv. 10. 168. 1.<BR>—2 Gold; अम्भो अरुणं रजतम् Av. 13. 4. 51.<BR>—3 Saffron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अरुणाग्रजः, अरुणानुजः, अरुणावरजः, अरुणार्चिस्, अरुणाश्व, अरुणात्मजः, अरुणेक्षण, अरुणोदकम्, अरुणोदयः, अरुणोपलः, अरुणकमलम्, अरुणकेतुब्राह्मणम्, अरुणचूडः, अरुणज्योतिस्, अरुणदूर्वा, अरुणपराशराः, अरुणप्रिय, अरुणप्सु, अरुणबभ्रु, अरुणयुज्, अरुणलोचन, अरुणसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणाग्रजः|अरुणाग्रज
अरुण + -अग्रजः N. of Garuḍa (अरुणः अग्रजो यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणानुजः|अरुणानुज
अरुण + -अनुजः, -अवरजः N. of Garuḍa, younger brother of Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणावरजः|अरुणावरज
अरुण + -अनुजः, -अवरजः N. of Garuḍa, younger brother of Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणार्चिस्
अरुण + -अर्चिस् <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणाश्व
अरुण + -अश्व <i>a.</i> having red horses, epithet of the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0218-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणात्मजः|अरुणात्मज
