अर्गली
अर्गलः, -ला, -ली, -लम्<BR> [अर्ज् कलच् न्यङ्क्वादि˚ कुत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A wooden bolt, pin, bar &c. (for fastening a door or the cover of a<BR> vessel), a bolt, latch, bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4, 16. 6;<BR> अनायतार्गलम् Mk. 2; ससंभ्रमेन्द्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR> भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलम् Ks. 4. 62 bolted from<BR> without; oft. used figuratively in the sense of a bar, impediment, something<BR> intervening as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118;<BR> ईप्सितं तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79 obstructed;<BR> वार्यर्गलाभङ्ग इव प्रवृत्तः 5. 45; कण्ठे केवलमर्गलेव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">Page0221-1</a>]<BR> निहिता जीवस्य निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>—2 A wave or billow.<BR>—3 The leaf of a door (कपाटम्).<BR>—4 A kind of ‘stotra’ or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0220-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलम्
अर्गलः, -ला, -ली, -लम्<BR> [अर्ज् कलच् न्यङ्क्वादि˚ कुत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A wooden bolt, pin, bar &c. (for fastening a door or the cover of a<BR> vessel), a bolt, latch, bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4, 16. 6;<BR> अनायतार्गलम् Mk. 2; ससंभ्रमेन्द्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR> भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलम् Ks. 4. 62 bolted from<BR> without; oft. used figuratively in the sense of a bar, impediment, something<BR> intervening as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118;<BR> ईप्सितं तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79 obstructed;<BR> वार्यर्गलाभङ्ग इव प्रवृत्तः 5. 45; कण्ठे केवलमर्गलेव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">Page0221-1</a>]<BR> निहिता जीवस्य निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>—2 A wave or billow.<BR>—3 The leaf of a door (कपाटम्).<BR>—4 A kind of ‘stotra’ or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0220-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका A small door-pin, small bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलित
अर्गलित <i>a.</i> Fastened by a bolt, chained, bolted; ˚द्वारा K. 357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलीय
अर्गलीय, -ल्य <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल्ल्य
अर्गलीय, -ल्य <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्
अर्घ् €1 P. [अर्घति, अर्घितुं, अर्घित] To be worth, have value, to<BR> cost; परीक्षका यत्र न सन्ति देशे नार्घन्ति रत्नानि समुद्रजानि Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घः|अर्घ
अर्घः [अर्घ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Price, value; कुर्युरर्घं यथापण्यम् Ms. 8. 398; Y. 2. 251; कुत्स्याः<BR> स्युः कुपरीक्षका हि मणयो यैरर्घतः पातिताः Bh. 2. 15 reduced in their<BR> true value, depreciated; so अनर्घ priceless; महार्घ very costly.<BR>—2 A material of worship, respectful offering or oblation to gods or venerable<BR> men, consisting of rice, Dūrvā grass &c. with or without water; दूर्वासर्षपपुष्पाणां<BR> दत्त्वार्घं पूर्णमञ्जलिम् Y. 1. 290; कुटजकुसुमैः कल्पितार्घाय तस्मै<BR> Me. 4; (the ingredients of this offering are:− आपः क्षीरं कुशाग्रं<BR> च दधि सर्पिः सतण्डुलम् । यवः सिद्धार्थकश्चैव अष्टाङ्गोऽर्घः प्रकीर्तितः ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घतन्त्रम्
अर्घः + .{@-तन्त्रम्@} cf. also रक्तबिल्वाक्षतैः पुष्पैर्दधिदूर्वाङ्कुशैस्तिलैः ।<BR> सामान्यः सर्वदेवानामर्घोऽयं परिकीर्तितः ॥ -देवीपुराणम् and आपः<BR> क्षीरं कुशाग्राणि घृतं मधु तथा दधि । रक्तानि करवीराणि तथा रक्तं<BR> च चन्दनम् । अष्टाङ्ग एष ह्यर्घो वै भानवे परिकीर्तितः ॥ -काशीखण्डः<BR> cf. also अर्घः पूजाविधौ मूल्ये … । Nm.; see अर्घ्य below.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्घापचयः, अर्घार्ह, अर्घेश्वरः, अर्घदानम्, अर्घबलाबलम्, अर्घसंख्यानम्, अर्घसंस्थापनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घापचयः|अर्घापचय
अर्घः + -अपचयः The diminution of price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घार्ह
अर्घः + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> worthy of a respectful offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घेश्वरः|अर्घेश्वर
अर्घः + -ईश्वरः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घदानम्
अर्घः + -दानम् presentation of a respectful offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घबलाबलम्
अर्घः + -बलाबलम् rate of price, proper price, the cheapness or dearness<BR> of articles, fall or rise in prices; गन्धानां च रसानां च विद्यादर्घबलाबलम्<BR> Ms. 9. 329. (cf. अर्घस्य ह्रासं वृद्धिं वा … । Y. 2. 249.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंख्यानम्
अर्घः + -संख्यानम्, -संस्थापनम् fixing the price of commodities, appraising,<BR> assizes of goods; कुर्वीत चैषां (वणिजां) प्रत्यक्षमर्घसंस्थापनं<BR> नृपः Ms. 8. 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंस्थापनम्
अर्घः + -संख्यानम्, -संस्थापनम् fixing the price of commodities, appraising,<BR> assizes of goods; कुर्वीत चैषां (वणिजां) प्रत्यक्षमर्घसंस्थापनं<BR> नृपः Ms. 8. 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घीशः|अर्घीश
अर्घीशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य <i>a.</i> [अर्घ-यत् अर्घमर्हति]<BR>—1 Valuable; अनर्घ्य invaluable; अनर्घ्यमपि माणिक्यम् see s. v.<BR>—2 Venerable, deserving respectful offering; तानर्घ्यानर्घ्यमादाय दूरात्प्रत्युद्ययौ<BR> गिरिः Ku. 6. 50; Śi. 1. 14; Y. 1. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्यम्
अर्घ्य + .{@-र्घ्यम्@} —1 A respectful offering or oblation to a god or venerable<BR> person (see अर्घ); अर्घः पूजाविधिः तदर्थं द्रव्यम् अर्घ्यम् Sk.;<BR> अर्घ्यमस्मै V. 5; ददतु तरवः पुष्पैरर्घ्यं फलैश्च मधुश्चुतः<BR> U. 3. 24; अर्घ्यंमर्घ्यमिति वादिनं नृपम् R. 11. 69, 1. 44; Ku. 1. 58, 6. 50;<BR> (it often consists only of water given in a droṇa and forms<BR> part of the Madhuparka ceremony). —2 A kind of honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घटम्
अर्घटम् Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् €1 U. (अर्चति-ते, आनर्च, आचींत्, अर्चितुम, अर्चित)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To adore worship, salute, welcome with respect; प्रणम्य चानर्च<BR> विशालमस्याः शृङ्गान्तरं द्वारमिवार्थसिद्धेः R. 2. 21, 1. 6, 90, 4. 84, 12. 89;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">Page0221-2</a>]<BR> Ms. 3. 93; आर्चीद् द्विजातीन् परमार्थविन्दान्<BR> Bk. 1. 15, 14. 63, 17. 5; यस्यार्चत्यसौ शासनम् Mv. 1. 29 honours,<BR> respectfully obeys.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To honour, <i>i. e.</i> decorate, adorn; स्वकुसुमैरर्चन्ति गोदावरीम् U. 2. 9.<BR>—2 To praise (Ved.) —3 To shine. €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To honour, adore, worship; स्वर्गौकसामर्चितमर्चयित्वा Ku. 1. 59.<BR>—2 To praise.<BR>—3 To cause to shine; हर्यन्नुषसमर्चयः Rv. 3. 44. 2. ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> [अर्चिचिषति] To wish to worship; ━<i>With</i> {@अनु@} to congratulate, hail with joy.<BR>━{@प्र@}<BR>—1 to praise, sing praises of.<BR>—2 To honour, worship; प्रानर्चुरर्च्या जगदर्चनीयम् Bk. 2. 20; ━<i>Caus.</i> to honour.<BR>━{@सम्@}<BR>—1 to worship, adore.<BR>—2 to fix, settle, establish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च|अर्च्च
अर्च <i>a.</i> Ved. Shining; अस्मा एतद् दिव्यर्चेव मासा Rv. 6. 34. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक <i>a.</i> [अर्च्-ण्वुल्] Worshipping, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चकः|अर्चक|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक + .{@-कः@} A worshipper; गुरुदेवद्विजार्चकः Ms. 11. 224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्रि
अर्चत्रि <i>a.</i> Ved. [अर्च वेदे बाहु˚ अत्रि] Adorable, venerable<BR> (Sāy.); roaring aloud, singing loudly. अर्चत्रयो धुनयो न वीरा Rv. 6. 66. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्र्य
अर्चत्र्य <i>a.</i> Ved. to be praised or worshipped. अर्चत्र्यो मघवा<BR> नृभ्य उक्थैः Rv. 6. 24. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन <i>a.</i> [अर्च्-ल्युट्] worshipping, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनम्
अर्चन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} Worshipping, reverence or respect paid to deities and superiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चना|अर्च्चना
अर्चन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} Worshipping, reverence or respect paid to deities and superiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनानस्
अर्चनानस् <i>m.</i> N. of a Ṛṣi belonging to the Atri family; नरा<BR> बिभ्रतावर्चनानसम् Rv. 5. 64. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनीय
अर्चनीय, अर्च्य <i>pot. p.</i> [अर्च्-अनीयर् ण्यत्] To be adored<BR> or worshipped, venerable, adorable, respectable. R. 2. 10; प्रानर्चुरर्च्यं<BR> जगदर्चनीयम् Bk. 6. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्य
अर्चनीय, अर्च्य <i>pot. p.</i> [अर्च्-अनीयर् ण्यत्] To be adored<BR> or worshipped, venerable, adorable, respectable. R. 2. 10; प्रानर्चुरर्च्यं<BR> जगदर्चनीयम् Bk. 6. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चयितव्य
अर्चयितव्य <i>a.</i> worthy of being worshipped or adored, adorable.<BR> गुरवोऽर्चयितव्याश्च पुराणं धर्ममिच्छता Mb. 12. 109. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा [अर्च्-अङ्]<BR>—1 Worship, adoration; अर्चायामेव हरये पूजां यः श्रद्धयेहते Bhāg. 11. 2. 47.<BR>—2 An idol or image intended to be worshipped; मौर्यैर्हिरण्यार्थिभिरर्चाः<BR> प्रकल्पिताः Mbh. 5. 3. 99. (there is some dispute among scholars as<BR> to the precise meaning of this passage); अर्चापूजाप्रतिमयोः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिः|अर्चि|अर्च्चिः
अर्चिः <i>f.</i> [अर्च्-इन] Ray, flame (of fire or of the morning<BR> twilight); आसीदासन्ननिर्वाणः प्रदीपार्चिरिवोषसि R. 12. 1; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज<BR> इव च्छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिमत्|अर्चिमन्त्
अर्चिमत्, -वत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Shining; उत त्या मे रौद्रावर्चिमन्ता Rv. 10. 61. 15;<BR> उद्यन्नक्षत्रमर्चिवत् Rv. 7. 81. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिवत्|अर्चिवन्त्
अर्चिमत्, -वत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Shining; उत त्या मे रौद्रावर्चिमन्ता Rv. 10. 61. 15;<BR> उद्यन्नक्षत्रमर्चिवत् Rv. 7. 81. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चित|अर्च्चितः
अर्चित <i>p. p.</i> Worshipped, respected, honoured; R. 10. 55; Ms. 4. 235^1;<BR> स्वर्गौकसामर्चितमर्चयित्वा Ku. 1. 59.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चितिन्
अर्चितिन् <i>a.</i> Honouring, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0221-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिन्
अर्चिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praising, honouring, worshipping.<BR>—2 Shining as a ray of light, radiating; स माया अर्चिना पदा Rv. 8. 41. 8. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ची
अर्चिन् + .({@-र्ची@}) A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् <i>n.</i> (-र्चिः)<BR> [अर्च्-इसि Uṇ. 2. 107]<BR>—1 A ray of light, flame; यत्ते पवित्रमर्चिष्यग्ने विततमन्तरा Rv. 9. 67. 23;<BR> प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14.<BR>—2 Light, lustre; प्रशमादर्चिषाम् Ku. 2. 20; Ratn. 4. 16. (said to<BR> be also <i>f.</i>) <i>f.</i> N. of the wife of कृशाश्व and mother of धूमकेतु. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 Fire. अर्चिर्मयूखशिखयोः .. Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिः|अर्चि|अर्च्चिः
अर्चिस् <i>n.</i> (-र्चिः)<BR> [अर्च्-इसि Uṇ. 2. 107]<BR>—1 A ray of light, flame; यत्ते पवित्रमर्चिष्यग्ने विततमन्तरा Rv. 9. 67. 23;<BR> प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14.<BR>—2 Light, lustre; प्रशमादर्चिषाम् Ku. 2. 20; Ratn. 4. 16. (said to<BR> be also <i>f.</i>) <i>f.</i> N. of the wife of कृशाश्व and mother of धूमकेतु. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 Fire. अर्चिर्मयूखशिखयोः .. Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मत्|अर्चिष्मन्त्
अर्चिष्मत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्] Flaming, brilliant, bright;<BR> अर्चिष्मतीः सन्ध्यामङ्गलदीपिकाः V. 3. 2. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire, the god of fire; जज्ञे तेजो महार्चिष्मान् पञ्चवर्णः प्रभावतः Mb. 3. 220. 3.<BR>—2 The Sun. अर्चिष्मानर्चितोऽत्यर्थं ब्रह्मचर्यव्रते स्थितः Rām. 5. 35. 12.<BR>—3 A sort of subordinate deity.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मती
अर्चिष्मत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 N. of the town or world of Agni.<BR>—2 One of the 10 earths according to Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् €1 P. [अर्जति, आनर्ज, अर्जिष्यति, आर्जीत्, अर्जितुम्, अर्जित]<BR>—1 To procure, secure, gain, earn, usually in the <i>caus.</i> in this sense;<BR> पितृद्रव्याविरोधेन यदन्यत्स्वयमर्जितम् Y. 2. 118.<BR>—2 To take up; आनर्जुर्नृभुजोऽस्त्राणि Bk. 14. 74. ━€10 P. or <i>caus.</i><BR>—1 To procure, acquire, obtain; स्वयमर्जित, स्वार्जित obtained by<BR> oneʼs own exertions, self-acquired.<BR>—2 To work or manufacture, make, prepare (सतो गुणान्तराधानम्).<BR>━<i>With</i> {@अति@}<BR>—1 to allow, permit, let go.<BR>—2 to remove, despatch, make away with.<BR>━{@अनु@} to let go, set free, deliver.<BR>━{@अपि@} to add to.<BR>━{@अन्वव@}<BR>—1 to cause to go after or in a particular direction. —2 To visit with<BR> anything, overcome.<BR>━{@अप्यति@} to add, append; say something in addition to what is already said.<BR>━{@अव@} to permit to leave, release, let go.<BR>━{@उद्@} to drive out, remove.<BR>━{@प्र@} <i>caus.</i> to furnish, supply, procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक <i>a.</i> [अर्ज्-ण्वुल्]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जिका
अर्जक + .({@-र्जिका@} <i>f.</i>) Procuring, acquiring; one who acquires or gets;<BR> अर्जको ह्यंशमाहरेत् Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जकः|अर्जक|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक + .{@-कः@} N. of several plants सितपर्णास, वर्वरीभेद; सामान्यतुलसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जनम्
अर्जनम् [अर्ज्-ल्युट्] Getting, acquisition; अर्थानामर्जने दुःखम्<BR> Pt. 1. 163; अर्जयितव्यापारोऽर्जनम् Dāy. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जित
अर्जित <i>a.</i> Acquired, gained, earned. विक्रमार्जितसत्त्वस्य स्वयमेव<BR> मृगेन्द्रता Pt. अर्जितानां च रक्षणे (दुःखम्) Pt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन <i>a.</i> [अर्ज्-उनन् णिलुक् च Uṇ. 3. 58] (-ना, -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 White, clear, bright, of the colour of day; अहश्च कृष्णमहरर्जुनं<BR> च Rv. 6. 9. 1; पिशङ्गमौञ्जीयुजमर्जुनच्छविम् Śi. 1. 6.<BR>—2 Silvery; यत्र वः प्रेङ्खा हरिता अर्जुना Av. 4. 37. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनः|अर्जुन|अर्जुनं
अर्जुन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 A peacock.<BR>—3 A sort of cutaneous disease.<BR>—4 A tree (Mar. अर्जुनसादडा), with useful rind; Mb. 3. 64. 3.<BR>—5 N. of the third Pāṇḍava who was a son of Kuntī by Indra and hence<BR> called ऐन्द्रि also. [Arjuna was so called because he was ‘white’ or<BR> ‘pure in actions’ (पृथिव्यां चतुरन्तायां वर्णो मे दुर्लभः समः । करोमि<BR> कर्म शुद्धं च तेन मामर्जुनं विदुः). He was taught the use<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-2" target="_blank">Page0222-2</a>]<BR> of arms by Droṇa and was his favourite pupil. By his skill in arms he<BR> won Draupadī at her Svayaṃvara (see Draupadī). For an involuntary transgression<BR> he went into temporary exile and during that time he learnt the science<BR> of arms from Paraśurāma. He married Ulūpī, a Nāga Princess, by whom<BR> he had a son named Irāvat, and also Chitrāṅgadā, daughter of the king<BR> of Maṇipura, who bore him a son named Babhruvāhana. During this exile<BR> he visited Dvārakā, and with the help and advice of Kṛṣṇa succeeded<BR> in marrying Subhadrā. By her he had a son named Abhimanyu. Afterwards<BR> he obtained the bow Gāṇḍīva from the god Agni whom he assisted in<BR> burning the Khāṇḍava forest. When Dharma, his eldest brother, lost<BR> the kingdom by gambling, and the five brothers went into exile, he went<BR> to the Himālayas to propitiate the gods and to obtain from them celestial<BR> weapons for use in the contemplated war against the Kauravas. There he<BR> fought with Śiva who appeared in the disguise of a Kirāta; but when<BR> he discovered the true character of his adversary he worshipped him and<BR> Śiva gave him the Pāśupatāstra. Indra, Varuṇa, Yama and Kubera also<BR> presented him with their own weapons. In the 13th year of their exile,<BR> the Pāṇḍavas entered the service of the King of Virāṭa and he had<BR> to act the part of a eunuch, and music and dancing master. In the great<BR> war with the Kauravas Arjuna took a very distinguished part. He secured<BR> the assistance of Kṛṣṇa who acted as his charioteer and related to<BR> him the Bhagavadgītā when on the first day of the battle he hesitated<BR> to bend his bow against his own kinsmen. In the course of the great struggle<BR> he slew or vanquished several redoubtable warriors on the side of the<BR> Kauravas, such as Jayadratha, Bhīṣma, Karṇa &c. After Yudhiṣṭhira<BR> had been installed sovereign of Hastināpura, he resolved to perform the<BR> Aśvamedha sacrifice, and a horse was let loose with Arjuna as its guardian.<BR> Arjuna followed it through many cities and Countries and fought with many<BR> kings. At the city of Maṇipura he had to fight with his own son Babhruvāhana<BR> and was killed; but he was restored to life by a charm supplied by his<BR> wife Ulūpī. He traversed the whole of Bharatakhaṇda and returned to<BR> Hastināpura, loaded with spoils and tributes, and the great horse-sacrifice<BR> was then duly performed. He was afterwards called by Kṛṣṇa to Dvārakā<BR> amid the internecine struggles of the Yādavas and there he performed<BR> the funeral ceremonies of Vasudeva and Kṛṣṇa. Soon after this the five<BR> Pāṇdavas repaired to heaven having installed Parīkṣit ━the only surviving<BR> son of Abhimanyu━ on the throne of Hastināpura. Arjuna was the bravest<BR> of the Pāṇdavas, high-minded, generous, upright, hand-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">Page0223-1</a>]<BR> some and the most prominent figure of all his brothers. He has several<BR> appellations, such a Pārtha, Gudākeśa, Savyasāchī, Dhanañjaya, Phālguna,<BR> Kirītin, Jīṣṇu, Śvetavāhana, Gāṇḍivin &c.] cf. अर्जुनः फाल्गुनो<BR> जिष्णुः किरीटी श्वेतवाहनः । बीभत्सुर्विजयः कृष्णः सव्यसाची धनञ्जयः ॥<BR>—6 N. of Kārtavīrya, slain by Parasurāma. See कार्तवीर्य.<BR>—7 N. of a country Bṛ. S. 14. 25.<BR>—8 The only son of his mother.<BR>—9 N. of Indra.<BR>—10 N. of a tree, Terminalia Arjuna (Mar. अईन). The tree is rarer<BR> in south India. The colour of its bark is white. It is a forest-tree bearing<BR> fragrant flowers appearing in panicles like those of the Mango-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनी|अर्ज्जुनी
अर्जुन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A procuress, bawd.<BR>—2 A cow. तथार्जुनीनां कपिला वरिष्ठा Mb. 13. 73. 42.<BR>—3 A kind of serpent; अर्जुनि पुनर्वोयन्तु˚ Av. 2. 24. 7.<BR>—4 N. of Uṣā, wife of Aniruddha.<BR>—5 N. of a river commonly called करतोया.<BR>—6 (न्यौ, -न्यः dual and pl.) N. of the constellation Phalgunī. अघासु<BR> हन्यन्ते गावोऽर्जुन्योः पर्युह्यते Rv. 10. 85. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनम्
अर्जुन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Silver. वीरुद्भिष्टे अर्जुनं संविदानम् Av. 5. 28. 5.<BR>—2 Gold.<BR>—3 Slight inflammation of the white of the eye.<BR>—4 Grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनाः
अर्जुन + .{@-नाः@} (Pl.) The descendants of Arjuna; cf. अर्जुनः ककुभे पार्थे<BR> कार्तवीर्यमयूरयोः । मातुरेकसुते वृक्षे धवले नयनामये । तृणभेदे<BR> गवि स्त्री स्यात् … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्जुनाभ्रम्, अर्जुनेश्वरतीर्थम्, अर्जुनोपमः, अर्जुनकाण्ड, अर्जुनच्छवि, अर्जुनध्वजः, अर्जुनपाकी, अर्जुनबदरः, अर्जुनमिश्रः, अर्जुनसखिः, अर्जुनसिंहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0222-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनाभ्रम्
अर्जुन + -अभ्रम्^1 N. of a medicament.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनेश्वरतीर्थम्
अर्जुन + -ईश्वरतीर्थम् N. of a holy place. Śiva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनोपमः|अर्जुनोपम|अर्ज्जुनोपम|अर्ज्जुनोपमः
अर्जुन + -उपमः the teak tree; also शाकद्रुम and महापत्राख्यवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनकाण्ड
अर्जुन + -काण्ड <i>a.</i> having a white stem or appendage. बभ्रोरर्जुनकाण्डस्य<BR> यवस्य ते Av. 2. 8. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनच्छवि|अर्जुनछवि
अर्जुन + -च्छवि <i>a.</i> white, of a white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनध्वजः|अर्जुनध्वज|अर्ज्जुनध्वजः
अर्जुन + -ध्वजः ‘white-bannered’, N. of Hanūmat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनपाकी
अर्जुन + -पाकी N. of a plant and its fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनबदरः
अर्जुन + -बदरः The fibre of the Arjuna plant; अर्जुनबदरा मेखलाः<BR> क्रियन्ताभू । ŚB. on MS. 9. 4. 25<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनमिश्रः|अर्जुनमिश्र
अर्जुन + -मिश्रः Name of a commentator on the Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

