अर्जुनस
अर्जुनस <i>a.</i> [तृणादिगण] Overgrown with Arjuna plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ण|अर्णः
अर्ण <i>a.</i> [ऋ-न]<BR>—1 Being in motion, agitated; restless<BR>—2 Foaming, effervescing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णः|अर्ण
अर्ण + .{@-र्णः@}<BR>—1 A flood, stream; water (Ved.).<BR>—2 The teak tree; Bhāg. 3. 15. 19.<BR>—3 A letter (of the alphabet); पञ्चार्णो मनुरीरितः.<BR>—4 N. of a metre having 10 feet and belonging to the class called Daṇḍaka<BR>—5 Colour; श्रीह्रीविभूत्यात्मवदद्भुतार्णम् Bhāg. 2. 6. 44. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णा
अर्ण + .{@-र्णा@} A river (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णम्
अर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} Tumult or din of battle, confused noise; नृमणा वीरपस्त्योऽर्णा<BR> धीरेव सनिता Rv. 5. 50. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव <i>a.</i> Being agitated, foaming, restless (Ved.); full of water<BR> (Sāy.); ततः समुद्रो अर्णवः Sandhyā.; यात्येव यमुना पूर्णं समुद्रमुदकार्णवम्<BR> Rām. 2. 105. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवः|अर्णव|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव + .{@-वः@} [अर्णांसि सन्ति यस्मिन्, अर्णस्-व सलोपः P. V. 2. 109. Vārt.]<BR>—1 A stream, flood, wave.<BR>—2 The (foaming) sea, ocean; पराहतः शैल इवार्णवाम्बुभिः Ki. 14. 1.<BR> (fig. also), Bhāg. 4. 22. 40;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">Page0223-2</a>]<BR> शोक˚ ocean of grief; so चिन्ता˚; जन˚ ocean of men; संसारार्णवलङ्घनम्<BR> Bh. 3. 10. &c. also नृणामेको गम्यस्त्वमसि पयसामर्णव इव −शिवमहिम्नस्तोत्रम् ▪ of पुष्पदन्ताचार्य.<BR>—3 The ocean of air.<BR>—4 N. of a metre.<BR>—5 N. of the sun or Indra (as givers of water).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्णवान्तः, अर्णवोद्भवः, अर्णवज, अर्णवपोतः, अर्णवयानम्, अर्णवमन्दिरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवान्तः|अर्णवान्त
अर्णव + -अन्तः the extremity of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवोद्भवः|अर्णवोद्भव|अर्ण्णवोद्भव
अर्णव + -उद्भवः —1 N. of a plant अग्निजार (Mar. समुद्रफेंस). —2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

