अर्णवज|अर्णवजः|अर्ण्णवज
अर्णव + -ज <i>a.</i> sea-born, marine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवजम्
अर्णव + -ज + .({@-जम्, -जः@}) cuttle-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवजः|अर्णवज|अर्ण्णवज
अर्णव + -ज + .({@-जम्, -जः@}) cuttle-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवपोतः|अर्णवपोत
अर्णव + -पोतः, -यानम् a boat or ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवयानम्
अर्णव + -पोतः, -यानम् a boat or ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवमन्दिरः|अर्णवमन्दिर
अर्णव + -मन्दिरः<BR>—1 ‘inhabiting the ocean’, N. of Varuṇa, regent of the waters.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्
अर्णस् <i>n.</i> [ऋ-असुन्-नुट् Uṇ. 4. 196]<BR>—1 Water; a wave, flood, stream; सवर्णमर्णः कथमन्यथास्य Śi. 12. 69.<BR>—2 The sea, ocean (usually ˚सः); अभ्राजि शर्धो मरुतो यदर्णसम् Rv. 5. 54. 6.<BR>—3 The ocean of air.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्णोदः, अर्णोभवः, अर्णोरुहम्, अर्णोवृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोदः|अर्णोद|अर्ण्णोद
अर्णस् + -दः<BR>—1 a cloud.<BR>—2 N. of a plant मुस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोभवः|अर्णोभव|अर्ण्णोभव
अर्णस् + -भवः conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोरुहम्
अर्णस् + -रुहम् (अर्णोरुहम्) A lotus; इत्थं सूतप्रसूतां वरगिरमुपकर्ण्यायमर्णोरुहाक्षी U. 7. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोवृत्
अर्णस् + -वृत् <i>a.</i> Ved. including the water; अहिमिन्द्रो अर्णोवृतं वि<BR> वृश्चत् Rv. 2. 19. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्वत्|अर्णस्वन्त्
अर्णस्वत् <i>a.</i> Having much water. ━<i>m.</i> The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तगलः|अर्तगल|अर्त्तगल|अर्त्तगलः
अर्तगलः = आर्तगल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तन|अर्त्तन|अर्त्तनं
अर्तन <i>a.</i> [ऋत्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Blaming, reviling; प्रतिश्रुत्कायाऽअर्तनम् Vāj. 30. 19.<BR>—2 Sorry, grieved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तनम्
अर्तन + .{@-नम्@} Censure, reproach, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तिः|अर्ति|अर्त्ति|अर्त्तिः
अर्तिः <i>f.</i> [अर्द्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Pain, sorrow, grief; पुत्रस्तेऽर्ति परामगात् Mb. 7. 150. 2. शिरोऽर्तिः<BR> head-ache. नान्नं वाञ्छति नो निद्रामुपेत्यर्तिनिपीडितः Suśr.<BR>—2 The end of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तिका|अर्त्तिका
अर्तिका [ऋत्-ङ्वुल्] An elder sister (in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तुक|अर्त्तुक
अर्तुक <i>a.</i> Ved. [ऋत्-बाहु˚ उकच्] Provoking, quarrelsome (स्पर्धक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्
अर्थ् €10 Ā. [अर्थयते, epic. अर्थते; अर्थयांचके, अर्थयिष्यते,<BR> आतर्थत, अर्थयितुम्, अर्थित]<BR>—1 To request, beg, supplicate, ask, entreat, solicit (with two acc.);<BR> त्वामिममर्थमर्थयते Dk. 71; तमाभिक्रम्य सर्वेऽद्य वयं चार्थामहे<BR> वसु Mb.; प्रहस्तमर्थयांचक्रे योद्धुम् Bk. 14. 88.<BR>—2 To strive to obtain, desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थः|अर्थ
अर्थः [In some of its senses from अर्थ्; in others from ऋ-थन्<BR> Uṇ. 2. 4; अर्थते ह्यसौ अर्थिभिः Nir.]<BR>—1 Object, purpose, end and aim; wish, desire; ज्ञातार्थो ज्ञातसंबन्धः<BR> श्रोतुं श्रोता प्रवर्तते; सिद्ध˚, ˚परिपन्थी Mu. 5; ˚वशात् 5. 8;<BR> स्मर्तव्योऽस्मि सत्यर्थे Dk. 117 if it be necessary; Y. 2. 46; M. 4. 6;<BR> oft. used in this sense as the last member of compounds and translated<BR> by ‘for’, ‘intended for’, ‘for the sake of’, ‘on account of’, ‘on behalf of’<BR>, and used like an adj. to qualify nouns; अर्थेन तु नित्यसमासो<BR> विशेष्यनिघ्नता च Vārt.; सन्तानार्थाय विधये R. 1. 34; तां देवतापित्रतिथिक्रियार्थाम्<BR> (धेनुम्) 2. 16; द्विजार्था यवागूः Sk.; यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र<BR> Bg. 3. 9. It mostly occurs in this sense as अर्थम्, अर्थे or अर्थाय<BR> and has an adverbial force;<BR>——(<i>a</i>) किमर्थम् for what purpose, why; यदर्थम् for whom or<BR> which; वेलोपलक्षणार्थम् Ś. 4; तद्दर्शनादभूच्छम्भोर्भूयान्दारार्थमादरः Ku. 6. 13;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) परार्थे प्राज्ञ उत्सृजेत् H. 1. 41;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-1" target="_blank">Page0224-1</a>]<BR> गवार्थे ब्राह्मणार्थे च Pt. 1. 420; मदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः Bg. 1. 9;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) सुखार्थाय Pt. 4. 18; प्रत्याख्याता मया तत्र नलस्यार्थाय<BR> देवताः Nala. 13. 19; ऋतुपर्णस्य चार्थाय 23. 9.<BR>—2 Cause, motive, reason, ground, means; अलुप्तश्च मुनेः क्रियार्थः<BR> R. 2. 55 means or cause; अतोऽर्थात् Ms. 2. 213.<BR>—3 Meaning, sense, signification, import; अर्थ is of 3 kinds:− वाच्य<BR> or expressed, लक्ष्य or indicated (secondary), and व्यङ्ग्य or<BR> suggested; तददोषौ शब्दार्थौ K. P. 1; अर्थो वाच्यश्च लक्ष्यश्च व्यङ्ग्यश्चेति<BR> त्रिधा मतः S. D. 2; वागर्थाविव R. 1. 1; अवेक्ष्य धातोर्गमनार्थमर्थवित् 3. 21.<BR>—4 A thing, object, substance; लक्ष्मणोऽर्थं ततः श्रुत्वा Rām. 7. 46. 18;<BR> अर्थो हि कन्या परकीय एव Ś. 4. 22; that which can be perceived<BR> by the senses, an object of sense; इन्द्रिय˚ H. 1. 146; Ku. 7. 71;<BR> R. 2. 51; न निर्बद्धा उपसर्गा अर्थान्निराहुः Nir.; इन्द्रियेभ्यः परा<BR> ह्यर्था अर्थेभ्यश्च परं मनः Kaṭh. (the objects of sense are five:−<BR> रूप, रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श and शब्द); शब्दः स्पर्शो रसो गन्धो<BR> रूपं चेत्यर्थजातयः Bhāg. 11. 22. 16.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) An affair, business, matter, work; प्राक् प्रतिपन्नोऽयमर्थोऽङ्गराजाय<BR> Ve. 3; अर्थोऽयमर्थान्तरभाव्य एव Ku. 3. 18; अर्थोऽर्थानुबन्धी<BR> Dk. 67; सङ्गीतार्थः Me. 66 business of singing <i>i. e.</i> musical concert<BR> (apparatus of singing); सन्देशार्थाः Me. 5 matters of message, <i>i. e.</i> messages;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Interest, object; स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः Ms. 4. 196; द्वयमेवार्थसाधनम्<BR> R. 1. 19, 2. 21; दुरापेऽर्थे 1. 72; सर्वार्थचिन्तकः Ms. 7. 121;<BR> मालविकायां न मे कश्चिदर्थः M. 3 I have no interest in M.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Subject-matter, contents (as of letters &c.); त्वामवगतार्थं<BR> करिष्यति Mu. 1 will acquaint you with the matter; उत्तरोऽयं लेखार्थः<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; तेन हि अस्य गृहीतार्था भवामि V. 2 if so I should know<BR> its contents; ननु परिगृहीतार्थोऽस्मि कृतो भवता V. 5; तया भवतोऽविनयमन्तरेण<BR> परिगृहीतार्था कृता देवी M. 4 made acquainted with; त्वया गृहीतार्थया<BR> अत्रभवती कथं न वारिता 3; अगृहीतार्थे आवाम् Ś. 6; इति पौरान्<BR> गृहीतार्थान् कृत्वा <i>ibid.</i><BR>—6 Wealth, riches, property, money (said to be of 3 kinds: शुक्ल honestly<BR> got; शबल got by more or less doubtful means, and कृष्ण dishonestly<BR> got); त्यागाय संभृतार्थानाम् R. 1. 7; धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1. 163;<BR> अर्थानामर्जने दुःखम् <i>ibid.</i>; यस्यार्थास्तस्य मित्राणि 1. 3;<BR> तेषामर्थे नियुञ्जीत शूरान् दक्षान् कुलोद्गतान् Ms. 7. 62.<BR>—7 Attainment of riches or worldly prosperity, regarded as one of the<BR> four ends of human existence, the other three being धर्म, काम and<BR> मोक्षः; with अर्थ and काम, धर्म forms the well-known triad;<BR> cf. Ku. 5. 38; अप्यर्थकामौ तस्यास्तां धर्म एव मनीषिणः R. 1. 25.<BR>—8<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Use, advantage, profit, good; तथा हि सर्वे तस्यासन् परार्थैकफला<BR> गुणाः R. 1. 29 for the good of others; अर्थानर्थावुभौ बुद्ध्वा Ms. 8. 24<BR> good and evil; क्षेत्रिणामर्थः 9. 52; यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः<BR> संप्लुतादेके Bg. 2. 46; also व्यर्थ, निरर्थक q. v.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Use, want, need, concern, with instr.; कोऽर्थः पुत्रेण जातेन<BR> Pt. 1 what is the use of a son being born; कश्च तेनार्थः Dk. 59;<BR> कोऽर्थस्तिरश्चां गुणैः Pt. 2. 33 what do brutes care for merits; Bh. 2. 48;<BR> योग्येनार्थः कस्य न स्याज्जनेन Ś. 18. 66; नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो<BR> नाकृतेनेह कश्चन Bg. 3. 18; यदि प्राणैरिहार्थो वो निवर्तध्वम् Rām.<BR> को नु मे जीवितेनार्थः Nala. 12. 65.<BR>—9 Asking, begging; request, suit, petition.<BR>—10 Action, plaint (in law); अर्थ विरागाः पश्यन्ति Rām. 2. 100. 58;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">Page0224-2</a>]<BR> असाक्षिकेषु त्वर्थेषु Ms. 8. 109.<BR>—11 The actual state, fact of the matter; as in यथार्थ, अर्थतः, ˚तत्त्वविद्,<BR> यदर्थेन विनामुष्य पुंस आत्मविपर्ययः Bhāg. 3. 7. 10.<BR>—12 Manner, kind, sort.<BR>—13 Prevention, warding off; मशकार्थो धूमः; prohibition, abolition<BR> (this meaning may also be derived from 1 above).<BR>—14 Price (perhaps an incorrect form for अर्घ).<BR>—15 Fruit, result (फलम्). तस्य नानुभवेदर्थं यस्य हेतोः स रोपितः<BR> Rām. 6. 128. 7; Mb. 12. 175. 5.<BR>—16 N. of a son of धर्म.<BR>—17 The second place from the लग्न (in astr.).<BR>—18 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—19 The category called अपूर्व (in पूर्वमीमांसा); अर्थ इति अपूर्वं<BR> ब्रूमः । ŚB. on MS. 7. 1. 2.<BR>—20 Force (of a statement or an expression); अर्थाच्च सामर्थ्याच्च क्रमो<BR> विधीयते । ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 2. [अर्थात् = by implication].<BR>—21 The need, purpose, sense; व्यवधानादर्थो बलीयान् । ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 23.<BR>—22 Capacity, power; अर्थाद्वा कल्पनैकदेशत्वात् । Ms. 1. 4. 30 (where<BR> Śabara paraphrases अर्थात् by सामर्थ्यात् and states the rule: आख्यातानामर्थं<BR> ब्रुवतां शक्तिः सहकारिणी ।), cf. अर्थोऽभिधेयरैवस्तुप्रयोजननिवृत्तिषु ।<BR> मोक्षकारणयोश्च … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्थातिदेशः, अर्थाधिकारः, अर्थाधिकारिन्, अर्थानुपपत्तिः, अर्थानुयायिन्, अर्थान्तरम्, अर्थान्वित, अर्थाभिधान, अर्थार्थिन्, अर्थालंकारः, अर्थागमः, अर्थापत्तिः, अर्थोत्पत्तिः, अर्थोपक्षेपकः, अर्थोपमा, अर्थोपार्जनम्, अर्थोष्मन्, अर्थौघः, अर्थराशिः, अर्थकर, अर्थकर्मन्, अर्थकाम, अर्थकार्श्यम्, अर्थकाशिन्, अर्थकिल्बिषिन्, अर्थकृच्छ्रम्, अर्थकृत्यम्, अर्थकोविद, अर्थक्रमः, अर्थक्रिया, अर्थगत, अर्थगतिः, अर्थगुणाः, अर्थगृहम्, अर्थगौरवम्, अर्थघ्न, अर्थचित्रम्, अर्थचिन्तक, अर्थचिन्ता, अर्थचिन्तनम्, अर्थजात, अर्थज्ञ, अर्थतत्त्वम्, अर्थदर्शकः, अर्थदर्शनम्, अर्थदूषणम्, अर्थदृश्, अर्थदृष्टिः, अर्थदोषः, अर्थद्वयविधानम्, अर्थनित्य, अर्थनिबन्धन, अर्थनिश्चयः, अर्थपतिः, अर्थपदम्, अर्थपर, अर्थलुब्ध, अर्थप्रकृतिः, अर्थप्रयोगः, अर्थप्राप्त, अर्थप्राप्तत्वम्, अर्थबन्धः, अर्थबुद्धि, अर्थबोधः, अर्थभाज्, अर्थभावनम्, अर्थभृत्, अर्थभेदः, अर्थमात्रम्, अर्थमात्रा, अर्थयुक्त, अर्थलक्षण, अर्थलाभः, अर्थलोभः, अर्थवशः, अर्थवादः, अर्थविकरणम्, अर्थविकल्पः, अर्थविज्ञानम्, अर्थविद्, अर्थविद्या, अर्थविपत्तिः, अर्थविभावक, अर्थविप्रकर्षः, अर्थविशेषणम्, अर्थवृद्धिः, अर्थव्ययः, अर्थशब्दौ, अर्थशालिन्, अर्थशास्त्रम्, अर्थशौचम्, अर्थश्री, अर्थसंस्थानम्, अर्थसंग्रहः, अर्थसंचयः, अर्थसंग्रहः, अर्थसतत्त्वम्, अर्थसमाजः, अर्थसमाहारः, अर्थसंपद्, अर्थसंपादनम्, अर्थसंबन्धः, अर्थसंबन्धिन्, अर्थसाधक, अर्थसारः, अर्थसिद्ध, अर्थसिद्धिः, अर्थहानिः, अर्थहारिन्, अर्थहर, अर्थहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0223-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थातिदेशः
अर्थः + -अतिदेशः Extension (of gender, number &c.) to the objects (as<BR> against words), <i>i. e.</i> to treat a single object as though it were many,<BR> a female as though it were male. (तन्त्रवार्त्तिक 1. 2. 58. 3, 6. 3. 34. 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकारः|अर्थाधिकार
अर्थः + -अधिकारः charge of money, office of treasurer ˚रे न नियोक्तव्यौ H. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकारिन्
अर्थः + -अधिकारिन् <i>m.</i> a treasurer, one charged with financial duties,<BR> finance minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थानुपपत्तिः
अर्थः + -अनुपपत्तिः <i>f.</i> The difficulty of accounting for or explaining<BR> satisfactorily a particular meaning; incongruity of a particular meaning<BR> (तन्त्रवार्त्तिक 4. 3. 42. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थानुयायिन्
अर्थः + -अनुयायिन् <i>a.</i> Following the rules (शास्त्र); तत्त्रिकालहितं<BR> वाक्यं धर्म्यमर्थानुयायि च Rām. 5. 51. 21. -अन्वेषणम् inquiry after a matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तरम्
अर्थः + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 another or different meaning.<BR>—2 another cause or motive; अर्थोऽयमर्थान्तरभाव्य एव Ku. 3. 18.<BR>—3 a new matter or circumstance, new affair.<BR>—4 opposite or antithetical meaning, difference of meaning. ˚न्यासः<BR> a figure of speech in which a general proposition is adduced to support<BR> a particular instance, or a particular instance, to support a general<BR> proposition; it is an inference from particular to general and <i>vice</i><BR> <i>versa</i>; उक्तिरर्थान्तरन्यासः स्यात् सामान्यविशेषयोः । (1) हनूमानब्धिमतरद्<BR> दुष्करं किं महात्मनाम् ॥ (2) गुणवद्वस्तुसंसर्गाद्याति नीचोऽपि गौरवम् ।<BR> पुष्पमालानुषङ्गेण सूत्रं शिरसि धार्यते Kuval.; cf. also K. P. 10<BR> and S. D. 709. (Instances of this figure abound in Sanskrit literature,<BR> especially in the works of Kālidāsa, Māgha and Bhāravi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्वित
अर्थः + -अन्वित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 rich, wealthy.<BR>—2 significant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाभिधान
अर्थः + -अभिधान <i>a.</i> —1 That whose name is connected with the purpose<BR> to be served by it; अर्थाभिधानं प्रयोजनसम्बद्धमभिधानं यस्य, यथा<BR> पुरोडाशकपालमिति पुरोडाशार्थं कपालं पुरोडाशकपालम् । ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 26.<BR>—2 Expression or denotation of the desired meaning (वार्त्तिक 3. 1. 2. 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थार्थिन्
अर्थः + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> one who longs for or strives to get wealth or gain<BR> any object. अर्थार्थीं जीवलोकोऽयम् । आर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी Bg. 7. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थालंकारः|अर्थालङ्कार
अर्थः + -अलंकारः^1 a figure of speech determined by and dependent on the<BR> sense, and not on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">Page0225-1</a>]<BR> sound (opp. शब्दालंकार). अलंकारशेखर of केशवमिश्र mentions<BR> (verse 29) fourteen types of अर्थालंकारs as follows:− उपमारूपकोत्प्रेक्षाः<BR> समासोक्तिरपह्नुतिः । समाहितं स्वभावश्च विरोधः सारदीपकौ ॥ सहोक्तिरन्यदेशत्वं<BR> विशेषोक्तिर्विभावना । एवं स्युरर्थालकाराश्चतुर्दश न चापरे ॥<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0224-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थागमः|अर्थागम
अर्थः + -आगमः<BR>—1 acquisition of wealth, income; ˚गमाय स्यात् Pt. 1. cf. also अर्थागमो<BR> नित्यमरोगिता च H.<BR>—2 collection of property.<BR>—3 conveying of sense: S. D. 737.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापत्तिः|अर्थापत्ति
अर्थः + -आपत्तिः <i>f.</i> [अर्थस्य अनुक्तार्थस्य आपत्तिः सिद्धिः]<BR>—1 an inference from circumstances, presumption, implication, one of the<BR> five sources of knowledge or modes of proof, according to the Mīmāṃsakas.<BR> It is ‘deduction of a matter from that which could not else be’; it is<BR> ‘assumption of a thing, not itself perceived but necessarily implied by another which is seen, heard, or proved’<BR>; it is an inference used to account<BR> for an apparent inconsistency; as in the familiar instance पीनो देवदत्तो<BR> दिवा न भुङ्क्ते the apparent inconsistency between ‘fatness’ and ‘not eating by day’<BR> is accounted for by the inference of his ‘eating by night’.<BR> पीनत्वविशिष्टस्य देवदत्तस्य रात्रिभोजित्वरूपार्थस्य शब्दानुक्तस्यापि<BR> आपत्तिः. It is defined by Śabara as दृष्टः श्रुतो वार्थोऽन्यथा नोपपद्यते<BR> इत्यर्थकल्पना । यथा जीवति देवदत्ते गृहाभावदर्शनेन बहिर्भावस्यादृष्टस्य<BR> कल्पना ॥ MS. 1. 1. 5. It may be seen from the words दृष्टः and<BR> श्रुतः in the above definition, that Śabara has suggested two varieties<BR> of अर्थापत्ति <i>viz.</i> दृष्टार्थापत्ति and श्रुतार्थापत्ति. The<BR> illustration given by him, however, is of दृष्टार्थापत्ति only. The<BR> former <i>i. e.</i> दृष्टार्थापत्ति consists in the presumption of some<BR> अदृष्ट अर्थ to account for some दृष्ट अर्थ (or अर्थs) which<BR> otherwise becomes inexplicable. The latter, on the other hand, consists<BR> in the presumption of some अर्थ through अश्रुत शब्द to account<BR> for some श्रुत अर्थ (<i>i. e.</i> some statement). This peculiarity of<BR> श्रुतार्थापत्ति is clearly stated in the following couplet; यत्र<BR> त्वपरिपूर्णस्य वाक्यस्यान्वयसिद्धये । शब्दोऽध्याह्रियते तत्र श्रुतार्थापत्तिरिष्यते ॥<BR> Mānameyodaya p. 129 (ed. by K. Raja, Adyar, 1933). Strictly speaking<BR> it is no separate mode of proof; it is only a case of अनुमान and<BR> can be proved by a व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति; cf. Tarka K. 17 and S. D. 460.<BR>—2 a figure of speech (according to some rhetoricians) in which a relevant<BR> assertion suggests an inference not actually connected with the the subject<BR> in hand, or <i>vice versa</i>; it corresponds to what is popularly called<BR> कैमुतिकन्याय or दण्डापूपन्याय; <i>e. g.</i> हारोऽयं हरिणाक्षीणां<BR> लुण्ठति स्तनमण्डले । मुक्तानामप्यवस्थेयं के वयं स्मरकिङ्कराः Amaru. 100;<BR> अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43;<BR> S. D. thus defines the figure:− दण्डापूपिकन्यायार्थागमोऽर्थापत्तिरिष्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोत्पत्तिः
अर्थः + -उत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> acquisition of wealth; so ˚उपार्जनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपक्षेपकः|अर्थोपक्षेपक
अर्थः + -उपक्षेपकः an introductory scene (in dramas); अर्थोपक्षेपकाः<BR> पञ्च S. D. 308. They are विष्कम्भ, चूलिका, अङ्कास्य, अङ्कावतार, प्रवेशक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपमा
अर्थः + -उपमा a simile dependent on sense and not on sound; see under उपमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपार्जनम्
अर्थः + -उपार्जनम् Acquiring wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोष्मन्
अर्थः + -उष्मन् <i>m.</i> the glow or warmth of wealth; अर्थोष्मणा विरहितः पुरुषः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">Page0225-2</a>]<BR> स एव Bh. 2. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थौघः|अर्थौघ
अर्थः + -ओघः, -राशिः treasure, hoard of money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थराशिः|अर्थराशि
अर्थः + -ओघः, -राशिः treasure, hoard of money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर
अर्थः + -कर (-री <i>f.</i>), {@-कृत्^1@} <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bringing in wealth, enriching; अर्थकरी च विद्या H. Pr. 3.<BR>—2 useful, advantageous.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर्मन्
अर्थः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 a principal action (opp. गुणकर्मन्).<BR>—2 (as opposed to प्रतिपत्तिकर्मन्), A fruitful act (as opposed to<BR> mere disposal or प्रतिपत्ति); अर्थकर्म वा कर्तृसंयोगात् स्रग्वत् ।<BR> MS. 4. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थः + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of wealth. (˚मौ dual), wealth and<BR> (sensual) desire or pleasure; अप्यर्थकामौ तस्यास्तां धर्म एव मनीषिणः<BR> R. 1. 25. हत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव Bg. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकार्श्यम्
अर्थः + -कार्श्यम् Poverty. निर्बन्धसंजातरुषार्थकार्श्यम्^1अचिन्तयित्वा गुरुणाहमुक्तः R. 5. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाशिन्
अर्थः + -काशिन् <i>a.</i> Only apparently of utility (not really).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकिल्बिषिन्
अर्थः + -किल्बिषिन् <i>a.</i> dishonest in money-matters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृच्छ्रम्
अर्थः + -कृच्छ्रम्<BR>—1 a difficult matter.<BR>—2 pecuniary difficulty; व्यसने वार्थकृच्छ्रे वा Rām. 4. 7. 9; Mb. 3. 2. 19;<BR> cf. also Kau. A. 1. 15 न मुह्येदर्थकृच्छ्रेषु Nīti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृत्यम्
अर्थः + -कृत्यम् doing or execution of a business; अभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Me. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकोविद
अर्थः + -कोविद <i>a.</i> Expert in matter, experienced. उवाच रामो धर्मात्मा<BR> पुनरप्यर्थकोविदः Rām. 6. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थक्रमः|अर्थक्रम
अर्थः + -क्रमः due order or sequence of purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थक्रिया
अर्थः + -क्रिया<BR>——(<i>a</i>) An implied act, an act which is to be performed as a matter of<BR> course (as opposed to शब्दोक्तक्रिया); असति शब्दोक्ते अर्थक्रिया भवति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 12.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A purposeful action. (see अर्थकर्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगत
अर्थः + -गत <i>a.</i> —1 based on the sense (as a दोष). —2 devoid of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगतिः|अर्थगति
अर्थः + -गतिः understanding the sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगुणाः
अर्थः + -गुणाः cf. भाविकत्वं सुशब्दत्वं पर्यायोक्तिः सुधर्मिता । चत्वारोऽर्थगुणाः<BR> प्रोक्ताः परे त्वत्रैव संगताः ॥ अलंकारशेखर 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगृहम्
अर्थः + -गृहम् A treasury. Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगौरवम्
अर्थः + -गौरवम् depth of meaning; भारवेरर्थगौरवम् Udb.; Ki. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थघ्न
अर्थः + -घ्न <i>a.</i> (-घ्नी <i>f.</i>) extravagant, wasteful, prodigal;<BR> सुरापी व्याधिता धूर्ता वन्ध्यार्थघ्न्यप्रियंवदा Y. 1. 73; व्याधिता<BR> वाधिवेत्तव्या हिंस्रार्थघ्नी च सर्वदा Ms. 9. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थचित्रम्
अर्थः + -चित्रम् ‘variety in sense’, a pun, Kāvyaprakāśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थचिन्तक
अर्थः + -चिन्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 thinking of profit.<BR>—2 having charge of affairs; सर्वार्थचिन्तकः Ms. 7. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थचिन्ता
अर्थः + -चिन्ता, -चिन्तनम् charge or administration of (royal) affairs;<BR> मन्त्री स्यादर्थचिन्तायाम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थचिन्तनम्
अर्थः + -चिन्ता, -चिन्तनम् charge or administration of (royal) affairs;<BR> मन्त्री स्यादर्थचिन्तायाम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थजात
अर्थः + -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 full of meaning.<BR>—2 wealthy (जातधन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थजातम्
अर्थः + -जात + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 a collection of things.<BR>—2 large amount of wealth, considerable property; Dk. 63; Ś. 6; ददाति<BR> च नित्यमर्थजातम् Mk. 2. 7.<BR>—3 all matters; कवय इव महीपाश्चिन्तयन्त्यर्थजातम् Śi. 11. 6.<BR>—4 its own meaning; वहन्द्वयीं यद्यफलेऽर्थजाते Ki. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थज्ञ
अर्थः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the sense or purpose; अर्थज्ञ इत्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतत्त्वम्
अर्थः + -तत्त्वम्<BR>—1 the real truth, the fact of the matter; योऽर्थतत्त्वमविज्ञाय क्रोधस्यैव<BR> वशं गतः H. 4. 94.<BR>—2 the real nature or cause of anything. -द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 yielding wealth; Dk. 41.<BR>—2 advantageous, productive of good, useful.<BR>—3 liberal, munificent Ms. 2. 109.<BR>—4 favourable, compliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतत्त्वदः
अर्थः + -तत्त्वम् + .({@-दः@}) N. of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदर्शकः|अर्थदर्शक
अर्थः + -दर्शकः ‘one who sees law-suits’; a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदर्शनम्
अर्थः + -दर्शनम् perception of objects; कुरुते दीप इवार्थदर्शनम्<BR> Ki. 2. 33; Dk. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदूषणम्
अर्थः + -दूषणम्<BR>—1 extravagance, waste; H. 3. 108; Ms. 7. 48.<BR>—2 unjust seizure of property or withholding what is due.<BR>—3 finding fault with the meaning. —4 spoiling of anotherʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदृश्
अर्थः + -दृश् <i>f.</i> Consideration of truth;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">Page0226-1</a>]<BR> क्षेमं त्रिलोकगुरुरर्थदृशं च यच्छन् Bhāg. 10. 86. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदृष्टिः|अर्थदृष्टि
अर्थः + -दृष्टिः Seeing profit; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदोषः|अर्थदोष
अर्थः + -दोषः a literary fault or blemish with regard to the sense, one<BR> of the four <i>doṣas</i> or blemishes of literary composition, the other<BR> three being पददोष, पदांशदोष, वाक्यदोष; for definitions &c.<BR> see K. P. 7. अलंकारशेखर of केशवमिश्र who mentions eight types<BR> of <i>doṣas</i> as follows: अष्टार्थदोषाः विरस, -ग्राम्य, -व्याहत, -खिन्नताः ।<BR> -हीना, -धिका, सदृक्साम्यं देशादीनां विरोधि च ॥ 17<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थद्वयविधानम्
अर्थः + -द्वयविधानम् Injunction of two ideas or senses; विधाने चार्थद्वयविधानं<BR> दोषः ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनित्य
अर्थः + -नित्य <i>a.</i> = अर्थप्रधान Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनिबन्धन
अर्थः + -निबन्धन <i>a.</i> dependent on wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनिश्चयः|अर्थनिश्चय
अर्थः + -निश्चयः determination, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपतिः|अर्थपति
अर्थः + -पतिः<BR>—1 ‘the lord of riches’, a king^1; किंचिद् विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R. 2. 46, 1. 59, 9. 3, 18. 1;<BR> Pt. 1. 74.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपदम्
अर्थः + -पदम् N. of the Vārt. on Pāṇini; ससूत्रवृत्त्यर्थपदं महार्थं<BR> ससंग्रहं सिद्ध्यति वै कपीन्द्रः Rām. 7. 36. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपर
अर्थः + -पर, -लुब्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 intent on gaining wealth, greedy of wealth, covetous.<BR>—2 niggardly, parsimonious; हिंस्रा दयालुरपि चार्थपरा वदान्या Bh. 2. 47;<BR> Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलुब्ध
अर्थः + -पर, -लुब्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 intent on gaining wealth, greedy of wealth, covetous.<BR>—2 niggardly, parsimonious; हिंस्रा दयालुरपि चार्थपरा वदान्या Bh. 2. 47;<BR> Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रकृतिः|अर्थप्रकृति
अर्थः + -प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i> the leading source or occasion of the grand object<BR> in a drama; (the number of these ‘sources’ is five:− बीजं बिन्दुः पताका<BR> च प्रकरी कार्यमेव च । अर्थप्रकृतयः पञ्च ज्ञात्वा योज्या यथाविधि S. D. 317.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रयोगः|अर्थप्रयोग
अर्थः + -प्रयोगः<BR>—1 usury.<BR>—2 administration of the affairs (of a state)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्राप्त
अर्थः + -प्राप्त <i>a.</i> derived or understood from the sense included as<BR> a matter of course, implied; परिसमाप्तिः शब्दार्थः । परिसमाप्त्यामर्थप्राप्तत्वादारम्भस्य ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्राप्तत्वम्
अर्थः + -प्राप्तत्वम् Implication^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by anonymous user on 20240627. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/AP90/issues/24#issuecomment-907699250. note: under -prayogaH -tvam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबन्धः|अर्थबन्ध
अर्थः + -बन्धः<BR>—1 arrangement of words, composition, text; stanza, verse; संचिन्त्य<BR> गीतक्षममर्थबन्धम् Ś. 7. 5; ललितार्थबन्धम् V. 2. 14 put or expressed<BR> in elegant words.<BR>—2 connection (of the soul) with the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबुद्धि
अर्थः + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबोधः|अर्थबोध
अर्थः + -बोधः indication of the (real) import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभाज्
अर्थः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> entitled to a share in the division of property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभावनम्
अर्थः + -भावनम् Deliberation over a subject (Pātañjala Yogadarśana 1. 28).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभृत्
अर्थः + -भृत् <i>a.</i> receiving high wages (as a servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभेदः|अर्थभेद
अर्थः + -भेदः distinction or difference of meaning; अर्थभेदेन शब्दभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थमात्रम्
अर्थः + -मात्रम्, -मात्रा<BR>—1 property, wealth; Pt. 2.<BR>—2 the whole sense or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थमात्रा
अर्थः + -मात्रम्, -मात्रा<BR>—1 property, wealth; Pt. 2.<BR>—2 the whole sense or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थयुक्त
अर्थः + -युक्त <i>a.</i> significant, full of यस्यार्थयुक्तं meaning;<BR> गिरिराजशब्दं कुर्वन्ति Ku. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलक्षण
अर्थः + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> As determined by the purpose or need (as opposed<BR> to शब्दलक्षण); लोके कर्मार्थलक्षणम् Ms. 11. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलाभः|अर्थलाभ
अर्थः + -लाभः acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलोभः|अर्थलोभ
अर्थः + -लोभः avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवशः|अर्थवश
अर्थः + -वशः power in the form of discrimination and knowledge. अर्थवशात्<BR> सप्तरूपविनिवृत्ताम् Sāv. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवादः|अर्थवाद
अर्थः + -वादः<BR>—1 declaration of any purpose.<BR>—2 affirmation, declaratory assertion, an explanatory remark, <i>exegesis</i>;<BR> speech or assertion having a certain object; a sentence. (It usually recommends<BR> a विधि or precept by stating the good arising from its proper observance,<BR> and the evils arising from its omission, and also by adducing historical<BR> instances in its support; स्तुतिर्निन्दा परकृतिः पुराकल्प इत्यर्थवादः<BR> Gaut. S.; said by Laugākṣi to be of 3 kinds:− गुणवादो विरोधे स्यादनु<BR> वादोऽवधारिते । भूतार्थवादस्तद्धानादर्थवादस्त्रिधा मतः; the last<BR> kind includes many varieties.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">Page0226-2</a>]<BR>—3 one of the six means of finding out the <i>tātparya</i> (real aim and<BR> object) of any work.<BR>—4 praise, eulogy; अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं तु मे कंचित्कथय U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविकरणम्
अर्थः + -विकरणम् = अर्थविक्रिया change of meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविकल्पः|अर्थविकल्प
अर्थः + -विकल्पः<BR>—1 deviation from truth, perversion of fact.<BR>—2 prevarication; also ˚वैकल्यम्^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविज्ञानम्
अर्थः + -विज्ञानम् comprehending the sense, one of the six exercises of<BR> the understanding (धीगुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविद्
अर्थः + -विद् <i>a.</i> sensible, wise, sagacious. भुङ्क्ते तदपि तच्चान्यो<BR> मधुहेवार्थविन्मधु Bhāg. 11. 8. 15. विवक्षतामर्थविदस्तत्क्षणप्रतिसंहृताम् Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविद्या
अर्थः + -विद्या knowledge of practical life; Mb. 7<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविपत्तिः|अर्थविपत्ति
अर्थः + -विपत्तिः Failing of an aim; समीक्ष्यतां चार्थविपत्तिमार्गताम्<BR> Rām. 2. 19. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविभावक
अर्थः + -विभावक <i>a.</i> money-giver; विप्रेभ्योऽर्थविभावकः Mb. 3. 33. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविप्रकर्षः|अर्थविप्रकर्ष
अर्थः + -विप्रकर्षः difficulty in the comprehension of the sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविशेषणम्
अर्थः + -विशेषणम् a reprehensive repetition of something uttered by another; S. D. 490.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवृद्धिः|अर्थवृद्धि
अर्थः + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> accumulation of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्ययः|अर्थव्यय
अर्थः + -व्ययः expenditure; ˚ज्ञ <i>a.</i> conversant with money-matters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशब्दौ
अर्थः + -शब्दौ Word and sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशालिन्
अर्थः + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> Wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशास्त्रम्
अर्थः + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 the science of wealth (political economy).<BR>—2 science of polity, political science, politics; अर्थशास्त्रविशारदं<BR> सुधन्वानमुपाध्यायम् Rām. 2. 100. 14; Dk. 120; इह खलु अर्थशास्त्रकारास्त्रिविधां<BR> सिद्धिमुपवर्णयन्ति Mu. 3; ˚व्यवहारिन् one dealing with politics,<BR> a politician; Mu. 5.<BR>—3 science giving precepts on general conduct, the science of practical life; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशौचम्
अर्थः + -शौचम् purity or honesty in money-matters; सर्वेषां चैव शौचानामर्थशौचं<BR> परं स्मृतं Ms. 5. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थश्री
अर्थः + -श्री Great wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंस्थानम्
अर्थः + -संस्थानम्<BR>—1 accumulation of wealth.<BR>—2 treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंग्रहः|अर्थसङ्ग्रह
अर्थः + -संग्रहः, -संचयः accumulation or acquisition of wealth, treasure,<BR> property. कोशेनाश्रयणीयत्वमिति तस्यार्थसंग्रहः R. 17. 60. कुदेशमासाद्य<BR> कुतोऽर्थसंचयः H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंचयः|अर्थसञ्चय|अर्थसंचय
अर्थः + -संग्रहः, -संचयः accumulation or acquisition of wealth, treasure,<BR> property. कोशेनाश्रयणीयत्वमिति तस्यार्थसंग्रहः R. 17. 60. कुदेशमासाद्य<BR> कुतोऽर्थसंचयः H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंग्रहः|अर्थसङ्ग्रह
अर्थः + -संग्रहः a book on Mīmāṃsā by Laugākṣi Bhāskara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसतत्त्वम्
अर्थः + -सतत्त्वम् truth; किं पुनरत्रार्थसतत्त्वम् । देवा ज्ञातुमर्हन्ति<BR> Mbh. or P. VIII. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसमाजः|अर्थसमाज
अर्थः + -समाजः aggregate of causes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसमाहारः|अर्थसमाहार
अर्थः + -समाहारः<BR>—1 treasure.<BR>—2 acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंपद्
अर्थः + -संपद् <i>f.</i> accomplishment of a desired object; उपेत्य संघर्षमिवार्थसंपदः Ki. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंपादनम्
अर्थः + -संपादनम् Carrying out of an affair; Ms. 7. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंबन्धः|अर्थसम्बन्ध|अर्थसंबन्ध
अर्थः + -संबन्धः connection of the sense with the word or sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंबन्धिन्|अर्थसम्बन्धिन्
अर्थः + -संबन्धिन् <i>a.</i> Concerned or interested in an affair; Ms. 8. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसाधक
अर्थः + -साधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 accomplishing any object.<BR>—2 bringing any matter to a conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसारः|अर्थसार
अर्थः + -सारः considerable wealth; Pt. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्ध
अर्थः + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> understood from the very context (though not expressed<BR> in words), inferable from the connection of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्धिः|अर्थसिद्धि
अर्थः + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> fulfilment of a desired object, success. द्वारमिवार्थसिद्धेः R. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहानिः|अर्थहानि
अर्थः + -हानिः Loss of wealth<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहारिन्
अर्थः + -हारिन् <i>a.</i> stealing money Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहर
अर्थः + -हर <i>a.</i> inheriting wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहीन
अर्थः + -हीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deprived of wealth, poor.<BR>—2 unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR>—3 failing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतः
अर्थतः <i>ind.</i> [अर्थ-तसिल्]<BR>—1 With reference to the meaning or a particular object; यच्चार्थतो<BR> गौरवम् Māl. 1. 7 depth of meaning; दधति परिस्फुटमर्थतोऽभिधानम् Śi. 7. 28.<BR>—2 In fact, really, truly; न नामतः केवलमर्थतोऽपि Śi. 3. 56.<BR> इत्यादिष्टमर्थतो भवति Mv. 3.<BR>—3 For the sake of money, gain or profit; ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं<BR> लोकोऽर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14.<BR>—4 On account of, by reason of.<BR>—5 By reason of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">Page0227-1</a>]<BR> wealth or a particular purpose; अर्थतः पुरुषो नारी या नारी सार्थतः<BR> पुमान् Mk. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना Request, entreaty, suit, petition; अर्थना मयि भवद्भिरिवास्यै<BR> कर्तुमर्हति मयाऽपि भवत्सु N. 5. 112. ब्राह्मणोऽनर्थनाधृतिः Mb. 13. 60. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wealthy, rich; तेनार्थवाँल्लोभपराङ्मुखेन R. 14. 23.<BR>—2 Significant, full of sense or meaning; वाक्यमर्थवदव्यग्रस्तमुवाच<BR> दशाननम् Rām. 5. 51. 1. अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः Ś. 5; Pt. 1. 136;<BR> Ki. 3. 51.<BR>—3 Having meaning; अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकम् P. I. 2. 45.<BR>—4 Serving some purpose; successful, useful; स पुमानर्थवज्जन्मा<BR> Ki. 11 62, 10. 62. <i>adv.</i> According to a purpose; विण्मूत्रोत्सर्गशुद्ध्यर्थं<BR> मृद्वार्यादेयमर्थवत् Ms. 5. 134; Y. 3. 2. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवान्
अर्थवत् + .({@-वान्@}) A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्ता
अर्थवत्ता Wealth, property; Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थात्
अर्थात् <i>ind.</i> (abl. of अर्थ)<BR>—1 As a matter of course, of course, in fact; मूषिकेण दण्डो भक्षित<BR> इत्यनेन तत्सहचरितमपूपभक्षणमर्थादायातं भवति S. D. 10.<BR>—2 According to the circumstances or state of the case; as a matter of fact.<BR>—3 That is to say, namely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थात्कृतम्
अर्थात् + .{@-कृतम्@} Performed through the force of implication or as a matter<BR> of course; न चार्थात्कृतं चोदकः प्रापयति ŚB. on MS. 5. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापय्
अर्थापय् = अर्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिकः|अर्थिक
अर्थिकः [अर्थयते इत्यर्थी कन्]<BR>—1 A crier, watchman.<BR>—2 Especially, a minstrel whose duty it is to announce (by song &c.) the<BR> different fixed periods of the day, such as the hours of rising, sleeping, eating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित
अर्थित <i>p. p.</i> Requested, asked, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थितम्
अर्थित + .{@-तम्@} [भावे-क्त] Wish, desire; supplication, petition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिता
अर्थिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 State or condition of a supplicant, begging, request; न व्यहन्यत<BR> कदाचिदर्थिता R. 11. 2; M. 3; K. 141; तेनार्थित्वं त्वयि विधिवशाद्<BR> दूरबन्धुर्गतोऽहम् Me. 6; Mv. 2. 9.<BR>—2 Wish, desire; Bhāg. 4. 3. 8. यद्यर्थिता R. 14. 42; अनर्थित्वान्मनुष्याणाम्<BR> Pt. 1. 142; Ki. 13. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित्वम्
अर्थिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 State or condition of a supplicant, begging, request; न व्यहन्यत<BR> कदाचिदर्थिता R. 11. 2; M. 3; K. 141; तेनार्थित्वं त्वयि विधिवशाद्<BR> दूरबन्धुर्गतोऽहम् Me. 6; Mv. 2. 9.<BR>—2 Wish, desire; Bhāg. 4. 3. 8. यद्यर्थिता R. 14. 42; अनर्थित्वान्मनुष्याणाम्<BR> Pt. 1. 142; Ki. 13. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> [अर्थ्-इनि]<BR>—1 Seeking to gain or obtain, wishing for, desirous of, with instr. or<BR> in comp. अर्थिनश्च राजानो हिरण्येन भवन्ति । Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1.<BR> etc. तुषैरर्थिनः Dk. 132; कोषदण्डाभ्याम्˚ Mu. 5; को वधेन ममार्थी<BR> स्यात् Mb.; Ve. 6. 25; अर्थार्थी Pt. 1. 4, अर्थार्थी जीवलोकोऽयम् Pt. 1. 9.<BR>—2 Entreating or begging anyone (with gen.); सर्वत्र मण्डूकवधः क्रियतामिति<BR> यो मयाऽर्थी Mb. 3. 192. 24. अर्थी वररुचिर्मेऽस्तु Ks. 3 Possessed<BR> of desires; अनर्थी प्रार्थनावहः R. 10. 18. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who asks, begs or solicits; a beggar, suppliant, suitor; यथाकामार्चितार्थिनाम्<BR> R. 1. 6, 2. 64, 4. 31, 9. 27; कोऽर्थी गतो गौरवम् Pt. 1. 146; One<BR> who asks for a girl in marriage, a wooer; Y. 1. 60; कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म<BR> भवतामास्ते वयं चार्थिनः Mv. 1. 30.<BR>—2 (In law) A plaintiff, complainant, prosecutor; स धर्मस्थसखः शश्वदर्थि<BR> प्रत्यर्थिनां स्वयम् । ददर्श संशयच्छेद्यान् व्यवहारानतन्द्रितः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">Page0227-2</a>]<BR> R. 17. 39; अर्थी कार्यं निवेदयेत् Śukra. 4. 575; सभान्तः साक्षिणः<BR> प्राप्तानर्थिप्रत्यर्थिसन्निधौ Ms. 8. 79.<BR>—3 A servant, follower.<BR>—4 A master or lord.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्थिभावः, अर्थिसात्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिभावः|अर्थिभाव
अर्थिन् + -भावः state of a suppliant, begging, request; कं याचे यत्र<BR> तत्र ध्रुवमनवसरग्रस्त एवार्थिभावः Māl. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिसात्
अर्थिन् + -सात् <i>adv.</i> at the disposal of beggars; विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः<BR> N. 1. 16. cf. अर्थी तु याचको विद्यात् यस्यार्थः स च अर्थवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीय
अर्थीय <i>a.</i> [अर्थ-छ] (In comp.)<BR>—1 Destined or intended for, doomed to suffer; शरीरं यातनार्थीयम् Ms. 12. 16.<BR>—2 Belonging or relating to; कर्म चैव तदर्थीयम् Bg. 17. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य <i>a.</i> [अर्थ्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 Fit to be asked or sought for.<BR>—2 [अर्थादनपेतः, अर्थ-यत्] Fit, proper, suitable; अर्थ्यो विरोधः Mv. 2. 7.<BR>—3 Appropriate, not deviating from the sense, significant; स्तुत्यं स्तुतिभिरर्थ्याभिरुपतस्थे<BR> सरस्वती R. 4. 6, 1. 59; Ku. 2. 3.<BR>—4 Rich, wealthy.<BR>—5 Wise, intelligent.<BR>—6 True, real; अर्थ्यं विज्ञापयन्नेव भरतं सत्यविक्रमम् Rām. 6. 127. 25.<BR>—7 Expert in getting money (अर्थसंपादनचतुर); अर्थी येनार्थकृत्येन<BR> संव्रजत्यविचारयन् । तमर्थमर्थशास्त्रज्ञाः प्राहुरर्थ्याः सुलक्ष्मण ।<BR> Rām. 3. 43. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्यम्
अर्थ्य + .{@-र्थ्यम्@} Red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् €1 P. [अर्दति, आनर्द, आर्दीत्, अर्दितुम्, अर्दित or अर्ण]<BR>—1 To afflict, torment; strike, hurt, kill; रक्षःसहस्राणि चतुर्दशादीत्<BR> Bk. 12. 56, see <i>caus.</i> below.<BR>—2 To beg, request, ask; निर्गलिताम्बुगर्भं शरद्घनं नार्दति चातकोऽपि R. 5. 17.<BR>—3 To go, to move, be agitated or moved; be scattered (as dust); आर्दन्<BR> धन्वानि सरयन्त आपः Rv. 4. 17. 2; fly in pieces, dissolve; श्लोणया<BR> काटमर्दति Av. 12. 4. 3. (The past participle is usually अर्दित,<BR> but अर्ण when the root is preceded by अभि, नि, वि, सम्; cf. अर्देः<BR> संनिविभ्यः अभेश्चाविदूर्ये P. VII. 2. 24-5). ━<i>Caus.</i> or €10 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To afflict, torment, distress; तत एनं महावेगैरर्दयामास<BR> तोमरैः Mb.; कामार्दित, कोप˚, भय˚ &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To strike, hurt, injure, kill; येनार्दिदत् दैत्यपुरं पिनाकी<BR> Bk. 2. 42, 9. 19, 15. 90.<BR>—2 To stir up, rouse, agitate, shake vehemently, make agitated or restless;<BR> अभि क्रन्द स्तनयार्दयोदधिम् Av. 4. 15. 6.<BR>—3 To distort; अर्दयित्वानिलो वक्त्रमर्दितं जनयत्यतः Suśr.<BR> ━<i>With</i> {@अति@} to torment excessively, fall upon or attack; अत्यार्दीत्<BR> वालिनः पुत्रम् (v. l. अभ्यार्दीत्) Bk. 15. 115.<BR>━{@अभि@} to distress, afflict, pain, oppress; अभ्यर्दितो वृषलः<BR> (शीतेन पीडितः) P. VII. 2. 25. Sk.<BR>━{@नि@} Ved. to stream forth, flow out.<BR>━{@प्र@} to overwork, to work or exert oneself beyond measure; to<BR> cause to flow away.<BR>━{@प्रति@} to oppress or press hard in return, assail in return, return an attack.<BR>━{@वि@} Ved. to go or move away; to oppress, harass, pain. ━<i>caus.</i><BR> to cause to be scattered or dissolved, destroy, annihilate.<BR>━{@सम्@} <i>caus.</i> to pain greatly, wound, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्दनः|अर्द्दन
अर्दन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distressing, afflicting, tormenting; पुर˚, बल˚.<BR>—2 Moving restlessly, being agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनः|अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्द्दन
अर्दन + .{@-नः@} N. of Śiva; Mbh. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनम्
अर्दन + .{@-नम्@} [भावे-ल्युट्] Distressing, afflicting; pain,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">Page0228-1</a>]<BR> trouble, anxiety, disturbance, excitement, agitation, restlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनम्
अर्दन + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Going, moving.<BR>—2 Asking, begging.<BR>—3 Killing, hurting, giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दना|अर्द्दना
अर्दन + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Going, moving.<BR>—2 Asking, begging.<BR>—3 Killing, hurting, giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0227-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनिः|अर्दनि
अर्दनिः<BR>—1 Asking, begging.<BR>—2 Sickness, disease.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दित|अर्दितं|अर्द्दित|अर्द्दितः
अर्दित <i>p. p.</i> [अर्द्-क्त] Tormented, afflicted; begged &c.<BR> {@-तम्@} A disease, spasm of the jaw-bones, tetanus or hemiflegia (paralysis of the muscles on one side of the face and neck).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दितिन्|अर्द्दितिन्
अर्दितिन् <i>a.</i> [अर्दितमस्त्यस्य-इनि] Suffering from the spasms of jaw-bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध (Written also as अर्द्ध) <i>a.</i> [ऋध्-णिच्-अच्; according<BR> to Nir. from धृ, or ऋध्] Half, forming a half (divided into 2 parts);<BR> अर्ध-अर्ध the one half-the other half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्ध
अर्ध (Written also as अर्द्ध) <i>a.</i> [ऋध्-णिच्-अच्; according<BR> to Nir. from धृ, or ऋध्] Half, forming a half (divided into 2 parts);<BR> अर्ध-अर्ध the one half-the other half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धः|अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः
अर्ध (Written also as अर्द्ध) + .{@-र्धः@} [ऋध्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A place, region, country; house, habitation (Ved.).<BR>—2 Increase (वृद्धि).<BR>—3 Wind.<BR>—4 A part, portion, side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धम्
अर्ध (Written also as अर्द्ध) + .{@-र्धम्, -र्धः@}<BR>—1 A half, half portion; पचाति नेमो न हि पक्षदर्धः Rv. 10. 27. 18.<BR> सर्वनाशे समुत्पन्ने अर्धं त्यजति पण्डितः; गतमर्धं दिवसस्य<BR> V. 2; पूर्वार्धः first half; so उत्तर˚ latter half; दक्षिण˚<BR> southern half (half on the right side); so अवर˚, जघन˚, पर˚, ग्राम˚<BR> &c.; यदर्धे विच्छिन्नम् Ś. 1. 9 divided in half; ऋज्वायतार्धम्<BR> M. 27; R. 3. 59, 12. 99; रात्रौ तदर्धं गतम् Bh. 3. 107; one part<BR> of two, a part, partly^1 (Ved.);<BR>—2 Nearness, proximity; see अर्धदेव. (अर्ध may be compounded<BR> with almost every noun and adjective; as first member of compound with<BR> nouns it means ‘a half of’ and forms an एकदेशिसमास or तत्पुरुष;<BR> ˚कायः = अर्धं कायस्य; ˚पिप्पली, ˚मार्गः; ˚पुरुषः &c.; with adjectives,<BR> it has an adverbial force; ˚श्याम half dark; ˚भुक्त half eaten;<BR> so ˚पिष्ट, ˚पूर्ण &c.; with numeral adjectives it may mean either<BR> ‘a half of’ or ‘with an additional half’; ˚शतम् half of 100 <i>i. e.</i> 50;<BR> or अर्धेन सहितं शतम् <i>i. e.</i> 150; with ordinal numerals ‘with a half or that number’<BR>; ˚तृतीयम् containing two and the third only<BR> half; <i>i. e.</i> two and a half; so ˚चतुर्थ three and a half. cf.<BR> अर्धं खण्डे समांशके Nm.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्धाक्षि, अर्धाङ्गम्, अर्धान्तरम्, अर्धांशः, अर्धांशिन्, अर्धार्धः, अर्धार्धम्, अर्धावभेदकः, अर्धावशेष, अर्धाकारः, अर्धासिः, अर्धासनम्, अर्धेन्दुः, अर्धेन्द्र, अर्धोक्त, अर्धोक्तिः, अर्धोदकम्, अर्धोदयः, अर्धोदित, अर्धोरुक, अर्धकर्णः, अर्धकृत, अर्धकेतुः, अर्धकोशः, अर्धकौडविक, अर्धखारम्, अर्धखारी, अर्धगङ्गा, अर्धगर्भ, अर्धगुच्छः, अर्धगुञ्जा, अर्धगोलः, अर्धचक्रवर्तिन्, अर्धचक्रिन्, अर्धचन्द्र, अर्धचन्द्राकार, अर्धचन्द्राकृति, अर्धचन्द्रकम्, अर्धचन्द्रिका, अर्धचित्र, अर्धचोलकः, अर्धजरतीयन्यायः, अर्धजीविका, अर्धज्या, अर्धतनुः, अर्धतिक्तः, अर्धतूरः, अर्धदिनम्, अर्धदिवसः, अर्धदेवः, अर्धद्रौणिक, अर्धधारः, अर्धनाराचः, अर्धनारायणः, अर्धनारीशः, अर्धनारीश्वरः, अर्धनारी, अर्धनटेश्वरः, अर्धनावम्, अर्धनिशा, अर्धपञ्चम, अर्धपञ्चाशत्, अर्धपणः, अर्धपथम्, अर्धपादः, अर्धपादा, अर्धपादिक, अर्धपाञ्चालिक, अर्धपारावतः, अर्धपुलायितः, अर्धप्रहर, अर्धप्राणम्, अर्धभागः, अर्धभागिक, अर्धभाज्, अर्धभास्करः, अर्धभेदः, अर्धभोटिका, अर्धमागधी, अर्धमाणवकः, अर्धमाणवः, अर्धमात्रा, अर्धमार्गे, अर्धमासः, अर्धमासतम, अर्धमासिक, अर्धमुष्टिः, अर्धयामः, अर्धरथः, अर्धरात्रः, अर्धरात्रार्धदिवसः, अर्धलक्ष्मीहरिः, अर्धविसर्गः, अर्धविसर्जनीयः, अर्धवीक्षणम्, अर्धवृद्ध, अर्धवृद्धिः, अर्धवैनाशिकः, अर्धवैशसम्, अर्धव्यासः, अर्धशतम्, अर्धशनम्, अर्धशफरः, अर्धशब्द, अर्धशेष, अर्धश्याम, अर्धश्लोकः, अर्धसम, अर्धसस्य, अर्धसहः, अर्धसीरिन्, अर्धहर, अर्धहारिन्, अर्धहारः, अर्धह्रस्वः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धः|अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः
अर्ध (Written also as अर्द्ध) + .{@-र्धम्, -र्धः@}<BR>—1 A half, half portion; पचाति नेमो न हि पक्षदर्धः Rv. 10. 27. 18.<BR> सर्वनाशे समुत्पन्ने अर्धं त्यजति पण्डितः; गतमर्धं दिवसस्य<BR> V. 2; पूर्वार्धः first half; so उत्तर˚ latter half; दक्षिण˚<BR> southern half (half on the right side); so अवर˚, जघन˚, पर˚, ग्राम˚<BR> &c.; यदर्धे विच्छिन्नम् Ś. 1. 9 divided in half; ऋज्वायतार्धम्<BR> M. 27; R. 3. 59, 12. 99; रात्रौ तदर्धं गतम् Bh. 3. 107; one part<BR> of two, a part, partly^1 (Ved.);<BR>—2 Nearness, proximity; see अर्धदेव. (अर्ध may be compounded<BR> with almost every noun and adjective; as first member of compound with<BR> nouns it means ‘a half of’ and forms an एकदेशिसमास or तत्पुरुष;<BR> ˚कायः = अर्धं कायस्य; ˚पिप्पली, ˚मार्गः; ˚पुरुषः &c.; with adjectives,<BR> it has an adverbial force; ˚श्याम half dark; ˚भुक्त half eaten;<BR> so ˚पिष्ट, ˚पूर्ण &c.; with numeral adjectives it may mean either<BR> ‘a half of’ or ‘with an additional half’; ˚शतम् half of 100 <i>i. e.</i> 50;<BR> or अर्धेन सहितं शतम् <i>i. e.</i> 150; with ordinal numerals ‘with a half or that number’<BR>; ˚तृतीयम् containing two and the third only<BR> half; <i>i. e.</i> two and a half; so ˚चतुर्थ three and a half. cf.<BR> अर्धं खण्डे समांशके Nm.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अर्धाक्षि, अर्धाङ्गम्, अर्धान्तरम्, अर्धांशः, अर्धांशिन्, अर्धार्धः, अर्धार्धम्, अर्धावभेदकः, अर्धावशेष, अर्धाकारः, अर्धासिः, अर्धासनम्, अर्धेन्दुः, अर्धेन्द्र, अर्धोक्त, अर्धोक्तिः, अर्धोदकम्, अर्धोदयः, अर्धोदित, अर्धोरुक, अर्धकर्णः, अर्धकृत, अर्धकेतुः, अर्धकोशः, अर्धकौडविक, अर्धखारम्, अर्धखारी, अर्धगङ्गा, अर्धगर्भ, अर्धगुच्छः, अर्धगुञ्जा, अर्धगोलः, अर्धचक्रवर्तिन्, अर्धचक्रिन्, अर्धचन्द्र, अर्धचन्द्राकार, अर्धचन्द्राकृति, अर्धचन्द्रकम्, अर्धचन्द्रिका, अर्धचित्र, अर्धचोलकः, अर्धजरतीयन्यायः, अर्धजीविका, अर्धज्या, अर्धतनुः, अर्धतिक्तः, अर्धतूरः, अर्धदिनम्, अर्धदिवसः, अर्धदेवः, अर्धद्रौणिक, अर्धधारः, अर्धनाराचः, अर्धनारायणः, अर्धनारीशः, अर्धनारीश्वरः, अर्धनारी, अर्धनटेश्वरः, अर्धनावम्, अर्धनिशा, अर्धपञ्चम, अर्धपञ्चाशत्, अर्धपणः, अर्धपथम्, अर