अल्पकम्
अल्पक + .{@-कम्@} Little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पकः|अल्पक
अल्पक + .{@-कः@} N. of a plant (यवास; Mar. धमासा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पता
अल्पता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 smallness, minuteness; Bh. 3. 47.<BR>—2 Smallness of intellect, folly; Ki. 6. 37.<BR>—3 Inferiority, insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पत्वम्
अल्पता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 smallness, minuteness; Bh. 3. 47.<BR>—2 Smallness of intellect, folly; Ki. 6. 37.<BR>—3 Inferiority, insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पंपच|अल्पम्पच|अल्पंपचः
अल्पंपच <i>a.</i> Cooking little, stingy, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पंपचः|अल्पम्पच|अल्पंपच
अल्पंपच + .{@-चः@} A miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशः
अल्पशः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In a low degree, slightly, a little; बहुशो ददाति आभ्युदयिकेषु,<BR> अल्पशः श्राद्धेषु P. V. 4. 42. Com.; P. II. 1. 38.<BR>—2 Separately.<BR>—3 Seldom, now and then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पित
अल्पित <i>a.</i> [अल्प कृतार्थे णिच् कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Diminished.<BR>—2 Lowered in estimation, disparaged; मृषा न चक्रेऽल्पितकल्पपादपः N. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पिष्ठ|अल्पिष्ठः
अल्पिष्ठ <i>a.</i> [अतिशयेन अल्पः इष्ठन्] Least, smallest, very small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीकृ
अल्पीकृ €8 U. To make small, diminish, reduce in number, commute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीभूत
अल्पीभूत <i>a.</i> Become small, diminished, reduced in number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीयस्
अल्पीयस् <i>a.</i> [अतिशयेन अल्पः ईयसुन्] Smaller, less; very small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्लकम्
अल्लकम् Seed of Coriander (कुस्तुम्बरी, Mar. धने)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्लका
अल्लकम् + .{@-का@} The plant coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्ला
अल्ला (Ety. ?)<BR>—1 A mother (Voc. अल्ल) अम्बार्थनद्योर्ह्रस्वः P. VII. 3. 107.<BR>—2 The Supreme Goddess. —3 See अल्लकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्ल्लः
अल्ला + .{@-ल्लः@} The Supreme God etc. (अल्लोपनिषत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्
अव् €1 P. [अवति, आव, आवीत्, अविष्यति, अवितुम्, अवित or ऊत]<BR>—1 To protect, defend; सह नाववतु T. Up. 2. 1. 1. यमवतामवतां<BR> च धुरि स्थितः R. 9. 1; प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—2 To please, satisfy, give pleasure to; do good to; विक्रमसेन मामवति<BR>नाजिते त्वयि R. 11. 75; न मामवति सद्वीपा रत्नसूरपि मेदिनी. 1. 65.<BR>—3 To like, wish, desire, love.<BR>—4 To favour, promote, animate. (In the Dhātupāṭha. several other meanings<BR> are assigned to this root, but they are very rarely used in classical<BR> literature; <i>e. g.</i> गति, कान्ति, अवगम, प्रवेश, श्रवण, स्वाम्यर्थ<BR> or सामर्थ्य, याचन, क्रिया, दीप्ति, अवाप्ति, ग्रहण, व्याप्ति, आलिङ्गन,<BR> हिंसा, आदान, दहन, भाव, भाग, and वृद्धि). ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> consume, devour. ━<i>With</i> {@अनु@} to encourage, inspire.<BR>━{@उद्@}<BR>—1 to regard, attend to.<BR>—2 to wait for.<BR>—3 to promote, impel.<BR>━{@उप@}<BR>—1 to cherish, behave friendly towards.<BR>—2 to encourage.<BR>━{@सम्@}<BR>—1 to satisfy, satiate.<BR>—2 to protect, maintain. [cf. L. <i>aveo</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवः|अव
अवः Favour; अग्नेरवेण मरुताम् Rv. 1. 128. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन|अवनं
अवन <i>a.</i> [अव्-ल्युट्] Protecting, defending; अनवनी नवनीपवनावलिः Śi. 6. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्
अवन + .{@-नम्@} Protection &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव <i>ind.</i> (the initial अ is sometimes dropped, as in पूर्वापरौ<BR> तोयनिधी वगाह्य Ku. 1. 1)<BR>—1 (As a preposition) Away, off, away from, down; कृत्वा मुखान्यवशुचः श्वसनेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">Page0238-1</a>]<BR> शुष्यत् Bhāg. 10. 29. 29.<BR>—2 (As a prefix to verbs) It expresses<BR>——(<i>a</i>) determination; अवधृ, अवसो;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) diffusion, pervasion; अवकॄ, -कीर्ण;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) disrespect; अवज्ञा, अवमन्;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) littleness; व्रीहीनवहन्ति;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) support, resting upon; अवलम्ब्; (<i>f.</i>) purification, अवदात;<BR>——(<i>g</i>) depreciation, discomfiture; अवहन्ति शत्रून् (पराभवति);<BR>——(<i>h</i>) commanding; अवकॢप्;<BR>——(<i>i</i>) depression, bending down; अवतॄ, अवगाह्<BR>——(<i>j</i>) knowledge; अवगम्, अवे.<BR>—3 As the first member of Tat. compounds it means अवक्रुष्ट; अवकोकिलः<BR> = अवकुष्टः कोकिलया Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0237-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरम्
अवतरम् <i>ind.</i> Farther away; अव स्रवेदघशंसोऽवतरमव क्षुद्रमिव<BR> स्रवेत् Rv. 1. 129. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंशः|अवंश
अवंशः A bad family, wrong family; ˚पतितो राजा Cāṇ. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंशम्
अवंशः + .{@-शम्@} That which has no pillars or support, the ether; अवंशे<BR> द्यामस्तभायद् Rv. 2. 15. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकट|अवकटं
अवकट <i>a.</i> [अव-स्वार्थे-कटच् अवात्कुटारच्च P. V. 2. 30]<BR>—1 Downwards; backwards.<BR>—2 Opposite, contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकटम्
अवकट + .{@-टम्@} Contrariety, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकटिका
अवकटिका Dissimulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकरः|अवकर
अवकरः [कॄ-अप्] Dust, sweepings; अवकरनिकरं विकिरती Bh. 2. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्ण्
अवकर्ण् €10 P. To hear; सहसावकर्ण्य निरियाय संसदः Śi. 15. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्णनम्
अवकर्णनम् Hearing; K. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षणम्
अवकर्षणम् Drawing with strength, removing a thing from one place to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Seen, observed.<BR>—2 Known.<BR>—3 Taken, received.<BR>—4 Wicked, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवका
अवका A grassy plant (शैवाल) growing in marshy land.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवकाद, अवकोल्ब<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाद
अवका + -अद <i>a.</i> eating moss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकोल्ब
अवका + -उल्ब <i>a.</i> covered or surrounded with अवका plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश्
अवकाश् €1. €4. Ā. To be visible, to be manifest. ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> cause to look at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशः|अवकाश
अवकाशः<BR>—1 Occasion, opportunity; ताते चापद्वितीये वहति रणधुरां को भयस्यावकाशः<BR> Ve. 3. 7; उत्तरावकाशमपाहरन्त्या K. 204, 265; साहाय्यदानावकाशः<BR> Dk. 96; M. 3. 13; M. 2; oft. used with लभ् in the sense of ‘to get an opportunity or scope for action’<BR>; लब्धावकाशोऽविध्यन्मां तत्र दग्धो<BR> मनोभवः Ks. 1. 41.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Place, space, room; अवकाशं किलोदन्वान्रामायाभ्यर्थितो ददौ<BR> R. 4. 58; अन्यमवकाशमवगाहे V. 4; Ms. 3. 207; यथावकाशं नी<BR> to take to its proper place, R. 6. 14; अस्माकमस्ति न कथंचिदिहावकाशः<BR> Pt. 4. 8; अवकाशो विविक्तोऽयं महानद्योः समागमे Rām.; सदोषावकाश<BR> इव ते वाक्यशेषः V. 3 your unfinished sentence shows that there is<BR> room to find fault.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Footing, admission, scope, access, entrance; (छाया) शुद्धे<BR> तु दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32; oft. used in these senses with<BR> लभ्; लब्धावकाशा मे प्रार्थना, लब्धावकाशो मे मनोरथः Ś. 1;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">Page0238-2</a>]<BR> शोकावेगदूषिते मे मनसि विवेक एव नावकाशं लभते Prab.; also with<BR> कृ or दा ‘to make room for’, ‘admit’, ‘give way to’; असौ हि<BR> दत्त्वा तिमिरावकाशम् Mk. 3. 6; तस्माद्देयो विपुलमतिभिर्नावकाशोऽधमानाम्<BR> Pt. 1. 366; शयने दत्तोऽवकाशः Amaru. 21; उदत्तावकाशो मत्सरस्य<BR> K. 45 not swayed by malice; Ms. 9. 271; Y. 2. 276; ददौ च निजचित्तेऽपि<BR> सोवकाशं मनोभुवः Ks. 20. 71; K. 132, 141, 207; Ratn. 2. 13; अवकाशं<BR> रुध् to obstruct, hinder or impede; नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशाम्<BR> (निद्राम्) Me. 92.<BR>—3 Interval, intermediate space or time.<BR>—4 An aperture, opening.<BR>—5 A glance cast on anything.<BR>—6 N. of certain verses during the recitation of which the eyes must be<BR> fixed upon certain objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशवत्|अवकाशवन्त्
अवकाशवत् <i>a.</i> Spacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश्य
अवकाश्य <i>a.</i> Admitted in the recitation of the <i>Avakāśa</i> verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण, -र्णिन्<BR> See under अवकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्ण, -र्णिन्<BR> See under अवकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीलकः|अवकीलक
अवकीलकः A peg or plug set inside; क्षुत्पिपासावकीलकम् Mbh. 14. 45. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुञ्चनम्
अवकुञ्चनम्<BR>—1 Bending, curving, contraction.<BR>—2 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटार|अवकुटारं
अवकुटार <i>a.</i> [अव-स्वार्थे अतिशये वा कुटारच्] Very deep,<BR> downwards, backwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटारम्
अवकुटार + .{@-रम्@} Deformity. See अवकट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुट्टित
अवकुट्टित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vexed, inflammed.<BR>—2 Cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठनम्
अवकुण्ठनम्<BR>—1 Investing, surrounding.<BR>—2 Attracting, engaging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठित|अवकुंठित
अवकुण्ठित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Invested, surrounded.<BR>—2 Attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुत्स्
अवकुत्स् €10 U. To blame, revile, condemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुत्सित
अवकुत्सित <i>p. p.</i> Blamed, reviled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुत्सितम्
अवकुत्सित + .{@-तम्@} Blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकूल्
अवकूल् To singe, to burn; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृत
अवकृत <i>a.</i> Directed downwards (as a root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृत्
अवकृत् €6 P. To cut off or away. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तः|अवकर्त
अवकर्तः A part cut off, a strip; वस्त्रावकर्तेन संवीता Nala. 10. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तनम्
अवकर्तनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off, excision; वस्त्रार्धस्यावकर्तनम् Nala. 10. 16.<BR>—2 Battle field; एकमुक्त्वा तु गांधारी कुरूणामवकर्तनम् । अपश्यत्तत्र<BR> तिष्ठन्ती सर्वं दिव्येन चक्षुषा Mb. 11. 16. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तिन्
अवकर्तिन् <i>a.</i> Cutting off or out; चर्म˚ यशश्चर्मावकर्तिनः<BR> (अन्नमादत्ते) Ms. 4. 218.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्
अवकृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw off or away, to pull off, drag down or pull down.<BR>—2 To extract, take out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षणम्
अवकर्षणम्<BR>—1 Taking or pulling out, extraction.<BR>—2 Expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्ट|अवकृष्टः
अवकृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drawn away or down, pulled down.<BR>—2 Removed.<BR>—3 Expelled, turned out or away.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">Page0239-1</a>]<BR>—4 Inferior, low, degraded, outcast (opp. उत्कृष्ट or प्रकृष्ट);<BR> पादावकृष्टो राजन्ये तथाधर्मो विधीयते Mb. 12. 35. 32. ˚जातिः<BR> Nyāya S. 8. 177; प्रतिकर्तुं प्रकृष्टस्य नावकृष्टेन युज्यते Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्टः|अवकृष्ट
अवकृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} A servant who performs the lowest menial duties (such as<BR> sweeping &c.). (संमार्जनशोधनविनियुक्त); पणो देयोऽवकृष्टस्य<BR> षडुत्कृष्टस्य वेतनम् Ms. 7. 1. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॄ
अवकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To bestow, pour upon, to shower upon, cover with, fill; Śi. 11. 62;<BR> (तं) अवाकिरन् बाललताः प्रसूनैः R. 2. 10, 4. 27; लाजाञ्जलिभिरवकीर्यमाणः<BR> K. 86; Ki. 6. 2; अवकीर्योत्तरीयाणि Mb. spreading on the ground; तीर्थानि<BR> अवकीर्णानि तपस्विभिः Mb. filled with; Y. 3. 281; Me. 56.<BR>—2 To pour out, throw out; सप्तद्वारावकीर्णां च न वाचमनृतां वदेत् Ms. 6. 48.<BR>—3 To shake off, throw off, leave.<BR>—4 (<i>Ātm.</i>) (Used reflexively)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To extend, spread itself; अवकिरते हस्ती स्वयमेव Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To fall asunder.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To pass away, fall off.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To become faithless or untrue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered, filled, covered over; किमैपति रजोभिरौर्वरैरवकीर्णस्य<BR> मणेर्महार्घता Śi. 16. 27.<BR>—2 Coarsely pounded.<BR>—3 Destroyed; अवकीर्णो हि समरे वीरो दुष्प्रज्ञया तदा Mb. 15. 16. 11.<BR>—4 Violated (as the vow of a ब्रह्मचारी), degraded.<BR>—5 Declining, dilapidating; दृष्ट्वा तथाऽवकीर्णं तु राष्ट्रम् Mb. 9. 41. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्णिन् <i>a.</i> [अवकीर्णमनेन इष्टा˚ इनि] Violating the vow<BR> or engagements of continence. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णी
अवकीर्णिन् + .({@-र्णी@}) A religious student who has committed an act of incontinence<BR> (such as sexual intercourse) against his vow of celibacy; अवकीर्णी भवेद्<BR> गत्वा ब्रह्मचारी तु योषितम् । गर्दभं पशुमालभ्य नैरृतं स विशुध्यति ॥<BR> Y. 3. 280; Ms. 3. 155, 11. 118-9; ˚व्रतम् penance for an act<BR> of incontinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॢप्
अवकॢप् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To correspond with, to answer.<BR>—2 To be right or fit, to be possible; इतश्च न प्रधानस्य प्रवृत्तिरवकल्पते<BR> Ś. B. 2. 2. 8.<BR>—3 To help to, to serve, to accomplish, result in (with dat.); शरीरिणां<BR> संसृतयेऽवकल्पते Bhāg. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To put in order, to prepare; to make ready; संभारानवकल्पय Mb.<BR>—2 To use or employ becomingly.<BR>—3 To consider as possible; नावकल्प्यमिदंग्लायेद्यत्कृच्छ्रेषु भवानपि<BR> Bk. 19. 17; यत्तत्रभवान्वृषलं याजयेन्नावकल्पयामि P. III. 3. 147. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकल्पित
अवकल्पित <i>p. p.</i> Corresponding with; right, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॢप्तिः|अवकॢप्ति
अवकॢप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Considering as possible, possiblity, probability; क्वेव भोक्ष्यसे<BR> अनवकॢप्तावेव Sk. (अनवकॢप्तिरसंभावना).<BR>—2 Suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेश
अवकेश <i>a.</i> Having the hair hanging down. यस्ते मदोऽवकेशो<BR> विकेशो Rv. 6. 30. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेशिन्
अवकेशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unfruitful, barren (as a tree).<BR>—2 [अवसन्नाः केशा विद्यन्ते अस्य इनि] Having small or very few hair.<BR> ━<i>m.</i> A fruitless tree. अपकारपरस्यापि प्रयास्यत्यवकेशिताम् Śiva B. 15. 21.<BR> द्वितीयो ह्यवकेशी स्यात् प्रथमस्तु फलेग्रहिः <i>ibid.</i> 16. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकोकिल
अवकोकिल <i>a.</i> [अवकुष्टः कोकिलया] Drawn or called down to by a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्तव्य|अवक्तव्यं
अवक्तव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not fit to be uttered, improper.<BR>—2 Censurable (as a saying).<BR>—3 False.<BR>—4 Indescribable, inexpressible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्त्र
अवक्त्र <i>a.</i> Having no opening (as a vessel, wound &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्र
अवक्र <i>a.</i> Not crooked, straight; (fig.) honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रक्षिन्
अवक्रक्षिन् [अव-कृष् णिनि पृषो] Dashing down, overcoming; अवक्रक्षिणं<BR> वृषभं यथा जुरम् Rv. 8. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्द्|अवक्रंद्
अवक्रन्द् €1 U. To cry out, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्द|अवक्रंद|अवक्रन्दः
अवक्रन्द <i>a.</i> Crying slowly, roaring, neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्दः|अवक्रन्द|अवक्रंद
अवक्रन्द + .{@-न्दः@} A cry; क्रन्दते स्वाहाऽवक्रन्दाय स्वाहा Vāj. 22. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्दनम्
अवक्रन्दनम् Crying out, weeping aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रम्
अवक्रम् €1 U., €4 P.<BR>—1 To step down or away, run away, escape, withdraw.<BR>—2 To tread down, overcome; अवक्रामन्दाः प्रपदैरमित्रान् Rv. 6. 75. 7.<BR> वज्रेणैवेनमवक्रामति Śat. Br.<BR>—3 To descend, come down. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to go down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रम|अवक्रमः
अवक्रम Descending, descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रान्तिः|अवक्रान्ति|अवक्रांतिः
अवक्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Descending, descent.<BR>—2 Approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रामिन्
अवक्रामिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Running away, escaping; बन्धमिवावक्रामी गच्छ Rv. 5. 14. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रिया
अवक्रिया Neglect, omission, non-performance of prescribed acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्री
अवक्री €9 U.<BR>—1 To purchase.<BR>—2 To let out, hire.<BR>—3 To bribe, buy off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रयः|अवक्रय
अवक्रयः<BR>—1 Price.<BR>—2 Wages, hire, farm rent.<BR>—3 Letting out to hire, leasing; Y. 2. 238.<BR>—4 A tax or tribute (to be paid to the king), duty (राजग्राह्यं द्रव्यम् Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुश्
अवक्रुश् €1 P. To call down to; to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुष्ट
अवक्रुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Sounded ill or badly, reviled, censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रोशः|अवक्रोश
अवक्रोशः<BR>—1 Discordant noise.<BR>—2 A curse.<BR>—3 Abuse, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लिन्न
अवक्लिन्न <i>a.</i> Wet, thoroughly wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदः|अवक्लेद
अवक्लेदः<BR>—1 Trickling, descent of moisture.<BR>—2 Ichor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदनम्
अवक्लेदनम् Trickling, falling (as dew or moisture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वणः|अवक्वण
अवक्वणः A discordant note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वाथः|अवक्वाथ
अवक्वाथः Imperfect digestion or decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षामः|अवक्षाम
अवक्षामः Ved. Propitiatory offering; satisfaction of claims, compensation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षि
अवक्षि €1. €5. €9 P. To remove, carry off, destroy. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR> To waste away, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षयः|अवक्षय
अवक्षयः<BR>—1 Destruction, decay, waste, loss; लब्धं रक्षेदवक्षयात् H. 2. 8.<BR>—2 A kind of malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षयणम्
अवक्षयणम् Means of extinguishing (fire &c.); as in अङ्गार˚ याज्ञवल्क्यस्त्वाꣳ<BR> स्विदिमे ब्राह्मणा अङ्गारावक्षयणमक्रता ३ इति Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षीण
अवक्षीण <i>p. p.</i> Wasted, emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षीणम्
अवक्षीण + .{@-णम्@} Loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्
अवक्षिप् €6 U.<BR>—1 To fling away, to throw or cast off; सूक्ष्मवस्त्रमवक्षिप्य मुनिवस्त्राण्यवस्त<BR> ह Rām.; to hurl.<BR>—2 To cause to fly down or away.<BR>—3 To reprimand, revile anyone, censure, slander; मदलेखामवक्षिप्य<BR> K. 317; अवाक्षिपद्वासुदेवम् Mb. अयाज्ययाजनाध्यापने नियुक्तममृष्यमाणं<BR> राजा अवक्षिपेत् Kau. A. 1. 10.<BR>—4 To grant, yield. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्त
अवक्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown down; badly thrown.<BR>—2 Said sarcastically, imputed, insinuated.<BR>—3 Reviled, censured, blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेपः|अवक्षेप
अवक्षेपः<BR>—1 Blaming, reviling.<BR>—2 Objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेपणम्
अवक्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Throwing down, considered as one of the five kinds of <i>karman</i>, q. v.<BR>—2 Contempt, despising; अवक्षेपणे कन् P. V. 3. 95.<BR>—3 Censure, blame; P. I. 3. 32, VI. 2. 195.<BR>—4 Overcoming, subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेपणी
अवक्षेपणम् + .{@-णी@} Rein, bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षु
अवक्षु €2 P. To sneeze upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षुत|अवक्षुतं
अवक्षुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sneezed upon; द्विषदन्नं नगर्यन्नं पतितान्नमवक्षुतम् Ms. 4. 213.<BR>—2 Spit upon or defiled; अवक्षुतावरुदितं तथा श्राद्धे च वर्जयेत्<BR> Mb. 13. 91. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखण्ड्|अवखंड्
अवखण्ड् €10 P.<BR>—1 To cut down, break into pieces.<BR>—2 To waste away, wear away; अर्धयाममात्रावखण्डितायां विभावर्याम्<BR> K. 49 when the night had advanced only half a watch.<BR>—3 To destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखण्डनम्
अवखण्डनम् Dividing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखातम्
अवखातम् [निम्नः खातः] A deep ditch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

