अवगथ|अवगथः
अवगथ <i>a.</i> [निपातः Uṇ. 2. 9] Bathed early in the morning<BR> (प्रातःस्नात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगदितः|अवगदित
अवगदितः<BR>—1 Having exception. —2 Censured, blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगम्
अवगम् €1 P. To go down, descend; अञ्जः समुद्रमवजग्मुरापः Rv. 1. 32. 2.<BR>—2 To come to, visit, go near.<BR>—3 To reach, obtain.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To know, learn, understand, think, believe; कृतापराधमिवावगच्छति<BR> आत्मानम् K. 203; मामेवमवगच्छति V. 2; कथं शान्तमित्यभिहिते<BR> श्रान्त इत्यवगच्छति मूर्खः Mk. 1; न खल्ववगच्छामि, परस्तादवगम्यत<BR> एव Ś. 1. तत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम तेजोंऽशसंभवम् Bg. 10. 41;<BR> R. 8. 88; Bk. 5. 81.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To consider, regard, look upon.<BR>—5 To assure oneself, be convinced. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bring near; अथेममिहावगमय Av. 3. 3. 6.<BR>—2 To inform oneself of, find out, know, तावदेतेभ्यः प्रियाप्रवृत्तिरवगमयितव्या V. 4.<BR>—3 To inform, cause to know, teach; पुरुषविशेषमवगमयति Mu. 5;<BR> सर्वमिदं पित्रोरवगमय्य Dk.<BR>—4 To indicate, show; संनाहोऽयं साहसमवगमयति Dk. 96; Bk. 10. 53, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगत|अवगतं
अवगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone away or down.<BR>—2 Known, learnt, understood; sometimes used actively; तदैव ध्यानादवगतोऽस्मि<BR> Ś. 7 I learn; ऊढपूर्वां तद्दुहितरमवगतोऽहम् <i>ibid.</i> came to know.<BR>—3 Assented, promised.<BR>—4 Well-known (प्रसिद्ध); मामप्यवगतं धर्माद् व्यतिक्रान्तपुरस्कृतम्<BR> Rām. 4. 18. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगतिः|अवगति
अवगतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Knowledge, perception, comprehension.<BR>—2 True or determinate knowledge; ब्रह्मावगतिर्हि पुरुषार्थः; ब्रह्मावगतिस्त्वप्रतिज्ञाता Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगमः|अवगम
अवगमः, -गमनम्<BR>—1 Going near, descending.<BR>—2 Understanding, comprehension, perception, knowledge, being acquainted with.<BR>—3 True or determinate knowledge; प्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् Bg. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगमनम्
अवगमः, -गमनम्<BR>—1 Going near, descending.<BR>—2 Understanding, comprehension, perception, knowledge, being acquainted with.<BR>—3 True or determinate knowledge; प्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् Bg. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगम्य
अवगम्य <i>a.</i> Intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगल्
अवगल् €1 P. To fall down, slip down; सौवर्णं वलयमवागलत्कराग्रात् Śi. 8. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगादः|अवगाद
अवगादः A small wooden basin for baling water out of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह्
अवगाह् €1 Ā.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To bathe oneself in, plunge into, dive into; with acc. or loc.;<BR> तमोऽपहन्त्रीं तमसां वगाह्य R. 14. 76; अन्यमवकाशमवगाहिष्ये<BR> V. 4; स्वप्नेऽवगाहतेत्यर्थं जलम् Y. 1. 272; Bk. 6. 29, 16. 38.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To go deep into, be absorbed into (fig.); अमात्यराक्षसेनाप्यनवगाहितमार्यचाणक्यस्य<BR> चरितमवगाहितुमिच्छसि Mu. 6.<BR>—2 To enter, penetrate, fully pervade; विमानशृङ्गाण्यवगाहमानः (घोषः)<BR> Ku. 7. 40; पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी वगाह्य Ku. 1. 1; पूर्वापरसमुद्रावगाढः<BR> Ś. 7; Mk. 2; see अवगाढ also.<BR>—3 To determine. विषयमवगाहते यस्मात् Sāṅ. K. 35. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To bathe, cause to bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढ
अवगाढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Plunged into, entered into, immersed; जलावगाढस्य वनद्विपस्य<BR> Mk. 2; अमृतह्रदमिवावगाढोऽस्मि Ś. 7; अवगाढः शोकसागरम् Rām.;<BR> समुद्रमवगाढानि पत्तनानि Rām.<BR>—2 Depressed, low, deep (lit. and fig.); Rām. 6. 88. 74. अभ्युन्नता<BR> पुरस्तादवगाढा जघनगौरवात्पश्चात् Ś. 3. 7; मन्युरभजदवगाढतरः Śi. 15. 2.<BR>—3 That in which one bathes; अवगाढा च पीता च (गङ्गा) पुनात्यासप्तमं कुलम् Mb.<BR>—4 Congealed, curdling (as blood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहः|अवगाह
अवगाहः, -हनम्<BR>—1 Bathing; सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3; अवगाहप्रस्थितमिव वनमहिषयूथम्<BR> K. 29; सदावगाहक्षमवारिसंचयः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">Page0241-1</a>]<BR> Ṛs. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Plunging, immersing (in general); entering into; हुतभुगवगाहनसाहसिकाम्<BR> Dk. 16; परदेशावगाहनात् H. 3. 88; जलावगाहक्षणमात्रशान्ता<BR> R. 5. 47; दग्धानामवगाहनाय विधिना रम्यं सरो निर्मितम् Ś. Til. 1.<BR>—3 (fig.) Mastering, learning, studying completely; सकलशास्त्रावगाहगम्भीरबुद्धिः K. 56.<BR>—4 A place of bathing.<BR>—5 A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहनम्
अवगाहः, -हनम्<BR>—1 Bathing; सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3; अवगाहप्रस्थितमिव वनमहिषयूथम्<BR> K. 29; सदावगाहक्षमवारिसंचयः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">Page0241-1</a>]<BR> Ṛs. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Plunging, immersing (in general); entering into; हुतभुगवगाहनसाहसिकाम्<BR> Dk. 16; परदेशावगाहनात् H. 3. 88; जलावगाहक्षणमात्रशान्ता<BR> R. 5. 47; दग्धानामवगाहनाय विधिना रम्यं सरो निर्मितम् Ś. Til. 1.<BR>—3 (fig.) Mastering, learning, studying completely; सकलशास्त्रावगाहगम्भीरबुद्धिः K. 56.<BR>—4 A place of bathing.<BR>—5 A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह्य
अवगाह्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Fit for bathing.<BR>—2 Fit to be plunged into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुणः|अवगुण
अवगुणः A fault, defect, demerit; अन्यदोषं परावगुणम् Malli. on Ki. 13. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठ्|अवगुंठ्
अवगुण्ठ् €10 P.<BR>—1 To cover with, shroud; परुषचर्मावगुण्ठितम् Pt. 1; Ms. 4. 49.<BR>—2 To draw over, conceal, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठनम्
अवगुण्ठनम्<BR>—1 The act of covering the head of women; hiding, veiling.<BR>—2 A veil (for the face); (fig. also); अवगुण्ठनसंवीता कुलजाभिसरेद्यदि<BR> S. D.; अवगुण्ठनपटक्षेपं विधत्ते विधुः <i>ibid.</i>; कृतशीर्षावगुण्ठनः<BR> Mu. 6; उत्सृष्टसत्पुरुषोचितलज्जावगुण्ठनानाम् Ve. 3; Mk. 4. 24; Śi. 5. 17.<BR>—3 A covering, पश्येष्टदारदारांस्ते भ्रष्टलज्जावगुण्ठनान् Rām. 6. 111. 62.<BR> mantle (in general).<BR>—4 A sweeping broom.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवगुण्ठनमुद्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठनमुद्रा
अवगुण्ठनम् + -मुद्रा [अवगुण्ठनाय मुद्रा] a sort of religious ceremony;<BR> सव्यहस्तकृता मुष्टिर्दीर्घाऽधोमुखतर्जनी । अवगुण्ठनमुद्रेयमभितो भ्रमिता मता ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठनवत्|अवगुण्ठनवन्त्
अवगुण्ठनवत् <i>a.</i> Covered with a veil, veiled; ˚वती नारी Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठिका|अवगुंठिका
अवगुण्ठिका<BR>—1 Veiling, hiding, covering.<BR>—2 A veil.<BR>—3 A curtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठित|अवगुंठित|अवगुण्ठितं
अवगुण्ठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Veiled, covered, concealed; रजनीतिमिरावगुण्ठिते Ku. 4. 11 enveloped<BR> in nocturnal darkness.<BR>—2 Powdered, pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्डित|अवगुंडित
अवगुण्डित <i>a.</i> Pounded, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुम्फित
अवगुम्फित <i>a.</i> Woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुर्
अवगुर् €6 U. To assail with threats, to attack, to raise a weapon<BR> for the purpose of striking a blow (with loc. or dat.); न कदाचिद् द्विजे<BR> तस्माद् विद्वानवगुरेदपि Ms. 4. 169; ब्राह्मणायावगुर्यैव 165, 11. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुरणम्
अवगुरणम्, -गोरणम्<BR> Menacing, assaulting with intent to kill, assailing with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगोरणम्
अवगुरणम्, -गोरणम्<BR> Menacing, assaulting with intent to kill, assailing with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुह्
अवगुह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To cover, to hide, conceal; (रविः) पांशुपुञ्जावगूढः Mb.<BR>—2 To put into or inside; उष्णीषं संवेष्ट्य निवीतेऽवगूहते Kāty.<BR>—3 To embrace; या ममोद्विजते नित्यं सा मामद्यावगूहते Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगूहनम्
अवगूहनम्<BR>—1 Hiding, concealing.<BR>—2 Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगै
अवगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To sing in a discordant tone.<BR>—2 To sing deprecatingly, satirize in a song, revile, reproach (mostly<BR> used in p. p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sung in a discordant tone, sung badly.<BR>—2 Reproached, abused, censured; अनवगीतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">Page0241-2</a>]<BR> परिचयः U. 2. 2; अवगीतां गमिते दशामिमाम् Ki. 2. 7; सोढावगीतप्रथमायुधस्य 17. 28;<BR> Śi. 11. 10.<BR>—3 Wicked, vile.<BR>—4 Satirized in a song.<BR>—5 Seen frequently, well-known (मुहुर्दृष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीतम्
अवगीत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A satire in song, derision.<BR>—2 Reproach, blame.<BR>—3 Bad or discordant singing: cf. … अवगीतं तु गर्हिते । जन्योपश्लिष्टयोर्वाच्यलिङ्गःकुत्सितकूजिते । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह्
अवग्रह् €9 U.<BR>—1 To let loose, let go (as reins).<BR>—2 To divide, separate (as words or parts of words); पितृयाणमित्यत्र<BR> हि पितृयाणमित्यृकारोऽवगृह्यते P. VIII. 2. 26. Com.<BR>—3 To break off, discontinue; to distinguish, discriminate, discern.<BR>—4 To punish, chastise; मन्दोऽपि नाम न महानवगृह्य साध्यः Śi. 5. 49.<BR>—5 To seize, choke; गद्गदिकावगृह्यमाणकण्ठा K. 307, 328.<BR>—6 To capture, take in possession, overpower; स्वामिनमवशमवगृह्णन्ति<BR> Dk. 157, 32; Ve. 46.<BR>—7 To oppose, resist, hinder, obstruct.<BR>—8 To lay hold of (with the feet). ━<i>Caus.</i> To knead, make dough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृहीत
अवगृहीत <i>p. p.</i> Obstructed, impeded, restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृह्य
अवगृह्य <i>a.</i> Separable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृह्यम्
अवगृह्य + .{@-ह्यम्@} A Pada having the name प्रगृह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहः|अवग्रह
अवग्रहः<BR>—1 Separation of the component parts of a compound, or of other grammatical forms.<BR>—2 The mark or interval of such a separation; समासेऽवग्रहो ह्रस्वसमकालः.<BR>—3 The syllable or letter after which such separation occurs, छन्दस्यृदवग्रहात्<BR> P. VIII. 4. 26.<BR>—4 A hiatus, absence of sandhi (as in धिक् तां च तं च मदनं च इमां<BR> च मां च instead of चेमां च) Bh. 2. 2.<BR>—5 The mark (ऽ) used to mark the elision of अ after ए and ओ.<BR>—6 Withholding of rain, drought, failure of rain; वृष्टिर्भवति शस्यानामवग्रहविशोषिणाम्<BR> R. 1. 62; रावणावग्रहक्लान्तमिति वागमृतेन सः 10. 48; नभोनभस्ययोर्वृष्टिमवग्रह<BR> इवान्तरे 12. 29; वृषेव सीतां तदवग्रहक्षताम् Ku. 5. 61.<BR>—7 An obstacle, impediment, hindrance, restraint; संसार˚ Māl. 1<BR> the bonds or fetters of worldly existence; प्रसह्य रक्षोभिरवग्रहं<BR> च Rām.; see अनवग्रह and निरवग्रह.<BR>—8 A herd of elephants<BR>—9 The forehead of an elephant; A part of the elephantʼs face, the flat<BR> level place in the middle of the elephantʼs forehead which joins the lower<BR> parts of the two Kumbhas; Mātaṅga L. 5. 6.<BR>—10 Nature, original temperament.<BR>—11 A sort of knowledge, a false idea.<BR>—12 Punishment (opp. अनुग्रह); अनुग्रहावग्रहयोर्विधाता Śi. 1. 71.<BR>—13 An imprecation, a term of abuse.<BR>—14 An iron hook with which elephants are driven.<BR>—15 Obstinate insistance; obstinacy; कर्मण्यवग्रहधियो भगवन्विदामः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहणम्
अवग्रहणम्<BR>—1 An obstacle, impediment.<BR>—2 Disrespect, disregard.<BR>—3 Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्राहः|अवग्राह
अवग्राहः<BR>—1 Breaking, separation.<BR>—2 Impediment; अवग्राहस्ते भूयात् Sk.<BR>—3 A curse; see अवग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्ट्
अवघट्ट् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To push or brush away or off.<BR>—2 To split, break or cut asunder; पञ्चबाणान् अवघट्ट्यन्ती<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">Page0242-1</a>]<BR> Dk. 124.<BR>—3 To touch, feel, rub; जलौकाव्रणान्मधुनाऽवघट्टयेत् Suśr.<BR>—4 To stir up, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0241-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्टः|अवघट्ट
अवघट्टः<BR>—1 A hole in the ground, a cave, a cavern.<BR>—2 A grindstone, stone-mill for grinding corn.<BR>—3 Stirring up, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्टनम्
अवघट्टनम् Rubbing away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघाटकम्
अवघाटकम् A kind of necklace gradually decreasing in size. Kau. A. 2. 11<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघात|अवघातः
अवघात See under अवहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघुष्
अवघुष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To proclaim aloud.<BR>—2 To send for, summon, convoke; as a conclave (समाज).<BR>—3 To fill with cries, make resonant; नदीषु क्रौञ्चावघुष्टासु Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघुष्ट
अवघुष्ट <i>a.</i> Proclaimed, addressed, summoned aloud; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषः|अवघोष
अवघोषः, -षणम्<BR> Proclaiming, denouncing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषणम्
अवघोषः, -षणम्<BR> Proclaiming, denouncing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषणा
अवघोषः, -षणम् + .{@-णा@} A proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्ण्
अवघूर्ण् €1 U. To whirl round, brandish, move to and fro; as in अवघूर्णमानताम्रदृष्टिः;<BR> वने यथा शाल इवावघूर्णितः Mb. rocked to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णः|अवघूर्ण
अवघूर्णः Whirling round, a whirl-pool. <i>a.</i> Agitated, perturbed;<BR> विष्टभ्य चित्तं प्रणयावघूर्णम् Bhāg. 11. 29. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णनम्
अवघूर्णनम् Rolling or whirling round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघृष्
अवघृष् €1 U. To rub off, rub to pieces, grind to powder; मृदुना<BR> सलिलेन खन्यमानान्यवघृष्यन्ति गिरेरपि स्थलानि Pt. 1 v. l. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To rub off, scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षणम्
अवघर्षणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing into.<BR>—2 Grinding.<BR>—3 Cleaning, rubbing off; सलिलैः शुद्धिरेतेषां गोवालैश्चावघर्षणम् Y. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोटित
अवघोटित <i>a.</i> Covered on all sides, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्रा
अवघ्रा €1 P.<BR>—1 To smell at; touch with the mouth; अवजिघ्रेच्च तान् पिण्डान् Ms. 3. 218.<BR>—2 To kiss (as the head); मूर्धनि त्रिरवघ्राय Āśval.; अवघ्रातश्च<BR> मूर्धनि Rām. ━<i>Caus.</i> (घ्रापयति) To cause to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्राणम्
अवघ्राणम् The act of smelling at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्रात
अवघ्रात <i>a.</i> Smelled, kissed; परिष्वक्तश्च बाहुभ्यामवघ्रातश्च<BR> मूर्धनि Rām. 2. 20. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्रापणम्
अवघ्रापणम् Causing to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच
अवच <i>a.</i> Lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचक्ष्
अवचक्ष् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To look down upon (Ved.).<BR>—2 To perceive, observe; रिपुणा नावचक्षे Rv. 4. 58. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचक्षण
अवचक्षण <i>a.</i> One telling a censured tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचक्षणम्
अवचक्षण + .{@-णम्@} Looking down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन
अवचन <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Not speaking, silent, speechless;<BR> शकुन्तला साध्वसादवचना तिष्ठति Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनम्
अवचन + .{@-नम्@} [अभावे, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1 Absence of assertion, silence, taciturnity; अवचनेऽग्निष्टोम; Kāty.<BR>—2 Censure, blame, reproof; ˚कर <i>a.</i> not doing what one is bid, disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीय
अवचनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be spoken or uttered, obscene or indecent (language); वादेष्ववचनीयेषु<BR> तदेव द्विगुणं भवेत् Ms. 8. 269.<BR>—2 Not censurable, not blamable, free from censure; लोकैरवचनीया भवति<BR> Mk. 2; ˚ता, -त्व impropriety of speech, freedom from censure; सर्वथा<BR> व्यवहर्तव्ये कुतो ह्यवचनीयता U. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचस्कर|अवचस्करः
अवचस्कर <i>a.</i> Not speaking, silent, taciturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन्द्रमसम्
अवचन्द्रमसम् The looking down of the moon (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचर्
अवचर् €1 U.<BR>—1 To move or come down; दिवश्चरन्ति भेषजा Rv. 10. 59. 9.<BR>—2 To go down towards. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to move or descend upon.<BR>—2 To employ, use, apply; लेपान्, शस्त्रम्, कषायम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचरः|अवचर
अवचरः (= परिचारकः) A groom; तुरगावचरं स बोधयित्वा Bu. C. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार|अवचारः
अवचार <i>a.</i> Going or moving down in or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचारः|अवचार
अवचार + .{@-रः@} A place of descent, road; field of action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचारण
अवचारण <i>a.</i> Moving, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचारणम्
अवचारण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Employing, application, mode of proceeding.<BR>—2 A kind of saline preparation (क्षारपाकविधि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार्य|अवचार्य्य
अवचार्य <i>a.</i> To be cast down, to be given, to be put on or applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचि
अवचि €3 P.<BR>—1 To worship, honour, respect.<BR>—2 (€5 U.) To gather, pick up, pluck (with two acc.); गता स्यादवचिन्वाना<BR> कुसुमान्याश्रमद्रुमान् Bk. 6. 10 वृक्षमवचिनोति फलानि Sk.<BR>—3 To take off.<BR>—4 To let down behind, to open (oneʼs cloak).<BR>—5 To examine, select; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचयः|अवचय
अवचयः Gathering (such as flowers, fruits &c.); ततः प्रविशतः<BR> कुसुमावचयमभिनयन्त्यौ सख्यौ Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचायः|अवचाय
अवचायः [अव-चि घञ्] P. III. 3. 40. Gathering flowers (with<BR> the hands); अविरतकुसुमावचायखेदात् Śi. 7. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचायिन्
अवचायिन् <i>a.</i> Gathering, picking off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचिचीषा
अवचिचीषा Desire to gather; समभिसृत्य रसादवलम्बितः प्रमदया<BR> कुसुमावचिचीषया Śi. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचित
अवचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gathered.<BR>—2 Filled, inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूडः|अवचूड
अवचूडः, -लः<BR> [अवनता चूडा अग्रं यस्य वा डो लः] The pendent cloth<BR> on a chariot, an ornament (like a <i>chowri</i>) hanging from the top of<BR> a banner, पिच्छावचूडमनु माधवधाम जग्मुः Śi. 5. 13; दिवसकरवारणस्यावचूलचामरकलापः<BR> K. 26, 114, 116; Śi. 20. 46, 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलः|अवचूल
अवचूडः, -लः<BR> [अवनता चूडा अग्रं यस्य वा डो लः] The pendent cloth<BR> on a chariot, an ornament (like a <i>chowri</i>) hanging from the top of<BR> a banner, पिच्छावचूडमनु माधवधाम जग्मुः Śi. 5. 13; दिवसकरवारणस्यावचूलचामरकलापः<BR> K. 26, 114, 116; Śi. 20. 46, 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूडा
अवचूडः, -लः + .{@-डा@} A garland; अवाप बाल्योचितनीलकण्ठपिच्छावचूडाकलनामिवोरः Śi. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूरिः|अवचूरि
अवचूरिः, अवचूरिका A gloss, short commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूरिका
अवचूरिः, अवचूरिका A gloss, short commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्ण्
अवचूर्ण् €10 P.<BR>—1 To sprinkle with meal, dust.<BR>—2 To cover, put on or over, overlay; चूर्णैः शनैर्व्रणमुखमवचूर्ण्य<BR> Suśr.; भेर्यो दिव्यपुष्पावचूर्णिताः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णनम्
अवचूर्णनम्<BR>—1 Pounding, grinding, reducing to powder.<BR>—2 Sprinkling with powder; especially,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">Page0243-1</a>]<BR> throwing absorbent powders on wounds.<BR>—3 A kind of disease or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0242-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णित|अवचूर्णितं|अवचूर्ण्णित
अवचूर्णित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pounded coarsely; त्रिजातावचूर्णितेन mixed with; Dk. 133.<BR>—2 Ground, crushed, reduced to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूल|अवचूलः
अवचूल = अवचूड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलकः|अवचूलक|अवचूलकं
अवचूलकः, -कम्<BR> A <i>chowri</i> or brush (formed of a cowʼs tail or peacockʼs<BR> feathers) for fanning off flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलकम्
अवचूलकः, -कम्<BR> A <i>chowri</i> or brush (formed of a cowʼs tail or peacockʼs<BR> feathers) for fanning off flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छद्
अवच्छद् €10 P.<BR>—1 To cover over, overspread.<BR>—2 To conceal, obscure, leave in darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छदः|अवच्छद
अवच्छ(च्छा)दः A cover, covering; काञ्चनावच्छादान् (खरान्) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छादः
अवच्छ(च्छा)दः A cover, covering; काञ्चनावच्छादान् (खरान्) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिद्
अवच्छिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To cut off, separate, tear in pieces, break asunder.<BR>—2 To discriminate, distinguish, characterize.<BR>—3 To define, limit, modify (as by time, space &c.) used in Nyāya; see<BR> अवच्छिन्न below.<BR>—4 To detach, excerpt.<BR>—5 To interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिन्न|अवच्छिन्नं
अवच्छिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cut off.<BR>—2 Separated, divided, detached, excerpted; अवच्छिन्नस्य पूर्णेन एकत्वं<BR> प्रतिपाद्यते A. Rām. 1. 1. 49.<BR>—3 (In Logic) Separated or excluded from all other things by the properties<BR> predicated of a thing as peculiar to itself.<BR>—4 Bounded, modified, determined; दिक्कालाद्यनवच्छिन्न Bh. 2. 1.<BR>—5 Particularized, distinguished, characterized, as by an attributive word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदः|अवच्छेद
अवच्छेदः<BR>—1 A part, portion (अवयव).<BR>—2 Boundary, limit.<BR>—3 Separation.<BR>—4 Distinction, distinguishing, particularization (as by attributes).<BR>—5 Determination, decision, settlement; शब्दार्थस्यानवच्छेदे विशेषस्मृतिहेतवः Vāk. P.<BR>—6 That property of a thing which distinguishes in from everything else,<BR> a characteristic property.<BR>—7 Bounding, defining.<BR>—8 Pervading (व्याप्तिः). ˚अवच्छेदः generalizing, removing distinctions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदक|अवच्छेदकं|अवच्छेदकः
अवच्छेदक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Separating.<BR>—2 Determining, deciding, प्रतियोगिकावच्छेदकावच्छिन्नम्.<BR>—3 Bounding, limiting,<BR>—4 Pervading.<BR>—5 Distinguishing, particularizing.<BR>—6 Peculiar, characteristic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदकः|अवच्छेदक|अवच्छेदकं
अवच्छेदक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 That which distinguishes.<BR>—2 A predicate, characteristic property.<BR>—3 Boundary, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदनम्
अवच्छेदनम् Cutting off, separating; determining, bounding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेद्य
अवच्छेद्य <i>a.</i> To be separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरित|अवच्छुरितं|अवछुरित
अवच्छुरित <i>a.</i> Mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरितम्
अवच्छुरित + .{@-तम्@} A hoarse laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजि
अवजि €1 P.<BR>—1 To spoil (deprive by conquest), to win; अवजित्य च तद्धनम् Mb.;<BR> Ms. 11. 80; पुष्पकं नाम विमानं वीर्यादवजितम् Rām.<BR>—2 To recover; हृतां कृष्णामवाजयत् Mb.<BR>—3 To ward off, prevent. Mb. 13.<BR>—4 To conquer; अवजितमधुना तवाहमक्ष्णोः Śi. 7. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजयः|अवजय
अवजयः Defeat, victory over; येनेन्द्रलोकावजयाय दृप्तः R. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजित
अवजित <i>p. p.</i> Conquered; condemned, disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजितिः|अवजिति
अवजितिः <i>f.</i> Conquest, defeat; सुखसङ्गिनं प्रति सुखावजितिः Ki. 6. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजुष्ट
अवजुष्ट <i>a.</i> Visited, frequented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा €9 P. To have a low opinion of, to despise, to treat with contempt,<BR> disregard; अवजानासि मां यस्मात् R. 1. 77; अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं<BR> तनुमाश्रितम् Bg. 9. 11; Bk. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा [अव-ज्ञा-अङ्] Disrespect, contempt; slighting, low opinion;<BR> नात्मन्यवज्ञा कर्तव्या H. 1; disregard (with the obj. in loc. or gen.);<BR> आत्मन्यवज्ञां शिथिलीचकार R. 2. 41; ये नाम केचिदिह नः प्रथयन्त्यवज्ञाम्<BR> Māl. 1. 6; Śānti. 3. 23; अविज्ञावज्ञेयं परितपति नोच्चैरपि बुधम् Udb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवज्ञोपहत, अवज्ञादुःखम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञोपहत
अवज्ञा + -उपहत <i>a.</i> treated with contempt, humiliated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञादुःखम्
अवज्ञा + -दुःखम् the agonies of humiliation; मा जीवन् यः परावज्ञादुःखदग्धोऽपि<BR> जीवति Śi. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञात|अवज्ञातं
अवज्ञात <i>p. p.</i> Disrespected, condemned, disregarded; (दानं)<BR> अवज्ञातं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् Bg. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञानम्
अवज्ञानम् Disrespect, disregard, contempt; अवज्ञानसहस्रैस्तु<BR> दोषाः कष्टतरा धने Mb. 12. 177. 35. ईप्सितं तदवज्ञानात् विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञेय
अवज्ञेय <i>pot. p.</i> To be treated with disrespect; contemptible;<BR> विप्रा हि क्षत्रियात्मानो नावज्ञेयाः कदाचन Y. 1. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट|अवटः
अवट <i>a.</i> [अव-अटन्] Produced in a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटः|अवट
अवट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A hole, cavity.<BR>—2 A pit; क्रौञ्चावटे Rām. 6. 107. 60; अवटे चापि मे राम प्रक्षिपेमं<BR> कलेवरम्; अवटे ये निधीयन्ते Rām. विपाटयन्निव जगद् दंष्ट्राट्टालघटावटैः Bm. 1. 762.<BR>—3 A well.<BR>—4 Any low or depressed part of the body, sinus; अवटश्चैवमेतानि स्थानान्यत्र<BR> शरीरके Y. 3. 98.<BR>—5 A juggler.<BR>—6 Drunk; the commentary of Mahendra on Hemacandraʼs Anekārthasaṃgraha<BR> प्रमत्तेऽपि मङ्खः यथा अवटातङ्कसंकेतनिकेतनसमाश्रयाम्<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवटकच्छपः, अवटनिरोधनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटकच्छपः|अवटकच्छप
अवट + -कच्छपः a tortoise in a hole; (fig.) one who has had no experience,<BR> who has seen nothing of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटनिरोधनः|अवटनिरोधन
अवट + -निरोधनः N. of a particular hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटिः|अवटि
अवटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [अव-अटि]<BR>—1 A hole.<BR>—2 A well.<BR>—3 A sinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटी
अवटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [अव-अटि]<BR>—1 A hole.<BR>—2 A well.<BR>—3 A sinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट <i>a.</i> [नासिकायाः नतम् अवटीटम्, अव-टीटन् नासिकायाः संज्ञायां;<BR> नासिकाप्यवटीटा, पुरुषोऽप्यवटीटः^1 P. V. 2. 31. Sk.] Having a flat nose, flat-nosed.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुः|अवटु
अवटुः [अव-टीक् मित्˚डु]<BR>—1 A hole in the ground.<BR>—2 A well.<BR>—3 The back or nape of the neck; ‘अवटुर्घाटा कृकाटिका’ इत्यमरः.<BR>—4 The depressed part of the body.<BR>—5 A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुः|अवटु
अवटुः + .{@-टुः@} <i>f.</i> The raised portion of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटु|अवटुः
अवटुः + .{@-टु@} <i>n.</i> A hole, a rent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवटुजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुजः|अवटुज
अवटुः + -जः a hind curl; hair on the back of the head; रागवानवटुजेष्ववकृष्य Śi. 10. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट्य
अवट्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Being in a hole; नमः कूप्याय चावट्याय Vāj. 16. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0243-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडङ्गः|अवडङ्ग|अवडंगः
अवडङ्गः, -कः<BR> A market, a mart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडङ्कः|अवडङ्क|अवडंकः
अवडङ्गः, -कः<BR> A market, a mart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडीनम्
अवडीनम् [अव-डी-भावे-क्त] The flight of a bird, flying downward;<BR> (पातानां शतम्) उड्डीनमवडीनं च प्रडीनं डीनमव च Mb. 8. 41. 26-28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवण्ड|अवंड
अवण्ड <i>a.</i> Ved. Not without a tail (said of a cow.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतः|अवत
अवतः [अव-अटच् वेदे पृषो˚ टस्य तः] A well, cistern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसः|अवतंस|अवतंसं
अवतंसः, -सम्<BR> [अव-तंस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A garland.<BR>—2 An earring, a ring-shaped ornament, an ear-ornament (fig. also); गणा<BR> नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः Ku. 1. 55; स्ववाहनक्षोभचलावतंसाः 7. 38;<BR> चन्दनपल्लवावतंसाम् K. 11, 12, 140, 97; R. 13. 49; Dk. 5, 88; Ki. 3. 11;<BR> Śi. 3. 81; ˚उत्पलम् a lotus used as an ornament; Ku. 4. 8;<BR> oft. with अ omitted; यैर्वतंसकुसुमैः प्रियमेताः Śi. 10. 67.<BR>—3 An ornament worn on the head, crest.<BR>—4 (fig.) anything that serves as an ornament; ‘decked with’; तामरसावतंसा<BR> जलसंनिवेशाः Cāt. 2. 3; पुण्डरीकावतंसाभिः परिखाभिः Rām. 5. 4. 25;<BR> पुष्पावतंसं सलिलम् Suśr.; कल्याणावतंसा कल्याणसंपद् Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसम्
अवतंसः, -सम्<BR> [अव-तंस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A garland.<BR>—2 An earring, a ring-shaped ornament, an ear-ornament (fig. also); गणा<BR> नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः Ku. 1. 55; स्ववाहनक्षोभचलावतंसाः 7. 38;<BR> चन्दनपल्लवावतंसाम् K. 11, 12, 140, 97; R. 13. 49; Dk. 5, 88; Ki. 3. 11;<BR> Śi. 3. 81; ˚उत्पलम् a lotus used as an ornament; Ku. 4. 8;<BR> oft. with अ omitted; यैर्वतंसकुसुमैः प्रियमेताः Śi. 10. 67.<BR>—3 An ornament worn on the head, crest.<BR>—4 (fig.) anything that serves as an ornament; ‘decked with’; तामरसावतंसा<BR> जलसंनिवेशाः Cāt. 2. 3; पुण्डरीकावतंसाभिः परिखाभिः Rām. 5. 4. 25;<BR> पुष्पावतंसं सलिलम् Suśr.; कल्याणावतंसा कल्याणसंपद् Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसयति
अवतंसयति Den. P. To use as ear-rings, make earrings of; अवतंसयन्ति<BR> दयमानाः प्रमदाः शिरीषकुसुमानि Ś. 1. 4; अवतंसयैनम् M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसकः|अवतंसक
अवतंसकः An ear-ornament, an ornament in general; अशोकस्तवकेनेव<BR> दिङ्मुखस्यावतंसकम् V. 5. 3; प्रासादाट्टावतंसका (लङ्का) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसित
अवतंसित <i>a.</i> Having a garland, crested; (fig.) decked, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतक्षणम्
अवतक्षणम्<BR>—1 Anything cut in pieces.<BR>—2 Chopped straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतड्
अवतड् €10 P. To strike downwards; विद्युदवताडयति Nir.; to<BR> crush under, trample down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवताडनम्
अवताडनम्<BR>—1 Crushing, trampling or treading under; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः कुसुमस्य<BR> सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि स्थितिर्न चरणैरवताडनानि U. 1. 14.<BR>—2 Striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतन्
अवतन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To stretch or extend downwards; ऋज्वीर्दधानैरवतत्य कन्धराः Śi. 12. 18;<BR> विशालमूलावततः (न्यग्रोध) Hariv.<BR>—2 To overspread, cover; नभसि मेघावतते Suśr.; खमवतत्य सलिलदाः<BR> Bṛ. S. 24. 19.<BR>—3 To loosen; undo (especially a bow-string).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतत
अवतत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Overspread, covered; लताशतैरवतता (नदी) Rām. 5. 14. 26<BR> तुरङ्गौघैरवतता (भूः) <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 Loosened, slackened; ˚धन्वन् whose bow is unbent. Vāj. 3. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवततिः|अवतति
अवततिः <i>f.</i> Stretching, extending; प्रालेयावततिम्लान Ki. 11. 4<BR> (snow-fall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतानः|अवतान
अवतानः<BR>—1 Stretching of a bow.<BR>—2 The unbending of a bow.<BR>—3 A downward face.<BR>—4 The spreading of a plant; लताशतैरवततामवतानशतैस्तथा Rām.<BR>—5 A cover (in general); an awning; Mb. 2. 9. 3.<BR>—6 N. of the verses; Vāj. 14. 56-63.<BR>—7 Tendril; लतावतानावतः (महाद्रुमः) Mb. 3. 24. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्
अवतप् €1 P. To radiate, heat or light downwards; महदेषावतपति<BR> Av. 12. 4. 39. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To irradiate, heat; अथावताप्य पृथिवीं पूषा दिवससंक्षये जगामास्तम् Mb.<BR>—2 To illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्त
अवतप्त <i>p. p.</i> Heated, irradiated; अवतप्ते नकुलस्थितम्<BR> an ichneumonʼs standing on hot ground (metaphorically said of the inconstancy<BR> of man). क्षेपे P. II. 1. 47; अवतप्ते नकुलस्थितं त एतत् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतापिन्
अवतापिन् <i>a.</i> (A place) where the sun strikes vertically down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतमसम्
अवतमसम् [अवततं व्याप्तं तमः अच्समासः अवसमन्धेभ्यस्तमसः P. V. 4. 79]<BR>—1 Slight or dim darkness; क्षीणेऽवतमसं तमः Ak.<BR>—2 Darkness (in general); अवतमसभिदायै भास्वताभ्युद्गतेन Śi. 11. 57<BR> (where Malli. says यद्यपि क्षीणेऽवतमसं तमः इत्युक्तं तथापि<BR> इह विरोधाद्विशेषानादरेण सामान्यमेव ग्राह्यम्).<BR>—3 Obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरम्
अवतरम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Farther away, more distantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतस्
अवतस् <i>ind.</i> Below, in the lower world; मता फणवतोऽवतो Ki. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतर्पणम्
अवतर्पणम् A soothing remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतॄ
अवतॄ^1 €1 P.<BR>—1 To descend, alight, come down; रथादवततार च R. 1. 54, 13. 68;<BR> वसन् ददर्शावतरन्तमम्बरात् Śi. 1. 1; यमुनातटमवतीर्णः<BR> Pt. 1; मेघपदवीमवतीर्णौ स्वः Ś. 7; कदैतदवतरिष्यति चक्रं<BR> मस्तकात् Pt. 5; (fig. also) इति मतिरेव न बोधपदवीमवतरति<BR> K. 289 fails to see; वागेव मे नाभिधेयविषयमवतरति त्रपया 151<BR> I cannot speak for very shame.<BR>—2 To flow or run into, discharge contents, join (as a river); सागरं<BR> वर्जयित्वा कुत्र वा महानद्यवतरति Ś. 3; see अवतीर्ण also.<BR>—3 To enter, to enter into, to come to; अवतरतः सिद्धिपथं शब्दः<BR> स्वमनोरथस्येव M. 1. 22; Śi. 9. 32; त्वदीयं देशमवतीर्य M. 5.<BR>—4 To begin, commence; अवतरतु भवान् Dk. 152; तत्प्रेयसीमाहूय<BR> सङ्गीतकमवतरामि Dhūrt. 1.<BR>—5 To present oneself, appear forth, come; प्रसभमवततार चित्तजन्मा Ki. 10. 17.<BR>—6 To descend (as a deity) into the world in the form of a mortal; शापावतीर्ण<BR> Ks. 2. 21; मुनिकन्या च सा शापात्तस्यां जाताववातरत् 2. 31; Rāj. T. 1. 130, 5. 66;<BR> विष्णुरेवावतीर्णोऽसौ Mārk. P.<BR>—7 To get over, subdue, conquer; अवतीर्णोऽस्मि यद्रोगमतिदुस्तरम्<BR> Ks. 21. 194; अव तस्य बलं तिर Rv. 10. 133. 5.<BR>—8 To cross over; त्वयावतीर्णोर्ण उताप्तकामः Bhāg. 3. 24. 34. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to descend, bring or fetch down; मार्गे कथंचिदवतार्य<BR> Mu. 3. 9; रथात्, वृक्षात्, शूलाग्रात् &c.<BR>—2 To take down, put or set down अवतारय सलिलसमीपम् K. 38; मात्रां<BR> कक्षान्तरादवतार्य Pt. 1; स्वभुजादवतारिता R. 1. 34; अवतार्यतां रथः V. 1.<BR>—3 To take off, remove, withdraw, put aside; स्वगात्रादवतार्य भूषणानि<BR> Mu. 2, 5; अथाङ्गराजादवतार्य चक्षुः R. 6. 30, अथोरुदेशादवतार्य<BR> पादम् Ku. 3. 11; Śi. 9. 36.<BR>—4 To bring downwards.<BR>—5 To bend down.<BR>—6 To introduce, set a-going, make current, begin; तेन विद्यावतारिता<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 485; तत्र तया सत्रेऽवतारिते 2. 58.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: The root is tF -  as AP and others spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0244-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरः|अवतर|अवतरं
अवतरः Descent शंसन्ति कार्यावतरं हि सन्तः N. 3. 53; Śi. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणम्
अवतरणम्<BR>—1 Descending for bathing in water &c. गङ्गा˚, अप्सरस्तीर्थ˚; descending;<BR> or alighting (in general), coming down; स्तन्य˚.<BR>—2 An incarnation; see अवतार,<BR>—3 Crossing.<BR>—4 Sudden disapperance.<BR>—5 Steps or stairs leading to a river.<BR>—6 A holy bathing place (तीर्थ).<BR>—7 Translating from one language into another.<BR>—8 Introduction.<BR>—9 An extract, a quotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणमङ्गलम्
अवतरणम् + .{@-मङ्गलम्@} A solemn reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणिका
अवतरणिका<BR>—1 A short prayer at the beginning of a work which, it is supposed, causes<BR> the divinity so addressed to descend from heaven.<BR>—2 Introduction, preface.<BR>—3 Synopsis. (fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणी
अवतरणी [अवतरति ग्रन्थोऽनया अवतॄ करणे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Preface.<BR>—2 Succession, order, method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारः|अवतार
अवतारः [अव-तॄ करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 Descent, alighting; descending or going down into; (fig) accepting,<BR> resorting to पाखण्डिपथावतारः Dk. 47; advent, setting in; वसन्तावतारसमये Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Form, manifestation; मत्स्यादिभिरवतारैरवतारवताऽवतावसुधाम् Śaṅkara.<BR>—3 Descent of a deity upon earth, incarnation in general; कोऽप्येष संप्रति<BR> नवः पुरुषावतारः U. 5. 33; धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामवतार इवाङ्गवान्<BR> R. 10. 84; ऋष्यवतारोऽयं नृपतिः Ks. 7. 18.<BR>—4 An incarnation of Viṣṇu; विष्णुर्येन दशावतारगहने क्षिप्तो महासंकटे<BR> Bh. 2. 95. (There are ten incarnations of Viṣṇu; the following verse<BR> from Gīt. describes them; वेदानुद्धरते जगन्निवहते भूगोलमुद्बिभ्रते<BR> दैत्यं दारयते बलिं छलयते क्षत्रक्षयं कुर्वते । पौलस्त्यं जयते<BR> हलं कलयते कारुण्यमातन्वते म्लेच्छान्मूर्च्छयते दशाकृतिकृते कृष्णाय<BR> तुभ्यं नमः ॥ मत्स्यः कूर्मो वराहश्च नरसिंहोऽथ वामनः । रामो रामश्च<BR> कृष्णश्च बुद्धः कल्की च ते दश ॥ Varāha P.)<BR>—5 Any new appearance, growth, rise; नवावतारं कमलोदिवोत्पलम्<BR> R. 3. 36; परीवादनवावतारः 5. 24; यौवनावतारे K. 289; Ve. 3;<BR> Śānti. 2. 26, 3. 14; Ks. 8. 30;<BR>—6 Any distinguished person (who, in the language of respect, is called<BR> an अवतार or incarnation of a deity).<BR>—7 Aiming at object.<BR>—8 A landing place; रुद्धे गजेन सरितः सरुषावतारे Śi. 5. 33.<BR>—9 A sacred bathing place.<BR>—10 Translation.<BR>—11 A poud, tank,<BR>—12 Introduction, preface.<BR>—13 Crossing; ˚रं लभ् to gain oneʼs object (with gen.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवतारकथा, अवतारमन्त्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारकथा
अवतारः + -कथा ‘account of an अवतार’, N. of a chapter in शङ्करविजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारमन्त्रः|अवतारमन्त्र
अवतारः + -मन्त्रः the prayer causing the descent of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारक
अवतारक <i>a.</i> (-रिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Making oneʼs appearance.<BR>—2 Making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारणम्
अवतारणम्<BR>—1 Causing to descend.<BR>—2 Translation.<BR>—3 Possession by an evil spirit.<BR>—4 Worship, adoration.<BR>—5 The ends or border of a garment.<BR>—6 Preface or introduction (to a work).<BR>—7 Descent, appearance (अवतरण); पौष्यं पौलोममास्तीकमादिरंशावतारणम् Mb. 1. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारिन्
अवतारिन् <i>a.</i> Making oneʼs appearance, making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्ण|अवतीर्णः|अवतीर्ण्ण
अवतीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Descended, alighted, come down; शैलराजावतीर्णां जह्नोः कन्याम्<BR> Me. 52; जलनिधिमनुरूपं जह्नुकन्यावतीर्णा R. 6. 85; संसारपथमवतीर्णानाम्<BR> K. 175 who have entered upon mundane life.<BR>—2 Bathed in; उदधिमिवावतीर्णः K. 158; come to, entered into.<BR>—3 Appeared as an incarnation; तदर्थमवतीर्णोऽसौ मन्नियोगाच्चतुर्भुजः Mb.; Pt. 1.<BR>—4 Crossed, passed over; अपि नामावतीर्णोऽसि बाणगोचरम् Māl. 1 crossed<BR> the path, gone within the range, of arrows; दर्शनपथमवतीर्णः Ś. 3.<BR>—5 Fallen (as the night); अवतीर्णायां तस्यां यामिन्याम् K. 269; भरेणावतीर्णायां<BR> रजन्याम् K. 368.<BR>—6 Translated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्णम्
अवतीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} (= अवतारः) Manifestation; cf. पद्मावतीर्णपूर्णा Svapna. 1. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवतीर्णर्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्णर्ण
अवतीर्ण + -ऋण <i>a.</i> absolved from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतूलयति
अवतूलयति Den. P. To rub with cotton; तूलैरवकृष्णाति तूलेन<BR> तृणाग्रमवघट्टयति Bop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतोका
अवतोका [अवपतितं तोकम् अस्याः; प्रा˚ ब˚] A woman or a cow miscarrying<BR> from accident यः कृणोति मृतवत्सामवतोकामिमां स्त्रियम् Av. 8. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्त
अवत्त, -अवत्तिन्<BR> See under अवदो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्तिन्
अवत्त, -अवत्तिन्<BR> See under अवदो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्रस्त
अवत्रस्त <i>a.</i> Terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्सारः|अवत्सार
अवत्सारः N. of a vedic seer, descendant of Kaśyapa; अवत्सारस्य<BR> स्पृणवाम रण्वभिः Rv. 5. 44. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्सीय
अवत्सीय <i>a.</i> Not suitable for a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदंश|अवदंशः
अवदंश [अवदश्यते पानरुच्यर्थम्; अवदंश् कर्मणि घञ्] —1 Any<BR> pungent food which excites thirst, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदत्त
अवदत्त <i>a.</i> P. VII. 4. 47. —1 Given away. -Finished, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदह्
अवदह् €1 P. To burn down, destroy; अवादहो दिव आ दस्युमुच्चा Rv. 1. 33. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाघः|अवदाघ
अवदाघः<BR>—1 Heat, burning down.<BR>—2 The hot season, summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहः|अवदाह|अवदाहं
अवदाहः, -हम्<BR> [अवसादितो दाहो येन; प्रा˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 N. of the root of a plant. Andropogon muricatum. (वीरण; Mar. वाळा).<BR>—2 Burning down, heat; ˚इष्टकापथम् the root of the वीरण plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहम्
अवदाहः, -हम्<BR> [अवसादितो दाहो येन; प्रा˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 N. of the root of a plant. Andropogon muricatum. (वीरण; Mar. वाळा).<BR>—2 Burning down, heat; ˚इष्टकापथम् the root of the वीरण plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात <i>a.</i> [अव-दै-क्त]<BR>—1 Beautiful; अवदातकान्तिः Dk. 107, 37.<BR>—2 Clean, clear, pure, spotless, refined, purified, polished; येषां<BR> त्रीण्यवदातानि विद्या योनिश्च कर्म च Mb. 3. 1. 27. सर्वविद्यावदातचेताः<BR> K. 36; so विद्यावदातं मुखम्; Bh. 2. 2. 5; शास्त्र˚<BR>—3 Bright, white; आपिशङ्गावदातया देहप्रभया K. 36, 65, 128, 187, 189, 43, 62, 95;<BR> रजनिकरकलावदातं कुलम् K. 233; कुन्दावदाताः<BR> कलहंसमाला; Bk. 2. 18; cf. also Ki. 11. 75, 3. 25, 13. 37; Śānti. 3. 14.<BR>—4 Virtuous, meritorious; अन्यस्मिञ्जन्मनि न कृतमवदातं कर्म K. 62.<BR>—5 Yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदातः|अवदात|अवदातं
अवदात + .{@-तः@} White or yellow colour. cf. अवदातः सिते पीते Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदानम्
अवदानम्<BR>—1 A pure or approved occupation.<BR>—2 An accomplished act.<BR>—3 A valorous or glorious act,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">Page0246-1</a>]<BR> prowess, heroic act, heroism, glorious achievement; संगीयमानत्रिपुरावदानः<BR> Ku. 7. 48; Śi. 7. 2, 18. 16; प्रापदस्त्रमवदानतोषितात् R. 11. 21;<BR> Ki. 17. 16; तत्त्वत्पूर्वावदानेभ्यो न रोचते Dk. 52; Ki. 3. 43, 13. 32.<BR>—4 Object of a legend.<BR>—5 Objection; जुहुयान्मूलमन्त्रेण षोडशर्चावदानतः Bhāg. 11. 27. 41<BR> Sacrificial object for an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0245-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान्तः
अवदान्तः Hyperanthera Morunga (Mar. शेवगा); Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान्य
अवदान्य <i>a.</i> Niggardly, stingy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदावद
अवदावद <i>a.</i> Ved. Having no bad reputation. स वै लोकोऽवदावदः<BR> Ait. Br. 7. 13. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदॄ
अवदॄ €9 P. To split or force open, to rend or tear asunder. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to burst, to rend, split; मनःशिलागिरेः शृङ्गं वज्रेणेवावदारितम् Rām.<BR>—2 To dig down, excavate; तदर्थमुर्वीमवदारयाद्भिः R. 13. 3;<BR> वसुधां चावदारयेत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदरणम्
अवदरणम् Breaking (as a boil), bursting, separating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारणम्
अवदारणम्<BR>—1 Tearing, dividing, digging down, cutting into pieces.<BR>—2 (करणे-ल्युट्) A spade, hoe.<BR>—3 Breaking open, bursting open; अवदारणकाले तु पृथिवी नावदीर्यते<BR> Rām. 2. 77. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्ण|अवदीर्णं
अवदीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Split into two, divided, broken; अवदीर्णशुक्तिपुटमुक्तमौक्तिकप्रकरैः Śi. 13. 37.<BR>—2 Melted, fused, liquefied.<BR>—3 Bewildered, perplexed: भयावदीर्णः संत्रासादबद्धं बहु भाषसे Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदो
अवदो €4 P.<BR>—1 To cut off, divide.<BR>—2 (Ved.) To appease (anger); अव स्तोमेभी रुद्रं दिषीय Rv. 2. 33. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यत्
अवद्यत् <i>a.</i> Breaking off; शतशो विशिखानवद्यते Ki. 15. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्त
अवत्त <i>p. p.</i> [अव-दो-खण्डने कर्मणि क्त] Cut off;<BR> उत्सादतोऽङ्गादङ्गादवत्तानां करतऽएव Vāj. 21. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्तिन्
अवत्तिन् <i>a.</i> [अवत्तमनेन इष्टा˚ इनि] One who divides or cuts<BR> off; पञ्च˚ dividing into five parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदानम्
अवदानम् [अव-दो-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Cutting or dividing into pieces.<BR>—2 A part, portion; हृदयाद्यवदानानाम् Ś. B.<BR>—3 Transgression.<BR>—4 The root of a plant (वीरण); see अवदाह^1 also.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदोहः|अवदोह
अवदोहः<BR>—1 Milking.<BR>—2 Milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit to be condemned, censurable, not to be praised; न चापि काव्यं<BR> नवमित्यवद्यम् M. 1. 2; किमवद्यः करिकुम्भजो मणिः Śi. 16. 45.<BR>—2 Defective, faulty, blamable, disagreeable, disliked; उदवहदनवद्यां<BR> तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70; see अनवद्य also.<BR>—3 Unfit to be told.<BR>—4 Low, inferior.<BR>—5 Sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यम्
अवद्य + .{@-द्यम्@}<BR>—1 A fault, defect, imperfection; किं न वोचस्यसद्वृत्ते आत्मावद्यं<BR> वदाशु मे Bhāg. 9. 14. 12.<BR>—2 Sin, vice; साक्षात्कृतं नेमुरवद्यमृग्यतः Bhāg. 10. 22. 20.<BR>—3 Blame, censure, reproach; उदवहदनवद्यां तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70.<BR>—4 Shame.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवद्यगोहन, अवद्यभीः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यगोहन
अवद्य + -गोहन <i>a.</i> concealing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">Page0246-2</a>]<BR> or keeping off want; समाने अहन् त्रिरवद्यगोहना Rv. 1. 33. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यभीः
अवद्य + -भीः <i>f.</i> fear of vices or sin; अवद्यभिया बहवः पृणन्ति<BR> Rv. 10. 107. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यवत्|अवद्यवन्त्
अवद्यवत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Disgraceful, lamentable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्योतनम्
अवद्योतनम्<BR>—1 Light.<BR>—2 Illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्योतिन्
अवद्योतिन् <i>a.</i> Shining down upon, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्रङ्गः|अवद्रङ्ग|अवद्रंगः
अवद्रङ्गः A market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध|अवधः
अवध <i>a.</i> Ved. Inviolable, invulnerable. हुवे स्वर्वदवधं<BR> नमस्वत् Rv. 1. 185. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधः|अवध
अवध + .{@-धः@} Exemption from death; यज्ञोऽस्य सूत्यै सर्वस्य तस्माद्यज्ञे<BR> वधोऽवधः Ms. 5. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्य
अवध्य <i>a.</i> Not to be killed, inviolable, sacred; यावानवध्यस्य<BR> वधे Ms. 9. 249. ˚ता, ˚भावः, ˚त्वम् exemption from death, inviolability;<BR> वधार्हाणामवध्यताम् R. 17. 19; सदैवावध्यभावेन यथार्थस्य हि वाचकः<BR> H. 3. 15; R. 10. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधर्ष्य
अवधर्ष्य <i>a.</i> To be defied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधा
अवधा €3 Ā.<BR>—1 To place down, deposit; अवधाय श्वभ्रे मृत्पिण्डम् Kāty.; यथा<BR> क्षुरः क्षुरधानेऽवहितः Śat. Br.; ततस्तांस्तेषु कुण्डेषु गर्भानवदधे<BR> तदा Mb.; वासुदेवः स्वमाययात्मन्यवधीयमानः Bhāg.; to fix; पादाग्रे<BR> दृशमवधाय निश्चलाङ्गी Mu. 5. 13.<BR>—2 To apply (as the mind).<BR>—3 To be attentive; इतोऽवधत्तां देवराजः Mv. 6.<BR>—4 To shut, close, press together. ━<i>Pass.</i> To be placed, applied,<BR> or directed (mind); अवधीयताम् listen, hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधातव्य
अवधातव्य, अवधानीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be attended to, deserving attention and care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानीय
अवधातव्य, अवधानीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be attended to, deserving attention and care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानम्
अवधानम्<BR>—1 Attention, अवधानपरे चकार सा प्रलयान्तोन्मिषिते विलोचने Ku. 4. 2;<BR> अवधानं दीयमानं प्रार्थये Ve. 1; intentness, attentiveness;<BR> दत्तावधानः शृणोति hears attentively.<BR>—2 Devotion, care, carefulness; अवधानात् carefully or attentively;<BR> शृणुत जना अवधानात् क्रियामिमां कालिदासस्य V. 1. 2, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानिन्
अवधानिन् <i>a.</i> Attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिः|अवधि
अवधिः [अव-धा-कि]<BR>—1 Application, attention.<BR>—2 Boundary, limit exclusive or inclusive, (in time or space); conclusion,<BR> determination; एकैकस्य जगत्त्रयप्रमथनत्राणावधिर्योग्यता Mv. 1. 46;<BR> रवितेजसामवधिनाधिवेष्टितम् Ki. 12. 22.<BR>—3 Furthest limit; दृष्ट आह्लादनीयानामवधिः K. 124; स्मरशापावधिदां<BR> सरस्वतीम् Ku. 4. 43; conclusion; oft. at the end of comp., in the sense<BR> of ‘ending with’, ‘as far as’, ‘till’; एष ते जीवितावधिः प्रवादः<BR> U. 1. तत्प्रत्यागमनकालावधयोऽपि तावत् ध्रियन्तां प्राणाः K. 171;<BR> व्याडी रक्षतु मे देहं ततः प्रत्यागमावधि Ks. 4. 100; स्कन्धः स्यान्मूलाच्छाखावधिस्तरोः Ak.<BR>—4 Period of time, time; सर्वे निदाघावधिना प्रमृष्टाः R. 16. 52; शेषान्<BR> मासान् विरहदिवसस्थापितस्यावधेर्वा Me. 89; अपि समाप्तः वनवासस्यावधिः<BR> Mv. 7, 2. 48; विवाहं मासावधिकमकल्पयत् Dk. 54, 174; K. 328; Ki. 12. 17;<BR> यदवधि-तदवधि from or ever since, till. Bv. 2. 79; अथ<BR> चेदवधिः प्रतीक्ष्यते Ki. 2. 16.<BR>—5 An engagement, appointment; रमणीयोऽवधिर्विधिना विसंवादितः Ś. 6.<BR>—6 A division, district, department; जनपदतदवध्योश्च P. IV. 2. 124.<BR>—7 A hole, pit.<BR>—8 Authority, standard<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">Page0247-1</a>]<BR> (प्रमाण); वयं तु भरतादेशावधिं कृत्वा हरीश्वर Rām. 4. 18. 25.<BR> ˚ता, ˚त्वम् limit, limitation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवधिज्ञानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0246-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिज्ञानम्
अवधिः + -ज्ञानम् The faculty of perceiving ever what is not within the<BR> reach of the senses; N. of the third degree of knowledge; (मतिज्ञान,<BR> श्रुतिज्ञान, अवधिज्ञान, मनःपर्यायज्ञान, केवलज्ञान Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिमत्|अवधिमन्त्
अवधिमत् <i>a.</i> Limited, bounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधेय
अवधेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be placed down or deposited.<BR>—2 To be attended to, to be believed.<BR>—3 To be known or apprehended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधेयम्
अवधेय + .{@-यम्@} Attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित|अवहितं
अवहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deposited, placed; यथा ह्यवहितो वह्निर्दारुष्वेकः स्वयोनिषु Bhāg. 1. 2. 32;<BR> यथा क्षुरः क्षुरधानेऽवहितः Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 7.<BR>—2 Attentive, careful; शृणु राजन्नवहितः सह भ्रातृभिरच्युत Mb. 3. 52. 54.<BR> शृणुत मनोभिरवहितैः V. 1. 2; शृणु मेऽवहिता वचः<BR> Rām.; Me. 102.<BR>—3 Celebrated, known.<BR>—4 Plunged into, fallen into; त्रितः कूपेऽवहितो देवान् हवत ऊतये<BR> Rv. 1. 105. 17. ˚ता application, attention.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवहिताञ्जलि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहिताञ्जलि
अवहित + -अञ्जलि <i>a.</i> with joined hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधाव्
अवधाव् €1 U. To run down, to drop down, to run after. अदो यदवधावत्यवत्कमधि<BR> पर्वतात् Av. 2. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावनम्
अवधावनम्<BR>—1 Running after, pursuing, seizure.<BR>—2 Cleaning, washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावित
अवधावित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Chased, pursued.<BR>—2 Cleaned, washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीर्
अवधीर् €10 P. To disregard, disrespect, treat with contempt, slight;<BR> अवधीरितसुहृद्वचनस्य H. 1; अवधीर्य धैर्यकलिता दयितम् Śi. 9. 59.<BR> Amaru. 83; to despise, repudiate, repulse; तत्किमवधीरयति<BR> मामार्यपुत्रः M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरणम्
अवधीरणम् Treating with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरणा
अवधीरणा Disrespect, despising; repulse; कृतवत्यसि नावधीरणामपराद्धेऽपि<BR> यदा चिरं मयि R. 8. 48; M. 3. 20; अयं स ते तिष्ठति संगमोत्सुको<BR> विशङ्कसे भीरु यतोऽवधीरणाम् Ś. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरित
अवधीरित <i>p. p.</i> Disrespected, disregarded, slighted; अवधीरितार्तवगुणम्<BR> Ki. 6. 25 excelled, set at naught; अचेतनं नाम गुणं न लक्षयेन्मयैव<BR> कस्मादवधीरिता प्रिया Ś. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरिन्
अवधीरिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Despising, scorning.<BR>—2 Excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधू
अवधू €5 U.<BR>—1 To shake, move, wave, cause to tremble; रेणुः पवनावधूतः R. 7. 43;<BR> लीलावधूतैः चामरैः Me. 37; Ṛs. 6. 15; Ki. 6. 3; Śi. 13. 36.<BR>—2 To shake off or out, shake, toss (lit. and fig.), remove (fig. also);<BR> overcome, get the better of; राजसत्त्वमवधूय मातृकम् R. 11. 90;<BR> सुरवधूरवधूतभयाः शरैः 9. 19 removing the fears of; अवधूय<BR> तद्वयथाम् 3. 61; व्रजन्ति शत्रूनवधूय निःस्पृहाः शमेन सिद्धिं मुनयो<BR> न भूभृतः Ki. 1. 42; रुषावधूय रक्षांसि Rām.<BR>—3 To discard, spurn, reject or treat with contempt, disregard; चण्ङी<BR> मामवधूय पादपतितम् V. 4. 67; Ku. 3. 8; अवधूतप्रणिपाताः V. 3. 5;<BR> अवधूतदुहितृप्रार्थनस्य Dk. 13. ━<i>Caus.</i> (-धूनयति) To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूत|अवधूतः
अवधूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken, waved. Māl. 9. 18.<BR>—2 Discarded, rejected, despised; R. 19. 43.<BR>—3 Insulted,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">Page0247-2</a>]<BR> humiliated. हृतदारोऽवधूतश्च नाहं जीवितमुत्सहे Mb. 3. 282. 36.<BR>—4 Excelled, surpassed; लीलावधूतपद्मा कथयन्ती पक्षपातमधिकं नः Ratn. 2. 8.<BR>—5 Attacked, overcome.<BR>—6 Separated from worldly attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूतः|अवधूत
अवधूत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 An ascetic who has renounced all worldly attachments and connections;<BR> यो विलङ्घ्याश्रमान्वर्णानात्मन्येव स्थितः पुमान् । अतिवर्णाश्रमी योगी अवधूतः<BR> स उच्यते ॥ or अक्षरत्वात् वरेण्यत्वात् धूतसंसारबन्धनात् । तत्त्वमस्यर्थसिद्धत्वादवधूतोऽभिधीयते<BR> ॥ सदाप्लुतोऽधःशयनोऽवधूतः Bhāg. 3. 1. 19. अवधूतोपेक्षिते च<BR> कम्पिते चाश्रमान्तरे । Nm.<BR>—2 Smelling sense, nose, नालिनी नालिनी च प्राग्द्वारावेकत्र निर्मिते ।<BR> अवधूतसखस्ताभ्यां विषयं याति सौरभम् ॥ Bhāg. 4. 25. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवधूतवेश<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूतवेश
अवधूत + -वेश <i>a.</i> undressed, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूननम्
अवधूननम्<BR>—1 Shaking, waving; पादस्पर्शस्तु रक्षांसि दुष्कृतीनवधूननम् Ms. 3. 230;<BR> अमन्ददष्टौष्ठकरावधूननम् Ki. 8. 6.<BR>—2 The practice of medicine, curing.<BR>—3 Agitation, trembling.<BR>—4 Disregarding.<BR>—5 Trampling on, treading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूकः|अवधूक
अवधूकः One having no wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूपित
अवधूपित <i>a.</i> Perfumed with incense; Rām. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूलनम्
अवधूलनम् Sprinkling absorbent powders on sores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधृ
अवधृ €10 U.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To determine, fix, resolve; इत्यवधार्य Pt. 1; यन्मयाऽवधारितम्<BR> Mk. 4. चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा Śi. 1. 3; विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयमवधारितम् M. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To ascertain, determine accurately, make out, know, perceive,<BR> understand; न विश्वमूर्तेरवधार्यते वपुः Ku. 5. 78; Mu. 3. 4.<BR>—2 To consider or regard, think, look upon; मृतां मामवधारय Mb.;<BR> कुलीनेत्यवधार्यताम् Ks. 21. 124; Śi. 9. 22.<BR>—3 To hear, listen to, become acquainted with; वानप्रस्थस्य धर्मं<BR> ते कथयाम्यवधार्यताम् Mārk. P.<BR>—4 To reflect, consider, think; बालकोऽयमित्यवधार्य Pt. 4.<BR>—5 To limit, restrict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारः|अवधार
अवधारः Accurate determination, limitation; सर्वत्र यदवधारेणोच्यते<BR> स एकान्तः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारक
अवधारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Determining accurately; इष्टावधारकं वाक्यम् आशीः Bharata.<BR>—2 Restricting oneself to anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारण|अवधारणं
अवधारण <i>a.</i> Restrictive, limiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणम्
अवधारण + .{@-णम्, -णा@}<BR>—1 Ascertainment, determination; मान˚ Dk. 161.<BR>—2 Affirmation, emphasis.<BR>—3 Limitation (of the sense of words); यावदवधारणे, एवावधारणे;<BR> मात्रं कार्त्स्न्येऽवधारणे Ak.; तुरत्रावधारणार्थः<BR>—4 Restriction to a certain instance or instances to the exclusion of all others.<BR>—5 Taking up, expressing, reciting (a name); न त्वां देवीमहं मन्ये<BR> राज्ञः संज्ञावधारणात् Rām. 5. 33. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणा
अवधारण + .{@-णम्, -णा@}<BR>—1 Ascertainment, determination; मान˚ Dk. 161.<BR>—2 Affirmation, emphasis.<BR>—3 Limitation (of the sense of words); यावदवधारणे, एवावधारणे;<BR> मात्रं कार्त्स्न्येऽवधारणे Ak.; तुरत्रावधारणार्थः<BR>—4 Restriction to a certain instance or instances to the exclusion of all others.<BR>—5 Taking up, expressing, reciting (a name); न त्वां देवीमहं मन्ये<BR> राज्ञः संज्ञावधारणात् Rām. 5. 33. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणीय
अवधारणीय, अवधार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be ascertained determined<BR> or considered; विष्णोरिवास्यानवधारणीयम् R. 13. 5; परिणतिरवधार्या<BR> यत्नतः पण्डितेन Bh. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधार्य|अवधार्य्य|अवधार्य्यः
अवधारणीय, अवधार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be ascertained determined<BR> or considered; विष्णोरिवास्यानवधारणीयम् R. 13. 5; परिणतिरवधार्या<BR> यत्नतः पण्डितेन Bh. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारित|अवधारितः
अवधारित <i>p. p.</i> Ascertained, known, well observed, marked; सम्यगवधारितम् Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधृत
अवधृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Determined, resolved, settled.<BR>—2 Heard<BR>—3 Understood, made out.<BR>—4 (<i>n.</i> pl.) Organs of Senses (in Sāṅkhya Phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्य
अवध्य See under अवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्यै
अवध्यै €1 P. To think ill of, disregard; सोऽवध्यातः सुतैरेवम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 12. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्यानम्
अवध्यानम् Disregard; यथा तरे सदवध्यानमंहः Bhāg. 5. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्र
अव(ब)ध्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Not injurious, innoxious, beneficent. See अवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्र
अव(ब)ध्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Not injurious, innoxious, beneficent. See अवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंस्
अवध्वंस् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To apply oneself to, set about.<BR>—2 To strew over, scatter, spread; ध्वान्तं तमोऽव दध्वसे Rv. 10. 113. 7.<BR> चूर्णैरवध्वंसते Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cast down.<BR>—2 To strew over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंसः|अवध्वंस
अवध्वंसः<BR>—1 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>—2 Powder, dust; यः पुरुषः पारुषेयोऽवध्वंस इवारुणः Av. 5. 22. 3.<BR>—3 Disrespect, Censure, Blame.<BR>—4 Falling off or from.<BR>—5 Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वस्त|अवध्वस्तः
अवध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Destroyed, perished.<BR>—2 Censured, disrespected.<BR>—3 Pounded coarsely or badly.<BR>—4 Abandoned.<BR>—5 Sprinkled.<BR>—6 Scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्
अवनम् [अव्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Protection, defence; भुजोऽनवने P. I. 3. 66; Nalod. 1. 4.<BR>—2 Gratifying, pleasing.<BR>—3 Wish, desire.<BR>—4 Delight, satisfaction.<BR>—5 Hurry, speed. cf. अवनं खण्डने त्राणे गतौ तृप्ते च याचने । श्रवणे<BR> च क्रियायां च अवाप्तिप्रीतिदीप्तिषु । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनक्षत्रम्
अवनक्षत्रम् The disappearance of the stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्
अवनम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bow down, to bend down, stoop; अवनम्य वक्षसि Śi. 9. 74<BR>—2 To bend oneself, hang down; त्वय्यादातुं जलमवनते Me. 48. See<BR> अवनत also. ━<i>Caus.</i> (अवननामयति) To bend down, bend;<BR> अवनमय द्विषतां शिरांसि K. 109;<BR> श्वपुच्छमवनामितम् Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनत|अवनतं
अवनत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bent down, hung down, downcast; विनय˚, प्रश्रय˚, लज्जा˚, ˚उत्तरकायम्<BR> R. 9. 60; फलपुष्पैरवनतान् Rām. cf. also लिखन्नास्ते भूमिं बहिरवनतः<BR> प्राणदयितः Amaru. 7.<BR>—2 Verging in the west, setting; रजनिरवनतेन्दुर्लज्जयाधोमुखी च Śi. 10. 91.<BR>—3 Bending, stooping, deepened, not projecting.<BR>—4 Humble.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवनताङ्ग, अवनतकाय, अवनतमुख, अवनतशीर्षन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनताङ्ग
अवनत + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> with stooping limbs;^1 अद्य प्रभृत्यवनताङ्गि तवास्मि<BR> दासः Ku. 5. 86.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनतकाय
अवनत + -काय <i>a.</i> bending the body, crouching down; ˚उत्तरकाय R. 9. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनतमुख
अवनत + -मुख <i>a.</i> with down-cast countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनतशीर्षन्
अवनत + -शीर्षन् <i>a.</i> bowing the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनतिः|अवनति
अवनतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bending, bowing down, stooping; अवनतिमवनेः Mu. 1. 2, 3. 8; Śi. 9. 8.<BR>—2 Declining in the west, setting; गतवत्यराजत जपाकुसुमस्तबकद्युतौ<BR> दिनकरेऽवनतिम् Śi. 9. 8.<BR>—3 A bow, prostration.<BR>—4 Bending (as a bow); धनुषामवनतिः K. (where अ˚ also means ‘stooping’).<BR>—5 Modesty, absence of insolence, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्र
अवनम्र <i>a.</i> Bowed, bent; पर्याप्तपुष्पस्तबकावनम्रा Ku. 3. 54;<BR> पाद˚ fallen at the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामः|अवनाम
अवनामः<BR>—1 Bending or bowing, falling at the feet; गलितनयनवारेर्याति पादावनामम् Śi. 11. 35.<BR>—2 Causing to bend down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामक
अवनामक <i>a.</i> What depresses or causes to bend or bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामिन्
अवनामिन् <i>a.</i> Bending or bowing down; कृच्छ्रेण क्षितिमवनामिनस्तुरङ्गाः<BR> (आनिन्युः) Ki. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनर्द्
अवनर्द् To slur or trill (chanting of the Hindu rituals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनह्
अवनह् €4 U. To bind on, tie on, put over, cover with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनद्ध|अवनद्धं
अवनद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Formed, made.<BR>—2 Fixed, seated; स्त्यानावनद्धघनशोणितशोणपाणिः Ve. 1. 21. जालावनद्धाङ्गुलिपाणिपादम् Bu. C. 1. 66.<BR>—3 Covered, encircled; ताम्वूलीलतावनद्धपूगखण्डमण्डितैः K. 19;<BR> Śi. 3. 7; bound on, tied; चर्मावनद्धं दुर्गन्धिपूर्णं मूत्रपुरीषयोः<BR> Ms. 6. 76; हेममालावनद्धः (रथः) Mb. पुष्पभारावनद्धः<BR> (पादपः) Rām.; नष्टार्कचन्द्रकिरणातिरजोवनद्धा Bṛ. S. 19. 20.<BR> fastened, woven, put together; स्रगवनद्धमनोरमपल्लवा Śi. 6. 53, 7. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनद्धम्
अवनद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} A drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाहः|अवनाह
अवनाहः<BR>—1 Binding, girding, putting on.<BR>—2 Binding rope; यूपं कृत्वा तु मलयमवनाहं च तक्षकम् Mb. 7. 202. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाट|अवनाटः
अवनाट <i>a.</i> [नतं नासिकायाः; अव-नाटच् see अवटीट] Flat nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाटम्
अवनाट + .{@-टम्@} The condition of having a flat nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिः|अवनि
अवनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> [अव्-अनि Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>—1 The earth; often used at the end of comp. meaning ‘ground’, ‘place’;<BR> काननावनौ Dk. 7, 13; लीलावनौ place of recreation 25.<BR>—2 A finger (Nir.)<BR>—3 A river; सं यं स्तुभोऽवनयो न यन्ति Rv. 1. 190.<BR>—4 Course, bed of a river, अवनिंगत <i>a.</i> fallen prostrate on the gound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवनीशः, अवनीश्वरः, अवनिनाथः, अवनिपतिः, अवनिपालः, अवनिचर,^1 अवनिजः, अवनितल, अवनिध्रः, अवनिभृत्, अवनिमण्डलम्, अवनिसारा<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनी
अवनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> [अव्-अनि Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>—1 The earth; often used at the end of comp. meaning ‘ground’, ‘place’;<BR> काननावनौ Dk. 7, 13; लीलावनौ place of recreation 25.<BR>—2 A finger (Nir.)<BR>—3 A river; सं यं स्तुभोऽवनयो न यन्ति Rv. 1. 190.<BR>—4 Course, bed of a river, अवनिंगत <i>a.</i> fallen prostrate on the gound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवनीशः, अवनीश्वरः, अवनिनाथः, अवनिपतिः, अवनिपालः, अवनिचर,^1 अवनिजः, अवनितल, अवनिध्रः, अवनिभृत्, अवनिमण्डलम्, अवनिसारा<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीशः|अवनीश
अवनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -नाथः, -पतिः, -पालः lord of the earth, king;<BR> पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 11. 93. सहैवावनिपालसंघैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीश्वरः|अवनीश्वर
अवनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -नाथः, -पतिः, -पालः lord of the earth, king;<BR> पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 11. 93. सहैवावनिपालसंघैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिनाथः|अवनिनाथ
अवनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -नाथः, -पतिः, -पालः lord of the earth, king;<BR> पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 11. 93. सहैवावनिपालसंघैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपतिः|अवनिपति
अवनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -नाथः, -पतिः, -पालः lord of the earth, king;<BR> पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 11. 93. सहैवावनिपालसंघैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपालः|अवनिपाल
अवनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -नाथः, -पतिः, -पालः lord of the earth, king;<BR> पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 11. 93. सहैवावनिपालसंघैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिचर
अवनिः + -चर^1 <i>a.</i> roving over the earth, vagabond.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिजः|अवनिज
अवनिः + -जः The planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनितल
अवनिः + -तल the surface of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिध्रः
अवनिः + -ध्रः a mountain स्फुटमेव समस्तमापदा तदिदानीमवनीध्रमूर्धसु Śi. 16. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिभृत्
अवनिः + -भृत् A mountain, a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिमण्डलम्
अवनिः + -मण्डलम् the globe. {@रुहः, -ट्@} a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिसारा
अवनिः + -सारा The plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिज्
अवनिज् €3 U. To wash, purify, cleanse, to wipe off. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to wash off.<BR>—2 To fill with, pervade; सुसुगन्धतयावनेजितानाम् Ghaṭ. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिक्त
अवनिक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Washed, cleansed.<BR>—2 Searched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेज्य
अवनेज्य <i>a.</i> To be Used for washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेजनम्
अवनेजनम्, अवनेजनी, अवनेज<BR>—1 Washing, ablution; पादावनेजसरितः शमलानि हन्तुम् Bhāg. 11. 6. 19.<BR> न कुर्याद् गुरुपुत्रस्य पादयोश्चावनेजनम् Ms. 2. 209.<BR>—2 Washing off. ablution.<BR>—3 Water for washing. ऋतं हस्तावनेजनम् Av. 11. 3. 13 foot-bath;<BR> आपः पादावनेजनीः Ait. Br. आपस्तेऽङ्घ्र्यवेनजन्यस्त्रींल्लोकान् शुचयोऽपुनन्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 41. 15.<BR>—4 Sprinkling water on the <i>darbha</i> grass at a Srāddha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेजनी
अवनेजनम्, अवनेजनी, अवनेज<BR>—1 Washing, ablution; पादावनेजसरितः शमलानि हन्तुम् Bhāg. 11. 6. 19.<BR> न कुर्याद् गुरुपुत्रस्य पादयोश्चावनेजनम् Ms. 2. 209.<BR>—2 Washing off. ablution.<BR>—3 Water for washing. ऋतं हस्तावनेजनम् Av. 11. 3. 13 foot-bath;<BR> आपः पादावनेजनीः Ait. Br. आपस्तेऽङ्घ्र्यवेनजन्यस्त्रींल्लोकान् शुचयोऽपुनन्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 41. 15.<BR>—4 Sprinkling water on the <i>darbha</i> grass at a Srāddha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेज
अवनेजनम्, अवनेजनी, अवनेज<BR>—1 Washing, ablution; पादावनेजसरितः शमलानि हन्तुम् Bhāg. 11. 6. 19.<BR> न कुर्याद् गुरुपुत्रस्य पादयोश्चावनेजनम् Ms. 2. 209.<BR>—2 Washing off. ablution.<BR>—3 Water for washing. ऋतं हस्तावनेजनम् Av. 11. 3. 13 foot-bath;<BR> आपः पादावनेजनीः Ait. Br. आपस्तेऽङ्घ्र्यवेनजन्यस्त्रींल्लोकान् शुचयोऽपुनन्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 41. 15.<BR>—4 Sprinkling water on the <i>darbha</i> grass at a Srāddha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

