अवनीत
अवनीत <i>a.</i> Led or pushed down into; ऋबीसे अत्रिमश्विनावनीतम् Rv. 1. 116. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेय
अवनेय <i>a.</i> To be led away; अरण्ये मुनिभिर्जुष्टे अवनेया भविष्यसि<BR> Rām. 7. 46. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिः|अवन्ति|अवंति|अवंतिः
अवन्तिः, -न्ती <i>f.</i><BR> [अव-बाहु˚ झिच् Uṇ. 3. 50.]<BR>—1 N. of a city, the modern उज्जयिनी, one of the seven sacred cities<BR> of the Hindus, to die at which is said to secure eternal happiness; cf.<BR> अयोध्या मथुरा माया काशी काञ्चिरवन्तिका । पुरी द्वारावती चैव सप्तैता<BR> मोक्षदायिकाः ॥ The women of Avanti are said to be very skilful in all<BR> erotic arts; cf. आवन्त्य एव निपुणाः सुदृशो रतकर्मणि B. R. 10. 82.<BR>—2 N. of a river. ━<i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants; its<BR> capital being उज्जयिनी on the river सिप्रा; and there is also the<BR> temple of महाकाल in the suburbs. [According to Hemacandra अवन्ति<BR> is synonymous with Mālava or the modern Mālavā; but the latter country<BR> covered in ancient times, as now, a wider area than Avanti, as Bāṇa<BR> applies the name to a neighbouring kingdom in the east, whose capital was<BR> Vidiśā on the Vetravatī or Betvā. In the time of the Mahābhārata<BR> Avanti appears to have extended on the south to the banks of the Narmadā<BR> and on the west probably to the banks of the Myhe or Mahī]; अवन्तिनाथोऽयमुदग्राबाहुः<BR> R. 6. 32; असौ महाकालनिकेतनस्य वसन्नदूरे किल चन्द्रमौलेः 6. 34, 35;<BR> प्राप्यावन्तीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30; अवन्तीषूज्जयिनी<BR> नाम नगरी K. 52.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवन्तिपुरम्, अवन्तिब्रह्मः, अवन्तिभूपालः, अवन्तिसोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ती|अवंती
अवन्तिः, -न्ती <i>f.</i><BR> [अव-बाहु˚ झिच् Uṇ. 3. 50.]<BR>—1 N. of a city, the modern उज्जयिनी, one of the seven sacred cities<BR> of the Hindus, to die at which is said to secure eternal happiness; cf.<BR> अयोध्या मथुरा माया काशी काञ्चिरवन्तिका । पुरी द्वारावती चैव सप्तैता<BR> मोक्षदायिकाः ॥ The women of Avanti are said to be very skilful in all<BR> erotic arts; cf. आवन्त्य एव निपुणाः सुदृशो रतकर्मणि B. R. 10. 82.<BR>—2 N. of a river. ━<i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants; its<BR> capital being उज्जयिनी on the river सिप्रा; and there is also the<BR> temple of महाकाल in the suburbs. [According to Hemacandra अवन्ति<BR> is synonymous with Mālava or the modern Mālavā; but the latter country<BR> covered in ancient times, as now, a wider area than Avanti, as Bāṇa<BR> applies the name to a neighbouring kingdom in the east, whose capital was<BR> Vidiśā on the Vetravatī or Betvā. In the time of the Mahābhārata<BR> Avanti appears to have extended on the south to the banks of the Narmadā<BR> and on the west probably to the banks of the Myhe or Mahī]; अवन्तिनाथोऽयमुदग्राबाहुः<BR> R. 6. 32; असौ महाकालनिकेतनस्य वसन्नदूरे किल चन्द्रमौलेः 6. 34, 35;<BR> प्राप्यावन्तीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30; अवन्तीषूज्जयिनी<BR> नाम नगरी K. 52.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवन्तिपुरम्, अवन्तिब्रह्मः, अवन्तिभूपालः, अवन्तिसोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिपुरम्
अवन्तिः + -पुरम् the city of Avanti उज्जयिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिब्रह्मः|अवन्तिब्रह्म
अवन्तिः + -ब्रह्मः [अवन्तिषु ब्रह्मा अच् समासान्तः. ब्रह्मणोजानपदाख्यायाम्<BR> P. V. 4. 104] a Brāhmaṇa residing in Avanti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिभूपालः|अवन्तिभूपाल
अवन्तिः + -भूपालः Bhoja, the king of Avanti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिसोमः|अवन्तिसोम|अवन्तिसोमं
अवन्तिः + -सोमः [अवन्तिषु सोम इव] sour gruel (prepared from the fermentation<BR> of rice-water काञ्जिकम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिका
अवन्तिका<BR>—1 The modern city of उज्जयिनी.<BR>—2 The language of the Avantis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ध्य|अवंध्य
अवन्ध्य <i>a.</i> Not barren, fruitful, productive; अवन्ध्यवाञ्छितफलप्रदान<BR> K. 260; अवन्ध्यपातेन बाणेन V. 2. 2;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">Page0249-2</a>]<BR> अवन्ध्यं दिवसं कुर्याद्दानाध्ययनकर्मसु H. 2. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवन्ध्यकाल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ध्यकाल
अवन्ध्य + -काल <i>a.</i> Regularly and fruitfully working; निश्चित्य यः<BR> प्रकमते नान्तर्वसति कर्मणः । अवन्ध्यकालो वश्यात्मा स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥<BR> Mb. 5. 33. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपट्
अवपट् €10 P. To split. ━<i>Pass.</i> To split oneself, to be split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाटिका
अवपाटिका Laceration of the prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपत्
अवपत् €1 P. To fall down, fly down, jump down, descend, alight, pounce<BR> or swoop upon; श्येनावपातमवपत्य Prab.; फलैर्वृक्षावपतितैः<BR> Rām. ━<i>Caus.</i> To throw down, fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपतनम्
अवपतनम् Alighting, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपतित
अवपतित <i>a.</i> Fallen down from; फलैर्वृक्षावपतितैः सीते दुःखमतो<BR> वनम् Rām. 2. 28. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातः|अवपात
अवपातः<BR>—1 Falling down; जलं कूलावपातेन प्रसन्नं कलुषायत Mk. 9. 24;<BR> अधश्चरणावपातम् Bh. 2. 31 falling down at the feet; (fig.) cringing.<BR>—2 Descent, descending; शस्त्रावपातः Y. 2. 277; कपोत˚ H. 1;<BR> श्येन˚ चकिता Māl. 8. 8 sudden swoop or pouncing.<BR>—3 A hole, pit.<BR>—4 Particularly, a hole or pit for catching elephants; अवपातस्तु हस्त्यर्थे<BR> गर्ते छन्ने तृणादिना Yādava; रोधांसि निघ्नन्नवपातमग्नः करीव<BR> वन्यः परुषं ररास R. 16. 78. The Mātaṅga L. 10. 1 enumerates<BR> the methods of catching elephants as follows वारीकर्म वशाविलोभनविधिभ्य<BR> चानुगत्या तथैवापातेन ततोऽवपातत इतीहेभग्रहः पञ्चधा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातनम्
अवपातनम्<BR>—1 Falling, knocking down, throwing down; द्रुमाणाम् Ms. 11. 64; कुड्यावपातनम् Y. 2. 223.<BR>—2 (In drama) a scene during which a person enters the stage in terror<BR> but leaves it at the end in good humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपद्
अवपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go down, glide down; to descend, fall down as केश, गर्भ &c.<BR>—2 To be deprived of (with abl.).<BR>—3 To fall, meet with an accident.<BR>—4 To overthrow, ruin. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to glide or go down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपन्न
अवपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mixed with.<BR>—2 Cooked together with.<BR>—3 Fallen on or into; केशकीरावपन्नम् Ms. 11. 159.<BR>—4 Alighted, descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपादः|अवपाद
अवपादः Falling down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाक|अवपाकः
अवपाक^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Badly or ill-cooked.<BR>—2 Without a net.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाकः|अवपाक
अवपाकः + .{@-कः@} Bad cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात्र
अवपात्र <i>a.</i> [अवरं भोजनायोग्यं पात्रं यस्य] A Mleccha<BR> whose eating in a vessel makes it useless for others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात्रित
अवपात्रित <i>a.</i> [अवपात्र कृत्यर्थे णिच्-क्त] One who has lost<BR> his caste, a person not allowed by his kindred to eat in a common vessel;<BR> see अपपात्रित (= भिन्नोदकीकृत Dāy. B.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपानम्
अवपानम् Drinking; सोमो भूत्ववपानेष्वाभगो Rv. 1. 136. 4. माप<BR> स्थातं महिषेवावपानात् Rv. 10. 106. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपालित
अवपालित <i>a.</i> Unprotected, neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाशित
अवपाशित <i>a.</i> [अवपाशः समन्तात् पाशो जातोऽस्य तार˚ इतच्]<BR> Snared, having a snare laid over (on all sides); यान्त्येव न निवर्तन्ते<BR> मृत्युपाशावपाशिताः Rām. 7. 6. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपिण्डित
अवपिण्डित <i>a.</i> (said of dew-drops) fallen down in the shape of globules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड्
अवपीड् €10 P. To compress; ममज्जेव मही तस्य भूरिभारावपीडिता<BR> Mb.; पादौ शिरोभिरवपीडितौ Rām.; to press or squeeze together; एकीकृतस्त्वचि<BR> निषिक्त इवावपीड्यः Māl. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड|अवपीडः
अवपीड <i>a.</i> Pressed on all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीडः|अवपीड
अवपीड + .{@-डः@}<BR>—1 Pressing down, pressure.<BR>—2 A kind of medicinal drug used to cause sneezing, sternutatory.<BR>—3 A kind of medical treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीडनम्
अवपीडनम्<BR>—1 The act of pressing down.<BR>—2 A sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीडना
अवपीडनम् + .{@-ना@} Damage, violation; अङ्गावपीडनायां समुत्थानव्ययं दाप्यः Ms. 8. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपूर्ण
अवपूर्ण <i>a.</i> Full of, filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपोथिका
अवपोथिका Anything used for knocking down as stones &c. thrown from<BR> the walls of a city on the besiegers. Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवप्रज्जनः|अवप्रज्जन
अवप्रज्जनः The end of the warp of a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवप्लु
अवप्लु €1 Ā. To jump down; स्वनिगममपहाय मत्प्रतिज्ञामृतमधिकर्तुमवप्लुतो<BR> रथस्थः Bhāg. 1. 9. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवप्लुत
अवप्लुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Jumped down from.<BR>—2 Gone away from; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवफः|अवफ
अवफः Flatulence, wind from the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबधा
अवबधा Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबन्ध्
अवबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind, fasten (fig. also); नीत्वा कामं गौरवेणावबद्धः Śi. 18. 19.<BR>—2 To arrest, rivet; शिल्पकुशलतयाऽवबध्नाति दृष्टिम् Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबन्ध|अवबंधः
अवबन्ध<BR>—1 Falling or palsy of the eyelids, Blepharoptosis; व्याधिर्नेत्रावबन्धकः Suśr.<BR>—2 A kind of disease.<BR>—3 Binding on all sides निद्रामुद्रावबन्धान्मधुकरमनिशं पद्मकोशादपास्य Nāg. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबाधा
अवबाधा<BR>—1 Pain, agony.<BR>—2 Resistance, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबाहुकः|अवबाहुक
अवबाहुकः [अवबद्धो बाहुर्येन प्रा˚ स˚] Spasm in the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबुध्
अवबुध् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To awake; to recognise; तं चावबुध्याब्रवम् Dk. 127.<BR>—2 To become sensible or aware of, feel, perceive, know, understand; त्वक्स्पर्शं<BR> नावबुध्यते Mb.; एकान्तमौग्ध्यानवबुद्धविभ्रमैः Śi. 12. 30; Bk. 15. 101;<BR> Ms. 8. 53; अधीत्यावबुद्ध्य च; येनावबुध्यते तत्त्वं प्रकृतेः<BR> पुरुषस्य च Bhāg. knows. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To awaken, rouse; रामो रामावबोधितः R. 12. 23.<BR>—2 To make one aware of, inform; ब्रह्मचोदनानुपुरुषमवबोधयत्येव<BR> केवलम् Ś. B.; प्रागेव विदुरो वेद तेनास्मानवबोधयत् Mb.<BR>—3 To remind, put in mind of; आर्ये सम्यगवबोधितोऽस्मि Ś. 1, v. l.<BR>—4 To teach, instruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबुद्ध
अवबुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Known, learnt; तत्र मे कौशलं सर्वमवबुद्धं विशाम्पते Mb. 4. 3. 10.<BR>—2 [कर्तरि-क्त] One who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधः|अवबोध
अवबोधः<BR>—1 Waking, becoming awake (opp. स्वप्न); यौ तु स्वप्नावबोधौ तौ भूतानां<BR> प्रलयोदयौ Ku. 2. 8; युक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य Bg. 6. 17.<BR>—2 Knowledge, perception; स्वभर्तृनामग्रहणाद्बभूव सान्द्रे रजस्यात्मपरावबोधः<BR> R. 7. 41; भावावबोधकलुषा दयितेव रात्रौ 5. 64; प्रतिकूलेषु तैक्ष्णस्यावबोधः<BR> क्रोध इष्यते S. D.; M. 3. 10; स्वात्मावबोधं महः Prab. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Discrimination judgment; अवबोधवारि रजसः शमनम् Ki. 6. 41.<BR>—4 Teaching, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधक|अवबोधकः
अवबोधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Indicating, showing; निजपराक्रमावबोधकानि चरितानि Dk. 175.<BR>—2 Enlightener; अगजगदोकसामखिलशक्त्यवबोधक ते Bhāg. 10. 87. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधकः|अवबोधक
अवबोधक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The awakener, the sun.<BR>—2 A panegyrist, bard.<BR>—3 A teacher.<BR>—4 Thought, intention; मदवबोधकं प्रकटयता Dk. 153; ˚त्वं<BR> instruction, guidance, explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधनम्
अवबोधनम् Knowledge, perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधित
अवबोधित <i>a.</i> Awakened; रामो रामावबोधितः R. 12. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवब्रवः|अवब्रव
अवब्रवः [कुत्सितः ब्रवः] Ill-report, defamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभञ्ज्|अवभंज्
अवभञ्ज् €7 P. To break off, smash; वनस्पतिं व्रज इवावभज्य<BR> Ku. 3. 74; अवभग्नश्च मे मानः Rām., broken down, humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभङ्ग|अवभंगः|अवभङ्गः
अवभङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Humbling, overcoming, defeating; मानावभङ्गनिपुणं त्वममोघमस्त्रम् V. 4. 25.<BR>—2 Broken off, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभङ्गः|अवभङ्ग|अवभंगः
अवभङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः@}<BR>—1 Breaking off (as a shaft).<BR>—2 Hollowing or sinking (of the nose); Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभंजनम्
अवभंजनम्^1 Breaking off, tearing, humbling.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Missing anusvAra. under root avaBaYj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभाषणम्
अवभाषणम् Speaking, telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभास्
अवभास् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine; नात्यर्थमस्त्रैरवभासमानः Ki. 3. 46; स तेजसा सूर्य<BR> इवावभासते Mb.<BR>—2 To shine forth, become manifest; आहोस्विन्मुखमवभासते युवत्याः Śi. 8. 29.<BR>—3 To appear, seem (apparently or falsely); एतत्त्रयं तप्तायःपिण्डवदेकत्वेनावभासते<BR> Vedānta. ━<i>Caus.</i> To irradiate. illuminate; अधिकावभासितदिशां<BR> निकरः Śi. 9. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासः|अवभास
अवभासः<BR>—1 Splendour, lustre, light; यैः शोभितोऽसि मुखचन्द्रकृतावभासः Mu. 5. 16.<BR>—2 Knowledge, perception.<BR>—3 Appearance, manifestation, inspiration; येनास्य तत्त्वेषु कृतेऽवभासे Ki. 3. 26.<BR>—4 Space, reach, compass.<BR>—5 False knowledge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवभासकरः, अवभासप्रभाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

