अवभासः + -करः N. of a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासप्रभाः
अवभासः + -प्रभाः (pl.) N. of a whole class of deities. (Buddhist.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासक
अवभासक <i>a.</i> Luminous, irradiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासकम्
अवभासक + .{@-कम्@} The supreme spirit; ˚त्वम् luminousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासित
अवभासित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Illumined, lighted, irradiated.<BR>—2 Evident, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासिन्
अवभासिन् <i>a.</i> Shining, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासिनी
अवभासिन् + .{@-नी@} The outer skin or cuticle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभिद्
अवभिद् €7 P. To break off, shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0250-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभेदः
अवभेदः Breaking off, shattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभेदिन्
अवभेदिन् <i>a.</i> Breaking off, shattering, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुज्
अवभुज् €6 P. To bend down, curve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुग्न
अवभुग्न <i>p. p.</i> Contracted, bent, crooked; अवभुग्नभोगिफणमण्डलां<BR> भुवम् Śi. 15. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथः|अवभृथ
अवभृथः [अव-भृ-क्थन् Uṇ. 2. 3]<BR>—1 The end or completion of a principal sacrifice; तन्मरणमेवास्यावभृथः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 17. 5.<BR>—2 Bathing at the end of a principal sacrifice for purification; नावभृथं<BR> सरस्वत्याम् Kāty.; भुवं कोष्णेन कुण्डोध्नी मेध्येनावभृथादपि R. 1. 84;<BR> प्रीत्याश्वमेधावभृथार्द्रमूर्तेः 6. 61, 9. 22, 11. 31, 13. 61;<BR> Y. 3. 244; Ms. 11. 82.<BR>—3 Purification by bathing of the sacrificer and the sacrificial vessels<BR> at the end of a sacrifice; अच्छावभृथमोजसा Rv. 8. 93. 23.<BR>—4 The water of purification.<BR>—5 A supplementary sacrifice to atone for defects in a principal and preceding<BR> one; a sacrifice in general; स्नातवत्यवभृथे ततस्त्वयि Śi. 14. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवभृथस्नपनम्, अवभृथस्नानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथस्नपनम्
अवभृथः + -स्नपनम्, -स्नानम् ablution after a sacrificial ceremony; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथस्नानम्
अवभृथः + -स्नपनम्, -स्नानम् ablution after a sacrificial ceremony; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रः|अवभ्र
अवभ्रः Abduction, carrying off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रट|अवभ्रटः
अवभ्रट <i>a.</i> [नतं नासिकायाः; अव-भ्रटच् P. V. 2. 31] Flat-nosed;<BR> see अवटीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रटम्
अवभ्रट + .{@-टम्@} The state of having a flat nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवम|अवमं|अवमः
अवम <i>a.</i> [अव्-अमच् Uṇ. 5. 54.]<BR>—1 Sinful, wicked.<BR>—2 Contemptible, mean, undermost, lowest.<BR>—3 Base, low, inferior (opp. परम); अनलकानलकानवमां पुरीम्<BR> R. 9. 14; see अनवम; या त उक्तिरवमा या परमा Rv. 6. 25. 1.<BR>—4 Next, intimate.<BR>—5 Last, youngest; उतावमस्य पुरुहूत बोधि Rv. 6. 21. 5. प्रद्युम्न<BR> इति विख्यातः सर्वतोऽनवमः पितुः Bhāg. 10. 55. 2.<BR>—6 decreasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमः|अवम|अवमं
अवम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 A protector.<BR>—2 A class of Manes; त्रिविधाः पितरः अवमा ऊर्वाः काव्याश्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमम्
अवम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Sin.<BR>—2 A lunar day exactly coinciding with a solar one; the difference between<BR> a Chāndra (29 days, 31 Ghaṭikās and 50 palas) and a solar month (30<BR> days); तिथ्यन्तद्वयमेको दिनवारः स्पृशति यत्र तद्भवत्यवमदिनम् Jyotiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्
अवमन् €4 Ā. (or Pot. P.)<BR>—1 To despise, contemn, disregard, disrespect; चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य<BR> मानिनी Ku. 5. 53; Ms. 2. 11, 4. 135, प्रभावविदितानुरागमवमन्यते<BR> वापि माम् V. 2. 11.<BR>—2 To undervalue, depreciate, slight, make light of; तदीशितारं चेदीनां<BR> भवांस्तमवमंस्त मा Śi. 2. 95; जगन्मङ्गलमात्मानं कथं त्वमवमन्यसे<BR> U. 7. 8; Bk. 8. 81, 12. 25, 15. 14, 66. ━<i>Caus.</i> To despise &c.;<BR> या चैनं नावमानयेत् Ms. 2. 50, 4. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमत|अवमतं
अवमत <i>p. p.</i> Despised, contemned &c. भिन्दन्त्यवमता मन्त्रम् Ms. 7. 150.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवमताङ्कुशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमताङ्कुशः|अवमताङ्कुश|अवमतांकुश
अवमत + -अङ्कुशः a restive elephant (that disdains the hook), one in rut;<BR> अन्वेतुकामोऽवमताङ्कुशग्रहः Śi. 12. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमतिः|अवमति
अवमतिः A master, an owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमतिः|अवमति
अवमतिः + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Disregard, disrespect.<BR>—2 Aversion, dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तव्य|अवमंतव्य
अवमन्तव्य, -अवमान्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be treated with disrespect, or slighted; बालोऽपि नावमन्तव्यो<BR> मनुष्य इति भूमिपः Ms. 7. 8, 9. 82.<BR>—2 Contemptible, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान्य|अवमान्यः
अवमन्तव्य, -अवमान्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be treated with disrespect, or slighted; बालोऽपि नावमन्तव्यो<BR> मनुष्य इति भूमिपः Ms. 7. 8, 9. 82.<BR>—2 Contemptible, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तृ|अवमंतृ
अवमन्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disrespectful, contemptuous, despising.<BR>—2 Arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानः|अवमान
अवमानः Disrespect, contempt, disregard; अमृतस्येव चाकाङ्क्षेदवमानस्य<BR> सर्वदा Ms. 2. 162; Bg. 14. 25. (v. l.) अपमान {@˚ता, -त्वम्@}<BR> dishonourableness, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमाननम्
अवमाननम्, -ना<BR> Despising, disrespect, contempt; अवमाननार्थमिह किं निमन्त्रितैः Śi. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानना
अवमाननम्, -ना<BR> Despising, disrespect, contempt; अवमाननार्थमिह किं निमन्त्रितैः Śi. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिन्
अवमानिन् <i>a.</i> Contemning, despising, slighting, undervaluing; धिङ्मामुपस्थितश्रेयोऽवमानिनम्<BR> Ś. 6; अयि आत्मगुणावमानिनि Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्थ|अवमंथ|अवमन्थः
अवमन्थ^1 <i>a.</i> [अवमथ्नाति अव-मन्थ्-अच्] Producing swellings.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: No virmama since adj. formed with '-ac'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्थः|अवमन्थ|अवमंथ
अवमन्थ + .{@-थः@} A kind of disease, swellings caused by boils or contusions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षः|अवमर्ष
अवमर्षः<BR>—1 Consideration, investigation.<BR>—2 One of the five principal parts or <i>Sandhis</i> of a play; यत्र मुख्यफलोपाय<BR> उद्भिन्नो गर्भतोऽधिकः । शापाद्यैः सान्तरायश्च सोऽवमर्ष इति स्मृतः<BR> S. D. 336; also written विमर्ष.<BR>—3 Attacking; वीर्यावदानेषु कृतावमर्षः Ki. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षणम्
अवमर्षणम्<BR>—1 Intolerance, impatience.<BR>—2 Effacing. obliterating, banishing from recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमुच्
अवमुच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To let loose, loosen (as a horse).<BR>—2 To take off (a garment &c. मेखलाम्, किरिटम्, वासांसि, भूषणानि &c.)<BR>—3 To unharness, to liberate oneʼs self from, to strip off; मृत्योः पड्वीशमवमुञ्चमानः Av. 8. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमोचनम्
अवमोचनम् Setting at liberty, loosening, letting go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्च्छ्
अवमूर्च्छ् To be appeased or allayed (as a quarrel) Mb. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्धन्
अवमूर्धन् <i>a.</i> [अवनतो मूर्द्धाऽस्य] With oneʼs head hanging down.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवमूर्धशय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्धशय|अवमूर्द्धशयः|अवमूर्धशयः
अवमूर्धन् + -शय <i>a.</i> [अवमूर्द्धा सन् शेते; शी अच्] lying with the head hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्धशयः|अवमूर्धशय|अवमूर्द्धशयः
अवमूर्धन् + -शय + .({@-यः@}) one who sleeps with his head hanging down, such as man<BR> (opp. देव); उत्तानशया देवा अवमूर्धशया मनुष्याः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृज्
अवमृज् €2 P.<BR>—1 To rub off, to strip off, remove; लेपमवमार्ष्टि.<BR>—2 To efface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमार्जनम्
अवमार्जनम्<BR>—1 Washing &c.<BR>—2 An instrument for rubbing down, a curry-comb इमा ते वाजिन्नवमार्जनानि Rv. 1. 163. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृद्
अवमृद् €9 P.<BR>—1 To grind or pound down, to reduce by friction; crush, tread down, trample<BR> upon; अवमृद्नन्स राष्ट्राणि पार्थिवानां हयोत्तमः Mb.<BR>—2 To rub. ━<i>Caus.</i> To pound down &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दः|अवमर्द|अवमर्द्द
अवमर्दः<BR>—1 Trampling upon.<BR>—2 Pain, toils; रणावमर्दमासाद्य Rām.<BR>—3 An expedient of a Government,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">Page0252-1</a>]<BR> inflicting punishment on an enemy by laying his country waste, devastation,<BR> oppression; अवमर्दः प्रतीघातस्तथा चैव बलीयसाम् Mb. 12. 59. 52<BR>—4 Slaying, killing; अवमर्दादिव दृप्तसिंहशावः (विनिवर्तितः) U. 5. 8.<BR>—5 Friction, turmoil; न त्वां समासाद्य रणावमर्दे मनःश्रमं गच्छति<BR> निश्चितार्थम् Rām. 5. 48. 6.<BR>—6 A kind of eclipse; Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0251-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दन
अवमर्दन <i>a.</i> Trampling down, grinding, crushing; शत्रुबल˚ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दनम्
अवमर्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Rubbing, shampooing; हस्तपाद˚ Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Oppression, crushing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दिन्
अवमर्दिन् <i>a.</i> Slayer, killer; श्रुताश्च दृष्टा हि मया पराक्रमा<BR> महात्मनस्तस्य रणावमर्दिनः Rām. 5. 37. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृश्
अवमृश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To touch; अवमृशन्ती कलहंसकान् K. 232.<BR>—2 To consider, ponder, reflect. तद्धावमृश्य न विवेद Ch. Up. 6. 13. 1.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to touch.<BR>—2 To destroy; interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्शः|अवमर्श
अवमर्शः Touch, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्शित
अवमर्शित <i>a.</i> Destroyed, disturbed; इति दक्षः कविर्यज्ञं<BR> भद्र रुद्रावमर्शितम् Bhāg. 4. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूत्रयत्
अवमूत्रयत् <i>a.</i> Soiling the body with urine; अवमूत्रयतो मेढ्रम्<BR> (छेदयेत्) Ms. 8. 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमेह
अवमेह Dirt; कामं प्रयाहि जहि विश्ववसोऽवमेहम् Bhāg. 9. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयज्
अवयज् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To expiate (sin), drive away, expel, disperse (enemies &c.) by performing sacrifices.<BR>—2 Not to worship; to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयजनम्
अवयजनम् Purification, means of expiating; देवकृतस्यैनसोऽवयजनमसि<BR> &c. Mahānār. Up. 18. 1; Tāṇḍya Br. (अपगमनसाधनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयाज्
अवयाज् <i>f.</i> [अव-यज्-ण्वि] A particular portion of a sacrifice.<BR> शुष्मिन्नवयाः Rv. 1. 173. 12; Av. 2. 35. 1. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयाजः
अवयाज् + .({@-याजः, -याजौ@}) A kind of priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजौ
अवयाज् + .({@-याजः, -याजौ@}) A kind of priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवः|अवयव
अवयवः [अवयूयते कार्यद्रव्येण संबध्यते, अव-यु-कर्मणि-अप्]<BR>—1 limb (of the body); मुखावयवलूनां ताम् R. 12. 43; Amaru. 45, 51;<BR> a member (in general); कस्मिंश्चिदपि जीवति नन्दान्वयावयवे Mu. 1.<BR>—2 A part, portion (as of a whole); पदे न वर्णा विद्यन्ते वर्णेष्ववयवा<BR> न च Bhartṛ; द्रव्याणां केनचिदवयवेन Dk. 61; क्तेनाहोरात्रावयवाः<BR> P. II. 1. 45, II. 1. 46.<BR>—3 A member or a component part of a logical argument or syllogism, (these<BR> are five:− प्रतिज्ञा, हेतु, उदाहरण, उपनय and निगमन).<BR>—4 The body.<BR>—5 A component, constituent, ingredient (in general), as of a compound &c.<BR>—6 A means (साधन, उपकरण).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवयवार्थः, अवयवप्रसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवार्थः|अवयवार्थ
अवयवः + -अर्थः The meaning of the component parts of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवप्रसिद्धिः
अवयवः + -प्रसिद्धिः Denotation of the parts, etymological signification,<BR> न चावयवप्रसिद्ध्या समुदायप्रसिद्धिर्बाध्यते इत्युक्तम् । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवशः
अवयवशः <i>ind.</i> Part by part, severally, piece-meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयविन्
अवयविन् <i>a.</i> [अवयवः कारणत्वेनास्त्यस्य इनि] Having limbs,<BR> having portions or subdivisions (as a whole);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">Page0252-2</a>]<BR> अवयविना सह पूर्वादयः समस्यन्ते P. II. 2. 1. Sk. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवी
अवयविन् + ({@-वी@})<BR>—1 A whole, any substance formed of several constituents; ननु अवयविनि<BR> किं मानम् Sid. Mukt.<BR>—2 A syllogism, or any logical argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवया
अवया €2 U.<BR>—1 To go down, to give way; अवयातां मरुतां हेळो अद्भुतः Rv. 1. 94. 12.<BR>—2 To desist from, turn off or away.<BR>—3 To know, understand; अथवा न धर्ममसुबोधसमयमवयात बालिशाः<BR> Śi. 15. 19; न जनोऽयमित्यवयये स तापसैः Ki. 12. 15.<BR>—4 To avert, prevent, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवया
अवया, -यात <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Giving way, desisting, ceasing; ˚हेळः Ved.<BR> one whose anger is appeased; भवा मरुद्भिरवयातहेळाः Rv. 1. 171. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयात
अवया, -यात <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Giving way, desisting, ceasing; ˚हेळः Ved.<BR> one whose anger is appeased; भवा मरुद्भिरवयातहेळाः Rv. 1. 171. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयातृ
अवयातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who separates.<BR>—2 Turning away, averting.<BR>—3 Appeasing, pacifying; अवयाता सदमिद् दुर्मतीनाम् Rv. 1. 129. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयानम्
अवयानम्<BR>—1 Going away, retreat (Ved.).<BR>—2 Appeasing, pacification; इयं धीर्भूया अवमानमेषा Rv. 1. 185. 8.<BR>—3 Expiation (of sins &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयुत्यनुवादः
अवयुत्यनुवादः A mention in parts; एकं वृणीते इत्यवयुत्यनुवादोऽयं<BR> त्रयाणामेव ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयुन
अवयुन <i>a.</i> [वयुनं प्रज्ञा निरु˚ न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Having no intellect (Ved.).<BR>—2 Undistinguishable, indistinct, dark; स इत् तमोऽवयुनं ततन्वत्<BR> सूर्येण वयुनवच्चकार Rv. 6. 21. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर|अवरं|अवरः
अवर <i>a.</i> [वृ-बा˚ अप्, न˚ त˚]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Younger (in years); मासेनावरः = मासावरः Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Later; Posterior hinder (in time or space); दक्षौ विवस्वानवरः<BR> Rām.; पूर्वजेनावरः पुत्रौ ज्येष्ठो राज्येऽभिषिच्यते Rām.; यदवरं<BR> कौशाम्ब्याः, यदवरमाग्रहायण्याः P. III. 3. 136-7. Sk.; रामाद्वर्षेणाधोक्षजोऽवरः Bop.<BR>—2 Following, succeeding; जरावराः (शब्दाः) Ak., अवरः श्रद्धयोपेतः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 18. 4. चतुरोऽवरान् Ms. 3. 33.<BR>—3 Below, under, lower, inferior, less; वर्णावरो भ्राता M. 1.<BR>—4 Mean, unimportant, worst, lowest (opp. उत्तम); अव्यङ्ग्यमवरं<BR> स्मृतम् K. P. 1; दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय Bg. 2. 49;<BR> श्रद्दधानं शुभां विद्यामाददीतावरादपि Ms. 2. 238.<BR>—5 Last (opp. प्रथम); सामान्यमेषां प्रथमावरत्वम् Ku. 7. 44.<BR>—6 Least; usually as the last member of comp. with numerals; त्र्यवरैः<BR> साक्षिभिर्भाव्यः Ms. 8. 60, 3. 187, 11. 80, 12. 110; त्र्यवरा परिषद्<BR> ज्ञेया 112; Y. 2. 69.<BR>—7 Western.<BR>—8 Nearer, next.<BR>—9 Most excellent (अत्यन्तश्रेष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरः|अवर|अवरं
अवर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A country behind.<BR>—2 Time gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरा
अवर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 A Direction.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरम्
अवर + .{@-रम्@} The hind thigh of an elephant (also ˚रा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवरार्धः, अवरार्धतः, अवरार्ध्य, अवरावर, अवरोक्त, अवरज, अवरपरम्, अवरपुरुषाः, अवरवर्ण, अवरवर्णकः, अवरवर्णजः, अवरव्रत, अवरशैलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्धः|अवरार्ध
अवर + -अर्धः<BR>—1 the least part, the minimum.<BR>—2 the last half.<BR>—3 the hinder part of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्धम्
अवर + -अर्धः + .({@-र्धम्@}) <i>ind.</i> in a certain succession of parts, successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्धतः
अवर + -अर्धतः <i>ind.</i> from below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्ध्य
अवर + -अर्ध्य <i>a.</i> [अवरार्धे भवः यत्]<BR>—1 being or on the lower or near side.<BR>—2 belonging to the last half.<BR>—3 beginning from below.<BR>—4 defective (न्यून).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्ध्यम्
अवर + -अर्ध्य + .({@-र्ध्यम्@}) the least or smallest part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरावर
अवर + -अवर <i>a.</i> lowest, most inferior of all; न हि प्रकृष्टान्<BR> प्रेष्यांस्तु प्रेषयत्यवरावरान् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोक्त
अवर + -उक्त <i>a.</i> named last.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">Page0253-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0252-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरज|अवरजः
अवर + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 younger, junior, born afterwards Śi. 14. 74.<BR>—2 of a low birth, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरजः|अवरज
अवर + -ज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a younger brother; भीमसेनादवरजः श्रेष्ठः सर्वधनुष्मताम् Mb. 14. 72. 14;<BR> R. 11. 54, 14. 11, 36.<BR>—2 a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरजा
अवर + -ज + .({@-जः@}) + ({@-जा@}) a younger sister; विदर्भराजावरजा R. 6. 58, 84, 12. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरपरम्
अवर + -परम् <i>ind.</i> one after (upon) another; यस्मिन्त्समुद्रो द्यौर्भूमिस्त्रयोऽवरपरं<BR> श्रिताः Av. 11. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरपुरुषाः
अवर + -पुरुषाः (pl.) oneʼs descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्ण|अवरवर्णः
अवर + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> belonging to a low caste or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्णः|अवरवर्ण
अवर + -वर्ण + .({@-र्णः@})<BR>—1 a Śūdra, a man of the fourth tribe.<BR>—2 the last or fourth tribe; स्पर्शेनावरवर्णजः (हन्ति) Ms. 3. 241.<BR> ब्राह्मणान् बाधमानं तु कामादवरवर्णजम् (हन्यात्) 9. 248.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्णकः|अवरवर्णक
अवर + -वर्णकः, -वर्णजः a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्णजः|अवरवर्णज
अवर + -वर्णकः, -वर्णजः a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरव्रत|अवरव्रतः
अवर + -व्रत <i>a.</i> having no vow (हीनव्रत or अधमव्रत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरव्रतः|अवरव्रत
अवर + -व्रत + .({@-तः@}) [अवरम् अत्यन्तश्रेष्ठं व्रतमस्य]<BR>—1 the Sun.<BR>—2 a kind of tree (<i>Arka</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरशैलः|अवरशैल
अवर + -शैलः [अवरः पश्चाद्वर्ती शैलः] the western mountain (behind<BR> which the sun is supposed to set).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरक्षणी
अवरक्षणी A rope for tying horses (Hariv. 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरङ्गसाहः|अवरङ्गसाह
अवरङ्गसाहः The king Aurangzeb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतः|अवरत
अवरतः <i>ind.</i> [अवर-तसिल्] Behind, afterwards, hinder, posterior,<BR> downwards, below, from below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरस्तात्
अवरस्तात् <i>ind.</i> [अवर-प्रथमाद्यर्थे अस्ताति P. V. 3. 29, 41]<BR> Behind, hinder, posterior, below, downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरीण|अवरीणं
अवरीण <i>a.</i> Degraded, censured, debased, despised (अधरीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरेण
अवरेण <i>ind.</i> (With acc.) Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्यति
अवर्यति Den. P. To become lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरम्
अवरम् €1 Ā. To leave off, cease (only in <i>p. p.</i>)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरत|अवरतः
अवरत <i>p. p.</i> Stopped, ceased, resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतिः|अवरति
अवरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Stopping, ceasing, cessation.<BR>—2 Repose, relaxation, rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरहस
अवरहस <i>a.</i> [अवततं रहः अच् अन्ववतप्ताद्रहसः P. V. 4. 81]<BR> Having no people, desolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुग्ण
अवरुग्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Broken, torn; अवरुग्णतुङ्गसुरदारुतरौ Ki. 6. 5.<BR>—2 Diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुदित
अवरुदित <i>a.</i> That upon which tears have fallen; अवक्षुतावरुदितं<BR> तथा श्राद्धे च वर्जयेत् Mb. 13. 91. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुध्
अवरुध् €7 U.<BR>—1 To obstruct, hinder, stop, prevent, detain; मा गा इत्यवरुद्धया Ś. 2. 2.<BR>—2 To shut up, besiege; अवारोधि गौर्गौपेन; अवारुद्ध गौः; (स्वयमेव)<BR> न रुधः P. III. 1. 64. Sk.; so पुरमवारुणत्; to confine, lock<BR> up (oft. with two acc.); शोकं चित्तमवारुधत् Bk. 6. 9; व्रजमवरुणद्धि<BR> गाम् Sk.; with loc. case also; आत्मानमात्मन्यवरुध्य Bhāg.<BR>—3 To furnish, supply, procure, obtain (for one), get, attain to; कामम्, अन्नम्.<BR>—4 To suspend; attach oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्ध
अवरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obstructed, stopped, checked, hindered.<BR>—2 Shut up or in, enclosed. अवरुद्धवृत्तम् Kau. A. 1.<BR>—3 <i>Incognito</i>, disguised; आस्ति कश्चिद्राजसूनुरवरुद्धश्चरन् Dk.;<BR> अवरुद्धोऽचरत्पार्थो वर्षाणि त्रिदशानि च Mb.<BR>—4 Protected, and not seen by others; अवरुद्धासु दासीषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">Page0253-2</a>]<BR> गम्यासु Y. 2. 290; Ms. 8. 236.<BR>—5 Imprisoned, secluded as in the inner apartments.<BR>—6 Overwhelmed, affected; प्रहर्षेणावरुद्धा सा व्याहर्तुं न शशाक ह<BR> Rām. 6. 113. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवरुद्धदेह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्धदेह
अवरुद्ध + -देह <i>a.</i> incarcerated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्धिः|अवरुद्धि
अवरुद्धिः <i>f.</i> [रुध्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Obstruction, restraint; इन्द्रियाणां वीर्याणां चावरुद्धौ Ait. Br.<BR>—2 Besieging.<BR>—3 Gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्धिका
अवरुद्धिः + .{@-का@} <i>f.</i> A woman secluded in the inner apartments; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधः|अवरोध
अवरोधः<BR>—1 Hindrance, obstruction; फेनायमानं स्रोतोऽवरोधः Suśr.<BR>—2 Restraint; अन्तःप्राणावरोध Mk. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Inner apartments or womenʼs apartments, harem, seraglio; निन्ये विनीतैरवरोधदक्षैः<BR> Ku. 7. 73; Śi. 5. 7; अवरोधजनः K. 57; ˚गृहेषु राज्ञः Ś. 5. 3, 6. 12.<BR>—4 The wives of a king taken collectively (oft. pl.); अवरोधे महत्यपि<BR> R. 1. 32, 4. 68, 87, also यस्यावरोधस्तनचन्दनानां प्रक्षालनाद्वारिविहारकाले 6. 48, 16. 58,<BR> Mv. 6. 20.<BR>—5 An enclosure, confinement.<BR>—6 Siege, investment, blockade; दुर्गावरोधः H. 3.<BR>—7 A covering, lid.<BR>—8 A fence, a pen.<BR>—9 A watchman.<BR>—10 Depression, hollow.<BR>—11 Layer (plant) see under अवरुह्.<BR>—12 Procuring; प्रजानन्दामृतावरोधेन गृहेषु लोकं नियमयत् Bhāg. 5. 4. 14.<BR> cf. अवरोधस्तिरोधाने राजदारेषु तद्गृहे Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवरोधायनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधायनम्
अवरोधः + -अयनम्<BR>—1 a seraglio.<BR>—2 siege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधक|अवरोधकः
अवरोधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstruction, hindering, impeding.<BR>—2 Besieging; सुधन्वा वीर्यवान् राजा मिथिलामवरोधकः Rām. 1. 71. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधकः|अवरोधक
अवरोधक + .{@-कः@} A guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधकम्
अवरोधक + .{@-कम्@} A barrier, fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधनम्
अवरोधनम्<BR>—1 A siege, blockade; प्रतारं च समुद्रस्य रात्रौ लङ्कावरोधनम्<BR> Rām. 1. 4. 35.<BR>—2 Hindering, obstructing.<BR>—3 An obstacle, impediment.<BR>—4 A closed or private place.<BR>—5 The innermost part of anything; यत्र राजा वैवस्वतो यत्रावरोधनं<BR> दिवः Rv. 9. 113. 8.<BR>—6 The inner or womenʼs apartments in a royal palace; राजावरोधनवधूरवतारयन्तः<BR> Śi. 5. 18; अवरोधने स्थास्यति Dk. 120.<BR>—7 An inmate of the harem, a queen, wife; अवरोधनानि सिन्धोः Śi. 8. 8.<BR> (समुद्रमहिष्यो नद्यः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोधिक <i>a.</i> Obstructive, impeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिकः|अवरोधिक
अवरोधिक + .{@-कः@} [अवरोधे तद्रक्षणादौ नियुक्तः ठन्] A guard of the queenʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिका
अवरोधिक + .{@-का@} A female of the inner apartments; ययुस्तरङ्गाधिरुहो- ऽवरोधिकाः Śi. 12. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिन्
अवरोधिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstructing, hindering.<BR>—2 Besieging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुह्
अवरुह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To descend, alight, go down to; कूपम् पन्थानम् &c.; come down (in<BR> general); to dismount, get down; यानासनस्थश्चैवैनमवरुह्याभिवादयेत्<BR> Ms. 2. 202; R. 4. 80; Bk. 8. 104; so प्रासादात्, वृक्षाग्रात्; ऐश्वर्यात् अवरूढः<BR> come down from, bereft of, prosperity.<BR>—2 To approach; अचिरादवरोत्स्यसि Bhāg. 3. 33. 10. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> रोहयति or रोपयति<BR>—1 To cause to descend or alight; तामवारोहयत् R. 1. 54; helped her<BR> down; to bring down, or set down; तां सरस्तीरेऽवरोप्य Dk. 139; वृक्षाद्धनूंषि, गाण्डीविम् &c.<BR>—2 To lower, lessen, reduce; Ms. 1. 82.<BR>—3 To plant (as trees).<BR>—4 To depose, dethrone, dismiss, remove (as from a throne &c.); मयाऽधिकाराभ्यामवरोप्य<BR> Mu. 3; चाणक्यं साचिव्यादवरोपयेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0253-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूढ
अवरूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Descended, alighted; dismounted.<BR>—2 Uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधः|अवरोध
अवरोधः<BR>—1 Moving down, descending.<BR>—2 A shoot sent up by the root of a plant; a slip (for planting); the<BR> pendent shoots of the (Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधनम्
अवरोधनम् Ved. Descending motion, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपणम्
अवरोपणम्<BR>—1 Uprooting.<BR>—2 Causing to descend.<BR>—3 Taking away, depriving, diminishing.<BR>—4 Setting (as of the sun).<BR>—5 Planting; अत ऊर्ध्वं प्रवक्ष्यामि वृक्षाणामवरोपणम् Mb. 13. 58. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपित
अवरोपित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Uprooted.<BR>—2 Deprived of, curtailed.<BR>—3 Diminished, lost.<BR>—4 Dethroned, bereaved of; पुराहं वालिना राम राज्यात्स्वादवरोपितः<BR> Rām. 4. 8. 32.<BR>—5 Lowered, lessened; इतरेष्वागमाद्धर्मः पादशस्त्ववरोपितः Ms. 1. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहः|अवरोह
अवरोहः<BR>—1 Descent, going or coming down.<BR>—2 A creeping plant winding itself round a tree from the bottom to the<BR> top (such as the गुडूची creeper).<BR>—3 Heaven (तस्माद्धि भोगावसाने सर्वेऽवरोहन्ति).<BR>—4 Mounting, ascending.<BR>—5 A shoot sent out by a plant, a pendent branch, one that strikes fresh<BR> roots into the earth, as of the fig-tree (वट); अवरोहशताकीर्णं<BR> वटमासाद्य तस्थतुः Rām.<BR>—6 The growth of a plant or vine.<BR>—7 (In music) The descending scale of notes.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवरोहशायिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहशायिन्
अवरोहः + -शायिन् the Indian fig-tree; so -शाखः, -शाखिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहणम्
अवरोहणम्<BR>—1 Alighting, descending.<BR>—2 Ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिका
अवरोहिका N. of a plant अश्वगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिन्
अवरोहिन् <i>a.</i> Descending.<BR>━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोही
अवरोहिन् + ({@-ही@}) N. of the Indian fig-tree (वट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिणी
अवरोहिन् + .{@-णी@} A particular condition (दशा) brought about by a particular<BR> position of the stars उच्चाङ्गपञ्चमस्थस्य दशा स्यादवरोहिणी । तस्यामल्पमवाप्नोति<BR> फलं क्लेशाच्छुभं नरः ॥. Jyotiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूप
अवरूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mis-shapen, deformed.<BR>—2 Degenerated, degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोकिन्
अवरोकिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोचकः|अवरोचक
अवरोचकः A kind of disease, loss of appetite; स्नेहगन्धिमुखं<BR> तत्र कामश्वासावरोचकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहित
अवरोहित <i>a.</i> Light red-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ग|अवर्गः
अवर्ग <i>a.</i> Having no class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्गः|अवर्ग
अवर्ग + .{@-र्गः@} The vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्चस्
अवर्चस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Without splendour, mean-looking अवर्चसं कृणुहि<BR> शत्रुमस्य Av. 4. 22. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्जिवस्
अवर्जिवस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not hindering, not being able to prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अवर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Colourless, having no marks.<BR>—2 Bad, low, destitute of good qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्णः|अवर्ण
अवर्ण + .({@-र्णः@})<BR>—1 Scandal, illrepute, stigma, spot; सोढुं न तत्पूर्वमवर्णमीशे R. 14. 38.<BR>—2 Blame, censure; न चावदद् भर्तुरवर्णमार्या 57 spoke no<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">Page0254-2</a>]<BR> ill words.<BR>—3 Epithet of 18 letters according to ह्रस्व, दीर्घ, प्लुत, उदात्त, अनुदात्त &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवर्णवादः, अवर्णसंयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्णवादः|अवर्णवाद
अवर्ण + -वादः reproach, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्णसंयोगः|अवर्णसंयोग
अवर्ण + -संयोगः No connection with any caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तन|अवर्त्तन
अवर्तन <i>a.</i> Destitute of livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तनम्
अवर्तन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Want of livelihood.<BR>—2 Non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तमान|अवर्त्तमान
अवर्तमान <i>a.</i> Not belonging to the present time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तिः|अवर्ति
अवर्तिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Bad fortune, poverty, distress, want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्त्र
अवर्त्र <i>a.</i> Ved. Not turning back; unimpeded; न मर्त्योऽवर्त्र<BR> ओषधीषु Rv. 6. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षः|अवर्ष
अवर्षः, -अवर्षणम्<BR> Want of rain, drought; करोतु भर्तृकोऽवर्षाम् Mb. 13. 94. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षणम्
अवर्षः, -अवर्षणम्<BR> Want of rain, drought; करोतु भर्तृकोऽवर्षाम् Mb. 13. 94. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षुक
अवर्षुक <i>a.</i> Ved. Not raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ष्य
अवर्ष्य <i>a.</i> Being active in rainless bright weather; नमो वर्ष्याय<BR> चावर्ष्याय च Vāj. 16. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष <i>a.</i> (also written वलक्ष) White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्ष|वलक्षः
अवलक्ष <i>a.</i> (also written वलक्ष) White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्षः|अवलक्ष
अवलक्ष <i>a.</i> (also written वलक्ष) + .{@-क्षः@} [अवलक्ष्यते, अव-लक्ष्-घञ्] The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलगितम्
अवलगितम् An additional mode in the prologue of the drama and not<BR> having any particular reference to the latter S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्न|अवलग्नः
अवलग्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clinging or adhering to, touching, in contact with; विपुलतरनिरन्तरावलग्न Śi. 7. 71.<BR>—2 Hanging down. —3 Placed contiguously, impressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्नः|अवलग्न
अवलग्न + .{@-ग्नः@} The waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्ब्|अवलंब्
अवलम्ब् €1 Ā.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To hang, slip or glide down, hang down, be suspended; कनकशृङ्खलावलम्बिनी<BR> Mu. 2 suspended by a golden chain; स्तनवदवलम्बते यः कण्ठेऽजानां<BR> मणिः स विज्ञेयः Bṛ. S. 65. 3; शाखायां मृतकमवलम्बितमास्ते Vet.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To rest, recline, sink down, remain; यस्य वचनात्तत्रावलम्बिताः H. 1.<BR>—2 To catch hold of, hold, cling to, throw or support onself on, lean<BR> on, rest on; ययौ तदीयामवलम्ब्य चाङ्गुलिम् R. 3. 25; उर्वशी राजानमवलम्बते<BR> V. 1; दण्डकाष्ठमवलम्ब्य स्थितः Ś. 2; चित्रलेखाहस्तावलम्बिता<BR> V. 1 leaning on, supported by; K. 17, 185.<BR>—3 To hold up, bear up, support, sustain, take up; अवलम्ब्यतां पुत्रः<BR> Ś. 7; हस्तेनावलम्ब्योर्वशीम् V. 3; हृदयमवललम्बे रात्रिसंभोगलक्ष्मीः<BR> Ki. 9. 78; अधिकारानवलम्ब्य Ku. 2. 18; हृदयं न त्ववलम्बितुं<BR> क्षमाः R. 8. 60; नात्मनैवावलम्बे Me. 111; हस्तेन तस्थाववलम्ब्य<BR> वासः R. 7. 9; Ku. 3. 55, 6, 68, 7. 58; तदर्हस्याजीवितमवलम्बितुम्<BR> Ś. 3; Dk. 162; Ve. 4; M. 3; V. 2; Mu. 5; K. 163.<BR>—4 To depend on or upon, hang or hinge on; सर्वोऽयं जनस्त्वामवलम्बते<BR> Bk. 18. 41; व्यवहारोऽयं चारुदत्तमवलम्बते, वसन्तसेनामातरमवलम्बते<BR> Mk. 9; Bhāṣā P. 167.<BR>—5 To have recourse to, resort to; नैराश्यमवलम्बितम् H. 1; व्यथाम्<BR> Bk. 7. 71; वैक्लव्यम् Māl. 8 to give way to despair; धैर्यमवलम्ब<BR> to summon or pluck up courage, not to despair; माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽप्यवलम्बतेऽर्थे<BR> Ku. 1. 52; दाक्षिण्यमवलम्ब्य M. 2 politely; K. 155; Ki. 2. 15; K. 220;<BR> आशाम् to cherish hopes; किं स्वातन्त्र्यमवलम्बसे Ś. 5 act<BR> wantonly, quite independently; अवलम्ब्योत्तरां दिशम् Ks. 37. 33 taking the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">Page0255-1</a>]<BR> northern direction.<BR>—6 To be slow or tardy, be late. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to hang down, suspend; तं कलशं नागदन्तेऽवलम्ब्य Pt. 4.<BR>—2 To make one rest upon or catch hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0254-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बः|अवलम्ब|अवलंबः
अवलम्बः<BR>—1 Hanging down.<BR>—2 Hanging on, dependence on (fig. also); तन्तुजालावलम्बाः Me. 72;<BR> कुनृपतिभवनद्वारसेवा˚ Bh. 1. 67.<BR>—3 A prop, stay, support (lit. and fig.); help, assistance (fig.); सावलम्बगमना<BR> R. 19. 50 walking supported by others; नभसि निरवलम्बे Cāt. 1. 8;<BR> संततिविच्छेदनिरवलम्बानाम् Ś. 6; दैवेनेत्थं दत्तहस्तावलम्बे<BR> Ratn. 1. 6; चित्रलेखादत्तहस्तावलम्बा V. 1; see हस्तावलम्ब also.<BR>—4 Hence, a crutch or stick for support.<BR>—5 A suspender.<BR>—6 An appendage.<BR>—7 A perpendicular line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बकः|अवलम्बक|अवलंबकः
अवलम्बकः A perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बकम्
अवलम्बकः + .{@-कम्@} N. of a meter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बनम्
अवलम्बनम्<BR>—1 A prop, support, stay; अवलम्बनाय दिनभर्तुरभून्न पतिष्यतः करसहस्रमपि<BR> Śi. 9. 6; सहिष्यते तत्प्रथमावलम्बनम् Ku. 5. 66; कथं स्यात्पुनरिहावलम्बनं<BR> भवत्याः H. 3; प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलम्बनार्थम् Ś. 5. 3; मम<BR> पुच्छे करावलम्बनं कृत्वोत्तिष्ठ H. 1.<BR>—2 Help, assistance.<BR>—3 Having recourse to, resorting to; adoption; इतरपक्षावलम्बनद्वारेण K. 160.<BR>—4 Walking-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बित|अवलंबित|अवलम्बितं
अवलम्बित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Supported, protected.<BR>—2 Suspended, hung down; सौधावलम्बितया वरत्रया Pt. 2; चूतशाखावलम्बिते<BR> समुद्रके Ś. 4;<BR>—3 Expeditious, prompt (शीघ्र).<BR>—4 Alighting, descending (actively used).<BR>—5 Depending upon, trusting to.<BR>—6 Clung to, caught hold of, समभिसृत्य रसादवलम्बितः Śi. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बितव्य|अवलंबितव्य
अवलम्बितव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be caught hold of or grasped.<BR>—2 Expeditious, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बिन्|अवलंबिन्
अवलम्बिन् <i>a.</i> Hanging down, depending upon, resting or reclining<BR> on, holding, supporting &c.; अस्ताचलचूडावलम्बिनि कुमुदिनीनायके<BR> H. 1; अथ धूमाभिताम्राक्षं वृक्षशाखावलम्बिनम् R. 15. 49; गवाक्षविवरावलम्बिना 19. 7;<BR> अपरधुर्यपदावलम्बी 5. 66; Ku. 7. 37; इयं हि निद्रा नयनावलम्बिनी<BR> Mk. 3. 8; पुष्पभारावलम्बिभिः (तरुभिः) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्
अवलिप् €6 P. To smear, anoint (generally used in <i>p. p.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्त|अवलिप्तः
अवलिप्त <i>p. p.</i> [लिप्-क्त]<BR>—1 Proud, arrogant, haughty, न मूर्खैर्नावलिप्तैश्च (संवसेत्) Ms. 4. 79.<BR>—2 Anointed, plastered, smeared<BR>—3 Killed; केनान्येनावलिप्ताः Mu. 3. 27.<BR>—4 Disgraced, defamed; अहंकृतावलिप्तैश्च Mb. 1. 158. 11. ˚ता, ˚त्वम्<BR> unction; pride, arrogance, vanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपः|अवलेप
अवलेपः^1<BR>—1 Pride, haughtiness; प्रियसंगमेष्वनवलेपमदः Śi. 9. 51 (where<BR> अ˚ also means ointment); व्यक्तमानावलेपाः Mu. 3. 22; R. 5. 53;<BR> हस्त˚ Me. 14.<BR>—2 Violence, attack, assault, insult, outrage; किं भवतीनामसुरावलेपेनापराद्धम्<BR> V. 1; असुर˚ <i>ibid.</i>; ददृशे पवनावलेपजं सृजती बाष्पमिवाञ्जनाविलम् R. 8. 35.<BR>—3 Smearing, anointing.<BR>—4 Ornament (भूषा).<BR>—5 Union, association (सङ्ग); cf. अवलेपस्तु गर्वे स्याल्लेपने दूषणेऽपि च Nm.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Under root avalip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपनम्
अवलेपनम्<BR>—1 Anointing.<BR>—2 Oil, any unctuous substance.<BR>—3 Union, association.<BR>—4 Pride, arrogance; तस्यावलेपनं ज्ञात्वा क्रुद्धस्तु भगवान्हरः Rām. 1. 43. 6.<BR>—5 The sandal tree (चन्दन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिह्
अवलिह् €2 U. To lick, lap; see अवलीढ below. ━<i>freq.</i> (लेलेढि)<BR> To lick again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढ|अवलीढं
अवलीढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Eaten, chewed; नोत्सहे परिभोगाय श्वावलीढं हविर्यथा Mb. 3. 291. 13.<BR> दर्भैरर्धावलीढैः Ś. 1. 7; Ms. 4. 208.<BR>—2 Licked, lapped; touched (fig. also); विषज्वालावलीढावयवा Dk. 9;<BR> नवयौवनावलीढावयवा 17, 75 pervaded by youth; अस्त्रज्वालावलीढप्रतिबलजलधेरन्तरौर्वायमाणे<BR> Ved. 3. 7 surrounded (on all sides); Ki. 13. 11; bit; बीजाञ्जलिः पतति<BR> कीटमुखावलीढः Mk. 1. 9.<BR>—3 Devoured, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढा
अवलीढ + .{@-ढा@} Disregard, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहः|अवलेह
अवलेहः<BR>—1 Licking, lapping.<BR>—2 An extract (as of Soma).<BR>—3 An electuary, confection; दाडिम˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहनम्
अवलेहनम् Licking with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहिका
अवलेहिका = अवलेह (3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह्य
अवलेह्य <i>a.</i> Fit to be licked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवली
अवली €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To stick, hang on.<BR>—2 To bow, stoop; Mb. 8.<BR>—3 To hide oneself in; Rām. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीन
अवलीन <i>p. p.</i> Sticking to, clinging to, resting under; विहगादिभिरवलीनैः<BR> Bṛ. S. 53. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीला
अवलीला [अवरा-लीला]<BR>—1 Sport, play, mirth.<BR>—2 Disrespect, contempt.<BR>—3 Facility, ease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुञ्च्|अवलुंच्
अवलुञ्च् €1 P. To pull down or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुञ्चनम्
अवलुञ्चनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off, tearing or pulling out; केश˚.<BR>—2 Uprooting.<BR>—3 Not tying up, allowing to hang down.<BR>—4 Taking away, pulling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठनम्
अवलुण्ठनम्<BR>—1 Rolling or wallowing on the ground.<BR>—2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुप्
अवलुप् €6 U.<BR>—1 To rush upon (as a wild beast on its prey), to burst or break in upon;<BR> वृकवच्चावलुम्पेत.<BR>—2 To eat, devour, swallow (fig. also); अन्योन्यस्यावलुम्पन्ति सारमेया<BR> यथामिषम् Mb.; सर्वमेवावलुम्पति H. 2. 99. अवलुप्यमान इव दृष्टिपातैः K. 93, 109.<BR>—3 To suppress, crush, keep down, stifle; रक्षत्यवलुम्पते च यः<BR> Bhāg.; जरावलुप्तमानावमानचित्तः having lost all sense of &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुम्पनम्
अवलुम्पनम् Leaping on suddenly; ततोऽवलुम्पनं कृत्वा प्रयातः<BR> पिशिताशनः Mb. 1. 140. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोपः|अवलोप
अवलोपः<BR>—1 Cutting off or away; destruction.<BR>—2 Biting, kissing (as a lip); अधरावलोप Śi. 7. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोप्य
अवलोप्य <i>a.</i> That can be broken in upon or assailed suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखः|अवलेख
अवलेखः<BR>—1 Breaking, scraping or scratching off.<BR>—2 Anything scraped off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0255-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखनम्
अवलेखनम् Scraping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखा
अवलेखा<BR>—1 Rubbing.<BR>—2 Adorning the person; अञ्जनाभ्यञ्जनोन्मर्दस्त्र्यवलेखामिषं मधु<BR> Bhāg. 7. 12. 12.<BR>—3 Drawing, painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक्
अवलोक् €1 Ā. or €10 P.<BR>—1 To see, behold, view, look at; observe (lit.); नोलूकोप्यवलोकते<BR> यदि दिवा सूर्यस्य किं दूषणम् Bh. 2. 93; परिक्रम्यावलोक्य च (in<BR> dramas); सलिलेष्ववलोकयत इवात्मानं प्रतिष्ठानस्य V. 2 being reflected<BR> in; मार्गम् or वर्त्म अवलोक् to wait for; प्रयोगम् witness<BR> a performance; M. 2; निमित्तानि अवलोकयेत् Bṛ. S. 53. 105; look out<BR> for, seek; consult (as opinions).<BR>—2 To look at or see (in astron.); exercise influence upon; सुरपतिगुरुणावलोकिते<BR> Bṛ. S. 5. 62; शुक्रवाचस्पतिभ्यां च तव भार्यावलोकिता Mārk. P.<BR>—3 To find; observe, see; be aware of, meditate or reflect upon; आत्मानमात्मन्यवलोकयन्तम्<BR> Ku. 3. 50; R. 8. 74, 11. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकः|अवलोक
अवलोकः<BR>—1 Seeing, beholding; जृम्भाङ्गभङ्गनयनमीलनाङ्गावलोककृत् S. D.;<BR> वनशोभावलोकाय V. 4. 31.<BR>—2 Sight.<BR>—3 Looking down upon with compassion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवलोकलवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकलवः
अवलोकः + -लवः A glance, side-look; स्मायावलोकलवदर्शितभाव Bhāg. 10. 61. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकक
अवलोकक <i>a.</i> Looking at, wishing to see; Rām. 6. 116. 11; तं<BR> विवाहे कृते राजन्सभार्यमवलोककः Mb. 3. 115. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकनम्
अवलोकनम्<BR>—1 Looking at, beholding, seeing; नो बभूवुरवलोकनक्षमाः R. 11. 60.<BR>—2 Looking over, commanding a view of; दीर्घिकावलोकनगवाक्षगता M. 1.<BR>—3 Sight, eye.<BR>—4 A look, glance; योगनिद्रान्तविशदैः पावनैरवलोकनः R. 10. 14.<BR>—5 Looking out for, inquiry, seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकयितृ
अवलोकयितृ <i>a.</i> Looking upon, considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकित|अवलोकितं|अवलोकितः
अवलोकित <i>p. p.</i> Seen &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकितः|अवलोकित|अवलोकितं
अवलोकित + .{@-तः@} N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकितम्
अवलोकित + .{@-तम्@} A look, glance; परिवृत्यावलोकितम् R. 4. 72.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवलोकितेश्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकितेश्वरः|अवलोकितेश्वर
अवलोकित + -ईश्वरः N. of a Boddhisattva worshipped by the northern Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकिन्
अवलोकिन् <i>a.</i> Looking at, seeing. चतुरावलोकिनः (चक्षुषः) Ku. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोभनम्
अवलोभनम् Sensual desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोम
अवलोम <i>a.</i> [अवनद्धं लोम आनुकूल्यम् P. V. 4. 75] One who<BR> is favourable; suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुज|अवल्गुजः
अवल्गुज <i>a.</i> Of no good origin or extraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुजः|अवल्गुज
अवल्गुज + .{@-जः@} N. of a plant सोमराजी. Vernonia Anthelminthica (Mar. बांबची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुली
अवल्गुली A poisonous insect. Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदः|अववद
अववदः, -वदनम्<BR> Censure, an evil report or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदनम्
अववदः, -वदनम्<BR> Censure, an evil report or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदितृ
अववदितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who speaks finally or decisively.<BR>—2 An adjudicator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववादः|अववाद
अववादः<BR>—1 Censure, reproach.<BR>—2 Trust, confidence.<BR>—3 Disregard, disrespect.<BR>—4 Support, dependence on.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">Page0256-2</a>]<BR>—5 Evil report.<BR>—6 A command, an order.<BR>—7 Information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववरकः|अववरक
अववरकः<BR>—1 An aperture.<BR>—2 Window; see अपवरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववर्षणम्
अववर्षणम् Raining upon (completely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवविद्ध
अवविद्ध <i>a.</i> Cast down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्च्
अवव्रश्च् €6 P. To splinter, to cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्चः|अवव्रश्च
अवव्रश्चः A splinter, chip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश <i>a.</i> [नास्ति वशम् आयत्तत्वं यस्य]<BR>—1 Independent, free; विशन्ति चावशाः पार्थ योगाद्योगबलान्विताः Mb. 12. 300. 24.<BR>—2 Not compliant or docile, disobedient, self-willed; स्त्री चावशा<BR> Pt. 1. 424; Ms. 5. 33.<BR>—3 Not subjected to or swayed; अवशो विषयाणाम् K. 45; uncontrolled,<BR> unrestrained; ˚इन्द्रियचित्तानाम् H. 1. 17, 2. 14; Dk. 34; मधुरैरवशानि<BR> लम्भयन् वशम् Ki. 2. 55 wild.<BR>—4 Not master of oneself, subject to the senses; कमपरमवशं न<BR> विप्रकुर्युः Ku. 6. 95.<BR>—5 Not having oneʼs own will, dependent, helpless, powerless; सकलमवशं<BR> सीदति जगत् H. 2. 76; कार्यते ह्यवशः Bg. 3. 5; K. 174; Pt. 1. 335;<BR> U. 3; कथमवशो ह्ययशोविषं पिबामि Mk. 10. 13; विमुञ्चन्त्यवशा<BR> देहं कालस्य वशमागताः Rām.; Mu. 1. 12.<BR>—6 Necessary, certain; किमस्य भवतो यथा सुहृद एव नाशोऽवशः Mu. 6. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवशेन्द्रियचित्त, अवशग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेन्द्रियचित्त
अवश + -इन्द्रियचित्त <i>a.</i> whose mind and senses are not held in subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशग
अवश + -ग <i>a.</i> Not being in any oneʼs power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशंगमः|अवशङ्गम
अवशंगमः Not submitting to anotherʼs will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिका
अवशिका = अवश; Mk. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीभूत
अवशीभूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unrestrained, independent.<BR>—2 Not influenced by magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अवश्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untameable, ungovernable, unruly.<BR>—2 Inevitable; अथ मरणमवश्यमेव जन्तोः Ve. 3. 6.<BR>—3 Indispensable, necessary.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवश्यपुत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यपुत्रः|अवश्यपुत्र
अवश्य + -पुत्रः a son whom it is impossible to govern or teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यम्
अवश्यम् <i>ind.</i> [अव-श्यै-डमु Tv.]<BR>—1 Necessarily, inevitably; त्वामप्यस्रं नवजलमयं मोचयिष्यन्त्यवश्यम् Me. 95.<BR>—2 Certainly, at all events, by all means, surely, of course; अवश्यं<BR> याति तिर्यक्त्वं जग्ध्वा चैवाहुतं हविः Ms. 12. 68; अवश्यं यातारश्चिरतरमुषित्वापि<BR> विषयाः Bh. 3. 16; तां चावश्यं दिवसगणनातत्परामेकपत्नीम् (द्रक्ष्यसि)<BR> Me. 10, 63; अवश्यमेव Most surely; if compounded with pot. pass.<BR> the final nasal is dropped, लुम्पेदवश्यमः कृत्ये; अवश्यपाच्य to be<BR> necessarily cooked; अवश्यकार्य to be necessarily done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यंभाविन्
अवश्यंभाविन् <i>a.</i> Destined to take place, inevitable; ˚आदेशः<BR> M. 5; अवश्यंभावि लक्षणम् H. 3; अवश्यंभाविनो भावा भवन्ति महतामपि<BR> H. Pr. 28; Ś. 6. cf. अवश्यंभाविभावामां प्रतीकारो भवेद् यदि । तदा<BR> दुःखैर्न लिप्येरन् नलरामयुधिष्ठिराः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अवश्यक <i>a.</i> Necessary, inevitable, indispensable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकता
अवश्यकता, -त्वम्<BR> Necessity, obligation, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकत्वम्
अवश्यकता, -त्वम्<BR> Necessity, obligation, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशक्थिका
अवशक्थिका = अवसक्थिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशप्त
अवशप्त <i>a.</i> Cursed; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0256-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशस्
अवशस् [अव-शंस्-क्विप्]<BR>—1 A wrong desire. अवशसा निःशसा यत् Av. 6. 45. 2.<BR>—2 Censure, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशा
अवशा Ved. Not a cow, a bad cow; य एनामवशामाह देवानां निहितं<BR> निधिम् Av. 12. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशातनम्
अवशातनम्<BR>—1 Destroying, cutting or lopping off.<BR>—2 Withering, drying up.<BR>—3 Emaciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिरस्
अवशिरस् <i>a.</i> Having the head bent or hung down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्
अवशिष् (Used mostly in <i>pass.</i>) To be left last or as a remainder,<BR> to remain over or behind; यज्ज्ञात्वा नेह भूयोऽन्यज्ज्ञातव्यमवशिष्यते<BR> Bg. 7. 2. पूर्णस्य पूर्णमादाय पूर्णमेवावशिष्यते Bṛ. Up. 5. 1. 1.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To leave as a remainder; देहमात्रावशेषितः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्ट|अवशिष्टः
अवशिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, remaining; स्तम्बेन नीवार इवावशिष्टः R. 5. 15; किमवशिष्टमह्नः<BR> Ratn. 3; निद्रागमसीम्नः कियदवशिष्टम् Mv. 6; कियदवशिष्टं रजन्याः<BR> Ś. 4 how much of the night yet remains (has yet to run).<BR>—2 Remaining over and above, surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्टम्
अवशिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्, -ष्टकम्@} Rest, remainder, remnant; सुराकामद्यूतकृतं<BR> दण्डशुल्कावशिष्टकम् Y. 2. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्टकम्
अवशिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्, -ष्टकम्@} Rest, remainder, remnant; सुराकामद्यूतकृतं<BR> दण्डशुल्कावशिष्टकम् Y. 2. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेषः|अवशेष
अवशेषः —1 Remnant, rest, leavings, remainder; रक्षसामवशेषेण,<BR> अह्नः, पुण्यानाम्, बलं तदवशेषं तु नाशयामास वानरः Rām. 5. 46. 38;<BR> वृत्तान्त˚ M. 5 the rest of the story; in this sense usually in<BR> comp.; अर्धम् having only one half left; कथा˚ or नाम˚ one<BR> who survives only in narration or name, having only the tale or name left<BR> behind; used figuratively for dead; see the words s. v., भस्म˚ remaining<BR> only in ashes, reduced to ashes, भस्मावशेषः कथमेवमुष्णः Ś. 3. 3;<BR> भस्मावशेषं मदनं चकार reduced to ashes Ku. 3. 72; Śi. 10. 16;<BR> सावशेषमिव भट्टिन्या वचनम् M. 4 unfinished; सावशेषो विषवेगः<BR> <i>ibid.</i> still remaining; शीर्षावशेषीकृतः Bh. 2. 34; Ratn. 2. 2;<BR> R. 2. 69; शृणु मे सावशेषं वचः Ś. 2 hear me out, let me finish<BR> my speech; अल्पावशेषायुः K. 46 having a short span of life; see निरवशेष also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेषित
अवशेषित <i>p. p.</i> Left, remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीनः|अवशीन
अवशीनः A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्ष|अवशीर्षः
अवशीर्ष, -र्षक <i>a.</i><BR> [अवनतं शीर्षं यस्य वा, कप्] Having the head bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्षक
अवशीर्ष, -र्षक <i>a.</i><BR> [अवनतं शीर्षं यस्य वा, कप्] Having the head bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्षः|अवशीर्ष
अवशीर्ष, -र्षक + .{@-र्षः@}<BR>—1 An error made in sleeping (as regards position).<BR>—2 A kind of eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशॄ
अवशॄ €9 P.<BR>—1 To break.<BR>—2 To be dispersed, to fly in every direction; स तस्या महिमां दृष्ट्वा<BR> समन्तादवशीर्यत Rām. 1. 37. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्ण
अवशीर्ण <i>a.</i> Broken, shattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या [अव-श्यै क]<BR>—1 Hoar-frost, fog or mist.<BR>—2 An independent woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यायः|अवश्याय
अवश्यायः [अव-श्यै-ण P. III. 1. 141]<BR>—1 Frost, dew; नावश्यायः पपातोर्व्याम् Mb. 1. 173. 40.<BR>—2 Hoar frost, white dew अवश्यायावसिक्तस्य पुण्डरीकस्य चारुताम् U. 6. 29.<BR>—3 Pride. अवश्यायो हिमे गर्वे … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवश्यायपटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यायपटः|अवश्यायपट
अवश्यायः + -पटः A kind of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्रयणम्
अवश्रयणम् Taking anything from off the fire (opp. अधिश्रयण);<BR> अधिश्रयणावश्रयणान्तादिपूर्वापरीभूतो व्यापारकलापः पाकादिशब्दवाच्यः S. D. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवषट्कार
अवषट्कार <i>a.</i> Without the exclamation वषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्कयणी
अवष्कयणी A cow that bears a calf after a long interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ्|अवष्टंभ्
अवष्टम्भ् €5. €9. P.<BR>—1 To lean or rest upon; धनुरवष्टभ्य Mv. 5; so दण्डम्; प्रकृतिं<BR> स्वामवष्टभ्य Bg. 9. 8 by the help of; वृद्धां भार्यामवष्टभ्य Rām. on account of.<BR>—2 To block up; कोसलनृपतेर्द्वारमवष्टभ्य Ratn. 4.<BR>—3 To wrap, envelop, cover with; K. 116; तिमिरेणावष्टभ्यमाने जीवलोके 159;<BR> occupy; Dk. 159.<BR>—4 To support, prop, hold up; clasp, embrace; अवष्टभ्यासौ माम् Mv. 5. 5;<BR> क्रोडविभागेन मामवष्टभ्य K. 33, 42, 54.<BR>—5 To hinder, stop, arrest, hold or keep back; अवष्टभ्यमान इव जलधरैः K. 303.<BR>—6 To be near.<BR>—7 To be astounded or bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अवष्टब्ध <i>p. p.</i> [अवस्तम्भ्-क्त, षत्वम्]<BR>—1 Supported, rested on, protected; held, seized. अंसाववष्टब्धनतौ<BR> समाधिः Ki. 16. 21.<BR>—2 Hanging from or upon; अवष्टब्धा यष्टिः Sk.<BR>—3 Near, contiguous; अद्यश्वीनावष्टब्धे P. V. 2. 13; Bk. 9. 72.<BR>—4 Obstructed, stopped, suspended. पतिव्रता च सुश्रोणी अवष्टब्धा च<BR> जानकी Rām. 5. 59. 23.<BR>—5 Paralysed.<BR>—6 Bound, tied, attached.<BR>—7 Wrapped up, enfolded.<BR>—8 Opposed.<BR>—9 Surpassed, overcome; अविदूरेऽप्यवष्टब्ध रुद्धे क्रान्ते तिरस्कृते Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भः|अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः
अवष्टम्भः [स्तम्भ्-घञ्, सस्य षत्वम्]<BR>—1 Leaning, resting upon.<BR>—2 Support, prop; मेरोश्चतुर्दिशमवष्टम्भगिरय उपकॢप्ताः Bhāg. 5. 16. 11.<BR> पक्षाभ्यामीषत्कृतावष्टम्भः K. 34, 44, 186, 231, 248; खड्गलतावष्टम्भनिश्चलः<BR> Māl. 3; (hence) having recourse to, plucking up or summoning (as courage);<BR> तत्कथमहं धैर्यावष्टम्भं करोमि Pt. 1; so पौरुष˚, धीरत्व˚<BR> Māl. 2; सहजसत्त्व˚ K. 286.<BR>—3 Haughtiness, pride, dignity, majestic greatness; सावष्टम्भाकृतिना<BR> K. 179 dignified, noble, see सावष्टम्भ.<BR>—4 A post, pillar.<BR>—5 Gold.<BR>—6 Commencement, beginning.<BR>—7 Stopping, standing still, staying.<BR>—8 Courage, steadiness K. 156, 157; resolute determination; ईदृशोऽस्यावष्टम्भः<BR> Ratn. 4; अविनयकोपितोऽवष्टम्भं कृत्वा K. 261 plucking up courage;<BR> पलायनमवष्टम्भो वा Pt. 4 holding out (as opposed to पलायनम्).<BR>—9 Obstruction, impediment.<BR>—10 Paralysis; stupefaction K. 141.<BR>—11 Excellence. cf. अवष्टम्भः सुवर्णे च स्तम्भप्रारम्भयोरपि । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भमय|अवष्टंभमय
अवष्टम्भमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Golden, made of gold, or as large as a post; रघोरवष्टम्भमयेन<BR> पत्रिणा R. 3. 53. (अ˚ is usually rendered in the above manner, but<BR> from the immediate context, it should more properly mean ‘full of dignified boldness’<BR>, ‘breathing defiance’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भनम्
अवष्टम्भनम्<BR>—1 Resting upon, having recourse to.<BR>—2 Supporting.<BR>—3 Paralysing, stupefying.<BR>—4 A post, pillar.<BR>—5 Stopping, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0257-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वन्
अवष्वन् €1 P. To smack (oneʼs lips), make a noise in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वाणः|अवष्वाण|अवष्वाणं
अवष्वाणः [अव-स्वन्-घञ् षत्वम्] Noisy eating, smacking (the lips).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्
अवस् <i>n.</i> [अव्-भावे असिच्] Ved.<BR>—1 Protection, assistance.<BR>—2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>—3 Food, provision.<BR>—4 Wealth; riches.<BR>—5 Going.<BR>—6 Satisfaction, pleasure.<BR>—7 Wish, will, desire, aspiration. ━<i>ind.</i> [अवर-प्रथमायाः पञ्चम्याः<BR> सप्तम्या वाऽर्थे असि, अव् आदेशः P. V. 3. 39]<BR>—1 Below, downwards, hitherward.<BR>—2 (As a preposition with instr. or abl.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Below, at the lowest place.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Without, on the outside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्वत्|अवस्वन्त्
अवस्वत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Striving, aspiring, Desirous; ऊर्ध्वायां दिश्यवस्वन्तो<BR> नाम देवाः Av. 3. 26. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसः|अवस|अवसं
अवसः [अव्-असच् Uṇ. 3. 117; अवतीत्यवसो राजा भानुश्च Ujjval.]<BR>—1 A king.<BR>—2 The Sun. —3 A kind of tree (अर्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसम्
अवसः + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Refreshment, food, यदमुष्णीतमवसं पणिं गाः Rv. 1. 93. 4.<BR> provision (especially for a journey), <i>viaticum</i> (˚सः also); एतत्ते<BR> रुद्रावसम् Yv. 3. 61.<BR>—2 Preserving, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका [अवबद्धे सक्थिनी यस्यां कप्]<BR>—1 A cloth girt round the legs and knees (by a person), when sitting on<BR> his hams; also, the act of girding round this cloth or the posture itself;<BR> शयानः प्रौढपादश्च कृत्वा चैवावसक्थिकाम् Ms. 4. 112; अहिना अवसक्थिकाबन्धहेतुभूतेन<BR> Malli. on Ki. 12. 22.<BR>—2 (Hence) A wrapper, a girth or band in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसञ्ज्|अवसंज्
अवसञ्ज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To suspend, attach, cling to, throw, place; अशिथिलमपरावसज्य<BR> कण्ठे Śi. 7. 16; so स्कन्धे पाणिम्, शरीरे भूषणानि &c.<BR>—2 To entrust to, throw on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्त
अवसक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Suspended from, placed; कर्णावसक्तामलदन्तपत्रम् Ku. 7. 23,<BR> K. 206; Ki. 7. 40; Śi. 5. 16, 18, 9. 7; C. P. 4.<BR>—2 In contact with, bound round, touching; अविज्ञातावसक्तेन दूषिता<BR> मम वाससा Mk. 1. 54.<BR>—3 Engaged in, intent on, eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्तम्
अवसक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसञ्जनम्
अवसञ्जनम् Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसज्जनम्
अवसज्जनम् Clinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसंडीनम्
अवसंडीनम् The downward flight of birds in a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथः|अवसथ
अवसथः [अव-सो-कथन्]<BR>—1 A dwelling place, habitation.<BR>—2 A village.<BR>—3 A school, college (छात्रालयः, मठः); see आवसथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथम्
अवसथः + .{@-थम्@} A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्यः|अवसथ्य
अवसथ्यः [अवसथ-स्वार्थे यत्] A college, school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसद्
अवसद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sink down, faint, fail, give away; आस्तिकः सततं शृण्वन् न कृच्छ्रेवसीदति<BR> Mb. 1. 1. 62. करिणी पङ्कमिवावसीदति Ki. 2. 6 sinks or fails; पौरुषम् 7;<BR> अवसीदन्ति मे प्राणाः Mb.; न हीङ्गितज्ञोऽवसरेऽवसीदति Ki. 4. 20<BR> fails not (does not shut his lips); न कृच्छ्रेष्ववसीदति Mb.;<BR> Ms. 4. 187; Bk. 6. 24.<BR>—2 to suffer, be neglected or interfered<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">Page0258-2</a>]<BR> with नावसीदति वा गुरु प्रयोजनम् K. 181.<BR>—3 To become disheartened or exhausted; Dk. 127.<BR>—4 To perish, come to an end, be ruined; सर्वमस्मत्कुटुम्बकमवसीदेत्<BR> Dk. 60; नास्त्युद्यमसमो बन्धुः कृत्वा यं नावसीदति Bh. 2. 86. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to sink; to dispirit, render down-hearted, to ruin; कुटुम्बकं<BR> चावसादितम् Dk. 41, ruined; आत्मानमात्मनाऽनवसाद्यैवोद्धरन्ति सन्तः 54<BR> without ruining or killing; Bg. 6. 5; राज्यस्य मूलं हस्त्यश्वमवसादयेत् Mu. 3 ruin.<BR>—2 To allay, remove; औत्सुक्यमात्रमवसादयति प्रतिष्ठा Ś. 5. 6 (v. l.<BR> अवसादयति); अवमहमवसादयामि वः सपत्नान् Dk. 127 destroy,<BR> kill; अवसादितवाचाम् Śi. 10. 30 rendered speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अवसन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sunk down (fig. also), enervated, sinking, drooping; अतिप्रबलपिपासावसन्नानि<BR> K. 36; Śi. 15. 85; मदावसन्नहस्त Dk. 62 powerless.<BR>—2 Dispirited, sad, melancholy, unhappy; कान्तारेष्ववसन्नानाम् Mb. 4. 6. 20;<BR> दधिकर्णोऽवसन्नो ब्रूते H. 2 lean, weakened.<BR>—3 Ended, terminated, gone off; अवसन्नतापमतमिस्रमभात् Śi. 9. 12<BR> devoid of heat; अवसन्नायां रात्रौ H. 1.<BR>—4 Unable to do oneʼs duty.<BR>—5 Lost, deprived of; पित्रोः सकाशमवसन्नदृशोर्निनाय R. 9. 77<BR> who had lost their sight.<BR>—6 (In law) Non-suited, defeated.<BR>—7 Dead, gone; ततस्तेष्ववसन्नेषु सेनापतिषु पञ्चसु Rām. 5. 46. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नता
अवसन्नता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Affliction, dejection.<BR>—2 Termination, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नत्वम्
अवसन्नता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Affliction, dejection.<BR>—2 Termination, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादः|अवसाद
अवसादः<BR>—1 Sinking, fainting, sitting down Ki. 18. 47; अनवसादः safety,<BR> protection; failure, as of the voice.<BR>—2 Ruin, loss, destruction, decline; धैर्यावसादेन कृतप्रसादा वन्यद्विपेनेव<BR> निदाघसिन्धुः Ki. 3. 38; पर्यायजयावसादा Ki. 17. 18; विपदेति<BR> तावदवसादकरी Ki. 18. 23, 6. 41; Mv. 2.<BR>—3 End, termination.<BR>—4 Want of energy, exhaustion, languor, fatigue, pain; बन्धनाच्चावसादान्मे<BR> श्रेयः प्रायोपवेशनम् Rām. 4. 55. 11. किमिवावसादकरमात्मवताम् Ki. 6. 19.<BR>—5 (In law) Badness of a cause, defeat, losing (a cause); अलं स्वपक्षावसादशङ्कया M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing to sink, faint, or fail.<BR>—2 Causing dejection or fatigue; एष शोकः परित्यक्तः सर्वकार्यावसादकः Rām.<BR>—3 Exhausting, wearisome, tiresome, fatiguing.<BR>—4 Ending, finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादनम्
अवसादनम्<BR>—1 Decline, loss, destruction; नन्दनं वानरेन्द्राणां रक्षसामवसादनम्<BR> Rām. 6. 108. 12. असूनामवसादनम् Ve. 6.<BR>—2 Inability to do oneʼs duty.<BR>—3 Oppression.<BR>—4 Finishing.<BR>—5 An escharotic.<BR>—6 Removing proud flesh (from boils) by escharotic application; उत्सन्नमृदुमांसानां<BR> व्रणानामवसादनम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादिन्
अवसादिन् <i>a.</i> Sinking, drooping; अपतदवसादिनः करात् Śi. 15. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसभ
अवसभ <i>a.</i> Ved. Excluded from society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृ
अवसृ €1 P. To spread, pervade; गगनाङ्गनावकाशावसरत्कलकलम् Māl. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0258-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरः|अवसर
अवसरः<BR>—1 Occasion, opportunity, time; उत्पन्नावसरमर्थित्वम् M. 3; नास्यावसरं<BR> दास्यामि Ś. 2; भवद्गिरामवसरप्रदानाय वचांसि नः Śi. 2. 8;<BR> विसर्जन˚ सत्कारः Ś. 7; ˚प्राप्तम् suited to the occasion M. 1;<BR> K. 158; ˚तुलिताभिः Pt. 5. 28 equal to the occasion; वेदस्यावसरोऽत्र<BR> कः Ks. 5. 62 what has the Veda to do here?<BR>—2 (Hence) A fit or proper opportunity, proper or opportune time; अवसरपठिता<BR> वाणी गुणगणरहितापि शोभते पुंसाम् Subh. Ratn. शशंस सेवावसरं<BR> सुरेभ्यः Ku. 7. 40; अवसरोऽयमात्मानं प्रकाशयितुम् Ś. 1; see अनवसर<BR> also; अवसरोऽपसर्पणीया राजानः Ś. 6.<BR>—3 Space, room, scope; कुमुदेङ्गना मनसि चावसरम् (अलभत) Śi. 9. 41.<BR>—4 Leisure, advantageous position.<BR>—5 Introduction.<BR>—6 A kind of संगति q. v.<BR>—7 A year.<BR>—8 Raining.<BR>—9 Descent.<BR>—10 A consultation in private.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवसरकाले, अवसरवेलायाम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरकाले
अवसरः + -काले, -वेलायाम् <i>ind.</i> On a favourable opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरवेलायाम्
अवसरः + -काले, -वेलायाम् <i>ind.</i> On a favourable opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरणम्
अवसरणम् Removing, causing to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पः|अवसर्प
अवसर्पः A spy, a secret emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पणम्
अवसर्पणम् Stepping or going down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिन्
अवसर्पिन् <i>a.</i> Stepping down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिणी
अवसर्पिन् + .{@-णी@} A long period of time (with the Jainas); the descending cycle<BR> is divided into six stages (good-good, good, good-bad, bad-good, bad,<BR> bad-bad) according to Hemacandra it is equal to 2000,000,000,000,000 Sāgaras of years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसव्य|अवसव्यं
अवसव्य <i>a.</i> Not left, right (= अपसव्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसामम्
अवसामम् [अवरं साम अच्समा˚ P. V. 4. 75] A bad song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसिच्
अवसिच् €6 P. To sprinkle, bedew, bespatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसिक्त
अवसिक्त <i>p. p.</i> Sprinkled; ˚अङ्ग having the limbs sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकः|अवसेक
अवसेकः<BR>—1 Sprinkling, bedewing; देशः को नु जलावसेकशिथिलः Mk. 3. 12.<BR>—2 A disease of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकिमः|अवसेकिम
अवसेकिमः [अवसेकेन निर्वृत्तः अवसेक-इमन्] A kind of cake,<BR> pulse ground with oil and butter (वटकभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेचनम्
अवसेचनम्<BR>—1 Sprinkling.<BR>—2 Water used for sprinkling; पाद˚ Ms. 4. 151.<BR>—3 Bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसुप्त
अवसुप्त <i>a.</i> Asleep; अथ रात्र्यां व्यतीतायामवसुप्तमनन्तरम्<BR> Rām. 2. 56. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृज्
अवसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To throw or cast down, pour out, let fall, drop; मयाभिमन्त्रिता पूर्वं<BR> कस्मात्त्वमवसर्जिता Rām. 7. 56. 23; U. 3. 23; Ms. 1. 8; so सायकान्,<BR> बीजम्, वृष्टिम् &c.<BR>—2 To let loose, liberate, dismiss &c.<BR>—3 To remit.<BR>—4 To form; create.<BR>—5 To place on, throw or cast at.<BR>—6 To leave, give up, abandon; as क्रोधम् वैरम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्गः|अवसर्ग
अवसर्गः<BR>—1 Letting off, relaxation.<BR>—2 Non-prevention, allowing one to follow oneʼs inclinations.<BR>—3 Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्जनम्
अवसर्जनम् Liberation; बन्धानामवसर्जनाय Vāj. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृष्ट
अवसृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Given away, left, abandoned, dismissed, let go.<BR> अथापि यत्पादनखावसृष्टम् Bhāg. 1. 18. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसो
अवसो €4 P.<BR>—1 To finish, accomplish.<BR>—2 To destroy.<BR>—3 To determine, understand; किमप्यनवसीयमानम् K. 278; अवासासीच्च<BR> वैयासिकीम् (वाणीम्) Malli.<BR>—4 (Intrans.) To fail; be at an end; शक्तिर्ममावस्यति हीनयुद्धे Ki. 16. 17.<BR>—5 To put up (as at an inn).<BR>—6 To let loose, liberate.<BR>—7 To draw near, approach.<BR>—8 To dwell, stay.<BR>—9 To settle, fix.<BR>—10 To stand firm, to persist in.<BR>—11 To know; अवसेयाश्च कार्याणि धर्मेण पुरवासिनाम् Bk. 19.<BR>—12 To get, attain to, reach. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to be completed, finish, complete; अथ विधिमवसाय्य शास्त्रदृष्टम् R. 5. 76.<BR>—2 To understand, comprehend; अवसाययितुं क्षमाः सुखम् Ki. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसा
अवसा Ved. Liberation, release. कथा शृण्वन्नवसामस्य वेद Rv. 4. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसातृ
अवसातृ <i>m.</i> Ved. A deliverer, liberator; अत्रा युक्तोऽवसातारमिच्छात् Rv. 10. 27. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानम्
अवसानम् [अव-सो-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Stopping.<BR>—2 Conclusion, termination, cessation, end; दोहावसाने पुनरेव दोग्ध्रीम्<BR> R. 2. 23, 45; तच्छिष्याध्ययननिवेदितावसानाम् 1. 95; इत्येतदवसानं<BR> कथायाः M. 5 thus ends the story; ˚विरसे K. 180; आत्मनः सुखावसानेन<BR> V. 3 at the sacrifice of; (at the end of comp.) ending with, terminating<BR> at; स चायमङ्गुलीयकदर्शनावसानः Ś. 7; यत्खलु दुःखावसानमेव<BR> दुःखम् K. 328.<BR>—3 Death, decease; अवसानेऽङ्गराजस्य योद्धव्यं भवता किल Ve. 5. 39;<BR> मूलपुरुषावसाने संपदः परमुपतिष्ठन्ति Ś. 6.<BR>—4 boundary, limit; विलोकिता दर्शनीयानामवसानभूमिः K. 124 furthest<BR> or highest limit.<BR>—5 (In gram.) The last part of a word or period (opp. आदि); आदिमध्यावसानेषु<BR> यरता यान्ति लाघवम्; अनीकपदावसानं देवादि नाम R. 18. 10 (<i>i. e.</i><BR> देवीनाक) विरामोऽवसानम्, वर्णानामभावोऽवसानसंज्ञः स्यात्<BR> P. I. 4. 110; रवरवसानयोर्विसर्जनीयः VIII. 3. 15.<BR>—6 A pause.<BR>—7 The end of a verse, or the verse itself; एकावसानाद्व्यवसाना-ऋक्.<BR>—8 A place of dismounting from a horse.<BR>—9 A place (स्थान); resting place, residence; यमो ददात्यवसानमस्मै<BR> Rv. 10. 14. 9. अवसानं भवत्वत्र Mb. 5. 31. 19 ˚दर्श <i>a.</i><BR> looking at oneʼs place of destination. श्येनो नृचक्षा अवसानदर्शः Av. 7. 41. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानक
अवसानक <i>a.</i> Coming to an end, dying, perishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान्य
अवसान्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Belonging to the end of a verse; नमः श्लोकाय<BR> चावसान्याय Vāj. 16. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायः|अवसाय
अवसायः [अव-सो-घञ् P. III. 1. 141]<BR>—1 Conclusion, end, termination; destruction; शरवर्षैरवसायमाश्रयाशः Śi. 20. 72.<BR>—2 Remainder.<BR>—3 Completion.<BR>—4 Determination, resolution, decision, certainty. cf. अथावसायः शेषः<BR> स्यात् समासो निश्चयोऽपि च Med.<BR>—5 One who brings to an end; अवसायो भविष्यामि दुःखस्यास्य कदा न्वहम् । Bk. 6. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायक
अवसायक <i>a.</i> Destructive; अवद्यन्पत्रिणः शम्भोः सायकैरवसायकैः Ki. 15. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायिन्
अवसायिन् <i>a.</i> Residing, dwelling in; cf. अन्त्यावसायिन्,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0259-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
अवसित <i>p. p.</i> [सो-क्त]<BR>—1 Finished, ended, completed; अवसितो दर्शनार्थः M. 2; यूपवत्यवसिते<BR> क्रियाविधौ R. 11. 37; अवसितश्च पशुरसौ Dk. 91 it is all over with<BR> the brute; ˚मण्डनासि Ś. 4; वचस्यवसिते तस्मिन्ससर्ज गिरमात्मभूः<BR> Ku. 2. 53; अनवसितवचन एव मयि Dk. 103; Bk. 10. 6.<BR>—2 Known, understood; करामलकवद् विश्वं विज्ञानावसितं तव Bhāg. 2. 5. 3.<BR>—3 Well-cooked; matured.<BR>—4 Resolved, determined, ascertained.<BR>—5 Standing in a pause.<BR>—6 Stored, gathered (as grain).<BR>—7 Tied, fastened, bound; त्वयैव लोकेऽवसिताश्च सेतवः Bhāg. 4. 6. 44.<BR>—8 Gone.<BR>—9 Remaining, dwelling (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसितम्
अवसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A dwelling place; नवावसिते वैनमाहरेयुः Śat. Br.<BR>—2 Corn ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेय
अवसेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be determined, finished.<BR>—2 Perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्द्|अवस्कंद्
अवस्कन्द् €1 P.<BR>—1 To attack, storm, assault; overpower, overwhelm; छायामप्यवस्कन्दितुम्<BR> Mv. 3; प्रभुरिव मामवस्कन्दयितुम् <i>ibid.</i> to attack or insult;<BR> पुरीमवस्कन्द लुनीहि नन्दनम् Śi. 1. 51; स्नेहावस्कन्नहृदया<BR> Rām. affected.<BR>—2 To spring or leap down.<BR>—3 To pour out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दः|अवस्कन्द|अवस्कंदः
अवस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 Attacking; attack, assault; अवस्कन्दं करिष्यामि शिबिरस्याद्य दुष्करम्<BR> Mb. 10. 3. 27. ˚प्रदानम् Pt. 3. 39 leading an assault.<BR>—2 Descending; स नद्यवस्कन्दमुपास्पृशच्च Bk. 2. 11.<BR>—3 A camp (जिगीषूणाम् निवेशस्थानम् Halāy.).<BR>—4 (in law) Accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दनम्
अवस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 Attacking; attack, assault; अवस्कन्दं करिष्यामि शिबिरस्याद्य दुष्करम्<BR> Mb. 10. 3. 27. ˚प्रदानम् Pt. 3. 39 leading an assault.<BR>—2 Descending; स नद्यवस्कन्दमुपास्पृशच्च Bk. 2. 11.<BR>—3 A camp (जिगीषूणाम् निवेशस्थानम् Halāy.).<BR>—4 (in law) Accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दित|अवस्कंदित
अवस्कन्दित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Attacked,<BR>—2 Gone down, descended.<BR>—3 Refuted.<BR>—4 Bathed, bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दिन्|अवस्कंदिन्
अवस्कन्दिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attacking, assaulting; outraging; गौतमदारावस्कन्दिनम् Mv. 1.<BR>—2 Covering.<BR>—3 Leaping upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्न
अवस्कन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spilt.<BR>—2 Attacked, overpowered. Rām. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कॄ
अवस्कॄ €6 U. To scratch, butt against; रोधांसि धीरमवचस्करिरे<BR> महोक्षाः Śi. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करः|अवस्कर
अवस्करः [अवकीर्यते इत्यवस्करः, कॄ-अप् सुट् वचस्केऽवस्करः P. VI. 1. 148]<BR>—1 Ordure, excrement.<BR>—2 The privities (गुह्यदेश).<BR>—3 Dirt, sweepings (in general); गृहद्वाराशुचिस्थानरथ्यावस्करशोधनम्<BR> Nārada. तद्वितीर्य स्वसर्वस्वमात्मानमनवस्करम् । चिकीर्षामि महाबाहो … ॥<BR> Śiva B. 29. 36.<BR>—4 A place for faeces, dung-hill. अवस्करस्तु विष्ठायां गुह्ये … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवस्करमन्दिरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करमन्दिरम्
अवस्करः + -मन्दिरम् a privy, water-closet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करक|अवस्करकः
अवस्करक <i>a.</i> [अवस्करे भवः, वुन् P. IV. 3. 28] Existing in the ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करकः|अवस्करक
अवस्करक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An insect.<BR>—2 A sweeper, scavenger.<BR>—3 A brush, broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कव|अवस्कवः
अवस्कव <i>a.</i> Noxious, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कवः|अवस्कव
अवस्कव + .{@-वः@} A kind of worm; अवस्कवं व्यध्वरं क्रिमीन्वचसा जम्भयामसि Av. 2. 31. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कारः|अवस्कार
अवस्कारः A part of the elephantʼs face, apparently the protuberance<BR> in the middle of the face just between the eyes; Mātaṅga L. 5. 8, 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तात्
अवस्तात् <i>ind.</i> [अवरस्मिन् अवरस्मात् अवरमिंत्यर्थे अस्ताति अव<BR> आदेशः विभाषाऽवरस्य P. V. 3. 41]<BR>—1 Below, from below, downwards, hitherwards; ˚प्रपदन <i>a.</i> attained<BR> from below (as heaven &c.).<BR>—2 (used as a preposition) Under.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तु
अवस्तु <i>n.</i> [कुत्सितार्थे नञ्]<BR>—1 A worthless thing or matter; अवस्तुनिर्बन्धपरे कथं नु ते Ku. 5. 66<BR> intent on a bad object.<BR>—2 Unreality (of matter), insubstantiality; वस्तुन्यवस्त्वारोपोऽज्ञानम्<BR> attribution of unreality; नावस्तुनो वस्तुसिद्धिः; ˚ता, -त्वम् unreality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तॄ
अवस्तॄ €9 P. To cover, spread, overspread, overcast; प्रकम्पयन्गामवतस्तरे<BR> दिशः Ki. 14. 29 pervaded, filled; उरसि रसादवतस्तरे स्तनाभ्याम् Śi. 7. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तरणम्
अवस्तरणम् Spreading out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तारः|अवस्तार
अवस्तारः [अव-स्तॄ कर्मणि घञ् P. III. 3. 120]<BR>—1 A curtain.<BR>—2 A covering; a screen or wall of cloth around a tent, hence concealing<BR> or fabricating. cf. Kau. A. 2. 8.<BR>—3 A mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तीर्ण
अवस्तीर्ण <i>a.</i> Strewed, covered with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्त्र
अवस्त्र <i>a.</i> Without clothes, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्था
अवस्था €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To remain, stay, abide; तेन सह सुखमवतिष्ठन्ते K. 108;<BR> oft. with an adj.; विलोकयन्ती तावदवतस्थे 205; पादौ विष्टभ्य;<BR> क्षणं भद्रावतिष्ठस्व Bk. 8. 11 stay, wait; अनीत्वा पङ्कतां धूलिमुदकं<BR> नावतिष्ठते Śi. 2. 34.<BR>—2 To abide by, conform to, obey; न शासनेऽवास्थित यो गुरूणाम् Bk. 3. 14.<BR>—3 To live; क्षणमप्यवतिष्ठते श्वसन् यदि जन्तुर्ननु लाभवानसौ R. 8. 87.<BR>—4 To stand (still), make a halt, stop; न च शक्नोम्यवस्थातुम् Bg. 1. 30, 14. 23;<BR> R. 2. 31; Ku. 3. 42; Śi. 9. 83.<BR>—5 To stand, exist, chance to be.<BR>—6 To fall to, devolve on.<BR>—7 To enter; reach, attain to.<BR>—8 To stand apart, go off, withdraw.<BR>—9 To descend; go to.<BR>—10 To place (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्थापयति-ते) —1 To cause to stand<BR> or stop, station, keep, place; पश्चादवस्थापितवाहिनीकः R. 13. 66;<BR> स्कन्धावारमवस्थाप्य Dk. 174 having encamped; भिक्षापात्रं नागदन्तकेऽवस्थाप्य H. 1, 3.<BR>—2 To fix, settle; शक्योऽवस्थापयितुम् Mu. 1.<BR>—3 To establish, found; द्वैराज्यमवस्थापयितुकामोऽस्मि M. 5.<BR>—4 To compose, collect, steady, fix (as heart &c.); न शकोमि हृदयमवस्थापयितुम् U. 4.<BR>—5 To comfort, console; ततो निर्याय कौरव्य अवस्थाप्य च तद्बलम् Mb. 3. 16. 29.<BR>—6 To separate, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थः|अवस्थ
अवस्थः The membrum virile; अवस्थस्य क्नदीवतः Av. 7. 90. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्था
अवस्थः + .{@-स्था@} [अव-स्था-अङ्]<BR>—1 State, condition, situation; स्वामिनो महत्यवस्था वर्तते Pt. 1<BR> a critical state, distress; तदनु कथयेर्माधवीयावमस्थाम् Māl. 9. 26;<BR> तुल्यावस्थः स्वसुः कृतः R. 12. 80; तां तामवस्थां प्रतिपद्यमानम् 13. 5;<BR> ईदृशीमवस्थां प्रपन्नोऽस्मि Ś. 5; Ku. 2. 6; सर्व˚ Me. 110;<BR> अवस्था खलु नाम शत्रुमपि मित्रत्वे कल्पयति Pratijñā. 1.<BR> oft. in comp.; तदवस्थः Pt. 5 reduced to that state; एतद˚, बालावस्थः<BR> अधिपतिः V. 5; अन्त्यावस्था Pt. 4; so कामयमानावस्थो राजा Ś. 3;<BR> स्फुलिङ्गावस्थया वह्निः 7. 15; अन्तर्मदावस्थो द्विपेन्द्रः R. 2. 7<BR> rutting state.<BR>—2 Position,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">Page0261-1</a>]<BR> circumstance.<BR>—3 Period, stage (of life &c.); यौवन˚; वयोवस्थां तस्याः शृणुत Māl. 9. 29.<BR>—4 Form, appearance.<BR>—5 Degree, proportion.<BR>—6 Stability, fixity, as in अनवस्थ q. v.<BR>—7 Appearance in a court of law; कृतावस्थो धनैषिणा Ms. 8. 60.<BR>—8 The female organ of generation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवस्थान्तरम्, अवस्थचतुष्टयम्, अवस्थत्रयम्, अवस्थदशकम्, अवस्थद्वयम्, अवस्थषट्कम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थान्तरम्
अवस्थः + -अन्तरम् another or altered state; ˚रम् आरोपिता Ś. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थचतुष्टयम्
अवस्थः + -चतुष्टयम् the four periods or states of human life; <i>i. e.</i><BR> बाल्यम् (childhood); कौमारम् (youth); यौवनम् (manhood); and<BR> वार्धक्यम् (old age).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थत्रयम्
अवस्थः + -त्रयम् the three states; <i>i. e.</i> जागृति (waking); स्वप्न<BR> (dreaming), and सुषुप्ति (sound sleep).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थदशकम्
अवस्थः + -दशकम् the ten states of lovers; दृङ् मनः संगसङ्कल्पौ जागरः<BR> कृशताऽरतिः । ह्रीत्यागोन्मादमूर्छान्ता इत्यनङ्गदशा दश ॥ D. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थद्वयम्
अवस्थः + -द्वयम् the two states of life <i>i. e.</i> सुखम् and दुःखम्<BR> (happiness and misery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थषट्कम्
अवस्थः + -षट्कम् the six states of an action mentioned by Yāska; जायतेऽस्ति<BR> वर्धते विपरिणमतेऽपक्षीयते नश्यति Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थानम्
अवस्थानम्<BR>—1 Standing, remaining, residing, abiding, dwelling; पूर्वकृतावस्थानेन<BR> राजलोकेन K. 92; किमिह निवृत्त्यावस्थानम् Pt. 1; चतुर्मण्डलावस्थानेन <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 Situation, station, position; मधुर˚ दर्शनीयः Ś. 6.<BR>—3 Residence, abode, place; घनावस्थानैः K. 127.<BR>—4 Period of staying.<BR>—5 Support, योऽवस्थानमनुग्रहः Bhāg. 3. 27. 16.<BR>—6 Stability; अलब्धावस्थानः परिक्रामति Bhāg. 5. 26. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापनम्
अवस्थापनम् —1 Fixing, settling. Residence, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थायिन्
अवस्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Staying, residing, dwelling; पश्चादवस्थायि बलम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थित|अवस्थितः
अवस्थित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Remained, stayed; कथमियतं कालमवस्थिता मया विना भवती V. 4;<BR> remaining, standing firm or fixed; staying, abiding, lasting &c.; R. 6. 19;<BR> एवमवस्थिते K. 158 under these circumstances.<BR>—2 Firm of purpose, steady; रूपयौवनसम्पन्ना यस्मात्त्वमनवस्थिता<BR> Rām. 7. 30. 37; see अनवस्थित.<BR>—3 Engaged in prosecuting; following; abiding by; Ms. 8. 42, ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः Bg. 4. 23.<BR>—4 Resting with, dependent on; मयि सृष्टिर्हि लोकानां रक्षा युष्मास्ववस्थिता<BR> Ku. 2. 28; K. 344.<BR>—5 Settled, a matter of course; पितुरस्याः समीपनयनमवस्थितमेव Ś. 5.<BR>—6 Resolved; युद्धाय Pt. 1.<BR>—7 Ready, alert; ते कपिं तं समासाद्य तोरणस्थमवस्थितम् Rām. 5. 43. 27.<BR>—8 motionless (निश्चेष्ट); अवस्थितमसंभ्रान्तम् (माम्) Rām. 5. 58. 39.<BR>—9 Well-arranged; कपित्वमनवस्थितम् Rām. 5. 55. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थितिः|अवस्थिति
अवस्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Abiding, dwelling; भीमो दुर्योधनः कर्णो नाविन्दंस्तदवस्थितिम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 83. 23.<BR>—2 Residence, abode; अत्र कृतावस्थितिना धर्मेण K. 44.<BR>—3 Following, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्नात
अवस्नात <i>a.</i> (water) in which one has bathed; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्पर्तृ
अवस्पर्तृ <i>a.</i> Preserver, saviour; अवस्पर्तरधिवक्तारमस्मयुम् Rv. 2. 23. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्फूर्ज्
अवस्फूर्ज् To snort, fill with noise. Mb. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्फूर्जितम्
अवस्फूर्जितम् Roar, thunder, K. 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्फोटः|अवस्फोट
अवस्फोटः Appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्यति
अवस्यति Den. P. Ved. To seek favour or assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्यु
अवस्यु <i>a.</i> [अवः रक्षणं तदिच्छति क्यच् उन्] Ved. Desiring<BR> favour, help or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्वत्|अवस्वन्त्
अवस्वत् <i>a.</i> [अवो रक्षणमस्त्यस्य मतुप् मस्य वः] Defended, protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्यन्दनम्
अवस्यन्दनम् Trickling, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्रंसनम्
अवस्रंसनम् Dropping or falling down, falling off, a fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्रंसित
अवस्रंसित <i>a.</i> Burst, fallen down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्रस्
अवस्रस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Apt to fall down.<BR>—2 Burst, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्वन्
अवस्वन् €1 P. To sound, to smack the lips, make a noise in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्वन्य
अवस्वन्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Roaring, boisterous; अवस्वन्याय च नमः Vāj. 16. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह|अवहः
अवह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not carrying.<BR>—2 Having no stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहः|अवह
अवह + .{@-हः@} A kind of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहन्
अवहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike, beat off, hit, kill.<BR>—2 To destroy, remove; दुरितम्, क्षुधाम्, द्विषः &c.<BR>—3 To thresh (as rice); अवहत्य तण्डुलान् Dk. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहतिः|अवहति
अवहतिः <i>f.</i> Beating, threshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहननम्
अवहननम्<BR>—1 Threshing, beating off rice; अवहननायोलूखलम् Mbh.<BR>—2 The lungs; वपा वसावहननम् Y. 3. 94 (अवहननम् = फुप्फुसः Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातः|अवघात
अवघातः [अव हन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Striking.<BR>—2 Hurting, killing.<BR>—3 A violent or sharp blow, stroke or blow in general; कर्णावघातनिपुणेन<BR> च ताड्यमाना दूरीकृताः करिवरेण (भृङ्गाः) Nītipr. 2; अधरे दत्तदन्तावघाते S. D.<BR>—4 Threshing corn by bruising it with a wooden pestle in a mortar.<BR>—5 Unnatural or accidental death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातिन्
अवघातिन् <i>a.</i> Striking, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्
अवहस् €1 P. To deride, mock, laugh or scoff at, ridicule; स्थिताऽवहस्येव<BR> पुरं मघोनः Bk. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहसनम्
अवहसनम् Deriding; तच्चावहसनं प्राप्य सभारोहणदर्शने Mb. 1. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहासः|अवहास
अवहासः<BR>—1 Smiling, a smile.<BR>—2 A jest, joke, ridicule, यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोऽसि Bg. 11. 42.<BR>—3 Derision, scoffing; अवहासं ततो मुक्त्वा रावणो वाक्यमब्रवीत् Rām. 7. 18. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहास्य
अवहास्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be derided or ridiculed, ridiculous; कथं<BR> तु सर्वलोकस्य नावहास्या भवेमहि Mb. 7. 75. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्तः|अवहस्त
अवहस्तः [अवरं हस्तस्य एक˚ त˚] The back of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहा
अवहा €3 P. To leave, abandon रयिं न कश्चिन्ममृवाँ अवाहाः Rv. 1. 116. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहानिः
अवहानिः <i>f.</i> Loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहीन
अवहीन <i>p. p.</i> Abandoned, left; अवहीनाः कथाः Dk. 129 over,<BR> at an end; अस्मास्ववहीनेषु Ś. 2 we being left behind, having fallen in the rear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहालिका
अवहालिका A wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्था
अव(ब)हित्था, -त्थम्<BR>—1 Dissimulation in general.<BR>—2 Dissimulation or concealment of an internal feeling, regarded as one<BR> of the 33 subordinate feelings (व्याभिचारिभाव); भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था<BR> S. D.; or according to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां गोपनाय<BR> जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थम्; for ex. see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबहित्था
अव(ब)हित्था, -त्थम्<BR>—1 Dissimulation in general.<BR>—2 Dissimulation or concealment of an internal feeling, regarded as one<BR> of the 33 subordinate feelings (व्याभिचारिभाव); भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था<BR> S. D.; or according to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां गोपनाय<BR> जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थम्; for ex. see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्थम्
अव(ब)हित्था, -त्थम्<BR>—1 Dissimulation in general.<BR>—2 Dissimulation or concealment of an internal feeling, regarded as one<BR> of the 33 subordinate feelings (व्याभिचारिभाव); भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था<BR> S. D.; or according to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां गोपनाय<BR> जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थम्; for ex. see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबहित्थम्
अव(ब)हित्था, -त्थम्<BR>—1 Dissimulation in general.<BR>—2 Dissimulation or concealment of an internal feeling, regarded as one<BR> of the 33 subordinate feelings (व्याभिचारिभाव); भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था<BR> S. D.; or according to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां गोपनाय<BR> जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थम्; for ex. see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृ
अवहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To take away, put or lay aside; place down; अर्भकं कस्मादवहृतं भवति Nir.<BR>—2 To hold, contain; कुडवमवहरति Sk.<BR>—3 To throw or knock down (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहरणम्
अवहरणम्<BR>—1 Taking away, removing.<BR>—2 Throwing away.<BR>—3 Stealing, plundering.<BR>—4 Removing from the battle-field to the camp.<BR>—5 Re-delivery.<BR>—6 Temporary suspension of hostilities, truce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारः|अवहार
अवहारः [अवहृ-कर्तरि ण P. III. 1. 141]<BR>—1 A thief.<BR>—2 A shark, a water elephant.<BR>—3 Taking away the wealth of invited Brāhmaṇas.<BR>—4 Temporary cessation of hostilities, suspension of arms, truce; एवं<BR> राजन्नवहारो बभूव Mb. 5. 182. 30, 1. 190. 35.<BR>—5 Removing to the camp; ततोऽवहारं सैन्यानां तव तेषां च भारत Mb.<BR>—6 Cessation, stop (in general).<BR>—7 Summoning, inviting.<BR>—8 Any object fit to be brought near (उपनेतव्यम्).<BR>—9 Apostacy, abandoning a sect or caste.<BR>—10 Redelivery, redeeming.<BR>—11 One who snatches away; न जीवस्यावहारो मां करोति सुखिनं यमः Bk. 6. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारक|अवहारकः
अवहारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One taking away from one place to another.<BR>—2 One who desists from fighting.<BR>—3 Preventing, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारकः|अवहारक
अवहारक + .{@-कः@} A shark, a marine monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार्य|अवहार्य्य|अवहार्य्यः
अवहार्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be taken away or removed.<BR>—2 Finable, punishable; अवहार्यो भवेच्चेव सान्वयः षट्शतं दमम् Ms. 8. 198.<BR>—3 What one is forced to restore or redeem; आधिश्चोपनिधिश्चोभौ न कालात्ययमर्हतः ।<BR> अवहार्यौ भवेतां तौ दीर्घकालमवस्थितौ ॥ Ms. 8. 145.<BR>—4 To be completed,<BR>—5 Recoverable, redeemable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृत
अवहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Taken off, back or away.<BR>—2 Seized, stolen.<BR>—3 Fined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलः|अवहेल|अवहेलं
अवहेलः, -ला<BR> Disrespect, disdain, contempt, disregard; सावहेलम् K. 244;<BR> अवहेलां कुटज मधुकरे मा गाः Bv. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेला
अवहेलः, -ला<BR> Disrespect, disdain, contempt, disregard; सावहेलम् K. 244;<BR> अवहेलां कुटज मधुकरे मा गाः Bv. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलनम्
अवहेलनम्, -ना<BR> Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलना
अवहेलनम्, -ना<BR> Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलित|अवहेलितं
अवहेलित <i>a.</i> Disregarded, slighted, contemned; किमिति बकैरवहेलितानभिज्ञैः Bv. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलितम्
अवहेलित + .{@-तम्@} Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह्वर|अवह्वरः
अवह्वर <i>a.</i> [अव-ह्व-अच्] Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह्वरः|अवह्वर
अवह्वर + .{@-रः@} A crooked way; (fig.) deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह्वे
अवह्वे To call down from; विशो अद्य मरुतामवह्वये Rv. 5. 56. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकिन्
अवाकिन् Ved. Not speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्क
अवाक्क Ved. Speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकॄ
अवाकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To strew, pour upon; sprinkle with.<BR>—2 To ward off, remove; विश्वा द्वेषांसि जहि चाव चा कृधि Rv. 8. 53. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकरः|अवाकर
अवाकरः A mint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्ष|अवाक्षः
अवाक्ष <i>a.</i> [अवनतान्यक्षाणि इन्द्रियाणि यस्य] A guardian, keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्र|अवाग्रं
अवाग्र <i>a.</i> [अवनतमग्रमस्य] Having the head bent down,<BR> stooping, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Speechless, dumb. <i>n.</i> Brahman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवाङ्मनसगोचर, अवाक्छ्रुति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मनसगोचर
अवाच् + -मनसगोचर <i>a.</i> beyond the power of thought and words, indescribable<BR> and inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्छ्रुति
अवाच् + -श्रुति <i>a.</i> deaf and dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not proper to be addressed; अवाच्यो दीक्षितो नाम्ना यवीयानपि यो भवेत् Ms. 2. 128.<BR>—2 Improper to be uttered; vile, bad; अवाच्यं वदतो जिह्वा कथं न<BR> पतिता तव Rām.; ˚वादांश्च बहून् वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः Bg. 2. 36.<BR>—3 Not distinctly expressed, not expressible in words; ˚ता, ˚त्वम्<BR> impropriety; reproach, calumny; दुर्लभा सत्स्ववाच्यता Ki. 11. 53.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवाच्यदेशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यदेशः|अवाच्यदेश
अवाच्य + -देशः ‘the unspeakable place’, the vulva (योनि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्छिद्
अवाच्छिद्^1 To tear away or out from.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20171110. note: error copied from MW..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्च्|अवांच्
अवाञ्च् <i>a.</i> [अवाञ्चति अव-अञ्च्-क्विप्]<BR>—1 Turned downwards, bent down, stooping; कुर्वन्तमित्यतिभरेण नगानवाचः<BR> Śi. 6. 79; वनान्यवाञ्चीव चकार संहतिः Ki. 14. 34.<BR>—2 Being or situated below, lower than (with abl.) यदवाक् पृथिव्याः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 8. 3.<BR>—3 Headlong, looking downwards.<BR>—4 South. <i>m., n.</i> Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्ची
अवाञ्च् + .{@-ची@}<BR>—1 The south.<BR>—2 The lower region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्चित
अवाञ्चित <i>a.</i> Turned, bent downwards; तृणवाञ्च्छया मुहुरवाञ्चितान् Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्
अवाक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Downwards; ऊर्ध्वतिर्यगवाक्सर्गो रुद्रसर्गस्तथैव च Bhāg. 12. 12. 11.<BR>—2 Southern, southward.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवाग्ज्ञानम्, अवाक्पुष्पी, अवाग्भागः, अवाग्भव, अवाङ्मुख, अवाक्छाखः, अवाक्छिरस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्ज्ञानम्
अवाक् + -ज्ञानम् disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्पुष्पी
अवाक् + -पुष्पी [अवाक् अधोमुखं पुष्पमस्याः] N. of a plant Anethum Sowa<BR> Roxb (अधःपुष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्भागः|अवाग्भाग
अवाक् + -भागः the part below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्भव
अवाक् + -भव <i>a.</i> southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मुख|अवाङ्मुखं|अवाङ्मुखः
अवाक् + -मुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 looking downwards, with the face hung downwards; अवाङ्मुखस्योपरि<BR> पुष्पवृष्टिः R. 2. 60; तस्थुस्तेऽवाङ्मुखाः सर्वे 15. 78.<BR>—2 headlong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मुखः|अवाङ्मुख|अवाङ्मुखं
अवाक् + -मुख + .({@-खः@}) N. of a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्छाखः
अवाक् + -शाखः [अवाच्यः शाखा अस्य] ‘having the branches turned downwards’,<BR> epithet of the sacred fig-tree (अश्वत्थ) ऊर्ध्वमूलोऽवाक्शाखः Kaṭh. 2. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्छिरस्
अवाक् + -शिरस् <i>a.</i> having the head hung downwards; स मूढो नरकं<BR> याति कालसूत्रमवाक्शिराः Ms. 3. 249, 8. 94, 11. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचीन|अवाचीनं
अवाचीन <i>a.</i> [अवाच्-ख विभाषाञ्चादेरदिक्स्त्रियाम् P. V. 4. 8]<BR>—1 Downward, headlong.<BR>—2 Southern.<BR>—3 Descended,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">Page0263-1</a>]<BR> gone down.<BR>—4 See अवाक्शिरस्; दुर्योधनमवाचीनं राज्यकामुकमातुरम् Mb. 8. 8. 17.<BR>—5 Base, evil (deed); यस्मै देवाः प्रयच्छन्ति पुरुषाय पराभवम् ।<BR> बुद्धिं तस्यापकर्षन्ति सोऽवाचीनानि पश्यति ॥ Mb. 5. 34. 81.<BR>—6 Unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाञ्चित
अवाञ्चित <i>a.</i> Bent, low, dropping down (अवगलित). बभूव<BR> पक्ष्मान्तरवाञ्चिताश्रुः Bu. C. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य <i>a.</i> Southern, southernly. cf. Śiva B. 6. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाजिन्
अवाजिन् <i>m.</i> A bad horse (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अवात <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Windless, not shaken by wind; मिहं कृण्वन्त्यवाताम् Rv. 1. 38. 7.<BR>—2 Not breathing the air.<BR>—3 Not exposed to, or not dried up by wind; fresh; शुष्मा इन्द्रमवाता<BR> अह्रुतासवः Rv. 1. 52. 4.<BR>—4 Unattacked, unconquered (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवातम्
अवात + .{@-तम@} The windless atmosphere; आनीदवातं स्वधया तदेकम् Rv. 10. 129. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवातल
अवातल <i>a.</i> Not flatulent; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवादिन्
अवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who is no speaker or disputer.<BR>—2 One who does not prosecute or bring any action, peace-loving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्
अवान् €2 P. [अव-अन्] To breath or inhale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवानः|अवान|अवानं
अवानः Breathing, inhaling; see अनवान also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
अवान <i>a.</i> [अव-अन्-अच्] Dried, dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तर|अवांतर|अवान्तरं
अवान्तर <i>a.</i> [अवगतमन्तरं मध्यं प्रा˚ स˚]<BR>—1 Situated or standing between; see compounds.<BR>—2 Included, involved.<BR>—3 Subordinate, secondary.<BR>—4 not closely connected, extraneous, extra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवान्तरदिश्, अवान्तरदिशा, अवान्तरदेशः, अवान्तरवाक्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तरदिश्
अवान्तर + -दिश्, -दिशा an intermediate quarter (such as the आग्नेयी, ऐशानी,<BR> नैरृती and वायवी). दिशोऽवान्तरदिशः T. Up. 1. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तरदिशा
अवान्तर + -दिश्, -दिशा an intermediate quarter (such as the आग्नेयी, ऐशानी,<BR> नैरृती and वायवी). दिशोऽवान्तरदिशः T. Up. 1. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तरदेशः|अवान्तरदेश
अवान्तर + -देशः a place situated between (two others), an intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तरवाक्यम्
अवान्तर + -वाक्यम्<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A sentence formed by dropping some word or words in the whole<BR> sentence; न च महावाक्ये सति अवान्तरवाक्यं प्रमाणं भवति ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 25.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A group of words which appear to form a complete sentence, but<BR> form only a part of a complete sentence (<i>i. e.</i> a महावाक्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तराम्|अवांतराम्
अवान्तराम् <i>ind.</i> [अवान्तर बा˚ आसु] Between (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्
अवाप् €5 U.<BR>—1 To get, obtain, secure, gain; तमवाप्य सप्ततिम् R. 3. 33; दीर्घमायुरवाप्नुयात्<BR> Ms. 4. 76; कीर्तिम्, फलम्, कामम् &c.; पुत्रं सम्राजमवाप्नुहि Ś. 4. 6.<BR>—2 To reach, go to, enter.<BR>—3 To suffer, incur, receive, meet with; निन्दामवाप्नोति Ms. 5. 161;<BR> so दोषम् &c.; मृत्युमवाप्रोति meets with death; नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि<BR> Bg. 2. 38, 53. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to obtain anything; अवापितो जङ्गमलेखलक्ष्मीम् N. 8. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्त
अवाप्त <i>p. p.</i> Got, obtained, received; अनवाप्तचक्षुःफलोऽसि Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तव्य
अवाप्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i> Attainable; नानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यम् Bg. 3. 22; R. 10. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तिः|अवाप्ति
अवाप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Obtaining, getting; तपःकिलेदं तदवाप्तिसाधनम् Ku. 5. 64.<BR>—2 (Arith.) A quotient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य <i>pot. p.</i> Attainable. ज्येष्ठता च निवर्तेत ज्येष्ठावाप्यं<BR> च यद्धनम् Ms. 11. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य <i>a.</i> [न˚ त˚] Uncut, not to be cut (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापित
अवापित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not sown (as grain) but planted.<BR>—2 Not cut (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाम
अवाम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not left, right.<BR>—2 Favourable, not adverse.<BR>—3 Inauspicious, inelegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवायः|अवाय
अवायः [अव-इ-घञ्]<BR>—1 A limb.<BR>—2 Giving way, conceding, complying with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारः|अवार|अवारं
अवारः, -रम्<BR> [न वार्यते जलेन वृ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 The near bank of a river; नास्य द्वीपः कुतः पारो नावारः संप्रदृश्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 224. 21.<BR>—2 This side; यो वै संवत्सरस्यावरं पारं च वेद Ait. Br. ˚तस्<BR> <i>ind.</i> to this side; पयो दुहाना व्रतनीरवारतः Rv. 10. 65. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवारपारः, अवारपारीण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारम्
अवारः, -रम्<BR> [न वार्यते जलेन वृ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 The near bank of a river; नास्य द्वीपः कुतः पारो नावारः संप्रदृश्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 224. 21.<BR>—2 This side; यो वै संवत्सरस्यावरं पारं च वेद Ait. Br. ˚तस्<BR> <i>ind.</i> to this side; पयो दुहाना व्रतनीरवारतः Rv. 10. 65. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवारपारः, अवारपारीण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपारः|अवारपार
अवारः + -पारः The ocean (राष्ट्रावारपाराद्धरवौ P. IV. 2. 93, अवारपारात्यन्तानुकामं<BR> गामी V. 2. 11.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपारीण|अवारपारीणः
अवारः + -पारीण <i>a.</i> [अवारपारे गच्छति, ख P. IV. 2. 93]<BR>—1 belonging to the ocean.<BR>—2 crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारीण|अवारीणः
अवारीण <i>a.</i> [अवारं गच्छति, ख P. IV. 2. 93] Crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य|अवार्य्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य <i>a.</i> Being on the near side; अवार्याय च नमः Vāj. 16. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारण
अवारण <i>a.</i> Insufferable, not to be remedied, irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारणम्
अवारण + .{@-णम्@} Not warding off or preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारणीय
अवारणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unable to be warded off (as enemies).<BR>—2 Treating of incurable diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारित|अवारितं
अवारित <i>a.</i> Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारितम्
अवारित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without obstacles, at pleasure; Mb. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवारितद्वार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारितद्वार
अवारित + -द्वार <i>a.</i> having open doors; अवारितद्वारतया तिरश्चामन्तःपुरे<BR> तस्य निविश्य राज्ञः N. 3. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य|अवार्य्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य, अवारयितव्य <i>a.</i> Not to be warded or kept off,<BR> irremediable; रववित्रासितवारणादवार्यः Ki. 13. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारयितव्य
अवार्य, अवारयितव्य <i>a.</i> Not to be warded or kept off,<BR> irremediable; रववित्रासितवारणादवार्यः Ki. 13. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारिका
अवारिका [नास्ति वारि यत्र] N. of a plant (धन्याक). Coriandrum<BR> Sativum; (Mar. घने).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावटः|अवावट
अवावटः The son of a woman by any man (of the same caste) other<BR> than her first husband; द्वितीयेन तु यः पित्रा सवर्णायां प्रजायते ।<BR> अवावट इति ख्यातः शूद्रधर्मा स जातितः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावन्
अवावन् <i>m.</i> विड्वनोरनुनासिकस्यात् [Said to be fr. ओण् <i>f.</i><BR> P. VI. 4. 41] A thief, stealing away. अवावा ब्राह्मणी Sāṅ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवासस्
अवासस् <i>a.</i> Unclothed, naked. ━<i>m.</i> N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तव|अवास्तवं
अवास्तव (-विक) <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Unreal, unsubstantial.<BR>—2 Unfounded, irrational (as an argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तविक
अवास्तव (-विक) <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Unreal, unsubstantial.<BR>—2 Unfounded, irrational (as an argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तु
अवास्तु <i>a.</i> Ved. Having no abode, homeless; अवास्तुमेनमस्वर्गमप्रजसं<BR> करोति Av. 12. 5. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाहन
अवाहन <i>a.</i> Having no carriage, not driving in a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाह्य
अवाह्य <i>a.</i> Not fit to be borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अवि <i>a.</i> Ved. [अव्-इन्] Favourable, kindly or favourably disposed.<BR> अविं वृधाम शग्मियं सखायं वरुणम् Av. 5. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविः|अवि
अवि + .{@-विः@}<BR>—1 A sheep; (<i>f.</i> also in this sense); जीनकार्मुकवस्तावीन् Ms. 11. 138, 3. 6, 12. 55.<BR>—2 The Sun.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (अर्क).<BR>—4 A goat.<BR>—5 A mountain.<BR>—6 Air, wind.<BR>—7 A woollen blanket (of the skin of mice).<BR>—8 A blanket, shawl in general.<BR>—9 A woollen strainer (for Soma juice).<BR>—10 A master.<BR>—11 A wall, enclosure. —12 A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविः|अवि
