अविका
अविकः + .{@-का@} An ewe. सर्वाहमस्मि रोमशा गन्धारीणामिवाविका Rv. 1. 125. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकम्
अविकः + .{@-कम्@} A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविता
अविता An ewe, a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकच
अविकच <i>a.</i> Closed, shut (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकत्थ
अविकत्थ <i>a.</i> Not boasting, not bragging or vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकत्थन
अविकत्थन <i>a.</i> One who does not boast, not vaunting सत्यप्रतिज्ञेऽप्यविकत्थनेऽपि<BR> R. 14. 73; विद्वांसोऽविकत्थना भवन्ति Mu. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल
अविकल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unimpaired, not defective, entire, perfect, whole, all; तानिन्द्रियाण्यविकलानि<BR> Bh. 2. 40; Pt. 5. 26; ˚लम् फलम् Me. 36; ˚शरच्चन्द्रमधुरः Māl. 2. 11<BR> full, full-orbed; ˚इन्द्रियः K. 35, 71; Mv. 2. 16, 4. 29; ˚लमरक्षत्<BR> Mv. 5. 5 entirely, completely; यल्लोकेष्वविकलमाप्तमाधिपत्यम् Ki. 18. 36<BR> entire, supreme.<BR>—2 Regular, orderly; consistent, not discordant; कलमविकलतालं गायकैर्बोधहेतोः Śi. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्प|अविकल्पः
अविकल्प <i>a.</i> Unchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्पः|अविकल्प
अविकल्प + .{@-ल्पः@}<BR>—1 Absence of doubt<BR>—2 Absence of option or alternative.<BR>—3 Positive act or precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्पम्
अविकल्प + .{@-ल्पम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without doubt, unhesitatingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार|अविकारः
अविकार <i>a.</i> Immutable, unchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकारः|अविकार
अविकार + .{@-रः@} Immutability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकारिन्
अविकारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unchangeable, invariable; Mb.<BR>—2 Faithful; स्थाने युद्धे च कुशलानभीरूनविकारिणः (गुल्माश्च स्थापयेत्) Ms. 7. 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार्य|अविकार्य्य
अविकार्य <i>a.</i> Invariable अविकार्योऽयमुच्यते Bg. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृत
अविकृत <i>a.</i> Unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृतिः|अविकृति
अविकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Absence of change.<BR>—2 (In Sāṅ. Phil.) The inanimate principle called प्रकृति, regarded<BR> as the material cause of the universe; मूलप्रकृतिरविकृतिः Sāṅ. K. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रिय
अविक्रिय <i>a.</i> Unchangeable, immutable; देशे देशे गुणेष्वेवमवस्थास्त्वमविक्रियः R. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रियम्
अविक्रिय + .{@-यम्@} Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रियत्वम्
अविक्रिय + .{@-त्वम्@} Unchangeableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रियात्मक
अविक्रियात्मक <i>a.</i> (Vedānta) Whose nature is unchangeable. दृशिस्तु<BR> शुद्धोऽहमविक्रियात्मकः Mukti. Up. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रम|अविक्रमः
अविक्रम <i>a.</i> Powerless, feeble; विपदोऽभिभवन्त्यविक्रमं रहयत्यापदुपेतमायतिः Ki. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रमः|अविक्रम
अविक्रम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Cowardice, timidity.<BR>—2 Non-prohibition of the change of Visarga into an Ūṣman; Rv. Pr. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रान्त|अविक्रांत
अविक्रान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unsurpassed.<BR>—2 Feeble, powerless.<BR>—3 See अविक्रमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लमः|अविक्लम
अविक्लमः Absence of fatigue, vigour, freshness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षत
अविक्षत <i>a.</i> Unimpaired, uninjured; unhurt, whole, entire; विकेतुः<BR> प्रतिदेयं तत्तस्मिन्नेवाह्नयविक्षतम् Smṛti. अविक्षते तत्र मयात्मसात्कृते Ki. 14. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षित
अविक्षित <i>a.</i> Unimpaired, unhurt; undiminished (Ved.). cf. also<BR> रक्षोगणं क्षिप्तुमविक्षितात्मा Bk. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षित्
अविक्षित् <i>m.</i> N. of a king, son of Kuru; Mb. 1. 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप
अविक्षिप <i>a.</i> [आकोशे च अच्कावशक्तौ P. VI. 2. 157-8.] Unable<BR> to distribute or dispense (आक्रोशार्थे), (विक्षेप्तुं न शक्तः or यो न विक्षिपति);<BR> not distributing or badly distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप्त
अविक्षिप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not thrown away.<BR>—2 Attentive, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षोभ्य
अविक्षोभ्य <i>a.</i> Invincible, that which cannot be disturbed; अविक्षोभ्याणि<BR> रक्षांसि सा विधूयोत्पतिष्यति Rām. 6. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविखण्डित
अविखण्डित <i>a.</i> Undisturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगत
अविगत <i>a.</i> Not gone off, retained, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगम|अविगमः
अविगम <i>a.</i> Unseparated, unremoved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगमः|अविगम
अविगम + .{@-मः@} Non-separation, association, inherence, presence, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगान
अविगान, -अविगीत <i>a.</i><BR> Without discord; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगीत|अविगीतं
अविगान, -अविगीत <i>a.</i><BR> Without discord; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्नः|अविग्न
अविग्नः N. of a fruit-tree (करमर्दक; Mar. करवंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्रह|अविग्रहः
अविग्रह <i>a.</i> [नास्ति विग्रहो यस्य]<BR>—1 Bodiless, incorporeal; epithet of the Supreme Being (who has no body).<BR>—2 Not known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्रहः|अविग्रह
अविग्रह + .{@-हः@} (In gram.) A compound the sense of which cannot be expressed<BR> by its constituent parts separately (नित्यसमास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघात|अविघातः
अविघात <i>a.</i> Unimpeded, unobstructed; ˚गति <i>a.</i> unobstructed<BR> in oneʼs course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघातः|अविघात
अविघात + .{@-तः@} Non-destruction. ऐश्वर्यादविघातः Sāṅ. K. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्न
अविघ्न <i>a.</i> Unobstructed, free from impediments; ˚कियोपलम्भाय Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्नम्
अविघ्न + .{@-घ्नम्@} Freedom from obstacle or impediment, welfare (this word<BR> is usually neuter, though विघ्न is <i>m.</i>); साधयाम्यहमविघ्नमस्तु<BR> ते R. 11. 91; अविघ्नमस्तु ते स्थेयाः पितेव धुरि पुत्रिणाम् R. 1. 91;<BR> अविघ्नमस्तु सावित्र्याः प्रदाने दुहितुस्तव Mb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविघ्नकरणव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्नकरणव्रतम्
अविघ्न + -करणव्रतम् N. of a particular rite on the fourth day of Phālguna. Varāha P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचक्षण
अविचक्षण <i>a.</i> Ignorant; अदत्त्वा तु य एतेभ्यः पूर्वं भुङ्क्तेऽविचक्षणः Ms. 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचाचल
अविचाचल, -लि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not staggering or fluctuating, standing firmly.<BR> खीला अविचाचला ये Av. 10. 8. 4. ध्रुवस्तिष्ठाविचाचलिः Rv. 10. 173. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचाचलि
अविचाचल, -लि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not staggering or fluctuating, standing firmly.<BR> खीला अविचाचला ये Av. 10. 8. 4. ध्रुवस्तिष्ठाविचाचलिः Rv. 10. 173. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचार|अविचारः
अविचार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Void of judgment, undiscriminating, ill-judging, unwise.<BR>—2 Unhesitating, prompt.<BR>—3 Having spies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारः|अविचार
अविचार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Absence of judgment, indiscretion, error, folly.<BR>—2 Promptitude.<BR>—3 A country fit for the grazing of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारणीय
अविचारणीय <i>a.</i> Not to be called in question; आज्ञा गुरूणां ह्यविचारणीया R. 14. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारित|अविचारितः
अविचारित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ill-judged, not well thought out or considered.<BR>—2 Determined, certain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविचारितनिर्णयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारितनिर्णयः|अविचारितनिर्णय
अविचारित + -निर्णयः a prejudice, prejudiced opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारिन्
अविचारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unthinking. inconsiderate, indiscreet.<BR>—2 Prompt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचालित
अविचालित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unmoved, unshaken.<BR>—2 Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचिन्त्य
अविचिन्त्य <i>a.</i> Not to be comprehended or conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचृत्य
अविचृत्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not to be loosened. यं ते देवी निरृतिरावबन्ध<BR> पाशं ग्रीवास्वविचृत्यम् Vāj. 12. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छिन्न|अविच्छिन्नं|अविछिन्न
अविच्छिन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not separated, undivided, having all along or over; हेमजालैरविच्छिन्ना<BR> Rām. 5. 6. 35.<BR>—2 Continuous, uninterrupted; ˚संताना संततिः K. 65. अन्वमीयत<BR> कल्याणं तस्याविच्छिन्नसंततिः R. 17. 11.<BR>—3 Ordinary, common; न विशेषेण गन्तव्यमविच्छिन्नेन वा पुनः Mb. 12. 152. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छेद|अविच्छेदः|अविछेद
अविच्छेद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uninterrupted.<BR>—2 Undivided, entire, whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छेदः|अविच्छेद|अविछेद
अविच्छेद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Entirety, wholeness; यज्ञस्याविच्छेदाय तद् व्रतम् Av. 9. 6. 38.<BR>—2 Connection, continuity; गणैरविच्छेदनिरुद्धमाबभौ Ki. 14. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्युत
अविच्युत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not deviated from, observed or followed strictly; यथाविधानेन पठन्सामगायमविच्युतम् Y. 3. 112<BR>—2 Eternal, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजात
अविजात <i>a.</i> Ved. Not having brought forth, having no offspring; Vāj. 30. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजातीय
अविजातीय <i>a.</i> Of the same kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञ|अविज्ञः
अविज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ignorant, untaught; प्रबोधयति माऽविज्ञं Bhāg. 4. 28. 20.<BR>—2 Clumsy, stupid, awkward; ˚ता ignorance, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञात
अविज्ञात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unknown; यदधीतमविज्ञातम् Mbh. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Unintelligible, doubtful, indistinct.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविज्ञातगद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञातगद
अविज्ञात + -गद <i>a.</i> Ved. Speaking in an unintelligible way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञातृ
अविज्ञातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not knowing. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञातृता
अविज्ञातृ + .({@-ता@}) The Supreme Being (परमेश्वर).<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu; अविज्ञाता सहस्रांशुः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञेय|अविज्ञेयं|अविज्ञेयः
अविज्ञेय <i>a.</i> Undistinguishable, not to be recognized or known,<BR> unknowable. सूक्ष्मत्वात्तदविज्ञेयम् Bg. 13. 15; अप्रतर्क्यमविज्ञेयं<BR> प्रसुप्तमिव सर्वतः Ms. 1. 5, 12. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञेयः|अविज्ञेय|अविज्ञेयं
अविज्ञेय + .{@-यः@} The Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविडीनम्
अविडीनम् A direct flight of birds (पक्षिणामाभिमुख्याभिगमनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथ|अवितथं
अवितथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not false, true; तदवितथमवादीर्यन्मम त्वं प्रियेति Śi. 11. 33;<BR> अवितथा वितथा सखि मा गिरः Śi. 6. 18.<BR>—2 Realised, not fruitless; अवितथफलाः स्वप्नाः K. 65; कुरु गुरुवचनमवितथम्<BR> K. 178; चकारावितथां भ्रातुः प्रतिज्ञाम् R. 15. 95, 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथम्
अवितथ + .{@-थम्@} Truth; अवितथमाह प्रियंवदा Ś. 3, P. is right, what<BR> P. says is right; Ve. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथम्
अवितथ + .{@-थम्@} <i>ind.</i> Not falsely, according to truth; य आवृणोत्यवितथं<BR> ब्रह्मणा श्रवणावुभौ Ms. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथा
अवितथ + .{@-था@} N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितर्कित
अवितर्कित <i>a.</i> Unforeseen; Rām. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितर्क्य
अवितर्क्य <i>a.</i> That which cannot be inferred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितारिन्
अवितारिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not doing any harm, harmless (अनपायिन्).<BR>—2 Not departing, remaining. मुमेधामवितारिणीम् Rv. 8. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितृ
अवितृ <i>a.</i> A protector, favourer; त्रातारमिन्द्रमवितारमिन्द्रम्<BR> Mahānār. Up. 20. 3; Mb. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्त
अवित्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not famous, unknown.<BR>—2 Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्ति|अवित्तिः
अवित्ति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not obtaining or getting.<BR>—2 Unwise. foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्तिः|अवित्ति
अवित्ति + .{@-त्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Not finding, getting, or possessing,<BR>—2 Want of wisdom.<BR>—3 Poverty; अवित्तेः संकल्पान् Av. 16. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यजः|अवित्यज|अवित्यजं
अवित्यजः, -जम्<BR> Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यजम्
अवित्यजः, -जम्<BR> Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथुर
अविथुर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not separated, united (Ved. for अविधुर)<BR>—2 Not staggering, firm; Rv. 1. 87. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथ्या
अविथ्या [अवये हिता, अवि थ्यन्, अजाविभ्यां थ्यन् P. V. 1. 8] N. of<BR> the plant अजथ्या (Mar. पिवळी जुई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद
अविद <i>ind.</i> Alas! Oh! Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद
अविद <i>a.</i> Ignorant, not knowing; अविदो भूरितमसो Bhāg. 3. 10. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदग्ध
अविदग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unlearned, inexperienced, stupid.<BR>—2 Not well burnt, undigested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदाहिन्
अविदाहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Imperfectly digested, producing heart-burn.<BR>—2 Not burning or afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदस्य
अविदस्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Unceasing, inexhaustible, perennial, perpetual;<BR> धाता रयिमविदस्यं सुदासाम् Rv. 7. 39. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0265-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदासिन्
अविदासिन् <i>a.</i> Perennial; निधेहि रक्षायोगेन हृदे मामविदासिनि<BR> Bhāg. 8. 24. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदित|अविदितः
अविदित <i>a.</i> Unknown; ˚गतयामा रात्रिः U. 1. 27 the watches<BR> of which stole away (glided imperceptibly away).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदितः|अविदित
अविदित + .{@-तः@} The Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदीधयु
अविदीधयु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not delaying or hesitating; दातारमविदीधयुम् Rv. 4. 31. 7.<BR>—2 Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूर
अविदूर <i>a.</i> Not distant, near, contiguous; तद्दुकूलादविदूरमौलिः Ku. 7. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूरम्
अविदूर + .{@-रम्@} Proximity, vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूरम्
अविदूर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Near to, not far from; so अविदूरेण, अविदूरात्,<BR> -दूरतः -विदूरे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूषक
अविदूषक <i>a.</i> Innocent; अहितं चापि पुरुषं न हिंस्युरविदूषकम्<BR> Rām. 1. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूसम्
अविदूसम् <i>n.</i> Sheep's milk; P. IV. 2. 36; Vārt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्ध|अविद्धः
अविद्ध <i>a.</i> Unpierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धः|अविद्ध
अविद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} A Yavana, because his ears are not pierced. (Mar. अविन्ध.)<BR> प्रतिबध्नास्यविद्धानामध्वानमकुतोभयः Śiva B. 18. 54.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविद्धकर्णा, अविद्धकर्णी, अविद्धदृश्, अविद्धनस्, अविद्धवर्चस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धकर्णा
अविद्ध + -कर्णा, -कर्णी [अविद्धः अच्छिद्रः पर्णरूपः कर्णोऽस्याः] N. of<BR> a plant (पाठा) Cissampelos Hexaudra (Mar. पहाडमूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धकर्णी|अविद्धकर्ण्णी
अविद्ध + -कर्णा, -कर्णी [अविद्धः अच्छिद्रः पर्णरूपः कर्णोऽस्याः] N. of<BR> a plant (पाठा) Cissampelos Hexaudra (Mar. पहाडमूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धदृश्
अविद्ध + -दृश् <i>a.</i> all-seeing; अविद्धदृक्साक्ष्युभयं तदीक्षते Bhāg. 8. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धनस्
अविद्ध + -नस् <i>a.</i> Having the nose not bored (said of a bull).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धवर्चस्|अविद्धवर्च्चस्
अविद्ध + -वर्चस् <i>a.</i> of unimpaired glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्य|अविद्यः
अविद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not educated, unlearned, foolish, unwise, अविद्यानां तु सर्वेषामीहात<BR> श्चेद्धनं भवेत् Ms. 9. 205; also अविद्यक <i>a.</i> Mb. 5. 160. 64.<BR>—2 Not pertaining to knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्या
अविद्य + .{@-द्या@}<BR>—1 Ignorance, folly, want of learning. अविद्यायामन्तरे वर्तमानाः<BR> Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 8.<BR>—2 Spiritual ignorance; Av. 11. 8. 23; Vāj. 40. 12, 14.<BR>—3 Illusion, illusion personified or Māyā (a term frequently occurring<BR> in Vedānta; by means of this illusion one perceives the universe, which<BR> does not really exist, as inherent in Brahman which alone really exists).<BR> The term appears also in the systems of Gautama, Patañjali, Kapila, where<BR> it has different bearings; (with Buddhists) ignorance together with non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्यामय
अविद्यामय <i>a.</i> Caused by ignorance or illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्रिय
अविद्रिय <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Without a rent or hole.<BR>—2 Impenetrable, solid. अविद्रियाभिरूतिभिः Rv. 1. 46. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधवा
अविधवा Not a widow, a married woman whose husband is still living;<BR> भर्तुर्मित्रं प्रियमविधवे विद्धि मामम्बुवाहम् Me. 101 अविधवे धीरा<BR> भव Nāg. 5; इदं तावदौषधं किं नाम । अविधवाकरणं नाम । Svapna. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधा
अविधा <i>ind.</i> An interjection meaning ‘help, help’ used in calling<BR> for help in danger. cf. Pratijñā. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधान
अविधान <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Deviating from the fixed rule, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधानम्
अविधान + .{@-नम्@} Absence of definite rule; irregularity, deviation from rule.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविधानतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधानतः
अविधान + -तः <i>ind.</i> Not according to what is prescribed, irregularly;<BR> नियुक्तायामपि पुमान्नार्यां जातोऽविधानतः Ms. 9. 144, 12. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधायक
अविधायक <i>a.</i> Non-injunctive; Non-injunctive statement; अविधायको<BR> मन्त्रः । न हि विधायकाविधायकयोरेकवाक्यत्वं भवति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधि|अविधिः
अविधि <i>a.</i> Not lawful, contrary to rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधिः|अविधि
अविधि + .{@-धिः@}<BR>—1 Irregularity, absence of a rule or precept;<BR>—2 Undefinable ब्रह्म; तपस्त्यागोऽविधिरिति Mb. 12. 19. 9. ˚पूर्वक<BR> not according to rule. तेऽपि मामेव कौन्तेय यजन्त्यविधिपूर्वकम् Bg. 9. 23, 16. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधेय
अविधेय <i>a.</i> Unmanageable, adverse; विधेरविधेयताम् Mu. 4. 2;<BR> हर्षविषादयोरविधेयत्वम् Dk. 161 not being influenced or swayed by &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनः|अविन
अविनः [अवति यज्ञं, अव्-इनच् Uṇ. 2. 46]<BR>—1 A sacrificer.<BR>—2 An officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनय|अविनयः
अविनय <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚] Immodest, insolent, ill-behaved, ill-mannered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनयः|अविनय
अविनय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Want of good manners or modesty; बहवोऽविनयान्नष्टा राजानः सपरिच्छदाः Ms. 7. 40, 41.<BR>—2 Rude behaviour, rudeness, immodest or rude act; ˚बहुलतया चाभिनवयौवनस्य<BR> K. 143; अयमाचरत्यविनयं मुग्धासु तपस्विकन्यासु Ś. 1. 24; indecorum,<BR> impropriety of conduct.<BR>—3 Incivility, disrespect.<BR>—4 Offence, crime, fault; श्रुत्वैव हास्तिनपुरं द्यूतं चाविनयोत्थितम् Mb. 3. 14. 22.<BR>—5 Pride, arrogance, insolence; अविनयमपनय विष्णो Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीत|अविनीतः
अविनीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Immodest, ill-bred, unmannered,<BR>—2 Acting improperly, wicked, vile.<BR>—3 Insolent, rude.<BR>—4 Not tamed, ill-trained; Ms. 4. 67; Y. 3. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीता
अविनीत + .{@-ता@} An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनेय
अविनेय <i>a.</i> Uncontrollable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनश्वर|अविनश्वरः
अविनश्वर <i>a.</i> Indestructible^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनश्वरः|अविनश्वर
अविनश्वर + .{@-रः@} The Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाभावः|अविनाभाव
अविनाभावः<BR>—1 Non-separation.<BR>—2 Inherent or essential character, inseparable connection.<BR>—3 Connection (in general); अविनाभावोऽत्र संबन्धमात्रं न तु नान्तरीयकत्वम् K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाशः|अविनाश
अविनाशः Absence of death, immortality; ततोऽविनाशाय दिवं जगाम Bu. C. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिगमः|अविनिगम
अविनिगमः An illogical conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिवृत्तिः
अविनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Absence of destruction; लिङ्गस्याविनिवृत्तेः Sāṅ. K. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिर्णयः|अविनिर्णय
अविनिर्णयः Indecision, irresolution; Mb. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीय
अविनीय <i>a.</i> Free from deceit or crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविन्ध्यः|अविन्ध्य|अविंध्यः
अविन्ध्यः N. of a Rākṣasa, minister of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविन्ध्या
अविन्ध्यः + .{@-न्ध्या@} N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्व
अविपक्व <i>a.</i> Not ripe (fig. also); immature, undigested; ˚बुद्धि<BR> inexperienced, of undeveloped understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्वकरण
अविपक्व + .{@-करण@} <i>a.</i> Having immature or undeveloped organs; तथाऽविपक्वकरण<BR> आत्मज्ञानस्य न क्षमः Y. 3. 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्वबुद्धि
अविपक्व + .{@-बुद्धि@} <i>a.</i> Having an immature or inexperienced mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपाक|अविपाकः
अविपाक <i>a.</i> Suffering from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपाकः|अविपाक
अविपाक + .{@-कः@} The state of not being ripe, indigestion, a disease arising<BR> from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपद्
अविपद् <i>f.</i> Absence of misery, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपन्न
अविपन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>—2 Not defiled or polluted, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपर्ययः|अविपर्यय
अविपर्ययः Non-existence of doubt and contrariety. Sāṅ. K. 64.<BR> अविपर्ययाद्विशुद्धम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्र|अविप्रः
अविप्र <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not (spiritually) excited, not inspired.<BR>—2 Not a worshipper or praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रः|अविप्र
अविप्र + .{@-प्रः@} One not a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रकृष्ट
अविप्रकृष्ट <i>a.</i> Which is not far removed (as time); P. V. 4. 20;<BR> near (in rank); P. II. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रतिपत्तिः|अविप्रतिपत्ति
अविप्रतिपत्तिः <i>f.</i> Absence of discrepancy; शब्दस्पर्शरूपरसगन्धेष्वविप्रतिपत्तिः<BR> इन्द्रियजयः Kau. A. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रवासः|अविप्रवास
अविप्रवासः Being together; अविप्रवासेन गुणा वसन्ति (Inscription<BR> about Skanda Gupta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रहत
अविप्रहत <i>a.</i> Untrodden (forest, path); अविप्रहतं वनमिदम्<BR> Rām. 1. 24. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्लुत
अविप्लुत <i>a.</i> Undeviating, steadily observing; unviolated; ब्रह्मचर्यमविप्लुतः Ms. 2. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविबुध|अविबुधः
अविबुध <i>a.</i> Not wise, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविबुधः|अविबुध
अविबुध + .{@-धः@} Not a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभक्त|अविभक्तः
अविभक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undivided, unpartitioned, joint, (as property of a family, or co-heirs);<BR> Ms. 9. 215; अविभक्ता विभक्ता वा सपिण्डाः स्थावरे समाः.<BR>—2 Not broken, entire; अविभक्तं च भूतेषु Bg. 13. 16, 18. 20.<BR>—3 Not different.<BR>—4 Existing everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाग|अविभागः
अविभाग <i>a.</i> Unpartitioned, undivided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभागः|अविभाग
अविभाग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Not dividing.<BR>—2 Undivided inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्य|अविभाज्यं
अविभाज्य <i>a.</i> Indivisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्यम्
अविभाज्य + .{@-ज्यम्@}<BR>—1 Indivisibility.<BR>—2 Not being liable to be partitioned; (said of certain articles which<BR> are not to be divided at the time of partition); <i>e. g.</i> वस्त्रं पात्रमलंकारं<BR> कृतान्नमुदकं स्त्रियः । योगक्षेमं प्रचारं च न विभाज्यं प्रचक्षते<BR> Ms. 9. 219. {@˚ता@} indivisibility, unfitness for partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावना
अविभावना, -नम्<BR> Non-perception; disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनम्
अविभावना, -नम्<BR> Non-perception; disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनीय
अविभावनीय, अविभाव्य <i>a.</i> Imperceptible, undistinguishable;<BR> अविभाव्यतारकम् Śi. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाव्य
अविभावनीय, अविभाव्य <i>a.</i> Imperceptible, undistinguishable;<BR> अविभाव्यतारकम् Śi. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाषित
अविभाषित <i>a.</i> That which is not taken into consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्त|अविमुक्तं|अविमुक्तः
अविमुक्त <i>a.</i> Unloosed, not quitted or let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तः|अविमुक्त|अविमुक्तं
अविमुक्त + .{@-क्तः@} The Lord of Benares; प्रीतोऽविमुक्तो भगवांस्तस्मै वरमदाद्भवः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 66. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तम्
अविमुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 N. of a Tīrtha or sacred place near Benares, or Benares itself; न<BR> विमुक्तं शिवाभ्यां यदविमुक्तं ततो विदुः.<BR>—2 The space between the chin and the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तकः|अविमुक्तक
अविमुक्त + .{@-कः@} N. of a plant (Mar. कुसरी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविमुक्तापीडः, अविमुक्तेश्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तापीडः|अविमुक्तापीड
अविमुक्त + -आपीडः N. of a king. Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तेश्वरः|अविमुक्तेश्वर
अविमुक्त + -ईश्वरः a celebrated Śiva-liṅga at Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमृष्य
अविमृष्य <i>a.</i> Undoubted, unquestionable; अविमृष्यमेतदभिलष्यति<BR> सः Ki. 6. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमोक्य
अविमोक्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Not to be loosened; दाम ग्रीवास्वविमोक्यं<BR> यत् Av. 6. 63. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियुक्त
अवियुक्त <i>a.</i> Undivided, conjoined, united; not separated R. 13. 31; not absent^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोग|अवियोगः
अवियोग <i>a.</i> Not separated, united, connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोगः|अवियोग
अवियोग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Non-separation, presence.<BR>—2 Conjunction, association.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवियोगतृतीया, अवियोगव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोगतृतीया
अवियोग + -तृतीया N. of a certain festival or holiday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोगव्रतम्
अवियोग + -व्रतम् a vow to be observed by women on the third day of the<BR> first fortnight of Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरत|अविरतं
अविरत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not desisting or ceasing from (with abl.) नाविरतो दुश्चरितात्<BR> Kaṭh.; uninterrupted, continual, unbroken, perpetual; अविरतोत्कण्ठमुत्कण्ठितेन<BR> Me. 104; Prov. मन्दोप्यविरतोद्योगः सदैव विजयी भवेत् ‘slow and steady wins the race’<BR>.<BR>—2 Abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरतम्
अविरत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Eternally, continually; अविरतं परकार्यकृतां सताम् Bv. 1. 113.<BR> cf. also भजामस्त्वां गौरीं नगपतिकिशोरीमविरतम् Saundaryalaharī.<BR>—2 Fast, deep, sound (asleep); रताविरतसंसुप्तं ददर्श हरियूथपः<BR> Rām. 5. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरति|अविरतिः
अविरति <i>a.</i> Incessant, ceaseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरतिः|अविरति
अविरति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Continuity, uninterruptedness.<BR>—2 Incontinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराम|अविरामः
अविराम <i>a.</i> Uninterrupted, continuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरामः|अविराम
अविराम + .{@-मः@} Uninterrupted succession, continuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरामम्
अविराम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i> Uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरल|अविरलं
अविरल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thick, dense; ˚वारिधारा U. 6 sharp-driving shower; ˚अश्रुबिन्दु;<BR> not thin, many; सादरमभिमुखदत्ताविरलपदः K. 95.<BR>—2 Contiguous, close.<BR>—3 Coarse, gross, substantial.<BR>—4 Uninterrupted, continuous.<BR>—5 Huge, big, bulky; अविरलवपुषः सुरेन्द्रगोपः Ki. 10. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरलम्
अविरल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Closely; अविरलमालिङ्गितुं पवनः Ś. 3. 6.<BR>—2 Uninterruptedly, incessantly, constantly; U. 3. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविरलधारासारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरलधारासारः|अविरलधारासार
अविरल + -धारासारः an incessant down-pour of heavy rain. cf. अविरलमदधाराधौतकुम्भः<BR> शरण्यः (गजवक्त्रः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरलित
अविरलित <i>a.</i> Closely stuck, lying very close; ˚कपोलम् U. 1. 27<BR> cheek to cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरविकन्यायः|अविरविकन्याय
अविरविकन्यायः See अव्यविकन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरहित
अविरहित <i>a.</i> unseparated, not being without; अविरहितमनेकेनाङ्कभाजा<BR> फलेन Ki. 5. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराधयत्|अविराधयन्त्
अविराधयत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not withdrawing oneself; not desisting; एवा<BR> भगस्य जुष्टेयमस्तु नारी सम्प्रिया पत्याविराधयन्ती Av. 2. 36. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरुद्ध
अविरुद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not opposed, compatible, consistent with.<BR>—2 Living together.<BR>—3 Unobstructed, unhindered, unimpeded.<BR>—4 Allowed; proper; यद्यविरुद्धं श्रोष्यामि V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोधः|अविरोध
अविरोधः<BR>—1 Consistency, compatibility, congruity; सामान्यास्तु परार्थमुद्यमभृतः<BR> स्वार्थाविरोधेन ये Bh. 2. 74 consistently<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">Page0268-1</a>]<BR> with their own interest; सर्वेषामविरोधेन ब्रह्मकर्म समारभे Pūjāmantra.<BR>—2 Absence of impediment.<BR>—3 Assent, concurrence, consistency, harmony; निजधर्माविरोधेन यस्तु<BR> सामायिको भवेत् Y. 2. 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेचनम्
अविरेचनम् Anything which causes constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेचनीय
अविरेचनीय, अविरेच्य <i>a.</i> Not to be purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेच्य
अविरेचनीय, अविरेच्य <i>a.</i> Not to be purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलक्ष्य
अविलक्ष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no aim or mark.<BR>—2 Guileless.<BR>—3 Irremediable.<BR>—4 Difficult to withstand, inconceived; अविलक्ष्यमस्त्रमपरं (v. l.<BR> अविपक्ष) Ki. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घनम्
अविलङ्घनम् Non-transgression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घनीय|अविलंघनीय
अविलङ्घनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be transgressed.<BR>—2 Prescribed, fixed, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्ब|अविलंब|अविलम्बः
अविलम्ब <i>a.</i> Prompt, not delaying, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बः|अविलम्ब|अविलंब
अविलम्ब + .{@-म्बः@} Absence of delay, quickness, promptitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बम्
अविलम्ब + .{@-म्बम्, -अविलम्बेन@} <i>ind.</i> Without delay, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बेन
अविलम्ब + .{@-म्बम्, -अविलम्बेन@} <i>ind.</i> Without delay, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बित|अविलंबित|अविलम्बितं|अविलम्बितः
अविलम्बित <i>a.</i> Without delay, quick, expeditions, prompt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बितम्
अविलम्बित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Quickly, without delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविला
अविला [अव्-इलच्] An ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलास|अविलासः
अविलास <i>a.</i> Free from whims, faithful, constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलासः|अविलास
अविलास + .{@-सः@} Absence of pastime or whim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलिख
अविलिख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not writing, or painting, or unable to do so; (P. VI. 2. 157-8.)<BR>—2 Writing badly.<BR>—3 Different from one who writes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलुप्त
अविलुप्त <i>a.</i> Undamaged, unhurt; Rāj. T.; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवक्षित
अविवक्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not intended or aimed at; भ्रातरः इत्यत्र एकशेषग्रहणमविवक्षितम्.<BR>—2 Not to be said or spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवक्षितवचनता
अविवक्षित + .{@-वचनता@} The state of mantras of not being meant to convey their meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादः|अविवाद
अविवादः Agreement, consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादिन्
अविवादिन् <i>a.</i> Not contending, quiet, peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहिन्
अविवाहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not marrying, remaining single or celibate.<BR>—2 Not relating to marriage.<BR>—3 Interdicted as to marriage; Ms. 9. 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविविक्त
अविविक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uninvestigated, not properly thought out.<BR>—2 Indiscriminate, confounded.<BR>—3 Public.<BR>—4 Making no difference; ˚दृश् viewing all as one with God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेक|अविवेकः
अविवेक <i>a.</i> Wanting in judgment or discrimination, thoughtless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकः|अविवेक
अविवेक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Want of discrimination or judgment, absence of prudence, imprudence;<BR> अविवेकः परमापदां पदम् Ki. 2. 30.<BR>—2 Hastiness, rashness, recklessness.<BR>—3 Ignorance; (अन्योन्यतादात्म्यरूपमिथ्याज्ञानम्).<BR>—4 Non-separation, non-distinction; पौरुषं कर्म दैवं च कालवृत्तिस्वभावतः ।<BR> त्रयमेतत्पृथग्भूतमविवेकं तु केचन ॥ Mb. 12. 238. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविवेककृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेककृत
अविवेक + -कृत <i>a.</i> done rashly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकिन्
अविवेकिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undiscriminating, inconsiderate, thoughtless.<BR>—2 Superficial, short-sighted, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचक|अविवेचकः
अविवेचक <i>a.</i> Undiscriminating; Sāṅ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचना
अविवेचना Absence of thoughtfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेनत्|अविवेनन्त्
अविवेनत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not disaffected, favourable; सध्रीचीनेन<BR> मनसाविवेनत् Rv. 4. 24. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेनम्
अविवेनत् + .{@-नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Not disaffectedly, favourably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्क|अविशंक
अविशङ्क <i>a.</i> Having no fears or doubt, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्का
अविशङ्क + .{@-का@} Absence of doubt or fear, confidence, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्कम्
अविशङ्क + .{@-ङ्कम्, अविशङ्केन@} <i>ind.</i> Without doubt, hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्केन
अविशङ्क + .{@-ङ्कम्, अविशङ्केन@} <i>ind.</i> Without doubt, hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्कित|अविशंकित
अविशङ्कित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unapprehensive, fearless.<BR>—2 Without doubt, confiding; गृध्रवाक्यात्कथं मूढास्त्यजध्वमविशङ्किताः K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशयः
अविशयः Absence of doubt. यदि वा अविशये नियमः Ms. 8. 3. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशस्तृ
अविशस्तृ <i>m.</i> An unskilful cutter up or killer (of animals at a<BR> sacrifice); मा ते गृध्नुरविशस्तातिहाय Rv. 1. 162. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशुद्धिः|अविशुद्धि
अविशुद्धिः <i>f.</i> Impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेष|अविशेषः
अविशेष <i>a.</i> Without any difference, alike, similar, uniform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषः|अविशेष
अविशेष + .{@-षः, -षम्@}<BR>—1 Absence of difference, uniformity, similarity.<BR>—2 Identity, sameness.<BR>—3 The subtle elements; तन्मात्राण्यविशेषाः Sāṅ. K. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषम्
अविशेष + .{@-षः, -षम्@}<BR>—1 Absence of difference, uniformity, similarity.<BR>—2 Identity, sameness.<BR>—3 The subtle elements; तन्मात्राण्यविशेषाः Sāṅ. K. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषक
अविशेष + .{@-क@} <i>a.</i> Inconclusive, not leading to any definite conclusion;<BR> अपि चैकेन संनिधानमविशेषको हेतुः Ms. 11. 1. 64.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अविशेषज्ञ, अविशेषवचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषज्ञ
अविशेष + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> not knowing the difference (in things), undiscriminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषवचन
अविशेष + -वचन <i>a.</i> Not expressive of any particular detail or aspect<BR> of a matter; अविशेषवचनः शब्दो न विशेषे व्यवस्थापितो भविष्यति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषतः
अविशेषतः <i>ind.</i> Without difference; Ms. 9. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रम्भः|अविश्रम्भ
अविश्रम्भः Want of confidence, diffidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रान्त|अविश्रांत|अविश्रान्तः
अविश्रान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untiring, incessant, ceaseless; Ś. 6.<BR>—2 Unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रान्तम्
अविश्रान्त + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Incessantly, continuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वास|अविश्वासः
अविश्वास <i>a.</i> Not inspiring confidence, mistrusted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासः|अविश्वास
अविश्वास + .{@-सः@} Mistrust, suspicion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासा
अविश्वास + .{@-सा@} A cow calving after long intervals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वस्त|अविश्वस्तः
अविश्वस्त <i>a.</i> Not trusted, suspected; न विश्वसेदविश्वस्ते H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासिन्
अविश्वासिन् <i>a.</i> Mistrusting, unbelieving, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष|अविषः
अविष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not poisonous.<BR>—2 Anti-venomous, antidote.<BR>—3 Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषः|अविष
अविष + .{@-षः@} [अव्-टिषच् Uṇ. 1. 45]<BR>—1 An ocean.<BR>—2 A king.<BR>—3 Sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषा
अविष + .{@-षा@} N. of a plant (निर्विषातृण) Curcuma Zedoaria. (Mar. कचरा, अतिवीण)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषी
अविष + .{@-षी@}<BR>—1 A river.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR>—3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषक्त
अविषक्त <i>a.</i> Not clinging or sticking तुभ्यं नमस्तेऽस्त्वविषक्तदृष्टये<BR> Bhāg. 10. 40. 12. Unrestrained, unchecked; अविषक्तवेगः Ki. 13. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषय|अविषयः
अविषय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unperceived, invisible, beyond the reach of the senses.<BR>—2 Insensible.<BR>—3 Disregarding<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">Page0269-1</a>]<BR> objects of sense; ˚मनसां यतीनाम् M. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषयः|अविषय
अविषय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Absence, disappearance; रवेरविषये किं न प्रदीपस्य प्रकाशनम् H. 2. 78.<BR>—2 Not an object of (anything), not within the reach of, beyond, transcending;<BR> न कश्चिद्धीमतामविषयो नाम Ś. 4; सकलवचनानामविषयः Māl. 1. 30<BR> beyond the reach (power) of words; सौमित्रेरपि पत्त्रिणामविषये<BR> तत्र प्रिये क्वासि मे U. 3. 45.<BR>—3 Disregard of the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषयीकरणम्
अविषयीकरणम् Not making anything an object of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषह्य
अविषह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Difficult to decide. सीमायामविषह्यायाम् Ms. 8. 265.<BR>—2 Impracticable, unfeasible; (Bk.).<BR>—3 Invisible.<BR>—4 Intolerable, insupportable; अविषह्यव्यसनेन धूमिताम् Ki. 4. 30.<BR>—5 Inaccessible; चक्षुषामविषह्यम् Mb. 14. 20. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्करः
अविष्करः A cock Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्ठ
अविष्ठ Ved. Gladly accepting, protecting very carefully or attentively;<BR> यो अर्चतो ब्रह्मकृतिमविष्ठो Rv. 7. 28. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्या
अविष्या [अव् गतौ इसुन् अविर्गतिमिच्छति-क्यच् भावे अ Tv.]<BR>—1 Wish to go (गमनेच्छा); अह्यर्षूणां चिन्न्ययाँ अविष्याम् Rv. 2. 38. 3.<BR>—2 Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्यु
अविष्यु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Attacking.<BR>—2 Desirous, wishing.<BR>—3 Violent, vehement.<BR>—4 Wishing to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्
अविस् <i>n.</i> [अव्-भावे इसुन्]<BR>—1 Protection.<BR>—2 Going. ━<i>m.</i> An extender, enlarger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसंवादः|अविसंवाद
अविसंवादः Non-contradiction; non-violation of oneʼs promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसंवादिन्
अविसंवादिन् <i>a.</i> Unfailing, not false; Ki. 13. 15; लक्षणान्येव<BR> तवाविसंवादीनि Dk. 67 entirely agreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसर्गिन्
अविसर्गिन् <i>a.</i> Not quitting, retaining, adhering to. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसर्गी
अविसर्गिन् + .({@-गी^1@}) An unintermittent fever.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: cf. ap90, pwg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तर
अविस्तर <i>a.</i> Of small extent or length, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तारः|अविस्तार
अविस्तारः Absence of amplification or diffuseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तीर्ण
अविस्तीर्ण <i>a.</i> Not extended or amplified, curtailed, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तृत
अविस्तृत <i>a.</i> Compact, compressed, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्थलम्
अविस्थलम् N. of one of the five towns demanded by the Pāṇḍavas<BR> from the Kauravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्ट|अविस्पष्टं
अविस्पष्ट <i>a.</i> Not clear or plain, indistinct, obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्टम्
अविस्पष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} An indistinct speech; नाविस्पष्टमधीयीत Ms. 4. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहर्यत|अविहर्य्यत
अविहर्यत <i>a.</i> Not desired (अनभिलषित); येनाविहर्यतकतोः<BR> Rv. 1. 63. 2 doer of undesired acts; whose will cannot be averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहस्तः|अविहस्त
अविहस्तः Not confounded, full of courage; अथ मृशमविहस्तस्तत्र<BR> कान्तारगर्भे Śiva B. 86 also 92. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहा
अविहा <i>ind.</i> Alas! Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहित
अविहित <i>a.</i> Unprescribed, forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्रुत
अविह्रुत <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not to be killed, unassailable.<BR>—2 Unbent, unbroken; आ मा भद्रस्य लोके पाप्मन् धेह्यविह्रुतम् Av. 6. 27. 1.<BR>—3 Not curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्वरत्|अविह्वरन्त्
अविह्वरत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not slipping, not falling.<BR>—2 Undeviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवी
अवी [अवत्यात्मानं लज्जया अव्-ई Uṇ. 3. 158] A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीक्षिन्
अवीक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Not seeing; दृशोर्द्वयं नस्तदवीक्षि चाफलम् N. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचि|अवीचिः
अवीचि <i>a.</i> Waveless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचिः|अवीचि
अवीचि + .{@-चिः@} N. of a particular hell; अवीचिमन्धतामिस्रं कुम्भीपाकं<BR> तथैव च Y. 3. 224. ˚मयः a place of punishment for liars (यत्र<BR> जलमिव स्थलमश्मपृष्ठमवभासते Bhāg.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचिसंशोषणः|अवीचिसंशोषण
अवीचि + .{@-संशोषणः@} A particular Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीज|अवीजः
अवीज, -जक (अबीज)<BR>—1 Seedless; अबीजकमपि क्षेत्रं केवलं स्थाण्डिलं भवेत् Ms. 10. 71.<BR>—2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—3 Having no prime cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजक
अवीज, -जक (अबीज)<BR>—1 Seedless; अबीजकमपि क्षेत्रं केवलं स्थाण्डिलं भवेत् Ms. 10. 71.<BR>—2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—3 Having no prime cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीज|अबीजः
अवीज, -जक (अबीज)<BR>—1 Seedless; अबीजकमपि क्षेत्रं केवलं स्थाण्डिलं भवेत् Ms. 10. 71.<BR>—2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—3 Having no prime cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजः|अवीज
अवीज, -जक (अबीज) + .{@-जः@} Restraint, controlling the mental passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजा
अवीज, -जक (अबीज) + .{@-जा@} Vine plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजम्
अवीज, -जक (अबीज) + .{@-जम्@}<BR>—1 Bad seed, bad grain; ˚विक्रयिन् Ms. 9. 291.<BR>—2 Absence of seed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवीजहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजहन्
अवीज + -हन् <i>a.</i> Ved. not pernicious to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीतम्
अवीतम् A variety of अनुमान or inference; (व्यतिरेकमुखेन<BR> प्रवर्तमानं निषेधकमवीतम्; यथा पृथिवी पृथिवीतरभिन्ना गन्धवत्त्वात् Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर|अवीरः
अवीर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unmanly, effeminate, weak; अयन् मासा अयज्वनामवीराः Rv. 7. 61. 4 cowardly.<BR>—2 Having no son (as a woman). मा त्वा वयं सहसावन्नवीरा Rv. 7. 4. 6.<BR>—3 helpless.<BR>—4 Destitute of heroes or men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीरा
अवीर + .{@-रा@} A woman who has neither sons nor husband; अजातपुत्रा विधवा<BR> साऽवीरा परिकीर्तिता; (opp. वीरा which is thus defined; पतिपुत्रवती<BR> नारी वीरा प्रोक्ता मनीषिभिः) Rv. 10. 86. 9; वरं त्ववीरा हतकिल्बिषा<BR> गतिम् Bhāg. 6. 28. 19. अनर्चितं वृथा मांसमवीरायाश्च योषितः<BR> Ms. 4. 213; Y. 1. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर्य
अवीर्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Weak, ineffective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृक
अवृक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from danger, safe.<BR>—2 Not hurting, inoffensive, true.<BR>—3 Free from one who obscures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृकम्
अवृक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Safety, peace, security.<BR>—2 Quiet, repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृक्ष
अवृक्ष <i>a.</i> Treeless, destitute of trees; अवृक्षं कामशैलं च<BR> Rām. 4. 43. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृजिन
अवृजिन <i>a.</i> Ved. Straightforward, sincere, not deserting (friends);<BR> an epithet of the Ādityas; आदित्यासः शुचयो धारपूता अवृजिना अनवद्या<BR> अरिष्टाः Rv. 2. 27. 2. श्रोतियोऽवृजिनोऽकामहतः Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत
अवृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unchecked, unimpeded.<BR>—2 Unselected.<BR>—3 Uncovered, unprotected.<BR>—4 Unsubdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत्ति|अवृत्तिः
अवृत्ति <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Not existing, not present, not being in.<BR>—2 Having no livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत्तिः|अवृत्ति
अवृत्ति + .{@-त्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Absence of subsistence or means of livelihood, inadequate support;<BR> अवृत्तिकर्षिता हि स्त्री प्रदुष्येत् स्थितिमत्यपि Ms. 9. 74, 10. 101;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">Page0270-1</a>]<BR> आददीताममेवास्मादवृत्तावेकरात्रिकम् 4. 223.<BR>—2 Absence of wages; ˚त्वम् non-exsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथा
अवृथा <i>ind.</i> Not in vain, successfully.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवृथार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथार्थ
अवृथा + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> successful, gaining oneʼs desired object; निरसनैरसनैरवृथार्थता Śi. 6. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृद्धिक
अवृद्धिक <i>a.</i> Not augmentative, not bearing interest (as capital);<BR> तत्कालकृतमूल्यो वा तत्र तिष्ठेदवृद्धिकः Y. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृद्धिकम्
अवृद्धिक + .{@-कम्@} Original capital, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृध
अवृध <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not increasing.<BR>—2 Not promoting, not honouring.<BR>—3 Not rendering prosperous or refreshing; अश्रद्धाँ अवृधाँ अयज्ञान् Rv. 7. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृष्टि|अवृष्टिः
अवृष्टि <i>a.</i> Not pouring down rain (as a cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृष्टिः|अवृष्टि
अवृष्टि + .{@-ष्टिः@} Want of rain, drought; famine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवे
अवे €2 P. [अव-इ]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To know, understand, learn, perceive, be aware of; अवैमि ते<BR> तस्यां सोदर्यस्नेहम् Ś. 4; अवैमि चैनामनघेति R. 14. 40; द्विषदभियोग<BR> इत्यवैति Mu. 1. 7; अवैमि ते सारम् Ku. 3. 13; R. 2. 35.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To know, look upon or consider, regard, तदवैमि कैतवम्<BR> Ku. 4. 9; Ś. 5. 11; Bk. 7. 33; किं मां सुतक्षयकरं सुत इत्यवैषि Ve. 5. 2.<BR>—2 To go or move away; अवैतु पृश्नि शैवलम् Av. 1. 11. 4.<BR>—3 To go to, approach (with acc.).<BR>—4 To rush upon, come down upon (Ved.). ━<i>Freq.</i> or <i>pass.</i><BR> (अवेयते) To beg pardon for, conciliate; Rv. 1. 24. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेत
अवेत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Elapsed, past.<BR>—2 Obtained, attained; P. V. 1. 134.<BR>—3 Joined or united with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्ष्
अवेक्ष् €1 Ā. [अव-ईक्ष्]<BR>—1 To look at, perceive, observe, behold.<BR>—2 To aim at, have in view; योत्स्यमानानवेक्षेहम् Bg. 1. 23; take into<BR> account or consideration, have regard to; स्वधर्ममपि चावेक्ष्य Bg. 2. 31;<BR> अवेक्ष्य धातोर्गमनार्थमर्थविद् R. 3. 21; किमपि निमित्तमवेक्ष्य<BR> V. 5; त्रिदिवोत्सुकयाप्यवेक्ष्य माम् R. 8. 60 out of regard for me; K. 329;<BR> oft. with न meaning ‘not to mind or heed’, ‘disregard’; R. 11. 69;<BR> न हि कमलिनीं दृष्ट्वा ग्राहमवेक्षते मतङ्गजः M. 3. (it may<BR> also mean ‘expect’ here); निद्रावशेन भवता ह्यनवेक्ष्यमाणा R. 5. 67.<BR>—3 To look to or after; attend to; अवेक्षमाणं महतीं मुहुर्मुहुः Śi. 1. 10.<BR>—4 To take care of, guard, watch over, protect; वसुधेयमवेक्ष्यतां<BR> त्वया R. 8. 83; श्लाघ्यां दुहितरमवेक्षस्व जानकीम् U. 1. 7.<BR>—5 To think, consider; यदवोचदवेक्ष्य मानिनी Ki. 2. 3.<BR>—6 To look into or examine, inspect; स कदाचिदवेक्षितप्रजः R. 8. 32;<BR> प्रकृतीरवेक्षितुम्<BR>—18 inquire into; Ś. 6.<BR>—7 To expect, hope for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षक
अवेक्षक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Showing, showing all round.<BR>—2 Inspecting, supervising; a superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षणम्
अवेक्षणम्<BR>—1 Looking towards or at, seeing दुर्व्याहृताच्छङ्कमाना दुःस्थताद् दुरवेक्षितात्<BR> Mb. 2. 233. 21.<BR>—2 Guarding, watching over, protection, taking care of, attending to,<BR> supervision, inspection; वर्णाश्रमावेक्षणजागरूकः R. 14. 85; हस्त्यश्वावेक्षणेऽनभियुक्तः Mu. 3.<BR>—3 Attention, care, observation.<BR>—4 Regarding, considering; see अनवेक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षणीय
अवेक्षणीय <i>pot. p.</i> to be looked to or respected, to be looked<BR> upon or considered; तपस्विसामान्यमवेक्षणीया R. 14. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षमाण
अवेक्षमाण <i>a.</i> Looking at, examining; अवेक्षमाणं महतीं मुहुर्मुहुः Śi. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षा
अवेक्षा<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at.<BR>—2 Attention, care, regard; Bhāg. 10. 74. 22. लब्धं रक्षेदवेक्षया<BR> Ms. 7. 101; अत्रास्त्यवेक्षा त्वयि मे Rām.<BR>—3 Agreement, engagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षितृ
अवेक्षितृ <i>a.</i> Looking at; thinking of, regarding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षिन्
अवेक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Seeing, observing; धर्मावेक्षिता Ś. 5 regard for<BR> justice or righteousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेणि
अवेणि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not braided.<BR>—2 Having no braid of hair.<BR>—3 Not flowing together or commingled (as the waters of rivers.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदः|अवेद
अवेदः Not the Veda; वेदा अवेदाः Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अवेदविद्, अवेदविहित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविद्
अवेदः + -विद् Not knowing the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविहित
अवेदः + -विहित <i>a.</i> Not prescribed by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदनाज्ञ
अवेदनाज्ञ <i>a.</i> One who is not sensitive to pain अवेदनाज्ञं<BR> कुलिशक्षतानाम् Ku. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदयान
अवेदयान <i>a.</i> Not knowing, not ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदिः|अवेदि
अवेदिः <i>f.</i> Absence of knowledge; न चेदवेदिर्महती विनष्टिः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्य|अवेद्यः
अवेद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unknowable, secret.<BR>—2 Unattainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्यः|अवेद्य
अवेद्य + .{@-द्यः@} A calf<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्या
अवेद्य + .{@-द्या@} (A woman) not to be married; व्यभिचारेण वर्णानामवेद्यावेदनेन<BR> च । स्वकर्मणां च त्यागेन जायन्ते वर्णसंकराः ॥ Ms. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेनत्|अवेनन्त्
अवेनत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Unconscious.<BR>—2 Not having any wish or desire; अवेनन्तं तुषयन्ती बिभर्ति Rv. 10. 27. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेल|अवेलः
अवेल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no boundary or limit, unlimited.<BR>—2 Having no time, untimely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेलः|अवेल
अवेल + .{@-लः@} Concealment of knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेला
अवेल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 Unfavourable time.<BR>—2 Chewed betel (supposed to be = अव + इला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेष्टिः|अवेष्टि
अवेष्टिः Ved. Expiation (of sins) by sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैद्य
अवैद्य <i>a.</i> Not learned, ignorant (of the Veda). अधीयानस्याप्यध्ययनं<BR> सफलं न भवति, दोषश्च जायते । अतोऽवैद्यः शूद्रः ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैद्यत्वम्
अवैद्य + .{@-त्वम्@} ignorance (of the veda) अवैद्यत्वादभावः कर्मणि स्यात् MS. 6. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैध|अवैधं
अवैध <i>a.</i> (-धी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Irregular, not conformable to law or rule; अवैधं पञ्चमं कुर्वन्<BR> राज्ञो दण्डेन शुध्यति.<BR>—2 Not sanctioned by the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैधव्यम्
अवैधव्यम् Non-widowhood; अवैधव्येन युक्ताम् Mb. 5. 11. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैमत्यम्
अवैमत्यम् Unanimity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैयात्यम्
अवैयात्यम् Having a sense of shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैयाकरण
अवैयाकरण Not a grammarian; Mbh. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैरहत्यम्
अवैरहत्यम् Ved. Security from slaughter; अवैरहत्यायेदमा पपत्यात् Av. 6. 29. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैशेषिक
अवैशेषिक <i>a.</i> Inconclusive, not leading to any definite conclusion;<BR> अवैशेषिकोऽयं हेतुः समुदायशब्दसंयोगः ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोक्षणम्
अवोक्षणम् [अव-उक्ष्-भावे ल्युट्] Ved. Sprinkling with the hand slightly<BR> bent; उत्तानेनैव हस्तेन प्रोक्षणं परिकीर्तितम् । न्यञ्चताभ्युक्षणं<BR> प्रोक्तं तिरश्चावोक्षणं स्मृतम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोद|अवोदं|अवोदः
अवोद <i>a.</i> [अव-उन्द्-भावे घञ् निपातः नलोपः P. VI. 4. 29] Wet, moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोदः|अवोद|अवोदं
अवोद + .{@-दः@} Sprinkling, moistening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोदेव
अवोदेव <i>a.</i> [देवानामवस्तात् अव्ययी˚ स˚] Bringing down the<BR> gods; below (the region of the) gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोषः|अवोष
अवोषः Hot food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्य|अव्यः
अव्य <i>a.</i> [अवि भवार्थे यत्] Coming or belonging to a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यः|अव्य
अव्य + .{@-व्यः, -व्यम्@} The woollen Soma-strainer; Rv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यम्
अव्य + .{@-व्यः, -व्यम्@} The woollen Soma-strainer; Rv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं|अव्यक्तः
अव्यक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Indistinct, not manifest or apparent, inarticulate; ˚वर्ण indistinct<BR> accents; Ś. 7. 17; फलमव्यक्तमब्रवीत्.<BR>—2 Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>—3 Undetermined; अव्यक्तोऽयमचिन्त्योऽयम् Bg. 2. 25, 8. 20.<BR>—4 Undeveloped, uncreated.<BR>—5 (In alg.) Unknown (as a quantity or number).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तः|अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं
अव्यक्त + .{@-क्तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 Cupid.<BR>—4 Primary matter which has not yet entered into real existence.<BR>—5 A fool.<BR>—6 N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तम्
अव्यक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} (In Vedānta Phil.)<BR>—1 The Supreme Being or Universal Spirit, Brahman.<BR>—2 Spiritual ignorance.<BR>—3 The subtle body.<BR>—4 The state of sleep (सुषुप्त्यवस्था).<BR>—5 (In Sāṅ. Phil.) The primary germ of nature (सर्वकारण), the<BR> primordial element or productive principle from which all the phenomena<BR> of the material world are developed; बुद्धेरिवाव्यक्तमुदाहरन्ति R. 13. 60;<BR> महतः परमव्यक्तमव्यक्तात्पुरुषः परः Kaṭh.; Sāṅ. K. 2.<BR> 10, 14, 16, 58.<BR>—6 The Soul.<BR>—7 Nature. अव्यक्तः शंकरे विष्णौ क्लीबे तु महदादिके । परमात्मन्यात्मनि<BR> च त्रिषु स्यादस्फुटे … Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तम्
अव्यक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Imperceptibly, indistinctly, inarticulately.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अव्यक्तानुकरणम्, अव्यक्तादि, अव्यक्तक्रिया, अव्यक्तपद, अव्यक्तमूर्ति, अव्यक्तमूलप्रभवः, अव्यक्तराग, अव्यक्तराशिः, अव्यक्तलक्षणः, अव्यक्तव्यक्तः, अव्यक्तलिङ्ग, अव्यक्तवर्त्मन्, अव्यक्तमार्ग, अव्यक्तवाच्, अव्यक्तसाम्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तानुकरणम्
अव्यक्त + -अनुकरणम् imitating inarticulate or unmeaning sounds; P. V. 4. 57;<BR> अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात इतौ VI. 1. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तादि
अव्यक्त + -आदि <i>a.</i> whose beginning is inscrutable; अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि Bg. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तक्रिया
अव्यक्त + -क्रिया<BR>—1 an algebraic calculation.<BR>—2 any act of an indistinct character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तपद
अव्यक्त + -पद <i>a.</i> inarticulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तमूर्ति|अव्यक्तमूर्त्ति
अव्यक्त + -मूर्ति <i>a.</i> having an incomprehensible form; मया … अव्यक्तमूर्तिना Bg. 9. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तमूलप्रभवः|अव्यक्तमूलप्रभव
अव्यक्त + -मूलप्रभवः the tree of mundane existence (in Sāṅ. Phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराग|अव्यक्तरागः
अव्यक्त + -राग <i>a.</i> dark-red, ruddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तरागः|अव्यक्तराग
अव्यक्त + -राग + .({@-गः@}) the colour of the dawn; अव्यक्तरागस्त्वरुणः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराशिः|अव्यक्तराशि
अव्यक्त + -राशिः an unknown number or quantity (in algebra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तलक्षणः|अव्यक्तलक्षण
अव्यक्त + -लक्षणः, -व्यक्तः an epithet of Śiva (whose qualities are not perceptible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तव्यक्तः|अव्यक्तव्यक्त
अव्यक्त + -लक्षणः, -व्यक्तः an epithet of Śiva (whose qualities are not perceptible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तलिङ्ग|अव्यक्तलिङ्गः
अव्यक्त + -लिङ्ग <i>a.</i> whose signs are invisible (as a disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तलिङ्गः|अव्यक्तलिङ्ग
अव्यक्त + -लिङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गः@}) an ascetic (संन्यासी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तलिङ्गम्
अव्यक्त + -लिङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गम्@}) the great principle (महत्) (in Sāṅ. Phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तवर्त्मन्
अव्यक्त + -वर्त्मन्, -मार्ग <i>a.</i> whose ways are mysterious or inscrutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तमार्ग
अव्यक्त + -वर्त्मन्, -मार्ग <i>a.</i> whose ways are mysterious or inscrutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तवाच्
अव्यक्त + -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तसाम्यम्
अव्यक्त + -साम्यम् an equation of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तिक
अव्यक्तिक <i>a.</i> See अव्यक्त; लभतेऽव्यक्तिकं स्थानं ज्ञात्वाऽव्यक्तं<BR> महीयते Mb. 12. 318. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्र
अव्यग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not agitated or ruffled, steady, cool.<BR>—2 Not engaged or occupied (in business); अव्यग्रस्य पुनरस्य U. 2.<BR>—3 Indifferent, undisturbed.<BR>—4 Attentive, careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्रम्
अव्यग्र + .{@-ग्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Quietly, at ease, coolly, leisurely; क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्ग|अव्यंग|अव्यङ्गः
अव्यङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not mutilated or defective, well-made, sound, perfect; अव्यङ्गाङ्गीं<BR> सौम्यनाम्नीम् Ms. 3. 10.<BR>—2 Plain, not figurative (as a meaning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्गा|अव्यंगा
अव्यङ्ग + .{@-गा@}<BR>—1 = अव्यण्डा q. v.<BR>—2 legume or pod of the awn of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्ग्य|अव्यङ्ग्यं
अव्यङ्ग्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Faultless.<BR>—2 Without a suggestive figure of speech. सव्यङ्ग्यमुत्तमं काव्यमव्यङ्ग्यं<BR> चाधमं स्मृतम् । काव्यचन्द्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यचस्
अव्यचस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not spacious; Av. 19. 68. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यञ्जन|अव्यंजन|अव्यञ्जनः
अव्यञ्जन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no distinctive or characteristic marks or signs (as of the sex);<BR> ˚ना कन्याः without consonants.<BR>—2 Having no good marks.<BR>—3 Indistinct.<BR>—4 Not figurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यञ्जनः|अव्यञ्जन|अव्यंजन
अव्यञ्जन + .{@-नः@} An animal without horns, though of an age to have them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यण्डा|अव्यंडा
अव्यण्डा [न विगतमण्डं बीजमस्याः]<BR>—1 N. of the plant Carpopogon Pruriens Roxb. (Mar. कुयली).<BR>—2 A legume or pod of the awn of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिः|अव्यति
अव्यतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Satisfaction, satiating.<BR>—2 Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिकीर्ण|अव्यतिकीर्ण्ण
अव्यतिकीर्ण <i>a.</i> Unmixed, unblended, distinct; specific, separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिरेकः|अव्यतिरेक
अव्यतिरेकः Non-exclusion, non-exception. <i>a.</i> Unerring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ|अव्यथः
अव्यथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not giving or inflicting pain, merciful.<BR>—2 Free from pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथः|अव्यथ
अव्यथ + .{@-थः@} [न व्यथते पद्भपां न संचलति व्यथ् भयचलवयोः अच्] A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथा
अव्यथ + .{@-था@}<BR>—1 N. of two plants; Terminalia Citrina Roxb (Mar. हिरडा); and Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—2 Dry ginger.<BR>—3 (Ved.) Firmness, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथयः|अव्यथय
अव्यथयः A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथि|अव्यथिः
अव्यथि <i>a.</i> Ved. [व्यथ्-इन्, न˚ त˚] Not tremulous or tottering<BR> (in steps), steady, sure-footed, undaunted; epithet of the horses of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिः|अव्यथि
अव्यथि + .{@-थिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A firm step.<BR>—2 Undauntedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिन्
अव्यथिन् <i>a.</i> [cf. P. III. 2. 157]<BR>—1 Free from pain.<BR>—2 Free from fear, fearless; Śi. 15. 12.<BR>—3 Not giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिषः|अव्यथिष
अव्यथिषः [न-व्यथ्-टिषच् Uṇ. 1. 49]<BR>—1 The Sun.<BR>—2 The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिषी
अव्यथिषः + .{@-षी@}<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 Midnight; night. (अव्यथिषी धरारात्र्योः Ujjval.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ्य|अव्यथ्यः
अव्यथ्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from pain; not giving pain.<BR>—2 Unshakable; अस्मै तिस्रो अव्यथ्याय नाराः Rv. 2. 35. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यनत्|अव्यनन्त्
अव्यनत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not breathing, lifeless. अव्यनच्च व्यनच्च<BR> सस्नि Rv. 10. 120. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यपदेश्य
अव्यपदेश्य <i>a.</i> Not to be defined; अलक्षणमचिन्त्यमव्यपदेश्यम् Māṇḍ. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यपेक्षा
अव्यपेक्षा Carelessness; ˚च्यूतने M. 3. 21 inadvertently fallen down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यपोह्य
अव्यपोह्य <i>a.</i> Undeniable, incontestable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारः|अव्यभिचार
अव्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>—1 Not-separation; अन्योऽन्यस्याव्यभीचारो भवेदामरणान्तिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR>—2 Constancy, steadiness, fidelity. <i>a.</i> steady, consistant; मां च<BR> योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्तियोगेन सेवते Bg. 14. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभीचारः|अव्यभीचार
अव्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>—1 Not-separation; अन्योऽन्यस्याव्यभीचारो भवेदामरणान्तिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR>—2 Constancy, steadiness, fidelity. <i>a.</i> steady, consistant; मां च<BR> योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्तियोगेन सेवते Bg. 14. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारिन्
अव्यभिचारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not opposed or adverse, favourable; भवन्त्यव्यभिचारिण्यो भर्तुरिष्टे<BR> पतिव्रताः Ku. 6. 86.<BR>—2 Not subject to exceptions, true in all cases, without any instance<BR> to the contrary; यदुच्यते पार्वति पापवृत्तये न रूपमित्यव्यभिचारि<BR> तद्वचः Ku. 5. 56; रन्ध्रोपनिपातिनोऽनर्था इति यदुच्यते तदव्यभिचारि<BR> वचः Ś. 6; इन्द्रियार्थसंनिकर्षज्ञानमव्यपदेश्यमव्यभिचारि Gaut. S.<BR>—3 Virtuous, moral, Chaste.<BR>—4 Steady, permanent, faithful (as devotion); भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी Bg. 13. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यय|अव्ययं|अव्ययः
अव्यय <i>a.</i> [नास्ति व्ययो यस्य]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Not liable to change, imperishable, undecaying, immutable; वेदाविनाशिनं<BR> नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययम् Bg. 2. 21; विनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित्कर्तुमर्हति<BR> Bg. 2. 17, 4. 1, 6, 13, 7. 24-25, 15. 5, 17; Ms. 1. 18, 19, 57, 2. 81; R. 8. 24.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Eternal, everlasting, अश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम् Bg. 15. 1; अकीर्ति<BR> कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम् Bg. 2. 24.<BR>—2 Unexpended, unwasted.<BR>—3 Economical.<BR>—4 Giving imperishable fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययः|अव्यय|अव्ययं
अव्यय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययम्
अव्यय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 (In the Vedānta) A member or corporeal part of an organized body.<BR>—2 Brahma^1.<BR>—3 (In gram.) An indeclinable particle &c.; सदृशं त्रिषु लिङ्गेषु सर्वासु<BR> च विभक्तिषु । वचनेषु च सर्वेषु यन्न व्येति तदव्ययम् ॥<BR>—4 welfare; युधिष्ठिरमथापृच्छत्सर्वांश्च सुहृदोऽव्ययम् Bhāg. 10. 83. 1.<BR>—5 Prosperity; कुशलं चाव्ययं चैव पर्यपृच्छन्नराधिपम् Rām. 1. 18. 45.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अव्ययात्मन्, अव्ययवर्गः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययात्मन्
अव्यय + -आत्मन् of an imperishable or eternal nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययात्मा
अव्यय + -आत्मन् + .({@-त्मा@}) the soul or spirit. अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा Bg. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययवर्गः|अव्ययवर्ग
अव्यय + -वर्गः the class of indeclinable words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययत्वम्
अव्ययत्वम् Imperishableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययीभावः|अव्ययीभाव
अव्ययीभावः [अनव्ययमव्ययं भवत्यनेन; अव्यय-च्वि-भू करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 N. of one of the four principal kinds of compounds in Sanskrit, an<BR> adverbial or indeclinable compound (formed of an indeclinable, <i>i. e.</i><BR> a preposition or an adverb, and a noun); अधिहरि, सतृणम् &c. पूर्वपदप्रधानोऽव्ययीभावः ।<BR>—2 Absence of expenditure (owing to poverty); द्वन्द्वो द्विगुरपि चाहं<BR> मद्गेहे नित्यमव्ययीभावः । तत्पुरुष कर्मधारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः ॥<BR> Udb. (which, by the bye, gives the names of compounds in Sanskrit).<BR>—3 Unchangeable state, imperishableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यर्ण
अव्यर्ण <i>a.</i> Unoppressed; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यर्थ|अव्यर्थः
अव्यर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not useless or fruitless, fruitful, profitable.<BR>—2 Effectual, successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यलीक
अव्यलीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not false, true.<BR>—2 Agreeable, having no disgreeable feelings (प्रिय); इत्थं गिरः<BR> प्रियतमा इव सोऽव्यलीकाः शुश्राव सूततनयश्च तदा व्यलीकाः Śi. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवच्छिन्न
अव्यवच्छिन्न <i>a.</i> Uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवच्छेदः|अव्यवच्छेद
अव्यवच्छेदः Uninterruptedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधान
अव्यवधान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Close, immediate, without any intervening object, direct.<BR>—2 Not screened or concealed, open.<BR>—3 Not covered, bare (as ground). —4 Careless, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधानम्
अव्यवधान + .{@-नम्@} Carelessness; ˚ता, ˚त्वम् contiguity; carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहित|अव्यवहितं
अव्यवहित <i>a.</i> = अव्यवधान (1) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायः|अव्यवसाय
अव्यवसायः Absence of determination or industry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायिन्
अव्यवसायिन् <i>a.</i> Inactive, negligent; बहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम् Bg. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थ
अव्यवस्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not fixed, moving, unstable; स्थलारविन्दश्रियमव्यवस्थाम् Ku. 1. 33.<BR>—2 Unlimited.<BR>—3 Unsettled, indiscriminate; भङ्गं जयं चापतुरव्यवस्थम् R. 7. 54;<BR> disorderly, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्था
अव्यवस्थ + .{@-स्था@}<BR>—1 Irregularity, deviation from established rule; किमव्यवस्थां चलितोऽपि<BR> केशवः Śi. 12. 36.<BR>—2 An incorrect opinion given on a point of religious or civil law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थित|अव्यवस्थितः
अव्यवस्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not conformable to law or practice, unacquainted with the law or custom.<BR>—2 Ill-regulated, fickle, unstable; अव्यवस्थितचित्तस्य प्रसादोऽपि भयङ्करः Nīti. 9.<BR>—3 Not due order, unmethodical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहार्य|अव्यवहार्य्य|अव्यवहार्य्यं
अव्यवहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not entitled to eat, drink, or commune in general with people of the<BR> same caste, excommunicated.<BR>—2 Not to be made the subject of litigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहृत|अव्यवहृतः
अव्यवहृत <i>a.</i> One who has not made a dealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यविकन्यायः|अव्यविकन्याय
अव्यविकन्यायः After the fashion of <i>avi</i> and <i>avika</i> (<i>i. e.</i><BR> though both these words mean ‘a goat’, a derivation in the sense of ‘goatʼs flesh’<BR> can be formed from <i>avika</i> as <i>āvikam</i> and not from <i>avi</i>;<BR> it would be <i>avermāṃsam</i>) Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसन
अव्यसन <i>a.</i> Free from evil practices, not vicious, moral. धार्मिकोऽव्यसनश्चैव Y. 1. 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसनम्
अव्यसन + .{@-नम्@} Absence of vice, morality, virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यस्त
अव्यस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undecomposed, simple.<BR>—2 Not separated, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकृत
अव्याकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not developed, not manifest; तद्धेदं तर्ह्यव्याकृतमासीत् इदं नामरूपाभ्यामव्याकृतम्<BR> Ś. B.; Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 7.<BR>—2 Not decomposed, elementary.<BR>—3 Incomprehensible (अतर्क्य); अव्याकृत विहाराय सर्वव्याकृतसिद्धये ।<BR> हृषीकेश नमस्तेऽस्तु Bhāg. 10. 16. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकृतम्
अव्याकृत + .{@-तम्@} (In Vedānta Phil.)<BR>—1 An elementary substance from which all things were created (considered<BR> identical with Brahman.)<BR>—2 (In Sāṅ. Phil.) The prime germ of nature (प्रधान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याक्षेपः|अव्याक्षेप
अव्याक्षेपः Absence of confusion or delay; अव्याक्षेपो भविष्यन्त्याः<BR> कार्यसिद्धेर्हि लक्षणम् R. 10. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्या
अव्याख्या, -ख्यानम्<BR> Want of clearness or explanation, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यानम्
अव्याख्या, -ख्यानम्<BR> Want of clearness or explanation, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यात
अव्याख्यात <i>a.</i> Unexplained, obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्येय
अव्याख्येय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inexplicable, unintelligible<BR>—2 Not requiring explanation, easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याज|अव्याजं|अव्याजः
अव्याज <i>a.</i> Free from guile or fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याजः|अव्याज|अव्याजं
अव्याज + .{@-जः, -जम्@}<BR>—1 Absence of guile or fraud, honesty.<BR>—2 Simplicity, artlessness; oft. in comp. with सुन्दर, मनोहर &c.<BR> in the sense of ‘artlessly’, ‘naturally’; इदं किलाव्याजमनोहरं वपुः<BR> Ś. 1. 18; M. 2. 14; ˚रमणीयं प्रेम K. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याजम्
अव्याज + .{@-जः, -जम्@}<BR>—1 Absence of guile or fraud, honesty.<BR>—2 Simplicity, artlessness; oft. in comp. with सुन्दर, मनोहर &c.<BR> in the sense of ‘artlessly’, ‘naturally’; इदं किलाव्याजमनोहरं वपुः<BR> Ś. 1. 18; M. 2. 14; ˚रमणीयं प्रेम K. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापक
अव्यापक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not comprehensive.<BR>—2 Not spread over or pervading the whole; not an invariable concomitant,<BR> special, individual, peculiar; ˚ता, ˚त्वम् non-comprehensiveness, speciality, individuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापिन्
अव्यापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not comprehensive, not invariably concomitant, special, individual.<BR>—2 Partial, limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्त
अव्याप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not pervaded, peculiar, special. अव्याप्ताश्चेदमेध्येन (आपः शुद्धाः) Ms. 5. 128.<BR>—2 Limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्तिः|अव्याप्ति
अव्याप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Inadequate extent or pervasion of a proposition.<BR>—2 Non-inclusion or exclusion of a part of the thing defined, one of the<BR> three faults of a definition; लक्ष्यैकदेशे लक्षणस्यावर्तनमव्याप्तिः;<BR> यथा शिखासूत्रवान् ब्राह्मणः इत्यस्य संन्यासिन्यव्याप्तिः; तस्य ब्राह्मणत्वेऽपि<BR> शिखासूत्रत्वाभावात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्य|अव्याप्यं
अव्याप्य <i>a.</i> Not extending to the whole circumstances, not pervading<BR> the whole extent; वह्निर्धूमस्याव्याप्यः<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अव्याप्यवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्यवृत्तिः|अव्याप्यवृत्ति
अव्याप्य + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> (In Vaiś. Phil.) a category of limited application,<BR> partial inherence with regard to time or space, as pleasure, pain &c.;<BR> अव्याप्तवृत्तिः क्षणिको विशेषगुण इष्यते Bhāṣā P. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापार|अव्यापारः
अव्यापार <i>a.</i> Having no work, unemployed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापारः|अव्यापार
अव्यापार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Cessation from work, state of being unemployed.<BR>—2 A business not practised or understood.<BR>—3 Not oneʼs own business; अव्यापारेषु व्यापारं {@कृ@} to meddle<BR> with affairs not oneʼs own (which do not concern one). cf. अव्यापारेषु<BR> व्यापारं यो नरः कर्तुमिच्छति Pt. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायाम|अव्यायामः
अव्यायाम <i>a.</i> Having no exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायामः|अव्यायाम
अव्यायाम + .{@-मः@} Non-exertion, absence of fatigue from exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायत
अव्यायत <i>a.</i> Not occupied; not detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहत|अव्याहतं
अव्याहत <i>a.</i> Not broken or interrupted, unobstructed; obeyed;<BR> भर्तुरव्याहताज्ञा R. 19. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहतम्
अव्याहत + .{@-तम्@} A true or uncontradicted statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहृतम्
अव्याहृतम् Silence; अव्याहृतं व्याहृताच्छ्रेय आहुः Mb. 5. 36. 12, 12. 299. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्युच्छिन्न
अव्युच्छिन्न <i>a.</i> Continuous, uninterrupted; कच्चित्कुरूणां सौभ्रात्रमव्युच्छिन्नं<BR> भविष्यति Mb. 3. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्युत्पन्न|अव्युत्पन्नः
अव्युत्पन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not proficient, inexperienced, not practised, ignorant; अव्युत्पन्नो<BR> बालभावः K. 196.<BR>—2 Having no proper or regular derivation (as a word) (अवयवार्थशून्य),<BR> उणादयोऽव्युत्पन्नानि प्रातिपदिकानि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्युत्पन्नः|अव्युत्पन्न
अव्युत्पन्न + .{@-न्नः@} A person not versed in the grammar, idiom &c. of a language,<BR> a smattering or superficial linguist (शब्दावयवार्थानभिज्ञोऽवैयाकरणः<BR> Mbh. on 1. 1. 51.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रण
अव्रण <i>a.</i> Without wounds or scars or rents, unhurt, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रणम्
अव्रण + .{@-णम्@} One of the four diseases of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत
अव्रत <i>a.</i> Not observing (the prescribed) religious rites or obligations;<BR> अव्रतानाममन्त्राणां जातिमात्रोपजीविनाम् । सहस्रशः समेतानां परिषत्त्वं<BR> न विद्यते ॥ Ms. 12. 114, 3. 170, 10. 20; Mb. 13. 13. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत्यम्
अव्रत्यम् [व्रताय हितम् यत्, न˚ त˚] Violation of religious<BR> duties, offence against the rule of an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्
अश् I. €5 Ā. [अश्नुते, आनशे, आशिष्ट-आष्ट, अशिता-अष्टा, अशिष्यते-अक्ष्यते,<BR> अशितुम्-अष्टुम्, अशित-अष्ट]<BR>—1 To pervade, fill completely, penetrate; खं प्रावृषेण्यैरिव चानशेऽब्दैः<BR> Bk. 2. 30; सदिगश्नुवानमिव विश्वमोजसा Ki. 12. 21; Śi. 17. 46, 65;<BR>—2 To reach, go or come to, arrive at, attain to; नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्रुते<BR> Bg. 3. 4; सर्वमानन्त्यमश्नुते Y. 1. 261.<BR>—3 To get, gain, obtain, enjoy, experience; अत्युत्कटैः पापपुण्यैरिहैव<BR> फलमश्नुते H. 1. 80; उदयमस्तमयं च रघूद्वहादुभयमानशिरे<BR> वसुधाधिपाः R. 9. 9; न वेदफलमश्नुते Ms. 1. 109, 4. 149, 5. 46;<BR> अर्थज्ञ इत्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते Nir.; फलं दृशोरानशिरे महिष्यः<BR> N. 6. 43; Bg. 3. 4, 5. 21; Bk. 3. 37, 5. 14, 14. 19.<BR>—4 To become master of; to master, to be able (Ved.).<BR>—5 To heap, accumulate. ━<i>With</i> {@अनु@}<BR>—1 to reach, come up to.<BR>—2 to equal.<BR>━{@आ@}<BR>—1 to reach to.<BR>—2 to obtain, get.<BR>—3 to addict oneself to.<BR>━{@उद्@}<BR>—1 to reach to the top of.<BR>—2 to reach, obtain, get<BR>—3 to be master of.<BR>━{@उप@} —1 to obtain, enjoy, acquire. न च लोकानुपाश्नुते Mb.;<BR> क्रियाफलमुपाश्नुते Ms. 6. 82, 12. 20, 81. 2<BR> to become master of.<BR>━{@परि@} to reach, attain; fill completely, pervade.<BR>━{@प्र@} to arrive at, reach, occupy; fill completely.<BR>—2 to fall to the lot of one (acc.). ━II. €9 P. (rarely Ā.) [अश्नाति,<BR> आशीत्, आश, अशिता, अशिष्यति, अशित]<BR>—1 To eat, to consume; निवेद्य गुरवेऽश्नीयात् Ms. 2. 51; अश्नीमहि<BR> वयं भिक्षाम् Bh. 3. 117.<BR>—2 To taste, enjoy; यद्ददाति यदश्नाति तदेव धनिनो धनम् H. 1. 143-44;<BR> अश्नन्ति दिव्यान् दिवि देवभोगान् Bg. 9. 20; प्रत्यक्षं फलमश्नन्ति<BR> कर्मणाम् Mb. ━<i>Caus.</i> (आशयति) To feed, give to eat, cause<BR> to eat or drink (with acc. of person); आशयच्चामृतं देवान् Sk.; Ms. 3. 83, 94, 219, 220;<BR> (for derivatives from the causal see under आ).<BR>━<i>With</i> {@अति@} to precede or surpass in eating.<BR>━{@उप@} to eat; taste, enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन|अशनं|अशनः
अशन [अश्-ल्युट्] <i>a.</i> Reaching, reaching across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनः|अशन|अशनं
अशन + .{@-नः@} N. of a tree = असन q. v. (Mar. आसणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनम्
अशन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Pervasion, penetration.<BR>—2 The act of eating, feeding.<BR>—3 Tasting, enjoying.<BR>—4 Food; अशनं धात्रा मरुत्कल्पितं व्यालानाम् Bh. 3. 10; भांसाशनं<BR> च नाश्नीयुः Ms. 5. 73; यज्ञशिष्ट˚ 3. 118;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">Page0274-1</a>]<BR> फलमूलाशनैः 5. 54; oft. at the end of adjective comp. in<BR> the sense of ‘eating’, ‘one whose food is’ &c.; फलमूलाशन, हुताशन,<BR> पवनाशन &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशनकृत्, अशनपतिः, अशनपर्णी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनकृत्
अशन + -कृत् <i>a.</i> Ved. preparing food; यदशनकृतं ह्वयन्ति हविष्कृतमेव<BR> तद्ध्वयन्ति Av. 9. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनपतिः|अशनपति
अशन + -पतिः lord of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनपर्णी
अशन + -पर्णी a kind of tree. (Mar. गोकर्णी ?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशना
अशना [अशनमिच्छति अशन-क्यच्-क्विप्] Desire to eat, hunger; सुप्तश्चिरं<BR> ह्यशनया च भवान्परीतो Bhāg. 6. 14. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायति
अशनायति Den. P. To desire food, to be hungry; P. VII. 4. 34; यावद्वै<BR> पुरुषस्य स्वं भवति नैव तावदशनायति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनाया
अशनाया [अशनमिच्छति अशन-क्यच् स्त्रियां भावे अ] Hunger; अशनाययाशनाया<BR> हि मृत्युः Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 1. च्युताशनायः फलवद्विभूत्या Bk. 3. 40;<BR> अन्नाद्वाऽशनाया निवर्तते पानात्पिपासा Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायित|अशनायितं
अशनायित, अशनायुक <i>a.</i> Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायुक
अशनायित, अशनायुक <i>a.</i> Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायितम्
अशनायित, अशनायुक + .{@-तम्@} Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित|अशितं
अशित <i>p. p.</i> [अश्-कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Eaten, निरृतिरशिता अशिता लोकाच्छिनत्ति ब्रह्मगवी Av. 12. 5. 37-38; satisfied.<BR>—2 Enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितम्
अशित + .{@-तम्@} The place where anybody has eaten; अधिकरण वाचिनश्च P. II. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितंगवीन|अशितङ्गवीन|अशितङ्गवीनं
अशितंगवीन <i>a.</i> Formerly grazed by cattle; see आशितंगवीन; P. V. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितृ
अशितृ <i>a.</i> [अश्-तृच्] An eater, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिन्
अशिन् <i>a.</i> [अश्-णिनि] Reaching far; enduring, lasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुनः|अशकुन|अशकुनं
अशकुनः, -नम्<BR> An inauspicious or bad omen; कलयन्नपि सव्यथोऽवतस्थेऽशकुनेन<BR> स्खलितः किलेतरोऽपि । Śi. 9. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुनम्
अशकुनः, -नम्<BR> An inauspicious or bad omen; कलयन्नपि सव्यथोऽवतस्थेऽशकुनेन<BR> स्खलितः किलेतरोऽपि । Śi. 9. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुनीभू
अशकुनीभू To turn into an auspicious omen. साह स्म नैवाशकुनीभवेन्मे<BR> भाविप्रियावेदक एष हंसः N. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुम्भी
अशकुम्भी <i>f.</i> The acquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes (आकाशमूली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्त|अशक्तं
अशक्त <i>a.</i> Unable, incompetent;<BR> {@˚ता, -त्वम्@} inability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्ति|अशक्तिः
अशक्ति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Weakness, impotence, powerlessness.<BR>—2 Inability, incapacity; श्रमेण तदशक्त्या वा न गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>—3 (In Sāṅ. Phil.) Incapacity of the intellect to produce knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्य|अशक्यं
अशक्य <i>a.</i> Impossible, impracticable^1, यदशक्यं न तच्छक्यम्<BR> H. 1. 87. अशक्यशङ्कव्यभिचारहेतुर्वाणी न वेदा यदि सन्ति के तु N.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशक्यार्थ<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्यार्थ
अशक्य + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> unavailing, useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्क|अशंक
अशङ्क, अशङ्कित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fearless, undaunted; प्रविशत्यशङ्कः H. 1. 78.<BR>—2 Secure, certain, having no doubt. यं शिष्टा ब्राह्मणा ब्रूयुः स धर्मः<BR> स्यादशङ्कितः Ms. 12. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्कित|अशंकित
अशङ्क, अशङ्कित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fearless, undaunted; प्रविशत्यशङ्कः H. 1. 78.<BR>—2 Secure, certain, having no doubt. यं शिष्टा ब्राह्मणा ब्रूयुः स धर्मः<BR> स्यादशङ्कितः Ms. 12. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशठ
अशठ <i>a.</i> Sincere, honest; अजिह्मस्याशठस्य च दासवर्गस्य<BR> भागधेयम् Ms. 3. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रु|अशत्रुः
अशत्रु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who has no enemy.<BR>—2 One whom no enemy defies or challenges.<BR>—3 Without opposition from foes. अशत्र्वर्यः समजाति वेदः Rv. 5. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रु|अशत्रुः
अशत्रु + .{@-त्रु@} <i>n.</i> The condition of having no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रुः|अशत्रु
अशत्रु + .{@-त्रुः@} The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन्
अशन् <i>m.</i> Ved. A stone for slinging; a stone or cloud. अश्नापिनद्धं<BR> मधु पर्यपश्यन् Rv. 10. 68. 8; दश प्राक् सानु वि तिरन्त्यश्नः Rv. 10. 27. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनिः|अशनि
अशनिः <i>m., f.</i> [अश्नुते संहति, अश् अनि Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>—1 Indraʼs thunderbolt; शक्रस्य महाशनिध्वजम् R. 3. 56.<BR>—2 Flash of lightning; अनुवनमशनिर्गतः Sk.; अशनिः कल्पित एष<BR> वेधसा R. 8. 47; अशनेरमृतस्य चोभयोर्वशिनश्चाम्बुधराश्च योनयः Ku. 4. 43.<BR>—3 A missile. अष्टचक्रां महाघोरामशनिं रुद्रनिर्मिताम् Mb. 7. 175. 96.<BR>—4 The tip of a missile.<BR>—5 A sacrificial rite (अनुयाज) to kill an enemy.<BR>—6 A master.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशनिदण्डः, अशनिनि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनिदण्डः
अशनिः + -दण्डः The thunderbolt. निर्भिद्याशनिदण्डचण्डतरया चञ्च्वाधुना<BR> वक्षसि Nāg. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनिनि
अशनिः + -नि <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Indra.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 Fire produced from lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशब्द|अशब्दः
अशब्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not expressed in words; किमर्थमशब्दं रुद्यते K. 60 inaudibly.<BR>—2 what is not actually expressed by a sacred word; न ह्यशब्दं प्रतीयते Ms. 4. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशब्दः|अशब्द
अशब्द + .{@-ब्दः@} Slander, abuse^1; दिवं स्पृशत्यशब्दोऽस्य त्रस्यन्ति पितरश्च<BR> वै Mb. 13. 126. 30.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशब्दम्
अशब्द + .{@-ब्दम्@}<BR>—1 The ‘Inexpressible’, <i>i. e.</i> Brahman.<BR>—2 (In Sāṅ. Phil.) प्रधान or primary germ of nature; ईक्षतेर्नाशब्दम्<BR> Ś. B. 1. 1. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशब्दार्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशब्दार्थः
अशब्द + -अर्थः<BR>——(<i>a</i>) sense not expressed by the word; अशब्दार्थो हि तदा आश्रीयेत ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 33; also न आनर्थक्यमापततीति अशब्दार्थः कल्पनीयः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 56.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) That which is not the direct signification of a word; अशब्दार्थोऽपि<BR> हि प्रतीयते । ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशम्
अशम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Non-welfare, harm, mischief. शं नो देवी पृश्निपर्ण्यशं<BR> निरृत्या अकः Av. 2. 25. 1; अशं केन शाम्यति Ki. 15. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरण
अशरण <i>a.</i> Helpless, forlorn, destitute of refuge; बलवदशरणोऽस्मि<BR> Ś. 6; so अशरण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीर|अशरीरः
अशरीर <i>a.</i> Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरः|अशरीर
अशरीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The Supreme Being (परमात्मन्), Brahman.<BR>—2 (In Mīmāṃsā) A god or deity in general.<BR>—3 Cupid, the god of love चेतांसि चिन्ताभिरिवाशरीरः Ki. 17. 10; Śi. 9. 61.<BR>—4 An ascetic who has renounced all worldly connections; ˚त्वम्, ˚ता absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरिन्
अशरीरिन् <i>a.</i> Incorporeal, unearthly, heavenly; usually; with words<BR> like वाणी, वाक् &c. U. 2; Ve. 3; Ś. 4.<BR>—1 Brahmā.<BR>—2 A God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशर्मन्|अशर्म्मन्
अशर्मन् <i>a.</i> Unhappy, afflicted, sorry. <i>n.</i> Unhappiness, misery,<BR> affliction, sorrow; एकौघभूतं तदशर्म कृष्णाम् (प्रपेदे) Ki. 3. 35, 12. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्
अशस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not blessing, not praising.<BR>—2 Cursing, hating; रुद्रा अशसो हन्तना वधः Rv. 2. 34. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त
अशस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inexpressible, untold.<BR>—2 Not esteemed, hated, ill-starred; unwished; परोऽपेहि मनस्पाप किमशस्तानि<BR> शंससि Av. 6. 45. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशस्तवार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्तवार
अशस्त + -वार <i>a.</i> Ved. who is not asked for wealth, <i>i. e.</i> who grants<BR> it of his own accord; स रुद्रेभिरशस्तवार ऋभ्वा Rv. 10. 99. 5; having<BR> indescribable treasures (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0274-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्तिः|अशस्ति
अशस्तिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not wishing well, an evil wish or design, curse, imprecation; प्र<BR> यो भनक्ति वनुषामशस्तीः Rv. 6. 68. 6.<BR>—2 A curser, hater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त्र
अशस्त्र <i>a.</i> Having no weapons, unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त्रम्
अशस्त्र + .{@-स्त्रम्@} Not a weapon; ˚विहितो वधः H. 2. 85; ˚पूतं मरणमुपदिशामि<BR> Ve. 2 (आत्मघातित्वेन शस्त्रेण न पूतम्); अशस्त्रपूतम् Māl. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशान्त|अशांत
अशान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not quelled, violent, wild, restless, anxious; नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य<BR> न चायुक्तस्य भावना … अशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम् Mb.<BR>—2 Not sacred, irreligious, profane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाब्द
अशाब्द <i>a.</i> Not conveyed by the word; अशाब्द इति चेत् स्याद् वाक्यशब्दत्वात् ।<BR> Ms. 5. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाम्य
अशाम्य <i>a.</i> Unappeasable, implacable, irreconcilable (as hatred, enmity &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशारीरिक
अशारीरिक = अशरीरिन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाश्वत
अशाश्वत <i>a.</i> Perishable, transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासन
अशासन <i>a.</i> Having no order or rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासनम्
अशासन + .{@-नम्@} Want of government, anarchy, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासनीय
अशासनीय <i>a.</i> Ungovernable, unruly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्र
अशास्त्र <i>a.</i> Not conformable to sacred authority, not scriptural, heterodox.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशास्त्रविहित, अशास्त्रसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रविहित
अशास्त्र + -विहित, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> not sanctioned or enjoined by scriptures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रसिद्ध
अशास्त्र + -विहित, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> not sanctioned or enjoined by scriptures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रीय
अशास्त्रीय <i>a.</i> Unscriptural, heterodox; illegal, immoral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित्रः|अशित्र
अशित्रः [अश्-संह्वतौ इत्र Uṇ. 4. 172] —1 A thief. —2 An oblation of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिथिल
अशिथिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not loose, tight, firm.<BR>—2 Effective, reliable; Mb. 3. अशिथिलपरिरम्भैर्दत्तसंवाहनानि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरः|अशिर|अशिरं
अशिरः [अश्-इरच्]<BR>—1 The fire.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 Wind.<BR>—4 A demon; N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरा
अशिरः + .{@-रा@} The wife of a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरम्
अशिरः + .{@-रम्@} A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्
अशिरस् <i>a.</i> Headless; Ms. 9. 237. ━<i>m.</i> A body without head, a trunk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशिरःस्नानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरःस्नानम्
अशिरस् + -स्नानम् bathing the whole body except the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्क
अशिरस्क <i>a.</i> Headless; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिव|अशिवः
अशिव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inauspicious, causing or threatening mischief; अशिवा दिशि दीप्तायां<BR> शिवास्तत्र भयावहाः (रुरुवुः) Rām.<BR>—2 Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR>—3 Unkind, unfriendly, envious.<BR>—4 Pernicious, dangerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवः|अशिव
अशिव + .{@-वः@} N. of a certain divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवा
अशिव + .{@-वा@} A female demon or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवम्
अशिव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Ill-luck, misfortune; grief; आपूरितं विमानं तद्भयशोकाशिवाश्नुभिः<BR> Rām. 7. 24. 5.<BR>—2 Mischief.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशिवाचारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवाचारः|अशिवाचार
अशिव + -आचारः<BR>—1 improper behaviour, rudeness of conduct.<BR>—2 conduct opposed to every (sacred) authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशिर
अशिशिर <i>a.</i> Not cool, hot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशिशिरकरः, अशिशिररश्मिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशिरकरः|अशिशिरकर
अशिशिर + -करः, -रश्मिः The sun; नीतोच्छ्रायं मुहुरशिशिररश्मेरुस्रैः Ki. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशिररश्मिः|अशिशिररश्मि
अशिशिर + -करः, -रश्मिः The sun; नीतोच्छ्रायं मुहुरशिशिररश्मेरुस्रैः Ki. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशिषु
अशिशिषु^1 <i>a.</i> (Fr. desiderative of अश्) Hungry.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशु|अशिशुः
अशिशु <i>a.</i> Childless, without young ones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशुः|अशिशु
अशिशु + .{@-शुः@} A youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्वीः
अशिशु + .{@-श्वीः, -अशिश्विका@}<BR>—1 A childless female; without young ones (as a cow); स्तनाभुजो अशिश्वीः Rv. 1. 120. 8.<BR>—2 A childless woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्विका
अशिशु + .{@-श्वीः, -अशिश्विका@}<BR>—1 A childless female; without young ones (as a cow); स्तनाभुजो अशिश्वीः Rv. 1. 120. 8.<BR>—2 A childless woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ट
अशिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ill-bred, ill-behaved, rude.<BR>—2 Unrefined, barbarous, not respectable, unworthy; ˚आलापेन Pt. 4.<BR>—3 Atheistical, profane.<BR>—4 Not sanctioned by any recognized authority.<BR>—5 Not left; शिष्टानशिष्टान्नि तिरामिवाचा Av. 2. 31. 3.<BR>—6 Not prescribed in any work of authority; ˚ता, ˚त्वम् rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्य
अशिष्य <i>a.</i> Not to be taught, not to be informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ठ|अशिष्ठः
अशिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eating much.<BR>—2 Ved. Reaching very far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ठः|अशिष्ठ
अशिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@} Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अशीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not cold, hot.<BR>—2 The eightieth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशीतकरः, अशीतरश्मिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतकरः|अशीतकर
अशीत + -करः, -रश्मिः &c. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतरश्मिः|अशीतरश्मि
अशीत + -करः, -रश्मिः &c. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतल
अशीतल <i>a.</i> Hot; दधत्युरोजद्वयमुर्वशीतलम् Śi. 9. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिः|अशीति
अशीतिः <i>f.</i> [निपातोयम् P. V. 1. 59] Eighty (used in the singular<BR> and fem. gender whatever be the number and gender of the noun it qualifies);<BR> sometimes in dual and pl.; पिण्डानां तिस्रोऽशीतीः Ms. 11. 220.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशीतितम, अशीतिभागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतितम
अशीतिः + -तम <i>a.</i> Eightieth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिभागः|अशीतिभाग
अशीतिः + -भागः the eightieth part, one part of eighty; अशीतिभागं गृह्णीयान्मासाद्वार्धुषिकः<BR> शते Śi. 9. 86; Ms. 8. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिक
अशीतिक <i>a.</i> [अशीतिः परिमाणं यस्य, ठन्]<BR>—1 An octogenerian, one eighty years of age.<BR>—2 Measuring eighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिकावर
अशीतिकावर <i>a.</i> Being at least eighty years of age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीर्षक
अशीर्षक <i>a.</i> = अशिरस्^1 q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशील
अशील <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ill-behaved, vulgar, rude.<BR>—2 Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीलम्
अशील + .{@-लम्@} Bad manners, rudeness, depravity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचि|अशुचिः
अशुचि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not clean, dirty, foul, impure; पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ Bg. 16. 16.<BR> सोऽशुचिः सर्वकर्मसु; in mourning; त्रिरात्रमशुचिर्भवेत्.<BR>—2 Black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचिः|अशुचि
अशुचि + .{@-चिः@} The black colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचिः|अशुचि
अशुचि + .{@-चिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Impurity.<BR>—2 Degradation; ˚ता (= ग्रीष्माभावः)<BR>—1 Absence of purity.<BR>—2 (= ग्रीष्माभावः) The months of ज्येष्ठ and आषाढ (cf. वैशाखे<BR> माधवो, राधो ज्येष्ठः शुक्रः शुचिस्त्वयम् । आषाढे श्रावणे तु स्यात् नभाः<BR> श्रावणिकश्च सः ॥ Ak.; अशुचिता यदि केलिवने, कथं शुचिरवचिरवाचितषट्पदैः ।<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 20.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्ध|अशुद्धं
अशुद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impure, foul.<BR>—2 Inaccurate, incorrect, wrong.<BR>—3 Unknown, unascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धम्
अशुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} Blood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशुद्धवासकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धवासकः|अशुद्धवासक
अशुद्ध + -वासकः a vagrant, a suspicious person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धि|अशुद्धिः
अशुद्धि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impure, foul.<BR>—2 Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धिः|अशुद्धि
अशुद्धि + .{@-द्धिः@} <i>f.</i> Impurity, foulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधन
अशोधन, -धित <i>a.</i><BR> Unclean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधित
अशोधन, -धित <i>a.</i><BR> Unclean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधनम्
अशोधन, -धित + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Uncleanliness.<BR>—2 Inaccuracy, incorrectness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभ|अशुभं
अशुभ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inauspicious.<BR>—2 Impure, dirty, foul (opp. शुभ); शुभेनाशुभेन वोपायेन K. 158<BR> by any means, fair or foul.<BR>—3 Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभम्
अशुभ + .{@-भम्@}<BR>—1 Inauspiciousness.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">Page0276-1</a>]<BR>—2 sin, a shameful deed.<BR>—3 Misfortune, calamity; नाथे कुतस्त्वग्यशुभं प्रजानाम् R. 5. 13;<BR> प्रायः शुभं विदधात्यशुभं च जन्तोः Māl. 1. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशुभोदयः, अशुभदर्शन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0275-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभोदयः|अशुभोदय
अशुभ + -उदयः an inauspicious omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभदर्शन
अशुभ + -दर्शन <i>a.</i> ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुष
अशुष <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Eating, consuming, voracious.<BR>—2 [न शुष्यति शुष्क. न˚ त˚] Not causing to dry up; रक्षो<BR> अग्निमशुषं तूर्वयाणम् Rv. 1. 174. 3.<BR>—3 Not extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशूकजा
अशूकजा A kind of rice (Mar. दोडक्यार्चे भात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्य
अशून्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not empty or vacant; तस्य निन्यतुरशून्यतामुभे R. 19. 13; occupied.<BR>—2 Not unattended to, fulfilled, executed; स्वनियोगमशून्यं कुरु<BR> (occurring frequently in dramas), execute or go about your business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्यम्
अशून्य + .{@-न्यम्@}<BR>—1 Not a void.<BR>—2 Something sent to accompany another; लेखस्याशून्यार्थं किंचिदनुप्रेषितम्<BR> Mu. 5; अयं लेखशून्यार्थो भविष्यति <i>ibid.</i> (an accompaniment such<BR> as a customary present accompanying a letter).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अशून्योपस्था, अशून्यशयनम्, अशून्यशयनद्वितीया, अशून्यशयनव्रतं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्योपस्था
अशून्य + -उपस्था <i>a.</i> woman whose womb is not empty, married. अशून्योपस्था<BR> जीवतामस्तु माता … प्रबुध्यताम्; सत्याषाढसूत्र 19. 6; Pāraskara Gṛhyasūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्यशयनम्
अशून्य + -शयनम् The day on which the Viśvakarman rests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्यशयनद्वितीया
अशून्य + -शयनद्वितीया, -शयनव्रतं N. of a certain ceremony or vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0276-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

