अश्वकः|अश्वक
अश्वक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A small horse; horse.<BR>—2 A hack, a bad horse; ससत्यश्वकः सुभद्रिकां काम्पीलवासिनीम् Vāj. 23. 18.<BR>—3 A stray horse, one whose owner is not known.<BR>—4 A horse (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकिनी
अश्वकिनी [अश्वस्य कं मुखं तत्सदृशाकारोऽस्त्यस्य इनि डीप् Tv.]<BR> The first Nakṣatra or lunar mansion (अश्विनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर <i>a.</i> Swift, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतरः|अश्वतर
अश्वतर + .{@-रः@} [तनुः अश्वः, अश्व तनुत्वे ष्टरच्, P. V. 3. 91]<BR>—1 A mule; Av. 4. 4. 8.<BR>—2 One of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent-race inhabiting the lower regions.<BR>—3 A male calf. —4 A class of Gandharvas. cf. अश्वतरः सुरवाजिनोः … । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतरी
अश्वतर + .{@-री@} A mule; व्यजायन्त खरा गोषु करभाऽश्वतरीषु च Mb. 16. 2. 9;<BR> उदरस्य समुत्थाने स्वगर्भोऽश्वतरीमिव Rām.; Pt. 2. 32; Cāṇ. 19.<BR> [cf. Pers. <i>aster</i>.].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अश्वतररथ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतररथ
अश्वतर + -रथ A chariot drawn by a she-mule. Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वति
अश्वति Den. P. To behave like a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थः|अश्वत्थ
अश्वत्थः [न श्वश्चिरं शाल्मलीवृक्षादिवत् तिष्ठति स्था-क पृषो.<BR> नित्यस. Tv.]<BR>—1 The holy fig tree; ऊर्ध्वमूलोऽवाक्शाख एषोऽश्वत्थः सनातनः Kaṭh.;<BR> the tree of this world; ऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम्<BR> Bg. 15. 1. (Mar. पिंपळ).<BR>—2 A kind of the Aśvattha tree (नन्दीवृक्ष; Mar. नांदुरखी).<BR>—3 N. of another tree गर्दभाण्ड (Mar. लाखी पिंपरी)<BR>—4 The constellation Aśvinī.<BR>—5 The time indicated or presided over by Aśvinī; अश्वत्थो मुहूर्तः<BR> Sk. on संज्ञायां श्रवणाश्वत्थाभ्याम् P. IV. 2. 5.<BR>—6 A vessel made of the अश्वत्थ tree (Ved.).<BR>—7 The fruit of the sacred fig-tree; अश्वत्थस्य फलमश्वत्थः Sk.<BR>—8 The time at which it bears fruit; अश्वत्थफलयुक्तः कालोऽप्यश्वत्थः<BR> P. IV. 3. 48. Sk.<BR>—9 An epithet of the Sun.<BR>—10 N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">Page0281-1</a>]<BR> a people; Bṛ. S. 14. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्था
अश्वत्थः + .{@-त्था@} The day of the full moon in the month of Āśvina, (in which<BR> month the fruits of the sacred fig-tree generally become ripe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थी
अश्वत्थः + .{@-त्थी@} [क्षुद्रोऽश्वत्थः अल्पार्थे ङीप्] A small fig-tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अश्वत्थकुणः, अश्वत्थफला, अश्वत्थभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थकुणः|अश्वत्थकुण
अश्वत्थः + -कुणः [अश्वत्थस्य पाकः पील्वादि˚ कुणप् P. V. 2. 24] the fruit-season<BR> of the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थफला
अश्वत्थः + -फला N. of a tree (Mar. लघुशेरणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थभेदः|अश्वत्थभेद
अश्वत्थः + -भेदः N. of a tree (स्थालीवृक्ष) Ficus Benjamina^1. (Mar. पाडळी ?)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थक|अश्वत्थकः
अश्वत्थक <i>a.</i> To be given or to be done when the Aśvattha tree bears fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थकः|अश्वत्थक
अश्वत्थक + .{@-कः@} [अश्वत्थस्तत्फलम् तद्युक्तः कालोऽप्यश्वत्थस्तत्र देयमृणम्<BR> वुन् P. IV. 3. 48. Sk.]<BR>—1 A debt to be given when the Aśvattha tree bears fruits.<BR>—2 [स्वार्थे कन्] The Aśvattha tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थामन्
अश्वत्थामन् <i>m.</i> [अश्वस्येव स्थाम बलमस्य, पृषो˚ समासः;<BR> cf. Mb. अश्वस्येवास्य यत्स्थाम नदतः प्रदिशो गतम् । अश्वत्थामैव बालोऽयं<BR> तस्मान्नाम्ना भविष्यति ॥] N. of a celebrated Brāhmaṇa warrior and<BR> general on the side of the Kauravas, son of Droṇa and Kṛpī. [After<BR> the last great battle in which Duryodhana was mortally wounded, Aśvatthāman,<BR> with two other surviving Kauravas, entered the Paṇdava camp at night,<BR> where he stamped Dhṛṣṭadyumna, the slayer of his father, to death<BR> and killed the five young sons of the Pāṇḍavas, killing even Parīkṣit<BR> while yet in the motherʼs womb who was, however, restored to life by Kṛṣṇa.<BR> The next morning Draupadī clamoured for revenge upon the murderer of<BR> her children, but she consented to forego her demand for his blood if the<BR> precious jewel he wore on his head were brought to her. Bhīma, Arjuna,<BR> and Kṛṣṇa overtook Aśvatthāman and compelled him to yield the jewel<BR> which, Yudhiṣṭhira afterwards wore on his head. He is represented as<BR> a very brave, fiery-tempered, young warrior, the embodiment of Brāhmanic<BR> and saintly lustre, and his altercation with Karṇa about the nomination<BR> of a general to succeed Droṇa clearly brings out the chief features of<BR> his character; see Ve. 3rd act. He is one of the 7 <i>Chirajivins</i><BR> ‘ever-living persons’.] cf. अश्वत्थामा बलिर्व्यासो हनूमांश्च विभीषणः ।<BR> कृपः परशुरामश्च सप्तैते चिरजीविनः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थिक
अश्वत्थिक <i>a.</i> [अश्वत्थेन चरति. ष्ठन् P. IV. 4. 10] Feeding<BR> on Aśvattha fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थिल
अश्वत्थिल <i>a.</i> See P. IV. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वयति
अश्वयति Den. P. To wish for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वया
अश्वया A desire to get horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वयु
अश्वयु <i>a.</i> [अश्वोऽस्त्यस्य युच्]<BR>—1 Having horses.<BR>—2 Desiring horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वलः|अश्वल
अश्वलः [अश्वं लाति ला-क.] N. of a sage, the Hotṛpriest of<BR> Janaka; अथ ह जनकस्य वैदेहस्य होताऽश्वलो बभूव Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्यति
अश्वस्यति Den. P. To wish for a stallion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वायति
अश्वायति Den. P. To wish for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विक
अश्विक <i>a.</i> [P. IV. 4. 10] Drawn or carried by horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन् <i>a.</i> [अश्व-अस्त्यर्थे इनि] Possessed of horses, consisting<BR> of horses; Rv. 4. 2. 5 ━<i>m.</i> A cavalier, a horse-tamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनौ
अश्विन् + .{@-नौ@} (du.)<BR>—1 The two physicians of the gods who are represented as the twin sons<BR> of the Sun by a nymph in the form of a mare; cf. त्वाष्ट्री तु सवितुर्भार्या<BR> वडवारूपधारिणी । असूयत महाभागा सान्तरीक्षेऽश्विनावुभौ ॥ [According<BR> to Vedic conception they are the harbingers of Uṣas or the dawn; they<BR> are young, beautiful, bright, swift &c.; and, according to Yāska, they<BR> represent the transition from darkness to light, when the intermingling<BR> of both produces that inseparable duality expressed by the twin nature<BR> of these deities; according to different interpretations quoted in the<BR> Nirukta they were ‘heaven and earth’, ‘day and night’, ‘two kings, performers of holy acts’<BR> which may be traced to their dual and luminous nature. Mythically<BR> they were the parents of Nakula and Sahadeva and the physicians of the<BR> gods and are called <i>Gadāgadau, Svarvaidyau, Dasrau, Nāsatyau, Vāḍaveyau</i>,<BR> <i>Abdhijau</i> &c. They were celebrated for their active benevolence and<BR> curative power which they showed in restoring the sage Cyavana, when<BR> grown old and decrepit, to youth, and prolonged his life.]<BR>—2 Two horses.<BR>—3 (In astr.) The twins of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनी
अश्विनी [अश्वस्तदुत्तमाङ्गाकारोऽस्त्यस्य इनि ङीप्]<BR>—1 The first of the 27 Nakṣatras or lunar mansions (consisting of three stars).<BR>—2 A nymph considered in later times as the mother of the Aśvins, the<BR> wife of the Sun, who concealed herself in the form of a mare^1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अश्विनीकुमारौ, अश्विनीपुत्रौ, अश्विनीसुतौ<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीकुमारौ
अश्विनी + -कुमारौ, -पुत्रौ, -सुतौ the twin sons of Aśvinī, the Sunʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीपुत्रौ
अश्विनी + -कुमारौ, -पुत्रौ, -सुतौ the twin sons of Aśvinī, the Sunʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीसुतौ
अश्विनी + -कुमारौ, -पुत्रौ, -सुतौ the twin sons of Aśvinī, the Sunʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विमत्|अश्विमन्त्
अश्विमत् <i>a.</i> Containing the word Aśvin (such as a Mantra). P. IV. 4. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विय
अश्विय <i>a.</i> Referring to horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विया
अश्विय + .{@-या@} Ved. (pl.). A troop of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीन|अश्वीनः
अश्वीन <i>a.</i> [अश्व-ख] Distant, a dayʼs journey for a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीय|अश्वीयं|अश्वीयः
अश्वीय <i>a.</i> [अश्व-छ] —1 Belonging or relating to a horse, agreeable to horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीयम्
अश्वीय + .{@-यम्@} [अश्वानां समूहः P. IV. 2. 48] A number of horses, cavalry;<BR> अश्वीयानामुच्चकैरुच्चलन्तः Śi. 18. 5; K. 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्य|अश्व्यः
अश्व्य <i>a.</i> [अश्व-यत्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a horse.<BR>—2 Consisting of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्यम्
अश्व्य + .{@-श्व्यम्@} A number of horses.<BR>—3 Possession of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्यः|अश्व्य
अश्व्य + .{@-श्व्यः@} ‘son of Aśva’, N. of Vaśa; याभिर्वशमश्व्यं प्रेणिमावतम्<BR> Rv. 1. 112. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वन्त|अश्वंत|अश्वन्तं|अश्वन्तः
अश्वन्त <i>a.</i> See अश्मन्त.<BR>—1 Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>—2 Unbounded, unlimited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वन्तः|अश्वन्त|अश्वंत|अश्वन्तं
अश्वन्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 Death.<BR>—2 A field.<BR>—3 Fireplace.<BR>—4 Termination, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तन
अश्वस्तन, -स्तनिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not of to-morrow, of to-day.<BR>—2 One who makes no provision for the morrow; त्र्यहैहिको वापि भवेदश्वस्तनिक<BR> एव वा Ms. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तनिक
अश्वस्तन, -स्तनिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not of to-morrow, of to-day.<BR>—2 One who makes no provision for the morrow; त्र्यहैहिको वापि भवेदश्वस्तनिक<BR> एव वा Ms. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्
अष् €1 U. [अषति-ते, अषितुम्]<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To go, move.<BR>—3 To receive, take (trans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्ष
अषडक्ष = अषडक्षीण. The ending ईन is स्वार्थे; <i>i. e.</i><BR> both अषडक्ष and अषडक्षीण mean the same thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीण|अषडक्षीणः
अषडक्षीण <i>a.</i> Not seen by six eyes, known or determined by two<BR> persons only, (to the exclusion of a third); [˚णो मंत्रः द्वाभ्यामेव<BR> कृत इत्यर्थः P. V. 4. 7. Sk.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीणम्
अषडक्षीण + .{@-णम्@} A secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषतर
अषतर <i>a.</i> Ved. More accessible or acceptable; वा कर्माषतरास्मै<BR> प्र च्यौत्नानि देवयन्तो भरन्ते Rv. 1. 173. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढ|अषाढः
अषाढ <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not to be overcome, invincible; अषाळहाय सहमानाय वेधसे Rv. 2. 21. 2.<BR>—2 Born under the constellation Āṣāḍha [P. IV. 3. 34]. अथाजिनाषाढधरः प्रमाथी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढः|अषाढ
अषाढ + .{@-ढः@}<BR>—1 The month Āṣāḍha commencing with the Sunʼs entrance into Gemini<BR> (usually written आषाढ).<BR>—2 A staff made of the wood of Palāśa, carried by a religious student or ascetic.<BR>—3 N. of the Malaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढा
अषाढ + .{@-ढा@} —1 N. of a constellation, the twentieth (पूर्वाषाढा) and<BR> twenty-first (उत्तराषाढा) lunar mansions; Av. 19. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढकः|अषाढक
अषाढकः The month of Āṣāḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन् <i>num. a.</i> [अश-व्याप्तौ कनिन् तुट् च Uṇ. 1. 154.] (nom.,<BR> acc. अष्ट-ष्टौ) Eight. It often occurs in comp. as अष्टा with numerals<BR> and some other nouns; as अष्टादशन्, अष्टाविंशतिः, अष्टापद &c. [cf.<BR> L. <i>octo</i>; Gr. <i>okto</i>; Zend. <i>astani</i> Pers. <i>hasht</i>.].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अष्टाक्षर, अष्टाङ्ग, अष्टाधिकाराः, अष्टाध्यायी, अष्टान्नानि, अष्टार, अष्टास्रम्, अष्टास्रः, अष्टास्रिय, अष्टाह, अष्टाहन्, अष्टादिशाब्दिकाः, अष्टापाद्य, अष्टोपद्वीपानि, अष्टकपाल, अष्टकर्ण, अष्टकुलम्, अष्टकुलाचलाः, अष्टकृत्वस्, अष्टकोणः, अष्टखण्डः, अष्टगन्धाः, अष्टगवम्, अष्टगाढ्, अष्टगुण, अष्टचत्वारिंशत्, अष्टाचत्वारिंशत्, अष्टतय, अष्टतारिणी, अष्टतालम्, अष्टत्रिंशत्, अष्टत्रिकम्, अष्टदलम्, अष्टादशन्, अष्टदिश्, अष्टदेहाः, अष्टद्रव्यम्, अष्टधातुः, अष्टनागाः, अष्टनायिकाः, अष्टपक्ष, अष्टपद, अष्टपद्, अष्टपदः, अष्टपदिका, अष्टपादिका, अष्टपदी, अष्टपलम्, अष्टपाद्य, अष्टपुत्र, अष्टप्रधानाः, अष्टभावाः, अष्टभैरवाः, अष्टभोगाः, अष्टमङ्गलः, अष्टमङ्गलघृत, अष्टमधु, अष्टमहारसाः, अष्टमहारोगाः, अष्टमहासिद्धयः, अष्टमातृकाः, अष्टमुद्राः, अष्टमानम्, अष्टमासिक, अष्टमुष्टिः, अष्टमूत्राणि, अष्टमूर्तिः, अष्टमूर्तयः, अष्टयोगिन्यः, अष्टरत्नम्, अष्टरसाः, अष्टलवणानि, अष्टलोहकम्, अष्टवर्गः, अष्टवक्रः, अष्टवर्ष, अष्टवसु, अष्टवायनानि, अष्टविनायकाः, अष्टविवाहाः, अष्टविध, अष्टाविंशतिः, अष्टशतम्, अष्टश्रवणः, अष्टश्रवस्, अष्टसमाधयः, अष्टसिद्धयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाक्षर|अष्टाक्षरः
अष्टन् + -अक्षर <i>a.</i> consisting of eight letters or parts; अष्टाक्षरं<BR> ह वा एकं गायत्र्यै पदम् Bṛ. Up. 5. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाक्षरः|अष्टाक्षर
अष्टन् + -अक्षर + .({@-रः@}) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्ग|अष्टांग
अष्टन् + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> consisting of eight parts or members.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गम्
अष्टन् + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गम्@})<BR>—1 the eight parts of the body with which a very low obeisance is performed;<BR> ˚पातः, -प्रणामः, साष्टाङ्गनमस्कारः a respectful obeisance made<BR> by the prostration of the eight limbs of the body; साष्टाङ्गपातं प्रणनाम<BR> fell prostrate on the ground in reverence; (जानुभ्यां च तथा पद्भ्यां<BR> पाणिभ्यामुरसा धिया । शिरसा वचसा दृष्ट्या प्रणामोऽष्टाङ्ग ईरितः).<BR> cf. also उरसा शिरसा दृष्ट्या वचसा मनसा तथा । पद्भ्यां कराभ्यां<BR> जानुभ्यां प्रणामोऽष्टाङ्ग उच्यते ॥ The eight limbs of the body in नमस्कार.<BR>—2 the 8 parts of yoga or concentration; यमो नियमश्चासनं च प्राणायामस्ततः<BR> परम् । प्रत्याहारो धारणा च ध्यानं सार्धं समाधिना । अष्टाङ्गान्याहुरेतानि<BR> योगिनां योगसिद्धये ॥<BR>—3 materials of worship taken collectively, namely, water, milk, ghee,<BR> curds, दर्भ, rice, barley, mustard seed.<BR>—4 the eight parts of every medical science; (they are:− शल्यम्, शालाक्यम्,<BR> कायचिकित्सा, भूतविद्या,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">Page0282-2</a>]<BR> कौमारभृत्यम्, अगदतन्त्रम्, रसायनतन्त्रम्, and वाजीकरणतन्त्रम्.)<BR>—5 the eight parts of a court:− 1 the law, 2 the judge, 3 assessors, 4<BR> scribe, 5 astrologer, 6 gold, 7 fire, and 8 water.<BR>—6 any whole consisting of eight parts.<BR>—7 a die, dice.<BR>—8 The eight functions of intellect (बुद्धि) are शुश्रूषा, श्रवण,<BR> ग्रहण, धारणा, चिन्तन, ऊहापोह, अर्थविज्ञान and तत्त्वज्ञान; बुद्ध्या<BR> ह्यष्टाङ्गया युक्तं त्वमेवार्हसि भाषितुम् Rām. 6. 113. 24. ˚अर्घ्यम्<BR> an offering of eight articles. ˚धूपः a sort of medical incense removing<BR> fever. ˚मैथुनम् sexual enjoyment of 8 kinds; the eight stages in<BR> the progress of a love suit; स्मरणं कीर्तनं केलिः प्रेक्षणं गुह्यभाषणम् ।<BR> संकल्पोऽध्यवसायश्च क्रियानिष्पत्तिरेव च ॥ {@˚वैद्यकम्@} It<BR> is constituted of द्रव्याभिधान, गदनिश्चय, कायसौख्य, शल्यादि, भूतनिग्रह,<BR> विषनिग्रह, बालवैद्यक, and रसायन. ˚हृदयम् N. of a medical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाधिकाराः
अष्टन् + -अधिकाराः जलाधिकारः, स्थलाधिकारः, ग्रामाधिकारः, कुललेखनम्,<BR> ब्रह्मासनम्, दण्डविनियोगः, पौरोहित्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाध्यायी
अष्टन् + -अध्यायी N. of Pāṇinīʼs grammatical work consisting of 8 Adhyāyas or chapters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टान्नानि
अष्टन् + -अन्नानि The eight types of food भोज्य, पेय, चोष्य, लेह्य, खाद्य,<BR> चर्व्य, निःपेय, भक्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टार
अष्टन् + -अर <i>a.</i> having a wheel with 8 spokes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्रम्
अष्टन् + -अस्रम् an octagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्रः|अष्टास्र
अष्टन् + -अस्रः A kind of single-storeyed building octangular in plan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्रि
अष्टन् + -अस्रि^1य <i>a.</i> octangular.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाह
अष्टन् + -अह, -अहन् <i>a.</i> lasting for 8 days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाहन्
अष्टन् + -अह, -अहन् <i>a.</i> lasting for 8 days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादिशाब्दिकाः
अष्टन् + -आदिशाब्दिकाः the first eight expounders of the science of words<BR> (grammar); इन्द्रश्चन्द्रः काशकृत्स्नापिशली शाकटायनः । पाणिन्यमरजैनेन्द्रा<BR> जयन्त्यष्टादिशाब्दिकाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापाद्य
अष्टन् + -आपाद्य Multiplied by eight. अष्टापाद्यं तु शूद्रस्य स्तेये भवति<BR> किल्बिषम् । Ms. 8. 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टोपद्वीपानि
अष्टन् + -उपद्वीपानि स्वर्णप्रस्थ, चन्द्राशुक्ल, आवर्तन, रमणक, मन्दरहरिण,<BR> पाञ्चजन्य, सिंहल, and लङ्का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकपाल|अष्टकपालः
अष्टन् + -कपाल <i>a.</i> (˚ष्टा˚) prepared or offered in ‘eight’ pans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकपालः|अष्टकपाल
अष्टन् + -कपाल + .({@-लः@}) a sacrifice in which ghee is offered in eight pans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्ण|अष्टकर्णः
अष्टन् + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> one who has the number eight as a mark burnt in<BR> his ears (P. VI. 3. 115).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्णः|अष्टकर्ण
अष्टन् + -कर्ण + .({@-र्णः@}) eight-eared, an epithet of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्मन्|अष्टकर्म्मन्
अष्टन् + -कर्ण + .({@-कर्मन्@} <i>m.</i>), {@-गतिकः@}<BR> a king who has 8 duties to perform; (they are:− आदाने<BR> च विसर्गे च तथा प्रैषनिषेधयोः । पञ्चमे चार्थवचने व्यवहारस्य चेक्षणे<BR> ॥ दण्डशुद्धयोः सदा रक्तस्तेनाष्टगतिको नृपः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकुलम्
अष्टन् + -कुलम् (Probably) Village jury. (Bh. List No. 1267).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकुलाचलाः
अष्टन् + -कुलाचलाः Eight principal mountains; नील, निषध, विन्ध्याचल,<BR> माल्यवान्, मलय, गंधमादन, हेमकूट, and हिमालय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमर्यादागिरयः
अष्टन् + -कुलाचलाः + .({@-मर्यादागिरयः@}) हिमालय, हेमकूट, निषध, गन्धमादन, नील,<BR> श्वेत, शृङ्गवार, and माल्यवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकृत्वस्
अष्टन् + -कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> eight times. चतुर्नमो अष्टकृत्वो भवाय Av. 11. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकोणः|अष्टकोण
अष्टन् + -कोणः<BR>—1 an octagon.<BR>—2 a kind of machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टखण्डः|अष्टखण्ड
अष्टन् + -खण्डः a title of a collection of several sections of the Ṛgveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगन्धाः
अष्टन् + -गन्धाः Eight fragrant substances (Mar. चन्दन, अगरु, देवदार,<BR> कोळिंजन, कुसुम, शैलज, जटामांसी, सुर-गोरोचन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगवम्
अष्टन् + -गवम् [अष्टानां गवां समाहारः] a flock of 8 cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगाढ्
अष्टन् + -गाढ् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a fabulous animal supposed to have eight legs.<BR>—2 a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुण
अष्टन् + -गुण <i>a.</i> eight-fold; अन्नादष्टगुणं चूर्णम्; दाप्योऽष्टगुणमत्ययम् Ms. 8. 400.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुणम्
अष्टन् + -गुण + .({@-णम्@}) the eight qualities which a Brāhmaṇa should possess;<BR> दया सर्वभूतेषु, क्षान्तिः, अनसूया, शौचम्, अनायासः, मङ्गलम्, अकार्पण्यम्,<BR> अस्पृहा चेति ॥ Gaut. S. ˚आश्रय <i>a.</i> endowed with these<BR> eight qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टचत्वारिंशत्
अष्टन् + अष्टचत्वारिंशत्, अष्टाचत्वारिंशत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">Page0283-1</a>]<BR>. <i>a.</i> forty-eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाचत्वारिंशत्
अष्टन् + अष्टचत्वारिंशत्, अष्टाचत्वारिंशत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">Page0283-1</a>]<BR>. <i>a.</i> forty-eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतय
अष्टन् + -तय <i>a.</i> eight-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतारिणी
अष्टन् + -तारिणी the eight forms of the goddess तारिणी; ताराचोग्रा महोग्रा<BR> च वज्रा काली सरस्वती । कावेश्वरी च चामुण्डा इत्यष्टौ तारिण्यो मताः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतालम्
अष्टन् + -तालम् A kind of sculptural measurement in which the whole height<BR> of an idol is generally eight times that of the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टत्रिंशत्
अष्टन् + -त्रिंशत् (-˚ष्टा˚)<BR> <i>a.</i> thirty-eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टत्रिकम्
अष्टन् + -त्रिकम् [अष्टावृत्तम् त्रिकम्] the number 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदलम्
अष्टन् + -दलम्<BR>—1 a lotus having eight petals.<BR>—2 an octagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टन् + अष्टादशन् ({@˚ष्टा˚@}) see above after अष्टातय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिश्
अष्टन् + -दिश् <i>f.</i> [कर्म˚ स˚ संज्ञात्वान्न द्विगुः दिक् सङ्ख्ये संज्ञायाम्<BR> P. II. 1. 50.] the eight cardinal points; पूर्वाग्नेयी दक्षिणा च नैरृती<BR> पश्चिमा तथा । वायवी चोत्तरैशानी दिशा अष्टाविमाः स्मृताः ॥. ˚करिण्यः<BR> the eight female elephants living in the eight points; करिण्योऽभ्रमुकपिलापिङ्गलानुपमाः<BR> क्रमात् । ताम्रकर्णी शुभ्रदन्ती चाङ्गना चाञ्जनावती ॥ Ak. ˚पालाः<BR> the eight regents of the cardinal points; इन्द्रो वह्निः पितृपतिः (यमः)<BR> नैरृतो वरुणो मरुत् (वायुः) । कुबेर ईशः पतयः पूर्वादीनां<BR> दिशां कमात् ॥ Ak. ˚गजाः the eight elephants guarding the 8 quarters;<BR> ऐरावतः पुण्डरीको वामनः कुमुदोऽञ्जनः । पुष्पदन्तः सार्वभौमः सुप्रतीकश्च<BR> दिग्गजाः ॥ Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदेहाः
अष्टन् + -देहाः (पिण्डब्रह्माण्डात्मकाः) Gross and subtle bodies; स्थूल,<BR> सूक्ष्म, कारण, महाकारण, विराट्, हिरण्य, अव्याकृत, मूलप्रकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टद्रव्यम्
अष्टन् + -द्रव्यम् the eight materials of a sacrifice; अश्वत्थोदुम्बुरप्लक्षन्यग्रोधसमिधस्तिलाः ।<BR> सिद्धार्थपायसाज्यानि द्रव्याण्यष्टौ विदुर्बुधाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधातुः|अष्टधातु
अष्टन् + -धातुः the eight metals taken collectively; स्वर्णं रूप्यं च<BR> ताम्रं च रङ्गं यशदमेव च । शीसं लौहं रसश्चेति धातवोऽष्टौ प्रकीर्किताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टनागाः
अष्टन् + -नागाः (Serpents) अनन्त, वासुकि, तक्षक, कर्कोटक, शङ्ख,<BR> कुलिक, पद्म, and महापद्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टनायिकाः
अष्टन् + -नायिकाः (of श्रीकृष्ण) रुक्मिणी, सत्यभामा, जाम्बवती, कालिन्दी,<BR> मित्रवृन्दा, याज्ञजिती, भद्रा, and लक्ष्मणा. (of इन्द्र) उर्वशी,<BR> मेनका, रम्भा, पूर्वचिती, स्वयंप्रभा, भिन्नकेशी जनवल्लभा and घृताची<BR> (तिलोत्तमा). (In Erotics) वासकसज्जा, विरहोत्कण्ठिता, स्वाधीनभर्तृका,<BR> कलहान्तरिता, खण्डिता, विप्रलब्धा, प्रोषितभर्तृका, and अभिसारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपक्ष
अष्टन् + -पक्ष <i>a.</i> Having eight side-pillars; अष्टपक्षां दशपक्षां<BR> शालाम् Av. 9. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपद|अष्टपदः
अष्टन् + -पद, -पद् (˚ष्ट˚ or ˚ष्टा˚) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 eight-footed.<BR>—2 a term for a pregnant animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपद्
अष्टन् + -पद, -पद् (˚ष्ट˚ or ˚ष्टा˚) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 eight-footed.<BR>—2 a term for a pregnant animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपदः|अष्टपद
अष्टन् + -पदः (˚ष्टा˚)<BR>—1 a spider.<BR>—2 a fabulous animal called Śarabha.<BR>—3 a worm.<BR>—4 a wild sort of jasmin.<BR>—5 a pin or bolt.<BR>—6 the mountain Kailāsa (the abode of Kubera).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपदः|अष्टपद
अष्टन् + -पदः + .({@-दः, -दम्@}) [अष्टसु धातुषु पदं प्रतिष्ठा यस्य Malli.]<BR>—1 gold; आवर्जिताष्टापदकुम्भतोयैः Ku. 7. 10; Śi. 3. 28.<BR>—2 a kind of chequered cloth or a board for drafts, dice-board (Mar. पट);<BR> ˚परिचयचतुराभिः K. 196. ˚पत्रम् a sheet of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपदम्
अष्टन् + -पदः + .({@-दः, -दम्@}) [अष्टसु धातुषु पदं प्रतिष्ठा यस्य Malli.]<BR>—1 gold; आवर्जिताष्टापदकुम्भतोयैः Ku. 7. 10; Śi. 3. 28.<BR>—2 a kind of chequered cloth or a board for drafts, dice-board (Mar. पट);<BR> ˚परिचयचतुराभिः K. 196. ˚पत्रम् a sheet of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपदिका
अष्टन् + -पदिका, -पादिका N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपादिका
अष्टन् + -पदः + .({@-दः, -दम्@}) [अष्टसु धातुषु पदं प्रतिष्ठा यस्य Malli.]<BR>—1 gold; आवर्जिताष्टापदकुम्भतोयैः Ku. 7. 10; Śi. 3. 28.<BR>—2 a kind of chequered cloth or a board for drafts, dice-board (Mar. पट);<BR> ˚परिचयचतुराभिः K. 196. ˚पत्रम् a sheet of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपदी
अष्टन् + -पदी (˚ष्ट˚, ˚ष्टा˚)<BR>—1 wild sort of jasmin (Mar. वेलमोगरी); श्यामान्वारणपुष्पांश्च<BR> तथाऽष्टपदिका लताः Mb. 13. 54. 6.<BR>—2 a variety of metre, often used in Jayadevaʼs Gītagovinda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपलम्
अष्टन् + -पलम् a kind of medicinal preparation of ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद्य
अष्टन् + -पाद्य <i>a.</i> (˚ष्टा˚) eight-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपुत्र
अष्टन् + -पुत्र <i>a.</i> Having eight sons; अष्टयोनिरदितिरष्टपुत्रा<BR> Av. 8. 9. 21.<BR> {@-(देह)प्रकृतयः@} पञ्चमहाभूतानि, मनः, बुद्धिः and अहङ्कारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टप्रधानाः
अष्टन् + -प्रधानाः, वैद्य, उपाध्याय, सचिव, मन्त्री, प्रतिनिधि, राजाध्यक्ष,<BR> प्रधान and अमात्य. (of शिवाजी) प्रधान, अमात्य, सचिव, मन्त्री,<BR> डबीर, न्यायाधीश, न्यायशास्त्री and सेनापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टभावाः
अष्टन् + -भावाः<BR>——(<i>a</i>) स्तम्भ, स्वेद, रोमाञ्च, वैस्वर्य, कम्प, वैवर्ण्य, अश्रुपात, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">Page0283-2</a>]<BR> प्रलय<BR>——(<i>b</i>) कम्प, रोमाञ्च, स्फुरण, प्रेमाश्रु, स्वेद, हास्य, लास्य, and गायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टभैरवाः
अष्टन् + -भैरवाः (शिवगणाः) असिताङ्ग, संहार, रुरु, काल, क्रोध,<BR> ताम्रचूड, चन्द्रचूड, and महाभैरव, (इतरे-कपाल, रुद्र, भीषण<BR> उन्मत्त, कुपित इत्यादयः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टभोगाः
अष्टन् + -भोगाः अन्न, उदक, ताम्बूल, पुष्प, चन्दन, वसन, शय्या,<BR> and अलंकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमङ्गलः|अष्टमङ्गल|अष्टमंगल|अष्टमङ्गलं
अष्टन् + -मङ्गलः a horse with a white face, tail, mane, breast and hoofs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमङ्गलम्
अष्टन् + -मङ्गलः + .({@-लम्@}) [अष्टगुणितं मङ्गलं शाक˚ त˚]] a collection<BR> of eight lucky things; according to some they are:− मृगराजो वृषो नागः<BR> कलशो व्यञ्जनं तथा । वैजयन्ती तथा भेरी दीप इत्यष्टमङ्गलम् ॥<BR> according to others लोकेऽस्मिन्मङ्गलान्यष्टौ ब्राह्मणो गौर्हुताशनः । हिरण्यं<BR> सर्पिरादित्य आपो राजा तथाष्टमः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमङ्गलघृत|अष्टमङ्गलघृतं
अष्टन् + -मङ्गलघृत Ghee mixed with Orris-root (Mar. वेखंड), Costus<BR> Arabicus (कोष्ट), ब्राह्मी Siphonanthus Indica, mustard, सैन्धव,<BR> पिप्पली, and (Mar. उपळसरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमधु
अष्टन् + -मधु Eight Kinds of honey माक्षिक, भ्रामर, क्षौद्र, पोतिका,<BR> छात्रक, अर्ध्य, औदाल, दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमहारसाः
अष्टन् + -महारसाः Eight रसs in Āyurveda, namely वैक्रान्तमणि,<BR> हिंगूळ, पारा, हलाहल, कान्तलोह, अभ्रक, स्वर्णमाक्षी, रौप्यमाक्षी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमहारोगाः
अष्टन् + -महारोगाः वातव्याधि, अश्मरी, कुष्ट, मेह, उदक, भगन्दर,<BR> अर्श, and संग्रहणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमहासिद्धयः
अष्टन् + -महासिद्धयः (<i>n.</i>) अणिमा, महिमा, लघिमा, प्राप्ति, प्राकाश्य,<BR> ईशिता, वशिता, and प्राकाम्य.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) अणिमा, महिमा, लघिमा, गरिमा, प्राप्ति, प्राकाम्य, ईशिता and वशिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमातृकाः
अष्टन् + -मातृकाः ब्राह्मी, माहेश्वरी, कौमारी, वैष्णवी, वाराही, इन्द्राणी,<BR> कौबेरी, and चामुण्डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमुद्राः
अष्टन् + -मुद्राः सुरभी, चक्र, ध्यान, योनि, कूर्म, पङ्कज, लिङ्ग and निर्याण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमानम्
अष्टन् + -मानम् one kuḍava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमासिक
अष्टन् + -मासिक <i>a.</i> occurring once in 8 months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमुष्टिः|अष्टमुष्टि
अष्टन् + -मुष्टिः a measure called कुञ्चि; अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत् कुञ्चिः<BR> कुञ्चयोऽष्टौ च पुष्कलः । हेमाद्रिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूत्राणि
अष्टन् + -मूत्राणि Urines of a cow, a sheep, a goat, a buffallo, a horse,<BR> an elephant, a camel, an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्तिः|अष्टमूर्ति|अष्टमूर्त्ति|अष्टमूर्त्तिः
अष्टन् + -मूर्तिः the ‘eight-formed’, an epithet of Śiva; the 8 forms being,<BR> the 5 elements (earth, water, fire, air and ether), the Sun and the Moon<BR> and the sacrificing priest; cf. Ś. 1. 1 -या सृष्टिः स्रष्टुराद्या वहति<BR> विधिहुतं या हविर्या च होत्री । ये द्वे कालं विधत्तः श्रुतिविषयगुणा<BR> या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वम् । यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिरिति यया प्राणिनः प्राणवन्तः ।<BR> प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः ॥; or briefly<BR> expressed, the names in Sanskrit (in the above order) are:− जलं वह्निस्तथा<BR> यष्टा सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ तथा । आकाशं वायुरवनी मूर्तयोऽष्टौ पिनाकिनः ॥.<BR> ˚धरः ‘having 8 forms’, Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्तयः
अष्टन् + -मूर्तयः Eight kinds of idols शैली, दारुमयी, लौही, लेप्या,<BR> लेख्या, सैकती, मनोमयी, and मणिमयी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टयोगिन्यः
अष्टन् + -योगिन्यः (Friends of पार्वती)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) मङ्गला, पिङ्गला, धन्या, भ्रामरी, भद्रिका, उल्का, सिद्धा, and सङ्कटा.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) मार्जनी, कर्पूरतिलका, मलयगन्धिनी, कौमुदिका, भेरुण्डा,<BR> मातालि, नायकी and जया (शुभाचारा) (sometimes सुलक्षणा and सुनन्दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टरत्नम्
अष्टन् + -रत्नम् the eight jewels taken collectively; the title of a collection<BR> of 8 Ślokas on morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टरसाः
अष्टन् + -रसाः the 8 sentiments in dramas &c.; शृङ्गारहास्यकरुनरौद्रवीरभयानकाः ।<BR> बीभत्साद्भुतसंज्ञौ चेत्यष्टौ नाट्ये रसाः स्मृताः ॥ K. P. 4 (to which<BR> is sometimes added a 9th Rasa called शान्त; निर्वेदस्थायिभावोऽस्ति शान्तोऽपि<BR> नवमो रसः <i>ibid.</i>); ˚आश्रय <i>a.</i> embodying or representing<BR> the eight sentiments; V. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टलवणानि
अष्टन् + -लवणानि अजमोदा, आम्लवेतस, एलची (cardamom), Black salt<BR> (Mar. पादेलोण), Garcinia Mangostona (Mar. आमसोल), Cinnamomum<BR> aromaticum (Mar. दालचिनी), Black pepper (Mar. मिरीं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टलोहकम्
अष्टन् + -लोहकम् a class of 8 metals; सुवर्णं रजतं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">Page0284-1</a>]<BR> ताम्रं सीसकं कान्तिकं तथा । वङ्गं लौहं तीक्ष्णलौहं लौहान्यष्टाविमानि तु ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0283-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवर्गः|अष्टवर्ग
अष्टन् + -वर्गः<BR>—1 a sort of diagram (चक्र) showing the good or bad stars of a person.<BR>—2 the 8 classes of letters; (अवर्ग, क˚, च˚, ट˚, त˚, प˚, य˚, श˚).<BR>—3 a class of eight^1 principal medicaments, Namely ऋषभ, जीवक, मेद,<BR> महामेद, ऋद्धि, वृद्धि, काकोली, and क्षीरकाकोली cf. जीवकर्षभकौ<BR> मेदौ काकोल्यावृद्धिवृद्धिकी.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवक्रः
अष्टन् + -वक्रः (˚ष्टा) See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवर्ष
अष्टन् + -वर्ष <i>a.</i> Eight years old; त्र्यष्टवर्षोऽष्टवर्षां वा धर्मे<BR> सीदति सत्वरः Ms. 9. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवसु
अष्टन् + -वसु The eight वसुs in the present मन्वन्तर are<BR>——(<i>a</i>) धर, ध्रुव, सोम, आप, अनिल, अनल, प्रत्यूष, प्रभास.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) द्रोण, प्राण, ध्रुव, अर्क, अग्नि, दोष, वसु, विभावसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवायनानि
अष्टन् + -वायनानि हरिद्रा, पूगीफल, दक्षिना, शूर्प, कङ्कण, काचमणि,<BR> धान्य, वस्त्र (Mar. खण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टविनायकाः
अष्टन् + -विनायकाः The eight Gaṇapatis at मोरगांव (Dist. Poona),<BR> पाली (Dist. कुलाबा), मढ (near Karjat, dist. कुलाबा),<BR> थेऊर (near लोणी, dist. Poona), जुन्नर (dist. Poona), ओझर<BR> (near जुन्नर, Dist. Poona). रांजणगांव (Poona-Nagar Road).<BR> सिद्धटेक (near दौंड, Dist. Ahmednagar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टविवाहाः
अष्टन् + -विवाहाः ब्राह्म, दैव, आर्ष, गान्धर्व, राक्षस, प्राजापत्य,<BR> आसुर, पैशाच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टविध
अष्टन् + -विध <i>a.</i> [अष्टविधाः प्रकाराः अस्य] eight-fold, of eight kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाविंशतिः|अष्टाविंशति
अष्टन् + अष्टाविंशतिः <i>f.</i> (˚ष्टा˚) [अष्टाधिका विंशतिः शाक˚ त˚]<BR> the number twenty-eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टशतम्
अष्टन् + -शतम्<BR>—1 One hundred and eight.<BR>—2 eight hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टश्रवणः|अष्टश्रवण
अष्टन् + -श्रवणः, -श्रवस् N. of Brahmā (having 8 ears or four heads.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टश्रवस्
अष्टन् + -श्रवणः, -श्रवस् N. of Brahmā (having 8 ears or four heads.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टसमाधयः
अष्टन् + -समाधयः यम, नियम, आसन, प्राणायाम, प्रत्याहार, धारणा,<BR> ध्यान, and समाधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टसिद्धयः
अष्टन् + -सिद्धयः (See -महासिद्धयः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक <i>a.</i> [अष्ट परिमाणमस्य कन्] Consisting of 8 parts<BR> eight-fold; क्रोधजोऽपि गणोऽष्टकः Ms. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकः|अष्टक
अष्टक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 [अष्टकं (पाणिनेः), विदन्ति अधीयते वा इत्यष्टकाः सूत्राच्च<BR> कोपधात् P. IV. 2. 65. Sk.] One who studies or is acquainted with the<BR> eight Adhyāyās of Pāṇiniʼs grammar.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Viśvāmitra (author of the hymn Rv. 10. 104.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टका
अष्टक + .{@-का@} [अश्नन्ति पितरोऽस्यां तिथौ अश्-तकन् Uṇ. 3. 148]<BR>—1 A collection of three days (7th, 8th, and 9th) beginning from the seventh<BR> day after the full moon.<BR>—2 The 8th day of three months on which the Manes are to be propitiated.<BR>—3 A Śrāddha to be performed on the above days; worship of the Manes<BR> on certain days; तस्य व्रातस्य योऽस्य द्वितीयोऽपानः साष्टका Av. 15. 16. 2;<BR> अष्टकापितृदैवत्यमित्ययं प्रसृतो जनः Rām. 2. 108. 14.<BR>—4 The 8th day of a month; Ms. 4. 113-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकम्
अष्टक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A whole consisting of 8 parts.<BR>—2 The 8 chapters of Pāṇinīʼs Sūtras; (अष्टावध्यायाः परिमाणमस्य<BR> इत्यष्टकम्; पाणिनेः सूत्रम् Sk.).<BR>—3 The study of the Sūtras.<BR>—4 A division of the Ṛgveda (it being divided into 8 Aṣṭakas or 10 Maṇḍalas).<BR>—5 Any group of eight; as वानराष्टकम्, ताराष्टकम्, मङ्गलाष्टकम्<BR> &c. गङ्गाष्टकं पठति यः प्रयतः प्रभाते वाल्मीकिना विरचितं शुभदं मनुष्यः<BR>—6 The number eight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अष्टकाङ्गः, अष्टकाङ्गम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकाङ्गः|अष्टकाङ्ग|अष्टकांग|अष्टकाङ्गं
अष्टक + -अङ्गः, -अङ्गम् a kind of board or cloth for playing with dice on<BR> (having eight divisions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकाङ्गम्
अष्टक + -अङ्गः, -अङ्गम् a kind of board or cloth for playing with dice on<BR> (having eight divisions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिक
अष्टकिक, अष्टकिन् <i>a.</i> [अष्टकाऽस्त्यस्य ठन् इनि वा]<BR> Having eight parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिन्
अष्टकिक, अष्टकिन् <i>a.</i> [अष्टकाऽस्त्यस्य ठन् इनि वा]<BR> Having eight parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिकी
अष्टकिक, अष्टकिन् + .{@-की@} One who performs an Aṣṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक्य
अष्टक्य <i>a.</i> [अष्टकेन कीतः यत् P. V. 1. 2] Bought for eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतय
अष्टतय <i>a.</i> [अष्टावयवा अस्य अष्टन्-तयप्] Having eight parts or limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतयम्
अष्टतय + .{@-यम्@} An aggregate of eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टधा <i>ind.</i> [अष्टन्-प्रकारे धाच् सङ्ख्याया विधार्येधा P. V. 3. 42]<BR>—1 Eight-fold, eight times.<BR>—2 In 8 parts or sections; भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा Bg. 7. 4; भिन्नेऽष्टधा<BR> विप्रससार वंशः R. 16. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Eighth; गर्भाष्टमेऽब्दे कुर्वीत ब्राह्मणस्योपनायनम् Ms. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमः|अष्टम
अष्टम + .{@-मः@} The eighth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमी
अष्टम + .{@-मी@}<BR>—1 The eighth day in a lunar half month; Ms. 4. 128; चतुर्दश्यष्टमी<BR> चैव अमावास्या च पूर्णिमा । पर्वाण्येतानि राजेन्द्र रविसंक्रान्तिरेव च ।<BR> V. P.<BR>—2 N. of a medical plant (कोटालता; Mar. क्षीरकाकोळी).<BR>—3 अष्टका Śrāddha; अष्टमी यज्ञपरता चातुर्मास्यनिषेवणम् Mb. 13. 142. 15.<BR> [cf. L. <i>octavus</i>; Zend. <i>astemo</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अष्टमांशः, अष्टमकालिक, अष्टमभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमांशः|अष्टमांश
अष्टम + -अंशः an 8th part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमकालिक
अष्टम + -कालिक <i>a.</i> [अष्टमः कालः भोजनेऽस्त्यस्य ठन्] one who<BR> omits seven meal times (<i>i. e.</i> full three days and the morning of the<BR> fourth) and partakes only of the 8th; नक्तं चान्नं समश्नीयाद्दिवा<BR> वाऽहृत्य शक्तितः । चतुर्थकालिको वास्यात्स्याद्वाऽप्यष्टमकालिकः ॥ Ms. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमभावः|अष्टमभाव
अष्टम + -भावः the eighth condition or position (in Astr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमक
अष्टमक <i>a.</i> The eighth; योंऽशमष्टमकं हरेत् Y. 2. 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमिका
अष्टमिका A weight of four Tolās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टागव
अष्टागव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 See अष्टगव.<BR>—2 (a car) drawn by eight oxen; P. VI. 3. 46; Vārt. अष्टतः कपाले<BR> हविषि, गवि च युक्ते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टातय|अष्टातयः
अष्टातय <i>a.</i> Consisting of eight parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टातयः|अष्टातय
अष्टातय + .{@-यः@} A collection of eight things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टादशन् <i>a.</i> [अष्ट च दश च] Eighteen; अगाहताष्टादशतां<BR> जिगीषया नवद्वयद्वीपपृथग्जयश्रियाम् N. 1. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अष्टादशाङ्गः, अष्टादशाङ्गम्, अष्टादशोपचारः, अष्टादशोपपुराणम्, अष्टादशतत्त्वानि, अष्टादशधान्यम्, अष्टादशपर्वाणि, अष्टादशपुराणम्, अष्टादशभुजा, अष्टादशमूलम्, अष्टादशविद्या, अष्टादशविवादपदम्, अष्टादशशिल्पशास्त्रोपदेशकाः, अष्टादशस्मृतिकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशाङ्गः|अष्टादशाङ्ग
अष्टादशन् + -अङ्गः, -अङ्गम् the eighteen parts of medical science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशाङ्गम्
अष्टादशन् + -अङ्गः, -अङ्गम् the eighteen parts of medical science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशोपचारः|अष्टादशोपचार
अष्टादशन् + -उपचारः [कर्म˚ स˚ संज्ञात्वान्न द्विगुः] the eighteen<BR> modes of showing respect or worshipping; आसनं स्वागतं पाद्यमर्ध्यमाचमनीयकम् ।<BR> स्नानं वस्त्रोपवीतं च भूषणानि च सर्वशः । गन्धपुष्पे तथा धूपदीपावन्नं<BR> च तर्पणम् । माल्यानुलेपनं चैव नमस्कारविसर्जने । अष्टादशोपचारैस्तु<BR> मन्त्री पूजां समाचरेत् Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशोपपुराणम्
अष्टादशन् + -उपपुराणम् a secondary or minor Purāṇa; अष्टान्युपपुराणानि<BR> मुनिभिः कथितानि तु । आद्यं सनत्कुमारोक्तं नारसिंहमतः परम् । तृतीयं<BR> नारदं प्रोक्तं कुमारेण तु भाषितम् । चतुर्थं शिवधर्माख्यं साक्षान्नन्दीशभाषितम् ।<BR> दुर्वाससोक्तमाचर्यं नारदोक्तमतः परम् । कापिलं मानवं चैव तथैवोशनसेरितम् ।<BR> ब्रह्माण्डं वारुणं चाथ कालिकाह्वयमेव च । माहेश्वरं तथा शाम्बं<BR> सौरं सर्वार्थसंचयम् । पराशरोक्तं प्रवरं तथा भागवतद्वयम् । इदमष्टादशं<BR> प्रोक्तं पुराणं कौर्मसंज्ञितम् । चतुर्धा संस्थितं पुण्यं संहितानां प्रभेदतः ॥ Hemādri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशतत्त्वानि
अष्टादशन् + -तत्त्वानि Eighteen fundamental principles; महत्, अहंकार,<BR> मनस्, पञ्चतन्मात्रs; दशेन्द्रियाणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशधान्यम्
अष्टादशन् + -धान्यम् the 18 kinds of corn; यवगोधूमधान्यानि तिलाः कङ्गुकुलन्थकाः ।<BR> माषा मुद्गा मसूराश्च निष्पावाः श्यामसर्षपाः ॥ गवेधुकाश्च नीवारा ओढक्योऽथ<BR> सतीनकाः । चणकाश्चीनकाश्चैव धान्यान्यष्टादशैव तु ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशपर्वाणि
अष्टादशन् + -पर्वाणि The eighteen पर्वs of Mahābhārata are आदि, सभा,<BR> वन, विराट्, उद्योग, भीष्म, द्रोण, कर्ण, शल्य, सौप्तिक, स्त्री, शान्ति,<BR> अनुशासन, अश्वमेध, आश्रमवासि, मौसल, महाप्रस्थानक, स्वर्गारोहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशपुराणम्
अष्टादशन् + -पुराणम् the eighteen Purāṇas━ ब्राह्मं पद्मं वैष्णवं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">Page0285-1</a>]<BR> च शैवं भागवतं तथा । तथान्यन्नारदीयं च मार्कण्डेयं च सप्तमम्<BR> ॥ आग्नेयमष्टकं प्रोक्तं भविष्यन्नवमं तथा । दशमं ब्रह्मवैवर्तं<BR> लिङ्गमेकादशं तथा ॥ वाराहं द्वादशं प्रोक्तं स्कान्दं चात्र त्रयोदशम् ।<BR> चतुदर्शं वामनं च कौर्मं पञ्चदशं तथा ॥ मत्स्यं च गारुडं चैव<BR> ब्रह्माण्डाष्टादशं तथा ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0284-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशभुजा
अष्टादशन् + -भुजा an epithet of the goddess महालक्ष्मी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशमूलम्
अष्टादशन् + -मूलम् The roots of the eighteen plants (Mar. बेल, ऐरणी, टेंट्ट,<BR> शिवण, पहाडमूळ, पुनर्नवा, रानौडीद, चिकणा, एरंड, जीवक, ऋषभक,<BR> जीवंती, शतावरी, तिरकांडे, ऊस, दर्भ, कसई, साळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशविद्या
अष्टादशन् + -विद्या the eighteen kinds of learning or lores; अङ्गानि वेदाश्चत्वारो<BR> मीमांसा न्यायविस्तरः । धर्मशास्त्रं पुराणं च विद्या ह्येताश्चतुर्दश ।<BR> आयुर्वेदो धनुर्वेदो गान्धर्वश्चेति ते त्रयः । अर्थशास्त्रं चतुर्थं तु<BR> विद्या ह्यष्टादशैव तु ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशविवादपदम्
अष्टादशन् + -विवादपदम् the eighteen subjects of litigation (causes of dispute);<BR> see Ms. 8. 4-7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशशिल्पशास्त्रोपदेशकाः
अष्टादशन् + -शिल्पशास्त्रोपदेशकाः Eighteen ancient writers on the science<BR> of Architecture; भृगुरत्रिर्वसिष्ठश्च विश्वकर्मा मयस्तथा । नारदो नग्नजिच्चैव<BR> विशालाक्षः पुरन्दरः ॥ १ ॥ ब्रह्मा कुमारो नन्दीशः शौनको गर्ग एव<BR> च । वासुदेवोऽनिरुद्धश्च तथा शुक्रबृहस्पती ॥ २ ॥ अष्टादशैते विख्याताः<BR> शिल्पशास्त्रोपदेशकाः ॥ Matsya P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशस्मृतिकारिन्
अष्टादशन् + -स्मृतिकारिन् <i>m.</i> pl. the eighteen Smṛtikāras or law-givers<BR> of the Āryas; विष्णुः पराशरो दक्षः संवर्तव्यासहारिताः । शातातपो<BR> वसिष्ठश्च यमापस्तम्बगौतमाः । देवलः शङ्खलिखितौ भरद्वाजोशनोऽत्रयः ।<BR> शौनको याज्ञवल्क्यश्च दशाष्टौ स्मृतिकारिणः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टावक्रः|अष्टावक्र
अष्टावक्रः [अष्टकृत्वः अष्टसु भागेषु वा वक्रः] N. of a celebrated<BR> Brāhmaṇa, son of the great sage Kahoḍa. [Kahoḍa married a daughter<BR> of his preceptor Uddālaka, but he was so devoted to study that he generally<BR> neglected her. When once she was far advanced in pregnancy, the unborn<BR> son was provoked at his fatherʼs neglect of her and rebuked him for his<BR> absorption in study to the neglect even of his wife. The sage was very<BR> angry at this impertinence and condemned him to be born crooked; so he<BR> came forth with his eight (aṣṭa) limbs crooked (vakra); whence his name;<BR> यस्मात्कुक्षौ वर्तमानो ब्रवीषि तस्माद्वक्रो भवितास्यष्टकृत्वः Mb. when<BR> Kahoḍa was drowned into a river as the result of a wager in a dispute<BR> with a Buddhist, young Aṣṭavakra defeated the sage and delivered his<BR> father, who, being pleased, directed his son to bathe into the Samaṅgā<BR> river, on doing which the lad became perfectly straight. See Mb. Adhyāyas 132-34<BR> of the Vanaparvan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाध्यायी
अष्टाध्यायी <i>f.</i> N. of the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa and also of Pāṇinīʼs grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टिः|अष्टि
अष्टिः <i>f.</i> [अस्यते भूमौ क्षिप्यते अस्-क्तिन् पृषो˚ षत्वम्]<BR>—1 A die for playing.<BR>—2 A metre consisting of sixty-four syllables.<BR>—3 [अक्ष्-व्याप्तौ-क्तिन्] Pervasion, reaching (Ved.) इन्द्रं शुम्भास्म्यष्टये Av. 6. 54. 1.<BR>—4 The body (the instrument of enjoyment).<BR>—5 The number sixteen.<BR>—6 Seed.<BR>—7 Kernel. कन्दाष्टिभिर्मूलफलैः Bhāg. 4. 28. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टिन्
अष्टिन् <i>a.</i> Consisting of eight members or parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ट्रा
अष्ट्रा [अक्ष्यते चाल्यतेऽनया अक्ष्-करणे ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 A prick or goad for driving cattle, whip; Rv. 4. 57. 4, 6. 53. 9.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">Page0285-2</a>]<BR>—2 A part of the wheel of a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ट्राविन्
अष्ट्रा + .{@-विन्@} <i>a.</i> obeying the goad (as a bull); शुनमष्ट्राव्यचरत्<BR> कपदीं Rv. 10. 102. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठिः|अष्ठि
अष्ठिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A stone or kernel.<BR>—2 Seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला [अष्ठिस्तत्तुल्यकठिनाश्मानं राति; रा-क, रस्य लः दीर्घः Tv.]<BR>—1 A round swelling below the navel produced by wind.<BR>—2 A kind of disease of urine.<BR>—3 A globular or round body (in general).<BR>—4 A round pebble or stone. ततो जज्ञे मांसपेशी लोहाष्ठीलेव संहता<BR> Mb. 1. 115. 12.<BR>—5 Kernel.<BR>—6 Seed corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीलिका
अष्ठीलिका<BR>—1 A kind of abscess.<BR>—2 A pebble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीवत्|अष्ठीवन्त्
अष्ठीवत् <i>m., n.</i> [निपातोऽयम् P. VIII. 2. 12] The knee, the knee-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
अस् I. €2 P. [अस्ति, आसीत्, अस्तु, स्यात्; defective in non-conjugational<BR> tenses, its forms being made up from the root भू.]<BR>—1 To be, live, exist (showing mere existence); नासदासीन्नो सदासीत्<BR> Rv. 10. 129. 1; आत्मा वा इदमेक एवाग्र आसीत् Ait. Up. 1. 1. श्रुतिद्वैधं<BR> तु यत्र स्यात् Ms. 2. 14; शपथे नास्ति पातकम् 8. 112; न त्वेवाहं<BR> जातु नासम् Bg. 2. 12; आसीद्राजा नलो नाम Nala. 1. 1; Ms. 5. 79;<BR> न अस् not to be, to be lost, disappear, perish, नायमस्तीति दुःखार्ता<BR> Nala. 7. 16; अस्ति भोक्तुम् Sk. it has to be eaten; (for other uses of<BR> अस्ति see अस्ति s. v.).<BR>—2 To be (used as a copula or verb of incomplete predication, being followed<BR> by a noun or adjective or adverb; or some other equivalent); भक्तोऽसि<BR> मे सखा च Bg. 4. 3; धार्मिके सति राजनि Ms. 11. 11; आचार्ये संस्थिते<BR> सति 5. 80; so एवमेव स्यात्, तूष्णीमासीत् &c.<BR>—3 To belong to, be in the possession of (expressed in English by <i>have</i>),<BR> with gen. of possessor; यन्ममास्ति हरस्व तत् Pt. 4. 76; यस्य<BR> नास्ति स्वयं प्रज्ञा 5. 70; न हि तस्यास्ति किंचित् स्वम् Ms. 8. 417;<BR> नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य Bg. 2. 66.<BR>—4 To fall to the share of, to happen to or befall anyone (with gen.);<BR> यदिच्छामि ते तदस्तु Ś. 4; तस्य प्रेत्य फलं नास्ति Ms. 3. 139<BR> he cannot enjoy or get.<BR>—5 To arise, spring out, occur; आसीच्च मम मनसि K. 142 (this) occurred to my mind.<BR>—6 To become; तां दृष्ट्वा दशविस्तारामासं विंशतियोजनः Rām.; also<BR> शुक्लीस्यात् राजसात् स्यात् &c. Sk.<BR>—7 To lead or tend to, turn out or prove to be (with dat.); स स्थाणुः<BR> स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः V. 1. 1; संगतं श्रीसरस्वत्योर्भूतयेऽस्तु<BR> सदा सताम् 5. 24; oft. with dat. alone without अस्; यतस्तौ स्वल्पदुःखाय Pt. 1.<BR>—8 To suffice (with dat.); सा तेषां पावनाय स्यात् Ms. 11. 85; अन्यैर्नृपालैः<BR> परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा स्याल्लवणाय वा स्यात् Jag.<BR>—9 To stay, reside, dwell, live हा पितःक्वासि हे सुभ्रु Bk. 6. 11.<BR>—10 To take place, happen.<BR>—11 To be in a particular relation, to be affected (with loc.); किं<BR> नु खलु यथा वयमस्यामेवमियमप्यस्मान् प्रति स्यात् Ś. 1. अस्तु well,<BR> let it be; एवमस्तु, तथास्तु so be it, amen. The form आस joined<BR> to roots in forming their periphrastic perfect is sometimes separated<BR> from the root and used by itself; तं पातयां प्रथममास पपात पश्चात्<BR> R. 9. 61, 16. 86. [cf. L. <i>est</i> and Gr. <i>esti</i> with अस्ति; <i>esse</i>;<BR> Zend. <i>āsti</i>; Pers. <i>hast, ast</i>] ━<i>With</i> {@अति@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">Page0286-1</a>]<BR> to be over, excel, surpass.<BR>━{@अनु@} to be at hand; reach.<BR>━{@अपि@} (with loc. or an adv. of place)<BR>—1 to be in anything.<BR>—2 to belong to, be closely connected with.<BR>━{@अभि@}<BR>—1 to belong to, to fall to oneʼs share; यन्मममाभिष्यात् Sk.<BR>—2 to be over.<BR>—3 to excel, surpass.<BR>—4 to domineer or to tyrannize over, rule over.<BR>━{@आविस्@} to arise, spring up, be visible; आचार्यकं विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26.<BR>━{@उप@} to be near to or in.<BR>━{@परि@}<BR>—1 to be in the way.<BR>—2 to surpass.<BR>—3 to pass or spend (time).<BR>—4 to pervade.<BR>━{@प्र@}<BR>—1 to be in front of.<BR>—2 to be in extraordinary degree, to preponderate, excel, surpass.<BR>━{@प्रति@}<BR>—1 to be equal to, be a match for.<BR>—2 to rival, emulate, vie with.<BR>—3 to be a representative of, stand in place of.<BR>━{@प्रादुस्@} to appear, spring up; प्रादुरासीत्तमोनुदः Ms. 1. 6; R. 11. 15.<BR>━{@व्यति@} (Ātm. व्यतिहे, व्यतिसे; व्यतिस्ते) to excel, surpass,<BR> be above or superior to, out-weigh; अन्यो व्यतिस्ते तु ममापि धर्मः Bk. 2. 35.<BR> ━II. €4 P. (अस्यति, आस, आस्थत्, असितुम्, अस्त)<BR>—1 To throw, cast, hurl, discharge, shoot (with loc. of the mark); हस्ते<BR> बिभर्ष्यस्तवे Śvet. Up. 3. 6; तस्मिन्नास्थदिषीकास्त्रम् R. 12. 23;<BR> Bk. 15. 91, 14. 77; sometimes with dat. or gen. दस्यवे हेतिमस्य Rv. 1. 103. 3.<BR>—2 To drive away. remove.<BR>—3 To frighten or scare away.<BR>—4 To throw or take away, let go, leave, give up; as in अस्तमान, अस्तशोक,<BR> अस्तकोप see अस्त.<BR>—5 To fight with; युयोध वलिरिन्द्रेण तारकेण गुहोऽस्यत Bhāg. 8. 10. 28.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@अति@} to shoot beyond or at, overpower (with arrows);<BR> अत्यस्त having shot beyond, having surpassed or excelled; joined in<BR> acc. (Tat. comp.; P. II. 1. 24.)<BR>━{@अभिप्र@} to throw over or upon, hurl at.<BR>━{@परिनि@} to stretch.<BR> ━III. €1 U. (असति-ते, असित).<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To take or receive, seize.<BR>—3 To shine (The examples usually cited to illustrate this sense are:−<BR> निष्प्रभश्च प्रभुरास भूभृताम् R. 11. 81; तेनास लोकः पितृमान् विनेत्रा 14. 23;<BR> लावण्य उत्पाद्य इवास यत्नः Ku. 1. 35. But the sense of दिदीपे<BR> or ‘shone’ is far-fetched, though Vāmana is disposed to take it. It seems<BR> preferable to regard आस in these instances as equivalent to बभूव,<BR> either taking it, as Śākaṭāyana does, as an indeclinable तिङन्तप्रतिरूपकमव्ययम्,<BR> or considering it, as Vallabha does, as an ungrammatical form used against<BR> the rules of grammar, प्रामादिकः प्रयोगः; see Malli. on Ku. 1. 35).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0285-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown, cast, given up, left; असमये यत्त्वयास्तोऽभिमानः Ve. 6.<BR>—2 Finished.<BR>—3 Despatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ता
अस्त + .{@-स्ता@} Ved. A missile, an arrow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्तकरुण, अस्तकोप, अस्तरुष्, अस्तधी, अस्तव्यस्त, अस्तसंख्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तकरुण
अस्त + -करुण <i>a.</i> merciless; हा धिक्कष्टमनिष्टमस्तकरुणः कोऽयं<BR> विधेः प्रक्रमः Māl. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तकोप
अस्त + -कोप, -रुष् <i>a.</i> whose anger is pacified; इति धियास्तरुषः<BR> परिरेभिरे Śi. 6. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तरुष्
अस्त + -कोप, -रुष् <i>a.</i> whose anger is pacified; इति धियास्तरुषः<BR> परिरेभिरे Śi. 6. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तधी
अस्त + -धी <i>a.</i> foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तव्यस्त
अस्त + -व्यस्त <i>a.</i> scattered here and there, confused, disordered;<BR> Ratn. 4. 6. (v. l. अस्त्रव्यस्त)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तसंख्य|अस्तसङ्ख्य
अस्त + -संख्य <i>a.</i> innumerable; उज्झत्सु संहार इवास्तसंख्यम् Ki. 16. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृ
अस्तृ <i>a.</i> Ved. Throwing, a shooter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तः|अस्त|अस्तं
अस्तः [अस्यन्ते सूर्यकिरणा यत्र अस्-आधारे क्त]<BR>—1 Setting, western mountain (behind which the Sun is supposed to set);<BR> यश्चैष विन्ध्यास्तमहेन्द्रकल्पो … अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1;<BR> विडम्बयत्यस्तनिमग्नसूर्यम् R. 16. 11; यात्येकतोऽस्तशिखरं<BR> पतिरोषधीनाम् Ś. 4. 2.<BR>—2 Sunset.<BR>—3 Setting in general; (fig.) fall, decline; see below.<BR>—4 Conjunction of a planet with the Sun; शुक्रास्त, बुधास्त &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तम्
अस्तः + .{@-स्तम्@}<BR>—1 Home, abode, residence (Ved.); तमग्निमस्ते वसवो न्यृण्वन् Rv. 7. 1. 2, 10. 34. 10.<BR>—2 Death, end. आकाशं प्रत्यस्तं यन्ति Ch. Up. 1. 9. 1.<BR>—3 The seventh house (in astr.; लग्नात्सप्तमं स्थानम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तम्
अस्तः + .{@-स्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> At home, home; अस्तं गम्, -या-इ-प्राप्<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To set, decline in the western horizon; गतोऽस्तमर्कः the<BR> Sun has set; (fig.) it is time to do the duties to be performed at sunset;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> for a cowherd to drive home his cattle, for a religious person<BR> to begin his prayers, for a thief to begin his nightly work &c.; कथमिहैव<BR> युवयोरस्तमितः सूर्यः V. 3 and Sarva. S. 1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To cease, vanish, be removed, disappear, be at an end; विषयिणः<BR> कस्यापदोऽस्तं गताः Pt. 1. 146. धृतिरस्तमिता R. 8. 66; दण्डेनास्तमितत्विषा<BR> Ku. 2. 23; अस्तिमितैषा कथा K. 156 at an end, over; 198, 204.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) to die; अथ चास्तमिता त्वमात्मना R. 8. 51, 12. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्ताचलः, अस्ताद्रिः, अस्तगिरिः, अस्तपर्वतः, अस्तावलम्बनम्, अस्तोदयौ, अस्तग, अस्तगमनम्, अस्तनिमग्न, अस्तमस्तकः, अस्तशिखरः, अस्तसमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताचलः|अस्ताचल
अस्तः + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः the setting or western mountain.<BR> अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताद्रिः|अस्ताद्रि
अस्तः + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः the setting or western mountain.<BR> अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगिरिः|अस्तगिरि
अस्तः + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः the setting or western mountain.<BR> अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तपर्वतः|अस्तपर्वत
अस्तः + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः the setting or western mountain.<BR> अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तावलम्बनम्
अस्तः + -अवलम्बनम् the resting of a heavenly body on the western part<BR> of the horizon, being about to set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तोदयौ
अस्तः + -उदयौ (dual) rising and setting, rise and fall; अस्तोदयावदिशदप्रविभिन्नकालम् Mu. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तग
अस्तः + -ग <i>a.</i> set, become invisible (as a planet or star).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगमनम्
अस्तः + -गमनम्<BR>—1 setting, disappearance.<BR>—2 death, sunset of life; Māl. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तनिमग्न
अस्तः + -निमग्न <i>a.</i> Set (as the Sun); विडम्बयत्यस्तनिमग्नसूर्यम् R. 16. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमस्तकः|अस्तमस्तक
अस्तः + -मस्तकः, -शिखरः The top of the setting mountain; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तशिखरः|अस्तशिखर
अस्तः + -मस्तकः, -शिखरः The top of the setting mountain; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तसमयः|अस्तसमय
अस्तः + -समयः The moment of Sunset, the moment of end or death; करजालमस्तसमयेऽपि<BR> सताम् Śi. 9. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तकः|अस्तक
अस्तकः Final beatitude, absolution (मोक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तकम्
अस्तकः + .{@-कम्@} Ved. Home. आ पत्नीरिदमस्तकम् Av. 2. 26. 5; also cf.<BR> उदये सविता रक्तो रक्तश्चास्तमने तथा । Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ततातिः|अस्तताति
अस्ततातिः Ved. Home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमनम्
अस्तमनम् Setting (of the Sun); रवेस्तमिस्रागमनिर्गमांस्ते तथोदयं<BR> चास्तमनं च वीराः Mb. 3. 164. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमयः|अस्तमय
अस्तमयः<BR>—1 Setting (of the Sun), करोत्यकालास्तमयं विवस्वतः Ki. 5. 35;<BR> (opp. उदय).<BR>—2 Destruction, end, decline, loss; भाग्यास्तमयमिवाक्ष्णोः M. 2. 11.<BR>—3 Fall, subjugation; उदयमस्तमयं च रघूद्वहात् R. 9. 9.<BR>—4 Obscuring, eclipsing; प्रभाप्ररोहास्तमयं रजांसि R. 6. 33.<BR>—5 Conjunction (of a planet) with the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमीके
अस्तमीके,^1 अस्ता <i>ind.</i> Ved. at hand, near.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: Based on AP90 and alph. ordering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ता
अस्तमीके,^1 अस्ता <i>ind.</i> Ved. at hand, near.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: Based on AP90 and alph. ordering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ति|अस्तिः
अस्ति <i>ind.</i> [अस्-शतिप्]<BR>—1 Being, existent, present; as in अस्तिक्षीरा, ˚कायः<BR>—2 Often used at the commencement of a tale or narrative in the sense<BR> of ‘so it is’, ‘there’, or merely as an expletive; अस्ति सिंहः प्रतिवसति<BR> स्म Pt. 4; अस्त्यत्र नगरे … त्रयः पुरुषा देवस्य श्रियं न सहन्ते Mu. 1, 5;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">Page0287-1</a>]<BR> अस्ति पूर्वमहं व्योमचारी विद्याधरोऽभवम् Ks. 22. 56, 1. 27;<BR> अस्ति तत्रभवान् वृषलं याजयिष्यति P. III. 3. 146 is it that &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिः|अस्ति
अस्ति + .{@-स्तिः@} <i>f.</i> N. of a sister of Prāpti, daughter of Jarāsandha<BR> and wife of Kaṃsa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्तिकायः, अस्तिक्षीर, अस्तिनास्ति, अस्तिप्रवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0286-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिकायः|अस्तिकाय
अस्ति + -कायः [अस्ति कायः स्वरूपं यस्य] a category or predicament<BR> (with the Jainas); these categories are 5; -जीव˚, पुद्गल˚, धर्म˚,<BR> अधर्म˚, and आकाश˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिक्षीर
अस्ति + -क्षीर <i>a.</i> [अस्ति क्षीरं यस्य P. II. 2. 24. Vārt.] having milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिनास्ति
अस्ति + -नास्ति <i>ind.</i> doubtful, partly true and partly not; ˚त्वम्,<BR> ˚ता doubtful or partial existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिप्रवादः|अस्तिप्रवाद
अस्ति + -प्रवादः N. of the fourth of the fourteen Pūrvas or older writings of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तित्वम्
अस्तित्वम् Existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिमत्|अस्तिमन्त्
अस्तिमत् <i>a.</i> [अस्ति विद्यमानं धनमस्य] Possessed of property, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्तु <i>ind.</i> (Strictly 3rd pers. sing. Imperative of अस्) Let<BR> it be, be it so, well, implying permission; it is also said to have the<BR> senses of pain, contest, jealousy, superiority, acceptance, praise, indication,<BR> and acceptance with envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुंकार
अस्तुंकार <i>a.</i> [कारेसत्यागदस्य P. VI. 3. 70. Vārt. अस्तोश्चेति वक्तव्यम्]<BR>—1 Efficacious, working (as a medicine).<BR>—2 Producing that which the physician promises shall be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंक्रान्तः|असङ्क्रान्त|असंक्रान्त
असंक्रान्तः An intercalary month (Hemādriʼs चतुर्वर्गचिन्तामणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयत|असंयतः
असंयत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unrestrained, not under control.<BR>—2 Not tied, as in असंयतोऽपि मोक्षार्थी; ˚आत्मन् having the soul unrestrained.<BR> असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः Bg. 6. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयतः|असंयत
असंयत + .{@-तः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयमः|असंयम
असंयमः Absence of control or restraint, especially of the senses;<BR> आपदां कथितः पन्थाः इन्द्रियाणामसंयमः Subh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयाज्य
असंयाज्य <i>a.</i> One with whom no body is allowed to sacrifice; Ms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुक्त
असंयुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Separated.<BR>—2 Not conjunct (as a consonant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुक्तम्
असंयुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 Non-combination.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुत|असंयुतः
असंयुत <i>a.</i> Unblended, ununited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुतः|असंयुत
असंयुत + .{@-तः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयोगः|असंयोग
असंयोगः<BR>—1 Absence of union or connection.<BR>—2 Not a conjunct consonant; P. I. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंरम्भः|असंरम्भ
असंरम्भः Fearlessness; Mb. 14. 38. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंरोधः|असंरोध
असंरोधः Non-injury; Mb. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंविदान
असंविदान <i>a.</i> Ignorant, foolish; तौ हासंविदानावेव Ch. Up. 8. 7. 2;<BR> असंविदानेव जामात्रे कुप्यसि U. 7; Ki. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवीत
असंवीत <i>a.</i> Naked; उन्माद इव मुक्तमूर्धजोऽसंवीत एव विचचार<BR> Bhāg. 5. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत
असंवृत^1 <i>a.</i> Uncovered, exposed; प्रविश्य हि घ्नन्ति शठास्तथाविधानसंवृताङ्गान्निशिता<BR> इवेषवः Ki. 1. 30.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृतम्
असंवृतः + .{@-तम्@} N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत्तिः|असंवृत्ति
असंवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंव्यवहार्य
असंव्यवहार्य <i>a.</i> With whom intercourse is forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंव्यवहित
असंव्यवहित <i>a.</i> Immediate, without any interval (of time or space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशब्द्य
असंशब्द्य <i>a.</i> Not worth mentioning; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
असंशय <i>a.</i> Free from doubt, certain मामेवैष्यस्यसंशयम्<BR> Bg. 8. 7, 18. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशयम्
असंशय + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without doubt, undoubtedly, certainly, assuredly;<BR> असंशयं महाबाहो Bg. 6. 55, 7. 1. असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा Ś. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
असंश्रव <i>a.</i> Out of hearing, inaudible; असंश्रवे out of<BR> the hearing of; असंश्रवे चैव गुरोर्न किंचिदपि कीर्तयेत् Ms. 2. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्लिष्ट|असंश्लिष्टः
असंश्लिष्ट <i>a.</i> Not joined or united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्लिष्टः|असंश्लिष्ट
असंश्लिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसक्त
असंसक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unconnected, incoherent; दुहितुर्ब्रूह्यसंसक्तो माभूत्तत्र विचारणा Mb. 13. 4. 11.<BR>—2 Unattached; अभिप्रेतमसंसक्तमात्मजं दातुमर्हसि Rām. 1. 19. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसूक्तगिल
असंसूक्तगिल <i>a.</i> Swallowing without chewing (as Rudraʼs dogs).<BR> रुद्रस्यैलबकारेभ्योऽसंसूक्तगिलेभ्यः । इदं महास्येभ्यः श्वभ्यो अकरं<BR> नमः Av. 11. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृतिः|असंसृति
असंसृतिः <i>f.</i> Non-return to worldly existence, absorption into<BR> the Supreme Spirit. निवृत्तिमार्गः कथितः ब्रह्मणा यदसंसृतिः Bhāg. 6. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृष्ट
असंसृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not mixed with, not connected.<BR>—2 Not living in common, not reunited after partition of property (as an heir).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कारः|असंस्कार
असंस्कारः<BR>—1 Non-consecration.<BR>—2 Natural state, want of embellishment or care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृत|असंस्कृतः
असंस्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unpolished, not refined or cleansed &c.<BR>—2 Not decorated or adorned.<BR>—3 One over whom no purificatory rite (any one of the saṃskāras) has<BR> been performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृतः|असंस्कृत
असंस्कृत + .{@-तः@} An ungrammatical form (अपशब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्तुत
असंस्तुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unknown, unacquainted, not familiar; असंस्तुत इव परित्यक्तो बान्धवो<BR> जनः K. 173, 308; Ki. 3. 2.<BR>—2 Unusual, strange; असंस्तुतेषु प्रसभं भयेषु Ki. 3. 21.<BR>—3 Not in harmony or agreement with; धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं चेतः Ś. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थानम्
असंस्थानम्<BR>—1 Absence of cohesion.<BR>—2 Disorder, confusion.<BR>—3 Want, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थित
असंस्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not arranged, disordered, irregular; असंस्थितमभूयिष्ठम् H. 3. 102.<BR>—2 Not collected.<BR>—3 Moving.<BR>—4 Unaccomplished; ब्रह्मेवासंस्थितं हविः Av. 6. 50. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थितिः|असंस्थिति
असंस्थितिः <i>f.</i> Disorder, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहत|असंहतः
असंहत <i>a.</i> Not joined or united, scattered, loose, straggling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहतः|असंहत
असंहत + .{@-तः@} The <i>Puruṣa</i> or soul (in Sāṅ. Phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहतम्
असंहत + .{@-तम्@} A form of array, open order of troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहार्य|असंहार्य्य
असंहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Irresistible, insuperable; उपस्थितमसंहार्यैर्हयैः Rām. 5. 6. 5;<BR> विधिर्नूनमसंहार्यः प्राणिनां प्लवगोत्तम Rām. 5. 37. 4.<BR>—2 Not to be diverted or misled; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
असकृत् <i>ind.</i> Not once, repeatedly, often and often; असकृदेकरथेन<BR> तरस्विना R. 9. 23; Me. 93.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असकृत्समाधिः, असकृद्गर्भवासः, असकृद्भवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्समाधिः|असकृत्समाधि
असकृत् + -समाधिः repeated meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृद्गर्भवासः|असकृद्गर्भवास
असकृत् + -गर्भवासः repeated birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृद्भवः|असकृद्भव
असकृत् + -भवः A tooth; Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकौ
असकौ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 = असौ this or that; पिबति च पाति च यासकौ रहस्त्वाम् Śi. 7. 53.<BR>—2 This wicked one. cf. अव्ययसर्वनाम्नाम् अकच् प्राक्टेः P. V. 3. 71.<BR> भार्योढं तमवज्ञाय तस्थे सैमित्रयेऽसकौ Bk. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
असक्त <i>a.</i> Not excessively attached, not feeling interested in,<BR> indifferent (to); असक्तः सुखमन्वभूत् R. 1. 21.<BR>—2 Not entangled; शाखासु वल्कलमसक्तमपि द्रुमाणाम् Ś. 2. 13.<BR>—3 Not united, detached.<BR>—4 Not attached to worldly feelings and connections. असक्तः स विशिष्यते Bg. 3. 7, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्तम्
असक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Without being excessively attached or addicted to; असक्तमाराधयतो<BR> यथायथम् Ki. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Without any hindrance, quickly; Dk. 35. तस्य मर्ध्नि शितं खड्गमसक्तं<BR> पर्वतेष्वपि Mb. 3. 39. 52.<BR>—3 Incessantly, ceaselessly असक्तमूधांसि पयः क्षरन्त्यम् Ki. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्तिः|असक्ति
असक्तिः <i>f.</i> The being detached from worldly feelings or passions;<BR> असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु Bg. 13. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्थ
असक्थ <i>a.</i> Thighless; also असक्थिः (P. V. 4. 121.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्र
असक्र <i>a.</i> Ved. not ceasing to flow, not drying up; not going elsewhere<BR> (असंक्रमणी); धेनुं न इषं पिन्वतमसक्राम Rv. 6. 63. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखिः|असखि
असखिः An enemy, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असगोत्र
असगोत्र <i>a.</i> Not belonging to the same <i>Gotra</i> or family; असगोत्रा<BR> च या पितुः Ms. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकरः|असङ्कर
असंकरः<BR>—1 Non-mixture of caste.<BR>—2 Absence of confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकल्पित|असङ्कल्पित|असङ्कल्पितः
असंकल्पित <i>a.</i> Not determined; असंकल्पितमेवेह यदकस्मात्प्रवर्तते<BR> Rām. 2. 22. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकसुक|असङ्कसुक
असंकसुक <i>a.</i> Not fickle, steady; Ms. 6. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकुल|असङ्कुल|असंकुलः|असङ्कुलः
असंकुल <i>a.</i> Not crowded, open, clear, broad, (as a road &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकुलः|असङ्कुल|असंकुल|असङ्कुलः
असंकुल + .{@-लः@} A broad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंक्रान्त|असङ्क्रान्त|असंक्रान्तः
असंक्रान्त <i>a.</i> Not gone over or transmitted; ˚मासः an intercalary month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्य|असङ्ख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
असंख्य <i>a.</i> Beyond calculation, numberless, countless, innumerable;<BR> मन्वन्तराण्यसंख्यानि सर्गः संहार एव च Ms. 1. 80, 12. 15;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यता|असङ्ख्यता
असंख्य + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} infinity. प्रसह्य तेजोभिरसंख्यतां गतैः । Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यत्वम्
असंख्य + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} infinity. प्रसह्य तेजोभिरसंख्यतां गतैः । Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यात|असङ्ख्यात|असंख्यातं
असंख्यात <i>a.</i> Countless, innumerable. असंख्याता ओप्यमानाः सुवर्णाः Av. 12. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येय|असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येयः
असंख्येय <i>a.</i> Innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येयः|असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येय
असंख्येय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu; V. Sahas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येयम्
असंख्येय + .{@-यम्@} An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">Page0288-2</a>]<BR> exceedingly large number. असंख्येयं स्वमस्मिन् निविष्टम् Av. 1. 8. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असंख्येयगुण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येयगुण
असंख्येय + -गुण <i>a.</i> innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंग|असङ्ग|असंगः
असंग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not attached, free from worldly ties.<BR>—2 Not hindered or obstructed, not blunted; असंगगतयः शीघ्रा हरिवीरा<BR> महाबलाः Rām. 5. 51. 14. असंगमद्रिष्वपि सारवत्तया R. 3. 63;<BR>—3 Not united, solitary, unassailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगः|असङ्ग|असंग
असंग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Non-attachment; अहिंसयेन्द्रियासंगैः (साधयन्तीह तत्पदम्) Ms. 6. 75.<BR>—2 <i>Puruṣa</i> or soul (in Sāṅ. Phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगचारिन्|असङ्गचारिन्
असंग + .{@-चारिन्@} <i>a.</i> moving without obstacle. Rām. 5. ˚वत् <i>a.</i><BR> not attached to. Rām. 3<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगत|असङ्गत
असंगत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ununited, unaccompanied with.<BR>—2 improbable, inconsistent.<BR>—3 Unequal.<BR>—4 Unesteemed.<BR>—5 Unbecoming, improper.<BR>—6 Rude, ill-mannered, unpolished.<BR>—7 unobstructed, not hindered; शक्तिं क्षिप्तामसंगताम् Rām. 6. 70. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगतिः|असङ्गति|असंगति
असंगतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Not associating with.<BR>—2 Incongruity, improbability.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech in which a cause and its effect are<BR> represented as locally different or separated (in which there is an apparent<BR> violation of the relation between cause and effect); भिन्नदेशतयात्यन्तं<BR> कार्यकारणभूतयोः । युगपद्धर्मयोर्यत्र ख्यातिः सा स्यादसंगतिः ॥<BR> K. P. 10; विरुद्धं भिन्नदेशत्वं कार्यहेत्वोरसंगतिः । विषं जलधरैः<BR> पीतं मूर्छिताः पथिकाङ्गनाः ॥ Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगम|असङ्गम|असंगमः
असंगम <i>a.</i> Not united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगमः|असङ्गम|असंगम
असंगम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Separation, disunion.<BR>—2 Incongruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगिन्|असङ्गिन्
असंगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not united or associated.<BR>—2 Not attached to the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असचद्विष्
असचद्विष् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Persecuting those who are not (his) worshippers.<BR>—2 Having no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात
असजात <i>a.</i> Ved. Not related by blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात्य
असजात्य <i>a.</i> Without consanguinity or blood-relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्ञ
असंज्ञ <i>a.</i> Insensible; करोत्यसंज्ञान् सङ्ग्रामे देवान्स वरुणानपि<BR> Rām. 6. 85. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्ञा
असंज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञा@} Disunion, disagreement, discord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्|असन्त्
असत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not being or existing; तदभावे सदप्यसत् H. 3. 3; असति त्वयि<BR> Ku. 4. 12; Ms. 9. 154.<BR>—2 Non-existent, unreal; आत्मनो ब्रह्मनोऽभेदमसन्तं कः करिष्यति.<BR>—3 Bad (opp. सत्); सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतवः R. 1. 10.<BR>—4 Wicked, vile, evil; ˚विचार.<BR>—5 Not manifest.<BR>—6 Wrong, improper, false, untrue; इति यदुक्तं तदसत् (oft. occurring<BR> in controversial works).<BR>—7 Not answering its purpose. ━<i>m.</i> (न्) Indra. <i>n.</i> (त्)<BR>—1 Non-existence, non-entity; नासदासीन्नो सदासीत् Rv. 10. 129. 1;<BR> असद्वा इदमग्र आसीत् ततो वै सदजायत T. Up. 2. 7. 1; नासतो<BR> विद्यते भावः Bg. 2. 16; Ms. 12. 118, 1. 11, 14, 74.<BR>—2 An evil, a harm.<BR>—3 Untruth, falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असती
असत् + .{@-ती@} An unchaste woman; असती भवति सलज्जा Pt. 1. 418.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असदध्येतृ, असदागमः, असदाचार, असदाचारिन्, असत्कर्मन्, असत्क्रिया, असत्कल्पना, असत्ख्यातिः, असद्ग्रहः, असद्ग्राहः, असच्चेष्टितम्, असज्जनः, असद्दृश्, असत्पथः, असत्परिग्रहः, असत्पुत्रः, असत्प्रतिग्रहः, असद्भावः, असद्वादिन्, असद्वृत्ति, असद्व्यवहार, असद्व्यवहार, असच्छास्त्रम्, असत्संसर्गः, असद्धेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदध्येतृ
असत् + -अध्येतृ <i>m.</i> a Brāhmaṇa who reads heterodox works, one who<BR> neglects his own Śākhā and studies another; also called<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">Page0289-1</a>]<BR> शाखारण्डः; स्वशाखां यः परित्यज्य अन्यत्र कुरुते श्रमम् । शाखारण्डः<BR> स विज्ञेयो वर्जयेत्तं क्रियासु च ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदागमः|असदागम
असत् + -आगमः<BR>—1 a heterodox Śāstra or doctrine.<BR>—2 acquisition (of wealth) by unfair or foul means.<BR>—3 a foul means itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचार|असदाचारः
असत् + -आचार <i>a.</i> following evil practices, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचारः|असदाचार
असत् + -आचार + .({@-रः@}) an evil practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचारिन्
असत् + -आचारिन् <i>a.</i> one who follows evil practices, wicked, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्मन्|असत्कर्म्मन्
असत् + -कर्मन्, -क्रिया &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्क्रिया
असत् + -कर्मन्, -क्रिया &c. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कल्पना
असत् + -कल्पना<BR>—1 an untrue action, one which never took place.<BR>—2 fabrication of falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्ख्यातिः|असत्ख्याति
असत् + -ख्यातिः <i>f.</i> wrong or improper perception or knowledge; आत्मख्याति<BR> रसख्यातिरख्यातिः ख्यातिरन्यथा Sarva. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्ग्रहः|असद्ग्रह
असत् + -ग्रहः, -ग्राहः<BR>—1 a bad trick.<BR>—2 a bad opinion, prejudice. मोहाद् गृहीत्वाऽसद्ग्राहान्प्रवर्तन्तेऽशुचिव्रताः Bg. 16. 10.<BR>—3 childish desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्ग्राहः|असद्ग्राह
असत् + -ग्रहः, -ग्राहः<BR>—1 a bad trick.<BR>—2 a bad opinion, prejudice. मोहाद् गृहीत्वाऽसद्ग्राहान्प्रवर्तन्तेऽशुचिव्रताः Bg. 16. 10.<BR>—3 childish desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असच्चेष्टितम्
असत् + -चेष्टितम् harm, injury; प्राणिष्वसच्चेष्टितम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्जनः|असज्जन
असत् + -जनः a bad, wicked, or contemptible man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्दृश्
असत् + -दृश् <i>a.</i> evil-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पथः|असत्पथ
असत् + -पथः<BR>—1 a bad road (lit.).<BR>—2 evil practices or doctrines; नाशो हन्त सतामसत्पथजुषामायुः समानां<BR> शतम् Bv. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्परिग्रहः|असत्परिग्रह
असत् + -परिग्रहः acceptance of unfit presents, receiving presents from<BR> improper persons; Ms. 12. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पुत्रः|असत्पुत्र
असत् + -पुत्रः<BR>—1 a childless man; Ms. 9. 154.<BR>—2 a bad son or disreputable son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्प्रतिग्रहः|असत्प्रतिग्रह
असत् + -प्रतिग्रहः<BR>—1 present of bad things; Ms. 11. 194.<BR>—2 receiving unfit presents (such as तिल) or from improper persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्भावः|असद्भाव
असत् + -भावः<BR>—1 non-existence, absence.<BR>—2 a bad or wicked opinion.<BR>—3 an evil disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्वादिन्
असत् + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> one who says that a matter (or idea) is non-existent,<BR> who negatives the existence or declares the non-existence of an idea or<BR> matter; असद्वादी हि विद्यमानमपि अनुपलभ्य ब्रूयात् । ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 4.<BR> ˚त्वम् Being an असद्वादिन्; सद्वादित्वाच्च पाणिनेर्वचनं<BR> प्रमाणम् । असद्वादित्वान्न कात्यायनस्य । ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्वृत्ति|असद्वृत्तिः
असत् + -वृत्ति, -व्यवहार <i>a.</i> following evil practices, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्वृत्तिः|असद्वृत्ति
असत् + -वृत्ति, -व्यवहार + .({@-त्तिः@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a low or degrading occupation.<BR>—2 wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहार|असद्व्यवहारः
असत् + -वृत्ति, -व्यवहार <i>a.</i> following evil practices, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहार|असद्व्यवहारः
असत् + -व्यवहार <i>a.</i> following evil practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहारः|असद्व्यवहार
असत् + -व्यवहार + .({@-रः@}) evil practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असच्छास्त्रम्
असत् + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 a wrong doctrine.<BR>—2 a heterodox doctrine (such as that of the Bauddhas); Ms. 11. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्संसर्गः|असत्संसर्ग
असत् + -संसर्गः bad company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्धेतुः|असद्धेतु
असत् + -हेतुः<BR>—1 a statement having exceptions (in न्याय).<BR>—2 a bad or fallacious <i>hetu</i>; see हेत्वाभास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतायी
असतायी Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृ
असत्कृ €8 U. To disrespect, dishonour, not to receive hospitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्मन्|असत्कर्म्मन्
असत्कर्मन् <i>a.</i> Of bad conduct, wicked. <i>n.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्म
असत्कर्मन् + .({@-र्म@})<BR>—1 A bad action (prohibited by the Vedas).<BR>—2 Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कारः|असत्कार
असत्कारः, असत्क्रिया Disrepect, dishonour, bad or inhospitable reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्क्रिया
असत्कारः, असत्क्रिया Disrepect, dishonour, bad or inhospitable reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत
असत्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not honoured, disrespected; यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोऽसि Bg. 11. 42.<BR>—2 Done from improper motives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृतम्
असत्कृत + .{@-तम्@} bad or wicked deed. असत्कृतमवज्ञातम् Bg. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्ता
असत्ता<BR>—1 Non-existence.<BR>—2 Untruth.<BR>—3 Wickedness, badness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्त्व
असत्त्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without energy or strength.<BR>—2 Having no animal.<BR>—3 Having no goodness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्त्वम्
असत्त्व + .{@-त्त्वम्@}<BR>—1 Non-existence.<BR>—2 Unreality, untruth.<BR>—3 Wickedness, badness.<BR>—4 Duet.<BR>—5 Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
असत्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untrue, false; पापासः सन्तो अनृता असत्याः Rv. 4. 5. 5; असत्यमप्रतिष्ठम् Bg. 16. 8.<BR>—2 Imaginary, unreal, असत्यकण्ठार्पितबाहुबन्धना Ku. 5. 27.<BR>—3 of uncertain result; असत्यानि च युद्धानि संशयो मे न रोचते Rām. 5. 30. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यः|असत्य
असत्य + .{@-त्यः@} A liar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यम्
असत्य + .{@-त्यम्@} Falsehood, untruth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असत्यवादिन्, असत्यसन्ध, असत्यसन्निभ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यवादिन्
असत्य + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking falsely, liar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्ध|असत्यसंध
असत्य + -सन्ध <i>a.</i> not true to oneʼs promise, false, perfidious, treacherous;<BR> ˚धे जने सखी पदं कारिता Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्निभ
असत्य + -सन्निभ <i>a.</i> improbable, unlikely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
असदृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Dissimilar, unlike.<BR>—2 Unfit, improper, incongruous; ˚व्यवहारिन् behaving improperly,<BR> H. 2; ˚संयोगकारिन् K. 12 unworthy; मातः किमप्यसदृशं विकृतं<BR> वचस्ते Ve. 5. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असदृशोपमम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृशोपमम्
असदृश + -उपमम् (in rhetoric) A dissimilar simile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्यस्
असद्यस् <i>ind.</i> Not immediately, after delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्
असन् <i>n.</i> Blood (used only in the declension of असृज् after acc. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनम्
असनम् Throwing, discharging, casting; as in इष्वसनम् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनः|असन|असनं
असनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of a tree (पीतसाल) Bridelia retusa (Mar. आसणा);<BR> Rām. 2. 94. 8; निरसनैरसनैरवृथार्थता Śi. 6. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असना
असनम् + .{@-ना@} Ved. A missile, an arrow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असनपर्णी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनपर्णी
असनम् + -पर्णी N. of a tree (सातल; Mar. गोकर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनिः|असनि
असनिः One who throws &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तति|असंतति|असन्ततिः
असन्तति, असन्तान <i>a.</i> Having no issue, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तान|असंतान|असन्तानः
असन्तति, असन्तान <i>a.</i> Having no issue, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्ततिः|असन्तति|असंतति
असन्तति, असन्तान + .{@-तिः, -नः@} Childlessness, failure of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तानः|असन्तान|असंतान
असन्तति, असन्तान + .{@-तिः, -नः@} Childlessness, failure of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतुष्ट|असन्तुष्ट|असन्तुष्टः
असंतुष्ट <i>a.</i> Discontented, displeased; असंतुष्टा द्विजा नष्टाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतोषः|असन्तोष|असंतोष
असंतोषः Displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदिग्ध|असन्दिग्ध
असंदिग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not doubtful, distinct, certain, clear.<BR>—2 Not vanished.<BR>—3 Confident, unsuspected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदिग्धम्
असंदिग्ध + .{@-ग्धम्@} <i>ind.</i> Certainly, undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदित|असन्दित
असंदित, -न <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not restrained, free. असंदिनो विसृज विष्वगुल्काः<BR> Rv. 4. 4. 2; असंदितानां संदाता Ms. 8. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदिन
असंदित, -न <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Not restrained, free. असंदिनो विसृज विष्वगुल्काः<BR> Rv. 4. 4. 2; असंदितानां संदाता Ms. 8. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्न
असन्न <i>a.</i> Ved. Without rest or repose, untiring, restless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंधानम्
असंधानम्<BR>—1 Want of aim or object.<BR>—2 Disjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंधि|असन्धि|असंधिः
असंधि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not joined together (as words).<BR>—2 Not bound or restrained, at liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंधिः|असन्धि|असंधि
असंधि + .{@-धिः@}<BR>—1 Absence of <i>Sandhi</i> or euphony.<BR>—2 Want of union, connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनद्ध|असन्नद्ध|असन्नद्धः
असंनद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unarmed.<BR>—2 Pretending to knowledge, conceited (पण्डितंमन्य).<BR>—3 Proud, arrogant.<BR>—4 Born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिकर्षः|असन्निकर्ष|असंनिकर्ष
असंनिकर्षः<BR>—1 Non-perception of objects, not bringing them to the mind.<BR>—2 Remoteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिकृष्ट|असन्निकृष्ट
असंनिकृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unperceived.<BR>—2 Not near, remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0289-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिधिः|असन्निधि|असंनिधि
असंनिधिः, -निधानम्<BR>—1 Absence, distance.<BR>—2 Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिधानम्
असंनिधिः, -निधानम्<BR>—1 Absence, distance.<BR>—2 Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिहित|असन्निहित
असंनिहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not near, distant.<BR>—2 Placed in a wrong manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिवृत्तिः|असन्निवृत्ति
असंनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Non-return; असंनिवृत्त्यै तदतीतमेव Ś. 6. 10<BR> gone never to return; परलोकमसंनिवृत्तये R. 8. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्न
असपत्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without a rival wife.<BR>—2 Not an enemy, friendly.<BR>—3 Without enemies, not attacked; इदं तदकि देवा असपत्ना किलाभुवम्<BR> Rv. 10. 159. 4; अवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धम् Bg. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्नम्
असपत्न + .{@-त्नम्@} Undisturbed condition, peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्नी
असपत्न + .{@-त्नी@} A sort of brick (इष्टकाभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिण्ड|असपिंड
असपिण्ड <i>a.</i> Not connected by offerings of rice-balls; or not<BR> connected by blood-relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असभ्य|असभ्यः
असभ्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unfit for an assembly.<BR>—2 Vulgar, low, obscene, indecent (words &c.). अयं त्वसभ्यस्तव जन्मनो<BR> गृहे श्रुत्वाग्रजांस्ते न्यवधीत् सुरेश्वर Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
असम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uneven, odd (as a number); असमशीलाः खलु मृगाः Bv. 1. 2; mean, contemptible.<BR>—2 Unequal (in space, number or dignity); असमैः समीयमानः Pt. 1. 74.<BR>—3 Unequalled, matchless, unsurpassed; समवतारसमैरसमैस्तटैः<BR> Ki. 5. 7; वाद्यविशेषाणामसमः श्रोता K. 12; Ms. 10. 73.<BR>—4 Uneven, not level (as ground).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमः|असम
असम + .{@-मः@} N. of Buddha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असमेषुः, असमबाणः, असमसायकः, असमनयन, असमनेत्र, असमलोचन, असमवृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमेषुः|असमेषु
असम + -इषुः, -बाणः, -सायकः ‘having an odd number of arrows’, epithets<BR> of Cupid who has five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमबाणः|असमबाण
असम + -इषुः, -बाणः, -सायकः ‘having an odd number of arrows’, epithets<BR> of Cupid who has five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमसायकः|असमसायक
असम + -इषुः, -बाणः, -सायकः ‘having an odd number of arrows’, epithets<BR> of Cupid who has five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमनयन
असम + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> ‘having an odd number of eyes’,<BR> epithets of Śiva, who has three eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमनेत्र
असम + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> ‘having an odd number of eyes’,<BR> epithets of Śiva, who has three eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमलोचन
असम + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> ‘having an odd number of eyes’,<BR> epithets of Śiva, who has three eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवृत्तम्
असम + -वृत्तम् a metre in which the <i>gaṇas</i> are not the same in all lines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
असमग्र <i>a.</i> Incomplete; partial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्रम्
असमग्र + .{@-ग्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Incompletely, not entirely; ततो निषङ्गादसमग्रमुद्धृतम् R. 3. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जस|असमंजस|असमञ्जसं
असमञ्जस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Indistinct, unintelligible; स्खलदसमञ्जसमुग्धजल्पितं ते U. 4. 4;<BR> Māl. 10. 2 faltering, inarticulate and pretty prattle.<BR>—2 Unbecoming, improper; यद्यपि न कापि हानिर्द्राक्षामन्यस्य रासभे<BR> चरति । असमञ्जसमिति मत्वा तथापि तरलायते चेतः ॥ Udb.<BR>—3 Absurd, nonsensical, foolish; कृतं किं वा सुपर्णस्य ते नैकेनासमञ्जसम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 17. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जसम्
असमञ्जस + .{@-सम्@} Non-conformity, disparity, difference. <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Unbecomingly, improperly.<BR>—2 In a fluctuating or confused manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमद्
असमद् <i>f.</i> Ved. Non-conflict, harmony, concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमद
असमद <i>a.</i> [सह मदेन गर्वेण समदः कलहः स नास्ति यत्र]<BR> Without a quarrel or opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमन
असमन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of different colours or minds.<BR>—2 Going in different directions; असमना अजिरासो रघुष्यदः Rv. 1. 140. 4.<BR>—3 Uneven, unequal; असमने अध्वनि वृजिने पथि Rv. 6. 46. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमयः|असमय
असमयः<BR>—1 Unseasonableness.<BR>—2 Unfit or unfavourable time; असमये मतिरुन्मिषति ध्रुवम् N. 4. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
असमर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not able or competent; अभ्यासेऽप्यसमर्थोऽसि Bg. 12. 10.<BR>—2 Weak, feeble.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Powerless to convey the intended meaning, a defect of a<BR> word; यत्तदर्थं पठ्यते न च तत्रास्य शक्तिः तदसमर्थत्वम् K. P. 7;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> in कुञ्जं हन्ति कृशोदरी; हन्, though read in root-books<BR> in the sense of ‘going’, is here powerless to convey that meaning.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असमर्थसमासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थसमासः|असमर्थसमास
असमर्थ + -समासः a compound in which the conjunction of words is not as<BR> it should be; <i>e. g.</i> in अश्राद्धभोजिन्, असूर्यंपश्य, अ goes not<BR> with श्राद्ध or सूर्य but with भोजिन् or पश्य; Mbh. on P. I. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
असमवायिन् <i>a.</i> Not intimate or inherent, accidental, separable.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असमवायिकारणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिकारणम्
असमवायिन् + -कारणम् (In logic) an accidental cause, not inherent and intimate<BR> relation; गुणकर्ममात्रवृत्तिज्ञेयमथाप्यसमवायिहेतुत्वम् Bhāṣā P.;<BR> यथा तन्तुसंयोगः पटस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवेत
असमवेत <i>a.</i> Not classed together, incoherent; ˚रूपम् incoherently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्त
असमस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Incomplete, imperfect, partial, not whole.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Not joined in a compound, not compounded.<BR>—3 Uncollected.<BR>—4 Separate, detached, unconnected (opp. व्यस्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्तम्
असमस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} An uncompounded word (the sentence showing the dissolution<BR> of a compound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाति
असमाति <i>a.</i> Having nothing equal, unparalleled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
असमान <i>a.</i> Unequalled, matchless; ˚लावण्यम् Dk. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्त|असमाप्तं
असमाप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not completed or finished, left incomplete; असमाप्तविधिर्यतो मुनिः<BR> R. 8. 76; Ku. 4. 19.<BR>—2 Not fully acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमायुक्त
असमायुक्त <i>a.</i> Not properly disciplined; अस्ति वाहनसामर्थ्यम् ।<BR> असमायुक्तस्तु सः Pratijñā. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तः|असमावृत्त
असमावृत्तः, -त्तकः, असमावर्तकः, असमावृत्तिकः A religious student who has not completed the period of his residence with his preceptor;<BR> मासिकान्नं तु योऽश्नीयादसमावर्तको द्विजः Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तकः|असमावृत्तक
असमावृत्तः, -त्तकः, असमावर्तकः, असमावृत्तिकः A religious student who has not completed the period of his residence with his preceptor;<BR> मासिकान्नं तु योऽश्नीयादसमावर्तको द्विजः Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावर्तकः|असमावर्तक|असमावर्त्तक
असमावृत्तः, -त्तकः, असमावर्तकः, असमावृत्तिकः A religious student who has not completed the period of his residence with his preceptor;<BR> मासिकान्नं तु योऽश्नीयादसमावर्तको द्विजः Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तिकः|असमावृत्तिक
असमावृत्तः, -त्तकः, असमावर्तकः, असमावृत्तिकः A religious student who has not completed the period of his residence with his preceptor;<BR> मासिकान्नं तु योऽश्नीयादसमावर्तको द्विजः Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार|असमाहारः
असमाहार <i>a.</i> Not joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहारः|असमाहार
असमाहार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Non-recovery of anything.<BR>—2 Disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमिध्य
असमिध्य <i>ind.</i> Not having kindled; असमिध्य च पावकम् Ms. 2. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्य
असमीक्ष्य <i>ind.</i> Not having (properly) considered.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असमीक्ष्यकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्यकारिन्
असमीक्ष्य + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> acting inconsiderately, imprudent, not circumspect;<BR> सर्वमिदं मम नृशंसस्य असमीक्ष्यकारिताया विजृम्भितम् Nāg. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीचीन
असमीचीन <i>a.</i> Erroneous, wrong; तस्माद् यस्य च दुष्टं करणं<BR> यत्र च मिथ्येति प्रत्ययः स एवासमीचीनः प्रत्ययो नान्य इति । ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्धिः|असमृद्धि
असमृद्धिः <i>f.</i> Non-accomplishment, ill-success; नात्मानमवमन्येत<BR> पूर्वाभिरसमृद्धिभिः Ms. 4. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0290-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमेत
असमेत <i>a.</i> Not arrived, absent; क्वचिदसमेतपरिच्छदः R. 9. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपत्ति|असम्पत्ति|असंपत्तिः
असंपत्ति <i>a.</i> Unlucky, poor, miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपत्तिः|असम्पत्ति|असंपत्ति
असंपत्ति + .{@-त्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Ill-luck, want of success or wealth.<BR>—2 Non-accomplishment, failure; न च शोचत्यसंपत्तौ Ms. 12. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपात
असंपात <i>a.</i> Not present or at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपातः|असम्पात
असंपात + .{@-तः@} Inactivity, cessation of any work; असंपातं करिष्यामि<BR> ह्यद्य त्रैलोक्यचारिणाम् Rām. 3. 64. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण्ण
असंपूर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not complete, unfinished.<BR>—2 Not whole or entire.<BR>—3 Not full, partial, as the moon; चन्द्रमसंपूर्नमण्डलमिदानीम् Mu. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंप्रज्ञात
असंप्रज्ञात <i>a.</i> Not well discerned, or distinguished, a kind<BR> of समाधि (= निर्विकल्पसमाधि q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबद्ध|असम्बद्ध|असम्बद्धं
असंबद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unconnected, incoherent.<BR>—2 Nonsensical, absurd, unmeaning; ˚प्रलापिनी talking nonsense; असंबद्धः<BR> खल्वसि Mk. 9 absurd fellow; ˚मनोरथाः Māl. 2; ˚द्धं प्रलपितुं<BR> प्रवृत्तः Ratn. 2.<BR>—3 Improper, wrong; Ms. 12. 6.<BR>—4 Not closely associated, not related; असंबद्धकृतश्चैव व्यवहारो<BR> न सिध्यति Ms. 8. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबद्धम्
असंबद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} An absurd sentence, unmeaning or nonsensical speech; <i>e. g.</i><BR> यावज्जीवमहं मौनी when uttered by some one; see अबद्ध also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबद्धार्थव्यवधान
असंबद्ध + .{@-अर्थव्यवधान@} <i>a.</i> Having the interception of an irrelevant<BR> matter; तस्मान्नासम्बद्धार्थव्यवधानैकवाक्यता भवति । ŚB. on MS. 3. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबन्ध|असम्बन्ध|असंबंध|असंबन्धः
असंबन्ध <i>a.</i> Unconnected, not relating or belonging to. परपत्नी<BR> तु या स्त्री स्यादसंबन्धा च योनितः Ms. 2. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबन्धः|असम्बन्ध|असंबंध|असंबन्ध
असंबन्ध + .{@-न्धः@} Non connection, absence of any relation or connection; यद्वा<BR> साध्यवदन्यस्मिन्नसंबन्ध उदाहृतः Bhāṣā P. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबाध|असम्बाध
असंबाध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not narrow, spacious, wide; असंबाधं बध्यतो मानवानाम् Av. 12. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Not crowded with people, lonely, solitary; वसन्नसंबाधशिवेऽपि<BR> देशे Ki. 3. 53.<BR>—3 Open, accessible.<BR>—4 Separated by an interval; द्विपैरसंबाधमयांबभूवे Śi. 3. 67.<BR>—5 Without pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबाधा
असंबाध + .{@-धा@} N. of a metre consisting of 56 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबाधम्
असंबाध + .{@-धम्@} Ved. Open space; असंबाधे पृथिव्या उरौ लोके नि धीयस्व Av. 18. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबोधः|असम्बोध
असंबोधः Non-knowledge, ignorance; Mb. 12<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव|असम्भव|असंभवः
असंभव <i>a.</i> Improbable, unlikely, inconsistent; असंभवं<BR> हेममृगस्य जन्म H. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभवः|असम्भव|असंभव
असंभव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Non-existence; अन्यदाहुरसंभवात् Vāj. 40. 10; Īśop. 13;<BR> रामेणापि कथं न हेमहरिणस्यासंभवो लक्षितः Pt. 2. 4; Śi. 16. 34.<BR>—2 Improbability, impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभवा
असंभव + .{@-वा, -वम्@} An extra-ordinary event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभवम्
असंभव + .{@-वा, -वम्@} An extra-ordinary event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभवत्
असंभवत् <i>a.</i> Improbable; असंभवद्घनरसा शताली परिसेविता ।<BR> करं न सहते राजन् भूमिर्नववधूरिव ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव्य
असंभव्य, -असंभाविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impossible; असंभवं न वक्तव्यम्.<BR>—2 Incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाविन्
असंभव्य, -असंभाविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impossible; असंभवं न वक्तव्यम्.<BR>—2 Incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव्यम्|असम्भव्यम्
असंभव्य, -असंभाविन् + .{@-व्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> In an incomprehensible or extraordinary manner,<BR> so as to prevent any restoration; प्रजां हिंसित्वा ब्राह्मणीमसंभव्यम्<BR> पराभवम् Av. 5. 18. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभावना|असम्भावना
असंभावना<BR>—1 Difficulty or impossibility of comprehending.<BR>—2 Improbability.<BR>—3 Want of respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभावनीय|असम्भावनीय
असंभावनीय, -असंभाव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impossible.<BR>—2 Inconceivable, incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाव्य
असंभावनीय, -असंभाव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impossible.<BR>—2 Inconceivable, incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाव्यम्
असंभावनीय, -असंभाव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} = असंभव्यम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभावित
असंभावित <i>a.</i> Unworthy of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाVइतोपमा
असंभावित + .{@-उपमा@} A simile that implies impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभूतिः|असम्भूति|असंभूति
असंभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-existence; illusion (माया); अन्धं तमः प्रविशन्ति येऽसंभूतिमुपासते<BR> Vāj. 40. 9; Īśop. 12<BR>—2 Not being born again.<BR>—3 Undeveloped cause (प्रकृति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाष्य
असंभाष्य <i>a.</i> Unfit for conversation; असंभाष्ये साक्षिभिश्च देशे<BR> संभाषते मिथः Ms. 8. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभृत
असंभृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not brought about by artificial means, not artificial, natural; असंभृतं<BR> मण्डनमङ्गयष्टेः Ku. 1. 31.<BR>—2 Not properly nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभेद्य
असंभेद्य <i>a.</i> Not to be brought into contact; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभोज्य
असंभोज्य <i>a.</i> One with whom one ought not to eat; असंभोज्या<BR> ह्यसंयाज्या असंपाठ्याविवाहिनः Ms. 9. 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रम|असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रमः
असंभ्रम <i>a.</i> Free from agitation, composed, cool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रमः|असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रम
असंभ्रम + .{@-मः@} Calmness, steadiness; शशंस तुल्यसत्त्वानां सैन्यघोषेऽप्यसंभ्रमम् R. 4. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रमम्
असंभ्रम + .{@-मम्, असंभ्रान्तम्@} Coolly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रान्तम्
असंभ्रम + .{@-मम्, असंभ्रान्तम्@} Coolly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमत|असम्मत|असंमतः|असम्मतः
असंमत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disapproved, not allowed or permitted, not consented to; असंमतः<BR> कस्तव मुक्तिमार्गम् Ku. 3. 5.<BR>—2 Disliked, averse.<BR>—3 Dissentient, differing from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमतः|असम्मत|असंमत|असम्मतः
असंमत + .{@-तः@} An enemy; द्यतु दोषैरसंमतान् K. P. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असंमतादायिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमतादायिन्
असंमत + -आदायिन् <i>a.</i> taking without the consent of the possessor, such<BR> as a thief. सुरापोऽसंमतादायी भ्रूणहा गुरुतल्पगः । तपसा तरते …<BR> Mb. 13. 122. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमतिः|असम्मति|असंमति
असंमतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Dissent, difference of opinion, disagreement,<BR>—2 Disapproval; dislike, aversion.<BR>—3 Dishonour; प्रणाय्योऽसंमतौ P. III. 1. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमानः|असम्मान|असंमान|असम्मानं
असंमानः Disrespect, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमित|असम्मित
असंमित <i>a.</i> Not limited, immense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमुख
असंमुख <i>a.</i> Having the face turned away from; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमूढ|असम्मूढ
असंमूढ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not infatuated, undeluded.<BR>—2 Steady, composed. स्थिरबुद्धिरसंमूढः Bg. 5. 20, 10. 3, 15. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमोहः|असम्मोह|असंमोह
असंमोहः<BR>—1 Absence of infatuation; बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसंमोहः Bg. 10. 4.<BR>—2 Steadiness, composure, coolness.<BR>—3 Real knowledge, true insight (into a thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमृष्ट|असम्मृष्ट
असंमृष्ट <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not blended or united together.<BR>—2 Without any hurt, uninjured, safe.<BR>—3 Not cleansed असंमृष्टो जायसे मात्रोः शुचिः; Rv. 5. 11. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यञ्च्|असम्यंच्
असम्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> (-मीची <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Bad, improper, incorrect.<BR>—2 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असम्यञ्कारिन्, असम्यञ्क्प्रयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यञ्कारिन्
असम्यञ्च् + -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inexpert, incompetent.<BR>—2 ill-conducted, profligate.<BR>—3 Acting improperly; Ms. 9. 259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यञ्क्प्रयोगः
असम्यञ्च् + -प्रयोगः Incorrect application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असरुः|असरु
असरुः [सरति सृ-उन्, न˚ त˚] N. of a medicinal plant Blumea<BR> Lacera (Mar. काकडशिंगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0291-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असर्व
असर्व <i>a.</i> Not all; ˚वीर <i>a.</i> Ved. not having all oneʼs<BR> men collected. असर्ववीरश्चरतु प्रणुतो द्वेष्यः Av. 9. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असलम्
असलम् [अस्यते क्षिप्यतेऽनेन; अस् + कलच्]<BR>—1 Iron.<BR>—2 A Mantra used in discharging a missile.<BR>—3 Arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असवर्ण|असवर्ण्ण
असवर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of a different caste or tribe; अपि नाम कुलपतेरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Not homogeneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असव्य
असव्य <i>a.</i> Not-left (<i>i. e.</i> right).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असश्चत्|असश्चन्त्
असश्चत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not disposed to go, not going; अस्य प्रजावती गृहेऽसश्चन्ती दिवे<BR> दिवे Rv. 6. 31. 4.<BR>—2 Unceasing, inexhaustible, not drying up.<BR>—3 Not closed up, not defeated or overcome, untouched (as by any one attempting<BR> to enter a door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अससत्|अससन्त्
अससत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Not sleeping, watchful, wakeful; अग्ने रेजन्ते<BR> अससन्तो अजराः Rv. 1. 143. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह
असह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not enduring, intolerant, impatient of; कालक्षेपासहः Ks. 9. 37.<BR>—2 Unable to bear, support, or endure; oft. with gen. of object, कुसुमपातस्यासहं<BR> शरीरम् K. 250; सा स्त्रीस्वभावादसहा भरस्य Mu. 4. 13; असहतरा<BR> कुचकुम्भयोर्भरस्य Śi. 7. 48, 10. 81; Ki. 7. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहम्
असह + .{@-हम्@} The middle of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहन|असहनः
असहन <i>a.</i> Not enduring, intolerant, impatient, envious, jealous,<BR> असहना खलुसा । दूरारूढश्चास्याः प्रणयः V. 4; Me. 54 (v. l.), प्रिया<BR> मुञ्चत्यद्य ध्रुवमसहना जीवितमसौ Ratn. 3. 15; Śi. 15. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनः|असहन
असहन + .{@-नः@} An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनम्
असहन + .{@-नम्@} Intolerance, impatience; jealousy परगुणासहनम् = असूया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनीय
असहनीय असहितव्य असह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unbearable, insufferable, intolerable; (ददर्श) तदपारमसह्यं<BR> च वानराणां महाबलम् Rām. 6. 26. 7; R. 18. 25. नववैधव्यमसह्यवेदनम् Ku. 4. 1.<BR>—2 Impracticable, impossible (असह्यं द्रष्टुं = invisible).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असहनीयपीड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनीयपीड
असहनीय + -पीड <i>a.</i> Causing intolerable pain; असह्यपीडं भगवन्नृणमन्त्यमवेहि मे R. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहमान
असहमान <i>a.</i> Impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णु
असहिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, unenduring, envious or jealous of; as in परसुखासहिष्णुः.<BR>—2 Quarrelsome; ˚ता impatience, envy; सुजनबन्धुजनेष्वसहिष्णुता Bh. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहाय
असहाय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Friendless, lonely, solitary; एकमसहायमगारम् P. V. 1. 113 Com.<BR>—2 Without companions or assistants; Ms. 7. 30. अपि यत्सुकरं कर्म<BR> तदप्येकेन दुष्करम् । विशेषतोऽसहायेन किं नु राज्यं महोदयम् ॥ 55;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहायता
असहाय + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} loneliness, solitude; Ms. 6. 44; ˚वत् without companions,<BR> friendless; एक एव चरेन्नित्यं सिद्धयर्थमसहायवान् Ms. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहायता
{{Lbody-6110.002}}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहित
असहित <i>a.</i> Unassociated, unaccompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षात्
असाक्षात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Not before the eyes, invisibly, imperceptibly.<BR>—2 Not present (used adjectively).<BR>—3 Indirectly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असाक्षात्कारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षात्कारः|असाक्षात्कार
असाक्षात् + -कारः absence; non-perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिक
असाक्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Having no witness, unattested, unwitnessed; असाक्षिकेषु त्वर्थेषु मिथो<BR> विवदमानयोः Ms. 8. 109.<BR>—2 Without a ruler.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असाक्षिकहत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिकहत
असाक्षिक + -हत <i>a.</i> Beaten (in law) without witness; Y. 2. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिन्
असाक्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not an eye-witness. Y. 2. 71.<BR>—2 One whose evidence is not admissible (in law).<BR>—3 One who is disqualified to attest a legal document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्ष्यम्
असाक्ष्यम् Want of evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाद
असाद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ved. Not sitting; having no seat; Not mounted (on horse-back); असादा<BR> ये च सादिनः Av. 11. 10. 24.<BR>—2 Not becoming tired, unwearied; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधन
असाधन <i>a.</i> Without means, destitute of resources, materials,<BR> or instruments; Pt. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधनम्
असाधन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Non-accomplishment.<BR>—2 Not proving or establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधनीय
असाधनीय, असाध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be accomplished or completed, not proper, easy, or capable of<BR> being accomplished; नास्ति असाध्यं नाम मनोभुवः K. 157.<BR>—2 Not capable of being proved; (see com. on Y. 2. 6.)<BR>—3 Incurable, irremediable (as a disease or patient); असाध्यः कुरुते<BR> कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा Śi. 2. 84; असाध्य इति वैद्येनातुर इव<BR> V. 3; Mv. 4. 23; भिषजामसाध्यम् R. 8. 93.<BR>—4 Not to be overpowered or mastered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्य|असाध्यं
असाधनीय, असाध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be accomplished or completed, not proper, easy, or capable of<BR> being accomplished; नास्ति असाध्यं नाम मनोभुवः K. 157.<BR>—2 Not capable of being proved; (see com. on Y. 2. 6.)<BR>—3 Incurable, irremediable (as a disease or patient); असाध्यः कुरुते<BR> कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा Śi. 2. 84; असाध्य इति वैद्येनातुर इव<BR> V. 3; Mv. 4. 23; भिषजामसाध्यम् R. 8. 93.<BR>—4 Not to be overpowered or mastered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारण|असाधारणं|असाधारणः
असाधारण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not common, peculiar; special, specific.<BR>—2 (In logic) Existing neither in सपक्ष or विपक्ष as a <i>hetu</i>;<BR> यस्तूभयस्माद् व्यावृत्तः स त्वसाधारणो मतः<BR>—3 Not to be claimed by anyone else, exclusively belonging to one (as<BR> wealth &c.); पिता पुत्रान्तरेष्वपि साधारणो माता त्वसाधारणी Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारणः|असाधारण|असाधारणं
असाधारण + .{@-णः@} A fallacy or हेत्वाभास in Logic; one of the three kinds<BR> of अनैकान्तिक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारणम्
असाधारण + .{@-णम्@} Speciality, special property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधु
असाधु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not good, bad, distasteful, unpleasant; अतोऽर्हसि क्षन्तुमसाधु साधु<BR> वा Ki. 1. 4.<BR>—2 Wicked.<BR>—3 Ill-behaved (with loc.); असाधुर्मातरि Sk., असाधुः पितरि Mbh. 2. 3. 36<BR>—4 Corrupt, not properly formed or <i>Sanskṛt</i> (as a word); यथा गोणीशब्दः<BR> सास्नादिमति असाधुः Bhartṛ. Mbh. Dīpikā<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असाधुवृत्ता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुता
असाधु + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} <i>a.</i><BR> Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुत्वम्
असाधु + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} <i>a.</i><BR> Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्वी
असाधु + .{@-ध्वी@} An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुवृत्ता
असाधु + -वृत्ता an unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असान्निध्यम्
असान्निध्यम् Non-nearness, Absence; असान्निध्यं कथं कृष्ण तवासीद्<BR> वृष्णिनन्दन Mb. 3. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामञ्जस्यम्
असामञ्जस्यम्<BR>—1 Incorrectness.<BR>—2 Impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामयिक
असामयिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Inopportune, unseasonable; किमसामयिकं वितन्वतां<BR> मनसः क्षोभमुपात्तरंहसः Ki. 2. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्य
असामान्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not common, peculiar, exclusive, sole; रामं सीतापरित्यागादसामान्यपतिं<BR> भुवः R. 15. 39.<BR>—2 Extraordinary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्यम्
असामान्य + .{@-न्यम्@} A peculiar or special property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामि
असामि <i>a.</i> Ved. Not half, whole, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामि
असामि + .{@-मि@} <i>ind.</i> Completely, fully.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असामिशवस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामिशवस्
असामि + -शवस् <i>a.</i> Having complete strength; अर्हन्तो ये सुदानवो<BR> नरो असामिशवसः Rv. 5. 52. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असांप्रत|असाम्प्रत|असाम्प्रतं
असांप्रत <i>a.</i> Unfit, unbecoming, improper; अनाचक्षाणयाऽसांप्रतं कृतम् M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असांप्रतम्|असाम्प्रतम्
असांप्रत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Improperly, unfitly; oft. used with an adjectival<BR> force = असांप्रत; विषवृक्षोऽपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">Page0293-1</a>]<BR> संवर्ध्य स्वयं छेत्तुमसांप्रतम् Ku. 2. 55; संप्रत्यसांप्रतं<BR> वक्तुमुक्ते मुसलपाणिना Śi. 2. 71; R. 8. 61; Pt. 1. 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असांप्रतिकता
असांप्रतिकता <i>f.</i> Improper behaviour; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असांप्रदायिक
असांप्रदायिक <i>a.</i> Not traditional, not sanctioned by the tradition. U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्यम्
असाम्यम्<BR>—1 Difference, dissimilarity; Mb. 2.<BR>—2 Unsuitableness (in medicine or diet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असार|असारं|असारः
असार <i>a.</i> [न˚ ब˚]<BR>—1 Sapless, insipid.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Without essence, useless; असारः खलु संसारः Udb.;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) worthless, unsubstantial, without strength, stuff or value, deprived<BR> of its essence; असारं संसारं परिमुषितरत्नं त्रिभुवनम् Māl. 5. 30;<BR> U. 1; असारे खलु संसारे सारमेतच्चतुष्टयम् Dharm. 12, 13;<BR> तत्संसारमसारमेव निखिलं बुद्ध्वा बुधा बोधकाः Bh. 3. 146.<BR>—3 Vain, unprofitable; Pt. 1. 28.<BR>—4 Weak, feeble, infirm, fragile; श्रुतिपथमसारम् Mu. 6. 14; बहूनामप्यसाराणां<BR> संहतिः कार्यसाधिका (समवायो हि दुर्जयः) Pt. 1. 331; Śi. 2. 50.<BR>—5 Poor; Dk. 40.<BR>—6 With no enthusiasm, not ready; सुयुद्धकामुकं सारमसारं विपरीतकम् ।<BR> Śukra. 4. 872.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असारः|असार|असारं
असार + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Unessential or unimportant portion; कुर्यादसारभङ्गो हि सारभङ्गमपि<BR> स्फुटम् H. 3. 82.<BR>—2 N. of a tree (एरण्ड).<BR>—3 Aloe wood. (Mar. अगरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असारम्
असार + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Unessential or unimportant portion; कुर्यादसारभङ्गो हि सारभङ्गमपि<BR> स्फुटम् H. 3. 82.<BR>—2 N. of a tree (एरण्ड).<BR>—3 Aloe wood. (Mar. अगरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असारता
असारता<BR>—1 Saplessness.<BR>—2 Worthlessness; आधेः स्वीकरणात्सिद्धी रक्षमाणोऽप्यसारताम् Y. 2. 60.<BR>—3 Unsubstantial nature; transitory or frail state; धिगिमां देहभृतामसारताम् R. 8. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असावधान
असावधान <i>a.</i> Careless, inadvertent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसम्
असाहसम् Absence of violence, gentleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसिक
असाहसिक <i>a.</i> Not acting boldly or inconsiderately; न सहास्मि<BR> साहसमसाहसिकी Śi. 9. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिः|असि
असिः [अस्यते क्षिप्यते; अस्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 139]<BR>—1 A sword<BR>—2 A knife used for killing animals.<BR>—3 [अस्यति सेवनेन पापानि] N. of a river to the south of Benares.<BR>—4 Breath ({@श्वास@}).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असि|असिः
असिः + .{@-सि@} <i>ind.</i> The 2nd pers. sing. of the present of अस् to be,<BR> used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘त्वम्’ thou; as in कृतवानसि<BR> विप्रियं न मे Ku. 4. 7 (where however असि may be taken as a verb).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्यसि, असिगण्डः, असिचर्या, असिजीविन्, असिदंष्ट्रः, असिदंष्ट्रकः, असिदन्तः, असिधारा, असिधाराव्रतम्, असिधावः, असिधावकः, असिधेनुः, असिधेनुका, असिपत्र, असिपत्रकः, असिपथः, असिपथम्, असिपुच्छः, असिपुच्छकः, असिपुत्रिका, असिपुत्री, असिमेदः, असिलता, असिहत्य, असिहस्तः, असिहेतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यसि
असिः + -असि <i>ind.</i> sword against sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिगण्डः|असिगण्ड
असिः + -गण्डः a small pillow for the cheeks; (असिः क्षिप्तो गण्डो यत्र Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिचर्या
असिः + -चर्या exercise or practice of arms; Mb. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिजीविन्
असिः + -जीविन् <i>a.</i> one who earns his livelihood by means of swords,<BR> a soldier fighting for wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्रः|असिदंष्ट्र
असिः + -दंष्ट्रः, -दंष्ट्रकः the marine monster <i>makara</i> or crocodile<BR> (painted on the banner of Kāmadeva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्रकः|असिदंष्ट्रक
असिः + -दंष्ट्रः, -दंष्ट्रकः the marine monster <i>makara</i> or crocodile<BR> (painted on the banner of Kāmadeva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदन्तः|असिदन्त|असिदंत
असिः + -दन्तः a crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधारा
असिः + -धारा the edge of a sword; सुरगज इव दन्तैर्भग्नदैत्यासिधारैः R. 10. 86, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधाराव्रतम्
असिः + -धाराव्रतम् [असिधारायां स्थितिरिव दुष्करं व्रतम्]<BR>—1 (according to some) the vow of standing on the edge of a sword; (according<BR> to others) the vow of keeping constant company with a young wife and yet<BR> steadily resisting the temptation of sexual intercourse with her; यत्रैकशयनस्थापि<BR> प्रमदा नोपभुज्यते । असिधाराव्रतं नाम वदन्ति मुनिपुंगवाः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">Page0293-2</a>]<BR> or शयने मध्ये खड्गं विधाय स्त्रीपुंसौ यत्र ब्रह्मचर्येण स्वपतस्तत्;<BR> or युवा युवत्या सार्धं यन्मुग्धभर्तृवदाचरेत् । अन्तर्निवृत्तसङ्गः स्यादसिधाराव्रतं<BR> हि तत् Yādava.<BR>—2 (hence fig.) any hopelessly difficult task; सतां केनोद्दिष्टं विषममसिधाराव्रतमिदम्<BR> Bh. 2. 28, 64; असिधाराव्रतमिदं यदरिणा सह संवासः Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधावः|असिधाव
असिः + -धावः, -धावकः an armourer, furbisher. वाद्यविद्याविदग्धाश्च<BR> लुब्धकाश्चासिधावकाः । Śiva B. 31. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधावकः|असिधावक
असिः + -धावः, -धावकः an armourer, furbisher. वाद्यविद्याविदग्धाश्च<BR> लुब्धकाश्चासिधावकाः । Śiva B. 31. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनुः|असिधेनु
असिः + -धेनुः, -धेनुका [असिर्धेनुरिव यस्याः वा कप् or असेर्धेनुका<BR> (धेनुशब्देन स्त्रीवाचकत्वं संदृअश्यते)] a knife; Vikr. 4. 69; cf.<BR> स्याच्छस्त्री चासिपुत्री च च्छुरिका चासिधेनुका । Ak. 2. 8. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनुका
असिः + -धेनुः, -धेनुका [असिर्धेनुरिव यस्याः वा कप् or असेर्धेनुका<BR> (धेनुशब्देन स्त्रीवाचकत्वं संदृअश्यते)] a knife; Vikr. 4. 69; cf.<BR> स्याच्छस्त्री चासिपुत्री च च्छुरिका चासिधेनुका । Ak. 2. 8. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्र|असिपत्रः
असिः + -पत्र <i>a.</i> having sword-shaped leaves; जातं तमात्मन्यसिपत्रवृक्षम् R. 14. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रः|असिपत्र
असिः + -पत्र + .({@-त्रः@})<BR>—1 the sugar-cane.<BR>—2 a kind of tree which grows in the lower world. (Mar. त्रिधारी निवडुंग.)<BR>—3 a hell paved with swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रम्
असिः + -पत्र + .({@-त्रम्@})<BR>—1 the blade of a sword.<BR>—2 a sheath, a scabbard. ˚वनम् a hell where the trees have leaves<BR> as sharp as swords. असिपत्रवनं चैव निशितं क्षुरसंवृतम् (ददर्श)<BR> Mb. 18. 2. 23; असिपत्रवनं चैव लोहदारकमेव च । Ms. 4. 90;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रकः|असिपत्रक
असिः + -पत्रकः<BR>—1 a sugar-cane.<BR>—2 white दर्भ grass, Bhāg. 5. 26. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपथः|असिपथ
असिः + -पथः, -पथम् the course of the breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपथम्
असिः + -पथः, -पथम् the course of the breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुच्छः|असिपुच्छ
असिः + -पुच्छः, -पुच्छकः the Gangetic porpoise; see शिशुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुच्छकः|असिपुच्छक
असिः + -पुच्छः, -पुच्छकः the Gangetic porpoise; see शिशुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्रिका
असिः + -पुत्रिका, -पुत्री a knife (असेः पुत्रीव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्री
असिः + -पुत्रिका, -पुत्री a knife (असेः पुत्रीव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिमेदः|असिमेद
असिः + -मेदः [असिरिव तीक्ष्णो मेदो निर्यासो यस्य] the fetid <i>Khadira</i>.<BR> (विट्खदिर; Mar. शेण्याखैर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिलता
असिः + -लता the blade of a sword; ददृशुरुल्लसितासिलतासिताः Śi. 6. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहत्य
असिः + -हत्य <i>a.</i> to be killed with a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहत्यम्
असिः + -हत्य + .({@-त्यम्@}) fighting with knives or swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहस्तः|असिहस्त
असिः + -हस्तः killing by right hand sword; (असिहस्तो दक्षिणबाहुविभ्रान्तच्छेदः ।<BR> इति नीलकण्ठटीका); असिहस्तापहस्ताभ्यां तेषां गात्राण्यकृन्तत Mb. 6. 90. 45<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहेतिः|असिहेति
असिः + -हेतिः [असिर्हेतिः साधनमस्य] a swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिकम्
असिकम् The part of the face between the underlip and the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्नी
असिक्नी [सिता केशादौ शुभ्रा जरती, तद्भिन्ना अवृद्धा, असित तकारस्य<BR> ङीप् च P. IV. 1. 39 छन्दसि क्नमेके Vārt.]<BR>—1 A young maidservant of the harem.<BR>—2 Night (Nir.).<BR>—3 N. of a river in the Punjab, mentioned along with others in the line.<BR> इमं मे गङ्गे यमुने … असिक्निया मरुद्वृधे … &c. Rv. 10. 75. 5;<BR> करीषिणीमसिक्नीं च कुशचीरां महानदीम् Mb. 6. 9. 23. <i>a.</i> black;<BR> त्वद् भिया विश आयन्नसिक्नीः Rv. 7. 5. 3. असिक्न्यस्योषधे Mbh. on 4. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्निका
असिक्निका A young woman-servant; गतो गणस्तूर्णमसिक्निकानाम्<BR> Kāśi. on P. IV. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unbound (Ved.).<BR>—2 [न सितः शुभ्रः] Not white, black, dark-blue, dark-coloured; असिता<BR> मोहरजनी Śānti. 3. 4; Y. 3. 166; ˚लोचना, ˚नयना &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितः|असित
असित + .{@-तः@} —1 The dark or blue colour. —2 the dark fortnight of lunar month.<BR>—3 N. of the planet Saturn.<BR>—4 A black snake.<BR>—5 N. of the sage देवल; असितो देवलो व्यासः Bg. 10. 13.<BR>—6 N. of a being presiding over darkness and magic.<BR>—7 N. of Kṛṣṇa; विसृजन्दिक्षु सर्वासु शरानसितसारथिः Mb. 7. 146. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिता
असित + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 The Indigo plant.<BR>—2 A girl attending upon the harem (whose hair is not whitened by age);<BR> see असिक्नी.<BR>—3 The river Yamunā.<BR>—4 N. of a daughter of Vīraṇa and wife of Dakṣa.<BR>—5 N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">Page0294-1</a>]<BR> river. Akesines (चन्द्रभागा) in the Punjab; Rv. 8. 20. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असिताञ्जनी, असिताम्बुजम्, असितोत्पलम्, असितार्चिस्, असिताश्मन्, असितकेशा, असितकेशान्त, असितगिरिः, असितनगः, असितग्रीव, असितज्ञु, असिताभ्रशेखरः, असितनयनम्, असितपक्षः, असितफलम्, असितभ्रू, असितमृगः, असितयवन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताञ्जनी
असित + -अञ्जनी The black cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताम्बुजम्
असित + -अम्बुजम्, -उत्पलम् the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितोत्पलम्
असित + -अम्बुजम्, -उत्पलम् the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितार्चिस्|असितार्च्चिस्
असित + -अर्चिस् <i>m.</i> fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताश्मन्
असित + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i>,<BR> {@-उपलः@} a dark-blue stone; lapis lazuli. निलयेषु नक्तमसिताश्मनां<BR> चयैः Śi. 13. 54; Ki. 16. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितकेशा
असित + -केशा a woman having black hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितकेशान्त
असित + -केशान्त <i>a.</i> having black locks of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितगिरिः|असितगिरि
असित + -गिरिः, -नगः ‘the blue mountain’; N. of a mountain. असितगिरिसमं<BR> स्यात् कज्जलं सिन्धुपात्रे । शिवमहिम्नस्तोत्र of पुष्पदन्ताचार्य,<BR> and Dr. Godeʼs papers Vol. III. असितनगनितम्बश्यामभासां घनानाम् Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितनगः
असित + -गिरिः, -नगः ‘the blue mountain’; N. of a mountain. असितगिरिसमं<BR> स्यात् कज्जलं सिन्धुपात्रे । शिवमहिम्नस्तोत्र of पुष्पदन्ताचार्य,<BR> and Dr. Godeʼs papers Vol. III. असितनगनितम्बश्यामभासां घनानाम् Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितग्रीव|असितग्रीवः
असित + -ग्रीव <i>a.</i> having a black neck. Vāj. 23. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितग्रीवः|असितग्रीव
असित + -ग्रीव + .({@-वः@})<BR>—1 fire.<BR>—2 A peacock; प्रावृषीवासितग्रीवो मज्जेत निशि निर्जने । मायूरेण गुणेनैव<BR> स्त्रीभिश्चावेक्षितश्चरेत् Mb. 12. 120. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितज्ञु
असित + -ज्ञु <i>a.</i> (for ˚जानु) having black knees. Av. 12. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताभ्रशेखरः|असिताभ्रशेखर
असित + -अभ्रशेखरः N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितनयन
असित + -नयन^1 <i>a.</i> black-eyed; मा कौलीनादसितनयने मय्यविश्वासिनी भूः Me. 114.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितपक्षः|असितपक्ष
असित + -पक्षः the dark fortnight; दुर्दिवसेऽसितपक्षे दुःसंचारासु<BR> नगरवीथीषु Pt. 1. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितफलम्
असित + -फलम् the sweet cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितभ्रू
असित + -भ्रू <i>a.</i> having black eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितमृगः|असितमृग
असित + -मृगः the black antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितयवन
असित + -यवन = कालयवन q. v. गुरुकोपरुद्धपदमापदसितयवनस्य<BR> रौद्रताम् Śi. 15. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
असिद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not accomplished.<BR>—2 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>—3 Unproved.<BR>—4 Unripe, raw, uncooked.<BR>—5 Not derivable by inference.<BR>—6 (in grammar) non-effective; inoperative (as a rule), not effected;<BR> as good as not effected <i>i. e.</i> null and void (as the operation of such<BR> a rule) पूर्वत्रासिद्धम् P. VIII. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धः|असिद्ध|असिद्धं
असिद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} A fallacious <i>hetu</i>; one of the five principal divisions<BR> of हेत्वाभास or fallacies. It is of three kinds:− (1) आश्रयासिद्ध<BR> where the existence of any such locality (आश्रय) as that where the<BR> property is said to reside, is not estabished; as ‘गगनारविन्दं सुरभि अरविन्दत्वात्’,<BR> (2) स्वरूपासिद्ध where the nature (स्वरूप) alleged<BR> does not really reside in the subject (पक्ष); as शब्दो गुणः चाक्षुषत्वात्;<BR> and (3) व्याप्यत्वासिद्ध where the alleged invariableness of concomitance<BR> is not real (the साध्यत्व not residing in साध्य); as पर्वतो<BR> वह्निमान् काञ्चनमयधूमात्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असिद्धान्तः, असिद्धार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धान्तः|असिद्धान्त
असिद्ध + -अन्तः Not an incontestable dogma; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धार्थ
असिद्ध + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> one who has not effected his aim; Rām. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धिः|असिद्धि
असिद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Imperfect accomplishment, failure; सिद्धपसिद्धपोः समो भूत्वा Bg. 2. 48, 4. 22.<BR>—2 Want of ripeness.<BR>—3 Non-accomplishment (in Yoga Phil.).<BR>—4 (In logic) Conclusion not warranted by the premises.<BR>—5 Want of resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिन्व
असिन्व <i>a.</i> Ved. Insatiable. असिन्वं वव्रं मह्याददुग्रः Rv. 5. 32. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिरः|असिर
असिरः [अस् क्षेपे किरच्]<BR>—1 A beam, a ray; यः सूर्यस्यासिरेण मृज्यते Rv. 9. 76. 4.<BR>—2 An arrow, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असी
असी N. of a river (near Banaras); see असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुः|असु
असुः [अस्यते क्षिप्यते अस्-उन् Uṇ. 1. 10; cf. Nir.; स हि अस्तः<BR> शरीरे भवति तस्य तत्र नित्यमवस्थानम्]<BR>—1 Breath; मीनगन्ध्यसुगन्धेन कुर्वन्तीं मार्गदूषणम् Bhāg. 6. 13. 13;<BR> life, spiritual<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">Page0294-2</a>]<BR> life; Rv. 10. 15. 1.<BR>—2 life of departed spirits.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 Heat.<BR>—5 (pl.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The five vital breaths or life-winds in the body; असुभिः स्थास्नु<BR> यशश्चिचीषितः Ki. 2. 19; परीक्षितं दुर्लभानसून् प्रापितवान् K. 175;<BR> Bh. 2. 110;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) wisdom (प्रज्ञा Nir.).<BR>—6 The time taken in pronouncing 10 long syllables.<BR>—7 A sixth part of a <i>pala</i> q. v. <i>n.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असु|असुः
असुः + .({@-सु@})<BR>—1 Reflection, thought.<BR>—2 Heart, mind.<BR>—3 Grief.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असुतृप्, असुतृप, असुभर, असुधारणम्, असुधारणा, असुनीतः, असुनीतिः, असुभङ्गः, असुभृत्, असुसम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृप्
असुः + -तृप्, -तृप, -भर <i>a.</i><BR> Enjoying oneʼs life, devoted to worldly pleasures;<BR> मातरं पितरं भ्रातॄन्सर्वांश्च सुहृदस्तथा । घ्नन्ति हपसुतृपो लुब्धा<BR> राजानः प्रायशो भुवि Bhāg. 10. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृप|असुतृपः
असुः + -तृप्, -तृप, -भर <i>a.</i><BR> Enjoying oneʼs life, devoted to worldly pleasures;<BR> मातरं पितरं भ्रातॄन्सर्वांश्च सुहृदस्तथा । घ्नन्ति हपसुतृपो लुब्धा<BR> राजानः प्रायशो भुवि Bhāg. 10. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभर
असुः + -तृप्, -तृप, -भर <i>a.</i><BR> Enjoying oneʼs life, devoted to worldly pleasures;<BR> मातरं पितरं भ्रातॄन्सर्वांश्च सुहृदस्तथा । घ्नन्ति हपसुतृपो लुब्धा<BR> राजानः प्रायशो भुवि Bhāg. 10. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुधारणम्
असुः + -धारणम्, -धारणा sustenance of life, life, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुधारणा
असुः + -धारणम्, -धारणा sustenance of life, life, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनीतः|असुनीत
असुः + -नीतः the lord of spirits; इमौ युनज्मि ते वह्नी असुनीताय वोढवे Av. 18. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनीतम्
असुः + -नीतः + .({@-तम्@}) the world of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनीतिः|असुनीति
असुः + -नीतिः <i>f.</i> the life or the spirits (personified as a female<BR> deity invoked for the preservation of life); असुनीते मनो अस्मासु धारय Rv. 10. 59. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभङ्गः|असुभङ्ग|असुभंग
असुः + -भङ्गः<BR>—1 destruction or loss of life; मलिनमसुभङ्गेप्यसुकरम् Bh. 2. 28.<BR>—2 danger or fear about life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभृत्
असुः + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a living being, a creature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसम|असुसमः
असुः + -सम <i>a.</i> as dear as life, dearly loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसमः|असुसम
असुः + -सम + .({@-मः@}) a husband, lover; मुहुरसुसममाघ्नती नितान्तम् Śi. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुमत्|असुमन्त्
असुमत् <i>a.</i> Living, breathing. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A living being; सततमसुमतामगम्यरूपाः Śi. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Life, the principle of vitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
असुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unhappy, sorrowful. अनित्यमसुखं लोकम् Bg. 9. 33<BR>—2 Not easy (to obtain), difficult श्रेयांसि लब्धुमसुखानि विनान्तरायैः Ki. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखम्
असुख + .{@-खम्@} Sorrow, pain, affliction; असुखं दर्शितं विकारेण M. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असुखावह, असुखाविष्ट, असुखोदय, असुखोदर्क, असुखजीविका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखावह
असुख + -आवह <i>a.</i> pained with grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखाविष्ट
असुख + -आविष्ट <i>a.</i> afflicted with grief or pain, causing great pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदय
असुख + -उदय <i>a.</i> causing or ending in unhappiness; न कर्म निष्फलं<BR> कुर्यान्नायत्यामसुखोदयम् Ms. 4. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदर्क
असुख + -उदर्क <i>a.</i> productive of or ending in unhappiness; तद्भवत्यसुखोदर्कं<BR> जीवतश्च मृतस्य च Ms. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखजीविका
असुख + -जीविका an unhappy life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखिन्
असुखिन् <i>a.</i> Unhappy, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुगन्ध|असुगन्धः
असुगन्ध <i>a.</i> Not fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुगन्धः|असुगन्ध
असुगन्ध + .{@-न्धः@} a bad smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Childless.<BR>—2 Ved. Not pressed out, not cleared or purified (as the Soma juice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्व
असुन्व [सु अभिषवे बा˚ श. न˚ त˚] Not pressing out<BR> the Soma juice. असुन्वामिन्द्र संसदं विषूचीं व्यनाशयः Rv. 8. 14. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतर
असुतर <i>a.</i> Not to be easily passed, see दुस्तरसततमसुतरं<BR> वर्णयन्त्यन्तरम् Ki. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृप|असुतृपः
असुतृप <i>a.</i> Insatiable; असुतृप उक्थशासश्चरन्ति Rv. 10. 82. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृपः|असुतृप
असुतृप^1 + .{@-पः@} A servant of Yama, messenger of death. See असु.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्दर
असुन्दर <i>a.</i> Not beautiful, or good or right; improper. किमप्यस्ति<BR> स्वभावेन सुन्दरं वाप्यसुन्दरम् Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुप्त
असुप्त <i>a.</i> Not asleep; असुप्तः सुप्तानाभिचाकशीति Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 11.<BR> ˚दृश्^1 not closing the eyes in sleep.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुम्न
असुम्न <i>a.</i> Ved. Contrary, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर <i>a.</i> [असु-र Uṇ. 1. 42]<BR>—1 Living, alive, spiritual.<BR>—2 An epithet of the Supreme Spirit or Varuṇa.<BR>—3 Incorporeal, super-human, divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरः|असुर
असुर + .{@-रः@} [According to Nir. अ सुरताः स्थानेषु न सुष्ठु रताः स्थानेषु<BR> चपला इत्यर्थः; or अस्ताः प्रच्याविता देवैः स्थानेभ्यः or from असु;<BR> असुः प्राणः तेन तद्वन्तो भवन्ति रो मत्वर्थे; or सोर्देवानसृजत<BR> तत्सुराणां सुरत्वम्, असोः असुरानसृजत तदसुराणामसुरत्वम्; सोः = प्रशस्तादात्मनः प्रदेशात्]<BR>—1 An evil spirit, a demon; the chief of the evil spirits; वृकद्वरसो<BR> असुरस्य वीरान् Rv. 2. 30. 4. The Rām. thus accounts for the name:−<BR> सुराप्रतिग्रहाद्देवाः सुरा इत्यभिविश्रुताः । अप्रतिग्रहणात्तस्या दैतेयाश्चासुरास्तथा ॥<BR> [In the oldest parts of the Ṛgveda the term <i>Asura</i> is used for<BR> the Supreme Spirit and in the sense of ‘god’, ‘divine’; it was applied<BR> to several of the chief deities such as Indra, Agni, and especially Varuṇa.<BR> It afterwards acquired an entirely opposite meaning, and came to signify<BR> a demon or an enemy of the gods. The Brāhmaṇas state that Prajāpati<BR> created <i>Asuras</i> with the breath (<i>Asu</i>); particularly from the lower<BR> breath. The Vāyu P. says that Asuras were first produced as sons from<BR> Prajāpatiʼs groin; cf. also Nir. above].<BR>—2 A general name for the enemies of gods, Daityas and Dānavas, distinguished<BR> from Rākṣasas descended from Pulastya; कानीयसा एव देवा ज्यायसा असुराः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 1; Bg. 11. 22.<BR>—3 A ghost or spectre.<BR>—4 The sun (said to be from अस् to shine).<BR>—5 An elephant.<BR>—6 An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>—7 A cloud.<BR>—8 N. of a warrior tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरा
असुर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 A zodiacal sign.<BR>—3 A prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरी
असुर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A female demon, wife of an Asura.<BR>—2 N. of the plant Sinapis Racemosa Roxb. (Mar. काळी मोहरी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असुराधिपः, असुरेन्द्रः, असुरराज्, असुरराजः, असुराचार्यः, असुरगुरुः, असुराह्वम्, असुरक्षयण, असुरक्षिति, असुरगुरुः, असुरद्रुह्, असुरद्विष्, असुरमाया, असुररक्षस, असुररिपुः, असुरसूदनः, असुरहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुराधिपः|असुराधिप
असुर + -अधिपः, -इन्द्रः, -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 the lord of the Asuras.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bali, grandson of Prahlāda; यज्ञं चकार सुमहानसुरेन्द्रो<BR> महाबलः Rām. 1. 29. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरेन्द्रः|असुरेन्द्र
असुर + -अधिपः, -इन्द्रः, -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 the lord of the Asuras.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bali, grandson of Prahlāda; यज्ञं चकार सुमहानसुरेन्द्रो<BR> महाबलः Rām. 1. 29. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरराज्
असुर + -अधिपः, -इन्द्रः, -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 the lord of the Asuras.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bali, grandson of Prahlāda; यज्ञं चकार सुमहानसुरेन्द्रो<BR> महाबलः Rām. 1. 29. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरराजः
असुर + -अधिपः, -इन्द्रः, -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 the lord of the Asuras.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bali, grandson of Prahlāda; यज्ञं चकार सुमहानसुरेन्द्रो<BR> महाबलः Rām. 1. 29. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुराचार्यः|असुराचार्य
असुर + -आचार्यः, -गुरुः<BR>—1 N. of the preceptor of the Asuras, Śukrācārya.<BR>—2 the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरगुरुः|असुरगुरु
असुर + -आचार्यः, -गुरुः<BR>—1 N. of the preceptor of the Asuras, Śukrācārya.<BR>—2 the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुराह्वम्
असुर + -आह्वम् bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्षयण
असुर + -क्षयण, -क्षिति <i>a.</i> destroying the Asuras; असुरक्षयणं<BR> वधं त्रिषन्धि दिव्याश्रयन् Av. 11. 10. 10; यमबध्नाद् बृहस्पतिर्देवेभ्यो<BR> असुरक्षितिम् Av. 10. 6. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्षिति
असुर + -क्षयण, -क्षिति <i>a.</i> destroying the Asuras; असुरक्षयणं<BR> वधं त्रिषन्धि दिव्याश्रयन् Av. 11. 10. 10; यमबध्नाद् बृहस्पतिर्देवेभ्यो<BR> असुरक्षितिम् Av. 10. 6. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरगुरुः|असुरगुरु
असुर + -गुरुः<BR>—1 The planet Venus (शुक).<BR>—2 Śukrācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरद्रुह्
असुर + -द्रुह् ‘Enemy of the Asuras’, a god; पुरः क्लिश्नाति सोमं हि<BR> सैंहिकेयोऽसुरद्रुहाम् Śi. 2. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरद्विष्
असुर + -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an enemy of the Asuras, <i>i. e.</i> a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरमाया
असुर + -माया demoniacal magic; येना श्रवस्यवश्चरथ देवा इवासुरमायया Av. 3. 9. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुररक्षस्
असुर + -रक्षस् <i>n.</i> (pl.) the Asuras and Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुररक्षसम्
असुर + -रक्षस् + .({@-सम्@}) a demoniacal being partaking of the qualities of both the classes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुररिपुः|असुररिपु
असुर + -रिपुः, -सूदनः ‘destroyer of Asuras’, an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR> भ्राता भव यवीयांस्त्वं शकस्यासुरसूदन Rām. 1. 29. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसूदनः|असुरसूदन
असुर + -रिपुः, -सूदनः ‘destroyer of Asuras’, an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR> भ्राता भव यवीयांस्त्वं शकस्यासुरसूदन Rām. 1. 29. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरहन्
असुर + -हन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who destroys the Asuras, an epithet of Agni, Indra &c.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्य|असुर्यः|असुर्य्य
असुर्य <i>a.</i> [असुराय हिताः गवा˚ यत्]<BR>—1 Incorporeal, spiritual, divine.<BR>—2 Demoniacal, belonging to the Asuras or sprung from them (असुरस्य<BR> स्वम् P. IV. 4. 123).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्यम्
असुर्य + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 The water of the clouds.<BR>—2 Spirituality, divine<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">Page0295-2</a>]<BR> nature.<BR>—3 The collective body of spiritual beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्यः|असुर्य|असुर्य्य
असुर्य + .{@-र्यः@} The Supreme Spirit; अपां नपादसुर्यस्य मह्ना Rv. 2. 35. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरत्वम्
असुरत्वम् Spirituality, supernatural or divine nature; महद् देवानामसुरत्वमेकम् Rv. 3. 55. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष
असुरक्ष <i>a.</i> Difficult to guard or preserve; perishable; असुरक्षा<BR> हि बहुच्छलाः श्रियः Ki. 3. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसा
असुरसा [न सुष्ठु रसो यस्याः] N. of a plant; a variety of तुलसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
असुलभ <i>a.</i> Not easily attainable, difficult to secure; असुलभा<BR> सकलेन्दुमुखी च सा V. 2. 9. (v. l. न सुलभा˚)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुषिर
असुषिर <i>a.</i> Not hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुष्वि
असुष्वि <i>a.</i> [सु-बा˚ कि द्वित्वम्, न˚ त˚ Tv.] Not pressing<BR> out the Soma juice, irreligious, wicked. See असुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसूः
असुसूः [असून् प्राणान् सुवति सू-क्विप्] An arrow; स सासिः सासुसूः<BR> सासो येयायेयाययाययः Ki. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुस्थ|असुस्थः
असुस्थ <i>a.</i> Unwell, indisposed; ˚ता indisposition, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
असुहृद् <i>m.</i> An enemy; शलभतां लभतामसुहृद्गणः Śi. 2. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असू
असू <i>a.</i> Not bringing forth, barren (as a cow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक
असूक <i>a.</i> See असूयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूत
असूत, असूतिक <i>a.</i> One who has not brought forth, barren;<BR> असूतिका रामायण्यपचित् प्र पतिष्यति Av. 6. 83. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूतिक
असूत, असूतिक <i>a.</i> One who has not brought forth, barren;<BR> असूतिका रामायण्यपचित् प्र पतिष्यति Av. 6. 83. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूतजरती
असूतजरती (a Woman) who grows old without having brought forth<BR> a child; P. VI. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूतिः|असूति
असूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Non-production, barrenness.<BR>—2 Obstruction, removal; तपसां सूतिरसूतिरापदाम् Ki. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्षणम्
असूक्षणम् [सूक्ष्-आदरे ल्युट्, न˚ त˚] Disrespect; also in<BR> the same sense, असुक्षणम्, असुर्क्षणम्, असूर्क्षणम्, अस्तर्क्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूय
असूय <i>a.</i> Grumbling at, displeased with; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयति
असूयति Den. P. (P. III. 1. 27)<BR>—1 To envy, to be jealous of; कथं चित्रगतो भर्ता मयाऽसूयितः M. 4.<BR>—2 To detract from; murmur, grumble at, be displeased with, scorn, be<BR> discontented with or angry with (with dat. of person or thing); असूयन्ति<BR> सचिवोपदेशाय K. 108; असूयन्ति मह्यं प्रकृतयः V. 4; न्यसनाय<BR> ससौरभस्य कस्तरुसूनस्य शिरस्यसूयति Śi. 16. 20; श्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो<BR> मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः Bg. 3. 31; sometimes with acc.; असूयन्ति हि<BR> राजानो जनाननृतवादिनः<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to murmur at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयक|असूयकः
असूयक <i>a.</i> [असूय्-ण्युल् P. III. 2. 146]<BR>—1 Envious, detracting, calumnious.<BR>—2 Discontented, displeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयकः|असूयक
असूयक + .{@-कः@} A detractor, an envious man; असूयकायानृणवे Nir. 2. 4;<BR> असूयकाय मां मा दाः Ms. 2. 114; Śānti. 3. 7; Y. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयनम्
असूयनम्<BR>—1 Detraction, calumny.<BR>—2 Envy, jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया<BR>—1 Envy, intolerance, jealousy (of the happiness of others); कुधद्रुहेर्ष्यासूयार्थानां<BR> यं प्रति कोपः P. I. 4. 37, III. 4. 28, VIII. 1. 8. सासूयम् enviously.<BR>—2 Calumny, detraction (of the merits of others); असूया परगुणेषु दोषाविष्करणम्<BR> Sk. (= दोषारोपो गुणेष्वपि Ak.); Ms. 7. 48; R. 4. 23.<BR>—3 Anger, indignation; वधूरसूयाकुटिलं ददर्श R. 6. 82; सासूयमुक्ता<BR> सखी Ś. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयितृ
असूयितृ <i>a.</i> Envious, detracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयुः|असूयु
असूयुः<BR>—1 Envious, jealous.<BR>—2 Displeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर
असूर <i>a.</i> Ved. Devoid of praise or worship; असूरेः सन्ति सूरयः<BR> Rv. 8. 10. 4. (स्तोत्ररहित). <i>ind.</i> In the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूरम्
असूर + .{@-रम्@} Ved. Absence of a person to extract the Soma juice; a place<BR> devoid of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्त|असूर्त्त
असूर्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not moving (अप्रेरित)<BR>—2 unilluminated, dark.<BR>—3 unvisited, unknown, romote. असूर्तं रजो अप्यगुस्ते यन्त्वधमं तमः<BR> Av. 10. 3. 9; असूर्तरजसो नाम धर्मारण्यं महामतिः Rām. 1. 32. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्य
असूर्य <i>a.</i> Sunless; असूर्ये तमसि वावृधानम् Rv. 5. 32. 6.<BR>━<i>ind.</i> At night.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असूर्यग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्यग
असूर्य + -ग <i>a.</i> not entering into the Sun, <i>i. e.</i> not set; ग्रहैस्ततः<BR> पञ्चभिरुच्चसंश्रयैरसूर्यगैः सूचितभाग्यसम्पदम् R. 3. 13; (रविणास्तमयो<BR> योगो वियोगस्तूदयो भवेत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्यंपश्य
असूर्यंपश्य <i>a.</i> [सूर्यमपि न पश्यति दृश् खश् मुम् च P. III. 2. 36]<BR> Not seeing even the sun; said of the wives of a king who, being<BR> shut up in the harem, have no opportunity of seeing the sun; असूर्यंपश्या<BR> राजदाराः Sk. असूर्यंपश्यान्यप्यहह सुलभान्यश्मभवनान्यरण्यानीभाजामतिपतति<BR> भाग्यं किल गिरः Viś. Guṇā. 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्यंपश्या|असूर्यम्पश्या|असूर्य्यम्पश्या
असूर्यंपश्य + .{@-श्या@} A chaste and loyal wife. असूर्यंपश्यया मूर्त्या हृता, तां<BR> मृगयामहे Bk. 6. 98, cf. also Śiva B. 6. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज् <i>n.</i> [न सृज्यते इतररागवत् संसृज्यते सहजत्वात् न-सृज्क्विन् Tv.]<BR>—1 Blood; भूम्या असुरसृगात्मा क्व स्वित् Rv. 1. 164. 4.<BR>—2 The planet Mars.<BR>—3 Saffron. ━<i>m.</i> N. of the 16th of the 27 Yogas; धनी कुरूपः कुमतिर्दुरात्मा<BR> विदेशगामी रुधिरप्रकोपः महाप्रलोभी पुरुषो बलीयानसृक्प्रसूतौ किल यस्य<BR> जन्तोः ॥ Śabdak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असृक्करः, असृग्ग्रहः, असृग्दरः, असृग्दोहः, असृग्धरा, असृग्धारा, असृक्पः, असृक्पाः, असृक्पातः, असृग्वन्, असृग्वहा, असृग्विमोक्षणम्, असृक्छ्रावः, असृक्स्रावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्करः|असृक्कर
असृज् + -करः [असृक् शोणितं करोति कृ-ट] the essence of the body;<BR> lymph, serum; (the process of रस turning into blood &c., is thus<BR> described by Suśr.:− रसाद्रक्तं ततो मांसं मांसान्मेदः प्रजायते ।<BR> मेदसोस्थि ततो मज्जा मज्ज्नः शुकस्य संभवः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्ग्रहः|असृग्ग्रह
असृज् + -ग्रहः Mars. Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्दरः|असृग्दर
असृज् + -दरः an irregular or excessive menstruation, maenorrhagia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्दोहः|असृग्दोह
असृज् + -दोहः shedding blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धरा
असृज् + -धरा the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धारा
असृज् + -धारा<BR>—1 a stream of blood.<BR>—2 the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पः|असृक्प
असृज् + -पः, -पाः ‘a blood-drinker’, a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पाः
असृज् + -पः, -पाः ‘a blood-drinker’, a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पातः|असृक्पात
असृज् + -पातः the falling of blood; कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्रोऽसृक्पाते Y. 3. 292<BR> (pl.) drops of blood; यथा नयत्यसृक्पातैर्मृगस्य मृगयुः पदम् Ms. 8. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्वन्
असृज् + -वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. drinking blood; अरायमसृक्वानं यश्च स्फातिं<BR> जिहीर्षति Av. 2. 25. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्वहा
असृज् + -वहा a blood-vessel; pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्विमोक्षणम्
असृज् + -विमोक्षणम् blood-letting, bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्छ्रावः
असृज् + -श्रावः, -स्रावः bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्स्रावः|असृक्स्राव
असृज् + -श्रावः, -स्रावः bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाटः|असृपाट
असृपाटः, -टी<BR> [असृजः पाटी परिपाटी पृषो˚] A stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाटी
असृपाटः, -टी<BR> [असृजः पाटी परिपाटी पृषो˚] A stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृणि
असृणि, -णी <i>a.</i><BR> Unrestrained (as by a goad); मनोवीर्यवरोत्सिक्तमसृण्यमकुतोभयम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृणी
असृणि, -णी <i>a.</i><BR> Unrestrained (as by a goad); मनोवीर्यवरोत्सिक्तमसृण्यमकुतोभयम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्ट
असृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uncreated.<BR>—2 Continued.<BR>—3 Unpresented or undistributed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असृष्टान्न<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्टान्न
असृष्ट + -अन्न <i>a.</i> one who does not distribute food; विधिहीनमसृष्टान्नम् Bg. 17. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचन
असेचन, -नक <i>a.</i><BR> That on which one cannot look enough, charming, lovely;<BR> नयनयुगासेचनकं मानसवृत्त्यापि दुष्प्रापम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचनक|असेचनकं
असेचन, -नक <i>a.</i><BR> That on which one cannot look enough, charming, lovely;<BR> नयनयुगासेचनकं मानसवृत्त्यापि दुष्प्रापम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेन्य
असेन्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not befitting an army.<BR>—2 Not striking; असेन्या वः पणयो वचांसि Rv. 10. 108. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवन
असेवन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not serving, disregarding.<BR>—2 Not following or practising, shunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवनम्
असेवन + .{@-नम्@} Disregard, disobedience, inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
असेवित <i>a.</i> Neglected; disused, abstained from.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: असेवितेश्वर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवितेश्वर
असेवित + -ईश्वर or ˚द्वार <i>a.</i> not waiting at the doors of the rich or great. H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवा
असेवा<BR>—1 Not following or practising; न तथैतानि शक्यन्ते सन्नियन्तुमसेवया Ms. 2. 96.<BR>—2 Disregard, inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असोढ
असोढ <i>a.</i> Not to be endured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौनामन्
असौनामन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Having such and such a name. असौ नामायमिदं<BR> रूपः Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्य
असौम्य <i>a.</i> Not lovely, ugly, disagreeable; ˚कृत्^1 <i>a.</i> Troublesome;<BR> ममापि सोऽपराध्नोति यो युष्माकमसौम्यकृत् Mb. 8. 33. 41. ˚स्वर<BR> <i>a.</i> having a bad or croaking voice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठव|असौष्ठवं
असौष्ठव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devoid of beauty or loveliness, not in good trim; शरीरमसौष्ठवम् Māl. 1. 17.<BR>—2 Ugly, deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठवम्
असौष्ठव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Worthlessness, absence of merit.<BR>—2 Deformity, ugliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्न
अस्कन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not spilt^1. अस्कन्नमद्य देवेभ्यऽआज्यं Vāj. 2. 8.<BR>—2 Not poured out or effused.<BR>—3 Not sprinkled, not covered (as a cow).<BR>—4 Permanent, durable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्दित|अस्कंदित
अस्कन्दित <i>a.</i> Not split; not gone, not attacked; ˚व्रत true to oneʼs vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कृधोयु
अस्कृधोयु <i>a.</i> Not short or deficient, abundant, uninterrupted (अविच्छिन्न<BR> Sāy.); अस्मेधत्तं यदसदस्कृधोयु Rv. 7. 53. 3, 6. 67. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अस्खलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unshaken, unyielding, firm, permanent.<BR>—2 unhurt, sound and safe; ˚भ्रातृशतः Ve. 5.<BR>—3 Not stumbling or slipping, undeviating, careful; स मे चिरायास्खलितोपचाराम्<BR> R. 5. 20; ˚प्रयाण <i>a.</i> with unfaltering steps, not stumbling in gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त, -अस्तु &c.<BR> see under अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्त, -अस्तु &c.<BR> see under अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अस्तब्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not firm or self-possessed, confused;<BR>—2 Not tired, moving, agile (as a bird); Rām. 3.<BR>—3 Not arrogant or obstinate; modest; Mb. 5, 12, ˚त्वम् want of self-possession, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तर्क्षणम्
अस्तर्क्षणम् = असूक्षणम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताघ|अस्ताघः
अस्ताघ <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिकः
अस्तिकः N. of a sage whose intercession saved the serpents from being<BR> burnt down in the sacrificial fire of Janamejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृत
अस्तृत <i>a.</i> Ved. Not overcome, invincible शास इत्था महाँ अस्यमित्रसाहो<BR> अस्तृतः Av. 1. 20. 4. ˚यज्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. sacrificing untiringly;<BR> इमे विप्रस्य वेधसोऽग्नेरस्तृतयज्वनः Rv. 8. 53. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेयम्
अस्तेयम् Not stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तोक
अस्तोक <i>a.</i> Not slight or little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तोभ
अस्तोभ <i>a.</i> Without having superfluous words; अस्तोभमनवद्यं<BR> च सूत्रं सूत्रविदो विदुः; Without stoppage or pause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्यानम्
अस्त्यानम्<BR>—1 Reproach, blame.<BR>—2 Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रम्
अस्त्रम् [अस्यते क्षिप्यते अस् ष्ट्रन् Uṇ. 4. 158.]<BR>—1 A missile; a weapon in general; प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रमितो वृथा स्यात्<BR> R. 2. 34; प्रत्याहतास्त्रो गिरिशप्रभावात् 2. 41, 3. 58; अशिक्षतास्त्रं<BR> पितुरेव R. 3. 31 the science of missiles. महर्षेरग्निवेशस्य सकाशमहमच्युत ।<BR> अस्त्रार्थमगमं पूर्वं धनुर्वेदचिकीर्षया ॥ Mb. 1. 131. 40. धनुर्वेदसंहिता<BR> mentions various kinds of missiles (179-82) as ब्रह्मास्त्र, ब्रह्मदण्डक,<BR> ब्रह्मशिरस, पाशुपत, वायव्य, आग्नेय, नारसिंह &c.<BR>—2 An arrow; sword.<BR>—3 A bow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्त्रागारम्, अस्त्रागारम्, अस्त्राघातः, अस्त्राहत, अस्त्रकण्टक, अस्त्रकारः, अस्त्रकारकः, अस्त्रकारिन्, अस्त्रक्षेपक, अस्त्रग्रामः, अस्त्रचिकित्सक, अस्त्रचिकित्सा, अस्त्रजित्, अस्त्रजीवः, अस्त्रजीविन्, अस्त्रधारणम्, अस्त्रनिवारणम्, अस्त्रपातिन्, अस्त्रभृत्, अस्त्रमन्त्रः, अस्त्रमर्जः, अस्त्रमर्जकः, अस्त्रयन्त्रम्, अस्त्रयुद्धम्, अस्त्रलाघवम्, अस्त्रविद्, अस्त्रविद्या, अस्त्रशास्त्रम्, अस्त्रवेदः, अस्त्रवृष्टि, अस्त्रशस्त्रम्, अस्त्रशिक्षा, अस्त्रसायकः, अस्त्रहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रागारम्
अस्त्रम् + -अगारम्, -आगारम् an arsenal, armoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रागारम्
अस्त्रम् + -अगारम्, -आगारम् an arsenal, armoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राघातः|अस्त्राघात
अस्त्रम् + -आघातः a wound, a cut (made by a weapon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राहत
अस्त्रम् + -आहत <i>a.</i> struck, wounded, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकण्टक|अस्त्रकंटक|अस्त्रकण्टकः
अस्त्रम् + -कण्टक [अस्त्रं कण्टक इव] an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकारः|अस्त्रकार
अस्त्रम् + -कारः, -कारकः, -कारिन् a maker of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकारकः|अस्त्रकारक
अस्त्रम् + -कारः, -कारकः, -कारिन् a maker of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकारिन्
अस्त्रम् + -कारः, -कारकः, -कारिन् a maker of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रक्षेपक
अस्त्रम् + -क्षेपक <i>a.</i> shooting arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रग्रामः|अस्त्रग्राम
अस्त्रम् + -ग्रामः A heap or collection of different missiles or weapons; Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सक|अस्त्रचिकित्सकः
अस्त्रम् + -चिकित्सक <i>a.</i> surgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सा
अस्त्रम् + -चिकित्सा surgery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रजित्
अस्त्रम् + -जित् <i>m.</i> N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रजीवः|अस्त्रजीव
अस्त्रम् + -जीवः, -जीविन् <i>m.</i>, {@-धारिन्@}<BR> <i>m.</i> a soldier, professional warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रजीविन्
अस्त्रम् + -जीवः, -जीविन् <i>m.</i>, {@-धारिन्@}<BR> <i>m.</i> a soldier, professional warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रधारणम्
अस्त्रम् + -धारणम् the bearing of arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रनिवारणम्
अस्त्रम् + -निवारणम् the warding of a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रपातिन्
अस्त्रम् + -पातिन् A gunner; अस्त्रपातिभिरावृतम् Śukra. 4. 1037.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रभृत्
अस्त्रम् + -भृत् <i>m.</i> A shooter; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रमन्त्रः|अस्त्रमन्त्र
अस्त्रम् + -मन्त्रः a Mantra to be repeated in discharging or withdrawing<BR> a missile; संमोहनं नाम सखे ममास्त्रं प्रयोगसंहारविभक्तमन्त्रम् R. 5. 57, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रमर्जः
अस्त्रम् + -मर्जः, -मर्जकः a furbisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रमर्जकः
अस्त्रम् + -मर्जः, -मर्जकः a furbisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रयन्त्रम्
अस्त्रम् + -यन्त्रम् A kind of missile (कंचिन्मर्मदेशमाक्षिप्य येन शत्रोरुत्क्षेपणमपक्षेपणं<BR> च क्रियते तदस्त्रयन्त्रम् । इति नीलकण्ठः) Mb. 9. 57. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रयुद्धम्
अस्त्रम् + -युद्धम् fighting with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रलाघवम्
अस्त्रम् + -लाघवम् dexterity in wielding or throwing missiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रविद्
अस्त्रम् + -विद् <i>a.</i> skilled in the science of arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रविद्या
अस्त्रम् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम्, -वेदः the art or science of throwing missiles,<BR> military science, science of arms; अस्त्रवेदमधिगम्य तत्त्वतः Ki. 13. 62,<BR> U. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रशास्त्रम्
अस्त्रम् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम्, -वेदः the art or science of throwing missiles,<BR> military science, science of arms; अस्त्रवेदमधिगम्य तत्त्वतः Ki. 13. 62,<BR> U. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रवेदः|अस्त्रवेद
अस्त्रम् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम्, -वेदः the art or science of throwing missiles,<BR> military science, science of arms; अस्त्रवेदमधिगम्य तत्त्वतः Ki. 13. 62,<BR> U. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रवृष्टि
अस्त्रम् + -वृष्टि <i>f.</i> a shower of missiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रशस्त्रम्
अस्त्रम् + -शस्त्रम् all sorts of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रशिक्षा
अस्त्रम् + -शिक्षा military exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रसायकः|अस्त्रसायक
अस्त्रम् + -सायकः<BR>—1 an iron arrow.<BR>—2 the नाराच missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रहीन
अस्त्रम् + -हीन <i>a.</i> unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रिन्
अस्त्रिन् <i>a.</i> Fighting with a missile weapon, an archer; अस्त्री<BR> जनः पुनरनेन कृतः किल स्त्री Udb. (a pun on the word); संदानान्तादस्त्रिभिः<BR> शिक्षितास्त्रैः Śi. 18. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्री
अस्त्री<BR>—1 Not a woman.<BR>—2 (In gram.) The masculine and neuter genders; वल्कं वल्कलमस्त्रियाम्<BR> Ak. अस्त्री पङ्कम् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रीक
अस्त्रीक <i>a.</i> Having no wife; without a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रैण
अस्त्रैण <i>a.</i> Ved. Without a wife; पर्यस्ताक्षा अप्रचङ्कशा अस्त्रैणाः<BR> सन्तु पण्डगाः Av. 8. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्
अस्थन् <i>n.</i> (the base used in some of the cases of अस्थिं; after acc.) A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्थवत्
अस्थन् + .{@-वत्@} <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having bones, bony; अस्थन्वन्तं यदनस्था बिभर्ति Rv. 1. 164. 4.<BR>—2 Vertebrated (animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्था
अस्था Ved. At once; नेममाविरस्था कृणोति Rv. 10. 48. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाग|अस्थागं
अस्थाग (-घः, -यः, -रः)<BR> <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाघः|अस्थाघ|अस्थाघं
अस्थाग (-घः, -यः, -रः)<BR> <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायः|अस्थाय|अस्थायं
अस्थाग (-घः, -यः, -रः)<BR> <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थारः|अस्थार|अस्थारं
अस्थाग (-घः, -यः, -रः)<BR> <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अस्थान <i>a.</i> Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थानम्
अस्थान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A bad or wrong place; अस्थाने पततामतीव महतामेतादृशी स्याद् गतिः S. D.<BR>—2 An improper place or object or occasion; ˚वर्षी Dk. 81 (= अपात्रदायिन्);<BR> अस्थानं परिभूतेः K. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाने
अस्थाने <i>ind.</i> Unseasonably, out of place, inopportunely, in a wrong<BR> place, on an unworthy object; उभयोरप्यस्थाने प्रयत्नः Mu. 2; अस्थाने<BR> महानर्थोत्सर्गः क्रियते Mu. 3; अस्थाने कोपः M. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अस्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Not permanent, transitory, perishable; प्रायेण साधुवृत्तानामस्थायिन्यो<BR> विपत्तयः Bh. 2. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थावर|अस्थावरं
अस्थावर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Movable, moving, not fixed.<BR>—2 (In law) Personal, as property, money, cattle &c. as opposed to land<BR> (= जंगम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थास्नु
अस्थास्नु <i>a.</i> Impatient; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि <i>n.</i> [अस्यते अस्-कथिन् Uṇ. 3. 154]<BR>—1 A bone (changed to अस्थ at the end of certain compounds; cf. अनस्थ, पुरुषास्थ).<BR>—2 The kernel or stone of a fruit; जम्बूफलानामत्युच्चनिपातविशीर्णानामनस्थिप्रायाणाम्<BR> Bhāg. 5. 16. 19; न कार्पासास्थि न तुषान् Ms. 4. 78. [cf. L. <i>os</i>;<BR> Gr. <i>osteon</i>; Zend. <i>asta</i>; Pers. <i>astah</i>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्थिकुण्डम्, अस्थिकृत्, अस्थितेजस्, अस्थिसंभवः, अस्थिसारः, अस्थिस्नेहः, अस्थिच्छलितम्, अस्थिजः, अस्थितुण्डः, अस्थितोदः, अस्थित्वच्, अस्थिधन्वन्, अस्थिपञ्जरः, अस्थिप्रक्षेपः, अस्थिबन्धनम्, अस्थिभक्षः, अस्थिभुक्, अस्थिभङ्गः, अस्थिभूयस्, अस्थिभेदः, अस्थिभेदकः, अस्थिभेदिन्, अस्थिमाला, अस्थिमालिन्, अस्थियज्ञः, अस्थियुज्, अस्थियोगः, अस्थिविग्रह, अस्थिविलयः, अस्थिशृङ्खला, अस्थिसंहारः, अस्थिसंहारिका, अस्थिशेष, अस्थिशोषः, अस्थिसंहारकः, अस्थिसंचयः, अस्थिसन्धिः, अस्थिसमर्पणम्, अस्थिसारः, अस्थिस्थूणः, अस्थिस्नेहः, अस्थिस्रंस<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिकुण्डम्
अस्थि + -कुण्डम् N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिकृत्
अस्थि + -कृत्, -तेजस्, -संभवः, -सारः, -स्नेहः marrow; (पिबन्ति)<BR> अस्थिस्नेहसुराः कपालचषकैः प्रीताः पिशाचाङ्गनाः Māl. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितेजस्
अस्थि + -कृत्, -तेजस्, -संभवः, -सारः, -स्नेहः marrow; (पिबन्ति)<BR> अस्थिस्नेहसुराः कपालचषकैः प्रीताः पिशाचाङ्गनाः Māl. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंभवः|अस्थिसम्भव
अस्थि + -कृत्, -तेजस्, -संभवः, -सारः, -स्नेहः marrow; (पिबन्ति)<BR> अस्थिस्नेहसुराः कपालचषकैः प्रीताः पिशाचाङ्गनाः Māl. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसारः|अस्थिसार
अस्थि + -कृत्, -तेजस्, -संभवः, -सारः, -स्नेहः marrow; (पिबन्ति)<BR> अस्थिस्नेहसुराः कपालचषकैः प्रीताः पिशाचाङ्गनाः Māl. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्नेहः|अस्थिस्नेह
अस्थि + -कृत्, -तेजस्, -संभवः, -सारः, -स्नेहः marrow; (पिबन्ति)<BR> अस्थिस्नेहसुराः कपालचषकैः प्रीताः पिशाचाङ्गनाः Māl. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिच्छलितम्
अस्थि + -च्छलितम् a particular fracture of the bone; (पार्श्वयोरस्थिहीनोद्गतम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिजः|अस्थिज
अस्थि + -जः<BR>—1 marrow.<BR>—2 thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितुण्डः|अस्थितुण्ड|अस्थितुंड
अस्थि + -तुण्डः [अस्थीव कठिनं तुण्डमस्य]<BR>—1 a kind of bird whose mouth or beak is as hard as a bone.<BR>—2 a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितोदः|अस्थितोद
अस्थि + -तोदः pain in the bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित्वच्
अस्थि + -त्वच् <i>f.</i> periosteum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिधन्वन्
अस्थि + -धन्वन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिपञ्जरः|अस्थिपञ्जर|अस्थिपंजर
अस्थि + -पञ्जरः ‘a cage of bones’, a skeleton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिप्रक्षेपः|अस्थिप्रक्षेप
अस्थि + -प्रक्षेपः throwing the bones of the dead into the Ganges or any holy waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिबन्धनम्
अस्थि + -बन्धनम् Sinew; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभक्षः|अस्थिभक्ष
अस्थि + -भक्षः, -भुक् ‘an eater of bones’, a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभुक्
अस्थि + -भक्षः, -भुक् ‘an eater of bones’, a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभङ्गः|अस्थिभङ्ग|अस्थिभंग
अस्थि + -भङ्गः fracture of the bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभूयस्
अस्थि + -भूयस् <i>a.</i> consisting chiefly of bones, dried up; भवत्यस्थिभूयान् Av. 5. 18. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेदः|अस्थिभेद
अस्थि + -भेदः<BR>—1 fracturing or breaking a bone.<BR>—2 a sort of bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेदकः|अस्थिभेदक
अस्थि + -भेदकः a bone-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेदिन्
अस्थि + -भेदिन् <i>a.</i> That cuts or pierces the bone; very smarting or<BR> severe; वाचस्तीक्ष्णास्थिभेदिन्यः सूतपुत्रेण भाषिताः Mb. 3. 312. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमाला
अस्थि + -माला<BR>—1 a string or wreath of bones.<BR>—2 a row of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमालिन्
अस्थि + -मालिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थियज्ञः|अस्थियज्ञ
अस्थि + -यज्ञः Bone sacrifice (part of a funeral ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थियुज्
अस्थि + -युज् <i>m.</i> [अस्थि युनक्ति] a kind of tree (हस्तिशुण्डावृक्ष;<BR> Mar. कांडवेल, हाडसंधि).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">Page0298-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थियोगः
अस्थि + -योगः the joining of a broken limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिविग्रह|अस्थिविग्रहः
अस्थि + -विग्रह <i>a.</i> reduced to a skeleton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिविग्रहः|अस्थिविग्रह
अस्थि + -विग्रह + .({@-हः@}) N. of भृङ्गिन् Śivaʼs attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिविलयः|अस्थिविलय
अस्थि + -विलयः Dissolving of bones in a sacred stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिशृङ्खला
अस्थि + -शृङ्खला, -संहारः, -संहारिका N. of the plant Heliotropium Indicum<BR> (ग्रन्थिमतीवृक्ष; Mar. इन्द्रवारुणी, कवंडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहारः|अस्थिसंहार
अस्थि + -शृङ्खला, -संहारः, -संहारिका N. of the plant Heliotropium Indicum<BR> (ग्रन्थिमतीवृक्ष; Mar. इन्द्रवारुणी, कवंडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहारिका
अस्थि + -शृङ्खला, -संहारः, -संहारिका N. of the plant Heliotropium Indicum<BR> (ग्रन्थिमतीवृक्ष; Mar. इन्द्रवारुणी, कवंडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिशेष
अस्थि + -शेष <i>a.</i> [अस्थिमात्रं शेषोऽस्य] very lean, reduced to skeleton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिशोषः|अस्थिशोष
अस्थि + -शोषः dryness and decay of the bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहारकः|अस्थिसंहारक
अस्थि + -संहारकः<BR>—1 bone-seizer. —2 the adjutant bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंचयः|अस्थिसञ्चय|अस्थिसंचय
अस्थि + -संचयः collecting the bones or their ashes after burning a corpse.<BR>—2 a heap of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसन्धिः|अस्थिसन्धि|अस्थिसंधि
अस्थि + -सन्धिः<BR>—1 a joint, an articulation.<BR>—2 uniting a broken bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसमर्पणम्
अस्थि + -समर्पणम् throwing the bones of the dead body into the Ganges<BR> or holy waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसारः|अस्थिसार
अस्थि + -सारः The marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्थूणः|अस्थिस्थूण
अस्थि + -स्थूणः ‘having the bones for its pillars’, the body; Ms. 6. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्नेहः|अस्थिस्नेह
अस्थि + -स्नेहः Marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्रंस
अस्थि + -स्रंस <i>a.</i> Ved. causing the bones to fall asunder; Av. 6. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्वत्|अस्थन्वन्त्
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bony, consisting of bones.<BR>—2 Vertebrated; अस्थिमतां सहस्रं तु तथानस्थिमतामनः Y. 3. 269.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमत्|अस्थिमन्त्
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bony, consisting of bones.<BR>—2 Vertebrated; अस्थिमतां सहस्रं तु तथानस्थिमतामनः Y. 3. 269.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमय
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bony, consisting of bones.<BR>—2 Vertebrated; अस्थिमतां सहस्रं तु तथानस्थिमतामनः Y. 3. 269.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित
अस्थित <i>a.</i> Not firm or fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिति|अस्थितिः
अस्थिति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not firm.<BR>—2 Having no settled boundary or limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितिः|अस्थिति
अस्थिति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Want of firmness or fixity (fig. also.).<BR>—2 Want of good manners or decorum. अस्थितिः सङ्गीतमुरजध्वनीनाम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अस्थिर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not stable or firm, unsteady, fickle. मनश्चञ्चलमस्थिरम् Bg. 6. 26.<BR>—2 Uncertain, unascertained, doubtful; जानीयादस्थिरां वाचम् Ms. 8. 71.<BR>—3 Unworthy of confidence; Rām. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अस्थैर्य <i>a.</i> Unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्यम्
अस्थैर्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Instability, unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूरिः|अस्थूरि
अस्थूरिः A cart furnished with more than one horse (एकाश्वयुक्तशकटं<BR> स्थूरि तद्विपरीतम्); अस्थूरि नो गार्हपत्यानि सन्तु Rv. 6. 15. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नात
अस्नात <i>a.</i> Not bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नातृ
अस्नातृ <i>a.</i> Not fond of bathing; not a swimmer; सो अस्नातॄनपारयत्<BR> स्वस्ति Rv. 2. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नावक
अस्नावक, अस्नाविर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without sinews or bands; Vāj. 40. 8; अकायमव्रणमस्नाविरम् Īśop. 8.<BR>—2 Without the gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नाविर
अस्नावक, अस्नाविर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without sinews or bands; Vāj. 40. 8; अकायमव्रणमस्नाविरम् Īśop. 8.<BR>—2 Without the gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्ध
अस्निग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not smooth, hard, dry.<BR>—2 Unkind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्निग्धदारु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्धदारु
अस्निग्ध + -दारु <i>n.</i> a kind of pine tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेह|अस्नेहः
अस्नेह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without oil or unctuousness; आसन्नोषधयो नंतुर्नक्तमस्नेहदीपिका R. 4. 75.<BR>—2 Unkind, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेहः|अस्नेह
अस्नेह + .{@-हः@} Unkindness, want of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेहनः|अस्नेहन
अस्नेहनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पन्द|अस्पंद
अस्पन्द <i>a.</i> Not trembling or moving, motionless. अथ लिखितमिवैतत्सैन्यमस्पन्दमास्ते U. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्श|अस्पर्शः
अस्पर्श <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not touching, not in contact, not having the touch-sense; अशब्दमस्पर्शमरूपम्<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 3. 15.<BR>—2 Intangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शः|अस्पर्श
अस्पर्श + .{@-र्शः@} Absence of contact<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शनम्
अस्पर्शनम् Non-contact, avoiding the contact (of anything); प्रक्षालनाद्धि<BR> पङ्कस्य दूरादस्पर्शनं वरम्; cf. ‘Prevention is better than cure’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृश्य
अस्पृश्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be touched.<BR>—2 Impure, unholy<BR>—3 Not tangible; स्पर्शनेन तदस्पृश्य मनसा त्ववगम्यते Mb. 14. 20. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्ट
अस्पृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untouched.<BR>—2 Not touched or referred to (by a word); अस्पृष्टपुरुषान्तरं शब्दम् Ku. 6. 75;<BR>—3 Not touched by organs of articulation. (as vowels, Anusvārs, sibilants); Rv. Pr.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्पृष्टमैथुना, अस्पृष्टरजस्, अस्पृष्टरजस्तमस्क, अस्पृष्टवह्निः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टमैथुना
अस्पृष्ट + -मैथुना A virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टरजस्
अस्पृष्ट + -रजस्, -रजस्तमस्क <i>a.</i> perfectly pure;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टरजस्तमस्क
अस्पृष्ट + -रजस्, -रजस्तमस्क <i>a.</i> perfectly pure;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टवह्नि
अस्पृष्ट + -वह्नि^1 <i>a.</i> unsheathed by fire.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टिः|अस्पृष्टि
अस्पृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Not touching, avoiding contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अस्पष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not clear, not clearly visible.<BR>—2 Indistinct, not clearly understood, doubtful; अस्पष्टब्रह्मलिङ्गानि<BR> वेदान्तवाक्यानि Ś. B. on 1. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृत
अस्पृत <i>a.</i> Irresistible, invincible. यं ते श्येनः पदाभरत्<BR> तिरो रजांस्यस्पृतम् Rv. 8. 82. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृह
अस्पृह <i>a.</i> Undesirous; स्वकायपरमोऽस्पृहः Ms. 7. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुट|अस्फुटं
अस्फुट <i>a.</i> Indistinct, obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटम्
अस्फुट + .{@-टम्@} An indistinct speech.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्फुटालंकारः, अस्फुटफलम्, अस्फुटवाच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटालंकारः|अस्फुटालङ्कार
अस्फुट + -अलंकारः An indistinct embellishment of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटफलम्
अस्फुट + -फलम् indistinct fruit or result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटवाच्
अस्फुट + -वाच् <i>a.</i> lisping, speaking indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फोतः
अस्फोतः N. of a plant. (Mar. कांचन, कोरळ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद् <i>pron.</i> [अस्-मदिक् Uṇ. 1. 136] A pronominal base from<BR> which several cases of the 1st personal pronoun are derived; it is also<BR> abl. pl. of the word. ━<i>m.</i> The individual soul, the embodied soul; यूयं<BR> वयं वयं यूयमित्यासीन्मतिरावयोः । किं जातमधुना येन यूयं यूयं<BR> वयं वयम् ॥ Bh. 3. 65 (quite estranged from each other).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्मद्द्रुह्, अस्मद्विध, अस्मादृश<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्द्रुह्
अस्मद् + -द्रुह् <i>a.</i> Ved. forming a plot against us or me, inimical; यो<BR> अस्मध्रुग् दुर्मन्मा कश्च वेनति Rv. 8. 60. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्विध
अस्मद् + -विध, अस्मादृश <i>a.</i> similar or like us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मादृश
अस्मद् + -विध, अस्मादृश <i>a.</i> similar or like us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मत्रा
अस्मत्रा <i>ind.</i> To us, with or among us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय <i>a.</i> [अस्मद् छ] Our, ours; यदस्मदीयं न हि तत्परेषाम्<BR> Pt. 2. 105; सहास्मदीयैरपि योधमुख्यैः Bg. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्र्यञ्च्|अस्मद्र्यंच्
अस्मद्र्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> [अस्मानञ्चति P. VI. 3. 92.] Turned towards<BR> us तुभ्यमस्मद्र्यञ्चो ददतो मघानि Rv. 7. 19. 10<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्र्यक्
अस्मद्र्यञ्च् + .{@-क्@} <i>ind.</i> Towards us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मयु
अस्मयु <i>a.</i> Endeavouring to secure us, desiring us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्माक
अस्माक <i>a.</i> Ved. for आस्माक^1 (our, ours).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मन्तम्
अस्मन्तम् = अश्मन्तम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरणम्
अस्मरणम् Forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मार्त|अस्मार्त्त
अस्मार्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not within memory, immemorial.<BR>—2 Illegal, not according to the Āryan institutes of law.<BR>—3 Not belonging to the <i>Smārta</i> sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृत
अस्मृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Forgotten.<BR>—2 Not mentioned in authoritative texts, not traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृतिः|अस्मृति
अस्मृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Want of memory, forgetfulness.<BR>—2 Not forming part of the institutes of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृति|अस्मृतिः
अस्मृतिः + .{@-ति@} <i>ind.</i> Ved. Inattentively; यदस्मृति चकृम किं चिदग्न<BR> उपारिम चरणे जातवेदः Av. 7. 106. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मि
अस्मि <i>ind.</i> (Strictly 1st pers. sing. pres. of अस् to be) Used<BR> in the sense of ‘I’, अहम्; आसंसृतेरस्मि जगत्सु जातः Ki. 3. 6; दासे<BR> कृतागसि भवत्युचितः प्रभूणां पादप्रहार इति सुन्दरि नास्मि दूये ॥<BR> quoted by Malli; त्वामस्मि वच्मि विदुषां समवायोऽत्र तिष्टति S. D.;<BR> अन्यत्र यूयं कुसुमावचायं कुरुध्वमत्रास्मि करोमि सख्यः K. P. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्मिमानः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मिमानः|अस्मिमान
अस्मि + -मानः Self-conceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मिता
अस्मिता Egotism; दृग्दर्शनशक्त्योरेकात्मतेवास्मिता Pātañjala S. 1. 17.<BR> ‘अविद्यास्मितारागद्वेषाभिनिवेशाः पञ्च क्लेशाः । तत्रानित्येषु नित्यत्वाभिमानः ।’<BR> इति टीका Śi. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मेर
अस्मेर <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not sullen, confiding.<BR>—2 Not bashful or confused. तमस्मेरा युवतयो युवानम् Rv. 2. 35. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यवामीयम्
अस्यवामीयम् [अस्यवामिति शब्दोऽस्त्यत्र सूक्ते मत्वर्थे छ P. V. 2. 59<BR> Vārt. 1] The hymn beginning with the words अस्य वाम् (Rv. 1. 164).<BR> cf. also सकृज्वप्त्वास्यवामीयं शिवसंकल्पमेव च Ms. 11. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्युद्यत
अस्युद्यत <i>a.</i> = उद्यतासि with the sword raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रः|अस्र|अस्रं
अस्रः [अस्-रन्]<BR>—1 A corner, an angle.<BR>—2 Hair of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रम्
अस्रः + .{@-स्रम्@}<BR>—1 Tear; अस्रोत्तरमीक्षितामिमाम् Ku. 5. 61. क्षणं सुधांशुः स्रवदस्रसिक्तः<BR> Rām. Ch. 6. 73.<BR>—2 Blood; अस्रस्तु कुन्तले कोणे रक्ते नेत्राम्बुनि स्मृतः Nm. तेषामद्य<BR> करिष्यामि तवास्रेणोदकक्रियाम् Mb. 3. 157. 49.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्रार्जक, अस्राह्वम्, अस्रकण्ठः, अस्रखदिरः, अस्रजम्, अस्रजित्, अस्रपः, अस्रपा, अस्रपत्रकः, अस्रपित्तम्, अस्रफला, अस्रफली, अस्रमातृका, अस्ररोधिनी, अस्रबिन्दुच्छदा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रार्जक|अस्रार्जकः|अस्रार्ज्जक|अस्रार्ज्जकः
अस्रः + -अर्जक <i>a.</i> producing blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रार्जकः|अस्रार्जक|अस्रार्ज्जक|अस्रार्ज्जकः
अस्रः + -अर्जक + .({@-कः@})<BR>—1 the white Tulsī plant.<BR>—2 the humour producing blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्राह्वम्
अस्रः + -आह्वम् Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रकण्ठः|अस्रकण्ठ|अस्रकंठ
अस्रः + -कण्ठः [अस्रः कोणः इव कण्ठोऽस्य] an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रखदिरः|अस्रखदिर
अस्रः + -खदिरः the red Mimosa (Mar. तांबडा खैर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रजम्
अस्रः + -जम् flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रजित्
अस्रः + -जित्^1 = अस्त्रजित् q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपः|अस्रप
अस्रः + -पः<BR>—1 ‘a blood-drinker’, a Rākṣasa or goblin: वध्यन्तेऽस्रपपुङ्गवाः Mv. 6. 24.<BR>—2 the Nakṣatra मूला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपा
अस्रः + -पा<BR>—1 a leech.<BR>—2 a Dākinī or female imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपत्रकः|अस्रपत्रक
अस्रः + -पत्रकः N. of a plant (भिंडावृक्ष)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपित्तम्
अस्रः + -पित्तम् hemorrhage, involuntary discharge of blood from the mouth, nostrils &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रफला
अस्रः + -फला, -फली N. of a plant (सल्लकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रफली
अस्रः + -फला, -फली N. of a plant (सल्लकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रमातृका
अस्रः + -मातृका chyle, chyme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ररोधिनी
अस्रः + -रोधिनी the plant लज्जालु Mimosa Pudica (Mar. लाजाळू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रबिन्दुच्छदा
अस्रः + -बिन्दुच्छदा N. of a tuberous plant (लक्षणावृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रायते
अस्रायते Den. Ā. To shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रिः|अस्रि
अस्रिः<BR>—1 An angle; अष्टास्रयः सर्व एव श्लक्ष्णरूपसमन्विताः Rām. 1. 14. 26.<BR>—2 Ten millions; see अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रिध्
अस्रिध्, -अस्रेधत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Devout, faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रेधत्|अस्रेधन्त्
अस्रिध्, -अस्रेधत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Devout, faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रु
अस्रु = अश्रु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रेमन्
अस्रेमन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praiseworthy.<BR>—2 Undecaying, immortal.<BR>—3 Faultless, perfect; अस्रेमा वत्सः शिमिवाँ अरावीत् Rv. 10. 8. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्व|अस्वः
अस्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Indigent, poor (नास्ति स्वं धनं यस्य) स्मृत्यनुरोधादस्वा स्यात्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 20.<BR>—2 Not oneʼs own.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्वग, अस्वजाति}^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वग
अस्व + -ग <i>a.</i> Ved. not going<BR> to oneʼs home, homeless; अवास्तुमेनमस्वगमप्रजसं करोति Av. 12. 5. 45.<BR> ˚ता Ved. homelessness; अस्वगता परिह्रुता Av. 12. 5. 40<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वजाति
अस्व + -जाति^1 <i>a.</i> of a different caste or kind; स्वा चैव कुर्यात्सर्वेषां<BR> नास्वजातिः कथंचन Ms. 9. 86.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वक
अस्वक, -अस्वकीय^1 <i>a.</i><BR> Not oneʼs own. belonging to another.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वकीय
अस्वक, -अस्वकीय^1 <i>a.</i><BR> Not oneʼs own. belonging to another.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वत्वम्
अस्वत्वम्, -ता<BR> Absence of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वता
अस्वत्वम्, -ता<BR> Absence of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छन्द|अस्वच्छंद|अस्वच्छन्दः
अस्वच्छन्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not self-willed, dependent.<BR>—2 Docile, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वतन्त्र|अस्वतंत्र|अस्वतन्त्रः
अस्वतन्त्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dependent, subject, not oneʼs own master; अस्वतन्त्रा स्त्री पुरुषप्रधाना; Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—2 Docile, humble, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्त|अस्वंत|अस्वन्तः
अस्वन्त <i>a.</i> Ending, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्तः|अस्वन्त|अस्वंत
अस्वन्त + .{@-न्तः@} Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्तम्
अस्वन्त + .{@-तम्@} Fire-place (अश्मन्त q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्न|अस्वप्नः
अस्वप्न <i>a.</i> Sleepless, wakeful; सदास्वप्नस्य मानवः Mb. 13. 93. 6;<BR> अजमनिद्रमस्वप्नम् Gauḍapāda Kār. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्नः|अस्वप्न
अस्वप्न + .{@-प्नः@}<BR>—1 A god, deity.<BR>—2 Sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्नज्
अस्वप्नज् <i>a.</i> Sleepless; अस्वप्नजो अनिमिषा अदब्धाः Rv. 2. 27. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभाव|अस्वभावः
अस्वभाव <i>a.</i> Of a different nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभावः|अस्वभाव
अस्वभाव + .{@-वः@} Different or unnatural character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अस्वर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a bad voice.<BR>—2 Indistinct, not loud, in a low tone (as a speech); Rām. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरः|अस्वर
अस्वर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A low tone.<BR>—2 A consonant.<BR>—3 Absence of any accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरम्
अस्वर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Not aloud, in a low tone.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्वरादि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरादि
अस्वर + -आदि <i>a.</i> Not beginning with a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरूप
अस्वरूप <i>a.</i> Essentially different, unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अस्वर्ग्य <i>a.</i> Not securing or leading to heaven; अस्वर्ग्यं लोकविद्विष्टं<BR> धर्ममप्याचरेन्न तु Y. 1. 156; अनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यम् Bg. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ववेश
अस्ववेश <i>a.</i> Expelled from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाधीन
अस्वाधीन <i>a.</i> See अस्वतन्त्र. अस्वाधीनं नराधिपम् वर्जयन्ति<BR> नरा दूरात् Rām. 3. 33. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाध्यायः|अस्वाध्याय
अस्वाध्यायः [न स्वाध्यायो वेदाध्ययनमस्य]<BR>—1 One who has not yet commenced his studies, not being invested with<BR> the sacred thread.<BR>—2 Interruption of studies (as on अष्टमी, eclipses &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अस्वस्थ <i>a.</i> —1 Not well, unwell, indisposed, sick; अस्वस्थः सर्वमेतत्तु<BR> भृत्येषु विनियोजयेत् Ms. 7. 226. बलवद् अस्वस्थ Ś. 3 seriously<BR> indisposed; ˚शरीरा <i>ibid.</i>, K. 159, 211; ˚ता want of firmness,<BR> weakness, illness. {sic}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वास्थ्यम्
अस्वास्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Indisposition, sickness.<BR>—2 Absence of ease or comfort, trouble, anxiety; य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं<BR> दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिक|अस्वामिकं
अस्वामिक <i>a.</i> Unowned, unclaimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिकम्
अस्वामिक + .{@-कम्@} (Unclaimed) Treasure &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अस्वामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no right to anything, not being master of it.<BR>—2 Unowned, unclaimed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अस्वामिविक्रयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिविक्रयः|अस्वामिविक्रय
अस्वामिन् + -विक्रयः a sale without ownership; Kau. A. 3; Ms. 8. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">Page0300-1</a>]<BR> निक्षिप्तं वा परद्रव्यं नष्टं लब्ध्वाऽपहृत्य वा । विक्रीयतेऽसमक्षं<BR> यत् स ज्ञेयोऽस्वामिविक्रयः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0299-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्य|अस्वाम्यं
अस्वाम्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unowned.<BR>—2 Not oneʼs own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्यम्
अस्वाम्य + .{@-म्यम्@} Absence of right to property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्विन्न
अस्विन्न <i>a.</i> Not thoroughly boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वेद्य
अस्वेद्य <i>a.</i> Where the application of sudorifics is prohibited; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् I. €1 Ā. or €10 U. = अंह् q. v. ━II. €1 P. to sing together,<BR> compose, celebrate. prepare. ━III. €5 P. (अह्नोति, आहीत्, आह) To pervade.<BR>━IV. (a defective verb preserved only in five forms; आत्थ, आहथुः, आह,<BR> आहतुः, आहुः)<BR>—1 To say, speak, mention.<BR>—2 To acknowledge, accept, state.<BR>—3 To declare, express, signify.<BR>—4 To hold, consider, regard; स्थाणुच्छेदस्य केदारमाहुः शल्यवतो मृगम् Ms. 9. 44.<BR>—5 To call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह <i>ind.</i> A particle implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) praise (पूजा);<BR>——(<i>b</i>) separation;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) resolution, ascertainment, certainty; and translated by ‘surely’,<BR> ‘certainly’, ‘yes’, ‘well’;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) rejecting;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) sending;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) deviation from custom, impropriety त्वमह ग्रामं गच्छ, त्वमह<BR> रथेनारण्यं गच्छ Sk. स्वयमह रथेन याति, उपाध्यायं पदातिं गमयति Sk.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) hence, therefore (अथ); शर्वरीं भगवन्नद्य सत्यशील<BR> तवाश्रमे । उषिताः स्मोऽह वसतिमनुजानातु नो भवान् ॥ Rām. 2. 54. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not hurt or struck, uninjured; अजीतोऽहतो अक्षतोऽध्यष्ठां पृथिवीमहम् Av. 12. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Unbeaten (as cloth in washing). अहतं वासः परिधत्ते Ts.<BR>—3 Unwashed, new बभूवुस्ते भृशं प्रीताः सर्वे चाहतवाससः Rām. 2. 91. 64.<BR>—4 Unblemished, unsoiled.<BR>—5 Not frustrated or disappointed (as hopes &c.)<BR>—6 Not beaten (as a drum) अहतायां प्रयाणभेर्याम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहतम्
अहत + .{@-तम्@} An unwashed or new cloth; cf. अप्रहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहतिः|अहति
अहतिः, अहन्तिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Safety, security from danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्तिः|अहन्ति|अहंतिः
अहतिः, अहन्तिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Safety, security from danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्त्य|अहंत्य
अहन्त्य, अहन्त्र, अहन्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Indestructible. invincible; सूतायाहन्त्यै<BR> वनानां पतये नमः Vāj. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्त्र
अहन्त्य, अहन्त्र, अहन्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Indestructible. invincible; सूतायाहन्त्यै<BR> वनानां पतये नमः Vāj. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्य
अहन्त्य, अहन्त्र, अहन्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Indestructible. invincible; सूतायाहन्त्यै<BR> वनानां पतये नमः Vāj. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् <i>n.</i> [न जहाति न त्यजति सर्वथा परिवर्तनं, न हा-कनिन्<BR> Uṇ. 1. 55.] (Nom. अहः, अह्नी-अहनी, अहानि, अह्ना, अहोभ्याम् &c.; अहरिति<BR> हन्ति पाप्मानं जहाति च Śat. Br.)<BR>—1 A day (including day and night); अहः शब्दोऽपि अहोरात्रवचनः ।<BR> रात्रिशब्दोऽपि । ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 16. अघाहानि Ms. 5. 84.<BR>—2 Day time सव्यापारामहनि न तथा पीडयेन्मद्वियोगः Me. 90; यदह्ना<BR> कुरुते पापम् by day; अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः शुक्लः Bg. 8. 54.<BR>—3 The sky (as traversed by the sun); समारूढे च मध्यमह्नः सवितरि K. 99; M. 2.<BR>—4 A sacrificial or festival day.<BR>—5 A dayʼs work.<BR>—6 Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 Night.<BR>—8 A portion of a book appointed for a day. —9 A day personified as one<BR> of the eight Vasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहनी
अहन् + .{@-नी@} (du.) Day and night (At the end of comp. अहन् is changed<BR> to अहः, -हं^1 or to अह्न; see P. V. 4. 88-91, VI. 3. 110, VIII. 4. 7.<BR> <i>Note</i>: At the beginning of comp. it assumes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">Page0300-2</a>]<BR> the forms अहस् or अहर्; <i>e. g.</i> सप्ताहः, एकाहः, पूर्वाह्णः,<BR> अपराह्णः पुण्याहं, सुदिनाहं, अहःपतिः or अहर्पतिः &c. &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहरहः, अहरागमः, अहरादिः, अहःकरः, अहर्गणः, अहर्जरः, अहर्जात, अहर्दिव, अहर्दिवि, अहर्दृश्, अहर्नाथः, अहर्निशम्, अहःपतिः, अहर्बान्धवः, अहर्भाज्, अहर्लोक, अहर्मणिः, अहर्मुखम्, अहारथन्तरम्, अहोरात्रः, अहर्विद्, अहःशेषः, अहःशेषम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes, user @Andhrabharati on 20251212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102#issuecomment-3647228881.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरहः|अहरह
अहन् + -अहः (अहरहः) <i>ind.</i> Day by day, daily. अहरहःस्नात्वा<BR> सन्ध्यामुपासीत; अहरहर्नयमानो गामश्वं पुरुषं पशुम् Mbh. on 2. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरागमः|अहरागम
अहन् + -आगमः (अहरा˚) the approach of day<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरादिः|अहरादि
अहन् + -आदिः dawn; शशधरमहरादौ रागवानुष्णरश्मिः Śi. 11. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःकरः|अहःकर
अहन् + -करः (˚हः or ˚स्करः)<BR>—1 the sun; अलंचकारास्य वधूरहस्करः Śi. 1. 58; (P. III. 2. 21.)<BR>—2 a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्गणः|अहर्गण
अहन् + -गणः, (˚हर्ग˚)<BR>—1 a series of sacrificial days.<BR>—2 a month.<BR>—3 any calculated term (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्जरः|अहर्जर|अहर्ज्जरः
अहन् + -जरः [अहोभिः परिवर्तमानो लोकान् जरयति जॄ-णिच् अच्, अहानि<BR> वा अस्मिन् जीर्यन्ति आधारे अप्-वा Tv.] Ved. the year as making days old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्जात
अहन् + -जात <i>a.</i> Ved. born in the day or from day, not belonging to night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्दिव
अहन् + -दिव <i>a.</i> (˚हर्दि˚) existing every day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्दिवम्
अहन् + -दिव + .({@-वम्@}) <i>ind.</i> [अहश्च दिवा च समा˚ द्व˚] daily, every day,<BR> day by day; य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्दिवि
अहन् + -दिवि <i>ind.</i> day by day, every day, constantly; यथा श्येनात्<BR> पतत्रिणः संविजन्ते अहर्दिवि सिंहस्य स्तनयोर्यथा Av. 5. 21. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्दृश्
अहन् + -दृश् <i>a.</i> Ved. belonging to the day; living; इन्द्रो विश्वान्<BR> बेकनाटाँ अहर्दृशः Rv. 8. 66. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्नाथः|अहर्नाथ
अहन् + -नाथः<BR>—1 the sun, the lord of the day.<BR>—2 a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्निशम्
अहन् + -निशम् [अहश्च निशा च समा˚ द्व˚] a day and night, a whole<BR> day; तस्य सोहर्निशस्यान्ते प्रसुप्तः प्रतिबुद्धयते Ms. 1. 74, 4. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्निशम्
अहन् + -निशम् + .({@-शम्@}) <i>ind.</i> day and night, during the whole day, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःपतिः|अहःपति
अहन् + -पतिः [अहःपतिः, अहर्पतिः, अहस्पतिः P. VIII. 2. 70. Mbh. Vārt.]<BR>—1 the sun; ननु राह्वाह्नमहर्पतिं तमः Śi. 16. 57; R. 10. 54.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 a kind of tree.<BR>—4 swallowwort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्बान्धवः|अहर्बान्धव|अहर्ब्बान्धवः
अहन् + -बान्धवः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्भाज्
अहन् + -भाज्, -लोक <i>a.</i> Ved. partaking of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्लोक
अहन् + -भाज्, -लोक <i>a.</i> Ved. partaking of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मणिः|अहर्मणि|अहर्म्मणिः
अहन् + -मणिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मुखम्
अहन् + -मुखम् commencement of the day, morning, dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहारथन्तरम्
अहन् + -रथन्तरम् (P. VIII. 2. 68. Vārt.) a portion of Sāma to be chanted at day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्रः|अहोरात्र
अहन् + -रात्रः + .({@-त्रम्@} also)<BR>—1 a day and night (P. II. 4. 29.); त्रीनहोरात्रान् Nala. 12. 44; त्रिंशत्कला<BR> मुहूर्तः स्यादहोरात्रं तु तावतः Ms. 1. 64, 65; Y. 1. 147.<BR>—2 a day of the Pitṛs, a month of the gods and a year of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्रम्
अहन् + -रात्रः + .({@-त्रम्@} also)<BR>—1 a day and night (P. II. 4. 29.); त्रीनहोरात्रान् Nala. 12. 44; त्रिंशत्कला<BR> मुहूर्तः स्यादहोरात्रं तु तावतः Ms. 1. 64, 65; Y. 1. 147.<BR>—2 a day of the Pitṛs, a month of the gods and a year of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्विद्
अहन् + -विद् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 existing many days.<BR>—2 known long ago.<BR>—3 one who knows the fit time or season of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःशेषः|अहःशेष
अहन् + -शेषः, -शेषम् (˚हः शेषम्)<BR>—1 evening.<BR>—2 the last day of defilement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःशेषम्
अहन् + -शेषः, -शेषम् (˚हः शेषम्)<BR>—1 evening.<BR>—2 the last day of defilement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहना
अहना Dawn, morning (उषा Sāy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्
अहम् <i>pron.</i> (Nom. sing. of अस्मद्). I [cf. Zend. <i>azem</i>;<BR> L. <i>ego</i>; Germ. <i>ich</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहमग्रिका, अहमहमिका, अहङ्कर्तव्य, अहङ्कारः, अहङ्कारिन्, अहङ्कार्यम्, अहङ्कृत, अहङ्कृतिः, अहञ्जुस्, अहम्पूर्व, अहम्पूर्विका, अहम्प्रथमिका, अहम्प्रत्ययः, अहम्भद्रम्, अहम्भावः, अहम्मतिः, अहंवादिन्, अहंश्रेयस्, अहंसन, अहंस्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमग्रिका
अहम् + -अग्रिका a contest for superiority, rivalry<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमहमिका
अहम् + -अहमिका [अहमहं शब्दोऽस्त्यत्र वीप्सायां द्वित्वं ठन् न टिलोपः P. II. 1. 72]<BR>—1 emulation, competition, assertion of superiority; अहमहमिका तु<BR> सा स्यात्परस्परं यो भवत्यहंकारः Ak.; अहमहमिकया प्रणामलालसानाम्<BR> K. 14, 81; अहमहमिकया मधुकरकुलैरनुबध्यमानम् 139; Mv. 6. 54.<BR>—2 egotism.<BR>—3 military vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कर्तव्य|अहंकर्तव्य
अहम् + -कर्तव्य <i>a.</i> to be referred to self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कर्तव्यम्
अहम् + -कर्तव्य + .({@-व्यम्@}) the object of अहंकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारः|अहङ्कार|अहंकार
अहम् + -कारः<BR>—1 egotism, sense of self, self-love considered as an अविद्या or spiritual<BR> ignorance in Vedānta Phil.; निर्ममो निरहंकारः … स शान्तिमधिगच्छति<BR> Bg. 2. 71, 7. 4; Ms. 1. 14; Y. 3. 177.<BR>—2 pride, self-consciousness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">Page0301-1</a>]<BR> self-conceit, haughtiness.<BR>—3 (in Sāṅ. Phil.) the third of the eight producers or elements of creation,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> the conceit or conception of individuality, one of the 25 elements;<BR> Sāṅ. K. 22, 24, 25; ˚वत् <i>a.</i> selfish, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0300-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारिन्|अहंकारिन्
अहम् + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> proud, self-conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कार्यम्
अहम् + -कार्यम् that which is to be done by oneself, personal business or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृत|अहंकृत
अहम् + -कृत^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 egotistic; यस्य नाहंकृतो भावः Bg. 18. 17.<BR>—2 proud, haughty, जातिरूपवयोवृत्तिविद्यादिभिरहंकृतः Y. 3. 151.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृतिः|अहङ्कृति|अहंकृति
अहम् + -कृतिः <i>f.</i> egotism, high opinion of oneself, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहञ्जुस्
अहम् + -जुस् <i>m.</i> Thinking only of oneself; Ku. 15. 53. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्व|अहंपूर्व
अहम् + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> desirous of being first; अहंपूर्वाः पचन्ति स्म<BR> प्रसन्नाः पानभोजनम् Rām. 2. 12. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्विका|अहंपूर्विका|अहम्पूर्व्विका
अहम् + -पूर्विका, -प्रथमिका [अहं पूर्वोऽहं पूर्व इत्यभिधानं यत्र]<BR>—1 the running forward of soldiers with emulation; (hence) emulation,<BR> competition; जवादहंपूर्विकया यियासुभिः Ki. 14. 32.<BR>—2 bragging, vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्प्रथमिका|अहंप्रथमिका
अहम् + -पूर्विका, -प्रथमिका [अहं पूर्वोऽहं पूर्व इत्यभिधानं यत्र]<BR>—1 the running forward of soldiers with emulation; (hence) emulation,<BR> competition; जवादहंपूर्विकया यियासुभिः Ki. 14. 32.<BR>—2 bragging, vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्प्रत्ययः|अहम्प्रत्यय
अहम् + -प्रत्ययः [अहमित्याकारकः प्रत्ययः] self-conceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्भद्रम्
अहम् + -भद्रम् [अहमेव भद्र इति निर्णयो यत्र] self-conceit, high<BR> opinion of oneʼs own superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्भावः|अहम्भाव|अहंभाव
अहम् + -भावः<BR>—1 pride, egotism; अहंभावावृतो निस्त्रपः Bv. 4. 10.<BR>—2 = ˚मति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्मतिः|अहम्मति|अहंमति
अहम् + -मतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 self-love or self-illusion regarded as spiritual ignorance (in Vedānta Phil.).<BR>—2 conceit, pride, egotism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंवादिन्
अहम् + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking only of oneself, proud, haughty; मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी …<BR> कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते Bg. 18. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंश्रेयस्
अहम् + -श्रेयस् or ˚सम् <i>n.</i> claiming superiority for oneself; अहंश्रेयसे<BR> विवदमानाः Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंसन
अहम् + -सन <i>a.</i> Ved. gaining for oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंस्तम्भः
अहम् + -स्तम्भः Conceit; दरिद्रो निरहंस्तम्भो मुक्तः सर्वमदैरिह ।<BR> कृच्छ्रं यदृच्छयाप्नोति तद्धि तस्य परं तपः ॥ Bhāg. 10. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु <i>a.</i> [अहम् अहंकारोऽस्त्यस्य, अहं युस् P. V. 2. 140]<BR> Selfish, proud, haughty; अहंयुनाथ क्षितिपः शुभंयुः Bk. 1. 20. अहंयुना<BR> घनारण्यवर्तिना जिह्मवृत्तिना Śiva B. 31. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयुः|अहंयु
अहंयु + .{@-युः@} A warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर|अहरः
अहर <i>a.</i> Not taking away; so अहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरः|अहर
अहर + .{@-रः@} A pure quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरणीय
अहरणीय, -अहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be stolen, removed, or taken away; अहार्यं ब्राह्मणद्रव्यं<BR> राज्ञां नित्यमिति स्थितिः Ms. 9. 189.<BR>—2 Not to be won over (by fraud), devoted, loyal; Ms. 7. 217.<BR>—3 Firm, unflinching, inexorable; ˚निश्चया Dk. 41. विमुच्य साऽऽहारमहार्यनिश्चया<BR> Ku. 5. 8. ˚विक्रम <i>a.</i> Bhāg. 3. 18. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्य|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहरणीय, -अहार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not to be stolen, removed, or taken away; अहार्यं ब्राह्मणद्रव्यं<BR> राज्ञां नित्यमिति स्थितिः Ms. 9. 189.<BR>—2 Not to be won over (by fraud), devoted, loyal; Ms. 7. 217.<BR>—3 Firm, unflinching, inexorable; ˚निश्चया Dk. 41. विमुच्य साऽऽहारमहार्यनिश्चया<BR> Ku. 5. 8. ˚विक्रम <i>a.</i> Bhāg. 3. 18. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्यः|अहार्य|अहार्य्य|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहरणीय, -अहार्य + .{@-र्यः@} A mountain; {@˚ता, -त्वम्@} not being liable to be taken<BR> away, security; सर्वद्रव्येषु विद्यैव द्रव्यमाहुरनुत्तमम् । अहार्यत्वात् … H. Pr. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल
अहल, -लि <i>a.</i> Unploughed, unfurrowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहलि
अहल, -लि <i>a.</i> Unploughed, unfurrowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्य|अहल्यः
अहल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unploughed.<BR>—2 Not arable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्यः|अहल्य
अहल्य + .{@-ल्यः@} N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्या
अहल्य + .{@-ल्या@} N. of the wife of Gautama [According to the Rāmāyana she<BR> was the first woman created by Brahmā, who gave her to Gautama. She was<BR> seduced by Indra who assumed the form of her husband and so deceived her,<BR> or, according to another version, she knew the god and was flattered by<BR> the great Godʼs condescension. There<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">Page0301-2</a>]<BR> is another story which states that Indra secured the assistance of the<BR> moon who, assuming the form of a cock, crowed at midnight. This roused<BR> Gautama to his morning devotions, and Indra went in and took his place.<BR> Gautama, when he knew of her seduction expelled her from his hermitage<BR> and cursed her to be a stone and become invisible till she should be touched<BR> by the feet of Dāśarathi Rāma which would restore her to her former<BR> shape. Rāma afterwards delivered her from her wretched state and she<BR> was reconciled to her husband. Ahalyā is one of the five very chaste and<BR> pure women whose names every one is recommended to repeat in the morning;<BR> अहल्या द्रौपदी सीता तारा मन्दोदरी तथा । पञ्चकं ना स्मरेन्नित्यं महापातकनाशनम् ॥<BR> Kumārila Bhaṭṭa explains the seduction of Ahalyā as Indraʼs (the<BR> sunʼs) carrying away the shades of night, Ahalyā signifying night.] For<BR> a very succinct account, see also Mv. 1.<BR>—2 N. of a sea.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहल्येश्वरतीर्थः, अहल्यजारः, अहल्यनन्दनः, अहल्यह्रदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्येश्वरतीर्थः|अहल्येश्वरतीर्थ
अहल्य + -ईश्वरतीर्थः N. of a तीर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्यजारः
अहल्य + -जारः Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्यनन्दनः
अहल्य + -नन्दनः the sage Śatānanda, son of Ahalyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्यह्रदः
अहल्य + -ह्रदः N. of a Tīrtha near the hermitage of Gautama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्लिकः|अहल्लिक
अहल्लिकः [अहनि लीयते, ली-ड, निपातः संज्ञायां कम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A (dead) body; अहल्लिकेति होवाच Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 25.<BR>—2 Ved. A talker; Śat. Br. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहवि
अहवि^1 <i>a.</i> Without oblations or sacrifices; जनो यः कश्चिदहविर्महीयते Rv. 1. 182. 3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/41b120c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्त
अहस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Handless.<BR>—2 One whose hand is cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहह
अहह, -हा [अहं जहाति, हा-क-पृषो˚] A particle or interjection implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) sorrow or regret (‘alas’, ‘ah’); अहह कष्टमपण्डितता विधेः<BR> Bh. 2. 92, 3. 21; अहह ज्ञानराशिर्विनष्टः Mu. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Wonder or surprise; अहह महतां निस्सीमानश्चरित्रविभूतयः<BR> Bh. 2. 35, 36. cf. अहहेत्यद्भुते खेदे … Nm.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Pity; ध्रुवं ते जीवन्तोप्यहह मृतकामन्दमतयः Bv. 4. 39.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Calling; अहहारे त्वा शूद्र Ch. Up.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहहा
अहह, -हा [अहं जहाति, हा-क-पृषो˚] A particle or interjection implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) sorrow or regret (‘alas’, ‘ah’); अहह कष्टमपण्डितता विधेः<BR> Bh. 2. 92, 3. 21; अहह ज्ञानराशिर्विनष्टः Mu. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Wonder or surprise; अहह महतां निस्सीमानश्चरित्रविभूतयः<BR> Bh. 2. 35, 36. cf. अहहेत्यद्भुते खेदे … Nm.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Pity; ध्रुवं ते जीवन्तोप्यहह मृतकामन्दमतयः Bv. 4. 39.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Calling; अहहारे त्वा शूद्र Ch. Up.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि <i>a.</i> Killing; pervaded, pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिः|अहि
अहि + .{@-हिः@} [आहन्ति, आ-हन्-इण् स च डित् आडो ह्रस्वश्च Uṇ. 4. 137]<BR>—1 A serpent, snake; अहयः सविषाः सर्वे निर्विषा डुण्डुमाः स्मृताः Ks. 14. 84.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 The planet Rāhu.<BR>—4 A traveller<BR>—5 The demon Vṛtra; रोमहर्षणमत्युग्रं शकस्य त्वहिना यथा (युद्धमासीत्)<BR> Mb. 11. 23. 12.<BR>—6 A wicked man.<BR>—7 A cheat, rogue.<BR>—8 The Āśleṣā Nakṣatra.<BR>—9 Water.<BR>—10 Earth.<BR>—11 A milch cow.<BR>—12 Lead.<BR>—13 The navel.<BR>—14 A cloud. अहिर्वृत्रासुरे सर्पे … च दुर्जने । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अही
अहि + .{@-ही@} (du.) Heaven and earth. [cf., L. <i>anguis</i>, Gr. <i>ehis</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अह्यर्षु, अहिकान्तः, अहिकोषः, अहिक्षत्रः, अहिक्षेत्रः, अहिगोप, अहिघ्नम्, अहिघ्नी, अहिचक्रम्, अहिच्छत्रः, अहिच्छत्रकम्, अहिच्छत्रकः, अहिजित्, अहिजिह्वा, अहितुण्डिकः, अहिदेवम्, अहिद्विष्, अहिद्रुह्, अहिमार, अहिरिपु, अहिविद्विष्, अहिनकुलम्, अहिनकुलिका, अहिनामभृत्, अहिनिर्मोकः, अहिनिर्व्लयनी, अहिपताकः, अहिपतिः, अहिपुत्रकः, अहिपुष्पः, अहिपूतनम्, अहिपूतना, अहिफेनः, अहिफेनम्, अहिबुध्नः, अहिवुध्नः, अहिब्रध्नः, अहिर्बुध्नः, अहिर्बुध्न्यः, अहिद्विष्, अहिबीजम्, अहिभयम्, अहिभानु, अहिभुज्, अहिमन्यु, अहिमर्दनी, अहिमाय, अहिमारकः, अहिमेदकः, अहिलता, अहिविषापहा, अहिशुष्म, अहिसक्थ, अहिहत्यम्, अहिहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्यर्षु
अहि + -अर्षु <i>a.</i> gliding away like a snake, not facing the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकान्तः|अहिकान्त|अहिकांत
अहि + -कान्तः air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकोषः|अहिकोष
अहि + -कोषः the slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिक्षत्रः|अहिक्षत्र
अहि + -क्षत्रः, -क्षेत्रः N. of a country in the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिक्षेत्रः|अहिक्षेत्र
अहि + -क्षत्रः, -क्षेत्रः N. of a country in the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिगोप
अहि + -गोप <i>a.</i> Ved. guarded by a serpent; दासपत्नीरहिगोपा अतिष्थन् Rv. 1. 32. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिघ्नम्
अहि + -घ्नम् the slaying of the serpent or demon Vṛtra. अनु त्वाहिघ्ने<BR> अध देव देवा Rv. 6. 18. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिघ्नी
अहि + -घ्नी <i>m.</i> killing snakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिचक्रम्
अहि + -चक्रम् A certain Tantric diagram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्रः|अहिच्छत्र
अहि + -च्छत्रः<BR>—1 N. of a country, conquered by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">Page0302-1</a>]<BR> Arjuna and given to Droṇa.<BR>—2 a kind of vegetable poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्रः|अहिच्छत्र
अहि + -च्छत्रः + .({@-त्रः@})<BR>—1 sugar.<BR>—2 the plant मेषशृङ्गी.<BR>—3 (Mar. बडीशेप)<BR>—4 N. of the city अहिच्छत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0301-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

