अहिमेदकः|अहिमेदक
अहि + -मारकः, -मेदकः<BR>—1 N. of a plant (अरिमेद; Mar. गन्धीहिवर)<BR>—2 = ˚द्विष् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिलता
अहि + -लता<BR>—1 the betel-nut plant.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (गन्धनाकुली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिविषापहा
अहि + -विषापहा <i>f.</i> ‘Neutralizing the poison of snakes’, The ichneumon<BR> plant (Mar. मुंगुसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिशुष्म
अहि + -शुष्म <i>a.</i> having all-pervading strength; ˚सत्वन् Ved.<BR> one whose men hiss like serpents (N. of Indra); आस्माञ्जगम्यादहिशुष्म<BR> सत्वा Rv. 5. 33. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिसक्थ|अहिसक्थः
अहि + -सक्थ <i>a.</i> having a long thigh like a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिसक्थः|अहिसक्थ
अहि + -सक्थ + .({@-क्थः@}) N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिहत्यम्
अहि + -हत्यम् Ved. the slaying of the serpent or demon Vṛtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिहन्
अहि + -हन् <i>a.</i> Killing serpents or Vṛtra, Garuḍa, Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकः|अहिक
अहिकः<BR>—1 The polar star ध्रुव.<BR>—2 A blind snake.<BR>—3 (At the end of comp.) Lasting for a certain number of days; दशाहिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिका
अहिकः + .{@-का@} The silk cotton tree (शाल्मली; Mar. सावरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अहिंसक <i>a.</i> Not hurting or injuring, harmless; योऽहिंसकानि<BR> भूतानि हिनस्त्यात्मसुखेच्छया Ms. 5. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अहिंसा<BR>—1 Harmlessness, abstaining from killing or giving pain to others in thought,<BR> word or deed; as अहिंसा परमो धर्मः, अहिंसा समता तुष्टिः Bg. 10. 5;<BR> यत्तपो दानमार्जवमहिंसा Ch. Up. 3. 17. 4; Ms. 10. 63. या वेदविहिता<BR> हिंसा नियताऽस्मिंश्चराचरे । अहिंसामेव तां विद्याद्वेदाद्धर्मो हि निर्बभौ ॥<BR> Ms. 5. 44, 6. 75. One of the cardinal virtues of most Hindu sects,<BR> The Jainas deserve special credit for making it social virtue of good<BR> conduct among the Hindus.<BR>—2 Security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसान
अहिंसान <i>a.</i> Ved. Not hurting, harmless; अस्यं प्रियस्य शर्मण्यहिंसानस्य<BR> सश्चिरे Rv. 5. 64. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अहिंस्र <i>a.</i> Harmless, innocent; Ms. 4. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्रः|अहिंस्र
अहिंस्र + .{@-स्रः, -स्रा@} N. of a plant (कुलिक Mar. फड्या निवडुंग<BR> or कर्कटी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्रा
अहिंस्र + .{@-स्रः, -स्रा@} N. of a plant (कुलिक Mar. फड्या निवडुंग<BR> or कर्कटी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्रम्
अहिंस्र + .{@-स्रम्@} Harmless behaviour, innocence; Ms. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिण्डुका|अहिंडुका
अहिण्डुका A kind of small poisonous animal. Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहित|अहितः
अहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not placed, put, or fixed.<BR>—2 Unfit, improper; चतुर्णामपि वर्णानां प्रेत्य चेह हिताहितान् Ms. 3. 20.<BR>—3 Hurtful, detrimental, harmful, injurious, prejudicial,<BR>—4 Disadvantageous, evil.<BR>—5 Inimical, hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितः|अहित
अहित + .{@-तः@} An enemy; अहिताननिलोद्धूतैस्तर्जयन्निव केतुभिः R. 4. 28, 9. 17, 11. 68;<BR> तदहितयुवतेरभीक्ष्णमक्ष्णोः Śi. 7. 57 rival;<BR> अवाच्यवादांश्च बहून्वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः Bg. 2. 36; K. 5, 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितम्
अहित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Damage.<BR>—2 Food.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहितेच्छु, अहितकारिन्, अहितनामन्, अहितमनस्, अहितहितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितेच्छु
अहित + -इच्छु <i>a.</i> not wishing well, malevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0302-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

