अहृणान <i>a.</i> Not being angry, friendly (अक्रोधन); किं मे<BR> हव्यमहृणानो जुषेत Rv. 7. 86. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृणीयमान
अहृणीयमान <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not angry or jealous.<BR>—2 Willing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृदय
अहृदय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heartless.<BR>—2 Absent-minded; K. 84; हृदयमहृदया न नाम पूर्वम् Ki. 10. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृद्य
अहृद्य <i>a.</i> Not desired or agreeable, unpleasant; ˚कृत् <i>a.</i><BR> causing disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहे
अहे <i>ind.</i> [अह्-ए] A particle implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Reproach,<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Regret.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतु|अहेतुः
अहेतु <i>a.</i> Causeless, spontaneous, involuntary; अहेतुः पक्षपातो<BR> यः U. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुः|अहेतु
अहेतु + .{@-तुः@} Absence of cause and reason.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहेतुसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुसमः|अहेतुसम
अहेतु + -समः A particular sophism tending to prove an argument to be<BR> untenable, Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुक
अहे(है)तुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Groundless, causeless, without any motive; कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम्<BR> Bg. 18. 22; व्रज धृतिं त्यज भीतिमहेतुकाम् N. 4. 105.<BR>—2 Disinterested, selfless; (भक्तिः) अहैतुक्यप्रतिहता ययात्मा सम्प्रसीदति<BR> Bhāg. 1. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहैतुक
अहे(है)तुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Groundless, causeless, without any motive; कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम्<BR> Bg. 18. 22; व्रज धृतिं त्यज भीतिमहेतुकाम् N. 4. 105.<BR>—2 Disinterested, selfless; (भक्तिः) अहैतुक्यप्रतिहता ययात्मा सम्प्रसीदति<BR> Bhāg. 1. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुकम्
अहे(है)तुक + .{@-कम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without extraneous aid, through oneʼs own ability or power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेळत्|अहेळन्त्
अहेळ(ड)त्, -हेडमान <i>a.</i> Ved. Not unwilling; अहेळमानो वरुणेह<BR> बोध्युरुशंस मा न आयुः प्रमोषीः Rv. 1. 24. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेडत्
अहेळ(ड)त्, -हेडमान <i>a.</i> Ved. Not unwilling; अहेळमानो वरुणेह<BR> बोध्युरुशंस मा न आयुः प्रमोषीः Rv. 1. 24. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेडमान
अहेळ(ड)त्, -हेडमान <i>a.</i> Ved. Not unwilling; अहेळमानो वरुणेह<BR> बोध्युरुशंस मा न आयुः प्रमोषीः Rv. 1. 24. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेरुः|अहेरु
अहेरुः N. of the plant शतमूली or महाशतावरी. Asparagus Racemosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A particle showing<BR>——(<i>a</i>) surprise or wonder; often agreeable (ah, how great or wonderful);<BR> अहो कामी स्वतां पश्यति Ś. 2. 2; अहो मधुरमासां दर्शनम् Ś. 1;<BR> अहो वकुलावलिका M. 1 Oh, it is वकुला˚ (meaning ‘I did not expect to see you here’<BR>); अहो रागबद्धचित्तवृत्तिरालिखित इव सर्वतो<BR> रङ्गः Ś. 1; अहो रूपमहो वीर्यमहो सत्त्वमहो द्युतिः Rām. (how<BR> wonderful his form &c.).<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Painful surprise; अहो ते विगतचेतनत्वम् K. 146.<BR>—2 Sorrow or regret in general; (‘alas’, ‘ah’); अहो दुष्यन्तस्य संशयमारूढाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">Page0303-2</a>]<BR> पिण्डभाजः Ś. 6; विधिरहो बलवानिति मे मतिः Bh. 2. 91.<BR>—3 Praise (‘bravo’, ‘well done’); अहो देवदत्तः पचति शोभनम् P. VIII. 1. 40<BR> Sk.<BR>—4 Reproach (‘fie’, ‘shame’); अहो वो धिग्बलं क्षात्रम् Mb.<BR>—5 Calling out or addressing; अहो हिरण्यक श्लाघ्योऽसि H. 1.<BR>—6 Envy or jealousy; कटमहो करिष्यसि P. VIII. 1. 41 Com.<BR>—7 Enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR>—8 Fatigue.<BR>—9 Doubt (probably for आहो q. v.).<BR>—10 In the sense, obvious, plain, clear; (प्रसिद्ध) अहोष्मान्तर्गतश्चापि<BR> गर्भत्वं समुपेयिवान् Mb. 12. 253. 11.<BR>—11 Sometimes merely as an expletive. Prov. अहो रूपमहो ध्वनिः (used<BR> to convey the idea of mutual adulation, the ass complimenting the camel<BR> upon its fine form, and the camel the ass upon its melodious voice); अहो<BR> नु खलु (भोः) generally indicates surprise, often agreeable (आश्चर्य)<BR> अहो नु खल्वीदृशीमवस्थां प्रपन्नोऽस्मि Ś. 5; अहो नु खलु भोस्तदेतत्काकतालीयं<BR> नाम Māl. 5. अहो बत shows<BR>——(<i>a</i>) compassion, pity, regret; अहो बत महत्पापं कर्तुं व्यवसिता<BR> वयम् Bg. 1. 44;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) satisfaction or admiration (संतोष); अहो बतासि स्पृहणीयवीर्यः<BR> Ku. 3. 20 (Oh, how enviable is your prowess; Malli. here takes अहो बत<BR> in the sense of संबोधन);<BR>——(<i>c</i>) addressing, calling;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) fatigue &c. (अहो बतानुकम्पायां खेदे संबोधने) Nm. (अहो<BR> धिगर्थे शोके च करुणार्थविषादयोः । संबोधने प्रशंसायां विस्मये पादपूरणे<BR> ॥ असूयायां वितर्के च प्रायशोहो प्रयुज्यतो अहो बतानुकम्पायां खेदामन्त्रणयोस्तथा ॥).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: अहोपुरुषिका, अहोलाभकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोपुरुषिका
अहो + -पुरुषिका = आहोपुरुषिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोलाभकर
अहो + -लाभकर <i>a.</i> (अल्पेऽपि लाभे, अहो लाभो जात इति विस्मयं कुर्वाणम्)<BR> satisfied with very little; Mb. 5. 133. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नः|अह्न
अह्नः (The last member of a comp.) see under अहन्. Day; यदह्नात्कुरुते<BR> पापम् Mb. 1. 2. 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्न्यम्
अह्नः + .{@-अह्न्यम्@} Daily course (of the sun) द्वात्रिंशतं वै देवस्याह्न्यान्ययं<BR> लोकः Bṛ. Up. 3. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नवाय्य
अह्नवाय्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Not concealing.<BR>—2 Not to be denied or set aside; सत्यं तत् तुर्वशे यदौ विदानो अह्नवाय्यम् Rv. 8. 45. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय <i>ind.</i> Instantly, speedily, at once; अह्नाय सा नियमजं<BR> क्लममुत्ससर्ज Ku. 5. 86; अह्नाय तावदरुणेन तमो निरस्तम् R. 5. 71;<BR> Ki. 16. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रय
अह्रय, अह्रयाण <i>a.</i> Shameless, proud, presumptuously<BR> bold; अग्र एति युवतिरह्रपाणा Rv. 7. 80. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रयाण
अह्रय, अह्रयाण <i>a.</i> Shameless, proud, presumptuously<BR> bold; अग्र एति युवतिरह्रपाणा Rv. 7. 80. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रि
अह्रि <i>a.</i> [हृ-कि]<BR>—1 Luxurious, fat.<BR>—2 Wise, learned. (कवि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्री
अह्री <i>a.</i> Shameless. <i>f.</i> shamelessness, infamy; प्रसीदन्तु<BR> भवन्तो मेऽह्रीरेषा तु मया तुला Rām. 3. 10. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीक|अह्रीकः
अह्री + .{@-क@} <i>a.</i> Shameless (beggar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीकः|अह्रीक
अह्री + .{@-कः@} A Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रुत
अह्रुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Not fluctuating or stumbling.<BR>—2 Not crooked (अकुटिल); अश्लोणा अङ्गैरह्रुताः Av. 6. 120. 3. {@˚प्सु@}<BR> <i>a.</i> Ved. of straight or upright appearance; वहन्ते अह्रुतप्सवः Rv. 8. 20. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्वला
अह्वला<BR>—1 Not fluctuating, firmness.<BR>—2 The plant Semecarpus Anacardium (भल्लातक; Mar. बिब्बा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0303-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ The second letter of the Alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ<BR>—1 Used as a particle or interjection showing<BR>——(<i>a</i>) assent; ‘yes’, ‘verily’.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Compassion (अनुकम्पा) ‘Ah’.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Pain or regret (usually written आस् or अः q. v.), ‘alas’.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Recollection (स्मरण). ‘Ah’, ‘Oh’; आ एवं किलासीत् U. 6.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) But (used as a disjunctive conjunction).<BR>——(<i>f</i>) And (used as a cumulative conjunction).<BR>——(<i>g</i>) Sometimes used as an expletive; आ एवं मन्यसे. In all these<BR> senses आ is treated as a Pragṛhya vowel (does not form any Sandhi<BR> with a following vowel) P. I. 1. 14.<BR>——(<i>h</i>) It shows ‘anger’ also.<BR>—2 (As a prefix to verbs and nouns.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) it expresses the senses of near, near to, towards, from all sides,<BR> all around (see the several verbs).<BR>——(<i>b</i>) With verbs of motion, taking, carrying &c. it shows the reverse<BR> of the action; as गम् to go, आगम् to come; दा to give, आदा<BR> to take; नी to carry, आनी to bring.<BR>—3 (As a separable preposition with abl.) it shows either<BR>——(<i>a</i>) the limit inceptive (अभिविधि), from, ever since, away from,<BR> out of, off, from among; आ मूलात् श्रोतुमिच्छामि Ś. 1; बहुभ्य आ<BR> from out of many; आ जन्मनः Ś. 5. 25 ever since (her) birth; आ<BR> मनोः U. 6. 18.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Or, it expresses the limit exclusive or conclusive (मर्यादा),<BR> till, until, upto, as far as, unto; आड् मर्यादाभिविध्योः P. II. 1. 13;<BR> see अभिविधि; आ परितोषाद्विदुषाम् Ś. 1. 2 till the learned are satisfied;<BR> आ कैलासात् Me. 11 upto or as far as Kailāsa; ओदकान्तात् Ś. 4;<BR> U. 1. 37; V. 2. 2. In this sense आ sometimes governs the acc.; शतमा<BR> जातीः upto a hundred births.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) In both these senses आ frequently enters into compound, forming<BR> either Avyayībhāva comp. or compound adjectives; आबालं (or आ<BR> बालेभ्यः) हरिभक्तिः commencing with or including children; आमुक्ति<BR> (or आ मुक्तेः) संसारः Sk. till final emancipation; आमेखलम्<BR> Ku. 1. 5 as far as; आमरणम् Pt. 1 till death; आगोपालं ननृतुः<BR> K. 70 down to the cowherd; आगोपाला द्विजातयः including the cowherds.<BR> Sometimes the compound so formed stands as the first member of other compounds,<BR> सोऽहमाजन्मशुद्धानामाफलोदयकर्मणाम् । आसमुद्रक्षितीशानामानाकरथवर्त्मनाम्<BR> R. 1. 5; आगण्डविलम्बि Ś. 6. 17; आकर्णलम्बि M. 5. 10.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Used with loc. it has the sense of ‘in’, ‘at’ (mostly Ved.);<BR> गावो न यवसेष्वा Rv. 1. 91. 13.<BR>—4 With adjectives (or sometimes with nouns) आ has a diminutive force;<BR> आपिञ्जर <i>a.</i> Little red, reddish; आपिञ्जरा बद्धरजःकणत्वान्मञ्जर्युदारा<BR> शुशुभेऽर्जुनस्य R. 16. 51; आपाण्डुर a little white, whitish; आलक्ष्य<BR> Ś. 7. 18 slightly visible; आकम्पः gentle shaking; so आनील, आरक्त.<BR>—5 (As a separable adverb) आ chiefly occurs in the Vedas and means<BR> near, near to, or towards, there to, further; and also, even; in many<BR> cases it emphasizes the word which precedes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">Page0304-2</a>]<BR> it, and when placed after prepositions it strengthens their sense. आ<BR> प्रगृह्ये स्मृतौ वाक्ये परितापे पितामहे । घटे भावे च आऽस्तु स्यादव्ययं<BR> कोपपीडयोः । आङीषदर्थेऽभिव्याप्तौ सीमार्थे धातुयोगजे ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ, -आः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 Grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आः
आ, -आः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 Grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्
आम् = आम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंहस्पत्य
आंहस्पत्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the dominion of अंहस्पति (as<BR> the intercalary month), Gobhila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आः
आः<BR>—1 = आस् q. v.<BR>—2 N. of Lakṣmī (आ). or Brahman.<BR>—3 Speech.<BR>—4 Boundary. cf. आः स्वयंभूरिभो वाजी खेदः शंकरवासवौ । पारिजातः<BR> समः प्राज्ञो निवासश्चणकः सुतः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकच्
आकच् €1 Ā. to tie or fasten on; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकण्ठम्
आकण्ठम् <i>ind.</i> Up to the throat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकण्ठतृप्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकण्ठतृप्त
आकण्ठम् + -तृप्त <i>a.</i> Satiated up to the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकत्थनम्
आकत्थनम् Boasting, swaggering; Rām. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प्|आकंप्
आकम्प् €1 Ā. To shake, tremble; to tremble with fear, Ś. 4. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To shake, put in motion (fig. also.); अनोकहाकम्पितपुष्पगन्धी R. 2. 19<BR> (some take आकम्पित = ईषत्कम्पनम्); Ṛs. 6. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पः|आकम्प|आकंपः
आकम्पः<BR>—1 Shaking a little.<BR>—2 Shaking, trembling; अनाकम्पधैर्ये V. 5. 22, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पन|आकंपन
आकम्पन^1 <i>a.</i> Slightly shaking.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: adj.  -nam given as subword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पनम्
आकम्पन + .{@-नम्@} Trembling motion, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पित|आकंपित|आकम्पितं
आकम्पित, आकम्प्र <i>a.</i><BR> Shaking, trembling; moved, agitated. अनोकहाकम्पितपुष्पगन्धी R. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प्र|आकंप्र
आकम्पित, आकम्प्र <i>a.</i><BR> Shaking, trembling; moved, agitated. अनोकहाकम्पितपुष्पगन्धी R. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकत्यम्
आकत्यम् [अ-कत-ष्यञ् P. V. 1. 121] Making anything impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर|आकरः
आकर -See under आकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ण्
आकर्ण् €10 P. (properly a Den. form) To hear, give ear to, listen;<BR> सर्वे सविस्मयमाकर्णयन्ति Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णनम्
आकर्णनम्<BR>—1 Hearing, listening. मुदा तदाकर्णनतत्पराभूत् N.<BR>—2 <i>ind.</i> upto the ear or from the ear (said of an arrow, drawn from a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्
आकल् €10 P.<BR>—1 To take hold of, seize, take; बाहुमूलप्रहितभुजाकलितस्तनेन<BR> Śi. 7. 21; कुतूहलाकलितहृदया K. 49 seized.<BR>—2 To consider, regard; स्पर्शमपि पावनमाकलयन्ति K. 108, 235;<BR> खिन्नमसूयया हृदयं तवाकलयामि Gīt. 3.<BR>—3 To observe, notice, take into consideration; भयहेतुमाकलय्य H. 1.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To bind, fasten, tie; स्वच्छदुकूलपल्लवाकलितमौलेः K. 99, 84;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To confine; to restrain, tie up; सुवर्णसूत्राकलिताधराम्बराम्<BR> Śi. 1. 6, 9. 45; Ks. 20. 52<BR>—5 To shake, agitate; मारुताकलितास्तत्र द्रुमाः Mb.; Bh. 1. 42.<BR>—6 To cast, throw; Śi. 3. 73, 9. 72.<BR>—7 To surrender, transfer.<BR>—8 To measure; आकलयन्तमिव त्रिभुवनम् K. 78 to count, reckon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0304-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलनम्
आकलनम्<BR>—1 Laying hold of, seizing; मेखलाकलनम् K. 183; binding; सेव्योऽपि<BR> सानुनयमाकलनाय यन्त्रा Śi. 5. 42 confinement.<BR>—2 Counting, reckoning.<BR>—3 Wish, desire.<BR>—4 Inquiry.<BR>—5 Comprehending, understanding;<BR>—6 Description, narration; प्राचेतसाद्याः कवयोऽनवद्या यदेकदेशाकलनेऽपि<BR> नेशाः Viś. Guṇā. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलना
आकलना<BR>—1 See आकलनम्.<BR>—2 Worship, devotion; तथाप्येषा दोषापनयनपटुः स्वाकलनया Viś. Guṇā. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पः|आकल्प
आकल्पः<BR>—1 an ornament, decoration; आत्मानं भूषयाञ्चकुर्वस्त्राकल्पाञ्जनादिभिः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 5. 9. आकल्पसारो रूपाजीवाजनः Dk. 68; K. 313, 365; R. 17. 22, 18. 52.<BR>—2 Dress (in general), accoutrement.<BR>—3 Sickness, disease.<BR>—4 Adding to, increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पम्
आकल्पम्, आकल्पान्तम् <i>ind.</i> Up to the time of Kalpa, till<BR> the end of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पान्तम्
आकल्पम्, आकल्पान्तम् <i>ind.</i> Up to the time of Kalpa, till<BR> the end of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पकः|आकल्पक
आकल्पकः<BR>—1 Remembering with regret, missing.<BR>—2 Fainting, loss of sense or perception.<BR>—3 Joy or delight.<BR>—4 Darkness.<BR>—5 A Knot or joint. cf. ‘आकल्पकस्तमोमोहग्रन्थिषूत्कलिकामुदोः’ Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्यम्
आकल्यम्^1 Sickness, disease.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: Sense = sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्लः|आकल्ल
आकल्लः Pellitory plant, Anthemis Pyrethrum (Mar. अक्कलकाढा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषः|आकष
आकषः A touch-stone,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषक
आकषक <i>a.</i> Cutting, Rubbing, or testing with a touch-stone; (आकषे<BR> कुशलः, तत्र नियुक्तो वा); testing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषिक
आकषिक <i>a.</i> [आकषेण चरति ष्ठल्] Testing, touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकस्मिक|आकस्मिकं
आकस्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [विनयादिगणः; अकस्मात्-ष्ठक् टिलोपः]<BR>—1 Accidental, unforeseen, unexpected, sudden; त्रासस्त्वाकस्मिकं भयम् Hem.<BR>—2 Causeless, groundless; नन्वदृष्टानिष्टौ जगद्वैचित्र्यमाकस्मिकं स्यात् । Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष्|आकांक्ष्
आकाङ्क्ष् €1 U.<BR>—1 To desire, long or wish for, expect; प्रत्याश्वसन्तं रिपुराचकाङ्क्ष<BR> R. 7. 47, 5. 38; Ms. 2. 162, 10. 121; Y. 1. 153; आकाङ्क्षन्ती नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशाम्<BR> (तां पश्य) Me. 91.<BR>—2 To try to reach a place, turn to; दक्षिणां दिशमाकाङ्क्षन् Ms. 3. 258.<BR>—3 To require, need.<BR>—4 (In gram.) To require some word or words to be supplied for the completion<BR> of the sense; see आकाङ्क्षा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष|आकांक्ष
आकाङ्क्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desiring, wishing.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Requiring some words to complete the sense; अङ्गयुक्तं<BR> तिडाकाङ्क्षम् P. VIII. 2. 96, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षा|आकांक्षा
आकाङ्क्ष + .{@-क्षा@}<BR>—1 Desire, wish; भक्त˚ Suśr., भ्रान्त्यालिङ्ग्य मया रहस्यमुदितं<BR> तत्सङ्गमाकाङ्क्षया Amaru. 46.<BR>—2 (In gram. &c.) The presence of a word necessary to complete the sense,<BR> one of the three elements necessary to convey a complete sense or thought<BR> (the other two being योग्यता and आसत्ति); आकाङ्क्षा प्रतीतिपर्यवसानविरहः<BR> S. D. 2 the absence of the completion of a sense; see Bhāṣā P. 82, 84<BR> and T. S. 49; in the ex. गौरश्वः पुरुषो हस्ती there is आकाङ्क्षा.<BR>—3 Looking at or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">Page0305-2</a>]<BR> towards.<BR>—4 Purpose, intention.<BR>—5 Inquiry.<BR>—6 The significance^1 of a word.<BR>—7 Expectancy. असत्यामाकाङ्क्षायां संनिधानमकारणम्, ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 23.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षित|आकांक्षित
आकाङ्क्षित <i>p. p.</i> Desired, wished, inquired; looked at, wanted, necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षिन्|आकांक्षिन्
आकाङ्क्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing, desiring, expecting; अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञः Bg. 17. 11;<BR> तं भावार्थप्रसवसमयाकाङ्क्षिणीनां प्रजानाम् । R. 19. 57.<BR>—2 Asking, inquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष्य|आकांक्ष्य
आकाङ्क्ष्य <i>a.</i> Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष्यम्
आकाङ्क्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यम्@} Need of supplying a word or words for the completion of<BR> the sense P. III. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकायः|आकाय
आकायः [आ-चि-कर्मणि घञ् चितौ कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 The fire on the funeral pile; आकायमग्निं चिन्वीत P. III. 3. 41. Sk.<BR>—2 A funeral pile.<BR>—3 Abode, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाय्य
आकाय्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Desirable; आकाय्यस्य दावने परुक्षोः Rv. 4. 29. 5.<BR>—2 Commendable in every way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालः|आकाल
आकालः<BR>—1 The right time.<BR>—2 Wrong time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिक|आकालिकं
आकालिक <i>a.</i> [अकाले भवः ठञ्]<BR>.(-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Momentary, transitory; Ms. 4. 103 एतानाकालिकान्विद्यादनध्यायानृतावपि 105;<BR> आकालिकः स्तनयित्नुः; आकालिकी विद्युत्, उत्पत्त्यनन्तरं विनाशिनीत्यर्थः P. V. 1. 114.<BR>—2 Unseasonable, premature, untimely; आकालिकीं वीक्ष्य मधुप्रवृत्तिम्<BR> Ku. 3. 34; आकालिकं सपदि दुर्दिनमन्तरिक्षम् Mk. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिकी
आकालिक + .{@-की@} Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश्
आकाश् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To view, recognize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशः|आकाश|आकाशं
आकाशः, -शम्<BR> [समन्तादाकाशन्ते सूर्यादयोऽत्र Tv.]<BR>—1 The sky आकाशभवा सरस्वती Ku. 4. 39; ˚ग, ˚चारिन् &c.<BR>—2 Ether (considered as the fifth element).<BR>—3 The subtle and ethereal fluid pervading the whole universe; one of<BR> the 9 <i>dravyas</i> or substances recognized by the Vaiśesikas. It is the<BR> substratum of the quality ‘sound’; शब्दगुणमाकाशम्; cf. also श्रुतिविषयगुणा<BR> या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वम् Ś. 1. 1; अथात्मनः शब्दगुणं गुणज्ञः पदं<BR> (scil. आकाशम्) विमानेन विगाहमानः R. 13. 1.<BR>—4 Free space or vacuity; यश्चायमन्तरात्मन्नाकाशः Bṛ. Up.<BR>—5 Space, place in general; सपर्वतवनाकाशां पृथिवीम् Mb.; भवनाकाशमजायताम्बुराशिः<BR> Bv. 2. 165 open space (not covered or surrounded by anything); मुनयः<BR> सलिलाहारा वायुभक्षास्तथापरे । आकाशनिलयाश्चैव तथा स्थण्डिलशायिनः ॥<BR> Rām. 3. 6. 4.<BR>—6 Brahman (as identical with ether); आकाशस्तल्लिङ्गात् Br. Sūt. 1. 1. 22;<BR> यावानयमाकाशस्तावानयमन्तर्हृदयाकाशः Ch. Up. 8. 1. 3.<BR>—7 Light, clearness.<BR>—8 A hole.<BR>—9 A dot, zero (in Math.). आकाशे in the air; आकाशे लक्ष्यं बद्ध्वा<BR> fixing the look on some object out of sight. आकाशे in the sense of<BR> ‘in the air’ is used in dramas as a stage-direction when a character on<BR> the stage asks questions to some one not on the stage, and listens to<BR> an imaginary speech supposed to be a reply, which is usually introduced<BR> by the words किं ब्रवीषि, किं कथयसि &c.; दूरस्थाभाषणं यत्स्यादशरीरनिवेदनम् ।<BR> परोक्षान्तरितं वाक्यं तदाकाशे निगद्यते ॥ Bharata; cf. आकाशभाषितम्<BR> below; (आकाशे) प्रियंवदे, कस्येदमुशीरानुलेपनं मृणालवन्ति च<BR> नलिनीपत्राणि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">Page0306-1</a>]<BR> नीयन्ते । (श्रुतिमभिनीय) किं ब्रवीषि &c. Ś. 3. This is a<BR> contrivance used by poets to avoid the introduction of a fresh character,<BR> and it is largely used in the species of dramatic composition called भाण<BR> where only one character conducts the whole play by a copious use of आकाशभाषित.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकाशानन्त्यायतनम्, आकाशास्तिकायः, आकाशेशः, आकाशकक्षा, आकाशकल्पः, आकाशग,^1 आकाशगङ्गा, आकाशगर्भः,^2 आकाशचमसः, आकाशज, आकाशजननिन्, आकाशदीपः, आकाशप्रदीपः, आकाशपथिकः, आकाशप्रतिष्ठितः, आकाशबद्धलक्ष, आकाशभाषितम्, आकाशमण्डलम्, आकाशमांसी, आकाशमुखिन्, आकाशमुष्टिहननाय, आकाशमूली, आकाशयानम्, आकाशरक्षिन्, आकाशवचनम्, आकाशवर्त्मन्, आकाशवल्ली, आकाशवाणी, आकाशशयनम्, आकाशसलिलम्, आकाशस्थ, आकाशस्फटिकः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशम्
आकाशः, -शम्<BR> [समन्तादाकाशन्ते सूर्यादयोऽत्र Tv.]<BR>—1 The sky आकाशभवा सरस्वती Ku. 4. 39; ˚ग, ˚चारिन् &c.<BR>—2 Ether (considered as the fifth element).<BR>—3 The subtle and ethereal fluid pervading the whole universe; one of<BR> the 9 <i>dravyas</i> or substances recognized by the Vaiśesikas. It is the<BR> substratum of the quality ‘sound’; शब्दगुणमाकाशम्; cf. also श्रुतिविषयगुणा<BR> या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वम् Ś. 1. 1; अथात्मनः शब्दगुणं गुणज्ञः पदं<BR> (scil. आकाशम्) विमानेन विगाहमानः R. 13. 1.<BR>—4 Free space or vacuity; यश्चायमन्तरात्मन्नाकाशः Bṛ. Up.<BR>—5 Space, place in general; सपर्वतवनाकाशां पृथिवीम् Mb.; भवनाकाशमजायताम्बुराशिः<BR> Bv. 2. 165 open space (not covered or surrounded by anything); मुनयः<BR> सलिलाहारा वायुभक्षास्तथापरे । आकाशनिलयाश्चैव तथा स्थण्डिलशायिनः ॥<BR> Rām. 3. 6. 4.<BR>—6 Brahman (as identical with ether); आकाशस्तल्लिङ्गात् Br. Sūt. 1. 1. 22;<BR> यावानयमाकाशस्तावानयमन्तर्हृदयाकाशः Ch. Up. 8. 1. 3.<BR>—7 Light, clearness.<BR>—8 A hole.<BR>—9 A dot, zero (in Math.). आकाशे in the air; आकाशे लक्ष्यं बद्ध्वा<BR> fixing the look on some object out of sight. आकाशे in the sense of<BR> ‘in the air’ is used in dramas as a stage-direction when a character on<BR> the stage asks questions to some one not on the stage, and listens to<BR> an imaginary speech supposed to be a reply, which is usually introduced<BR> by the words किं ब्रवीषि, किं कथयसि &c.; दूरस्थाभाषणं यत्स्यादशरीरनिवेदनम् ।<BR> परोक्षान्तरितं वाक्यं तदाकाशे निगद्यते ॥ Bharata; cf. आकाशभाषितम्<BR> below; (आकाशे) प्रियंवदे, कस्येदमुशीरानुलेपनं मृणालवन्ति च<BR> नलिनीपत्राणि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">Page0306-1</a>]<BR> नीयन्ते । (श्रुतिमभिनीय) किं ब्रवीषि &c. Ś. 3. This is a<BR> contrivance used by poets to avoid the introduction of a fresh character,<BR> and it is largely used in the species of dramatic composition called भाण<BR> where only one character conducts the whole play by a copious use of आकाशभाषित.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकाशानन्त्यायतनम्, आकाशास्तिकायः, आकाशेशः, आकाशकक्षा, आकाशकल्पः, आकाशग,^1 आकाशगङ्गा, आकाशगर्भः,^2 आकाशचमसः, आकाशज, आकाशजननिन्, आकाशदीपः, आकाशप्रदीपः, आकाशपथिकः, आकाशप्रतिष्ठितः, आकाशबद्धलक्ष, आकाशभाषितम्, आकाशमण्डलम्, आकाशमांसी, आकाशमुखिन्, आकाशमुष्टिहननाय, आकाशमूली, आकाशयानम्, आकाशरक्षिन्, आकाशवचनम्, आकाशवर्त्मन्, आकाशवल्ली, आकाशवाणी, आकाशशयनम्, आकाशसलिलम्, आकाशस्थ, आकाशस्फटिकः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0305-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशानन्त्यायतनम्
आकाशः + -अनन्त्यायतनम् the abode of infinity or of infinite space;<BR> N. of a world with the Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशास्तिकायः|आकाशास्तिकाय
आकाशः + -अस्तिकायः N. of a category with the Jainas; धर्माधर्माकाशास्तिकायास्ते Sarva. S. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशेशः|आकाशेश
आकाशः + -ईशः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 (in law) any helpless person (such as a child, a woman, a pauper) who<BR> has no other possession than the air. आकाशेशास्तु विज्ञेया बालवृद्धकृशातुराः Ms. 4. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशकक्षा
आकाशः + -कक्षा ‘the girdle of the sky’, horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशकल्पः|आकाशकल्प
आकाशः + -कल्पः Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशग|आकाशगः
आकाशः + -ग^1 <i>a.</i> moving through the atmosphere.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशगः|आकाशग
आकाशः + -गः + .({@-गः@}) a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशगा
आकाशः + -गः + .({@-गा@}) the heavenly Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशगङ्गा|आकाशगंगा
आकाशः + -गङ्गा [आकाशपथवाहिनी गङ्गा] the celestial Ganges; नदत्याकाशगङ्गायाः<BR> स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R. 1. 78; cf. also उभौ यदि व्योम्नि पृथक् प्रवाहावाकाशगङ्गापयसः<BR> पतेताम् Śi. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशगर्भः|आकाशगर्भ
आकाशः + -गर्भः^1 <i>m.</i> N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशचमसः|आकाशचमस
आकाशः + -चमसः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशज
आकाशः + -ज <i>a.</i> produced in the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशजननिन्
आकाशः + -जननिन् <i>m.</i> a casement, loophole, an embrasure (left in castle<BR> walls); प्रगण्डीः कारयेत्सम्यगाकाशजननीस्तदा Mb. 12. 69. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशदीपः|आकाशदीप
आकाशः + -दीपः, -प्रदीपः<BR>—1 a lamp lighted in honour of Lakṣmī or Viṣṇu and raised on a pole<BR> in the air at the Divāli festival in the month of Kārtika.<BR>—2 a beacon-light, a lantern on a pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशप्रदीपः|आकाशप्रदीप
आकाशः + -दीपः, -प्रदीपः<BR>—1 a lamp lighted in honour of Lakṣmī or Viṣṇu and raised on a pole<BR> in the air at the Divāli festival in the month of Kārtika.<BR>—2 a beacon-light, a lantern on a pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशपथिकः|आकाशपथिक
आकाशः + -पथिकः The sun; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशप्रतिष्ठितः|आकाशप्रतिष्ठित
आकाशः + -प्रतिष्ठितः N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशबद्धलक्ष
आकाशः + -बद्धलक्ष (in Nāṭaka) fixing the gaze on some object out of<BR> sight; ततः प्रविशति आकाशबद्धलक्षः उन्मत्तवेषो राजा V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशभाषितम्
आकाशः + -भाषितम्<BR>—1 speaking off the stage, a supposed speech to which a reply is made<BR> as if it had been actually spoken and heard; किं ब्रवीषीति यन्नाटपे<BR> विना पात्रं प्रयुज्यते । श्रुत्वेवानुक्तमप्यर्थं तत्स्यादाकाशभाषितम् S. D. 425.<BR>—2 a sound or voice in the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमण्डलम्
आकाशः + -मण्डलम् the celestial sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमांसी
आकाशः + -मांसी [आकाशभवा मांसी] N. of a plant (क्षुद्रजटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमुखिन्
आकाशः + -मुखिन् pl. N. of Śaiva sect, the adherents of which keep their<BR> faces turned towards the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमुष्टिहननाय
आकाशः + -मुष्टिहननाय Ā. To be foolish like one who beats the air with<BR> his fist; Sarva. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमूली
आकाशः + -मूली the aquatic plant (कुम्भिका) Pistia Stratiotes (Mar. शेवाळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशयानम्
आकाशः + -यानम्<BR>—1 a heavenly car, a balloon. cf. वायुबन्धकवस्त्रेण सुबद्धो यानमस्तके ।<BR> उदानस्य लघुत्वेन बिभर्त्याकाशयानकम् ॥ गरुत्मद्धंसैः कङ्कालैरन्यैः<BR> पक्षिगणैरपि । आकाशे वाहयेद् यानं विमानमिति संज्ञितम् ॥ -अगस्त्यसंहिता.<BR>—2 moving or travelling through the sky; आकाशयानेन प्रविशति enter<BR> passing through the sky (frequently occurring in dramas).<BR>—3 one who moves through the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशरक्षिन्
आकाशः + -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a watchman on the outer battlements of a castle<BR> (आकाश इव अत्युच्चप्राचीरोपरि स्थित्वा रक्षति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवचनम्
आकाशः + -वचनम् = ˚भाषितम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवर्त्मन्
आकाशः + -वर्त्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the firmament.<BR>—2 the atmosphere, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवल्ली
आकाशः + -वल्ली a sort of creeper, a parasitical plant (अमरवेल;<BR> Mar. बांडगूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवाणी
आकाशः + -वाणी a voice from heaven, an incorporeal speech (अशरीरिणी वाणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशशयनम्
आकाशः + -शयनम् Sleeping in the open air; निवृत्ताकाशशयनाः Rām. 3. 16. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशसलिलम्
आकाशः + -सलिलम् rain; dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशस्थ
आकाशः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> abiding in the sky. aerial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशस्फटिकः|आकाशस्फटिक
आकाशः + -स्फटिकः a kind of crystal supposed to be formed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">Page0306-2</a>]<BR> in the atmosphere (two kinds सूर्यकान्त and चन्द्रकान्त); hail (करका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवत्|आकाशवन्त्
आकाशवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Filling a certain vacuum or space.<BR>—2 Going through the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशीय
आकाशीय, -आकाश्य <i>a.</i><BR> [आकाशस्येदम्; छ-यत्] Atmospherical, aerial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश्य
आकाशीय, -आकाश्य <i>a.</i><BR> [आकाशस्येदम्; छ-यत्] Atmospherical, aerial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिंचनम्
आकिंचनम्, -आकिंचन्यम्<BR> Poverty, want of any possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिंचन्यम्
आकिंचनम्, -आकिंचन्यम्<BR> Poverty, want of any possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीम्
आकीम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. From (with abl.); leaving, excluding; आकीं सूर्यस्य<BR> रोचनाद् Rv. 1. 14. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्च्|आकुंच्
आकुञ्च् €1 Ā., €6 P. To bend.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> —1 To draw together, contract, bend<BR> inward, curve, compress; आकुञ्चितसव्यपादम् Ku. 3. 70; R. 6. 15; Bh. 1. 3.<BR>—2 To shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चनम्
आकुञ्चनम्<BR>—1 Bending, contraction, compression; Ku. 78 &c. also उत्क्षेपणं तथावक्षेपणमाकुञ्चनं<BR> तथा Bhāṣā P.<BR>—2 Contraction regarded as one of the 5 <i>karmans</i> q. v.<BR>—3 Collecting, heaping.<BR>—4 Curving.<BR>—5 Contortion.<BR>—6 A kind of army movement; आकुञ्चनं तथा यानं प्रयाणमपयानकम्<BR> Śukra. 4. 1100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Full of, burdened or filled with (in general); अश्रुर्ण्णाकुलेक्षणम्<BR> Bg. 2. 1. प्रचलदूर्मिमालाकुलम् (समुद्रम्) Bh. 2. 4; मृगपक्षिगणाकुलम्<BR> Rām.; बाष्पाकुलां वाचम् Nala. 4. 18; आलापकुतूहलाकुलतरे श्रोत्रे Amaru. 87.<BR>—2 Overcome, affected, or afflicted, smitten; हर्ष˚, शोक˚, विस्मय˚, स्नेह˚ &c.<BR>—3 Busily or intently engaged or absorbed in; विभवगुरुभिः कृत्यैस्तस्य<BR> प्रतिक्षणमाकुला Ś. 4. 19.<BR>—4 Confounded, agitated, flurried distracted; नगरीमाकुलां कृत्वा वञ्चयित्वा<BR> च रावणम् Rām. 5. 56. 24; अभिचैद्यं प्रतिष्ठासुरासीत्कार्यद्वयाकुलः<BR> Śi. 2. 1; perplexed, at a loss what to do, undetermined; नयवर्त्माकुलमर्जुनाग्रजम्<BR> Ki. 2. 54. ˚आकुल very much agitated; K. 10, 28; Ki. 14. 32.<BR>—5 Dishevelled, disordered (as hair); असंयताकुलालकान् K. 60, 243;<BR> स्रस्तः स्रग्दामशोभां त्यजति विरचितामाकुलः केशपाशः Ratn. 1. 17; Ki. 8. 18.<BR>—6 Wild dreary; Ś. 2.<BR>—7 Taken out of oneʼs natural condition.<BR>—8 Incoherent, contradictory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलम्
आकुल + .{@-लम्@} An inhabited place; रहितेष्वाकुलेषु च Rām. ━<i>adv.</i><BR> In bewilderment; किमेतदित्याकुलमीक्षितं जनैः Śi. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलता
आकुलता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 A multitude.<BR>—2 Perplexity, bewilderment, confusion; Amaru. 74; तव चित्तं किमाकुलत्वम् Bh. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलत्वम्
आकुलता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 A multitude.<BR>—2 Perplexity, bewilderment, confusion; Amaru. 74; तव चित्तं किमाकुलत्वम् Bh. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलयति
आकुलयति Den. P. To confound, make disordered, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलित
आकुलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distressed, confounded, agitated; मार्गाचलव्यतिकराकुलितेव सिन्धुः Ku. 5. 85.<BR>—2 Entangled; K. 83.<BR>—3 Obscured, blinded; धूम˚ दृष्टेः Ś. 4.<BR>—4 Overcome or affected; शोक˚, पिपासा˚ &c.<BR>—5 Disordered, deranged; R. 16. 67; मन्दानिलाकुलितनम्रमृदुप्रवालाः Ṛs. 6. 17.<BR>—6 Tilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीकृ
आकुलीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To fill with.<BR>—2 To confound, perplex, bewilder.<BR>—3 To overcome; कुतूहलेनाकुलीक्रियमाणो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">Page0307-1</a>]<BR> लघिमा K. 134.<BR>—4 To trouble, pain; Ś. 2. ━<i>pass.</i> To be confounded, bewildered;<BR> आकुल्यकारि कटकस्तुरगेण तूर्णम् Śi. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0306-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीभू
आकुलीभू €1 P. To be perplexed or agitated; इति प्रतिपादितमाकुलीभवेत्<BR> Ś. B. this conclusion would be shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलिः|आकुलि
आकुलिः <i>m.</i> N. of an Asura priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूणित
आकूणित <i>a.</i> [आ-कूण्-क्त] Contracted a little^1; मदनशरशल्यवेदनाकूणितत्रिभागेन K. 166, 81.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूतम्
आकूतम् [आ-कू-भावे-क्त]<BR>—1 Meaning, intention, purpose; दुर्योधनस्य चाकूतं तृषितस्येव विप्रुषः<BR> Mb. 8. 9. 20. इतीरिताकूतमनीलवाजिनम् Ki. 14. 26.<BR>—2 A feeling, state of heart, emotion; चूडा मण्डलबन्धनं तरलयत्याकूतजो<BR> वेपथुः U. 5. 35; भावाकूतम् Amaru. 4; Sāṅ. K. 31; स्नेहाकूत<BR> Māl. 9. 11; U. 6. 35; साकूतम् feelingly, meaningly, (oft. occurring<BR> in plays as a stage-direction). cf. also चिरयति मयि व्यक्ताकूता मनाक्<BR> स्फुरिताधरा Nāg. 2. 6.<BR>—3 Wonder or curiosity; सर्वं ˚करम् U. 4.<BR>—4 Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूतिः|आकूति
आकूतिः <i>f.</i> [आ-कू-भावे-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Intention; wish, desire; आकूतिः सत्या मनसो मे अस्तु Rv. 10. 128. 4;<BR> आकूतीनां च चित्तीनां प्रवर्तकः Mb. ˚पर <i>a.</i> accomplishing<BR> oneʼs own intentions.<BR>—2 An organ of action (कर्मेन्द्रिय); चेतोभिराकूतिभिरातनोति निरङ्कुशं<BR> कुशलं चेतरं वा Bhāg. 5. 11. 4.<BR>—3 An action; चेत आकूतिरूपाय नमो वाचो विभूतये Bhāg. 4. 24. 44.<BR>—4 N. of a Kalpa; Vāyu P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूपारम्
आकूपारम् N. of different Sāman verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृ
आकृ €8 U., €5 P.<BR>—1 To bring near or towards; to drive near or together.<BR>—2 To bring down; form wholly (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To invite, call, summon; रदनिकामाकारय Mk. 3; Dk. 174; Pt. 1;<BR> मध्यस्थस्य दृष्टिमाकारयति Mk. 4 calls or arrests; Śi. 16. 52.<BR>—2 To prompt, incite, propel; ममापि कौतूहलेनाकारित एषः Ś. 6.<BR>—3 To call out boldly, challenge; Mk. 2.<BR>—4 To cause to appear, produce.<BR>—5 To ask anything of one; पुनराकारयामास तमेव वरमङ्गना Rām. 2. 13. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरः|आकर
आकरः [by पुंसि संज्ञायां घः प्रायेण P. III. 3. 118 आकुर्वन्त्यस्मिन्; Kāśi.]<BR>—1 A mine; मणिराकरोद्भवः R. 3. 18; आकरे पद्मरागाणां जन्म काचमणेः<BR> कुतः H. Pr. 38; Ms. 7. 62; आकरेष्वधिकारिता Y. 3. 242; (fig.)<BR> a mine or rich source of anything (उत्पत्तिस्थानम्); मासो नु पुष्पाकरः<BR> V. 1. 10; अशेषगुणाकरम् Bh. 2. 92; सौभाग्यपण्याकरः Mk. 8. 38;<BR> आकरः सर्वशास्त्राणाम् Mu. 7. 7.<BR>—2 A collection, group; पद्माकरं दिनकरो विकचीकरोति Bh. 2. 73;<BR> कमलाकर Ku. 2. 29; स्नेहाकराणि Māl. 9. 47.<BR>—3 Best, excellent.<BR>—4 N. of a country.<BR>—5 N. of the Mahābhāṣya.<BR>—6 N. of a country (the modern Khandesh); Bṛ. S. <i>a.</i> Best, excellent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकरकर्मन्, आकरग्रन्थः, आकरजम्, आकरतीर्थम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरकर्मन्
आकरः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> A mining operation; आकरकर्मान्तप्रवर्तनम् Kau. A. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरग्रन्थः
आकरः + -ग्रन्थः A source-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरजम्
आकरः + -जम् A jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरतीर्थम्
आकरः + -तीर्थम् Name of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारः|आकार
आकारः [आ-कृ-घञ्]<BR>—1 Form, shape, figure, द्विधा˚ of two forms or sorts; Pt. 3. 37.<BR>—2 Aspect, appearance. mien, countenance; आकारसदृशप्रज्ञः R. 1. 15, 16. 7,<BR> Ś. 1;<BR>—3 (Particularly) expression of the face, as giving a clue to oneʼs inward<BR> thoughts or mental disposition; तस्य संवृतमन्त्रस्य गूढाकारेङ्गितस्य<BR> च R. 1. 20; Pt. 1; भवानपि संवृताकारमास्ताम् V. 2; Ś. 7; Ki. 1. 14;<BR> साकारो निःस्पृहः Pt. 3. 88 giving no clue to his inward thoughts,<BR> reserved; K. 233; Mv. 6; Ms. 7. 63, 8. 25; -आकारैरिङ्गितैर्गत्या चेष्टया<BR> भाषितेन च । नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च गृह्यतेऽन्तर्गतं मनः ॥ Ms. 8. 26.<BR>—4 Hint, sign, token.<BR>—5 Identity, oneness<BR>—6 Recognition of identity (in Sāṅ. Phil.).<BR>—7 The letter आ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकारगुप्तिः, आकारगोपनम्, आकारगूहनम्, आकारवर्ण, आकारसुश्लक्ष्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगुप्तिः|आकारगुप्ति
आकारः + -गुप्तिः, -गोपनम्, -गूहनम् dissimulation, suppressing all outward<BR> manifestation of the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगोपनम्
आकारः + -गुप्तिः, -गोपनम्, -गूहनम् dissimulation, suppressing all outward<BR> manifestation of the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगूहनम्
आकारः + -गुप्तिः, -गोपनम्, -गूहनम् dissimulation, suppressing all outward<BR> manifestation of the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवर्ण
आकारः + -वर्ण, -सुश्लक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> Delicate in shape and colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारसुश्लक्ष्ण
आकारः + -वर्ण, -सुश्लक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> Delicate in shape and colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारणम्
आका(क)रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Invitation, calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>—2 A challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरणम्
आका(क)रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Invitation, calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>—2 A challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारणा
आका(क)रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Invitation, calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>—2 A challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवत्|आकारवन्त्
आकारवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Embodied.<BR>—2 Symmetrical, well-formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारित
आकारित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Called.<BR>—2 Agreed upon.<BR>—3 Demanded, exacted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृत
आकृत <i>p. p.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Arranged, built (as a house); यद् वा समुद्रे अध्याकृते गृहे Rv. 8. 10. 1.<BR>—2 Brought near to, being near; ध्यायन्त आकृतधियः शयनासनादौ तत्साम्यमापुरनुरक्तधियां<BR> पुनः किम् Bhāg. 11. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिः|आकृति
आकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Form, figure, shape (of anything); गन्धाकृतिः Bhāg. 5. 11. 10.<BR> गोवर्धनस्याकृतिरन्वकारि Śi. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Bodily form, body; किमिव हि मधुराणां मण्डनं नाकृतीनाम् Ś. 1. 20;<BR> विकृताकृति Ms. 11. 52; घोर˚, सौम्य˚ &c.<BR>—3 Appearance; oft. a good or noble appearance, good form; न ह्याकृतिः<BR> सुसदृशं विजहाति वृत्तम् Mk. 9. 16; यत्राकृतिस्तत्र गुणा वसन्ति<BR> Subhāṣ. आकृतिमनुगृह्णन्ति गुणाः Vb. 2.<BR>—4 Specimen, character.<BR>—5 Tribe, species.<BR>—6 A form ascertained by senses; मनस्याकृतयो मग्ना Mb. 12. 204. 19.<BR> cf. आकृतिस्तु शरीरे स्याद्रूपसामान्ययोरपि.<BR>—7 A metre.<BR>—8 (Arith.) The number twenty-two.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकृतिगणः, आकृतिच्छत्रा, आकृतियोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिगणः|आकृतिगण
आकृतिः + -गणः a list of words belonging to a certain grammatical rule<BR> which does not give every word belonging to that rule, but only specimens,<BR> a list of specimens (frequently occurring in the Gaṇapāṭha); <i>e. g.</i><BR> अर्श आदिगण, स्वरादिगण, चादि गण &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिच्छत्रा
आकृतिः + -च्छत्रा the plant Achyranthes Aspera (Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतियोगः|आकृतियोग
आकृतिः + -योगः A certain class of constellations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिमत्|आकृतिमन्त्
आकृतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Embodied.<BR>—2 Self-formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्
आकृष् €1 P., €6 U.<BR>—1 To draw towards, draw, drag, pull, attract (fig. also); केशेष्वाकृष्य<BR> चुम्बति H. 1. 109; दूरममुना सारङ्गेण वयमाकृष्टाः Ś. 1; (मनः)<BR> शम्भोर्यतध्वमाकष्टुमयस्कान्तेन लोहवत् Ku. 2. 59; अनाकृष्टस्य<BR> विषयैः R. 1. 23 not attracted or seduced; लोभाकृष्टः H. 1; Śānti. 3. 5, 4. 16;<BR> पादाकृष्टव्रतति Ś. 1. 32; Amaru. 1. 80.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">Page0308-1</a>]<BR>—2 To draw, or bend (as a bow); (अमुना) यदधर्मधाम्नि धनुराचकृषे<BR> Śi. 9. 40; Ś. 3. 5. (v. l.)<BR>—3 To draw or take out; हस्तात्कटकमाकृष्य Mk. 2; U. 1.<BR>—4 To extract, borrow (from another source); पञ्चतन्त्रात्तथान्यस्माद्<BR> ग्रन्थादाकृष्य लिख्यते H. Pr. 9.<BR>—5 To draw or carry along; to waft or be charged with; आकर्षद्भिः पद्मकिञ्जल्कगन्धान् U. 3. 2.<BR>—6 To deprive, take away by force, snatch; आकर्क्ष्यामि यशः Bk. 16. 30.<BR>—7 To supply a word or words from another rule or sentence. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To draw near to oneself, pull together; वस्त्रमाकर्षयन्ती Ṛs. 5. 11. (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0307-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षः|आकर्ष
आकर्षः<BR>—1 Attracting or drawing towards oneself.<BR>—2 Drawing away from, withdrawing; U. 3. 46. (v. l.)<BR>—3 Drawing (a bow).<BR>—4 Attraction, fascination.<BR>—5 Spasm.<BR>—6 Playing with dice; आकर्षस्तेऽवाक्फलः Mb.<BR>—7 A die or dice.<BR>—8 A board for a game with dice.<BR>—9 An organ of sense.<BR>—10 A magnet, a loadstone; यथा श्राम्यत्ययो ब्रह्मन् स्वयमाकर्षसन्निधौ<BR> Bhāg. 7. 5. 14.<BR>—11 A touch-stone.<BR>—12 A bow. cf. आकर्षः शारिफलके द्यूतेऽक्षे कार्मुकेऽपि च Nm.<BR>—13 A poisonous plant; Mb. 5. 40. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षक|आकर्षकः
आकर्षक <i>a.</i> attracting, attractive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षकः|आकर्षक
आकर्षक + .{@-कः@} A magnet, a loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आकर्षण <i>a.</i> Attracting, carrying to another place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षणम्
आकर्षण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Pulling, drawing, attracting.<BR>—2 Seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षणी
आकर्षण + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A curved stick for pulling down fruits, flowers &c. (standing on elevated<BR> places); any instrument for pulling.<BR>—2 A variety of Mudrā (or mark on the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिक
आकर्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Magnetic, attractive (आकर्षेण चरति). P. IV. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिन्
आकर्षिन् <i>a.</i> Attractive (as a smell at a distance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिणी
आकर्षिन् + .{@-णी@} A rod with a hook at the end for pulling down boughs in order<BR> to gather fruits &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्ट|आकृष्टं
आकृष्ट <i>a.</i> Attracted, pulled; नाकृष्टं न च टङ्कितं न नमितं<BR> नोत्थापितं स्थानतः Mahān.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टिः|आकृष्टि
आकृष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Attraction (in general).<BR>—2 Attraction, gravitation (in astr.); आकृष्टिशक्तिश्च मही तया यत्<BR> खस्थं गुरु स्वाभिमुखं स्वशक्त्या । आकृष्यते तत्पततीव भाति समे समन्तात्<BR> क्व पतत्वियं खे ॥ Golādh. 1.<BR>—3 Drawing or bending of a bow; ज्या˚ Amaru. 1.<BR>—4 (Tantric texts) Attracting an absent person by a magic formula.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आकृष्टिमन्त्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टिमन्त्रः|आकृष्टिमन्त्र
आकृष्टिः + -मन्त्रः an incantation by which another person is attracted;<BR> आकृष्टिमन्त्रोपमम् H. 1. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकॄ
आकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To scatter or spread over, fill, fill up, cover, heap up (used chiefly<BR> in <i>p. p.</i> q. v.) आ नः सोम पवमानः किरा Rv. 9. 81. 3. विचिन्वतीमाकिरन्तीम् Av. 4. 38. 2.<BR>—2 To dig up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिकः|आकरिक
आकरिकः [आकरे नियुक्तः ठञ्]<BR>—1 A person appointed (by the king) to superintend a mine.<BR>—2 A miner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिन्
आकरिन् <i>a.</i> [आकर-इनि]<BR>—1 Produced in a mine, mineral.<BR>—2 Of good breed; दधतमाकरिभिः करिभिः क्षतैः Ki. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्ण|आकीर्णं|आकीर्ण्ण
आकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered or spread over.<BR>—2 Filled or overspread with, crowded, full of, abounding in; जनाकीर्णं<BR> मन्ये हुतवहपरीतं गृहमिव Ś. 5. 10; आकीर्णमृषिपत्नीनामुटजद्वाररोधिभिः<BR> R. 1. 50; ग्राहाकीर्णं सरः Pt. 1. 375; (श्वभिः भिक्षुकैः) आकीर्णम् Ms. 6. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्णम्
आकीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} A crowd; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आके
आके <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Near in the neighbourhood; तमग्न ऋभुराके नमस्य Rv. 2. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकेकर
आकेकर <i>a.</i> Half-shut, half-closed (eyes); निमीलदाकेकरलोलचक्षुषा<BR> Ki. 8. 53; Māl. 5; K. 81; चिरमवतु हरेर्दृष्टिराकेकरा वः Mu. 3. 21<BR> दृष्टिराकेकरा किंचित्स्फुटापाङ्गे प्रसारिता । मीलितार्धपुटालोके<BR> ताराव्यावर्तनोत्तरा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकेनिप
आकेनिप <i>a.</i> Ved. Advancing near (as rays of light); wise (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकोकेरः|आकोकेर
आकोकेरः The sign Capricornus (मकर); (a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकोपः|आकोप
आकोपः A slight anger; Śi. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकौशलम्
आकौशलम् Inexpertness, want of skill; विवरीतुमथात्मनो गुणान् भृशमाकौशलमार्यचेतसाम् Śi. 16. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्द्|आक्रंद्
आक्रन्द् €1 U.<BR>—1 To lament, weep, cry, cry out, creak; scream; तृणाग्रलग्नैस्तुहिनैः<BR> पतद्भिराक्रन्दतीवोषसि शीतकालः Ṛs. 4. 7; Bk. 15. 50.<BR>—2 To shout, roar.<BR>—3 To invoke, call out to; आक्रन्दीद्भीमसेनं वै Mb. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to weep or cry.<BR>—2 To call out to; एह्येहीति शिखण्डिनां पटुतरैः केकाभिराक्रन्दितः Mk. 5. 23.<BR>—3 To inspire courage by the sound of a drum; आक्रन्दय बलमोजो न आ<BR> धा Rv. 6. 47. 30.<BR>—4 To shout or roar at; to cry incessantly. आक्रन्दय धनपते वरमामनसं<BR> कृणु Av. 2. 36. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दः|आक्रन्द|आक्रंदः
आक्रन्दः<BR>—1 Weeping, crying out; किं क्रन्दसि दुराक्रन्द Pt. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Calling, invoking, calling out to; आक्रन्दे चाप्यपैहीति न दण्डं मनुरब्रवीत् Ms. 8. 292.<BR>—3 Sound, war-cry, a cry (in general); आक्रन्द उदभूत्तत्र Ks. 10. 94.<BR>—4 A friend, defender; दष्टमेवमनाक्रन्दे भद्रे काममहाहिना Mb. 1. 172. 9.<BR>—5 A brother.<BR>—6 A fierce or violent combat, war, battle.<BR>—7 A place of crying.<BR>—8 A king who prevents an ally from aiding another; a king whose kingdom<BR> lies next but one. पार्ष्णिग्राहं च संप्रेक्ष्य तथाक्रन्द्रं च मण्डले<BR> Ms. 7. 207 (see Kull. thereon). cf. also Kau. A. 6. 2. cf. … आक्रन्दो<BR> दारुणे रणे । आरावे रोदने त्रातरि … । Nm. मित्रमाक्रन्दाभ्यां वा<BR> व्यापादयितुकामः Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दनम्
आक्रन्दनम्<BR>—1 Lamentation, weeping, cry of lamentation;<BR>—2 Calling out. आक्रन्दनया विलेपिरे Bhāg. 7. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दिक|आक्रंदिक
आक्रन्दिक <i>a.</i> [आक्रन्दं धावति ठञ् P. IV. 4. 38] one who runs<BR> to a place where cries (of distress) are heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दित|आक्रंदित
आक्रन्दित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Roaring, crying, or weeping bitterly.<BR>—2 Invoked, called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दितम्
आक्रन्दित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A cry, roar;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">Page0309-1</a>]<BR> तदीयमाक्रन्दितमार्तसाधोः R. 2. 28.<BR>—2 Lamentation, weeping, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0308-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दिन्|आक्रंदिन्
आक्रन्दिन् <i>a.</i> Calling out in a weeping tone, weeping, shouting at;<BR> परस्पराक्रन्दिनि चक्रवाकयोः Ku. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रम्
आक्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To go towards or near, approach; अन्तरिक्षम्, आश्रमम् &c.<BR>—2 To step or tread upon; आ वो मूर्धानमक्रमीम् Rv. 10. 166. 5; enter,<BR> fill, take possession of, cover, भुजगपतिरयं मे मार्गमाक्रम्य सुप्तः<BR> Mk. 9. 12 covering; खं केशवोऽपर इवाक्रमितुं प्रवृत्तः 5. 2; छायामप्याक्रमितुम्<BR> Ve. 3; Śi. 8. 28 to enter or cross; Ms. 4. 130; Y. 1. 152; पदा मस्तकमाक्रम्य<BR> Ms. 11. 43; जम्बुद्वीपमाक्रम्य H. 3; आक्रामति धूमो हर्म्यतलम् Mbh.<BR> and Kāśi. on P. I. 3. 40.<BR>—3 To occupy, extend over; योजनानां सहस्राणि बहूनाक्रम्य तिष्ठति Ks. 1. 15.<BR>—4 To attack, invade, seize, fall upon, conquer, overcome, vanquish; पक्षिशावकानाक्रम्य<BR> H. 1; सर्वस्वं ग्रसते बन्धुराक्रम्य ज्ञातिभावतः 2. 97; पौरस्त्यानेवमाक्रामंस्तांस्ताञ्जनपदाञ्जयी<BR> R. 4. 34; H. 4; तं न … शेकुराक्रमितुमन्यपार्थिवाः R. 19. 48; Śi. 1. 70.<BR>—5 To surpass, excel, eclipse.<BR>—6 To undertake, begin, commence.<BR>—7 (Ā.) To rise, come up (as the sun); यावत्प्रतापनिधिराक्रमते न<BR> भानुः R. 5. 71, आक्रमते सूर्यः Mbh. on P. I. 3. 40.<BR>—8 To ascend, mount, occupy (as sky, throne &c.); अजो नाक्रमा क्रमतां<BR> तृतीयम् Av. 9. 5. 1. दिवमाक्रममाणेव Bk. 8. 23; Śi. 18. 14, 51;<BR> सिंहासनम्˚, खर्गलोकम्˚; ध्वजम्˚ &c.<BR>—9 to lie heavily upon, to press (as a load). (For further illustrations<BR> of the several senses see आकान्त below). ━<i>Caus.</i> (क्र(क्रा)मयति)<BR> To cause to enter, introduce, show into; स तैराक्रमयामास शुद्धान्तम् Ku. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमः|आक्रम
आक्रमः, -मणम्<BR>—1 Coming near, approaching.<BR>—2 Falling upon, attacking; an attack; हरिराक्रमणेन संनतिं किल<BR> बिभ्रीत भियेत्यसंभवः Śi. 16. 34.<BR>—3 Seizing, taking, covering, occupying.<BR>—4 Overcoming; obtaining. Vāj. 15. 9.<BR>—5 Spreading or going over, surpassing.<BR>—6 Mounting overloading. Bhāg. 7. 5. 44.<BR>—7 Might, valour.<BR>—8 Possession of learning &c.<BR>—9 Food.<BR>—10 A step for ascending; केनाक्रमेण यजमानः खर्गं लोकमाक्रमते<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमणम्
आक्रमः, -मणम्<BR>—1 Coming near, approaching.<BR>—2 Falling upon, attacking; an attack; हरिराक्रमणेन संनतिं किल<BR> बिभ्रीत भियेत्यसंभवः Śi. 16. 34.<BR>—3 Seizing, taking, covering, occupying.<BR>—4 Overcoming; obtaining. Vāj. 15. 9.<BR>—5 Spreading or going over, surpassing.<BR>—6 Mounting overloading. Bhāg. 7. 5. 44.<BR>—7 Might, valour.<BR>—8 Possession of learning &c.<BR>—9 Food.<BR>—10 A step for ascending; केनाक्रमेण यजमानः खर्गं लोकमाक्रमते<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्त|आक्रांत|आक्रान्तः
आक्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seized, taken possession of, overpowered, defeated, vanquished, overcome;<BR> आक्रान्तविमानमार्गम् R. 13. 37 reaching upto; रुजा˚ Pt. 5. 52;<BR> दिदृक्षा˚ हृदयः Dk. 141 seized with; आतपाक्रान्तोऽयमुद्देशः M. 3<BR> exposed to heat; आक्रान्तपूर्वमिव भुजङ्गम् R. 9. 79 trodden or trampled<BR> under foot; filled with, full of, occupied, covered, overspread; शुशुभे<BR> तेन चाक्रान्तं मङ्गलायतनं महत् R. 17. 29; Bh. 2. 108; बलिभिर्मुखमाक्रान्तम्<BR> Bh. 3. 14, 62; U. 2. 20; Mv. 5. 40; Śi. 1. 70; H. 1. 22; Dk. 141; K. 55;<BR> Ve. 2. 27; ˚मति having the mind engrossed or occupied; U. 5. 19;<BR> Māl. 9. 49; so मदन˚, भय˚, शोक˚ &c.<BR>—2 Loaded (as with a burden); pressed by; शैलाक्रान्तेन यो मुक्तस्तस्यारावः<BR> सुदारुणः Rām. 7. 16. 36. भाराक्रान्ता वसुन्धरा Mk. 8. 6; K. 118;<BR> साक्रान्ता जघनस्थलेन गुरुणा गन्तुं न शक्ता Amaru. 34.<BR>—3 Surpassed, eclipsed, superseded;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">Page0309-2</a>]<BR> R. 10. 38; Ve. 5, आक्रान्ता तिलकक्रियापि तिलकैः M. 3. 5.<BR>—4 Obtained, possessed of; वर्णान्तराक्रान्तपयोधराग्राम् R. 14. 27; Ki. 11. 7.<BR>—5 Accompanied, attended.<BR>—6 Pained, distressed.<BR>—7 Graced, adorned, decorated; न खलु नरके हाराक्रान्तं घनस्तनमण्डलम्<BR> (शरणम्) Bh. 1. 67.<BR>—8 Seated, ridden; निर्ययुस्तुरगाक्रान्ताः Rām. 6. 127. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आक्रान्तनायका, आक्रान्तमति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्तनायका
आक्रान्त + -नायका (In drama) One whose lover is won or kept in obedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्तमति
आक्रान्त + -मति <i>a.</i> Mentally overcome, deeply impressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्तिः|आक्रान्ति|आक्रांतिः
आक्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Placing upon, occupying; stepping or treading upon; आक्रान्तिसम्भावितपादपीठम् Ku. 3. 11.<BR>—2 Overcoming, pressing upon, loading; पृथुजघनभराक्रान्तिमन्दैः प्रयातैः Mu. 3. 10.<BR>—3 Ascending, rising,<BR>—4 Might, valour, force; {@˚तः@} <i>ind.</i> From violence; आक्रान्तितो<BR> न वशमेति महान्परस्य Śi. 5. 41.<BR>—5 Assault, taking away (अपहार); यो भूतानि धनाक्रान्त्या वधात्क्लेशाच्च<BR> रक्षति Mb. 12. 97. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रामकः|आक्रामक
आक्रामकः An invader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्री
आक्री €9 U. To purchase, buy; obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रयः|आक्रय
आक्रयः<BR>—1 A dealer, petty trader, a pedlar.<BR>—2 Trade, Commerce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड्
आक्रीड् €1 U. To play, sport, amuse oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड|आक्रीडः
आक्रीड <i>a.</i> Playing, sporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडः|आक्रीड
आक्रीड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 Play, sport, pleasure; गजेन्द्राक्रीडमथिता Rām. 7. 26. 42.<BR>—2 A pleasure-grove, pleasure-garden; (पुमानाक्रीड उद्यानम् । Ak.);<BR> देवाकीडशताकीर्णाम् Rām. 2. 50. 15. कमप्याक्रीडमासाद्य तत्र विशश्रमिषुः<BR> Dk. 12. कुबेरस्यापि चाक्रीडं प्रागेव वसुधामिमाम् Bu. C. 4. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आक्रीडगिरिः, आक्रीडपर्वतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडम्
आक्रीड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 Play, sport, pleasure; गजेन्द्राक्रीडमथिता Rām. 7. 26. 42.<BR>—2 A pleasure-grove, pleasure-garden; (पुमानाक्रीड उद्यानम् । Ak.);<BR> देवाकीडशताकीर्णाम् Rām. 2. 50. 15. कमप्याक्रीडमासाद्य तत्र विशश्रमिषुः<BR> Dk. 12. कुबेरस्यापि चाक्रीडं प्रागेव वसुधामिमाम् Bu. C. 4. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आक्रीडगिरिः, आक्रीडपर्वतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडगिरिः|आक्रीडगिरि
आक्रीड + -गिरिः, -पर्वतः A pleasure-hill; आक्रीडपर्वतास्तेन कल्पिताः<BR> खेषु वेश्ममु Ku. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडपर्वतः|आक्रीडपर्वत
आक्रीड + -गिरिः, -पर्वतः A pleasure-hill; आक्रीडपर्वतास्तेन कल्पिताः<BR> खेषु वेश्ममु Ku. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडनम्
आक्रीडनम् Sporting, playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडिन्
आक्रीडिन् <i>a.</i> Playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुश्
आक्रुश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To cry, cry out loudly; अये गौरीनाथ त्रिपुरहर शम्भो त्रिनयन<BR> प्रसीदेत्याक्रोशन् Bh. 3. 123; call out loudly to; पतिमाचुक्रुशुः Rām.<BR>—2 To revile, abuse, scold, assail with angry words; परस्य हेतोर्नामाक्रोशसि<BR> Dk. 58, 97; शतं ब्राह्मणमाक्रुश्य क्षत्रियो दण्डमर्हति Ms. 8. 267; Bk. 5. 39.<BR>—3 To curse.<BR>—4 To censure, express displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुष्ट
आक्रुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scolded, reviled, censured, abused, calumniated &c.; क्रुध्यन्तं न<BR> प्रतिक्रुध्येदाक्रुष्टः कुशलं वदेत् Ms. 6. 48; Śi. 12. 27.<BR>—2 Sounded, vociferated.<BR>—3 Cursed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुष्टम्
आक्रुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Calling out.<BR>—2 A harsh cry or sound, an abusive speech (परुषभाषणम्); मार्जारमूषिकास्पर्शे<BR> आक्रुष्टे क्रोधसंभवे Kāty.; प्रपातजलनिर्घोषैः प्राक्रुष्टमिव सर्वतः<BR> Rām. 5. 56. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशः|आक्रोश
आक्रोशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Calling or crying out, vociferation, loud cry or sound.<BR>—2 Censure, blame, reviling; आक्रोशमपि परिहासमाकलयन्ति K. 235, 291;<BR> abuse Y. 2. 302.<BR>—3 A curse, imprecation; ˚गर्भमेवमुक्तम् K. 291, 346.<BR>—4 An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशनम्
आक्रोशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Calling or crying out, vociferation, loud cry or sound.<BR>—2 Censure, blame, reviling; आक्रोशमपि परिहासमाकलयन्ति K. 235, 291;<BR> abuse Y. 2. 302.<BR>—3 A curse, imprecation; ˚गर्भमेवमुक्तम् K. 291, 346.<BR>—4 An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशकः|आक्रोशक
आक्रोशकः, -क्रोष्टॄ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vociferous, one who calls out or vociferates.<BR>—2 A reviler, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोष्टॄ
आक्रोशकः, -क्रोष्टॄ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vociferous, one who calls out or vociferates.<BR>—2 A reviler, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0309-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्लिन्न
आक्लिन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wet.<BR>—2 Touched with pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ली
आक्ली <i>ind.</i> An indeclinable joined to the roots, कृ, भू and<BR> अस्; see ऊर्यादि Gaṇa on P. I. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्लेदः|आक्लेद
आक्लेदः Moistening, wetting, sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षद्यूतिक
आक्षद्यूतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अक्षद्यूतेन निर्वृत्तम् ठक्] Effected or completed by gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपटलिकः|आक्षपटलिक
आक्षपटलिकः<BR>—1 A keeper of archives or records.<BR>—2 An officer of accounts. आक्षपटले गाणनिक्याधिकारः Kau. A. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपणम्
आक्षपणम् Fasting, purifying by fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाटिकः|आक्षपाटिक
आक्षपाटिकः [अक्षपट-ठक्]<BR>—1 A judge at playing with dice, superintendent of a gambling house;<BR>—2 A judge, arranger^1 of law suits; see अक्षपाटक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाद|आक्षपादः
आक्षपाद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अक्षपाद-अण्] Taught by Akṣapāda or Gautama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपादः|आक्षपाद
आक्षपाद + .{@-दः@} A follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy, a logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपादम्
आक्षपाद + .{@-दम्@} The Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षर्
आक्षर् €10 P.<BR>—1 To abuse, revile, accuse falsely, calumniate; मातरं पितरं जायां<BR> भ्रातरं तनयं गुरुम् आक्षारयन् Ms. 8. 275.<BR>—2 To punish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षरसमाम्नायिक
आक्षरसमाम्नायिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारः|आक्षार
आक्षारः<BR>—1 A charge or calumny, accusation (of adultery).<BR>—2 N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारणम्
आक्षारणम्, -णा<BR> Calumnious accusation (especially of adultery); तत्र त्वाक्षारणा<BR> यः स्यादाक्रोशो मैथुनं प्रति Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारणा
आक्षारणम्, -णा<BR> Calumnious accusation (especially of adultery); तत्र त्वाक्षारणा<BR> यः स्यादाक्रोशो मैथुनं प्रति Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारित|आक्षारितं
आक्षारित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Calumniated.<BR>—2 Accused of adultery or fornication यस्त्वनाक्षारितः पूर्वम् Ms. 8. 355, 354.<BR>—3 Guilty, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षि
आक्षि €2. €6 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To abide, dwell in, stay (with).<BR>—2 To be or exist. य अन्नं भुवस्पत आक्षियति पृथिवीमनु Av. 10. 5. 45.<BR>—3 To possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षित्
आक्षित् <i>a.</i> Abiding, dwelling. आक्षित् पूर्वास्वपरा अनूरुत् Rv. 3. 55. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिक|आक्षिकः
आक्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अक्षेण दीव्यति जयति जितं वा; अक्ष ठक् P. IV. 4. 2.]<BR>—1 One who plays at dice.<BR>—2 One who uses loaded dice. (भारभूतानक्षानाहरति, वहति).<BR>—3 One who gains by gambling.<BR>—4 Won by gambling.<BR>—5 Relating to dice or gambling; आक्षिकम् ऋणम् Ms. 8. 159 incurred in gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकः|आक्षिक
आक्षिक + .{@-कः@} N. of a tree (= अक्षिक q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकम्
आक्षिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Money gained by gambling.<BR>—2 Gambling debt, money lost at play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकी
आक्षिक + .{@-की@} <i>f.</i> A kind of spirituous liquor prepared from the seeds<BR> of Teroninabia Bellerica (बिभीतक; Mar. बेहडा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आक्षिकपणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकपणः|आक्षिकपण
आक्षिक + -पणः a stake, a wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्
आक्षिप् €6 U.<BR>—1 To throw or cast down, dash down; फलं तरङ्गाक्षिप्तम् Pt. 4; शिलायामाक्षिप्य. Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To attract, entice, allure, win over; यथा नाक्षिप्यसे विषयैः K. 109;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-2" target="_blank">Page0310-2</a>]<BR> Śi. 10. 79<BR>—3 To strike with a dart, missile &c.<BR>—4 To draw near or together, contract, convulse (used in medicine).<BR>—5 To interrput, cut short, एवंवादिनो वचनमाक्षिप्य K. 18, 207; Ve. 6.<BR>—6 To draw back or withdraw; take or throw off, snatch or draw away, pull<BR> off; अग्रपादमाक्षिप्य R. 7. 7; Ku. 7. 58 वासो बलादाक्षिपन् Bh. 1. 43; Me. 70.<BR>—7 To chase, drive out of a place, remove; स एतानाक्षिपद्राष्ट्रात् Mb.;<BR> आक्षिप्ताधिकारयोः Mu. 1.<BR>—8 To hang out, expose to view (as a banner).<BR>—9 To point to, refer to, hint at, indicate; वस्तुतस्तु नेह पूर्वपदमाक्षिप्यते<BR> P. VI. 3. 34. Sk.; अश्वादय आक्षिप्यन्ते S. D. 2.<BR>—10 To reject, neglect, disregard, spurn; Amaru. 85.<BR>—11 To object to (as argument).<BR>—12 To insult; अरेरे राधागर्भभारभूत किमेवमाक्षिपसि Ve. 3; to<BR> blame; Śānti. 1. 18.<BR>—13 To eclipse, obscure; आक्षिपन्तीमिव प्रभां शशिनः स्वेन तेजसा Mb.<BR>—14 To infer (from circumstance); जात्या व्यक्तिराक्षिप्यते K. P. 2.<BR>—15 To say or state ironically.<BR>—16 To pass (as time); याचिनस्तु न च कालमाक्षिपत् Śi. 14. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्त
आक्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cast, thrown down.<BR>—2 Overthrown, repulsed; आक्षिप्तो जयकुञ्जरेण तुरगान् Ratn. 4. 12.<BR>—3 Seized, grasped, snatched away; V. 5. 5.<BR>—4 Drawn, attracted, overpowered; कौतुक˚, कुतूहल˚ U. 4; seduced,<BR> enticed; K. 281. मन्मथाक्षिप्तचेतसः Bu. C. 4. 3.<BR>—5 Perplexed, distracted, bewildered; ˚मिव मे चेतः Ve. 2.<BR>—6 Insulted, reviled, abused.<BR>—7 Equal or equivalent to.<BR>—8 Interpolated, inserted, see प्रक्षिप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्तिका
आक्षिप्तिका A particular air or song sung by a character while approaching<BR> the stage; [चञ्चत्पुटादितालेन मार्गत्रयविभूषिता । आक्षिप्तिका स्वरपदग्रथिता<BR> कथिता बुधैः (भरतनाट्यशास्त्र)]; प्रावेशिकी आक्षिप्तिका V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपः|आक्षेप
आक्षेपः<BR>—1 Throwing off, tossing, pulling off, snatching away; अंशुकाक्षेपविलज्जितानाम्<BR> Ku. 1. 14; withdrawing; वदनमपहरन्तीं तत्कृताक्षेपमीशः Ku. 7. 95;<BR> movement, shaking; K. 13.<BR>—2 Reviling, censure, blame, abuse, reproach, defiant censure; इति ब्रह्मोदिताक्षेपैः<BR> स्थानादिन्द्रः प्रचालितः Bhāg. 12. 6. 22. ˚प्रचण्डतया U. 5. 28;<BR> बिरुद्धमाक्षेपवचस्तितिक्षितम् Ki. 14. 25; Bh. 2. 69.<BR>—3 Drawing together, attraction, diverting; कथारसस्याक्षेपसामर्थ्यम्<BR> K. 346, 348 power to interest<BR>—4 Distraction, allurement; विषयाक्षेपपर्यस्तबुद्धेः Bh. 3. 47, 23.<BR>—5 Throwing away, giving up.<BR>—6 Applying, laying on, putting in or into (as a colour); गोरोचनाक्षेपनितान्तगौरैः Ku. 7. 17.<BR>—7 Hinting at, reference to, taking to oneself or assuming as the meaning<BR> of another word; स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः K. P. 2.<BR>—8 An inference.<BR>—9 A deposit.<BR>—10 An objection or doubt.<BR>—11 Convulsion, palpitation.<BR>—12 Sustaining, as a sound.<BR>—13 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech (cf. Greek paralipsis) in which something<BR> really intended to be said is apparently suppressed or denied to convey<BR> a particular meaning; आक्षेपः स्वयमुक्तस्य प्रतिषेधो विचारणात् । चन्द्रसंदर्शयात्मानमथवास्ति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">Page0311-1</a>]<BR> प्रियामुखम् ॥ Kuval. For fuller definitions and explanations see K. P. 10,<BR> S. D. 714 and <i>Akṣepaprakaraṇa</i> in R. G.<BR>—14 Reach (of an arrow); सोऽयं प्राप्तस्तवाक्षेपम् Mb. 7. 102. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आक्षेपरूपकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0310-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपरूपकम्
आक्षेपः + -रूपकम् A simile in which the object compared is only hinted at; Kāv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपक|आक्षेपकः
आक्षेपक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drawing; drawing or snatching off.<BR>—2 Censuring, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपकः|आक्षेपक
आक्षेपक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A thrower.<BR>—2 A detractor, calumniator, accuser.<BR>—3 A hunter.<BR>—4 (In medic.) Convulsion, spasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपणम्
आक्षेपणम् Throwing, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपिन्
आक्षेपिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drawing or snatching up; इमामाक्षेपिणीं सिद्धिमातनोमि शिवाय वः Māl. 9. 51.v<BR>—2 Drawing in with a minute eye; बाह्याभ्यन्तरविषयाक्षेपी चतुर्थः Pātañjala S.<BR>—3 Applying to, regarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीब|आक्षीबः
आक्षीब <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Somewhat drunk.<BR>—2 Intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीबः|आक्षीब
आक्षीब + .{@-बः@} = अक्षीव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीलम्
आक्षीलम् N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यम्
आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यम् [अक्ष्वेत्रज्ञ-ष्यञ्] Spiritual ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोटः|आक्षोट
आक्षोटः, -डः<BR> A walnut; see अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोडः|आक्षोड
आक्षोटः, -डः<BR> A walnut; see अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोदनम्
आक्षोदनम् Hunting (for आच्छोदनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ष्यत्|आक्ष्यन्त्
आक्ष्यत् <i>a.</i> (fr. अश् or अक्ष्) Leading to completion (as days),<BR> epithet of certain days on which the ceremony Ayana performed for the<BR> Ādityas and Aṅgirasas is finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण
आखण <i>a.</i> Hard (to dig up) (as a stone); यथाश्मानमाखणमृत्वा<BR> विध्वंसते Ch. Up. 1. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डलः|आखण्डल|आखंडलः
आखण्डलः [आखण्डयति भेदयति पर्वतान्, खण्ड्-डलच् डस्य नेत्वम्<BR> Tv.] Indra; आखण्डलः काममिदं बभाषे Ku. 3. 11; तमीशः कामरूपाणामत्याखण्डलविक्रमम्<BR> R. 4. 83; Me. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आखण्डलचापः, आखण्डलधनुः, आखण्डलसूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डलचापः|आखण्डलचाप
आखण्डलः + -चापः, -धनुः <i>n.</i> The rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डलधनुः
आखण्डलः + -चापः, -धनुः <i>n.</i> The rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डलसूनुः|आखण्डलसूनु
आखण्डलः + -सूनुः The son of Indra <i>i. e.</i> Arjuna<BR> … अनुस्मृताखण्डलसूनुविकमः Ki. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डिः|आखण्डि
आखण्डिः <i>m.</i> N. of an artisan.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आखण्डिशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डिशाला
आखण्डिः + -शाला The workshop of the artisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखः|आख
आखः, [आखन्-ड], आखनः [खन्-घ P. III. 3. 125]<BR> A spade, hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनः|आखन
आखः, [आखन्-ड], आखनः [खन्-घ P. III. 3. 125]<BR> A spade, hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकः|आखनिक
आखनिकः [आ-खन्-इक]<BR>—1 A digger, ditcher, miner.<BR>—2 A mouse or rat.<BR>—3 A hog.<BR>—4 A thief.<BR>—5 A spade. भवेदाखनिकश्चोरे शूकरे मूषिकेऽपि च Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकबकः|आखनिकबक
आखनिकबकः [आ-खन्-करणे कर्तरि वा इकबक P. Mbh. on P. III. 3. 125]<BR>—1 A stork in relation to a mouse; (fig.) a man who behaves like a hero<BR> towards a weak person.<BR>—2 = आखनिक q. v. above (= खनित्रम् Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखरः|आखर
आखरः [आखन्-डर]<BR>—1 A spade.<BR>—2 A digger, miner.<BR>—3 A cover of any animal; a stable; यथाऽऽखरो मघवंश्चारुरेष प्रियो<BR> मृगाणां सुषदा बभूव Av. 2. 36. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखाटीश्वरतीर्थम्
आखाटीश्वरतीर्थम् N. of तीर्थ; Śiva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखातः|आखात|आखातं
आखातः, -तम्<BR> A natural pond or pool of water, bay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखातम्
आखातः, -तम्<BR> A natural pond or pool of water, bay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखानः|आखान
आखानः [आ-खन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Digging all around<BR>—2 A spade, a digger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुः|आखु
आखुः [आखनतीत्याखुः, आखन्-कुः डिच्च Uṇ. 1. 33]<BR>—1 A mouse, rat, mole; आखुं चिदेव देव सोम Rv. 9. 67. 30. अत्तुं<BR> वाञ्छति शाम्भवो गणपतेराखुं क्षुधार्तः फणी Pt. 1. 159.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR>—3 A hog. cf. पोत्रिमूषिकयोराखुः Nm.<BR>—4 A spade.<BR>—5 A miser; विभवे सति नैवात्ति न ददाति जुहोति न । तमाहुराखुम्.<BR>—6 The grass Lipeocercis Serrata (देवताड).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आखूत्करः, आखूत्थ, आखुकरीषम्, आखुकर्णपर्णिका, आखुपार्णिका, आखुकर्णी, आखुपर्णी, आखुगः, आखुपत्रः, आखुरथः, आखुवाहनः, आखुघातः, आखुपाषाणः, आखुफला, आखुभुज्, आखुभुजः, आखुविषहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखूत्करः|आखूत्कर
आखुः + -उत्करः a mole-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखूत्थ|आखूत्थः
आखुः + -उत्थ <i>a.</i> produced from a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

