आखेटक|आखेटकः
आखेटक <i>a.</i> Hunting, frightening (as beasts of prey &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटकः|आखेटक
आखेटक + .{@-कः@} A hunter; आखेटकस्य धर्मेण विभवाः स्युर्वशे नृणाम् Pt. 1. 129, 388.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटकम्
आखेटक + .{@-कम्@} Hunting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आखेटकाटवी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटकाटवी
आखेटक + -अटवी <i>f.</i> A hunting forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिक|आखेटिकः
आखेटिक <i>a.</i> [आखेटे कुशलः ठक्]<BR>—1 Skilful in chase.<BR>—2 Terrible, frightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिकः|आखेटिक
आखेटिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A hunter.<BR>—2 A hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखोटः|आखोट
आखोटः The walnut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या €2 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To tell, say, inform, communicate, narrate (usually with dat.<BR> of person); इमानि शुक्लानि यजूंषि वाजसनेयेन याज्ञवल्क्येनाख्यायन्ते<BR> Bṛ. Up. 6. 5. 3. ते रामाय वधोपायमाचख्युर्विबुधद्विषः R. 15. 5, 41, 71, 93, 12. 42, 91;<BR> आख्याहि मे को भवानुग्ररूपो Bg. 11. 31, 18. 63;<BR> Me. 100; Ms. 8. 224, 9. 73; Y. 1. 66, 2. 65; sometimes with gen. of<BR> person; आख्याहि भद्रे प्रियदर्शनस्य Pt. 4. 15; केनाहं तवाख्यातः Mb.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To declare, announce, signify; धनुर्भृतोऽप्यस्य दयार्द्रभावमाख्यातम् R. 2. 11.<BR>—2 To call, denominate, name; सुवर्णबिन्दुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9; R. 10. 21,<BR> Ms. 4. 6.<BR>—3 To look at, count; to recite (Ved.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (ख्यापयति)<BR>—1 To cause to tell or narrate.<BR>—2 To declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्य
आख्य <i>a.</i> A narrator; संपतन्ति च मे शिष्याः प्रबृत्ताख्याः पुरीमितः<BR> Rām. 6. 124. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या [आ-ख्यायते अनया; आख्या-अङ् P. III. 3. 106]<BR>—1 A name, appellation; किं वा शकुन्तलेत्यस्य मातुराख्या Ś. 7, 7. 33;<BR> पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी जगाम Ku. 1. 26; तपाख्यया भुवि पप्रथे<BR> R. 15. 101 become known by that name; often at the end of compounds meaning ‘named’ or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">Page0312-1</a>]<BR> ‘called’; अथ किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः सा धर्मपत्नी Ś. 7; रघुवंशाख्यं काव्यम् &c.<BR>—2 Appearance, aspect; न हि तस्य विकल्पाख्या या च मद्वीक्षया हता<BR> Bhāg. 11. 18. 37.<BR>—3 Beauty, splendour; वृसीषु रुचिराख्यासु निषेदुः काञ्चनीषु ते Rām. 7. 60. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0311-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आख्यात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Said, told, declared; इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातम् Bg. 18. 63.<BR>—2 Counted, recited.<BR>—3 Made known.<BR>—4 Inflected or conjugated.<BR>—5 Called; सेवा श्ववृत्तिराख्याता Ms. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातम्
आख्यात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A verb; भावप्रधानमाख्यातम् Nir.; धात्वर्थेन विशिष्टस्य विधेयत्वेन<BR> बोधने । समर्थः स्वार्थयत्नस्य शब्दो वाऽऽख्यातमुच्यते ॥<BR>—2 Telling auspicious time for departure; (अभिमन्त्रितदुन्दुभिध्वनिना<BR> प्रयाणादिकथनम्); तथाख्यातविधानं च योगः संचार एव च Mb. 12. 59. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातिक
आख्यातिक <i>a.</i> Verbal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातिकी
आख्यातिक + .{@-की@} Com. on Jaina and Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातिः|आख्याति
आख्यातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Telling, informing, communication, publication (of a report &c.)<BR>—2 Fame.<BR>—3 A name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातृ
आख्यातृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who tells, communicates &c.<BR>—2 A teacher, instructor; P. I. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानम्
आख्यानम्<BR>—1 Speaking, declaration, making known, relation, communication; इत्थंभूताख्याने<BR> P. I. 4. 90. रामसंदेश˚ Rām.<BR>—2 Allusion to some old tale; आख्यानं पूर्ववृत्तोक्तिः S. D.; (<i>e. g.</i><BR> देशः सोऽयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन्ह्रदाः पूरिता Ve. 3. 33.).<BR>—3 A tale, story; especially a legendary story, legend; अप्सराः पुरूरवसं<BR> चकम इत्याख्यानविद आचक्षते Māl. 2; Ms. 3. 232.<BR>—4 A legendary work such as the Mahābhārata; योऽधीते चतुरो वेदान्सर्वानाख्यानपञ्चमान् Mb. 3. 58. 9.<BR>—5 A reply; प्रश्नाख्यानयोः P. VIII. 2. 105, III. 3. 110.<BR>—6 A differentiating property (भेदकधर्म).<BR>—7 A canto of an epic poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानकम्
आख्यानकम् A tale, a short legendary narrative, an episode; आख्यानकाख्यायिकेतिहासपुराणाकर्णनेन<BR> K. 7; P. IV. 2. 60. Vārt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानकी
आख्यानकम् + .{@-की@} N. of a metre which is a combination of Indravajrā and Upendravajrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आख्यायक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Telling, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायकः|आख्यायक
आख्यायक + .{@-कः@} A messenger, courier; आख्यायकेभ्यः श्रुतसूनुवृत्तिः Bk. 2. 44.<BR>—2 A herald; U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिका
आख्यायिका<BR>—1 A species of prose composition, a connected story or narrative; आख्यायिका<BR> कथावत् स्यात् कवेर्वंशादिकीर्तनम् । अस्यामन्यकवीनां च वृत्तं गद्यं<BR> क्वचित् क्वचित् । कथांशानां व्यवच्छेद आश्वास इति बध्यते । आर्यावक्त्रापवक्त्राणां<BR> छन्दसां येन केनचित् ॥ अन्यापदेशेनाश्वासमुखे भाव्यर्थसूचनम् । S. D. 568.<BR> Writers on Rhetoric usually divide prose composition into कथा<BR> and आख्यायिका and make a distinction between them. Thus they regard<BR> Bāṇaʼs हर्षचरित as an आख्यायिका and कादंबरी as a कथा;<BR> according to Daṇḍin, however, (Kāv. 1. 28) there is no distinction<BR> between the two; तत्कथाख्यायिकेत्येका जातिः संज्ञाद्वयाङ्किता<BR>—2 Narration (of what is known).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिन्
आख्यायिन् <i>a.</i> One who tells, informs, or communicates; रहस्याख्यायीव<BR> स्वनसि मृदु कर्णान्तिकचरः Ś. 1. 23; Ms. 7. 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आख्येय <i>pot. p.</i> Fit to be communicated or told; शब्द˚ fit<BR> to be told in words, verbal message; शब्दाख्येयं यदपि किल ते यः<BR> सखीनां पुरस्तात् Me. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्
आगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To come, come near, approach.<BR>—2 To arrive at, attain, reach; fall into (a particular state or condition);<BR> आनृण्यमागम् to become free from debt; so विश्वासम्˚, ध्यानम्˚ &c.<BR>—3 To have recourse to. ━<i>Caus.</i> (-गमयति)<BR>—1 To cause to come or draw near; तं त्वमा गमयागमे Av. 6. 81. 2.<BR>—2 To lead towards, take, convey; आगमितापि विदूरम् Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 To announce the arrival of; राजानमागमयति = राजागमनमाचष्टे Sk.<BR>—4 To ascertain, inform oneself about; सर्वमागमयामास पाण्डवानां<BR> विचेष्टितम् Mb. 5. 7. 4. प्रज्ञामेवागमयति यः प्राज्ञेभ्यः स पंडितः Vop.<BR>—5 To learn, acquire, study; सम्यगागमिता विद्या प्रबोधविनयाविव<BR> R. 10. 71; तदप्यागमितं मया Mb.; आगमय दण्डनीतिं कुलविद्याम्<BR> Dk. 155; Mv. 5; Śi. 9. 79.<BR>—6 (Ātm.) To wait for, have patience; आगमयस्व तावत् = क्षमस्व<BR> Sk. आगमयते कालम् Vop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग|आगः
आग <i>a.</i> Accidental, sudden; ˚त्वम् accident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Come, arrived; मम साधर्म्यमागताः Bg. 14. 2.<BR>—2 Occurred, happened. विज्ञाप्यं तु ममैतद्धि यद्वदाम्यागतस्पृहः<BR> Rām. 7. 36. 54; Ms. 2. 152.<BR>—3 Obtained, got; न्यायागतधनम् Y. 3. 205; ˚साध्वस afraid; ˚क्षोभ<BR> perplexed; अन्वय˚ hereditary; ˚मन्यु angry; ˚विस्मय surprised.<BR>—4 Reduced to, fallen into (a particular state); दासत्वम्, पञ्चत्वम्,<BR> संदेहम्, विस्मयम् &c.<BR>—5 Living or residing in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगतम्
आगत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Coming, arrival; कथं नु खल्वद्य भवेत्सुगतम् Rām. 5. 41. 8; Bg. 9. 21.<BR>—2 Occurrence, event.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगतत्वम्, आगतसाध्वस<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगतत्वम्
आगत + -त्वम् Origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगतसाध्वस
आगत + -साध्वस <i>a.</i> Terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगतिः|आगति
आगतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Arrival, coming; rise, origination; लोकस्यास्य गतागतिम् Rām. 2. 110. 1;<BR> इति निश्चितप्रियतमागतयः Śi. 9. 43.<BR>—2 Obtaining, acquisition; Y. 3. 170.<BR>—3 Return.<BR>—4 Origin.<BR>—5 Accident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तव्य|आगंतव्य
आगन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i> Likely to come, to be arrived; coming necessarily.<BR> आगन्तव्यं झटिति मथुरामण्डलाद् गोपकान्ते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आगन्तु <i>a.</i> [आ-गम्-तुन्]<BR>—1 Coming, arriving.<BR>—2 Stray.<BR>—3 Coming from the outside; external (as a cause &c.)<BR>—4 Adventitious, accidental, casual नियमस्तु स यत्कर्म नित्यमागन्तुसाधनम्<BR> Ak. 5 what (or who) comes later or afterwards. वास्तव्यैराकान्ते देशे<BR> आगन्तुर्जनोऽसम्भवादन्ते निविशते । ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुः|आगन्तु|आगंतु
आगन्तु + .{@-न्तुः@}<BR>—1 A newcomer, stranger, guest; (मेने) वैदर्भमागन्तुमजं गृहेशम्<BR> R. 5. 62; H. 1.<BR>—2 A late-comer, what comes later or afterwards (See आगमः for quotation)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगन्तुज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुज
आगन्तु + -ज <i>a.</i> arising accidentally or casually; आगन्तुजे रोगे Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक <i>a.</i> (-का, -की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Coming of oneʼs own accord, arriving uninvited; आगन्तुका वयम् Dhūrt.<BR>—2 Stray (as an animal); Y. 2. 163.<BR>—3 Incidental, accidental, adventitious; इत्यागन्तुका विकाराः <i>Aśval.</i><BR>—4 Interpolated, spurious (as a reading), having crept in without authority;<BR> अगन्धवद्गन्धमादनमित्यागन्तुकः पाठः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">Page0313-1</a>]<BR> Malli. on Ku. 6. 46.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगन्तुकज्वरः, आगन्तुकज्वरकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0312-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुकज्वरः
आगन्तुक + -ज्वरः A kind of fever<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुकज्वरकः
आगन्तुक + -ज्वरकः<BR>—1 An intruder, interpoler.<BR>—2 A stranger, guest, new-comer; Ś. 4, 6.<BR>—3 Interpolated reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमः|आगम|आगमं
आगमः<BR>—1 Coming, arrival, approach, appearance; लतायां पूर्वलूनायां प्रसूनस्यागमः<BR> कुतः U. 5. 20; Śi. 1. 30; अव्यक्ताद् व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे ।<BR> रात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते Bg. 8. 18; R. 14. 80; Pt. 3. 48; Ms. 8. 401;<BR> so व्यसन˚, अन्धकार˚ &c.<BR>—2 Acquisition; एषोऽस्या मुद्राया आगमः Mu. 1; Ś. 6 this is how I<BR> came by this ring; Dk. 139; वेदानामागमः K. 18; विद्यागमनिमित्तम् V. 5.<BR>—3 Birth, origin, source; आगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत<BR> Bg. 2. 14 coming and going, of short birth or duration, transient; आगमः<BR> काव्यामृतरसानाम् K. 5.<BR>—4 Addition, accumulation, acquisition (of wealth); अर्थ˚, धन˚ &c.<BR>—5 Flow, course, current (of water); Ms. 8. 252, 9. 281; रक्त˚, फेण˚.<BR>—6 A voucher or written testimony; see अनागम. संभोगो दृश्यते<BR> यत्र न दृश्येतागमः क्वचित् Ms. 8. 200.<BR>—7 Knowledge; शिष्यप्रदेयागमाः Bh. 2. 15; प्रज्ञया सदृशागमः ।<BR> आगमः सदृशारम्भः R. 1. 15; यस्यागमः केवलजीविकायै M. 1. 17;<BR> Y. 2. 212, 92.<BR>—8 Supply of money, income, revenue.<BR>—9 Lawful acquisition of anything; आगमेपि बलं नैव भुक्तिः स्तोकापि<BR> यत्र नो Y. 2. 27, 28.<BR>—10 Increase of property.<BR>—11 A traditional doctrine or precept, a sacred writing or scripture,<BR> Śāstra; अनुमानेन न चागमः क्षतः Ki. 2. 28, 5. 18; परिशुद्ध<BR> आगमः 2. 33; K. 55, 337.<BR>—12 The study of Śāstras, sacred knowledge or learning.<BR>—13 Science, a system of philosophy; साङ्ख्यागमेनेव प्रधानपुरुषोपेतेन<BR> K. 51; बहुधाप्यागमैर्भिन्नाः पन्थानः सिद्धिहेतवः R. 10. 26<BR>—14 the Vedas, the sacred scripture; आत्मन्युपरते सम्यङ् मुनिर्व्युपरतागम<BR> Bhāg. 10. 20. 40. न्यायनिर्णीतसारत्वान्निरपेक्षमिवागमे Ki. 11. 39;<BR> आगमः खल्पपि Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1.<BR>—15 The last of the four kinds of proof, recognized by the Naiyāyikas<BR> (also called शब्द or आप्तवाक्य, the Vedas being so regarded).<BR>—16 An affix or suffix.<BR>—17 The addition or insertion of a letter; भवेद्वर्णागमाद्धंसः Sk.<BR>—18 An augment; इडागमः.<BR>—19 Theory (opp. प्रयोग); चतुःषष्टिकलागमप्रयोगचतुरः Dk. 120.<BR>—20<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमः|आगम|आगमं
आगमः + ({@-मः, -मम्@})<BR> A work inculcating the mystical worship of शिव<BR> and शक्ति, a Tantra; आगतं पञ्चवक्त्रात्तु गतं च गिरिजानने ।<BR> मतं च वासुदेवस्य तस्मादागममुच्यते ॥ Śabdak.<BR>—21 The mouth of a river.<BR>—22 What comes later or afterwards. आगमवदन्त्यलोपः स्यात् MS. 10. 5. 1.<BR> (आगमवत् as explained by शबर is यथा समाजेषु समासेषु<BR> च ये आगन्तवो भवन्ति ते पूर्वोपविष्टाननुपमृद्यैव निविशन्ते एवमिहापि द्रष्टव्यम् ।)<BR>—23 A way of worship; लब्धानुग्रह आचार्यात्तेन सन्दर्शितागमः । महापुरुषमभ्यर्चेन्मूर्त्याभिमतमात्मनः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 11. 3. 48.<BR>—24 A road or way, journey; आगमास्ते शिवाः सन्तु Rām. 2. 25. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगमापायिन्, आगमावर्ता, आगमनिरपेक्ष, आगमनीत, आगमरहित, आगमवृद्ध, आगमवेदिन्, आगमशास्त्रम्, आगमश्रुतिः, आगमसाक्षेप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमम्
आगमः + ({@-मः, -मम्@})<BR> A work inculcating the mystical worship of शिव<BR> and शक्ति, a Tantra; आगतं पञ्चवक्त्रात्तु गतं च गिरिजानने ।<BR> मतं च वासुदेवस्य तस्मादागममुच्यते ॥ Śabdak.<BR>—21 The mouth of a river.<BR>—22 What comes later or afterwards. आगमवदन्त्यलोपः स्यात् MS. 10. 5. 1.<BR> (आगमवत् as explained by शबर is यथा समाजेषु समासेषु<BR> च ये आगन्तवो भवन्ति ते पूर्वोपविष्टाननुपमृद्यैव निविशन्ते एवमिहापि द्रष्टव्यम् ।)<BR>—23 A way of worship; लब्धानुग्रह आचार्यात्तेन सन्दर्शितागमः । महापुरुषमभ्यर्चेन्मूर्त्याभिमतमात्मनः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 11. 3. 48.<BR>—24 A road or way, journey; आगमास्ते शिवाः सन्तु Rām. 2. 25. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगमापायिन्, आगमावर्ता, आगमनिरपेक्ष, आगमनीत, आगमरहित, आगमवृद्ध, आगमवेदिन्, आगमशास्त्रम्, आगमश्रुतिः, आगमसाक्षेप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमः + -अपायिन् Having creation and destruction; आगमापायिनो नित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व<BR> भारत Bg. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमावर्ता|आगमावर्त्ता
आगमः + -आवर्ता N. of the plant Targia Involucrata Lin. (वृश्चिकाली;<BR> Mar. लघुमेडशिंगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनिरपेक्ष
आगमः + -निरपेक्ष^1 <i>a.</i> independent of a voucher.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनीत
आगमः + -नीत <i>a.</i> studied, read, examined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमरहित
आगमः + -रहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 without a voucher.<BR>—2 devoid of Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमवृद्ध
आगमः + -वृद्ध<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">Page0313-2</a>]<BR> <i>a.</i> advanced in knowledge, a very learned man; प्रतीप इत्यागमवृद्धसेवी R. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमवेदिन्
आगमः + -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing the Vedas.<BR>—2 learned in Śāstras; (<i>m.</i>) an epithet of Śaṅkarācāryaʼs preceptor Gauḍapāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमशास्त्रम्
आगमः + -शास्त्रम् N. of a supplement to the माण्डूक्योपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमश्रुतिः|आगमश्रुति
आगमः + -श्रुतिः <i>f.</i> Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमसाक्षेप
आगमः + -साक्षेप <i>a.</i> supposed by a voucher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमवत्|आगमवन्त्
आगमवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an augment or addition.<BR>—2 Having approached for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनम्
आगमनम्<BR>—1 Coming, approaching, arrival; भरतागमनं पुनः R. 12. 24.<BR>—2 Return, returning.<BR>—3 Acquisition, getting into; एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं वैरस्यागमनं महत् Rām.<BR>—4 Arising, birth.<BR>—5 Approaching a woman for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमापायिन् <i>a.</i> Coming and going; Transient; मात्रास्पर्शास्तु<BR> कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः । आगमापायिनः Bg. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमित|आगमितं
आगमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Learnt from or taught by; प्रकृतिस्थमेव निपुणागमितम् Śi. 9. 79.<BR>—2 Read over, pursued, studied.<BR>—3 Ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिन्
आगमिन्, -आगामिन् <i>a.</i><BR> [आ-गम् णिनि वा ह्रस्वः]<BR>—1 Coming, future; कथयत्यागामिनमर्थम् K. 46.<BR>—2 Impending, arriving.<BR>—3 Learned, versed in theory; द्वावप्यागमिनौ M. 3.<BR>—4 An intruder.<BR>—5 Having an augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आगमिन्, -आगामिन् <i>a.</i><BR> [आ-गम् णिनि वा ह्रस्वः]<BR>—1 Coming, future; कथयत्यागामिनमर्थम् K. 46.<BR>—2 Impending, arriving.<BR>—3 Learned, versed in theory; द्वावप्यागमिनौ M. 3.<BR>—4 An intruder.<BR>—5 Having an augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिष्ठ
आगमिष्ठ^1 <i>a.</i> Coming very quickly, or gladly.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf MW and  Whitney roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिक
आगामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the future time; मतिरागामिका ज्ञेया बुद्धिस्तत्कालदशिंनी Haima.<BR>—2 Impending, arriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामुक
आगामुक <i>a.</i> [आ-गम्-उकञ् P. III. 2. 154]<BR>—1 Coming, arriving. सुग्रीवस्वार्जितं मित्रं सर्वांश्चागामुकान् द्रुतम् Bk.<BR>—2 Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगरः|आगर
आगरः [आगॄ-अप्] The day of new moon (अमावास्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगलित
आगलित <i>a.</i> Drooping, languid, dejected, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगवीन
आगवीन <i>a.</i> [गोः प्रत्यर्पणपर्यन्तं यः कर्म करोति स आगवीनः<BR> P. V. 2. 14 आगो-ख] One who is engaged in business till the return of the cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् <i>n.</i> [इ-असुन्-आगादेशः Uṇ. 4. 211]<BR>—1 Fault, offence, transgression; सहिष्ये शतमागांसि सूनोस्त इति यत्त्वया<BR> Śi. 2. 108, 1. 61; द्वौ रिपू मम मतौ समागसौ R. 11. 74; कृतागाः<BR> Mu. 3. 11; N. 3. 52; Amaru. 46, 48.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>—3 Punishment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगस्कृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्कृत्
आगस् + आगस्कृत् <i>a.</i> committing an offence, offender, criminal; अभ्यर्णमागस्कृतमस्पृशद्भिः R. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्ती
आगस्ती [अगस्त्यस्य इयं, अण्, यलोपः] The south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्तीय
आगस्तीय <i>a.</i> [अगस्तये हितः यलोपः] Relating to or for the<BR> advantage of अगस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्य|आगस्त्यः
आगस्त्य <i>a.</i> [अगस्त्यस्येदम् यञ् यलोपः]<BR>—1 Southern (दिग्भाग). कौबेरदिग्भागमपास्य मार्गमागस्त्यमुष्णांशुरिवावतीर्णः । Śi.<BR>—2 Pertaining to Āgastya; ˚आख्यानं सरः Mb.<BR>—3 Originating from the plant Agasti Grandiflorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्यः|आगस्त्य
आगस्त्य + .{@-स्त्यः, -स्त्यी@}<BR>—1 The descendants of Agasti.<BR>—2 Persons of their race (गोत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्यी
आगस्त्य + .{@-स्त्यः, -स्त्यी@}<BR>—1 The descendants of Agasti.<BR>—2 Persons of their race (गोत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0313-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्यायन
आगस्त्यायन <i>a.</i> Connected with Agasti; U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध <i>a.</i> [अगाध एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 Very deep or unfathomable (fig. also).<BR>—2 Difficult to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारम्
आगारम् [आगमृच्छति ऋ अण्] A house, dwelling; room, covered place.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आगारगोधिका, आगारदाहः, आगारदाहिन्, आगारधुमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारगोधिका
आगारम् + -गोधिका a small lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाहः|आगारदाह
आगारम् + -दाहः setting a house on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाहिन्
आगारम् + -दाहिन् <i>a.</i> an incendiary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारधुमः
आगारम् + -धुमः<BR>—1 smoke coming out from a house.<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर् €6 Ā. To approve, agree or assent to, promise to pronounce the<BR> आगुर्, see below. पुरोडाशं पचत्यं जुषस्वेन्द्रा गुरस्व च Rv. 3. 52. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगु(गू)र् <i>f.</i> [आ-गुर्-क्विप्]<BR>—1 Assent, agreement, promise.<BR>—2 N. of a class of plauditory exclamations or formularies used by the<BR> priests in sacrificial rites; ये ३ यजामह इत्यागूः Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्
आगु(गू)र् <i>f.</i> [आ-गुर्-क्विप्]<BR>—1 Assent, agreement, promise.<BR>—2 N. of a class of plauditory exclamations or formularies used by the<BR> priests in sacrificial rites; ये ३ यजामह इत्यागूः Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरणम्
आगु(गू)रणम्<BR>—1 Recitation of the Āgur.<BR>—2 A secret suggestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूरणम्
आगु(गू)रणम्<BR>—1 Recitation of the Āgur.<BR>—2 A secret suggestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्ण|आगूर्ण्ण
आगूर्ण, -र्त <i>p. p.</i><BR> Repeated (as an exclamation &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्त|आगूर्त्त
आगूर्ण, -र्त <i>p. p.</i><BR> Repeated (as an exclamation &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्णम्
आगूर्ण, -र्त + .{@-र्णम्, -र्तम्@} Exertion, resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्तम्
आगूर्ण, -र्त + .{@-र्णम्, -र्तम्@} Exertion, resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्तिन्|आगूर्त्तिन्
आगूर्तिन् <i>a.</i> [आगूर्त-इनि]<BR>—1 Performing or pronouncing the Āgur; आगूर्ती वा एष भवति यो दर्शपौर्णमासाभ्यां<BR> यजते Śat. Br.<BR>—2 Resolute, industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरव
आगुरव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to agallochum (अगुरु) साङ्गानि धूमरुचिमागुरवीं<BR> दधानैर्धूपायतीव पटलैर्नवनीरदानाम् Śi. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुल्फम्
आगुल्फम् A shoe; Hc. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्
आगूर् (<i>f.</i>) An agreement, promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगै
आगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To sing to, आपशुं गासि Rv. 8. 27. 2.<BR>—2 To obtain by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगातृ
आगातृ <i>a.</i> Obtaining by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगानम्
आगानम् Obtaining by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नापौष्ण
आग्नापौष्ण <i>a.</i> [आग्नापूषणौ देवते अस्य अण्] Belonging or referring<BR> to Agni and Pūṣan (as an oblation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नावैष्णव
आग्नावैष्णव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Referring to Agni and Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Containing the word अग्नाविष्णू (as a chapter अध्याय, or अनुवाक section).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निक
आग्निक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अग्नेरिदं बा˚ ठक्] Belonging to the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निपद
आग्निपद <i>a.</i> [अग्निपदे दीयते कार्यं वा व्युष्टा˚ अण्] To be<BR> done at or given to the fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निमारुत
आग्निमारुत <i>a.</i> [अग्नामरुतौ देवते अस्य अण्] Belonging to Agni<BR> and Marut (offerings &c.) Vāj. 24. 7; so आग्निवारुण belonging to<BR> Agni and Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निष्टोमिक
आग्निष्टोमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अग्निष्टोम-ठक्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the अग्निष्टोम; ˚कं भक्तम् ˚की दक्षिणा.<BR>—2 One who recites or is conversant with अग्निष्टोम (अग्निष्टोममधीते वेद वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निहोत्रिक
आग्निहोत्रिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the Agnihotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र <i>a.</i> Belonging to the अग्नीध्र (the priest who kindles the fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रम्
आग्नीध्र + .{@-ध्रम्@} [अग्निमिन्धे अग्नीत् तस्य शरणम्, रण् भत्वान्न जश् Tv.]<BR>—1 The place where the sacrificial or sacred fire is kindled. सद आग्नीध्रशालां<BR> च तद्विहारं महानसम् (केचिद् बभञ्जुः) Bhāg. 4. 5. 14.<BR>—2 The duty of the priest who kindles the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रा
आग्नीध्र + .{@-ध्रा@} Care of the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रः|आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं
आग्नीध्र + .{@-ध्रः@} The priest who kindles the sacred fire. आग्नीध्रश्चोत्तरां<BR> दिशम् Mb. 12. 98. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रीय|आग्नीध्रीयः
आग्नीध्रीय <i>a.</i> Being within the आग्नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रीयः|आग्नीध्रीय
आग्नीध्रीय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 The fire within the आग्नीध्र.<BR>—2 The fire-place within the आग्नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र्य
आग्नीध्र्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the priest who kindles the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र्या
आग्नीध्र्य + .{@-ध्र्या@} The place for the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेन्द्र|आग्नेंद्र
आग्नेन्द्र <i>a.</i> [अग्निश्च इन्द्रश्च-अण् P. VI. 3. 28; Sk., VII. 3. 22]<BR> Belonging to Agni and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अग्नेरिदम् अग्निर्देवता वास्य ढक्]<BR>—1 Belonging to Agni; fiery. Vāj. 24. 6.<BR>—2 Offered or consecrated to Agni; अभिशस्तो मृषा कृच्छ्रं चरेदाग्नेयमेव<BR> वा Y. 3. 287.<BR>—3 Similar to fire (as an insect).<BR>—4 Increasing the fire in the stomach; stimulating digestion.<BR>—5 Kindling the fire (as ghee &c.) शणसर्जरसादीनि यानि द्रव्याणि कानिचित् ।<BR> आग्नेयान्युत सन्तीह Mb. 1. 144. 9.<BR>—6 Belonging to Āgnāyī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेयः|आग्नेय|आग्नेयं
आग्नेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Skanda or Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 N. of Agastya.<BR>—3 N. of a country.<BR>—4 A worshipper of Agni.<BR>—5 An offering or oblation to Svāhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेयी
आग्नेय + .{@-यी@}<BR>—1 N. of the wife of Agni.<BR>—2 The south-east quarter (presided over by Agni).<BR>—3 The first day of a month (प्रतिपत्तिथि which is presided over by Agni).<BR>—4 A kind of योगधारणा; Bhāg. 11. 31. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेयम्
आग्नेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 The lunar mansion called Kṛttikā. Mb. 13. 104. 127.<BR>—2 Gold.<BR>—3 Blood.<BR>—4 Lac, the red animal dye.<BR>—5 Ghee.<BR>—6 A missile presided over by Agni.<BR>—7 A <i>Mantra</i> used in the worship of Agni.<BR>—8 A descendant of Agni.<BR>—9 Bathing by applying sacred ashes to the body (भस्ममर्दनपूर्वकस्नानम्).<BR>—10 A kind of worm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आग्नेयकीटः, आग्नेयपुराणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेयकीटः
आग्नेय + -कीटः a kind of insect which flies into the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेयपुराणम्
आग्नेय + -पुराणम् = अग्निपुराण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्न्याधानिकी
आग्न्याधानिकी [अग्न्याधानस्य यज्ञस्य दक्षिणा ठञ् P. V. 1. 95] The<BR> Dakṣiṇā or a gift of money given to Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रभोजनिकः|आग्रभोजनिक
आग्रभोजनिकः [अग्रभोजनं नियतं दीयते अस्मै ठक् P. IV. 4. 66]<BR> A Brāhmaṇa always entitled to occupy the foremost seat at a dinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणः|आग्रयण|आग्रयणं
आग्रयणः [अग्रे अयनं शस्यादेर्येन कर्मणा पृषो˚ ह्रस्वदीर्घव्यत्ययः]<BR>—1 The first Soma libation at the Agniṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR>—2 A form of Agni.<BR>—3 The time of the sacrifice.<BR>—4 See आग्रयणी; नवाग्रयणपूजाभिरभ्यर्च्य पितृदेवताः Rām. 3. 16. 6;<BR> Bhāg. 10. 20. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणकम्
आग्रयणः + .{@-णकम्, -णी@} —1 An oblation consisting of first fruits; see आग्रयणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणी
आग्रयणः + .{@-णकम्, -णी@} —1 An oblation consisting of first fruits; see आग्रयणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणम्
आग्रयणः + .{@-णम्@} An oblation consisting of first fruits at the end of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">Page0315-1</a>]<BR> the rainy season (आश्विनी पूर्णिमा); आग्रयणं त्रिविधं श्यामाक˚,<BR> व्रीहि˚, यव˚, यथापूर्वं वर्षासु शरदि वसन्ते च तत्करणोपदेशात्<BR> Āryā. S.; आग्रयणेनेष्ट्वा नवान्नं प्राश्नीयात् Ait. Br.; आग्रयणं<BR> व्रीहिश्यामाकयवानाम् Āśval.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आग्रयणेष्टिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0314-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणेष्टिः|आग्रयणेष्टि
आग्रयणः + -इष्टिः <i>f.</i> Oblation of the first fruit; कर्तव्याग्रयणेष्टिश्च<BR> चातुर्मास्यानि चैव हि Y. 1. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह्
आग्रह् €9 U.<BR>—1 To seize, take hold of, catch.<BR>—2 To draw tight (as the reins) Ś. 1. (v. l.)<BR>—3 To persist in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहः|आग्रह
आग्रहः<BR>—1 Seizing, taking.<BR>—2 Attack.<BR>—3 Determination, strong attachment, persistence, insisting (स्नेह,<BR> अभिनिवेश); चलेऽपि काकस्य पदार्पणाग्रहः Naiṣadha; Dk. 176; also<BR> Malli. on Ku. 5. 7.<BR>—4 Favour, patronage.<BR>—5 Surpassing, surmounting.<BR>—6 Moral power, courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहिका
आग्रहिका Favour, patronage, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणः|आग्रहायण
आग्रहायणः [= अग्रहायण-अण्] N. of the month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणी
आग्रहायणः + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 The full moon day of मार्गशीर्ष; कार्तिक्या आग्रहायणी मासे Sk.<BR>—2 A particular kind of Pākayajña.<BR>—3 N. of a constellation called मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणक|आग्रहायणकः
आग्रहायण(णि)क <i>a.</i> [आग्रहायण्यां देयमृणं वुञ् ठञ् वा P. IV. 3. 50]<BR> To be paid on the full moon day in मार्गशीर्ष (as debt.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिक|आग्रहायणिकः
आग्रहायण(णि)क <i>a.</i> [आग्रहायण्यां देयमृणं वुञ् ठञ् वा P. IV. 3. 50]<BR> To be paid on the full moon day in मार्गशीर्ष (as debt.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणकः|आग्रहायणक
आग्रहायण(णि)क + .{@-कः@},<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिकः|आग्रहायणिक
आग्रहायण(णि)क + .{@-कः@} + .({@-णिकः@}) [आग्रहायणी पौर्णिमास्यस्मिन् मासे ठक् P. IV. 2. 22]<BR> The month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहारिक
आग्रहारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अग्रहार-ठञ्; see आग्रभोजनिक] One who<BR> appropriates to himself an अग्रहार (endowments of land conferred upon<BR> Brāhmaṇas). Supervisor of Agrahāra lands, <i>i. e.</i> lands offered as<BR> free gifts to Brāhmaṇas for their subsistence or settlement therein<BR> or for some religious purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्ट्
आघट्ट् €10 P.<BR>—1 To strike against, touch; आघट्टयामास गतागताभ्याम् Ki. 17. 38.<BR>—2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टक|आघट्टकः
आघट्टक <i>a.</i> Moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टकः|आघट्टक
आघट्टक + .{@-कः@} The red Apāmārga (Mar. तांबडा आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टना
आघट्टना<BR>—1 Moving, shaking, striking against; रणद्भिराघट्टनया नभस्वतः Śi. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Friction, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षः|आघर्ष
आघर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR> Rubbing, friction, striking against; गण्डस्थलाघर्षगलन्मदोदकद्रवद्रुमस्कन्धनिलायिनोऽलयः Śi. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षणम्
आघर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR> Rubbing, friction, striking against; गण्डस्थलाघर्षगलन्मदोदकद्रवद्रुमस्कन्धनिलायिनोऽलयः Śi. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्ष्णी
आघर्षः, -र्षणम् + .{@-णी@} A brush, rubber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाटः|आघाट
आघाटः [आ-हन् घञ् निपातः]<BR>—1 Killing, striking (sometimes used as an adj.).<BR>—2 A musical instrument.<BR>—3 A cymbal or rattle; उत यत्राघाटाः कर्कर्यः संवदन्ति Av. 4. 37. 5.<BR>—4 Boundary, limit.<BR>—5 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग; Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाटिः|आघाटि
आघाटिः <i>m., f.</i> Musical instruments; आघाटिभिरिव धावयन्नरण्यानिर्महीयते<BR> Rv. 10. 146. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातः|आघात
आघातः See under आहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघुष्
आघुष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To proclaim, cry aloud, declare.<BR>—2 To praise.<BR>—3 To listen.<BR>—4 To make oneself audible; आस्यश्रवस्याद् रथ आ च घोषात् Rv. 5. 37. 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">Page0315-2</a>]<BR> €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To make a noise, to cause to sound.<BR>—2 To proclaim, announce publicly.<BR>—3 To complain continually, weep bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषः|आघोष
आघोषः Calling out, invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषणम्
आघोषणम्, -णा<BR> A proclamation, public announcement; एवमाघोषणायां कृतायाम् Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषणा
आघोषणम्, -णा<BR> A proclamation, public announcement; एवमाघोषणायां कृतायाम् Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्ण्
आघूर्ण् €1 Ā., €6 P.<BR>—1 To roll, stagger, whirl, toss about; आघूर्णतीवानिलैः<BR> (अम्बरम्) Mk. 5. 27; पवनाघूर्णितपादप Hariv.; Bk. 14. 77.<BR>—2 To swim, roll (as eyes); पुष्पासवाधूर्णितनेत्रशोभि Ku. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णनम्
आघूर्णनम् Rolling, tossing about, whirling round, swimming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृ
आघृ €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i> To pour down upon, sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघारः|आघार
आघारः<BR>—1 Sprinkling (in general).<BR>—2 Especially, sprinkling clarified butter upon the fire at certain sacrifices;<BR> प्रासाज्यभागावाघारौ दत्त्वा चाज्यप्लुतं हविः Bhāg. 11. 27. 40.<BR>—3 Ghee, clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणि|आघृणिः
आघृणि <i>a.</i> [आगतो घृणिर्दीप्तिरस्य] Glowing with heat or endowed<BR> with splendour, having splendid wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणीवसु
आघृणि + .{@आघृणी-वसु@} <i>a.</i> Rich with heat (N. of Agni); मानो रक्ष आवेशीदाघृणीवसो Rv. 8. 60. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणिः|आघृणि
आघृणि + .{@-णिः@} The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रा
आघ्रा €1 P.<BR>—1 To smell, smell at; गन्धमाघ्राय Me. 21.<BR>—2 To kiss, touch (with the nose) as the head, आजघ्रुर्मूर्ध्नि बालांश्च Bk. 14. 12.<BR>—3 (Fig.) To attack; devour, seize upon; मामाघ्रातुमागतवान् Dk. 6;<BR> कामाघ्रातया अनया 116 smitten, affected; Māl. 5. 29; Bh. 3. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राण|आघ्राणं
आघ्राण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Smelt (as flowers).<BR>—2 Satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राणम्
आघ्राण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Smelling.<BR>—2 Satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रात|आघ्रातः
आघ्रात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Smelt, scented, touched.<BR>—2 Satisfied.<BR>—3 Surmounted, surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रातम्
आघ्रात + .{@-तम्@} (Astron.) One of the ten kinds of eclipses; Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्क्षी|आंक्षी
आङ्क्षी A musical instrument, a tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्कुशिकः|आङ्कुशिक|आंकुशिकः
आङ्कुशिकः [अङ्कुश-ठक्] One who strikes with the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आङ्ग <i>a.</i> (-गी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अङ्ग-स्वार्थे-अण्]<BR>—1 Bodily, corporeal.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Relating to the base (अङ्ग).<BR>—3 Having limbs or parts.<BR>—4 Relating to the minor personages in a drama.<BR>—5 Belonging to a portion of the Vedas.<BR>—6 Produced or born in the country of the Aṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गः|आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं
आङ्ग + .{@-गः@} A prince of the Aṅga country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गम्
आङ्ग + .{@-गम्@} A delicate body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गक|आंगक|आङ्गकः
आङ्गक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अङ्गेषु जनपदेषु भवः वुञ्] Produced in the<BR> अङ्ग country; ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गकः|आङ्गक|आंगक
आङ्गक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An inhabitant of the Aṅga country.<BR>—2 A ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गविद्य|आंगविद्य
आङ्गविद्य <i>a.</i> [अङ्गविद्यां वेद अण्] Occurring in, or being<BR> familiar with, अङ्गविद्या (chiromancy or the knowledge of lucky and<BR> unlucky marks on the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गविद्या
आङ्गविद्य + .{@-द्या@} A work on अङ्गविद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0315-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिक|आंगिक|आङ्गिकः
आङ्गिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अङ्ग निर्वृत्तार्थे-ठक्]<BR>—1 Bodily, corporeal.<BR>—2 Gesticulated, expressed by bodily actions; आङ्गिकोऽभिनयः, see अभिनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिकः|आङ्गिक|आंगिक
आङ्गिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A player on a tabor or drum.<BR>—2 Manʼs sleeved outer body, garment, a coat reaching below the knees.<BR> कश्मीरजपृषद्वर्षरञ्जितेनाङ्गिकेन च Śiva B. 21. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गारम्
आङ्गारम्^1 [अङ्गाराणां समूहः अण्] A multitude of firebrands, charcoal.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter noun missing 'm'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गारिकः|आङ्गारिक
आङ्गारिकः A charcoal burner; मालाकारोपमो राजन् भव माऽऽङ्गारिकोपमः<BR> Mb. 12. 71. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आङ्गिरस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Descended from or referring to Aṅgiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरसः|आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस
आङ्गिरस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 N. of Bṛhaspati, son of Aṅgiras; अध्यापयामास पितॄन् शिशुराङ्गिरसः<BR> कविः Ms. 2. 151. तं भासुरं चाङ्गिरसाधिदेवं यथावदानर्च तदायुषे<BR> सः Bu. C. 2. 36.<BR>—2 Descendants of Aṅgiras (pl.).<BR>—3 A particular Sūkta or hymn in the Atharvaveda<BR>—4 the soul; अधमास्येऽन्तरिति सोऽयास्य आङ्गिरसोऽङ्गानां हि रसः Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 8.<BR>—5 A Kṣatriya by will of Brahmā and by profession.<BR>—6 N. of a particular year. cf. आङ्गीरसस्त्वब्दभेदे मुनिभेदे तदीरितम् । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आङ्गिरससत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरससत्रम्
आङ्गिरस + -सत्रम् The वृहस्पति Satra; सत्रमाङ्गिरसं नाम ह्यासते<BR> स्वर्गकाम्यया Bhāg. 10. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गूषः|आङ्गूष|आंगूषः
आङ्गूषः, षम् [अङ्गूष-स्वार्थे-अन्] Praise, hymn. ब्रह्माङ्गूषं<BR> सदनं रोदस्योः Rv. 1. 117. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गूषम्
आङ्गूषः, षम् [अङ्गूष-स्वार्थे-अन्] Praise, hymn. ब्रह्माङ्गूषं<BR> सदनं रोदस्योः Rv. 1. 117. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग्य
आङ्ग्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the Anga country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्ष्
आचक्ष् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To speak, announce, declare, teach, tell, relate, communicate, say,<BR> narrate (usually with dat. of person); गुरवे … प्रस्तुतमाचचक्षे<BR> R. 5. 19, 12. 55, 14. 36; Ms. 4. 59, 81; M. 5; इत्याख्यानविद आचक्षते<BR> Māl. 2; sometimes with acc.; तत्त्वां किमाचक्ष्महे Bv. 1. 63 say to or address.<BR>—2 To name, call, say; शर्व इति प्राच्या आचक्षते Śat. Br.<BR>—3 To divine, bespeak; यथा मे हृदयमाचष्टे M. 4.<BR>—4 To make known, acquaint, introduce to.<BR>—5 To look at, inspect (Ved.). आ चष्ट आसां पाथो नदीनाम् Rv. 7. 34. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षुस्
आचक्षुस् <i>m.</i> [Uṇ. 2. 120] A learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुरम्
आचतुरम् <i>ind.</i> [चतुः पर्यन्तम् अच् समासान्त] Till the fourth<BR> generation; आचतुरं हीमे पशवो द्वन्द्वं मिथुनायन्ते P. VIII. 1. 15. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचन्द्रतारकम्
आचन्द्रतारकम् <i>ind.</i> As long as there are the moon and stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचपराच
आचपराच <i>a.</i> Moving towards and away from. Tāṇḍya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्
आचम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sip, lick, lap, drink (a small quantity); नाचेमे हिममपि वारि<BR> वारणेन Ki. 7. 34; पर्याप्तमाचामति U. 4. 1; Bv. 4. 38; त्रिराचामेदपः<BR> पूर्वम् Ms. 2. 60, 5. 139.<BR>—2 To rinse the mouth (with instr. of the thing); Ms. 2. 61.<BR>—3 To lick up, dry or drink up, absorb; आचामति स्वेदलवान् मुखे ते<BR> R. 13. 20. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">Page0316-2</a>]<BR> To cause to sip water; पृष्ट्वा स्वदितमित्येवं तृप्तानाचामयेत्ततः<BR> Ms. 3. 251, 5. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमः|आचम
आचमः Rinsing the mouth, sipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनम्
आचमनम्<BR>—1 Rinsing the mouth, sipping water before religious ceremonies, before<BR> and after meals &c. from the palm of the hand; दद्यादाचमनं ततः<BR> Y. 1. 243, 195 (part of the water sipped being usually allowed to drop down).<BR>—2 The water used for rinsing the mouth.<BR>—3 Gargling the throat.<BR>—4 N. of a plant Andropogon muricatum (Mar. वाळा).<BR>—5 Water for rinsing the vulva (Āyurveda).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आचमनधारिन्, आचमनवाहिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनधारिन्
आचमनम् + -धारिन्, -वाहिन् <i>m.</i> A drawer of water; (Hc. 5. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनवाहिन्
आचमनम् + -धारिन्, -वाहिन् <i>m.</i> A drawer of water; (Hc. 5. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनकम्
आचमनकम् [स्वार्थे आधारे वा कन्]<BR>—1 The water used for sipping.<BR>—2 A spitting pot (Mar. पिकदाणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीय|आचमनीयं
आचमनीय <i>pot. p.</i> Used for rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीयम्
आचमनीय + .{@-यम्, -आचमनीयकम्@} Water used for rinsing the mouth; a gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीयकम्
आचमनीय + .{@-यम्, -आचमनीयकम्@} Water used for rinsing the mouth; a gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्त|आचांत|आचान्तः
आचान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sipped and ejected as water.<BR>—2 (Actively used) One who has rinsed his mouth or sipped water.<BR>—3 Fit for sipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्तिः|आचान्ति
आचान्त + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Sipping (water) for purifying the mouth; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामः|आचाम
आचामः [चम् भावे-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sipping water, rinsing the mouth.<BR>—2 The water or foam of boiled rice (Mar. पेज); Y. 3. 322<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामक
आचामक <i>a.</i> Rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामनकम्
आचामनकम् A spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्य
आचाम्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be rinsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्यम्
आचाम्य + .{@-म्यम्@} Water used for rinsing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचयः|आचय
आचयः<BR>—1 Collecting, gathering.<BR>—2 A collection, heap, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचयक
आचयक <i>a.</i> Skilful in collecting or gathering (आचये कुशलः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्
आचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To act, practise, do, perform, undertake, exercise; असक्तो ह्याचरन्<BR> कर्म Bg. 3. 19; तपस्विकन्यास्वविनयमाचरति Ś. 1. 24 practises<BR> rudeness; ˚स्थितिम् R. 1. 89, 12. 22; त्वं च तस्येष्टमाचरेः V. 5. 20, 1. 19;<BR> नाचरेत्किंचिदप्रियम् Ms. 5. 156; Y. 3. 65; न चाप्याचरितः<BR> पूर्वैरयं धर्मः Mb.; so सेवाम्, विधिम्, स्नानम्, वृत्तिम्.<BR>—2 To act or behave towards (with loc.); तस्यां त्वं साधु नाचरः<BR> R. 1. 76; विष्णाविवाचरति शिवे Vop.<BR>—3 To act, proceed, manage (without loc.); यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठः Bg. 3. 21;<BR> जडवल्लोक आचरेत् Ms. 2. 110.<BR>—4 To treat; पुत्रं मित्रवदाचरेत् Cāṇ. 11; पुत्रमिवाचरति<BR> शिष्यम् Sk.; Ms. 8. 102;<BR>—5 To observe the usual formality; Ś. 7.<BR>—6 To come near; approach (Ved.); आ वां चरन्तु वृष्टयः Rv. 8. 25. 6.<BR>—7 To step upon, pass through, wander over or about; frequent, resort<BR> to, follow; तस्कराचरितो मार्गः Rām.; श्वापदाचरिते वने Mb.;<BR> अगस्त्याचरितामाशाम् R. 4. 44; परेताचरितां दिशम् Rām.; अविद्वज्जनाचरित<BR> एष मार्गः K. 173.<BR>—8 To have intercourse<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">Page0317-1</a>]<BR> with; Ms. 11. 180, 189.<BR>—9 To devour, eat into, corrode.<BR>—10 To help forward, put into; हस्तेनाचरति Kāty. (हस्तेन प्रेरयति प्रक्षिपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0316-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणम्
आचरणम्<BR>—1 Practising, doing, performing, following, observing; धर्म˚, मंगल˚ &c.<BR>—2 Conduct, behaviour; अधीतिबोधाचरणप्रचारणैः N. 1. 4 example<BR> (opp. precept); अधर्म˚, दुर्˚ &c.<BR>—3 Usage, practice.<BR>—4 An institute; rite or rule of conduct.<BR>—5 Approaching, arrival (as of the dawn); ये अस्या आचरणेषु दध्रिरे Rv. 1. 48. 3.<BR>—6 A chariot, carriage; cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणीय
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be done, performed, followed,<BR> observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरितव्य
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be done, performed, followed,<BR> observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्य|आचर्य्य
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be done, performed, followed,<BR> observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरित|आचरितं
आचरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Done, observed, practised, as a rite or usage &c.<BR>—2 Usual, customary.<BR>—3 Enjoined, fixed by rule.<BR>—4 Inhabited, colonied; देशमुत्सादयत्येनमगस्त्याचरितं शुभम् Rām. 1. 25. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरितम्
आचरित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Conduct. behaviour. वाग्देवताचरितचित्रितचित्रसद्मा जयदेवः<BR>—2 One of the five means of recovering or paying back debt; धर्मेण<BR> व्यवहारेण छलेनाचरितेन च । प्रयुक्तं साधयेदर्थं पञ्चमेन बलेन<BR> च ॥ Ms. 8. 49; see also Bṛhaspati quoted by Kull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारः|आचार
आचारः [आचार-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Conduct, behaviour, manner of action or of conducting oneself; सदाचारः<BR> good conduct; नीच˚ &c.; लोकाचारविवर्जिताः Pt. 5. 40 ignorant<BR> of the ways of the world.<BR>—2 Good conduct or behaviour; न शौचं नापि चाचारो न सत्यं तेषु विद्यते<BR> Bg. 16. 7; Ms. 1. 109, 5. 4, 3. 165.<BR>—3 A custom, usage, practice; तस्मिन्देशे य आचारः पारंपर्यकमागतः<BR> Ms. 2. 18; Y. 1. 343.<BR>—4 An established usage, fixed rule of conduct in life, customary law,<BR> institute or precept (opp. व्यवहार in law); आचार्य आचाराणाम्<BR> K. 56; Ms. 1. 109; oft. as the first member of comp. in the sense of ‘customary’,<BR> ‘usual’, ‘as is the custom’, ‘according to form’, ‘as a formality’; ˚पुष्पग्रहणार्थम्<BR> M. 4; see ˚धूम, ˚लाज below; परिकर्मन् Ś. 2.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Any customary observance or duty; ˚प्रयतः V. 3. 2; गृहाचारव्यपदेशेन U. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A form, formality; आचार इत्यवहितेन मया गृहीता Ś. 5. 3; Mv. 3. 26.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) The customary salutation or bow, usual formality; आचारं प्रतिपद्यस्व<BR> Ś. 4; V. 2; अविषयस्तावदाचारस्य Mv. 2.<BR>—6 Diet.<BR>—7 A rule (of conduct).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आचाराङ्गम्, आचारचक्रिन्, आचारचन्द्रिका, आचारतन्त्रम्, आचारदीपः, आचारधूमग्रहणम्, आचारपूत, आचारभेदः, आचारभ्रष्ट, आचारपतित, आचारमयूखः, आचारलाज, आचारवर्जित, आचारव्यपेत, आचारहीन, आचारवेदी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाराङ्गम्
आचारः + -अङ्गम् title of the first of the twelve sacred books of the Jainas<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारचक्रिन्
आचारः + -चक्रिन् N. of a Vaisṇava sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारचन्द्रिका
आचारः + -चन्द्रिका N. of a work on the religious customs of the Śūdras<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारतन्त्रम्
आचारः + -तन्त्रम् one of the four classes of the Tantras (with Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारदीपः|आचारदीप
आचारः + -दीपः [आचारार्थः नीराजनार्थो दीपः]<BR>—1 ‘a lamp of religious customs’, title of a work.<BR>—2 a lamp waved about a person as a formality and token of auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारधूमग्रहणम्
आचारः + -धूमग्रहणम् inhaling smoke as a customary rite (as of the sacrificial<BR> ceremony) R. 7. 27; वधूमुखं क्लान्तयवावतंसमाचारधूमग्रहणाद् बभूव Ku. 7. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारपूत
आचारः + -पूत <i>a.</i> purified by customary observances, of pure conduct;<BR> तमातपक्लान्तमनातपत्रमाचारपूतं पवनः सिषेवे R. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारभेदः|आचारभेद
आचारः + -भेदः difference in the customary law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारभ्रष्ट
आचारः + -भ्रष्ट, -पतित <i>a.</i> apostate, fallen<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">Page0317-2</a>]<BR> from established usages or rules of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारपतित
आचारः + -भ्रष्ट, -पतित <i>a.</i> apostate, fallen<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">Page0317-2</a>]<BR> from established usages or rules of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारमयूखः|आचारमयूख
आचारः + -मयूखः ‘Ray of religious customs’; N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारलाज
आचारः + -लाज (<i>m.</i> pl.) fried grain customarily showered upon a king<BR> or other important personage as a mark of respect (as when he passes through<BR> the streets of his capital); अवाकिरन्बाललताः प्रसूनैराचारलाजैरिव<BR> पौरकन्याः R. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवर्जित|आचारवर्ज्जित|आचारवर्ज्जितः
आचारः + -वर्जित, -व्यपेत, -हीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 irregular, out of rule.<BR>—2 outcast, who has renounced all customary observances. स्मृत्याचारव्यपेतेन<BR> Y. 2. 5; Ms. 3. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारव्यपेत
आचारः + -वर्जित, -व्यपेत, -हीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 irregular, out of rule.<BR>—2 outcast, who has renounced all customary observances. स्मृत्याचारव्यपेतेन<BR> Y. 2. 5; Ms. 3. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारहीन
आचारः + -वर्जित, -व्यपेत, -हीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 irregular, out of rule.<BR>—2 outcast, who has renounced all customary observances. स्मृत्याचारव्यपेतेन<BR> Y. 2. 5; Ms. 3. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवेदी
आचारः + -वेदी [आचारस्य वेदीव] ‘altar of religious customs’, N. of<BR> Āryāvarta, the sacred region of the Āryas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवत्|आचारवन्त्
आचारवत् <i>a.</i> Well-conducted, virtuous; भवत्याचारवान्नित्यं<BR> यथेष्टां प्राप्नुयाद्गतिम् Ms. 12. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिक
आचारिक <i>a.</i> [आचार-ठक्] Conformable to rule or practice, authorized, prescriptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिकम्
आचारिक + .{@-कम्@} Rule for the preservation of health; hygiene, regimen, diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिन्
आचारिन् <i>a.</i> [आचार्-णिनि, आचार-इनि वा] Following established customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारी
आचारी N. of a plant (हिलमोचिका; Mar. चाकवत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यः|आचार्य|आचार्य्य|आचार्य्यः
आचार्यः [आ-चर्-ण्यत् P. III. 1. 100. Vārt. Kāśi.]<BR>—1 A teacher or preceptor (in general).<BR>—2 A spiritual guide or preceptor, holy teacher (one who invests a boy<BR> with the sacred thread, instructs him in the Vedas &c.); उपनीय तु<BR> यः शिष्यम् वेदमध्यापयेद् द्विजः । सकल्पं सरहस्यं च तमाचार्यं प्रचक्षते<BR> Ms. 2. 140; cf. also आचिनोति च शास्त्रार्थम् आचारे स्थापयत्यपि । स्वयमाचरते<BR> यस्तु स आचार्य इति स्मृतः ॥ read also वेदाध्यापनेन च आचार्यो भवति<BR> Ms. 6. 1. 35; see अध्यापक also.<BR>—3 One who propounds a particular doctrine.<BR>—4 (When affixed to proper names) Learned, venerable (somewhat like the English Dr.).<BR>—5 An adviser or preceptor at a sacrifice &c.<BR>—6 An epithet of Droṇa; आचार्यमुपसंगम्य राजा वचनमब्रवीत् Bg. 1. 2.<BR>—7 A degree or title of proficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्या|आचार्य्या
आचार्यः + .{@-र्या@} A female preceptor, a spiritual preceptress.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आचार्योपासनम्, आचार्यकरणम्, आचार्यदेवः, आचार्यदेशीय, आचार्यभोगीन, आचार्यमिश्र, आचार्यसवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्योपासनम्
आचार्यः + -उपासनम् waiting upon or serving the spiritual preceptor; आचार्योपासनं<BR> शौचम् Bg. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यकरणम्
आचार्यः + -करणम् acting as a teacher; P. I. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यदेवः|आचार्यदेव
आचार्यः + -देवः one whose preceptor is his god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यदेशीय
आचार्यः + -देशीय <i>a.</i> Somewhat inferior to Ācārya (a title applied<BR> by commentators to scholars or disputants whose statements contain only<BR> a part of the truth. The term is opposed to ‘Ācārya’ and ‘Siddhāntin’<BR> Kaiyata and Nāgojibhatta on Pat.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यभोगीन|आचार्य्यभोगीन
आचार्यः + -भोगीन <i>a.</i> [आचार्यभोगाय हितम् ख] to be enjoyed by, fit<BR> for the use of, a preceptor; delighting the preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यमिश्र|आचार्य्यमिश्र
आचार्यः + -मिश्र <i>a.</i> venerable, honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यसवः|आचार्यसव
आचार्यः + -सवः N. of an Ekāha sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यक|आचार्य्यक
आचार्यक <i>a.</i> Originating from a spiritual preceptor; P. IV. 2. 104. Vārt. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यकम्
आचार्यक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Instruction, tuition, teaching (lessons &c.); लङ्कास्त्रीणां पुनश्चक्रे<BR> विलापाचार्यकं शरैः R. 12. 78; आचार्यकम् विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26;<BR>—2 The proficiency of a spiritual teacher.<BR>—3 A post of a preceptor आचार्यकं कौरवाणां वाञ्छंस्तस्थौ कृपालये<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">Page0318-1</a>]<BR> Bm. 1. 625. ताण्डवाचार्यकं कुर्वन्निव कीडाशिखण्डिनाम् Bm. 1. 1106.<BR>—4 Honouring the preceptor. चकाराचार्यकं तत्र कुन्तीपुत्रो धनञ्जयः Mb. 7. 147. 6.<BR>—5 Commenting, expounding (व्याख्यातृत्व); श्रुत्यञ्चलाचार्यकम् Viś. Guṇā. 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0317-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यता
आचार्यता, -त्वम्<BR> The office or proficiency of a holy teacher; वाचामाचार्यतायाः<BR> पदमनुभवितुं कोस्ति धन्यो मदन्यः Bṛ. S. 4. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यत्वम्
आचार्यता, -त्वम्<BR> The office or proficiency of a holy teacher; वाचामाचार्यतायाः<BR> पदमनुभवितुं कोस्ति धन्यो मदन्यः Bṛ. S. 4. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यानी
आचार्यानी [आचार्य-स्त्रियाम् आनुक् P. IV. 1. 49. Vārt.] The wife of<BR> an आचार्य or holy preceptor; शत्रुमूलमनुत्खाय न पुनर्द्रष्टुमुत्सहे ।<BR> त्र्यम्बकं देवमाचार्यमाचार्यानीं च पार्वतीम् Mv. 3. 6. cf. आचार्यानी<BR> भर्तृयोगे आचार्या तूपदेशिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचीर्ण
आचीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Devoured or eaten into; पिपीलिकाभिराचीर्णम् Bhāg. 7. 3. 15.<BR>—2 Practised; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण्यति
आचरण्यति Den. P. To move oneself, to move or extend towards; वां<BR> जिह्वा घृतमा चरण्यात् Av. 7. 29. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचि
आचि €5 U.<BR>—1 To accumulate, heap up, collect.<BR>—2 To load with, fill or cover with, cover over, spread; शैलैरिवाचिनोद्<BR> भूमिम् Bk. 17. 69, 14. 46, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित|आचितं|आचितः
आचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Filled, loaded with, covered with; कचाचितौ विष्वगिवागजौ गजौ<BR> Ki. 1. 36; कुसुमाचिता वनराजी, आचितनक्षत्रा द्यौः &c.<BR>—2 Tied, strung, woven; अर्धाचिता सत्वरमुत्थितायाः R. 7. 10 (v. l.<BR> for अर्धाञ्चिता); Ku. 7. 61; inlaid, set (as with gems).<BR>—3 Collected, accumulated, heaped. परि ग्राममिवाचितम् Av. 4. 7. 5.<BR>—4 Spread, diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितः|आचित|आचितं
आचित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A cart-load.<BR>—2 (<i>n.</i> also) A measure of 10 Bhāras or cart-loads (80,000 Tolas);<BR> आचितं दश भाराः स्यात् शाकटो भार आचितः<BR>—3 A measure equal to 2000 <i>palas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिक
आचितिक (-की <i>f.</i>), आचितीन<BR> <i>a.</i> [आचित ठञ् ख वा P. V. 1. 53]<BR> Holding, or being equal to, or cooking, a quantity equal to an<BR> <i>Achita</i>; <i>e. g.</i> त्र्याचितिक^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिकी
आचितिक (-की <i>f.</i>), आचितीन<BR> <i>a.</i> [आचित ठञ् ख वा P. V. 1. 53]<BR> Holding, or being equal to, or cooking, a quantity equal to an<BR> <i>Achita</i>; <i>e. g.</i> त्र्याचितिक^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितीन
आचितिक (-की <i>f.</i>), आचितीन<BR> <i>a.</i> [आचित ठञ् ख वा P. V. 1. 53]<BR> Holding, or being equal to, or cooking, a quantity equal to an<BR> <i>Achita</i>; <i>e. g.</i> त्र्याचितिक^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचूषणम्
आचूषणम्<BR>—1 Suction, sucking up.<BR>—2 Sucking out.<BR>—3 (In medic.) Application of cupping-glasses to the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचेष्टित
आचेष्टित <i>a.</i> Undertaken, done; Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
आच्छद् €10 P.<BR>—1 To cover (in general); नाच्छादयति कौपीनम् Pt. 3. 97.<BR>—2 To hide; भानोराच्छादयत्प्रभाम् Mb.<BR>—3 To clothe, dress, put on clothes; Ms. 3. 27; अनेन वाससाच्छन्नः<BR> Mb. वस्त्रम्, प्रावारान् &c. आच्छादयति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
आच्छद् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A cover, covering. आस्थद् दृष्टेराच्छदम् Śi. 18. 30.<BR>—2 A sheath; ˚विधानम् an arrangement made for defence, a means for covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छन्न|आच्छन्नं
आच्छन्न <i>a.</i> Clothed; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादः|आच्छाद|आछाद
आच्छादः [छद्-घञ्] Cloth, clothes, षाण्मासिकस्तथाच्छादो Ms. 7. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादक
आच्छादक <i>a.</i> Covering, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादनम्
आच्छादनम्<BR>—1 Covering, concealing, hiding.<BR>—2 A covering, sheath.<BR>—3 Cloth, clothes; भूषणाच्छादनाशनैः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">Page0318-2</a>]<BR> Y. 1. 82.<BR>—4 A mantle, cloak &c.<BR>—5 Disappearance.<BR>—6 The wooden frame of a roof.<BR>—7 A bed-sheet; स तद्विहाय शयनं पाण्डुराच्छादनास्तृतम् Rām. 7. 37. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आच्छादनवस्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादनवस्त्रम्
आच्छादनम् + -वस्त्रम् The lower garment; Pt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादिन्
आच्छादिन् <i>a.</i> Covering, concealing; स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छादिना<BR> वल्कलेन Ś. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाकः|आच्छाक
आच्छा(च्छु)कः N. of a tree (= आक्षिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुकः|आच्छुक
आच्छा(च्छु)कः N. of a tree (= आक्षिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छिद्
आच्छिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To cut off or away, tear, cut in pieces, break; आच्छिद्य धमनीमपि<BR> Mb.; धनुः, ज्याम् &c.<BR>—2 To snatch away, tear from, take away; जातवेदोमुखान्मायी मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति<BR> नः Ku. 2. 46; Māl. 5. 28, 8. 9; Dk. 99.<BR>—3 To disregard, take no notice of (as words); मम वच आच्छिद्य in<BR> spite of, notwithstanding, my words.<BR>—4 To cut off, exclude; भर्तारमाच्छेत्स्यसि कामिनीभ्यः Mb.<BR>—5 To remove.<BR>—6 To take out, extract, draw or pull off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदः|आच्छेद
आच्छेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off, exclusion.<BR>—2 Cutting a little.<BR>—3 Taking away by force, snatching away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदनम्
आच्छेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off, exclusion.<BR>—2 Cutting a little.<BR>—3 Taking away by force, snatching away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरित|आच्छुरितं|आछुरित
आच्छुरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mixed, blended with.<BR>—2 Scratched. सामोन्मुखेनाच्छुरिता प्रियेण Bk. 11. 14.<BR>—3 Irritated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरितम्
आच्छुरित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Making a noise with the finger-nails by rubbing them on one another<BR> (नखवाद्यम्).<BR>—2 A horse-laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरितकम्
आच्छुरितकम्<BR>—1 A scratch with a finger-nail.<BR>—2 A horse-laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोटनम्
आच्छोटनम् Cracking the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोदनम्
आच्छोदनम्^1 Hunting, chase.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma. not an adj..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजनिः|आजनि
आजनिः <i>f.</i> Ved. A stick for driving; आजामि त्वाजन्या परि मातुरथो<BR> पितुः Av. 3. 25. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज|आजं|आजः
आज <i>a.</i> (-जी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अजस्येदं-अण्] Coming from, belonging to, or<BR> produced by, goats; आजेन मासान्प्रीयन्ते पञ्चैव पितरो नृप Mb. 13. 88. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0318-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजः|आज|आजं
