आज्ञासंपादक
आज्ञा + -अनुग, -अनुगामिन्, -अनुयायिन्, -अनुवर्तिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -संपादक, -वह<BR> <i>a.</i> obedient, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0319-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञावह
आज्ञा + -अनुग, -अनुगामिन्, -अनुयायिन्, -अनुवर्तिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -संपादक, -वह<BR> <i>a.</i> obedient, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0319-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकर|आज्ञाकरः
आज्ञा + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> obeying or executing orders, obedient.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">Page0320-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0319-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकरः|आज्ञाकर
आज्ञा + -कर, -कारिन् + .({@-रः@}) a servant; ˚करत्वमधिगम्य V. 3. 19 being the obedient<BR> servant; कार्याणां गतयो विधेरपि नयन्त्याज्ञाकरत्वं चिरात् Mu. 7. 16 subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0319-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकारिन्
आज्ञा + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> obeying or executing orders, obedient.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">Page0320-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0319-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकरणम्
आज्ञा + -करणम्, -पालनम् obedience, execution of commands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापालनम्
आज्ञा + -करणम्, -पालनम् obedience, execution of commands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाचक्रम्
आज्ञा + -चक्रम् a mystical circle or diagram; one of the six described in Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापत्रम्
आज्ञा + -पत्रम् an edict, written order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाप्रतिघातः|आज्ञाप्रतिघात
आज्ञा + -प्रतिघातः, -भङ्गः<BR>—1 disobedience, insubordination; नाज्ञाभङ्गं सहन्ते नृवर नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः<BR> सार्वभौमाः Mu. 3. 22.<BR>—2 rebellion, disloyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाभङ्गः|आज्ञाभङ्ग|आज्ञाभंग
आज्ञा + -प्रतिघातः, -भङ्गः<BR>—1 disobedience, insubordination; नाज्ञाभङ्गं सहन्ते नृवर नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः<BR> सार्वभौमाः Mu. 3. 22.<BR>—2 rebellion, disloyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाविधेय
आज्ञा + -विधेय <i>a.</i> obedient to commands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाशतंप्रापयिता
आज्ञा + -शतंप्रापयिता An officer charged with carrying the kingʼs orders<BR> into effect. EI. XII. p. 65, XIX. p. 118 f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञातृ
आज्ञातृ <i>a.</i> Ved. One who orders or directs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानम्
आज्ञानम् The act of observing, perceiving (आज्ञानं = आज्ञप्तिः ईश्वरभावः Śaṅkara.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापक|आज्ञापकः
आज्ञापक <i>a.</i> Giving orders, a commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापनम्
आज्ञापनम्<BR>—1 Ordering, commanding.<BR>—2 Making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञायिन्
आज्ञायिन् <i>a.</i> Perceiving, knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यम्
आज्यम् [आज्यते, आ-अञ्ज्-क्यप्]<BR>—1 Clarified butter, ghee; मन्त्रोऽहमहमेवाज्यम् Bg. 9. 16. आज्यधूमोद्गमेन<BR> Ś. 1. 15; (it is often distinguished from घृत; सर्पिर्विलीनमाज्यं<BR> स्याद् घनीभूतम् घृतं भवेत्).<BR>—2 (In a wider sense) Oil, milk &c. used instead of clarified butter;<BR> घृतं वा यदि वा तैलं पयो वा दधि यावकम् । आज्यस्थाने नियुक्तानामाज्यशब्दो विधीयते ॥<BR>—3 N. of a sort of chant or religious service (सामस्तोमभेदः); आजिमीयुस्तस्मादाज्यानामाज्यत्वम् Nir.<BR>—4 Turpentine.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आज्यग्रहः, आज्यपात्रम्, आज्यस्थाली, आज्यदोहम्, आज्यप, आज्यभागः, आज्यभुज्, आज्यवारिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यग्रहः|आज्यग्रह
आज्यम् + -ग्रहः, -पात्रम्, -स्थाली a vessel or dish to hold clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यपात्रम्
आज्यम् + -ग्रहः, -पात्रम्, -स्थाली a vessel or dish to hold clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यस्थाली
आज्यम् + -ग्रहः, -पात्रम्, -स्थाली a vessel or dish to hold clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यदोहम्
आज्यम् + -दोहम् a hymn to be recited by a Sāmavedin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यप
आज्यम् + -प <i>a.</i> drinking ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यपाः
आज्यम् + -प + .({@-पाः@} pl.) a class of Manes who are the sons of Pulastya and the<BR> ancestors of the Vaiśya order; पुलस्त्यस्याज्यपाः पुत्राः Mb.; Ms. 3. 197-8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यभागः|आज्यभाग
आज्यम् + -भागः A portion of clarified butter; (du.) belonging to Agni<BR> and Soma; यदाज्यभागावन्तरेणाहुतीः प्रतिपादयेत् Māṇḍ. 1. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यभुज्
आज्यम् + -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Agni (the consumer of clarified butter).<BR>—2 a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यवारिः|आज्यवारि
आज्यम् + -वारिः ‘sea of clarified butter’, one of the seven seas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्चनम्
आञ्चनम् Partial extraction of thorns, arrows and the like from the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्छ्|आंछ्
आञ्छ् €1 P. (आञ्छति, आनञ्छ, आञ्छित)<BR>—1 To lengthen, stretch, extend.<BR>—2 To make straight.<BR>—3 To regulate, bring or draw into the right position; set (as a bone<BR> or leg); चकयोगेनाञ्छेदूर्वस्थि निर्गतम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्छनम्
आञ्छनम् Setting (a bone or leg); bringing into the right position<BR> by stretching, bending, or drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जन|आंजन|आञ्जनः
आञ्जन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) [अञ्जनस्येदं-अण्] Anointing<BR> or belonging to ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनम्
आञ्जन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Ointment, especially for the eyes.<BR>—2 Fat; इमा नारीरविधवाः सुपत्नीराञ्जनेन सर्पिषा संविशन्तु Rv. 10. 18. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनः|आञ्जन|आंजन
आञ्जन + .{@-नः@} N. of Māruti or Hanūmat दाशरथिबलैरिवाञ्जननीलनलपरिगतप्रान्तैः K. 58.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आञ्जनाभ्यञ्जनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनाभ्यञ्जनम्
आञ्जन + -अभ्यञ्जनम् (du.) Ointment for the eyes and for the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनी
आञ्जनी<BR>—1 Ointment, especially for the eyes.<BR>—2 A box filled with the ointment; आञ्जनीः कङ्कतान्कूर्चांश्छत्राणि च<BR> धनूंषि च Rām. 2. 91. 77.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आञ्जनीकारी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनीकारी
आञ्जनी + -कारी a woman who anoints or prepares ointments; शीलायाञ्जनीकारीम् Vāj. 30. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनिक्यम्
आञ्जनिक्यम् [पुरोहितादिगण P. V. 1. 128] That which is used to<BR> prepare ointments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनेयः|आञ्जनेय|आंजनेयः
आञ्जनेयः [अञ्जनायाः अपत्यं ढक्] N. of Māruti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जलिकः
आञ्जलिकः A kind of crescent (अर्धचन्द्राकृति) arrow; Mb. 6. 62. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जलिक्यम्
आञ्जलिक्यम्, आञ्जल्यकम् [cf. आञ्जानिक्यम्] Folding the hands<BR> in supplication; ततो दुर्योधनो राजा कर्णशल्याववारयत् । सखिभावेन<BR> राधेयं शल्यं स्वाञ्जल्यकेन च ॥ Mb. 8. 45. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जल्यकम्
आञ्जलिक्यम्, आञ्जल्यकम् [cf. आञ्जानिक्यम्] Folding the hands<BR> in supplication; ततो दुर्योधनो राजा कर्णशल्याववारयत् । सखिभावेन<BR> राधेयं शल्यं स्वाञ्जल्यकेन च ॥ Mb. 8. 45. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जिनेयः|आञ्जिनेय|आंजिनेयः
आञ्जिनेयः [अञ्जिन्यां भवः ढक्] A kind of insect, a kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटरूषः|आटरूष
आटरूषः [अटरूष एव, स्वार्थे अण्] N. of a tree, see अटरूष<BR> (Mar. अडुळसा). आटरूषकवर्णाभा हयाः पाण्डयानुयायिनाम् Mb. 7. 23. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविकः|आटविक
आटविकः [अटव्यां चरति भवो वा ठक्]<BR>—1 A forester, a woodman, inhabitant of a forest; Mb. 12. 59. 48; Ms. 9. 257.<BR>—2 A pioneer.<BR>—3 One of the six kinds of armies.<BR>—4 A chief of wild-tribes; Kau. A. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटवी
आटवी [अटव्याः सव्निकृष्टा पूः अण्] N. of a city of the Yavanas in the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटव्य
आटव्य <i>a.</i> See आटविक (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिः|आटि
आटिः [आ-अट्-इण्]<BR>—1 A kind of bird (शरारि) (also written आटि) cf. आटिराडी शराडी<BR> च शरारी राडिराडिका<BR>—2 A sort of fish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आटिमुखः, आटिमुखम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिमुखः
आटिः + -मुखः, -मुखम् a surgical instrument used in blood letting (so called<BR> from its being like the beak of the bird आटि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिमुखम्
आटिः + -मुखः, -मुखम् a surgical instrument used in blood letting (so called<BR> from its being like the beak of the bird आटि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक
आटिक, आटिक्य <i>a.</i> [आटाय गमनाय प्रवृत्तः ठन्, ष्यञ्<BR> वा] Able to wander, being on a voyage or journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक्य
आटिक, आटिक्य <i>a.</i> [आटाय गमनाय प्रवृत्तः ठन्, ष्यञ्<BR> वा] Able to wander, being on a voyage or journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिकी
आटिक, आटिक्य + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 A woman fit to go out (अनुपजातपयोधरादिस्त्रीव्यञ्जना Śaṅkara.).<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Uṣasti; Ch. Up. 1. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकनम्
आटीकनम् [आटीक्-ल्युट्] The leaping motion of a calf; so आटीलकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकरः|आटीकर
आटीकरः A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोपः|आटोप
आटोपः [आ-तुप्-घञ् पृषो˚ टत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 Pride, self-conceit, arrogance; साटोपम् proudly, in a stately or<BR> majestic manner, frequently used as a stage-direction.<BR>—2 Swelling, spreading, expanding, puffing; Prov. फटाटोपो भयंकरः;<BR> said also of clouds, अद्यापि साटोपा मेघा दृश्यन्ते Pt. 1; Śi. 3. 74.<BR>—3 Flatulence (in the belly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरः|आडम्बर|आडंबरः
आडम्बरः [आ-डम्ब्-क्षेपे, अरन्]<BR>—1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>—2 Show; means, external appendage; विरचितनारसिंहरूपाडम्बरम्<BR> K. 5, 309; निर्गुणः शोभते नैव विपुलाडम्बरोऽपि ना Bv. 1. 115.<BR>—3 The sounding of a trumpet as a sign<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">Page0321-1</a>]<BR> of attack.<BR>—4 Commencement.<BR>—5 Fury, anger, passion; दन्तिनामाडम्बररवेण K. 114.<BR>—6 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>—7 The roaring of clouds and of elephants; धातः किन्नु विधौ विधातुमुचितो<BR> धाराधराडम्बरः Bv. 1. 4. cf. … आडम्बरोऽस्त्रियाम् । तुर्यशब्दे च<BR> संरम्भे गजेन्द्राणां च गर्जिते । Nm.<BR>—8 The eyelid.<BR>—9 A drum used in a battle; काचिदाडम्बरं नारीभुजसंभोगपीडितम्<BR> Rām. 5. 10. 45.<BR>—10 (Hence) A charge sounded by musical instruments; the din or uproar<BR> of the battle; Mb. 7. 72. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरम्
आडम्बरः + .{@-रम्@} Rubbing and kneading the body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आडम्बराघातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0320-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बराघातः|आडम्बराघात
आडम्बरः + -आघातः One who beats a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरिन्|आडंबरिन्
आडम्बरिन् <i>a.</i> Arrogant, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडिः|आडि
आडिः = आटि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडूः
आडूः [अल्-ऊ, लस्य डः नि˚ वृद्धि Tv.]<BR>—1 A raft, a float.<BR>—2 Moon; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकः|आढक|आढकं
आढकः, -कम्<BR> A measure of grain, the 4th of a Droṇa = 4 Prasthas^1 = 16<BR> Kuḍavas (= nearly 7 lbs. 11 ozs. avoir.); अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत् कुञ्चिः कुञ्चयोऽष्टौ<BR> तु पुष्कलम् । पुष्कलानि च चत्वारि आढकः परिकीर्तितः ॥<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकम्
आढकः, -कम्<BR> A measure of grain, the 4th of a Droṇa = 4 Prasthas^1 = 16<BR> Kuḍavas (= nearly 7 lbs. 11 ozs. avoir.); अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत् कुञ्चिः कुञ्चयोऽष्टौ<BR> तु पुष्कलम् । पुष्कलानि च चत्वारि आढकः परिकीर्तितः ॥<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकी
आढकः, -कम् + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 A kind of pulse (Mar. तूर).<BR>—2 A kind of fragrant earth (Mar. गोपीचंदन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकिक|आढकिकः
आढकिक, आढकीन <i>a.</i> [cf. आचितिक] Holding an Āḍhaka,<BR> sown with an Āḍhaka of seed; cooking an Āḍhaka (of rice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकीन|आढकीनः
आढकिक, आढकीन <i>a.</i> [cf. आचितिक] Holding an Āḍhaka,<BR> sown with an Āḍhaka of seed; cooking an Āḍhaka (of rice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य <i>a.</i> [आ-ध्यै-क पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>—1 Rich, wealthy; आढ्योऽभिजनवानस्मि कोऽन्योऽस्ति सद्दृशो मया Bg. 16. 15;<BR> Pt. 5. 8; Ms. 8. 169.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Rich in, abounding in, possessing abundantly, with instr. or<BR> as the last member of comp.; सत्य˚ Pt. 3. 9 very truthful; वंशसंपल्लावण्याढ्याय<BR> Dk. 18; एवमादिगुणैराढ्यः Vet.; समुद्रमिव रत्नाढ्यम् Rām.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Mixed with, watered with; गन्धाढ्य; स्रज उत्तमगन्धाढ्याः<BR> Mb.; मूत्राढ्यैः करञ्जफलसर्षपैः Suśr.<BR>—3 Abundant, copious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आढ्याडु, आढ्यकुलीन, आढ्यचर, आढ्यरोगः, आढ्यवातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्याडु
आढ्य + -आडु <i>a.</i> striving to get wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यकुलीन
आढ्य + -कुलीन <i>a.</i> [आढ्यकुले भवः ख] Descended from a rich family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यचर
आढ्य + -चर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भूतपूर्व आढ्यः चरट्] once opulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यरोगः|आढ्यरोग
आढ्य + -रोगः Rheumatism, gout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यवातः|आढ्यवात
आढ्य + -वातः [आढ्यो वातो यत्र] a convulsive or rheumatic palsy of the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंकरण|आढ्यङ्करण
आढ्यंकरण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [P. III. 2. 56.] Enriching. आढ्यंकरणविक्रान्तो<BR> महिषस्य सुरद्विषः Bk. 6. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंकरणम्
आढ्यंकरण + .{@-णम्@} The means of enriching, wealth, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंभविष्णु|आढ्यम्भविष्णु
आढ्यंभविष्णु, -भावुक <i>a.</i><BR> [P. III. 2. 57] Becoming rich or eminent. आढ्यंभविष्णुर्यशसा कुमारः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंभावुक|आढ्यम्भावुक
आढ्यंभविष्णु, -भावुक <i>a.</i><BR> [P. III. 2. 57] Becoming rich or eminent. आढ्यंभविष्णुर्यशसा कुमारः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यता
आढ्यता Opulence, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणक|आणकः
आणक <i>a.</i> [अणक एव स्वार्थे अण्] Low, inferior, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणकम्
आणक + .{@-कम्@} Sexual enjoyment in a particular position; आणकं सुरतं<BR> नाम दम्पत्योः पार्श्वसंस्थयोः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणव
आणव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Exceedingly small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवम्
आणव + .{@-वम्@} Exceeding smallness or minuteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवीन|आणवीनं
आणवीन <i>a.</i> [अणुधान्यानां भवनं क्षेत्रं वा खञ्] धान्यानां<BR> भवने क्षेत्रे खञ् P. V. 2. 1. Bearing or fit to bear Aṇu Panicum Miliaceum<BR> (Mar. कांग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणि|आणिः
आणि <i>m., f.</i> [अण्-इण्-स्त्रियां वा डीप्]<BR>—1 The pin of the axle of a cart, the linch-pin आणिं न रथ्यममृताधि<BR> तस्थुः Rv. 1. 35. 6.<BR>—2 The part of the leg just above the knee (जानुन ऊर्ध्वमुभयतस्त्र्यङ्गुलमणिर्नाम Suśr.)<BR>—3 The corner of a house.<BR>—4 A boundary, limit.<BR>—5 The edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्ड|आंड|आण्डः
आण्ड <i>a.</i> [अण्डे भवः अण्] Born from an egg (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डः|आण्ड|आंड
आण्ड + .{@-डः@} An epithet of Hiraṇyagarbha or Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डम्
आण्ड + .{@-डम्@}<BR>—1 A multitude of eggs, brood.<BR>—2 Scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डौ
आण्ड + .{@-डौ@} (Ved.) The testicles. क्रोधो वृक्कौ मन्युराण्डौ प्रजा शेपः Av. 9. 7. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आण्डकोशः, आण्डज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डकोशः|आण्डकोश
आण्ड + -कोशः An egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डज|आण्डजः
आण्ड + -ज <i>a.</i> born from eggs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डजः|आण्डज
आण्ड + -ज + .({@-जः@}) a bird or a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डजम्
आण्ड + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) the body of a bird; आण्डजं जीवजमुद्भिज्जम् Ch. Up. 6. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डी|आंडी
आण्डी Ved. A testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीक|आंडीक
आण्डीक <i>a.</i> Bearing eggs. आण्डीकं कुमुदं संतनोति Av. 4. 34. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीर|आंडीर
आण्डीर <i>a.</i> [आण्डमस्त्यस्य ईरच्]<BR>—1 Having many eggs.<BR>—2 Grown up, full-grown (as a bull).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्
आत् The letter आ. <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Afterwards, then; generally used antithetically to यद्, यदा, यदि<BR> and then sometimes strengthened by the particles अह, उ, इद् &c.<BR>—2 Then, further, also, and (अपि च).<BR>—3 Some-times it only strengthens the meaning of another word or gives<BR> emphasis to an interrogative pronoun like उ, अङ्ग, नु added to किम्<BR> (possibly, at all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत|आतः
आत <i>a.</i> [आ-अत्-अच्] Spread around.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतः|आत
आत + .{@-तः@} Ved.<BR>—1 A quarter of the sky.<BR>—2 A scaffold.<BR>—3 The frame of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्च्|आतंच्
आतञ्च् €7 P. To coagulate, to cause to shrink or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्कः|आतङ्क|आतंक|आतंकः
आतङ्कः [आ-तञ्च्-घञ्-कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 Disease, sickness of the body; दीर्घतीव्रामयग्रस्तं ब्राह्मणं गामथापि<BR> वा । दृष्ट्वा पथि निरातङ्कं कृत्वा वा ब्रह्महा शुचिः ॥ Y. 3. 245.<BR>—2 Fever.<BR>—3 Pain, affliction (of the mind), disquietude; anguish, agony; किन्निमित्तोयमातङ्कः;<BR> आतङ्कस्फूरितकठोरगर्भगुवीम् U. 1. 49; Ś. 3; V. 3.<BR>—4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>—5 Fear, apprehension; पुरुषायुषजीविन्यो निरातङ्का निरीतयः R. 1. 63;<BR> fright, terror; दत्तातङ्कोऽङ्गनानाम् Ratn. 2. 2.<BR>—6 The sound of a drum or tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्कम्
आतङ्कः + .{@-कम्@} The constellation भरणी; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्चनम्
आतञ्चनम्<BR>—1 Causing to coagulate or curdle, casting butter-milk into heated milk to turn it.<BR>—2 Causing to contract in general.<BR>—3 Curdled milk.<BR>—4 That which causes coagulation, a runnet.<BR>—5 A sort of whey.<BR>—6 Conveying.<BR>—7 Gratifying, satisfying.<BR>—8 Casting away, destroying.<BR>—9 Danger, calamity.<BR>—10 Speed, velocity.<BR>—11 Calcining, adding flux to metals in fusion.<BR>—12 The flux so used.<BR>—13 Making fat; cf. आतञ्चनं प्रतीवापे जवनाप्यायनार्थयोः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन्
आतन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To extend, stretch over, overspread, cover; निषादिवक्षःस्थलमातनोति<BR> Ki. 16. 15 pervade,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">Page0322-1</a>]<BR> penetrate; Ki. 7. 25.<BR>—2 To spread, diffuse.<BR>—3 To cause, produce; आनन्दनेन जडतां पुनरातनोति U. 3. 12; Ki. 6. 18, 7. 39;<BR> K. 176; Māl. 5. 9; Mv. 4. 31.<BR>—4 To bring to pass, effect, accomplish, do, perform; सुरतमाततान<BR> K. 57; सपर्याम् 64.<BR>—5 To illuminate.<BR>—6 To take hold of; seek to attain.<BR>—7 To assume a hostile attitude.<BR>—8 To stretch (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0321-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतत
आतत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread, extended.<BR>—2 Stretched (as a bow-string); मौर्वीं धनुषि चातता R. 1. 19; ˚ज्य<BR> stretched out on the bow; आततज्यमकरोत् स संसदा 11. 45, 16. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन् <i>a.</i> or <i>s.</i> [आततेन विस्तीर्णेन शस्त्रादिना अयितुं<BR> शीलमस्य Tv.]<BR>—1 ‘One whose bow is stretched to take anotherʼs life’, endeavouring to<BR> kill some one; a desperado; गुरुं वा बालवृद्धौ वा ब्राह्मणं वा बहुश्रुतम् ।<BR> आततायिनमायान्तं हन्यादेवाविचारयन् ॥ Ms. 8. 350-51; Mb. 3. 36. 10,<BR> Bg. 1. 36.<BR>—2 Anyone who commits a heinous crime; such as a thief, ravisher, murderer,<BR> incendiary, a felon &c.; अग्निदो गरदश्चैव शस्त्रोन्मत्तो धनापहः ।<BR> क्षेत्रदारहरश्चैतान् षड् विद्यादाततायिनः ॥ Śukra. {@˚ता, -त्वम्@}<BR> murdering, stealing, destroying &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतताविन्
आतताविन् <i>a.</i> Ved. One whose bow is stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतनम्
आतनम्<BR>—1 Spreading, penetrating, expanding.<BR>—2 Sight, view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतनि
आतनि <i>a.</i> Ved. [तन्-इन्] Spreading; pervading; त्वं विशिक्षुरसि<BR> यज्ञमातनिः Rv. 2. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतानः|आतान
आतानः [तन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 An extended cord or string; Vāj. 6. 12.<BR>—2 Long extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
आतप् €1 P. To radiate, heat, blaze; inflame, to cause to glow. ━<i>pass.</i><BR> To suffer pain, be afflicted; to inflict (austerities) upon oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
आतप् <i>a.</i> Ved. Heating (आतापिन्). <i>f.</i> Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आतप <i>a.</i> Ved. Causing pain or affliction; भीमस्तुविष्माञ्चर्षणिभ्य<BR> आतपः Rv. 1. 55. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपः|आतप
आतप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Heat (of the sun, fire &c.), sunshine; आतपायोज्झितं धान्यम् Mb.<BR> exposed to the sun; तमातपक्लान्तम् R. 2. 13; शीतातपाभिघातान्<BR> Ms. 12. 77; प्रचण्ड˚ Ṛs. 1. 11; सूर्य˚ 10; Me. 110; बालातपः<BR> Ms. 4. 69 the morning sun; ˚आक्रान्त exposed to heat.<BR>—2 Light; छायातपौ ब्रह्मविदो वदन्ति Kaṭh. 3. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आतपात्ययः, आतपाभावः, आतपोदकम्, आतपत्रम्, आतपत्रकम्, आतपलङ्घनम्, आतपवर्ष्य, आतपवारणम्, आतपशुष्क<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपात्ययः|आतपात्यय
आतप + -अत्ययः passing of the sunʼs heat, sunset; आतपात्ययसंक्षिप्तनीवारासु R. 1. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपाभावः|आतपाभाव
आतप + -अभावः non-existence of the sunʼs heat, shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपोदकम्
आतप + -उदकम् mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्रम्
आतप + -त्रम्, -त्रकम् [आतपात् त्रायते, त्रै-क] an umbrella (of silk<BR> or leaves used as a parasol); तमातपक्लान्तमनातपत्रम् R. 2. 13, 47;<BR> पद्म˚ 4. 5; राज्यं स्वहस्तधृतदण्डमिवातपत्रम् Ś. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्रकम्
आतप + -त्रम्, -त्रकम् [आतपात् त्रायते, त्रै-क] an umbrella (of silk<BR> or leaves used as a parasol); तमातपक्लान्तमनातपत्रम् R. 2. 13, 47;<BR> पद्म˚ 4. 5; राज्यं स्वहस्तधृतदण्डमिवातपत्रम् Ś. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपलङ्घनम्
आतप + -लङ्घनम् being exposed to heat, catching the sun-stroke; आतपलङ्घनाद्बलवदस्वस्थशरीरा<BR> शकुन्तला Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवर्ष्य
आतप + -वर्ष्य <i>a.</i> (water &c.) produced by rain during sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवारणम्
आतप + -वारणम् [आतापं वारयति] an umbrella, parasol; नृपतिककुदं<BR> दत्त्वा यूने सितातपवारणम् R. 3. 70, 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपशुष्क
आतप + -शुष्क <i>a.</i> dried in the sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपनः|आतपन
आतपनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवत्|आतपवन्त्
आतपवत् <i>a.</i> Exposed to sunshine, sunny; शृङ्गाणि यस्यातपवन्ति<BR> सिद्धाः Ku. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपीय
आतपीय <i>a.</i> Sunny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्त
आतप्त <i>a.</i> Refined by heat (as gold).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्य
आतप्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Being in the sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतमाम्
आतमाम् <i>ind.</i> Very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिः|आतापि
आतापिः <i>m.^1</i> [आ-तप्-इण्] N. of a demon; आतापिर्भक्षितो येन<BR> वातापिश्च महासुरः । समुद्रः शोषितो येन स मेऽगस्त्यः प्रसीदतु ॥<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिन्
आतापि(यि)न् N. of a bird, a kite, falcon (Falco Cheela; Mar. घार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतायिन्
आतापि(यि)न् N. of a bird, a kite, falcon (Falco Cheela; Mar. घार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आताली
आताली <i>ind.</i> Compounded with अस्, भू and कृ; P. I. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिः|आति
आतिः A kind of acquatic bird. ता आतयो न तन्वः शुम्भत स्वा Rv. 10. 95. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिः|आति
आतिः = आटि q. v. (cf. P. III. 3. 108. Vārt. and Uṇ. 4. 130).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अतिथिषु साधुः ढञ्; अतिथये इदं ढक्]<BR>—1 Attentive to guests, hospitable (as a man); प्रत्युज्जगामातिथिमातिथेयः<BR> R. 5. 2, 12. 25 तमातिथेयी बहुमानपूर्वया Ku. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Proper for, or suited to, a guest, intended for a guest; आतिथेयः<BR> सत्कारः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेयम्
आतिथेय + .{@-यम्@} Hospitality; आतिथेयमनिवारितातिथिः Śi. 14. 38; Ms. 3. 18;<BR> सज्जातिथेया वयम् Mv. 2. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेयी
आतिथेय + .{@-यी@} Hospitality; Bv. 1. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य <i>a.</i> [अतिथेरिदं ष्यञ्] Hospitable, proper for a guest<BR> &c. (= आतिथेय); हविरातिथ्यम्, आतिथ्या इष्टिः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्यः|आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं
आतिथ्य + .{@-थ्यः@} A guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्यम्
आतिथ्य + .{@-थ्यम्@} or {@-थ्या@}<BR>—1 Hospitable reception, hospitality; तमातिथ्यक्रियाशान्तरथक्षोभपरिश्रमम् R. 1. 58.<BR>—2 a particular rite, the reception of Soma when it is brought to the<BR> sacrificial place (also called आतिथ्येष्टिः)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आतिथ्यरूप, आतिथ्यसत्कारः, आतिथ्यसत्क्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्या
आतिथ्य + .{@-थ्यम्@} or {@-थ्या@}<BR>—1 Hospitable reception, hospitality; तमातिथ्यक्रियाशान्तरथक्षोभपरिश्रमम् R. 1. 58.<BR>—2 a particular rite, the reception of Soma when it is brought to the<BR> sacrificial place (also called आतिथ्येष्टिः)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आतिथ्यरूप, आतिथ्यसत्कारः, आतिथ्यसत्क्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्यरूप
आतिथ्य + -रूप <i>a.</i> being in the place of the आतिथ्य sacrifice; आतिथ्यरूपं<BR> मासरम् Vāj. 19. 14<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्यसत्कारः|आतिथ्यसत्कार
आतिथ्य + -सत्कारः, -सत्क्रिया the rites of hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्यसत्क्रिया
आतिथ्य + -सत्कारः, -सत्क्रिया the rites of hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिदेशिक
आतिदेशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> (In gram.) Connected with अतिदेश q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरेक्यम्
आतिरे(रै)क्यम् [आतिरेक-ष्यञ्] Superfluity, excess, abundance. Ms. 11. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरैक्यम्
आतिरे(रै)क्यम् [आतिरेक-ष्यञ्] Superfluity, excess, abundance. Ms. 11. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिवाहिक
आतिवाहिक <i>a.</i> [अतिवाहे नियुक्तः ठक्] Employed to convey to<BR> the other world; आतिवाहिकास्तल्लिङ्गात् Br. Sūt. 4. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिवाहिकम्
आतिवाहिक + .{@-कम्@} An epithet of the <i>Sūkṣma Śarīra</i> (in Sāṅ. Phil.)<BR> from its surpassing the wind in swiftness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशयिक
आतिशयिक <i>a.</i> Super-abundant; व्याप्तमातिशयिकेन रसेन Śi. 10. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशय्यम्
आतिशय्यम् [अतिशय-स्वार्थे-ष्यञ्] Excess, abundance, large quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिष्ठम्
आतिष्ठम् [अतिष्ठस्य भावः अण्] Being a universal ruler (अतिष्ठ) (Ait. Br.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0322-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिष्ठद्गु
आतिष्ठद्गु [तिष्ठन्ति गावः यस्मिन् काले दोहाय] <i>ind.</i> Upto the<BR> time when cows stand to be milked (after an hour or an hour and a half<BR> after evening). आतिष्ठद्गु जपन् सन्ध्यां प्रकान्तामायतीगवम् Bk. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुः|आतु
आतुः [अत्-उण्] A raft, float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुच्
आतुच् <i>f.</i> Evening, growing dusk; यदद्य सूर उदिते यन्मध्यंदिन<BR> आतुचि Rv. 8. 27. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुज्
आतुज् <i>m.</i> Destroyer of enemies or giver of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुजि
आतुजि <i>a.</i> Ved. [तुज्-इन्]<BR>—1 Rushing on, hastening towards; पिबतं सोममातुजी Rv. 7. 66. 18.<BR>—2 Carrying off (आदातृ).<BR>—3 Injuring, destructive (हिंसक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुद्
आतुद् €6 U. To strike, push, spur on, stir up. प्रतोदेनातुदन्भृशम् Ms. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोदिन्
आतोदिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Striking, pushing, pricking; आतोदिनौ नितोदिनावथो<BR> संतोदिनावुत (अपि नह्यामि) Av. 7. 95. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्यम्
आतोद्यम्, -द्यकम्<BR> A musical instrument; आतोद्यविन्यासादिका विधयः Ve. 1;<BR> स्रजमातोद्यशिरोनिवेशिताम् R. 8. 34, 15. 88; U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्यकम्
आतोद्यम्, -द्यकम्<BR> A musical instrument; आतोद्यविन्यासादिका विधयः Ve. 1;<BR> स्रजमातोद्यशिरोनिवेशिताम् R. 8. 34, 15. 88; U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर <i>a.</i> [ईषदर्थे आ, अत्-उरच्]<BR>—1 Hurt, injured.<BR>—2 Suffering from, influenced or affected by, tormented, afflicted; रावणावरजा<BR> तत्र राघवं मदनातुरा R. 12. 32; Ku. 4. 25; so काम˚, भय˚, व्याधि˚ &c.<BR>—3 Sick (in body or mind), disabled, diseased; आकाशेशास्तु विज्ञेया बालवृद्धकृशातुराः<BR> Ms. 4. 184, 6. 77.<BR>—4 Eager, over-anxious; M. 2.<BR>—5 Weak, feeble, incapable of doing anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुरः|आतुर
आतुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A patient, one suffering from a disease V. 3; आतुराणां चिकित्सकाः Pt. 1. 155.<BR>—2 Illness, disease; आतुरे व्यसने प्राप्ते Pt. 5. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आतुरशाला, आतुरसंन्यासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुरशाला
आतुर + -शाला a hospital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुरसंन्यासः|आतुरसन्न्यास
आतुर + -संन्यासः a kind of संन्यास (taken by a person when sick<BR> and grown hopeless of life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर्यम्
आतुर्यम् [आतुरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 A kind of fever.<BR>—2 Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृद्
आतृद् €7 P.<BR>—1 To split, sever, pierce.<BR>—2 To push open, open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्दनम्
आतर्दनम् Pushing open, opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृण्ण
आतृण्ण <i>p. p.</i> [आ-तृद्-क्त] Pierced, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृण्णम्
आतृण्ण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 An opening, hole.<BR>—2 An open wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्
आतृप् €4. €5. €6 P. To be satisfied; आ यत् तृपन्मरुतो वावशानाः<BR> Rv. 7. 56. 10. ━<i>Caus.</i> To satisfy; अनुकामं तर्पयेथामिन्द्रावरुण<BR> राय आ Rv. 1. 17. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्पणम्
आतर्पणम्<BR>—1 Satisfaction, gratification.<BR>—2 Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>—3 White-washing the wall, floor or seat (on festive occasions) (मङ्गलालेपनम्).<BR>—4 The pigment used for the above purpose; आतर्पणं प्रीणने स्यान्मङ्गलालेपनेऽपि च Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्यः|आतृप्य|आतृप्यं
आतृप्यः A kind of tree, the custard apple tree (Mar. सीताफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्यम्
आतृप्यः + .{@-प्यम्@} The fruit of the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतॄ
आतॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To pass through or over; उक्षन्ते अश्वान् तरुषन्त आ रजः Rv. 5. 59. 1.<BR>—2 To cross over.<BR>—3 To overcome.<BR>—4 To enlarge, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतरः|आतर
आतरः, -आतारः<BR> [आतरति अनेन आतॄ अप्-घञ्-वा]<BR>—1 Fare for being ferried over a river, passage-money, freight.<BR>—2 Distance to be crossed by a boat &c.; आतरलाघवहेतोर्मुरहर तरणिं<BR> तवालम्बे । Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतारः|आतार
आतरः, -आतारः<BR> [आतरति अनेन आतॄ अप्-घञ्-वा]<BR>—1 Fare for being ferried over a river, passage-money, freight.<BR>—2 Distance to be crossed by a boat &c.; आतरलाघवहेतोर्मुरहर तरणिं<BR> तवालम्बे । Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार्य
आतार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be crossed.<BR>—2 Landing, coming to shore (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आत्त See under आदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन् <i>m.</i> [अत्-मनिण् Uṇ. 4. 152 said to be from अन् to<BR> breathe also] ‘आत्मा यत्नो धृतिर्बुद्धिः स्वभावो ब्रह्मवर्ष्म च’ इत्यमरः<BR>—1 The soul, the individual soul, the breath, the principle of life and<BR> sensation; किमात्मना यो न जितेन्द्रियो भवेत् H. 1; आत्मानं रथिनं<BR> विद्धि शरीरं रथमेव तु Kaṭh. 3. 3. (In आत्मा नदी संयमपुण्यतीर्था<BR> H. 4. 87 आत्मन् is compared to a river).<BR>—2 Self, oneself; in this sense mostly used reflexively for all three<BR> persons and in the singular number, masculine gender, whatever be the gender<BR> or number of the noun to which it refers; अनया चिन्तयात्मापि मे न प्रतिभाति<BR> Ratn. 1; आश्रमदर्शनेन आत्मानं पुनीमहे Ś. 1; गुप्तं ददृशुरात्मानं<BR> सर्वाः स्वप्नेषु वामनैः R. 10. 60, 4. 35, 14. 57; Ku. 6. 20; देवी<BR> … प्राप्तप्रसवमात्मानं गङ्गादेव्यां विमुञ्चति U. 7. 2; गोपायन्ति<BR> कुलस्त्रिय आत्मानमात्मना Mb.; K. 107; sometimes used in pl. also; आत्मनः<BR> स्तुवन्ति Śi. 17. 19; Māl. 8.<BR>—3 Supreme deity and soul of the universe, Supreme Soul, Brahman; तस्माद्वा<BR> एतस्मादात्मन आकाशः संभूतः T. Up. 2. 1. 1; Ms. 1. 15, 12. 24.<BR>—4 Essence, nature; काव्यस्यात्मा ध्वनिः S. D., see आत्मक below.<BR>—5 Character, peculiarity; आत्मा यक्ष्मस्य नश्यति Rv. 10. 97. 11.<BR>—6 The natural temperament or disposition; Bhāg. 11. 22. 20.<BR>—7 The person or whole body (considered as one and opposed to the separate<BR> members of it); स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वी क्रान्त्वा मेरुरिवात्मना R. 1. 14;<BR> योस्यात्मनः कारायिता Ms. 12. 12; Ki. 9. 66.<BR>—8 Mind, intellect; मन्दात्मन्, नष्टात्मन्, महात्मन् &c. अथ रामः<BR> प्रसन्नात्मा श्रुत्वा वायुसुतस्य ह Rām. 6. 18. 1.<BR>—9 The understanding; cf. आत्मसंपन्न, आत्मवत् &c.<BR>—10 Thinking faculty, the faculty of thought and reason.<BR>—11 Spirit, vitality, courage; त्यक्त्वाऽऽत्मानमथाब्रवीत् Mb. 12. 180. 6.<BR>—12 Form, image; आत्मानमाधाय Ku. 3. 24 assuming his own form; 2. 61;<BR> संरोपितेऽप्यात्मनि Ś. 6. 24 myself being implanted in her.<BR>—13 A son; ‘आत्मा वै पुत्रनामासि’ इति श्रुतेः । तस्यात्मा शितिकण्ठस्य Śi. 2. 61.<BR>—14 Care, efforts, pain.<BR>—15 The sun.<BR>—16 Fire.<BR>—17 Wind, air.<BR>—18 Mental quality; बाहुश्रुत्यं तपस्त्यागः श्रद्धा यज्ञक्रिया क्षमा ।<BR> भावशुद्धिर्दया सत्यं संयमश्चात्मसंपदः ॥ Mb. 12. 167. 5. आत्मन्<BR> is used as the last member of comp. in the sense of ‘made or consisting of’<BR>; see आत्मक. The form त्मन् is also found to be used; कृतार्थं<BR> मन्यते त्मानं Mb. [cf. Gr. <i>atmos, aitmen</i>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आत्माधीन, आत्मानुरूप, आत्मानुगमनम्, आत्मापहारः, आत्मापहारकः, आत्मादिष्ट, आत्मानन्द, आत्माराम, आत्माशिन्, आत्माश्रय, आत्मेश्वर, आत्मोदयः, आत्मोद्भव, आत्मोपजीविन्, आत्मोपनिषद्, आत्मोपम, आत्मौपम्यम्, आत्मकर्मन्, आत्मकाम, आत्मकार्यम्, आत्मकृत, आत्मगत, आत्मगतिः, आत्मगुप्ता, आत्मगुप्तिः, आत्मग्राहिन्, आत्मघातः, आत्मघातकः, आत्मघातिन्, आत्मघोषः, आत्मजः, आत्मजन्मन्, आत्मजा, आत्मजयः, आत्मज्योतिस्, आत्मज्ञः, आत्मविद्, आत्मज्ञानम्, आत्मतत्त्वम्, आत्मतृप्त, आत्मतुष्टि, आत्मत्यागः, आत्मत्यागिन्, आत्मत्राणम्, आत्मदर्शः, आत्मदर्शनम्, आत्मदा, आत्मदानम्, आत्मदूषि, आत्मदेवता, आत्मद्रोहिन्, आत्मनित्य, आत्मनिन्दा, आत्मनिवेदनम्, आत्मनिष्ठ, आत्मपराजित, आत्मपुराणम्, आत्मप्रत्ययिक, आत्मप्रबोधः, आत्मप्रभ, आत्मप्रवादः, आत्मप्रशंसा, आत्मबन्धुः, आत्मबान्धवः, आत्मबोधः, आत्मभावः, आत्मभू, आत्मयोनिः, आत्मभूत, आत्मभूयम्, आत्ममात्रा, आत्ममानिन्, आत्ममूर्तिः, आत्ममूल, आत्ममूलि, आत्ममूली, आत्मयाजिन्, आत्मयोनिः, आत्मरक्षा, आत्मलाभः, आत्मलोमन्, आत्मवञ्चक, आत्मवञ्चना, आत्मवधः, आत्मवध्या, आत्महत्या, आत्मवर्ग्य, आत्मवश, आत्मवश्य, आत्मविक्रयः, आत्मविद्, आत्मविद्या, आत्मविवृद्धिः, आत्मवृद्धिः, आत्मवीर, आत्मवृत्तम्, आत्मवृत्तान्तः, आत्मवृत्ति, आत्मशक्तिः, आत्मशल्या, आत्मशुद्धिः, आत्मश्लाघा, आत्मस्तुतिः, आत्मसंयमः, आत्मसंस्थ, आत्मसतत्त्वम्, आत्मसद्, आत्मसंतुष्ट, आत्मसनि, आत्मसम, आत्मसंदेहः, आत्मसंभवः, आत्मसमुद्भवः, आत्मसंपन्न, आत्मसंभावना, आत्मसिद्धिः, आत्मसुख, आत्मस्थ, आत्महन्, आत्महननम्, आत्महत्या, आत्महित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीन|आत्माधीनः
आत्मन् + -अधीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dependent on oneself, independent.<BR>—2 sentient, existing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीनः|आत्माधीन
आत्मन् + -अधीन + .({@-नः@})<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 a wifeʼs brother. —3 the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">Page0324-1</a>]<BR> jester or विदूषक (in dramatic literature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0323-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मानुरूप
आत्मन् + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i> worthy of oneself; तस्यामात्मानुरूपायामात्मजन्मसमुत्सुकः<BR> Ku. 1. 18; R. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मानुगमनम्
आत्मन् + -अनुगमनम् peronal attendance; शश्वदात्मानुगमनेन गाम् R. 1. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मापहारः|आत्मापहार
आत्मन् + -अपहारः concealing oneself; कथं वा आत्मापहारं करोमि Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मापहारकः|आत्मापहारक
आत्मन् + -अपहारकः one who pretends to belong to a higher class than<BR> his own, an impostor, a pretender; योऽन्यथा सन्तमात्मानमन्यथा सत्सु<BR> भाषते । स पापकृत्तमो लोके स्तेन आत्मापहारकः ॥ Ms. 4. 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मादिष्ट|आत्मादिष्टः
आत्मन् + -आदिष्ट <i>a.</i> self-counselled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मादिष्टः|आत्मादिष्ट
आत्मन् + -आदिष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@}) a treaty dictated by the party wishing it himself; स्वसैन्येन<BR> तु संघानमात्मादिष्ट उदाहृतः H. 4. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मानन्द
आत्मन् + -आनन्द <i>a.</i> Rejoicing in the soul or Supreme Spirit; आत्ममिथुनः<BR> आत्मानन्दः Ch. Up. 7. 25. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माराम
आत्मन् + -आराम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 striving to get knowledge (as an ascetic or योगिन्), seeking spiritual<BR> knowledge; आत्मारामा विहितरतयो निर्विकल्पे समाधौ Ve. 1. 23.<BR>—2 self-pleased, delighted in self; आत्मारामः फलाशी. see आत्मानन्द<BR> Bh. 3. 93; cf. Bg. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माशिन्
आत्मन् + -आशिन् <i>m.</i> a fish supposed to feed on its young, or on the weakest<BR> of its species; cf. मत्स्या इव जना नित्यं भक्षयन्ति परस्परम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माश्रय|आत्माश्रयः
आत्मन् + -आश्रय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dependent on oneself or on his own mind.<BR>—2 About or relating to oneself; कौलीनमात्माश्रयमाचचक्षे R. 14. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माश्रयः|आत्माश्रय
आत्मन् + -आश्रय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 self dependence.<BR>—2 innate idea, abstract knowledge independent of the thing to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मेश्वर
आत्मन् + -ईश्वर <i>a.</i> Self-possessed, master of self; आत्मेश्वराणां<BR> न हि जातु विघ्नाः समाधिभेदप्रभवो भवन्ति Ku. 3. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोदयः|आत्मोदय
आत्मन् + -उदयः self-exaltation or elevation; आत्मोदयः परज्यानिर्द्वयं<BR> नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भव|आत्मोद्भवः
आत्मन् + -उद्भव <i>a.</i> born or produced from oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भवः|आत्मोद्भव
आत्मन् + -उद्भव + .({@-वः@})<BR>—1 a son; आत्मोद्भवे वर्णचतुष्टयस्य R. 18. 12.<BR>—2 Cupid.<BR>—3 sorrow, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भवा
आत्मन् + -उद्भव + .({@-वा@})<BR>—1 daughter.<BR>—2 intellect.<BR>—3 N. of a plant (माषपर्णी; Mar. रानौडीद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपजीविन्
आत्मन् + -उपजीविन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 one who lives by his own labour; Ms. 7. 138.<BR>—2 a day-labourer.<BR>—3 one who lives by his wife (Kull. on Ms. 8. 362).<BR>—4 an actor, public performer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपनिषद्
आत्मन् + -उपनिषद् <i>f.</i> N. of an उपनिषद् which treats of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपम|आत्मोपमः
आत्मन् + -उपम <i>a.</i> like oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपमः|आत्मोपम
आत्मन् + -उपम + .({@-मः@}) a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मौपम्यम्
आत्मन् + -औपम्यम् Likeness to self. आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र Bg. 6. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकर्मन्|आत्मकर्म्मन्
आत्मन् + -कर्मन् Oneʼs own duty; आत्मकर्मक्षमं देहं क्षात्रो धर्म इवाश्रितः R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकाम
आत्मन् + -काम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 loving oneself, possessed of self-conceit, proud; आत्मकामा सदा चण्डी<BR> Rām. 2. 70. 10.<BR>—2 loving Brahman or the Supreme Spirit only; भगवन् वयमात्मकामाः<BR> Maitr. Up. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकार्यम्
आत्मन् + -कार्यम् oneʼs own business, private affair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकृत
आत्मन् + -कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-executed, done by oneself; पौरा ह्यात्मकृताद्दुःखाद्विप्रमोच्या<BR> नृपात्मजैः Rām. 2. 46. 23.<BR>—2 done against oneʼs own self; Vāj. 8. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगत|आत्मगतं
आत्मन् + -गत <i>a.</i> produced in oneʼs mind; ˚तो मनोरथः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगतम्
आत्मन् + -गत + .({@-तम्@}) <i>ind.</i> aside (to oneself) being considered to be spoken<BR> privately (opp. प्रकाशम् aloud); frequently used as a stage-direction<BR> in dramas; it is the same as स्वगतम् which is thus defined; अश्राव्यं<BR> खलु यद्वस्तु तदिह स्वगतं मतम् S. D. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगतिः|आत्मगति
आत्मन् + -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 course of the soulʼs existence.<BR>—2 oneʼs own course; Bhāg. 5. 17. 3. ˚गत्या by oneʼs own act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगतिगत्या
आत्मन् + -गतिः + ˚गत्या by oneʼs own act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगुप्ता
आत्मन् + -गुप्ता The plant Mucuna Pruritus Hook (Mar. कुयली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगुप्तिः|आत्मगुप्ति
आत्मन् + -गुप्तिः <i>f.</i> a cave, the hiding place of an animal, lair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मग्राहिन्
आत्मन् + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> selfish, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातः|आत्मघात
आत्मन् + -घातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">Page0324-2</a>]<BR>—1 suicide.<BR>—2 heresy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातकः|आत्मघातक
आत्मन् + -घातकः, -घातिन्<BR>—1 a suicide, a self-destroyer; K. 174; व्यापादयेद् वृथात्मानं स्वयं<BR> योऽग्न्युदकादिभिः । अवैधेनैव मार्गेण आत्मघाती स उच्यते ॥<BR>—2 a heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातिन्
आत्मन् + -घातकः, -घातिन्<BR>—1 a suicide, a self-destroyer; K. 174; व्यापादयेद् वृथात्मानं स्वयं<BR> योऽग्न्युदकादिभिः । अवैधेनैव मार्गेण आत्मघाती स उच्यते ॥<BR>—2 a heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघोषः|आत्मघोष
आत्मन् + -घोषः<BR>—1 a cock (calling out to himself).<BR>—2 a crow.<BR>—3 One who flatters himself. cf. आत्मघोषो वायसे स्यादात्मस्तुतिपरेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजः|आत्मज
आत्मन् + -जः, -जन्मन् <i>m.</i>, {@-जातः, -प्रभवः, -संभवः, -समुद्भवः@}<BR>—1 a son; यः स वासवनिर्जेता रावणस्यात्मसंभवः Rām. 6. 86. 33;<BR> हतान्निहन्मेह नरर्षभेण वयं सुरेशात्मसमुद्भवेन Mb. 7. 118. 2;<BR> तमात्मजन्मानमजं चकार R. 5. 36; तस्यामात्मानुरूपायामात्मजन्मसमुत्सुकः<BR> R. 1. 33; Māl. 1; Ku. 6. 28.<BR>—2 Cupid; ममायमात्मप्रभवो भूयस्त्वमुपयास्यति Rām. 4. 1. 34.<BR>—3 a descendant; मृगयां विचरन्कश्चिद्विजने जनकात्मजः Mb. 12. 309. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजन्मन्
आत्मन् + -जः, -जन्मन् <i>m.</i>, {@-जातः, -प्रभवः, -संभवः, -समुद्भवः@}<BR>—1 a son; यः स वासवनिर्जेता रावणस्यात्मसंभवः Rām. 6. 86. 33;<BR> हतान्निहन्मेह नरर्षभेण वयं सुरेशात्मसमुद्भवेन Mb. 7. 118. 2;<BR> तमात्मजन्मानमजं चकार R. 5. 36; तस्यामात्मानुरूपायामात्मजन्मसमुत्सुकः<BR> R. 1. 33; Māl. 1; Ku. 6. 28.<BR>—2 Cupid; ममायमात्मप्रभवो भूयस्त्वमुपयास्यति Rām. 4. 1. 34.<BR>—3 a descendant; मृगयां विचरन्कश्चिद्विजने जनकात्मजः Mb. 12. 309. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजा
आत्मन् + -जा<BR>—1 a daughter; वन्द्यं युगं चरणयोर्जनकात्मजायाः R. 13. 78; cf.<BR> नगात्मजा &c.<BR>—2 the reasoning faculty, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजयः|आत्मजय
आत्मन् + -जयः<BR>—1 oneʼs own victory.<BR>—2 victory over oneself, self-denial or abnegation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्योतिस्
आत्मन् + -ज्योतिस् <i>n.</i> The light of the soul or Supreme Spirit (चैतन्य);<BR> कौस्तुभव्यपदेशेन स्वात्मज्योतिर्बिभर्त्यजः Bhāg. 12. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञः|आत्मज्ञ
आत्मन् + -ज्ञः, -विद् <i>m.</i> a sage, one who knows himself; तस्मादात्मज्ञं<BR> ह्यर्चयेद्भूतिकामः Muṇḍ. 3. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्
आत्मन् + -ज्ञः, -विद् <i>m.</i> a sage, one who knows himself; तस्मादात्मज्ञं<BR> ह्यर्चयेद्भूतिकामः Muṇḍ. 3. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञानम्
आत्मन् + -ज्ञानम्<BR>—1 self-knowledge.<BR>—2 spiritual knowledge, knowledge of the soul or the Supreme Spirit; सर्वेषामपि<BR> चैतेषामात्मज्ञानं परं स्मृतम् Ms. 12. 85, 92.<BR>—3 true wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्त्वम्
आत्मन् + -तत्त्वम्<BR>—1 the true nature of the soul or the supreme spirit; यदात्मतत्त्वेन<BR> तु ब्रह्मतत्त्वं प्रपश्येत Śvet. Up. 2. 15.<BR>—2 the highest thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्त्वम्
आत्मन् + -तत्त्वम् + ˚ज्ञः a sage versed in the Vedānta doctrines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतृप्त
आत्मन् + -तृप्त <i>a.</i> Self-satisfied; आत्मतृप्तश्च मानवः Bg. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतुष्टि|आत्मतुष्टिः
आत्मन् + -तुष्टि <i>a.</i> self-satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतुष्टिः|आत्मतुष्टि
आत्मन् + -तुष्टि + .({@-ष्टिः@} <i>f.</i>) self-satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्यागः|आत्मत्याग
आत्मन् + -त्यागः<BR>—1 self-sacrifice.<BR>—2 suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्यागिन्
आत्मन् + -त्यागिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 suicide; आत्मत्यागिन्यो नाशौचोदकभाजनाः Y. 3. 6.<BR>—2 a heretic, an unbeliever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्राणम्
आत्मन् + -त्राणम्<BR>—1 self-preservation.<BR>—2 a body-guard; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्शः|आत्मदर्श
आत्मन् + -दर्शः a mirror; प्रसादमात्मीयमिवात्मदर्शः R. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्शनम्
आत्मन् + -दर्शनम्<BR>—1 seeing oneself.<BR>—2 spiritual knowledge, true wisdom; सर्वभूतात्मदर्शनम् Y. 3. 157;<BR> cf. Ms. 12. 91; see आत्मयाजिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदा
आत्मन् + -दा <i>a.</i> Ved. granting oneʼs existence or life; य आत्मदा<BR> बलदा यस्य विश्व Rv. 10. 121. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदानम्
आत्मन् + -दानम् self-sacrifice, resigning oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदूषि
आत्मन् + -दूषि <i>a.</i> Ved. corrupting the soul; self-destroying; Av. 16. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदेवता
आत्मन् + -देवता a tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मद्रोहिन्
आत्मन् + -द्रोहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-tormenting, fretful.<BR>—2 suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनित्य
आत्मन् + -नित्य <i>a.</i> being constantly in the heart, greatly endeared to oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनिन्दा
आत्मन् + -निन्दा self-reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनिवेदनम्
आत्मन् + -निवेदनम् offering oneself (as a living sacrifice to the deity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनिष्ठ
आत्मन् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> one who constantly seeks for spiritual knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मपराजित
आत्मन् + -पराजित <i>a.</i> one who has lost himself (Ved.) Av. 5. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मपुराणम्
आत्मन् + -पुराणम् N. of a work elucidating the Upaniṣads (consisting of 18 chapters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रत्ययिक
आत्मन् + -प्रत्ययिक <i>a.</i> knowing from oneʼs experience; आत्मप्रत्ययिकं<BR> शास्त्रमिदम् Mb. 12. 246. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रबोधः|आत्मप्रबोध
आत्मन् + -प्रबोधः<BR>—1 cognition of the soul; self-consciousness.<BR>—2 title of an उपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रभ
आत्मन् + -प्रभ <i>a.</i> self-illuminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रवादः|आत्मप्रवाद
आत्मन् + -प्रवादः<BR>—1 conversation about the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 N. of the seventh of the fourteen Pūrvas of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मप्रशंसा
आत्मन् + -प्रशंसा self-praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबन्धुः|आत्मबन्धु
आत्मन् + -बन्धुः, -बान्धवः<BR>—1 oneʼs own kinsman; आत्ममातुः स्वसुः पुत्रा आत्मपितुः स्वसुः सुताः ।<BR> आत्ममातुलपुत्राश्च विज्ञेया ह्यात्मबान्धवाः Śabdak. <i>i. e.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">Page0325-1</a>]<BR> motherʼs sisterʼs son, fatherʼs sisterʼs son, and motherʼs brotherʼs son.<BR>—2 the soul, the self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबान्धवः|आत्मबान्धव
आत्मन् + -बन्धुः, -बान्धवः<BR>—1 oneʼs own kinsman; आत्ममातुः स्वसुः पुत्रा आत्मपितुः स्वसुः सुताः ।<BR> आत्ममातुलपुत्राश्च विज्ञेया ह्यात्मबान्धवाः Śabdak. <i>i. e.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">Page0325-1</a>]<BR> motherʼs sisterʼs son, fatherʼs sisterʼs son, and motherʼs brotherʼs son.<BR>—2 the soul, the self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0324-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबोधः|आत्मबोध
आत्मन् + -बोधः<BR>—1 spiritual knowledge.<BR>—2 knowledge of self. —3 N. of a work of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभावः|आत्मभाव
आत्मन् + -भावः<BR>—1 existence of the soul; संयोग एषां न तु आत्मभावात् Śvet. Up. 1. 2.<BR>—2 the self proper, peculiar nature.<BR>—3 the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभू
आत्मन् + -भू <i>a.</i> self-born, self-existent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूः
आत्मन् + -भू + .({@-भूः@}) वचस्यवसिते तस्मिन् ससर्ज गिरमात्मभूः Ku. 2. 53, 3. 16, 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयोनिः|आत्मयोनि
आत्मन् + -योनिः<BR>—1 N. of Brahmā;<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva; Ś. 7. 35.<BR>—4 Cupid, god of love.<BR>—5 a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूः
आत्मन् + -योनिः + .({@-भूः@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a daughter.<BR>—2 talent, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूत|आत्मभूतः
आत्मन् + -भूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-produced; peculiar, belonging to.<BR>—2 attached, devoted, faithful; तत्रात्मभूतैः कालज्ञैरहार्यैः परिचारकैः<BR> Ms. 7. 217 (Kull. = आत्मतुल्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूतः|आत्मभूत
आत्मन् + -भूत + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूता
आत्मन् + -भूत + .({@-ता@})<BR>—1 a daughter.<BR>—2 talent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूयम्
आत्मन् + -भूयम्<BR>—1 peculiarity, own nature. —2 Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममात्रा
आत्मन् + -मात्रा a portion of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममानिन्
आत्मन् + -मानिन् <i>a.</i> self-respecting, respectable.<BR>—2 arrogant, proud; विवेकशून्यः प्रभुरात्ममानी, महाननर्थः सुहृदां<BR> बतायम् Bk. 12. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूर्तिः|आत्ममूर्ति|आत्ममूर्त्ति
आत्मन् + -मूर्तिः<BR>—1 a brother; भ्राता स्वमूर्तिरात्मनः<BR>—2 soul, Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूल
आत्मन् + -मूल <i>a.</i> self-luminous, shining (God); स आत्ममूलोऽवतु<BR> मां परात्परः Bhāg. 8. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूलि
आत्मन् + -मूलि <i>n.</i> the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूली
आत्मन् + -मूली N. of a plant (दुरालभाः^1 Mar. धमासा).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयाजिन्
आत्मन् + -याजिन् —1 sacrificing for oneself or himself. ━<i>m.</i> a learned<BR> man who studies his own nature and that of the soul (of others) to secure<BR> eternal felicity, one who looks upon all beings as self; सर्वभूतेषु<BR> चात्मानं सर्वभूतानि चात्मनि । समं पश्यन्नात्मयाजी स्वाराज्यमधिगच्छति ॥<BR> Ms. 12. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयोनिः|आत्मयोनि
आत्मन् + -योनिः = ˚भू <i>m.</i> s. v. ददर्श चक्रीकृतचारुचापं प्रहर्तुमभ्युद्यतमात्मयोनिम् Ku. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मरक्षा
आत्मन् + -रक्षा<BR>—1 N. of a plant (इन्द्रवारुणीवृक्ष).<BR>—2 self protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मलाभः|आत्मलाभ
आत्मन् + -लाभः birth, production, origin; यैरात्मलाभस्त्वया लब्धः<BR> Mu. 3. 1, 5. 23; Ki. 3. 32, 17. 19, 18. 34; K. 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मलोमन्
आत्मन् + -लोमन्<BR>—1 the hair of the body.<BR>—2 the beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवञ्चक
आत्मन् + -वञ्चक <i>a.</i> self-deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवञ्चना
आत्मन् + -वञ्चना self-delusion; self-deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवधः|आत्मवध
आत्मन् + -वधः, -वध्या, -हत्या suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवध्या
आत्मन् + -वधः, -वध्या, -हत्या suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महत्या
आत्मन् + -वधः, -वध्या, -हत्या suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवर्ग्य
आत्मन् + -वर्ग्य <i>a.</i> of oneʼs party or class; उद्बाहुना जुहुविरे मुहुरात्मवर्ग्याः Śi. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवश|आत्मवशः
आत्मन् + -वश <i>a.</i> depending on oneʼs own will; यद्यत्परवशं कर्म<BR> तत्तद्यत्नेन वर्जयेत् । यद्यदात्मवशं तु स्यात्तत्तत्सेवेत यत्नतः ।<BR> Ms. 4. 159, सर्वमात्मवशं सुखम् 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवशः|आत्मवश
आत्मन् + -वश + .({@-शः@})<BR>—1 self-control, self-government.<BR>—2 oneʼs control, subjection; ˚शं नी, ˚वशीकृ to reduce to subjection, win over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवश्य
आत्मन् + -वश्य <i>a.</i> having control over self, self-possessed, self-restrained;<BR> आत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा Bg. 2. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविक्रयः|आत्मविक्रय
आत्मन् + -विक्रयः sale of oneself or oneʼs own liberty; Ms. 11. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्
आत्मन् + -विद् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a wise man, sage; as in तरति शोकमात्मवित्; सोऽहं भगवो मन्त्रविदेवास्मि<BR> नात्मविच्छ्रुतँह्येव Ch. Up. 7. 1. 3.<BR>—2 knowing oneʼs own self (family &c.); य इहात्मविदो विपक्षमध्ये Śi. 2. 116.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्या
आत्मन् + -विद्या knowledge of the soul, spiritual knowledge; आन्वीक्षिकीं<BR> चात्मविद्याम् Ms. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविवृद्धिः|आत्मविवृद्धि
आत्मन् + -विवृद्धिः, -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> self-exaltation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृद्धिः|आत्मवृद्धि
आत्मन् + -विवृद्धिः, -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> self-exaltation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवीर|आत्मवीरः
आत्मन् + -वीर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 mighty, powerful, strong.<BR>—2 appropriate, suitable, good for oneself (as diet &c.).<BR>—3 existent, sentient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवीरः|आत्मवीर
आत्मन् + -वीर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 wifeʼs brother.<BR>—3 a jester (in dramas); आत्मवीरः प्राणवति श्यालके च विदूषके.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्तम्
आत्मन् + -वृत्तम्, -वृत्तान्तः account of oneʼs own self, autobiography.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">Page0325-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्तान्तः|आत्मवृत्तान्त
आत्मन् + -वृत्तम्, -वृत्तान्तः account of oneʼs own self, autobiography.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">Page0325-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्ति|आत्मवृत्तिः
आत्मन् + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> dwelling in <i>Ātman</i> or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्तिः|आत्मवृत्ति
आत्मन् + -वृत्ति + .({@-त्तिः@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 state of the heart; किमेभिराशोपहतात्मवृत्तिभिः Ku. 5. 76.<BR>—2 action as regards oneself, oneʼs own state or circumstance; विस्माययन्<BR> विस्मितमात्मवृत्तौ R. 2. 33. —3 practising oneʼs own duties or occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशक्तिः|आत्मशक्ति
आत्मन् + -शक्तिः^1 <i>f.</i><BR>—1 oneʼs own power or ability, inherent power or effort; दैवं निहत्य<BR> कुरु पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या Pt. 1. 361 to the best of oneʼs power.<BR>—2 illusion.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशल्या
आत्मन् + -शल्या N. of a plant (शतावरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशुद्धिः|आत्मशुद्धि
आत्मन् + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> self-purification; Ms. 11. 164; योगिनः कर्म<BR> कुर्वन्ति संगं त्यक्त्वाऽत्मशुद्धये Bg. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मश्लाघा
आत्मन् + -श्लाघा, -स्तुतिः <i>f.</i> self-praise, boasting, bragging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मस्तुतिः|आत्मस्तुति
आत्मन् + -श्लाघा, -स्तुतिः <i>f.</i> self-praise, boasting, bragging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंयमः|आत्मसंयम
आत्मन् + -संयमः self-restraint; आत्मसंयमयोगाग्रौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते Bg. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंस्थ
आत्मन् + -संस्थ <i>a.</i> Based upon or connected with the person; आत्मसंस्थं<BR> मनःकृत्वा Bg. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसतत्त्वम्
आत्मन् + -सतत्त्वम् See आत्मतत्त्वम्; आत्मसतत्त्वं विगणयतः Bhāg. 5. 13. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसद्
आत्मन् + -सद् <i>a.</i> Ved. dwelling in oneself; आत्मसदौ स्तं मा मा हिंसिष्टम् Av. 5. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंतुष्ट
आत्मन् + -संतुष्ट <i>a.</i> self-sufficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसनि
आत्मन् + -सनि <i>a.</i> Ved. granting the breath of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसम
आत्मन् + -सम <i>a.</i> worthy of oneself, equal to oneself; कार्ये गुरुण्यात्मसमं<BR> नियोक्ष्ये Ku. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंदेहः|आत्मसन्देह|आत्मसंदेह
आत्मन् + -संदेहः<BR>—1 internal or personal doubt.<BR>—2 risk of life, personal risk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंभवः|आत्मसम्भव|आत्मसंभव
आत्मन् + -संभवः, -समुद्भवः<BR>—1 a son; चकार नाम्ना रघुमात्मसंभवम् R. 3. 21, 11. 57, 17. 8.<BR>—2 Cupid, god of love.<BR>—3 epithet of Brahmā, Viṣṇu, or Śiva.<BR>—4 the Supreme Being (परमात्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंभवा|आत्मसम्भवा
आत्मन् + -संभवः, -समुद्भवः + .({@-वा@})<BR>—1 a daughter. —2 understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसमुद्भवः|आत्मसमुद्भव
आत्मन् + -संभवः, -समुद्भवः<BR>—1 a son; चकार नाम्ना रघुमात्मसंभवम् R. 3. 21, 11. 57, 17. 8.<BR>—2 Cupid, god of love.<BR>—3 epithet of Brahmā, Viṣṇu, or Śiva.<BR>—4 the Supreme Being (परमात्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंपन्न
आत्मन् + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> —1 self-possessed; Pt. 1. 49.<BR>—2 talented, intelligent; तमात्मसंपन्नमनिन्दितात्मा कृत्वा युवानं<BR> युवराजमेव R. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंभावना|आत्मसम्भावना
आत्मन् + -संभावना self-conceit; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसिद्धिः|आत्मसिद्धि
आत्मन् + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> self-aggrandizement, attainment of object or purpose;<BR> आगच्छदात्मसिद्ध्यर्थं गोकर्णस्याश्रमं शुभम् Rām. 7. 9. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसुख
आत्मन् + -सुख <i>a.</i> self-delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसुखम्
आत्मन् + -सुख + .({@-खम्@}) the highest bliss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मस्थ
आत्मन् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> At oneʼs own disposal (स्वाधीन); तावदेव मया<BR> सार्धमात्मस्थं कुरु शासनम् Rām. 2. 21. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महन्
आत्मन् + -हन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who kills his own soul (neglects its welfare &c.); ये के चात्महनो<BR> जनाः Śvet. Up. 3.<BR>—2 a suicide, self-destroyer.<BR>—3 a heretic, unbeliever.<BR>—4 a priest in a temple, a servant or attendant upon an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महननम्
आत्मन् + -हननम्, -हत्या suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महत्या
आत्मन् + -हननम्, -हत्या suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महित
आत्मन् + -हित <i>a.</i> beneficial to oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महितम्
आत्मन् + -हित + .({@-तम्@}) oneʼs own good or welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मक
आत्मक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Made up or composed of, of the<BR> nature or character of &c.; पञ्च˚ fivefold, made up of five; संशय˚<BR> of a doubtful nature; so दुःख˚ sorry, grieved; दहन˚ hot; विष˚<BR> poisonous &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकीय
आत्मकीय, आत्मीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to oneself, oneʼs own;<BR> सर्वः कान्तमात्मीयं पश्यति Ś. 2; स्वामिनमात्मीयं करिष्यामि H. 2.<BR> win over; अहमात्मीयो न भविष्यामि Mk. 8 I shall lose my life; आत्मीयं<BR> कुर्वन्ति subject K. 135, 167; अयमात्मीयः क्रियताम् 12; let him be<BR> taken under your protection; प्रसादमात्मीयमिवात्मदर्शः R. 7. 68;<BR> Ku. 2. 19; kindred, related, of kin, न कश्चिच्चण्डकोपानामात्मीयो नाम<BR> भूभुजाम् Bh. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीय|आत्मीयः
आत्मकीय, आत्मीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to oneself, oneʼs own;<BR> सर्वः कान्तमात्मीयं पश्यति Ś. 2; स्वामिनमात्मीयं करिष्यामि H. 2.<BR> win over; अहमात्मीयो न भविष्यामि Mk. 8 I shall lose my life; आत्मीयं<BR> कुर्वन्ति subject K. 135, 167; अयमात्मीयः क्रियताम् 12; let him be<BR> taken under your protection; प्रसादमात्मीयमिवात्मदर्शः R. 7. 68;<BR> Ku. 2. 19; kindred, related, of kin, न कश्चिच्चण्डकोपानामात्मीयो नाम<BR> भूभुजाम् Bh. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मता
आत्मता, -त्वम्<BR> Identity with self, spirituality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्वम्
आत्मता, -त्वम्<BR> Identity with self, spirituality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मना
आत्मना <i>ind.</i> (instr. of आत्मन्) Used reflexively; अथ चास्तमिता<BR> त्वमात्मना R. 8. 51 thou thyself; आत्मना शुकनासमादाय K. 293.<BR> It is oft. compounded with ordinal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">Page0326-1</a>]<BR> numerals; <i>e. g.</i> {@˚द्वितीयः@} second including himself, <i>i. e.</i><BR> himself and one more; so {@˚तृतीयः@} himself with two others;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनासप्तमः|आत्मनासप्तम
आत्मना + .{@-˚सप्तमः@} Being oneself the seventh; आत्मना सप्तमो राजा निर्ययौ<BR> गजसाह्वयात् Mb. 17. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0325-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं|आत्मनीनः
आत्मनीन <i>a.</i> [आत्मने हितः ख]<BR>—1 Belonging to oneself, oneʼs own; कस्यैष आत्मनीनः M. 4 on whose side is he?<BR>—2 Beneficial to oneself; आत्मनीनमुपतिष्ठते Ki. 13. 69, 3. 16; तमात्मनीनामुदवोढ<BR> रामः Bh. 3. 77; good, fit, suitable, appropriate (as diet &c.); आत्मनीनतया<BR> श्रीमान् शिवः श्रीभिः समार्धयत् Śiva B. 23. 57.<BR>—3 Existent, sentient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीनः|आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं
आत्मनीन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A son.<BR>—2 A wifeʼs brother.<BR>—3 A jester (in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेपदम्
आत्मनेपदम् [आत्मने आत्मार्थफलबोधनाय पदं अलुक् स˚]<BR>—1 A voice for oneself, one of the two voices in which roots are conjugated in Sanskrit.<BR>—2 The terminations of this voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मंभरि|आत्मम्भरि|आत्मम्भरिः
आत्मंभरि <i>a.</i> [आत्मानं बिभर्ति, भृ खि मुम् च P. III. 2. 26]<BR> Selfish, greedy (one who feeds his ownself); आत्मंभरिस्त्वं पिशितैर्नराणाम्<BR> Bk. 2. 33; H. 3. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मंभरित्वम्
आत्मंभरि + .{@-˚त्वम्@} Selfishness … अहो ते आत्मंभरित्वम् । नागानन्द 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्वत्|आत्मन्वन्त्
आत्मन्वत्, आत्मन्विन् Ved. Having a soul, animated, alive; मृत्युस्तन्मनोऽकुरुतात्मन्वी<BR> स्यामिति Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 1, 1. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्विन्
आत्मन्वत्, आत्मन्विन् Ved. Having a soul, animated, alive; मृत्युस्तन्मनोऽकुरुतात्मन्वी<BR> स्यामिति Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 1, 1. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्|आत्मवन्त्
आत्मवत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप् मस्य वः]<BR>—1 Self-possessed, possessed of self-restraint; शास्त्रदृष्टेन विधिना<BR> संयोज्यात्मानमात्मवान् Mb. 3. 126. 8; Mu. 3.<BR>—2 Composed, prudent, wise; किमिवावसादकरमात्मवताम् Ki. 6. 19;<BR> Bg. 2. 45, 4. 41; Ms. 1. 108, 5. 43, 7. 52. ━<i>ind.</i> Like oneself; आत्मवत्<BR> सर्वभूतेषु यः पश्यति स पण्डितः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्ता
आत्मवत्ता Self-possession, self-control, prudence, wisdom; प्रकृतिष्वात्मजमात्मवत्तया<BR> R. 8. 10, 84; Ms. 11. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्
आत्मसात् <i>ind.</i> In oneʼs own possession, oneʼs own; mostly in combination<BR> with कृ or भू; ˚कृ to appropriate to oneself, take for oneself;<BR> दुरितैरपि कर्तुमात्मसात् R. 8. 2 to bring under subjection or power;<BR> so ˚भू come under oneʼs subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीकृ
आत्मीकृ €8 U. To conquer, subdue; K. 117, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीभावः|आत्मीभाव
आत्मीभावः Identification with the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्म्य
आत्म्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to oneself, oneʼs own, personal.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Having the nature of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिक|आत्यंतिक
आत्यन्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अत्यन्त भवार्थे ठञ्]<BR>—1 Continual, uninterrupted, endless, infinite, permanent, everlasting;<BR> स आत्यन्तिको भविष्यति Mu. 4; विष्णुगुप्तहतकस्यात्यन्तिकश्रेयसे 2. 15;<BR> Ms. 2. 242; Bg. 6. 21.<BR>—2 Excessive, abundant, superlative.<BR>—3 Supreme, absolute; आत्यन्तिकी स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः Mit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आत्यन्तिकदुःखनिवृत्तिः, आत्यन्तिकप्रलयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिकदुःखनिवृत्तिः|आत्यन्तिकदुःखनिवृत्ति
आत्यन्तिक + -दुःखनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिकप्रलयः|आत्यन्तिकप्रलय
आत्यन्तिक + -प्रलयः the grand or universal destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिक
आत्ययिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अत्ययः नाशः प्रयोजनमस्य ठक्]<BR>—1 Destructive, disastrous.<BR>—2 Painful, unpropitious, ill-omened, distressing.<BR>—3 Pressing, urgent, emergent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">Page0326-2</a>]<BR> ending quickly, not suffering delay; किंचिदात्ययिकं कार्यं तेषां त्वं<BR> दर्शनं कुरु Rām. 6. 32. 37; Ms. 7. 165; H. 3; K. 294; अशिश्रयन्नात्ययिकं<BR> समेत्य Bk. कार्यगौरवादात्ययिकवशेन वा Kau. A. 1. 19; सर्वमात्ययिकं<BR> कार्यं शृणुयान्नातिपातयेत् <i>ibid.</i> extraordinary, special. —4 Delayed,<BR> already late; तां हत्वा पुनरेवाहं कृत्यमात्ययिकं स्मरन् Rām. 5. 58. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिकम्
आत्ययिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Difficulty, calamity; अगमन्नो मनः कर्णं बन्धुमात्ययिकेष्विव Mb. 7. 1. 46.<BR>—2 Essential duty; Hc. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेय|आत्रेयः
आत्रेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अत्रेरपत्यं ढक्] P. IV. 1. 122 Belonging to,<BR> descended or sprung from, Atri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेयः|आत्रेय
आत्रेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Atri.<BR>—2 The head of the descendants of Atri.<BR>—3 A priest closely related to the Sadasya.<BR>—4 An epithet of Śiva. —5 An essential humor or juice of the body, lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेयी
आत्रेय + .{@-यी@}<BR>—1 A female descendant of Atri; गोत्रप्रशंसार्थमात्रेष्या अवधसंकीर्तनम् ।<BR> न चापन्नसत्त्वा आत्रेयी । गोत्रं ह्येतत् । ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 9.<BR>—2 The wife of Atri.<BR>—3 A woman in her courses (रजस्वला); Ms. 11. 87; Y. 3. 251.<BR>—4 Any woman of the Brāhmaṇical order.<BR>—5 N. of a river in the north of Bengal, also called Tista.<BR>—6 A pregnant woman; Mb. 12. 165. 54; आत्रेयीमापन्नगर्भामाहुः । अत्र<BR> कुक्षौ अस्या विद्यत इत्यात्रेयी । ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेयिका
आत्रेयिका [आत्रेयी स्वार्थे कन्] A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वण|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्वण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अथर्वणा मुनिना दृष्टः वेदः अण् आथर्वणः तमधीते<BR> वेत्ति वा अण् P. IV. 3. 133] Originating from, relating or belonging to,<BR> the Atharvaveda or the Atharvans; अग्नौ साक्षिण्याथर्वणेन विधिना Dk.;<BR> आथर्वणस्तीव्र इवाभिचारः Mv. 1. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणः|आथर्वण|आथर्व्वण|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्वण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa knowing or studying the Atharvaveda.<BR>—2 A descendant of Atharvan; इदं वै तन्मधु दध्यङ्ङार्थवणोऽश्विभ्यामुवाच<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 16.<BR>—3 A priest whose ritual is comprised in the Atharvaveda.<BR>—4 The Atharvaveda itself (अथर्वणां समूहः).<BR>—5 A house-priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणम्
आथर्वण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 A private room in which the sacrificer is informed of the happy event<BR> of the sacrifice by the officiating Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—2 The black art, magic (जारणमारण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणशिरस्
आथर्वण + .{@-शिरस्@} <i>n.</i> N. of an Upaniṣad belonging to the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणिक|आथर्वणिकः|आथर्व्वणिक
आथर्वणिक <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to the अथर्ववेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणिकः|आथर्वणिक|आथर्व्वणिक
आथर्वणिक + .{@-कः@} A Brāhmaṇa who has studied the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदंश्
आदंश् €1 P. To bite, peck at, nibble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदंशः|आदंश
आदंशः<BR>—1 A bite, a wound caused by biting.<BR>—2 A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदष्ट
आदष्ट <i>a.</i> Nibbled, pecked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदघ्न
आदघ्न <i>a.</i> Ved. Reaching up to the mouth (आस् + दघ्न); आदघ्नास<BR> उपकक्षास उ त्वे Rv. 10. 71. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आददि
आददि <i>a.</i> Ved. Taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर, आदर्श &c. See under आदृ, आदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर, आदर्श &c. See under आदृ, आदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदहनम्
आदहनम्<BR>—1 Burning.<BR>—2 Injuring, killing.<BR>—3 Reviling, despising.<BR>—4 A cemetery, a place where<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">Page0327-1</a>]<BR> anything is burnt (आदह्यतेऽस्मिन्निति); क्षिप्रं वै तस्यादहनं परि<BR> नृत्यन्ति केशिनीः Av. 12. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0326-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदा
आदा €3 Ā. (आदत्ते)<BR>—1 To receive, accept, take (to oneself), resort to; व्यवहारासनमाददे<BR> युवा R. 8. 18, 10. 40; मलीमसामाददते न पद्धतिम् R. 3. 46 follow<BR> or resort to; प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे 3. 14, 14. 1; Ms. 2. 238, 117.<BR>—2 (With words expressing speech) To begin to speak, utter; वाचम् आदा<BR> to speak, utter; विनिश्चितार्थामिति वाचमाददे Ki. 1. 3, 14. 2; Śi. 2. 13;<BR> R. 1. 59; शिव शिव शिवेत्यात्तवचसः Bh. 3. 42, v. l.<BR>—3 To seize, take hold of; क्षितिधरपतिकन्यामाददानः करेण Ku. 7. 94;<BR> R. 2. 28, 3. 60; Ms. 8. 315; इदमेव निमित्तमादाय M. 1; स<BR> हि सर्वस्य लोकस्य मन आददे R. 4. 8 attracted, had a hold on the mind.<BR>—4 To put on (as clothes &c.); यद्यच्छरीरमादत्ते Śvet. Up.<BR>—5 To take up, absorb, drink up; R. 1. 18; प्रदीपः स्नेहमादत्ते दशयाभ्यन्तरस्थया Śi. 2. 85.<BR>—6 To exact, take in (as taxes); take away, carry off; अगृध्नुराददे<BR> सोऽर्थम् R. 1. 21; Ms. 8. 341, 222; so वलिम्, शुल्कम्, दण्डम् &c.<BR>—7 To pluck, lop off, separate; Ś. 4. 8.<BR>—8 To carry, take, bear; जालमादाय Pt. 2 carrying, or along with<BR> the net; कुशानादाय Ś. 3; तोयमादाय गच्छेः Me. 20, 48, 64; see<BR> आदाय below; काश्यपसंदेशमादाय bearing K.ʼs message.<BR>—9 To perceive, comprehend; घ्नाणेन रूपमादत्स्व रसानादत्स्व चक्षुषा ।<BR> श्रोत्रेण गन्धानादत्स्व &c. Mb.<BR>—10 To agree to, undertake, begin.<BR>—11 To imprison, make captive. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to take. ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> (दित्सते) To wish to take, carry off &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद
आद <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Taking, receiving; as in दायाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्त
आदत्त, आत्त <i>p. p.</i> [आ -दा -क्त] —1 Taken, received,<BR> assumed, accepted; आत्तसारश्चक्षुषा स्वविषयः M. 2; एवमात्तरतिः<BR> R. 11. 57; M. 5. 1; ˚हासः Ratn.<BR>—1 smiling;<BR>—2 Agreed to, undertaken, begun.<BR>—3 Attracted.<BR>—4 Drawn out, extracted; गामात्तसारां रघुरप्यवेक्ष्य R. 5. 26; ˚बलम् 11. 76<BR> taken away.<BR>—5 Seized, overpowered; दृष्ट्वाग्रे वरमात्तसाध्वसरसा गौरी नवे संगमे Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदत्तगन्ध, आदत्तगर्व, आदत्तदण्ड, आदत्तमनस्क, आदत्तलक्ष्मि, आदत्तवचस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आदत्त, आत्त <i>p. p.</i> [आ -दा -क्त] —1 Taken, received,<BR> assumed, accepted; आत्तसारश्चक्षुषा स्वविषयः M. 2; एवमात्तरतिः<BR> R. 11. 57; M. 5. 1; ˚हासः Ratn.<BR>—1 smiling;<BR>—2 Agreed to, undertaken, begun.<BR>—3 Attracted.<BR>—4 Drawn out, extracted; गामात्तसारां रघुरप्यवेक्ष्य R. 5. 26; ˚बलम् 11. 76<BR> taken away.<BR>—5 Seized, overpowered; दृष्ट्वाग्रे वरमात्तसाध्वसरसा गौरी नवे संगमे Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदत्तगन्ध, आदत्तगर्व, आदत्तदण्ड, आदत्तमनस्क, आदत्तलक्ष्मि, आदत्तवचस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तगन्ध
आदत्त + -गन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having oneʼs pride humbled, attacked, insulted, defeated; पक्षच्छिदा<BR> गोत्रभिदात्तगन्धाः R. 13. 7; केनात्तगन्धो माणवकः Ś. 6.<BR>—2 already smelt (as a flower); आत्तगन्धमवधूय शत्रुभिः Śi. 14. 84<BR> (where आ˚ has sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तगर्व
आदत्त + -गर्व <i>a.</i> humiliated, insulted, degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तदण्ड
आदत्त + -दण्ड <i>a.</i> assuming the royal sceptre; नियमयसि विमार्गप्रस्थितानात्तदण्डः Ś. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तमनस्क
आदत्त + -मनस्क <i>a.</i> one whose mind is transported (with joy &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तलक्ष्मि
आदत्त + -लक्ष्मि^1 <i>a.</i> stripped of wealth.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्तवचस्
आदत्त + -वचस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 destitute of speech.<BR>—2 having commenced speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदातृ
आदातृ <i>a.</i> One who takes or receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदानम्
आदानम्<BR>—1 Taking, receiving, accepting, seizing, कुशाङ्कुरादानपरिक्षताङ्गुलिः<BR> Ku. 5, 11; आदानं हि विसर्गाय सतां वारिमुचामिव R. 4. 86.<BR>—2 Earning, getting.<BR>—3 A symptom (of a disease).<BR>—4 Binding, fettering (from आदा €2 P.).<BR>—5 A horseʼs trappings.<BR>—6 An action;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">Page0327-2</a>]<BR> आदानमुभयाश्रयम् Bhāg. 2. 10. 24.<BR>—7 Subjugating, overpowering; अथवा मन्त्रवद् ब्रूयुरात्मादानाय दुष्कृतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 212. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदानी
आदानम् + .{@-नी@} N. of a plant हस्तिघोषा (Mar. घोसाळें).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदानसमितिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदानसमितिः|आदानसमिति
आदानम् + -समितिः A method of cautious seizing so that no creature be hurt.<BR> It is one of the पञ्चसमितिs or rules of careful conduct in Jaina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदापनम्
आदापनम् Inviting or causing another to receive something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाय|आदायः
आदाय <i>ind.</i> Having taken; oft. with a prepositional force ‘with’;<BR> जालमादाय H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायः|आदाय
आदायः Receiving, taking &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदायचर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायचर
आदायः + -चर <i>a.</i> one who goes away after taking anything; त्वमादायचरो वने Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायिन्
आदायिन् <i>a.</i> Taking, receiving, inclined to receive (gifts); अदत्त˚,<BR> परस्व˚ &c. चोदनादायिनो हस्ताल्लिप्सेत ब्राह्मणो धनम् । Ms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आदित्सु <i>a.</i> (fr. desid. of आदा) Wishing to take; आदित्सुभिर्नूपुरशिञ्जितानि Ku. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आदेय <i>a.</i> To be taken or received, receivable. acceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदादिक
आदादिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the class of roots of which the first<BR> is अद् <i>i. e.</i> to the second class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाल्भ्यम्
आदाल्भ्यम् Fearlessness; Mb. 12. 120. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 First, primary, primitive; निदानं त्वादिकारणम् Ak.<BR>—2 Chief, first, principal, pre-eminent; oft. at the end of comp. in this<BR> sense; see below. —3 First in time existing before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिः|आदि
आदि + .{@-दिः@}<BR>—1 Beginning, commencement (opp. अन्त); अप एव ससर्जादौ तासु बीजमवासृजत्<BR> Ms. 1. 8; Bg. 3. 41; अनादि &c.; जगदादिरनादिस्त्वम् Ku. 2. 9;<BR> oft. at the end of comp. and translated by ‘beginning with’, ‘{{et caetera->et cætera||20260515|Dr. Dhaval Patel|https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/pull/2845}}’,<BR> ‘and others’, ‘and so on’ (of the same nature or kind), ‘such like’; इन्द्रादयो<BR> देवाः the gods Indra and others (इन्द्रः आदिर्येषां ते); एवमादि<BR> this and the like; भ्वादयो धातवः भू and others, or words beginning<BR> with भू, are called roots; oft. used by Pāṇini to denote classes<BR> or groups of grammatical words; अदादि, दिवादि, स्वादि &c.<BR>—2 First part or portion.<BR>—3 A firstling, first-fruits.<BR>—4 Prime cause.<BR>—5 Nearness.<BR>—6 One of the seven parts of Sāma; अथ सप्तविधस्य वाचि सप्तविधं<BR> सामोपासीत यत्किंच वाचो हुमिति स हिंकारो यत्प्रेति स प्रस्तावो यदेति<BR> स आदिः Ch. Up. 2. 8. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आद्यन्त, आद्यन्तयमकम्, आद्यन्तवत्, आद्यन्तान्तरवर्तिन्, आद्युदात्त, आद्युपान्तम्, आदिकरः, आदिकर्तृ, आदिकृत्, आदिकर्मन्, आदिकविः, आदिकाण्डम्, आदिकारणम्, आदिकाव्यम्, आदिकेशवः, आदिजिनः, आदितालः, आदिदीपकम्, आदिदेवः, आदिदैत्यः, आदिनाथः, आदिपर्वन्, आदिपुराणम्, आदिपुरुषः, आदिपूरुषः, आदिबलम्, आदिबुद्ध, आदिभव, आदिभूत, आदिमूलम्, आदियोगाचार्यः, आदिरसः, आदिराजः, आदिरूपम्, आदिवंशः, आदिवराहः, आदिविद्वस्, आदिविपुला, आदिवृक्षः, आदिशक्तिः, आदिशरीरम्, आदिसर्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्त
आदि + -अन्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having beginning and end. —2 first and last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तम्
आदि + -अन्त + .({@-तम्@}) beginning and end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तयमकम्
आदि + -अन्त + ˚यमकम् N. of a figure in poetry.<BR> cf. Bk. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तवत्|आद्यन्तवन्त्
आदि + -अन्त + ˚वत् having beginning and end, finite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तान्तरवर्तिन्|आद्यन्तान्तरवर्त्तिन्
आदि + -अन्त + ˚अन्तरवर्तिन्^1 <i>a.</i> having a beginning, end and middle; being all-in-all.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्युदात्त
आदि + -उदात्त <i>a.</i> having the acute accent on the first syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्युपान्तम्
आदि + -उपान्तम् <i>ind.</i> from first to last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकरः|आदिकर
आदि + -करः, -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the creator, an epithet of Brahmā<BR> or Viṣṇu; गरीयसे ब्रह्मणोऽप्यादिकर्त्रे Bg. 11. 37; विशेषणे द्वे<BR> य इहादिकर्तुर्वदेदधीती स हि कैयटीयः Śab. Kau.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर्तृ|आदिकर्त्तृ
आदि + -उपान्तम् <i>ind.</i> from first to last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकृत्
आदि + -उपान्तम् <i>ind.</i> from first to last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर्मन्|आदिकर्म्मन्
आदि + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> the beginning of an action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकविः|आदिकवि
आदि + -कविः ‘the first poet’, an epithet of Brahmā and of Vālmīki;<BR> the former is so called because he first produced and promulgated the Vedas;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">Page0328-1</a>]<BR> (तेने ब्रह्म हृदा य आदिकवये मुह्यन्ति यत्सूरयः Bhāg. 1. 1. 1.)<BR> and the latter, because he was the first to show to others ‘the path of poets’<BR>; when he beheld one of a pair of Krauñca birds being killed<BR> by a fowler, he cursed the wretch, and his grief unconsciously took the<BR> form of a verse (श्लोकत्वमापद्यत यस्य शोकः); he was subsequently<BR> told by Brahmā to compose the life of Rāma, and he thus gave to the<BR> world the first poem in Sanskrit, the Rāmāyaṇa; cf. U. 2 Viṣkambhaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0327-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकाण्डम्
आदि + -काण्डम् the first book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकारणम्
आदि + -कारणम् the first or primary cause (of the universe), which,<BR> according to the Vedāntins, is Brahman; while, according to the Naiyāyikas<BR> and particularly the Vaiśeṣikas, atoms are the first or material cause<BR> of the universe, and not God.<BR>—2 analysis.<BR>—3 algebra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकाव्यम्
आदि + -काव्यम् the first poem; <i>i. e.</i> the Rāmāyaṇa; see आदिकवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकेशवः|आदिकेशव
आदि + -केशवः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिजिनः|आदिजिन
आदि + -जिनः N. of Ṛṣabha, the first तीर्थंकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितालः|आदिताल
आदि + -तालः a sort of musical time or ताल; एक एव लघुर्यत्र आदितालः स कथ्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदीपकम्
आदि + -दीपकम् N. of a figure in rhetoric (the verb standing at the<BR> beginning of the sentence). cf. Bk. 10. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदेवः|आदिदेव
आदि + -देवः<BR>—1 the first or Supreme God; पुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यम् आदिदेवमजं विभुम्<BR> Bg. 10. 12, 11. 38.<BR>—2 Nārāyaṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Śiva.<BR>—4 Brahmā; Mb. 12. 188. 20.<BR>—5 the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदैत्यः|आदिदैत्य
आदि + -दैत्यः an epithet of Hiraṇyakaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिनाथः|आदिनाथ
आदि + -नाथः N. of Ādibuddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपर्वन्|आदिपर्व्वन्
आदि + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> ‘the first section or chapter’, N. of the first<BR> book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुराणम्
आदि + -पुराणम् ‘the first Purāṇa’, N. of the Brahma-Purāṇa. N. of<BR> a Jaina religious book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुषः|आदिपुरुष
आदि + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः<BR>—1 the first or primeval being, the lord of the creation.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu, Kṛṣṇa, or Nārāyaṇa; ते च प्रापुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे<BR> चादिपूरुषः R. 10. 6; तमर्ध्यमर्ध्यादिकयादिपूरुषः Śi. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपूरुषः|आदिपूरुष
आदि + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः<BR>—1 the first or primeval being, the lord of the creation.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu, Kṛṣṇa, or Nārāyaṇa; ते च प्रापुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे<BR> चादिपूरुषः R. 10. 6; तमर्ध्यमर्ध्यादिकयादिपूरुषः Śi. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिबलम्
आदि + -बलम् generative power; first vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिबुद्ध|आदिबुद्धः
आदि + -बुद्ध <i>a.</i> perceived in the beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिबुद्धः|आदिबुद्ध
आदि + -बुद्ध + .({@-द्धः@}) the primitive Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभव|आदिभवः
आदि + -भव, -भूत <i>a.</i> produced at first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूत|आदिभूतः
आदि + -भव, -भूत <i>a.</i> produced at first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभवः|आदिभव
आदि + -भव, -भूत + .({@-वः, -तः@})<BR>—1 ‘the first-born’, primeval being, an epithet of Brahmā; इत्युक्त्वादिभवो<BR> देवः Bhāg. 7. 3. 22.<BR>—2 also N. of Viṣṇu; रसातलादादि. भवेन पुंसा R. 13. 8.<BR>—3 an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूतः|आदिभूत
आदि + -भव, -भूत + .({@-वः, -तः@})<BR>—1 ‘the first-born’, primeval being, an epithet of Brahmā; इत्युक्त्वादिभवो<BR> देवः Bhāg. 7. 3. 22.<BR>—2 also N. of Viṣṇu; रसातलादादि. भवेन पुंसा R. 13. 8.<BR>—3 an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूतम्
आदि + -भव, -भूत + .({@-तम्@}) minute five elements (पञ्चमहाभूतानि); नष्टे लोके<BR> द्विपरार्धावसाने महाभूतेष्वादिभूतं गतेषु Bhāg. 10. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिमूलम्
आदि + -मूलम् first foundation, primeval cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदियोगाचार्यः|आदियोगाचार्य
आदि + -योगाचार्यः ‘the first teacher of devotion’, an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिरसः|आदिरस
आदि + -रसः the first of the 8 Rasas, <i>i. e.</i> शृङ्गार or love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिराजः|आदिराज
आदि + -राजः the first king पृथु; an epithet of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिरूपम्
आदि + -रूपम् Symptom (of disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवंशः|आदिवंश
आदि + -वंशः primeval race, primitive family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवराहः|आदिवराह
आदि + -वराहः ‘the first boar’, an epithet of Visṇu, alluding to his<BR> third or boar-incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिविद्वस्
आदि + -विद्वस् <i>m.</i> the first learned man; कपिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिविपुला
आदि + -विपुला <i>f.</i> N. of an Āryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवृक्षः|आदिवृक्ष
आदि + -वृक्षः N. of a plant (Mar. आपटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिशक्तिः|आदिशक्ति
आदि + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the power of माया or illusion. —2 an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिशरीरम्
आदि + -शरीरम् —1 the primitive body.<BR>—2 ignorance.<BR>—3 the subtle body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिसर्गः|आदिसर्ग
आदि + -सर्गः the first creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिक
आदिक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Beginning with, and so on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितः
आदितः, आदौ <i>ind.</i> From the first or beginning, at first;<BR> तद्दैवेनादितो हतम् U. 5. 20. पतीन् प्रजानामसृजन् महर्षीनादितो<BR> दश Ms. आदौ रामतपोवनाधिगमनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदौ
आदितः, आदौ <i>ind.</i> From the first or beginning, at first;<BR> तद्दैवेनादितो हतम् U. 5. 20. पतीन् प्रजानामसृजन् महर्षीनादितो<BR> दश Ms. आदौ रामतपोवनाधिगमनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम <i>a.</i> [आदौ भवः आदि-डिमच्] First, primitive, original;<BR> आदिमः श्येनशैलादिसंयोगः परिकीर्तितः Bhāṣā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिता
आदिता, -त्वम्<BR> Priority, precedence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्वम्
आदिता, -त्वम्<BR> Priority, precedence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिमत्|आदिमन्त्
आदिमत् <i>a.</i> Having a beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य <i>a.</i> [आदौ भवः यत्]<BR>—1 First, primitive, being at the beginning.<BR>—2 Being at the head, excellent, unparalleled, pre-eminent, foremost;<BR> योगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम् Bg. 8. 28, 11. 31, 11. 47, 15. 4. आसीन्महीक्षितामाद्यः<BR> प्रणवश्छन्दसामिव R. 1. 11.<BR>—3 (At the end of comp.) Beginning with, and so on; see आदि.<BR>—4 Immediately preceding; एकादशाद्यम् Śrut. 27 immediately before<BR> the 11th, <i>i. e.</i> 10th; so संयुक्ताद्यम् 2.<BR>—5 Eatable (अद्ण्यत्); वयमाद्यस्य दातारः Praśna. Up. 2. 11; हितं<BR> च परिणामे यत्तदाद्यं भूतिमिच्छता Pt. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्द्याः
आद्य + .{@-द्याः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) A class of deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्या
आद्य + .{@-द्या@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—2 The first day (तिथि) of a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यम्
आद्य + .{@-द्यम्@}<BR>—1 The beginning.<BR>—2 Grain, food.<BR>—3 A kind of funeral obsequial ceremony (पितृश्राद्धभेद).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आद्यकविः, आद्यकालिक, आद्यबीजम्, आद्यमाषकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकविः|आद्यकवि
आद्य + -कविः ‘the first poet’, an epithet of Brahmā or Vālmīki; see आदिकवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकालिक
आद्य + -कालिक <i>a.</i> Seeing only the present (वर्तमानमात्रदार्शिन्);<BR> आद्यकालिकया बुद्धया दूरे श्व इति निर्भयाः Mb. 12. 321. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यबीजम्
आद्य + -बीजम् the primary or material cause of the universe, which, according<BR> to the Sāṅkhyas, is प्रधान or the inanimate principle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यमाषकः|आद्यमाषक
आद्य + -माषकः a measure of five guñjas (about. 17½ grains Troy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय [अदितेरपत्यं ढक्]<BR>—1 A son of Aditi.<BR>—2 A god, divinity in general.<BR>—3 The sun; दिवि देवाः सूर्यमादितेयम् Rv. 10. 88. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य <i>a.</i> [अदितेरपत्यं ण्य P. IV. 1. 85.]<BR>—1 Solar, belonging to, or born in, the solar line; आदित्यैर्यदि विग्रहो<BR> नृपतिभिर्धन्यं ममैतत्ततो U. 6. 18.<BR>—2 Devoted to, or originating from, Aditi आदित्यं चरुं निर्वपेत्<BR> Yaj. Ts. 2. 2. 6. 1.<BR>—3 Belonging to, or sprung from, the Ādityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यः|आदित्य
आदित्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 A son of Aditi; a god, divinity in general. [The number of Ādityas<BR> appears to have been originally seven, of whom Varuṇa is the head, and<BR> the name Āditya was restricted to them, देवा आदित्या ये सप्त Rv. 9. 114. 3.<BR> In the time of the Brāhmaṇas, however, the number of Ādityas<BR> rose to 12, representing the sun in the 12 months of the year; धाता<BR> मित्रोऽर्यमा रुद्रो वरुणः सूर्य एव च । भगो विवस्वान् पूषा च सविता दशमः<BR> स्मृतः ॥ एकादशस्तथा त्वष्टा विष्णुर्द्वादश उच्यते ।]; आदित्यानामहं<BR> विष्णुः Bg. 10. 21; Ku. 2. 24. (These 12 suns are supposed to shine only<BR> at the destruction of the universe; cf. Ve. 3. 8; दग्धुं विश्वं दहनकिरणैर्नोदिता<BR> द्वादशार्काः).<BR>—2 The sun; Vāj. 4. 21.<BR>—3 A name of Viṣṇu in his fifth or dwarf-incarnation; स्वयंभूः शंभुरादित्यः V. Sah.<BR>—4 N. of the <i>Arka</i> plant (Mar. रुई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यौ
आदित्य + .{@-त्यौ@} (dual) N. of a constellation, the seventh lunar mansion (पुनर्वसु).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदित्यकेतुः, आदित्यचन्द्रौ, आदित्यदर्शनम्, आदित्यपत्रः, आदित्यपर्णिनी, आदित्यपुराणम्, आदित्यपुष्पिका, आदित्यबन्धुः, आदित्यभक्ता, आदित्यमण्डलम्, आदित्यव्रतम्, आदित्यसूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यकेतुः|आदित्यकेतु
आदित्य + -केतुः<BR>—1 N. of a son of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">Page0329-1</a>]<BR> Dhṛtarāṣtra.<BR>—2 The charioteer of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0328-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यचन्द्रौ
आदित्य + -चन्द्रौ (dual) the sun and the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यदर्शनम्
आदित्य + -दर्शनम् ‘Showing the sun’ (to a child of 4 months), one of the<BR> संस्काराs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपत्रः|आदित्यपत्र
आदित्य + -पत्रः^1 N. of a plant.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपत्रम्
आदित्य + -पत्रः + .({@-त्रम्@}) the leaf of the <i>Arka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपर्णिनी
आदित्य + -पर्णिनी a creeping plant with gold-coloured flowers, growing<BR> near the bank of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपुराणम्
आदित्य + -पुराणम् N. of an Upapurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपुष्पिका
आदित्य + -पुष्पिका red swallow wort (Mar. शिरदोडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यबन्धुः|आदित्यबन्धु
आदित्य + -बन्धुः N. of Śākyamuni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यभक्ता
आदित्य + -भक्ता [आदित्ये भक्ता] N. of a plant. see अर्कभक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यमण्डलम्
आदित्य + -मण्डलम् the disc or orb of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यव्रतम्
आदित्य + -व्रतम्<BR>—1 worship of the sun; a व्रत or rite.<BR>—2 N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यसूनुः|आदित्यसूनु
आदित्य + -सूनुः ‘the son of the sun’, N. of Sugrīva, Yama, Saturn, Manu and Karṇa &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिन्
आदिन् <i>a.</i> [अत्तीति अद् णिनि] Eating (in comp.); परस्परादिनः Ms. 12. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिनवः|आदिनव|आदिनवं
आदि(दी)नवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Misfortune, distress.<BR>—2 Hindrance; want of luck (in dice); आदिनवं प्रतिदीन्वे Av. 7. 109. 4.<BR>—3 Fault, transgression; Śi. 2. 22; see अनादीनव.<BR>—4 An inflictor of distress; आदीनवः पुमान् दोषे परिक्लेशदुरन्तयोः Med.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदिनवदर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनवः|आदीनव|आदीनवं
आदि(दी)नवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Misfortune, distress.<BR>—2 Hindrance; want of luck (in dice); आदिनवं प्रतिदीन्वे Av. 7. 109. 4.<BR>—3 Fault, transgression; Śi. 2. 22; see अनादीनव.<BR>—4 An inflictor of distress; आदीनवः पुमान् दोषे परिक्लेशदुरन्तयोः Med.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदिनवदर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिनवम्
आदि(दी)नवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Misfortune, distress.<BR>—2 Hindrance; want of luck (in dice); आदिनवं प्रतिदीन्वे Av. 7. 109. 4.<BR>—3 Fault, transgression; Śi. 2. 22; see अनादीनव.<BR>—4 An inflictor of distress; आदीनवः पुमान् दोषे परिक्लेशदुरन्तयोः Med.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदिनवदर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनवम्
आदि(दी)नवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Misfortune, distress.<BR>—2 Hindrance; want of luck (in dice); आदिनवं प्रतिदीन्वे Av. 7. 109. 4.<BR>—3 Fault, transgression; Śi. 2. 22; see अनादीनव.<BR>—4 An inflictor of distress; आदीनवः पुमान् दोषे परिक्लेशदुरन्तयोः Med.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदिनवदर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिनवदर्श
आदिनवः + -दर्श <i>a.</i> having evil designs towards a fellow-player at dice<BR> (Ved.); अक्षराजाय कितवं कृतायादिनवदर्शम् Vāj. 30. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्
आदिश् €6 U.<BR>—1 To point out, indicate, show; मार्ग आदिश् (oft. in dramas) lead the way; Ś. 5.<BR>—2 To order, direct, command; वेलोपलक्षणार्थमादिष्टोऽस्मि Ś. 4; पुनरप्यादिश<BR> तावदुत्थितः Ku. 4. 16; तेषामप्येतदादिशेत् Ms. 11. 192; आदिक्षदस्याभिगमं<BR> वनाय Bk. 3. 9, 7. 28; R. 1. 54, 2. 65; to appoint; वसुमित्रं गोप्तारमादिश्य M. 5.<BR>—3 To aim at; assign; आदिक्षत्सिंहासनं तस्य Bk. 3. 3; हरिवीराणामादिशद्दक्षिणां दिशम् Rām.<BR>—4 To report, announce; teach, lay down, prescribe, instruct, advise;<BR> न चास्य व्रतमादिशेत् Ms. 4. 80; बुद्धिमादिश्य R. 12. 68.<BR>—5 To specify, determine; प्रतिषिद्धमनादिष्टम् Y. 2. 260.<BR>—6 To foretell, predict; सा सिद्धेनादिष्टा Ratn. 4; Bṛ. S. 5. 96;<BR> आदिष्टः सुरासुरसंगरो भावी V. 5.<BR>—7 To undertake, try; ब्रह्मास्त्रमादिश Mb.<BR>—8 To provoke, challenge.<BR>—9 To profess as oneʼs own duty. ━<i>Caus.</i> To indicate, show, point<BR> out, announce &c. (same as आदिश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्
आदिश् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Aim, design, intention; अस्याऽश्रीणीतादिशं गभस्तौ Rv. 10. 61. 3.<BR>—2 A project, proposition.<BR>—3 A proposal, declaration.<BR>—4 A region, quarter. —5 A sacrifice offered to a particular deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्ट|आदिष्टं|आदिष्टः
आदिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Directed, commanded, advised, enjoined &c. इत्युभयमादिष्टं भवति<BR> Ch. Up. 3. 18. 1.<BR>—2 Said, foretold.<BR>—3 Substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टम्
आदिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Command, order.<BR>—2 Advice.<BR>—3 Leavings of a meal (उच्छिष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन् <i>a.</i> One who gives orders. ━<i>m.</i> (अस्त्यर्थे इनि).<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa in the first order of his life; pupil, student (ब्रह्मचारिन्);<BR> आदिष्टिनो ये राजेन्द्र ब्राह्मणा वेदपारगाः Mb. 13. 22. 17.<BR>—2 A penitent, one engaged in any expiatory rite; आदिष्टी नोदकं कुर्यादावृतस्य<BR> समापनात् Ms. 5. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशः|आदेश
आदेशः<BR>—1 An order, command; भ्रातुरादेशमादाय Rām.; आदेशं देशकालज्ञः<BR> प्रतिजग्राह R. 1. 92; राजद्विष्टादेशकृतः Y. 2. 304 doing acts<BR> forbidden by the king.<BR>—2 Advice, instruction, precept, rule; आदित्यो ब्रह्मेत्यादेशः Ch. Up. 3. 19. 1;<BR> Ken. 4. 4; Bṛ. Up. 2. 3. 6.<BR>—3 Account, information, relation, pointing out, indication.<BR>—4 A prediction, prophecy; विप्रश्निकादेशवचनानि K. 64; see सिद्धादेश also.<BR>—5 (Gram.) A substitute; धातोः स्थान इवादेशं सुग्रीवं संन्यवेशयत् R. 12. 58.<BR>—6 (In astrology) Event, result, consequence of the conjunction of stars.<BR>—7 Determination to perform (a ritual &c. संकल्प), vow; उद्धृतं<BR> मे स्वयं तोयं व्रतादेशं करिष्यति Rām. 2. 22. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदेशकृत्, आदेशकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशकृत्
आदेशः + -कृत् See ग्रामणी; आदेशकृत् वृत्तिहन्ता द्विजानां प्रेषकश्च यः Mb. 5. 37. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशकारिन्
आदेशः + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशनम्
आदेशनम् The act of instructing or commanding. कृतोपनयनस्यास्य<BR> व्रतादेशनमिष्यते Ms. 2. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिकः
आदेशिकः An astrologer (पुष्पभद्रादिकैरादेशिकैरादिष्टा Svapna. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आदेशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ordering, commanding.<BR>—2 Causing, producing.<BR>—3 Exciting, instigating; कपोलपाटलादेशि बभूव रघुचेष्टितम् R. 4. 68. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A commander, director.<BR>—2 An astrologer, fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेष्टृ
आदेष्टृ <i>a.</i> One who orders. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An adviser, commander, director.<BR>—2 An employer of priests (यजमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीप्
आदीप् <i>Caus.</i> To kindle, set on fire; to illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपनम्
आदीपनम्<BR>—1 Setting on fire, inflaming.<BR>—2 Exciting, stimulating; embellishing.<BR>—3 Whitening the walls, floors &c. on festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपित
आदीपित, आदीप्त <i>p. p.</i> Set on fire, blazing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीप्त
आदीपित, आदीप्त <i>p. p.</i> Set on fire, blazing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृ
आदृ €6 Ā. (द्रियते)<BR>—1 To respect, honour, reverence; सीतां रघूत्तम भवत्स्थितिमाद्रियस्व<BR> Mv. 7. 3 receive respectfully; take or receive respectfully; द्वितीयाद्रियते<BR> सदा H. Pr. 7; सर्वे तस्यादृता धर्मा यस्यैते त्रय आदृताः Ms. 2. 234;<BR> Bk. 6. 55.<BR>—2 To heed or care for, mind, take notice of; usually with न; न त्यागमाद्रियते<BR> K. 104, 167; वाक्यं नाद्रियते च बान्धवजनः Bh. 3. 111; अनादृत्य<BR> disregarding; मम वचनमनादृत्य in spite of or notwithstanding my words.<BR>—3 to feel timid from a feeling of respect, be awed.<BR>—4 To apply or devote oneself closely to, have regard for; भूरि श्रुतं<BR> शाश्वतमाद्रियन्ते Māl. 1. 5.<BR>—5 To desire, be eager for; यत्किंचिद् दुर्मदाः स्वैरमाद्रियन्ते निरर्गलम् Mv. 6. 3.<BR>—6 To enjoy honour, be honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरः|आदर
आदरः [आ-दृ-कप्]<BR>—1 Respect, reverence, honour; निर्माणमेव हि तदादरलालनीयम् Māl. 9. 50;<BR> न जातहार्देन न विद्विषादरः Ki. 1. 33; Ku. 6. 20.<BR>—2 Attention, care, notice, close application; आदरप्रयत्न Māl. 7<BR> careful efforts; तां प्रणामादरस्रस्तजाम्बूनदवतंसकाम् Ku. 6. 91.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Eagerness, desire, regard; भूयान्दारार्थमादरः Ku. 6. 13;<BR> आदरादुपसर्पिततुरङ्गः K. 119 eagerly; यत्किंचनकारितायामादरः 120;<BR> अन्वेष्टु-मादरमकरवम् 152<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">Page0330-1</a>]<BR> made up my mind; Ki. 8. 26, 41, 13. 58.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Earnest desire, request; Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Effort, endeavour; गृहयन्त्रपताकाश्रीरपौरादरनिर्मिता Ku. 6. 41.<BR>—5 Commencement, beginning.<BR>—6 Love, attachment.<BR>—7 Acceptance; तस्मादेषां व्यर्थहिंसानिवृत्त्यै स्यादुत्कृष्टः पिष्टपश्वादरोऽपि<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0329-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरणम्
आदरणम् Notice, respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरणीय
आदरणीय, आदर्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i> Venerable, respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्तव्य|आदर्त्तव्य
आदरणीय, आदर्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i> Venerable, respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदारः|आदार
आदारः Ved.<BR>—1 Allurement, attraction, an instigator (Sāy.).<BR>—2 N. of a plant used instead of Soma (when it is not available).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदारिन्
आदारिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Attracting.<BR>—2 Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदुरि
आदुरि <i>a.</i> Ved. Careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आदृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Honoured, respected.<BR>—2 (Used actively),<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Zealous, diligent, earnest; आदृततरमवोचत् K. 211, 170; Ku. 7. 30.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Attentive, careful; दण्डनीत्यां नात्यादृअतोऽभूत् Dk. 154.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Respectful (सादर); इत्यादृतेन कथितौ R. 13. 72; इति<BR> स्म पृच्छत्यनुवेलमादृतः 3. 5 respectfully or earnestly; Ms. 11. 225, 7. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृश्
आदृश् €1 P. To look at, see, behold. ━<i>Caus.</i> To show, indicate,<BR> exhibit; उत्कलादर्शितपथः R. 4. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शः|आदर्श
आदर्शः [आदृश्यतेऽत्र, दृश् आधारे घञ्]<BR>—1 A mirror, a looking-glass; यथादर्शे तथात्मनि Kaṭh. 6. 5.<BR> यथादर्शो मलेन च Bg. 3. 38. आत्मानमालोक्य च शोभमानमादर्शबिम्बे<BR> स्तिमितायताक्षी Ku. 7. 22.<BR>—2 The original manuscript from which a copy is taken; (fig.) a pattern,<BR> model, type; आदर्शः शिक्षितानाम् Mk. 1. 48; आदर्शः सर्वशास्त्राणाम्<BR> K. 5; so गुणानाम् &c.<BR>—3 A copy of a work.<BR>—4 A commentary, gloss. cf. आदर्शो दर्पणे टीका प्रतिपुस्तकयोरपि Med.<BR>—5 A particular boundary of a country.<BR>—6 N. of a country.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदर्शमण्डलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शमण्डलः|आदर्शमण्डल
आदर्शः + -मण्डलः^1<BR>—1 a globular mirror.<BR>—2 the surface of a mirror.<BR>—3 a kind of snake (with globular spots).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: remove n. gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शकः|आदर्शक
आदर्शकः A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शनम्
आदर्शनम्<BR>—1 Showing, making apparent, displaying.<BR>—2 A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृष्टिः|आदृष्टि
आदृष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Looking at, power of looking.<BR>—2 Sight, glance, look.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आदृष्टिगोचरम्, आदृष्टिप्रसरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृष्टिगोचरम्
आदृष्टिः + -गोचरम्, -प्रसरम् <i>ind.</i> Within range of sight; आदृष्टिप्रसरात्प्रियस्य<BR> पदवीमुद्वीक्ष्य निर्विण्णया Amaru. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृष्टिप्रसरम्
आदृष्टिः + -गोचरम्, -प्रसरम् <i>ind.</i> Within range of sight; आदृष्टिप्रसरात्प्रियस्य<BR> पदवीमुद्वीक्ष्य निर्विण्णया Amaru. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदॄ
आदॄ €9 U. Ved.<BR>—1 To crush, split open.<BR>—2 To make accessible, bring to light, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्दिर
आदर्दिर <i>a.</i> Ved. Crushing, splitting open; आदर्दिरासो अद्रयो<BR> न विश्वहा Rv. 10. 78. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदारिन्
आदारिन्, आदुरि <i>a.</i> Crushing, destroying; आदारिणं यथा<BR> गयम् Rv. 8. 45. 13; वामंवामं त आदुरे देवो ददात्वर्यमा Rv. 4. 30. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदुरि
आदारिन्, आदुरि <i>a.</i> Crushing, destroying; आदारिणं यथा<BR> गयम् Rv. 8. 45. 13; वामंवामं त आदुरे देवो ददात्वर्यमा Rv. 4. 30. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवक
आदेवक <i>a.</i> [दिव्-ण्वुल्] One who sports or plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवनम्
आदेवनम्<BR>—1 Gambling.<BR>—2 A die used in gambling.<BR>—3 A board for gambling; place for playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य see under आदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
आद्यून <i>a.</i> [आ-दिव्-क्त, ऊठ् नत्वं च P. V. 2. 67; perhaps derived<BR> from अद् to eat] Shamelessly voracious, gluttonous, hungry; ‘आद्यूनः स्यादौदरिको विजिगीषाविवर्जिते’ इत्यमरः;<BR> न चैनमाद्यून इति क्षिपन्ति<BR> Mb. 5. 37. 34; आद्यूनः सद्गृहिण्येव प्रायो यष्टपावलम्बितः Ki. 11. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्योतः|आद्योत
आद्योतः Light, brilliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्रिसार
आद्रिसार <i>a.</i> Made of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमनम्
आधमनम्<BR>—1 A deposit, pledge; एको ह्यनीशः सर्वत्र दानाधमनविकये; Kāty.;<BR> योगाधमनविकीतं योगदानप्रतिग्रहम् Ms. 8. 165.<BR>—2 Fraudulent puffing of goods at a sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमर्णिकः
आधमर्णिकः A debtor; मूलात्तु द्विगुणा वृद्धिर्गृहीता चाधमर्णिकात्<BR> Śukra. 4. 830.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमर्ण्यम्
आधमर्ण्यम् [अधमर्णस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] The state of being indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्मिक|आधर्म्मिक
आधर्मिक <i>a.</i> [अधर्मं चरति ठञ् P. IV. 4. 41. Vārt.] Unjust,<BR> unrighteous; तदिदं पार्षतेनेह महदाधर्मिकं कृतम् Mb. 7. 195. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधा
आधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To put, place, deposit, implant, lodge; ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि Bg. 5. 10, 8. 12.<BR> जनपदे न गदः पदमादधौ R. 9. 4; Bg. 5. 10; दुष्यन्तेनाहितं<BR> तेजः Ś. 4. 4; आहितो जयविपर्ययोऽपि मे R. 11. 86 inflicted on<BR> me 19. 26; संभृते शिखिनि गूढमादधुः 19. 54 consigned to the flames,<BR> burnt; धैर्यं चाऽऽधिषताधिकम् Bk. 7. 102 plucked up greater courage.<BR>—2 To apply, propose, fix upon, direct towards; प्रतिपात्रमाधयितां<BR> यत्नः Ś. 1; मग्येव मन आधत्स्व Bg. 12. 8; गमने मतिमाधत्त<BR> Rām.; Ś. 2. 3; आधीयतां धैर्ये धर्मे च धीः K. 63 direct; सर्वकार्येष्वाहितमतिः K. 56.<BR>—3 To appropriate to oneself, hold, possess, take, carry, have, bear;<BR> भूयो बभौ दर्पणमादधानाम् Ku. 7. 26; आधत्ते कनकमयातपत्रलक्ष्मीम्<BR> Ki. 5. 39 takes or assumes; गर्भमाधत्त राज्ञी R. 2. 75, 5. 57; आहितक्रोधा Amaru. 21.<BR>—4 To bear up, uphold, support; शेषः सदैवाहितभूमिभारः Ś. 5. 4.<BR>—5 To cause, produce, create, rouse, excite (fear, wonder &c.); छायाश्चरन्ति<BR> बहुधा भयमादधानाः Ś. 3. 26; Ki. 4. 12, 6. 19, 8. 46, 57; Ku. 6. 20;<BR> Bk. 2. 8; विस्मयमादधाति M. 5. 17; K. 246; नवरसरुचिरां निर्मितिमादधती<BR> भारती K. P. 1; to put in, infuse; Śi. 2. 76.<BR>—6 To supply, give, impart (with dat., gen. or loc.); शुद्धिमादधाना<BR> R. 1. 85; इन्द्रं त्रैलोक्यमाधाय Mb.<BR>—8 To appoint; तमेव चाधाय विवाहसाक्ष्ये R. 7. 20.<BR>—8 To consecrate (as fire); तत्राग्निमाधाय समित्समिद्धम् Ku. 1. 57.<BR>—9 To perform, practise (as a vow &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधातृ
आधातृ <i>a.</i> One that puts in, deposits, imparts &c.; पात्रविशेषे<BR> न्यस्तं गुणान्तरं व्रजति शिल्पमाधातुः M. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानम्
आधानम्<BR>—1 Placing, putting upon; समिदाधानं, तुलाधानम् &c.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Taking, having.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Receiving, recovering.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">Page0331-1</a>]<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Containing or being in possession of anything or consecrating.<BR>—3 Keeping the sacred fire (अग्न्याधान), a ceremony performed with<BR> the sacred fire; पुनर्दारक्रियां कुर्यात् पुनराधानमेव च Ms. 5. 168.<BR>—4 Doing, executing, performing; आज्ञापयामास नरेन्द्रसूनुः स्वर्गीयमाधानमदीनसत्त्वः<BR> Rām. 6. 109. 24. (स्वर्गीयमाधानम् = प्रेतकृत्यम्)<BR>—5 Infusing, putting in, inspiring, imparting; गुणो विशेषाधानहेतुः<BR> सिद्धो वस्तुधर्मः S. D. 2; निश्चयाधानम् K. 262; प्रजानां विनयाधानाद्रक्षणाद्<BR> भरणादपि R. 1. 24 imparting or providing moral instruction.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Engendering, producing, कौतुकाधानहेतोः Me. 3; गर्भाधानक्षणपरिचयात् 9.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Assigning, attributing, employing.<BR>—7 Effort, exertion, application; Mv. 3. 13.<BR>—8 A pledge, deposit; Y. 2. 238, 247. विक्रयाधानवर्ज्यम् Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR>—9 A place where anything is deposited, a receptacle, as in पक्वाधानम्,<BR> पुरुषाधानम्, अयं मध्यमः प्राणः तस्येदमेवाधानम् Bṛ. Up. 2. 2. 1.<BR>—10 A surety.<BR>—11 Enclosure, circuit.<BR>—12 A ceremony performed previous to conception; see गर्भाधान.<BR>—13 cohabitation (मैथुन) तवापि मृत्युराधानादकृतप्रज्ञ दर्शितः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 9. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0330-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानिकः|आधानिक|आधानिकं
आधानिकः [आधान-ठञ्] A ceremony performed after cohabitation<BR> to cause or favour conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधायः|आधाय
आधायः One who has placed anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधायक
आधायक <i>a.</i> Putting, placing, assigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिः|आधि
आधिः <i>m.</i> [आधीयते स्थाप्यते प्रतीकाराय मनोऽनेन, आ-धा-कि<BR> P. III. 3. 92; connected with आध्यै in some senses]<BR>—1 Mental pain or anguish, agony, anxiety (opp. व्याधि which is bodily<BR> pain); न तेषामापदः सन्ति नाधयो व्याधयस्तथा Mb.; मनोगतमाधिहेतुम्<BR> Ś. 3. 10; R. 8. 27, 9. 54; Bh. 3. 105; Bv. 4. 11; Māl. 4; Ki. 1. 37.<BR>—2 A bane, curse, misery; यान्त्येवं गृहिणीपदं युवतयो वामाः कुलस्याधयः<BR> Ś. 4. 18; Mv. 6. 28.<BR>—3 A pledge, deposit, pawn, mortgage; Y. 2. 23; Ms. 8. 143; आधिश्चोपनिधिश्चोभौ<BR> न कालात्ययमर्हतः 145.<BR>—4 A place, residence.<BR>—5 Location, site.<BR>—6 Definition, epithet, attribute, title.<BR>—7 Misfortune, calamity (व्यसन).<BR>—8 Reflection on religion or duty (धर्मचिन्ता)<BR>—9 Hope, expectation.<BR>—10 A man solicitous for the maintenance of his family (कुटुम्बव्यापृत).<BR>—11 Punishment; एनमाधिं दापयिष्येद्यस्मात्तेन भयं क्वचित् Śukra. 4. 641.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आधिज्ञ, आधिभोगः, आधिमन्युः, आधिस्तेनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिज्ञ|आधिज्ञः
आधिः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 suffering pain, distressed.<BR>—2 crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभोगः|आधिभोग
आधिः + -भोगः the use or enjoyment of a deposit (as of a horse, cow &c. when pledged).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिमन्युः|आधिमन्यु
आधिः + -मन्युः (pl.) feverish heat or burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिस्तेनः|आधिस्तेन
आधिः + -स्तेनः one who uses a deposit without the ownerʼs consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधित्वम्
आधित्वम्, -ता<BR> The nature or circumstance of a pledge; ˚उपाधि the object<BR> or purpose for which a pledge is given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिता
आधित्वम्, -ता<BR> The nature or circumstance of a pledge; ˚उपाधि the object<BR> or purpose for which a pledge is given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृ
आधीकृ €8 P. To pledge, mortgage, pawn, deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकरणम्
आधीकरणम् Pledging, a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेय|आधेयं
आधेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be placed, pledged, appointed &c.<BR>—2 To be assigned, attributed, or given.<BR>—3 To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">Page0331-2</a>]<BR> received, held, or supported; to be contained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेयम्
आधेय + .{@-यम्@} = आधानम् Putting, placing; अग्न्याधेयानि गुर्वर्थम् Mb. 12. 18. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहित|आहितः
आहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed, set, deposited; मनस्याहितकर्तव्याः Ku. 2. 62 bearing<BR> in mind what they had to do; भारतीमाहितभराम् Śi. 2. 69 full of deep meaning.<BR>—2 Given, imparted.<BR>—3 Entertained, felt.<BR>—4 Comprising, containing.<BR>—5 Performed, done.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहिताग्नि, आहिताङ्क, आहितौत्सुक्य, आहितक्लम, आहितलक्षण, आहितव्यथ, आहितस्वन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताग्नि|आहिताग्निः
आहित + -अग्नि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who keeps or places the fire on the altar, sacrificer; cf. अग्न्याहित.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa who maintains and consecrates sacred fire in his house perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताङ्क|आहितांक
आहित + -अङ्क <i>a.</i> marked, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितौत्सुक्य
आहित + -औत्सुक्य <i>a.</i> one who creates anxiety; तमाहितौत्सुक्यमदर्शनेन R. 2. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितक्लम
आहित + -क्लम <i>a.</i> exhausted, tired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितलक्षण|आहितलक्षणः
आहित + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> bearing a characteristic epithet; ककुत्स्थ इत्याहितलक्षणोऽभूत<BR> R. 6. 71; (according to Malli. = प्रख्यातगुण noted or well-known for<BR> good qualities).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितव्यथ
आहित + -व्यथ <i>a.</i> pained, grieved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितस्वन
आहित + -स्वन <i>a.</i> making a sound, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितिः|आहिति
आहितिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Placing on, anything placed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकरणिकः|आधिकरणिक
आधिकरणिकः [अधिकरणे नियुक्तः ठक्] A judge; Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारण्यम्
आधिकारण्यम् Possession, location.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारिक
आधिकारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Supreme, superior, relating to a person or thing in authority.<BR>—2 Official, belonging to any office or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्यम्
आधिक्यम् [अधिकस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Excess, abundance, preponderance, high degree; ऋद्धेराधिक्यं समृद्धिः Sk.<BR>—2 Superiority, supremacy; आधिक्यं साधितम् H. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अधिदेव-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Relating to अधिदेव or tutelary deity (as a Mantra); अधियज्ञं<BR> ब्रह्म जपेदाधिदैविकमेव च Ms. 6. 83.<BR>—2 Caused by fate (as pain &c.); according to Suśruta pain is of three<BR> kinds; आध्यात्मिक, आधिभौतिक or आधिदैविक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्यम्
आधिपत्यम् [अधिपतेर्भावः कर्म वा यक्]<BR>—1 Supremacy, power, sovereignty, lordship; अश्मान्नानामाधिपत्यं जगाम<BR> Av. 18. 4. 54. राज्यं सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम् (अवाप्य) Bg. 2. 8.<BR>—2 The duties of a king; पाण्डोः पुत्रं प्रकुरुष्वाधिपत्ये Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिक|आधिभौतिकं
आधिभौतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अधिभूत-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Caused by animals (as pain).<BR>—2 Relating to beings.<BR>—3 Elementary, material, derived from the primitive elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिमासिक
आधिमासिक <i>a.</i> Relating to an intercalary month; करणाधिष्ठितमाधिमासिकं<BR> कुर्यात् Kau. A. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिरथिः|आधिरथि
आधिरथिः N. of Karṇa. हतं भीष्ममथाधिरथिर्विदित्वा Mb. 7. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिराज्यम्
आधिराज्यम् [अधिराजस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] Royalty, sovereignty,<BR> supreme sway; बभौ भूयः कुमारत्वादाधिराज्यमवाप्य सः R. 17. 30; Mu. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिवेदनिकम्
आधिवेदनिकम् [अधिवेदनाय हितं ठक् तत्र काले दत्तं ठञ् वा]<BR> Property, gifts &c. made to a first wife upon marrying a second; यच्च<BR> द्वितीयविवाहार्थिना पूर्वस्त्रियै पारितोषिकं घनं दत्तं तदाधिवेदनिकम्<BR> Viṣṇu.; cf. Y. 2. 143, 148 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0331-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधु
आधु €5 U. To shake, stir, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधवः|आधव
आधवः Ved.<BR>—1 One who stirs up or agitates.<BR>—2 That which is agitated, mixture.<BR>—3 Throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधवनम्
आधवनम् Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधवनीयः|आधवनीय
आधवनीयः A vessel in which the Soma plant is shaken and cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधावः|आधाव
आधावः That which is shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूत|आधूतः
आधूत <i>a.</i> Shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुनिक|आधुनिकः
आधुनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अधुना भवः ठञ्] New, modern, of recent origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृ
आधृ €1. €10. P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To hold, keep, contain; सर्वं चाधारयेत् हृदि Ks. 2. 37.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To support, bear.<BR>—2 To bring, supply; आ पवमान धारय रयिं सहस्रवर्चसम् Rv. 9. 12. 9.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To stop, to suspend; हंसक वृत्तान्तं तावदाधारय, यावदहमुच्छ्वसिमि Pratijñā. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारः|आधार
आधारः [आ-घृ घञ्; आध्रियन्तेऽस्मिन्क्रियाः इति Kāśi.]<BR>—1 Support, prop, stay; इत्याधारानुरोधात्त्रिपुरविजयिनः पातु वो दुःखनृत्तम्<BR> (Some annotators explain आधार as local conditions); Mu. 1. 2.<BR>—2 (Hence) Power of sustaining, aid, patronage, assistance; त्वमेव<BR> चातकाधारः Bh. 2. 50.<BR>—3 A receptacle, reservoir; तिष्ठन्त्याप इवाधारे Pt. 1. 67; चराचराणां<BR> भूतानां कुक्षिराधारतां गतः Ku. 6. 67; अपामिवाधारमनुत्तरङ्गम्<BR> Ku. 3. 48; तोयाधारपथाश्च वल्कलशिखानिष्यन्दरेखाङ्किताः Ś. 1. 14;<BR> आधारः क्षमाम्भसाम् K. 44; Y. 3. 144, 165.<BR>—4 That which holds or contains, a vessel, recipient.<BR>—5 A part, character (in dramas); भेदैः सूक्ष्मैरभिव्यक्तैः प्रत्याधारं<BR> विभज्यते Mv. 1. 3.<BR>—6 A basin round the foot of a tree; आधारबन्धप्रमुखैः प्रयत्नैः R. 5. 6.<BR>—7 A dike, dam, embankment.<BR>—8 A canal.<BR>—9 The sense of the locative case, location, comprehension; आधारोऽधिकरणम्;<BR> (आधार is of 3 kinds.━ औपश्लेषिक, वैषयिक, and अभिव्यापक<BR> see Sk. on P. I. 4. 45).<BR>—10 Relation.<BR>—11 A ray. cf. आधार आलवालेऽम्बुबन्धे च किरणेऽपि च Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आधाराधेयभावः, आधारचक्रम्, आधारशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाराधेयभावः|आधाराधेयभाव
आधारः + -आधेयभावः the influence, relation, or action of the support<BR> or recipient upon the thing received or supported; H. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारचक्रम्
आधारः + -चक्रम् N. of a mystical circle on the posterior part of the body; Rasikaramaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारशक्तिः|आधारशक्ति
आधारः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Māyā or illusion.<BR>—2 the Supreme goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारकः|आधारक
आधारकः A foundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारणम्
आधारणम् Holding, supporting, sustaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार्य
आधार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be located.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आधार्याधारसंबन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार्याधारसंबन्धः
आधार्य + -आधारसंबन्धः the relation of the recipient and the thing to<BR> be received or located.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृत
आधृत <i>a.</i> Ved. Contained, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्
आधृष् €5 P.<BR>—1 To assail, defy.<BR>—2 To overcome, injure, hurt. €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To defy, challenge; assail, attack; स्मृत्याचारव्यपेतेन मार्गेणाधर्षितः<BR> परैः Y. 2. 5; injure, hurt, overcome.<BR>—2 To convict, refute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षः|आधर्ष
आधर्षः<BR>—1 Contempt.<BR>—2 Injuring forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षणम्
आधर्षणम्<BR>—1 Conviction of crime or error; sentence.<BR>—2 Refutation.<BR>—3 Injuring, annoying; आधर्षणं न कुर्वन्तु यस्य कस्यापि सर्वदा<BR> Śukra. 1. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षित
आधर्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Injured, annoyed forcibly.<BR>—2 Aggrieved, censured, injured.<BR>—3 Refuted in argument, disproved.<BR>—4 Sentenced, convicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्ट
आधृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Checked, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्टिः|आधृष्टि
आधृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Assailing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेनवम्
आधेनवम् [अधेनु-अञ्] अधेनूनां समूहः Mbh. on P. IV. 2. 45. Want of cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधोरणः|आधोरण
आधोरणः [आ-धोर्-ल्युट्; धोरृ गतिचातुर्ये €1 P.] The rider or driver<BR> of an elephant; आधोरणानां गजसन्निपाते शिरांसि चकैर्निशितैः क्षुराग्रैः<BR> R. 7. 46, 5. 48, 18. 39; Śi. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मा
आध्मा €1 P.<BR>—1 To inflate, puff up, swell.<BR>—2 To blow or fill with wind, sound (as a conch &c.). ━<i>pass.</i> To<BR> be elated or inflated, be filled; तव भुजबलदर्पाध्मायमानस्य वामः<BR> शिरसि चरण एष न्यस्यते वारयैनम् Ve. 3. 40; Mv. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मात|आध्मातः
आध्मात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Puffed up, inflated, elated, filled with (lit. and fig.). charged with;<BR> पापेनेवाध्मातमूर्तयः K. 107; Dk. 110; मिथ्याध्मात Mv. 3. 28, 6. 30;<BR> Mk. 9. 12; अमृत˚ U. 6. 21; Mk. 5. 22; भर˚ हृदयः U. 1. 29;<BR> दर्प˚ filled with pride.<BR>—2 Excessively affected, increased, magnified; ज्यानिर्घोषममन्ददुन्दुभिरवैराध्मातम्<BR> U. 5. 6; Mk. 5. 18.<BR>—3 Sounded, sounding, dinned; जनकोलाहलाध्माता (नगरी) Rām. 5. 55. 31.<BR>—4 Burnt.<BR>—5 Sick by the swelling of the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मातः|आध्मात
आध्मात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Flatulence, swelling of the abdomen with noise.<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मानम्
आध्मानम् [आ-ध्मा-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Blowing inflation; (fig.) growth, increase; अयं विन्ध्यो येनाहृतविहृतिराध्मानमजहात् Mv. 7. 14.<BR>—2 Boasting, vaunting.<BR>—3 A bellows.<BR>—4 Intumescence, swelling of the belly, body &c., dropsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मानी
आध्मानम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A kind of fragrant substance.<BR>—2 A blow-pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मापनम्
आध्मापनम् A means of inflating or causing a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यक्ष्यम्
आध्यक्ष्यम् [अध्यक्ष-ष्यञ्] Ved.<BR>—1 Superintendence.<BR>—2 Presence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यात्मिक|आध्यात्मिकं
आध्यात्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आत्मानम् अधिकृत्य भवः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Relating to the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 Spiritual, holy; जपयज्ञप्रसिद्धपर्थं विद्यां चाध्यात्मिकीं जपेत्<BR> Y. 1. 101; Ms. 2. 117<BR>—3 Relating to self.<BR>—4 Caused by the mind (pain, sorrow &c.); see आधिदैविक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यापकः|आध्यापक
आध्यापकः [अध्यापक एव स्वार्थे अण्] A teacher, a spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यायिक
आध्यायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अध्याय ठञ्] Occupied or employed in reading<BR> or studying (the Vedas) (अधीतवेद); युवा स्यात्साधुयुवाध्यायिकः T. Up. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यासिक
आध्यासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अध्यासेन कल्पितः ठक्] Caused by <i>adhyāsa</i><BR> <i>i. e.</i> by attributing the nature and properties of one thing to another<BR> (in Vedānta Phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यै
आध्यै €1 P. To think on, meditate, remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधी
आधी <i>f.</i> Ved. Thinking, longing, care, anxiety; विकुर्वन्क्रियया<BR> चाधीरनिर्वृत्तिश्च चेतसाम् Bhāg. 11. 25. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीत
आधीत <i>p. p.</i> Ved. Reflected or meditated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीतम्
आधीत + .{@-तम्@} The object or subject of oneʼs thought; that which is intended or hoped for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्या
आध्या [आध्या-अड्] Remembering, especially with regret, sorrowful recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यानम्
आध्यानम्<BR>—1 Anxiety.<BR>—2 Remembering with regret, pensive or sorrowful recollection; आध्यानमुत्कण्ठापूर्वकस्मरणम् Sk.<BR>—3 Meditating or reflecting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्र|आध्रः
आध्र <i>a.</i> Ved. [आ-धृ-क] Poor, indigent, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्रः|आध्र
आध्र + .{@-ध्रः@} Support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वनिक
आध्वनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अध्वनि व्यापृतः कुशलो वा ठक्] Being on a journey,<BR> way-faring; कान्तारेष्वपि विश्रामो जनस्याध्वनिकस्य वै Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वरिक|आध्वरिकः
आध्वरिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अध्वर-ठक्] One who knows or has studied works<BR> relating to the (Soma) sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वरिकः|आध्वरिक
आध्वरिक + .{@-कः@} [अध्वरस्य व्याख्यानो ग्रन्थः] A work which treats of (Soma) sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वर्यव|आध्वर्य्यव
आध्वर्यव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अध्वर्योः इदम् अञ्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the <i>adhvaryu</i> (q. v.) or to the Yajurveda.<BR>—2 One conversant with the Yajurveda; (P. IV. 3. 123).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वर्यवम्
आध्वर्यव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Service at a sacrifice.<BR>—2 Particularly, the office of an Adhvaryu priest; अहरहरश्विनाध्वर्यवं<BR> वाम् Rv. 10. 52. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनः|आन
आनः<BR>—1 Inhalation, breath inspired.<BR>—2 Mouth or nose (Sāy.); त्वमिन्द्र प्रत्यानं जघन्थ Rv. 1. 52. 15.<BR> Breathing, blowing<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्
आनः + .{@-नम्@} Living leings; अनितीत्यानं प्राणिजातम् Mahānār. Dīpikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकः|आनक
आनकः [आनयति उत्साहवतः करोति अन्-णिच्-ण्वुल् Tv.]<BR>—1 A large military drum (beaten at one end), a double drum, a drum or<BR> tabor in general; पणवानकगोमुखाः । सहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त Bg. 1. 13.<BR>—2 The thundercloud. cf.<BR> … आनकः स्वनदम्बुदे । भेर्यां मृदङ्गे पटहे … Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आनकदुन्दुभिः, आनकस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभिः|आनकदुन्दुभि
आनकः + -दुन्दुभिः epithet of Vasudeva, father of Kṛṣṇa; cf. Hariv.<BR> वसुदेवो महाबाहुः पूर्वमानकदुन्दुभिः । जज्ञे यस्य प्रसूतस्य दुन्दुभ्यः<BR> प्राणदन्दिवि ॥ आनकानां च संह्रादः सुमहानभवद्दिवि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभिः|आनकदुन्दुभि
आनकः + -दुन्दुभिः + .({@-भिः, -भी@} <i>f.</i>) a large drum or <i>dhol</i>, kettle-drum (beaten at one end).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभी
आनकः + -दुन्दुभिः + .({@-भिः, -भी@} <i>f.</i>) a large drum or <i>dhol</i>, kettle-drum (beaten at one end).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकस्थली
आनकः + -स्थली N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनडुह
आनडुह <i>a.</i> (-ही <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनडुह इदम् अण्] Belonging to or originating<BR> from a bull; चर्मण्यानडुहे रक्ते स्थाप्यं भद्रासनं ततः Y. 1. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आननम्
आननम् [आनित्यनेन, आ-अन् करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The mouth, face; R. 3. 3; नृपस्य कान्तं पिबतः सुताननम् 17.<BR>—2 A large division of a work, chapter, book &c. (<i>e. g.</i> the two <i>ānanas</i><BR> of Rasagaṅgādhara.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्तर्यम्
आनन्तर्यम् [अनन्तर-ष्यञ् P. IV. 1. 104.]<BR>—1 Immediate succession; आनन्तर्यं चारभते Rām. 5. 133. 17.<BR>—2 Immediate<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">Page0333-2</a>]<BR> proximity, absence of interval (of time or space); आनन्तर्याद्विधास्यामि<BR> संप्रधार्य बलाबलम् Rām. 4. 8. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्त्यम्
आनन्त्यम् [अनन्त-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Infinity, endlessness (in time, space or number); आनन्त्याद् व्यभिचाराच्च K. P. 2.<BR>—2 Boundlessness.<BR>—3 Immortality, eternity; स चानन्त्याय कल्पते Śvet. Up. 5. 9; Ms. 3. 266, 6. 84, 9. 107;<BR> लोकानन्त्यं दिवः प्राप्तिः पुत्रपौत्रप्रपौत्रके<BR> Y. 1. 78, 261; स्वधर्मः स्वर्गायानन्त्याय च Kau. A. 1. 3; न वयं<BR> साध्वि साम्राज्यं स्वाराज्यं भोज्यमप्युत । वैराज्यं पारमेष्ठपं च आनन्त्यं<BR> वा हरेः पदम् ॥ Bhāg. 10. 83. 41.<BR>—4 An upper world, heaven, future happiness; यस्तु नित्यं कृतमतिर्धर्ममेवाभिपद्यते ।<BR> अशङ्कमानः कल्याणि सोऽमुत्रानन्त्यमश्नुते Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द्|आनंद्
आनन्द् €1 P. To rejoice, be glad or delighted; आनन्दितारस्त्वां दृष्ट्वा Bk. 22. 14; Gīt. 11.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To gladden, delight; जगदानन्दयेत्सर्वम्<BR> Y. 1. 356; Bk. 21. 12; एष ह्येवानन्दयति T. Up. 2. 7. 1, 2. 4. 1, 2. 9. 1.<BR>—2 To amuse oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दः|आनन्द|आनंदः
आनन्दः [आनन्द्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Happiness, joy, delight, pleasure; आनन्दं ब्रह्मणो विद्वान्न बिभेति<BR> कदाचन T. Up. supreme bliss or felicity; आनन्द एवास्य विज्ञानमात्मानन्दात्मनो<BR> हैवं सर्वे देवाः Śat. Br.<BR>—2 God, Supreme Spirit (ब्रह्मन्) (said to be <i>n.</i> also in this sense;<BR> cf. विज्ञानमानन्दं ब्रह्म Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.).<BR>—3 N. of the forty-eighth year of the cycle of Jupiter.<BR>—4 N. of Śiva.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 N. of Balarāma (according to Jaina doctrines).<BR>—7 N. of a cousin and follower and favourite disciple of Buddha Śākyamuni,<BR> compiler of the Sūtras.<BR>—8 A variety of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दा
आनन्दः + .{@-दा, -दी@} N. of two plants (Mar. भाङ्ग, रानमोगरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दी
आनन्दः + .{@-दा, -दी@} N. of two plants (Mar. भाङ्ग, रानमोगरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दम्
आनन्दः + .{@-दम्@}<BR>—1 Wine, liquor.<BR>—2 A kind of house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आनन्दार्णवः, आनन्दकाननम्, आनन्दवनम्, आनन्दगिरिः, आनन्दज्ञानः, आनन्दज्ञानगिरिः, आनन्दज, आनन्दतीर्थः, आनन्दद, आनन्दकर, आनन्दकरः, आनन्ददत्तः, आनन्दपटः, आनन्दपूर्ण, आनन्दप्रभवः, आनन्दभैरव, आनन्दलहरिः, आनन्दलहरी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दार्णवः
आनन्दः + -अर्णवः the delight of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दकाननम्
आनन्दः + -काननम्, -वनम् N. of Kāśī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दवनम्
आनन्दः + -काननम्, -वनम् N. of Kāśī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दगिरिः|आनन्दगिरि
आनन्दः + -गिरिः, -ज्ञानः, -ज्ञानगिरिः N. of a celebrated annotator on Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दज्ञानः|आनन्दज्ञान
आनन्दः + -गिरिः, -ज्ञानः, -ज्ञानगिरिः N. of a celebrated annotator on Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दज्ञानगिरिः|आनन्दज्ञानगिरि
आनन्दः + -गिरिः, -ज्ञानः, -ज्ञानगिरिः N. of a celebrated annotator on Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दज
आनन्दः + -ज <i>a.</i> caused by joy (as tears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दतीर्थः|आनन्दतीर्थ
आनन्दः + -तीर्थः N. of Madhva, the founder of a Vaiṣṇava school of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दद
आनन्दः + -द, -कर <i>a.</i> exhilarating, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दकर|आनन्दकरः
आनन्दः + -द, -कर <i>a.</i> exhilarating, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दकरः|आनन्दकर
आनन्दः + -करः The moon; दधार सर्वात्मकमात्मभूतं काष्ठा यथानन्दकरं<BR> मनस्तः Bhāg. 10. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्ददत्तः|आनन्ददत्त
आनन्दः + -दत्तः [आनन्दो दत्तो येन] the membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दपटः|आनन्दपट|आनन्दपटं
आनन्दः + -पटः [आनन्दजनको पटः] a bridal garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दपूर्ण|आनन्दपूर्णः|आनन्दपूर्ण्ण
आनन्दः + -पूर्ण <i>a.</i> delighted supremely, full of bliss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दपूर्णः|आनन्दपूर्ण|आनन्दपूर्ण्ण
आनन्दः + -पूर्ण + .({@-र्णः@}) the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दप्रभवः|आनन्दप्रभव|आनन्दप्रभवं
आनन्दः + -प्रभवः semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दभैरव|आनन्दभैरवः
आनन्दः + -भैरव <i>a.</i> causing both joy and fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दभैरवः|आनन्दभैरव
आनन्दः + -भैरव + .({@-वः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दलहरिः|आनन्दलहरि
आनन्दः + -लहरिः, -लहरी <i>f.</i> ‘wave of enjoyment’, title of a small hymn<BR> by Śaṅkarācārya addressed to Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दलहरी
आनन्दः + -लहरिः, -लहरी <i>f.</i> ‘wave of enjoyment’, title of a small hymn<BR> by Śaṅkarācārya addressed to Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दक|आनंदक
आनन्दक <i>a.</i> Delighting, gladdening, blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दता
आनन्दता Joyfulness, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दथु|आनंदथु|आनन्दथुः
आनन्दथु <i>a.</i> [आ-नन्द् अथुच् P. III. 3. 89.] Happy, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दथुः|आनन्दथु|आनंदथु
आनन्दथु + .{@-थुः@} Happiness, joy, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दन|आनंदन|आनन्दनं
आनन्दन <i>a.</i> Pleasing, delighting; Rām. 2. 2. 27. (fig. a son);<BR> ˚नं चेतसः H. 1. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दनम्
आनन्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Delighting, making happy.<BR>—2 Paying respects to.<BR>—3 Courteous treatment of a friend or a guest at meeting and parting,<BR> courtesy, civility.<BR>—4 What gives or produces delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमय|आनंदमय|आनन्दमयः
आनन्दमय <i>a.</i> Blissful, full of joy, made up or consisting of<BR> happiness; सुषुप्तिस्थान एकीभूतः प्रज्ञानघन एवानन्दमयो ह्यानन्दभुक्<BR> Māṇḍ. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमयः|आनन्दमय|आनंदमय
आनन्दमय + .{@-यः@} The Supreme Spirit; Br. Sūt. 1. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमयी
आनन्दमय + .{@-यी^1@} A form of Durgā. {@˚कोशः@} the innermost wrapper or<BR> vesture of the body, causal frame enshrining the soul; see कोश.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दयितव्यम्
आनन्दयितव्यम् The object of enjoyment or sensual pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दयितृ|आनंदयितृ
आनन्दयितृ <i>a.</i> One who gives joy or delight; आनन्दयिता कर्ता<BR> Maitr. Up. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिः|आनन्दि|आनंदिः
आनन्दिः [आ-नन्द्-इन्]<BR>—1 Joy, happiness; कौसल्यानन्दिवर्धनः Rām.<BR>—2 Curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिन्|आनंदिन्
आनन्दिन् <i>a.</i> [आ-नन्द्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Happy, joyful, delighted.<BR>—2 Pleasing, giving delight. रस ह्येवायं लब्ध्वाऽनन्दी भवति T. Up. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनपत्यम्
आनपत्यम् Childlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्
आनम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bend, bend down, bow, incline, stoop; अथ प्रयत्नोन्नमितानमत्फणैः Śi. 1. 13.<BR>—2 To salute (respectfully), bow down to; तमपि राजकमाननाम K. 59.<BR>—3 To humble. ━<i>Caus.</i> (-नमयति) To cause to bend down; कुचभारानमिता<BR> न योषितः Bh. 3. 27; विदर्भपतिमानमितं बलैश्च M. 5. 3 humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनत|आनतः
आनत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Respectfully saluted or bowed to.<BR>—2 (Actively used) Bent down, bending, stooping, inclined; कुसुमानताः<BR> (तरवः) Ki. 5. 25; Ṛs. 6. 3 (v. l.); पादानतः Ku. 3. 8; so<BR> प्रश्रय˚, फलभार˚.<BR>—3 Making a low bow, saluting respectfully; (प्रतिजग्राह) आदेशं<BR> देशकालज्ञः शिष्यः शासितुरानतः R. 1. 92, 4. 69.<BR>—4 Humble, obedient, submissive, pacified, conciliated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनतिः|आनति
आनतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bending, bowing, stooping (fig. also); गुणवन्मित्रमिवानतिं प्रपेदे<BR> Ki. 13. 15; चरणानतिव्यतिकरे Amaru. 49; किं वक्षश्चरणानतिव्यतिकरव्याजेन<BR> गोपाय्यते 26.<BR>—2 A bow or salutation, obeisance; आत्मजातिसदृशीं किलानतिम् Ki. 13. 36;<BR> Śi. 1. 11.<BR>—3 Homage, reverence,<BR>—4 Delight, satisfaction, pleasure; भृतिश्च कर्मकरेभ्य आनत्यर्थं<BR> यद्दीयते । ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 27.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आनतिकरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनतिकरः
आनतिः + -करः A present, a reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनमः|आनम
आनमः Bending, stretching (as a bow); cf. दुरानम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्र
आनम्र <i>a.</i> A little bent, bowing, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तः|आनर्त|आनर्त्त|आनर्त्तः
आनर्तः [आनृत्यत्यत्र आधारे घञ्]<BR>—1 A stage, theatre, a dancing-hall.<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR>—3 N. of a king of the solar race.<BR>—4 N. of a country or its inhabitants, or its king. (It was also called<BR> Saurāṣtra and may be identified with the modern Kathewar. Dwārakā<BR> was its capital, which is called Ānartanagarī. There was also an important<BR> town called Valabhī which afterwards became its capital. The celebrated<BR> Tīrtha called Prabhāsa also stood in the same peninsula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तम्
आनर्तः + .{@-र्तम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Dancing (<i>m.</i> also) cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">Page0334-2</a>]<BR> आनर्तः समरे नृत्तस्थाननीवृद्विशेषयोः Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आनर्तपुरम्, आनर्तनगरी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तपुरम्
आनर्तः + -पुरम्, -नगरी the capital of the Ānarta country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तनगरी
आनर्तः + -पुरम्, -नगरी the capital of the Ānarta country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तक|आनर्त्तक
आनर्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to Ānarta.<BR>—2 Dancing about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तीय|आनर्त्तीय
आनर्तीय <i>a.</i> [आनर्त-छ] Belonging to or coming from Ānarta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्थक्यम्
आनर्थक्यम् [अनर्थस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Uselessness, unprofitableness; श्रुत्यानर्थक्यमिति चेत् Kāty.; आम्नायस्य<BR> क्रियार्थत्वादानर्थक्यमतदर्थानाम् Jaimini S.<BR>—2 Unfitness, impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनव|आनवः
आनव <i>a.</i> [आनुः प्राणी तस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Human (as strength &c.).<BR>—2 Kind to men, benevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनवः|आनव
आनव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Men, people.<BR>—2 Foreign men or people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनस
आनस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनसः शकटस्य पितुर्वा इदम् अण्] Ved.<BR>—1 Belonging to a waggon or cart.<BR>—2 Belonging to a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनह्
आनह् €4 U.<BR>—1 To bind to, fasten; एषु नह्य वृषाजिनं हरिणस्या भियं कृधि Av. 6. 67. 3.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To be stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्ध|आनद्धं|आनद्धः
आनद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied, fastened.<BR>—2 Costive (as stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्धः|आनद्ध|आनद्धं
आनद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}<BR>—1 A drum in general.<BR>—2 Dressing, putting on clothes, ornaments &c., accoutring.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आनद्धवस्तिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्धवस्तिता
आनद्ध + -वस्तिता retention of urine or constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाहः|आनाह
आनाहः<BR>—1 Binding.<BR>—2 Suppression of urine, constipation, epistasis; ततो रुद्धे शकृन्मूत्रे<BR> सैन्यमानाहदुःखितम् Mb. 3. 122. 15.<BR>—3 Length (especially of cloth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाहिक
आनाहिक <i>a.</i> [आनाह-ठक्] To be used in cases of constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाथ्यम्
आनाथ्यम् [अनाथस्य भावः ष्यञ्] The state of being helpless or<BR> forlorn, orphanism, helplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिर्हत|आनिर्हतः
आनिर्हत <i>a.</i> Ved. Of indestructible nature; wholly gone out of<BR> the world (Mahīdhara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिर्हतः|आनिर्हत
आनिर्हत + .{@-तः@} A class of principal deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिल|आनिलः
आनिल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनिलस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Proceeding from or produced by wind, windy.<BR>—2 Presided over by or sacred to Vāyu (as an oblation &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिलः|आनिल
आनिल + .{@-लः, -आनिलिः@} N. of Hanūmat or Bhīma. —3 N. of the lunar asterism स्वाती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिलिः|आनिलि
आनिल + .{@-लः, -आनिलिः@} N. of Hanūmat or Bhīma. —3 N. of the lunar asterism स्वाती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनी
आनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring, fetch; भुवनं मत्पार्श्वमानीयते Ś. 7. 8; तेषामुदकमानीय Ms. 3. 210.<BR>—2 To bring on, produce, cause; आनिनाय भुवः कम्पम् R. 15. 24.<BR>—3 To lead towards or near, convey.<BR>—4 To mix in.<BR>—5 To reduce or lead to any condition; वशम् आनी to reduce to subjection.<BR>—6 To lead off, divert. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to bring (with instr.<BR> of person who brings); मौलैरानाययामासुर्भरतं स्तम्भिताश्रुभिः R. 12. 12, 15. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयः|आनय
आनयः, आनयनम्<BR>—1 Bringing.<BR>—2 Investiture with the sacred thread (cf. उपनय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयनम्
आनयः, आनयनम्<BR>—1 Bringing.<BR>—2 Investiture with the sacred thread (cf. उपनय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनायः|आनाय
आनायः [आनीयते मत्स्योऽनेन नी-करणे-घञ्] A net; जालमानायः<BR> P. III. 3. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनायिन्
आनायिन् <i>m.</i> [आनाय-इनि] A fisherman, fisher; आनायिभिस्तामपकृष्टनकाम्<BR> R. 16. 55, 75. cf. जालमानायवृन्दयोः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्य|आनाय्यः
आनाय्य <i>a.</i> To be brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्यः|आनाय्य
आनाय्य + .{@-य्यः@} [आनी-ण्यत् आयादेशः P. III. 1. 127] Consecrated fire<BR> taken from गार्हपत्य or household fire and placed on the south side<BR> (also called दक्षिणाग्नि); दक्षिणाग्निविशेष एवेदं स हि गार्हपत्यादानीयते<BR> अनित्यश्च सततमप्रज्वलनात् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीत
आनीत <i>a.</i> Brought; आनीता भवता यदा पतिरता साध्वी धरित्रीसुता ।<BR> हनुमन्नाटकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीतिः|आनीति
आनीतिः <i>f.</i> [आ-नी-क्तिन्] Leading near; चङ्कमित्वा प्रियानीतिं<BR> रामो रक्षोवधे स्थितः । Mugdha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतव्य
आनेतव्य <i>a.</i> To be brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेय
आनेय <i>a.</i> To be fetched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतृ
आनेतृ <i>a.</i> Bringer, bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनील|आनीलः
आनील <i>a.</i> Darkish, slightly blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीलः|आनील
आनील + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A black horse.<BR>—2 Tin. (Nigh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकल्पिक
आनुकल्पिक <i>a.</i> [अनुकल्पं वेत्ति अधीते वा उक्था˚ ठक्]<BR>—1 One who knows or studies the <i>anukalpa</i> q. v.<BR>—2 To be obtained by अनुकल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूलिक
आनुकूलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुकूल ठक्] Favourable, conformable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूल्यम्
आनुकूल्यम् [अनुकूलस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Favourableness, conformity, suitableness; यत्रानुकूल्यं दम्पत्योस्त्रिवर्गस्तत्र<BR> वर्धते Y. 1. 74.<BR>—2 Kindness, favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगत्यम्
आनुगत्यम् [अनुगत-ष्यञ्] Acquaintance, familiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगतिक
आनुगतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Relating to a follower, following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगुण्यम्
आनुगुण्यम् [अनुगुणस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] Favourableness, suitableness, congruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुग्रामिक
आनुग्रामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [अनुग्रामं भवः ठञ्] Rural, rustic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुजावर
आनुजावर^1 <i>a.</i> Ved. Posthumous.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Change to jAvara based on other dictionaries..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुजीव्यम्
आनुजीव्यम् The decorum due to a servant; पशुपकुलनिवासाद् आनुजीव्यानभिज्ञः<BR> Dūtavākyam 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुनासिक्यम्
आनुनासिक्यम् [अनुनासिकस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Nasality; आनुनासिक्यं<BR> तेषामधिको गुणः Mbh. on P. I. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपथ्य
आनुपथ्य <i>a.</i> Along the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपदिक
आनुपदिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुपदं धावति ठक् P. IV. 4. 37, IV. 2. 59.<BR> वेद अधीते वा] Following, pursuing, tracking, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्वम्
आनुपूर्वम्, -र्व्यम्, -र्वी<BR> [अनुपूर्वस्य भावः ष्यञ् ततो वा ङीषि यलोपः]<BR>—1 Order, succession, series; देव्या चाख्यातं सर्वमेवानुपूर्व्याद्वाचा<BR> संपूर्णं वायुपुत्रः शशंस Rām. 5. 65. 28 वसीरन्नानुपूर्व्येण शाणक्षौमाविकानि<BR> च Ms. 2. 41.<BR>—2 (In law) The regular order of the castes; षडानुपूर्व्या विप्रस्य क्षत्रस्य<BR> चतुरोऽवरान् Ms. 3. 23.<BR>—3 (In logic) Conclusion regularly or syllogistically drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्यम्
आनुपूर्वम्, -र्व्यम्, -र्वी<BR> [अनुपूर्वस्य भावः ष्यञ् ततो वा ङीषि यलोपः]<BR>—1 Order, succession, series; देव्या चाख्यातं सर्वमेवानुपूर्व्याद्वाचा<BR> संपूर्णं वायुपुत्रः शशंस Rām. 5. 65. 28 वसीरन्नानुपूर्व्येण शाणक्षौमाविकानि<BR> च Ms. 2. 41.<BR>—2 (In law) The regular order of the castes; षडानुपूर्व्या विप्रस्य क्षत्रस्य<BR> चतुरोऽवरान् Ms. 3. 23.<BR>—3 (In logic) Conclusion regularly or syllogistically drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्वी|आनुपूर्व्वी
आनुपूर्वम्, -र्व्यम्, -र्वी<BR> [अनुपूर्वस्य भावः ष्यञ् ततो वा ङीषि यलोपः]<BR>—1 Order, succession, series; देव्या चाख्यातं सर्वमेवानुपूर्व्याद्वाचा<BR> संपूर्णं वायुपुत्रः शशंस Rām. 5. 65. 28 वसीरन्नानुपूर्व्येण शाणक्षौमाविकानि<BR> च Ms. 2. 41.<BR>—2 (In law) The regular order of the castes; षडानुपूर्व्या विप्रस्य क्षत्रस्य<BR> चतुरोऽवरान् Ms. 3. 23.<BR>—3 (In logic) Conclusion regularly or syllogistically drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्यवत्
आनुपूर्वम्, -र्व्यम्, -र्वी + .{@-वत्@} Having a (definite) order; आनुपूर्व्यवतामेकदेशग्रहणेषु<BR> आगमवदन्त्यलोपः स्यात् । Ms. 10. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्वे
आनुपूर्वे, -र्व्ये, -ण, अनुपूर्व्या <i>ind.</i><BR> One after another, in due order;<BR> आनुपूर्व्येणोत्थितराजलोकः K. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्ये
आनुपूर्वे, -र्व्ये, -ण, अनुपूर्व्या <i>ind.</i><BR> One after another, in due order;<BR> आनुपूर्व्येणोत्थितराजलोकः K. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्येण
आनुपूर्वे, -र्व्ये, -ण, अनुपूर्व्या <i>ind.</i><BR> One after another, in due order;<BR> आनुपूर्व्येणोत्थितराजलोकः K. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्या
आनुपूर्वे, -र्व्ये, -ण, अनुपूर्व्या <i>ind.</i><BR> One after another, in due order;<BR> आनुपूर्व्येणोत्थितराजलोकः K. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमानिक|आनुमानिकः
आनुमानिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुमानादागतः ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to a conclusion.<BR>—2 Derived from an inference, subject to inference, inferential.<BR>—3 Inferred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमानिकम्
आनुमानिक + .{@-कम्@} The Pradhāna of the SāNkhyas; आनुमानिकमप्येकेषामिति<BR> चेन्न Br. Sūt. 1. 4. 1; ˚त्वम् the state of being inferable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुयात्रम्
आनुयात्रम् Retinue, attendants; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुयात्रिकः|आनुयात्रिक
आनुयात्रिकः A follower, attendant; Māl. 6; U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुरक्तिः|आनुरक्ति
आनुरक्तिः <i>f.</i> Passion, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुरूप्यम्
आनुरूप्यम् Suitableness, conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलेपिक
आनुलेपिक <i>a.</i> [अनुलेपिकायाः स्त्रिया धर्म्यम्] Forming the duty<BR> of an अनुलेपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोमिक
आनुलोमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुलोमं वर्तते अनुलोम ठक्]<BR>—1 Regular, orderly, in due course.<BR>—2 Favourable, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्य
आनुलोम्य <i>a.</i> ‘In the direction of the hair’, produced in natural<BR> or direct order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्यम्
आनुलोम्य + .{@-म्यम्@} [अनुलोमस्य भावः कर्म वा ब्राह्म ˚ष्यञ् P.]<BR>—1 Natural or direct order, proper arragement; आनुलोम्येन संभूता जात्या<BR> ज्ञेयास्त एव ते Ms. 10. 5, 13.<BR>—2 Regular series or succession.<BR>—3 Favourableness, fit disposition.<BR>—4 Bringing to oneʼs right place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुवंश्य
आनुवंश्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to a race, conformable to genealogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुविधित्सा
आनुविधित्सा Ingratitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुवेश्यः|आनुवेश्य
आनुवेश्यः [अनुवेशं वसति] A neighbour who lives next to the<BR> next-door neighbour; प्रातिवेश्यानुवेश्यौ च कल्याणे विंशतिद्विजे Ms. 8. 392;<BR> (on which Kull. says; निरन्तरगृहवासी प्रातिवेश्यः, तदनन्तरगृहवास्यानुवेश्यः).<BR> The word is also found to be written as अनुवेश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुशासनिक
आनुशासनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुशासनाय हितं ठक्] Relating to or treating<BR> of instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुशूक
आनुशूक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Being with or within the awns (as rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुश्रव
आनुश्रव <i>a.</i> See next word; आनुश्रवं श्रुतिभिरङ्घ्रिजमङ्गसङ्गैः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुश्रविक|आनुश्रविकः
आनुश्र(श्रा)विक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [गुरुपाठादनुश्रूयते; अनुश्रवो वेदस्तत्र विहितः<BR> ठक्] According to hearing, resting on Veda or tradition; देवानां गुणलिङ्गानामानुश्रविककर्मणाम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 25. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुश्राविक
आनुश्र(श्रा)विक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [गुरुपाठादनुश्रूयते; अनुश्रवो वेदस्तत्र विहितः<BR> ठक्] According to hearing, resting on Veda or tradition; देवानां गुणलिङ्गानामानुश्रविककर्मणाम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 25. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुश्रविकः|आनुश्रविक
आनुश्र(श्रा)विक + .{@-कः@} Means of obtaining Heaven, absolution &c. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषक्
आनुषक् <i>ind.</i> Ved. In continuous order, uninterruptedly, one after<BR> the other. वि हव्यमग्निरानुषग्भगो न वारमृण्वति Rv. 5. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषङ्गिक|आनुषंगिक
आनुषङ्गिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुषङ्गात् आगतः ठक् स्त्रियां डीप्]<BR>—1 Connected with, concomitant.<BR>—2 Implied, inherent.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">Page0336-1</a>]<BR>—3 Necessarily following, inevitable, necessary.<BR>—4 Of secondary importance, secondary; असुभिः स्थास्नु यशश्चिचीषतः …<BR> ननु लक्ष्मीः फलमानुषङ्गिकम् Ki. 2. 19; अन्यतरस्यानुषङ्गिकत्वेऽन्वाचयः<BR> Sk.; see अन्वाचय.<BR>—5 Attached to, fond of, frequenting; तत्र˚ Pt. 1.<BR>—6 Like, analogous.<BR>—7 Relative, proportionate.<BR>—8 (In gram.) Elliptical, including words not included in the sentence.<BR>—9 Incidental; यस्यैव प्रधानकर्मफलं तस्यैवानुषङ्गिकमपि भवितुमर्हति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 10.<BR>—10 Lasting, enduring; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषज्
आनुषज् <i>ind.</i> In order, successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषूक
आनुषूक <i>a.</i> (In the manner of the aftershoot of rice) Promoting,<BR> urging, driving forward; तस्मा एतमैन्द्रमानुषूकम् Yaj. Ts. 2. 3. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुष्टुभ
आनुष्टुभ <i>a.</i> (-भी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुष्टुप् छन्दोऽस्य उत्सा˚ अञ्]<BR>—1 Consisting of Anuṣṭubhs.<BR>—2 Relating to Anuṣṭubh, formed like the metre; आनुष्टुभस्य हविषो<BR> हविर्यत् Rv. 10. 181. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुष्टुभम्
आनुष्टुभ + .{@-भम्@} The Anuṣṭup metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुसूय
आनुसूय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनुसूयया अत्रिपत्न्या दत्तम् अण्] Coming from<BR> or given by Anusūyā; स्फुरत्प्रभामण्डलमानुसूर्यं सा बिभ्रती शाश्वतमङ्गरागम् R. 14. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूकम्
आनूकम्^1 Ved. Ornament, jewels; आनूकमर्यो वपुषे नार्चत् Rv. 5. 33. 9.<BR> <i>ind.</i> In abundance, greatly.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Print blurred. Cf AP90  MW etc. and quotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूप|आनूपः
आनूप <i>a.</i> (-पी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनूपदेशे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Watery, marshy, wet.<BR>—2 Produced in a marshy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूपः|आनूप
आनूप + .{@-पः@} Any animal frequenting marshy or watery places (as a buffalo);<BR> ˚मांसम् the flesh of such animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूपक
आनूपक <i>a.</i> Living in marshy places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्यम्
आनृण्यम्, -आनृण्यता<BR> [अनृणस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] Acquittance of debt<BR> or obligation; पितुरानृण्यतां प्राप्ते स्वपिष्ये परमं सुखम् Rām. 2. 24. 35.<BR> see अनृणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्यता
आनृण्यम्, -आनृण्यता<BR> [अनृणस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] Acquittance of debt<BR> or obligation; पितुरानृण्यतां प्राप्ते स्वपिष्ये परमं सुखम् Rām. 2. 24. 35.<BR> see अनृणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृत्
आनृत् €4 P. To dance towards, hasten near, jump near; आनृत्यतः शिखण्डिनो Av. 4. 37. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृत
आनृत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अनृतं शीलमस्य अण्] Always telling lies, untruthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस
आनृशंस, -स्य <i>a.</i><BR> Mild, kind; merciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस्य|आनृशंस्यं
आनृशंस, -स्य <i>a.</i><BR> Mild, kind; merciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंसम्
आनृशंस, -स्य + .{@-सम्, -स्यम्@}<BR>—1 Mildness.<BR>—2 Kindness; आनृशंस्याद् ब्राह्मणस्य Ms. 1. 101; बिभृयादानृशंस्येन<BR> स्वानि कर्माणि कारयन् 8. 411.<BR>—3 Compassion, pity, mercy.<BR>—4 Patronising, Protective nature; स्त्री प्रणष्टेति कारुण्यादाश्रितेत्यानृशंस्यतः<BR> Rām. 5. 15. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस्यम्
आनृशंस, -स्य + .{@-सम्, -स्यम्@}<BR>—1 Mildness.<BR>—2 Kindness; आनृशंस्याद् ब्राह्मणस्य Ms. 1. 101; बिभृयादानृशंस्येन<BR> स्वानि कर्माणि कारयन् 8. 411.<BR>—3 Compassion, pity, mercy.<BR>—4 Patronising, Protective nature; स्त्री प्रणष्टेति कारुण्यादाश्रितेत्यानृशंस्यतः<BR> Rām. 5. 15. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैपुणम्
आनैपुणम्, -ण्यम्<BR> [अनिपुणस्य भावः अण्, ष्यञ् वा] Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैपुण्यम्
आनैपुणम्, -ण्यम्<BR> [अनिपुणस्य भावः अण्, ष्यञ् वा] Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैश्वर्यम्
आनैश्वर्यम् [अनीश्वरस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Absence of power or supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त <i>a.</i> (-न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्त-अण्] Final, terminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तम्
आन्त + .{@-न्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Completely, to the end; Mbh. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्यः|आन्त्य|आंत्यः
आन्त्यः Ved. One who finishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तःपुरिक
आन्तःपुरिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to womenʼs apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तःपुरिकम्
आन्तःपुरिक + .{@-कम्@} Anything done in womenʼs apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर|आंतर
आन्तर <i>a.</i> [अन्तर् मध्ये भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Internal, secret, hidden; व्यतिषजति पदार्थानान्तरः कोऽपि हेतुः<BR> U. 6. 12; Māl. 1. 24.<BR>—2 Inmost, inward; U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरम्
आन्तर + .{@-रम्@} Inmost nature; न बाह्यं किंचन वेद नान्तरम् Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आन्तरज्ञ, आन्तरप्रपञ्चः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरज्ञ
आन्तर + -ज्ञ Knowing the hidden secret (of things &c.); विवृण्वतेव कल्याणमान्तरज्ञेन<BR> चक्षुषा Māl. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरप्रपञ्चः|आन्तरप्रपञ्च
आन्तर + -प्रपञ्चः (In phil.) The fantasies of the soul produced by ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरतम्यम्
आन्तरतम्यम्, आन्तर्यम् Nearest or closest relationship (as<BR> of letters); तथाप्यान्तरतम्यपरीक्षायामुपयोक्ष्यन्ते । Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्यम्
आन्तरतम्यम्, आन्तर्यम् Nearest or closest relationship (as<BR> of letters); तथाप्यान्तरतम्यपरीक्षायामुपयोक्ष्यन्ते । Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरागारिक|आन्तरागारिकः
आन्तरागारिक <i>a.</i> belonging to the duties of a storekeeper or chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरागारिकः|आन्तरागारिक
आन्तरागारिक + .{@-कः@} The chamberlain<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरागारिकम्
आन्तरागारिक + .{@-कम्@} The office of the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तराल
आन्तराल <i>a.</i> [अन्तरालं वेत्ति अण्] ‘One conversant with the inner nature’, N. of a philosophical sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरिक्ष|आंतरिक्ष
आन्तरि(री)क्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्तरिक्षे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Atmospherical, heavenly, celestial; आन्तरीक्षाः पुनरमी सर्वतः सदृशा इव Mv. 7. 22.<BR>—2 Produced in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरीक्ष|आंतरीक्ष|आन्तरीक्षं
आन्तरि(री)क्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्तरिक्षे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Atmospherical, heavenly, celestial; आन्तरीक्षाः पुनरमी सर्वतः सदृशा इव Mv. 7. 22.<BR>—2 Produced in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरिक्षम्
आन्तरि(री)क्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} The firmament, the intermediate region between the earth and sky.<BR>—2 Rain-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गणिक|आंतर्गणिक
आन्तर्गणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्तर्गणं भवः ठञ्] Included, comprised (as<BR> in a class, troop &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गेहिक|आंतर्गेहिक
आन्तर्गेहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्तर्गेहं वेश्मनि भवः ठञ्] Being or produced<BR> inside a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्वेदिक
आन्तर्वेदिक <i>a.</i> Being within the place of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तिका|आंतिका
आन्तिका [अन्तिकेव अण् टाप्] An elder sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्र|आंत्र
आन्त्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्त्र-अण्] Relating to the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्रम्
आन्त्र + .{@-त्रम्@} Ved. Bowels, ontrails; केचिदान्त्रैर्विनिःसृताः Rām. 6. 52. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्रिक|आंत्रिक|आन्त्रिकः
आन्त्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Visceral, being within or relating to the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल्
आन्दोल् Den. P. [-दोलयति-दोलित]<BR>—1 To swing, rock or move to and fro.<BR>—2 To shake, tremble (fig. also); Māl. 4; मन्दमारुतान्दोलिता लतेव Dk. 17, 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलः|आन्दोल|आंदोलः
आन्दोलः<BR>—1 Swinging, a swing.<BR>—2 Trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलनम्
आन्दोलनम् [आन्दोल् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Swinging, a swing.<BR>—2 Moving to and fro, shaking, rocking; किंत्वासामरविन्दसुन्दरदृशां<BR> द्राक् चामरान्दोलनात् Udb.<BR>—3 Trembling, oscillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धसः|आन्धस|आंधसः
आन्धसः The scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धसिकः|आन्धसिक|आंधसिकः
आन्धसिकः [अन्धो भक्तं शिल्पमस्य ठक्] A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्यम्
आन्ध्यम् [अन्धस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Blindness; तेनेदमान्ध्यं किल नान्धकारैः N. 22. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्र|आंध्र|आन्ध्रः
आन्ध्र <i>a.</i> Belonging to Āndhra (as language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्रः|आन्ध्र|आंध्र
आन्ध्र + .{@-ध्रः@} (pl.) The Telagu country, modern Telangana; see अन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्री
आन्ध्र + .{@-न्ध्री@} An Āndhra wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्न
आन्न <i>a.</i> (-न्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्नं लब्धा अन्न-ण P. IV. 4. 85]<BR>—1 Fed, having food.<BR>—2 Relating to, derived from food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्यतरेय|आन्यतरेयः
आन्यतरेय <i>a.</i> Belonging to the school of another teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्यतरेयः|आन्यतरेय
आन्यतरेय + .{@-यः@} N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्यभाव्यम्
आन्यभाव्यम् Another form. Mbh. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वयिक|आन्वयिकः
आन्वयिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्वये प्रशस्तकुले भवः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Of a good family, well-born, of noble birth.<BR>—2 Orderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वाहिक
आन्वाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्वह-ठञ्] Daily occurring or to be performed<BR> every day; पक्तिं चान्वाहिकीम् Ms. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वीक्षिकी
आन्वीक्षिकी [अन्वीक्षा प्रयोजनमस्याः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Logic, logical philosophy.<BR>—2 Metaphysics (आत्मविद्या q. v.); आन्वीक्षिक्यात्मविद्या स्यादीक्षणात्सुखदुःखयोः ।<BR> ईक्षमाणस्तया तत्त्वं हर्षशोकौ व्युदस्यति ॥ Kām. 2. 11; आन्वीक्षिकीश्रवणाय<BR> Māl. 1; Ms. 7. 43; (न्याय आन्वीक्षिकी पञ्चाध्यायी गौतमेन प्रणीता Madhusūdana).<BR>—3 Philosophy of Sāṅkhya, Yoga and Lokāyata; साङ्ख्यं योगो लोकायतं<BR> चेत्यान्वीक्षिकी Kau. A. 1. 2. cf. also आन्वीक्षिकी त्रयी वार्ता दण्डनीतिश्चेति<BR> विद्याः Kau. A. 1. 2. आश्रयः सर्वधर्माणां शश्वदान्वीक्षिकी मता<BR> Kau. A. 1. 2; Bhāg. 7. 12. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वीपिक
आन्वीपिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अन्वीपं वर्तते ठक्] Favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्
आप् €5 P., rarely €1 P. (आप्नोति or आपति, आप, आपत्, आप्स्यति, आप्तुम्, आप्त)<BR>—1 To obtain, attain, get; स शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी Bg. 2. 70, 3. 2, 3. 19.<BR> पुत्रमेवंगुणोपेतं चकवर्तिनमाप्नुहि Ś. 1. 12; अनुद्योगेन<BR> तैलानि तिलेभ्यो नाप्तुमर्हति H. Pr. 25; शतं कतूनामपविध्नमाप सः<BR> R. 3. 38; so फलम्, कीर्तिम्, सुखम् &c.<BR>—2 To reach, go to; overtake, meet, fall in with; शबरीमापतुर्वने Bk. 6. 59.<BR>—3 To pervade, occupy, enter into.<BR>—4 To undergo, suffer, meet with; दिष्टान्तमाप्स्यति भवान् R. 9. 79; Ms. 8. 188.<BR>—5 To equal. ━<i>pass.</i> (आप्यते)<BR>—1 To be reached, found, met with, obtained &c.<BR>—2 To arrive at oneʼs end or aim.<BR>—3 To become filled. ━<i>Caus.</i> (आपयति)<BR>—1 To cause to reach or obtain.<BR>—2 To cause any one to feel or perceive.<BR>—3 To hit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपः|आप
आपः [आप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 N. of one of the 8 demigods called Vasus. —2 (At the end of comp.) दुराप<BR> difficult to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपम्
आपः + .{@-पम्@} [अपां समूहः] A flood or stream of water, water.<BR>—2 Sky (Nir.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक
आपक <i>a.</i> [आप्-ण्वुल्] Getting, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनम्
आपनम् [आप्-ल्युट]<BR>—1 Getting, obtaining, reaching &c.<BR>—2 Pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपयितृ
आपयितृ <i>a.</i> [आप्-णिच्-तृच्] One who gets or procures, procuring;<BR> आपयिता ह वै कामानां भवति Ch. Up. 1. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिः|आपि
आपिः [आप्-णिच्-इन्]<BR>—1 Obtaining wealth &c.<BR>—2 A friend, acquaintance, ally (बन्धु); ˚त्वम् friendship, alliance;<BR> आपित्वे नः प्रपित्वे तूयमा गहि Rv. 8. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त <i>p. p.</i> [आप्-क्त]<BR>—1 Got, obtained, gained; ˚कामः, ˚शापः &c.<BR>—2 Reached, overtaken, equalled, engrossed; यदिदं सर्वं मृत्युनाप्तं<BR> सर्वं मृत्युनाभिपन्नं केन यजमानो मृत्योराप्तिमतिमुच्यते Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 3.<BR>—3 Reaching to, extending as far as.<BR>—4 Trustworthy, reliable, credible (as news &c.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">Page0337-2</a>]<BR>—5 Trusty, confidential, faithful (person); कुमारभृत्याकुशलैरनुष्टिते<BR> भिषग्भिराप्तैः R. 3. 12, 5. 39; आप्ताः सर्वेषु वर्णेषु Ms. 8. 63.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Clever, skilful; प्राजकश्चेद्भवेदाप्तः Ms. 8. 294.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Apt, fit.<BR>—7 Full, complete, abundant; न सत्यं दानमानौ वा यज्ञो वाप्याप्तदक्षिणः<BR> Rām. 2. 30. 35. यजेत राजा कतुभिर्विविधैराप्तदक्षिणैः Ms. 7. 79.<BR>—8 True, exact.<BR>—9 Intimate, closely related, acquainted; कन्यायाः किल पूजयन्ति पितरो<BR> जामातुराप्तं जनम् U. 4. 17 relatives; Ms. 5. 101.<BR>—10 Appointed.<BR>—11 Generally received, commonly used; authentic.<BR>—12 Accused, prosecuted.<BR>—13 Reasonable, sensible.<BR>—14 Beneficial, useful; अधिष्टितं हयज्ञेन सूतेनाप्तोपदेशिना Rām. 6. 90. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तः|आप्त
आप्त + .{@-प्तः@}<BR>—1 A trustworthy, reliable, or fit person; credible person or source,<BR> guarantee; आप्तः यथार्थवक्ता T. S.<BR>—2 A relative, friend; निग्रहात्स्वसुराप्तानां वधाच्च धनदानुजः R. 12. 52;<BR> कथमाप्तवर्गोऽयं भवत्याः M. 5; Y. 1. 28, 2. 71; Ms. 2. 109, 8. 64.<BR>—3 An Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ता
आप्त + .{@-प्ता@} A twisted lock of hair (जटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तम्
आप्त + .{@-प्तम्@}<BR>—1 A quotient.<BR>—2 (In Math.) Equation of a degree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आप्तागमः, आप्ताधीन, आप्तोक्तिः, आप्तकाम, आप्तकारिन्, आप्तगर्भा, आप्तदक्षिण, आप्तवचनम्, आप्तवाक्यम्, आप्तवचनम्, आप्तवाच्, आप्तश्रुतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तागमः|आप्तागम
आप्त + -आगमः Proper knowledge परोक्षमाप्तागमात् सिद्धम् Sāṅ. K. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ताधीन
आप्त + -आधीन <i>a.</i> Dependent on trustworthy person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तोक्तिः|आप्तोक्ति
आप्त + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 an augment.<BR>—2 an affix. —3 a word of received acceptation and established by usage<BR> only; see आप्तवाच् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकाम|आप्तकामः
आप्त + -काम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has obtained his desire; येनाक्रमन्त्यृषयो ह्याप्रकामाः Muṇḍ. 3. 1. 6.<BR>—2 one who has renounced all worldly desires and attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकामः|आप्तकाम
आप्त + -काम + .({@-मः@}) the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकारिन्
आप्त + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> doing things in a fit or confidential manner; अरक्षिता<BR> गृहे रुद्धाः पुरुषैराप्तकारिभिः Ms. 9. 12. ━<i>m.</i> a trusty agent or<BR> confidential servant; तस्माद्गच्छन्तु पुरुषाः स्मारणायाप्तकारिणः Mb. 3. 239. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्भा
आप्त + -गर्भा a pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तदक्षिण
आप्त + -दक्षिण <i>a.</i> having proper or abundant gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवचनम्
आप्त + -वचनम्<BR>—1 received text or authority, revelation.<BR>—2 the words of a credible or trustworthy person; R. 11. 42, इत्याप्तवचनाद्रामो<BR> विनेष्यन्वर्णविक्रियाम् 15. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवाक्यम्
आप्त + -वाक्यम् a true or correct sentence; आप्तवाक्यं शब्दः T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवचनम्
आप्त + -वचनम् above. cf. आप्तश्रुतिराप्तवचनम् तु Sāṅ. K. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवाच्
आप्त + -वाच् <i>a.</i> worthy of belief, regarded as authority, one whose<BR> words are credible and authoritative; परातिसंधानमधीयते यैर्विद्येति<BR> ते सन्तु किलाप्तवाचः Ś. 5. 25. <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the advice of a friend or credible person.<BR>—2 the Vedas or Śruti; a word of authority (said to apply to Smṛtis,<BR> Itihāsas and Purāṇas also, which are considered as authoritative evidence);<BR> आप्तवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं त्वां प्रति का कथा R. 10. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तश्रुतिः|आप्तश्रुति
आप्त + -श्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the Vedas.<BR>—2 Smṛtis &c. आप्तश्रुतिराप्तवचनम् तु । Sāṅ. K. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तिः|आप्ति
आप्तिः <i>f.</i> [आप्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Getting obtaining, gain, acquisition; ध्यायन्ति वेदहृदया मुनयस्तदाप्त्यै<BR> Bhāg. 12. 8. 42. मित्र˚, काम˚ &c.<BR>—2 Reaching, overtaking, meeting with; केन यजमानो मृत्योराप्तिमतिमुच्यते<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 3.<BR>—3 Binding, connection, relation.<BR>—4 Union; especially with a woman (Med.).<BR>—5 Fitness, aptitude, propriety.<BR>—6 Completion, fulfilment; कामस्याप्तिं जगतः प्रतिष्ठाम् Kaṭh. 1. 2. 11.<BR>—7 Future time. ━pl. N. of 12 sacrificial verses beginning with Āpaye. Vāj. 9. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य <i>a.</i> [अपाम् इदम् अण् स्वार्थे ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Watery. —2 Obtainable, attainable (आप्-ण्यत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यः|आप्य|आप्यं
आप्य + .{@-प्यः@} A class of gods. इन्द्रो मन्त्रद्रुमस्तत्र देव आप्यादयो गणाः<BR>—2 A kind of horse, born in water; अक्रोधवेगाः सस्वप्ना आप्यास्ते तुरगाधमाः ।<BR> शालिहोत्र of भोज ed. by Kulkarni, Appendix II, 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यम्
आप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 Confederation, alliance; किं सनेन वसव आप्येन Rv. 2. 29. 3.<BR>—2 A friend; यो नो नेदिष्ठमाप्यम् Rv. 7. 15. 1,<BR>—3 Water; पृथ्व्याप्यतेजोनिलखानि Śvet. Up. 2. 12, 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपकर
आपकर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अपकरे भवः अण् अञ् च] Offensive, unfriendly, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्व|आपक्वं
आपक्व <i>a.</i> Crude, raw, half-baked<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्वम्
आपक्व + .{@-क्वम्@} A cake, bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा [अपां समूहः आपम्; तेन गच्छति गम्-ड] A river, stream;<BR> फेनायमानं पतिमापगानाम् Śi. 3. 72; Ki. 13. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगेयः|आपगेय
आपगेयः [आपगायां गङ्गायां भवः ढक्] A son of the river, an<BR> epithet of Bhīṣma or Kṛṣṇa; यदाश्रौषं चापगेयेन संख्ये Mb. 1. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणः|आपण
आपणः [आपण्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A market; shop. विपणापणवान् रम्यः Mb. 14. 59. 11; भक्ष्यमाल्यापणानां<BR> च ददृशुः श्रियमुत्तमाम् Mb.<BR>—2 Trade, commercial commodity; पिहितापणोदया Rām. 2. 48. 37.<BR>—3 A group of shopkeepers; शकटापणवेशाश्च यानं युग्यं च सर्वशः<BR> Mb. 5. 196. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपणवीथिका, आपणवेदिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणवीथिका
आपणः + -वीथिका A row of stalls, market; Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणवेदिका
आपणः + -वेदिका A shop-counter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणक|आपणकः
आपणक, आपणिक <i>a.</i> [आपणादागतः ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to traffic, market &c.; mercantile; सम्मार्जितमहामार्गरथ्यापणकचत्वराम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 11. 14.<BR>—2 Got from the market (as duties.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणिक|आपणिकः
आपणक, आपणिक <i>a.</i> [आपणादागतः ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to traffic, market &c.; mercantile; सम्मार्जितमहामार्गरथ्यापणकचत्वराम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 11. 14.<BR>—2 Got from the market (as duties.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणकः|आपणक
आपणक, आपणिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A shop-keeper, merchant, dealer.<BR>—2 A tax on market shops.<BR>—3 Assize, market-rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्
आपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fall upon, attack, assail; उदायुधानापततः R. 12. 44, 5. 50; Bk. 3. 48.<BR>—2 To approach, come towards K. 202; एतत् प्रायेण श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव<BR> K. 136 has reached the ears; 268.<BR>—3 To fly towards, come in flying, come or drive in haste, rush upon;<BR> अपि नाध्वश्रमः शीघ्रं रथेनापततस्तव Rām. 2. 72. 5<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To happen, take place, occur, come to pass; कथमिदमापतितम्<BR> U. 2; K. 262, 158; अहो न शोभनमापतितम् Pt. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To fall to oneʼs lot or share, befall; अहोऽस्माकं महद्भोजनमापतितम्<BR> Pt. 1; आपतन्ति हि संसारपथमवतणिनामेते वृत्तान्ताः K. 175, 132;<BR> सर्वस्यैव स्खलितमापतति 291; H. 1. 28, 168.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To occur to, cross (the mind); इति हृदये नापतितम् K. 288<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To be felt or regarded; मधुरतराण्यापतन्ति मनसः K. 103<BR> are felt or regarded; 202, 236, 329. ━<i>Caus.</i> (पातयति) To<BR> go towards, approach (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतनम्
आपतनम्<BR>—1 Approaching, coming, assailing &c.<BR>—2 Happening, occurrence.<BR>—3 Descending, alighting.<BR>—4 Obtaining.<BR>—5 Knowledge; क्वचित् प्राकरणिकादर्थादप्राकरणिकस्यार्थस्यापतनम् S. D. 10.<BR>—6 Natural sequence, necessarily following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपति|आपतिः
आपति <i>a.</i> Ved. Coming in haste, rushing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिः|आपति
आपति + .{@-तिः@} The wind (always blowing) (सततगतिर्वायुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिक|आपतिकः
आपतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Accidental, unforeseen, sent from heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिकः|आपतिक
आपतिक + .{@-कः@} A hawk, falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतित
आपतित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fallen to the lot of.<BR>—2 Happened, befallen, occurred, come to pass.<BR>—3 Alighted, descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात <i>a.</i> Rushing upon, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातः|आपात
आपात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Rushing or falling upon, attack, descending, alighting; तदापातभयात्पथि<BR> Ku. 2. 45; गरुडापातविश्लिष्टमेघनादास्त्रबन्धनः R. 12. 76.<BR>—2 Throwing down.<BR>—3 Causing to descend or fall, falling down; धारापातैः Me. 50.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The present or current moment, the instant; आपातरम्या विषयाः<BR> पर्यन्तपरितापिनः Ki. 11. 12; आपातसुरसे भोगे निमग्नाः किं न<BR> कुर्वत S. D.; आपातरमणीयानां संयोगानां प्रियैः सह । अपथ्यानामिवान्नानां<BR> परिणामोऽतिदारुणः ॥ H. 4. 75; Bv. 1. 115; Māl. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) (Hence) First sight or appearance; see आपाततः.<BR>—5 Happening, becoming apparent, appearance.<BR>—6 Assault, a method of catching elephants (Mātaṅga L. 10. 1. 13).<BR>—7 Hell (नरक) आपातान्प्रतितिष्ठन्ति पुलिन्दशबरा इव Mb. 12. 151. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपातदुःसह, आपातदुष्प्रसह, आपातमात्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातदुःसह
आपात + -दुःसह <i>a.</i> unbearable at the first attack; U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातदुष्प्रसह
आपात + -दुष्प्रसह <i>a.</i> unbearable in its onset, making a furious charge;<BR> आपातदुष्प्रसहमाविरभूदनीकम् M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातमात्र
आपात + -मात्र <i>a.</i> Being only momentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाततः
आपाततः <i>ind.</i> At the first sight or attack, instantly, immediately; S. D. 632.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातिन्
आपातिन् <i>a.</i> Falling on, attacking, descending, happening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात्य
आपात्य <i>a.</i> Rushing on, approaching to attack; आपात्यसैनिकनिराकरणाकुलेन Śi. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्य
आपत्य <i>a.</i> (-त्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अपत्य-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to offspring.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Relating to the formation of patronymic words; आपत्यस्य<BR> च तद्धितेऽनाति P. VI. 4. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथि|आपथिः
आपथि <i>a.</i> Ved. Being on the way or journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथिः|आपथि
आपथि + .{@-थिः, -थीः, -थ्यः@} Ved. A wanderer, traveller, आपथयो विपथयो<BR> ऽन्तस्पथा अनुपथाः Rv. 5. 52. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथीः
आपथि + .{@-थिः, -थीः, -थ्यः@} Ved. A wanderer, traveller, आपथयो विपथयो<BR> ऽन्तस्पथा अनुपथाः Rv. 5. 52. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथ्यः
आपथि + .{@-थिः, -थीः, -थ्यः@} Ved. A wanderer, traveller, आपथयो विपथयो<BR> ऽन्तस्पथा अनुपथाः Rv. 5. 52. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go near, walk towards, approach; एष रावणिरापादि वानराणां भयंकरः Bk. 15. 89.<BR>—2 To enter into, go to, attain to (a place, state &c.); वक्त्रमापद्य<BR> मारुतः Śik. 9; निर्वेदमापद्यते becomes disgusted Mk. 1. 14; आपेदिरेऽम्बरपथम्<BR> Bv. 1. 17; क्षीरं दधिभावमापद्यते Ś. B. milk turns into curds;<BR> पाण्डुरतामापद्यमानस्य K. 69 becoming pale; 160; विस्मयमापेदे 179;<BR> श्लोकत्वमापद्यत यस्य शोकः R. 14. 70 assumed the form of a<BR> verse; चिन्तामापेदे Dk. 130 fell a-thinking; so विश्वासम्, निर्वृतिम्,<BR> संशयम्, वशम्, पञ्चत्वम् &c. पुनः पुनर्वशमापद्यते मे Kaṭh. 1. 2. 6.<BR>—3 To get into trouble, fall into misfortune; अर्थधर्मौ परित्यज यः<BR> काममनुवर्तते । एवमापद्यते क्षिप्रं राजा दशरथो यथा ॥ Rām.;<BR> see आपन्न below.<BR>—4 To happen, occur; जिवत्सोर्नूनमापादि ध्वंसोऽयं तां निशाचरात् Bk. 6. 31;<BR> एवमापद्यते M. 1 so it is. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bring about, bring to pass, accomplish, effect; कूजद्भिरापादितवंशकृत्यम्<BR> R. 2. 12; Śānti. 3. 19.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">Page0339-1</a>]<BR>—2 To lead or reduce to, cause to suffer; आपाद्यते न व्ययमन्तरायैः R. 5. 5.<BR>—3 To cause, to produce, bring on; लघिमानमापादयति K. 105, 109;<BR> दोषमपि गुणत्वमापादयति makes the best of a bad matter.<BR>—4 To reach or attain to.<BR>—5 To spread, circulate (as news).<BR>—6 To turn or change into; एकामपि काकिणीं कार्षापणलक्षमापादयेम Dk. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्तिः|आपत्ति
आपत्तिः <i>f.</i> [आ-पद्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Turning or changing into, entering into any state or condition.<BR>—2 Obtaining, procuring, getting; स्थानापत्तेर्द्रव्येषु धर्मलाभः Kāty.<BR>—3 Misfortune, calamity, adversity; Y. 3. 42.<BR>—4 A fault, transgression.<BR>—5 Remonstrance, expostulation.<BR>—6 (In phil.) An undesirable conclusion or occurrence (अनिष्टप्रसङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् <i>f.</i> [आ-पद्-क्विप्] A calamity, misfortune, danger, distress,<BR> adversity; दैवीनां मानुषीणां च प्रतिहर्ता त्वमापदाम् R. 1. 60; अविवेकः<BR> परमापदां पदम् Ki. 2. 30, 14; प्रायो गच्छति यत्र भाग्यरहितस्तत्रैव<BR> यान्त्यापदः Bh. 2. 90; {@आपदि स्था, आपदं प्राप्@} to fall into difficulty.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपत्कल्पः, आपत्कालः, आपत्कालिक, आपद्गत, आपद्ग्रस्त, आपत्प्राप्त, आपद्धर्मः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्कल्पः|आपत्कल्प
आपद् + -कल्पः an alternative to be used in times of difficulty;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्कालः|आपत्काल
आपद् + -कालः days of adversity, time of distress, hour of danger; अब्राह्मणादध्ययनमापत्काले<BR> विधीयते Ms. 2. 241, 11. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्कालिक
आपद् + -कालिक <i>a.</i> (-का, -की <i>f.</i>) occurring in time of difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्गत
आपद् + -गत, -ग्रस्त, -प्राप्त<BR>—1 fallen into misfortune, involved in difficulties.<BR>—2 unfortunate, unhappy, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्ग्रस्त
आपद् + -गत, -ग्रस्त, -प्राप्त<BR>—1 fallen into misfortune, involved in difficulties.<BR>—2 unfortunate, unhappy, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्प्राप्त|आपत्प्राप्तः
आपद् + -गत, -ग्रस्त, -प्राप्त<BR>—1 fallen into misfortune, involved in difficulties.<BR>—2 unfortunate, unhappy, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्धर्मः|आपद्धर्म|आपद्धर्म्म
आपद् + -धर्मः [आपदि कर्तव्यो धर्मः] a practice, profession, or<BR> course of procedure, not usually proper for a caste, but allowable in<BR> timess of extreme distress or calamity; Ms. 1. 116, एते चतुर्णां वर्णानामापद्धर्माः<BR> प्रकीर्तिताः 10. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्धर्मम्
आपद् + -धर्मः + .({@-मम्@})<BR>—1 N. of a पर्व in Bhārata.<BR>—2 A series of calamities; पीडा चापदकालश्च Mb. 12. 59. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपच्चिक
आपच्चिक <i>a.</i> One who crosses over the difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदा
आपदा <i>f.</i> Misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्न|आपन्नः
आपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gained, obtained, acquired; जीविकापन्नः for आपन्नजीविकः Sk.<BR>—2 Gone or reduced to, fallen into; कष्टां दशामापन्नोऽपि Bh. 2. 29; so दुःख˚.<BR>—3 Afflicted, distressed, being in difficulty; आपन्नाभयसत्रेषु दीक्षिताः<BR> खलु पौरवाः Ś. 2. 17; Me. 55; H. 4. 106; V. 2.<BR>—4 Befallen; परिच्छेदो हि पाण्डित्यं यदापन्ना विपत्तयः H. 128.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपन्नसत्त्वा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्नसत्त्वा
आपन्न + -सत्त्वा pregnant, quick or big with child; a pregnant woman; सममापन्नसत्त्वास्ता<BR> रेजुरापाण्डुरत्विषः R. 10. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपादः|आपाद
आपादः [आ-पद्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Attainment, obtaining.<BR>—2 Reward, remuneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपादनम्
आपादनम् Causing to arrive at, leading or contributing to, bringing<BR> about; tending to; द्रव्यस्य संख्यान्तरापादने Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदेवः|आपदेव
आपदेवः<BR>—1 N. of the god Varuṇa.<BR>—2 N. of the author of मीमांसान्यायप्रकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनिकः|आपनिक
आपनिकः [आ-पन्-इकन् Uṇ. 2. 46]<BR>—1 An emerald, sapphire.<BR>—2 A <i>Kirāta</i> or barbarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यक|आपमित्यकं
आपमित्यक <i>a.</i> [अपमित्य परिवर्त्य निर्वृत्तम् कक्] Received<BR> by barter or exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यकम्
आपमित्यक + .{@-कम्@} Property or anything obtained by barter or for a consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपया
आपया [आपेन जलपूरेन याति या-क] N. of a river near the Sarasvatī;<BR> दृषद्वत्या मानुष आपयायां सरस्वत्यां रेवदग्ने दिदीहि Rv. 3. 23. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपरपक्षीय
आपरपक्षीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to the second half (of a month); कुर्यादापरपक्षीयं<BR> मासि प्रौष्ठपदे द्विजः (श्राद्धं पित्रोः) Bhāg. 7. 14. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपराह्णिक
आपराह्णिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Being in the afternoon, श्वः कार्यमद्य कुर्वीत<BR> पूर्वाह्णे चापराह्णिकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपर्तुक|आपर्त्तुक
आपर्तुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Not restricted to particular times or seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपवः|आपव
आपवः An epithet of Vasiṣṭha; तत्ते शापाद्विनिर्मुक्ता आपवस्य<BR> महात्मनः Mb. 1. 98. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपवर्ग्य
आपवर्ग्य <i>a.</i> Conferring final beatitude; मौनव्रतश्रुततपोध्ययनस्वधर्मव्याख्यारहोजपसमाधय<BR> आपवर्ग्याः Bhāg. 7. 9. 46, 10. 49. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्
आपस् <i>n.</i> [आप्-असुन्]<BR>—1 Water; आपोभिर्मार्जनं कृत्वा.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>—3 A religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्करः|आपस्कर
आपस्करः (see अपस्करः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्कारम्
आपस्कारम् The root or extremity of the trunk or body; आपस्काराल्लूनगात्रस्य<BR> भूमिम् Śi. 18. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपा
आपा €1 P.<BR>—1 To drink up (lit. and fig.); षडाननापीतपयोधरासु R. 14. 22;<BR> आपीतसूर्यं नभः Mk. 5. 20 quite concealed or obscured; दिवाकरापीतरसा<BR> महौषधीः Mb.<BR>—2 To drink with the ears or eyes, hear or see intently; ता राघवं<BR> दृष्टिभिरापिबन्त्यः R. 7. 12; K. 86; भगवत्कथासुधामापीय कर्णाञ्जलिभिः Bhāg.<BR>—3 To eclipse, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपानम्
आपानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 A drinking party, banquet; Mk. 8; आपाने पानकलिता दैवेनाभिप्रचोदिताः Mb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपानोत्सवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपानकम्
आपानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 A drinking party, banquet; Mk. 8; आपाने पानकलिता दैवेनाभिप्रचोदिताः Mb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आपानोत्सवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपानोत्सवः
आपानम् + -उत्सवः Drinking festival.<BR> … समन्ताद् आपानोत्सवमनुभवन्तीव मधुपाः । Nāg. 3. 8.<BR>—2 A tavern, liquor-shop, a place for drinking in company (˚भूमि);<BR> आपाने पानकलिता दैवेनाभिप्रचोदिताः Mb. 1. 2. 355; ताम्बूलीनां दलैस्तत्र<BR> रचितापानभूमयः R. 4. 42; Ku. 6. 42; आपानकमुत्सवः K. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपायिन्
आपायिन् <i>a.</i> Drinking, fond of drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाकः|आपाक
आपाकः [समन्तात् परिवेष्टय पच्यतेऽत्र] A baking oven, a potterʼs kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाङ्ग्यम्
आपाङ्ग्यम् [अपाङ्गे देयं ञ्य] To be used for anointing the corners<BR> of the eyes (as अञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपालिः|आपालि
आपालिः A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिञ्जर|आपिंजर|आपिञ्जरं
आपिञ्जर^1 <i>a.</i> Somewhat red, reddish; मञ्जर्युदारा शुशुभेऽर्जुनस्य<BR> आपिञ्जराबद्धरजःकणत्वात् R. 16. 51.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिञ्जरम्
आपिञ्जर + .{@-रम्@} Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशर्वर
आपिशर्वर <i>a.</i> Nightly, nocturnal. Yaj. Ts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशलिः|आपिशलि
आपिशलिः N. of an old grammarian; वासुप्यापिशलेः P. VI. 1. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशल|आपिशलः
आपिशल <i>a.</i> Originating from आपिशलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशलः|आपिशल
आपिशल + .{@-लः@} A pupil of आपिशलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशला
आपिशल + .{@-ला@} A female pupil; आपिशलमधीते आपिशला ब्राह्मणी Mbh. on P. IV. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी, आपीन See आप्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपी, आपीन See आप्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड्
आपीड् €10 P.<BR>—1 To press, weigh down; पयोधरभारेणापीडितः Gīt. 12; भुजाभ्यां<BR> तमापीड्य clasping him to the bosom.<BR>—2 To press hard, afflict, perplex, worry.<BR>—3 To compress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आपीड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Giving pain, hurting.<BR>—2 Squeezing, compressing.<BR>—3 A chaplet (tied on the crown of the head), garland in general; ते<BR> हयाः काञ्चनापीडा रुक्मभाण्डपरिच्छदाः Mb. 6. 89. 32; चूडापीडकपालसंकुलगलन्मन्दाकिनीवारयः Māl. 1. 2.<BR>—4 (Hence fig.) A crest-jewel; तस्मिन्कुलापीडनिभे विपीडम् R. 18. 29;<BR> Māl. 1, 6, 7.<BR>—5 A stream; अभवच्छोणितोद्गारी सापीड इव पर्वतः Rām. 4. 16. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडनम्
आपीडनम्<BR>—1 Compressing, squeezing; tying tightly.<BR>—2 Embracing, clasping.<BR>—3 Giving pain, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आपीडित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Compressed, bound tightly; embraced &c.<BR>—2 Decorated with chaplets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आपीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Yellowish.<BR>—2 Drunk or sipped a little (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीतः|आपीत|आपीतं
आपीत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Yellowish colour.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (Mar. नांदुरकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीतम्
आपीत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A pyritic mineral (माक्षिकधातु).<BR>—2 Filament of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिक|आपूपिकं|आपूपिकः
आपूपिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अपूप-ठक्]<BR>—1 A good maker of अपूप (cakes).<BR>—2 Accustomed to eat cakes.<BR>—3 Fond of cakes, eating cakes (with benefit).<BR>—4 Selling cakes.<BR>—5 Baking cakes.<BR>—6 Forming an ingredient of cakes, good for cakes (as गुड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिकः|आपूपिक|आपूपिकं
आपूपिक + .{@-कः@} A baker; confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिकम्
आपूपिक + .{@-कम्@} A multitude of cakes (अपूपानां समूहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूप्यः|आपूप्य
आपूप्यः [अपूपाय साधुः बाहु˚ य] Flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूषम्
आपूषम् A kind of metal (perhaps tin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्
आपृच् €7 U.<BR>—1 To fill, pervade, occupy completely; वस्वो वीरस्यापृचः Rv. 8. 40. 9.<BR>—2 To mix or blend with.<BR>—3 (Ā.) To satiate oneself; दुर्मन्मानं सुमन्तुभिरेमिषा पृचीमहि Rv. 1. 129. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्
आपृच् <i>a.</i> [पृच्-क्विप्] Connected, blended. ━<i>ind.</i> In a mixed<BR> manner, confusedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपॄ
आपॄ €9 U. or <i>Caus.</i> —1 To fill; अमी जलापूरितसूत्रमार्गाः<BR> R. 16. 65; तेजोभिरापूर्य जगत्समग्रम् Bg. 11. 30; Bk. 6. 118; (fig.)<BR> to make full, complete, to fulfil (wishes); भृत्यैरापूर्यते नृपः H. 2. 73.<BR>━<i>pass.</i> To be filled, to be filled with wind, be blown (as<BR> a conch); आपूर्यमाणानां स्नानशङ्खानाम् K. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर|आपूरः
आपूर <i>a.</i> Becoming full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरः|आपूर
आपूर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Flow, current, large flood, quantity; स्वेदापूरो युवतिसरितां व्याप<BR> गण्डस्थलानि Śi. 7. 74; हर्षभरापूरपीडनोत्फुल्लया दृशा Ks. 23. 71.<BR>—2 Filling, making full; मन्दानिलापूरकृतं दधानो Śi. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरण
आपूरण <i>a.</i> Becoming full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरणम्
आपूरण + .{@-णम्@} Filling, making full; गर्त˚ कृतम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्ण
आपूर्ण <i>p. p.</i> Filled &c.; आपूर्णश्च कलाभिरिन्दुरमलः Māl. 9. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्तिः|आपूर्ति|आपूर्त्ति|आपूर्त्तिः
आपूर्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Filling.<BR>—2 Fulness, satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्यमाण|आपूर्य्यमाण
आपूर्यमाण <i>a.</i> Becoming full, being filled; आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं<BR> समुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत् Bg. 2. 70; ˚पक्षः the crescent or<BR> waxing moon; आपूर्यमाणपक्षस्य पुण्याहे Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपेक्षिक
आपेक्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अपेक्षा-ठक्] Raising expectations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोक्लिमम्
आपोक्लिमम् N. of the 3rd, 6th, 9th, or 12th position (in Astrol.);<BR> तृतीयं षष्ठनवममन्त्यं चापोक्लिमं विदुः; also केन्द्रात् परं<BR> पणफरं पूर्वमापोक्लिमं मतम्. [cf. Gr. <i>apoklima</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमय
आपोमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आपस्-विकारे प्राचुर्ये वा मयट्] Consisting of<BR> water; आपोमयः प्राणः Ch. Up. 6. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमात्रा
आपोमात्रा The subtle elementary principle of water; आपश्चापोमात्रा<BR> च Praśna. Up. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोशानः|आपोशान
आपोशानः N. of a kind of prayer or formula repeated before and after<BR> eating (the formulas being respectively अमृतोपस्तरणमसि स्वाहा and<BR> अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा); आपोशानक्रियापूर्वं सत्कृतान्नमकुत्सयन् Y. 1. 31, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोशानम्
आपोशानः + .{@-नम्@} The act of making an उपस्तरण (seat) and अपिधान<BR> (covering) for the food eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त, आप्य see आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्त, आप्य see आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तोर्यामः|आप्तोर्याम
आप्तोर्यामः A kind of यज्ञ in the सप्तसोमसंस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त्यः|आप्त्य
आप्त्यः Ved. N. of a class of deities, especially of the deity Trita<BR> as belonging to that class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यै
आप्यै €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To grow fat, stout, or full, become full, increase; आहुत्याप्यायते<BR> सूर्यः Y. 3. 71.<BR>—2 To make full, strengthen, enlarge.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> (प्याययति) —1 To make fat, full, or comfortable, increase,<BR> enlarge; तेजसा तव तेजश्च विष्णुराप्याययिष्यति Mb.; सैव कान्तिर्मन्मथाप्यायिता<BR> द्युतिः S. D.; वायुभिराप्यायितशरीरः Pt. 1;<BR> Me. 44; क्षयी चाप्यायतिः सोमः Ms. 9. 314. 2 To gratify, regale,<BR> satisfy, please; आप्यायितो वचनामृतेन H. 1; K. 124; Mv. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी <i>a.</i> Fat, stout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीः
आपी + .{@-पीः@} <i>f.</i> The 20th Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपीन <i>p. p.</i> [प्यै-क्त] Stout, fat, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीनः|आपीन|आपीनं
आपीन + .{@-नः@} A well; आपीनोऽन्धुः Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीनम्
आपीन + .{@-नम्@} An udder, teat; आपीनभारोद्वहनप्रयत्नात् R. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यान
आप्यान <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fat, stout, robust, strong; आप्यानश्चन्द्रमाः Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 28.<BR> आप्यानस्कन्धकण्ठांऽसम् Bk. 5. 56, 9. 2.<BR>—2 Pleased, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यानम्
आप्यान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Love.<BR>—2 Growth, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायः|आप्याय
आप्यायः Becoming full or fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन <i>a.</i> Causing fulness or stoutness, promoting welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायनम्
आप्यायन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} [प्याय्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of making full or fat; क्लेदनं पिण्डनं तृप्तिः प्राणनाप्यायनोन्दनम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 43.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">Page0341-1</a>]<BR>—2 Satisfying, refreshing, pleasing.<BR>—3 Satisfaction, satiety; देवस्याप्यायना भवति Pt. 1; Ms. 3. 211.<BR>—4 Advancing, promoting.<BR>—5 Corpulency, growing fat or stout.<BR>—6 Anything which causes corpulency or good condition.<BR>—7 A strengthening medicine.<BR>—8 Pouring water on Soma and thus causing it to swell.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आप्यायनशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायना
आप्यायन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} [प्याय्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of making full or fat; क्लेदनं पिण्डनं तृप्तिः प्राणनाप्यायनोन्दनम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 43.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">Page0341-1</a>]<BR>—2 Satisfying, refreshing, pleasing.<BR>—3 Satisfaction, satiety; देवस्याप्यायना भवति Pt. 1; Ms. 3. 211.<BR>—4 Advancing, promoting.<BR>—5 Corpulency, growing fat or stout.<BR>—6 Anything which causes corpulency or good condition.<BR>—7 A strengthening medicine.<BR>—8 Pouring water on Soma and thus causing it to swell.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आप्यायनशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायनशील
आप्यायन + -शील <i>a.</i> satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायित|आप्यायितः
आप्यायित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Satisfied, pleased.<BR>—2 Improved; grown, increased.<BR>—3 Stout, fat, robust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्याय्य
आप्याय्य <i>a.</i> To be satisfied or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्र
आप्र <i>a.</i> Ved. [आ-पृ-मूल˚ क]<BR>—1 Filling.<BR>—2 Able to reach (Sāy.).<BR>—3 Busy, zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छ्|आप्रछ्
आप्रच्छ् €6 Ā.<BR>—1 To bid adieu, bid farewell; आपृच्छस्व प्रियसखममुं तुङ्गमालिङ्ग्य<BR> शैलम् Me. 12; R. 8. 49, 12. 103; Māl. 7; Bk. 14. 63.<BR>—2 To salute on receiving, but particularly parting with a visitor (साधो<BR> यामि इति वचनम्)<BR>—3 To ask.<BR>—4 To extol. Irregularly it is used in Parasmaipada also; cf. आपृच्छ<BR> पुत्रकृतकान् हरिणान् द्रुमांश्च Pratimā 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आपृच्छा [प्रच्छ्-अड्]<BR>—1 Conversation.<BR>—2 Bidding farewell.<BR>—3 Curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छ्य|आपृछ्य
आपृच्छ्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be saluted, welcomed or honoured.<BR>—2 Praiseworthy, commendable.<BR>—3 Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृष्ट
आपृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Welcomed, saluted.<BR>—2 Asked for. नापृष्टः कस्यचिद् ब्रूयात् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छनम्
आप्रच्छनम्<BR>—1 Bidding adieu, taking leave at the time of departure.<BR>—2 Welcoming, hailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छन्न|आप्रच्छन्नं
आप्रच्छन्न <i>a.</i> Secret, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रदिवम्
आप्रदिवम् <i>ind.</i> Forever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदम्
आप्रपदम् [प्रपदं पदाग्रं तत्पर्यन्तम् अव्ययी˚] A dress reaching<BR> to the feet. ━<i>ind.</i> To the end of the foot, reaching to the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीन|आप्रपदीनं
आप्रपदीन <i>a.</i> [आप्रपदं व्याप्नोति ख] Reaching to the feet<BR> (as dress); भाति स्म दामाप्रपदीनमस्य Śi. 3. 10; K. 130; (आप्रपदीनकम् also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रवण
आप्रवण <i>a.</i> Slightly humble or precipitous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्री
आप्री <i>f.</i> [आप्रीणात्यनया आ-प्री-ड-गौरा˚ ङीष्] Ved.<BR>—1 Conciliation, propitiation, gaining oneʼs favour.<BR>—2 (pl.) ‘Propitiatory verses’, a name given to certain invocations addressed<BR> to several deified objects in consecutive order, and said to be introductory<BR> to the animal sacrifice; some take the <i>Apris</i> to represent the objects<BR> themselves, the verses being consequently called <i>Apri</i> verses. The<BR> objects invoked are 12:− Susamiddha, Tanūnapāt, Narāśaṃsa, the divine<BR> being bearing invocations to the gods, Barhis, the doors of the sacrificial<BR> chamber, night and dawn the two divine beings protecting the sacrifice,<BR> the three goddesses Ilā,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">Page0341-2</a>]<BR> Sarasvatī, and Mahī, Tvaṣṭṛ, Vanaspati and Svāhā, (all these being<BR> regarded by Sāyaṇa to be different forms of Agni); स एता आप्रीरपश्यत्ताभिर्वै<BR> स मुखत आत्मानमाप्रीणीत; cf. also Max Mullerʼs Hist. Anc. Lit. pp. 463-466.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रीतपः|आप्रीतप
आप्रीतपः, -पाः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu (protecting those who have appeased his anger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रीतपाः
आप्रीतपः, -पाः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu (protecting those who have appeased his anger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लु
आप्लु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To jump up, dance, spring; आप्लुत्य पदान्यष्टौ Mb.; (रथं)<BR> आपुप्लुवे सिंह इवाचलाग्रम्.<BR>—2 To bathe, wash, immerse oneself (fig. also); प्रयागे आप्लुत्य गात्राणि<BR> Mb.; आप्लुत्याकाशगङ्गायाम् <i>ibid.</i>; Ms. 7. 216, 11. 202. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (प्लावयति)<BR>—1 To cause to be washed or bathed; आप्लावयत गात्राणि Mb.<BR>—2 To wash, wet, sprinkle; अन्नमाप्लाव्य वारिणा Ms. 3. 244, 11. 98.<BR>—3 To overflow, overwhelm, inundate, flood over.<BR>—4 To set in commotion.<BR>—5 (Ātm.) To bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवः|आप्लव
आप्लवः, -प्लवनम्<BR>—1 Bathing, immersing.<BR>—2 Sprinkling with water (on all sides).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आप्लवव्रतिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवनम्
आप्लवः, -प्लवनम्<BR>—1 Bathing, immersing.<BR>—2 Sprinkling with water (on all sides).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आप्लवव्रतिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवव्रतिन्
आप्लवः + -व्रतिन् or {@आप्लुतव्रतिन्@} <i>m.</i> a house-holder who has<BR> passed through the first order (ब्रह्मचर्य) and is admitted into the<BR> second (गार्हस्थ्य), an initiated householder; cf. स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुतव्रतिन्
आप्लवः + -व्रतिन् or {@आप्लुतव्रतिन्@} <i>m.</i> a house-holder who has<BR> passed through the first order (ब्रह्मचर्य) and is admitted into the<BR> second (गार्हस्थ्य), an initiated householder; cf. स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लावः|आप्लाव
आप्लावः<BR>—1 Bathing, immersing,<BR>—2 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>—3 Submerging.<BR>—4 A flood, an inundation; प्रलयाप्लावमिवाभिदर्शयन्तः Śi. 20. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत|आप्लुतः
आप्लुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bathed; अवभृथाप्लुतो मुनिः R. 11. 31; Ku. 6. 5. ततः समुत्सुकोऽभ्येत्य<BR> नृपतिर्द्रुतमाप्लुतः Śiva B. 1. 79.<BR>—2 Wetted, sprinkled; यावन्नाश्यायते वेदिरभिषेकजलाप्लुता R. 17. 37.<BR>—3 Overflowing with, filled or overcome with; बाष्प˚, व्यसन˚, रुधिर˚ &c.<BR>—4 Possessed by, eclipsed; अवाङ्मुखमथो दीनं दृष्ट्वा सोममिवाप्लुतम्<BR> Rām. 7. 106. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुतः|आप्लुत
आप्लुत + .{@-तः@}, ˚व्रती An initiated house-holder, see आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुतम्
आप्लुत + .{@-तम्@} Bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुष्ट
आप्लुष्ट <i>a.</i> A little singed or burnt; दिवाकराप्लुष्टविभूषणास्पदाम् Ku. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वन्
आप्वन् <i>m.</i> [आप्-वन् Uṇ. 1. 152] Wind, air (आप्वः according to Ujjval.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वा
आप्वा The neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आफलकः|आफलक
आफलकः Enclosure, palisade; वार्याफलकपर्यन्तां पिबन्निक्षुमतीं<BR> नदीम् Rām. 1. 70. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आफीनम्
आफीनम् An Opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आफूकम्
आफूकम् Opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध्|आबंध्
आबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind, fasten, tie on, place, fix; क्व समाधानमाबध्नातु अवष्टम्भः<BR> K. 290; न क्वचिन्निर्भरमाबध्नति पदम् 104 places; तेऽपि पोषिताः<BR> पोषितरि स्नेहमाबध्नान्ति 289.<BR>—2 To make, form; {@आबद्धाञ्जलिः@}, see आबद्ध below.<BR>—3 To hold fast, cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्ध|आबद्धः
आबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied.<BR>—2 Fixed; स्यन्दनाबद्धदृष्टिषु R. 1. 40.<BR>—3 Formed, made; आबद्धमण्डला तापसपरिषद्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">Page0342-1</a>]<BR> K. 49 sitting in a circle; आबद्धरेखमभितो रविमञ्जरीभिः Gīt. 11;<BR> Bk. 3. 30; Ki. 5. 33.<BR>—4 Obtained.<BR>—5 Hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्धम्
आबद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} + ({@-द्धः@} also)<BR>—1 Binding, joining.<BR>—2 A yoke.<BR>—3 Ornament; Sāṅ. Gṛ. Sūtras 2. 1. 25.<BR>—4 Affection.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आबद्धमण्डल, आबद्धमाल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्धः|आबद्ध
आबद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} + ({@-द्धः@} also)<BR>—1 Binding, joining.<BR>—2 A yoke.<BR>—3 Ornament; Sāṅ. Gṛ. Sūtras 2. 1. 25.<BR>—4 Affection.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आबद्धमण्डल, आबद्धमाल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0341-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्धमण्डल
आबद्ध + -मण्डल <i>a.</i> Forming a circle, sitting in a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्धमाल
आबद्ध + -माल <i>a.</i> forming a wreath, arranged in a row; गर्भाधानक्षणपरिचयान्नूनमाबद्धमालाः Me. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबधः|आबध
आबधः Ved. Binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्धः|आबन्ध|आबंधः
आबन्धः, -धनम्<BR>—1 A tie or bond (fig. also); प्रेमाबन्धविवर्धित Ratn. 3. 18; गते<BR> प्रेमाबन्धे प्रणयबहुमाने विगलिते । Amaru. 43.<BR>—2 The tie of a yoke, or that which fastens the ox to the yoke, or the<BR> yoke to the plough.<BR>—3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>—4 Affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्धनम्
आबन्धः, -धनम्<BR>—1 A tie or bond (fig. also); प्रेमाबन्धविवर्धित Ratn. 3. 18; गते<BR> प्रेमाबन्धे प्रणयबहुमाने विगलिते । Amaru. 43.<BR>—2 The tie of a yoke, or that which fastens the ox to the yoke, or the<BR> yoke to the plough.<BR>—3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>—4 Affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्धुर
आबन्धुर <i>a.</i> A little deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्ह|आबर्हः
आबर्ह (also आबर्हित) <i>a.</i> Having the power of tearing<BR> or pulling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हित
आबर्ह (also आबर्हित) <i>a.</i> Having the power of tearing<BR> or pulling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हः|आबर्ह
आबर्ह (also आबर्हित) + .{@-र्हः, -र्हणम्@} [आ-बर्ह्-हिंसायां घञ् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Tearing or pulling out.<BR>—2 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हणम्
आबर्ह (also आबर्हित) + .{@-र्हः, -र्हणम्@} [आ-बर्ह्-हिंसायां घञ् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Tearing or pulling out.<BR>—2 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हिन्
आबर्हिन् <i>a.</i> [आबर्ह्-इनि] Fit for tearing out; मूलमस्याबर्हि P. IV. 4. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबल्यम्
आबल्यम् [अबलस्य भावः] Weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाध्
आबाध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To check, rein in, restrain.<BR>—2 To interrupt, obstruct.<BR>—3 To annoy, harass, attack, molest, injure.<BR>—4 To set forth or declare wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाधः|आबाध
आबाधः<BR>—1 Affliction, injury, trouble, molestation, damage; न प्राणाबाधमाचरेत् Ms. 4. 54, 51.<BR>—2 Interruption, hindrance; दर्शनीयं निराबाधं कुम्भकर्णस्य चकिरे<BR> Rām. 7. 13. 4.<BR>—3 Attack (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाधा
आबाधः + .{@-धा@}<BR>—1 Pain, distress.<BR>—2 Mental agony or anguish.<BR>—3 Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबालम्
आबालम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Down to or including children;<BR>—2 Beginning with infants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाल्यम्
आबाल्यम् Age ending with childhood. See above. आबाल्याद्विप्रवर्गैः<BR> स्ववदनविवरे धारिता वैरिणी मे Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबिल|आबिलः
आबिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Turbid, dirty (= आविल q. v.).<BR>—2 Clearing, breaking.<BR>—3 Confounded, embarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुत्त|आबुत्तः
आबुत्त = आवुत्त q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुध्
आबुध् €1 P. To perceive, notice, understand (Ved.); Rv. 7. 22. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुध्यम्
आबुध्यम् Want of discernment, foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबोधनम्
आबोधनम्<BR>—1 Knowledge, understanding.<BR>—2 Instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्द
आब्द <i>a.</i> [अब्द-अण्] Belonging to, or produced from, a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्दी
आब्द + .({@-ब्दी@} <i>f.</i>) [अब्द-अण्] Belonging to, or produced from, a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्दिक
आब्दिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अब्द-ठक्] Annual, yearly; आब्दिकः करः<BR> Ms. 7. 129, 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्रह्म
आब्रह्म <i>ind.</i> Up to or including ब्रह्मन्; यशोभिराब्रह्मसभं<BR> प्रकाशः R. 18. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभगः|आभग
आभगः Ved. A partner (of anything); to be shared in (Sāy.); देवो<BR> देवेष्वाभगः Rv. 1. 136. 4; कर्मन्कर्मन्नाभगमग्निमीडे Av. 4. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभङ्गम्
आभङ्गम् A pose in which the idol is slightly bent. आभङ्ग-समभङ्गं<BR> चातिभङ्गं त्रिधा भवेत् Māna. 67. 95. 96. ग्रीवाभङ्गाभिरामम् Ś. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभङ्गिन्
आभङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> A little curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरणम्
आभरणम् See under आभृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा €2 P.<BR>—1 To shine, blaze; सुतरां रत्नमाभाति चामीकरनियोजितम् Subhāṣ.; R. 3. 33.<BR>—2 To appear, look like; आभासि तीर्थप्रतिपादितार्द्धिः R. 5. 15, 70, 13. 14;<BR> Bk. 7. 8, 66.<BR>—3 To outshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा [भा-अड्]<BR>—1 Light, splendour, lustre; तत्र ताराधिपस्याभा ताराणां भा तथैव च ।<BR> तयोराभरणाभा च ज्वलिता द्यामभासयत् ॥ Rām. 6. 75. 51 दीपाभां<BR> शलभा यथा Pt. 4.<BR>—2 Colour, appearance, beauty; प्रशान्तमिव शुद्धाभम् Ms. 12. 27.<BR>—3 Likeness, resemblance; oft. at the end of comp. in these two senses;<BR> रुक्माभम् appearing or shining like gold; यमदूताभम् Pt. 1. 58;<BR> मरुत्सखाभम् R. 2. 10.<BR>—4 A reflected image, shadow, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभात
आभात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shining, blazing.<BR>—2 Appearing, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभातिः|आभाति
आभातिः <i>f.</i> [आ-भा-क्तिच्] —1 Reflection.<BR>—2 Splendour, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाणकः|आभाणक
आभाणकः A popular saying, proverb; तथा च लौकिकानामाभाणकः<BR> as the proverb goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्
आभाष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To address, speak to, converse with; वैशम्पायनश्चन्द्रापीडमाबभाषे<BR> K. 117; कुरुते नालापमाभाषिता Nāg. 4.<BR>—2 To say or speak (something) (with two acc.); आभाषि रामेण वचः कनीयान् Bk. 3. 51.<BR>—3 To say or speak; सखी वेत्रभृदावभाषे R. 6. 82, 14. 44.<BR>—4 To name<BR>—5 To talk aloud, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषः|आभाष
आभाषः [भाष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Addressing.<BR>—2 An introduction, preface.<BR>—3 Speech, talk.<BR>—4 A saying, proverb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषणम्
आभाषणम्<BR>—1 Addressing, speaking to (संबोधन).<BR>—2 Conversation; सम्बन्धमाभाषणपूर्वमाहुः R. 2. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्य
आभाष्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be addressed, worthy of being spoken to; जनमाभाष्यमिमं<BR> न मन्यसे R. 8. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्यम्
आभाष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} What is to be said by way of address; Me. 103. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine, blaze.<BR>—2 To be bright.<BR>—3 To appear, seem, look like; स्थानान्तरं स्वर्ग इवावभासे Ku. 7. 3;<BR> R. 7. 43, 63, 14. 12.<BR>—4 To appear untruly, have an appearance; शुक्तिः रजतवदाभासते; Ki. 17. 21.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् <i>f.</i> Splendour, lustre, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासः|आभास
आभासः [भास्-अच्]<BR>—1 Splendour, light, lustre.<BR>—2 A reflection; तत्राज्ञानं धिया नश्येदाभासात्तु घटः स्फुरेत् Vedānta.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Resemblance, likeness; oft. at the end of comp.; नभश्च रुधिराभासम्<BR> Rām. &c.; चिदाभास,<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Semblance,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">Page0343-1</a>]<BR> phantom; युक्तिवाक्यतदाभाससमाश्रयाः Ś. B.; तत्साहसाभासम् Māl. 2<BR> looks like wantonness.<BR>—4 Any unreal or fallacious appearance (as in हेत्वाभास); पुनरुक्तवदाभासः S. D.<BR>—5 A fallacy, fallacious reasoning, semblance of a reason, an erroneous<BR> but plausible argument; see हेत्वाभास; S. D. 270.<BR>—6 An intention, purpose.<BR>—7 One of the nine materials of which idols are made, a marble.<BR>—8 A class of buildings.<BR>—9 An irreligious kind of worship; विधर्मः परधर्मश्च आभास उपमा<BR> छलः । अधर्मशाखाः पञ्चेमा धर्मज्ञोऽधर्मवत्त्यजेत् ॥ Bhāg. 7. 15. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0342-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासनम्
आभासनम् Making apparent or clear; illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासुर|आभासुरः
आभासु(स्व)र <i>a.</i> Splendid, bright, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्वर|आभास्वरः
आभासु(स्व)र <i>a.</i> Splendid, bright, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासुरः|आभासुर
आभासु(स्व)र + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A collective name of 64 demigods.<BR>—2 N. of an attendant <i>Gaṇa</i>.<BR>—3 N. of a particular set of 12 subjects; आत्मा ज्ञाता दमो दान्तः शान्तिर्ज्ञानं<BR> शमस्तपः । कामः क्रोधो मदो मोहो द्वादशाभास्वरा इमे ॥ (तारानाथ<BR> तर्कवाचस्पतिकोश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचरणिक
आभिचरणिक, आभिचार, आभिचारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिचरण-चर-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Magical.<BR>—2 Imprecatory, maledictory; तमाभिचारदहनमायान्तं द्वारकौकसः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 66. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचार
आभिचरणिक, आभिचार, आभिचारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिचरण-चर-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Magical.<BR>—2 Imprecatory, maledictory; तमाभिचारदहनमायान्तं द्वारकौकसः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 66. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचारिक
आभिचरणिक, आभिचार, आभिचारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिचरण-चर-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Magical.<BR>—2 Imprecatory, maledictory; तमाभिचारदहनमायान्तं द्वारकौकसः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 66. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचरणिकम्
आभिचरणिक, आभिचार, आभिचारिक + .{@-कम्@} A spell or incantation, magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजन|आभिजनः
आभिजन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिजन-अण्] Relating to birth (अभिजन),<BR> patronymic (as a name); तां पार्वतीत्याभिजनेन नाम्ना Ku. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजनम्
आभिजन + .{@-नम्@} Nobility or loftiness of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्यम्
आभिजात्यम् [अभिजातस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Nobility of birth; आभिजात्यं हि ते मन्ये यथा मातुस्तथैव च Rām. 2. 35. 17.<BR> ˚शंसिनी च नम्रता Dk. 137; Ratn. 3. 18; Mv. 2. 18.<BR>—2 Rank.<BR>—3 Learning.<BR>—4 Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजित
आभिजित <i>a.</i> [अभिजिति नक्षत्रे जातः अण्] Born under the constellation<BR> <i>Abhijit</i>. आभिजितो मुहूर्तः, आभिजितः स्थालीपाकः Mbh. on P. V. 3. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधा
आभिधा [अभिधैव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 A sound, word.<BR>—2 A name; mentioning; see अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानिक|आभिधानिकः
आभिधानिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Contained in a dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानिकः|आभिधानिक
आभिधानिक + .{@-कः@} A lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयक
आभिधानीयक <i>a.</i> Relating to a word or name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयकम्
आभिधानीयक + .{@-कम्@} The property of a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिप्रायिक
आभिप्रायिक <i>a.</i> Voluntary, optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिप्लविक
आभिप्लविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभिप्लव-ढक्] Relating to the religious ceremony<BR> called आभिप्लव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमन्यवः|आभिमन्यव
आभिमन्यवः A descendant of अभिमन्यु. N. of Parīkṣita; Bhāg. 1. 18. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्यम्
आभिमुख्यम् [अभिमुखस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Direction towards; ˚ख्यं याति goes to meet or encounter.<BR>—2 Being in front of or face to face; नीताभिमुख्यं पुनः Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>—3 Favourableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभियोगिक
आभियोगिक <i>a.</i> Done with skill or dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरामिक
आभिरामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Good, agreeable; Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरूपकम्
आभिरूपकम्, आभिरूप्यम् [आभिरूप वुञ् ष्यञ् च] Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरूप्यम्
आभिरूपकम्, आभिरूप्यम् [आभिरूप वुञ् ष्यञ् च] Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिषेचनिक
आभिषेचनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आभिषेचन-ठञ्] Relating to the inauguration<BR> of a king; आभिषेचनिकं भाण्डं कृत्वा रामः प्रदक्षिणम् Rām. 2. 19. 31; Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिषेचनिकम्
आभिषेचनिक + .{@-कम्@} The material required for अभिषेक; आभिषेचनिकान्यस्मा आजह्नुः<BR> सर्वतो जनाः Bhāg. 4. 15. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिक
आभिहारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आभिहार-ठञ्]<BR>—1 To be offered as a present.<BR>—2 Taken by force, or fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिकम्
आभिहारिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A present.<BR>—2 A room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीकम्
आभीकम् [आभीकेन दृष्टं साम अण्] N. of a Sāma melody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण्यम्
आभीक्ष्ण्यम् [अभीक्ष्णस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Continued repetition; बहुलमाभीक्ष्ण्ये<BR> P. III. 2. 81, 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीय
आभीय <i>a.</i> Contained in rules or Sūtras of Pāṇinī from VI. 4. 22<BR> to VI. 4. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरः|आभीर
आभीरः [आ समन्तात् भियं राति, रा-क Tv.]<BR>—1 A cowherd; आभीरवामनयनाहृतमानसाय दत्तं मनो यदुपते तदिदं<BR> गृहाण Udb.; according to Ms. 10. 15 आभीर is the offspring of a<BR> Brāhmaṇa and a female of the Ambaṣṭha tribe.<BR>—2 (pl.) N. of a country or its inhabitants; श्रीकोंकणादधोभागे तापीतः<BR> पश्चिमे तटे । आभीरदेशो देवेशि विन्ध्यशैले व्यवस्थितः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरी
आभीरः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A cowherdʼs wife.<BR>—2 A woman of the Ābhīra tribe.<BR>—3 The language of the Ābhīras; आभीरेषु तथाभीरी (प्रयोक्तव्या) S. D. 432.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आभीरपल्लिः, आभीरपल्ली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्लिः|आभीरपल्लि
आभीरः + -पल्लिः, -पल्ली <i>f.</i>, {@-पल्लिका@}<BR> a station or abode of herdsmen, a village inhabited by cowherds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्ली
आभीरः + -पल्लिः, -पल्ली <i>f.</i>, {@-पल्लिका@}<BR> a station or abode of herdsmen, a village inhabited by cowherds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील <i>a.</i> [आभियं लाति ददाति ला क] —1 Fearful, terrible;<BR> रात्रौ निशीथे त्वाभीले Mb. 3. 11. 4; आभीलानि प्राणिनः प्रत्यवस्यन् Śi. 18. 78.<BR>—2 Suffering from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीलम्
आभील + .{@-लम्@} Injury, physical pain; आभीलं न द्वयोः कृच्छ्रे वाच्यलिङ्गे<BR> भयानके Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभु
आभु <i>a.</i> [आ-भू-डु] Pervading, reaching; तुच्छ्येनाभ्वपिहितं<BR> यदासीत् Rv. 10. 129. 3. (Sāy.); empty; stingy, empty-handed; सत्यध्वृतं<BR> वृजिनायन्तमाभुम् Rv. 10. 27. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूक
आभूक <i>a.</i> Ved. Empty, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभुग्न
आभुग्न <i>a.</i> A little curved or bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू €1 P. Ved. To be present, continue oneʼs existence; यद्यद्भवन्ति<BR> तदाभवन्ति Ch. Up. 6. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू <i>a.</i> Ved. Approaching (as a praiser); इन्द्रः श्नथयन्ननाभुवः Rv. 1. 51. 9.<BR>—2 Strong, sufficient, efficacious.<BR>—3 Applied according to rule (as a hymn).<BR>—4 Very prosperous. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A prison, a place of confinement.<BR>—2 A helper or assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूतिः|आभूति
आभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Pervasion.<BR>—2 Overpowering strength; आभूत्या सहजा वज्रसायक Rv. 10. 84. 6.<BR>—3 Capability, efficiency.<BR>—4 Production; आभूतिरेषाभूतिर्बीजमेतन्निधीयते Ait. Br. 7. 13. 8^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूषेण्य
आभूषेण्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0343-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभृ
आभृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring; आ नो अग्ने रयिं भर Rv. 1. 79. 8; कदपत्याभृतं<BR> दुःखम् Bhāg.<BR>—2 To carry.<BR>—3 To fill, fill with.<BR>—4 To bear, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरणम्
आभरणम्<BR>—1 An ornament, decoration (fig. also); किमित्यपास्याभरणानि यौवने<BR> धृतं त्वया वार्द्धकशोभि वल्कलम् Ku. 5. 44; प्रशमाभरणं पराकमः<BR> Ki. 2. 32. (आभरण occurs in the names of works; <i>e. g.</i> सरस्वतीकण्ठाभरण).<BR>—2 The act of nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरित
आभरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Filled.<BR>—2 Decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभृत
आभृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Produced, caused to exist; ताभ्यो लोहितमाभृतम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 60.<BR>—2 Filled up, firmly fixed; आभृतात्मा मुनिः Bhāg. 4. 8. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभेरी
आभेरी One of the modes of music (रागिणी) personified as a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगः|आभोग
आभोगः [आ-भुज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Curving, winding.<BR>—2 A curve; आभोगकुटिला (गङ्गा) Mb.; crumpling.<BR>—3 Circuit, circumference, expanse, extension, precincts, environs; अकथितोऽपि<BR> ज्ञायत एव यथायमाभोगस्तपावेनस्येति Ś. 1; गगनाभोगः the expanse<BR> of heaven, wide firmament of the sky; Bh. 3. 57; Mv. 6. 30; शैलाभोगभुवो<BR> भवन्ति ककुभः Māl. 9. 16. प्रासादाभोगः the middle part of a palace;<BR> प्रासादाभोगविस्तीर्णः स्तुतिशब्दो ह्यवर्तत Rām. 2. 65. 3.<BR>—4 Magnitude, fulness, extent, expansive form; गण्डाभोगात् Me. 93 from<BR> the broad cheek; प्रतिरवाभोग Māl. 3. 8, 4. 10, 5. 11; प्रतिभयाभोगैः<BR> प्लवङ्गाधिपैः Mv. 6. 24 bodily form or stature; U. 2. 14; भवाभोगोद्विग्नाः<BR> Bh. 3. 42, 86; Mv. 2; K. 305, 333.<BR>—5 Effort.<BR>—6 The expanded hood of a cobra (used by Varuṇa as his umbrella).<BR>—7 Enjoyment, satiety, completion; विषयाभोगेषु नैवादरः Śāntilakṣaṇa.<BR>—8 Serpent. आभोगं हन्मना हतम् Rv. 7. 94. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगय
आभोगय^1 <i>a.</i> [आभोगं याति या-क] To be enjoyed (as Soma juice); Rv. 1. 110. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: alph. order; RV quote; AP and most others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगयम्
आभोगय + .{@-यम्@} Livelihood (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगिः|आभोगि
आभोगिः Ved.<BR>—1 Enjoyment.<BR>—2 Living, supporting life.<BR>—3 Food, nourishment; Rv. 1. 113. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यन्तर|आभ्यंतर|आभ्यन्तरः
आभ्यन्तर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभ्यन्तरे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Interior, inner, inward; as आभ्यन्तरो भृत्यवर्ग.<BR>—2 One of the two kinds of प्रयत्न or effort giving rise to the vocal sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यन्तरः|आभ्यन्तर|आभ्यंतर
आभ्यन्तर + .{@-रः@} An officer in close contact or specially intimate with the<BR> king. RT. 8. 426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यन्तरिकः|आभ्यन्तरिक
आभ्यन्तर + .{@-रिकः@} An officer connected with harem. Rāmgani Copperplate of<BR> Īśvaraghoṣa (Inscriptions of Bengal, p. 149).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यवकाशिक
आभ्यवकाशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Living in the open air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यवहारिक
आभ्यवहारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभ्यवहाराय हितं ठक्] Eatable (as food &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यागारिक
आभ्यागारिक <i>a.</i> Fit to be nourished in the house or a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यादायिकम्
आभ्यादायिकम् [अभ्यादान-ठक्] A kind of स्त्रीधन or womanʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभ्यास-ठक्]<BR>—1 Resulting from practice; तल्पैश्चाभ्यासिकैर्युक्तं शुशुभे योधरक्षितम्<BR> Mb. 1. 207. 34.<BR>—2 Practising, repeating.<BR>—3 Being near, neighbouring, adjoining (आभ्याशिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
आभ्युदयिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभ्युदय-ठक्]<BR>—1 Tending to good, granting prosperity; अनाभ्युदयिकं श्रमणकदर्शनम् Mk. 8.<BR>—2 Relating to the rise or beginning of anything; सुख˚ Ms. 12. 88.<BR>—3 High, exalted, important.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिकम्
आभ्युदयिक + .{@-कम्@} A Śrāddha or offering to ancestors; an occasion of rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्रिक
आभ्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अभ्प्या खनति ठक्] One who digs with a spade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्
आम् <i>ind.</i> An interjection of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) assent, acceptance, ‘oh’, ‘yes’; आं कुर्मः M. 1;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) recollection; आं तस्मिन्नुर्वश्या वचनं स्खलितमासीत् V. 3;<BR> आं ज्ञातम् Ś. 3, Oh, I see it now; M. 3;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) determination, ‘surely’, ‘verily’, आं चिरस्य खलु प्रतिबुद्धोऽस्मि;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भीयः|आम्भीय
आम्भीयः (Generally used in plural) A school of writers on politics<BR> … इति आम्भीयाः । Kau. A. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम <i>a.</i> [आम्यते ईषत् पच्यते; आ अम् कर्मणि घञ् Tv.]<BR>—1 Raw, uncooked, undressed (opp. पक्व) (oft. applied to the cow<BR> in the Veda; Rv. 3. 30. 14.); आमान्नम् Ms. 4. 223; Y. 1. 287.<BR>—2 Unripe, immature; तुदन्त्यामत्वचं दंशा मशका मत्कुणादयः Bhāg. 3. 31. 27.<BR>—3 Unbaked, unannealed (as a jar); आमकुम्भ इवाम्भःस्थो विशीर्णः H. 4. 66.<BR>—4 Undigested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमम्
आम + .{@-म्@}<BR>—1 State of being raw; शनैः शनैर्जहुः पङ्कं स्थलान्यामं च वीरुधः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 20. 39.<BR>—2 Constipation, passing hard excretion.<BR>—3 Grain freed from chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमः|आम|आमं
आम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Disease; sickness.<BR>—2 Indigestion; आहारस्य रसः सारः यो न पक्वोऽग्निलाघवात् । आमसंज्ञां<BR> स लभते महाव्याधिसमाश्रयः ॥ Suśr.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आमातिसारः, आमाद्, आमान्नम्, आमाशयः, आमकुम्भः, आमगन्धि, आमगन्धिकम्, आमज्वरः, आमत्वच्, आमपाकः, आमपात्रम्, आमपीनसम्, आमपेशाः, आममांसाशिन्, आमरक्तम्, आमरसः, आमवातः, आमशूलः, आमश्राद्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमातिसारः|आमातिसार
आम + -अतिसारः dysentery or diarrhoea caused by vitiated mucus in the<BR> abdomen (the excretion being in this case mixed with hard and fetid matter).<BR> आमातिसारे नो कार्यमादौ संग्रहणं नृणाम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाद्
आम + -अद् <i>a.</i> eating raw flesh or food; आमादः क्षिवङ्कास्त मदन्त्वेनीः Rv. 10. 87. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमान्नम्
आम + -अन्नम् undressed rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाशयः|आमाशय
आम + -आशयः [आमस्यापक्वान्नस्याशयः] ‘receptacle of undigested food’<BR>, the upper part of the belly to the navel, stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमकुम्भः|आमकुम्भ
आम + -कुम्भः a jar of unbaked clay; H. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमगन्धि
आम + -गन्धि <i>n.</i> smelling of raw meat of a burning corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमगन्धिकम्
आम + -गन्धिकम् the smell of raw meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमज्वरः|आमज्वर
आम + -ज्वरः a kind of fever; cf. स्वेद्यमामज्वरं प्राज्ञः कोऽम्भसा<BR> परिषिञ्चति Śi. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमत्वच्
आम + -त्वच् <i>a.</i> of tender skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपाकः|आमपाक
आम + -पाकः<BR>—1 a preliminary stage of the disease called dropsy.<BR>—2 A method of mellowing or ripening a tumour; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपात्रम्
आम + -पात्रम् an unannealed vessel; Av. 8. 10. 28; विनाशं व्रजति<BR> क्षिप्रमामपात्रमिवाम्भसि Ms. 3. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपीनसम्
आम + -पीनसम् running at the nose, defluxion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपेशाः
आम + -पेशाः Grains pounded in a raw condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आममांसाशिन्
आम + -मांसाशिन् <i>m.</i> a cannibal, an eater of raw flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरक्तम्
आम + -रक्तम् dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरसः|आमरस
आम + -रसः imperfect chyme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमवातः|आमवात
आम + -वातः constipation, torpor of the bowels attended with flatulence and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">Page0345-1</a>]<BR> intumescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0344-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमशूलः|आमशूल
आम + -शूलः pain of indigestion, colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमश्राद्धम्
आम + -श्राद्धम् a Śrāddha performed with uncooked food; आपद्यनग्नौ<BR> तीर्थे च चन्द्रसूर्यग्रहे तथा । आमश्राद्धं द्विजैः कार्यं शूद्रेण च सदैव<BR> हि ॥ Prācetasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमक
आमक <i>a.</i> Raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमता
आमता, -त्वम्<BR> Rawness, unreadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमत्वम्
आमता, -त्वम्<BR> Rawness, unreadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमञ्जु
आमञ्जु <i>a.</i> Lovely, charming; आमञ्जुवञ्जुलरुतानि च तान्यमूनि U. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमण्डः|आमण्ड|आमंडः
आमण्डः The castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनम्
आमनम् Ved. Friendly disposition or inclination, affection; Yaj. Ts. 2. 3. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्यम्
आम(मा)नस्यम् [अमनस्-ष्यञ्] Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्यम्
आम(मा)नस्यम् [अमनस्-ष्यञ्] Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्|आमंत्र्
आमन्त्र् €10 Ā.<BR>—1 To bid farewell, bid adieu; आमन्त्रयस्व सहचरम् Ś. 3; लताभगिनीम्<BR> Ś. 4; Ku. 6. 94; K. 223.<BR>—2 To speak to, call out to, address, converse with; तमामन्त्रयाम्बभूव<BR> K. 81, 197; Ve. 1; A. R. 3.<BR>—3 To say, speak; परिजनोप्येवमामन्त्रयते K. 195.<BR>—4 To call, invite, ask (to come); आमन्त्रयध्वं राष्ट्रेषु ब्राह्मणान् Mb.<BR>—5 To invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रणम्
आमन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Addressing, calling, calling out to; अम्बेति वै योषाया आमन्त्रणम् Śat. Br.<BR>—2 Bidding adieu, taking leave of.<BR>—3 Greeting, welcome, courtesy.<BR>—4 Invitation; अनिन्द्यामन्त्रणादृते Y. 1. 112.<BR>—5 Permission.<BR>—6 Conversation; अन्योन्यामन्त्रणं यत्स्याज्जनान्ते तज्जनान्तिकम् S. D. 6.<BR>—7 The vocative case.<BR>—8 Deliberation; asking; interrogation; यन्त्यस्यामन्त्रणमामन्त्रणीयो<BR> भवति य एवं वेद Av. 8. 10. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रणा
आमन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Addressing, calling, calling out to; अम्बेति वै योषाया आमन्त्रणम् Śat. Br.<BR>—2 Bidding adieu, taking leave of.<BR>—3 Greeting, welcome, courtesy.<BR>—4 Invitation; अनिन्द्यामन्त्रणादृते Y. 1. 112.<BR>—5 Permission.<BR>—6 Conversation; अन्योन्यामन्त्रणं यत्स्याज्जनान्ते तज्जनान्तिकम् S. D. 6.<BR>—7 The vocative case.<BR>—8 Deliberation; asking; interrogation; यन्त्यस्यामन्त्रणमामन्त्रणीयो<BR> भवति य एवं वेद Av. 8. 10. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रयितृ|आमंत्रयितृ
आमन्त्रयितृ <i>a.</i> Asking, inviting, calling &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रयितृता
आमन्त्रयितृ + .({@-ता@}) An inviter, entertainer, especially of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रित|आमंत्रित
आमन्त्रित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Invited, called.<BR>—2 Appointed to do a thing which is not obligatory. आमन्त्रणं कामचारानुज्ञा Sk.<BR>—3 Consecrated with a मन्त्र; शरणामामन्त्रितानाम् Mb. 3. 20. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आमन्त्रितविभक्ति, आमन्त्रिततम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रितविभक्ति
आमन्त्रित + -विभक्ति <i>f.</i> Vocative case; तत्र आमन्त्रितविभक्तिवचनं<BR> स्तुतये । ŚB. on MS. 9. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रितविभक्ति
आमन्त्रित + -विभक्ति + ˚वचनम् The employment of an expression<BR> in the vocative case; तत्र आमन्त्रितविभक्तिवचनं स्तुतये । ŚB. on MS. 9. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रिततम्
आमन्त्रित + -तम्<BR>—1 Addressing.<BR>—2 Talk, conversation; V. 2.<BR>—3 The vocative case; संबोधने या प्रथमा सामन्त्रितसंज्ञा स्यात् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्य|आमंत्र्य
आमन्त्र्य <i>pot. p.</i> to be addressed or called to, to be invited &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्यम्
आमन्त्र्य + .{@-त्र्यम्@} A word in the vocative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रः|आमन्त्र|आमंत्रः
आमन्त्रः The castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्द्र|आमंद्र|आमन्द्रः
आमन्द्र <i>a.</i> Having a slightly deep tone, uttering a low, muttering<BR> sound, rumbling; आमन्द्राणाम् फलमविकलं लप्स्यसे गर्जितानाम् Me. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्द्रः|आमन्द्र|आमंद्र
आमन्द्र + .{@-न्द्रः@} A slightly deep tone, rumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयः|आमय|आमयं
आमयः [आ-मी करणे अच्; Tv.; said to be fr. अम् also the word<BR> may also be derived as आमेन अप्यते इति आमयः]<BR>—1 Disease, sickness, distemper; दुःखशोकामयप्रदाः Bg. 17. 9; दर्पामयः<BR> Mv. 4. 22; आमयस्तु रतिरागसंभवः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">Page0345-2</a>]<BR> R. 19. 48; समौ हि शिष्टैराम्नातौ वर्त्स्यन्तावामयः स च Śi. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Damage, hurt, distruction; देवानामिव सैन्यानि सड्ग्रामे तारकामये<BR> Rām. 6. 4. 54.<BR>—3 Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयम्
आमयः + .{@-यम्@} N. of the medical plant Costus Speciosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन् <i>a.</i> [आमय-विन्-निपातः P. V. 2. 122. Vārt.] Sick,<BR> dyspeptic, affected with indigestion; ˚वित्वम् indigestion, dyspepsia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्त|आमरणांत
आमरणान्त, -तिक <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्तिकी
आमरणान्त, -तिक + .({@-की@} <i>f.</i>) Lasting till death, lasting for life, आमरणान्ताः<BR> प्रणयाः कोपास्तत्क्षणभङ्गुराः H. 1. 118; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारो भवेदामरणान्तिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्तिक|आमरणांतिक
आमरणान्त, -तिक <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरीतृ
आमरीतृ <i>m.</i> Ved. A destroyer; न राधस आमरीता मघस्य Rv. 4. 20. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षः|आमर्ष
आमर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR> Anger, wrath, impatience; see अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षणम्
आमर्षः, -र्षणम्<BR> Anger, wrath, impatience; see अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलकः|आमलक|आमलकं
आमलकः, -की<BR>—1 The tree, Emblic Myrobalan, Emblica Officinalis Gaertn (Mar. आंवळा).<BR>—2 N. of another tree (वासक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलकी
आमलकः, -की<BR>—1 The tree, Emblic Myrobalan, Emblica Officinalis Gaertn (Mar. आंवळा).<BR>—2 N. of another tree (वासक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलकम्
आमलकः, -की + .{@-कम्@} Fruit of the Emblic Myrobalan; बदरामलकाम्रदाडिमानाम् Bv. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमहीया
आमहीया <i>f.</i> N. of a particular <i>Ṛk</i> or verse of the Ṛgveda;<BR> (Rv. 8. 48. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमात्यः|आमात्य
आमात्यः [अमात्य एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 A minister, counsellor.<BR>—2 A general; see अमात्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्यम्
आमानस्यम् [अमानस-ष्यञ्] Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमालकः|आमालक
आमालकः A hill-station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्य
आमावास्य <i>a.</i> (-स्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अमावास्या-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the new moon or its festival.<BR>—2 Happening or born at the time of new moon or conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्यम्
आमावास्य + .{@-स्यम्@} The new moon oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षा
आमिक्षा [आमिष्यते सिच्यते, मिष्-सक् Tv.] Curd of milk and whey,<BR> a mixture of boiled and coagulated milk; तप्ते पयसि दध्यानयति सा<BR> वैश्वदेव्यामिक्षा भवति; आज्येन पयसा दध्ना शकृताऽऽमिक्षया त्वचा Mb. 12. 268. 27;<BR> Av. 10. 9. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्ष्यम्
आमिक्ष्यम्, आमिक्षीयम् [आमिक्षा यत्-छ] Curd suitable for<BR> the preparation of Āmikṣā; so आमिक्षीणम् in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षीयम्
आमिक्ष्यम्, आमिक्षीयम् [आमिक्षा यत्-छ] Curd suitable for<BR> the preparation of Āmikṣā; so आमिक्षीणम् in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमित्र
आमित्र <i>a.</i> [अमित्र-अण्] Inimical; odious; छित्वा शरासनं<BR> शत्रोर्नागमामित्रमार्दयत् Mb. 8. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमित्रिः|आमित्रि
आमित्रिः <i>m., f.</i> The child of an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिश्र
आमिश्र, -श्ल <i>a.</i> Readily mixing; स सोम आमिश्लतमः सुते भूद् Rv. 6. 29. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिश्ल
आमिश्र, -श्ल <i>a.</i> Readily mixing; स सोम आमिश्लतमः सुते भूद् Rv. 6. 29. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषम्
आमिषम् [अम् टिषच् दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 1. 46]<BR>—1 Flesh; उपानयत् पिण्डमिवामिषस्य R. 2. 59; यथामिषं जले मत्स्यैर्भक्ष्यते<BR> श्वापदैर्भुवि । आकाशे पक्षिभिश्चैव तथा सर्वत्र वित्तवान् Subhāṣ. (Skanda P.)<BR>—2 (Hence fig.) A prey, victim, object of enjoyment; (राज्यं) रन्ध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां<BR> द्विषामाभिषतां ययौ R. 12. 11 fell a prey &c.; Dk. 164.<BR>—3 Food, bait.<BR>—4 A bribe.<BR>—5 Desire, lust; निरामिषो विनिर्मुक्तः प्रशान्तः सुसुखी भव Mb. 12. 17. 2;<BR> निरपेक्षो निरामिषः Ms. 6. 49.<BR>—6 Enjoyment; pleasing or lovely or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">Page0346-1</a>]<BR> attractive object; नामिषेषु प्रसंगोऽस्ति Mb. 12. 158. 23.<BR>—7 Form.<BR>—8 A leaf.<BR>—9 The fruit of the Jambīra; means of livelihood; आमिषं यच्च पूर्वेषां<BR> राजसं च मलं भृशम् । अनृतं नाम तद्भूतं क्षिप्तेन पृथिवीतले ॥<BR> Rām. 7. 74. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आमिषाशिन्, आमिषप्रियः, आमिषभुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0345-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषाशिन्
आमिषम् + -आशिन् <i>a.</i> carnivorous, eating flesh; दिनोपवासी च निशामिषाशी ।<BR> हास्यार्णवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषप्रियः|आमिषप्रिय
आमिषम् + -प्रियः, -भुज् ‘fond of flesh’, a kind of bird, heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषभुज्
आमिषम् + -प्रियः, -भुज् ‘fond of flesh’, a kind of bird, heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिस्
आमिस् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Raw flesh or meat; Rv. 6. 46. 14.<BR>—2 A dead body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषी
आमिषी N. of a plant (जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीक्षा
आमीक्षा = आमिक्षा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमील्
आमील् €1 P. To close (the eyes); नेत्रे चामीलयन्नेष Kāv. 2. 11;<BR> to shut; चैतन्यमामीलयन् Mv. 2. 22 benumbing; धाराकदम्बरजोवृष्टिषु<BR> चामीलयन् K. 303 being absorbed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीलनम्
आमीलनम् Shutting or closing of the eyes; K. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीलित
आमीलित <i>a.</i> Intensely occupied with, fond of, (cf. Mātaṅga L. 5. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीवत्|आमीवन्त्
आमीवत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Attacking; pushing, pressing; नम आमीवत्केभ्यः<BR> Yaj. Ts. 4. 5. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुकुलित
आमुकुलित <i>a.</i> A little open (as a blossom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुखम्
आमुखम्<BR>—1 Commencement.<BR>—2 (In dramas) A prologue, prelude (प्रस्तावना); (every Sanskrit play<BR> is introduced by आमुख. It is thus defined in S. D. नटी विदूषको<BR> वाऽपि पारिपार्श्वक एव वा । सूत्रधारेण सहिताः संलापं यत्र कुर्वते<BR> ॥ चित्रैर्वाक्यैः स्वकार्योत्थैः प्रस्तुताक्षेपिभिर्मिथः । आमुखं तत्तु विज्ञेयं<BR> नाम्ना प्रस्तावनाऽपि सा ॥ 287.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुखम्
आमुखम् + .{@-खम्@} <i>ind.</i> To the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुच्
आमुच् €6 U.<BR>—1 To loosen, let go.<BR>—2 To wear, tie round or fasten; put on (as a garment &c.); accoutre with;<BR> करोऽयमामुक्तविवाहकौतुकः Ku. 5. 66, 7. 21; आमुञ्चतीवाभरणं<BR> द्वितीयम् R. 13. 21, 12. 86, 16. 74, 17. 25; Ki. 11. 15; आमुञ्चद्वर्म<BR> रत्नाढपम् Bk. 17. 6.<BR>—3 To throw, cast, discharge; आमोक्ष्यन्ते त्वयि कटाक्षान् Me. 37.<BR>—4 To throw or cast off, take off, put aside (as garments &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्त|आमुक्तः
आमुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Loosened, let go, liberated.<BR>—2 Put on, worn &c. आमुक्तमुक्तालतमस्य वक्षः । Śi. see above.<BR>—3 Discharged, cast, shot off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्तम्
आमुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} Armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्तिः|आमुक्ति
आमुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Liberation, being let loose.<BR>—2 Final beatitude.<BR>—3 Putting on, wearing (clothes, ornaments &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्ति|आमुक्तिः
आमुक्तिः + .{@-क्ति@} <i>ind.</i> Till final beatitude is obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोक्षणम्
आमोक्षणम्, -आमोचनम्<BR>—1 Loosening, liberating.<BR>—2 Emitting, shedding, letting forth, discharging.<BR>—3 Putting or tying on; केयूरामोक्षणस्य च Rām. 2. 24. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचनम्
आमोक्षणम्, -आमोचनम्<BR>—1 Loosening, liberating.<BR>—2 Emitting, shedding, letting forth, discharging.<BR>—3 Putting or tying on; केयूरामोक्षणस्य च Rām. 2. 24. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुपः|आमुप
आमुपः The thorny Bamboo; Bambusa Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुर्
आमुर्, -रि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Destroying, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुरि
आमुर्, -रि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Destroying, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्मिक
आमुष्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अमुष्मिन् परलोके भवः ठक्] Belonging to the<BR> next or other world; आमुष्मिकं श्रेयः Suśr.; नैवालोच्य गरीयसीरपि<BR> चिरादामुष्मिकीर्यातनाः S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायण|आमुष्यायणः
आमुष्यायण <i>a.</i> or -णः (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अमुष्य ख्यातस्यापत्यं नडा˚ फक् अलुक्] Well-born,<BR> a son or descendant of such a one; <i>i. e.</i> of an illustrious person<BR> or family; आमुष्यायणो वै त्वमसि Śat. Br.; तदामुष्यायणस्य तत्रभवतः<BR> सुगृहीतनाम्नो भट्टगोपालस्य पौत्रः Māl. 1; Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायणः|आमुष्यायण
आमुष्यायण <i>a.</i> or -णः (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अमुष्य ख्यातस्यापत्यं नडा˚ फक् अलुक्] Well-born,<BR> a son or descendant of such a one; <i>i. e.</i> of an illustrious person<BR> or family; आमुष्यायणो वै त्वमसि Śat. Br.; तदामुष्यायणस्य तत्रभवतः<BR> सुगृहीतनाम्नो भट्टगोपालस्य पौत्रः Māl. 1; Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायणी
आमुष्यायण <i>a.</i> or -णः (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अमुष्य ख्यातस्यापत्यं नडा˚ फक् अलुक्] Well-born,<BR> a son or descendant of such a one; <i>i. e.</i> of an illustrious person<BR> or family; आमुष्यायणो वै त्वमसि Śat. Br.; तदामुष्यायणस्य तत्रभवतः<BR> सुगृहीतनाम्नो भट्टगोपालस्य पौत्रः Māl. 1; Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृण
आमृण <i>a.</i> Vulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृद्
आमृद् €9 P.<BR>—1 To crush by rubbing.<BR>—2 To crumple.<BR>—3 To press, squeeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दः|आमर्द
आमर्दः<BR>—1 Crushing.<BR>—2 Roughly handling; अर्धपीतस्तनं मातुरामर्दक्लिष्टकेशरम् Ś. 7. 14.<BR>—3 Pressing, squeezing.<BR>—4 N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दिन्|आमर्द्दिन्
आमर्दिन् <i>a.</i> Crushing, pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृश्
आमृश् €6 P.<BR>—1 to touch; handle (roughly), lay hands upon; नवातपामृष्टसरोजचारुभिः<BR> Ki. 4. 14; (ताम्) मुहुरामृशन्भृगधरोऽग्रकरैः Śi. 9. 34; शरासनज्यां<BR> मुहुराममर्श Ku. 3. 64; K. 163; Dk. 71; Ś. 7. 2.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To seize upon, eat, eat up; R. 5. 9.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To attack, assail; आमृष्टं नः परैः पदम् Ku. 2. 31.<BR>—3 To rub, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्शः|आमर्श
आमर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Touching, close contact.<BR>—2 Rubbing, wiping.<BR>—3 Counsel, advice.<BR>—4 Disposition of the mind (मनोवृत्ति); विद्वान्स्वप्न इवामर्शसाक्षिणं<BR> विररामह Bhāg. 4. 28. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्शनम्
आमर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Touching, close contact.<BR>—2 Rubbing, wiping.<BR>—3 Counsel, advice.<BR>—4 Disposition of the mind (मनोवृत्ति); विद्वान्स्वप्न इवामर्शसाक्षिणं<BR> विररामह Bhāg. 4. 28. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृष्ट
आमृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Touched, attacked, seized &c.<BR>—2 Sweetened, made delicious; तैरामृष्टशुचो लोकाः Bhāg. 10. 40. 16; Pt. 4.<BR>—3 Rubbed, struck against; Ś. 7. 2.<BR>—4 Wiped, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमेन्य
आमेन्य <i>a.</i> To be measured from all sides; to be reached with an<BR> arrow or bolt (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोगः
आमोगः An ending verse containing the poetʼs name (यत्रैव कविनाम<BR> स्यात् स आमोग इतीरितः इति संगीतदामोदरः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोटनम्
आमोटनम् Crushing; Māl. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद <i>a.</i> Gladdening, cheering up, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदः|आमोद
आमोद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Joy, pleasure, delight; आमोदं परमं जग्मुः Rām.<BR>—2 Fragrance (diffusive), perfume; आमोदमुपजिघ्नन्तौ स्वनिःश्वासानुकारिणम्<BR> R. 1. 43; आमोदं कुसुमभवं मृदेव धत्ते मृद्गन्धं न हि कुमुमानि धारयन्ति<BR> Subhāṣ.; आमोदकर्मव्यतिहारमीयुः Śi. 2. 20; Me. 31.<BR>—3 Strong smell; आमोदो न हि कस्तूर्याः शपथेन प्रकाश्यते Subhāṣ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आमोदजननी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदजननी
आमोद + -जननी ‘causing a strong smell’, betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदन|आमोदनं
आमोदन <i>a.</i> Delighting, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदनम्
आमोदन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Delighting, rejoicing; अभुञ्जतामोदनमोदनं जनाः N.<BR>—2 Making fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदित|आमोदितः
आमोदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pleased, delighted.<BR>—2 Made fragrant, scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
आमोदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Happy, delighted.<BR>—2 Fragrant; fragrant or perfumed with; oft. at the end of comp.; नवकुटजकदम्बामोदिनो<BR> गन्धवाहाः Bh. 1. 35. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदी
आमोदिन् + .({@-दी@}) A perfume for the mouth (made in the form of a pill of camphor &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0346-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदकः
आमोदकः A seed of the Dill kind, Lingusticum Ajwaen (Mar. ओंवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोष|आमोषः
आमोष <i>a.</i> Robbing, stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषः|आमोष
आमोष + .{@-षः@} Theft, robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषिन्
आमोषिन् <i>m.</i> A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोहनिका
आमोहनिका A kind of fragrant odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ना
आम्ना €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To hand down traditionally or in sacred texts; भवत्प्रणीतमाचारमामनन्ति<BR> हि साधवः Ku. 6. 31; एवं किल सूत्रकारा आमनन्ति Māl. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Hence, to regard, consider, mention, lay down; सर्वे वेदा यत्पदमामनन्ति<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 2. 15. त्वामामनन्ति प्रकृतिं पुरुषार्थ प्रवर्तिनीम् Ku. 2. 13, 5. 81;<BR> M. 1. 4; Bk. 18. 5; Kām. 8. 24; U. 5; Mv. 4. 30.<BR>—2 To keep in mind, commit to memory, learn, study, repeat; आमनन्मन्त्रमुत्तमम्<BR> Bk. 17. 30; यद् ब्रह्म सम्यगाम्रातम् Ku. 6. 16 learnt.<BR>—3 To celebrate, hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नात
आम्नात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Considered, regarded, said to be; समौ हि शिष्टैराम्नातौ वर्त्स्यन्तावामयः<BR> स (शत्रुः) च Śi. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Studied, repeated.<BR>—3 Remembered, kept in mind.<BR>—4 Handed down in sacred texts or traditionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नातम्
आम्नात + .{@-तम्@} Study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नातिन्
आम्नातिन् <i>a.</i> [आम्नात-इनि] One who has studied the Vedas; आम्नातिनी<BR> नीतिषु बुद्धिमद्भिः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नानम्
आम्नानम् [आ-म्ना-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Recitation or study of the sacred texts or Vedas.<BR>—2 Mention; repetition in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायः|आम्नाय
आम्नायः [आ-म्ना-घञ्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Sacred tradition, sacred texts handed down by tradition or repetition.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Hence, the Veda, Vedas taken collectively (including Brāhmaṇas,<BR> Upaniṣads and Āraṇyakas also); अधीती चतुर्ष्वाम्नायेषु Dk. 120; आम्नायवचनं<BR> सत्यमित्ययं लोकसंग्रहः । आम्नायेभ्यः पुनर्वेदाः प्रसृताः सर्वतोमुखाः ॥<BR> Mb.; Ki. 11. 39.<BR>—2 Study (by repetition); अनाम्नायमला वेदा ब्राह्मणस्याव्रतं मलम्<BR> Mb. 12. 328. 20.<BR>—3 A sacred text or precept in general; आम्नायादन्यत्र नूतनश्छन्दसामवतारः U. 4.<BR>—4 Traditional usage, family or national customs; U. 6.<BR>—5 Received doctrine.<BR>—6 Advice or instruction (in past and present usage).<BR>—7 A Tantra.<BR>—8 A series of families.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आम्नायसारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायसारिन्
आम्नायः + -सारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 pious, observing the traditional usages.<BR>—2 containing the essence of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायवत्
आम्नायवत् <i>a.</i> Attended with, or learnt by, traditional instruction; U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बरीषपुत्रकः|आम्बरीषपुत्रक|आंबरीषपुत्रकः
आम्बरीषपुत्रकः A country inhabited by the Ambarīṣaputras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बष्ठः|आम्बष्ठ|आंबष्ठः
आम्बष्ठः An inhabitant of Ambaṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बिकेयः|आम्बिकेय|आंबिकेयः
आम्बिकेयः [अम्बिकाया अपत्यं ढक्] An epithet of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Dhṛtarāṣṭra; न मे तच्च श्रुतवानाम्बिकेयः Mb. 3. 5. 14.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भस|आंभस
आम्भस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अम्भस्-अण्] Watery, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भसिक|आंभसिक|आम्भसिकः
आम्भसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अम्भसी वर्तते ठक्] Acquatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भसिकः|आम्भसिक|आंभसिक
आम्भसिक + .{@-कः@} A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रः|आम्र
आम्रः [अम् गत्यादिषु रन् दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 2. 16.] The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रम्
आम्रः + .{@-म्रम्@} The fruit of the mango tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आम्रास्थि, आम्रावर्त, आम्रकूटः, आम्रगन्धकः, आम्रनिशा, आम्रपञ्चमः, आम्रपाली, आम्रपेशी, आम्रफलप्रपाणकम्, आम्रवण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रास्थि
आम्रः + -अस्थि The seed of the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावर्त|आम्रावर्त्त|आम्रावर्त्तः
आम्रः + -आवर्त<BR>—1 N. of a tree (आम्रातक).<BR>—2 inspissated mango juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावर्तम्
आम्रः + -आवर्त + .({@-र्तम्@}) the fruit of आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रकूटः|आम्रकूट
आम्रः + -कूटः N. of a mountain; सानुमानाम्रकूटः Me. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रगन्धकः|आम्रगन्धक
आम्रः + -गन्धकः N. of a plant (समष्ठिलवृक्ष; Mar. सुरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रनिशा
आम्रः + -निशा N. of the plant Curcuma Reclinata (Mar. आंबेहळद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रपञ्चमः|आम्रपञ्चम
आम्रः + -पञ्चमः A particular Rāga in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रपाली
आम्रः + -पाली <i>f.</i> N. of a prostitute famous for her beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रपेशी
आम्रः + -पेशी [आम्रस्य पेशीव] a portion of dried mango fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रफलप्रपाणकम्
आम्रः + -फलप्रपाणकम् A cooling drink made of mangoes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रवण
आम्रः + -वण [आम्रस्य वनम् cf. P. VIII. 4. 5] a grove of mango trees;<BR> सोऽहमाम्रवणं छित्त्वा Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातः|आम्रात
आम्रातः [आम्रम् आम्ररसम् अतति अत्-अच् Tv.] The hog-plum, Spondias<BR> Mangifera (its juice resembling that of the mango. Mar. आंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातम्
आम्रातः + .{@-तम्@} The fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातकः|आम्रातक
आम्रातकः<BR>—1 The hog plum.<BR>—2 Inspissated mango juice (Mar. साट); आम्रस्य सहकारस्य कटे<BR> विस्तारितो रसः । घर्मशुष्को मुहुर्दत्त आम्रातक इति स्मृतः ॥ Bhāva P.<BR>—3 N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावती
आम्रावती N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रिमन्
आम्रिमन् <i>m.</i> Acid taste; see Gaṇa to P. V. 1. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेड्
आम्रेड् <i>Caus.</i> To repeat; एतदेव यदा वाक्यमाम्रेडयति देवराट् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडनम्
आम्रेडनम् Tautology; repetition of words or sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडित|आम्रेडितं
आम्रेडित <i>p. p.</i> Reiterated, repeated (as words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडितम्
आम्रेडित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Repetition of sound or word.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Reduplication, the second word in reduplication; द्वितीयाम्रेडितान्तेषु Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लः|आम्ल
आम्लः, -म्ला<BR> The tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ला
आम्लः, -म्ला<BR> The tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लम्
आम्लः, -म्ला + .{@-म्लम्@} Sourness, acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लपञ्चकम्
आम्लः, -म्ला + .{@-पञ्चकम्@} The aggregate of the five following Ziziphus Jujuba<BR> (Mar. बोर), Pomegranate (Mar. डाळिंब), Mangosteen (Mar. कोकंब),<BR> Tamarind (Mar. चिंच), Averrhoa Carambola (Mar. करमर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लवेतसः|आम्लवेतस
आम्लः, -म्ला + .{@-वेतसः@} N. of the plant Rumex Vesicarius (Mar. चुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लिका
आम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>—1 The tamarind tree.<BR>—2 Acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लीका
आम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>—1 The tamarind tree.<BR>—2 Acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयः|आय
आयः [आ-इ-अच्, अय्-घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Arrival, approach; आये वामस्य संगथे रयीणाम् Rv. 2. 38. 10.<BR>—2 Gaining or acquisition of money, acquiring (opp. व्यय); आये<BR> दुःखं व्यये दुःखं धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1. 163.<BR>—3 Income, revenue; receipt; ग्रामेषु स्वामिग्राह्यो भाग आयः Sk.; Y. 1. 322, 327;<BR> Mk. 2. 6; आयद्वाराणि Dk. 162 sources of income; आयव्ययौ<BR> च नियतावाकरान् कोषमेव च Ms. 8. 419; आयाधिकं व्ययं करोति<BR> he lives beyond his means.<BR>—4 Gain, profit.<BR>—5 The eleventh house (in astrology).<BR>—6 The guard of the womenʼs apartments.<BR>—7 Means, source; मार्गत्यायशतैरर्थान् Mb. 13. 163. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आयदर्शिन्, आयमुखम्, आयव्ययौ, आयशरीरम्, आयस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयदर्शिन्
आयः + -दर्शिन् seeing (<i>i. e.</i> having) revenues, revenue-collector; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयमुखम्
आयः + -मुखम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">Page0348-1</a>]<BR> Forms of revenue; Kau. A. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0347-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयव्ययौ
आयः + -व्ययौ (dual) receipt and disbursement, income and expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयशरीरम्
आयः + -शरीरम् Body of income; Kau. A. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्थानम्
आयः + -स्थानम् a place where revenues are collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयकस्कम्भः
आयकस्कम्भः A kind of pillar (cf. Māna.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Coming, approaching; ˚वसु one to whom good<BR> or wealth comes; Av. 13. 4. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतीगवम्
आयतीगवम् <i>ind.</i> At the time when cows return home; आतिष्ठेद्गु<BR> जपन् सन्ध्यां प्रकान्तामायतीगवम् Bk. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयनम्
आयनम्^1 Ved. Coming, approaching.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter noun missing 'm'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयिन्
आयिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Coming or driving near, Yaj. Ts. 2. 47. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिक|आयःशूलिकः
आयःशूलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अयःशूल-ठक् P. V. 2. 76]. Active, diligent, indefatigable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिकः|आयःशूलिक
आयःशूलिक + .{@-कः@} A man who, in order to gain an object, uses forcible instead<BR> of gentle means (तीक्ष्णोपायेन योऽन्विच्छेत्स आयःशूलिको जनः); cf.<BR> K. P. 10; अयःशूलेन अन्विच्छति (scil. अर्थान्) इत्यायःशूलिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्
आयज् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To honour, worship (the gods).<BR>—2 To give, present, furnish, supply.<BR>—3 To consecrate, ordain, dedicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजि
आयजि, आयजिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Performing sacrifices from all<BR> sides; procuring, granting; आयजी वाजसातमा Rv. 1. 28. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजिन्
आयजि, आयजिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Performing sacrifices from all<BR> sides; procuring, granting; आयजी वाजसातमा Rv. 1. 28. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजिष्ठ
आयजिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Sacrificing or procuring best; यष्टा देवाँ आयजिष्ठः<BR> स्वास्ति Rv. 2. 9. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्यु
आयज्यु <i>a.</i> Inclined to sacrifice; आयज्यवः सुमतिं विश्ववारा Rv. 9. 97. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयागः|आयाग
आयागः A gift given at a sacrifice; ˚भूत <i>a.</i> obtained by sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To strive, endeavour.<BR>—2 To rest or depend on, rest with (with loc.); वयं त्वय्यायतामहे<BR> Mv. 1. 49 (v. l.); 3. 34; Dk. 42.<BR>—3 To arrive, come to, reach, dwell (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनम्
आयतनम् [आयतन्तेऽत्र, यत् आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Place, abode, house, resting-place; भूमेर्महदायतनं वृष्णीष्व<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 1. 23. (fig. also); शूलायतनाः Mu. 7 hangmen; स्नेहस्तदेकायतनं<BR> जगाम Ku. 7. 5 was centred in her; R. 3. 36; सर्वाविनयानामेकैकमप्येषामायतनम्<BR> K. 103; ˚मृगेण 130 domestic deer; Cāṇ. 32; (hence) a receptacle,<BR> home, support, seat.<BR>—2 The place of the sacred fire, altar, shed for sacrifices.<BR>—3 A sanctuary, sacred place; as in देवायतनम्, मठायतनम् &c. यथाकमविशेषेण<BR> सर्वाण्यायतनानि च । दर्शितानि Mb. 13. 156. 11; विजने वायतने गिरौ<BR> वने वा । Bu. C. 5. 19.<BR>—4 The site of a house, ground-plot.<BR>—5 A barn; Y. 2. 154.<BR>—6 An inner seat (with Buddhists who consider the five senses with <i>manas</i><BR> as the six Āyatanas).<BR>—7 The cause of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनत्वम्
आयतनत्वम् State of being an altar or seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनवत्|आयतनवन्त्
आयतनवत् <i>a.</i> Having a certain seat or home. ━<i>m.</i> N. of the<BR> fourth foot of Brahmā; य एतमेवं विद्वाँश्चतुष्कलं पादं ब्रह्मण<BR> आयतनवानित्युपास्ते Ch. Up. 4. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्त|आयत्तः
आयत्त <i>p. p.</i> [आ-यत्-क्त]<BR>—1 Dependent on, resting with (with loc. or in comp.); दैवायत्तं कुले<BR> जन्म मदायत्तं तु पौरुषम् Ve. 3. 33; भाग्यायत्तमतः परम् Ś. 4. 17.<BR>—2 Docile, tractable.<BR>—3 Attempted, tried; प्रहस्तः परमायत्तस्ततः सुस्राव शोणितम् Rām. 6. 58. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तता
आयत्त + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} dependence, humility, docility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तत्वम्
आयत्त + .{@˚ता, -त्वम्@} dependence, humility, docility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तिः|आयत्ति
आयत्तिः <i>f.</i> [आ-यत्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Dependence, subjection.<BR>—2 Affection.<BR>—3 Strength, power, might.<BR>—4 Boundary, limit.<BR>—5 An expedient, remedy.<BR>—6 Majesty, dignity.<BR>—7 A day.<BR>—8 Steadiness of conduct, continuance in the right path.<BR>—9 Length.<BR>—10 Future time (These two senses should perhaps be referred to आयति q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथातथ्यम्
आयथातथ्यम् Unfitness, unsuitableness, impropriety; गुणानामायथातथ्यादर्थं<BR> विप्लावयन्ति ये Śi. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथापुर्यम्
आयथापुर्यम्, -पूर्व्यम्<BR> The state of being not as formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथापूर्व्यम्
आयथापुर्यम्, -पूर्व्यम्<BR> The state of being not as formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयन|आयनं
आयन <i>a.</i> Belonging to the solistice (as in उत्तरायण, दक्षिणायन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्
आयम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To extend, lengthen out, stretch out; वस्त्रं-पाणिं-आयच्छते Sk.;<BR> स्वाङ्गमायच्छमानः Ś. 4, v. l.; आयच्छति कूपाद्रज्जुम् Sk. draws<BR> up; बाणमुद्यतमायसीत् Bk. 6. 119 stretched out.<BR>—2 To restrain, draw in (as breath &c.); त्रिरायम्य शनैरसून् Ms. 3. 217, 11. 100;<BR> प्राणानायम्य Y. 1. 24.<BR>—3 To stretch oneself, to grow long (Ātm.); P. I. 3. 28.<BR>—4 To grasp, possess; श्रियमायच्छमानाभिः Bk. 8. 46.<BR>—5 To bring or lead towards. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To lengthen, stretch, spread or draw out.<BR>—2 To remove, transplant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत|आयतः
आयत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Long; दशाङ्गुलमायता यष्टिः a stick ten fingers long; शतमध्यर्धं<BR> (योजनं) आयता Mb.; ˚स्वभावानि च दुःखानि K. 175 lasting.<BR>—2 Diffuse, prolix.<BR>—3 Big, large, great; Pt. 1.<BR>—4 Drawn, attracted.<BR>—5 Long drawn, distant; high-pitched; स्वचित्तायतनिःस्वनम् Rām. 1. 4. 33.<BR>—6 Curbed, restrained.<BR>—7 Asleep; तं नायतं बोधयेदित्याहुः Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतः|आयत
आयत + .{@-तः@} An oblong (in geometry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतम्
आयत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Deeply, long; मैथिलीमाहृतां दृष्ट्वा ध्यात्वा निःश्वस्य<BR> चायतम् Rām. 6. 111. 71.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आयताक्ष, आयतेक्षण, आयतनेत्र, आयतलोचन, आयतापाङ्ग, आयतार्धः, आयतायतिः, आयतच्छदा, आयतलेख, आयतस्तूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयताक्ष
आयत + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतेक्षण
आयत + -ईक्षण, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> (a woman) with large eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनेत्र
आयत + -ईक्षण, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> (a woman) with large eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतलोचन
आयत + -ईक्षण, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> (a woman) with large eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतापाङ्ग|आयतापांग
आयत + -अपाङ्ग <i>a.</i> having long cornered eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतार्धः|आयतार्ध
आयत + -अर्धः half an oblong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतायतिः|आयतायति
आयत + -आयतिः <i>f.</i> long-continuance, remote futurity; सा विभूतिरनुभावसम्पदां<BR> भूयसी तव यदायतायतिः Śi. 14. 5. चतुरस्र, दीर्घचतुरस्र <i>a.</i> Oblong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतच्छदा
आयत + -च्छदा a plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतलेख
आयत + -लेख <i>a.</i> long-curved; कान्तिर्भ्रुवोरायतलेखयोर्या Ku. 1. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतस्तूः
आयत + -स्तूः <i>m.</i> [आयतं स्तौति, नि˚ पा˚ दीर्घः] a panegyrist, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिः|आयति
आयतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Length, extension; Mb. 5. 166. 3; stretching, extending; तेषां देवेष्वायतिरस्माकं<BR> तेषु नाभयः Rv. 1. 139. 9.<BR>—2 Future time, the future; आयतिप्रदर्शनम्; Kau. A. 2. 10.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">Page0349-1</a>]<BR> ˚भङ्ग K. 55 (length also), 58; Dk. 29; भूयसी तव यदायतायतिः<BR> Śi. 14. 5; रहयत्यापदुपेतमायतिः Ki. 2. 14; Ms. 7. 169; अनायतिक्षमं<BR> वचः Pt. 3. 111 imprudent, not good for the future; ˚ग्लानिभीतः<BR> Mu. 4. 12; स्थिर˚ Ki. 1. 23 permanent.<BR>—3 Future consequence or result; आयतिं सर्वकार्याणां तदात्वं च विवारयेत्<BR> Ms. 7. 178; Ki. 1. 15, 2. 43, 3. 43; Ki. 4. 21; fruit-yielding season.<BR>—4 Majesty, dignity; आयतीमिव विध्वस्ताम् Rām. 5. 19. 12.<BR>—5 Stretching the hand, accepting, obtaining.<BR>—6 Work (कर्मन्); यथा मित्रं ध्रुवं लब्ध्वा कृशमप्यायतिक्षमम्<BR> Ms. 7. 208 (कर्मक्षमम् Kull.).<BR>—7 Connection, junction.<BR>—8 Meeting, union.<BR>—9 Source, descent; तदायतिः Dk. 154 descended from him.<BR>—10 Restraint (of mind).<BR>—11 Arrival; उत्पत्तिमायतिं स्थानं विभुत्वं चैव पञ्चधा Praśna. Up. 3. 12.<BR>—12 A long line, succession; द्रक्ष्यन्ति समरे योधाः शलभानामिवायतीः<BR> Mb. 7. 159. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0348-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिमत्
आयतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Long, extended.<BR>—2 Dignified, majestic, stately.<BR>—3 Self-restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयन्तृ|आयंतृ
आयन्तृ <i>m.</i> Ved. One who approaches, one who fastens or raises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयमनम्
आयमनम्<BR>—1 Length, extension.<BR>—2 Restraint, curbing.<BR>—3 Stretching (as a bow); दृढस्य धनुष आयमनम् Ch. Up. 1. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामः|आयाम
आयामः [आ-यम्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Length; तिर्यगायामशोभी Me. 59.<BR>—2 Expansion, extension; Ki. 7. 6.<BR>—3 Stretching, extending.<BR>—4 Restraint, control, stopping; प्राणायामपरायणाः Bg. 4. 29; प्राणायामः<BR> परं तपः Ms. 2. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामवत्|आयामवन्त्
आयामवत् <i>a.</i> Extended, long; चित्रन्यस्तमिवाचलं हयशिरस्यायामवच्चामरम्<BR> V. 1. 4; Śi. 12. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामित
आयामित <i>a.</i> Stretched out, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामिन्
आयामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who restrains.<BR>—2 Long (in space or time); K. 25, 55; ˚यामासु Ki. 11. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयल्लकः|आयल्लक|आयल्लकं
आयल्लकः Impatience, longing; गाढायल्लकदुःसहामिव दशां धत्ते<BR> गजानां पतिः Nāg. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवनम्
आयवनम् Ved. A spoon for stirring or any similar implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवसः|आयवस|आयवसं
आयवसः, -सम्<BR> Pasture-ground, place for feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवसम्
आयवसः, -सम्<BR> Pasture-ground, place for feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्
आयस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To exert oneself; पिण्डार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>—2 To weary oneself, become exhausted or fatigued; नायस्यसि तपस्यन्ती<BR> Bk. 6. 69, 14. 104, 15. 54. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To trouble, afflict; आयासयति मां जलाभिलाषः K. 35; Mu. 7. 8; V. 2.<BR>—2 To weary, tire out, worry.<BR>—3 To injure, affect; lessen, diminish; नाऽऽयासयन्त संत्रस्ता Bk. 8. 61.<BR>—4 To string (as a bow); अनायासितकार्मुकः Pt. 1. 385.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आयस्त <i>p. p.</i> [यस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR>—2 Hurt, injured, killed; नित्यायस्तो बालको (न ईशे) Mb. 13. 1. 26.<BR>—3 Vexed, angry.<BR>—4 Effected with difficulty.<BR>—5 Thrown, cast, sent forth.<BR>—6 Sharpened, whetted.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">Page0349-2</a>]<BR>—7 (Actively used) Toiling, labouring, exerting oneself.<BR>—8 Eager, anxiously desirous; आयस्तः (संप्राप्तुम्) Ki. 7. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्तम्
आयस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} A great effort; न मे गर्वितमायस्तं सहिष्यति दुरात्मवान्<BR> Rām. 4. 16. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासः|आयास
आयासः [आ-यस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Effort, exertion, trouble, difficulty, pain, labour; बहुलायास<BR> Bg. 18. 24; cf. अनायास also.<BR>—2 Fatigue, weariness; स्नेहमूलानि दुःखानि देहजानि भयानि च । शोकहर्षौ<BR> तथायासः सर्वं स्नेहात् प्रवर्तते ॥ Mb.<BR>—3 Mental pain, anguish; सा विनीय तमायासम् Rām. 2. 25. 1; अपूर्वः<BR> खलु अस्य आयासः Pratimā 1.<BR>—4 Unsteadiness, wavering; आत्मज्ञानमनायासस्तितिक्षा धर्मनित्यता Mb. 5. 34. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासक
आयासक <i>a.</i> [आ-यस्-ण्वुल्] Causing fatigue, wearisome; troublesome;<BR> एतस्माद्विरमेन्द्रियार्थगहनादायासकात् Bh. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आयासिन् <i>a.</i> [आ-यस्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Exhausted, fatigued.<BR>—2 Making exertions, striving; मनस्तु तद्भावदर्शनायासि Ś. 2. 1, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>) [अयसो विकारः अण्]<BR>—1 Made of iron, iron, metallic; शतं मा पुर आयसीररक्षन् Ait. Up. 4. 5.<BR> आयसं दण्डमेव वा Ms. 8. 315; सखि मा जल्प तवायसी<BR> रसज्ञा Bv. 2. 59.<BR>—2 Armed with an iron weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयसी
आयस + .{@-सी@} A coat of mail, an armour for the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयसम्
आयस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Iron; मूढं बुद्धमिवात्मानं हैमीभूतमिवायसम् Ku. 6. 55; स चकर्ष<BR> परस्मात्तदयस्कान्त इवायसम् R. 17. 63.<BR>—2 Anything made of iron.<BR>—3 A weapon.<BR>—4 A wind instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्कारः|आयस्कार
आयस्कारः The upper part of the thigh of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आया
आया €2 P.<BR>—1 To come, arrive, approach.<BR>—2 To reach, attain, go to (any particular state); क्षयम्, वशम्, बन्धनम्,<BR> तुलाम् &c. ब्राह्मणो निर्वेदमायात् Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 12; आयातु वरदा<BR> देवी Mahānār. Up. 15. 1.<BR>—3 To follow, result.<BR>—4 To be possible or practicable (with inf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयात|आयातं
आयात <i>a.</i> Come, approached; आयाता मधुयामिनी यदि पुनर्नायात<BR> एव प्रभुः Ś. Til.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयातम्
आयात + .{@-तम्@} Excess, superabundance (उद्रेक); रागायाते Ki. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयातिः|आयाति
आयातिः <i>f.</i> [आ-या-क्तिन्] Coming near, arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयानम्
आयानम्<BR>—1 Coming, arrival; अस्मिन्ना वामायाने वाजिनीवसू Rv. 8. 22. 18.<BR>—2 Natural temperament, disposition, nature.<BR>—3 An ornament of the horse; Hc. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयापनम्
आयापनम् Causing to come, inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाचित
आयाचित <i>a.</i> Urgently requested or asked for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयिकपादः
आयिकपादः A kind of pillar (cf. Māna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयु|आयुः
आयु <i>a.</i> [इ-ठण् Uṇ. 1. 2] Ved. Living, going, movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुः|आयु
आयु + .{@-युः@}<BR>—1 A living being, man.<BR>—2 Mankind, human race.<BR>—3 Living beings taken collectively.<BR>—4 The first man.<BR>—5 Life, duration of life.<BR>—6 Wind, अहं केशरिणः क्षेत्रे वायुना जगदायुना Mb.<BR>—7 A son, descendant, offspring.<BR>—8 The son of Purūravas and Urvaśī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आयुषक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुषक्
आयु + -षक् <i>a.</i> attached to; joined with men; सोमः पवत आयुषक् Rv. 9. 25. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0349-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुज्
आयुज् €7 U. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To join, fasten or tie, yoke (to anything).<BR>—2 To appoint.<BR>—3 To fix or direct (the mind) towards; आयोजितस्तपस्यात्मा K. 173. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fix, or place; मालाः कदम्बनवकेसरकेतकीभिरायोजिताः शिरसि<BR> बिभ्रति योषितोऽद्य Ṛs. 2. 21.<BR>—2 To make or form; कुसुमायोजितकार्मुको मधुः Ku. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्त|आयुक्तः
आयुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Appointed, charged with (with gen. or loc.); ये तत्र ब्राह्मणाः संमर्शिनः<BR> युक्ता आयुक्ताः T. Up. 1. 11. 4. कुशलोऽन्वेषणस्याहमायुक्तो दूतकर्मणि Bk. 8. 115.<BR>—2 United, joined, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्तः|आयुक्त
आयुक्त + .{@-क्तः@}<BR>—1 A minister, an agent or deputy.<BR>—2 Provincial governor, according to lexicons; possibly a treasury-officer,<BR> in inscriptions (GI. p. 6 ff.; EI. XX. 61 ff.; EI. XXIII, pp. 159 ff. &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगः|आयोग
आयोगः<BR>—1 Appointment, entrusting one with something.<BR>—2 Action, performance of an act.<BR>—3 Offering flowers, perfumes &c.<BR>—4 A shore or bank; a quay to which boats are attached.<BR>—5 Connection, union; स देशो भ्रमरायोगः प्रदीप इव लक्ष्यते Rām.<BR>—6 Obstruction (रोध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजनम्
आयोजनम्<BR>—1 Joining.<BR>—2 Taking, seizing.<BR>—3 Collecting.<BR>—4 Effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुत
आयुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mixed, mingled.<BR>—2 Melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुतम्
आयुत + .{@-तम्@} Half-melted butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध्
आयुध् €4 Ā. To fight with, attack, oppose. ━<i>Caus.</i> To oppose,<BR> attack, fight with; रथिनः पादचारमायोधयन्ति U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधः|आयुध|आयुधं
आयुधः, -धम्<BR> [आयुध्-घञ्र्थे क]<BR>—1 A weapon, shield &c.; it is of 3 kinds (1) प्रहरण, <i>e. g.</i><BR> a sword; (2) हस्तमुक्त, <i>e. g.</i> a disc; (3) यन्त्रमुक्त, <i>e. g.</i><BR> an arrow; आयुधानामहं वज्रम् Bg. 10. 28. न मे त्वदन्येन<BR> विसोढमायुधम् R. 3. 63. An implement; वशाया यज्ञ आयुधम् Av. 10. 10. 18.<BR>—2 A vessel (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधम्
आयुधः, -धम्<BR> [आयुध्-घञ्र्थे क]<BR>—1 A weapon, shield &c.; it is of 3 kinds (1) प्रहरण, <i>e. g.</i><BR> a sword; (2) हस्तमुक्त, <i>e. g.</i> a disc; (3) यन्त्रमुक्त, <i>e. g.</i><BR> an arrow; आयुधानामहं वज्रम् Bg. 10. 28. न मे त्वदन्येन<BR> विसोढमायुधम् R. 3. 63. An implement; वशाया यज्ञ आयुधम् Av. 10. 10. 18.<BR>—2 A vessel (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधम्
आयुधः, -धम् + .{@-धम्@}<BR>—1 Gold used for ornaments.<BR>—2 (pl.) Water (Ved.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आयुधागारम्, आयुधागारम्, आयुधागारिकः, आयुधजीविन्, आयुधधर्मिणी, आयुधपालः, आयुधपिशाचिका, आयुधशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागारम्
आयुधः + -आगारम्, -अगारम् an armoury, arsenal; अहमप्यायुधागारं प्रविश्यायुधसहायो भवामि Ve. 1; Ms. 9. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागारम्
आयुधः + -आगारम्, -अगारम् an armoury, arsenal; अहमप्यायुधागारं प्रविश्यायुधसहायो भवामि Ve. 1; Ms. 9. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागारिकः|आयुधागारिक
आयुधः + -आगारिकः Governor of an arsenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधजीविन्
आयुधः + -जीविन् <i>a.</i> living by oneʼs weapon. (<i>m.</i>) a warrior, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधधर्मिणी|आयुधधर्म्मिणी
आयुधः + -धर्मिणी the tree called जयन्ती (रोगनाशने तस्या आयुधधर्मत्वात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधपालः|आयुधपाल
आयुधः + -पालः the governor of an arsenal; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधपिशाचिका
आयुधः + -पिशाचिका ‘devil of arms’, devilish warlike spirit; Mv. 3; A. R. 4; B. R. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधशाला
आयुधः + -शाला see आयुधागार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक <i>a.</i> Relating to arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिकः|आयुधिक
आयुधिक + .{@-कः@} [आयुधेन जीवनि ठञ्] A soldier, warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिन्
आयुधिन्, -आयुधीय <i>a.</i><BR> [आयुध-इनि-छ] Bearing or using weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधिन्, -आयुधीय <i>a.</i><BR> [आयुध-इनि-छ] Bearing or using weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधी
आयुधिन्, -आयुधीय + .{@-धी, -धीयः@} A warrior; शिक्षाशाक्तिं प्राहरन् दर्शयन्तो मुक्तामुक्तैरायुधैरायुधीयाः Śi. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीयः|आयुधीय
आयुधिन्, -आयुधीय + .{@-धी, -धीयः@} A warrior; शिक्षाशाक्तिं प्राहरन् दर्शयन्तो मुक्तामुक्तैरायुधैरायुधीयाः Śi. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधनम्
आयोधनम्<BR>—1 A battle, fight, war; आयोधने कृष्णगतिं सहायम् R. 6. 42; आयोधनाग्रसरतां<BR> त्वयि वीर याते 5. 71.<BR>—2 Battle-field; प्रविश्यायोधनं घोरं विचिन्वन्त्यो हतं पतिम् Rām. 6. 110. 3.<BR> प्रययौ तूर्णमायोधनं प्रति Mb. विचित्रमभिवर्तते भुवनभीममायोजनम् U. 6.<BR>—3 Slaughter, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस् <i>n.</i> [इ-असि-णिच्च Uṇ. 2. 117] —1 Life, duration of life;<BR> दीर्घमायुः R. 9. 62, 12. 48; तक्षकेणापि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">Page0350-2</a>]<BR> दष्टस्य आयुर्मर्माणि रक्षति H. 2. 16; आयुर्वर्षशतं नृणां परिमितम्<BR> Bh. 3. 107, शतायुर्वै पुरुषः Ait. Br.; प्राणो हि भूतानामायुः । तस्मात्सर्वायुषमुच्यते<BR> सर्वमेव त आयुर्यान्ति T. Up. 2. 3. 1.<BR>—2 Vital power.<BR>—3 Food.<BR>—4 N. of a ceremony called आयुष्टोम performed to secure long life,<BR> together with the गो and ज्योतिस् part of the अभिप्लव ceremony.<BR> (In comp. the final स् of this word is changed to ष् before hard<BR> consonants, and to र् before soft ones).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आयुष्कर, आयुष्काम, आयुष्कृत्, आयुर्द्रव्यम्, आयुर्योगः, आयुर्वृद्धिः, आयुर्वेदः, आयुर्वेददृश्, आयुर्वेदमय, आयुर्वेदिक, आयुर्वेदिन्, आयुःशेषः, आयुष्टोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्कर
आयुस् + -कर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> promoting long life; K. 351.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्काम
आयुस् + -काम <i>a.</i> wishing for long life or health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्कृत्
आयुस् + -कृत् <i>a.</i> giving or producing life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्द्रव्यम्
आयुस् + -द्रव्यम्<BR>—1 a medicament.<BR>—2 ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्योगः|आयुर्योग
आयुस् + -योगः N. of a योग in astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वृद्धिः|आयुर्वृद्धि
आयुस् + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> long life, longevity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदः|आयुर्वेद|आयुर्व्वेदः
आयुस् + -वेदः [आयुरस्मिन् विद्यतेऽनेन वा आयुर्विंदतीत्यायुर्वेदः Suśr.]<BR> the science of health or medicine, counted as a sacred science, and regarded<BR> as a supplement to the Atharvaveda; [it comprises 8 different departments;<BR> (1) शल्यम् surgery; (2) शालाक्यम् diagnosis of diseases belonging<BR> to the head and its organs; (3) कायचिकित्सा treatment of diseases<BR> of the whole body; (4) भूतविद्या treatment of diseases of the mind<BR> supposed to be caused by the influence of evil spirits; (5) कौमारभृत्यम्<BR> treatment of children; (6) अगदतन्त्रम् doctrine of antidotes; (7)<BR> रसायनतन्त्रम् doctrine of elixirs; and (8) वाजीकरणतन्त्रम्<BR> treatment of remedies to increase generative power]; Śukra. 4. 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेददृश्
आयुस् + -वेददृश्, -वेदमय, -वेदिक, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to medicine.<BR>—2 acquainted with medical science, medical. ━<i>m.</i> a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदमय
आयुस् + -वेददृश्, -वेदमय, -वेदिक, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to medicine.<BR>—2 acquainted with medical science, medical. ━<i>m.</i> a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदिक
आयुस् + -वेददृश्, -वेदमय, -वेदिक, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to medicine.<BR>—2 acquainted with medical science, medical. ━<i>m.</i> a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदिन्
आयुस् + -वेददृश्, -वेदमय, -वेदिक, -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to medicine.<BR>—2 acquainted with medical science, medical. ━<i>m.</i> a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुःशेषः|आयुःशेष
आयुस् + -शेषः<BR>—1 remainder of life; ˚शेषतया Pt. 1; ˚जीवित Pt. 4 being destined<BR> to live longer.<BR>—2 end or decline of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्टोमः|आयुष्टोम
आयुस् + -स्तोमः (आयुष्टोमः) a sacrifice performed to obtain long life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्मत्|आयुष्मन्त्
आयुष्मत् <i>a.</i> [आयुस् मतुप्]<BR>—1 Alive, living.<BR>—2 Long-lived; आयुष्मन्तं सुतं सूते Ms. 3. 263. (Generally used in<BR> dramas by elderly persons in addressing a nobly-born person; <i>e. g.</i><BR> a charioteer addresses a prince as आयुष्मन्. A Brāhmaṇa is also so<BR> addressed in saluting; cf. Ms. 2. 125; आयुष्मान् भव सौम्येति वाच्यो विप्रोऽभिवादने).<BR>—3 Lasting; गायन्ति पृथगायुष्मन्निदं नो वक्तुमर्हसि Bhāg. 11. 22. 3.<BR>—4 Old. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The third of the 27 Yogas or divisions of the ecliptic.<BR>—2 The Yoga star कृत्तिका; the third lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुषम्
आयुषम् (At the end of a few comps.) Life; <i>e. g.</i> पुरुषायुषजीविन्यः R. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्कः|आयुष्क
आयुष्कः [आयुः कायते, कै-क Tv.]<BR>—1 That which proclaims age or duration of life.<BR>—2 (With Jainas) Connection with the body or person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य <i>a.</i> [आयुः प्रयोजनमस्य, यत्] Promoting long life,<BR> vital, preservative of life; इदं यशस्यमायुष्यमिदं निःश्रेयसं परम्<BR> Ms. 1. 106, 3. 106, 4. 13; M. 4. 4 v. l.; Dk. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्यम्
आयुष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@}<BR>—1 Vital power, abundance of life or vigour.<BR>—2 N. of a ceremony performed after the birth of a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आये
आये <i>ind.</i> An interjection of calling, expressive of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0350-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगवः|आयोगव
आयोगवः [अयोगव एव, स्वार्थे अण्] The son of a Śūdra by a Vaiśya<BR> wife (his business being carpentry; cf Ms. 10. 48); शूद्रादायोगवः क्षत्ता<BR> चाण्डालश्चाधमो नृणाम् । वैश्यराजन्यविप्रास्तु जायन्ते वर्णसंकराः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगवी
आयोगवः + .{@-वी@} A woman of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजनम्
आयोजनम् <i>ind.</i> Up to one योजन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोदः|आयोद
आयोदः Son of अयोद <i>i. e.</i> धौम्यमुनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरः|आर|आरं
आरः, -रम्<BR> [आ-ऋ-घञ्]<BR>—1 Brass; ताम्रारकोष्ठां परिखादुरासदाम् Bhāg. 10. 41. 20.<BR>—2 Oxide of iron.<BR>—3 An angle, corner.<BR>—4 N. of a tree (मधुराम्रफल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्
आरः, -रम्<BR> [आ-ऋ-घञ्]<BR>—1 Brass; ताम्रारकोष्ठां परिखादुरासदाम् Bhāg. 10. 41. 20.<BR>—2 Oxide of iron.<BR>—3 An angle, corner.<BR>—4 N. of a tree (मधुराम्रफल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरः|आर|आरं
आरः, -रम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The planet Mars.<BR>—2 The planet Saturn.<BR>—3 Going.<BR>—4 Distance.<BR>—5 Nearness, as in आरात् q. v.<BR>—6 Extremity (प्रान्तभाग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरा
आरः, -रम् + .{@-रा@} (आ-ऋ-अच्)<BR>—1 A shoemakerʼs awl. ˚मुखम् An arrow-head shaped like an awl; आरामुखेन<BR> चर्मच्छेदनम् । Dhanur. 66.<BR>—2 A knife, probe, instrument of iron.<BR>—3 A spoke; cf. अर.<BR>—4 A goad, or whip; उद्यम्यारामग्रकायोत्थितस्य Śi. 18. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आराग्र, आरावली, आरकूटः, आरकूटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराग्र|आराग्रं
आरः + -अग्र<BR>—1 the point of an awl; आराग्रमात्रो ह्यवरोऽपि दृष्टः Śvet. Up. 5. 8.<BR>—2 the iron thong at the end of a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरावली
आरः + -आवली^1 N. of a chain of mountains, a part of the Vindhya.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकूटः|आरकूट
आरः + -कूटः, -कूटम् brass; उत्तप्तस्फुरदारकूटकपिलज्योतिर्ज्वलद्दीप्तिभिः<BR> U. 5. 14. किमारकूटाभरणेन श्रियः N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकूटम्
आरः + -कूटः, -कूटम् brass; उत्तप्तस्फुरदारकूटकपिलज्योतिर्ज्वलद्दीप्तिभिः<BR> U. 5. 14. किमारकूटाभरणेन श्रियः N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकात्
आरकात् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Far from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष <i>a.</i> Preserved, defended, fit to be protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षः|आरक्ष|आरक्षं
आरक्ष + .{@-क्षः, -क्षा@}<BR>—1 Protection, preservation, guard; आरक्षस्य विधिं कृत्वा Mb. 5. 160. 3;<BR> आरक्षे मध्यमे स्थितान् Rām.; Śānti. 3. 5; Ms. 3. 204. शतसाहस्रमारक्षं<BR> मध्यगं रक्षसां कपिः Bk.<BR>—2 The junction of the frontal sinuses of an elephant (कुम्भसन्धि).<BR>—3 The part of the forehead below this junction.<BR>—4 An army; आरक्षो मे हतस्तात Rām. 3. 31. 40.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरक्षाधिकृतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षा
आरक्ष + .{@-क्षः, -क्षा@}<BR>—1 Protection, preservation, guard; आरक्षस्य विधिं कृत्वा Mb. 5. 160. 3;<BR> आरक्षे मध्यमे स्थितान् Rām.; Śānti. 3. 5; Ms. 3. 204. शतसाहस्रमारक्षं<BR> मध्यगं रक्षसां कपिः Bk.<BR>—2 The junction of the frontal sinuses of an elephant (कुम्भसन्धि).<BR>—3 The part of the forehead below this junction.<BR>—4 An army; आरक्षो मे हतस्तात Rām. 3. 31. 40.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरक्षाधिकृतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षाधिकृतः|आरक्षाधिकृत
आरक्ष + -अधिकृतः Guard. EI. I. p. 5. f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षकः|आरक्षक
आरक्ष(क्षि)कः<BR>—1 A watchman, patrol, sentinel.<BR>—2 A village or police magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षिकः|आरक्षिक
आरक्ष(क्षि)कः<BR>—1 A watchman, patrol, sentinel.<BR>—2 A village or police magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरङ्गरः|आरङ्गर
आरङ्गरः A bee. आरङ्गरेव मध्वेरयेथे Rv. 10. 106. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्वधः|आरग्वध
आरग्वधः The tree Cassia Fistula (Mar. बाहवा) largely used<BR> in medicinal recipes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्वधम्
आरग्वधः + .{@-धम्@} Its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरचित
आरचित <i>a.</i> Arranged, prepared, formed &c.; see रचित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरटः|आरट
आरटः [आ-रट्-अच्] An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्टः|आरट्ट
आरट्टः<BR>—1 N. of a country to the north-east of Punjab, famous for its breed of<BR> horses; (the people of Guzarath in Ravalpindi still call their country<BR> Hairat or Airatdesa); the inhabitants of this country (pl.).<BR>—2 A horse from this country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणम्
आरणम् Ved.<BR>—1 Depth, abyss.<BR>—2 A precipice; याभिरन्तकं जसमानमारणे Rv. 1. 112. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणजाः
आरणम् + .{@-जाः@} N. of a class of Jaina deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणिः|आरणि
आरणिः [आ-ऋ-अनि] An eddy, whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणेय|आरणेयः
आरणेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अरणि-ठक्] Relating to or sprung from Araṇi q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणेयः|आरणेय
आरणेय + .{@-यः@} N. of Śuka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणेयम्
आरणेय + .{@-यम्@} or ˚पर्वन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">Page0351-2</a>]<BR> Title of the last section of the third book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य <i>a.</i> (-ण्या, -ण्यी <i>f.</i>) [अरण्ये भवः ण्] Wild,<BR> forest-born, relating to a forest (opp. ग्राम्य); ˚पशुः Ms. 10. 48.<BR> (आरण्यपशु is of 7 kinds:− सरीसृपो रुरुश्चैव महिषो वानरस्तथा ।<BR> पृषतर्क्षौ मृगश्चैव पशुर्वै सप्तधा मतः ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यः|आरण्य
आरण्य + .{@-ण्यः, -ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 A forest.<BR>—2 A kind of corn growing without sowing seed.<BR>—3 N. of certain signs of the zodiac (see ˚राशि below).<BR>—4 Cow-dung<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यः|आरण्य
आरण्य + .{@-ण्यः, -ण्यम्@} + .({@-ण्यः@} only).<BR>—5 N. of a Parvan in the Mahābhārata.<BR>—6 N. of a Kāṇḍa in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरण्यकुक्कुटः, आरण्यगानम्, आरण्यपर्वन्, आरण्यपशुः, आरण्यमुद्गा, आरण्यराशिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यम्
आरण्य + .{@-ण्यः, -ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 A forest.<BR>—2 A kind of corn growing without sowing seed.<BR>—3 N. of certain signs of the zodiac (see ˚राशि below).<BR>—4 Cow-dung<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यकुक्कुटः|आरण्यकुक्कुट
आरण्य + -कुक्कुटः a wild cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यगानम्
आरण्य + -गानम् one of the four Gānas or psalm-books of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यपर्वन्
आरण्य + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> N. of the third book of the Mahābhārata, usually<BR> called Vana-Parvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यपशुः|आरण्यपशु
आरण्य + -पशुः a wild beast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यमुद्गा
आरण्य + -मुद्गा a kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यराशिः|आरण्यराशि
आरण्य + -राशिः (in the zodiac)<BR>—1 The signs Leo, Aries, and Taurus.<BR>—2 The former half of Capricorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक <i>a.</i> [अरण्ये भवः वुञ्] Relating to or produced in<BR> a forest, wild, forest-born (usually with the words अध्याय, मनुष्य,<BR> न्याय, पथिन्, विहार, and हस्तिन् P. IV. 2. 129. Vārt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यकः|आरण्यक
आरण्यक + .{@-कः@} A forester, an inhabitant of the woods; तपः षड्भागमक्षग्यं<BR> ददत्यारण्यका हि नः Ś. 2. 14; द्वावप्यत्रारण्यकौ Ś. 5. आरण्यकोपात्तफलप्रसूतिः R. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यकम्
आरण्यक + .{@-कम्@} An Āraṇyaka; it is one of a class of religious and philosophical<BR> writings (connected with the Brāhmaṇas) which are either composed in<BR> forests, or must be studied there; <i>e. g.</i> एतरेयारण्यकम्; बृहदारण्यकम्<BR> and तैत्तिरीयारण्यकम्; अरंयेऽनूच्यमानत्वात् आरण्यकम्, Bṛ. Ār. Up.;<BR> (अरण्येऽध्ययनादेव आरण्यकमुदाहृतम्); वेदवादानतिक्रम्य शास्त्राण्यारण्यकानि<BR> च Mb. 12. 19. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरण्यककाण्डम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यककाण्डम्
आरण्यक + -काण्डम् the title of the third book of the Rāmāyaṇa. {@गानम्@}<BR> = अरण्यगानम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरथः|आरथ
आरथः [ईषत्स्वल्पो रथः] A carriage drawn by one horse or ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनालम्
आरनालम् Gruel made from the fermentation of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्
आरभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To begin, commence, undertake; अथ वा मृदु वस्तु हिंसितुं मृदुनैवारभते<BR> प्रजान्तकः R. 8. 45; आरभन्तेऽल्पमेवाज्ञाः Subhāṣ.; आरब्धा बलिविग्रहम् Bk. 5. 38.<BR>—2 To be active or energetic, be busy; अप्यनारभमाणस्य Śi. 2. 91.<BR>—3 To rely on.<BR>—4 To reach or attain to, obtain.<BR>—5 To seize, grasp.<BR>—6 To form, make; भूतैः पञ्चभिरारब्धे देहे Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्ध|आरब्धं
आरब्ध <i>p. p.</i> Begun, commenced; आरब्धे हि सुदुष्करेऽपि महतां<BR> मध्ये विरामः कुतः Subh. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्धम्
आरब्ध + .{@-ब्धम्@} Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्धिः|आरब्धि
आरब्धिः <i>f.</i> Beginning, commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभटः|आरभट
आरभटः [आरभ्-अटि] An enterprising or courageous man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभटः|आरभट
आरभटः + .{@-टः, -टी@} Boldness, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभटी
आरभटः + .{@-टः, -टी@} Boldness, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभटी
आरभटः + .{@-टी@}<BR>—1 A branch of the dramatic art, machinery of the drama, representation<BR> of supernatural, horrible events on the stage; मायेन्द्रजालसंग्रामक्रोधोद्भ्रान्तादिचेष्टितैः ।<BR> संयुक्ता वधबन्धाद्यैरुद्धतारभटी मता ॥ (said to be of four kinds,<BR> see S. D. 420 <i>et seq.</i>).<BR>—2 A kind of literary style (वृत्ति).<BR>—3 A particular style of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0351-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्य
आरभ्य <i>ind.</i> Having begun, beginning with, ever since, since,<BR> with a prepositional force (with abl.); मालत्याः प्रथमावलोकदिवसादारभ्य<BR> Māl. 6. 3; Ś. 3; K. 102, 134, 196; sometimes with acc. also; प्रतिपद्दिनमारभ्य Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भः|आरम्भ|आरंभः
आरम्भः [आ-रभ्-घञ् मुम्]<BR>—1 Beginning, commencement; ˚उपायः plan of commencement; नृत्तारम्भे<BR> हर पशुपतेरार्द्रनागाजिनेच्छाम् Me. 38.<BR>—2 An introduction.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) An act, undertaking, deed, work; आगमैः सदृशारम्भः R. 1. 15;<BR> Ku. 7. 71; V. 3; Bh. 2. 69; R. 7. 31; Bg. 12. 16. cf. also आरम्भस्य<BR> शब्दपूर्वत्वात् । MS. 11. 1. 10 (शबर writes आरम्भो व्यापारः<BR> क्रियेत्यनर्थान्तरम् ।).<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Preparation; U. 4.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) A thing begun; U. 4.<BR>—4 Haste, speed, velocity; चण्डारम्भः समीरः Ve. 2. 19.<BR>—5 Effort, exertion; Bg. 14. 12.<BR>—6 Scene, action; चित्रार्पितारम्भ इवावतस्थे R. 2. 31.<BR>—7 Pride.<BR>—8 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—9 The first act that is done.<BR>—10 The first movement or activity on the part of man; आरम्भो हि प्रथमः<BR> पदार्थः स्यात् । प्रथमं वा पुरुषस्य प्रवर्तनम् । (= प्रथमप्रवर्तनमारम्भः<BR> औदासीन्याद् व्यावृत्तिः पुरुषस्य व्यापृतता) ŚB. on MS. 10. 104.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरम्भभाव्यत्वम्, आरम्भरुचि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भभाव्यत्वम्
आरम्भः + -भाव्यत्वम् The fact of being produced through activity; कर्मणि<BR> आरम्भभाव्यत्वात् कृषिवत् प्रत्यारम्भं फलानि स्युः । MS. 11. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भरुचि
आरम्भः + -रुचि <i>a.</i> Enjoying new undertakings. आरम्भरुचिताऽधैर्यमसत्कार्यपरिग्रहः ।<BR> Ms. 12. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भक|आरंभक
आरम्भक <i>a.</i> [आ-रभ् ण्वुल् मुम्] undertaking, beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भणम्
आरम्भणम् [आ-रभ् ल्युट् मुम्]<BR>—1 Taking hold of, seizing.<BR>—2 The place of seizing, a handle;<BR>—3 Forming, making; तदनन्यत्वमारम्भणशब्दादिभ्यः Br. Sūt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भिन्|आरंभिन्
आरम्भिन् <i>a.</i> Enterprizing; one who forms new projects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्
आरम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To delight in, take pleasure in, sport; आरमन्तं परं स्मरे Bk. 8. 52, 3. 38.<BR>—2 To cease, stop (to speak); leave off; अन्तर्वत्नी त्वहं भ्रात्रा ज्येष्ठेनारम्यतामिति<BR> Mb. 1. 104. 11; विरामोऽस्त्विति चारमेत् Ms. 2. 73.<BR>—3 To rest, take rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरत
आरत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stopped, ceased; उदितपक्षमिवारतनिःस्वनैः Ki. 5. 6; see अनारत also.<BR>—2 Quiet, gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरतिः|आरति
आरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cessation, stopping.<BR>—2 Waving lights before an image (Mar. आरती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरमणम्
आरमणम्<BR>—1 Taking delight.<BR>—2 Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>—3 Sexual pleasure.<BR>—4 Cessation, pause.<BR>—5 A resting place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराम|आरामः
आराम <i>a.</i> [रम्-घञ्] Pleasing, delightful; रामभद्र गुणाराम Mv. 7. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरामः|आराम
आराम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Delight, pleasure; इन्द्रियारामः Bg. 3. 16; आत्मारामाः Ve. 1. 31;<BR> एकाराम Y. 3. 58.<BR>—2 A garden, grove; प्रियारामा हि वैदेह्यासीत् U. 2; आरामाधिपतिर्विवेकविकलः<BR> Bv. 1. 31. आरामः कल्पवृक्षाणाम् (रामरक्षा) [cf. Pers. <i>ārām</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरामशीतला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरामशीतला
आराम + -शीतला N. of a fragrant plant (आनन्दी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरामिकः|आरामिक
आरामिकः A gardener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्बणम्
आरम्बणम् (Vedic for आलम्बनम्) Support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आरव &c. See under आरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्यम्
आरस्यम् [अरसस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Insipidity, tastelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरा
आरा See under आर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्
आरात् <i>ind.</i> [आ-रा-बा˚ आति Tv.; abl. of आर q. v.]<BR>—1 Near, in the vicinity of; (with abl. or by itself); तमर्च्यमारादभिवर्तमानम्<BR> R. 2. 10, 5. 3.<BR>—2 Far from; with acc. also in both these senses; Śi. 3. 31, 8. 29, कथंचिदारादपथेन<BR> निन्यिरे 12. 28; to a distant place, distant.<BR>—3 Far, from a distance; मेघमालेव यश्चायमारादिव विभाव्यते U. 2. 24.<BR>—4 Directly, immediately.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरादुपकारक, आरादुपकारिणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरादुपकारक
आरात् + -उपकारक (fem. उपकारिका), (An अङ्ग) that subserves<BR> the purpose of the principal act only indirectly; द्विविधान्यङ्गानि आरादुपकारकाणि<BR> सामवायिकानि च । आरादुपकारकेभ्यः सामवायिकानि गरीयांसि । ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 38;<BR> Also ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरादुपकारिणी
आरात् + -उपकारिणी See आरादुपकारक. आरादुपकारिणी तु सा । ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातीय
आरातीय <i>a.</i> [आरात्-छ; P. IV. 2. 114^1. Vārt.]<BR>—1 Near, proximate.<BR>—2 Remote, distant.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes, user @Andhrabharati on 20251212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102#issuecomment-3647228881.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्तात्
आरात्तात् <i>ind.</i> Ved. From a distant place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातिः|आराति
आरातिः [आ-रा क्तिच्] An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्रिकम्
आरात्रिकम् [अरात्रावपि निर्वृत्तं ठञ्]<BR>—1 Waving a light (or the vessel containing it) at night before an idol<BR> (Mar. आरती ओंवाळणें); सर्वेषु चाङ्गेषु च सप्तवारान् आरात्रिकं<BR> भक्तजनस्तु कुर्यात्.<BR>—2 The light so waved; शिरसि निहितभारं पात्रमारात्रिकस्य भ्रमयति<BR> मयि भूयस्ते कृपार्द्रः कटाक्षः Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्
आराध् €5. €10 P.<BR>—1 To propitiate, conciliate, please, try to win the favour of; परेषां<BR> चेतांसि प्रतिदिवसमाराध्य बहुधा Bh. 3. 34, 2. 4-5; R. 1. 77, 81, 10. 86, 18. 23;<BR> Me. 47.<BR>—2 To honour, worship, respect.<BR>—3 To deserve, merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधक
आराधक <i>a.</i> A worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनम्
आराधनम्<BR>—1 Pleasing, satisfaction, entertainment, gratification; येषामाराधनाय<BR> U. 1; यदि वा जानकीमपि, आराधनाय लोकानां मुञ्चतो नास्ति मे व्यथा 1. 12, 41.<BR>—2 Serving, worshipping, adoration, propitiation (as of a deity); आराधनायास्य<BR> सखीसमेताम् Ku. 1. 58; Bg. 7. 22; कृतमाराधनं रवेः Mb.<BR>—3 A means of pleasing; इदं तु ते भक्तिनम्रं सतामाराधनं वपुः Ku. 6. 73.<BR>—4 Honouring, respecting; सम्बन्धे विपरीतमेव तदभूदाराधनं ते मयि U. 4. 17.<BR>—5 Cooking.<BR>—6 Accomplishment, undertaking.<BR>—7 Acquirement, attainment; मन्त्राराधनतत्परेण मनसा नीताः श्मशाने<BR> निशाः Bh. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधना
आराधनम् + .{@-ना@} Service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनी
आराधनम् + .{@-नी@} Worship, adoration, propitiation (of a deity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनीय
आराधनीय, आराध्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Fit to be worshipped or propitiated; सोऽहं कथं नाम तवाचरेयमाराधनीयस्य<BR> ऋषेर्विधानम् R. 16. 82.<BR>—2 To become accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्य
आराधनीय, आराध्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Fit to be worshipped or propitiated; सोऽहं कथं नाम तवाचरेयमाराधनीयस्य<BR> ऋषेर्विधानम् R. 16. 82.<BR>—2 To become accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयितृ
आराधयितृ <i>a.</i> An adorer, humble servant, worshipper; नन्वयमाराधयिता<BR> जनस्तव समीपे वर्तते Ś. 3; पितरमाराधयिता भव V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधित
आराधित <i>a.</i> Propitiated; नाराधितो यैः पुरुषः प्रधानस्तेषां<BR> वृथा जन्म नराधिपानाम् Bhāg.; आराधितोऽपि नृपतिः परिसेवनीयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0352-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयिष्णु
आराधयिष्णु <i>a.</i> Endeavouring to please, desirous of worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरालिकः|आरालिक
आरालिकः [अरालं कुटिलं चरति ठक्]<BR>—1 ‘One who deals crookedly’, a cook; (धनलोभेन परप्रोत्साहितः पाचको<BR> विषादिसंसृष्टं पचतीति तस्य तथात्वम्) Kau. A. 1. 12; आरालिको<BR> गोविकर्ता सूपकर्ता नियोधकः Mb. 4. 2. 9. (आरालिकोऽन्नपाकी स्यात् सूपकर्ता<BR> तु शाककृत् । तैलान्नं पचते यस्तु गोविकर्ता स उच्यते ॥)<BR>—2 A controller of wild elephants; Mb. 4. 2. 9; (अराला मत्तगजास्तैः<BR> सह क्रीडति तान् जयति वा आरालिकः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरासः|आरास
आरासः Tumultuous noise; ततमानवजारासा Śi. 11. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरिच्
आरिच् €7 U. To empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरीण
आरीण <i>a.</i> Completely dried; आरीणं लवणजलं समिद्ध-फल-बाण-विद्ध-घोर-फणि-वरम् Bk. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेकः|आरेक
आरेकः^1 [आ-रिच् घञ्]<BR>—1 Emptying.<BR>—2 Contraction.<BR>—3 Doubt.<BR>—4 Excess.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेचित
आरेचित <i>a.</i> [अ-रिच्-णिच् क्त]<BR>—1 Emptied.<BR>—2 Mixed.<BR>—3 Contracted; आरेचितभ्रूचतुरैः कटाक्षैः Ku. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरित्रिक
आरित्रिक <i>a.</i> [P. IV. 2. 116] Pertaining to an oar &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु €2 P.<BR>—1 To cry out, shout; Bk. 17. 24, to low (as cows).<BR>—2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरवः|आरव
आर(रा)वः [आ-रु-अप् पक्षे घञ्]<BR>—1 A cry, howling; वानराश्चक्रुरारवम् Rām.<BR>—2 Sound; दधति दधनि धीरानारवान् वारिणीव Śi. 11. 8, 12. 18, नारावं<BR> व्यतनुत मेखलाकलापः 8. 45. Humming; प्रतिमिलिन्दमारावाः Viś. Guṇā. 167.<BR>—3 N. of a people.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरवडिण्डिमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरावः|आराव
आर(रा)वः [आ-रु-अप् पक्षे घञ्]<BR>—1 A cry, howling; वानराश्चक्रुरारवम् Rām.<BR>—2 Sound; दधति दधनि धीरानारवान् वारिणीव Śi. 11. 8, 12. 18, नारावं<BR> व्यतनुत मेखलाकलापः 8. 45. Humming; प्रतिमिलिन्दमारावाः Viś. Guṇā. 167.<BR>—3 N. of a people.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरवडिण्डिमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरवडिण्डिमः|आरवडिण्डिम
आरवः + -डिण्डिमः A kind of drum; चण्डि रसितरशनारवडिण्डिममभिसर<BR> सरसमलज्जम् Gīt. 11. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराविन्
आराविन् <i>a.</i> Sounding, noisy; नूपुराराविणा M. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुतम्
आरुतम् Cry, Crying; निषेदुःशतशस्तत्र दारुणा दारुणारुताः Rām. 6. 106. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुः|आरु
आरुः [ऋ-उण्]<BR>—1 A hog.<BR>—2 A crab.<BR>—3 N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुः|आरु
आरुः + .{@-रुः@} <i>f.</i> A pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुकः|आरुक
आरुकः A medicinal plant having cooling properties (growing on the Himālayas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुच्
आरुच् <i>Caus.</i> To regard as pleasant, choose, like; वासं नारोचयेऽरण्ये Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोकः|आरोक
आरोकः<BR>—1 Shining through.<BR>—2 Small points of light between the threads of a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोचन
आरोचन <i>a.</i> Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज्
आरुज्, -ज <i>a.</i><BR> [आ-रुज्-क]<BR>—1 Distressing, giving pain.<BR>—2 Killing, destroying, breaking; इन्द्र दृळहा चिदारुजम् Rv. 8. 45. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज
आरुज्, -ज <i>a.</i><BR> [आ-रुज्-क]<BR>—1 Distressing, giving pain.<BR>—2 Killing, destroying, breaking; इन्द्र दृळहा चिदारुजम् Rv. 8. 45. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुजत्नु
आरुजत्नु <i>a.</i> Ved. Breaking; वीळु चिदारुजत्नुभिर्गुहा चिदिन्द्र<BR> वह्निभिः Rv. 1. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणि|आरुणिः
आरुणि <i>a.</i> [अरुणस्य अपत्यम् इञ्] Belonging to, or sprung from,<BR> Aruṇa, q. v.; औद्दालकिरारुणिर्मत्प्रसृष्टः Kaṭh. 1. 11.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">Page0353-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणिः|आरुणि
आरुणि + .{@-णिः@}<BR>—1 N. of Uddālaka; उद्दालक आरुणिः Bṛ. Up. 3. 6. 1.<BR>—2 Descendants of the sage अरुण; परिसरपद्धतिं हृदयमारुणयो दहरम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 87. 18.<BR>—3 The son of the sun, as Yama.<BR>—4 The son of Vinatā (वैनतेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणी
आरुणी <i>f.</i> Ved. ‘The red one’, a name given to the horses of the<BR> Maruts which are females; यदारुणीषु तविषीरयुग्ध्वम् Rv. 1. 64. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणेयः|आरुणेय
आरुणेयः The son of आरुणि, श्वेतकेतु; श्वेतकेतुर्हारुणेय आस<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 3. 1; Bṛ. Up. 6. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुध्
आरुध् €7 U.<BR>—1 To keep or ward off, keep away, restrain; बन्धुता शुचमारुणत् Bk. 17. 49.<BR>—2 To shut up, confine.<BR>—3 To besiege.<BR>—4 To hold fast, grasp. ━<i>Caus.</i> To obstruct, impede, block, besiege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोधनम्
आरोधनम् Ved.<BR>—1 Obstruction, means of obstruction.<BR>—2 A secret place, innermost part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुषी
आरुषी N. of a daughter of Manu and mother of और्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुष्करम्
आरुष्करम् The fruit of the tree called भल्लातक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
आरुह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To ascend, mount, bestride, get upon (with acc., sometimes loc.); सिंहासनमारुरोह<BR> K. 111; आरुरुहू रथदिषु Bk. 14. 8; आरूढकुलालचक्रमिव Mu. 5. 5;<BR> mounted on a potterʼs wheel; 7. 12.<BR>—2 To ride upon, get ascendancy over, domineer over (fig.); वृषल भृत्यमिव<BR> मामारोढुमिच्छसि Mu. 3; Pt. 1. 36.<BR>—3 To venture upon, undertake, enter upon, make; प्रतिज्ञामारोढुं पुनरपि<BR> चलत्येष चरणः Mu. 3. 30, 27; so यौवनारूढ, योगारूढ.<BR>—4 To attain, gain, get to, reach; सौन्दर्यस्य पारमारूढा न वा Dk. 88;<BR> Ki. 2. 13; तुलां यदारोहति दन्तवाससा Ku. 5. 34; आरुरोह कुमदाकरोपमाम्<BR> R. 19. 34. The senses of this root are modified according to the noun<BR> with which it is joined; आरूढरुषा Ku. 7. 67 excited to anger; तदागमारूढगुरुप्रहर्षः<BR> R. 5. 61; मन्त्रिपदमारूढः Mu. 6; तर्कारूढा 6. 19 engaged in<BR> guessing; Ś. 5. 9; शीघ्रं बुद्धिमारोहति Ś. B. strikes the mind; यौवनपदवीमारूढः<BR> attained his majority; अवस्थान्तरमारूढा M. 3; संशयं पुनरारुह्य<BR> H. 1. 7 running a risk; संशयमारुरोह शैलः Ki. 13. 16. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (रोह(प)यति)<BR>—1 To cause to go up or ascend, raise up, elevate; अमात्योऽस्मान्पुरातनीमवस्थामारोपयिष्यति<BR> Mu. 2 will raise or elevate; शूलानारोपयेत् Y. 2. 273; आरोपिता मनोविषयमात्मनः Ku. 6. 17.<BR>—2 To cause to mount or sit (on oneself) (Ātm.); करेणुरारोहयते निषादिनम् Śi. 12. 5.<BR>—3 To cause to grow, plant (lit.).<BR>—4 To establish, install, seat (fig.); राज्ये चारोपिता वयम् Mu. 7. 18;<BR> इत्यारोपितपुत्रास्ते R. 15. 91.<BR>—5 To cause, produce, bring out; उष्माणम् K. 105; प्रणयम् 134, 142;<BR> आरोपितप्रीतिरभूत् 173, 212; प्रतापमारोपयितुम् 110, 119 show or exhibit.<BR>—6 To place, fix, direct; अङ्कमारोप्य placing in the lap; R. 3. 26, 14. 27;<BR> Ku. 1. 37; चक्षुः˚ cast a look at; Pt. 1. 243; आशीर्वादमारोपयन्तः<BR> Ki. 18. 46 conferring or pronouncing; आभरणभारमङ्गेषु नारोपयन्ति<BR> K. 203 put or wear; पत्रे आरोपितं कुरु Ś. 6 commit to paper; आरोप्यते<BR> शिला शैले H. 2. 46.<BR>—7 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">Page0354-1</a>]<BR> entrust to, appoint to, charge with; मन्त्रिणि राज्यभारमारोप्य K. 57;<BR> अमात्यपदे आरोपितः Pt. 1.<BR>—8 To cause to go to or attain a particular state; करतलं कर्णपूरतामारोपितम्<BR> K. 60; आरोपय गरीयस्त्वम् 207 raise to greatness 315; Dk. 118.<BR>—9 To ascribe, attribute, impute; आत्मन्यारोपिताभिमानाः K. 108, 185;<BR> छाया हि भूमेः शशिनो मलत्वेनारोपिता शुद्धिमतः प्रजाभिः R. 14. 40.<BR>—10 To string (as a bow); धनुरारोपयन् U. 4; तं देशमारोपितपुष्पचापे<BR> Ku. 3. 35; Bk. 14. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0353-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षु
आरुरुक्षु <i>a.</i> Wishing to ascend, mount or reach; कैलासगौरं<BR> वृषमारुरुक्षोः R. 2. 35; आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगम् Bg. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
आरुह् <i>a.</i> Ved. Ascending; Rv. 1. 124. 7. <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Excrescence.<BR>—2 A shoot (of a plant); यास्ते रुहः प्ररुहो यास्त आरुहः Av. 13. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह|आरुहः
आरुह <i>a.</i> [आ-रुह्-क] Ascending, mounting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुहः|आरुह
आरुह + .{@-हः@} Ascent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढ|आरूढः
आरूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mounted, ascended; seated on; आरूढो वृक्षो भवता Sk.; oft. used<BR> actively; आरूढमद्रीन् R. 6. 77; Me. 8, 18; Ś. 4; so वृक्षम्, नावम्,<BR> हयम्, स्थम् &c.; चक्र˚, दोला˚.<BR>—2 Raised up, elevated on high.<BR>—3 Arisen, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढम्
आरूढ + .{@-ढम्@} Ascending, mounting; see अत्यारूढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढिः|आरूढि
आरूढिः <i>f.</i> Ascent, mounting; rise, elevation (lit. and fig.);<BR> अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोढृ
आरोढृ <i>a.</i> One who climbs, ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपः|आरोप
आरोपः<BR>—1 Attributing the nature or properties of one thing to another; वस्तुन्यवस्त्वारोपोऽध्यारोपः<BR> Vedānta S.; attributing or assigning to, imputation; दोषारोपो गुणेष्वपि Ak.<BR>—2 Considering as equal; identification (as in सारोपा लक्षणा).<BR>—3 Super-imposition.<BR>—4 Imposing (as a burden), burdening or charging with.<BR>—5 Placing in or upon.<BR>—6 Relating to.<BR>—7 Superior position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपक
आरोपक <i>a.</i> Placing, fixing, planting गृहसंवेशको दूतो वृक्षारोपक एव च Ms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपणम्
आरोपणम्<BR>—1 placing or fixing in or upon, putting; आर्द्राक्षतारोपणमन्वभूताम्<BR> R. 7. 28; Ku. 7. 88; (fig.) establishing, installing; अधिकारारोपणम् Mu. 3.<BR>—2 Causing to mount or ascend, raising (to heaven).<BR>—3 Planting.<BR>—4 The stringing of a bow.<BR>—5 Trusting, delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपयितृ
आरोपयितृ <i>a.</i> One who places upon (his body), wears; न तानि<BR> कश्चिन्माल्यानि तत्रारोपयिता नरः 3. 73. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपित|आरोपितं
आरोपित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, elevated.<BR>—2 Fixed, placed, made; आरोपितपर्याणं च त्वरिततुरगपरिचारकोपनीतमिन्द्रायुधम्; K.<BR>—3 Strung (as a bow).<BR>—4 Deposited, entrusted.<BR>—5 Consecrated, hallowed.<BR>—6 Accidental, adventitious, ascribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहः|आरोह
आरोहः [आ-रुह्-घञ्]<BR>—1 One who mounts, a rider, as in अश्वारोह, स्यन्दनारोह; सारोहाणां<BR> च वाजिनाम् Rām.; one who is seated in a carriage.<BR>—2 Ascent, rising, mounting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">Page0354-2</a>]<BR> ascending, riding; आरोहे विनये चैव युक्तो वारणवाजिनाम् Rām. 2. 1. 28.<BR>—3 An elevated place, elevation, altitude; height; नगाद्यारोह; उच्छ्रायः<BR> Ak.; Mb. 13. 147. 16.<BR>—4 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>—5 A mountain, a heap.<BR>—6 A womanʼs waist; the buttocks; सा रामा न वरारोहा Udb.; आरोहैर्निबिडबृहन्नितम्बबिम्बैः<BR> Śi. 8. 8; Bhāg. 10. 6. 16.<BR>—7 Length.<BR>—8 A kind of measure.<BR>—9 A mine.<BR>—10 Descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहक|आरोहकः
आरोहक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ascending, mounting, riding.<BR>—2 Raising up, elevating. —3 Rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहकः|आरोहक
आरोहक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A rider, driver; हस्त्यारोहकः Pt. 2.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहणम्
आरोहणम्<BR>—1 The act of rising, ascending, mounting; आरोहणार्थं नवयौवनेन<BR> कामस्य सोपानमिव प्रयुक्तम् Ku. 1. 39.<BR>—2 Riding (on a horse &c.).<BR>—3 A stair-case, ladder; अथारोहणमासाद्य वेदिकान्तरमाश्रितः Rām. 5. 10. 13.<BR>—4 The rising or growing of new shoots, growing (of plants).<BR>—5 A raised stage for dancing.<BR>—6 A carriage (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहणिक
आरोहणिक <i>a.</i> Relating to mounting or ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहिन्
आरोहिन् <i>a.</i> Ascending, mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरू
आरू <i>a.</i> Of a tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरू
आरू + .{@-रू@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The tawny colour.<BR>—2 A hog; a crab; see आरु.<BR>—3 N. of a medicinal plant on the Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरे
आरे <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Far, far from, (with abl.).<BR>—2 Near.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरेघ, आरेवद्य, आरेशत्रु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेघ
आरे + -अघ <i>a.</i> Ved. having evil far removed; पूर्वीरिषो बृहतीरारेअघा Rv. 6. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवद्य
आरे + -अवद्य <i>a.</i> one from whom blame is far removed; हित्वी गयमारेअवद्य<BR> आगात् Rv. 10. 99. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेशत्रु
आरे + -शत्रु <i>a.</i> one whose enemies are driven far away; आरेशत्रुं<BR> कृणुहि सर्ववीरम् Av. 7. 8. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवतः|आरेवत|आरेवतं
आरेवतः N. of a tree (आरग्वध q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवतम्
आरेवतः + .{@-तम्@} The fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेहणम्
आरेहणम् Ved. Licking, kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यम्
आरोग्यम् [अरोगस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Freedom from disease, good health;<BR> लघुत्वमारोग्यमलोलुपत्वम् Śvet. Up. 2. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आरोग्याम्बु, आरोग्यचिन्तामणिः, आरोग्यप्रतिपद्व्रतम्, आरोग्यशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्याम्बु
आरोग्यम् + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> Healthful water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यचिन्तामणिः|आरोग्यचिन्तामणि
आरोग्यम् + -चिन्तामणिः N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यप्रतिपद्व्रतम्
आरोग्यम् + -प्रतिपद्व्रतम् A ceremony for gaining health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यशाला
आरोग्यम् + -शाला a hospital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यय्
आरोग्यय् Den. P. To wish health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्कम्
आर्कम् <i>ind.</i> as far as the sun; आकल्पमार्कमर्हन्भगवन्नमस्ते<BR> Bhāg. 10. 14. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्किः|आर्कि
आर्किः [अर्कस्य अपत्यम् इञ्] A son of अर्क, epithet of (1)<BR> Yama, (2) The planet Saturn, (3) Karṇa, (4) Sugrīva, (5) वैवस्वतमनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्ष|आर्क्षः
आर्क्ष (-र्क्षी <i>f.</i>) [ऋक्षस्येदम् अण्] Stellar, regulated<BR> by stars or pertaining to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षः|आर्क्ष
आर्क्ष + .{@-र्क्षः@} A son or descendant of <i>Ṛkṣa</i>; Rv. 8. 68. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आर्क्षवर्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षवर्षः|आर्क्षवर्ष
आर्क्ष + -वर्षः a stellar year or revolution of a constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षोद
आर्क्षोद [ऋक्षोद-अण्] Inhabiting the mountain Ṛkṣoda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0354-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गलः|आर्गल
आर्गलः, -ली<BR> [अर्गलमेव स्वार्थे अण्] A bolt or bar; see अर्गलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गली
आर्गलः, -ली<BR> [अर्गलमेव स्वार्थे अण्] A bolt or bar; see अर्गलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ग्वध|आर्ग्वधः
आर्ग्वध = आरग्वध. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घा
आर्घा [आ-अर्घ-अच्] A kind of yellow bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घ्य|आर्घ्यं
आर्घ्य <i>a.</i> Relating to this bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घ्यम्
आर्घ्य + .{@-र्घ्यम्@} Wild honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च|आर्च्च
आर्च <i>a.</i> (-र्ची <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अर्चा अस्त्यस्य ण P. V. 2. 101]<BR>—1 Devout, worshipping, pious.<BR>—2 Relating to the Ṛk or Ṛgveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चायण
आर्चायण <i>a.</i> Existing in Ṛks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चिक|आर्च्चिक
आर्चिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋचि भवः, ऋचो व्याख्यानो ग्रन्थो वा ठञ्] Relating<BR> to the Ṛgveda, or explaining it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चिकम्
आर्चिक + .{@-कम्@} An epithet of the Sāma-Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चीक|आर्चीकः
आर्चीक <i>a.</i> [ऋचीके पर्वते भवः अण्] Belonging to the ऋचीक mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चीकः|आर्चीक
आर्चीक + .{@-कः@} The mountain ऋचीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जवम्
आर्जवम् [ऋजोर्भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Straightness; दूरं यात्युदरं च रोमलतिका नेत्रार्जवं धावति S. D.<BR>—2 Straightforwardness, rectitude of conduct, uprightness, honesty, sincerity,<BR> open-heartedness; आर्जवं कुटिलेषु न नीतिः; अहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवं<BR> Bg. 13. 7, 16. 1, 17. 4, 18. 42. क्षेत्रमार्जवस्य K. 45; Bh. 2. 22.<BR>—3 Simplicity, humility; कृतानुकारानिव गोभिरार्जवे Ki. 4. 13; Mv. 5. 46.<BR>—4 Front (Loc. आर्जवे straight in the front); देवदत्तस्यार्जवे<BR> ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीक|आर्जीकः
आर्जीक <i>a.</i> [ऋजीकस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to the ऋजीक country,<BR> or a vessel called ऋजीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीकः|आर्जीक
आर्जीक + .{@-कः@} A lake in the ऋजीक country; (according to others) perhaps<BR> a milk-vessel or celestial-vessel in which the heavenly Soma is purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीकीय
आर्जीकीय = आर्जीक <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीकीया
आर्जीकीय + .{@-या@}<BR>—1 A terrestrial river.<BR>—2 N. of a river (विपाशा.); आजींकीये शृणुह्या सुषोमया Rv. 10. 75. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनायनाः
आर्जुनायनाः N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनिः|आर्जुनि|आर्ज्जुनि
आर्जुनिः [अर्जुनस्य अपत्यम् इञ्] The son of Arjuna, अभिमन्यु;<BR> अभिमन्युमिति प्राहुरार्जुनिं पुरुषर्षभम् Mb. 1. 221. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त|आर्त्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त <i>a.</i> [आ-ऋ-क्त]<BR>—1 Afflicted with, struck by, suffering from, pained by; सा त्रियामा<BR> तदार्तस्य चन्द्रमण्डलमण्डिता Rām. 2. 13. 15; usually in comp., कामार्त,<BR> क्षुधार्त, तृषार्त &c.<BR>—2 Sick, diseased; आर्तस्य यथौषधम् R. 1. 28; Ms. 4. 236.<BR>—3 Distressed, afflicted, struck by calamity, oppressed, unhappy; आर्तो<BR> जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी Bg. 7. 16; आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR> Ś. 1. 11; R. 2. 28, 8. 31, 12. 10, 32.<BR>—4 Perishable (विनाशिन् अतोऽन्यदार्तम्) Bṛ. Up. 3. 4. 2.<BR>—5 Inconvenient; आर्ता यस्मिन् काले भवन्ति स आर्तः कालः । ŚB. on MS. 6. 5. 37.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आर्तनादः, आर्तध्वनिः, आर्तस्वरः, आर्तबन्धुः, आर्तसाधुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तनादः|आर्तनाद|आर्त्तनाद
आर्त + -नादः, -ध्वनिः, -स्वरः a cry of distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तध्वनिः
आर्त + -नादः, -ध्वनिः, -स्वरः a cry of distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तस्वरः|आर्तस्वर
आर्त + -नादः, -ध्वनिः, -स्वरः a cry of distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तबन्धुः|आर्तबन्धु|आर्त्तबन्धु
आर्त + -बन्धुः, -साधुः a friend of the distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तसाधुः
आर्त + -बन्धुः, -साधुः a friend of the distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तिः|आर्ति|आर्त्ति|आर्त्तिः
आर्तिः <i>f.</i> [आ-ऋ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Distress, affliction, suffering, pain, injury (bodily or mental); आर्तिं<BR> न पश्यसि पुरूरवसस्तदर्थे V. 2. 16; आपन्नार्तिप्रशमनफलाः संपदो<BR> ह्युत्तमानाम् Me. 55.<BR>—2 Mental agony, anguish; उत्कण्ठार्ति Amaru. 44.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">Page0355-2</a>]<BR> v. l.<BR>—3 Evil, mischief.<BR>—4 Sickness, disease.<BR>—5 The end of a bow.<BR>—6 Ruin, destruction; दुःखार्तिप्रभवं सुखम् Mb. 12. 25. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तिमत्|आर्तिमन्त्
आर्तिमत् <i>a.</i> Suffering from pain, afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तगलः|आर्तगल|आर्त्तगल|आर्त्तगलः
आर्तगलः N. of a tree नीलझिंटी (Mar. कोन्हांटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तना
आर्तना Ved.<BR>—1 A mortal combat.<BR>—2 An uncultivated ground; Rv. 1. 127. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तव|आर्तवः|आर्त्तव|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्तव <i>a.</i> (-वा, -वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋतुरस्य प्राप्तः, अण्]<BR>—1 Conforming or relating to the season; seasonal; अभिभूय विभूतिमार्तवीम्<BR> R. 8. 36, स्वयमङ्गेषु ममेदमार्तवम् Ku. 4. 68; लताभिः श्रीरिवार्तवी<BR> V. 1. 13; vernal; R. 9. 28, 48.<BR>—2 Menstrual, relating to or produced by this discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तवः|आर्तव|आर्त्तव|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्तव + .{@-वः@} A section of the year, a combination of several seasons (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तवी|आर्त्तवी
आर्तव + .{@-वी@} A mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तवम्
आर्तव + .{@-वम्@} The menstrual discharge (of women), नोपगच्छेत्प्रमत्तोऽपि<BR> स्त्रियमार्तवदर्शने Ms. 4. 40, 3. 48.<BR>—2 Certain days after menstrual discharge, favourable to conception.<BR>—3 Menstrual ablution; गिरिकायाः प्रयच्छाशु तस्या ह्यार्तवमद्य वै Mb. 1. 63. 55.<BR>—4 A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तवेयी
आर्तवेयी A woman during her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्निः|आर्त्नि
आर्त्निः The end of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विजीन
आर्त्विजीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋत्विजं तत्कर्मार्हति खञ्] Fit for the office<BR> of a sacrificial priest (ऋत्विज्) दाक्षिण्यदिष्टं कृतमार्त्विजीनैः । Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विज्यम्
आर्त्विज्यम् [ऋत्विजो भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्] The office of a priest,<BR> his rank; आर्त्विज्यं करिष्यन्वाचि स्वरमिच्छेत Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थ
आर्थ <i>a.</i> (-र्थी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अर्थादागतः अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a thing or object.<BR>—2 Relating to, dependent on, sense (opp. शाब्द); आर्थी उपमा &c.<BR>—3 Material, significant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थपत्यम्
आर्थपत्यम् Power over a thing, possession of a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थिक
आर्थिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अर्थं गृह्णाति ठक्]<BR>—1 Significant.<BR>—2 Wise.<BR>—3 Rich.<BR>—4 Substantial, real, material.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्र|आर्द्रं
आर्द्र <i>a.</i> [आ-अर्द्-रक् दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 2. 18]<BR>—1 Wet, moist, damp; तन्त्रीमार्द्रां नयनसलिलैः Me. 88. 45; आर्द्राक्षतारोपणमन्वभूताम् R. 7. 28.<BR>—2 Succulent, living, not dry, green, juicy; आर्द्रं द्रव्यं द्विधा प्रोक्तं<BR> सरसं नीरसं तथा.<BR>—3 Fresh, new; कामीवार्द्रापराधः Amaru. 2; कान्तमार्द्रापराधम्<BR> M. 3. 12; R. 14. 4. आर्द्रमञ्जरी a cluster of fresh blossoms.<BR>—4 Soft, tender; oft. used with words like स्नेह, दया, करुणा in<BR> the sense of ‘flowing with’, ‘moved’, ‘melted’; स्नेहार्द्रं हृदयम्<BR> a heart wet or melted with pity; करुणा˚, दया˚; प्रेमार्द्राः चेष्टाः Māl. 5. 7.<BR>—5 Full of feeling, warm.<BR>—6 Loose, flaccid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रा
आर्द्र + .{@-र्द्रा@} N. of a constellation or the sixth lunar mansion so called<BR> (consisting of one star). [cf. Gr. <i>ardo</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आर्द्रैधाग्निः, आर्द्रकपोलितः, आर्द्रकाष्ठम्, आर्द्रदानु, आर्द्रनयन, आर्द्रपटिन्, आर्द्रपत्रकः, आर्द्रपदी, आर्द्रपवित्र, आर्द्रपृष्ठ, आर्द्रभावः, आर्द्रमाषा, आर्द्रशाकम्, आर्द्रलुब्धकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रैधाग्निः|आर्द्रैधाग्नि
आर्द्र + -एधाग्निः a fire maintained by wet wood; यथैवार्द्रैधाग्नेः पृथग्धूमा<BR> विनिश्चरन्ति Śat. Br.; Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रकपोलितः
आर्द्र + -कपोलितः The designation of an elephant in the second stage<BR> of rut. (cf. Mātaṅga L. 9. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रकाष्ठम्
आर्द्र + -काष्ठम् green wood.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">Page0356-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0355-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रदानु
आर्द्र + -दानु <i>a.</i> Ved. giving moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रनयन
आर्द्र + -नयन <i>a.</i> weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रपटिन्
आर्द्र + -पटिन् An exorciser clad in red cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रपत्रकः|आर्द्रपत्रक
आर्द्र + -पत्रकः Bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रपदी
आर्द्र + -पदी a woman with wet feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रपवित्र
आर्द्र + -पवित्र <i>a.</i> Ved. having a wet strainer, epithet of the soma;<BR> सर्वदा वा एष युक्तग्रावार्द्रपावित्रः Av. 9. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रपृष्ठ
आर्द्र + -पृष्ठ <i>a.</i> watered, refreshed; आर्द्रपृष्टाः क्रियन्तां वाजिनः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रभावः|आर्द्रभाव
आर्द्र + -भावः<BR>—1 wetness, dampness.<BR>—2 Tenderness of heart; धनुर्भृतोऽप्यस्य दयार्द्रभावम् R. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रमाषा
आर्द्र + -माषा <i>f.</i>^1 leguminous shrub (माषपर्णी; Mar. रानौडीद).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रशाकम्
आर्द्र + -शाकम् fresh ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रलुब्धकः
आर्द्र + -लुब्धकः (˚र्द्रा˚) ‘the dragonʼs tail or descending node’, N. of Ketu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रता
आर्द्रता Wetness, moisture, freshness, tenderness, softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रक|आर्द्रकं
आर्द्रक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आर्द्रा-वुन्] Born under the constellation Ārdrā;<BR> cf. P. IV. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रकम्
आर्द्रक + .{@-कम्@} Ginger in its undried state, wet ginger (Mar. आलें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रयति
आर्द्रयति Den. P. To wet, moisten; केचिद् वृष्टिभिरार्द्रयन्ति वसुधाम् Bh. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रिका
आर्द्रिका Wet ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धम्
आर्द्धम् Abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ध
आर्ध <i>a.</i> (Only used at the beginning of comp.) Half.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आर्धधातुक, आर्धनारीश्वरम्, आर्धप्रस्थिक, आर्धकंसिक, आर्धमासिक, आर्धरात्रिकाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धधातुक
आर्ध + -धातुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> (In gram.) applicable to half the root or to the<BR> shorter form of the verbal base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धधातुकम्
आर्ध + -धातुक + .({@-कम्@}) a name given to those terminations and affixes which belong<BR> to the six non-conjugational or general tenses (opp. सार्व. धातुक);<BR> cf. P. III. 4. 114, I. 1. 4, II. 4. 35, VII. 2. 35 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धनारीश्वरम्
आर्ध + -नारीश्वरम् The story of the lord Śiva in his form as अर्धनारीश्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धप्रस्थिक
आर्ध + -प्रस्थिक, -कंसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> bought with half a Prastha or Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धकंसिक
आर्ध + -प्रस्थिक, -कंसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> bought with half a Prastha or Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धमासिक
आर्ध + -मासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> lasting for half a month, observing or practising<BR> (penance &c.) for a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धरात्रिकाः
आर्ध + -रात्रिकाः (pl.) N. of an astronomical school who reckoned the<BR> beginning of the motions of the planets from midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धिक|आर्धिकः
आर्धिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अर्धमर्हति ठक्] Sharing half, relating to a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धिकः|आर्धिक
आर्धिक + .{@-कः@} One who ploughs the land for half the crop; one born of a<BR> Vaiśya woman, and brought up by a Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 4. 253; see the quotation<BR> under अर्धिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धुक
आर्धुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Ved.<BR> Conducive to success, beneficial, profitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्पयितृ
आर्पयितृ <i>m.</i> Ved. One who injures or hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्भव
आर्भव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging or sacred to the Ṛbhus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्य|आर्य्यः
आर्य <i>a.</i> [ऋ-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 Āryan, an inhabitant of आर्यावर्त, N. of the race migrated into<BR> India in Vedic times.<BR>—2 Worthy of an Ārya.<BR>—3 Worthy, venerable, respectable, honourable, noble, high; यदार्यमस्यामभिलाषि<BR> मे मनः Ś. 1. 22; R. 2. 33; so आर्यवेषः respectable dress; oft.<BR> used in theatrical language as an honorific adjective and a respectful<BR> mode of address; आर्यचाणक्यः, आर्या अरुन्धती &c.; आर्य revered<BR> or honoured Sir; आर्ये revered or honoured lady. The following rules are laid down<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">Page0356-2</a>]<BR> for the use of आर्य in addressing persons:− (1) वाच्यौ नटीसूत्रधारावार्यनाम्ना<BR> परस्परम् । (2) वयस्येत्युत्तमैर्वाच्यो मध्यैरार्येति चाग्रजः । (3)<BR> (वक्तव्यो) अमात्य आर्येति चेतरैः । (4) स्वेच्छया नामभिर्विप्रैर्विप्र आर्येति चेतरैः । S. D. 431.<BR>—4 Noble, fine, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यः|आर्य|आर्य्य|आर्य्यः
आर्य + .{@-र्यः@}<BR>—1 N. of the Hindu and Iranian people, as distinguished from अनार्य,<BR> दस्यु and दास; विजानीह्यार्यान्ये च दस्यवः Rv. 1. 51. 8.<BR>—2 A man who is faithful to the religion and laws of his country; कर्तव्यमाचरन्<BR> कार्यमकर्तव्यमनाचरन् । तिष्ठति प्रकृताचारे स वा आर्य इति स्मृतः ॥<BR>—3 N. of the first three castes (as opp. to शूद्र).<BR>—4 respectable or honourable man, esteemed person; वृत्तेन हि भवत्यार्यो<BR> न धनेन न विद्यया Mb.; परमार्यः परमां कृपां बभार Bu. C. 5. 6.<BR>—5 A man of noble birth.<BR>—6 A man of noble character.<BR>—7 A master, owner.<BR>—8 A preceptor; वैमानिकार्यसमभूमा Viś. Guṇā. 124; Mu. 3. 33.<BR>—9 A friend.<BR>—10 A Vaiśya.<BR>—11 A father-in-law (as in आर्यपुत्र).<BR>—12 A Buddha.<BR>—13 (With the Buddhists) A man who has thought on the four chief principles<BR> of Buddhism and lives according to them.<BR>—14 A son of Manu Sāvarṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्या|आर्य्या
आर्य + .{@-र्या@}<BR>—1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—2 A mother-in-law.<BR>—3 A respectable woman; यत्रार्या रुदती भीता पाण्डवानिदमब्रवीत् Mb. 3. 12. 87.<BR>—4 N. of a metre; राजानमुद्दिश्य आर्यामिमां पपाठ K. {@˚गीतिः@}<BR> <i>f.</i> A variety of the Āryā metre, see Appendix.<BR>—5 That which comes from truth; आराद् याता तत्त्वेभ्य इति आर्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यम्
आर्य + .{@-र्यम्@}<BR>—1 Virtue, sacredness; नहि दुष्टात्मनामार्यमावसत्यालये चिरम् Rām. 3. 50. 12.<BR>—2 Discrimination (विवेक); कोपमार्येण यो हन्ति स वीरः पुरुषोत्तमः<BR> Rām. 4. 31. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आर्याष्टशतम्, आर्यागमः, आर्यावर्तः, आर्यगृह्य, आर्यजुष्ट, आर्यदेशः, आर्यपुत्रः, आर्यप्राय, आर्यबलः, आर्यभट्टः, आर्यभावः, आर्यमतिः, आर्यमार्गः, आर्यमिश्र, आर्ययुवन्, आर्यरूप, आर्यलिङ्गिन्, आर्यवाक्, आर्यवृत्त, आर्यवेश, आर्यव्रत, आर्यशील, आर्यश्वेतः, आर्यसंघः, आर्यसत्यम्, आर्यसिद्धान्तः, आर्यस्त्री, आर्यहलम्, आर्यहृद्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्याष्टशतम्
आर्य + -अष्टशतम् title of a work of Ārya Bhaṭṭa consisting of eight<BR> hundred verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यागमः|आर्यागम
आर्य + -आगमः The approaching an Ārya woman sexually; अन्त्यस्यार्यागमे<BR> वधः Y. 2. 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यावर्तः|आर्यावर्त|आर्यावर्त्त|आर्य्यावर्त्त|आर्य्यावर्त्तः
आर्य + -आवर्तः [आर्याम् आवर्तन्ते अत्र] ‘abode of the noble or excellent (Āryas)’<BR>; particularly N. of the tract extending from the eastern to<BR> the western ocean, and bounded on the north and south by the Himālaya<BR> and Vindhya respectively; cf. Ms. 2. 22; आ समुद्रात्तु वै पूर्वादा समुद्राच्च<BR> पश्चिमात् । तयोरेवान्तरं गिर्योः (हिमवद्विन्ध्ययोः) आर्यावर्तं<BR> विदुर्बुधाः ॥; also 10. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यगृह्य|आर्य्यगृह्य
आर्य + -गृह्य <i>a.</i> [आर्यस्य गृह्यः पक्षः]<BR>—1 to be respected by the noble.<BR>—2 a friend of the noble, readily accessible to honourable men; तमार्यगृह्यं<BR> निगृहीतधेनुः R. 2. 33.<BR>—3 respectable, right, decorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यजुष्ट
आर्य + -जुष्ट <i>a.</i> liked by or agreeable to noble ones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यदेशः|आर्यदेश|आर्य्यदेश
आर्य + -देशः a country inhabited by the Āryas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यपुत्रः|आर्यपुत्र|आर्य्यपुत्त्रः|आर्य्यपुत्र
आर्य + -पुत्रः<BR>—1 son of an honourable man.<BR>—2 the son of a spiritual preceptor.<BR>—3 honorific designation of the son of the elder brother; of a husband<BR> by his wife; or of a prince by his general &c.<BR>—4 the son of the father-in law, <i>i. e.</i> a husband (occurring in every<BR> drama; mostly in the vocative case in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यप्राय|आर्य्यप्राय
आर्य + -प्राय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inhabited by the Āryas. —2 abounding with respectable people; Ms. 7. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यबलः|आर्यबल
आर्य + -बलः N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यभट्टः|आर्यभट्ट|आर्य्यभट्ट
आर्य + -भट्टः N. of a renowned astronomer, the inventor of Algebra among<BR> the Hindus; he flourished before the 5th century of the Christian era.<BR> Hence his work is called आर्यभटीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यभावः|आर्यभाव
आर्य + -भावः honourable character or behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यमतिः|आर्यमति
आर्य + -मतिः One having a noble<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">Page0357-1</a>]<BR> intellect; संक्षिप्तमार्यमतिना Sāṅ. K. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0356-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यमार्गः|आर्यमार्ग
आर्य + -मार्गः the path or course of the respectable, a respectable way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्रः|आर्य्यमिश्र|आर्य्यमिश्रः
आर्य + -मिश्र <i>a.</i> respectable, worthy, distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यमिश्रः|आर्यमिश्र|आर्य्यमिश्र|आर्य्यमिश्रः
आर्य + -मिश्र + .({@-श्रः@}) a gentleman, a man of consequence; (pl.) —1 worthy or respectable<BR> men, an assembly of honourable men; आर्यमिश्रान् विज्ञापयामि V. 1.<BR>—2 your reverence or honour (a respectful address); नन्वार्यमिश्रैः प्रथममेव<BR> आज्ञप्तम् Ś. 1; आर्यमिश्राः प्रमाणम् M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ययुवन्
आर्य + -युवन् <i>m.</i> an Āryan youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यरूप|आर्य्यरूप
आर्य + -रूप <i>a.</i> having only the form of an Āryan, a hypocrite, impostor;<BR> आर्यरूपमिवानार्यं कर्मभिः स्वैर्विभावयेत् Ms. 10. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यलिङ्गिन्|आर्य्यलिङ्गिन्
आर्य + -लिङ्गिन् <i>m.</i> an impostor; Ms. 9. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवाक्
आर्य + -वाक् <i>a.</i> speaking the Āryan language; म्लेच्छवाचश्चार्यवाचः<BR> सर्वे ते दस्यवः स्मृताः Ms. 10. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवृत्त|आर्य्यवृत्त
आर्य + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> virtuous, good, pious; Ms. 9. 253; R. 14. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवृत्तम्
आर्य + -वृत्त + .({@-त्तम्@}) the conduct of an Āryan or nobleman; Ms. 4. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवेश|आर्य्यवेश
आर्य + -वेश <i>a.</i> well-clothed, having a respectable dress, fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यव्रत|आर्य्यव्रत
आर्य + -व्रत <i>a.</i> observing the laws and ordinances of the Āryans or noblemen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यव्रतम्
आर्य + -व्रत + .({@-तम्@}) the duty of an Aryan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यशील
आर्य + -शील <i>a.</i> Having an honest character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यश्वेतः|आर्यश्वेत|आर्य्यश्वेत
आर्य + -श्वेतः a noble or honourable man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यसंघः|आर्यसङ्घ
आर्य + -संघः the whole body of the Āryans, especially Buddhists; it<BR> is also the name of a renowned philosopher (founder of the school of Yogācāras).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यसत्यम्
आर्य + -सत्यम् a noble or sublime truth; [there are four such truths<BR> forming the chief principles of Buddhism. In Pāli they are called चत्तारि<BR> अरियसच्चानि. They are, (1) life is suffering, (2) Desire of life is<BR> the cause of suffering, (3) Extinction of that desire is the cessation<BR> of suffering, (4) The eight-fold path leads to that extinction.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यसिद्धान्तः|आर्यसिद्धान्त
आर्य + -सिद्धान्तः N. of a work of आर्यभट्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यस्त्री
आर्य + -स्त्री An Āryan woman, or a woman of the first three castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यहलम्|आर्य्यहलम्
आर्य + -हलम् <i>ind.</i> forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यहृद्य|आर्य्यहृद्य
आर्य + -हृद्य <i>a.</i> liked by the noble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यकः|आर्यक|आर्य्यक|आर्य्यकं|आर्य्यकः
आर्यकः [आर्य-स्वार्थे-कन्]<BR>—1 An honourable or respectable man.<BR>—2 A grandfather; बलेन गुप्तो भरतो महात्मा सहार्यकस्यात्मसमैरमात्यैः<BR> Rām. 2. 70. 30.<BR>—3 N. of a cowherd who became a king; cf. Mk. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यकम्
आर्यकः + .{@-कम्@} A ceremony performed to the Manes or the vessel used in sacrifices to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यका|आर्य्यका
आर्यका, आर्यिका<BR>—1 A respectable woman.<BR>—2 N. of a Nakṣatra. —3 N. of a river; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यिका|आर्य्यिका
आर्यका, आर्यिका<BR>—1 A respectable woman.<BR>—2 N. of a Nakṣatra. —3 N. of a river; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यवम्
आर्यवम् Honourable behaviour; honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्वाक्|आर्व्वाक्
आर्वाक् <i>ind.</i> After, afterwards; behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्श
आर्श <i>a.</i> Belonging to the antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष|आर्षः
आर्ष <i>a.</i> (-र्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋषेरिदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Used by a Ṛṣi only, relating or belonging to sages, beneficial to<BR> sages; शमो दमस्तथा धैर्यं सत्यं शौचमथार्जवम् । यज्ञो घृतिश्च धर्मश्च<BR> नित्यमार्षो विधिः स्मृतः ॥ Mb. 12. 12. 17; archaic, Vedic (opp. लौकिक<BR> or classical); आर्षः प्रयोगः; संबुद्धौ शाकल्यस्येतावनार्षे P. I. 1. 16<BR> Sk.; आर्षो धर्मः Ms. 3. 29; Y. 1. 59; आर्षः प्रत्ययः P. II. 4. 58.<BR>—2 Sacred, holy, divine, superhuman; आदिकाव्यमिदं चार्षं पुरा वाल्मीकिना<BR> कृतम् Rām. 6. 128. 105; U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षः|आर्ष
आर्ष + .{@-र्षः@} A form of marriage derived from the Ṛṣis; one of the eight<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">Page0357-2</a>]<BR> forms of marriage in which the father of the bride receives one or two<BR> pairs of cows from the bridegroom; आदायार्षस्तु गोद्वयम् Y. 1. 59;<BR> Ms. 3. 53, 9. 196; for the names of the 8 forms see उद्वाह; आर्षोढा<BR> a wife married according to this form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षा
आर्ष + .{@-र्षा@} A class of Vedic metres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षम्
आर्ष + .{@-र्षम्@}<BR>—1 The holy text, the Vedas; आर्षं धर्मोपदेशं च वेदशास्त्राविरोधिना Ms. 12. 106.<BR>—2 Sacred descent.<BR>—3 Derivation (of a poem) from a Ṛṣi author. {@आर्षंधरम्@} N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षिक्यम्
आर्षिक्यम् (= आर्षो धर्मः) The धर्म as laid down by the Ṛṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेय
आर्षेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋषि-ढक्]<BR>—1 Relating to a Ṛṣi.<BR>—2 Worthy, venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेयम्
आर्षेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Sacred descent; नानार्षेयप्रवरान्समेतानभ्यर्त्त्य राजा शिरसा ववन्दे<BR> Bhāg. 1. 19. 11.<BR>—2 A collection of Ṛṣis (ऋषिसमूहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ
आर्षभ <i>a.</i> (-भी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ऋषभ-अण्] Derived from or produced by a bull;<BR> मोघं स्कन्दितमार्षभम् Ms. 9. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभिः|आर्षभि
आर्षभिः N. of king Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ्यः|आर्षभ्य
आर्षभ्यः [ऋषभ-ञ्य] A steer sufficiently full-grown to be used<BR> or let loose, one fit to be castrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत|आर्हतः
आर्हत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अर्हत्-अण्] Belonging to the Jaina doctrines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हतः|आर्हत
आर्हत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A Jaina, a follower of Jaina doctrines.<BR>—2 A Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हतम्
आर्हत + .{@-तम्@} The doctrines of Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत्यम्
आर्हत्यम् The quality or practice of an Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हन्ती
आर्हन्ती, -न्त्यम्<BR> [P. V. 1. 124. Vārt.] Fitness; श्रौत्रार्हन्ती चणैर्गुण्यैर्महर्षिभिरहर्निशम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हन्त्यम्
आर्हन्ती, -न्त्यम्<BR> [P. V. 1. 124. Vārt.] Fitness; श्रौत्रार्हन्ती चणैर्गुण्यैर्महर्षिभिरहर्निशम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आल|आलं|आलः
आल <i>a.</i> [आ-अल्-पर्याप्तौ अच्] Large, extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलः|आल|आलं
आल + .{@-लः, -लम्@}<BR>—1 Spawn, any discharge of venomous matter from poisonous animals; ˚अक्त<BR> anointed with poison as an arrow.<BR>—2 Trick, fraud; येषां श्रुतमालजालाय K. 288; ˚जालानि चिन्तयन्ती 310.<BR>—3 Yellow arsenic, orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्
आल + .{@-लः, -लम्@}<BR>—1 Spawn, any discharge of venomous matter from poisonous animals; ˚अक्त<BR> anointed with poison as an arrow.<BR>—2 Trick, fraud; येषां श्रुतमालजालाय K. 288; ˚जालानि चिन्तयन्ती 310.<BR>—3 Yellow arsenic, orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलकन्दकम्
