आलक्ष्
आलक्ष् €10 U. To descry, behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्षि
आलक्षि <i>a.</i> [लक्ष्-इन्] Knowing, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्य
आलक्ष्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Visible, apparent; आलक्ष्यपारिप्लवसारसानि R. 13. 30.<BR>—2 Slightly visible; ˚दन्तमुकुलान् Ś. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्षण्यम्
आलक्षण्यम् [अलक्षणस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Misfortune, crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलग्न
आलग्न <i>a.</i> Adhered, clung to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलगर्दः|आलगर्द|आलगर्द्द|आलगर्द्दः
आलगर्दः [अलगर्द एव स्वार्थे अण्] A water cobra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलप्
आलप् €1 P. To address, speak to, converse; कमालपामि K. 164;<BR> तस्या नामधेयेन भर्त्रा देव्यालपिता V. 2 addressed. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To talk with, engage in conversation with, to question; यदा कश्चित्त्वामालापयिष्यति<BR> Pt. 5, 1. 387; K. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापः|आलाप
आलापः<BR>—1 Talking, speaking to, speech, conversation; अये दक्षिणेन वृक्षवाटिकामालाप<BR> इव श्रूयते Ś. 1; प्रवसनालाप Amaru. 54; ललितालापे Śrut. 36.<BR>—2 Narration, mention.<BR>—3 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">Page0358-1</a>]<BR> seven notes in music (Mar. सा, रि, ग, म, प, ध, नि).<BR>—4 Statement of a question in an arithmetical or algebraical sum.<BR>—5 A question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापा
आलापः + .{@-पा@} A particular मूर्च्छना or melody in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0357-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापन
आलापन <i>a.</i> Causing to speak or converse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनम्
आलापन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Speaking to, conversation.<BR>—2 Congratulation (स्वस्तिवाचनम्); benediction; मङ्गलालापनैर्होमैः<BR> शोभिताः क्षौमवाससः Rām. 1. 77. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप्य|आलाप्यः
आलाप्य, -लापनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be spoken to, conversed with or narrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनीय
आलाप्य, -लापनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be spoken to, conversed with or narrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिन्
आलापिन् <i>a.</i> Speaking to, conversing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिनी
आलापिन् + .{@-नी@} A lute made of a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्
आलभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To touch; गामालभ्यार्कमीक्ष्य वा Ms. 5 87, 4. 117; Bk. 14. 91; सत्येनायुधमालभे;<BR> सत्येन (सत्यं) आत्मानमालभे Mb.<BR>—2 To get, attain to; अतितरां कान्तिमालप्स्यते ते (वपुः) Me. 15<BR> v. l.; Kām. 9. 63.<BR>—3 To kill, immolate (as a victim in sacrifices); प्रातर्वै पशूनालभन्ते<BR> Śat. Br.; गर्दभं पशुमालभ्य Y. 3. 280.<BR>—4 To take hold of, seize, grasp, handle.<BR>—5 To gain or win over. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To touch.<BR>—2 To commence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलब्ध
आलब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Touched; united or in contact with.<BR>—2 Killed.<BR>—3 Gained, Conciliated; एवं सामभिरालब्धः श्वफल्कतनयो मणिम् Bhāg. 10. 57. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलब्धिः|आलब्धि
आलब्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Touching.<BR>—2 Killing; immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभनम्
आलभनम्<BR>—1 Taking hold of, seizing.<BR>—2 Touching.<BR>—3 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
आलभ्य, आल(लम्)भनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be<BR> killed or sacrificed; to be touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभनीय
आलभ्य, आल(लम्)भनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be<BR> killed or sacrificed; to be touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भनीय|आलंभनीय
आलभ्य, आल(लम्)भनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be<BR> killed or sacrificed; to be touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भः|आलम्भ|आलंभः
आलम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR> [आ-लभ् घञ् ल्युट् मुम्]<BR>—1 Taking hold of, seizing, touching; स्त्र्यालोकालम्भविगमः Y. 3. 157; Ms. 2. 179.<BR>—2 Tearing off, uprooting (of plants); Ms. 11. 144.<BR>—3 Killing (especially an animal at a sacrifice); अश्वालम्भं गवालम्भम्<BR> Ādipurāṇa; आलम्भयज्ञाः क्षत्राश्च हविर्यज्ञा विशः स्मृताः । परिचारयज्ञाः<BR> शूद्रास्तु तपोयज्ञा द्विजातयः ॥ Mb. 12. 232. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भनम्
आलम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR> [आ-लभ् घञ् ल्युट् मुम्]<BR>—1 Taking hold of, seizing, touching; स्त्र्यालोकालम्भविगमः Y. 3. 157; Ms. 2. 179.<BR>—2 Tearing off, uprooting (of plants); Ms. 11. 144.<BR>—3 Killing (especially an animal at a sacrifice); अश्वालम्भं गवालम्भम्<BR> Ādipurāṇa; आलम्भयज्ञाः क्षत्राश्च हविर्यज्ञा विशः स्मृताः । परिचारयज्ञाः<BR> शूद्रास्तु तपोयज्ञा द्विजातयः ॥ Mb. 12. 232. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भिन्|आलंभिन्
आलम्भिन् <i>a.</i> Touching, seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब्|आलंब्
आलम्ब् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To rest or lean upon, support oneself on; शाखामालम्ब्य Rām.<BR>—2 To lay hold of, seize, take; अथालम्ब्य धनू रामः Bk. 6. 35, 14. 95.<BR>—3 To support, hold or take up; आथोरणालम्बितम् R. 18. 39.<BR>—4 To win, conquer, overcome; तस्य कविता मच्चित्तमालम्बते Dhūrt.<BR>—5 To resort to, have recourse to, take, assume; अमुमेवार्थमालम्ब्य<BR> Mu. 2. 20; स्वातन्त्र्यमालम्ब्य K. 181; Ki. 13. 14; यशः शरीरं<BR> नवमाललम्बे Mv. 7. 18 obtained; Ki. 17. 34; so ध्यानम्, धैर्यम्, क्रोधम्,<BR> औदास्यम्, दक्षिणाम् दिशम् &c.<BR>—6 To hang from, be suspended; मुखालम्बितहेमसूत्रम् V. 5. 2.<BR>—7 To depend upon; तमालम्ब्य रसोद्गमात् S. D. 63.<BR>—8 To stretch forth; V. 4. 62.<BR>—9 To strike up (a tune or note).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब|आलंब|आलम्बः
आलम्ब <i>a.</i> Hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बः|आलम्ब|आलंब
आलम्ब + .{@-बः@}<BR>—1 Depending on or from.<BR>—2 That on which one rests or leans, prop, stay; इह हि पततां नास्त्यालम्बा<BR> न चापि निवर्तनम् Śānti. 3. 2.<BR>—3 Support, protection; तवालम्बादम्ब स्फुरदलघुगर्वेण सहसा Jag.;<BR> सीतां शून्ये यथासुखं, निरालम्बां हरिष्यामि Rām.; अपश्यन्त निरालम्बं<BR> तं ययातिं परिच्युतम् Mb. 5. 121. 5.<BR>—4 Receptacle.<BR>—5 A perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बा
आलम्ब + .{@-बा@} N. of a plant with poisonous leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बनम्
आलम्बनम्<BR>—1 Depending on or from, hanging from.<BR>—2 Support, prop, stay; एतदालम्बनं श्रेष्ठमेतदालम्बनं परम् Kaṭh. 2. 17.<BR> Ki. 2. 13; जातस्य नदीतीरे तस्यापि तृणस्य जन्मसाफल्यम् ।<BR> यत्सलिलमज्जनाकुलजनहस्तावलम्बनं भवति ॥ Pt. 1. 28; sustaining,<BR> supporting; Me. 4.<BR>—3 Receptacle, abode; U. 6. 10 (v. l.).<BR>—4 Reason, cause.<BR>—5 Base.<BR>—6 (In Rhet.) That on which a रस or sentiment, as it were, hangs,<BR> person or thing with reference to which a sentiment arises, the natural<BR> and necessary connection of sentiment with the cause which excites it.<BR> The causes (विभाव) giving rise to a <i>Rasa</i> are classified as<BR> two:− आलम्बन and उद्दीपन; <i>e. g.</i> in the Bībhatsa sentiment<BR> stinking flesh &c. is the आलम्बन of the <i>Rasa</i>, and the attendant<BR> circumstances which enhance the feeling of loathing (the worms &c. in<BR> the flesh) are its उद्दीपनानि (exciters); for the other <i>Rasas</i> see S. D. 210-238.<BR>—8 The mental exercise practised by the Yogin in endeavouring to bring<BR> before his thoughts the gross form of the Eternal.<BR>—9 Silent repetition of a prayer.<BR>—10 (With Buddhists) The five attributes of things corresponding to five<BR> senses, <i>i. e.</i> रूप, रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श and शब्द.<BR>—11 <i>Dharma</i> or law corresponding to <i>manas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बित|आलंबित
आलम्बित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pendent, suspended.<BR>—2 Supported, sustained, held; R. 7. 7; मुखालम्बितहेमसूत्रम् V. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बिन्|आलंबिन्
आलम्बिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hanging from, resting or leaning upon; दशालम्बी शाटकः Pt. 1. 144;<BR> depending on; देवसूतभुजालम्बी R. 12. 35.<BR>—2 Laying hold of, supporting, maintaining, upholding; कुलालम्बी पुत्रः H. Pr. 20.<BR>—3 Wearing; गजाजिनालम्बि Ku. 5. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलर्क
आलर्क <i>a.</i> [अलर्कस्येदम् अण्] Relating to or caused by a mad<BR> dog; आलर्कं विषमिव सर्वतः प्रसृप्तम् U. 1. 40; निहन्ति विषमालर्कं<BR> मेघवृन्दमिवानिलः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवण्यम्
आलवण्यम् [अलवणस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Insipidity, tastelessness.<BR>—2 Ugliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवालम्
आलवालम् [आसमन्तात् लवं जललबम् आलाति, आ-ला-क Tv.] A basin<BR> or trench for water (round the root of a tree); ˚पूरणे नियुक्ता Ś. 1;<BR> विश्वासाय विहङ्गानामालवालाम्बुपायिनाम् R. 1. 51. विपुलालवालभृतवारिदर्पणः Śi. 13. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस|आलसः
आलस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आलसति ईषत् व्याप्रियते अच्] Idle, lazy, slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्य|आलस्यं|आलस्यः
आलस्य <i>a.</i> Idle, slothful, apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्यम्
आलस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} [अलसस्य भावः, ष्यञ्] —1 Idleness, sloth, want of energy;<BR> प्रमादालस्य-निद्राभिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">Page0359-1</a>]<BR> Bg. 14. 8. शक्तस्य चाप्यनुत्साहः कर्मस्वालस्यमुच्यते Suśr.; आलस्यं<BR> हि मनुष्याणां शरीरस्थो महारिपुः Bh. 2. 86. आलस्य ‘want of energy’<BR> is regarded as one of the 33 subordinate feelings (व्यभिचारि भाव);<BR> for example:− न तथा भूषयत्यङ्गं न तथा भाषते सखीम् । जृम्भते मुहुरासीना<BR> बाला गर्भभरालसा S. D. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0358-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलातम्
आलातम्^1 [अलातमेव स्वार्थे अण्] A fire-brand.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: because from अलातम् without न्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलानम्
आलानम् [आलीयतेऽत्र, आ-ली-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The post to which an elephant is tied; tying post, also the rope that<BR> ties him; अरुंतुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य दन्तिनः R. 1. 71, 4. 69, 81;<BR> आलाने गृह्यते हस्ती Mk. 1. 50; वन्या इव विनालानं क्रीडन्तु करिणो<BR> मम Śiva B. 19. 19, 20. 52.<BR>—2 A fetter, tie.<BR>—3 A chain, rope, string.<BR>—4 Tying, binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलानिक
आलानिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आलान-ठक्] Serving as a post to which an elephant<BR> is tied; आलानिकं स्थाणुमिव द्विपेन्द्रः R. 14. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबुः|आलाबु
आलाबुः(बूः) <i>f.</i> A pumpkin gourd; see अलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबूः
आलाबुः(बूः) <i>f.</i> A pumpkin gourd; see अलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलावर्तम्
आलावर्तम् A fan made of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलास्यः|आलास्य
आलास्यः [अलं पर्याप्तमास्यम् अस्य] A crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलि|आलिः
आलि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Useless, idle, unmeaning.<BR>—2 Honest, sincere (विशदाशय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिः|आलि
आलि + .{@-लिः@}<BR>—1 A scorpion.<BR>—2 A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिः|आलि
आलि + .{@-लिः, -ली@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A female companion or friend (of a woman); निवार्यतामालि किमप्ययं<BR> बटुः Ku. 5. 83, 7. 68; Amaru. 28.<BR>—2 A row, range, continuous line; (cf. आवलि); तोयान्तर्भास्करालीव<BR> रेजे मुनिपरम्परा Ku. 6. 49; रथ्यालि Amaru. 89; खद्योतालि Me. 83.<BR>—3 A line, streak.<BR>—4 A bridge.<BR>—5 A dike.<BR>—6 A line, race, family.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आलिक्रमः, आलिजनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आलि + .{@-लिः, -ली@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A female companion or friend (of a woman); निवार्यतामालि किमप्ययं<BR> बटुः Ku. 5. 83, 7. 68; Amaru. 28.<BR>—2 A row, range, continuous line; (cf. आवलि); तोयान्तर्भास्करालीव<BR> रेजे मुनिपरम्परा Ku. 6. 49; रथ्यालि Amaru. 89; खद्योतालि Me. 83.<BR>—3 A line, streak.<BR>—4 A bridge.<BR>—5 A dike.<BR>—6 A line, race, family.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आलिक्रमः, आलिजनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिक्रमः|आलिक्रम
आलि + -क्रमः A kind of musical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिजनः|आलिजन
आलि + -जनः A ladyʼs female friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिख्
आलिख् €6 P.<BR>—1 To write, delineate, draw lines; मनो निष्ठाशून्यं भ्रमति च किमप्यालिखति<BR> च Māl. 1. 31; Mk. 2.<BR>—2 To paint, draw in a picture; आलिखित इव सर्वतो रङ्गः Ś. 1;<BR> V. 2; त्वामालिख्य प्रणयकुपिताम् Me. 107; R. 19. 19; M. 2. 2.<BR>—3 To portray, write, sketch.<BR>—4 To scratch, scrape, touch; as in विन्ध्यमालिखन्तमिवाम्बरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखः|आलेख
आलेखः<BR>—1 Writing.<BR>—2 A letter, document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखनम्
आलेखनम् <i>n.</i>^1 Scratching, painting.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखनी
आलेखनम् + .{@-नी@} A brush, pencil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखनम्
आलेखनम् + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Writing.<BR>—2 Painting.<BR>—3 Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखनः|आलेखन|आलेखनं
आलेखनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of an old authority quoted by Jaimini; MS. 6. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्य|आलेख्यं
आलेख्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be written, painted &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यम्
आलेख्य + .{@-ख्यम्@}<BR>—1 A painting, picture; इति संरम्भिणो वाणीर्बलस्यालेख्यदेवताः Śi. 2. 67;<BR> R. 3. 15; V. 2. 10.<BR>—2 A writing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आलेख्यलेखा, आलेख्यशेष, आलेख्यसमर्पित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यलेखा
आलेख्य + -लेखा a painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यशेष|आलेख्यशेषः
आलेख्य + -शेष <i>a.</i> having nothing left but a painting, <i>i. e.</i> deceased,<BR> dead; आलेख्यशेषस्य पितुः R. 14. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यसमर्पित
आलेख्य + -समर्पित <i>a.</i> Fixed on a picture, painted; निशीथदीपाः सहसा<BR> हतत्विषो बभूवुरालेख्यसमर्पिता इव R. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्|आलिंग्
आलिङ्ग् €1 U. or €10 P. To embrace, clasp, encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गः|आलिङ्ग|आलिंगः
आलिङ्गः<BR>—1 Embracing.<BR>—2 A kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गनम्
आलिङ्गनम् Embracing, clasping, an embrace; (संप्राप) आलिङ्गननिर्वृत्तिम्<BR> R. 12. 65; (said to be of seven kinds:− आमोद˚, मुदित˚, प्रेमन्˚, मानस˚,<BR> रुचि˚, मदन˚ and विनोद˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गित|आलिंगित|आलिङ्गितः
आलिङ्गित <i>p. p.</i> Embraced, clasped; योगो नाभ्यसितो व्रतं न<BR> चरितं नालिङ्गिता कामिनी S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गितः|आलिङ्गित|आलिंगित
आलिङ्गित + .{@-तः@} A kind of Mantra of 20 letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गितम्
आलिङ्गित + .{@-तम्@} An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गिन्|आलिंगिन्
आलिङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> Embracing &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गी
आलिङ्गिन् + .({@-गी@}), {@आलिङ्ग्यः@} A small drum shaped like a barley-corn<BR> (यव); चतुरङ्गुलहीनोंक्यान्मुखे चैकाङ्गुलेन यः । यवाकृतिः स<BR> आलिङ्ग्य आलिङ्ग्य स हि वाद्यते ॥ Śabdārṇava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिञ्जरः|आलिञ्जर|आलिंजर|आलिंजरः
आलिञ्जरः [अलिञ्जर एव स्वार्थे अण्] A large earthen waterjar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्दः|आलिन्द|आलिंद|आलिंदः
आलिन्दः, -दकः<BR> [अलिन्द एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 A terrace before a house.<BR>—2 A raised place for sleeping upon; see अलिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्दकः|आलिन्दक|आलिंदकः
आलिन्दः, -दकः<BR> [अलिन्द एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 A terrace before a house.<BR>—2 A raised place for sleeping upon; see अलिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्
आलिन् <i>m.</i> A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप्
आलिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To anoint, besmear; आलिम्पन्नमृतमयैरिव प्रलेपैः U. 3. 39; plaster, bedaub.<BR>—2 To rub (on the body); आलिप्यते चन्दनमङ्गनाभिः Ṛs. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप
आलिप <i>a.</i> Anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिम्पनम्
आलिम्पनम् [लिप्-ल्युट्-मुम्] Whitening the walls, floor &c. on festive<BR> occasions; cf. आदीपन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप्त
आलिप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Anointed.<BR>—2 Smeared, plastered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेप|आलेपः
आलेप <i>a.</i> To be anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेपः|आलेप
आलेप + .{@-पः, -पनम्@}<BR>—1 Anointing, smearing.<BR>—2 Liniment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेपनम्
आलेप + .{@-पः, -पनम्@}<BR>—1 Anointing, smearing.<BR>—2 Liniment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिह्
आलिह् €2 Ā. To lick, lap. see आलीढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली = आलि q. v. भास्करालीव रेजे मुनिपरंपरा Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To settle down upon; निर्भिद्योपरि कर्णिकारकुसुमान्यालीयते षट्पदः V. 2. 23.<BR>—2 To faint; मुहूरालीयते भीता Mb.<BR>—3 To melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलयः|आलय|आलयं
आलयः, -यम्<BR> [आलीयतेऽस्मिन्, आली-अच्]<BR>—1 An abode, a house, a dwelling; आलयं देवशत्रूणां सुघोरं खाण्डवं<BR> वनम् Mb. 1. 223. 75; न हि दुष्टात्मनामार्या निवसन्त्यालये चिरम्<BR> Rām.; सर्वाञ्जनस्थानकृतालयान् Rām. who lived or dwelt in Janasthāna.<BR>—2 A village; मन्दरस्य च ये कोटिं संश्रिताः केचिदालयाः Rām. 4. 40. 25.<BR>—3 A receptacle, seat, place; हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1;<BR> so देवालयम्, विद्यालयम् &c.; fig. also; दुःख˚ Bg. 8. 15; गुण˚.<BR>—4 Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलयम्
आलयः, -यम्<BR> [आलीयतेऽस्मिन्, आली-अच्]<BR>—1 An abode, a house, a dwelling; आलयं देवशत्रूणां सुघोरं खाण्डवं<BR> वनम् Mb. 1. 223. 75; न हि दुष्टात्मनामार्या निवसन्त्यालये चिरम्<BR> Rām.; सर्वाञ्जनस्थानकृतालयान् Rām. who lived or dwelt in Janasthāna.<BR>—2 A village; मन्दरस्य च ये कोटिं संश्रिताः केचिदालयाः Rām. 4. 40. 25.<BR>—3 A receptacle, seat, place; हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1;<BR> so देवालयम्, विद्यालयम् &c.; fig. also; दुःख˚ Bg. 8. 15; गुण˚.<BR>—4 Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलयम्
आलयः, -यम् + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Till destruction, death; पिबत भागवतं रसमालयम् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीन
आलीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Embraced.<BR>—2 Sticking or clinging to; आलीनचन्दनौ R. 4. 51; so ˚भ्रमरे पद्मे.<BR>—3 Melted, fused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीनम्
आलीन + .{@-नम्, -नकम्@}<BR>—1 Tin.<BR>—2 Lead.<BR>—3 Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीनकम्
आलीन + .{@-नम्, -नकम्@}<BR>—1 Tin.<BR>—2 Lead.<BR>—3 Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढ|आलीढं
आलीढ <i>p. p.</i> [आ-लिह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Licked, eaten, lapped, scraped.<BR>—2 Wounded, hurt; सेनान्यमालीढमिवासुरास्त्रैः R. 2. 37.<BR>—3 Closed (as in sleep) Dk. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढम्
आलीढ + .{@-ढम्@} A particular attitude in shooting, the right knee being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">Page0360-1</a>]<BR> advanced and the left leg retracted; अतिष्ठदालीढविशेषशोभिना R. 3. 52;<BR> see Malli. on Ku. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0359-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढकम्
आलीढकम् The frolicing of a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढा
आलीढा A woman in menstruation; नालीढ्या परिहतं भक्षयीत कदाचन<BR> Mb. 18. 104. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुः|आलु
आलुः<BR>—1 An owl.<BR>—2 An esculent root (not applied to potato &c.).<BR>—3 Ebony; black ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुः|आलु
आलुः + .{@-लुः@} <i>f.</i> A pitcher, waterjar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलु|आलुः
आलुः + .{@-लु@} <i>n.</i> A raft, float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुकः|आलुक|आलुकं
आलुकः<BR>—1 A kind of ebony (कामालु).<BR>—2 An epithet of Śeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुकम्
आलुकः + .{@-कम्@} An esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुञ्चनम्
आलुञ्चनम् Rending, tearing to pieces; श्येनो ग्रहालुञ्चने Mk. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुड्
आलुड् €1 P. or. <i>Caus.</i> To stir up, agitate, shake, disturb; कौरववनमालोडयन्तौ<BR> Ve. 3, 4; विषमालोड्य पास्यामि Mb.; (fig.) to dive into; Pt. 1; to<BR> examine scrutinizingly; भरतादिमतं सर्वमालोड्यातिप्रयत्नतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडनम्
आलोडनम्<BR>—1 Stirring, shaking, agitating.<BR>—2 Mixing, blending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडित
आलोडित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken, agitated.<BR>—2 Mixed, blended.<BR>—3 Powdered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुण्टनम्
आलुण्टनम् Plundering, taking away by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुल
आलुल <i>a.</i> Shaking, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुलित
आलुलित <i>a.</i> A little moved or agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलू
आलू See आलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलून
आलून <i>p. p.</i> Cut, cut off; तेनामरवधूहस्तैः सदयालूनपल्लवाः Ku. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेपकः|आलेपक
आलेपकः A mason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोक्
आलोक् €1 Ā., €10 P.<BR>—1 To see, perceive. behold; त्वन्मार्गमालोकते S. D.; अथालुलोके<BR> तपोवनम् Bk. 2. 24; used in an astrological sense also.<BR>—2 To consider, regard, contemplate; तृणमिव जगज्जालमालोकयामः Bh. 3. 66.<BR>—3 To express congratulations, greet; इति वीरलोक आलोकयितुं प्रवृत्तः Ve. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकः|आलोक
आलोकः, -कनम्<BR>—1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>—2 Sight, aspect. appearance; यदालोके सूक्ष्मम् Ś. 1. 9; Ku. 7. 22, 46;<BR> व्रजति हि सफलत्वं वल्लभालोकनेन Śi. सुख˚ V. 4. 24;<BR> Ś. 1. 32; R. 1. 84; Me. 3, 39.<BR>—3 Range of sight; आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला वा Me. 87;<BR> R. 7. 5; Ku. 2. 45.<BR>—4 Light, lustre, splendour; आलोकमार्गं सहसा व्रजन्त्या R. 7. 6<BR> air-hole, or window; निरालोकं लोकम् Māl. 5. 30, 9. 37, 10. 4, 11;<BR> Ve. 2; K. 160, 290, 348, 68, 98.<BR>—5 Panegyric, praise, complimentary language; especially, a word of praise<BR> uttered by a bard (such as जय, आलोकय); ययावुदीरितालोकः R. 17. 27, 2. 9;<BR> K. 14.<BR>—6 Section, chapter.<BR>—7 Mild light (सात्त्विकः प्रकाशः) cf. Pātañjala Yogadarśana 3. 25.<BR>—8 A trace of sight; आलोकमपि रामस्य न पश्यन्ति स्म दुःखिताः Rām. 2. 47. 2.<BR>—9 A lamp, light; आलोकदानं नामैतत्कीदृशं भरतर्षभ Mb. 13. 98. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकनम्
आलोकः, -कनम्<BR>—1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>—2 Sight, aspect. appearance; यदालोके सूक्ष्मम् Ś. 1. 9; Ku. 7. 22, 46;<BR> व्रजति हि सफलत्वं वल्लभालोकनेन Śi. सुख˚ V. 4. 24;<BR> Ś. 1. 32; R. 1. 84; Me. 3, 39.<BR>—3 Range of sight; आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला वा Me. 87;<BR> R. 7. 5; Ku. 2. 45.<BR>—4 Light, lustre, splendour; आलोकमार्गं सहसा व्रजन्त्या R. 7. 6<BR> air-hole, or window; निरालोकं लोकम् Māl. 5. 30, 9. 37, 10. 4, 11;<BR> Ve. 2; K. 160, 290, 348, 68, 98.<BR>—5 Panegyric, praise, complimentary language; especially, a word of praise<BR> uttered by a bard (such as जय, आलोकय); ययावुदीरितालोकः R. 17. 27, 2. 9;<BR> K. 14.<BR>—6 Section, chapter.<BR>—7 Mild light (सात्त्विकः प्रकाशः) cf. Pātañjala Yogadarśana 3. 25.<BR>—8 A trace of sight; आलोकमपि रामस्य न पश्यन्ति स्म दुःखिताः Rām. 2. 47. 2.<BR>—9 A lamp, light; आलोकदानं नामैतत्कीदृशं भरतर्षभ Mb. 13. 98. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोककः|आलोकक
आलोककः A spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकनीयता
आलोकनीयता The state of being looked at; चित्रन्यस्ता इव गताः<BR> प्रकामालोकनीयताम् Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकित
आलोकित <i>p. p.</i> Seen, beheld &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकितम्
आलोकित + .{@-तम्@} A look, glance; Māl. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकिन्
आलोकिन् <i>a.</i> Seeing, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोच्
आलोच् €1 Ā., €10 U.<BR>—1 To see, perceive.<BR>—2 To consider, reflect, think, ponder over, study; K. 7; आलोचयन्तो<BR> विस्तारमम्भसां दक्षिणोदधेः Bk. 7. 40; इति-एवंआलोच्य so thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचक
आलोचक <i>a.</i> Seeing, beholding.<BR>—3 Causing to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचकम्
आलोचक + .{@-कम्@} The faculty of vision, the cause of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचनम्
आलोचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Seeing, perceiving, survey, view; आलोचनमात्रमिष्यते वृत्तिः Sāṅ. K. 28.<BR>—2 Considering, reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचना
आलोचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Seeing, perceiving, survey, view; आलोचनमात्रमिष्यते वृत्तिः Sāṅ. K. 28.<BR>—2 Considering, reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोल|आलोलः
आलोल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Slightly trembling, rolling (as eyes); आलोलायतलोचनाः Bh. 3. 48.<BR>—2 Shaken, agitated; आलोलामलकावलीम् Amaru. 3; कीडालोलाः Me. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोलः|आलोल
आलोल + .{@-लः@} Trembling, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोलित
आलोलित <i>a.</i> Shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोहित
आलोहित <i>a.</i> Reddish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवक
आवक <i>a.</i> [अव्-ण्वुल्] Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवत्|आवन्त्
आवत् <i>f.</i> Ved. Proximity; आवतस्त आवतः परावतस्त आवतः Av. 5. 30. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवत्सरम्
आवत्सरम् <i>ind.</i> For a year, during a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवनेयः|आवनेय
आवनेयः [अवन्या अपत्यं ढक्] ‘Son of the earth’, an epithet<BR> of the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्तः|आवन्त|आवंतः
आवन्तः [अवन्तेरयं राजा अण्] A king of Avantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्तिक|आवंतिक|आवन्तिकः
आवन्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Coming from or belonging to Avantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्तिकः|आवन्तिक|आवंतिक
आवन्तिक + .{@-कः@} N. of a Buddhist school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्त्य|आवंत्य|आवन्त्यः
आवन्त्य <i>a.</i> [अवन्तिषु भवः ञ्य] Coming from or belonging to Avantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्त्यः|आवन्त्य|आवंत्य
आवन्त्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 A prince or an inhabitant of Avantī.<BR>—2 The offspring of a degraded Brāhmaṇa; see Ms. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवप्
आवप् €1 U.<BR>—1 To scatter, throw about; वयोभ्यश्चावपेद्भुवि Mb.; so अक्षान् throws.<BR>—2 To sow (as seed).<BR>—3 To fit in, insert.<BR>—4 To pour out or forth.<BR>—5 To offer (as in a sacrifice), perform (as a Śrāddha). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To shave, cut off.<BR>—2 To trim, to comb; केशानावापयन्ती Mb. 1. 3. 157.<BR>—3 To mix with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपनम्
आवपनम्<BR>—1 The act of sowing, throwing, scattering.<BR>—2 Sowing seed.<BR>—3 Wearing; भूमिरावपने प्रभुः Mb. 1. 88. 13.<BR>—4 Shaving.<BR>—5 A vessel, jar, ewer.<BR>—6 Instilling, inserting.<BR>—7 Place of origin, birth; यस्य छन्दोमयं ब्रह्म देह आवपनं विभो<BR> Bhāg. 10. 80. 45.<BR>—8 A hempen cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपनी
आवपनम् + .{@-नी@} Ved. A vessel, jar; त्वमस्यावपनी जनानामदितिः Av. 12. 1. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0360-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपन्तक
आवपन्तक, आवपन्तिक <i>a.</i> Ved. Scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपन्तिक|आवपंतिक
आवपन्तक, आवपन्तिक <i>a.</i> Ved. Scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाप|आवापः
आवाप <i>a.</i> [आवप्-घञ्] Throwing, scattering; (as in अक्षावाप q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापः|आवाप
आवाप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Sowing seed.<BR>—2 Scattering, throwing in general; casting, directing.<BR>—3 Mixing, inserting.<BR>—4 Especially, throwing additional ingredients into a compound in course<BR> of preparation.<BR>—5 A basin for water round the root of a tree (आलवाल).<BR>—6 A vessel, jar for corn.<BR>—7 Setting out or arranging vessels.<BR>—8 Hostile purpose, intention of fighting (with another); foreign affairs;<BR> ‘तन्त्रः स्वराङ्कचिन्तायामावापः परचिन्तने’ इति वैजयन्ती; तन्त्रावापविद् Śi. 2. 88.<BR>—9 A principal sacrifice or oblation to fire.<BR>—10 A kind of drink.<BR>—11 A bracelet (आवापक).<BR>—12 Uneven ground.<BR>—13 Decentralisation, a matter which serves several persons or things<BR> only if repeated with each one of them (opp. तन्त्र q. v.) यस्तु<BR> आवृत्त्या उपकरोति स आवापः । यथा तेषामेव ब्राह्मणानामनुलेपनम् । ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापकः|आवापक
आवापकः A bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापनम्
आवापनम्<BR>—1 A loom.<BR>—2 A reel or frame for winding thread.<BR>—3 Shaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापिक
आवापिक <i>a.</i> [आवापाय साधु ठक्]<BR>—1 Good for sowing, shaving &c.<BR>—2 Additional, supplementary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयः|आवय
आवयः<BR>—1 Coming.<BR>—2 One who comes.<BR>—3 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयः|आवय
आवयः + .{@-यः, -या@} Water (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवया
आवयः + .{@-यः, -या@} Water (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयम्
आवयः + .{@-यम्@} Ved. Non-conception, barrenness; अप्रजास्त्वं मार्तवत्समाद्<BR> रोदमघमावयम् Av. 8. 6. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयाज्
आवयाज् <i>m.</i> One who makes a sacrifice to reach the gods (Sāy.);<BR> or one who averts by means of sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक, आवरण &c. see आवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरक, आवरण &c. see आवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरसमक
आवरसमक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अवरसमे देयमृणं वुञ्] (A debt) To be paid<BR> in the following year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्हित|आवर्हितः
आव(ब)र्हित <i>a.</i> Eradicated, uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हित
आव(ब)र्हित <i>a.</i> Eradicated, uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरीवस्
आवरीवस् <i>a.</i> That which covers (Śataślokī 23).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलिः|आवलि
आवलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> [आ-वल्-इन् वा डीप्]<BR>—1 A line, row, range; अरावलीम् V. 1. 4; द्विजावली बालनिशाकरांशुभिः<BR> Śi., so अलक˚, धूम˚, दन्त˚, हार˚, रत्न˚ &c.<BR>—2 A series, continuous line.<BR>—3 A dynasty, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवली
आवलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> [आ-वल्-इन् वा डीप्]<BR>—1 A line, row, range; अरावलीम् V. 1. 4; द्विजावली बालनिशाकरांशुभिः<BR> Śi., so अलक˚, धूम˚, दन्त˚, हार˚, रत्न˚ &c.<BR>—2 A series, continuous line.<BR>—3 A dynasty, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलित
आवलित <i>a.</i> [वल्-क्त] Slightly turned; K. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्गित
आवल्गित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shaking gently; स मन्थरावल्गितपीवरस्तनीः Ki. 4. 17.<BR>—2 Springing, jumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्गिन्
आवल्गिन् <i>a.</i> Dancing; कामेनाकृष्य चापं हतपटुपटहावल्गिभिर्मारवीरैः Nāg. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्गुज
आवल्गुज <i>a.</i> Produced from the plant अवल्गुज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यम्
आवश्यम् [अवश्य-अण्] Necessity, inevitable act or conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यक|आवश्यकं
आवश्यक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अवश्य वुञ्] Inevitable, necessary; ऐतष्वावश्यकस्त्वसौ<BR> Bhāṣā P. 22, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकम्
आवश्यक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Necessity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">Page0361-2</a>]<BR> inevitable act or duty. ˚कृ to do what nature compels one to do; उत्थायावश्यकं<BR> कृत्वा Ms. 4. 93; Bhāg. 9. 4. 37.<BR>—2 An inevitable conclusion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आवश्यकबृहद्वृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकबृहद्वृत्तम्
आवश्यक + -बृहद्वृत्तम् N. of a Jaina work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकता
आवश्यकता, -त्वम्<BR> Necessity, inevitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकत्वम्
आवश्यकता, -त्वम्<BR> Necessity, inevitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवस्
आवस् €1 P. (With acc.)<BR>—1 To inhabit, dwell in; रविमावसते सतां क्रियायै V. 3. 7; पुरीमिमामावसत्<BR> Rām.; sometimes with loc.; Ms. 7. 69; रम्यं पशव्यमाजीव्यं जाङ्गलं<BR> देशमावसेत् Y. 1. 321.<BR>—2 To be occupied or engaged, enter upon; गृहस्थाश्रमम् Ms. 3. 2.<BR>—3 To take part carnally; cohabit. गुरोस्तल्पमावसन् Ch. Up. 5. 10. 9.<BR>—4 To pass, spend (as night). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To allow one to dwell, receive hospitably.<BR>—2 To inhabit, settle in a place.<BR>—3 To halt or encamp (for the night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसतिः|आवसति
आवसतिः <i>f.</i> Night (the time during which one rests); midnight;<BR> माद्रीसुताभ्यां सहितः किरीटी सुष्वाप तामावसतिं प्रतीतः Mb. 3. 165. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथः|आवसथ|आवसथं
आवसथः [आवस्-अथच् Uṇ. 3. 116]<BR>—1 A dwelling, dwelling-place, residence, house, habitation; निवसन्नावसथे<BR> पुराद्बहिः R. 8. 14; रोगी चिरप्रवासी परान्नभोजी परावसयशायी ।<BR> यज्जीवति तन्मरणं यन्मरणं सोऽस्य विश्रामः ॥ Subh. Ratn.<BR>—2 A resting place, asylum; Ms. 3. 107; Mb. 12. 140-41; स ह सर्वत<BR> आवसथान् मापयाञ्चक्रे । Ch. Up. 4. 1. 1. स … ग्रासाच्छादनावसथान्<BR> प्रतिविदध्यात् Kau. A. 1. 11.<BR>—3 A dwelling for pupils and ascetics.<BR>—4 A village.<BR>—5 A particular religious observance.<BR>—6 A fire-sanctuary, a place where sacrificial fire is preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथिक|आवसथिकः
आवसथिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आवसथे गृहे वसति ठक् Tv.]<BR>—1 Inhabiting a house.<BR>—2 Household, domestic.<BR>—3 Keeping a sacred fire in a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथिकः|आवसथिक
आवसथिक + .{@-कः@} Prob. a supervisor of royal palace and other government buildings,<BR> including temples, rest-houses &c. EI. XXIII, pp. 155 ff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्य|आवसथ्यः
आवसथ्य <i>a.</i> [आवसथ-ञ्य] Being in a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्यः|आवसथ्य
आवसथ्य + .{@-थ्यः@} The sacred fire kept in the house, one of the five fires<BR> used in sacrifices; see पञ्चाग्नि; Bhāg. 3. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्यः|आवसथ्य
आवसथ्य + .{@-थ्यः, -थ्यम्@} A dwelling for pupils and ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्यम्
आवसथ्य + .{@-थ्यः, -थ्यम्@} A dwelling for pupils and ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्यम्
आवसथ्य + .{@-थ्यम्@}<BR>—1 Placing a sacred fire within a house.<BR>—2 A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवासः|आवास
आवासः<BR>—1 A house, habitation, abode; आवासवृक्षोन्मुखबर्हिणानि R. 2. 17.<BR>—2 Apartment, room.<BR>—3 A place of refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवास्य
आवास्य <i>a.</i> Inhabited by, full of; आत्मावास्यमिदं विश्वम् Bhāg. 8. 1. 10.<BR> ईशावास्यमिदं सर्वम् Īśop. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसान
आवसान <i>a.</i> [अवसानमभिजनोऽस्य अञ्] Living at the extremity<BR> of a town (as a चाण्डाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसित|आवसितं
आवसित <i>a.</i> [आ-अव-सो-क्त]<BR>—1 Finished or completed.<BR>—2 Decided, determined, settled.<BR>—3 Stored (as grain); winnowed. —4 Ripe, full-grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसितम्
आवसित + .{@-तम्@} Ripe corn when (thrashed.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवास्
आवास् €10 P. [वास् with आ] To perfume; आवासयन्तो गन्धेन<BR> जग्मुरन्यद्वनं ततः Rām. 2. 103. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0361-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवस्थिक
आवस्थिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अवस्थायां भवः ठञ्] Suited or adapted to circumstances;<BR> धर्मो ह्यावस्थिकः स्मृतः Mb. 12. 36. 11; आवस्थिकक्रमं चापि मत्वा<BR> कार्यं निरूपणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह्
आवह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring; अग्ने पत्नीरिहावह Rv. 1. 22. 9.<BR>—2 To bring home (as a bride).<BR>—3 To conduce, lead or tend to, produce, bring on; क्रीडमावहति मे स<BR> संप्रति R. 11. 73 shames me; मनसो रुजमावहन् Ś. 3. 4 tending<BR> to mental anguish; न मे सौख्यमावहति does not tend to my happiness<BR> Pt. 1; संगमम् K. 174; Ms. 3. 82.<BR>—4 To pay; गृहीतवेतनः कर्म त्यजन्द्विगुणमावहेत् Y. 2. 193.<BR>—5 To lead forth, conduct away.<BR>—6 To flow (as blood &c.).<BR>—7 To bear, support, wear; मण्डनमावहन्तीम् C. P. 18.<BR>—8 To apply, use, employ; मा रोदीर्घैर्यमावह Mārk. P. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To send for, cause to be brought.<BR>—2 To invoke a deity (by means of Mantras); गायत्रीमावाहयामि, गणपतिमावाहयामि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह|आवहः
आवह <i>a.</i> (As last member of comp.) Producing, leading or tending<BR> to, bringing on; क्लेशावहा भर्तुरलक्षणाऽहम् R. 14. 5; so दुःख˚,<BR> भय˚, क्षय˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहः|आवह
आवह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 N. of one of the seven winds or bands of air, usually assigned to the<BR> भुवर्लोक or atmospheric region between the भूर्लोक and स्वर्लोक.<BR>—2 One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहनम्
आवहनम् Bringing near, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहमान|आवहमानं
आवहमान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bringing near.<BR>—2 Followed or succeeded by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहः|आवाह
आवाहः<BR>—1 Marrying.<BR>—2 A religious observance; आवाहाश्च विवाहाश्च सह सूतैर्मया कृताः<BR> Mb. 5. 141. 14, 13. 63. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहनम्
आवाहनम्<BR>—1 Sending for, inviting, calling.<BR>—2 Invoking a deity (to be present) (opp. विसर्जन); आवाहने विनियोगः,<BR> आवाहनं न जानामि न जानामि तवार्चनम् Pūjāmantra.<BR>—3 Offering oblations to fire; आवाहनाग्नौकरणरहितं ह्यपसव्यवत् Y. 1. 251.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहनी
आवाहनम् + .{@-नी@} A particular position of the hands at the time of invoking<BR> a deity; हस्ताभ्यामञ्जलिं बद्ध्वाऽनामिकामूलपर्वणोः । अङ्गुष्ठौ निक्षिपेत्सेयं<BR> मुद्रा त्वावाहनी स्मृता ॥ Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवालम्
आवालम् [आ-वल्-णिच् अच् Tv.] A basin for water round the root of<BR> a tree; cf. आलवालम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविः|आवि
आविः See आवी <i>f.</i> Pain, suffering. (pl.) Pangs of child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविक|आविकः
आविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अविना तल्लोम्ना निर्मितं ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to a sheep; आविकं क्षीरम् Ms. 5. 8, 2. 41.<BR>—2 Woollen; वासो यथा पाण्ड्वाविकम् Bṛ. Up. 2. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविकम्
आविक + .{@-कम्@} A woollen cloth, blanket; परमास्तरणास्तीर्णमाविकाजिनसंवृतम्<BR> Rām. 5. 10. 6; Ms. 5. 120.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आविकसौत्रिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविकसौत्रिक
आविक + -सौत्रिक <i>a.</i> made of woollen thread; वैश्यस्याविकसौत्रिकम् Ms. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविक्षितः|आविक्षित
आविक्षितः N. of Marutta, a descendant of अविक्षित; आविक्षितः पार्थिवोसौ<BR> मरुत्तः Mb. 12. 20. 13. आविक्षितस्य कामप्रेः …<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविग्न|आविग्नः
आविग्न <i>a.</i> Distressed, troubled, agitated, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविग्नः|आविग्न
आविग्न + .{@-ग्नः@} N. of a fruit-tree (अविग्न; Mar. करवंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवितन्
आवितन् €8 Ā. To spread over (as rays of light); त्रींल्लोकानावितन्वाना<BR> Bhāg. 5. 20. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्
आविद् €2 U. <i>Caus.</i> —1 To make known, report, declare, announce,<BR> tell, communicate, inform; किमिति नावेदयसि अथवा किमावेदितेन Ve. 1;<BR> राज्ञ आवेदयध्वं मां संप्राप्तम् Rām.; आयुषः प्रमाणमावेदयति<BR> K. 46, 47, आवेदयन्ति प्रत्यासन्नमानन्दं … निमित्तानि 65, 67<BR> foreshadow; 81, 168; Bk. 3. 49; Ku. 6. 21; R. 5. 23; आत्मनः सुमहत्कर्म<BR> व्रणैरावेद्य R. 12. 55; K. 158.<BR>—3 To bring to, offer, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवित्त
आवित्त <i>a.</i> Existing, being; Vāj. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्
आविद् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 A technical name of the Vedic formulas (in Vāj. 10. 9.) beginning<BR> with आविस् and आवित्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्वस्
आविद्वस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Knowing fully, skilled in; आविद्वाँ आहे विदुषे<BR> करांसि Rv. 4. 19. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदक|आवेदकः
आवेदक <i>a.</i> Making known, reporting, communicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदकः|आवेदक
आवेदक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 One who makes known, an informer.<BR>—2 A suitor, plaintiff; Śukra. 4. 586.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदनम्
आवेदनम्<BR>—1 Communicating, reporting, or addressing respectfully.<BR>—2 Representation.<BR>—3 Stating a complaint (in law); राज्ञे कुर्यात् पूर्वमावेदनं यः Nārada.<BR>—4 A plaint; Śukra. 4. 606<BR>—5 Marriage; न विवाहविधावुक्तं विधवावेदनं पुनः Ms. 9. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदनीय
आवेदनीय, -वेद्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be declared or reported.<BR>—2 To be made the subject of a plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्य
आवेदनीय, -वेद्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be declared or reported.<BR>—2 To be made the subject of a plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदित|आवेदितः
आवेदित <i>p. p.</i> Made known, communicated &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदितः|आवेदित
आवेदित + .{@-तः@} The person to whom something is made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदितम्
आवेदित + .{@-तम्@} That which is communicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदिन्
आवेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Declaring, announcing.<BR>—2 Giving orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविदूर्यम्
आविदूर्यम् [अविदूरस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध, आविध See under आव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविध|आविधः
आविद्ध, आविध See under आव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भाव|आविर्भावः
आविर्भाव &c. See आविस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविल
आविल <i>a.</i> [आविलति दृष्टिं स्तृणाति विल् स्तृतौ-क Tv.]<BR>—1 Turbid, foul, dirty, muddy; पङ्कच्छिदः फलस्येव निकषेणाविलं<BR> पयः M. 2. 8; तस्याविलाम्भःपरिशुद्धिहेतोः R. 13. 36.<BR>—2 Impure, spoiled; Ki. 8. 37 fig. also; त्वदीयैश्चरितैरनाविलैः Ku. 5. 37.<BR>—3 Dark-coloured, dark-blue, darkish; आविलपयोधराग्रम् V. 5. 8<BR>—4 Dim, obscure; आविलां मृगलेखाम् R. 8. 42.<BR>—5 Bedimmed, blurred; प्रवृद्धभतया उद्धर्षहृदयास्राविलेक्षणः Bhāg. 10. 86. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविलयति
आविलयति Den. P. To sully, make turbid, stain, blot; त्यपदेशमाविलयितुं<BR> किमीहसे Ś. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविश्
आविश् €6 U.<BR>—1 To enter; गौरीगुरोर्गह्वरमाविवेश R. 2. 26, 3. 28.<BR>—2 To take possession of, possess, affect; मूढमाविशन्ति न पण्डितम्<BR> H. 1. 3; so भयम्, मोहः, क्रोधः &c.<BR>—3 To go towards, approach.<BR>—4 To go or attain to a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">Page0363-1</a>]<BR> particular state; सुखम्, मन्युम् &c.<BR>—5 To arise. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to enter; मय्यावेशित चेतसाम् Bg. 12. 7.<BR>—2 To possess; K. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0362-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्ट|आविष्टः
आविष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Entered.<BR>—2 Possessed (by an evil spirit); आविष्टासि गृहे शून्ये सा त्वं परवशंगता<BR> Rām. 2. 12. 18; K. 120, 167, 318.<BR>—3 Possessed of, seized or filled with, full of, overpowered or overcome;<BR> भय˚, क्रोध˚, निद्रा˚; कृपयाविष्टम् Bg. 2. 1; भोगिनः कञ्चुकाविष्टाः<BR> Pt. 1. 65 covered with, clad in.<BR>—4 Engrossed or occupied in, intent on (तत्पर, उद्युक्त).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आविष्टलिङ्ग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्टलिङ्ग
आविष्ट + -लिङ्ग <i>a.</i> (noun) which in every relationship preserves its<BR> own gender (नियतलिङ्ग), <i>e. g.</i> प्रधानम्, अर्धः, उपसर्जनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशः|आवेश
आवेशः<BR>—1 Entering into, entrance; आवेशं कृ Pt. 1 to enter or infuse oneself into.<BR>—2 Taking possession of, influence, exercise; स्मय˚ influence of<BR> pride R. 5. 19; so मदन˚, क्रोध˚, भय˚ &c.<BR>—3 Intentness, devotedness to an object, complete absorption in one wish or idea.<BR>—4 Pride, arrogance.<BR>—5 Flurry, agitation, anger, passion; K. 291.<BR>—6 Demoniacal possession.<BR>—7 Apoplectic or epileptic giddiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशनम्
आवेशनम्<BR>—1 Entering, entrance.<BR>—2 Demoniacal possession.<BR>—3 Passion, anger, fury.<BR>—4 A manufactory, work-shop; कारुकावेशनानि Ms. 9. 265.<BR>—5 The disc of the sun or the moon.<BR>—6 A house, dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिक|आवेशिकः
आवेशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आवेश-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Peculiar, oneʼs own (असाधारण).<BR>—2 Inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिकः|आवेशिक
आवेशिक + .{@-कः@} A guest, visitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिकम्
आवेशिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Entering into.<BR>—2 Hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्
आविस् <i>ind.</i> A particle meaning ‘before the eyes’, ‘openly’, ‘evidently’<BR> (usually prefixed to the roots अस्, भू and कृ); आचार्यकं विजयि<BR> मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भू
आविर्भू €1 P. To become manifest, appear, become visible, show oneself<BR> to; तमस्तपति घर्मांशौ कथमाविर्भविष्यति^1 Ś. 5. 14; तेषामाविरभूद्<BR> ब्रह्मा परिम्लानमुखश्रियाम् Ku. 2. 2; आविर्बभूव कुशगर्भमुखं मृगाणां<BR> यूथम् R. 9. 55; आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः कन्दलीश्चानुकच्छम् Me.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भावः|आविर्भाव
आविर्भावः, आविर्भूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Manifestation, presence, appearance.<BR>—2 An incarnation.<BR>—3 Nature or property of things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भूतिः|आविर्भूति
आविर्भावः, आविर्भूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Manifestation, presence, appearance.<BR>—2 An incarnation.<BR>—3 Nature or property of things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भूत|आविर्भूतः
आविर्भूत <i>a.</i> Become apparent, visible, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्मण्डल
आविर्मण्डल <i>a.</i> Manifesting the form of a circle; विधुवति धनुराविर्मण्डलं<BR> पाण्डुसूनौ Ki. 14. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्हित
आविर्हित <i>a.</i> Made visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कृ
आविष्कृ €8 U. To make apparent, lay bare, reveal, show, manifest, put<BR> forth; (याति) आविष्कृतारुणपुरस्सर एकतोऽर्कः Ś. 4. 2; Śi. 20. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्करणम्
आविष्करणम्, -ष्कारः<BR>—1 Manifestation, making visible, showing; असूया गुणेषु दोषाविष्करणम् Sk.<BR>—2 The means of making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कारः|आविष्कार
आविष्करणम्, -ष्कारः<BR>—1 Manifestation, making visible, showing; असूया गुणेषु दोषाविष्करणम् Sk.<BR>—2 The means of making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कृत|आविष्कृतः
आविष्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Made visible, manifest, revealed.<BR>—2 Known; मोहं नृपतिशार्दूल गन्तुमाविष्कृतः क्षितौ Mb. 1. 172. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्ट्य
आविष्ट्य^1 <i>a.</i> Ved. Manifest.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्तराम्
आविस्तराम् <i>ind.</i> In a more manifest way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवी
आवी <i>f.</i> [अवीरेव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 A woman in her courses.<BR>—2 A pregnant woman.<BR>—3 The pangs of child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीरजा
आवीरजा See आवी (1); आवीरजानुगमनम् Mb. 16. 8. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीत
आवीत <i>a.</i> [आ-व्ये-क्त]<BR>—1 Worn, put on, held after throwing round.<BR>—2 Entered, passed, gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीतम्
आवीत + .{@-तम्@} The sacrificial cord worn in any particular position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीतिन्
आवीतिन् <i>m.</i> [आवीत-इनि] A Brāhmaṇa who makes the sacrificial<BR> cord hang over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीरचूर्णः|आवीरचूर्ण|आवीरचूर्णं|आवीरचूर्ण्ण
आवीरचूर्णः^1 The opposite-leaved fig-tree.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost diacritics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीरचूर्णम्
आवीरचूर्णः + .{@-र्णम्@} Red powder used in the <i>Holi</i> festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवुकः|आवुक
आवुकः A father (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवुत्तः|आवुत्त
आवुत्तः A sisterʼs husband; brother-in-law; U. 1; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृ
आवृ €5. €9. €10 U.<BR>—1 To cover, hide, conceal; आवृणोदात्मनो रन्ध्रम् R. 17. 61; K. 199;<BR> आवरीतुमिवाकाशम् Bk. 9. 24; धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निः Bg. 3. 38.<BR>—2 To fill, pervade; सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति Bg. 13. 13; Ms. 2. 144.<BR>—3 To choose, desire.<BR>—4 To enclose, obstruct, shut, hem in, block; आवृत्य पन्थानमजस्य<BR> तस्थौ R. 7. 31, 12. 28.<BR>—5 To keep off; आवव्रे मुसली तरुम् Bk. 14. 109. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cover or conceal.<BR>—2 To ward or keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक <i>a.</i> Covering, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरकम्
आवरक + .{@-कम्@} A cover, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरण <i>a.</i> Covering, hiding, obscuring, obstructing; नेत्रावरणमश्रु R. 14. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणम्
आवरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Covering, concealing, hiding, obscuring; सूर्ये तपत्यावरणाय दृष्टेः<BR> कल्पेत लोकस्य कथं तमिस्रा R. 5. 13, 19. 46, 19. 16.<BR>—2 Shutting, enclosing, fencing.<BR>—3 A covering, anything that covers or protects &c.; हस्तौ स्वौ नयति<BR> स्तनावरणताम् M. 4. 14; Ś. 3. 21; (fig.) protection, defence; शीलमावरणं<BR> स्त्रियाः Rām.; चरित्रावरणाः स्त्रियः Cāṇ. 76.<BR>—4 Obstruction, interruption, restraint (of bashfulness &c.); कालेनावरणात्ययात् U. 1. 39.<BR>—5 An enclosure, fence, surrounding wall; लब्धान्तरा सावरणेऽपि गेहे<BR> R. 16. 7; Ki. 5. 25.<BR>—6 A bolt, latch.<BR>—7 A shield.<BR>—8 An armour; आक्षिप्तचापावरणेषु जालानि Ki. 17. 59.<BR>—9 (in phil.) mental blindness (Jaina).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आवरणशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणशक्तिः|आवरणशक्ति
आवरण + -शक्तिः mental ignorance (which veils the real nature of things).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणिनः
आवरणिनः <i>m.</i> pl. N. of a Buddhist sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणीय
आवरणीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to mental blindness (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरितृ
आवरि(री)तृ <i>a.</i> One that covers or envelops; शरैरावारितस्तस्य<BR> संयुगे पतगेश्वरः Rām. 3. 51. 12; यः सर्वेषामावरीता वरीयान् Ki. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरीतृ
आवरि(री)तृ <i>a.</i> One that covers or envelops; शरैरावारितस्तस्य<BR> संयुगे पतगेश्वरः Rām. 3. 51. 12; यः सर्वेषामावरीता वरीयान् Ki. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारः|आवार
आवारः Enclosing, keeping off, as in दुरावार q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरिका
आवरिका, आवारिः [आवृ बाहु˚ इण्] A shop, a stall (<i>n.</i><BR> according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारिः|आवारि
आवरिका, आवारिः [आवृ बाहु˚ इण्] A shop, a stall (<i>n.</i><BR> according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत|आवृतः
आवृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Covered, screened, concealed.<BR>—2 Invested, blocked.<BR>—3 Enclosed, surrounded (by a ditch,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">Page0364-1</a>]<BR> wall &c.).<BR>—4 Spread, overspread, overcast; आवृते नभस्तले H. 3.<BR>—5 Filled or abounding with; सोऽमरावतिसंकाशां हृष्टपुष्टजनावृताम्<BR> (प्रविवेश पुरीम्) Rām. 7. 33. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृतः|आवृत
आवृत + .{@-तः@} A man of mixed origin, the son of a Brāhmaṇa by a woman<BR> of the Ugra caste; व्राह्मणादुग्रकन्यायामावृतो नाम जायते Ms. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0363-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृतिः|आवृति
आवृतिः <i>f.</i> Covering, hiding; see आवरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृज्
आवृज् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To bestow, give (Ved.)<BR>—2 To turn to or towards.<BR>—3 To choose; तमेव दयितं भूय आवृङ्क्ते पतिमाम्बिका Bhāg. 4. 7. 59.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bend, bend down; incline; गौरवेणावर्जितः Pt. 4; आवर्ज्य<BR> शाखाः सदयं च यासाम् R. 16. 19, 13. 17, 24; Mv. 5. 63; K. 14, 58; Ku. 2. 26, 3. 54, 7. 54;<BR> Me. 48.<BR>—2 To subdue, win or gain over, attract, please; आवर्जितानि मनांसि<BR> Nāg. 1; मरीचिमावर्जितवतीव श्लाघसे Dk. 45, 58, 133, 155; Mv. 2;<BR> K. 368; पवनावर्जितरुग्णपुष्करस्य Bu. C. 5. 62; आवर्जितानि<BR> च मया सकलसामाजिकमनांसीति मे निश्चयः Nāg. Act 1, between verses 2 and 3.<BR>—3 To bring, collect; चतुर्दिगावर्जितसंभृताम् R. 6. 76.<BR>—4 To pour out, offer, give; अपि त्वदावर्जितवारिसंभृतम् Ku. 5. 34;<BR> R. 15. 80; तनयावर्जितपिण्डकाङ्क्षिणः 8. 26, 1. 62, 67; Mu. 4; K. 241.<BR>—5 To draw or force out; Nāg. 4 and 5; आवर्जितं मया चञ्च्वा हृदयात्तव<BR> शोणितम् Nāg. 5.<BR>—6 To empty, pour out the contents of (as a jar &c.); कलशमावर्जयति<BR> Ś. 1; V. 5; Ku. 7. 10; K. 82, 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्जक
आवर्जक <i>a.</i> Attracting, propitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्जनम्
आवर्जनम्<BR>—1 Bending down &c.<BR>—2 Giving.<BR>—3 Winning over; Dk. 139, 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्जित
आवर्जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inclined, bent down; आवर्जिता किंचिदिव स्तनाभ्याम् Ku. 3. 54.<BR>—2 Poured out, made to flow downwards.<BR>—3 Overcome, humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्जितम्
आवर्जित + .{@-तम्@} A particular position of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn round, revolve.<BR>—2 To return, come or turn back; धेनुराववृते वनात् R. 1. 82, 2. 19;<BR> एकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययावर्तते पुनः Bg. 8. 26.<BR>—3 To go to or towards.<BR>—4 To be restless or uneasy; रणरणकविवृद्धिं बिभ्रदावर्तमानम्<BR> Māl. 1. 41. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to turn or revolve; अक्षवलयमावर्तयन्तम् K. 42 telling the beads.<BR>—2 To roll, turn about or over.<BR>—3 To cause to roll down, shed (as tears &c.).<BR>—4 To attract, win over (see आवृज्).<BR>—5 To repeat, recite; आवरीवर्ति भुवनेष्वन्तः Av. 9. 10. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तः|आवर्त|आवर्त्त|आवर्त्तं|आवर्त्तः
आवर्तः<BR>—1 Turning round, winding, revolving; प्रदक्षिणावर्तशिखः Rām. 6. 73. 23.<BR>—2 A whirlpool, an eddy, whirl; नृपं तमावर्तमनोज्ञनाभिः R. 6. 52;<BR> दर्शितावर्तनाभेः Me. 28; Dk. 2; आवर्तः संशयानाम् Pt. 1. 191.<BR>—3 Deliberation, revolving (in the mind), anxiety.<BR>—4 A lock of hair curling backwards, especially on a horse (considered<BR> lucky); आवर्ता यस्य जायन्ते धन्यः स तुरगोत्तमः (शालिहोत्र of भोज).<BR>—5 The two depressions of the forehead above the eye-brows.<BR>—6 A crowded place (where many men live closely together).<BR>—7 A kind of jewel.<BR>—8 N. of a form of cloud personified; आवर्तो निर्जलो मेघः.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">Page0364-2</a>]<BR>—9 Melting (of metals).<BR>—10 Doubt; भ्रमं संमोहमावर्तमभ्यासाद्विनिवर्तयेत् Mb. 12. 274. 7.<BR>—11 Worldly existence (संसार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तम्
आवर्तः + .{@-र्तम्@} A mineral substance, pyrites (माक्षिकधातु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तक|आवर्तकः|आवर्त्तक
आवर्तक <i>a.</i> [आवर्त एव स्वार्थे कन्] Revolving again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तकः|आवर्तक|आवर्त्तक
आवर्तक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of a form of cloud personified; जातं वंशे भुवनविदिते पुष्करावर्तकानाम्<BR> Me. 6; Ku. 2. 50.<BR>—2 Depression above the eye-brows.<BR>—3 A whirlpool.<BR>—4 Revolution.<BR>—5 Revolution of the mind from the influence of the senses.<BR>—6 A curl of hair.<BR>—7 A sort of poisonous insect.<BR>—8 N. of a plant (Mar. टाकळा);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तकी|आवर्त्तकी
आवर्तक + .{@-की@} N. of a creeping plant (बृहद्दन्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तन|आवर्तनः|आवर्त्तन|आवर्त्तनं
आवर्तन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Turning round or towards.<BR>—2 Revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तनम्
आवर्तन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Turning round; returning, revolution.<BR>—2 Circular motion, gyration.<BR>—3 Churning or stirring up anything in fusion.<BR>—4 Melting together, fusion, alligation (said of metals).<BR>—5 Mid-day, the time when shadows are cast in an opposite direction.<BR>—6 Repeating, doing over and over again.<BR>—7 Study, practising.<BR>—8 A year; आवर्तनानि चत्वारि Mb. 13. 107. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तनः|आवर्तन|आवर्त्तन|आवर्त्तनं
आवर्तन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of an उपद्वीप in the जम्बुद्वीप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तनी|आवर्त्तनी
आवर्तन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 a crucible.<BR>—2 a spoon, ladle.<BR>—3 magic art; विद्यामावर्तनीं पुण्यामावर्तयति स द्विजः Rām. 7. 88. 20.<BR> (सांग्रहणी विद्या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तिन्|आवर्त्तिन्
आवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Whirling or turning upon itself, returning; आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन<BR> Bg. 8. 16; कालान्तरावर्ति H. 1. 180.<BR>—2 Melting, mixing &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्ती
आवर्तिन् + .({@-र्ती@}) A horse having curls of hair on various parts of the body<BR> (considered as a sign of auspiciousness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तिनी|आवर्त्तिनी
आवर्तिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A whirlpool.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (अजशृङ्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Causing to turn towards.<BR>—2 Turning towards or round; entering.<BR>—3 Order, succession, method, mode, manner; अनयैवावृता कार्यं पिण्डनिर्वपणं<BR> सुतैः Ms. 3. 248; Y. 3. 2.<BR>—4 Progress of an action; occurrence.<BR>—5 Turn of a path, course, direction.<BR>—6 A purificatory rite; अमन्त्रिका तु कार्येयं स्त्रीणामावृदशेषतः Ms. 2. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्त|आवृत्तः
आवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Turned round, whirled, returned; आवृत्तवृन्तशतपत्रनिभम् Māl. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Repeated; द्विरावृत्ता दश द्विदशाः Sk.<BR>—3 Learnt (by heart), studied; U. 6.<BR>—4 Reverted, returned.<BR>—5 Averted.<BR>—6 Retreated, fled.<BR>—7 Upside down (अधोमुख); (इत्यूर्ध्वेषु) अथावृत्तेषु Ch. Up. 2. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्तम्
आवृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} Addressing a prayer or songs to a god<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्तिः|आवृत्ति
आवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Turning towards; return, coming back; तपोवनावृत्तिपथम् R. 2. 18;<BR> यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः Bg. 8. 23.<BR>—2 Reversion, retreat, flight.<BR>—3 Revolving, whirling, going round; रटति कृतावृत्तिखट्वाङ्घण्टा Māl. 5. 4.<BR>—4 Recurrence to the same point or place (of the sun); उदगावृत्तिपथेन<BR> नारदः R. 8. 33.<BR>—5 Repetition of birth and death, wordly existence; अनावृत्तिभयम् Ku. 6. 77.<BR>—6 Repetition in general, an edition (modern use); सप्तमीयमङ्कनावृत्तिः<BR> seventh edition.<BR>—7 Repeated reading, study; आवृत्तिः सर्वशास्त्राणां बोधादपि गरीयसि<BR> Udb. cf. also तस्मादावृत्तिः स्तरणमन्त्रस्य । ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 42.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">Page0365-1</a>]<BR>—8 Use, employment, application.<BR>—9 Turn of a way, course or direction.<BR>—10 Occurrence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आवृत्तिदीपकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0364-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्तिदीपकम्
आवृत्तिः + -दीपकम् a rhetorical figure; त्रिविधं दीपकावृत्तौ भवेदावृत्तिदीपकम् ।<BR> (पदस्यार्थस्योभयोर्वा आवृत्तिः). क्रमेणोदाहरणम्:− वर्षत्यम्बुदमालेयं<BR> वर्षत्येषा च शर्वरी ॥ उन्मीलन्ति कदम्बानि स्फुटन्ति कुटजोद्गमाः । माद्यन्ति<BR> चातकास्तृप्ता माद्यन्ति च शिखावलाः ॥ Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृद्धबालकम्
आवृद्धबालकम् <i>ind.</i> From old men to children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृष्टिः|आवृष्टि
आवृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Raining, a shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेगः|आवेग
आवेगः<BR>—1 Uneasiness, anxiety, excitement, agitation, flurry; अलमावेगेन<BR> Ś. 3, 7; Amaru. 22; शोक˚, दुःख˚, साध्वस˚ &c. किमस्थानमिदमावेगस्य Nāg. 5.<BR>—2 Hurry, haste; Ś. 4.<BR>—3 Agitation, regarded as one of the 33 subordinate feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेगी
आवेगः + .{@-गी@} N. of a tree (वृद्धदारकवृक्ष; Mar. म्हैसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्ट्
आवेष्ट् €10 P.<BR>—1 To surround; तृणैरावेष्टयते रज्जुः is made or formed of straw. Pt. 1. 331.<BR>—2 To throttle, strangle; पीडाकर्षांशुकावेष्टपादाध्यासे शतं दमः Y. 2. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टकः|आवेष्टक
आवेष्टकः A wall, fence, an enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टनम्
आवेष्टनम्<BR>—1 Wrapping round, tying, binding.<BR>—2 A wrapper, an envelope.<BR>—3 A wall, fence, enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्य
आव्य <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अवेर्मेषस्य विकारः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a sheep.<BR>—2 Woollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्यक्त
आव्यक्त <i>a.</i> Quite clear, intelligible; तद्वाक्यमाव्यक्तपदं<BR> तासां स्त्रीणां निशम्य च Rām. 7. 88. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्यध्
आव्यध् €4 P.<BR>—1 To hit, pierce; see अनाविद्ध.<BR>—2 To wound.<BR>—3 To break or pierce through.<BR>—4 To put on; निवस्स्वाऽऽविध्य च स्रजम् Bk. 20. 11.<BR>—5 To shoot at, throw or cast towards.<BR>—6 To throw away, cast off.<BR>—7 To wave, brandish; आविद्धावेव दृश्येते Mb. 1. 226. 3; आविध्य<BR> शूलं तरसा Bhāg. 10. 59. 8.<BR>—8 To pin on.<BR>—9 To rouse, agitate, stir up.<BR>—10 To drive away, expel; निर्बन्धमाविध्यति Mv. 5. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pierced, bored, rent, splintered, broken down; उत्पाताविद्धमूर्तिः<BR> Mv. 5. 44 rent or contracted; R. 12. 73.<BR>—2 Curved, crooked, uneven; V. 4. 52; हर्षाविद्धमभ्युत्थितः Dk. 37.<BR>—3 Cast with force; दूरनिक्षेप˚ Māl. 8 cast forth in taking long<BR> strides; Mv. 2; Ms. 9. 40; thrown, put in motion.<BR>—4 Disappointed.<BR>—5 Fallacious, false.<BR>—6 Stupid, foolish.<BR>—7 Thrown, placed closely near one another; स पाण्डुराविद्धविमानमालिनीम्<BR> Rām. 5. 2. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्धम्
आविद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} A particular manner of fencing; Hariv.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आविद्धकर्णी, आविद्धकर्णिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्धकर्णी
आविद्ध + -कर्णी, -कर्णिका N. of a plant (पाठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्धकर्णिका
आविद्ध + -कर्णी, -कर्णिका N. of a plant (पाठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविधः|आविध
आविधः [आ-व्यध्-घञ्र्थे-क] An awl; drill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्याधिन्
आव्याधिन् <i>a.</i> [आ-व्यध्-णिनि] Giving pain, wounding, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्याधिनी
आव्याधिन् + .{@-नी@} A gang of robbers; नम आव्याधिनीभ्यः Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रश्च्
आव्रश्च् €6 P. To tear off, cut off; यो अस्याः कर्णावास्कुनोत्या स<BR> देवेषु वृश्चते Av. 12. 4. 6; tear in pieces, interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रश्चनम्
आव्रश्चनम्<BR>—1 Cutting or tearing off.<BR>—2 The stump of a tree (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रस्कः|आव्रस्क
आव्रस्कः Being torn off or tearing itself off (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रीडकः|आव्रीडक
आव्रीडकः [आव्रीडानां विषयो देशः] A country inhabited by shameless people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश|आशः
आश <i>a.</i> One who eats, eater (mostly as the last member of comp.);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> हुताश, आश्रयाश &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशः|आश
आश + .{@-शः@} [अश्-घञ्] Eating (as in प्रातराश); पिशिताशदोषः Rām. 5. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशकम्
आशकम् Eating; Mb. 13. 7. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयितृ
आशयितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Feeding, a feeder.<BR>—2 Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिः|आशि
आशिः <i>f.</i> The act of eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eaten, given to eat.<BR>—2 Satisfied by eating; अद्य दीर्घस्य कालस्य भविष्याम्यहमाशिता Rām. 5. 1. 174.<BR>—3 Voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितम्
आशित + .{@-तम@}<BR>—1 Eating.<BR>—2 Giving food (in charity); Bṛ. Up. 4. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितंगवीन|आशितङ्गवीन|आशितङ्गवीनं
आशितंगवीन <i>a.</i> [आशिता अशनेन तृप्ता गावो यत्र, खञ् निपातनात्<BR> मुम्] Formerly grazed by cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितंभव|आशितम्भव|आशितम्भवं
आशितंभव <i>a.</i> [आशितोऽशनेन तृप्तो भवत्यनेन P. III. 2. 45]<BR> Satiating, satisfying (as food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितंभवम्
आशितंभव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Food which produces satisfaction when eaten or enjoyed; आशितंभवं<BR> यद् द्रव्यं सा भूतिः सा दक्षिणा । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 45, victuals.<BR>—2 Satisfaction, satiety (<i>m.</i> also); फलैर्येष्वाशितंभवम् Bk. 4. 11;<BR> also आशितंभवमुत्कृष्टं वल्गितं शयितं स्थितम् Bk. 6. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितृ
आशितृ <i>a.</i> Voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन्
आशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eating (in comp.); फलाशी &c.<BR>—2 Aged; नमो युवभ्यो नम आशिनेभ्यः Rv. 1. 27. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंस्
आशंस् €1 Ā. (rarely P.)<BR>—1 To hope for, expect, desire, wish or long for; स्वकार्यासिद्धिं<BR> पुनराशशंसे Ku. 3. 57; Bk. 14. 70, 90; आशंसन्ते सुरसमितयः<BR> Ś. 2. 16; M. 1; मनोरथाय नाशंसे Ś. 7. 13.<BR>—2 To bless, wish well to; एवं ते देवा आशंसन्तु Mk. 1; इत्याशशंसे<BR> करणैरबाह्यैः R. 14. 50.<BR>—3 To speak, say.<BR>—4 To tell; आशंसता बाणगतिं वृषाङ्के Ku. 3. 14.<BR>—5 To ask for, beg.<BR>—6 To praise.<BR>—7 To repeat, recite.<BR>—8 To fear, be afraid of. ━<i>Caus.</i> To render famous or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसनम्
आशंसनम्<BR>—1 Expecting, wishing; इष्टाशंसनमाशीः Sk.<BR>—2 Telling, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसा
आशंसा<BR>—1 Desire, wish, expectation, hope; निदधे विजयाशंसां चापे सीतां च<BR> लक्ष्मणे R. 12. 44; आशंसा च हि नः Bk. 19. 5.<BR>—2 Speech, declaration.<BR>—3 Indication, reference; शरत्समयवर्णनाशंसया Ve. 1.<BR>—4 Imagination; आशंसापरिकल्पितास्वपि भवत्यानन्दसान्द्रो लयः Māl. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसित
आशंसित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wished, hoped, expected.<BR>—2 Said, declared.<BR>—3 Considered, said to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसितृ
आशंसितृ, आशंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing, desiring, expecting; V. 2.<BR>—2 Announcing, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसिन्
आशंसितृ, आशंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing, desiring, expecting; V. 2.<BR>—2 Announcing, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसु|आशंसुः
आशंसु <i>a.</i> [आ-शंस्-उ] सनाशंसभिक्ष उः P. III. 2. 168.<BR>—1 Wishing, hoping, desiring; स दुष्टः पापमाशंसुः पाण्डवानां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">Page0366-1</a>]<BR> महात्मनाम् Mb. 12. 39. 25.<BR>—2 Desirous, hopeful. लक्ष्मीः पुंयोगमाशंसुः Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0365-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशस्
आशस् <i>a.</i> Ved. [आ-शंस्-क्विप्] Hoping. <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Praise.<BR>—2 Desire; यदाशसा वदतो मे विचुक्षुभे Av. 7. 57. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्
आशक् €5 P. Ved. To make one capable or a master or possessor (of a thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्त|आशक्तः
आशक्त <i>a.</i> Able, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्तिः|आशक्ति
आशक्तिः <i>f.</i> Power, ability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिक्षा
आशिक्षा Desire of learning; Vāj. 30. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्क्|आशंक्
आशङ्क् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To suspect, distrust; दयितां साध्वीं त्वमाशङ्किष्वथाः कथम् Bk. 21. 1.<BR>—2 To suspect, or believe to be; आशङ्कसे यदग्निम् Ś. 1. 27; Śi. 3. 72;<BR> Bk. 6. 6.<BR>—3 To be in doubt or suspense; संदिग्धमेव सिद्धौ कातरमाशङ्कते चेतः M. 4. 5.<BR>—4 To fear, be afraid, apprehend; भरतागमनमाशङ्क्य R. 12. 24;<BR> Pt. 392; दत्तपूर्वेत्याशङ्क्यते Māl. 4.<BR>—4 To start a doubt or objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कनीय|आशंकनीय
आशङ्कनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be doubted or suspected.<BR>—2 To be apprehended.<BR>—3 Doubtful, questionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्का|आशंका
आशङ्का<BR>—1 Fear, apprehension; नष्टाशङ्का हरिणशिशवो मन्दमन्दं चरन्ति<BR> Ś. 1. 15; आशङ्कया भुक्तम् Bh. 3. 5.<BR>—2 Doubt, uncertainty; इत्याशङ्कायामाह Gadādhara.<BR>—3 Distrust, suspicion; ˚अन्वित <i>a.</i> apprehensive, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कित|आशंकित
आशङ्कित <i>p. p.</i> —1 Feared, dreaded; इदं तदाशङ्कितं गुरुजनेनापि<BR> U. 3; doubted, suspected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कितम्
आशङ्कित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Fear; apprehension.<BR>—2 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्किन्|आशंकिन्
आशङ्किन् <i>a.</i> —1 Doubting, fearing; रघोरभिभवाशाङ्कि R. 4. 21;<BR> attended with fears; तस्मादम्बुपतेरिवावनिपतेः सेवा सदाशाङ्किनी Pt. 1. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशन|आशनः
आशन <i>a.</i> [अशन-अण्] One who feeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशनः|आशन
आशन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 N. of a tree (Mar. आसणा); see अशन.<BR>—2 The thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशय|आशयः
आशय &c. See under आशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशरः|आशर
आशरः [आ-शॄ-अच्]<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 A demon, goblin (रक्षस्); स शरदाऽऽशरदावदवानलः Rām. Ch. 4. 67.<BR>—3 Wind; आशरस्तु पुमान् वैश्वानरे च रजनीचरे Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशरीकः|आशरीक
आशरीकः^1, आशरीकम् Violent and acute pain in the limbs; rheumatic<BR> pains; Av. 19. 34. 10.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशरीकम्
आशरीकः^1, आशरीकम् Violent and acute pain in the limbs; rheumatic<BR> pains; Av. 19. 34. 10.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशलः|आशल
आशलः A tree; see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशवम्
आशवम् [आशोर्भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Speed, quickness.<BR>—2 Distilled spirit; more usually written आसव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशसनम्
आशसनम् Ved. Cutting up an animal (when killed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशा
आशा [आसमन्तात् अश्नुते आ-अश्-अच्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Hope, expectation, prospect; तामाशां च सुरद्विषाम् R. 12. 96;<BR> आशा हि परमं दुःखं नैराश्यं परमं सुखम् Subhāṣ.; त्वमाशे<BR> मोघाशे Bh. 3. 6; so ˚भग्न, ˚हत, ˚निराश &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Wish, desire (in Bh. 3. 45 आशा is compared to a river).<BR>—2 False hope or expectation.<BR>—3 Space, region, quarter of the compass, direction; अगस्त्याचरितामाशामनाशास्यजयो<BR> ययौ R. 4. 44; Ki. 7. 9; Mark<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">Page0366-2</a>]<BR> also the pun on the word आशा (a direction, a desire) in आशापूरैककर्मप्रवणनिजकरप्राणिताशेषविश्वः<BR> (सूर्यः) Nāg. 3. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आशान्वित, आशाजनन, आशाकृत, आशागजः, आशातन्तुः, आशापालः, आशापिशाचिका, आशापुरगुग्गुलुः, आशाप्राप्त, आशाबन्धः, आशाभङ्गः, आशावह, आशावासस्, आशाविभिन्न, आशाहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशान्वित
आशा + -अन्वित, -जनन <i>a.</i> hopeful, inspiring hope; वचोभिराशाजननैः V. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाजनन
आशा + -अन्वित, -जनन <i>a.</i> hopeful, inspiring hope; वचोभिराशाजननैः V. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाकृत
आशा + -कृत <i>a.</i> attended with the hope of success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशागजः|आशागज
आशा + -गजः a guardian elephant of a quarter or point of the compass;<BR> see अष्टदिग्गज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशातन्तुः|आशातन्तु|आशातंतु
आशा + -तन्तुः a thread of hope, slender hope; चिरादाशातन्तुस्त्रुटतु<BR> Māl. 4. 3, 9. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशापालः|आशापाल
आशा + -पालः<BR>—1 a guardian or regent of the regions or quarters; see अष्टदिक्पाल.<BR>—2 A chief ruling over 10000 villages. Śukra. 1. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशापिशाचिका
आशा + -पिशाचिका deceptive or illusive hope, phantom of hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशापुरगुग्गुलुः|आशापुरगुग्गुलु
आशा + -पुरगुग्गुलुः or {@-संभवः@}<BR> a kind of Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशासंभवः
आशा + -पुरगुग्गुलुः or {@-संभवः@}<BR> a kind of Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाप्राप्त
आशा + -प्राप्त <i>a.</i> successful (= प्राप्ताश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाबन्धः|आशाबन्ध
आशा + -बन्धः<BR>—1 the tie or bond of hope, confidence, trust, expectation; गुर्वपि<BR> विरहदुःखमाशाबन्धः साहयति Ś. 4. 16; Ve. 6. 25; V. 3; U. 3; Me. 10.<BR>—2 consolation.<BR>—3 a spiderʼs web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाभङ्गः|आशाभङ्ग|आशाभंग
आशा + -भङ्गः disappointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावह|आशावहः
आशा + -वह <i>a.</i> inspiring hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावहः|आशावह
आशा + -वह + .({@-हः@}) N. of a son of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावासस्
आशा + -वासस् <i>a.</i> Naked; Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाविभिन्न
आशा + -विभिन्न <i>a.</i> disappointed in expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाहीन
आशा + -हीन <i>a.</i> despairing, despondent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावत्|आशावन्त्
आशावत् <i>a.</i> Having hopes, trusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाढः|आशाढ
आशाढः See अ(आ)षाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशारः|आशार
आशारः Shelter; ˚एषिन् seeking shelter; आशारैषी कृशगुरेत्वस्तम् Av. 4. 15. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्
आशास् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To bless, pronounce or give a blessing; ऋक्छन्दसा आशास्ते Ś. 4;<BR> किमन्यदाशास्महे केवलं वीरप्रसवा भूयाः U. 1.<BR>—2 To desire, wish, hope, expect; यस्य भवान् मङ्गलमाशास्ते Ve. 6;<BR> Ms. 3. 80; सर्वमस्मिन्वयमाशास्महे Ś. 7; आशासत ततः शान्तिम् Bk. 17. 1.<BR>—3 To order, command, relate (P. also in this sense).<BR>—4 To praise.<BR>—5 To subdue; आ नो जीवान् वरुण तासु शाधि Rv. 2. 28. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्य
आशास्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be obtained by a boon.<BR>—2 To be blessed; अस्माभिरप्यनाशास्यो रामस्य महिमान्वयः Mv. 4. 13.<BR>—3 To be wished for, desirable; अनाशास्यजयो ययौ R. 4. 44 (who had<BR> not to <i>wish for victory</i>, to whom victory came unsought).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्यम्
आशास्य + .{@-स्यम्@}<BR>—1 A thing to be wished for, wish, desire; संपन्नास्ते सर्वाशिषः<BR> Mu. 7; आशास्यमीतिविगमप्रभृति प्रजानाम् M. 5. 20.<BR>—2 A blessing, benediction; आशास्यचिन्तास्तिमितो बभूव Ku. 7. 87; आशास्यमन्यत्<BR> पुनरुक्तभूतम् R. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
आशिस् <i>f.</i> (˚शीः, ˚शीर्भ्याम् &c.) [आशास्-क्विप्, अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 A blessing, benediction. (It is thus defined:− वात्सल्याद्यत्र मान्येन<BR> कनिष्ठस्याभिधीयते । इष्टावधारकं वाक्यमाशीः सा परिकीर्तिता.) आशिस्<BR> is sometimes distinguished from वर, the former being taken to be<BR> merely an expression of oneʼs good wishes which may or may not be realized;<BR> while a वर is a boon which is more permanent in character and surer<BR> of fulfilment; cf. वरः खल्वेष नाशीः Ś. 4; आशिषो गुरुजनवितीर्णा<BR> वरतामापद्यन्ते K. 291; अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णन्तावर्ध्यानुपदमाशिषः<BR> R. 1. 44, 11. 6; Ku. 5. 76, 7. 47.<BR>—2 Act of bestowing a blessing upon others.<BR>—3 A prayer, wish, desire; जगच्छरण्यस्य निराशिषः सतः Ku. 5. 76,<BR> Bg. 4. 21, 6. 10.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">Page0367-1</a>]<BR>—4 A serpentʼs fang (cf. आशी).<BR>—5 One of the eight chief medicaments (वृद्धि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आशीरुक्तिः, आशीर्वादः, आशीर्वचनम्, आशीर्विषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0366-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीरुक्तिः|आशीरुक्ति
आशिस् + -उक्तिः, -वादः, -वचनम् (आशीर्वादः &c.) a blessing, benediction,<BR> expression of a prayer or wish; आशीर्वचनसंयुक्तां नित्यं यस्मात् प्रकुर्वते<BR> S. D. 6; Ms. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वादः|आशीर्वाद|आशीर्व्वादः
आशिस् + -उक्तिः, -वादः, -वचनम् (आशीर्वादः &c.) a blessing, benediction,<BR> expression of a prayer or wish; आशीर्वचनसंयुक्तां नित्यं यस्मात् प्रकुर्वते<BR> S. D. 6; Ms. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वचनम्
आशिस् + -उक्तिः, -वादः, -वचनम् (आशीर्वादः &c.) a blessing, benediction,<BR> expression of a prayer or wish; आशीर्वचनसंयुक्तां नित्यं यस्मात् प्रकुर्वते<BR> S. D. 6; Ms. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्विषः|आशीर्विष
आशिस् + -विषः (आशीर्विषः) ‘having poison in its fangs’, a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिञ्जित|आशिंजित
आशिञ्जित (also आसिञ्जित) <i>a.</i> Tinkling (as of the ornaments<BR> worn on the hands and feet); पादेन नापैक्षत सुन्दरीणां संपर्कमासिज्जितनूपुरेण Ku. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिञ्जित
आशिञ्जित (also आसिञ्जित) <i>a.</i> Tinkling (as of the ornaments<BR> worn on the hands and feet); पादेन नापैक्षत सुन्दरीणां संपर्कमासिज्जितनूपुरेण Ku. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित, आशिन् &c. See under आश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन्
आशित, आशिन् &c. See under आश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन
आशिन <i>a.</i> Ved. Aged; see आशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर्
आशिर् <i>f.</i> [आश्रीयते पच्यते आ-श्री-क्विप् Tv.] Milk &c. that is<BR> being boiled; (क्षीरादिकम् श्रपणद्रव्यम् Sāy.); the milk mixed with<BR> the Soma juice to purify it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर|आशिरः
आशिर <i>a.</i> Voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिरः|आशिर
आशिर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी [आशीर्यतेऽनया, आ-शॄ-क्विप् पृषो˚]<BR>—1 A serpentʼs fang; विषमाशीभिरनारतं धमन्तः Śi.<BR>—2 A kind of venom.<BR>—3 A blessing, benediction.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आशीविषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीविषः|आशीविष
आशी + -विषः [आश्यां विषमस्य]<BR>—1 a snake; गरुत्मदाशीविषभीमदर्शनैः R. 3. 57.<BR>—2 a particular kind of snake; कर्णाशीविषभोगिनि प्रशमिते Ve. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To lie or sleep on; कुसुमान्याशेरते षट्पदाः V. 2. 23, v. l.<BR>—2 To pass (the night) in sleep.<BR>—3 To wish, pray for; सुद्युम्नस्याशयन्पुंस्त्वमुपाधावत शंकरम् Bhāg. 9. 1. 37.<BR>—4 To dwell, live, inhabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयः|आशय
आशयः [आ-शी-अच्]<BR>—1 A bed-chamber, resting-place, asylum.<BR>—2 A place of residence, abode, seat, retreat; वायुर्गन्धानिवाशयात्<BR> Bg. 15. 8; अपृथक्˚ U. 1. 45, v. l.<BR>—3 Sleeping, lying down.<BR>—4 Receptacle, reservoir; विषमोऽपि विगाह्यते नयः कृततीर्थः पयसामिवाशयः<BR> Ki. 2. 3; cf. also words like जलाशय, आमाशय, रक्ताशय &c.; कामात्पिबति<BR> चाशयान् Mb. 12. 236. 24.<BR>—5 Any recipient vessel of the body; the Āśayas are 7:− वात˚, पित्त˚,<BR> श्लेष्मन्˚, रक्त˚, आम˚, पक्व˚ (and गर्भ˚ in the case of women).<BR>—6 The stomach; आशयाग्निदीप्तिः Dk. 160.<BR>—7 Meaning, intention, purport, gist; अर्थेन्द्रियाशयज्ञानैर्भगवान्परिभाव्यते<BR> Bhāg. 12. 11. 22. इत्याशयः; एवं कवेराशयः (oft. used by commentators;<BR> see अभिप्राय).<BR>—8 The seat of feelings, mind, heart; तन्मे दहति गात्राणि विषं पीतमिवाशये<BR> Rām. 6. 5. 6. अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः Bg. 10. 20; Mv. 2. 37.<BR>—9 Disposition of mind; द्रव्यस्वभावाशयकर्मकालैरेकादशामी मनसो<BR> विकारः Bhāg. 5. 11. 11.<BR>—10 Prosperity.<BR>—11 A barn.<BR>—12 Will or pleasure.<BR>—13 Virtue or vice (as the eventual cause of pleasure or pain).<BR>—14 Fate, fortune.<BR>—15 Property, possession.<BR>—16 A miser.<BR>—17 A kind of pit (made for catching animals); आस्ते परमसंतप्तो नूनं<BR> सिंह इवाशये Mb.<BR>—18 N. of a tree (पनस).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आशयाशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयाशः|आशयाश
आशयः + -आशः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु <i>a.</i> [अश्-व्याप्तौ उण्] Fast, quick<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुः|आशु
आशु + .{@-शुः@} Ved.<BR>—1 ‘The quick one’, a horse.<BR>—2 Rice (ripening<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">Page0367-2</a>]<BR> quickly in the rainy season).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु + .{@-शु@} <i>ind.</i> Fast, quickly, immediately, directly; Bg. 2. 65;<BR> वर्त्म भानोस्त्यजाशु Me. 41, 22. [cf. L. <i>acu</i>; Gr. <i>okus</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्वापस्, आशुकारिन्, आशुकृत्, आशुकोपिन्, आशुक्रिया, आशुग, आशुगामिन्, आशुतोष, आशुपत्री, आशुपत्वन्, आशुफलः, आशुबोध, आशुया, आशुव्रीहिः, आशुषेण, आशुसंधेय, आशुहेमन्, आशुहेषस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वापस्
आशु + -आपस् <i>a.</i> obtaining quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुकारिन्
आशु + -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing anything quickly, smart, active.<BR>—2 operating quickly (as a medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुकृत्
आशु + -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing anything quickly, smart, active.<BR>—2 operating quickly (as a medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुकोपिन्
आशु + -कोपिन् <i>a.</i> irascible, irritable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुक्रिया
आशु + -क्रिया quick operation of a medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुग|आशुगः
आशु + -ग <i>a.</i> swift, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुगः|आशुग
आशु + -ग + .({@-गः@})<BR>—1 the wind.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR>—3 an arrow; पपावनास्वादितपूर्वमाशुगः R. 3. 54, 11. 83, 12. 91<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुगामिन्
आशु + -गामिन् <i>a.</i> going quickly. ━<i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुतोष|आशुतोषः
आशु + -तोष <i>a.</i> easily appeased or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुतोषः|आशुतोष
आशु + -तोष + .({@-षः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुपत्री
आशु + -पत्री a tree which yields frankincense (शल्लकीलता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुपत्वन्
आशु + -पत्वन् <i>a.</i> flying quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुफलः|आशुफल
आशु + -फलः A kind of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुबोध
आशु + -बोध <i>a.</i> ‘teaching quickly’, N. of a treatise of grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुया
आशु + -या <i>a.</i> going quickly. ━<i>ind.</i> quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुव्रीहिः|आशुव्रीहि
आशु + -व्रीहिः rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुषेण
आशु + -षेण <i>a.</i> Ved. having swift arrows. नम आशुषेणाय चाशुरथाय च Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुसंधेय
आशु + -संधेय <i>a.</i> Easy to be joined together or reconciled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुहेमन्
आशु + -हेमन् <i>a.</i> running on quickly, urging the horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुहेषस्
आशु + -हेषस् <i>a.</i> Ved. quickly neighing; having quick horses, quickly<BR> praised; (शीघ्रशब्दायमान). N. of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुत्वम्
आशुत्वम्, -ता<BR> Quickness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुता
आशुत्वम्, -ता<BR> Quickness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुमत्|आशुमन्त्
आशुमत्^1 <i>ind.</i> Quickly; यथा मनो मनस्केतैः परापनत्याशुमत् Av. 6. 105. 1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: corrected after the quotation of AV 6.105.1 where there is the word आशुमत् (and not आशुमन्); confirmed by MW and PWG and the text of AV.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिमन्
आशिमन्^1 <i>m.</i> [आशोर्भावः इमनिच्] Quickness.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: imanic suffix; cf AP90 MW for short 'I'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणि|आशुशुक्षणिः
आशुशुक्षणि <i>a.</i> [आ शष् सन् अनि Uṇ. 2. 102]<BR>—1 Being worshipped on account of shining very quickly, or causing sorrow<BR> to oneʼs enemies (Sāy.).<BR>—2 Shining forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणिः|आशुशुक्षणि
आशुशुक्षणि + .{@-णिः@}<BR>—1 Wind, air.<BR>—2 Fire; Bhāg. 8. 19. 26; मन्त्रपूतानि हवींषि प्रतिगृह्णात्येतत् प्रीत्याशुशुक्षणिः<BR> K. 44. cf. also Bhāg. 8. 19. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशू
आशू <i>a.</i> Quick, fast (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशेकुटिन्
आशेकुटिन् <i>m.</i> A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशोकेय
आशोकेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अशोक-ढञ्] (A place &c.) Near an Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशोषणम्
आशोषणम् The act of drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौचम्
आशौचम् [अशुचेर्भावः अण्; P. VII. 3. 30] Impurity, see अशौचम्;<BR> दशाहं शावमाशौचं सपिण्डेषु विधीयते Ms. 5. 59, 61, 62, 74, 80; Y. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौचनिर्णयः|आशौचनिर्णय
आशौचम् + .{@-निर्णयः@} N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौचिन्
आशौचिन् <i>a.</i> Impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य्यं
आश्चर्य <i>a.</i> [आ-चर्-ण्यत् सुट् आश्चर्यमानेत्ये P. VI. 1. 147]<BR> Marvellous, wonderful, extraordinary, astonishing, strange, curious आश्चर्यो<BR> गवां दोहोऽगोपेन Sk.; तदनु ववृषुः पुष्पमाश्चर्यमेघाः R. 16. 87;<BR> ˚दर्शनो मनुष्यलोकः Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यम्
आश्चर्य + .{@-र्यम्@}<BR>—1 A wonder, miracle, marvel; किमाश्चर्यं क्षारदेशे प्राणदा यमदूतिका<BR> Udb. कर्माश्चर्याणि U. 1 wonderful deeds; K. 65; Mv. 1; Bg. 11. 6, 2. 29.<BR>—2 Surprise, wonder, astonishment; ˚मय Bg. 11. 11.<BR>—3 A strange appearance, prodigy.<BR>—4 (Used as an exclamation) A wonder, how strange or curious; आश्चर्यं<BR> परिपीडितोऽभिरमते यच्चातकस्तृष्णया<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">Page0368-1</a>]<BR> Cāt. 2. 4; usually with यच्च, यत्र or यदि with a following<BR> potential or future.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्चर्यभूत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0367-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यभूत
आश्चर्य + -भूत <i>a.</i> wonderful, being an object of wonder; K. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यता
आश्चर्यता, -त्वम्<BR> Wonderfulness, astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यत्वम्
आश्चर्यता, -त्वम्<BR> Wonderfulness, astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतन
आश्चो(श्च्यो)तन <i>a.</i> Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्च्योतन
आश्चो(श्च्यो)तन <i>a.</i> Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतनम्
आश्चो(श्च्यो)तन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Aspersion, sprinkling; U. 2.<BR>—2 Applying ghee &c. to the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्म|आश्मः
आश्म <i>a.</i> (-श्मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्मन-अण्] Made of stone, stony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मः|आश्म
आश्म + .{@-श्मः@} Anything made of stone.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्मभारिक, आश्मरथ्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मभारिक
आश्म + -भारिक <i>a.</i> having a mass of stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मरथ्यः|आश्मरथ्य
आश्म + -रथ्यः N. of a teacher of ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मन|आश्मनः
आश्मन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्मनो विकारः अण्] Stony, made of stones. स<BR> चापमाश्मनप्रख्यं सेषुं धत्तेऽन्यदुर्वहाम् Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मनः|आश्मन
आश्मन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 Anything made of stone.<BR>—2 N. of Aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मरिक|आश्मरिकः
आश्मरिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्मर्येव स्वार्थे बा˚ ठञ्] Suffering from stone<BR> in the bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मरिकः|आश्मरिक
आश्मरिक + .{@-कः@} N. of a disease (अश्मरी q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मिक
आश्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Made of stone.<BR>—2 Carrying or bearing stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यै
आश्यै €1 Ā. To become congealed or coagulated, to become dry; यावन्नाश्यायते<BR> वेदिः R. 17. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
आश्यान <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Congealed, consolidated; पङ्कैरिवाश्यानघनैस्तटानि Ki. 16. 10;<BR> अन्तरालग्नाश्यानरुधिरबिन्दुना K.<BR>—2 Partially dried; पथश्चाश्यानकर्दमान् R. 4. 24; Ku. 7. 9; dried<BR> by fumigation (as hair); R. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रपणम्
आश्रपणम् [आ-श्रा-णिच् ल्युट्] The act of cooking or boiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रम्
आश्रम् [अश्रमेव, स्वार्थेऽण्] Tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमः|आश्रम|आश्रमं
आश्रमः, -मम्<BR> [आ-श्रम् आधारे घञ् वृद्धयभावः]<BR>—1 A hermitage, hut, cell, dwelling or abode of ascetics; शरणान्यशरण्यानि<BR> आश्रमाणि कृतानि नः Rām. 7. 6. 5.<BR>—2 A stage, order, or period of the (religious) life of a Brāhmaṇa [These<BR> are four:− ब्रह्मचर्य the life of a student; गार्हस्थ्य the life<BR> of a house-holder; वानप्रस्थ the life of an anchorite or hermit,<BR> and संन्यास the life of a Bhikṣu or beggar. Kṣatriyas (and Vaiśyas<BR> also) can enter, upon the first three Āśramas; cf. Ś. 7. 18; V. 5;<BR> (according to some authorities they can enter the fourth also; cf. स<BR> किलाश्रममन्त्यमाश्रितः R. 8. 14; पूर्वाश्रमः Ku. 5. 50.)]<BR>—3 A college, school.<BR>—4 A wood or thicket (where ascetics practise penance).<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्रमोपनिषद्, आश्रमगुरुः, आश्रमधर्मः, आश्रमपदम्, आश्रममण्डलम्, आश्रमस्थानम्, आश्रमपर्वन्, आश्रमभ्रष्ट, आश्रमलक्षणम्, आश्रमवासः, आश्रमवासिक, आश्रमवासिन्, आश्रमालयः, आश्रमसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमम्
आश्रमः, -मम्<BR> [आ-श्रम् आधारे घञ् वृद्धयभावः]<BR>—1 A hermitage, hut, cell, dwelling or abode of ascetics; शरणान्यशरण्यानि<BR> आश्रमाणि कृतानि नः Rām. 7. 6. 5.<BR>—2 A stage, order, or period of the (religious) life of a Brāhmaṇa [These<BR> are four:− ब्रह्मचर्य the life of a student; गार्हस्थ्य the life<BR> of a house-holder; वानप्रस्थ the life of an anchorite or hermit,<BR> and संन्यास the life of a Bhikṣu or beggar. Kṣatriyas (and Vaiśyas<BR> also) can enter, upon the first three Āśramas; cf. Ś. 7. 18; V. 5;<BR> (according to some authorities they can enter the fourth also; cf. स<BR> किलाश्रममन्त्यमाश्रितः R. 8. 14; पूर्वाश्रमः Ku. 5. 50.)]<BR>—3 A college, school.<BR>—4 A wood or thicket (where ascetics practise penance).<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्रमोपनिषद्, आश्रमगुरुः, आश्रमधर्मः, आश्रमपदम्, आश्रममण्डलम्, आश्रमस्थानम्, आश्रमपर्वन्, आश्रमभ्रष्ट, आश्रमलक्षणम्, आश्रमवासः, आश्रमवासिक, आश्रमवासिन्, आश्रमालयः, आश्रमसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमोपनिषद्
आश्रमः + -उपनिषद् N. of an upaniṣad<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमगुरुः|आश्रमगुरु
आश्रमः + -गुरुः the head of a religious order, a preceptor, principal.<BR> कर्तुमाश्रमगुरुः स चाश्रमत् Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमधर्मः|आश्रमधर्म|आश्रमधर्म्म
आश्रमः + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the special duties of each order or life.<BR>—2 the duties of one leading a hermitʼs life; य इमामाश्रमधर्मे नियुङ्क्ते Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमपदम्
आश्रमः + -पदम्, -मण्डलम्, -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a hermitage (including the surrounding grounds), a penance forest (तपोवनम्);<BR> शान्तमिदमाश्रमपदम् Ś. 1. 16.<BR>—2 a period in the religious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">Page0368-2</a>]<BR> life of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रममण्डलम्
आश्रमः + -पदम्, -मण्डलम्, -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a hermitage (including the surrounding grounds), a penance forest (तपोवनम्);<BR> शान्तमिदमाश्रमपदम् Ś. 1. 16.<BR>—2 a period in the religious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">Page0368-2</a>]<BR> life of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमस्थानम्
आश्रमः + -पदम्, -मण्डलम्, -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a hermitage (including the surrounding grounds), a penance forest (तपोवनम्);<BR> शान्तमिदमाश्रमपदम् Ś. 1. 16.<BR>—2 a period in the religious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">Page0368-2</a>]<BR> life of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमपर्वन्
आश्रमः + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> The first section of the fifteenth book of the<BR> Mahābhārata. <i>i. e.</i> आश्रमवासिकपर्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमभ्रष्ट
आश्रमः + -भ्रष्ट <i>a.</i> fallen from any religious order, apostate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमलक्षणम्
आश्रमः + -लक्षणम् An indicatory mark of the religous order, cf. मेखलाजिनदण्डेन<BR> ब्रह्मचारीति लक्ष्यते । गृहस्थो दानवेदाद्यैर्नखलोम्ना वनाश्रिताः ॥ त्रिदण्डेन<BR> यतिश्चैव लक्षणानि पृथक् पृथक् । यस्यैतल्लक्षणं नास्ति प्रायश्चित्ती<BR> न चाश्रमी ॥ (दक्षसंहिता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमवासः|आश्रमवास
आश्रमः + -वासः residence in a hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमवासिक
आश्रमः + -वासिक <i>a.</i> relating to residence in a hermitage; ˚कं पर्व<BR> the 15th book of the Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमवासिन्
आश्रमः + -वासिन्, -आलयः, -सद् <i>m.</i> an ascetic, hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमालयः|आश्रमालय
आश्रमः + -वासिन्, -आलयः, -सद् <i>m.</i> an ascetic, hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमसद्
आश्रमः + -वासिन्, -आलयः, -सद् <i>m.</i> an ascetic, hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिक|आश्रमिकः
आश्रमिक <i>a.</i>, आश्रमिन् <i>a.</i> [आश्रम-ठन् इनि]<BR>—1 Belonging to one of the four orders or periods of religious life; Ms. 6. 90-91, 12. 111;<BR> यस्मात्त्रयोऽप्याश्रमिणो ज्ञानेनान्नेन चान्वहं । गृहस्थेनैव<BR> धार्यन्ते 3. 78.<BR>—2 Belonging to a hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिन्
आश्रमिक <i>a.</i>, आश्रमिन् <i>a.</i> [आश्रम-ठन् इनि]<BR>—1 Belonging to one of the four orders or periods of religious life; Ms. 6. 90-91, 12. 111;<BR> यस्मात्त्रयोऽप्याश्रमिणो ज्ञानेनान्नेन चान्वहं । गृहस्थेनैव<BR> धार्यन्ते 3. 78.<BR>—2 Belonging to a hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रवः|आश्रव|आश्रवं
आश्रवः<BR>—1 Stream, river.<BR>—2 Fault, transgression; see आस्रव and under आश्रु also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि<BR>—1 U. 1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To resort or betake oneself to; to have recourse to (a place,<BR> way, course of action &c.); विचरितमृगयूथान्याश्रयिष्ये वनानि V. 5. 17;<BR> निम्नगाम् आश्रयन्ते Ṛs. 1. 27; दक्षिणां मूर्तिमाश्रित्य K. 128, 132;<BR> न वयं कुमारमाश्रयामहे Mu. 4; आशिश्राय च भूतलम्<BR> Bk. 14. 111 fell on the ground; 17. 92; वृत्तिमाश्रित्य वैतसीम् R. 4. 35<BR> resorting to or following; so धैर्यम्, शोकम्, बलम्. मित्रभावम्,<BR> संस्कृतमाश्रित्य &c.; आश्रित्य having recourse or reference; तामाश्रित्य<BR> M. 4. 1, कतमत्प्रकरणमाश्रित्य गीयताम् Ś. 1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To seek refuge with, dwell with or in, inhabit (as a place &c.);<BR> शरण्यमेनमाश्रयन्ते R. 13. 7; Pt. 1. 51; तथा गृहस्थमाश्रित्य<BR> वर्तन्ते सर्व आश्रमाः Ms. 3. 77; सर्वे गुणाः काञ्चनमाश्रयन्ते.<BR>—2 To go through, experience; एको रसः … पृथक् पृथगिवाश्रयते<BR> विवर्तान् U. 3. 47.<BR>—3 To rest or depend upon.<BR>—4 To adhere or stick to, fall to the lot of, happen, occur; पापमेवाश्रयेदस्मान्<BR> Bg. 1. 36 we shall incur sin.<BR>—5 To choose, prefer. —6 To assist, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयः|आश्रय
आश्रयः [आश्रि-अच्]<BR>—1 A resting-place, seat, substratum; सौहृदादपृथगाश्रयामिमाम् U. 1. 45.<BR> so आश्रयासिद्ध q. v. below.<BR>—2 That on which anything depends or rests or with which it is closely connected.<BR>—3 Recipient, receptacle, a person or thing in which any quality is present<BR> or retained &c.; तमाश्रयं दुष्प्रसहस्य तेजसः R. 3. 58.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A place of refuge, asylum; shelter; भर्ता वै ह्याश्रयः स्त्रीणाम्<BR> Vet.; तदहमाश्रयोन्मूलनेनैव त्वामकामां करोमि Mu. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A dwelling, house.<BR>—5 Having recourse or resort to, resort; oft. in comp. साभूद्रामाश्रया<BR> भूयः R. 12. 35; नानाश्रया प्रकृतिः &c.<BR>—6 Following, practising; योऽवमन्येत ते मूले हेतुशास्त्राश्रयाद् द्विजः Ms. 2. 11.<BR>—7 Choosing, taking, attaching oneself to.<BR>—8 Dependence on; oft. in comp.; मम सर्वे विषयास्त्वदाश्रयाः R. 8. 69.<BR>—9 Patron, supporter; विनाश्रयं न तिष्ठन्ति पण्डिता वनिता लताः Udb.<BR>—10 A prop, support; वृक्षेषु विद्धमिषुभिर्जघनाश्रयेषु R. 9. 60.<BR>—11 Help, assistance, protection.<BR>—12 A quiver; बाणमाश्रयमुखात् समुद्धरन् R. 11. 26.<BR>—13 Authority, sanction, warrant.<BR>—14 Connection, relation, association. राघवाश्रयसत्कथाः Rām. 6. 90. 93.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">Page0369-1</a>]<BR>—15 Union, attachment.<BR>—16 A plea, an excuse.<BR>—17 Contiguity, vicinity.<BR>—18 Seeking shelter or protection with another (= संश्रय), one of<BR> the six <i>guṇas</i>, q. v.<BR>—19 An appropriate act, or one consistent with character.<BR>—20 Source, origin.<BR>—21 (In gram.) The subject, or that to which the predicate is attached.<BR>—22 (With Buddhists) The five organs of sense with <i>Manas</i> or mind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आश्रयासिद्धः, आश्रयासिद्धिः, आश्रयाशः, आश्रयभुज्, आश्रयभूत, आश्रयलिङ्गम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0368-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयासिद्धः|आश्रयासिद्ध
आश्रयः + -असिद्धः, -असिद्धिः <i>f.</i> a kind of fallacy, one of the three sub-divisions<BR> of असिद्ध; (that whose substratum is false or fictitious); <i>e. g.</i><BR> गगनारविन्दं सुरभि अरविन्दत्वात्सरोजारविन्दवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयासिद्धिः|आश्रयासिद्धि
आश्रयः + -असिद्धः, -असिद्धिः <i>f.</i> a kind of fallacy, one of the three sub-divisions<BR> of असिद्ध; (that whose substratum is false or fictitious); <i>e. g.</i><BR> गगनारविन्दं सुरभि अरविन्दत्वात्सरोजारविन्दवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयाशः|आश्रयाश
आश्रयः + -आशः, -भुज् <i>a.</i> consuming everything with which it comes in contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयाशः|आश्रयाश
आश्रयः + -आशः, -भुज् + .({@-आशः, -क्@})<BR>—1 fire; दुर्वृत्तः क्रियते धूर्तैः श्रीमानात्मविवृद्धये । किं नाम खलसंसर्गः<BR> कुरुते नाश्रयाशवत् ॥ Udb.<BR>—2 <i>a.</i> forfeiter of asylum.<BR>—3 the constellation कृत्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयाशक्
आश्रयः + -आशः, -भुज् + .({@-आशः, -क्@})<BR>—1 fire; दुर्वृत्तः क्रियते धूर्तैः श्रीमानात्मविवृद्धये । किं नाम खलसंसर्गः<BR> कुरुते नाश्रयाशवत् ॥ Udb.<BR>—2 <i>a.</i> forfeiter of asylum.<BR>—3 the constellation कृत्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयभुज्
आश्रयः + -आशः, -भुज् <i>a.</i> consuming everything with which it comes in contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयभूत
आश्रयः + -भूत <i>a.</i> one who is the refuge or support (of another person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयलिङ्गम्
आश्रयः + -लिङ्गम् an adjective (a word which must agree in gender with the<BR> word which it qualifies or refers to).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयण
आश्रयण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Resorting to, seeking refuge with; पुनरङ्काश्रयणी भवामि ते Ku. 4. 20.<BR>—2 Referring to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणम्
आश्रयण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Betaking oneself to, taking refuge with.<BR>—2 Accepting, choosing.<BR>—3 Joining.<BR>—4 Refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणीय
आश्रयणीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be had recourse to; कोशेनाश्रयणीयत्वमिति तस्यार्थसंग्रहः R. 17. 60.<BR>—2 To be practised or followed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयिन्
आश्रयिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Resting with, dependent on.<BR>—2 Related to, concerning; तदाश्रयिणी कथा V. 3. 10; K. 213.<BR>—3 Resorting to; मयूरपृष्ठाश्रयिणा गुहेन R. 6. 4; Ratn. 2. अहमेत्य<BR> पतङ्गवर्त्मना पुनरङ्काश्रयिणी भवामि ते Ku. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयिन्
आश्रयिन् + .{@-आश्रयिन्@} <i>m.</i> A complementary detail. आश्रयिष्वविशेषेण भावोऽर्थः<BR> प्रतीयेत । MS. 4. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आश्रित <i>p. p.</i> (Used actively) (with an acc.)<BR>—1 Resorting to, having recourse to; स किलाश्रममन्त्यमाश्रितः R. 8. 14;<BR> कृष्णाश्रितः = कृष्णमाश्रितः Sk.; मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम् Bg. 9. 11;<BR> R. 1. 13.<BR>—2 Dwelling in, inhabiting, seated or resting on, stationing oneself at<BR> or on; इदं स्फटिकतलमाश्रितो भवामि M. 4; so वातायनमाश्रितः<BR> पश्यति; द्रव्याश्रितो गुणः Ak.; R. 12. 21, 1. 75; हार˚, दुर्ग˚ &c.<BR>—3 Using, employing.<BR>—4 Following. practising, observing; माध्यस्थ्यम्, धर्मम्, प्रव्रज्याम्;<BR> कल्पवृक्षा इवाश्रिताः Ku. 6. 6; Bk. 7. 42.<BR>—5 Receiving anything as an inherent or integral part.<BR>—6 Dependent on; राष्ट्रं बाहुबलाश्रितम् Ms. 9. 255.<BR>—7 Referring to, regarding; भीष्माश्रिताः कथाः Mb.; उवाच धर्मसंयुक्तमश्वमेधाश्रितं<BR> वचः Rām. 7. 91. 6.<BR>—8 (Passively used) Resorted to, inhabited &c.; चटकाश्रिता शाखा Pt. 1; R. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रितः|आश्रित
आश्रित + .{@-तः@} A dependent servent, follower; अस्मदाश्रितानाम् H. 1; प्रभूणां<BR> प्रायश्चलं गौरवमाश्रितेषु Ku. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रितम्
आश्रित + .{@-तम्@} (pl.) The objects perceived by the senses and mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रिः|आश्रि
आश्रिः <i>f.</i> The edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रु
आश्रु €5 P.<BR>—1 To hear, listen to.<BR>—2 To promise (with dat. of person; cf. P. I. 4. 40; Y. 2. 196).<BR>—3 To accept, undertake. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to hear,<BR>—2 To call, particularly in ritualistic formulas; ओमित्याश्रावयति<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 1. 9.<BR>—3 To draw towards, win over, attract; आश्रावयेदस्य जनं Bk. 12. 30.<BR>—4 To say, repeat (as a Mantra). ॐ श्रावयेत्याश्रावयन्ति T. Up. 1. 8. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव <i>a.</i> [आ-श्रु-अच्] Obedient, compliant; भिषजामनाश्रवः<BR> R. 19. 49; यशःपथादाश्रवतापदोत्थात् N. 3. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रवः|आश्रव|आश्रवं
आश्रव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A promise, engagement.<BR>—2 Fault, transgression.<BR>—3 One of the categories according to the Jainas.<BR>—4 Worldly torment or pain (cf. अविद्याऽस्मितारागद्वेषाभिनिवेशाः क्लेशाः<BR> आश्रवाः -इति पतञ्जलिः). सवितर्कविचारमवाप शान्तं प्रथमं ध्यानमनाश्रवप्रकारम्<BR> Bu. C. 5. 10. (see आस्रव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रावणम्
आश्रावणम्<BR>—1 Calling out so as to make one listen.<BR>—2 N. of certain short words uttered at ceremonies; ॐ स्वधेत्याश्रावणमस्तु<BR> स्वधेति प्रत्याश्रावणम् Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत|आश्रुतः
आश्रुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heard.<BR>—2 Promised, agreed, accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुतम्
आश्रुत + .{@-तम्@} Calling so as to make one listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुतिः|आश्रुति
आश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Hearing.<BR>—2 Accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत्कर्ण
आश्रुत्कर्ण^1 <i>a.</i> One whose ears hear all around (Ved.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्
आश्लिष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To embrace, clasp; प्रदीप्ते रागाग्नौ सुदृढतरमाश्लिष्यति वधूम् Bh. 3. 92.<BR>—2 To cleave or stick to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्ट
आश्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Embraced, clasped; used actively also; P. III. 4. 72. आश्लिष्टो लक्ष्मीम् Sk.<BR>—2 Connected, interwoven, blended; परस्पराश्लिष्टशाखैः पादपैः Mb.<BR>—3 Joined to, touching, in contact with; अवनितलाश्लिष्टललाटरेखया<BR> K. 67; अङ्गद ˚भुज R. 6. 53; Śi. 3. 72; मेघमाश्लिष्टसानुम् Me. 2.<BR>—4 Joining what adheres or attaches to.<BR>—5 Invested; spread.<BR>—6 Deduced, concluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेषः|आश्लेष
आश्लेषः<BR>—1 Embracing, clasping, an embrace; आश्लेष; लोलुपवधूस्तनकार्कश्यसाक्षिणीम्<BR> Śi. 2. 17; Amaru. 17, 74, 95 कण्ठाश्लेषप्रणयिनि जने Me. 3, 108.<BR>—2 Contact, intimate connection; relation; सामीप्याश्लेषविषयैर्व्याप्त्याधारश्चतुर्विधः Mugdha.<BR>—3 The site of an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेषाः
आश्लेषः + .{@-षाः@} <i>f.</i> (pl.) N. of the ninth Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेषण
आश्लेषण Adherence, hanging on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्व|आश्वं
आश्व <i>a.</i> (-श्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्वस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to or coming from a horse, equestrian; आश्वं कफहरं<BR> मूत्रं कृमिदद्रुषु शस्यते Suśr.<BR>—2 Drawn by horses (as a chariot).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वम्
आश्व + .{@-श्वम्@}<BR>—1 A number of horses.<BR>—2 A chariot drawn by horses.<BR>—3 The state or action of a horse (अश्वस्य भावः कर्म वा Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थ|आश्वत्थं
आश्वत्थ <i>a.</i> (-त्थी <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@आश्वत्थिक@}<BR> (-की <i>f.</i>) [अश्वत्थस्येदम् अण् ठक् वा P. IV. 2. 22]<BR>—1 Relating to or made of the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 Relating to the fruit-bearing season of this tree, as a मुहूर्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थी
आश्वत्थ <i>a.</i> (-त्थी <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@आश्वत्थिक@}<BR> (-की <i>f.</i>) [अश्वत्थस्येदम् अण् ठक् वा P. IV. 2. 22]<BR>—1 Relating to or made of the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 Relating to the fruit-bearing season of this tree, as a मुहूर्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थिक
आश्वत्थ <i>a.</i> (-त्थी <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@आश्वत्थिक@}<BR> (-की <i>f.</i>) [अश्वत्थस्येदम् अण् ठक् वा P. IV. 2. 22]<BR>—1 Relating to or made of the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 Relating to the fruit-bearing season of this tree, as a मुहूर्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थिकी
आश्वत्थ <i>a.</i> (-त्थी <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@आश्वत्थिक@}<BR> (-की <i>f.</i>) [अश्वत्थस्येदम् अण् ठक् वा P. IV. 2. 22]<BR>—1 Relating to or made of the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 Relating to the fruit-bearing season of this tree, as a मुहूर्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्था
आश्वत्थ + .{@-त्था@} The night having the अश्वत्थ Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थम्
आश्वत्थ + .{@-त्थम्@} The fruit of the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0369-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वभारिक
आश्वभारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> = अश्वभारं हरति, वहति आवहति वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वमेधिक
आश्वमेधिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्वमेधाय हितं ठक्] Belonging to the Horse-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वमेधिकम्
आश्वमेधिक + .{@-कम्@} N. of the 14th Parvan of Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुज|आश्वयुजः
आश्वयुज <i>a.</i> (-जी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्वयुज-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the month Āśvina.<BR>—2 Born under the constellation अश्वयुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुजः|आश्वयुज
आश्वयुज + .{@-जः@} The month आश्विन; भाद्रपदाश्वयुजौ वर्षाः Suśr.; त्यजेदाश्वयुजे<BR> मासि मुन्यन्नं पूर्वसंचितम् Ms. 6. 15; Y. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुजी
आश्वयुज + .{@-जी@} The day of the full moon in Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुजक
आश्वयुजक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sown on the day of full moon in Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वरथ
आश्वरथ <i>a.</i> (-थी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्वरथ-अञ्] Belonging to a chariot drawn by horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्वलक्षण-ठक्] Knowing the marks of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिकः|आश्वलक्षणिक
आश्वलक्षणिक + .{@-कः@} A farrier, groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्व-ठञ्] Relating to a horse, drawn by horses,<BR> equestrian, cavalier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विकः|आश्विक
आश्विक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A cavalier.<BR>—2 A combination of stars or omens presaging acquisition of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging or sacred to the Aśvins (अश्विनौ देवते अस्य).<BR>—2 Pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनः|आश्विन
आश्विन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 N. of a month (in which the moon is near the constellation Aśvini).<BR>—2 A sacrifice or a weapon presided over by the Aśvins.<BR>—3 (du.) The Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनी
आश्विन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 N. of certain bricks.<BR>—2 A pile, stack (चितिभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनम्
आश्विन + .{@-नम्@} A dayʼs journey for a horse or rider (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनचिह्नितम्
आश्विन + .{@-चिह्नितम्@} The autumnal equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेयः|आश्विनेय
आश्विनेयः <i>m.</i> [अश्विन्याः अपत्यं ढक्]<BR>—1 The two Aśvins (physicians of gods).<BR>—2 N. of Nakula and Sahadeva, the last two of the five Pānḍava princes<BR>—3 A dayʼs journey for a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अश्व-खञ्] Made or traversed by a horse as a<BR> journey &c.; ˚नोऽध्वा Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीनः|आश्वीन|आश्वीनं
आश्वीन + .{@-नः, -नम्@} The distance travelled by a horse in a day; सहस्राश्वीने<BR> वा इतः स्वर्गो लोकः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीनम्
आश्वीन + .{@-नः, -नम्@} The distance travelled by a horse in a day; सहस्राश्वीने<BR> वा इतः स्वर्गो लोकः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीयम्
आश्वीयम् A number of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायनः|आश्वलायन
आश्वलायनः N. of the author of a celebrated ritual work, called<BR> the Āśvalāyana Sūtras; कौसल्यश्चाश्वलायनः Praśna. Up. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायनशाखा
आश्वलायनः + .{@-शाखा@} The school of आश्वलायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वस्
आश्वस् €2 P.<BR>—1 To breathe; सुखमाश्वसन्ति गिरयः Mv. 5. 51 are lying at ease.<BR>—2 To breathe freely, recover breath, take courage, take heart, rest secure,<BR> be at ease; प्रत्ययादाश्वसत्यः Me. 8; दूरस्थोऽस्मीति नाश्वसेत्<BR> Pt. 1. 307; Bk. 4. 38, 5. 23.<BR>—3 To revive.<BR>—4 To have confidence in. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To encourage, comfort, console, cheer up; Bg. 11. 50; आश्वास्य पाययित्वा<BR> च परिप्लाव्य च वाजिनः Mb. 4. 67. 19. तदा संकीर्तनेनाश्वासयाम्यात्मानम्<BR> V. 3; R. 12. 5, 14. 58, 15. 45; Me. 115; V. 5. 16.<BR>—2 To refresh, gratify; छायाश्वासितपथिकजनसार्थः Pt. 2.<BR>—3 To conciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासः|आश्वास
आश्वासः<BR>—1 Taking or recovering breath, breathing freely, recovery, revival.<BR>—2 Consolation, cheering up, inspiring confidence; आश्वासस्नेहभक्तीनामेकमालम्बनं<BR> महत् U. 6. 10.<BR>—3 An assurance of safety or protection.<BR>—4 Cessation, completion, stop.<BR>—5 A chapter or section of a book.<BR>—6 A probable story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासक|आश्वासकः
आश्वासक <i>a.</i> Consolatory, comforting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासकः|आश्वासक
आश्वासक + .{@-कः@} Clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासनम्
आश्वासनम् Consoling, encouraging, cheering up, consolation; तदिदं<BR> द्वितीयं हृदयाश्वासनम् Ś. 7; देवस्याश्वासनं भवति Pt. 1 cheering<BR> up of spirits, recovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासिक
आश्वासिक <i>a.</i> Trustworthy, reliable; Mb. 12. 218. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासिन्
आश्वासिन् <i>a.</i> [आ-श्वस्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Breathing freely, reviving, becoming cheerful; मनस्तु तद्भावदर्शनाश्वासि Ś. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढः|आषाढ
आषाढः [आषाढी पूर्णिमा अस्मिन्मासे अण्]<BR>—1 N. of a Hindu month (corresponding to part of June and July); आषाढस्य<BR> प्रथमदिवसे Me. 2; शेते विष्णुः सदाषाढे कार्तिके प्रतिबोध्यते V. P.<BR>—2 A staff of the Palāśa wood carried by an ascetic; अथाजिनाषाढधरः<BR> प्रगल्भवाक् Ku. 5. 30.<BR>—3 The Malaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढा
आषाढः + .{@-ढा@} The 20th and the 21st lunar mansions usually called पूर्वाषाढा<BR> and उत्तराषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढी
आषाढः + .{@-ढी@} The day of full moon in the month of Āṣāḍha; तस्य नित्यं<BR> सदा ऽऽषाढ्यां माध्यां च बहवो द्विजाः Mb. 12. 171. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आषाढभव, आषाढभू<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभव|आषाढभवः
आषाढः + -भव, -भू <i>a.</i> produced in the month of Āṣāḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभू
आषाढः + -भव, -भू <i>a.</i> produced in the month of Āṣāḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभवः|आषाढभव
आषाढः + -भव, -भू + .({@-वः, -भूः@}) the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढाभूः
आषाढः + -भव, -भू + .({@-वः, -भूः@}) the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढकः|आषाढक
आषाढकः The month आषाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढिन्
आषाढिन् <i>a.</i> Bearing a Palāśa staff; गृहीतव्रतेनाषाढिना; K. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढीय
आषाढीय <i>a.</i> [आषाढा-छ] Born under the constellation Āṣāḍhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्टमः|आष्टम
आष्टमः [अष्टमो भागः, अष्टम-ञ्] The 8th part; P. V. 3. 50-1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्रम्
आष्ट्रम् [अश्-व्याप्ता ष्ट्रन् Uṇ. 4. 159] Sky, ether, atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्रा
आष्ट्रम् + .{@-ष्ट्रा@} A prick or goad for driving cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्री
आष्ट्री<BR>—1 An extensive forest; आष्ट्र्यां पदं कृणुते अग्निधाने Rv. 10. 165. 3.<BR>—2 A kitchen, fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस्, आः <i>ind.</i> An interjection, implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Recollection; आः उपनयतु भवान् भूर्जपत्रम् V. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Anger; आः कथमद्यापि राक्षसत्रासः U. 1; आः पापे तिष्ठ<BR> तिष्ठ Māl. 8.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Pain; आः शीतम् K. P. 10.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Angry contradiction (अपाकरण); आः क एष मयि स्थिते<BR> Mu. 1; आः वृथामङ्गल पाठक Ve. 1.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Sorrow, regret; विद्यामातरमाः प्रदर्श्य नृपशून् भिक्षामहे<BR> निस्त्रपाः Udb.; (आः स्मरणेऽपाकरणे कोपसंतापयोस्तथा Med.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आः
आस्, आः <i>ind.</i> An interjection, implying<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Recollection; आः उपनयतु भवान् भूर्जपत्रम् V. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Anger; आः कथमद्यापि राक्षसत्रासः U. 1; आः पापे तिष्ठ<BR> तिष्ठ Māl. 8.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Pain; आः शीतम् K. P. 10.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Angry contradiction (अपाकरण); आः क एष मयि स्थिते<BR> Mu. 1; आः वृथामङ्गल पाठक Ve. 1.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) Sorrow, regret; विद्यामातरमाः प्रदर्श्य नृपशून् भिक्षामहे<BR> निस्त्रपाः Udb.; (आः स्मरणेऽपाकरणे कोपसंतापयोस्तथा Med.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् I. €2 Ā. (आस्ते, आसांचके, आसिष्ट; आसितुम्, आसित)<BR>—1 To sit, lie, rest; Bg. 2. 45; एतदासनमास्यताम् V. 5; आस्यतामिति<BR> चोक्तः सन्नासीताभिमुखं गुरोः Ms. 2. 193.<BR>—2 To live, dwell; तावद्वर्षाण्यासते देवलोके Mb.; यत्रास्मै रोचते<BR> तत्रायमास्ताम् K. 196; कुरूनास्ते Sk.; यत्रामृतास आसते Rv. 9. 15. 2;<BR> Bk. 4. 6, 8. 79.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">Page0371-1</a>]<BR>—3 To sit quietly, take no hostile measures, remain idle; आसीनं त्वामुत्थापयति<BR> द्वयम् Śi. 2. 57.<BR>—4 To be, exist.<BR>—5 To be contained in; जगन्ति यस्यां सविकाशमासत Śi. 1. 23.<BR>—6 To abide, remain, continue or be in any state, be doing anything, last;<BR> oft. used with present participles to denote a continuous or uninterrupted<BR> action; विदारयन्प्रगर्जंश्चास्ते Pt. 1 kept on, continued, tearing<BR> up and bellowing; used in this sense also with an adj., subst., indeclinable,<BR> past part., an adverb (तूष्णीम् &c.), or with the instr. of a noun;<BR> सुखेनास्ते &c.<BR>—7 To lead to, result in (with dat.); आस्तां मानसतुष्टये सुकृतिनां<BR> नीतिर्नवोढेव वः H. 1. 185.<BR>—8 To cease, have an end.<BR>—9 To solemnize, celebrate.<BR>—10 To let go, lay or put aside; आस्तां तावत् let it aside, let it<BR> go, to say nothing of, not to mention; K. 18.<BR>—11 To be indifferent; ननु आस्ते इत्युपवेशने भवति । नावश्यमुपवेशने<BR> एव, औदासीन्येऽपि दृश्यते । ŚB. on MS. 3. 6. 24. ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> cause to sit, seat, fix; आसयत्सलिले पृथ्वीम् Sk. <i>Desid.</i> आसिसिषते<BR> To wish to sit &c. ━II. €4 P. [आस्यति, आसितुम्]<BR>—1 To enclose; border.<BR>—2 To admit (as water) into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0370-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसः|आस
आसः [आस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A seat.<BR>—2 A bow<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसम्
आसः + .({@-सम्@} also); स सासिः सासुसूः सासः Ki. 15. 5.<BR>—3 Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसम्
आसः + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Seat or lower part of the body.<BR>—2 Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनम्
आसनम् [आस्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sitting down.<BR>—2 A seat, place, stool; Bg. 11. 42; स वासवेनासनसन्निकृष्टम् Ku. 3. 2;<BR> आसनं मुच् to leave oneʼs seat, rise; R. 3. 11.<BR>—3 A particular posture or mode of sitting; cf. पद्म˚, वीर˚, भद्र˚,<BR> वज्र˚ &c. cf. अनायासेन येन स्यादजस्रं ब्रह्मचिन्तनम् । आसनं<BR> तद् विजानीयाद् योगिनां सुखदायकम् ॥<BR>—4 Sitting down or halting, stopping, encamping.<BR>—5 Abiding, dwelling; Ms. 2. 246, 6. 59.<BR>—6 Any peculiar mode of sexual enjoyment (84 such <i>āsanas</i> are usually mentioned).<BR>—7 Maintaining a post against an enemy (opp. यानम्), one of the six<BR> modes of foreign policy; which are:− संधिर्ना विग्रहो यानमासनं द्वैधमाश्रयः<BR> Ak.; प्रतिबद्धशक्त्योः कालप्रतीक्षया तूष्णीमवस्थानमासनम्; परस्परस्य<BR> सामर्थ्यविघातादासनं स्मृतम् Agni P.; Ms. 7. 160, 162, 166; Y. 1. 347; Pt. 3.<BR>—8 The front part of an elephantʼs body, withers.<BR>—9 Throwing (fr. अस् to throw).<BR>—10 N. of two trees (असन and जीवक).<BR>—11 Place where the elephant-rider sits, cf. मस्तकद्वितयं दन्तावासनं<BR> वंश एव च । षडेते प्रोन्नता यस्य स गजो राजवाहनः ॥ Mātaṅga L. 2. 1.<BR>—12 Neutrality (as of a nation); Kau. A. 7. 1.<BR>—13 A moving piece (draught) in the game of dice; प्राणग्लहोऽयं समर<BR> इष्वक्षो वाहनासनः Bhāg. 6. 12. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसना
आसनम् + .{@-ना@} A seat, stool, stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनी
आसनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 Stay, abiding, sitting.<BR>—2 A small seat or stool.<BR>—3 A shop, stall.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आसनबन्धधीर, आसनमचूडकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनबन्धधीर
आसनम् + -बन्धधीर <i>a.</i> resolute to sit down, firm in oneʼs seat; निषेदुषीमासनबन्धधीरः R. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनमचूडकम्
आसनम् + -मचूडकम् Semen (मचूडकं विथावीति ख्यातम्); आसनमचूडकं<BR> शयनीयप्रच्छदपटापवारितं भवति किं न वेति Māl. 7. (v. l. आसनमथूरकम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसित
आसित <i>p. p.</i> [आस्-क्त] Seated, at rest; आसितः सः; आसितं तेन Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसितम्
आसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Sitting down.<BR>—2 A seat; इदमेषामासितम् Sk.<BR>—3 Abode, a place where one has lived; a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीन|आसीनः
आसीन <i>Pres. p.</i> Sitting, seated; आसीनानां सुरभितशिलं नाभिगन्धैर्मृगाणाम्<BR> ˚प्रचलायितम nodding when seated; falling asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या Sitting, abode, state of rest; आस्या वर्णकफस्थौल्यसौकुमार्यकरी सुखा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसा
आसा, आसः (Instr. and abl. of आस्) Before oneʼs eyes,<BR> by word of mouth, personally; in close vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसः|आस
आसा, आसः (Instr. and abl. of आस्) Before oneʼs eyes,<BR> by word of mouth, personally; in close vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसार
आसंसार, -संसृति <i>a.</i><BR> Liable to progress or alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसृति
आसंसार, -संसृति <i>a.</i><BR> Liable to progress or alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसारम्
आसंसार, -संसृति + .{@-रम्, -ति@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Till the end of the world or worldly existence; Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Within the limits or range of worldly existence, throughout the sphere<BR> of worldly life; आसंसारं त्रिभुवनमिदं चिन्वताम् तात तादृक् Bh. 3. 46;<BR> आसंसृतेरस्मि जगत्सु जातः Ki. 3. 6 (Malli. यावत्संसारम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसृति
आसंसार, -संसृति + .{@-रम्, -ति@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Till the end of the world or worldly existence; Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Within the limits or range of worldly existence, throughout the sphere<BR> of worldly life; आसंसारं त्रिभुवनमिदं चिन्वताम् तात तादृक् Bh. 3. 46;<BR> आसंसृतेरस्मि जगत्सु जातः Ki. 3. 6 (Malli. यावत्संसारम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गत्यम्
आसङ्गत्यम् Detachment, disunion. Separation; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंज्ञित
आसंज्ञित <i>a.</i> One with whom one has agreed or concerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंबाध
आसंबाध <i>a.</i> Blocked up, obstructed, confined (on all sides);<BR> आसंबाधा भविष्यन्ति पन्थानः शरवृष्टिभिः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसञ्ज्|आसंज्
आसञ्ज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fasten, fix on, attach to, join or add to, place or put on (dress,<BR> armour &c.); चापमासज्यकण्ठे Ku. 2. 64; अनुबन्ध आसज्यते Sk.;<BR> आसज्यमानेक्षणः Ś. 3. 25 with the eyes intently fixed; (fig. also);<BR> भुजे … स भूमेर्धुरमाससञ्ज R. 2. 74; so पुत्रे राज्यम्; जने<BR> दोषम् &c.; आससञ्ज भयं तेषाम् Bk. 14. 104 fear overtook them.<BR>—2 To confer upon, conduce to; तिष्ठतां तपसि पुण्यमासजन् Ki. 13. 44.<BR>—3 To stick or adhere to, depend upon.<BR>—4 To take up. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to attach, have anything fastened or put on.<BR>—2 To place, put, throw round; आसञ्जयामास यथाप्रदेशं कण्ठे गुणम् R. 6. 83.<BR>—3 To entrust or appoint. <i>pass.</i> (सज्यते) To adhere, stick,<BR> be attached; यदि नेष्टात्मनः पीडा मासञ्जि भवता जने Ki. 11. 29;<BR> cf. “Do unto others as you would be done by”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आसक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Strongly attached to, intent on, devoted or addicted to, (usually with<BR> loc. or in comp.) द्यूत˚, मृगया˚.<BR>—2 Absorbed or engaged in, zealously following or pursuing.<BR>—3 Fixed on, directed towards, joined or attached to, placed or resting<BR> on; मन्मुखासक्तदृष्टिः K. 158; यदासक्तं सख्यं जने Mv. 5. 58<BR> formed; शिखरासक्तमेघाः Ku. 6. 40 resting on; ˚बाहुलतया 8.<BR>—4 Surrounded, encircled.<BR>—5 Continuous, perpetual, eternal.<BR>—6 Trusting to, confiding in.<BR>—7 Obstructed, checked; कार्तवीर्यमुजासक्तं तज्जलं प्राप्य निर्मलम्<BR> Rām. 7. 32. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तम्
आसक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Eternally, perpetually.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आसक्तचित्त, आसक्तचेतस्, आसक्तमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचित्त
आसक्त + -चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचेतस्
आसक्त + -चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तमनस्
आसक्त + -चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तिः|आसक्ति
आसक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Attachment, devotion, fondness; बालिशचरितेष्वासक्तिः K. 120; intentness, application.<BR>—2 Waylaying (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ति|आसक्तिः
आसक्तिः + .{@-क्ति@} <i>ind.</i> Ved. Purposely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्ग|आसंग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आसङ्ग <i>a.</i> Uninterrupted, perpetual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गः|आसङ्ग|आसंग|आसङ्गं
आसङ्ग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 Attachment, devotion (to any object) (to enjoy or protect it); सुख˚<BR> लुब्धः K. 173; U. 3; चेतः स्वर्गतरङ्गिणीतटभुवामासङ्ग-मङ्गीकुरु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">Page0372-1</a>]<BR> Bh. 3. 60.<BR>—2 Intentness, close application.<BR>—3 Contact, adherence, clinging; (पङ्कजम्) सशैवलासङ्गमपि प्रकाशते<BR> Ku. 5. 9, 3. 46; व्रततिवलयासङ्गसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33; Mu. 1. 14;<BR> अनासङ्गः absence of consolation; Māl. 2.<BR>—4 Association, connection, union; त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गम् Bg. 4. 20;<BR> so कान्तासङ्ग &c.<BR>—5 Fixing, fastening to.<BR>—6 Pride about the authorship of a thing (कर्तृत्वाभिमान),<BR>—7 That which is fastened; cf. उत्तरासङ्ग.<BR>—8 Waylaying (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गम्
आसङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गम्@} A kind of fragrant earth (सौराष्ट्रमृत्तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गम्
आसङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गम्@} <i>ind.</i> Without interruption, eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0371-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिनी|आसंगिनी
आसङ्गिनी A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिमः|आसङ्गिम|आसंगिमः
आसङ्गिमः [आसङ्गे भवः डिमच्] (In surgery) A kind of bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसञ्जनम्
आसञ्जनम्<BR>—1 Fastening to, fixing, putting on the body (as dress, armour &c.).<BR>—2 Getting entangled, clinging; व्रततिवलयासञ्जनात् Ś. 1. 33 v. l.<BR>—3 Attachment, devotion.<BR>—4 Contact, proximity.<BR>—5 A handle, hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसद्
आसद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sit down or near (with acc. or loc.).<BR>—2 To watch or lie in, wait for य आसीदन्ति दम्पती Rv. 10. 85. 32.<BR>—3 To approach, reach, to go to or towards (a place &c.); हिमालयस्यालयमाससाद<BR> Ku. 7. 69; Bk. 7. 31; Śi. 2. 2; आसनम् R. 6. 4, 53, 11. 23.<BR>—4 To meet with, find, form; सख्यम् R. 5. 60, 14. 25; अपायम् Bk. 3. 26<BR> suffering; केचिद् वेपथुमासेदुः 4. 43.<BR>—5 To encounter, attack.<BR>—6 To commence, undertake.<BR>—7 To place.<BR> €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To meet with, find; मृत्युभयमासादितः Bhāg.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To get, obtain; अमरगणनालेख्यमासाद्य R. 8. 95; Ms. 4. 227;<BR> धनम्, सुखम् &c.<BR>—2 To approach, go to, reach; नकः स्वस्थानमासाद्य गजेन्द्रमपि कर्षति;<BR> ते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेन्द्रलोकम् Bg. 9. 20; Me. 36; Bk. 8. 37.<BR>—3 To overtake, come up with; अनेन रथवेगेन पूर्वप्रस्थितं वैनतेयमप्यासादयेयम्<BR> V. 1; Ve. 3. 9.<BR>—4 To encounter, attack; आसादितौ कथं ब्रूतं न गजैः कूलमुद्रुजैः Bk. 6. 95.<BR>—5 To effect, occasion, accomplish.<BR>—6 To make one sit down (Ved.).<BR>—7 To put on, wear; आसाद्य कवचं दिव्यं सहस्रार्कसमद्युति; Rām. 7. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्तिः|आसत्ति
आसत्तिः <i>f.</i> [आ-सद्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Meeting, junction.<BR>—2 Intimate union, nearness, close contact; किमपि किमपि मन्दं मन्दमासत्तियोगात् U. 1. 27.<BR>—3 Gain, profit, acquirement.<BR>—4 (In Logic) Proximity, the absence of interruption in the apprehension<BR> of what is said; relation between two or more proximate terms and the<BR> sense conveyed by them; कारणं सन्निधानं तु पदस्यासत्तिरुच्यते<BR> Bhāṣā P. 83; वाक्यं स्याद् योग्यताकाङ्क्षासत्तियुक्तः पदोच्चयः S. D. 2.<BR>—5 Embarrassment, perplexity; न च ते क्वचिदासत्तिर्बुद्धेः प्रादुर्भविष्यति Mb. 12. 52. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसदनम्
आसदनम्<BR>—1 Gain, profit.<BR>—2 Contact, union.<BR>—3 Nearness, proximity.<BR>—4 The act of sitting down.<BR>—5 A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आसन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drawn near, approached, near (in time, place or number); आसन्नविंशाः<BR> nearly or about 20; at hand, close by आसन्नमेव नृपतिर्भजते मनुष्यम्<BR> Pt.; impending, imminent; पूर्वमासन्नशृङ्गा वै गाव इत्यनुशुश्रुम<BR> Mb. 13. 81. 13; आसन्नपतने कूले Ś. B.; ˚मरण ˚काल q. v.<BR>—2 Adjacent, adjoining.<BR>—3 Well-placed.<BR>—4 about to die.<BR>—5 Obtained, got; बाह्वोरासन्नामतिमात्रं ननन्द Rām. 5. 63. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नः|आसन्न
आसन्न + .{@-न्नः@} The setting sun.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आसन्नकालः, आसन्नचर, आसन्नपरिचारकः, आसन्नपरिचारिका, आसन्नप्रसव, आसन्नमृत्यु, आसन्नशरीरपात<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नकालः|आसन्नकाल
आसन्न + -कालः<BR>—1 the hour of death.<BR>—2 one whose death is near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नचर
आसन्न + -चर <i>a.</i> moving round about in the proximity; Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नपरिचारकः
आसन्न + -परिचारकः, -परिचारिका personal attendant, body-guard; U. 1; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नपरिचारिका
आसन्न + -परिचारकः, -परिचारिका personal attendant, body-guard; U. 1; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नप्रसव
आसन्न + -प्रसव <i>a.</i> about to be confined or delivered; about to bring<BR> forth or lay eggs (as a hen &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नमृत्यु
आसन्न + -मृत्यु, -शरीरपात <i>a.</i> one whose death has drawn near; आसीनमासन्नशरीरपातस्त्रियम्बकं<BR> संयमिनं ददर्श Ku. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नशरीरपात
आसन्न + -मृत्यु, -शरीरपात <i>a.</i> one whose death has drawn near; आसीनमासन्नशरीरपातस्त्रियम्बकं<BR> संयमिनं ददर्श Ku. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादः|आसाद
आसादः Ved. Cushion. सामासाद उद्गीथे उपश्रयः Av. 15. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादनम्
आसादनम्<BR>—1 Putting or laying down.<BR>—2 Attacking.<BR>—3 Overtaking, meeting with, going towards.<BR>—4 Obtaining, attaining, accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादयितव्य
आसादयितव्य, आसाद्य <i>pot. p.</i> Attainable, to be attained &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
आसादयितव्य, आसाद्य <i>pot. p.</i> Attainable, to be attained &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादित|आसादितः
आसादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obtained, got; क्वचिदासादितमीक्षितं श्रुतं वा Udb.<BR>—2 Reached, gone to.<BR>—3 Spread, extended.<BR>—4 Effected, completed.<BR>—5 Met with, attacked, overtaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्
आसन् <i>n.</i> Mouth; (a word optionally substituted for आस्य in<BR> all cases after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्वत्|आसन्वन्त्
आसन्वत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Having a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्य
आसन्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Being in the mouth. Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्दः|आसन्द|आसंदः
आसन्दः [आसीदत्यस्मिन् प्रलयकाले; निपातः] Viṣṇu or Vāsudeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्दी
आसन्दः + .{@-न्दी@} [आसद्यतेऽस्याम्]<BR>—1 A small couch or oblong chair; an arm-chair; K. 94; इयं वा आसन्दी<BR> अस्यां हीदं सर्वमासन्नम् Śat. Br. स आगच्छति विचक्षणामासन्दीम्;<BR> Kauṣ. Up. 1-5.<BR>—2 A raised seat in a hall or assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्दिका
आसन्दिका [स्वल्पार्थे कन्] A small chair; K. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसमुद्रान्तम्
आसमुद्रान्तम् <i>ind.</i> As far as the shore of the ocean (including it); R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव see under आसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसा
आसा Ved. Proximity, nearness; आसया near, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाधनम्
आसाधनम् Accomplishment, attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसारः|आसार
आसारः [आ-सृ-घञ्]<BR>—1 A hard or sharp-driving shower (of anything); आसारसिक्तक्षितिबाष्पयोगात्<BR> R. 13. 29; Me. 17; पुष्पासारैः 43; so तुहिन˚, रुधिर˚ &c.; बाष्पासारा<BR> M. 3. 20 flooded or suffused with tears; धारासारैर्वृष्टिर्बभूव H. 3<BR> it rained in torrents.<BR>—2 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>—3 Attack, incursion.<BR>—4 The army of an ally or king (whose dominions are separated by other intervening<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">Page0373-1</a>]<BR> states); पार्ष्णिग्राहासरौ अन्तःकोपम् आटविकं वा समुत्थापयितुकामः Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR>—5 Provision, food; अज्ञानविविधासारतोयशस्यो व्रजेत्तु यः Pt. 3. 41, 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिकः|आसिक
आसिकः [असिः प्रहरणमस्य ठक्] A swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिका
आसिका [पर्यायेण आसनम्, आस्-ण्वुल्] Turn or order of sitting, sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिधारम्
आसिधारम् [असिधारा इव अस्त्यत्र अण्] N. of a particular vow; अभ्यस्यतीव<BR> व्रतमासिधारम् R. 13. 67; for explanation see असिधारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
आसिच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To pour in or on, wet, water, sprinkle.<BR>—2 To fill with; तप्तमासेचयेत्तैलं वक्त्रे श्रोते च पार्थिवः Ms. 8. 272.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To have anything poured in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
आसिच् <i>f.</i> An oblation which is poured out; पूर्णां विवष्ट्यासिचम्<BR> Rv. 7. 16. 11 a dish, vessel (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक्त
आसिक्त <i>a.</i> Poured in or on; sprinkled. Kaṭh. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेकः|आसेक
आसेकः Wetting, watering, pouring in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक्यः|आसेक्य
आसेक्यः A kind of eunuch or neuter man; पित्रोस्तु तुल्यवीर्यत्वादासेक्यः<BR> पुरुषो भवेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आसेचन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Charming, beloved; so आसेचनक. नयनयुगासेचनकं<BR> मानसवृत्त्यापि दुष्प्रापम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनम्
आसेचन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Pouring into, wetting, sprinkling.<BR>—2 A vessel for fluids (Ved.); ˚वत् hollow, concave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनी
आसेचन + .{@-नी@} A small vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनकः|आसेचनक
आसेचनकः Soma Juice or butter poured out for the gods; कथं<BR> त्वयाऽऽसेचनकाङ्गि लुप्यते त्रपा न संप्रत्यपि दृष्टपारया Rām. Ch. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिध्
आसिध् €1 P. To arrest, keep in custody (only in <i>p. p.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेद्धृ
आसेद्धृ <i>m.</i> One who arrests another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधः|आसेध
आसेधः Arrest, custody, legal restraint, it is of four kinds:− स्थानासेधः<BR> कालकृतः प्रवासात् कर्मणस्तथा Nārada; <i>i. e.</i><BR>——(<i>a</i>) confinement to a place,<BR>——(<i>b</i>) limitation of time,<BR>——(<i>c</i>) prohibition against departure, and<BR>——(<i>d</i>) restriction from doing anything. आसेधकाल आसिद्ध आसेधं यो<BR> निवर्तते Śukra. 4. 616.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधक
आसेधक <i>a.</i> Restraining, confining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसु
आसु €5 U.<BR>—1 To press out Soma juice, distil (mostly Ved.).<BR>—2 (P.) To excite, enliven (Ved.); Ch. Up. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवः|आसव
आसवः [आ सु-अण्]<BR>—1 Distillation.<BR>—2 Decoction.<BR>—3 Any spirituous liquor (distilled from sugar, molasses &c.); अनासवाख्यं<BR> करणं मदस्य Ku. 1. 31; कुमारी˚, द्राक्षा˚ &c.; यच्च पक्वौषधाम्बुभ्यां<BR> सिद्धं मद्यं स आसवः Bhāva P. Mādhava, however, seems to differ<BR> and says, शीधुरिक्षुरसैः पक्वैरपक्वैरासवो भवेत् । मैरेयं धातकीपुष्पैर्गुडधानाम्लसंहितम् ॥;<BR> आसवरागताम्रम् Ki. 16. 46.<BR>—5 A vessel for liquor.<BR>—6 Exciting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आसवद्रुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवद्रुः|आसवद्रु
आसवः + -द्रुः [आसवस्य कारणं द्रुः शाक˚ त˚] N. of the Palmyra<BR> tree (the juice of which, on fermenting, forms a spirituous liquor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसावः|आसाव
आसावः A presser, or one who extracts Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुति|आसुतिः
आसुति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Distilling, distillation.<BR>—2 Decoction.<BR>—3 A drought so prepared.<BR>—4 Birth, production (प्रसव).<BR>—5 Exciting, enlivening (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुतीवलः|आसुतीवल
आसुतीवलः [आसुतिरस्त्यस्य वलच् दीर्घः P. V. 2. 112]<BR>—1 A sacrificing priest (who extracts Soma juice).<BR>—2 A sacrificer at the full and change of the moon.<BR>—3 A distiller.<BR>—4 A guardian of girls (कन्यापालक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [असुरस्येदम् अण् opp. दैव]<BR>—1 Belonging to <i>Asuras</i>.<BR>—2 Belonging to evil spirits; आसुरी माया, आसुरी रात्रिः &c.<BR>—3 Infernal, demoniacal; आसुरं भावमाश्रितः Bg. 7. 15 (for a full<BR> exposition of what constitutes आसुर conduct, see Bg. 16. 7-24).<BR>—4 Not performing sacrifices.<BR>—5 Divine, spiritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरः|आसुर|आसुरं
आसुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A demon [स्वार्थे अण्].<BR>—2 One of the eight forms of marriage, in which the bridegroom purchases<BR> the bride from her father or other paternal kinsmen; (see उद्वाह);<BR> आसुरो द्रविणादानात् Y. 1. 61; Ms. 3. 31.<BR>—3 (pl.) The stars of the southern hemisphere.<BR>—4 A prince of the warrior-tribe Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरी
आसुर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 Surgery, curing by cutting by instruments.<BR>—2 A female demon, demoness; संभ्रमादासुरीभिः Ve. 1. 3.<BR>—3 N. of a plant Sinapis Ramosa Roxb. (Mar. मोहरी; राई)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरम्
आसुर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Blood.<BR>—2 Black salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरिः|आसुरि
आसुरिः A pupil of Kapila. मुनिरासुरयेऽनुकम्पया प्रददौ Sāṅ. K. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरिकल्पः
आसुरिः + .{@-कल्पः@} N. of a Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरीय
आसुरीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to or coming from Āsuri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरायणः|आसुरायण
आसुरायणः<BR>—1 A descendant of Āsuri; Bṛ. Up. 2. 6. 3.<BR>—2 N. of a Vedic school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसूत्रित
आसूत्रित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Forming or wearing a garland.<BR>—2 Interwoven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेव्
आसेव् Ā.<BR>—1 To carry out, practise, perform zealously; धर्मम्, व्रतम् &c.<BR>—2 To indulge in, enjoy; अग्रवातमासेवमाना M. 1; V. 4; Ku. 1. 15.<BR>—3 To accomplish, attend to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवा
आसेवा, -वनम्<BR>—1 Zealous practice, assiduous performance of any action.<BR>—2 Frequency, repetition; P. VIII. 3. 102; आसेवनं पौनःपुन्यम् Sk.<BR>—3 Intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवनम्
आसेवा, -वनम्<BR>—1 Zealous practice, assiduous performance of any action.<BR>—2 Frequency, repetition; P. VIII. 3. 102; आसेवनं पौनःपुन्यम् Sk.<BR>—3 Intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवित
आसेवित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Performed, done.<BR>—2 Repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवितम्
आसेवित + .{@-तम्@} Performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेविन्
आसेविन् <i>a.</i> Performing assiduously, indulging in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्द्|आस्कंद्
आस्कन्द् €1 P.<BR>—1 To invade, attack; कथमिदानीमुन्मादोपरागो माधवेन्दुमास्कन्दति<BR> Māl. 9; आस्कन्दल्लक्ष्मणं बाणैः Bk. 17. 82.<BR>—2 To step over, tread; चयमास्कन्दति भस्मनां जनः Ki. 2. 20.<BR>—3 To depend or hang on (as the Vedāṅgas on the Vedas).<BR>—4 To jump, leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दः|आस्कन्द|आस्कंदः
आस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 An attack, assault; assailing; outraging; परवनिता ˚प्रगल्भस्य<BR> Ve. 2. विविधास्कन्दनाकाङ्क्षी …<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">Page0374-1</a>]<BR> Śiva B. 31. 68<BR>—2 Ascending, mounting; treading, stepping over; चरणास्कन्दननामिताचलेन्द्रः Ki. 13. 18.<BR>—3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>—4 The walk of a horse.<BR>—5 An assailant<BR>—6 Battle, war.<BR>—7 Drying.<BR>—8 Effacing, destroying. आस्कन्दनं तिरस्कारे रणे संशोषणेऽपि च Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दनम्
आस्कन्दः, -न्दनम्<BR>—1 An attack, assault; assailing; outraging; परवनिता ˚प्रगल्भस्य<BR> Ve. 2. विविधास्कन्दनाकाङ्क्षी …<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">Page0374-1</a>]<BR> Śiva B. 31. 68<BR>—2 Ascending, mounting; treading, stepping over; चरणास्कन्दननामिताचलेन्द्रः Ki. 13. 18.<BR>—3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>—4 The walk of a horse.<BR>—5 An assailant<BR>—6 Battle, war.<BR>—7 Drying.<BR>—8 Effacing, destroying. आस्कन्दनं तिरस्कारे रणे संशोषणेऽपि च Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दितम्
आस्कन्दितम्, -तकम्<BR> The walk of a horse, galloping at full speed. आस्कन्दिता<BR> च सा ज्ञेया गतिविद्भिस्तु वाजिनाम् Śukra. 4. 982.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दितकम्
आस्कन्दितम्, -तकम्<BR> The walk of a horse, galloping at full speed. आस्कन्दिता<BR> च सा ज्ञेया गतिविद्भिस्तु वाजिनाम् Śukra. 4. 982.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दिन्|आस्कंदिन्
आस्कन्दिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Jumping upon, assailing, attacking; न हि सिंहो गजास्कन्दी भयाद्गिरिगुहाशयः R. 17. 52.<BR>—2 Causing to flow.<BR>—3 Granting.<BR>—4 Spending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्क्र
आस्क्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attacking or assailing enemies, approaching.<BR>—2 Joined or united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तावः|आस्ताव
आस्तावः [आ-स्तु-घञ्; P. III. 3. 120]<BR>—1 The place of reciting hymns in a sacrifice; तत्रोद्गातॄनास्तावे स्तोष्यमाणानुपोपविवेश<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 10. 8.<BR>—2 Praise, hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अस्ति परलोकः इति मतिर्यस्य, ठक्]<BR>—1 One who believes in God and another world; यन्नास्त्येव तदस्ति वस्त्विति<BR> मृषा जल्पद्भिरेवास्तिकैः Prab. 2<BR>—2 A believer in sacred tradition.<BR>—3 Pious, faithful, believing; आस्तिकः श्रद्दधानश्च Y. 1. 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकः|आस्तिक
आस्तिक + .{@-कः@} or {@आस्तीकः@} N. of a Muni. cf. अगस्त्यो माधवश्चैव<BR> मुचकुन्दो महामुनिः । कपिलो मुनिरास्तीकः पञ्चैते सुखशायिनः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकः|आस्तीक
आस्तिक + .{@-कः@} or {@आस्तीकः@} N. of a Muni. cf. अगस्त्यो माधवश्चैव<BR> मुचकुन्दो महामुनिः । कपिलो मुनिरास्तीकः पञ्चैते सुखशायिनः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकता
आस्तिकता, -त्व, आस्तिक्यम्<BR>—1 Belief in God and another world; आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मम् Ki. 18. 43.<BR>—2 Piety, faith, belief; ज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यम् Bg. 18. 42; आस्तिक्यं<BR> श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकत्व|आस्तिकत्वं
आस्तिकता, -त्व, आस्तिक्यम्<BR>—1 Belief in God and another world; आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मम् Ki. 18. 43.<BR>—2 Piety, faith, belief; ज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यम् Bg. 18. 42; आस्तिक्यं<BR> श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक्यम्
आस्तिकता, -त्व, आस्तिक्यम्<BR>—1 Belief in God and another world; आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मम् Ki. 18. 43.<BR>—2 Piety, faith, belief; ज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यम् Bg. 18. 42; आस्तिक्यं<BR> श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक|आस्तीकः
आस्तीक <i>a.</i> Relating to, or treating of, the sage आस्तीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकः|आस्तीक
आस्तीक + .{@-कः@} N. of an old saint, son of Jaratkāru; (at whose intercession<BR> King Janamejaya spared the Nāga Takṣaka from the destruction to which<BR> he had doomed the serpent race). Mb. gives the following etymology of<BR> the name; नाम चास्याभवत्ख्यातं लोकेष्वास्तीक इत्युत । अस्तीत्युक्त्वा गतो<BR> यस्मात्पिता गर्भस्थमेव तम् ॥ cf. सर्पापसर्प भद्रं ते गच्छ सर्प<BR> वनान्तरम् । जनमेजयस्य यज्ञान्ते आस्तीकवचनं स्मर ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकम्
आस्तीक + .{@-कम्@} A section (पर्व) of the first book of the Mahābhārata.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्तीकार्थदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकार्थदः|आस्तीकार्थद
आस्तीक + -अर्थदः N. of Janamejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृ
आस्तृ, -स्तॄ €5. €9 U.<BR> To spread over, strew, cover, scatter over, bestrew,<BR> deck; दर्भानास्तीर्य, वसनमास्तीर्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तॄ
आस्तृ, -स्तॄ €5. €9 U.<BR> To spread over, strew, cover, scatter over, bestrew,<BR> deck; दर्भानास्तीर्य, वसनमास्तीर्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरः|आस्तर
आस्तरः [आ-स्तृ-अप्]<BR>—1 A covering, coverlet. दण्डिनीमजिनास्तराम् Bk. 6. 60.<BR>—2 A carpet, bed, mat; वासो वल्कलमास्तरः किसलयानि Śānti. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Spreading (clothes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरकः|आस्तरक
आस्तरकः One who spreads the bed; Kau. A. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आस्तरण <i>a.</i> —1 Spreading, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरणम्
आस्तरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Spreading, strewing.<BR>—2 A bed, layer; कुसुम˚ a bed of flowers; क्रुसुमास्तरणे सहायतां<BR> बहुशः सौम्य गतस्त्वमावयोः Ku. 4. 35; सकुसुम˚ strewn with flowers<BR> Ś. 3; तमालपत्रास्तरणासु रन्तुम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">Page0374-2</a>]<BR> R. 6. 64.<BR>—3 A cushion, quilt, bed clothes; गत˚ without the bed clothes.<BR>—4 A rug, carpet.<BR>—5 An elephantʼs housings, painted cloth (thrown on his back).<BR>—6 A layer of Kuśa grass spread out at a sacrifice. वेद आस्तरणं<BR> ब्रह्मोपबर्हणम् Av. 15. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरणिक
आस्तरणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [आस्तरणं प्रयोजनमस्य ठक्]<BR>—1 For spreading (as clothes &c.).<BR>—2 Resting on a carpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तारः|आस्तार
आस्तारः [आ-स्तॄ-घञ्] Spreading, strewing, scattering.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्तारपङ्क्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तारपङ्क्तिः|आस्तारपङ्क्ति
आस्तारः + -पङ्क्तिः N. of a metre, see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीर्ण|आस्तीर्ण्ण
आस्तीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spread, scattered.<BR>—2 Covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तारकः|आस्तारक
आस्तारकः A fire-receptacle, grate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्त्र
आस्त्र, -आस्त्रिक <i>a.</i><BR> [अस्त्रस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to a missile; चतुर्थमास्त्रिकबलम्<BR> Śukra. 4. 866.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्त्रिक
आस्त्र, -आस्त्रिक <i>a.</i><BR> [अस्त्रस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to a missile; चतुर्थमास्त्रिकबलम्<BR> Śukra. 4. 866.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था €1 P.<BR>—1 To stand or remain on or by, to occupy. Śvet. Up. 2. 5.<BR>—2 To ascend, mount; रथम्, स्यन्दनम् &c.<BR>—3 To use, have recourse to, resort to, practise, take, assume, follow;<BR> यथा यथा हि सद्वृत्तमातिष्ठन्त्यनसूयकाः Ms. 10. 128, 2. 133, 10. 101;<BR> समाधिमास्थाय Ku. 5. 2 practising concentration of mind; स्वरूपम्<BR> Ku. 5. 84 assuming his own form; तनुम् Mu. 7. 19; R. 6. 72; कूर्मसंकोचमास्थाय<BR> प्रहारानपि मर्षयेत् Pt. 3. 21 contracting himself like a tortoise;<BR> पदमातस्थुषा Ku. 6. 72 taking a place among; व्रतम् Ve. 3. 21;<BR> so स्त्रीरूपम् Pt. 3. 31; आस्थितविषादधियः Ki. 6. 29 gloomy; तं<BR> तं नियममास्थाय Bg. 7. 20, 8. 12; K. 165; आस्थितविष्टरः R. 15. 79;<BR> सुहृदास्थितायां सभायाम् Ku. 7. 29; विषमग्निं जलं रज्जुमास्थास्ये<BR> तव कारणात् Mb. use; चिन्तामौनमिवास्थिता V. 4. 67 lost in moody abstraction.<BR>—4 To do, perform, carry out.<BR>—5 To recognise, acknowledge, own.<BR>—6 To exhibit, aim at.<BR>—7 To undertake, promise, agree.<BR>—8 To behave.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to stand.<BR>—2 To hold fast, cling to.<BR>—3 To collect, obtain.<BR>—4 To place in, infix.<BR>—5 To show, represent, introduce; प्रविश्य स्थापकस्तद्वत्काव्यमास्थापयेत्ततः<BR> S. D. 283; Mv. 1. 13.<BR>—6 To step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था [आस्था-अङ्]<BR>—1 Regard, care, respect, consideration, care for (with loc.); न संभ्रमो<BR> न भीः काचिदास्था वा समजायत Mb. 12. 281. 12; मर्त्येष्वास्थापराङ्मुखः<BR> R. 10. 43; मय्यप्यास्था न ते चेत् Bh. 3. 30, 2. 98; see अनास्था also.<BR>—2 Assent, promise.<BR>—3 Prop, support, stay.<BR>—4 Hope, confidence; जयलक्ष्म्यां बबन्धास्थाम् Rāj. T. 5. 245.<BR>—5 An effort.<BR>—6 State, condition.<BR>—7 An assembly.<BR>—8 A place or means of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थातृ
आस्थातृ <i>a.</i> Standing, mounting; आस्थाता ते जयतु जत्वानि Rv. 6. 47. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानम्
आस्थानम्<BR>—1 A place, site.<BR>—2 Ground, base.<BR>—3 An assembly; आस्थानाध्यासनाश्रितः Bhāg. 6. 7. 5.<BR>—4 Care, regard; see आस्था.<BR>—5 A hall of audience; K. 8, 14.<BR>—6 Recreation ground (विश्रामस्थानम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानी
आस्थानम् + .{@-नी@} An assembly-room. आस्थानीं समये समं नृपजनः सायंतने<BR> संपतन् Ratnamālā निजामशाहमास्थानीमेत्य सिंहासने स्थितम् Śiva B. 3. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्थानगृहम्, आस्थाननिकेतनम्, आस्थानमण्डपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0374-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

