आस्थायिका An audience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थित
आस्थित <i>p. p.</i> (Used actively)<BR>—1 Dwelt, abiding; यत्नम् Pt. 1. 220 using efforts carefully; उपायमास्थितस्यापि<BR> Śi. 2. 80, 9. 84; so नियमम्, ध्यानम्, धर्मम् &c.<BR>—2 Having recourse to, resorting to, using, practising, betaking oneself<BR> to; इत्येवं सा समाभाष्य भूयः संदेष्टुमास्थिता Rām. 5. 67. 40. सलिलाशयम् Pt. 2.<BR>—3 Having obtained or got, having reached to; ऐश्वर्यम्, कामवशम्<BR> &c. आस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम् Bg. 7. 18.<BR>—4 Occupied; enclosed (as a hunting ground); श्वगणिवागुरिकैः प्रथमास्थितम्<BR> R. 9. 53; दानवास्थितः शैलः Rām.<BR>—5 Engrossed, engaged.<BR>—6 Covered (व्याप्त); Ki. 9. 9; spread, overspread.<BR>—7 Got, obtained; कर्मणैवहि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः Bg. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थितिः|आस्थिति
आस्थितिः Condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थेय
आस्थेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be approached or seized, to be applied.<BR>—2 To be regarded or acknowledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नानम्
आस्नानम्<BR>—1 Purity.<BR>—2 Water for washing, bath; आस्नाने तां नि दध्मसि Av. 14. 2. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नेय
आस्नेय <i>a.</i> Bloody (fr. असन्); being in the mouth (fr. आसन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पदम्
आस्पदम् [आ-पद्-घ सुट् च]<BR>—1 A place, site, seat, room; तस्यास्पदं श्रीर्युवराजसंज्ञितम् R. 3. 36;<BR> ध्यानास्पदं भूतपतेर्विवेश Ku. 3. 43, 5. 10, 48, 69; कथं<BR> तादृशानां गिरि वैतथ्यमास्पदं कुर्यात् K. 174; राजन्यास्पदमलभत<BR> Dk. 160 obtained a hold on the king.<BR>—2 (Fig.) An abode, subject, receptacle; निधनता सर्वापदामास्पदम्<BR> Mk. 1. 14; करिण्यः कारुण्यास्पदम् Bv. 1. 2. आस्पदं त्वमसि सर्वसंपदाम्<BR> Ki. 13. 39; so दोष˚, उपहास˚ &c.<BR>—3 Rank, position, station; काव्यार्थभावनेनायमपि सभ्यपदास्पदम् S. D.<BR>—4 Dignity, authority, office; लब्धास्पदोऽस्मीति विवादभीरोः M. 1. 17.<BR>—5 Business, affair.<BR>—6 Prop, support.<BR>—7 The tenth place from the लग्न (in Astrol.) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धा
आस्पर्धा Emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धिन्
आस्पर्धिन् <i>a.</i> Emulous, striving after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पृश्य
आस्पृश्य <i>ind.</i> Having touched softly; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फल्
आस्फल्, -स्फुल् €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to flap, rock or shake; to strike or press against; आस्फालितं<BR> यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैः R. 16. 13; पयोराशेरोघः प्रलयपवनास्फालित इव<BR> U. 5. 9 lashed, stirred; Nāg. 1; शिलायामास्फालितः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To twang; धनुरास्फालयन् U. 4.<BR>—3 To sound, play upon (as a lute), strike; वीणामास्फालयन्तीम् K. 131; Śi. 1. 9.<BR>—4 To rend assunder, tear in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुल्
आस्फल्, -स्फुल् €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to flap, rock or shake; to strike or press against; आस्फालितं<BR> यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैः R. 16. 13; पयोराशेरोघः प्रलयपवनास्फालित इव<BR> U. 5. 9 lashed, stirred; Nāg. 1; शिलायामास्फालितः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To twang; धनुरास्फालयन् U. 4.<BR>—3 To sound, play upon (as a lute), strike; वीणामास्फालयन्तीम् K. 131; Śi. 1. 9.<BR>—4 To rend assunder, tear in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालः|आस्फाल
आस्फालः<BR>—1 Striking, rubbing, causing to move gently.<BR>—2 Flapping.<BR>—3 Particularly, the flapping motion of an elephantʼs ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालनम्
आस्फालनम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, striking or pressing against, stirring (as water &c.); flapping;<BR> अनवरतधनुर्ज्यास्फालनक्रूर पूर्वम् Ś. 2. 4; आसां जलास्फालनतत्पराणाम्<BR> R. 16. 62, 3. 55, 6. 73; Amaru. 54; कुचतट˚ K. 6, 14, 57; ऐरावत˚<BR> कर्कशेन हस्तेन Ku. 3. 22 striking against.<BR>—2 Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुजित्
आस्फुजित् <i>m.</i> N. of the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुट्
आस्फुट् €1 P. To agitate, shake; धृष्टमास्फोटयामास लङ्कां शब्देन<BR> पूरयन् Rām. 5. 43. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटः|आस्फोट
आस्फोटः<BR>—1 The Arka plant.<BR>—2 The sound made by striking on the arms (Mar. छड्डू ठोकर्णे); कर˚<BR> मिश्रेण K. 28.<BR>—3 Trembling, quivering.<BR>—4 Striking or rubbing against, blow; पुच्छ˚ Mv. 5. 63; लाङ्गूलास्फोटशब्दाच्च<BR> चलितः स महागिरिः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटा
आस्फोटः + .{@-टा@} The नवमल्लिका plant, wild variety of Jasmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटक|आस्फोटकः
आस्फोटक Making a sound by striking on the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटकः|आस्फोटक
आस्फोटक + .{@-कः@} = पर्वतजपीलुभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटनम्
आस्फोटनम्<BR>—1 Flapping, moving to and fro.<BR>—2 Trembling, shaking.<BR>—3 Blowing, expanding.<BR>—4 Contracting, closing.<BR>—5 Slapping or clapping the arms, or the sound produced by it.<BR>—6 Disclosing, manifesting.<BR>—7 Winnowing, thrashing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटनी
आस्फोटनम् + .{@-नी@} A gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटितम्
आस्फोटितम्<BR>—1 Clapping; आस्फोटितनिनादांश्च Rām. 5. 43. 12.<BR>—2 Striking on the arms; तस्यास्फोटितशब्देन महता श्रोत्रघातिना । पेतुर्विहंगमास्तत्र<BR> चैत्यपालाश्च मोहिताः Rām. 5. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोतः|आस्फोत
आस्फोतः, -तकः<BR> [आ-स्फुट् अच् पृषो˚ टस्य तत्वम्] N. of several trees;<BR> अर्क, कोविदार, भूपलाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोतकः|आस्फोतक
आस्फोतः, -तकः<BR> [आ-स्फुट् अच् पृषो˚ टस्य तत्वम्] N. of several trees;<BR> अर्क, कोविदार, भूपलाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोता
आस्फोतः, -तकः + .{@-ता, -तका@} N. of several plants; मल्लिका, अपराजिता, सारिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोतका
आस्फोतः, -तकः + .{@-ता, -तका@} N. of several plants; मल्लिका, अपराजिता, सारिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माक
आस्माक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), आस्माकीन <i>a.</i><BR> [अस्मद्-अण्खञ् अस्माकादेशः ।]<BR> Our, ours; आस्माकदन्तिसान्निध्यात् Śi. 2. 63, 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माकी
आस्माक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), आस्माकीन <i>a.</i><BR> [अस्मद्-अण्खञ् अस्माकादेशः ।]<BR> Our, ours; आस्माकदन्तिसान्निध्यात् Śi. 2. 63, 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माकीन
आस्माक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), आस्माकीन <i>a.</i><BR> [अस्मद्-अण्खञ् अस्माकादेशः ।]<BR> Our, ours; आस्माकदन्तिसान्निध्यात् Śi. 2. 63, 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the mouth or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यम्
आस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} [अस्यते ग्रासोऽत्र, अस्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 The mouth, jaws; आस्यकुहरे, विवृतास्यः.<BR>—2 Face; आस्यकमलम्.<BR>—3 A part of the mouth used in pronouncing letters; तुल्यास्यप्रयत्नं<BR> सवर्णम् P. I. 1. 9; आस्ये भवमास्यं ताल्वादिस्थानम् Sk; षडास्यानि<BR> Pt. 5. 55; (the six parts being the throat, head or brain, palate, tooth, lip, and nose.)<BR>—4 Mouth, opening; व्रणास्यम् अङ्कास्यम् &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्यासवः, आस्यपत्रम्, आस्यलाङ्गलः, आस्यलोमन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यासवः|आस्यासव
आस्य + -आसवः spittle, saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यपत्रम्
आस्य + -पत्रम् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलाङ्गलः|आस्यलाङ्गल|आस्यलांगल
आस्य + -लाङ्गलः<BR>—1 a dog.<BR>—2 a boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलोमन्
आस्य + -लोमन् <i>n.</i> beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यंधय
आस्यंधय <i>a.</i> [आस्यं धयति धे-ख मुम्] Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यन्दनम्
आस्यन्दनम् Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या See under आस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यूत
आस्यूत^1 <i>a.</i> Sewn together.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रम्
आस्रम् [अस्रमेव स्वार्थेऽण्] Blood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्रपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रपः|आस्रप
आस्रम् + -पः<BR>—1 ‘blood-drinker’, demon.<BR>—2 the 19th lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0375-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रवः|आस्रव
आस्रवः [आस्रू-अप्]<BR>—1 Pain, affliction, distress.<BR>—2 Flowing, running.<BR>—3 Discharge, emission.<BR>—4 Fault, transgressing.<BR>—5 The foam on boiling rice.<BR>—6 (With Jainas) The impulse called योग or attention which the soul<BR> participates in the movement of its various bodies; it is defined as the<BR> ‘action of the senses which impels the soul towards external objects’;<BR> it is good or evil according as it is directed towards good or evil objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राव|आस्रावः
आस्राव <i>a.</i> Flowing, running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रावः|आस्राव
आस्राव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A wound; कण्टको ह्यपि दुच्छिन्न आस्रावं जनयेच्चिरम् Mb. 1. 140. 9.<BR>—2 Flow, issue, discharge.<BR>—3 Spittle, saliva.<BR>—4 Pain, affliction.<BR>—5 A disease of the body; तदास्रावस्य भेषजं तदु रोगमनीनशत् Av. 2. 3. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आस्रावभेषजम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रावभेषजम्
आस्राव + -भेषजम् medicament, medicine; श्रेष्ठमास्रावभेषजम् Av. 6. 44. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राविन्
आस्राविन् <i>a.</i> Flowing, emitting fluid or humour; an epithet of the<BR> elephant when ichor is issuing from its temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रु
आस्रु <i>a.</i> Flowing or streaming in abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रुपयस्
आस्रु + .{@-पयस्@} <i>a.</i> One whose milk is streaming in abundance. (as a<BR> cow); अगाद्धुङ्कृतैरास्रुपया जवेन Bhāg. 10. 13. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वद्
आस्वद् €1 Ā. To taste. ━<i>Caus.</i> To taste, enjoy; संभोगं<BR> Me. 89; R. 3. 54; (fig.) to plunder, defraud; नास्वाद्यसे भुजङ्गैः K. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद|आस्वादः
आस्वाद <i>a.</i> Tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादः|आस्वाद
आस्वाद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Tasting, eating; चूताङ्कुरास्वादकषायकण्ठः Ku. 3. 32; काव्यामृतरसास्वादः<BR> H. 1. 132; मुखास्वादः Y. 3. 229 kissing.<BR>—2 Relish, flavour, taste; ज्ञातास्वादो विवृतजघनां को विहातुं समर्थः<BR> Me. 43; सुखास्वादपरः H. 4. 77; चित्रास्वादकथैर्भृत्यैः Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Enjoying, experiencing; ˚वत् <i>a.</i> delicious in flavour, palatable;<BR> आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानाम् R. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादक
आस्वादक <i>a.</i> Tasting, enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादनम्
आस्वादनम् Tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादित
आस्वादित <i>a.</i> Tasted. आस्वादितद्विरदशोणितशोणजिह्वः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद्य
आस्वाद्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be tasted, delicious, sweet, palatable. आस्वाद्यतोयाः<BR> प्रवहन्ति नद्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वनित
आस्वनित or आस्वान्त [आ-स्वन्-क्त] Sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वान्त
आस्वनित or आस्वान्त [आ-स्वन्-क्त] Sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 An interjection showing<BR>——(<i>a</i>) reproof;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) severity;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) command;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) casting, sending.<BR>—2 An irregular verbal form of the 3rd pers. sing. Perf.^1 of a defective<BR> verb meaning ‘to say’, or ‘to speak’ (supposed by Indian grammarians to<BR> be derived from ब्रू and by European scholars from अह्र; the only<BR> forms of the root existing in the language are:− आत्थ, आहथुः, आह,<BR> आहतुः, and आहुः).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहकः|आहक
आहकः [आ-हन्-ड-कन्]<BR>—1 A peculiar disease of the nose; तनुना रक्तशोथेन युक्तो नासापुटान्तरे ।<BR> गात्रशूलज्वरकरः श्लेष्मणा ह्याहको ज्वरः ॥.<BR>—2 A crab; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहंकार्यम्
आहंकार्यम् Conceitedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहन्
आहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike, hit, beat; कुट्टिममाजघान K. 10; परस्य शिर आहन्ति<BR> Sk.; Śi. 7. 17; दुर्जयान् करिणः … आहन्यात् Kām. 19. 60; said<BR> to be Ātm. when the object is some limb of oneʼs own body; आहते शिरः;<BR> but cf. आजघ्ने विषमविलोचनस्य वक्षः Ki. 17. 63; so आहध्वं मा<BR> रघूत्तमम्; Bk. 8. 15, 5. 102 (see Sk. on P. I. 3. 28 also).<BR>—2 To strike, ring, beat (as a bell, drum &c.) तुमुलकलनिनादं तूर्यमाजध्नुरन्ये<BR> Bk. 1. 27, 17. 7; Me. 68; R. 17. 11.<BR>—3 To kill, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत|आहतं|आहतः
आहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck, beaten (as a drum &c.); हृदये दिग्धशरैरिवाहतः Ku. 4. 25, 30;<BR> R. 4. 23, 12. 77.<BR>—2 Trodden; पादाहतं यदुत्थाय मूर्धानमधिरोहति Śi. 2. 46; गजदन्ताहता वृक्षाः Rām.<BR>—3 Injured, killed.<BR>—4 Dispelled, destroyed, removed.<BR>—5 Multiplied (in Math.) सूर्याब्धिसंख्यया द्वित्रिसागरैरयुताहतैः<BR> Sūrya S.; एकैकमब्देषु नवाहतेषु Bṛ. S. 8. 22.<BR>—5 Known, understood.<BR>—6 Rolled (as dice).<BR>—7 Uttered falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतः|आहत|आहतं
आहत + .{@-तः@} A drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतम्
आहत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A new cloth or garment.<BR>—2 An old garment.<BR>—3 A nonsensical or meaningless speech, an assertion of impossibility;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> एष वन्ध्यासुतो याति Subhāṣ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहतलक्षण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतलक्षण|आहतलक्षणः
आहत + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> = आहितलक्षण q. v. under आधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतिः|आहति
आहतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Killing.<BR>—2 A blow, hit, striking.<BR>—3 Coming (आगति).<BR>—4 Multiplication; अंशाहतिच्छेदवधेन भक्ता Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत्य
आहत्य <i>ind.</i> Having struck or beaten; striking, hitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत्यवचनम्
आहत्य + .{@-वचनम्, -वादः@} An explicit or energetic explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत्यवादः|आहत्यवाद
आहत्य + .{@-वचनम्, -वादः@} An explicit or energetic explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहननम्
आहननम्<BR>—1 Striking at, beating.<BR>—2 A stick. (for beating a drum). Av. 20. 133. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहननीय
आहननीय <i>a.</i> Making oneself known by beating a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनस्
आहनस् <i>a.</i> [आ-हन्-असुन्]<BR>—1 To be beaten or pressed out (as Soma).<BR>—2 Unchaste, wanton, profligate; य आहना दुहितुर्वक्षणासु Rv. 5. 42. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातः|आघात
आघातः [आ-हन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Striking, striking against; अभ्यस्यन्ति तटाघातम् Ku. 2. 50; U. 5. 9.<BR>—2 A blow, stroke; तीव्राघातप्रतिहततरुस्कन्धलग्नैकदन्तः Ś. 1. 32;<BR> कठिनकुचतट˚ Amaru. 55; पवन˚, पाद˚ &c.<BR>—3 A wound.<BR>—4 Killing; प्राणाघातान्निवृत्तिः Bh. 2. 26; Y. 3. 275.<BR>—5 One who beats or strikes.<BR>—6 A misfortune, distress.<BR>—7 Retention of urine (मूत्राघात).<BR>—8 A slaughter-house; आघातं नीयमानस्य वध्यस्येव पदे पदे H. 4. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातनम्
आघातनम्<BR>—1 Striking, killing.<BR>—2 A slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c. See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c. See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवन|आहवनं
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c. See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिकः|आहिक
आहिकः [अहिरिव, कन्, स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 The descending node (केतु).<BR>—2 An epithet of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्ड्|आहिंड्
आहिण्ड् €1 Ā. To roam about, wander; आहिण्ड्यते अटव्या अटवीम् Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्डिकः|आहिण्डिक|आहिंडिकः
आहिण्डिकः A man of mixed origin, the son of a Niṣāda father and<BR> Vaidehī mother; आहिण्डिको निषादेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">Page0377-1</a>]<BR> वैदेह्यामेव जायते Ms. 10. 37 (according to Kull., he was employed<BR> as a watchman on the outside of jails; and hence called आहिण्डिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0376-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितक
आहितक A hireling; Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितुण्डिकः|आहितुण्डिक|आहितुंडिकः
आहितुण्डिकः [अहितुण्डेन दीव्यति ठक्] A juggler, a snake-catcher,<BR> conjurer; अहंखल्वाहितुण्डिको जीर्णविषो नाम Mu. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहीरणिन्
आहीरणिन् <i>m.</i> A two-headed snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहु|आहुः
आहु €3 U. To sacrifice, offer an oblation, worship (as fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवः|आहव
आहवः A sacrifice; तत्र नाभवदसौ महाहवे Śi. 14. 44. (for<BR> other meanings see under आह्वे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनम्
आहवनम्<BR>—1 A sacrifice; द्रष्टुमाहवनमग्रजन्मनाम् Śi. 14. 38.<BR>—2 An oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीय|आहवनीयः
आहवनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be offered as an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयः|आहवनीय
आहवनीय + .{@-यः@} A consecrated fire taken from the house-holderʼs perpetual<BR> fire, one of the three fires (<i>i. e.</i> the eastern) burning at a sacrifice;<BR> गार्हपत्यादाहवनीयं ज्वलन्तमुद्धरेत् । पिता वा एषोऽग्नीनां यदक्षिणः<BR> पुत्रो गार्हपत्यः पौत्र आहवनीयः Āśval.; see also अग्नित्रेता<BR> under अग्नि. अथ हैनमाहवनीयोऽनुंशशास Ch. Up. 4. 13. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयक|आहवनीयकः
आहवनीयक <i>a.</i> Fit for a burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयकः|आहवनीयक
आहवनीयक + .{@-कः@} consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहावः|आहाव
आहावः [आ-हु-आधारे घञ्]<BR>—1 Fire; see under आह्वे also.<BR>—2 A pond, a lake (आहावस्तु निपानं स्यादुपकूपजलाशये). प्राविशन्नाहवप्रज्ञा<BR> आहावमुपलिप्सवः Bk. 7. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुत|आहुतं
आहुत <i>p. p.</i> Offered to the gods, sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतम्
आहुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 An offering made to men, hospitality.<BR>—2 The nourishment of all created beings (भूतयज्ञ or मनुष्ययज्ञ),<BR> regarded as one of the five principal sacrifices of the Hindus cf. पञ्चमहायज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतिः|आहुति
आहुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Offering an oblation to a deity, any solemn rite accompanied with oblations;<BR> होतुराहुतिसाधनम् R. 1. 82.<BR>—2 An oblation offered to a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतीकृ
आहुतीकृ, -भू<BR> To offer, to become an oblation; Ratn.; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतीभू
आहुतीकृ, -भू<BR> To offer, to become an oblation; Ratn.; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुकः|आहुक
आहुकः N. of a prince, grand-father of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुकाः
आहुकः + .{@-काः@} N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुल्यम्
आहुल्यम् N. of a leguminous shrub (तगर, तरवट &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृ
आहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring, fetch; यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम् R. 3. 6; पुष्पं<BR> फलं चार्तवमाहरन्त्यः 14. 77, 18. 8; प्रतिवाक्यम् to bring an<BR> answer; वार्ताम् bring news.<BR>—2 To bring near, give; चन्द्रगुप्ताय मेदिनीम् Kām. 1. 5; अयाचिताहृत Y. 1. 215.<BR>—3 To recover, bring back.<BR>—4 To obtain, get, receive; व्रह्मचार्याहरेद्भैक्षम् Ms. 2. 183, 6. 27, 7. 80, 8. 151.<BR> (v. l.) 11. 12; Y. 1. 97.<BR>—5 To have, assume; आजह्रतुस्तच्चरणौ … श्रियम् Ku. 3. 33.<BR>—6 To cause, produce, lead to; बलोपचयम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">Page0377-2</a>]<BR> K. 105; प्रीतिम्, क्रोधम् &c.; जनकानां कुले कीर्तिमाहरिष्यति मे सुता Rām.<BR>—7 To bring near (as wife), marry; अत आहर्तुमिच्छामि पार्वतीमात्मजन्मने Ku. 6. 28.<BR>—8 To wear, put on (as armour &c.); स वल्कवासांसि तवाधुनाहरन् Ki. 1. 35.<BR>—9 To offer in a sacrifice; to perform (as a sacrifice); स विश्वजितमाजह्रे<BR> R. 4. 86, 14. 87.<BR>—10 To take away, attract (as mind).<BR>—11 To separate, remove, draw off from.<BR>—12 To scare or frighten away, drive forth.<BR>—13 To use as food or drink, eat.<BR>—14 To speak, say, name, call.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To make one fetch or bring, cause to give or pay; शस्त्रेण वैश्यान्<BR> रक्षित्वा धर्म्यमाहारयेद् बलिम् Ms. 10. 119.<BR>—2 To eat.<BR>—3 To bring together, collect; Pt. 3. 151.<BR>—4 To cause, produce.<BR>—5 To exact.<BR>—6 To show, exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर|आहरः
आहर <i>a.</i> (at the end of comp.) Bringing, fetching, taking, seizing<BR> समित्कुशफलाहरैः R. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरः|आहर
आहर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Taking, seizing.<BR>—2 Accomplishing, performing.<BR>—3 Offering a sacrifice.<BR>—4 Drawing in breath, inhaling.<BR>—5 The air so inhaled.<BR>—6 Inspiration, breath inspired.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहरकरटा, आहरचेला, आहरनिवपा, आहरनिष्किरा, आहरवसना, आहरवितना, आहरसेना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

