आहर + -करटा, -चेला, -निवपा, -निष्किरा, -वसना, -वितना, -सेना, compounds<BR> of the class called; मयूरव्यंसकादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरवसना
आहर + -करटा, -चेला, -निवपा, -निष्किरा, -वसना, -वितना, -सेना, compounds<BR> of the class called; मयूरव्यंसकादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरवितना
आहर + -करटा, -चेला, -निवपा, -निष्किरा, -वसना, -वितना, -सेना, compounds<BR> of the class called; मयूरव्यंसकादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरसेना
आहर + -करटा, -चेला, -निवपा, -निष्किरा, -वसना, -वितना, -सेना, compounds<BR> of the class called; मयूरव्यंसकादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरण|आहरणं
आहरण <i>a.</i> Taking away, robbing; as in अमृताहरणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरणम्
आहरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Fetching, bringing (near); समिदाहरणाय प्रस्थिता वयम् Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Seizing, taking; को लम्बयेदाहरणाय हस्तम् R. 6. 75.<BR>—3 Removing, extracting,<BR>—4 Performing, accomplishing (as sacrifice); अश्वमेधस्य कौरव्य चकाराहरणे मतिम् Mb.<BR>—5 A dowry or present given to a bride (at the time of her marriage.);<BR> सत्त्वानुरूपाहरणीकृतश्रीः R. 7. 32.<BR>—6 Causing, inducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्तृ|आहर्त्तृ
आहर्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who takes or seizes.<BR>—2 Bringing, fetching.<BR>—3 Performing; आहर्तैषोऽश्वमेधानाम् आहर्ता कतूनाम् K. 5.<BR>—4 Causing, bringing on; आत्मनो वधमाहर्ता क्वासौ विहगतस्करः V. 5. 1. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्ता
आहर्तृ + .({@-र्ता@}) A copy-holder (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार|आहारः
आहार <i>a.</i> (-रा or -री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Bringing near, procuring, getting; भाराहारः कार्यवशात् Sk.<BR>—2 Going to fetch; अयं गच्छति भर्ता मे फलाहारो महावनम् Mb. 3. 296. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारः|आहार
आहार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Taking, fetching, or bringing near; निर्गतस्तु पुराद्वीरो भक्ष्याहारप्रचोदितः<BR> Rām. 7. 68. 2.<BR>—2 Employing, using.<BR>—3 Taking food.<BR>—4 Food; (आहरन्ति रसमस्मादित्याहारः Sk.); ˚वृत्तिमकरोत् Pt. 1<BR> took his dinner; फलाहार, ˚वृत्तिः means of livelihood; भैक्षाहारः<BR> living on alms; यवाहार, निराहार &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहारार्थिन्, आहारतेजस्, आहारनिःसरणमार्गः, आहारपाकः, आहारविरहः, आहारसंभवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारार्थिन्
आहार + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> begging or seeking for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारतेजस्
आहार + -तेजस् Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारनिःसरणमार्गः|आहारनिःसरणमार्ग
आहार + -निःसरणमार्गः the posterior part, passage of voiding excrements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारपाकः|आहारपाक
आहार + -पाकः<BR>—1 cooking.<BR>—2 digestion (of food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारविरहः|आहारविरह
आहार + -विरहः want of food, privation, starvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारसंभवः|आहारसम्भव|आहारसंभव|आहारसम्भवः
आहार + -संभवः the juice of the body, chyle, lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारक
आहारक <i>a.</i> Going to fetch or bring; एधानाहारको व्रजति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारिकम्
आहारिकम् (With the Jainas) One of the five bodies belonging to the<BR> soul; according to Colebrooke, it is ‘a minute form issuing from the head of a meditative sage to consult an omniscient saint and returning with the desired information’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0377-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य|आहार्यः|आहार्य्य|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आहार्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be taken or seized. अनीहयागताहार्यनिर्वर्तितनिजक्रियः Bhāg. 10. 86. 14.<BR>—2 To be fetched or brought near.<BR>—3 To be extracted or removed.<BR>—4 To be pervaded (व्याप्य).<BR>—5 Artificial, adventitious, incidental, external, accessary; आहार्यशोभारहितैरमायैः<BR> Bk. 2. 14; न रम्यमाहार्यमपेक्षते गुणम् Ki. 4. 23; निसर्गसुभगस्य<BR> किमाहार्यकाडम्बरेन Malli. on Ku. 7. 20.<BR>—6 Purposed, intended (as for instance, the identification or आरोप<BR> of उपमान or उपमेय in रूपक of which the speaker is fully<BR> cognisant); अयं चन्द्रो मुखमित्यादौ चन्द्रभिन्ने मुखे चन्द्राभेदज्ञानं<BR> तच्चाहार्यमेव Tv.<BR>—7 Conveyed or effected by decoration or ornamentation, one of the 4 kinds<BR> of अभिनय q. v.<BR>—8 To be eaten.<BR>—9 To be worshipped (as Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्यः|आहार्य|आहार्य्य|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आहार्य + .{@-र्यः@} A kind of bandage (बन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्यम्
आहार्य + .{@-र्यम्@}<BR>—1 Any disease to be treated by means of extracting.<BR>—2 Extraction.<BR>—3 A vessel.<BR>—4 The ornamentative part of the drama, such as dress, decorations &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्यशोभा|आहार्य्यशोभा
आहार्य + .{@-शोभा@} Adventitious beauty (not natural).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत
आहृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Brought near, fetched, procured.<BR>—2 Taken, seized.<BR>—3 Eaten.<BR>—4 Spoken, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहेय|आहेयं
आहेय <i>a.</i> [अहेरिदम् ढक्] pertaining to a serpent; प्रविशेन्मुखमाहेयम् Pt. 1. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहो
आहो <i>ind.</i> An interjection expressing<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Doubt or alternative (or), and usually standing as a correlative<BR> of किम्; किम् वैखानसं व्रतं निषेवितव्यं … आहो निवत्स्यति समम्<BR> हरिणाङ्गनाभिः Ś. 1. 27; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांसुलः Ś. 5. 29.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Interrogation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहोपुरीषकम्, आहोपुरुषा, आहोपुरुषिका, आहोस्वित्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोपुरीषकम्
आहो + -पुरीषकम् Officiousness, intrepidity, undue boldness of a man<BR> (against श्रुति). आहो पुरीषकं स्यात् MS. 12. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोपुरुषा
आहो + -पुरुषा, -पुरुषिका [अहो पुरुष वुञ् P. II. 1. 72 मयूरव्यंसकादि]<BR>—1 great self-conceit or pride; आहोपुरुषिका दर्पाद्या स्यात्संभावनात्मनि<BR> Ak.; आहोपुरुषिकां पश्य मम सद्रत्नकान्तिभिः Bk. 5. 27.<BR>—2 military vaunting, boasting.<BR>—3 vaunting of oneʼs own prowess; निजभुजबलाहोपुरुषिकाम् Bv. 1. 84.<BR> अहो रणरसोत्साहादाहोपुरुषिकामधात् Śiva B. 26. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोपुरुषिका
आहो + -पुरुषा, -पुरुषिका [अहो पुरुष वुञ् P. II. 1. 72 मयूरव्यंसकादि]<BR>—1 great self-conceit or pride; आहोपुरुषिका दर्पाद्या स्यात्संभावनात्मनि<BR> Ak.; आहोपुरुषिकां पश्य मम सद्रत्नकान्तिभिः Bk. 5. 27.<BR>—2 military vaunting, boasting.<BR>—3 vaunting of oneʼs own prowess; निजभुजबलाहोपुरुषिकाम् Bv. 1. 84.<BR> अहो रणरसोत्साहादाहोपुरुषिकामधात् Śiva B. 26. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोस्वित्
आहो + -स्वित् <i>ind.</i> a particle implying doubt, ‘or perhaps’, or ‘may … may it be’<BR> &c. (corr. of किम्); आहोस्वित्प्रसवो ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो<BR> वीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9; किं द्विजः पचति आहोस्विद् गच्छति P. VIII. 1. 44. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्न|आह्नः
आह्न <i>a.</i> (-ह्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Daily, performed in a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्नम्
आह्न + .{@-ह्नम्@} [अह्नां समूहः अञ्] A series of days, many days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्नीनैबुकम्
आह्न + .{@-आह्नीनैबुकम्@} Some religious act performed by the Southerners (<i>i. e.</i><BR> those that hail from South India). येऽपि श्यामा बृहन्तो लोहिताक्षास्तेऽपि<BR> न सर्वे आह्नीनैबुकादीन् कुर्वते ŚB. on MS. 1. 3. 18; ये दाक्षिणात्या<BR> इति समाख्यातास्ते आह्नीनैबुकादीन् करिष्यन्ति । ŚB. on MS. 1. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निक|आह्निकं
आह्निक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [अह्नि भवः, अह्ना निर्वृत्तः साध्यः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Daily, diurnal, performed every day or on a day; संग्रामाद्वयपयातव्यमेतत्कर्म<BR> ममाह्निकम् Mb. 6. 109. 27. आह्निकः स्वाध्यायः daily course of study;<BR> ˚आचारः daily observances.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">Page0378-2</a>]<BR>—2 Employed or occurring every day (as a teacher, servant, or fever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकम्
आह्निक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Any religious rite or duty which is to be performed every day at a<BR> fixed hour; अत्राह्निकं सुरश्रेष्ठो जपते Mb.<BR>—2 Anything to be performed daily, such as taking meals, bathing &c.;<BR> प्रभाते काल्यमुत्थाय कृत्वाह्निकमरिंदमः Rām. 7. 82. 5. कृताह्निकः<BR> संवृत्तः V. 4; समुद्रे कृताह्निकः Mv. 5.<BR>—3 Daily food.<BR>—4 Daily work or occupation, what may be read on one day.<BR>—5 A division of a work (such as that of the Mahābhāṣya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकचन्द्रिका
आह्निक + .{@-चन्द्रिका, -दीपिका, -प्रदीप, -मञ्जरी@} &c. N. of works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकदीपिका
आह्निक + .{@-चन्द्रिका, -दीपिका, -प्रदीप, -मञ्जरी@} &c. N. of works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकप्रदीप
आह्निक + .{@-चन्द्रिका, -दीपिका, -प्रदीप, -मञ्जरी@} &c. N. of works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकमञ्जरी
आह्निक + .{@-चन्द्रिका, -दीपिका, -प्रदीप, -मञ्जरी@} &c. N. of works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादः|आह्लाद
आह्लादः^1 Delight, joy; साह्लादं^2 वचनम् Pt. 4; ˚दुघ <i>a.</i><BR> conferring delight.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादन
आह्लादन^1 <i>a.</i> Giving delight.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादनम्
आह्लादन + .{@-नम्@} Gladdening, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादिन्
आह्लादिन्^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Delighted, glad.<BR>—2 Giving delight, gladdening.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृ
आह्वृ €1 P. Ved. To make crooked, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूर्य
आहूर्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be invoked.<BR>—2 To be bent down or brought near.<BR>—3 To be made favourable; जने न शेव आहूर्यः सन् Rv. 1. 69. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृत
आह्वृत <i>p. p.</i> Injured; ˚भेषज <i>a.</i> curing what is injured<BR> or bent; Av. 19. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वरकः|आह्वरक
आह्वरकः A low or expelled man (who, after having offered a sacrifice<BR> to the manes, takes the sacrificial food for himself); अन्नमपहर्तार<BR> आह्वरका भवन्ति श्राद्धे सिद्धे P. III. 2. 135. Com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वारकः|आह्वारक
आह्वारकः A recension of the black Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृति
आह्वृति <i>a.</i> Making crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वे
आह्वे €1 P.<BR>—1 To call, summon.<BR>—2 To invite, invoke (in a liturgical sense).<BR>—3 (Ā.) To provoke, challenge; कृष्णश्चाणूरमाह्वयते Sk.; आह्वत<BR> चेदिराण्मुरारिम् Śi. 20. 1; Bk. 6. 25, 8. 18, 15. 28, 42, 89. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To send for, call; कविमाह्वाययामास प्रस्तुतप्रतिपत्तये R. 15. 75;<BR> Bk. 6. 121.<BR>—2 To cause to invite or summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवः|आहव
आहवः [आहूयन्तेऽरयोऽत्र, आ-ह्वे-अप्]<BR>—1 Battle, war, fight; एवंविधेनाहवचेष्टितेन R. 7. 67; हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे<BR> Bg. 1. 31. आहवः स तथाप्यासीद् भारताहवसोदरः Śiva B. 25. 25.<BR>—2 Challenge, provoking, calling; ˚काम्या desire of fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवभूमिः|आहवभूमि
आहवः + .{@-भूमिः@} <i>f.</i> Battle-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहावः|आहाव
आहावः<BR>—1 A trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR>—3 Invoking, calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतिः|आहुति
आहुतिः <i>f.</i> Calling, invoking, challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूः
आहूः Ved. Calling, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूत|आहूतं|आहूतः
आहूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Called, invoked, invited; यियक्षमाणेनाहूतः पार्थेनाथ द्विषन्मुरम् Śi. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Named, called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतम्
आहूत + .{@-तम्@} Calling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आहूतप्रपलायिन्, आहूतसंप्लवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतप्रपलायिन्
आहूत + -प्रपलायिन् <i>m.</i> a defendant or witness not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">Page0379-1</a>]<BR> appearing when summoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0378-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतसंप्लवः|आहूतसम्प्लव
आहूत + -संप्लवः the time of universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतिः|आहूति
आहूतिः <i>f.</i> [आ-ह्वे-क्तिन्] Calling, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्व
आह्व <i>a.</i> [आ-ह्वे-ड]<BR>—1 Who or what calls, a crier.<BR>—2 Named, called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वा
आह्व + .{@-ह्वा@} [आ-ह्वे-अड्]<BR>—1 Calling, calling out.<BR>—2 A name, appellation, oft. at the end of comp.; अमृताह्वः शताह्वा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयः|आह्वय
आह्वयः<BR>—1 A name, appellation (as last member of comp.); काव्यं रामायणाह्वयम्<BR> Rām.; चकसाह्वयम्, चरणाह्वयाः; वृद्धेरप्याह्वया इमे Ak.<BR>—2 A law-suit arising from a dispute about games with animals, as cock-fighting<BR> &c.; (one of the 18 titles of law); पणपूर्वकपक्षिमेषादियोधनम् आह्वयः<BR> Rāghavānanda on Ms. 8. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयन
आह्वयन <i>a.</i> Taking oneʼs name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयनम्
आह्वयन + .{@-नम्@} Name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानम्
आह्वानम्<BR>—1 Calling, inviting.<BR>—2 A call, invitation, summons (in general); सुहृदाह्वानं प्रकुर्वीत Pt. 3. 47.<BR>—3 A legal summons (from court or govt. to appear before a tribunal); Mk. 9.<BR>—4 Invocation of a deity; जन्मज्येष्ठेन चाह्वानं सुब्रह्मण्यास्वपि स्मृतम् Ms. 9. 126.<BR>—5 A challenge.<BR>—6 A name, appellation.<BR>—7 N. of a liturgical formula.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: आह्वानदर्शनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानदर्शनम्
आह्वानम् + -दर्शनम् day of trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानयति
आह्वानयति Den. P. (In law) To summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायः|आह्वाय
आह्वायः<BR>—1 A summons.<BR>—2 A name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायक|आह्वायकः
आह्वायक <i>a.</i> Calling, inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायकः|आह्वायक
आह्वायक + .{@-कः@} A messenger, courier; आह्वायकान् भूमिपतेरयोध्याम् Bk. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ The third letter of the Devanāgarī alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इः|इ
इः [अ-इञ्]<BR>—1 N. of Kāmadeva; cf. Ki. 15. 45.<BR>—2 the number 100; Gīrvāṇa. <i>ind.</i> An interjection of (1) anger; (2)<BR> calling; (3) compassion; (4) reproach; (5) wonder; (6) sorrow; (7) distress.<BR> cf. इः कामः स्थाणुरिन्द्रोऽर्को वरुणः पादपो द्विपः । शुचिः श्रीमानजो<BR> बालो विरिञ्चिः कृत्तिकासुतः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ I. €2 P. (In Dhātup. written as इण्) (एति, इयाय, अगात्, एतुम्, इत)<BR>—1 To go, go to or towards, come to or near; शशिनं पुनरेति शर्वरी<BR> R. 8. 56; ईयुर्भरद्वाजमुनेर्निकेतम् Bk. 3. 40.<BR>—2 To arrive at, reach, obtain, attain to, go to or be reduced to a particular<BR> state, fall into; निर्बुद्धिः क्षयमेति Mk. 1. 14 goes to (ruin, is<BR> ruined; so वशम्, शत्रुत्वम्, शूद्रताम् &c.).<BR>—3 To return.<BR>—4 To go away, retire; elapse, pass.<BR>—5 To spring from, come or arise from.<BR>—6 To undertake anything (with acc.); सत्रमायन् Vāj.<BR>—7 To ask, beg.<BR>—8 To be; to appear.<BR>—9 To be employed in, go on with, be in a particular condition or relation,<BR> with a part. or instr.; कृषन्तो ह स्म वै वपन्तो यन्ति Śat. Br.;<BR> गवामयनेनेयुः Kāty.<BR>—10 To thrive, prosper. ━II. €1 U. = अय् q. v. ━III. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To come, appear.<BR>—2 To run, wander.<BR>—3 To go quickly or repeatedly.<BR>—4 To ask, request. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to go or come. [cf. L. <i>eo</i>;<BR> Gr. <i>eimi</i> with एमि].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्
इत् <i>a.</i> [इ-क्विप्] Going (at the end of a few comp.; as अर्थेत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत|इतः
इत <i>p. p.</i> [इ-क्त]<BR>—1 gone to; रुचिरं कमनीयत रागमिता Śi. 6. 71.<BR>—2 Returned.<BR>—3 Obtained.<BR>—4 Remembered.<BR>—5 Attended by; स खलु तुरगैः सप्तभिरितः K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतम्
इत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Course, mode of going.<BR>—2 A way.<BR>—3 Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिः|इति
इतिः <i>f.</i> Going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्य|इत्यः
इत्य <i>a.</i> To be gone towards or approached; इत्यः शिष्येण गुरुवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्या
इत्य + .{@-त्या@}<BR>—1 Going; way. अन्यमस्मदिच्छ सा तऽइत्या Vāj. 12. 62.<BR>—2 A litter, palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वन्
इत्वन् <i>a.</i> [इ-क्वनिन्] Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इ-क्वरप्]<BR>—1 Going; Rv. 10. 88. 4 travelling, a traveller.<BR>—2 Cruel, harsh, Śiva B. 14. 106.<BR>—3 Low, vile.<BR>—4 Despised, contemned.<BR>—5 Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वरः|इत्वर
इत्वर + .{@-रः@} A eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वरी
इत्वर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR>—2 An abhisārikā q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0379-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

