इज्यः|इज्य
इज्य + .{@-ज्यः@}<BR>—1 A teacher; हंसा य एकं बहुरूपमिज्यैर्मायामयं वेद स वेद वेदम्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 12. 23.<BR>—2 An epithet of वृहस्पति, the teacher of the gods.<BR>—3 The Puṣya Nakṣatra.<BR>—4 The Supreme Being; खधीः कलत्रादिषु भौम इज्यधीः Bhāg. 10. 84. 13.<BR>—5 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0380-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्या
इज्य + .{@-ज्या@}<BR>—1 A sacrifice; जगत्प्रकाशं तदशेषमिज्यया R. 3. 48, 1. 68, 15. 2;<BR> Bg. 11. 53, भूतानि यान्ति भूतेज्याः 9. 25.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR>—3 An image.<BR>—4 Worship, reverence.<BR>—5 Meeting, union.<BR>—6 A bawd or procuress.<BR>—7 A cow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इज्यशीलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0380-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्यशीलः|इज्यशील
इज्य + -शीलः a constant sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0380-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इञ्चाकः|इञ्चाक|इंचाकः
