इडस्पतिः|इडस्पति
इड(ल)स्पतिः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu or of Pūṣan; आराधयन्मन्त्रमिममभ्यस्यन्त<BR> इडस्पतिम् Bhāg. 6. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलस्पतिः
इड(ल)स्पतिः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu or of Pūṣan; आराधयन्मन्त्रमिममभ्यस्यन्त<BR> इडस्पतिम् Bhāg. 6. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडः|इड
इडः An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडविडा
इडविडा<BR>—1 A species of she-goat.<BR>—2 The bleating of a goat; सोऽपि चानुगतः स्त्रैणं कृपणस्तां प्रसादितुम् ।<BR> कुर्वन्निडविडाकारं नाशक्नोत्पथि सन्धितुम् ॥ Bhāg. 9. 19. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा, -ला<BR> [इल्-अच्, वा लस्य डत्वम्]<BR>—1 The earth; प्रवुध्यते नूनमिडातलस्थः Mb.<BR>—2 Speech.<BR>—3 An offering, libation (coming between प्रयाज and अनुयाज);<BR> अग्निश्च ते योनिरिडा च देहः Mb. 3. 114. 28.<BR>—4 Refreshing draught.<BR>—5 (Hence) Food.<BR>—6 (Fig.) Stream or flow of praise or worship personified as the goddess<BR> of sacred speech; इडोपहूताः कोशन्ति कुञ्जरास्त्वङ्कुशरिताः Mb. 12. 98. 26.<BR>—7 Libation and offering of milk.<BR>—8 A cow. इडेरन्ते &c. ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49.<BR>—9 N. of a goddess, daughter of Manu. (She is the wife of Budha and mother<BR> of Purūravas; she is also called मैत्रावरुणी as the daughter of मित्र<BR> and वरुण).<BR>—10 N. of Durgā<BR>—11 Heaven.<BR>—12 A tubular vessel (नाडीभेद), (being in the right side of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इडा, -ला<BR> [इल्-अच्, वा लस्य डत्वम्]<BR>—1 The earth; प्रवुध्यते नूनमिडातलस्थः Mb.<BR>—2 Speech.<BR>—3 An offering, libation (coming between प्रयाज and अनुयाज);<BR> अग्निश्च ते योनिरिडा च देहः Mb. 3. 114. 28.<BR>—4 Refreshing draught.<BR>—5 (Hence) Food.<BR>—6 (Fig.) Stream or flow of praise or worship personified as the goddess<BR> of sacred speech; इडोपहूताः कोशन्ति कुञ्जरास्त्वङ्कुशरिताः Mb. 12. 98. 26.<BR>—7 Libation and offering of milk.<BR>—8 A cow. इडेरन्ते &c. ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49.<BR>—9 N. of a goddess, daughter of Manu. (She is the wife of Budha and mother<BR> of Purūravas; she is also called मैत्रावरुणी as the daughter of मित्र<BR> and वरुण).<BR>—10 N. of Durgā<BR>—11 Heaven.<BR>—12 A tubular vessel (नाडीभेद), (being in the right side of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडावत्|इडावन्त्
इडावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of sacrificial food.<BR>—2 Refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाचिका
इडाचिका A cell-building wasp (Mar. कुंभारीण). Vespa solitaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाजातः|इडाजात
इडाजातः A fragrant gum, Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिका
इडिका The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिक्कः|इडिक्क
इडिक्कः A wild goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्वरः|इड्वर
इड्वरः^1 see इट्चर.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: corrected after AP90 and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्डीकः
इण्डीकः A pen-knife; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्ड्रः|इण्ड्र|इंड्रं|इंड्रः
इण्ड्रः, -ण्ड्रम् (इण्ड्वम्) (<i>Dual</i>)<BR> Two round small plates used as<BR> coverings for the hands in taking the fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिण्ड्राभ्यां<BR> परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यन्ते तौ इण्ड्रौ Karka.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्ड्रम्
इण्ड्रः, -ण्ड्रम् (इण्ड्वम्) (<i>Dual</i>)<BR> Two round small plates used as<BR> coverings for the hands in taking the fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिण्ड्राभ्यां<BR> परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यन्ते तौ इण्ड्रौ Karka.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्ड्वम्
इण्ड्रः, -ण्ड्रम् (इण्ड्वम्) (<i>Dual</i>)<BR> Two round small plates used as<BR> coverings for the hands in taking the fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिण्ड्राभ्यां<BR> परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यन्ते तौ इण्ड्रौ Karka.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर <i>pron. a.</i> (-रा <i>f.</i>, -रत् <i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 Another, the other (of two), the remaining one of the two; इतरो<BR> दहने स्वकर्मणाम् R. 8. 20 v. l.<BR>—2 The rest or others (pl.). what is left. इतरदधिकार्थे˚ । MS. 7. 1. 16<BR> (on which शबर writes इतरदधिकार्थे समानमितरत् समानमधिकमित्यर्थः ।).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">Page0381-2</a>]<BR>—3 Other than, different from (with abl.); इतरतापशतानि यथेच्छया<BR> वितर तानि सहे चतुरानन Udb.; इतरो रावणादेष राघवानुचरो यदि Bk. 8. 106.<BR>—4 Opposite of, either used by itself as an adj. or at the end of comp.;<BR> जङ्गमानीतराणि च Rām.; विजयायेतराय वा Mb.; सुलभेतरसंप्रयोगाम्<BR> M. 5. 3 opposite of, other than easy, difficult; so दक्षिण˚ left;<BR> वाम˚ right &c.<BR>—5 Low, mean, vulgar, ordinary; इतर इव परिभूय ज्ञानं मन्मथेन<BR> जडीकृतः K. 154, 160, 203, 273. इतर━इतर the one━the other, this━that.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इतरेतर, इतरजनाः, इतरजातीय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतर|इतरेतरं
इतर + -इतर <i>pron. a.</i> respective, reciprocal, one with another (chiefly<BR> in oblique cases or in comp.); वियुक्तावितरेतरम् Ms. 9. 102; ˚काम्यया 3. 35;<BR> R. 7. 54. ˚आश्रयः mutual dependence, inter-connection. ˚योगः<BR>—1 mutual connection or union, मोदितालिरितरेतरयोगात् Śi. 10. 24.<BR>—2 a variety of the Dvandva compound (opp. समाहारद्वन्द्व) where<BR> each member of the compound is viewed separately; as प्लक्षन्यग्रोधौ छिनात्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरजनाः
इतर + -जनाः (pl.)<BR>—1 other men.<BR>—2 euphemistically said of certain beings considered as spirits of darkness<BR> of which Kubera is one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरजातीय
इतर + -जातीय <i>a.</i> Ordinary, common-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरतः
इतरतः, इतरत्र <i>ind.</i> Otherwise than, different from,<BR> elsewhere; see अन्यतः, अन्यत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरत्र
इतरतः, इतरत्र <i>ind.</i> Otherwise than, different from,<BR> elsewhere; see अन्यतः, अन्यत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरथा
इतरथा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In another manner, in a contrary manner.<BR>—2 Perversely.<BR>—3 On the other hand. यदि वा इतरथा ब्रह्मचर्यादेव प्रव्रजेत् Jābāla Up. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेद्युः
इतरेद्युः <i>ind.</i> P. V. 3. 22. On another day, the other day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस् <i>ind.</i> [इदम्-तसिल् इशादेशः Tv.]<BR>—1 Hence, from here or hence.<BR>—2 From this person, from me; इतः स दैत्यः प्राप्तश्रीर्नेत एवार्हति<BR> क्षयम् Ku. 2. 55.<BR>—3 In this direction towards me, here; इतो निषीदेति विसृष्टभूमिः Ku. 3. 2;<BR> प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रमितो वृथा स्यात् R. 2. 34; इतः स्वपिति केशवः<BR> &c. Bh. 2. 76; इतो गतमनुरागम् V. 2; ˚गतवृत्तान्तं न स्मरति<BR> Ś. 4 news of this place; इत इतो देवः this way, this way, my lord (in dramas).<BR>—4 Hence, for this reason, on this ground; इतश्च परमात्मैवेहात्ता भवितुमर्हति<BR> Ś. B. 1. 2. 10.<BR>—5 From this world.<BR>—6 From this time. {@इतः━इतः@}<BR>——(<i>a</i>) on the one hand━on the other hand; इतस्तपस्विकार्यमितो गुरुजनाज्ञा Ś. 2;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) in one place━in another place, here━there; K. 27; इतश्चेतश्च<BR> hither and thither; hence and thence, here and there, to and fro; इतश्चेतश्च<BR> धावताम्; now, therefore; इतस्ततः here and there, hither and thither,<BR> to and fro; लाङ्गूलविक्षेपविसर्पिशोभैरितस्ततश्चन्द्रमरीचिगौरैः Ku. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 this particle is most generally used to report the very words spoken<BR> or supposed to be spoken by some one, as represented by quotation marks<BR> in English. The speech reported may be (1) a single word used merely to<BR> express what the form of the word is, when it is used as it is (शब्दस्वरूपद्योतक);<BR> कूजन्तं रामरामेति मधुरं मधुराक्षरम् Rāmarakṣā. अत एव गवित्याह<BR> Bh.; (2) or a substantive, which must be put in the nominative case<BR> when its meaning is to be indicated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">Page0382-1</a>]<BR> (प्रातिपदिकार्थद्योतक); चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा … कमादमुं<BR> नारद इत्यबोधि सः Śi. 1, 3; अवैमि चैनामनघेति R. 14. 40; दिलीप<BR> इति राजेन्दुः R. 1. 12; sometimes with acc. कैवर्तमिति यं प्राहुः<BR> Ms. 10. 34; Bg. 6. 2; (3) or a whole sentence when इति is merely<BR> used at the end of that sentence; (वाक्यार्थद्योतक); ज्ञास्यसि कियद्<BR> भुजो मे रक्षति मौर्वींकिणाङ्क इति Śi. 1. 13; तयोर्मुनिकुमारयोरन्यतरः<BR> कथयति अक्षमालामुपयाचितुमागतोस्मीति K. 151.<BR>—2 Besides this general sense इति has the following senses:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Cause, as expressed by ‘because’, ‘since’, ‘on the ground that’,<BR> in English; वैदेशिकोऽस्मीति पृच्छामि U.; पुराणमित्येव नःसाधु सर्वम्<BR> M. 1. 2, oft. with किम् q. v.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Purpose or motive, as expressed by ‘that’, ‘in order that’ शरीरस्य<BR> विनाशो मा भूदिति मयेदमुत्क्षिप्य समानीतम् K. 320; R. 1. 37.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Thus, to mark the conclusion (opp. अथ); इति प्रथमोऽङ्कः<BR> thus or here ends the first Act.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) It is often used to include under one head a number of separate<BR> objects grouped together; पृथिव्यापस्तेजो वायुराकाशं कालो दिगात्मा मन<BR> इति द्रव्याणि T. S.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) So, thus, in this manner; इत्युक्तवन्तं परिरभ्य दोर्भ्याम् Ki. 11. 80.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) Of this nature or description; गौरश्वः पुरुषो हस्तीति जातिः.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) As follows, to the following effect; रामाभिधानो हरिरित्युवाच R. 13. 1.<BR>——(<i>h</i>) As for, in the capacity of, as regards, showing capacity or relation;<BR> पितेति स पूज्यः, अध्यापक इति निन्द्यः, शीघ्रमिति सुकरं, निभृतमिति<BR> चिन्तनीयं भवेत् Ś. 3.<BR>——(<i>i</i>) It is often used with the name of an author to form an <i>Avyayibhāva</i><BR> comp. इतिपाणिनि thus according to Pāṇini.<BR>——(<i>j</i>) Illustration (usually with आदि); इन्दुरिन्दुरिव श्रीमानित्यादौ<BR> तदनन्वयः Candr.; गौः शुक्लश्चलो डित्थ इत्यादौ K. P. 2.<BR>——(<i>k</i>) A quotation or an opinion accepted; इति पाणिनिः, इत्यापिशलिः,<BR> इत्यमरः, विश्वः &c.<BR>——(<i>l</i>) It is often used by commentators after quoting a rule in the<BR> sense of ‘according to such a rule’; शकि लिङ् च (P. III. 3. 172) इति<BR> शक्यार्थे लिङ् Malli. Other senses mentioned are:−<BR>——(<i>m</i>) Manifestation.<BR>——(<i>n</i>) Order.<BR>——(<i>o</i>) Arrangement.<BR>——(<i>p</i>) Identity.<BR>——(<i>q</i>) Proximity.<BR>——(<i>r</i>) Visibility.<BR>——(<i>s</i>) Excess or superiority.<BR>——(<i>t</i>) Requiring. (इति स्वरूपे सान्निध्ये विवक्षानियमे मते । हेतौ<BR> प्रकारप्रत्यक्षप्रकाशेष्यवधारणे, एवमर्थे समाप्तौ च ॥ Hem.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इत्यर्थः, इत्यर्थम्, इत्यादि, इत्युक्तम्, इतिकथ, इतिकर्तव्य, इतिकरणीय, इतिकार्य, इतिकृत्य, इतिकर्तव्यता, इतिकार्यता, इतिकृत्यता, इतिपाणिनि, इतिमात्र, इतिवृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0381-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यर्थः|इत्यर्थ
इति + -अर्थः sum and substance, meaning in short (often used by commentators).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यर्थम्
इति + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> for this purpose, hence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यादि
इति + -आदि <i>a.</i> having such a thing or things at the beginning, so<BR> forth, {{et caetera->et cætera||20260515|Dr. Dhaval Patel|https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/pull/2845}} (&c.). इत्यादिप्रचुराः पुरातनकथाः सर्वेभ्य एवं श्रुताः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्युक्तम्
इति + -उक्तम् information, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकथ|इतिकथं
इति + -कथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not fit to be believed, untrustworthy.<BR>—2 wicked, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकथा
इति + -कथ + .({@-था@}) a meaningless or nonsensical talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्तव्य|इतिकर्त्तव्य
इति + -कर्तव्य, -करणीय, -कार्य, -कृत्य <i>a.</i> proper or necessary<BR> to be done according to certain rules. ({@कर्तव्यम्, -णीयम्@}) duty,<BR> obligation; श्रूयतामितिकर्तव्यं सर्वानेव ब्रवीमि वः Rām. 2. 68. 5.<BR> एवं सर्वं विधायेदमितिकर्तव्यमात्मनः Ms. 7. 142, संसिद्धावितिकरणीयसंनिबद्धैरालापैः<BR> Ki. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकरणीय
इति + -कर्तव्य, -करणीय, -कार्य, -कृत्य <i>a.</i> proper or necessary<BR> to be done according to certain rules. ({@कर्तव्यम्, -णीयम्@}) duty,<BR> obligation; श्रूयतामितिकर्तव्यं सर्वानेव ब्रवीमि वः Rām. 2. 68. 5.<BR> एवं सर्वं विधायेदमितिकर्तव्यमात्मनः Ms. 7. 142, संसिद्धावितिकरणीयसंनिबद्धैरालापैः<BR> Ki. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकार्य
इति + -कर्तव्य, -करणीय, -कार्य, -कृत्य <i>a.</i> proper or necessary<BR> to be done according to certain rules. ({@कर्तव्यम्, -णीयम्@}) duty,<BR> obligation; श्रूयतामितिकर्तव्यं सर्वानेव ब्रवीमि वः Rām. 2. 68. 5.<BR> एवं सर्वं विधायेदमितिकर्तव्यमात्मनः Ms. 7. 142, संसिद्धावितिकरणीयसंनिबद्धैरालापैः<BR> Ki. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकृत्य
इति + -कर्तव्य, -करणीय, -कार्य, -कृत्य <i>a.</i> proper or necessary<BR> to be done according to certain rules. ({@कर्तव्यम्, -णीयम्@}) duty,<BR> obligation; श्रूयतामितिकर्तव्यं सर्वानेव ब्रवीमि वः Rām. 2. 68. 5.<BR> एवं सर्वं विधायेदमितिकर्तव्यमात्मनः Ms. 7. 142, संसिद्धावितिकरणीयसंनिबद्धैरालापैः<BR> Ki. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्तव्यता|इतिकर्त्तव्यता
इति + -कर्तव्यता, -कार्यता, -कृत्यता any proper or necessary duty, obligation; स<BR> मुहूर्तमिव ध्यात्वा विनिश्चित्योतिकृत्यताम् Mb. 3. 36. 4. इतिकर्तव्यतामूढः<BR> wholly at a loss what to do, embarrassed, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकार्यता
इति + -कर्तव्यता, -कार्यता, -कृत्यता any proper or necessary duty, obligation; स<BR> मुहूर्तमिव ध्यात्वा विनिश्चित्योतिकृत्यताम् Mb. 3. 36. 4. इतिकर्तव्यतामूढः<BR> wholly at a loss what to do, embarrassed, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकृत्यता
इति + -कर्तव्यता, -कार्यता, -कृत्यता any proper or necessary duty, obligation; स<BR> मुहूर्तमिव ध्यात्वा विनिश्चित्योतिकृत्यताम् Mb. 3. 36. 4. इतिकर्तव्यतामूढः<BR> wholly at a loss what to do, embarrassed, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिपाणिनि
इति + -पाणिनि <i>ind.</i> Thus according to Pāṇiniʼs<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">Page0382-2</a>]<BR> very words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिमात्र
इति + -मात्र <i>a.</i> of such extent or quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिवृत्तम्
इति + -वृत्तम्<BR>—1 occurrence, event.<BR>—2 a tale, story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिः|इति
इतिः<BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 Speed; Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिक
इतिक <i>a.</i> Having gait or speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिथ
इतिथ <i>a.</i> Ved. Such a one, such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिवत्
इतिवत् <i>ind.</i> In the same manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिशः|इतिश
इतिशः Name of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिह
इतिह <i>ind.</i> Thus indeed, quite in conformity to tradition; सुप्रसिद्धः<BR> प्रवादोऽयमितिहेतीह गीयते Mv. 2. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासः|इतिहास
इतिहासः [fr. इति-ह-आस (3rd pers. sing. Perf. of अस् to<BR> be); so it has been]<BR>—1 History (legendary or traditional); धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामुपदेशसमन्वितम्<BR> पूर्ववृत्तं कथायुक्तमितिहासं प्रचक्षते; Mb. cf. also आर्यादिबहुव्याख्यानं<BR> देवर्षिचरिताश्रयम् । इतिहासमिति प्रोक्तं भविष्याद्भुतधर्मयुक् ॥<BR>—2 Heroic history (such as the Mahābhārata).<BR>—3 Historical evidence, tradition (which is recognized as a proof by the Paurāṇikas).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इतिहासनिबन्धनम्, इतिहासपुराणम्, इतिहासवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासनिबन्धनम्
इतिहासः + -निबन्धनम् legendary composition or narrative; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासपुराणम्
इतिहासः + -पुराणम् history and legendary stories; इतिहासपुराणानि पञ्चमो<BR> वेद उच्यते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासवादः|इतिहासवाद
इतिहासः + -वादः historical story, legend; Māl. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्कटः|इत्कट
इत्कटः A kind of grass (इक्डी)^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: a Marathi word in the regional dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्किला
इत्किला N. of a perfume (Mar. गोरोचना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्
इत्थम् <i>ind.</i> Thus, so, in this manner; इत्थं रतेः किमपि भूतमदृश्यरूपम्<BR> Ku. 4. 45; इत्थंगते under these circumstances, such being the case;<BR> इत्थंगते किमस्माभिः करणीयम् Ś. 4; R. 9. 81.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इत्थङ्कारम्, इत्थम्भूत, इत्थम्भावः, इत्थंविध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थङ्कारम्|इत्थंकारम्
इत्थम् + -कारम् <i>ind.</i> in this manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्भूत|इत्थंभूत
इत्थम् + -भूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 so circumstanced, being in this state, being thus; ˚आख्याने P. I. 4. 90;<BR> Me. 96; Ku. 6. 26; Ś. 3. 5; कथमित्थंभूता M. 5; K. 146.<BR>—2 true or faithful (as a story).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्भावः|इत्थम्भाव|इत्थंभाव
इत्थम् + -भावः being thus endowed, having these qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थंविध
इत्थम् + -विध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of such kind.<BR>—2 endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थशालः|इत्थशाल
इत्थशालः N. of the third Yoga in Astronomy (Arabic origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्था
इत्था <i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 In this manner, thus; क इत्थावेद यत्र सः Kaṭh. 1. 2. 24.<BR>—2 A particle of affirmation used to lay stress on a following word, indeed.<BR>—3 Truly, really. {@˚धी@} <i>a.</i> performing such or true works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थात्
इत्थात् <i>ind.</i> Thus, in this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A traveller,<BR>—2 A poor person.<BR>—3 A wicked and a debaucherous man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A particle of affirmation, even, just, only; यथा वशन्ति देवास्तथेदसद्<BR> Rv. 8. 28. 4 especially in strengthening a statement; अर्थज्ञ इत्सकलं<BR> भद्रमश्नुते Nir.<BR>—2 It is often added to words expressing excess or exclusion: विश्व इत् एक इत् &c.<BR>—3 At the beginning of sentences it often adds emphasis to pronouns, prepositions<BR> &c. (its place is taken by एव in classical Sanskrit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0382-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् <i>pron. a.</i> [अयम् <i>m.</i>, इयम् <i>f.</i>, इदम् <i>n.</i>]<BR>—1 This, here, referring to something near the speaker; [इदमस्तु संनिकृष्टं<BR> रूपम्]; इदं तत् … इति यदुच्यते Ś. 5 here is the truth of the saying.<BR>—2 Present, seen; the nominative forms are used with verbs in the sense<BR> of ‘here’; इयमस्मि here am I; so इमे स्मः; अयमागच्छामि here I come.<BR>—3 It often refers to something immediately following, while एतद्<BR> refers to what precedes; अनुकल्पस्त्वयं ज्ञेयः सदा सद्भिरनुष्ठितः<BR> Ms. 3. 147 (अयम् = वक्ष्यमाणः Kull.); श्रुत्वैतदिदमूचुः<BR>—4 It occurs connected with यत्, तत्, एतद्, अदस्, किम् or a personal<BR> pronoun, either to point out anything more distinctly and emphatically,<BR> or sometimes pleonastically; कोऽयमाचरत्यविनयम् Ś. 1. 25; सेयम्,<BR> सोऽयम्, this here; so इमास्ताः; अयमहं भोः Ś. 4 ho, here am I. ━<i>ind.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Here, to this place.<BR>—2 Now.<BR>—3 There.<BR>—4 With these words, herewith.<BR>—5 In this manner; नैतदौपयिकं राम यदिदं परितप्यसे Rām. 2. 53. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इदङ्कार्या, इदम्प्रथम, इदम्प्रकारम्, इदंयुगम्, इदंरूप, इदंवसु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदङ्कार्या|इदंकार्या|इदंकार्य्या|इदङ्कार्य्या
इदम् + -कार्या The plant Hedysarum Alhagi (Mar. कांटे धमासा, यवासा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्प्रथम|इदंप्रथम
इदम् + -प्रथम <i>a.</i> doing anything for the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्प्रकारम्|इदंप्रकारम्
इदम् + -प्रकारम् <i>ind.</i> in this manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंयुगम्
इदम् + -युगम् the present Yuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंरूप
इदम् + -रूप <i>a.</i> of this shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंवसु
इदम् + -वसु <i>a.</i> Ved. rich in this and that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंतन
इदंतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Of this time, present; momentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंता
इदंता [इदमो भावः] Identity, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदन्द्र|इदंद्र
इदन्द्र <i>a.</i> One who sees this; तस्मादिदन्द्रो नामेदन्द्रो ह वै<BR> Ait. Up. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्बरम्
इदम्बरम् A blue lotus; Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंमय
इदंमय <i>a.</i> Made or consisting of this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंयु
इदंयु <i>a.</i> Wishing this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदा
इदा <i>ind.</i> Now, at this (present) moment; oft. with अहन्; इदाचिदह्नः;<BR> इदा ह्यः only yesterday.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इदावत्सरः, इदावत्सरीय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदावत्सरः|इदावत्सर
इदा + -वत्सरः so इदुवत्सरः or इद्वत्सरः one of the five<BR> years in which gifts of clothes and food are said to be productive of<BR> great rewards. cf. Bhāg. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदावत्सरीय
इदा + -वत्सरीय or {@इद्वत्सरीय@} <i>a.</i> belonging to such year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्वत्सरीय
इदा + -वत्सरीय or {@इद्वत्सरीय@} <i>a.</i> belonging to such year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीम्
इदानीम् <i>ind.</i> [इदं-दानीम् इश् च]<BR>—1 Now, at this moment, in this case, just now, even now; वत्से प्रतिष्ठस्वेदानीम्<BR> Ś. 4; आर्यपुत्र इदानीमसि U. 3; इदानीमौदास्यं भजसि यदि भागीरथि<BR> तदा G. L. इदानीमह्नः now-a-days; इदानीमेव just now; इदानीमपि<BR> now also, in this case also; तत इदानीम् thereupon, then, from that time.<BR>—2 As a measure of time, it is equal to one fifteenth part of an एतर्हि;<BR> cf. यावन्त्येतर्हीणि तावन्ति पंचदशकृत्व इदानीनि Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानींतन|इदानीन्तन|इदानीन्तनं
इदानींतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Present, momentary, of the present moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्धा
इद्धा <i>ind.</i> Explicit, manifest, apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म, इद्ध See under इन्ध. औदुम्बर इध्मः Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इध्म, इद्ध See under इन्ध. औदुम्बर इध्मः Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्
इन् €6. €8 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To advance or rush upon, press upon; drive.<BR>—3 To invigorate.<BR>—4 To force, compel.<BR>—5 To drive away, remove.<BR>—6 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">Page0383-2</a>]<BR> take possession of, pervade, fill.<BR>—7 To dispose.<BR>—8 To be lord or master (of anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन|इनः
इन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Able, strong, powerful, mighty.<BR>—2 Bold, determined.<BR>—3 Glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनः|इन
इन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A lord, master. लोके भवाञ्जगदिनः कलयावतीर्णः Bhāg. 10. 70. 27.<BR>—2 The sun; तपत्विनः Śi. 2. 65. भजति कल्पमिनः प्रतिपद्ययम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 21. (cf. इनो भागो धामनिधिरंशुमाल्यब्जिनीपतिः Ak.)<BR>—3 A king; न न महीनमहीनपराकमम् R. 9. 5.<BR>—4 The lunar mansion Hasta.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इनकान्तः, इनसभम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनकान्तः
इन + -कान्तः sun-stone (सूर्यकान्त); Bh. 2. 37. यदचेतनोऽपि<BR> पादैः स्पृष्टः प्रज्वलति सवितुरिनकान्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनसभम्
इन + -सभम् a royal court or assembly. P. II. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनक्ष
इनक्ष (Desid. of नक्ष्) Ved. To try to reach, strive to get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनानी
इनानी <i>f.</i> A kind of tree (वटपत्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्थिहा|इंथिहा
इन्थिहा An astronomical term taken from the Arabic (= मुथहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्|इंद्
इन्द् €1 P. [इन्दति, इन्दितुम्] To be powerful (occurring in the etymology<BR> of इन्द्र q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वका
इन्वका^1 A king of star remaining overhead in the मृगशीर्ष-नक्षत्र.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दम्बरम्
इन्दम्बरम् = इन्दीवर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिन्दिरः|इन्दिन्दिर|इंदिंदिरः
इन्दिन्दिरः A large bee; लोभादिन्दिन्दिरेषु निपतत्सु Bv. 2. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरा|इंदिरा
इन्दिरा [इन्द्-किरच्] N. of Lakṣmi, wife of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इन्दिरालयम्, इन्दिरामन्दिरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरालयम्
इन्दिरा + -आलयम् ‘abode of Indirā’, the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरामन्दिरः|इन्दिरामन्दिर|इन्दिरामन्दिरं
इन्दिरा + -मन्दिरः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरामन्दिरम्
इन्दिरा + -मन्दिरः + .({@-रम्@}) the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिवरम्
इन्दि(न्दी)वरम् [इन्दीर्लक्ष्मीस्तस्या वरं वरणीयम् Tv.] The blue<BR> lotus; बाले तव मुखाम्भोजे कथमिन्दीवरद्वयम् Ś. Til. 17. इन्दीवरदलश्यामः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu; इन्दीवरदलश्याममिन्दिरानन्दकन्दलम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवरम्
इन्दि(न्दी)वरम् [इन्दीर्लक्ष्मीस्तस्या वरं वरणीयम् Tv.] The blue<BR> lotus; बाले तव मुखाम्भोजे कथमिन्दीवरद्वयम् Ś. Til. 17. इन्दीवरदलश्यामः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu; इन्दीवरदलश्याममिन्दिरानन्दकन्दलम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवरिणी|इंदीवरिणी
इन्दीवरिणी A group of blue lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवारः|इन्दीवार|इन्दीवारं|इंदीवारः
इन्दीवारः A blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुः|इन्दु|इंदुः
इन्दुः [उनत्ति क्लेदयति चन्द्रिकया भुवनम् उन्द्-उ आदेरिच्च Uṇ. 1. 12]<BR>—1 The moon; दिलीप इति राजेन्दुरिन्दुः क्षीरनिधाविव R. 1. 12 (इन्दु<BR> is said to mean in the Veda a drop of Soma juice, a bright drop or spark;<BR> सुतास इन्दवः Rv. 1. 16. 6).<BR>—2 The मृगाशिरस् Nakṣatra.<BR>—3 (in Math.) The number ‘one’.<BR>—4 Camphor.<BR>—5 The point on a die; तेभ्यो व इन्दवो हविषा विधेम Av. 7. 109. 6.<BR>—6 Designation of the अनुस्वार. ━(pl.)<BR>—1 The periodical changes of the moon.<BR>—2 The time of moon-light, night.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इन्दुकमलम्, इन्दुकला, इन्दुकलिका, इन्दुकान्तः, इन्दुक्षयः, इन्दुजः, इन्दुपुत्रः, इन्दुजनकः, इन्दुदलः, इन्दुपुष्पिका, इन्दुभम्, इन्दुभा, इन्दुभृत्, इन्दुशेखरः, इन्दुमौलिः, इन्दुमणिः, इन्दुमुखी, इन्दुमण्डलम्, इन्दुरत्नम्, इन्दुलेखा, इन्दुरेखा, इन्दुलोकः, इन्दुलोहकम्, इन्दुलौहम्, इन्दुवदना, इन्दुवल्ली, इन्दुवारः, इन्दुवासरः, इन्दुव्रतम्, इन्दुशफरी, इन्दुसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकमलम्
इन्दुः + -कमलम् the white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकला
इन्दुः + -कला<BR>—1 a digit of the moon. (These are 16, each of which is mythologically<BR> said to be devoured by 16 deities in succession).<BR>—2 N. of several plants; अमृता, गुडूची, सोमलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकलिका
इन्दुः + -कलिका<BR>—1 N. of a plant (केतकी).<BR>—2 a digit of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकान्तः|इन्दुकान्त
इन्दुः + -कान्तः the moon-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकान्ता
इन्दुः + -कान्तः + .({@-ता@})<BR>—1 night.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (केतकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुक्षयः|इन्दुक्षय
इन्दुः + -क्षयः<BR>—1 waning or disappearance of the moon.<BR>—2 the new moon day. Ms. 3. 122.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">Page0384-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0383-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजः|इन्दुज
इन्दुः + -जः, -पुत्रः the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजा
इन्दुः + -जः, -पुत्रः + .({@-जा@}) N. of the river Revā or Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुपुत्रः|इन्दुपुत्र
इन्दुः + -जः, -पुत्रः the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजनकः|इन्दुजनक
इन्दुः + -जनकः<BR>—1 the ocean (the moon being produced amongst other jewels at the churning of the ocean)<BR>—2 the sage अत्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुदलः|इन्दुदल
इन्दुः + -दलः a digit, crescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुपुष्पिका
इन्दुः + -पुष्पिका N. of a plant (कलिकारी or जांगली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुभम्
इन्दुः + -भम्<BR>—1 the sign called Cancer.<BR>—2 the Nakṣatra called मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुभा
इन्दुः + -भा a kind of water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुभृत्
इन्दुः + -भृत्, -शेखरः, -मौलिः ‘the moon-crested god’, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुशेखरः|इन्दुशेखर
इन्दुः + -भृत्, -शेखरः, -मौलिः ‘the moon-crested god’, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमौलिः|इन्दुमौलि
इन्दुः + -भृत्, -शेखरः, -मौलिः ‘the moon-crested god’, epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमणिः|इन्दुमणि
इन्दुः + -मणिः<BR>—1 the moon-stone.<BR>—2 a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमुखी
इन्दुः + -मुखी A lotus-creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमण्डलम्
इन्दुः + -मण्डलम् the orb or disc of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरत्नम्
इन्दुः + -रत्नम् a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलेखा
इन्दुः + -लेखा, -रेखा<BR>—1 a digit of the moon.<BR>—2 N. of several plants, especially, plant Flacourtia Sapida. Its seed<BR> is much used by women as a detergent to their oiled hair (Mar. बांवच्या).<BR>—3 Ligusticum Ajwaen (Mar. ओंवा). see इन्दुकला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरेखा
इन्दुः + -लेखा, -रेखा<BR>—1 a digit of the moon.<BR>—2 N. of several plants, especially, plant Flacourtia Sapida. Its seed<BR> is much used by women as a detergent to their oiled hair (Mar. बांवच्या).<BR>—3 Ligusticum Ajwaen (Mar. ओंवा). see इन्दुकला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0384-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलोकः|इन्दुलोक
