इन्द्रः + -पुरोगम, -पुरःसर, -श्रेष्ठ <i>a.</i> led or preceded by Indra,<BR> having Indra at the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रश्रेष्ठ
इन्द्रः + -पुरोगम, -पुरःसर, -श्रेष्ठ <i>a.</i> led or preceded by Indra,<BR> having Indra at the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुरोहितः|इन्द्रपुरोहित
इन्द्रः + -पुरोहितः N. of बृहस्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुरोहिता
इन्द्रः + -पुरोहितः + .({@-ता@}) the asterism Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रमतिः|इन्द्रप्रमति
इन्द्रः + -प्रमतिः N. of the pupil of Paila and the author of some ṛks of the Rv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रस्थम्
इन्द्रः + -प्रस्थम् N. of a city on the Yamunā, the residence of the Pāṇḍavas<BR> (identified with the modern Delhi); इन्द्रप्रस्थगमस्तावत्कारि मा सन्तु<BR> चेदयः Śi. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रहरणम्
इन्द्रः + -प्रहरणम् Indraʼs weapon, the thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रभगिनी
इन्द्रः + -भगिनी N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रभेषजम्
इन्द्रः + -भेषजम् dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमखः|इन्द्रमख
इन्द्रः + -मखः a sacrifice in honour of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमहः|इन्द्रमह
इन्द्रः + -महः<BR>—1 a festival in honour of Indra.<BR>—2 the rainy season; ˚कामुकः a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमादन
इन्द्रः + -मादन <i>a.</i> animating or delighting Indra; ये वायव इन्द्रमादनासः Rv. 7. 92. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमेदिन्
इन्द्रः + -मेदिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. whose friend or ally is Indra; इन्द्रमेदी<BR> सत्वनो नि ह्वयस्व Av. 5. 20. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयज्ञः|इन्द्रयज्ञ
इन्द्रः + -यज्ञः (See इन्द्रमह and इन्द्रमख) श्वोऽस्माकं घोषस्योचित<BR> इन्द्रयज्ञो नामोत्सवः भविष्यति Bālacharitam 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयवः|इन्द्रयव
इन्द्रः + -यवः, -यवम् seed of the <i>Kuṭaja</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयवम्
इन्द्रः + -यवः, -यवम् seed of the <i>Kuṭaja</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्तः|इन्द्रलुप्त|इन्द्रलुप्तं
इन्द्रः + -लुप्तः, -लुप्तम्, -लुप्तकम्<BR>—1 excessive baldness of the head.<BR>—2 loss of beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्तम्
इन्द्रः + -लुप्तः, -लुप्तम्, -लुप्तकम्<BR>—1 excessive baldness of the head.<BR>—2 loss of beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्तकम्
इन्द्रः + -लुप्तः, -लुप्तम्, -लुप्तकम्<BR>—1 excessive baldness of the head.<BR>—2 loss of beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोकः|इन्द्रलोक
इन्द्रः + -लोकः Indraʼs world, Svarga or Paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोकेशः|इन्द्रलोकेश
इन्द्रः + -लोकेशः<BR>—1 lord of Indraʼs world, <i>i. e.</i> Indra.<BR>—2 a guest (who, if hospitably received, confers paradise on his host).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवंशा
इन्द्रः + -वंशा, -वज्रा N. of two metres, see Appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवज्रा
इन्द्रः + -वंशा, -वज्रा N. of two metres, see Appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवल्लरी
इन्द्रः + -वल्लरी, -वल्ली N. of a plant (पारिजात) or of इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवल्ली
इन्द्रः + -वल्लरी, -वल्ली N. of a plant (पारिजात) or of इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवस्तिः|इन्द्रवस्ति
इन्द्रः + -वस्तिः [इन्द्रस्य आत्मनः वास्तिरिव] the calf (of the leg).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवाततम
इन्द्रः + -वाततम <i>a.</i> Ved. desired by Indra. अस्मे ऊतीरिन्द्रवाततमाः Rv. 10. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवानकम्
इन्द्रः + -वानकम् A variety of diamonds. Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवायू
इन्द्रः + -वायू (du.) Indra and Vāyu. इन्द्रवायू उभाविह सुहवेह हवामहे Av. 3. 20. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणी
इन्द्रः + -वारुणी, -वारुणिका Colocynth, a wild bitter gourd cucumis colocynthis.<BR> (Mar. मोठी कंवडळ) किमिन्द्रवारुणी राम सितया कटुकीयते Laghu Yogavāsiṣṭha-sāra X.<BR> सौवर्चलं हरिद्रा च पिप्पली चेन्द्रवारुणिः ।<BR> मूत्रकृच्छ्रे प्रशंसन्ति पिण्डोऽयं वाजिनां हितः ॥ शालिहोत्र of भोज 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणिका
इन्द्रः + -वारुणी, -वारुणिका Colocynth, a wild bitter gourd cucumis colocynthis.<BR> (Mar. मोठी कंवडळ) किमिन्द्रवारुणी राम सितया कटुकीयते Laghu Yogavāsiṣṭha-sāra X.<BR> सौवर्चलं हरिद्रा च पिप्पली चेन्द्रवारुणिः ।<BR> मूत्रकृच्छ्रे प्रशंसन्ति पिण्डोऽयं वाजिनां हितः ॥ शालिहोत्र of भोज 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवाह्
इन्द्रः + -वाह् <i>a.</i> carrying Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृक्षः|इन्द्रवृक्ष
इन्द्रः + -वृक्षः the Devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृद्धा
इन्द्रः + -वृद्धा a kind of abscess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवैडूर्यम्
इन्द्रः + -वैडूर्यम् a kind of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रव्रतम्
इन्द्रः + -व्रतम् Indraʼs rule of conduct; one of the duties of a king (who<BR> is said to follow इन्द्रव्रत when he distributes benefits as Indra<BR> pours down rain); वार्षिकांश्चतुरो मासान् यथेन्द्रोऽप्यभिवर्षति । तथाभिवर्षेत्स्वं<BR> राष्ट्रं कामैरिन्द्रव्रतं चरन् ॥ Ms. 9. 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशक्तिः|इन्द्रशक्ति
इन्द्रः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> Indrāṇī, the wife of Indra, or his energy personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशत्रुः|इन्द्रशत्रु
इन्द्रः + -शत्रुः<BR>—1 an enemy or destroyer of Indra (when the accent is on the last syllable),<BR> an epithet of प्रह्लाद; इन्द्रशत्रो विवर्धस्व मा चिरं जहि विद्विषम्<BR> Bhāg. 6. 9. 12. बलिप्रदिष्टां श्रियमाददानं त्रैविकमं पादमिवेन्द्रशत्रुः R. 7. 35.<BR>—2 [इन्द्रः शत्रुः यस्य] one whose enemy is Indra, an epithet of वृत्र<BR> (when the accent is on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">Page0386-2</a>]<BR> first syllable). [This refers to a legend in the Śat. Br., where it is<BR> said that Vṛtraʼs father intended his son to become the destroyer of<BR> Indra, and asked him to say इन्द्रशत्रुर्वधस्व &c. but who, through<BR> mistake, accented the word on the first syllable, and was killed by Indra;<BR> cf. Śik. 52; मन्त्रो हीनः स्वरतो वर्णतो वा मिथ्याप्रयुक्तो न तमर्थमाह ।<BR> स वाग्वज्रो यजमानं हिनस्ति यथेन्द्रशत्रुः स्वरतोऽपराधात् ॥].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशलभः|इन्द्रशलभ
इन्द्रः + -शलभः a kind of insect (इन्द्रगोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसंजयम्
इन्द्रः + -संजयम् N. of a sāman. Ārṣeya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसंधा
इन्द्रः + -संधा connection or alliance with Indra. तयाहमिन्द्रसंधया<BR> सर्वान् देवानिह हुव Av. 11. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसारथिः|इन्द्रसारथि
इन्द्रः + -सारथिः<BR>—1 N. of Mātali.<BR>—2 an epithet of Vāyu, driving in the same carriage with Indra; Rv. 4. 46. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसावर्णिः|इन्द्रसावर्णि
इन्द्रः + -सावर्णिः N. of the fourteenth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुतः|इन्द्रसुत
इन्द्रः + -सुतः, -सूनुः<BR>—1 N. of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Jayanta;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Arjuna;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Vāli, the king of monkeys.<BR>—2 N. of the अर्जुन tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसूनुः|इन्द्रसूनु
इन्द्रः + -सुतः, -सूनुः<BR>—1 N. of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Jayanta;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Arjuna;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Vāli, the king of monkeys.<BR>—2 N. of the अर्जुन tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरसः|इन्द्रसुरस
इन्द्रः + -सुरसः, -सुरा a shrub the leaves of which are used in discutient<BR> applications (निर्गुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरा
इन्द्रः + -सुरसः, -सुरा a shrub the leaves of which are used in discutient<BR> applications (निर्गुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसेनः|इन्द्रसेन
इन्द्रः + -सेनः N. of several men; of Bali; of a mountain; Bhāg. 8. 20. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसेना
इन्द्रः + -सेना<BR>—1 Indraʼs missile or host.<BR>—2 Indraʼs army; Rv. 10. 102. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसेनानीः
इन्द्रः + -सेनानीः the leader of Indraʼs armies, epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रस्तुत्
इन्द्रः + -स्तुत् <i>m.</i>, {@-स्तोमः@}<BR>—1 praise of Indra; N. of a particular hymn addressed to Indra in certain ceremonies.<BR>—2 a sacrifice in honour of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रहवः|इन्द्रहव
इन्द्रः + -हवः invocation of Indra; भद्रान् कृण्वन्निन्द्रहवान्त्सखिभ्य Rv. 9. 96. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रहस्तः|इन्द्रहस्त
इन्द्रः + -हस्तः a kind of medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकम्
इन्द्रकम् [इन्द्रस्य राज्ञः कं सुखं यत्र Tv.] An assembly room, a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रतम
इन्द्रतम <i>a.</i> Ved. Most Indra-like, mighty, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रता
इन्द्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Power and dignity of Indra, kingship, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रत्वम्
इन्द्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Power and dignity of Indra, kingship, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रस्वत्|इन्द्रस्वन्त्
इन्द्रस्वत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Accompanied by Indra, possessed of power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयु|इंद्रयु
इन्द्रयु <i>a.</i> Longing to go to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणिका|इंद्राणिका
इन्द्राणिका The plant निर्गुंडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी [इन्द्रस्य पत्नी आनुक् डीप् P. IV. 1. 49.]<BR>—1 The wife of Indra; आजगाम सहेन्द्राण्या शकः सुरगणैर्वृतः Mb. 3. 14. 13.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā, considered as one of the eight mothers or divine energies.<BR>—3 A kind of coitus.<BR>—4 Large cardamoms.<BR>—5 N. of a tree (नीलसिंदुवार); also the plant निर्गुंडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> Fit for or belonging to or agreeable to, Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियः|इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं
इन्द्रिय + .{@-यः@} A friend or companion of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियम्
इन्द्रिय + .{@-यम्@} [इन्द्र-घ; इन्द्रेण दुर्जयम्; by P. V. 2. 93 इन्द्रियमिन्द्रलिङ्गमिन्द्रदृष्टमिन्द्रसृष्टमिन्द्रजुष्टमिन्द्रदत्तमिति वा]<BR>—1 Power, force, the quality which belongs to Indra.<BR>—2 An organ of sense, sense, or faculty of sense. (Indriyas are often<BR> compared to restive horses, which, if not properly checked, will lead one<BR> astray; cf. मा भूवन्नपथवरास्तवेन्द्रियाश्वाः Ki. 5. 50). There are<BR> two kinds of Indriyas:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) ज्ञानेन्द्रियाणि or बुद्धीन्द्रियाणि; श्रोत्रं त्वक्चक्षुषी जिह्वा<BR> नासिका चैव पञ्चमी (also मनः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">Page0387-1</a>]<BR> according to some); and<BR>——(<i>b</i>) कर्मेन्द्रियाणिः-पायूपस्थं हस्तपादं वाक् चैव दशमी स्मृता<BR> Ms. 2. 90; Ms. further adds एकादशं मनो ज्ञेयं स्वगुणेनोभयात्मकम् ।<BR> यस्मिञ् जिते जितावेतौ भवतः पञ्चकौ गणौ ॥ In the Vedanta मनः,<BR> बुद्धि, अहंकार and चित्त are said to be the four internal organs,<BR> the total number of organs being, therefore, 14, each presided over by<BR> its own ruler or नियन्तृ. In Nyāya each organ is connected with its<BR> own peculiar element; the eye, ear, tongue, nose, and skin being connected<BR> respectively with Light or fire, Ether, Water, Earth and Air.<BR>—3 Bodily or virile power, power of the sense.<BR>—4 Semen; गणिकान्नमथेन्द्रियम् Mb. 12. 36. 28.<BR>—5 Symbolical expression for the number ‘5’.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इन्द्रियागोचर, इन्द्रियार्थः, इन्द्रियासङ्गः, इन्द्रियात्मन्, इन्द्रियादिः, इन्द्रियायतनम्, इन्द्रियाराम, इन्द्रियेशः, इन्द्रियगोचर, इन्द्रियग्रामः, इन्द्रियवर्गः, इन्द्रियज, इन्द्रियज्ञानम्, इन्द्रियधारणा, इन्द्रियनिग्रहः, इन्द्रियप्रसङ्गः, इन्द्रियबुद्धिः, इन्द्रियबोधन, इन्द्रियवधः, इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्तिः, इन्द्रियवृत्तिः, इन्द्रियसंप्रयोगः, इन्द्रियसुख, इन्द्रियसन्निकर्षः, इन्द्रियस्वापः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0386-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियागोचर
इन्द्रिय + -अगोचर <i>a.</i> imperceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियार्थः|इन्द्रियार्थ
इन्द्रिय + -अर्थः<BR>—1 an object of sense; these objects are:− रूपं शब्दो गन्धरसस्पर्शाश्च<BR> विषया अमी Ak.; इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वैषौ व्यवस्थितौ Bg. 3. 34;<BR> Bh. 3. 5, 8; R. 14. 25.<BR>—2 anything exciting these senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियासङ्गः|इन्द्रियासङ्ग
इन्द्रिय + -असङ्गः non-attachment to sensual objects, stoicism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियात्मन्
इन्द्रिय + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियादिः|इन्द्रियादि
इन्द्रिय + -आदिः the principle called <i>ahaṅkāra</i> (in Sāṅ. Phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियायतनम्
इन्द्रिय + -आयतनम्<BR>—1 the abode of the senses, <i>i. e.</i> the body.<BR>—2 the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियाराम
इन्द्रिय + -आराम <i>a.</i> given to enjoying the objects of sense; अघायुरिन्द्रियारामो<BR> मोघं पार्थ स जीवति Bg. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियेशः|इन्द्रियेश
इन्द्रिय + -ईशः the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियगोचर|इन्द्रियगोचरः
इन्द्रिय + -गोचर <i>a.</i> perceptible to the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियगोचरः|इन्द्रियगोचर
इन्द्रिय + -गोचर + .({@-रः@}) an object of sense; पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचराः Bg. 13. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियग्रामः|इन्द्रियग्राम
इन्द्रिय + -ग्रामः, -वर्गः the assemblage or collection of organs, the five<BR> organs of sense taken collectively; बलवानिन्द्रियग्रामो विद्वांसमपि<BR> कर्षति Ms. 2. 215, 100, 175; निर्ववार मधुनीन्द्रियवर्गः Śi. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवर्गः|इन्द्रियवर्ग
इन्द्रिय + -ग्रामः, -वर्गः the assemblage or collection of organs, the five<BR> organs of sense taken collectively; बलवानिन्द्रियग्रामो विद्वांसमपि<BR> कर्षति Ms. 2. 215, 100, 175; निर्ववार मधुनीन्द्रियवर्गः Śi. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियज
इन्द्रिय + -ज <i>a.</i> in oneʼs presence, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियज्ञानम्
इन्द्रिय + -ज्ञानम् consciousness, the faculty of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियधारणा
इन्द्रिय + -धारणा restraint of senses; स्थिरामिन्द्रियधारणाम् Kaṭh. 2. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियनिग्रहः|इन्द्रियनिग्रह
इन्द्रिय + -निग्रहः restraint of senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियप्रसङ्गः|इन्द्रियप्रसङ्ग
इन्द्रिय + -प्रसङ्गः sensuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबुद्धिः|इन्द्रियबुद्धि
इन्द्रिय + -बुद्धिः <i>f.</i> perception by the senses, exercise of any organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबोधन
इन्द्रिय + -बोधन <i>a.</i> exciting power; stimulating or sharpening the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबोधनम्
इन्द्रिय + -बोधन + .({@-नम्@}) any excitement of senses, a stimulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवधः|इन्द्रियवध
इन्द्रिय + -वधः insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्तिः|इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति
इन्द्रिय + -विप्रतिपत्तिः <i>f.</i> perversion of the organs, wrong preception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवृत्तिः|इन्द्रियवृत्ति
इन्द्रिय + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> function of the organs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियसंप्रयोगः|इन्द्रियसम्प्रयोग
इन्द्रिय + -संप्रयोगः Functioning of senses with reference to objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियसुख
इन्द्रिय + -सुख sensual pleasures; एवमिन्द्रियसुखानि निर्विशन्नन्यकार्यविमुखः<BR> स पार्थिवः R. 19. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियसन्निकर्षः|इन्द्रियसन्निकर्ष
इन्द्रिय + -सन्निकर्षः the contact of an organ of sense (either with its<BR> object or with the mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियस्वापः|इन्द्रियस्वाप
इन्द्रिय + -स्वापः insensibility, unconsciousness, stupor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवत्|इन्द्रियवन्त्
इन्द्रियवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who has curbed his senses.<BR>—2 One having the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध्|इंध्
इन्ध् €7 Ā. (इन्द्धे or इन्धे, इन्धाञ्चक्रे, ऐन्धिष्ट, इद्ध) To kindle,<BR> light, set on fire; वयं त्वेन्धानास्तन्वं पुषेम Av. 5. 3. 1. ━<i>pass.</i><BR> (इध्यते) To be lighted, blaze, flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध <i>p. p.</i> [इन्ध्-क्त]<BR>—1 Kindled, lighted; रामस्य त्रिपुरान्तकृद्दिविषदां तेजोभिरिद्धं धनुः<BR> Mv. 1. 53; क्रोध˚ Ratn. 1. 3; Mu. 1. 2; ˚राग Ś. 7. 16 whose glow<BR> or red colour has just broken out.<BR>—2 Shining, glowing, blazing, bright;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">Page0387-2</a>]<BR> तन्वन्तमिद्धमभितो गुरुमंशुजालम् Ki. 2. 59; Śi. 1. 63; ˚बोधै<BR> Bk. 1. 5 (पटुबुद्धिभिः) sharp.<BR>—3 Clean, clear.<BR>—4 Wonderful.<BR>—5 Obeyed, unresisted (as order); ˚शासनः Ki. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्धम्
इद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 Sunshine, heat.<BR>—2 Refulgence, splendour.<BR>—3 Wonder.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इद्धदीधितिः, इद्धमन्यु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्धदीधितिः|इद्धदीधिति
इद्ध + -दीधितिः fire; कुरुते न खलु स्वयेच्छया शलभानिन्धनमिद्धदीधितिः Śi. 16. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्धमन्यु
इद्ध + -मन्यु <i>a.</i> having the anger excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मः|इध्म|इध्मं
इध्मः [इध्यतेऽग्निरनेन इन्ध्-मक्] Fuel, especially that used for<BR> the sacred fire; ग्रीष्म इध्मः शरद्धविः Rv. 10. 90. 6; तत्रेध्मानयने<BR> शको नियुक्तः कश्यपेन ह Mb. 1. 31. 6; R. 14. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मम्
इध्मः + .{@-ध्मम्@} Wood, fuel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इध्मजिह्वः, इध्मप्रव्रश्चनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मजिह्वः|इध्मजिह्व
इध्मः + -जिह्वः fire; Bhāg. 5. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मप्रव्रश्चनः|इध्मप्रव्रश्चन
इध्मः + -प्रव्रश्चनः a hatchet, an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्या
इध्या <i>f.</i> Kindling, lighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध|इंध|इन्धः
इन्ध <i>a.</i> [इन्ध्-अच्] Kindling, lighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धः|इन्ध|इंध
इन्ध + .{@-धः@} [इन्ध्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Fuel.<BR>—2 The Supreme Being; इन्धो ह वै नामैष योऽयं दक्षिणेऽक्षन्पुरुषः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 4. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन|इंधन|इन्धनं
इन्धन <i>a.</i> [इन्ध्-णिच्-ल्युट्] Kindling, lighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धनम्
इन्धन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Kindling, lighting,<BR>—2 Fuel, wood &c.; शोकानलेन्धनताम् K. 169.<BR>—3 Expectation, desire (वासना); ये तु दग्धेन्धना लोके पुण्यपापविवर्जिताः<BR> Mb. 12. 348. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धनवत्|इन्धनवन्त्
इन्धनवत् <i>a.</i> Possessed of fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन्वन्
इन्धन्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved. possessed of fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्व्
इन्व् €6 P.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To pervade, surround.<BR>—3 To seize, take possession of.<BR>—4 To invigorate, gladden; see इन् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वकाः
इन्वकाः Stars in the head of Orion. (See इल्वकाः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभः|इभ
इभः [इ-भन्-किच्च Uṇ. 3. 151]<BR>—1 An elephant.<BR>—2 Fearless power (Sāy.).<BR>—3 Servants, dependents (Ved.)<BR>—4 The number eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभी
इभः + .{@-भी@} A female elephant. [cf. L. <i>ebur</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इभारिः, इभाख्यः, इभकेशरा, इभाननः, इभोषणा, इभकणा, इभकर्णकः, इभगन्धा, इभदन्ता, इभनिमीलिका, इभपालकः, इभपोटा, इभपोतः, इभभरः, इभयुवतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभारिः|इभारि
इभः + -अरिः a lion दृष्ट्वा मृधे गरुडवाहमिभारिवाहः Bhāg. 8. 11. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभाख्यः|इभाख्य
इभः + -आख्यः, -केशरा the plant नागकेशर Mesua ferrea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभकेशरा
इभः + -आख्यः, -केशरा the plant नागकेशर Mesua ferrea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभाननः|इभानन
इभः + -आननः N. of Gaṇeśa; cf. गजानन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभोषणा
इभः + -उषणा, -कणा a kind of aromatic plant, Scindapsus officinalis<BR> गजपिप्पली (Mar. गजपिंपळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभकणा
इभः + -उषणा, -कणा a kind of aromatic plant, Scindapsus officinalis<BR> गजपिप्पली (Mar. गजपिंपळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभकर्णकः
इभः + -कर्णकः N. of a plant (Mar. तांबडा एरंड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभगन्धा
इभः + -गन्धा N. of a plant (the fruit of which is poisonous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभदन्ता
इभः + -दन्ता <i>f.</i> The plant Tiaridium Indicum (Mar. भुरुंडी, नागदवणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभनिमीलिका
इभः + -निमीलिका<BR>—1 shrewdness, sagacity, sharpness.<BR>—2 hemp (भङ्गा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपालकः|इभपालक
इभः + -पालकः the driver or keeper of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपोटा
इभः + -पोटा [पोटा पुंल्लक्षणा इभी] a hermaphrodite female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपोतः|इभपोत
इभः + -पोतः a young elephant, a cub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभभरः|इभभर
इभः + -भरः a collection of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभयुवतिः|इभयुवति
इभः + -युवतिः <i>f.</i> a female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभमाचलः|इभमाचल
इभमाचलः [इभमाचलयति] A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभया
इभया N. of the tree स्वर्णक्षीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य <i>a.</i> [इभं गजमर्हति यत्]<BR>—1 Wealthy, opulent, rich; Dk. 41.<BR>—2 Belonging to oneʼs servants (Ved.). भ्रातेव स्वस्रामिभ्यान्न राजा Rv. 1. 65. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्यः|इभ्य
इभ्य + .{@-भ्यः@} —1 A king. Ch. Up. 1. 10. 1.<BR>—2 An elephant-driver.<BR>—3 An enemy or foe (Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्या
इभ्य + .{@-भ्या@}<BR>—1 A female elephant.<BR>—2 N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">Page0388-1</a>]<BR> Olibanum tree, Boswellia Serrata (Mar. कवड्या ऊद).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इभ्यतिल्विल, इभ्यतिल्वल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्यतिल्विल
इभ्य + -तिल्विल, -तिल्वल <i>a.</i> wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्यतिल्वल
इभ्य + -तिल्विल, -तिल्वल <i>a.</i> wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्यक
इभ्यक a Wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इमथा
इमथा <i>ind.</i> Ved. As here, as now, in this way or manner; तं<BR> प्रत्नथा पूर्वया विश्वथेमथा Rv. 5. 44. 1. cf. P. V. 3. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयक्षु
इयक्षु <i>a.</i> Ved. Longing for, seeking to gain; इयक्षवे पूरवे<BR> प्रत्न राजन् Rv. 10. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्|इयन्त्
इयत् <i>a.</i> —1 So much, so large, of this extent; इयत्तवायुः<BR> Dk. 93; इयन्ति वर्षाणि तया सहोग्रम् R. 13. 67 so many years; द्वयं<BR> नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30 this much; इयतो दिवसानुत्सव आसीत् U. 1.<BR> इयदिति गुरुजनसविधे विधृतधनिष्ठापयोधरः पायात् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्ता
इयत्ता, इयत्त्वम्<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) So much, fixed measure or quantity; ईदृक्तया रूपमियत्तया<BR> वा R. 13. 5; न … यशः परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालम् 6. 77; K. 129, 182.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Limited number, limitation; न गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>—2 Limit, standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्त्वम्
इयत्ता, इयत्त्वम्<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) So much, fixed measure or quantity; ईदृक्तया रूपमियत्तया<BR> वा R. 13. 5; न … यशः परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालम् 6. 77; K. 129, 182.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Limited number, limitation; न गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>—2 Limit, standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्तक
इयत्तक <i>a.</i> So small, very small. इयत्तिका शकुन्तिका सका जघास<BR> ते विषम् Rv. 1. 191. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्तका
इयत्तक + .{@-का@} A bad limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयस्
इयस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयसा
इयसा Ved. Low spirits, dejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्
इर् €6 P. (इरति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्य
इरज्य Ved. (इरज्यति-ते)<BR>—1 To grow.<BR>—2 To be jealous.<BR>—3 To order, prepare; arrange, dispose of.<BR>—4 To be master of.<BR>—5 To lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्यु
इरज्यु <i>a.</i> Ved. Engaged in preparations for the sacrificial rite;<BR> विश्वेषामिरज्यवो देवानां वार्महः Rv. 10. 93. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरणम्
इरणम्<BR>—1 A desert.<BR>—2 Salt or barren ground; cf. इरिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरम्मद|इरंमद|इरम्मदः
इरम्मद <i>a.</i> [cf. P. III. 2. 37] Delighting in drinking, an epithet<BR> of Agni; इरम्मदं वृहदुक्थं यजत्रम् Vāj. 11. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरम्मदः|इरम्मद|इरंमद
इरम्मद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 A flash of lightning, the fire attending the fall of a thunderbolt;<BR> इरम्मदमिव मेघमालाऽसूत K. 70.<BR>—2 The submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्यति
इरस्यति Ved.<BR>—1 To behave insolently, be angry.<BR>—2 (With dat.) To be ill-affected towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्या
इरस्या<BR>—1 Ill will, malevolence; इरस्या द्रुग्धो भियसा नि गारीत् Rv. 5. 40. 7.<BR>—2 Wish for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा [इ-रन् Uṇ. 2. 28; इं कामं राति रा-क वा Tv.] (‘इरा तु मदिरावारिभारत्यशनभूमिषु’ इति विश्वलोचनः)<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 Speech.<BR>—3 The goddess of speech, Sarasvatī,<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 Food; इरावतीं धारिणीं भूधराणाम् Mb. 13. 26. 95.<BR>—6 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—7 Any drinkable fluid; a draught (especially of milk).<BR>—8 Refreshment, comfort (Ved. in the last three senses).<BR>—9 N. of one of the wives of Kaśyapa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इरेशः, इराक्षीर, इराचर, इराजः, इरावेल्लिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरेशः|इरेश
इरा + -ईशः<BR>—1 N. of Varuṇa, of Viṣṇu, of Gaṇeśa and of Brahman; इतीरेशेऽतर्क्ये<BR> निजमहिमनि स्वप्रमितिके Bhāg. 10. 13. 57.<BR>—2 a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराक्षीर|इराक्षीरः
इरा + -क्षीर <i>a.</i> Ved. whose milk is a refreshment<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">Page0388-2</a>]<BR> or enjoyment; यज्ञपदीराक्षीरा स्वधाप्राणा महीलुका Av. 10. 10. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराक्षीरः|इराक्षीर
इरा + -क्षीर + .({@-रः@}) the milk ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराचर|इराचरं
इरा + -चर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 earth-born, terrestrial.<BR>—2 aquatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराचरम्
इरा + -चर + .({@-रम्@}) hail; so इरावरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराजः|इराज
इरा + -जः N. of Kāma or Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावेल्लिका
इरा + -वेल्लिका pimples on the head or, pimples on the face produced<BR> at the time of puberty (Mar. मुरुमाची पुटकुळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावत्|इरावन्त्
इरावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Granting drink or refreshment, satiating.<BR>—2 Endowed with provisions, comfortable. आत्मा हि जज्ञ आत्मनः स इरावत्यतितारिणी<BR> Ait. Br. VII. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावान्
इरावत् + .({@-वान्@}) <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Ocean.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 A king.<BR>—4 N. of a son of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावती
इरावत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 N. of a river in the Panjab (रावी).<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR>—3 N. of Durgā, Rudraʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिका
इरिका N. of a plant or tree. ˚वनम् a grove of such trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिणम्
इरिणम् [ऋ-इनच्-किदिच्च Uṇ. 2. 51.]<BR>—1 A salt-ground, saline soil; यथेरिणे बीजमुप्त्वा न वप्ता लभते फलम्<BR> Ms. 3. 142; Y. 1. 151.<BR>—2 Hence, a bare or barren soil, desert, dreary region.<BR>—3 Non-support.<BR>—4 A rivulet, well (Ved.).<BR>—5 A hollow, hole.<BR>—6 A dice-board; प्रवातेजा इरिणे वर्वृताना Rv. 10. 34. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिणः|इरिण|इरिणं
इरिणम् + .{@-णः@} Calamus Scriptorious (Mar. बोरू), Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण्य
इरिण्य <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to a desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिन्
इरिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Instigating.<BR>—2 Powerful, violent, an instigator; न येषामिरी सधस्थ ईष्ट आँ Rv. 5. 87. 3.<BR>—3 A proud or overbearing fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिमेदः|इरिमेद
इरिमेदः = अरिमेद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिम्बिठिः|इरिम्बिठि
इरिम्बिठिः <i>m.</i> N. of a Ṛṣi of the family of Kaṇva (author of<BR> several hynms of the Ṛgveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिविल्ला
इरिविल्ला or इरिविल्लिका Pimples on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिविल्लिका
इरिविल्ला or इरिविल्लिका Pimples on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्गलम्
इर्गलम्, -ला<BR> = अर्गल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्गला
इर्गलम्, -ला<BR> = अर्गल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्य|इर्य्य
इर्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Instigating (प्रेरक).<BR>—2 Destroying the enemies.<BR>—3 A lord, master.<BR>—4 Active, powerful, an epithet of Pūṣan and of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारु|इर्वारुः|इर्व्वारु|इर्व्वारुः
इर्वारु, -लु <i>a.</i><BR> Destructive, carnivorous (हिंसक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वालु|इर्व्वालु|इर्व्वालुः
इर्वारु, -लु <i>a.</i><BR> Destructive, carnivorous (हिंसक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारुः|इर्वारु|इर्व्वारु|इर्व्वारुः
इर्वारु, -लु + .{@-रुः@} <i>m., f.</i> A cucumber.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इर्वारुशुक्तिका, इर्वालुशुक्तिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारुशुक्तिका|इर्व्वारुशुक्तिका
इर्वारु + इर्वारुशुक्तिका, इर्वालुशुक्तिका a kind of melon (Mar. खरबूज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वालुशुक्तिका
इर्वारु + इर्वारुशुक्तिका, इर्वालुशुक्तिका a kind of melon (Mar. खरबूज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारुकः|इर्वारुक
इर्वारुकः An animal living in caves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्
इल् €6 P. (इलति, इयेल, ऐलीत्, एलितुम्, इलित) or €10 U. (इलयति<BR> or एलयति, ऐलयीत् or ऐलिलत्)<BR>—1 To go, to move.<BR>—2 To sleep.<BR>—3 To throw, send, cast.<BR>—4 To keep still, not to move.<BR>—5 To become quiet. [cf. Germ. <i>Eile</i>, Gr. <i>elao</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलय
इलय <i>a.</i> Motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलव|इलवः
इलव <i>a.</i> Ved. Loud, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलवः|इलव
इलव + .{@-वः@} A ploughman, boor; Ait. Br. 5. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलविला
इलविला N. of the wife of Viśravas and mother of Kubera; (hence<BR> the name ऐलविल for Kubera). See under इडबिडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल
इल <i>a.</i> [इल्-क] Sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 The earth; पुष्टिकाम इलां यजेत् Bhāg. 2. 3. 5.<BR>—2 A cow; Bhāg. 3. 18. 19.<BR>—3 Speech; Bhāg. 10. 13. 64 &c.; see इडा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इलगोलः, इलगोलम्, इलतलम्, इलधरः, इलवृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलगोलः
इल + -गोलः, -गोलम् the earth, the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलगोलम्
इल + -गोलः, -गोलम् the earth, the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलतलम्
इल + -तलम्<BR>—1 the fourth place in the circle of the zodiac.<BR>—2 the surface of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलधरः
इल + -धरः a mountain; गगनार्णवमन्तरा सुमेरोः कुलजानां गरुडैरिलाधराणाम् Śi. 20. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलवृत्तम्
इल + -वृत्तम् one of the nine Varṣas or divisions of the known world;<BR> पश्चान्माल्यवतः प्राच्यां गन्धमादनशैलतः । इलावृतं नीलगिरेर्याम्यतो<BR> निषधादुदक् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिः
इलिः <i>f.</i> = इली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिका
इलिका<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 The middle arch of a niche; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिनी
इलिनी N. of the daughter of मेधातिथि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इली
इली [इल्-क ङीष्] A cudgel, a stick shaped like a sword, a short<BR> sword (करवाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीबिशः|इलीबिश
इलीबिशः N. of a demon conquered by Indra; न्याविध्यदिलीबिशस्य<BR> दृह्ळा Rv. 1. 33. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीशः|इलीश
इलीशः, इल्लिशः A sort of fish, commonly hilsa or sable.<BR> इलीशोचितपीयूषो वाचा वाचामगोचरः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लिशः|इल्लिश
इलीशः, इल्लिशः A sort of fish, commonly hilsa or sable.<BR> इलीशोचितपीयूषो वाचा वाचामगोचरः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्यः|इल्य
इल्यः N. of a mythical tree in the other world; स आगच्छतील्यं<BR> वृक्षम् Kauṣ. Up. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वकाः
इल्वकाः, -लाः (<i>pl.</i>)<BR> N. of the five stars in the head of Orion (मृगशिरस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वलाः
इल्वकाः, -लाः (<i>pl.</i>)<BR> N. of the five stars in the head of Orion (मृगशिरस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Like, as (showing उपमा or comparison); वागर्थाविव संपृक्तौ<BR> R. 1. 1; वैनतेय इव विनतानन्दनः K. 5.<BR>—2 As if, as it were (denoting उत्प्रेक्षा); पश्यामीव पिनाकिनम्<BR> Ś. 1. 6. लिम्पतीव तमोङ्गानि वर्षतीवाञ्जनं नभः Mk. 1. 34.<BR>—3 Little, somewhat, perhaps; कडार इवायम् G. M.<BR>—4 (Added to interrogative words), ‘Possibly’, ‘I should like to know’,<BR> ‘indeed’; विना सीतादेव्या किमिव हि न दुःखं रघुपतेः U. 6. 30; {@क इव@}<BR> of what sort, what-like; क इव कालः Māl. 2; what a long<BR> time has elapsed.<BR>—5 इव is frequently used with adverbs, especially with such as involve<BR> restriction, by way of emphasis in the sense of even or just so, just,<BR> exactly, quite, indeed, very; मुहूर्तमिव but for a moment; किंचिदिव<BR> just a little bit; so ईषदिव, नाचिरादिव, &c.; (इव is considered<BR> by grammarians as forming compounds with the word after which it stands;<BR> इवेन समासो विभक्त्यलोपश्च Vārt. on P. II. 4. 71. Sk.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इवोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इवोपमा
इव + -उपमा <i>f.</i> A simile in which इव is used. Bk. 10. 41 is<BR> given as an illustration of इवोपमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इशीका
इशीका A pupil in the elephantʼs eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् I. €6 P. (इच्छति, इयेष, ऐषीत्, एषितुम्-एष्टुम्, इष्ट)<BR>—1 To wish, desire, long for; इच्छामि संवर्धितमाज्ञया ते Ku. 3. 3;<BR> oft. with pot. or imperat. mood; इच्छामि भुञ्जीत or भुङ्क्तां भवान्;<BR> भुञ्जीयेतीच्छति Sk.<BR>—2 To choose; मूत्रेण मौण्ड्यमिच्छेत् तु क्षत्रियो दण्डमेव वा Ms. 8. 384.<BR>—3 To endeavour to obtain, strive or seek for; भूतिमिच्छता, स्वर्गम् &c.<BR>—4 To be willing, be about to do anything, mean or intend (with inf.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">Page0389-2</a>]<BR>—5 To ask or expect anything (acc.) from any one (loc. or abl.); देवेषु<BR> यज्ञे भागमीषिरे Śat. Br.<BR>—6 To acknowledge, regard.<BR>—7 To request, ask.<BR>—8 To be favourable.<BR>—9 To try to make favourable.<BR>—10 To assent or consent. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be wished or liked.<BR>—2 To be asked, or requested.<BR>—3 To be prescribed or laid down; हस्तच्छेदनमिष्यते Ms. 8. 322;<BR> त्रिरात्रं दशरात्रं वा शावमाशौचमिष्यते Y. 3. 18.<BR>—4 To be approved, accepted, or regarded as जम्भो दन्तेऽपि चेष्यते<BR> Trik. ━II. €4 P. (इष्यति इयेष एषिष्यति, एषितुम्)<BR>—1 To move; to cause to move; केनेषितं पतति प्रेषितं मनः Ken. 1.<BR> येनषिता वागसवश्चरन्ति Bhāg. 11. 28. 35.<BR>—2 To let fly, cast, throw.<BR>—3 To raise (as oneʼs voice).<BR>—4 To sprinkle. ━III. €9 P. (इष्णाति)<BR>—1 To cause to move quickly, let fly, cast.<BR>—2 To fly off, escape.<BR>—3 To strike, smite; न वेद खं गां च परिश्रमेषितः Bhāg. 12. 9. 16.<BR>—4 To impel, urge, incite, animate, promote.<BR>—5 To perform frequently; इष्णाति वैष्णवो व्रतम् ━IV. €1 U. (एषति-ते,<BR> ऐषीत्-ऐषिष्ट) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक <i>a.</i> Wishing, desiring &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छकः|इच्छक
इच्छक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 (In Arith.) The sum sought.<BR>—2 N. of a tree; Shaddock, which is a large species of orange; citrus,<BR> Medica (Mar. महाळुंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्
इच्छत् <i>pres. p.</i> Wishing, desirous, willing; अनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय<BR> बलादिव नियोजितः Bg. 3. 36. अनिच्छतोऽपि तस्य against his will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छा [इष् भावे श]<BR>—1 Wish, desire, inclination of mind, will; इच्छया according to oneʼs<BR> desire, at will.<BR>—2 Willingness.<BR>—3 (In Math.) A question or problem. —4 (In gram.) The form of the Desiderative.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इच्छादानम्, इच्छानिवृत्तिः, इच्छाफलम्, इच्छारतम्, इच्छारूपम्, इच्छावसु, इच्छासंपद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छादानम्
इच्छा + -दानम् fulfilment of a wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छानिवृत्तिः|इच्छानिवृत्ति
इच्छा + -निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> suppression of desire, indifference to worldly desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छाफलम्
इच्छा + -फलम् the solution of a question or problem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छारतम्
इच्छा + -रतम् desired sports, favourite pastimes; नीता रात्रिः क्षणमिव<BR> मया सार्धमिच्छारतैर्या Me. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छारूपम्
इच्छा + -रूपम्<BR>—1 Desire (personified).<BR>—2 The first manifestation of divine power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छावसु|इच्छावसुः
इच्छा + -वसु <i>a.</i> ‘possessing wealth according to wish’, epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छासंपद्|इच्छासम्पद्
इच्छा + -संपद् <i>f.</i> fulfilment of oneʼs wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छु|इच्छुः
इच्छु <i>a.</i> [बिन्दुरिच्छुः P. III. 2. 169.] Wishing, desirous;<BR> usually in comp. इच्छुः कामयितुं त्वं माम् … Bk. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छुक|इच्छुकः
इच्छुक <i>a.</i> Wishing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Speedy, going quickly.<BR>—2 Wishing, desirous. <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A draught, refreshment, food; वनस्पतीनोषधीश्च ससर्जोर्जमिषं<BR> विभुः Bhāg. 6. 4. 8.<BR>—2 Libation; नम ऊर्ज इषे त्रय्याः पतये यज्ञरेतसे Bhāg. 4. 24. 38.<BR>—3 Strength, power, sap, freshness.<BR>—4 Comfort; increase.<BR>—5 Affluence.<BR>—6 Refreshing waters of the sky.<BR>—7 Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषः|इष
इषः<BR>—1 One possessed of sap or strength.<BR>—2 The month आश्विन; … ध्वनिमिषेऽनिमिषेक्षणमग्रतः Śi. 6. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणयते
इषणयते Den. Ā. To move, excite; इयानास इषणयन्त धीभिः Rv. 10. 67. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणिः|इषणि
इषणिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Sending, despatching.<BR>—2 Wish, desire, impulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्यति
इषण्यति Den. P. To excite, drive, urge on; ऋतस्य बुध्न उषसामिषण्यन् Rv. 3. 61. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्या
इषण्या Impulse, desire; इषण्यया नः पुरुरूपमाभर Rv. 8. 60. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषयति
इषयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To be juicy.<BR>—2 To swell, increase.<BR>—3 To be fresh or active.<BR>—4 To animate, strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषव्य
इषव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 (The object) of aim.<BR>—2 Skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषि
इषि <i>a.</i> [इष्-कि] Wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषित
इषित <i>p. p.</i> (fr. इष् €4 cl.)<BR>—1 Moved, driven, sent, despatched.<BR>—2 Excited, animated.<BR>—3 Quick, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिर|इषिरः
इषिर <i>a.</i> Ved. [इष्-गतौ-किरच्]<BR>—1 Juicy, succulent, refreshing, fresh.<BR>—2 Powerful, strong, quick, active. —3 Moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिरः|इषिर
इषिर + .{@-रः@} Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिरम्
इषिर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Quickly. स्वधामिषिरां पर्यपश्यन् Rv. 10. 157. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
इष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [इष् इच्छायां कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Wished, desired, longed for, wished for; उपपन्नो गुणैरिष्टैः Nala. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Beloved, agreeable, liked, favourite, dear; ˚आत्मजः Mu. 2. 8 fond of sons.<BR>—3 Worshipped, reverenced.<BR>—4 Respected.<BR>—5 Approved, regarded as good.<BR>—6 Desirable; see इष्टापूर्त.<BR>—6 Valid.<BR>—7 Sacrificed, worshipped with sacrifices.<BR>—8 Supposed (कल्पित); oft. used in Līlavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टः|इष्ट|इष्टं
इष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@}<BR>—1 A lover, husband, beloved person; इष्टप्रवासजनितानि Ś. 4. 3.<BR>—2 A friend; इष्टानामिष्टकर्मकृत् Pt. 1. 57, 2. 172.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (एरंड).<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टा
इष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@} N. of a tree (शमी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टम्
इष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Wish, desire.<BR>—2 A holy ceremony or संस्कार. एतदिष्टं प्रवृत्ताख्यम् Bhāg. 7. 15. 49.<BR>—3 A sacrifice; Bṛ. Up. 4. 1. 2; see इष्टापूर्त. ━<i>ind.</i> Voluntarily.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इष्टार्थः, इष्टापत्तिः, इष्टकर्मन्, इष्टकापथः, इष्टकामदुह्, इष्टगन्ध, इष्टजनः, इष्टदेवः, इष्टदेवता, इष्टभागिन्, इष्टयामन्, इष्टव्रत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टार्थः|इष्टार्थ
इष्ट + -अर्थः desired object. ˚उद्युक्त <i>a.</i> zealously engaged in<BR> gaining oneʼs desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापत्तिः|इष्टापत्ति
इष्ट + -आपत्तिः <i>f.</i> occurrence of what is desired; a statement by<BR> a debater which is favourable to his opponent also; इष्टापत्तौ दोषान्तरमाह Jag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकर्मन्|इष्टकर्म्मन्
इष्ट + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> (In Arith.) rule of supposition, operation with<BR> an assumed number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकापथः|इष्टकापथ|इष्टकापथं
इष्ट + -कापथः the root of a fragrant grass (वीरणमूल; Mar. वाळा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकामदुह्
इष्ट + -कामदुह् <i>a.</i> granting the desired objects, an epithet of the<BR> cow of plenty; एष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक् Bg. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टगन्ध|इष्टगन्धं|इष्टगन्धः
इष्ट + -गन्ध <i>a.</i> fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टगन्धः|इष्टगन्ध|इष्टगन्धं
इष्ट + -गन्ध + .({@-धः@}) any fragrant substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टगन्धम्
इष्ट + -गन्ध + .({@-धम्@}) sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टजनः|इष्टजन
इष्ट + -जनः a beloved person (whether man or woman); U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेवः|इष्टदेव
इष्ट + -देवः, -देवता a favourite god, oneʼs tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेवता
इष्ट + -देवः, -देवता a favourite god, oneʼs tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टभागिन्
इष्ट + -भागिन् <i>a.</i> One who has attained his object; अपूजयन्राघवमिष्टभागिनम्<BR> Rām. 6. 67. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टयामन्
इष्ट + -यामन् <i>a.</i> going according to oneʼs desire. वायुर्न यो नियुत्वाँ<BR> इष्टयामा Rv. 9. 88. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टव्रत
इष्ट + -व्रत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 performing desired vows.<BR>—2 obeying oneʼs wish.<BR>—3 (food &c.) for the fulfilment of a vow.<BR>—4 that by which good works succeed. इष इष्टव्रता अकः Rv. 3. 59. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका N. of a deity (Nārā. Up. 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्तम्
इष्टापूर्तम्, इष्टापूर्तिः <i>f.</i> [इष्टं च पूर्तं च तयोः<BR> समाहारः पूर्वपददीर्घत्वम्] Performance of pious or charitable deeds;<BR> performing sacrifices, and digging wells and doing other acts of charity;<BR> इष्टापूर्तविधेः सपत्नशमनात् Mv. 3. 1; cf. also इष्टापूर्ते पुत्रपशूंश्च<BR> सर्वान् Kaṭh. 1. 8. वापीकूपतडागादिदेवतायतनानि च । अन्नप्रदानमारामाः<BR> पूर्तमर्थ्याः प्रचक्षते ॥ एकाग्निकर्महवनं त्रेतायां यच्च हूयते ।<BR> अन्तर्वेद्यां च यद्दानमिष्टं तदभिधीयते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्तिः|इष्टापूर्ति
इष्टापूर्तम्, इष्टापूर्तिः <i>f.</i> [इष्टं च पूर्तं च तयोः<BR> समाहारः पूर्वपददीर्घत्वम्] Performance of pious or charitable deeds;<BR> performing sacrifices, and digging wells and doing other acts of charity;<BR> इष्टापूर्तविधेः सपत्नशमनात् Mv. 3. 1; cf. also इष्टापूर्ते पुत्रपशूंश्च<BR> सर्वान् Kaṭh. 1. 8. वापीकूपतडागादिदेवतायतनानि च । अन्नप्रदानमारामाः<BR> पूर्तमर्थ्याः प्रचक्षते ॥ एकाग्निकर्महवनं त्रेतायां यच्च हूयते ।<BR> अन्तर्वेद्यां च यद्दानमिष्टं तदभिधीयते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिः|इष्टि
इष्टिः <i>f.</i> [इष्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Wish, request, desire.<BR>—2 Seeking, striving to get.<BR>—3 Any desired object.<BR>—4 A desired rule or desideratum; (a term used with reference to Patañjaliʼs<BR> additions to Kātyāyanaʼs Vārttikas; इष्टयो भाष्यकारस्य, इति भाष्यकारेष्टया<BR> &c.; cf. उपसंख्यान).<BR>—5 Impulse, hurry.<BR>—6 Invitation, order.<BR>—7 (यज्-क्तिन्) A sacrifice. Ms. 11. 2. 20. शबर seems to interpret<BR> the word especially in the sense of ‘a दर्शपूर्णमास sacrifice’.<BR> इष्टिराजसूयचातुर्मास्येषु । &c. MS. 11. 2. 12.<BR>—8 An oblation consisting of butter, food &c.<BR>—9 Summary in verses (= संग्रहश्लोक). एभिर्यज्ञेभिस्तदभीष्टिमश्याम्<BR> Rv. 1. 166. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इष्ट्ययनम्, इष्टिपचः, इष्टिपशु, इष्टिश्राद्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट्ययनम्
इष्टिः + -अयनम् a sacrifice lasting for a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपचः|इष्टिपच
इष्टिः + -पचः<BR>—1 a miser.<BR>—2 a demon; an Asura; so ˚मुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपशु
इष्टिः + -पशु an animal to be killed at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिश्राद्धम्
इष्टिः + -श्राद्धम् A particular funeral rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टुः|इष्टु
इष्टुः <i>f.</i> A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म <i>a.</i> [इष्-इच्छायां कर्मणि मक्] Wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्मः|इष्म
इष्म + .{@-ष्मः@}<BR>—1 Cupid, god of love.<BR>—2 The spring.<BR>—3 Course, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्मिन्
इष्मिन् <i>a.</i> Speedy, impetuous, an epithet of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्यः|इष्य|इष्यं
इष्यः, -ष्यम्<BR> [इष्-क्यप्] The spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्यम्
इष्यः, -ष्यम्<BR> [इष्-क्यप्] The spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिका
इषि(षी)का [इष् गत्यादौ क्वुन् अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 Reed, rush, stalk of grass; कुशकाशशरेषिकाः Rām.; Kaṭh. 2. 6. 17.<BR> ˚अस्त्रम् R. 12. 23.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR>—3 A sort of sugar-cane; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—4 A small stick of wood or iron used to see whether gold in a crucible<BR> is melted or not.<BR>—5 A brush.<BR>—6 The eye-ball of an elephant.<BR>—7 A thorny plant; संनिकर्षादिषीकाभिर्मोचितः परमाद्भयात् Rām. 2. 8. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इषिकातूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीका
इषि(षी)का [इष् गत्यादौ क्वुन् अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 Reed, rush, stalk of grass; कुशकाशशरेषिकाः Rām.; Kaṭh. 2. 6. 17.<BR> ˚अस्त्रम् R. 12. 23.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR>—3 A sort of sugar-cane; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—4 A small stick of wood or iron used to see whether gold in a crucible<BR> is melted or not.<BR>—5 A brush.<BR>—6 The eye-ball of an elephant.<BR>—7 A thorny plant; संनिकर्षादिषीकाभिर्मोचितः परमाद्भयात् Rām. 2. 8. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इषिकातूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिकातूलम्
इषिका + -तूलम् also इषीकतूलम् the point or upper part of a reed;<BR> इष्टकेषीकामालानां चिततूलभारिषु P. VI. 3. 35; यथेषीकातूलग्नौ प्रोतम्<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 24. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुः|इषु
इषुः <i>m., f.</i> [इष्-उ; cf. also Uṇ. 1. 13]<BR>—1 An arrow; यामिषुं … हस्ते बिभर्षि Śvet. Up. 3. 6; इषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि Bg. 2. 4.<BR>—2 The number five.<BR>—3 (In Math.) A versed sine.<BR>—4 N. of a Soma ceremony.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इष्वग्रम्, इष्वनीकम्, इष्वसनम्, इष्वस्त्रम्, इष्वास, इषुकारः, इषुकृत्, इषुधरः, इषुभृत्, इषुपथः, इषुविक्षेपः, इषुपातरामक्षेत्रम्, इषुपुङ्खा, इषुप्रयोगः, इषुमात्र, इषुहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वग्रम्
इषुः + -अग्रम्, -अनीकम् the point of an arrow; वायुरमित्राणामिष्वग्राण्याञ्चतु<BR> Av. 11. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वनीकम्
इषुः + -अग्रम्, -अनीकम् the point of an arrow; वायुरमित्राणामिष्वग्राण्याञ्चतु<BR> Av. 11. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वसनम्
इषुः + -असनम्, -अस्त्रम् the bow; राममिष्वसनदर्शनोत्सुकम् R. 11. 37;<BR> ˚यन्त्रमुक्तो बाणः Dk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वस्त्रम्
इषुः + -असनम्, -अस्त्रम् the bow; राममिष्वसनदर्शनोत्सुकम् R. 11. 37;<BR> ˚यन्त्रमुक्तो बाणः Dk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वास|इष्वासं|इष्वासः
इषुः + -आस <i>a.</i> throwing arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वासः|इष्वास|इष्वासं
इषुः + -आस + .({@-सः@})<BR>—1 a bow.<BR>—2 an archer, a warrior; अत्र शूरा महेष्वासा भीमार्जुनसमा युधि Bg. 1. 4, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुकारः|इषुकार
इषुः + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> an arrow-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुकृत्
इषुः + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> an arrow-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधरः|इषुधर
इषुः + -धरः, -भृत् <i>m.</i> an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुभृत्
इषुः + -धरः, -भृत् <i>m.</i> an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुपथः|इषुपथ
इषुः + -पथः, -विक्षेपः an arrow-shot, the range of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुविक्षेपः|इषुविक्षेप
इषुः + -पथः, -विक्षेपः an arrow-shot, the range of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुपातरामक्षेत्रम्
इषुः + -पातरामक्षेत्रम् The holy place called Paraśurāma.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">Page0391-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुपुङ्खा
इषुः + -पुङ्खा A particular plant (Mar. उन्हाळी); The indigo plant;<BR> Mātaṅga L. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुप्रयोगः
इषुः + -प्रयोगः discharging an arrow; प्रत्यब्रवीच्चैनमिषुप्रयोगे R. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुमात्र
इषुः + -मात्र <i>a.</i> having the length of an arrow (about 5 short spans<BR> or three feet); cf. यदा हि द्विजवरस्येषुमात्रावलोकनानुगतेर्न समाहिता<BR> पुरुषगतिः Bhāg. 5. 10. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुमात्रम्
इषुः + -मात्र + .({@-त्रम्@})<BR>—1 the length of an arrow.<BR>—2 an altar (कुण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुहस्त
इषुः + -हस्त <i>a.</i> carrying arrows in the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुस्त्रिकाण्डा
इषुस्त्रिकाण्डा ‘The three-fold arrow’, N. of a constellation. (Mar.<BR> तिकाटणें ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुक
इषुक <i>a.</i> Arrow-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुका
इषुक + .{@-का@} Ved. An arrow. यथेषुका परापतदवसृष्टाऽधि धन्वनः Av. 1. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधिः|इषुधि
इषुधिः [इषवो धीयन्तेऽत्र धा-कि] A quiver. धन्वी खड्गी धृतेषुधिः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्यति
इषुध्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To contain arrows.<BR>—2 To Implore, request, ask.<BR>—3 To desire oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्या
इषुध्या Imploring, request; इषुध्येव मरुतो रोदस्योः Rv. 1. 122. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्यु
इषुध्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going.<BR>—2 Requesting; इषुध्यव ऋतसापः पुरन्धीः Rv. 5. 41. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषूयति
इषूयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To long for food.<BR>—2 To request.<BR>—3 To strive for; ऋत्वा वेधा इषूयते Rv. 1. 128. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वः|इष्व
इष्वः A spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृ
इष्कृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To arrange, set in order.<BR>—2 To prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कर्तृ|इष्कर्त्तृ
इष्कर्तृ <i>a.</i> Arranging &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृत
इष्कृत <i>a.</i> Arranged &c. ˚आहव <i>a.</i> whose Soma vessel is<BR> prepared or ready; इष्कृताहावमवतं सुवरत्रं सुषेचनम् Rv. 10. 101. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृतिः|इष्कृति
इष्कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A mother.<BR>—2 Healing; इष्कृतिर्नाम वो माता Rv. 10. 97. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका [इष्-तकन् टाप् Uṇ. 3. 148]<BR>—1 A brick; Mk. 3.<BR>—2 A brick used in preparing the sacrificial altar &c. लोकादिमग्निं<BR> तमुवाच तस्मै या इष्टकी यावतार्वा यथा वा Kaṭh. 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इष्टकागृहम्, इष्टकाचयनम्, इष्टकाचित, इष्टकान्यासः, इष्टकापथः, इष्टकामात्रा, इष्टकाराशिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकागृहम्
इष्टका + -गृहम् a brick-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकाचयनम्
इष्टका + -चयनम् collecting fire by means of a brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकाचित
इष्टका + -चित <i>a.</i> made of bricks; Dk. 84; also इष्टकचित; cf. P. VI. 3. 65.^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकान्यासः|इष्टकान्यास
इष्टका + -न्यासः laying the foundation of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकापथः|इष्टकापथ|इष्टकापथं
इष्टका + -पथः a road made of bricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकामात्रा
इष्टका + -मात्रा size of the bricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकाराशिः|इष्टकाराशि
इष्टका + -राशिः a pile of bricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका A brick &c.; see इष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस् <i>ind.</i> An interjection of anger, pain, or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह <i>ind.</i> [इदं-ह इशादेशः P. V. 3. 11. Sk.]<BR>—1 Here (referring to time, place or direction); in this place or case.<BR> नेहाभिकमनाशोऽस्ति Bg. 2. 40.<BR>—2 In this world (opp. परत्र or अमुत्र); oft. with जगति; K. 35.<BR>—3 In this case; in this book or system.<BR>—4 Now, at this time. [cf. Zend. <i>idha</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: इहामुत्र, इहागत, इहेह, इहकालः, इहक्रतु, इहचित्त, इहभव, इहलोकः, इहसमये, इहस्थ, इहस्थान<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहामुत्र
इह + -अमुत्र <i>ind.</i> in this world and the next world, here and there;<BR> cf. इहामुत्रार्थभोगविरागः । शाङ्करभाष्य on ब्रह्मसूत्र 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहागत
इह + -आगत <i>a.</i> come here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहेह
इह + -इह <i>ind.</i> here and there, now and then, repeatedly. ˚मातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 whose mother is here and there; that is, everywhere; समानो वां जनिता<BR> भ्रातरा युवं यमाविहेहमातरा Rv. 6. 59. 2.<BR>—2 of whose mothers one is here and one there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहकालः|इहकाल
इह + -कालः this life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहक्रतु
इह + -क्रतु, -चित्त <i>a.</i> whose intentions or thoughts are centred<BR> in this world or place, इहैवैधि धनसनिरिहचित्त इहक्रतुः Av. 18. 4. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहचित्त
इह + -क्रतु, -चित्त <i>a.</i> whose intentions or thoughts are centred<BR> in this world or place, इहैवैधि धनसनिरिहचित्त इहक्रतुः Av. 18. 4. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहभव
इह + -भव or {@-तन@} <i>a.</i><BR> belonging to this world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहतन
इह + -भव or {@-तन@} <i>a.</i><BR> belonging to this world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलोकः|इहलोक
इह + -लोकः this world or life; ˚के in this world; cf. श्रेयो<BR> भोक्तुंभैक्ष्यमपीह लोके Bg. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहसमये
इह + -समये <i>ind.</i> here, now, at such a time as this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहस्थ
इह + -स्थ <i>a.</i> standing here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहस्थान
इह + -स्थान <i>a.</i> one whose residence is on the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहत्य
इहत्य <i>a.</i> [इह-त्यप्] Being here, of this place or world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलः|इहल
इहलः N. of a country (चेदि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईः
ईः (<i>m.</i>) N. of Kāmadeva, Cupid. <i>f.</i> N. of Lakṣmī. ━<i>ind.</i><BR> An interjection of (1) dejection; (2) pain; (3) sorrow; (4) anger; (5)<BR> compassion; (6) perception or consciousness; (7) calling; cf. also ईरीश्वरो<BR> भवेच्छत्रुः पुरुषः करुणोऽरुणः । अप्रजाः सुप्रजाः शङ्कुर्मुकुरो नकुलोऽकुलः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई I. €4 Ā. (ईयते) To go. ━II. €2 P.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR>—3 To pervade.<BR>—4 To desire, wish.<BR>—5 To throw.<BR>—6 To eat.<BR>—7 To beg (Ā.).<BR>—8 To become pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्
ईक्ष् €1 Ā. (ईक्षते, ईक्षाञ्चक्रे, ऐक्षिष्ट, ईक्षितुम्, ईक्षित्वा, ईक्षित)<BR>—1 To see, behold, view, perceive, observe, look or gaze at.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-a2" target="_blank">Page0391-a2</a>]<BR>—2 To regard, consider, look upon; सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानम् … ईक्षते<BR> योगयुक्तात्मा Bg. 6. 29.<BR>—3 To take into account, care for; नाभिजनमीक्षते K. 104; न कामवृत्तिर्वचनीयमीक्षते Ku. 5. 82.<BR>—4 To think, reflect; स ऐक्षत लोकान्तु सृजै Ait. Up. 1. 1. तत्तेज<BR> ऐक्षत बहु स्यां प्रजायेय Ch. Up. 6. 2. 3.<BR>—5 To require; नाभ्यासकममीक्षते Pt. 1. 151.<BR>—6 To look to, or to investigate, the good or bad luck of any one (with<BR> dat. of the person); कृष्णाय ईक्षते गर्गः Sk. (शुभाशुभं पर्यालोचयति)<BR> Bk. 8. 76. ━<i>With</i> {@अधि@} to suspect; सत्येऽप्यपायमधीक्षते H. 4. 102 v. l.<BR>━{@अन्वव@}<BR>—1 to see, behold.<BR>—2 to consider.<BR>—3 to care for, take into account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षकः|ईक्षक
ईक्षकः [ईक्ष्-ण्वुक्ष्] A spectator, beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0391-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणम्
ईक्षणम् [ईक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Seeing, beholding &c.<BR>—2 A look, sight, aspect, view.<BR>—3 An eye; अश्रुपूर्णाकुलेक्षणम् Bg. 2. 1. इत्यद्रिशोभाप्रहितेक्षणेन<BR> R. 2. 27; so अलसेक्षणा.<BR>—4 Regarding, looking after, caring for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणश्रवस्
ईक्षणम् + .{@-श्रवस्@} <i>m.</i> A serpent; एषा नो नैष्ठिकी बुद्धिः सर्वेषामीक्षणश्रवः Mb. 1. 37. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिकः|ईक्षणिक
ईक्षणिकः [ईक्षण-ठन्] A fortune-teller; मङ्गलादेशवृत्ताश्च<BR> भद्राश्चेक्षाणिकैः सह Ms. 9. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिका
ईक्षणिकः + .{@-का@} A female fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षतिः|ईक्षति
ईक्षतिः [ईक्ष्-शतिप्] Looking, sight; ईक्षतेर्नाशब्दम् Br. Sūt. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षा
ईक्षा [ईक्ष्-अ टाप्]<BR>—1 Sight. ईक्षया जीवयामास निर्जरान्निर्व्रणान्यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 37.<BR>—2 Viewing, considering; Bhāg. 7. 11. 8.<BR>—3 Knowledge of soul (आत्मविद्या); Bhāg. 7. 6. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षिका
ईक्षिका<BR>—1 An eye.<BR>—2 A glance, look; Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षित
ईक्षित <i>p. p.</i> Seen, beheld, regarded &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षितम्
ईक्षित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A look, sight.<BR>—2 An eye; अभिमुखे मयि संहृतमीक्षितम् Ś. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षितृ
ईक्षितृ <i>a.</i> [ईक्ष्-तृच्] Seeing, beholding, a beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षेण्य
ईक्षेण्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Deserving to be seen; curious. ईक्षेण्यासो अह्यो<BR> न चारवो Rv. 9. 77. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख्
ईख्, -ईङ्ख् €1 P. (ईङ्खति, ईङ्खाञ्चक्रे, ईङ्खितुम्, ईङ्खित)<BR> To go, move,<BR> vacillate. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To move backwards and forwards, swing, oscillate.<BR>—2 To shake, cause to tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईङ्ख्|ईंख्
ईख्, -ईङ्ख् €1 P. (ईङ्खति, ईङ्खाञ्चक्रे, ईङ्खितुम्, ईङ्खित)<BR> To go, move,<BR> vacillate. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To move backwards and forwards, swing, oscillate.<BR>—2 To shake, cause to tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज्
ईज्, -ईञ्ज् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईञ्ज्
ईज्, -ईञ्ज् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईजान
ईजान <i>a.</i> [यज् कानच्] Performing sacrifices. One who has sacrificed;<BR> यः सेतुरीजानानामक्षरं ब्रह्म यत्परम् Kaṭh. 1. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईजिकाः
ईजिकाः N. of a people; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् €2 Ā. (ईट्टे, इडाञ्चक्रे, ऐडिष्ट, ईडितुं, ईडित)<BR>—1 To praise; अग्निमीडे पुरोहितम् Rv. 1. 1. 1; शालीनतामव्रजदीड्यमानः<BR> R. 18. 17; नेडिषे यदि काकुत्स्थम् Bk. 9. 57, 18. 15.<BR>—2 To implore, request, ask for (with two acc.); उपस्थाय मातरमन्नमैट्टे<BR> Rv. 3. 48. 3. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To ask.<BR>—2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Refreshment, libation.<BR>—2 Praise, extolling; Rv. 8. 39. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडनम्
ईडनम् [ईड्-ल्युट्] Praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा [ईड्-अ-टाप्] Praise, commendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडेन्य
ईडे(ले)न्य Ved. = ईड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलेन्य
ईडे(ले)न्य Ved. = ईड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्य
ईड्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be praised or glorified, praiseworthy, laudable;<BR> ब्रह्मजज्ञं देवमीड्यं विदित्वा Kaṭh. 1. 17. भवन्तमीड्यं<BR> भवतः पितेव R. 5. 34; प्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम् Bg. 11. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईण्मत्|ईण्मन्त्
ईण्मत् <i>a.</i> [ईट्-अस्त्यस्य मतुप्] Having a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति <i>a.</i> [ई-क्तिच्]<BR>—1 Produced, effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईतिः|ईति
ईति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Plague, distress, a calamity of the season. The <i>itis</i><BR> are usually said to be six:− (1) excessive rain; (2) drought; (3) locusts;<BR> (4) rats; (5) parrots; and (6) foreign invasions; अतिवृष्टिरनाव्रष्टिः<BR> शलभा मूषकाः शुकाः । प्रत्यासन्नाश्च राजानः षडेता ईतयः स्मृताः ॥<BR> (some read for the second line स्वचक्रं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">Page0392-2</a>]<BR> परचक्रं च सप्तैता ईतयः स्मृताः ॥ making the total number seven);<BR> आशास्यमीतिविगमप्रभृति प्रजानाम् M. 5. 20; Mv. 7. 42; निरातङ्का<BR> निरीतयः R. 1. 63.<BR>—2 An infectious disease.<BR>—3 Travelling (in a foreign country), sojourning (प्रवास).<BR>—4 An affray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष, -श <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्श
ईदृक्ष, -श <i>a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्षी
ईदृक्ष, -श + .({@-क्षी, -शी@} <i>f.</i>), also ईदृश् Such, of this kind, of this aspect,<BR> endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृसी
ईदृक्ष, -श + .({@-क्षी, -शी@} <i>f.</i>), also ईदृश् Such, of this kind, of this aspect,<BR> endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्
ईदृक्ष, -श + .{@-क्@} <i>n.</i> Such a condition; such occasion; लभन्ते युद्धमीदृशम्<BR> Bg. 2. 32, 6. 42, 11. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ता
ईदृक्ता Quality (Opp. इयत्ता); विष्णोरिवस्यानवधारणीयम् ईदृक्ताया<BR> रूपमियत्तया वा R. 13. 5; मामीदृक्तया जानाति knows me to be so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईन्त्|ईंत्
ईन्त् €1 P. To bind; cf. अत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सनम्
ईप्सनम्, ईप्सा [आप्तुमिच्छा आप्-सन्-अ]<BR>—1 Desire to obtain.<BR>—2 A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सा
ईप्सनम्, ईप्सा [आप्तुमिच्छा आप्-सन्-अ]<BR>—1 Desire to obtain.<BR>—2 A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित <i>a.</i> Desired, wished for, dear to; अपीप्सितं क्षत्रकुलाङ्गनानाम्<BR> R. 14. 4; Ś. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सितम्
ईप्सित + .{@-तम्@} Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सितफलम्
ईप्सित + .{@-फलम्@} A kind of sweet Cocoanut (Mar. मोहाचा नारळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु <i>a.</i> Striving to obtain, wishing or desiring to get (with<BR> acc. or inf. but usually in comp.); सौरभ्यमीप्सुरिव ते मुखमारुतस्य<BR> R. 5. 69. काम˚ Bg. 18. 24. धन˚ &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईप्सुयज्ञः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सुयज्ञः|ईप्सुयज्ञ
ईप्सु + -यज्ञः a particular Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईम्
ईम् <i>ind.</i> [ई-बा˚ मुच्] Ved.<BR>—1 A particle of affirmation or restriction; usually after short words<BR> at the beginning of a sentence, after यत्, relative pronouns prepositions<BR> and particles like उत, अथ &c.; प्र यदीमुवाचेति Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 16.<BR>—2 Now.<BR>—3 This, here (एनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईय
ईय [ई-बा˚ क्यप्] Pervading; ˚चक्षस् of pervading sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् €2 Ā. (ईर्ते^1, ईराञ्चक्रे, ऐरिष्ट, ईरितुम्, ईर्ण); also €1 P. (<i>p. p.</i> ईरित)<BR>—1 To go, move, shake (trans. also).<BR>—2 To rise, arise or spring from.<BR>—3 To go away, retire.<BR>—4 To agitate, elevate; raise oneʼs voice.<BR> €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i> (ईरयति, ईरित) —1 To agitate, throw, cast;<BR> Śi. 8. 39; discharge, dart, hurl; ऐरिरच्च महाद्रुमम् Bk. 15. 52; R. 15. 20.<BR>—2 To excite, prompt, urge; क्षेमंकरेऽर्थे मुहुरीर्यमाणः Bk. 12. 6.<BR>—3 To cause to rise, produce.<BR>—4 To utter, pronounce, proclaim, say, repeat; Māl. 1. 25; इतीरयन्तीव<BR> तया निरैक्षि N. 14. 21; Śi. 9. 69; Ki. 1. 26; R. 9. 8; निबोध चेमां<BR> गिरमीरितां मया.<BR>—5 To cause to go, set in motion, move, shake; वातेरितपल्लवाङ्गुलिभिः<BR> Ś. 1; अपरागसमीरणेरितः Ki. 2. 50; Śi. 8. 20.<BR>—6 To draw towards, attract; उद्धतैरिव परस्परसङ्गादीरितान्युभयतः<BR> कुचकुम्भैः Śi. 10. 32.<BR>—7 To employ, use.<BR>—8 To bring to life, revive.<BR>—9 To elevate. ━To raise oneself (Ā.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20260605. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरः|ईर
ईरः Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरजः|ईरज
ईरः + .{@-जः, -पुत्रः@} N. of Hanūmat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरपुत्रः|ईरपुत्र
ईरः + .{@-जः, -पुत्रः@} N. of Hanūmat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरण|ईरणः
ईरण <i>a.</i> [ईर-ल्युट्] Agitating, driving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरणः|ईरण
ईरण + .{@-णः@} The wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरणम्
ईरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Agitating, moving, driving.<BR>—2 Going.<BR>—3 = इरण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sent, despatched.<BR>—2 Said, uttered &c.; ˚आकूतम् declared purpose or intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिन्
ईरिन् <i>a.</i> [ईर्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Moving, agitating.<BR>—2 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य
ईर्य <i>a.</i> To be excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्या|ईर्य्या
ईर्य + .{@-र्या@} Wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईर्यपथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्यपथः
ईर्य + -पथः<BR>—1 the observances of a religious mendicant to obtain knowledge.<BR>—2 the four positions of the body, <i>i. e.</i> going, standing upright,<BR> sitting and lying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण <i>a.</i> [ईर्-इनन्] Desert, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिणम्
ईरिण + .{@-णम्@} A desert, barren soil; मुहूर्तमिव निःशब्दमासीदीरिणसंनिभम्<BR> Rām. 1. 55. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
ईर्क्ष्य्^1 See ईर्ष्य्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: missing virama on root..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म|ईर्मः|ईर्म्म
ईर्म <i>a.</i> [ईर्-मक्]<BR>—1 Agitated.<BR>—2 Going constantly or instigating everything (Sāy.). ━<i>ind.</i> Here,<BR> in or to this place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्मः|ईर्म|ईर्म्म
ईर्म + .{@-र्मः@} The arm; the fore-quarter of an animal; ईर्माभ्यामयनं<BR> जातम् Av. 10. 10. 21; तस्य प्राची दिक्छिरोऽसौ चासौ चेर्मौ Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्मम्
ईर्म + .{@-र्मम्@} A wound, sore (<i>m.</i> also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्मान्त|ईर्मांत
ईर्मान्त <i>a.</i> Ved. Full-haunched, or thin-haunched. N. of a team<BR> of horses (of the sunʼs car); ईर्मान्तासः सिलिकमध्यमासः Rv. 1. 163. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्वारुः|ईर्वारु|ईर्व्वारु|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्वारुः <i>m., f.</i> A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा = ईर्ष्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य्, ईर्क्ष्य् €1 P. (ईर्ष्यति, ईर्ष्याञ्चकार, ईर्ष्यितुम्, ईर्ष्यित)<BR> To envy, be jealous of, be impatient of the success of (with dat. of person);<BR> हरये ईर्ष्यति Sk.; ईर्ष्यन्त्या वदनमसिक्तमपि Śi. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य्, ईर्क्ष्य् €1 P. (ईर्ष्यति, ईर्ष्याञ्चकार, ईर्ष्यितुम्, ईर्ष्यित)<BR> To envy, be jealous of, be impatient of the success of (with dat. of person);<BR> हरये ईर्ष्यति Sk.; ईर्ष्यन्त्या वदनमसिक्तमपि Śi. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक <i>a.</i> Envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यु
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक <i>a.</i> Envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक <i>a.</i> Envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्या
ईर्ष्या, -र्षा<BR> [ईर्ष्य्-अप्] Envy, jealousy, envy of anotherʼs success, spite, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्ष्या, -र्षा<BR> [ईर्ष्य्-अप्] Envy, jealousy, envy of anotherʼs success, spite, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) <i>a.</i> Envious, impatient.<BR> ईर्ष्योर्मृतं मनः Av. 6. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) <i>a.</i> Envious, impatient.<BR> ईर्ष्योर्मृतं मनः Av. 6. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यु
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) <i>a.</i> Envious, impatient.<BR> ईर्ष्योर्मृतं मनः Av. 6. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षु
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) <i>a.</i> Envious, impatient.<BR> ईर्ष्योर्मृतं मनः Av. 6. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलिः|ईलि
ईलिः (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A weapon, a cudgel or a short sword.<BR>—2 A stick shaped like a sword (Mar. गुप्ति). (करवालिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलिनः|ईलिन
ईलिनः N. of a son of Taṃsu and father of Duṣyanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलिनी
ईलिनः + .{@-नी@} <i>f.</i> N. of a daughter of Medhātithi; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईवत्|ईवन्त्
ईवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going.<BR>—2 So large, so stately or magnificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् €2 Ā. (ईष्टे, ईशाञ्चक्रे, ऐशिष्ट, ईशिता, ईशितुम्, ईशित) —1 To<BR> rule, be master of, govern, command (with gen.); नायं गात्राणामीष्टे<BR> K. 312 v. l.; अर्थानामीशिषे त्वं वयमपि च गिरामीश्महे यावदर्थम्<BR> Bh. 3. 30; sometimes with acc.; इमाँल्लोकानीशत ईशनीभिः Śvet. Up. 3. 1.<BR> (also used in the Veda with gen. of an infinitive or loc. of an abstract noun).<BR>—2 To be able, have power; expressed by ‘can’; माधुयर्मीष्टे हरिणान्<BR> ग्रहीतुम् R. 18. 13, 14. 38; कमिवेशते रमयितुं न गुणाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">Page0393-2</a>]<BR> Ki. 6. 24; U. 7. 4; Śi. 1. 38; Māl. 10. 13.<BR>—3 To act like a master, allow.<BR>—4 To own, possess.<BR>—5 To belong to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् <i>m.</i> A master, lord, the Supreme Spirit. ईशावास्यमिदं सर्वम् Īśop. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश <i>a.</i> [ईश्-क]<BR>—1 Owning, possessing, sharing, master or lord of; see below.<BR>—2 One who is completely master of anything.<BR>—3 Capable of (with gen.)<BR>—4 Powerful, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशः|ईश|ईशं
ईश + .{@-शः@}<BR>—1 A lord, master; with gen. or in comp.; कथंचिदीशा मनसां बभूवुः<BR> Ku. 3. 34 with great difficulty controlled (were masters of) their minds;<BR> so वागीश, सुरेश &c.<BR>—2 A husband.<BR>—3 A Rudra.<BR>—4 The number 11 (derived from the eleven Rudras).<BR>—5 N. of Śiva (as regent of the north-east quarter).<BR>—6 The Supreme god (परमेश्वर); व्यक्ताव्यक्तं भरते विश्वमीशमीड्यम्<BR> Śvet. Up. 1. 8; प्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम् Bg. 11. 44. श्रीवत्सधामापररात्र<BR> ईशः Bhāg. 6. 8. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशा
ईश + .{@-शा@}<BR>—1 Supremacy, power, dominion, greatness. Śvet. Up. 4. 7.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR>—3 A woman having supremacy; a rich lady.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईशकान्तः, ईशकोणः, ईशगीता, ईशदण्डः, ईशपुरी, ईशनगरी, ईशबलम्, ईशसखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशकान्तः
ईश + -कान्तः A class of the eleven-storeyed buildings. (Māna. 21. 10-11).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशकोणः|ईशकोण
ईश + -कोणः the north-east quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशगीता
ईश + -गीता <i>f.</i> N. of a section of the Kūrma Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशदण्डः
ईश + -दण्डः Axle-pole of a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशपुरी
ईश + -पुरी, -नगरी N. of Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशनगरी
ईश + -पुरी, -नगरी N. of Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशबलम्
ईश + -बलम् the missile पाशुपत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशसखः|ईशसख
ईश + -सखः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशावास्यम्
ईशावास्यम् N. of the ईशावास्योपनिषद्, also called ईशोपनिषद्;<BR> the only instance of an upaniṣad included in a Saṃhitā (Vāj. 40. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशनम्
ईशनम् [ईश्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Commanding, reigning &c.<BR>—2 Greatness, glory; एतदीशनमीशस्य प्रकृतिस्थोऽपि तद्गुणैः Bhāg. 1. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान <i>a.</i> [ईश् ताच्छील्ये चानश्]<BR>—1 Owning, possessing, master or lord.<BR>—2 Reigning, ruling.<BR>—3 Wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानः|ईशान|ईशानं
ईशान + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A ruler, master, lord; ईशानो भूतभव्यस्य Kaṭh. 4. 12.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva; ईशानसंदर्शनलालसानाम् Ku. 7. 56; K. 10.<BR>—3 The Ārdrā Nakṣtra.<BR>—4 One of the Rudras.<BR>—5 The number ‘eleven’.<BR>—6 The sun as a form of Śiva. पर्जन्यो यमो मृत्युरीशानः Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11.<BR>—7 A Sādhya.<BR>—8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानी
ईशान + .{@-नी@} N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानी
ईशान + .{@-नी, -नः@} The silk-cotton tree (शाल्मली; Mar. सांवरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानः|ईशान|ईशानं
ईशान + .{@-नी, -नः@} The silk-cotton tree (शाल्मली; Mar. सांवरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानम्
ईशान + .{@-नम्@} Light, splendour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईशानादिपञ्चमूर्तिः, ईशानकल्पः, ईशानकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानादिपञ्चमूर्तिः|ईशानादिपञ्चमूर्ति
ईशान + -आदिपञ्चमूर्तिः <i>f.</i> one of the five forms of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानकल्पः|ईशानकल्प
ईशान + -कल्पः N. of a Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानकृत्
ईशान + -कृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 making one a master or able.<BR>—2 acting like a competent person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितृ
ईशितृ <i>a.</i> [ईश्-तृच्] An owner, a master, proprietor. ━<i>m.</i><BR> The lord of the Universe; न चेशिता नैव च तस्य लिङ्गम् Śvet. Up. 6. 9.<BR> अव्यक्तोऽभूदीशितेव प्रणादः Śi. 18. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितव्य|ईशितव्यं
ईशितव्य <i>a.</i> To be reigned or ruled over; ईशितव्यैः किमस्माभिरीशस्यैतद्विडम्बनम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 23. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितव्यम्
ईशितव्यम् Power, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिता
ईशिता, -त्वम्<BR> Superiority, greatness, one of the eight <i>Siddhis</i> or<BR> attributes of Śiva. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशित्वम्
ईशिता, -त्वम्<BR> Superiority, greatness, one of the eight <i>Siddhis</i> or<BR> attributes of Śiva. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिन्
ईशिन् <i>a.</i> [ईश्-णिनि] Commanding, reigning &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A god.<BR>—2 A husband.<BR>—3 A lord, master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिनी
ईशिन् + .{@-नी@} Supremacy; ईशत ईशिनीभिः Śvet. Up. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर <i>a.</i> (-रा, -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ईश्-वरच् P. III. 2. 175]<BR>—1 Powerful, able, capable of (with inf.); वसतिं प्रिय कामिनां प्रियास्त्वदृते<BR> प्रापयितुं क ईश्वरः Ku. 4. 11; R. 15. 7.<BR>—2 Rich, wealthy Pt. 2. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरः|ईश्वर|ईश्वरं
ईश्वर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A lord, master; ईश्वरं लोकोऽर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14; so कपीश्वरः,<BR> कोशलेश्वरः, हृदयेश्वरः &c.<BR>—2 A king, prince, ruler; राज्यमस्तमितेश्वरम् R. 12. 11; Ms. 4. 153, 9. 278.<BR>—3 A rich or great man; तृणेन कार्यं भवतीश्वराणाम् Pt. 1. 71; R. 3. 46;<BR> Bh. 3. 59; मा प्रयच्छेश्वरे धनम् H. 1. 14; cf. “To carry coals to Newcastle”.<BR>—4 A husband; नेश्वरे परुषता सखि साध्वी Ki. 9. 39.<BR>—5 The Supreme God (परमेश्वर); ईश एवाहमत्यर्थं न च मामीशते<BR> परे । ददामि च सदैश्वर्यमीश्वरस्तेन कीर्तितः ॥ Skanda P.; cf.<BR> also ईश्वरस्तु पर्जन्यवद् द्रष्टव्यः Brahmasūtra-Śāṅkarabhāṣya.<BR>—6 N. of Śiva; यस्मिन्नीश्वर इत्यनन्यविषयः शब्दो यथार्थाक्षरः V. 1. 1.<BR>—7 The god of love, cupid.<BR>—8 The Supreme Soul; the soul.<BR>—9 The eleventh year (संवत्सर) of the Śālivāhana era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरा
ईश्वर + .{@-रा, -री@} N. of Durgā; of Lakṣmī; or of one of the śaktis;<BR> ईश्वरीं सर्वभूतानां त्वामिहोपह्वये श्रियम् (श्रीसूक्तम्);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरी
ईश्वर + .{@-रा, -री@} N. of Durgā; of Lakṣmī; or of one of the śaktis;<BR> ईश्वरीं सर्वभूतानां त्वामिहोपह्वये श्रियम् (श्रीसूक्तम्);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरी
ईश्वर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 N. of several plants and trees; लिङ्गिनीलता, वन्ध्याकर्कटी, क्षुद्रजटा<BR> and नाकुलीवृक्ष.<BR>—2 A rich woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईश्वराधीन, ईश्वरकान्तम्, ईश्वरकृष्णः, ईश्वरनिषेधः, ईश्वरनिष्ठ, ईश्वरपूजक, ईश्वरपूजा, ईश्वरप्रसादः, ईश्वरभावः, ईश्वरविभूतिः, ईश्वरसद्मन्, ईश्वरसभम्, ईश्वरसेवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वराधीन
ईश्वर + -अधीन <i>a.</i> subject to a lord or king, dependent on a a lord or god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरकान्तम्
ईश्वर + -कान्तम्<BR>—1 A class of buildings.<BR>—2 A ground plan in which the whole area is divided into 961 equal squares<BR> (एकषष्टिसमाधिक्यं पदं नवशतायुतम् । एवमीश्वरकान्तं स्यात् …<BR> Māna. 7. 46-48.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरकृष्णः|ईश्वरकृष्ण
ईश्वर + -कृष्णः N. of the author of Sāṅkhya Kārikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरनिषेधः|ईश्वरनिषेध
ईश्वर + -निषेधः denial of the existence of god, atheism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरनिष्ठ
ईश्वर + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> trusting in god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरपूजक
ईश्वर + -पूजक <i>a.</i> pious, devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरपूजा
ईश्वर + -पूजा worship of god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरप्रसादः|ईश्वरप्रसाद
ईश्वर + -प्रसादः divine favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरभावः|ईश्वरभाव
ईश्वर + -भावः royal or imperial state; दानमीश्वरभावाय Bg. 18. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरविभूतिः|ईश्वरविभूति
ईश्वर + -विभूतिः <i>f.</i> the several forms of the Supreme god; for a full<BR> enumeration see Bg. 10. 19-42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसद्मन्
ईश्वर + -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसभम्
ईश्वर + -सभम् a royal court or assembly. सभा राजामनुष्यपूर्वा P. II. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसेवा
ईश्वर + -सेवा worship of god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरता
ईश्वरता, -त्वम्<BR> Superiority, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरत्वम्
ईश्वरता, -त्वम्<BR> Superiority, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्
ईष् €1 U. (ईषति-ते, ऐषीत्, ईषितुम्, ईषित)<BR>—1 To fly away escape.<BR>—2 To creep along.<BR>—3 To glean, collect a few grains.<BR>—4 To look, see.<BR>—5 To give.<BR>—6 To attack, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषः|ईष
ईषः [ईष्-क]<BR>—1 The month Āśvina; cf. इषः^1.<BR>—2 A servant of Śiva.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषण
ईषण, ईषणिन् <i>a.</i> Hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषणिन्
ईषण, ईषणिन् <i>a.</i> Hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषणा
ईषण, ईषणिन् + .{@-णा@} Haste, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत् <i>ind.</i> [ईष्-अति] —1 Slightly, to some extent, a little;<BR> ईषत् चुम्बितानि Ś. 1. 4; ईषच्च कुरुते सेवाम् Pt. 1. 141. Easily<BR> done, with very little exertion; ईषत्कार्यमिदं कार्यं कृतमासीन्न संशयः<BR> Rām. 5. 55. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईषदुष्ण, ईषदून, ईषत्कर, ईषत्कार्य, ईषद्गुण, ईषज्जलम्, ईषद्दर्शनम्, ईषद्दीर्घः, ईषन्नाद, ईषन्निमय, ईषत्पाण्डु, ईषत्पान, ईषत्पुरुषः, ईषद्बीजा, ईषद्रक्त, ईषल्लभ, ईषत्प्रलाभ, ईषद्विवृत, ईषद्वीर्यः, ईषच्छ्वास, ईषत्स्पृष्ट, ईषद्धासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदुष्ण|ईषदुष्णं
ईषत् + -उष्ण <i>a.</i> tepid,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">Page0394-2</a>]<BR> slightly warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदून
ईषत् + -ऊन <i>a.</i> not quite complete, a little less than; ईषदूनार्धे कल्पप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्कर|ईषत्करः
ईषत् + -कर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing little.<BR>—2 easy to be accomplished; Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्करम्
ईषत् + -कर + .({@-रम्@}) very little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्कार्य
ईषत् + -कार्य <i>a.</i> very easy, connected with slight effort; ईषत्कार्यो<BR> वधस्तस्य Mb. 5. 74. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्गुण
ईषत् + -गुण <i>a.</i> of little merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषज्जलम्
ईषत् + -जलम् shallow water, a little water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्दर्शनम्
ईषत् + -दर्शनम् a glance, sight, view, glimpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्दीर्घः
ईषत् + -दीर्घः An almond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषन्नाद
ईषत् + -नाद <i>a.</i> slightly sounding (a term applied to unaspirated<BR> soft consonants).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषन्निमय
ईषत् + -निमय <i>a.</i> exchanged for a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पाण्डु|ईषत्पाण्डुः
ईषत् + -पाण्डु <i>a.</i> a little white or pale, whitish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पाण्डुः|ईषत्पाण्डु
ईषत् + -पाण्डु + .({@-ण्डुः@}) a pale or light-brown colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पान
ईषत् + -पान <i>a.</i> that of which a little is drunk. ईषत्पानः सोमो<BR> भवता Sk. आनोयुच् P. III. 3. 128. ({@नम्@}) a small draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पुरुषः|ईषत्पुरुष
ईषत् + -पुरुषः a mean or contemptible person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्बीजा
ईषत् + -बीजा Quince-seed, Dyrus Cydonia (Mar. बेदाणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्रक्त|ईषद्रक्तः
ईषत् + -रक्त <i>a.</i> pale red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्रक्तः|ईषद्रक्त
ईषत् + -रक्त + .({@-क्तः@})<BR>—1 pale-red colour.<BR>—2 undistinguishable colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषल्लभ
ईषत् + -लभ, -प्रलाभ <i>a.</i> to be got for little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्प्रलाभ
ईषत् + -लभ, -प्रलाभ <i>a.</i> to be got for little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्विवृत
ईषत् + -विवृत <i>a.</i> slightly open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्वीर्यः|ईषद्वीर्य
ईषत् + -वीर्यः Almond tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषच्छ्वास
ईषत् + -श्वास <i>a.</i> slightly resounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्स्पृष्ट
ईषत् + -स्पृष्ट <i>a.</i> slightly touched (applied to the semivowels) ईषत्स्पृष्टमन्तस्थानम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्धासः|ईषद्धास
ईषत् + -हासः slight laughter, a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा [ईष्-क]<BR>—1 The pole or shafts of a carriage or a plough. ईषा चकादिसंनिधाने<BR> चेदक्षमानयेत्युच्यते तदा यानाक्षमधिकृत्य ब्रूते इति गम्यते । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 35.<BR> द्वीषम् (रथम्) Bhāg. 4. 26. 1. ‘ईषा लाङ्गलदण्डः स्यात्’ इत्यमरः<BR>—2 A part of a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषे
ईषा + .{@-षे@} (du.) The double or fork-shaped pole.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईषादण्डः, ईषादन्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादण्डः|ईषादण्ड
ईषा + -दण्डः the handle of a plough; ईषादण्डौ मृत्युशय्यातलस्य Śi. 18. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादन्त|ईषादन्तः
ईषा + -दन्त <i>a.</i> with projecting teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादन्तः|ईषादन्त
ईषा + -दन्त + .({@-न्तः@})<BR>—1 an elephant with a large tusk or tooth.<BR>—2 the handle of a plough; ईषादन्तः कुञ्जरं शात्रवीयम् Śi. 18. 38.<BR>—3 the tusk of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषिका<BR>—1 An elephantʼs eye-ball. Edgerton, the author of Mātaṅga L., however,<BR> says that this meaning is wrong and points out that it means, ‘The under surface of the top of the eye-socket of an elephant. ईषिका त्वक्षिकूटकम्’<BR> Mātaṅga L. 6. 9.<BR>—2 A painterʼs brush.<BR>—3 A weapon, arrow, dart.<BR>—4 A kind of missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिरः|ईषिर
ईषिरः [ईष्-किरच्] Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषीका<BR>—1 A painterʼs brush.<BR>—2 An ingot-mould.<BR>—3 = इषीका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म, -ष्वः<BR> See इष्मः, इष्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्वः|ईष्व
ईष्म, -ष्वः<BR> See इष्मः, इष्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईसराफः|ईसराफ
ईसराफः N. of the fourth yoga in Astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह्
ईह् €1 Ā. (ईहते, ईहाञ्चक्रे, ऐहिष्ट, ईहिष्यते, ईहितुम्, ईहित)<BR>—1 To wish, desire, long for; have in mind, think of with acc. or inf.;<BR> ईहन्ते … अर्थसंचयान् Bg. 16. 12, 7. 22; Ms. 4. 15, 3. 126;<BR> ऐहिष्ट तं कारयितुं कृतात्मा Bk. 1. 11.<BR>—2 To endeavour to obtain.<BR>—3 To aim at or attempt, endeavour, strive; माधुर्यं मधुबिन्दुना रचयितुं<BR> क्षाराम्बुधेरीहते Bh. 2. 6; Y. 2. 116.<BR>—4 To take care of. ━<i>Caus.</i> To impel, urge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहः|ईह
ईहः Attempt; as in ऊर्ध्वेहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा [ईह्-अ]<BR>—1 Wish, desire; जलनिधिमकरोत्तरीतुमीहाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-1" target="_blank">Page0395-1</a>]<BR> Rām.; cf. also हन्तुं क्रोधवशादीहां चक्राते नौ परस्परम् Ki. see अनीह also.<BR>—2 An undertaking, act.<BR>—3 Effort, exertion, activity; ईहातश्चेद्धनं भवेत् Ms. 9. 205; प्रजागरांचकारारेरीहास्वनिशमादरात् Bk. 6. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ईहार्थिन्, ईहामृगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0394-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहार्थिन्
ईहा + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> aiming at any object, seeking wealth; वैश्यस्येहार्थिनोऽष्टमे<BR> (कार्यम्) Ms. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहामृगः|ईहामृग
ईहा + -मृगः [ईहाप्रधानो मृगः]<BR>—1 a wolf; सुकृतेहामृगाकीर्णम् Rām. 2. 15. 35.<BR>—2 an artificial deer. —3 a division<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-2" target="_blank">Page0395-2</a>]<BR> of the drama consisting of four acts; for definition &c. see S. D. 518<BR> = वृकः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहित
ईहित <i>p. p.</i> [ईह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Wished, desired; शिरसीहितः Ratn. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Attempted, sought, striven for; यद् विस्मर्तुमपीहितं शमवता Ve. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहितम्
ईहित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A wish, desire;<BR>—2 Effort, exertion.<BR>—3 An undertaking, deed, act; प्रतीयते धातुरिवेहितं फलैः Ki. 1. 20, 8. 46, 11. 43, 18. 31;<BR> Śi. 9. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ I. €1 Ā. (अवते, ऊवे, औष्ट, ओतुम्, उत)<BR>—1 To sound, make a noise.<BR>—2 To roar, bellow (as a bull &c.). ━II. €5 P. (उनोति) Ved. To ask, demand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उः|उ
उः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva, the second of the three syllables in ओम्; see अ.<BR>—2 N. of Brahmā.<BR>—3 The orb of the moon; cf. also उर्गौरीपतिरुः कालः सेतुर्नाथः परायणः ।<BR> नारदोऽर्कोऽनिलः पाशी मार्कण्डेयोऽथ रावणः ॥ Enm. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a particle used expletively; उ उमेशः Sk.<BR>—2 An interjection of:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) calling; उ मेति मात्रा तपसो निषिद्धा पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी जगाम Ku. 1. 26;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) anger;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) compassion;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) command;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) acceptance;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) interrogation; उ मेति मात्रा तपसो निषिद्धा Ku. 1. 26.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) wonder; यत्सन्निधावहमु खाण्डवमग्नयेऽदाम् Bhāg. 1. 15. 8.<BR> or used merely as an expletive. In the Veda used as an enclitic copula<BR> implying restriction and emphasis (and, but, on the other hand, now, I<BR> ask &c.); in classical literature used chiefly with अथ (अथो),<BR> न ({@नो@}) and किम् (किमु); see these words. उ━उ ▪<BR> or उत on the one hand━on the other hand, partly━partly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उका
उका Residue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकारः|उकार
उकारः<BR>—1 The vowel उ; अकार उकारो मकारः Māṇḍ. 8.<BR>—2 The god Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकानहः|उकानह
उकानहः A horse of a red and yellow (or red and black) colour, a<BR> bay or chestnut horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकुणः|उकुण
उ(उं)कुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंकुणः|उङ्कुण|उङ्कुणः
उ(उं)कुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त, उक्ति See under वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्त, उक्ति See under वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थम्
उक्थम् [वच्-थक्]<BR>—1 A saying, sentence, verse, hymn (स्तोत्रम्); यं बृहन्तं बृहत्युक्थे<BR> Mb. 12. 47. 41.<BR>—2 Eulogy, praise.<BR>—3 N. of the Sāmaveda (Trik.); a variety of Sāma; (सामभेदः सामविशेषः).<BR>—4 (In ritual) A kind of recitation or certain recited verses (opp. सामन्<BR> chanted, and यजुस् muttered verses).<BR>—5 The उक्थ sacrifice; Bhāg. 3. 12. 40.<BR>—6 Life; उक्थेन रहितो ह्येष मृतकः प्रोच्यते यथा Bhāg. 1. 15. 6.<BR>—7 A proximate cause (उपादानकारण); एतदेषामुक्थमथो हि सर्वाणि<BR> नामान्युत्तिष्ठन्ति Bṛ. Up. 1. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थः|उक्थ|उक्थं
उक्थम् + .{@-क्थः@} N. of Agni; उक्थो नाम महाभाग त्रिभिरुक्थैरभिष्टुतः Mb. 3. 219. 25.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">Page0395-a2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्था
उक्थम् + .{@-क्था@} N. of a metre, see Appendix.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उक्थपत्रः, उक्थपात्रम्, उक्थभृत्, उक्थवर्धन, उक्थवाहस्, उक्थशंसिन्, उक्थशस्, उक्थशास्, उक्थशस, उक्थशुष्म, उक्थावी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थपत्रः|उक्थपत्र
उक्थम् + -पत्रः<BR>—1 a sacrifice (having verses as its vehicle or leaves); Vāj. 17. 55.<BR>—2 a sacrificer (यजमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थपात्रम्
उक्थम् + -पात्रम्<BR>—1 a sacrificer.<BR>—2 vessels or libations offered during the recitation of an उक्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थभृत्
उक्थम् + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a sage who offers or divides Ukthas; उक्थभृतं सामभृतं<BR> बिभर्ति Rv. 7. 33. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थवर्धन
उक्थम् + -वर्धन <i>a.</i> to be magnified or celebrated in praise, an epithet<BR> of Indra; त्वं हि स्तोमवर्धन इन्द्रास्युक्थवर्धनः Rv. 8. 14. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थवाहस्
उक्थम् + -वाहस् <i>a.</i> offering verses; or one to whom verses are offered;<BR> यं चित्रा उक्थवाहसो Rv. 8. 12. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थशंसिन्
उक्थम् + -शंसिन् <i>a.</i> praising, uttering the Ukthas. कृणोष्युक्थशंसिनः<BR> Rv. 6. 45. 6. (<i>m.</i>) a kind of priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थशस्
उक्थम् + -शस्, -शास्, -शस <i>a.</i> Ved. uttering a verse, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थशास्
उक्थम् + -शस्, -शास्, -शस <i>a.</i> Ved. uttering a verse, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थशस
उक्थम् + -शस्, -शास्, -शस <i>a.</i> Ved. uttering a verse, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थशुष्म
उक्थम् + -शुष्म <i>a.</i><BR>—1 whose strength is praise.<BR>—2 loudly resonant with verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थावी
उक्थम् + उक्थावी<BR> <i>a.</i> fond of or reciting verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थिन्
उक्थिन् <i>a.</i> [उक्थ-इनि]<BR>—1 Uttering verses, praising.<BR>—2 Accompanied by praise or Ukthas. ━<i>m.</i> Indra and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ्य|उक्थ्यः
उक्थ्य <i>a.</i> [उक्थमर्हति यत्]<BR>—1 Accompanied by praise.<BR>—2 Deserving praise or verses.<BR>—3 Generator: नाना गोष्ठी विहिता एकदोहनास्तावश्विनौ दुहतो धर्ममुक्थ्यम् Mb. 1. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ्यः|उक्थ्य
उक्थ्य + .{@-क्थ्यः@}<BR>—1 A libation at the morning and mid-day sacrifices.<BR>—2 N. of a sacrifice forming part of the ज्योतिष्टोम sacrifice.<BR>—3 A Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष्
उक्ष् €1. €6 U. (उक्षति, उक्षाञ्चकार, ववक्ष-क्षे Ved., औक्षीत्,<BR> उक्षितुम्, उक्षित)<BR>—1 To sprinkle, wet, moisten, pour down upon; औक्षन् शोणितमम्भोदाः<BR> Bk. 17. 9, 3. 5; उक्षांबभवुरभितो वपुरम्बुवर्षैः Śi. 5. 30; R. 11. 5, 20;<BR> Ku. 1. 54.<BR>—2 To emit, send forth.<BR>—3 To scatter, throw out (as sparks).<BR>—4 To clean, purify.<BR>—5 To grow up, become strong (Ved.); मा न उक्षन्तमुत मा न उक्षितम् Rv. 1. 114. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष <i>a.</i> [उक्ष्-अच्]<BR>—1 Sprinkling.<BR>—2 Sprinkled.<BR>—3 Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षणम्
उक्षणम् [उक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sprinkling.<BR>—2 Consecrating as by sprinkling; वसिष्ठमन्त्रोक्षणजात् प्रभावात् R. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यति
उक्षण्यति Den. P. To desire one who sends down riches. वयं हि<BR> वां हवामह उक्षण्यन्तो व्यश्ववत् Rv. 8. 26. 9<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0395-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यु
उक्षण्यु <i>a.</i> Desirous of one who sends down riches; व्यश्वस्त्वा<BR> वसुविदमुक्षण्युरप्रीणादृषिः Rv. 8. 23. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Large.<BR>—2 Sprinkling. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षा
उक्षन् + .({@-क्षा@}) [उक्ष् कनिन् Uṇ. 1. 156]<BR>—1 An ox or bull; Ku. 7. 70; cf. also विदलितमहाकूलामुक्ष्णां विषाणविघट्टनैः<BR> Śi. 12. 77; (changed to उक्ष in some comp. महोक्षः, वृद्धोक्षः<BR> &c.) P. V. 4. 77.<BR>—2 An epithet of Soma; the Maruts, the Sun and the Agni.<BR>—3 One of the eight chief medicaments (ऋषभौषधि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उक्षान्न, उक्षतरः, उक्षवश<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षान्न
उक्षन् + -अन्न <i>a.</i> one whose food is oxen. (Ved.); उक्षान्नाय वशान्नाय<BR> सोमपृष्ठाय वेधसे Rv. 8. 43. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षतरः|उक्षतर
उक्षन् + -तरः a small bull or ox; अनुक्षणं नोक्षतरः प्रतीच्छति<BR> Śi. 12. 10; cf. वत्सतर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षवश
उक्षन् + -वश <i>a.</i> dependent on a bull (यदि वशां न विन्देदप्युक्षवश<BR> एव स्यात्); male calf (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षाल|उक्षालः
उक्षाल <i>a.</i> Swift, terrible, high; large, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षालः|उक्षाल
उक्षाल + .{@-लः@} A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
उक्षित <i>p. p.</i> [उक्ष-क्त]<BR>—1 Sprinkled, moistened. अश्वो यमस्य यः श्यावस्तस्य हास्नास्युक्षिता Av. 5. 5. 8.<BR>—2 Cleansed, perfumed.<BR>—3 Adult, of full growth.<BR>—4 Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्
उख्, उङ्ख् €1 P. (ओखति, उङ्खति, उवोख or उङ्खाञ्चकार,<BR> उङ्खित) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्ख्
उख्, उङ्ख् €1 P. (ओखति, उङ्खति, उवोख or उङ्खाञ्चकार,<BR> उङ्खित) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखः|उख
उखः A boiler, pot, vessel. चरुं पञ्चबिलमुखं धर्मोऽभीन्धे Av. 11. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखा
उखः + .{@-खा@}<BR>—1 A boiling vessel, a boiler or cooking pot (such as a sauce-pan; Mar.<BR> शेगडी). अन्यो ह्यग्निरुखाप्यन्या नित्यमेवमवेहि भोः Mb. 12. 315. 15.<BR>—2 A fireplace at a sacrifice.<BR>—3 A part of the body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उखासंभरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

