उग्रक <i>a.</i> Brave, powerful &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रता
उग्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Violence, fearfulness, passion, anger, pungency, acrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रत्वम्
उग्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Violence, fearfulness, passion, anger, pungency, acrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रंपश्य|उग्रम्पश्य
उग्रंपश्य <i>a.</i> [उग्रं पश्यति, उग्रं-दृश्, खश्-मुम् P. III. 2. 37]<BR>—1 Fierce-looking, frightful, hideous.<BR>—2 Malignant, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0396-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्कुणः|उङ्कुण|उंकुणः
उङ्कुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्
उच् €4 P. (उच्यति, उवोच, औचीत्, उचिष्यति, उचितुम्, उचित or उग्र<BR> mostly used in <i>p. p.</i>)<BR>—1 To collect, to gather together.<BR>—2 To take pleasure in, delight in, be fond of.<BR>—3 To be accustomed or used to.<BR>—4 To be suitable, suit, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fit, proper, right, suitable; उचितस्तदुपालम्भः U. 3; usually<BR> with inf.; उचितं न ते मङ्गलकाले रोदितुम् Ś. 4.<BR>—2 Usual, customary; उचितेषु करणीयेषु Ś. 4. 7. 12; K. 64; M. 3. 3.<BR>—3 Accustomed or used to, in comp.; नीवारभागधेयोचितैः R. 1. 50, 2. 25, 3. 54, 60, 11. 9;<BR> चन्दनोचितः Ki. 1. 34.<BR>—4 Praiseworthy.<BR>—5 Delightful, agreeable, pleasurable.<BR>—6 Known, understood.<BR>—7 Entrusted, deposited.<BR>—8 Measured, accurate, adjusted (मित).<BR>—9 Acceptable (ग्राह्य).<BR>—10 Natural (स्वभावसिद्ध); उचितं च महाबाहुर्न जहौ हर्षमात्मवान्<BR> Rām. 2. 19. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचितज्ञ
उचित + .{@-ज्ञ@} <i>n.</i> Knowing what is becoming, proper or convenient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथम्
उचथम् [उच्यते स्तूयतेऽनेन वच्-कथन्] Praise, verse (स्तोत्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथ्य
उचथ्य <i>a.</i> [उचथ-यत्] Deserving praise; उचथ्ये वपुषि यः<BR> स्वराळुत वायो घृतस्नाः Rv. 8. 45. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्च|उच्चं|उच्चः
उच्च <i>a.</i><BR>—1 High (in all senses); tall; क्षितिधारणोच्चं Ku. 7. 63; elevated,<BR> superior, exalted (family &c.)<BR>—2 Loud, high-sounding; उच्चाः पक्षिगणाः Śi. 4. 18.<BR>—3 Intense, violent, strong.<BR>—4 (In astr.) Ascendant; see उच्चसंश्रय below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चः|उच्च|उच्चं
उच्च + .{@-च्चः@}<BR>—1 The apex of the orbit of a planet.<BR>—2 Height, high place; ज्वरश्च मरणं जन्तोरुच्चाच्च पतनं यथा<BR> Mb. 12. 28. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्चावच, उच्चगिर्, उच्चतरुः, उच्चतालः, उच्चदेवः, उच्चदेवता, उच्चध्वजः, उच्चनीच, उच्चभाषणम्, उच्चभाषिन्, उच्चललाटा, उच्चललाटिका, उच्चसंश्रय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चावच|उच्चावचः
उच्च + -अवच <i>a.</i> High and low, great and small; see उच्चावच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चगिर्
उच्च + -गिर्^1 <i>a.</i> Having a loud voice; स्वगुणोच्चगिरो मुनिव्रताः Śi. 16. 29.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतरुः|उच्चतरु
उच्च + -तरुः<BR>—1 the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—2 a lofty tree in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतालः|उच्चताल|उच्चतालं
उच्च + -तालः (heightened) music, dancing &c. at a tavern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेवः|उच्चदेव
उच्च + -देवः N. of Viṣṇu or kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेवता
उच्च + -देवता time personified, chronos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चध्वजः|उच्चध्वज
उच्च + -ध्वजः N. of Śākyamuni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चनीच
उच्च + -नीच <i>a.</i><BR>—1 high and low.<BR>—2 various, multiform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चनीचम्
उच्च + -नीच + .({@-चम्@})<BR>—1 the upper or lower stations of planets.<BR>—2 change of accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चभाषणम्
उच्च + -भाषणम् speaking aloud, vociferous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चभाषिन्
उच्च + -भाषिन् <i>a.</i> shouting, bawling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चललाटा
उच्च + -ललाटा, -ललाटिका a woman with a high or projecting forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चललाटिका
उच्च + -ललाटा, -ललाटिका a woman with a high or projecting forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चसंश्रय
उच्च + -संश्रय <i>a.</i> occupying a high station (said of a planet);<BR> ग्रहैस्ततः पञ्चभिरुच्चसंश्रयैः R. 3. 13; see Malli. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटम्
उच्चटम् Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चता
उच्चता, -त्वम्<BR> Height, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चत्वम्
उच्चता, -त्वम्<BR> Height, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकैः
उच्चकैः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 High, above, lofty (fig. also); श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16, 16. 46;<BR> Ki. 2. 57.<BR>—2 Pre-eminently; युवा कराक्रान्तमहीभृदुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 70.<BR>—3 Loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चा
उच्चा <i>ind.</i> High, above, upwards, aloft; उच्चा पतन्तमरुणं<BR> सुपर्णम् Av. 13. 2. 36. ˚चक्र, ˚बुध्न; Rv. 8. 61. 10; Rv. 1. 116. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैः
उच्चैः <i>ind.</i> [cf. Uṇ. 5. 12]<BR>—1 Aloft, high, on high, above, upwards (opp. नीचम्-चैः); पश्चादुच्चैर्भवति<BR> हरिणः Ś. 4, v. l.; विपद्युच्चैः स्थेयम् Bh. 2. 28; उच्चैरुदात्तः P. I. 2. 29.<BR>—2 Loudly, with a loud noise; उच्चैर्विहस्य; R. 2. 12, 51; Bg. 1. 12.<BR>—3 Powerfully, intensely, very much, greatly; विदधति भयमुच्चैर्वीक्ष्यमाणा<BR> वनान्ताः Ṛs. 1. 22; आश्लेषमर्पय मदर्पितपूर्वमुच्चैः Amaru. 133.<BR>—4 (Used as an adj. in comp. or by itself)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) high, noble; जनोऽयमुच्चैः पदलङ्घनोत्सुकः Ku. 5. 64, 6. 75;<BR> ˚कुलं चात्मनः Ś. 4. 17; किं पुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः Me. 17; Ratn. 4. 16.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) distinguished, pre-eminent, famous; उच्चैरुच्चैःश्रवास्तेन<BR> Ku. 2. 47; M. 5. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्चैःकर, उच्चैर्घुष्टम्, उच्चैर्घोष, उच्चैर्द्विष्, उच्चैर्भुजतरु, उच्चैर्वादः, उच्चैःशिरस्, उच्चैःश्रवस्, उच्चैःश्रवस, उच्चैःस्वर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःकर
उच्चैः + -कर <i>a.</i> making acutely accented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्घुष्टम्
उच्चैः + -घुष्टम्<BR>—1 clamour, great uproar.<BR>—2 loud proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्घोष|उच्चैर्घोषः
उच्चैः + -घोष <i>a.</i> boisterous, crying, roaring; वयोधा उच्चैर्घोषाभ्येति^1<BR> या व्रतम् Av. 9. 1. 8.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्घोषः|उच्चैर्घोष
उच्चैः + -घोष + .({@-षः@})<BR>—1 loud noise.<BR>—2 a form of Rudra<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्द्विष्
उच्चैः + -द्विष् <i>a.</i> having strong or powerful enemies; निबोध यज्ञांशुभुजामिदानीमुच्चैर्द्विषामीप्सितमेतदेव Ku. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्भुजतरु
उच्चैः + -भुजतरु <i>a.</i> having trees like outstretched arms; Me. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्वादः|उच्चैर्वाद
उच्चैः + -वादः high praise; जामदग्न्यस्य दमन इति कोऽयमुच्चैर्वादः U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःशिरस्
उच्चैः + -शिरस् <i>a.</i> high-minded, one of high rank, magnanimous; क्षुद्रेऽपि<BR> नूनं शरणं प्रपन्ने ममत्वमुच्चैःशिरसां सतीव Ku. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःश्रवस्
उच्चैः + -श्रवस्, -श्रवस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 long-eared.<BR>—2 deaf. (<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of the horse of Indra (said to be churned out of the ocean); उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानाम्<BR> Bg. 10. 27; उच्चैरुच्चैः श्रवास्तेन् हयरत्नमहारि च Ku. 2. 47.<BR>—2 N. of a horse of the god sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःश्रवस
उच्चैः + -श्रवस्, -श्रवस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 long-eared.<BR>—2 deaf. (<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of the horse of Indra (said to be churned out of the ocean); उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानाम्<BR> Bg. 10. 27; उच्चैरुच्चैः श्रवास्तेन् हयरत्नमहारि च Ku. 2. 47.<BR>—2 N. of a horse of the god sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःस्वर|उच्चैःस्वरः
उच्चैः + -स्वर <i>a.</i> high-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःस्वरः|उच्चैःस्वर
उच्चैः + -स्वर + .({@-रः@}) a loud sound or voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तम
उच्चैस्तम <i>a.</i> Highest, tallest, loudest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तमाम्
उच्चैस्तमाम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Exceedingly high.<BR>—2 Very loudly<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तर|उच्चैस्तरं
उच्चैस्तर <i>a.</i> Higher, taller, louder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तरम्
उच्चैस्तरम्, -राम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Very loud; Bhāg. 5. 9. 18.<BR>—2 Exceedingly high, on high; उच्चैस्तरां वक्ष्यति शैलराजः Ku. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तराम्
उच्चैस्तरम्, -राम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Very loud; Bhāg. 5. 9. 18.<BR>—2 Exceedingly high, on high; उच्चैस्तरां वक्ष्यति शैलराजः Ku. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चक्
उच्चक् €1 P. To look up steadfastly or dauntlessly; यं चेकितानमनु<BR> चित्तयीमुच्चकन्ति Bhāg. 6. 16. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकित
उच्चकित <i>a.</i> Looking up perplexedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चक्षुस्
उच्चक्षुस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 With the eyes directed upwards, looking upwards; सर्वा उच्चक्षुषः<BR> पश्यन्ति v. l.<BR>—2 With the eyes taken out, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चघनम्
उच्चघनम् A secret smile, a laughter in the mind not expressed in<BR> the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चट्
उच्चट् €1 P. To go away, disappear. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To scare or drive away, expel; मोहतिमिरप्राग्भारमुच्चाटयन्<BR>—2 To destroy, root out; Bh. 3. 129; उच्चाटनीयः करतालिकानाम् N. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटनम्
उच्चाटनम्<BR>—1 Driving away, expulsion, removal from a place; उच्चाटनं त्वमपि<BR> लम्भयसे तदेव Kuval.<BR>—2 Separation.<BR>—3 Eradication; तापत्रयोच्चाटनम् Viś. Guṇā. 533; extirpation (of a plant).<BR>—4 A kind of charm or magical incantation.<BR>—5 Working this charm,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">Page0398-1</a>]<BR> ruining oneʼs enemy, making a person leave his business by magical spells<BR> by making him disgusted with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटनः|उच्चाटन|उच्चाटनं
उच्चाटनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of one of the five arrows of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटित
उच्चाटित <i>a.</i> Driven away; येनाङ्गुष्ठेन पदा दशकन्धरो योजनायुतायुतम्<BR> दिग्विजय उच्चाटितः Bhāg. 5. 24. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटा
उच्चटा<BR>—1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>—2 Habit, usage.<BR>—3 A kind of garlic.<BR>—4 N. of different plants; गुञ्जा, चूडाला, भूम्यामलकी, नागरमुस्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चण्ड|उच्चंड|उच्चण्डः
उच्चण्ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fierce, terrible, formidable; U. 6.<BR>—2 Quick, expeditious.<BR>—3 Loud.<BR>—4 Angry, irascible, violent; बृहत्खण्डमुच्चण्डरोचिः Mv. 1. 45.<BR>—5 Hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चन्द्रः|उच्चन्द्र|उच्चंद्र|उच्चंद्रः
उच्चन्द्रः [उच्छिष्टः चन्द्रो यत्र] The last watch of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चर्
उच्चर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go upwards, to rise; बाष्पमुच्चरति Mbh.; K. 14.<BR>—2 To ascend (as the sun); issue or go forth, go up; बलैश्चलच्चरणविधूतमुच्चरद्धनावलीः<BR> Śi. 17. 52; Māl. 5. 21.<BR>—3 To arise, appear forth, rise (as a voice), to be heard; उच्चचार<BR> निनदोम्भसि तस्याः R. 9. 73, 15. 46, 16. 87; कोलाहलध्वनिरुदचरत्<BR> K. 27; U. 2; Ratn. 1.<BR>—4 To empty the body by evacuations, void oneʼs excrement; तिरस्कृत्योच्चरेत्काष्ठलोष्टपत्रतृणादिना Ms. 4. 49.<BR>—5 To emit (sounds), utter, pronounce; शब्द उच्चरित एव मामगात् R. 11. 73.<BR>—6 (Used in the Ātm.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To quit, leave.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To sin against, be unfaithful (to a husband or wife), transgress<BR> against; धर्ममुच्चरते Sk.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To violate or transgress in general, stray or deviate from; पानशौण्डाः<BR> पथः क्षीबा वृन्दैरुदचरन्त च Bk. 8. 31.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To rise up to, ascend (trans.); यो मघोनि दिवमुच्चरमाणे<BR> N. 5. 48; Śi. 17. 52. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to issue.<BR>—2 To utter, pronounce, declare.<BR>—3 To void oneʼs excrement.<BR>—4 To emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरणम्
उच्चरणम्<BR>—1 Going up or out.<BR>—2 Utterance, pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरित
उच्चरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone up or out, risen.<BR>—2 Uttered. pronounced &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरितम्
उच्चरित + .{@-तम्@} Excrement, faeces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारः|उच्चार
उच्चारः<BR>—1 Utterance, pronunciation, declaration; वर्ण˚, काम˚.<BR>—2 Excrement, dung, faeces; मातुरुच्चार एव सः H. Pr. 16; मूत्रोच्चारसमुत्सर्गम् Ms. 4. 50.<BR>—3 Discharge (in general).<BR>—4 Passage (of heavenly bodies) to another zodiacal sign or asterism.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्चारप्रस्रवणम्, उच्चारप्रस्रावस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारप्रस्रवणम्
उच्चारः + -प्रस्रवणम् Excrement (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारप्रस्रावस्थानम्
उच्चारः + -प्रस्रावस्थानम् A privy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणम्
उच्चारणम्<BR>—1 Pronunciation, utterance; वाचः Śik. 2; वेद˚.<BR>—2 Declaration, announcement, enunciation.<BR>—3 Lifting up; स्कन्धोच्चारणनम्यमानवदनप्रच्योतितोये घटे Pratimā 1. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्चारणार्थ, उच्चारणज्ञः, उच्चारणस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणार्थ
उच्चारणम् + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 useful for pronunciation.<BR>—2 necessary for pronunciation, such as a redundant letter only used to<BR> facilitate pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणज्ञः|उच्चारणज्ञ
उच्चारणम् + -ज्ञः a linguist. उच्चारणज्ञोऽथ गिरा दधानम् Śi. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणस्थानम्
उच्चारणम् + -स्थानम् the part of the throat from which certain sounds (such<BR> as nasals, gutturals &c.) issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारित
उच्चारित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pronounced, uttered.<BR>—2 Having excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारितम्
उच्चारित + .{@-तम्@} Evacuation of the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारक
उच्चारक <i>a.</i> Pronouncing, uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्यमाण|उच्चार्य्यमाण
उच्चार्यमाण <i>a.</i> Which is being pronounced. कस्मैचित्. कार्यायोच्चार्यमाणो<BR> वर्ण इत्संज्ञः । मुग्धबोधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल्
उच्चल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To start, set out; स्थितः स्थितामुच्चलितः प्रयाताम् R. 2. 6; उच्चचाल<BR> बलभित्सखो वशी 11. 51; sometimes with dat. of place; नगरायोदचलम् Dk.<BR>—2 To go or remove away or fly away (from oneʼs place), fly away from;<BR> स्थानादनुच्चलन्नपि Ś. 1. 28; पुष्पोच्चलितषट्पदम् R. 12. 27.<BR>—3 To free or extricate oneself from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल|उच्चलं
उच्चल <i>a.</i> Moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलम्
उच्चल + .({@-लम्@}) Mind, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलनम्
उच्चलनम् Moving away, setting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलित
उच्चलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 On the point of going, setting out.<BR>—2 Gone up or out; winnowed (as grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चावच|उच्चावचः
उच्चावच <i>a.</i> [मयूरव्यंसकादिगण] P. II. 1. 72.<BR>—1 High and low, uneven, irregular, undulating; Ms. 6. 73.<BR>—2 Great and small, variegated, heterogeneous.<BR>—3 Various, multiform, of various kinds, diverse; उच्चावचाश्च पदार्था<BR> भवन्तीति गार्ग्यः Nir.; Ms. 1. 38; Śi. 4. 46; Dk. 48, 104, 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चि
उच्चि €5 U. To collect, gather, accumulate. उच्चिक्यिरे पुष्पफलं<BR> वनानि Bk. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चयः|उच्चय
उच्चयः<BR>—1 A collection, heap, multitude; रूपोच्चयेन Ś. 2. 10; पदोच्चयः<BR> S. D. 2; cf. शिलोच्चय also.<BR>—2 Gathering, collecting (flowers &c.); पुष्पोच्चयम् नाटयति Ś. 4; Ku. 3. 61.<BR>—3 The knot of a womanʼs (wearing) garment (नीवीबन्ध); ‘नारीकट्यंशुकग्रन्थौ नीवी स्यादुच्चयोऽप्यथ’ इति मार्तण्डः<BR> Ki. 8. 15, सखीव काञ्ची पयसा<BR> घनीकृता बभार वीतोच्चयबन्धमंशुकम् 51.<BR>—4 Nīvāra rice (collected by winnowing).<BR>—5 Prosperity, rise; उच्चयापचयौ H. 3. 126.<BR>—6 The opposite side of a triangle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्चयापचयौ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चयापचयौ
उच्चयः + -अपचयौ Prosperity and decline, rise and fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिङ्गटः|उच्चिङ्गट|उच्चिंगटः
उच्चिङ्गटः<BR>—1 A passionate or angry man.<BR>—2 A kind of crab.<BR>—3 A kind of cricket; cf. उच्चिङ्गटस्तृणगढ मत्स्यकोपनयोः पुमान् Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिटङ्गः|उच्चिटङ्ग|उच्चिटंगः
उच्चिट(टि)ङ्गः A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिटिङ्गः|उच्चिटिङ्ग|उच्चिटिंगः
उच्चिट(टि)ङ्गः A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चित्र
उच्चित्र <i>a.</i> With the pictures prominently appearing; उच्चित्रचीनांशुक Māl. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चुम्ब्य
उच्चुम्ब्य <i>ind.</i> Having lifted up and kissed; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूडः|उच्चूड
उच्चूडः, -लः<BR>—1 The flag of a banner, or the banner itself.<BR>—2 An ornament fastened on the top of a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूलः|उच्चूल
उच्चूडः, -लः<BR>—1 The flag of a banner, or the banner itself.<BR>—2 An ornament fastened on the top of a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छन्न|उच्छन्नं
उच्छन्न <i>a.</i> [उद्-छद्-क्त]<BR>—1 Destroyed, cut down (perhaps for उत्सन्न); see उच्छिन्न.<BR>—2 Extinct (as a work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छल्
उच्छल् €1 U. To fly upwards or away, move onwards, wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलत्|उच्छलन्त्
उच्छलत् <i>pres. a.</i><BR>—1 Shining, moving about; Śi. 3. 37; Māl. 3; स्वच्छन्दोच्छलदच्छकच्छकुहरच्छातेतराम्बुच्छटा K. P.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">Page0399-1</a>]<BR>—2 Appearing, bursting forth; Māl. 7.<BR>—3 Moving, going on; <i>ibid.</i><BR>—4 Flying up or away, going up high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0398-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलनम्
उच्छलनम् Going or moving upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलित
उच्छलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Moved, waved above निर्झरोच्छलितशीतलशीकरासारवाही … । नागानन्द 1.<BR>—2 Shaken.<BR>—3 Gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छादनम्
उच्छादनम्<BR>—1 Covering.<BR>—2 Rubbing the body with perfumes; cf. स्नापनोच्छादनेन च Rām. 2. 111. 10.<BR> ‘उच्छादनं समुल्लेखोद्वाहनोद्वर्तनेषु च ।’ इति विश्वकोषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छासन
उच्छासन <i>a.</i> [उत्क्नान्तः शासनम्] Not amenable to rule or command,<BR> ungovernable, unruly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्र
उच्छास्त्र, ˚वर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Contrary or opposed to शास्त्र (civil or religious law-books).<BR>—2 Deviating from or transgressing the law-books; न राज्ञः प्रतिगृह्णीयाल्लुब्धस्योच्छास्त्रवर्तिनः<BR> Y. 1. 140; Ms. 4. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्रवर्तिन्|उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्
उच्छास्त्र, ˚वर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Contrary or opposed to शास्त्र (civil or religious law-books).<BR>—2 Deviating from or transgressing the law-books; न राज्ञः प्रतिगृह्णीयाल्लुब्धस्योच्छास्त्रवर्तिनः<BR> Y. 1. 140; Ms. 4. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिख
उच्छिख <i>a.</i> [उद्गता शिखा यस्य]<BR>—1 Crested, with erected crest; मणिमुकुट इवोच्छिखः U. 3. 18.<BR>—2 Having the flame pointed upwards, flaming, blazing up; कथं न मन्युर्ज्वलयत्युदीरितः<BR> शमीतरुं शुष्कमिवाग्निरुच्छिखः Ki. 1. 32; K. 127; R. 16. 87. —3 Radiant, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिखण्ड
उच्छिखण्ड <i>a.</i> Having an upright tail (as a peacock); Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिङ्घनम्
उच्छिङ्घनम् Breathing through the nostrils, snoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिद्
उच्छिद् €7 U.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To cut off, extirpate, eradicate, destroy; नोच्छिन्द्यादात्मनो<BR> मूलं परेषां चातितृष्णया Mb.; किं वा रिपूंस्तव गुरुः स्वयमुच्छिनत्ति<BR> R. 5. 71, 2. 23; Pt. 1. 47, 365.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To dispel, snap, chase away; उच्छेत्तुं प्रभवति यन्न सप्तसप्तिः Ś. 6. 30;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To snap (thread); आशातन्तुर्न च कथयतात्यन्तमुच्छेदनीयः Māl. 9. 26.<BR>—2 To interfere with, interrupt, stop; न्यायानुच्छिद्य Mb.; तैस्तैर्भावैरनुच्छिन्नाः<BR> S. D. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be cut or snapped.<BR>—2 To be stopped or interrupted, cease; उच्छिद्यन्ते क्रियाः सर्वाः ग्रीष्मे<BR> कुसरितो यथा Pt. 2. 89.<BR>—3 To waste away, fail, be wanting or deficient; एतान्यपि सतां गेहे<BR> नोच्छिद्यन्ते कदाचन Ms. 3. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छित्तिः|उच्छित्ति
उच्छित्तिः <i>f.</i> Extirpation, destruction; परोच्छित्त्या लभ्यामभिलषति<BR> लक्ष्मीं हरिसुते Ki. 10. 63. कोसल˚ Ratn. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिन्न|उच्छिन्नः
उच्छिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Extirpated, destroyed, cut down or off; उच्छिन्नाश्रयकातरेव कुलटा<BR> गोत्रान्तरं श्रीर्गता Mu. 6. 5.<BR>—2 Abject, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिन्नः|उच्छिन्न
उच्छिन्न + .{@-न्नः@} Peace obtained by ceding valuable lands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेत्तृ
उच्छेत्तृ <i>a.</i> An extirpator, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदः|उच्छेद
उच्छेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off.<BR>—2 Extirpation, eradication, destruction, putting an end to; सतां भवोच्छेदकरः<BR> पिता ते R. 14. 74.<BR>—3 Excision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदनम्
उच्छेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off.<BR>—2 Extirpation, eradication, destruction, putting an end to; सतां भवोच्छेदकरः<BR> पिता ते R. 14. 74.<BR>—3 Excision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदिन्
उच्छेदिन् <i>a.</i> Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिरस्
उच्छिरस् <i>a.</i> [उन्नतम् शिरोऽस्य]<BR>—1 With the neck raised (lit.).<BR>—2 High, lofty.<BR>—3 (Hence) Noble, great, exalted; शैलात्मजापि पितुरुच्छिरसोऽभिलाषम्<BR> Ku. 3. 75, 6. 70<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिलीन्ध्र|उच्छिलींध्र
