उच्छूडा
उच्छूडा = उच्चूड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छून|उच्छूनं
उच्छून <i>a.</i> [उद्-श्वि-क्त]<BR>—1 Swollen; प्रबलरुदितोच्छूननेत्रं प्रियायाः Me. 86; उत्तानोच्छूनमण्डूकपाटितोदरसंनिभम्<BR> K. P. 7; अनवरतरुदितोच्छूनताम्रदृष्टिम् Dk. 95; स्वर्गग्रामटिकाविलुण्ठनवृथोच्छूनैः<BR> किमेभिर्भुजैः S. D.<BR>—2 Fat, bulky.<BR>—3 High, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृङ्खल|उच्छृंखल|उच्छृङ्खलं
उच्छृङ्खल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unbridled, unrestrained, uncurbed; ˚वाचा Pt. 3; अन्यदुच्छृङ्खलं<BR> सत्त्वमन्यच्छास्त्रनिवन्त्रितम् Śi. 2. 62;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">Page0400-1</a>]<BR>—2 Self-willed, perverse.<BR>—3 Irregular, desultory, unsystematic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0399-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृङ्गित
उच्छृङ्गित <i>a.</i> Having erected horns; उच्छृङ्गितान्यवृषभाः Śi. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोचनम्
उच्छोचनम् Burning (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोफः|उच्छोफ
उच्छोफः Swelling; पृथूच्छोफभूयांसि मांसानि (जग्ध्वा) Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रावणम्
उच्छ्रावणम् Making one hear loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रि
उच्छ्रि [उद्-श्रि] U.<BR>—1 To rise, be erected. (Ā.)<BR>—2 To raise, erect, lift up. —3 To praise, extol. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To increase; विजयसहजमस्त्रैर्वीर्यमुच्छ्राययिष्यन् Mv. 1. 8.<BR>—2 To raise, erect; उर्ध्वमेनामुच्छ्रापय Vāj. 23. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयः|उच्छ्रय
उच्छ्र(च्छ्रा)यः [उद्-श्रि अच् घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Rising (of a planet &c.); शक्रपाते तथोच्छ्रये Y. 1. 147.<BR>—2 Raising, erecting.<BR>—3 Height, elevation (physical and moral); शृङ्गोच्छ्रायैः कुमुदविशदैर्यो<BR> वितत्य स्थितः खम् Me. 60; K. 105; Ki. 7. 27, 8. 23, 23 17; Śi. 4. 10, 8. 22.<BR>—4 Growth, increase, intensity; गुण˚ Ki. 8. 21, 16. 10; नीतोच्छ्रायम् 5. 31, 31 14.<BR>—5 Pride.<BR>—6 The upright side of a triangle.<BR>—7 A kind of pillar (Junāgaḍh Rock Inscription of Rudradāman, EI. Vol. III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायः|उच्छ्राय
उच्छ्र(च्छ्रा)यः [उद्-श्रि अच् घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Rising (of a planet &c.); शक्रपाते तथोच्छ्रये Y. 1. 147.<BR>—2 Raising, erecting.<BR>—3 Height, elevation (physical and moral); शृङ्गोच्छ्रायैः कुमुदविशदैर्यो<BR> वितत्य स्थितः खम् Me. 60; K. 105; Ki. 7. 27, 8. 23, 23 17; Śi. 4. 10, 8. 22.<BR>—4 Growth, increase, intensity; गुण˚ Ki. 8. 21, 16. 10; नीतोच्छ्रायम् 5. 31, 31 14.<BR>—5 Pride.<BR>—6 The upright side of a triangle.<BR>—7 A kind of pillar (Junāgaḍh Rock Inscription of Rudradāman, EI. Vol. III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयी
उच्छ्र(च्छ्रा)यः + .{@-यी@} (उच्छ्रायी) Plank.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उच्छ्रयोपेत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयोपेत
उच्छ्रयः + -उपेत <i>a.</i> possessing height, high, lofty, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयण
उच्छ्रयण <i>a.</i> Raised, erected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयणम्
उच्छ्रयण + .{@-णम्@} Raising, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायिन्
उच्छ्रायिन्^1 <i>a.</i> High, raised, lofty; Śi. 5. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: corrected after AP90 and MW; confirmed by the source shi. 5.21 (उच्छ्रायिभिर्)..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रित|उच्छ्रितं
उच्छ्रित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, lifted up; नात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचं चैलाजिनकुशोत्तरम् Bg. 6. 11.<BR> H. 2. 123; R. 17. 33.<BR>—2 Gone up, risen; ˚सितांशुकर Śi. 4. 25; K. 206<BR>—3 High, tall, lofty, exalted; अभिययौ स हिमाचलमुच्छ्रितम् Ki. 5. 1;<BR> Bg. 6. 11, 9. 19; पञ्चयोजनमुच्छ्रिता Mb.<BR>—4 Produced, born.<BR>—5 Increasing, growing, Prosperous; अत्युच्छ्रितम् तथात्मानम् (मन्येत)<BR> Ms. 7. 170; उच्छ्रितान्द्वेष्टि दुर्मतिः Rām. 1. 15. 8; increased (in<BR> size or bulk); grown.<BR>—6 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रितिः|उच्छ्रिति
उच्छ्रितिः = उच्छ्रय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रेय
उच्छ्रेय <i>a.</i> High, lofty, tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्लङ्खः
उच्छ्लङ्खः Ved. A part of the human body (used only in dual). केनोच्छ्लङ्खौ<BR> मध्यतः कः प्रतिष्ठाम् Av. 10. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वङ्कः|उच्छ्वङ्क|उच्छ्वंकः
उच्छ्वङ्कः Ved. Gaping; cleaving open; Śat. Br. 5. 4. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वस्
उच्छ्वस् €2 P.<BR>—1 To breathe, live; आत्मेच्छया न शक्यमुच्छ्वसितुमपि K. 175; Ve. 5. 15;<BR> Ms. 3. 72; अनुच्छ्वस्य without breathing, in one breath.<BR>—2 To take heart or courage, cheer up, revive, breathe a sigh of relief;<BR> नाद्याप्युच्छ्वसिति U. 3, 7; त्वत्सन्निधावुच्छ्वसितीव चेतः Ki. 3. 8<BR> is delighted; Śi. 18. 58; Ratn. 4; दिगन्तः Ki. 9. 21.<BR>—3 To open, bloom (as a lotus); नोच्छ्वसिति तपनकिरणैः (कुमुदम्)<BR> V. 3. 16; M. 2. 11; Śi. 10. 58, 11. 15.<BR>—4 To take a deep breath, pant, sigh deeply; निष्पिष्टः कोष्णमुच्छ्वसन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">Page0400-2</a>]<BR> Bk. 6. 120, 14. 55.<BR>—5 To throb, heave, palpitate.<BR>—6 To be loosened or relaxed.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to breathe.<BR>—2 To console, cheer up, delight, give rest; उच्छ्वासयन्त्यः श्लथबन्धनानि;<BR> Ṛs. 6. 8; U. 3; Śi. 9. 34.<BR>—3 To loosen, relax, disjoin; दशमुखभुजोच्छ्वासितप्रस्थसन्धिः Me. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसनम्
उच्छ्वसनम्<BR>—1 Breathing, sighing.<BR>—2 Taking a deep breath, heaving.<BR>—3 Loosening; नीवीबन्धोच्छ्वसनम् Māl. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसित|उच्छ्वसितं
उच्छ्वसित <i>p. p.</i> (Used actively).<BR>—1 Heaving, breathing; U. 3.<BR>—2 Emitting or sending out vapour (refreshed); V. 4.<BR>—3 Full blown, opened, expanded; Māl. 4; ˚मूर्तिः K. 92 raised up, C. P. 13.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Enlivened, gladdened, refreshed; त्वन्निष्यन्दोच्छ्वसितवसुधागन्धसंपर्करम्यः Me. 44.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Inspired or animated with hope; कामस्योच्छ्वसितं मनः Ku. 6. 14.<BR>—5 Breathing a sigh of relief; हृदयमुच्छ्वसितं मम विक्लवम् M. 3. 6;<BR> R. 10. 73; K. 181.<BR>—6 Consoled; उत्कण्ठोच्छ्वसितहृदया Me. 102.<BR>—7 Waving, dishevelled; ˚अलकम् R. 8. 55.<BR>—8 Effaced; (सम्˚) किंचित्समुच्छ्वासितपत्रलेखनम् Ku. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसितम्
उच्छ्वसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Breath, the (very) life; सा कुलपतेरुच्छ्वसितमिव Ś. 3; Ku. 7. 4.<BR>—2 Blooming, blowing.<BR>—3 Exhalation; विशदोच्छ्वसितेन मेदिनी कथयामास कृतार्थतामिव R. 8. 3.<BR>—4 Heaving upheaval, throbbing; केयूरबन्धोच्छ्वसितैर्नुनोद R. 6. 68; V. 1.<BR>—5 Becoming loose or relaxed.<BR>—6 Sighing.<BR>—7 The vital airs of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासः|उच्छ्वास
उच्छ्वासः<BR>—1 Breath, exhalation, breathing out; मुखोच्छ्वासगन्धम् V. 4. 22; Ṛs. 1. 3; Me. 104.<BR>—2 Support of life, being alive; तदद्याप्युच्छ्वासो भवति U. 3. 30; K. 158.<BR>—3 A sigh.<BR>—4 Consolation, encouragement; Amaru. 13.<BR>—5 Expiring, dying.<BR>—6 An air-hole.<BR>—7 A division or chapter of a book, as of the Harṣa-charita; cf. अध्याय.<BR>—8 Froth, foam; सिन्धोरुच्छ्वासे पतयन्तमुक्षणम् Rv. 9. 86. 43.<BR>—9 Swelling up, rising, increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासित
उच्छ्वासित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Breathless, out of breath.<BR>—2 Much, excessive.<BR>—3 Loosened, released.<BR>—4 Detached, separated, divided.<BR>—5 Consoled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासिन्
उच्छ्वासिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Breathing, inhaling air.<BR>—2 Heaving, throbbing; स्तनमध्योच्छ्वासिना कथितः V. 1. 8; Me. 104.<BR>—3 Sighing.<BR>—4 Expiring, dying.<BR>—5 Vanishing, fading away; उच्छ्वासिकालाञ्जनरागमक्ष्णोः Ku. 7. 82.<BR>—6 Pausing, stopping.<BR>—7 Rising, coming forward.<BR>—8 Disjointed, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्|उछ्
उच्छ् €6 P. (उच्छति, औच्छीत्, उच्छितुम्, उष्ट)<BR>—1 To finish.<BR>—2 To bind.<BR>—3 To abandon, transgress.<BR>—4 To cease, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जस्
उज्जस् €4 P. <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To kill, destroy, extirpate (with gen.); बिडौजसोज्जासयितुं जगद्<BR> द्रुहाम् Śi. 1. 37.<BR> … मन्योरुज्जासयात्मनः Bk. 8. 120.<BR>—2 Cause to run away. सद्यस्तद् येदिलस्याप्यतुलमथोज्जासयित्वा जवेन<BR> Śiva B. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जासनम्
उज्जासनम् Killing, slaughter; चोरस्योज्जासनम् Sk. उज्जासनाय<BR> परितः परिवेषकृतां द्विषाम् Śiva B. 26. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयनी
उज्जय(यि)नी N. of a city, the modern Ujjain in Mālvā, the capital<BR> of Vikramāditya. It is one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus (cf.<BR> अवन्ति), and the first meridian of their geographers from which they<BR> calculate longitude; सौधोत्सङ्गप्रणयविमुखो मास्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयिनी
उज्जय(यि)नी N. of a city, the modern Ujjain in Mālvā, the capital<BR> of Vikramāditya. It is one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus (cf.<BR> अवन्ति), and the first meridian of their geographers from which they<BR> calculate longitude; सौधोत्सङ्गप्रणयविमुखो मास्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जागर
उज्जागर <i>a.</i> Excited, irritated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जानकः|उज्जानक
उज्जानकः N. of a province in the North.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जि
उज्जि €1 P.<BR>—1 To win, acquire by conquest, conquer.<BR>—2 To be victorious, triumph. ━<i>Caus.</i> (जापयति)<BR>—1 To cause to conquer.<BR>—2 To help one in winning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जितिः|उज्जिति
उज्जितिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Victory.<BR>—2 N. of certain verses in the Vājasaneyī Saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जेष|उज्जेषः
उज्जेष <i>a.</i> Victorious. ईशानां त्वा भेषजानामुज्जेष आरभामहे Av. 4. 17. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जेषः|उज्जेष
