उत्कुटक + -आसनम् a posture with the face upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुणः|उत्कुण
उत्कुणः<BR>—1 A bug.<BR>—2 A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुल
उत्कुल <i>a.</i> [उत्कान्तः कुलात्] Fallen from the family, disgracing<BR> or dishonouring oneʼs family; यदि यथा वदति क्षितिपस्तथा । त्वमसि<BR> किं पितुरुत्कुलया त्वया ॥ Ś. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूजः|उत्कूज
उत्कूजः The singing (of the cuckoo).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूटः|उत्कूट|उत्कूटं
उत्कूटः [उन्नतं कूटमस्य] A parasol or umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूर्चक
उत्कूर्चक <i>a.</i> With a कूर्च in hand; Hc. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

