उत्कृष्टत्वम्
उत्कृष्टता, -त्वम्<BR> Excellence, eminence; greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कॄ
उत्कॄ €6 U.<BR>—1 To scatter upwards, throw up, pile up or heap; रजोभिस्तुरगोत्कीर्णैः R. 1. 42.<BR>—2 To dig up, excavate.<BR>—3 To engrave, carve, sculpture; उत्कीर्णा इव वासयष्टिषु निशानिद्रालसा<BR> बर्हिणः V. 3. 2; R. 4. 59; see उत्कीर्ण also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर|उत्करः
उत्कर <i>a.</i> (-रा, -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कॄ-अप्] That which piles or throws up or raises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करः|उत्कर
उत्कर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A heap, multitude; नखांशूत्करः Ki. 8. 5.<BR>—2 A pile, stack.<BR>—3 Rubbish, what is thrown up (मूषिकोत्कर) Mk. 3.<BR>—4 A bunch (as of flowers); पादपान्कुसुमोत्करान् Rām. 2. 55. 30;<BR> Bhāg. 7. 10. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करिका
उत्करिका A sort of sweetmeat made with milk, treacle, and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करीय
उत्करीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारः|उत्कार
उत्कारः [कॄ-घञ् कॄ धान्ये P. III. 3. 30]<BR>—1 Winnowing corn.<BR>—2 Piling up corn. उत्कारेण धान्यानामनभीष्टपरिग्रहाः Bk.<BR>—3 One who sows corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारिका
उत्कारिका [कॄ-ण्वुल्] Poultice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्किर
उत्किर <i>a.</i> [कॄ-कर्तरि श] Carrying or bearing away, wafting,<BR> scattering upwards (at the end of comp.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">Page0405-1</a>]<BR> पुष्परेणूत्किरैः R. 1. 38; निनाय सात्यन्तहिमोत्किरानिलाः Ku. 5. 26, 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0404-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्ण|उत्कीर्ण्ण
उत्कीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or piled up, scattered.<BR>—2 Engraven, carved, sculptured; Māl. 5. 10; K. 17, 36, 79, 106, 129, 133, 141, 186, 206;<BR> ˚नामधेयम् engraven with a name.<BR>—3 Bored, perforated; घुण˚ Pt. 3. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कॄत्
उत्कॄत् €10 P. To proclaim, celebrate, praise, extol; महिमानं यदुत्कीर्त्य R. 10. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्तनम्
उत्कीर्तनम्<BR>—1 Crying out, proclaiming.<BR>—2 Praising, celebrating, extolling; S. D. 495.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्तित|उत्कीर्त्तित
उत्कीर्तित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Proclaimed, promulgated.<BR>—2 Praised, celebrated, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचः|उत्कोच
उत्कोचः [उत्कुच्-अञ्]<BR>—1 A bribe (lit. bending one from the right path); Śukra. 1. 297; उत्कोचमिव<BR> ददती K. 232; Dk. 155; उत्कोचजीविनो द्रव्यहीनान् कृत्वा विवासयेत्<BR> Y. 1. 339. संगम्योत्कोचदानादि दत्त्वा सैन्यं प्रयाच्यताम् Parṇāl. 5. 44.<BR>—2 Receiving a bribe; उत्कोचैर्वञ्चनाभिश्च कार्याण्यनुविहन्ति च Mb. 12. 56. 51.<BR>—3 Penalty, tribute; Hc. 4. (Gīrvāṇa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचक|उत्कोचकः
उत्कोचक <i>a.</i> Bribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचकः|उत्कोचक
उत्कोचक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A bribe.<BR>—2 The receiver of a bribe; Ms. 9. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचिन्
उत्कोचिन् To be bribed, corruptible. उत्कोचिनां मृषोक्तीनांवञ्चकानां<BR> च या गतिः Mb. 7. 73. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोटि
उत्कोटि <i>a.</i> Pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोठः|उत्कोठ
उत्कोठः A Kind of leprosy. Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रम्
उत्क्रम् €1 U., €4 P.<BR>—1 To go up, step up, ascend; उत्क्रामन्तं स्थितं वापि Bg. 15. 10.<BR>—2 To step beyond; उत्क्रान्तशैशवौ R. 15. 33; past childhood.<BR>—3 To step out, go out or away, depart; ऊर्ध्वं प्राणा ह्युत्कामन्ति Ms. 2. 120; Mv. 1.<BR>—4 To pass away, die; यच्चाप्युत्क्रामतीश्वरः Bg. 15. 8.<BR>—5 To go or pass over, omit.<BR>—6 To disregard, not to notice, neglect; आर्षं प्रमाणमुत्क्रम्य, धर्ममुत्क्रम्य Mb.<BR>—7 To transgress, violate; उत्क्रान्तसीमा Dk. 101, 97. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (क्रामयति) To cause to go up or ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमः|उत्क्रम
उत्क्रमः<BR>—1 Going up or out, departure.<BR>—2 Progressive increase.<BR>—3 Going astray, deviation, transgression, violation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्क्रमज्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमज्या
उत्क्रमः + -ज्या (in Geometry) The versed sine; Sūrya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमणम्
उत्क्रमणम्<BR>—1 Going up or out, departure.<BR>—2 Ascent, soaring aloft.<BR>—3 Surpassing, exceeding.<BR>—4 The flight or passage of the soul (out of the body), <i>i. e.</i> death<BR> (= प्राणोत्क्रमणम्) देहादुत्क्रमणं चास्मात्पुनर्गर्भे च संभवम्<BR> Ms. 6. 63; विष्वङ्ङ्न्या उत्क्रमणे भवन्ति Kaṭh. 2. 6. 16; Ch. Up. 8. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमणीय
उत्क्रमणीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be transgressed, to be given up or abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्त|उत्क्रांत
उत्क्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone forth or out, departed; उत्क्रान्तमिवासुभिः K. 33; R. 7. 53.<BR>—2 Faded, effaced (as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">Page0405-2</a>]<BR> colour); उत्क्रान्तवर्णक्रमधूसराणाम् R. 16. 17.<BR>—3 Gone over or beyond, passed, surpassed.<BR>—4 Dead.<BR>—5 Trespassing, exceeding, surpassing (actively used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्ति|उत्क्रांति|उत्क्रांतिः
उत्क्रान्ति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going up or out, departure. योगधारणयोत्क्रान्तिः संवादो नारदाजयोः<BR> Bhāg. 12. 12. 7.<BR>—2 The flight or passage of the soul (out of the body), death; उत्क्रान्तिगत्यागतीनाम्<BR> Br. Sūt. 2. 3. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्क्रान्तिधेनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्तिधेनुः
उत्क्रान्ति + -धेनुः A cow gifted at the time of oneʼs death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्तिन्|उत्क्रांतिन्
उत्क्रान्तिन् <i>a.</i> passing away, gone, departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रामः|उत्क्राम
उत्क्रामः<BR>—1 Going out or up, departure.<BR>—2 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>—3 Violation, transgression.<BR>—4 Opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुश्
उत्क्रुश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To cry out, exclaim, cry aloud.<BR>—2 To call out to; उदक्रोशत् स पाण्डवान् Mb.<BR>—3 To proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्ट
उत्क्रुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Crying out, exclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्टम्
उत्क्रुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Crying out, calling, exclaiming. क्ष्वेडितोत्क्रुष्टगर्जितैः Mb. 7. 36. 17.<BR>—2 Loud speaking or conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोशः|उत्क्रोश
उत्क्रोशः<BR>—1 Clamour, outcry, loud noise.<BR>—2 Proclamation.<BR>—3 An osprey (कुररी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्क्रोशपातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोशपातः
उत्क्रोशः + -पातः A kind of dance; श्येनपातोत्क्रोशपातादीनि दर्शयन् Dk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोदः|उत्क्रोद
उत्क्रोदः Ved. Exultation, joy. यथा बन्धान्मुमुचाना उत्क्रोदं कुर्वत<BR> Ts. 7. 5. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लिश्
उत्क्लिश् €9 P. To feel uneasy or distressed. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To excite, stir up, agitate, torment.<BR>—2 To expel, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशः|उत्क्लेश
उत्क्लेशः<BR>—1 Excitement, disquietude, agitation.<BR>—2 Disorder of the humours (of the body).<BR>—3 Sickness; particularly, sea-sickness, nausea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशक|उत्क्लेशकः
उत्क्लेशक <i>a.</i> Causing the disorder of the humours<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशकः|उत्क्लेशक
उत्क्लेशक + .{@-कः@} A kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशन
उत्क्लेशन, -शिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Exciting, stirring up, producing disorder; as in कफ˚<BR> exciting phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशिन्
उत्क्लेशन, -शिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Exciting, stirring up, producing disorder; as in कफ˚<BR> exciting phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेदः|उत्क्लेद
उत्क्लेदः Becoming wet or moist; महानदी चर्मराशेरुत्क्लेदात्ससृजे<BR> यतः Mb. 12. 29. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेदिन्
उत्क्लेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wet.<BR>—2 Making wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्वथ्
उत्क्वथ् P. To boil out, to extract by boiling. ━<i>pass.</i> to<BR> be boiled, to be consumed (by love); K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्
उत्क्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To throw or toss up, raise, set up, erect; उत्क्षिप्तगात्रः Śi. 12. 5, 8. 14;<BR> बलिमाकाश उत्क्षिपेत् Ms. 3. 90; Ṛs. 1. 22; so वाहुम्<BR> भ्रुवम् &c.; R. 6. 14.<BR>—2 To throw away, reject, get rid of.<BR>—3 To emit, vomit up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्त|उत्क्षिप्तः
उत्क्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown upwards, tossed, raised.<BR>—2 Held up, supported; तत्र नागफणोत्क्षिप्तसिंहासन निषेदुषी R. 15. 83.<BR>—3 Seized or overcome with, distracted by, struck with; विस्मय˚ Ratn. 1;<BR> so लोभ˚, अनुराग˚.<BR>—4 Demolished, destroyed.<BR>—5 Thrown out, rejected, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तः|उत्क्षिप्त
उत्क्षिप्त + .{@-प्तः@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">Page0406-1</a>]<BR> The thorn apple, the Dhaūttra plant क्षणं क्षणोत्क्षिप्तगजेन्द्रकृत्तिना Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0405-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तिका
उत्क्षिप्तिका A crescent-shaped ornament worn in the upper part of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेप|उत्क्षेपः
उत्क्षेप <i>a.</i> Throwing up, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपः|उत्क्षेप
उत्क्षेप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Throwing or tossing up; पक्ष्मोत्क्षेप Me. 49.<BR>—2 That which is thrown or tossed up; बिन्दूत्क्षेपान् पिपासुः M. 2. 13.<BR>—3 Sending, despatching.<BR>—4 Throwing away, rejecting.<BR>—5 Vomiting.<BR>—6 The region above the temples (dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपक|उत्क्षेपकः
उत्क्षेपक <i>a.</i> One who throws or tosses up, who or what elevates<BR> or raises; उत्क्षेपकग्रन्थिभेदो करसंदंशहीनकौ Y. 2. 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपकः|उत्क्षेपक
उत्क्षेपक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A stealer of clothes &c.; वस्त्राद्युत्क्षिपत्यपहरतीत्युत्क्षेपकः Mit.<BR>—2 One who sends or orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपणम्
उत्क्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Throwing upwards, lifting or tossing up; अतिमात्रलोहिततलौ बाहू<BR> घटोत्क्षेपणात् Ś. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Throwing upwards, regarded by the Vaiśeṣikas as one of the five <i>karmans</i> q. v.<BR>—3 Vomiting.<BR>—4 Sending away, despatching.<BR>—5 A kind of basket for cleaning corn; a kind of stick for threshing corn.<BR>—6 A fan.<BR>—7 A measure of sixteen Paṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खचित
उत्खचित <i>a.</i> Intermixed, interwoven, set or inlaid with; कुसुमोत्खचितान्<BR> वलीभृतः R. 8. 53, 13. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खन्
उत्खन् €1 P.<BR>—1 To dig up or out, excavate; उत्खातं निधिशङ्कया क्षितितलम् Bh. 3. 4.<BR>—2 To tear up by the roots, eradicate; वङ्गानुत्खाय तरसा R. 4. 36, 33, 14. 73, 18. 22;<BR> Me. 54; Bk. 12. 5, 15. 55.<BR>—3 To draw or tear out (eye &c.); उच्चख्नाते नलेनाऽऽजौ स्फुरत्प्रतपनाऽक्षिणी Bk. 14. 32.<BR>—4 To draw or pull out; Śi. 5. 59, 18. 37; उत्खातखड्गः Ve. 3 unsheathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खात|उत्खातं
उत्खात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Excavated, dug up. उत्खातं निधिशङ्कया क्षितितलं ध्माता गिरेर्घातवः Bh. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Extracted, drawn out; उत्खातं परित्यागशल्यम् U. 3.<BR>—3 Uprooted, plucked up by the roots (lit.); लीला˚ uprooted in sport<BR> U. 3. 16; Māl. 9. 34.<BR>—4 (fig.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Eradicated, totally destroyed, annihilated; किमुत्खातं नन्दवंशस्य<BR> Mu. 1; ˚लवणो मधुरेश्वरः प्राप्तः U. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Deposed, deprived of power or authority; फलैः संवर्धयामासुरुत्खातप्रतिरोपिताः<BR> R. 4. 37 (where उत्खात means ‘uprooted’ also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खातम्
उत्खात + .{@-तम्@} A hole, cavity, hollow, uneven ground; अनुत्खातस्तिमित<BR> not stopped by uneven ground; Ś. 7. 33.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्खातकेलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खातकेलिः|उत्खातकेलि
उत्खात + -केलिः <i>f.</i> digging out earth in sport (by means of horns, tusks<BR> &c.); उत्खातकेलिः शृङ्गाद्यैर्वप्रकीडा निगद्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खातिन्
उत्खातिन् (उत्खात-इनि)<BR>—1 Uneven, having ups and downs, rugged (opp. सम). उत्खातिनी भूमिरिति<BR> मया रश्मिसंयमनाद्रथस्य मन्दीकृतो वेगः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खला
उत्खला A kind of perfume. (See मुरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खिद्
उत्खिद् €6 P. To draw out, extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खेदः|उत्खेद
उत्खेदः Cutting out; drawing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त|उत्तं
उत्त See उन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंस|उत्तंसः
उत्तंस <i>a.</i> Sharpening, whetting (as जिह्वाजाड्य); तथाम्ललवणोत्तंसैर्विविधै<BR> रागखाण्डवैः Rām. 5. 11. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसः|उत्तंस
उत्तंसः [उद् तंस् अच्]<BR>—1 A crest, chaplet, an ornament worn on the crown of the head; उत्तंसानहरत<BR> वारि मूर्धजेभ्यः Śi. 8. 57; सुधांशुकलितोत्तंसस्तापं हरतु वः<BR> शिवः Candr. 5. 59; cf. कर्णोत्तंस.<BR>—2 An ear-ring; Māl. 5. 18; Bv. 2. 55. नोत्तंसं क्षिपति क्षितौ श्रवणतः S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसयति
उत्तंसयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To cause to serve as a crest, to deck, adorn.<BR>—2 To tie or bind up (as hair); उत्तंसयिष्यति कचांस्तव देवि भीमः Ve. 1. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसित
उत्तंसित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having ear-rings.<BR>—2 Put or worn on the crest; चूडोत्तंसितचारुचन्द्रकलिका Bh. 3. 129;<BR> अञ्जलिकिसलय˚ Dk. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तट
उत्तट <i>a.</i> [उत्कान्तः तटम्] Overflowing the bank; उत्तटा<BR> इव नदीरयाः स्थलीम् R. 11. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तन्
उत्तन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To stretch upwards or out.<BR>—2 To try to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Stretched out, spread out, expanded, dilated; उत्तानतारकस्य लोचनयुगलस्य<BR> K. 143; U. 3. 23.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Lying on the back, with the face upwards, supine; Māl. 3; उत्तानोच्छूनमण्डूकपाटितोदरसंनिभे<BR> K. P. 7; पितृपात्रं तदुत्तानं कृत्वा विप्रान्विसर्जयेत् Y. 1. 248.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Upright, erect.<BR>—3 Open, turned upwards; उत्तान आस्येन हविर्जुहोति Mb. 12. 245. 27.<BR> उत्तानपाणिद्वयसंनिवेशात् Ku. 3. 45; ˚रश्मिषु Pt. 3. 151.<BR>—4 Open, unreserved, frank, candid; स्वभावोत्तानहृदयम् Ś. 5; frank-minded.<BR>—5 Elevated; Māl. 7.<BR>—6 Concave; having the mouth upwards.<BR>—7 Shallow<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्तानार्थ, उत्तानकूर्मकम्, उत्तानपट्टम्, उत्तानपत्रकः, उत्तानपद्, उत्तानपाद, उत्तानशय, उत्तानशीवन्, उत्तानहस्त, उत्तानहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानार्थ
उत्तान + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> Superficial, shallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानकूर्मकम्
उत्तान + -कूर्मकम् a particular posture in sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपट्टम्
उत्तान + -पट्टम् A pavement; व्यूढं चोत्तानपट्टं सकलकनखले …<BR> यश्चकार … (An Abu inscription in the reign of Bhūmadeva. Ind. Ant. Vol. XI).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपत्रकः|उत्तानपत्रक
उत्तान + -पत्रकः a^1 species of Ricinus (रक्तैरण्ड).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपद्
उत्तान + -पद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 vegetation, the whole creation of upward germinating plants (Sāy.).<BR>—2 One whose legs are extended (in parturition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपाद|उत्तानपादः
उत्तान + -पाद <i>a.</i> with extended legs (children).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपादः|उत्तानपाद
उत्तान + -पाद + .({@-दः@})<BR>—1 N. of a king, father of Dhruva.<BR>—2 the Supreme Spirit. ˚जः N. of Dhruva, the polar star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशय|उत्तानशयः
उत्तान + -शय <i>a.</i> sleeping supinely or on the back, lying with the<BR> face upwards; कदा उत्तानशयः पुत्रकः जनयिष्यति मे हृदयाह्लादम् K. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशयः|उत्तानशय
उत्तान + -शय + .({@-यः, -या@}) a little child, suckling, infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशया
उत्तान + -शय + .({@-यः, -या@}) a little child, suckling, infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशीवन्
उत्तान + -शीवन् <i>a.</i> lying extended; stagnant. आप उत्तानशीवरीः Av. 3. 21. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानहस्त
उत्तान + -हस्त <i>a.</i> having the hands stretched out in prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानहस्तौ
उत्तान + -हस्त + .({@-स्तौ@}) (du.) the two hands with the fingers stretched out and<BR> with the backs turned towards the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानहृदय
उत्तान + -हृदय Open-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानकः|उत्तानक
उत्तानकः A species of the Cyperus grass (उच्चटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानिका
उत्तानिका N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानित
उत्तानित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Raised, up-lifted; K. 38, 209, 298.<BR>—2 Dilated, expanded; K. 82, 84.<BR>—3 Wide open (the mouth); K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्
उत्तप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To warm, make hot, heat thoroughly, scorch, burn, sear; उत्तप्तनाराचलीलाम्<BR> Śi. 11. 50; उत्तपति सुवर्णं सुवर्णकारः Mbh. melts; so चैत्रो<BR> मैत्रस्य पाणिमुत्तपति. (Used in the Ā. when used intransitively ‘to shine’<BR>, or when it has a limb of the body for its object; उत्तपमानः<BR> आतपः Bk. 8. 15 scorching heat; Śi. 20. 40; उत्तपते पाणी Mbh.).<BR>—2 To pain, torment, torture by heat; कुसुमेषुरुत्तपति यद्विशिखैः Śi. 9. 67.<BR>—3 To excite, urge on, press hard. ━<i>Caus.</i> To warm, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तपनः|उत्तपन
उत्तपनः A particular kind of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्त|उत्तप्तं|उत्तप्तः
उत्तप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Burnt, heated, seared, made red-hot. ˚कनक K. 43, 36; U. 5. 14.<BR>—2 Bathed, washed.<BR>—3 Anxious.<BR>—4 Enraged, inflamed, fired; Ve. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्तम्
उत्तप्त + .{@-प्तम्@}<BR>—1 Dried flesh.<BR>—2 Great heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापः|उत्ताप
उत्तापः<BR>—1 Great heat, inflammation.<BR>—2 Affliction, torment, distress.<BR>—3 Excitement, passion; प्रत्यूहः सर्वसिद्धीनामुत्तापः प्रथमः किल H. 3. 38.<BR>—4 Anxiety, ardour.<BR>—5 Energy, effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापित
उत्तापित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heated, made hot.<BR>—2 Tormented, distressed.<BR>—3 Excited, urged, roused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्
उत्तम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be afflicted or distressed, lose heart, faint.<BR>—2 To be uneasy or impatient, be anxious; हृदय मा उत्ताम्य Ś. 1;<BR> K. 85, 231, 268, 275; Māl. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमनम्
उत्तमनम् Losing heart, impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम|उत्तमः
उत्तम <i>a.</i> [उद्-तमप्]<BR>—1 Best, excellent (oft. in comp.); उत्तमे शिखरे देवी Mahānār. Up. 15. 5.<BR> स उत्तमः पुरुषः Ch. Up. 8. 12. 3. उत्तमः पुरुषस्त्वन्यः<BR> Bg. 15. 17. द्विजोत्तमः the best of Brāhmaṇas; so सुर˚, नर˚<BR> &c.; प्रायेणाधममध्यमोत्तमगुणः संसर्गतो जायते Bh. 2. 67.<BR>—2 Foremost, uppermost, highest (opp. हीन, जघन्य).<BR>—3 Most elevated, chief, principal.<BR>—4 Greatest, first; स गच्छत्युत्तमस्थानम् Ms. 2. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमः|उत्तम
उत्तम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 The third person (= first person according to English phraseology).<BR> (pl.) N. of a people; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमा
उत्तम + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 An excellent woman.<BR>—2 A kind of pustule or pimple.<BR>—3 The plant Asclepias Rosea Roxb. (दुग्धिका; Mar. भुईआंवळी, अळिता).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्तमाङ्गम्, उत्तमाधम, उत्तमाम्भस्, उत्तमारणी, उत्तमार्धः, उत्तमार्ध्य, उत्तमाहः, उत्तमोपपद, उत्तमौजस्, उत्तमगन्धाढ्य, उत्तमगुण, उत्तमदशतालम्, उत्तमपदम्, उत्तमपुरुषः, उत्तमपूरुषः, उत्तमफलिनी, उत्तमलाभः, उत्तमवयसम्, उत्तमव्रता, उत्तमवेशः, उत्तमशाखः, उत्तमश्रुत, उत्तमश्लोक, उत्तमकः, उत्तमसंग्रहः, उत्तमसाहसः, उत्तमसाहसम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाङ्गम्
उत्तम + -अङ्गम् ‘the best limb of the body’, the head; कश्चिद् द्विषत्खड्गहृतोत्तमाङ्गः<BR> R. 7. 51; Ms. 1. 93, 8. 300; Ku. 7. 41; Bg. 11. 27 the back; तान् क्षिप्रं<BR> व्रज सतताग्निहोत्रयाजिन् । मत्तुल्यो भव गरुडोत्तमाङ्गयानः ॥ Mb. 7. 143. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाधम
उत्तम + -अधम <i>a.</i> high and low; ˚मध्यम good, middling, and bad;<BR> high, low, and middling; (the order is often reversed); cf. भक्षयित्वा<BR> बहून्मत्स्यानुत्तमाधममध्यमान् Pt. 1. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाम्भस्
उत्तम + -अम्भस् <i>n.</i> a sort of satisfaction (acquiescence) one of the<BR> nine kinds of तुष्टि in Sāṅ. Phil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमारणी
उत्तम + -अरणी the plant Asparagus Racemosus (इन्दीवरी शतावरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमार्धः|उत्तमार्ध
उत्तम + -अर्धः<BR>—1 the best half.<BR>—2 the last half or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमार्ध्य
उत्तम + -अर्ध्य <i>a.</i> pertaining to the best half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाहः|उत्तमाह
उत्तम + -अहः the last or latest day; a fine or lucky day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमोपपद
उत्तम + -उपपद <i>a.</i> one to whom the best term is applicable, best,<BR> excellent. {@ऋणः, -ऋणिकः@} (उत्तमर्णः) a creditor (opp. अधमर्णः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">Page0407-2</a>]<BR> धारेरुत्तमर्णः P. I. 4. 35; अधमर्णार्थसिद्धपर्थमुत्तमर्णेन चोदितः<BR> Ms. 8. 47, 50; Y. 2. 42; Śukra. 4. 831. (pl.) N. of a people; V. P.; Mārk. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमौजस्
उत्तम + -ओजस् <i>a.</i> ‘of excellent valour’, N. of one of the warriors of<BR> the Mahābhārata; उत्तमौजाश्च वीर्यवान् Bg. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमगन्धाढ्य
उत्तम + -गन्धाढ्य <i>a.</i> possessing copiously the most delicious fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमगुण
उत्तम + -गुण <i>a.</i> of the best qualities, best, highest; विघ्नैः पुनः<BR> पुनरपि प्रतिहन्यमानाः प्रारब्धमुत्तमगुणा न परित्यजन्ति Mu. 2. 17. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमदशतालम्
उत्तम + -दशतालम् A sculptural measurement in which the whole height<BR> of an image is generally divided into 120 equal parts. The same measurement<BR> in 112 equal parts is called उत्तमनवताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमपदम्
उत्तम + -पदम् a high office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमपुरुषः|उत्तमपुरुष
उत्तम + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः —1 the third person in verbal conjugation;<BR> (= first person according to English phraseology; in Sanskrit, verbs are<BR> conjugated by putting the English<BR> 1st person last and 3rd person first).<BR>—2 the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—3 an excellent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमपूरुषः|उत्तमपूरुष
उत्तम + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः —1 the third person in verbal conjugation;<BR> (= first person according to English phraseology; in Sanskrit, verbs are<BR> conjugated by putting the English<BR> 1st person last and 3rd person first).<BR>—2 the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—3 an excellent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमफलिनी
उत्तम + -फलिनी <i>f.</i> The plant Oxystelma Esculentum (Mar. दुधी, दुधाणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमलाभः|उत्तमलाभ
उत्तम + -लाभः an excellent profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमवयसम्
उत्तम + -वयसम् The last period of life; Śat. Br. 12. 9. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमव्रता
उत्तम + -व्रता A wife devoted to the husband; हृदयस्येव शोकाग्निसंतप्तस्योत्तमव्रताम् Bk. 9. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमवेशः|उत्तमवेश
उत्तम + -वेशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमशाखः|उत्तमशाख
उत्तम + -शाखः<BR>—1 a tree having excellent branches.<BR>—2 N. of a region<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमश्रुत
उत्तम + -श्रुत <i>a.</i> Possessing the utmost learning. Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमश्लोक
उत्तम + -श्लोक <i>a.</i> of excellent fame, illustrious, glorious, well-known, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमकः|उत्तमक
उत्तम + -कः N. of Viṣṇu, क उत्तमश्लोकगुणानुवादात् पुमान् विरज्येत<BR> विना पशुघ्नात् Bhāg. 10. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसंग्रहः|उत्तमसङ्ग्रह
उत्तम + -संग्रहः (˚स्त्री˚) intriguing with another manʼs wife, <i>i. e.</i><BR> speaking with her privately, looking amorously at her &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसाहसः|उत्तमसाहस
उत्तम + -साहसः, -साहसम् —1 the highest (of the fixed) pecuniary punishments;<BR> a fine of 1000 (or according to some 80,000) paṇas; Ms. 9. 240; Y. 1. 366;<BR> पणानां द्वे शते सार्धे प्रथमः साहसः स्मृतः । मध्यमः पञ्च<BR> विज्ञेयः सहस्रं त्वेष चोत्तमः ॥ Capital punishment, banishment,<BR> confiscation, and mutilation are also regarded as forms of this punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसाहसम्
उत्तम + -साहसः, -साहसम् —1 the highest (of the fixed) pecuniary punishments;<BR> a fine of 1000 (or according to some 80,000) paṇas; Ms. 9. 240; Y. 1. 366;<BR> पणानां द्वे शते सार्धे प्रथमः साहसः स्मृतः । मध्यमः पञ्च<BR> विज्ञेयः सहस्रं त्वेष चोत्तमः ॥ Capital punishment, banishment,<BR> confiscation, and mutilation are also regarded as forms of this punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

