उत्तर + -अभिमुख <i>a.</i> Turned towards the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरायनम्
उत्तर + -अयनम् (˚यणं. न being changed to ण)<BR>—1 the progress of the sun to the north (of the equator); अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः<BR> शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम् Bg. 8. 24. cf. भानोर्मकरसंकान्तेः षण्मासा<BR> उत्तरायणम् । कर्कादेस्तु तथैव स्यात्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">Page0408-2</a>]<BR> षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम् ॥<BR>—2 the period or time of the summer solstice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराराणिः
उत्तर + -अराणिः, -अराणी <i>f.</i> the upper अरणि (which by cutting becomes<BR> the प्रमन्थ or churner); दारुपात्राणि सर्वाणि अरणिं चोत्तरारणिम्<BR> (दत्त्वा) Rām. 6. 111. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराराणी
उत्तर + -अराणिः, -अराणी <i>f.</i> the upper अरणि (which by cutting becomes<BR> the प्रमन्थ or churner); दारुपात्राणि सर्वाणि अरणिं चोत्तरारणिम्<BR> (दत्त्वा) Rām. 6. 111. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरार्थ
उत्तर + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> for the sake of what follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरार्धम्
उत्तर + -अर्धम्<BR>—1 the upper part of the body.<BR>—2 the northern part.<BR>—3 the latter half (opp. पूर्वार्ध).<BR>—4 the further end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरार्ध्य
उत्तर + -अर्ध्य <i>a.</i> being on the northern side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहः|उत्तराह
उत्तर + -अहः the following day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराभासः|उत्तराभास
उत्तर + -आभासः a false reply, an indirect, evasive, or prevaricating<BR> reply. ˚ता, -त्वम् the semblance of a reply without reality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशा
उत्तर + -आशा the northern direction. ˚अधिपतिः, -पतिः the regent<BR> of the northern direction, an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराषाढा
उत्तर + -आषाढा<BR>—1 the 21st lunar mansion consisting of three stars.<BR>—2 N. of bread-fruit or Jak tree (Mar. फणस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरासङ्गः|उत्तरासङ्ग|उत्तरासंग
उत्तर + -आसङ्गः<BR>—1 an upper garment; कृतोत्तरासङ्गम् K. 43; Śi. 2. 19; Ku. 5. 16.<BR>—2 contact with the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेतर
उत्तर + -इतर <i>a.</i> other than उत्तर <i>i. e.</i> southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेतरा
उत्तर + -इतर + .({@-रा@}) the southern direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तर
उत्तर + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> [उत्तरस्मादुत्तरः]<BR>—1 more and more, higher and higher, further and further.<BR>—2 successive, ever increasing; ˚स्नेहेन दृष्टः Pt. 1; Y. 2. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तरम्
उत्तर + -उत्तर + .({@-रम्@})<BR>—1 a reply to an answer, reply on reply; अलमुत्तरोत्तरेण Mu. 3.<BR>—2 conversation, a rejoinder.<BR>—3 excess, exceeding quantity or degree.<BR>—4 succession, gradation, sequence.<BR>—5 descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तरम्
उत्तर + -उत्तर + .({@-रम्@}) <i>ind.</i> higher and higher, in constant continuation, more<BR> and more उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षः K. P. 10; उत्तरोत्तरं वर्धते H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तरिन्
उत्तर + -उत्तरिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ever-increasing.<BR>—2 one following the other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरौष्ठः|उत्तरौष्ठ
उत्तर + -ओष्ठः the upper lip (उत्तरो-रौ-ष्ठः). Vārt. on P. VI. 1. 94.<BR> ओत्वोष्ठयोस्समासे वा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकाण्डम्
उत्तर + -काण्डम् the seventh book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकायः|उत्तरकाय
उत्तर + -कायः the upper part of the body; तं वाहनादवनतोत्तरकायमीषत् R. 9. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकालः|उत्तरकाल
उत्तर + -कालः<BR>—1 future time.<BR>—2 time calculated from one full moon to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकुरु|उत्तरकुरुः
उत्तर + -कुरु (<i>m.</i> pl.) one of the nine divisions of the world, the<BR> country of the northern Kurus (said to be a country of eternal beatitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकोसलाः
उत्तर + -कोसलाः (<i>m.</i> pl.) the northern Kosalas; पितुरनन्तरमुत्तरकोसलान् R. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकोशला
उत्तर + -कोशला the city of Ayodhyā; यदुपतेः क्व गता मथुरा पुरी<BR> रघुपतेः क्व गतोत्तरकोशला ॥ Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरक्रिया
उत्तर + -क्रिया funeral rites, obsequies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरखण्डम्
उत्तर + -खण्डम् the last section of a book^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरखण्डनम्
उत्तर + -खण्डनम् refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरगीता
उत्तर + -गीता N. of a section of the sixth book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरग्रन्थः|उत्तरग्रन्थ
उत्तर + -ग्रन्थः supplement to a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरच्छदः|उत्तरच्छद
उत्तर + -च्छदः a bed-covering, covering (in general); शय्योत्तरच्छदविमर्दकृशाङ्गरागम्<BR> R. 5. 65, 17. 21; नागचर्मोत्तरच्छदः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज
उत्तर + -ज <i>a.</i> born subsequently or afterwards; चतुर्दश प्रथमजः<BR> पुनात्युत्तरजश्च षट् Y. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज्या
उत्तर + -ज्या the versed sine of an arc (Wilson); the second half of the<BR> chord halved by the versed sine (B. and R.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज्योतिषाः
उत्तर + -ज्योतिषाः (<i>m.</i> pl.) the northern Jyotiṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरततिः
उत्तर + -ततिः <i>f.</i> Ectype (lit. subsequent proceedings) उत्तरस्यां<BR> ततौ तत्प्रकृतित्वात् MS. 10. 4. 25. (शबर explains उत्तरस्यां<BR> ततौ as विकृतौ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतन्त्रम्
उत्तर + -तन्त्रम् N. of a supplementary section in the medical work of Suśruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतापनीयम्
उत्तर + -तापनीयम् N. of the second part of the नृसिंहतापनीयोपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदायक
उत्तर + -दायक <i>a.</i> replying, disobedient, pert, impertinent; दुष्टा<BR> भार्या शठं मित्रं मृत्याश्चोत्तरदायकाः H. 2. 110.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">Page0409-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदिश्
उत्तर + -दिश् <i>f.</i> the north. {@˚ईशः, -पालः@}<BR>—1 Kubera, the regent of the north.<BR>—2 the planet बुध. ˚बलिन्<BR>—1 the planet Venus.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदेशः|उत्तरदेश
उत्तर + -देशः the country towards the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरधेय
उत्तर + -धेय <i>a.</i> to be done subsequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरनारायणः|उत्तरनारायण
उत्तर + -नारायणः the second part of the नारायणसूक्त or पुरुषसूक्त (Rv. 10. 90.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपक्षः|उत्तरपक्ष
उत्तर + -पक्षः<BR>—1 the northern wing or side.<BR>—2 the dark half of a lunar month.<BR>—3 the second part of an argument, <i>i. e.</i> a reply, the reason <i>pro</i>.<BR> (opp. पूर्वपक्ष); प्रापयन् पवनव्याधेर्गिरमुत्तरपक्षताम् Śi. 2. 15.<BR>—4 a demonstrated truth or conclusion.<BR>—5 the minor proposition in a syllogism.<BR>—6 (in Mīm.) the fifth member of an <i>Adhikaraṇa</i>, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपटः|उत्तरपट
उत्तर + -पटः<BR>—1 an upper garment.<BR>—2 a bed-covering (उत्तरच्छदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपथः|उत्तरपथ
उत्तर + -पथः the northern way, way leading to the north; the northern<BR> country; P. V. 1. 77. उत्तरपथेनाहृतं च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपथिक
उत्तर + -पथिक <i>a.</i> travelling in the northern country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपदम्
उत्तर + -पदम्<BR>—1 the last member of a compound.<BR>—2 a word that can be compounded with another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपदिक
उत्तर + -पदिक, -पदकीय <i>a.</i> relating to, studying, or knowing the<BR> last word or term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपदकीय
उत्तर + -पदिक, -पदकीय <i>a.</i> relating to, studying, or knowing the<BR> last word or term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपर्वतकम्
उत्तर + -पर्वतकम् A variety of hides. Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपश्चार्धः|उत्तरपश्चार्ध
उत्तर + -पश्चार्धः the northwestern half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपश्चिम|उत्तरपश्चिमः
उत्तर + -पश्चिम <i>a.</i> northwestern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपश्चिमः|उत्तरपश्चिम
उत्तर + -पश्चिम + .({@-मः@}) the northwestern country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपश्चिमा
उत्तर + -पश्चिम + .({@-मा@}) [उत्तरस्याः पश्चिमायाश्च दिशोन्तरालम्] the northwest;<BR> आलोकयन्नुत्तरपश्चिमेन Mb. 12. 335. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपादः|उत्तरपाद
उत्तर + -पादः the second division of a legal plaint, that part which<BR> relates to the reply or defence; पूर्वपक्षः स्मृतः पादो द्वितीयश्चोत्तरः<BR> स्मृतः । क्रियापादस्तृतीयः स्याच्चतुर्थो निर्णयः स्मृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपुरस्तात्
उत्तर + -पुरस्तात् <i>ind.</i> north-eastward (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपुराणम्
उत्तर + -पुराणम् N. of a Jaina work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपुरुषः|उत्तरपुरुष
उत्तर + -पुरुषः = उत्तमपुरुषः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपूर्व
उत्तर + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> north-eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपूर्वा|उत्तरपूर्व्वा
उत्तर + -पूर्व + .({@-र्वा@}) the north-east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरप्रच्छदः|उत्तरप्रच्छद
उत्तर + -प्रच्छदः a cover lid, quilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरप्रत्युत्तरम्
उत्तर + -प्रत्युत्तरम्<BR>—1 a dispute, debate, a rejoinder, retort.<BR>—2 the pleadings in a law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरफल्गुनी
उत्तर + -फल्गुनी, -फाल्गुनी the twelfth lunar mansion consisting<BR> of two stars (having the figure of a bed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरफाल्गुनी
उत्तर + -फल्गुनी, -फाल्गुनी the twelfth lunar mansion consisting<BR> of two stars (having the figure of a bed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरभागः|उत्तरभाग
उत्तर + -भागः The second part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरभाद्रपद्
उत्तर + -भाद्रपद्, -भाद्रपदा<BR>—1 the 26th lunar mansion consisting of two stars (figured by a couch).<BR>—2 N. of a plant (Mar. कडुनिंब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरभाद्रपदा
उत्तर + -भाद्रपद्, -भाद्रपदा<BR>—1 the 26th lunar mansion consisting of two stars (figured by a couch).<BR>—2 N. of a plant (Mar. कडुनिंब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरमन्द्रा
उत्तर + -मन्द्रा a loud but slow manner of singing. ˚मन्द्राद्या <i>a.</i><BR> particular मूर्च्छना in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरमात्रम्
उत्तर + -मात्रम् a mere reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरमीमांसा
उत्तर + -मीमांसा the later Mīmāmsā, the Vedānta Philosophy, an inquiry<BR> into the nature of Brahman or Jṅāna Kāṇḍa (distinguished from मीमांसा<BR> proper which is usually called पूर्वमीमांसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरयुगम्
उत्तर + -युगम् A particular measure (= 13 Aṅgulas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तररहित
उत्तर + -रहित <i>a.</i> without a reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तररामचरितम्
उत्तर + -रामचरितम्, -त्रम् N. of a celebrated drama by Bhavabhūti, which<BR> describes the later life of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्रम्
उत्तर + -रामचरितम्, -त्रम् N. of a celebrated drama by Bhavabhūti, which<BR> describes the later life of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तररूपम्
उत्तर + -रूपम् The second of two combined vowels or consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरलक्षणम्
उत्तर + -लक्षणम् the indication of an actual reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरलोमन्
उत्तर + -लोमन् <i>a.</i> having the hair turned upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवयसम्
उत्तर + -वयसम्, -स् <i>n.</i> old age, the declining period of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरस्
उत्तर + -वयसम्, -स् <i>n.</i> old age, the declining period of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवरितः
उत्तर + -वरितः a kind of small syringe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवल्ली
उत्तर + -वल्ली <i>f.</i> N. of the second section of the काठकोपनिषद्<BR> when divided into two अध्यायs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवस्त्रम्
उत्तर + -वस्त्रम्, -वासस् <i>n.</i> an upper garment, mantle, cloak; जग्राह<BR> तामुत्तरवस्त्रदेशे Mb. 3. 268. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवासस्
उत्तर + -वस्त्रम्, -वासस् <i>n.</i> an upper garment, mantle, cloak; जग्राह<BR> तामुत्तरवस्त्रदेशे Mb. 3. 268. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवादिन्
उत्तर + -वादिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a defendant, respondent; (Opp. पूर्ववादिन्.) साक्षिषूभयतः सत्सु<BR> साक्षिणः पूर्ववादिनः । पूर्वपक्षेऽधरीभूते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">Page0409-2</a>]<BR> भवन्त्युत्तरवादिनः ॥ Y. 2. 17.<BR>—2 one whose claims are of later date than anotherʼs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरविद्
उत्तर + -विद्, -वेदन or {@वेदिन्@} An elephant sensitive to slight<BR> stimuli (Mātaṅga L. 1. 29, 9. 39).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवेदन
उत्तर + -विद्, -वेदन or {@वेदिन्@} An elephant sensitive to slight<BR> stimuli (Mātaṅga L. 1. 29, 9. 39).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवेदिन्
उत्तर + -विद्, -वेदन or {@वेदिन्@} An elephant sensitive to slight<BR> stimuli (Mātaṅga L. 1. 29, 9. 39).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवीथिः|उत्तरवीथि
उत्तर + -वीथिः <i>f.</i> The northern orbit; Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवेदिः|उत्तरवेदि
उत्तर + -वेदिः<BR>—1 the northern altar made for the sacred fire.<BR>—2 N. of a Tīrtha near the कुरुक्षेत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसक्थम्
उत्तर + -सक्थम् the left thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसंज्ञित
उत्तर + -संज्ञित <i>a.</i> denoted or named in reply (as a witness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसंज्ञितः|उत्तरसञ्ज्ञित
उत्तर + -संज्ञित + .({@-तः@}) hearsay-witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाक्षिन्
उत्तर + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a witness for the defence.<BR>—2 a witness deposing to facts from the reports of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाधक|उत्तरसाधकः
उत्तर + -साधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 finishing what remains or follows, assisting at a ceremony.<BR>—2 who or what proves a reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाधकः|उत्तरसाधक
उत्तर + -साधक + .({@-कः@}) an assistant, helper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरहनुः|उत्तरहनु
उत्तर + -हनुः Ved. the upper jaw-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्गम्
उत्तरङ्गम् [उत्तरमङ्गं शकन्ध्वा˚ गण] A wooden arch surmounting<BR> the door-frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतर
उत्तरतर <i>a.</i> Still further, or higher, remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतः
उत्तरतः, उत्तरात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the north; to the north;<BR>—2 To the left (opp. दक्षिणतः).<BR>—3 At the top, above.<BR>—4 Behind.<BR>—5 Afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्
उत्तरतः, उत्तरात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the north; to the north;<BR>—2 To the left (opp. दक्षिणतः).<BR>—3 At the top, above.<BR>—4 Behind.<BR>—5 Afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्र
उत्तरत्र <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Subsequently, later or further on, below (in a work), in the sequel.<BR>—2 In the second case (opp. पूर्वत्र in the first case).<BR>—3 Northward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहि
उत्तराहि <i>ind.</i> [उत्तर-आहि] उत्तराञ्च P. V. 3. 38. Northerly,<BR> to the north of (with abl.); उत्तराहि वसन् रामः समुद्रात् .. Bk. 8. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरिन्
उत्तरिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Superior.<BR>—2 Increasing, becoming more and more intensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीयम्
उत्तरीयम्^1, -यकम्<BR> [उत्तर-छ-वा-कप्] An upper garment; स्तनोत्तरीयाणि<BR> भवन्ति सङ्गान्निर्मोकपट्टाः फणिभिर्विमुक्ताः R. 16. 17, 43.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीयकम्
उत्तरीयम्^1, -यकम्<BR> [उत्तर-छ-वा-कप्] An upper garment; स्तनोत्तरीयाणि<BR> भवन्ति सङ्गान्निर्मोकपट्टाः फणिभिर्विमुक्ताः R. 16. 17, 43.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेण
उत्तरेण <i>ind.</i> [उत्तर-एनप्] (with gen., acc. or at the end<BR> of comp.) Northward, on the north side of; तत्रागारं धनपतिगृहानुत्तरेणास्मदीयम्<BR> Me. 77, v. l.; K. 120; निषधस्योत्तरेण तु V. P.; Māl. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेद्युः
उत्तरेद्युः <i>ind.</i> P. V. 3. 22. On a subsequent day, on the day<BR> following, tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंग|उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्गं
उत्तरङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ruffled or washed by waves, inundated; trembling, tremulous; कशाप्रहारभयेन<BR> जातकम्पोत्तरङ्गाः (तुरङ्गाः) Mu. 6. 3.<BR>—2 With surging waves; प्रत्यग्रहीत् पार्थिववाहिनीं तां भागीरथीं शोण<BR> इवोत्तरङ्गः R. 7. 36; Ku. 3. 48.<BR>—3 Bouncing; Dk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत्तरङ्गः
उत्तरङ्ग + .{@-गः^1@} A high wave. Ks. 123. 196.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260426. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्गि
उत्तरङ्गि <i>a.</i> Heaving, panting; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर्जनम्
उत्तर्जनम् [उच्चैस्तर्जनम्] Violent threatening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तलित
उत्तलित Thrown or cast upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान see under उत्तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताल|उत्तालः
उत्ताल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Great, strong; अनुत्तालतालवृन्तवात K. 251.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Violent, loud (as sound); Māl. 1; उत्तेरुरुत्तालखुरारवं द्रुताः Śi. 12. 31.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Roaring, gusty (wind); उत्तालः किङ्किणीनामनवरतरणत्कारहेतुः<BR> पताकाः Māl. 5. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">Page0410-1</a>]<BR>—3 Formidable, terrific, fierce; उत्तालास्त इमे गभीरपयसः पुण्याः<BR> सरित्संगमाः U. 2. 30; ˚तुमुल U. 6; Śi. 20. 68; Māl. 5. 11, 23.<BR>—4 Huge, of monstrous shape; ˚ताडका Mv. 1. 37. शिवश्चोत्तालकुन्ताग्रः<BR> Śiva B. 13. 53.<BR>—5 Arduous, difficult.<BR>—6 Manifest, distinctly visible; तूर्यारावैराहितोत्तालतालैः Śi. 18. 54<BR>—7 Speedy, swift.<BR>—8 Best, excellent; Śi. 12. 31.<BR>—9 Elevated, lofty, tall; उत्तालतालीवनम् Śi. 3. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तालः|उत्ताल
उत्ताल + .{@-लः@} An ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तालम्
उत्ताल + .{@-लम्@} A particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तावल
उत्तावल <i>a.</i> Impatient, hurrying Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तिज्
उत्तिज् <i>Caus.</i> P. To excite, stimulate, instigate, stir up, animate, provoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजक
उत्तेजक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Instigating, stirring up.<BR>—2 Exciting, stimulating; क्षुध˚, काम˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजनम्
उत्तेजनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Excitement, instigation, animating, stirring up; ˚समर्थः श्लोकैः Mu. 4; Mv. 2.<BR>—2 Urging on, driving.<BR>—3 Sending, despatching.<BR>—4 Whetting, sharpening, furbishing, polishing (weapons &c.); मन्दरकूटकोटिव्याघट्टनोत्तेजना Śi. 3. 6.<BR>—5 An exciting speech.<BR>—6 An inducement, incentive, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजना
उत्तेजनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Excitement, instigation, animating, stirring up; ˚समर्थः श्लोकैः Mu. 4; Mv. 2.<BR>—2 Urging on, driving.<BR>—3 Sending, despatching.<BR>—4 Whetting, sharpening, furbishing, polishing (weapons &c.); मन्दरकूटकोटिव्याघट्टनोत्तेजना Śi. 3. 6.<BR>—5 An exciting speech.<BR>—6 An inducement, incentive, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजित|उत्तेजितं
उत्तेजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Instigated, excited.<BR>—2 Animated.<BR>—3 Sent.<BR>—4 Sharpened, polished &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजितम्
उत्तेजित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 An inducement.<BR>—2 One of the five paces of a horse, sidling; moderate velocity in a horseʼs<BR> pace; उत्तेजितं मध्यवेगं योजनं श्लथवल्गया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुङ्ग|उत्तुंग|उत्तुङ्गः
उत्तुङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lofty, high, tall; करप्रचेयामुत्तुङ्गः प्रभुशाक्तिं प्रथीयसीम्<BR> Śi. 2. 89; ˚हेमपीठानि 2. 5.<BR>—2 Swollen, increased (as a stream).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुण्डितम्
उत्तुण्डितम् The head of a thorn (which enters the skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुल्
उत्तुल् €10 P.<BR>—1 To raise up (by means of a balance).<BR>—2 To raise, erect, lift up.<BR>—3 To weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलनम्
उत्तोलनम् Lifting up, raising (by means of a balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुषः|उत्तुष
उत्तुषः [उद्गतः तुषोऽस्मात्]; ‘Freed from husks’, fried grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तॄ
उत्तॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To pass out of (water), disembark, come out of; उत्तेरे तरलतरङ्गरङ्गलीलानिष्णातैरथ<BR> सरसः प्रियासमूहैः Śi. 8. 63, 64; to get or jump out of, rise from; 12. 31;<BR> पल्वलोत्तीर्ण R. 2. 17; अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय, स्नानोत्तीर्णः Ś. 4.<BR>—2 To cross, pass or get over (a river &c.); उदतारिषुरम्भोधिम् Bk. 15. 33, 10;<BR> शोकसागरमुत्तीर्य Ve. 3; तेनोत्तीर्य पथा R. 12. 71, 16. 33;<BR> Me. 49.<BR>—3 To vanquish, overcome, get out of, escape from (a difficulty); व्यसनमहार्णवादपारादुत्तीर्णम् Mk. 10. 49.<BR>—4 To descend, alight; तद्गृहे उत्तीर्णौ Vet.<BR>—5 To give up, leave, quit.<BR>—6 To raise, strengthen, increase. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to come out, deliver, lift up, rescue; जलनिधिजलमध्यादेष<BR> उत्तार्यतेऽर्कः Śi. 11. 44; Dk. 30, 77.<BR>—2 To take down, to take off (as ornaments); let down, place down.<BR>—3 To cause to cross over,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">Page0410-2</a>]<BR> convey, transport across.<BR>—4 To land, disembark.<BR>—5 To vomit up, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
उत्तर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Crossing over.<BR>—2 To be crossed over, as in दुरुत्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरण|उत्तरणं
उत्तरण <i>a.</i> Coming out of, crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरणम्
उत्तरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Coming forth or out of (water &c.).<BR>—2 Landing, disembarking.<BR>—3 Crossing, passing over; संसारसमुद्र˚; सज्जनदुःखानामुत्तरणसेतुः Mk. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार|उत्तारः
उत्तार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Surpassing others, excellent, preeminent.<BR>—2 Having the eye-balls turned up (as eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारः|उत्तार
उत्तार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Transporting over, conveying.<BR>—2 Fording, crossing; सुखोत्तारताम् K. 326.<BR>—3 Landing, disembarking.<BR>—4 Delivering, rescuing.<BR>—5 Getting rid of.<BR>—6 Vomiting.<BR>—7 Instability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारकः|उत्तारक
उत्तारकः<BR>—1 A deliverer, saviour.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारण|उत्तारणः
उत्तारण <i>a.</i> Transporting or bringing over, conveying; rescuing, delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारणः|उत्तारण
उत्तारण + .{@-णः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारणम्
उत्तारण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of landing, delivering or rescuing.<BR>—2 Transportation, conveying across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारिन्
उत्तारिन्<BR>—1 Transporting over.<BR>—2 Unsteady, unstable, changeable.<BR>—3 Sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार्य|उत्तार्य्य
उत्तार्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be vomited; अज्ञानभुक्तं तूत्तार्यं शोध्यं वाप्याशु शोधनैः Ms. 11. 160.<BR>—2 To be made to land.<BR>—3 To be crossed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीर्ण|उत्तीर्णं|उत्तीर्ण्ण
उत्तीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Landed, crossed, passed over.<BR>—2 Rescued, delivered.<BR>—3 Released from obligation.<BR>—4 One who has finished his course of studies; experienced, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेरितम्
उत्तेरितम् One of the five paces of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोरण
उत्तोरण <i>a.</i> [उन्नतं तोरणमत्र] Adorned with raised or<BR> upright arches; उत्तोरणं राजपथं प्रपेदे Ku. 7. 63; उत्तोरणामन्वयराजधानीम् R. 14. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यक्त|उत्त्यक्तः
उत्त्यक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Abandoned, left.<BR>—2 Thrown, tossed.<BR>—3 Free from passion or attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यागः|उत्त्याग
उत्त्यागः<BR>—1 Abandonment, leaving.<BR>—2 Throwing, throwing up, tossing.<BR>—3 Renunciation of all worldly attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रस्
उत्त्रस् €1. €4 P. To be afraid. ━<i>Caus.</i> To frighten, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रस्त
उत्त्रस्त <i>a.</i> Frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रासः|उत्रास
उत्त्रासः Extreme fear, terror, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रिपदम्
उत्त्रिपदम् An upright tripod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रुटित
उत्त्रुटित <i>a.</i> Torn, broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्था
उत्था €1 P. [उद्-स्था]<BR>—1 To get up, stand, rise, raise oneself; उत्तिष्ठेत्प्रथमं चास्य Ms. 2. 194;<BR> R. 9. 59; Śi. 9. 39.<BR>—2 To get up from, leave, give up or cease from; अनाशनादुत्तिष्ठति Pt. 4<BR>—3 To rise, come up (as the sun<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">Page0411-1</a>]<BR> &c.).<BR>—4 To rebound (as a ball); कराभिघातोत्थितकन्दुकेयम् R. 16. 83,<BR>—5 To come forth, arise, spring or originate from, accrue from; ग्रामाच्छतमुत्तिष्ठति<BR> Mbh.; यदुत्तिष्ठति वर्णेभ्यो नृपाणां क्षयि तत्फलम् Ś. 2. 14; अन्यदमृतादुत्थितम्<BR> K. 136; उदतिष्ठन् प्रशंसावाचः Dk. 49 shouts of applause burst forth<BR> (were heard); असंशयं सागरभागुदस्थात् N. 22. 44.<BR>—6 To rise, increase in strength or power, grow, (as an enemy, disease<BR> &c.); (Ātm.) उत्तिष्ठमानस्तु परो नोपेक्ष्यः पथ्यमिच्छता Śi. 2. 10<BR> (= Pt. 1. 234.)<BR>—7 To become animated, rise (from the dead) मृतोत्थिता; Ku. 7. 4.<BR>—8 To be active or brave, rise up; हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ Bg. 2. 3, 37;<BR> Mv. 2; Pt. 3. 21.<BR>—9 To make efforts; take pains, strive, try; उत्तिष्ठमानं मित्रार्थे कस्त्वां<BR> न बहु मन्यते Bk. 8. 12, 20. 18; Mv. 4. 6; मुक्तावुत्तिष्ठते जनः<BR> Ki. 11. 13; उदस्थित ऋतौ Śi. 14. 17.<BR>—10 To excel, surpass. ━<i>Caus.</i> (उत्थापयति) —1 To cause to stand<BR> up, raise, lift up; उत्थाप्यते ग्रावा H. 3. 35; R. 14. 59; raise or<BR> throw up (as dust); R. 7. 39.<BR>—2 To instigate, excite, rouse to action; त्वामुत्थापयति द्वयम् Śi. 2. 57, 102;<BR> Kām. 5. 40; H. 3. 85; Dk. 107.<BR>—3 To arouse, awaken, raise to life, make alive; प्राणो हीदं सर्वमुत्थापयति Śat. Br.<BR>—4 To support, feed, aid; अत्र परिकरोत्थापितोऽर्थान्तरन्यासालङ्कारः<BR> Malli. on Ki. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थ|उत्थः
उत्थ <i>a.</i> [उद्-स्था-क] (Used only at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Born or produced from, arising, springing up, or originating from;<BR> दरीमुखोत्थेन समीरणेन Ku. 1. 8; भवत्संभावनोत्थाय परितोषाय<BR> मूर्च्छते 6. 59; R. 12. 82; आनन्दोत्थं नयनसलिलम् v. l.; Pt. 1. 274.<BR>—2 Standing up, coming up or forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थः|उत्थ
उत्थ + .{@-त्थः@} Arising, coming forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थातृ
उत्थातृ <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 One who rises or gets up; निद्रालस्यप्रमादोत्थम् Bg. 18. 39; यदा<BR> बली भवत्यथोत्थाता भवति Ch. Up. 7. 8. 1.<BR>—2 Resolving; उत्थातुरब्रुवन् पदः Av. 9. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थान|उत्थानं
उत्थान <i>a.</i> Causing to arise or spring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानम्
उत्थान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The act of rising or standing up, getting up; शनैर्यष्टपुत्थानम् Bh. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Rising (as of luminaries); इन्दुं नवोत्थानमिवेन्दुमत्यै R. 6. 31 newly risen.<BR>—3 Rise, origin.<BR>—4 Resurrection.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Effort, exertion, activity; मेदच्छेदकृशोदरं लघु भवत्युत्थानयोग्यं<BR> वपुः Ś. 2. 5; ˚शीलः Dk. 153 disposed to work; Mv. 6. 23; यद्युत्थानं<BR> भवेत्सह Ms. 9. 215, effort (for money), acquisition of property.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Manly exertion, manhood, Mb. 10. 2. 6; राज्ञो हि व्रतमुत्थानम्<BR> Kau. A. 1. 19; also अर्थस्य मूलमुत्थानम्<BR>—5 Energy. उत्थानेन सदा पुत्र प्रयतेथा युधिष्ठिर । न हयुत्थानमृते<BR> दैवं राज्ञामर्थं प्रसाधयेत् ॥ Mb. 12. 56. 14.<BR>—6 Joy, pleasure.<BR>—7 War, battle.<BR>—8 An army.<BR>—9 Evacuating (by stool &c.).<BR>—10 A book.<BR>—11 A court-yard.<BR>—12 A shed where sacrifices are offered.<BR>—13 A term, limit, boundary.<BR>—14 Business (cares &c.) of a family or realm.<BR>—15 Reflection.<BR>—16 Proximate cause of a disease.<BR>—17 Awakening.<BR>—18 A monastery.<BR>—19 Readiness of the army for fight; युद्धानुकूलव्यापार उत्थानमिति कीर्तितम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">Page0411-2</a>]<BR> Śukra. 1. 325.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्थानैकादशी, उत्थानवीरः, उत्थानशीलिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानैकादशी
उत्थान + -एकादशी the eleventh day in the light fortnight of Kārttika<BR> when Viṣṇu rises from his four monthsʼ sleep (also called प्रबोधिनी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानवीरः|उत्थानवीर
उत्थान + -वीरः A man of action, one who makes effort; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानशीलिन्
उत्थान + -शीलिन् <i>a.</i> Industrious; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापक|उत्थापकः
उत्थापक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Raising up, causing to get up.<BR>—2 Exciting, instigating, animating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापकः|उत्थापक
उत्थापक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A waiting man; Caraka.<BR>—2 A particular composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापनम्
उत्थापनम्<BR>—1 Causing to rise, come up, or get up.<BR>—2 Raising, elevating.<BR>—3 Causing to leave (a house).<BR>—4 Exciting, instigating.<BR>—5 Awakening, rousing (fig. also).<BR>—6 Vomiting.<BR>—7 Finishing, completing.<BR>—8 Bringing about.<BR>—9 Bringing forth.<BR>—10 (In Math.) Finding the quantity sought, an answer to the question,<BR> substitution of a value (Colebr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापनी
उत्थापनम् + .{@-नी@} The concluding verse (ऋच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाप्य
उत्थाप्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be raised or lifted.<BR>—2 To be excited or animated.<BR>—3 To be mixed.<BR>—4 (In math.) To be brought out by substitution; Bīg.^1 45.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Thomas Malten on 20210623. note: Abbreviation for Bījagaṇita; cf. MW utTApya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थायिन्
उत्थायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rising (fig. also); coming forth, becoming visible; चन्द्रगुप्तसहोत्थायिनाम्<BR> Mu. 3; Pt. 3. 153.<BR>—2 Exerting oneʼs self, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थित|उत्थितं
उत्थित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Risen or rising (as from a seat); वचो निशम्योत्थितमुत्थितः सन्<BR> R. 2. 61, 7. 10, 3. 61; Ku. 7. 61; बिल्वोत्थितां भूमिमिवोरगाणाम् Śi. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Raised, gone up; पांशुः Śi. 5. 11; R. 6. 33; Śi. 4. 1, 17. 7.<BR>—3 Rescued, saved, Ratn. 4.<BR>—4 Born, produced, sprung up, arisen; वचः R. 2. 61, 12. 49; broken<BR> out (as fire); अग्निः Ratn. 4. 14; हृदयेऽग्निरिवोत्थितः R. 4. 2.<BR> burst into a flame.<BR>—5 Striving, active, diligent; Kām. 1. 17, 8. 49.<BR>—6 Increasing, growing (in strength), advancing.<BR>—7 Bounded up, rebounded; पतिता उत्थिता Mu. 1.<BR>—8 Occurring.<BR>—9 High, lofty, eminent.<BR>—10 Extended, stretched; आपर्वभाग˚ Ś. 4. 5.<BR>—11 An epithet of a Pragātha consisting of ten Pādas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थितम्
उत्थित + .{@-तम्@} Rising, arising; शुनं नो अस्तु चरितमुत्थितं च Av. 3. 15. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्थिताङ्गुलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थिताङ्गुलिः|उत्थिताङ्गुलि|उत्थितांगुलि
उत्थित + -अङ्गुलिः the palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थितिः|उत्थिति
उत्थितिः <i>f.</i> Elevation, rising up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पक्ष्मन्
उत्पक्ष्मन्, -उत्पक्ष्मल <i>a.</i><BR> With up-turned eyelashes; उत्पक्ष्मणोर्नयनयोरुपरुद्धवृत्तिम्<BR> Ś. 4. 15; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पक्ष्मल
उत्पक्ष्मन्, -उत्पक्ष्मल <i>a.</i><BR> With up-turned eyelashes; उत्पक्ष्मणोर्नयनयोरुपरुद्धवृत्तिम्<BR> Ś. 4. 15; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पचनिपचा
उत्पचनिपचा <i>f.</i> Any act in which it is said ‘उत्पच, निपच, (<i>i. e.</i> cook thoroughly and well!) मयूरव्यंसकादयश्च’ P. II. 1. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाचित
उत्पाचित^1 <i>a.</i> Boiled or heated thoroughly.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पचिष्णु
उत्पचिष्णु <i>a.</i> Apt to ripen or cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पट्
उत्पट् €10 P.<BR>—1 To root up, extirpate, eradicate, pull up by the roots; R. 15. 19; Ku. 2. 43.<BR>—2 To tear up or out, draw out; दन्तैर्नोत्पाटयेन्नखान् Ms. 4. 69; कीलमुत्पाटयन् Pt. 1.<BR>—3 To remove, dispel; भयम्, रुषम्, कोपम् &c.; राज्यात् to depose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0411-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पटः|उत्पट
उत्पटः Sap issuing from the cleft of a tree. त्वच एवास्य रुधिरं<BR> प्रस्यन्दि त्वच उत्पटः Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटः|उत्पाट
उत्पाटः<BR>—1 Uprooting, eradication, destroying root and branch.<BR>—2 A disease of the external ear.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पाटयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटयोगः|उत्पाटयोग
उत्पाटः + -योगः A particular yoga (in Astrology).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटकः|उत्पाटक
उत्पाटकः<BR>—1 One who roots out.<BR>—2 A disease of the external ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटनम्
उत्पाटनम् Uprooting, eradicating, destroying root and branch. चकतुः<BR> समरे तीव्रमाकर्षोत्पाटनं भृशम् Rām. 6. 76. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिका
उत्पाटिका The external bark of a tree; त्वगत्सोत्पाटिका बहिः Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिन्
उत्पाटिन् <i>a.</i> (oft. at the end of comp.) Eradicating, tearing out;<BR> कीलोत्पाटीव वानरः Pt. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्
उत्पत् €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To fly or jump up; मङ्क्षूदपाति परितः पटलैरलीनाम् Śi. 5. 37, 3. 77;<BR> oft. with acc. or dat. of place. पितुः पदं मध्यममुत्पतन्ती<BR> V. 1. 19; उत्पतोदङ्मुखः खम् Me. 14; Bk. 5. 30, 6. 89; Ku. 6. 36;<BR> K. 46, 132; V. 4; स्वर्गायोत्पतिता भवेत् V. 4. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To go or rush towards; R. 9. 63.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To start up, emerge into view; मातङ्गनक्रैः सहसोत्पतद्भिः R. 13. 11.<BR>—2 To rebound (as a ball); पातितोऽपि कराघातैरुत्पतत्येव कन्दुकः Bh. 2. 85.<BR>—3 To rise, be produced or originated; निष्पेषोत्पतितानलम् R. 4. 77;<BR> रसात्तस्माद्वरस्त्रिय उत्पेतुः Rām.; Ṛs. 1. 26.<BR>—4 To be born (as from the womb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतः|उत्पत
उत्पतः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतनिपता
उत्पतनिपता <i>f.</i> Any act in which it is said ‘उत्पत, निपत’<BR> (<i>i. e.</i> fly up and down). P. II. 1. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतनम्
उत्पतनम्<BR>—1 Flying up, a leap, spring.<BR>—2 Rising or going up, ascending.<BR>—3 Throwing up.<BR>—4 Birth, production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतित
उत्पतित <i>a.</i> Ruined, destroyed; भात्युत्पतितपद्माभः समृणाल<BR> इव ह्रदः Rām. 4. 15. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतिष्णु|उत्पतिष्णुः
उत्पतिष्णु <i>a.</i> Flying, going up, springing up; R. 4. 47; Pt. 3.<BR> उत्पतिष्णू सहिष्णू च चेरतुः खरदूषणौ Bk. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातः|उत्पात
उत्पातः<BR>—1 Flying up, a spring, jump; एकोत्पातेन at one jump; एकोत्पातेन<BR> ते लङ्कामेष्यन्ति हरियूथपाः Rām. 5. 39. 40.<BR>—2 Rebounding, rising up (fig. also); करनिहतकन्दुकसमाः पातोत्पाता<BR> मनुष्याणाम् H. 1, v. l. Upward jolt; विचलन् प्रथमोत्पाते हयानां भरतर्षभ<BR> Mb. 3. 168. 40.<BR>—3 portent, any portentous or unusual phenomenon boding calamity; उत्पातेन<BR> ज्ञापिते च Vārt. on P. I. 4. 44. Sk. ˚जलधरः K. 111, 287; Ve. 1. 22;<BR> सापि सुकुमारसुभगेत्युत्पातपरंपरा केयम् K. P. 10; Mv. 1. 37.<BR>—4 Any public calamity (as an eclipse, earthquake &c.); a calamity (in<BR> general); अधर्मात्तु महोत्पातो भविष्यति हि सांप्रतम् Rām. 5. 26. 32.<BR> ˚केतु K. 5; ˚धूमलेखा Ketu; Māl. 9. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पातपवनः, उत्पातवातः, उत्पातवातालिः, उत्पातप्रतीकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातपवनः|उत्पातपवन
उत्पातः + -पवनः, -वातः, -वातालिः portentous or violent wind, whirlwind,<BR> a hurricane; R. 15. 23; Mv. 1. ओषामासे मत्सरोत्पातवातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">Page0412-2</a>]<BR> Śi. 18. 35; उत्पातवाततरलीकृततारकाभम् Nāg. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातवातः|उत्पातवात
उत्पातः + -पवनः, -वातः, -वातालिः portentous or violent wind, whirlwind,<BR> a hurricane; R. 15. 23; Mv. 1. ओषामासे मत्सरोत्पातवातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">Page0412-2</a>]<BR> Śi. 18. 35; उत्पातवाततरलीकृततारकाभम् Nāg. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातवातालिः
उत्पातः + -पवनः, -वातः, -वातालिः portentous or violent wind, whirlwind,<BR> a hurricane; R. 15. 23; Mv. 1. ओषामासे मत्सरोत्पातवातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">Page0412-2</a>]<BR> Śi. 18. 35; उत्पातवाततरलीकृततारकाभम् Nāg. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातप्रतीकारः
उत्पातः + -प्रतीकारः provision made to counteract the evil portents; Kau. A. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातक|उत्पातकः
उत्पातक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing a calamity.<BR>—2 Flying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातकः|उत्पातक
उत्पातक + .{@-कः@} = उत्पादकः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातिक
उत्पातिक <i>a.</i> Supernatural; Jaina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पताक
उत्पताक <i>a.</i> [उत्तोलिता पताका यत्र] With uplifted banners,<BR> where flags are hoisted; पुरंदरश्रीः पुरमुत्पताकम् R. 2. 74,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथः|उत्पथ
उत्पथः [उत्कान्तः पन्थानम्] A wrong road (fig. also); गुरोरप्यवलिप्तस्य<BR> कार्याकार्यमजानतः । उत्पथप्रतिपन्नस्य न्याग्यं भवति शासनम् Mb.<BR> (परित्यागो विधीयते Pt. 1. 306); Ms. 2. 214; क्षिप्तावरोधाङ्गनमुत्पथेन<BR> गाम् Śi. 12. 24; a mistaken path, (wrong guess), error; U. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथम्
उत्पथः + .{@-थम्@} <i>ind.</i> Astray, on the wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पद्
उत्पद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born or produced, arise, originate, spring up; उत्पत्स्यतेऽस्ति<BR> मम कोऽपि समानधर्मा Māl. 1. 6; वायोर्ज्योतिरुत्पद्यते Ms. 1. 77.<BR>—2 To occur, happen; उदपादि चास्य मनसि K. 132 it occurred to his<BR> mind; युद्धमुत्पत्स्यते महत् Mb.; उत्पन्नावसरमर्थित्वम् M. 3.<BR> for which an occasion has presented itself; Ms. 5. 48. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To produce, beget, cause, effect, bring about, prepare; वस्त्राणि<BR> सदैवोत्पादयति Pt. 2; Ms. 1. 63, 2. 147, 9. 60; so दुःखम्, दोषम्,<BR> भयम्, शङ्काम् &c.<BR>—2 To bring forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिः|उत्पत्ति
उत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Birth; विपदुत्पत्तिमतामुपस्थिता R. 8. 83.<BR>—2 Production; कुसुमे कुसुमोत्पत्तिः श्रूयते न तु दृश्यते Ś. Til. 17.<BR>—3 Source, origin; उत्पत्तिः साधुतायाः K. 45.<BR>—4 Rising, going up, becoming visible, coming into existence.<BR>—5 Profit, productiveness, produce; स्वल्पोत्पत्तिदेशः Rāj. T. 5. 68.<BR>—6 Producing as a result or effect.<BR>—7 Resurrection.<BR>—8 A sacrifice; उत्पत्तिरिति यजिं ब्रूमः । ŚB. on MS. 7. 1. 3, 7.<BR>—9 An original injunction, a scriptural text enjoining (a particular matter),<BR> also called उत्पत्तिश्रुति or उत्पत्तिविधि. उत्पत्तेश्चातत्प्रधानत्वात् । Ms. 4. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पत्त्यर्थः, उत्पत्तिकालीन, उत्पत्तिक्रमः, उत्पत्तिनामधेयत्वम्, उत्पत्तिप्रयोगः, उत्पत्तिवाक्यम्, उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः, उत्पत्तिशिष्ट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्त्यर्थः
उत्पत्तिः + -अर्थः The अपूर्व resulting from a sacrifice; उत्पत्त्यर्थाविभागाद्वा<BR> सत्त्ववदैकधर्म्यं स्यात् MS. 7. 1. 2. ˚अविभागः Non-separation of<BR> याग and its अपूर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिकालीन
उत्पत्तिः + -कालीन <i>a.</i> taking place at the time of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिक्रमः|उत्पत्तिक्रम
उत्पत्तिः + -क्रमः order of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिनामधेयत्वम्
उत्पत्तिः + -नामधेयत्वम् Being a name inherent in the verse; उत्पत्तिनामधेयत्वात्<BR> भक्त्या पृथक् सतीषु स्यात् । MS. 8. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिप्रयोगः|उत्पत्तिप्रयोग
उत्पत्तिः + -प्रयोगः<BR>—1 production by the combined action of cause and effect.<BR>—2 purport, meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिवाक्यम्
उत्पत्तिः + -वाक्यम् a sentence quoted from the Veda, an authoritative sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः|उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जक|उत्पत्तिव्यंजक
उत्पत्तिः + -व्यञ्जकः a type of birth (as investiture with the sacred thread);<BR> a mark of the twice-born; उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः पुण्यः Ms. 2. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिशिष्ट
उत्पत्तिः + -शिष्ट <i>a.</i> taught authoritatively (by a passage occurring in the Veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्न|उत्पन्नः
उत्पन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Born, produced, arisen.<BR>—2 Risen, gone up.<BR>—3 Acquired, gained.<BR>—4 Effected, accomplished.<BR>—5 Occurred.<BR>—6 Known, ascertained.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पन्नाधिकारः, उत्पन्नतन्तु, उत्पन्नभक्षिन्, उत्पन्नविनाशिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नाधिकारः
उत्पन्न + -अधिकारः remention, restatement; समाने पूर्ववत्त्वादुत्पन्नाधिकारः स्यात् ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">Page0413-1</a>]<BR> MS. 7. 1. 13. (where शबर explains उत्पन्नाधिकार as अनुवाद); also 7. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0412-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नतन्तु
उत्पन्न + -तन्तु <i>a.</i> having a line of descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नभक्षिन्
उत्पन्न + -भक्षिन् <i>a.</i> living from hand to mouth, (eating what is earned).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नविनाशिन्
उत्पन्न + -विनाशिन् <i>a.</i> perishing as soon as born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाद|उत्पादः
उत्पाद <i>a.</i> With the feet up-lifted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादः|उत्पाद
उत्पाद + .{@-दः@} Birth, production, appearance; उत्पादस्याप्रसिद्धत्वात्<BR> Gauḍ. 4. 38; Sarva. S. 3. 28. दुःखे च शोणितोत्पादे शाखाङ्गच्छेदने तथा<BR> Y. 2. 225; ˚भङ्गुरम् Pt. 2. 177.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पादपूर्वम्, उत्पादशयः, उत्पादशयनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादपूर्वम्
उत्पाद + -पूर्वम् N. of the first fourteen Pūrvas (ancient writings of the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादशयः|उत्पादशय
उत्पाद + -शयः, -शयनः<BR>—1 a child.<BR>—2 a kind of partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादशयनः|उत्पादशयन
उत्पाद + -शयः, -शयनः<BR>—1 a child.<BR>—2 a kind of partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादक|उत्पादकः
उत्पादक <i>a.</i> (-दिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Productive, effective, bringing about; अर्थस्योत्पादकं<BR> मन्त्रिणम् H. 3. 17; acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादकः|उत्पादक
उत्पादक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A producer, generator, a father; उत्पादकब्रह्मदात्रोर्गरीयान् ब्रह्मदः<BR> पिता Ms. 2. 146, 9. 32.<BR>—2 A fabulous animal with eight feet, called शरभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादकम्
उत्पादक + .{@-कम्@} Origin, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादन|उत्पादनं
उत्पादन <i>a.</i> Bringing forth, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादनम्
उत्पादन + .{@-नम्@} Giving birth, production, generating; उत्पादनमपत्यस्य<BR> जातस्य परिपालनम् Ms. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादिन्
उत्पादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Produced, born; सर्वमुत्पादि भङ्गुरम् H. I. 208.<BR>—2 Bringing forth, causing, producing (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादिका
उत्पादिका<BR>—1 N. of a certain insect, the white ant.<BR>—2 A mother.<BR>—3 A vegetable हेलंची (Mar. चाकवत)<BR>—4 The herb पूतिका (Mar. थोर मयाळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादित
उत्पादित <i>a.</i> Produced; अप्यनारभमाणस्य विभोरुत्पादिताः परैः Śi. 2. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाद्य
उत्पाद्य <i>a.</i> Which was to be brought about; लावण्य उत्पाद्य इवास<BR> यत्नः Ku. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पल|उत्पलं|उत्पलः
उत्पल <i>a.</i> [उत्कान्तः पलं मांसम्] Fleshless, emaciated, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पली
उत्पल + .{@-ली@} A kind of cake made with unwinnowed corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलम्
उत्पल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A blue lotus, any lotus or water lily; नवावतारं कमलादिवोत्पलम्<BR> R. 3. 36, 12. 86; Me. 26; नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया Ś. 1. 18; so रक्त˚.<BR>—2 The plant Costus Speciosus (कोष्ठ).<BR>—3 A plant in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्पलाक्ष, उत्पलचक्षुस्, उत्पलाभ, उत्पलकोष्ठम्, उत्पलगोपा, उत्पलगन्धिकम्, उत्पलपत्रम्, उत्पलपत्रकम्, उत्पलभेद्यकः, उत्पलमाला, उत्पलराजः, उत्पलशारिवा, उत्पलश्रीगर्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलाक्ष
उत्पल + -अक्ष, -चक्षुस् <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलचक्षुस्
उत्पल + -अक्ष, -चक्षुस् <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलाभ
उत्पल + -आभ <i>a.</i> lotus-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलकोष्ठम्
उत्पल + -कोष्ठम् N. of a plant (Mar. कोष्ठकोळिंजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलगोपा
उत्पल + -गोपा N. of a plant (Mar. श्वेत उपळसरी), the प्रियंगु creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलगन्धिकम्
उत्पल + -गन्धिकम् a variety of sandal of the colour of brass (which is<BR> very fragrant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलपत्रम्
उत्पल + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 a lotus-leaf.<BR>—2 a wound on the breast caused by a femaleʼs finger-nail, (generally<BR> made by loverʼs finger-nail); nail-print.<BR>—3 a Tilaka or mark on the forehead made with sandal.<BR>—4 a broad-bladed knife or lancet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलपत्रकम्
उत्पल + -पत्रकम् a broad-bladed knife or lancet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलभेद्यकः|उत्पलभेद्यक
उत्पल + -भेद्यकः a kind of bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलमाला
उत्पल + -माला N. of a lexicon compiled by Utpala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलराजः|उत्पलराज
उत्पल + -राजः N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलशारिवा
उत्पल + -शारिवा see उत्पलगोपा (= श्यामा) Ichnocarpus Frutescens<BR> (Mar. काळी उपळसरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलश्रीगर्भः|उत्पलश्रीगर्भ
उत्पल + -श्रीगर्भः N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलिन्
उत्पलिन् <i>a.</i> Abounding in lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलिनी
उत्पलिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>—2 A lotus plant having lotuses.<BR>—3 A species of the Atijagatī metre (चन्द्रिका q. v.).<BR>—4 N. of a Dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवनम्
उत्पवनम् See under उत्पू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पश्य|उत्पश्यः
उत्पश्य <i>a.</i> P. III. 1. 137 Looking upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पारणम्
उत्पारणम् Ved. Conveying over, transportation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाली
उत्पाली Health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जर|उत्पिंजर
उत्पिञ्जर, -ल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unconfined, uncaged.<BR>—2 Out of order, excessively confused, disordered; कुर्वाणमुत्पिञ्जलजातपत्रैः Śi. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जल|उत्पिंजल|उत्पिञ्जलः
उत्पिञ्जर, -ल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unconfined, uncaged.<BR>—2 Out of order, excessively confused, disordered; कुर्वाणमुत्पिञ्जलजातपत्रैः Śi. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्
उत्पिष् €7 P.<BR>—1 To rub together.<BR>—2 To crush, grind, reduce to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्ट
उत्पिष्ट <i>a.</i> Ground, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्टम्
उत्पिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} A disease, a grating of the bones or of the joints upon each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड्
उत्पीड् €10 P.<BR>—1 To press against, strike or rub against; अन्योन्यमुत्पीडयदुत्पलाक्ष्याः<BR> Ku. 1. 40; Śi. 3. 66.<BR>—2 To throw or strike upwards; press out, propel, urge; एताः करोत्पीडितवारिधाराः<BR> R. 16. 66, 5. 46.<BR>—3 To overwhelm, overpower, trouble; K. 242.<BR>—4 To fasten, make tight; इत्युक्त्वैनमतिक्रुद्धः कक्ष्यामुत्पीड्य पाण्डवः Mb. 3. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड|उत्पीडः
उत्पीड <i>a.</i> Pressing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीडः|उत्पीड
उत्पीड + .{@-डः@}<BR>—1 Pressing out.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Gush, gushing flow, rushing column or mass; बाष्पोत्पीडः<BR> K. 296; उत्पीड इव धूमस्य मोहः प्रागावृणोति माम् U. 3. 9; नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशाम्<BR> Me. 92; cf. also आपातोत्पीडहेलाहृतकुसुमरजःपिञ्जरोऽयं जलौघः<BR> Nāg. 3. 7. आदावुत्पीडपृथ्वीं प्रविरलपतितस्थूलबिन्दुं ततोऽग्रे<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 5. 18.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Overflow, excess; पूरोत्पीडे तडागस्य (v. l. तटाकस्य)<BR> परीवाहः प्रतिक्रिया U. 3. 29; Māl. 6. 7.<BR>—3 Froth, foam, पाण्डुरैः सलिलोत्पीडैः Rām. 1. 43. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीडनम्
उत्पीडनम्<BR>—1 Pressing out.<BR>—2 Pressing or striking against; K. 82.<BR>—3 Foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुच्छ
उत्पुच्छ <i>a.</i> With the tail erect, P. VI. 2. 196; विभाषोत्पुच्छे<BR> and Vārt. on P. III. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुच्छयते
उत्पुच्छयते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To raise the tail.<BR>—2 (P.) To make one raise the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुट
उत्पुट <i>a.</i> Blown, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुटकः|उत्पुटक
उत्पुटकः A sort of disease in the lobe of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुलक
उत्पुलक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thrilled, bristling.<BR>—2 Joyful, delighted<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुलकम्
उत्पुलक + .{@-कम्@} Erection of the hairs of the body (through rapture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पू
उत्पू €9 U.<BR>—1 To cleanse, purify; पवित्रेण पृथिवि भोत् पुनामि Av. 12. 1. 30.<BR> सवितुर्वः प्रसव उत्पुनाम्यच्छिद्रेण पवित्रेण Vāj. 1. 12.<BR>—2 To extract anything that has been purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवनम्
उत्पवनम्<BR>—1 Cleansing, purifying; द्रव्याणां चैव सर्वेषां शुद्धिरुत्पवनं स्मृतम् Ms. 5. 115.<BR>—2 Straining liquids for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">Page0414-1</a>]<BR> domestic or religious purposes.<BR>—3 Any instrument for cleansing.<BR>—4 Sprinkling ghee (or other fluids) on the sacrificial fire with two<BR> blades of Kuśa grass, the ends of which are held in either hand and the<BR> centre dipped into the liquid; अप्रच्छिन्नाग्रावनन्तर्गर्भौ प्रादेशमात्रौ<BR> कुशौ नानान्तयोर्गृहीत्वा अङ्गुष्ठोपकनिष्ठिकाभ्यामुत्तानाभ्यां प्रागुत्पुनाति<BR> सकृन्मन्त्रेण द्विस्तूष्णीम् Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवितृ
उत्पवितृ <i>a.</i> Purifying, a purifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पावः|उत्पाव
उत्पावः [पू-घञ्] Purifying ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रबन्ध
उत्प्रबन्ध <i>a.</i> Continuous, unceasing; स्तनमुकुलयोरुत्प्रबन्धः<BR> प्रकम्पः Māl. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रभ|उत्प्रभः
उत्प्रभ <i>a.</i> Flashing forth or diffusing light, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रभः|उत्प्रभ
उत्प्रभ + .{@-भः@} Blazing fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रसवः|उत्प्रसव
उत्प्रसवः Abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्राशनम्
उत्प्राशनम् Eating by lifting up anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासः|उत्प्रास
उत्प्रासः, -सनम्<BR>—1 Hurling, flinging away.<BR>—2 Jest, joke.<BR>—3 Violent burst of laughter.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Ridicule, derision.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Satire, irony; Ratn. 3; Mv. 6; S. D. 478.<BR>—5 Excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासनम्
उत्प्रासः, -सनम्<BR>—1 Hurling, flinging away.<BR>—2 Jest, joke.<BR>—3 Violent burst of laughter.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Ridicule, derision.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Satire, irony; Ratn. 3; Mv. 6; S. D. 478.<BR>—5 Excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रुष्
उत्प्रुष् <i>f.</i> Ved. A bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्ष्
उत्प्रेक्ष् €1 Ā. [उत्प्र-ईक्ष्]<BR>—1 To look up to; Pt. 1 to expect; K. 35, 229;<BR> to anticipate, see in prospect; उत्प्रेक्षमाणा जघनाभिघातम् Mu. 2.<BR>—2 To see, perceive, behold<BR>—3 To guess, conjecture; भगवति किमुत्प्रेक्षसे कुतस्त्योऽयमिति U. 4, 6;<BR> K. 67, 121, 198-9.<BR>—4 To believe, fancy; K. 108; Ve. 2. 10; उत्प्रेक्षामो वयं तावन्मतिमन्तं<BR> विभीषणम् Rām.<BR>—5 To remember, think of; तदुत्प्रेक्ष्योत्प्रेक्ष्य प्रियसखि गतांस्तांश्च<BR> दिवसान् Amaru. 43; U. 6. 37.<BR>—6 To transfer (with loc.).<BR>—7 To illustrate by a supposed simile; see उत्प्रेत्क्षा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षणम्
उत्प्रेक्षणम्<BR>—1 Looking into, perceiving.<BR>—2 Looking upwards.<BR>—3 Guess, conjecture.<BR>—4 Comparing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षा
उत्प्रेक्षा<BR>—1 Conjecture, guess.<BR>—2 Disregarding, carelessness, indifference.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech, ‘Poetical fancy’, which consists in<BR> supposing उपमेय and उपमान as similar to each other in some<BR> respects and in indicating, expressly or by implication, a probability<BR> of their identity based on such similarity; it is the imagining of one<BR> object under the character of another; संभावनमथोत्प्रेक्षा प्रकृतस्य<BR> परेण यत् K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> लिम्पतीव तमोऽङ्गानि वर्षतीवाञ्जनं<BR> नभः Mk. 1. 34; स्थितः पृथिव्या इव मानदण्डः Ku. 1. 1. It is usually<BR> expressed by इव, or by words like मन्ये, शङ्के, ध्रुवम्, प्रायः,<BR> नूनम् &c. (see Kāv. 2. 234); cf. S. D. 686-692 and R. G. under उत्प्रेक्षा also.<BR>—4 A parable.<BR>—5 An ironical comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षावययः
उत्प्रेक्षा + .{@-अवयवः@} A kind of simile<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्प्रेक्षावल्लभः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षावल्लभः|उत्प्रेक्षावल्लभ
उत्प्रेक्षा + -वल्लभः N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षित
उत्प्रेक्षित <i>a.</i> Compared (as in a simile).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्प्रेक्षितोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षितोपमा
उत्प्रेक्षित + -उपमा A kind of उपमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लु
उत्प्लु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To jump or leap up, bound, bound away; दुर्दान्तमुत्प्लुत्य निरस्तसादिनम्<BR> Śi. 12. 22, 5. 5; leap out of; सपङ्कतोयात्सरसोऽभितापितः उत्प्लुत्य<BR> भकः Ṛs. 1. 18.<BR>—2 To spring or jump upon; यामुत्प्लुत्य वृको हन्यात् Ms. 8. 236.<BR>—3 To float; K. 42.<BR>—4 To be fluctuating; K. 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवः|उत्प्लव
उत्प्लवः A jump, leap, bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवा
उत्प्लवः + .{@-वा@} A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवनम्
उत्प्लवनम्<BR>—1 Jumping or leaping up, springing upon.<BR>—2 Skimming off impure oil or ghee or any dirt floating upon a liquid<BR> by passing a blade of Kuśa grass over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत
उत्प्लुत <i>a.</i> Jumped up, upon or over; sprung upon suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फण
उत्फण <i>a.</i> Having an expanded hood (as a snake).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल्
उत्फल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To spring, leap.<BR>—2 To part asunder, expand, open (as a flower). ━<i>Caus.</i> To open,<BR> cause to expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फालः|उत्फाल
उत्फालः<BR>—1 A jump, spring, leaping up; rapid motion; Mk. 6.<BR>—2 Shuffling of feet.<BR>—3 The jumping attitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्ल|उत्फुल्लः
उत्फुल्ल^1 <i>p. p.</i> [उद्-फल्-क्त] Vārt. on P. VII. 4. 89. उत्फुल्लसंफुल्लयोरुपसंख्यानम्.<BR>—1 Opened, full blown (as flowers); उत्फुल्लनीलनलिनोदरतुल्यभासः Śi. 11. 36.<BR>—2 Widely opened, expanded, dilated (eyes); विस्मय ˚नयनः Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Swollen, increased in bulk.<BR>—4 Sleeping supinely or on the back; cf. उत्तान.<BR>—5 Insolent, impudent.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: the printed blobs are not anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्लम्
उत्फुल्ल + .{@-ल्लम्@}<BR>—1 The female organ of generation (स्त्रीकरणम्)<BR>—2 A kind of coitus; cf. उत्फुल्लं करणे स्त्रीणामुत्तानेऽपि विकस्वरे Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फलम्
उत्फलम् An excellent fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुलिङ्ग
उत्फुलिङ्ग^1 (for उत्स्फुलिङ्ग) Emitting sparks, sparkling.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सः|उत्स
उत्सः [उनात्ति जलेन, उन्द्-स किच्च नलेपः Uṇ. 3. 68]<BR>—1 A spring, fountain; विष्णोः पदे परमे मध्व उत्सः Rv. 1. 154. 5;<BR> यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरन्तः Śat. Br.<BR>—2 A watery place.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सधिः|उत्सधि
उत्सः + -धिः Ved. a well. नुनुद्र उत्सधिं पिबध्यै Rv. 1. 88. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सक्थ
उत्सक्थ <i>a.</i> Opening the thighs (Ved.); Vāj. 23. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संकलित
उत्संकलित Permitted; अनुत्˚ K. 260, 275.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गः|उत्सङ्ग|उत्संग|उत्संगः
उत्सङ्गः [उद्-सञ्ज्-आधारं घञ्]<BR>—1 The lap; पुत्रपूर्णोत्सङ्गा with a boy seated in the lap U. 1; उत्सङ्गवर्धितानां<BR> गुरुषु भवेत्कीदृशः स्नेहः V. 5. 10; न केवलमुत्सङ्गश्चिरान्मनोरथोऽपि<BR> मे पूर्णः U. 4; Me. 88; cf. also विशालतरमुत्सङ्गं कुरु (spread<BR> out the garment on the lap Pratimā Act. I.).<BR>—2 Embrace, contact, union; विस्तारिस्तनकुम्भकुड्मलभरोत्सङ्गेन संभाविता<BR> (माला) Māl. 8. 6;<BR>—3 Interior, vicinity; दरीगृहोत्सङ्गनिषक्तभासः Ku. 1. 10; कर्ण˚<BR> K. 15; शय्योत्सङ्गे Me. 95.<BR>—4 Surface, side, slope; दृषदो वासितोत्सङ्गाः R. 4. 74, 14. 76.<BR>—5 The haunch or part above the hip (नितम्ब).<BR>—6 The upper part, top; सौधोत्सङ्गप्रणयविमुखो मा स्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः Me. 27; K. 52.<BR>—7<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The acclivity or edge of a hill; तुङ्गं नगोत्सङ्गमिवारुरोह R. 6. 3;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Peak, summit; उत्सङ्गे महाद्रेः Ki. 7. 21.<BR>—8 The roof of a house.<BR>—9 Vault, canopy (as of sky); अपिहितगगनोत्सङ्ग-मङ्गं धुनोति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">Page0415-1</a>]<BR> Mv. 5. 53.<BR>—10 The bottom or deep part of an ulcer.<BR>—11 A high number (= 100 Vivāhas).<BR>—12 An ascetic (उत्क्रान्तः सङ्गम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गम्
उत्सङ्गः + .{@-गम्@} A high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गकः|उत्सङ्गक
उत्सङ्गकः A particular position of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गित|उत्संगित
उत्सङ्गित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Associated, joined, brought in contact with; उत्सङ्गिताम्भःकणिको<BR> नभस्वान् Śi. 3. 79 wafting sprays.<BR>—2 Taken in the lap; ˚एकैकदारकाभ्याम् U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गिन्|उत्संगिन्
उत्सङ्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Associating with, an associate, partner.<BR>—2 Deep-seated (as an ulcer). ━<i>m.</i> An ulcer, a deep sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गिनी
उत्सङ्गिन् + .{@-नी@} Pimples on the inner edge of the eye-lids (Mar. रांजणवाडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सञ्जनम्
उत्सञ्जनम् Throwing upwards, lifting up; P. I. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सक्त
उत्सक्त <i>a.</i> Prospering, going on progressingly; उत्सक्ताः पाण्डवा<BR> नित्यम् Mb. 1. 140. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सद्
उत्सद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sink (fig. also), fall into ruin or decay; उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोकाः Bg. 3. 24.<BR>—2 To leave off, quit. —3 To rise up. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To destroy, annihilate, bring to ruin; उत्साद्यन्ते जातिधर्माः Bg. 1. 43;<BR> Ms. 9. 267.<BR>—2 To overturn, upset (pots &c.).<BR>—3 To rub in, anoint (as with oil, perfumes &c.); गौरसर्षपकल्केन<BR> साज्येनोत्सादितस्य च Y. 1. 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सत्तिः|उत्सत्ति
उत्सत्तिः Ruin, destruction, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्न
उत्सन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Decayed.<BR>—2 Destroyed, ruined; uprooted, left off; उत्सन्नोऽस्मि K. 164 undone;<BR> मकरध्वज इवोत्सन्नविग्रहः K. 54; उत्सन्नकुलधर्माणाम् Bg. 1. 44;<BR> ˚निद्रा K. 171; उत्सन्नो युधिष्ठिरः Ve. 2 extirpated.<BR>—3 Cursed, wretched; K. 198.<BR>—4 Fallen into disuse, extinct (as a book).<BR>—5 Finished, completed.<BR>—6 Risen, increased (opp. अवसन्न).<BR>—7 Accomplished easily (Ved.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सन्नयज्ञः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्नयज्ञः|उत्सन्नयज्ञ
उत्सन्न + -यज्ञः An interrupted or suspended sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादः|उत्साद
उत्सादः<BR>—1 Destruction, decay, ruin, loss; सकलरिपुकुलोत्साददीर्घा प्रतिज्ञा<BR> Mu. 3. 27. गीतमुत्सादकारि मृगाणाम् K. 32.<BR>—2 A particular part of the sacrificial animal (Ved.). Vāj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादक
उत्सादक <i>a.</i> Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनम्
उत्सादनम्<BR>—1 Destroying, overturning; उत्सादनार्थं लोकानाम् Mb.; Bg. 17. 19.<BR>—2 Suspending, interrupting.<BR>—3 Cleaning the person with perfumes, chafing the limbs; उत्सादनं च<BR> गात्राणां स्नापनोच्छिष्टभोजने । न कुर्याद् गुरुपुत्रस्य पादयोश्चावनेजनम् ।<BR> Ms. 2. 209, 211. अथ गन्धोत्सादने (v. l. त्सदने) वाससी ।<BR> मानवगृह्यसूत्र of मैत्रायणीय शाखा and the commentator says<BR> गन्धश्चन्दनादि । उत्सादनम् उद्वर्तनं पक्वतैलादिना । उद्वर्तनोत्सादने<BR> द्वे समे । Ak. cf. also अभ्यङ्गोत्सादनं मूर्ध्नि तैलं जेन्ताकमातपं<BR> भजेत् &c. चरकसंहिता, सूत्रस्थान, chap. 6, verse 14. वात्स्यायन<BR> mentions it as one of the 64 Arts in his कामसूत्र. यशोधर says<BR> पादाभ्यां यन्मर्दनं तदुत्सादनमुच्यते ।<BR>—4 Healing a sore.<BR>—5 Going up, ascending, rising.<BR>—6 Elevating, raising.<BR>—7 Ploughing a field twice (or thoroughly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीय
उत्सादनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be destroyed, effected or ascended &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीयम्
उत्सादनीय + .{@-यम्@} Any application to a sore that produces granulations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादित|उत्सादितं
उत्सादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Destroyed.<BR>—2 Cleansed, purified with oil or perfumes &c. उत्सादितः कषायेण बलवद्भिः<BR> सुशिक्षितैः । आप्लुतः साधिवासेन जलेन स सुगन्धिना ॥ Mb. 7. 82. 10.<BR>—3 Risen, ascended.<BR>—4 Raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सवः|उत्सव
उत्सवः [उद्-सू-अप्]<BR>—1 A festival, joyous or festive occasion, jubilee; रत˚ Ś. 6. 20;<BR> ताण्डव˚ festive or joyous dance. U. 3. 18 (v. l.); Ms. 3. 59.<BR>—2 Joy, merriment, delight, pleasure; स कृत्वा विरतोत्सवान् R. 4. 78, 16. 10;<BR> Mv. 3. 41; Ratn. 1. 23; Śi. 2. 61; पराभवोप्युत्सव एव<BR> मानिनाम् Ki. 1. 41.<BR>—3 Height, elevation.<BR>—4 Wrath,<BR>—5 Wish, rising of a wish. तावुभौ नरशार्दूलौ त्वद्दृशन्कृतोत्सवौ<BR> Rām. 5. 35. 23.<BR>—6 A section of a book.<BR>—7 Enterprise.<BR>—8 An undertaking, beginning.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सवोदयम्, उत्सवविग्रहः, उत्सवसङ्केताः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सवोदयम्
उत्सवः + -उदयम् The height of the vehicle animal in comparison with that<BR> of the principal idol; मूलबेरवशं मानमुत्सवोदयमीरितम् (Māna. 64. 91-93).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सवविग्रहः
उत्सवः + -विग्रहः Image for procession (Koṇḍavīḍu^1 Inscription of Kṛṣṇarāya).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सवसङ्केताः
उत्सवः + -सङ्केताः (<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a people, a wild tribe of the Himālaya;<BR> शरैरुत्सवसङ्केतान् स कृत्वा विरतोत्सवान् R. 4. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सह्
उत्सह् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To be able, have power or energy; (expressed by ‘can’); dare,<BR> venture (with inf.); तवानुवृत्तिं न च कर्तुमुत्सहे Ku. 5. 65; Ś. 5;<BR> Mu. 4. 14; Śi. 14. 83; Bk. 3. 54, 5. 59, 14. 89, sometimes with acc.<BR> and dat. also; Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To attempt, be prompted or incited; Ki. 1. 36; to cheer up, not to<BR> sink or give way; अज्ञवन्नोत्सहेथास्त्वम् Bk. 19. 16.<BR>—3 To feel at ease, enjoy pleasure; क्षणमप्युत्सहते न मां विना Ku. 4. 36.<BR>—4 To go forward, march on; K. 249. ━<i>Caus.</i> To encourage, excite,<BR> instigate, incite; वरुणोत्साहितेन वेधसा K. 22; Bk. 9. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहः|उत्साह
उत्साहः [उद्-सह्-धञ्]<BR>—1 Effort, exertion; धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः Bg. 18. 26.<BR>—2 Energy, inclination, desire; त्वद्दर्शनकृतोत्साहौ Rām. 5. 67. 28.<BR> मन्दोत्साहः कृतोऽस्मि मृगयापवादिना माठव्येन Ś. 2; ममोत्साहभङ्गं<BR> मा कृथाः H. 3 do not damp my energy.<BR>—3 Perseverance, strenuous effort, energy, one of the three Śaktis or<BR> powers of a ruler (the other two being मन्त्र and प्रभाव); नीताविवोत्साहगुणेन<BR> सम्पद् Ku. 1. 22.<BR>—4 Determination, resolution; हसितेन भाविमरणोत्साहस्तया सूचितः Amaru. 10.<BR>—5 Power, ability; सौरान्मन्त्रान् यथोत्साहम् (जपेत्) Ms. 5. 86.<BR>—6 Firmness, fortitude, strength.<BR>—7 (In Rhet.) Firmness or fortitude, regarded as the feeling which gives<BR> rise to the वीर or heroic sentiment; कार्यारम्भेषु संरम्भः स्थेयानुत्साह<BR> उच्यते S. D. 3; परपराकमदानादिस्मृतिजन्मा औन्नत्याख्य उत्साहः R. G.<BR>—8 Happiness.<BR>—9 A thread.<BR>—10 Rudeness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्साहयोगः, उत्साहवर्धनः, उत्साहवृत्तान्तः, उत्साहशक्तिः, उत्साहसम्पन्न, उत्साहहेतुक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहयोगः|उत्साहयोग
उत्साहः + -योगः Bestowing oneʼs energy, exercising oneʼs strength; चारेणोत्साहयोगेन<BR> (विद्यान्महीपतिः) Ms. 9. 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवर्धनः|उत्साहवर्धन|उत्साहवर्द्धनं
उत्साहः + -वर्धनः the heroic sentiment (वीररस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवर्धनम्
उत्साहः + -वर्धनः + .({@-नम्@}) increase of energy. heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवृत्तान्तः
उत्साहः + -वृत्तान्तः plan or scheme of encouraging or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">Page0416-1</a>]<BR> exciting; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0415-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहशक्तिः|उत्साहशक्ति
उत्साहः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> firmness, energy; see (3) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहसम्पन्न|उत्साहसंपन्न
उत्साहः + -सम्पन्न <i>a.</i> active, energetic, persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहहेतुक
उत्साहः + -हेतुक <i>a.</i> one who encourages or excites to exertion; अपेहि<BR> रे उत्साहहेतुक Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहक
उत्साहक <i>a.</i> Persevering, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहनम्
उत्साहनम्<BR>—1 Effort, perseverance. —2 Encouraging, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहिन्
उत्साहिन् <i>a.</i> Active, persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्
उत्सिच् €6 P. To sprinkle, spread, pour down.<BR>—2 To make proud. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To spout or foam up; उत्सिच्यमाने पयसि Bhāg.<BR>—2 To be puffed up or proud, be elated; न तस्योत्सिषिचे मनः R. 17. 43;<BR> स्तूयमाना नोत्सिच्यन्ते K. 329.<BR>—3 To overflow, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिक्त|उत्सिक्तः
उत्सिक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sprinkled; रराज शोणितोत्सिक्तो गिरिः प्रस्रवणौरिव Rām. 6. 67. 89.<BR>—2 Proud, haughty, puffed up; अर्थवन्तो न चोत्सिक्ताः Mb. 7. 144. 26.<BR>—3 Flooded, overflowing, excessive.<BR>—4 Enlarged, increased.<BR>—5 Raised, elevated.<BR>—6 Fickle, disturbed (in mind); जानीयादस्थिरां वाचमुत्सिक्तमनसां तथा Ms. 8. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेकः|उत्सेक
उत्सेकः<BR>—1 Sprinkling, pouring.<BR>—2 Spouting out or over, showering.<BR>—3 Overflow, increase, excess; रुधिरोत्सेकाः Mv. 5. 33 streams of<BR> blood; Me. 55 v. l.; दर्प˚, बल˚ &c.<BR>—4 Pride, haughtiness, insolence; उपदा विविशुः शश्वन्नोत्सेकाः कोसलेश्वरम्<BR> R. 4. 70; अनुत्सेको लक्ष्म्याम् Bh. 2. 64; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR>—5 Exuberance; मामकस्यास्य सैन्यस्य हृतोत्सेकस्य सञ्जय । अवशेषं<BR> न पश्यामि … Mb. 8. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेकिन्
उत्सेकिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overflowing, excessive; उत्सेकिना मदबलेन विगाह्यमानम् Mu. 26.<BR>—2 Proud, haughty, puffed up; भाग्येष्वनुत्सेकिनी Ś. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेचनम्
उत्सेचनम् The act of showering or spouting upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सु
उत्सु €5 U. To stir up, agitate; उत्सुनोषीक्षमाणानां कन्दुककीडया<BR> मनः Bhāg. 3. 20. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुक|उत्सुकः
उत्सुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Anxiously desirous, eagerly expecting; striving for (any object) (with<BR> instr. or loc. or in comp.); P. II. 3. 44. निद्रया निद्रायां वोत्सुकः<BR> Sk.; मनो नियोगक्रिययोत्सुकं मे R. 5. 11; सोत्सुका सुतजन्मनि<BR> Ks. 21. 139; R. 2. 45; Me. 99; संगम˚ Ś. 3. 13; so रण˚, गमन˚, जय˚ &c.<BR>—2 Restless, uneasy, anxious; आशङ्क्योत्सुकसारङ्गां चित्रकूटस्थलीं<BR> जहौ R. 12. 24.<BR>—3 Fond of, attached to; वत्सोत्सुकापि R. 2. 22.<BR>—4 Regretting, repining, sorrowing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकः|उत्सुक
उत्सुक + .{@-कः@} Longing for, anxious desire; प्रकुर्वते कस्य मनो न सोत्सुकम् Ṛs. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकः|उत्सुक
उत्सुक + .{@-कः@} Longing for, anxious desire; प्रकुर्वते कस्य मनो न सोत्सुकम् Ṛs. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकता
उत्सुकता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Restlessness, uneasiness.<BR>—2 Zeal, ardent desire.<BR>—3 Attachment, affection.<BR>—4 Sorrow, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकत्वम्
उत्सुकता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Restlessness, uneasiness.<BR>—2 Zeal, ardent desire.<BR>—3 Attachment, affection.<BR>—4 Sorrow, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकयति
उत्सुकयति Den. P. To make uneasy; परिणामाभिमुखमृतोरुत्सुकयति<BR> यौवनं चेतः M. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकायते
उत्सुकायते Den. Ā. To become uneasy or anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूत्र
उत्सूत्र <i>a.</i> [उत्कान्तः सूत्रम्]<BR>—1 Unstrung, loose, detached (from the string); ˚मणिभिः Śi. 8. 53.<BR>—2 Irregular.<BR>—3 Deviating from the rule (सूत्र) of Pāṇini; यो ह्युत्सूत्रं कथयेन्नादो<BR> गृह्येत Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1. अनुत्सूत्रपदन्यासा सद्वृत्तिः सन्निबन्धना Śi. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूरः|उत्सूर
उत्सूरः [उत्कान्तः सूरं सूर्यम्] Evening, twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूर्यशायिन्
उत्सूर्यशायिन् <i>a.</i> One who sleeps even at sunrise; Mb. 12. 228. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृ
उत्सृ <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To expel, turn out, drive away; वेत्रदण्डैरिवोत्सार्यन्ते गुणाः K. 106;<BR> Mv. 4. 39.<BR>—2 To remove, keep or put aside; K. 204; to push far; R. 4. 53; परमेश्वरस्य<BR> चार्वाकेण दूरोत्सारितत्वात् Sarva. S. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृतिः
उत्सृतिः <i>f.</i> A higher caste; यज्ञार्थं निधनं प्राप्ताः प्राप्नुवन्त्युत्सृतीः<BR> (v. l. उच्छृतीः) पुनः Ms. 5. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सरः|उत्सर
उत्सरः<BR>—1 A variety of the अतिशक्वरी metre having 15 syllables.<BR>—2 N. of the month Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्या|उत्सर्य्या
उत्सर्या [उद्-सृ-यत्] A cow when she is fit to take the bull (गर्भयोग्यावस्थापन्ना गौः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारकः|उत्सारक
उत्सारकः<BR>—1 A policeman, (one who drives away men and makes room for others.)<BR>—2 A guard.<BR>—3 A porter, door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारणम्
उत्सारणम्<BR>—1 Removing, keeping at a distance, driving out of the way; तूर्णमुत्सारणं<BR> तत्र कारयामास धर्मवित् Rām. 6. 114. 20. ˚वेत्रलता K. 106, 112.<BR>—2 Helping out to step out (of a palanquin &c.).<BR>—3 Reception of a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्
उत्सृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 to pour out, emit, send forth or down; व्यलीकनिश्वासमिवोत्ससर्ज<BR> Ku. 3. 25; सहस्रगुणमुत्स्रष्टुमादत्ते हि रसं रविः R. 1. 18 to<BR> give back; Bg. 9. 19; so बाष्पम्, वारि.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To quit, leave, abandon, give up. मातापितृभ्यामुत्सृष्टम् Ms. 9. 171;<BR> नियतमात्मानमुत्स्रक्ष्यामि K. 177, 191, 194; R. 5. 51, 6. 46, 7. 7;<BR> Ku. 2. 36, 5. 86; kill; so तनुम्, प्राणान्, रणम् &c. परार्थे<BR> प्राज्ञ उत्सृजेत् H. 1. 41.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To put off; lay aside; भयोत्सृष्टविभूषाणाम् R. 4. 54, 3. 60.<BR>—3 To let loose, allow to roam at liberty; तुरङ्गम् R. 3. 39.<BR>—4 To avoid, escape.<BR>—5 To cast forth or away, discharge, throw (as arrows); उत्ससर्ज शरान् Bk. 14. 45.<BR>—6 To let fall down, sow, scatter (as seed &c.); अक्षेत्रे बीजमुत्सृष्टमन्तरैव<BR> विनश्यति Ms. 10. 71.<BR>—7 To present, give; मित्राय … अस्माभिरुत्सृज्यते Māl. 10. 23.<BR>—8 To widen, stretch out, extend.<BR>—9 To abolish (as a rule), restrict or limit the scope of a rule.<BR>—10 To send one to a place.<BR>—11 To permit to go, discharge, dismiss.<BR>—12 To adjourn.<BR>—13 To hear to the end.<BR>—14 To make, form, shape (Ved.).<BR>—15 To erect, fix (उच्छ्रि); आत्मानं यूपमुत्सृज्य स यज्ञोऽनन्तदक्षिणः<BR> Mb. 12. 97. 10.<BR>—16 To make a sound or noise; तद्यथा नः सुसमाहितमुत्सर्जद्यायात्<BR> Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गः|उत्सर्ग
उत्सर्गः<BR>—1 Laying or leaving a side, abandoning, suspension; श्रीलक्षणोत्सर्गविनीतवेषाः Ku. 7. 45.<BR>—2 Pouring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">Page0417-1</a>]<BR> out, dropping down, emission; तोयोत्सर्गद्रुततरगतिः Me. 19, 39; so शुक˚.<BR>—3 A gift, donation, giving away; (धनस्य) उत्सर्गेण शुध्यन्ति Ms. 11. 193.<BR>—4 Spending; अर्थ˚ Mu. 3.<BR>—5 Loosening, letting loose; as in वृषोत्सर्गः<BR>—6 An oblation, libation.<BR>—7 Excretion, voiding by stool &c.; पुरीष˚, मलमूत्र˚.<BR>—8 Completion (as of study or a vow); cf. उत्सृष्टा वै वेदाः (opp. उपाकृता वै वेदाः).<BR>—9 A general rule or precept (opp. अपवाद a particular rule or exception);<BR> अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः कृतव्यावृत्तयः परैः Ku. 2. 27, उपवाद इवोत्सर्गं<BR> व्यावर्तयितुमीश्वरः R. 15. 7.<BR>—10 Offering what is promised (to gods, Brāhmaṇas &c.) with due ceremonies.<BR>—11 The anus; मित्रमुत्सर्गे Ms. 12. 121.<BR>—12 A heap, mass; अन्नस्य सुबहून् राजन्नुत्सर्गान्पर्वतोपमान् Mb. 14. 85. 38.<BR>—13 Dedication, securing the services (of priests). उत्सर्गे तु प्रधानत्वात्<BR> etc. MS. 3. 7. 19. (where शबर paraphrases उत्सर्ग by परिक्रय).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सर्गसमितिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0416-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गसमितिः|उत्सर्गसमिति
उत्सर्गः + -समितिः carefulness in the act of excretion so that no living<BR> creature be hurt (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गतः
उत्सर्गतः <i>ind.</i> Generally, without any exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गिन्
उत्सर्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Leaving out or off.<BR>—2 Omitting, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्जनम्
उत्सर्जनम्<BR>—1 Leaving, abandoning, letting loose, quitting &c.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR>—3 Suspension of a Vedic study.<BR>—4 A ceremony connected with this suspension (to be performed half yearly);<BR> पुष्ये तु च्छन्दसां कुर्याद् बहिरुत्सर्जनं द्विजः Ms. 4. 96; वेदोत्सर्जनाख्यं<BR> कर्म करिष्ये Śrāvaṇī Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्ट|उत्सृष्टः
उत्सृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, cast, thrown.<BR>—2 Used, employed; बुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतोत्सृष्टा हन्याद्राष्ट्रं सराजकम् Pt. 1. 206.<BR>—3 Given, offered.<BR>—4 Poured forth, cast into or upon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सृष्टपशु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टपशु
उत्सृष्ट + -पशु a bull set at liberty upon particular occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टिः|उत्सृष्टि
उत्सृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Abandonment, leaving, emission.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उत्सृष्टिकारिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टिकारिकः|उत्सृष्टिकारिक
उत्सृष्टिः + -कारिकः A drama in a single act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्रष्टुकाम
उत्स्रष्टुकाम <i>a.</i> Wishing to let go or put down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृप्
उत्सृप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go upwards, glide or soar upwards; अधरोधर उत्तरेभ्यो गूढः पृथिव्या<BR> मोत्सृपत् Av. 6. 134. 2.<BR>—2 To go up to, approach; सरित्प्रवाहस्तटमुत्ससर्प R. 5. 46.<BR>—3 To spread out.<BR>—4 To rise (as the sun).<BR>—5 To wish to get up; मायाभिरुत्सिसृप्सत् इन्द्र द्यामारुरुक्षतः Rv. 8. 14. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पः|उत्सर्प|उत्सर्प्प
उत्सर्पः, -र्पणम्<BR>—1 Going or gliding upwards; उत्सर्पणापसर्पणैश्चान्योन्यं प्रत्यरुन्धताम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 44. 4.<BR>—2 Swelling, heaving, undulating.<BR>—3 Sun-rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पणम्
उत्सर्पः, -र्पणम्<BR>—1 Going or gliding upwards; उत्सर्पणापसर्पणैश्चान्योन्यं प्रत्यरुन्धताम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 44. 4.<BR>—2 Swelling, heaving, undulating.<BR>—3 Sun-rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिन्|उत्सर्प्पिन्
उत्सर्पिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Moving or gliding upwards, rising; पयोधरोत्सर्पिषु (शीकरेषु) R. 16. 62.<BR>—2 Soaring, towering; उत्सर्पिणी खलु महतां प्रार्थना Ś. 7.<BR>—3 Causing to increase or rise. —4 Transcendental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिणी
उत्सर्पिन् + .{@-णी@} <i>f.</i> A division of time (with the Jainas), a long period<BR> said to be = ten crores of crores of oceans of years; cf. अवसर्पिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेध|उत्सेधः
उत्सेध <i>a.</i> High, tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेधः|उत्सेध
उत्सेध + .{@-धः@}<BR>—1 A height, elevation; (fig. also); पयोधरोत्सेधविशीर्णसंहति (वल्कलम्)<BR> Ku. 5. 8, 24. cf. also Kau. A. 1. 3; Śukra. 4. 495; high or projecting<BR> breasts; सोत्सेधैः स्कन्धदेशैः Mu. 4. 7 raised high up.<BR>—2 Thickness, fatness.<BR>—3 Intumescence, swelling.<BR>—4 The body.<BR>—5 Sublimity, greatness; prosperity; मामकस्यास्य सैन्यस्य हतोत्सेधस्य<BR> सञ्जय । अवशेषं न पश्यामि Mb. 8. 9. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेधम्
उत्सेध + .{@-धम्@}<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—2 The height from the basement to the top; उत्सेधं जन्मादिस्तूपिकान्तम् ।<BR> Māna. 35. 26. The different technical names of the heights of<BR> the idols are शान्तिक, पौष्टिक, जयद, सार्वकामिक, धनद and अद्मुत.<BR> Their lengths are respectively 1¼th, 1½, 1⅓rd of their breadths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्नात
उत्स्नात <i>a.</i> One who has emerged from the water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्नेहनम्
उत्स्नेहनम् Sliding, slipping, deviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मि
उत्स्मि €1 Ā. To smile at, deride; उत्स्मयित्वा महाबाहुः Rām. 1. 1. 65.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To ridicule, make a fool of one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मयः|उत्स्मय
उत्स्मयः Smile. ━<i>a.</i> Open, blooming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मितम्
उत्स्मितम् Smile; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्य
उत्स्य <i>a.</i> Coming from a well or fountain (as water); Av. 19. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्रोतस्
उत्स्रोतस् <i>a.</i> Having the flow (of life) upward; opposed to अर्वाक्स्रोतस्^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वन|उत्स्वनः
उत्स्वन <i>a.</i> High-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वनः|उत्स्वन
उत्स्वन + .{@-नः@} A loud sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वप्नायते
उत्स्वप्नायते Den. Ā. To talk in oneʼs sleep, dream through uneasiness;<BR> सीतोत्स्वप्नायते U. 1; साम्प्रतं मालविकामुत्स्वप्नायते M. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् <i>ind.</i> A prefix to verbs and nouns. G. M. gives the following<BR> senses with illustrations:− (1) Superiority in place, rank or power; up,<BR> upwards, upon, on, over, above (उद्बल). (2) Separation, disjunction<BR> उत्कञ्चुकः; out, out off, from, apart &c.; उद्गच्छति. (3) Motion<BR> upwards (उत्कन्धरः, उत्पताक, उत्तिष्ठति) पुरन्दरश्रीः परमुत्पताकं<BR> प्रविश्य पौरैरभिनन्द्यमानः R. 2. 74. (4) acquisition, gain; उपार्जति.<BR> (5) Publicity; उच्चरति. (6) Wonder; anxiety; उत्सुक. (7) Liberation;<BR> उद्गत. (8) Absence; उत्पथ. (9) Blowing, expanding, opening;<BR> उत्फुल्ल. (10) Pre-eminence; उद्दिष्ट. (11) Power; उत्साहः; उत्<BR> प्राबल्यवियोगोर्ध्वकर्मलाभप्रकाशाश्चर्यमोक्षणाभावदलप्राधान्यशक्तिषु.<BR> With nouns it forms adj. and adv. compounds; उदर्चिस्, उच्छिख, उद्बाहु,<BR> उन्निद्रम्, उत्पथम्, उद्दामम् &c. It is sometimes used in the Veda as an<BR> expletive simply to fill out the verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् = उन्द् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदम्
उदम् Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकम्
उदकम् [उन्द्-ण्वुल् नि ˚नलोपश्च Uṇ. 2. 39] Water; अनीत्वा पङ्कतां<BR> धूलिमुदकं नावतिष्ठते Śi. 2. 34.<BR>{@उदकं दा, -प्रदा@} or {@-कृ@} To offer a libation of water to a dead person;<BR> इत्येवमुक्तो मारीचः कृत्वोदकमथात्मनः Mb. 3. 278. 14. उदकम् उपस्पृश्<BR> to touch certain parts of the body with water,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0418-1" target="_blank">Page0418-1</a>]<BR> bathe; [cf. Gr. <i>hudor</i>; L. <i>unda</i> ‘a wave’].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदकाञ्जलिः, उदकान्तः, उदकार्थिन्, उदकात्मन्, उदकाधारः, उदकोदञ्जनः, उदकोदरम्, उदकोदरिन्, उदकौदनः, उदककर्मन्, उदककार्यम्, उदकक्रिया, उदकदानम्, उदककार्यम्, उदककुम्भः, उदककृच्छ्रः, उदकक्ष्वेडिका, उदकगाहः, उदकगिरिः, उदकपर्वतः, उदकग्रहणम्, उदकचन्द्रः, उदकद, उदकदातृ, उदकदायिन्, उदकदानिक, उदकदानम्, उदकधरः, उदकपरीक्षा, उदकपूर्वकम्, उदकप्रतीकाश, उदकप्रवेशः, उदकभारः, उदकवीवधः, उदकभूमः, उदकमञ्जरी, उदकमण्डलुः, उदकमन्थः, उदकमेहः, उदकमेहिन्, उदकवज्रः, उदकवाद्यम्, उदकशाकम्, उदकशान्तिः, उदकशील, उदकशुद्ध, उदकसक्तुः, उदकस्पर्शः, उदकहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0417-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकाञ्जलिः|उदकाञ्जलि
उदकम् + -अञ्जलिः<BR>—1 A handful water.<BR>—2 See उदककर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0418-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकान्तः|उदकान्त|उदकांत
उदकम् + -अन्तः margin of water, bank, shore; ओदकान्तात्स्निग्धो जनोऽनुगन्तव्य<BR> इति श्रूयते Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0418-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

