उदयनम्
उदयः, उदयनम् See under उदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरम्
उदरम् [उद्-ऋ-अप्]<BR>—1 The belly; दुष्पूरोदरपूरणाय Bh. 2. 119; cf. कृशोदरी, उदरभरणम्,<BR> उदरंभरि &c.<BR>—2 The interior or inside of anything, cavity; तडाग˚ Pt. 2. 150;<BR> R. 5. 70; U. 2. 16, 4. 29; त्वां कारयामि कमलोदरबन्धनस्थम् Ś. 6. 20;<BR> Śānti. 1. 5; Ś. 1. 19; Amaru. 88; जलदोदरेभ्यः Mk. 5;<BR> Ṛs. 3. 12; घनानां वारिगर्भोदराणाम् Ś. 7. 7.<BR>—3 Enlargement of the abdomen from dropsy or flatulence; तस्य होदरं<BR> जज्ञे Ait. Br.<BR>—4 Any morbid abdominal affection, such as liver, spleen &c. (said to<BR> be of 8 kinds वात˚, पित्त˚, कफ˚, त्रिलिङ्ग˚ or दूषी˚, प्लीहा˚, बद्धगुद˚,<BR> आगन्तुक˚ and जल˚).<BR>—5 Slaughter [cf. L. <i>uterus</i>; Zend. <i>udara</i>].<BR>—6 Battle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदराग्निः, उदराध्मानः, उदरामयः, उदरामयिन्, उदरावर्तः, उदरावेष्टः, उदरग्रन्थिः, उदरगुल्मः, उदरत्राणम्, उदरपिशाच, उदरपूरम्, उदरपोषणम्, उदरभरणम्, उदरशय, उदरसर्वस्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदराग्निः|उदराग्नि
उदरम् + -अग्निः The digestive faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदराध्मानः|उदराध्मान
उदरम् + -आध्मानः flatulence of the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरामयः|उदरामय
उदरम् + -आमयः disease of the belly, dysentery, diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरामयिन्
उदरम् + -आमयिन् <i>a.</i> suffering from dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावर्तः|उदरावर्त|उदरावर्त्त|उदरावर्त्तः
उदरम् + -आवर्तः the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावेष्टः|उदरावेष्ट
उदरम् + -आवेष्टः the tape-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरग्रन्थिः|उदरग्रन्थि
उदरम् + -ग्रन्थिः, -गुल्मः disease of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरगुल्मः
उदरम् + -ग्रन्थिः, -गुल्मः disease of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरत्राणम्
उदरम् + -त्राणम्<BR>—1 a cuirass, armour covering the front of the body.<BR>—2 a belly-band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपिशाच|उदरपिशाचः
उदरम् + -पिशाच <i>a.</i> [उदरे तत्पूर्तौ पिशाच इव] gluttonous, voracious<BR> (having a devilish appetite).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपिशाचः|उदरपिशाच
उदरम् + -पिशाच + .({@-चः@}) a glutton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपूरम्
उदरम् + -पूरम् <i>ind.</i> till the belly is full; P. III. 4. 31. उदरपूरं<BR> भुङ्क्ते Sk. eats his fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपोषणम्
उदरम् + -पोषणम्, -भरणम् feeding the belly, support of life (cf. उदरंभरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरभरणम्
उदरम् + -पोषणम्, -भरणम् feeding the belly, support of life (cf. उदरंभरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरशय|उदरशयः
उदरम् + -शय <i>a.</i> अधिकरणे शेतेः P. III. 2. 15; sleeping on the<BR> face or the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरशयः|उदरशय
उदरम् + -शय + .({@-यः@}) foetus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरसर्वस्वः|उदरसर्वस्व
उदरम् + -सर्वस्वः a glutton, an epicure (one to whom the belly is all-in-all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरक
उदरक <i>a.</i> Abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरंभरि|उदरम्भरि|उदरम्भरिः
उदरंभरि <i>a.</i> [उदरं बिभर्ति, भृ खि मुम् च P. III. 2. 26]<BR>—1 Nourishing oneʼs own belly, selfish.<BR>—2 Gluttonous, voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरवत्|उदरवन्त्
उदरवत्, उदरिक, -ल <i>a.</i> Having a large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिक
उदरवत्, उदरिक, -ल <i>a.</i> Having a large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिल|उदरिलः
उदरवत्, उदरिक, -ल <i>a.</i> Having a large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिन्
उदरिन् <i>a.</i> [उदर-ज्ञनि]<BR>—1 Having a large belly, fat, corpulent; उदरिणी कन्या Mbh. 5. 2. 94.<BR>—2 Abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिणी
उदरिन् + .{@-णी@} A pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्य|उदर्यः|उदर्य्य
उदर्य <i>a.</i> [उदर-यत्] Belonging to the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्यम्
उदर्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Contents of the belly; Vāj. 25. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदराटः|उदराट
उदराटः A species of worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरथिः|उदरथि
उदरथिः (-थिन्)<BR> [उद्-ऋ-घथिन् Uṇ. 4. 88]<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरथिन्
उदरथिः (-थिन्)<BR> [उद्-ऋ-घथिन् Uṇ. 4. 88]<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्कः|उदर्क
उदर्कः [Said to be fr. ऋच्] —1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) End, conclusion; ˚स्वादुनः कर्मणः Dk. 79; सुखोदर्कम् K. 328.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Result, consequence, future result of an action; उदर्कस्तव<BR> कल्याणो भविता Nala. 12. 67; किंतु कल्याणोदर्कं भविष्यति U. 4;<BR> प्रयत्नः सफलोदर्क एव Māl. 8; Ms. 4. 176, 11. 10, 9. 25, 12. 18;<BR> यो लौल्यात्कुरुते कर्म नैवोदर्कमवेक्षते Pt. 5. 73.<BR>—3 Remote consequence, reward.<BR>—4 Future time, futurity.<BR>—5 Elevation of a building (as a tower).<BR>—6 Surpassing. sometimes used as an adjective in this sense; तेन हि<BR> उदर्केण गुणेनात्र भवितव्यम् Pratimā 1.<BR>—7 N. of a tree<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">Page0421-1</a>]<BR> Vanguiera Spinosa Roxb (मदनवृक्ष).<BR>—8 Increase; सर्वर्द्ध्युपचयोदर्कम् Bhāg. 3. 23. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0420-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्चिस्|उदर्च्चिस्
उदर्चिस् <i>a.</i> [ऊर्ध्वमर्चिः शिखाऽस्य] Shining or blazing upwards,<BR> resplendent, radiant, glowing; स्फुरन्नुदार्चिः सहसा तृतीयादक्ष्णः कृशानुः<BR> किल निष्पपात Ku. 3. 71, 7. 79; R. 7. 24, 15. 76. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire; प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते तेऽभिमारुतम् Śi. 2. 42, 20. 75.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्दः|उदर्द|उदर्द्द
उदर्दः [अर्द्-अच्] (In Medic.) Erysipelas (विसर्प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्धः|उदर्ध
उदर्धः Scarlet fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवग्रहः|उदवग्रह
उदवग्रहः A Svarita accent depending on an Udātta which stands<BR> in the Avagraha q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसानीय
उदवसानीय <i>a.</i> Ved. Last, final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवस्य
उदवस्य <i>ind.</i>^1 Last, final, concluding; उदवस्य सहर्त्विग्भिः<BR> सस्नाववभृथं ततः Bhāg. 4. 7. 56.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसितम्
उदवसितम् [उद्-अव-सो-क्त] A house, dwelling; जानीषे रेभिलस्योदवसितम्<BR> Mk. 4; Śi. 11. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्रु
उदश्रु <i>a.</i> [उद्गतान्यश्रूणि यस्य] Bursting into tears, one<BR> whose tears gush forth, weeping; तस्य पश्यन् ससौमित्रेरुदश्रुर्वसतिद्रुमान्<BR> R. 12. 14; Amaru. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्रयणम्
उदश्रयणम् The act of causing to weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्
उदस् €4 P. [उद्-अस्]<BR>—1 To cast up, throw up; दयिताय सासवमुदस्तमपतदवसादिनः करात्<BR> Śi. 15. 81; to raise, lift up, elevate, erect; स्वयमिति मुग्धवधूमुदास<BR> दोर्भ्याम् Śi. 7. 49; पुच्छमुदस्यति Sk.<BR>—2 To throw down; उदस्ताधोरणः Dk. 35.<BR>—3 To throw out, expel, drive away, leave, quit; उदस्य धैर्यं दयितेन<BR> सादरम् Ki. 8. 50.<BR>—4 To destroy, dispel; रिपुतिमिरमुदस्य Ki. 1. 46.<BR>—5 To drive, propel; इत्थं विहृत्य वनिताभिरुदस्यमानम् Ki. 8. 55.<BR>—6 To turn away.<BR>—7 To take pains, make efforts. ━<i>pass.</i> To be driven off, fall<BR> off, deviate from; अतिमूढ उदस्यते नयात् Ki. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदसनम्
उदसनम्<BR>—1 Throwing, raising, erecting; पुच्छादुदसने व्यसने पर्यसने च<BR> Mbh. 3. 1. 20.<BR>—2 Expelling, turning out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्त
उदस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or cast up, raised, erected.<BR>—2 Turned out, expelled.<BR>—3 Removed, scattered.<BR>—4 Shamed, humbled, humiliated.<BR>—5 Come out, bulged out; परिभ्रमद्गात्र उदस्तलोचनः Bhāg. 3. 19. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्तात्
उदस्तात् <i>ind.</i> On, above विधूतकल्कोऽथ हरेरुदस्तात्प्रयाति चकं<BR> नृप शैशुमारम् Bhāg. 2. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासः|उदास
उदासः [उद्-अस्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Throwing upwards, elevation, raising.<BR>—2 Expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाजः|उदाज
उदाजः Encouragement to the army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त <i>a.</i> [उद्-आदा-क्त]<BR>—1 High, elevated, lofty, exalted, noble; इतश्चोदात्तदन्तानां कुञ्जराणां<BR> तरस्विनाम् Rām. 2. 99. 11. उदात्तकुलजातीय उदात्ताभिजनः सदा<BR> Mb. 13. 145. 31. ˚अन्वयैः K. 92; Ratn. 4; sublime; Ve. 1.<BR>—2 Noble, dignified; अत्युदात्तसुजनश्चन्द्रकेतुः U. 6.<BR>—3 Generous,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">Page0421-2</a>]<BR> bountiful, donor.<BR>—4 Famous, illustrious, great; Śi. 20. 82; ललितोदात्तमहिमा Bv. 1. 79.<BR>—5 Dear, beloved.<BR>—6 Highly or acutely accented (as a Svara), see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्तः|उदात्त|उदात्तं
उदात्त + .{@-त्तः@}<BR>—1 The acute accent, a high or sharp tone; उच्चैरुदात्तः P. I. 2. 29;<BR> ताल्वादिषु सभागेषु स्थानेषूर्ध्वभागे निष्पन्नोऽनुदात्तः Sk.; see under<BR> अनुदात्त also; निहन्त्यरीनेकपदे य उदात्तः स्वरानिव Śi. 2. 95.<BR>—2 Gift, donation.<BR>—3 A kind of musical instrument, a large drum.<BR>—4 A variety of the hero; see धीरोदात्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्तम्
उदात्त + .{@-त्तम्@} (In Rhet.) A figure of speech which describes supermundane<BR> prosperity, or an action of one that is great represented collaterally<BR> to the subject in hand; लोकातिशयसंपत्तिवर्णनोदात्तमुच्यते । यद्वापि<BR> प्रस्तुतस्याङ्गं महतां चरितं भवेत् ॥ S. D. 752; cf. also K. P. 10;<BR> उदात्तं वस्तुनः संपन्महतां चोपलक्षणम्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदात्तराघवः, उदात्तश्रुति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्तराघवः|उदात्तराघव
उदात्त + -राघवः N. of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्तश्रुति
उदात्त + -श्रुति <i>a.</i> pronounced with the acute accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्ततर
उदात्ततर <i>a.</i> More elevated, more acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त्यूहः
उदात्त्यूहः A kind of water-crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उदान See under 1. उदन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदानी
उदानी Ā. To raise, elevate; विनेष्ये वा प्रियान् प्राणानुदानेष्येऽथवा<BR> यशः Bk. 8. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाप्यम्
उदाप्यम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Against the stream; Av. 10. 1. 7. (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदायुध
उदायुध <i>a.</i> With uplifted weapon, upraising weapons; मनुजपशुभिर्निर्मर्यादैर्भवद्भिरुदायुधैः<BR> Ve. 3. 22; उदायुधानापततस्तान्दृप्तान्प्रेक्ष्य राघवः R. 12. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Generous, liberal, munificent.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Noble, exalted, dignified; स तथेति विनेतुरुदारमतेः R. 8. 91, 5. 12;<BR> वाचः 65; उदाराः सर्व एवैते Bg. 7. 18.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) High, lofty, great, best, illustrious, distinguished; ˚कीर्तेः<BR> Ki. 1. 18; ˚तपसः Bh. 3. 51.<BR>—3 Honest, sincere, upright.<BR>—4 good, nice, fine; कृतः कटोभीष्म उदारः शोभनः Mbh. 2. 3. 1;<BR> उदारः कल्पः Ś. 5.<BR>—5 Proper, right.<BR>—6 Eloquent.<BR>—7 Kind, soft, agreeable; ˚वाचः कन्यकाः R. 14. 77.<BR>—8 Rich, plentiful; उदारा श्रीः स्थिता ह्यस्याम् Rām. 4. 22. 16. उदारमभ्यवहारविधिम्<BR> Dk. 49; Mu. 3. 8.<BR>—9 Large, extensive, grand, splendid; साकेतोपवनमुदारमध्युवास<BR> R. 13. 79; उदारनेपथ्यभृताम् 6. 6 richly dressed.<BR>—10 Beautiful, charming, lovely; Ku. 7. 14; Śi. 5. 21; see उदारदर्शन<BR> below; R. 16. 26, 51.<BR>—11 Unperplexed.<BR>—12 Exciting, driving forth (Ved.). श्रीणामुदारो धरुणो रयीणाम् Rv. 10. 45. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारम्
उदार + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Loudly; प्रगीयते सिद्धगणैश्च योषितामुदारमन्ते कलभाविकखरैः Śi. 4. 33.<BR>—2 By means of arguments; इति तानुदारमनुनीय Ki. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारः|उदार
उदार + .{@-रः@} Ved.<BR>—1 A rising fog or vapour.<BR>—2 A sort of grain with long stalks.<BR>—3 A figure in Rhetoric which attributes greatness to inanimate objects.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदारात्मन्, उदारचेतस्, उदारचरित, उदारमनस्, उदारसत्त्व, उदारधी, उदारदर्शन, उदाररमणीय, उदारवीर्य, उदारवृत्तार्थपद, उदारसत्त्वाभिजन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारात्मन्
उदार + -आत्मन्, -चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> noble-minded magnanimous;<BR> उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् H. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचेतस्
उदार + -आत्मन्, -चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> noble-minded magnanimous;<BR> उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् H. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचरित
उदार + -आत्मन्, -चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> noble-minded magnanimous;<BR> उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् H. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारमनस्
उदार + -आत्मन्, -चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> noble-minded magnanimous;<BR> उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् H. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारसत्त्व
उदार + -आत्मन्, -चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> noble-minded magnanimous;<BR> उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् H. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारधी
उदार + -धी <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of sublime genius, highly intelligent; धियः समग्रैः स गुणैरुदारधीः R. 3. 30.<BR>—2 noble-minded. (<i>m.</i>) N. of Viṣṇu. (<i>f.</i>) good abilities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारदर्शन
उदार + -दर्शन <i>a.</i> good-looking<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">Page0422-1</a>]<BR> (having large-eyes); तथा हि ते शलिमुदारदर्शने Ku. 5. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0421-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाररमणीय
उदार + -रमणीय <i>a.</i> grand and lovely, transcendental; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारवीर्य|उदारवीर्य्य
उदार + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> of great power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारवृत्तार्थपद
उदार + -वृत्तार्थपद <i>a.</i> of excellent words and meaning and metre;<BR> उदारवृत्तार्थपदैर्मनोरमैस्तदास्य रामस्य चकार कीर्तिमान् Rām. 1. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारसत्त्वाभिजन
उदार + -सत्त्वाभिजन <i>a.</i> Of noble character and descent; उदारसत्त्वाभिजनो<BR> हनूमान् Rām. 4. 47. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारता
उदारता<BR>—1 Liberality, genorosity.<BR>—2 Richness (as of expression); वचसाम् Māl. 1. 7; Ś. 6; (as applied<BR> to words) उदारता = कठिनवर्णघटनारूपविकटत्वलक्षणा R. G.; (as<BR> applied to the sense) चुम्बनं देहि मे भार्ये कामचाण्डालतृप्तये इत्यादिग्राम्यार्थपरिहारः <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारथि|उदारथिः
उदारथि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going upwards.<BR>—2 Rising, enlightening the organs of sense.<BR>—3 Steaming (as a hot dish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारथिः|उदारथि
उदारथि + .{@-थिः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावत्सरः|उदावत्सर
उदावत्सरः A year, one of the five years forming a period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावर्तः|उदावर्त|उदावर्त्त|उदावर्त्तः
उदावर्तः A disease of the bowels, ‘iliac passion’ (characterized<BR> by the retention of excrements).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावर्ता
उदावर्तः + .{@-र्ता@} A painful menstruation with foamy blood; सफेनिलमुदावर्ता<BR> रजः कृच्छ्रेण मुञ्चति Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावसुः|उदावसु
उदावसुः N. of a son of Janaka (king of Videha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्
उदास् €2 Ā. [उद्-आस्] To be indifferent or unconcerned, be careless<BR> or apathetic; to be passive or inactive; तत्किमित्युदासते भरताः<BR> Māl. 1; विधाय वैरं सामर्षे नरोऽरौ य उदासते Śi. 2. 42; Bg. 9. 9;<BR> Sāṅ. K. 20; not to share in; show no interest in; Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास, -सिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Indifferent, apathetic, unconcerned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उदास, -सिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Indifferent, apathetic, unconcerned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासः|उदास
उदास, -सिन् + .{@-सः, -सिन्@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A stoic, philosopher.<BR>—2 One who has no passion for anything, a religious mendicant in general.<BR>—3 Indifference, apathy; stoicism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उदास, -सिन् + .{@-सः, -सिन्@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A stoic, philosopher.<BR>—2 One who has no passion for anything, a religious mendicant in general.<BR>—3 Indifference, apathy; stoicism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासितृ
उदासितृ <i>a.</i> —1 Indifferent, apathetic, stoical; उदासितारं निगृहीतमानसैर्गृहीतमध्यात्मदृशा<BR> कथंचन Śi. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन <i>pres. p.</i><BR>—1 Indifferent, unconcerned, apathetic, passive; उदासीनवदासीनम्<BR> Bg. 9. 9. तद्दर्शिनमुदासीनं त्वामेव पुरुषं विदुः Ku. 2. 13. (taking<BR> no part in the creation of the material universe); see साङ्ख्य; Pt. 1.<BR>—2 (In law) Not involved in any dispute.<BR>—3 Neutral (as a king or nation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीनः|उदासीन
उदासीन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A stranger.<BR>—2 A neutral, an indifferent person; अरिमित्रोदासीनव्यवस्था Mu. 5;<BR> Ms. 7. 158; Y. 1. 345; Bg. 6. 9.<BR>—3 A common acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित <i>a.</i> Set over, appointed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थितः|उदास्थित
उदास्थित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A superintendent.<BR>—2 A door-keeper.<BR>—3 A spy, an emissary; com. on Ms. 7. 154.<BR>—4 An ascetic who has given up his vow. Kau. A. 1. 11<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहित
उदाहित <i>a.</i> Elevated, raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृ
उदाहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To relate, narrate, declare, announce.<BR>—2 To say, speak, utter; उदाजहार द्रुपदात्मजा गिरः Ki. 1. 27; Mk. 9. 4;<BR> Pt. 2; चिकित्सका दोषमुदाहरन्ति M. 2; Māl. 1; त्वां कामिनो<BR> मदनदूतिमुदाहरन्ति V. 4. 11; mutter, repeat; धर्माक्षराणि Mk. 8.<BR>—3 To cite as an instance or illustration, illustrate; त्वमुदाह्रियस्व<BR> कथमन्यथा जनैः Śi. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरणम्
उदाहरणम्<BR>—1 Relating, declaration, saying, utterance.<BR>—2 Narration, recital, opening a conversation; अथाङ्गिरसमग्रण्यमुदाहरणवस्तुषु<BR> Ku. 6. 65; अद्भुतोदाहरणानि Mv. 5 stories or narrations.<BR>—3 A declaratory song or poem, a sort of panegyric beginning with words<BR> like जयति and full of alliteration; पत्रे निवेशितमुदाहरणं<BR> प्रियायाः V. 2. 14; चारणेभ्यस्त्वदीयं जयोदाहरणं श्रुत्वा V. 1;<BR> जयोदाहरणं बाह्वोर्गापयामास किन्नरान् R. 4. 78; (येन केनापि तालेन<BR> गद्यपद्यसमन्वितम् । जयत्युपकमं मालिन्यादिप्रासविचित्रितम् ॥ तदुदाहरणं<BR> नाम विभक्त्यष्टाङ्गसंयुतम् । Pratāparudra.)<BR>—4 An instance, example, illustration; समूलघातमघ्नन्तः परान्नोद्यन्ति<BR> मानिनः । प्रध्वंसितान्धतमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं रविः ॥ Śi. 2. 33;<BR> किमुदाहरणम् Kāśi. पुराणमितिवृत्ताख्यायिकोदाहरणम् … । Kau. A. 1. 5.<BR>—5 (In Nyāya) The third member of an Indian syllogism (which has five members).<BR>—6 Beginning, commencement, introduction.<BR>—7 Exhibition, illustration; U. 1.<BR>—8 (In Rhet.) An illustration reckoned as a figure of speech by some rhetoricians.<BR> It resembles अर्थान्तरन्यास; <i>e. g.</i> अमितगुणोऽपि पदार्थो दोषेणैकेन<BR> निन्दितो भवति । निखिलरसायनराजो गन्धेनोग्रेण लशुन इव ॥ R. G.<BR> (For a clear distinction between the two figures see R. G., under उदाहरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहारः|उदाहार
उदाहारः<BR>—1 An example or illustration.<BR>—2 The beginning of a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृत
उदाहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Said, uttered; तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् Bg. 17. 19.<BR>—2 Named, called; श्रुतान्वितो दशरथ इत्युदाहृतः Bk. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Illustrated.<BR>—4 Stipulated; वनवासं त्वयाऽज्ञप्तः शुल्केत्येतदुदाहृतम् Pratimā 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृतिः|उदाहृति
उदाहृतिः^1 <i>f.</i> An example, illustration.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: from ud-ā-hṛ + suf. ti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदि
उदि €2 P.<BR>—1 To rise (as a star, cloud &c.) (fig. also); come up; उदेति पूर्वं<BR> कुसुमं ततः फलम् Ś. 7. 30; उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति<BR> च Subhāṣ.; Māl. 2. 10; Ki. 2. 36; Bk. 6. 110, 8. 35, 18. 20; to be seen, appear.<BR>—2 To be produced, come out or arise from, spring or proceed from; उदितदयः<BR> Dk. 13; पुण्यः कृशानोरुदियाय धूमः R. 7. 26; उदितश्रियम् 1. 93<BR> v. l.; Ś. 1. 25.<BR>—3 To go out, escape.<BR>—4 To start up; एवमुद्यन्प्रभावेण R. 17. 77.<BR>—5 To rise up against; सयुगे सांयुगीनं तमुद्यन्तं प्रसहेत कः<BR> Ku. 2. 57; य एनमुदीयाद्रथी Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उदय <i>a.</i> (In gram.) Following, coming after or upon (as a letter,<BR> accent &c.); उदयशब्दः परशब्दसमानार्थः प्रातिशाख्येषु प्रसिद्धः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयः|उदय
उदय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Rise (fig. also); चन्द्रोदय इवोदधेः R. 12. 36, 2. 73; going upwards,<BR> ascending (as of the sun, stars &c.).<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Rising up, coming forth; द्रविण˚ acquisition of wealth;<BR> Pt. 2; so भाग्य˚ dawn of fortune; Amaru. 25; स्वगुणोदयेन Pt. 1. 94.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Appearance,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">Page0423-1</a>]<BR> becoming visible, production; घनोदयः प्राक् Ś. 7. 30; मेघ˚<BR> Ku. 6. 54; हसितमन्यनिमित्तकृतोदयम् Ś. 2. 12 raised from some other<BR> cause; Amaru. 88; Ś. 7. 8; फलोदय R. 1. 5; rising or accomplishment<BR> of the fruit; Ms. 3. 169; Ku. 3. 18.<BR>—3 Creation (opp. प्रलय); यः सिन्धूनामुपोदये Rv. 8. 41. 2.<BR> यौ तौ स्वप्नावबोधौ तौ भूतानां प्रलयोदयौ Ku. 2. 8.<BR>—4 The eastern mountain (behind which the sun is supposed to rise); ददर्श<BR> पिङ्गाधिपतेरमात्यं वातात्मजं सूर्यमिवोदयस्थम् Rām. 5. 31. 18. यैर्यत्र<BR> दृश्यते भास्वान्स तेषामुदयः स्मृतः; उदयगूढशशाङ्कमरीचिभिः V. 3. 6.<BR>—5 Advancement, prosperity, rise; (opp. व्यसन), तेजोद्वयस्य युगपद्व्यसनोदयाभ्याम्<BR> Ś. 4. 2; उदये मदवाच्यमुज्झता R. 8. 84; K. 5; importance, celebrity;<BR> ˚उन्मुखे त्वयि R. 11. 73.<BR>—6 Elevation, exaltation, rise, growth; उदयमस्तमयं च रघूद्वहात्<BR> R. 9. 9; तमुदयाय नवा नवयौवना 7; आत्मोदयः परग्लानिः Śi. 2. 30, 11. 60.<BR>—7 Result, consequence; असुखोदयं कर्म Ms. 4. 70; Amaru. 47; following;<BR> नोदात्तस्वरितोदयम् P. VIII. 4. 67.<BR>—8 Accomplishment, fulfilment; उपस्थितोदयम् R. 3. 1; प्रारम्भसदृशोदयः 1. 15.<BR>—9 Profit, advantage.<BR>—10 Income, revenue; Ms. 7. 55; Y. 2. 43.<BR>—11 Interest, consideration paid for the use of money; Y. 2. 67, 146.<BR>—12 Light, splendour.<BR>—13 Outlet, exit.<BR>—14 Beginning; अभिगम्योदयं तस्य कार्यस्य प्रत्यवेदयत् Mb. 3. 282. 22.<BR>—15 Efficacy, influence; पर्याप्तः परवीरघ्न यशस्यस्ते बलोदयः<BR> Rām. 5. 56. 11.<BR>—16 Birthday celebration; हस्ते गृहीत्वा सहराममच्युतं नीत्वा स्ववाटं<BR> कृतवत्यथोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 11. 20. —17 The first lunar mansion; the orient sine.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदयाचलः, उदयाद्रिः, उदयगिरिः, उदयपर्वतः, उदयशैलः, उदयेन्दुः, उदयोन्मुख, उदयक्रमः, उदयज्या, उदयपुरम्, उदयप्रस्थः, उदयप्राणः, उदयराशिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0422-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयाचलः|उदयाचल
उदय + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः, -शैलः the eastern mountain<BR> behind which the sun, moon &c. are supposed to rise; उदयगिरिवनालीबालमन्दारपुष्पम्<BR> Udb.; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत उदयगिरेरिवैक<BR> एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयाद्रिः|उदयाद्रि
उदय + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः, -शैलः the eastern mountain<BR> behind which the sun, moon &c. are supposed to rise; उदयगिरिवनालीबालमन्दारपुष्पम्<BR> Udb.; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत उदयगिरेरिवैक<BR> एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयगिरिः|उदयगिरि
उदय + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः, -शैलः the eastern mountain<BR> behind which the sun, moon &c. are supposed to rise; उदयगिरिवनालीबालमन्दारपुष्पम्<BR> Udb.; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत उदयगिरेरिवैक<BR> एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयपर्वतः|उदयपर्वत|उदयपर्व्वत
उदय + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः, -शैलः the eastern mountain<BR> behind which the sun, moon &c. are supposed to rise; उदयगिरिवनालीबालमन्दारपुष्पम्<BR> Udb.; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत उदयगिरेरिवैक<BR> एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयशैलः|उदयशैल
उदय + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -पर्वतः, -शैलः the eastern mountain<BR> behind which the sun, moon &c. are supposed to rise; उदयगिरिवनालीबालमन्दारपुष्पम्<BR> Udb.; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत उदयगिरेरिवैक<BR> एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयेन्दुः|उदयेन्दु
उदय + -इन्दुः The town इन्द्रप्रस्थ; पुरे कुरूणामुदयेन्दुनाम्नि Mb. 7. 23. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयोन्मुख
उदय + -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> About to rise, expecting prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयक्रमः
उदय + -क्रमः Gradual rise; नाडीनाम् Māl. 5. 2 by gradually inflating<BR> or filling with wind the Nādīs, (as in the act of restraining the wind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयज्या
उदय + -ज्या <i>f.</i> See उदय (17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयपुरम्
उदय + -पुरम् N. of the capital of Mārwār.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयप्रस्थः|उदयप्रस्थ
उदय + -प्रस्थः the plateau of the mountain behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयप्राणः|उदयप्राण
उदय + -प्राणः (pl.) A particular measure of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयराशिः|उदयराशि
उदय + -राशिः The constellation in which the planet is seen when on the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनम्
उदयनम्<BR>—1 Rising, ascending, going up; सूर्यस्योदयनादधि Rv. 1. 48. 7.<BR>—2 Result, consequence.<BR>—3 End, conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनः|उदयन|उदयनं
उदयनम् + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 N. of Agastya.<BR>—2 N. of the king Vatsa; प्राप्यावन्तीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान्<BR> Me. 30. [A celebrated Prince of the lunar race, who is usually styled Vatsarāja.<BR> He reigned at Kauśambī. Vāsavadattā, Princess of Ujjayinī, saw him<BR> in a dream and fell in love with him. He was decoyed to that city and<BR> there kept in prison by Chaṇḍamahāsena, the king. But on being released<BR> by the minister, he carried off Vāsavadattā from her father and a rival<BR> suitor. Udayana is the hero of the play called Ratnāvalī and his life<BR> has been made the subject of several other minor<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">Page0423-2</a>]<BR> compositions. See Vatsa also].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदयनाचार्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनाचार्यः|उदयनाचार्य
उदयनम् + -आचार्यः N. of a philosopher and author of several works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनीय
उदयनीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to the end or conclusion, concluding (as<BR> a ceremony); त्वं प्रायणीयोदयनीयदंष्ट्रः Bhāg. 3. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनीया
उदयनीय + .{@-या@} A concluding sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयिन्
उदयिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rising or ascending.<BR>—2 Streaming or flowing forth; एते निष्कुष्य जङ्घानलकमुदयिनीर्मज्जधाराः<BR> पिबन्ति Māl. 5. 17.<BR>—3 Prosperous, flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Risen, ascended; उदितभूयिष्ठः Māl. 1 mostly risen; Bv. 2. 85;<BR> नित्योदितः Bh. 3. 80; ever-existing.<BR>—2 High, tall, lofty.<BR>—3 Grown, augmented; संमानं मेनिरे सर्वाः प्रहर्षोदितचेतसः Rām. 1. 16. 30.<BR>—4 Born, produced.<BR>—5 Spoken, uttered (fr. वद्).<BR>—6 Renowned, reputed; चित्रयोधी समाख्यातो बभूवातिरथोदितः Mb. 1. 139. 19.<BR>—7 Begun, started; प्रभुभिरुदितक्षत्यै क्षित्यै बुधः स्पृहयेत कः<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 26.<BR>—8 Awaken, got up; तां रात्रिमुषितं रामं सुखोदितमरिन्दमम् Rām. 6. 121. 1.<BR>—9 Ready; अयमनघ तवोदितः प्रियार्थम् Rām. 6. 83. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितम्
उदित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A kind of perfume.<BR>—2 A kind of accent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदितोदित, उदितहोमिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितोदित|उदितोदितः
उदित + -उदित <i>a.</i> Well grounded in the Śāstras, highly spoken of;<BR> पुरोहितमुदितोदितकुलशीलम् Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितहोमिन्
उदित + -होमिन् <i>a.</i> Sacrificing after sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितिः|उदिति
उदितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Ascending, rising (of the sun); पश्येम तदुदितौ सूर्यस्य Av. 7. 5. 3.<BR>—2 Setting, मध्यन्दिन उदिता सूर्यस्य Rv. 5. 69. 3, 76. 3.<BR>—3 Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित्वर
उदित्वर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going up, rising; अविहतगतिर्दैवोद्रेकादुदित्वरविकमः Śiva B. 14. 106.<BR>—2 Exceeding, extra-ordinary; गोप्तुं शौरिरुदित्वरत्वर उदैद् ग्राहग्रहार्तं<BR> गजम् Viś. Guṇā. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेष्यत्
उदेष्यत् <i>a.</i> Increasing, rising; तौ हि मूलमुदेष्यन्त्या जिगीषोरात्मसम्पदः Śi. 2. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्
उदीक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To look up to, look at, view, behold; तमुदीक्ष्याभ्युवाद Bṛ. Up. 6. 2. 1;<BR> सप्रणाममुदीक्षिताः Ku. 6. 7, 7. 67; Amaru. 71.<BR>—2 To expect, look out for, wait for, शत्रुव्यसनम् Mu. 4; त्रीणि<BR> वर्षाण्युदीक्षेत कुमार्यृतुमती सती Ms. 9. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षणम्
उदीक्षणम्<BR>—1 Looking up to.<BR>—2 Seeing, beholding; seeking. द्विपद्वीपिशरण्यानामरण्यानामुदीक्षणम्<BR> Śiva B. 19. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन, उदीच्य See under उदञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीचीन, उदीच्य See under उदञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीप|उदीपः
उदीप <i>a.</i> [उद्गता आपो यत्र, अप् ईप्] P. VI. 3. 97 Flooded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीपः|उदीप
उदीप + .{@-पः@} High water, inundation, flood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्
उदीर् €2 Ā. [उद्-ईर्]<BR>—1 To rise (sound &c.); उदैरत रणितानि Dk. 123 were heard.<BR>—2 To start (to go or come).<BR>—3 To move upwards, ascend, go up.<BR>—4 To arise, originate. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to rise or move.<BR>—2 To utter, pronounce, speak; गिरमुदीरयति K. 13; U. 5, 6; उदीरितोऽर्थः<BR> पशुनापि गृह्यते Pt. 1. 43; so आलोकशब्दम् R. 2. 9.<BR>—3 To call, name; स भीमरूपः शिव इत्युदीर्यते Ku. 5. 77.<BR>—4 To put forth; यदशोकोयमुदीरयिष्यति R. 8. 62.<BR>—5 To cast, throw, roll down (as dice); उदीरयामास सलीलमक्षान् R. 6. 18;<BR> to discharge, drive forward.<BR>—6 To raise, throw up; उदीरितं रजः Śi. 12. 8; उदैरयच्छिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">Page0424-1</a>]<BR> Dk. 103 expanded its hood.<BR>—7 To display, manifest, make visible, cause; तिसृभिस्त्वमवस्थाभिर्महिमानमुदीरयन्<BR> Ku. 2. 6; Śi. 11. 7.<BR>—8 To bring about, effect; विधिनेवार्थमुदीरितं प्रयत्नः Ki. 13. 28.<BR>—9 To rouse, excite, stimulate; उदीरितेन्द्रियः Ku. 4. 41; समुत्पपाताथ<BR> सदस्युदीरितो द्विजातिमुख्यैर्हविषेव पावकः Rām. 5. 47. 2; लोभात्क्रोधः<BR> प्रभवति परदोषैरुदीर्यते Mb. 12. 163. 7. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be cast or thrown upwards, excited, uttered &c.<BR>—2 To sound.<BR>—3 To issue forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरणम्
उदीरणम्<BR>—1 Utterance, pronunciation, expression; उद्घातः प्रणवो यासां न्यायैस्त्रिभिरुदरिणम् Ku. 2. 12.<BR>—2 Speaking, saying.<BR>—3 Throwing, discharging (as a missile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्ण|उदीर्णः
उदीर्ण <i>p. p.</i> [ईर्-क्त]<BR>—1 Grown, ascended, risen, produced, caused; तारोदीर्णग्रैवनादं व्रजन्तः Śi. 18. 37.<BR>—2 Puffed up, elated, grown haughty; स हि देवैरुदीर्णस्य रावणस्य<BR> वधार्थिभिः । भवल्लब्धवरोदीर्णस्तारकाख्यो महासुरः ॥ Ku. 2. 32.<BR>—3 Excited, stimulated, roused; उदीर्णरागप्रतिरोधकं जनैः Śi. 1. 32;<BR> Dk. 43, 47.<BR>—4 Increased, intense.<BR>—5 Generous, great; excellent.<BR>—6 Uttered, pronounced; अनुदीर्णवर्णनिभृतार्थमाह्वयत् Śi. 13. 42.<BR>—7 Ready, strung; ˚धन्वा U. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्णः|उदीर्ण
उदीर्ण + .{@-र्णः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उदीर्णदीधिति, उदीर्णवेग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्णदीधिति
उदीर्ण + -दीधिति <i>a.</i> intensely bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्णवेग
उदीर्ण + -वेग <i>a.</i> violent, impetuous in its course (as a torrent);<BR> महीतलात्केचिदुदीर्णवेगाः Rām. 5. 61. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीषित
उदीषित <i>a.</i> Risen, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बरः|उदुम्बर|उदुंबर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः
उदुम्बरः See उडुम्बर. Threshold; विद्रुमोदुम्बरद्वारैर्वैदूर्यस्तम्भपङ्क्तिभिः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 11. 32. ˚मशक = कूपमण्डूक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बल|उदुंबल|उदुम्बलः
उदुम्बल <i>a.</i> Ved. Mighty, of extended power (उरुबल). उपेषन्तमुदुम्बलम् Av. 8. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बलः|उदुम्बल|उदुंबल
उदुम्बल + .{@-लः@} The fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुष्ट
उदुष्ट <i>a.</i> Ved. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूखल|उदूखलं
उदूखल = उलूखल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदृच्
उदृच् <i>f.</i> [उत्कृष्टा ऋक्]<BR>—1 An excellent Ṛk.<BR>—2 Future time.<BR>—3 Remainder, conclusion, end.<BR>—4 Prosperity, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदे
उदे P. [उद्-आ-इ II. P.] To go up, rise, arise from, come up;<BR> Rv. 6. 51. 1; स ह प्रातः सभाग उदेयाय Ch. Up. 5. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेयिवस्
उदेयिवस् <i>a.</i> Produced, originated, born; सख उदेयिवान्सात्वतां<BR> कुले Bhāg. 10. 31. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजय
उदेजय <i>a.</i> Shaking, causing to tremble, terrifying; उदेजयान्<BR> भूतगणान् न्यषेधीत् Bk. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजया
उदेजय + .{@-या@} <i>f.</i> Perturbance; न तं पश्यामि यस्यासौ भवेन् नोदेजया<BR> मतेः Bk. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदोजस्
उदोजस् <i>a.</i> Very powerful, violent (Ved.). स्तनयदमा रभसा<BR> उदोजसः Rv. 5. 54. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गद्गदिका
उद्गद्गदिका <i>f.</i> Sobbing; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गन्धि|उद्गंधि
उद्गन्धि <i>a.</i> [P. V. 4. 135.]<BR>—1 Fragrant; विजृम्भणोद्गन्धिषु कुड्मलेषु R. 16. 47.<BR>—2 Having a strong smell (good or bad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गम्
उद्गम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To rise or go up, ascend (as a star &c.); असह्यवातोद्गतरेणुमण्डला<BR> Ṛs. 1. 10, v. l.<BR>—2 To shoot up, dart upwards, appear; अचिरोद्गतपल्लवम् V. 4. 23;<BR> Ṛs. 6. 18; so उद्गतशृङ्गो वत्सः वयोतिपातोद्गतवातवेपिते Ki.<BR>—3 To rise or spring from, proceed, originate, arise; इत्युद्गताः पौरवधूमुखेभ्यः<BR> शृण्वन् कथाः R. 7. 16; Amaru. 96.<BR>—4 To go out, break out, depart (as life &c.).<BR>—5 To be famous or well-known, spread; उन्नाभ इत्युद्गतनामधेयः R. 18. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गत|उद्गतं
उद्गत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone up, risen, ascended.<BR>—2 Proceeded forth or from.<BR>—3 Gone, departed.<BR>—4 Vomited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गता
उद्गत + .{@-ता@} N. of a metre.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्गतासु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गतासु
उद्गत + -असु <i>a.</i> deceased, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गतिः|उद्गति
उद्गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going up, rising, ascent.<BR>—2 Appearance; कुसुम˚ K. 59; rise, origin.<BR>—3 Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमः|उद्गम
उद्गमः<BR>—1 Going up, rising (of stars); ascent; आज्यधूमोद्गमेन Ś. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Standing erect (of hair); रोमोद्गमः प्रादुरभूदुमायाः Ku. 7. 77;<BR> व्यक्तरोमोद्गमत्वात् M. 4. 1; Amaru. 40.<BR>—3 Going out, departure, expiry; as in प्राण˚.<BR>—4 Birth, production, creation; पारिजातस्योद्गमः Māl. 2; हरिततृणोद्गमशङ्कया<BR> मृगीभिः Ki. appearance; फलेन सहकारस्य पुष्पोद्गम इव प्रजाः<BR> R. 4. 9; V. 4. 38; भवन्ति नम्रास्तरवः फलोद्गमैः Bh. 2. 70; कतिपयकुसुमोद्गमः<BR> कदम्बः U. 3. 20; so मांस˚, पक्ष˚, ग्रन्थि˚ &c.; Amaru. 81; origin,<BR> parentage; Māl. 2.<BR>—5 Action, vision (of eyes); वारंवारं तिरयति दृशोरुद्गमं बाष्पपूरः Māl. 1. 35.<BR>—6 Projection, elevation; पयोधरोद्गमाम् Māl. 7.<BR>—7 A shoot (of a plant); हरिततृणोद्गमशङ्कया मृगीभिः Ki. 5. 38.<BR>—8 Vomiting, casting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनम्
उद्गमनम् Rising, becoming visible. आड् उद्गमने Vārt. ज्योतिरुद्गमन<BR> इति वक्तव्यम् P. I. 3. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीय|उद्गमनीयं
उद्गमनीय <i>pot. p.</i> To be gone up or ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीयम्
उद्गमनीय + .{@-यम्@} A pair of bleached or washed clothes (तत्स्यादुद्गमनीयं<BR> यद्धौतयोर्वस्त्रयोर्युगम्); धौतोद्गमनीयवासिनी Dk. 42; गृहीतपत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा<BR> Ku. 7. 11 (where Malli. renders उ˚ by धौतवस्त्रम्, and says युगग्रहणं<BR> तु प्रायिकाभिप्रायम् &c.; see <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गल
उद्गल <i>a.</i> Raising the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाढ|उद्गाढं
उद्गाढ <i>a.</i> Deep, intense, violent, strong, excessive, much; उद्गाढरागोदयाः<BR> Māl. 5. 7, 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाढम्
उद्गाढ + .{@-ढम्@} Excess. ━<i>ind.</i> Excessively, extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ, उद्गार &c. See under उद्गै, उद्गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गार|उद्गारः
उद्गातृ, उद्गार &c. See under उद्गै, उद्गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारकमणिः|उद्गारकमणि
उद्गारकमणिः coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गुर्
उद्गुर् €6 Ā. To raise the voice in a menacing manner, to raise (a<BR> weapon, &c.), lift up; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गूर्ण|उद्गूर्णं|उद्गूर्ण्ण
उद्गूर्ण <i>p. p.</i> [गुर्-क्त]<BR>—1 Raised, uplifted, held up; चित्रेष्वप्युद्गूर्णा निपतिताश्च प्रहारा<BR> दृश्यन्ते Mbh. on P. III. 1. 26. क्रोधोद्गूर्णगदस्य Ve. 6. 12; Śi. 5. 25.<BR>—2 Erected, excited.<BR>—3 The act of raising a weapon, threatening; उद्गूर्णे प्रथमो दण्डः<BR> संस्पर्शे तु तदर्धिकः Y. 2. 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गॄ
उद्गॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To eject, spit out, vomit; उद्गिरतो यद्गरलं फणिनः पुष्णासि परिमलोद्गारैः<BR> Bv. 1. 11; उद्गिरन्निव स्नेहम् Śi. 14. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">Page0425-1</a>]<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To emit, send or put forth, pour down or out, discharge, belch<BR> out; सहाम्भसैवापदमुद्गिरन्ति Pt. 5. 67; निक्षेपणात् रागमिवोद्गिरन्तौ Ku. 1. 33.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To send out of the mouth, speak, utter (as words); महीपतेः<BR> शासनमुज्जगार R. 14. 53; Ve. 5. 14; यदुद्गिरति भ्रमरः Mu. 2. 11<BR> (where it also means ‘vomits’ or ‘emits’).<BR>—3 To breathe out.<BR>—4 To rise from. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to pour forth, raise (as sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारः|उद्गार
उद्गारः [उद्-गॄ-घञ् P. III. 3. 29] उन्न्योर्ग्रः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Ejection, spitting out, vomiting, giving out, emitting; खर्जूरीस्कन्धनद्धानां<BR> मदोद्गारसुगन्धिषु R. 4. 57; Bh. 2. 36; सलिलोद्गारमुच्चैर्विमानाः<BR> Me. 65, धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणा जर्जरा निष्पतन्ति Me. 71; Śi. 12. 9.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Oozing, flowing out, stream, issuing out; सनिर्झरोद्गार इवाद्रिराजः<BR> R. 6. 60; रुधिर˚दिग्धाखिलाङ्गाः Mv. 6. 33.<BR>—2 Repeating, narration, citing repeatedly; पुरावृत्तोद्गारैरपि च कथिता<BR> कार्यपदवी Māl. 2. 13; साम˚ K. 42; H. 3. 99; सौजन्य˚ Mv. 4<BR> expression of goodness.<BR>—3 Quantity, mass (thrown out); Mu. 3.<BR>—4 Spittle, saliva.<BR>—5 Eructation, belching. दृष्ट्वोद्गारान् सान्नरसांस्तृप्त्या परमया युताः<BR> Mb. 3. 263. 29.<BR>—6 Sound, roaring, echo, hissing sound (शब्दः, कण्ठगर्जनं नागवायुकर्म);<BR> Śānti. 1. 21; गम्भीरगह्वर˚ Māl. 9.<BR>—7 Overflow, swelling; पश्चिमेन तु तं दृष्ट्वा सागरोद्गारसंनिभम्<BR> Rām. 7. 32. 9, 32. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्गारचूडकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारचूडकः|उद्गारचूडक
उद्गारः + -चूडकः A species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारिन्
उद्गारिन्<BR>—1 Going up, rising, being sent forth; उद्गारिघोरघनघर्घरघोषमेतत्<BR> Mv. 3. 29; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Emitting, sending forth, pouring down; धारास्वनोद्गारिदरीमुखोऽसौ<BR> R. 13. 47; Mk. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारिः
उद्गारिन् + .{@-रिः@} (<i>m.</i>) The 57th year of the Jupiter cycle; उद्गारिसंज्ञं<BR> तदनु क्षयाय नरेश्वराणां विषमा च वृष्टिः Bṛ. S. 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गिरणम्
उद्गिरणम्<BR>—1 Vomiting.<BR>—2 Ejecting anything (as saliva) from the mouth, slavering.<BR>—3 Eructation, belch.<BR>—4 Extermination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीर्ण|उद्गीर्ण्णं
उद्गीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vomited; Śukra. 1. 163; उद्गीर्णस्य वावगीर्णस्य वा मन्थो रोमन्थः<BR> Mbh. on P. III. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Fallen out, ejected; ह्युद्गीर्णद्व्ष्टेर्भ्रमतस्त्वितस्ततः Bhāg. 10. 12. 31.<BR>—3 Caused, effected; कोकिलकाकलीकलकलैरुद्गीर्णकर्णज्वराः Gīt. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गै
उद्गै €1 P.<BR>—1 To sing in a loud tone, sing aloud; उद्गास्यतामिच्छति किन्नराणाम्<BR> Ku. 1. 8; गेयमुद्गातुकामा Me. 88; to sing (in general); उद्गीयमानं<BR> वनदेवताभिः R. 2. 12; निभृताक्षरमुज्जगे Śi. 6. 20.<BR>—2 To begin to sing; त्वं न उद्गायेति तथेति तेभ्योवागुदगायत् Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 2.<BR>—3 To sing or chant (applied to the singing of Sāmaveda); साम सामविदसङ्गमुज्जगौ<BR> Śi. 14. 21; cf. उद्गातृ.<BR>—4 To announce, to celebrate in song.<BR>—5 To sing before one (with acc.).<BR>—5 To fill or make resonant with song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ <i>m.</i> One of the four principal priests at a sacrifice, one<BR> who chants the hymns of the Sāmaveda. उद्गातेव शकुने साम गायसि<BR> Rv. 2. 43. 2; Bṛ. Up. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाथा
उद्गाथा A variety of the Āryā measure, the same as Gīti. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गानम्
उद्गानम् A phase of the साम chant. द्वितीयम् (<i>i. e.</i> उद्गानम्)<BR> साम्नः पर्व उत्पूर्वस्य गायतेरभिधेयं प्रसिद्धम् ŚB. on MS. 3. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीतिः|उद्गीति
उद्गीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Singing aloud.<BR>—2 Chanting of the Sāmaveda.<BR>—3 A variety of the Aryā metre; see Appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीतक
उद्गीतक <i>a.</i> One who sings loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीथः|उद्गीथ
उद्गीथः [उद्-गै-थक्]<BR>—1 Chanting of the Sāmaveda (the office of an Udgātṛ). सामासाद<BR> उद्गीथेऽपश्रयः Av. 15. 3. 8; ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 44.<BR>—2 (The second part of the Sāmaveda; एष उ वा उद्गीथः प्राणो वा उत्प्राणेन<BR> हीदं सर्वमुत्तब्धं वागेव गीथोच्चगीथा चेति स उद्गीथः Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 23.)<BR> भूयांस उद्गीथविदो वसन्ति U. 2. 3.<BR>—3 Designation of ओम् the three syllabled name of God; ओमित्येदक्षरमुद्गीथमुपासीत<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रन्थ्|उद्ग्रंथ्
उद्ग्रन्थ्^1 €1. €9. U.<BR>—1 To bind up, tie into bundles.<BR>—2 To tie up, put or sew together (as garlands &c.); इयमुद्ग्रथते स्रजो<BR> विचित्राः Mu. 1. 4; tie or fasten, intertwine; लताप्रतानोद्ग्रथितैः<BR> स केशैः R. 2. 8.<BR>—3 To unbind, loosen (as a knot &c.). ━<i>Caus.</i> कर्माशयं ग्रथितमुद्ग्रथयन्ति<BR> सन्तः Bhāg. 4. 22. 39; ग्रन्थिमुद्ग्रथयितुं हृदयेशे वाससः स्पृशति<BR> मानधनायाः Śi. 10. 63.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Both grath and granth are possible. But in the dic the main verb granth 'to tie' is given with nasal  and without nasal is given another verb grath/granth with another meaning 'to be crooked'. So for consistency the spelling of the headword should be restored as udgranth (so in AP90 and MW).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रन्थ|उद्ग्रंथ|उद्ग्रन्थः
उद्ग्रन्थ <i>a.</i> Unbound, loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रन्थः|उद्ग्रन्थ|उद्ग्रंथ
उद्ग्रन्थ + .{@-थः@} A section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रथनम्
उद्ग्रथनम् The act of winding, binding; साभिवीक्ष्य दिशः सर्वा<BR> वेण्युद्ग्रथनमुत्तमम् (मणिम्) Rām. 5. 67. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रन्थि|उद्ग्रंथि
उद्ग्रन्थि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untied (fig. also).<BR>—2 Free from worldly ties or attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रह्
उद्ग्रह् €9 P.<BR>—1 To take up, lift up; शक्तिं चोग्रामुदग्रहीत् Bk. 15. 52; elevate,<BR> erect, raise; उद्गृहीतालकान्ताः Me. 8.<BR>—2 To take or draw out, take away. स यथा सैन्धवखिल्य उदके प्रास्त<BR> उदकमेवानुविलीयेत न हास्योद्ग्रहणायेव स्यात् Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 12.<BR>—3 To deposit.<BR>—4 To preserve.<BR>—5 To cease (to rain). यद् गृह्णाति तन्निधनम् Ch. Up. 2. 3. 2.<BR>—6 To break off, discontinue (speaking); उद्गृह्णन् निधनम् Av. 9. 6. 47.<BR>—7 To concede, grant, allow; मायां मदीयामुद्गृह्य वदतां किं नु दुर्घटम्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 22. 4. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to take up or out; cause to pay.<BR>—2 To state, place before, adduce; विशेषविदुषः शास्त्रं यत्तवोद्ग्राह्यते<BR> पुरः Śi. 2. 75.<BR>—4 To extol, laud up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रभणम्
उद्ग्रभणम्, -उद्ग्रामः<BR> [उद्-ग्रह-अन् or अ ‘ग्रहोर्भेच्छन्दसि’ Sk.<BR> on P. III. 1. 84; Vārt.]<BR>—1 Ved. Taking up, raising; उद्ग्राभं च निग्राभं ब्रह्मदेवा अवीवृधन् Ts. 1. 1. 13. 1^1.<BR>—2 Giving, donation.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रामः
उद्ग्रभणम्, -उद्ग्रामः<BR> [उद्-ग्रह-अन् or अ ‘ग्रहोर्भेच्छन्दसि’ Sk.<BR> on P. III. 1. 84; Vārt.]<BR>—1 Ved. Taking up, raising; उद्ग्राभं च निग्राभं ब्रह्मदेवा अवीवृधन् Ts. 1. 1. 13. 1^1.<BR>—2 Giving, donation.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रहणम्
उद्ग्रहणम्<BR>—1 Taking up, raising.<BR>—2 An object that can be accomplished by religious or other acts.<BR>—3 Eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहः|उद्ग्राह
उद्ग्राहः उदि ग्रहः P. III. 3. 35.<BR>—1 Lifting or taking up.<BR>—2 (In the Prātiśākhyas) The rule of Sandhi<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">Page0426-1</a>]<BR> which causes the change of the terminations अः, ए and ओ to<BR> अ before a following vowel.<BR>—3 Replying in argument; rejoinder.<BR>—4 An objection.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्ग्राहपदवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहपदवृत्तिः|उद्ग्राहपदवृत्ति
उद्ग्राहः + -पदवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> the Sandhi called Udgrāha; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहणिका
उद्ग्राहणिका Replying in argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहित|उद्ग्राहितः
उद्ग्राहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Lifted or taken up.<BR>—2 Taken away.<BR>—3 Excellent; exalted.<BR>—4 Deposited, delivered.<BR>—5 Bound, tied.<BR>—6 Recalled, remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रीव
उद्ग्रीव, उद्ग्रीविन् <i>a.</i> With the neck uplifted; उद्ग्रीवैर्मयूरैः<BR> M. 1. 21; Amaru. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रीविन्
उद्ग्रीव, उद्ग्रीविन् <i>a.</i> With the neck uplifted; उद्ग्रीवैर्मयूरैः<BR> M. 1. 21; Amaru. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घः|उद्घ
उद्घः [उद्-हन् अप् निपात˚ P. III. 3. 86.]<BR>—1 Excellence, eminence; (at the end of comp.); ब्राह्मणोद्घः = an<BR> excellent or superior Brāhmaṇa; उद्घादयश्च नियतलिङ्गा न तु विशेष्यलिङ्गाः<BR> Sk.; cf. मतल्लिकामचर्चिका प्रकाण्डमुद्घतल्लजौ । प्रशस्तवाचकान्यमूनि Ak.; cf.<BR> … उद्घान् संघसमागतान् Bk. 7. 64 where उद्घ is used as an adjective.<BR>—2 Happiness.<BR>—3 The hollow hand.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR>—5 A model.<BR>—6 Organic air in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घनः|उद्घन
उद्घनः P. III. 3. 80. A carpenterʼs bench (the plank on which he<BR> works); लौहोद्घनघनस्कन्धां ललितापघनां स्त्रियम् Bk. 7. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घातिन्
उद्घातिन् <i>a.</i> Uneven, rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्
उद्घट् Ā.<BR>—1 To open; द्वारे पुरस्योद्घटितापिधाने Ku. 7. 53. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (-घाटयति) —1 To open, unlock; निरयनगरद्वारमुद्घाटयन्ती<BR> Bh. 1. 63; कपाटमुद्घाटयामि Mk. 3.<BR>—2 To peel off, shell.<BR>—3 To reveal, expose, make known.<BR>—4 To undertake, commence.<BR>—5 To rub over, stroke gently, tickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घटितम्
उद्घटितम् A hint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटः|उद्घाट
उद्घाटः<BR>—1 A watch or guard-house.<BR>—2 The act of exposing or showing (the teeth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटकः|उद्घाटक|उद्घाटकं
उद्घाटकः<BR>—1 A key; उद्घाटको भवति यन्त्रदृढे कपाटे Mk. 3. 16.<BR>—2 The rope and bucket of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटकम्
उद्घाटकः + .({@-कम्@} also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटन|उद्घाटनं
उद्घाटन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Opening, unlocking; धर्मं यो न करोति निन्दितमतिः स्वर्गार्गलोद्घाटनम् H. 1. 133.<BR>—2 Revealing, manifesting; Mārk. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटनम्
उद्घाटन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Opening; Ve. 1.<BR>—2 Raising, lifting up, hoisting.<BR>—3 A key, any means of opening.<BR>—4 The rope and bucket of a well; a water-wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटित|उद्घाटितः
उद्घाटित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Opened, manifested.<BR>—2 Undertaken; commenced.<BR>—3 Raised, lifted up.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्घाटिताङ्ग, उद्घाटितज्ञ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटिताङ्ग
उद्घाटित + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Naked.<BR>—2 Intelligent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटितज्ञ|उद्घाटितज्ञः
उद्घाटित + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> Wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टकः|उद्घट्टक
उद्घट्टकः A kind of time (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टनम्
उद्घट्टनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Friction, striking against; तत्रावश्यं वलयकुलिशोद्घट्टनोद्गीर्णतोयम् Me. 63.<BR>—2 Opening upwards (as a lid).<BR>—3 Outbreak (of violence or passion); Ks.; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टना
उद्घट्टनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Friction, striking against; तत्रावश्यं वलयकुलिशोद्घट्टनोद्गीर्णतोयम् Me. 63.<BR>—2 Opening upwards (as a lid).<BR>—3 Outbreak (of violence or passion); Ks.; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टित
उद्घट्टित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Opened, unlocked.<BR>—2 Separated; अनुकृतिमनुवेलं घट्टितोद्घट्टितस्य Śi. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घसम्
उद्घसम् Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घातः|उद्घात
उद्घातः<BR>—1 P. VII. 3. 54. Beginning, commencement; उद्घातः प्रणवो यासाम् Ku. 2. 12;<BR> आकुमारकथोद्घातं शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR>—2 Allusion, reference; कथोद्घाताः U. 2.<BR>—3 Striking, wounding, inflicting an injury.<BR>—4 A stroke, blow, wound.<BR>—5 Tripping, slipping, jolting, shaking (as of a carriage); ययावनुद्घातसुखेन<BR> सोऽध्वना Śi. 12. 2; R. 2. 72; Ve. 2. 28; चक्र˚ V. 1; U. 5. 1, v. l.<BR>—6 Rising, elevation.<BR>—7 A club, mallet.<BR>—8 A weapon (in general).<BR>—9 Breathing through the nostrils as a religious exercise (Wilson).<BR>—10 A division of a book, chapter; section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घातिन्
उद्घातिन् <i>a.</i> Having ups and downs. उद्घातिनी भूमिरिति मया संयमिता अश्वाः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्
उद्घुष् €1 P. To sound, cry out or shout.<BR> €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To proclaim, declare aloud.<BR>—2 To fill with cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्ट
उद्घुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Sounded out, proclaimed; वार्भिः स्रवद्भिरुद्घुष्टे<BR> निर्विन्ध्यायाः समन्ततः Bhāg. 4. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्टम्
उद्घुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} A sound, noise; उद्घुष्टं वानराणां च राक्षसानां च निःस्वनम्<BR> Rām. 6. 75. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घोषः|उद्घोष
उद्घोषः<BR>—1 Announcing aloud, proclaiming.<BR>—2 Popular talk, general report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घृष्
उद्घृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To rub; lessen by rubbing.<BR>—2 To rub over, strike against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घर्षणम्
उद्घर्षणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, rubbing up; यस्योद्घर्षणलोष्टकैरपि सदा पृष्ठे न जातः<BR> किणः Mk. 2. 11.<BR>—2 Rubbing the skin with hard substances.<BR>—3 A cudgel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घृष्टम्
उद्घृष्टम् A peculiar fault in pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घोण
उद्घोण <i>a.</i> With swelling upturned nostrils. or erected nose (as a boar);<BR> … स्फुरदुद्घोणवदनः …<BR> Śiva B. 22. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंशः|उद्दंश
उद्दंशः<BR>—1 A bug.<BR>—2 A louse.<BR>—3 A mosquito, gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्ड|उद्दंड|उद्दण्डः
उद्दण्ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 With the stalk, stem, or staff raised or rising up; उद्दण्डपद्मं<BR> गृहदीर्घिकाणाम् R. 16. 46; ˚धवलातपत्राः Māl. 6 long; H. 2. 29.<BR>—2 Formidable, terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्डः|उद्दण्ड|उद्दंड
उद्दण्ड + .{@-ण्डः@} A kind of time (in music).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्दण्डपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्डपालः|उद्दण्डपाल|उद्दंडपाल
उद्दण्ड + -पालः<BR>—1 a punisher (whether king or magistrate).<BR>—2 a kind of fish.<BR>—3 a kind of serpent; cf. (उदण्डपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्डित
उद्दण्डित <i>a.</i> Raised, devoted; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दन्तुर|उद्दंतुर|उद्दन्तुरः
उद्दन्तुर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Large-toothed or having projecting teeth.<BR>—2 High, tall (उत्तुङ्ग).<BR>—3 Terrific, formidable (कराल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दमः|उद्दम
उद्दमः Subduing, overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दान्त|उद्दांत
उद्दान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Energetic.<BR>—2 Humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दानम्
उद्दानम् [दो बन्धने ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Binding, confinement; उद्दाने क्रियमाणे तु मत्स्यानां तत्र रज्जुभिः<BR> Mb. 12. 137. 14.<BR>—2 Taming, subduing.<BR>—3 The middle, the waist.<BR>—4 A fire-place.<BR>—5 The submarine fire.<BR>—6 Entrance of the sun into a zodiacal sign (संक्रान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दानकः|उद्दानक
उद्दानकः N. of a tree (शिरीष), Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाम|उद्दामः
उद्दाम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unbound, unrestrained, unchecked, free, bold; भवन्ति नोद्दामगिरां<BR> कवीनाम् Śi. 4. 10.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Strong, powerful, violent; कर्मणोद्दामदण्डानामेव स्याद्वशवर्तिनी<BR> (लक्ष्मीः) Pt. 3. 148; Māl. 3, 7; ˚देहपरिदाहमहाज्वराणि 6. 13.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Furious, intoxicated; स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R. 1. 78; Śi. 11. 19;<BR> U. 3. 6.<BR>—3 Dreadful, formidable; ˚शरीरसंनिवेशः Māl. 3.<BR>—4 Self-willed.<BR>—5 Luxuriant, large, great, excessive; उद्दामानि प्रथयति शिलावेश्मभिर्यौवनानि<BR> Me. 25; उद्दामोत्कलिकाम् Ratn. 2. 4, 4. 22; गन्धोद्दामा धरा exhaling<BR> great smell; Mk. 5. 22.<BR>—6 Proud, haughty; पौलस्त्यविजयोद्दाम Mv. 3. 45 elated.<BR>—7 Unlimited, extra-ordinary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दामः|उद्दाम
उद्दाम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 N. of Yama.<BR>—2 N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दामम्
उद्दाम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i> Violently, fiercely, strongly; अद्योद्दामं ज्वलिष्यतः U. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दित|उद्दितः
उद्दित <i>a.</i> [उद्-दो-क्त] Tied, bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दलन|उद्दलनः
उद्दलन <i>a.</i> Tearing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दलनः|उद्दलन
उद्दलन + .{@-नः@} The act of splitting, causing to burst (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालः|उद्दाल
उद्दालः<BR>—1 N. of a plant, Cordia Myxa or Latifolia (बहुवारक; Mar. भोकरी).<BR>—2 The sage उद्दालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालकः|उद्दालक
उद्दालकः =<BR>—1 उद्दाल q. v.<BR>—2 N. of a sage; उद्दालक आरुणिः Bṛ. Up. 3. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालकम्
उद्दालकः + .{@-कम्@} A kind of honey.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्दालकपुष्पभञ्जिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालकपुष्पभञ्जिका
उद्दालकः + -पुष्पभञ्जिका [उद्दालकानां पुष्पाणि भज्यन्ते यत्र कीडायां ण्वुल्]<BR> a sort of game played by the people in the eastern districts (in which<BR> Uddālaka flowers are broken or crushed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालकायनः|उद्दालकायन
उद्दालकायनः A descendant or son of उद्दालक <i>i. e.</i> श्वेतकेतु;<BR> गार्ग्यायण उद्दालकायनात् Bṛ. Up. 4. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिनम्
उद्दिनम् Mid-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्
उद्दिश् €6 U.<BR>—1 To point out, signify, declare, denote, mention, tell; प्रथमोद्दिष्टमास्पदम्<BR> Ku. 6. 35; Ms. 8. 52, 3. 182; Me. 30; यथोद्दिष्टव्यापारा Ś. 3; अनेडमूक<BR> उद्दिष्टः शठे Med. denotes or signifies.<BR>—2 To enunciate, prophesy; त्वं साधुभिरुद्दिष्टः Ś. 5.<BR>—3 To refer or allude to, have reference to; स्मरमुद्दिश्य Ku. 4. 38;<BR> Ś. 6, see उद्दिश्य below.<BR>—4 To mean, intend, aim at, direct towards, destine for, assign to, dedicate<BR> to; K. 40; उद्दिष्टामुपनिहितां भजस्व पूजाम् Māl. 5. 25; फलमुद्दिश्य Bg. 17. 21.<BR>—5 To explain, teach, advise; सतां केनोद्दिष्टं विषममसिधाराव्रतमिदम् Bh. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्य
उद्दिश्य <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With reference to, aiming at, in the direction of, towards; वध्यशिलामुद्दिश्य<BR> प्रस्थितः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 For, for the sake of, on account of, in the name of; त्वां˚ Ś. 3<BR> on thy account; किं˚ for what purpose, on what account; निमित्तम्˚<BR> Pt. 1. 283 for some cause; त्वामुद्दिश्य सभाजनाक्षराणि M. 5 in your name.<BR>—3 Demanding, stipulating for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिष्ट
उद्दिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mentioned, particularized, specially told.<BR>—2 Desired, wished for.<BR>—3 Explained, taught &c.<BR>—4 Renowned, famous; पलायनेन चोद्दिष्टाः प्राणान्रक्षामहे वयम् । एकेन<BR> वहवो भग्ना यशोनाशं गमिष्यति ॥ Rām. 6. 66. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशः|उद्देश
उद्देशः<BR>—1 Pointing to or at, directing; सूर्योद्देशेन तिला दातव्याः Pt. 2 in the name of.<BR>—2 Mention, specification; सार्धप्रहरद्वयोद्देशे Pt. 5; स्वरसंस्कारोद्देशः Nir.<BR>—3 Illustration, explanation, exemplification.<BR>—4 Ascertainment, determination, inquiry, investigation, search.<BR>—5 A brief statement or account; एष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो<BR> मया Bg. 10. 40; Mb. 8. 69. 54.<BR>—6 Assignment, allotment.<BR>—7 Stipulation, bargain.<BR>—8 Object, motive; कृतोद्देशः स बीभत्सुः Mb. 3. 158. 3.<BR>—9 A spot, region, place; अहो प्रवातसुभगोयमुद्देशः Ś. 3; M. 3;<BR> वन˚ a part of the forest.<BR>—10 Upper region, high position.<BR>—11 (In phil.) The enunciation of a thing by its name (which is to be<BR> further discussed and explained), the other two processes being लक्षण<BR> and परीक्षा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्देशपदम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशपदम्
उद्देशः + -पदम् The term (or terms) which form the subject; नात्रैषा वचनव्यक्तिः<BR> ये यजमाना इत्युद्देशपदम्, ऋत्विजः इति विधेयपदम् । ŚB. on MS. 6. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशक|उद्देशकः
उद्देशक <i>a.</i> Illustrative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशकः|उद्देशक
उद्देशक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An illustration, example.<BR>—2 An illustrator, a guide.<BR>—3 (In Math.) A question, problem; अत्रोद्देशकः (frequently occurring<BR> in Līlāvatī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशतः
उद्देशतः <i>ind.</i> Pointedly, distinctly; एष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तः Bg. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्य|उद्देश्यः
उद्देश्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be illustrated or explained.<BR>—2 To be intended or aimed at.<BR>—3 That to which one refers or which one has in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्यम्
उद्देश्य + .{@-श्यम्@}<BR>—1 The object in view, an incentive.<BR>—2 The subject of an assertion (opp. विधेय); see the word अनुवाद्य also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्यक
उद्देश्यक <i>a.</i> Pointing at or to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देष्टृ
उद्देष्टृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pointing out.<BR>—2 One who acts with a certain object in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्
उद्दीप् €4 Ā. To flame, blaze up, be kindled; बाणवदनमुददीपि<BR> भिये Śi. 15. 48; उद्दीप्यस्व जातवेदः Mahānār. Up. 2. 8; Kauś.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To light up, inflame, illuminate, kindle; पुनस्त्वोद्दीपयामसि Av. 12. 2. 5.<BR> उद्दीपितकोपानलाः Ve. 2.<BR>—2 To excite, animate, fire; पुत्रवधामर्षोद्दीपितेन Ve. 2; न वैरमुद्दीपयति<BR> प्रशान्तम् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपः|उद्दीप
उद्दीपः<BR>—1 Inflaming, lighting.<BR>—2 An inflamer.<BR>—3 That which animates or excites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपम्
उद्दीपः + .{@-पम्@} Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपक|उद्दीपकः
उद्दीपक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Exciting, rendering more intense; गरलस्योद्दीपकतया Dk. 9 virulence.<BR>—2 Lighting, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपकः|उद्दीपक
उद्दीपक + .{@-कः@} A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपका
उद्दीपक + .{@-का@} A kind of ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपनम्
उद्दीपनम्<BR>—1 Inflaming, exciting; क्रोध˚, अग्नि˚.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) That which excites or feeds (a sentiment or <i>rasa</i>), any<BR> aggravating or attendant circumstance<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">Page0428-1</a>]<BR> which gives poignancy to a feeling or passion; उद्दीपनविभावास्ते रसमुद्दीपयन्ति<BR> ये S. D. 160; see आलम्बनम् also.<BR>—3 Illuminating, lighting, setting fire to, burning; जतुमयशरणोद्दीपनः Ve. 5. 26.<BR>—4 Burning of a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्त|उद्दीप्तः
उद्दीप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Lighted, set on fire.<BR>—2 Shining, bright.<BR>—3 Inflamed, excited, aggravated (as passion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्र|उद्दीप्रं|उद्दीप्रः
उद्दीप्र <i>a.</i> [दीप-रन्] P. III. 2. 147. Shining, blazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्रः|उद्दीप्र|उद्दीप्रं
उद्दीप्र + .{@-प्रः, -प्रम्@} Bdellium (Mar. गुग्गुळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्रम्
उद्दीप्र + .{@-प्रः, -प्रम्@} Bdellium (Mar. गुग्गुळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दूष्य
उद्दूष्य <i>ind.</i> Having publicly calumniated or discredited; Śi. 2. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दृश्
उद्दृश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To see above, look upwards (lit.)<BR>—2 To look into the future; expect; look up to; Mv. 6; उत्पश्यतः सिंहनिपातमुग्रम् R. 2. 60.<BR>—3 To doubt.<BR>—4 To be aware of. ━<i>Caus.</i> To make visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दर्शनम्
उद्दर्शनम् Making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीर्ण
उद्दीर्ण <i>a.</i> Torn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देहिका
उद्देहिका The white ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्युत्
उद्द्युत् €1 Ā. To blaze up, shine; उदु ष्टुतः समिधा यह्णो अद्यौद्<BR> Rv. 3. 5. 9. ━<i>Caus.</i> —1 To cause to shine; (hence) adorn, grace;<BR> जाते पुनरप्युद्द्योतयोत्संगम् U. 4; अलमुद्द्योतयामासुर्देवारण्यमिवर्तवः R. 10. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योत|उद्द्योतः
उद्द्योत <i>a.</i> Shining, blazing; हर्षरश्मिभिरुद्द्योतं तस्यान्तःपुरमाबभौ<BR> Rām. 1. 16. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योतः|उद्द्योत
उद्द्योत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Light, lustre (lit. and fig.); देहोद्द्योतैर्दशाशाः कपिशयति मुहुर्द्वादशादित्यदीप्तिः<BR> Nāg. 4. 22. त्रिभिर्नेत्रैः कृतोद्द्योतम् Mb.; कुलोद्द्योतकरी तव<BR> Rām. adorning or gracing.<BR>—2 Revelation.<BR>—3 A division of a book, chapter, section.<BR>—4 N. of the commentary on Ratnāvalī, on Kāvyapradīpa, and on महाभाष्यप्रदीप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योतनम्
उद्द्योतनम् The act of enlightening, illumination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्राव|उद्द्रावः
उद्द्राव <i>a.</i> Running away; स्वाहोद्द्रावाय Vāj. 22. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्रावः|उद्द्राव
उद्द्राव + .{@-वः@} Flight, retreat; P. III. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धन्
उद्धन् €2 P. [उद्-हन्] To raise up, elevate (fig. also) Rv. 10. 102. 7.<BR> Ā. To kill oneʼs self; Rām.; Pt. see उद्धत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धत|उद्धतं|उद्धतः
उद्धत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised up, elevated, lifted up; लाङ्गूलमुद्धतं धुन्वन् Bk. 9. 7;<BR> आत्मोद्धतैरपि रजोभिः Ś. 1. 8 raised; खुर˚ R. 9. 50, heaved; Ki. 8. 53.<BR>—2 Excessive, very much, exceeding.<BR>—3 Haughty, vain, puffed up; प्रहितो रावणेनैष सह वीरैर्मदोद्धतैः<BR> Rām. 5. 58. 130. अक्षवधोद्धतः R. 12. 63.<BR>—4 Harsh; वचनै रसतां महीयसो न खलु व्येति गुरुत्वमुद्धतैः Śi. 16. 27.<BR>—5 Excited, inflamed, intensified; ˚मनोभवरागा Ki. 9. 68, 69; मदोद्धताः<BR> प्रत्यनिलं विचेरुः Ku. 3. 31,<BR>—6 Majestic, stately; ill-mannered.<BR>—7 Abounding in, full; ततस्तु धारोद्धतमेघकल्पम् Rām. 6. 67. 142.<BR>—8 Eager, ready; युद्धोद्धतकृतोत्साहः संग्रामं सम्प्रपद्यत Rām. 5. 48. 16.<BR>—9 Shining, glittering; अन्योन्यं रजसा तेन कौशेयोद्धतपाण्डुना Rām. 6. 55. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतः|उद्धत|उद्धतं
उद्धत + .{@-तः@} A kingʼs wrestler.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्धतमनस्, उद्धतमनस्क<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्
उद्धत + -मनस्, -मनस्क <i>a.</i> high-minded, haughty, proud, ˚त्वम् Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्क
उद्धत + -मनस्, -मनस्क <i>a.</i> high-minded, haughty, proud, ˚त्वम् Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतिः|उद्धति
उद्धतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Elevation.<BR>—2 Pride, haughtiness; नैवोद्धतिमाजगाम Śi. 3. 28.<BR>—3 Rudeness, insolence; नयति द्रुतमुद्धतिश्रितः 16. 72.<BR>—4 A stroke, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धम|उद्धमः
उद्धम See under उद्ध्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर
उद्धर, -उद्धार<BR> See under उद्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धार|उद्धारं|उद्धारः
उद्धर, -उद्धार<BR> See under उद्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्ष|उद्धर्षः
उद्धर्ष <i>a.</i> Delighted, glad; पतिमागतमाकर्ण्य पत्न्युद्धर्षाऽतिसम्भ्रमा<BR> Bhāg. 10. 81. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षः|उद्धर्ष
उद्धर्ष + .{@-र्षः@}<BR>—1 Great joy or delight.<BR>—2 Courage or energy to undertake a thing; अमर्षजनितोद्धर्षाश्चकुः<BR> कर्माण्यभीतवत् Rām. 6. 52. 6.<BR>—3 A festival (especially a religious one).<BR>—4 Excess, abundance; (उद्रेक); आपूर्यत बलोद्धर्षैर्वायुवेगैरिवार्णवः<BR> Rām. 6. 74. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षण|उद्धर्षणं
उद्धर्षण <i>a.</i> Animating, encouraging, exciting; हितमुद्धर्षणं<BR> चैव उवाच प्रथितं वचः Rām. निदर्शनान्युपायांश्च बहून्युद्धर्षणानि<BR> च Mb. 5. 135. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षणम्
उद्धर्षण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Animating.<BR>—2 Erection of the hair (on the body), thrill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षिन्
उद्धर्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Encouraging.<BR>—2 (Ved.) One whose hair is erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धवः|उद्धव
उद्धवः<BR>—1 A sacrificial fire.<BR>—2 A festival, holiday.<BR>—3 N. of a Yādava, uncle and friend of Kṛṣṇa. [When Kṛṣṇa was<BR> taken by Akrūra to Maṭhurā, Uddhava was implored by the citizens of<BR> Gokula to go and fetch him. He was very much attached to Kṛṣṇa. On<BR> seeing the destruction of the Yādavas to be inevitable, he went to Kṛṣṇa<BR> and asked him what to do; whereupon he was told to go to Badarikāśrama<BR> to practise penance and to secure heaven. He is the subject of two short<BR> poems, उद्धवदूत and उद्धवसंदेश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धस्त
उद्धस्त <i>a.</i> Extending or raising the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धा
उद्धा I. €3 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To abandon or expose (an infant).<BR>—2 To set up, erect, build. ━II. €3 Ā.<BR>—1 To go or move upwards, rise (as the sun, dust &c.); यतो रजः पार्थिवमुज्जिहीते<BR> R. 13. 64; Mu. 4. 21; Bk. 18. 27; N. 22. 45, 55.<BR>—2 To go away from, depart; उज्जिहानजीविताम् Māl. 10.<BR>—3 To raise; शिरसा यूपमुज्जिहीते Kāty.<BR>—4 To throw up, knit (as eyebrows); सौमित्रिरक्षिभ्रुवमुज्जिहानः Bk. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जिहाना
उज्जिहाना N. of a town; उद्यानमुज्जिहानायाः प्रियका यत्र पादपाः<BR> Rām. 2. 71. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान|उद्धानं|उद्धानः
उद्धान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ejected, vomited.<BR>—2 Inflated, corpulent, fat.<BR>—3 Gone up, ascended, risen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धानम्
उद्धान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A fireplace.<BR>—2 Ejecting, vomiting.<BR>—3 Abandonment, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धिः|उद्धि
उद्धिः [उद्-धा-कि] उपसर्गे धोः किः P. III. 3. 92. Ved.<BR>—1 A particular part of a carriage (the part which rests on the axles).<BR>—2 An earthen stand on which the Ukhā rests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धित
उद्धित <i>p. p.</i> Set up, erected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान्त|उद्धांत|उद्धान्तः
उद्धान्त <i>a.</i> Ejected, vomited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान्तः|उद्धान्त|उद्धांत
उद्धान्त + .{@-तः@} An elephant out of rut (from whose temples ichor ceases to flow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धुर
उद्धुर <i>a.</i> [उद्गता धूरस्मात्]<BR>—1 Freed from a burden or yoke, unrestrained, unchecked, free. <i>cf.</i><BR> सैन्धवाः समरोद्धुराः Śiva B. 9. 65; also सङ्गरोद्धुराः <i>ibid.</i> 25. 19.<BR>—2 Firm, intrepid, bold; अभियोग˚ Mv. 6.<BR>—3 Victorious, conquering.<BR>—4 High, loud (voice &c.); पितरमुद्धुरध्वनिमहाजनानुयातमानीय Dk. 104.<BR>—5 Heavy, full of; जग्मे जयोद्धुरविशालविषाणमुक्ष्णा Śi. 5. 64.<BR>—6 Thick, gross.<BR>—7 Lively, cheerful.<BR>—8 Able, competent; मृद्वीकामधुमाधुरीमदपरीहारोद्धुराणां गिराम् Bv. 4. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धू
उद्धू €5. €9. U.<BR>—1 To shake, move up, raise, throw up, wave (as a <i>chawari</i>); कैर्नोद्धूतानि<BR> चामराणि K. 117, 200; Ku. 2. 29; उद्धूनीयात सत्केतून् Bk. 19. 8; Ki. 5. 39.<BR>—2 To shake or throw off; संमार्जन्यो नूनमुद्धूयमाना भान्ति स्मोच्चैः<BR> केतनानां पताकाः Śi. 18. 8 dispel, destroy (fig.); उद्धूतपापाः Me. 57.<BR>—6 To disturb, excite, rouse up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूत
उद्धूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken off, fallen from; raised or thrown up; मारुतभरोद्धूतोऽपि<BR> धूलिव्रजः Dhan. V.<BR>—2 Exalted, high, loud.<BR>—3 Ruffled, tossed up; उद्धूतमिव सागरम् Mb. 5. 193. 4.<BR>—4 Blossomed, cheerful; आसीद्वनमिवोद्धूत स्त्रीवनं रावणस्य तत् Rām. 5. 9. 66.<BR>—5 High, gone up (उन्नत); देवदारुभिरुद्धूतैरूर्ध्वबाहुमिव स्थितम्<BR> Rām. 5. 56. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूतम्
उद्धूत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Stamping.<BR>—2 Throwing up.<BR>—3 Turning up; digging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूननम्
उद्धूननम्<BR>—1 Throwing upwards, raising.<BR>—2 Shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूपनम्
उद्धूपनम् Fumigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूलनम्
उद्धूलनम्<BR>—1 Powdering, sprinkling with dust or powder; भस्मोद्धूलन भद्रमस्तु<BR> भवने K. P. 10; K. 129.<BR>—2 An article used to season food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूलयति
उद्धूलयति Den. P. To powder, sprinkle with powder or dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूषणम्
उद्धूषणम् Erection of the hair (on the body), thrill, horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृषित
उद्धृषित <i>a.</i> Having the hairs erect (through joy); Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृ
उद्धृ I. €1. €10 P.<BR>—1 To draw out, raise up. —2 To save, deliver; भगवति तव स्पृष्टानद्भिश्चिरादुददीधरत्<BR> U. 1. 23. ━II. [उद्-हृ] —1 To draw or take out, extract, extricate; शरं<BR> … उद्धर्तुमैच्छत् R. 2. 30, 3. 64; to deliver from, relieve of, save,<BR> rescue, protect (with abl.); मां तावदुद्धर शुचो दयिताप्रवृत्त्या<BR> V. 4. 31; Pt. 1. 358; Bg. 6. 5.<BR>—2 To uproot, extirpate, eradicate; tear or pull out; नमयामास नृपाननुद्धरन्<BR> R. 8. 9, 4. 66; त्रिदिवमुद्धृतदानवकण्टकम् Ś. 7. 3; Mv. 3. 13;<BR> Māl. 9. 22; उद्धरणीये चक्षुषी Dk. 102.<BR>—3 To pluck up (flowers &c.); K. 21, 144.<BR>—4 To raise, lift up, elevate, extend (as hands); पातयितुमेव शक्तिर्नान्नपिटमुद्धर्तुम्<BR> Pt. 1. 363; Ms. 4. 62; V. 4. 34.<BR>—5 To take up, absorb (water); उद्धरिष्यन्रसानिव R. 4. 66; उद्धृत्य<BR> मेघैस्तत एव तोयम् Śi. 3. 75.<BR>—6 To sustain, bear up; राज्यधुरमुद्धर्तुम् Pt. 1.<BR>—7 To separate, abstract.<BR>—8 To remove, put away.<BR>—9 To deduct, subtract. विट्पण्यमुद्धृतोद्धारं विकेयं वित्तवर्धनम् Ms. 10. 85.<BR>—10 To select, pick out; एवं समुद्धतोद्धारे समानंशान्प्रकल्पयेत् Ms. 9. 116.<BR>—11 To present,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">Page0429-2</a>]<BR> offer; Y. 1. 159.<BR>—12 To prove; आगमस्तु कृतो येन सोऽभियुक्तस्तमुद्धरेत् Y. 2. 28.<BR>—13 To divide (as with partners).<BR>—14 To publish, make known.<BR>—15 To undo, destroy; एष त्वां सजनामात्यमुद्धरामि स्थिरो भव Mb. 5. 189. 23.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to extract or draw out; शल्यं<BR> निखातमुदहारयतामुरस्तः R. 9. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरणम्
उद्धरणम्<BR>—1 Drawing or taking out, taking off (clothes &c.).<BR>—2 Extraction, pulling or tearing out; कण्टक˚ Ms. 9. 252; चक्षुषोरुद्धरणम्<BR> Mit.; so शल्य˚.<BR>—3 Extricating, deliverance, rescuing (from danger); दीनोद्धरणोचितस्य<BR> R. 2. 25; स बन्धुर्यो विपन्नानामापदुद्धरणक्षमः H. 1. 29.<BR>—4 Destruction, eradication, extermination, deposition, dethronement;<BR> चन्द्रगुप्तस्योद्धरणात् Mu. 4.<BR>—5 Lifting, raising.<BR>—6 Taking a part or share.<BR>—7 Taking from the Gārhapatya fire to supply the other sacred fires.<BR>—8 Vomiting; जग्धस्य मोहाद्धि विशुद्धिमन्धसो जुगुप्सितस्योद्धरणं प्रचक्षते<BR> Bhāg. 4. 4. 18.<BR>—9 Anything vomited.<BR>—10 Final emancipation.<BR>—11 Acquittance of debt.<BR>—12 Hoping, expecting; अपि ते ब्राह्मणा भुक्त्वा गताः सोद्धरणान् गृहान्<BR> Mb. 13. 60. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्तृ|उद्धर्त्तृ
उद्धर्तृ, उद्धारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who raises or lifts up.<BR>—2 A sharer, co-heir.<BR>—3 One who recovers property. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A destroyer, exterminator; Y. 2. 271.<BR>—2 A saviour, deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारक
उद्धर्तृ, उद्धारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who raises or lifts up.<BR>—2 A sharer, co-heir.<BR>—3 One who recovers property. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A destroyer, exterminator; Y. 2. 271.<BR>—2 A saviour, deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारकविधिः|उद्धारकविधि
उद्धारकविधिः <i>m.</i> Mode of giving or paying; तत्कथय कथमस्योद्धारकविधिर्भविष्यति Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारः|उद्धार|उद्धारं
उद्धारः<BR>—1 Drawing out, extraction.<BR>—2 Deliverance, redemption, saving, rescuing, extrication.<BR>—3 Raising, lifting up.<BR>—4 Deduction, a part to be set aside.<BR>—5 (In law) A part to be set aside from the paternal property for the<BR> benefit of the eldest son; the surplus allowed by law to the eldest beyond<BR> the shares of the younger brothers; ज्येष्ठस्य विंश उद्धारः सर्वद्रव्याच्च<BR> यद्वरम् Ms. 9. 112.<BR>—6 The sixth part of booty taken in war which belongs to the king; राज्ञश्च<BR> दद्युरुद्धारमित्येषा वैदिकी श्रुतिः Ms. 7. 97.<BR>—7 An obligation.<BR>—8 Debt, particularly such as bears no interest.<BR>—9 Recovering property.<BR>—10 Marching out.<BR>—11 Citing (a passage), quoting.<BR>—12 Final beatitude.<BR>—13 Prosperity, elevation.<BR>—14 Compilation.<BR>—15 Leavings of dishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारा
उद्धारः + .{@-रा@} The plant गुडूची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारम्
उद्धारः + .{@-रम्@} A fire-place.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्धारकोशः, उद्धारविभागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारकोशः|उद्धारकोश
उद्धारः + -कोशः N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारविभागः|उद्धारविभाग
उद्धारः + -विभागः Division of shares, partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारणम्
उद्धारणम्<BR>—1 Raising, elevating.<BR>—2 Rescuing, drawing out of (danger), delivering.<BR>—3 Sharing, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारित
उद्धारित <i>a.</i> Taken out, drawn forth, extricated, released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृत|उद्धृतः
उद्धृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drawn up or out (water), extracted &c.<BR>—2 Raised, elevated, lifted up, thrown up or upwards; निक्षेपणाय पदमुद्धृतमुद्वहन्ती Ku. 5. 85.<BR>—3 Uprooted, eradicated; उद्धृतारिः R. 2. 30.<BR>—4 Separated, set<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-1" target="_blank">Page0430-1</a>]<BR> apart.<BR>—5 Divided, partitioned; ऋग्यजुःसामाथर्वाख्या वेदाश्वत्वार उद्धृताः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 4. 20.<BR>—6 Selected.<BR>—7 Dispersed, scattered.<BR>—8 Holding, containing.<BR>—9 Uncovered.<BR>—10 Vomited, cast up.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्धृतोद्धार, उद्धृतस्नेह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतोद्धार
उद्धृत + -उद्धार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has received his share of the patrimony.<BR>—2 that from which the proper part has been deducted; Ms. 10. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतस्नेह
उद्धृत + -स्नेह <i>a.</i> skimmed (as milk); न भुञ्जीतोद्धृतस्नेहम् Ms. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतिः|उद्धृति
उद्धृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Drawing or pulling out, extracting.<BR>—2 An extract, passage selected.<BR>—3 Delivering, rescuing.<BR>—4 Especially, delivering or purifying from sin, final liberation; त्रपन्ते<BR> तीर्थानि त्वरितमिह यस्योद्धृतिविधौ G. L. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्मा
उद्ध्मा €1 P.<BR>—1 To breathe out, puff, blow.<BR>—2 To inflate, to make known by blowing (a trumpet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

