उद्भिद|उद्भिदं
उद्भिद <i>a.</i> Sprouting, germinating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिदम्
उद्भिद + .{@-दम्@} Culinary salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिन्न
उद्भिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Produced, generated, developed; formed; स्वयमेव ब्रह्मबन्धनोद्भिन्नो<BR> दुर्गप्रयोगः M. 4; R. 13. 21; रविप्रभोद्भिन्नशिरोमणिप्रभः Ṛs. 1. 20.<BR>—2 Shot forth, germinated; नीतिपादपस्य पुष्पमुद्भिन्नम् M. 1; Ku. 1. 24.<BR>—3 Opened, expanded, budded; as in यौवनोद्भिन्नशैशवा.<BR>—4 Breaking out, appearing; ˚रोमपुलकैः C. P. 34; Ś. 6.<BR>—5 Betrayed; उद्भिन्नास्मि सहवासिन्या विस्रम्भेण Māl. 7; Kām. 17. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0430-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भेदः|उद्भेद
उद्भेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Breaking through or out, becoming visible, appearance, display, manifestation,<BR> growth, development; किसलयोद्भेदप्रतिद्वन्द्विभिः Ś. 4. 5; उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु<BR> प्रवृद्धः Ku. 7. 24; तं यौवनोद्भेदविशेषकान्तम् R. 5. 38; Śi. 18. 36;<BR> Mu. 5. 3. पुष्पोद्भेदं शरकिसलयैर्भूषणानां विशेषात् । Me. 76.<BR>—2 Breaking, splitting; प्रस्तरोद्भेदयोग्यः U. 3. 25.<BR>—3 A spring, fountain.<BR>—4 Horripilation; as in पुलकोद्भेद, रोमोद्भेद,<BR>—5 Treason, betrayal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भेदनम्
उद्भेदः, -दनम्<BR>—1 Breaking through or out, becoming visible, appearance, display, manifestation,<BR> growth, development; किसलयोद्भेदप्रतिद्वन्द्विभिः Ś. 4. 5; उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु<BR> प्रवृद्धः Ku. 7. 24; तं यौवनोद्भेदविशेषकान्तम् R. 5. 38; Śi. 18. 36;<BR> Mu. 5. 3. पुष्पोद्भेदं शरकिसलयैर्भूषणानां विशेषात् । Me. 76.<BR>—2 Breaking, splitting; प्रस्तरोद्भेदयोग्यः U. 3. 25.<BR>—3 A spring, fountain.<BR>—4 Horripilation; as in पुलकोद्भेद, रोमोद्भेद,<BR>—5 Treason, betrayal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भू
उद्भू €1 P.<BR>—1 To arise, spring up, be produced from; उदभून्मुरजध्वनिः, अन्तरीक्षात्सरस्वती<BR> &c. see उद्भव below.<BR>—2 To occur, take place; उदभवत्तीव्रो दुर्भिक्षः Ks. 27. 94.<BR>—3 To ascend, go up, mount.<BR>—4 To suffice.<BR>—5 To rise in arms, revolt, rebel. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to exist, create, produce; मायां मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोसि R. 2. 62.<BR>—2 To proclaim; माहात्म्यम् K. 109.<BR>—3 To use, employ.<BR>—4 To raise, elevate.<BR>—5 To consider, think; Vikr. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवः|उद्भव
उद्भवः<BR>—1 Production, creation, birth, generation (lit. and fig.); इति हेतुस्तदुद्भवे<BR> K. P. 1; Y. 3. 80; the place or object of origin; मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहमुद्भवश्च<BR> भविष्यताम् Bg. 10. 34; oft. at the end of comp. in the sense of ‘springing or arising from’<BR>, ‘produced from’; ऊरूद्भवा V. 1. 3; मणिराकरोद्भवः R. 3. 18.<BR>—2 Source, origin; उद्भवो यशसः K. 54.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu; उद्भवः क्षोभणो देवः V. Sah.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्भवकर, उद्भवक्षेत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवकर
उद्भवः + -कर <i>a.</i> productive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवक्षेत्रम्
उद्भवः + -क्षेत्रम् birth-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावः|उद्भाव
उद्भावः<BR>—1 Production, generation.<BR>—2 Magnanimity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावनम्
उद्भावनम्<BR>—1 Thinking, thinking over.<BR>—2 Production, generation, creation; Mb. 13.<BR>—3 Speaking, saying.<BR>—4 Inattention, neglect, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावयितृ
उद्भावयितृ <i>a.</i> Raising upwards, lifting up, exalting (fig. also);<BR> उद्भावयिता बन्धून् Dk. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूत|उद्भूतः
उद्भूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Born, produced, generated.<BR>—2 Lofty (lit. and fig.).<BR>—3 Visible, perceptible, capable of being perceived by the senses; as a गुण.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्भूतरूपम्, उद्भूतस्पर्शवत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतरूपम्
उद्भूत + -रूपम् Visible form or shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतस्पर्शवत्|उद्भूतस्पर्शवन्त्
उद्भूत + -स्पर्शवत् <i>a.</i> Tangible; Bhāṣā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतिः|उद्भूति
उद्भूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Generation, production.<BR>—2 Elevation, exaltation, prosperity; वरः शंभुरलं ह्येष त्वत्कुलोद्भूतये<BR> विधिः Ku. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रम्
उद्भ्रम् €1. €4. P. To wander, roam about; धावत्युद्भ्रमति प्रमीलति<BR> पतत्युद्याति मूर्छत्यपि Gīt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रमः|उद्भ्रम
उद्भ्रमः<BR>—1 Whirling, turning round, flourishing (as of a sword).<BR>—2 Wandering.<BR>—3 Regret.<BR>—4 N. of a class of beings attending on Śiva; Skanda P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रमणम्
उद्भ्रमणम्<BR>—1 Moving or wandering about.<BR>—2 Rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रान्त|उद्भ्रांत|उद्भ्रान्तं
उद्भ्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Agitated, bewildered, distracted; विमूढसंज्ञो दुष्टाश्वैरुद्भ्रान्तैरिव<BR> सारथिः Mb. 3. 2. 66. ˚चेतनाम् R. 12. 74; gone mad; Mv. 4.<BR>—2 Terrified, frightened; मारीचोद्भ्रान्तहारीताः R. 4. 46; U. 6.<BR>—3 Whirled, flourished, waved (as a sword).<BR>—4 Come on by breaking (the earth); स तमभ्रमिवाविष्टमुद्भ्रान्तमिव<BR> मोदिनीम् Rām. 7. 31. 14.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">Page0431-2</a>]<BR>—5 Wandering upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रान्तम्
उद्भ्रान्त + .{@-न्तम्@}<BR>—1 Flourishing a sword.<BR>—2<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रान्तकम्
उद्भ्रान्त + .{@-न्तम्@} + ({@-˚न्तकम्@})<BR> Rising (in the air).<BR>—3 Excitement, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्मन्
उद्मन् <i>n.</i> Ved. Flooding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यन्धा
उद्यन्धा An ant infesting wild and dry wood. It is small, blackish<BR> and a sharp biter (Mar. तेलमुंगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम्
उद्यम् €1 Ā. (P. in some cases)<BR>—1 To raise, elevate, lift up; बाहू उद्यम्य<BR> Ś. 1; परस्य दण्डं नोद्यच्छेत् Ms. 4. 164, 8. 280; धनुरुद्यम्य<BR> पाण्डवः Bg. 1. 20; R. 15. 23, 11. 17; भारमुद्यच्छते Sk.; Bk. 4. 31, 17. 92.<BR>—2 To offer, give.<BR>—3 To prepare, become ready for, begin, set about (with dat., loc. or<BR> inf.); उद्यच्छमाना गमनाय पश्चात् R. 16. 29; Bk. 8. 47; see उद्यत.<BR>—4 To strive, be diligent, strive hard for; उद्यच्छति वेदम् Sk.<BR>—5 To reign, manage, govern.<BR>—6 To keep back, stop, hinder.<BR>—7 To rise. ━<i>Caus.</i> To prompt, stimulate; मधुमदोद्यमिता वनिता Ki. 9. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत|उद्यतं|उद्यतः
उद्यत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, lifted up; महद्भयं वज्रमुद्यतम् Kaṭh. 2. 6. 2; उद्यतेष्वपि<BR> शस्त्रेषु H. 3. 15; so ˚असिः, ˚पाणिः &c.<BR>—2 Persevering, diligent, active.<BR>—3 Bent, drawn (as a bow); न तेन सज्यं क्वचिदुद्यतं धनुः Ki. 1. 21.<BR>—4 Ready, prepared, on the point of, eager, bent or intent on, engaged<BR> in; with dat., loc., inf., or usually in comp.; अनर्थायोद्यता Rām.;<BR> उद्यतः स्वेषु कर्मसु R. 17. 61; हन्तुं स्वजनमुद्यताः Bg. 1. 45;<BR> पक्षच्छेदोद्यतं शक्रम् R. 4. 40; जय˚, वध˚ &c.<BR>—5 Trained, disciplined.<BR>—6 Commenced, begun; शक्या दैवगतिर्लोके निवर्तयितुमुद्यता Rām. 6. 110. 25.<BR>—7 Harsh, severe; अभिपन्नमिदं लोके राज्ञामुद्यतदण्डनम् Mb. 12. 32. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यतः|उद्यत|उद्यतं
उद्यत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Time (in music).<BR>—2 A section, chapter, or any such division of a book.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्यतायुध, उद्यतशस्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यतायुध
उद्यत + -आयुध, -शस्त्र <i>a.</i> Having an uplifted weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यतशस्त्र
उद्यत + -आयुध, -शस्त्र <i>a.</i> Having an uplifted weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत्|उद्यन्त्
उद्यत् <i>a.</i> Rising. ━<i>m.</i> A star.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्यत्पर्वतः, उद्यद्गिरिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत्पर्वतः|उद्यत्पर्वत
उद्यत् + -पर्वतः, -गिरिः The Eastern mountain (उदयगिरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यद्गिरिः|उद्यद्गिरि
उद्यत् + -पर्वतः, -गिरिः The Eastern mountain (उदयगिरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यतिः|उद्यति
उद्यतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Raising, elevation. उपस्तुतिं नमस उद्यतिं च Rv. 1. 190. 3.<BR>—2 Effort, exertion. अकल्प्स्यदुद्यतिः सर्वा हनूमानित्यचिन्तयत् Bk. 8. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यन्तृ|उद्यंतृ
उद्यन्तृ <i>a.</i> Raising, elevating; उद्यन्ता गिरो यदि च त्मना भूत् Rv. 1. 178. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमः|उद्यम
उद्यमः<BR>—1 Raising, elevation.<BR>—2 Strenuous or assiduous effort, exertion, diligence, perseverance; निशम्य<BR> चैनां तपसे कृतोद्यमाम् Ku. 5. 3; शशाक मेना न नियन्तुमुद्यमात् 5,<BR> firm resolve; उद्यमेन हि सिध्यन्ति कार्याणि न मनोरथैः Pt. 2. 135.<BR>—3 Readiness, preparation; गन्तुमुद्यमो विहितः became ready to go Pt. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्यमभङ्गः, उद्यमभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमभङ्गः|उद्यमभङ्ग|उद्यमभंग
उद्यमः + -भङ्गः discouragement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमभृत्
उद्यमः + -भृत् <i>a.</i> undergoing exertions, striving hard; सामान्यास्तु<BR> परार्थमुद्यमभृतः स्वार्थाविरोधेन ये Bh. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमनम्
उद्यमनम्<BR>—1 Raising, elevation; यत्समाने उद्यमने निपातये च Mbh. on P. I. 4. 23.<BR>—2 Effort, exertion; भुव्यन्नमम्भूद्यमने च वृत्तिम् Bhāg. 8. 6. 12.<BR>—3 Example, experiment; आवर्जयत वैदेहीं दण्डस्योद्यमनेन च Rām. 5. 22. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0431-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमित
उद्यमित^1 <i>a.</i> Instigated to action. आत्मनो मधुमदोद्यमितानाम् Ki. 9. 66.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमिन्
उद्यमिन् <i>a.</i> Diligent, persevering, active, making effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यामः|उद्याम
उद्यामः<BR>—1 Erecting, stretching out, elevation.<BR>—2 A rope, a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्या
उद्या €2 P.<BR>—1 To go up, rise, ascend; क्रमशस्ते पुनस्तस्य चापात्सममिवोद्ययुः<BR> R. 12. 47; पतत्युद्याति Gīt. 4.<BR>—2 To originate, spring, arise; इति मतिरुदयासीत् पक्षिणः प्रेक्ष्य भैमीम् N. 2. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानम्
उद्यानम् (-नः also)<BR>—1 Going or walking out. उद्यानं ते पुरुष नावयानम् Av. 8. 1. 6.<BR>—2 A garden, park, pleasure garden; वाह्योद्यानस्थितहरशिरश्चन्द्रिकाधौतहर्म्या<BR> Me. 7, 26, 35; oft. opp. to वन; cf. दूरीकृताः खलु गुणैरुद्यानलता<BR> वनलताभिः Ś. 1. 17.<BR>—3 Purpose, motive.<BR>—4 N. of a country to the North of India.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्यानपालः, उद्यानपालकः, उद्यानरक्षकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानः|उद्यान|उद्यानं
उद्यानम् (-नः also)<BR>—1 Going or walking out. उद्यानं ते पुरुष नावयानम् Av. 8. 1. 6.<BR>—2 A garden, park, pleasure garden; वाह्योद्यानस्थितहरशिरश्चन्द्रिकाधौतहर्म्या<BR> Me. 7, 26, 35; oft. opp. to वन; cf. दूरीकृताः खलु गुणैरुद्यानलता<BR> वनलताभिः Ś. 1. 17.<BR>—3 Purpose, motive.<BR>—4 N. of a country to the North of India.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उद्यानपालः, उद्यानपालकः, उद्यानरक्षकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

