उद्वासस्
उद्वास, -सस् <i>a.</i><BR> One who has put off oneʼs clothes. (said of a woman<BR> after her period of impurity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विज्
उद्विज् €6 Ā. (P. epic.)<BR>—1 To be grieved or afflicted, be agitated; नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम्<BR> Bg. 5. 20; tremble, shake (lit. and fig.).<BR>—2 To fear, be afraid of, shrink from, abhor (with abl.); तीक्ष्णादुद्विजते<BR> Mu. 3. 5; Bg. 12. 15; लोकापवादान्नोद्विग्नम् K. 197; नायमुद्विजितुं<BR> कालः स्वामिकार्यात् Bk. 7. 92.<BR>—3 To be tired or sick of, be disgusted with; जीवितादुद्विजमानेन<BR> Māl. 3; sometimes with gen. या ममोद्विजते नित्यं साद्य मामवगूहते Pt. 4. 76.<BR>—4 To grieve, afflict, frighten. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To trouble, harass, afflict, oppress; उद्वेजयत्यङ्गुलिपार्ष्णिभागान्<BR> Ku. 1. 11; उद्वेजिता वृष्टिभिः 5; म्लेच्छैरुद्वेज्यमाना Mu. 7. 19.<BR>—2 To terrify, frighten; उद्वेजिताः कूजितैः U. 2. 29.<BR>—3 To produce disgust or abhorrence; रमणीयाप्युद्वेजयति K. 12; सीधुपानोद्वेजितस्य M. 3; Ś. 2.<BR>—4 To revive a fainting person (by sprinkling water) Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्न|उद्विग्नः
उद्विग्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Grieved, afflicted, sorrowful, anxious (as for any absent lover);<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

