उद्वेजनम्
उद्वेजन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Agitation, anxiety.<BR>—2 Infliction of pain, torture, affliction; उद्वेजनकरैर्दण्डैश्चिह्नयित्वा<BR> प्रवासयेत् Ms. 8. 352 painful.<BR>—3 Regret, sorrow for oneʼs absence.<BR>—4 Shudder, shuddering; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजयितृ
उद्वेजयितृ <i>a.</i> Terrifying; अत्यर्थमुद्वेजयिता परेषाम् Śi. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विवर्हणम्
उद्विवर्हणम् Rescuing, lifting; plucking up; Bhāg. 3. 13. 43. रसां<BR> गताया भुव उद्विवर्हणम् (v. l. उद्विबर्हणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्ष्
उद्वीक्ष् [उद्-वि-ईक्ष्]<BR>—1 Ā. To look up, view, see, perceive; दृष्टिरधिकं सोत्कण्ठमुद्वीक्षते<BR> Amaru. 28; प्रियस्य पदवीमुद्वीक्ष्य 76 looking at (waiting for); R. 13. 68.<BR>—2 To examine, consider; आत्मनः शक्तिमुद्वीक्ष्य Pt. 1. 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्षणम्
उद्वीक्षणम्<BR>—1 Looking up or upwards.<BR>—2 Sight, an eye; seeing, looking at; सखीजनोद्वीक्षणकौमुदीमुखम् R. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीज्
उद्वीज् €10 P.<BR>—1 To fan.<BR>—2 To blow upon or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीजनम्
उद्वीजनम् Fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृंहणम्
उद्वृंहणम् Increase, growth; MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्
उद्वृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go upwards, ascend.<BR>—2 To fly asunder, burst out; उद्वर्तमानमूलबन्धनम् U. 4 the strings<BR> of which are giving way or being snapped.<BR>—3 To tumble over, fall down.<BR>—4 To go out, depart.<BR>—5 To rise, swell, increase.<BR>—6 To be puffed up with pride, be haughty. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To extirpate, eradicate, destroy; उद्वर्तितं रसान्तरेण लज्जालुत्वम् Mv. 2.<BR>—2 To throw up, elevate.<BR>—3 To turn round, roll (as eyes).<BR>—4 To anoint, smear.<BR>—5 To beat to pieces, split, burst; अपां फेनेन नमुचेः शिर इन्द्रोदवर्तयः Rv. 8. 14. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त|उद्वर्तः|उद्वर्त्त|उद्वर्त्तः
उद्वर्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Superfluous, redundant, plentiful.<BR>—2 Left over as a remainder, surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तः|उद्वर्त|उद्वर्त्त|उद्वर्त्तः
उद्वर्त + .{@-र्तः@}<BR>—1 A remainder, surplus.<BR>—2 Excess, preponderance.<BR>—3 Rubbing or smearing the body with perfumes.<BR>—4 The time of destruction of the world (प्रलयकाल); उद्वर्त इव<BR> सत्त्वानां समुद्राणामभूत्स्वनः Rām. 6. 44. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तक|उद्वर्तकः|उद्वर्त्तक
उद्वर्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing to rise.<BR>—2 Rubbing and cleaning the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तकः|उद्वर्तक|उद्वर्त्तक
उद्वर्तक + .{@-कः@} (In Math.) The quantity assumed for the purpose of the operation (Colebrooke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तनम्
उद्वर्तनम्<BR>—1 Going up, rising.<BR>—2 Springing up, growth (of plants, grain &c.)<BR>—3 Prosperity, elevation.<BR>—4 Turning from side to side; springing up, popping the head; चटुलशफरोद्वर्तनप्रेक्षितानि Me. 42.<BR>—5 Grinding, pounding.<BR>—6 Drawing out metal, wire-drawing.<BR>—7 Anointing, smearing; करोद्वर्तनार्थे चन्दनं समर्पयामि; cf.<BR> also सायणʼs commentary on the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa 12. 8. 3. 16.━ सर्वसुरभिचन्दनादि<BR> उन्मर्दनम् उद्वर्तनं यजमानस्य भवति ।<BR>—8 Particularly, rubbing and cleaning the body with perfumes or fragrant<BR> unguents, or the unguents used for this purpose or to relieve pain; नाक्रामेद्रक्तविण्मूत्रष्ठीवनोद्वर्तनादि<BR> च Y. 1. 152; Ms. 4. 132 (अभ्यङ्गमलापकर्षणपिष्टकादि Kull.).<BR> In this connection the meaning ‘vomiting’ seems appropriate, along with<BR> other filthy objects; cf. उद्वृत्त = vomited.<BR>—9 Bad behaviour or conduct, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तित|उद्वर्त्तित
उद्वर्तित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Risen, elevated.<BR>—2 Sprung up, drawn out.<BR>—3 Perfumed, scented, rubbed, kneaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्त|उद्वृत्तः
उद्वृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, elevated (स्तन, दन्त, मेघ &c.). गर्जन्तमुद्वृत्तशिताग्रदंष्ट्रम्<BR> Rām. 6. 59. 95.<BR>—2 Flowing out, not contained in, swollen, overflowing; हृदयभरितोद्वृत्तविस्मय<BR> Māl. 4; अपामुद्वृत्तानाम् Mu. 3. 8 overflowing; उद्वृतः क इव सुखावहः<BR> परेषाम् Śi. 8. 18. (where उ˚ means also ‘gone astray, ill-behaved’).<BR>—3 Grown, increased.<BR>—4 Exalted, prosperous.<BR>—5 Proud, furious, haughty; परिधत्त किमुद्वृत्ता राजद्रव्याण्यभीप्सथ<BR> Bhāg. 10. 41. 35. ˚मृगपति K. 90.<BR>—6 Vomited up.<BR>—7 Left as a remainder.<BR>—8 Ill-conducted, ill-mannered, rude.<BR>—9 Agitated;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-1" target="_blank">Page0435-1</a>]<BR> उद्वृत्तनक्रात् सहसोन्ममज्ज R. 16. 79.<BR>—10 Turned up, opened wide (as eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्तः|उद्वृत्त
उद्वृत्त + .{@-त्तः@} A particular position of the hands in dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्तम्
उद्वृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} (in astronomy) The east and west hour circle or six oʼclock line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृषभयज्ञः|उद्वृषभयज्ञ
उद्वृषभयज्ञः A religious act performed by the persons that hail<BR> from North India; ये उदीच्या इति समाख्यातास्ते उद्वृषभयज्ञादीन् (करिष्यन्ति)<BR> ŚB. on MS. 1. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृह्
उद्वृह् €6 P.<BR>—1 raise up, elevate.<BR>—2 To draw up, eradicate, uproot. उद्वृह रक्षः सहमूलमिन्द्र Rv. 3. 30. 17.<BR>—3 To draw out (a sword from the scabbard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्हित|उद्वर्हितः
