उन्दरुः, उन्दुरः, उन्दुरुः, उन्दूरुः [उन्द्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्दरुकर्णी, उन्दरुकर्णिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दूरुः|उन्दूरु|उंदूरुः
उन्दरुः, उन्दुरः, उन्दुरुः, उन्दूरुः [उन्द्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्दरुकर्णी, उन्दरुकर्णिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दरुकर्णी
उन्दरुः + -कर्णी, -कर्णिका the plant Salvinia Cuccullata. (Mar. उन्दीरकानी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दरुकर्णिका
उन्दरुः + -कर्णी, -कर्णिका the plant Salvinia Cuccullata. (Mar. उन्दीरकानी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्
उन्नद् €1 P. To roar or bellow aloud, sound, roar (in general); असोढसिंहध्वनिरुन्ननाद<BR> Ku. 1. 56; कालमेघ इवोन्नदन् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नादः|उन्नाद
उन्नादः<BR>—1 Crying out, roar, humming, chirping &c.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्
उन्नम् €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To rise, appear; उन्नम्योन्नम्य लीयन्ते दरिद्राणां मनोरथाः Pt. 2. 95.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To hang over, arise, impend; उन्नमत्यकालदुर्दिनम् Mk. 4, 5<BR> an untimely storm impends; बहलोन्नमदम्बुधराः Māl. 9. 18.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To rise, ascend, go up (fig. also); उन्नमति नमति वर्षति<BR> गर्जति मेघः Mk. 5. नम्रत्वेनोन्नमन्तः Bh. 2. 69.<BR>—2 To bend up, raise, elevate, erect; द्यौरुन्ननामेव दिशः प्रसेदुः<BR> Ki. 16. 35. ━<i>Caus.</i> (नमयति)<BR>—1 To bend upwards, raise, erect; मुखमुन्नमय्य Ku. 7. 23; Ś. 3. 25; R. 1. 41.<BR>—2 (fig.) To elevate, raise to eminence; उन्नमय बन्धुवर्गम् K. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नत|उन्नतः
उन्नत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, elevated, uplifted (fig. also); त्रिरुन्नतं स्थाप्य समं<BR> शरीरम् Śvet. Up. 2. 8; उपासितगुरुप्रज्ञाभिमानोन्नताः Bh. 3. 24;<BR> Śi. 9. 79; नतोन्नतभूमिभागे Ś. 4. 15.<BR>—2 High (fig. also), tall, lofty; great, eminent; स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वी<BR> कान्त्वा मेरुरिवात्मना R. 1. 14; V. 5. 22; Ki. 5. 15, 14. 23; Pt. 1. 29;<BR> ˚इच्छः R. 6. 71; Śi. 7. 27; ˚चेतस् <i>a.</i> noble-minded; Pt. 1. 122.<BR>—3 Projecting, plump, full (as breasts); निबिडोन्नतस्तनम् M. 2. 3; Ṛs. 1. 7.<BR>—4 Pleased, in high spirit; समाधाय समृद्धार्थाः कर्मसिद्धिभिरुन्नताः<BR> Rām. 5. 61. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतः|उन्नत
उन्नत + .{@-तः@} A boa (अजगर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतम्
उन्नत + .{@-तम्@} —1 Elevation. —2 Ascension, altitude.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्नतानत, उन्नतकालः, उन्नतकोकिला, उन्नतचरण, उन्नतनाभि, उन्नतशिरस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतानत|उन्नतानतं
उन्नत + -आनत <i>a.</i> elevated and depressed, uneven, high and low; बन्धुरं<BR> तून्नतानतम् Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतकालः|उन्नतकाल
उन्नत + -कालः A method of determining the time from the shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतकोकिला
उन्नत + -कोकिला A kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतचरण
उन्नत + -चरण <i>a.</i> with uplifted paws, rampant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतनाभि|उन्नतनाभिः
उन्नत + -नाभि <i>a.</i> having a projecting navel, <i>i. e.</i> corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतशिरस्
उन्नत + -शिरस् <i>a.</i> carrying the head high, holding up the head, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतत्वम्
उन्नतत्वम् Height, sublimity, majesty; तदेव नैसर्गिकमुन्नतत्वम् R. 5. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतिः|उन्नति
उन्नतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Elevation, height (fig. also); see उन्नतिमत् below.<BR>—2 Exaltation, dignity, rise, prosperity, increase; स्तोकेनोन्नतिमायाति<BR> स्तोकेनायात्यधोगतिम् Pt. 1. 150; ध्वजानामुन्नतिः K. 55; Śi. 16. 22, 72;<BR> Bv. 1. 40; महाजनस्य संपर्कः कस्य नोन्नतिकारकः H. 3.<BR> v. l.; मान˚ Bh. 2. 23.<BR>—3 Raising.<BR>—4 The wife of Garuḍa.<BR>—5 N. of a daughter of दक्ष and wife of धर्म.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्नतीशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतीशः|उन्नतीश
उन्नतिः + -ईशः N. of Garuḍa (Lord of उन्नति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतिमत्|उन्नतिमन्त्
उन्नतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Elevated, projecting, plump (as breasts); सा पीनोन्नतिमत्पयोधरयुगं<BR> धत्ते Amaru. 34; Śi. 9. 72.<BR>—2 High, sublime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमनम्
उन्नमनम्<BR>—1 Raising, lifting up.<BR>—2 Height, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमित|उन्नमितः
उन्नमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Raised, lifted up. प्रयत्नोन्नमिता नमत्फणैः K.<BR>—2 Heightened, increased, proved to be superior; ˚उपदेशः M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्र
उन्नम्र <i>a.</i> Erect, upright, lofty, high (fig. also); उन्नम्रताम्रपटमण्डपमण्डितं<BR> तत् Śi. 5. 68; ˚ता erectness, uprightness (of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नामः|उन्नाम
उन्नामः Raising, lifting up; शतबुद्धिः कृतोन्नामः Pt. 5. 45 lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्नय, -यनम्<BR> See under उन्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयनम्
उन्नय, -यनम्<BR> See under उन्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नस
उन्नस <i>a.</i> [उन्नता नासिका यस्य] P. V. 4. 119 Having a prominent<BR> nose; सुकपोलोन्नसाननम् Bhāg. 8. 8. 42. उन्नसं दधती वक्त्रम् Bk. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नह्
उन्नह् €4 P.<BR>—1 To tie up, bind up, fasten round.<BR>—2 To draw out, pull out.<BR>—3 To come out of, rise from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्ध
उन्नद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Tied or bound up, fastened; तेऽस्य मुक्तागुणोन्नद्धं मौलिमन्तर्गतस्रजम्<BR> R. 17. 23, 18. 50; Ku. 3. 46.<BR>—2 Swelled, increased, heaving; श्वासोन्नद्धपयोधर Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 Unbound.<BR>—4 Elated, flushed with; वीर्य˚, मद˚, बल˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नहन
उन्नहन Unfettered, unbound; नैवान्यतः परिभवोऽस्य भवेत्कथं<BR> चिन्मत्संश्रयस्य विभवोन्नहनस्य नित्यम् Bhāg. 11. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाहः|उन्नाह|उन्नाहं
उन्नाहः<BR>—1 Projection, protuberance; स्तन˚ Māl. 9; rise; बलाहक˚ K. 26.<BR>—2 Tying up.<BR>—3 Excess, abundance^1; नरकस्तमौन्नाहो Bhāg. 11. 19. 43.<BR>—4 Impudence, haughtiness; N.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाहम्
उन्नाहः + .{@-हम्@} Sour gruel made from the fermentation of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाभ|उन्नाभः
उन्नाभ <i>a.</i> —1 Having a projecting navel, corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाभः|उन्नाभ
उन्नाभ + .{@-भः@} N. of a king of the Solar race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाल
उन्नाल <i>a.</i> With the stalk prominently appearing; Māl. 9. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्र|उन्निद्रः
उन्निद्र <i>a.</i> [उद्गता निद्रा यस्य]<BR>—1 Sleepless, awake, without one wink of sleep; तामुन्निद्रामवनिशयनां<BR> सौधवातायनस्थः Me. 90; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 5;<BR> Mu. 4. 2; Māl. 3.<BR>—2 Expanded, full-blown, budded (as lotuses); ˚अरविन्दम् K. 22; उन्निद्रपुष्पाक्षिसहस्रभाजा<BR> Śi. 4. 13, 31, 8. 28.<BR>—3 Shining (as the moon).<BR>—4 Bristling (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्रकम्
उन्निद्रकम्, उन्निद्रता <i>f.</i> Sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्रता
उन्निद्रकम्, उन्निद्रता <i>f.</i> Sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नी
उन्नी €1 P.<BR>—1 To lead upwards, bring up; ऊर्ध्वं प्राणमुन्नयति Kaṭh. 2. 5. 3;<BR> ब्रह्मादित्य मुन्नयति Mb. 3. 313. 46.<BR>—2 To raise, erect, lift up; (Ā.) दण्डमुन्नयते Sk.; स्वदंष्ट्रोन्नीतधरो<BR> वराहः Bhāg.<BR>—3 To bring out of, free from, help, rescue, redeem; रसाया लीलयोन्नीताम् उर्वीम् Bhāg.<BR>—4 To draw up (as water); वने निपूतं वन उन्नयध्वम् Rv. 2. 14. 9.<BR>—5 To stroke; straighten out.<BR>—6 To lead<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">Page0436-2</a>]<BR> out or aside, lead away; एकान्तमुन्नीय Mb.<BR>—7 To press out, extract.<BR>—8 To infer, ascertain, guess, conjecture; कथमपि स इत्युन्नेतव्यस्तथापि<BR> दृशोः प्रियः U. 3. 22, 1. 29, 6. 26; V. 4; प्रकृतिप्रत्ययाद्यर्थैः<BR> संकीर्णे लिङ्गमुन्नयेत् Ak.<BR>—9 To fill completely.<BR>—10 To lead off (in singing), काचित्समं मुकुन्देन स्वरजातीरमिश्रिताः ।<BR> उन्निन्ये पूजिता तेन प्रीयतां साधुसाध्विति ॥ Bhāg. 10. 33. 10.<BR>—11 To lead aside, separate; दैवेनैकत्र नीतानामुन्नीतानां स्वकर्मभिः<BR> Bhāg. 7. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयः|उन्नय
उन्नयः, उन्नायः P. III. 3. 26. अवोदोर्नियः<BR>—1 Raising, elevating.<BR>—2 Height, elevation.<BR>—3 Analogy, resemblance.<BR>—4 Inference, induction, conclusion.<BR>—5 A heap. उन्नायानधिगच्छन्तः प्रद्रावैर्वसुधाभृताम् Bk. 7. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायः|उन्नाय
उन्नयः, उन्नायः P. III. 3. 26. अवोदोर्नियः<BR>—1 Raising, elevating.<BR>—2 Height, elevation.<BR>—3 Analogy, resemblance.<BR>—4 Inference, induction, conclusion.<BR>—5 A heap. उन्नायानधिगच्छन्तः प्रद्रावैर्वसुधाभृताम् Bk. 7. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयन|उन्नयनं
उन्नयन <i>a.</i> With the eyes raised upwards; पुरुहूतध्वजस्येव<BR> तस्योन्नयनपङ्क्तयः R. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयनम्
उन्नयन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Raising, elevating, lifting up.<BR>—2 Drawing up water.<BR>—3 The vessel out of which a fluid is taken.<BR>—4 Leading away, extracting.<BR>—5 Making straight, smoothing; सीमन्त˚.<BR>—6 Deliberation, discussion.<BR>—7 Inference; श्रवणादनु पश्चादीक्षा अन्वीक्षा उन्नयनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायक
उन्नायक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Raising, lifting up.<BR>—2 What leads to an inference or conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेतृ
उन्नेतृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Raising, leading up.<BR>—2 Leading to an inference. ━<i>m.</i> One of the 16 priests at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेत्रम्
उन्नेत्रम् The office of the उन्नेतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेय
उन्नेय <i>a.</i> To be inferred or ascertained by analogy; Śivamahimna 17;<BR> परेषामुन्नेयो भवति U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्ज्
उन्मज्ज् (मस्ज्) €6 P. To emerge, rise up; वन्यः सरित्तो गज<BR> उन्ममज्ज R. 5. 43, 16. 79; उन्ममज्ज शनकैस्तुहिनांशुः Ki. 9. 23;<BR> Ś. 7. 8; Śi. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मस्ज्
उन्मज्ज् (मस्ज्) €6 P. To emerge, rise up; वन्यः सरित्तो गज<BR> उन्ममज्ज R. 5. 43, 16. 79; उन्ममज्ज शनकैस्तुहिनांशुः Ki. 9. 23;<BR> Ś. 7. 8; Śi. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जक|उन्मज्जकः
उन्मज्जक <i>a.</i> Emerging, rising up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जकः|उन्मज्जक
उन्मज्जक + .{@-कः@} A kind of ascetic; कण्ठदघ्ने जले स्थित्वा तपः कुर्वन्<BR> प्रवर्तते । उन्मज्जकः स विज्ञेयस्तापसो लोकपूजितः ॥; दन्तोलूखलिनश्चैव<BR> तथैवोन्मज्जकाः परे Rām. 3. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जनम्
उन्मज्जनम् Emerging, coming out of water. सलिलोन्मज्जनमुज्झति स्फुटम् N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जनः|उन्मज्जन|उन्मज्जनं
उन्मज्जनम् + .{@-नः@} An attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मणिः|उन्मणि
उन्मणिः <i>m.</i> A gem lying on the surface; अकृष्टपच्यौषधयो गिरयो<BR> बिभ्रदुन्मणीन् Bhāg. 10. 27. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मण्डलम्
उन्मण्डलम् An imaginery circle going from South to North and meant<BR> for measuring the day; the east and west circle; Sūrya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथ्
उन्मथ्, उन्मन्थ् €1. €9. P.<BR>—1 To shake up, disturb, excite, stir; pain.<BR>—2 To strike, kill, destroy; मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं<BR> जैमिनिम् Pt. 2. 34; धैर्यमुन्मथ्य Māl. 1. 18; विकल्पनिद्रामुन्मथ्य Prab.<BR>—3 To tear, cut off, peel off; वन्यद्विपेनोन्मथिता त्वगस्य R. 2. 37.<BR>—4 To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थ्
उन्मथ्, उन्मन्थ् €1. €9. P.<BR>—1 To shake up, disturb, excite, stir; pain.<BR>—2 To strike, kill, destroy; मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं<BR> जैमिनिम् Pt. 2. 34; धैर्यमुन्मथ्य Māl. 1. 18; विकल्पनिद्रामुन्मथ्य Prab.<BR>—3 To tear, cut off, peel off; वन्यद्विपेनोन्मथिता त्वगस्य R. 2. 37.<BR>—4 To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथन
उन्मथन <i>a.</i> Tearing, disturbing, paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथनम्
उन्मथन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Shaking off, throwing off or down.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter; अन्योन्यसूतोन्मथनात् R. 7. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थः|उन्मन्थ|उन्मंथ|उन्मंथः
उन्मन्थः<BR>—1 Agitation, disturbance.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—3 A disease of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थक|उन्मंथक|उन्मन्थकः
उन्मन्थक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shaking off, agitating, stirring.<BR>—2 Throbbing, beating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थकः|उन्मन्थक|उन्मंथक
उन्मन्थक + .{@-कः@} Inflammation of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थनम्
उन्मन्थनम्<BR>—1 Shaking off, agitating.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter; अन्योन्यसूतोन्मथनादभूताम् R. 7. 52; hurting;<BR> मारीचदर्शनं चैव सीतोन्मथनमेव च Rām. 6. 124. 11.<BR>—3 Beating (with a stick).<BR>—4 Probing, stirring a dart lodged in the body.<BR>—5 The instrument used for this purpose.<BR>—6 Churning up; कौर्मे धृतोऽद्रिरमृतोन्मथने स्वपृष्ठे Bhāg. 11. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथ|उन्माथः
उन्माथ <i>a.</i> Destroying or Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथः|उन्माथ
उन्माथ + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 Torment, pang, deep pain; ˚वेगाः Māl. 9. 45.<BR>—2 Shaking, agitation.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—4 A snare or trap; प्रयोजयति चोन्माथं नित्यमस्तं गते रवौ Mb. 12. 138. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथिन्
उन्माथिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shaking, agitating.<BR>—2 Tormenting. excruciating; चिरमविरतोन्माथी (उनङ्गमहाज्वरः) Māl. 9. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद्
उन्मद् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be or become mad.<BR>—2 To delight, gratify. ━<i>Caus.</i> (˚न्म-न्मा-दयति)<BR>—1 To madden, inebriate, render drunk (lit. and fig.); लक्ष्म्योन्मादिताः<BR> K. 107; Ki. 4. 16.<BR>—2 To excite, agitate; उन्मादयत मरुत उदन्तरिक्ष मादय Av. 6. 130. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्मत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 drunk, intoxicated.<BR>—2 Insane, frantic, mad; द्वावत्रोन्मत्तौ V. 2; अहो उन्मत्तास्मि संवृत्ता<BR> U. 3, 5. 30; Ś. 6; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Puffed, elevated.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Furious, wild; मदोन्मत्तस्य भूपस्य कुञ्जरस्य च गच्छतः<BR> Pt. 1. 161; U. 2; Śi. 6. 31.<BR>—4 Possessed by a ghost or an evil-spirit; Y. 2. 32; Ms. 3. 161 (वातपित्तश्लेष्मसंनिपातग्रहसंभवेनोपसृष्टः Mit.).<BR>—5 Very great, abnormal. उन्मत्तवेगाः प्लवगा मधुमत्ताश्च हृष्टवत्<BR> Rām. 5. 62. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तः|उन्मत्त
उन्मत्त + .{@-त्तः@}<BR>—1 the thorn apple (धत्तूर); N. of another tree (मुचकुन्द).<BR>—2 N. of one of the eight forms of Bhairava.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्मत्तकीर्तिः, उन्मत्तवेशः, उन्मत्तगङ्गम्, उन्मत्तदर्शन, उन्मत्तरूप, उन्मत्तप्रलपित, उन्मत्तभैरवः, उन्मत्तलिङ्गिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तकीर्तिः|उन्मत्तकीर्ति
उन्मत्त + -कीर्तिः, -वेशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तवेशः|उन्मत्तवेश
उन्मत्त + -कीर्तिः, -वेशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तगङ्गम्
उन्मत्त + -गङ्गम् N. of a country (where the Gaṅgā roars furiously along).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तदर्शन
उन्मत्त + -दर्शन, -रूप <i>a.</i> maniac-like, mad in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तरूप
उन्मत्त + -दर्शन, -रूप <i>a.</i> maniac-like, mad in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तप्रलपित
उन्मत्त + -प्रलपित <i>a.</i> spoken in drunkenness or madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तप्रलपितम्
उन्मत्त + -प्रलपित + .({@-तम्@}) the words of a madman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तभैरवः|उन्मत्तभैरव
उन्मत्त + -भैरवः A form of Bhairava. ˚वी A form of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तलिङ्गिन्
उन्मत्त + -लिङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> pretending to be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तक
उन्मत्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Insane, mad.<BR>—2 Drunk, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद|उन्मदः
उन्मद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intoxicated, drunk; उदीरयामासुरिवोन्मदानाम् R. 2. 9, 16. 54.<BR>—2 Mad, furious, extravagant; Śi. 10. 4; उन्मदसारसारवः 12. 44, 77, 16. 59.<BR>—3 Causing intoxication, intoxicating; मधुकराङ्गनया मुहुरुन्मदध्वनिभृता<BR> निभृताक्षरमुज्जगे Śi. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदः|उन्मद
उन्मद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Insanity.<BR>—2 Intoxication, ecstacy; कृतमनुकृतवत्य उन्मदान्धाः प्रकृतिमगन्किल<BR> यस्य गोपवध्वः Bhāg. 1. 9. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदन
उन्मदन <i>a.</i> [उद्भूतो-मदनोऽस्य] Affected or inflamed with<BR> love; तदाप्रभृत्युन्मदना बभूव Ku. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदिष्णु|उन्मदिष्णुः
उन्मदिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mad, insane.<BR>—2 Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>—3 In rut (as an elephant); व्यालद्विपा यन्तृभिरुन्मदिष्णवः कथंचिदारादपथेन<BR> निन्यिरे Śi. 12. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माद|उन्मादः
उन्माद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mad, insane.<BR>—2 Extravagant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादः|उन्माद
उन्माद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Madness, insanity; अहो उन्मादः U. 3; Māl. 9.<BR>—2 Intense passion, intoxication or extravagance of love; Māl. 3, 2. 11;<BR> वीररभसोन्मादः Mv. 2. 22 rapturous joy.<BR>—3 Lunacy, mania (considered as a disease of the mind); मदयन्त्युद्धता<BR> दोषा यस्मादुन्मार्गमाश्रिताः । मानसोऽयमतो व्याधिरुन्माद इति कीर्तितः ॥ Suśr.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.) Madness considered as one of the 33 subordinate feelings;<BR> चित्तसंमोह उन्मादः कामशोकभयादिभिः S. D. 3; or according to R. G.<BR> विप्रलम्भमहापत्तिपरमानन्दादिजन्माऽन्यस्मिन्नन्यावभास उन्मादः.<BR>—5 Bloom; उन्मादं वीक्ष्य पद्मानाम् S. D. 2.<BR>—6 A kind of पिशाच; Bhāg. 2. 10. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादकः|उन्मादक
उन्मादकः N. of the plant धत्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादन|उन्मादनः
उन्मादन <i>a.</i> Maddening, exciting, intoxicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादनः|उन्मादन
उन्मादन + .{@-नः@} One of the five arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादयितृक
उन्मादयितृक <i>a.</i> Intoxicating, enrapturing; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादिन्
उन्मादिन् <i>a.</i> Mad, intoxicated. उन्मादिनो मातुलपुत्रकस्य कथं<BR> सहामो वनकण्टकित्वम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादुक
उन्मादुक <i>a.</i> Fond of drinking (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उन्मनस्, -नस्क <i>a.</i><BR> [उद्भ्रान्तं मनोऽस्य]<BR>—1 Excited or disturbed in mind, perplexed, agitated, uneasy; उन्मनाः<BR> प्रथमजन्मचेष्टितान्यस्मरन्नपि बभूव राघवः R. 11. 22; Ki. 14. 45.<BR>—2 Regretting, repining for a lost or departed friend.<BR>—3 Anxious, eager, impatient; गन्तुं पावकमुन्मनस्तदभवत् Bh. 2. 75.<BR>—4 Proud (मनस्विन्); मुदमायातु नितान्तमुन्मनाः Śi. 16. 3 (where<BR> it also means “anxious”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्क
उन्मनस्, -नस्क <i>a.</i><BR> [उद्भ्रान्तं मनोऽस्य]<BR>—1 Excited or disturbed in mind, perplexed, agitated, uneasy; उन्मनाः<BR> प्रथमजन्मचेष्टितान्यस्मरन्नपि बभूव राघवः R. 11. 22; Ki. 14. 45.<BR>—2 Regretting, repining for a lost or departed friend.<BR>—3 Anxious, eager, impatient; गन्तुं पावकमुन्मनस्तदभवत् Bh. 2. 75.<BR>—4 Proud (मनस्विन्); मुदमायातु नितान्तमुन्मनाः Śi. 16. 3 (where<BR> it also means “anxious”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनायते
उन्मनायते Den. Ā., उन्मनीभू €1 P. To become excited or disturbed<BR> in mind, be uneasy, regret; अस्मद्विना मा भृशमुन्मनीभूः Ki. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनी
उन्मनी अस्<BR>—1 To become perplexed, excited.<BR>—2 To become absent-minded; Kāśi. on P. V. 4. 51.<BR>—3 To be one with god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीअस्
उन्मनी अस्<BR>—1 To become perplexed, excited.<BR>—2 To become absent-minded; Kāśi. on P. V. 4. 51.<BR>—3 To be one with god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीकृ
उन्मनीकृ €8 U. To make excited, disturb; तमृतुगणः क्षणमुन्मनीचकार Ki. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीभू
उन्मनीभू To be excited, disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीभावः|उन्मनीभाव
उन्मनीभावः Absence of mind; यद्वा यात्युन्मनीभावम् Brahmabindu. Up. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मयूख
उन्मयूख <i>a.</i> Shining, radiant; प्राप्येन्द्रनीलं किमुतोन्मयूखम् R. 16. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मर्दनम्
उन्मर्दनम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, kneading.<BR>—2 A fragrant essence used for the purpose of rubbing.<BR>—3 Act of purifying air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मा
उन्मा Ved. A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मानम्
उन्मानम्<BR>—1 Weighing, measuring upwards; ऊर्ध्वमानं किलोन्मानम्; Mbh. V. 1. 19. Vārt.<BR>—2 A measure of size or quantity.<BR>—3 Price.<BR>—4 Measurement of thickness or diameter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मित
उन्मित <i>a.</i> Measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मितिः|उन्मिति
उन्मितिः <i>f.</i> Measure; price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेय
उन्मेय <i>a.</i> To be weighed; what is weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेयम्
उन्मेय + .{@-यम्@} Weight, burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्ग|उन्मार्गः
उन्मार्ग <i>a.</i> [उत्कान्तः मार्गात्] Going to a wrong path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गः|उन्मार्ग
उन्मार्ग + .{@-र्गः@}<BR>—1 A wrong road, deviation from the right road (fig. also); नित्यमुन्मार्गगामिनाम् Pt. 1.<BR>—2 An improper conduct, evil course, moral turpitude; उन्मार्गप्रस्थितानि<BR> इन्द्रियाणि K. 155; ˚प्रवर्तकः 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गम्
उन्मार्ग + .{@-र्गम्@} <i>ind.</i> Astray, by a wrong way; उन्मार्गं गच्छतः मदोन्मत्तस्य<BR> भूपस्य Pt. 1. 161.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्मार्गगत, उन्मार्गगमनम्, उन्मार्गगामिन्, उन्मार्गवर्तिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगत
उन्मार्ग + -गत <i>a.</i> going wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगमनम्
उन्मार्ग + -गमनम् following evil courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगामिन्
उन्मार्ग + -गामिन्, -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> going wrong, erring, taking a wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गवर्तिन्
उन्मार्ग + -गामिन्, -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> going wrong, erring, taking a wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गिन्
उन्मार्गिन् <i>a.</i> Going astray; finding an outlet (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मालकम्
उन्मालकम् The offer of a gift as a mark of complete gratification.<BR> शरीरम् उन्मालकायेव निजं मुमोच; Śrīkaṇṭhacharitam 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिश्र
उन्मिश्र <i>a.</i> Mixed with, variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिष्
उन्मिष् €6 P.<BR>—1 To open the eyes; उन्मिमेष तदा मुनिः Bhāg.; Bg. 5. 9; Dk. 111.<BR>—2 To open (as the eyes); प्रलयान्तोन्मिषिते विलोचने Ku. 4. 2.<BR>—3 To open, bloom, be expanded (as lotuses); उन्मिषदुत्पलवन K. 22.<BR>—4 To rise, peep up (as stars); उन्मिषत्सु ग्रहग्रामणीषु K. 176.<BR>—5 To shine, glitter, flash; as तेजस्<BR>—6 To arise, originate; उन्मिषद्रोमहर्ष, उन्मिषत्तोषम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिष|उन्मिषः
उन्मिष <i>a.</i> Blown, opened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषः|उन्मिष
उन्मिष + .{@-षः@} Opening of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषित|उन्मिषितः
उन्मिषित <i>p. p.</i> Opened (as eyes), blown, expanded &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषितम्
उन्मिषित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A look, glance; व्यलोकयन्नुन्मिषितैस्तडिन्मयैः Ku. 5. 25; K. 72.<BR>—2 Opening; तद्वल्गुना युगपदुन्मिषितेन तावत् R. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषः|उन्मेष|उन्मेषं
उन्मेषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Opening (of the eyes), winking, twinkling (of the eyes); प्रत्यग्रोन्मेषजिह्मा Mu. 3. 21.<BR>—2 Blowing, opening, expansion; उन्मेषं यो मम न सहते जातिवैरी निशायाम्<BR> K. P. 10; दीर्घिकाकमलोन्मेषः Ku. 2. 33.<BR>—3 Light, flash, brilliancy; सतां प्रज्ञोन्मेषः Bh. 2. 114 light or<BR> flash; विद्युदुन्मेषदृष्टिम् Me. 83.<BR>—4 Awakening, rising, becoming visible, manifestation; ज्ञान˚ Śānti. 3. 13.<BR>—5 The act of increasing, supporting, making strong; addition, expansion;<BR> इतिहासपुराणानामुन्मेषं निर्मितं च यत् Mb. 1. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषणम्
उन्मेषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Opening (of the eyes), winking, twinkling (of the eyes); प्रत्यग्रोन्मेषजिह्मा Mu. 3. 21.<BR>—2 Blowing, opening, expansion; उन्मेषं यो मम न सहते जातिवैरी निशायाम्<BR> K. P. 10; दीर्घिकाकमलोन्मेषः Ku. 2. 33.<BR>—3 Light, flash, brilliancy; सतां प्रज्ञोन्मेषः Bh. 2. 114 light or<BR> flash; विद्युदुन्मेषदृष्टिम् Me. 83.<BR>—4 Awakening, rising, becoming visible, manifestation; ज्ञान˚ Śānti. 3. 13.<BR>—5 The act of increasing, supporting, making strong; addition, expansion;<BR> इतिहासपुराणानामुन्मेषं निर्मितं च यत् Mb. 1. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषिन्
उन्मेषिन् <i>a.</i> Flying about, glittering about; उन्मेषिचाषच्छदः Māl. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मील्
उन्मील् €1 P.<BR>—1 To open (as the eyes); उदमीलीच्च लोचने Bk. 15. 102, 16. 8.<BR>—2 To be awakened or roused, be excited; उन्मिमील विशदं विषमेषुः<BR> Śi. 10. 72; Bk. 1. 33.<BR>—3 To expand, blow (as lotuses); सरोभिरुन्मीलितपद्मलोचनैः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">Page0438-2</a>]<BR> Ki. 4. 3; Māl. 1. 38, 9. 15.<BR>—4 To be diffused or spread, cluster round; प्रान्तीन्मीलन्मनोहरकुन्तलैः U. 1. 20; उन्मीलन्मधुगन्ध Gīt. 1.<BR>—5 To appear, become manifest; खं वायुर्ज्वलनो जलं क्षितिरिति त्रैलोक्यमुन्मीलति Prab. 1. 2.<BR>—6 To break forth, burst out; U. 4.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To open (eyes, lotuses &c.); तदेतदुन्मीलय चक्षुरायतम् V. 1. 6; Mk. 1. 33.<BR>—2 To display, show; त्वयाद्य साधुतोन्मीलिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलः|उन्मील
उन्मीलः, -लनम्<BR>—1 Opening (of the eyes), awaking; ज्ञानाञ्जनशलाकाभिर्नेत्रोन्मीलनकारकः Mb.<BR>—2 Unfolding, opening (in general); प्रियागुणसहस्राणामेकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>—3 Touching up, painting; आलेख्य˚ K. 267.<BR>—4 Expanding, blowing.<BR>—5 Action, working; परं निर्वेदमागम्य न हि नोन्मीलनं क्षमम् Rām. 4. 49. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलनम्
उन्मीलः, -लनम्<BR>—1 Opening (of the eyes), awaking; ज्ञानाञ्जनशलाकाभिर्नेत्रोन्मीलनकारकः Mb.<BR>—2 Unfolding, opening (in general); प्रियागुणसहस्राणामेकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>—3 Touching up, painting; आलेख्य˚ K. 267.<BR>—4 Expanding, blowing.<BR>—5 Action, working; परं निर्वेदमागम्य न हि नोन्मीलनं क्षमम् Rām. 4. 49. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलित|उन्मीलितः
उन्मीलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Opened; अज्ञानतिमिरान्धस्य ज्ञानाञ्जनशलाकया । चक्षुरुन्मीलितं<BR> येन तस्मै पाणिनये नमः ॥ Śik. 58; Ki. 16. 12.<BR>—2 Blown, expanded; ते चोन्मीलितमालतीसुरभयः प्रौढाः कदम्बानिलाः;<BR> K. P. 1; awakened; झटित्युन्मीलितप्रज्ञम् Mv. 1. 48; K. 110.<BR>—3 Touched up, painted; उन्मीलितं तूलिकयेव चित्रम् Ku. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलितम्
उन्मीलित + .{@-तम्@} (In Rhet.) An open reference (to anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुख|उन्मुखः
उन्मुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [उद्-ऊर्ध्वं मुखं यस्य]<BR>—1 Raising the face, looking up; ˚दर्शन looking upwards; अद्रेः<BR> शृङ्गं हरति पवनः किंस्विदित्युन्मुखीभिः Me. 14, 105; R. 1. 39, 11. 26;<BR> आश्रम˚ 1. 53.<BR>—2 Ready, intent on, on the point of, about to, prepared for; तमरण्यसमाश्रयोन्मुखम्<BR> R. 8. 12 about to retire to the woods; 16. 9, 9. 3; उदयोन्मुखचन्द्रिका<BR> M. 5. 7; भेदोन्मुखम् V. 2. 7; Ku. 6. 48.<BR>—3 Eager, waiting for, expecting, looking up to; तस्मिन् संयमिनामाद्ये<BR> जाते परिणयोन्मुखे Ku. 6. 34; लक्ष्मीरिव गुणोन्मुखी R. 12. 26, 6. 21, 11. 23.<BR>—4 Sounding, speaking or making a sound; परभृतोन्मुखी Ku. 6. 2 speaking<BR> through the cuckoo.<BR>—5 Coming from the mouth (मुखोत्पन्न); यस्तून्मुखत्वाद्वर्णानां मुख्योऽभूद्<BR> ब्राह्मणो गुरुः Bhāg. 3. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुखता
उन्मुखता<BR>—1 The state of having the face raised.<BR>—2 The state of expectancy; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुखर
उन्मुखर <i>a.</i> Loud-sounding, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुच्
उन्मुच् €6 U.<BR>—1 To unfasten, pull off; उन्मुच्य सूत्रेण विनैव हाराः R. 6. 28; take<BR> off (clothes &c.); आत्मकण्ठादुन्मुच्य K. 147, 67; Bk. 3. 22.<BR>—2 To loosen, liberate, free from (as a bond); ऋणमुन्मुच्य देवानाम्<BR> Mb.; open (as a letter); लेखमुन्मुच्य Rāj. T. 3. 235; K. 221.<BR>—3 To raise, elevate, send forth (as sound); आर्तनादो हि यः पौरैरुन्मुक्तः Rām.<BR>—4 To fling, hurl (as a missile). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To extricate, loosen, free; उन्मोच्य सोऽपि निपुणः Mv. 6. 46.<BR>—2 To deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुक्त
उन्मुक्त <i>p. p.</i> Pulled off, loosened &c.; ˚कण्ठम् bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मोचनम्
उन्मोचनम् Unfastening, loosening.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उन्मोचनप्रमोचनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मोचनप्रमोचनम्
उन्मोचनम् + -प्रमोचनम् (du.) unfastening completely; उन्मोचनप्रमोचने<BR> उभे वाचा वदामि ते Av. 5. 30. 2-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुद्र|उन्मुद्रः
उन्मुद्र <i>a.</i> [उद्गता मुद्रा यस्मात्]<BR>—1 Unsealed.<BR>—2 Opened, blown, expanded (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुग्ध
उन्मुग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Confounded, confused.<BR>—2 Silly, stupid. या पूर्वा सोत्तरास्य उन्मुग्धस्य सोयं पूर्वोत्तर उन्मुग्धः Mbh. 1. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूल्
उन्मूल् €10 P. To eradicate, pluck up by the roots, exterminate; समूलमुन्मूलयतीव<BR> मे मनः Ki. 1. 41; उन्मूलिता हलधरेण पदावघातैः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूल
उन्मूल <i>a.</i> Plucked, destroyed. तमिमं शैलमुन्मूलं करोमि तव<BR> गोपते Rām. 7. 16. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलनम्
उन्मूलनम् —1 Plucking up by the roots, eradication, destroying, uprooting;<BR> न पादपोन्मूलनशक्ति रंहः R. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृज्
उन्मृज् €2 P.<BR>—1 To rub or wipe off, clean by washing; त्रिः प्राश्यापो द्विरुन्मृज्य खान्याद्भिः<BR> समुपस्पृशेत् Y. 1. 20.<BR>—2 To efface, blot out, obliterate. यौ ते मातोन्ममार्ज जातायाः पतिवेदनौ Av. 8. 6. 1.<BR>—3 To receive, accept (Ved.); उद् राधो गव्यं मृजे Rv. 5. 52. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्जनम्
उन्मार्जनम् Rubbing, wiping off, removing; मनःशल्य˚ Dk. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृजावमृजा
उन्मृजावमृजा Repeatedly rubbing up and down. P. II. 1. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृष्ट
उन्मृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Blotted out, effaced, cleared, removed, wiped off;<BR> स तौ कुशलवोन्मृष्टगर्भक्लेदौ R. 15. 32; Y. 2. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृद्
उन्मृद् €9 P. To rub, to do massage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मर्दनम्
उन्मर्दनम् A rubbing down of the sacrificer with sweet-smelling substances<BR> before sprinkling him with fat. cf. सर्वसुरभ्युन्मर्दनं भवति Śat. Br. 12. 8. 3. 16.<BR> and Sāyaṇa says उन्मर्दनम् उद्वर्तनं भवति ।<BR> (For details read Dr. Godeʼs paper on, ‘Massage in Ancient and Medieval India’, Annals of Bhandarkar Oriental Research Institute XXXVI, parts I━II, pp. 85. 113).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेदा
उन्मेदा <i>f.</i> Corpulence, fatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप
उप <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a prefix to verbs and nouns it expresses towards, near to, by the<BR> side of, with, under, down (opp. अप). According to G. M. the following<BR> are its senses:− उप सामीप्यसामर्थ्यव्याप्त्याचार्यकृतिमृतिदोषदानक्रियावीप्सारम्भाध्ययनपूजनेषुः:−<BR> (1) nearness, contiguity उपविशति, उपगच्छति goes near; (2) power,<BR> ability उपकरोति; (3) pervasion उपकीर्ण; (4) advice, instructing<BR> as by a teacher उपदिशति, उपदेश; (5) death, extinction, उपरत;<BR> (6) defect, fault उपघात; (7) giving उपनयति, उपहरति; (8)<BR> action, effort उप त्वानेष्ये; (9) beginning, commencement उपक्रमते,<BR> उपक्रम; (10) study उपाध्यायः; (11) reverence, worship उपस्थानम्,<BR> उपचरति पितरं पुत्रः. It is also said to have the senses of disease,<BR> ornament, command, reproof, killing, wish, resemblance &c.<BR>—2 As unconnected with verbs and prefixed to nouns, it expresses direction<BR> towards, nearness, resemblance, relationship, contiguity in space, number, time, degree<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">Page0439-2</a>]<BR> &c., but generally involving the idea of subordination or inferiority;<BR> उपकनिष्ठिका the finger next to the little finger; उपपुराणम्<BR> a secondary Purāṇa; उपगुरुः an assistant master; उपाध्यक्षः<BR> a vice-president. It usually, however, forms Avyayī. comp. in these senses;<BR> उपगङ्गम् = गङ्गायाः समीपे; उपकूलम्, ˚वनम् &c.; these are again<BR> compounded with other words; उपकूपजलाशयः; उपकण्ठनिवासिनी.<BR> Prefixed to proper nouns it means a ‘younger brother’; उपेन्द्रः.<BR>—3 With numerals it forms संख्याबहुव्रीहि and means ‘nearly’, ‘almost’;<BR> उपत्रिंशाः nearly thirty; उपविंशाः about twenty &c.<BR>—4 As a separable preposition<BR>——(<i>a</i>) with acc. when it means inferiority उपोधिकेच (P. I. 4. 87)<BR> उपहरिं सुराः Sk. the gods are under <i>i. e.</i> are inferior to Hari;<BR> शकादय उपाच्युतम् Vop.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) With loc. it expresses (1) over, above, superior to; उपनिष्के<BR> कार्षापणम्, उपपरार्धे हरेर्गुणाः; (2) addition; (3) near to, towards,<BR> in the direction of, under; (4) at, on, upon; (5) upto, in, above; <i>e. g.</i><BR> उप सानुषु on or above the peaks; वयो न वसतीरुप; or sometimes<BR>——(<i>c</i>) with the instr.; with, at the same time with, according to.<BR>—5 As a separable adverb it is rarely used in the senses of further, moreover.<BR> उपासन्नेऽधिके हीने सादृश्यप्रतियत्नयोः । तद्योगव्याप्तिपूजासु शक्तावारम्भदानयोः<BR> ॥ दक्षिणाचार्यकरणदोषाख्यानात्ययेषु च । [cf. Gr. <i>hupo</i>; L. <i>sub</i>;<BR> Goth. <i>up</i>; Germ. <i>ob</i>.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकक्ष
उपकक्ष <i>a.</i> Ved. Reaching to the shoulder; आदध्नास उपकक्षास<BR> उ त्वे Rv. 10. 71. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकक्षम्
उपकक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} The hair under the armpit; Gopath. Br. 1. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठ|उपकंठ|उपकण्ठं|उपकण्ठः
उपकण्ठ <i>a.</i> Near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठः|उपकण्ठ|उपकंठ|उपकण्ठं
उपकण्ठ + .{@-ण्ठः, -ण्ठम्@}<BR>—1 Proximity, vicinity, neighbourhood; प्राप तालीवनश्याममुपकण्ठं<BR> महोदधेः R. 4. 34, 13. 48; Ku. 7. 51; Māl. 9. 2; आकृष्य चापं श्रवणोपकण्ठे<BR> Ś. 3. 5 to the very ear. तस्योपकण्ठे घननीलकण्ठः Ku.<BR>—2 Space near a village or its boundary.<BR>—3 One of a horseʼs paces. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Upon the neck, near the throat; प्रेम्णोपकण्ठं मुहुरङ्कभाजः Śi. 3. 36.<BR>—2 In the vicinity of, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठम्|उपकंठम्
उपकण्ठ + .{@-ण्ठः, -ण्ठम्@}<BR>—1 Proximity, vicinity, neighbourhood; प्राप तालीवनश्याममुपकण्ठं<BR> महोदधेः R. 4. 34, 13. 48; Ku. 7. 51; Māl. 9. 2; आकृष्य चापं श्रवणोपकण्ठे<BR> Ś. 3. 5 to the very ear. तस्योपकण्ठे घननीलकण्ठः Ku.<BR>—2 Space near a village or its boundary.<BR>—3 One of a horseʼs paces. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Upon the neck, near the throat; प्रेम्णोपकण्ठं मुहुरङ्कभाजः Śi. 3. 36.<BR>—2 In the vicinity of, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकथा
उपकथा A short story or tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकनिष्ठिका
उपकनिष्ठिका [उपगता कनिष्ठिकाम्] The finger next to the little<BR> finger, the last but one finger (अनामिका); Śik. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकन्या
उपकन्या The friend of oneʼs daughter; P. VI. 2. 194; ˚पुरम्<BR> near the womanʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्ण्
उपकर्ण्^1 €10 U. To hear; शितिकण्ठैरुपकर्णयाम्बभूवे Śi. 20. 5.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. note: missing virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णम्
उपकर्णम् <i>ind.</i> Close to the ear, into the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णनम्
उपकर्णनम् Hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णिका
उपकर्णिका Rumour, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्मन्
उपकर्मन् <i>n.</i> A rite in which the head of the boy (वटुः)<BR> is smelt at the उपनयन ceremony; जातकर्मणि यत्प्राद पिता यच्चोपकर्मणि<BR> Mb. 12. 266. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पः|उपकल्प
उपकल्पः An ornament, तपनीयोपकल्पम् Bhāg. 3. 18. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकान्तः
उपकान्तः A class of six-storeyed buildings (Māna. 24. 16.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकालिका
उपकालिका Smaller variety of cardamom, or Fennel-flower-seed, Nigella<BR> Indica (Mar. काळे जिरें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकिरण|उपकिरणं
उपकिरण See under उपकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकीचकः|उपकीचक
उपकीचकः<BR>—1 A relation or follower of Kīchaka.<BR>—2 The army of Virāṭa under Kīchaka.<BR>—3 A sub-branch of a Bamboo tree; cf. the paronomastic quotation विराटनगरे<BR> राजन् कीचकादुपकीचकम् (where विराट can be separated as विः + आट,<BR> meaning a bird wandered).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चिः|उपकुञ्चि|उपकुंचिः
उपकुञ्चिः, -ञ्चिका<BR>—1 The plant Nigella Indica (कृष्णजीरक).<BR>—2 Small cardamom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चिका|उपकुंचिका
उपकुञ्चिः, -ञ्चिका<BR>—1 The plant Nigella Indica (कृष्णजीरक).<BR>—2 Small cardamom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुम्भ|उपकुंभ|उपकुम्भं
उपकुम्भ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Near, proximate.<BR>—2 Solitary, retired, secluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुम्भम्
उपकुम्भ + .{@-भम्@} <i>ind.</i> Near a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुल्या
उपकुल्या<BR>—1 The plant Piper Longum (Mar. पिंपळी).<BR>—2 A canal, trench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुशः|उपकुश
उपकुशः Gum-boil; a disease of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूज्
उपकूज् €1 P. To fill with cooing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूजित
उपकूजित <i>p. p.</i> Made to resound (with cooing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूजितम्
उपकूजित + .{@-तम्@} Filling with cooing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपम्
उपकूपम्, -पे <i>ind.</i><BR> Near a well; ˚जलाशयः a trough near a well<BR> for watering cattle; also<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपे
उपकूपम्, -पे <i>ind.</i><BR> Near a well; ˚जलाशयः a trough near a well<BR> for watering cattle; also<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपः|उपकूप|उपकूपं
उपकूपम्, -पे + .{@-पः@} A small cistern made of stone (Mar. टांकें, डोणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूलम्
उपकूलम् <i>ind.</i> On the shore; उपकूलं स कालिन्द्याः पुरीं पौरुषभूषणः<BR> (निर्ममे) R. 15. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृ
उपकृ €8 U.<BR>——(<i>a</i>) उपकरोति-कुरुते.<BR>—1 To place or bring near, furnish or provide with, do or render; किं<BR> ते भूयः प्रियमुपकरोतु पाकशासनः V. 5; Ms. 2. 149, 245, 5. 32.<BR>—2 To assist, serve, befriend, oblige, favour, benefit, help; प्राणैरप्युपकुर्वते<BR> Pt. 1. 83; Bk. 8. 18; (oft. with gen. of person); सा लक्ष्मीरुपकुरुते<BR> यया परेषाम् Ki. 7. 28, 8. 13; आत्मनश्चोपकर्तुम् Me. 103; Śi. 20. 74;<BR> K. 174; न हि दीपौ परस्परस्योपकुरुतः Ś. B.; sometimes with<BR> loc. also; Me. 8. 394.<BR>—3 To foster, take care of.<BR>—4 To render homage, serve, wait or attend upon (with acc.), हरिमुपकुरुते Sk.<BR>—5 To begin, set about anything (with dat.).<BR>—6 To subdue, overcome.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) उपस्करोति, -स्कुरुते.<BR>—1 To add, supply (वाक्याध्याहारे); उपस्कृतं ब्रूते P. VI. 1. 139. Sk.<BR>—2 To provide or furnish with; सितातपत्रव्यजनैरुपस्कृतः Bhāg.<BR>—3 To attend or wait on, serve.<BR>—4 To adorn, decorate, elaborate, refine, polish, prepare, perfect; राजतं<BR> चानुपस्कृतम् Ms. 5. 112; उपस्कृता कन्या Sk.; शास्त्रोपस्कृतशब्दसुन्दरगिरः Bh. 2. 15.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To care for, take care of (with acc. of person); P. I. 3. 32, VI. 1. 139.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To make efforts (with gen. of thing); एधोदकस्योपस्कुरुते,<BR> मा कस्यचिदुपस्कृथाः Bk. 8. 19, 119.<BR>—6 To furnish badly, deform; मांसं यच्चानुपस्कृतम् Ms. 3. 257.<BR>—7 To corrupt, defile, censure; एषोऽनुपस्कृतः प्रोक्तो योधधमः सनातनः 7. 98.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">Page0440-2</a>]<BR>—8 To bring or call together; उपस्कृता ब्राह्मणाः (= समुदिताः Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्या
उपकर्या A palace; also उपकार्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरणम्
उपकरणम्<BR>—1 Doing service or favour, helping, assisting.<BR>—2 Material, implement, instrument, means; यथैवोपकरणवतां जीवितं<BR> तथैव ते जीवितं स्यात् Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 2; स्वेषूपकरणेषु U. 5;<BR> ˚द्रव्यम् Mk. 3; उपकरणीभावमायाति U. 3. 3 serve as helping instruments,<BR> or assistants; परोपकारोपकरणं शरीरम् K. 207; so स्नान˚<BR> bathing materials; Pt. 1; व्यायाम˚ athletic materials; आत्मा परोपकरणीकृतः<BR> H. 2. 24; K. 80, 102, 198, 204; Y. 2. 276; Ms. 9. 270.<BR>—3 An engine, machine, apparatus, paraphernalia (in general).<BR>—4 Means of subsistence, anything supporting life.<BR>—5 A means or expedient; कर्म˚, वेद˚, यज्ञ˚ &c.<BR>—6 Fabricating, composing, elaborating.<BR>—7 The insignia of royalty. —8 The attendants of a king.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपकरणार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरणार्थ
उपकरणम् + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> Suitable, requisite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्तृ|उपकर्त्तृ
उपकर्तृ <i>a.</i> One who does a service or favour, useful, friendly;<BR> आपत्सूपकर्ता Dk. 160; हीनान्यनुपकर्तॄणि प्रवृद्धानि विकुर्वते<BR> R. 17. 58; उपकर्त्री रसादीनाम् S. D. 624; Śi. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारः|उपकार
उपकारः<BR>—1 Service, help, assistance, favour, kindness, obligation (opp. अपकार);<BR> अशक्यो द्रव्यपदार्थिकेन द्रव्यस्य गुणकृत उपकारः प्रतिज्ञातुम् Mbh.<BR> on P. II. 1. 1. उपकारापकारौ हि लक्ष्यं लक्षणमेतयोः Śi. 2. 37;<BR> शाम्येत्प्रत्यपकारेण नोपकारेण दुर्जनः Ku. 2. 40, 3. 73; Y. 3. 284;<BR> Pt. 1. 22; उपकारे वृत् to be of service or useful (to another);<BR>—2 Preparation.<BR>—3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>—4 Particularly, flowers, garlands &c. suspended at gate-ways as embellishments<BR> on festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारी
उपकारः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A royal tent, palace.<BR>—2 Caravansera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारक
उपकारक <i>a.</i> Doing service or favour, helping, contributing to,<BR> assisting, productive (of good results); उपकारकमायतेर्भृशम् Ki. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिका
उपकारिका (also उपकारी)<BR>—1 Protectress, a female assistant.<BR>—2 A palace.<BR>—3 A tent, a caravansera.<BR>—4 A kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारी
उपकारिका (also उपकारी)<BR>—1 Protectress, a female assistant.<BR>—2 A palace.<BR>—3 A tent, a caravansera.<BR>—4 A kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिन्
उपकारिन् <i>a.</i> Helping, serving, beneficial &c.; subservient, benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार्य|उपकार्य्य|उपकार्य्यः
उपकार्य <i>a.</i> —1 Deserving assistance or favour, fit to be assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार्या|उपकार्य्या
उपकार्य + .{@-र्या@} A royal house, palace; रम्यां रघुप्रतिनिधिः स नवोपकार्यां<BR> बाल्यात्परामिव दशां मदनोध्युवास R. 5. 63; a royal tent; तस्योपकार्यारचितोपचाराः 5. 41, 11. 93, 13. 79, 16. 55, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुर्वाण|उपकुर्वाणः|उपकुर्व्वाण|उपकुर्व्वाणः
उपकुर्वाण <i>a.</i> Doing service &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुर्वाणः|उपकुर्वाण|उपकुर्व्वाण|उपकुर्व्वाणः
उपकुर्वाण + .{@-णः@} A Brāhmaṇa in a state of pupilage (ब्रह्मचारिन्) who<BR> wishes to pass on to the state of a house-holder (गृहस्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृत
उपकृत <i>p. p.</i> Assisted, benefited, served &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृतम्
उपकृत + .{@-तम्@} Aid, favour, obligation; गता नाशं तारा उपकृतमसाधाविव<BR> जने Mk. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृतिः|उपकृति
उपकृतिः <i>f.</i>, उपक्रिया Favour, obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रिया
उपकृतिः <i>f.</i>, उपक्रिया Favour, obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0440-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॄ
उपकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To bestrew, scatter or throw down, scatter or pour upon; रत्नोपकीर्णां वसुधाम् Mb.<BR>—2 (उपस्कॄ)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To cut up, split, lop.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To hurt, strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकिरणम्
उपकिरणम्<BR>—1 Scattering or throwing over, covering up; burying.<BR>—2 Pervasion. ━<i>ind.</i> Near the rays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकीर्ण
उपकीर्ण <i>a.</i> Covered, strewed with; पुष्पोपकीर्णानि महाचलस्य<BR> (शृङ्गाणि) Mb. 3. 164. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्
उपकॢप् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To be fit for; तत्रेदमुपकल्पते Bhāg.<BR>—2 To be prepared or ready (at hand); आसनेषूपकॢप्तेषु Ms. 3. 208, 8. 333.<BR>—3 To result in, serve as, lead to (with dat.); वार्यपि श्रद्धया दत्तमक्षयायोपकल्पते Ms. 3. 202.<BR>—4 To become, take a (particular) form or shape. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To prepare, get ready, equip; रथम् Ve. 2.<BR>—2 To appoint, assign, allot; उपकल्पितं पशुम् Pt. 1; U. 2; Y. 1. 109.<BR>—3 To vow, promise; देवतोपकल्पित Pt. 4.<BR>—4 To set up, exhibit; इति मतिरुपकल्पिता वितृष्णा Bhāg. 1. 9. 32.<BR>—5 To render (homage), communicate.<BR>—6 To bring near, fetch.<BR>—7 To assume, take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पः|उपकल्प
उपकल्पः An appurtenance; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पनम्
उपकल्पनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Preparation; एवं विज्ञाय मतिमान् भोजनस्योपकल्पनाम् Suśr.<BR>—2 Fabricating, making &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पना
उपकल्पनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Preparation; एवं विज्ञाय मतिमान् भोजनस्योपकल्पनाम् Suśr.<BR>—2 Fabricating, making &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पित
उपकल्पित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Prepared, made &c.<BR>—2 Secondary, substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्त
उपकॢप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Brought near, at hand.<BR>—2 Ready, prepared.<BR>—3 Fitted for, adapted to.<BR>—4 Formed, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकोशा
उपकोशा N. of a daughter of उपवर्ष and wife of वररुचि Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रम्
उपक्रम् €1 Ā., €4 P.<BR>—1 To go near, approach, come to, advance towards; राज्ञस्तस्याज्ञया<BR> देवी वसिष्ठमुपचक्रमे Mb.; Bk. 8. 25. कुमारं विविधैस्तैस्तैरुपचक्रमिरे<BR> नयैः Bu. C. 4. 53.<BR>—2 To do, perform, set about; यथोक्तं निपुणमुपक्रान्तवान् Dk. 120;<BR> माधवसमक्षमुत्तरमुपक्रमिष्ये Māl. 3, 2. 7; Y. 3. 200.<BR>—3 To begin, commence (with inf. or dat.); (Ātm.); प्रसभं वक्तुमुपक्रमेत<BR> कः Ki. 2. 28; प्रतिग्रहीतुम् … त्रिलोचनस्तामुपचक्रमे च Ku. 3. 66;<BR> R. 17. 13.<BR>—4 To go against, attack, assail, उपचक्रमाते वाग्भिः Rām.<BR>—5 To make advances (of love) to; सर्वोपायैरुपक्रम्य सीताम् Rām.<BR> win over; Dk. 65.<BR>—6 To step over, stride, traverse.<BR>—7 To treat, act towards, attend on (as a physician). cure or heal (as<BR> wounds); यत्नादुपक्रम्यताम् Ś. 3 v. l.; सर्वथोपक्रान्तः Dk. 68; ˚व्रणा 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रन्तृ|उपक्रंतृ
उपक्रन्तृ A beginner, one who undertakes; प्रक्रन्ता उपक्रन्ता Mbh.<BR> on P. VII. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमः|उपक्रम
उपक्रमः<BR>—1 Beginning, commencement; रामोपक्रममाचख्यौ रक्षःपरिभवं नवम्<BR> R. 12. 42 begun by Rāma; किमुपक्रमो रावणः Mv. 2.<BR>—2 Approach, advance; साहस˚ forcible advance Māl. 7; so योषितः<BR> सुकुमारोपक्रमाः <i>ibid.</i><BR>—3 An undertaking, work, enterprize.<BR>—4 A plan, contrivance,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">Page0441-2</a>]<BR> means, expedient, stratagem, remedy; सामादिभिरुपक्रमैः Ms. 7. 107, 159;<BR> M. 3; R. 18. 15; Y. 1. 345; Śi. 20. 76.<BR>—5 Attendance on a patient, treatment, practice of medicine, physicking.<BR>—6 A test of honesty, trying the fidelity of a friend &c.; see उपधा.<BR>—7 A kind of ceremony preparatory to reading the Vedas.<BR>—8 Heroism, Courage.<BR>—9 Flight.<BR>—10 Behaviour, action; यद्यप्यकृतकृत्यानामीदृशः स्यादुपक्रमः Rām. 5. 64. 30.<BR>—11 The rim of a wheel; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणम्
उपक्रमणम्<BR>—1 Approaching.<BR>—2 Undertaking.<BR>—3 Commencement.<BR>—4 (Medic.) Treatment, physicking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणिका
उपक्रमणिका A preface, introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणीय
उपक्रमणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be gone to, approached, commenced &c.<BR>—2 Relating to the attendance (on a patient).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणीयम्
