उपक्षित्
उपक्षित् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Dwelling near.<BR>—2 Clinging or attached to; उपक्षितो वया इव Rv. 8. 19. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षीण
उपक्षीण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Decayed, exhausted, consumed.<BR>—2 Disappeared; vanished.<BR>—3 Powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेतृ
उपक्षेतृ <i>a.</i> One who draws near; or one who dwells near, attached<BR> to (उपक्षेतारस्तव) सुप्रणीते Rv. 3. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षिप्
उपक्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To throw at, cast on, hurl against; वपुषि वधाय तत्र तव शस्त्रमुपक्षिपतः<BR> Māl. 5. 31; to direct; त्वयि उपक्षिप्त आत्मा M. 2; to entrust, assign; M. 3.<BR>—2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">Page0442-1</a>]<BR> insult, upbraid, accuse, charge with; परस्परं वाग्भिरुपक्षिपन्ति Rām.<BR>—3 To throw out (a hint), hint, indicate, put forth, adduce; छन्नं<BR> कार्यमुपक्षिपन्ति Mk. 9. 3; इति उपक्षिप्तमनेन Mu. 1; Māl. 1.<BR>—4 To throw down.<BR>—5 To commence, introduce, set on foot, begin; उपक्षिप्तमनेन किमपि<BR> Mu. 1; K. 162; Dk. 59; उपक्षिप्तो भित्तिबन्धः M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेपः|उपक्षेप
उपक्षेपः<BR>—1 Throwing at, hurling.<BR>—2 Mention, allusion, hint, suggestion; कार्योपक्षेपमादौ तनुमपि रचयन्<BR> Mu. 4. 3; दारुणः खलूपक्षेपः पापस्य Ve. 5.<BR>—3 A threat, specific mention or charge; कर्णनासाच्छेदोपभीषिताभ्याम् Dk. 61.<BR>—4 Commencement; उपाय˚ M. 3.<BR>—5 Poetical or figurative style in composition (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेपक
उपक्षेपक <i>a.</i> Alluding, suggesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेपणम्
उपक्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Throwing or casting down.<BR>—2 Accusing; Charging; ˚धर्मः = शूद्रस्वामिकामान्नस्य पाकार्थं ब्राह्मणगृहे<BR> समर्पणम् Śabdak.<BR>—3 Disregard, negligence; उपक्षेपणजोऽधर्मः सुमहान्स्यान्महीपतेः<BR> Mb. 1. 213. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपखिलम्
उपखिलम् Supplement to a supplement, sub-supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगण|उपगणः
उपगण <i>a.</i> Forming a small or subordinate class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगणः|उपगण
उपगण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A small or subordinate class.<BR>—2 A small number less than a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगन्धः|उपगन्ध|उपगंधः
उपगन्धः Perfume, scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगम्
उपगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go to, approach; attain, reach (fig. also), arrive at, visit; शशिनमुपगतेयं<BR> कौमुदी मेघमुक्तम् R. 6. 85; so दैवादुपगतं तृणम् Pt. 4; पदमुपगता<BR> Bh. 2. 10; Bk. 1. 1; तदुपगतम् Mu. 5 duly received.<BR>—2 To enter into, penetrate; अवलम्ब्य जालकमुखोपगतानुदतिष्ठदिन्दुकिरणान्मदनः Śi. 9. 39.<BR>—3 To undergo, suffer; तमो घोरमुपागतम् Rām.<BR>—4 To go to the state of, attain, acquire; तानप्रदायित्वमिवोपगन्तुम्<BR> Ku. 1. 8; प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ Śi. 9. 6; so निद्रावशम्,<BR> हर्षम्, तृप्तिम्, शान्तिम्, विषादम् &c.<BR>—5 To approach a woman (for sexual intercourse); सुप्तां मत्तां प्रमत्तां<BR> वा रहो यत्रोपगच्छति Ms. 3. 34, 4. 40.<BR>—6 To come upon, attack.<BR>—7 To occur, happen, present itself; कस्यात्यन्तं सुखमुपगतम् Me. 109, v. l.<BR>—8 To undertake, begin.<BR>—9 To suffer, share in.<BR>—10 To admit, agree to, consent, allow; वेदान्तोपगतं फलम् Ms. 2. 160.<BR>—11 To worship; सहपत्न्या विशालाक्ष्या नारायणमुपागमत् Rām. 2. 6. 1.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to come near or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग
उपग <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp. only)<BR>—1 Approaching, following, joining.<BR>—2 Receiving; ओषध्यः फलपाकान्ता बहुपुष्पफलोपगाः Ms. 1. 46; Śi. 16. 68.<BR>—3 Fit for, conducive; Mb.<BR>—4 Covered (as a female).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगत|उपगतः
उपगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone to, approached, arrived.<BR>—2 Occurred, happened.<BR>—3 Near, at hand.<BR>—4 Got, obtained.<BR>—5 Undergone, experienced.<BR>—6 Furnished with; (सहित, युक्त); जहार स शिरस्त्राणं कुण्डलोपगतं<BR> शिरः Rām. 6. 97. 32.<BR>—7 Gone to, become.<BR>—8 Promised, agreed.<BR>—9 Passed away, dead.<BR>—10 Feeling, suffering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">Page0442-2</a>]<BR> (actively used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगतम्
उपगत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth acquired.<BR>—2 Receipt; धनी वोपगतं दद्यात् स्वहस्तपरिचिह्नितम् Y. 2. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगतिः|उपगति
उपगतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approach, going near; कररुद्धनीवि दयितोपगतौ Śi. 9. 75.<BR>—2 Knowledge, acquaintance.<BR>—3 Acceptance, receipt.<BR>—4 Attainment, acquirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगन्तृ
उपगन्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Approaching.<BR>—2 Getting, acquiring.<BR>—3 Knowing.<BR>—4 Accepting, receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगमः|उपगम
उपगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Going to, drawing towards, approach; सीमन्ते च त्वदुपगमजं यत्र<BR> नीपं वधूनाम् Me. 67 your advent; व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी R. 6. 69, 9. 50.<BR>—2 Knowledge, acquaintance.<BR>—3 Attainment, acquiring; विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—4 Intercourse (as of the sexes).<BR>—5 Society, company; न पुनरधमानामुपगमः H. 1. 117.<BR>—6 Undergoing, suffering, feeling.<BR>—7 Acceptance, receipt.<BR>—8 An agreement, promise.<BR>—9 A particular high number.<BR>—10 {@-नम्@}<BR> Assumption, accepting, taking up; अप्राप्तस्य हि प्रापणमुपगमनम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 21.<BR>—11 Performing, observing (आचरण); चकार सन्ध्योपगमादि सत्तमः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 70. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगमनम्
उपगमः, -मनम्<BR>—1 Going to, drawing towards, approach; सीमन्ते च त्वदुपगमजं यत्र<BR> नीपं वधूनाम् Me. 67 your advent; व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी R. 6. 69, 9. 50.<BR>—2 Knowledge, acquaintance.<BR>—3 Attainment, acquiring; विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—4 Intercourse (as of the sexes).<BR>—5 Society, company; न पुनरधमानामुपगमः H. 1. 117.<BR>—6 Undergoing, suffering, feeling.<BR>—7 Acceptance, receipt.<BR>—8 An agreement, promise.<BR>—9 A particular high number.<BR>—10 {@-नम्@}<BR> Assumption, accepting, taking up; अप्राप्तस्य हि प्रापणमुपगमनम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 21.<BR>—11 Performing, observing (आचरण); चकार सन्ध्योपगमादि सत्तमः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 70. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगामिन्
उपगामिन् <i>a.</i> Coming near; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिगमिषु
उपजिगमिषु <i>a.</i> Wishing or desiring to go near; नीचैर्वास्यत्युपजिगमिषोर्देवपूर्वं<BR> गिरिं ते Me. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगाह्
उपगाह् P. To penetrate or force oneʼs way into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरि|उपगिरिः
उपगिरि, -रम् <i>ind.</i><BR> [गिरेश्च सेनकस्य P. V. 4. 112] Near a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरम्
उपगिरि, -रम् <i>ind.</i><BR> [गिरेश्च सेनकस्य P. V. 4. 112] Near a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरिः|उपगिरि
