उपगुरु|उपगुरुः
उपगुरुः + .{@-रु@} <i>ind.</i> Near a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगुह्
उपगुह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To clasp, embrace; तरङ्गहस्तैरुपगूहतीव R. 13. 63, 18. 47;<BR> Bk. 14. 52; Śi. 9. 38.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal, cover, encircle, gird round; वनमालोपगूढः K. 24, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूढ
उपगूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Hidden, concealed; उपान्तवानीरवनोपगूढानि R. 13. 30.<BR>—2 Embraced, clasped.<BR>—3 Held, supported; कश्चित्कराभ्यामुपगूढनालम् R. 6. 13<BR>—4 Suppressed.<BR>—5 Seized, harassed; कन्योपगूढो नष्टश्रीः कृपणो विषयात्मकः Bhāg. 4. 28. 6.<BR>—6 Filled with, covered; लताभिः पुष्पिताग्राभिरुपगूढानि सर्वतः Rām. 4. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूढम्
उपगूढ + .{@-ढम्@} An embrace; उपगूढानि सवेपथूनि च Ku. 4. 17; विश्रामार्थमुपगूढमजस्रम् ।<BR> Śi. 10. 88; कण्ठाश्लेषोपगूढम् Bh. 3. 82; गाढोपगूढम् Me. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूहनम्
उपगूहनम्<BR>—1 Hiding, concealing.<BR>—2 An embrace.<BR>—3 Astonishment, surprise; (in drama) an occurance of any wonderful event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगोह्य|उपगोह्यः
उपगोह्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be embraced.<BR>—2 To be taken or seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगोह्यः|उपगोह्य
उपगोह्य + .{@-ह्यः@}<BR>—1 An embrace.<BR>—2 A kind of fire regarded as impure (and therefore to be hidden).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगॄ
उपगॄ P. To swallow down; Suśr. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगै
उपगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To sing to any one (with dat. or acc.); साम्नैनमुपागात् Ch. Up.<BR>—2 To join in singing.<BR>—3 To praise in song, celebrate, extol; तपोलक्ष्म्या दीप्तं दिनकृतमिवोच्चैरुपजगुः Ki. 18. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगा
उपगा <i>m.</i> (-गाः) A priest in a sacrifice who sings the<BR> hymns. <i>f.</i> Accompaniment of a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगातृ
उपगातृ <i>a.</i> Singing near. ━<i>m.</i> One who accompanies the song<BR> of the Udgātṛ priest, a chorister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगानम्
उपगानम् Accompanying music; किं गानोपगानमेतत् उत वादित्रोपगानम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगायनम्
उपगायनम् Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीत
उपगीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Celebrated, sung by bards.<BR>—2 Commencing to sing; नात्र कान्तमुपगीतया तया Śi. 4. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीतिः|उपगीति
उपगीतिः <i>f.</i> A variety of the Āryā metre; see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगेयम्
उपगेयम् Song; Bhāg. 5. 26. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रन्थः|उपग्रन्थ|उपग्रंथः
उपग्रन्थः A subsidiary writing or a class of such writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रस्
उपग्रस् €1 P. To swallow down, devour, eclipse; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रह्
उपग्रह् €9 U.<BR>—1 To hold under, seize or collect from below; as रसम्.<BR>—2 To seize, take, take possession of; तवैव पादावुपगृह्य Rām.;<BR> उपगृह्यास्पदं चैव Ms. 7. 184.<BR>—3 To meet with, obtain; स मृत्युमुपगृह्णाति गर्भमश्वतरी यथा Cāṇ. 19.<BR>—4 To subdue, vanquish.<BR>—5 To provide.<BR>—6 To conciliate, take as oneʼs ally, favour, support; तदुपगृहीतेन<BR> म्लेच्छराजबलेन Mu. 1.<BR>—7 To conceive with oneʼs mind, grasp mentally; धियोपगृह्णन्स्मितशोभितेन<BR> Bhāg. 3. 22. 21.<BR>—8 To decide, determine.<BR>—9 To accept, approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहः|उपग्रह
उपग्रहः<BR>—1 Confinement, seizure.<BR>—2 Defeat, frustration; अपि च विहिते मत्कृत्यानां निकाममुपग्रहे Mu. 4. 2.<BR>—3 A prisoner.<BR>—4 Joining, addition.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Favour, encouragement, assistance, conciliation; सोपग्रहम्<BR> K. 156. परविषये कृत्याकृत्यपक्षोपग्रहः । Kau. A. 1. अमित्रोपग्रहं<BR> चास्य ते कुर्युः क्षिप्रमापदि Mb. 12. 96. 14.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Favourableness, kindness, complacence; सोपग्रहं K. 264.<BR>—6 Use.<BR>—7 A kind of peace purchased by giving over every thing; cf. क्रियते<BR> प्राणरक्षार्थं सर्वदानादुपग्रहः H. 4. 121.<BR>—8 The voice or pada of a verb; सुप्तिङुपग्रहलिङ्गनराणां Mbh. III. 1. 85, 1. 40;<BR> and 2. 127.<BR>—9 A pile or heap of kuśa grass.<BR>—10 The presiding spirit or cause which directs a planetʼs motion.<BR>—11 A minor planet (राहु, केतु &c.), a secondary heavenly body, such<BR> as a comet, meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहणम्
उपग्रहणम्<BR>—1 Seizing (from below); taking hold of; as in पादोपग्रहणम्.<BR>—2 Seizure, capture, taking one prisoner.<BR>—3 Supporting, furthering, promoting.<BR>—4 Holy study, study of the Vedas (after being initiated into them); वेदोपग्रहणार्थाय<BR> तावग्राहयत प्रभुः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राहः|उपग्राह
उपग्राहः<BR>—1 Making a present.<BR>—2 A present; उच्चावचानुपग्राहान् राजभिः प्रापितान् बहून् Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राह्य|उपग्राह्यः
उपग्राह्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be favoured or retained in service; Mu. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राह्यः|उपग्राह्य
उपग्राह्य + .{@-ह्यः@}<BR>—1 An offering or present.<BR>—2 Particularly, a present or offering to a great man or king; the modern<BR> <i>Nazarāṇā</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघात|उपघातः
उपघात See under उपहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातकः|उपघातक
उपघातकः A smaller variety of a plant Cassia fistula (Mar. लघुबाहवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघुष्
उपघुष् €1. €10 P. To fill with noise, make resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघुष्ट
उपघुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Resounding with, noisy.<BR>—2 Resonant.<BR>—3 Sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघोषणम्
उपघोषणम् Proclaiming, publication, making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघ्नः|उपघ्न
उपघ्नः [उप-हन्-क] P. III. 3. 85 उपघ्न आश्रये.<BR>—1 Contiguous support; पर्वतोपघ्नः Sk.; छेदादिवोपघ्नतरोर्व्रतत्यौ R. 14. 1.<BR>—2 Shelter, support, stay, protection. (स्यादुपघ्नोऽन्तिकाश्रये ।)<BR> पिप्रायाद्रि-गुहोपघ्नान् … । Bk. 7. 64; cf. also अपश्यतां दाशरथी<BR> जनन्यौ छेदादिवोपघ्नतरोर्व्रतत्यौ । R. 14. 1.<BR>—3 That which rests upon or is supported by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघ्रा
उपघ्रा P. To smell, to touch with the mouth; पर्यश्रुरस्वजत<BR> मूर्धनि चोपजघ्रौ R. 13. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्रः|उपचक्र
उपचक्रः [उपगतः चक्रं चक्रवाकम्] A variety of the ruddy goose. Mb. 3. 178. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्षुस्
उपचक्षुस् <i>n.</i> [उपगतं चक्षुरिव]<BR>—1 An eye-glass, spectacles cf. उपनेत्रम्.<BR>—2 A superhuman or divine eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचतुर
उपचतुर <i>a.</i> (P. V. 4. 77. Vārt. 1) About four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्
उपचर् €1 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To serve, wait or attend upon; गिरिशमुपचचार Ku. 1. 60;<BR> निमित्तज्ञान् K. 64; Ms. 3. 193, 4. 254; सममुपचर भद्रे सुप्रियं<BR> चाप्रियं च Mk. 1. 31; K. 326.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To honour, worship; प्रतिमाः पूजासत्कारेणोपचर्यन्ते K. 40, 323; V. 3.<BR>—2 To treat, deal with, act towards; entertain; मित्रत्वेन उपचरितस्य<BR> Dk. 71 treated as a friend; भोजनादिना मामुपाचरत् 77, 117; तां<BR> प्रियसखीमिवोपाचरत् 134; उपाचरत् कृत्रिमसंविधाभिः R. 14. 17 honoured<BR> or entertained; 5. 62; स्थाने इयं देवीशब्देनोपचर्यते V. 3 honoured<BR> with the title of queen. तत्रभवन्तो युवत्वेनोपचर्यमाणाः प्रीता भवन्ति<BR> Mbh. on IV. 1. 163.<BR>—3 To attend on (as a patient), treat, tend, nurse; यत्नादुपचर्यताम्<BR> Ś. 3; मन्त्रवादिभिरुपचर्यमाणः Pt. 1.<BR>—4 To approach, go towards.<BR>—5 To undertake, begin (mostly Vedic in these senses). ━<i>pass.</i><BR> To be used figuratively or metaphorically, be applied figuratively to any<BR> one (with loc.); तस्माच्चेतनवदुपचर्यते Ś. B.; पर एवात्मा बालैः<BR> शारीर इत्युपचर्यते <i>ibid.</i>; कालोऽयं द्विपरार्धाख्यो निमेष उपचर्यते<BR> Bhāg.; भुक्ता ब्राह्मणा इत्यत्र अन्नस्य भुक्तत्वं ब्राह्मणेषूपचर्यते<BR> Malli. on Ki. 1. 1; Bṛ. S. 5. 15; प्रत्यासत्त्या उपचर्य योज्यते K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर|उपचरः
उपचर <i>a.</i> Accessory, supplementary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचरः|उपचर
उपचर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Access, approach.<BR>—2 Cure, treatment; त्वग्भेदी व्रणः सूपचरः easily curable.<BR>—3 {@उपचरणम्@} Approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचरितम्
उपचरितम् A particular rule of Sandhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्य|उपचर्य्य
उपचर्य <i>pot. p.</i> [P. III. 1. 100] —1 To be served or waited upon;<BR> to be honoured or worshipped; उपचर्यः स्त्रिया साध्व्या सततं देववत्पतिः<BR> Ms. 5. 154; अनुपचर्ये (भृत्ये) Pt. 1. 101 not requiring flattery,<BR> unassuming; दुःख˚ Mu. 3. 5 difficult to serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्या|उपचर्य्या
उपचर्य + .{@-र्या@}<BR>—1 Service, attendance.<BR>—2 Physicking, treating, curing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारः|उपचार
उपचारः<BR>—1 Service, attendance; honouring worshipping, entertaining; Mk. 4; अस्खलितोपचाराम्<BR> R. 5. 20; K. 344.<BR>—2 Civility, politeness, courtesy, polite behaviour, (external display<BR> of courtesy); ˚परिभ्रष्टः H. 1. 114 devoid of civility, uncourteous;<BR> ˚विधिर्मनस्विनीनाम् M. 3. 3; उपचारैरुपाचरत् Ks. 16. 29; मिथ्योपचारैश्च<BR> वशीकृतानाम् H. 1. 75; नोपचारेण ब्रूयाः Rām.; ˚पदं न चेदिदम्<BR> Ku. 4. 9 a merely complimentary saying, a flattering compliment; ˚मात्रमधुरम्<BR> K. 222, 207; M. 4; ˚क्रिया Ms. 8. 357 showing marks of favour, courting,<BR> (sending perfumes &c.).<BR>—3 Salutation, usual or customary obeisance, homage; नोपचारमर्हन्ति<BR> Ś. 3. 17; ˚यन्त्रणया M. 4; ˚अतिक्रमम् 4, 5; ˚अञ्जलिः R. 3. 11<BR> folding the hands in salutation.<BR>—4 A form or mode of address or salutation; तेन वाक्योपचारेण विस्मिताः<BR> राजसत्तमाः Mb. 5. 162. 45; रामभद्र इत्येव मां प्रत्युपचारः शोभते<BR> तातपरिजनस्य U. 1; यथा गुरुस्तथोपचारेण 6; V. 5; Śi. 9. 78.<BR>—5 External show or form, ceremony; प्रावृषेण्यैरेव लिङ्गैर्मम राजोपचारः<BR> V. 4 royal service, pomp or state of royalty; भूषणाद्युपचारेण Mu. 3. 23, v. l.<BR>—6 A remedy, physicking, application of cure, of remedy; शिशिर˚ Dk. 15;<BR> शीत˚ Pt. 1; Dk. 23; K. 102.<BR>—7 Practice, performance, act, conduct, management, procedure; व्रतचर्या˚<BR> Ms. 1. 111; प्रसाधन˚ 10. 32, 32 9; कामोपचारेषु Dk. 81 in<BR> the conduct of love-affairs; समन्त्रं सोपचारम् (अस्त्रम्) Mb.;<BR> अवेशसदृशप्रणयोपचाराम् Mk. 8. 23 course of love &c.; वाक्योपचारे<BR> कुशला Rām. 2. 44. 30 skilled in the employment of words; use, usage;<BR> यत्र लौकिकानामुपचारः v. l. for व्याहारः in U. 6.<BR>—8 Means of doing homage or showing respect; प्रकीर्णाभिनवोपचारम्<BR> (राजमार्गम्) R. 7. 4 (hanging garlands &c.); 5. 41.<BR>—9 Hence, any necessary or requisite article (of worship, ceremony, decoration,<BR> furniture &c.); presenting flowers, perfumes &c.; सन्मङ्गलोपचाराणाम्<BR> R. 10. 77; कॢप्तोपचारां चतुरस्रवेदीम् Ku. 7. 88; कुसुमैः कृतोपचारः<BR> V. 2; so ˚रमणीयतया Ś. 6; ˚वत्सु मञ्चेषु R. 6. 1 the necessary<BR> decorations (canopy &c.); (the Upachāras or articles of worship are variously<BR> numbered, being 5, 10, 16, 18 or 64).<BR>—10 Behaviour, conduct, demeanour; वैश्यशूद्रोपचारं च Ms. 1. 116;<BR> (religious) conduct in life; साधूनामुपचारज्ञः Rām.; परिजन˚ Mk. 1.<BR>—11 Use, employment; K. 183.<BR>—12 Any religious performance, a ceremony; प्रयुक्तपाणिग्रहणोपचारौ<BR> Ku. 7. 86; Mv. 1. 24.<BR>—13<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Figurative or metaphorical use, secondary application (opp. मुख्य<BR> or primary sense); अचेतनेऽपि चेतनवदुपचारदर्शनात् Ś. B.; कूलं<BR> पिपतिषतीत्यचेतनेऽपि कूले चेतनवदुपचारो दृश्यते Mbh. on P. IV. 3. 86<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">Page0444-2</a>]<BR> personification; so छत्रिणो गच्छन्तीत्येकेनापि छत्रिणा बहूनां<BR> छत्रित्वोपचारदर्शनात् Ś. B.; करणे कर्तृत्वोपचारात् <i>ibid.</i>;<BR> न चास्य करधृतत्वं तत्त्वतोऽस्तीति मुख्येऽपि उपचार एव शरणं स्यात् K. P. 10.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Supposed or fancied identification founded on resemblance; उभयरूपा<BR> चेयं शुद्धा उपचारेणामिश्रितत्वात् K. P. 2. (S. D. explains उपचार<BR> by अत्यन्तं विशकलितयोः सादृश्यातिशयमहिम्ना भेदप्रतीतिस्थगनमात्रम्).<BR>—14 A bribe.<BR>—15 A pretext; Śi. 10. 2.<BR>—16 A request, solicitation.<BR>—17 Occurrence of स् and ष् in the place of Visarga.<BR>—18 N. of a परिशिष्ट of the Sāmaveda.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपचारच्छलम्, उपचारपदम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारच्छलम्
उपचारः + -च्छलम् A kind of fallacious inference to be refuted by reference<BR> to the real sense of a word used metaphorically, <i>e. g.</i> if any one<BR> from the sentence मञ्चाः कोशन्ति were to conclude that the मञ्च<BR> (platform) really cries and not persons on the platform. Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारपदम्
उपचारः + -पदम् A courteous or polite word, a mere compliment. उपचारपदं<BR> न चेदिदं त्वमनङ्गः कथमक्षता रतिः । Ku. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारिक
उपचारिक <i>a.</i> Serving for, belonging to; युद्धोपचारिकं यत्तु<BR> तच्छीध्रं प्रविधीयताम् Mb. 4. 52. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारिन्
उपचारिन् <i>a.</i> Attending, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्य|उपचार्यः|उपचार्य्य|उपचार्य्यः
उपचार्य <i>pot. p.</i> To be served or waited upon; to be worshipped &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्यः|उपचार्य|उपचार्य्य|उपचार्य्यः
उपचार्य + .{@-र्यः@} Practice of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्यम्
उपचार्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्म|उपचर्मं|उपचर्म्म
उपचर्म, -र्मम् <i>ind.</i><BR> On the skin, near the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्मम्
उपचर्म, -र्मम् <i>ind.</i><BR> On the skin, near the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचि
उपचि €5 U.<BR>—1 To gather together, heap up, accumulate, collect; शश्वत्सिद्धैरुपचितबलिम्<BR> Me. 57. (v. l.)<BR>—2 To add, increase, strengthen; उपचिन्वन् प्रभां तन्वीं प्रत्याह परमेश्वरः<BR> Ku. 6. 25; चेतःपीडामुपचिनोति Mu. 2; अधोधः पश्यतः कस्य महिमा<BR> नोपचीयते H. 2. 2; Bk. 6. 33; Śi. 4. 10, 8. 6; उपचीयमानगर्भा<BR> K. 66 being developed; बलेनैव सहोपचीयते मदः K. 290; क्षीणोऽप्युपचीयते<BR> पुनश्चन्द्रः Bh. 2. 87 waxes.<BR>—3 To cover over with; स्मरजन्मघर्मपयसोपचिताम् Śi. 9. 35; Ms. 6. 41.<BR>━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be collected or accumulated; to increase, become strong, to be covered<BR> with &c.; see above.<BR>—2 To be prosperous, succeed, thrive, be better off; चत्वारस्तूपचीयन्ते<BR> विप्र आढ्यो वणिङ् नृपः Ms. 8. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचयः|उपचय
उपचयः<BR>—1 Accumulation, addition, accession; येन मूर्तीनामुपचयापचयाश्च<BR> लक्ष्यन्ते तं कालमाहुः Mbh. on II. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Increase, growth, excess; बल˚ K. 105; स्वशक्त्युपचये Śi. 2. 57;<BR> अम्भसामुपचयाय 9. 32; भाग्य˚ Ratn. 1. 6 dawn of good<BR> fortune; so ज्ञान˚, मांस˚.<BR>—3 Quantity, heap.<BR>—4 Prosperity, elevation, rise. शिवस्योपचयं वीक्ष्य तथापचयमात्मनः ।<BR> Śiva B. 25. 32.<BR>—5 The third, sixth, tenth and eleventh house or position from the first<BR> of a zodiacal sign (or a <i>lagna</i> q. v.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपचयापचय, उपचयभवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचयापचय
उपचयः + -अपचय (du.) rise and fall, prosperity and decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचयभवनम्
उपचयः + -भवनम् a species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचायिन्
उपचायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Increasing, growing.<BR>—2 Thriving, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचाय्यः|उपचाय्य
उपचाय्यः [उपचीयतेऽग्निरत्र आधारे ण्यत् P. III. 1. 131]<BR>—1 A kind of sacred fire.<BR>—2 A place for holding sacrificial fire, altar, hearth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित|उपचितः
उपचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Collected, gathered together, accumulated; अस्रैरुपचितैः Me. 107.<BR>—2 Increased, grown; U. 6. 28; R. 9. 27; ˚अवयवा मञ्जरी 9. 44 full-grown.<BR>—3 Grown in power, strengthened; Śi. 6. 63; R. 17. 54; ˚महामोहगहनः<BR> Māl. 1. 30; ˚वपुः Me. 34; लोकप्रसिद्धिः उपचिता Mu. 2 the popular<BR> idea was strengthened.<BR>—4 Full of, abounding in, covered over with; R. 9. 53; वियदुपचितमेघम् Bh. 1. 35.<BR>—5 Abundantly furnished with, plastered, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचितिः|उपचिति
उपचितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Accumulation, collection, growth, increase; सहायोपचितिम् कृत्वा Mb. 5. 134. 5.<BR>—2 honour, gain; लब्धोपचितयः सर्वे Bhāg. 1. 12. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित्र
उपचित्र <i>a.</i> Variegated, Coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित्रा
उपचित्रा<BR>—1 N. of a tree (चित्रा). Salvinia Cucullata (Mar. उन्दीरकानी, थोरदान्ती);<BR> also उपचित्रका.<BR>—2 N. of a lunar mansion स्वाति; also हस्त.<BR>—3 A particular metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचिल्ली
उपचिल्ली A species of Chenopodium (Mar. चन्दनबटवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचूलनम्
उपचूलनम् Heating, burning; also उपचूडन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छदः
उपच्छदः A coverlet, cover in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छन्न|उपछन्न
उपच्छन्न <i>a.</i> Covered, concealed, hidden, secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छन्द्
उपच्छन्द् €10 P.<BR>—1 To wheedle, flatter, coax, entice, invite; जलेनोपच्छन्दितः Ś. 5.<BR> coaxed to drink water; परदारानुपच्छन्दयति Sk.<BR>—2 To conciliate.<BR>—3 To beseech, request; R. 5. 58.<BR>—4 To persuade one to do a thing.<BR>—5 To give one something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छन्दः|उपच्छन्द
उपच्छन्दः<BR>—1 A requisite, apparatus; पिपासया न म्रियते सोपच्छन्दश्च जायते<BR> Mb. 13. 65. 12.<BR>—2 Cover.<BR>—3 Request, coaxing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छन्दनम्
उपच्छन्दनम्<BR>—1 Coaxing, persuading; उपच्छन्दनैरेव स्वं ते दापयितुम् प्रयतिष्यते Dk. 65.<BR>—2 Inviting; उपमन्त्रणमुपच्छन्दनम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्यवः|उपच्यव
उपच्यवः Passing into the chamber (from the house); यत्र नार्यपच्यवमुपच्यवं<BR> च शिक्षते Rv. 1. 28. 3; passing close to (in sexual intercourse ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छल्
उपच्छल् <i>p. p.</i> To decline, overreach; Prab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजगती
उपजगती A variety of the Triṣṭubh metre in which three Pādas<BR> contain twelve instead of eleven syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजन्
उपजन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born or produced, originate, arise, grow; उष्मणश्चोपजायन्ते<BR> Ms. 1. 45; H. Pr. 38; संगस्तेषूपजायते Bg. 2. 62, 14. 11.<BR>—2 To happen, take place, become visible, appear; प्राणविपत्तिरुपजायते K. 160.<BR>—3 To be or become, be or exist; सतीत्वमुपजायते Pt. 1. 138.<BR>—4 To be born again; सर्गेऽपि नोपजायन्ते Bg. 14. 2; Y. 3. 256. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (जनयति) To produce, cause, rouse; उत्तराप्रलापोपजनितकृपः K. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज
उपज <i>a.</i> Increased, being produced in addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजनः|उपजन
उपजनः<BR>—1 Addition, increase.<BR>—2 Appendage.<BR>—3 Rise, origin.<BR>—4 Addition of a letter in the formation of words; उपजन आगमः<BR> Mbh. on Śiva Sūtra 5. वर्ण˚ Nir.<BR>—5 Any letter, syllable or affix so added; अनर्थका उपजनाः Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजनम्
उपजनः + .{@-नम्@} The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजा
उपजा Ved. Remote posterity. पितामहाः पितरः प्रजोपजाहम् Av. 11. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजात
उपजात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Produced, caused; ˚कोप, ˚क्रोध excited, moved to anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजातखेद
उपजात + .{@-˚खेद@} Suffering from exhaustion, faint, feeble; ˚विश्वास<BR> confiding, believing, trusting.<BR>—2 Happened, taken place; U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजातिः|उपजाति
उपजातिः <i>f.</i> A mixed metre (see App.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजप्
उपजप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To whisper into the ears of (another), win over to oneʼs party by secretly<BR> suggesting anything in the ear; अङ्गारवर्षं राजवधायोपजप्य Dk. 104;<BR> क्षत्तारं कुरुराजस्तु शनैः कर्णमुपाजपत् Mb.<BR>—2 (Hence) to instigate to rebellion or treachery, conspire with; उपजप्यानुपजपेत् Ms. 7. 197.<BR>—3 To commit mischief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजप्य
उपजप्य <i>a.</i> To be brought over or instigated to rebellion by<BR> whispering into the ear; उपजप्यानुपजपेत् Ms. 7. 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापः|उपजाप
उपजापः<BR>—1 Secretly whispering into the ear or communicating; परकृत्य˚ Mu. 2.<BR>—2 Secret overtures or negotiations (with the enemyʼs friends), sowing<BR> the seeds of dissension, treachery, treason, instigating to rebellion^1;<BR> उपजापः कृतस्तेन तानाकोपवतस्त्वयि Śi. 2. 99; उपजापसहान् विलङ्घयन्<BR> स विधाता नृपतीन्मदोद्धतः Ki. 2. 47, 16. 42; अपि सहन्ते अस्मदुपजापं<BR> प्रजाः Mu. 2.<BR>—3 Disunion, separation. उपलब्धस्य उपजापमुपेयात् Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापक
उपजापक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Whispering into the ears of, instigating to rebellion; घातयोद्विविधैर्दण्डैररीणां<BR> चोपजापकान् Ms. 9. 275.<BR>—2 Treacherous, traitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजरसम्
उपजरसम्^1 <i>ind.</i> Towards old age or in old age; P. V. 4. 107. Vārt.<BR> जराया जरस् च.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्प्
उपजल्प् €1 P.<BR>—1 To talk to, converse with, chatter.<BR>—2 To advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पनम्
उपजल्पनम्, उपजल्पितम् A talk; इदमेव स्मराम्यस्याः सहसैवोपजल्पितम्<BR> Rām. 2. 60. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पितम्
उपजल्पनम्, उपजल्पितम् A talk; इदमेव स्मराम्यस्याः सहसैवोपजल्पितम्<BR> Rām. 2. 60. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पिन्
उपजल्पिन् <i>a.</i> Giving advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजानु
उपजानु <i>a.</i> Near the Knee; उपजानुभवं गडु Mbh. on IV. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्वा
उपजिह्वा, -ह्विका<BR>—1 The uvula or soft palate; epiglottis; Y. 3. 97.<BR>—2 Enlargement of the under side of the tongue.<BR>—3 A kind of ant; यदत्त्युपजिह्विका यद्वम्रो अतिसर्पति । सर्वं तदस्तु<BR> ते घृतम् Rv. 8. 102. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्विका
उपजिह्वा, -ह्विका<BR>—1 The uvula or soft palate; epiglottis; Y. 3. 97.<BR>—2 Enlargement of the under side of the tongue.<BR>—3 A kind of ant; यदत्त्युपजिह्विका यद्वम्रो अतिसर्पति । सर्वं तदस्तु<BR> ते घृतम् Rv. 8. 102. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीक|उपजीकः
उपजीक <i>a.</i> Living upon, subsisting by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीकः|उपजीक
उपजीक + .{@-कः@} Ved. A water-deity; उपजीका उद्भरन्ति समुद्रादधि भेषजम् Av. 2. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्
उपजीव् €1 P.<BR>—1 To live upon, subsist by, derive livelihood from, be supported by;<BR> उपजीव्यमानपादच्छायः K. 5; कां वृत्तिमार्य उपजीवति Mk. 2; संवाहकस्य<BR> वृत्तिम् <i>ibid.</i>; शेषास्तमुपजीवेयुर्यथैव पितरं तथा Ms. 9. 105; Y. 2. 301.<BR>—2 To live under, be dependent on, serve; अम्भसामुपचयाय उपजीवति<BR> स्म Śi. 9. 32.<BR>—3 To make use of, derive materials (for writing from); तदेतद्भारतं<BR> नाम कविभिस्तूपजीव्यते Mb.<BR>—4 To practise; ते (ब्राह्मणाः) सम्यगुपजीवेयुः षट्कर्माणि<BR> यथाकमम् Ms. 10. 74. ━<i>Caus.</i> To use, to make the most of; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव
उपजीव <i>a.</i> Ved. Living on &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवा
उपजीव + .{@-वा@} Subsistence; T. Br. 1. 5. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवक
उपजीवक, -विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living upon, subsisting by (instr. or in comp.); जातिमात्रोपजीविनाम्<BR> Ms. 12. 114, 8. 20, नानापण्योपजीविनाम् 9. 257; द्यूतोपजीव्यस्मि Mk. 2.<BR>—2 Living under, depending upon, subject to, a dependant, servant (<i>m.</i>);<BR> भीमकान्तैर्नृपगुणैः स बभूवोपजीविनाम् R. 1. 16; अस्मद्˚ K. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविन्
उपजीवक, -विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living upon, subsisting by (instr. or in comp.); जातिमात्रोपजीविनाम्<BR> Ms. 12. 114, 8. 20, नानापण्योपजीविनाम् 9. 257; द्यूतोपजीव्यस्मि Mk. 2.<BR>—2 Living under, depending upon, subject to, a dependant, servant (<i>m.</i>);<BR> भीमकान्तैर्नृपगुणैः स बभूवोपजीविनाम् R. 1. 16; अस्मद्˚ K. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवकम्
उपजीवक, -विन् + .{@-कम्@} Means of subsistence, profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवनम्
उपजीवनम्, -जीविका<BR>—1 Living.<BR>—2 Subsistence, livelihood; निन्दितार्थोपजीवनम् Y. 3. 236; क्षत्रियस्यैतदेवाहुर्धर्मं<BR> कृष्णोपजीवनम् Mb.<BR>—3 A means of living, such as property; किंचिद्दत्त्वोपजीवनम् Ms. 9. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविका
उपजीवनम्, -जीविका<BR>—1 Living.<BR>—2 Subsistence, livelihood; निन्दितार्थोपजीवनम् Y. 3. 236; क्षत्रियस्यैतदेवाहुर्धर्मं<BR> कृष्णोपजीवनम् Mb.<BR>—3 A means of living, such as property; किंचिद्दत्त्वोपजीवनम् Ms. 9. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्य|उपजीव्यः
उपजीव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Affording a livelihood; उपजीव्यद्रुमाः Y. 2. 227.<BR>—2 Giving patronage, patronizing (as a king &c.).<BR>—3 (fig.) Supplying materials for writing, that from which one derives<BR> his materials; सर्वेषां कविमुख्यानामुपजीव्यो भविष्यति Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्यः|उपजीव्य
उपजीव्य + .{@-व्यः@}<BR>—1 A patron.<BR>—2 A source or authority (from which one derives his materials); इत्यलमुपजीव्यानां<BR> मान्यानां व्याख्यानेषु कटाक्षनिक्षेपेण S. D. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्यम्
उपजीव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} A means of subsistence, अन्तपालाश्च यास्यन्ति सदारो यत्र<BR> राघवः । सहोपजीव्यं राष्ट्रं च पुरं च सपरिच्छदम् Rām. 2. 37. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजुष्ट
उपजुष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Approached, received with courtesy; इत्याचारादसि यदि मया प्रश्रयेणोपजुष्टः Mv. 3. 26.<BR>—2 Frequented, resorted to; Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषः|उपजोष
उपजोषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Affection.<BR>—2 Enjoyment; Bhāg. 5. 16. 18.<BR>—3 Frequenting, resorting to.<BR>—4 Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषणम्
उपजोषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Affection.<BR>—2 Enjoyment; Bhāg. 5. 16. 18.<BR>—3 Frequenting, resorting to.<BR>—4 Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषम्
उपजोषः, -षणम् + .{@-षम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to oneʼs desire or pleasure; यथोपजोषं भुञ्जानो नातृप्यदजितेन्द्रियः<BR> Bhāg. 7. 4. 19.<BR>—2 Silently. Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा €9 Ā.<BR>—1 To ascertain; to know.<BR>—2 To invent, find out, hit upon. (उपज्ञातम् = विनोपदेशेन ज्ञातम्);<BR> न पापमुपजानते Av. 4. 36. 8; see उपज्ञा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा [उपज्ञायते इत्युपज्ञा कर्मण्यङ्]<BR>—1 Knowledge acquired by oneself and not handed down by tradition, invention,<BR> primitive or untaught knowledge; usually in comp. which is treated as<BR> a neuter noun (P. II. 4. 21); पाणिनेरुपज्ञा पाणिन्युपज्ञं ग्रन्थः Sk.;<BR> प्राचेतसोपज्ञं रामायणम् R. 15. 63.<BR>—2 Undertaking or commencing a thing not done<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">Page0446-2</a>]<BR> before; लोकेऽभूद्यदुपज्ञमेव विदुषां सौजन्यजन्यं यशः Malli. on Raghuvaṃśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञात
उपज्ञात <i>a.</i> Invented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्मन्
उपज्मन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Striding or stepping upon, यं शूरस्तातौ यमपामुपज्मन्यं<BR> विप्रासो वाजयन्ते स इन्द्रः Sv. 1. 4. 1. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्योतिषम्
उपज्योतिषम् A Compendium on astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्वलित
उपज्वलित <i>a.</i> Lighted, inflamed; Śat. Br. 11. 8. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौक्
उपढौक् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To present (as an offering), make a respectful offering; एकैकं पशुमुपढौकयामः H. 2.<BR>—2 To carry out, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौकनम्
उपढौकनम् A respectful offering or present, <i>Nazarāṇā</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतटः|उपतट
उपतटः The skirt or border; Me. 59<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतटम्
उपतटः + .{@-टम्@} <i>ind.</i> Near the skirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्
उपतप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To make warm, heat; उपतप्तोदका नद्यः Rām.; Śi. 9. 65 (where<BR> it means to pain also).<BR>—2 To feel pain, become sick; आहिताग्निश्चेदुपतपेत् Āśval.<BR>—3 To afflict, befall (as a sickness); sometimes used impersonally. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be pained, become ill, be afflicted with; इत्यपूर्वमुपतप्यतेऽस्माभिः Mv. 2; so दुःखेनोपतप्यते &c.<BR>—2 To be emaciated with penance, practise penance; उपतप्यामहे तपः Av.<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To kindle, ignite, burn; न नो गृहाणामुप तीतपासि Av. 6. 32. 1.<BR>—2 To torment, hurt, pain.<BR>—3 To offend, oppress.<BR>—4 To mortify the body by penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतपत्|उपतपन्त्
उपतपत् <i>m.</i> Interior heat, disease (Ved.). जरया वोपतपता<BR> वाणिमानं निगच्छति Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतपन
उपतपन <i>a.</i> Paining, afflicting; वपुरिन्द्रियोपतपनेषु सततमसुखेषु<BR> पाण्डवः (स्थिरतां व्याप) Ki. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्त
उपतप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated, parched; consumed.<BR>—2 Distressed, pained, tormented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्तृ
उपतप्तृ <i>a.</i> Burning, heating. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Morbid or extra-ordinary heat.<BR>—2 Any cause of heat, burning or inflammation.<BR>—3 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापः|उपताप
उपतापः<BR>—1 Heat, warmth.<BR>—2 Trouble, distress, pain, sorrow; सर्वथा न कंचन न स्पृशन्त्युपतापाः<BR> K. 135, 177; शरीरोपतापेन Māl. 3.<BR>—3 Calamity, misfortune.<BR>—4 Sickness, disease, injury.<BR>—5 Haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापक
उपतापक <i>a.</i> Heating, igniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापनम्
उपतापनम्<BR>—1 Heating.<BR>—2 Distressing, tormenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापिन्
उपतापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heating, inflaming; causing pain.<BR>—2 Suffering heat or pain, being sick; गुर्वर्थं पितृमात्रर्थं स्वाध्यायार्थ्युपतापिनः<BR> Ms. 11. 1; cf. also पुरुषं सोम्योपतापिनं ज्ञातयः पर्युपासते Ch. Up. 6. 15. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतल्पः|उपतल्प
उपतल्पः<BR>—1 An upper story, a room on the top of a house.<BR>—2 A kind of wooden seat or stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतारक
उपतारक <i>a.</i> Overflowing (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतिष्यम्
उपतिष्यम्<BR>—1 N. of the lunar mansion or asterism called आश्लेषा.<BR>—2 N. of another asterism called पुनर्वसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतीर्थम्
उपतीर्थम्<BR>—1 Bank, a landing place on a bank of a river; Mb. 3. 153. 3.<BR>—2 The country in the vicinity; Mb. 5. 152. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतुला
उपतुला A part of the column (Bṛ. S. 5. 53, 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतृण्यः|उपतृण्य
उपतृण्यः Ved. A serpent (lurking in the grass); Av. 5. 13. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्य
उपत्य <i>a.</i> Situated under or below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्यका
उपत्यका [उप-त्यकन् P. V. 2. 34; पर्वतस्यासत्रं स्थलम्<BR> उपत्यका Sk. उपाधिभ्यां त्यकन्नासन्नारूढयोः]<BR>—1 A land at the foot of a mountain, low land; मलयाद्रेरुपत्यकाः<BR> R. 4. 46; एते खलु हिमवतो गिरेरुपत्यकारण्यवासिनं संप्राप्ताः Ś. 5.<BR> जलनीलीमिलत्पङ्कपिच्छलोपत्यकातलात् Śiva B. 26. 52.<BR>—2 A vale, valley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंश्
उपदंश् €1 P. To bite or eat anything (as a relish or condiment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशः|उपदंश
उपदंशः<BR>—1 Anything which excites thirst or appetite, a relish, condiment &c.;<BR> मूलकेनोपदंशं भुङ्क्ते Mbh. on P. IV. 1. 48; cf. P. III. 4. 47. द्वित्रानुपदंशानुपपाद्य<BR> Dk. 133; अग्रमांसोपदंशं पिब नवशोणितासवम् Ve. 3.<BR>—2 Biting, stinging.<BR>—3 The venereal disease, chancre.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A tree the root of which is used for horse-radish (शिग्रु).<BR>——(<i>b</i>) N. of another plant (समष्ठिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशनम्
उपदंशः + .{@-नम्@} Context; छागोपकरणमस्योपदंशितं यदुपदंशने पशुशब्दच्छागाभिप्राय<BR> इति गम्यते । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशितम्
उपदंशितम् Context, mention of a thing by way of context; छागोपकरणमस्योपदंशितम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 35; युगवरत्रे उपदंशिते ईषाचकादिसन्निधाने<BR> चेदक्षमानय इत्युच्यते &c. ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशिन्
उपदंशिन् <i>a.</i> Afflicted with chancre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदश
उपदश <i>a.</i> (pl.) About or nearly ten; अथोपदशा इति कोऽयं समासः<BR> बहुव्रीहिरित्याह Mbh. on P. II. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदस्
उपदस् €4 P. To fail, be wanting, dry up or be consumed. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To cause to fail or cease, extinguish; अनुगच्छन्ती प्राणानुप दासयति<BR> ब्रह्मगवी ब्रह्मज्यस्य Av. 12. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदासुक
उपदासुक <i>a.</i> Ved. Wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा €3 U.<BR>—1 To give in addition.<BR>—2 To offer, give, grant (in general). उपेद् ददाति न स्वं मुषायति Rv. 6. 28. 2.<BR>—3 To add.<BR>—4 (1 Ā.) (Ved.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To take upon oneself.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To erect, raise, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा <i>a.</i> Ved. Giving a present; Vāj. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा + .{@-दा@} (cf. आतश्चोपसर्गे P. III. 3. 106)<BR>—1 A present, an offering to a king or a great man, a <i>Nazarāṇā</i>;<BR> पञ्च उपदा दीयन्तेऽस्मै पञ्चकः Mbh. V. 1. 47. उपदा विविशुः शश्वन्नोत्सेकाः<BR> कोसलेश्वरम् R. 4. 70, 5. 41, 7. 30; P. V. 1. 47. cf. also प्रीणयित्वोपदाभिः<BR> Śiva B. 15. 53.<BR>—2 A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदातृ
उपदातृ <i>a.</i> One who gives, or grants; उपदेशोपदातॄणां नराणाम् Pt. 4. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीकृ
उपदीकृ €8 U. To offer as a present; तस्य रत्नमुपदीकृतं नृपाः Śi. 14. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानम्
उपदानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 An oblation, a present (in general).<BR>—2 A gift made for procuring favour or protection, such as a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानकम्
उपदानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 An oblation, a present (in general).<BR>—2 A gift made for procuring favour or protection, such as a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानवी
उपदानवी<BR>—1 N. of the daughter of the demon Vṛṣaparvan and mother of Duṣyanta.<BR>—2 N. of a daughter of Vaiśvānara; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिग्ध
उपदिग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Smeared, covered, anointed.<BR>—2 Spotted over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेहः|उपदेह
उपदेहः<BR>—1 An ointment, liniment.<BR>—2 A cover.<BR>—3 A minor or secondary body (such as that which grows on diseased parts of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
उपदिश् €6 U.<BR>—1 To instruct, teach, explain, advise; यद्यत्प्रयोगविषये भाविकमुपदिश्यते<BR> मया तस्य … तत्तत्प्रत्युपदिशतीव मे बाला M. 1. 5; सुखमुपदिश्यते<BR> परस्य K. 156 it is easy to advise others; ज्ञानमुपदिश् Bg. 4. 34; R. 16. 43.<BR>—2 To point, indicate, refer to; गुणशेषामुपदिश्य भामिनीम् R. 8. 73;<BR> सुवर्णपुरमार्गमुपदेक्ष्यति K. 120, 92 point out or tell.<BR>—3 To assign the right place to a thing, arrange.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To mention, specify, tell; किं कुलेनोपदिष्टेन शीलमेवात्र<BR> कारणम् Mk. 9. 7; पृषोदरादीनि यथोपदिष्टम् P. VI. 3. 109.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To inform, announce.<BR>—5 To prescribe, settle, sanction, lay down; न द्वितीयश्च साध्वीनां<BR> क्वचिद् भर्तोपदिश्यते Ms. 5. 162, 2. 190, 3. 14, 43.<BR>—6 To rule over, govern, command.<BR>—7 To name, call; द्रुतविलम्बितमित्युपदिश्यते Śrut. 28; Ms. 12. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
उपदिश् <i>f.</i>, उपदिशा An intermediate quarter, such as ऐशानी,<BR> आग्नेयी, नैरृती and वायवी. चतस्रो दिशश्चतस्र उपदिशः Maitr. Up. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिशा
उपदिश् <i>f.</i>, उपदिशा An intermediate quarter, such as ऐशानी,<BR> आग्नेयी, नैरृती and वायवी. चतस्रो दिशश्चतस्र उपदिशः Maitr. Up. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्य
उपदिश्य <i>a.</i> Being in an intermediate quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्ट|उपदिष्टः
उपदिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Specified, pointed out, particularized; पृथूपदिष्टां दुदुहुर्धरित्रीम्<BR> Ku. 1. 2. पृषोदरादीनि यथोपदिष्टम् P. VI. 3. 109.<BR>—2 Taught, instructed, advised.<BR>—3 Put forward as a plea or reason.<BR>—4 Initiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्टम्
उपदिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Advice, counsel; (in drama) a persuasive speech; S. D. 449.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशः|उपदेश
उपदेशः<BR>—1 Instruction, teaching, advice, prescription; एष आदेशः, एष उपदेशः<BR> T. Up. 1. 11. 4. सुशिक्षितोऽपि सर्व उपदेशेन निपुणो भवति M. 1<BR> (see the act <i>inter alia</i>); स्थिरोपदेशामुपदेशकाले प्रपेदिरे प्राक्तनजन्मविद्याः<BR> Ku. 1. 30; अचिरप्रवृत्तोपदेशं नाट्यम् M. 1, 2. 10; Ś. 2. 3; Ms. 8. 272;<BR> Amaru. 29; R. 12. 57; K. 26; M. 6; परोपदेशे पाण्डित्यम् H. 1. 99.<BR>—2 Pointing out or referring to; शब्दानामितरेतरोपदेशः Nir.<BR>—3 Specification, mentioning, naming.<BR>—4 A plea, pretext.<BR>—5 Initiation, communication of an initiatory Mantra or formula; चन्द्रसूर्यग्रहे<BR> तीर्थे सिद्धक्षेत्रे शिवालये । मन्त्रमात्रप्रकथनमुपदेशः स उच्यते ॥<BR>—6 (In gram.) A form in a rule, an indicatory form (any word or part of<BR> a word, such as an affix, augment &c. with its <i>anubandhas</i> which show<BR> what particular grammatical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">Page0448-1</a>]<BR> rules are to be applied. उपदेश आद्योच्चारणम् Sk.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपदेशार्थवाक्यम्, उपदेशवचनम्, उपदेशसाहस्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशार्थवाक्यम्
उपदेशः + -अर्थवाक्यम्, -वचनम् a parable, moral fable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशवचनम्
उपदेशः + -अर्थवाक्यम्, -वचनम् a parable, moral fable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशसाहस्री
उपदेशः + -साहस्री N. of a philosophical work by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उपदेशक <i>a.</i> Giving instruction, teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशकः|उपदेशक
उपदेशक + .{@-कः@} An instructor, a guide, preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशता
उपदेशता<BR>—1 The state of being a precept or rule; तपस्विनामप्युपदेशतां गतम् Ku. 5. 36.<BR>—2 Instruction, teaching.<BR>—3 Doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशनम्
उपदेशनम् Advising, instructing; किं पुनरुपदेशनम् शास्त्रम्<BR> Mbh. on P. I. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशना
उपदेशनम् + .{@-ना@} Information, doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशिन्
उपदेशिन् <i>a.</i> Advising, instructing. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A teacher, adviser.<BR>—2 A word or affix &c. in the form in which it appears in grammatical rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उपदेष्टृ <i>a.</i> Giving instruction or advice.<BR>━<i>m.</i> ({@ष्टा@}) A teacher, preceptor; especially a spiritual preceptor; चत्व्रो वयमृत्विजः<BR> स भगवान्कर्मोपदेष्टा हरिः Ve. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदी
उपदी N. of a plant (वंदाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीका
उपदीका A kind of ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीक्षिन्
उपदीक्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Partaking in an initiatory or other religious rites.<BR>—2 A near relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
उपदृश् €1 P. —1 To see, behold, look at, perceive. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be or become visible. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to see, show or exhibit.<BR>—2 To place before, show up, communicate, make (one) acquainted (with);<BR> राज्ञः पुरो मामुपदर्श्य H. 3; नयविद्भिर्नवे राज्ञि सदसच्चोपदर्शितम् R. 4. 10.<BR>—3 To present a false appearance, deceive a person by a false appearance, illude.<BR>—4 To explain, illustrate; चतुष्पाद्व्यवहारोऽयं विवादेषूपदर्शितः Y. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उपदर्शक <i>a.</i> Showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शकः|उपदर्शक
उपदर्शक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 One who shows the way, a guide.<BR>—2 A door-keeper.<BR>—3 A witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शनम्
उपदर्शनम्<BR>—1 Exhibiting, representing.<BR>—2 A commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
उपदृश् <i>a.</i> Seeing, witnessing (as the sun and moon). <i>f.</i> Aspect, view (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृष्टिः|उपदृष्टि
उपदृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Show, view, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रष्टृ
उपद्रष्टृ <i>a.</i> Seeing, overlooking. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A supervisor, inspector; आर्यावर्तमुपद्रष्ट्रे सदस्येभ्यस्ततः परम्<BR> Bhāg. 9. 16. 22,<BR>—2 A witness; उपद्रष्टानुमन्ता च Bg. 13. 22; त्रिभिः साक्षाद् दृष्टं<BR> भवति यश्च ददाति यस्मै च दीयते यश्चोपद्रष्टा Mbh. on V. 2. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवः|उपदेव
उपदेवः, -देवता<BR> A minor or inferior god (as the Yakṣas, Gandharvas and Apsarasas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उपदेवः, -देवता<BR> A minor or inferior god (as the Yakṣas, Gandharvas and Apsarasas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेहिका
उपदेहिका A kind of insect, white ant (Mar. वाळवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदोहः|उपदोह
उपदोहः<BR>—1 A nipple of the udder of a cow.<BR>—2 A milking vessel, also उपदुहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रु
उपद्रु €1 P.<BR>—1 To run near to, run towards; स व्रीहिणां यावदपासितुं गताः शुकान्मृगैस्तावदुपद्रुतश्रियाम् Śi. 12. 42.<BR>—2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">Page0448-2</a>]<BR> attack, assault, rush at; तमुपाद्रवदुद्यम्य दक्षिणं दोर्निशाचरः<BR> R. 15. 23; प्राग्ज्योतिषमुपाद्रवत् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रवः|उपद्रव
उपद्रवः<BR>—1 An unhappy accident, misfortune, calamity.<BR>—2 Injury, trouble, harm; पुंसामसमर्थानामुपद्रवायात्मनो भवेत्कोपः<BR> Pt. 1. 324; निरुपद्रवं स्थानम् Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Outrage, violence.<BR>—4 A national distress (whether caused by the king or famine, seasons &c.).<BR>—5 A national disturbance, rebellion.<BR>—6 A symptom, a supervenient disease (one brought on whilst a person is<BR> suffering from another).<BR>—7 The sixth part of a Vedic sāman consisting of seven limbs. अथ सप्तविधस्य<BR> वाचि सप्तविधं सामोपासीत … यदुपेति स उपद्रवः Ch. Up. 2. 8. 2.<BR>—8 A servant; अनृग्यजुरसामा च प्राजापत्य उपद्रवः Mb. 12. 60. 44.<BR>—9 Loss, waste; अष्टकापितृदेवत्यमित्ययं प्रसृतो जनः । अन्नस्योपद्रवं<BR> पश्य मृतो हि किमशिष्यति ॥ Rām. 2. 108. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रविन्
उपद्रविन् <i>a.</i> —1 Attacking, oppressive, tyrannical, factious. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A tyrant, an oppressor.<BR>—2 A rebel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुत
उपद्रुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Visited by calamities, oppressed, attacked, infested; वेदनाभिरुपद्रुतम् H. 4. 88.<BR>—2 (In astr.) Eclipsed.<BR>—3 Boding evil, inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुतम्
उपद्रुत + .{@-तम्@} A term used by the Bāṣkalas for a kind of Sandhi, also<BR> called उद्ग्राहवत् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्वारम्
उपद्वारम् A side-door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्वीपः|उपद्वीप
उपद्वीपः An adjacent small island, minor island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्मः|उपधर्म|उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्मः<BR>—1 A by-law, a secondary or minor religious precept (opp. पर); एष<BR> धर्मः परः साक्षादुपधर्मोऽन्य उच्यते Ms. 2. 237, 4. 147.<BR>—2 A heretic, false faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place or lay upon, place under or in; अधिजानु बाहुमुपधाय Śi. 9. 54;<BR> उपहितं शिशिरापगमश्रिया मुकुलजालमशोभत किंशुके R. 9. 31;<BR> Bk. 15. 47; Ku. 1. 44; हृदि चैनामुपधातुमर्हसि R. 8. 77 treasure<BR> up-lay to heart; Ms. 4. 54; उपहितसूक्ष्मग्रन्थिना Ś. 1. 19.<BR>—2 To place, lay; वामहस्तोपहितवदना Ś. 4 resting on.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To place near; अक्ष्णोर्मुखेन्दुमुपधेहि Mv. 4. 56.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To put to or yoke (as a horse to a carriage &c.); उप त्मनि<BR> दधानो धुर्याशून्.<BR>—4 To cause, bring on or produce; नरः कृतान्तोपहितां (दशां)<BR> प्रपद्यते Mk. 1. 53.<BR>—5 To impose, entrust with, charge with (as a duty); तदुपहितकुटुम्बः R. 7. 71.<BR>—6 To lay a command upon, enjoin, instruct in (with acc.); स्त्रीषु नृत्यमुपधाय<BR> शिक्षयन् R. 19. 36.<BR>—7 To lie down upon, use as a pillow; उपधाय वामभुजमशयिषि Dk. 111.<BR>—8 To apply, employ, lay or bestow upon, क्रिया हि वस्तूपहिता प्रसीदति R. 3. 29.<BR>—9 To place over, cover, conceal.<BR>—10 To add, place in addition.<BR>—11 To communicate, impart, give, bestow; उपहितशोभा Bk. 2. 55.<BR>—12 To locate; एतदुपहितं चैतन्यम् Vedānta S.<BR>—13 (In gram.) To precede without the intervention of another syllable.<BR>—14 To deceive (वञ्च्); स्वयं चापहृता भृत्या ये चाप्युपहिताः परैः<BR> Mb. 12. 111. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा<BR>—1 Imposition, forgery, fraud, deceit, trick, pretence; उपधाभिश्च यः<BR> कश्चित्परद्रव्यं हरेन्नरः Ms. 8. 193.<BR>—2 Trial or test of honesty, (भेदोपजापौ उपधा धर्माद्यैर्यत्परीक्षणम्);<BR> (said to be of 4 kinds:− 1 loyalty, 2 disinterestedness, 3 continence, 4<BR> courage <i>i. e.</i> धर्मोपधा Religious allurement, अर्थोपधा Monetary<BR> allurement, कामोपधा Love allurement, भयोपधा Allurement under<BR> the pressure of fear. ‘भिया धर्मार्थकामैश्च परीक्षा या तु सोपधा’ इत्यभिधानचिन्तामणिः);<BR> (शोधयेत्) धर्मोपधाभिर्विप्रांश्च सर्वाभिः सचिवान् पुनः Kālikā P.<BR> उपधाभिः शौचाशौचज्ञानममात्यानाम् । Kau. A. 1. 10; अमात्यानुपधातीनान् Mb. 15. 5. 14.<BR>—3 A means or expedient; अयशोभिदुरा लोके कोपधा मरणादृते Śi. 19. 58.<BR>—4 (In gram.) A penultimate letter (अन्त्याद्वर्णात्पूर्वम् उपधा). अलोन्त्यात्<BR> पूर्व उपधा P. I. 1. 65.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपधाभृतः, उपधालोपः, उपधाशुचि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाभृतः|उपधाभृत
उपधा + -भृतः a servant who has been guilty of dishonesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधालोपः|उपधालोप
उपधा + -लोपः Elision of the penultimate letter (<i>e. g.</i> in the case<BR> of a बहुव्रीहि compound ending in अन्) P. IV. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाशुचि
उपधा + -शुचि <i>a.</i> tried, of approved loyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उपधान <i>a.</i> Used (as a Mantra) in the putting up of the sacrificial<BR> bricks; P. IV. 4. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानम्
उपधान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Placing or resting upon.<BR>—2 A pillow, cushion; रामबाहुरुपधानमेष U. 1. विपुलमुपधानं<BR> भुजलता Bh. 3. 79.<BR>—3 Peculiarity, individuality (विशेषम्); फलोपाधानाभावात् P. VI. 3. 39. Sk.<BR>—4 Affection, kindness.<BR>—5 A religious observance among especially the Jainas for preparing the<BR> ground for future monkhood.<BR>—6 Excellence or excellent quality; सोपधानां धियं धीराः स्थेयसीं खट्वयन्ति<BR> ये Śi. 2. 77. (where उ˚ also means a pillow).<BR>—7 Poison.<BR>—8 A small wooden pin of a stringed musical instrument; पाशोपधानां<BR> ज्यातन्त्रीं चापदण्डां महास्वनाम् Mb. 4. 35. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानी
उपधान + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A pillow, cushion.<BR>—2 A foot-stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानकम्
उपधानकम् A pillow, cushion; Hemādri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय <i>a.</i> To be placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीयम्
उपधानीय + .{@-यम्@} A pillow; अशेत भूमौ सह पाण्डुपुत्रैः पादोपधानीयकृता<BR> कुशेषु Mb. 1. 192. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधायिन्
उपधायिन् <i>a.</i> Using as a pillow; अशेत सा बाहुलतोपधायिनी Ku. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिः|उपधि
उपधिः [उप-धा-कि] उपसर्गे घोः किः P. III. 3. 92.<BR>—1 Fraud, dishonesty; निरुपधि विशुद्धं विजयते U. अरिषु हि विजयार्थिनः<BR> क्षितीशा विदधति सोपधि सन्धिदूषणानि Ki. 1. 45, also Mb. 12. 57. 17;<BR> see अनुपधि also.<BR>—2 (In law) Suppression of the truth, a false suggestion; यत्र वाप्युपधिं<BR> पश्येत्तत्सर्वं विनिवर्तते Ms. 8. 165.<BR>—3 Terror, threat, compulsion, false inducement; बलोपधिविनिर्वृत्तान्<BR> व्यवहारान्निवर्तयेत् Y. 2. 31, 89.<BR>—4 The part of a wheel between the nave and the circumference, or the<BR> wheel itself; नभ्येव न उपधीव प्रधीव Rv. 2. 39. 4.<BR>—5 Foundation (with the Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिकः|उपधिक
उपधिकः A cheat, knave, one who imposes by threats, fraud &c.; see<BR> औपधिक, the more correct form. उत्कोचकाश्चौपधिका वञ्चकाः कितवास्तथा Ms. 9. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उपहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed in or upon, deposited; Ś. 1; ˚मध्यमस्वर M. 1. 21 taken as a basis.<BR>—2 Preceded by.<BR>—3 Joined, mixed, connected with.<BR>—4 Possessed of; अर्थोपहितया वाचा मधुरं रघुनन्दनः (अब्रवीत्)<BR> Rām. 6. 128. 43; विनयोपहितः Śi. 16. 7.<BR>—5 Ready; deputed to act as a spy.<BR>—6 Given, bestowed.<BR>—7 Brought over, instigated to rebellion (उपजप्त); व्यक्तं त्वमप्युपहितः<BR> पाण्डवैः पापदेशज Mb. 8. 40. 46.<BR>—8 Somewhat good; Mb. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहितिः|उपहिति
उपहितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The putting or placing upon.<BR>—2 Devotedness to; Yv. Ts 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातुः|उपधातु
उपधातुः<BR>—1 An inferior metal, semi-metal. They are seven; सप्तोपधातवः स्वर्णं<BR> माक्षिकं तारमाक्षिकम् । तुत्थं कांस्यं च रीतिश्च^1 सिन्दूरं च शिलाजतु ॥<BR>—2 A secondary secretion of the body (six in number); <i>e. g.</i> milk,<BR> menses, adeps, sweat, teeth, hair, and lymph; स्तन्यं रजो वसा स्वेदो<BR> दन्ताः केशास्तथैव च । औजस्यं सप्तधातूनां कमात्सप्तोपधातवः ॥<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाव्
उपधाव्<BR>—1 U. 1 To run towards, approach hastily; येन साम्ना स्तोष्यन् स्यात् तत्सामोपधावेत्<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 3. 8.<BR>—2 To resort to; to have recourse to for assistance; तं भूतनिलयं<BR> देवं सुपर्णमुपधावत Bhāg. 8. 1. 11.<BR>—3 To run, glide (Ā.); Rv. 8. 3. 21.<BR>—4 To worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधावनः|उपधावन
उपधावनः A follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधावनम्
उपधावनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Going after, following.<BR>—2 Meditating upon.<BR>—3 Worship; Bhāg. 7. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिः|उपधि
उपधिः See under उपधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fumigated.<BR>—2 Being at the point of death;<BR>—3 Suffering extreme pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपितः|उपधूपित
उपधूपित + .{@-तः@} Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपिता
उपधूपित + .{@-ता, उपधूमिता@} The quarter of the heavens to which the sun is proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूमिता
उपधूपित + .{@-ता, उपधूमिता@} The quarter of the heavens to which the sun is proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृ
उपधृ €1. €10 P.<BR>—1 To hold up, support, sustain.<BR>—2 To bear, carry.<BR>—3 To hold as, consider or regard as; सत्त्वं तदुपधारयेत् Ms. 12. 27;<BR> एतद्योनीनि भूतानि सर्वाणीत्युपधारय Bg. 7. 6, 9. 6.<BR>—4 To comprehend, perceive, hear, experience, observe; पुरुषो रामचरितश्रवणैरुपधारयन् Bhāg.<BR>—5 To reflect or meditate upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधारणम्
उपधारणम्<BR>—1 Consideration, reflection.<BR>—2 Drawing, pulling (as by a hook).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृतिः|उपधृति
उपधृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 Holding up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
उपध्मा €1 P. To blow or breathe out; excite by blowing, fan; नाग्निं<BR> मुखेनोपधमेत् Ms. 4. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
उपध्मा<BR>—1 Blowing upon, breathing.<BR>—2 The effort of the voice which gives rise to the sound उपध्मानीय q. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानः|उपध्मान
उपध्मानः A lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानम्
उपध्मानः + .{@-नम्@} Blowing upon, breathing. (<i>a.</i>) पूतिरज्जुरुपध्मानी Av. 8. 8. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानिन्
उपध्मानिन् <i>a.</i> Blowing upon, fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानीयः|उपध्मानीय
उपध्मानीयः The aspirate Visarga before the letters प् and फ्;<BR> उपूपध्मानीयानामोष्टौ Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्वस्त
उपध्वस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Destroyed.<BR>—2 Mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनक्षत्रम्
उपनक्षत्रम् A subordinate constellation, secondary star (their number<BR> is said to be 729); सप्तविंशतिः सप्तविंशतिर्होपनक्षत्राण्येकैकं<BR> नक्षत्रमुपतिष्ठन्ते Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनखम्
उपनखम् A disease of the finger-nails, whitlow. (Mar. नखुरडें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनगरम्
उपनगरम् A suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनम्
उपनम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To come to, arrive at, approach, bend or tend towards.<BR>—2 To befall, fall to the lot of, occur, happen (used by itself or with<BR> gen., dat., or acc. of person); मत्संभोगः कथमुपनमेत् स्वप्नजोऽपि<BR> Me. 92; तत्तस्योपनमेत् Bh. 2. 121; अन्ध आत्मने नोपनमति Bhāg.;<BR> उपैनं सहस्रं नमति Ait. Br.<BR>—3 To share in. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To lead towards, introduce (with gen.).<BR>—2 To offer, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Come near, brought, arrived, approached, brought near to; Ś. 5. 19;<BR> R. 12. 102;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Got, obtained; अचिरोपनतां स मेदिनीम् R. 8. 7, 5. 52. चिन्तितोपनताम्<BR> K. 129; V. 3. 22; V. 2.<BR>—2 Presenting itself, fallen to the lot of, befallen, occurred; कस्यात्यन्तं<BR> सुखमुपनतं दुःखमेकान्ततो वा Me. 111; यदेवोपनतं दुःखात्सुखं<BR> तद्रसवत्तरम् V. 3. 21; अनुपनतमनोरथस्य 22, 4. 3; so सुहृदुपनतः<BR> Me. 102; Māl. 10; K. 33, 132, 348; सुख˚ that readily or without<BR> efforts presented itself Ś. 3; अकामोपनतम् R. 10. 39 unconsciously committed.<BR>—3 Formed, brought about, effected.<BR>—4 Presented to, offered, given; परलोकोपनतं जलाञ्जलिम् R. 8. 68.<BR>—5 Bent down, humbled, subjected, surrendered; दण्डोपनतचरितम्<BR> R. 17. 81, 8. 81; दण्डोपनतं शत्रुम् Mb.<BR>—6 Dependent on (for protection).<BR>—7 Approximate, near (in time or space.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनतिः|उपनति
उपनतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approach.<BR>—2 Bending, bow, salutation.<BR>—3 Inclination, affection; Vāj. 20. 13.<BR>—4 The falling to oneʼs share; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनम्र
उपनम्र <i>a.</i> Coming to, being present; N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामुक
उपनामुक <i>a.</i> Ved. Bending towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनह्
उपनह् €4 P.<BR>—1 To tie up, tie together.<BR>—2 To form into a bundle, bind together.<BR>—3 To inlay, set with; as चर्मोपनद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनद्ध
उपनद्ध <i>a.</i> Covered with, inlaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनहनम्
उपनहनम्<BR>—1 A cloth in which anything is bound up.<BR>—2 Binding, tying together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहः|उपनाह
उपनाहः<BR>—1 A bundle; देव्नां भाग उपनाहः Av. 9. 4. 5.<BR>—2 An unguent applied to a wound or sore, a plaster, poultice; शोफयोरुपनाहं<BR> कुर्यात् Suśr.<BR>—3 The tie of a lute, a peg to which the strings of a lyre are attached<BR> and by which they are tightened.<BR>—4 Inflammation of the ciliary glands, stye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहनम्
उपनाहनम्<BR>—1 Applying an unguent.<BR>—2 Anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनागरः|उपनागर
उपनागरः A particular Prākṛt dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनागरिका
उपनागरिका A variety of वृत्त्यनुप्रास. It is formed by sweet-sounding<BR> letters (माधुर्यव्यञ्जकवर्ण); <i>e. g.</i> cf. the example cited in<BR> K. P. 9; अपसारय घनसारं कुरु हारं दूर एव किं कमलैः । अलमलमालि<BR> मृणालैरिति वदति दिवानिशं बाला ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामन्
उपनामन् <i>n.</i> A surname, nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनासिकम्
उपनासिकम् The part which is near the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षिप्
उपनिक्षिप् €6 U.<BR>—1 To throw or place down विप्रान्तिके पितॄन् ध्यायन् शनकैरुपनिक्षिपेत् Ms. 3. 224.<BR>—2 To deposit = निक्षिप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेपः|उपनिक्षेप
उपनिक्षेपः<BR>—1 The act of depositing or placing down.<BR>—2 An open deposit, any article given in anotherʼs charge by letting him<BR> know its form, quantity &c. Y. 2. 25; (on which Mit. says:− उपनिक्षेपो<BR> नाम रूपसंख्याप्रदर्शनेन रक्षणार्थं परस्य हस्ते निहितं द्रव्यम्).<BR>—3 A deposit sealed or covered up (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधा
उपनिधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To put or place near; to bring or lead near to; कर्णयोरुपनिधाय<BR> (मुखम्) Āśval.; वहति समीरे मदनमुपनिधाय Gīt. 5.<BR>—2 To produce, cause; भयमुपनिदधे स राक्षसानाम् Bk. 4. 45.<BR>—3 To present; उद्दिष्टामुपनिहितां भजस्व पूजाम् Māl. 5. 25.<BR>—4 To deposit, entrust दृष्ट्वा पूर्वोपनिहितं निधिम् Ms. 8. 37, 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधातृ
उपनिधातृ, -धायक <i>a.</i><BR> Depositing, placing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधायक
उपनिधातृ, -धायक <i>a.</i><BR> Depositing, placing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधानम्
उपनिधानम्<BR>—1 Placing near.<BR>—2 Depositing, entrusting to oneʼs care.<BR>—3 A deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधिः|उपनिधि
उपनिधिः<BR>—1 A deposit, pledge, property entrusted to another. प्रादायोपनिधिं<BR> राजा पाण्डुः स्वर्गमितो गतः Mb. 1. 126. 3.<BR>—2 (In law) A sealed deposit; Y. 2. 25; आधिश्चोपनिधिश्चोभौ न कालात्ययमर्हतः<BR> Ms. 8. 145, 149; cf. Medhātithi:− यत् प्रदर्शितरूपं सचिह्नवस्त्रादिना<BR> पिहितं निक्षिप्यते; also cf. Y. 2. 65 and Nārada quoted in Mit.<BR>—3 Pretext, guise; उपनिधिभिरसुखकृत्स परमनिरयगो भृशमसुखमनुभवति<BR> दुष्कृतकर्मा Mb. 12. 321. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिहित
उपनिहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deposited with. प्रीत्योपनिहितस्य (धनस्य) Ms. 8. 196.<BR>—2 Placed near to; ये म इम उपनिहिता इति Ch. Up. 1. 10. 2.<BR>—3 Presented, offered, Māl. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपत्
उपनिपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly down to.<BR>—2 To take place in addition.<BR>—3 To be stated incidentally or casually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपातः|उपनिपात
उपनिपातः<BR>—1 Approaching, coming near.<BR>—2 A sudden and unexpected attack or occurrence. उपनिपातप्रतीकारः Kau. A. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपातिन्
उपनिपातिन् <i>a.</i> Coming (unexpectedly); रन्ध्रोपनिपातिनोऽनर्थाः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिबन्ध्
उपनिबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To compose, write;<BR>—2 To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिबद्ध
उपनिबद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Written, composed.<BR>—2 Discussed. किंचिदुपनिबद्ध U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिबन्धनम्
उपनिबन्धनम्<BR>—1 A means of accomplishment.<BR>—2 Binding.<BR>—3 Description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिमन्त्रणम्
उपनिमन्त्रणम् Invitation, inauguration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिम्रेड्
उपनिम्रेड् €1 P., Ā. To make happy, gladden; साधवो घोषाआ च गच्छेयुरुप<BR> च निम्रेडेरन् Ch. Up. 3. 19. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिर्गमः|उपनिर्गम
उपनिर्गमः A main or royal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिर्गमनम्
उपनिर्गमनम् A way to go out; Hc. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिर्हारः
उपनिर्हारः An attack, assault; नेदानीमुपनिर्हारं रावणो दातुमर्हति<BR> Rām. 6. 75. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवपनम्
उपनिवपनम् The act of scattering or pouring down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिविष्ट
उपनिविष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Besieging.<BR>—2 Occupying, inhabiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशः|उपनिवेश
उपनिवेशः A suburb; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशित
उपनिवेशित <i>a.</i> Placed, established, colonized; स्वर्गाभिष्यन्दवमनं<BR> कृत्वेवोपनिवेशितम् Ku. 6. 37; R. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशिन्
उपनिवेशिन् <i>a.</i> Attached to, inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद्
उपनिषद् <i>f.</i> [said to be from उपनि-सद् ‘knowledge derived from sitting at the feet of the preceptor’<BR>; but, according to Indian authorities,<BR> it means ‘to destroy ignorance by revealing the knowledge of the Supreme Spirit and cutting off the bonds of worldly existence’<BR>; यथा य इमां<BR> ब्रह्मविद्यामुपयन्त्यात्मभावेन श्रद्धाभक्तिपुरःसराः सन्तस्तेषां गर्भजन्मजरारोगाद्यनर्थपूगं<BR> निशातयति परं वा ब्रह्म गमयति अविद्यादिसंसारकारणं चात्यन्तमवसादयति<BR> विनाशयतीत्युपनिषद् । उपनिपूर्वस्य सदेरेवमर्थस्मरणात्; Śaṅkara.]<BR>—1 N. of certain mystical writings attached to the Brāhmaṇas, the chief<BR> aim of which is to ascertain the secret meaning of the Vedas; Bv. 2. 40;<BR> Māl. 1. 7; [other etymologies also are given to explain the name:− (1)<BR> उपनीय तमात्मानं ब्रह्मापास्तद्वयं यतः । निहन्त्यविद्यां तज्जं च<BR> तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत् ॥ or (2) निहत्यानर्थमूलं स्वाविद्यां प्रत्यक्तया<BR> परम् । नयत्यपास्तसंभेदमतो वोपनिषद्भवेत् ॥ or (3) प्रवृत्तिहेतून्निःशेषांस्तन्मूलोच्छेदकत्वतः ।<BR> यतोवसादयेद्विद्या तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत् ॥ In the मुक्तकोपनिषद् 108<BR> Upaniṣads are mentioned, but some more have been added to this number.<BR> They are said to have been the source of the six Darśanas or systems<BR> of philosophy, particularly of the Vedānta Philosophy. The more important<BR> Upaniṣads are:− ईशकेनकठप्रश्नमुण्डमाण्डूक्यतित्तिरः । ऐतरेयं च<BR> छान्दोग्यं बृहदारण्यकं तथा ॥].<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) An esoteric or secret doctrine, mystical meaning, words of mystery;<BR> साङ्गोपाङ्गोपनिषदः सरहस्यः प्रदीयताम् Rām. 1. 55. 16.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Mystical knowledge or instruction; मन्त्रपारायण˚ U. 6;<BR> दिव्यामस्त्रोपनिषदमृषेर्यः कृशाश्वस्य शिष्यात् Mv. 2. 2.<BR>—3 True knowledge regarding the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—4 Sacred or religious lore.<BR>—5 Secrecy, seclusion.<BR>—6 A neighbouring mansion.<BR>—7 A lonely place.<BR>—8 A religious observance.<BR>—9 Meditation, यदेव विद्यया करोति श्रद्धयोपनिषदा तदेव वीर्यवत्तरं<BR> भवति Ch. Up. 1. 1. 10<BR>—10 One that takes to (like a boat); तस्योपनिषत्सत्यस्य सत्यमिति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषादिन्
उपनिषादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sitting at the feet (of another, such as a preceptor).<BR>—2 Subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषेव्
उपनिषेव् Ā. To devote oneʼs self to; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्करः|उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं
उपनिष्करः A street, a principal road, highway. (about 40 cubit width).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमणम्
उपनिष्क्रमणम्<BR>—1 Going out, issuing.<BR>—2 One of the Saṃskāras or religious rites, <i>i. e.</i> taking out a child<BR> for the first time into the open air (which is usually performed in the<BR> fourth month of its age); cf. चतुर्थे मासि कर्तव्यं शिशोर्निष्क्रमणं<BR> गृहात् Ms. 2. 34.<BR>—3 A main or royal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनी
उपनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To bring near, fetch; उपनयति मुनिकुमारकेभ्यः फलानि K. 45, 62;<BR> विधिनैवोपनीतस्त्वम् Mk. 7. 6; अन्नम् Ms. 3. 225; M. 2. 5; Y. 3. 122;<BR> तेन ह्युपनय शरम् V. 5; R. 10. 52; Ku. 7. 72.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To offer, present to; हरये स्वदेहमुपानयत् R. 2. 59; Bk. 6. 70;<BR> Ku. 3. 65; आर्यस्यासनमुपनय Mk. 9; M. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To hand over, give over; अन्तःपुरपरिचारिकामध्यमुपनीता<BR> K. 101; Māl. 1; Ś. 1; U. 2; अचिरोपनीता वः शिष्या M. 1 recently<BR> made over (for instruction).<BR>—3 To bring to, subject, expose or put to; आत्मा क्लेशस्य पदमुपनीतः<BR> Ś. 1; R. 13. 39; K. 173.<BR>—4 To bring about, cause, produce, accomplish; उपनयन्नर्थान् Pt. 3. 180;<BR> उपनयन्नङ्गैरनङ्गोत्सवम् Gīt. 1; K. 171.<BR>—5 To bring information, communicate.<BR>—6 To bring into any state, lead or reduce to; अयोऽभेद्यमुपायेन द्रवतामुपनीयते Kām. 11. 47.<BR>—7 To take into oneʼs possession, lead away, lead; K. 169.<BR>—8 To bring near to oneself, <i>i. e.</i> invest with the sacred thread (Ātm.<BR> P. I. 3. 36); उप त्वा नेष्ये Ch. Up. 4. 4. 5. क्षात्रेण कल्पेनोपनीय<BR> U. 2; माणवकमुपनयते Sk.; R. 3. 29; Bk. 1. 15; Ms. 2. 49, 69, 140.<BR>—9 To hire, employ as hired servants; कर्मकरानुपनयते Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To cause (a master) to receive (a pupil), cause to invest with the sacred<BR> thread. तांश्चारयित्वा त्रीन्कृच्छ्रान् यथाविध्युपनाययेत् Ms. 11. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयः|उपनय
उपनयः<BR>—1 Bringing near, fetching.<BR>—2 Gaining, attaining, procuring. नान्यं तवाङ्घ्रपुपनयादपवर्गमूर्तेः<BR> क्षेमं जनस्य परितो भिय ईश विद्मः Bhāg. 12. 8. 43.<BR>—3 Employing<BR>—4 Investiture with the sacred thread, initiation into sacred study, handing<BR> a youth of the first three castes to a teacher; गृह्योक्तकर्मणा येन<BR> समीपं नीयते गुरोः । बालो वेदाय तद्योगात् बालस्योपनयं विदुः ॥<BR> [By this ceremony spiritual birth is conferred upon the youth, and he becomes<BR> a द्विजन्मन्; the ages at which the ceremony may be performed by the<BR> three castes are respectively 8-16, 11-22 and 12-24; (see Ms. 2. 36-38;<BR> of what materials &c. the cords should be, is mentioned in 2. 41-46)].<BR>—5 The fourth member of the five-membered Indian syllogism (in logic),<BR> the application to the special case in question; व्याप्तिविशिष्टस्य हेतोः<BR> पक्षधर्मताप्रतिपादकं वचनमुपनयः Tarka K.<BR>—6 Introduction, initiation (into any science); see next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयनम्
उपनयनम्<BR>—1 Leading to or near.<BR>—2 Presenting, offering; धारासारोपनयनपरा नैगमाः सानुमन्तः V. 4. 13.<BR>—3 Investiture with the sacred thread; गर्भाष्टमे ब्राह्मण उपनेय इत्युपनयनं<BR> संस्कारार्थम् Mbh. 6. 6. 84. आसमावर्तनात्कुर्यात् कृतोपनयनो द्विजः<BR> Ms. 2. 108, 173.<BR>—4 Employment, application.<BR>—5 Introduction (into any science).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायः|उपनाय
उपनायः, -नायनम्<BR> = उपनय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायनम्
उपनायः, -नायनम्<BR> = उपनय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायक|उपनायकः
उपनायक <i>a.</i> Leading to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायकः|उपनायक
उपनायक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 (उप गौणो नायकः) A character in a dramatic or any other work<BR> of art next in importance to the hero; (नायकस्य गुणोत्कर्षकथका उपनायकाः);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> Lakṣmaṇa in Rāmāyaṅa; Makaranda in Mālatimādhava &c. &c.<BR>—2 A paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायिका
उपनायिका A character in a dramatic or any other work of art next<BR> in importance to the heroine; <i>e. g.</i> Madayantikā in Mālatimādhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीत|उपनीतः
उपनीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Brought near.<BR>—2 Known.<BR>—3 Obtained, attained.<BR>—4 Presented, given.<BR>—5 Adduced.<BR>—6 Married (?), led to a man; भीमा जाया ब्राह्मणस्योपनीता Rv. 10. 109. 4.<BR>—7 Initiated; भवत्पूर्वं चरेद्भैक्षमुपनीतो द्विजोत्तमः Ms. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीतः|उपनीत
उपनीत + .{@-तः@} A youth led to the teacher and invested with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीतिः|उपनीति
उपनीतिः <i>f.</i> see उपनयन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतव्य
उपनेतव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be brought near; एष स चिरदृष्टः कथमुपनेतव्यः M. 2. 4.<BR>—2 To be employed or observed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृ
उपनेतृ <i>a.</i> One who leads or brings near, fetching; नियमविधिजलानां<BR> बर्हिषां चोपनेत्री Ku. 1. 60; मालत्यभिज्ञानस्योपनेत्री Māl. 9. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृता
उपनेतृ + .({@-ता@}) A preceptor who performs the उपनयन ceremony, an<BR> <i>Acārya</i>; जनिता चोपनेता च यस्तु विद्यां प्रयच्छति । अन्नदाता भयत्राता<BR> पञ्चैते पितरः स्मृताः ॥ Pt. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनुन्न
उपनुन्न <i>a.</i> Driven, wafted; द्रुतमरुदुपनुन्नैरुन्नमद्भिः सहेलम् Śi. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनृत्
उपनृत् €4 P. To dance before somebody; dance with insulting gestures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनृत्यम्
उपनृत्यम् A place for dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेत्रम्
उपनेत्रम् Spectacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्
उपन्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To lay upon, place or put down, put near, place before.<BR>—2 To entrust any one with, commit to the care of.<BR>—3 To explain, describe minutely.<BR>—4 To propose, suggest, hint, point out, state; मयोपन्यस्तेषु मन्त्रेषु<BR> H. 3; इत्युभयलोकाविरुद्धं वचनमुपन्यस्तं Māl. 2 spoken; सदुपन्यस्यति<BR> कृत्यवर्त्म यः Ki. 2. 3 tells or points out; किमिदमपन्यस्तम्<BR> Ś. 5 what is this that is proposed or said.<BR>—5 To prove, establish argumentatively; भूतमप्यनुपन्यस्तं हीयते<BR> व्यवहारतः Y. 2. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्त
उपन्यस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed near, deposited.<BR>—2 Said, proposed, spoken.<BR>—3 Pledged, entrusted.<BR>—4 Given, communicated; पितामहेनोपन्यस्तम् (आसनम्) Bhāg. 1. 17. 43.<BR>—5 Brought forward as an example, adduced, hinted.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">Page0452-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्तम्
उपन्यस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} The holding of hands to the chest (a skilful move in fighting);<BR> उपन्यस्तमपन्यस्तं युद्धमार्गं विशारदौ । तौ विचेरतुरन्योन्यं वानरेन्द्रश्च<BR> रावणः ॥ Rām. 6. 40. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यासः|उपन्यास
उपन्यासः<BR>—1 Placing near to, juxta-position.<BR>—2 A deposit, pledge.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Statement, suggestion, proposal; विषम उपन्यासः Mbh. on 1. 1. 1, 1. 1. 21, 46<BR> etc. = This is a misstatement (a favourite remark<BR> of the महाभाष्यकार). पावकः खलु एष वचनोपन्यासः Ś. 5; Māl. 1, 3, 8.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Preface, introduction; निर्यातः शनकैरलीकवचनोपन्यासमालीजनः<BR> Amaru. 27; चतुरो मधुरश्चायमुपन्यासः Ak.; so शम˚ Ve. 5 overtures of peace.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Allusion, reference, hinting at; आत्मन उपन्यासपूर्वम् Ś. 3;<BR> M. 4; S. D. 363.<BR>—4 A precept, law.<BR>—5 A kind of peace; आत्मकार्यस्य सिद्धिं तु समुद्दिश्य क्रियेत यः ।<BR> स उपन्यासकुशलैरुपन्यास उदाहृतः H. 4. 114.<BR>—6 Propitiating (प्रसादनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपक्षः|उपपक्ष
उपपक्षः Ved. The shoulder, arm-pit or the hair under the arm-pit; T. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपक्ष्य
उपपक्ष्य <i>a.</i> Near the shoulder, being on the shoulder; या उपपक्ष्याः<BR> (स्वयं स्रसः) Av. 7. 76. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपतिः|उपपति
उपपतिः [उपमितः पत्या, उप गौणः पतिः] A paramour; उपपतिरिव<BR> नीचैः पश्चिमान्तेन चन्द्रः Śi. 11. 65, 15. 63; Ms. 3. 155, 4. 216, 217;<BR> Vāj. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपतित
उपपतित <i>a.</i> One guilty of an उपपातक <i>i. e.</i> a minor<BR> sin (Dānasāgara, Bibliotheca Indica 274, Fascicule I, P. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपथम्
उपपथम् <i>ind.</i> Near the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपद्
उपपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To reach, come to, approach, go near; यमुनातटमुपपेदे Pt. 1;<BR> उपपद्यख स्वकर्मोचितां गतिम् Dk. 93.<BR>—2 To be got or obtained, fall to oneʼs share; त्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य<BR> छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते Bg. 6. 39, 13. 18.<BR>—3 To take place, occur, happen, be produced; देवि एवमुपपद्यते<BR> M. 1 even as you say, just so; अर्थास्तस्योपपत्स्यन्ते Mb.; उपपन्ना<BR> हि दारेषु प्रभुता सर्वतोमुखी Ś. 5. 26.<BR>—4 To be possible; कर्तव्यं वो न पश्यामि स्याच्चेत्किं नोपपद्यते<BR> Ku. 6. 61; Ms. 9. 121, 40, 10. 102; नेश्वरो जगतः कारणमुपपद्यते Ś. B.<BR>—5 To be suitable, be fit for, be adequate for, fit, suit (with loc.);<BR> क्लैब्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते Bg. 2. 3, 18. 7; उपपद्यते<BR> it is fit; ते गुणाः परस्मिन् ब्रह्मण्युपपद्यन्ते Ś. B.<BR>—6 To go against, attack.<BR>—7 To put in a word or statement; इति ह विश्वामित्र उपपपाद Ait. Br.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bring into any state, cause to arrive or be obtained; विश्वासमुपपादिता<BR> Rām. inspired with confidence; get ready; रथमुपपादय Ve. 2.<BR>—2 To offer, present any one with (acc.), bring to; दिष्टपा त्वमसि<BR> मे धात्रा भीतेनेवोपपादितः R. 15. 18, 14. 8, 16. 32; Ms. 9. 72, 73, 3. 96;<BR> sometimes with dat.; सर्वस्वं वेदविदुषे ब्राह्मणायोपपादयेत्<BR> Ms. 11. 76, 9. 244; or with loc.; अक्षयोऽयं निधी राज्ञां यद्विप्रेषूपपादितम् Y. 1. 315.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To cause to happen or occur, bring about; मरणमुपपादयेत् K. 36.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To accomplish, effect, cause, do, perform; यावत्तु मानुष्यके<BR> शक्यमुपपादयितुम् K. 62, 113, 120, 134; देवकार्यम् R. 11. 91, 17. 55; Me. 29.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To make a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">Page0453-1</a>]<BR> statement, adduce, put forward.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To justify.<BR>—5 To make good, establish, prove; कथमीश्वरं विनाशधर्मिणमुपपादयसि Prab.<BR>—6 To pronounce, declare.<BR>—7 To make fit or adequate for; कालोपपादिते क्षेत्रे Ms. 9. 36.<BR>—8 To furnish with, endow with; Kām. 11. 57; K. 2; आत्मानं प्रथमं<BR> राजा विनयेनोपपादयेत् Subhāṣ.<BR>—9 To find out, ascertain; दक्षिणाप्रवणं चैव प्रयत्नेनोपपादयेत् Ms. 3. 206.<BR>—10 To examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिः|उपपत्ति
उपपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Happening, occurring, becoming visible, appearance, production, birth;<BR> अथोपपत्तिं छलनापरोऽपराम् Śi. 1. 69 (जन्म); इष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु Bg. 13. 9.<BR>—2 Cause, reason, ground; प्रियेषु यैः पार्थ विनोपपत्तेः Ki. 3. 52.<BR>—3 Reasoning, argument; उपपत्तिमदूर्जितं वचः Ki. 2. 1; देवि<BR> सोपपत्तिकमभिहितम् । Nāg. 5 argumentative; giving a reason for the<BR> establishment of a matter; S. D. 482.<BR>—4 Fitness, propriety.<BR>—5 Termination, end.<BR>—6 Association, connection.<BR>—7 Acceptance, adoption; Mv. 5.<BR>—8 Ascertainment, demonstration, demonstrated conclusion; उपपत्तिरुदाहृता<BR> बलात् Ki. 2. 28.<BR>—9 (In Arith. or Geom.) Proof, demonstration.<BR>—10 A means, an expedient.<BR>—11 Assistance, support, help; ततः प्रजह्ने सममेव तत्र तैरपेक्षितान्योन्यबलोपपत्तिभिः Ki. 14. 44.<BR>—12 Doing, effecting, gaining; accomplishment; स्वार्थोपपत्तिं दुर्बलाशः<BR> R. 5. 12; तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः Bhāṣā P.; H. 3. 111; see अनुपपत्ति.<BR>—13 Attainment, getting; असंशयं प्राक् तनयोपपत्तेः R. 14. 78; Ki. 3. 1.<BR>—14 Religious abstraction (समाधि).<BR>—15 Accident, chance; उपपत्त्योपलब्धेषु लोकेषु च समो भव Mb. 12. 288. 11.<BR>—16 Suitability, expediency; उपपत्तिमदूर्जिताश्रयं नृपमूचे<BR> वचनं वृकोदरः Ki. 2. 1; Bhāg. 4. 28. 68.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपपत्तिसमः, उपपत्तिपरित्यक्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिसमः|उपपत्तिसम
उपपत्तिः + -समः (in logic) a kind of contradiction in which both the contradictory<BR> assertions are supposed to be demonstrable (<i>e. g.</i> sound is eternal<BR> because it is produced; it is eternal because it is not tangible). Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिपरित्यक्त
उपपत्तिः + -परित्यक्त <i>a.</i> Unproved, unreasonable, destitute of argument<BR> or proof; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्न
उपपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obtained; secured; अतीन्द्रियेष्वप्युपपन्नदर्शनः R. 3. 41; V. 5. 15;<BR> R. 1. 60.<BR>—2 Accompanied or attended by, in company with; श्रद्धेव साक्षाद्विधिनोपपन्ना R. 2. 16, 22.<BR>—3 Coming, presenting itself; कुमारी अपूर्वपतिः पतिमुपपन्ना कौमारी<BR> भार्या Mbh. 4. 2. 13. उपपन्नाश्च सन्ध्ये द्वे व्याहरन्त्यशिवं शिवाः<BR> Rām. 6. 10. 20<BR>—4 Right, fit, proper, suitable (with gen. or loc.); उपपन्नस्ते तर्कः<BR> V. 2; उपपन्नमिदं विशेषणं वायोः <i>ibid.</i> this epithet befits the<BR> wind; उपपन्नमेतदस्मिन् राजनि Ś. 2.<BR>—5 Possible; उभयमप्यनुपपन्नम् V. 2; Ku. 3. 12.<BR>—6 Full of, endowed with, possessed of, furnished with; उपपन्नो गुणैरिष्टैः<BR> N. 1. 1; Ms. 9. 141, 244; तल्लक्षणोपपन्नः Ś. 5.<BR>—7 Demonstrated, proved.<BR>—8 Offered, presented.<BR>—9 Cured.<BR>—10 Allowed, agreed (संमत); कामकारो महाप्राज्ञ गुरूणां सर्वदानघ ।<BR> उपपन्नेषु दारेषु पुत्रेषु च विधीयते ॥ Rām. 2. 101. 18.<BR>—11 One who has approached a teacher (as a pupil), approached for protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादक
उपपादक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Producing, effecting.<BR>—2 Well reasoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादनम्
उपपादनम्<BR>—1 Effecting, accomplishing, doing. सामान्यतः किं विषयोपपादनैः.<BR>—2 Giving, delivering, presenting.<BR>—3 Proving, demonstration, establishing by arguments; अपि त्वां न लभेत्<BR> कर्ण राज्यलम्भोपपादनम् Mb. 5. 142. 2.<BR>—4 Examination, ascertainment, exposition (of a subject).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपाद्य
उपपाद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be effected or done.<BR>—2 To be proved or shown.<BR>—3 Coming into existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक <i>a.</i> Self-produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुकः|उपपादुक
उपपादुक + .{@-कः@} A superhuman being, God; दिव्योपपादुका देवाः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपदम्
उपपदम्<BR>—1 A word prefixed or previously uttered; धनुरुपपदं वेदम् Ki. 18. 44<BR> (धनुर्वेदम्); तस्याः स राजोपपदं निशान्तम् R. 16. 40.<BR>—2 A title, a degree; epithet of respect, such as आर्य, शर्मन्; कथं<BR> निरुपपदमेव चाणक्यमिति न आर्यचाणक्यमिति Mu. 3.<BR>—3 A secondary word of a sentence, a preposition, particle &c. prefixed<BR> to a verb or a noun derived from a verb which determines or qualifies<BR> the sense of the verb; उपपदमतिड् P. II. 2. 19; (see Sk. thereon).<BR> ˚तत्पुरुषः a kind of Tat. comp. in which the last member is some<BR> form of a verbal character; <i>e. g.</i> वेदविद्, ग्रामणी, आकर्णलम्बिन् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षा
उपपरीक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR> Investigation, examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षणम्
उपपरीक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR> Investigation, examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्चन
उपपर्चन, उपपृच् <i>a.</i> Closely touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपृच्
उपपर्चन, उपपृच् <i>a.</i> Closely touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्चनम्
उपपर्चन, उपपृच् + .{@-नम्@} Impregnation or admixture (Ved.). उपेदमुपपर्चनमासु<BR> गोषूप पृच्यताम् Rv. 6. 28. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्वन्
उपपर्वन् <i>n.</i> The day before the Parvan or change of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्शुका
उपपर्शुका false ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातः|उपपात
उपपातः<BR>—1 An unexpected occurrence.<BR>—2 A calamity, misfortune, accident. उपपातो हि आर्तिसम्बद्धं द्रव्यम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 23.<BR>—3 Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकम्
उपपातकम् A minor sin, crime or sin of the second degree; महापातकतुल्यानि<BR> पापान्युक्तानि यानि तु । तानि पातकसंज्ञानि तन्न्यूनमुपपातकम् ॥ Y. 2. 210;<BR> Ms. 11. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकिन्
उपपातकिन् <i>a.</i> One who has committed an उपपातक. उपपातकिनस्त्वेवमेभिर्नानाविधैर्व्रतैः<BR> Ms. 11. 107, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादः|उपपाद
उपपादः The upper or dwarf pillar subordinate to a larger column.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक <i>a.</i> Having shoes, shod (as a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपापम्
उपपापम् = उपपातकम् q. v. Y. 3. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपार्श्वः|उपपार्श्व|उपपार्श्वं
उपपार्श्वः, -र्श्वम्<BR>—1 A shoulder.<BR>—2 A flank, side,<BR>—3 The opposite side.<BR>—4 The lesser ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपार्श्वम्
उपपार्श्वः, -र्श्वम्<BR>—1 A shoulder.<BR>—2 A flank, side,<BR>—3 The opposite side.<BR>—4 The lesser ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीड्
उपपीड् €10 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To press down or against, hurt, injure, pain; स्तनोपपीडं<BR> परिरब्धुकामा Ki. 3. 54, 8. 16; Śi. 10. 47; पार्श्वोपपीडम्, पार्श्वयोरुपपीडम्,<BR> पार्श्वभ्यामुपपीडम् Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To oppress, devastate, lay waste; क्षुत्तृष्णोपपीडित troubled;<BR> Ms. 8. 67, 7. 195; Kām. 8. 72.<BR>—2 To eclipse,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडनम्
उपपीडनम्<BR>—1 Pressing down, devastating, laying waste.<BR>—2 Inflicting pain, injuring; व्याधिभिश्चोपपीडनम् Ms. 6. 62, 12. 80.<BR>—3 Pain, agony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुरम्
उपपुरम् A suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुरी
उपपुरम् + .{@-री@} The environs of a city; इमामुपपुरीं भीरु किं चिकीर्षसि<BR> शंस मे Bhāg. 4. 25. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपौरिक
उपपौरिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to a suburb, suburban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुराणम्
उपपुराणम् A secondary or minor Purāṇa (for an enumeration of their<BR> names, see under अष्टादशन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुष्पिका
उपपुष्पिका Yawning, gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपौर्णमासि
उपपौर्णमासि, -मासम् <i>ind.</i><BR> just preceding or at the time of the full-moon day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपौर्णमासम्
उपपौर्णमासि, -मासम् <i>ind.</i><BR> just preceding or at the time of the full-moon day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदर्शनम्
उपप्रदर्शनम् Pointing out, indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदानम्
उपप्रदानम्<BR>—1 Delivering over, entrusting.<BR>—2 A bribe, present; Rām. 6. 13. 7. उपप्रदानैर्मार्जारो हितकृत्प्रार्थ्यते<BR> जनैः Pt. 1. 95.<BR>—3 A tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रलोभनम्
उपप्रलोभनम्<BR>—1 Seducing, alluring.<BR>—2 A bribe, an inducement, allurement; उच्चावचान्युपप्रलोभनानि Dk. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्राणः|उपप्राण
उपप्राणः A secondary life-wind (belonging to the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रेक्ष्
उपप्रेक्ष् = उपेक्ष्. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रेक्षणम्
उपप्रेक्षणम् Overlooking, disregarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रैषः|उपप्रैष
उपप्रैषः Invitation, summons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लु
उपप्लु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To float, swim; यदुपप्लवते तल्लघु Sk.<BR>—2 To overwhelm, cover with; उपप्लुतमघौघेन Rām.<BR>—3 To assault violently, assail; to trouble, oppress, distress; पौलस्त्योपप्लुता<BR> हरिम् R. 10. 5, 14. 64; Ms. 4. 118.<BR>—4 To jump or spring upon.<BR>—5 To depart from. ━<i>Caus.</i> To water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लवः|उपप्लव
उपप्लवः<BR>—1 Misfortune, evil, calamity, distress, adversity; अथ मदनवधूरुपप्लवान्तं …<BR> परिपालयाम्बभूव Ku. 4. 46; जीवन्पुनः शश्वदुपप्लवेभ्यः<BR> प्रजाः वासि R. 2. 48;<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) An unlucky accident, injury, trouble; कच्चिन्न वाय्वादिरुपप्लवो<BR> वः R. 5. 6; Me. 17.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) An obstacle, impediment; तौ (अर्थकामौ) हि तत्त्वावबोधस्य<BR> दुरुच्छेदावुपप्लवौ Ki. 11. 20.<BR>—3 Oppression, harassing, troubling; उपप्लवाय लोकानां धूमकेतुरिवोत्थितः Ku. 2. 32.<BR>—4 Danger, fear; see उपप्लविन् below.<BR>—5 Agitation, perturbation; इन्द्रिय˚ K. 146.<BR>—6 A portent or natural phenomenon foreboding evil.<BR>—7 Particularly, an eclipse of the sun or moon; चन्द्रमिवोपप्लवान्मुक्तम् V. 1. 11.<BR>—8 N. of Rāhu, the ascending node, केतूपप्लवभौममन्दगतयः षष्ठे<BR> तृतीये शुभाः.<BR>—9 Anarchy.<BR>—10 N. of Śiva.<BR>—11 Doubt, scepticism (with Buddhists).<BR>—12 Loss, absence; मायया विभ्रमच्चित्तो न वेद स्मृत्युपप्लवात् Bhāg. 10. 84. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लविन्
उपप्लविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who has suffered a calamity, distressed, troubled; K. 208.<BR>—2 Suffering oppression; तृपा इवोपप्लविनः परेभ्यः R. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लव्यम्
उपप्लव्यम् N. of the capital of the Matsyas; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लुत
उपप्लुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Violently attacked, beset, distressed, pained &c.<BR>—2 Harassed (by Rāhu), eclipsed.<BR>—3 Marked by prodigies.<BR>—4 Moistened, watered; {@˚अक्ष, -नयन@} weeping; कामानुजेन सहसा<BR> त उपप्लुताक्षाः Bhāg. 3. 15. 31.<BR>—5 Pressed, squeezed; उपप्लुतास्तत्क्षणशोचनीयतां च्युताधिकाराः सचिवा<BR> इवाययुः Ki. 8. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लुता
उपप्लुत + .{@-ता@} Morbid sensibility of the uterus, a particular disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबन्धः|उपबन्ध|उपबंध|उपबंधः
उपबन्धः<BR>—1 Connection.<BR>—2 An affix.<BR>—3 A particular mode of sexual enjoyment; C. P. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबर्हः|उपबर्ह
उपबर्हः, -र्हणम्<BR>—1 A pillow; चित्तिरा उपबर्हणम् Rv. 10. 85. 7.<BR>—2 Pressing down, oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबर्हणम्
उपबर्हः, -र्हणम्<BR>—1 A pillow; चित्तिरा उपबर्हणम् Rv. 10. 85. 7.<BR>—2 Pressing down, oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबृंहणम्
उपबृंहणम् Increase; A. Rām. 7. 6. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबृंहित
उपबृंहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Increased, magnified; य एतत्पुण्यमाख्यानं विष्णोर्वीर्योपबृंहितम्<BR> (कीर्तयेत्) Bhāg. 7. 10. 46; K. 27, 136; Dk. 42.<BR>—2 Accompanied by; तस्य त्रैकालिकी बुद्धिर्जन्ममृत्यूपबृंहिता Bhāg. 11. 15. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबृंहिन्
उपबृंहिन् <i>a.</i> Supplementary, additional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबहु
उपबहु <i>a.</i> A few, a tolerable number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबाहुः|उपबाहु
उपबाहुः The lower arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपब्दः|उपब्द
उपब्दः, -ब्दि<BR> Sound produced at the sprinkling of Soma; noise, sound in<BR> general; ग्रावाणो ध्नन्तु रक्षस उपब्दैः Rv. 7. 104. 17 (= Av. 8. 4. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपब्दि|उपब्दिः
उपब्दः, -ब्दि<BR> Sound produced at the sprinkling of Soma; noise, sound in<BR> general; ग्रावाणो ध्नन्तु रक्षस उपब्दैः Rv. 7. 104. 17 (= Av. 8. 4. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्बिः
उपब्दः, -ब्दि + .{@-उपद्बिः@} <i>m.</i> A particular venomous animal; उपब्दे पुनर्वो<BR> यन्तु Av. 2. 24. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभङ्गः|उपभङ्ग|उपभंग|उपभंगः
उपभङ्गः<BR>—1 Fleeing away, retreat.<BR>—2 A division (of a verse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभाषा
उपभाषा A secondary dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुज्
उपभुज् €7 U.<BR>—1 To enjoy, taste (in all senses); तपसामुपभुञ्जानाः फलानि Ku. 6. 10;<BR> नोपभुज्यते is not enjoyed, Pt. 2. 142; Ms. 12. 8.<BR>—2 To eat, drink; पयः R. 2. 65, 1. 67; Bk. 8. 40; अर्धोपभुक्तेन<BR> Ku. 3. 37; Y. 3. 325.<BR>—3 To possess; स्त्रीरत्नमुपभुङ्क्ष्व Hariv.<BR>—4 To use, make use of, receive; मानसं मनसैवायमुपभुङ्क्ते शुभाशुभम् Ms. 12. 8.<BR>—5 To be useful; उप वयं तं भुञ्जामः Ch. Up. 4. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुक्तिः|उपभुक्ति
उपभुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Enjoyment, use.<BR>—2 (in astr.) The daily course of a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोक्तृ
उपभोक्तृ <i>a.</i> Enjoying, an enjoyer; Possessing, Possessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोगः|उपभोग
उपभोगः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Enjoyment, eating, tasting; न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन<BR> शाम्यति Ms. 2. 94, 8. 285; Y. 2. 171. कामोपभोगपरमाः Bg. 16. 11;<BR> प्रियोपभोग R. 12. 22.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Use, application; चरणोपभोगसुलभः Ś. 4. 4.<BR>—2 Enjoyment (of a woman), cohabitation; उपस्थितश्चारु वपुस्तदीयं<BR> कृत्वोपभोगोत्सुकयेव लक्ष्म्या R. 14. 24.<BR>—3 Usufruct.<BR>—4 Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोगिन्
उपभोगिन् <i>a.</i> Enjoying, using.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग्य
उपभोग्य, -भोक्तव्य, -भोज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be enjoyed, used or eaten; असूत<BR> सा नागवधूपभोग्यम् Ku. 1. 20;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">Page0455-1</a>]<BR> किंचित्कालोपभोग्यानि यौवनानि धनानि च Pt. 2. 117; अस्माकमुपभोग्यो<BR> भविष्यति Pt. 1 will become our prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोक्तव्य
उपभोग्य, -भोक्तव्य, -भोज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be enjoyed, used or eaten; असूत<BR> सा नागवधूपभोग्यम् Ku. 1. 20;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">Page0455-1</a>]<BR> किंचित्कालोपभोग्यानि यौवनानि धनानि च Pt. 2. 117; अस्माकमुपभोग्यो<BR> भविष्यति Pt. 1 will become our prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोज्य
उपभोग्य, -भोक्तव्य, -भोज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR> To be enjoyed, used or eaten; असूत<BR> सा नागवधूपभोग्यम् Ku. 1. 20;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">Page0455-1</a>]<BR> किंचित्कालोपभोग्यानि यौवनानि धनानि च Pt. 2. 117; अस्माकमुपभोग्यो<BR> भविष्यति Pt. 1 will become our prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग्यम्
उपभोग्य, -भोक्तव्य, -भोज्य + .{@-ग्यम्@}<BR>—1 Any object of enjoyment.<BR>—2 Food.<BR>—3 Expense incurred for protection (on food, clothing, education &c.);<BR> व्ययीकृतं रक्षणार्थमुपभोग्यं तदुच्यते Śukra. 2. 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोगिन्
उपभोगिन् <i>a.</i> Eating, enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभूषणम्
उपभूषणम् A minor or inferior ornament; implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृ
उपभृ €3 U. To bear; अविचलं शिखरैरुपबिभ्रतं ध्वनितसूचितमम्बुमुचां<BR> चयम् Ki. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृत्
उपभृत् <i>f.</i> [उप-मृ-आधारे क्विप्] A round cup used in sacrifices,<BR> made of the wood of the Banian tree; a sacrificial vessel; जुहूर्दाधार<BR> द्यामुपभृदन्तरिक्षम् Av. 18. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृत
उपभृत <i>a.</i> Procured for, brought near; शिष्यायोपभृतं तेजो<BR> यत एतत्समुद्यमः Bhāg. 8. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभेदः|उपभेद
उपभेदः subdivision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपम
उपम <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Highest, uppermost.<BR>—2 Most excellent, best, eminent, first.<BR>—3 Nearest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमश्रवस्
उपमश्रवस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of highest fame,<BR>—2 <i>m.</i> N. of a son of Kuruśravaṇa and grandson of Mitrātithi; कविं<BR> कवीनामुपमश्रवस्तमम् Rv. 2. 23. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्त्र्|उपमंत्र्
उपमन्त्र् €10 Ā.<BR>—1 To invoke, call, invite.<BR>—2 To address, call to; उपमन्त्रयते स हिंकारः Ch. Up. 2. 13. 1.<BR> स्त्री पुंसोपमन्त्रिता.<BR>—3 To persuade, conciliate. प्रियामनुगतः कामी वचोभिरुपमन्त्रयन्<BR> Bhāg. 9. 18. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्त्रणम्
उपमन्त्रणम्<BR>—1 The act of addressing, inviting, calling.<BR>—2 Persuading, coaxing (उपच्छन्दनम्); P. I. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्त्रिन्|उपमंत्रिन्
उपमन्त्रिन् <i>a.</i> Inviting, persuading; अश्वो वोळहा सुखं रथं<BR> हसनामुपमन्त्रिणः Rv. 9. 112. 4. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A messenger; स्मररुज उपमन्त्रिन्भव्यतामन्यवार्ता Bhāg. 10. 47. 19.<BR>—2 A subordinate counsellor; Bhāg. 10. 71. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्थनी|उपमंथनी
उपमन्थनी A staff for stirring; औदुम्बर्या उपमन्थन्यौ Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्थितृ|उपमंथितृ
उपमन्थितृ <i>a.</i> Ved. Stirring; Vāj. 30. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमन्यु
उपमन्यु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Understanding, intelligent.<BR>—2 Zealous, striving after.<BR>—3 (<i>m.</i>) N. of the pupil of Āyoda-dhaumya, who aided Śiva in the<BR> propagation of his doctrine and received the ocean of milk from him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमा
उपमा €2 P., €3. €4. Ā.<BR>—1 To compare, liken; तेनोपमीयेत तमालनीलम् Śi. 3. 8; स्तनौ<BR> मांसग्रन्थी कनककलशावित्युपमितौ Bh. 3. 20.<BR>—2 To give, grant (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमा
उपमा<BR>—1 Resemblance, similarity, equality; स्फुटोपमं भूतिसितेन शम्भुना<BR> Śi. 1. 4, 17. 69; Ki. 6. 23; इहोपमा सताम् Pt. 2. 8 the same is the<BR> case with the good.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) Comparison of two objects different from each other, simile,<BR> comparison; साधर्म्यमुपमा भेदे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">Page0455-2</a>]<BR> K. P. 10; or सादृश्यं सुन्दरं वाक्यार्थोपस्कारकमुपमालंकृतिः<BR> R. G.; or उपमा यत्र सादृश्यलक्ष्मीरुल्लसतिः द्वयोः । हंसीव कृष्ण ते<BR> कीर्तिः स्वर्गङ्गायवगाहते ॥ Candr. 5. 3; Kāv. 2. 14; उपमा कालिदासस्य<BR> Subhāṣ. (Daṇdin mentions 32 varieties of उपमा; see Kāv. 2. 15-50;<BR> as to words expressive of उपमा see 2. 57-65); see K. P. 10 <i>ad loc.</i> also.<BR>—3 The standard of comparison (उपमान); यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते<BR> सोपमा स्मृता Bg. 6. 19; (आत्मानमुपमां कृत्वा स्वेषु दारेषु रम्यताम्<BR> Rām. 5. 21. 8; see ˚द्रव्य below; mostly at the end of comp., ‘like’,<BR> ‘resembling’; बुबुधे न बुधोपमः R. 1. 47; so स्वर्गोपम, अमरोपम, अनुपम &c.)<BR>—4 A likeness (as a picture, portrait &c.)<BR>—5 Heresy, irreligious doctrine; विधर्मः परधर्मश्च आभास उपमा छलः ।<BR> अधर्मशाखाः पञ्चेमा धर्मज्ञोऽधर्मवत्त्यजेत् ॥ Bhāg. 7. 15. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपमाद्रव्यम्, उपमारूपकम्, उपमाव्यतिरेकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमाद्रव्यम्
उपमा + -द्रव्यम् any object used for a comparison; सर्वोपमाद्रव्यसमुच्चयेन Ku. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमारूपकम्
उपमा + -रूपकम् a figure in Rhetoric being a mixture of simile and metaphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमाव्यतिरेकः|उपमाव्यतिरेक
उपमा + -व्यतिरेकः A particular figure combining comparison and contrast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातृ
उपमातृ <i>m.</i> An image-maker, a portrait-painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमानम्
उपमानम्<BR>—1 Comparison, resemblance; जातास्तदूर्वोरुपमानबाह्याः Ku. 1. 36.<BR>—2 The standard of comparison, that with which anything is compared; one<BR> of the four requisites of an उपमा; उपमानमभूद्विलासिनां Ku. 4. 5;<BR> उपमानस्यापि सखे प्रत्युपमानं वपुस्तस्याः V. 2. 3; Śi. 20. 49.<BR>—3 (In Nyāya Phil.) Analogy, recognition of likeness, considered as one<BR> of the four kinds of pramāṇas or means of arriving at correct knowledge.<BR> It is defined as प्रसिद्धसाधर्म्यात् साध्यसाधनम्; or उपमितिकरणमुपमानं<BR> तच्च सादृश्यज्ञानात्मकम् Tarka K. तन्न विश्वसनीयं वो राक्षसानां<BR> रणाजिरे । एतेनैवोपमानेन नित्यं जिह्मा हि राक्षसाः ॥ Rām. 6. 50. 54.<BR>—4 A particle of comparison.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपमेयभावः, उपमानचिन्तामणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयभावः
उपमानम् + उपमेयभावः relation between the subject of comparison and the standard of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमानचिन्तामणिः|उपमानचिन्तामणि
उपमानम् + -चिन्तामणिः <i>m.</i> N. of a philosophical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमित
उपमित <i>p. p.</i> P. II. 1. 56. Compared, likened, similar &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमितिः|उपमिति
उपमितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Resemblance, comparison, similarity; पल्लवोपमितिसाम्यसपक्षम्<BR> S. D.; तदाननस्योपमितौ दरिद्रता N. 1. 24.<BR>—2 (In Nyāya Phil.) Analogy, inference, deduction, knowledge of things<BR> derived from analogy, a conclusion deduced by means of an उपमान; प्रत्यक्षमप्यनुमितिस्तथोपमितिशब्दजे<BR> Bhāṣā P. 52.<BR>—3 A figure of speech = उपमा q. v.<BR>—4 A likeness, picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेय
उपमेय <i>pot. p.</i> Fit to be likened or compared, comparable with;<BR> (with instr. or in comp.); भूयिष्ठमासीदुपमेयकान्तिः गुहेन R. 6. 4, 18. 34, 37;<BR> अन्तःपुरं चैककुलोपमेयम् Ku. 7. 2; C. P. 29 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयम्
उपमेय + .{@-यम्@} The subject of comparison, that which is compared उपमानोपमेयत्वं<BR> यदेकस्यैव वस्तुनः Candr. 5. 7, 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपमेयोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयोपमा
उपमेय + -उपमा a figure of speech in which the उपमान and उपमेय<BR> are compared to each other with a view to imply that the like of them<BR> does not exist; reciprocal comparison;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">Page0456-1</a>]<BR> विपर्यास उपमेयोपमानयोः K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> कमलेव मतिर्मतिरिव<BR> कमला तनुरिव विभा विभेव तनुः । &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातिः|उपमाति
उपमातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Comparison.<BR>—2 Killing.<BR>—3 Approaching with a prayer, addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातिः|उपमाति
उपमातिः + .{@-तिः@} <i>m.</i> Granting wealth (Sāy.), approaching in a friendly<BR> way; affable, an epithet of Agni (B. and R.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपमातिवनि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातिवनि
उपमातिः + -वनि <i>a.</i> destroyer of an enemy (Sāy.); मा नोऽहिर्बुध्न्यो<BR> रिषे धादस्माकं भूदुपमातिवनिः Rv. 5. 41. 16 one who receives addresses<BR> in a friendly way (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमीमांसा
उपमीमांसा Ved. Deliberation, investigation, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातृ
उपमातृ <i>f.</i> [उपमिता मात्रा उप गौणे वा]<BR>—1 ‘A second mother’, wet nurse.<BR>—2 A near female relative; मातृष्वसा मातुलानी पितृव्यस्त्री पितृष्वसा ।<BR> श्वश्रूः पूर्वजपत्नी च मातृतुल्याः प्रकीर्तिताः Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमाद|उपमादः
उपमाद <i>a.</i> Giving delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमादः|उपमाद
उपमाद + .{@-दः@} Enjoyment, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमारणम्
उपमारणम् Ved. Submerging (in water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमास्य
उपमास्य <i>a.</i> Occurring every month, monthly (Ved.); तस्मात् पितृभ्यो<BR> मास्युपमास्यं ददति Av. 8. 10. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमास्यम्
उपमास्य + .{@-स्यम्@} The Śrāddha ceremony to be performed every month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमित्
उपमित् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Dug up, excavated.<BR>—2 Placing near. ━<i>f.</i> A prop, stay, pillar (स्थूणा); स्थूणेव जनाँ<BR> उपमिद् ययन्थ Rv. 1. 59. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमृद्
उपमृद् €9 U.<BR>—1 To crush, bruise, dash to pieces, destroy, kill; पिण्डाकृतिमुपमृद्य<BR> घटिकाः क्रियन्ते Mbh. 1. 1. 1; यामिकाननुपमृद्य N. 5. 110.<BR>—2 To rub down.<BR>—3 To pass through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्दः|उपमर्द|उपमर्द्द
उपमर्दः<BR>—1 Friction, rubbing or pressing down, crushing under oneʼs weight; अन्यासु<BR> तावदुपमर्दसहासु भृङ्गं लोलं विनोदय मनः सुमनोलतासु S. D. (where<BR> उ˚ also means rough handling or enjoyment).<BR>—2 Destruction, injury, killing.<BR>—3 Reproach, abuse, insult, harsh or insulting treatment; Mk. 1.<BR>—4 Unhusking.<BR>—5 Refutation of a charge.<BR>—6 Stirring, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्दक|उपमर्दकः|उपमर्द्दक
उपमर्दक <i>a.</i> Crushing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्दकः|उपमर्दक|उपमर्द्दक
उपमर्दक + .{@-कः@} Refutation of a charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्दनम्
उपमर्दनम् Suppression, oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेखलम्
उपमेखलम् <i>ind.</i> On the slope or side; Ki. 7. 23<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेतः|उपमेत
उपमेतः The tree Vatica Robusta, Śāla tree (Mar. साग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयज्
उपयज् <i>m.</i> (P. III. 2. 73) N. of eleven additional formulas (enumerated<BR> in Vāj. 6. 21.) at a sacrifice; एकादशोपयजः यद्यजन्तमुपयजति<BR> तस्मादुपयजो नाम Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयष्टृ
उपयष्टृ <i>m.</i> The priest who utters the above formulas; Śat. Br. 3. 8. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाजः|उपयाज
उपयाजः Additional formulas at a sacrifice; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्त्रम्
उपयन्त्रम् A minor surgical instrument, a secondary application of any kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयम्
उपयम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To marry, take a wife (Ā. in this sense); भवान् मिथः समयादिमामुपायंस्त<BR> Ś. 5; आत्मानुरूपां विधिनोपयेमे Ku. 1. 18; R. 14. 87; Śi. 15. 27;<BR> Ms. 3. 11; Bk. 4. 20, 28, 7. 101.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To seize, hold; उपयच्छ शूर्पम् Av.; उपायंस्त महास्त्राणि<BR> Bk. 15. 21; शस्त्राण्युपायंसत जित्वराणि 1. 16.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To take, receive, accept; कोपात्काश्चित्प्रियैः प्रत्तमुपायंसत<BR> नासवम् Bk. 8. 33.<BR>—3 To show, indicate (सूच्); मोपयध्वं भयम् Bk. 7. 101.<BR>—4 To lie under, support, prop up (Ved.).<BR>—5 To go to (a woman); एतास्तिस्रस्तु भार्यार्थे नोपयच्छेत्तु बुद्धिमान् Ms. 11. 172.<BR>—6 To curb, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्तृ|उपयंतृ
उपयन्तृ <i>m.</i> A husband; अथोपयन्तारमलं समाधिना Ku. 5. 45;<BR> R. 7. 1; Śi. 10. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयमः|उपयम
उपयमः<BR>—1 Marriage, marrying; कन्या त्वजातोपयमा सलज्जा नवयौवना S. D.<BR>—2 Restraint.<BR>—3 A support; stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयमनम्
उपयमनम्<BR>—1 Marrying, taking a wife; P. I. 2. 16. विभाषोपयमने.<BR>—2 Restraining, curbing.<BR>—3 Placing down the fire<BR>—4 Support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयमनी
उपयमनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 Any support of stone for holding fire-wood; उपयमनीरुपकल्पयन्ति Śat. Br.<BR>—2 A sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयामः|उपयाम
उपयामः<BR>—1 A kind of vessel in a sacrifice.<BR>—2 The formulas uttered in taking out the Soma juice by means of a ladle<BR> (Vāj. 7. 4 seqq.)<BR>—3 Marriage (see उपयम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपया
उपया €2 P.<BR>—1 To approach, go towards, reach; उपयामगृहीतोऽसि Ts. 1. 4. 15. 1^1.<BR> येन मामुपयान्तिते Bg. 10. 10; so पुरम्, गतिम्, नयनम्, पदवीम्;<BR> दुर्मन्त्रिणं कमुपयान्ति न नीतिदोषाः H. 3. 110.<BR>—2 To attain to a particular state, meet with &c.; तनुताम्, मृत्युम्,<BR> रुजम्, पाकम्, प्रसादम् &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयात
उपयात <i>p. p.</i> Come, arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयातम्
उपयात + .{@-तम्@} Arrival, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयानम्
उपयानम्<BR>—1 Approaching, coming near; उपयानापयाने च स्थानं प्रत्यपसर्पणम् ।<BR> सर्वमेतद्रथस्थेन ज्ञेयं रथकुटुम्बिना ॥ Rām. 6. 104. 20.<BR>—2 Acquisition, obtaining; हरोपयाने त्वरिता बभूव Ku. 7. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयायिन्
उपयायिन् <i>a.</i> Coming towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाच्
उपयाच् €1 U. To wish or ask for, solicit; अक्षमालामुपयाचितुम् K. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचक|उपयाचकः
उपयाचक <i>a.</i> One who asks or solicits, suitor, beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचनम्
उपयाचनम् Soliciting, begging, approaching with a request or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचित|उपयाचितं
उपयाचित <i>p. p.</i> Begged, requested, solicited. त्वया पुरस्तादुपयाचितो<BR> यः R. 13. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचितम्
उपयाचित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A request or prayer in general.<BR>—2 A present promised to a deity for the fulfilment of a desired object<BR> and generally to propitiate her, (the present may be an animal or even<BR> a human being); निक्षेपी म्रियते तुभ्यं प्रदास्याम्युपयाचितम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">Page0457-1</a>]<BR> Pt. 1. 14, 2. 50; अद्य मया भगवत्याः करालायाः प्रागुपयाचितं स्त्रीरत्नमुपहर्तव्यम्<BR> Māl. 5; दीयते यत्तु देवेभ्यो मनोराज्यस्य सिद्धये । उपयाचितकं दिव्यं<BR> दोहदं तद्विदुर्बुधाः ॥<BR>—3 A request or prayer to a deity for the accomplishment of a desired object; K. 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचितकम्
उपयाचितकम् = उपयाचित above; सिद्धायतनानि कृतविविधदेवतोपयाचितकानि K. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयापनम्
उपयापनम्<BR>—1 The act of causing to come near, leading near.<BR>—2 A marriage; पुत्राणां दुहितॄणां च काले विध्युपयापनम् । दारैर्वरैस्तत्सदृशं<BR> कल्पयन्तं विभूतिभिः Bhāg. 10. 69. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुज्
उपयुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To use, employ, apply; षाड्गुण्यमुपयुञ्जीत Śi. 2. 93; षडुपायुङ्क्त<BR> समीक्ष्य तत्फलम् R. 8. 21; M. 5. 12; अनुपयुज्यमान useless, good<BR> for nothing, Ś. 7; U. 4.<BR>—2 To enjoy, taste; पय उपयुज्य Me. 13 v. l.; फलान्युपायुङ्क्त<BR> स दण्डनीतेः R. 18. 46; Bk. 8. 39;<BR>—3 To devote or attach oneself to; न मृगैरुपयुज्यते is not loved<BR> Pt. 2. 23; न वै प्राज्ञा गतश्रीकं भर्तारमुपयुञ्जते Subhāṣ.<BR>—4 To yoke or harness (as horses to a carriage); यामन्यामन्नुपयुक्तं<BR> वहिष्ठम् Av. 4. 23. 3.<BR>—5 To appropriate, consume, eat; राजा तत् (धनम्) उपयुञ्जानश्चौरस्याप्नोति<BR> किल्बिषम् Ms. 8. 40. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be used or applied.<BR>—2 To be fit or proper; तस्येयमुपयुज्यते Bhāg.<BR>—3 To be of use, be taken into account; तेजसा सह जातानां वयः कुत्रोपयुज्यते Pt. 1. 328.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुक्त|उपयुक्तः
उपयुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Attached &c.<BR>—2 Suited, appropriate, fit, right, proper.<BR>—3 Worthy, serviceable, useful.<BR>—4 Eaten, consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुक्तः|उपयुक्त
उपयुक्त + .{@-क्तः@} A subordinate officer; Kau. A. 2. 5; Bhāg. 9. 2. 14; उपयुक्तोदकां<BR> भग्नां प्रपां निपतितामिव Rām. 2. 114. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगः|उपयोग
उपयोगः<BR>—1 Employment, use, application, service; ओषधान्नविहाराणामुपयोगः<BR> सुखावहः Mādh. N. उपयोगं गम् or व्रज् to be used or employed,<BR> serve; व्रजन्ति … अनङ्गलेखक्रिययोपयोगम् Ku. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Administration of medicines, or their preparation.<BR>—3 Fitness, suitableness, propriety.<BR>—4 Contact, proximity.<BR>—5 Any act contributing to the fulfilment of a desired object.<BR>—6 Good conduct, observing established customs.<BR>—7 Food; गते च दुर्वाससि सोऽम्बरीषो द्विजोपयोगातिपवित्रमाहरत्<BR> Bhāg. 9. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिन्
उपयोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Employing, using.<BR>—2 Conducive or contributing to, serviceable, useful.<BR>—3 Appropriate, fit, proper.<BR>—4 Favourable, propitious.<BR>—5 Touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिता
उपयोगिता or ˚त्वम्<BR>—1 Usefulness, utility.<BR>—2 Fitness, propriety.<BR>—3 Occasion, need.<BR>—4 Favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगित्वम्
उपयोगिता or ˚त्वम्<BR>—1 Usefulness, utility.<BR>—2 Fitness, propriety.<BR>—3 Occasion, need.<BR>—4 Favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोजनम्
उपयोजनम्<BR>—1 Harnessing a horse, Ait. Br. 5. 30. 6.<BR>—2 A team.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोज्य
उपयोज्य <i>a.</i> To be employed, used or applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपर|उपरः
उपर <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Being below, under.<BR>—2 Posterior, later. —3 Nearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरः|उपर
उपर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The lower stone on which the Soma plant is laid that it may be ground by means<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">Page0457-2</a>]<BR> of other stones (ग्रावन्); त्वचं पृञ्चन्त्युपरस्य योनौ Rv. 1. 79. 3.<BR>—2 The lower part of the sacrificial post.<BR>—3 A cloud.<BR>—4 A region, direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरताति
उपरताति <i>ind.</i> In the proximity, near to; विश्वाँ अर्य उपरताति<BR> वन्वन् Rv. 7. 48. 3, 1. 151. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरञ्ज्
उपरञ्ज् €4 U. or in <i>pass.</i> To be red; to be eclipsed; उपरज्यते<BR> भगवान् चन्द्रः Mu. 1. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To colour, tint, dye.<BR>—2 To affect, grieve, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्त|उपरक्तः
उपरक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Afflicted, overtaken by calamity, distressed.<BR>—2 Eclipsed; K. 314.<BR>—3 Tinged, coloured; द्विषद्द्वेषोपरक्ताङ्गसङ्गिनीः Śi. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्तः|उपरक्त
उपरक्त + .{@-क्तः@}<BR>—1 The sun or moon in eclipse.<BR>—2 Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरज्य
उपरज्य <i>ind.</i> Darkening, obscuring, तमश्चन्द्रमसीवेदमुपरज्यावभासते<BR> Bhāg. 4. 29. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरञ्जक
उपरञ्जक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dyeing.<BR>—2 Affecting, influencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरागः|उपराग
उपरागः<BR>—1 An eclipse of the sun or moon; उपरागान्ते शशिनः समुपगता रोहिणी<BR> योगम् Ś. 7. 22; Śi. 20. 45.<BR>—2 Hence, Rāhu or the ascending node.<BR>—3 Redness, red colour, colour; कोपोपरागजनिताम् Ratn. 3. 14; Mk. 4;<BR> कलहकोप˚ Māl. 9.<BR>—4 A calamity, affliction, injury; blighting influence; मृणालिनी हैममिवोपरागम् R. 16. 7.<BR>—5 Misbehaviour, ill-conduct.<BR>—6 Reproach, blame, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्षः|उपरक्ष
उपरक्षः A body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्षणम्
उपरक्षणम् A guard, an out-post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत्नम्
उपरत्नम् [उपमितं रत्नेन उप गौणे वा] A secondary or inferior<BR> gem; उपरत्नानि काचश्च कर्पूरोश्मा तथैव च । मुक्ताशुक्तिस्तथा शङ्क<BR> इत्यादीनि बहून्यपि ॥ गुणा यथैव रत्नानामुपरत्नेषु ते तथा । किं तु<BR> किंचित्ततो हीना विशेषोऽयमुदाहृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरथ्या
उपरथ्या A bye-road, minor road; तथा रथ्योपरथ्याश्च Rām. 5. 53. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरम्
उपरम् €1 P. (Sometimes Ā. also)<BR>—1 To cease, end, terminate; संगतावुपरराम च लज्जा Ki. 9. 44, 13. 69;<BR> इत्युक्त्वोपरराम; युद्धमुपारमत् ceased &c.<BR>—2 To cease or desist from, stop (oft. with pres. part.); व्यापादयन्नोपरराम<BR> Pt. 1; or with abl.; Bg. 2. 35; Bk. 8. 54, 9. 51; or with inf.; Ki. 4. 17;<BR> or by itself; Bk. 8. 55.<BR>—3 To be quiet or calm; यत्रोपरमते चित्तम् Bg. 6. 20.<BR>—4 To await, wait for; Śat. Br. 2. 2. 1-2, 3. 8. 2-29.<BR>—5 To make quiet (= <i>Caus.</i>). ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to cease, stop,<BR> make quiet or still.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत|उपरतः
उपरत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stopped, ceased; उपरतान्यस्मिन् कुले व्रतानि Mbh. on P. I. 4. 110;<BR> रजस्युपरते Ms. 5. 66.<BR>—2 Dead; अद्य दशमो मासस्तातस्योपरतस्य Mu. 4.<BR>—3 Withdrawn or retired from; रणात्, कलहात् &c. भयाद्रणादुपरतम् Bg. 2. 34.<BR>—4 One who is disgusted with the world and has retired from it.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपरतारि, उपरतकर्मन्, उपरतविषयाभिलाष, उपरतशोणिता, उपरतस्पृह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतारि
उपरत + -अरि <i>a.</i> having no foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतकर्मन्
उपरत + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> ceasing from works, not relying on worldly acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतविषयाभिलाष
उपरत + -विषयाभिलाष <i>a.</i> one who has renounced all desire for worldly things.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">Page0458-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतशोणिता
उपरत + -शोणिता (a woman) whose menses have ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतस्पृह|उपरतस्पृहः
उपरत + -स्पृह <i>a.</i> void of desire, indifferent to worldly attachments<BR> or possessions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतिः|उपरति
उपरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Ceasing, stopping.<BR>—2 Death.<BR>—3 Abstaining from sexual enjoyment.<BR>—4 Indifference.<BR>—5 Abstaining from prescribed acts; the conviction that ceremonial acts<BR> are futile and ceasing to rely on them.<BR>—6 Intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरमः|उपरम
उपर(रा)मः<BR>—1 Ceasing, stopping; ending; भवप्रवाहोपरमं पदाम्बुजम् Bhāg. 1. 8. 36.<BR>—2 Abstaining from, giving up.<BR>—3 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरामः|उपराम
उपर(रा)मः<BR>—1 Ceasing, stopping; ending; भवप्रवाहोपरमं पदाम्बुजम् Bhāg. 1. 8. 36.<BR>—2 Abstaining from, giving up.<BR>—3 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरमणम्
उपरमणम्<BR>—1 Abstaining from sexual pleasures.<BR>—2 Refraining from ceremonial acts.<BR>—3 Ceasing, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरम्भ्
उपरम्भ् P. To cause to resound; जातहर्ष उपरम्भति विश्वम् Bhāg. 10. 35. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरवः|उपरव
उपरवः A sort of hole used in the extraction of Soma juice (सोमाभिषवाङ्गो<BR> गर्ताकारो देशभेदः); name of certain holes which increase the sound<BR> of the stones when Soma juice is being extracted; cf. also पीठपादचतुष्टयाकारो<BR> बाहुमात्रो गर्तभेद उपरवः । ŚB. on MS. 11. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरावः|उपराव
उपरावः A near sound; P. III. 3. 22. उपसर्गे रुवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरसः|उपरस
उपरसः<BR>—1 A secondary mineral, (red chalk, bitumen, माक्षिक, शिलाजित &c.).<BR>—2 A secondary passion or feeling.<BR>—3 A subordinate flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराजः|उपराज
उपराजः A viceroy, one inferior to the ruling authority; P. IV. 2. 116.<BR> उपराजेव राजर्द्धि ज्ञातिर्न सहते सदा Mb. 12. 80. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरि
उपरि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a separable preposition (usually with gen., rarely with acc. or loc.) it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Above, over, upon, on, towards; (opp. अधः) (with gen.);<BR> गतमुपरि घनानाम् Ś. 7. 7; अवाङ्मुखस्योपरि वृष्टिः पपात R. 2. 60;<BR> अर्कस्योपरि Ś. 2. 9; प्रासादानाम् Māl. 7. 5; U. 5. 2; Śi. 16. 9, 12. 37;<BR> so ˚स्थापनम्, ˚स्थित &c.; with loc. उपर्येव स लङ्कायाम्<BR> Rām.; or acc. यन्त्राण्युपरि यन्त्राणि <i>ibid.</i>; oft. at the end of<BR> comp.; रथ˚, तरुवर˚, तद्˚.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) At the end of, at the head of; सर्वानन्दानामुपरि वर्तमाना K. 158.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Beyond, in addition to; पणस्योपरि संस्थाप्य व्ययम् Y. 2. 253;<BR> भुक्तस्योपरि Suśr.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) In connection with, with regard to, towards, upon; परस्परस्योपरि<BR> पर्यचीयत R. 3. 24; Śānti. 3. 23; तस्योपरि क्रुद्धः, ममोपरि दुष्टबुद्धिः<BR> &c.; तवोपरि प्रायोपवेशनं करिष्यामि on your account.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) After; मुहूर्तादुपरि उपाध्यायश्चेदागच्छेत् P. III. 3. 9. Sk.<BR> उपरि joined to उपरि (with acc. or gen. or by itself) means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Just above; लोकानुपर्युपर्यास्ते माधवः Vop.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) higher and higher, far high, high above; उपर्युपरि सर्वेषामादित्य<BR> इव तेजसा Mb.<BR>—2 (As a separable adverb) It means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) high above, upon, towards the upper side of (opp. अधः);<BR> त्रिदशान्विनिहत्याशु स्वयं स्थास्याम्यथोपरि Rām. 7. 29. 6. उपर्युपरि<BR> पश्यन्तः सर्वम् एव दरिद्रति H. 2. 2; so उपरि या; ˚स्थापन, ˚स्थित<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">Page0458-2</a>]<BR> &c.; oft. in comp. स्वमुद्रोपरिचिह्नितम् Y. 1. 319.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Besides, in addition, further, more; शतान्युपरि चैवाष्टौ तथा<BR> भूयश्च सप्ततिः Mb.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Afterwards; यदा पूर्वं नासीदुपरि च तया नैव भविता Śānti. 2. 7;<BR> सर्पिः पीत्वोपरि पयः पिबेत् Suśr.; उपर्युपरि more and<BR> more, repeatedly, continuously. [cf. Zend. <i>upairi, upara</i>; Gr. <i>huper</i>;<BR> L. <i>super</i>; Old Germ. <i>obar</i>; Germ. <i>uber</i>; Eng. <i>over</i>;<BR> Hind. <i>upar</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपर्यासनम्, उपरिकरः, उपरिकाण्डम्, उपरिगत, उपरिचर, उपरिचरः, उपरिचित, उपरिज, उपरितन, उपरिस्थ, उपरितलम्, उपरिप्रुत, उपरिबुध्न, उपरिबृहती, उपरिभागः, उपरिभावः, उपरिभूमिः, उपरिमर्त्यम्, उपरिशयनम्, उपरिश्रेणिक, उपरिष्ठः, उपरिसद्, उपरिसद्यम्, उपरिस्थायिन्, उपरिस्पृश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपर्यासनम्
उपरि + -आसनम् sitting on high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिकरः|उपरिकर
उपरि + -करः A tax paid by temporary tenants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिकाण्डम्
उपरि + -काण्डम् The third division of the Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिगत
उपरि + -गत <i>a.</i> gone up, ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचर|उपरिचरः
उपरि + -चर <i>a.</i> moving above (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचरः|उपरिचर
उपरि + -चरः N. of the king Vasu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचित
उपरि + -चित <i>a.</i> piled over or above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिज
उपरि + -ज <i>a.</i> produced above, elevated, high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरितन
उपरि + -तन, -स्थ <i>a.</i> upper, higher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिस्थ
उपरि + -तन, -स्थ <i>a.</i> upper, higher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरितलम्
उपरि + -तलम् Upper part; उपरितलनिपातितेष्टकः Mk. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिप्रुत
उपरि + -प्रुत <i>a.</i> Ved. coming from above; Vāj. 7. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिबुध्न
उपरि + -बुध्न <i>a.</i> Ved. raised above the ground; Rv. 10. 73. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिबृहती
उपरि + -बृहती A variety of बृहती metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिभागः|उपरिभाग
उपरि + -भागः the upper portion or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिभावः|उपरिभाव
उपरि + -भावः being above or higher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिभूमिः|उपरिभूमि
उपरि + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> the ground above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिमर्त्यम्
उपरि + -मर्त्यम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. above men; अवो देवमुपरिमर्त्यं कृधि Rv. 8. 19. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिशयनम्
उपरि + -शयनम् a place of rest. यदुपरिशयनमाहरन्ति स्वर्गमेव<BR> तेन लोकमवरुन्द्धे Av. 9. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिश्रेणिक
उपरि + -श्रेणिक <i>a.</i> being in the upper line or series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्ठः|उपरिष्ठ
उपरि + -ष्ठः (-स्थ) <i>a.</i> Above, staying up; पर्वतस्योपरिष्ठस्य<BR> कर्मेदं कस्यचिद्भवेत् Rām. 7. 16. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिसद्
उपरि + -सद् <i>a.</i> lying or sitting above; Vāj. 9. 35. (<i>m.</i>) a class of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिसद्यम्
उपरि + -सद्यम् sitting above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिस्थायिन्
उपरि + -स्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Standing higher, prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिस्पृश्
उपरि + -स्पृश् Reaching above, elevated; वसवो रुद्रा आदित्या उपरिस्पृशम्<BR> Rv. 10. 128. 9. {@कः@} A provincial governor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टात्
उपरिष्टात् <i>ind.</i> [cf. उपर्युपरिष्टान् P. V. 3. 31]<BR>—1 As an adverb it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Over, above, from above, on high; परहितकरणे नोपरिष्टान्न<BR> चाधः Bh. 3. 131; Y. 1. 106.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Further or later on, afterwards; कल्याणावतंसा हि कल्याणसंपदुपरिष्टाद्<BR> भवति Māl. 6; इदमुपरिष्टाद् व्याख्यातम् in the sequel.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Behind (opp. पुरस्तात्); पुरसाच्चोपरिष्टाच्च अद्भिः परिदधति<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 2. 2.<BR>—2 (As a preposition) it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Over, upon (with gen., rarely acc.); स्फुटतरमुपरिष्टादल्पमूर्तेर्ध्रुवस्य<BR> स्फुरति सुरमुनीनां मण्डलं व्यस्तमेतत् Śi. 11. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Down upon.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Behind (with gen.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपरिष्टाज्ज्योतिष्मती, उपरिष्टाज्ज्योतिः, उपरिष्टाद्बृहती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टाज्ज्योतिष्मती
उपरिष्टात् + -ज्योतिष्मती N. of a Vedic metre consisting of 43 or 44 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टाज्ज्योतिः
उपरिष्टात् + -ज्योतिः <i>f.</i> a verse of the Triṣṭubh metre, the last line<BR> of which consists of eight syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टाद्बृहती
उपरिष्टात् + -बृहती N. of a Vedic metre having four Pādas, the first of which<BR> contains 12 syllables, each of the three others having only eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरीतकः|उपरीतक
उपरीतकः A particular mode or posture of sexual enjoyment; (also<BR> called विपरीतक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरुध्
उपरुध् €7 U.<BR>—1 To obstruct, hinder, interrupt, stop; मा मोपरोत्सीरिति मा सृजैनम्<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 21. उत्पक्ष्मणोर्नयनयोरुपरुद्धवृत्तिम् Ś. 4. 15; Ve. 3. 8;<BR> उपरुध्यते तपोऽनुष्ठानम् Ś. 4; V. 5; पण्यमुपरुन्धताम्<BR> Y. 2. 250; to detain; अन्याय्यमुपरोद्धुम् V. 5.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To disturb, trouble; पौरास्तपोवनमुपरुन्धन्ति Ś. 1.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To press, trouble<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">Page0459-1</a>]<BR> with a request; अभ्युत्सहे संप्रति नोपरोद्धुम् R. 5. 22.<BR>—3 To overcome, subdue; भेजे भिन्नकटैर्नागैरन्यानुपरुरोध यैः R. 4. 83.<BR>—4 To besiege (an enemy, town &c.); उपरुध्यारिमासीत Ms. 7. 195; Kām. 13. 67;<BR> उपरुद्धं कुसुमपुरम् Mu. 2.<BR>—5 To lock up, pen, confine; व्रजोपरोधं गाः स्थापयति Sk.<BR>—6 To conceal, hide; नेत्रकमेणोपरुरोध सूर्यम् R. 7. 39.<BR>—7 To cast off, repudiate, reject; ज्येष्ठपुत्रमुपारुधत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरुद्ध|उपरुद्धः
उपरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Obstructed, impeded, stopped, confined, captive; वृत्तं हि राज्ञामुपरुद्धवृत्तम् R. 18. 18.<BR>—2 Covered, spread, concealed.<BR>—3 Protected, favoured.<BR>—4 Besieged, locked up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरुद्धः|उपरुद्ध
उपरुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} A captive; R. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधः|उपरोध
उपरोधः<BR>—1 Obstruction, impediment, obstacle; शरत्प्रमृष्टाम्बुधरोपरोधः<BR> R. 6. 44; Śi. 20. 74; सकौतुक˚ विनयम् U. 4.<BR>—2 Disturbance, trouble, molestation; तपोवननिवासिनामुपरोधो मा भूत<BR> Ś. 1. 5, 6; अनुग्रहः खल्वेष नोपरोधः V. 3; उपरोधःसह्यताम्<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; detention; किं राजर्षेरुपरोधेन Ś. 3.<BR>—3 Opposition, refusal, check, restraint.<BR>—4 Covering, surrounding, blocking up.<BR>—5 Binding, tying, seizing.<BR>—6 Protection, favour. बलवता विगृह्योपरोधहेतवः Measures conducive<BR> to peace; Kau. A. 7.<BR>—7 sublation, dropping; आनर्थक्याद्धि प्राकृतस्योपरोधः स्यात् । MS. 8. 4. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपरोधकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधकारिन्
उपरोधः + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> impeding, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधक|उपरोधकं
उपरोधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstructing, obstructor; रामोऽभ्येति पुरीं लङ्कामस्माकमुपरोधकः<BR> Rām. 6. 6. 16.<BR>—2 Covering, surrounding<BR>—3 Favouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधकम्
उपरोधक + .{@-कम्@} An inner room, a private apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधनम्
उपरोधनम् Obstruction, impediment &c.; see उपरोध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधिन्
उपरोधिन् <i>a.</i> Obstructing, impeding; सुखानि सोऽभुङ्क्तसुखोपरोधि R. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरूपकम्
उपरूपकम् [उपगतं रूपकं दृश्यकाव्यं सादृश्येन] A drama<BR> of an inferior class, of which 18 kinds are enumerated; नाटिका त्रोटकं<BR> गोष्ठी सट्टकं नाट्यरासकम् । प्रस्थानोल्लाप्यकाव्यानि प्रेङ्खणं रासकं<BR> तथा ॥ संलापकं श्रीगदितं शिल्पकं च विलासिका । दुर्मल्लिका प्रकरणी<BR> हल्लीशो भाणिकेति च ॥ S. D. 276.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलः|उपल
उपलः<BR>—1 A stone, rock; उपलशकलमेतद् भेदकं गोमयानाम् Mu. 3. 15; कान्ते<BR> कथं घटितवानुपलेन चेतः Ś. Til. 3; Me. 19; Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—2 A precious stone, jewel. Y. 3. 36. ‘उपलः प्रस्तरे मणौ’ इति विश्वः.<BR>—3 Sand (Ved.).<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR>—5 A ball thrown from some artifice (as gun); कपाटयन्त्रदुर्धर्षा<BR> बभूवुः सहुडोपलाः Mb. 3. 284. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपला
उपलः + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 Refined sugar, (उपलासिता Sugar-candy).<BR>—2 The upper and smaller millstone which rests on the Dṛṣad. [cf. L. <i>opatus</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपलप्रक्षिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलप्रक्षिन्
उपलः + -प्रक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Grinding grain upon millstones; कारुरहं ततो<BR> भिषगुपलप्रक्षिणी नवा Rv. 9. 112. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलकः|उपलक
उपलकः A stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्ष्
उपलक्ष् €10 P.<BR>—1 To look at, observe, behold, mark; आसन्नवर्तिजन उपलक्षयति<BR> K. 197; सम्यगुपलक्षितं भवत्या Ś. 1.<BR>—2 To regard or consider; लोकप्रवादः सत्योऽयं पण्डितैरुपलक्षितः Rām.<BR>—3 To mark, put a sign upon; आदिमध्यावसानेषु भवच्छब्दोपलक्षिता<BR> Y. 1. 30, 2. 151; Kām. 7. 47.<BR>—4 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">Page0459-2</a>]<BR> denote, designate, describe.<BR>—5 To imply in addition; नक्षत्रशब्देन ज्योतिःशास्त्रमुपलक्ष्यते<BR> Kull. on Ms. 3. 162.<BR>—6 To mind, have in view; Kām. 16. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षक
उपलक्षक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Observing; marking; परचित्त˚<BR>—2 Designating, indicating (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षणम्
उपलक्षणम्<BR>—1 Looking at, beholding, observing, marking, ascertainment; वेलोपलक्षणार्थम् Ś. 4.<BR>—2 A mark, characteristic or distinctive feature; उपलब्धमुपलक्षणम्<BR> V. 4, 4. 33; उपलक्षणे तृतीया Sk.<BR>—3 Designation; प्राद्युपलक्षणम् Sk.<BR>—4 Implying something that has not been actually expressed, implication<BR> of something in addition or any similar object where only one is mentioned;<BR> synecdoche of a part for the whole, of an individual for the species,<BR> or of a quality for that in which the quality exists (स्वप्रतिपादकत्वे<BR> सति स्वेतरप्रतिपादकत्वं); मन्त्रग्रहणं ब्राह्मणस्याप्युपलक्षणम्<BR> P. II. 4. 80. Sk.; so अस्ति नास्तेरुपलक्षणम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षित
उपलक्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Observed, marked, comprehended, implied, metaphorically expressed &c.<BR>—2 Understood, comprehended.<BR>—3 Characterized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्ष्य|उपलक्ष्यः
उपलक्ष्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Inferable.<BR>—2 To be described, designated &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्ष्यः|उपलक्ष्य
उपलक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यः@}<BR>—1 A prop, stay, support.<BR>—2 An asylum, shelter.<BR>—3 An inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलधिप्रियः|उपलधिप्रिय
उपलधिप्रियः [बालधिः प्रियोऽस्य पृषो˚] A kind of antelope (चमर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलभ्
उपलभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To know, understand, see, perceive (directly); सव्यदक्षिणयोर्यत्र<BR> विशेषो नोपलभ्यते Pt. 1. 76; अन्या प्रतिक्रिया नोपलभ्यते K. 152.<BR>—2 To ascertain, find out, learn, know; ब्रूहि यदुपलब्धम् U. 1; तत्त्वत<BR> एनामुपलप्स्ये Ś. 1; Mv. 7. 30; R. 12. 60; Bk. 3. 27; K. 159; M. 41, 3. 6, 4. 6.<BR>—3 To get, obtain, acquire, enjoy, experience (happiness &c.); उपलब्धसुखः<BR> Ku. 4. 42 experiencing; कथमुपलभे निद्राम् V. 2. 10 enjoy; इदानीं<BR> स्मृतिरुपलब्धा Mu. 2 now I recollect; Ms. 11. 17; R. 8. 82, 10. 2, 18. 21.<BR>—4 To conceive, become pregnant. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to get; बुभुजे च श्रियं स्वृद्धां द्विजदेवोपलम्भिताम् Bhāg. 8. 15. 37.<BR>—2 To produce, bring about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्ध
उपलब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gained, obtained.<BR>—2 Conceived.<BR>—3 Perceived, understood, known, guessed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपलब्धार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धार्थ
उपलब्ध + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> having the meaning understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धार्था
उपलब्ध + -अर्थ + .({@-ब्धार्था@} <i>f.</i>) a tale, a true or probable story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धिः|उपलब्धि
उपलब्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Getting, obtaining, acquisition; उपलब्धौ यत्नः क्रियताम् Mbh. on 1. 1. 1.<BR> वृथा हि मे स्यात्स्वपदोपलब्धिः R. 5. 56, 8. 17.<BR>—2 Observation, perception, knowledge (ज्ञान); बुद्धिरुपलब्धिर्ज्ञानं<BR> प्रत्यय इत्यनर्थान्तरम् Nyāya S., नाभाव उपलब्धेः<BR> Br. Sūt. 2. 2. 28; भावे चोपलब्धेः 2. 1. 15. cf. Nyāya S. 2. 28, 30.<BR>—3 Understanding, mind (मति).<BR>—4 A conjecture, guess.<BR>—5 Perceptibility appearance (recognized as a kind of proof by the Mīmāṃsakas);<BR> तत्र वेदविधिः स स्याज्ज्ञानं चेत्पुरुषं प्रति ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">Page0460-1</a>]<BR> उपपत्त्युपलब्धिभ्याम् Mb. 12. 238. 3; see अनुपलब्धि.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपलब्धिसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धिसमः|उपलब्धिसम
उपलब्धिः + -समः (in logic) A kind of sophistical refutation of an argument<BR> (<i>e. g.</i> the argument ‘sound is uneternal because it is produced by some effort’<BR>━ is refuted by saying that sound is also produced by wind);<BR> Nyāyadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धृ
उपलब्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gaininig, acquiring.<BR>—2 Knowing, perceiving. ━<i>m.</i> Soul, self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भः|उपलम्भ|उपलंभ|उपलंभः
उपलम्भः [लभ्-घञ्-मुम् च P. VII. 4. 64]<BR>—1 Acquisition; अस्मादङ्गुलीयोपलम्भात्स्मृतिरुपलब्धा Ś. 7.<BR>—2 Direct perception or recognition, comprehension otherwise than from<BR> memory (same as अनुभव q. v.); प्राक्तनोपलम्भ Māl. 5; ज्ञातौ<BR> सुतस्पर्शसुखोपलम्भात् R. 14. 2.<BR>—3 Ascertaining, knowing; अविध्नकियोपलम्भाय Ś. 1.<BR>—4 Seeing, looking at (दर्शन); लावण्यधाम्नो भवितोपलम्भनम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 38. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भक|उपलंभक
उपलम्भक <i>a.</i> Causing to observe, reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भनम्
उपलम्भनम् Apprehension &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलभ्य
उपलभ्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Obtainable.<BR>—2 Respectable, commendable, praise-worthy. आरम्भसिद्धौ समयोपलभ्यम् R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्सा
उपलिप्सा A desire to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलल्
उपलल् €10 P. To fondle, coax, flatter; नताङ्गीमुपलालयन् Dk. 29;<BR> Ś. 7; M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलालनम्
उपलालनम् Fondling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलालिका
उपलालिका<BR>—1 Thirst.<BR>—2 Tyranny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिङ्गम्
उपलिङ्गम् A portent, natural phenomenon, considered as boding evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्
उपलिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To anoint, smear, besmear.<BR>—2 To defile, pollute; तथात्मा नोपलिप्यते Bg. 13. 32.<BR>—3 To stick or adhere to; यो वक्त्रमुपलिम्पति Vāgb. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To besmear (esp. with cow-dung); शुचिं देशं विविक्तं च गोमयेनोपलेपयेत् Ms. 3. 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेपः|उपलेप
उपलेपः<BR>—1 Anointing, smearing. Bhāg. 11. 11. 39.<BR>—2 Cleaning, white-washing.<BR>—3 Obstruction, being concealed.<BR>—4 Becoming deadened or dull (said of senses), bluntness, dullness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेपनम्
उपलेपनम्<BR>—1 Smearing, anointing, plastering.<BR>—2 An ointment, unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेपिन्
उपलेपिन्<BR>—1 Serving as an ointment.<BR>—2 Anointing, smearing.<BR>—3 Obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपली
उपली €4 Ā. To lie close to, cling to; Mb. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेखः|उपलेख
उपलेखः N. of a grammatical work connected with the Prātiśākhyas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपलेखपञ्जिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेखपञ्जिका
उपलेखः + -पञ्जिका <i>f.</i>, {@-भाष्यम्@}<BR> Names of Commentaries on the above work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलोहम्
उपलोहम् A secondary metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवक्तृ
उपवक्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A priest at a sacrifice<BR>—2 One who animates (by his words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवञ्चनम्
उपवञ्चनम् The act of crouching or lying close to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवञ्चित
उपवञ्चित <i>a.</i> Deceived, disappointed; वयं खलु हता राम<BR> यत्त्वया उपवञ्चिताः Rām. 2. 52. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवटः|उपवट
उपवटः The tree Buchanania Latifolia (प्रियासाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवद्
उपवद् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To talk over, conciliate.<BR>—2 To flatter, cajole, coax; भृत्यानुपवदते Sk.; दातारम् Bk. 8. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवादः|उपवाद
उपवादः Censure, blame (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवादिन्
उपवादिन् <i>a.</i> Censuring, blaming; अल्पाः कलहिनः पिशुना उपवादिनः<BR> Ch. Up. 7. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवनम्
उपवनम् [उपमितं वनेन] A garden, grove, a planted forest;<BR> पाण्डुच्छायोपवनवृतयः केतकैः सूचिभिन्नैः Me. 23; R. 8. 73, 13. 79;<BR> ˚लता a garden creeper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपवनविनोदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवनविनोदः|उपवनविनोद
उपवनम् + -विनोदः N. of a work on gardening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ण्
उपवर्ण् €10 P. To describe in detail; उपवर्णयेदानीं कुसुमपुरवृत्तान्तम् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्णः|उपवर्ण
उपवर्णः Minute or detailed description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्णनम्
उपवर्णनम् Minute description, delineation in detail; अतिशयोपवर्णनं<BR> व्याख्यानम् Suśr.; Y. 1. 320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्षः|उपवर्ष
उपवर्षः N. of a son of Śaṅkara Svāmin, author of several writings<BR> on the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवल्गित
उपवल्गित <i>a.</i> Swollen or dimmed with tears (as eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवल्लिका
उपवल्लिका N. of a plant (अमृतश्रवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवल्हः|उपवल्ह
उपवल्हः Ved. Emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्
उपवस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To dwell in or at, inhabit (with acc.); तपःश्रद्धे ये ह्युपवसन्त्यरण्ये<BR> Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 11. वैकुण्ठम् उपवसति Sk.<BR>—2 To be in a state of abstinence, abstain from food, fast; उपवसेद्दिनम्<BR> Ms. 2. 220, 5. 20; Y. 3. 292, 64; (fig. also); उपोषिताभ्यामिव नेत्राभ्यां<BR> पिबन्ती Dk. 4.<BR>—3 To go to (a master).<BR>—4 To enter upon, learn, take to, begin. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसथः|उपवसथ
उपवसथः [उप-वस्-आधारे अथ]<BR>—1 A village.<BR>—2 The day preceding a Soma sacrifice; or a day of preparation for this<BR> sacrifice; a fast-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसथीय
उपवसथीय, उपवसथ्य <i>a.</i> Selected for an उपवसथ (as a day).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसथ्य
उपवसथीय, उपवसथ्य <i>a.</i> Selected for an उपवसथ (as a day).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्तम्
उपवस्तम् A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसनम्
उपवसनम्<BR>—1 A fast, fasting.<BR>—2 The state of being near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्तिः|उपवस्ति
उपवस्तिः <i>f.</i> Support of life (as food, sleep &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्तृ
उपवस्तृ <i>a.</i> One who fasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवास|उपवासः
उपवास <i>a.</i> Staying near; तेषूपवासान्विबुधानुपोष्य Mb. 3. 118. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासः|उपवास
उपवास + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 A fast; सोपवासस्त्र्यहं वसेत् Y. 1. 175, 3. 190; Ms. 11. 196 (a<BR> fast is a religious act and consists in abstaining from every kind of<BR> sensual gratification).<BR>—2 Kindling a sacred fire.<BR>—3 A fire-altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासक
उपवासक <i>a.</i> Fasting, observing a fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासकम्
उपवासक + .{@-कम्@} A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासिन्
उपवासिन् <i>a.</i> Fasting. दिनोपवासी तु निशामिषाशी जटाधरः सन्<BR> कुलटाभिलाषी । हास्यार्णवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषणम्
उपोषणम् A fast, fasting; नास्ति स्त्रीणां पृथग् यज्ञो न व्रतं नाप्युपोषणम् Ms. 3. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषित|उपोषितं|उपोषितः
उपोषित <i>a.</i> One who has fasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषितम्
उपोषित + .{@-तम्@} A fast, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवह्
उपवह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bear or lead near, lead towards.<BR>—2 To bring about, commence.<BR>—3 To gather together; कृत्स्नगोधनमुपोह्य दिनान्ते Bhāg. 10. 35. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Collected, accumulated, increased, stored up; उपोढतपसाम् Ś. 5. 7;<BR> ˚बलस्य ते M. 5. 1; V. 2. 7; so ˚मदः, ˚हर्षः &c.<BR>—2 Brought near, proximate, near; उपोढकल्याणफलोऽभिरक्षन् Ki. 17. 54, 13. 23.<BR>—3 Arrayed for battle (as an army).<BR>—4 Begun, commenced; तदुपोढं महद्युद्धमन्योन्यवधकाङ्क्षिणोः Rām. 6. 106. 18.<BR> उपोढशब्दा न रथाङ्गनेमयः Ś. 7. 10 causing sound.<BR>—5 Married.<BR>—6 A battle-array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढा
उपोढ + .{@-ढा@} A second, favourite wife; cf. वावाता in Rām. 1. 14. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवहम्
उपवहम् Ved. Anything placed on the neck of an ox under the yoke,<BR> to raise it to the right level for a yoke-fellow of greater height; MW.<BR> cf. Śat. Br. 1. 4. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवहनम्
उपवहनम् (In music) Preliminary singing, humming a tune before<BR> beginning to sing it aloud; M. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाहनम्
उपवाहनम् Carrying to, bringing near; कृतकृत्यं तदात्मानं मेने<BR> तस्योपवाहनात् Rām. 1. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाहिन्
उपवाहिन् <i>a.</i> Flowing towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाह्यः|उपवाह्य
उपवाह्यः, -ह्या<BR>—1 A kingʼs riding elephant (male or female); चन्द्रगुप्तोपवाह्यां गजवशाम् Mu. 2.<BR>—2 A royal vehicle (in general); देवोपवाह्यमक्षय्यं सदा दृष्टिमनःसुखम्<BR> Rām. 7. 15. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाह्या
उपवाह्यः, -ह्या<BR>—1 A kingʼs riding elephant (male or female); चन्द्रगुप्तोपवाह्यां गजवशाम् Mu. 2.<BR>—2 A royal vehicle (in general); देवोपवाह्यमक्षय्यं सदा दृष्टिमनःसुखम्<BR> Rām. 7. 15. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवा
उपवा Ved. Blowing at; वातस्य प्रवामुपवामनु वात्यर्चिः Av. 12. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाकः|उपवाक
उपवाकः<BR>—1 Addressing, speaking to, conversing.<BR>—2 Praising.<BR>—3 Indra-grain (इन्द्रयव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाजनम्
उपवाजनम् A fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासनम्
उपवासनम् A dress, garment (Ved.); यावतीः कृत्याः उपवासने Av. 14. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविचारः|उपविचार
उपविचारः Environs, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविद्
उपविद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>—2 Knowing. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Acquisition.<BR>—2 Investigating, inquiring into, knowledge, practical knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविद्या
उपविद्या<BR>—1 Profane science, inferior kind of knowledge.<BR>—2 Practical knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेदः|उपवेद
उपवेदः ‘Inferior knowledge’, a class of writings subordinate to<BR> the Vedas. There are four such <i>Upavedas</i>,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">Page0461-2</a>]<BR> one being attached to each of the four Vedas:− thus आयुर्वेद or Medicine<BR> to ऋग्वेद; (according to some authorities such as Suśruta it is a<BR> part of the Atharvaveda); धनुर्वेद or military science to यजुर्वेद;<BR> गान्धर्ववेद or Music to सामवेद, and स्थापत्य-शास्त्र-वेद<BR> or Architecture to अथर्ववेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविश्
उपविश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To sit down, take a seat; एवमुक्त्वाऽर्जुनः संख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् Bg. 1. 47.<BR>—2 To sit near to, wait upon.<BR>—3 To pitch a camp, encamp.<BR>—4 To go down, set (as the sun).<BR>—5 To enter upon, practise; as प्रायम् उपविशति; so अनशनोपविष्ट.<BR>—6 To abstain from food, fast; सोऽप्युक्त्वैवमुपाविशत् Bk. 7. 75.<BR>—7 To seize, take possession of. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to sit down,<BR> place or set down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष्ट|उपविष्टः
उपविष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Seated, come to, arrived.<BR>—2 Occupied with, engaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष्टक
उपविष्ट + .{@-क@} <i>a.</i> Firmly settled (said of a foetus which remains in the<BR> womb beyond the usual time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशः|उपवेश
उपवेशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Sitting, sitting down; as in प्रायोपवेशन.<BR>—2 Directing oneʼs mind to, being attached to.<BR>—3 Voiding by stool.<BR>—4 Placing down.<BR>—5 Surrendering; सागरस्योपवेशनम् Rām. 6. 19. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशनम्
उपवेशः, -शनम्<BR>—1 Sitting, sitting down; as in प्रायोपवेशन.<BR>—2 Directing oneʼs mind to, being attached to.<BR>—3 Voiding by stool.<BR>—4 Placing down.<BR>—5 Surrendering; सागरस्योपवेशनम् Rām. 6. 19. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशिन्
उपवेशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sitting.<BR>—2 Devoting oneself to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविश्रम्भय्य
उपविश्रम्भय्य <i>ind.</i> Having inspired with confidence; वैश्रम्भकैरुपसृतानुपविश्रम्भय्य<BR> Bhāg. 5. 26. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेष्टृ
उपवेष्टृ <i>a.</i> One who sits, sitting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविषः|उपविष|उपविषं
उपविषः, -षम्<BR>—1 An artificial poison.<BR>—2 A narcotic, any poisonous drug; अर्कक्षीरं स्नुहीक्षीरं तथैव कलिहारिका ।<BR> धत्तूरः करवीरश्च पञ्च चोपविषाः स्मृताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविषम्
उपविषः, -षम्<BR>—1 An artificial poison.<BR>—2 A narcotic, any poisonous drug; अर्कक्षीरं स्नुहीक्षीरं तथैव कलिहारिका ।<BR> धत्तूरः करवीरश्च पञ्च चोपविषाः स्मृताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविषा
उपविषः, -षम् + .{@-षा@} N. of a plant (अतिविषा) It is a plant used in medicine.<BR> The bark is employed in dying. It is white, red and black (Atis or Betula).<BR> It is also referred to as उपविषाणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीक्ष्
उपवीक्ष् [उप-वि-ईक्ष्] Ā.<BR>—1 To look at or towards.<BR>—2 To regard as fit or proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीणयति
उपवीणयति Den. P. [P. III. 1. 25] To play on the Vīṇā or lute<BR> (before a deity &c.); उपवीणयितुं ययौ रवेरुदगावृत्तिपथेन नारदः<BR> R. 8. 33; N. 6. 65; K. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीणितम्
उपवीणितम् Singing on a lute; श्रुतिसुखमुपवीणितं सहायैः Ki. 10. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीतम्
उपवीतम् [उप-वे-क्त]<BR>—1 Investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>—2 The sacred thread worn by the first three classes of the Hindus; पित्र्यमंशमुपवीतलक्षणं<BR> मातृकं च धनुरूर्जितं दधत् R. 11. 64; मुक्तायज्ञोपवीतानि Ku. 6. 6;<BR> Śi. 1. 7; Ki. 12. 23; Ms. 2. 44, 64, 4. 36, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीतकम्
उपवीतकम् The sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीतिन्
उपवीतिन् <i>a.</i> Wearing the sacred thread. उद्धृते दक्षिणे पाणावुपवीत्युच्यते<BR> द्विजः Ms. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीरम्
उपवीरम् A kind of demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृंह
उपवृंह, -हणम् &c.<BR> See उपबृंह् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृंहणम्
उपवृंह, -हणम् &c.<BR> See उपबृंह् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृत्
उपवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go towards, approach.<BR>—2 To return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्तः|उपवर्त
उपवर्तः A particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्तनम्
उपवर्तनम्<BR>—1 A place for exercise.<BR>—2 A place whether inhabited or not.<BR>—3 A district or <i>Pargaṇā</i>.<BR>—4 A kingdom (राज्य) उपवर्तनमाहर्तुमुद्यतोऽस्म्यहमञ्जसा Śiva B. 31. 11.<BR>—5 A bog, marshy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृत्तिः|उपवृत्ति
उपवृत्तिः Motion towards, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेद|उपवेदः
उपवेद See under उपविद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेषः|उपवेष
उपवेषः Ved. A stick (of green wood) used for stirring the sacrificial<BR> fire; स उपवेषमादत्ते Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवैणवम्
उपवैणवम् The three periods of the day; <i>i. e.</i> morning, mid-day,<BR> and evening (त्रिसंध्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपव्याख्यानम्
उपव्याख्यानम् A supplementary explanation or interpretation; तस्योपव्याख्यानम्<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपव्याघ्रः|उपव्याघ्र
उपव्याघ्रः A small hunting leopard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपव्रजम्
उपव्रजम् <i>ind.</i> Near a cattle pen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशक्
उपशक् €4 U.<BR>—1 To endeavour, help, serve.<BR>—2 To learn, enquire into.<BR>—3 €5 P. To be able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशम्
उपशम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To become calm or quiet, be assuaged; उपशाम्यतु ते बुद्धिः Bk. 20. 5.<BR>—2 To cease, stop; अग्निः, शब्दः, कोपः &c.; cease to speak; K. 110. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To calm, tranquillize.<BR>—2 To appease, pacify, assuage, mitigate.<BR>—3 To extinguish, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशमः|उपशम
उपशमः<BR>—1 Becoming quiet, assuagement, pacification; कुतोऽस्या उपशमः Ve. 3;<BR> मन्युर्दुःसह एष यात्युपशमं नो सान्त्ववादैः स्फुटम् Amaru. 6;<BR> cessation, stopping, extinction.<BR>—2 Relaxation, intermission.<BR>—3 Tranquility, calmness, patience; उपशमशीलाः परमर्षयः Bhāg. 5. 4. 27.<BR> उपशमायनेषु स्वतनयेषु Bhāg. 5. 1. 29. ज्ञानस्योपशमः Bh. 2. 82.<BR>—4 Control or restraint of the senses.<BR>—5 (in Astron.) N. of the twentieth Muhūrta.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपशमक्षयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशमक्षयः|उपशमक्षय
उपशमः + -क्षयः (with Jainas) the destruction of activity &c. through quietism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशमक
उपशमक <i>a.</i> Appeasing, pacifying, affording repose, making patient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशमनम्
उपशमनम्<BR>—1 Quieting, calming, appeasing.<BR>—2 Mitigation, assuagement.<BR>—3 Extinction, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्त|उपशांत
उपशान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Calmed, appeased, pacified.<BR>—2 Calm, tranquil.<BR>—3 Lessened, diminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्तिः|उपशान्ति|उपशांति|उपशांतिः
उपशान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cessation, allaying, quieting, alleviation; आर्तभयोपशान्तये R. 8. 31;<BR> Amaru. 65.<BR>—2 Appeasing, assuaging, pacification, satisfaction (of desires); स्त्रीषु<BR> कामोपशान्तिः (केन दृष्टं श्रुतं वा) Pt. 1. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्तिन्|उपशांतिन्
उपशान्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Appeased, pacified.<BR>—2 Calm, tranquil. ━<i>m.</i> A tame elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशय|उपशयः
उपशय See under उपशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशल्यम्
उपशल्यम् An open place in the vicinity of a town or village, suburb;<BR> अथोपशल्ये रिपुमग्नशल्यः R. 16. 37, 15. 60; Śi. 5. 8; K. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशल्यः|उपशल्य|उपशल्यं
उपशल्यम् + .{@-ल्यः@} A spear, nail (to a door); Mb. 3. 15. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशाखा
उपशाखा A secondary branch, little branch; यथा तरोर्मूलनिषेचनेन<BR> तृप्यन्ति तत्स्कन्धभुजोपशाखाः Bhāg. 4. 31. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्त्वनम्
उपशान्त्वनम् Appeasing (see उपसान्त्वन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिता
उपशायिता Means to cure some disease like the prescribed diet etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशालम्
उपशालम् A place near a house, a court before a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशालम्
उपशालम् + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Near a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशास्त्रम्
उपशास्त्रम् A minor science or treatise. (medicine, music &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिक्षा
उपशिक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR> Learning, training.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिक्षणम्
उपशिक्षा, -क्षणम्<BR> Learning, training.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिङ्घनम्
उपशिङ्घ(ह)नम्<BR>—1 Smelling.<BR>—2 Anything given to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिङ्हनम्
उपशिङ्घ(ह)नम्<BR>—1 Smelling.<BR>—2 Anything given to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशिष्यः|उपशिष्य
उपशिष्यः The pupil of a pupil; शिष्योपशिष्यैरुपगीयमानमवेहि<BR> तन्मण्डनमिश्रधाम Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशी
उपशी €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To lie near. गतासुमेतमुपशेष एहि Rv. 10. 18. 8.<BR>—2 To cohabit.<BR>—3 To do good to, agree with; यन्ममोपशेते Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशय|उपशयः
उपशय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lying by the side of<BR>—2 Productive of happiness or rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशयः|उपशय
उपशय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Lying by the side of.<BR>—2 A lair, ambush; हन्ति नोपशयस्थोऽपि शयालुर्भृगयुर्मृगान् Śi. 2. 80.<BR>—3 Diagnosis by the effect of certain articles of food, or medicine (one<BR> of the five elements of निदान).<BR>—4 Allaying disease by diet, regimen &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशया
उपशय + .{@-या@} A prepared piece of clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशयस्थ
उपशय + .{@-स्थ@} <i>a.</i> Lying in ambush (as a hunter); see उपशयः (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायः|उपशाय
उपशायः Sleeping in turn, rotation for sleeping with (another who<BR> keeps watch at night). ‘उपशायोपशायश्च पर्यायशयनार्थकाः’; cf.<BR> निशोपशायः कर्तव्यः फलोच्चायश्च संहतैः Bk. 7. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिन्
उपशायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lying near to.<BR>—2 Sleeping, going to bed.<BR>—3 Allaying, calming.<BR>—4 Composing or narcotic (in medicine); {@˚ता, -त्वम्@} tranquilling;<BR> calming, secondary means of cure (as diet &c.).<BR>—5 One who keeps watch; रावणस्योपशायिन्यो ददर्श हरिसत्तमः Rām. 5. 6. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशीर्षकम्
उपशीर्षकम्<BR>—1 A kind of disease of the head.<BR>—2 A necklace of pearls with five big pearls uniform in size at the centre; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशुभ्
उपशुभ् Ā. To be beautiful, brilliant; उपशुम्भमान Bhāg. 5. 17. 13.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> P. To adorn, ornament, decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोभनम्
उपशोभनम्, -शोभा<BR> Adorning, ornamenting; विहितोपशोभमुपयाति माधवे<BR> (नगर) Śi. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोभा
उपशोभनम्, -शोभा<BR> Adorning, ornamenting; विहितोपशोभमुपयाति माधवे<BR> (नगर) Śi. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशूर
उपशूर <i>a.</i> Inferior to the brave; उपशूरं न ते वृत्तं कथं<BR> रात्रिंचराधम Bk. 8. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोषः|उपशोष
उपशोषः, उपशोषणम् Drying up, withering; शत्रुरक्षोमयं<BR> तोयमुपशोषं नयिष्यति Rām. 5. 37. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोषणम्
उपशोषः, उपशोषणम् Drying up, withering; शत्रुरक्षोमयं<BR> तोयमुपशोषं नयिष्यति Rām. 5. 37. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्री
उपश्री <i>f.</i> Covering, anything thrown above or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रु
उपश्रु €5 P. (€1 P. also)<BR>—1 To hear, listen; यावदस्या गोपतिर्नोपशृणुयाद्वचः स्वयम् Av. 12. 4. 27;<BR> तदु ह जानश्रुतिः पौत्रायण उपशुश्राव Ch. Up. 4. 1. 5.<BR> वचः, गिरः &c.<BR>—2 To promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुत्
उपश्रुत् <i>m.</i> A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुत|उपश्रुतं
उपश्रुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heard; तस्मात्परोक्षेऽस्मदुपश्रुतान्यलङ्करिष्यथ स्तोत्रमपीच्यवाचः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 15. 23.<BR>—2 Promised, agreed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुतिः|उपश्रुति
उपश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Hearing, listening.<BR>—2 Range of hearing.<BR>—3 A supernatural voice heard at night, and personified as a nocturnal<BR> deity revealing the future; नक्तं निर्गत्य यत्किंचिच्छुभाशुभकरं वचः ।<BR> श्रूयते तद्विदुर्धीरा देवप्रश्नमुपश्रुतिम् ॥ Hārāvalī; परिजनोऽपि<BR> चास्याः सततमुपश्रुत्यै निर्जगाम K. 65.<BR>—4 Aspect of the stars, fortune-telling.<BR>—5 Promise, assent.<BR>—6 Rumour, report; नोपश्रुतिं कटुकां नोत मुक्ताम् Mb. 5. 30. 5.<BR>—7 Inclusion, incorporation (अन्तर्भाव); यथा त्रयाणां वर्णानां<BR> संख्यातोपश्रुतिः पुरा Mb. 12. 64. 6.<BR>—8 N. of a deity; अनेनैव व्रतेन तपसा चान्विता देवीं वरदामुपश्रुतिमाह्वय<BR> Mb. 12. 342. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रोतृ
उपश्रोतृ <i>a.</i> Listening, hearing; उपश्रोता म ईवतो वचांसि Rv. 7. 23. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लिष्
उपश्लिष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To embrace.<BR>—2 To draw near, approach. ━<i>Caus.</i> To bring near, place at hand;<BR> उपश्लेषय रथम् V. 1; -शरम् V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लिष्ट
उपश्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Placed near, contiguous, adjoining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लेषः|उपश्लेष
उपश्लेषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Juxta-position, contact.<BR>—2 An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लेषणम्
उपश्लेषः, -षणम्<BR>—1 Juxta-position, contact.<BR>—2 An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लोकः|उपश्लोक
उपश्लोकः N. of the father of the tenth Manu; दशमो ब्रह्मसावर्णिरुपश्लोकसुतो<BR> महान् Bhāg. 8. 13. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्लोकयति
उपश्लोकयति Den. P. [P. III. 1. 25.] To extol or praise in verses;<BR> समुत्तेजनसमर्थैः श्लोकैरुपश्लोकयितव्यः Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्वस|उपश्वसः
उपश्वस <i>a.</i> Ved. Sounding, roaring;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्वसः|उपश्वस
उपश्वस + .{@-सः@} Breeze, draught of air; उपश्वसे द्रुवये सीदता यूयम् Av. 11. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपष्टम्भक|उपष्टम्भकः
उपष्टम्भक <i>a.</i> Strengthening. उपष्टम्भकं चलं च रजः Sāṅ. K. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपष्टुत्
उपष्टुत् <i>ind.</i> Ved. (Ready) At oneʼs call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंयत
उपसंयत <i>a.</i> Closely joined, wedged in; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंयमः|उपसंयम
उपसंयमः<BR>—1 Curbing, restraining, binding.<BR>—2 The end of the world, universal destruction; यां विलोक्य प्रजास्त्रस्ता<BR> मेनिरेऽस्योपसंयमम् Bhāg. 3. 19. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंयमनम्
उपसंयमनम्<BR>—1 Binding.<BR>—2 A means of fastening together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंयोगः|उपसंयोग
उपसंयोगः A secondary connection; modification; नामाख्यातयोः<BR> कर्मोपसंयोगद्योतकाः Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंरोहः|उपसंरोह
उपसंरोहः Growing together or over, cicatrizing; शल्यमार्गानुपसंरोहः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंवादः|उपसंवाद
उपसंवादः An agreement, a contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंव्यानम्
उपसंव्यानम् An under garment; अन्तरं बहिर्योगोपसंव्यानयोः P. I. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंव्रज्
उपसंव्रज् P. To step into, enter; अगारमुपसंव्रजेत् Ms. 6. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंस्कृ
उपसंस्कृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To prepare (as a meal).<BR>—2 To ornament.<BR>—3 To consecrate, purify; K. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंस्करणम्
उपसंस्करणम् Preparing, purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंसृष्ट
उपसंसृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 United with, joined together.<BR>—2 Afflicted, blasted (by curse); ब्रह्मशापोपसंसृष्टे स्वकुले Bhāg. 11. 30. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंस्कृत
उपसंस्कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Prepared, dressed, cooked.<BR>—2 Adorned, filled with; अमृतोपमतोयाभिः शिवाभिरुपसंस्कृताः Rām. 5. 14. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृ
उपसंहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw or bring together, collect.<BR>—2 To sum or wind up, conclude; इदानीमुपसंहरति; प्रकृतमुपसंहरति<BR> Kull. on Ms. 1. 57.<BR>—3 To contract; as कूर्मोऽङ्गानि.<BR>—4 To withdraw, take away, withhold; छेत्तुः पार्श्वगतां छायां नोपसंहरते<BR> द्रुमः H. 1. 59.<BR>—5 To check, stop, curb.<BR>—6 To absorb, destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहरणम्
उपसंहरणम्<BR>—1 Withdrawing, taking away or back.<BR>—2 Refusing, withholding.<BR>—3 Excluding.<BR>—4 Attacking, invading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहारः|उपसंहार
उपसंहारः<BR>—1 Drawing in or together, contracting; क्रियतामुपसंहारो गुर्वर्थं<BR> द्विजसत्तम Mb. 5. 116. 13.<BR>—2 Drawing away, withdrawing, excluding, withholding. अजानन्नुपसंहारं<BR> प्राणकृच्छ्रमुपस्थिते Bhāg. 1. 7. 20.<BR>—3 A collection, assemblage; न तु धर्मोपसंहारमधर्मफलसंहितम्<BR> Rām. 5. 51 28.<BR>—4 Summing up, winding up, conclusion (opp. उपक्रम).<BR>—5 A preparation (of a speech &c.).<BR>—6 A compendium, resume.<BR>—7 Brevity, conciseness.<BR>—8 Perfection.<BR>—9 Destruction, death, end.<BR>—10 Attacking, invading.<BR>—11 (In logic) Refutation.<BR>—12 N. of the concluding chapters in several books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहारिन्
उपसंहारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Comprehending.<BR>—2 Exclusive. ━<i>m.</i> A <i>hetu</i> (हेतु) which is not exclusive;<BR> see अनुपसंहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृतिः|उपसंहृति
उपसंहृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Comprehension.<BR>—2 Seizing, taking.<BR>—3 End, conclusion.<BR>—4 The catastrophe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंकॢप्त|उपसङ्कॢप्त
उपसंकॢप्त <i>a.</i> Put above, being above; तत्र तत्रोपसंकॢप्तैर्लसन्मकरतोरणैः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 9. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंक्रान्त|उपसङ्क्रान्त
उपसंक्रान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Handed down.<BR>—2 Turned to, changed into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंक्षेपः|उपसङ्क्षेप
उपसंक्षेपः An abstract, summary, resume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंख्यानम्
उपसंख्यानम्<BR>—1 Addition.<BR>—2 Supplementary addition, further or additional enumeration (a term technically<BR> applied to the <i>Vārtikas</i> of Kātyāyana which are intended to supply<BR> omissions in Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras and generally to supplement them); <i>e. g.</i><BR> जुगुप्साविरामप्रमादार्थानामुपसंख्यानम्; cf. इष्टि.<BR>—3 (In gram.) A substitute in form or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्रह्|उपसङ्ग्रह्
उपसंग्रह् €9 P.<BR>—1 To take upon oneself, experience, feel, suffer.<BR>—2 To receive, accept.<BR>—3 To seize, catch hold of; पाणिभ्यां तूपसंगृह्य Ms. 3. 224.<BR>—4 To take into custody or possession.<BR>—5 To win over, conciliate, make favourable; पिण्डदानादिनोपसंगृह्य Dk. 58.<BR>—6 To clasp, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्रहः|उपसङ्ग्रह
उपसंग्रहः, -हणम्<BR>—1 Keeping pleased, supporting, maintaining; तीक्ष्णरसदायिनामुपसंग्रहार्थम् Mu. 2.<BR>—2 Respectful salutation (as by touching the feet of the person saluted);<BR> स्फुरति रभसात्पाणिः पादोपसंग्रहणाय च Mv. 2. 30.<BR>—3 Accepting, adopting; Br. Sūt. 1. 4. 41.<BR>—4 Polite address, obeisance.<BR>—5 Collecting, joining.<BR>—6 Taking, accepting (as a wife); दारोपसंग्रहः Y. 1. 56.<BR>—7 (An external) appendage, any necessary article either for use or decoration<BR> (उपकरण).<BR>—8 A pillow, cushion; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्रहणम्
उपसंग्रहः, -हणम्<BR>—1 Keeping pleased, supporting, maintaining; तीक्ष्णरसदायिनामुपसंग्रहार्थम् Mu. 2.<BR>—2 Respectful salutation (as by touching the feet of the person saluted);<BR> स्फुरति रभसात्पाणिः पादोपसंग्रहणाय च Mv. 2. 30.<BR>—3 Accepting, adopting; Br. Sūt. 1. 4. 41.<BR>—4 Polite address, obeisance.<BR>—5 Collecting, joining.<BR>—6 Taking, accepting (as a wife); दारोपसंग्रहः Y. 1. 56.<BR>—7 (An external) appendage, any necessary article either for use or decoration<BR> (उपकरण).<BR>—8 A pillow, cushion; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्राह्य
उपसंग्राह्य <i>a.</i> To be respectfully saluted, respectable, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसञ्ज्
उपसञ्ज् €6 Ā. To be attached to, fond of; अथापि नोपसज्जेत स्त्रीषु<BR> स्त्रैणेषु चार्थवित् Bhāg. 11. 26. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसक्त
उपसक्त <i>a.</i> Attached to (worldly desires); Rām. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद्
उपसद् €1. €6 P.<BR>—1 To sit near to, go near, approach; अथ हैनं प्रस्तोता उपससाद<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 11. 4. उपसेदुर्दशग्रीवम् Bk. 9. 92, 3. 12, 6. 135.<BR>—2 To sit at the feet of; उपाध्यायमुपासदम् Ks. 108. 21.<BR>—3 To wait upon, serve; (तं) आकल्पसाधनैस्तैस्तैरुपसेदुः प्रसाधकाः<BR> R. 17. 22; Śi. 13. 24.<BR>—4 To march against.<BR>—5 To try to get or obtain.<BR>—6 To sink down. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To place near.<BR>—2 To lead towards.<BR>—3 To get, find.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसत्तिः|उपसत्ति
उपसत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Connection, union.<BR>—2 Service, worship, attendance upon.<BR>—3 Gift, donation.<BR>—4 Informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद्
उपसद् <i>a.</i> Serving, waiting upon. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Siege, assault, attack.<BR>—2 Laying up, accumulating.<BR>—3 Service, worship.<BR>—4 N. of a ceremony, forming part of the ज्योतिष्ठोम ceremony, and<BR> lasting for several days. दीक्षानुजन्मोपसदः शिरोधरम् Bhāg. 3. 13. 37.<BR>—5 N. of a sacrificial fire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपसद्व्रतिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद्व्रतिन्
उपसद् + -व्रतिन् <i>a.</i> observing the rules of the <i>Upasad</i>, <i>i. e.</i> drinking<BR> milk in certain quantities, sleeping on the bare earth, keeping silence<BR> &c. द्वादशाहमुपसद्व्रती भूत्वा Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद|उपसदः
उपसद <i>a.</i> Going near to, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसदः|उपसद
उपसद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Approach.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR>—3 The उपसद् sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसदनम्
उपसदनम्<BR>—1 Going near to, approaching.<BR>—2 Sitting at the feet of a teacher, becoming a pupil; Mb. 1. 132. 5;<BR> तत्रोपसदनं चक्रे द्रोणस्येष्वस्त्रकर्मणि Mb.<BR>—3 Neighbourhood.<BR>—4 Service.<BR>—5 Partaking of.<BR>—6 An abode, place; यज्ञोपसदनं ब्रह्मन्प्राप्तोऽसि मुनिभिः सह Rām. 1. 50. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसदी
उपसदी Ved.<BR>—1 A body of attendants (collectively).<BR>—2 Continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्न|उपसन्नः
उपसन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Approached; अङ्गिरसं विधिवदुपसन्नः Muṇḍ. 1. 1. 3, 1. 2. 13;<BR> Praśna. Up. 1. 1. 13; रुद्धा गुहाः किमजितोऽवति नोपसन्नान् Bhāg. 2. 2. 5;<BR> near, approximate.<BR>—2 Worshipped, served.<BR>—3 Serving, waiting upon.<BR>—4 Easily obtainable; got, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसादनम्
उपसादनम् Approaching respectfully, reverence, respect; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंतानः|उपसन्तान|उपसंतान
उपसंतानः<BR>—1 Immediate connection.<BR>—2 A descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंधा|उपसन्धा
उपसंधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To put together, add, increase.<BR>—2 To join, connect; त्रिवर्गेणोपसंधत्ते Kām. 1. 13.<BR>—3 To aim at, direct towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहित
उपसंहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Connected with, furnished or endowed with; श्रुतवृत्तोपसंहितः Mb.<BR>—2 Accompanied or surrounded by; regarding, referring to.<BR>—3 Attached to, devoted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंधानम्
उपसंधानम् Adding, joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंध्यम्|उपसन्ध्यम्
उपसंध्यम् <i>ind.</i> About twilight; उपसंध्यमास्त तनु सानुमतः Śi. 9. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंन्यासः|उपसन्न्यास
उपसंन्यासः Laying down, giving up, resignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसमाधा
उपसमाधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To put on (as fuel on fire).<BR>—2 To arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसमाधानम्
उपसमाधानम् Gathering together, heaping; उपसमाधानं राशीकरणम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसमाहार्य
उपसमाहार्य <i>a.</i> To be brought together; or arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंपद्|उपसम्पद्
उपसंपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To come to, arrive at; गान्धारानेवोपसंपद्येत Ch. Up. 6. 14. 2;<BR> परं ज्योतिरुपसंपद्य Ch. Up. 8. 3. 4. तं देशमुपसंपेदे Mb.<BR>—2 To get, obtain. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bring or lead near.<BR>—2 To give, grant.<BR>—3 To receive into the order of priests, ordain. (Buddh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंपत्तिः|उपसम्पत्ति|उपसंपत्ति
उपसंपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approaching, arriving at.<BR>—2 Entering into any condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंपन्न|उपसम्पन्न|उपसम्पन्नः
उपसंपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gained, obtained. भ्रातृत्वमुपसंपन्नौ परिष्वज्य परस्परम् Rām. 7. 35. 42.<BR>—2 Arrived at.<BR>—3 Furnished with, possessing; कुसुमैरुपसंपन्ना नदी Rām.<BR>—4 Familiar with.<BR>—5 Enough, sufficient.<BR>—6 Killed at a sacrifice (as an animal), immolated.<BR>—7 Dead, deceased.<BR>—8 Cooked, dressed (as food).<BR>—9 Staying or dwelling in the same house; श्रोत्रिये तूपसंपन्ने M. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंपन्नम्
उपसंपन्न + .{@-न्नम्@} Condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंभाषः
