उपसुन्दः|उपसुन्द|उपसुंदः
उपसुन्दः N. of an Asura, son of Nikumbha and younger brother of Sunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसूर्यकम्
उपसूर्यकम् The disc of the sun or its halo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसूर्यकः|उपसूर्यक|उपसूर्यकं|उपसूर्य्यक|उपसूर्य्यकं
उपसूर्यकम् + .{@-कः@} A fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृ
उपसृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To go towards, approach, draw near; वरुणं पितरमुपससार T. Up. 3. 1. 1 etc.<BR> राजानं … दुर्गं … उपसृत्य &c. वल्लभाभिरुपसृत्य<BR> चक्रिरे साभिभुक्तविषयाः समागमाः R. 19. 16.<BR>—2 To go against, attack.<BR>—3 To have intercourse (as of a woman with a man); Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर|उपसरः
उपसर <i>a.</i> P. III. 3. 71 Approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसरः|उपसर
उपसर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Approaching (as a cow). प्रजनः स्यादुपसरः cf. also उपसरो<BR> हि स्त्रीगवीषु पुङ्गवानामभिगमनमुच्यते स च नैरन्तर्येण भवति.<BR>—2 The first pregnancy of a cow; गवामुपसरः Sk.<BR>—3 A continuous line. वीनामुपसरं दृष्ट्वा .. Bk. 7. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसरणम्
उपसरणम्^1<BR>—1 Going towards.<BR>—2 Rapid flowing of the blood towards the heart (as in sickness).<BR>—3 That which is approached as a refuge.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्या|उपसर्य्या
उपसर्या A cow fit for a bull (cf. P. III. 1. 104). उपसर्या काल्या<BR> प्रजने वृषो यथोपसर्याया गोष्ठे गोर्दण्डताडितः Bk. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृज्
उपसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To pour out or on, offer (water &c.).<BR>—2 To add to, annex; to join, attach, connect with, bring to; एता देवताः<BR> पाप्मभिरुपासृजन् Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 6.<BR>—3 To beset with, oppress, infest; तेनोपसृष्टो यस्तस्य लक्षणानि निबोधत<BR> Y. 1. 272; Ms. 4. 61; see उपसृष्ट below; रोषेण, व्याधिना &c.<BR>—4 To eclipse; Ms. 4. 37.<BR>—5 To come in contact with.<BR>—6 To produce, effect, create; उपसृज्य तमस्तीव्रं जहाराश्वं पुनर्हरिः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 19. 19.<BR>—7 To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्गः|उपसर्ग
उपसर्गः<BR>—1 Sickness, disease, change occasioned by a disease; also a disease superinduced<BR> on another; क्षीणं हन्युश्चोपसर्गाः प्रभूताः Suśr.<BR>—2 Misfortune, trouble, calamity, injury, harm; प्रशामिताशेषोपसर्गाः<BR> प्रजाः Ratn. 1. 10; सोपसर्गं वो नक्षत्रम् M. 4 sorrow; आपेदे<BR> उपसर्गस्तं तमः सूर्यमिवासुरम् Rām. 2. 63. 2.<BR>—3 Portent, natural phenomenon foreboding evil.<BR>—4 An eclipse.<BR>—5 An indication or symptom of death.<BR>—6 Addition.<BR>—7 Possession<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">Page0465-2</a>]<BR> by an evil spirit.<BR>—8 A preposition prefixed to roots; निपाताश्चादयो ज्ञेयाः प्रादयस्तूपसर्गकाः ।<BR> द्योतकत्वात् क्रियायोगे लोकादवगता इमे ॥ उपसर्गास्तु विज्ञेयाः क्रियायोगेन<BR> विंशतिः । विवेचयन्ति ते ह्यर्थं नामाख्यातविभक्तिषु ॥ बृहद्देवता; आख्यातमुपगृह्यार्थविशेषमिमे<BR> तस्यैव सृजन्तीत्युपसर्गाः । Durga under Nirukta 1. 3. उपेत्य नामाख्यातयोरर्थस्य<BR> विशेषं सृजन्त्युत्पादयन्तीत्युपसर्गाः । Skanda P. The नाट्यशास्त्र<BR> defines उपसर्ग thus: प्रातिपदिकार्थयुक्तं धात्वर्थमुपसृजन्ति<BR> ये स्वार्थैः । उपसर्गा उपदिष्टास्तस्मात् संस्कारशास्त्रेऽस्मिन् ॥ A poetaster<BR> has framed the following समस्यापूरण stanza with the rule उपसर्गाः<BR> क्रियायोगे (Pāṇini I. 4. 59): उपसर्गाः क्रियायोगे पाणिनेरपि संमतम् ।<BR> निष्कियोऽपि तवारातिः सोपसर्गः सदा कथम् ॥ <i>Upasargas</i> are 20<BR> in number:− प्र, परा, अप, सम्, अनु, अव, निस् or निर्, दुस्<BR> or दुर्, वि, आ(ङ्), नि, अधि, अपि, अति, सु, उत्, अभि, प्रति, परि,<BR> उप; or 22 if निस्-निर् and दुस्-दुर् be taken as separate words.<BR> There are two theories as to the character of these prepositions. According<BR> to one theory roots have various meanings in themselves (अनेकार्था हि<BR> धातवः); when prepositions are prefixed to them they simply bring to<BR> light those meanings already existent but hidden in them, but they do<BR> not <i>express</i> them, being meaningless themselves; cf. Śi. 10. 15:− सन्तमेव<BR> चिरमप्रकृतत्वादप्रकाशितमदिद्युतदङ्गे । विभ्रमं मधुमदः प्रमदानां<BR> धातुलीनमुपसर्ग इवार्थम् ॥ According to the other theory prepositions<BR> <i>express</i> their own independent meanings; they modify, intensify, and<BR> sometimes entirely alter, the senses of roots; cf. Sk.:− उपसर्गेण<BR> धात्वर्थो बलादन्यत्र नीयते । प्रहाराहारसंहारविहारपरिहारवत् ॥<BR> cf. also धात्वर्थं बाधते कश्चित्कश्चित्तमनुवर्तते । तमेव विशिनष्टपन्य<BR> उपसर्गगतिस्त्रिधा ॥ (The latter theory appears to be more correct.<BR> For a fuller exposition see Nirukta).<BR>—9 An obstacle; ते समाधावुपसर्गा व्युत्थाने सिद्धयः । योगसूत्रs 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जनम्
उपसर्जनम्<BR>—1 Pouring on.<BR>—2 A misfortune, calamity (as an eclipse), portent; ज्योतिषां चोपसर्जने<BR> (अनध्यायान्) Ms. 4. 105.<BR>—3 Leaving.<BR>—4 Eclipsing.<BR>—5 Any person or thing subordinate to another, a substitute.<BR>—6 (In gram.) A word which either by composition or derivation loses its<BR> original independent character, while it also determines the sense of<BR> another word (opp. प्रधान); <i>e. g.</i> in पाणिनीयः a pupil of<BR> पाणिनि, पाणिनि becomes उपसर्जन; or in राजपुरुषः, राजन्<BR> is उपसर्जन, having lost its independent character; P. I. 2. 43, 48, 57, II. 2. 30, IV. 1. 14, 54, VI. 3. 82;<BR> आचार्योपसर्जनश्चान्तेवासी.<BR>—7 A kind of war-manoeuvre; तथा प्राग्भवनं चापसरणं तूपसर्जनम्<BR> Śuka. Up. 4. 1105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जित
उपसर्जित <i>a.</i> Sent off or out; तक्षकादात्मनो मृत्युं द्विजपुत्रोपसर्जितान्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 12. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Joined, connected with, accompanied by; किं क्षत्रबन्धून्कलिलोपसृष्टान्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 16. 23.<BR>—2 Seized or possessed by (a demon or evil spirit); उपसृष्टा इव क्षुद्राधिष्ठितभवनाः K. 107.<BR>—3 Troubled, affected, injured; (उपसृष्टः परेणोति मूर्च्छितो गदया<BR> हतः Bhāg. 10. 76. 33; रोगोपसृष्टतनुर्दुर्वसतिं मुमुक्षुः R. 8. 94; K. 289.)<BR>—4 Eclipsed;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">Page0466-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 13. 104. 18; Ms. 4. 37.<BR>—5 Furnished with an उपसर्ग (as a root); कुधद्रुहोरुपसृष्टयोः<BR> कर्म P. I. 4. 38.<BR>—6 Let loose, thrown off; अश्वत्थाम्नोपसृष्टेन ब्रह्मशीर्ष्णोरुतेजसा ।<BR> उत्तराया हतो गर्भ ईशेनाजीवितः पुनः Bhāg. 1. 12. 1.<BR>—8 Ruined; कालोपसृष्टनिगमावन आत्तयोगमायाकृतिं परमहंसगतिं<BR> नताः स्म Bhāg. 10. 83. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्टः|उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं
उपसृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} The sun or moon when eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्टम्
उपसृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृप्
उपसृप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To approach, move towards, draw near to; ममोपान्तिकमुपसर्पन् M. 1, 1. 12.<BR>—2 To meet unexpectedly.<BR>—3 To move, go; प्रतिवातं न हि घनः कदाचिदुपसर्पति Pt. 3. 23;<BR> so प्रलयम्, दुःखम् &c.<BR>—4 To begin (with inf.); to become ready; अजीगर्तः सुतं हन्तुमुपासर्पद्<BR> बुभुक्षितः Ms. 10. 105.<BR>—5 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पः|उपसर्प
उपसर्पः<BR>—1 Approach, access.<BR>—2 Following a person.<BR>—3 An elephant in the third year; दृढतररदपङ्क्तिश्चोपसर्पस्तृतीये<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पणम्
उपसर्पणम् Going near, approaching, advancing towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पिन्
उपसर्पिन् <i>a.</i> Going near, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेक्तृ
उपसेक्तृ <i>a.</i> One who sprinkles or pours down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेचन
उपसेचन <i>a.</i> Pouring, sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेचनम्
उपसेचन + .{@-नम्, उपसेकः@}<BR>—1 Pouring or sprinkling upon, watering; मृत्युर्यस्योपसेचनम् Kaṭh. 2. 25.<BR>—2 Infusion; juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेकः|उपसेक
उपसेचन + .{@-नम्, उपसेकः@}<BR>—1 Pouring or sprinkling upon, watering; मृत्युर्यस्योपसेचनम् Kaṭh. 2. 25.<BR>—2 Infusion; juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेचनी
उपसेचन + .{@-नी@} A ladle or cup for pouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेव्
उपसेव् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To serve, worship, honour; वैरिणं नोपसेवते Ms. 4. 133.<BR>—2 To practise, follow, pursue, cultivate; as a vow; तान् सर्वानेवोपसेवेत<BR> Ch. Up. 2. 22. 1.<BR>—3 To make use of.<BR>—4 To be addicted to, enjoy; अधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते<BR> Bg. 15. 9; so सुखम्, संधिम्, विग्रहम् &c.<BR>—5 To frequent, inhabit.<BR>—6 To rub or anoint with (sandal &c.).<BR>—7 To have sexual intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवक
उपसेवक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Worshipping, serving.<BR>—2 Following, practising.<BR>—3 Enjoying (carnally); परदारोपसेवकः Y. 3. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवनम्
उपसेवनम्, -सेवा<BR>—1 Worshipping, honouring, adoring.<BR>—2 Service; राज˚ Ms. 3. 64.<BR>—3 Addiction to; विषय˚ Ms. 12. 7.<BR>—4 Using, enjoying (carnally also); छाया˚; परदार˚ Ms. 4. 134.<BR>—5 Experiencing, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवा
उपसेवनम्, -सेवा<BR>—1 Worshipping, honouring, adoring.<BR>—2 Service; राज˚ Ms. 3. 64.<BR>—3 Addiction to; विषय˚ Ms. 12. 7.<BR>—4 Using, enjoying (carnally also); छाया˚; परदार˚ Ms. 4. 134.<BR>—5 Experiencing, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेविन्
उपसेविन् <i>a.</i> Serving, practising; Rām. 5. 29. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कन्न
उपस्कन्न <i>a.</i> Agitated, afflicted; स्नेहोपस्कन्नहृदया तदा<BR> मोहमुपागमत् Rām. 6. 111. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृ
उपस्कृ €8 U. To prepare, elaborate, perfect, adorn; (see उपकृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्करः|उपस्कर
उपस्करः<BR>—1 Any article which serves to make anything complete, an ingredient;<BR> यथा कीडोपस्कराणां संयोगविगमाविह । इच्छया कीडितुः स्यातां तथैवेशेच्छया<BR> नृणाम् ॥ Bhāg. 1. 13. 43; Rām. 2. 30. 44.<BR>—2 (Hence) Condiment or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">Page0466-2</a>]<BR> seasoning for food (as mustard, pepper &c.)<BR>—3 Furniture, appurtenance, apparatus, instrument (उपकरण); उपस्करो<BR> रथस्यासीत् Mb.; Śi. 18. 72.<BR>—4 Any article or implement of household use (such as a broomstick); संयतोपस्करा<BR> दक्षा Y. 1. 83, 2. 193; Ms. 3. 68, 12. 66, 5. 150.<BR>—5 An ornament.<BR>—6 Censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्करणम्
उपस्करणम्<BR>—1 Killing, injuring.<BR>—2 A collection.<BR>—3 A change, modification.<BR>—4 An ellipsis.<BR>—5 Blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कारः|उपस्कार
उपस्कारः<BR>—1 Anything additional, a supplement.<BR>—2 (Supplying) An ellipsis; वानप्रस्थानां च द्रव्योपस्कार इति Mb. 12. 191. 11.<BR> साकाङ्क्षमनुपस्कारं विष्वग्गति निराकुलम् Ki. 11. 38.<BR>—3 Beautifying, ornamenting by way of adding grace; उक्तमेवार्थं सोपस्कारमाह<BR> Malli. on R. 11. 47.<BR>—4 An ornament; सोपस्काराः प्रावहन्नस्रतोयाः Śi. 18. 72.<BR>—5 A stroke.<BR>—6 A collection.<BR>—7 Condiment, seasoning material; उपस्कारैः स्कारैरुपचितरसामोदभरणम्<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 472.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृत
उपस्कृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Prepared, perfected; तत्स्पर्शनाद् भूय उपस्कृताकृतिः Bhāg. 10. 88. 19.<BR>—2 Censured, blamed.<BR>—3 Killed, injured.<BR>—4 Collected.<BR>—5 Beautified, ornamented.<BR>—6 Supplied (as ellipsis).<BR>—7 Modified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृतिः|उपस्कृति
उपस्कृतिः <i>f.</i> Supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भ्|उपस्तंभ्
उपस्तम्भ् €5. €9 P. To prop, support (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तब्ध
उपस्तब्ध <i>a.</i> Supported, stayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भः|उपस्तम्भ|उपस्तंभ|उपस्तंभः
उपस्तम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR>—1 Stay, support.<BR>—2 Support of life (as food, sleep &c.).<BR>—3 Encouragement, incitement, aid; मन्त्रोपस्तम्भेन H. 3.<BR>—4 Basis, ground, occasion; मूषकबलोपस्तम्भेन कारणेन भवितव्यम् H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भनम्
उपस्तम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR>—1 Stay, support.<BR>—2 Support of life (as food, sleep &c.).<BR>—3 Encouragement, incitement, aid; मन्त्रोपस्तम्भेन H. 3.<BR>—4 Basis, ground, occasion; मूषकबलोपस्तम्भेन कारणेन भवितव्यम् H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भक|उपस्तंभक
उपस्तम्भक <i>a.</i> Supporting, aiding, encouraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भकता
उपस्तम्भक + .{@-ता@} Abundance, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तरणम्
उपस्तरणम् See under उपस्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तिः|उपस्ति
उपस्तिः Ved.<BR>—1 A tree.<BR>—2 An attendant, a follower, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तु
उपस्तु €2 U.<BR>—1 To praise, extol; उप त्वा नमस्म वयं होतर्वैश्वानर स्तुमः Av. 3. 15. 7.<BR>—2 To invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुत्
उपस्तुत् <i>f.</i> Ved. Praise, invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तवः|उपस्तव
उपस्तवः, उपस्तुतिः <i>f.</i> Invocation, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुतिः|उपस्तुति
उपस्तवः, उपस्तुतिः <i>f.</i> Invocation, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तृ
उपस्तृ, -स्तॄ €5. €9 U.<BR>—1 To spread out (for another); spread under; उप स्तृणीतमत्रये हिमेन<BR> धर्ममश्विना Rv. 8. 73. 3.<BR>—2 To strew or cover with.<BR>—3 To arrange, set in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तॄ
उपस्तृ, -स्तॄ €5. €9 U.<BR>—1 To spread out (for another); spread under; उप स्तृणीतमत्रये हिमेन<BR> धर्ममश्विना Rv. 8. 73. 3.<BR>—2 To strew or cover with.<BR>—3 To arrange, set in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तरणम्
उपस्तरणम्<BR>—1 Spreading out, scattering.<BR>—2 A covering, garment; तद् वै ब्रह्मज्य ते देवा उपस्तरणमब्रुवन् Av. 5. 19. 12.<BR>—3 A bed.<BR>—4 Anything spread out (as a covering), a substratum (said of the water<BR> which is sipped before taking food) अमृतोपस्तरणमसि स्वाहा. Scattering<BR> grass (around sacred fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तिर्
उपस्तिर् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Spreading.<BR>—2 A covering, what is spread; अभि शुक्रामुपस्तिरम् Rv. 9. 62. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तीर्ण
उपस्तीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spread; scattered over.<BR>—2 Clothed, wrapped.<BR>—3 Poured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्त्री
उपस्त्री <i>f.</i> [गौणी स्त्री] A concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्था
उपस्था €1 U. (cf. P. I. 3. 25-6 and Vārt. 1)<BR>—1 To stand near; fall to oneʼs share; नादत्तमुपतिष्ठति Pt. 2. 127<BR> remain; विष्टभ्य पादावुपतिष्ठते श्रीः Mu. 4. 13.<BR>—2 To come near, approach; मामुपतिष्ठस्व Mu. 1 come to me; रामं<BR> मुनिरुपस्थितः R. 15. 76; Ku. 2. 64; Pt. 1. राजद्वारम् U. 1; R. 1. 45, 87, 2. 39, 15. 15.<BR>—3 To wait or attend upon, serve; नाटकेनोपस्थातव्यमस्माभिः Ś. 1.<BR> We must wait upon (serve) (the audience) with a play; Ms. 2. 48, 3. 189;<BR> पुरा शकमुपस्थाय R. 1. 75, 14. 24; U. 1.<BR>—4 To approach with prayers, worship (said to be Ātm. only in this sense);<BR> ये सूर्यमुपतिष्ठन्ते मन्त्रैः Bk. 8. 13; न त्र्यम्बकादन्यमुपास्थितासौ 1. 3;<BR> Ku. 2. 3; R. 4. 6, 10. 63, 17. 10, 18. 22; Māl.; U. 2, 3, 7; सख्येन<BR> मामुपतिष्ठते treats me as a friend.<BR>—5 To be or remain near, stay with.<BR>—6 To go to with the desire of getting (P. or Ā.); प्रभुमुपतिष्ठति-ते Sk.<BR>—7 To approach for intercourse; कं रहस्युपतिष्ठसे Bk. 5. 68; पतिमुपतिष्ठते नारी Vop.<BR>—8 To meet, join (as a river) (Ā.); गङ्गा यमुनामुपतिष्ठते Sk.<BR>—9 To form friendship with, make a friend of; रथिकानुपतिष्ठते Sk.;<BR> उपास्थितैवमुक्ते तं सखायं राघवः पितुः Bk. 6. 42; सन्तमुपतिष्ठते साधुः Vop.<BR>—10 To approach with hostile intentions.<BR>—11 To lead to, go to or reach (Ā.) (as a way); पन्थाः स्रुघ्नमुपतिष्ठते<BR> Sk. (प्राप्नोति); Ms. 3. 76.<BR>—12 To pass over to, devolve upon, fall to the share of; मूलपुरुषावसाने<BR> संपदः परमुपतिष्ठन्ति Ś. 6; Ki. 13. 69; वीरसूरिति शब्दोऽयं<BR> तनयात्त्वामुपस्थितः M. 5. 16, applies to you; R. 8. 2; विपदुत्पत्तिमतामुपस्थिता 8. 83<BR> awaits or falls to the lot of.<BR>—13 To occur, arise; be got; अहोऽस्माकं भोजनमुपस्थितम् H. 1.<BR>—14 To be present (Ā.); स्मृत्युपस्थितौ श्लोकौ U. 6; भोजनकाले उपतिष्ठते Sk.<BR>—15 To stand under for support.<BR>—16 To resort to; वेशमुपतिष्ठन्ति Dk. 60.<BR>—17 To conciliate. ━<i>Caus.</i> (-स्थापयति) —1 To provide, present<BR> with, furnish with; to get ready, prepare; अस्खलितसुखसंपातं रथमुपस्थापय<BR> U. 1; सबाणासनं रथम् Ś. 2.<BR>—2 To place upon or near.<BR>—3 To produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उपस्थ <i>a.</i> Near, approximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थः|उपस्थ
उपस्थ + .{@-स्थः@}<BR>—1 The lap; उपस्थं कृ to make a lap; ˚स्थे कृ to take on the lap.<BR>—2 The middle part in general. तस्मिन्निर्मनुजेऽरण्ये पिप्पलोपस्थ आस्थितः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थः|उपस्थ
उपस्थ + .{@-स्थः, -स्थम्@} —1 The organ of generation (of men and women, particularly<BR> of the latter); स्नानं मौनोपवासेज्यास्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहाः Y. 3. 313<BR> (male); स्थूलोपस्थस्थलीषु Bh. 1. 37 (female); हस्तौ पायुरुपस्थश्च<BR> Y. 3. 92 (where the word is used in both senses).<BR>—2 The anus.<BR>—3 The haunch or hip.<BR>—4 A sheltered place, seat. एवमुक्त्वाऽर्जुनः संख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् Bg. 1. 47.<BR>—5 Surface, ground; तं शयानं धरोपस्थे Bhāg. 7. 13. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपस्थदघ्न, उपस्थनिग्रहः, उपस्थपत्रः, उपस्थदलः, उपस्थपदा, उपस्थपाद, उपस्थसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थम्
उपस्थ + .{@-स्थः, -स्थम्@} —1 The organ of generation (of men and women, particularly<BR> of the latter); स्नानं मौनोपवासेज्यास्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहाः Y. 3. 313<BR> (male); स्थूलोपस्थस्थलीषु Bh. 1. 37 (female); हस्तौ पायुरुपस्थश्च<BR> Y. 3. 92 (where the word is used in both senses).<BR>—2 The anus.<BR>—3 The haunch or hip.<BR>—4 A sheltered place, seat. एवमुक्त्वाऽर्जुनः संख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् Bg. 1. 47.<BR>—5 Surface, ground; तं शयानं धरोपस्थे Bhāg. 7. 13. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपस्थदघ्न, उपस्थनिग्रहः, उपस्थपत्रः, उपस्थदलः, उपस्थपदा, उपस्थपाद, उपस्थसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थदघ्न
उपस्थ + -दघ्न <i>a.</i> reaching to the lap.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">Page0467-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थनिग्रहः|उपस्थनिग्रह
उपस्थ + -निग्रहः restraint of sensual passions, continence; स्नानं<BR> मौनोपवासेज्यास्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहाः Y. 3. 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थपत्रः|उपस्थपत्र
उपस्थ + -पत्रः, -दलः,<BR> the Indian fig-tree (so called because its leaves resemble<BR> in shape the female organ of generation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थदलः|उपस्थदल
उपस्थ + -पत्रः, -दलः,<BR> the Indian fig-tree (so called because its leaves resemble<BR> in shape the female organ of generation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थपदा
उपस्थ + -पदा <i>f.</i> A particular artery leading to the generative organs<BR> (of a male); Sāyaṇa on Ait. Br. 3. 37. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थपाद
उपस्थ + -पाद <i>a.</i> Sitting with the legs bent down so as to form a lap;<BR> Sāṅ. Gṛ. Sūtras 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थसद्
उपस्थ + -सद् <i>a.</i> sitting in the lap. प्रेष्ठः श्रेष्ठ उपस्थसत् Rv. 10. 156. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थातृ
उपस्थातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dependent on, humbled (उपनत).<BR>—2 Not late, come in time. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An attendant, a servant.<BR>—2 A sacrificial priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानम्
उपस्थानम्<BR>—1 Presence, proximity, nearness.<BR>—2 Approaching, coming, appearance, coming into the presence of; युगपदाचार्ययोरुपस्थानम् M. 1.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Worshipping, waiting upon (with prayers); attendance, service;<BR> सूर्योपस्थानात्प्रतिनिवृत्तं पुरूरवसं मामुपेत्य V. 1; सूर्यस्योपस्थानं<BR> कुर्वः V. 4; Y. 1. 22, 3. 282.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Obeisance; greeting; ˚स्तोत्रपद्धतिम् U. 1 a form of congratulatory panegyric.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Accepting, agreeing (as a lover &c.); सोऽयं मामनुपस्थाने<BR> व्यक्तं नैराश्यमागतः Rām. 6. 92. 47.<BR>—4 Attending to, guarding; रावणहित˚ Mv. 5.<BR>—5 An abode, abode of wrestling; चाणूरो मुष्टिकः कूटः शलस्तोशल एव<BR> च । त आसेदुरुपस्थानं वल्गुवाद्यप्रहर्षिताः ॥ Bhāg. 10. 42. 37.<BR>—6 The sanctuary, any sacred place (approached with respect).<BR>—7 An appeal, application; यदि कुर्युरुपस्थानं वादं तत्र प्रवर्तयेत्<BR> Śukra. 4. 630.<BR>—8 Remembrance, recollection, memory; तत्त्वस्मृतेरुपस्थानात् (योगः<BR> प्रवर्तते) Y. 3. 160.<BR>—9 Obtaining, getting; दृष्टः कश्चिदुपायो मे सीतोपस्थानकारकः Rām. 6. 64. 21.<BR>—10 A reception room; assembly; palace; a court; उपस्थानगतः कार्यार्थिनामद्वारासङ्गं<BR> कारयेत् Kau. A. 1. 14; Rām. 2. 15. 1.<BR>—11 A particular part of the संध्या.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपस्थानशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानशाला
उपस्थानम् + -शाला An assembly-room (in monastery); Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानीय
उपस्थानीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be stayed with, be kept near.<BR>—2 To be waited upon or served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापक
उपस्थापक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Placing or bringing near.<BR>—2 Explaining, teaching.<BR>—3 Causing to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापनम्
उपस्थापनम्<BR>—1 Placing near, getting ready.<BR>—2 The awakening of memory.<BR>—3 Attendance, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापना
उपस्थापनम् + .{@-ना@} The act of ordaining (a monk); Jaina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायकः|उपस्थायक
उपस्थायकः<BR>—1 A servant.<BR>—2 A follower of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायिन्
उपस्थायिन् <i>a.</i> Standing near, waiting upon, approaching &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थित|उपस्थितः
उपस्थित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Approached, arrived, come (person or thing); तस्मिन्नन्तरे भर्तोपस्थितः<BR> M. 1; ˚श्रेयोऽवमानिनम् Ś. 6; K. 157; Ms. 3. 243; Y. 2. 62; उपस्थिता<BR> शोणितपारणा मे R. चिन्तित˚ Ku. 6. 24 come as soon as thought of.<BR>—2 Close or near, at hand, impending, drawing near; उपस्थिता रजनी<BR> Ś. 3 the night is at hand (arrived);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">Page0468-1</a>]<BR> ˚संप्रहारः V. 1; ˚उदयम् R. 3. 1 approaching its: fulfilment;<BR> Māl. 10; Ratn. 1; R. 14. 39; ready for; उपस्थितमसंहार्यैर्हयैः स्यन्दनमायिभिः Rām. 5. 6. 5.<BR>—3 Worshipped or waited upon, served.<BR>—4 Got, obtained, received; अयाचित˚ Ku. 5. 22 got without solicitation;<BR> अचिन्तित˚ Pt. 2.<BR>—5 Taken place, happened, occurred, fallen to the lot; वृक्षस्य वैद्युत<BR> इवाग्निरुपस्थितोऽयम् V. 5. 16.<BR>—6 Caused, occasioned, produced, felt.<BR>—7 Known.<BR>—8 Cleansed, clean.<BR>—9 Followed by the particle इति in the Pada text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थितः|उपस्थित
उपस्थित + .{@-तः@} A door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थितम्
उपस्थित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The particle used in this manner.<BR>—2 The position of words before and after इति so used.<BR>—3 Service, worship.<BR>—4 A particular pose (आसन); उपस्थितकृतौ तौ च नासिकाग्रमधो भ्रुवोः<BR> Mb. 12. 200. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपस्थितवक्तृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थितवक्तृ
उपस्थित + -वक्तृ <i>m.</i> A ready speaker, an eloquent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थितिः|उपस्थिति
उपस्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Approach.<BR>—2 Proximity, presence.<BR>—3 Obtaining, getting.<BR>—4 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>—5 Remembrance, recollection,<BR>—6 Service, attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेहः|उपस्नेह
उपस्नेहः Moistening. उपस्नेहेन जीवामि जीवन्तीं यच्छृणोमि ताम्<BR> Rām. 6. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेहता
उपस्नेहः + .{@-ता@} Moistness, humidity; Pratimā 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेहयति
उपस्नेहयति Den. P. To melt (to love); U. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नुत
उपस्नुत <i>a.</i> Streaming forth; खयं प्रदुद्धेऽस्य गुणैरुपस्नुता Ki. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृश्
उपस्पृश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To touch (water), bathe; स्नानमुपस्पृशन्ती K. 172; तथेत्युपस्पृश्य<BR> जलं पवित्रम् R. 5. 59, 18. 31; उपस्पृश्य मणिकर्णिकायाम् Dk. 95, 110;<BR> Ms. 11. 133.<BR>—2 To wash or rinse the mouth (or teeth); to sip water (and eject it);<BR> स नद्यवस्कन्दमुपास्पृशच्च Bk. 2. 11; K. 100; Ms. 2. 53, 58, 5. 63;<BR> Y. 3. 30, 1. 18. नदीमुपस्प्रष्टुमिवावतीर्णः Pañc. 1. 15.<BR>—3 To sprinkle; अद्भिः प्राणानुपस्पृशेत् Ms. 4. 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शः|उपस्पर्श
उपस्पर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Touching, contact.<BR>—2 Bathing, ablution, washing oneself; Mb. 12. 192. 1.<BR>—3 Rinsing the mouth, sipping and ejecting water as a religious act. त्रिर्हृदयंगमाभिरद्भिरशब्दाभिरुपस्पृशेदित्युपस्पर्शनं<BR> शौचार्थम् Mbh. on VI. 1. 84.<BR>—4 A gift (दान); उपस्पर्शनषड्भागं लभते पुरुषः सदा Mb. 13. 65. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शनम्
उपस्पर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Touching, contact.<BR>—2 Bathing, ablution, washing oneself; Mb. 12. 192. 1.<BR>—3 Rinsing the mouth, sipping and ejecting water as a religious act. त्रिर्हृदयंगमाभिरद्भिरशब्दाभिरुपस्पृशेदित्युपस्पर्शनं<BR> शौचार्थम् Mbh. on VI. 1. 84.<BR>—4 A gift (दान); उपस्पर्शनषड्भागं लभते पुरुषः सदा Mb. 13. 65. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शिन्
उपस्पर्शिन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Touching.<BR>—2 Sipping water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्मृतिः|उपस्मृति
उपस्मृतिः <i>f.</i> A minor law-book. (They are 18 in all <i>e. g.</i><BR> जाबालि, नचिकेत, स्कन्द, लौगाक्षिन्, कश्यप, व्यास, सनत्कुमार, शतर्जु,<BR> जनक, व्याघ्र, कात्यायन, जातूकर्ण्य, कपिञ्जल, बौधायन, कणाद, विश्वामित्र.<BR> &c. Hc. 1. 528. 21 ff.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्रवणम्
उपस्रवणम्<BR>—1 The periodical flow of a woman, menses.<BR>—2 Flow (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वत्वम्
उपस्वत्वम् Revenue, profit (derived from land or capital).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वेदः|उपस्वेद
उपस्वेदः<BR>—1 Moisture, sweat.<BR>—2 Heat; सोपस्वेदेषु भाण्डेषु Mb. 1. 16. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्
उपहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike, smite; दण्डोपघातं गाः कालयति Sk.<BR>—2 To waste, injure, destroy, kill; अनुपध्नन् पितृद्रव्यम् Ms. 9. 208;<BR> लङ्का चोपहनिष्यते Bk. 16. 12, 5. 12; Bg. 3. 24.<BR>—3 To thrust in or into.<BR>—4 To err, mistake in reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत|उपहतः
उपहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Injured, struck, impaired; अनुपहतविधिः पन्थाः Bh. 2. 26; pained,<BR> hurt; Ku. 5. 76.<BR>—2 Affected by, smit, injured, struck with, overpowered; भूत˚ K. 167;<BR> दारिद्र्य˚, लोभ˚, दर्प˚, काम˚, शोक˚ &c.; Mu. 7.<BR>—3 Struck by lightning &c.<BR>—4 Doomed (to destruction); कथमत्रापि दैवेनोपहता वयम् Mu. 2;<BR> दैवेनोपहतस्य बुद्धिरथवा पूर्वं विपर्यस्यति Mu. 6. 8.<BR>—5 Censured, rebuked, disregarded.<BR>—6 Vitiated, polluted, made impure; शारीरैर्मलैः सुराभिर्मद्यैर्वा यदुपहतं<BR> तदत्यन्तोपहतम् Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपहतात्मन्, उपहतदृश्, उपहतधी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतात्मन्
उपहत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> agitated in mind, mentally affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतदृश्
उपहत + -दृश् <i>a.</i> dazzled, blinded शंभुमुपहतदृशः (महर्षयः) Ki. 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतधी
उपहत + -धी <i>a.</i> infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतक
उपहतक <i>a.</i> Ill-fated, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतिः|उपहति
उपहतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Stroke.<BR>—2 Killing, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्नु
उपहत्नु <i>a.</i> Ved. Attacking, hitting, hurting; मगं न भीममुपहत्नुमुग्रम् Rv. 2. 33. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्या
उपहत्या Dazzling of the eyes; morbid affection (as of the eyes);<BR> उपहत्यामक्ष्योः Av. 5. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्तृ|उपहंतृ
उपहन्तृ <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Having a contrary effect, disturbing, exciting.<BR>—2 destroyer; cf. Rv. 2. 33. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातः|उपघात
उपघातः<BR>—1 A stroke, injury, insult; Ms. 2. 179; राजदैवोपघातेन पण्ये दोषमुपागते Y. 2. 256.<BR>—2 Destruction, ruin.<BR>—3 Touch, contact (with an intention to hurt).<BR>—4 Personal violence, assault. मैत्रेय भोः किमिदमद्य ममोपघातो Mk. 9. 29.<BR>—5 Disease, sickness.<BR>—6 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातक|उपघातकः
उपघातक, -घातिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Injuring, hurting, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातिन्
उपघातक, -घातिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Injuring, hurting, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातकः|उपघातक
उपघातकः See आरग्वधू (Mar. लघुबाहवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्
उपहस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To ridicule, deride, laugh at; (fig.) to excel, surpass; अमरगुरुमपि<BR> प्रज्ञयोपहसद्भिः K. 7; Dk. 10.<BR>—2 To couple oneself with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उपहसित <i>p. p.</i> Ridiculed, derided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसितम्
उपहसित + .{@-तम्@} Satirical laughter, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासः|उपहास
उपहासः<BR>—1 Ridicule, derision; फलमस्योपहासस्य सद्यः प्राप्यसि पश्य माम् R. 12. 37.<BR>—2 Satirical laughter.<BR>—3 Fun, play; एवंविच्छोत्रियस्य दारेण नोपहासमिच्छेत् Bṛ. Up. 6. 4. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपहासास्पदम्, उपहासपात्रम्, उपहासगिर्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासास्पदम्
उपहासः + -आस्पदम्, -पात्रम् laughing-stock, butt of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासपात्रम्
उपहासः + -आस्पदम्, -पात्रम् laughing-stock, butt of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासगिर्
उपहासः + -गिर् <i>f.</i> A joke, jest; क्वचिच्च दर्दुरप्लावैर्विविधैरुपहासकैः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 18. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासक|उपहासकः
उपहासक <i>a.</i> Ridiculing others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासकः|उपहासक
उपहासक + .{@-कः@} A jester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासकम्
उपहासक + .{@-कम्@} Drollery, fun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्य
उपहास्य <i>pot. p.</i> Ridiculous; ˚ता ridiculousness; ˚तां गम्<BR> or या become an object of ridicule, be exposed to derision; गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम्<BR> R. 1. 3; सर्वजनस्योपहास्यतामुपयान्ति K. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्तिका
उपहस्तिका [उपगता हस्तम् अत इत्वम्] A small purse (or box)<BR> containing the ingredients necessary for betel-chewing (<i>e. g.</i> leaves,<BR> chunam, catechu, betel &c.) (Mar. चंची, बटवा, झोळणा); उपहस्तिकायास्ताम्बूलं<BR> कर्पूरसहितमुद्धृत्य Dk. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहा
उपहा €3 Ā. To descend, come down upon; निजौजसोज्जासयितुं जगद्द्रुहामुपाजिहीथा<BR> न महीतलं यदि Śi. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालकः|उपहालक
उपहालकः N. of the Kuntala country, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृ
उपहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To fetch, bring near, भक्त्युपहृत Bg. 9. 26; फलमिश्रमर्घमुपहर<BR> Ś. 1; तमस्योपहर Ś. 7; so बलिम् अन्नम् &c.<BR>—2 To offer, present, give (with dat. or gen.); विमानप्रतिमां तत्र<BR> मयेन सुकृतां सभाम् । पाण्डवानामुपहृतां स दृष्ट्वा पर्यतप्यत ॥<BR> Mb. 1. 1. 135. तथापि राजपरिग्रहोऽस्य प्रभुत्वमुपहरति M. 1 invests<BR> with importance; मातृभ्यो बलिमुपहर Mk. 1; नीवारभागधेयमस्माकमुपहरन्तु<BR> Ś. 2; दर्भान् ऋत्विग्भ्य उपहरामि Ś. 3; Mv. 6. 22; K. 40, 65; R. 14. 19, 16. 86, 19. 12;<BR> उपहर पादम् M. 3 give.<BR>—3 To serve out or distribute (food).<BR>—4 To offer as a victim, sacrifice; प्रागुपयाचितं स्त्रीरत्नमुपहर्तव्यम्<BR> Māl. 5; मालतीमुपहरन् 9.<BR>—5 To put down, throw.<BR>—6 To collect, gather together.<BR>—7 To take away, destroy.<BR>—8 To employ, apply, use. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to offer or bring; मां<BR> प्रियाण्युपहारय Bk. 8. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरणम्
उपहरणम्<BR>—1 Bringing near, fetching.<BR>—2 Taking, seizing.<BR>—3 Offering gifts to superiors, deities &c.<BR>—4 Offering victims.<BR>—5 Serving out food or distributing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्तृ|उपहर्त्तृ
उपहर्तृ <i>a.</i> One who offers, presents; Server (of food &c.); a<BR> host; Ms. 5. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारः|उपहार
उपहारः<BR>—1 An oblation.<BR>—2 A gift, present (In general); रत्नपुष्पोपहारेण छायामानर्च पादयोः<BR> R. 4. 84; नृत्योपहारः Me. 34; K. 17, 41, 130, 183.<BR>—3 A victim, sacrifice, an offering to a deity; सपर्यां सपशूपहाराम्<BR> R. 16. 39; Māl. 1; उपहारीकृतास्मि Māl. 2; Ve. 4. 7.<BR>—4 A complimentary gift, present to a superior &c.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Offering of flowers &c.; flowery gifts; collection of flowers;<BR> म्लानपुष्पोपहारः R. 5. 74; Ku. 6. 42.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Presents (to gods) of flowers &c.; materials of worship; गन्धैर्माल्यैः<BR> सुरभिभिर्बलिभिर्धूपदीपकैः । उच्चावचैश्चोपहारैः प्रवालफलतण्डुलैः ।<BR> Bhāg. 10. 22. 3; V. 3; Śi. 11. 36.<BR>—6 Honour.<BR>—7 Indemnity, presents given as the price of peace; कपालसन्धिर्विज्ञेयः<BR> केवलं समसन्धितः । संप्रदानाद्भवति य उपहारः स उच्यते ॥ H. 4. 110.<BR>—8 Food distributed to guests.<BR>—9 Exultation, mirth (consisting of laughter, dance, singing &c.); कृतपुष्पोपहारा<BR> भूरधिकां पुष्यति श्रियम् Rām. 5. 11. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारकः|उपहारक
उपहारकः, उपहारिका<BR>—1 An offering, oblation.<BR>—2 Gift, present; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिका
उपहारकः, उपहारिका<BR>—1 An offering, oblation.<BR>—2 Gift, present; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिन्
उपहारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Giving, presenting, bringing on; परिभवोपहारिणः M. 5.<BR>—2 Sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार्यम्
उपहार्यम् An offering, oblation; अथ कृत्वोपहार्याणि चतुर्दश्यां<BR> महामतिः Mb. 13. 91. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृत
उपहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Offered, presented.<BR>—2 Immolated, offered as a victim.<BR>—3 Served out (as a food).<BR>—4 Taken, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहोमः|उपहोम
उपहोमः A supplementary sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वरः|उपह्वर|उपह्वरं
उपह्वरः<BR>—1 A solitary or lonely place, privacy; उपह्वरे पुनरित्यशिक्षयं धनमित्रम्<BR> Dk. 54 in secret.<BR>—2 Proximity; गत्वैका कथयामास क्षत्रियाणामुपह्वरे Mb. 1. 179. 23.<BR> उपह्वरे समानाग्य Śiva B. 15. 27. (रहोऽन्तिकमुपह्वरे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वरः|उपह्वर|उपह्वरं
उपह्वरः + .{@-रः@} Ved.<BR>—1 Bend, curve, slope.<BR>—2 Declivity; उपह्वरे यदु परा अपिन्वन्. Rv. 1. 62. 6.<BR>—3 The curved form of the Soma vessel.<BR>—4 A car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वे
उपह्वे €1 Ā. (P. also)<BR>—1 To invoke, call near to (in a liturgical sense); (with acc., dat. or<BR> loc.); तामिहोपह्वये श्रियम्.<BR>—2 To call; त्वयोपहूतः U. 5. 8; Śi. 7. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहवः|उपहव
उपहवः<BR>—1 Calling to, invitation.<BR>—2 Summoning, invoking; वीनामुपसरं दृष्ट्वा तेऽन्योन्योपहवा गुहाम् Bk. 7. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव्यः|उपहव्य
उपहव्यः A kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूत
उपहूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Summoned, invoked, called उपहूता भूरिधनाः सखायः स्वादुसंमुदः Av. 7. 60. 4.<BR>—2 Called near; अविरतमेधितभावनोपहूतः Bhāg. 4. 31. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूतिः|उपहूति
उपहूतिः <i>f.</i> Calling, inviting; उपहूतिषु पतिषु Śi. 14. 30, 17. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वानम्
उपह्वानम्<BR>—1 Calling, inviting.<BR>—2 Invoking with prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In low voice or whisper; ववर्ष पर्जन्य उपांशुगर्जितः Bhāg. 10. 3. 50.<BR>—2 Secretly, in secret or private; परिचेतुमुपांशु धारणाम् R. 8. 18;<BR> cf. also तस्मात् यत् किंचित् प्राजापत्यं क्रियते उपांश्वेव तत् क्रियते इति ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 57. ˚व्रतम् a vow observed in secret; भिन्द्यामहं<BR> तस्य शिर इत्युपांशुव्रतं मम Mb. 8. 69. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुः|उपांशु
उपांशु + .{@-शुः@}<BR>—1 A prayer uttered in a low voice, muttering of prayers; जिह्वोष्टौ चालयेत्<BR> किंचिद् देवतागतमानसः । निजश्रवणयोग्यः स्यादुपांशुः स जपः स्मृतः ॥;<BR> विधियज्ञाज्जपयज्ञो विशिष्टो दशभिर्गुणैः । उपांशुः स्याच्छतगुणः साहस्रो<BR> मानसः स्मृतः ॥ Ms. 2. 85.<BR>—2 (Hence) silence itself.<BR>—3 N. of a Soma offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुत्वम्
उपांशु + .{@-त्वम्@} Silence. उपांशुत्वं प्रजापतेर्धर्मः । ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 52.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपांशुक्रीडित, उपांशुग्रहः, उपांशुदण्डः, उपांशुयाजः, उपांशुवधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुक्रीडित
उपांशु + -क्रीडित <i>a.</i> made the companion of; (a kingʼs) private amusements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुग्रहः|उपांशुग्रह
उपांशु + -ग्रहः The first ladle full of soma pressed at the sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुदण्डः|उपांशुदण्ड
उपांशु + -दण्डः A punishment inflicted in secret; विद्विष्टानुपांशुदण्डेन<BR> जनपदकोपेन वा साधयेत् Kau. A. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुयाजः|उपांशुयाज
उपांशु + -याजः a kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशुवधः|उपांशुवध
उपांशु + -वधः A clandestine murder; ˚वधमाकलय्य Mu. 2; Śi. 13. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक
उपाक <i>a.</i> Ved. Joined together, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाके
उपाक + .{@-के@} (du.) An epithet of night and morning; आ भन्दमाने उपाके<BR> Rv. 1. 142. 7. ━<i>ind.</i> In the immediate neighbourhood, before or in<BR> the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृ
उपाकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To fetch, bring near; तेभ्य इमं बलिमुपाकरोति Āśval.<BR>—2 To summon, invite.<BR>—3 To deliver, offer, grant, bestow, give (to another); गोसहस्रमुपाकुरु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">Page0470-1</a>]<BR> Rām.<BR>—4 To acquire, obtain (as fame)<BR>—5 To bring about, make preparations for a sacred rite; perform a rite;<BR> श्रावण्यां प्रौष्ठपद्यां वाऽप्युपाकृत्य यथाविधि Ms. 4. 95, 5. 7; Y. 1. 171.<BR>—6 To undertake, begin, enter upon.<BR>—7 To learn, teach; उपाकृत्य तु वै विद्यामाचार्येभ्यो नरर्षभाः Mb. 7. 147. 21, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरणम्
उपाकरणम्<BR>—1 An invitation to begin, bringing near; पवमान˚, प्रातरनुवाक˚ &c.<BR>—2 A term given to certain sentences called <i>Praiṣas</i> (with which one<BR> priest calls another to perform a sacrifice).<BR>—3 Immolation, sacrifice of an animal consecrated according to rites.<BR>—4 Preparation, beginning, commencement.<BR>—5 Commencement of reading the Veda after the performance of the preparatory<BR> rite; cf. उपाकर्मन्; वेदोपाकरणाख्यं कर्म करिष्ये Śrāvaṇī Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्मन्|उपाकर्म्मन्
उपाकर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Preparation, beginning, commencement; अध्याय˚.<BR>—2 A ceremony performed before commencing to read the Veda after the monsoons<BR> (cf. श्रावणी); अध्यायानामुपाकर्म श्रावण्यां श्रवणेन वा । हस्तेनौषधिभावे<BR> वा पञ्चम्यां श्रावणस्य तु ॥ Y. 1. 142; Ms. 4. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपाकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Brought near; उपाकृतं शशमानं यदस्थात्प्रियं देवानामप्येतु पाथः Av. 2. 34. 2.<BR>—2 Invited, called with प्रैष sentences.<BR>—3 Killed at a sacrifice (an animal).<BR>—4 Begun, commenced.<BR>—5 Ominous, disastrous, calamitous.<BR>—6 Consecrated with mantras; इति बालकमादाय सामर्ग्यजुरुपाकृतैः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 7. 14.<BR>—7 Prepared, used for; यज्ञेषूपाकृतं विश्वं प्राहुरुत्तमसंज्ञितम्<BR> Mb. 12. 268. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृतः|उपाकृत|उपाकृतं
उपाकृत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A sacrificial animal killed during the recitation of prescribed prayers.<BR>—2 A misfortune, portent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृतम्
उपाकृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—2 The performance of the usual rites (संस्कार) over the sacrificial animal.<BR>—3 Invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्रम्
उपाक्रम् €1 P. To fall upon, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्षम्
उपाक्षम् <i>ind.</i> [अक्ष्णोः समीपम्] Before the eyes, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्या
उपाख्या €2 P. To tell, narrate, relate, give an account of (with acc.).<BR> यथासीत्तदुपाख्यास्ये प्रश्नानन्यांश्च कृत्स्नशः Bhāg. 2. 9. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्या
उपाख्या<BR>—1 Observing with oneʼs own eyes; द्वितीये चानुपाख्ये P. VI. 3. 80 (उपाख्यायते<BR> प्रत्यक्षत उपलभ्यते).<BR>—2 Describing in words.<BR>—3 A secondary name, surname, epithet; कामं न्ययुङ्क्त सगणं स बदर्युपाख्यम्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानम्
उपाख्यानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 A short tale or narrative, an episode; नाचिकेतमुपाख्यानं मृत्युप्रोक्तं<BR> सनातनम् Kaṭh. 1. 3. 16. उपाख्यानैर्विना तावद् भारतं प्रोच्यते<BR> बुधैः Mb. 1. 1. 103.<BR>—2 Repetition of a story already heard from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानकम्
उपाख्यानम्, -नकम्<BR>—1 A short tale or narrative, an episode; नाचिकेतमुपाख्यानं मृत्युप्रोक्तं<BR> सनातनम् Kaṭh. 1. 3. 16. उपाख्यानैर्विना तावद् भारतं प्रोच्यते<BR> बुधैः Mb. 1. 1. 103.<BR>—2 Repetition of a story already heard from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम्
उपागम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To come, approach, go or draw near (a person or place); ताभिर्नो अद्य<BR> सुमना उपागहि सहस्रापोषं सुभगे रराणा Av. 7. 48. 2.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go to, go to the state of; पञ्चत्वमुपागतः or परां<BR> तृप्तिमुपागतः; so क्रोधम्, मोहम्, क्षयम् &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To undergo, suffer, endure.<BR>—3 To obtain, get;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">Page0470-2</a>]<BR> दायादुपागतो दासः Mit.; Y. 2. 143.<BR>—4 To occur, fall to the lot of.<BR>—5 To come back, return; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागत
उपागत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Come, approached; तपोधनं वेत्सि न मामुपागतम् Ś. 4. 1, v. l.<BR>—2 Occurred, happened.<BR>—3 Promised.<BR>—4 Suffering, feeling, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागमः|उपागम
उपागमः<BR>—1 Approach, arrival.<BR>—2 Occurrence.<BR>—3 A promise, agreement.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 Suffering, feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्निका
उपाग्निका A properly married wife; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रम्
उपाग्रम्<BR>—1 The part next to the end or top.<BR>—2 A secondary member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहणम्
उपाग्रहणम् Reading the Vedas after being initiated to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाघ्रा
उपाघ्रा P.<BR>—1 To smell at.<BR>—2 To Kiss, apply the lips to; Mb.; Rām.; R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्गः|उपाङ्ग|उपांग|उपांगः
उपाङ्गः A mark of sandal on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्गम्
उपाङ्गः + .{@-गम्@}<BR>—1 A subdivision, a sub-head. Mb. 1. 100. 38<BR>—2 Any minor limb or member (of anything); वर्गाः … साङ्गोपाङ्गैरिहोदिताः Ak.<BR>—3 A supplement of a supplement.<BR>—4 A supplementary work (of inferior value).<BR>—5 A secondary portion of science; a class of writings supplementary to<BR> the Vedāngas; (these are four:− पुराणन्यायमीमांसाधर्मशास्त्राणि).<BR>—6 N. of the class of sacred writings of the Jainas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपाङ्गगीतम्, उपाङ्गललिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्गगीतम्
उपाङ्गः + -गीतम् A kind of song; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्गललिता
उपाङ्गः + -ललिता A deity, whose व्रत is observed on the fifth of bright<BR> half of Āświna month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचर्
उपाचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To approach, युवोरुषा अनु श्रियं परिज्मनोरुपाचरत् Rv. 1. 46. 14.<BR>—2 To attend or wait upon, serve, be attached to.<BR>—3 To be obedient or humble.<BR>—4 To treat (in medic. also); ज्वरान् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचरित|उपाचरितः
उपाचरित <i>p. p.</i> Attached to any oneʼs service, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचरितः|उपाचरित
उपाचरित + .{@-तः@} (In gram.) That rule of Sandhi by which the sound Visarga<BR> becomes स् before क् and प्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचारः|उपाचार
उपाचारः<BR>—1 Position (of a word in a sentence).<BR>—2 Procedure.<BR>—3 Same as उपाचरित q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाजे
उपाजे <i>ind.</i> (Used only with the root कृ) Supporting; उपाजेकृत्य<BR> or कृत्वा having supported; उपानेऽन्वाजे P. I. 4. 73. Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाञ्जनम्
उपाञ्जनम् Anointing, plastering the ground with cow-dung, chunam<BR> &c.; Ms. 5. 105, 122, 124; (मठादेः सुधागोमयादिना संमार्जनानुलेपनम् Medhātithi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपातङ्क्यम्
उपातङ्क्यम् Runnet for coagulating milk; T. Br. 3. 7. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्ययः|उपात्यय
उपात्ययः<BR>—1 Transgression of, deviation from, established customs.<BR>—2 Disorderly conduct, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादा
उपादा €3 Ā. (<i>p. p.</i> उपात्त)<BR>—1 To receive, accept, take.<BR>—2 To acquire, obtain; भूर्या पितामहोपात्ता निबन्धो द्रव्यमेव च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">Page0471-1</a>]<BR> Y. 2. 121.<BR>—3 To give to, furnish with; उपाददे तस्य सहस्ररश्मिः; Ku. 7. 41.<BR>—4 To take, appropriate to oneself, assume; मदलौल्यमुपाददे Śi. 6. 23.<BR>—5 To take away or off, carry away; steal.<BR>—6 To seize, attack; Pt. 3. 154.<BR>—7 To take, lay hold of; धनुरधिज्यमनाधिरुपाददे R. 9. 54; to draw (water)<BR>—8 To assume a form.<BR>—9 To feel, perceive, experience; उपात्तहर्षैः पुंस्कोकिलैः Ṛs. 6. 21.<BR>—10 To consider, regard.<BR>—11 To take in addition, include, comprise; अत्र तैलशब्दस्तिलभवस्नेहरूपमुख्यार्थमुपादाय<BR> सार्षपादिस्नेहेषु वर्तते S. D. 2.<BR>—12 To employ, apply, use; यत्परस्य कुत्सार्थमुपादीयते Mbh.<BR>—14 To undertake, begin; as in उपात्तयज्ञः; प्रजासर्गमुपादार्य Mb. 12. 228. 49.<BR>—15 To mention, enumerate; इति पूर्वसूत्रोपात्तानाम् Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to use, apply or employ.<BR>—2 To make use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्त|उपात्तं|उपात्तः
उपात्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Got, received, acquired, obtained; ˚विद्यः R. 5. 1; जन्मान्तर˚<BR> K. 96, 166, 334, 346.<BR>—2 Appropriated.<BR>—3 Taken away, seized.<BR>—4 Felt, perceived, regarded.<BR>—5 Employed, used; न चक्षुषोः कान्तिविशेषबुद्धपा कालाञ्जनं मङ्गलमित्युपात्तम् Ku. 7. 20.<BR>—6 Comprised.<BR>—7 Begun, commenced.<BR>—8 Mentioned.<BR>—9 Allowed in argument, granted, conceded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तः|उपात्त|उपात्तं
उपात्त + .{@-त्तः@} An elephant out of rut.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपात्तरंहस्, उपात्तवर्ण, उपात्तशस्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तरंहस्
उपात्त + -रंहस् <i>a.</i> Speedy, quick, fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तवर्ण
उपात्त + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> Celebrated in song; उपात्तवर्णे चरिते पिनाकिनः Ku. 5. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तशस्त्र
उपात्त + -शस्त्र <i>a.</i> taking up arms, armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानम्
उपादानम्<BR>—1 Taking, receiving, acquisition, obtaining; विश्रब्धं ब्राह्मणः शूद्राद्<BR> द्रव्योपादानमाचरेत् Ms. 8. 417, 12. 7; विद्या˚ K. 75.<BR>—2 Taking away, appropriating to oneself.<BR>—3 Employment, using; becoming familiar with.<BR>—4 Mention, enumeration; किमास्योपादाने प्रयोजनम् Mbh. on I. 1. 9.<BR>—5 Saying, speaking.<BR>—6 Including, containing.<BR>—7 Withdrawing the organs of sense and perception from the external world<BR> and its objects.<BR>—8 A cause; motive, natural or immediate cause; पाटवोपादानः भ्रमः<BR> U. 3, v. l.; प्रकृष्टपुण्यपरिपाकोपादानो महिमा स्यात् U. 6.<BR>—9 The material out of which anything is made, the material cause; निमित्तमेव<BR> ब्रह्म स्यादुपादानं च वेक्षणात् Adhikaraṇamālā.<BR>—10 A mode of expression in which a word used elliptically, besides retaining<BR> its own primary sense, conveys another (in addition to that which is actually<BR> expressed); स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः … उपादानम् K. P. 2.<BR>—11 (With Buddhists) conception; grasping at or clinging to existence<BR> (caused by तृष्णा and causing भव). (With Rāmānujas) preparation<BR> (of perfumes, flowers &c. as one of the five elements of worship).<BR>—12 Effort of body or speech.<BR>—18 N. of the four contentments mentioned in सांख्यकारिका as प्रकृत्युपादानकालभागाख्याः Sāṅ. K. 50.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपादानकारणम्, उपादानलक्षणा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानकारणम्
उपादानम् + -कारणम् a material cause; प्रकृतिश्चोपादानकारणं च ब्रह्माभ्युपगन्तव्यम् Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानलक्षणा
उपादानम् + -लक्षणा = अजहत्स्वार्था q. v.; see K. P. 2; S. D. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादेय|उपादेयः
उपादेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Capable of being taken.<BR>—2 Capable of being endured; Māl. 10.<BR>—3 Acceptable,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">Page0471-2</a>]<BR> admissible.<BR>—4 To be chosen or selected.<BR>—5 Excellent, admirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिकः|उपादिक
उपादिकः A sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिका
उपादिकः + .{@-का@} N. of plant पूतिका (Mar. थोर मयाळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधा
उपाधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place near or upon.<BR>—2 To offer, give, impart. अपि नः खर्गतिं सूक्ष्मामुपाधास्यदधीश्वरः Bhāg. 10. 28. 11.<BR>—3 To put on, wear.<BR>—4 To create, cause, produce; कोपोपाहितबाष्प Bh. 3. 85; Gīt. 10.<BR>—5 To render, make, effect.<BR>—6 To keep, hold.<BR>—7 To seduce (a woman); Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिः|उपाधि
उपाधिः<BR>—1 Fraud, deceit, trick.<BR>—2 Deception, disguise (in Vedānta).<BR>—3 Discriminative or distinguishing property, attribute, peculiarity;<BR> तदुपाधावेव संकेतः K. P. 2. It is of four kinds:− जाति, गुण, क्रिया, संज्ञा.<BR>—4 A title, nick-name; (भट्टाचार्य, महामहोपाध्याय, पण्डित &c.);<BR> बी. ए. इत्युपाधिधारिणः (modern use).<BR>—5 Limitation, condition (as of time, space &c.); न ह्युपाधेरुपाधिर्भवति<BR> विशेषणस्य वा विशेषणम् Mbh. I. 3. 2 अनुपाधिरमणीयो देशः Prob.<BR> a country altogether (or naturally) beautiful; (oft. occurring in Vedānta<BR> Phil.); देहाद्युपाधिरचितो भेदः Ś. B.; न खलु बहिरुपाधीन्प्रीतयः<BR> संश्रयन्ते U. 6. 12; Māl. 1. 24.<BR>—6 A trace, mark; भौमा उपाधयः Mv. 7. 22.<BR>—7 A purpose, occasion, object.<BR>—8 (In logic) A special cause for a general effect; साध्यव्यापकत्वे<BR> सति साधनाव्यापक उपाधिः; as आर्द्रेन्धनम् (wet fuel) is the उपाधि<BR> of the <i>hetu</i> वह्निमत्त्व in the inference पर्वतो धूमवान् वह्नेः.<BR>—9 Reflection on duty or a virtuous reflection.<BR>—10 A man who is careful to support his family.<BR>—11 An incidental purpose, an additional adjunct (which does not modify<BR> the original idea to which it is added). काष्ठाहरणे शाकाहरणमुपाधिः<BR> क्रियते इति । किमिदमुपाधिः क्रियत इति । काष्ठाहरणाधिकारसमीपे द्वितीयं<BR> कर्मोपाधीयते । सति काष्ठाहरणे इदमपरं कर्तव्यमिति । ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 20;<BR> also ŚB. on MS. 12. 4. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपाधिकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिकर
उपाधिः + -कर <i>a.</i> That which comes only incidentally adding another<BR> adjunct or उपाधि. उपाधिकरः एषः । यथा काष्ठान्याहर्तुं प्रस्थित<BR> उच्यते भवता शाकमप्याहर्तव्यमिति । ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 20.<BR>—12 A substitute, substitution; उपाधिर्न मया कार्यो वनवासे जुगुप्सितः<BR> Rām. 2. 111. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिक
उपाधिक <i>a.</i> Exceeding, supernumerary, additional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहित|उपाहितः
उपाहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deposited, placed.<BR>—2 Put on, worn.<BR>—3 Connected, joined, ˚श्यामरुचश्च चन्दनाः Ki. 8. 12 showing.<BR>—4 Ascribed or attributed to (आरोपित).<BR>—5 Agreed upon, done by mutual agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहितः|उपाहित
उपाहित + .{@-तः@} A fiery portent, danger or destruction from fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायः|उपाध्याय
उपाध्यायः [उपेत्याधीयते अस्मात्, उप-अधि-इ-घञ्]<BR>—1 A teacher or preceptor in general. —2 Particularly, a spiritual teacher,<BR> religious preceptor; य उदात्ते कर्तव्ये ऽनुदात्तं करोति खण्डिकोपाध्यायस्तमै<BR> चपेटां ददाति Mbh. I. 1. 1. (by Y. 1. 35 a sub-teacher who instructs<BR> for wages only in a part of the Veda and is inferior to an आचार्य; एकदेशमुपाध्यायः);<BR> cf. Ms. 2. 141; एकदेशं तु वेदस्य वेदाङ्गान्यपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">Page0472-1</a>]<BR> वा पुनः । योऽध्यापयति वृत्त्यर्थमुपाध्यायः स उच्यते ॥ see अध्यापक,<BR> and under आचार्य also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याया
उपाध्यायः + .{@-या@} A female preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायी
उपाध्यायः + .{@-यी@} —1 A female preceptor. उपेत्य अधीयते तस्या उपाध्यायी, उपाध्याया<BR> and Vārt. या तु स्वयमेवाध्यापिका तत्र वा ङीष् वाच्यः on P. IV. 1. 49. Sk.<BR>—2 The wife of a preceptor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपाध्यायसर्वस्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायसर्वस्वम्
उपाध्यायः + -सर्वस्वम् N. of a grammar frequently referred to by the commentary<BR> on the Uṇādi Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायानी
उपाध्यायानी The wife of a preceptor. Vārt. मातुलोपाध्याययोरानुग्वा ।<BR> on P. IV. 1. 49<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्वर्युः|उपाध्वर्यु
उपाध्वर्युः A second अध्वर्यु; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानस्
उपानस् <i>a.</i> [उपगतमनः शकटं पितरं वा]<BR>—1 Like a cart, being in a cart; सचायोरिन्द्रश्चर्कृष आँ उपानसः सपर्यन्<BR> Rv. 10. 105. 4.<BR>—2 Like a father (uncle &c.). <i>n.</i><BR>—1 The space in a carriage; निरक्षान्निरुपानसात् Av. 2. 14. 2.<BR>—2 Anything placed in a carriage, carriage-load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह्
उपानह् <i>f.</i> [उप-नह्-क्विप् उपसर्गदीर्घः] A sandal, shoe; उपानद्गूढपादस्य<BR> सर्वा चर्मावृतेव भूः H. 1. 122; Ms. 2. 246; श्वा यदि क्रियते राजा<BR> स किं नाश्नात्युपानहम् H. 3. 51; cf. ‘What is bred in the bones cannot go out of flesh’<BR>, or ‘Habit is second nature’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानयनम्
उपानयनम् The act of leading near or home (a wife); Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त|उपांत|उपान्तः
उपान्त <i>a.</i> Near to the end, last but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तः|उपान्त|उपांत
उपान्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Border, edge, margin, skirt, point (of anything); उपान्तयोर्निष्कुषितं<BR> विहङ्गैः R. 7. 50; Ku. 3. 69, 7. 32; Amaru. 27; U. 1. 26; वल्कल˚ K. 136.<BR>—2 The corner or angle of the eye; विलोचने तिर्यगुपान्तलोहिते Ku. 5. 74;<BR> नयनोपान्तविलोकितं च यत् 4. 23; R. 3. 26.<BR>—3 Immediate proximity, vicinity; तयोरुपान्तस्थितसिद्धसैनिकम् R. 3. 57,<BR> उपान्तवानीरगृहाणि दृष्ट्वा R. 7. 24, 16. 21; Me. 24.<BR>—4 Side or slope (नितम्ब); Me. 18.<BR>—5 The last letter but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिक|उपांतिक
उपान्तिक <i>a.</i> Near, proximate, neighbouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिकम्
उपान्तिक + .{@-कम्@} Vicinity, proximity; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिम
उपान्तिम <i>a.</i> Proximate, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त्य|उपांत्य|उपान्त्यः
उपान्त्य <i>a.</i> Last but one; उत्तमपदमुपान्त्यस्योपलक्षणार्थम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त्यः|उपान्त्य|उपांत्य
उपान्त्य + .{@-त्यः@} The corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त्यम्
उपान्त्य + .{@-न्त्यम्@} Vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप्तिः|उपाप्ति
उपाप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Reaching to.<BR>—2 Obtaining, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाभृत्
उपाभृत् <i>f.</i> Bringing near or taking away (उपाहरण); स<BR> न ऊर्जामुपाभृत्यया कृपा न जूर्यति Rv. 1. 128. 2. (Monier Williams gives<BR> as उपाभृतिः <i>f.</i> which appears to be wrong).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायः|उपाय
उपायः, उपायन See under उपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायः, उपायन See under उपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायात
उपायात <i>a.</i> Approached, come near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायातम्
उपायात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Arrival.<BR>—2 An event, incident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारः|उपार
उपारः [उप-ऋ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 Proximity.<BR>—2 A mistake, offence, sin; अस्ति ज्यायान् कनीयस उपारे Rv. 7. 86. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम्
उपारम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sport, amuse oneself, delight in.<BR>—2 To cease, desist (from); दानप्रवृत्तेरनुपारतानाम् R. 16. 3;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">Page0472-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 3. 58; to rest, come to a stand-still वातवर्षमुपारतम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारत
उपारत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Delighted.<BR>—2 Returned; Ki. 4. 10.<BR>—3 Engaged in, occupied with.<BR>—4 Frequenting, resorting to.<BR>—5 Leaving off, giving up, free from; A. Rām. 7. 5. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारमः|उपारम
उपारमः The act of ceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम्भः|उपारम्भ|उपारंभ|उपारंभः
उपारम्भः Beginning, commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारुद्
उपारुद् €2 P. To weep for; उपारुरोदेव नदत्पतङ्गः Bk. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारूढ
उपारूढ <i>a.</i> Grown, increased, attained to; ˚यौवन attained<BR> to majority; ˚स्नेह K. 173 whose affection has increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्
उपार्ज् €1 P. To bring near to. ━<i>Caus.</i> To gain, earn, acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जक
उपार्जक <i>a.</i> Acquiring, earning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जनम्
उपार्जनम्^1, -ना<BR> Acquiring, gaining.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter or fem..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जना
उपार्जनम्^1, -ना<BR> Acquiring, gaining.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter or fem..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जित|उपार्ज्जित
उपार्जित <i>a.</i> Procured, acquired. तदर्थं च क्षेत्रमुपार्जितम् Mbh. II. 3. 19<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्थ
उपार्थ <i>a.</i> Of little worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालभ्
उपालभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To censure, blame, revile, scold, taunt; पयोधरविस्तारयितृकमात्मनो<BR> यौवनमुपालभस्व मां किमुपालभसे Ś. 1; रहस्युपालभ्यत चन्द्रशेखरः<BR> Ku. 5. 58; R. 7. 44; Śi. 9. 60; Bk. 3. 30, 6. 125.<BR>—2 To obtain (Ved.). तं यदि खरेषूपालभेत Ch. Up. 2. 22. 3.<BR>—3 To lay hold of, seize (a sacrificial animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालम्भः|उपालम्भ|उपालंभ|उपालंभः
उपालम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR>—1 Abuse, taunt, censure; अस्या महदुपालम्भनं गतोऽस्मि<BR> Ś. 5; तवोपालम्भे पतितास्मि M. 1.<BR> laid myself open to your censure; उचितस्तदुपालम्भः U. 3.<BR>—2 Delaying, putting off.<BR>—3 Escorting, conducting; केचिदस्मदुपालम्भे मतिं चक्रुर्हि तापसाः Mb. 5. 176. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालम्भनम्
उपालम्भः, -म्भनम्<BR>—1 Abuse, taunt, censure; अस्या महदुपालम्भनं गतोऽस्मि<BR> Ś. 5; तवोपालम्भे पतितास्मि M. 1.<BR> laid myself open to your censure; उचितस्तदुपालम्भः U. 3.<BR>—2 Delaying, putting off.<BR>—3 Escorting, conducting; केचिदस्मदुपालम्भे मतिं चक्रुर्हि तापसाः Mb. 5. 176. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालिः|उपालि
उपालिः N. of one of the Buddhaʼs most eminent pupils; he was formerly a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावसायिन्
उपावसायिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Submissive, compliant, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावसु
उपावसु <i>a.</i> Ved. Bringing or granting wealth. देवानां सुम्न<BR> इषयन्नुपावसुः Rv. 9. 84. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावहरणम्
उपावहरणम् Bringing down, taking down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाविश्
उपाविश् P. To enter, enter into any state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत
उपावृत <i>a.</i> Covered, veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्
उपावृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn or go towards, approach.<BR>—2 To turn away from, return.<BR>—3 To give.<BR>—4 To roll on the ground; उपावृत्योत्थितां दीनां वडवामिव वाहितां<BR> Rām. 2. 20. 34. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To win over, induce; Māl. 8.<BR>—2 To cause to turn; lead or bring back; M. 5.<BR>—3 To give to.<BR>—4 To cause, produce.<BR>—5 To stretch out more and more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावर्तनम्
उपावर्तनम्<BR>—1 Coming or turning back, return; त्वदुपावर्तनशङ्कि मे मनः (करोति) R. 8. 53.<BR>—2 Revolving, turning round.<BR>—3 Approaching.<BR>—4 Ceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्
उपावृत् <i>f.</i> Ved. Return. सहस्रं त उपावृतस्ताभिर्नः पुनरा<BR> कृधि Av. 6. 77. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्त|उपावृत्तः
उपावृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Returned, come, arrived. ततः काल उपावृत्ते Bhāg. 9. 6. 30.<BR>—2 Ceased, refraining.<BR>—3 Fit, proper.<BR>—4 Turned round; rolling or wallowing on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्तः|उपावृत्त
उपावृत्त + .{@-त्तः@} A horse rolling on the ground (to remove his fatigue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाव्याधः|उपाव्याध
उपाव्याधः A vulnerable or unprotected place. तेषां न कुतश्चनोपाव्याधोऽभवत्<BR> Yv. Ts. 7. 2. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाशंसनीय
उपाशंसनीय <i>a.</i> To be expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रि
उपाश्रि €1 U. To have recourse to, resort to इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य<BR> Bg. 14. 2, 18. 57 हाराणां मणिभिरुपाश्रितौ समन्तात् (रेजाते) Śi. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रयः|उपाश्रय
उपाश्रयः<BR>—1 Recourse (for aid), asylum, support; कोर्थस्तेषां पार्थिवोपाश्रयेण<BR> Bh. 2. 48; पर्यङ्कस्योपाश्रये K. 186 resting-place.<BR>—2 Receptacle, recipient; ईप्सितस्य न भवेदुपाश्रयः Ki. 18. 40.<BR>—3 Reliance, dependence upon.<BR>—4 A cushion, pillow or reclining bolster (Mar. लोड); महत्सोपाश्रयं<BR> भेजे रावणः परमासनम् Rām. 6. 11. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रित
उपाश्रित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relying or depending upon.<BR>—2 Supporting (fig. also), bearing, holding, protecting. चिन्तामपरिमेयां<BR> तां प्रलयान्तामुपाश्रिताः Bg. 16. 11.<BR>—3 An indirect dependent; (as against संश्रित direct. dependent);<BR> संश्रितोपाश्रितांस्तथा यथाशक्त्यनुकम्पेत Mb. 12. 87. 24.<BR>—4 See उपाश्रय (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्लिष्ट
उपाश्लिष्ट <i>a.</i> One who has clasped or laid hold of; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्
उपास् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To sit near to (with acc.), sit at the side of (as a mark of submission<BR> and respect); wait upon, serve, worship; ओमित्येतदक्षरमुद्गीथमुपासीत<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 1. 1 &c. मां ध्यायन्त उपासते Bg. 12. 6, 9. 14, 15. उद्यानपालसामान्यमृतवस्तमुपासते<BR> Ku. 2. 36; अम्बामुपास्व सदयाम् Aśvad. 13; Śi. 16. 47; Ms. 3. 189.<BR>—2 To use, occupy, abide in, reside; ऐन्द्रं स्थानमुपासीना ब्रह्मभूता<BR> हि ते सदा Rām. 1. 35. 1; Ms. 5. 93.<BR>—3 To pass (as time); उपास्य रात्रिशेषं तु Rām.<BR>—4 To approach, go to or towards; उपासाञ्चक्रिरे द्रष्टुं देवगन्धर्वकिन्नराः<BR> Bk. 5. 107; परलोकमुपास्महे 7. 89.<BR>—5 To invest or blockade (as an enemyʼs town).<BR>—6 To be intent upon, be engaged in, take part in, (perform as a sacred<BR> rite); उपास्य पश्चिमां सन्ध्याम् K. 176, 179; तेप्युपासन्तु मे मखम्<BR> Mb.; Ms. 2. 222, 3. 104, 7. 223, 11. 42.<BR>—7 To undergo, suffer; अलं ते पाण्डुपुत्राणां भक्त्या क्लेशमुपासितुम्<BR> Mb.; Ms. 11. 184.<BR>—8 To remain or continue in any state or action; oft. with a <i>pres. p.</i>;<BR> अनन्येनैव योगेन मां ध्यायन्त उपासते Bg. 12. 6.<BR>—9 To expect, wait for; दिष्टमुपासीनः Mb.<BR>—10 To attach<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">Page0473-2</a>]<BR> oneself to, practise; उपासते द्विजाः सत्यम् Y. 3. 192.<BR>—11 To resort to, employ, apply, use; लक्षणोपास्यते यस्य कृते S. D. 2;<BR> बस्तिरुपास्यमानः Suśr.<BR>—12 To respect, recognize, acknowledge.<BR>—13 To practise archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासकः|उपासक
उपासकः<BR>—1 One who waits upon, a worshipper.<BR>—2 A servant, follower.<BR>—3 A Śūdra, a low fellow.<BR>—4 A worshipper of Buddha as distinguished from the <i>Bhikṣu</i>.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपासकदशाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासकदशाः
उपासकः + -दशाः N. of one of the Aṅgas or chief Jaina sacred writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासनम्
उपासनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Service, serving, attendance, waiting upon; शीलं खलोपासनात् (विनश्यति);<BR> उपासनामेत्य पितुः स्म सृज्यते N. 1. 34; Pt. 1. 169; Ms. 3. 107; Bg. 13. 7;<BR> Y. 3. 156; Bh. 2. 42.<BR>—2 Engaging in, being intent on, performing; संगीत˚ Mk. 6; सन्ध्या˚ Ms. 2. 69.<BR>—3 Worship, respect, adoration.<BR>—4 Practice of archery.<BR>—5 Regarding as, reflecting upon.<BR>—6 Religious meditation. न कर्मसांख्ययोगोपासनादिभिः Mukti. Up. 1. 1.<BR>—7 The sacred fire. वानप्रस्थो ब्रह्मचारी साग्निः सोपासनो व्रजेत्. Y. 3. 45.<BR>—8 Injuring, hurting; (fr. अस् 2).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपासनाखण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासना
उपासनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Service, serving, attendance, waiting upon; शीलं खलोपासनात् (विनश्यति);<BR> उपासनामेत्य पितुः स्म सृज्यते N. 1. 34; Pt. 1. 169; Ms. 3. 107; Bg. 13. 7;<BR> Y. 3. 156; Bh. 2. 42.<BR>—2 Engaging in, being intent on, performing; संगीत˚ Mk. 6; सन्ध्या˚ Ms. 2. 69.<BR>—3 Worship, respect, adoration.<BR>—4 Practice of archery.<BR>—5 Regarding as, reflecting upon.<BR>—6 Religious meditation. न कर्मसांख्ययोगोपासनादिभिः Mukti. Up. 1. 1.<BR>—7 The sacred fire. वानप्रस्थो ब्रह्मचारी साग्निः सोपासनो व्रजेत्. Y. 3. 45.<BR>—8 Injuring, hurting; (fr. अस् 2).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपासनाखण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासनाखण्डः|उपासनाखण्ड
उपासनम् + उपासनाखण्डः, N. of the first section of the Gaṇeśa Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासा
उपासा<BR>—1 Service, attendance.<BR>—2 Worship, adoration; सात्त्विकोपासया सत्त्वं ततो धर्मः प्रवर्तते<BR> Bhāg. 11. 13. 2.<BR>—3 Religious meditation. शरं ह्युपासानिशितं संदधीत Muṇḍ. 2. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासीन
उपासीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sitting near to; उपासीनेषु विप्रेषु पाण्डवेषु महात्मसु Mb. 3. 233. 1.<BR>—2 Attending on, serving; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासितृ
उपासितृ <i>a.</i> A worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तिः|उपास्ति
उपास्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Service, attendance upon (especially a deity).<BR>—2 Worship, adoration; सन्ध्योपास्त्यादिकर्माणि Bhāg. 11. 27. 11. स्वर्गापवर्गयोर्मार्गमामनान्ति<BR> मनीषिणः । यदुपास्तिमसावत्र परमात्मा निरूप्यते ॥ Kusum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्य
उपास्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be served or worshipped.<BR>—2 To be performed or accomplished.<BR>—3 To be respected;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्यता
उपास्य + .{@-ता, -त्वम्@} respectability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्यत्वम्
उपास्य + .{@-ता, -त्वम्@} respectability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासङ्गः|उपासङ्ग|उपासंग|उपासंगः
उपासङ्गः<BR>—1 Proximity, vicinity.<BR>—2 A quiver, (borne by elephants and horses); Mb. 5. 155. 3.<BR>—3 Collection, heap; उपासङ्गानाचरद्दक्षिणेन वराङ्गानां नकुलश्चित्रयोधी Mb. 5. 48. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तमनम्
उपास्तमनम् Sunset; Mb. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तमयम्
उपास्तमयम् <i>ind.</i> About sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्त्रम्
उपास्त्रम् A secondary or minor weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्थित
उपास्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mounting, standing.<BR>—2 Devoted to oneself.<BR>—3 Satisfying; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्नात
उपास्नात N. of a sacred place उपास्नातं स्थूलसिक्तं तूष्णींगङ्गं<BR> महाह्रदम् Mbh. 2. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहृ
उपाहृ €1 U.<BR>—1 To offer, give.<BR>—2 To cause, produce; स्पर्शसुखम् K. 124.<BR>—3 To make, prepare.<BR>—4 To seize.<BR>—5 To propitiate; Bhāg. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहारः|उपाहार
उपाहारः Slight refreshment (fruits, sweetmeats &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपे
उपे €2 P. [उप-इ]<BR>—1 To approach, come near, arrive at, reach (a place, person &c.); परमं<BR> साभ्यमुपैति Muṇḍ. 3. 1. 3. लतामुपेत्य Ś. 1; so राजानम्,<BR> दुर्गम् &c. योगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम् Bg. 8. 28, 10. 15, 9. 28.<BR>—2 To go to (a master), become a pupil. उपेत्य पप्रच्छ Praśna. Up. 1. 2, 6. 1.<BR>—3 To have intercourse with (a woman), cohabit; वाच्यश्चानुपयन् पतिः Ms. 9. 4.<BR>—4 To under go, perform, undertake, practise; तपः, सत्रम् &c.<BR>—5 To go to or pass into any state; योगम् R. 16. 84; भेदम् Ku. 2. 4;<BR> to fall into (misfortune &c.); क्षयम्, मत्युम्, सुखम्, दुःखम्, निद्राम् &c.<BR>—6 To obtain, attain to; तस्य प्रिया ज्ञातयः सुकृतमुपयन्ति Kauṣ. Up. 1. 1;<BR> उपैति शस्यं परिणामरम्यताम् Ki. 4. 22.<BR>—7 To incur, be present at.<BR>—8 To fall to oneʼs lot or share, befall; उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति<BR> लक्ष्मीः Pt. 1. 361; Bg. 6. 27.<BR>—9 To consider as, admit, acknowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायः|उपाय
उपायः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Means, an expedient, remedy; शक्योवाप्तुमुपायतः Bg. 6. 36.<BR> उपायं चिन्तयेत्प्राज्ञस्तथापायं च चिन्तयेत् Pt. 1. 406; मयि<BR> क्षीणोपाये प्रणिपतनमात्रैकशरणे Amaru. 25; Bhāg. 10. 48. 2; Ms. 8. 48, 7. 177.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A plan, contrivance; ˚निलया Mu. 1. 5.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) A mode, way, stratagem. उपायेन तु यच्छक्यं न तच्छक्यं पराक्रमैः । H.<BR>—2 A fact, circumstance; U. 7.<BR>—3 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—4 Effort, exertion; वश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः (योगः)<BR> Bg. 6. 36; Ms. 9. 248, 10. 2.<BR>—5 A means of success against an enemy; [these are four:− सामन् conciliation<BR> or negotiation, दानम् bribery; भेदः sowing dissensions; and दण्डः<BR> punishment (open attack); some authorities add three more:− माया deceit;<BR> उपेक्षा trick, deceit or neglect; इन्द्रजाल conjuring, thus making<BR> the total number 7]; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> सामादीनामुपायानां चतुर्णामपि पण्डिताः Ms. 7. 109.<BR>—6 Joining (as in singing).<BR>—7 Approach.<BR>—8 Initiation, thread ceremony (= उपनयन); अपि वा वेदतुल्यत्वाद्<BR> उपायेन प्रवर्तेरन् MS. 6. 2. 22 (where शबर explains उपायेन<BR> प्रवर्तेरन् as उपनयनेन सह प्रवर्तेरन् ।).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपायाक्षेपः, उपायचतुष्टयम्, उपायचिन्ता, उपायज्ञ, उपायतुरीयः, उपाययोगः, उपायविकल्पः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायाक्षेपः|उपायाक्षेप
उपायः + -आक्षेपः (In Rhet.) Deprecatory speech making mention of the remedy; Kāv. 2. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायचतुष्टयम्
उपायः + -चतुष्टयम् the four expedients against an enemy; see above (5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायचिन्ता
उपायः + -चिन्ता devising an expedient or scheme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायज्ञ
उपायः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> fertile in expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायतुरीयः|उपायतुरीय
उपायः + -तुरीयः the 4th expedient, <i>i. e.</i> दण्ड or punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाययोगः|उपाययोग
उपायः + -योगः application of means or remedy; एतैरुपाययोगैस्तु शक्यास्ताः<BR> परिरक्षितुम् Ms. 9. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायविकल्पः
उपायः + -विकल्पः Alternative strategic means; Kau. A. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायनम्
उपायनम्<BR>—1 Going near, approach.<BR>—2 Becoming a pupil of.<BR>—3 Engaging in any religious rite.<BR>—4 Undertaking, beginning; व्रत˚.<BR>—5 A present, gift; मालविकोपायनं प्रेषिता M. 1; तस्योपायनयोग्यानि<BR> वस्तूनि सरितां पतिः Ku. 2. 37; R. 4. 79; शरीरिणां श्रेय उपायनं<BR> वपुः Bhāg. 10. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिक
उपायिक <i>a.</i> Conducive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिन्
उपायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Skilled in the use of means, having means.<BR>—2 Approaching.<BR>—3 Having sexual intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायु
उपायु <i>a.</i> Ved. Approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Come near, approached, arrived at; लोकाश्च वो मयोपेता देवा अप्यनुमन्वते<BR> Bhāg. 10. 23. 32.<BR>—2 Present.<BR>—3 Endowed with, possessed of, having; with instr. or in comp.; पुत्रमेवंगुणोपेतं<BR> चक्रवर्तिनमाप्नुहि Ś. 1. 12.<BR>—4 Blockaded.<BR>—5 Fallen into.<BR>—6 Approached for sexual gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतिः|उपेति
उपेतिः <i>f.</i> Arrival, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतृ
उपेतृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Approaching near to.<BR>—2 Contriving, one who uses expedients; Ms. 7. 215.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be gone to or approached.<BR>—2 To be effected by means; ˚उपायदर्शने M. 1.<BR>—3 Assailable.<BR>—4 To be sought; Ms. 7. 215.<BR>—5 To be obtained.<BR>—6 To be approached sexually;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयः|उपेय
उपेय + .{@-यः@} A thing to be obtained; अवरः श्रद्धयोपेत उपेयान्विन्दतेऽञ्जसा<BR> Bhāg. 4. 18. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयिवस्
उपेयिवस् <i>a.</i> (उप इण् क्वसु P. III. 2. 109) One who has gone<BR> near उपेयिवांसि कर्तारः पुरीमाजातशात्रवीम् Śi. 2. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्ष्
उपेक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To neglect, overlook, disregard, connive at; किमात्मनिर्वादकथामुपेक्षे<BR> R. 14. 34; उपेक्षते यः श्लथलम्बिनीर्जटाः Ku. 5. 47.<BR>—2 To let escape or let go; नोपेक्षेत क्षणमपि राजा साहासिकं नरम् Ms. 8. 344.<BR>—3 To quit, abandon.<BR>—4 To despise, slight.<BR>—5 To notice, consider, have regard to; एवमुच्चावचानर्थान् प्राहुः ते<BR> उपेक्षितव्याः Nir.<BR>—6 To look at, regard, perceive; प्रासादस्था ह्युपैक्षत Nala. 22. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षक
उपेक्षक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disregarding, neglecting.<BR>—2 Patient, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षणम्
उपेक्षणम् = उपेक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षणीय
उपेक्षणीय <i>a.</i> To be overlooked, disregarded; object of indifference<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षा
उपेक्षा<BR>—1 Overlooking, disregard, neglect.<BR>—2 Indifference, contempt, disdain; कुर्यामुपेक्षां हतजीवितेऽस्मिन् R. 14. 65.<BR>—3 Leaving, quitting.<BR>—4 Endurance, patience.<BR>—5 Dissent.<BR>—6 Neglect, trick or deceit (one of the 7 expedients in war).<BR>—7 A sort of भावना in Yoga, q. v.<BR>—8 Regard, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेडकीय्
उपेडकीय् Den. P. (उप-एडक) To behave as a sheep towards; Kāśi.<BR> on Pāṇini VI. 1. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेनित
उपेनित <i>a.</i> Driven or pressed in. Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्रः|उपेन्द्र|उपेंद्र|उपेंद्रः
उपेन्द्रः [उपगत इन्द्रम् अनुजत्वात्] N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa<BR> as the younger brother of Indra in his 5th or dwarf incarnation; see इन्द्र;<BR> उपेन्द्रवज्रादपि दारुणोऽसि Gīt. 5; यदुपेन्द्रस्त्वमतीन्द्र एव सः Śi. 16. 70.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपेन्द्रवज्रा, उपेन्द्रापत्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्रवज्रा
उपेन्द्रः + -वज्रा <i>f.</i> N. of a metre; see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्रापत्यम्
उपेन्द्रः + -अपत्यम् Madana, God of love … उद्भटोपेन्द्रापत्यपराक्रमैकनिधयो<BR> भद्राणि संतन्वते Cola-Campū. P. 27, verse 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ See under उपवह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोती
उपोती = उपोदिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोत्त
उपोत्त <i>a.</i> Moistened, wet; Yv. Ts. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोत्तम
उपोत्तम <i>a.</i> Last but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोत्तमम्
उपोत्तम + .{@-मम्@} (अक्षरम्) The last letter but one; cf. उपोत्तमं रिति P. IV. 1. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदक|उपोदकः
उपोदक <i>a.</i> Near water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदकः|उपोदक
उपोदक + .{@-कः@} proximity of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदकम्
उपोदक + .{@-कम्@} <i>ind.</i> Near water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदकी
उपोदक + .{@-की,^1 -दिका, -दीका@} The plant Basella Rubra (पूतिका; Mar. थोर मयाळ).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदिका
उपोदक + .{@-की,^1 -दिका, -दीका@} The plant Basella Rubra (पूतिका; Mar. थोर मयाळ).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदीका
उपोदक + .{@-की,^1 -दिका, -दीका@} The plant Basella Rubra (पूतिका; Mar. थोर मयाळ).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by users @aumsanskrit, @Andhrabharati on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101#issuecomment-37002842552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्ग्रहः|उपोद्ग्रह
उपोद्ग्रहः Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्घातः|उपोद्घात
उपोद्घातः<BR>—1 A beginning, commencement.<BR>—2 An introduction, a preface.<BR>—3 An example, an apposite argument or illustration.<BR>—4 An occasion, medium, means; तत्प्रतिच्छन्दकमुपोद्घातेन माधवान्तिकमुपेयात् Māl. 1.<BR>—5 Analysis, ascertaining the elements of anything.<BR>—6 Alluding to, mentioning; Mu. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उपोद्घातपादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्घातपादः|उपोद्घातपाद
उपोद्घातः + -पादः N. of the third part of the Vāyu P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलयति
उपोद्बलयति Den. P. To confirm, strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलक
उपोद्बलक <i>a.</i> Confirming; तस्य पक्षस्योपोद्बलकानि Ś. B.<BR> तस्यैवोपोद्बलकमेतत् 1. 2. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलनम्
उपोद्बलनम् Confirmation, corroboration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषणम्
उपोषणम्, -उपोषितम्<BR> A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषितम्
उपोषणम्, -उपोषितम्<BR> A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोह्
उपोह् €1 P. (उप-ऊह्)<BR>—1 To propel, push or impel towards; उपोह्य रुचिरां नावम् Rām.; so धनुः.<BR>—2 To push under, insert; कूर्चावधस्तादुपोह्य Kāty.<BR>—3 To bring near, produce; connected with उपवह् in this sense; q. v.<BR>—4 To accumulate, collect. ━<i>pass.</i><BR>—1 To be brought about.<BR>—2 To advance, begin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ <i>p. p.</i> See under उपवह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोहः|उपोह
उपोहः Ved. Adding, accumulating; उपोहश्च समहश्च क्षत्तारौ ते<BR> प्रजापते Av. 3. 24. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त|उप्तः
उप्त, उप्तिः See under वप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तिः|उप्ति
उप्त, उप्तिः See under वप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज्
उब्ज् €6 P. (उब्जति, उब्जाञ्चकार, औब्जीत्, उब्जित)<BR>—1 To press down, subdue, keep under or check. इन्द्रासोमा तपतं रक्ष<BR> उब्जतम् Av. 8. 4. 1.<BR>—2 To make straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ्
उभ्, उम्भ् €6. €7. €9. P. (उभति or उम्भति, उनप्ति, उभ्नाति, उम्भित)<BR>—1 To confine.<BR>—2 To compact together.<BR>—3 To fill with; जलकुम्भमुम्भितरसं सपदि सरस्याः समानयन्त्यास्ते Bv. 2. 144.<BR>—4 To cover or overspread with; सर्वमर्मसु काकुत्स्थमौम्भत्तीक्ष्णैः<BR> शिलीमुखैः Bk. 17. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्भ्|उंभ्
उभ्, उम्भ् €6. €7. €9. P. (उभति or उम्भति, उनप्ति, उभ्नाति, उम्भित)<BR>—1 To confine.<BR>—2 To compact together.<BR>—3 To fill with; जलकुम्भमुम्भितरसं सपदि सरस्याः समानयन्त्यास्ते Bv. 2. 144.<BR>—4 To cover or overspread with; सर्वमर्मसु काकुत्स्थमौम्भत्तीक्ष्णैः<BR> शिलीमुखैः Bk. 17. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ <i>pron. a.</i> (Used only in the dual) Both; उभौ तौ न विजानीतः<BR> Bg. 2. 19; सूर्याचन्द्रमसावुभौ Ch. Up. 7. 12. 1; Ku. 4. 43; Ms. 2. 14;<BR> Śi. 3. 8. [cf. Zend. <i>uba</i>; Gr. <i>amphi</i>; L. <i>ambo</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभय|उभयं|उभयः
उभय <i>pron. a.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयी
उभय + .({@-यी@} <i>f.</i>) (Though dual in sense, it is used in the singular<BR> and plural only; according to some grammarians in the dual also) Both<BR> (of persons or things); यस्तद्वेदोभयं सह Īśop. 11 उभयमप्यपरितोषं समर्थये<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">Page0475-2</a>]<BR> Ś. 7; उभयमानशिरे वसुधाधिपाः R. 9. 9; उभयीं सिद्धिमुभाववापतुः 8. 23, 17. 38;<BR> Amaru. 60; Ku. 7. 78; Ms. 2. 55, 4. 224, 9. 34,<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उभयान्वयिन्, उभयालंकारः, उभयार्थम्, उभयात्मक, उभयचर, उभयच्छन्ना, उभयद्युः, उभयपदिन्, उभयभागहर, उभयमुख, उभयविद्या, उभयविध, उभयविपुला, उभयविभ्रष्ट, उभयवेतन, उभयव्यञ्जन, उभयसंभवः, उभयस्नातक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयान्वयिन्
उभय + -अन्वयिन् <i>a.</i> Tending towards both, keeping connection with both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयालंकारः|उभयालङ्कार
उभय + -अलंकारः (in Rhet.) A figure of speech, which sets off both<BR> the sense and sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयार्थम्
उभय + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> for a double object (for earthly prosperity and<BR> heavenly happiness also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयात्मक
उभय + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> belonging to both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयचर|उभयचरः
उभय + -चर <i>a.</i> living in water and on land or in the air, amphibious.<BR> Mātaṅga L. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयचरः|उभयचर
उभय + -चर + .({@-रः@}) a class of birds who live both on land and in the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयच्छन्ना
उभय + -च्छन्ना (in Rhet.) A kind of enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयद्युः
उभय + -द्युः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 on both days.<BR>—2 the day past and to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयपदिन्
उभय + -पदिन् <i>a.</i> Having both Parasmai and Atmane pada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयभागहर
उभय + -भागहर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 applicable to two objects.<BR>—2 taking two shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयभागहरम्
उभय + -भागहर + .({@-रम्@}) a medicine that acts in two ways (both as an emetic and a purgative).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयमुख
उभय + -मुख <i>a.</i> two-faced; a pregnant female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयविद्या
उभय + -विद्या two-fold sciences; <i>i. e.</i> religious knowledge and knowledge<BR> about worldly affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयविध
उभय + -विध <i>a.</i> of both kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयविपुला
उभय + -विपुला <i>f.</i> N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयविभ्रष्ट
उभय + -विभ्रष्ट <i>a.</i> losing both कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टः Bg. 6. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयवेतन
उभय + -वेतन <i>a.</i> receiving wages from both (parties), serving two<BR> masters, treacherous, perfidious; उभयवेतनो भूत्वा Pt. 1; Śi. 2. 113.<BR> Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयव्यञ्जन|उभयव्यंजन
उभय + -व्यञ्जन <i>a.</i> having the marks of both sexes, hermaphrodite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयसंभवः|उभयसम्भव|उभयसंभव
उभय + -संभवः a dilemma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयस्नातक
उभय + -स्नातक <i>a.</i> one who has performed the prescribed ablutions<BR> after finishing both his time of studying and his vow. See Kullūka on Ms. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतः|उभयत
उभयतः <i>ind.</i> —1 From both sides, on both sides, to both sides<BR> (with acc.) एतदनृतमुभयतः सत्येन परिगृहीतम् Bṛ. Up. 5. 5. 1.<BR> उभयतः कृष्णं गोपाः Sk. तज्जः पुनात्युभयतः पुरुषानेकविंशतिम्<BR> Y. 1. 58; Ms. 8. 315.<BR>—2 In both cases.<BR>—3 In both ways; पुष्पिणः फलिनश्चैव वृक्षास्तूभयतः स्मृताः Ms. 1. 47.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उभयतःक्ष्णुत्, उभयतोदत्, उभयतोदन्त, उभयतःपाश, उभयतःप्रज्ञ, उभयतोभाष, उभयतोमुख, उभयतोह्रस्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतःक्ष्णुत्
उभयतः + -क्ष्णुत् <i>a.</i> two-edged (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोदत्|उभयतोदन्त्
उभयतः + -दत्, -दन्त <i>a.</i> having a double row of teeth; पशून् मृगान्<BR> मनुष्यांश्च व्यालांश्चोभयतोदतः Ms. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोदन्त|उभयतोदंत
उभयतः + -दत्, -दन्त <i>a.</i> having a double row of teeth; पशून् मृगान्<BR> मनुष्यांश्च व्यालांश्चोभयतोदतः Ms. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतःपाश
उभयतः + -पाश <i>a.</i> having trap on both sides. lit. and fig. सैषोभयतस्पाशा<BR> रज्जुर्भवति Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतःप्रज्ञ
उभयतः + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> one whose cognizance is directed both inwards and<BR> outwards. नान्तःप्रज्ञं न बहिःप्रज्ञं नोभयतः प्रज्ञं Māṇḍ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोभाष
उभयतः + -भाष <i>a.</i> occurring both in Parasmaibhāṣā and Ātmanebhāṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोमुख
उभयतः + -मुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking either way. —2 two-faced (as a house &c.).<BR>—2 Two-edged (a sword) पट्टीशात्मसमोहस्तबुध्नश्चोभयतो मुखः Śukra. 4. 1044.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोमुखी
उभयतः + -मुख + .({@-खी@}) a cow; (‘यावद्वत्सस्य पादौ द्वौ मुखं योऽन्यां च दृश्यते’<BR> तत्काले उभयतो मुखी) Y. 1. 206-7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोह्रस्व
उभयतः + -ह्रस्व <i>a.</i> (an accented vowel) produced by two short vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयत्र
उभयत्र <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In both places.<BR>—2 On both sides; भ्रातरुभयत्रा ते अर्थम् Rv. 3. 53. 5. ˚उदात्त<BR> having an Udātta accent on both sides.<BR>—3 In both cases; Ms. 3. 125, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयथा
उभयथा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In both ways; उभयथापि घटते V. 3.<BR>—2 In both cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभया
उभया <i>ind.</i> Ved. In both ways; बृहस्पतिर्व उभया न मृळात्<BR> Rv. 10. 108. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: उभयादत्, उभयाविन्, उभयाहस्ति, उभयाहस्त्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयादत्|उभयादन्त्
उभया + -दत् <i>a.</i> having teeth on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">Page0476-1</a>]<BR> both sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0475-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयाविन्
उभया + -विन् <i>a.</i> being on both sides, partaking of both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयाहस्ति
उभया + -हस्ति <i>ind.</i> as much as may be grasped with both hands; उभयाहस्त्या<BR> भर Rv. 5. 39. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयाहस्त्य
उभया + -हस्त्य <i>a.</i> filling both hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयायिन्
उभयायिन् <i>a.</i> Tending towards or fit for both (worlds); Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयीय
उभयीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयेद्युस्
उभये(य)द्युस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 On both days.<BR>—2 On two subsequent days. उभयोरह्वोरुभयेद्युः Mbh. on P. V. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0476-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयद्युस्
