ऋणशोधनम्
ऋण + -अपनयनम्, -अपनोदनम्, -अपाकरणम्, -दानम्, -मुक्तिः, -मोक्षः, -शोधनम्<BR> paying off debt, discharge or liquidation of debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणादानम्
ऋण + -आदानम् ‘recovery of debt’ Kau. A. 3; receipt of money lent &c.<BR> (one of the 18 titles or subjects of litigation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणोद्ग्रहणम्
ऋण + -उद्ग्रहणम् recovering a debt in any way from the creditor (by<BR> friendly or legal proceedings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणार्णम्
ऋण + -ऋणम् + ({@-ऋणार्णम्@}) debt for a debt, debt incurred to liquidate<BR> another debt. ऋणस्य अपनयनाय यदन्यदृणं क्रियते तत् ऋणार्णम्<BR> Sk. 73; Vārt. on P. VI. 1. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणकर्तृ|ऋणकर्त्तृ
ऋण + -कर्तृ <i>a.</i> one who gets into debt; Mb. 13. 23. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणकाति
ऋण + -काति <i>a.</i> one to whom praise is due as a debt; or one who receives<BR> praise as a debt to be repaid in benefits (Sāy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रस्त
ऋण + -ग्रस्त <i>a.</i> indebted, involved in debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रहः|ऋणग्रह
ऋण + -ग्रहः<BR>—1 borrowing (money).<BR>—2 a borrower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्राहिन्
ऋण + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> borrowing. ━<i>m.</i> a debtor, borrower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणचित्
ऋण + -चित् <i>a.</i> acknowledging (praise) as a debt to be paid for.<BR> N. of ब्रह्मणस्पति; Rv. 2. 27. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणच्छेदः|ऋणच्छेद
ऋण + -च्छेदः Payment of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणञ्चयः|ऋणञ्चय
ऋण + -च्छेदः + ({@-णम् चयः@}) N. of<BR> a king; Rv. 5. 30. 12, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदातृ
ऋण + -दातृ, -दायिन् <i>a.</i> one who pays a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदायिन्
ऋण + -दातृ, -दायिन् <i>a.</i> one who pays a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदासः|ऋणदास
ऋण + -दासः [ऋणात् मोचनेन कृतो दासः] one who is bought as a slave<BR> by paying off his debts; ऋणमोचनेन दास्यत्वमभ्युपगतः ऋणदासः Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणनिर्णयपत्रकम्
ऋण + -निर्णयपत्रकम्, -पत्रम् A note of acknowledgment of debt; Śukra. 1. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणपत्रम्
ऋण + -निर्णयपत्रकम्, -पत्रम् A note of acknowledgment of debt; Śukra. 1. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणनिर्मोक्षः|ऋणनिर्मोक्ष
ऋण + -निर्मोक्षः Discharge or acquittance of debt (to ancestors &c.);<BR> न चोपलेभे पूर्वेषामृणनिर्मोक्षसाधनम् R. 10. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणप्रदातृ
ऋण + -प्रदातृ moneylender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमत्कुणः|ऋणमत्कुण
ऋण + -मत्कुणः, -मार्गणः security, bail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमार्गणः|ऋणमार्गण
ऋण + -मत्कुणः, -मार्गणः security, bail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमुक्तः
ऋण + -मुक्तः released from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमुक्तिः|ऋणमुक्ति
ऋण + -मुक्तिः &c. see ऋणापनयनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणलेख्यम्
ऋण + -लेख्यम् ‘debt-bond’ a bond acknowledging a debt (in law; Mar. कर्जरोखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणवत्|ऋणवन्त्
ऋणवत्, -वन् or ऋणावत् <i>a.</i><BR> One who is in debt, indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणवन्
ऋणवत्, -वन् or ऋणावत् <i>a.</i><BR> One who is in debt, indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणावत्
ऋणवत्, -वन् or ऋणावत् <i>a.</i><BR> One who is in debt, indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिकः|ऋणिक
ऋणिकः [ऋणमस्त्यस्य-ठन्] A debtor; Y. 2. 56, 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिन्
ऋणिन् <i>a.</i> A debtor, one indebted to another (on any account).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्
ऋत् Ā. ऋतीयते (a Sautra root)<BR>—1 To reproach, contemn.<BR>—2 To pity.<BR>—3 To go.<BR>—4 To rival; have power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत <i>a.</i> [ऋ-क्त]<BR>—1 Proper, right.<BR>—2 Honest, true; सर्वमेतदृतं मन्ये यन्मां वदसि केशव Bg. 10. 14; Ms. 8. 82.<BR>—3 Worshipped, respected.<BR>—4 Bright, luminous (दीप्त)<BR>—5 Gone, risen, moved, affected by; सुखेन ऋतः = सुखार्तः ऋते च तृतीयासमासे<BR> Vārt. on P. VI. 1. 89; so दुःखः˚ काम˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतम्
ऋत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Rightly, properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतः|ऋत|ऋतं
ऋत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A sacrifice.<BR>—2 The sun (<i>n.</i> also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतम्
ऋत + .{@-तम्@} (Not usually found in classical literature)<BR>—1 A fixed or settled rule, law (religious).<BR>—2 Sacred custom, pious action. यस्तनोति सतां सेतुमृतेनामृतयोनिना<BR> Mb. 12. 47. 49.<BR>—3 Divine law, divine truth.<BR>—4 Absolution. मर्त्यानामृतमिच्छताम् Bhāg. 1. 16. 7.<BR>—5 Water; सत्यं त्वा ऋतेन परिषिञ्चामि.<BR>—6 Truth (in general), right; ऋतं वदिष्यामि T. Up. 1. 1. 1. ऋतानृते<BR> Ms. 1. 29, 2. 52, 8. 61, 104.<BR>—7 Truth (personified as an object of worship; in later Sanskrit regarded<BR> as a child of Dharma).<BR>—8 Livelihood by picking or gleaning grains in a field (as opposed to<BR> the cultivation of ground); ऋतमुञ्च्छशिलं वृत्तम् Ms. 4. 4.<BR>—9 The fruit of an action; एकं चक्रं वर्तते द्वादशारं षण्णाभिमेकाक्षमृतस्य<BR> धारणम् Mb. 1. 3. 62.<BR>—10 Agreeable speech; ऋतं च सूनृता वाणी कविभिः परिकीर्तिता Bhāg. 11. 19. 38.<BR>—11 N. of an Āditya.<BR>—12 The Supreme Spirit. (In the Vedas ऋत is usually interpreted by<BR> Sāyaṇa to mean ‘water’, ‘sun’ or ‘sacrifice’, where European scholars<BR> take it in the sense of ‘divine truth’, ‘faith’ &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋतजा, ऋतजात, ऋतजातसत्य, ऋतजित्, ऋतज्ञा, ऋतद्युम्न, ऋतधामन्, ऋतधीति, ऋतध्वजः, ऋतनी, ऋतपर्णः, ऋतपेयः, ऋतपेशस्, ऋतप्सुः, ऋतयुक्तिः, ऋतयुज्, ऋतवाकः, ऋतसद्, ऋतसदनम्, ऋतनी, ऋतसाप्, ऋतसामन्, ऋतस्था<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतजा
ऋत + -जा, -जात <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 of a true nature, sprung from sacred truth; अब्जा गोजा ऋतजा अद्रिजा<BR> ऋतम् Rv. 4. 40. 5.<BR>—2 Well-made, excellent; Rv. 3. 58. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतजात
ऋत + -जा, -जात <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 of a true nature, sprung from sacred truth; अब्जा गोजा ऋतजा अद्रिजा<BR> ऋतम् Rv. 4. 40. 5.<BR>—2 Well-made, excellent; Rv. 3. 58. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतजातसत्य
ऋत + -जातसत्य <i>a.</i> (Sāy.) born for the sake of sacrifice and having true result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतजित्
ऋत + -जित् <i>a.</i> Ved. gaining the right; Vāj. 17. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतज्ञा
ऋत + -ज्ञा <i>a.</i> (Sāy.) knowing the sacrifice, familar with the sacred law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतद्युम्न
ऋत + -द्युम्न <i>a.</i> shining with truth; Rv. 9. 113. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतधामन्
ऋत + -धामन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of a true or pure nature.<BR>—2 having an imperishable place. ━<i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतधीति
ऋत + -धीति <i>a.</i> Ved. of true disposition; or receiving true praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतध्वजः|ऋतध्वज
ऋत + -ध्वजः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतनी
ऋत + -नी <i>a.</i> leading in the right way; Rv. 2. 27. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतपर्णः|ऋतपर्ण|ऋतपर्ण्ण
ऋत + -पर्णः = ऋतुपर्णः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतपेयः|ऋतपेय
ऋत + -पेयः a sacrifice lasting one day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतपेशस्
ऋत + -पेशस् <i>a.</i> Ved. having a perfect shape; Rv. 5. 66. 1. ━<i>m.</i><BR> one whose form consists of water; <i>i. e.</i> Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतप्सुः|ऋतप्सु
ऋत + -प्सुः<BR>—1 a god who consumes sacrificial food; Rv. 1. 180. 3.<BR>—2 one whose form is truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतयुक्तिः|ऋतयुक्ति
ऋत + -युक्तिः <i>f.</i> true application of a hymn; Rv. 10. 61. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतयुज्
ऋत + -युज् <i>a.</i> going to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतवाकः|ऋतवाक
ऋत + -वाकः Ved. true speech; Rv. 9. 113. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतसद्
ऋत + -सद् <i>a.</i> dwelling in the sacrifice or truth; Rv. 4. 40. 5. ━<i>m.</i> fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतसदनम्
ऋत + -सदनम्, -नी the right or usual alter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतनी
ऋत + -सदनम्, -नी the right or usual alter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतसाप्
ऋत + -साप् <i>a.</i> pervading truth; steady in religious belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतसामन्
ऋत + -सामन् <i>n.</i> N. of a Sāman; Ārṣeya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतस्था
ऋत + -स्था <i>a.</i> standing right; स हि दिवः स पृथिव्या ऋतस्था. Av. 4. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतंभरः|ऋतम्भर|ऋतंभर
ऋतंभरः God, upholder of truth. ऋतंभरध्याननिवारिताघः Bhāg. 6. 13. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतंभरा
ऋतंभरः + .{@-रा@} Intellect (Pātañjala Yogadarśana 1. 47).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतयति
ऋतयति To desire sacrifice; Rv. 8. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0489-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतया
ऋतया <i>ind.</i> Through desire of reward; धियं वनेम ऋतया सपन्तः Rv. 2. 11. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतस्पतिः|ऋतस्पति
ऋतस्पतिः Lord of sacrifices or of divine truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतावन्
ऋतावन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Bestowing food; ऋतावरनं मघवानमीमहे Mbh. on P. V. 2. 109.<BR>—2 Possessed of sacrifice.<BR>—3 Of true nature or character; according to fixed order, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतावृध्
ऋतावृध् <i>a.</i> Increaser of sacrifice, water, or of truth; holy-minded (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतयु
ऋत(ता)यु <i>a.</i> Desirous of sacrifice; त्वं न इन्द्र ऋतयुः Rv. 8. 70. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतायु
ऋत(ता)यु <i>a.</i> Desirous of sacrifice; त्वं न इन्द्र ऋतयुः Rv. 8. 70. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतेन
ऋतेन <i>ind.</i> Duly, rightly, truly, honestly, justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतिः|ऋति
ऋतिः [ऋ-क्तिन्] An army. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going, motion.<BR>—2 Assault, combat; ऋतिर्हन्यमाना Av. 12. 5. 25.<BR>—3 Abuse, censure.<BR>—4 Emulation, envy.<BR>—5 A road.<BR>—6 Manner of proceeding.<BR>—7 Prosperity.<BR>—8 Fitness, truth.<BR>—9 Remembrance.<BR>—10 Misfortune.<BR>—11 Protection.<BR>—12 Auspiciousness (most of these meanings are found only in lexicons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतिंकर|ऋतिङ्कर
ऋतिंकर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Injuring, giving pain.<BR>—2 Unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीयति
ऋतीयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To quarrel, fight.<BR>—2 To be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीया
ऋतीया<BR>—1 Censure, reproach.<BR>—2 Shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीषह्
ऋतीषह् <i>a.</i> Able to resist, enduring; overpowering an assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुः|ऋतु
ऋतुः [ऋ-तु-किच्च Uṇ. 1. 71]<BR>—1 A season, period of the year, commonly reckoned to be six; शिशिरश्च<BR> वसन्तश्च ग्रीष्मो वर्षाः शरद्धिमः; sometimes only five; शिशिर<BR> and हिम or हेमन्त being counted together; cf. पञ्चर्तवो हेमन्तशिशिरयोः<BR> समासेन Ait. Br. वसन्तश्चैत्रवैशाखौ ज्येष्ठाषाढौ च ग्रीष्मकौ । वर्षा<BR> श्रावणभाद्राभ्यां शरदश्विनकार्तिकौ ॥ मार्गपौषौ च हेमन्तः शिशिरो माघफाल्गुनौ ॥<BR> गोरक्षसंहिता.<BR>—2 An epoch, a period, any fixed or appointed time.<BR>—3 Menstruation, courses, menstrual discharge.<BR>—4 A period favourable for conception; वरमृतुषु नैवाभिगमनम् Pt. 1;<BR> ऋतुः स्वाभाविकः स्त्रीणां रात्रयः षोडश स्मृताः Ms. 3. 46, 9. 70; Y. 1. 11, 79.<BR>—5 Any fit season or right time.<BR>—6 Fixed order or rule; द्वा यन्तारा भवतस्तथ ऋतुः Rv. 1. 162. 19.<BR>—7 Light, splendour.<BR>—8 A month.<BR>—9 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—10 A symbolical expression for the number ‘six’.<BR>—11 A kind of collyrium.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋत्वन्तः, ऋतुकालः, ऋतुसमयः, ऋतुवेला, ऋतुगणः, ऋतुगामिन्, ऋतुग्रहः, ऋतुचर्या, ऋतुजुष्, ऋतुधामन्, ऋतुपतिः, ऋतुपर्णः, ऋतुपर्यायः, ऋतुवृत्तिः, ऋतुपशुः, ऋतुपाः, ऋतुपात्रम्, ऋतुप्राप्त, ऋतुप्रैषः, ऋतुमुखम्, ऋतुयाजः, ऋतुराजः, ऋतुलिङ्गम्, ऋतुलोका, ऋतुष्ठा, ऋतुसंहारः, ऋतुसन्धिः, ऋतुसात्म्यम्, ऋतुस्तोमः, ऋतुस्नाता, ऋतुस्नानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्वन्तः|ऋत्वन्त
ऋतुः + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the close of a season.<BR>—2 termination of menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुकालः|ऋतुकाल
ऋतुः + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला<BR>—1 the time of menstruation, time favourable for conception, <i>i. e.</i> 16<BR> nights from menstrual discharge; see ऋतु above.<BR>—2 the duration of a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसमयः|ऋतुसमय
ऋतुः + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला<BR>—1 the time of menstruation, time favourable for conception, <i>i. e.</i> 16<BR> nights from menstrual discharge; see ऋतु above.<BR>—2 the duration of a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुवेला
ऋतुः + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला<BR>—1 the time of menstruation, time favourable for conception, <i>i. e.</i> 16<BR> nights from menstrual discharge; see ऋतु above.<BR>—2 the duration of a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुगणः|ऋतुगण
ऋतुः + -गणः the seasons taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुगामिन्
ऋतुः + -गामिन् <i>a.</i> having intercourse with a wife (at the time fit<BR> for conception, <i>i. e.</i> after the period of menstruation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुग्रहः|ऋतुग्रह
ऋतुः + -ग्रहः a libation offered to the seasons,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">Page0490-2</a>]<BR> a kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुचर्या
ऋतुः + -चर्या <i>f.</i> seasonal proceeding; उथातः संप्रवक्ष्यामि ऋतुचर्यास्तु<BR> वाजिनाम् Bhojaʼs Śālihotra 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुजुष्
ऋतुः + -जुष् <i>f.</i> A woman enjoying intercourse at the time fit for procreation; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुधामन्
ऋतुः + -धामन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपतिः|ऋतुपति
ऋतुः + -पतिः<BR>—1 the lord of seasons, <i>i. e.</i> the spring.<BR>—2 N. of Agni; Rv. 10. 2. 1. —3 N. of other deities; Av. 3. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपर्णः|ऋतुपर्ण
ऋतुः + -पर्णः N. of a king of Ayodhyā; son of Ayutāyu, a descendant<BR> of Ikṣvāku. [Nala, king of Niṣadha, entered into his service after<BR> he had lost his kingdom and suffered very great adversity. He was ‘profoundly skilled in dice’<BR>; and he exchanged with Nala this skill for his skill<BR> in horsemanship; and by virtue of it the king succeeded in taking Nala<BR> to Kuṇḍinapura before Damayantī had put into execution her resolve of<BR> taking a second husband].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपर्यायः|ऋतुपर्याय|ऋतुपर्य्याय
ऋतुः + -पर्यायः, -वृत्तिः the revolution of the seasons; cf. Ms. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुवृत्तिः|ऋतुवृत्ति
ऋतुः + -पर्यायः, -वृत्तिः the revolution of the seasons; cf. Ms. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपशुः|ऋतुपशु
ऋतुः + -पशुः An animal to be sacrificed at a particular season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपाः
ऋतुः + -पाः <i>m.</i> N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपात्रम्
ऋतुः + -पात्रम् the cup in which the libation is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुप्राप्त|ऋतुप्राप्तः
ऋतुः + -प्राप्त <i>a.</i> fertile, fruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुप्रैषः|ऋतुप्रैष
ऋतुः + -प्रैषः N. of particular invocations spoken before the sacrifice<BR> to the seasons. Ait. Br. 5. 9. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमुखम्
ऋतुः + -मुखम् the beginning or first day of a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुयाजः|ऋतुयाज
ऋतुः + -याजः a sacrifice offered to the seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुराजः|ऋतुराज
ऋतुः + -राजः the spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुलिङ्गम्
ऋतुः + -लिङ्गम्<BR>—1 a characteristic or sign of the season (as the blossom of the mango<BR> tree in spring); यथर्तुलिङ्गान्यृतवः स्वयमेवर्तुपर्यये Ms. 1. 30.<BR>—2 a symptom of menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुलोका
ऋतुः + -लोका <i>f.</i> N. of particular bricks; Śat. Br. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुष्ठा
ऋतुः + -ष्ठा<BR>(-स्था) <i>a.</i> fixed at the proper seasons; Vāj. 17. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसंहारः|ऋतुसंहार
ऋतुः + -संहारः ‘collection of the seasons’, N. of Kālidāsaʼs work<BR> on the six seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसन्धिः|ऋतुसन्धि|ऋतुसंधि
ऋतुः + -सन्धिः<BR>—1 the junction of two seasons.<BR>—2 the last day in the bright fortnight (पौर्णमासी) and in the dark<BR> one (दर्श).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसात्म्यम्
ऋतुः + -सात्म्यम् diet &c. suited to the season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्तोमः|ऋतुस्तोम
ऋतुः + -स्तोमः a kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्नाता
ऋतुः + -स्नाता a woman who has bathed after menstruation and who is, therefore,<BR> fit for sexual intercourse; धर्मलोपभयाद्राज्ञीमृतुस्नातामिमां स्मरन् R. 1. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्नानम्
ऋतुः + -स्नानम् bathing after menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमत्|ऋतुमन्त्
ऋतुमत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Coming regularly; अग्निष्वात्तानृतुमतो हवामहे Vāj. 19. 61.<BR>—2 Enjoying the seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमती
ऋतुमत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 A woman during her courses.<BR>—2 A girl at the age of puberty, marriagable girl; काममामरणात्तिष्ठेद्<BR> गृहे कन्यर्तुमत्यपि Ms. 9. 89 ff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतव्य
ऋतव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Seasonable, relating to the season.<BR>—2 Devoted to or worshipping the season (as divinities).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुया
ऋतुया <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In order, duly.<BR>—2 Precisely, exactly.<BR>—3 At the right or fixed time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विय
ऋत्विय, -ऋत्व्य (cf. P. VI. 4. 175.) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Due, regular. अयं ते योनिरृत्वियः Jābāla Up. 4; Mbh. on P. I. 4. 1, VI. 1. 127.<BR>—2 Conforming to, or familiar with, ceremonial rules.<BR>—3 Menstruating.<BR>—4 Being in the period most favourable to conception. ━<i>n.</i> Menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्व्य
ऋत्विय, -ऋत्व्य (cf. P. VI. 4. 175.) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Due, regular. अयं ते योनिरृत्वियः Jābāla Up. 4; Mbh. on P. I. 4. 1, VI. 1. 127.<BR>—2 Conforming to, or familiar with, ceremonial rules.<BR>—3 Menstruating.<BR>—4 Being in the period most favourable to conception. ━<i>n.</i> Menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋते
ऋते <i>ind.</i> Except, without, with the exception of (usually with<BR> abl.); ऋते कौर्यात्समायातः Bk. 8. 105;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">Page0491-1</a>]<BR> अवेहि मां प्रीतमृते तुरङ्गमात् R. 3. 63; पापादृते Ś. 6. 22;<BR> Ku. 1. 51, 2. 57; sometimes with acc. ऋतेऽपि त्वां न भविष्यन्ति सर्वे<BR> Bg. 11. 32; rarely with instr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0490-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विज्
ऋत्विज् <i>a.</i> Ved. Sacrificing at the proper season or regularly;<BR>━<i>m.</i> A priest who officiates at a sacrifice; यज्ञस्य देवमृत्विजम्<BR> Rv. 1. 1. 1; ऋत्विग्यज्ञकृदुच्यते Y. 1. 35; cf. Ms. 2. 143 also; the<BR> four chief Ṛtvijas are होतृ, उद्गातृ, अध्वर्यु and ब्रह्मन्; at<BR> grand ceremonies 16 are enumerated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋदूदर
ऋदूदर <i>a.</i> Ved. Mild, kind. ऋदूदरः सुहवो मा नो अस्यै Rv. 2. 33. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋध्
ऋध् €4. €5 P. (ऋध्यति, ऋध्नोति, आनर्ध, आर्धीत् अर्धितुम्, ऋद्ध); sometimes €7 P. (ऋणद्धि)<BR>—1 To prosper, flourish, thrive, succeed; नाब्रह्म क्षत्रमृध्नोति Ms. 9. 322.<BR>—2 To grow, increase (fig. also).<BR>—3 To cause to succeed, make prosperous.<BR>—4 To satisfy, gratify, please, propitiate; सोऽहं प्राग्भवतैव भूतजननीमृध्नोमि Māl. 5. 29.<BR>—5 To accomplish. ━<i>Desid.</i> ईर्त्सति or अर्दिधिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्ध|ऋद्धं|ऋद्धः
ऋद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Prosperous, thriving, rich; अवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धं राज्यं<BR> Bg. 2. 8; ऋद्धापणं राजपथं स पश्यन् R. 14. 30, 85, 2. 50, 5. 40, 8. 6;<BR> splendidly furnished; मन्दिरम् Ku. 7. 55.<BR>—2 Increased, growing.<BR>—3 Stored (as grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धः|ऋद्ध|ऋद्धं
ऋद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धम्
ऋद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 Increase, growth.<BR>—2 A demonstrated conclusion; distinct result.<BR>—3 Collection of grain after beating it out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिः|ऋद्धि
ऋद्धिः <i>f.</i> [ऋध्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Growth, increase. नियमर्द्धये Bhāg. 12. 8. 9.<BR>—2 Success, prosperity; affluence, good fortune. तेषामृद्धिरतीवात्र<BR> Bhāg. 3. 139. 8.<BR>—3 Elevation, exaltation, greatness. संजीवितः शिशुरसौ मम चेयमृद्धिः U. 2. 11.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Extent, magnitude, excellence; परिच्छिन्नप्रभावर्द्धिर्न मया<BR> न च विष्णुना Ku. 2. 58.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Grandeur, magnificence; व्यक्तर्धि वः क्रीडितम् Māl. 5. 22.<BR>—5 Supernatural power or supremacy, perfection.<BR>—6 Accomplishment.<BR>—7 Prosperity personified as the wife of Kubera.<BR>—8 N. of Pārvatī, and of Lakṣmī.<BR>—9 N. of a medicinal plant; (Mar. केवणी, मुरुडशेंग)<BR>—10 magic; MW.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋद्धिकाम, ऋद्धिसाक्षात्क्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिकाम
ऋद्धिः + -काम <i>a.</i> desiring increase or prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिसाक्षात्क्रिया
ऋद्धिः + -साक्षात्क्रिया manifestation of supernatural power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धित
ऋद्धित <i>a.</i> Made to prosper; राजसूयजिताँल्लोकान् स्वयमेवासि<BR> ऋद्धितान् Mb. 18. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिमत्|ऋद्धिमन्त्
ऋद्धिमत् <i>a.</i> Prosperous, wealthy, respectable, rich; ऋद्धिमन्तमधिकर्द्धिरुत्तरः<BR> पूर्वमुत्सवमपोहदुत्सवः R. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधत्
ऋधत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Prospering thriving.<BR>—2 Exceedingly swift (as horses); दश श्यावा ऋधद्रयो Rv. 8. 46. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधद्द्वार
ऋधत् + .{@˚द्वार@} having abundant wealth; ऋधद्वारा याग्नये ददाश Rv. 6. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधज्
ऋधज्(क्) <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Separately.<BR>—2 Aside, apart.<BR>—3 Singly, one by one.<BR>—4 Particularly.<BR>—5 Truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधक्
ऋधज्(क्) <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Separately.<BR>—2 Aside, apart.<BR>—3 Singly, one by one.<BR>—4 Particularly.<BR>—5 Truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋफ्
ऋफ्, ऋम्फ्, ऋन्फ् €6 P. To kill, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋम्फ्
ऋफ्, ऋम्फ्, ऋन्फ् €6 P. To kill, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋन्फ्
ऋफ्, ऋम्फ्, ऋन्फ् €6 P. To kill, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋबीसम्
ऋबीसम् Ved.<BR>—1 Warmth of the earth; fire.<BR>—2 A fissure, rent, abyss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभु|ऋभुः
ऋभु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Skilful, clever, prudent (as an epithet of Indra, Agni, Ādityas, property<BR> and wealth) ऋभुमृभुक्षणो रयिम् Rv. 4. 37. 5.<BR>—2 Handy (as a weapon).<BR>—3 Shining far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुः|ऋभु
ऋभु + .{@-भुः@}<BR>—1 A deity, divinity; a god (dwelling in heaven).<BR>—2 The god who is worshipped by the gods; ऋभवो नाम तत्रान्ये देवानामपि<BR> देवताः Mb. 3. 261. 19.<BR>—3 A class of the attendants of gods.<BR>—4 An artist, smith, especially a coach-builder (रथकार).<BR>—5 N. of three semi-divine beings called Ṛbhu, Vibhvan and Vāja, sons<BR> of Sudhanvan, a descendant of Aṅgiras, who were so called from the name<BR> of the eldest son. [Through their performance of good works they obtained<BR> divinity, exercised superhuman powers, and became entitled to worship.<BR> They are supposed to dwell in the Solar sphere, and are the artists who<BR> formed the horses of Indra, the carriage of the Aśvins, and the miraculous<BR> cow of Bṛhaspati. They made their aged parents young, and constructed<BR> four cups at a sacrifice from the one cup of Tvaṣṭṛ, who as the proper<BR> artificer of the gods, was in this respect their rival. They appear generally<BR> as accompanying Indra at the evening sacrifices. MW.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्षः|ऋभुक्ष
ऋभुक्षः<BR>—1 N. of Indra.<BR>—2 Heaven (of Indra) or paradise.<BR>—3 The thunderbolt of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्षिन्
ऋभुक्षिन् <i>m.</i> [ऋभुक्षः वज्रं स्वर्गो वा अस्यास्ति इनि] (Nom. ऋभुक्षाः,<BR> acc. pl. ऋभुक्षः)<BR>—1 N. of Indra.<BR>—2 N. of the Maruts; इमां मे मरुतो गिरमिमं स्तोममृभुक्षणः Rv. 8. 7. 9.<BR>—3 A Ṛbhu in general.<BR>—4 Governing far; reigning over Ṛbhus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुमत्|ऋभुमन्त्
ऋभुमत् <i>a.</i> Skilful, prudent; आ नो यज्ञाय तक्षत ऋभुमदूयः Rv. 1. 111. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभ्व
ऋभ्व, ऋभ्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Attacking.<BR>—2 Courageous, determined.<BR>—3 Spreading far.<BR>—4 Clever, skilful; स्तुष्व वर्ष्मन् पुरुवर्त्मानं समृभ्वाणम् Av. 5. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभ्वन्
ऋभ्व, ऋभ्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Attacking.<BR>—2 Courageous, determined.<BR>—3 Spreading far.<BR>—4 Clever, skilful; स्तुष्व वर्ष्मन् पुरुवर्त्मानं समृभ्वाणम् Av. 5. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभ्वन्
ऋभ्वन् <i>a.</i> Shining far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋल्लकः|ऋल्लक
ऋल्लकः A player on a kind of musical instrument. (probably wrong<BR> reading for झल्लक; MW.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋल्लरी
ऋल्लरी A kind of musical instrument; cf. झल्लरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्
ऋश् (A Sautra root)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्य|ऋश्यः
ऋश्य <i>a.</i> [ऋश्-कर्मणि-क्यप्] To be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यः|ऋश्य
ऋश्य + .{@-श्यः@} A white-footed antelope; ऋश्यो न तृप्यन्नवपानमा गहि<BR> Rv. 8. 4. 10. वराहमृश्य पृषतं महारुरुम् Rām. 2. 52. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यम्
ऋश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} Killing, hurt, violation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋश्यकेतुः, ऋश्यकेतनः, ऋश्यदः, ऋश्यपद्, ऋश्यसूकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यकेतुः|ऋश्यकेतु
ऋश्य + -केतुः, -केतनः<BR>—1 N. of Aniruddha, son of Pradyumna.<BR>—2 N. of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यकेतनः|ऋश्यकेतन
ऋश्य + -केतुः, -केतनः<BR>—1 N. of Aniruddha, son of Pradyumna.<BR>—2 N. of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यदः|ऋश्यद
ऋश्य + -दः a pit for catching antelopes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यपद्
ऋश्य + -पद् <i>a.</i> having the feet of an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्यसूकः
ऋश्य + -सूकः N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्
ऋष् I. €6 P. (ऋषति, आर्षीत्, आनर्ष, अर्षितुम्, ऋष्ट)<BR>—1 To go, approach; नैनद्देवा आष्नुवन्पूर्वमवर्षत् Īśop. 4.<BR>—2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">Page0492-1</a>]<BR> kill, injure, pierce; शृङ्गाभ्यां रक्ष ऋषति Av. 9. 4. 17.<BR>—3 To push. ━II. €1 P. (अर्षति)<BR>—1 To flow.<BR>—2 To glide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0491-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभः|ऋषभ
ऋषभः [ऋष्-अभक्; Uṇ. 3. 123]<BR>—1 A bull.<BR>—2 (With names of other animals) the male animal, as अजर्षभः a goat.<BR>—3 The best or most excellent (as the last member of a comp.); as पुरुषर्षभः,<BR> भरतर्षभः &c.<BR>—4 The second of the seven notes of the gamut; (said to be uttered by<BR> cows; गावस्त्वृषभभाषिणः); श्रुतिसमधिकमुच्चैः पञ्चमं पीडयन्तः<BR> सततमृषभहीनं भिन्नकीकृत्य षड्जम् Śi. 11. 1; ऋषभोऽत्र गीयत<BR> इति Āryā. S. 141.<BR>—5 The hollow of the ear.<BR>—6 A boarʼs tail.<BR>—7 A crocodileʼs tail.<BR>—8 A dried plant, one of the 8 principal medicaments. (Mar. बैलघाटी, काकडाशिंगी)<BR>—9 N. of an antidote.<BR>—10 An incarnation of Viṣṇu; नाभेरसावृषभ आस सुदेविसूनुः Bhāg. 2. 7. 10.<BR>—11 A sacrifice (to be performed by kings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभाः
ऋषभः + .{@-भाः@} <i>m.</i> The inhabitants of क्रौञ्चद्वीप; Bhāg. 5. 20. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभी
ऋषभः + .{@-भी@}<BR>—1 A woman with masculine features (as a beard &c.).<BR>—2 A cow.<BR>—3 A widow.<BR>—4 The plant Carpopogon Pruriens (शूकशिंवी); also another plant (शिराला)<BR> (Mar. कुयली)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋषभकूटः, ऋषभद्वीपः, ऋषभद्वीपम्, ऋषभध्वजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभकूटः|ऋषभकूट
ऋषभः + -कूटः N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभद्वीपः|ऋषभद्वीप
ऋषभः + -द्वीपः, -द्वीपम् N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभद्वीपम्
ऋषभः + -द्वीपः, -द्वीपम् N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभध्वजः|ऋषभध्वज
ऋषभः + -ध्वजः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभकः|ऋषभक
ऋषभकः<BR>—1 N. of a medicinal plant.<BR>—2 A bull<BR>—3 N. of a mountain; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभतरः|ऋषभतर
ऋषभतरः A small or young bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिः|ऋषि
ऋषिः [cf. Uṇ. 4. 119]<BR>—1 An inspired poet or sage, a singer of sacred hymns, (<i>e. g.</i> कुत्स,<BR> वसिष्ठ, अत्रि, अगस्त्य &c.). [These Ṛṣis form a class of beings distinct<BR> from gods, men, Asuras &c. (Av. 10. 10. 26). They are the authors or <i>seers</i><BR> of the Vedic hymns; ऋषयो मन्त्रद्रष्टारो वसिष्ठादयः; or, according<BR> to Yāska, यस्य वाक्यं स ऋषिः, <i>i. e.</i> they are the persons to<BR> whom the Vedic hymns were revealed. In every Sūkta the ऋषि is mentioned<BR> along with the देवता, छन्दस् and विनियोग. The later works mention<BR> seven Ṛṣis or <i>saptarṣis</i> whose names, according to Śat. Br., are<BR> गौतम, भरद्वाज, विश्वामित्र, जमदग्नि, वसिष्ठ, कश्यप and अत्रि;<BR> according to Mahābhārata, मरीचि, अत्रि, अङ्गिरस्, पुलह, क्रतु, पुलस्त्य<BR> and वसिष्ठ; Manu calls these sages Prajāpatis or progenitors of<BR> mankind, and gives ten names, three more being added to the latter list,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> दक्ष or प्रचेतस्, भृगु and नारद. In astronomy<BR> the seven Ṛṣis form the constellation of “the Great Bear”; यत्रा<BR> सप्त ऋषीन् पर एकमाहुः Rv. 10. 82. 2.]<BR>—2 A sanctified sage, saint, an ascetic, anchorite; (there are usually<BR> three classes of these saints); देवर्षि, ब्रह्मर्षि and राजार्षि;<BR> sometimes four more are added; महर्षि, परमर्षि, श्रुतर्षि and काण्डर्षि.<BR>—3 A ray of light.<BR>—4 An imaginary circle.<BR>—5 A hymn (मन्त्र) composed by a Ṛṣi; एतद्वोऽस्तु तपोयुक्तं ददामीत्यृषिचोदितम्<BR> Mb. 12. 11. 18;<BR>—6 The Veda; P. III. 2. 186.<BR>—7 A symbolical expression for number seven.<BR>—8 Life; Bhāg. 10. 87. 50.<BR>—9 The moon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋष्यृणम्, ऋषिकुल्या, ऋषिकृत्, ऋषिगिरिः, ऋषिचान्द्रायणम्, ऋषिच्छन्दस्, ऋषिजाङ्गलः, ऋषिजाङ्गलिका, ऋषितर्पणम्, ऋषिधान्यम्, ऋषिपञ्चमी, ऋषिपुत्रकः, ऋषिप्रोक्ता, ऋषिबन्धु, ऋषिमनस्, ऋषिमुखम्, ऋषियज्ञः, ऋषिलोकः, ऋषिश्राद्धम्, ऋषिश्रेष्ठः, ऋषिस्तोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यृणम्
ऋषिः + -ऋणम् A debt<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">Page0492-2</a>]<BR> due to Ṛṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिकुल्या
ऋषिः + -कुल्या<BR>—1 a sacred river.<BR>—2 N. of महानदी, N. of सरस्वती; अथ तस्योशतीं देवीमृषिकुल्यां<BR> सरस्वतीम् Bhāg. 3. 16. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिकृत्
ऋषिः + -कृत् <i>a.</i> making oneʼs appearance; Rv. 1. 31. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिगिरिः|ऋषिगिरि
ऋषिः + -गिरिः N. of a mountain in Magadha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिचान्द्रायणम्
ऋषिः + -चान्द्रायणम् N. of a particular observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिच्छन्दस्
ऋषिः + -च्छन्दस् <i>n.</i> the metre of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गलः|ऋषिजाङ्गल
ऋषिः + -जाङ्गलः, -जाङ्गलिका the plant ऋक्षगन्धा. (Mar. म्हैसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गलिका
ऋषिः + -जाङ्गलः, -जाङ्गलिका the plant ऋक्षगन्धा. (Mar. म्हैसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषितर्पणम्
ऋषिः + -तर्पणम् libation offered to the Ṛṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिधान्यम्
ऋषिः + -धान्यम् The grain Coix barbata (Mar. वरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिपञ्चमी|ऋषिपंचमी
ऋषिः + -पञ्चमी N. of a festival or ceremony on the fifth day in the<BR> first half of Bhādrapada (observed by women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिपुत्रकः|ऋषिपुत्रक
ऋषिः + -पुत्रकः Southern wood, Artemisia abrotanum (Mar. दवणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिप्रोक्ता
ऋषिः + -प्रोक्ता the plant माषपर्णी (Mar. रानौडीद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिबन्धु
ऋषिः + -बन्धु <i>a.</i> connected or related to the Ṛṣi; Rv. 8. 100. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिमनस्
ऋषिः + -मनस् <i>a.</i> inspired; far-seeing, enlightened; Rv. 9. 96. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिमुखम्
ऋषिः + -मुखम् the beginning of a Maṇḍala composed by a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषियज्ञः|ऋषियज्ञ
ऋषिः + -यज्ञः a sacrifice offered to a Ṛṣi (consisting of a prayer<BR> in low voice). Ms. 4. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिलोकः|ऋषिलोक
ऋषिः + -लोकः the world of the Riṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिश्राद्धम्
ऋषिः + -श्राद्धम् Funeral oblations for the Ṛṣis. a figurative expression<BR> for insignificant acts which are preceded by great preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिश्रेष्ठः
ऋषिः + -श्रेष्ठः + ({@-ष्ठम्@}) The pod of Helicteres isora: also the<BR> shrub of tree (Mar. मुरुडर्शेग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिश्रेष्ठम्
ऋषिः + -श्रेष्ठः + ({@-ष्ठम्@}) The pod of Helicteres isora: also the<BR> shrub of tree (Mar. मुरुडर्शेग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिस्तोमः|ऋषिस्तोम
ऋषिः + -स्तोमः<BR>—1 praise of the Ṛṣis.<BR>—2 a particular sacrifice completed in one day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीतत
ऋषीतत <i>a.</i> Celebrated by the (sacred) sages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीवत्|ऋषीवन्त्
ऋषीवत् <i>a.</i> Praising Ṛṣi; associated with Ṛṣis; शिप्रिन्नृषीवः<BR> शचीव्रो Rv. 8. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीवन्
ऋषीवन् <i>a.</i> Ved. Accompanied by sages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिकः|ऋषिक
ऋषि(षी)कः<BR>—1 A Ṛṣi of a lower degree.<BR>—2 N. of a country or its inhabitants (pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीकः|ऋषीक
ऋषि(षी)कः<BR>—1 A Ṛṣi of a lower degree.<BR>—2 N. of a country or its inhabitants (pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिका
ऋषिका <i>f.</i> A female author composing the Ṛks <i>e. g.</i> Viśvārā, Romaśā &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषु|ऋषुः
ऋषु <i>a.</i> (ऋष्-गतौ-कु)<BR>—1 Going.<BR>—2 Great, powerful, strong.<BR>—3 Wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषुः|ऋषु
ऋषु + .{@-षुः@}<BR>—1 A ray of the sun.<BR>—2 A firebrand.<BR>—3 Glowing fire.<BR>—4 A Ṛṣi (who sees the Mantras).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टिः|ऋष्टि
ऋष्टिः <i>m. f.</i> [ऋष्-करणे-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 A double-edged sword. Mb. 1. 194. 7.<BR>—2 A sword (in general). Bhāg. 8. 10. 36.<BR>—3 Any weapon (as a spear or lance &c.).<BR>—4 A kind of musical instrument; सतालवीणामुरजर्ष्टिवेणुभिः Bhāg. 8. 15. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋष्टिविद्युत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टिविद्युत्
ऋष्टिः + -विद्युत् <i>a.</i> shining with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टिमत्|ऋष्टिमन्त्
ऋष्टिमत् <i>a.</i> Furnished with spears (as the Maruts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यः|ऋष्य
ऋष्यः [ऋष्-क्यप्] —1 A white-footed antelope. see ऋश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यम्
ऋष्यः + .{@-ष्यम्@} A kind of leprosy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऋष्याङ्कः, ऋष्यकेतनः, ऋष्यकेतुः, ऋष्यगता, ऋष्यगन्धा, ऋष्यजिह्वम्, ऋष्यप्रोक्ता, ऋष्यमूकः, ऋष्यशृङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्याङ्कः|ऋष्याङ्क
ऋष्यः + -अङ्कः, -केतनः, -केतुः N. of Aniruddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यकेतनः|ऋष्यकेतन
ऋष्यः + -अङ्कः, -केतनः, -केतुः N. of Aniruddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यकेतुः|ऋष्यकेतु
ऋष्यः + -अङ्कः, -केतनः, -केतुः N. of Aniruddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगता
ऋष्यः + -गता the plant Asparagus Racemosus (= ऋष्यप्रोक्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगन्धा
ऋष्यः + -गन्धा the plant ऋक्षगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यजिह्वम्
ऋष्यः + -जिह्वम् a kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यप्रोक्ता
ऋष्यः + -प्रोक्ता N. of several plants; शूकशिंबी, अतिबला, शतावरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यमूकः|ऋष्यमूक
ऋष्यः + -मूकः a mountain near the lake Pampā which formed the temporary<BR> abode of Rāma with the monkey-chief Sugrīva; ऋष्यसूकस्तु पम्पायाः<BR> पुरस्तात् पुष्पितद्रुमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यशृङ्गः|ऋष्यशृङ्ग
ऋष्यः + -शृङ्गः N. of a sage. [He<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-1" target="_blank">Page0493-1</a>]<BR> was the son of Vibhāṇḍaka. According to mythical account he was born<BR> of a female deer, and had a small horn on his forehead, and hence called<BR> ‘Ṛṣyaśṛnga’, or ‘deer-horned’. He was brought up in the forest by<BR> his father, and he saw no other human being till he nearly reached his<BR> manhood. When a great drought well nigh devastated the country of Aṅga,<BR> its king Lomapāda, at the advice of Brāhmaṇas, caused Ṛṣyaśṛṅga<BR> to be brought to him by means of a number of damsels, and gave his daughter Śantā<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-2" target="_blank">Page0493-2</a>]<BR> (adopted by him, her real father being Daśaratha) in marriage to him,<BR> who being greatly pleased caused copious showers of rain to fall in his<BR> kingdom. It was this sage that performed for king Daśaratha the sacrifice<BR> which brought about the birth or Rāma and his three brothers].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0492-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यकः|ऋष्यक
ऋष्यकः A painted or white-footed antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्व|ऋष्वः
ऋष्व <i>a.</i> Ved. Great, high, noble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्वः|ऋष्व
ऋष्व + .{@-ष्वः@} N. of Indra and Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋहत्|ऋहन्त्
ऋहत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Small, weak; Rv. 10. 28. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ <i>ind.</i> An interjection of (1) terror; (2) warding off; (3) reproach<BR> or censure; (4) compassion; (5) remembrance; (6) Commencement of speech;<BR> (7) protection; (8) pride; (9) looking up. ━<i>m.</i> ({@ॠः@})<BR>—1 N. of Bhairava.<BR>—2 A Dānava or demon. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-a2" target="_blank">Page0493-a2</a>]<BR> mother of the gods; also of the demons.<BR>—2 Recollection.<BR>—3 Motion, going. ━<i>n.</i> The breast. (cf. also ॠर्निषेधो भवः पूषा<BR> वरुणोऽमरराडजः । करी तरुर्नरः पाप्मा विद्वानथ रमापतिः ॥ Enm.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ €9 P. (ऋणाति, ईर्ण) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 The mother of the gods.<BR>—4 The female nature.<BR>—5 A mystical letter. (<i>N. B.</i>:− No Sanskrit word begins with ऌ<BR> or ॡ, except some of the technical names of Pāṇini for tenses and<BR> moods; <i>e. g.</i> ऌङ् and ऌट्). cf. also ऌर्म्लेच्छो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-b2" target="_blank">Page0493-b2</a>]<BR> ऽरुणवर्णः स्यात्क्लीबः पापी पराजितः । वीतरागोऽथ पाखण्डी कमलं मरणं च ऌ ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-b1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ <i>f.</i> A mother, a divine female. ━<i>m.</i> Śiva. ━<i>f.</i> = ऌ.<BR> cf. ॡमहात्मा सुरो बालो भूपः स्तोमः कथानकः (वक्ता) | मूर्खो<BR> शिश्नो गुदः कक्षा केशः पापरतो नरः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-b2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए €2 P. (आ + इ)<BR>—1 To come, approach &c.; आमायन्तु ब्रह्मचारिणः T. Up. 1. 4. 2.<BR>—2 To reach, attain, come into (a state or position) स सर्वसमतामेत्य Ms. 12. 125.<BR>—3 To submit; fall to oneʼs share; तस्मात्त्वां पृथग्वलय आयन्ति Ch. Up. 5. 14. 1.<BR> (आययन्ति ?). (See इ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एः
एः <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 The number खर्व; cf. also एः कुमारोऽसुरोऽरातिर्ज्ञातीयोऽहित उद्धतः ।<BR> आत्मा शेषो विवस्वांश्च कृतार्थो मध्वरिः शरः ॥ Enm. ━<i>ind.</i> An<BR> interjection of (1) remembering; (2) envy; (3) compassion; (4) calling;<BR> (5) contempt or censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक|एकं|एकः
एक <i>pron. a.</i> [इ-कन्]<BR>—1 One, single, alone, only; वायुर्यथैको भुवनं प्रविष्टो … एकस्तथा …<BR> Kaṭh. 2. 5. 10; Mb. 4. 49. 5, 6; बलिभिर्मुखमाक्रान्तं पलितैरङ्कितं<BR> शिरः । गात्राणि शिथिलायन्ते तृणैका तरुणायते ॥ Bh. 3. 14.<BR>—2 Not accompanied by anyone; एकः संप्रति नाशितप्रियतमस्तामद्य<BR> रामः कथम् U. 2. 28.<BR>—3 The same, one and the same, identical;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c2" target="_blank">Page0493-c2</a>]<BR> एकान्वयो मम Ś. 7; मनस्येकं वचस्येकं कर्मण्येकं महात्मनाम् H. 1. 197.<BR>—4 Firm, unchanged; एको ग्रहस्तु Pt. 1. 260.<BR>—5 Single of its kind, unique, singular.<BR>—6 Chief, supreme, prominent, sole; ब्राह्मण्यास्तद्धरेत्पुत्र एकांशं<BR> वै पितुर्धनात् Mb. 13. 47. 11. ˚पार्थिव, ˚धनुर्धरः, ˚ऐश्वर्य M. 1. 1<BR> sole sovereignty; एको रागिषु राजते Bh. 3. 121.<BR>—7 Peerless, matchless.<BR>—8 One of two or many; Me. 30. एकः सख्यास्तव सह मया वामपादाभिलाषी Me. 80.<BR>—9 Oft. used like the English indefinite article ‘a’ or ‘an’; ज्योतिरेकम् Ś. 5. 30.<BR>—10 True.<BR>—11 Little. Oft. used in the middle of comp. in the sense of ‘only’, with<BR> an adjectival or adverbial force; दोषैकदृक् looking only to faults;<BR> त्वदेकेषु Ku. 3. 15 your arrow only; so भोगैकबद्धस्पृहः. एकः ━अन्यः,<BR> or अपरः the one━the other; अजामेकां लोहित …<BR> नमामः । अजो ह्येको … अजोन्यः Śvet. Up. 4. 5; it is used in the<BR> plural in the sense of some, its correlative being अन्ये or अपरे<BR> (others); एके समूहुर्बलरेणुसंहतिं शिरोभिराज्ञामपरे महीभृतः ॥<BR> Śi. 12. 45; see अन्य, अपर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकः|एक|एकं
एक + .{@-कः@} N. of Viṣṇu. the Supreme Being or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0494-1" target="_blank">Page0494-1</a>]<BR> Prajāpati; एक इति च प्रजापतेरभिधानमिति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकम्
एक + .{@-कः@} + .({@-कम्@})<BR>—1 The mind; एकं विनिन्ये स जुगोप सप्त सप्तैव तत्याज ररक्ष पञ्च<BR> Bu. C. 2. 41. 2 unity, a unit; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0493-c1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एका
एक + .{@-का@} N. of Durgā. [cf. Persian <i>yak</i>; L. <i>aequs</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: एकांशः, एकाक्ष, एकाक्षर, एकाग्नि, एकाग्र, एकाग्र्य, एकाङ्गः, एकाञ्जलिः, एकाङ्गिका, एकाण्डः, एकाधिपतिः, एकानंशा, एकानुदिष्ट, एकान्त, एकान्तर, एकान्तिक, एकान्तित्वम्, एकान्तिन्, एकान्नम्, एकापचयः, एकापायः, एकाब्दा, एकायन, एकार्णवः, एकार्थ, एकावम, एकावयव, एकाशीत, एकाशीतिः, एकाष्टका, एकाष्ठीका, एकाष्ठील, एकाहन्, एकातपत्र, एकात्मन्, एकादेशः, एकायु, एकावलिः, एकावली, एकाहार्य, एकोक्तिः, एकोत्तर, एकोदकः, एकोदरः, एकोदरा, एकोदात्त, एकोद्दिष्टम्, एकोन, एकर्च्, एकैक, एकैकश्यम्, एकैकश्येन, एकौघः, एककपाल, एककर, एककार्य, एककालः, एककालिकम्, एककालीन, एककुण्डलः, एककुण्डलिन्, एककुष्ठम्, एकक्षीरम्, एकगम्यः, एकगुरु, एकगुरुक, एकग्राम, एकग्रामीण, एकचक्र, एकचत्वारिंशत्, एकचर, एकचरण, एकचारिन्, एकचित्त, एकचिन्तनम्, एकचिन्मय, एकचेतस्, एकमनस्, एकचोदन, एकच्छत्र, एकच्छायाश्रित, एकज, एकजः, एकजा, एकजटा, एकजन्मन्, एकजात, एकजाति, एकजातीय, एकजीववादः, एकज्या, एकज्योतिस्, एकतान, एकताल, एकतालः, एकलम्, एकतीर्थिन्, एकतेजन, एकत्रिंशत्, एकत्रिकः, एकदंष्ट्रः, एकदन्तः, एकदण्डिन्, एकदलः, एकपत्रः, एकदिश्, एकदुःखसुख, एकदृश्, एकदृष्टि, एकदृश्य, एकदृष्टिः, एकदेवः, एकदेवत, एकदेवत्य, एकदैवत्य, एकदेश, एकदेशिन्, एकदेह, एकदेहिन्, एकधनः, एकधनिन्, एकधर्मन्, एकधर्मिन्, एकधुर, एकधुरावह, एकधुरीण, एकधुरा, एकनक्षत्रम्, एकनटः, एकनयनः, एकनवतः, एकनवतिः, एकनाथ, एकनायकः, एकनिश्चय, एकनिपातः, एकनिष्ठ, एकनेत्रः, एकपक्ष, एकपक्षीभावः, एकपञ्चाशत्, एकपतिक, एकपत्नी, एकपत्रिका, एकपद्, एकपाद्, एकपद, एकपर, एकपरि, एकपर्णा, एकपलाशः, एकपाटला, एकपाणः, एकपात, एकतः, एकपातिन्, एकपाद, एकपादिका, एकपार्थिवः, एकपिङ्गः, एकपिङ्गलः, एकपिण्ड, एकपिण्डता, एकपिण्डत्वम्, एकपुत्र, एकपुरुषः, एकपुष्कलः, एकप्रकार, एकप्रख्य, एकप्रभुत्वम्, एकप्रयत्नः, एकप्रस्थः, एकप्रहारिक, एकप्राणयोगः, एकबुद्धि, एकभक्त, एकभक्ति, एकभार्या, एकभाव, एकभूत, एकभूमः, एकभोजन, एकभुक्त, एकमति, एकमनस्, एकमात्र, एकमुख, एकमूर्धन्, एकमूला, एकयष्टिः, एकयष्टिका, एकयोनि, एकरजः, एकरथः, एकरश्मि, एकरस, एकराज्, एकराजः, एकरात्रः, एकरात्रिक, एकराशिः, एकरिक्थिन्, एकरूप, एकरूप्य, एकलिङ्गः, एकवचनम्, एकवर्ण, एकवर्णिक, एकवर्