एरु
एरु <i>a.</i> Ved. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0500-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्वारुः|एर्वारु|एर्व्वारुः
एर्वारुः, एर्वारुकः A species of cucumber. कट्वैर्वारौ यथाऽपक्वे<BR> मधुरः सन् रसोऽपि न Y. 3. 142.<BR> q. v. उर्वारुक and उर्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0500-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्वारुकः|एर्वारुक
एर्वारुः, एर्वारुकः A species of cucumber. कट्वैर्वारौ यथाऽपक्वे<BR> मधुरः सन् रसोऽपि न Y. 3. 142.<BR> q. v. उर्वारुक and उर्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0500-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलकः|एलक
एलकः A ram; see एडक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0500-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालु
एलवालु <i>n.</i>, एलवालकम्<BR>—1 The fragrant bark of कपित्थ (Feronia Elephantum).<BR>—2 A granular substance (used as a drug and perfume).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालकम्
एलवालु <i>n.</i>, एलवालकम्<BR>—1 The fragrant bark of कपित्थ (Feronia Elephantum).<BR>—2 A granular substance (used as a drug and perfume).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलविलः|एलविल
एलविलः N. of Kubera; see ऐलेविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एला
एला<BR>—1 Cardamom plant; एलानां फलरेणवः R. 4. 47, 6. 64.<BR>—2 Cardamoms (the seed of the plant).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: एलापर्णी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलापर्णी|एलापर्ण्णी
एला + -पर्णी the plant Mimosa Octandra. (Mar. रास्ना, कोळिंजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलानः|एलान
एलानः An orange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलीका
एलीका Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलायति
एलायति Den. P.<BR>—1 To be merry or frolicsome.<BR>—2 To be wantonly mischievous in behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलुकम्
एलुकम्<BR>—1 A kind of perfume.<BR>—2 A medicinal substance or plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
1. एव <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Going, moving.<BR>—2 Speedy, quick; एवो गन्ता; ये च एवा मरुतः Uṇ. 1. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवः|एव|एवं
1. एव + .{@-वः@} —1 A course, way; or a courser, a fleet horse; स्वेभिरेवैश्चरतः<BR> Rv. 1. 62. 8; (pl.) mode of proceeding, custom, habit; or according to<BR> Sāyaṇa a desire or hymn.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: एवया, एवयावन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवया
एव + -या <i>a.</i> granting protection; or going in ways or courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवयावन्
एव + -यावन् <i>a.</i> going with horses or granting desires, going quickly.<BR>━<i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
2. एव <i>ind.</i> This particle is most frequently used to strengthen<BR> and emphasize the idea expressed by a word:− (1) Just, quite, exactly;<BR> एवमेव quite so, just so; (2) same, very, identical; अर्थोष्मणा<BR> विरहितः पुरुषः स एव Bh. 2. 40 that very man; (3) only, alone, merely,<BR> (implying exclusion); सा तथ्यमेवाभिहिता भवेन Ku. 3. 63 only the<BR> truth, nothing but the truth; so नाम्नैव, स एव वीरः he alone (and<BR> not others); (4) already; गत एव न ते निवर्तते Ku. 4. 30; (5)<BR> scarcely, the moment, as soon as; chiefly with participles; उपस्थितेयं<BR> कल्याणी नाम्नि कीर्तित एव यत् R. 1. 87 as soon as the name was uttered;<BR> इति चिन्तयन्नेव while just thinking &c.; (6) also, likewise; तथैव<BR> so also; (7) like, as (showing similarity); श्रीस्त एव मेस्तु G. M.<BR> (= तव इव); and (8) generally to emphasize a statement; भवितव्यमेव<BR> तेन U. 4 it <i>will</i> (surely) take place. It is also said to imply<BR> the senses of (9) detraction; (10) diminution (11) command; (12) restraint;<BR> or (13) used merely as an expletive. (This particle is used in the Vedas<BR> in the senses of so, just so, like, indeed, truly, really) (14) Again;<BR> एवशब्दश्च पुनरित्यस्मिन्नर्थे भविष्यति । यथा क्षीरेण भुक्त्वा देवदत्तः<BR> क्षीरेणैव भुञ्जीतेति । भुञ्जीतैवेति पुनरिति गम्यते । ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्
एवम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Thus, so, in this manner or way; (referring to what precedes as well<BR> as to what follows); अस्त्येवम् Pt. 1 it is so; एवंवादिनि देवर्षौ<BR> Ku. 6. 84; ब्रूया एवम् Me. 103 (what follows); एवमस्तु be it so,<BR> amen; यद्येवम् so;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">Page0501-2</a>]<BR> किमेवम् why so; मैवम्, मा मैवम् oh, not so, (do not do so) एवम्<BR> has sometimes an adjectival force; एवं वचनम् such words.<BR>—2 Yes, quite so (implying assent); सीता -अहो जाने तास्मिन्नेव काले वर्ते ।<BR> राम- एवम् U. 1; एवं यदात्थ भगवन् Ku. 2. 31. It is also said<BR> to have the senses of.<BR>—3 likeness.<BR>—4 sameness of manner;<BR>—5 affirmation or determination;<BR>—6 command; or it is often used merely as an expletive. (In the Vedas<BR> एवम् occurs very rarely; its place being usually taken up by एव).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: एवमवस्थ, एवमादि, एवमाद्य, एवङ्कान्तम्, एवङ्कारम्, एवङ्काल, एवङ्क्रतु, एवङ्गत, एवङ्गुण, एवन्नामन्, एवम्प्रकार, एवम्प्राय, एवम्भूत, एवंरूप, एवंवादः, एवंविद्, एवंविद्वस्, एवंविध, एवंवीर्य, एवंवृत्त, एवंवृत्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवमवस्थ
एवम् + -अवस्थ <i>a.</i> so situated or circumstanced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवमादि
एवम् + -आदि, -आद्य <i>a.</i> of such qualities or kind, such and the like;<BR> एवमादिभिः Ś. 5; Ku. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवमाद्य
एवम् + -आदि, -आद्य <i>a.</i> of such qualities or kind, such and the like;<BR> एवमादिभिः Ś. 5; Ku. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्कान्तम्
एवम् + -कान्तम् A column connected with one, two or three minor pillars<BR> and having a lotus-shaped base; एकोपपादसंयुक्तं द्वित्र्युपपादेन संयुतम् ।<BR> एवंकान्तमिति प्रोक्तं मूले पद्मासनान्वितम् ॥ Māna. 15. 242-3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्कारम्
एवम् + -कारम् <i>ind.</i> in this manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्काल
एवम् + -काल <i>a.</i> containing so many syllabic instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्क्रतु
एवम् + -क्रतु <i>a.</i> Ved. thus minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्गत
एवम् + -गत <i>a.</i> being in this condition or so circumstanced; एवं<BR> गते under these circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवङ्गुण
एवम् + -गुण <i>a.</i> possessing such virtues; पुत्रमेवंगुणोपेतं चक्रवर्तिनमाप्नुहि Ś. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवन्नामन्
एवम् + -नामन् <i>a.</i> so called, bearing this name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्प्रकार
एवम् + -प्रकार, -प्राय <i>a.</i> of such a kind; वयमपि न खल्वेवंप्रायाः<BR> क्रतुप्रतिघातिनः U. 5. 29; Ś. 7. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्प्राय
एवम् + -प्रकार, -प्राय <i>a.</i> of such a kind; वयमपि न खल्वेवंप्रायाः<BR> क्रतुप्रतिघातिनः U. 5. 29; Ś. 7. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्भूत|एवंभूत
एवम् + -भूत <i>a.</i> of such quality or description, so, such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंरूप
एवम् + -रूप <i>a.</i> of such a kind or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंवादः|एवंवाद
एवम् + -वादः such an expression. एवंवादिनि देवर्षौ पार्श्वे पितुरधोमुखी K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंविद्
एवम् + -विद्, -विद्वस् <i>a.</i> knowing so or such, well-informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंविद्वस्
एवम् + -विद्, -विद्वस् <i>a.</i> knowing so or such, well-informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंविध
एवम् + -विध <i>a.</i> of such a kind, such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंवीर्य
एवम् + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> possessing such a power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंवृत्त
एवम् + -वृत्त, -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> behaving such; of such a kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवंवृत्ति
एवम् + -वृत्त, -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> behaving such; of such a kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवावद|एवावदः
एवावद <i>a.</i> Ved. So speaking, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवावदः|एवावद
एवावद + .{@-दः@} N. of a Ṛṣi; Rv. 5. 44. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्
एष् €1 U. (एषति-ते, एषितुम्, एषित)<BR>—1 To go or approach.<BR>—2 To hasten towards, fly at, attack any one.<BR>—3 To endeavour to reach or gain.<BR>—4 To request.<BR>—5 To desire.<BR>—6 To creep or glide; पराङ्मित्र एषतु Av. 6. 67. 3.<BR>—7 To know; एषितुं प्रेषितो यातो मया तस्यानुजो वनम् Bk. 5. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
एष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirable, to be desired.<BR>—2 Gliding, running; epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषः|एष
एष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 Running or hastening towards.<BR>—2 Seeking.<BR>—3 Wish, choice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषा
एष + .{@-षा@} Wish, desire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: एषवीरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषवीरः|एषवीर
एष + -वीरः N. of a despised Brāhmaṇa family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषण|एषणः
एषण <i>a.</i> Seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणः|एषण
एषण + .{@-णः@} An iron-arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणम्
एषण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Seeking.<BR>—2 Wish, desire.<BR>—3 Driving, pressing.<BR>—4 Probing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणा
एषण + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 Seeking; wish, desire; अपहतसकलैषणामलात्मन्यविरतमेधितभावनोपहूतः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 31. 20.<BR>—2 Begging, request. ˚समितिः Correct behaviour when eating food,<BR> one of the पञ्चसमितिs or five rules of careful Conduct (Jainism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणी
एषण + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A goldsmithʼs balance.<BR>—2 A probe (of iron or steel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिका
एषणिका A goldsmithʼs balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिन्
एषणिन् <i>a.</i> Seeking, striving to get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0501-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणीय
एषणीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be desired or desirable; जायापतीलौकिकमेषणीयम् Ku. 7. 88; Ki. 13. 28.<BR>—2 To be aimed at or sought.<BR>—3 To be approached.<BR>—4 (At the end of comp.) Relating to medical examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषिका
एषिका The iron beam without a ring or a cap (Mar. सळई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषितृ
एषितृ <i>a.</i> Wishing, desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषिन्
एषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Driving, impelling.<BR>—2 Desiring, desirous of, wishing (at the end of comp.); यौवने विषयैषिणाम् R. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टव्य
एष्टव्य <i>a.</i> To be striven after, wished for; एष्टव्या बहवः<BR> पुत्रा गुणवन्तो बहुश्रुताः Rām. 2. 107. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टव्यम्
एष्टव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} Desire; एष्टव्ये सति चिन्त्योऽहम् Mb. 14. 55. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टिः|एष्टि
एष्टिः <i>f.</i> Wish, desire; शश्वद् बभूथ सुहव एष्टौ Rv. 6. 21. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्य
एष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be desired or sought; ब्रह्मैव विद्वानेष्यः Av. 12. 2. 39.<BR>—2 To be approached.<BR>—3 To be probed, examined medically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एह
एह Ved.<BR>—1 Desirous.<BR>—2 Striving well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एहस्
एहस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Anger.<BR>—2 Emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एहिमाय
एहिमाय <i>a.</i> Ved. Of all-pervading intellect, an epithet of the<BR> Viśvedevas; cf. एहिमायासो अद्रुहः Rv. 1. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ (निपातोऽभिमुखीकरणे) An interjection to attract attention;<BR> ऐ वाचं देहि … … Bk. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐः
ऐः <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva. ━<i>ind.</i> An interjection of (1) calling (=<BR> Hallo, ho); (2) remembrance; (3) inviting. cf. also ऐः क्रूरो धरणीनाथः<BR> पूरो मारोऽमरोऽसुरः । कुलालो राधरः प्राज्ञो मन्दः पुत्रोऽथवा नरः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक
ऐक <i>a.</i> Belonging to one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐककर्म्यम्
ऐककर्म्यम्<BR>—1 Unity of action (Jaina.).<BR>—2 The state of having one fruit; ऐककर्म्यमिति । कर्मशब्देनात्र फलमुच्यते ।<BR> क्रियते इति । तद् येषामेकं तानि एककर्माणि । तेषां भाव ऐककर्म्यम् एकफलमित्यर्थः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐककाल्यम्
ऐककाल्यम् (see सद्यस्कालता). वचनाद्वैककाल्यं स्यात् । Ms. 5. 4. 24.<BR> unity of time (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकगुण्यम्
ऐकगुण्यम् The value of single unit, simple unity; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकद्यम्
ऐकद्यम् <i>ind.</i> At once, together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकध्यम्
ऐकध्यम् Singleness of time or occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपत्यम्
ऐकपत्यम्<BR>—1 Sole sovereignty, supreme power.<BR>—2 Absolute monarchy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपदिक
ऐकपदिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a simple word.<BR>—2 Consisting of single words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपदिकम्
ऐकपदिक + .{@-कम्@} The name given to the Naigama section of Yāskaʼs commentary<BR> on the Nighaṇṭavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपद्यम्
ऐकपद्यम्<BR>—1 Unity of words.<BR>—2 Being formed into one word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकभाव्यम्
ऐकभाव्यम् Singleness of nature or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकमत्यम्
ऐकमत्यम् Unanimity, agreement, sameness of opinion; ऐकमत्यादमात्यवर्गः<BR> साकेतनाथं विधिवच्चकार R. 18. 36; अत्र सर्वेषामैकमत्यम् H. 1<BR> all are unanimous on this point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकमुख्यम्
ऐकमुख्यम्<BR>—1 Complete ownership (Gīrvāṇa.).<BR>—2 Subordination; नीतं चास्मान्प्रति शिथिलतामैकमुख्यं सुराणाम् Mv. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकराज्यम्
ऐकराज्यम् Sole Monarchy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशतिक
ऐकशतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Provided with 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशफ
ऐकशफ <i>a.</i> (-फी <i>f.</i>) Produced by or relating to animals<BR> with uncloven hoofs (as milk &c.); Ms. 5. 8; Y. 1. 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशब्द्यम्
ऐकशब्द्यम्<BR>—1 The state of having the same term (to express them), the state of being<BR> expressed or referred to by the same term; सर्वस्य वैकशब्द्यात् । MS. 7. 1. 18.<BR>—2 Sameness or identity of words (Jaina.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकश्रुत्यम्
ऐकश्रुत्यम्, ऐकस्वर्यम् The one accentless-monotonous tone, monotony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकस्वर्यम्
ऐकश्रुत्यम्, ऐकस्वर्यम् The one accentless-monotonous tone, monotony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकसहस्रिक
ऐकसहस्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Provided with 1001.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकागारिकः|ऐकागारिक
ऐकागारिकः (P. IV. 1. 113.)<BR>—1 A thief (breaking into lonely houses); केनचित्तु हस्तवतैकागारिकेण<BR> Dk. 67; Śi. 19. 111.<BR>—2 The owner of a single house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाग्र
ऐकाग्र <i>a.</i> Intent on one object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाग्र्यम्
ऐकाग्र्यम् Intentness on one object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाङ्गः|ऐकाङ्ग|ऐकांग|ऐकांगः
ऐकाङ्गः A soldier who serves as the body-guard; Rāj. T. 5. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकात्म्यम्
ऐकात्म्यम्<BR>—1 Unity, unity of soul; यथैकात्म्यानुभावानां विकल्परहितः स्वयम्<BR> Bhāg. 6. 8. 32.<BR>—2 Identity, sameness.<BR>—3 Oneness with the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाधिकरण्यम्
ऐकाधिकरण्यम्<BR>—1 Oneness of relation.<BR>—2 Existence in the same subject; co-extension (in Logic); साध्येन हेतोरैकाधिकारण्यं<BR> व्याप्तिरुच्यते Bhāṣā P. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्तिक|ऐकांतिक
ऐकान्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Absolute, complete, perfect; Bg. 14. 27.<BR>—2 Assured, certain; ऐकान्तिकमात्यन्तिकमुभयम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">Page0503-1</a>]<BR> Sāṅ. K. 68; Mu. 4.<BR>—3 Exclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्तिके
ऐकान्तिक + .{@-के@} In private, apart from others; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0502-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्त्यम्
ऐकान्त्यम्<BR>—1 Absoluteness, exclusiveness.<BR>—2 Friendship (सख्य); तन्मन्यसे यत्र नैकान्त्यमस्ति Mb. 8. 42. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्यिकः|ऐकान्यिक
ऐकान्यिकः A pupil who commits one error in reading or reciting (the<BR> Vedas). ऐकान्यिकोऽपि न बभूव यतोऽत्र तेन प्रापाभिधा नमिह बालसरस्वतीति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकार्थ्यम्
ऐकार्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Sameness of aim or purpose.<BR>—2 Consistency in meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाहिक|ऐकाहिकं
ऐकाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Ephemeral.<BR>—2 Of one or the same day, quotidian.<BR>—3 Lasting for one day (as a sacrifice, fever, festival &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्यम्
ऐक्यम्<BR>—1 Oneness, unity, harmony; तेषां द्वयोर्द्वयोरैक्यं बिभिदे न कदाचन<BR> R. 10. 82; U. 6. 33.<BR>—2 Unanimity.<BR>—3 Identity, sameness.<BR>—4 Especially, the identity of the human soul or of the universe with the Deity.<BR>—5 An aggregate, whole.<BR>—6 (In alg.) The product of the length and depth of the portions or little<BR> excavations differing in depth (Colebrooke).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐक्यारोपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्यारोपः|ऐक्यारोप
ऐक्यम् + -आरोपः Equalization; Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव|ऐक्षवं
ऐक्षव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>) [इक्षु-अण्] Made of, or produced<BR> from, sugarcane, sugary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षवम्
ऐक्षव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Sugar.<BR>—2 A kind of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव्य
ऐक्षव्य <i>a.</i> Made of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुक|ऐक्षुकः
ऐक्षुक <i>a.</i> [इक्षु-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Suitable for sugar-cane.<BR>—2 Bearing sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुकः|ऐक्षुक
ऐक्षुक + .{@-कः@} A carrier of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुभारिक
ऐक्षुभारिक <i>a.</i> [इक्षुभार-ठञ्] Carrying a load of sugar-canes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाक|ऐक्ष्वाकः
ऐक्ष्वाक <i>a.</i> [इक्ष्वाकु-अण्] Belonging to Ikṣvāku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाकः|ऐक्ष्वाक
ऐक्ष्वाक + .{@-कः, -कुः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Ikṣvāku; सत्यमैक्ष्वाकः खल्वसि U. 5.<BR>—2 The country ruled by the Aikṣvākus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाकुः|ऐक्ष्वाकु
ऐक्ष्वाक + .{@-कः, -कुः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Ikṣvāku; सत्यमैक्ष्वाकः खल्वसि U. 5.<BR>—2 The country ruled by the Aikṣvākus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐङ्गुद|ऐंगुद|ऐङ्गुदं
ऐङ्गुद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>) [इङ्गुदी-अण्] Produced from<BR> the इङ्गुदी tree; ऐङ्गुदं बदरैर्मिश्रं पिण्याकं दर्भसंस्तरे Rām. 2. 103. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐङ्गुदम्
ऐङ्गुद + .{@-दम्@} The nut of the इङ्गुदी tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐच्छिक
ऐच्छिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [इच्छा-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Optional, voluntary; विकल्पो व्यवस्थितो न त्वैच्छिकः Dāy. B.<BR>—2 Arbitrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐड|ऐडः
ऐड <i>a.</i> Ved. [इडा-अण्]<BR>—1 Containing anything refreshing; Vāj. 15. 7.<BR>—2 Containing the word (इडा) (such as a chapter).<BR>—3 Belonging to a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडः|ऐड
ऐड + .{@-डः@} N. of Purūravas (इडाया अपत्यम्); cf. Rv. 10. 95. 18 (ऐळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडक|ऐडकः
ऐडक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Belonging to a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडकः|ऐडक
ऐडक + .{@-कः@} A species of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडविडः|ऐडविड
ऐड(ल)विडः(लः)<BR>—1 N. of Kubera. अवलम्बितैलविलपाणिपल्लवः Śi. 13. 18.<BR>—2 The planet Mars (मङ्गल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविलः|ऐलविल
ऐड(ल)विडः(लः)<BR>—1 N. of Kubera. अवलम्बितैलविलपाणिपल्लवः Śi. 13. 18.<BR>—2 The planet Mars (मङ्गल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडुकम्
ऐडु(डू)कम्^1 A wall &c. of bones and rubbish.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडूकम्
ऐडु(डू)कम्^1 A wall &c. of bones and rubbish.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐण|ऐणं
ऐण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>) [एण-अण्] Of or belonging to an<BR> antelope (as skin, wool &c.); Y. 1. 259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणिक|ऐणिकः
ऐणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Hunting black antelopes, a deer-killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेय|ऐणेयं|ऐणेयः
ऐणेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>) [एणी-ठक्] Produced from the<BR> black doe or from anything connected with her. ऐणेयचर्माम्बरमर्कधामभिर्युतं<BR> जटाभिर्ददृशे पुरीं विशन् Bhāg. 9. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेयः|ऐणेय|ऐणेयं
ऐणेय + .{@-यः@} A black antelope; a little doe (हरिणशाव); ते तानावारयिष्यन्ति<BR> ऐणेयानिव तन्तुना Mb. 5. 57. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेयम्
ऐणेय + .{@-यम्@} A kind of coitus (रतिबन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतदात्म्यम्
ऐतदात्म्यम् The state of having this property or peculiarity; स<BR> य एषोऽणिमैतदात्म्यमिदं सर्वं तत्सत्यम् Ch. Up. 6. 9. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेय|ऐतरेयः
ऐतरेय <i>a.</i> [इतरा-ठक्] Originating from Aitareya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयः|ऐतरेय
ऐतरेय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} A descendant of Itarā (or Itara, a sage) to whom the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa and Āraṇyaka were revealed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐतरेयारण्यकम्, ऐतरेयोपनिषद्, ऐतरेयब्राह्मणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयम्
ऐतरेय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} A descendant of Itarā (or Itara, a sage) to whom the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa and Āraṇyaka were revealed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐतरेयारण्यकम्, ऐतरेयोपनिषद्, ऐतरेयब्राह्मणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयारण्यकम्
ऐतरेय + -आरण्यकम् N. of the Āraṇyaka composed by Aitareya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयोपनिषद्
ऐतरेय + -उपनिषद् N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयब्राह्मणम्
ऐतरेय + -ब्राह्मणम् N. of the Brāhmaṇa composed by Aitareya (attached<BR> to the Ṛgveda and prescribing the duties of the Hotṛ priest) It is<BR> divided into forty Adhyāyas or eight Pañcikās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयिन्
ऐतरेयिन् <i>m.</i> A reader of the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतशः|ऐतश
ऐतशः N. of a Muni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐतशप्रलापः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतशप्रलापः|ऐतशप्रलाप
ऐतशः + -प्रलापः N. of a section of the Atharvaveda by the above Muni<BR> (Coming after the Kuntāpa hymns).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिक|ऐतिहासिकः
ऐतिहासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [इतिहास-ठक्]<BR>—1 Traditional.<BR>—2 Historical<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिकः|ऐतिहासिक
ऐतिहासिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An historian.<BR>—2 One who knows or studies ancient legends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिह्यम्
ऐतिह्यम् —1 Traditional instruction, legendary account; ऐतिह्यमनुमानं<BR> च प्रत्यक्षमपि चागमम् Rām.; किलेत्यैतिह्ये (ऐतिह्य is regarded<BR> as one of the Pramāṇas or proofs by the Paurāṇika as and reckoned<BR> along with प्रत्यक्ष अनुमान &c.; see अनुभव). प्रत्यक्षं ह्येतयोर्मूलं<BR> कृतान्तैतिह्ययोरपि Mb. 12. 218. 27; श्रुतिः प्रत्यक्षमैतिह्यमनुमानं<BR> चतुष्टयम् । प्रमाणेष्वनवस्थानाद्रिकल्पात्स विरज्यते ॥ Bhāg. 11. 19. 17.<BR>—2 Tradition -a figure of speech; Kuval. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐदंपर्यम्
ऐदंपर्यम् Substance, scope, bearing (lit. state of being इदंपर,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> having this meaning, purport or scope); इदं त्वैदंपर्यम् Māl. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐदंयुगीन
ऐदंयुगीन <i>a.</i> Fit for this yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन
ऐन <i>a.</i> (इनः सूर्यः, तस्य इदम्) Of the sun. निर्वर्ण्य<BR> वर्णेन समानमैनं बिम्बेन बिम्बं च्युतमस्तशृङ्गात् Rām. Ch. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐनसम्
ऐनसम् Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दव|ऐंदव|ऐन्दवं|ऐन्दवः
ऐन्दव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>) [इन्दु-अण्] Lunar; ऐन्दवः<BR> प्राक्प्रकाशः Māl. 8. 1; U. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दवः|ऐन्दव|ऐंदव|ऐन्दवं
ऐन्दव + .{@-वः@} A lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दवी
ऐन्दव + .{@-वी@} The plant सोमराजी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दवम्
ऐन्दव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 The asterism Mṛgaśiras.<BR>—2 The <i>Vrata</i> called चान्द्रायण q. v.; संकरापात्रकृत्यासु<BR> मासं शोधनमैन्दवम् Ms. 11. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0503-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दुमतेयः|ऐन्दुमतेय
ऐन्दुमतेयः A descendant of Indumatī. N. of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्र|ऐंद्र|ऐन्द्रं|ऐन्द्रः
ऐन्द्र <i>a.</i> (-न्द्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इन्द्र-अण्] Belonging or sacred to Indra; ऋद्धं<BR> हि राज्यं पदमैन्द्रमाहुः R. 2. 50: 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रः|ऐन्द्र|ऐंद्र|ऐन्द्रं
ऐन्द्र + .{@-न्द्रः@}<BR>—1 N. of Arjuna and of Vāli (who are regarded as sons of इन्द्र).<BR>—2 N. of a Saṃvatsara.<BR>—3 The part of a sacrifice offered to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्री
ऐन्द्र + .{@-न्द्री@}<BR>—1 N. of a <i>Ṛk</i> addressed to Indra; इत्यादिका काचिदैन्द्री समाम्नाता J. N. V.<BR>—2 The east, eastern direction (presided over by Indra); अयमैन्द्रीमुखं<BR> पश्य रक्तश्चुम्बति चन्द्रमाः Candr. 5. 58; Ki. 9. 18.<BR>—3 The eighteenth lunar mansion.<BR>—4 The eighth day in the second half of the months of मार्गशीर्ष and पौष.<BR>—5 Indraʼs energy (personified as his wife Śachī).<BR>—6 Misfortune, misery.<BR>—7 A kind of cucumber.<BR>—8 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—9 Small cardamom; यष्ट्याह्वमैन्द्रीनलिनानि दूर्वा Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रम्
ऐन्द्र + .{@-न्द्रम्@}<BR>—1 The eighteenth lunar mansion (ज्येष्ठा).<BR>—2 Wild ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रजालिक|ऐंद्रजालिक|ऐन्द्रजालिकः
ऐन्द्रजालिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इन्द्रजालेन चरति ठक्]<BR>—1 Deceptive, magical; illusive.<BR>—2 Familiar with magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रजालिकः|ऐन्द्रजालिक|ऐंद्रजालिक
ऐन्द्रजालिक + .{@-कः@} A juggler; छलयन्प्रजास्त्वमनृतेन कपटपटुरैन्द्रजालिकः Śi. 15. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रतुरीयः|ऐन्द्रतुरीय|ऐंद्रतुरीयः
ऐन्द्रतुरीयः The fourth part of a libation to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक|ऐंद्रलुप्तिक|ऐन्द्रलुप्तिकः
ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Affected with morbid baldness of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रशिरः|ऐन्द्रशिर|ऐंद्रशिरः
ऐन्द्रशिरः A species of elephant; Rām. 2. 70. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्राग्न|ऐंद्राग्न
ऐन्द्राग्न <i>a.</i> Relating to Indra and Agni; so ऐन्द्रवारुण, ऐन्द्रसौम्य<BR> &c. ऐन्द्राग्नेन विधानेन दक्षिणामिति न श्रुतम् Mb. 12. 60. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रिः|ऐन्द्रि|ऐंद्रिः
ऐन्द्रिः [इन्द्रस्यापत्यं-इञ्]<BR>—1 N. of Jayanta, Arjuna, or Vāli, the monkey-chief.<BR>—2 A crow; ऐन्द्रिः किल नखैस्तस्या विददार स्तनौ द्विजः R. 12. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रिय|ऐंद्रिय
ऐन्द्रिय, -यक <i>a.</i><BR> [इन्द्रिय-अण्, वुञ् वा]<BR>—1 Belonging to the senses, sensual. यथा मनोरथः स्वप्नः सर्वमैन्द्रियकं<BR> मृषा Bhāg. 7. 2. 48. मूढमैन्द्रियकं लुब्धमनार्यचरितं शठम् Mb. 12. 93. 16.<BR>—2 Present, perceptible to the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियक|ऐंद्रियक|ऐन्द्रियकं
ऐन्द्रिय, -यक <i>a.</i><BR> [इन्द्रिय-अण्, वुञ् वा]<BR>—1 Belonging to the senses, sensual. यथा मनोरथः स्वप्नः सर्वमैन्द्रियकं<BR> मृषा Bhāg. 7. 2. 48. मूढमैन्द्रियकं लुब्धमनार्यचरितं शठम् Mb. 12. 93. 16.<BR>—2 Present, perceptible to the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियम्
ऐन्द्रिय, -यक + .{@-यम्@} The world of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियेधी|ऐंद्रियेधी
ऐन्द्रियेधी <i>a.</i> Thinking only of sensual pleasures. मत्प्राप्तयेऽजेशसुरासुरादयस्तप्यन्त<BR> उग्रं तप ऐन्द्रियेधियः Bhāg. 5. 18. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्धन|ऐंधन|ऐन्धनः
ऐन्धन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) [इन्धन-अण्] Consisting of<BR> fuel. produced from fuel (fire); Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्धनः|ऐन्धन|ऐंधन
ऐन्धन + .{@-नः@} N. of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्य|ऐन्यः
ऐन्य <i>a.</i> [इन्य-ण्य] Belonging to a master or the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्यः|ऐन्य
ऐन्य + .{@-न्यः@} N. of a Sāman; Ārṣeya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्वकम्
ऐन्वकम् N. of a Sāman Ārṣeya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐभि
ऐभि <i>a.</i> (भी <i>f.</i>) [इभ-अण्] Belonging to an elephant;<BR> शीतांशोरंशुजालैर्जलधरमलिनां क्लिश्नती कृत्तिमैभीम् Mu. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐभी
ऐभि + .{@-भी@} A kind of pumpkin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐयत्यम्
ऐयत्यम् [इयत्-ष्यञ्] Quantity, number, value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरम्
ऐरम् A heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावणः|ऐरावण
ऐरावणः (see ऐरावत below); Indraʼs elephant (produced at the<BR> churning of the ocean), मागधोऽथ महापालो गजमैरावणोपमम् Mb. 6. 62. 46.<BR> See ऐरावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावतः|ऐरावत|ऐरावतं
ऐरावतः [इरा आपः तद्वान् इरावान् समुद्रः तस्मादुत्पन्नः अण्]<BR>—1 N. of the elephant of Indra. ऐरावतं गजेन्द्राणाम् Bg. 10. 27.<BR>—2 An excellent elephant; a species of elephant; ऐरावतानैन्द्रशिरान्नागान्वै<BR> प्रियदर्शनान् Rām. 2. 70. 23.<BR>—3 One of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent-race (inhabiting Pātāla);<BR> अहमैरावत ज्येष्ठभ्रातृभ्योऽकरवं नमः Mb. 1. 3. 139.<BR>—4 The elephant presiding over the east.<BR>—5 A kind of rainbow.<BR>—6 A kind of lightning; (said to be <i>n.</i> also in these two senses).<BR>—7 The orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावतम्
ऐरावतः + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A vast and waterless region.<BR>—2 (pl.) N. of a Varṣa.<BR>—3 N. of the northern path of the moon.<BR>—4 A kind of cloud; ‘मेघस्योपरि मेघो यः स ऐरावत उच्यते’ इति दक्षिणावर्तः<BR> (Commentator of मेघदूत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावती
ऐरावतः + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 The female of Indraʼs elephant.<BR>—2 Lightning.<BR>—3 N. of a plant (वटपत्री)<BR>—4 N. of river Rāvī in the Panjab (= इरावती).<BR>—5 N. of a particular portion of the moonʼs path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरिणम्
ऐरिणम् [इरिणे भवम् अण्]<BR>—1 Fossil or rock salt.<BR>—2 Saline earth (Mar. उखर); खातकण्टकपाषाणैर्दुष्पथं दुर्गमैरिणम्<BR> (Śukra. 4. 848).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरेयम्
ऐरेयम् [इरायाम् अन्ने भवं ढक्] Spirituous liquor (prepared from food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐर्म्यम्
ऐर्म्यम् [ईर्म-ष्यञ्] A plaster good for healing wounds; Suśr. 2. 86. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलः|ऐल
ऐलः [इलाया अपत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 N. of Purūravas (son of Ilā and Budha).<BR>—2 The planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलम्
ऐलः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Food, a quantity of food.<BR>—2 A particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविल|ऐलविलः
ऐलविल N. of Kubera अवलम्बितैलविलपाणिपल्लवः श्रयति स्म मेघमिव<BR> मेघवाहनः Śi. 13. 18. See एलविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवः
ऐलवः Ved. Noise, cry; तौविलिकेऽवेलयावायमैलव ऐलयीत् Av. 6. 16. 3.<BR> ˚कारः Rudraʼs dog; Av. 11. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवालुकः|ऐलवालुक
ऐलवालुकः N. of a perfume. see एलवालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलूषः|ऐलूष
ऐलूषः ‘Descendant of Ilūṣa’, N. of Kavaṣa (author of a Vedic hymn.<BR> Ait. Br. 2. 19. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलेयः|ऐलेय|ऐलेयं
ऐलेयः<BR>—1 A kind of perfume.<BR>—2 Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश
ऐश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>) [ईश-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to Śiva; सुरसरिदिव तेजो वह्निनिष्ठपूतमैशम् R. 2. 75.<BR> हास्यश्रीराजहंसा हरतु तनुरिव क्लेशमैशी शरद्वः Mu. 1.<BR>—2 Supreme, regal. (ऐशी) N. of the Nakṣatra रोहिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशान
ऐशान <i>a.</i> [ईशान-अण्] Belonging to Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशानी
ऐशान + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 The north-eastern direction.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्य
ऐश्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to ईश;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्यम्
ऐश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} Supremacy, power; महतीतरमायैश्यं निहन्त्यात्मनि युञ्जतः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 13. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर
ऐश्वर <i>a.</i> [ईश्वर-अण्] (री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to or produced by a lord or the Supreme Being, majestic.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">Page0505-1</a>]<BR> पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम् Bg. 9. 5, 11. 3, 9.<BR>—2 Powerful, mighty.<BR>—3 Belonging to Śiva; ऐश्वरं धनुरभाजि यत्त्वया R. 11. 76.<BR>—4 Supreme, royal.<BR>—5 Divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरम्
ऐश्वर + .{@-रम्@} Supremacy, power; एकान्तधाम यशसः श्रिय ऐश्वरस्य<BR> Bhāg. 10. 44. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरी
ऐश्वर + .{@-री@} N. of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐश्वरकारणिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरकारणिकः|ऐश्वरकारणिक
ऐश्वर + -कारणिकः A Naiyāyika; Hc. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरिकः|ऐश्वरिक
ऐश्वरिकः (With Buddhists) Atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर्यम्
ऐश्वर्यम् [ईश्वर-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Supremacy, sovereignty; एकैश्वर्यस्थितोऽपि M. 1. 1; निशाचर˚.<BR>—2 Might, power, sway.<BR>—3 Dominion.<BR>—4 Affluence, wealth, greatness; ˚मत्तेषु Ś. 5. 18.<BR>—5 Super-human power.<BR>—6 The divine faculties of omnipotence, omnipresence &c. cf. अणिमा लघिमा<BR> व्याप्तिः प्राकाम्यं महिमा तथा । ईशित्वं च वशित्वं च तथा कामावसायिता ॥<BR>—7 Pervasion, comprehensiveness; एष सप्तविधः प्रोक्तो गुण आकाशसम्भवः ।<BR> ऐश्वर्येण तु सर्वत्र स्थितोऽपि पटहादिषु Mb. 12. 184. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्
ऐषमस् [Vārt. on P. V. 3. 22.] <i>ind.</i> During this year, in the present year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्तन|ऐषमस्तनः
ऐषमस्तन, -मस्त्य <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to the present year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्त्य|ऐषमस्त्यः
ऐषमस्तन, -मस्त्य <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to the present year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषावीर
ऐषावीर <i>a.</i> Ved. Weak, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषीक
ऐषीक <i>a.</i> Consisting of stalks; made of reeds or canes; ऐषीकं<BR> पर्व a section of the सौप्तिक पर्व of Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टकम्
ऐष्टकम् Ved. Sacrificial bricks collectively. <i>a.</i> built of bricks; Kau. A. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिक
ऐष्टिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इष्टि-ठक्]<BR>—1 Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR>—2 Treating of इष्टि or sacrifice (as a work).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐष्टिकपूर्तिक, ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिकपूर्तिक
ऐष्टिक + -पूर्तिक, -पौर्तिक <i>a.</i> belonging to इष्टापूर्त (belonging<BR> to sacrifices or charitable works); दानधर्मं निषेवेत नित्यमैष्टिकपौर्तिकम् Ms. 4. 227.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक|ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक
ऐष्टिक + -पूर्तिक, -पौर्तिक <i>a.</i> belonging to इष्टापूर्त (belonging<BR> to sacrifices or charitable works); दानधर्मं निषेवेत नित्यमैष्टिकपौर्तिकम् Ms. 4. 227.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहलौकिक
ऐहलौकिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इहलोक-ठञ् P. IV. 3. 60. Vārt.] Happening in<BR> or belonging to this world, temporal, sublunary (opp. पारलौकिक);<BR> ऐहलौकिकपारक्यं कर्म पुम्भिर्निषेव्यते Rām. 6. 64. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिक|ऐहिकं
ऐहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [इह-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Of this world or place, temporal, secular, worldly.<BR>—2 Local, of this place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिकम्
ऐहिक + .{@-कम्@} Business (of this world).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ऐहिकदर्शिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिकदर्शिन्
ऐहिक + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> worldly-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ <i>m.</i> (औः) N. of Brahmā. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A Vocative particle (oh).<BR>—2 An interjection of (1) calling; (hallo, ho); (2) remembrance; (3) compassion (ah!).<BR>—3 The number महापद्म. cf. also ओर्वेधा ज्ञो ध्रुवोऽगस्त्यो गरुडोऽगोऽक्षयोऽसुरः ।<BR> आखुः काणोऽथ मार्जारः साधुः सङ्गः पराशरः ॥ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकः|ओक|ओकं
ओकः<BR>—1 A house.<BR>—2 A refuge, shelter.<BR>—3 A bird.<BR>—4 A Śūdra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओकज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकज
ओकः + -ज <i>a.</i> Born in the house; bred at home (as cows); Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकस्
ओकस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 A house, residence; as in दिवौकस् or स्वर्गौकस् a god.<BR>—2 An asylum, refuge.<BR>—3 A resting place.<BR>—4 Pleasure, gratification. [cf. Gr. <i>oikos</i>].<BR>—5 Beauty or form. ग्रन्थीन्हृदय्यान्विवृणु स्वमोकः Bhāg. 8. 24. 53.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओकोनिधनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकोनिधनम्
ओकस् + -निधनम् N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकिवस्
ओकिवस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Meeting together, united (समवेत).<BR>—2 Accustomed to; having a liking for; ओकिवांसा सुते सचाँ Rv. 6. 59. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्य
ओक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Favourable to the house; <i>i. e.</i> to its inmates.<BR>—2 Good for a house, kind to a household, belonging to a house; ज्योतीरथः<BR> पर्वते राय ओक्यः Rv. 9. 86. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्यम्
ओक्य + .{@-क्यम्@}<BR>—1 Gratification, pleasure.<BR>—2 A comfortable place.<BR>—3 A resting place, house (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकणः|ओकण
ओकणः(णिः) A bug; so ओकोदनी, ओक्कणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकणिः|ओकणि
ओकणः(णिः) A bug; so ओकोदनी, ओक्कणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकणी
ओकणी A boundary-forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुलः|ओकुल
ओकुलः A cake of flour; wheat slightly fried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुली
ओकुलः + .{@-ली@} An ear of wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख्
ओख् €1 P. (ओखति, ओखाञ्चकार, ओखितुम्, ओखित)<BR>—1 To be dry.<BR>—2 To be able; be sufficient.<BR>—3 To adorn or grace.<BR>—4 To refuse.<BR>—5 To ward off, prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओगण
ओगण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 United; महि व्राधन्त ओगणास इन्द्रः Rv. 10. 89. 15.<BR>—2 Solitary; despised, cast off by oneʼs friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओगीयस्
ओगीयस् <i>a.</i> Vigorous, powerful; बलं सत्यादोगीयः Bṛ. Up. 5. 14. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघः|ओघ
ओघः [उच्-घञ् पृषो˚ घ]<BR>—1 A flood, stream, current; नायं शक्यस्त्वया बद्धुं महानोघस्तपोधन<BR> Mb. 3. 135. 37; पुनरोघेन हि युज्यते नदी Ku. 4. 44; so रुधिर˚, बाष्प˚ &c.<BR>—2 An inundation.<BR>—3 A heap, quantity, mass, multitude; सन्ति चौघबलाः केचित् Rām. 5. 43. 23.<BR> दीपयन्नथ नभः किरणौघैः Ki. 9. 23. बाण˚, अघ˚, जन˚ &c.<BR>—4 The whole.<BR>—5 Continuity.<BR>—6 Quick time in music.<BR>—7 Tradition, traditional instruction.<BR>—8 A kind of dance.<BR>—9 One of the three वाद्यविधिs, the other two being तत्त्व and<BR> अनुगत (cf. तत्त्वं भवेदनुगतमोघश्चेति निरूपितम् । गीतानुगं<BR> त्रिप्रकारं वाद्यं तल्लक्ष्म कथ्यते ॥ त्रिविधं गीते कार्यं वादित्रं<BR> वैणमेव वाद्यजैः । तत्त्वं तथाप्यनुगतमोघो वा नैककरणं तु ॥) तत्त्वौघानुग्ताश्च<BR> वाद्यविधयः सम्यक् त्रयो दर्शिताः Nāg. 1. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओघनिर्युक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघनिर्युक्तिः|ओघनिर्युक्ति
ओघः + -निर्युक्तिः N. of some Buddhist and Jaina works<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0505-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओङ्कारः|ओङ्कार|ओंकार|ओंकारः
ओङ्कारः See under ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्
ओज् €1. €10 U. (ओजति, ओजयति, ओजयितुम्, ओजित)<BR>—1 To be strong or able.<BR>—2 To increase, grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज <i>a.</i> Odd, uneven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजम्
ओज + .{@-जम्@} = ओजस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Bodily strength, vigour; energy, ability.<BR>—2 Vitality; Ms. 1. 16.<BR>—3 Virility, the generative faculty. The writers on Āyurveda, however,<BR> distinguish^1 between ओजस् and शुक्रम्; cf. क्षीरस्थघृतमिव भिन्नमोजः<BR> शुक्रेण Ḍalhaṇa. रसादीनां शुक्रान्तानां धातूनां यत् परं तेजस्तत्<BR> खलु ओजः Sruśr. ओजोविवृद्धौ देहस्य तुष्टि-पुष्टिबलोदयाः Aṣṭāṅga.<BR>—4 Splendour, light; Bhāg. 7. 3. 23.<BR>—5 (In Rhet.) An elaborate form of style, abundance of compounds; (considered<BR> by Daṇḍin to be the ‘soul of prose’); ओजः समासभूयस्त्वमेतद्गद्यस्य<BR> जीवितम् Kāv. 1. 80; see K. P. 8 also; said to be of 5 kinds in R. G.<BR>—6 (In Astr.) Each alternate sign of the zodiac (as the first, third &c.).<BR>—7 Water.<BR>—8 Metallic lustre.<BR>—9 Manifestation, appearance.<BR>—10 Skill in the use of weapons.<BR>—11 Speed; एष ह्यतिबलः सैन्ये रथेन पवनौजसा Rām. 7. 29. 12.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजसीन
ओजसीन, ओजस्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्य
ओजसीन, ओजस्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्वत्|ओजस्वन्त्
ओजस्वत्, ओजस्विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, vigorous, energetic, powerful; रूपं तदोजस्वि तदेव वीर्यम्<BR> R. 5. 37; Śi. 12. 35.<BR>—2 Splendid, bright.<BR>—3 See ओजस् (5); प्रसादरम्यमोजस्वि Ki. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्विन्
ओजस्वत्, ओजस्विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, vigorous, energetic, powerful; रूपं तदोजस्वि तदेव वीर्यम्<BR> R. 5. 37; Śi. 12. 35.<BR>—2 Splendid, bright.<BR>—3 See ओजस् (5); प्रसादरम्यमोजस्वि Ki. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजायते
ओजायते €10 Den. Ā. [Vārt. on P. III. 1. 11.] To show strength<BR> or vigour, exhibit oneʼs heroism; ओजायमानं यो अहिं जघान Rv. 2. 12. 11,<BR> ओजायमाना तस्यार्ध्यं प्रणीय जनकात्मजा Bk. 5. 76; U. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजायितम्
ओजायितम् Stout-hearted, courageous behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजिष्ठ
ओजिष्ठ <i>a.</i> (Super. of उग्र also) Most strong, vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजीयस्
ओजीयस् <i>a.</i> More vehement, stronger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्मन्
ओज्मन् <i>a.</i> An instigator. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Speed; velocity; अपामोज्मानं परि गोभिरावृतम् Rv. 6. 47. 27.<BR>—2 Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडक
ओडक, -डवः<BR> A musical mode which omits two of the notes of the scale<BR> (रि and प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडवः|ओडव
ओडक, -डवः<BR> A musical mode which omits two of the notes of the scale<BR> (रि and प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडिका
ओडिका, -ओडी f.<BR> Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडी
ओडिका, -ओडी f.<BR> Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रः|ओड्र
ओड्रः, -ओण्ड्रः (<i>m.</i> pl.)<BR> N. of a people and their country (the modern<BR> Orissa); Ms. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्ड्रः|ओण्ड्र
ओड्रः, -ओण्ड्रः (<i>m.</i> pl.)<BR> N. of a people and their country (the modern<BR> Orissa); Ms. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रः|ओड्र
ओड्रः, -ओण्ड्रः + .{@-ड्रः@} The China-rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रम्
ओड्रः, -ओण्ड्रः + .{@-ड्रम्@} The <i>Javā</i>-flower,<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओड्राख्या, ओड्रपुष्पम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्राख्या
ओड्रः + -आख्या the China-rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रपुष्पम्
ओड्रः + -पुष्पम् the <i>Javā</i>-flower; Hibiscus Rosa Sinensis and its flowers<BR> (Mar. जास्वंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्
ओण् €1 P. (ओणति, ओणितुम्) To remove, take or drag along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओणि
ओणि <i>a.</i> Removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्णी
ओणि + .{@-णी@} (du.)<BR>—1 Heaven and earth. प्र ते सोतार ओण्यो रसं मदाय घृष्वये Rv. 9. 16. 1.<BR>—2 Vessel used in the preparation of Soma.<BR>—3 Preserving power, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओत
ओत <i>a.</i> [आ-वे-क्त] Woven, sewn with threads across.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओतप्रोत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतप्रोत
ओत + -प्रोत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 sewn cross-wise and lengthwise.<BR>—2 extending in all directions Mb. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतप्रोतम्
ओत + -प्रोत + ({@-तम्@}) <i>ind.</i> cross-wise<BR> and lengthwise, vertically and horizontally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतुः|ओतु
ओतुः<BR>—1 The woof or cross threads of a web; नाहं तन्तुं न वि जानाम्योतुम् Rv. 6. 9. 2.<BR>—2 A cat (<i>f.</i> also); as in स्थूलो(लौ)तुः. [Vārt. ओत्वोष्ठयोः<BR> समासे वा on P. VI. 1. 94], Śukra. 4. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदती
ओदती Issuing out, rising upwards; epithet of the Dawn; नदं व<BR> ओदतीनाम् Rv. 8. 69. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनः|ओदन|ओदनं
ओदनः, -नम्<BR> [उन्द्-युच् Uṇ. 2. 76]<BR>—1 Food, boiled rice; <i>e. g.</i> दध्योदनः, घृत˚, गुड˚, मांस˚ &c.<BR>—2 Grain mashed and cooked with milk.<BR>—3 A cloud. [Sometimes ओदन is prefixed to the names of pupils to<BR> denote that the pupilʼs object is more to be fed by his master than be<BR> taught; <i>e. g.</i> ओदनपाणिनीयाः P. VI. 2. 69. Sk.; Mbh. on P. I. 1. 73.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनम्
ओदनः, -नम्<BR> [उन्द्-युच् Uṇ. 2. 76]<BR>—1 Food, boiled rice; <i>e. g.</i> दध्योदनः, घृत˚, गुड˚, मांस˚ &c.<BR>—2 Grain mashed and cooked with milk.<BR>—3 A cloud. [Sometimes ओदन is prefixed to the names of pupils to<BR> denote that the pupilʼs object is more to be fed by his master than be<BR> taught; <i>e. g.</i> ओदनपाणिनीयाः P. VI. 2. 69. Sk.; Mbh. on P. I. 1. 73.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनी
ओदनः, -नम् + .{@-नी@} The plant (बला) Sida Cordifolia (Mar. चिकणा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओदनाह्वया, ओदनाह्वा, ओदनिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनाह्वया
ओदनः + -आह्वया, -आह्वा, ओदनिका N. of a medicinal plant (महासमंगां).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनाह्वा
ओदनः + -आह्वया, -आह्वा, ओदनिका N. of a medicinal plant (महासमंगां).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनिका
ओदनः + -आह्वया, -आह्वा, ओदनिका N. of a medicinal plant (महासमंगां).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनीयति
ओदनीयति Den. P. To wish to make mashed food of anything; पुरोडाशं<BR> यद्योदनीयन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्मः|ओद्म
ओद्मः, -ओद्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Flowing; flooding; Vāj. 13. 53.<BR>—2 Wetting; P. VI. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्मन्
ओद्मः, -ओद्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Flowing; flooding; Vāj. 13. 53.<BR>—2 Wetting; P. VI. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओधस्
ओधस् <i>n.</i> An udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओपशः|ओपश
ओपशः Ved.<BR>—1 Pillow, cushion; हरिरोपशं कृणुते नभस्पयः Rv. 9. 71. 1.<BR>—2 Support, stay, pillar; चकाण ओपशं दिवि Rv. 8. 14. 5.<BR>—3 An ornament of the head; curl; a horn (Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओपशिन्
ओपशिन् <i>a.</i> Lying upon cushions; effeminate; इमं मे अद्य पूरुषं<BR> क्लीबमोपशिनं कृधि Av. 6. 138. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 The sacred syllable <i>om</i>, uttered as a holy exclamation at the<BR> beginning and end of a reading of the Vedas, or previous to the commencement<BR> of a prayer or sacred work.<BR>—2 As a particle it implies<BR>——(<i>a</i>) solemn affirmation and respectful assent (so be it, amen!);<BR>——(<i>b</i>) assent or acceptance (yes, all right); ओमित्युच्यताममात्यः<BR> Māl. 6; ओमित्युक्तवतोऽथ शार्ङ्गिण इति Śi. 1. 75; द्वितीयश्चेदोमिति<BR> ब्रूमः S. D. 1;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) command;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) auspiciousness;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) removal or warding off.<BR>—3 Brahman. [This word first appears in the Upaniṣads as a mystic monosyllable,<BR> and is regarded as the object of the most profound religious meditation.<BR> In the Maṇḍūkya Upaniṣad it is said that this syllable is all what<BR> has been, that which is and is to be; that all is <i>om</i>, only <i>om</i>.<BR> Literally analysed, <i>om</i> is taken to be made up of three letters or<BR> quarters; the letter <i>a</i> is Vaiśvānara, the spirit of waking souls<BR> in the waking world; <i>u</i> is Taijasa, the spirit of dreaming souls in<BR> the world of dreams; and <i>m.</i> is Prajñā, the spirit of sleeping and<BR> undreaming souls; and the whole <i>om</i> is said<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">Page0507-1</a>]<BR> to be unknowable, unspeakable, into which the whole world passes away,<BR> blessed above duality; (for further account see <i>Goughʼs Upaniṣads</i> pp. 69-73).<BR> In later times <i>om</i> came to be used as a mystic name for<BR> the Hindu triad, representing the union of the three gods <i>a</i> (Viṣṇu),<BR> <i>u</i> (Śiva), and <i>m</i> (Brahmā). It is usually called Praṇava or Ekakṣaram;<BR> cf. अकारो विष्णुरुद्दिष्ट उकारस्तु महेश्वरः । मकारेणोच्यते ब्रह्मा प्रणवेन<BR> त्रयो मताः ॥]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओकारः, ओरा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0506-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकारः|ओकार
ओम् + -कारः<BR>—1 the sacred syllable ओम्; त्रिमात्रमोकारं त्रिमात्रमोंकारं वा विदधति<BR> Mbh. on VIII. 2. 89.<BR>—2 the exclamation ओम्, or pronunciation of the same; प्राणायामैस्त्रिभिः<BR> पूतस्तत ओंकारमर्हति Ms. 2. 75.<BR>—3 (fig.) commencement; एष तावदोंकारः Mv. 1; B. R. 3. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओरा
ओम् + -रा N. of a Buddhist śakti (personification of divine energy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमः|ओम
ओमः Ved.<BR>—1 A protector; ओमासश्चर्षणीधृतो Rv. 1. 3. 7.<BR>—2 One who is favourably disposed (towards another)<BR>—3 Any one fit to be protected or favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमन्
ओमन्^1 <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Protection.<BR>—2 Favour, kindness.<BR>—3 A kind person.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमना
ओमन् + .{@-ना@} A friend, helper, protector; परि घ्रंसमोमना वां वयो<BR> गात् Rv. 7. 69. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमन्वत्|ओमन्वन्त्
ओमन्वत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Friendly; helping, useful; ओमन्वन्तं चकथुः सप्तवध्रये Rv. 10. 39. 9.<BR>—2 Favourable, kind.<BR>—3 Satiating, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमात्रा
ओमात्रा Protection, kindness, assistance; महीं त ओमात्रां कृष्टयो<BR> विदुः Rv. 10. 50. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्या
ओम्या Ved. Favour, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओरम्फः|ओरम्फ
ओरम्फः A hard scratch; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओरिमिका
ओरिमिका <i>f.</i> N. of a section of the Kāṭhaka recension of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल|ओलं|ओलः
ओल <i>a.</i> Wet, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलः|ओल|ओलं
ओल + .{@-लः@} An esculent root (शूरण; Mar. सुरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलज्
ओलज् €1 P. (ओलञ्जति) To cast or throw up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलण्ड्|ओलंड्
ओलण्ड् €1 P., €10 U. (ओलण्डति, ओलण्डयति, ओलण्डित) To cast or<BR> throw upwards, throw up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल्ल|ओल्लः
ओल्ल <i>a.</i> Wet, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल्लः|ओल्ल
ओल्ल + .{@-ल्लः@}<BR>—1 hostage.<BR>—2 The esculent root (Mar. सुरण). ˚आगतः come or received as<BR> a hostage (this word occurs once or twice in Viddhaśālabhañjikā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषः|ओष|ओषं
ओषः<BR>—1 Burning, combustion; ओषमित् पृथिवीमहम् Rv. 10. 119. 10.<BR>—2 Cooking, baking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषणः|ओषण
ओषणः Pungency, sharp flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषणी
ओषणः + .{@-णी@} A pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधिः|ओषधि
ओषधिः, -धी <i>f.</i><BR> [ओषः पाको धीयते अत्र-धा-कि Tv.]<BR>—1 A herb, plant (in general); ओषध्यः फलपाकान्ताः Ms. 1. 46; cf.<BR> संजीवन˚.<BR>—2 A medicinal plant or drug.<BR>—3 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">Page0507-2</a>]<BR> annual plant or herb which dies after becoming ripe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओषधीशः, ओषधिगर्भः, ओषधिनाथः, ओषधिज, ओषधिधरः, ओषधिपतिः, ओषधिप्रस्थः, ओषधिवनस्पतिम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधी
ओषधिः, -धी <i>f.</i><BR> [ओषः पाको धीयते अत्र-धा-कि Tv.]<BR>—1 A herb, plant (in general); ओषध्यः फलपाकान्ताः Ms. 1. 46; cf.<BR> संजीवन˚.<BR>—2 A medicinal plant or drug.<BR>—3 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">Page0507-2</a>]<BR> annual plant or herb which dies after becoming ripe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओषधीशः, ओषधिगर्भः, ओषधिनाथः, ओषधिज, ओषधिधरः, ओषधिपतिः, ओषधिप्रस्थः, ओषधिवनस्पतिम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधीशः|ओषधीश
ओषधिः + -ईशः, -गर्भः, -नाथः the moon (as presiding over and feeding<BR> plants); cf. पुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः Bg. 15. 13;<BR> R. 2. 73; Ku. 7. 1; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधिगर्भः|ओषधिगर्भ
ओषधिः + -ईशः, -गर्भः, -नाथः the moon (as presiding over and feeding<BR> plants); cf. पुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः Bg. 15. 13;<BR> R. 2. 73; Ku. 7. 1; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधिनाथः
ओषधिः + -ईशः, -गर्भः, -नाथः the moon (as presiding over and feeding<BR> plants); cf. पुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः Bg. 15. 13;<BR> R. 2. 73; Ku. 7. 1; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

