ओष्ठः|ओष्ठ
ओष्ठः [उष्यते उष्णाहारेण, उष्-कर्मणि थन् Uṇ. 2. 4.] A lip (lower<BR> or upper); द्वावोष्ठौ छेदयेन्नृपः Ms. 8. 282; अधर˚, बिम्ब˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठी
ओष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठी@} A creeper bearing a red fruit to which the lip is commonly<BR> compared (बिम्बफल; Mar. तोण्डली). [In comp. the अ or आ<BR> of words before ओष्ठ may be optionally dropped, and the fem. may end<BR> in आ or ई as बिम्बो(म्बौ)ष्ठा -ष्ठी. (Vārt. ओत्वोष्ठयोः<BR> समासे वा Sk. on P. VI. 1. 94.)] [cf. L. <i>ostium</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ओष्ठाधरौ, ओष्ठाधरम्, ओष्ठावलोप्य, ओष्ठकोपः, ओष्ठप्रकोपः, ओष्ठज, ओष्ठजाहम्, ओष्ठपल्लवः, ओष्ठपल्लवम्, ओष्ठपाकः, ओष्ठपुटम्, ओष्ठपुष्पः, ओष्ठपुष्पम्, ओष्ठरोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठाधरौ
ओष्ठः + -अधरौ, -अधरम् the upper and lower lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठाधरम्
ओष्ठः + -अधरौ, -अधरम् the upper and lower lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठावलोप्य
ओष्ठः + -अवलोप्य <i>a.</i> Which could be eaten with lips; मांसान्योष्ठावलोप्यानि<BR> साधनीयानि, देवताः । अश्नन्ति … ॥ Bk. 5. 14. {@उपमफला, -भा, -फला@}<BR> the creeper Bryonia Grandis (whose fruit resembles a lip. Mar. तोंडली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

