ओहस्
ओहस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Praise; idea, true notion (?).<BR>—2 A vehicle, means; न ये देवास ओहसा न मर्ताः Rv. 6. 67. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0507-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A sound.<BR>—2 N. of Śeṣa or Ananta.<BR>—3 The number जलधि; cf. also औः श्वा युवा नरो नारी भावः सूक्ष्मः<BR> प्रजापतिः । स्थूलो जारः कलावांश्च सुखी दुर्गा रतिः कविः ॥ Enm.<BR>—4 The sacred syllable of the Śūdras; Kālikā P. ━<i>f.</i> The earth.<BR>━<i>ind.</i> An interjection of (1) calling (ho, hallo); (2) addressing (oh!);<BR> (3) opposition; (4) asseveration or determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0508-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिकः|औक्थिक
औक्थिकः [उक्थ-ठक्] P. IV. 2. 60. A Brāhmaṇa who knows or studies<BR> or recites the <i>ukthas</i>. औक्थिक्यमधीते उक्थान्यधीते औक्थिकः Mbh. 4. 2. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0508-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

