और्वशेयः [उर्वश्याः अपत्यं ठक्] N. of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूकम्
औलूकम् [उलूकानां समूहः अञ्] A collection of owls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक्यः|औलूक्य
औलूक्यः [उलूकस्यापत्यं, यञ्] N. of Kaṇāda, the propounder<BR> of the Vaiśeṣika philosophy; (see औलूक्यदर्शन in Sarva. S.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूखल
औलूखल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>) [उलूखले क्षुण्णम् अण्] Coming<BR> from, pounded or ground in, a mortar; औलूखलो यावकः Mbh. on IV. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औल्बण्यम्
औल्बण्यम् [उल्बण-ष्यञ्] Excess, superabundance, virulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औवेणकम्
औवेणकम् A kind of song; Y. 3. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0512-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशन
औशन, औशनस <i>a.</i> (-नी, -सी <i>f.</i>) [उशनस्-अण्]<BR> Belonging or peculiar to Uśanas; originating from Uśanas, or taught<BR> by him; पितामहाद्वरं लेभे सर्वमौशनसं धनम् Rām. 4. 51. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनस
औशन, औशनस <i>a.</i> (-नी, -सी <i>f.</i>) [उशनस्-अण्]<BR> Belonging or peculiar to Uśanas; originating from Uśanas, or taught<BR> by him; पितामहाद्वरं लेभे सर्वमौशनसं धनम् Rām. 4. 51. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनसम्
औशन, औशनस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 The law-book of उशनस् (a treatise on civil polity).<BR>—2 N. of an Upapurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनसाः
औशन, औशनस + .{@-साः@} N. of a school of writers on the science of government mentioned<BR> by Kauṭilya; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनसी
औशन, औशनस + .{@-सी@} N. of Devayanī; तं वीरमाहौशनसी प्रेमनिर्भरया गिरा<BR> Bhāg. 9. 18. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशिज
औशिज <i>a.</i> (-जी <i>f.</i>) [उशिज्-अण्] Desirous, zealous,<BR> wishing; कक्षीवन्तं य औशिजः Mbh. on VI. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीनरः|औशीनर
औशीनरः [उशीनरस्यापत्यम् अङ्] The son of Uśīnara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीनरी
औशीनरः + .{@-री@} N. of the wife of king Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीरम्
औशीरम् [उशीरं-अण्]<BR>—1 The handle of a fan or Chowri.<BR>—2 A bed; औशीरे कामचारः कृतोऽभूत् Dk. 72 at liberty to sleep or sit.<BR>—3 A seat (chair, stool &c.).<BR>—4 An unguent made of Uśīra; अचन्दनमनौशीरं हृदयस्यानुलेपनम् Mk. 10. 23.<BR>—5 The root of the fragrant grass उशीर q. v.<BR>—6 A fan. ━<i>a.</i> made from उशीर; छत्रं वेष्टनमौशीरम् Mb. 12. 60. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीरिका
औशीरिका<BR>—1 The shoot (of a plant).<BR>—2 A basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषणम्
औषणम् [उषण्-अण्]<BR>—1 Pungency.<BR>—2 Black pepper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: औषणशौण्डी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषणशौण्डी
औषणम् + -शौण्डी dried ginger; black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषध|औषधं
औषध <i>a.</i> (-धी <i>f.</i>) [औषधि-अण्] Consisting of herbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधम्
औषध + .{@-धम्@}<BR>—1 A herb; herbs taken collectively.<BR>—2 A medicament, medicinal drug, medicine in general.<BR>—3 A vessel for herbs.<BR>—4 A mineral.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 Counter-action, prevention; अतिकुधं निषधमनौषधं जनः Śi. 17. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: औषधपेषकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधपेषकः|औषधपेषक
औषध + -पेषकः One who grinds or pounds medicaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधिः|औषधि
औषधिः, -धी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A herb, plant (in general); Y. 3. 276 v. l.; see ओषधि.<BR>—2 A medicinal herb; अचिन्त्यो हि मणिमन्त्रौषधीनां प्रभावः Ratn. 2.<BR>—3 An herb which emits fire; विरमन्ति न ज्वलितुमौषधयः Ki. 5. 24<BR> (तृणज्योतींषि Malli.); cf. Ku. 1. 10.<BR>—4 An annual or deciduous plant; ˚धीपतिः N. of Soma, the lord of plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधी
औषधिः, -धी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A herb, plant (in general); Y. 3. 276 v. l.; see ओषधि.<BR>—2 A medicinal herb; अचिन्त्यो हि मणिमन्त्रौषधीनां प्रभावः Ratn. 2.<BR>—3 An herb which emits fire; विरमन्ति न ज्वलितुमौषधयः Ki. 5. 24<BR> (तृणज्योतींषि Malli.); cf. Ku. 1. 10.<BR>—4 An annual or deciduous plant; ˚धीपतिः N. of Soma, the lord of plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधिपञ्चप्रकाराः
औषधिः, -धी + .{@-पञ्चप्रकाराः@} (1) Juice of a green herb (रस). (2) Powder<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">Page0513-2</a>]<BR> of dry medicinal billets चूर्ण. (3) Decoction of medicinal herbs (कषाय).<BR> (4) Decoction mixed with medicinal powder (अवलेह). (5) A medicine<BR> to be pounded like condiment (कल्क). पञ्चामृतं गुडूची, गोक्षुर,<BR> मुसली, मुण्डी, शतावरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधिप्रतिनिधिः
औषधिः, -धी + .{@-प्रतिनिधिः@} A substitute for a herb which cannot be secured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीकृ
औषधीकृ €8 U. To reduce to a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीय
औषधीय <i>a.</i> Medicinal, consisting of herbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषरम्
औषरम्, -रकम्<BR> [उषरे भवम् अण्, ततः कन्]<BR>—1 Rock-salt.<BR>—2 Iron stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषरकम्
औषरम्, -रकम्<BR> [उषरे भवम् अण्, ततः कन्]<BR>—1 Rock-salt.<BR>—2 Iron stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस
औषस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [उषस्-अण्] Relating to dawn, early; ˚आतप Ki. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषसी
औषस + .{@-सी@} Day-break, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस्य
औषस्य <i>a.</i> Sacred to Uṣas or the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषसिक
औषसिक, औषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Walking out at day-break.<BR>—2 Early born or produced at dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिक
औषसिक, औषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Walking out at day-break.<BR>—2 Early born or produced at dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्र
औष्ट्र <i>a.</i> (-ष्ट्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [उष्ट्र-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to, or produced from, a camel; Ms. 5. 8.<BR>—2 Abounding in camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रम्
औष्ट्र + .{@-ष्ट्रम्@}<BR>—1 The milk of a camel.<BR>—2 Camel-nature.<BR>—3 The skin of a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [उष्ट्र-वुञ्] Relating to a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रकम्
औष्ट्रक + .{@-कम्@} A multitude of camels; लोलोष्ठमौष्ट्रकमुदग्रमुखं तरूणाम् Śi. 5. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्ररथ
औष्ट्ररथ <i>a.</i> (-थी <i>f.</i>) Belonging to a carriage drawn by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रिक|औष्ट्रिकः
औष्ट्रिक <i>a.</i> Coming from a camel (as milk); Mb. 8. 44. 28;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रिकः|औष्ट्रिक
औष्ट्रिक + .{@-कः@} An oil-miller; मानुषाणां मलं म्लेच्छा म्लेच्छानामौष्ट्रिका<BR> मलम् । औष्ट्रिकाणां मलं षण्ढाः षण्ढानां राजयाजकाः ॥ Mb. 8. 45. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्य
औष्ठ्य <i>a.</i> [ओष्ठ-यत्] Relating to the lip, labial.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: औष्ठ्यवर्णः, औष्ठ्यस्थान, औष्ठ्यस्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यवर्णः|औष्ठ्यवर्ण
औष्ठ्य + -वर्णः a labial letter; <i>i. e.</i> उ, ऊ, प्, फ्, ब्, भ्, म् and व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यस्थान
औष्ठ्य + -स्थान <i>a.</i> pronounced with the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यस्वरः|औष्ठ्यस्वर
औष्ठ्य + -स्वरः a labial vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्णम्
औष्णम् [उष्ण-अण्] Heat, warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ण्यम्
औष्ण्यम्, औष्म्यम् [उष्ण-उष्म-ष्यञ्] Heat; पूर्वराजवियोगौष्म्यं<BR> कृत्स्नस्य जगतो हतम् R. 17. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्यम्
औष्ण्यम्, औष्म्यम् [उष्ण-उष्म-ष्यञ्] Heat; पूर्वराजवियोगौष्म्यं<BR> कृत्स्नस्य जगतो हतम् R. 17. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क The first consonant of the alphabet, and first letter of the guttural<BR> class (क वर्ग).<BR> Zक् Jivhāmūlīya letter occurring before the guttural क् or ख्<BR> and written as Z (Zक्, Zख्).<BR> Vप् Upadhmānīya letter occurring before the labial प् or फ्<BR> and written also V (Vप्, Vफ्); These are called अर्धविसर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कः|क|कं
कः<BR>—1 Brahman. प्रजाः सिसृक्षुः क इवादिकाले Bu. C. 2. 51. यावद्गमं<BR> रुद्रभयाद्यथा कः Bhāg. 1. 7. 18.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Kāmadeva.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR>—5 Wind or air.<BR>—6 Yama.<BR>—7 The sun.<BR>—8 The soul.<BR>—9 A king or prince.<BR>—10 Knot or joint.<BR>—11 A peacock.<BR>—12 The king of birds.<BR>—13 A bird.<BR>—14 The mind.<BR>—15 Body.<BR>—16 Time.<BR>—17 A cloud.<BR>—18 A word, sound.<BR>—19 Hair.<BR>—20 Light,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">Page0514-1</a>]<BR> splendour.<BR>—21 Wealth, property.<BR>—22 Dakṣa Prajāpati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Happiness, joy, pleasure (as in नाक which is explained thus; न<BR> कं = अकं न अकं दुःखं यत्र) नुतपदकमला कमला<BR> करधृतकमला करोतु मे कमलम् (कम् + अलम्) Subhāṣ.; Ch. Up. 4. 10. 5.<BR>—2 Water; सत्येन माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कम् Y. 2. 108; के<BR> शवं पतितं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवा हर्षनिर्भराः Subhāṣ. (where a pun is<BR> intended on केशव, the apparent meaning being Keśava.)<BR>—3 The head; as in -कन्धरा<BR> (= कं शिरो धारयतीति). वलीपलित एजत्क इत्यहं<BR> प्रत्युदाहृतः Bhāg. 9. 6. 41.<BR>—4 Hair.<BR>—5 An act of a woman.<BR>—6 Flock of hair.<BR>—7 A collection of womanʼs acts (कं केशे कं च नारीणां करणे च तयोर्गणे).<BR>—8 milk.<BR>—9 Misery.<BR>—10 Poison.<BR>—11 Fear; cf. कं शिरः कं सुखं तोयं पयो दुःखं विषं भयम् Enm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कज, कजम्, कदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0513-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कः + -ज <i>a.</i> watery, aquatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कजम्
कः + -जम् A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदः|कद
कः + -दः a cloud (giving water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क A Taddhita affix added to nouns and adjectives, mostly to the<BR> former, in the sense of diminution, deterioration, similarity, endearment,<BR> or sometimes to express the original meaning of the word itself; <i>e. g.</i><BR> वृक्षकः small tree; बालकः a chap; पुत्रकः dear boy;<BR> अश्वकः a bad horse, or like a horse, or a horse itself (स्वार्थे कन्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंयु
कंयु <i>a.</i> Happy, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बूलम्
कम्बूलम् N. of the eighth Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंशः|कंश
कंशः A drinking vessel. (कं जलं शेते अत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस्
कंस् €2 Ā. (कंस्ते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To command. —3 To destroy; see कस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसः|कंस|कंसं
कंसः, -सम्<BR>—1 A drinking vessel, cup, can, goblet; उदुम्बरे कंसे चमसे वा सर्वौषधं<BR> फलानीति संभृत्य Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 1.<BR>—2 Bell metal^1, white copper. किं यत्तद्देवदत्तः कंसपात्र्यां पाणिनौदनं<BR> भुङ्क्ते Mbh. on P. I. 3. 1.<BR>—3 A particular measure known as आढक, q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260405. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/125#issuecomment-4183819710.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसम्
कंसः, -सम्<BR>—1 A drinking vessel, cup, can, goblet; उदुम्बरे कंसे चमसे वा सर्वौषधं<BR> फलानीति संभृत्य Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 1.<BR>—2 Bell metal^1, white copper. किं यत्तद्देवदत्तः कंसपात्र्यां पाणिनौदनं<BR> भुङ्क्ते Mbh. on P. I. 3. 1.<BR>—3 A particular measure known as आढक, q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260405. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/125#issuecomment-4183819710.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसः|कंस|कंसं
कंसः, -सम् + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 N. of a king of Mathurā, son of Ugrasena and enemy of Kṛṣṇa. [He<BR> is identified with the Asura Kālanemi, and acted inimically towards Kṛṣṇa<BR> and became his implacable foe. The circumstance which made him so was<BR> the following. While, after the marriage of Devakī with Vasudeva, he was<BR> driving the happy pair home, a heavenly voice warned Kaṃsa that the eighth<BR> child of Devakī would kill him. Thereupon he threw both of them into<BR> prison, loaded them with strong fetters, and kept the strictest watch over<BR> them. He took from Devakī every child as soon as it was born and slew<BR> it, and in this way he disposed of her first six children. But the 7th<BR> and 8th, Balarāma and Kṛṣṇa, were safely conveyed to Nandaʼs house<BR> in spite of his vigilance, and Kṛṣṇa grew up to be his slayer according<BR> to the prophecy. When Kaṃsa heard this, he was very much enraged and<BR> sent several demons to kill Kṛṣṇa, who killed them all with ease. At<BR> last he sent Akrūra to bring the boys to Mathurā. A severe<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">Page0514-2</a>]<BR> duel was fought between Kaṃsa and Kṛṣṇa, in which the former was<BR> slain by the latter.] cf. कंसं जघान कृष्णः which is an answer to<BR> the query कं संजघान कृष्णः ।<BR>—2 Anything metallic.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसा
कंसः, -सम् + .{@-सा@} N. of a daughter of Ugrasena and sister of Kaṃsa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कंसारिः, कंसारातिः, कंसजित्, कंसकृष्, कंसद्विष्, कंसहन्, कंसास्थि, कंसोद्भवा, कंसकारः, कंसकृषः, कंसमाक्षिकम्, कंसवणिक्, कंसवधः, कंसहननम्, कंसवधम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारिः|कंसारि
कंसः + -अरिः, -अरातिः, -जित्, -कृष्, -द्विष्, -हन् <i>m.</i> ‘slayer of Kaṃsa’, <i>i. e.</i><BR> Kṛṣṇa; स्वयं सन्धिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve. 1;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारातिः|कंसाराति
