कंसकारः|कंसकार
कंसः + -कारः<BR> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a mixed tribe; कंसकारशङ्खकारौ ब्राह्मणात्संबभूवतुः Śabdak.<BR>—2 a worker in pewter or white-brass, a bell-founder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकृषः
कंसः + -कृषः Vāsudeva Śrīkṛṣṇa; निषेदिवान् कंसकृषः स विष्टरे Śi. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसमाक्षिकम्
कंसः + -माक्षिकम् a metallic substance in large grains; a sort of pyrites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसवणिक्
