कंसवधः|कंसवध
कंसः + -वधः, -हननम् the slaying of Kaṃsa. कंसवधमाचष्टे कंसं<BR> घातयति Mbh. on P. III. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसहननम्
कंसः + -वधः, -हननम् the slaying of Kaṃsa. कंसवधमाचष्टे कंसं<BR> घातयति Mbh. on P. III. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसवधम्
कंसः + -वधम् N. of a drama by Śeṣakriṣṇa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकम्
कंसकम्<BR>—1 Bell-metal.<BR>—2 Green sulphate of iron (an eye-cure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसवती
कंसवती N. of a daughter of उग्रसेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Made of bell-metal &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय <i>a.</i> Fit for, or relating to, a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीयम्
कंसीय + .{@-यम्@} Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारम्
कंसारम् Ved.<BR>—1 A bone.<BR>—2 Rice, the grain of which becomes hard in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्
कक् €1 Ā. (ककते, ककित)<BR>—1 To wish.<BR>—2 To be proud.<BR>—3 To be unsteady; see कङ्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककजाकृत
ककजाकृत <i>a.</i> Ved. Mutilated; विविद्धा ककजाकृता Av. 11. 10. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककन्दः|ककन्द|ककंदः
ककन्दः Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककरः|ककर
ककरः A kind of bird (Ved.); Vāj. 24. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककर्दुः|ककर्दु|ककर्द्दु
ककर्दुः Destruction of happiness or of enemies; ककर्दवे वृषभो<BR> युक्त आसीत् Rv. 10. 102. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

