ककुञ्जलः|ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुंजलः
ककुञ्जलः The Chātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A summit, peak.<BR>—2 Chief, head; see ककुद below; अग्निर्मूर्धा दिवः ककुत् Rv. 8. 44. 16.<BR>—3 The hump on the shoulders of the Indian bull; ककुद्दोषणी याचते<BR> महादेवः Mbh. on VI. 1. 63. ककुदे वृषस्य कृतबाहुम् Ki. 12. 20; R. 4. 22.<BR>—4 A horn.<BR>—5 An ensign or symbol of royalty (as the छत्र, चामर &c.); ‘ककुद्वत्ककुदं श्रेष्ठे वृषाङ्के राजलक्ष्मणि’ इति विश्वः;<BR> नृपतिककुदं दत्त्वा यूने सितातपवारणम् R. 3. 70.<BR>—6 Any projecting corner; Bhāg. 5. 25. 7.<BR>—7 N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma. According to Pāṇini V. 4. 146-147<BR> ककुद् is the form to be substituted for ककुद in<BR> adj. or Bah. comps.; <i>e. g.</i> त्रिककुद्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ककुत्स्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्स्थः|ककुत्स्थ
ककुद् + -स्थः [ककुदि तिष्ठतीति] an epithet of Purañjaya, son of Śaśāda,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">Page0515-1</a>]<BR> a king of the solar race, and a descendant of Ikṣvāku; इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः<BR> ककुदं नृपाणां ककुत्स्थ इत्याहितलक्षणोऽभूत्^1 R. 6. 71. [Mythology relates<BR> that, when in their war with the demons, the gods were often worsted,<BR> they, headed by Indra, went to the powerful king Purañjaya, and requested<BR> him to be their friend in battle. The latter consented to do so, provided<BR> Indra carried him on his shoulders. Indra accordingly assumed the form<BR> of a bull, and Purañjaya, seated on its hump, completely vanquished the<BR> demons. Purañjaya is, therefore, called <i>Kakutstha</i> ‘standing on a hump’].<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260112. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/1812.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0514-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुदः|ककुद|ककुदं
ककुदः, -दम्<BR>—1 The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>—2 A hump (on the shoulders of an Indian bull). किं यत्तत्सास्नालाङ्गूलककुदखुरविषाण्यर्थरूपं<BR> स शब्दः Mbh. on I. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Chief, foremost, pre-eminent; ककुदं वेदविदां तपोधनश्च Mk. 1. 5;<BR> इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः ककुदं नृपाणाम् R. 6. 71.<BR>—4 A sign or symbol of royalty; नृपतिककुदम् R. 3. 70, 17, 27.<BR>—5 A species of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुदम्
ककुदः, -दम्<BR>—1 The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>—2 A hump (on the shoulders of an Indian bull). किं यत्तत्सास्नालाङ्गूलककुदखुरविषाण्यर्थरूपं<BR> स शब्दः Mbh. on I. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Chief, foremost, pre-eminent; ककुदं वेदविदां तपोधनश्च Mk. 1. 5;<BR> इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः ककुदं नृपाणाम् R. 6. 71.<BR>—4 A sign or symbol of royalty; नृपतिककुदम् R. 3. 70, 17, 27.<BR>—5 A species of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुदिन्
ककुदिन् <i>a.</i> Chief, superior; आस्यं विवृत्य ककुदी पाणिना प्राक्षिपच्छनैः<BR> Mb. 12. 289. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्मत् <i>a.</i> [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्]<BR>—1 Furnished with a hump; अरंहत पद्याभिः ककुद्मान् Rv. 10. 102. 7; Pt. 1.<BR>—2 Running high (as a wave). ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A mountain (having peaks).<BR>—2 A buffalo; मदोदग्राः ककुद्मन्तः R. 4. 22; a humped bull; 13. 47;<BR> तुषारसंघातशिलाः खुराग्रैः समुल्लिखन् दर्पकलः ककुद्मान् Ku. 1. 56.<BR>—3 N. of a medicinal plant (ऋषभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मती
ककुद्मत् + .{@-ती@} The hip and the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्वत्|ककुद्वन्त्
ककुद्वत् <i>m.</i> A buffalo with a hump on his shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Peaked; furnished with a hump &c. ━<i>m.</i> —1 A bull with a hump on his<BR> shoulders; एवं ककुद्मिनं हत्वा Bhāg. 10. 36. 15.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu; and of king रैवतक. ˚कन्या, -सुता N. of Revatī<BR> and wife of Balarāma; ककुद्मिकन्यावक्त्रान्तर्वासलब्धाधिवासया Śi. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुन्दरम्
ककुन्दरम् The cavities of the loins; Y. 3. 36 (जघनकूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A direction, quarter of the compass; वियुक्ताः कान्तेन स्त्रिय इव<BR> न राजन्ति ककुभः Mk. 5. 26; Śi. 9. 25, 3. 33.<BR>—2 Splendour, beauty.<BR>—3 A wreath of Champaka flowers.<BR>—4 A sacred treatise or Śāstra.<BR>—5 A peak, summit.<BR>—6 A Rāgiṇī or personified mode of music.<BR>—7 The personified quarter of the sky.<BR>—8 Breath, animation.<BR>—9 Unornamented hair; or hair hanging down as a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ <i>a.</i> Ved. Distinguished, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभः|ककुभ
ककुभ + .{@-भः@}<BR>—1 A crooked piece of wood at the end of the lute.<BR>—2 The tree Arjuna; ककुभसुरभिः शैलः U. 1. 33.<BR>—3 A kind of goblin or evil spirit.<BR>—4 One of the Rāgas or personified musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभा
ककुभ + .{@-भा@}<BR>—1 Space; quarter.<BR>—2 One of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">Page0515-2</a>]<BR> Rāgiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभम्
ककुभ + .{@-भम्@} A flower of the Kuṭaja tree; कालक्षेपं ककुभसुरभौ पर्वते<BR> पर्वते ते (उत्पश्यामि)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ककुभादनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभादनी
ककुभ + -अदनी ‘food of the sky, a kind of fragrance or perfume’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुह|ककुहः
ककुह <i>a.</i> Ved. Eminent; excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुहः|ककुह
ककुह + .{@-हः@} A part of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुकः|ककेरुक
ककेरुकः A worm in the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क्
कक्क् €1 P. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कटः|कक्कट
कक्कटः A kind of animal; Vāj. 24. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कुलः|कक्कुल
कक्कुलः The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोलः|कक्कोल
कक्कोलः^1, -ली<BR> N. of a plant bearing a berry; कक्कोलीफलजग्धि Māl. 6. 19, v. l.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: bad printing. follows after kakkulaḥ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोली
कक्कोलः^1, -ली<BR> N. of a plant bearing a berry; कक्कोलीफलजग्धि Māl. 6. 19, v. l.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: bad printing. follows after kakkulaḥ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोलम्
कक्कोलः, -ली + .{@-लम्, -लकम्@}<BR>—1 A berry of this plant.<BR>—2 A perfume prepared from its berries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोलकम्
कक्कोलः, -ली + .{@-लम्, -लकम्@}<BR>—1 A berry of this plant.<BR>—2 A perfume prepared from its berries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख्
कक्ख् €1 P. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hard, solid.<BR>—2 Laughing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कक्खटपत्रकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटपत्रकः|कक्खटपत्रक
कक्खट + -पत्रकः The plant शाणि whose fibre is jute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटी
कक्खटी Chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षः|कक्ष
कक्षः<BR>—1 lurking or hiding place; कोष्टा वराहं निरतक्त कक्षात् Rv. 10. 28. 4.<BR>—2 The end of the lower garment; see कक्षा.<BR>—3 A climbing plant, creeper.<BR>—4 Grass, dry grass; यतस्तु कक्षस्तत एव वह्निः R. 7. 55, 11. 75;<BR> यथोद्धरति निर्दाता कक्षं धान्यं च रक्षति Ms. 7. 110.<BR>—5 A forest of dead trees, dry wood; Bṛ^1. Up. 2. 9. 7.<BR>—6 The arm-pit; ˚अन्तर Pt. 1 the cavity of the armpit; प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं<BR> कक्षे शेरते तेऽभिमारुतम् Śi. 2. 42.<BR>—7 The harem of a king.<BR>—8 The interior of a forest; आशु निर्गत्य कक्षात् Ṛs. 1. 27; कक्षान्तरगतो वायुः Rām.<BR>—9 The side of flank (of anything); ते सरांसि सरित्कक्षान् Rām. 4. 47. 2.<BR>—10 A womanʼs girdle; as in आबद्धनिबिडकक्षैः.<BR>—11 A surrounding wall.<BR>—12 A part of a boat.<BR>—13 The orbit of a planet.<BR>—14 A buffalo.<BR>—15 A gate; उपेत्य स यदुश्रेष्ठो बाह्यकक्षाद्विनिर्गतः Mb. 2. 2. 12.<BR>—16 The Beleric Myrobalan or Terminalia Belerica (Mar. गुग्गुळ, बेहडा).<BR>—17 A marshy ground.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116. note: text has Bṛī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षा
कक्षः + .{@-क्षा@}<BR>—1 Painful boils in the arm-pit.<BR>—2 An elephantʼs rope; also his girth.<BR>—3 A womanʼs girdle or zone; a girdle, waist-band (in general); ‘कक्षा बृहतिकायां स्यात्काञ्च्यां मध्येभबन्धने’ इति विश्वः;<BR> युधे परैः सह दृढबद्धकक्षया Śi. 17. 24.<BR>—4 A surrounding wall; a wall,<BR>—5 The waist, middle part; एते हि विद्युद्गुणबद्धकक्षा Mk. 5. 21.<BR>—6 A courtyard; area, Rām. 4. 33. 19 (सप्तकक्षा); त्रीणि गुल्मान्यतीयाय<BR> तिस्रः कक्षाश्च स द्विजः Bhāg. 10. 80. 16.<BR>—7 An enclosure.<BR>—8 An inner apartment, a private chamber; room in general; ‘कक्षा कच्छे वस्त्रायां काञ्च्यां गेहे प्रकोष्ठके’ इति यादवः;<BR> Ku. 7. 70; Ms. 7. 224;<BR> गृहकलहंसकाननुसरन् कक्षान्तरप्रधावितः K. 63, 182;<BR> कक्षासु रक्षितैर्दक्षैस्तार्क्ष्यः सर्पेष्विवापतत् Parṇāl. 3. 38.<BR>—9 A harem.<BR>—10 Similarity.<BR>—11 An upper garment; दुर्योधनो हस्तिनं पद्मवर्णं सुवर्णकक्षम् Mb. 6. 20. 7.<BR>—12 Objection or reply in argument (in Logic &c.).<BR>—13 Emulation or rivalry.<BR>—14 A secluded part of an edifice; गत्वा कक्षान्तरं त्वन्यत् Ms. 7. 224.<BR>—15 A particular part of a carriage.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">Page0516-1</a>]<BR>—16 The jewellerʼs weight, <i>Rati</i>.<BR>—17 The end of the lower garment which, after the cloth is girt round<BR> the lower part of the body, is brought up behind and tucked into the waist-band<BR> (Mar. कांसोटा)<BR>—18 Tying up the waist.<BR>—19 The wrist.<BR>—20 Border or lace; स्वर्णकक्षपताकाभिः Bhāg. 9. 10. 37.<BR>—21 The basin of a balance (कक्षः also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षम्
कक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@}<BR>—1 A star.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कक्षाग्निः, कक्षान्तरम्, कक्षावेक्षकः, कक्षोत्था, कक्षधरम्, कक्षपः, कक्षापटः, कक्षपुटः, कक्षरुहा, कक्षशायः, कक्षशायुः, कक्षस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0515-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षाग्निः|कक्षाग्नि
कक्षः + -अग्निः wild fire, conflagration; कक्षाग्निलङ्घिततरोरिव वृष्टिपातः R. 11. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षान्तरम्
कक्षः + -अन्तरम् inner or private apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावेक्षकः|कक्षावेक्षक
कक्षः + -अवेक्षकः<BR>—1 a superintendent of the harem.<BR>—2 a keeper of a royal garden.<BR>—3 a door-keeper.<BR>—4 a poet.<BR>—5 a debauchee.<BR>—6 a player; painter.<BR>—7 an actor.<BR>—8 a paramour.<BR>—9 strength of feeling or sentiment (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षोत्था
कक्षः + -उत्था a fragrant grass, (भद्रमुस्ता Cyperus, Mar. नागरमोथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षधरम्
कक्षः + -धरम् the shoulder-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षपः|कक्षप
कक्षः + -पः<BR>—1 a tortoise.<BR>—2 one of the 9 treasures of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षापटः|कक्षापट
कक्षः + कक्षापटः a cloth passed between the legs to cover the privities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षपुटः|कक्षपुट
कक्षः + -पुटः<BR>—1 the arm-pit.<BR>—2 N. of a work on magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षरुहा
कक्षः + -रुहा = नागरमुस्ता q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशायः|कक्षशाय
कक्षः + -शायः, -शायुः a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशायुः|कक्षशायु
कक्षः + -शायः, -शायुः a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षस्थ
कक्षः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> seated on the hip or the flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीकृत
कक्षीकृत <i>a.</i> Agreed to, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षायते
कक्षायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To lie in ambush.<BR>—2 To intend anything wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीवत्|कक्षीवन्त्
कक्षीवत् <i>m.</i> [कक्ष्या-मत् Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 37] N. of a renowned<BR> Ṛṣi, sometimes called Pajriya; author of several hymns of the Ṛgveda;<BR> कक्षीवन्तं य औशिजः Rv. 1. 18. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Consisting of shrubs or dry grass.<BR>—2 Secret. मधु प्रवोचदृतायन्त्वाष्ट्रं यद्दस्रावपि कक्ष्यं वामिति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 17.<BR>—3 Filling the girth (Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्या
कक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्या@}<BR>—1 The girth of an elephant or horse. यो हि दत्त्वा द्विपश्रेष्ठं कक्षायां<BR> कुरुते मनः Rām. 2. 37. 3.<BR>—2 A womanʼs girdle or zone; सिन्दूरैः कृतरुचयः सहेमकक्ष्याः Ki. 7. 8;<BR> Śi. 10. 62.<BR>—3 Fingers.<BR>—4 The upper garment.<BR>—5 The border of a garment.<BR>—6 The inner apartment of a palace. गृहकक्ष्यां प्रथमं विनिर्जगाम<BR> Bu. C. 5. 67. कक्ष्यां द्वितीयामासाद्य तिष्ठन्तु नृपवेश्मनः Rām. 2. 3. 18.<BR>—7 A wall, enclosure; हेमकक्ष्या पुरी रम्या Rām. 3. 48. 11.<BR>—8 Similarity.<BR>—9 A shrub yielding the black and red berry that serves as a weight.<BR>—10 A military girdle.<BR>—11 Rivalry.<BR>—12 Promise.<BR>—13 A balance.<BR>—14 See कक्षा (17, 18); इत्युक्त्वैनमतिकुद्धः कक्ष्यामुत्पीड्य पाण्डवः Mb. 3. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्यम्
कक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यम्@}<BR>—1 The cup or receptacle of a balance.<BR>—2 A part of a carriage.<BR>—3 The hinder part.<BR>—4 A shrub or dry grass forest; प्रधक्ष्यति यथा कक्ष्यं चित्रभानुर्हिमात्यये<BR> Rām. 2. 24. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कक्ष्यावेक्षक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्यावेक्षक
कक्ष्य + -अवेक्षक = कक्षावेक्षक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्
कख् €1 P. [कखति] To laugh at, deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या An enclosure; division of a large building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग्
कग् €1 P. To act, perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क्|कंक्
कङ्क् €1 Ā. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कः|कङ्क|कंक|कंकः
कङ्कः<BR>—1 A heron; Mb. 11. 16. 7.<BR>—2 A variety of mango.<BR>—3 N. of Yama.<BR>—4 A Kṣatriya.<BR>—5 A Vṛṣṇi.<BR>—6 A false or pretended Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—7 Name assumed by Yudhiṣṭhira in the palace of Virāṭa.<BR>—8 One of the 18 divisions of the continent.<BR>—9 N. of a people (pl.); cf. कङ्कस्तरङ्गे गुप्ते च गृध्रे काके युधिष्ठिरे ।<BR> कूले मधुरिपौ कोके पिके वैवस्वतेऽप्यथ ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्का|कंका
कङ्कः + .{@-ङ्का@}<BR>—1 A sort of sandal.<BR>—2 Scent of the lotus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कङ्कत्रोटः, कङ्कत्रोटिः, कङ्कपत्र, कङ्कपत्रिन्, कङ्कमाला, कङ्कमुख, कङ्कवदन, कङ्कवासस्, कङ्कशायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोटः|कङ्कत्रोट
कङ्कः + -त्रोटः, -त्रोटिः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोटिः|कङ्कत्रोटि
कङ्कः + -त्रोटः, -त्रोटिः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
कङ्कः + -पत्र <i>a.</i> furnished with the feathers of a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्रः|कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र
कङ्कः + -पत्र + ({@-त्रः@})<BR> an arrow furnished with a heronʼs feathers; नखप्रभाभूषितकङ्कपत्रे<BR> R. 2. 31; U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18. ({@त्रम्@}) a heronʼs feather fixed on an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्रिन्|कंकपत्रिन्
कङ्कः + -पत्रिन् <i>m.</i> = कङ्कपत्रः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमाला
कङ्कः + -माला<BR>—1 a kind of musical instrument.<BR>—2 beating time by the clapping of hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमुख|कंकमुख|कङ्कमुखः
कङ्कः + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> shaped like a heronʼs mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कवदन
कङ्कः + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> shaped like a heronʼs mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0516-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

