कच्चित् <i>ind.</i> A particle of (1) interrogation (often translatable<BR> by ‘I hope’); कच्चिदेतच्छ्रुतं पार्थ Bg. 18. 72. कच्चित् अहमिव विस्मृतवानसि<BR> त्वम् Ś. 6; कच्चिन्मृगीणामनघा प्रसूतिः R. 5. 7; also 5, 6, 8, 9.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) joy;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0517-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छः|कच्छ|कच्छं
कच्छः, -च्छम्<BR>—1 Bank, margin, skirt, bordering region (whether near water or not);<BR> यमुनाकच्छमवतीर्णः Pt. 1; गन्धमादनकच्छोऽध्यासितः V. 5; Śi. 3. 80;<BR> Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—2 A marsh, morass, fen. ‘जलप्रायमनूपं स्यात्पुंसि कच्छस्तथाविधः’ Nm.<BR>—3 The hem of the lower garment tucked into<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">Page0518-1</a>]<BR> the waist-band; see कक्षा.<BR>—4 A part of boat.<BR>—5 A particular part of a tortoise (in कच्छप).<BR>—6 A tree, the timber of which is used for making furniture of (तुन्न,<BR> Mar. नांदुरकी); Mb. 1. 70. 21.<BR>—7 A populous region.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कच्छान्तः, कच्छदेशः, कच्छपः, कच्छपी, कच्छभूः, कच्छरुहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0517-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छम्
कच्छः, -च्छम्<BR>—1 Bank, margin, skirt, bordering region (whether near water or not);<BR> यमुनाकच्छमवतीर्णः Pt. 1; गन्धमादनकच्छोऽध्यासितः V. 5; Śi. 3. 80;<BR> Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—2 A marsh, morass, fen. ‘जलप्रायमनूपं स्यात्पुंसि कच्छस्तथाविधः’ Nm.<BR>—3 The hem of the lower garment tucked into<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">Page0518-1</a>]<BR> the waist-band; see कक्षा.<BR>—4 A part of boat.<BR>—5 A particular part of a tortoise (in कच्छप).<BR>—6 A tree, the timber of which is used for making furniture of (तुन्न,<BR> Mar. नांदुरकी); Mb. 1. 70. 21.<BR>—7 A populous region.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कच्छान्तः, कच्छदेशः, कच्छपः, कच्छपी, कच्छभूः, कच्छरुहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0517-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छा
कच्छः + -च्छा<BR>—1 A cricket.<BR>—2 The plant Lycopodium Imbricatum (वाराही).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0517-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छान्तः|कच्छान्त|कच्छांत
कच्छः + -अन्तः the border of a lake or stream; marshy place; Ki. 7. 39;<BR> कच्छान्ते सुरसरितो निधाय सेनाम् 12. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छदेशः|कच्छदेश
कच्छः + -देशः N. of a place in the South.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपः|कच्छप
कच्छः + पः (-पी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a turtle, tortoise; केशव धृतकच्छपरूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1;<BR> Ms. 1. 44, 12. 42 (thus explained by Durga; कच्छम् आत्मनो मुखसंपुटं<BR> पाति स हि किंचित् दृष्ट्वा शरीर एव मुखसंपुटं प्रवेशयति).<BR>—2 a tumour on the palate.<BR>—3 an apparatus used in the distillation of spirituous liquor.<BR>—4 an attitude in wrestling.<BR>—5 the tree Cedrela Toona (Mar. नांदुरकी)<BR>—6 one of the nine treasures of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपी
कच्छः + पः (-पी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a turtle, tortoise; केशव धृतकच्छपरूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1;<BR> Ms. 1. 44, 12. 42 (thus explained by Durga; कच्छम् आत्मनो मुखसंपुटं<BR> पाति स हि किंचित् दृष्ट्वा शरीर एव मुखसंपुटं प्रवेशयति).<BR>—2 a tumour on the palate.<BR>—3 an apparatus used in the distillation of spirituous liquor.<BR>—4 an attitude in wrestling.<BR>—5 the tree Cedrela Toona (Mar. नांदुरकी)<BR>—6 one of the nine treasures of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपी
कच्छः + -पी<BR>—1 a female tortoise.<BR>—2 a cutaneous disease, wart or blotch.<BR>—3 a kind of lute; also the lute of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छभूः
कच्छः + -भूः <i>f.</i> marshy ground, morass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छरुहा
कच्छः + -रुहा a kind of grass (दूर्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छटिका
कच्छ(च्छा)टिका, कच्छाटी The end or hem of a lower garment which,<BR> after being carried round the body, is gathered up behind and tucked into<BR> the waist-band.<BR>—2 The borderline of a water-course, where people get down to draw water<BR> (दण्डविवेक, G. O. S. 52, p. 297).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छाटिका
कच्छ(च्छा)टिका, कच्छाटी The end or hem of a lower garment which,<BR> after being carried round the body, is gathered up behind and tucked into<BR> the waist-band.<BR>—2 The borderline of a water-course, where people get down to draw water<BR> (दण्डविवेक, G. O. S. 52, p. 297).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छाटी
कच्छ(च्छा)टिका, कच्छाटी The end or hem of a lower garment which,<BR> after being carried round the body, is gathered up behind and tucked into<BR> the waist-band.<BR>—2 The borderline of a water-course, where people get down to draw water<BR> (दण्डविवेक, G. O. S. 52, p. 297).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपिका
कच्छपिका^1<BR>—1 Pimple, blotch.<BR>—2 A wart accompanying gonorrhoea.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: misspelled; compare with ap90; also the added new source GOS-52 Daṇḍaviveka, p.297 gives कच्छपिका in the text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोटिका
कच्छोटिका = कच्छटिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुः|कच्छु
कच्छुः, -कच्छू <i>f.</i><BR> Itch, scab.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कच्छुघ्नी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छू
कच्छुः, -कच्छू <i>f.</i><BR> Itch, scab.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कच्छुघ्नी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुघ्नी
कच्छुः + -घ्नी the plant (पटोल; Mar. कडू पडवळ); another plant<BR> (हपुषाभेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुमती
कच्छुमती The plant Carpopogon Pruriens शूकशिम्बी (said to cause<BR> itching on being applied to the skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुर|कच्छुरः
कच्छुर <i>a.</i> [कच्छू-र ह्रस्वश्च P. V. 2. 107. Vārt.]<BR>—1 Scabby, itchy.<BR>—2 Unchaste, libidinous.<BR>—3 Poor, wretched<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुरा
कच्छुर + .{@-रा@} N. of several plants; शटी, शूकशिम्बी (Mar. धमासा,<BR> कुयली, धायटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुरालः
कच्छुरालः A kind of plant (Mar. भोंकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोरम्
कच्छोरम् A kind of turmeric Curcuma (शटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्वी
कच्वी A plant with an esculent root (Arum Colocasia) cultivated for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्
कज् €1 P. (कजति)<BR>—1 To be happy.<BR>—2 To be confused with joy, pride, or sorrow.<BR>—3 To grow (in the last sense a Sautra root.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज See under क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलम्
कज्जलम् [कुत्सितं जलमस्मात्प्रभवति, कोः कदादेशः]<BR>—1 Lamp-black or soot, considered as a collyrium and applied to the eyelashes<BR> or eyelids medicinally, or sometimes as an ornament; यथा यथा चेयं<BR> चपला दीप्यते तथा तथा दीपशिखेव कज्जलमलिनमेव कर्म केवलमुद्वमति<BR> K. 105; अद्यापि तां विधृतकज्जललोलनेत्राम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">Page0518-2</a>]<BR> C. P. 15; ˚कालिमा Amaru. 88.<BR>—2 Sulphuret of lead or antimony (used as a collyrium.)<BR>—3 (fig.) Dregs; धिङ् मां विगर्हितं सद्भिर्दुष्कृतं कुलकज्जलम् Bhāg. 6. 2. 27.<BR>—4 Ink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जला
कज्जलम् + .{@-ला(ली)@}<BR> A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जली
कज्जलम् + .{@-ला(ली)@}<BR> A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जली
कज्जलम् + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 Sulphuret of mercury, aethiopʼs mineral.<BR>—2 Ink.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कज्जलध्वजः, कज्जलरोचकः, कज्जलरोचकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलध्वजः|कज्जलध्वज
कज्जलम् + -ध्वजः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलरोचकः|कज्जलरोचक
कज्जलम् + -रोचकः, -रोचकम् the wooden stand on which a lamp is placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलरोचकम्
कज्जलम् + -रोचकः, -रोचकम् the wooden stand on which a lamp is placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलिका
कज्जलिका Powder (esp. made of mercury).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलित
कज्जलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Covered with lamp-black or with a collyrium prepared from it.<BR>—2 Blackened, soiled; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वलम्
कज्ज्वलम् Lamp-black (especially considered as an application to the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्च्|कंच्
कञ्च् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To bind.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चटः|कञ्चट|कञ्चटं
कञ्चटः, -डः<BR> N. of an acquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चडः|कञ्चड
कञ्चटः, -डः<BR> N. of an acquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चारः|कञ्चार|कंचार|कंचारः
कञ्चारः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The Arka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चिका|कंचिका
कञ्चिका<BR>—1 A small boil.<BR>—2 The branch of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकः|कञ्चुक|कंचुक|कंचुकः
कञ्चुकः<BR>—1 An armour, mail; घनाश्च कञ्चुकाः Śi. 1. 45. The skin of a snake,<BR> slough; भोगिनः कञ्चुकाविष्टाः Pt. 1. 65.<BR>—2 आस्तां स्वस्तिकलक्ष्म वक्षसि, तनौ नालोक्यते कञ्चुकः Nāg. 5. 17.<BR>—3 A dress, garb, cloth (in general); धर्म˚ प्रवेशिनः Ś. 5; कपटधर्म˚ Dk. 29.<BR>—4 A dress fitting close to the upper part of the body, robe; अन्तःकञ्चुकिकञ्चुकस्य<BR> विशति त्रासादयं वामनः Ratn. 2. 3; सुभाषितरसास्वादजातरोमाञ्चकञ्चुकम् Pt. 2. 168.<BR>—5 A bodice, jacket; क्वचिदिवेन्द्रगजाजिनकञ्चुकाः Śi. 6. 51, 12. 20;<BR> Amaru. 81; (Phrase:− निन्दति कञ्चुककारं प्रायः शुष्कस्तनी नारी;<BR> cf. “a bad workman quarrels with his tools”).<BR>—6 A kind of drawers or short breeches.<BR>—7 A strap of leather.<BR>—8 Husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकालुः|कञ्चुकालु|कंचुकालु|कंचुकालुः
कञ्चुकालुः A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकित|कंचुकित
कञ्चुकित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Furnished with armour, mailed.<BR>—2 Having a garment; कन्थाकंञ्चुकिताः प्रविश्य भवनद्वाराणि Bh. 3. 130.<BR>—3 (A pearl) having several coatings; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकिन्|कंचुकिन्
कञ्चुकिन् <i>a.</i> Furnished with armour or mail. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An attendant on the womenʼs apartments, a chamberlain; (an important<BR> character in dramas); अन्तःपुरचरो वृद्धो विप्रो गुणगणान्वितः । सर्वकार्यार्थकुशलः<BR> कञ्चुकीत्यभिधीयते ॥ (he must be a Brāhmaṇa, very old, &c.; cf. V. 3.<BR> and Ś. 5. 3).<BR>—2 A libidinous man, debauchee.<BR>—3 A serpent.<BR>—4 A door-keeper.<BR>—5 Barley.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कञ्चुकिवरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकिवरः
कञ्चुकिन् + -वरः The head कञ्चुकिन्. आकर्ण्य कञ्चुकिवरस्य वचः क्षितीशः ।<BR> Bil. C. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0518-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकीयः|कञ्चुकीय
