कट् €1 P. (कटति, अकटीत्, कटितुम्)<BR>—1 To rain.<BR>—2 To surround.<BR>—3 To encompass, cover or screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटः|कट
कटः<BR>—1 A straw mat; Ms. 2. 204.<BR>—2 The hip; Mb. 13. 53. 42.<BR>—3 Hip and loins; the hollow above the hips.<BR>—4 The temples of an elephant; कण्डूयमानेन कटं कदाचित् R. 2. 37, 3. 37, 4. 47.<BR>—5 A particular throw of the dice in hazard; नर्दितदशिंतमार्गः कटेन<BR> विनिपातितो यामि Mk. 2. 8.<BR>—6 A kind of grass; दग्धव्यौ वा कटाग्निना Ms. 8. 377.<BR>—7 Excess (as in उत्कट).<BR>—8 A corpse; कटधूमस्य सौरभ्यमवघ्राय व्रजौकसः Bhāg. 10. 6. 41.<BR>—9 A hearse, bier.<BR>—10 An arrow.<BR>—11 A custom.<BR>—12 A cemetery, burial ground.<BR>—13 A time or season.<BR>—14 The plant Saccharum Sara (शर).<BR>—15 An annual plant.<BR>—16 Grass (in general).<BR>—17 A thin piece of wood, plank.<BR>—18 See कटाक्ष; घ्नन्तीवैक्षत्कटाक्षेपैः Bhāg. 10. 32. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

