कटाक्षः|कटाक्ष
कटः + -अक्षः a glance, a side-long look, leer; गाढं निखात इव मे<BR> हृदये कटाक्षः Māl. 1. 29; also 25, 28; Me. 37. ˚मुष्ट <i>a.</i><BR> caught by a glance. ˚विशिखः an arrow-like look of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाग्निः|कटाग्नि
कटः + -अग्निः a fire kept up with dry grass or straw; the straw placed<BR> round a criminal to be burnt. दग्धव्यौ वा कटाग्निना Ms. 8. 377; Y. 2. 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटान्तः
कटः + -अन्तः the extremity of the temples; आताम्राभा रोषभाजः कटान्तात् Śi. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोदकम्
कटः + -उदकम् —1 water for a funeral libation; कृत्वा कटोदकादीनि भ्रातुःपुत्रानसान्त्वयत्<BR> Bhāg. 7. 2. 17,<BR>—2 rut, ichor (issuing from an elephantʼs temples).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0519-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

