कटारिका
कटारिका A Small dagger (Mar. कट्यार); गुप्तामात्मकटारिकां<BR> तदुदरे गाढं निखाय स्वयम् Śiva B. 20. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाहः|कटाह
कटाहः [कटमाहन्ति, आ-हन्-ड Tv.]<BR>—1 A frying-pan, a shallow boiler for oil or butter (of a semi-spheriodal<BR> shape and furnished with handles; Mar. कढई); तदैव तस्मिन्निनदोऽतिभीषणो<BR> बभूव येनाण्डकटाहमस्फुरत् Bhāg. 7. 8. 16.<BR>—2 A turtleʼs shell.<BR>—3 A well.<BR>—4 A hill or mound of earth.<BR>—5 A fragment of a broken jar; ‘कटाहः खर्परस्तूपः’ इति वैजयन्ती;<BR> यद्दन्तिनः कटकटाहतटान्मिमङ्क्षोः Śi. 5. 37; N. 22. 32.<BR>—6 A winnowing basket.<BR>—7 Hell, the infernal regions.<BR>—8 A young female buffalo whose horns are just appearing.<BR>—9 A Dvīpa or division of a known continent.<BR>—10 A heap or pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाहकम्
कटाहकम् A pan, pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिः|कटि
कटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [कट्-इन्]<BR>—1 The hip.<BR>—2 The buttocks (considered by rhetoricians as vulgar and colloquial in<BR> these senses; the word कटि in कटिस्ते हरते मनः is said to<BR> be ग्राम्य.)<BR>—3 An elephantʼs cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटी
कटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [कट्-इन्]<BR>—1 The hip.<BR>—2 The buttocks (considered by rhetoricians as vulgar and colloquial in<BR> these senses; the word कटि in कटिस्ते हरते मनः is said to<BR> be ग्राम्य.)<BR>—3 An elephantʼs cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटी
कटिः, -टी + .{@-टी@} Long pepper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कटिकुष्ठम्, कटिकूपः, कटितटम्, कटित्रम्, कटिदेशः, कटिमालिका, कटिरोहकः, कटिशीर्षकः, कटिशूलः, कटिशृङ्खला, कटिसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिकुष्ठम्
कटिः + -कुष्ठम् A kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिकूपः|कटिकूप
कटिः + -कूपः the hollow above the hip, the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटितटम्
कटिः + -तटम् the loins; कटीतटनिवेशितम् Mk. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटित्रम्
कटिः + -त्रम्<BR>—1 a cloth girt round the loins.<BR>—2 a zone, girdle; किरीटिकेयूरकटित्रकङ्कणम् Bhāg. 6. 16. 30.<BR>—3 an ornament of small bells worn round the loins.<BR>—4 an armour of the hip or the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिदेशः|कटिदेश
कटिः + -देशः the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिप्रोथः|कटिप्रोथ
कटिः + -देशः + ({@-टि@} or {@टी@}) {@प्रोथः@} the buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिमालिका
कटिः + -मालिका a womanʼs zone or girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

