कटीरकम् The posteriors, hips; व्यचलन्विशङ्ककटकटीरकस्थली Śi. 13. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटु|कटुः
कटु <i>a.</i> (टु or ट्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Pungent, acrid; (said of a <i>rasa</i> or flavour; the <i>rasas</i><BR> are six; मधुर, कटु, अम्ल, तिक्त, कषाय, and लवण); कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः ।<BR> आहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकाभयप्रदाः ॥ Bg. 17. 9.<BR>—2 Fragrant, exhaling strong odour; सप्तच्छदक्षीरकटुप्रवाहम् R. 5. 48.<BR>—3 Ill-smelling, having a bad smell.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Bitter. This sense is found given to the words कटु and कटुक<BR> in Prākrit and later sanskrit works; cf. अतिकटुः कारवेल्लादिः अतितीक्ष्णो<BR> मरिचादिः; अमृततरङ्गिणी on Bg. 17. 9, नीलकण्ठ gives the same sense.<BR>—5 caustic (words); Y. 3. 142.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Disagreeable, unpleasant; श्रवणकटु नृपाणामेकवाक्यं विवव्रुः R. 6. 85.<BR>—6 Envious.<BR>—7 Hot, impetuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुः|कटु
कटु + .{@-टुः@}<BR>—1 Pungency, acerbity (one of the six flavours).<BR>—2 N. of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुः|कटु
कटु + .{@-टुः@} <i>f.</i> A medical plant (कटुरोहिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटु|कटुः
कटु + .{@-टु@} <i>n.</i><BR>—1 An improper action.<BR>—2 Blaming, reviling, scandal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कट्वङ्गः, कटूत्कटम्, कटूदरी, कटुकन्दः, कटुकन्दम्, कटुकीटः, कटुकीटकः, कटुक्वाणः, कटुग्रन्थिः, कटुग्रन्थि, कटुचातुर्जातकम्, कटुच्छदः, कटुज, कटुतिक्तकः, कटुतिक्ता, कटुतुम्बी, कटुतैलः, कटुत्रयम्, कटुदला, कटुनिष्प्लावः, कटुपत्रः, कटुपत्रिका, कटुपाक, कटुपाकिन्, कटुफलः, कटुबीजा, कटुभङ्गः, कटुभद्रः, कटुमञ्जरिका, कटुमोदम्, कटुख, कटुरोहिणी, कटुविपाक, कटुस्नेहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वङ्गः|कट्वङ्ग
कटु + -अङ्गः<BR>—1 the श्योनाक tree (Mar. टेटू).<BR>—2 N. of the king Dilīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0520-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

