कटोरम् An earthen vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोरा
कटोरा A shallow cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोल|कटोलः
कटोल <i>a.</i> Pungent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोलः|कटोल
कटोल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A pungent flavour.<BR>—2 A man of an inferior and degraded tribe, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कटोलवीणा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोलवीणा
कटोल + -वीणा a kind of lute played by the Cāṇḍālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्ट्
कट्ट् €10 P. To heap, cover with earth; Kṛṣisaṃgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टरिनृत्यम्
कट्टरिनृत्यम् A kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टारः|कट्टार
कट्टारः A weapon, dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टारिका
कट्टारिका <i>f.</i> A butcherʼs cleaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्फलः|कट्फल
कट्फलः N. of a tree, commonly called कायफळ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वर|कट्वरं
कट्वर^1 <i>a.</i> Despised.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: follows after कट्फलः ; so here seems to be lost consonant below ट; corrected after AP90 and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वरम्
कट्वर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The skim or whey of curds.<BR>—2 Buttermilk with water.<BR>—3 A sauce, condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ्
कठ् €1 P. (कठति, अकठीत्, कठित) To live in distress; see कण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठः|कठ
कठः<BR>—1 N. of a sage, pupil of Vaiśampāyana, teacher of that branch of Yajurveda<BR> which is called after him.<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 A note or simple sound.<BR>—4 A kind of <i>ṛk</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाः
कठः + .{@-ठाः@} The followers of that sage. के सब्रह्मचारिणोस्येति । कठाः ।<BR> Mbh. on P. II. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठी
कठः + .{@-ठी@}<BR>—1 A female follower of Kaṭha. कठी वृन्दारिका कठवृन्दारिका Mbh.<BR> on P. VI. 3. 42.<BR>—2 The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कठाध्यापकः, कठोपनिषद्, कठकालापाः, कठधूर्तः, कठश्रोत्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाध्यापकः|कठाध्यापक
कठः + -अध्यापकः a teacher of the Kaṭha branch of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोपनिषद्
कठः + -उपनिषद् N. of an Upaniṣad (generally said to belong to अथर्ववेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठकालापाः
कठः + -कालापाः P. II. 4. 3. Schools of कठ and कालाप; नन्दन्तु<BR> कठकालापाः वर्धन्तां कठकौथुमाः Mbh. on II. 4. 3. ये च मे कठकालापा<BR> बहवो दण्डमाणवाः Rām. 2. 32. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठधूर्तः|कठधूर्त|कठधूर्त्त
कठः + -धूर्तः a Brāhmaṇa well-versed in the कठ branch of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठश्रोत्रियः|कठश्रोत्रिय
कठः + -श्रोत्रियः P. V. 2. 84 a Brāhmaṇa who has mastered the कठ<BR> branch of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0521-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठमर्दः|कठमर्द|कठमर्द्द|कठमर्द्दः
