कण्टालुः|कण्टालु|कंटालुः
कण्टालुः <i>f.</i> N. of several plants:− वार्तकी, वंश, वर्वुर, बृहती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टिन्|कंटिन्
कण्टिन् <i>a.</i> Thorny. ━<i>m.</i> N. of several trees:− खदिर, अपामार्ग, गोक्षुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्|कंठ्
कण्ठ् €1. €10 U. (कण्ठति-ते, कण्ठयति-ते, कण्ठित)<BR>—1 To mourn, grieve for.<BR>—2 To miss, be anxious or long for, remember with regret; (in this sense<BR> generally used with the preposition उद् and a noun in the gen., loc. or dat. case).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठः|कण्ठ|कंठ|कंठं|कंठः
कण्ठः, -ण्ठम्<BR>—1 Throat; कण्ठे निपीडयन् मारयति Mk. 8. कण्ठः स्तम्भितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः<BR> Ś. 4. 6; कण्ठेषु स्खलितं गतेऽपि शिशिरे पुंस्कोकिलानां रुतम् 6. 4.<BR>—2 The neck; अयं कण्ठे बाहुः U. 1. कण्ठाश्लेषपरिग्रहे शिथिलता<BR> Pt. 4. 6; कण्ठाश्लेषप्रणयिनि जने किं पुनर्दूरसंस्थे Me. 3, 99, 114;<BR> Amaru. 19, 57; Ku. 5. 57.<BR>—3 Sound, tone, voice; सा मुक्तकण्ठं चकन्द R. 14. 68; किमिदं<BR> किन्नरकण्ठि सुप्यते 8. 64; आर्यपुत्रोऽपि प्रमुक्तकण्ठं रोदिति U. 3.<BR>—4 The neck or brim of a vessel &c.<BR>—5 Vicinity, immediate proximity (as in उपकण्ठ).<BR>—6 The opening of the womb.<BR>—7 A bud on a stalk.<BR>—8 The space of an inch from the edge of the hole in which sacrificial<BR> fire is deposited.<BR>—9 The मदन tree. —10 Guttural sound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ठाग्निः, कण्ठावसक्त, कण्ठागत, कण्ठाभरणम्, कण्ठाश्लेषः, कण्ठोक्ताम्, कण्ठकुब्जः, कण्ठकूणिका, कण्ठग, कण्ठगत, कण्ठतटः, कण्ठतटम्, कण्ठतटी, कण्ठतलासिका, कण्ठत्रः, कण्ठदघ्न, कण्ठनालम्, कण्ठनाली, कण्ठनडिकः, कण्ठनीलकः, कण्ठपाशः, कण्ठपाशकः, कण्ठबन्धः, कण्ठभूषणम्, कण्ठभूषा, कण्ठभङ्गः, कण्ठमणिः, कण्ठरोधम्, कण्ठलग्न, कण्ठलता, कण्ठवर्तिन्, कण्ठशालुकम्, कण्ठशुण्डी, कण्ठशोषः, कण्ठसज्जनम्, कण्ठसूत्रम्, कण्ठस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठम्
कण्ठः, -ण्ठम्<BR>—1 Throat; कण्ठे निपीडयन् मारयति Mk. 8. कण्ठः स्तम्भितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः<BR> Ś. 4. 6; कण्ठेषु स्खलितं गतेऽपि शिशिरे पुंस्कोकिलानां रुतम् 6. 4.<BR>—2 The neck; अयं कण्ठे बाहुः U. 1. कण्ठाश्लेषपरिग्रहे शिथिलता<BR> Pt. 4. 6; कण्ठाश्लेषप्रणयिनि जने किं पुनर्दूरसंस्थे Me. 3, 99, 114;<BR> Amaru. 19, 57; Ku. 5. 57.<BR>—3 Sound, tone, voice; सा मुक्तकण्ठं चकन्द R. 14. 68; किमिदं<BR> किन्नरकण्ठि सुप्यते 8. 64; आर्यपुत्रोऽपि प्रमुक्तकण्ठं रोदिति U. 3.<BR>—4 The neck or brim of a vessel &c.<BR>—5 Vicinity, immediate proximity (as in उपकण्ठ).<BR>—6 The opening of the womb.<BR>—7 A bud on a stalk.<BR>—8 The space of an inch from the edge of the hole in which sacrificial<BR> fire is deposited.<BR>—9 The मदन tree. —10 Guttural sound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ठाग्निः, कण्ठावसक्त, कण्ठागत, कण्ठाभरणम्, कण्ठाश्लेषः, कण्ठोक्ताम्, कण्ठकुब्जः, कण्ठकूणिका, कण्ठग, कण्ठगत, कण्ठतटः, कण्ठतटम्, कण्ठतटी, कण्ठतलासिका, कण्ठत्रः, कण्ठदघ्न, कण्ठनालम्, कण्ठनाली, कण्ठनडिकः, कण्ठनीलकः, कण्ठपाशः, कण्ठपाशकः, कण्ठबन्धः, कण्ठभूषणम्, कण्ठभूषा, कण्ठभङ्गः, कण्ठमणिः, कण्ठरोधम्, कण्ठलग्न, कण्ठलता, कण्ठवर्तिन्, कण्ठशालुकम्, कण्ठशुण्डी, कण्ठशोषः, कण्ठसज्जनम्, कण्ठसूत्रम्, कण्ठस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाग्निः|कण्ठाग्नि
कण्ठः + -अग्निः a bird (digesting in the throat or gizzard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठावसक्त
कण्ठः + -अवसक्त <i>a.</i> clinging to the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठागत
कण्ठः + -आगत <i>a.</i> come to the throat (as the breath or soul of a dying person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाभरणम्
कण्ठः + -आभरणम् a neck-ornament, necklace; परीक्षितं काव्यसुवर्णमेतल्लोकस्य<BR> कण्ठाभरणत्वमेतु Vikr. 1. 24; cf. names like सरस्वतीकण्ठाभरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाश्लेषः|कण्ठाश्लेष
कण्ठः + -आश्लेषः neck-embrace;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">Page0524-1</a>]<BR> Me. 3; कण्ठाश्लेषपरिग्रहे शिथिलता Pt. 4. 6; ˚उपगूढ Bh. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठोक्ताम्
कण्ठः + -उक्ताम् personal testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठकुब्जः|कण्ठकुब्ज
कण्ठः + -कुब्जः a kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठकूणिका|कंठकूणिका
कण्ठः + -कूणिका the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठग
कण्ठः + -ग <i>a.</i> reaching or extending to the throat; हृद्गाभिः पूयते<BR> विप्रः कण्ठगाभिस्तु भूमिपः Ms. 2. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठगत|कंठगत
कण्ठः + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being at or in the throat, coming to the throat; <i>i. e.</i> on the point<BR> of departing; न वदेद्यावनीं भाषां प्राणैः कण्ठगतैरपि Subhāṣ.; Pt. 1. 296.<BR>—2 approaching or reaching the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतटः|कण्ठतट|कंठतट
कण्ठः + -तटः, -तटम्, -तटी the side of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतटम्
कण्ठः + -तटः, -तटम्, -तटी the side of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतटी
कण्ठः + -तटः, -तटम्, -तटी the side of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतलासिका
कण्ठः + -तलासिका the leather or rope passing round the neck of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठत्रः|कण्ठत्र
कण्ठः + -त्रः A necklace; शुक्लकेयूरकण्ठत्राः Mb. 5. 143. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठदघ्न|कंठदघ्न
कण्ठः + -दघ्न <i>a.</i> reaching to the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनालम्
कण्ठः + -नालम् Stalk-like throat, a throat, neck; कण्ठनालादपातयत्<BR> R. 15. 52 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनाली
कण्ठः + -नाली, -नडिकः a kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीडकः|कण्ठनीडक|कंठनीडक
कण्ठः + -नाली, -नडिकः a kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीलकः|कण्ठनीलक|कंठनीलक
कण्ठः + -नीलकः a large lamp or torch, a whisp of lighted straw &c. (Mar. मशाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठपाशः
कण्ठः + -पाशः, -पाशकः<BR>—1 a rope tied round an elephantʼs neck.<BR>—2 a halter in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठपाशकः|कण्ठपाशक|कंठपाशक
कण्ठः + -पाशः, -पाशकः<BR>—1 a rope tied round an elephantʼs neck.<BR>—2 a halter in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठबन्धः|कण्ठबन्ध
कण्ठः + -बन्धः a rope for an elephantʼs neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठभूषणम्
कण्ठः + -भूषणम्, -भूषा a short necklace; विदुषां कण्ठभूषात्वमेतु Vikr. 18. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठभूषा|कंठभूषा
कण्ठः + -भूषणम्, -भूषा a short necklace; विदुषां कण्ठभूषात्वमेतु Vikr. 18. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठभङ्गः|कण्ठभङ्ग
कण्ठः + -भङ्गः Stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठमणिः|कण्ठमणि|कंठमणि
कण्ठः + -मणिः<BR>—1 a jewel worn on the neck.<BR>—2 (fig.) a dear or beloved object.<BR>—3 Thyroid Cartilage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठरोधम्
कण्ठः + -रोधम् Stopping or lowering the voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलग्न
कण्ठः + -लग्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 clinging to the throat.<BR>—2 suspended round the neck.<BR>—3 throwing the arms round the neck (in embraces); कण्ठेलग्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलता
कण्ठः + -लता<BR>—1 a collar.<BR>—2 a horseʼs halter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठवर्तिन्|कंठवर्तिन्
कण्ठः + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> being at or in the throat, <i>i. e.</i> on the point<BR> of departing; ˚प्राणैः R. 12. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठशालुकम्
कण्ठः + -शालुकम् a hard tumour in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठशुण्डी
कण्ठः + -शुण्डी swelling of the tonsils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठशोषः|कण्ठशोष|कंठशोष
कण्ठः + -शोषः (lit.)<BR>—1 drying up or parching of the throat.<BR>—2 (fig.) fruitless expostulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठसज्जनम्
कण्ठः + -सज्जनम् hanging on, by, or round the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठसूत्रम्
कण्ठः + -सूत्रम् a kind of embrace; (thus defined:− यत्कुर्वते वक्षसि<BR> वल्लभस्य स्तनाभिघातं निबिडोपगूहात् । परिश्रमार्थं शनकैर्विदग्धास्तत्कण्ठसूत्रं<BR> प्रवदन्ति सन्तः ॥); कण्ठसूत्रमपदिश्य योषितः R. 19. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठस्थ
कण्ठः + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being in the throat.<BR>—2 guttural (as a letter).<BR>—3 being in the mouth, ready to be repeated by rote.<BR>—4 learnt and ready to be repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतः|कण्ठत
कण्ठतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the throat.<BR>—2 Distinctly, explicitly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिका|कंठिका
कण्ठिका A necklace of a single string or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिन्|कंठिन्
कण्ठिन् <i>a.</i> Belonging to the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठी
कण्ठी<BR>—1 Neck, throat.<BR>—2 A necklace, a collar.<BR>—3 A rope round the neck of a horse.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ठीरवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीरवः|कण्ठीरव|कंठीरव
कण्ठी + -रवः<BR>—1 a lion.<BR>—2 an elephant in rut; कण्ठीरवो महाग्रहेण न्यपतत् Dk. 7.<BR>—3 a pigeon.<BR>—4 explicit declaration or mention; इति कण्ठीरवेणोक्तम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठेकालः|कण्ठेकाल|कंठेकाल|कंठेकालः
कण्ठेकालः N. of Śiva (blue on the neck). कण्ठेकालेन कैलासः … … ।<BR> Śiva B. 16. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्य|कंठ्य|कण्ठ्यः
कण्ठ्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating or suitable to, or being at, the throat.<BR>—2 Guttural.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ठ्यवर्णः, कण्ठ्यस्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्यवर्णः|कण्ठ्यवर्ण|कंठ्यवर्ण
कण्ठ्य + -वर्णः a guttural letter; namely अ, आ, क्, ख्, ग्, घ्, ङ् and ह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्यस्वरः|कण्ठ्यस्वर|कंठ्यस्वर
कण्ठ्य + -स्वरः a guttural vowel (अ and आ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठला
कण्ठला A basket made of canes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठालः|कण्ठाल|कंठाल|कंठालः
कण्ठालः<BR>—1 A boat.<BR>—2 A spade, hoe.<BR>—3 War.<BR>—4 A camel.<BR>—5 An esculent root.<BR>—6 A churning vessel.<BR>—7 A bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाला
कण्ठालः + .{@-ला@} A churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीलः|कण्ठील|कंठील|कंठीलः
कण्ठीलः A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीलः|कण्ठील|कंठील|कंठीलः
कण्ठीलः + .{@-लः, -ला@} A churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीला
कण्ठीलः + .{@-लः, -ला@} A churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्|कंड्
कण्ड् I. €1 U. (कण्डति-ते, कण्डित)<BR>—1 To be glad or satisfied.<BR>—2 To be proud.<BR>—3 To unhusk. ━II. €10 U. (कण्डयति-ते, कण्डित)<BR>—1 To thresh (corn, grain &c.), unhusk.<BR>—2 To protect, defend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डनम्
कण्डनम्<BR>—1 Threshing, separating the chaff from the grain; अजानतार्थं तत्सर्वं<BR> (अध्ययनं) तुषाणां कण्डनं यथा.<BR>—2 Chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डनी|कंडनी
कण्डनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A wooden mortar in which the threshing of corn or grain is performed.<BR>—2 A pestle; Ms. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डित
कण्डित <i>a.</i> Dislocated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डरा|कंडरा
कण्डरा<BR>—1 A sinew (of which 16 are considered to be in the human body).<BR>—2 A principal vessel of the body, a large artery, vein &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डानकः|कण्डानक|कंडानकः
कण्डानकः N. of a servant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डिका|कंडिका
कण्डिका<BR>—1 A short section, shortest subdivision; (as in the शुक्लयजुर्वेद).<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डिल
कण्डिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drunken.<BR>—2 Saucy. कण्डिललट्टुका मे प्रतीष्टाः Pratijñā. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुः|कण्डु|कंडु|कंडुः
कण्डुः <i>m., f.</i>, कण्डूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Scratching.<BR>—2 Itching, itching sensation; कपोलकण्डूः करिभिर्विनेतुम् Ku. 1. 9;<BR> Śānti. 4. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ड्वादि, कण्डुकरी, कण्डुघ्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूः
कण्डुः <i>m., f.</i>, कण्डूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Scratching.<BR>—2 Itching, itching sensation; कपोलकण्डूः करिभिर्विनेतुम् Ku. 1. 9;<BR> Śānti. 4. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्ड्वादि, कण्डुकरी, कण्डुघ्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्वादि
कण्डुः + -आदि <i>m.</i> (pl.) the nominal verbs. P. III. 1. 27; mentioned<BR> separately with the root कण्डू given as the first root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुकरी
कण्डुः + -करी N. of a plant शूकशिम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुघ्नः
कण्डुः + -घ्नः<BR>—1 N. of a plant (Mar. बाहवा).<BR>—2 white mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुर|कंडुर|कण्डुरः
कण्डुर <i>a.</i> Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुरः|कण्डुर|कंडुर
कण्डुर + .{@-रः@} A species of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूतिः|कण्डूति|कंडूति|कंडूतिः
कण्डूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Scratching.<BR>—2 Itching, itch; सुभग त्वत्कथारम्भे कर्णे कण्डूतिलालसा S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूमत्|कण्डूमन्त्
कण्डूमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Scratching.<BR>—2 Itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयति
कण्डूयति, -ते Den. U. (<i>p. p.</i> कण्डूयित)<BR>—1 To scratch, rub gently;<BR> कण्डूयमानेन कटं कदाचित् R. 2. 37; मृगीमकण्डूयत कृष्णसारः<BR> Ku. 3. 36; so शृङ्गे कृष्णमृगस्य वामनयनं कण्डूयमानां मृगीम् Ś. 16; Ms. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयते
कण्डूयति, -ते Den. U. (<i>p. p.</i> कण्डूयित)<BR>—1 To scratch, rub gently;<BR> कण्डूयमानेन कटं कदाचित् R. 2. 37; मृगीमकण्डूयत कृष्णसारः<BR> Ku. 3. 36; so शृङ्गे कृष्णमृगस्य वामनयनं कण्डूयमानां मृगीम् Ś. 16; Ms. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयन|कंडूयन|कण्डूयनं
कण्डूयन, -नक <i>a.</i><BR> Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक|कण्डूयनकः
कण्डूयन, -नक <i>a.</i><BR> Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनम्
कण्डूयन, -नक + .{@-नम्@} Scratching, rubbing; कण्डूयनैर्दंशनिवारणैश्च R. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनी|कंडूयनी
कण्डूयन, -नक + .{@-नी@} A brush for rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनकः|कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक
कण्डूयन, -नक + .{@-कः@} A tickler; कर्णस्य कण्डूयनकेन वापि (तृणेन कार्यं<BR> भवतीश्वराणाम्) Pt. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूया|कंडूया
कण्डूया<BR>—1 Scratching.<BR>—2 Itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयितम्
कण्डूयितम् Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयितृ|कंडूयितृ
कण्डूयितृ <i>a.</i> Scratching, a scratcher; कण्डूयितारं कुशसूचिलावम्<BR> (भुजम्) R. 13. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूरा|कंडूरा
कण्डूरा N. of a plant causing itch (Mucana Pruritus Mar. खाजकुयली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूल|कंडूल|कण्डूलः
कण्डूल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an itchy sensation, feeling the itch, itchy; कण्डूलद्विपगण्डपिण्डकषणोत्कम्पेन<BR> संपातिभिः U. 2. 9.<BR>—2 Causing itch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूलः|कण्डूल|कंडूल
कण्डूल + .{@-लः@} An esculent root; (Mar. खाजरासुरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्वोघः|कण्ड्वोघ
कण्ड्वोघः^1 A caterpillar^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/166.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलः|कण्डोल|कंडोल|कंडोलः
कण्डोलः<BR>—1 A basket for holding grain (made of cane or bamboo).<BR>—2 A safe, store-room.<BR>—3 A camel (also <i>f.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोली|कंडोली
कण्डोलः + .{@-ली@} The lute of a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्डोलवीणा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलवीणा
कण्डोलः + -वीणा The lute of a Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलकः|कण्डोलक|कंडोलकः
कण्डोलकः<BR>—1 A basket.<BR>—2 A safe, store-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोषः|कण्डोष|कंडोष|कंडोषः
कण्डोषः<BR>—1 A caterpillar^1<BR>—2 A scorpion; MW.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व <i>a.</i> [कण् क्वन्] Ved.<BR>—1 Talented, intelligent.<BR>—2 Praising; प्र सक्षणो दिव्यः कण्वहोता Rv. 5. 41. 4.<BR>—3 Fit to be praised or honoured; Rv. 10. 115. 5.<BR>—4 Deaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वः|कण्व|कण्वं
कण्व + .{@-ण्वः@}<BR>—1 N. of a renowned sage, foster-father of Śakuntalā and progenitor<BR> of the line of काण्व Brāhmaṇas. He was the author of several hymns<BR> of the Ṛgveda.<BR>—2 (Ved.) A peculiar class of evil spirits against whom charms or hymns<BR> (Av. 2. 25) are used; गर्भादं कण्वं नाशय Av. 2. 25. 3.<BR>—3 A praiser.<BR>—4 The founder of Vedic schools.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वम्
कण्व + .{@-ण्वम्@} Sin, evil.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कण्वोपनिषद्, कण्वजम्भन, कण्वदुहितृ, कण्वसुता, कण्वसखिन्, कण्वहोतृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वोपनिषद्
कण्व + -उपनिषद् N. of an upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वजम्भन
कण्व + -जम्भन <i>a.</i> consuming or destroying the evil spirits called Kaṇvas (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वदुहितृ
कण्व + -दुहितृ, -सुता Śakuntalā, Kaṇvaʼs daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वसुता
कण्व + -दुहितृ, -सुता Śakuntalā, Kaṇvaʼs daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वसखिन्
कण्व + -सखिन् <i>a.</i> Ved. a friend of the Kaṇvas, friendly disposed<BR> to them; स इदग्निः कण्वतमः कण्वसखा Rv. 10. 115. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वहोतृ
कण्व + -होतृ <i>a.</i> one whose priest is a Kaṇva; प्र सक्षणो दिव्यः<BR> कण्वहोता Rv. 5. 41. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वतम
कण्वतम <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Very wise;<BR>—2 A real कण्व; स इदग्निः कण्वतमः कण्वसखाः Rv. 10. 115. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वमत्|कण्वमन्त्
कण्वमत् <i>a.</i> United with a praiser or with the Kaṇvas (as Indra);<BR> आ तू षिञ्च कण्वमन्तम् Rv. 8. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतः|कत
कतः, -कतकः<BR> [कं जलं शुद्धं तनोति तन् -ड Tv.] The clearing-nut<BR> plant, (Mar. निवळी) (the nut of which is said to clear muddy water);<BR> फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यम्बुप्रसादनम् । न नामग्रहणादेव तस्य<BR> वारि प्रसीदति ॥ Ms. 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतकः|कतक
कतः, -कतकः<BR> [कं जलं शुद्धं तनोति तन् -ड Tv.] The clearing-nut<BR> plant, (Mar. निवळी) (the nut of which is said to clear muddy water);<BR> फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यम्बुप्रसादनम् । न नामग्रहणादेव तस्य<BR> वारि प्रसीदति ॥ Ms. 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम्
कतः, -कतकः + .{@-तम्, -तकम्@} The nut of this tree, see अम्बुप्रसादन also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतकम्
कतः, -कतकः + .{@-तम्, -तकम्@} The nut of this tree, see अम्बुप्रसादन also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतफलः|कतफल
कतफलः The clearing nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम <i>pron. a.</i> [किम्-डतम्] (˚मत् <i>n.</i>) P. II. 1. 63.<BR> Who or which of many; अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन गतः स जाल्म<BR> इति V. 1; अथ कतमं पुनरृतुमधिकृत्य गास्यामि Ś. 1; कतमे ते<BR> गुणास्तत्र यानुदाहरन्त्यार्यमिश्राः Māl. 1; G. L. 22; Ki. 6. 40. (sometimes<BR> it is used merely as a strengthened substitute for किम्). When followed<BR> by च and preceded by यतम it means ‘any whosoever’, ‘whatsoever’.<BR> In negative sentences कतम with चन or अपि means ‘not even one’<BR>, ‘none at all’. It also means ‘best or excessively good-looking’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर <i>pron. a.</i> (˚रत् <i>n.</i>) Who or who or which of two;<BR> नैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg. 2. 6.<BR> कतरः स आत्मा Ait. Up. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतरतः
कतरतः On which of the two sides?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति <i>pron. a.</i> [किम्-डति] (always declined in the plural only;<BR> कति, कतिभिः &c.)<BR>—1 How many; कत्यग्नयः कति सूर्यासः Rv. 10. 88. 18; एभिर्भूतैः<BR> स्मर कति कृताः स्वान्त ते विप्रलम्भाः Śānti. 3. 18;<BR>—2 Some. When followed by चित्, चन or अपि, कति loses its interrogative<BR> force and becomes indefinite in sense, meaning ‘some’, ‘several’, ‘a few’;<BR> तन्वी स्थिता कतिचिदेव पदानि गत्वा Ś. 2. 12; कत्यपि वासराणि<BR> Amaru. 25; तस्मिन्नद्रौ कतिचिदबलाविप्रयुक्तः स कामी नीत्वा मासान् Me. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिकृत्वस्
कतिकृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> How many times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिधा
कतिधा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 How often<BR>—2 In how many places or parts.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कतिधाचिद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिधाचिद्
कतिधा + -चिद् Everywhere; द्विमाता शयुः कतिधा चिदायवे Rv. 1. 31. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कतिपय <i>a.</i> [कति-अयच् पुक् च्] —1 Some, several, a certain<BR> number; कतिपयकुसुमोद्गमः कदम्बः U. 3. 20; Me. 23; कतिपयदिवसापगमे<BR> some days having elapsed; वर्णैः कतिपयैरेव ग्रथितस्य स्वरैरिव<BR> Śi. 2. 72; कतिपयेन or कतिपयात् with some effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपयथ
कतिपयथ <i>a.</i> Advanced to a certain place or degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिविध
कतिविध <i>a.</i> How many kinds; राम वेदाः कतिविधाः Mukti. Up. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिशस्
कतिशस् <i>ind.</i> How many at a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमालः|कतमाल
कतमालः [कस्य जलस्य तमाय शोषणायालति पर्याप्नोति अलच्<BR> Tv.] Fire; cf. खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्ताशब्दः|कत्ताशब्द
कत्ताशब्दः The rattling sound of dice; अरे कत्ताशब्दो निर्नाणकस्य<BR> हरति हृदयं मनुष्यस्य Mk. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ्
कत्थ् €1 Ā. (कत्थते, कत्थित)<BR>—1 To boast, swagger; कृत्वा कत्थिष्यते<BR> न कः Bk. 16. 4; कृत्वैतत्कर्मणा सर्वं कत्थेथाः Mb.<BR>—2 To praise, celebrate.<BR>—3 To flatter or coax<BR>—4 To abuse, revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थन
कत्थन <i>a.</i> Boasting, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थनम्
कत्थन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} Bragging, boasting; इक्ष्वाकूणां विशेषेण बाहुवीर्ये<BR> न कत्थनम् Mb. 3. 99. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थना
कत्थन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} Bragging, boasting; इक्ष्वाकूणां विशेषेण बाहुवीर्ये<BR> न कत्थनम् Mb. 3. 99. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्पय
कत्पय <i>a.</i> Ved. Swelling, rising; त्यं चिदित्था कत्पयं शयानम् Rv. 5. 32. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्पयम्
कत्पय + .{@-यम्@} Water causing happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्र्
कत्र् €10 P. (कत्रयति, कत्रित) To loosen, slacken, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्सवरम्
कत्सवरम् The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्
कथ् €10 U. (कथयति-ते, कथित)<BR>—1 To tell, relate, narrate, communicate (usually with dat. of person);<BR> राममिष्वसनदर्शनोत्सुकं मैथिलाय कथयांबभूव सः R. 11. 37.<BR>—2 To declare, state, mention; अकीर्तिं चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम्<BR> Bg. 2. 34; R. 11. 15.<BR>—3 To converse, talk with, hold conversation with; कथयित्वा सुमन्त्रेण सह<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">Page0526-1</a>]<BR> Rām.<BR>—4 To indicate, betray, bespeak, show; V. 1. 6; Māl. 8. 10; आकारसदृशं<BR> चेष्टितमेवास्य कथयति Ś. 7.<BR>—5 To describe, relate; किं कथ्यते श्रीरुभयस्य तस्य Ku. 7. 78;<BR> कथाच्छलेन बालानां नीतिस्तदिह कथ्यते H. Pr. 8; Pt. 4. 37.<BR>—6 To inform, give information about, complain against; Mk. 3.<BR>—7 To denounce.<BR>—8 To suppose.<BR>—9 To praise, narrate devotedly; भुवि त्वां कथयन्तो हि सिद्धिमेष्यन्ति<BR> राघव Rām. 7. 82. 12. ━<i>Pass.</i> (कथ्यते)<BR>—1 To be called.<BR>—2 To be regarded or considered as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक <i>a.</i> [कथ्-ण्वुल्] A narrator, a relator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथकः|कथक
कथक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A chief actor, speaker of a prologue.<BR>—2 A disputant.<BR>—3 A story-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन्ता|कथंता
कथन्ता Indescribable uneasiness; Yogas. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन <i>a.</i> Telling, talkative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनम्
कथन + .{@-नम्@} Narration, relation, description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनिकः|कथनिक
कथनिकः A narrator, story-teller; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनीय
कथनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be said or told or declared. —2 Worthy of relation, to be named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथयान
कथयान <i>a.</i> Telling, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
कथा [कथ् नि˚ अ] A tale, story; ˚प्रावीण्यम् U. 4 historical knowledge.<BR>—2 A fable, feigned story; कथाच्छलेन बालानां नीतिस्तदिह कथ्यते H. Pr. 8.<BR>—3 An account, allusion, mention; कथापि खलु पापानामलमश्रेयसे यतः Śi. 2. 40.<BR>—4 Talk, conversation, speech; प्रथमं कृतां कथाम् Ś. 4. 1.<BR>—5 A variety of prose composition, often distinguished from आख्यायिका;<BR> (प्रबन्धकल्पनां स्तोकसत्यां प्राज्ञाः कथां विदुः । परंपराश्रया या<BR> स्यात् सा मताख्यायिका बुधैः ॥); see under आख्यायिका also.<BR>—6 (In phil.) Disputation. का कथा or कथा with प्रति (what<BR> mention) is often used in the sense of ‘what need one say of’, ‘not to mention’<BR>, ‘to say nothing of’, ‘how much more’, or ‘how much less’; का<BR> कथा बाणसंधाने ज्याशब्देनैव दूरतः । हुंकारेणेव धनुषः स हि विघ्नानपोहति<BR> Ś. 3. 1; अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43;<BR> आप्तवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं त्वां प्रति का कथा 10. 28; Ve. 2. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कथानुरागः, कथान्तरम्, कथावशेष, कथाक्रमः, कथारम्भः, कथारामः, कथालापः, कथोदयः, कथोद्घातः, कथोपकथनम्, कथोपाख्यानम्, कथाच्छलम्, कथानायकः, कथापुरुषः, कथापीठम्, कथाप्रबन्धः, कथाप्रसङ्ग, कथाप्राणः, कथामात्र, कथामुखम्, कथायोगः, कथाविपर्यासः, कथाविरक्त, कथाशेष<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानुरागः|कथानुराग
कथा + -अनुरागः taking pleasure in conversation, attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथान्तरम्
कथा + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 the course of conversation; स्मर्तव्योऽस्मि कथान्तरेषु भवता Mk. 7. 7.<BR>—2 another tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथावशेष
कथा + -अवशेष or कथाशेष <i>a.</i> one of whom only the narrative<BR> remains, <i>i. e.</i> deceased, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाक्रमः|कथाक्रम
कथा + -आक्रमः the commencement of a conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथारम्भः|कथारम्भ|कथारंभ
कथा + -आरम्भः commencement of a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथारामः|कथाराम
कथा + -आरामः garden of fable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथालापः|कथालाप
कथा + -आलापः speech, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोदयः|कथोदय
कथा + -उदयः the beginning of a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोद्घातः|कथोद्घात
कथा + -उद्घातः<BR>—1 the second of the five kinds of प्रस्तावना, where the first character<BR> enters the stage after overhearing and repeating either the words of the<BR> manager (सूत्रधार) or their sense; see S. D. 290; <i>e. g.</i> in Ratn.,<BR> Ve. or Mudrārākṣasa.<BR>—2 commencement of a tale or narration; आकुमारकथोद्घातं शालिगोप्यो<BR> जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपकथनम्
कथा + -उपकथनम्, -उपाख्यानम् narration, relation, telling a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपाख्यानम्
कथा + -उपकथनम्, -उपाख्यानम् narration, relation, telling a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाच्छलम्
कथा + -छलम्<BR>—1 the guise of a fable.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">Page0526-2</a>]<BR>—2 giving a false account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानायकः
कथा + -नायकः, -पुरुषः the hero or leading character of a story; रामायण˚ U. 4, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथापुरुषः|कथापुरुष
कथा + -नायकः, -पुरुषः the hero or leading character of a story; रामायण˚ U. 4, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथापीठम्
कथा + -पीठम्<BR>—1 the introductory part of a tale or story.<BR>—2 N. of the first लम्बक or book of the कथासरित्सागर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रबन्धः|कथाप्रबन्ध|कथाप्रबंध
कथा + -प्रबन्धः a tale, fiction, fable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसंग|कथाप्रसङ्गः
कथा + -प्रसङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 talkative, talking much and foolishly. —2 mad, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसङ्गः|कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसंग
कथा + -प्रसङ्ग + ({@-ङ्गः@})<BR>—1 conversation, talk or course of conversation; नानाकथाप्रसङ्गावस्थितः<BR> H. 1; कथाप्रसङ्गेन विवादं किल चक्रतुः Ks. 22. 181; N. 1. 35.<BR>—2 a curer of poisons (विषवैद्य); कथाप्रसङ्गो वार्तायां विषवैद्येऽपि<BR> वाच्यवत् Viśvakośa. कथाप्रसंगेन जनैरुदाहृताम् Ki. 1. 24 (where<BR> the word is used in sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्राणः|कथाप्राण
कथा + -प्राणः<BR>—1 an actor.<BR>—2 a professional story-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथामात्र
कथा + -मात्र <i>a.</i> One of whom nothing but the narrative is left; deceased,<BR> dead. कालेन ते कृताः सर्वे कथामात्राः कथासु च Bhāg. 12. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथामुखम्
कथा + -मुखम् the introductory portion of a story; Pt. 1<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथायोगः|कथायोग
कथा + -योगः course of conversation, talk, discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाविपर्यासः|कथाविपर्यास
कथा + -विपर्यासः changing the course of a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाविरक्त
कथा + -विरक्त <i>a.</i> reserved, taciturn, disliking conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाशेष
कथा + -शेष <i>a.</i> see कथावशेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानकम्
कथानकम् A small tale; <i>e. g.</i> Vetālapañcaviṃśati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथापयति
कथापयति Den. P. To tell, relate &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथिकः|कथिक
कथिकः<BR>—1 A narrator.<BR>—2 A story-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथित|कथितः
कथित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Told, described, narrated; प्रत्येकं कथिता ह्येताः Ms. 7. 157.<BR>—2 Expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितः|कथित
कथित + .{@-तः@} The supreme being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितम्
कथित + .{@-तम्@} A conversation, discourse; पूर्ववृत्तकथितैः पुराविदः R. 11. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कथितपदम्, कथितपदता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितपदम्
कथित + -पदम्, -पदता tautology, repetition, considered as a fault of<BR> composition relating to a sentence, where a word is used without any specific<BR> purpose; see K. P. 7; and S. D. 575 <i>ad hoc</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितपदता
कथित + -पदम्, -पदता tautology, repetition, considered as a fault of<BR> composition relating to a sentence, where a word is used without any specific<BR> purpose; see K. P. 7; and S. D. 575 <i>ad hoc</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथीकृ
कथीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To reduce to a tale.<BR>—2 To cause to remain only in narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथीकृत
कथीकृत <i>a.</i> Remaining in narration (only), dead, deceased; अवगम्य<BR> कथीकृतं वपुः Ku. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् <i>ind.</i> [किम्-प्रकारार्थे थमु कादेशश्च]<BR>—1 How, in what way, in what manner, whence; कथं मारात्मके त्वयि विश्वासः H. 1;<BR> अथ स वैद्यः कथम् Mu. 2 ‘well, how did the physician fare’; सानुबन्धाः<BR> कथं न स्युः संपदो मे निरापदः R. 1. 64, 3. 44; कथमात्मानं निवेदयामि<BR> कथं वाऽऽत्मापहारं करोमि Ś. 1<BR> (where the speaker is doubtful as to the propriety of what he says).<BR>—2 Oh what indeed! (expressing surprise); कथं मामेवोद्दिशति Ś. 6.<BR>—3 It is often connected with the particles इव, नाम, नु, वा, or<BR> स्वित् in the sense of, ‘how indeed’, ‘how possibly’, ‘I should like to know’<BR>, (where the question is generalized); कथं वा गम्यते U. 3;<BR> कथं नामैतत् U. 6.<BR>—4 When connected with the particles चित्, चन or अपि it means<BR> ‘in every way’, ‘on any account’, ‘somehow’, ‘with great difficulty’,<BR> ‘with great efforts’; तस्य स्थित्वा कथमपि पुरः Me. 3; कथमप्युन्नमितं<BR> न चुम्बितं तु Ś. 3. 24; न लोकवृत्तं वर्तेत वृत्तिहेतोः कथंचन<BR> Ms. 4. 11, 5. 143; कथंचिदीशा मनसां बभूवुः Ku. 3. 34; कथं कथमपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">Page0527-1</a>]<BR> उत्थितः Pt. 1; विसृज्य कथमप्युमाम् Ku. 6. 3; Me. 22; Amaru. 12, 39, 50, 73;<BR> Pt. 1.<BR>—5 Scarcely, hardly; कथमपि भुवनेऽस्मिंस्तादृशाः संभवन्ति Māl. 2. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कथङ्कथिकः, कथङ्कारम्, कथम्प्रमाण, कथम्भावः, कथम्भूत, कथंरूप, कथंवीर्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0526-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथिकः|कथङ्कथिक|कथंकथिक
कथम् + -कथिकः an inquisitive person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कारम्
कथम् + -कारम् <i>ind.</i> in what manner, how; कथंकारमनालम्बा कीर्तिर्द्यामधिरोहति<BR> Śi. 2. 52; कथंकारं भुङ्क्ते Sk.; N. 17. 126. सोऽहंकारं कथंकारं<BR> न करिष्यति मय्यरौ Śiva B. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्प्रमाण
कथम् + -प्रमाण <i>a.</i> of what measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्भावः|कथम्भाव
कथम् + -भावः what state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्भूत
कथम् + -भूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 how being.<BR>—2 of what nature or kind (oft. used by commentators).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंरूप
कथम् + -रूप <i>a.</i> of what shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंवीर्य
कथम् + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> of what power; Rām. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंता|कथन्ता
कथंता<BR>—1 What sort or manner.<BR>—2 Inquiry, question, demand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् I. €4 Ā. (कद्यते) To be confounded or confused, to suffer<BR> mentally. ━II. €1 Ā. (कदते) also €1 P.<BR>—1 To cry, to weep or shed tears.<BR>—2 To grieve.<BR>—3 To call.<BR>—4 To kill or hurt; see कन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदनम्
कदनम्<BR>—1 Slaughter, havoc, destruction; नारदाच्चैव शुश्राव वृष्णीनां कदनं<BR> महत् Mb. 1. 2. 351, 3. 178. 2; U. 5. 10.<BR>—2 War.<BR>—3 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् <i>ind.</i> [कद्-क्विप] Ved. A particle of interrogation, ‘where’.<BR> This particle which is a substitute for the word कु is often used<BR> as the first member of a comp. and expresses the senses of badness, littleness,<BR> deterioration, uselessness, defectiveness &c. of anything; नियच्छ मन्युं<BR> कददाः स्म मानः Bhāg. 7. 5. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कदक्षरम्, कदाग्निः, कदध्वन्, कदन्नम्, कदपत्यम्, कदभ्यासः, कदर्थ, कदर्थनम्, कदर्थना, कदर्थयति, कदर्थित, कदर्थीकृ, कदर्थीकृत, कदर्य, कदश्वः, कदाकार, कदाख्यम्, कदाचार, कदिन्द्रियम्, कदुष्ट्रः, कदुष्ण, कत्तृणम्, कत्तोयम्, कत्त्रि, कद्रथः, कद्वद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक्षरम्
कद् + -अक्षरम्<BR>—1 a bad letter.<BR>—2 bad writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाग्निः
कद् + -आग्निः a little fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदध्वन्
कद् + -अध्वन् a bad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन्नम्
कद् + -अन्नम् bad food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदपत्यम्
कद् + -अपत्यम् a bad child, bad posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदभ्यासः|कदभ्यास
कद् + -अभ्यासः a bad habit or custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थ|कदर्थः
कद् + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 useless, unmeaning.<BR>—2 having what purpose or aim? कदर्था न आ गृहम् Rv. 10. 22. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थः|कदर्थ
कद् + -अर्थ + ({@-र्थः@})<BR> a useless thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थनम्
कद् + -अर्थनम्, -अर्थना troubling, tormenting, torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थना
कद् + -अर्थनम्, -अर्थना troubling, tormenting, torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थयति
कद् + -अर्थयति Den. P.<BR>—1 to despise, slight.<BR>—2 to trouble, torment; रे कन्दर्प करं कदर्थयसि किं कोदण्डटङ्कारितैः<BR> Bh. 3. 100; N. 8. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थित
कद् + -अर्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 despised, disdained, slighted; कदर्थितस्यापि हि धैर्यवृत्तेर्न शक्यते<BR> धैर्यगुणः प्रमार्ष्टुम् Bh. 2. 106.<BR>—2 tormented, teased; आः कदर्थितोऽहमेभिर्वारंवारं वीरसंवादविघ्नकारिभिः U. 5.<BR>—3 insignificant, mean.<BR>—4 bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थीकृ
कद् + -अर्थीकृ €8 U. to disdain, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थीकृत
कद् + -अर्थीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 despised, disdained. क्लेशैः कदर्थीकृतवीर्यसारः Ki. 3. 47.<BR>—2 rendered useless and unavailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य|कदर्यः|कदर्य्य|कदर्य्यः
कद् + -अर्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 avaricious, miserly.<BR>—2 little, insignificant, mean.<BR>—3 bad, disagreeable; जनपदे न कदर्यो न मद्यपः Ch. Up. 5. 11. 5.<BR> निःसंशयं मया मन्ये पुरा वीरकदर्यया Rām. 2. 43. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्यः|कदर्य|कदर्य्य|कदर्य्यः
कद् + -अर्य + ({@-र्यः@})<BR> a miser; Bhāg. 11. 23. 6; Ms. 4. 210, 224; Y. 1. 161. ˚ता, त्वम्<BR>—1 avarice.<BR>—2 insignificance.<BR>—3 badness. ˚भावः avarice, stinginess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदश्वः|कदश्व
कद् + -अश्वः a bad horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाकार|कदाकारः
कद् + -आकार <i>a.</i> deformed, ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाख्यम्
कद् + -आख्यम् A medicinal plant (कुष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचार|कदाचारः
कद् + -आचार <i>a.</i> following evil practices, wicked, depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचारः|कदाचार
कद् + -आचार + ({@-रः@}) bad conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदिन्द्रियम्
कद् + -इन्द्रियम् a bad organ of sense; कदिन्द्रियाणामनवाप्यवर्त्मने<BR> Bhāg. 8. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदुष्ट्रः|कदुष्ट्र
कद् + -उष्ट्रः a bad camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदुष्ण|कदुष्णं
कद् + -उष्ण (also कोष्ण) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 tepid, lukewarm; श्वसन् कदुष्णं पुरमाविवेश Bk. 3. 17.<BR>—2 Harsh, sharp (as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">Page0527-2</a>]<BR> word); प्रियोक्तिरप्याह कदुष्णमक्षरम् N. 9. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदुष्णम्
कद् + -उष्ण + .({@-ष्णम्@}) lukewarmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तृणम्
कद् + -तृणम्<BR>—1 a fragrant grass.<BR>—2 the plant कुम्भिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तोयम्
कद् + -तोयम् an intoxicating drink, wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्त्रि
कद् + -त्रि <i>m.</i> (pl.) three inferior articles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रथः|कद्रथ
कद् + -रथः a bad chariot or carriage; युधि कद्रथवद्भीमं बभञ्ज<BR> ध्वजशालिनम् Bk. 5. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वद|कद्वदः
कद् + -वद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 speaking ill or inaccurately or indistinctly; येन जातं प्रियापाये<BR> कद्वदं हंसकोकिलम् Bk. 6. 75; वाग्विदां वरमकद्वदो नृपः Śi. 14. 1.<BR>—2 vile, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Giving water.<BR>—2 Giving happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदः|कद
कद + .{@-दः@} A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदकम्
कदकम् A canopy, awning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदनम्
कदनम् See under कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बः|कदम्ब|कदंब|कदम्बं|कदंबः
कदम्बः, -कदम्बकः<BR> [कद् करणे अम्बच् Tv.]<BR>—1 A kind of tree [Stephegyne Parviflora Korth] (said to put forth buds<BR> at the roaring of thunder-clouds); कतिपयकुसुमोद्गमः कदम्बः U. 3. 20, 42;<BR> Māl. 3. 7; Me. 25; R. 12. 99; मुक्त्वा कदम्ब-कुटजार्जुन-सर्ज-नीपान्<BR> Ṛs. 3. 13. The tree is common throughout India except in Konkan. Its<BR> fruit is hard and inedible.<BR>—2 A kind of grass.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR>—4 The mustard-seed plant.<BR>—5 A particular mineral substance.<BR>—6 Dust.<BR>—7 Fragrance; cf. कदम्बः पुंसि नीपे स्यात्तिनिशे वरुणद्रुमे । धूल्यां<BR> समूहे गन्धे च … Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बकः|कदम्बक|कदंबक|कदम्बकं|कदंबकः
कदम्बः, -कदम्बकः<BR> [कद् करणे अम्बच् Tv.]<BR>—1 A kind of tree [Stephegyne Parviflora Korth] (said to put forth buds<BR> at the roaring of thunder-clouds); कतिपयकुसुमोद्गमः कदम्बः U. 3. 20, 42;<BR> Māl. 3. 7; Me. 25; R. 12. 99; मुक्त्वा कदम्ब-कुटजार्जुन-सर्ज-नीपान्<BR> Ṛs. 3. 13. The tree is common throughout India except in Konkan. Its<BR> fruit is hard and inedible.<BR>—2 A kind of grass.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR>—4 The mustard-seed plant.<BR>—5 A particular mineral substance.<BR>—6 Dust.<BR>—7 Fragrance; cf. कदम्बः पुंसि नीपे स्यात्तिनिशे वरुणद्रुमे । धूल्यां<BR> समूहे गन्धे च … Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बी
कदम्बः, -कदम्बकः + .{@-म्बी@} N. of a plant (देवदाली). Ś. 6; U. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बम्
कदम्बः, -कदम्बकः + .{@-म्बम्@} A multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बकम्
कदम्बः, -कदम्बकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A multitude, group; छायाबद्धकदम्बकं मृगकुलं रोमन्थमभ्यस्यतु Ś. 2. 6.<BR>—2 The flower of the Kadamba tree; पृथुकदम्बकदम्बकराजितम् Ki. 5. 9.<BR>—3 A kind of grass (देवताड).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कदम्बानिलः, कदम्बकोरकन्यायः, कदम्बपुष्पा, कदम्बपुष्पी, कदम्बभ्रममण्डलम्, कदम्बयुद्धम्, कदम्बवायुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बानिलः|कदम्बानिल|कदंबानिल
कदम्बः + -अनिलः<BR>—1 a fragrant breeze (charged with the odour of Kadamba flowers); ते<BR> चोन्मीलितमालतीसुरभयः प्रौढाः कदम्बानिलाः K. P. 1.<BR>—2 Autumn (वर्षर्तु); इदं कदम्बानिलभर्तुरत्यये Ki. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बकोरकन्यायः|कदम्बकोरकन्याय|कदंबकोरकन्याय
कदम्बः + -कोरकन्यायः see under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बपुष्पा
कदम्बः + -पुष्पा, -पुष्पी a plant the flowers of which resemble those of Kadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बपुष्पी
कदम्बः + -पुष्पा, -पुष्पी a plant the flowers of which resemble those of Kadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बभ्रममण्डलम्
कदम्बः + -भ्रममण्डलम् (in Astro.) The polar circle of the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बयुद्धम्
कदम्बः + -युद्धम् A kind of amorous play; Vātsyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बवायुः|कदम्बवायु|कदंबवायु
कदम्बः + -वायुः a fragrant breeze; = ˚अनिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बदः|कदम्बद|कदंबदः
कदम्बदः The mustard seed plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदरः|कदर|कदरं
कदरः<BR>—1 A saw.<BR>—2 An iron goad for driving an elephant.<BR>—3 N. of a tree sometimes substituted for Khadira as a sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदरः|कदर|कदरं
कदरः + .{@-रः, -रम्@} A corn, a callosity of the feet caused by external friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदरम्
कदरः + .{@-रः, -रम्@} A corn, a callosity of the feet caused by external friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदरम्
कदरः + .{@-रम्@} coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलः|कदल
कदलः, -कदलकः<BR> The plantain tree; ऊरुद्वयं मृगदृशः कदलस्य<BR> काण्डौ Amaru. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलकः|कदलक
कदलः, -कदलकः<BR> The plantain tree; ऊरुद्वयं मृगदृशः कदलस्य<BR> काण्डौ Amaru. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदला
कदलः, -कदलकः + .{@-ला@} N. of several plants:− पृश्नि, डिम्बिका, and शाल्मलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदली
कदलः, -कदलकः + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 The plantain tree; किं यासि बालकदलीव विकम्पमाना Mk. 1. 20;<BR> यास्यत्यूरुः सरसकदलीस्तम्भगौरश्चलत्वम् Me. 98, 79; Ku. 1. 36;<BR> R. 12. 96; Y. 3. 8.<BR>—2 A kind of deer.<BR>—3 A flag carried by an elephant.<BR>—4 A flag or banner; कदली वैजयन्त्यां च रम्भायां च मृगेऽपि च Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कदलीकुसुमम्, कदलीक्षता, कदलीगर्भः, कदलदण्डः, कदलस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीकुसुमम्
कदलः + कदलीकुसुमम् the flower of the कदली plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीक्षता
कदलः + कदलीक्षता<BR>—1 A sort of cucumber (Mar. पडवळ).<BR>—2 A fine woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीगर्भः|कदलीगर्भ
कदलः + कदलीगर्भः the pith of the plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलदण्डः
कदलः + -दण्डः, -स्कन्धः a kind of illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलस्कन्धः
कदलः + -दण्डः, -स्कन्धः a kind of illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0527-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलिका
कदलिका<BR>—1 A banner, flag; Māl. 6.<BR>—2 Kadala tree; अभ्युल्लसत्कदलिकावनराजिम् Śi. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलिन्
कदलिन् <i>m.</i> A kind of antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीक्षता
कदलीक्षता<BR>—1 A sort of cucumber.<BR>—2 A beautiful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदा
कदा <i>ind.</i> When, at what time; कदा गमिष्यसि-एष गच्छामि; कदा<BR> कथयिष्यसि &c.; when connected with a following अपि it means ‘now and then’<BR>, ‘at times’, ‘sometimes’, ‘at some time’; न कदापि never;<BR> with a following चन it means ‘at some time’, ‘one day’, ‘at one time or another’<BR>, ‘once’; आनन्दं ब्रह्मणो विद्वान्न बिभेति कदाचन;<BR> Ms. 2. 54, 144, 3. 25, 101; with a following चित् it means ‘at one time’<BR>, ‘once upon a time’, ‘at some time or other’; अथ कदाचित् once<BR> upon a time; R. 2. 37, 12. 21; नाक्षैः क्रीडेत्कदाचित्तु Ms. 4. 74, 65, 169;<BR> कदाचित्-कदाचित् ‘now-now’; कदाचित् काननं जगाहे कदाचित् कमलवनेषु<BR> रेमे K. 58 <i>et seq.</i> [cf. L. <i>quando</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रु|कद्रुः
कद्रु <i>a.</i> [कद्-रु] (द्रु or द्रू <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Tawny.<BR>—2 Variegated, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुः|कद्रु
कद्रु + .{@-द्रुः@}<BR>—1 The tawny colour.<BR>—2 The variegated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुः|कद्रु
कद्रु + .{@-द्रुः, -द्रूः@} <i>f.</i> Wife of Kaśyapa and the mother of the Nāgas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कद्रुपुत्रः, कद्रुसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रूः
कद्रु + .{@-द्रुः, -द्रूः@} <i>f.</i> Wife of Kaśyapa and the mother of the Nāgas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कद्रुपुत्रः, कद्रुसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुपुत्रः|कद्रुपुत्र
कद्रु + -पुत्रः, -सुतः a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुसुतः|कद्रुसुत
कद्रु + -पुत्रः, -सुतः a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुण
कद्रुण <i>a.</i> Reddish-brown, tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वरम्
कद्वरम्<BR>—1 Whey.<BR>—2 Buttermilk mixed with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कधप्रिय
कधप्रिय, -कधप्री <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Fond of praise; कस्त उषः कधप्रिये Rv. 1. 30. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कधप्री
कधप्रिय, -कधप्री <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Fond of praise; कस्त उषः कधप्रिये Rv. 1. 30. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्
कन् €1 P. Ved. (कनति, कन्तुम्)<BR>—1 To be satisfied or contented; भूयसा वस्तमचरत् कनीयो Rv. 4. 24. 9.<BR>—2 To love, wish.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR>—4 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकम्
कनकम् Gold; कनकवलयं स्रस्तं स्रस्तं मया प्रतिसार्यते<BR> Ś. 3. 12; Me. 2, 39, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकः|कनक|कनकं
कनकम् + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The Palāśa tree.<BR>—2 The Dhattūra tree (several other plants as गुग्गुळ, चन्दन, चम्पक &c.)<BR>—3 Mountain ebony.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कनकाङ्गदम्, कनकाचलः, कनकाद्रिः, कनकगिरिः, कनकशैलः, कनकाध्यक्षः, कनकाह्वः, कनकालुका, कनकाह्वयः, कनककदली, कनककारः, कनकक्षारः, कनकटङ्कः, कनकदण्डम्, कनकदण्डकम्, कनकदण्डिका, कनकनिकषः, कनकपट्टम्, कनकपत्रम्, कनकपरागः, कनकपर्वतः, कनकपलः, कनकप्रभ, कनकप्रसवा, कनकभङ्गः, कनकरम्भा, कनकरसः, कनकशक्तिः, कनकसूत्रम्, कनकस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाङ्गदम्
कनकम् + -अङ्गदम् a gold bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाचलः|कनकाचल
कनकम् + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -शैलः epithets of the mountain Sumeru;<BR> अधुना कुचौ ते स्पर्धेते किल कनकाचलेन सार्धम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाद्रिः|कनकाद्रि
कनकम् + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -शैलः epithets of the mountain Sumeru;<BR> अधुना कुचौ ते स्पर्धेते किल कनकाचलेन सार्धम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकगिरिः|कनकगिरि
कनकम् + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -शैलः epithets of the mountain Sumeru;<BR> अधुना कुचौ ते स्पर्धेते किल कनकाचलेन सार्धम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकशैलः
कनकम् + -अचलः, -अद्रिः, -गिरिः, -शैलः epithets of the mountain Sumeru;<BR> अधुना कुचौ ते स्पर्धेते किल कनकाचलेन सार्धम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाध्यक्षः|कनकाध्यक्ष
कनकम् + -अध्यक्षः the treasurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाह्वः|कनकाह्व|कनकाह्वं
कनकम् + -आह्वः the धत्तूर tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0528-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

