करटः|करट
करटः [किरति मदं, कॄ-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81.]<BR>—1 An elephantʼs cheek; प्रभिन्नकरटौ मत्तौ भूत्वा कुञ्जररूपिणौ Mb. 1. 210. 20.<BR>—2 Safflower.<BR>—3 A crow; Śānti. 4. 19.<BR>—4 An atheist, unbeliever.<BR>—5 A degraded Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—6 A man of a low profession.<BR>—7 A musical instrument.<BR>—8 The first Śrāddha ceremony performed in honour of a dead man; करट<BR> त्वं रट कस्तवापराधः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0535-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटम्
करटः + .{@-टम्@} Hard. (a variety of coral); Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0535-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटा
करटः + .{@-टा@}<BR>—1 An elephantʼs cheek.<BR>—2 A cow difficult to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0535-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटमुखम्
