कर्णलतिका
कर्ण + -लता, -लतिका the lobe of the ear; मन्येऽमुना कर्णलतामयेन N. 7. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवंशः|कर्णवंश|कर्ण्णवंश
कर्ण + -वंशः a raised platform or <i>dais</i> of bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवर्जित|कर्णवर्जितः|कर्णवर्ज्जितः|कर्ण्णवर्ज्जित
कर्ण + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> earless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवर्जितः|कर्णवर्जित|कर्णवर्ज्जितः|कर्ण्णवर्ज्जित
कर्ण + -वर्जित + .({@-तः@}) a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविवरम्
कर्ण + -विवरम्, -छिद्रम्, -पुरम्, -रन्ध्रम् the auditory passage of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णच्छिद्रम्
कर्ण + -विवरम्, -छिद्रम्, -पुरम्, -रन्ध्रम् the auditory passage of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपुरम्
कर्ण + -विवरम्, -छिद्रम्, -पुरम्, -रन्ध्रम् the auditory passage of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णरन्ध्रम्
कर्ण + -विवरम्, -छिद्रम्, -पुरम्, -रन्ध्रम् the auditory passage of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविष्|कर्ण्णविष्
कर्ण + -विष् <i>f.</i> ear-wax; Ms. 5. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविषम्
कर्ण + -विषम् ‘poisoning the ear’, slandering, back-biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधः|कर्णवेध|कर्ण्णवेध
कर्ण + -वेधः piercing the ears to put ear-rings on; a religious ceremony<BR> (संस्कार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनी
कर्ण + -वेधनी, -वेधनिका an instrument for piercing the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनिका
कर्ण + -वेधनी, -वेधनिका an instrument for piercing the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टः|कर्णवेष्ट|कर्ण्णवेष्ट
कर्ण + -वेष्टः, -वेष्टनम् an ear-ring; सुकृतौ कर्णवेष्टौ च Rām. 5. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टनम्
कर्ण + -वेष्टः, -वेष्टनम् an ear-ring; सुकृतौ कर्णवेष्टौ च Rām. 5. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशष्कुली|कर्ण्णशष्कुली
कर्ण + -शष्कुली the outer part of the ear (leading to the auditory passage);<BR> Av. 9. 8. 1. अवलम्बितकर्णशष्कुलीकलसीकं रचयन्नवोचत N. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशूलः|कर्णशूल|कर्ण्णशूल
कर्ण + -शूलः, -लम् ear-ache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णलम्
कर्ण + -शूलः, -लम् ear-ache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णश्रव|कर्ण्णश्रव
कर्ण + -श्रव <i>a.</i> audible, loud; कर्णश्रवेऽनिले Ms. 4. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णश्रावः|कर्णश्राव
कर्ण + -श्रावः, -संश्रवः ‘running of the ear’, discharge of pus or<BR> ichorous matter from the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसंश्रवः|कर्णसंश्रव
कर्ण + -श्रावः, -संश्रवः ‘running of the ear’, discharge of pus or<BR> ichorous matter from the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसूः
कर्ण + -सूः <i>f.</i> Kuntī, mother of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णस्रोतस्|कर्ण्णस्रोतस्
कर्ण + -स्रोतस् <i>n.</i> excretion of the ear (कर्णमल) कर्णस्रोतोभवं<BR> चापि मधुं नाम महासुरम् Mb. 6. 67. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णहर्म्यम्
कर्ण + -हर्म्यम् a tower, a side-tower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णहीन|कर्णहीनः|कर्ण्णहीन
कर्ण + -हीन <i>a.</i> earless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णहीनः|कर्णहीन|कर्ण्णहीन
कर्ण + -हीन + ({@-नः@}) a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकः|कर्णक
कर्णकः Ved.<BR>—1 A prominence; handle.<BR>—2 The leaves and branches &c. of trees.<BR>—3 A tendril.<BR>—4 White hair; तं त्वां पुनः पलितकर्णकभाजमेनम् Bh. 3. 126.<BR>—5 A kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णल|कर्णलः|कर्ण्णल
कर्णल^1 <i>a.</i> Having ears.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवत्|कर्णवन्त्
कर्णवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having ears; अक्षण्वन्तः कर्णवन्तः सखायो Rv. 10. 71. 7.<BR>—2 Long-eared.<BR>—3 Having tendrils or hooks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाकर्णि
कर्णाकर्णि <i>ind.</i> From ear to ear. कर्णाकर्णि हि कपयः कथयन्ति<BR> चलत्कथाम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिक|कर्णिकः
कर्णिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having ears.<BR>—2 Having a helm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकः|कर्णिक
कर्णिक + .{@-कः@} A steersman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिका|कर्ण्णिका
कर्णिक + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 An ear-ring; रत्नरञ्जितकर्णिकाम् Śiva B. 20. 5; वदनेनाकुलकर्णिकोज्ज्वलेन Bu. C. 5. 55.<BR>—2 A knot, round protuberance.<BR>—3 Pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—4 A small brush or pen.<BR>—5 The middle finger.<BR>—6 A fruit-stalk.<BR>—7 The tip of an elephantʼs trunk.<BR>—8 Chalk.<BR>—9 A trowel. —10 A bawd.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्णिकाचलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकाचलः|कर्णिकाचल|कर्ण्णिकाचल
कर्णिक + -अचलः N. of the mountain सुमेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिन्
कर्णिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having ears; Av. 10. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Long-eared.<BR>—3 Barbed (as an arrow). ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An ass.<BR>—2 A helmsman.<BR>—3 An arrow furnished with knots &c.<BR>—4 A disease of the uterus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0539-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकिन्
कर्णिकिन् <i>m.</i> An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिल
कर्णिल <i>a.</i> Long-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णालवाद्यम्
कर्णालवाद्यम् A semi-circular ear-like wind-instrument; तूर्णं<BR> कर्णालवाद्यस्य शब्दं चक्रुः समन्ततः Parṇāl. 3. 33, 5. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाटः|कर्णाट
कर्णाटः, कर्णाटकः (pl.) N. of a country in the south of<BR> the Indian Peninsula; (काव्यम्) कर्णाटेन्दोर्जगति विदुषां कण्ठभूषत्वमेतु Vikr. 18. 102<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाटकः|कर्णाटक
कर्णाटः, कर्णाटकः (pl.) N. of a country in the south of<BR> the Indian Peninsula; (काव्यम्) कर्णाटेन्दोर्जगति विदुषां कण्ठभूषत्वमेतु Vikr. 18. 102<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाटी
कर्णाटः, कर्णाटकः + .{@-टी@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A woman of the above country; कर्णाटीचीनपीनस्तनवसनदशादोलनस्पन्दमन्दः<BR> Udb. कर्णाटीचिकुराणां ताण्डवकरः Vb. 1. 29.<BR>—2 The हंसपदी plant.<BR>—3 One of the Rāgiṇīs or musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकारः|कर्णिकार|कर्ण्णिकार
कर्णिकारः<BR>—1 N. of a tree; Cassia fistula. The golden yellow flower of this tree<BR> has its petals bending inwards so that the flower looks like a saucer.<BR> Its stamens and style are longer than the petals and looks like so many<BR> wicks jutting^1 out of an oil lamp. cf. Vikr. 3. 3. निर्भिद्योपरि<BR> कर्णिकारमुकुलान्यालीयते षट्पदः V. 2. 23; Ṛs. 6. 6, 20.<BR>—2 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकारम्
कर्णिकारः + .{@-रम्@} A flower of the Karṇikāra tree. (This flower, though it<BR> has an excellent colour, has no smell and hence it is not liked; cf. Ku. 3. 28;<BR> वर्णप्रकर्षे सति कर्णिकारं दुनोति निर्गन्धतया स्म चेतः ।<BR> प्रायेण सामग्र्यविधौ गुणानां पराङ्मुखी विश्वसृजः प्रवृत्तिः ॥).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्णिकारप्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकारप्रियः|कर्णिकारप्रिय
कर्णिकारः + -प्रियः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णी
कर्णी<BR>—1 An arrow of a particular shape (barbed arrow).<BR>—2 N. of the mother of Mūladeva, the father of the science and art of thieving.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्णीरथः, कर्णीसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीरथः|कर्णीरथ|कर्ण्णीरथ
कर्णी + -रथः a covered litter; a ladyʼs vehicle, palanquin; कर्णीरथस्थां<BR> रघुवीरपत्नीम् R. 14. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीसुतः|कर्णीसुत|कर्ण्णीसुत
कर्णी + -सुतः Mūladeva, father of the science and art of thieving; कर्णीसुतकथेव<BR> संनिहितविपुलाचला K. 19; कर्णीसुतप्रहिते च पथि मतिमकरवम् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेचुरचुरा|कर्ण्णेचुरचुरा
कर्णेचुरचुरा <i>f.</i> A secret whispering in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेजपः|कर्णेजप
कर्णेजपः [कर्णे-जप्-अच् अलुक् समास; cf. P. III. 2. 13.] A secret<BR> tale-bearer, An informer (Mar. कानाशीं लागणारा); पुरा कर्णेजपीभूय<BR> पुनः पुनरुपेयुषा Śiva B. 23. 37. कर्णेजपैराहितराज्यलोभा Bk. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेटिरिटिरा
कर्णेटिरिटिरा^1 <i>f.</i> (cf. कर्णेचुरचुरा above)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260405. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/125#issuecomment-4183819710. note: wa-wi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्|कर्त्त्
कर्त् €10 P. (कर्तयति-कर्तित)<BR>—1 To slacken, unloose.<BR>—2 To remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त|कर्तः|कर्त्त|कर्त्तः
कर्त <i>a.</i> Ved. Cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तः|कर्त|कर्त्त|कर्त्तः
कर्त + .{@-र्तः@}<BR>—1 A hole, cavity; यदि कर्तं पतित्वा संशश्रे Av. 4. 12. 7.<BR>—2 Rending, tearing; गतो मुकुन्दं परिहृत्य कर्तम् Bhāg. 11. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तक
कर्तक <i>a.</i> (A pearl) having scratches. Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तन|कर्त्तन|कर्त्तनं
