कर्फरः A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब्
कर्ब् €1 P. (कर्बति) To go, move, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बु
कर्बु <i>a.</i> Variegated, spotted; कर्बुरूपाः (नीलाः) Y. 3. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुर|कर्बुरः|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बु(र्वु)र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Variegated, or spotted; क्वचिल्लसद्घननिकुरम्बकर्बुरः Śi. 17. 56.<BR>—2 Of the colour of pigeons, whitish, grey; पवनैर्भस्म कपोतकर्बुरम् Ku. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वुर|कर्व्वुरः
कर्बु(र्वु)र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Variegated, or spotted; क्वचिल्लसद्घननिकुरम्बकर्बुरः Śi. 17. 56.<BR>—2 Of the colour of pigeons, whitish, grey; पवनैर्भस्म कपोतकर्बुरम् Ku. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरः|कर्बुर|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बु(र्वु)र + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The variegated colour.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>—3 An evil spirit, demon.<BR>—4 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>—5 Rice growing amidst inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरा|कर्ब्बुरा
कर्बु(र्वु)र + .{@-रा@} N. of a plant (वर्वरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरी|कर्ब्बुरी
कर्बु(र्वु)र + .{@-री@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरम्
कर्बु(र्वु)र + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Gold.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 The Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरित
कर्बु(र्वु)रित <i>a.</i> Variegated; अवदग्धकर्बुरितकेतुचामरैः<BR> U. 6. 4; Śi. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वुरित
कर्बु(र्वु)रित <i>a.</i> Variegated; अवदग्धकर्बुरितकेतुचामरैः<BR> U. 6. 4; Śi. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूर|कर्बूरः|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बू(र्वू)र <i>a.</i> Variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वूर|कर्व्वूरः
कर्बू(र्वू)र <i>a.</i> Variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरः|कर्बूर|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बू(र्वू)र + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A demon.<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR>—3 The variegated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरा
कर्बू(र्वू)र + .{@-रा@} A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरम्
कर्बू(र्वू)र + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Gold.<BR>—2 Yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्|कर्म्मन्
कर्मन् <i>m.</i> Viśvakarmā; शकस्य नु सभा दिव्या भास्वरा कर्मनिर्मिता<BR> Mb. 2. 7. 1. ━<i>n.</i> [कृ-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 144]<BR>—1 Action, work, deed.<BR>—2 Execution, performance; प्रीतोऽस्मि सोऽहं यद् भुक्तं वनं तैः कृतकर्मभिः<BR> Rām. 5. 63. 30.<BR>—3 Business, office, duty; संप्रति विषवैद्यानां कर्म M. 4.<BR>—4 A religious rite (it may be either नित्य, नैमित्तिक or काम्य).<BR>—5 A specific action, moral duty.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Performance of religious rites as opposed to speculative religion<BR> or knowledge of Brahman (opp. ज्ञान); अपरो दहने स्वकर्मणां ववृते R. 8. 20.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Labour, work.<BR>—7 Product, result.<BR>—8 A natural or active property (as support of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">Page0541-2</a>]<BR> earth).<BR>—9 Fate, the certain consequence of acts done in a former life; कर्मायत्तं<BR> फलं पुंसां बुद्धिः कर्मानुसारिणी Bh. 2. 89, 94.<BR>—10 (In gram.) The object of of an action; कर्तुरीप्सिततमं कर्म P. I. 4. 49.<BR>—11 (In Vaiś. Phil.) Motion considered as one of the seven categories<BR> of things; thus defined:− एकद्रव्यमगुणं संयोगविभागेष्वनपेक्षकारणं<BR> कर्म Vaiś. Sūtra. (It is five-fold:− उत्क्षेपणं ततोऽवक्षेपणमाकुञ्चनं<BR> तथा । प्रसारणं च गमनं कर्माण्येतानि पञ्च च ॥ Bhāṣā P. 6.)<BR>—12 Organ of sense. प्रजापतिर्ह कर्माणि ससृजे Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 21.<BR>—13 Organ of action; कर्माणि कर्मभिः कुर्वन् Bhāg. 11. 3. 6.<BR>—14 (In Astr.) The tenth lunar mansion. —15 Practice, training; सर्वेषां<BR> कर्मणा वीर्यं जवस्तेजश्च वर्धते Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्माक्षम, कर्माङ्गम्, कर्माधिकारः, कर्मानुरूप, कर्मानुष्ठानम्, कर्मानुसारः, कर्मान्तः, कर्मान्तरम्, कर्मान्तिक, कर्मापनुत्तिः, कर्मार्ह, कर्माख्या, कर्माजीवः, कर्मात्मन्, कर्मायतनम्, कर्माशयः, कर्मेन्द्रियम्, कर्मोदारम्, कर्मोद्युक्त, कर्मकरः, कर्मकर्तृ, कर्मकाण्डः, कर्मकाण्डम्, कर्मकारः, कर्मकारिन्, कर्मकार्मुकः, कर्मकम्, कर्मकीलकः, कर्मकृत्यम्, कर्मक्षम, कर्मक्षेत्रम्, कर्मगतिः, कर्मगृहीत, कर्मग्रन्थिः, कर्मघातः, कर्मचण्डालः, कर्मचाण्डालः, कर्मचेष्टा, कर्मचोदना, कर्मच्छेदः, कर्मज,^1 कर्मज्ञ, कर्मत्यागः, कर्मदुष्ट, कर्मदेवः, कर्मदोषः, कर्मधारयः, कर्मध्वंसः, कर्मनामन्, कर्मनामधेयम्, कर्मनाशा, कर्मनिश्चयः, कर्मनिषद्या, कर्मनिष्ठ, कर्मन्यासः, कर्मपथः, कर्मपाकः, कर्मप्रवचनीयः, कर्मफलम्, कर्मबन्धः, कर्मबन्धनम्, कर्मभूः, कर्मभूमिः, कर्ममासः, कर्ममीमांसा, कर्ममूलम्, कर्मयुगम्, कर्मयोगः, कर्मवचनम्, कर्मवज्रः, कर्मवशः, कर्मवाटी, कर्मविपाक, कर्मशाला, कर्मशील, कर्मशूर, कर्मशौचम्, कर्मश्रुतिः, कर्मसङ्गः, कर्मसचिवः, कर्मसंन्यासिकः, कर्मसंन्यासिन्, कर्मसाक्षिन्, कर्मसिद्धिः, कर्मस्थानम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माक्षम
कर्मन् + -अक्षम <i>a.</i> incapable of doing anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माङ्गम्
कर्मन् + -अङ्गम् part of any act; part of a sacrificial rite (as प्रयाज<BR> of the Darśa sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माधिकारः|कर्माधिकार
कर्मन् + -अधिकारः the right of performing religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मानुरूप|कर्म्मानुरूप
कर्मन् + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i> —1 according to action or any particular office.<BR>—2 according to actions done in a previous existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मानुष्ठानम्
कर्मन् + -अनुष्ठानम् practising oneʼs duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मानुसारः|कर्मानुसार|कर्म्मानुसार
कर्मन् + -अनुसारः consequence of, or conformity to, acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तः|कर्मान्त|कर्मांत|कर्म्मान्त|कर्म्मान्तः
कर्मन् + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the end of any business or task.<BR>—2 a work, business, execution of business.<BR>—3 a barn, a store of grain &c. Ms. 7. 62 (कर्मान्तः इक्षुधान्यादिसंग्रहस्थानम् Kull.)<BR>—4 cultivated ground.<BR>—5 a worker; कच्चिन्न सर्वे कर्मान्ताः Rām. 2. 100. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तरम्
कर्मन् + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 difference or contrariety of action.<BR>—2 penance, expiation.<BR>—3 suspension of a religious action.<BR>—4 another work or action; कर्मान्तरनियुक्तासु निर्ममन्थ स्वयं दधि<BR> Bhāg. 10. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तिक|कर्मांतिक|कर्मान्तिकः|कर्म्मान्तिक
कर्मन् + -अन्तिक <i>a.</i> final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मान्तिकः|कर्मान्तिक|कर्मांतिक|कर्म्मान्तिक
कर्मन् + -अन्तिक + ({@-कः@}) a servant, workman, Rām. 1. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मापनुत्तिः
कर्मन् + -अपनुत्तिः <i>f.</i> removing, sending away of कर्म; जन्म कर्मापनुत्तये<BR> Bhāg. 12. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मार्ह|कर्मार्हः|कर्म्मार्ह|कर्म्मार्हः
कर्मन् + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> fit or suitable to an act or the rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मार्हः|कर्मार्ह|कर्म्मार्ह|कर्म्मार्हः
कर्मन् + -अर्ह + .({@-र्हः@}) a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माख्या
कर्मन् + -आख्या <i>f.</i> Name received from the act performed; तस्मात् छिन्नगमनोऽश्वोऽपि<BR> छाग इति कर्माख्या भविष्यति । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माजीवः|कर्माजीव|कर्म्माजीव
कर्मन् + -आजीवः one who maintains himself by some profession (as that<BR> of an artisan &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मात्मन्|कर्म्मात्मन्
कर्मन् + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> endowed with the principles of action, active; कर्मात्मनां<BR> च देवानां सोऽसृजत्प्राणिनां प्रभुः Ms. 1. 22. ━(<i>m.</i>) the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मायतनम्
कर्मन् + -आयतनम् see कर्मेन्द्रियम्; शब्दः स्पर्शो रसो गन्धो रूपं चेत्यर्थजातयः ।<BR> गत्युक्त्युत्सर्गशिल्पानि कर्मायतनसिद्धयः Bhāg. 11. 22. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्माशयः|कर्माशय|कर्म्माशय
कर्मन् + -आशयः receptacle or accumulation of (good and evil) acts; निर्हृत्य<BR> कर्माशयमाशु याति परां गतिम् Bhāg. 10. 46. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मेन्द्रियम्
कर्मन् + -इन्द्रियम् an organ of action, as distinguished from ज्ञानेन्द्रिय;<BR> (they are:− वाक्पाणिपादपायूपस्थानि; Ms. 2. 99; see under इन्द्रिय<BR> also) कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य Bg. 3. 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मोदारम्
कर्मन् + -उदारम् any valiant or noble act, magnanimity, prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मोद्युक्त|कर्म्मोद्युक्त
कर्मन् + -उद्युक्त <i>a.</i> busy, engaged, active, zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकरः|कर्मकर|कर्म्मकर|कर्म्मकरः
कर्मन् + -करः<BR>—1 a hired labourer (a servant who is not a slave); आ तस्य गोः प्रतिदानात्<BR> कर्मकारी आगवीनः कर्मकरः Mbh. on P. V. 2. 14. कर्मकराः स्थपत्यादयः<BR> Pt. 1; Śi. 14. 16.<BR>—2 Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकर्तृ|कर्म्मकर्त्तृ
कर्मन् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> (in gram.) an agent who is at the same time the<BR> object of the action; <i>e. g.</i> पच्यते ओदनः, it is thus defined:−<BR> क्रियमाणं तु यत्कर्म स्वयमेव प्रसिध्यति । सुकरैः स्वैर्गुणैः कर्तुः<BR> कर्मकर्तेति तद्विदुः ॥ न चान्तरेण कर्मकर्तारं सकर्मका अकर्मका<BR> भवन्ति Mbh. on P. I. 3. 27<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकाण्डः|कर्मकाण्ड|कर्मकांड|कर्म्मकाण्ड
कर्मन् + -काण्डः, -काण्डम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">Page0542-1</a>]<BR> that department of the Veda which relates to ceremonial<BR> acts and sacrificial rites and the merit arising from a due performance thereof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकाण्डम्
कर्मन् + -काण्डः, -काण्डम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">Page0542-1</a>]<BR> that department of the Veda which relates to ceremonial<BR> acts and sacrificial rites and the merit arising from a due performance thereof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकारः|कर्मकार|कर्म्मकार|कर्म्मकारः
कर्मन् + -कारः<BR>—1 one who does any business, a mechanic, artisan (technically a worker not hired).<BR>—2 any labourer in general (whether hired or not).<BR>—3 a black-smith; हरिणाक्षि कटाक्षेण आत्मानमवलोकय । न हि खड्गो<BR> विजानाति कर्मकारं स्वकारणम् ॥ Udb.<BR>—4 a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकारिन्|कर्म्मकारिन्
कर्मन् + -कारिन् <i>m.</i> a labourer, artisan, workman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकार्मुकः|कर्मकार्मुक|कर्म्मकार्म्मुक
कर्मन् + -कार्मुकः, -कम् a strong bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकम्
कर्मन् + -कार्मुकः, -कम् a strong bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकीलकः|कर्मकीलक|कर्म्मकीलक|कर्म्मकीलकः
कर्मन् + -कीलकः a washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मकृत्यम्
कर्मन् + -कृत्यम् activity, the state of active exertion; यः प्रथमः<BR> कर्मकृत्याय जज्ञे Av. 4. 24. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मक्षम|कर्म्मक्षम|कर्म्मक्षमः
कर्मन् + -क्षम <i>a.</i> able to perform any work or duty; आत्मकर्मक्षमं<BR> देहं क्षात्रो धर्म इवाश्रितः R. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मक्षेत्रम्
कर्मन् + -क्षेत्रम् the land of religious acts, <i>i. e.</i> भरतवर्ष;<BR> Bhāg. 5. 17. 11; cf. कर्मभूमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मगतिः|कर्मगति
कर्मन् + -गतिः <i>f.</i> the course of fate; अथ कर्मगतिं चित्रां दृष्ट्वाऽस्य<BR> हसितं मया Ks. 59. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मगृहीत
कर्मन् + -गृहीत <i>a.</i> caught in the very act (as a thief.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मग्रन्थिः
कर्मन् + -ग्रन्थिः <i>f.</i> a term in Jaina metaphysics connoting ‘weakness in the form of वासनाs produced by अज्ञान’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मघातः|कर्मघात
कर्मन् + -घातः leaving off or suspending work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मचण्डालः|कर्मचण्डाल|कर्मचंडाल|कर्म्मचण्डाल
कर्मन् + -चण्डालः, -चाण्डालः<BR>—1 ‘base in deed’, a man of very low acts or deeds; Vasiṣṭha mentions<BR> these kinds:− असूयकः पिशुनश्च कृतघ्नो दीर्घरोषकः । चत्वारः कर्मचाण्डाला<BR> जन्मतश्चापि पञ्चमः ॥<BR>—2 one who commits an atrocious deed; अपूर्वकर्मचण्डालमयि मुग्धे विमुञ्च<BR> माम् U. 1. 46.<BR>—3 N. of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मचाण्डालः
कर्मन् + -चण्डालः, -चाण्डालः<BR>—1 ‘base in deed’, a man of very low acts or deeds; Vasiṣṭha mentions<BR> these kinds:− असूयकः पिशुनश्च कृतघ्नो दीर्घरोषकः । चत्वारः कर्मचाण्डाला<BR> जन्मतश्चापि पञ्चमः ॥<BR>—2 one who commits an atrocious deed; अपूर्वकर्मचण्डालमयि मुग्धे विमुञ्च<BR> माम् U. 1. 46.<BR>—3 N. of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मचेष्टा|कर्म्मचेष्टा
कर्मन् + -चेष्टा active exertion, action. कर्मचेष्टास्वहः Ms. 1. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मचोदना|कर्म्मचोदना
कर्मन् + -चोदना<BR>—1 The motive impelling one to ritual acts. ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं परिज्ञाता<BR> त्रिविधा कर्मचोदना Bg. 18. 18.<BR>—2 any positive rule enjoining a religious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मच्छेदः|कर्मच्छेद
कर्मन् + -च्छेदः The loss caused by absence on duty; Kau. A. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मज|कर्मजः|कर्म्मज|कर्म्मजः
कर्मन् + -ज^1 <i>a.</i> resulting from an act; सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा Bg. 4. 12.<BR> कर्मजा गतयो नॄणामुत्तमाधममध्यमाः Ms. 12. 3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मजः|कर्मज|कर्म्मज|कर्म्मजः
कर्मन् + -जः + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 the Kali age.<BR>—3 the banian tree.<BR>—4 the effect arising from human acts:− संयोग, विभाग &c.<BR>—5 heaven.<BR>—6 hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मज्ञ|कर्म्मज्ञ
कर्मन् + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> one acquainted with religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मत्यागः|कर्मत्याग|कर्म्मत्याग
कर्मन् + -त्यागः renunciation of worldly duties or ceremonial acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मदुष्ट|कर्म्मदुष्ट
कर्मन् + -दुष्ट <i>a.</i> corrupt in action, wicked, immoral, disrespectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मदेवः|कर्मदेव|कर्म्मदेव
कर्मन् + -देवः a god through religious action; ये शतं गन्धर्वलोक<BR> आनन्दाः स एकः कर्मदेवानामानन्दः Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मदोषः|कर्मदोष|कर्म्मदोष
कर्मन् + -दोषः<BR>—1 sin, vice; अवेक्षेत गतीर्नॄणां कर्मदोषसमुद्भवाः Ms. 6. 61, 95.<BR>—2 an error, defect, or blunder (in doing an act); कर्मदोषैर्न लिप्यते Ms. 1. 104^1.<BR>—3 evil consequence of human acts.<BR>—4 discreditable conduct.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मधारयः|कर्मधारय|कर्म्मधारय
कर्मन् + -धारयः N. of a compound, a subdivision of Tatpuruṣa, (in which<BR> the members of the compound are in apposition) तत्पुरुषः समानाधिकरणः<BR> कर्मधारयः P. I. 2. 42; तत्पुरुष कर्म धारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मध्वंसः|कर्मध्वंस|कर्म्मध्वंस
कर्मन् + -ध्वंसः<BR>—1 loss of fruit arising from religious acts.<BR>—2 disappointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनामन्
कर्मन् + -नामन् (in gram.) a participial^1 noun.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260507. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनामधेयम्
कर्मन् + -नामधेयम् N. of an act or sacrifice. These names are not arbitrary<BR> or technical such as गुण and वृद्धि but are always significant;<BR> सर्वेष्वेव कर्मनामधेयेषु अर्थसमन्वयेनानुवादभूतो नामशब्दो वर्तते,<BR> न लौकिकार्थतिरस्कारेण परिभाषामात्रेण वृद्धिगुणवत् ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनाशा|कर्म्मनाशा
कर्मन् + -नाशा N. of a river between Kaśī and Bihar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनिश्चयः
कर्मन् + -निश्चयः a decision of action; न लेभे कर्मनिश्चयम् Bm. 1. 648.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनिषद्या
कर्मन् + -निषद्या a manufactory;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">Page0542-2</a>]<BR> Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मनिष्ठ|कर्म्मनिष्ठ
कर्मन् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> devoted to the performance of religious acts; अग्निर्वीरं<BR> श्रुत्यं कर्मनिष्ठाम् Rv. 10. 80. 1; Ms. 3. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्यासः|कर्मन्यास|कर्म्मन्यास
कर्मन् + -न्यासः renunciation of the result of religious acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मपथः|कर्मपथ|कर्म्मपथ
कर्मन् + -पथः<BR>—1 the direction or source of an action.<BR>—2 the path of religious rites (opp. ज्ञानमार्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मपाकः|कर्मपाक
कर्मन् + -पाकः ripening of actions, reward of actions done in a former<BR> life; Pt. 1. 372.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मप्रवचनीयः|कर्मप्रवचनीय|कर्म्मप्रवचनीय
कर्मन् + -प्रवचनीयः a term for certain prepositions, particles, or adverbs<BR> when they are not connected with verbs and govern a noun in some case;<BR> literally, the term means, ‘Concerned with the setting forth of an action’.<BR> According to Indian grammarians it means ‘that which spoke of an action (क्रियां प्रोक्तवन्तः)’<BR> <i>e. g.</i> आ in आ मुक्तेः संसारः is<BR> a कर्मप्रवचनीय; so अनु in जपमनु प्रावर्षत् &c.; कर्म<BR> प्रोक्तवन्तः कर्मप्रवचनीया इति Mbh. on P. I. 4. 83. cf. उपसर्ग,<BR> गति and निपात also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मफलम्
कर्मन् + -फलम्<BR>—1 fruit or reward of actions done in a former life; (pain, pleasure);<BR> न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा Bg. 4. 14, 5. 12, 6. 1; ˚फलत्याग Bg. 12. 11, 18. 2;<BR> ˚फलत्यागिन् Bg. 18. 11; ˚फलप्रेप्सुः Bg. 18. 27; ˚फलसंयोग<BR> Bg. 5. 14; ˚फलहेतु Bg. 2. 47. एवं संचिन्त्य मनसा प्रेत्य कर्मफलोदयम् Ms. 11. 231.<BR>—2 the fruit of Averrhoa Carambola (Mar. कर्मर); also कर्मरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मबन्धः|कर्मबन्ध|कर्मबंध|कर्म्मबन्ध
कर्मन् + -बन्धः, -बन्धनम् confinement to repeated birth, as the consequence<BR> of religious acts, good or bad (by which the soul is attached to worldly<BR> pleasures &c.); बुद्ध्या युक्तो यथा पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यति Bg. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मबन्धनम्
कर्मन् + -बन्धः, -बन्धनम् confinement to repeated birth, as the consequence<BR> of religious acts, good or bad (by which the soul is attached to worldly<BR> pleasures &c.); बुद्ध्या युक्तो यथा पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यति Bg. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मभूः|कर्म्मभूः
कर्मन् + -भूः, -भूमिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the land of religious rites, <i>i. e.</i> भरतवर्ष, this world<BR> (a place for manʼs probation); प्राप्येमां कर्मभूमिम् Bh. 2. 100; K. 174, 319.<BR>—2 ploughed ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मभूमिः|कर्मभूमि|कर्म्मभूमि|कर्म्मभूमिः
कर्मन् + -भूः, -भूमिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the land of religious rites, <i>i. e.</i> भरतवर्ष, this world<BR> (a place for manʼs probation); प्राप्येमां कर्मभूमिम् Bh. 2. 100; K. 174, 319.<BR>—2 ploughed ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ममासः|कर्ममास
कर्मन् + -मासः the Calendar month of thirty days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ममीमांसा|कर्म्ममीमांसा
कर्मन् + -मीमांसा the Mīmāṃsā of ceremonial acts; see मीमांसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ममूलम्
कर्मन् + -मूलम् a kind of sacred grass called कुश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मयुगम्
कर्मन् + -युगम् the fourth (the present) age of the world, <i>i. e.</i> the Kaliyuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मयोगः|कर्मयोग|कर्म्मयोग|कर्म्मयोगः
कर्मन् + -योगः<BR>—1 performance of actions, worldly and religious rites; कर्मयोगेन<BR> योगिनाम् Bg. 3. 3, 3. 7, 5. 2, 13. 24.<BR>—2 active exertion, industry; Ms. 10. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवचनम्
कर्मन् + -वचनम् (with Buddhists) the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवज्रः|कर्मवज्र|कर्म्मवज्र|कर्म्मवज्रः
कर्मन् + -वज्रः an epithet of a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवशः|कर्मवश|कर्म्मवश
कर्मन् + -वशः fate considered as the inevitable result of actions done<BR> in a former life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मवाटी|कर्म्मवाटी
कर्मन् + -वाटी a lunar day (तिथि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाकः
कर्मन् + -विपाक = कर्मपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मशाला|कर्म्मशाला
कर्मन् + -शाला a work-shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मशील|कर्म्मशील|कर्म्मशीलः
कर्मन् + -शील, -शूर <i>a.</i> assiduous, active, laborious; cf. कर्मशीलस्तु<BR> कर्मठे । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मशूर|कर्म्मशूर|कर्म्मशूरः
कर्मन् + -शील, -शूर <i>a.</i> assiduous, active, laborious; cf. कर्मशीलस्तु<BR> कर्मठे । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मशौचम्
कर्मन् + -शौचम् humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मश्रुतिः
कर्मन् + -श्रुतिः <i>f.</i> The word expressive of the act; कर्मश्रुतेः परार्थत्वात्<BR> MS. 11. 2. 6. (read या अत्र कर्मश्रुतिः दर्शपूर्णमासाभ्यामिति सा परार्था<BR> तृतीया-योगात् &c. शबर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसङ्गः|कर्मसङ्ग|कर्मसंग|कर्म्मसङ्ग
कर्मन् + -सङ्गः attachment to worldly duties and their results. तन्निबध्नाति … कर्मसङ्गेन Bg. 14. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसचिवः|कर्मसचिव|कर्म्मसचिव|कर्म्मसचिवः
कर्मन् + -सचिवः a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसंन्यासिकः|कर्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्म्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्म्मसंन्यासिक|कर्म्मसन्न्यासिकः
कर्मन् + -संन्यासिकः, -संन्यासिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a religious person who has withdrawn from every kind of worldly act.<BR>—2 an ascetic who performs religious deeds without looking to their reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसंन्यासिन्
कर्मन् + -संन्यासिकः, -संन्यासिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a religious person who has withdrawn from every kind of worldly act.<BR>—2 an ascetic who performs religious deeds without looking to their reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसाक्षिन्|कर्म्मसाक्षिन्
कर्मन् + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an eyewitness; वह्निर्विवाहं प्रति कर्मसाक्षी Ku. 7. 83.<BR>—2 one who witnesses the good or bad actions of man; आदित्य भो लोककृताकृतज्ञ<BR> लोकस्य सत्यानृतकर्मसाक्षिन् Rām. 3. 63. 16. (There are nine divinities<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">Page0543-1</a>]<BR> which are said to witness and watch over all human actions; सूर्यः सोमो<BR> यमः कालो महाभूतानि पञ्च च । एते शुभाशुभस्येह कर्मणो नव साक्षिणः ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मसिद्धिः|कर्मसिद्धि|कर्म्मसिद्धि
कर्मन् + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> accomplishment of any business or desired object;<BR> success. स्वकर्मसिद्धिं पुनराशशंसे Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मस्थानम्
कर्मन् + -स्थानम् a public office, a place of business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मठ|कर्मठः|कर्म्मठ|कर्म्मठः
कर्मठ <i>a.</i> [कर्मन्-अठच् P. V. 2. 35].<BR>—1 Proficient in any work, clever. skilful. पटुसंगरकर्मकर्मठम् … …<BR> Śiva B. 32. 2. ज्ञाताशयस्तस्य ततो व्यतानीत्स कर्मठः कर्म<BR> सुतानुबन्धम् Bk. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Working diligently.<BR>—3 Exclusively devoted to the performance of religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मठः|कर्मठ|कर्म्मठ|कर्म्मठः
कर्मठ + .{@-ठः@} The director of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मण्य|कर्म्मण्य|कर्म्मण्यः
कर्मण्य <i>a.</i> [कर्मन्-यत्] Skilful, clever. यतो वीरः कर्मण्यः<BR> सुदक्षः Nṛ. P. Up. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मण्या|कर्म्मण्या
कर्मण्य + .{@-ण्या@} Wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मण्यम्
कर्मण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@} Activity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिन्|कर्म्मिन्
कर्मिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Working, active, busy.<BR>—2 Engaged in any work or business.<BR>—3 One who performs religious deeds with the expectation of reward or<BR> recompense; यत् कर्मिणो न प्रवेदयन्ति रागात् Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 9.<BR> कर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन Bg. 6. 46. ━<i>m.</i> A mechanic,<BR> artisan; अनेन विधिराख्यात ऋत्विक्कर्षककर्मिणाम् Y. 2. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठः
कर्मिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Skilled in business, clever, diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्दिन्|कर्मंदिन्|कर्म्मन्दिन्
कर्मन्दिन् <i>m.</i> P. IV. 3. 111 An ascetic, a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मरी|कर्म्मरी
कर्मरी The manna of the bamboo (वंशलोचन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मारः|कर्मार|कर्म्मार|कर्म्मारः
कर्मारः<BR>—1 A blacksmith; Y. 1. 163; Ms. 4. 215; a polisher of tools and weapons<BR> (Mar. शिकलगार); ततः संधाय विमलान् भल्लान् कर्मारमार्जितान् Mb. 6. 94. 34.<BR>—2 A bamboo; … कर्मारकुलसंकुला Śiva B. 19. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मीर|कर्म्मीर|कर्म्मीरः
कर्मीर <i>a.</i> Variegated; spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्
कर्व् €1 P. (कर्वति, कर्वित) To be proud, boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वः|कर्व|कर्व्व|कर्व्वः
कर्वः<BR>—1 Love, desire.<BR>—2 A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वटः|कर्वट|कर्व्वट|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्वटः<BR>—1 The market-town or capital of a district (of two hundred villages).<BR>—2 Declivity of a mountain; (also कर्वटक in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वटम्
कर्वटः + .{@-टम्@} A city. See खर्वट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वुदारः|कर्वुदार
कर्वुदारः The कोविदार tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वूरकः
कर्वूरकः Zedoary (A kind of aromatic gingerlike substance used<BR> in medicine, perfumery, and dying.) (Mar. कचोरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वर|कर्वरः|कर्व्वर
कर्व(र्ब)र <i>a.</i> Variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बर
कर्व(र्ब)र <i>a.</i> Variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वरः|कर्वर|कर्व्वर
कर्व(र्ब)र + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Sin.<BR>—2 Tiger.<BR>—3 A demon.<BR>—4 A sort of medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वरी|कर्व्वरी
कर्व(र्ब)र + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—2 Night.<BR>—3 A Rākṣasī.<BR>—4 A tigress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वरम्
कर्व(र्ब)र + .{@-रम्@} Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शन|कर्शनः
कर्शन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rendering lean.<BR>—2 troubling, hurting; यदाश्रौषमसुराणां वधार्थे किरीटिनं यान्तममित्रकर्शनम् Mb. 1. 1. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शनः|कर्शन
कर्शन + .{@-नः@} Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षः|कर्ष
कर्षः [कृष्-अच् घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Drawing, dragging, pulling; Y. 2. 217.<BR>—2 Attracting.<BR>—3 Ploughing<BR>—4 A furrow, a trench.<BR>—5 A scratch.<BR>—6 Terminalia Bellerica (Mar. बिब्बा, बेहडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षः|कर्ष
कर्षः + .{@-र्षः, -र्षम्@} A weight of gold or silver equal to 16 Māṣas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्षापण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षम्
कर्षः + .{@-र्षः, -र्षम्@} A weight of gold or silver equal to 16 Māṣas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कर्षापण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षापण
कर्षः + -आपण = कार्षापण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक <i>a.</i> [कृष्-ण्वुल्] Who or what draws, attracts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षकः|कर्षक
कर्षक + .{@-कः@} A cultivator, husbandman; Y. 2. 265. त्वं समीरण इव<BR> प्रतीक्षितः कर्षकेण वलजान्पुपूषता Śi. 14. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dragging.<BR>—2 Injuring.<BR>—3 Extending (in time), see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणम्
कर्षण + .{@-णम्@} [कृष् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Drawing, dragging, pulling, bending (as of a bow); भज्यमानमतिमात्रकर्षणात्<BR> R. 11. 46, 7. 62.<BR>—2 Attracting.<BR>—3 Ploughing, tilling; प्रभृतं कर्षणं स्मृतम् Ms. 4. 5.<BR>—4 Injuring, tormenting; emaciation; तथा राज्ञामपि प्राणाः क्षीयन्ते<BR> राष्ट्रकर्षणात् Ms. 7. 112.<BR>—5 Cultivated land; पुत्रस्य ते पशवः कर्षणं च Mb. 3. 113. 13.<BR>—6 a weapon; इषुभिस्तोमरैः प्रासैस्त्रिशूलैर्वज्रकर्षणैः Rām. 7. 32. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणिः|कर्षणि
कर्षणिः <i>f.</i> An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षित
कर्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drawn, attracted.<BR>—2 Tormented. harassed &c.<BR>—3 Worn out, decayed; अर्जुनं कथयामास बहुसंग्रामकार्षितम् Mb. 14. 86. 7.<BR>—4 Ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Who or what draws &c. स्तम्बेरमा मुखरशृङ्खलकर्षिणस्ते R.<BR>—2 Attractive. घ्नाणकान्तमधुगन्धकर्षिणीः R. 19. 11. ━<i>m.</i> A ploughman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिणी
कर्षिन् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 The bit of a bridle.<BR>—2 A medicinal moon-plant (Mar. खिरणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षूः
कर्षूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A furrow, trench.<BR>—2 A river.<BR>—3 Canal.<BR>—4 A pit; कर्षू खात्वा … विभरासि । Śat. Br. (मत्स्योपाख्यान);<BR> कर्षूर्वार्ताकरीषाग्निलेखनेषु च खातने कुल्यायां तु कर्षूः … Nm. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A fire of dried cow-dung.<BR>—2 Agriculture, cultivation.<BR>—3 Livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि <i>ind.</i> Ved. When, at what time? with अपि चिद् and स्विद्<BR> = at any time; यन्निर्मितां कर्ह्यपि कर्मपर्वणीम् Bhāg. 5. 17. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हिचित्
कर्हिचित् <i>ind.</i> At any time, usually with न; अकामस्य क्रिया<BR> काचित् दृश्यते नेह कर्हिचित् Ms. 2. 4, 40, 97, 4. 77, 6. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
कल् I. €1 Ā. (कलते, कलित)<BR>—1 To count.<BR>—2 To sound. ━II. €10 U. (कलयति-ते, कलित)<BR>—1 To hold, bear, carry, wield, have, put on; करालकरकन्दलीकलितशस्त्रजालैर्बलैः<BR> U. 5. 5; म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालम् Gīt. 1; कलितललितवनमालः;<BR> हलं कलयते <i>ibid.</i>; कलय वलयश्रेणीं पाणौ पदे कुरु नूपुरौ 12;<BR> Mb. 12. 4. 18.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To count, reckon; कालः कलयतामहम् Bg. 10. 30.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To measure; सदा पान्थः पूषा गगनपरिमाणं कलयति Bh. 2. 114.<BR>—3 To assume, take, have, possess; कलयति हि हिमांशोर्निष्कलङ्कस्य<BR> लक्ष्मीम् Māl. 1. 22; Śi. 4. 36, 9. 59.<BR>—4 To know, understand, observe, take notice of, think of; कलयन्नपि<BR> सव्यथोऽवतस्थे Śi. 9. 83; कोपितं विरहखेदितचित्ता कान्तमेव कलयन्त्यनुनिन्ये 10. 29;<BR> N. 2. 65, 3. 12,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">Page0544-1</a>]<BR> Māl. 2. 9.<BR>—5 To think, regard, consider; कलयेदमानमनसं सखि माम् Śi. 9. 58, 6. 54, 15. 55, 16. 64;<BR> Mb. 12. 4. 15; व्यालनिलयमिलनेन गरलमिव<BR> कलयति मलयसमीरम् Gīt. 4, 7; cf. कलयति स कथं ते पाशमुद्बन्धनाय Nāg. 2. 11.<BR>—6 To undergo, be influenced by; मदलीलाकलितकामपाल Māl. 8; धन्यः<BR> कोऽपि न विक्रियां कलयति प्राप्ते नवे यौवने Bh. 1. 72.<BR>—7 To do, perform.<BR>—8 To go.<BR>—9 To attach to, tie on; furnish with.<BR>—10 To urge on, impel, incite; कलय शिखिनः केकोत्कण्ठान् Māl. 9. 42.<BR>—11 To utter a sound, murmur.<BR>—12 To take hold of the die called ‘Kali’. ━III. €10 P. (कालयति, कालित)<BR>—1 To push on, urge, drive forward; गावो न काल्यन्त इदं कुतो रजो<BR> Bhāg. 4. 5. 8.<BR>—2 To carry off.<BR>—3 To collect.<BR>—4 To throw, cast. —5 To proclaim the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल <i>a.</i> [कल्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sweet and indistinct (अस्पष्टमधुर); कर्णे कलं किमपि रौति<BR> H. 1. 78; सारसैः कलनिर्ह्रदैः R. 1. 41, 8. 59; M. 5. 1. वाग्भिः<BR> कलाभिर्ललितैश्च हावैः Bu. C. 2. 30. (Hence<BR>—2 Low, soft, sweet (note &c.); melodious, pleasing, निशामु भास्वत्कलनूपुराणाम् R. 16. 12.<BR>—3 Making noise, jingling, tinkling &c.; भास्वत्कलनूपुराणाम् R. 16. 12;<BR> कलकिङ्किणीरवम् Śi. 9. 74, 82; कलमेखलाकलकलः 6. 14, 4. 57;<BR>—4 Weak.<BR>—5 Crude; undigested.<BR>—6 Vigorous.<BR>—7 Full; दीनस्य ताम्राश्रुकलस्य राज्ञः Rām. 2. 13. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कला
कल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 A low or soft and inarticulate tone.<BR>—2 (In poetry) Time equal to four Mātrās.<BR>—3 (<i>m.</i> <i>pl.</i>) A class of manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्
कल + .{@-लम्@} Semen.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कलाङ्कुरः, कलानुवादिन्, कलाविकलः, कलालापः, कलोत्ताल, कलकण्ठ, कलकलः, कलकूजिका, कलकूणिका, कलघोषः, कलचुरिः, कलचूरिः, कलतूलिका, कलधूतम्, कलधौतम्, कलध्वनिः, कलनाद, कलभाषणम्, कलरवः, कलविशुद्ध, कलव्याघ्रः, कलहंसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाङ्कुरः|कलाङ्कुर|कलांकुर|कलांकुरः
कल + -अङ्कुरः the Sārasa bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानुवादिन्
कल + -अनुवादिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a sparrow.<BR>—2 a bee.<BR>—3 the Chātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविकलः|कलाविकल
कल + -अविकलः a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलालापः|कलालाप
कल + -आलापः<BR>—1 a sweet humming sound.<BR>—2 sweet and agreeable discourse; स्फुरत्कलालापविलासकोमला करोति रागं हृदि कौतुकाधिकम् K. 2.<BR>—3 a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलोत्ताल
कल + -उत्ताल <i>a.</i> high, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकण्ठ|कलकंठ|कलकण्ठः
कल + -कण्ठ <i>a.</i> having a sweet voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकण्ठः|कलकण्ठ|कलकंठ
कल + -कण्ठ + .({@-ण्ठः@}) ({@ण्ठी@}) <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>—2 a goose, swan.<BR>—3 a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकलः|कलकल
कल + -कलः<BR>—1 murmuring or hum of a crowd.<BR>—2 indistinct or confused noise; चलितया विदधे कलमेखलाकलकलोऽलकलोलदृशान्यया<BR> Śi. 6. 14; नेपथ्ये कलकलः (in dramas); Bh. 1. 27, 37; Amaru. 31.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR>—4 resin, pitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकूजिका
कल + -कूजिका, -कूणिका a wanton woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकूणिका
कल + -कूजिका, -कूणिका a wanton woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलघोषः|कलघोष
कल + -घोषः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलचुरिः|कलचुरि
कल + -चुरिः, -चूरिः N. of a royal family; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलचूरिः|कलचूरि
कल + -चुरिः, -चूरिः N. of a royal family; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलतूलिका
कल + -तूलिका a wanton or lascivious woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधूतम्
कल + -धूतम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौतम्
कल + -धौतम्<BR>—1 silver; कलधौतधौत-शिलवेश्मनां रुचौ Śi. 13. 21, 4. 41.<BR>—2 gold; विमलकलधौतत्सरुणा खड्गेन Ve. 3. कन्येयं कलधौतकोमलरुचिः<BR> कीर्तिस्तु नातः परा Mahār.<BR>—3 a low or pleasing tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौतलिपि
कल-धौतम् + -लिपि ˚लिपि <i>f.</i><BR>—1 illumination of a manuscript with gold.<BR>—2 characters written in gold; मरकतशकलकलितकलधौतलिपेरिव<BR> रतिजयलेखम् Gīt. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलध्वनिः|कलध्वनि
कल + -ध्वनिः<BR>—1 a low sweet tone.<BR>—2 a pigeon.<BR>—3 a peacock.<BR>—4 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलनाद|कलनादः
कल + -नाद <i>a.</i> having a low and sweet tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलनादः|कलनाद
कल + -नाद + .({@-दः@}) a swan; see कलध्वनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभाषणम्
कल + -भाषणम् lisping, the prattle of childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलरवः|कलरव
कल + -रवः<BR>—1 a low sweet tone.<BR>—2 a dove.<BR>—3 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविशुद्ध
कल + -विशुद्ध <i>a.</i> soft and clear; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलव्याघ्रः|कलव्याघ्र
कल + -व्याघ्रः a mongrel breed between a tigress and panther.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहंसः|कलहंस
कल + -हंसः<BR>—1 a gander, a swan; वधूदुकूलं कलहंसलक्षणम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">Page0544-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 5. 67.<BR>—2 a duck, drake; Bk. 2. 18; कलमन्यभृतासु भाषितं कलहंसीषु मदालसं<BR> गतम् R. 8. 59.<BR>—3 the supreme soul.<BR>—4 an excellent king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कषः|कलङ्कष|कलंकष|कलंकषः
कलङ्कषः<BR>—1 A lion.<BR>—2 A musical instrument, cymbal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कुरः|कलङ्कुर|कलंकुर|कलंकुरः
कलङ्कुरः A whirlpool, eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन <i>a.</i> (at the end of comp.) Causing, effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलनः|कलन|कलनं
कलन + .{@-नः@} A sort of cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलनम्
कलन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A spot, mark.<BR>—2 A defect, an offence, fault.<BR>—3 Taking, seizing, grasping; कलनात्सर्वभूतानां स कालः परिकीर्तितः.<BR>—4 Knowing, understanding, apprehension.<BR>—5 Sounding.<BR>—6 An embryo at the first stage after conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलना
कलन + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 Taking, seizing, grasping; कालकलना Ā. L. 29.<BR>—2 Doing, effecting.<BR>—3 Subjection.<BR>—4 Understanding, comprehension.<BR>—5 Putting on, wearing; also letting loose; चूडाकलनाम् Śi. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Held, seized, taken; U. 5. 5, v. l.<BR>—2 Broken; Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Plucked, gathered; सीतादेव्याः स्वकरकलितैः U. 3. 6.<BR>—4 Arisen, produced; U. 5. 2; कलितकुलिशघाताः केपि खेलन्ति वाताः R. G.<BR>—5 Influenced; Māl. 8.<BR>—6 Mixed; अनलस्फुलिङ्गकलितः किमयमनभ्रः सुधावर्षः Māl. 10. 10.<BR>—7 Known, understood; कलयसि कलितोऽहम् Māl. 8. 13, 2. 9.<BR>—8 Furnished, endowed, Māl. 6. 6: कलितान्योन्यसामर्थ्यैः Ku. 6. 76.<BR>—9 Gained, obtained.<BR>—10 Reckoned, counted.<BR>—11 Separated, divided.<BR>—12 Sounded indistinctly, murmured.<BR>—13 Made, formed; लवङ्गमालाकलितावतंसाः Śi. 3. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकः|कलक
कलकः<BR>—1 A kind of fish.<BR>—2 A kind of prose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कः|कलङ्क|कलंक|कलंकः
कलङ्कः<BR>—1 A spot, a mark, a dark spot (lit.); धारानिबद्धेव कलङ्करेखा R. 13. 15.<BR>—2 (Fig.) A stain, stigma, obloquy, disrepute; व्यपनयतु कलङ्कं<BR> स्वस्वभावेन सैव Mk. 10. 34; R. 14. 37; so कुल˚.<BR>—3 A fault, defect; विद्या नाधिगता कलङ्करहिता Bh. 3. 48.<BR>—4 Rust of iron.<BR>—5 A sectarial mark on the forehead; ‘कलङ्कः कृष्णवर्णे स्यात् तमाले तिलकेऽपि च’ Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कलङ्कहृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कहृत्
कलङ्कः + -हृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कयति
कलङ्कयति Den. P. To defame, stain with stigma, sully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कित|कलंकित
कलङ्कित <i>a.</i> Spotted, stained, defamed; अकुङ्कुमकलङ्कितोज्ज्वलकपोलमुत्प्रेक्ष्यते U. 6. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्जः|कलञ्ज|कलंज|कलंजः
कलञ्जः<BR>—1 A bird.<BR>—2 A deer or any other animal struck with a poisoned weapon.<BR>—3 Tobacco.<BR>—4 A particular weight (= 10 Rūpakas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्जम्
कलञ्जः + .{@-ञ्जम्@} Flesh of such an animal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कलञ्जन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्जन्यायः
कलञ्जः + -न्यायः the rule according to which a negation connected with<BR> an act constitutes prohibition of that act. This is discussed and established<BR> by जैमिनि (6. 2. 19) and शबर in connection with texts like<BR> न कलञ्जं भक्षयेत् in MS. 6. 2. 19-20; ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलटम्
कलटम् The thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत
कलत <i>a.</i> Bald-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्रम्
कलत्रम्<BR>—1 A wife; वसुमत्या हि नृपाः कलत्रिणः R. 8. 83, 1. 32, 12. 34;<BR> यद्भर्तुरेव हितमिच्छति तत्कलत्रम् Bh. 2. 68.<BR>—2 The female of an animal.<BR>—3 The hip and loins; इन्दुमूर्तिमिवोद्दाममन्मथविलासगृहीतगुरुकलत्राम्<BR> K. 189 (where क˚ has both senses); Ki. 8. 9, 17.<BR>—4 Any royal citadel.<BR>—5 The seventh lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दरः|कलन्दर|कलंदरः
कलन्दरः A man of a mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दिका|कलंदिका
कलन्दिका Wisdom, intelligence (सर्वविद्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभः|कलभ
कलभः (-भी <i>f.</i>) [कल्-अभच् Uṇ. 3. 122; करेण शुण्डया<BR> भाति; भा-क, रस्य लत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A young elephant, cub; ननु कलभेन यूथपतेरनुकृतम् M. 5; द्विपेन्द्रभावं<BR> कलभः श्रयन्निव R. 3. 32, 11. 39, 18. 38; Bhāg. 8. 2. 23.<BR>—2 An elephant 30 years old.<BR>—3 A young camel; the young of any other animal.<BR>—4 A particular fragrant substance used as an unguent, कलभः करिपोतके ।<BR> अङ्गलेपन वस्तूनां विशेषेऽपि पुमान् भवेत् । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलमः|कलम
कलमः [Uṇ. 4. 84]<BR>—1 Rice which is sown in May-June and ripens in December-January; प्रसूतं<BR> कलमक्षेत्रं वर्षेणेव शतकतुः Rām. 4. 14. 16. सुतेन पाण्डोः कलमस्य<BR> गोपिकाम् Ki. 4. 9, 34; Ku. 5. 47; आपादपद्मप्रणता कलमा इव ते रघुम् ।<BR> फलैः संवर्धयामासुरुत्खातप्रतिरोपिताः ॥ R. 4. 37. कलयता कलमावनकामिनीकलमनोहरगानममन्यत<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 72.<BR>—2 A pen, a reed for writing with.<BR>—3 A thief.<BR>—4 A rogue, rascal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कलमगोपवधू^1, कलमगोपी<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260403. Reference: Scott batch 20260402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलमगोपवधू
कलमः + -गोपवधू, -गोपी a woman employed to guard a rice-field; Śi. 6. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलमगोपी
कलमः + -गोपवधू, -गोपी a woman employed to guard a rice-field; Śi. 6. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बः|कलम्ब|कलंब|कलंबः
कलम्बः<BR>—1 An arrow.<BR>—2 The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बिका|कलंबिका
कलम्बिका<BR>—1 The nape of the neck.<BR>—2 An aquatic pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बुट|कलंबुट|कलम्बुटं
कलम्बुट (Fresh) Butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बूः
कलम्बूः An aquatic pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललः|कलल|कललं
कललः, -लम्<BR>—1 The foetus, uterus.<BR>—2 A term for the embryo a short time after conception. कार्याश्रयिणश्च<BR> कललाद्याः Sāṅ. K. 43. कललं त्वेकरात्रेण पञ्चरात्रेण बुद्बुदम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 31. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललम्
कललः, -लम्<BR>—1 The foetus, uterus.<BR>—2 A term for the embryo a short time after conception. कार्याश्रयिणश्च<BR> कललाद्याः Sāṅ. K. 43. कललं त्वेकरात्रेण पञ्चरात्रेण बुद्बुदम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 31. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललजः|कललज
कललजः<BR>—1 The resinous exudation of the Shorea Robusta.<BR>—2 Womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्कः|कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविंकः
कलविङ्कः, -गः<BR>—1 A sparrow; Ms. 5. 12; Y. 1. 174. कलविङ्कस्वर उत्तरं बभाषे Bu. C. 5. 34.<BR>—2 A spot, stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्गः|कलविङ्ग|कलविंगः
कलविङ्कः, -गः<BR>—1 A sparrow; Ms. 5. 12; Y. 1. 174. कलविङ्कस्वर उत्तरं बभाषे Bu. C. 5. 34.<BR>—2 A spot, stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशः|कलश
कलशः, -सः (-शम्, -सम्)<BR> [केन जलेन लश(स)ति Tv.]<BR>—1 A pitcher, water-pot, a jar, dish; हिरण्मयं कलशं विभर्षि Mbh.<BR> on P. VI. 4. 174; Śi. 11; स्तनौ मांसग्रन्थी कनककलशावित्युपमितौ<BR> Bh. 3. 20, 1. 97; Amaru. 54.<BR>—2 A churn.<BR>—3 A kind of measure.<BR>—4 A rounded pinnacle on the top of a temple<BR>—5 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-2" target="_blank">Page0545-2</a>]<BR> ocean; क्षोभ्यतां कलशः सर्वैर्मन्दरः परिवर्त्यताम् Mb. 1. 18. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कलशजन्मन्, कलशोद्भवः, कलशाम्भोधिः, कलशार्णवः, कलशोदधि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

