कवकः|कवक|कवकं
कवकः A mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवकम्
कवकः + .{@-कम्@} A mushroom; विड्जानि कवकानि च Y. 1. 171; Ms. 5. 5, 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचः|कवच|कवचं
कवचः, -चम्<BR> [cf. Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>—1 An armour, coat of mail, a mail.<BR>—2 An amulet, a charm, a mystical syllable ({@हुम्, हूम्@}) considered<BR> as a preservative like armour.<BR>—3 A kettle-drum.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कवचपत्रः, कवचहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचम्
