कवरकी A prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलः|कवल|कवलं
कवलः, -लम्<BR> [केन जलेन वलते चलति, वल्-अच् Tv.]<BR>—1 A mouthful; आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानाम् R. 2. 5, 9. 59; कवलच्छेदेषु<BR> संपादिताः U. 3. 16.<BR>—2 A gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलम्
कवलः, -लम्<BR> [केन जलेन वलते चलति, वल्-अच् Tv.]<BR>—1 A mouthful; आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानाम् R. 2. 5, 9. 59; कवलच्छेदेषु<BR> संपादिताः U. 3. 16.<BR>—2 A gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलयति
कवलयति Den. P. To eat, devour; Pt. 4; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका A bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eaten, swallowed up (as a mouthful).<BR>—2 Chewed.<BR>—3 (Hence) Taken, seized; as in^1 मृत्युना कवलिता.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260410. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवष|कवषः
कवष, -कवष् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Sounding, creaking (as the door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवष्
कवष, -कवष् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR> Sounding, creaking (as the door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवषः|कवष
कवष, -कवष् + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 A shield.<BR>—2 N. of a Ṛṣi (कवष ऐलूष); Rv. 7. 18. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवसः|कवस
कवसः<BR>—1 An armour.<BR>—2 A prickly shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट (-टी) See कपाट. पुरीं महायन्त्रकवाटमुख्याम्<BR> Rām. 6. 39. 27. कवाटदुर्धर्षतिरःप्रसारिता N.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कवाटयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटी
कवाट (-टी) See कपाट. पुरीं महायन्त्रकवाटमुख्याम्<BR> Rām. 6. 39. 27. कवाटदुर्धर्षतिरःप्रसारिता N.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कवाटयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटयोगः
कवाट + -योगः door panel; Kau. A. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवारम्
कवारम् A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवारि
कवारि^1 <i>a.</i> Ved. Selfish, stingy; a mean or contemptible enemy;<BR> न कवारिभ्यो न हि ते पृणन्ति Rv. 10. 107. 3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: the adj. in -ī is improbable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि <i>a.</i> [कु-इ Uṇ. 4. 138]<BR>—1 Omniscient; Mb. 1. 5. 27; कविं पुराणमनुशासितारम् Bg. 8. 9; Ms. 4. 24.<BR>—2 Intelligent, clever, wise; कविर्मूकवदात्मानं स दृष्टपा दर्शयेन्नृणाम्<BR> Bhāg. 7. 13. 10, 18.<BR>—3 Thinking, thoughtful.<BR>—4 Praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविः|कवि
कवि + .{@-विः@}<BR>—1 A wise man, a thinker, a sage; कवीनामुशना कविः Bg. 10. 37; Ms. 7. 49, 2. 151.<BR>—2 A poet; तद् ब्रूहि रामचरितम् आद्यः कविरसि U. 2; मन्दः कवियशःप्रार्थी<BR> R. 1. 3; इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे U. 1. 1; Śi. 2. 86.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śukra, the preceptor of the Asuras; कविरिव वृषपर्वणः K. 56.<BR>—4 Vālmīki, the first poet.<BR>—5 Brahmā; Bhāg. 5. 18. 6.<BR>—6 The sun. ━<i>f.</i> The bit of a bridle; see कविका.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कविज्येष्ठः, कविपुत्रः, कविराजः, कविरामायणः, कविसमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविज्येष्ठः|कविज्येष्ठ
कवि + -ज्येष्ठः an epithet of Vālmīki, the first poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविपुत्रः|कविपुत्र
कवि + -पुत्रः an epithet of Śukra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविराजः|कविराज
कवि + -राजः<BR>—1 a great poet; श्रीहर्षं कविराजराजिमुकुटालङ्कारहीरः सुतम् occurring<BR> in the last verse of every canto of Naiṣadha Charita.<BR>—2 N. of a poet, author of a poem called राघवपाण्डवीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविरामायणः|कविरामायण
कवि + -रामायणः an epithet of Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविसमयः
कवि + -समयः convention of Poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविकः|कविक|कविकं
कविकः, -का<BR> The bit of a bridle. खरतरकविकाकर्षणात्यर्थभुग्नैः<BR> (स्कन्धदेशैः) Mu. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविका
कविकः, -का<BR> The bit of a bridle. खरतरकविकाकर्षणात्यर्थभुग्नैः<BR> (स्कन्धदेशैः) Mu. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविता
कविता Poetry; सुकविता यद्यस्ति राज्येन किम् Bh. 2. 21; यस्याश्चोरश्चिकुरनिकरः<BR> कर्णपूरो मयूरो भासो हासः कविकुलगुरुः कालिदासो विलासः । हर्षो हर्षो<BR> हदयवसतिः पञ्चबाणस्तु बाणः केषां नैषा कथय कविताकामिनी कौतुकाय ॥<BR> P. R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवित्वम्
कवित्वम्<BR>—1 Intelligence; कविः कवित्वा दिवि रूपमासजत् Rv. 10. 124. 7.<BR>—2 Poetic skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवियम्
कवि(वी)यम् The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीयम्
कवि(वी)यम् The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवेलम्
कवेलम् A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
कवोष्ण <i>a.</i> Slightly warm, tepid; पयः पूर्वैः स्वनिःश्वासैः<BR> कवोष्णमुपभुज्यते । R. 1. 67. मुहुर्मुहुर्^1न्यश्वसिषुः कवोष्णम् Bk. 3. 17.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260410. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यम्
कव्यम् (opp. हव्य) An oblation of food to deceased ancestors;<BR> एष वै प्रथमः कल्पः प्रदाने हव्यकव्ययोः Ms. 3. 147, 97, 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यः|कव्य|कव्यं
कव्यम् + .{@-व्यः@} A class of manes. कव्योऽसि हव्यसूदन Mbh. on P. VI. 4. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कव्यवालः, कव्यवाह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवालः|कव्यवाल
कव्यम् + -वालः<BR>—1 fire.<BR>—2 a class of manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवाह्
कव्यम् + -वाह् <i>m.</i>, {@-वाहः, -वाहनः@}<BR> fire. cf. कव्यवाहनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्
कश् €1 P. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशः|कश
कशः<BR>—1 A whip (usually in pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशा
कशः + .{@-शा@} A whip; इदानीं सुकुमारेऽस्मिन् निःशङ्कं कर्कशाः कशाः ।<BR> तव गात्रे पतिष्यन्ति सहास्माकं मनोरथैः ॥ Mk. 9. 35 (where the word<BR> may be <i>m.</i> or <i>f.</i>)<BR>—2 Flogging.<BR>—3 A string, rope.<BR>—4 The mouth.<BR>—5 A quality.<BR>—6 Fat; कशशब्दो मेदसि प्रसिद्धः । यथा कशवाहिनो रथाः मेदोवाहिन<BR> इति गम्यते । ŚB. on MS. 9. 4. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कशात्रयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशात्रयम्
कशा + -त्रयम् the three modes of flogging a horse; सम्यक् कशात्रयविचारवता<BR> नियुक्तः Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य <i>a.</i> [कशामर्हति, कशा-यत्] Fit to be whipped or flogged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यम्
कश्य + .{@-श्यम्@}<BR>—1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—2 A horseʼs flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशस्
कशस् <i>n.</i> Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिकः|कशिक
कशिकः A mungoose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु <i>m.</i> or <i>n.</i><BR>—1 A mat.<BR>—2 A pillow.<BR>—3 A bed. सत्यां क्षितौ किं कशिपोः प्रयासैः Bhāg. 2. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपुः|कशिपु
कशिपु + .{@-पुः@}<BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 Clothing.<BR>—3 Food and clothing (according to विश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशे(से)रु <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 The back-bone.<BR>—2 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरु|कसेरुः
कशे(से)रु <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 The back-bone.<BR>—2 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुः|कशेरु
कशे(से)रु + .{@-रुः@} One of the nine divisions of Jambudvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुकः|कशेरुक|कशेरुकं
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकम्,^1 -काः A sort of grass.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/73eb19d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुकम्
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकम्,^1 -काः A sort of grass.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/73eb19d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुकाः
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकम्,^1 -काः A sort of grass.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/73eb19d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुका
कशेरुकः, कसेरुक, -काः + .{@-का@} The back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 1. 106.] Foul, dirty, disgraceful, ignominious;<BR> मत्सबंधात्कश्मला किंवदन्ती स्याच्चेदस्मिन्हन्त धिङ् मामधन्यम् U. 1. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मलम्
कश्मल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Dejection of mind, lowness or depression of spirits; delusion (मोह);<BR> यदाश्रौषं कश्मलेनाभिपन्ने Mb. 1. 1. 181. कश्मलं महदाविशत<BR> Mb.; कुतस्त्वा कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपास्थितम् Bg. 2. 2.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>—3 A swoon. शोचन्विमुह्यन्नुपयाति कश्मलम् Bhāg. 5. 13. 7.<BR>—4 Consternation, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरः|कश्मीर
कश्मीरः (pl.) N. of a country, the modern Kaṣmir. अभिजानासि देवदत्त<BR> यत्कश्मीरेषु वत्स्यामः Mbh. on I. 1. 44; also on III. 2. 114. (Its position<BR> is thus described in Tantras:− शारदामठमारभ्य कुङ्कुमाद्रितटान्तकः ।<BR> तावत्कश्मीरदेशः स्यात् पञ्चाशद्योजनात्मकः)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कश्मीरजः, कश्मीरजम्, कश्मीरजन्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरजः|कश्मीरज
कश्मीरः + -जः, -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>m., n.</i> saffron; कश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि<BR> नितान्तरम्या Bv. 1. 71, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरजम्
कश्मीरः + -जः, -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>m., n.</i> saffron; कश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि<BR> नितान्तरम्या Bv. 1. 71, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरजन्मन्
कश्मीरः + -जः, -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>m., n.</i> saffron; कश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि<BR> नितान्तरम्या Bv. 1. 71, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यप|कश्यपः
कश्यप^1 <i>a.</i> Having black teeth.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपः|कश्यप
कश्यपः + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 A tortoise.<BR>—2 A sort of fish.<BR>—3 A kind of deer.<BR>—4 N. of a Ṛṣi^1, the husband of Aditi and Diti, and thus the father both<BR> of gods and demons, (so called because he drank कश्य ‘liquor’; cf.<BR> कश्यपस्तस्य पुत्रोऽभूत कश्यपानात् स कश्यपः । Mārk. P.) [He was<BR> the son of Marīci, the son of Brahmā. He bears a very important share<BR> in the work of creation. According to Māhabhārata<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">Page0551-1</a>]<BR> and other accounts, he married Aditi and 12 other daughters of Dakṣa,<BR> and begot on Aditi the twelve Ādityas. By his other twelve wives he had<BR> a numerous and very diversified progeny: serpents, reptiles, birds, demons,<BR> nymphs of the lunar constellation. He was thus the father of gods, demons,<BR> men, beasts, birds and reptiles━ in fact of all living beings. He is<BR> therefore often called Prajāpati].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कश्यपनन्दनः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपनन्दनः|कश्यपनन्दन
कश्यपः + -नन्दनः an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्
कष् I. €1 U. (कषति-ते, कषित)<BR>—1 To rub, scratch, scrape; समूलकाषं कषति Sk.; Bk. 3. 49.<BR>—2 To test, try, rub on a touch-stone (as gold); छदहेम कषन्निवालसत्कषपाषाणनिभे<BR> नभस्तले N. 2. 69.<BR>—3 To injure, destroy.<BR>—4 To itch.<BR>—5 To leap. ━II. €10 P. (काषयति) To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष <i>a.</i> [कष्-अच्] Rubbing, scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषः|कष
कष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 Rubbing.<BR>—2 A touch-stone; छदहेम कषन्निवालसत्कषपाषाणनिभे नभस्तले<BR> N. 2. 69; सुवर्णरेखेव कषे निवेशिता Mk. 3. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कषपट्टिका, कषपाषाणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषपट्टिका
कष + -पट्टिका, -पाषाणः a touch-stone; Vikr. 1. 3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषपाषाणः|कषपाषाण
कष + -पट्टिका, -पाषाणः a touch-stone; Vikr. 1. 3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण <i>a.</i> [कष्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Unripe, immature.<BR>—2 Removing, destroying; adopting oneʼs self to कर्माणि कर्मकषणानि<BR> यदूत्तमस्य Bhāg. 10. 90. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषणम्
कषण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Rubbing, marking, scratching; कण्डूलद्विपगण्डपिण्डकषणोत्कम्पेन<BR> संपातिभिः U. 2. 9; कषणकम्पनिरस्तमहाहिभिः Ki. 5. 47.<BR>—2 Test of gold by the touch-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषा
कषा = कशा q. v. कृच्छ्रेण पृष्ठे कषयाभिताडितः । Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाणः
