काकः [कै शब्दकरणे-कन् Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>—1 A crow; काकोऽपि जीवति चिराय बलिं च भुङ्क्ते Pt. 1. 24.<BR>—2 (Fig.) A contemptible fellow, base or impudent person.<BR>—3 A lame man.<BR>—4 Bathing by dipping the head only into water<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0552-2" target="_blank">Page0552-2</a>]<BR> (as crows do).<BR>—5 A sectarial mark (तिलक).<BR>—6 A kind of measure.<BR>—7 N. of a Dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काका
काकः + .{@-का@} N. of several plants काकनासा, काकोली &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकी
काकः + .{@-की@} A female crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

