काकः + -वन्ध्या a woman that bears only one child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकस्नानम्
काकः + -स्नानम् Bathing like a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकस्पर्शः|काकस्पर्श
काकः + -स्पर्शः<BR>—1 The touching of a crow.<BR>—2 A ceremony performed on the tenth day after a death, consisting in<BR> the offering of rice to crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकस्वरः|काकस्वर
काकः + -स्वरः a shrill tone (as that of a crow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणम्
काकणम् Leprosy with black and red spots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणिः|काकणि
काकणिः A kind of small coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरु(रू)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Timid, cowardly.<BR>—2 Naked.<BR>—3 Poor, indigent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरूक|काकरूकः
काकरु(रू)क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Timid, cowardly.<BR>—2 Naked.<BR>—3 Poor, indigent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुकः|काकरुक
काकरु(रू)क + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A hen-pecked husband.<BR>—2 (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> An owl.<BR>—3 Fraud, deceit, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलः|काकल|काकलं
काक(का)लः<BR>—1 A raven.<BR>—2 The thyroid cartilage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकालः|काकाल
काक(का)लः<BR>—1 A raven.<BR>—2 The thyroid cartilage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलम्
काक(का)लः + .{@-लम्@} A jewel worn upon the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलकः|काकलक
काकलकः<BR>—1 The top of the windpipe. लौकिकमास्यम् ओष्ठात्प्रभृति प्राक् काकलकात्<BR> Mbh. on P. I. 1. 9.<BR>—2 The thyroid cartilage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलकः|काकलक
काकलकः + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An ornament of the neck.<BR>—2 A kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलिः|काकलि
काकलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A low and sweet tone; अनुबद्धमुग्धकाकलीसहितम् U. 3; Ṛs. 1. 8.<BR> प्रमदकोकिलकोमलकाकली Rām. Ch. 4. 2. काकलीप्रधानं च गीयते,<BR> तथा तर्कयामि Nāg. 1. क्रीडत्कोकिलकाकलीकलकलैरुद्गीर्णकर्णज्वराः S. D.<BR>—2 A musical instrument with a low tone used by thieves to ascertain whether<BR> a person is asleep or not; फणिमुखकाकलीसंदंशक … प्रभृत्यनेकोपकरणयुक्तः<BR> Dk. 49. छेदात्समासु सकृदर्पितकाकलीषु Cārudatta 3. 10.<BR>—2 Scissors.<BR>—4 the Guñjā plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काकलिरवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकली
काकलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A low and sweet tone; अनुबद्धमुग्धकाकलीसहितम् U. 3; Ṛs. 1. 8.<BR> प्रमदकोकिलकोमलकाकली Rām. Ch. 4. 2. काकलीप्रधानं च गीयते,<BR> तथा तर्कयामि Nāg. 1. क्रीडत्कोकिलकाकलीकलकलैरुद्गीर्णकर्णज्वराः S. D.<BR>—2 A musical instrument with a low tone used by thieves to ascertain whether<BR> a person is asleep or not; फणिमुखकाकलीसंदंशक … प्रभृत्यनेकोपकरणयुक्तः<BR> Dk. 49. छेदात्समासु सकृदर्पितकाकलीषु Cārudatta 3. 10.<BR>—2 Scissors.<BR>—4 the Guñjā plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काकलिरवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलिरवः|काकलिरव
काकलिः + -रवः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीकः|काकलीक
काकलीकः A low sweet tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकार
काकार <i>a.</i> Scattering water (कं जलमाकिरति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाष्टम्
काकाष्टम् A synonym of पर्यङ्क or bed-stead; Māna. 3. 11-12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणि
काकिणि, काकिणिका, also काकणी<BR>—1 A shell or <i>cowrie</i> used as a coin.<BR>—2 A sum of money equal to 20 <i>cowries</i> or to a quarter of a Paṇa.<BR> एका स्निग्धाः काकिणिना सद्यः सर्वेऽरयः कृताः Bhāg. 11. 23. 20.<BR>—3 A weight equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.<BR>—4 A part of a measure.<BR>—5 The beam of a balance.<BR>—6 A cubit.<BR>—7 A kind of jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणिका
काकिणि, काकिणिका, also काकणी<BR>—1 A shell or <i>cowrie</i> used as a coin.<BR>—2 A sum of money equal to 20 <i>cowries</i> or to a quarter of a Paṇa.<BR> एका स्निग्धाः काकिणिना सद्यः सर्वेऽरयः कृताः Bhāg. 11. 23. 20.<BR>—3 A weight equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.<BR>—4 A part of a measure.<BR>—5 The beam of a balance.<BR>—6 A cubit.<BR>—7 A kind of jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणी
काकिणि, काकिणिका, also काकणी<BR>—1 A shell or <i>cowrie</i> used as a coin.<BR>—2 A sum of money equal to 20 <i>cowries</i> or to a quarter of a Paṇa.<BR> एका स्निग्धाः काकिणिना सद्यः सर्वेऽरयः कृताः Bhāg. 11. 23. 20.<BR>—3 A weight equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.<BR>—4 A part of a measure.<BR>—5 The beam of a balance.<BR>—6 A cubit.<BR>—7 A kind of jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणिक
काकिणिक, also काकिणीक [Mbh. on P. V. 1. 33.] <i>a.</i> worth<BR> a काकिणी; कलौ काकिणिकेऽप्यर्थे विगृह्य त्यक्तसौहृदाः Bhāg. 12. 3. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणीक
काकिणिक, also काकिणीक [Mbh. on P. V. 1. 33.] <i>a.</i> worth<BR> a काकिणी; कलौ काकिणिकेऽप्यर्थे विगृह्य त्यक्तसौहृदाः Bhāg. 12. 3. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिनी
काकिनी<BR>—1 A small coin (equal to twenty cowries), quarter of a Paṇa q. v.<BR>—2 A part of a measure.<BR>—3 cowrie; यः काकिनीमप्यपथप्रपन्नां समुद्धरेन्निष्कसहस्रतुल्याम्<BR> H. 3. 123. न हि काकिन्यां नष्टायां तदन्वेषणं कार्षापणेन क्रियते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिलः|काकिल
काकिलः<BR>—1 A jewel worn upon the neck.<BR>—2 The upper part of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुः|काकु
काकुः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Change of the voice under different emotions, such as fear, grief,<BR> anger; ‘काकुः स्त्रियां विकारो यः शोकभीत्यादिभिर्ध्वनेः’ Ak.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">Page0553-2</a>]<BR> भिन्नकण्ठध्वनिधीरैः काकुरित्यभिधीयते<BR> S. D. अलीककाकुकरणकुशलताम् K. 222; कामे कान्ते सारसिकाकाकुरुतेन<BR> Śi. 6. 76. (Hence)<BR>—2 A word of negation used in such a manner that it implies the contrary<BR> (affirmative), as in questions of appeal (in such cases intended meaning<BR> is suggested by a change of the voice.); cf. Pt. 1. 146.<BR>—3 Muttering, murmuring.<BR>—4 Tongue काकुर्जिह्वा सास्मिन्नुद्यत इति काकुदम् Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1.<BR>—5 Stress, emphasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थः|काकुत्स्थ
काकुत्स्थः [ककुत्स्थस्यापत्यं, ककुत्स्थ-अण्] A descendant of ककुत्स्थ,<BR> an epithet of the kings of the solar dynasty; काकुत्स्थमालोकयतां नृपाणाम्<BR> R. 6. 2, 12. 30, 46; see ककुत्स्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुदम्
काकुदम् The palate अनुक्षरन्ति काकुदं सूर्म्यं सुषिरामिव Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकेची
काकेची <i>f.</i>, काकोचिकः A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोचिकः|काकोचिक
काकेची <i>f.</i>, काकोचिकः A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोलः|काकोल|काकोलं
काकोलः<BR>—1 A raven; Y. 1. 174; Mb. 11. 16. 7.<BR>—2 A snake.<BR>—3 A boar.<BR>—4 A potter.<BR>—5 A division of the infernal regions or hell; महानरककाकोलं संजीवनमहापथम् Y. 3. 223.<BR>—6 A poisonous substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोली
काकोलः + .{@-ली@} A drug prepared through अष्टवर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षः|काक्ष
काक्षः [कुत्सितमक्षम् अत्र, कोः कादेशः; Sk. on P. VI. 3. 104]<BR> A side-long look, a glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षम्
काक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@} Frown, look of displeasure, malicious look; काक्षेणानादरेक्षितः<BR> Bk. 5. 24. काक्षेण पश्यति लिखत्यभिखां नयज्ञः Dūtavākyam 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षी
काक्षी A perfume, a kind of fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवः|काक्षीव
काक्षीवः, -काक्षीवकः<BR> N. of a tree (शोभाञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवकः|काक्षीवक
काक्षीवः, -काक्षीवकः<BR> N. of a tree (शोभाञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कागः|काग
कागः A crow; cf. काक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्ष्|कांक्ष्
काङ्क्ष् €1 P. (काङ्क्षति, काङ्क्षित) (epic. Ātm. also).<BR>—1 To wish, desire, long for; यत्काङ्क्षन्ति तपोभिरन्यमुनयस्तस्मिंस्तपस्यन्त्यमी<BR> Ś. 7. 12; न शोचति न काङ्क्षति Bg. 12. 7; न काङ्क्षे विजयं कृष्ण<BR> Bg. 1. 32; R. 12. 58; Ms. 2. 242.<BR>—2 To expect, wait for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षा|कांक्षा
काङ्क्षा [काङ्क्ष्-अ]<BR>—1 Wish, desire.<BR>—2 Inclination, appetite; as in भक्तकाङ्क्षा. प्रेषितो चाऽपि रामेण<BR> सीतान्वेषणकाङ्क्षया Rām. 5. 42. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षित|कांक्षित
काङ्क्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Wished, desired.<BR>—2 Expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षिन्|कांक्षिन्
काङ्क्षिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>) [काङ्क्ष-णिनि] Wishing for,<BR> desirous; दर्शन˚, जल˚ &c.; देवा अप्यस्य रूपस्य नित्यं दर्शनकाङ्क्षिणः Bg. 11. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षिता
काङ्क्षित + .{@-ता, -तम्@} A wish, desire; अहं त्वरण्ये वत्स्यामि न मे राज्यस्य<BR> काङ्क्षिता Rām. 2. 34. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षितम्
काङ्क्षित + .{@-ता, -तम्@} A wish, desire; अहं त्वरण्ये वत्स्यामि न मे राज्यस्य<BR> काङ्क्षिता Rām. 2. 34. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षोरुः|काङ्क्षोरु|कांक्षोरुः
काङ्क्षोरुः A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचः|काच|काचं
काचः<BR>—1 Glass, crystal; आकरे पद्मरागाणां जन्म काचमणेः कुतः H. Pr. 38;<BR> काचमूल्येन विकीतो हन्त चिन्तामणिर्मया Śānti. 1. 12; मणिर्लुठति<BR> पादेषु काचः शिरसि धार्यते । यथैवास्ते तथैवास्तां काचः काचो मणिर्मणिः ॥ H. 2. 67.<BR>—2 A loop, a swinging shelf, a string so fastened to the yoke as to support burdens.<BR>—3 An eye-disease, an affection of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">Page0554-1</a>]<BR> the optic nerve, producing dimness of sight.<BR>—4 Alkaline ashes.<BR>—5 The string of the balance.<BR>—6 A house with a southern and a northern hall; पूर्वापरे तु शाले गृहचुल्ली<BR> दक्षिणोत्तरे काचम् Bṛ. S. 53. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचम्
काचः + .{@-चम्@}<BR>—1 Alkaline salt.<BR>—2 Wax.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काचाक्षः, काचकामलम्, काचघटी, काचभाजनम्, काचमणिः, काचमलम्, काचलवणम्, काचसंभवम्, काचसौवर्चलम्, काचस्थाली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0553-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचाक्षः|काचाक्ष
काचः + -अक्षः N. of an aquatic bird (बक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचकामलम्
काचः + -कामलम् a kind of disease of the eyes, (काचबिन्दु)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचघटी
काचः + -घटी a glass ewer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचभाजनम्
काचः + -भाजनम् a glass vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमणिः|काचमणि
काचः + -मणिः<BR>—1 crystal, quartz.<BR>—2 Metallic beads. शेषाः काचमणयः Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

