काणेलीमातृ
काणेली + -मातृ <i>m.</i> one whose mother is an unmarried woman; son of an<BR> unmarried woman; (a term of reproach occurring usually in the voc. case<BR> only); काणेलीमातः अस्ति किंचिच्चिह्नं यदुपलक्षयसि Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डः|काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः
काण्डः, -ण्डम्<BR>—1 A section, a part in general.<BR>—2 The portion of a plant from one knot to another. काण्डात्काण्डत्प्ररोहन्ती<BR> Mahānār. Up. 4. 3.<BR>—3 A stem, stock, branch;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">Page0555-1</a>]<BR> लीलोत्खातमृणालकाण्डकवलच्छेदे U. 3. 16; Amaru. 95; Ms. 1. 46, 48; Māl. 3. 34.<BR>—4 Any division of a work, such as a chapter of a book; as the seven Kāṇḍas of the Rām.<BR>—5 A separate department or subject; <i>e. g.</i> कर्म˚ &c.<BR>—6 A cluster, bundle, multitude.<BR>—7 An arrow. मनो दृष्टिगतं कृत्वा ततः काण्डं विसर्जयेत् Dhanur. 30;<BR> Mb. 5. 155. 7.<BR>—8 A long bone, a bone of the arms or legs.<BR>—9 cane, reed.<BR>—10 A stick, staff.<BR>—11 Water. निवृत्ताः काण्डचित्राणि क्रियन्ते दाशबन्धुभिः Rām. 2. 89. 18.<BR>—12 Opportunity, occasion.<BR>—13 Private place.<BR>—14 A kind of measure.<BR>—15 Praise, flattery.<BR>—16 A horse.<BR>—17 Vile, bad, sinful (at the end of comp. only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डम्
काण्डः, -ण्डम्<BR>—1 A section, a part in general.<BR>—2 The portion of a plant from one knot to another. काण्डात्काण्डत्प्ररोहन्ती<BR> Mahānār. Up. 4. 3.<BR>—3 A stem, stock, branch;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">Page0555-1</a>]<BR> लीलोत्खातमृणालकाण्डकवलच्छेदे U. 3. 16; Amaru. 95; Ms. 1. 46, 48; Māl. 3. 34.<BR>—4 Any division of a work, such as a chapter of a book; as the seven Kāṇḍas of the Rām.<BR>—5 A separate department or subject; <i>e. g.</i> कर्म˚ &c.<BR>—6 A cluster, bundle, multitude.<BR>—7 An arrow. मनो दृष्टिगतं कृत्वा ततः काण्डं विसर्जयेत् Dhanur. 30;<BR> Mb. 5. 155. 7.<BR>—8 A long bone, a bone of the arms or legs.<BR>—9 cane, reed.<BR>—10 A stick, staff.<BR>—11 Water. निवृत्ताः काण्डचित्राणि क्रियन्ते दाशबन्धुभिः Rām. 2. 89. 18.<BR>—12 Opportunity, occasion.<BR>—13 Private place.<BR>—14 A kind of measure.<BR>—15 Praise, flattery.<BR>—16 A horse.<BR>—17 Vile, bad, sinful (at the end of comp. only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0554-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डी
