काण्डः + -पुष्पम् The कुन्द flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपृष्ठः|काण्डपृष्ठ|कांडपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठं
काण्डः + -पृष्ठः<BR>—1 one of the military profession, a soldier; cf. काण्डस्पृष्ठः.<BR>—2 the husband of a Vaiśya woman.<BR>—3 an adopted son, any other than oneʼs own son.<BR>—4 (as a term of reproach) a base-born fellow, one who is faithless to<BR> his family, caste, religion, profession &c. In Mv. 3 Jāmadagnya is styled<BR> by शतानन्द as काण्डपृष्ठ. (स्वकुलं पृष्ठतः कृत्वा यो वै परकुलं<BR> व्रजेत् । तेन दुश्चरितेनासौ काण्डपृष्ठ इति स्मृतः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपृष्ठम्
काण्डः + -पृष्ठः + -ष्ठम् the bow of Karṇa & Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डभङ्गः|काण्डभङ्ग
काण्डः + -भङ्गः, -भग्नम् a fracture of the bone or limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डभग्नम्
काण्डः + -भङ्गः, -भग्नम् a fracture of the bone or limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डवीणा|कांडवीणा
काण्डः + -वीणा the lute of a Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डसन्धिः|काण्डसन्धि|कांडसंधि|काण्डसंधि
काण्डः + -सन्धिः a knot, joint (as of a plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डस्पृष्टः|काण्डस्पृष्ट|कांडस्पृष्ट
काण्डः + -स्पृष्टः one who lives by arms, a warrior, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डहीनम्
काण्डः + -हीनम् a kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डमायनः|काण्डमायन
काण्डमायनः N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डवत्|कांडवत्|काण्डवन्त्
काण्डवत् <i>m.</i> An archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डारः|काण्डार
काण्डारः A kind of mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डालः|काण्डाल|कांडालः
काण्डालः A reed-basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डिका|कांडिका
काण्डिका<BR>—1 A kind of corn (Mar. लांक).<BR>—2 A kind of gourd.<BR>—3 A part or division of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डीरः|काण्डीर|कांडीर|कांडीरः
काण्डीरः [काण्ड-इरन् ईरच् वा P. V. 2. 111.] An archer (this<BR> word also is sometimes used like काण्डपृष्ठ as a term of reproach; cf. Mv. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डेरी
काण्डेरी The Mañjiṣṭhā plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डोलः|काण्डोल|कांडोल|कांडोलः
काण्डोलः A basket of reed; see कण्डोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्वः|काण्व
काण्वः A descendant or follower of Kaṇva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ण्वाः
काण्वः + .{@-ण्वाः@} <i>m.</i> pl. The school of Kāṇvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्
कात् <i>ind.</i> An exclamation of abuse or insult, usually in combination<BR> with कृ; कात्कृ to insult, dishonour; यन्मयैश्वर्यमत्तेन गुरुः<BR> सदसि कात्कृतः Bhāg. 6. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातन्त्रम्
कातन्त्रम् N. of a grammar (said to have been written by Śarvavarman<BR> through the favour of Kārttikeya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर <i>a.</i> [ईषत्तरति स्वकार्यसिद्धिं गच्छति तॄ-अच् कोः कादेशः Tv.]<BR>—1 Cowardly, timid, discouraged; वर्जयन्ति च कातरान् Pt. 4. 42;<BR> Amaru. 8, 34, 77; R. 11. 78; Me. 79.<BR>—2 Distressed, grieved, afraid; किमेवं कातरासि Ś. 4.<BR>—3 Agitated; perplexed, confused; उन्मत्तप्रेमसंरम्भादारभन्ते यदङ्गनाः ।<BR> तत्र प्रत्यूहमाधातुं ब्रह्मापि खलु कातरः ॥ Bh. 1. 60.<BR>—4 Tremulous through fear (as eyes); R. 2. 52; Amaru. 79.<BR>—5 Eager; सन्तं वयसि कैशोरे भृत्यानुग्रहकातरम् Bhāg. 3. 28. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरः|कातर
कातर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A large kind of fish.<BR>—2 A boat, raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर्यम्
कातर्यम् Cowardice; कातर्यं केवला नीतिः शौर्यं श्वापदचेष्टितम् R. 17. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातलः|कातल
कातलः A large species of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काति
काति <i>a.</i> Wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातीय|कातीयः
कातीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातीयः|कातीय
कातीय + .{@-यः@} A pupil of the sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनः|कात्यायन
कात्यायनः<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated writer on grammar who wrote Vārtikas to supplement<BR> the Sūtras of Pāṇini; न स्म पुराद्यतन इति ब्रुवता कात्यायनेनेह<BR> Mbh. on P. III. 2. 118; Rām. 2. 67. 3.<BR>—2 N. of a sage who is a writer on civil and religious law; Y. 1. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कात्यायनसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनसूत्रम्
कात्यायनः + -सूत्रम् the Śrauta sūtras of Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनी
कात्यायनी<BR>—1 An elderly or middle aged widow (dressed in red clothes).<BR>—2 N. of a wife of Yājñavalkya मैत्रेयी च कात्यायनी च Bṛ. Up. 4. 5. 1.<BR>—3 N. of Pārvatī; cf. उमा कात्यायनी गौरी काली हैमवतीश्वरी Ak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कात्यायनीतन्त्रम्, कात्यायनीपुत्रः, कात्यायनीसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीतन्त्रम्
कात्यायनी + -तन्त्रम् <i>n.</i> a Tantra containing the description of the methods<BR> of दुर्गापूजा and said to have been composed by Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीपुत्रः|कात्यायनीपुत्र
कात्यायनी + -पुत्रः, -सुतः N. of Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीसुतः|कात्यायनीसुत
कात्यायनी + -पुत्रः, -सुतः N. of Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीय|कात्यायनीयः
कात्यायनीय <i>a.</i> Composed by Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीयः|कात्यायनीय
कात्यायनीय + .{@-यः@} A pupil of the sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातुः|कातु
कातुः A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथंचित्क|काथञ्चित्क
काथंचित्क <i>a.</i> (-त्की <i>f.</i>) Accomplished with difficulty.<BR> यथैव तस्य काथंचित्कः प्रयोगः एवं वृत्तिरपि भविष्यति Mbh. on P. V. 1. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथिकः|काथिक
काथिकः [कथायां साधुः, कथा-ठक्] A narrator of stories; also<BR> a writer of stories.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बः|कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः
कादम्बः [cf. Uṇ. 4. 83]<BR>—1 A kind of goose (कलहंस); क्वचित्खगानां प्रियमानसानां कादम्बसंसर्गवतीव<BR> भूमिः R. 13. 55; Ṛs. 4. 9.<BR>—2 An arrow; कादम्बानामेकपातैरसीव्यत् Śi. 18. 29; cf. कादम्बमार्गणशराः Ak.<BR>—3 A sugar-cane.<BR>—4 The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बम्
कादम्बः + .{@-म्बम्@} Flower of the Kadamba tree; कादम्बमर्धोद्गतकेसरं च R. 13. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0555-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बकः|कादम्बक|कादंबकः
कादम्बकः An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बिनी|कादंबिनी
कादम्बिनी A long line of clouds, Māl. 9. 16; मदीयमतिचुम्बिनी<BR> भवतु कापि कादम्बिनी R. G.; Bv. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरम्
कादम्बरम् —1 A spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the<BR> Kadamba tree; निषेध्य मधु माधवाः सरसमत्र कादम्बरम् Śi. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरी|कादंबरी
कादम्बरम् + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the कदम्ब tree.<BR>—2 Spirituous liquor or wine in general; कादम्बरीसाक्षिकं प्रथमसौहृदमिष्यते<BR> Ś. 6; or कादम्बरीमदविघूर्णितलोचनस्य युक्तं हि लाङ्गलभृतः पतनं<BR> पृथिव्याम् Udb.; ˚रसभरेण K. 240.<BR>—3 The fluid issuing from the temples of a rutting elephant.<BR>—4 An epithet of Sarasvatī, the goddess of learning.<BR>—5 A female cuckoo.<BR>—6 The rain-water collected into clefts or hollow places.<BR>—7 A female bird (सारिका).<BR>—8 N. of a celebrated story by Bāṇa; the heroine is of the same name,<BR> being a daughter of Citraratha Gandharva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कादम्बरबीजम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरबीजम्
कादम्बरम् + -बीजम् a ferment, yeast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादल
कादल <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to the kadalī^1 kind of deer; Rām. 3. 43. 36.<BR> (मृदूच्चकर्बुरनीलाग्ररोमा मृगविशेषः कदली).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादाचित्क|कादाचित्कं
कादाचित्क <i>a.</i> (-त्की <i>f.</i>) Incidental, occasional; Bhāg. 12. 10. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादिक्षान्तः
कादिक्षान्तः (क-आदि-क्ष-अन्त) A consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काद्रवेयः|काद्रवेय
काद्रवेयः (कद्रू टक्)<BR>—1 A kind of snake; अमृताग्रभुवः पुरेव पुच्छं वडवाभर्तुरवारि काद्रवेयैः Śi. 20. 43.<BR>—2 N. of certain Nāgas (serpent-demons) supposed to people the lower regions.<BR>—3 Son of कद्रू;^1 काद्रवेयो मन्त्रमपश्यत् Mbh. on P. I. 4. 1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानक|कानकं
कानक <i>a.</i> [कनक-अण्] Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानकम्
कानक + .{@-कम्@} The seed of a plant (जयपाल-बीज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननम्
काननम् —1 A forest, a grove; R. 12. 27, 13. 18; छन्नोपान्तः परिणतफलज्योतिभिः<BR> काननाम्रैः Me. 18, 44; काननावनि forest-ground.<BR>—2 The mouth of Brahmā.<BR>—3 A house. cf. काननं विपिने गेहे परमेष्टिमुखेऽपि च Med.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काननाग्निः, काननारिः, काननौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननाग्निः|काननाग्नि
काननम् + -अग्निः wild fire, conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननारिः|काननारि
काननम् + -अरिः a species of the mimosa tree (शमी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननौकस्
काननम् + -ओकस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an inhabitant of a forest.<BR>—2 a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानिष्ठिकम्
कानिष्ठिकम्, -का<BR> The little finger; Mb. 12. 127. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानिष्ठिका
कानिष्ठिकम्, -का<BR> The little finger; Mb. 12. 127. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानिष्ठिनेयः|कानिष्ठिनेय
कानिष्ठिनेयः, -यी<BR> [कनिष्टा-अपत्यार्थे ठक् इनङ् च] The offspring of the youngest<BR> child or wife; कृते कानिष्ठिनेयस्य ज्यैष्ठिनेयं विवासितम् Bk. 5. 84;<BR> cf. com. on Ms. 9. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानिष्ठिनेयी
कानिष्ठिनेयः, -यी<BR> [कनिष्टा-अपत्यार्थे ठक् इनङ् च] The offspring of the youngest<BR> child or wife; कृते कानिष्ठिनेयस्य ज्यैष्ठिनेयं विवासितम् Bk. 5. 84;<BR> cf. com. on Ms. 9. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानिष्ठ्यम्
कानिष्ठ्यम् The position of the youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीनः|कानीन
कानीनः [कन्याया अनूढाया अपत्यम्म् अण् कनीनादेशः P. IV. 1. 116]<BR>—1 The son of an unmarried woman; कानीनः कन्यकाजातो मातामहसुतो<BR> मतः Y. 2. 129; see also the definition given in Ms. 9. 172.<BR>—2 N. of Vyāsa. —3 N. of Karṇa. ━<i>a.</i> Suitable to or designed for the<BR> eye-ball; Suśr. 2. 353. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीयस
कानीयस <i>a.</i> younger ततः कानीयसा एव देवाः Bṛ. Up. I. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्त|कांत|कान्तं|कान्तः
कान्त <i>p. p.</i> [कम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Desired, favourite, loved, dear; कान्तं कतुं चाक्षुषम् M. 1. 4.<BR>—2 Pleasing, agreeable; भीमकान्तैर्नृपगुणैः R. 1. 16.<BR>—3 Lovely, beautiful; सर्वः कान्तमात्मीयं पश्यति Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तः|कान्त|कांत|कान्तं
कान्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A lover.<BR>—2 A husband; कान्तोदन्तः सुहृदुपगतः संगमात् किंचिदूनः Me. 102;<BR> Śi. 10. 3, 29.<BR>—3 Any beloved person.<BR>—4 The moon.<BR>—5 The spring.<BR>—6 A kind of iron.<BR>—7 A precious stone (in comp. with सूर्य, चन्द्र and अयस्).<BR>—8 An epithet of (1) Kārttikeya, (2) Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तम्
कान्त + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Saffron.<BR>—2 A kind of iron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कान्तायसम्, कान्तनावकम्, कान्तपक्षिन्, कान्तपुष्पः, कान्तलोहम्, कान्तलौहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तायसम्
कान्त + -अयसम् the loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तनावकम्
कान्त + -नावकम् <i>n.</i> Variety of hides; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपक्षिन्|कांतपक्षिन्
कान्त + -पक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a peacock (of iron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपुष्पः|कान्तपुष्प
कान्त + -पुष्पः a kind of tree (कोविदारवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तलोहम्
कान्त + -लोहम् the loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तलौहम्
कान्त + -लौहम् steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ता
कान्ता<BR>—1 A beloved or lovely woman.<BR>—2 A mistress, wife in general; कान्तासखस्य शयनीयशिलातलं ते<BR> U. 3. 21; Śi. 10. 73.<BR>—3 The Priyaṅgu creeper.<BR>—4 Large cardamoms.<BR>—5 A kind of perfume. —6 The earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहदः|कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद|कांतांघ्रिदोहद
कान्ता + -अङ्घ्रिदोहदः the Aśoka tree; see अशोक. (cf. also कान्ताचरणदोहदः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारः|कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः
कान्तारः, -रम्<BR>—1 A large or dreary forest; गृहं तु गृहिणीहीनं कान्तारादतिरिच्यते<BR> Pt. 4. 81; Bh. 1. 86; Y. 2. 38.<BR>—2 A bad road.<BR>—3 A hole, cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारम्
कान्तारः, -रम्<BR>—1 A large or dreary forest; गृहं तु गृहिणीहीनं कान्तारादतिरिच्यते<BR> Pt. 4. 81; Bh. 1. 86; Y. 2. 38.<BR>—2 A bad road.<BR>—3 A hole, cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारः|कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः
कान्तारः, -रम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A red variety of the sugar-cane.<BR>—2 Mountain ebony.<BR>—3 A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारी
कान्तारः, -रम् + .{@-री@} A kind of sugar-cane<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारम्
कान्तारः, -रम् + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A symptom.<BR>—2 A lotus.<BR>—3 A class of the six-storeyed buildings. Māna. 24. 13-14<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारकः|कान्तारक|कांतारकः
कान्तारकः A kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिः|कान्ति|कांति|कांतिः
कान्तिः [कम् भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Loveliness, beauty, Me. 15; अक्लिष्टकान्ति Ś. 5. 19.<BR>—2 Brightness, lustre, brilliance; Me. 84.<BR>—3 Personal decoration or embellishment.<BR>—4 Wish, desire.<BR>—5 (In Rhet.) Beauty enhanced by love; (S. D. thus distinguishes कान्ति<BR> from शोभा and दीप्तिः-रूपयौवनलालित्यं भोगाद्यैरङ्गभूषणम् । शोभा<BR> प्रोक्ता सैव कान्तिर्मन्मथाप्यायिता द्युतिः । कान्तिरेवातिविस्तीर्णा दीप्तिरित्यभिधीयते 130, 131).<BR>—6 A lovely or desirable woman.<BR>—7 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—8 A digit of the moon.<BR>—9 N. of Lakṣmī; भूषणानि महार्हाणि ददौ कान्तिः शुभां स्रजम् Bhāg. 10. 65. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कान्तिकर, कान्तिद, कान्तिद, कान्तिदायक, कान्तिदायिन्, कान्तिभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिकर|कांतिकर
कान्तिः + -कर <i>a.</i> beautifying, illuminating, brightening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिद|कांतिद|कान्तिदं
कान्तिः + -द <i>a.</i> beautifying, adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिदम्
कान्तिः + -द + .({@-दम्@})<BR>—1 bile.<BR>—2 clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिद|कांतिद|कान्तिदं
कान्तिः + -द, -दायक, -दायिन् <i>a.</i> adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिदायक|कांतिदायक|कान्तिदायकं
कान्तिः + -द, -दायक, -दायिन् <i>a.</i> adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिदायिन्
कान्तिः + -द, -दायक, -दायिन् <i>a.</i> adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिभृत्|कांतिभृत्
कान्तिः + -भृत् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिमत्|कांतिमत्|कान्तिमन्त्
कान्तिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lovely, beautiful, splendid; कला च सा कान्तिमती कलावतः Ku. 4. 5, 5. 71;<BR> Me. 30. ━<i>m.</i> The moon.<BR>—2 N. of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दवम्
कान्दवम् Anything roasted or baked in an iron pan or oven; “वारिणा<BR> कोमलां कृत्वा समितां लवणान्विताम् । विनीय सन्धानं किञ्चित् स्थापयेद् भाजने<BR> नवे ॥ चण्डातपे तावद्रक्षेद् यावदम्लत्वमाप्नुयात् । उद्धृत्य च पुनः<BR> पश्चात् सन्नयेद् दृढपाणिना ॥ ततोऽपूपाकृतिं कुर्याद् घनमूर्च्छितया तया ।<BR> भूर्यङ्गारप्रतप्ते तु कन्दुगर्भे निवेश्य च । पङ्केन रन्ध्रमालिप्य<BR> स्वेदयेत्तां यथाविधि ॥ कान्दवं मलकृद् वृष्यं त्रिषु दोषेषु पूजितम् ।<BR> सद्यो रुचिकरं हृद्यं शीघ्रमिन्द्रियतर्पणम् ॥” (वृन्दग्रन्थस्य कृतान्नवर्गे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0556-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दविकः|कान्दविक|कांदविक|कांदविकः
कान्दविकः A baker, a confectioner (Mar. हलवाई); गान्धिकाश्च<BR> तथा कान्दविकाः काम्बविकाः पुनः Śiva B. 31. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिश्
कान्दिश् <i>a.</i> [काम् दिशम्] Put to flight, running away, flying; Mb. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिग्भूत|कान्दिग्भूतः
कान्दिग्भूत <i>a.</i> Runaway, frightened; कान्दिग्भूतं छिन्नगात्रं<BR> विसंज्ञं, दुर्योधनो द्रक्ष्यति सर्वसैन्यम् Mb. 5. 48. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिशीक|कांदिशीक|कान्दिशीकः
कान्दिशीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Put to flight, running away, fugitive; मृगजनः कान्दिशीकः संवृत्तः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 (Hence) Terrified, afraid; Bv. 2. 178; येदिलस्यापि पृतना कान्दिशीकतमाऽभवत्<BR> Śiva B. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुब्जः|कान्यकुब्ज|कान्यकुब्जं
कान्यकुब्जः N. of a city; see कन्याकुब्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट
कापट, कापटिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कपट-ठक्]<BR>—1 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>—2 Wicked, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटिक|कापटिकः
कापट, कापटिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कपट-ठक्]<BR>—1 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>—2 Wicked, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटकः
कापट, कापटिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A flatterer, parasite.<BR>—2 A student, scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट्यम्
कापट्यम् Wickedness, fraud, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथः|कापथ
कापथः [कुत्सितः पन्थाः] A bad road; (lit. and fig.) आस्थातुं<BR> कापथं दुष्टं विषमं बहुकण्टकम् Rām. 2. 108. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथम्
कापथः + .{@-थम्@} N. of a fragrant root (उशीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल, कापालिक <i>a.</i> [कपाल-अण्-ठक्-वा]<BR>—1 Relating to skulls; कङ्कालं मुसलं घोरं कापालमथ किङ्किणीम्<BR> Rām. 1. 27. 12.<BR>—2 like a beggar; of a beggar कापालीं नृप पापिष्ठां वृत्तिमासाद्य जीवितः Mb. 12. 8. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापाल, कापालिक <i>a.</i> [कपाल-अण्-ठक्-वा]<BR>—1 Relating to skulls; कङ्कालं मुसलं घोरं कापालमथ किङ्किणीम्<BR> Rām. 1. 27. 12.<BR>—2 like a beggar; of a beggar कापालीं नृप पापिष्ठां वृत्तिमासाद्य जीवितः Mb. 12. 8. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालः|कापाल|कापालं
कापाल, कापालिक + .{@-लः, -लिकः@} A follower of a certain Śaiva sect (the left-hand<BR> order) characterized by carrying skulls of men in the form of garlands<BR> and eating and drinking from them; भस्मास्थिशकलकीर्णा कापालमिव व्रतं<BR> धत्ते Pt. 1. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिकः|कपालिक
कापाल, कापालिक + .{@-लः, -लिकः@} A follower of a certain Śaiva sect (the left-hand<BR> order) characterized by carrying skulls of men in the form of garlands<BR> and eating and drinking from them; भस्मास्थिशकलकीर्णा कापालमिव व्रतं<BR> धत्ते Pt. 1. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालम्
कापाल, कापालिक + .{@-लम्@} A kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाली
कापाल, कापालिक + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 A wreath of skulls; कापालीमुद्वहन्ती स्रजमिव धवलां कौमुदीम् Mu. 3. 20.<BR>—2 A clever woman.<BR>—3 The Embelia Ribes (Mar. वावडिंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिकत्वम्
कापालिकत्वम् Cruelty, brutality; Māl. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिन्
कापालिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva; रुद्राणामिव कापाली Mb. 7. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिक
कापिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Shaped or behaving like a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Peculiar or belonging to Kapila.<BR>—2 Taught by, or derived from, Kapila; योगशास्त्रं च निखिलं कापिलं<BR> चैव भारत Mb. 12. 325. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिलः|कापिल
कापिल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A follower of the Sāṅkhya system of philosophy propounded by Kapila.<BR>—2 Tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशम्
कापिशम् A spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायनम्
कापिशायनम्<BR>—1 Liquor; ‘कश्यं कल्पं तथा मद्यं मैरेयं कापिशायनम्’ इति वैजयन्ती;<BR> कापिशायनसुगन्धि विघूर्णन् Śi. 10. 4. कपिरपि च कापिशायनमदमत्तः Kuv. 148.<BR>—2 A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशेयः|कापिशेय
कापिशेयः An imp, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुषः|कापुरुष
कापुरुषः A mean contemptible fellow, coward, wretch; तां कापुरुषदुस्तरां<BR> युद्धभूमिमयीं नदीम् Rām. 6. 58. 32. सुसंतुष्टः कापुरुषः स्वल्पकेनापि<BR> तुष्यति Pt. 1. 25, 361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय <i>a.</i> Belonging or peculiar to a monkey; कच्चिन्न खलु<BR> कापेयी सेव्यते चलचित्तता Rām. 6. 127. 23; Mv. 5. 63.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">Page0557-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेयम्
कापेय + .{@-यम्@} monkey tricks; P. V. 1. 127. {@कापेयम्@} [कपेर्भावः<BR> कर्म वा ढक्]<BR>—1 The monkey species.<BR>—2 Monkey-like behaviour, monkey tricks. एतदप्यस्य कापेयं यदर्कमुपतिष्ठति<BR> Mbh. on P. I. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेयः|कापेय|कापेयं
कापेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>N. of a sage, the son of कपिः शौनकः कापेयः Ch. Up. 4. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>) [कपोत-अण्]<BR>—1 grey, of a dirty white colour.<BR>—2 Not hoarding much, very frugal; स्तुवन्वृत्तिं च कापोतीं दुहित्रा स<BR> ययौ पुरात् Bhāg. 9. 18. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोतम्
कापोत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A flock of pigeons.<BR>—2 Antimony.<BR>—3 Natron.<BR>—4 Fossil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोतः|कापोत|कापोतं
कापोत + .{@-तः@} The grey colour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कापोताञ्जनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोताञ्जनम्
कापोत + -अञ्जनम् antimony applied to the eyes as collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यः|काप्य
काप्यः^1 <i>m.</i> N. of a sage^2, son of कपि, पतञ्जलः काप्यः Bṛ. Up. 3. 7. 1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/166. note: Added masculine lex tag..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकरः|काप्यकर
काप्यकरः, -कारः<BR> A penitent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकारः|काप्यकार
काप्यकरः, -कारः<BR> A penitent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकारः|काप्यकार
काप्यकारः Avowal or confession of sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काफलः|काफल
काफलः A bitter seed (Mar. कायफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काबन्ध्यम्
काबन्ध्यम् The state of being a trunk; इन्द्रास्त्रकृतकाबन्ध्यः पूतोऽस्मि<BR> भवदाश्रयात् Mv. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्
काम् <i>ind.</i> An interjection used in calling out to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामः|काम|कामं
कामः [कम्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Wish, desire; संतानकामाय R. 2. 65, 3. 67; oft. used with the<BR> inf. form; गन्तुकामः desirous to go; संगात्संजायते कामः Bg. 2. 62;<BR> Ms. 2. 94.<BR>—2 Object of desire; सर्वान् कामान् समश्नुते Ms. 2. 5; Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 25.<BR>—3 Affection, love.<BR>—4 Love or desire of sensual enjoyments, considered as one of the ends<BR> of life (पुरुषार्थ); cf. अर्थ and अर्थकाम.<BR>—5 Desire of carnal gratification, lust; Ms. 2. 214; न मय्यावेशितधियां<BR> कामः कामाय कल्पते Bhāg. 10. 22. 26.<BR>—6 The god of love.<BR>—7 N. of Pradyumna.<BR>—8 N. of Balarāma.<BR>—9 A kind of mango tree.<BR>—10 The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामा
कामः + .{@-मा@} Desire, wish; उवाच च महासर्पं कामया ब्रूहि पन्नग Mb. 3. 179. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामम्
कामः + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Object of desire.<BR>—2 Semen virile. [Kāma is the Cupid of the Hindu mythology the son of<BR> Kṛṣṇa and Rukmiṇī. His wife is Rati. When the gods wanted a commander<BR> for their forces in their war with Tāraka, they sought the aid of Kāma<BR> in drawing the mind of Śiva towards Pārvatī, whose issue alone could<BR> vanquish the demon. Kāma undertook the mission; but Śiva, being offended<BR> at the disturbance of his penance, burnt him down with the fire of his<BR> third eye. Subsequently he was allowed by Śiva to be born again in the<BR> form of Pradyumna at the request of Rati. His intimate friend is Vasanta<BR> or the spring; and his son is Aniruddha. He is armed with a bow and arrows<BR> −the bow-string being a line of bees, and arrows of flowers of five<BR> different plants].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कामाग्निः, कामाङ्कुशः, कामाङ्गः, कामाधिकारः, कामाधिष्ठित, कामानलः, कामान्ध, कामान्धा, कामान्निन्, कामाभिकाम, कामारण्यम्, कामारिः, कामार्थिन्, कामावतारः, कामावशायिता, कामावसायिता, कामावसायः, कामाशनम्, कामाख्या, कामाक्षी, कामातुर, कामात्मजः, कामात्मन्, कामायुधम्, कामायुस्, कामार्त, कामाश्रमः, कामासक्त, कामेष्टः, कामेप्सु, कामेशः, कामेश्वरः, कामोदकम्, कामोपहत, कामकला, कामकाम, कामकामिन्, कामकार, कामकूटः, कामकृत्, कामकेलि, कामक्रीडा, कामग, कामगति, कामगुणः, कामचर, कामचार, कामचार, कामचारिन्, कामज, कामजः, कामजननी, कामजानः, कामजानिः, कामजित्, कामतन्त्रम्, कामतालः, कामद, कामदहनम्, कामदा, कामदर्शन, कामदानम्, कामदुघ, कामदुघा, कामदुह्, कामदूती, कामदृश्, कामदेव, कामदोहिन्, कामधर्मः, कामधेनुः, कामध्वंसिन्, कामपति, कामपत्नी, कामपालः, कामप्रद, कामप्रवेदनम्, कामप्रश्नः, कामफलः, कामफला, कामभाज्, कामभोगाः, काममहः, काममालिन्, काममूढ, काममोहित, कामरसः, कामरसिक, कामरूप, कामरूपिन्, कामरेखा, कामलेखा, कामलता, कामलोल, कामवरः, कामवल्लभः, कामवश, कामवश्य, कामवाद, कामविहन्तृ, कामवीर्य, कामवृक्षम्, कामवृत्त, कामवृत्ति, कामवृद्धिः, कामवृन्ता, कामशर, कामशास्त्रम्, कामसंयोगः, कामसखः, कामसू, कामसूत्रम्, कामहैतुक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाग्निः|कामाग्नि
कामः + -अग्निः<BR>—1 a fire of love, violent or ardent love.<BR>—2 violent desire, fire of passion. ˚संदीपनम्<BR>—1 inflaming fire of love.<BR>—2 an aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाग्निसंदीपनम्
कामः + -अग्निः + ˚संदीपनम्<BR>—1 inflaming fire of love.<BR>—2 an aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्कुशः|कामाङ्कुश|कामांकुश
कामः + -अङ्कुशः<BR>—1 a fingernail (which plays an important part in erotic acts).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">Page0558-1</a>]<BR>—2 the male organ of generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्गः|कामाङ्ग|कामांग
कामः + -अङ्गः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिकारः|कामाधिकार
कामः + -अधिकारः the influence of love or desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिष्ठित
कामः + -अधिष्ठित <i>a.</i> overcome by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामानलः|कामानल
कामः + -अनलः see कामाग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्ध|कामांध|कामान्धः
कामः + -अन्ध <i>a.</i> blinded by love or passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्धः|कामान्ध|कामांध
कामः + -अन्ध + ({@-न्धः@}) the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्धा|कामांधा
कामः + -अन्धा musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्निन्
कामः + -अन्निन् <i>a.</i> getting food at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाभिकाम
कामः + -अभिकाम <i>a.</i> libidinous, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारण्यम्
कामः + -अरण्यम् a pleasant grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारिः|कामारि
कामः + -अरिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva; ते समेत्य तु कामारिं त्रिपुरारिं त्रिलोचनम् Rām. 7. 6. 3.<BR>—2 a mineral substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामार्थिन्
कामः + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> amorous, lustful, lascivious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावतारः|कामावतार
कामः + -अवतारः N. of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावशायिता
कामः + -अवशायिता, -अवसायिता <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Self-control.<BR>—2 a kind of Yogic power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायिता
कामः + -अवशायिता, -अवसायिता <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Self-control.<BR>—2 a kind of Yogic power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायः|कामावसाय
कामः + -अवसायः suppression of passion or desire, stoicism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाशनम्
कामः + -अशनम्<BR>—1 eating at will.<BR>—2 unrestrained enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाख्या
कामः + -आख्या, -अक्षी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाक्षी
कामः + -आख्या, -अक्षी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामातुर|कामातुरः
कामः + -आतुर <i>a.</i> love-sick, affected by love; कामातुराणां न भयं<BR> न लज्जा Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मजः|कामात्मज
कामः + -आत्मजः an epithet of Aniruddha, son of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मन्
कामः + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> lustful, libidinous, enamoured. कामात्मानः स्वर्गफलाः<BR> Bg. 2. 43; Mb. 1. 119. 3-4; Ms. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुधम्
कामः + -आयुधम्<BR>—1 arrow of the god of love.<BR>—2 membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुधः|कामायुध
कामः + -आयुधम् + .({@-धः@}) the mango-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुस्
कामः + -आयुस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a vulture.<BR>—2 Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामार्त|कामार्त्त|कामार्त्तः
कामः + -आर्त <i>a.</i> love-stricken, affected by love; कामार्ता हि प्रकृतिकृपणाश्चेतनाचेतनेषु Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाश्रमः|कामाश्रम
कामः + -आश्रमः the hermitage of the god of love; Rām. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्त
कामः + -आसक्त <i>a.</i> overcome with love or desire, impassioned, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेष्टः|कामेष्ट
कामः + -इष्टः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेप्सु
कामः + -ईप्सु <i>a.</i> striving to obtain a desired object, यत्तु कामेप्सुना<BR> कर्म Bg. 18. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेशः|कामेश
कामः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera;<BR>—2 the Supreme soul.<BR>—3 a person possessing all wealth. अपास्य कामान्कामेशो वसेत्तत्राविचारयन्<BR> Mb. 12. 287. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेश्वरः|कामेश्वर
कामः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera;<BR>—2 the Supreme soul.<BR>—3 a person possessing all wealth. अपास्य कामान्कामेशो वसेत्तत्राविचारयन्<BR> Mb. 12. 287. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदकम्
कामः + -उदकम्<BR>—1 voluntary libation of water.<BR>—2 a voluntary libation of water to deceased friends exclusive of those<BR> who are entitled to it by law; कामोदकं सखिप्रत्तास्वस्रीयश्वशुरर्त्विजाम् Y. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोपहत
कामः + -उपहत <i>a.</i> affected by or overcome with passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकला
कामः + -कला N. of Rati, the wife of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकाम
कामः + -काम, -कामिन् <i>a.</i> following the dictates of love or passion,<BR> गतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते Bg. 9. 21; स शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी Bg. 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकामिन्
कामः + -काम, -कामिन् <i>a.</i> following the dictates of love or passion,<BR> गतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते Bg. 9. 21; स शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी Bg. 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकार|कामकारः
कामः + -कार <i>a.</i> acting at will, indulging oneʼs desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकारः|कामकार
कामः + -कार + ({@-रः@})<BR>—1 voluntary action, spontaneous deed; Rām. 2. 101. 18; Ms. 11. 41, 45.<BR>—2 desire, influence of desire; अयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते Bg. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकूटः|कामकूट
कामः + -कूटः<BR>—1 the paramour of a harlot.<BR>—2 harlotry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकृत्
कामः + -कृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 acting at will, acting as one likes.<BR>—2 granting or fulfilling a desire. ━(<i>m.</i>) the Supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकेलि|कामकेलिः
कामः + -केलि <i>a.</i> lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकेलिः|कामकेलि
कामः + -केलि + ({@-लिः@})<BR>—1 a paramour.<BR>—2 amorous sport.<BR>—3 copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामक्रीडा
कामः + -क्रीडा<BR>—1 dalliance of love, amorous sport.<BR>—2 copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामग
कामः + -ग <i>a.</i> going of oneʼs own accord, able to act or move as one<BR> likes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगा
कामः + -ग + ({@-गा@})<BR>—1 an unchaste or libidinous woman; Y. 3. 6.<BR>—2 a female Kokila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगति
कामः + -गति <i>a.</i> able to go to any desired place; अध्यास्त कामगति<BR> सावरजो विमानम् R. 13. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगुणः|कामगुण
कामः + -गुणः<BR>—1 the quality of passion, affection.<BR>—2 satiety, perfect enjoyment.<BR>—3 an object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचर
कामः + -चर, -चार <i>a.</i> moving freely or unrestrained, wandering at<BR> will; सर्वेषु लोकेष्वकामचारो भवति Bṛ. Up. 7. 25. 2; नारदः<BR> कामचरः Ku. 1. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचार|कामचारः
कामः + -चर, -चार <i>a.</i> moving freely or unrestrained, wandering at<BR> will; सर्वेषु लोकेष्वकामचारो भवति Bṛ. Up. 7. 25. 2; नारदः<BR> कामचरः Ku. 1. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचार|कामचारः
कामः + -चार <i>a.</i> unchecked, unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारः|कामचार
कामः + -चार + ({@-रः@})<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">Page0558-2</a>]<BR>—1 unrestrained motion.<BR>—2 independent or wilful action, wantonness; न कामचारो मयि शङ्कनीयः R. 14. 62.<BR>—3 oneʼs will or pleasure, free will; अव्यपवृक्ते कामचारः Mbh. on<BR> Śiva Sūtra 3. 4. कामचारानुज्ञा Sk.; Ms. 2. 220.<BR>—4 sensuality.<BR>—5 selfishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारिन्
कामः + -चारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 moving unrestrained; Me. 65.<BR>—2 libidinous, lustful.<BR>—3 self-willed. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 Garuḍa.<BR>—2 a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामज|कामजः
कामः + -ज <i>a.</i> produced by passion or desire; Ms. 7. 46, 47, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजः|कामज
कामः + -जः anger; रथो वेदी कामजो युद्धमग्निः Mb. 12. 24. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजननी
कामः + -जननी betel-pepper (नागवेली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजानः|कामजान
कामः + -जानः, -जानिः See कामतालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजानिः
कामः + -जानः, -जानिः See कामतालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजित्
कामः + -जित् <i>a.</i> conquering love or passion; R. 9. 33. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामतन्त्रम्
कामः + -तन्त्रम् N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामतालः|कामताल
कामः + -तालः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामद|कामदः
कामः + -द <i>a.</i> fulfilling a desire, granting a request or desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदः|कामद
कामः + -द + .({@-दः@}) an epithet of Skanda and of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदहनम्
कामः + -दहनम् a particular festival on the day of full moon in the<BR> month फाल्गुन (Mar. होलिकोत्सव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदा
कामः + -दा = कामधेनु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदर्शन
कामः + -दर्शन <i>a.</i> looking lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदानम्
कामः + -दानम्<BR>—1 a gift to oneʼs satisfaction.<BR>—2 a kind of ceremony among prostitutes; B. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुघ
कामः + -दुघ <i>a.</i> ‘milking oneʼs desires’, granting every desired object;<BR> प्रीता कामदुघा हि सा R. 1. 81, 2. 63; Māl. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुघा
कामः + -दुघा, -दुह् <i>f.</i> a fabulous cow yielding all desires; आयुधानामहं<BR> वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक् Bg. 10. 28. स्वर्गे लोके कामधुग्भवति<BR> Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुह्
कामः + -दुघा, -दुह् <i>f.</i> a fabulous cow yielding all desires; आयुधानामहं<BR> वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक् Bg. 10. 28. स्वर्गे लोके कामधुग्भवति<BR> Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदूती
कामः + -दूती the female cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदृश्
कामः + -दृश् <i>f.</i> a woman; विमोचितुं कामदृशां विहारकीडामृगो यन्निगडो<BR> विसर्गः Bhāg. 7. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदेव
कामः + -देव<BR>—1 the god of love.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदोहिन्
कामः + -दोहिन् <i>a.</i> granting desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामधर्मः|कामधर्म
कामः + -धर्मः amorous behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामधेनुः|कामधेनु
कामः + -धेनुः <i>f.</i> the cow of plenty, a heavenly cow yielding all desires;<BR> कलतिवलती कामधेनू; or कलिवली कामधेनू Vyākaraṇa Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामध्वंसिन्
कामः + -ध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपति
कामः + -पति, -पत्नी <i>f.</i> Rati, wife of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपत्नी
कामः + -पति, -पत्नी <i>f.</i> Rati, wife of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपालः|कामपाल
कामः + -पालः N. of Balarāma; also of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रद|कामप्रदः
कामः + -प्रद <i>a.</i> granting desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रदः|कामप्रद
कामः + -प्रद + ({@-दः@})<BR>—1 a kind of coitus.<BR>—2 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रवेदनम्
कामः + -प्रवेदनम् expressing oneʼs desire, wish or hope; कच्चित् कामप्रवेदने Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रश्नः|कामप्रश्न
कामः + -प्रश्नः an unrestrained or free question; स ह कामप्रश्नमेव<BR> वव्रे Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामफलः|कामफल
कामः + -फलः a species of the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामफला
कामः + -फलः + -ला the plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभाज्
कामः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> partaking of sensual enjoyment; कामानां त्वा कामभाजं<BR> करोमि Kaṭh. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभोगाः
कामः + -भोगाः (pl.) sensual gratifications; प्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु Bg. 16. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममहः|काममह
कामः + -महः a festival of the god of love celebrated on the full-moon<BR> day in the month of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममालिन्
कामः + -मालिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममूढ
कामः + -मूढ, -मोहित <i>a.</i> influenced or infatuated by love; यत्क्रौञ्चमिथुनादेकमवधीः<BR> काममोहितम् U. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममोहित
कामः + -मूढ, -मोहित <i>a.</i> influenced or infatuated by love; यत्क्रौञ्चमिथुनादेकमवधीः<BR> काममोहितम् U. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरसः|कामरस
कामः + -रसः<BR>—1 seminal discharge.<BR>—2 the spring^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/169. note: spling is not a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरसिक
कामः + -रसिक <i>a.</i> lustful, libidinous; क्षणमपि युवा कामरसिकः Bh. 3. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूप|कामरूपः
कामः + -रूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 taking any form at will; जानामि त्वां प्रकृतिपुरुषं कामरूपं मघोनः Me. 6.<BR>—2 beautiful, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूपाः
कामः + -रूप + .({@-पाः@}) (pl.) a district lying in the east of Bengal (the western<BR> portion of Assam); तमीशः कामरूपाणाम् R. 4. 83, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूपिन्
कामः + -रूपिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 taking any form at will; कामान्नी कामरूपी T. Up. 3. 10. 5.<BR>—2 beautiful. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 a pole-cat.<BR>—2 a boar.<BR>—3 a Vidyādhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरेखा
कामः + -रेखा, -लेखा a harlot, courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलेखा
कामः + -रेखा, -लेखा a harlot, courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलता
कामः + -लता membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलोल
कामः + -लोल <i>a.</i> overcome with passion,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">Page0559-1</a>]<BR> love-stricken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवरः|कामवर
कामः + -वरः a gift chosen at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवल्लभः|कामवल्लभ
कामः + -वल्लभः<BR>—1 the spring.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवल्लभा
कामः + -वल्लभः + .({@-भा@}) moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवश|कामवशः
कामः + -वश <i>a.</i> influenced by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवशः|कामवश
कामः + -वश + ({@-शः@}) subjection to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवश्य
कामः + -वश्य <i>a.</i> subject to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवाद
कामः + -वाद <i>a.</i> saying anything at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामविहन्तृ|कामविहंतृ
कामः + -विहन्तृ <i>a.</i> disappointing desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवीर्य
कामः + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> ‘showing heroism at will’, an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृक्षः|कामवृक्ष
कामः + -वृक्षः <i>m.</i> a parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृत्त
कामः + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> addicted to sensual gratification, licentious, dissipated;<BR> विशीलः कामवृत्तो वा गुणैर्वा परिवर्जितः । उपचर्यः स्त्रिया साध्व्या<BR> सततं देववत्पतिः ॥ Ms. 5. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृत्ति|कामवृत्तिः
कामः + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> acting according to will, self-willed, independent;<BR> न कामवृत्तिर्वचनीयमीक्षते Ku. 5. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृत्तिः|कामवृत्ति
कामः + -वृत्ति + ({@-त्तिः@}) <i>f.</i><BR>—1 free and unrestrained action.<BR>—2 freedom of will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृद्धिः|कामवृद्धि
कामः + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> increase of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृन्ता
कामः + -वृन्ता^1 the trumpet flower.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/170. note: Rest of dictionaries have this as feminine..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामशर|कामशरः
कामः + -शर<BR>—1 a love shaft.<BR>—2 the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामशास्त्रम्
कामः + -शास्त्रम् the science of love, erotic science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसंयोगः|कामसंयोग
कामः + -संयोगः attainment of desired objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसखः|कामसख
कामः + -सखः<BR>—1 the spring.<BR>—2 the month of Chaitra.<BR>—3 the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसू
कामः + -सू <i>a.</i> fulfilling any desire. किमत्र चित्रं यदि कामसूर्भूः<BR> R. 5. 33. ━<i>m.</i> N. of Vāsudeva. ━<i>f.</i> N. of Rukmiṇī;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसूत्रम्
कामः + -सूत्रम्<BR>—1 N. of an erotic work by Vātsyāyana.<BR>—2 ‘thread of love’, love-incident; औद्धत्यमायोजितकामसूत्रम् Māl. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामहैतुक
कामः + -हैतुक <i>a.</i> produced by mere desire without any real cause; Bg. 16. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामतः|कामत
कामतः, कामेन <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Of oneʼs own accord, willingly.<BR>—2 Voluntarily, knowingly, intentionally, wilfully; Ms. 4. 130; पदा<BR> स्पृष्टं च कामतः Y. 1. 168.<BR>—3 From passion or feeling, lustfully; भ्रातुर्मृतस्य भार्यायां योऽनुरज्येत<BR> कामतः Ms. 3. 173.<BR>—4 At will, freely, unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेन
कामतः, कामेन <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Of oneʼs own accord, willingly.<BR>—2 Voluntarily, knowingly, intentionally, wilfully; Ms. 4. 130; पदा<BR> स्पृष्टं च कामतः Y. 1. 168.<BR>—3 From passion or feeling, lustfully; भ्रातुर्मृतस्य भार्यायां योऽनुरज्येत<BR> कामतः Ms. 3. 173.<BR>—4 At will, freely, unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन|कामनः
कामन <i>a.</i> Lustful, libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामनम्
कामन + .{@-नम्@} Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामना
कामन + .{@-ना@} Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामनीयकम्
कामनीयकम्, कामनीयम् Beauty, attractiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामनीयम्
कामनीयकम्, कामनीयम् Beauty, attractiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन्धमिन्|कामंधमिन्
कामन्धमिन् <i>m.</i> Brazier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामम्
कामम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to wish or inclination, at will; कामंगामीः<BR>—2 Agreebly {sic} to desire; ये तिष्ठन्ति भवन्तु तेऽपि गमने कामं प्रकामोद्यमाः Mu. 1. 25.<BR>—3 To the heartʼs content, U. 3. 16.<BR>—4 Willingly, joyfully; Śānti. 4. 4.<BR>—5 Well, very well (a particle of assent), it may be that; मनागनभ्यावृत्त्या<BR> वा कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी Śi. 2. 43.<BR>—6 Granted or admitted (that), true that, no doubt, (generally followed<BR> by तु, तथापि, yet, still); कामं न तिष्ठति मदाननसंमुखी सा<BR> भूयिष्ठमन्यविषया न तु दृष्टिरस्याः Ś. 1. 30, 2. 1; कामं कर्णान्तविश्रान्ते<BR> विशाले तस्य लोचने R. 4. 13; कामं जीवति मे नाथः R. 12. 75; कामं<BR> नृपाः सन्तु सहस्रशोऽन्ये R. 6. 22; Māl. 9. 34.<BR>—7 Indeed, forsooth, really; R. 2. 43; (often implying unwillingness or<BR> contradiction).<BR>—8 Better, rather (usually with न); काममामरणात्तिष्ठेद् गृहे कन्यर्तुमत्यपि ।<BR> न चैवेनां प्रयच्छेत्तु गुणहीनाय कर्हिचित् ॥ Ms. 9. 89; H. 1. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयमान
कामयमान, कामयान, कामयितृ <i>a.</i> Lustful, libidinous;<BR> स्त्रियमकृत विरूपां स्त्रीजितः कामयागम् Bhāg. 10. 47. 17; R. 19. 50; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयान
कामयमान, कामयान, कामयितृ <i>a.</i> Lustful, libidinous;<BR> स्त्रियमकृत विरूपां स्त्रीजितः कामयागम् Bhāg. 10. 47. 17; R. 19. 50; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयितृ
कामयमान, कामयान, कामयितृ <i>a.</i> Lustful, libidinous;<BR> स्त्रियमकृत विरूपां स्त्रीजितः कामयागम् Bhāg. 10. 47. 17; R. 19. 50; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामल|कामलः
कामल <i>a.</i> Lustful, libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलः|कामल
कामल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 The spring.<BR>—2 A desert.<BR>—3 Excessive obstruction of bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलिन्
कामलिन् <i>a.</i> Suffering from jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलिका
कामलिका Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवत्|कामवन्त्
कामवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirous, wishing.<BR>—2 Lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिः|कामि
कामिः A libidinous man, lecher. ━<i>f.</i> N. of Rati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिक|कामिकः
कामिक <i>a.</i> Desired, wished for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिकः|कामिक
कामिक + .{@-कः@} A wild duck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामित
कामित <i>a.</i> Wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामितम्
कामित + .{@-तम्@} A desire, wish, love; दरिद्रस्येव कामितम् Mb. 8. 9. 19.<BR> वदति हि संवृत्तिरेव कामितानि Ki. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिन्
कामिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) [कम्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Lustful.<BR>—2 Desirous.<BR>—3 Loving, fond. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A lover, a lustful person (paying particular attention to ladies);<BR> त्वया चन्द्रमसा चातिसन्धीयते कामिजनसार्थः Ś. 3; त्वां कामिनो<BR> मदनदूतिमुदाहरन्ति V. 4. 11; Amaru. 2; M. 3. 14.<BR>—2 A uxorious^1 husband.<BR>—3 The ruddy goose or चक्रवाक bird.<BR>—4 A sparrow.<BR>—5 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—6 The moon.<BR>—7 A pigeon.<BR>—8 The Supreme Being.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260622. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिनी
कामिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A loving, affectionate, or fond woman; Ms. 8. 112.<BR>—2 A lovely or beautiful woman; उदयति हि शशाङ्कः कामिनीगण्डपाण्डुः<BR> Mk. 1. 57; केषां नैषा कथय कविताकामिनी कौतुकाय P. R. 1. 22.<BR>—3 A woman (in general); मृगया जहार चतुरेव कामिनी R. 9. 69; Me. 65;<BR> Ṛs. 1. 28.<BR>—4 A timid woman.<BR>—5 Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुक|कामुकः
कामुक <i>a.</i> (-का or -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कम्-उकञ् P. III. 2. 154.]<BR>—1 Wishing, desirous. दुर्योधनमवाचीनं राज्यकामुकमातुरम् Mb. 8. 8. 17.<BR>—2 Lustful, libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुकः|कामुक
कामुक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A lover, a libidinous man. दास्याः कामुकः, वृषल्याः कामुकः Mbh.<BR> on P. II. 3. 69. कामुकैः कुम्भीलकैश्च परिहर्तव्या चन्द्रिका M. 4;<BR> R. 19. 33; Ṛs. 6. 9.<BR>—2 A sparrow.<BR>—3 The Aśoka tree. ˚कान्ता <i>f.</i> N. of Mādhavi creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुका
कामुक + .{@-का@} A woman desirous of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुकी
कामुक + .{@-की@} A libidinous or lustful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्य|काम्यं
काम्य <i>a.</i> [कम्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be desired, desirable; सुधा विष्ठा च काम्याशनम् Śānti. 2. 8.<BR>—2 Optional, performed for some particular object (opp. नित्य); अन्ते<BR> काम्यस्य कर्मणः R. 10. 50; Ms. 2. 2, 12. 89; Bg. 18. 2.<BR>—3 Beautiful, lovely, charming, handsome; नासौ न काम्यः R. 6. 30; U. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यम्
काम्य + .{@-म्यम्@} A class of buildings (Māna. 31. 2. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्या
काम्य + .{@-म्या@}<BR>—1 A wish, desire, intention, request; ब्राह्मणकाम्या Mk. 3; R. 1. 35; Bg. 10. 1.<BR>—2 A cow; ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काम्याभिप्रायः, काम्यकर्मन्, काम्यगिर्, काम्यदानम्, काम्यमरणम्, काम्यव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्याभिप्रायः|काम्याभिप्राय
काम्य + -अभिप्रायः a self-interested motive or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यकर्मन्|काम्यकर्म्मन्
काम्य + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> a rite performed for some particular object and<BR> with a view to future fruition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यगिर्
काम्य + -गिर् <i>a.</i> sweet-voiced, having a pleasing voice; प्रियसखीसदृशं<BR> प्रतिबोधिताः किमपि काम्यगिरा परपुष्टया Śi. 6. 8. ━(<i>f.</i>) an agreeable speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यदानम्
काम्य + -दानम्<BR>—1 an acceptable gift.<BR>—2 a free-will offering; voluntary gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यमरणम्
काम्य + -मरणम् voluntary death, suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यव्रतम्
काम्य + -व्रतम्^1 voluntary vow.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260427. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यकः|काम्यक
काम्यकः N. of a forest, of a lake; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठ
कामठ <i>a.</i> [कमठ-अण्] Peculiar or belonging to the tortoise.<BR> इति श्रुत्वा हृषीकेशः कामठं रूपमास्थितः Rām. 1. 45. 29.<BR> … … कामठीं तनुमाददे Śiva B. 13. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठक
कामठक<BR>—1 N. of धृतराष्ट्र.<BR>—2 N. of one of the serpents burnt in the सर्पसत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामण्डलुक
कामण्डलुक <i>a.</i> (A pearl) shaped like a कमण्डलु; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन्दकिः|कामन्दकि
कामन्दकिः N. of the author of a नीतिसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामातुः
कामातुः N. of a plant (रक्तकाञ्चन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामालिका
कामालिका Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिनीशः|कामिनीश
कामिनीशः The शोभाञ्जन tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामीलः|कामील
कामीलः A kind of betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुकायनः|कामुकायन
कामुकायनः N. of an old authority quoted in the MS. by Jaimini (MS. 11. 1. 56, 61).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदा
कामोदा A musical note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिलः|काम्पिल|कांपिलः
काम्पिलः, काम्पिल्लः, काम्पिल्लकः<BR>—1 N. of a tree; काम्पिल्लकप्रसवपाटवगण्डपालि Māl. 9. 31.<BR>—2 A perfume (शुण्डारोचनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्लः|काम्पिल्ल|कांपिल्ल|कांपिल्लः
काम्पिलः, काम्पिल्लः, काम्पिल्लकः<BR>—1 N. of a tree; काम्पिल्लकप्रसवपाटवगण्डपालि Māl. 9. 31.<BR>—2 A perfume (शुण्डारोचनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्लकः|काम्पिल्लक|कांपिल्लकः
काम्पिलः, काम्पिल्लः, काम्पिल्लकः<BR>—1 N. of a tree; काम्पिल्लकप्रसवपाटवगण्डपालि Māl. 9. 31.<BR>—2 A perfume (शुण्डारोचनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बलः|काम्बल|कांबल|कांबलः
काम्बलः [कम्बल-अण्] A carriage covered with a woollen cloth or blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बलिकः|काम्बलिक
काम्बलिकः Gruel, barley-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बविकः|काम्बविक|कांबविक|कांबविकः
काम्बविकः [कम्बु-ठक्] A vendor of shell ornaments, dealer in<BR> shells. गान्धिकाश्च तथा कान्दविकाः काम्बविकाः पुनः Śiva B. 31. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोजः|काम्बोज|कांबोज|कांबोजः
काम्बोजः [कम्बोज-अण्]<BR>—1 A native of the Kambojas; Ms. 10. 44.<BR>—2 A king of the Kambojas.<BR>—3 The Punnāga tree.<BR>—4 A species of horse from the Kamboja country. शतं वै यस्तु काम्बोजान्ब्राह्मणेभ्यः<BR> प्रयच्छति Mb. 12. 35. 14.<BR>—5 A conch.<BR>—6 A kind of plant (सोमवल्क); काम्बोजो हस्तिभेदे च शङ्खदेशविशेषयोः ।<BR> अश्वे पुंनागवृक्षे च सोमवल्के तदिष्यते ॥ Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काम्बोजास्तरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोजास्तरणम्
काम्बोजः + -आस्तरणम् a blanket; Mb. 11. 25. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोजी
काम्बोजी <i>f.</i> A kind of plant (माषपर्णी, हिंगुपर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ल
काम्ल [ईषदम्लम्] Slightly acid, aciduous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायः|काय|कायं
कायः, -यम्<BR> [चीयतेऽस्मिन् अस्थ्यादिकमिति काय; चि-घञ् आदेः ककारः<BR> P. III. 3. 41. Sk.]<BR>—1 The body; विभाति कायः करुणापराणां परोपकारैर्न तु चन्दनेन<BR> Bh. 2. 71; कायेन मनसा बुद्धया Bg. 5. 11; so कायेन, वाचा, मनसा &c.<BR>—2 The trunk of a tree.<BR>—3 The body of a lute (the whole lute except the wires).<BR>—4 A multitude, assemblage, collection.<BR>—5 Principal, capital.<BR>—6 Home, residence, habitation.<BR>—7 A butt, a mark.<BR>—8 Natural temperament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायम्
कायः, -यम्<BR> [चीयतेऽस्मिन् अस्थ्यादिकमिति काय; चि-घञ् आदेः ककारः<BR> P. III. 3. 41. Sk.]<BR>—1 The body; विभाति कायः करुणापराणां परोपकारैर्न तु चन्दनेन<BR> Bh. 2. 71; कायेन मनसा बुद्धया Bg. 5. 11; so कायेन, वाचा, मनसा &c.<BR>—2 The trunk of a tree.<BR>—3 The body of a lute (the whole lute except the wires).<BR>—4 A multitude, assemblage, collection.<BR>—5 Principal, capital.<BR>—6 Home, residence, habitation.<BR>—7 A butt, a mark.<BR>—8 Natural temperament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायम्
कायः, -यम् + .{@-यम्@} (with or without तीर्थ) The part of the hand just below<BR> the fingers, especially the litle finger, or the last two fingers (this<BR> part being considered sacred to Prajāpati is called प्रजापतितीर्थ;<BR> cf. Ms. 2. 58-59).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायः|काय|कायं
कायः, -यम् + .{@-यः@} One of the eight forms of marriage, generally known as प्राजापत्य<BR> q. v.; स कायः पावयेत्तज्जः Y. 1. 60; Ms. 3. 38.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">Page0560-2</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कायाग्निः, कायक्लेशः, कायोत्सर्गः, कायचिकित्सा, कायदण्डः, कायमानम्, कायबन्धनम्, कायवलनम्, कायस्थः, कायस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायाग्निः|कायाग्नि
कायः + -अग्निः the digestive faculty. मनः कायाग्निमाहन्ति Maitr. Up. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक्लेशः|कायक्लेश
कायः + -क्लेशः bodily suffering or pain; कायक्लेशभयात्त्येजत् Bg. 18. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायोत्सर्गः|कायोत्सर्ग
कायः + -उत्सर्गः a kind of religious austerity in Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायचिकित्सा
कायः + -चिकित्सा the third of the eight departments of medical science,<BR> treatment of diseases affecting the whole body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायदण्डः|कायदण्ड
कायः + -दण्डः a complete command over oneʼs body; वाग्दण्डोऽथ मनोदण्डः<BR> कायदण्डस्तथैव च । यस्यैते निहिता बुद्धौ त्रिदण्डीति स उच्यते ॥ Ms. 12. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमानम्
कायः + -मानम् measurement of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायबन्धनम्
कायः + -बन्धनम्<BR>—1 girdle.<BR>—2 the union of semen virile and blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायवलनम्
कायः + -वलनम् an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थः|कायस्थ
कायः + -स्थः<BR>—1 the Supreme Being.<BR>—2 the writer-caste (born from a क्षत्रिय father and a शूद्र mother).<BR> कायस्थेनोदरस्थेन मातुर्मांसं न भक्षितम् । दयावृत्तिर्न चैवात्र दन्ताभावो<BR> हि कारणम् ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 a man of that caste; कायस्थ इति लघ्वी मात्रा Mu. 1; Y. 1. 336;<BR> Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्था
कायः + -स्थः + .({@-स्था@})<BR>—1 a woman of that caste.<BR>—2 the Myrobalan tree (Mar. हिरडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थी
कायः + -स्थः + .({@-स्थी@}) the wife of a कायस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थित
कायः + -स्थित <i>a.</i> corporeal, bodily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक
कायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), कायिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [काय-ठक्] Relating to the body, bodily,<BR> corporeal; कायिकतपः Ms. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिका
कायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), कायिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [काय-ठक्] Relating to the body, bodily,<BR> corporeal; कायिकतपः Ms. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिक|कायिकः
कायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), कायिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [काय-ठक्] Relating to the body, bodily,<BR> corporeal; कायिकतपः Ms. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिकी
कायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), कायिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [काय-ठक्] Relating to the body, bodily,<BR> corporeal; कायिकतपः Ms. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायका
कायक (-यिका <i>f.</i>), कायिक (-की <i>f.</i>) + .{@-का@} Interest (whatever is given for the use of money); Ms. 8. 153.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कायिका^1वृद्धिः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिकावृद्धिः|कायिकावृद्धि
कायिका^1 + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 interest consisting in the use of any animal or capital stock pawned.<BR>—2 interest of which the payment does not affect the principal, or the<BR> use of the body of an animal pledged by the person to whom it is pledged.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायवत्|कायवन्त्
कायवत् <i>a.</i> Having a body, embodied; त्रातुं लोकानिव परिणतः<BR> कायवानस्त्रवेदः U. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिन्
कायिन् <i>a.</i> large bodied; समूलशाखान्पश्यामि निहतान्कायिनो द्रुमान्<BR> Mb. 12. 113. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमानम्
कायमानम् A hut made of thatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायाधवः|कायाधव
कायाधवः N. of Prahlāda^1 (son of कयाधु); बहवो मत्पदं प्राप्तास्त्वाष्ट्रकायाधवादयः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 12. 5.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260430. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) [कृ-घञ्] (At the end of comp.)<BR> Making, doing, performing, working, maker, doer, author; ग्रन्थकारः<BR> author; कुम्भकारः, सुवर्णकारः &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारः|कार
कार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Act, action; as in पुरुषकार.<BR>—2 A term denoting a sound or a word which is not inflected; as अकार<BR> Ms. 2. 76, 125; ककार, फूत्कार &c.<BR>—3 Effort, exertion; ‘कारौ वधे निश्चये च बले यत्ने रतावपि’ इति<BR> विश्वः. Śi. 19. 27.<BR>—4 Religious austerity.<BR>—5 A husband, lord; master.<BR>—6 Determination.<BR>—7 Power, strength.<BR>—8 A tax or toll.<BR>—9 A heap of snow.<BR>—10 The Himālaya mountain.<BR>—11 Water produced by hail. —12 Killing, slaughter.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कारावरः, कारकर, कारभूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावरः|कारावर
कार + -अवरः a man of a mixed and low caste, born from a Niṣāda father<BR> and Vaidehī^1 mother; a shoemaker; कारावरो निषाद्यां तु चर्मकारः प्रसूयते<BR> Mb. 13. 48. 26; cf. Ms. 10. 36.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260430. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकर
कार + -कर <i>a.</i> working, acting as agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारभूः
कार + -भूः <i>f.</i> a toll-station^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260430. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारक|कारकं|कारकः
कारक <i>a.</i> (-रिका <i>f.</i>) [कृ-ण्वुल्] (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Making, acting, doing, performing, creating, doer &c. स्वप्नस्य कारकः<BR> Y. 3. 150, 2. 156; वर्णसंकर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">Page0561-1</a>]<BR> -कारकैः Bg. 1. 42; Ms. 7. 204; Pt. 5. 36. कारका मित्रकार्याणि<BR> सीतालाभाय सोऽब्रवीत् Bk. 7. 29.<BR>—2 An agent.<BR>—3 Intending to act or do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकम्
कारक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 (In Gram.) The relation subsisting between a noun and a verb in a sentence,<BR> (or between a noun and other words governing it); there are six such Kārakas,<BR> belonging to the first seven cases, except the genitive: (1) कर्तृ;<BR> (2) कर्मन्; (3) करण; (4) संप्रदान; (5) अपादान; (6) अधिकरण.<BR>—2 That part of grammar which treats of these relations; <i>i. e.</i> syntax.<BR>—3 Water produced from hail.<BR>—4 An organ (इन्द्रिय); जगाद जीमूतगभीरया गिरा बद्धाञ्जलीन्संवृतसर्वकारकान्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 6. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कारकगुप्तिः, कारकदीपकम्, कारकहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकगुप्तिः|कारकगुप्ति
कारक + -गुप्तिः <i>f.</i> a sentence with a hidden meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकदीपकम्
कारक + -दीपकम् (in Rhet.) Case illuminator, a figure of speech in which<BR> the same Kāraka is connected with several verbs in succession; <i>e. g.</i><BR> रिवद्यति कूणति वेल्लति विचलति निमिषति विलोकयति तिर्यक् । अन्तर्नन्दति<BR> चुम्बितुमिच्छति नवपरिणया वधूः शयने ॥ K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकहेतुः|कारकहेतु
कारक + -हेतुः the active or efficient cause (opp. ज्ञापकहेतु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकवत्|कारकवन्त्
कारकवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to one who is busy with anything.<BR>—2 Instrumental, causal, शब्दो न यत्र पुरुकारकवान्क्रियार्थः Bhāg. 2. 7. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकुक्षीयः|कारकुक्षीय
कारकुक्षीयः N. of the शाल्व country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारज
कारज <i>a.</i> Relating to the fingernail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणम्
कारणम् [कृ-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A cause, reason; कारणकोपाः कुटुम्बिन्यः M. 1. 18; R. 1. 74; Bg. 13. 21;<BR> oft. with loc. of the effect; Bh. 2. 84.<BR>—2 Ground, motive, object; प्रव्राज्य चीरवसनं किं नु पश्यसि कारणम्<BR> Rām. 2. 73. 12. किं पुनः कारणम् Mbh.; Y. 2. 203; Ms. 8. 347; कारणमानुषीं<BR> तनुम् R. 16. 22.<BR>—3 An instrument, means; गर्भस्रावे मासतुल्या निशाः शुद्धेस्तु कारणम् Y. 3. 20, 65.<BR>—4 (In Nyāya phil.) A cause, that which is invariably antecedent to some<BR> product and is not otherwise constituted; or, according to Mill, ‘the antecedent or concurrence of antecedents on which the effect is invariably and unconditionally consequent’<BR>; according to Naiyāyikas it is of three<BR> kinds; (1) समवायि (intimate or inherent); as threads in the case<BR> of cloth; (2) असमवायि (non-intimate or non-inherent), as the conjunction<BR> of the threads in the case of cloth; (3) निमित्त (instrumental) as<BR> the weaverʼs loom.<BR>—5 The generative cause, creator, father; Ku. 5. 81.<BR>—6 An element, elementary matter; Y. 3. 148; Bg. 18. 13.<BR>—7 The origin or plot of a play, poem &c.<BR>—8 An organ of sense; हित्वा तनुं कारणमानुषीं ताम्.<BR>—9 The body.<BR>—10 A sign, document, proof or authority; प्रमाणं चैव लोकस्य ब्रह्मात्रैव<BR> हि कारणम् Ms. 11. 84.<BR>—11 That on which any opinion or judgment is based.<BR>—12 Action; आत्मना कारणैश्चैव समस्येह महीक्षितः Mb. 12. 59. 130.<BR>—13 A legal instrument or document.<BR>—14 Agency, instrumentality.<BR>—15 A deity (as the proximate or remote cause of creation).<BR>—16 Killing, injuring.<BR>—17 A desire (वासना) created formerly (as पूर्ववासना);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">Page0561-2</a>]<BR> पूर्वं नित्यं सर्वगतं मनोहेतुमलक्षणम् । अज्ञानकर्मनिर्दिष्टमेतत्कारणलक्षणम् ॥<BR> Mb. 12. 211. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणा
कारणम् + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 Pain, agony.<BR>—2 Casting into hell.<BR>—3 Urging, instigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणात्
कारणम् + .{@-णा@} + .({@-कारणात्@} for the reason that; द्वेष˚ on account of hatred;<BR> मत्कारणात् for my sake; Pt. 1. 22.)<BR>—4 Action; निमित्ते कारणात्मके Mb. 12. 289. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कारणान्तरम्, कारणान्वित, कारणाख्या, कारणोत्तरम्, कारणकारणम्, कारणकारितम्, कारणगत, कारणगुणः, कारणबलवत्, कारणभूत, कारणमाला, कारणमूलम्, कारणवादिन्, कारणवारि, कारणविहीन, कारणशरीरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणान्तरम्
कारणम् + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 a particular reason; प्रविष्टोऽस्मि दुराधर्षं वालिनः कारणान्तरे<BR> Rām. 4. 10. 28;<BR>—2 instrumental cause; येन वैश्रवणो भ्राता वैमात्राः कारणान्तरे Rām. 3. 48. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणान्वित
कारणम् + -अन्वित <i>a.</i> having a cause or reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणाख्या
कारणम् + -आख्या <i>f.</i>^1 N. of the organ of perception and action, of बुद्धि,<BR> अहंकार and मनस्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260430. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणोत्तरम्
कारणम् + -उत्तरम् a special plea, denial of the cause of complaint; admission<BR> of the charge generally, but denial of the actual issue (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणकारणम्
कारणम् + -कारणम् an elementary or primary cause; an atom; त्वं कारणं<BR> कारणकारणानाम् Ki. 18. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणकारितम्
कारणम् + -कारितम् <i>ind.</i> in consequence of; यदि प्रव्राजितो रामो लोभकारणकारितम्<BR> Rām. 2. 58. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगत
कारणम् + -गत <i>a.</i> referred to its cause, resolved into its principles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगुणः|कारणगुण
कारणम् + -गुणः a quality of the cause; Sāṅ. K. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणबलवत्
कारणम् + -बलवत् <i>a.</i> strong by motives; Pt. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणभूत
कारणम् + -भूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 caused.<BR>—2 forming the cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणमाला
कारणम् + -माला a figure of speech, ‘a chain of causes’; यथोत्तरं चेत्<BR> पूर्वस्य पूर्वस्यार्थस्य हेतुता । तदा कारणमाला स्यात् K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i><BR> Bg. 2. 62, 63; also S. D. 728.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणमूलम्
कारणम् + -मूलम् (in Rhet.) a law of causation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणवादिन्
कारणम् + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a complainant, plaintiff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणवारि
कारणम् + -वारि <i>n.</i> the original water produced at the beginning of the creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणविहीन
कारणम् + -विहीन <i>a.</i> without a cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणशरीरम्
कारणम् + -शरीरम् (in Vedānta phil.) the inner rudiment of the body, causal frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणक
कारणक (At the end of comp.) Cause, reason &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणता
कारणता Causality, causation; प्रलयस्थितिसर्गाणामेकः कारणतां<BR> गतः Ku. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणिक|कारणिकः
कारणिक <i>a.</i> (-का or -की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 An examiner, a judge.<BR>—2 Causal, causative.<BR>—3 A teacher; कच्चित्कारणिका धर्मे सर्वशास्त्रेषु कोविदाः Mb. 2. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितव्य
कारयितव्य <i>a.</i> To be caused or performed; ˚दक्षा Ku. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितृ
कारयितृ, कारयिष्णु Causing to do, perform, effect &c. योऽस्यात्मनः<BR> कारयिता तं क्षेत्रज्ञं प्रचक्षते Ms. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयिष्णु
कारयितृ, कारयिष्णु Causing to do, perform, effect &c. योऽस्यात्मनः<BR> कारयिता तं क्षेत्रज्ञं प्रचक्षते Ms. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारापकः|कारापक
कारापकः A person appointed to look after the construction of a<BR> temple or a building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिः|कारि
कारिः <i>f.</i> Action, act, work; यां कारिं राजपुत्रोऽयमनुतिष्ठति …<BR> Bk. 7. 75. ━<i>m.</i> An artist, a mechanic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारित|कारितः
कारित <i>a.</i> Caused to be done or effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिता
कारित + .{@-ता@} Interest, the amount of which is fixed by the debtor (being<BR> forced to do so by the creditor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारितम्
कारित + .{@-तम्@} The causal form of a verb. कारितार्थ causal sense शेत्यर्थः<BR> कारितार्थो वा निर्देशोऽयं समीक्षितः Mbh. on P. V. 3. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिन्
कारिन् <i>a.</i> Making, doing, causing, bringing about (at the end of<BR> comp.). ━<i>m.</i> A mechanic, artist. preparer न कारिसोमं प्रपपौ अग्ने<BR> Mbh. on III. 2. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डः|कारण्ड
कारण्डः, कारण्डवः A sort of duck; Rām. 7. 31. 21; Bhāg. 8. 2. 16;<BR> तप्तं वारि विहाय तीरनलिनीं कारण्डवः सेवते V. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डवः|कारण्डव|कारंडव|कारंडवः
कारण्डः, कारण्डवः A sort of duck; Rām. 7. 31. 21; Bhāg. 8. 2. 16;<BR> तप्तं वारि विहाय तीरनलिनीं कारण्डवः सेवते V. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारन्धमिन्|कारंधमिन्
कारन्धमिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Brazier.<BR>—2 A mineralogist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारभ
कारभ <i>a.</i> Produced or coming from a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारमिहिका
कारमिहिका Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारम्भा|कारंभा
कारम्भा N. of a tree (प्रिंयङ्गु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवः|कारव
कारवः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवी
कारवी N. of many plants. (Mar. शोप, ओवा, जिरेम् इ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्लः|कारवेल्ल|कारवेल्लं
कारवेल्लः, -ल्लकः<BR>—1 N. of a bitter vegetable (Mar. कारलें ?)<BR>—2 A missile of the shape of कारवेल्ल, covered all over with sharp<BR> edges; गण्डशैलैः कारवेल्लैः लोहकण्टकवेष्टितैः Parṇāl. 4. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्लकः|कारवेल्लक
कारवेल्लः, -ल्लकः<BR>—1 N. of a bitter vegetable (Mar. कारलें ?)<BR>—2 A missile of the shape of कारवेल्ल, covered all over with sharp<BR> edges; गण्डशैलैः कारवेल्लैः लोहकण्टकवेष्टितैः Parṇāl. 4. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्करः|कारस्कर
कारस्करः [कार-स्-कर P. VI. 1. 56.] N. of a tree (किंपाक;<BR> Mar. कुचला) Bhāg. 5. 14. 12; कारस्करो वृक्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कराटिका
कारस्कराटिका A small centipede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारा
कारा<BR>—1 Imprisonment, confinement.<BR>—2 A prisonhouse, a jail; Mv. 6. 25.<BR>—3 Part of a lute below the neck.<BR>—4 Pain, affliction.<BR>—5 A female messenger.<BR>—6 A female worker in gold.<BR>—7 A sound.<BR>—8 An instrument for drawing the sound of the lute.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कारागारम्, कारागृहम्, कारावेश्मन्, कारागुप्तः, कारापालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागारम्
कारा + -अगारम्, -गृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a prison-house, a jail; कारागृहे<BR> निर्जितवासवेन लङ्केश्वरेणोषितमा प्रसादात् R. 6. 40; Śānti. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागृहम्
कारा + -अगारम्, -गृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a prison-house, a jail; कारागृहे<BR> निर्जितवासवेन लङ्केश्वरेणोषितमा प्रसादात् R. 6. 40; Śānti. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावेश्मन्
कारा + -अगारम्, -गृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a prison-house, a jail; कारागृहे<BR> निर्जितवासवेन लङ्केश्वरेणोषितमा प्रसादात् R. 6. 40; Śānti. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागुप्तः|कारागुप्त
कारा + -गुप्तः a prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारापालः|कारापाल
कारा + -पालः a guard of a prison, jailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काराधुनी
काराधुनी A musical instrument (as a conch) काराधुनीव चितयत्<BR> सहस्रैः Rv. 1. 180. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारायिका
कारायिका A female crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिका
कारिका<BR>—1 A female dancer.<BR>—2 A business, or trade<BR>—3 A memorial verse, or a collection of such verses, on grammatical, philosophical,<BR> or scientific subjects, <i>e. g.</i> Bhattojī Dīkṣitaʼs Kārikās on grammar;<BR> called वैयाकरणसिद्धान्तकारिका; सांख्यकारिका.<BR>—4 Torment, torture.<BR>—5 Interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीर
कारीर <i>a.</i> [करीर-अञ्] Made of the shoots of reed or bamboo;<BR> दुर्गतीर्था बृहत्कूला कारीरा वेत्रसंयुता Mb. 12. 82. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीषम्
कारीषम् [करीषाणां समूहः अण्] A heap of dried cowdung; ━<i>a.</i><BR> Produced from dried cow-dung; कारीषोग्निरध्यापयति Mbh. on P. III. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु <i>a.</i> (-रू <i>f.</i>) [कृ-उण् Uṇ. 1. 1]<BR>—1 A maker, doer, an agent, servant; राघवस्य ततः कार्यं कारुर्वानरपुङ्गवः Bk. 7. 28.<BR>—2 An artisan, mechanic, artist; कारुभिः कारितं तेन कृत्रिमं स्वप्नहेतवे<BR> Vb. 1. 13; इति स्म सा कारुतरेण लेखितं नलस्य च स्वस्य च सख्यमीक्षते<BR> N. 1. 38; Y. 2. 249, 1. 187; Ms. 5. 129, 10. 12. (They are:− तक्षा च<BR> तन्त्रवायश्च नापितो रजकस्तथा । पञ्चमश्चर्मकारश्च कारवः शिल्पिनो मताः ॥)<BR>—3 Terrible, horrible; जरेति क्षयमाहुर्वै दारुणं कारुसंज्ञितम् Mb. 1. 40. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुः|कारु
कारु + .{@-रुः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of विश्वकर्मन् the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-2" target="_blank">Page0562-2</a>]<BR> architect of the gods.<BR>—2 An art, a science.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कारुचौरः, कारुजः, कारुशिल्पिगणः, कारुहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुचौरः|कारुचौर
कारु + -चौरः one who commits burglary, a dacoit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुजः|कारुज
कारु + -जः<BR>—1 a piece of mechanism, any product of manufacture.<BR>—2 a young elephant.<BR>—3 a hillock, an ant-hill.<BR>—4 froth.<BR>—5 sesamum growing spontaneously.<BR>—6 red orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुशिल्पिगणः|कारुशिल्पिगण
कारु + -शिल्पिगणः a corporation of artisans and handicraftsmen; Kau. A. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुहस्तः|कारुहस्त
कारु + -हस्तः the hand of an artisan; नित्यं शुद्धः कारुहस्तः Ms. 5. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुकः|कारुक
