काल + -यापः, -यापनम् procrastination, delay, putting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयापनम्
काल + -यापः, -यापनम् procrastination, delay, putting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयोगः|कालयोग
काल + -योगः fate, destiny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयोगतः
काल + -योगतः according to the requirements of the time; Pt. 1. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयोगिन्
काल + -योगिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरात्रिः|कालरात्रि
काल + -रात्रिः, -रात्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a dark night.<BR>—2 a sister of Yama.<BR>—3 the Amāvasyā on which lamps are lighted (in the Divali holidays).<BR>—4 the night of destruction at the end of the world (identified with Durgā);<BR> कालरात्रीति तां (सीतां) विद्धि सर्वलङ्काविनाशिनीम् Rām. 5. 51. 34.<BR>—5 a particular night in the life of man, on the 7th day of the 7th month<BR> of the 77th year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरात्री
काल + -रात्रिः, -रात्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a dark night.<BR>—2 a sister of Yama.<BR>—3 the Amāvasyā on which lamps are lighted (in the Divali holidays).<BR>—4 the night of destruction at the end of the world (identified with Durgā);<BR> कालरात्रीति तां (सीतां) विद्धि सर्वलङ्काविनाशिनीम् Rām. 5. 51. 34.<BR>—5 a particular night in the life of man, on the 7th day of the 7th month<BR> of the 77th year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरुद्रः|कालरुद्र
काल + -रुद्रः Rudra regarded as the fire that is to destroy the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललवणम्
काल + -लवणम् the बिड salt. (Mar. संचळखार)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललोहम्
काल + -लोहम्, -लौहम् steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललौहम्
काल + -लोहम्, -लौहम् steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवलनम्
काल + -वलनम् the armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालविप्रकर्षः|कालविप्रकर्ष
काल + -विप्रकर्षः prolongation of time. विषयबाहुल्यं कालविप्रकर्षश्च<BR> स्मृतिं प्रमुष्णाति Mv. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालविभक्तिः|कालविभक्ति
काल + -विभक्तिः <i>f.</i> a section or part of time; Ms. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृद्धिः|कालवृद्धि
काल + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> periodical interest (payable monthly, quarterly,<BR> or at stated times); Ms. 8. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृन्तः|कालवृन्त
काल + -वृन्तः a kind of pulse (कुलत्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवेला
काल + -वेला the time of Saturn, <i>i. e.</i> a particular time of the day<BR> (half a watch every day) at which any religious act is improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंकर्षा
काल + -संकर्षा a girl nine years old personating Durgā at a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंकर्षिन्
काल + -संकर्षिन् <i>a.</i> shortening time (as a mantra); कालसंकर्षिणीं<BR> विद्यां दीक्षापूर्वमुपादिशत् Ks. 68. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंगः
काल + -संगः a delay; जानामि कार्यस्य च कालसंगम् Rām. 4. 33. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंरोधः|कालसंरोध
काल + -संरोधः<BR>—1 keeping back for a long time; Ms. 8. 143.<BR>—2 lapse of a long period of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसदृश
काल + -सदृश <i>a.</i> opportune, timely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसमन्वित
काल + -समन्वित, -समायुक्त <i>a.</i> dead; Rām. 2. 65. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसमायुक्त
काल + -समन्वित, -समायुक्त <i>a.</i> dead; Rām. 2. 65. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंपन्न|कालसम्पन्न
काल + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> dated, bearing a date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसर्पः|कालसर्प
काल + -सर्पः the black and most poisonous variety of the snake; Gīt. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसारः|कालसार|कालसारं
काल + -सारः the black antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसारम्
काल + -सारः + ({@-रम्@}) a yellow sort of sandal<BR> wood. ━<i>a.</i> having a black centre or pupil; न कालसारं हरिणं तदक्षिद्वयं<BR> प्रभुर्बद्धुमभून्मनोभूः N. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसूत्रम्
काल + -सूत्रम्, -सूत्रकम्<BR>—1 thread of time or death.<BR>—2 N. of a particular hell; Y. 3. 222; Ms. 4. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसूत्रकम्
काल + -सूत्रम्, -सूत्रकम्<BR>—1 thread of time or death.<BR>—2 N. of a particular hell; Y. 3. 222; Ms. 4. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालस्कन्दः
काल + -स्कन्दः the Tamāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालस्वरूप
काल + -स्वरूप <i>a.</i> terrible as death, (deathlike in form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालहरः|कालहर
काल + -हरः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालहरणम्
काल + -हरणम् loss of time, delay; Ś. 3; U. 5; यात्वन्येन (वरेण)<BR> विहाय कालहरणं रामो वनं दण्डकाम् Mv. 4. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालहानिः|कालहानि
काल + -हानिः <i>f.</i> delay; मामक्षमं मण्डनकालहानेर्वेत्तीव बिम्बाधरबद्धतृष्णम् R. 13. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक|कालकं|कालकः
कालक <i>a.</i> Black, dark-blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकः|कालक|कालकं
कालक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A mole, freckle, mark.<BR>—2 A water-snake.<BR>—3 The black part of the eye.<BR>—4 A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालका
कालक + .{@-का@} Ved.<BR>—1 A kind of bird.<BR>—2 A daughter of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकम्
कालक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The liver.<BR>—2 An unknown quantity (in Alg.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कालकाचार्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकाचार्यः|कालकाचार्य
कालक + -आचार्यः N. of a Jaina teacher and astronomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालङ्कतः|कालङ्कत
कालङ्कतः (कासमर्दः) A cure for the cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालन
कालन <i>a.</i> Destroyer; कलिमलसंहतिकालनोऽखिलाशः Bhāg. 12. 12. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालायनी
कालायनी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
कालिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [काल-ठन्-ठक् वा]<BR>—1 Relating to time.<BR>—2 Depending on time; विशेषः कालिकोऽवस्था Ak.<BR>—3 Seasonable, timely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिकः|कालिक|कालिकं
कालिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A crane.<BR>—2 A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिका
कालिक + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 Blackness, black colour.<BR>—2 Ink, black ink.<BR>—3 Price of an article to be paid by instalments.<BR>—4 Periodical interest paid at stated times.<BR>—5 A multitude of clouds, a dark cloud threatening rain; कुतस्त्रपा<BR> नश्यति न त्वदाननक्षपाकरादर्शनकारिकालिका Rām. Ch. 2. 55; कालिकेव<BR> निबिडा बलाकिनी R. 11. 15 —6 Flaw (alloy &c.) in gold.<BR>—7 The liver.<BR>—8 A female crow.<BR>—9 A scorpion.<BR>—10 A spirituous liquor.<BR>—11 N. of Durgā; व्यभाव्यत प्रलयजकालिकाकृतिः Śi. 17. 44.<BR>—12 A particular blood-vessel in the ear.<BR>—13 A line of hair extending from the pudenda to the navel.<BR>—14 A small singing bird.<BR>—15 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR>—16 A girl four years old personating Durgā at a festival.<BR>—17 N. of a Yoginī.<BR>—18 A kind of vegetable.<BR>—19 A kind of cucumber.<BR>—20 The Indian spikenard.<BR>—21 Mist.<BR>—22 An oil-woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिकम्
कालिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Black sandalwood.<BR>—2 Hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालित
कालित <i>a.</i> Dead; नाधुना सन्ति कालिताः Bhāg. 10. 51. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिनी
कालिनी N. of the sixth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुञ्चः|कालकुञ्च|कालकुंचः
कालकुञ्चः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जरः|कालञ्जर|कालंजर|कालंजरः
कालञ्जरः<BR>—1 N. of a mountain and adjacent country (modern Kallinjar); तस्मात्कालञ्जरगिरौ<BR> गत्वा Ks. 111. 70.<BR>—2 An assembly of religious mendicants.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जरा
कालञ्जरः + .{@-रा@} or {@री@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जरी
{Circular ref 12132.004}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालधौतम्
कालधौतम् (= कलधौतम्) Silver or gold. स कालधौतातनुदुग्धपूर्णतत्कटाहमध्यास्थितनूतनाज्यवत्<BR> Rām. Ch. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशेयम्
कालशे(से)यम् Buttermilk (produced in a jar by churning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसेयम्
कालशे(से)यम् Buttermilk (produced in a jar by churning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालापः|कालाप
कालापः<BR>—1 The hair of the head.<BR>—2 A serpentʼs hood.<BR>—3 A demon, an imp, a goblin.<BR>—4 A student of the Kalāpa grammar. कलापिना प्रोक्तमधीयते इति अण् P. IV. 3. 108.<BR>—5 One who knows this grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालापकम्
कालापकम्<BR>—1 An assemblage of the pupils of Kalāpa.<BR>—2 The doctrines or teachings of Kalāpa.<BR>—3 N. of the Kātantra grammar; अधुना स्वल्पतन्त्रत्वात्कातन्त्राख्यं भविष्यति ।<BR> मद्वाहनकलापस्य नाम्ना कालापकं तथा ॥ Ks. 7. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्ग|कालिंग|कालिङ्गं|कालिङ्गः
कालिङ्ग <i>a.</i> (-ङ्गी <i>f.</i>) [कलिङ्ग-अण्] Produced in,<BR> or belonging to, the Kaliṅga country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्गः|कालिङ्ग|कालिंग|कालिङ्गं
कालिङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः@}<BR>—1 A king of that country; प्रतिजग्राह कालिङ्गस्तमस्त्रैर्गजसाधनः R. 4. 40.<BR>—2 A snake of that country.<BR>—3 An elephant.<BR>—4 A species of cucumber.<BR>—5 A poisonous plant.<BR>—6 A sort of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्गाः
कालिङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गाः@} (pl.) N. of a country; see कलिङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्गम्
कालिङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गम्@} A water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदासः|कालिदास
कालिदासः<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated poet (author of many works like Śākuntala, Raghuvaṃśa &c.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">Page0568-1</a>]<BR>—2 N. of two other poets (authors of Nalodaya and Śrutabodha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्द|कालिंद
कालिन्द <i>a.</i> (-न्दी <i>f.</i>) [कलिन्द-अण्] Connected with<BR> or coming from the mountain Kalinda or the river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दी|कालिंदी
कालिन्द + .{@-न्दी@}<BR>—1 The river Yamunā; कालिन्द्याः पुलिनेषु केलिकुपिताम् Ve. 1. 2; R. 15. 28;<BR> Śānti. 4. 13.<BR>—2 A sort of vessel.<BR>—3 N. of a wife of Kṛṣṇa (a daughter of Sūrya).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कालिन्दीकर्षणः, कालिन्दीभेदनः, कालिन्दीसूः, कालिन्दीसोदरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दम्
कालिन्द + .{@-न्दम्@} A water melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दिकर्षणः
कालिन्दि + -कर्षणः, -भेदनः an epithet of Balarāma q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीभेदनः|कालिन्दीभेदन|कालिंदीभेदन
कालिन्दि + -कर्षणः, -भेदनः an epithet of Balarāma q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसूः
कालिन्दी + -सूः <i>f.</i> Saṃjñā, a wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसूः
कालिन्दी + -सूः ━(<i>m.</i>) the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसोदरः|कालिन्दीसोदर|कालिंदीसोदर
कालिन्दी + -सोदरः Yama, the god of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Blackness; Amaru. 88; Śi. 4. 57.<BR>—2 Paleness; Śi. 8. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
कालिय <i>a.</i>^1 Relating to time, timely.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260510. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियः|कालिय
कालिय + .{@-यः@} The Kaliyuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियः|कालिय
कालियः N. of a tremendously large serpent who dwelt at the bottom<BR> of the Yamunā (which was a ground forbidden to Garuḍa, the enemy of<BR> serpents, owing to the curse of the sage Saubhari). He was crushed to death<BR> by Kṛṣṇa when he was but a boy; R. 6. 49; Śi. 17. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियाः
कालियः + .{@-याः@} (pl.) The family of black serpents; Śi. 19. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कालियदमनः, कालियमर्दनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियदमनः|कालियदमन
कालियः + -दमनः, -मर्दनः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियमर्दनः
कालियः + -दमनः, -मर्दनः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीकः|कालीक
कालीकः A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीची
कालीची The judgment hall of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
कालीन <i>a.</i> [काल-ख]<BR>—1 Belonging to a particular time.<BR>—2 Seasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयम्
कालीयम् [काल-छ] A kind of sandal-wood; also कालीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयकः|कालीयक|कालीयकं
कालीयकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A species of aloe wood.<BR>—2 A kind of turmeric.<BR>—3 Yellow sandal. … गात्राणि कालीयकचर्चितानि Ṛs. 4. 5. Here comm.<BR> मणिराम says, ‘कालीयकेन जायकेन’.<BR>—4 A dark kind of sandalwood.<BR>—5 Saffron; कालीयकक्षोदविलेपनश्रियम् Śi. 12. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयकम्
कालीयकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A species of aloe wood.<BR>—2 A kind of turmeric.<BR>—3 Yellow sandal. … गात्राणि कालीयकचर्चितानि Ṛs. 4. 5. Here comm.<BR> मणिराम says, ‘कालीयकेन जायकेन’.<BR>—4 A dark kind of sandalwood.<BR>—5 Saffron; कालीयकक्षोदविलेपनश्रियम् Śi. 12. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालुष्यम्
कालुष्यम्<BR>—1 Foulness, dirtiness, turbidness, muddiness (fig. also); चोलकेश्वरकीर्तिश्च<BR> कालुष्यं ययतुः समम् Ks. 19. 95. कालुष्यमुपयाति बुद्धिः K. 103<BR> becomes muddy or defiled.<BR>—2 Opacity.<BR>—3 Disagreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
कालेय <i>a.</i> Belonging to the Kali age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयम्
कालेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 The liver.<BR>—2 Black sandal-wood; आश्यानकालेयकृताङ्गरागाम् Ku. 7. 9.<BR>—3 Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयाः
कालेय + .{@-याः@} ━(<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a school of the black Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयकः|कालेयक|कालेयकं
कालेयकः A kind of aloe wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयकम्
कालेयकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A fragrant wood.<BR>—2 The black sandalwood; मधुकरकुलकलङ्ककालीकृतकालेयककुसुमकुड्मलेषु K.<BR>—3 A disease like jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयकः|कालेयक|कालेयकं
कालेयकः + .{@-कः@} A dog, hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयरुः
कालेयरुः<BR>—1 A dog.<BR>—2 A species of sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोलः|कालोल
कालोलः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्प|काल्पः
काल्प <i>a.</i> [कल्प-अण्]<BR>—1 Preceptive, laying down a rule, ritual.<BR>—2 Relating to Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पः|काल्प
काल्पः, -ल्पकः<BR> Zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पकः|काल्पक
काल्पः, -ल्पकः<BR> Zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पनिक|काल्पनिकः
काल्पनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [कल्पना ठक्]<BR>—1 Existing only in fancy, fictitious; काल्पनिकी व्युत्पत्तिः<BR>—2 Counterfeit, fabricated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य <i>a.</i> [काल-यत्]<BR>—1 Timely, seasonable.<BR>—2 Agreeable, pleasant, auspicious.<BR>—3 Of the morning time; प्रभाते काल्यमुत्थाय चक्रे गोदानमुत्तमम् Rām. 1. 72. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्या
काल्य + .{@-ल्या@}<BR>—1 A cow fit for the the bull.<BR>—2 A woman arrived at puberty or maturity (who has reached the time favourable<BR> to conception). उपसर्या काल्या प्रजने P. III. 1. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्यम्
काल्य + .{@-ल्यम्@} Day-break; Rām. 2. 7. 26; काल्यं विषादविमुखः प्रतिवेशवर्गः ।<BR> दोषाश्च मे वदतु कर्मसु कौशलं च ॥ Cārudatta 3. 10. काल्याग्नौ<BR> द्विजकुलनादमन्त्रवादैरुद्दीप्ते तिमिरतिलाहुतिं विधाय … Rām. Ch. 7. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्याणकम्
काल्याणकम् Auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावचिक|कावचिकं
कावचिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [कवच-ठञ् ठञ् कवचिनश्च<BR> P. IV. 2. 41.] Armorial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावचिकम्
कावचिक + .{@-कम्@} A multitude of men in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावारम्
कावारम् Moss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावारी
कावारम् + .{@-री@} An umbrella without a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावृकः|कावृक
कावृकः<BR>—1 A cock.<BR>—2 The Cakravāka bird; ‘कावृकः कृवाकौ स्यात्पीतमस्तककोकयोः’ Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेरम्
कावेरम् Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेरी
कावेरी<BR>—1 N. of a river in the south of India; कावेरीं सरितां पत्युः शङ्कनीयामिवाकरोत् R. 4. 45.<BR>—2 A harlot, courtezan.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य <i>a.</i> [कवि-ष्यञ्^1]<BR>—1 Possessed of the qualities of a sage or a poet.<BR>—2 Praiseworthy, fit to be described<BR>—3 Prophetic, inspired, poetical; अशंसीत् काव्यः कविः Rv. 8. 8. 11.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260708. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यः|काव्य|काव्यं
काव्य + .{@-व्यः@} N. of Śukra, preceptor of the Asuras; Mb. 1. 76. 6; दानवेन्द्रैर्हतं<BR> दूरात् काव्यः कचमजीवयत् Bm. 1. 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्या
काव्य + .{@-व्या@}<BR>—1 Intelligence.<BR>—2 A female fiend;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्व्याः
काव्य + .{@-व्याः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) A class of manes; Ms. 3. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यम्
काव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 A poem; महाकाव्यम्; मेघदूतं नाम काव्यम् &c.<BR>—2 Poetics, poetry, poetical composition. (काव्य is defined by writers<BR> on Poetics in different ways; तददोषौ शब्दार्थौ सगुणावनलङ्कृती पुनः<BR> क्वापि K. P. 1; वाक्यं रसात्मकं काव्यम् S. D. 1; रमणीयार्थप्रतिपादकः<BR> शब्दः काव्यम् R. G.; शरीरं तावदिष्टार्थव्यवच्छिन्ना पदावली Kāv. 1. 10;<BR> निर्दोषा लक्षणवती सरीतिर्गुणभूषिता । सालङ्काररसाऽनेकवृत्तिर्वाक्<BR> काव्यनामभाक् ॥ Candr. 1. 7.)<BR>—3 Happiness, welfare.<BR>—4 Wisdom; काव्यानि वदतां तेषां संयच्छामि वहामि च Mb. 12. 124. 34.<BR>—5 Inspiration. (The purposes of a Kāvya as mentioned by Mammaṭa are:−<BR> काव्यं यशसेऽर्थकृते व्यवहारविदे शिवेतरक्षतये । सद्यःपरनिर्वृतये<BR> कान्तासंमिततयोपदेशयुजे ॥ K. P. 1.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काव्यार्थः, काव्यालङ्कारः, काव्यादर्शः, काव्यचौरः, काव्यचौर्यम्, काव्यप्रकाशः, काव्यमीमांसकः, काव्यमीमांसा, काव्यरसिक, काव्यलिङ्गम्, काव्यहास्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यार्थः|काव्यार्थ
काव्य + -अर्थः a poetical thought or idea. {@˚आपत्तिः@} Necessary<BR> conclusion; a figure of speech; Kuval. 59. {@˚चौरः@} a robber of the<BR> ideas of another poet, a plagiarist; यदस्य दैत्या इव लुण्ठनाय काव्यार्थचौराः<BR> प्रगुणीभवन्ति Vikr. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यालङ्कारः|काव्यालङ्कार
काव्य + -अलङ्कारः N. of a work on poetics by Vāmana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यादर्शः|काव्यादर्श
काव्य + -आदर्शः N. of a work on poetics by Daṇḍin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौरः|काव्यचौर
काव्य + -चौरः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">Page0569-1</a>]<BR> stealer of other menʼs poems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौर्यम्
काव्य + -चौर्यम् plagiarism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यप्रकाशः|काव्यप्रकाश
काव्य + -प्रकाशः N. of a work on Rhetorics by Mammaṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यमीमांसकः|काव्यमीमांसक
काव्य + -मीमांसकः a rhetorician, critic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यमीमांसा
काव्य + -मीमांसा N. of a work on Rhetorics by Rājaśekhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यरसिक
काव्य + -रसिक <i>a.</i> one who has a taste for and can appreciate the<BR> beauties of poetry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यलिङ्गम्
काव्य + -लिङ्गम् Poetic Reason, a figure of speech; thus defined:− काव्यलिङ्गं<BR> हेतोर्वाक्यपदार्थता K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> जितोऽसि मन्द कन्दर्प मच्चित्तेऽस्ति<BR> त्रिलोचनः Candr. 5. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यहास्यम्
काव्य + -हास्यम् a farce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् €1. €4 Ā. (काश-श्य-ते, काशित)<BR>—1 To shine, look brilliant or beautiful; पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे<BR> चतुर्भिः R. 10. 86, 7. 24; Ku. 1. 24; Bk. 2. 25; Śi. 6. 74.<BR>—2 To appear, be visible; नैव भूमिर्न च दिशः प्रदिशो वा चकाशिरे Mb.<BR>—3 To appear, or look like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशः|काश|काशं
काशः, -शकः, -शम्<BR> [काश्-अच्] A kind of grass used for mats, roofs, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशकः|काशक
काशः, -शकः, -शम्<BR> [काश्-अच्] A kind of grass used for mats, roofs, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशम्
काशः, -शकः, -शम्<BR> [काश्-अच्] A kind of grass used for mats, roofs, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशम्
काशः, -शकः, -शम् + .{@-शम्@} A flower of that grass; Ku. 7. 11; R. 4. 17; Ṛs. 3. 1, 2, 28.<BR> चरति पुलिनेषु हंसी काशांशुकवासिनी सुसंहृष्टा Pratimā 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशः|काश|काशं
काशः, -शकः, -शम् + .{@-शः@}<BR>—1 = कास q. v.<BR>—2 Appearance.<BR>—3 Splendour. यन्माययापि विबुधा मुह्यन्ति ज्ञानकाशया Bhāg. 12. 10. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काशकृत्स्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशकृत्स्नः|काशकृत्स्न
काशः + -कृत्स्नः N. of a Grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
काशिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) (Usually at the end of comp.) Shining,<BR> appearing or looking like, having the semblance of; जितकाशिन् <i>e. g.</i><BR> one who behaves like a conqueror; see the word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिल
काशिल <i>a.</i> Made of Kāśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिष्णु
काशिष्णु <i>a.</i> Shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिः|काशि
काशिः, -शी <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a celebrated city on the Ganges, the modern Benares<BR> and one of the seven sacred cities; काशी काशीति काशीति त्रिवारं यः<BR> पठेत् नरः । सोऽपि देशान्तरेवासी काशीवासफलं लभेत् ॥ see काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशी
काशिः, -शी <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a celebrated city on the Ganges, the modern Benares<BR> and one of the seven sacred cities; काशी काशीति काशीति त्रिवारं यः<BR> पठेत् नरः । सोऽपि देशान्तरेवासी काशीवासफलं लभेत् ॥ see काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिः|काशि
काशिः, -शी + .{@-शिः@}<BR>—1 The clenched hand, fist.<BR>—2 A handful; आप इव काशिना संगृभीता Rv. 7. 104. 8.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR>—4 Light, splendour;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काशिपः, काशिराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिपः|काशिप
काशिः + -पः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिराजः|काशिराज
काशिः + -राजः N. of a king, father of अम्बा, अम्बिका and अम्बालिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिक
काशिक <i>a.</i> A product of Kāśī; silken; (<i>n.</i>) A silken garment.<BR> Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिका
काशिका<BR>—1 The city of Benares.<BR>—2 N. of a commentary on Pāṇiṇiʼs Sūtras (called काशिकावृत्ति).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काशिकाप्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिकाप्रियः|काशिकाप्रिय
काशिका + -प्रियः N. of Dhanvantarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशी
काशी See काशि.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काशीनाथः, काशीयात्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीनाथः|काशीनाथ
काशी + -नाथः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीयात्रा
काशी + -यात्रा pilgrimage to Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशेय
काशेय <i>a.</i> Belonging to, born in Kāśī; तद्भवानद्य काशेयपुरीं<BR> वाराणसीं व्रज Rām. 7. 38. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मकराष्ट्रक
काश्मकराष्ट्रक <i>a.</i> A variety of diamonds; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मरी
काश्मरी (also काश्मर्यः, -यम्) A plant commonly called गाम्भारी;<BR> Rām. 2. 94. 9. काश्मर्याः कृतमालमुद्गतदलं कोयष्टिकष्टीकते Māl. 9. 7.<BR> The word appears sometimes as कार्श्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मर्यः|काश्मर्य|काश्मर्य्य|काश्मर्य्यः
काश्मरी (also काश्मर्यः, -यम्) A plant commonly called गाम्भारी;<BR> Rām. 2. 94. 9. काश्मर्याः कृतमालमुद्गतदलं कोयष्टिकष्टीकते Māl. 9. 7.<BR> The word appears sometimes as कार्श्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मर्यम्
काश्मरी (also काश्मर्यः, -यम्) A plant commonly called गाम्भारी;<BR> Rām. 2. 94. 9. काश्मर्याः कृतमालमुद्गतदलं कोयष्टिकष्टीकते Māl. 9. 7.<BR> The word appears sometimes as कार्श्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर|काश्मीरं|काश्मीरः
काश्मीर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) Born in, belonging to, or coming<BR> from, Kāśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीराः
काश्मीर + .{@-राः@} (pl.) N. of a country or its inhabitants; see कश्मीर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीराः
काश्मीर + .{@-राः@} A sort of grape; see कश्मीर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरम्
काश्मीर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Saffron; काश्मीरगन्धमृगनाभिकृताङ्गरागाम् C. P. 8; Bh. 1. 41,<BR> काश्मीरगौरवपुषामभिसारिकाणाम् Gīt. 11; also 1; cf. also कस्तूरिकां<BR> च काश्मीरं पाटीरं हिमवालुकाम् Śiva B. 30. 13. काश्मीरद्रवसान्द्रदिग्धवपुषः Bhāg.<BR>—2 Root of a tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काश्मीरजम्, काश्मीरजन्मन्, काश्मीरपङ्कः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरजम्
काश्मीर + -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> saffron; काश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि नितान्तरम्या<BR> Bv. 1. 71; Śi. 11. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरजन्मन्
काश्मीर + -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> saffron; काश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि नितान्तरम्या<BR> Bv. 1. 71; Śi. 11. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरपङ्कः
काश्मीर + -पङ्कः Musk; काश्मीरपङ्ककृतनाभिकृताङ्गरागाम् (स्मरामि) …<BR> Bil. C. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरक
काश्मीर(रि)क <i>a.</i> Born or produced in Kaśmīra. काश्मीरकः<BR> कविरयं गुणिनं दिदृक्षुः Bil. C. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरिक
काश्मीर(रि)क <i>a.</i> Born or produced in Kaśmīra. काश्मीरकः<BR> कविरयं गुणिनं दिदृक्षुः Bil. C. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर्यम्
काश्मीर्यम् Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मल्यम्
काश्मल्यम् Dejection of mind, despair; Mv. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यम्
काश्यम् Spirituous liquor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काश्यपम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपम्
1. काश्यम् + -पम् flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपः|काश्यप|काश्यपं
काश्यपः<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated sage.<BR>—2 N. of Kaṇāda.<BR>—3 An epithet of Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपी
काश्यपः + .{@-पी@} The earth; Mb. 13. 62. 62. तानपि दधासि मातः काश्यपि यातस्तवापि<BR> च विवेकः Bv. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपम्
2. काश्यपः + .{@-पम्@} Flesh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काश्यपनन्दनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपनन्दनः|काश्यपनन्दन|काश्यपनंदन
काश्यपः + -नन्दनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—2 N. of Aruṇa.<BR>—3 a god.<BR>—4 a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपिः|काश्यपि
काश्यपिः An epithet of Garuḍa and of Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपेयः|काश्यपेय
काश्यपेयः<BR>—1 An epithet of the twelve Ādityas.<BR>—2 Of the sun.<BR>—3 Garuḍa.<BR>—4 Dāruka; सारथेस्तु रथस्थस्य काश्यपेयस्य विस्मिताः Mb. 7. 147. 55.<BR>—5 Gods and demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्वरी
काश्वरी (= काश्मरी q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषः|काष|काषं
काषः [कष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Rubbing, scratching; पथिषु विटपिनां स्कन्धकाषैः सधूमः Ve. 2. 18.<BR>—2 That against which anything is rubbed (as the stock of a tree); लीनालिः<BR> सुरकरिणां कपोलकाषः Ki. 5. 26; see कपोलकाष also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषण
काषण <i>a.</i> Unripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषाय
काषाय (-यी <i>f.</i>) [कषायेण रक्तम् अण् तेव रक्तं रागात्<BR> P. IV. 2. 1.] Red, dyed of a reddish colour; काषायवसनाधवा Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषायम्
काषाय + .{@-यम्@} A red cloth or garment; सीता काषायवासिनी Rām. 7. 97. 13.<BR> इमे काषाये गृहीते M. 5; R. 15. 77; न काषायैर्भवेद्यतिः ‘it is not the hood that makes a monk’<BR>.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काषायवसना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषायवसना
काषाय + -वसना a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठम्
काष्ठम् [काश्-क्थन् Uṇ. 2. 2]<BR>—1 A piece of wood, especially one used as fuel; Ms. 4. 49, 241, 5. 69.<BR>—2 Wood or timber, a piece or log of wood in general; यथा काष्ठं च<BR> काष्ठं च समेयातां महोदधौ H. 4. 69; Ms. 4. 40.<BR>—8 A stick; शोणितेन विना दुःखं कुर्वन् काष्ठादिभिर्नरः Y. 2. 218.<BR>—4 An instrument for measuring length.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: काष्ठागारः, काष्ठागारम्, काष्ठाधिरोहणम्, काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी, काष्ठकदली, काष्ठकीटः, काष्ठकुटः, काष्ठकूटः, काष्ठभङ्गिन्, काष्ठकुद्दालः, काष्ठचिता, काष्ठतक्ष्, काष्ठतन्तुः, काष्ठदारुः, काष्ठद्रुः, काष्ठपुत्तलिका, काष्ठपूलकः, काष्ठप्रदानम्, काष्ठभारः, काष्ठभारिकः, काष्ठमठी, काष्ठमल्लः, काष्ठलेखकः, काष्ठलोहिन्, काष्ठवाटः, काष्ठवाटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठागारः|काष्ठागार
काष्ठम् + -आगारः, -आगारम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">Page0570-1</a>]<BR> a wooden house or enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठागारम्
काष्ठम् + -आगारः, -आगारम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">Page0570-1</a>]<BR> a wooden house or enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0569-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठाधिरोहणम्
काष्ठम् + -अधिरोहणम् ascending the funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी|काष्ठांबुवाहिनी
काष्ठम् + -अम्बुवाहिनी a wooden bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकदली
काष्ठम् + -कदली the wild plantain (Mar. चवई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकीटः|काष्ठकीट
काष्ठम् + -कीटः a small insect found in decayed wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकुटः
काष्ठम् + -कुटः, -कूटः, -भङ्गिन् a wood-pecker; Pt. 1. 332 (a worm generally<BR> found in wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकूटः|काष्ठकूट
काष्ठम् + -कुटः, -कूटः, -भङ्गिन् a wood-pecker; Pt. 1. 332 (a worm generally<BR> found in wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठभङ्गिन्
काष्ठम् + -कुटः, -कूटः, -भङ्गिन् a wood-pecker; Pt. 1. 332 (a worm generally<BR> found in wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकुद्दालः|काष्ठकुद्दाल
काष्ठम् + -कुद्दालः a kind of wooden shovel used for baling water out of<BR> a boat or for scraping and cleaning its bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठचिता
काष्ठम् + -चिता <i>f.</i> a^1 funeral pile.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतक्ष्
काष्ठम् + -तक्ष् <i>m.</i>, {@-तक्षकः@}<BR> a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतन्तुः|काष्ठतन्तु|काष्ठतंतु
काष्ठम् + -तन्तुः a small worm found in timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठदारुः|काष्ठदारु
काष्ठम् + -दारुः the Indian pine tree; also called देवदारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठद्रुः|काष्ठद्रु
काष्ठम् + -द्रुः the Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठपुत्तलिका
काष्ठम् + -पुत्तलिका a wooden statue or image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठपूलकः
काष्ठम् + -पूलकः + ({@-कम्@}) a bundle of sticks or faggots; न हि<BR> अबद्धे काष्ठपूलके एकस्मिन्नाकृष्यमाणे काष्ठान्तराणि कृष्यन्ते । ŚB. on MS. 9. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठपूलकम्
काष्ठम् + -पूलकः + ({@-कम्@}) a bundle of sticks or faggots; न हि<BR> अबद्धे काष्ठपूलके एकस्मिन्नाकृष्यमाणे काष्ठान्तराणि कृष्यन्ते । ŚB. on MS. 9. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठप्रदानम्
काष्ठम् + -प्रदानम् piling up wood, forming a funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठभारः|काष्ठभार
काष्ठम् + -भारः a particular weight of wood; Rām. 1. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठभारिकः|काष्ठभारिक
काष्ठम् + -भारिकः wood-carrier; काष्ठभारिकसंघाय सप्रश्रयमदामहम् Ks. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमठी
काष्ठम् + -मठी a funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमल्लः|काष्ठमल्ल
काष्ठम् + -मल्लः a bier, a wooden frame on which dead bodies are carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलेखकः|काष्ठलेखक
काष्ठम् + -लेखकः a small worm found in wood (= काष्ठकूट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलोहिन्
काष्ठम् + -लोहिन् <i>m.</i> a cudgel armed with iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठवाटः|काष्ठवाट
काष्ठम् + -वाटः, -वाटम् a wall made of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठवाटम्
काष्ठम् + -वाटः, -वाटम् a wall made of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकम्
काष्ठकम् Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिकः|काष्ठिक
काष्ठिकः A bearer of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिका
काष्ठिका A small piece of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठा
काष्ठा<BR>—1 A quarter of region of the world, direction, region; काष्ठा (दिश)<BR> मुदीचीमिव तिग्मरश्मिः (दिदीपे) Ki. 3. 55; cf. also पूर्वा तु<BR> काष्ठा तिमिरानुलिप्ता Avimārkam 2. 12.<BR>—2 A limit, boundary; स्वां काष्ठामधुनोपेते Bhāg. 1. 1. 23; स्वयं<BR> विशीर्णद्रुमपर्णवृत्तिता परा हि काष्ठा तपसः Ku. 5. 28.<BR>—3 The last limit, extremity, pitch, climax, excess; काष्ठागतस्नेहरसानुविद्धम् Ku. 3. 35.<BR>—4 Race ground, course.<BR>—5 A mark, goal.<BR>—6 The path of the wind and clouds in the atmosphere.<BR>—7 A measure of time = A Kalā; शुक्लस्त्वं बहुलस्त्वं च कला काष्ठा<BR> त्रुटिस्तथा Mb. 1. 25. 14.<BR>—8 Water.<BR>—9 The sun.<BR>—10 A fixed place of a lunar mansion.<BR>—11 N. of a wife of Kaśyapa and daughter of Dakṣa.<BR>—12 The yellow colour or the कदम्ब tree; cf. काष्ठा दिक्कालहारिद्रस्थित्युत्कर्षेषु<BR> तु स्त्रियाम् Nm.<BR>—13 A form, form of appearance; काष्ठां भगवतो ध्यायेत्स्वनासाग्रावलोकनः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 28. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठीला
काष्ठीला The plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास्
कास् €1 Ā. (कासते, कासित)<BR>—1 To shine; see काश्.<BR>—2 To cough, make a sound indicating any disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासः|कास
कासः, -सा<BR> [कास्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Cough, catarrh. मुञ्च शीपेक्त्था उत कास एनम् Av. 1. 12. 3; कासश्वासकृतायासः<BR> कण्ठे घुरघुरायते Bhāg. 3. 30. 16.<BR>—2 Sneezing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कासकुण्ठ, कासघ्न, कासहृत्, कासनाशिनी, कासमर्दः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0570-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासा
