किञ्जलः|किञ्जल|किंजल|किंजलः
किञ्जम्, किञ्जलः, किञ्जल्कः<BR> The filament or blossom of a lotus or any<BR> other plant; आकर्षद्भिः पद्मकिञ्जल्कगन्धान् U. 3. 2; R. 15. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्जल्कः|किञ्जल्क|किंजल्क|किञ्जल्कं|किंजल्कः
किञ्जम्, किञ्जलः, किञ्जल्कः<BR> The filament or blossom of a lotus or any<BR> other plant; आकर्षद्भिः पद्मकिञ्जल्कगन्धान् U. 3. 2; R. 15. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्
किट् €1 P. (केटति)<BR>—1 To go or approach.<BR>—2 To frighten, terrify.<BR>—3 To fear, dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटिः|किटि
किटिः A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटिभः|किटिभ
किटिभः<BR>—1 A louse.<BR>—2 A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटिमः|किटिम
किटिमः A kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टम्
किट्टम्, -किट्टकम्<BR> Secretion, excrement, sediment, dirt; अग्नौ विवर्णं<BR> परितप्यमानं किट्टं यथा राघव जातरूपम् Rām. 4. 24. 18. अन्न˚. cf. स्यात् किट्टं केशलोमास्थ्नो मज्जः^1 स्नेहोऽक्षिविट्त्वचाम् charak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किट्टवर्जितम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260518. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टकम्
किट्टम्, -किट्टकम्<BR> Secretion, excrement, sediment, dirt; अग्नौ विवर्णं<BR> परितप्यमानं किट्टं यथा राघव जातरूपम् Rām. 4. 24. 18. अन्न˚. cf. स्यात् किट्टं केशलोमास्थ्नो मज्जः^1 स्नेहोऽक्षिविट्त्वचाम् charak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किट्टवर्जितम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260518. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टवर्जितम्
किट्टम् + -वर्जितम् semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टालः|किट्टाल
किट्टालः<BR>—1 A copper vessel.<BR>—2 Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टिमम्
किट्टिमम् unclean water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किणः|किण
किणः<BR>—1 A corn, callosity, a scar. ज्ञास्यसि कियद्भुजो मे रक्षति मौर्वीकिणाङ्क<BR> इति Ś. 1. 13; Mk. 2. 11; R. 16. 84, 18. 47; Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 A wart, a mole.<BR>—3 An insect found in wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्वम्
किण्वम् Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्वः|किण्व|किण्वं
किण्वम् + .{@-ण्वः, -ण्वम्@} A drug or seed used to cause fermentation in the<BR> manufacture of spirits; Ms. 8. 326.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्वम्
किण्वम् + .{@-ण्वः, -ण्वम्@} A drug or seed used to cause fermentation in the<BR> manufacture of spirits; Ms. 8. 326.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्विन्
किण्विन् <i>m.</i> A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कित्
कित् I. €1 P. (केतति)<BR>—1 To desire.<BR>—2 To live.<BR>—3 (चिकित्सति) To heal, cure.<BR>—4 To doubt, suspect. ━II. €3 P. Ved. (चिकेत्ति^1) To know.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 202605. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कितवः|कितव
कितवः (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A rogue, liar, cheat; अर्हति किल कितव उपद्रवम् M. 4; Amaru. 20, 46;<BR> Me. 113.<BR>—2 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>—3 A kind of perfume (commonly रोचन).<BR>—4 A gamester, gambler; Ms. 3. 159.<BR>—5 A mad or crazy person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किनाटम्
किनाटम् The inner bark of a tree; किनाटं स्नाव तस्थिरम् Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्धिन्|किंधिन्
किन्धिन् <i>m.</i> A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नर|किंनर|किन्नरः
किन्नर See under किम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
1. किम् <i>ind.</i> Used for कु only at the beginning of comp. to<BR> convey the senses of ‘badness’, ‘deterioration’, ‘defect’, ‘blame’ or ‘censure’;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> किंसखा a bad friend; किन्नरः a bad or deformed man<BR> &c.; see comp. below.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किञ्ज, किन्दासः, किन्नरः, किम्पुरुषः, किम्प्रभुः, किंराजन्, किंविवक्षा, किंसखि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्ज|किंज|किंजं|किञ्जं
किम् + -ज <i>a.</i> born somewhere (not in a noble family) मन्ये किंजमहं<BR> घ्नन्तं त्वामक्षत्रियजे रणे Bk. 6. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्दासः|किन्दास
किम् + -दासः a bad slave, or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नरः|किन्नर|किंनर
किम् + -नरः a bad or deformed man; a mythical being with a human figure<BR> and the head of a horse (अश्वमुख); जयोदाहरणं बाह्वोर्गापयामास<BR> किन्नरान् R. 4. 78; उद्गास्यतामिच्छति किन्नराणां तानप्रदायित्वमिवोपगन्तुम्<BR> Ku. 1. 8. ˚ईशः, ˚ईश्वरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera.<BR>—2 a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नरी
किम् + -नरः + ({@-री@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a female Kinnara; Me. 58.<BR>—2 a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुषः|किम्पुरुष|किंपुरुष
किम् + -पुरुषः ‘a low or despicable man’, a mythical being with a human<BR> head and the form of a horse; Ku. 1. 14; किंपुरुषाणां हनुमान् Bhāg. 11. 16. 29.<BR> ˚ईश्वरः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्प्रभुः|किम्प्रभु|किंप्रभु
किम् + -प्रभुः a bad master or king; हितान्न यः संशृणुते स किंप्रभुः Ki. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंराजन्
किम् + -राजन् <i>a.</i> having a bad king. ━(<i>m.</i>) a bad king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंविवक्षा
किम् + -विवक्षा Slandering; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंसखि
किम् + -सखि <i>m.</i> (nom. sing. किंसखा) a bad friend; स किंसखा<BR> साधु न शास्ति योऽधिपम् Ki. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
2. किम् <i>pron. a.</i> (nom. sing. कः <i>m.</i>, का <i>f.</i>, किम् <i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 Who, what, which (used interrogatively); प्रजासु कः केन पथा प्रयातीत्यशेषतो<BR> वेदितुमस्ति शक्तिः Ś. 6. 26; करुणाविमुखेन मृत्युना हरता त्वां वद<BR> किं न मे हृतम् R. 8. 67; का खल्वनेन प्रार्थ्यमानात्मना विकत्थते<BR> V. 2; कः कोऽत्र भोः. कः कौ के कं कौ कान् हसति च हसतो हसन्ति<BR> हरणाक्ष्यः Udb. The pronoun is often used to imply ‘power or authority to do a thing’<BR>; <i>i. e.</i> के आवां परित्रातुं दुष्यन्तमाकन्द Ś. 1;<BR> ‘who are we &c.’, <i>i. e.</i> what power have we &c.; नृपसद्मनि नाम<BR> के वयम् Bh. 3. 27; who are we, <i>i. e.</i> what position have we &c.<BR> Sometimes किम् means ‘long’ as applied to time especially in combination<BR> with खलु or अपि or इव; का खलु वेला तत्रभवत्याः प्राप्तायाः<BR> Ve. 1; ‘what a time’ <i>i. e.</i> a long time has elapsed, &c.; so कोऽपि<BR> कालस्तस्या आगत्य गतायाः Ratn. 3; or क इव कालः Māl. 3.<BR>—2 The neuter (किम्) is frequently used with instr. of nouns in the<BR> sense of ‘what is the use of’; किं स्वामिचेष्टानिरूपणेन H. 1; लोभश्चेदगुणेन<BR> किम् &c. Bh. 2. 55; किं तया दृष्टपा Ś. 3; किं कुलेनोपदिष्टेन<BR> शीलमेवात्र कारणम् Mk. 9. 7. अपि, चित्, चन, चिदपि or स्वित्<BR> are often added to किम् to give it an indefinite sense; विवेश कश्चिज्जटिलस्तपोवनम्<BR> Ku. 5. 30 a certain ascetic; दमघोषसुतेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">Page0572-1</a>]<BR> कश्चन प्रतिशिष्टः प्रतिभानवानथ Śi. 16. 1; कश्चित्कान्ताविरहगुरुणा<BR> स्वाधिकारात्प्रमत्तः Me. 1 &c.; काऽपि तत एवागतवती Māl. 1;<BR> a certain lady; कस्याऽपि कोऽपिति निवेदितं च 1. 33; किमपि किमपि …<BR> जल्पतोरकमेण U. 1. 27; कस्मिंश्चिदपि महाभागधेयजन्मनि मन्मथविकारमुपलक्षितवानस्मि<BR> Māl. 1; किमपि, किंचित् ‘a little’, वस्तुसिद्धिर्विचारेण न किंचित्<BR> कर्मकोटिभिः Vivekacūḍāmaṇi; ‘somewhat’ Y. 2. 116; U. 6. 35. किमपि<BR> also means ‘indescribable’; see अपि. इव is sometimes added to<BR> किम् in the sense of ‘possibly’, ‘I should like to know’; (mostly adding<BR> force and elegance to the period); विना सीतादेव्या किमिव हि न दुःखं<BR> रघुपतेः U. 6. 30; किमिव हि मधुराणां मण्डनं नाकृतीनाम् Ś. 1. 20;<BR> see इव also. ━<i>ind.</i> A particle of interrogation; जातिमात्रेण<BR> किं कश्चिद्धन्यते पूज्यते क्वचित् H. 1. 55 ‘is any one killed or worshipped’<BR> &c.; ततः किम् what then.<BR>—2 A particle meaning ‘why’, ‘wherefore’; किमकारणमेवं दर्शनं विलपन्त्यै<BR> रतये न दीयते Ku. 4. 7.<BR>—3 Whether (its correlatives in the sense of ‘or’ being किं, उत, उताहो,<BR> आहोस्वित्, वा, किंवा, अथवा; see these words).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किमपि, किमर्थ, किमर्थम्, किमाख्य, किमिति, किमु, किमुत, किङ्कथिका, किङ्करः, किङ्कर्तव्यता, किङ्कार्यता, किङ्कारण, किङ्किल, किङ्कृते, किङ्क्षण, किङ्गोत्र, किञ्च, किञ्चन, किञ्चित्, किञ्चिज्ज्ञ, किञ्चित्कर, किञ्चित्काल, किञ्चित्प्राण, किञ्च्न्मात्र, किञ्छन्दस्, किंतनुः, किन्तर्हि, किन्तु, किन्तुघ्नः, किन्देवः, किन्देवत, किन्नामधेय, किन्नामन्, किन्निमित्त, किन्निमित्तम्, किन्नु, किन्नुखलु, किम्पच, किम्पचान, किम्पराक्रम, किम्पाक, किम्पाकः, किम्पुनर्, किम्पुरुषः, किम्प्रकारम्, किम्प्रभाव, किम्भूत, किंरूप, किंवदन्ति, किंवदन्ती, किंवराटकः, किंवा, किंविद्, किंव्यापार, किंशील, किंस्वित्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0571-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमपि
किम् + -अपि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 to some extent, somewhat, to a considerable extent.<BR>—2 inexpressibly, indescribably (as to quality, quantity, nature &c.).<BR>—3 very much, by far; किमपि कमनीयं वपुरिदम् Ś. 3; किमपि भीषणम्,<BR> किमपि करालम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थ
किम् + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> having what motive or aim; किमर्थोऽयं यत्नः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थम्
किम् + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> why, wherefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमाख्य
किम् + -आख्य <i>a.</i> having what name; किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः सा पत्नी. Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमिति
किम् + -इति <i>ind.</i> why, indeed, why to be sure, for what purpose (emphasizing<BR> the question); तत्किमित्युदासते भरताः Māl. 1; किमित्यपास्याभरणानि<BR> यौवने धृतं त्वया वार्धकशोभि वल्कलम् Ku. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमु
किम् + -उ, -उत<BR>—1 whether━or (showing doubt or uncertainty); किमु विषविसर्पः<BR> किमु मदः U. 1. 35; Amaru. 12.<BR>—2 why (indeed) कं च ते परमं कामं करोमि किमु हर्षितः Rām. 1. 18. 52.<BR> प्रियसुहृत्सार्थः किमु त्यज्यते.<BR>—3 how much more, how much less; यौवनं धनसंपत्तिः प्रभुत्वमविवेकिता ।<BR> एकैकमप्यनर्थाय किमु यत्र चतुष्टयम् ॥ H. Pr. 11; सर्वाविनयानामेकैकमप्येषामायतनं<BR> किमुत समवायः K. 103; R. 14. 35; Ku. 7. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमुत
किम् + -उ, -उत<BR>—1 whether━or (showing doubt or uncertainty); किमु विषविसर्पः<BR> किमु मदः U. 1. 35; Amaru. 12.<BR>—2 why (indeed) कं च ते परमं कामं करोमि किमु हर्षितः Rām. 1. 18. 52.<BR> प्रियसुहृत्सार्थः किमु त्यज्यते.<BR>—3 how much more, how much less; यौवनं धनसंपत्तिः प्रभुत्वमविवेकिता ।<BR> एकैकमप्यनर्थाय किमु यत्र चतुष्टयम् ॥ H. Pr. 11; सर्वाविनयानामेकैकमप्येषामायतनं<BR> किमुत समवायः K. 103; R. 14. 35; Ku. 7. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कथिका
किम् + -कथिका <i>f.</i> A doubt or hesitation; यत्र कर्मणि क्रियमाणे<BR> किंकथिका न भवति तत्कर्तव्यम् । यत्र तु हृदयं न तुष्यति तद्वर्जनीयम् ॥<BR> Medhātithiʼs gloss on Ms. 4. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्करः|किङ्कर|किंकर
किम् + -करः a servant, slave; अवेहि मां किंकरमष्टमूर्तेः R. 2. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्करा
किम् + -करः + .({@-रा@}) a female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्करी
किम् + -करः + .({@-री@}) the wife of a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कर्तव्यता
किम् + -कर्तव्यता, -कार्यता any situation in which one asks oneself<BR> what should be done; यथा किंकार्यतामूढा वयस्यास्तस्य जज्ञिरे Ks. 10. 101.<BR> किंकर्तव्यतामूढः ‘being at a loss or perplexed what to do’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कार्यता
किम् + -कर्तव्यता, -कार्यता any situation in which one asks oneself<BR> what should be done; यथा किंकार्यतामूढा वयस्यास्तस्य जज्ञिरे Ks. 10. 101.<BR> किंकर्तव्यतामूढः ‘being at a loss or perplexed what to do’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कारण
किम् + -कारण <i>a.</i> having what reason or cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किल|किंकिल
किम् + -किल <i>ind.</i> what a pity (expressing displeasure or dissatisfaction)<BR> न संभावयामि न मर्षयामि तत्रभवान् किंकिल वृषलं याजयिष्यति<BR> Kāśi. on P. III. 3. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कृते
किम् + -कृते <i>ind.</i> what for? कामस्य किंकृते पुष्पकार्मुकारोपणग्रहः Ks. 71. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्क्षण|किंक्षण
किम् + -क्षण <i>a.</i> one who says ‘what is a moment’, a lazy fellow who<BR> does not value moments; H. 2. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्गोत्र
किम् + -गोत्र <i>a.</i> belonging to what family; किंगोत्रो नु सोम्यासि<BR> Ch. Up. 4. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्च|किंच
किम् + -च <i>ind.</i> moreover, and again, further.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चन|किंचन|किञ्चनः
किम् + -चन <i>ind.</i> to a certain degree, a little;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्|किंचित्
किम् + -चित् <i>ind.</i> to a certain degree, somewhat, a little; किंचिदुत्कान्तशैशवौ<BR> R. 15. 33, 2. 46, 12. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चिज्ज्ञ
किम् + -चित् + ˚ज्ञ <i>a.</i> ‘knowing little’, a smatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्कर
किम् + -चित् + ˚कर <i>a.</i> doing something useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्काल
किम् + -चित् + ˚कालः sometime, a little<BR> time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्प्राण
किम् + -चित् + ˚प्राण <i>a.</i> having a little life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चिन्मात्र
किम् + -चित् + ˚मात्र <i>a.</i> only a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्छन्दस्|किंछंदस्
किम् + -छन्दस् <i>a.</i> conversant with which Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तनुः|किन्तनु|किंतनु
किम् + -तनुः a species of spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तर्हि
किम् + -तर्हि <i>ind.</i> how then, but, however.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तु|किंतु
किम् + -तु <i>ind.</i> but, yet, however, nevertheless; अवैमि चैनामनघेति<BR> किंतु लोकापवादो बलवान्मतो मे R. 14. 43, 1. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तुघ्नः|किन्तुघ्न|किंतुघ्न
किम् + -तुघ्नः one of the eleven periods called Karaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्देवः|किन्देव|किंदेव
किम् + -देवः an inferior god, demi-god; किंदेवाः किन्नराः नागाः किम्पुरुषादयः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 14. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्देवत
किम् + -देवत <i>a.</i> having what deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नामधेय
किम् + -नामधेय, -नामन् <i>a.</i> having what name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नामन्
किम् + -नामधेय, -नामन् <i>a.</i> having what name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्निमित्त|किंनिमित्त
किम् + -निमित्त <i>a.</i> having what cause or reason, for what purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्निमित्तम्
किम् + -निमित्तम् <i>ind.</i> why, wherefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नु|किंनु
किम् + -नु <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 whether; किं नु मे मरणं श्रेयो परित्यागो जनस्य वा Nala. 10. 10.<BR>—2 much more, much less; अपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते Bg. 1. 35.<BR>—3 what indeed; किं नु मे राज्येनार्थः<BR>—4 but, however; किं नु चित्तं मनुष्याणामनित्यमिति मे मतम् Rām. 2. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नुखलु|किंनुखलु
किम् + -नुखलु <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 how possibly, how is it that, why indeed, why to be sure; किं नु<BR> खलु गीतार्थमाकर्ण्य इष्टजनविरहादृतेऽपि बलवदुत्कण्ठितोऽस्मि Ś. 5.<BR>—2 may it be that; किं नु खलु यथा वयमस्यामेवमियमप्यस्मान् प्रति स्यात् Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पच|किंपच|किम्पचः
किम् + -पच, -पचान <i>a.</i> miserly, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पचान|किंपचान|किम्पचानः
किम् + -पच, -पचान <i>a.</i> miserly, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पराक्रम|किंपराक्रम
किम् + -पराक्रम <i>a.</i> of what power or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पाक|किंपाक|किम्पाकः
किम् + -पाक <i>a.</i> not mature, ignorant, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पाकः|किम्पाक|किंपाक
किम् + -पाक + -कः a medical plant, Strychnos nux vomica (Mar. कुचला);<BR> न लुब्धो बुध्यते दोषान्किंपाकमिव भक्षयन् Rām. 2. 66. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुनर्|किंपुनर्
किम् + -पुनर् <i>ind.</i> how much more, how much less; स्वयं रोपितेषु<BR> तरुषूत्पद्यते स्नेहः किं पुनरङ्गसंभवेष्वपत्येषु K. 291; Me. 3, 17; Ve. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुषः|किम्पुरुष|किंपुरुष
किम् + -पुरुषः an inferior man, Bhāg. 11. 14. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्प्रकारम्|किंप्रकारम्
किम् + -प्रकारम् <i>ind.</i> in what manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्प्रभाव
किम् + -प्रभाव <i>a.</i> possessing what power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्भूत|किंभूत
किम् + -भूत <i>a.</i> of what sort or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंरूप
किम् + -रूप <i>a.</i> of what form or shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवदन्ति|किंवदंति|किंवदन्तिः
किम् + -वदन्ति, -वदन्ती <i>f.</i> rumour, report; स किंवदन्तीं वदतां<BR> पुरोगः (पप्रच्छ) R. 14. 31. मत्संबन्धात्कश्मला किंवदन्ती<BR> U. 1. 42; U. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवदन्ती|किंवदंती
किम् + -वदन्ति, -वदन्ती <i>f.</i> rumour, report; स किंवदन्तीं वदतां<BR> पुरोगः (पप्रच्छ) R. 14. 31. मत्संबन्धात्कश्मला किंवदन्ती<BR> U. 1. 42; U. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवराटकः|किंवराटक
किम् + -वराटकः an extravagant man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवा
किम् + -वा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 a particle of interrogation; किं वा शकुन्तलेत्यस्य मातुराख्या Ś. 7.<BR>—2 or (corr. of किं ‘whether’); राजपुत्रि सुप्ता किं वा जागर्षि<BR> Pt. 1; तत्किं मारयामि किं वा विषं प्रयच्छामि किं वा पशुधर्मेण व्यापादयामि<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; Ś. Til. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंविद्
किम् + -विद् <i>a.</i> knowing what.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंव्यापार
किम् + -व्यापार <i>a.</i> following what occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशील
किम् + -शील <i>a.</i> of what habits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंस्वित्
किम् + -स्वित् <i>ind.</i> whether, how; अद्रेः शृङ्गं हरति पवनः किंस्विदित्युन्मुखीभिः Me. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंवरः
किंवरः A crocodile, a shark; Māna. 18. 311.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमीय
किमीय <i>a.</i> Whose, belonging to whom or what.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियत्|कियन्त्
कियत् <i>a.</i> [cf. किमिदंभ्यां वो घः P. V. 2. 40] (Nom. sing.<BR> कियान् <i>m.</i>, कियती <i>f.</i>, कियत् <i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 How great, how far, how much, how many, of what extent of qualities<BR> (having an interrogative force); कियान्कालस्तवैवं स्थितस्य संजातः<BR> Pt. 5; N. 1. 130; अयं भूतावासो विमृश कियतीं याति न दशाम् Śānti. 1. 25;<BR> ज्ञास्यसि कियद्भुजो मे रक्षति Ś. 1. 13; कियदवशिष्टं रजन्याः<BR> Ś. 4; गन्तव्यमस्ति कियदित्यसकृद् ब्रुवाणा S. D.<BR>—2 Of what consideration, <i>i. e.</i> of no account,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">Page0573-1</a>]<BR> worthless; राजेति कियती मात्रा Pt. 1. 40; मातः कियन्तोऽरयः Ve. 5. 9.<BR>—3 Some, a little; a small number, a few (having an indefinite force);<BR> निजहृदि विकसन्तः सन्ति सन्तः कियन्तः Bh. 2. 78; त्वदभिसरणरभसेन<BR> वलन्ती पतति पदानि कियन्ति चलन्ती Gīt. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कियदेतद्, कियदेतिका, कियत्कालम्, कियच्चिरम्, कियद्दूरम्, कियन्मात्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियदेतद्
कियत् + -एतद् of what importance is this to; कियदेतद्धनं पुंसः Ks. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियदेतिका
कियत् + -एतिका effort, vigorous and persevering exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियत्कालम्
कियत् + -कालम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 how long.<BR>—2 some little time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियच्चिरम्
कियत् + -चिरम् <i>ind.</i> how long; कियच्चिरं श्राम्यसि गौरि Ku. 5. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियद्दूरम्
कियत् + -दूरम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 how far, how distant, how long; कियद्दूरे स जलाशयः Pt. 1; N. 1. 137.<BR>—2 for a short time, a little way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियन्मात्रः|कियन्मात्र
कियत् + -मात्रः a trifle, small matter; कियन्मात्रे कृतोऽनेन संरम्भोऽयं<BR> कियानिति Ks. 65. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियाहः|कियाह
कियाहः A horse of a red or bay colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरः|किर
किरः A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरकः|किरक
किरकः<BR>—1 A scribe.<BR>—2 A pig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणः|किरण
किरणः [कृ-क्यु Uṇ. 2. 81]<BR>—1 A ray or beam of light, a ray (of the sun, moon or any shining substance);<BR> रविकिरणसहिष्णु Ś. 2. 4; एको हि दोषो गुणसंनिपाते निमज्जतीन्दोः<BR> किरणेष्विवाङ्कः Ku. 1. 3; Śānti. 4. 6; R. 5. 74; Śi. 4. 58; ˚मय<BR> radiant, brilliant.<BR>—2 A small particle of dust.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किरणपतिः, किरणमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणपतिः|किरणपति
किरणः + -पतिः, -मालिन् <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणमालिन्
किरणः + -पतिः, -मालिन् <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराटः|किराट
किराटः A merchant; पणयिष्यन्ति वै क्षुद्राः किराटाः कूटकारिणः<BR> Bhāg. 12. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातः|किरात
किरातः [किरं पर्यन्तभूमिम् अतति गच्छतीति किरातः]<BR>—1 N. of a degraded mountain tribe who live by hunting, a mountaineer;<BR> वैयाकरणकिरातादपशब्दमृगाः क्व यान्तु संत्रस्ताः । यदि नटगणकचिकित्सकवैतालिकवदनकन्दरा<BR> न स्युः ॥ Subhāṣ.; Pt. 1. 17; पर्यन्ताश्रयिभिर्निजस्य सदृशं नाम्नः<BR> किरातैः कृतम् Ratn. 2. 3; Ku. 1. 6, 15. जवार इति यद्राज्यं किरातानां<BR> पुरातनम् Parṇāl. 1. 39.<BR>—2 A savage, barbarian.<BR>—3 A dwarf.<BR>—4 A groom, a horseman.<BR>—5 N. of Śiva in the disguise of a Kirāta.<BR>—6 A species of fish; किरातो लुब्धके देववाहिनीमत्स्यभेदयोः Nm.<BR>—7 N. of a medicinal herb (Mar. किराईत, चिराईत, भूनिंब)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराताः
किरातः + .{@-ताः@} (pl.) N. of a country.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किरातार्जुनीयम्, किराताशिन्, किराततिक्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातार्जुनीयम्
किरातः + -अर्जुनीयम् N. of a poem by Bhāravi (in which the combat of Arjuna<BR> with Śiva in the form of a Kirāta or mountaineer is poetically described.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराताशिन्
किरातः + -आशिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराततिक्तः|किराततिक्त
किरातः + -तिक्तः N. of a medicinal herb (Mar. किराईत, चिराईत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातकः|किरातक
किरातकः, -तिकः<BR>—1 The bitter gentianaceae (Mar. चिराईत).<BR>—2 A man of the Kirāta tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिकः
किरातकः, -तिकः<BR>—1 The bitter gentianaceae (Mar. चिराईत).<BR>—2 A man of the Kirāta tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिः|किराति
किरातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The Ganges.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिनी
किरातिनी <i>f.</i> N. of a plant (जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराती
किराती<BR>—1 A female Kirāta, a woman of the Kirāta tribe.<BR>—2 A woman who carries a fly-flap or chowri; नौसंश्रयः पार्श्वगतां<BR> किरातीमुपात्तबालव्यजनां बभाषे R. 16. 57.<BR>—3 A bawd, a procuress.<BR>—4 Pārvatī in the disguise of a Kirātī.<BR>—5 The celestial Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिः|किरि
किरिः [किरति भूमिम्, कॄ-इक्]<BR>—1 A hog, boar.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिटिः|किरिटि
किरिटिः The fruit of the marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटः|किरीट|किरीटं
किरीटः, -टम्<BR> [कॄ-किटन्; Uṇ. 4. 184]<BR>—1 A diadem, crown, crest, tiara; किरीटबद्धाञ्जलयः Ku. 7. 92.<BR>—2 A trader. See किराट.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किरीटधारिन्, किरीटमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटम्
किरीटः, -टम्<BR> [कॄ-किटन्; Uṇ. 4. 184]<BR>—1 A diadem, crown, crest, tiara; किरीटबद्धाञ्जलयः Ku. 7. 92.<BR>—2 A trader. See किराट.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किरीटधारिन्, किरीटमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटधारिन्
किरीटः + -धारिन् <i>m.</i> a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटमालिन्
किरीटः + -मालिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटिन्
किरीटिन् <i>a.</i> [किरीट-इनि] Wearing a crown or diadem; Bg. 11. 17,<BR> किरीटिनं गदिनं चकहस्तमिच्छामि त्वां द्रष्टुमहं तथैव 46;<BR> Pt. 3. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of Arjuna; एतच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं केशवस्य कृताञ्जलिर्वेपमानः किरीटी<BR> Bg. 11. 35. (Mb. thus accounts for the name:− पुरा शक्रेण मे बद्धं<BR> युध्यतो दानवर्षभैः । किरीटं मूर्ध्नि सूर्याभं तेनाहुर्मां किरीटिनम् ॥)<BR>—2 N. of Indra; Mb. 1. 34. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मिः
किर्मिः, -र्मी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A hall, building.<BR>—2 An image of gold or iron.<BR>—3 The Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मी|किर्म्मी
किर्मिः, -र्मी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A hall, building.<BR>—2 An image of gold or iron.<BR>—3 The Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीर|किर्मीरः|किर्म्मीर|किर्म्मीरः
किर्मीर <i>a.</i> Variegated, spotted. कान्तिभिः सकलं ञ्योम तदा<BR> किर्मीरतां दधौ Śiva B. 24. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरः|किर्मीर|किर्म्मीर|किर्म्मीरः
किर्मीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 N. of a Rākṣasa slain by Bhīma; Mb. 3; Ve. 6.<BR>—2 The variegated colour.<BR>—3 The orange tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किर्मीरजित्, किर्मीरनिषूदनः, किर्मीरसूदनः, किर्मीरत्वच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरजित्|किर्म्मीरजित्
किर्मीर + -जित्, -निषूदनः, -सूदनः epithets of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरनिषूदनः|किर्मीरनिषूदन
किर्मीर + -जित्, -निषूदनः, -सूदनः epithets of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरसूदनः|किर्मीरसूदन|किर्म्मीरसूदन|किर्म्मीरसूदनः
किर्मीर + -जित्, -निषूदनः, -सूदनः epithets of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरत्वच्|किर्म्मीरत्वच्
किर्मीर + -त्वच् The orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरित|किर्म्मीरित
किर्मीरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Variegated, spotted. शर्मोर्मिकिर्मीरितधर्मलिप्सुः N. 6. 97.<BR>—2 Mingled with; तत्रास्मि पत्युर्वरिवस्ययेह शर्मोर्मिकिर्मीरितधर्मलिप्सुः<BR> Hc. 6. 97; cf. also क्षुत्क्षामार्भकसंभ्रमोक्तिनिगडैः किर्मीरिताः …<BR> Sūkti. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्याणी
किर्याणी A wild hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्
किल् I. €6 P. (किलति, किलित)<BR>—1 To be or become white.<BR>—2 To freeze.<BR>—3 To play, sport. ━II. €10 P.<BR>—1 To urge, instigate.<BR>—2 To throw, cast, send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलः|किल
किलः —1 Play, trifling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किलकिञ्चितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिञ्चितम्
किलः + -किञ्चितम् amorous agitation, weeping, laughing, being angry &c.<BR> in the society of a lover; त्वयि वीर विराजते परं दमयन्तीकिलकिञ्चितं<BR> किल N. 2. 44. जानानाभिरलं लीला-किल-किंचित-विभ्रमान् । Bk. 8. 47.<BR> The नाट्यशास्त्र refers to it in the following context विलासलीलाः<BR> किलकिंचितानि विव्वोक-मोट्टायित-विभ्रमाणि । विच्छित्तमाकुट्टिमितेक्षितानि<BR> योज्यानि तज्ज्ञैः सुकुमारनृत्ते ॥ (cf. also ‘क्रोधाश्रुहर्षभीत्यादेः संकरः किलकिञ्चितम्’ इति आलङ्कारिकाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Verily, indeed, assuredly, certainly; अर्हति किल कितव उपद्रवम्<BR> M. 4; इदं किलाव्याजमनोहरं वपुः Ś. 1. 18.<BR>—2 As they say, as is reported (showing report or tradition ऐतिह्य);<BR> बभूव योगी किल कार्तवीर्यः R. 6. 38, 13. 51; जघान कंसं किल<BR> वासुदेवः Mbh.<BR>—3 A feigned action (अलीक); प्रसह्य सिंहः किल तां चकर्ष<BR> R. 2. 27; Mu. 7. 9; पयस्यगाधे किल जातसंभ्रमा Ki. 8. 48, 11. 2.<BR>—4 Hope, expectation or probability; पार्थः किल विजेष्यते कुरून् G. M.<BR>—5 Dissatisfaction, dislike; एवं किल केचिद्वदन्ति G. M.<BR>—6 Contempt; त्वं किल योत्स्यसे G. M.<BR>—7 Cause, reason (हेतु); (very rare) स किलैवमुक्तवान् G. M. ‘for he said so’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिलः|किलकिल
किलकिलः, -ला<BR> A sound, a cry expressing joy or pleasure; विनेदुर्मुदिताः<BR> केचित्केचित्किलकिलां तथा Rām. 5. 57. 34; Māl. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिला
किलकिलः, -ला<BR> A sound, a cry expressing joy or pleasure; विनेदुर्मुदिताः<BR> केचित्केचित्किलकिलां तथा Rām. 5. 57. 34; Māl. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिलः|किलकिल
किलकिलः, -ला + .{@-लः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिलायति
किलकिलायति, -ते Den.<BR> To make a chattering noise; सर्वे (वानराः) किलकिलायन्तः Bk. 7. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिलायते
किलकिलायति, -ते Den.<BR> To make a chattering noise; सर्वे (वानराः) किलकिलायन्तः Bk. 7. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिकिलितम्
किलिकिलितम् Sounds expressing joy; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटः|किलाट
किलाटः Coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटिन्
किलाटिन्, -टः <i>m.</i><BR> A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटः|किलाट
किलाटिन्, -टः <i>m.</i><BR> A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलातः|किलात
किलातः A dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलास|किलासं
किलास <i>a.</i> Ved. Leprous; चन्द्रमसे किलासम् Vāj. 30. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासम्
किलास + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 A white leprous spot; इदं रजनि रजय किलासं पलितं च यत् Av. 1. 23. 1.<BR>—2 A blotch, scab.<BR>—3 A kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासिन्
किलास + .{@-सिन्@} <i>a.</i> Leprous; P. V. 2. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्जम्
किलिञ्जम्<BR>—1 A mat, also किलञ्जम्.<BR>—2 A thin plank of green wood, board; also किलिञ्चम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्जकः|किलिञ्जक|किलिंजकः
किलिञ्जकः<BR>—1 A mat.<BR>—2 A screen or twist of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिमम्
किलिमम् The fir or pine tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्किन्
किल्कि(ल्वि)न् <i>m.</i> A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विन्
किल्कि(ल्वि)न् <i>m.</i> A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्बिषम्
किल्बिषम्<BR>—1 Sin; Ms. 4. 243, 10. 118; यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः<BR> Bg. 3. 13, 6. 45; R. 11. 34.<BR>—2 A fault, offence, injury, guilt; तस्य तत्किल्बिषं नित्यं हृदि वर्तति<BR> भार्गव Mb. 1. 5. 20; Ms. 8. 235.<BR>—3 A disease, sickness.<BR>—4 A calamity, adversity; पितेव पुत्रं धर्मात्मंस्त्रातुमर्हसि किल्बिषात्<BR> Rām. 1. 62. 7.<BR>—5 Fraud, deceit; यदयं किल्बिषाद्भेदः कृतोऽप्येवं न गृह्यते Rām. 2. 23. 13.<BR>—6 Enmity, hostility; भास्करस्यौरसः पुत्रो वालिना कृतकिल्बिषः Rām. 3. 72. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्बिषः|किल्बिष
किल्बिषम् + .{@-षः@} as किल्बिषम्; प्राणायामैर्दहेद्दोषान्धारणाभिश्च किल्बिषान्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 28. 11. ━<i>a.</i> Sinful; नैतन्मनसि वाक्यं मे किल्बिषं प्रतितिष्ठति<BR> Rām. 5. 24. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलम्
किशलम् A sprout, shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलयः|किशलय|किशलयं
किशलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young shoot; see किसलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलयम्
किशलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young shoot; see किसलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशोरः|किशोर
किशोरः [Uṇ. 1. 65]<BR>—1 A colt, cub, the young of any animal; केसरिकिशोरः &c. ततः<BR> किशोरा म्रियन्ते Av. 12. 4. 7.<BR>—2 A youth, lad, a boy below fifteen, a minor in law (अप्राप्तव्यवहारः);<BR> न बालो न किशोरस्त्वं बलश्च बलिनां वरः Bhāg. 10. 43. 39.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशोरी
किशोरः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A young one of any animal (as horse), mare; उद्दामेव किशोरी नियतिः<BR> खलु प्रत्येषितुं याति Mk. 10. 19.<BR>—2 A maiden, a young woman.<BR>—3 A daughter; भजामस्त्वां गौरीं नगपतिकिशोरीमविरतम् Sundaralaharī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्धः|किष्किन्ध|किष्किंध|किष्किंधः
किष्किन्धः, -न्ध्यः<BR> [P. VI. 1. 157.]<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 N. of a mountain situated in that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्यः|किष्किन्ध्य|किष्किंध्य|किष्किंध्यः
किष्किन्धः, -न्ध्यः<BR> [P. VI. 1. 157.]<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 N. of a mountain situated in that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्धा|किष्किंधा
किष्किन्धः, -न्ध्यः + .{@-न्धा, -न्ध्या@} N. of a city, the capital of Kiṣkindha. किष्किन्धाकाण्डम्<BR> N. of the fourth book of Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्या|किष्किंध्या
किष्किन्धः, -न्ध्यः + .{@-न्धा, -न्ध्या@} N. of a city, the capital of Kiṣkindha. किष्किन्धाकाण्डम्<BR> N. of the fourth book of Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कु|किष्कुः
किष्कु <i>a.</i> [P. VI. 1. 157.] Vile, contemptible, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कुः|किष्कु
किष्कु + .{@-ष्कुः@} <i>m.</i> or <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The fore-arm. fore-arm measure (= 24<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">Page0574-2</a>]<BR> Aṅgulas); Rām. 5. 35. 18.<BR>—2 A cubit, span; अवर्धत महातेजाः किष्कून्राजंस्त्रयोदश Mb. 3. 126. 32.<BR>—3 An instrument for measuring lengths.<BR>—4 A cubit of 24 or 42 Aṅgulas; किष्कुः स्मृतो द्विरत्निस्तु द्विचत्वारिंशदङ्गुलः ।<BR> (Brahmāṇḍa P. Ch. 7. 5. 99.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: किष्कुपर्वन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कुपर्वन्|किष्कुपर्व्वन्
किष्कु + -पर्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Sugar-cane.<BR>—2 A bamboo.<BR>—3 A kind of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलः|किसल|किसलं
किसलः, -लम्, किसलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young and tender shoot or foliage;<BR> अधरः किसलयरागः Ś. 1. 21; किसलयमलूनं कररुहैः 2. 10;<BR> किसलयैः सलयैरिव पाणिभिः R. 9. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलम्
किसलः, -लम्, किसलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young and tender shoot or foliage;<BR> अधरः किसलयरागः Ś. 1. 21; किसलयमलूनं कररुहैः 2. 10;<BR> किसलयैः सलयैरिव पाणिभिः R. 9. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलयः|किसलय|किसलयं
किसलः, -लम्, किसलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young and tender shoot or foliage;<BR> अधरः किसलयरागः Ś. 1. 21; किसलयमलूनं कररुहैः 2. 10;<BR> किसलयैः सलयैरिव पाणिभिः R. 9. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलयम्
किसलः, -लम्, किसलयः, -यम्<BR> A sprout, a young and tender shoot or foliage;<BR> अधरः किसलयरागः Ś. 1. 21; किसलयमलूनं कररुहैः 2. 10;<BR> किसलयैः सलयैरिव पाणिभिः R. 9. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकट|कीकटः
कीकट <i>a.</i> (-टी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Poor, indigent.<BR>—2 Miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकटाः
कीकट + .{@-टाः@} (pl.) N. of a country (Behār). N. of a people not belonging<BR> to the Āryan race; किं ते कृण्वन्ति कीकटेषु गावो नाशिरं दुह्रे न तपन्ति<BR> धर्मम् Rv. 3. 53. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकटः|कीकट
कीकट + .{@-टः@} A horse. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Poor.<BR>—2 Avaricious. See कोटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकस|कीकसं|कीकसः
कीकस <i>a.</i> Hard, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसम्
कीकस + .{@-सम्@} A bone (<i>m.</i> also); Mv. 5. 19; cf. ‘कीकसं कुल्यमस्थि च’ Ak.;<BR> अचिरनष्टहिमागमकीकसभ्रमकृतां Rām. Ch. 4. 86.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कीकसास्थि, कीकसास्यः, कीकसमुखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसास्थि
कीकस + -अस्थि <i>n.</i> Vertebra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसास्यः|कीकसास्य
कीकस + -आस्यः, -मुखः a bird in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसमुखः|कीकसमुख
कीकस + -आस्यः, -मुखः a bird in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकिः|कीकि
कीकिः A blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकः|कीचक
कीचकः [Uṇ. 5. 56]<BR>—1 A hollow bamboo.<BR>—2 A bamboo rattling or whistling in the wind; शब्दायन्ते मधुरमनिलैः<BR> कीचकाः पूर्यमाणाः Me. 58; R. 2. 12, 4. 73; Ku. 1. 8.<BR>—3 N. of a people.<BR>—4 N. of the commander-in-chief of king Virāṭa; कीचकानां वधः पर्व<BR> Mb. 1. 2. 58. [While Draupadī in the guise of Sairandhrī was residing<BR> at the court of king Virāṭa with her five husbands also disguised, Kīchaka<BR> once happened to see her, and her beauty stirred up wicked passion in<BR> his heart. He, thenceforward, kept a sinister eye on her, and endeavoured<BR> through the help of his sister, the kingʼs wife, to violate her chastity.<BR> Draupadī complained of his unmannerly conduct towards herself to the<BR> king; but when he declined to interfere, she sought the assistance of Bhīma,<BR> and at his suggestion showed herself favourable to his advances. It was<BR> then agreed that they should meet at midnight in the dancing hall of the<BR> palace. Pursuant to appointment Kīchaka went there and attempted to embrace<BR> Draupadi (as he fancied Bhīma to be owing to the darkness of night).<BR> But the wretch was at once seized and crushed to death by the powerful Bhīma.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कीचकजित्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकजित्
कीचकः + -जित् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Bhīma, the second Pāṇḍava prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीज|कीजः
कीज <i>a.</i> Ved. Wonderful<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीजः|कीज
कीज + .{@-जः@} A kind of instrument; यो वा कीजो हिरण्ययः Rv. 8. 66. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट्
कीट् €10 P. (कीटयति, कीटित)<BR>—1 To tinge or colour.<BR>—2 To bind, fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट <i>a.</i> Hard, harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटः|कीट
कीट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A worm, an insect; Ms. 1. 40; कीटोऽपि सुमनःसङ्गादारोहति सतां<BR> शिरः H. Pr. 39.<BR>—2 A term expressive of contempt (generally at the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0575-1" target="_blank">Page0575-1</a>]<BR> end of comp.); द्विपकीटः a wretched elephant; so पक्षिकीटः Pt. 1; &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कीटावपन्न, कीटोत्करम्, कीटघ्नः, कीटजम्, कीटजा, कीटनामा, कीटपादिका, कीटपादी, कीटमाता, कीटमणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटावपन्न
कीट + -अवपन्न <i>a.</i> anything on which an insect has fallen; worm-eaten;<BR> क्षतं कीटावपन्नं च Mb. 9. 43. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटोत्करम्
कीट + -उत्करम् an ant-hill; तत्र कीटोत्कराकीर्णे Ks. 101. 290. 11<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

