कुक्षः|कुक्ष
कुक्षः The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिः|कुक्षि
कुक्षिः<BR>—1 The belly (in general); जिह्मिताध्मातकुक्षिः (भुजगपतिः) Mk. 9. 12.<BR>—2 The womb, the part of the belly containing the foetus; कुम्भीनस्याश्च<BR> कुक्षिजः R. 15. 15; Śi. 13. 40.<BR>—3 The interior of anything; विभक्तात्मा विभुस्तासामेकः कुक्षिष्वनेकधा<BR> R. 10. 65 (where the word is used in sense 2 also.)<BR>—4 A cavity in general.<BR>—5 A cavern, cave;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0577-2" target="_blank">Page0577-2</a>]<BR> अद्रिकुक्षौ, हैमवताच्च कुक्षेः R. 2. 38, 67; a valley; अस्तीह हिमवत्कुक्षौ<BR> देशः पृथ्वीशिरोमणिः Ks. 65. 214.<BR>—6 The sheath of a sword.<BR>—7 N. of Bali.<BR>—8 A bay, gulf.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुक्षिगत, कुक्षिजः, कुक्षिशूलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिगत
