कुधिः|कुधि
कुधिः An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुध्रः|कुध्र
कुध्रः A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनकः|कुनक
कुनकः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनालिका
कुनालिका The (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तः|कुन्त|कुंत|कुंतः
कुन्तः<BR>—1 A lance, a barbed dart, spear; कुन्ताः प्रविशन्ति K. P. 2. (<i>i. e.</i><BR> कुन्तधारिणः पुरुषाः); विरहिणीकृन्तनकुन्तमुखाकृतिकेतकीदन्तुरिताशे<BR> Gīt. 1; Mb. 6. 96. 57.<BR>—2 A small animal, an insect.<BR>—3 A kind of grain.<BR>—4 Passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलः|कुन्तल|कुंतल|कुंतलः
कुन्तलः<BR>—1 The hair of the head, a lock of hair; प्रतनुविरलैः प्रान्तोन्मीलन्मनोहरकुन्तलैः<BR> U. 1. 20; C. P. 4, 6; Gīt. 2.<BR>—2 A drinking cup.<BR>—3 A plough.<BR>—4 Barley.<BR>—5 A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलाः
कुन्तलः + .{@-लाः@} (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुन्तलोशीरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलोशीरम्
कुन्तलः + -उशीरम् a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलिका|कुंतलिका
कुन्तलिका A butter-knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तयः|कुन्तय
कुन्तयः (pl. of कुन्ति <i>m.</i>) N. of a country and its people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तिः|कुन्ति|कुंति|कुंतिः
कुन्तिः<BR>—1 N. of a king, son of क्रथ; क्रथस्य कुन्तिः पुत्रोऽभूत् Bhāg. 9. 24. 3.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa; Bhāg. 10. 61. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुन्तिभोजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तिभोजः|कुन्तिभोज
कुन्तिः + -भोजः N. of a Yādava prince, king of the Kunties, who being<BR> childless, adopted Kuntī. पुरुजित् कुन्तिभोजश्च Bg. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्ती
कुन्ती<BR>—1 N. of पृथा, daughter of a Yādava named शूर, adopted by कुन्तिभोज.<BR> [She was the first wife of Pāṇḍu. As he was prevented by a curse from<BR> having progeny, he allowed his wife to make use of a charm she had acquired<BR> from the sage Durvāsas, by means of which she was to have a son by any<BR> god she liked to invoke. She invoked Dharma, Vāyu and Indra, and had<BR> from them Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma and Arjuna respectively. She was also mother<BR> of Karṇa by the deity Sun whom she invoked in her virginhood to test her charm.]<BR>—2 A fragrant resin.<BR>—3 The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द्र्
कुन्द्र्^1 €10 P. To speak falsehood.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260701. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थ्|कुंथ्
कुन्थ् €1. €9 P. (कुन्थति, कुथ्नाति, कुन्थित)<BR>—1 To suffer pain.<BR>—2 To cling to.<BR>—3 To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दः|कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः
कुन्दः, -न्दम्<BR> [Uṇ. 4. 98] A kind of jasmine (white and delicate); कुन्दावदाताः<BR> कलहंसमालाः Bk. 2. 18; प्रातः कुन्दप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं धारयेथाः<BR> Me. 115; Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दम्
कुन्दः, -न्दम्<BR> [Uṇ. 4. 98] A kind of jasmine (white and delicate); कुन्दावदाताः<BR> कलहंसमालाः Bk. 2. 18; प्रातः कुन्दप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं धारयेथाः<BR> Me. 115; Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दम्
कुन्दः, -न्दम् + .{@-न्दम्@} The flower of this plant; अलके बालकुन्दानुविद्धम् Me. 67, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दः|कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः
कुन्दः, -न्दम् + .{@-न्दः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 A fragrant oleander.<BR>—3 One of the nine treasures of Kubera.<BR>—4 The number ‘nine’.<BR>—5 A lotus.<BR>—6 A turnerʼs lathe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुन्दकरः, कुन्दचतुर्थी, कुन्दसमदन्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दकरः|कुन्दकर|कुंदकर
कुन्दः + -करः a turner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दचतुर्थी
कुन्दः + -चतुर्थी the fourth day in the light half of the month माघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दसमदन्त
कुन्दः + -समदन्त <i>a.</i> One whose teeth are like the jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दिनी|कुंदिनी
कुन्दिनी A multitude of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दमः|कुन्दम|कुंदम|कुंदमः
कुन्दमः A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दरः|कुन्दर|कुंदरः
कुन्दरः<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 A kind of grass (Mar. पालख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुः|कुन्दु|कुंदु|कुंदुः
कुन्दुः A rat, mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्
कुप् I. €4 P. (कुप्यति, चुकोप, अकुपत्, कोपितुम्, कुपित)<BR>—1 To be angry, (generally with the dat. of the person who is the object<BR> of anger, but sometimes with the acc. or gen. also); कुप्यन्ति हितवादिने<BR> K. 108; कुपितश्चन्द्रगुप्तश्चाणक्यस्योपरि Mu. 2; M. 3. 21; U. 7;<BR> चुकोप तस्मै स भृशम् R. 3. 56.<BR>—2 To be excited, to gather strength, be virulent; as in दोषाः प्रकुप्यन्ति<BR> Suśr. ━<i>Caus.</i> (कोपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To provoke, irritate; to excite, agitate.<BR>—2 To stir up. ━II. €10 U.<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित <i>a.</i> Provoked, offended, angry.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुपितवायुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितवायुः|कुपितवायु
कुपित + -वायुः aggravated flatulence, hypochondria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपः|कोप
कोपः [कुप्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Anger, wrath, passion; कोपं न गच्छति नितान्तबलोऽपि नागः Pt. 1. 123;<BR> न त्वया कोपः कार्यः do not be angry.<BR>—2 (In medicine) Morbid irritation or disorder of the humours of the body;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> पित्तकोप, वातकोप. &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोपाकुल, कोपाविष्ट, कोपक्रमः, कोपजन्मन्, कोपदीप्त, कोपज्वलित, कोपपदम्, कोपवशः, कोपवेगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपाकुल
कोपः + -आकुल, -आविष्ट <i>a.</i> enraged, furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपाविष्ट
कोपः + -आकुल, -आविष्ट <i>a.</i> enraged, furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपक्रमः|कोपक्रम|कोपक्रमं
कोपः + -क्रमः<BR>—1 an angry or passionate man.<BR>—2 the course of anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपजन्मन्
कोपः + -जन्मन् produced by wrath or anger; बलवानपि कोपजन्मनः Ki. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपदीप्त
कोपः + -दीप्त, -ज्वलित <i>a.</i> inflamed with anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपज्वलित
कोपः + -दीप्त, -ज्वलित <i>a.</i> inflamed with anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपपदम्
कोपः + -पदम्<BR>—1 cause of anger.<BR>—2 pretended anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवशः|कोपवश
कोपः + -वशः subjection to anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवेगः|कोपवेग
कोपः + -वेगः violence, fury of anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपन|कोपनः
कोपन <i>a.</i> [कुप्-ताच्छील्ये युच्]<BR>—1 Passionate, irascible, angry; रैभश्चापि तपस्वी च कोपनश्च महानृषिः<BR> Mb. 3. 135. 58.<BR>—2 Causing anger.<BR>—3 Irritating, causing morbid disorder of the humours of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपनम्
कोपन + .{@-नम्@} Becoming angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपना
कोपन + .{@-ना@} A passionate or angry woman; कयासि कामिन् सुरतापराधात्<BR> पादानतः कोपनयाऽवधूतः Ku. 3. 8; Amaru. 68. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपनक|कोपनकः
कोपनक <i>a.</i> Angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपनकः|कोपनक
कोपनक + .{@-कः@} A kind of perfume (Mar. किरमाणी ओवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपयिष्णु
कोपयिष्णु <i>a.</i> [कुप-णिच् बा˚ इष्णुच्] Intending to enrage or<BR> exasperate, inclined to make angry; श्रावितास्ते महात्मानः पाण्डवाः कोपयिष्णुभिः<BR> Mb. 7. 137. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0582-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपित
कोपित <i>a.</i> Enraged, furious, provoked &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपिन्
कोपिन् <i>a.</i> [अवश्यं कुप्यति कुप्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Angry, irritated; सत्यमेवासि यदि मयि कोपिनी Gīt. 10.<BR>—2 Causing anger.<BR>—3 Irritating, causing disorder of the humours of the body. ━<i>m.</i> A water-pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपः|कुप
कुपः Ved. The beam or lever of a pair of scales.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपय
कुपय <i>a.</i> Ved. To be guarded or protected. मा साच्यं कुपयं<BR> वर्धनं पितुः Rv. 1. 140. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिन्द|कुपिंद|कुपिंदः|कुपिन्दः
कुपिन्द See कुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनिन्
कुपिनिन् <i>m.</i> A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनी
कुपिनी A kind of net for catching small fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपूय|कुपूयः
कुपूय <i>a.</i> Despised, low, mean, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यम्
कुप्यम्<BR>—1 A base metal.<BR>—2 Any metal but silver and gold; Ki. 1. 35; Ms. 7. 96, 10. 113; cf. स्यात्<BR> कोशश्च हिरण्यं च हेमरूप्ये कृताऽकृते । ताभ्यां यदन्यत् तत् कुप्यम् …<BR> Nm. रत्नान्नपानकुप्यानामाटतुर्नष्टसंस्मृती । Bk. 6. 59. कुप्यप्रदिष्टानां<BR> च द्रव्याणामेकैकशो वा वनं निवेशयेत् Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुप्यधौतम्, कुप्यशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यधौतम्
कुप्यम् + -धौतम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यशाला
कुप्यम् + -शाला a braziery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबलम्
कुबलम् (See कबलम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेरः|कुबेर
कुबे(वे)रः [कुत्सितं बे(वे)रं शरीरं यस्य सः]<BR>—1 The god of riches and treasure and the regent of the northern quarter;<BR> कुबेरगुप्तां दिशमुष्णरश्मौ गन्तुं प्रवृत्ते समयं विलङ्घ्य Ku. 3. 25<BR> (<i>vide</i> Malli. thereon). [Kubera is the son of Viśravas by Iḍāviḍā,<BR> and thus the half brother of Rāvaṇa. Besides, being the lord of riches<BR> and regent of the north, he is the king of the Yakṣas and Kinnaras, and<BR> a friend of Rudra. His abode is Kailāsa. He is represented as being deformed<BR> in body-having three legs, only eight teeth, and a yellow mark in place of one eye.]<BR>—2 N. of a tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुबेराक्षी, कुबेराद्रिः, कुबेराचलः, कुबेरदिश्, कुबेरबान्धवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेरः|कुवेर
कुबे(वे)रः [कुत्सितं बे(वे)रं शरीरं यस्य सः]<BR>—1 The god of riches and treasure and the regent of the northern quarter;<BR> कुबेरगुप्तां दिशमुष्णरश्मौ गन्तुं प्रवृत्ते समयं विलङ्घ्य Ku. 3. 25<BR> (<i>vide</i> Malli. thereon). [Kubera is the son of Viśravas by Iḍāviḍā,<BR> and thus the half brother of Rāvaṇa. Besides, being the lord of riches<BR> and regent of the north, he is the king of the Yakṣas and Kinnaras, and<BR> a friend of Rudra. His abode is Kailāsa. He is represented as being deformed<BR> in body-having three legs, only eight teeth, and a yellow mark in place of one eye.]<BR>—2 N. of a tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुबेराक्षी, कुबेराद्रिः, कुबेराचलः, कुबेरदिश्, कुबेरबान्धवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेराक्षी
कुबेरः + -अक्षी N. of a plant (Mar. सागरगोटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेराद्रिः|कुबेराद्रि
कुबेरः + -अद्रिः, -अचलः an epithet of mountain Kailāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेराचलः|कुबेराचल
कुबेरः + -अद्रिः, -अचलः an epithet of mountain Kailāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेरदिश्
कुबेरः + -दिश् <i>f.</i> the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेरबान्धवः|कुबेरबान्धव
कुबेरः + -बान्धवः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज <i>a.</i> [कु ईषत् उब्जमार्जवं यत्र शकं˚ Tv.] Hump-backed,<BR> crooked. अन्धाः खञ्जाः कुब्जा वामनकाश्च Garbha. Up. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जः|कुब्ज
कुब्ज + .{@-ब्जः@}<BR>—1 A curved sword.<BR>—2 A hump on the back.<BR>—3 A sort of fish; Mb. 7. 56. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जा
कुब्ज + .{@-ब्जा@} A young female servant of Kaṃsa, said to be deformed in<BR> three parts of her body. [Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, while proceeding to<BR> Mathurā, saw her on the high road carrying unguent to Kaṃsa. They asked<BR> her if she would give them some portion of it, and she gave as much as<BR> they wanted. Kṛṣṇa, being very much pleased with her kindness, made<BR> her perfectly straight, and she began to appear a most beautiful woman.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुब्जकिरातः, कुब्जवामनः, कुब्जगामिन्, कुब्जलीला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जकिरातम्
कुब्ज + -किरातम्^1, -वामनम्^2 a^3 hump-backed person and a dwarf.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जवामन
कुब्ज + -किरातम्^1, -वामनम्^2 a^3 hump-backed person and a dwarf.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जगामिन्
कुब्ज + -गामिन् <i>a.</i> going crookedly, going astray; बुद्धयः कुब्जगामिन्यो<BR> भवन्ति महतामपि Pt. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जलीला
कुब्ज + -लीला the manner, gait or character of a hump-backed person; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

