कुमारः + -संभवम् N. of Kalidāsaʼs epic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारकः|कुमारक
कुमारकः<BR>—1 A child, a youth; नहि वो अस्त्यर्भको देवासो न कुमारकः Rv. 8. 30. 1.<BR>—2 The pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयति
कुमारयति Den. P. [कुमार इव आचरति] To play, sport (like a child).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयुः|कुमारयु
कुमारयुः A prince, heir-apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिक
कुमारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Furnished with girls, abounding in girls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिकी
कुमारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Furnished with girls, abounding in girls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिन्
कुमारिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> {{Furnished with girls, abounding in girls->Having children; granting children||20260705|Scott Rhodes|https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/288}}}.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिणी
कुमारिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> {{Furnished with girls, abounding in girls->Having children; granting children||20260705|Scott Rhodes|https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/288}}}.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिका
कुमारिका, कुमारी<BR>—1 A young girl, one from 10 to 12 years old.<BR>—2 A maiden, virgin; त्रीणि वर्षाण्युदीक्षेत कुमार्यृतुमती सती Ms. 9. 90, 11. 59;<BR> व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी R. 6. 69.<BR>—3 A girl or daughter in general.<BR>—4 N. of Durgā.<BR>—5 N. of several plants (Mar. कोरफड, कर्टोली, कांटेशेवंती, बटमोगरा इ).<BR>—6 N. of Sītā.<BR>—7 Large cardamoms.<BR>—8 The southern extremity of the Indian peninsula (cf. the modern name Cape Comorin).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुमारिकापुत्रः, कुमारिकापुरम्, कुमारिकाश्वशुरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारी
कुमारिका, कुमारी<BR>—1 A young girl, one from 10 to 12 years old.<BR>—2 A maiden, virgin; त्रीणि वर्षाण्युदीक्षेत कुमार्यृतुमती सती Ms. 9. 90, 11. 59;<BR> व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी R. 6. 69.<BR>—3 A girl or daughter in general.<BR>—4 N. of Durgā.<BR>—5 N. of several plants (Mar. कोरफड, कर्टोली, कांटेशेवंती, बटमोगरा इ).<BR>—6 N. of Sītā.<BR>—7 Large cardamoms.<BR>—8 The southern extremity of the Indian peninsula (cf. the modern name Cape Comorin).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कुमारिकापुत्रः, कुमारिकापुरम्, कुमारिकाश्वशुरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिकापुत्रः|कुमारिकापुत्र
कुमारिका + -पुत्रः<BR>—1 the son of an unmarried woman.<BR>—2 N. of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिकापुरम्
कुमारिका + -पुरम् a gymansium or a girlʼs apartment. अपुंस्त्वमप्यस्य निशम्य<BR> च स्थिरं ततः कुमारीपुरमुत्ससर्ज तम् Mb. 4. 11. 12; Kau. A. यदि<BR> कुमारीपुरप्रवेशाभ्युपायं नावबुध्यसे Dk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिकाश्वशुरः|कुमारिकाश्वशुर
कुमारिका + -श्वशुरः the father-in-law of a girl defiled before marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालकः|कुमालक
कुमालकः N. of a country, a Taluka in the Mālava country (सौवीरदेश ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>—2 Avaricious. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 The white water-lily.<BR>—2 The red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदः|कुमुद|कुमुदं
कुमुदः, -दम्<BR> [कौ भोदते इति कुमुदम्]<BR>—1 The white water-lily said to open at moon-rise [Nymphea alba] नोच्छ्वसिति<BR> तपनकिरणैश्चन्द्रस्येवांशुभिः कुमुदम् V. 3. 16; so Ś. 5. 28; Ṛs. 3. 2, 21, 23;<BR> Me. 42. कुमुदवनमपश्रि श्रीमदम्भोजषण्डम् Śi. 11. 64.<BR>—2 A red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदम्
कुमुदः, -दम्<BR> [कौ भोदते इति कुमुदम्]<BR>—1 The white water-lily said to open at moon-rise [Nymphea alba] नोच्छ्वसिति<BR> तपनकिरणैश्चन्द्रस्येवांशुभिः कुमुदम् V. 3. 16; so Ś. 5. 28; Ṛs. 3. 2, 21, 23;<BR> Me. 42. कुमुदवनमपश्रि श्रीमदम्भोजषण्डम् Śi. 11. 64.<BR>—2 A red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

