कुमुदः|कुमुद|कुमुदं
कुमुदः, -दम् + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of the elephant supposed to guard the south.<BR>—3 Camphor.<BR>—4 A species of monkey.<BR>—5 N. of a Nāga who gave his younger sister कुमुद्वती to Kuśa, son<BR> of Rāma; see R. 16. 79, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

