कूर्चिन् <i>a.</i> Stuffed, puffy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्द्
कूर्द् €1 U. (कूर्दति-ते, कूर्दित)<BR>—1 To leap, jump; फेनायमानाः कूपाश्च कूर्दन्ति वृषभा इव Mb. 6. 3. 34.<BR>—2 To frolic; वव्रश्चुराजुघूर्णुश्च स्येमुश्चुकूर्दिरे तथा Bk. 14. 77, 9, 15. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्दनम्
कूर्दनम्<BR>—1 Leaping.<BR>—2 Playing, sporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्दनी|कूर्द्दनी
कूर्दनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A festival in honour of Kāmadeva, held on the fifteenth day of Chaitra.<BR>—2 The full moon day in Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्पः|कूर्प|कूर्पं|कूर्प्प
कूर्पः<BR>—1 The part between the eye-brows.<BR>—2 A variety of inferior gems; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR>—3 A stone, pebble; कूर्पादिभिर्भ्रमति धीर्भवदायुषां नः Bhāg. 10. 31. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्परः|कूर्पर|कूर्प्पर
कूर्परः<BR>—1 The elbow; Śi. 20. 19.<BR>—2 The knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्पास|कूर्पासः|कूर्प्पास
कूर्पास = कुर्पास q. v. also<BR> कूर्पासकः cf. कूर्पासकं क्षतनखक्षतमुत्क्षिपन्ती Śi. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मः|कूर्म|कूर्म्म|कूर्म्मः
कूर्मः [कौ जले ऊर्मिर्वेगोऽस्य पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>—1 A tortoise; गूहेत्कूर्म इवाङ्गानि रक्षेद्विवरमात्मनः Ms. 7. 105;<BR> Bg. 2. 58; कूर्मः पादोऽत्र यष्टिर्भुजगपतिरसौ भाजनं भूतधात्री Udb.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu in his second or Kūrma incarnation.<BR>—3 One of the outer winds of the body.<BR>—4 A particular gesticulation with the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मी
कूर्मः + .{@-र्मी@} A female tortoise.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कूर्मावतारः, कूर्मासनम्, कूर्मद्वादशी, कूर्मपुराणम्, कूर्मपृष्ठम्, कूर्मपृष्ठकम्, कूर्मराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मावतारः|कूर्मावतार
कूर्मः + -अवतारः the Kūrma incarnation of Viṣṇu; cf. Gīt. 1:− क्षितिरतिविपुलतरे<BR> तव तिष्ठति पृष्ठे धरणिधरणकिणचक्रगरिष्ठे । केशवधृत-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">Page0594-1</a>]<BR> -कच्छरूप जय जगदीश हरे ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0593-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मासनम्
कूर्मः + -आसनम् a particular posture in sitting (practised by ascetics).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मद्वादशी
कूर्मः + -द्वादशी the twelvth day in the light (or dark ?) half of पौष month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मपुराणम्
कूर्मः + -पुराणम् one of the eighteen Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मपृष्ठम्
कूर्मः + -पृष्ठम्, -पृष्ठकम्<BR>—1 the back or shell of a tortoise.<BR>—2 a lid or cover of a dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मपृष्ठकम्
कूर्मः + -पृष्ठम्, -पृष्ठकम्<BR>—1 the back or shell of a tortoise.<BR>—2 a lid or cover of a dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मराजः|कूर्मराज|कूर्म्मराज|कूर्म्मराजः
कूर्मः + -राजः Viṣṇu in the shape of tortoise in his second incarnation;<BR> पृथ्वि स्थिरा भव भुजङ्गम धारयैनाम् । त्वं कूर्मराज तदिदं द्वितयं<BR> दधीथाः ॥ Mahān.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मक
कूर्मक <i>a.</i> (A pearl) shaped like a tortoise; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मिका
कूर्मिका A kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल्
कूल् €1 P. (कूलति, कूलित)<BR>—1 To cover, hide, screen, protect.<BR>—2 To enclose.<BR>—3 To keep off, obstruct, prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलम्
कूलम्<BR>—1 A shore, bank; राधामाधवयोर्जयन्ति यमुनाकूले रहःकेलयः Gīt. 1;<BR> नदीवोभयकूलभाक् R. 12. 35, 68; चुकूज कूले कलहंसमण्डली<BR> N. यथा महामत्स्य उभे कूले अनुसंचरति Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 18.<BR>—2 A slope, declivity.<BR>—3 Skirt, edge, border, proximity; आस्तीर्य दर्भान्प्राक्कूलान् Bhāg. 8. 24. 40;<BR> कुलायकूलेषु विलुट्य तेषु ते N. 1. 141.<BR>—4 A pond.<BR>—5 The rear of an army.<BR>—6 A heap, mound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कूलचर, कूलतण्डुलः, कूलभूः, कूलहण्डकः, कूलहुण्डकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलचर
कूलम् + -चर <i>a.</i> frequenting or grazing on the banks of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलतण्डुलः|कूलतण्डुल
कूलम् + -तण्डुलः Breakers, surges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलभूः
कूलम् + -भूः <i>f.</i> the land on a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलहण्डकः|कूलहण्डक|कूलहंडक
कूलम् + -हण्डकः, -हुण्डकः an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलहुण्डकः|कूलहुण्डक|कूलहुंडक
कूलम् + -हण्डकः, -हुण्डकः an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलकः|कूलक|कूलकं
कूलकः, -कम्<BR>—1 Bank, shore.<BR>—2 A heap, mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलकम्
कूलकः, -कम्<BR>—1 Bank, shore.<BR>—2 A heap, mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलकः|कूलक|कूलकं
कूलकः, -कम् + .{@-कः@} An ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलवती
कूलवती A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिका
कूलिका <i>f.</i> The lower part of the lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिन्
कूलिन् <i>a.</i> Furnished with banks or shores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलंकष|कूलङ्कष|कूलंकषः|कूलङ्कषः
कूलंकष <i>a.</i> Tearing away or undermining the bank; कूलंकषेव<BR> सिंधुः प्रसन्नमम्भस्तटतरुं च Ś. 5. 21; Māl. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलंकषः|कूलङ्कष|कूलंकष|कूलङ्कषः
कूलंकष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 The current or stream of a river.<BR>—2 The ocean, sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलंकषा
कूलंकष + .{@-षा@} A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलंधय
कूलंधय <i>a.</i> Kissing, <i>i. e.</i> bordering on the bank of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्रुज
कूलमुद्रुज <i>a.</i> Breaking down banks, (as rivers, elephants &c.);<BR> सरितां कूलमुद्रुजाः R. 4. 22; आसादितौ कथं ब्रूतं न गजैः कूलमुद्रुजैः<BR> Bk. 6. 95; ऋषभं कूलमुद्रुजम् Mbh. on P. I. 4. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्वह
कूलमुद्वह <i>a.</i> Tearing up or carrying away the bank; उत्तीर्णौ<BR> वा कथं भीमाः सरितः कूलमुद्वहाः Bk. 6. 95; ऋषभं कूलमुद्वहम्<BR> Mbh. on P. I. 4. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवर|कूवरः
कूवर = कूबर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवारः|कूवार
कूवारः The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डः|कूष्माण्ड|कूष्मांड|कूष्मांडः
कूष्माण्डः<BR>—1 A kind of pumpkin gourd.<BR>—2 A kind of spell or magical formula; cf. Vāj. 20. 14-16.<BR>—3 A kind of spirit, or imp; Bhāg. 2. 6. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डी
कूष्माण्डः + .{@-डी@} N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहना
कूहना (= कुहना q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहा
कूहा A fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ I. €5 U. (कृणोति-कृणुते) To hurt, injure, kill. ━II. €8 U.<BR> (करोति-कुरुते, चकार-चक्रे, अकार्षीत्-अकृत; कर्तुम्, करिष्यति-ते कृत)<BR>—1 To do (in general); तात किं करवाण्यहम्<BR>—2 To make; गणिकामवरोधमकरोत् Dk.; नृपेण चक्रे युवराजशब्दभाक्<BR> R. 3. 35; युवराजः कृतः &c.<BR>—3 To manufacture, shape, prepare; कुम्भकारो घटं करोति; कटं करोति &c.<BR>—4 To build, create; गृहं कुरु; सभां कुरु मदर्थे भोः.<BR>—5 To produce, cause, engender; रतिमुभयप्रार्थना कुरुते Ś. 2. 1.<BR>—6 To form, arrange; अञ्जलिं करोति; कपोतहस्तकं कृत्वा.<BR>—7 To write, compose; चकार सुमनोहरं शास्त्रम् Pt. 1.<BR>—8 To perform, be engaged in; पूजां करोति.<BR>—9 To tell, narrate; इति बहुविधाः कथाः कुर्वन् &c.<BR>—10 To carry out, execute, obey; एवं क्रियते युष्मदादेशः Māl. 1;<BR> or करिष्यामि वचस्तव or शासनं मे कुरुष्व &c.<BR>—11 To bring about, accomplish, effect; सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति<BR> पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR>—12 To throw or let out, discharge, emit; मूत्रं कृ to discharge urine,<BR> make water; so पुरीषं कृ to void excrement.<BR>—13 To assume, put on, take; स्त्रीरूपं कृत्वा; नानारूपाणि कुर्वाणः Y. 3. 162.<BR>—14 To send forth, utter; मानुषीं गिरं कृत्वा, कलरवं कृत्वा &c.<BR>—15 To place or put on (with loc.); कण्ठे हारमकरोत् K. 212; पाणिमुरसि कृत्वा &c.<BR>—16 To entrust (with some duty), appoint; अध्यक्षान् विविधान्कुर्यात्तत्र<BR> तत्र विपश्चितः Ms. 7. 81.<BR>—17 To cook (as food) as in कृतान्नम्.<BR>—18 To think, regard, consider; दृष्टिस्तृणीकृतजगत्त्रयसत्त्वसारा U. 6. 19.<BR>—19 To take (as in the hand); कुरु करे गुरुमेकमयोघनं N. 4. 59.<BR>—20 To make a sound, as in खात्कृत्य, फूत्कृत्य भुङ्क्ते; so वषट्कृ, स्वाहाकृ &c.<BR>—21 To pass, spend (time); वर्षाणि दश चक्रुः spent; क्षणं कुरु wait a moment.<BR>—22 To direct towards, turn the attention to, resolve on; (with loc. or<BR> dat.); नाधर्मे कुरुते मनः Ms. 12. 118;<BR> नगरगमनाय मतिं न करोति Ś. 2.<BR>—23 To do a thing for another (either for his advantage or injury); प्राप्ताग्निनिर्वापणगर्वमम्बु<BR> रत्नाङ्कुरज्योतिषि किं करोति Vikr. 1. 18, 18;<BR> यदनेन कृतं मयि, असौ किं मे करिष्यति &c.<BR>—24 To use, employ, make use of; किं तया क्रियते धेन्वा Pt. 1.<BR>—25 To divide, break into parts (with adverbs ending in धा); द्विधा<BR> कृ to divide into two parts; शतधा कृ, सहस्रधा कृ &c.<BR>—26 To cause to become subject to, reduce completely to (a particular<BR> condition, with adverbs ending in सात्); आत्मसात् कृ to subject or<BR> appropriate to oneself; दुरितैरपि कर्तुमात्मसात्प्रयतन्ते नृपसूनवो<BR> हि यत् R. 8. 2; भस्मसात् कृ to reduce to ashes.<BR>—27 To appropriate, secure for oneself.<BR>—28 To help, give aid.<BR>—29 To make liable.<BR>—30 To violate or outrage (as a girl).<BR>—31 To begin.<BR>—32 To order.<BR>—33 To free from.<BR>—34 To proceed with, put in practice.<BR>—35 To worship, sacrifice.<BR>—36 To make like, consider equal to, cf. तृणीकृ (said to be Ātm.<BR> only in the last 10 senses).<BR>—37 To take up, gather; आदाने करोतिशब्दः Ms. 4. 2. 6; यथा काष्ठानि<BR> करोति गोमयानि करोति इति आदाने करोतिशब्दो भवति एवमिहापि द्रष्टव्यम्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 6. This root is often used with nouns, adjectives, and<BR> indeclinables to form<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">Page0595-1</a>]<BR> verbs from them, somewhat like the English affixes ‘en’ or ‘(i) fy’, in<BR> the sense of ‘making a person or thing to be what it previously is not’;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> कृष्णीकृ to make that which is not already black, black,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> blacken; so श्वेतीकृ to whiten; घनीकृ to solidify; विरलीकृ<BR> to rarefy &c. &c. Sometimes these formations take place in other senses<BR> also; <i>e. g.</i> क्रोडीकृ ‘to clasp to the bosom’, embrace; भस्मीकृ<BR> to reduce to ashes; प्रवणीकृ to incline, bend; तृणीकृ to value<BR> as little as straw; मन्दीकृ to slacken, make slow; so शूलीकृ to<BR> roast on the end of pointed lances; सुखीकृ to please; समयाकृ<BR> to spend time &c. <i>N. B.</i> This root by itself admits of either Pada;<BR> but it is Ātm. generally with prepositions in the following senses:− (1)<BR> doing injury to; (2) censure, blame; (3) serving; (4) outraging, acting<BR> violently or rashly; (5) preparing, changing the condition of, turning<BR> into; (6) reciting; (7) employing, using; see P. I. 3. 32 and गन्धनावक्षेपणसेवनसाहसिक्यप्रतियत्नप्रकथनोपयोगेषु<BR> कृञः “Studentsʼ Guide to Sanskrit Composition” § 338. <i>Note</i>.<BR> The root कृ is of the most frequent application in Sanskrit literature,<BR> and its senses are variously modified, or almost infinitely extended,<BR> according to the noun with which the root is connected; <i>e. g.</i> पदं<BR> कृ to set foot (fig. also); आश्रमे पदं करिष्यसि Ś. 4. 19; क्रमेण<BR> कृतं मम वपुषि नवयौवनेन पदम् K. 141; मनसा कृ to think<BR> of, meditate; मनसि कृ to think; दृष्ट्वा मनस्येवमकरोत् K. 136;<BR> or to resolve or determine; सख्यम्, मैत्रीं कृ to form friendship with;<BR> अस्त्राणि कृ to practise the use of weapons; दण्डं कृ to inflict<BR> punishment; हृदये कृ to pay heed to; कालं कृ to die; मतिं-बुद्धिं<BR> कृ to think of, intend, mean; उदकं कृ to offer libations of water<BR> to manes; चिरं कृ to delay; दर्दुरं कृ to play on the lute;<BR> नखानि कृ to clean the nails; कन्यां कृ to outrage or violate a<BR> maiden; विना कृ to separate from, to be abandoned by, as in मदनेन<BR> विनाकृता रतिः Ku. 4. 21; मध्ये कृ to place in the middle, to have<BR> reference to; मध्येकृत्य स्थितं क्रथकौशिकान् M. 5. 2; वशे कृ<BR> to win over, place in subjection, subdue; चमत्कृ to cause surprise;<BR> make an exhibition or a show; सत्कृ to honour, treat with respect;<BR> तिर्यक्कृ to place aside. ━<i>Caus.</i> (कारयति-ते) To cause<BR> to do, perform, make, execute &c.; आज्ञां कारय रक्षोभिः Bk. 8. 84;<BR> भृत्यं भृत्येन वा कटं कारयति Sk. ━<i>Desid.</i> (चिकीर्षतिते)<BR> To wish to do &c.; Śi. 14. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0594-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् <i>a.</i> [कृ-क्विप्] (Generally at the end of comp.) Accomplisher,<BR> doer, maker, performer, manufacturer, composer &c.; पाप˚, पुण्य˚, प्रतिमा˚ &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A class of affixes used to form derivatives (nouns, adjectives &c.) from roots.<BR>—2 A word so formed; कृद्ग्रहणे गतिकारकपूर्वस्यापि ग्रहणम् Pari. Śekh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृदन्त, कृल्लोपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदन्त
कृत् + -अन्त a word ending with a kṛt affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृल्लोपः|कृल्लोप
कृत् + -लोपः the rejection of kṛt affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत <i>p. p.</i> [कृ-क्त]<BR>—1 Done, performed, made, effected accomplished, manufactured &c.; (<i>p. p.</i><BR> of कृ €8 U. q. v.) ते करान् संप्रयच्छन्तु सुवर्णं च कृताकृतम्<BR> Mb. 3. 255. 17;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">Page0595-2</a>]<BR> दिव्याः प्रसन्ना विविधाः सुराः कृतसुरा अपि Rām. 5. 11. 22; natural<BR> and manufactured wines.<BR>—2 Wounded, hurt; सिद्धयेत ते कृतमनोभवधर्षितायाः Bhāg. 3. 23. 11.<BR>—3 Acquired, bought (a kind of son); Mb. 13. 49. 4.<BR>—4 Cultivated; अकृतं च कृतात्क्षेत्राद् गौरजाविकमेव च Ms. 10. 114.<BR>—5 Appointed (as a duty); सोऽपि यत्नेन संरक्ष्यो धर्मो राजकृतश्च<BR> यः Y. 2. 186.<BR>—6 Relating to, referring to; पतनीयकृते क्षेपे Y. 2. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतम्
कृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Work, deed, action; कृतं न वेत्ति Pt. 1. 424; ungrateful; Ms. 7. 197.<BR>—2 Service, benefit.<BR>—3 Consequence, result.<BR>—4 Aim, object.<BR>—5 N. of that side of a die which is marked with four points; this is<BR> lucky; cf. Vāj. 30. 18.<BR>—6 N. of the first of the four Yugas of the world extending over 1728000<BR> years of men (see Ms. 1. 69 and Kull. thereon).<BR>—7 The number ‘4’.<BR>—8 A stake at a game.<BR>—9 Prize or booty gained in a battle.<BR>—10 An offering.<BR>—11 Magic sorcery.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृताकृत, कृताङ्क, कृताञ्जलि, कृतानुकर, कृतानुसारः, कृतान्त, कृतान्नम्, कृतापराध, कृताभय, कृताभिषेक, कृताभ्यास, कृतायः, कृतार्थ, कृतावधान, कृतावधि, कृतावमर्ष, कृतावस्थ, कृतास्त्र, कृताहक, कृतागम, कृतागस्, कृतात्मन्, कृताभरण, कृतायास, कृतालय, कृतावास, कृतास्पद, कृताहार, कृताह्वान, कृतोत्साह, कृतोदक, कृतोद्वाह, कृतोपकार, कृतोपभोग, कृतकर, कृतकारिन्, कृतकर्मन्, कृतकाम, कृतकार्य, कृतकाल, कृतकृत्य, कृतक्रिय, कृतक्रयः, कृतक्रियः, कृतक्षण, कृतघ्न, कृतचूडः, कृतजन्मन्, कृतज्ञ, कृततीर्थ, कृतदार, कृतदासः, कृतदूषणम्, कृतदूषा, कृतधी, कृतनामधेय, कृतनिर्णेजनः, कृतनिश्चय, कृतपुङ्ख, कृतपूर्व, कृतप्रतिकृतम्, कृतप्रतिज्ञ, कृतप्रयोजन, कृतफल, कृतबुद्धि, कृतब्रह्मन्, कृतमङ्गल, कृतमति, कृतमन्यु, कृतमालः, कृतमालकः, कृतमुख, कृतयुगम्, कृतरूप, कृतलक्षण, कृतवर्मन्, कृतवापः, कृतविद्, कृतविद्य, कृतवीर्य, कृतवेतन, कृतवेदिन्, कृतवेश, कृतव्यावृत्ति, कृतशिल्प, कृतशोभ, कृतशौच, कृतश्मश्रुः, कृतश्रमः, कृतपरिश्रमः, कृतसंकल्प, कृतसंकेत, कृतसंज्ञ, कृतसंनाह, कृतसंस्कार, कृतसापत्निका, कृतसापत्नी, कृतसापत्नीका, कृतसापत्नका, कृतसपत्निका, कृतहस्त, कृतहस्तक, कृतहस्तता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताकृत|कृताकृतः
कृत + -अकृत <i>a.</i> done and not done; <i>i. e.</i> done in part but not<BR> completed; कृताकृतस्यैव च काञ्चनस्य Bu. C. 2. 2; that which is<BR> done and that which is not done (Dvandva Comp.) मा त्वा ताप्तां कृताकृते<BR> Mbh. on P. II. 2. 29; कृताकृतप्रसङ्गि नित्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताकृतः|कृताकृत
कृत + -अकृत + ({@-तः@}) the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताङ्क|कृतांक|कृताङ्कः
कृत + -अङ्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 marked, branded; कट्यां कृताङ्को निर्वास्यः Ms. 8. 281.<BR>—2 numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताङ्कः|कृताङ्क|कृतांक
कृत + -अङ्क + .({@-ङ्कः@}) that side of a die which is marked with four points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलि|कृतांजलि|कृताञ्जलिः
कृत + -अञ्जलि <i>a.</i> folding the hands in supplication; प्रणम्य शिरसा<BR> देवं कृताञ्जलिरभाषत Bg. 11. 14, 35; Ms. 4. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुकर
कृत + -अनुकर <i>a.</i> following anotherʼs example, subservient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुसारः|कृतानुसार
कृत + -अनुसारः custom, usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृत + -अन्त <i>a.</i> bringing to an end, terminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्तः|कृतान्त|कृतांत
कृत + -अन्त + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 Yama, the god of death; कृतान्त आसीत्समरो देवानां सह दानवैः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 6. 13; द्वितीयं कृतान्तमिवाटन्तं व्याधमपश्यत् H. 1.<BR>—2 fate, destiny; कृतान्त एव सौमित्रे द्रष्टव्यो मत्प्रवासने Rām. 2. 22. 15;<BR> क्रूरस्तस्मिन्नपि न सहते संगमं नौ कृतान्तः Me. 107.<BR>—3 a demonstrated conclusion, dogma, a proved doctrine; दैवं पुरुषकारश्च<BR> कृतान्तेनोपपद्यते Mb. 12. 153. 50; यथा लौकिकेषु वैदिकेषु च कृतान्तेषु<BR> Mbh. on P. I. 1. 1, 56; साङ्ख्ये कृतान्ते प्रोक्तानि Bg. 18. 13.<BR>—4 a sinful or inauspicious action.<BR>—5 an epithet of Saturn.<BR>—6 Saturday.<BR>—7 the inevitable result of former actions.<BR>—8 the second lunar mansion.<BR>—9 the number ‘two’. ˚कुशल an astrologer; आधिराज्येऽभिषेको मे ब्राह्मणैः<BR> पतिना सह । कृतान्तकुशलैरुक्तं तत्सर्वं वितथीकृतम् Rām. 6. 48. 14.<BR> ˚जनकः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्नम्
कृत + -अन्नम्<BR>—1 cooked food; कृतान्नमुदकं स्त्रियः Ms. 9. 219, 11. 3.<BR>—2 digested food.<BR>—3 excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापराध
कृत + -अपराध <i>a.</i> guilty, offender, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभय
कृत + -अभय <i>a.</i> saved from fear or danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभिषेक|कृताभिषेकः
कृत + -अभिषेक <i>a.</i> crowned, inaugurated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभिषेकः|कृताभिषेक
कृत + -अभिषेक + ({@-कः@}) a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभ्यास
कृत + -अभ्यास <i>a.</i> practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतायः|कृताय
कृत + -अयः the die called कृत marked with four points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थ|कृतार्थः
कृत + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having gained oneʼs object, successful; एकः कृतार्थो भवते वीतशोकः<BR> Śvet. Up. 2. 14.<BR>—2 satisfied; happy, contented; वयं कृतार्था इत्यभिमन्यन्ति बालाः<BR> Muṇḍ. 1. 2. 9; कृतः कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29; R. 8. 3;<BR> Ki. 4. 9; Ś. 2. 1; Pt. 1. 194.<BR>—3 clever.<BR>—4 that which has served its purpose (and hence incapable of yielding<BR> any further sense or serving any other purpose); पुरुषे यागं श्रावयित्वा<BR> कृतार्थः शब्द एकस्य द्वयोर्बहूनां वा यागं न वारयति । ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 3.<BR> सकृत् कृत्वा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">Page0596-1</a>]<BR> कृतार्थः शब्दः न नियमः पौनःपुन्ये । ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 27; सा<BR> चाकाङ्क्षा एकेनापि कृतार्था भवतीत्युक्तम् । ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 13. (कृतार्थीकृ<BR>—1 to render fruitful or successful; कृतार्थीकृत्य तं विप्रम् Ks. 74. 125.<BR>—2 to make good; कान्तं प्रत्युपचारतश्चतुरया कोपः कृतार्थीकृतः<BR> Amaru. 15; so कृतार्थयति to make fruitful; Māl. 3. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0595-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधान
कृत + -अवधान <i>a.</i> careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधि
कृत + -अवधि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fixed, appointed.<BR>—2 bounded, limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावमर्ष
कृत + -अवमर्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 effacing from recollection.<BR>—2 intolerant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावस्थ
कृत + -अवस्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 summoned, caused to be present; Ms. 8. 60.<BR>—2 fixed, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्त्र
कृत + -अस्त्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 armed.<BR>—2 trained in the science of arms or missiles; पित्रा संवर्धितो नित्यं<BR> कृतास्त्रः सांपरायिकः R. 17. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताहक
कृत + -अहक <i>a.</i> having performed the daily ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागम
कृत + -आगम <i>a.</i> advanced, proficient, skilled. ━(<i>m.</i>) the Supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागस्
कृत + -आगस् <i>a.</i> guilty, offending, criminal, sinful; अध्ने प्र शिरो<BR> जहि ब्रह्मजस्य कृतागसः Av. 12. 5. 60; कृतागाः कौटिल्यो भुजग इव<BR> निर्याय नगरात् Mu. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतात्मन्
कृत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having control over oneself, self-possessed, of a self-governed spirit;<BR> कृतात्मा ब्रह्मलोकमभिसंभवामि Ch. Up. 8. 13. 1; कृतात्मानो वीतरागाः<BR> प्रशान्ताः Muṇḍ. 3. 2. 5; Rām. 5. 61. 6; ऐहिष्ट तं कारयितुं<BR> कृतात्मा Bk. 1. 11.<BR>—2 purified in mind; magnanimous; तमरिघ्रं कृतात्मानं क्षिप्रं द्रक्ष्यसि<BR> राघवम् Rām. 5. 39. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभरण
कृत + -आभरण <i>a.</i> adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतायास
कृत + -आयास <i>a.</i> labouring, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतालय|कृतालयः
कृत + -आलय <i>a.</i> one who has taken up his abode in any place; यत्र<BR> ते दयिता भार्या तनयाश्च कृतालयाः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतालयः|कृतालय
कृत + -आलय + ({@-यः@}) a frog; dog ? MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावास
कृत + -आवास a lodging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्पद
कृत + -आस्पद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 governed; ruled.<BR>—2 supporting, resting on.<BR>—3 residing in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताहार
कृत + -आहार <i>a.</i> having taken oneʼs meals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताह्वान
कृत + -आह्वान <i>a.</i> challenged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोत्साह
कृत + -उत्साह <i>a.</i> diligent, making effort, striving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोदक
कृत + -उदक <i>a.</i> one who has performed his ablutions; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोद्वाह
कृत + -उद्वाह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 married.<BR>—2 practising penance by standing with up-lifted hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपकार
कृत + -उपकार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 favoured, befriended, assisted; अज्ञातभर्तृव्यसना मुहूर्तं कृतोपकारेव<BR> रतिर्बभूव Ku. 3. 73.<BR>—2 friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपभोग
कृत + -उपभोग <i>a.</i> used, enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर
कृत + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> Enjoining what is already known or done;<BR> कृतकरो हि विधिरनर्थकः स्यात् ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 58; कृतकरं<BR> शास्त्रमनर्थकं स्यात् ŚB. on MS. 10. 7. 25; कृतकारि खलु शास्त्रं<BR> पर्जन्यवत् Mbh. on P. I. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकारिन्
कृत + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> Enjoining what is already known or done;<BR> कृतकरो हि विधिरनर्थकः स्यात् ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 58; कृतकरं<BR> शास्त्रमनर्थकं स्यात् ŚB. on MS. 10. 7. 25; कृतकारि खलु शास्त्रं<BR> पर्जन्यवत् Mbh. on P. I. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्मन्|कृतकर्म्मन्
कृत + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has done his work; R. 9. 3.<BR>—2 skilful, clever. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the Supreme spirit.<BR>—2 a <i>Saṃnyāsin</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाम
कृत + -काम <i>a.</i> one whose desires are fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकार्य|कृतकार्य्य
कृत + -कार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has done his work or obtained his object.<BR>—2 having no need of anotherʼs aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाल|कृतकालः
कृत + -काल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fixed or settled as to time.<BR>—2 who has waited a certain time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकालः|कृतकाल
कृत + -काल + .({@-लः@}) appointed time; कृतशिल्पोऽपि निवसेत्कृतकालं गुरोर्गृहे Y. 2. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्य|कृतकृत्यः
कृत + -कृत्य, -क्रिय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 who has accomplished his object; Bg. 15. 20.<BR>—2 satisfied, contented; Śānti. 3. 19; Māl. 4. 3.<BR>—3 clever.<BR>—4 having done his duty; कृतकृत्यो विधिर्मन्ये न वर्धयति तस्य ताम् Śi. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रिय|कृतक्रियः
कृत + -कृत्य, -क्रिय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 who has accomplished his object; Bg. 15. 20.<BR>—2 satisfied, contented; Śānti. 3. 19; Māl. 4. 3.<BR>—3 clever.<BR>—4 having done his duty; कृतकृत्यो विधिर्मन्ये न वर्धयति तस्य ताम् Śi. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रयः|कृतक्रय
कृत + -क्रयः a purchaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रियः|कृतक्रिय
कृत + -क्रियः<BR>—1 one who has accomplished any act.<BR>—2 one who has fulfilled his duty. —3 one who has performed a religious<BR> ceremony; Ms. 5. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्षण
कृत + -क्षण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 waiting impatiently for the exact moment; कृतक्षणाहं भद्रं ते<BR> गमनं प्रति राघव Rām. 2. 29. 15; वयं सर्वे सोत्सुकाः कृतक्षणास्तिष्ठामः Pt. 1.<BR>—2 one who has got<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">Page0596-2</a>]<BR> an opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्न|कृतघ्नः
कृत + -घ्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ungrateful; Ms. 4. 214, 8. 89.<BR>—2 defeating all previous measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतचूडः|कृतचूड
कृत + -चूडः a boy on whom the ceremony of tonsure has been performed;<BR> Ms. 5. 58, 67; नृणामकृतचूडानां विशुद्धिर्नौशिकी स्मृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतजन्मन्
कृत + -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> planted; Ku. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञ|कृतज्ञः
कृत + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 grateful; Ms. 7. 209, 210; Y. 1. 308.<BR>—2 correct in conduct; कृतज्ञतामस्य वदन्ति सम्पदः Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञः|कृतज्ञ
कृत + -ज्ञ + ({@-ज्ञः@})<BR>—1 a dog.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृततीर्थ
कृत + -तीर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has visited or frequented holy places.<BR>—2 one who studies with a professional teacher.<BR>—3 fertile in means or expedients.<BR>—4 a guide.<BR>—5 rendered accessible or easy; Ki. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदार
कृत + -दार <i>a.</i> married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदासः|कृतदास
कृत + -दासः a servant hired for a stated period, a hired servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदूषणम्
कृत + -दूषणम् spoiling what is done; उद्धतायाः पुनरुद्धनने न हि<BR> किञ्चित्कार्यमस्ति । केवलं कृतदूषणं भवेत् । ŚB. on MS. 12. 2. 16.<BR> (see कृतदूषा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदूषा
कृत + -दूषा <i>f.</i> a blemish or vitiating factor for what is done; अकर्म<BR> वा कृतदूषा स्यात् MS. 12. 1. 10.(कृतायाः दूषणम् ŚB. on MS.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतधी
कृत + -धी <i>a.</i><BR>—1 prudent, considerate.<BR>—2 learned, educated, wise; पुत्रेभ्यः कृतवेदिनां कृतधियां येषां न<BR> भिन्ना वयम् Mu. 5. 20; Bg. 2. 54; Śi. 2. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनामधेय
कृत + -नामधेय <i>a.</i> named, called as; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिर्णेजनः|कृतनिर्णेजन
कृत + -निर्णेजनः a penitent. ━<i>a.</i> one who has performed penance;<BR> कृतनिर्णेजनांश्चैव न जुगुप्सेत कर्हिचित् Ms. 11. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिश्चय
कृत + -निश्चय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 resolute, resolved; युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः Bg. 2. 37.<BR>—2 confident, sure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपुङ्ख|कृतपुंख|कृतपुङ्खः
कृत + -पुङ्ख <i>a.</i> skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्व|कृतपूर्व्व
कृत + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> done formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रतिकृतम्
कृत + -प्रतिकृतम् assault and counter-assault, attack and resistance; R. 12. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रतिज्ञ
कृत + -प्रतिज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has made an agreement or engagement.<BR>—2 one who has fulfilled his promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रयोजन
कृत + -प्रयोजन <i>a.</i> one who has attained his object; Ks. 13. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतफल|कृतफलं
कृत + -फल <i>a.</i> successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतफलम्
कृत + -फल + ({@-लम्@}) result, consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबुद्धि
कृत + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 learned, educated, wise; विद्वत्सु कृतबुद्धयः (श्रेष्ठाः) Ms. 1. 97, 7. 30.<BR>—2 a man of resolute character.<BR>—3 informed of oneʼs duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतब्रह्मन्
कृत + -ब्रह्मन् <i>a.</i> Ved. one who has performed his devotions; कृतब्रह्मा<BR> शूशुवद् रातहव्य इत् Rv. 2. 25. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमङ्गल
कृत + -मङ्गल <i>a.</i> blessed, consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमति
कृत + -मति <i>a.</i> firm, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमन्यु
कृत + -मन्यु <i>a.</i> indignant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमालः|कृतमाल
कृत + -मालः, -मालकः<BR>—1 a kind of cassia.<BR>—2 the spotted antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमालकः|कृतमालक
कृत + -मालः, -मालकः<BR>—1 a kind of cassia.<BR>—2 the spotted antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमुख|कृतमुखः
कृत + -मुख <i>a.</i> learned, clever, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतयुगम्
कृत + -युगम् the first (golden) of the four ages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरूप
कृत + -रूप one who knows the customary rites (कृतकल्प); Rām. 2. 100. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतलक्षण|कृतलक्षणः
कृत + -लक्षण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 stamped, marked.<BR>—2 branded; ज्ञातिसम्बन्धिभिस्त्वेतास्त्यक्तव्याः कृतलक्षणाः Ms. 9. 239.<BR>—3 excellent, amiable.<BR>—4 defined, discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवर्मन्|कृतवर्म्मन्
कृत + -वर्मन् <i>m.</i> N. of a warrior on the side of the Kauravas who<BR> with Kṛpa and Aśvatthāman survived the general havoc of the great<BR> Bhārata war. He was afterwards slain by Sātyaki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवापः|कृतवाप
कृत + -वापः a penitent who has shaven his head and chin; Ms. 11. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविद्
कृत + -विद् <i>a.</i> grateful; तस्यापवर्ग्यशरणं तव पादमूलं विस्मर्यते<BR> कृतविदा कथमार्तबन्धो Bhāg. 4. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविद्य
कृत + -विद्य <i>a.</i> learned, educated; शूरोऽसि कृतविद्योऽसि Pt. 4. 43;<BR> सुवर्णपुष्पितां पृथ्वीं विचिन्वन्ति त्रयो जनाः । शूरश्च कृतविद्यश्च<BR> यश्च जानाति सेवितुम् ॥ Pt. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवीर्य|कृतवीर्यः|कृतवीर्य्य
कृत + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> being strong or powerful; Av. 17. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवीर्यः|कृतवीर्य|कृतवीर्य्य
कृत + -वीर्य + ({@-र्यः@})<BR> N. of the father of Sahasrārjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेतन|कृतवेतनः
कृत + -वेतन <i>a.</i> hired, paid (as a servant); प्रमादमृतनष्टांश्च<BR> प्रदाप्यः कृतवेतनः Y. 2. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेदिन्
कृत + -वेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 grateful; न तथा कृतवेदिनां करिष्यन्प्रियतामेति यथा कृता-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">Page0597-1</a>]<BR> -वदानः Ki. 13. 32; see कृतज्ञ.<BR>—2 observant of propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0596-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेश
कृत + -वेश <i>a.</i> attired, decorated; गतवति कृतवेशे केशवे कुञ्जशय्याम् Gīt. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतव्यावृत्ति
कृत + -व्यावृत्ति <i>a.</i> dislodged or dismissed from office, set aside; Ku. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशिल्प
कृत + -शिल्प <i>a.</i> skilled in art or trade; कृतशिल्पोऽपि निवसेत्कृतकालं<BR> गुरोर्गृहे Y. 2. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशोभ
कृत + -शोभ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 splendid.<BR>—2 beautiful.<BR>—3 handy, dexterous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशौच
कृत + -शौच <i>a.</i> purified; पुण्डरीकमवाप्नोति कृतशौचो भवेच्च सः Mb. 3. 83. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्मश्रुः
कृत + -श्मश्रुः one who is shaven; न हि कृतश्मश्रुः पुनः श्मश्रूणि<BR> कारयति Mbh. on P. I. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्रमः|कृतश्रम
कृत + -श्रमः, -परिश्रमः one who has studied; कृतपरिश्रमोऽस्मि<BR> ज्योतिःशास्त्रे Mu. 1; I have devoted my time to (spent my labours on) the<BR> science of astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपरिश्रमः
कृत + -श्रमः, -परिश्रमः one who has studied; कृतपरिश्रमोऽस्मि<BR> ज्योतिःशास्त्रे Mu. 1; I have devoted my time to (spent my labours on) the<BR> science of astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंकल्प
कृत + -संकल्प <i>a.</i> resolved, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंकेत|कृतसङ्केत
कृत + -संकेत <i>a.</i> making an appointment; नामसमेतं कृतसंकेतं<BR> वादयते मृदु वेणुम् Gīt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंज्ञ
कृत + -संज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having presence of mind … स्थापयेद् दासान् कृतसंज्ञान् समन्ततः Ms.<BR>—2 restored to consciousness or senses.<BR>—3 aroused.<BR>—4 one to whom sign has been given; Rāj. T. 4. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंनाह
कृत + -संनाह <i>a.</i> clad in armour, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंस्कार
कृत + -संस्कार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has performed all purificatory rites, initiated; वैश्यस्तु<BR> कृतसंस्कारः Ms. 9. 326; R. 10. 78.<BR>—2 Prepared, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्निका
कृत + -सापत्निका, -सापत्नी, -सापत्नीका, -सापत्नका, -सपत्निका a woman<BR> whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife<BR> or a superseded wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्नी
कृत + -सापत्निका, -सापत्नी, -सापत्नीका, -सापत्नका, -सपत्निका a woman<BR> whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife<BR> or a superseded wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्नीका
कृत + -सापत्निका, -सापत्नी, -सापत्नीका, -सापत्नका, -सपत्निका a woman<BR> whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife<BR> or a superseded wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्नका
कृत + -सापत्निका, -सापत्नी, -सापत्नीका, -सापत्नका, -सपत्निका a woman<BR> whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife<BR> or a superseded wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसपत्निका
कृत + -सापत्निका, -सापत्नी, -सापत्नीका, -सापत्नका, -सपत्निका a woman<BR> whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife<BR> or a superseded wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्त|कृतहस्तः
कृत + -हस्त, -हस्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dexterous, clever, skilful, handy.<BR>—2 skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्तक
कृत + -हस्त, -हस्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dexterous, clever, skilful, handy.<BR>—2 skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्तता
कृत + -हस्तता<BR>—1 skill, dexterity; … संनिपाते । सुमहति कृतहस्ताः सैनिकास्तं ररक्षुः ॥<BR> Śiva B. 13. 30. 47.<BR>—2 skill in archery or generally in handling arms; कौरव्ये कृतहस्तता<BR> पुनरियं देवे यथा सीरिणि Ve. 6. 13; Mv. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक <i>a.</i> [कृत-कन्]<BR>—1 Done, made, prepared; (opp. नैसर्गिकृ); यद्यत्कृतकं तत्तदनित्यम् Nyāya S..<BR>—2 Artificial, done or prepared artificially; अकृतकविधि सर्वाङ्गीणमाकल्पजातम् R. 18. 52.<BR>—3 Feigned, pretended, false, sham, assumed; कृतककलहं कृत्वा Mu. 3; Ki. 8. 46.<BR>—4 Adopted (as a son &c.); oft. at the end of comp. also; यस्योपान्ते<BR> कृतकतनयः कान्तया वधिंतो मे (बालमन्दारवृक्षः) Me. 77; सोऽयं<BR> न पुत्रकृतकः पदवीं मृगस्ते (जहाति) Ś. 4. 14; U. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकम्
कृतक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A kind of salt (Mar. बिडलोण).<BR>—2 Sulphate of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकम्
कृतक + .{@-कम्@} <i>ind.</i> In a simulated manner; अपयाति सरोषया निरस्ते<BR> कृतकं कामिनि चुक्षुवे मृगाक्ष्या Śi. 9. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतम्
कृतम् <i>ind.</i> Enough, no more of, away; (with instr.); अथवा कृतं<BR> संदेहेन Śi. 1; अथवा गिरा कृतम् R. 11. 41; कृतमाविष्कृतपौरुषैर्भुजैः<BR> Ki. 2. 17; कृतमश्वेन U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवत्|कृतवन्त्
कृतवत् (<i>pres. p.</i>) <i>a.</i> One who has done; कृतवानसि<BR> विप्रियं न मे प्रतिकूलं न च मे त्वया कृतम् Ku. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिः|कृति
कृतिः <i>f.</i> [कृ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Doing, manufacturing, making, performing.<BR>—2 Action, deed.<BR>—3 Creation, literary work, composition; (तौ) स्वकृतिं गापयामास<BR> कविप्रथमपद्धतिम् R. 15. 33, 64, 69; N. 22. 155.<BR>—4 Magic, enchantment.<BR>—5 Injuring, killing; स कृत्या चकितो गत्वा मुनिं वव्रे पुरोहितम् Bm. 1. 27.<BR>—6 The number ‘20’.<BR>—7 An enchantress, a witch.<BR>—8 A knife.<BR>—9 Way-laying; hurting, injuring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">Page0597-2</a>]<BR> (Ved.).<BR>—10 A square number.<BR>—11 (in drama) Confirmation of any obtainment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृतिकरः, कृतिसाध्यत्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिकरः|कृतिकर
कृतिः + -करः<BR>—1 an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—2 one practising magic, a witch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिसाध्यत्वम्
कृतिः + -साध्यत्वम् the state of being accomplished by exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिन्
कृतिन् <i>a.</i> [कृतमनेन, कृत-इनि]<BR>—1 One who has done his work or gained his end, satisfied, contented,<BR> happy, successful; यस्य वीर्येण कृतिनो वयं च भुवनानि च U. 1. 32;<BR> न खल्वनिर्जित्य रघुं कृती भवान् R. 3. 51, 12. 64.<BR>—2 (Hence) Lucky, fortunate, blessed; Ś. 1. 23, 7. 19.<BR>—3 Clever, competent, able, expert, skilful, wise, learned; तं क्षुरप्रशकलीकृतं<BR> कृती R. 11. 29, 19. 14; Ku. 2. 10; Ki. 2. 9; Śi. 2. 25, 30; H. 3. 89; Ve. 4. 12.<BR>—4 Good, virtuous, pure, pious; तावदेव कृतिनामपि स्फुरत्येष निर्मलविवेकदीपकः Bh. 1. 56.<BR>—5 Following, obeying, doing what is enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृते
कृते, -कृतेन <i>ind.</i><BR> (With gen. or in comp.) For, for the sake of,<BR> on account of; अमीषां प्राणानां … कृते Bh. 3. 36. कृते किं नास्माभिर्विगलितविवेकैः …<BR> <i>ibid.</i> काव्यं यशसेऽर्थकृते K. P. 1; Bg. 1. 35; Y. 1. 216; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतेन
कृते, -कृतेन <i>ind.</i><BR> (With gen. or in comp.) For, for the sake of,<BR> on account of; अमीषां प्राणानां … कृते Bh. 3. 36. कृते किं नास्माभिर्विगलितविवेकैः …<BR> <i>ibid.</i> काव्यं यशसेऽर्थकृते K. P. 1; Bg. 1. 35; Y. 1. 216; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु <i>a.</i> [कृ-क्त्नु; Uṇ. 3. 30]<BR>—1 Working well, able to work, powerful.<BR>—2 Clever, skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नुः|कृत्नु
कृत्नु + .{@-त्नुः@} A mechanic, an artist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य <i>a.</i> [कृ-क्यप्; cf. P. III. 1. 120]<BR>—1 What should or ought to be done, right, proper, fit; साधु पर्याप्तमेतावत्कृत्यश्चारित्रसंग्रहः<BR> Rām. 7. 13. 18.<BR>—2 Feasible, practicable.<BR>—3 One who may be seduced from allegiance, treacherous; Rāj. T. 5. 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यम्
कृत्य + .{@-त्यम्@}<BR>—1 What ought to be done, duty, (इतिकृत्य) function; Ms. 2. 237, 7. 67.<BR>—2 Work, business, deed, commission; बन्धुकृत्यम् Me. 116; अन्योन्यकृत्यैः Ś. 7. 34.<BR>—3 Purpose, object, end; कूजद्भिरापादितवंशकृत्यम् R. 2. 12; Ku. 4. 15.<BR>—4 Motive, cause; किमागमनकृत्यं ते देवगन्धर्वसेवित Rām. 7. 21. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यः|कृत्य|कृत्यं
कृत्य + .{@-त्यः@} A class of affixes used to form potential (future) passive<BR> participle; these are तव्य, अनीय, य and also एलिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्या
कृत्य + .{@-त्या@}<BR>—1 Action, deed.<BR>—2 Magic.<BR>—3 A female deity to whom sacrifices are offered for destructive and magical<BR> purposes; परं यत्नमकरोद्यो मे पापकृत्यां शमयेदिति Mb. 1. 31. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृत्याकृत्यरक्षणम्, कृत्यविधिः, कृत्यशेष<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्याकृत्यरक्षणम्
कृत्य + -अकृत्यरक्षणम् protection of parties for or against oneʼs cause; Kau. A. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविधिः|कृत्यविधि
कृत्य + -विधिः <i>m.</i> the rule, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यशेष
कृत्य + -शेष <i>a.</i> One who has not finished his task; व्रजस्त्रियो<BR> दृग्भिरनुप्रवृत्तधियोऽवतस्थुः किल कृत्यशेषाः Bhāg. 3. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यका
कृत्यका A witch, enchantress; Nala. 13. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यवत्|कृत्यवन्त्
कृत्यवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having any business.<BR>—2 Having any request.<BR>—3 Wanting, longing for; यः कृत्यवान्सुवर्णेन सुवर्णं लभते स्म सः<BR> Rām. 7. 92. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकः|कृक
कृकः<BR>—1 The throat.<BR>—2 The navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकणः|कृकण
कृकणः, -रः<BR>—1 A kind of partridge.<BR>—2 A worm.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकरः|कृकर
कृकणः, -रः<BR>—1 A kind of partridge.<BR>—2 A worm.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकरच्छटः
कृकरच्छटः A saw; क्रकचे कृकरच्छटः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलः|कृकल
कृकलः<BR>—1 A kind of partridge; Rām. 7.<BR>—2 One of the five vital airs (that which assists in digestion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0597-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकला
कृकला Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलः|कृकल
कृकलः, कृकलासः, -शः A lizard, chameleon; प्राणं न<BR> विच्छिन्द्यादपि कृकलासस्य Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 14; पत्रोर्णं चोरयित्वा<BR> तु कृकलत्वं निगच्छति Mb. 13. 111. 104; कृकलासं गिरिनिभं वीक्ष्य<BR> विस्मितमानसाः Bhāg. 10. 64. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलासः|कृकलास
कृकलः, कृकलासः, -शः A lizard, chameleon; प्राणं न<BR> विच्छिन्द्यादपि कृकलासस्य Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 14; पत्रोर्णं चोरयित्वा<BR> तु कृकलत्वं निगच्छति Mb. 13. 111. 104; कृकलासं गिरिनिभं वीक्ष्य<BR> विस्मितमानसाः Bhāg. 10. 64. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलाशः|कृकलाश
कृकलः, कृकलासः, -शः A lizard, chameleon; प्राणं न<BR> विच्छिन्द्यादपि कृकलासस्य Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 14; पत्रोर्णं चोरयित्वा<BR> तु कृकलत्वं निगच्छति Mb. 13. 111. 104; कृकलासं गिरिनिभं वीक्ष्य<BR> विस्मितमानसाः Bhāg. 10. 64. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकुः|कृकवाकु
कृकवाकुः<BR>—1 A cock; Rām. 2. 28. 10.<BR>—2 A peacock.<BR>—3 A lizard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृकवाकुध्वजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकुध्वजः|कृकवाकुध्वज
कृकवाकुः + -ध्वजः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटकम्
कृकाटकम्<BR>—1 The neck.<BR>—2 A part of a column.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटिका
कृकाटिका<BR>—1 The raised and straight part of the neck.<BR>—2 The back of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र <i>a.</i> [cf. Uṇ. 2. 21]<BR>—1 Causing trouble, painful; तथात्यजन्निमं देहं कृच्छ्राद् ग्राहाद्विमुत्त्यते Ms. 6. 78.<BR>—2 Bad, miserable, evil.<BR>—3 Wicked, sinful.<BR>—4 Being in a difficult or painful situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रः|कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रः, -च्छ्रम्@}<BR>—1 A difficulty, trouble, hardship, misery, calamity, danger; कृच्छ्रं<BR> महत्तीर्णः R. 14. 6, 13. 77.<BR>—2 Bodily mortification, penance, expiation; Ms. 4. 222, 5. 21, 11. 106.<BR>—3 Torment, torture.<BR>—4 A particular kind of religious penance (प्राजापत्य); कृच्छ्राणि<BR> चीर्त्वा च ततो यथोक्तानि द्विजोत्तमैः Mb. 13. 10. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रम्
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रः, -च्छ्रम्@}<BR>—1 A difficulty, trouble, hardship, misery, calamity, danger; कृच्छ्रं<BR> महत्तीर्णः R. 14. 6, 13. 77.<BR>—2 Bodily mortification, penance, expiation; Ms. 4. 222, 5. 21, 11. 106.<BR>—3 Torment, torture.<BR>—4 A particular kind of religious penance (प्राजापत्य); कृच्छ्राणि<BR> चीर्त्वा च ततो यथोक्तानि द्विजोत्तमैः Mb. 13. 10. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रः|कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रः@} Ischury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रम्
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्@} Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रम्
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्, कृच्छ्रेत्, कृच्छ्रत्@} <i>ind.</i> With great difficulty, painfully,<BR> miserably; लब्धं कृच्छ्रेण रक्ष्यते H. 1. 163.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृच्छ्रार्धः, कृच्छ्रकृत्, कृच्छ्रप्राण, कृच्छ्रसाध्य, कृच्छ्रसांतपनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रेत्
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्, कृच्छ्रेत्, कृच्छ्रत्@} <i>ind.</i> With great difficulty, painfully,<BR> miserably; लब्धं कृच्छ्रेण रक्ष्यते H. 1. 163.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृच्छ्रार्धः, कृच्छ्रकृत्, कृच्छ्रप्राण, कृच्छ्रसाध्य, कृच्छ्रसांतपनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रत्
कृच्छ्र + .{@-च्छ्रम्, कृच्छ्रेत्, कृच्छ्रत्@} <i>ind.</i> With great difficulty, painfully,<BR> miserably; लब्धं कृच्छ्रेण रक्ष्यते H. 1. 163.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृच्छ्रार्धः, कृच्छ्रकृत्, कृच्छ्रप्राण, कृच्छ्रसाध्य, कृच्छ्रसांतपनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रार्धः|कृच्छ्रार्ध
कृच्छ्र + -अर्धः a penance lasting for six days only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रकृत्
कृच्छ्र + -कृत् <i>a.</i> Undergoing a penance; कृच्छ्रकृद्धर्मकामस्तु महतीं<BR> श्रियमाप्नुयात् Y. 3. 327.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रप्राण
कृच्छ्र + -प्राण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one whose life is in danger.<BR>—2 breathing with difficulty.<BR>—3 hardly supporting life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रसाध्य
कृच्छ्र + -साध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 curable with difficulty (as a patient or disease).<BR>—2 accomplished with difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रसांतपनम्
कृच्छ्र + -सांतपनम् a kind of expiatory vow laid down in the स्मृतिs;<BR> गोमूत्रं गोमयं क्षीरं दधि सर्पिः कुशोदकम् । एकरात्रोपवासश्च कृच्छ्रं<BR> सांतपनं स्मृतम् ॥ Ms. 11. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रायते
कृच्छ्रायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To suffer, pain.<BR>—2 To have wicked designs (in mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणुः|कृणु
कृणुः A painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् I. €6 P. (कृन्तति-कृत्त) To cut, cut off, divide, tear asunder,<BR> cut in pieces, destroy; प्रहरति विधिर्मर्मच्छेदी न कृन्तति जीवितम्<BR> U. 3. 31, 35; Bk. 9. 42, 15. 97, 16. 15; Ms. 8. 12. ━II. €7 P. (कृणत्ति, कृत्त)<BR>—1 To spin.<BR>—2 To surround, encompass.<BR>—3 To attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्त|कृत्तं
कृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cut, divided.<BR>—2 Desired, sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिः|कृत्ति
कृत्तिः <i>f.</i> [कृत्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Skin, hide (in general); Mu. 3. 20.<BR>—2 Especially, the hide of an antelope on which a religious student sits.<BR>—3 The bark of the birch-tree used for writing upon &c.<BR>—4 The birch-tree.<BR>—5 One of the lunar mansions, Pleiades.<BR>—6 A house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृत्तिवासः, कृत्तिवासस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासः|कृत्तिवास
कृत्तिः + -वासः, -वासस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva; स कृत्तिवासास्तपसे<BR> यतात्मा Ku. 1. 54; M. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासस्
कृत्तिः + -वासः, -वासस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva; स कृत्तिवासास्तपसे<BR> यतात्मा Ku. 1. 54; M. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका (pl.) [कृत्-तिकन् किच्च; Uṇ. 3. 147]<BR>—1 The third of the 27 lunar mansions or asterisms, (consisting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">Page0598-2</a>]<BR> of 6 stars) the Pleiades; Bhāg. 6. 14. 30.<BR>—2 The six stars represented as nymphs acting as nurses to Kārtikeya,<BR> the god of war.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृत्तिकाञ्जिः, कृत्तिकातनयः, कृत्तिकापुत्रः, कृत्तिकासुतः, कृत्तिकाभवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकाञ्जिः|कृत्तिकाञ्जि
कृत्तिका + -अञ्जिः a kind of horse in an Aśvamedha sacrifice having a carriage as an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकातनयः|कृत्तिकातनय
कृत्तिका + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Kārtikeya; अनुगच्छति<BR> देवेशं ब्रह्मण्यः कृत्तिकासुतः Mb. 3. 231. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकापुत्रः|कृत्तिकापुत्र
कृत्तिका + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Kārtikeya; अनुगच्छति<BR> देवेशं ब्रह्मण्यः कृत्तिकासुतः Mb. 3. 231. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकासुतः|कृत्तिकासुत
कृत्तिका + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Kārtikeya; अनुगच्छति<BR> देवेशं ब्रह्मण्यः कृत्तिकासुतः Mb. 3. 231. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकाभवः|कृत्तिकाभव
कृत्तिका + -भवः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यम्
कृत्यम् (from कृन्त्) An instrument of an architect; अन्येषु शिल्पेषु<BR> च यान्यपि स्युः सर्वाणि कृत्यान्यखिलेन तत्र Mb. 1. 194. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तत्रम्
कृन्तत्रम् Ved.<BR>—1 A section.<BR>—2 A chip.<BR>—3 A plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तनम्
कृन्तनम् Cutting, cutting off, dividing, tearing asunder; नातः<BR> परं कर्मनिबन्धकृन्तनम् Bhāg. 6. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तनिका
कृन्तनिका, -नी<BR>—1 A small knife.<BR>—2 The sharp edge of a knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तनी
कृन्तनिका, -नी<BR>—1 A small knife.<BR>—2 The sharp edge of a knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम <i>a.</i> [कृत्या निर्मितम्; cf. P. IV. 4. 20]<BR>—1 Artificial, fictitious, not spontaneous, acquired; ˚मित्रम्, ˚शत्रुः<BR> &c.; न स्यन्दनैस्तुलितकृत्रिमभक्तिशोभाः R. 13. 75, 14. 17.<BR>—2 Adopted (as a child); see below.<BR>—3 Adorned, ornamented; तदप्रमेयप्रतिकारकृत्रिमं कृतं स्वयं साध्विति<BR> विश्वकर्मणा Rām. 5. 8. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमः|कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं
कृत्रिम + .{@-मः, ˚पुत्रः@} an artificial or adopted son; one of the 12 kinds<BR> of sons recognised by the Hindu law; he is a grown up son adopted without<BR> the consent of his natural parents; {@˚पुत्रिका@} adopted daughter;<BR> अद्यैव नर्मणा सा हि कृतकृत्रिमपुत्रिका Ks. 24. 29; cf. कृत्रिमः<BR> स्यात्स्वयं कृतः Y. 2. 131; cf. also Ms. 9. 169.<BR>—2 Incense. olibanum.<BR>—3 Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्रः|कृत्रिमपुत्र|कृत्रिमपुत्त्रः
कृत्रिम + .{@-मः, ˚पुत्रः@} an artificial or adopted son; one of the 12 kinds<BR> of sons recognised by the Hindu law; he is a grown up son adopted without<BR> the consent of his natural parents; {@˚पुत्रिका@} adopted daughter;<BR> अद्यैव नर्मणा सा हि कृतकृत्रिमपुत्रिका Ks. 24. 29; cf. कृत्रिमः<BR> स्यात्स्वयं कृतः Y. 2. 131; cf. also Ms. 9. 169.<BR>—2 Incense. olibanum.<BR>—3 Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्रिका
कृत्रिम + .{@-मः, ˚पुत्रः@} an artificial or adopted son; one of the 12 kinds<BR> of sons recognised by the Hindu law; he is a grown up son adopted without<BR> the consent of his natural parents; {@˚पुत्रिका@} adopted daughter;<BR> अद्यैव नर्मणा सा हि कृतकृत्रिमपुत्रिका Ks. 24. 29; cf. कृत्रिमः<BR> स्यात्स्वयं कृतः Y. 2. 131; cf. also Ms. 9. 169.<BR>—2 Incense. olibanum.<BR>—3 Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमम्
कृत्रिम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 A kind of salt.<BR>—2 A kind of perfume.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृत्रिमधूपः, कृत्रिमधूपकः, कृत्रिमपुत्रः, कृत्रिमपुत्रकः, कृत्रिमभूमिः, कृत्रिमवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमधूपः|कृत्रिमधूप
कृत्रिम + -धूपः, -धूपकः incense, a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमधूपकः|कृत्रिमधूपक
कृत्रिम + -धूपः, -धूपकः incense, a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्रः|कृत्रिमपुत्र|कृत्रिमपुत्त्रः
कृत्रिम + -पुत्रः see कृत्रिमः;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्रकः|कृत्रिमपुत्रक
कृत्रिम + -पुत्रकः a doll, puppet; मन्दाकिनीसैकतवेदिकाभिः सा कन्दुकैः कृत्रिमपुत्रकैश्च (रेमे) Ku. 1. 29<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमभूमिः|कृत्रिमभूमि
कृत्रिम + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> an artificial floor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमवनम्
कृत्रिम + -वनम् a park, garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वन्
कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Causing, effecting &c.<BR>—2 Active, diligent, busy; येना दंसिष्ठ कृत्वने Rv. 8. 24. 25.<BR>—3 Practising magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वस्
कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> An affix added to numerals to denote ‘fold’ or ‘times’;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> अष्टकृत्वः eight times, eight-fold; so दश˚, पञ्च˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वाचिन्ता
कृत्वाचिन्ता A consideration of some hypothetical case; ननु<BR> नैवास्थ्गां यज्ञो, जीवतामसावित्युक्तम् । अत्रोच्यते । कृत्वाचिन्ता एषा । अस्थ्नामिति<BR> कृत्वा चिन्त्यते ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 49; कृत्वाचिन्तायां प्रयोजनं न<BR> वक्तव्यम् ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्व्य
कृत्व्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Strong, efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्सम्
कृत्सम् [Uṇ. 3. 66]<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 A multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्सः|कृत्स|कृत्सं
कृत्सम् + .{@-त्सः@} Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्न|कृत्स्नं|कृत्स्नः
कृत्स्न <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 3. 17] All, whole, entire; कृत्स्नो रसघन<BR> एव Bṛ. Up. 4. 5. 13; एकः कृत्स्नां नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति<BR> Ś. 2. 16; Bg. 3. 29; Ms. 1. 105, 5. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नम्
कृत्स्न + .{@-त्स्नम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 The flank or hip.<BR>—3 The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0598-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदरम्
कृदरम् Ved.<BR>—1 A store-room.<BR>—2 The lap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदरः|कृदर|कृदरं
कृदरम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Granary, a cupboard.<BR>—2 A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृधु
कृधु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Shortened, mutilated.<BR>—2 Deficient; प्रतीत्येन कृधुना तृपासः Rv. 4. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप्
कृप् I. €1 Ā. (कर्पते, कृपित) To have pity or mercy. ━II. €10 P.<BR> [कृप(पा)यति]<BR>—1 To be weak.<BR>—2 To pity; पुंसः कृपयते भद्रे सर्वात्मा प्रीयते हरिः Bhāg. 8. 7. 40.<BR>—3 To mourn, grieve, lament; अश्रूणि कृपमाणस्य यानि जीतस्य वावृतुः Av. 5. 19. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपः|कृप
कृपः The maternal uncle of अश्वत्थामन. [He was born of the<BR> sage Śaradvat by a nymph called Jānapadī, but along with his sister<BR> Kṛpī, also born from the nymph, he was brought up by Śantanu. He was<BR> proficient in the science of archery. In the great war he sided with the<BR> Kauravas, and after all had been slain he was given an asylum by the Pāṇḍavas.<BR> He is one of the seven Chirajīvins.] कृपश्च समितिञ्जयः Bg. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण|कृपणः
कृपण <i>a.</i> [कृप्-क्युन् न लत्वम्]<BR>—1 Poor, pitiable, wretched, helpless; राजन्नपत्यं रामस्ते पाल्याश्च<BR> कृपणाः प्रजाः U. 4. 25; व्रजतु च कृपा क्वाद्य कृपणा Nāg. 5. 30;<BR> Rām. 2. 32. 28.<BR>—2 Void of judgment, unable or unwilling to discriminate or to do a thing;<BR> कामार्ता हि प्रकृतिकृपणाश्चेतनाचेतनेषु Me. 5; so जराजीर्णैश्वर्यग्रसनगहनाक्षेपकृपणः Bh. 3. 17.<BR>—3 Low, mean, vile; कृपणाः फलहेतवः Bg. 2. 49; Mu. 2. 18; Bh. 2. 49.<BR>—4 Miserly, stingy.<BR>—5 Avaricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणम्
कृपण + .{@-णम्@} Wretchedness; कुत्साय शुष्णं कृपणे परादात् Rv. 10. 99. 9; Ms. 4. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणः|कृपण
कृपण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A worm.<BR>—2 A miser; कृपणेन समो दाता भुवि कोऽपि न विद्यते । अनश्नन्नेव वित्तानि<BR> यः परेभ्यः प्रयच्छति Vyāsa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृपणधी, कृपणबुद्धि, कृपणवत्सल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणधी
कृपण + -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> little or low-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणबुद्धि
कृपण + -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> little or low-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणवत्सल
कृपण + -वत्सल <i>a.</i> kind to the poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणिन्
कृपणिन् Miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण्यति
कृपण्यति Den. P. To wish, desire; तत्तदग्निर्वयो दधे यथायथा<BR> कृपण्यति Rv. 8. 39. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपा
कृपा [क्रप्-भिदा˚ अङ् संप्र.] Pity, tenderness, compassion; कृपया<BR> परयाविष्टः Bg. 1. 28; चक्रवाकयोः पुरो वियुक्ते मिथुने कृपावती<BR> Ku. 5. 26; Śānti. 4. 19; सकृपम् kindly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृपान्वित, कृपाकरः, कृपासागरः, कृपासिन्धुः, कृपादृष्टिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपान्वित
कृपा + -अन्वित <i>a.</i> merciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाकरः|कृपाकर
कृपा + -आकरः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः extremely compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपासागरः|कृपासागर
कृपा + -आकरः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः extremely compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपासिन्धुः|कृपासिन्धु
कृपा + -आकरः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः extremely compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपादृष्टिः|कृपादृष्टि
कृपा + -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i> a look with favour, a kind look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणः|कृपाण
कृपाणः [कृपां नुदति नुद्-ड संज्ञायां णत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A sword; स पातु वः कंसरिपोः कृपाणः Vikr. 1. 2; कृपणस्य<BR> कृपाणस्य च केवलमाकारतो भेदः Subhāṣ.; Ks. 53. 87.<BR>—2 A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणकः|कृपाणक
कृपाणकः A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणिका
कृपाणकः + .{@-णिका@} A knife, dagger; सेवापरिकरश्चान्यत्त्रयं कट्यां कृपाणिका Ks. 53. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणी
कृपाणी<BR>—1 A pair of scissors.<BR>—2 A dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपायते
कृपायते Den. Ā. To lament, mourn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपालु|कृपालुः
कृपालु <i>a.</i> [कृपां लाति ला-आदाने मि˚ डु] Merciful, compassionate,<BR> kind; गुरो कृपालो कृपया वहैनम् Maṇiratnamālā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपी
कृपी The sister of कृप and wife of Droṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृपीपतिः, कृपीसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीपतिः|कृपीपति
