कृमिलिका Linen cloth dyed with red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमीलकः|कृमीलक
कृमीलकः A white sort of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृव्
कृव् €1 P. = कृ €5 P. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश्
कृश् €4 P. (कृश्यति, कृश)<BR>—1 To become lean or emaciated; य एषां ज्योतिष्माँ उत यश्चकर्श Av. 12. 3. 16.<BR>—2 To wane (as the moon).<BR>.━<i>Caus.</i> To emaciate; कर्षयन्तः शरीरस्थं भूतग्राममचेतसः Bg. 17. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश <i>a.</i> [कृश्-क्त नि˚] (Compar. क्रशीयस्; superl. क्रशिष्ट)<BR>—1 Lean, weak, feeble, emaciated; कृशतनुः, कृशोदरी &c.; कृशः<BR> काशः खञ्जः श्रवणरहितः पुच्छविकलः Bh. 1. 78.<BR>—2 Small, little, minute (in size or quantity); सुहृदपि न याच्यः कृशधनः Bh. 2. 28.<BR>—3 Poor, insignificant; Ms. 7. 208.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृशाक्षः, कृशाङ्ग, कृशातिथि, कृशोदर, कृशगव, कृशभृत्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाक्षः|कृशाक्ष
कृश + -अक्षः a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाङ्ग|कृशाङ्गः
कृश + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> lean, thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाङ्गः|कृशाङ्ग
कृश + -अङ्ग + ({@-ङ्गः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाङ्गी|कृशांगी
कृश + -अङ्ग + ({@-ङ्गी@})<BR>—1 a woman with a slender frame; कृशाङ्ग्याः संतापं वदति नलिनीपत्रशयनम् Ratn.<BR>—2 the Priyaṅgu creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशातिथि
कृश + -अतिथि <i>a.</i> one who keeps his guests short of food; Mb. 12. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशोदर
कृश + -उदर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 thin-waisted; सद्यस्त्वया<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">Page0600-1</a>]<BR> सह कृशोदरि विप्रयोगः V. 5. 16; Ku. 5. 42.<BR>—2 having the belly reduced in bulk; मेदच्छेदकृशोदरं लघु भवत्युत्थानयोग्यं<BR> वपुः Ś. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0599-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशगव
कृश + -गव <i>a.</i> one who has lean cattle; यः कृशार्थः कृशगवः<BR> कृशभृत्यः कृशातिथिः । स वै राजन् कृशो नाम न शरीरकृशः कृशः ॥ Mb. 12. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशभृत्य
कृश + -भृत्य <i>a.</i> one who feeds his servants scantily; see above quotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशनम्
कृशनम् Ved.<BR>—1 A pearl; अभीवृतं कृशनैर्विश्वरूपम् Rv. 1. 35. 4.<BR>—2 Gold.<BR>—3 Form, shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशरः|कृशर
कृशरः<BR>—1 A dish made of milk, sesamum and rice; ददौ द्विजेभ्यः कृशरं च<BR> गाश्च Bu. C. 2. 36.<BR>—2 Rice and peas boiled together with a few spices (Mar. खिचडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशला
कृशला Hair (of the head).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुः|कृशानु
कृशानुः [कृश् आनुक्; Uṇ. 4. 2] Fire; गुरोः कृशानुप्रतिमाद्बिभेषि<BR> R. 2. 49, 7. 24, 10. 74; Ku. 1. 51; Bh. 2. 107.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृशानुयन्त्रम्, कृशानुरेतस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुयन्त्रम्
कृशानुः + -यन्त्रम् (= अग्नियन्त्रम्) a cannon; अथ सपदि कृशानुयन्त्रगोलैः … …<BR> Śiva B. 28. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुरेतस्
कृशानुः + -रेतस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्विन्
कृशाश्विन् <i>m.</i> An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्
कृष् I. €6 U. (कृषति-ते, कृष्ट) To plough, make furrows; ततस्ते<BR> देवयजनं ब्राह्मणाः स्वर्णलाङ्गलैः । कृष्ट्वा तत्र यथाम्नायं दीक्षयां<BR> चक्रिरे नृपम् ॥ Bhāg. 10. 74. 12. ━II. €1 P. (कर्षति, कृष्ट)<BR>—1 To draw, drag, pull, drag away, tear; प्रसह्य सिंहः किल तांचकर्ष<BR> R. 2. 27; V. 1. 19.<BR>—2 To draw towards oneself, attract; हस्ताभ्यां नश्यदक्राक्षीद् Bk. 15. 47;<BR> Bg. 15. 7.<BR>—3 To lead or conduct as an army; स सेनां महतीं कर्षन् R. 4. 32.<BR>—4 To bend (as a bow); नात्यायतकृष्टशार्ङ्गः R. 5. 50.<BR>—5 To become master of, subdue, vanquish, overpower; बलवानिन्द्रियग्रामो<BR> विद्वांसमपि कर्षति Ms. 2. 215; नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य गजेन्द्रमपि<BR> कर्षति Pt. 3. 46.<BR>—6 To plough, till; अनुलोमकृष्टं क्षेत्रं प्रतिलोमं कर्षति Sk.<BR>—7 To obtain; कुलसंख्यां च गच्छन्ति कर्षन्ति च महद्यशः Ms. 3. 66.<BR>—8 To take away from, deprive one of (with two acc.).<BR>—9 To scratch; सुवीरकं याच्यमाना मद्रिका कर्षति स्फिचौ Mb. 8. 40. 38.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To draw out, tear up.<BR>—2 To extract.<BR>—3 To torture, torment, give pain.<BR>—4 To plough, till, cultivate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषक|कृषकः
कृषक <i>a.</i> [कृष्-क्वन्]<BR>—1 Attractive, drawing.<BR>—2 Ploughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषकः|कृषक
कृषक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A ploughman, husbandman; कच्चिन्न भक्तं बीजं च कर्षकस्यावसीदति Mb. 2. 5. 78.<BR>—2 An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषकम्
कृषक + .{@-कम्@} A ploughshare. (also <i>m.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाणः|कृषाण
कृषाणः, -कृषिकः<BR> [कृष्-आनक्-किकन् वा] A ploughman, husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिकः|कृषिक
कृषाणः, -कृषिकः<BR> [कृष्-आनक्-किकन् वा] A ploughman, husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिः|कृषि
कृषिः <i>f.</i> [कृष्-इक्; cf. P. III. 3. 108. Vārt. 8]<BR>—1 Ploughing.<BR>—2 Agriculture, husbandry; चीयते बालिशस्यापि सत्क्षेत्रपतिता कृषिः<BR> Mu. 1. 3; कृषिः क्लिष्टाऽवृष्ट्या Pt. 1. 11; Ms. 1. 90, 3. 64, 10. 79; Bg. 18. 44.<BR>—3 The harvest (कृषिफल); Y. 1. 276.<BR>—4 The earth; Mb. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृषिकर्मन्, कृषिजीविन्, कृषिद्विष्टः, कृषिपराशरः, कृषिसंग्रहः, कृषिफलम्, कृषिसेवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिकर्मन्
कृषिः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिजीविन्
कृषिः + -जीविन् <i>a.</i> living by husbandry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिद्विष्टः|कृषिद्विष्ट
कृषिः + -द्विष्टः a kind of sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिपराशरः|कृषिपराशर
कृषिः + -पराशरः, -संग्रहः N. of a treatise on agriculture (see<BR> Annals of the Bhandarkar Oriental Research Institute Vol. XXXVI Nos. 1━2).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">Page0600-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिसंग्रहः|कृषिसङ्ग्रह
कृषिः + -पराशरः, -संग्रहः N. of a treatise on agriculture (see<BR> Annals of the Bhandarkar Oriental Research Institute Vol. XXXVI Nos. 1━2).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">Page0600-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिफलम्
कृषिः + -फलम् agricultural produce or profit; Me. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिसेवा
कृषिः + -सेवा agriculture, husbandry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषीवलः|कृषीवल
कृषीवलः [कृषि वलच् दीर्घः; cf. P. V. 2. 112] One who lives<BR> by husbandry, a farmer; कृषिं चापि कृषीवलः Y. 1. 276; Ms. 9. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ट|कृष्टं
कृष्ट <i>a.</i> [कृष् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Drawn, pulled, dragged, attracted &c.<BR>—2 Ploughed; न हि तस्मात्फलं तस्य सुकृष्टादूषरादिव Pt. 1. 47.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृष्टोप्त, कृष्टज, कृष्टपच्य, कृष्टपाक्य, कृष्टफलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टोप्त
कृष्ट + -उप्त <i>a.</i> sown on cultivated ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टज
कृष्ट + -ज <i>a.</i> grown in cultivated ground; Ms. 11. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपच्य|कृष्टपच्यः
कृष्ट + -पच्य, -पाक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ripening in cultivated ground; यो हि कृष्टे पक्तव्यः कृष्टपाक्यः<BR> स भवति Mbh. on P. III. 1. 114; cf. अकृष्टपच्य; न कृष्टपच्यमश्नीयादकृष्टं<BR> चाप्यकालतः Bhāg. 7. 12. 18.<BR>—2 cultivated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपाक्य|कृष्टपाक्यं
कृष्ट + -पच्य, -पाक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ripening in cultivated ground; यो हि कृष्टे पक्तव्यः कृष्टपाक्यः<BR> स भवति Mbh. on P. III. 1. 114; cf. अकृष्टपच्य; न कृष्टपच्यमश्नीयादकृष्टं<BR> चाप्यकालतः Bhāg. 7. 12. 18.<BR>—2 cultivated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टफलम्
कृष्ट + -फलम् the product of a harvest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टिः|कृष्टि
कृष्टिः [कृष्-क्तिन्] A learned man. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Drawing, attracting.<BR>—2 Ploughing, cultivating the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्करः|कृष्कर
कृष्करः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
कृष्ण <i>a.</i> [कृष्-नक्]<BR>—1 Black, dark, dark-blue.<BR>—2 Wicked, evil; मनो गुणान्वै सृजते बलीयस्ततश्च कर्माणि विलक्षणानि ।<BR> शुक्लानि कृष्णान्यथ लोहितानि तेभ्यः सवर्णाः सृतयो भवन्ति ॥ Bhāg. 11. 23. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णः|कृष्ण|कृष्णं
कृष्ण + .{@-ष्णः@}<BR>—1 The black colour.<BR>—2 The black antelope; Bhāg. 10. 35. 19.<BR>—3 A crow.<BR>—4 The (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>—5 The dark half of a lunar month (from full to new moon); Bg. 8. 25.<BR>—6 The Kali age.<BR>—7 Viṣṇu in his eighth incarnation, born as the son of Vasudeva and<BR> Devakī. [Kṛṣṇa^1 is the most celebrated hero of Indian mythology and<BR> the most popular of all the deities. Though the real son of Vasudeva and<BR> Devakī and thus a cousin of Kaṃsa, he was, for all practical purposes,<BR> the son of Nanda and Yaśodā, by whom he was brought up and in whose<BR> house he spent his childhood. It was here that his divine character began<BR> to be gradually discovered, when he easily crushed the most redoubtable<BR> demons, such as Baka, Pūtanā &c., that were sent to kill him by Kaṃsa,<BR> and performed many other feats of surprising strength. The chief companions<BR> of his youth were the <i>Gopis</i> or wives of the cowherds of Gokula,<BR> among whom Rādhā was his special favourite (cf. Jayadevaʼs <i>Gitagovinda</i>).<BR> He killed Kaṃsa, Naraka, Keśin, Ariṣṭa and a host of other powerful<BR> demons. He was a particular friend of Arjuna, to whom he acted as charioteer<BR> in the great war, and his staunch support of the cause of the Pāṇḍavas<BR> was the main cause of the overthrow of the Kauravas. On several critical<BR> occasions, it was Kṛṣṇa^2ʼs assistance and inventive mind that stood<BR> the Pāṇḍavas in good stead. After the general destruction of the Yādavas<BR> at Prabhāsa, he was killed unintentionally by a hunter named Jaras who<BR> shot him with an arrow mistaking him at a distance for a deer. He had<BR> more than 16000 wives,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0601-1" target="_blank">Page0601-1</a>]<BR> but Rukmiṇī and Satyabhāmā, (as also Rādhā) were his favourites.<BR> He is said to have been of dark-blue or cloud-like colour; cf. बहिरिव<BR> मलिनतरं तव कृष्ण मनोऽपि भविष्यति नूनं Gīt. 8. His son was Pradyumna].<BR>—8 N. of Vyāsa, the reputed author of the Mahābhārata; कुतः सञ्चोदितः<BR> कृष्णः कृतवान्संहितां मुनिः Bhāg. 1. 4. 3.<BR>—9 N. of Arjuna.<BR>—10 Aloe wood.<BR>—11 The Supreme spirit.<BR>—12 Black pepper.<BR>—13 Iron.<BR>—14 A Śūdra; कृष्णस्तु केशवे व्यासे कोकिलेऽर्जुनकाकयोः । शूद्रे तामिस्रपक्षेऽग्निकलिनीलगुणेषु<BR> च ॥ Nm. 15 The marking nut (भल्लातक); विरक्तं शोध्यते वस्त्रं<BR> न तु कृष्णोपसंहितम् Mb. 12. 291. 10.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णा
कृष्ण + .{@-ष्णा@}<BR>—1 N. of Draupadī, wife of the Pāṇḍavas; तेजो हृतं खलु मयाभिहतश्च<BR> मत्स्यः सज्जीकृतेन धनुषाधिगता च कृष्णा Bhāg. 1. 15. 7; प्रविश्य<BR> कृष्णासदनं महीभुजा Ki. 1. 26.<BR>—2 N. of a river in the Deccan that joins the sea at Machalipaṭṭaṇa.<BR>—3 A kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—4 N. of several plants.<BR>—5 A grape.<BR>—6 A kind of perfume.<BR>—7 An epithet of Durgā; Bhāg. 4. 6. 7.<BR>—8 One of the 7 tongues of fire.<BR>—9 N. of the river Yamunā; विलोक्य दूषितां कृष्णां कृष्णः कृष्णाहिना<BR> विभुः Bhāg. 10. 16. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णी
कृष्ण + .{@-ष्णी@} A dark night; रिणक्ति कृष्णीररुषाय पन्थाम् Rv. 7. 71. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णम्
कृष्ण + .{@-ष्णम्@}<BR>—1 Blackness, darkness (moral also); शुक्रा कृष्णादजनिष्ट श्वितीची Rv. 1. 123. 9.<BR>—2 Iron.<BR>—3 Antimony.<BR>—4 The black part of the eye.<BR>—5 Black pepper.<BR>—6 Lead.<BR>—7 An inauspicious act. —8 Money acquired by gambling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कृष्णागुरु, कृष्णाचलः, कृष्णाजिनम्, कृष्णाध्वन्, कृष्णार्चिस्, कृष्णायस्, कृष्णार्जकः, कृष्णाष्टमी, कृष्णजन्माष्टमी, कृष्णावासः, कृष्णोदरः, कृष्णकञ्चुकः, कृष्णकन्दम्, कृष्णकर्मन्, कृष्णकाकः, कृष्णकायः, कृष्णकाष्ठम्, कृष्णकोहलः, कृष्णगङ्गा, कृष्णगति, कृष्णगर्भाः, कृष्णगोधा, कृष्णग्रीवः, कृष्णचञ्चुकः, कृष्णचन्द्रः, कृष्णचर, कृष्णचूर्णम्, कृष्णच्छविः, कृष्णताम्रम्, कृष्णतारः, कृष्णतालु, कृष्णत्रिवृता, कृष्णदेहः, कृष्णधनम्, कृष्णद्वादशी, कृष्णद्वैपायनः, कृष्णपक्षः, कृष्णपदी, कृष्णपविः, कृष्णपाकः, कृष्णपिङ्गल, कृष्णपिण्डीतकः, कृष्णपुष्पी, कृष्णफलः, कृष्णवीजम्, कृष्णभस्मन्, कृष्णमृगः, कृष्णमुखः, कृष्णवक्त्रः, कृष्णवदनः, कृष्णमृत्तिका, कृष्णयजुर्वेदः, कृष्णयामः, कृष्णरक्तः, कृष्णरूप्य, कृष्णलवणम्, कृष्णलोहः, कृष्णवर्णः, कृष्णवर्त्मन्, कृष्णविषाणा, कृष्णवेणी, कृष्णशकुनिः, कृष्णशारः, कृष्णसारः, कृष्णसारङ्गः, कृष्णशृङ्गः, कृष्णसखः, कृष्णसारथिः, कृष्णस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0600-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

