कैलासः + -ओकस् <i>m.</i><BR> {@-निकेतनः, -नाथः@}<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 of Kubera; कैलासनाथं तरसा जिगीषुः R. 5. 28; कैलासनाथमुपसृत्य<BR> निवर्तमाना V. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्तः|कैवर्त|कैवर्त्त|कैवर्त्तः
कैवर्तः [के जले वर्तते वृत्-अच्; केवर्तः ततः स्वार्थे अण् Tv.]<BR> A fisherman; मनोभूः कैवर्तः क्षिपति परितस्त्वां प्रति मुहुः (तनूजालीजालम्)<BR> Śānti. 3. 16; Ms. 8. 260; (as to his descent see Ms. 10. 34).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्तकः|कैवर्तक|कैवर्त्तक
कैवर्तकः A fisherman; Rām. 2. 83. 15; Ks. 112. 113; सोत्तीर्णा<BR> खलु पाण्ङवै रणनदी कैवर्तकः केशवः Bg. (ध्यानम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवल्यम्
कैवल्यम् [केवलस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Perfect isolation, soleness, exclusiveness.<BR>—2 Individuality; Bhāg. 5. 3. 17.<BR>—3 Detachment of the soul from matter, identification with the supreme spirit<BR>—4 Final emancipation or beatitude; Bhāg. 1. 8. 27.<BR>—5 Ever-lasting disappearance of the three pains; कैवल्यं माध्यस्थ्यम्<BR> Sāṅ. K. 19; कैवल्यार्थं प्रवृत्तेश्च <i>ibid.</i> 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिक|कैशिकं|कैशिकः
कैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [केश-ठक्] Hairlike, fine as hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिकः|कैशिक|कैशिकं
कैशिक + .{@-कः@} The sentiment of love, lust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिकम्
कैशिक + .{@-कम्@} A quantity of hair; कपटकैशिकभूषितमल्लिका Rām. Ch. 4. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिकी
कैशिक + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 One of the four varieties of dramatic style; Rām. 5. 1. 163; more<BR> usually and correctly written कैशिकी q. v.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोरम्
कैशोरम् [किशोरस्य भावः अञ्] Youth, childhood, tender age (below<BR> fifteen); कैशोरमापञ्चदशात्; सन्तं वयसि कैशोरे भृत्यानुग्रहकातरम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 28. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कैशोरवयस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोरवयस्
कैशोरम् + -वयस् <i>a.</i> having the age of a youth; निवेश्य चित्ते पुरुषं<BR> स्वरोचिषं विवेश कैशोरवयाः परं गतः Bhāg. 9. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोर्यः|कैशोर्य
कैशोर्यः^1 <i>m.</i> N. of a sage शाण्डिल्यः कैशोर्यात्काप्यात् Bṛ. Up. 2. 6. 3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैश्यम्
कैश्यम् The whole mass of hair, quantity of hair; कलय केशिनि<BR> कैश्यमसंयतम् N. 4. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकः|कोक
कोकः [कुक्-आदाने अच् Tv.]<BR>—1 A wolf; वने यूथपरिभ्रष्टा मृगी कोकैरिवार्दिता Rām. 5. 25. 5.<BR>—2 The ruddy goose (चक्रवाक); कोकानां करुणस्वरेण सदृशी दीर्घा<BR> मदभ्यर्थना Gīt. 5.<BR>—3 A cuckoo जनितकोकनदानि जलाशये, शरदि कोकनदानि चकाशिरे<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 62; हिरण्मया हस्तिमृगाश्च कोकाः Bu. C. 2. 22.<BR>—4 A frog.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 A wild lizard.<BR>—7 A wild date tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोकदेवः, कोकबन्धुः, कोकशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकदेवः|कोकदेव
कोकः + -देवः a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकबन्धुः|कोकबन्धु
कोकः + -बन्धुः an epithet of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकशास्त्रम्
कोकः + -शास्त्रम् N. of a treatise on the art of love (ascribed to a pandit<BR> named कोक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकडः|कोकड
कोकडः The Indian fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकथुः|कोकथु
कोकथुः The wood-pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनदम्
कोकनदम् [कोकान् चक्रवाकान् नदति नादयति नद्-अच्]<BR>—1 The red lotus; किंचित्कोकनदच्छदस्य सदृशे नेत्रे स्वयं रज्यतः<BR> U. 5. 36; नीलनलिनाभमपि तन्वि तव लोचनं धारयति कोकनदरूपम्<BR> Gīt. 10; Śi. 4. 46; जनितकोकनदानि जलाशये, शरदि कोकनदानि चकाशिरे ।<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 62.<BR>—2 The red water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनदिनी
कोकनदम् + .{@-दिनी@} The red water-lily; न भेकः कोकनदिनीकिंजल्कास्वादकोविदः Ks. 30. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकामुखम्
कोकामुखम् N. of a famous holy place in India; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकाहः|कोकाह
कोकाहः A white horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0606-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलः|कोकिल
कोकिलः, -ला<BR> [कुल-इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54.]<BR>—1 The (Indian or black) cuckoo; पुंस्कोकिलो यन्मधुरं चुकूज Ku. 3. 32, 4. 16;<BR> R. 12. 39.<BR>—2 A fire-brand.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोकिलावासः, कोकिलोत्सवः, कोकिलेक्षुः, कोकिलप्रियः, कोकिलव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिला
कोकिलः, -ला<BR> [कुल-इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54.]<BR>—1 The (Indian or black) cuckoo; पुंस्कोकिलो यन्मधुरं चुकूज Ku. 3. 32, 4. 16;<BR> R. 12. 39.<BR>—2 A fire-brand.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोकिलावासः, कोकिलोत्सवः, कोकिलेक्षुः, कोकिलप्रियः, कोकिलव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलावासः|कोकिलावास
कोकिलः + -आवासः, -उत्सवः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलोत्सवः|कोकिलोत्सव
कोकिलः + -आवासः, -उत्सवः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलेक्षुः|कोकिलेक्षु
कोकिलः + -इक्षुः a kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलप्रियः|कोकिलप्रिय
कोकिलः + -प्रियः (in music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलव्रतम्
कोकिलः + -व्रतम् N. of an observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलकः|कोकिलक
कोकिलकः N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कः|कोङ्क|कोंक|कोंकः
कोङ्कः, कोङ्कणः (Pl.) N. of a country, the strip of land<BR> between the Sahyādri and the ocean; Mb. 6; आक्रम्य क्रमुकश्यामान्कोङ्कणान्सप्त<BR> तापयन् । तुरगानिव तिग्मांशोः प्रतापस्तस्य पप्रथे ॥ Rāj. T. 4. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणः|कोङ्कण|कोंकण|कोङ्कणं|कोंकणः
कोङ्कः, कोङ्कणः (Pl.) N. of a country, the strip of land<BR> between the Sahyādri and the ocean; Mb. 6; आक्रम्य क्रमुकश्यामान्कोङ्कणान्सप्त<BR> तापयन् । तुरगानिव तिग्मांशोः प्रतापस्तस्य पप्रथे ॥ Rāj. T. 4. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणम्
कोङ्कः, कोङ्कणः + .{@-णम्@} A kind of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणा
कोङ्कणा N. of Reṇukā, wife of Jamadagni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोङ्कणासूतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणासूतः
कोङ्कणा + -सूतः an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्काण
कोङ्काण, कोक्काण <i>a.</i> Coming from कोङ्कण; श्यामा कुवलयमाला<BR> कोक्काणी कीर्तिवर्मणस्तुरगी Ks. 121. 278.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक्काण
कोङ्काण, कोक्काण <i>a.</i> Coming from कोङ्कण; श्यामा कुवलयमाला<BR> कोक्काणी कीर्तिवर्मणस्तुरगी Ks. 121. 278.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोच|कोचः
कोच <i>a.</i> [कुच् कर्तरि ण] Drying, becoming dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोचः|कोच
कोच + .{@-चः@}<BR>—1 Drying up, withering, aridity.<BR>—2 A man of mixed caste, (the offspring of a fisherman by a female butcher.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोजागरः|कोजागर
कोजागरः [को जागर्ति इति लक्ष्म्या उक्तिरत्र काले पृषो˚ Tv.] N.<BR> of a festival held on the full moon night in the month of Āśvina and<BR> celebrated with several games.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटः|कोट
कोटः [कुट्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A fort.<BR>—2 A hut, shed.<BR>—3 Crookedness (moral also).<BR>—4 A beard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोटपः, कोटपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटपः|कोटप
कोटः + -पः, -पालः The commander of the fort (Mar. किल्लेदार). See कोटिपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटपालः|कोटपाल
