कोटक|कोटकः
कोटक <i>a.</i> Curving, bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटकः|कोटक
कोटक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A builder of sheds, thatcher.<BR>—2 A mixed caste (offspring of a mason by a daughter of a potter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटनः|कोटन
कोटनः Winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटरः|कोटर|कोटरं
कोटरः, -रम्<BR> [कोटं कौटिल्यं राति रा-क Tv.] The hollow of a tree;<BR> नीवाराः शुकगर्भकोटरमुखभ्रष्टास्तरूणामधः Ś. 1. 14; कोटरमकालवृष्टया<BR> प्रबलपुरोवातया गमिते M. 4. 2; Ṛs. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटरम्
कोटरः, -रम्<BR> [कोटं कौटिल्यं राति रा-क Tv.] The hollow of a tree;<BR> नीवाराः शुकगर्भकोटरमुखभ्रष्टास्तरूणामधः Ś. 1. 14; कोटरमकालवृष्टया<BR> प्रबलपुरोवातया गमिते M. 4. 2; Ṛs. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटरी
कोटरी, -कोटवी<BR>—1 A naked woman; पाटयन्क्षुरिकाघातैः कोटवीस्तनकोटरम् Rāj. T. 5. 440.<BR>—2 An epithet of the goddess Durgā (represented as naked).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटवी
कोटरी, -कोटवी<BR>—1 A naked woman; पाटयन्क्षुरिकाघातैः कोटवीस्तनकोटरम् Rāj. T. 5. 440.<BR>—2 An epithet of the goddess Durgā (represented as naked).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिः|कोटि
कोटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [कुट्-इञ्]<BR>—1 The curved end of a bow; भूमिनिहितैककोटिकार्मुकम् R. 11. 81; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 The end or extremity, edge or point in general; सहचरीं दन्तस्य<BR> कोटया लिखन् Māl. 9. 32; अङ्गदकोटिलग्नम् R. 6. 14, 7. 46, 8. 36.<BR>—3 The edge or point of a weapon.<BR>—4 The highest point, excess, pitch, climax, excellence; परां कोटिमानन्दस्याध्यगच्छन्<BR> K. 369; so कोपकोटिमापन्ना Pt. 4; excessively angry; कल्याणीं कलयामि<BR> कञ्जनिलयां कल्याणकोटिस्थिताम् Viś. Guṇā. 275.<BR>—5 The horns or digits of the moon; आवर्जितजटामौलिविलम्बिशशिकोटयः Ku. 2. 26.<BR>—6 Ten millions, a crore; वित्तस्य विद्यापरिसंख्यया मे कोटीश्चतस्रो<BR> दश चाहरेति R. 5. 21, 12. 82; Ms. 6. 63.<BR>—7 The complement of an arc to 90° (in math.).<BR>—8 The perpendicular side of a right-angled triangle (in math.).<BR>—9 A class, department, kingdom; मनुष्य˚, प्राणि˚ &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">Page0607-2</a>]<BR>—10 One side of a question in dispute, an alternative.<BR>—11 The pinnacle, peak (शिखर); कोटिं तस्य समुद्रस्य काञ्चनीं<BR> शतयोजनाम् Rām. 4. 42. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोटीश्वरः, कोटिजित्, कोटिजीवा, कोटिज्या, कोटिद्वयम्, कोटिपात्रम्, कोटिपालः, कोटिवर्षम्, कोटिवेधिन्, कोटिश्रीः, कोटिहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटी
कोटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [कुट्-इञ्]<BR>—1 The curved end of a bow; भूमिनिहितैककोटिकार्मुकम् R. 11. 81; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 The end or extremity, edge or point in general; सहचरीं दन्तस्य<BR> कोटया लिखन् Māl. 9. 32; अङ्गदकोटिलग्नम् R. 6. 14, 7. 46, 8. 36.<BR>—3 The edge or point of a weapon.<BR>—4 The highest point, excess, pitch, climax, excellence; परां कोटिमानन्दस्याध्यगच्छन्<BR> K. 369; so कोपकोटिमापन्ना Pt. 4; excessively angry; कल्याणीं कलयामि<BR> कञ्जनिलयां कल्याणकोटिस्थिताम् Viś. Guṇā. 275.<BR>—5 The horns or digits of the moon; आवर्जितजटामौलिविलम्बिशशिकोटयः Ku. 2. 26.<BR>—6 Ten millions, a crore; वित्तस्य विद्यापरिसंख्यया मे कोटीश्चतस्रो<BR> दश चाहरेति R. 5. 21, 12. 82; Ms. 6. 63.<BR>—7 The complement of an arc to 90° (in math.).<BR>—8 The perpendicular side of a right-angled triangle (in math.).<BR>—9 A class, department, kingdom; मनुष्य˚, प्राणि˚ &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">Page0607-2</a>]<BR>—10 One side of a question in dispute, an alternative.<BR>—11 The pinnacle, peak (शिखर); कोटिं तस्य समुद्रस्य काञ्चनीं<BR> शतयोजनाम् Rām. 4. 42. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोटीश्वरः, कोटिजित्, कोटिजीवा, कोटिज्या, कोटिद्वयम्, कोटिपात्रम्, कोटिपालः, कोटिवर्षम्, कोटिवेधिन्, कोटिश्रीः, कोटिहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीश्वरः|कोटीश्वर
कोटिः + -ईश्वरः a millionaire; ततः कोटीश्वराख्येन वणिजा स समं<BR> ययौ Ks. 56. 64; नवनवतिशतद्रव्यकोटीश्वरास्ते नन्दाः … हताः<BR> पश्यतो राक्षसस्य Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिजित्
कोटिः + -जित् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kālidāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिजीवा
कोटिः + -जीवा, -ज्या the cosine of an angle in a right-angled triangle (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिज्या
कोटिः + -जीवा, -ज्या the cosine of an angle in a right-angled triangle (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिद्वयम्
कोटिः + -द्वयम् two alternatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिपात्रम्
कोटिः + -पात्रम् a rudder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिपालः|कोटिपाल
कोटिः + -पालः the guard of a stronghold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिवर्षम्
कोटिः + -वर्षम् N. of the capital of the demon-chief Bāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिवेधिन्
कोटिः + -वेधिन् <i>a.</i> (lit.) striking a point; (fig.) performing the most<BR> difficult things; कोटिवेधिनि सिद्धे हि Rāj. T. 1. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिश्रीः
कोटिः + -श्रीः an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिहोमः|कोटिहोम
कोटिः + -होमः a kind of sacrificial offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिक|कोटिकः
कोटिक <i>a.</i> Forming the highest point of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिमत्|कोटिमन्त्
कोटिमत् <i>a.</i> Edged, pointed; चापेन यस्य विनिवर्तितकर्म जातं<BR> तत्कोटिमत्कुलिशमाभरणं मघोनः Ś. 7. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिशः|कोटिश
कोटिशः <i>ind.</i> By crores, by tens of millions, in innumerable numbers;<BR> गां कोटिशः स्पर्शयता घटोध्नीः R. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिरः|कोटिर
कोटिरः [कोटिं राति रा-क Tv.]<BR>—1 The hair collected on the forehead by ascetics in the shape of a horn.<BR>—2 An ichneumon.<BR>—3 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिशः|कोटिश
कोटि(टी)शः A harrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीशः|कोटीश
कोटि(टी)शः A harrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीरः|कोटीर
कोटीरः [कोटिमीरयति ईर् अण् Tv.]<BR>—1 A diadem, crown; यत्पादाम्बुजचुम्बिनां सुरपतेः कोटीरगारुत्मतस्तोमानां<BR> तुलसीदलप्रकरतः Viś. Guṇā. 260.<BR>—2 A crest.<BR>—3 The hair collected (by ascetics) on the forehead in the shape of a<BR> horn, matted hair in general; कोटीरबन्धनधनुर्गुणयोगपट्टव्यापारपारगममुं<BR> भज भूतभर्तुः N. 11. 18; कठोरे कोटीरे स्खलसि जहि जम्भारिमुकुटम् Ā. L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टः|कोट्ट|कोट्टं
कोट्टः [कुट्ट्-घञ् नि˚ गुणः] A fort, castle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवी
कोट्टवी [कोट्टं वाति वा-क, गौरा˚ ङीष् Tv.] See कोटरी, -वी.<BR>—1 A naked woman with dishevelled hair.<BR>—2 N. of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—3 N. of the mother of Bāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टारः|कोट्टार
कोट्टारः [कुट्ट्-आरक् पृषो˚]<BR>—1 A fortified town, stronghold.<BR>—2 The stairs of a pond.<BR>—3 A well.<BR>—4 A libertine, a dissolute person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोठः|कोठ
कोठः<BR>—1 A variety of leprosy with large round spots.<BR>—2 Ring-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणः|कोण
कोणः [कुण्-करणे घञ् कर्त्तरि अच् वा Tv.]<BR>—1 A corner, an angle (of anything); भयेन कोणे क्वचन स्थितस्य<BR> Vikr. 1. 99; युक्तमेतन्न तु पुनः कोणं नयनपद्मयोः Bv. 2. 173.<BR>—2 An intermediate point of the compass.<BR>—3 The bow of a lute; a fiddle-stick.<BR>—4 The sharp edge of a sword or weapon.<BR>—5 A stick, staff, club.<BR>—6 A drum-stick; … कोणैर्भेर्यो निजघ्निरे Bk. 14. 2.<BR>—7 N. of the planet Mars.<BR>—8 N. of the planet Saturn.<BR>—9 A sort of musical instrument [cf. Gr. <i>gonia</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोणाघातः, कोणकुणः, कोणपारावतम्, कोणवादिन्, कोणवृत्तम्, कोणशङ्कुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणाघातः|कोणाघात
कोणः + -आघातः striking of drums, tabors &c., used in the sense of ‘a mingled sound of various musical instruments’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">Page0608-1</a>]<BR>; कोणाघातेषु गर्जत्प्रलयधनघटान्योन्यसंघट्टचण्डः<BR> Ve. 1. 22. (It is thus defined by Bharata:− ढक्काशतसहस्राणि भेरीशतशतानि<BR> च । एकदा यत्र हन्यन्ते कोणाघातः स उच्यते ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0607-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणकुणः|कोणकुण
कोणः + -कुणः, -पारावतम् (see कपोतपालिका) A dove-cot or doveridge, a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणपारावतम्
कोणः + -कुणः, -पारावतम् (see कपोतपालिका) A dove-cot or doveridge, a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणवादिन्
कोणः + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणवृत्तम्
कोणः + -वृत्तम् a vertical circle extending from north-east to south-west<BR> or from north-west to south-east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणशङ्कुः|कोणशङ्कु
कोणः + -शङ्कुः the sinus of the height of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणपः|कोणप
कोणपः See कौणप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणाकोणि
कोणाकोणि^1 <i>ind.</i> From angle to angle, corner-wise, diagonally.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Must end in short 'i' acc. to Pan. 5.4.127 referenced by PWG and MW..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणि|कोणिः
कोणि <i>a.</i> Having a crooked hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोथ|कोथः
कोथ <i>a.</i> [कुथ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Afflicted with pain.<BR>—2 Churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोथः|कोथ
कोथ + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 Putrefaction, corruption.<BR>—2 A sore.<BR>—3 Gangrene.<BR>—4 A disease of the eyes.<BR>—5 Churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डः|कोदण्ड|कोदंड|कोदंडं|कोदण्डं|कोदंडः
कोदण्डः, -ण्डम्<BR> A bow; रे कन्दर्प करं कदर्थयसि किं कोदण्डटङ्कारवैः<BR> Bh. 3. 100; कोदण्डपाणिनिनदत्प्रतिरोधकानाम् M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डम्
कोदण्डः, -ण्डम्<BR> A bow; रे कन्दर्प करं कदर्थयसि किं कोदण्डटङ्कारवैः<BR> Bh. 3. 100; कोदण्डपाणिनिनदत्प्रतिरोधकानाम् M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डः|कोदण्ड|कोदंड|कोदंडं|कोदण्डं|कोदंडः
कोदण्डः, -ण्डम् + .{@-ण्डः@}<BR>—1 An eye-brow.<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डिन्|कोदंडिन्
कोदण्डिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदारः|कोदार
कोदारः A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोद्रवः|कोद्रव
कोद्रवः A species of grain eaten by the poor; अश्राद्धेयानि धान्यानि<BR> कोद्रवाः पुलकास्तथा Mb. 13. 91. 38; छित्त्वा कर्पूरखण्डान् वृतिमिह<BR> कुरुते कोद्रवाणां समन्तात् Bh. 2. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोनालकः|कोनालक|कोनालकं
कोनालकः, -का, -कम्<BR> A kind of acquatic bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोनालका
कोनालकः, -का, -कम्<BR> A kind of acquatic bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोनालकम्
कोनालकः, -का, -कम्<BR> A kind of acquatic bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोन्वशिरः|कोन्वशिर
कोन्वशिरः A Kṣatriya cursed by a Brāhmaṇa to be a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोप|कोपः
कोप and other derived words see under कुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमल|कोमलं|कोमलः
कोमल <i>a.</i> [कु-कलच् मुट् च नि˚ गुणः; cf Uṇ. 1. 106]<BR>—1 Tender, soft, delicate (fig. also); बन्धुरकोमलाङ्गुलिम् (करम्)<BR> Ś. 6. 13; कोमलविटपानुकारिणौ बाहू 1. 21; संपत्सु महतां चित्तं<BR> भवत्युत्पलकोमलम् Bh. 2. 66.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Soft, low; कोमलं गीतम्.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Agreeable, pleasing, sweet; रे रे कोकिल कोमलैः कलरवैः<BR> किं त्वं वृथा जल्पसि Bh. 3. 100.<BR>—3 Handsome, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलम्
कोमल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Clay, earth.<BR>—3 Silk.<BR>—4 Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमला
कोमल + .{@-ला@} A kind of date; मुकुष्टाः कोमलास्तत्र वारणीयाः प्रयत्नतः<BR> Śālihotra of Bhoja 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलकम्
कोमलकम् The fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमासिका
कोमासिका A small net for fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टिः|कोयष्टि
कोयष्टिः, कोयष्टिकः<BR>—1 The lapwing; काश्मर्याः कृतमालमुद्गतदलं कोयष्टिकष्टीकते Māl. 9. 7;<BR> Ms. 5. 13; Y. 1. 173.<BR>—2 A small white crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टिकः|कोयष्टिक
कोयष्टिः, कोयष्टिकः<BR>—1 The lapwing; काश्मर्याः कृतमालमुद्गतदलं कोयष्टिकष्टीकते Māl. 9. 7;<BR> Ms. 5. 13; Y. 1. 173.<BR>—2 A small white crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरः|कोर
कोरः [कुल् संस्त्याने अच् लस्य-रः Tv.]<BR>—1 A movable joint (as the fingers, the knees &c.).<BR>—2 A bud; cf. कोरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरकः|कोरक|कोरकं
कोरकः, -कम्<BR> [Uṇ. 5. 35]<BR>—1 A bud, an unblown flower; संनद्धं यदपि स्थितं कुरबकं तत्कोरकावस्थया Ś. 6. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">Page0608-2</a>]<BR>—2 (fig.) Anything resembling a bud, <i>i. e.</i> partially opened but not<BR> fully developed; राधायाः स्तनकोरकोपरि चलन्नेत्रो हरिः पातु वः Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 The fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR>—4 A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरकम्
कोरकः, -कम्<BR> [Uṇ. 5. 35]<BR>—1 A bud, an unblown flower; संनद्धं यदपि स्थितं कुरबकं तत्कोरकावस्थया Ś. 6. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">Page0608-2</a>]<BR>—2 (fig.) Anything resembling a bud, <i>i. e.</i> partially opened but not<BR> fully developed; राधायाः स्तनकोरकोपरि चलन्नेत्रो हरिः पातु वः Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 The fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR>—4 A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरकित
कोरकित <i>a.</i> Covered with buds; स्मितेन यः कोरकितस्तवास्ते N. 3. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरित
कोरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Budded, sprouted.<BR>—2 Ground, pounded, reduced to small particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरण्डः
कोरण्डः N. of a plant (probably Mar. कोरांटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरदूषः|कोरदूष
कोरदूषः = कोद्रवः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलः|कोल|कोलं
कोलः [कुल् संस्त्याने अच्]<BR>—1 A hog, boar; Y. 3. 273; Śi. 14. 43, 86.<BR>—2 A raft, boat.<BR>—3 The breast.<BR>—4 The haunch, hip, lap.<BR>—5 An embrace.<BR>—6 The planet Saturn.<BR>—7 An out-cast, one of a degraded tribe.<BR>—8 A barbarian.<BR>—9 N. of a tribe inhabiting the hills in Central India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलम्
कोलः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 The weight of one Tola.<BR>—2 Black pepper.<BR>—3 A kind of berry.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोलाञ्चः, कोलपुच्छः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाञ्चः|कोलाञ्च|कोलांच
कोलः + -अञ्चः N. of the country of the Kaliṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलपुच्छः|कोलपुच्छ
कोलः + -पुच्छः a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलकम्
कोलकम्<BR>—1 A kind of village; Māna. 9. 486.<BR>—2 A kind of fort; Māna. 10. 41.<BR>—3 Some fruit or material employed in the foundation-pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलकुणः|कोलकुण
कोलकुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलम्बकः|कोलम्बक|कोलंबक|कोलंबकः
कोलम्बकः The body of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोला
कोला, -लिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> See बदरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलिः|कोलि
कोला, -लिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> See बदरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोली
कोला, -लिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> See बदरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाहलः|कोलाहल|कोलाहलं
कोलाहलः, -लम्<BR> A loud and confused noise, an uproar; ततो हलहलाशब्दः<BR> पुनः कोलाहलोऽभवत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाहलम्
कोलाहलः, -लम्<BR> A loud and confused noise, an uproar; ततो हलहलाशब्दः<BR> पुनः कोलाहलोऽभवत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल्या
कोल्या Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविद|कोविदः
कोविद <i>a.</i> Experienced, learned, skilled, wise, proficient (with<BR> gen. or loc. but usually in comp.); व्युत्पत्तिरावर्जितकोविदापि Vikr. 1. 16;<BR> गुणदोषकोविदः Śi. 14. 54, 69; प्राप्यावन्तीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान्<BR> Me. 30; Ms. 7. 26; स्फुटचतुरकथा˚ Mu. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविदारः|कोविदार|कोविदारं
कोविदारः, -रम्<BR> N. of a tree; चित्तं विदारयति कस्य न कोविदारः Ṛs. 3. 6; U. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविदारम्
कोविदारः, -रम्<BR> N. of a tree; चित्तं विदारयति कस्य न कोविदारः Ṛs. 3. 6; U. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशः|कोश|कोशं
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्)<BR> [कुश्(ष्)आधारादौ घञ् कर्तरि अच् वा Tv.]<BR>—1 A vessel for holding liquids, a pail.<BR>—2 A bucket, cup.<BR>—3 A vessel in general.<BR>—4 A box, cupboard, drawer, trunk; Rv. 6. 47. 23; स एष कोशो वसुधानस्तस्मिन्विश्वमिदं<BR> श्रितम् Ch. Up. 3. 15. 1.<BR>—5 A sheath, scabbard; Ki. 17. 45.<BR>—6 A case, cover, covering.<BR>—7 A store, mass; ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां धर्मकोशस्य गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR>—8 A store-room.<BR>—9 A treasury, an apartment where money is kept; Ms. 8. 419.<BR>—10 Treasure, money, wealth; निःशेषविश्राणितकोषजातम् R. 5. 1; (fig.<BR> also); कोशस्तपसः K. 45; कोशपूर्वाः सर्वारम्भाः Kau. A. 2. 8.<BR>—11 Gold or silver wrought or unwrought.<BR>—12 A dictionary, lexicon, vocabulary.<BR>—13 A closed flower, bud; सुजातयोः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">Page0609-1</a>]<BR> पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8, 13. 29; इत्थं विचिन्तयति कोशगते<BR> द्विरेफे हा हन्त हन्त नलिनीं गज उज्जहार Subhāṣ.<BR>—14 The stone of a fruit.<BR>—15 A pod.<BR>—16 A nut-meg, nut-shell.<BR>—17 The cocoon of a silk-worm; निजलालासमायोगात्कोशं वा कोशकारकः Y. 3. 147.<BR>—18 Vulva, the womb.<BR>—19 An egg.<BR>—20 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>—21 The penis.<BR>—22 A ball, globe.<BR>—23 (In Vedānta phil.) A term for the five (अन्न, प्राण, मनः, विज्ञान,<BR> आनन्द) vestures (sheaths or cases) which successively make the body,<BR> enshrining the soul.<BR>—24 (In law) A kind of ordeal; the defendant drinks thrice of the water<BR> after some idol has been washed in it; cf. Y. 2. 112.<BR>—25 A house.<BR>—26 A cloud.<BR>—27 The interior of a carriage.<BR>—28 A kind of bandage or ligature (in surgery).<BR>—29 An oath; कोशं चक्रतुरन्योन्यं सखड्गौ नृपडामरौ Rāj. T. 5. 326.<BR>—30 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—31 A piece of meat.<BR>—32 A cup used in the ratification of a treaty of peace; देवी कोशमपाययत्<BR> Rāj. T. 7. 8, 75, 459, 492.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोशाधिपतिः, कोशाध्यक्षः, कोशागारः, कोशागारम्, कोशकारः, कोशकारकः, कोशकृत्, कोशगृहम्, कोशग्रहणम्, कोशचञ्चुः, कोशनायकः, कोशपालः, कोशपेटकः, कोशकम्, कोशफलम्, कोशवारि, कोशवासिन्, कोशवृद्धिः, कोशवेश्मन्, कोशशायिका, कोशशुद्धिः, कोशस्कृ, कोशस्थ, कोशहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशम्
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्)<BR> [कुश्(ष्)आधारादौ घञ् कर्तरि अच् वा Tv.]<BR>—1 A vessel for holding liquids, a pail.<BR>—2 A bucket, cup.<BR>—3 A vessel in general.<BR>—4 A box, cupboard, drawer, trunk; Rv. 6. 47. 23; स एष कोशो वसुधानस्तस्मिन्विश्वमिदं<BR> श्रितम् Ch. Up. 3. 15. 1.<BR>—5 A sheath, scabbard; Ki. 17. 45.<BR>—6 A case, cover, covering.<BR>—7 A store, mass; ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां धर्मकोशस्य गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR>—8 A store-room.<BR>—9 A treasury, an apartment where money is kept; Ms. 8. 419.<BR>—10 Treasure, money, wealth; निःशेषविश्राणितकोषजातम् R. 5. 1; (fig.<BR> also); कोशस्तपसः K. 45; कोशपूर्वाः सर्वारम्भाः Kau. A. 2. 8.<BR>—11 Gold or silver wrought or unwrought.<BR>—12 A dictionary, lexicon, vocabulary.<BR>—13 A closed flower, bud; सुजातयोः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">Page0609-1</a>]<BR> पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8, 13. 29; इत्थं विचिन्तयति कोशगते<BR> द्विरेफे हा हन्त हन्त नलिनीं गज उज्जहार Subhāṣ.<BR>—14 The stone of a fruit.<BR>—15 A pod.<BR>—16 A nut-meg, nut-shell.<BR>—17 The cocoon of a silk-worm; निजलालासमायोगात्कोशं वा कोशकारकः Y. 3. 147.<BR>—18 Vulva, the womb.<BR>—19 An egg.<BR>—20 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>—21 The penis.<BR>—22 A ball, globe.<BR>—23 (In Vedānta phil.) A term for the five (अन्न, प्राण, मनः, विज्ञान,<BR> आनन्द) vestures (sheaths or cases) which successively make the body,<BR> enshrining the soul.<BR>—24 (In law) A kind of ordeal; the defendant drinks thrice of the water<BR> after some idol has been washed in it; cf. Y. 2. 112.<BR>—25 A house.<BR>—26 A cloud.<BR>—27 The interior of a carriage.<BR>—28 A kind of bandage or ligature (in surgery).<BR>—29 An oath; कोशं चक्रतुरन्योन्यं सखड्गौ नृपडामरौ Rāj. T. 5. 326.<BR>—30 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—31 A piece of meat.<BR>—32 A cup used in the ratification of a treaty of peace; देवी कोशमपाययत्<BR> Rāj. T. 7. 8, 75, 459, 492.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोशाधिपतिः, कोशाध्यक्षः, कोशागारः, कोशागारम्, कोशकारः, कोशकारकः, कोशकृत्, कोशगृहम्, कोशग्रहणम्, कोशचञ्चुः, कोशनायकः, कोशपालः, कोशपेटकः, कोशकम्, कोशफलम्, कोशवारि, कोशवासिन्, कोशवृद्धिः, कोशवेश्मन्, कोशशायिका, कोशशुद्धिः, कोशस्कृ, कोशस्थ, कोशहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषः|कोष|कोषं
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्)<BR> [कुश्(ष्)आधारादौ घञ् कर्तरि अच् वा Tv.]<BR>—1 A vessel for holding liquids, a pail.<BR>—2 A bucket, cup.<BR>—3 A vessel in general.<BR>—4 A box, cupboard, drawer, trunk; Rv. 6. 47. 23; स एष कोशो वसुधानस्तस्मिन्विश्वमिदं<BR> श्रितम् Ch. Up. 3. 15. 1.<BR>—5 A sheath, scabbard; Ki. 17. 45.<BR>—6 A case, cover, covering.<BR>—7 A store, mass; ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां धर्मकोशस्य गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR>—8 A store-room.<BR>—9 A treasury, an apartment where money is kept; Ms. 8. 419.<BR>—10 Treasure, money, wealth; निःशेषविश्राणितकोषजातम् R. 5. 1; (fig.<BR> also); कोशस्तपसः K. 45; कोशपूर्वाः सर्वारम्भाः Kau. A. 2. 8.<BR>—11 Gold or silver wrought or unwrought.<BR>—12 A dictionary, lexicon, vocabulary.<BR>—13 A closed flower, bud; सुजातयोः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">Page0609-1</a>]<BR> पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8, 13. 29; इत्थं विचिन्तयति कोशगते<BR> द्विरेफे हा हन्त हन्त नलिनीं गज उज्जहार Subhāṣ.<BR>—14 The stone of a fruit.<BR>—15 A pod.<BR>—16 A nut-meg, nut-shell.<BR>—17 The cocoon of a silk-worm; निजलालासमायोगात्कोशं वा कोशकारकः Y. 3. 147.<BR>—18 Vulva, the womb.<BR>—19 An egg.<BR>—20 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>—21 The penis.<BR>—22 A ball, globe.<BR>—23 (In Vedānta phil.) A term for the five (अन्न, प्राण, मनः, विज्ञान,<BR> आनन्द) vestures (sheaths or cases) which successively make the body,<BR> enshrining the soul.<BR>—24 (In law) A kind of ordeal; the defendant drinks thrice of the water<BR> after some idol has been washed in it; cf. Y. 2. 112.<BR>—25 A house.<BR>—26 A cloud.<BR>—27 The interior of a carriage.<BR>—28 A kind of bandage or ligature (in surgery).<BR>—29 An oath; कोशं चक्रतुरन्योन्यं सखड्गौ नृपडामरौ Rāj. T. 5. 326.<BR>—30 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—31 A piece of meat.<BR>—32 A cup used in the ratification of a treaty of peace; देवी कोशमपाययत्<BR> Rāj. T. 7. 8, 75, 459, 492.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोशाधिपतिः, कोशाध्यक्षः, कोशागारः, कोशागारम्, कोशकारः, कोशकारकः, कोशकृत्, कोशगृहम्, कोशग्रहणम्, कोशचञ्चुः, कोशनायकः, कोशपालः, कोशपेटकः, कोशकम्, कोशफलम्, कोशवारि, कोशवासिन्, कोशवृद्धिः, कोशवेश्मन्, कोशशायिका, कोशशुद्धिः, कोशस्कृ, कोशस्थ, कोशहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषम्
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्)<BR> [कुश्(ष्)आधारादौ घञ् कर्तरि अच् वा Tv.]<BR>—1 A vessel for holding liquids, a pail.<BR>—2 A bucket, cup.<BR>—3 A vessel in general.<BR>—4 A box, cupboard, drawer, trunk; Rv. 6. 47. 23; स एष कोशो वसुधानस्तस्मिन्विश्वमिदं<BR> श्रितम् Ch. Up. 3. 15. 1.<BR>—5 A sheath, scabbard; Ki. 17. 45.<BR>—6 A case, cover, covering.<BR>—7 A store, mass; ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां धर्मकोशस्य गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR>—8 A store-room.<BR>—9 A treasury, an apartment where money is kept; Ms. 8. 419.<BR>—10 Treasure, money, wealth; निःशेषविश्राणितकोषजातम् R. 5. 1; (fig.<BR> also); कोशस्तपसः K. 45; कोशपूर्वाः सर्वारम्भाः Kau. A. 2. 8.<BR>—11 Gold or silver wrought or unwrought.<BR>—12 A dictionary, lexicon, vocabulary.<BR>—13 A closed flower, bud; सुजातयोः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">Page0609-1</a>]<BR> पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8, 13. 29; इत्थं विचिन्तयति कोशगते<BR> द्विरेफे हा हन्त हन्त नलिनीं गज उज्जहार Subhāṣ.<BR>—14 The stone of a fruit.<BR>—15 A pod.<BR>—16 A nut-meg, nut-shell.<BR>—17 The cocoon of a silk-worm; निजलालासमायोगात्कोशं वा कोशकारकः Y. 3. 147.<BR>—18 Vulva, the womb.<BR>—19 An egg.<BR>—20 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>—21 The penis.<BR>—22 A ball, globe.<BR>—23 (In Vedānta phil.) A term for the five (अन्न, प्राण, मनः, विज्ञान,<BR> आनन्द) vestures (sheaths or cases) which successively make the body,<BR> enshrining the soul.<BR>—24 (In law) A kind of ordeal; the defendant drinks thrice of the water<BR> after some idol has been washed in it; cf. Y. 2. 112.<BR>—25 A house.<BR>—26 A cloud.<BR>—27 The interior of a carriage.<BR>—28 A kind of bandage or ligature (in surgery).<BR>—29 An oath; कोशं चक्रतुरन्योन्यं सखड्गौ नृपडामरौ Rāj. T. 5. 326.<BR>—30 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—31 A piece of meat.<BR>—32 A cup used in the ratification of a treaty of peace; देवी कोशमपाययत्<BR> Rāj. T. 7. 8, 75, 459, 492.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोशाधिपतिः, कोशाध्यक्षः, कोशागारः, कोशागारम्, कोशकारः, कोशकारकः, कोशकृत्, कोशगृहम्, कोशग्रहणम्, कोशचञ्चुः, कोशनायकः, कोशपालः, कोशपेटकः, कोशकम्, कोशफलम्, कोशवारि, कोशवासिन्, कोशवृद्धिः, कोशवेश्मन्, कोशशायिका, कोशशुद्धिः, कोशस्कृ, कोशस्थ, कोशहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशी
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्) + .{@-शी@} + ({@-षी@})<BR>—1 A bud.<BR>—2 A seed-vessel.<BR>—3 The beard of corn. —4 A shoe, sandal (पादुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषी
कोशः, -शम् (षः, -षम्) + .{@-शी@} + ({@-षी@})<BR>—1 A bud.<BR>—2 A seed-vessel.<BR>—3 The beard of corn. —4 A shoe, sandal (पादुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0608-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशाधिपतिः|कोशाधिपति
कोशः + -अधिपतिः, -अध्यक्षः a treasure, paymaster; (cf. the modern ‘minister of finance’).<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशाध्यक्षः|कोशाध्यक्ष
कोशः + -अधिपतिः, -अध्यक्षः a treasure, paymaster; (cf. the modern ‘minister of finance’).<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशागारः|कोशागार
कोशः + -अगारः, -अगारम् a treasurer, store-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशागारम्
कोशः + -अगारः, -अगारम् a treasurer, store-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकारः|कोशकार
कोशः + -कारः<BR>—1 one who makes scabbards.<BR>—2 a lexicographer.<BR>—3 the silk-worm while in the cocoon; भूमिं च कोशकाराणाम् Rām. 4. 40. 23.<BR>—4 a chrysalis.<BR>—5 sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकारकः|कोशकारक
कोशः + -कारकः a silk-worm. Y. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकृत्
कोशः + -कृत् <i>m.</i> a kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशगृहम्
कोशः + -गृहम् a treasury, store-room; R. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशग्रहणम्
कोशः + -ग्रहणम् undergoing an ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशचञ्चुः|कोशचञ्चु|कोशचंचु
कोशः + -चञ्चुः the (Indian) crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशनायकः|कोशनायक
कोशः + -नायकः, -पालः<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 An epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशपालः|कोशपाल
कोशः + -नायकः, -पालः<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 An epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशपेटकः|कोशपेटक
कोशः + -पेटकः, -कम् a chest in which treasure is kept, coffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकम्
कोशः + -पेटकः, -कम् a chest in which treasure is kept, coffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशफलम्
कोशः + -फलम्<BR>—1 a kind of perfume.<BR>—2 a nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवारि
कोशः + -वारि water used at an ordeal; Ks. 119. 35, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवासिन्
कोशः + -वासिन् <i>m.</i> an animal living in a shell, a chrysalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवृद्धिः|कोशवृद्धि
कोशः + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 increase of treasure.<BR>—2 enlargement of the scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवेश्मन्
कोशः + -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a treasury; भाण्डं च स्थापयामास तदीये कोषवेश्मनि Ks. 24. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशशायिका
कोशः + -शायिका a clasped knife, knife lying in a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशशुद्धिः|कोशशुद्धि
कोशः + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purification by ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशस्कृ
कोशः + -स्कृ <i>m.</i> a silk-worm; त्यजेत कोशस्कृदिवेहमानः Bhāg. 7. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशस्थ|कोशस्थः
कोशः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> incased, sheathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशस्थः|कोशस्थ
कोशः + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः@}) an animal living in a shell (as a snail).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशहीन
कोशः + -हीन <i>a.</i> deprived of riches, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकः|कोशक
कोशकः<BR>—1 An egg.<BR>—2 A testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशिका
कोशिका A drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशिन्
कोशि(षि)न्^1 <i>m.</i> The mango tree.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषिन्
कोशि(षि)न्^1 <i>m.</i> The mango tree.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलिकम्
कोशलिकम् A bribe (= कौशलिक q. v. which is the more correct form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकः|कोशातक
कोशा(षा)तकः Hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषातकः|कोषातक
कोशा(षा)तकः Hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकिन्
कोशातकिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Trade, business.<BR>—2 A trader, merchant.<BR>—3 Submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकी
कोशातकी N. of a tree (पटोलि); Śi. 12. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ|कोष्ठः
कोष्ठ <i>a.</i> [कुष्-थन् Uṇ. 2. 4] Own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठः|कोष्ठ
कोष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@}<BR>—1 Any one of the viscera of the body, such as the heart, lungs &c.<BR>—2 The belly, abdomen; आकोष्ठं ज्यां समुत्कृष्य Bhāg. 10. 83. 22.<BR>—3 An inner apartment.<BR>—4 A granary, storeroom; कन्दुः कोष्ठः कुशूलः Mbh. on P. I. 2. 45 etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठम्
कोष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@}<BR>—1 A surrounding wall; Bhāg. 4. 28. 56.<BR>—2 The shell of anything.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कोष्ठागारम्, कोष्ठागारिकाः, कोष्ठाग्निः, कोष्ठपालः, कोष्ठशुद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठागारम्
कोष्ठ + -अगारम्<BR>—1 a storehouse, store room; पर्याप्तभरितकोष्ठागारं मांसशोणितैर्मे<BR> गृहं भविष्यति Ve. 3; Ms. 9. 280.<BR>—2 a treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठागारिकाः
कोष्ठ + -अगारिकाः<BR>—1 an animal living in a shell.<BR>—2 the manager of a store-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठाग्निः|कोष्ठाग्नि
कोष्ठ + -अग्निः the digestive faculty, gastric juice; कोष्ठाग्निर्नाम अशितपीतलेह्यचोष्यं<BR> पचतीति Garbha. Up. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठपालः|कोष्ठपाल
कोष्ठ + -पालः<BR>—1 a treasurer, store-keeper.<BR>—2 a guard, watch.<BR>—3 a constable (resembling the modern municipal officer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठशुद्धिः|कोष्ठशुद्धि
कोष्ठ + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> evacuation of the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठकः|कोष्ठक
कोष्ठकः<BR>—1 A granary.<BR>—2 A surrounding wall.<BR>—3 An apartment; Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठकम्
कोष्ठकः + .{@-कम्@} A brick trough for watering cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठकीकृ
कोष्ठकीकृ €8 U. To surround, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठीकृ
कोष्ठीकृ To surround, enclose; कोष्ठीकृत्य च तं वीरम् Mb. 6. 101. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ्य
कोष्ठ्य <i>a.</i> [कोष्ठ-य] Proceeding from the chest (as a sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ण|कोष्णं
कोष्ण <i>a.</i> [ईषदुष्ण; कोः कादेशः] Luke-warm, tepid; भुवं<BR> कोष्णेन कुण्डोध्नी मेध्येनावभृथादपि R. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्णम्
कोष्ण + .{@-ष्णम्@} Warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोसलः|कोसल
कोस(श)लः (pl.) N. of a country and its people; पितुरनन्तरमुत्तरकोसलान्<BR> R. 9. 1, 3. 5, 6. 71; मगधकोसलकेकयशासिनां दुहितरः 9. 17.<BR> ˚नक्षत्र N. of a lunar mansion; कोसलानां च नक्षत्रं व्यक्तमिन्द्राग्निदैवतम्<BR> Rām. 6. 102. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलः|कोशल
कोस(श)लः (pl.) N. of a country and its people; पितुरनन्तरमुत्तरकोसलान्<BR> R. 9. 1, 3. 5, 6. 71; मगधकोसलकेकयशासिनां दुहितरः 9. 17.<BR> ˚नक्षत्र N. of a lunar mansion; कोसलानां च नक्षत्रं व्यक्तमिन्द्राग्निदैवतम्<BR> Rām. 6. 102. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोसला
कोस(श)ला The city of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशला
कोस(श)ला The city of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहल|कोहलः
कोहल <i>a.</i> [कौ हलति स्पर्धते अच् पृषो˚ Tv.] Speaking indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहलः|कोहल
कोहल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>—2 A sort of spirituous liquor.<BR>—3 The inventor or first teacher of the drama.<BR>—4 N. of a Prākṛt grammarian (v. l. कोहर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकृत्यम्
कौकृत्यम्<BR>—1 Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>—2 Repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुट
कौकृत्यम् + .{@-कौक्कुट@} <i>a.</i> [कुक्कुट-अण्] Relating to a cock; Rām. 2. 91. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिकः|कौक्कुटिक
कौक्कुटिकः [कुक्कुट-ठक्]<BR>—1 A poulterer.<BR>—2 A mendicant who walks always fixing his eyes on the ground for fear<BR> of treading upon worms, insects &c.<BR>—3 (Hence) A hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्ष
कौक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Tied to, or being on the sides.<BR>—2 Abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेय
कौक्षेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) [कुक्षि-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Being in the belly.<BR>—2 Being in a sheath; असिं कौक्षेयमुद्यम्य चकारापनसं मुखम् Bk. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0609-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेयकः|कौक्षेयक
कौक्षेयकः [कुक्षौ बद्धोऽसिः ढकञ् cf. P. IV. 2. 96.] A sword,<BR> scimitar; वामपार्श्वावलम्बिना कौक्षेयकेण K. 8; Vikr. 1. 90; आधावन्तः<BR> संमुखं धारितानामन्यैरन्ये तीक्ष्णकौक्षेयकाणाम् Śi. 18. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्कः|कौङ्क|कौंक|कौंकः
कौङ्कः, कौङ्कणः (pl.) N. of a country and its people or<BR> rulers; Mb. 6. 9. 60; (see कोङ्कण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्कणः|कौङ्कण|कौंकण|कौंकणः
कौङ्कः, कौङ्कणः (pl.) N. of a country and its people or<BR> rulers; Mb. 6. 9. 60; (see कोङ्कण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्कुम
कौङ्कुम <i>a.</i> of saffron. … दवदहनः कौंङ्कुमो दिग्वधूनां … …<BR> अङ्गरागः Sūkti. 5. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौचपक
कौचपक <i>a.</i> A variety of carpets; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौचुमार
कौचुमार, -योगः<BR> A particular art (कला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौचुमारयोगः|कौचुमारयोग
कौचुमार, -योगः<BR> A particular art (कला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौज
कौज <i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्जर|कौंजर
कौञ्जर <i>a.</i> Belonging to an elephant; आपन्नः कौञ्जरीं योनिम्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्जरम्
कौञ्जर + .{@-रम्@} A particular method of sitting (of yogi); सर्वाण्येवापिधीयन्ते<BR> पदजातानि कौञ्जरे Mb. 12. 245. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौट|कौटः
कौट <i>a.</i> (-टी <i>f.</i>) [कूट-अञ्]<BR>—1 Living in oneʼs own house; hence, independent, free.<BR>—2 Domestic, homely, home-bred.<BR>—3 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>—4 Snared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटः|कौट
कौट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 Fraud, falsehood.<BR>—2 Giving false evidence.<BR>—3 A variety of gems; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौटजः, कौटतक्षः, कौटसाक्षिन्, कौटसाक्ष्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटजः|कौटज
कौट + -जः the Kuṭaja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटतक्षः|कौटतक्ष
कौट + -तक्षः (opp. ग्रामतक्षः) an independent carpenter, one who<BR> works at home on his own account and not for the village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्षिन्
कौट + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a false witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्ष्यम्
कौट + -साक्ष्यम् false evidence, perjury; Ms. 8. 117, 122-23, 11. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटकिकः|कौटकिक
कौटकिकः, कौटिकः<BR>—1 One whose business is to catch birds &c. in traps.<BR>—2 One who sells the flesh of birds, animals &c.; a butcher, poacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिकः|कौटिक
कौटकिकः, कौटिकः<BR>—1 One whose business is to catch birds &c. in traps.<BR>—2 One who sells the flesh of birds, animals &c.; a butcher, poacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिक|कौटिकः
कौटिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to a snare or trap.<BR>—2 Dishonest, fraudulent; see कौटकिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटभी
कौटभी An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटल्य|कौटल्यः
कौटल्य = कौटिल्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटवी
कौटवी A naked woman; cf. कोट्टवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिलिकः|कौटिलिक
कौटिलिकः<BR>—1 A hunter.<BR>—2 A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्यम्
कौटिल्यम् [cf. नित्यं कौटिल्ये गतौ P. III. 1. 23.]<BR>—1 Crookedness (lit. and fig.); कौटिल्यं कचनिचये करचरणाधरतलेषु<BR> रागस्ते K. P.<BR>—2 Wickedness.<BR>—3 dishonesty, fraud; यो मित्राणि करोत्यत्र न कौटिल्येन वर्तते Pt. 2. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्यः|कौटिल्य|कौटिल्यं
कौटिल्यम् + .{@-ल्यः@} ‘The crooked’, N. of Cāṇakya, a celebrated writer on<BR> civil polity, (the work being known as चाणक्यनीति), the friend and<BR> adviser of Chandragupta and a very important character in the Mudrārākṣasa;<BR> कौटिल्यः कुटिलमतिः स एष येन क्रोधाग्नौ प्रसभमदाहि नन्दवंशः<BR> Mu. 1. 7; स्पृशति मां भृत्यभावेन कौटिल्यशिष्यः Mu. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्यशास्त्रम्
कौटिल्यम् + .{@-शास्त्रम्@} Cāṇakyaʼs doctrine (diplomacy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटीर
कौटीर <i>a.</i> Belonging to the plant कुटीर or made of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटीर्या
कौटीर्या An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्ब|कौटुंब
कौटुम्ब <i>a.</i> (-बी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कुटुम्बं तद्भरणं प्रयोजनमस्य अण्] Necessary<BR> for the family or household.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्बम्
कौटुम्ब + .{@-बम्@} Family relationship; Rāj. T. 5. 396.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्बिक|कौटुंबिक|कौटुम्बिकः
कौटुम्बिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [कुटुम्बे तद्भरणे प्रसृतः<BR> ठक्] Constituting a family; अथ च कौटुम्बिका दारापत्यादयः Bhāg. 5. 14. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्बिकः|कौटुम्बिक|कौटुंबिक
कौटुम्बिक + .{@-कः@} The father or master of a family; <i>pater-familias</i>;<BR> पदेपदेऽभ्यन्तरवह्निनार्दितः कौटुम्बिकः क्रुध्यति वै जनाय Bhāg. 5. 13. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौट्टन्यम्
कौट्टन्यम् The procuring of women for immoral purposes; शनैर्लेभे<BR> स वात्सल्यं कौट्टन्यान्नवभूपतेः Rāj. T. 7. 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपः|कौणप
कौणपः A goblin, demon; Mb. 1. 170. 15; Māl. 5. साहसी शोणतनयः<BR> कोपी कोणपविक्रमः Śiva B. 22. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौणपदन्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपदन्तः|कौणपदन्त|कौणपदंत
कौणपः + -दन्तः an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपदन्तः|कौणपदन्त|कौणपदंत
कौणपदन्तः N. of an author on अर्थशास्त्र mentioned by Kauṭilya<BR> in connection with राजपुत्ररक्षण; Kau. A. 1. 17<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्डिन्यः|कौण्डिन्य
कौण्डिन्यः N. of a sage cf. तक्रकौण्डिन्यन्याय Appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्यम्
कौण्यम् Distortion or paralysis of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकम्
कौतुकम् [कुतुकस्य भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Desire, curiosity, wish.<BR>—2 Eagerness, vehemence, impatience.<BR>—3 Anything creating curiosity or wonder.<BR>—4 The marriage thread (worn on the wrist); करोयमामुक्तविवाहकौतुकः<BR> Ku. 5. 66; R. 8. 1.<BR>—5 The ceremony with the marriage thread preceding a marriage; सबाष्पा<BR> कौतुकक्रिया Pratijñā. 4. 24.<BR>—6 Festivity, gaiety.<BR>—7 Particularly auspicious festivity, solemn occasion (such as marriage);<BR> ‘कौतुकं मङ्गले हर्षे हस्तसूत्रे कुतूहले’ इति शाश्वतः; प्रस्थान˚<BR> Ś. 4; Ku. 7. 25.<BR>—8 Delight, joy, pleasure, happiness; निवृत्तनानारसकाव्यकौतुकम्<BR> Bh. 3. 140; ˚रसाः U. 6. 33; Māl. 10. 3; U. 3. 37.<BR>—9 Sport, pastime.<BR>—10 A song, dance, show or spectacle.<BR>—11 Joke, mirth.<BR>—12 Friendly greeting, salutation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौतुकागारः, कौतुकागारम्, कौतुकगृहम्, कौतुकोदयम्, कौतुकक्रिया, कौतुकमङ्गलम्, कौतुकतोरणः, कौतुकतोरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकागारः|कौतुकागार
कौतुकम् + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -गृहम् a pleasure-house; कौतुकागारमागात् Ku. 7. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकागारम्
कौतुकम् + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -गृहम् a pleasure-house; कौतुकागारमागात् Ku. 7. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकगृहम्
कौतुकम् + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -गृहम् a pleasure-house; कौतुकागारमागात् Ku. 7. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकोदयम्
कौतुकम् + -उदयम् a kind of the height (of an idol &c.) (cf. उत्सव<BR> and उत्सेध); उत्सवे चार्धमानेन कौतुकोदयमीरितम् Māna. 61. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकक्रिया
कौतुकम् + -क्रिया, -मङ्गलम्<BR>—1 A solemn ceremony; उपवासैस्तिथेज्याभिर्व्रतकौतुकमङ्गले । लभन्ते<BR> मातरो गर्भान् … Mb. 12. 7. 14;<BR>—2 particularly marriage ceremony; R. 11. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकमङ्गलम्
कौतुकम् + -क्रिया, -मङ्गलम्<BR>—1 A solemn ceremony; उपवासैस्तिथेज्याभिर्व्रतकौतुकमङ्गले । लभन्ते<BR> मातरो गर्भान् … Mb. 12. 7. 14;<BR>—2 particularly marriage ceremony; R. 11. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकतोरणः|कौतुकतोरण
कौतुकम् + -तोरणः, -तोरणम् a triumphal arch erected on festive occasions;<BR> गोपुरद्वारमार्गेषु कृतकौतुकतोरणाम् Bhāg. 1. 11. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकतोरणम्
कौतुकम् + -तोरणः, -तोरणम् a triumphal arch erected on festive occasions;<BR> गोपुरद्वारमार्गेषु कृतकौतुकतोरणाम् Bhāg. 1. 11. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकवत्|कौतुकवन्त्
कौतुकवत् <i>ind.</i> Through curiosity or interest; सुरैः कौतुकवत्पृष्टः Bm. 1. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकित
कौतुकित <i>a.</i> Eager, eagerly interested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकिता
कौतुकित + .{@-ता@} curiosity, eagerness; दूरमालपनकौतुकितायाम् N. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकिन्
कौतुकिन् <i>a.</i> Festive, gay; विजहार तदुद्यानवनभूमिषु कौतुकी Ks. 54. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहलम्
कौतूहलम्(ल्यम्) [कुतूहल-अण्]<BR>—1 Desire, curiosity, interest; विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 9; Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Eagerness, vehement or eager desire; कौतूहलानुप्रवणा (कथा)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">Page0611-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 12. 37. 3.<BR>—3 Anything exciting curiosity, a wonder, curiosity; Me. 49.<BR>—4 A solemn ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहल्यम्
कौतूहलम्(ल्यम्) [कुतूहल-अण्]<BR>—1 Desire, curiosity, interest; विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 9; Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Eagerness, vehement or eager desire; कौतूहलानुप्रवणा (कथा)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">Page0611-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 12. 37. 3.<BR>—3 Anything exciting curiosity, a wonder, curiosity; Me. 49.<BR>—4 A solemn ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0610-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौत्सम्
कौत्सम् A Sāman composed by Kutsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौत्सः|कौत्स|कौत्सं
कौत्सम् + .{@-त्सः@}<BR>—1 N. of a sage; माण्डव्यः कौत्सात् Bṛ. Up. 6. 5. 4; उपसेदित्वात्<BR> कौत्सः पाणिनिम् Mbh. on P. III. 2. 108.<BR>—2 N. of a pupil of Varatantu; R. 5. 1.<BR>—3 N. of a degraded family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौथुमः|कौथुम
कौथुमः<BR>—1 N. of a Vedic Śākhā.<BR>—2 N. of a Brāhmaṇa who belongs to this Śākhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौदालिकः|कौदालिक
कौदालिकः A man of a mixed caste, a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रविकम्
कौद्रविकम् Sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्यम्
कौनख्यम्<BR>—1 Ugliness of nails.<BR>—2 The condition of one who has a disease of the nails; सुवर्णचौरः<BR> कौनख्यम् Ms. 11. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तिकः|कौन्तिक|कौंतिक|कौंतिकः
कौन्तिकः [कुन्तः प्रहरणमस्य ठञ्] A spearman, lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तेयः|कौन्तेय|कौंतेय|कौंतेयः
कौन्तेयः [कुन्त्याः अपत्यं ढक्] ‘Son of Kunti’, an epithet of<BR> Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma or Arjuna. Bg. 1. 27, 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप|कौपं
कौप <i>a.</i> (-पी <i>f.</i>) [कूप-अण्] Relating to or coming<BR> from a well (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपम्
कौप + .{@-पम्@} Well-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपीनम्
कौपीनम् [कूप-खञ्; see Sk. on शालीनकौपीने अधृष्टाकार्ययोः P. V. 2. 20]<BR>—1 The pudenda.<BR>—2 A privity, privy part.<BR>—3 A small piece of cloth (usually a small strip worn over the privities;<BR> कौपीनं शतखण्डजर्जरतरं कन्था पुनस्तादृशी Bh. 3. 101.)<BR>—4 (Hence sometimes) A ragged or tattered garment.<BR>—5 Sin, an improper or wrong act; नाच्छादयति कौपीनं न दंशमशकापहम् Pt. 3. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपोदकी
कौपोदकी The mace of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौबेर
कौबेर <i>a.</i> See कौवेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौब्ज्यम्
कौब्ज्यम् [कुब्ज-ष्यञ् P. V. 1. 124]<BR>—1 Crookedness.<BR>—2 Hump-backedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमार|कौमारं
कौमार <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) [कुमार-अण्]<BR>—1 Juvenile, youthful, virgin, maidenly (of men and women); कौमारः<BR> पतिः a man who marries a virgin; कौमारी भार्या a virgin wife; cf.<BR> Mbh. on P. IV. 2. 13.<BR>—2 Soft, tender.<BR>—3 Belonging to the god of war; Māl. 1. 1.<BR>—4 Of principal incarnation; स एव प्रथमं देवः कौमारं सर्गमास्थितः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारी
कौमार + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 The wife of one who has not married another wife.<BR>—2 The Śakti (power) of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारम्
कौमार + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Childhood (to the age of five).<BR>—2 Maidenhood (to the age of sixteen), virginity; पिता रक्षति कौमारे<BR> भर्ता रक्षति यौवने Ms. 9. 3; देहिनोऽस्मिन् यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं<BR> जरा Bg. 2. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौमारचारिन्, कौमारब्रह्मचारिन्, कौमारतन्त्रम्, कौमारबन्धकी, कौमारभृत्यम्, कौमारराज्यम्, कौमारव्रतः, कौमारहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारचारिन्
कौमार + -चारिन्, -ब्रह्मचारिन् <i>a.</i> abstinent, chaste; Ks. 66. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारब्रह्मचारिन्
कौमार + -चारिन्, -ब्रह्मचारिन् <i>a.</i> abstinent, chaste; Ks. 66. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारतन्त्रम्
कौमार + -तन्त्रम् the section of a medical work, treating of the rearing<BR> or education of children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारबन्धकी
कौमार + -बन्धकी a harlot; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारभृत्यम्
कौमार + -भृत्यम् the rearing and general treatment of children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारराज्यम्
कौमार + -राज्यम् the position of an heir-apparent; कौमार (v. l. कुमार)<BR> राज्ये जीवस्व Rām. 2. 58. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारव्रतः|कौमारव्रत
कौमार + -व्रतः ({@तम्@}) a vow of abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारहर
कौमार + -हर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 marrying or gaining a woman as a girl.<BR>—2 devirginating; यः कौमारहरः स एव हि वरः K. P. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारकम्
कौमारकम् Boyhood, juvenile or tender age; कौमारकेऽपि गिरिवद्गुरुतां<BR> दधानः U. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारिकः|कौमारिक
कौमारिकः A father of girls. ━<i>a.</i> Liking girls or daughters; कौमारिकाणां<BR> शीलेन वक्ष्याम्यहमरिंदम Mb. 1. 100. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारिकेयः|कौमारिकेय
कौमारिकेयः [कुमारिकाया अपत्यं ढक्] The son of an unmarried woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदः|कौमुद
कौमुदः The month Kārtika; कौमुदे मासि रेवत्यां शरदन्ते हिमागमे Mb. 5. 83. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदी
कौमुदी [कुमुदस्येयं प्रकाशकत्वात् अण् ङीष् Tv.]<BR>—1 Moonlight; शशिना सह याति कौमुदी Ku. 4. 33; शशिनमुपगतेयं<BR> कौमुदी मेघमुक्तम् R. 6. 85; (the word is thus popularly derived:− कौ<BR> मोदन्ते जना यस्यां तेनासौ कौमुदी मता).<BR>—2 Anything serving as moonlight, <i>i. e.</i> causing delight and balmy<BR> coolness; त्वं कौमुदी नयनयोरमृतं त्वमङ्गे U. 2; त्वमस्य लोकस्य<BR> च नेत्रकौमुदी Ku. 5. 71; या कौमुदी नयनयोर्भवतः सुजन्मा Māl. 1. 34;<BR> cf. चन्द्रिका.<BR>—3 The full moon day in Kārtika; तस्मात्तु कपिला देया कौमुद्यां ज्येष्ठपुष्करे<BR> Mb. 13. 130. 32.<BR>—4 The full moon day in Āśvina.<BR>—5 Festivity (in general).<BR>—6 Particularly, a festive day on which temples, houses &c. are illuminated.<BR>—7 (At the end of titles of works &c.) Elucidation, throwing light on<BR> the subject treated; <i>e. g.</i> तर्ककौमुदी, सांख्यतत्त्वकौमुदी, सिद्धान्तकौमुदी &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौमुदीचारः, कौमुदीतरुः, कौमुदीपतिः, कौमुदीमुखम्, कौमुदीवृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीचारः|कौमुदीचार
कौमुदी + -चारः the day of full moon in the month Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीतरुः|कौमुदीतरु
कौमुदी + -तरुः the stick of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीपतिः|कौमुदीपति
कौमुदी + -पतिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीमुखम्
कौमुदी + -मुखम् appearance of moonlight; सखीजनोद्वीक्षणकौमुदीमुखम् R. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीवृक्षः|कौमुदीवृक्ष
कौमुदी + -वृक्षः the stick or stand of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदकी
कौमोदकी, कौमोदी N. of the mace of Viṣṇu; Bhāg. 8. 4. 19;<BR> कौमोदकी मोदयति स्म चेतः Śi. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदी
कौमोदकी, कौमोदी N. of the mace of Viṣṇu; Bhāg. 8. 4. 19;<BR> कौमोदकी मोदयति स्म चेतः Śi. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव|कौरवः
कौरव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>) [कुरोरपत्यं, तद्देशस्य राजा<BR> तेषु भवो वा, कुरु अण्] Relating to the Kurus; क्षेत्रं क्षत्रप्रधनपिशुनं<BR> कौरवं तद् भजेथाः Me. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरवः|कौरव
कौरव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Kuru; मथ्नामि कौरवशतं समरे न कोपात् Ve. 1. 15;<BR> Cāṇ. 50.<BR>—2 A ruler of the Kurus. (so कौरवक, कौरवायणि and कौरवेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्यः|कौरव्य
कौरव्यः [कुरु-ण्य P. IV. 1. 151]<BR>—1 A descendant of Kuru; कौरव्यवंशदावेऽस्मिन् क एष शलभायते Ve. 1. 19;<BR> कौरव्याः पशवः प्रियापरिभवक्लेशोपशान्तिः फलम् 25; कौरव्ये<BR> कृतहस्तता पुनरियं देवे यथा सीरिणि 6. 12.<BR>—2 A ruler of the Kurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्णेयः
कौर्णेयः<BR>—1 A demon.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 Śiva.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR>—5 Engaged in penance.<BR>—6 फाल्गुनिक (?) cf. कौर्णेयो राक्षसे वायावीशानानलयोरपि । तपःस्थिते<BR> फाल्गुनिके … ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्प्यः|कौर्प्य
कौर्प्यः The zodiacal sign Scorpio (a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्म|कौर्मः|कौर्म्म
कौर्म <i>a.</i> [कूर्म-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a tortoise.<BR>—2 Belonging to the Avatāra of Viṣṇu as a tortoise; (˚पुराण);<BR> कौर्मे धृतोऽद्रिरमृतोन्मथने स्वपृष्ठे Bhāg. 11. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्मः|कौर्म|कौर्म्म
कौर्म + .{@-र्मः@} N. of a Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल|कौलः
कौल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>) [कुले भवः अण् cf. P. IV. 2. 96]<BR>—1 Relating to a family, राज्यं प्राप्तं यशश्चैव कौली श्रीरभिवर्धिता;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">Page0612-1</a>]<BR> Rām. 4. 29. 9.<BR>—2 ancestral, hereditary; Bhāg. 12. 3. 36.<BR>—3 Of a noble family, well-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलः|कौल
कौल + .{@-लः@} A worshipper of शक्ति according to the left hand ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलम्
कौल + .{@-लम्@} The doctrine and practices of the left hand Śāktas (for<BR> a short description of कौलधर्म see Karpūr. 1, speech of भैरवानन्द).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौलमार्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलमार्गः|कौलमार्ग
कौल + -मार्गः the doctrine of the Kaulas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेय|कौलकेयः
कौलकेय <i>a.</i> Sprung from a noble family, of a good family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेयः|कौलकेय
कौलकेय + .{@-यः@} The son of an unchaste woman, a bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटिनेयः|कौलटिनेय
कौलटिनेयः [कुलटायाः अपत्यम् P. IV. 1. 127]<BR>—1 The son of a (chaste) female beggar.<BR>—2 A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेयः|कौलटेय
कौलटेयः [P. IV. 1. 127]<BR>—1 The son of a female beggar (chaste or unchaste).<BR>—2 A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेयम्
कौलटेयः + .{@-यम्@} Adultery (जारकर्म); Mb. 12. 63. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेरः|कौलटेर
कौलटेरः [P. IV. 1. 127]<BR>—1 A bastard, son or daughter of a disloyal wife.<BR>—2 the child of a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालः|कौलाल
कौलालः [P. V. 4. 36] A potter; यथा चक्रं तु कौलालो दण्डविद्धं<BR> तु भारत Mb. 7. 142. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालम्
कौलालः + .{@-लम्@} Pottery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालक
कौलालक <i>a.</i> Made by, or pertaining to, a potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालकम्
कौलालक + .{@-कम्@} Earthenware, porcelain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिक|कौलिकः
कौलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [कलादागतः ठक्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a family. —2 Customary in a family, ancestral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिकः|कौलिक
कौलिक + .{@-कः@} A weaver; कौलिको विष्णुरूपेण राजकन्यां निषेवते Pt. 1. 202.<BR>—2 An impostor, a heretic.<BR>—3 A follower of the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन|कौलीनं|कौलीनः
कौलीन <i>a.</i> [कौ पृथिव्यां लीनः अलुक्स˚; कुलादागतः खञ् वा; कुलालवः<BR> P. IV. 1. 139] Belonging to a noble family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीनः|कौलीन|कौलीनं
कौलीन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 The son of a female beggar.<BR>—2 A follower of the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीनम्
कौलीन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 An evil report, a scandal; मालविकागतं किमपि कौलीनं श्रूयते<BR> M. 3; तदेव कौलीनमिव प्रतिभाति V. 2; Me. 114; कौलीनमात्माश्रयमाचचक्षे R. 14. 36, 84.<BR>—2 An improper act, bad or scandalous conduct; ख्याते तस्मिन् वितमसि<BR> कुले जन्म कौलीनमेतत् Ve. 2. 10.<BR>—3 A combat of animals.<BR>—4 Cock-fighting.<BR>—5 War, battle (in general).<BR>—6 High birth.<BR>—7 A privity, the pudenda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन्यम्
कौलीन्यम्<BR>—1 High birth; न कौलीन्यान्न सौहार्दान्नृपो वाक्ये प्रवर्तते (मन्त्रिणाम्) Pt. 1. 116.<BR>—2 Family scandal.<BR>—3 Family honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलूतः|कौलूत
कौलूतः A king of the Kulūtas; कौलूतश्चित्रवर्मा Mu. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेय|कौलेयः
कौलेय <i>a.</i> A pearl obtained in the river near the village मयूर<BR> in सिंहल; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयक|कौलेयकः
कौलेयक [कुल-ढकञ् P. IV. 2. 96] <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of a noble family.<BR>—2 Pertaining to a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयकः|कौलेयक
कौलेयक + .{@-कः@} A dog, hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्य|कौल्यः
कौल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Noble-born, of a high birth.<BR>—2 Of the left hand Śākta sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्यम्
कौल्य + .{@-ल्यम्@} noble descent, high birth; Mb. 12. 286. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौविन्दी
कौविन्दी The wife of a weaver (कुविन्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेर|कौवेरं
कौवे(बे)र <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कुवेरस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to or coming from<BR> Kubera; यानं सस्मार कौबेरम् R. 15. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौबेर
कौवे(बे)र <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [कुवेरस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to or coming from<BR> Kubera; यानं सस्मार कौबेरम् R. 15. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेरी
कौवे(बे)र + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 The north (the direction presided over by Kubera); ततः प्रतस्थे<BR> कौवेरीं भास्वानिव रघुर्दिशम् R. 4. 66.<BR>—2 The Śakti or female energy of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>) [कुश-अण्]<BR>—1 Silken; Bhāg. 3. 4. 7.<BR>—2 Made of Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशम्
कौश + .{@-शम्@} An epithet of Kānyakubja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलम्
कौशलम्(ल्यम्) [कुशल-अण् ष्यञ् वा P. V. 1. 124]<BR>—1 Well-being, welfare, happiness, prosperity; वैदेहि कुशली रामः स<BR> त्वां कौशलमब्रवीत् Rām. 5. 34. 3.<BR>—2 Skill, skilfulness, cleverness; किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षितया<BR> Mu. 3; हावहारि हसितं वचनानां कौशलं दृशि विकारविशेषाः Śi. 10. 13.<BR>—3 (कौशल्यम्) A pavilion with forty-six pillars; Matsya P. (Ch. 270) 5. 8;<BR> योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् Bg. 2. 50<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यम्
कौशलम्(ल्यम्) [कुशल-अण् ष्यञ् वा P. V. 1. 124]<BR>—1 Well-being, welfare, happiness, prosperity; वैदेहि कुशली रामः स<BR> त्वां कौशलमब्रवीत् Rām. 5. 34. 3.<BR>—2 Skill, skilfulness, cleverness; किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षितया<BR> Mu. 3; हावहारि हसितं वचनानां कौशलं दृशि विकारविशेषाः Śi. 10. 13.<BR>—3 (कौशल्यम्) A pavilion with forty-six pillars; Matsya P. (Ch. 270) 5. 8;<BR> योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् Bg. 2. 50<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिकम्
कौशलिकम् A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिका
कौशलिका, कौशली<BR>—1 A present, an offering.<BR>—2 Friendly inquiry after oneʼs health &c., greeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशली
कौशलिका, कौशली<BR>—1 A present, an offering.<BR>—2 Friendly inquiry after oneʼs health &c., greeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलेयः|कौशलेय
कौशलेयः [कौशल्याया अपत्यं ठक् यलोपः] An epithet of Rāma,<BR> son of Kauśalyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्या
कौशल्या [कोशलदेशे भवा छण्] The eldest wife of Daśaratha and<BR> mother of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यायनिः|कौशल्यायनि
कौशल्यायनिः [काशल्याया अपत्यं फिञ्] Rāma, son of Kauśalyā;<BR> म्रियामहे न गच्छामः कौशल्यायनिवल्लभाम् Bk. 7. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बी|कौशांबी
कौशाम्बी [कुशाम्बेन निर्वृत्ता अण्] N. of an ancient city on the<BR> Ganges in the lower part of the Doab; निष्कान्तः कौशाम्ब्या निष्क्रौशाम्बिः<BR> Mbh. on P. II. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की)<BR> [कुश-ठञ्, कुशिकअण् वा]<BR>—1 Incased, sheathed; विक्रम्य कौशिकं खड्गं मोक्षयित्वा ग्रहं रिपोः<BR> Mb. 3. 157. 11.<BR>—2 Coming from an owl.<BR>—3 Born of the family of Kuśika; कौशिकाश्च कथं वंशात्क्षत्राद्वै ब्राह्मणो<BR> भवेत् Mb. 13. 52. 4.<BR>—4 Silken; या त्वाहं कौशिकैर्वस्त्रैः शुभ्रैराच्छादितं पुस Mb. 3. 27. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकी
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की)<BR> [कुश-ठञ्, कुशिकअण् वा]<BR>—1 Incased, sheathed; विक्रम्य कौशिकं खड्गं मोक्षयित्वा ग्रहं रिपोः<BR> Mb. 3. 157. 11.<BR>—2 Coming from an owl.<BR>—3 Born of the family of Kuśika; कौशिकाश्च कथं वंशात्क्षत्राद्वै ब्राह्मणो<BR> भवेत् Mb. 13. 52. 4.<BR>—4 Silken; या त्वाहं कौशिकैर्वस्त्रैः शुभ्रैराच्छादितं पुस Mb. 3. 27. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषिक|कौषिकः
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की)<BR> [कुश-ठञ्, कुशिकअण् वा]<BR>—1 Incased, sheathed; विक्रम्य कौशिकं खड्गं मोक्षयित्वा ग्रहं रिपोः<BR> Mb. 3. 157. 11.<BR>—2 Coming from an owl.<BR>—3 Born of the family of Kuśika; कौशिकाश्च कथं वंशात्क्षत्राद्वै ब्राह्मणो<BR> भवेत् Mb. 13. 52. 4.<BR>—4 Silken; या त्वाहं कौशिकैर्वस्त्रैः शुभ्रैराच्छादितं पुस Mb. 3. 27. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषिकी
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की)<BR> [कुश-ठञ्, कुशिकअण् वा]<BR>—1 Incased, sheathed; विक्रम्य कौशिकं खड्गं मोक्षयित्वा ग्रहं रिपोः<BR> Mb. 3. 157. 11.<BR>—2 Coming from an owl.<BR>—3 Born of the family of Kuśika; कौशिकाश्च कथं वंशात्क्षत्राद्वै ब्राह्मणो<BR> भवेत् Mb. 13. 52. 4.<BR>—4 Silken; या त्वाहं कौशिकैर्वस्त्रैः शुभ्रैराच्छादितं पुस Mb. 3. 27. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकः|कौशिक
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की) + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of विश्वामित्र q. v.<BR>—2 An owl; U. 2. 29.<BR>—3 A lexicographer.<BR>—4 Marrow.<BR>—5 Bdellium.<BR>—6 An ichneumon.<BR>—7 A snake-catcher.<BR>—8 The sentiment of love (शृङ्गार).<BR>—9 One who knows hidden treasures.<BR>—10 An epithet of Indra; Bhāg. 10. 38. 17; N. 5. 64.<BR>—11 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—12 N. of a priest in charge of Sāmaveda.<BR>—13 A dealer in Kuśa grass.<BR>—14 Gum, resin; ‘कौशिंको मुनिभेदे च नकुले शक्रघूकयोः । उद्गातरि कुशाजीवे कोशवत्यहितुण्डिके ॥ गुग्गुलावपि …’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिका
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की) + .{@-का@} A cup, drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकी
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की) + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 N. of a river in Bihar.<BR>—2 N. of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—3 N. of one of the four varieties of dramatic style; सुकुमारार्थसंदर्भा<BR> कौशिकी तासु कथ्यते; see S. D. 411 <i>et seq.</i> also.<BR>—4 The earth; ‘गायत्र्याः सांख्यायनगोत्रत्ववद्भूः कौशिकी’ इति कतकः;<BR> त्रातुमर्हसि वीर त्वं पातालादिव कौशिकीम् Rām. 5. 38. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकम्
कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), also कौषिक (-की) + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Silk, silken garment; Mb. 13. 111. 104; Bhāg. 10. 83. 28.<BR>—2 A way of flying (सर्वतोभद्र); Mb. 7. 48. 35.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौशिकारातिः, कौशिकारिः, कौशिकात्मजः, कौशिकायुधम्, कौशिकफलः, कौशिकप्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकारातिः|कौशिकाराति
कौशिक + -अरातिः, -अरिः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">Page0613-1</a>]<BR> a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकारिः|कौशिकारि
कौशिक + -अरातिः, -अरिः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">Page0613-1</a>]<BR> a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकात्मजः|कौशिकात्मज
कौशिक + -आत्मजः an epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकायुधम्
कौशिक + -आयुधम् rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकफलः|कौशिकफल
कौशिक + -फलः the cocoa-nut tree, said to have been created by Viśvāmitra<BR> (कौशिक); the nut being the rudiment of a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकप्रियः|कौशिकप्रिय
कौशिक + -प्रियः an epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीतकी
कौशीतकी Wife of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीधान्यम्
कौशीधान्यम् A leguminous plant, pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीलवम्
कौशीलवम् The profession of an actor or dancer; Gobhilaʼs श्राद्धकल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशे(षे)य <i>a.</i> [कोशे संभूतम् or कोशस्य विकारः ढञ्<BR> P. IV. 3. 42; Vārt. 1] Silk, silken; कौशेयान्यथ तार्णानि … Śiva B. 30. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषेय|कौषेयं
कौशे(षे)य <i>a.</i> [कोशे संभूतम् or कोशस्य विकारः ढञ्<BR> P. IV. 3. 42; Vārt. 1] Silk, silken; कौशेयान्यथ तार्णानि … Śiva B. 30. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेयम्
कौशे(षे)य + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Silk; कौशेयं कृमिजं सुवर्णमुपलादिन्दीवरं गोमयम् । Pt. 1. 94.<BR>—2 A silken cloth in general; Ms. 5. 120.<BR>—3 A womanʼs lower garment of silk; निर्नाभि कौशेयमुपात्तबाणमभ्यङ्गनेपथ्यमलंचकार<BR> Ku. 7. 7; विद्युद्गणकौशेयः Mk. 5. 3; Ṛs. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषीतकम्
कौषीतकम् N. of a Brāhmaṇa; also कौषीतकिब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्य|कौसल्यं|कौसल्यः
कौसल्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the people of the Kosalas; Mb. 7. 49. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्यः|कौसल्य|कौसल्यं
कौसल्य + .{@-ल्यः@} A prince of the Kosalas; कौसल्यश्चाश्वलायनः Praśna. Up. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्या
कौसल्य + .{@-ल्या@} The wife of Daśaratha and mother of Rāma.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौसल्यनन्दनः, कौसल्यमातृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्यनन्दनः
कौसल्य + -नन्दनः, -मातृ <i>m.</i> epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्यमातृ
कौसल्य + -नन्दनः, -मातृ <i>m.</i> epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद
कौसीद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Connected with a loan; न त्वेवाधौ सोपकारे कौसीदीं वृद्धिमाप्नुयात् Ms. 8. 143.<BR>—2 Usurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद्यम्
कौसीद्यम् [कुसीद-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 The practice of usury.<BR>—2 Sloth, indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम|कौसुमं
कौसुम <i>a.</i> [कुसुम-अण्] Flowery, flowering; सेयं मृदुः कौसुमचापयष्टिः N. 7. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुमम्
कौसुम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 The ashes of brass (used as a collyrium).<BR>—2 Pollen of flowers (पराग); विनयति सुदृशे दृशः परागं प्रणयिनि<BR> कौसुममाननानिलेन । Śi. 7. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम्भ|कौसुंभ|कौसुम्भः
कौसुम्भ <i>a.</i> [कुसुम्भ-अण्]<BR>—1 Prepared with safflower.<BR>—2 Dyed with safflower, red; कौसुम्भं पृथु कुचकुम्भसङ्गि वासः Śi. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम्भः|कौसुम्भ|कौसुंभ
कौसुम्भ + .{@-भः@} Wild safflower; दिनकरकरसङ्ग व्यक्तकौसुम्भकान्तिः Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसृतिकः|कौसृतिक
कौसृतिकः [कुसृत्या चरति ठक् P. V. 2. 75]<BR>—1 A cheat, knave.<BR>—2 A juggler;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभः|कौस्तुभ
कौस्तुभः [कुस्तुभो जलधिस्तत्र भवः अण्]<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated gem obtained with 13 other jewels at the churning<BR> of the ocean and worn by Viṣṇu on his breast; सकौस्तुभं ह्रेपयतीव<BR> कृष्णम् R. 6. 49, 10. 10.<BR>—2 A kind of oil.<BR>—3 A manner of joining the fingers.<BR>—4 A twist of hair on a horseʼs neck; कौस्तुभः स्याद्देवमणौ कण्ठावर्तेऽपि वाजिनाम् Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: कौस्तुभलक्षणः, कौस्तुभवक्षस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभलक्षणः|कौस्तुभलक्षण
कौस्तुभः + -लक्षणः, -वक्षस् <i>m.</i>, {@-हृदयः@} epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभवक्षस्
कौस्तुभः + -लक्षणः, -वक्षस् <i>m.</i>, {@-हृदयः@} epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नथ्
क्नथ् €1. €10 P. To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नस्
क्नस् €4. €10 P.<BR>—1 To be crooked.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूय्
क्नूय् €1 Ā. (क्नूयते, caus. क्नोपयति)<BR>—1 To make a creaking sound.<BR>—2 To sink.<BR>—3 To be wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्मर्
क्मर् €1 P. To act dishonestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचः|क्रकच
क्रकचः<BR>—1 A saw; U. 4. 3; Mv. 5. 19.<BR>—2 A kind of instrument of war music (जयमङ्गल); Mb. 6. 43. 8;<BR> क्रकचानां काहलानां पणवानां च सर्वशः Śiva B. 24. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचा
क्रकचः + .{@-चा@} The Ketaka tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्रकचच्छदः, क्रकचपत्रः, क्रकचपाद, क्रकचपादः, क्रकचपृष्ठी, क्रकचव्यवहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचच्छदः|क्रकचच्छद
क्रकचः + -च्छदः the Ketaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपत्रः|क्रकचपत्र
क्रकचः + -पत्रः the teak tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपाद|क्रकचपादः
क्रकचः + -पाद, -पादः <i>m.</i>, a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपादः|क्रकचपाद
क्रकचः + -पाद, -पादः <i>m.</i>, a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपृष्ठी
क्रकचः + -पृष्ठी The कवयी fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचव्यवहारः|क्रकचव्यवहार
क्रकचः + -व्यवहारः a particular method of computing or rating a heap of wood; Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकरः|क्रकर
क्रकरः<BR>—1 A kind of partridge.<BR>—2 A saw.<BR>—3 A poor man. —4 A disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकरटः|क्रकरट
क्रकरटः A lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुः|क्रतु
क्रतुः [कृ-कतु Uṇ. 1. 77]<BR>—1 A sacrifice; क्रतोरशेषेण फलेन युज्यताम् R. 3. 65; शतं क्रतूनामपविघ्नमाप<BR> सः 3. 38; M. 1. 4; Ms. 7. 79.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 One of the ten Prajāpatis; क्रतुं प्रजापतिमब्रुवन् Maitr. Up. 2. 3;<BR> Ms. 1. 35.<BR>—4 Intelligence, talent.<BR>—5 Power, ability.<BR>—6 Plan, design, purpose; क्रतो स्मर कृतं स्मर Īśop. 17; Bṛ. Up. 5. 15. 1.<BR>—7 Resolution, determination; यत्क्रतुर्भवति तत्कर्म कुरुते Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 5.<BR>—8 Desire, will.<BR>—9 Fitness, adequacy, efficiency.<BR>—10 Deliberation, consultation.<BR>—11 Inspiration.<BR>—12 Enlightenment.<BR>—13 Offering, worship; कामस्याप्तिं जगतः प्रतिष्ठां क्रतोरानन्त्यमभयस्य<BR> पारम् Kaṭh. 1. 2. 11; Personified, as married to क्रिया and father<BR> of 60000 वालखिल्यs; क्रतोरपि क्रिया भार्या वालखिल्यानसूयत Bhāg. 4. 1. 39.<BR>—14 An Aśvameḍha sacrifice (these senses are mostly Vedic).<BR>—15 The month Āṣāḍha.<BR>—16 Excess of fondness or liking.<BR>—17 An organ [cf. Gr. <i>kratos</i>; Zend. <i>khratu</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्रत्वर्थः, क्रतूत्तमः, क्रतुकर्मन्, क्रतुद्रुह्, क्रतुद्विष्, क्रतुध्वंसिन्, क्रतुपतिः, क्रतुपशुः, क्रतुपुरुषः, क्रतुफलम्, क्रतुभुज्, क्रतुराज्, क्रतुराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रत्वर्थः|क्रत्वर्थ
क्रतुः + -अर्थः Something that is meant to subserve the purpose of the<BR> sacrifice (opp. पुरुषार्थ q. v.); पुरुषार्थे लक्षिते तद्विपरीतः<BR> क्रत्वर्थः इति क्रत्वर्थस्य लक्षणं सिद्धम् । ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतूत्तमः|क्रतूत्तम
क्रतुः + -उत्तमः the राजसूय sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुकर्मन्
क्रतुः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-क्रिया@} a sacrificial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्रुह्
क्रतुः + -द्रुह्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a demon, goblin,<BR>—2 The epithet of Ravaṇa; ऋणाद् बद्ध इवोन्मुक्तो वियोगेन क्रतुद्विषः Bk. 8. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्विष्
क्रतुः + -द्रुह्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a demon, goblin,<BR>—2 The epithet of Ravaṇa; ऋणाद् बद्ध इवोन्मुक्तो वियोगेन क्रतुद्विषः Bk. 8. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुध्वंसिन्
क्रतुः + -ध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva (who destroyed Dakṣaʼs sacrifice.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपतिः|क्रतुपति
क्रतुः + -पतिः the performer of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपशुः|क्रतुपशु
क्रतुः + -पशुः a sacrificial horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपुरुषः|क्रतुपुरुष
क्रतुः + -पुरुषः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुफलम्
क्रतुः + -फलम् The reward of a sacrifice, its object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुभुज्
क्रतुः + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुराज्
क्रतुः + -राज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the lord of sacrifices; यथाश्वमेधः क्रतुराट् Ms. 9. 260.<BR>—2 the राजसूय sacrifice;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुराजः|क्रतुराज
क्रतुः + -राजः the राजसूय sacrifice; क्रतुराजेन गोविन्द राजसूयेन<BR> पावनीः (यक्ष्ये) Bhāg. 10. 72. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ्
क्रथ् €1 P. (क्रथति, क्रथित) To injure, hurt, kill (with gen. of person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथनम्
क्रथनम्<BR>—1 A slaughter.<BR>—2 Cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथकैशिकः|क्रथकैशिक
क्रथकैशिकः (Pl.) N. of a country; अथेश्वरेण क्रथकैशिकानाम्<BR> R. 5. 39; M. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रद्
क्रद् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To be confused.<BR>—2 To grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द्|क्रंद्
क्रन्द् €1 P. (क्रन्दति, चक्रन्द, अक्रन्दीत्, क्रन्दित)<BR>—1 To cry, weep, shed tears; किं क्रन्दसि दुराक्रन्द स्वपक्षक्षयकारक<BR> Pt. 4. 29; क्रन्दत्यतः करुणमप्सरसां गणोऽयम् V. 1. 3; चक्रन्द<BR> विग्ना कुररीव भूयः R. 14. 68, 15. 42; Bk. 3. 28, 5. 5.<BR>—2 To call out to, call out piteously to any one, (with acc.); क्रन्दत्यविरतं<BR> सोऽथ भ्रातृमातृसुतानथ Mārk. P.<BR>—3 To cry out, exclaim.<BR>—4 To yell, howl.<BR>—5 To neigh (as a horse); हरिर्वाजमचिक्रन्दत् Rv. 9. 67. 4.<BR>—6 To roar.<BR>—7 To creak (as a wheel).<BR> €10 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cry out continuously.<BR>—2 To roar, rave.<BR>—3 To cause to weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दः|क्रन्द|क्रंदः
क्रन्दः Ved.<BR>—1 Neighing; अश्वस्येव वृषणः क्रन्द एति Av. 11. 2. 22.<BR>—2 A cry, calling out; क्रन्दाय ते प्राणाय Av. 11. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दन|क्रंदन|क्रन्दनं|क्रंदनः|क्रन्दनः
क्रन्दन [क्रन्द् भावे ल्युट्] A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दनम्
क्रन्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A cry of distress or weeping, lamentation; व्यसनं प्राप्य यो मोहात्केवलं<BR> परिदेवयेत् । क्रन्दनं वर्धयत्येव Pt. 2. 188.<BR>—2 Mutual defiance.<BR>—3 Calling, inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दस्|क्रंदस्
क्रन्दस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Battle-cry; शिमीवति क्रन्दसि प्राव सातये Rv. 10. 38. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दित|क्रंदित|क्रन्दितं
क्रन्दित <i>a.</i> [क्रन्द्-क्त] Wept, called or cried out; ततस्तद्वासिभिर्देवः<BR> क्रन्दितः शरणार्थिभिः Ks. 114. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दितम्
क्रन्दित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Cry of distress or weeping, lamentation; हा तातेति क्रन्दितमाकर्ण्य<BR> विषण्णः R. 9. 75.<BR>—2 Mutual defiance, challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप्
क्रप् €1 Ā. (क्रपते)<BR>—1 To pity.<BR>—2 To mourn.<BR>—3 To lament.<BR>—4 To go.<BR>—5 To long for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप्
क्रप् €10 P. (क्रापयति) To speak clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम्
क्रम् €1 U., €4 P. (क्रामति, क्रमते, क्राम्यति, चक्राम, चक्रमे,<BR> अक्रमीत्, अक्रस्त, क्रान्त)<BR>—1 To walk, step, go; क्रामत्यनुदिते सूर्ये वाली व्यपगतक्लमः Rām.;<BR> गम्यमानं न तेनासीदगतं क्रामता पुरः Bk. 8. 2, 25.<BR>—2 To go to, approach (with acc.); देवा इमान् लोकानक्रमन्त Śat. Br.<BR>—3 To pass or go over, go across, traverse; U. 2. 13; सुखं योजनपञ्चाशत्क्रमेयम् Rām.<BR>—4 To leap, jump; क्रमं बबन्ध क्रमितुं सकोपः (हरिः) Bk. 2. 9, 5. 51.<BR>—5 To go up, ascend; क्रामत्युच्चैर्भूभृतो यस्य तेजः Śi. 16. 83.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To cover, occupy, take possession of, fill; क्रान्ता यथा चेतसि<BR> विस्मयेन R. 14. 17.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To reach up to, pervade, penetrate; क्रामद्भिर्घनपदवीमनेकसंख्यैः Ki. 5. 34.<BR>—7 To surpass, excel; स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वी क्रान्त्वा मेरुरिवात्मना R. 1. 14.<BR>—8 To undertake, strive after, be able or competent for, show energy for<BR> (with dat. or inf.); व्याकरणाध्ययनाय क्रमते Sk.; धर्माय क्रमते<BR> साधुः Vop.; व्युत्पत्तिरावर्जितकोविदापि न रञ्जनाय क्रमते जडानाम्<BR> Vikr. 1. 16; हत्वा रक्षांसि लवितुमक्रमीन्मारुतिः पुनः । अशोकवनिकामेव Bk. 9. 23.<BR>—9 To be developed or increased, to have full scope, be at home (with<BR> loc.); कृत्येषु क्रमन्ते Dk. 170; क्रमन्तेऽस्मिञ्शास्त्राणि, or ऋक्षु<BR> क्रमते बुद्धिः Sk. क्रममाणोऽरिसंसदि Bk. 8. 22.<BR>—10 To succeed, have effect (Ātm.); न चक्रमस्याक्रमताधिकं धरम् Śi. 1. 54.<BR>—11 To be repeated (as a letter or word in the arrangement called क्रम q. v.).<BR>—12 To fulfil, accomplish.<BR>—13 To have sexual intercourse with; to cover (in copulation); क्रमस्पर्श<BR> इव रोहितमनवग्लायता सदा Av. 4. 4. 7.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-2" target="_blank">Page0614-2</a>]<BR> (By वृत्तिसर्गतायनेषु क्रमः P. I. 3. 38; क्रम् by itself is used<BR> in the Ātm. in the sense of ‘continuity’ or ‘want of interruption’, ‘energy or application’<BR>, and ‘development or increase’, and also ‘conquering or getting over’<BR>). ━<i>Caus.</i> (क्रमयति, क्रामयति)<BR>—1 To cause to go &c.<BR>—2 To repeat a letter (as in the क्रम arrangement). ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> चिक्रमिषति, चिक्रंसते &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमः|क्रम
क्रमः [क्रम्-भावकरणादौ घञ्]<BR>—1 A step, pace; त्रिविक्रमः; सागरः प्लवगेन्द्रेण क्रमेणैकेन लङ्घितः<BR> Mb.; Śi. 12. 18.<BR>—2 A foot; (अपनेष्यति) असुरेभ्यः श्रियं दीप्तां विष्णुस्त्रिभिरिव<BR> क्रमैः Rām. 5. 21. 28.<BR>—3 Going, proceeding, course; क्रमात् or क्रमेण in course of,<BR> gradually; कालक्रमेण gradually, in course of time; कालक्रमेण<BR> जगतः परिवर्तमाना Svapna., भाग्यक्रमः course or turn of fate;<BR> R. 3. 7, 30, 32.<BR>—4 Performance, commencement; अविचार्य क्रमं न करिष्यति । इत्थमत्र<BR> विततक्रमे क्रतौ Śi. 14. 53.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Regular course, order, series, succession; निमित्तनैमित्तकयोरयं<BR> क्रमः Ś. 7. 30; Ms. 7. 24, 9. 85, 2. 173, 3. 69.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Traditional order; U. 6.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Order of propriety; लोकान्तरगतेनापि नोज्झितो विनयक्रमः<BR> Nāg. 5. 11. आत्मीयः पर इत्ययं खलु कुतः सत्यं कृपायाः क्रमः ।<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 5. 20; Ku. 5. 32; प्रियवचननिवेदनत्वरया क्रमविशेषो<BR> नावेक्षितः Pratijñā.<BR>—6 Method, manner; वर्तस्व च सतां क्रमे Rām. 2. 25. 2; नेत्रकमेणोपरुरोध<BR> सूर्यम् R. 7. 39.<BR>—7 Grasp, hold; क्रमगता पशोः कन्यका Māl. 3. 13.<BR>—8 A position of attack (assumed by an animal before making a spring);<BR> न मया क्रमः सज्जीकृत आसीत् Pt. 4.<BR>—9 Preparation, readiness; Bk. 2. 9.<BR>—10 An undertaking, enterprize.<BR>—11 An act or deed, manner of proceeding; कोप्येष कान्तः क्रमः Amaru. 48, 33.<BR>—12 Particular manner of reciting Vedic texts, leaving at each time one<BR> word and taking up another; वेदैः साङ्गपदक्रमोपनिषदैर्गायन्ति यं<BR> सामगाः Bhāg. 12. 13. 1. चर्चागुणान् क्रमगुणांश्चापेक्ष्य भवति<BR> Mbh. on P. V. 1. 119.<BR>—13 Power, strength; स ईश्वरः काल उरुक्रमोऽसौ Bhāg. 7. 8. 9.<BR>—14 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्रमानुसारः, क्रमान्वयः, क्रमागत, क्रमायात, क्रमोद्वेगः, क्रमज्यका, क्रमज्या, क्रमपाठः, क्रमभङ्गः, क्रमभाविन्, क्रममाला, क्रमरथः, क्रमलेखा, क्रमशठः, क्रमशिखा, क्रमयोगः, क्रमयोगेन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

