क्वणितेक्षणः|क्वणितेक्षण
क्वणित + -ईक्षणः a vulture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणितवेणु
क्वणित + -वेणु <i>a.</i> one who has breathed the flute; श्रुत्वा च तत्क्वाणितवेणुविचित्रगीतम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 21. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाणः|क्वाण
क्वाणः Sound; सरत्नकङ्कणक्वाणवितीर्णकरतालिके Ks. 120. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ्
क्वथ् €1 P. (क्वथति, क्वथित)<BR>—1 To boil, decoct.<BR>—2 To digest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथः|क्वथ
क्वथः A decoction, solution prepared with a continued or gentle heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथनम्
क्वथनम् [क्वथ्-ल्युट्] Boiling, decocting; समेत्य सद्यः क्वथनेन<BR> फेनताम् Ki. 16. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथित|क्वथितः
क्वथित <i>a.</i> [क्वथ्-क्त]<BR>—1 Boiled, decocted; पक्षान्तयोर्वाऽप्यश्नीयाद्यवागूं क्वथितां सकृत् Ms. 6. 20.<BR>—2 Hot; अश्रुधाराः प्रमुञ्चन्ती संतापक्वथिताङ्गका Ks. 90. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथितम्
क्वथित + .{@-तम्@} Spirituous liquor (prepared with honey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथः|क्वाथ
क्वाथः [क्वथ्-करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 A decoction, solution prepared with a continued or gentle heat.<BR>—2 The mixture of the materials for decoction.<BR>—3 Pain, sorrow, distress.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्वाथोद्भवम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथोद्भवम्
क्वाथः + -उद्भवम् blue vitriol used a collyrium. (Mar. मोरचूद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाचित्क
क्वाचित्क <i>a.</i> (-त्की <i>f.</i>) Met with occasionally, rare,<BR> unusual; इति क्वाचित्कः पाठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वेल्
क्वेल् €1 P. (क्वेलति) To shake, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षः|क्ष
क्षः<BR>—1 Destruction.<BR>—2 Disappearance, loss.<BR>—3 Lightning.<BR>—4 A field.<BR>—5 A farmer.<BR>—6 Viṣṇu in his 4th or Narasiṃha incarnation.<BR>—7 A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षञ्ज्
क्षञ्ज्, क्षज् €10 U. (क्षञ्जयति-ते) To live in distress<BR> or pain. €1 Ā. (क्षजते) To kill. €1 Ā. (क्षञ्जते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षज्
क्षञ्ज्, क्षज् €10 U. (क्षञ्जयति-ते) To live in distress<BR> or pain. €1 Ā. (क्षजते) To kill. €1 Ā. (क्षञ्जते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण्
क्षण्(न्) €8 U. (क्षणोति, क्षणुते, क्षत)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure; इमां हृदि व्यायतपातमक्षणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR>—2 To break (to pieces); (धनुः) त्वं किलानमितपूर्वमक्षणोः<BR> R. 11. 72; (with {@परा, परि, वि@} used in the same senses as क्षण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्
क्षण्(न्) €8 U. (क्षणोति, क्षणुते, क्षत)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure; इमां हृदि व्यायतपातमक्षणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR>—2 To break (to pieces); (धनुः) त्वं किलानमितपूर्वमक्षणोः<BR> R. 11. 72; (with {@परा, परि, वि@} used in the same senses as क्षण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणः|क्षण|क्षणं
क्षणः, -णम्<BR> [क्षणोति दुःखं क्षण्-अच्]<BR>—1 An instant, moment, measure of time equal to ⁴⁄₅ of a second; न<BR> हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि Bg. 3. 5; क्षणमात्रमृषिस्तस्थौ सुप्तमीन इव ह्रदः<BR> R. 1. 73, 2. 60; Me. 26; क्षणमवतिष्ठस्व wait a moment.<BR>—2 Leisure; अहमपि लब्धक्षणः स्वगेहं गच्छामि M. 1; Pt. 1. 138;<BR> गृहीतः क्षणः Ś. 2 ‘my leisure is at your disposal’ <i>i. e.</i> I<BR> pledge my word to do your work.<BR>—3 A fit moment or opportunity; रहो नास्ति क्षणो नास्ति नास्ति प्रार्थयिता<BR> नरः Pt. 1. 138; Me. 64; अधिगतक्षणः Dk. 147.<BR>—4 An auspicious or lucky moment.<BR>—5 A festival, joy, delight; तदेव वीरोऽभिजगाम तोरणं कृतक्षणः<BR> काल इव प्रजाक्षये Rām. 5. 47. 38.<BR>—6 Dependence, servitude.<BR>—7 The centre, the middle.<BR>—8 A certain day of the fortnight (as the full moon).<BR>—9 Rule, resolution; गन्तुं भूमीं कृतक्षणाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">Page0621-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 1. 64. 51. (In comp. क्षण is translated by ‘momentary’, ‘temporary’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणम्
क्षणः, -णम्<BR> [क्षणोति दुःखं क्षण्-अच्]<BR>—1 An instant, moment, measure of time equal to ⁴⁄₅ of a second; न<BR> हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि Bg. 3. 5; क्षणमात्रमृषिस्तस्थौ सुप्तमीन इव ह्रदः<BR> R. 1. 73, 2. 60; Me. 26; क्षणमवतिष्ठस्व wait a moment.<BR>—2 Leisure; अहमपि लब्धक्षणः स्वगेहं गच्छामि M. 1; Pt. 1. 138;<BR> गृहीतः क्षणः Ś. 2 ‘my leisure is at your disposal’ <i>i. e.</i> I<BR> pledge my word to do your work.<BR>—3 A fit moment or opportunity; रहो नास्ति क्षणो नास्ति नास्ति प्रार्थयिता<BR> नरः Pt. 1. 138; Me. 64; अधिगतक्षणः Dk. 147.<BR>—4 An auspicious or lucky moment.<BR>—5 A festival, joy, delight; तदेव वीरोऽभिजगाम तोरणं कृतक्षणः<BR> काल इव प्रजाक्षये Rām. 5. 47. 38.<BR>—6 Dependence, servitude.<BR>—7 The centre, the middle.<BR>—8 A certain day of the fortnight (as the full moon).<BR>—9 Rule, resolution; गन्तुं भूमीं कृतक्षणाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">Page0621-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 1. 64. 51. (In comp. क्षण is translated by ‘momentary’, ‘temporary’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणात्
क्षणः, -णम् + .{@क्षणात्, -क्षणेन@} in a moment, at once, immediately).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणात्
क्षणः, -णम् + .{@क्षणात्, -क्षणेन@} in a moment, at once, immediately).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणेक्षणे
क्षणः, -णम् + .{@-क्षणेक्षणे@} <i>ind.</i> Every instant, moment; क्षणेक्षणे यन्नवतामुपैति<BR> तदेव रूपं रमणीयतायाः आरब्धैर्व्यसनैर्भूम्ना क्षीणकोशः क्षणे क्षणे<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 166.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षणान्तरे, क्षणार्धम्, क्षणक्षेपः, क्षणदः, क्षणद्युतिः, क्षणनिःश्वासः, क्षणभङ्गवादः, क्षणभङ्गुर, क्षणमात्रम्, क्षणरामिन्, क्षणविध्वंसिन्, क्षणवीर्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0620-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणान्तरे|क्षणांतरे
क्षणः + -अन्तरे <i>ind.</i> the next moment, after a little while.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणार्धम्
क्षणः + -अर्धम् half a moment, small space of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणक्षेपः|क्षणक्षेप
क्षणः + -क्षेपः a momentary delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदः|क्षणद|क्षणदं
क्षणः + -दः an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदम्
क्षणः + -दः + .({@-दम्@})<BR>—1 night-blindness.<BR>—2 water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदा
क्षणः + -दः + .({@-दम्@}) + ({@-दा@})<BR>—1 night; क्षणादथैष क्षणदापतिप्रभः N. 1. 67; R. 8. 74, 16. 45; Śi. 3. 53.<BR>—2 turmeric. ˚करः, ˚पतिः the moon; उदिते क्षणदाकरे Śi. 9. 70.<BR> ˚चरः a night-walker, a demon; सानुप्लवः प्रभुरपि क्षणदाचराणां<BR> R. 13 75. ˚आन्ध्यम् night-blindness, nyctalopsis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणद्युतिः|क्षणद्युति
क्षणः + -द्युतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-प्रकाशा, -प्रभा@} lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनिःश्वासः|क्षणनिःश्वास
क्षणः + -निःश्वासः the porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभङ्गवादः|क्षणभङ्गवाद
क्षणः + -भङ्गवादः the doctrine of the continual decay of things (Buddh.);<BR> Bādarāyaṇa 2. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभङ्गुर|क्षणभंगुर|क्षणभङ्गुरः
क्षणः + -भङ्गुर <i>a.</i> transient, frail, perishable; मृगतृष्णासमं<BR> वीक्ष्य संसारं क्षणभङ्गुरम् H. 4. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणमात्रम्
क्षणः + -मात्रम् <i>ind.</i> for a moment; क्षणमात्रमृषिस्तस्थौ सुप्तमीन<BR> इव ह्रदः R. 1. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणरामिन्
क्षणः + -रामिन् <i>m.</i> a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणविध्वंसिन्
क्षणः + -विध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i> perishable in a moment. ━(<i>m.</i>) a class of<BR> atheistic philosophers who deny the continued identity of any part of<BR> nature, and maintain that the universe perishes and undergoes a new creation every instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणवीर्यम्
क्षणः + -वीर्यम् an auspicious moment (क्षण, मुहूर्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतुः|क्षणतु
क्षणतुः A wound, sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनम्
क्षणनम् Injuring, killing, wounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिक|क्षणिकः
क्षणिक <i>a.</i> [क्षणः स्वसत्ताव्याप्यतयाऽस्त्यस्य ठन्] Momentary,<BR> transient; स्वप्नेषु क्षणिकसमागमोत्सवैश्च R. 8. 92; एकस्य क्षणिका<BR> प्रीतिः H. 1. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिका
क्षणिक + .{@-का@} Lightning.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षणिकालयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिकालयम्
क्षणिक + -आलयम् a temple where temporary idols are worshipped; Māna. 61. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिन्
क्षणिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Having leisure.<BR>—2 Momentary.<BR>—3 Having a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिनी
क्षणिन् + .{@-नी@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणेपाकः|क्षणेपाक
क्षणेपाकः An article cooked in a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्
क्षत् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Killing.<BR>—2 Tearing. —3 Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत|क्षतं
क्षत <i>p. p.</i> [क्षण्-क्त]<BR>—1 Wounded, hurt, injured, bitten, torn, rent, broken down &c.; see क्षण्;<BR> रक्तप्रसाधितभुवः क्षतविग्रहाश्च Ve. 1. 7; Ku. 4. 6; R. 1. 28, 2. 56, 3. 53.<BR>—2 Diminished; trodden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतम्
क्षत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Scratching, a scratch.<BR>—2 A wound, hurt, injury; क्षते प्रहारा निपतन्त्यभीक्ष्णम् Pt. 2. 178;<BR> क्षते क्षारमिवासह्यं जातं तस्यैव दर्शनम् U. 4. 7; क्षारं क्षते<BR> प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18; नख˚ Ku. 3. 29.<BR>—3 Danger, destruction, peril; क्षतात् किल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः R. 2. 53.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षतारि, क्षतास्रवम्, क्षतोदरम्, क्षतकासः, क्षतजम्, क्षतयोनिः, क्षतविक्षत, क्षतवृत्तिः, क्षतव्रतः, क्षतहरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतारि
क्षत + -अरि <i>a.</i> victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतास्रवम्
क्षत + -आस्रवम् Blood; Bhāg. 3. 18. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतोदरम्
क्षत + -उदरम् dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतकासः|क्षतकास
क्षत + -कासः a cough produced by injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतजम्
क्षत + -जम्<BR>—1 blood; स च्छिन्नमूलः क्षतजेन रेणुः R. 7. 43; Ve. 2. 27; Rām. 5. 10. 19.<BR>—2 puss, matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतयोनिः|क्षतयोनि
क्षत + -योनिः <i>f.</i> a violated woman, a woman who is no longer a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतविक्षत
क्षत + -विक्षत <i>a.</i> mangled, covered with cuts and wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतवृत्तिः|क्षतवृत्ति
क्षत + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> destitution, being deprived of any means of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">Page0621-2</a>]<BR> support; क्षतवृत्तिर्वने नित्यं फालकुद्दाललाङ्गली Rām. 2. 32. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतव्रतः|क्षतव्रत
क्षत + -व्रतः a student who has violated his vow or religious engagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतहरम्
क्षत + -हरम् aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतिः|क्षति
क्षतिः <i>f.</i> [क्षण्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Injury, wound; द्विषां क्षतीर्याः प्रथमे शिलीमुखा विभिद्य देहावरणानि<BR> चक्रिरे Ki. 14. 55.<BR>—2 Destruction, cutting, tearing down; विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षंतिः<BR> पल्वले Ś. 2. 6.<BR>—3 (Fig.) Ruin, loss, disadvantage; सुखं संजायते तेभ्यः सर्वेभ्योपीति<BR> का क्षतिः S. D. 37.<BR>—4 Decline, decay, diminution; प्रतापक्षतिशीतलाः Ku. 2. 24; H. 1. 114.<BR>—5 Death; आचक्षते शुद्धिदमा प्रसूतेरा च क्षते रागमधोक्षजे च Viś. Guṇā. 572.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ <i>m.</i> [क्षद् संज्ञायाम् तृच् Uṇ. 2. 91.]<BR>—1 One who cuts or carves anything; क्षत्ता वामस्य देव भूरेः Rv. 6. 13. 2.<BR>—2 An attendant, a door-keeper; यत् क्षत्तारं ह्वयत्या Av. 9. 6. 1;<BR> मुनिः प्रवेशितः क्षत्रा कन्यान्तःपुरमृद्धिमत् Bhāg. 9. 6. 43; chamberlain; Ks. 52. 106.<BR>—3 A coachman, charioteer; Vāj. 16. 26.<BR>—4 A man born of a Śūdra man and Kṣatriya woman; cf. Ms. 10. 9.<BR>—5 The son of a female slave; (<i>e. g.</i> विदुर); यावतः कृतवान्प्रश्नान्क्षत्ता<BR> कौषारवाग्रतः Bhāg. 1. 13. 2.<BR>—6 Brahmā.<BR>—7 A fish.<BR>—8 One who fights from a chariot.<BR>—9 The manager of a treasure (कोषाध्यक्ष).<BR>—10 A guard (?); Gīrvāṇa.; एवमाघोषयत्क्षत्रा नन्दगोपः स्वगोकुले<BR> Bhāg. 10. 39. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रः|क्षत्र|क्षत्त्रं|क्षत्त्रः|क्षत्रं
क्षत्रः, -त्रम्<BR>—1 Dominion, power, supremacy, might.<BR>—2 A man of the Kṣatriya caste, or the Kṣatriya tribe taken collectively;<BR> क्षतात्किंल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः क्षत्रस्य शब्दो भुवनेषु रुढः R. 2. 53, 11. 69, 71;<BR> असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा Ś. 1. 22; Ms. 9. 322;<BR> ब्राह्मणेनैधितं क्षत्रं मन्त्रिमन्त्राभिमन्त्रितम् । जयत्यजितमत्यन्तम् … Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR>—3 A man of the warrior class, a soldier; क्षत्रप्रताप U. 6. 18;<BR> martial or heroic valour; 6. 16;<BR>—4 Injury, harm (हिंसा); ‘क्षत्रं हिंसा तदर्थं जातं क्षत्रजम्’<BR> -com. of Nīlakaṇṭha on Mb. 12. 189. 5; (क्षत्रजं सेवते कर्म वेदाध्ययनसंगतः ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रम्
क्षत्रः, -त्रम्<BR>—1 Dominion, power, supremacy, might.<BR>—2 A man of the Kṣatriya caste, or the Kṣatriya tribe taken collectively;<BR> क्षतात्किंल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः क्षत्रस्य शब्दो भुवनेषु रुढः R. 2. 53, 11. 69, 71;<BR> असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा Ś. 1. 22; Ms. 9. 322;<BR> ब्राह्मणेनैधितं क्षत्रं मन्त्रिमन्त्राभिमन्त्रितम् । जयत्यजितमत्यन्तम् … Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR>—3 A man of the warrior class, a soldier; क्षत्रप्रताप U. 6. 18;<BR> martial or heroic valour; 6. 16;<BR>—4 Injury, harm (हिंसा); ‘क्षत्रं हिंसा तदर्थं जातं क्षत्रजम्’<BR> -com. of Nīlakaṇṭha on Mb. 12. 189. 5; (क्षत्रजं सेवते कर्म वेदाध्ययनसंगतः ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्री
क्षत्रः, -त्रम् + .{@-त्री@}<BR>—1 A woman of the military caste.<BR>—2 The rank of a member of the military caste.<BR>—3 Wealth.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 The body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षत्रान्तकः, क्षत्रधर्मः, क्षत्रपः, क्षत्रपतिः, क्षत्रबन्धुः, क्षत्रविद्या, क्षत्रवेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रान्तकः|क्षत्रान्तक|क्षत्रांतक
क्षत्रः + -अन्तकः an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रधर्मः|क्षत्रधर्म
क्षत्रः + -धर्मः<BR>—1 bravery, military heroism; क्षत्रधर्महतः Ms. 5. 98.<BR>—2 the duties of a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रपः|क्षत्रप
क्षत्रः + -पः a governor, satrap; (a word found on coins and inscriptions.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रपतिः|क्षत्रपति
क्षत्रः + -पतिः the possessor of dominion; क्षत्राणां क्षत्रपतिः Vāj. 10. 17;<BR> (cf. छत्रपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रबन्धुः|क्षत्रबन्धु|क्षत्त्रबन्धुः|क्षत्रबंधु
क्षत्रः + -बन्धुः<BR>—1 a Kṣatriya by caste; Ms. 2. 38.<BR>—2 a mere Kṣatriya, a vile or wretched Kṣatriya; (as a term of abuse);<BR> cf. ब्रह्मबन्धु; Bhāg. 4. 28. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रविद्या
क्षत्रः + -विद्या, -वेदः the science of the warrior class (क्षत्रिय);<BR> धनुर्वेद; अध्येमि क्षत्रविद्याम् Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2; क्षत्रवेदविदां<BR> श्रेष्ठो ब्रह्मवेदविदामपि Rām. 1. 65. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रवेदः|क्षत्रवेद
क्षत्रः + -विद्या, -वेदः the science of the warrior class (क्षत्रिय);<BR> धनुर्वेद; अध्येमि क्षत्रविद्याम् Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2; क्षत्रवेदविदां<BR> श्रेष्ठो ब्रह्मवेदविदामपि Rām. 1. 65. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिन्
क्षत्रिन् <i>m.</i> A man of the military order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियः|क्षत्रिय|क्षत्त्रियः
क्षत्रियः [क्षत्रे राष्ट्रे साधु तस्यापत्यं जातौ वा घः Tv.]<BR>—1 A member of the military or second caste; धर्म्याद्धि युद्धाच्छ्रेयोऽन्यत्<BR> क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते Bg. 2. 31. ब्राह्मणः क्षत्रियो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">Page0622-1</a>]<BR> वैश्यस्त्रयो वर्णा द्विजातयः Ms. 10. 4. The Mahābhārata (Śāntiparvan)<BR> says; ब्राह्मणानां क्षतत्राणात्ततः क्षत्रिय उच्यते ।<BR>—2 A kind of horse; क्षत्रिया वह्निसंभवाः Śālihotra, Appendix II, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियम्
क्षत्रियः + .{@-यम्@} The rank or power of the Kṣatriya class; Rv. 4. 12. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षत्रियधर्मः, क्षत्रियहनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0621-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियधर्मः|क्षत्रियधर्म
क्षत्रियः + -धर्मः See क्षत्रधमः; Ms. 10. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियहनः
क्षत्रियः + -हनः + ({@-णः@})<BR> an epithet of Paraśurāma; Mb. 5. 178. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियहणः|क्षत्रियहण
क्षत्रियः + -हनः + ({@-णः@})<BR> an epithet of Paraśurāma; Mb. 5. 178. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियका
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman of the Kṣatriya<BR> caste; Mb. 1. 2. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिया
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman of the Kṣatriya<BR> caste; Mb. 1. 2. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियिका
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman of the Kṣatriya<BR> caste; Mb. 1. 2. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियाणी
क्षत्रियाणी [P. IV. 1. 49; Vārt. 7]<BR>—1 A woman of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR>—2 The wife of a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियी
क्षत्रियी The wife of a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्
क्षद् €1 Ā. (क्षदते) Ved.<BR>—1 To cut.<BR>—2 To kill; जारः कनीन इव चक्षदान Rv. 1. 117. 18.<BR>—3 To consume, eat; Rv. 1. 25. 17.<BR>—4 To cover, protect.<BR>—5 To distribute (food); तस्मै घृतं सुरां मध्वन्नमन्नं क्षदामहे Av. 10. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदनम्
क्षदनम्<BR>—1 Carving, dividing, tearing.<BR>—2 Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्मन्
क्षद्मन् <i>n.</i> [क्षद् भक्षणे मनिन्]<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्द्
क्षन्द् See क्षुन्द् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् €1 U. (क्षपति-ते, क्षपित) To fast, to be abstinent; अरण्ये<BR> काष्ठवत्त्यक्त्वा क्षपेयुस्त्र्यहमेव च Ms. 5. 69. ━<i>Caus.</i> or €10 U.<BR> (क्षपयति-ते, क्षपित)<BR>—1 To throw, send, cast.<BR>—2 To miss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपित
क्षपित <i>a.</i> Destroyed, diminished; क्षपिता तद्विटपाश्रया लता<BR> R. 8. 47; Bhāg. 4. 31. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 A measure of time.<BR>—3 Darkness; क्षपो जिन्वन्तः पृषतीभिरृष्टिभिः Rv. 1. 64. 8.<BR>—4 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपः|क्षप
क्षपः Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणः|क्षपण
क्षपणः A Bauddha mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणम्
क्षपणः + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Defilement, impurity (अशौच); सब्रह्मचारिण्येकाहमतीते क्षपणं<BR> स्मृतम् Ms. 5. 71.<BR>—2 Destroying, suppressing, expelling.<BR>—3 Fasting; चतुर्थभक्तक्षपणं वैश्ये शूद्रे विधीयते Mb. 13. 106. 13.<BR>—4 Abstinence, chastisement of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणकः|क्षपणक
क्षपणकः A Bauddha or Jaina mendicant; नग्नक्षपणके देशे रजकः<BR> किं करिष्यति Cāṇ. 110; कथं प्रथममेव क्षपणकः Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी<BR>—1 An oar.<BR>—2 A net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्युः|क्षपण्यु
क्षपण्युः An offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा [क्षपयति चेष्टाम्; क्षि-णिच् अच्]<BR>—1 A night; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 5; R. 2. 2; Me. 112.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षपाटः, क्षपाचरः, क्षपान्ध्यम्, क्षपाकरः, क्षपानाथः, क्षपाघनः, क्षपाचरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाटः|क्षपाट
क्षपा + -अटः, -चरः<BR>—1 night-stalker.<BR>—2 a demon, goblin; ततः क्षपौटः पृथुपिङ्गलाक्षैः Bk. 2. 30, 5. 64, 8. 56;<BR> दनुजः स्विदयं क्षपाचरो वा Ki. 13. 8; Rām. 5. 2. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाचरः|क्षपाचर
क्षपा + -अटः, -चरः<BR>—1 night-stalker.<BR>—2 a demon, goblin; ततः क्षपौटः पृथुपिङ्गलाक्षैः Bk. 2. 30, 5. 64, 8. 56;<BR> दनुजः स्विदयं क्षपाचरो वा Ki. 13. 8; Rām. 5. 2. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपान्ध्यम्
क्षपा + -आन्ध्यम् night-blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाकरः|क्षपाकर
क्षपा + -करः, -नाथः<BR>—1 the moon; क्षिप्रं क्षपानाथ इवाधिरूढः Śi. 3. 22.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपानाथः|क्षपानाथ
क्षपा + -करः, -नाथः<BR>—1 the moon; क्षिप्रं क्षपानाथ इवाधिरूढः Śi. 3. 22.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाघनः|क्षपाघन
क्षपा + -घनः a dark cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाचरः|क्षपाचर
क्षपा + -चरः a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् €1 Ā., €4 P.<BR> (क्षमते, क्षाम्यति, चक्षमे, चक्षाम, क्षान्त or क्षमित)<BR>—1 To permit, allow, suffer; अतो नृपाश्चक्षमिरे समेताः स्त्रीरत्नलाभं<BR> न तदात्मजस्य R. 7. 34, 12. 46.<BR>—2 To pardon, forgive (as an offence); क्षान्तं न क्षमया Bh. 3. 13;<BR> क्षमस्व परमेश्वर; निघ्नस्य मे भर्तृनिदेशरौक्ष्यं देवि क्षमस्वेति<BR> बभूव नम्रः R. 14. 58.<BR>—3 To be patient or quiet, wait; स मुहूर्तं क्षमस्वेति (v. l. सहस्वेति)<BR> द्विजमाश्वास्य दुःखितम् R. 15. 45.<BR>—4 To endure, put up with, suffer; अपि क्षमन्तेऽस्मदुपजापं प्रकृतयः<BR> Mu. 2; नाज्ञाभङ्गकरान् राजा क्षमेत स्वसुतानपि H. 2. 105.<BR>—5 To oppose, resist; Rām. 7. 58. 6.<BR>—6 To be competent or able (to do anything); ऋते रवेः क्षालयितुं क्षमेत<BR> कः क्षपातमस्काण्डमलीमसं नभः Śi. 1. 38, 9. 65. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To beg pardon, forgive; एकोऽथवाप्यच्युत तत्समक्षं तत्क्षामये त्वामहमप्रमेयम् Bg. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तव्य|क्षंतव्य
क्षन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be borne or endured.<BR>—2 Pardonable, fit to be forgiven; उक्तं मया प्राक्क्षन्तव्यमेतस्मान्मेऽपराधतः Ks. 119. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तृ|क्षंतृ
क्षन्तृ <i>a.</i> [क्षम्-तृच्] Patient, enduring, forbearing, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् <i>f.</i> Ved. The ground, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम <i>a.</i> [क्षम्-अच्]<BR>—1 Patient (said of the earth); विमृग्वरीं पृथिवीमा वदामि क्षमां भूमिं<BR> ब्रह्मणा वावृधानाम् Av. 12. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Enduring, submissive; अतोऽत्र किंचिद्भवतीं बहुक्षमाम् Ku. 5. 40.<BR>—3 Adequate, competent, able (with gen., loc., inf. or in comp.) मलिनो<BR> हि यथादर्शो रूपालोकस्य न क्षमः Y. 3. 141; सा हि रक्षणविधौ तयोः<BR> क्षमा R. 11. 6; हृदयं न त्ववलम्बितुं क्षमाः R. 8. 60; गमनक्षम,<BR> निर्मूलनक्षम &c.<BR>—4 Appropriate, fit, proper, suitable; तन्नो यदुक्तमशिवं न हि तत्क्षमं<BR> ते U. 1. 14; आत्मकर्मक्षमं देहं क्षात्रो धर्म इवाश्रितः R. 1. 13; Ś. 5. 27.<BR>—5 Fit for, capable of, suited to; उपभोगक्षमे देशे V. 2; तपःक्षमं<BR> साधयितुं य इच्छति Ś. 1. 18; स्पर्शक्षमं रत्नम् 1. 27, 7. 5.<BR>—6 Bearable, endurable.<BR>—7 Favourable, friendly.<BR>—8 Worthy; यूयमेव स्तवक्षमाः Mv. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमम्
क्षम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Propriety, fitness.<BR>—2 Battle, war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमः|क्षम|क्षमं
क्षम + .{@-मः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमणीय
क्षमणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be borne, patiently borne.<BR>—2 To be pardoned or forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमा
क्षमा [क्षम्-अङ्]<BR>—1 Patience, forbearance, forgiveness; क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः Bg. 10. 4, 34, 16. 3;<BR> क्षमा शत्रौ च मित्रे च यतीनामेव भूषणम् H. 2;<BR> R. 1. 22, 18. 9; तेजः क्षमा वा नैकान्तं कालज्ञस्य महीपतेः Śi. 2. 83.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR>—3 The number ‘one’.<BR>—4 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षमाजः, क्षमाभुज्, क्षमाभुजः, क्षमाभृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाजः|क्षमाज
क्षमा + -जः the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाभुज्
क्षमा + -भुज्, -भुजः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाभुजः|क्षमाभुज
क्षमा + -भुज्, -भुजः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाभृत्
क्षमा + -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a mountain.<BR>—2 a prince; प्रातिष्ठन्त क्षमाभृताम् Śi. 19. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमावत्|क्षमावन्त्
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Patient, indulgent.<BR>—2 Knowing what is proper or right; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमान्वित
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Patient, indulgent.<BR>—2 Knowing what is proper or right; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमायुक्त
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Patient, indulgent.<BR>—2 Knowing what is proper or right; Rām. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापयति
क्षमापयति Den. P. To ask any oneʼs pardon, beg pardon; क्षमापय<BR> महाभागं ततः शान्तिर्भविष्यति Bhāg. 9. 4. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापनम्
क्षमापनम् Begging pardon. क्षमापनैश्च सा देवी प्रसन्नवदनाम्बुजा<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0622-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितृ
क्षमितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>), क्षमिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Patient, forbearing, of a forgiving nature; समदुःखसुखः क्षमी<BR> Bg. 12. 13. कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी Śi. 2. 43; Y. 2. 200, 1. 133.<BR>—2 Capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमित्री
क्षमितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>), क्षमिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Patient, forbearing, of a forgiving nature; समदुःखसुखः क्षमी<BR> Bg. 12. 13. कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी Śi. 2. 43; Y. 2. 200, 1. 133.<BR>—2 Capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमिन्
क्षमितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>), क्षमिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Patient, forbearing, of a forgiving nature; समदुःखसुखः क्षमी<BR> Bg. 12. 13. कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी Śi. 2. 43; Y. 2. 200, 1. 133.<BR>—2 Capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमिणी
क्षमितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>), क्षमिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Patient, forbearing, of a forgiving nature; समदुःखसुखः क्षमी<BR> Bg. 12. 13. कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी Śi. 2. 43; Y. 2. 200, 1. 133.<BR>—2 Capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्य
क्षम्य <i>a.</i> Being in the earth, terrestrial; यः पार्थिवस्य क्षम्यस्य<BR> राजा Rv. 2. 14. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त <i>p. p.</i> [क्षम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Patient, forbearing, enduring.<BR>—2 Forgiven.<BR>—3 Borne, endured.<BR>—4 Friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तः|क्षान्त|क्षांत
क्षान्त + .{@-तः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्ता|क्षांता
क्षान्त + .{@-ता@} The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तम्
क्षान्त + .{@-तम्@} Patience, indulgence; Rām. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तिः|क्षान्ति|क्षांति|क्षांतिः
क्षान्तिः <i>f.</i> [क्षम्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Patience, forbearance, forgiveness; क्षान्तिश्चेद्वचनेन किम् Bh. 2. 21;<BR> अहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम् Bg. 13. 7, 18. 42.<BR>—2 The state of saintly abstraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तु|क्षांतु|क्षान्तुः
क्षान्तु <i>a.</i> [क्षम्-तुन् वृद्धिश्च] Patient, forbearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तुः|क्षान्तु|क्षांतु
क्षान्तु + .{@-तुः@} A father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम्य
क्षाम्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be borne.<BR>—2 To be pardoned or forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्प्
क्षम्प् €10 P. To forgive; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
क्षय See under क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर्
क्षर् €1 P. [क्षरति-क्षरित] (Used transitively or intransitively)<BR>—1 To flow, glide.<BR>—2 To send or stream forth, pour out, emit; तेषु क्षरत्सु बहुधा मदवारिधाराः<BR> R. 13. 74; Bk. 9. 8.<BR>—3 To drop, trickle, ooze.<BR>—4 To waste away, wane, perish.<BR>—5 To become useless, have no effect; यज्ञोऽनृतेन क्षरति तपः क्षरति<BR> विस्मयात् Ms. 4. 237.<BR>—6 To melt.<BR>—7 To slip from, be deprived of (with abl.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (क्षारयति-ते)<BR> To accuse, traduce (usually with आ). ━<i>With</i> {@वि@} to melt away, dissolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर <i>a.</i> [क्षरति स्यन्दते मुञ्चति बा, क्षर्-अच्]<BR>—1 Melting away.<BR>—2 Movable.<BR>—3 Perishable; क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थो ऽक्षर उच्यते Bg. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरः|क्षर|क्षरं
क्षर + .{@-रः@} A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरम्
क्षर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 The body; ततः सवेदनः सद्यो जीवः प्रच्यवते क्षरात् Mb. 14. 17. 17.<BR>—3 Ignorance.<BR>—4 The Supreme Being.<BR>—5 Cause and effect.<BR>—6 The natural form (प्रकृति); अक्षरक्षरयोरेव द्वयोः सम्बन्ध<BR> इष्यते Mb. 12. 305. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षरात्मक, क्षरजः, क्षरभाव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरात्मक
क्षर + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> Of a perishable nature, perishable; Mārk. P. 23. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरजः|क्षरज
क्षर + -जः (also क्षरेज) <i>a.</i> produced by distillation or from a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरभाव
क्षर + -भाव <i>a.</i> mutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरणम्
क्षरणम् [क्षर्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of flowing, trickling, dropping, oozing.<BR>—2 The act of perspiring; अङ्गुलीक्षरणसन्नवर्तिकः R. 19. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरित
क्षरित <i>p. p.</i> Dropped, liquefied, oozed, melted &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरिन्
क्षरिन् <i>m.</i> The rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार <i>a.</i> [क्षर्-ज्वला बा˚ ण]<BR>—1 Corrosive, caustic, acid, pungent, saline.<BR>—2 Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारः|क्षार|क्षारं
क्षार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Juice, essence.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">Page0623-2</a>]<BR>—2 Treacle, molasses.<BR>—3 Any corrosive or acid substances; क्षते क्षारमिवासह्यं जातं तस्यैव<BR> दर्शनम् U. 4. 7; क्षारं क्षते प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18; (क्षारं क्षते<BR> क्षिप् &c. has become proverbial, and means ‘to aggravate the pain which is already unbearable’<BR>, ‘to make bad, worse’, ‘to add insult to injury’).<BR>—4 Glass.<BR>—5 Salt; caustic alkali; Y. 3. 36.<BR>—6 Ashes.<BR>—7 A rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारम्
क्षार + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Black salt.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 See क्षारः (3); आः क्षते क्षारमेतन्मे क्षिप्तं केनेत्यभाषत Ks. 93. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षाराच्छम्, क्षाराञ्जनम्, क्षाराम्बु, क्षाराष्टकम्, क्षारोदः, क्षारोदकः, क्षारोदधिः, क्षारसमुद्रः, क्षारसिन्धुः, क्षारकर्दमः, क्षारक्षत, क्षारतैलम्, क्षारत्रयम्, क्षारत्रितयम्, क्षारदशकम्, क्षारनदी, क्षारपञ्चकम्, क्षारभूमिः, क्षारमेलकः, क्षाररसः, क्षारश्रेष्ठम्, क्षारषट्कम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराच्छम्
क्षार + -अच्छम् sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराञ्जनम्
क्षार + -अञ्जनम् an alkaline unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराम्बु|क्षारांबु
क्षार + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> an alkaline fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराष्टकम्
क्षार + -अष्टकम् N. of a collection of eight articles [Mar. पळस<BR> (Butea frondose), निवडुंग (Cactus Indicus), सर्जी (Saltpetre),<BR> चिंच (Tamarind), आघाडा (Achryanthes Aspara), रुई, तिलनाल,<BR> जव (Nitrate of Potash)].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारोदः|क्षारोद
क्षार + -उदः, -उदकः, -उदधिः, -समुद्रः, -सिन्धुः the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारोदकः|क्षारोदक
क्षार + -उदः, -उदकः, -उदधिः, -समुद्रः, -सिन्धुः the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारोदधिः|क्षारोदधि
क्षार + -उदः, -उदकः, -उदधिः, -समुद्रः, -सिन्धुः the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारसमुद्रः|क्षारसमुद्र
क्षार + -उदः, -उदकः, -उदधिः, -समुद्रः, -सिन्धुः the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारसिन्धुः|क्षारसिन्धु
क्षार + -उदः, -उदकः, -उदधिः, -समुद्रः, -सिन्धुः the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारकर्दमः|क्षारकर्दम
क्षार + -कर्दमः<BR>—1 a pool of saline mud.<BR>—2 N. of a hell; Bhāg. 5. 26. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारक्षत
क्षार + -क्षत <i>a.</i> damaged by saltpetre; Mk. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारतैलम्
क्षार + -तैलम् oil cooked with alkaline ingredients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारत्रयम्
क्षार + -त्रयम्, -त्रितयम् natron, salt-petre and borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारत्रितयम्
क्षार + -त्रयम्, -त्रितयम् natron, salt-petre and borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारदशकम्
क्षार + -दशकम् N. of a collection of ten plants (Mar. शेवगा, मुळा,<BR> पळस, चिंच, चुका, आलें, निंब, आघाडा, ऊंस, कदली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारनदी
क्षार + -नदी a river of alkaline water in hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारपञ्चकम्
क्षार + -पञ्चकम् N. of a collection of five articles (Mar. जव, पुष्कर,<BR> सर्जी, पळस and तिलनाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारभूमिः|क्षारभूमि
क्षार + -भूमिः <i>f.</i>, {@-मृत्तिका@}<BR> saline soil; किमाश्चर्यं क्षारभूमौ प्राणदा यमदूतिका Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारमेलकः|क्षारमेलक
क्षार + -मेलकः an alkaline substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाररसः|क्षाररस
क्षार + -रसः a saline flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारश्रेष्ठम्
क्षार + -श्रेष्ठम् alkaline earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारषट्कम्
क्षार + -षट्कम् N. of a collection of six plants (Mar. गुळवेल, कुडा,<BR> आघाडा, कळलावी, पुष्करमूल, तिलनाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारकः|क्षारक
क्षारकः [क्षर्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Alkali.<BR>—2 Juice, essence.<BR>—3 A cage, basket or net for birds; स वै क्षारकमादाय द्विजान् हत्वा<BR> वने सदा Mb. 12. 143. 15.<BR>—4 A washerman.<BR>—5 A blossom; a bud or new-blown flower (कलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारणम्
क्षारणम्, -णा<BR> Accusing, especially of adultery<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारणा
क्षारणम्, -णा<BR> Accusing, especially of adultery<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारणम्
क्षारणम्, -णा + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Converting to alkali or ashes.<BR>—2 Distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारयति
क्षारयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To furnish or mix with acid substances.<BR>—2 To torture a person with acid substances.<BR>—3 To speak ill of a person, accuse.<BR>—4 To abuse, calumniate, traduce, censure; cf. आक्षर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारिका
क्षारिका Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारित|क्षारितः
क्षारित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distilled from saline matter.<BR>—2 Falsely accused (especially of adultery).<BR>—3 Accused of a crime, calumniated; कच्चिदार्योऽपि शुद्धात्मा क्षारितश्चापकर्मणा<BR> Rām. 2. 100. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल्
क्षल् €10 U. (क्षालयति-ते, क्षालित)<BR>—1 To wash, wash off, purify, cleanse; ऋते रवेः क्षालयितुं क्षमेत<BR> कः क्षपातमस्काण्डमलीमसं नभः Śi. 1. 38; H. 4. 60.<BR>—2 To wipe away. ━<i>With</i> {@वि@} to wash off; निःशेषविक्षालितधातुनापि R. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाल
क्षाल <i>a.</i> Cleaning, washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनम्
क्षालनम् [क्षल्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Washing, cleansing (with water); तत्क्षालनाय यास्यामि तीर्थान्युज्झितमत्सरः Ks. 52. 239.<BR>—2 Sprinkling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षालनयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनयन्त्रम्
क्षालनम् + -यन्त्रम् an apparatus for washing clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0623-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालित|क्षालितं
क्षालित <i>p. p.</i> [क्षल्-क्त]<BR>—1 Washed, cleansed, purified,<BR>—2 Wiped away, requited; तथा वृत्तं पापैर्व्यथयति यथा क्षालितमपि<BR> U. 1. 28; Rāj. T. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवः|क्षव
क्षवः, क्षवथुः See under क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथुः|क्षवथु
क्षवः, क्षवथुः See under क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षा
क्षा <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 Sleep; क्षा स्त्री क्षमायां निद्रायाम् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाणम्
क्षाणम् Burning, what is burnt; निमित्तं हि उपसंप्राप्तं क्षाणं<BR> नाम ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 18; एकदेशक्षाणमपि क्षाणमेव ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्र
क्षात्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>) [क्षत्रस्य कर्म भावो वा अण्]<BR> Relating or peculiar to the military tribe; क्षात्रो धर्मः श्रित इव<BR> तनुं ब्रह्मघोषस्य गुप्त्यै U. 6. 9; R. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्रम्
क्षात्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 The Kṣatriya tribe.<BR>—2 The qualifications of a Kṣatriya; the Gītā thus describes them:−<BR> -शौर्यं तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनम् । दानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं<BR> कर्म स्वभावजम् Bg. 18. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्रिः|क्षात्रि
क्षात्रिः The son of a Kṣatriya by a woman of another caste; P. IV. 1. 138. Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त &c. See under क्षम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम <i>a.</i> [क्षै-कर्तरि क्त क्षायो मः P. VIII. 2. 53]<BR>—1 Scorched, singed.<BR>—2 Diminished, thin, wasted; emaciated, lean; क्षामक्षामकपोलमाननम्<BR> Ś. 3. 9; मध्ये क्षामा Me. 84; क्षामच्छायं भवनमधुना मद्वियोगेन<BR> नूनम् 82, 91.<BR>—3 Slight, little, small.<BR>—4 Weak, infirm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामः|क्षाम
क्षाम + .{@-मः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामा
क्षाम + .{@-मा@} The earth; द्यावा ह क्षामा Mbh. on P. I. 2. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामम्
क्षाम + .{@-मम्@} Destruction.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षामास्यम्, क्षामेष्टिन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामास्यम्
क्षाम + -आस्यम् unwholesome diet; अपथ्यमहितं रोग्यं क्षामास्यं परिकीर्तितम्<BR> (शब्दचन्द्रिका)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामेष्टिन्यायः
क्षाम + -इष्टिन्यायः The rule according to which a conditional cause laying<BR> down a निमित्त must be so construed as to avoid it involving a नित्य<BR> or unavoidable circumstance. This is discussed and established by Jaimini<BR> and Śabara in MS. 6. 4. 17-21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामन्
क्षामन्^1 <i>a.</i> [क्षै-मनिन्] Destructive. ━<i>n.</i> Ved. The earth, ground.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: manin affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामवत्|क्षामवन्त्
क्षामवत् <i>a.</i> Ved. Scorching, withering, drying; an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारः|क्षार|क्षारं
क्षारः &c. See under क्षर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनम्
क्षालनम् &c. See under क्षल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि I. €1 P. (क्षयति, क्षित or क्षीण)<BR>—1 To decay or waste.<BR>—2 To rule, govern, be master of; भरद्वाजेषु क्षयदिन्मघोनः Rv. 6. 23. 10.<BR>━II. €1. €5. €9 P. (क्षयति, क्षिणोति, क्षिणाति)<BR>—1 To destroy, affect, ruin, corrupt; न तद्यशः शस्त्रभृतां क्षिणोति R. 2.<BR>—2 To diminish, cause to waste away; दक्षशाप इव चन्द्रमक्षिणोत् R. 19. 48.<BR>—3 To kill, injure.<BR>—4 To spend, pass (as time); कति पुनरहं वासराणि क्षयिष्ये Ud. S. 83.<BR>━III. €6 P. (क्षियति)<BR>—1 To abide, stay, dwell. यस्मिन् क्षियन्ति भुवनानि विश्वा Nṛ. P. Up. 2. 4.<BR>—2 To inhabit.<BR>—3 To remain.<BR>—4 To go, move, approach.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">Page0624-2</a>]<BR>━<i>Pass.</i> (क्षीयते) To waste, wane; decay, be diminished (fig.<BR> also) प्रतिक्षणमयं कायः क्षीयमाणो न लक्ष्यते H. 4. 66; प्रत्यासन्नविपत्तिमूढमनसां<BR> प्रायो मतिः क्षीयते Pt. 2. 4; Amaru. 93; Bh. 2. 19. ━<i>Caus.</i> (क्षययति<BR> or क्षपयति)<BR>—1 To destroy, remove, put an end to; ममापि च क्षपयतु नीललोहितः<BR> पुनर्भवं परिगतशक्तिरात्मभूः Ś. 7. 35; R. 8. 47; Me. 55.<BR>—2 To spend or pass (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयः|क्षय
क्षयः [क्षि-अच्]<BR>—1 A house, residence, abode; यातनाश्च यमक्षये Ms. 6. 61; निर्जगाम<BR> पुनस्तस्मात्क्षयान्नारायणस्य ह Mb.<BR>—2 Loss, decline, waste, wane, decay, diminution; आयुषः क्षयः R. 3. 69;<BR> धनक्षये वर्धति जाठराग्निः Pt. 2. 186; so चन्द्रक्षयः,<BR> क्षयपक्षः &c.<BR>—3 Destruction, end, termination; निशाक्षये याति ह्रियैव पाण्डुताम्<BR> Ṛs. 1. 9; Amaru. 60.<BR>—4 Pecuniary loss; Ms. 8. 401.<BR>—5 Fall (as of prices.)<BR>—6 Removal.<BR>—7 Universal destruction (प्रलय).<BR>—8 Consumption.<BR>—9 A disease in general.<BR>—10 The negative sign or quantity, minus (in algebra).<BR>—11 Family, race.<BR>—12 The house of Yama.<BR>—13 A part of the elephantʼs knee (गजजानुभागविशेषः); Mātaṅga L. 5. 15.<BR>—14 Power (क्षि क्षयैश्वर्ययोरित्यैश्वर्यार्थस्य क्षिधातो रूपम् -Com.<BR> on Mb. 12. 303. 2); उपपद्यति संयोगाद् गुणैः सह गुणक्षयात् <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयम्
क्षयः + .{@-यम्@} N. of the last year in the sixty years cycle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षयोपशमः, क्षयकर, क्षयकालः, क्षयकासः, क्षयतिथिः, क्षयपक्षः, क्षयमासः, क्षययुक्तिः, क्षयरोगः, क्षयवायुः, क्षयसंपद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयोपशमः|क्षयोपशम
क्षयः + -उपशमः complete annihilation of the desire of being active (Jaina).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकर
क्षयः + -कर (also क्षयंकर) <i>a.</i> causing decay or destruction, ruinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकालः|क्षयकाल
क्षयः + -कालः<BR>—1 time of universal destruction. —2 the period of decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकासः|क्षयकास
क्षयः + -कासः consumptive cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयतिथिः
क्षयः + -तिथिः, <i>f.</i> {@क्षयाहः@} the lunar day not beginning with<BR> the sun-rise, hence omitted in the calendar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयपक्षः|क्षयपक्ष
क्षयः + -पक्षः the dark fortnight. क्षयपक्ष इवैन्दवीः कलाः सकला<BR> हन्ति स शक्तिसंपदः Ki. 2. 37.<BR>—2 a fortnight of 13 days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयमासः|क्षयमास
क्षयः + -मासः the month in which two संक्रान्तिs occur and which is<BR> omitted in the adjustment of the lunar-solar calendar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षययुक्तिः|क्षययुक्ति
क्षयः + -युक्तिः <i>f.</i>, {@-योगः@}<BR> an opportunity of destroying; Ki. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोगः|क्षयरोग
क्षयः + -रोगः consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयवायुः|क्षयवायु
क्षयः + -वायुः the wind that is to blow at the destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयसंपद्|क्षयसम्पद्
क्षयः + -संपद् <i>f.</i> total loss, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयण|क्षयणः
क्षयण <i>a.</i> Destroying &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयणः|क्षयण
क्षयण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A place with calm water.<BR>—2 A bay or harbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयणम्
क्षयण + .{@-णम्@} A dwelling-place, habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथुः|क्षयथु
क्षयथुः Consumptive cough, consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयस्
क्षयस् <i>n.</i> A dwelling-place, habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिन्
क्षयिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Diminishing, decaying; आरम्भगुर्वी क्षयिणी क्रमेण Bh. 2. 60;<BR> waning, wasting; न चाभूत्ताविव क्षयी R. 17. 71; Ms. 9. 314.<BR>—2 Consumptive.<BR>—3 Perishable, fragile. ━<i>m.</i> The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिष्णु
क्षयिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wasting, decaying.<BR>—2 Perishable, fragile; सर्वं चेदं क्षयिष्णु पश्यामः Maitr. Up. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिः|क्षि
क्षिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Abode.<BR>—2 Going.<BR>—3 Destruction.<BR>—4 Waste, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0624-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्
क्षित् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Ruling, a ruler; उताहो हतवीर्यास्ते बभूवुः पृथिवीक्षितः Rām. 7. 31. 4.<BR>—2 Dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित|क्षितः
क्षित <i>p. p.</i> [क्षि-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Wasted, decayed, lost.<BR>—2 Weakened.<BR>—3 Poor, miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितम्
क्षित + .{@-तम्@} Killing; injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिता
क्षिता The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिः|क्षिति
क्षितिः <i>f.</i> [क्षि निवासे आधारे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 The earth, soil of the earth; Mb. 4.<BR>—2 A dwelling, an abode, a house; तं भक्तिभावोऽभ्यगृणादसत्वरं परिश्रुतोरुश्रवसं<BR> ध्रुवक्षितिः Bhāg. 4. 9. 5.<BR>—3 Loss, destruction.<BR>—4 The end of the world.<BR>—5 Wane.<BR>—6 A man (Ved.)<BR>—7 Prosperity; क्षिते रोहः प्रवहः शश्वदेव Mb. 13. 76. 10.<BR>—8 Number ‘one’; Bīj.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: क्षित्यदितिः, क्षितीशः, क्षितीश्वरः, क्षितिकणः, क्षितिकम्पः, क्षितिक्षित्, क्षितिजः, क्षितिरुहः, क्षितिसुतः, क्षितितलम्, क्षितित्राणम्, क्षितिदेवः, क्षितिसुरः, क्षितिधरः, क्षितिधेनुः, क्षितिनाथः, क्षितिपः, क्षितिपतिः, क्षितिपालः, क्षितिभुज्, क्षितिपुत्रः, क्षितिप्रतिष्ठ, क्षितिभृत्, क्षितिमण्डलम्, क्षितिरन्ध्रम्, क्षितिवर्धनः, क्षितिवृत्तिः, क्षितिव्युदासः, क्षितिसंक्रन्दनः, क्षितिस्पृश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्यदितिः|क्षित्यदिति
क्षितिः + -अदितिः an epithet of Devakī, mother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीशः|क्षितीश
क्षितिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः a king; R. 1. 5; तदाननं मृत्सुरभिक्षितीक्षरो<BR> रहस्युपाघ्राय न तृप्तिमाययौ 3. 3, 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीश्वरः|क्षितीश्वर
क्षितिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः a king; R. 1. 5; तदाननं मृत्सुरभिक्षितीक्षरो<BR> रहस्युपाघ्राय न तृप्तिमाययौ 3. 3, 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिकणः|क्षितिकण
क्षितिः + -कणः dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिकम्पः|क्षितिकम्प|क्षितिकंप
क्षितिः + -कम्पः an earth-quake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिक्षित्
क्षितिः + -क्षित् <i>m.</i> a king, prince; Śi. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0625-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

