गन्धोली|गंधोली
गन्धोली<BR>—1 A wasp; गन्धोलिपालीगृहसिक्थकुम्भात् Rām. Ch. 6. 89.<BR>—2 Dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभः|गभ
गभः Ved.<BR>—1 A slit, cleft.<BR>—2 The vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिः|गभस्ति
गभस्तिः <i>m., f.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light, a sunbeam or moonbeam; यथा राजन्प्रजाः सर्वाः सूर्यः<BR> पाति गभस्तिभिः Mb. 3. 33. 71.<BR>—2 Ved. The shaft (of a car).<BR>—3 The forepart of the arm, the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिः|गभस्ति
गभस्तिः + .{@-स्तिः@} The sun. ━<i>f.</i> An epithet of Svāhā, the wife of Agni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गभस्तिकरः, गभस्तिपाणिः, गभस्तिमालिन्, गभस्तिनेमिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिकरः|गभस्तिकर
गभस्तिः + -करः, -पाणिः, -मालिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-हस्तः, -मत्@} <i>m.</i><BR> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिपाणिः|गभस्तिपाणि
गभस्तिः + -करः, -पाणिः, -मालिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-हस्तः, -मत्@} <i>m.</i><BR> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिमालिन्
गभस्तिः + -करः, -पाणिः, -मालिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-हस्तः, -मत्@} <i>m.</i><BR> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिनेमिः|गभस्तिनेमि
गभस्तिः + -नेमिः N. of Viṣṇu; Mb. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिमत्|गभस्तिमन्त्
गभस्तिमत् <i>m.</i> The sun; घनव्यपायेन गभस्तिमानिव R. 3. 37.<BR>━<i>n.</i> One of the seven divisions of Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीर|गभीरं
गभीर <i>a.^1</i> [गच्छति जलमत्र, गभ् ईरन् भान्तादेशश्च Uṇ. 4. 35]<BR>—1 Deep (in all senses); उत्तालास्त इमे गभीरपयसः पुण्याः सरित्संगमाः<BR> U. 2. 30; Bv. 2. 105.<BR>—2 Deep-sounding (as a drum).<BR>—3 Thick, dense, impervious (as a forest); Ki. 14. 39.<BR>—4 Profound, sagacious.<BR>—5 Grave, serious, solemn, earnest.<BR>—6 Secret, mysterious.<BR>—7 Inscrutable, difficult to be perceived or understood; गभीरमर्थं<BR> कतिचित्प्रकाशताम् (नयन्ति) Ki. 14. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गभीरात्मन्, गभीरवेध<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरात्मन्
गभीर + -आत्मन् the Supreme Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरवेध
गभीर + -वेध <i>a.</i> very penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरिका
गभीरिका<BR>—1 A large drum with a deep sound.<BR>—2 A gong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभोलिकः|गभोलिक
गभोलिकः A small round pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्
गम् €1 P. (गच्छति, जगाम, अगमत्, गमिष्यति, गन्तुम्, गत <i>desid.</i>;<BR> जिगमिषति, जिगांसते Ātm.; <i>freq.</i> जङ्गम्यते; जङ्गमीति<BR> or जङ्गन्ति)<BR>—1 To go, move in general; गच्छत्वार्या पुनर्दर्शनाय V. 5; गच्छति<BR> पुरः शरीरं धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं चेतः Ś. 1. 33; क्वाधुना गम्यते<BR> ‘where art thou going’.<BR>—2 To depart, go forth, go away, set forth or out; उत्क्षिप्यैनां ज्योतिरेकं<BR> जगाम Ś. 5. 3.<BR>—3 To go to, reach, resort to, arrive at, approach; यदगम्योऽपि गम्यते<BR> Pt. 1. 7; एनो गच्छति कर्तारम् Ms. 8. 19 the sin goes to (recoils<BR> on) the doer; 4. 199; so धरणिं मूर्ध्ना गम् &c.<BR>—4 To pass, pass away, elapse (as time); दिनेषु गच्छत्सु R. 3. 8 as<BR> days rolled on, in course of time; Me. 85; काव्यशास्त्रविनोदेन कालो<BR> गच्छति धीमताम् H. 1. 1; गच्छता कालेन in the long run.<BR>—5 To go to the state or condition of, become, undergo, suffer, partake<BR> of &c. (usually joined with nouns ending<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">Page0648-2</a>]<BR> in<BR> -ता, -त्व &c. or any noun in the acc.); गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम्<BR> R. 1. 3; पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी जगाम Ku. 1. 26 went by or received<BR> the name of Umā; so तृप्तिं गच्छति becomes satisfied; विषादं गतः<BR> became dejected; कोपं न गच्छति does not become angry; आनृण्यं<BR> गतः became released from debt; मनसा गम् to think of, remember;<BR> Ku. 2. 63; वृषेण गच्छतः riding a bull; Ku. 5. 80.<BR>—6 To cohabit, have sexual intercourse with; गुरोः सुतां … यो<BR> गच्छति पुमान् Pt. 2. 107; Y. 1. 80. ━<i>Caus.</i> (गमयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to go, lead or reduce to (as a state); गमितः गतिम् Ku. 4. 24;<BR> Bh. 3. 38; Ki. 2. 7.<BR>—2 To spend, pass (as time).<BR>—3 To make clear, explain, expound.<BR>—4 To signify, denote, convey an idea or sense of; द्वौ नञौ प्रकृतार्थं<BR> गमयतः ‘two negatives make one affirmative’.<BR>—5 To send to.<BR>—6 To bring to a place (acc.).<BR>—7 To impart, grant, bestow.<BR>—8 To intend, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत|गतं
गत <i>p. p.</i> [गम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Gone, departed, gone for ever; Mu. 1. 25; किं गते सलिले सेतुबन्धेन,<BR> किं गते विवाहे नक्षत्रपरीक्षया Vb. 4 ‘what is the use of locking the stable-door when the steed is stolen?’<BR>—2 Passed away, elapsed, past; गतायां रात्रौ.<BR>—3 Dead, deceased, departed to the next world; गत एव न ते निवर्तते Ku. 4. 30.<BR>—4 Gone to, arrived at, reaching to.<BR>—5 Being in, situated in, resting on, contained in; usually in comp.;<BR> प्रासादप्रान्तगतः Pt. 1 seated on &c.; सदोगतः R. 3. 66 seated<BR> in the assembly; भर्तारं गता Ś. 4. 13 united to a husband; so आद्य˚;<BR> सर्वगत existing everywhere.<BR>—6 Fallen into, reduced to; <i>e. g.</i> आपद्गतः<BR>—7 Referring or relating to, with regard to, about, concerning, connected<BR> with (usually in comp.); राजा शकुन्तलागतमेव चिन्तयति Ś. 5; भर्तृगतया<BR> चिन्तया Ś. 4; वयमपि भवत्यौ सखीगतं किमपि पृच्छामः Ś. 1;<BR> so पुत्रगतः स्नेहः &c.<BR>—8 Frequented, resorted to; सुहृद्˚ Ku. 4. 24.<BR>—9 Known, celebrated.<BR>—10 Directed towards, belonging to.<BR>—11 Known, understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतम्
गत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Motion, going; गतमुपरि घनानां वारिगर्भोदराणाम् Ś. 7. 7; Śi. 1. 2, 7. 4.<BR>—2 Gait, manner of going; Ku. 1. 34; हंस प्रयच्छ मे कान्ता गतिरस्यास्त्वया<BR> हृता V. 4. 16.<BR>—3 An event.<BR>—4 The place where one has gone.<BR>—5 Celebration, being known, diffusion; यावन्नाम्नो गतम् Ch. Up. 7. 1. 5.<BR>—6 Manner. (As first member of comp. translated by ‘free from’, ‘bereft of’<BR>, ‘deprived of’, ‘without’.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गताक्ष, गताध्वन्, गतानुगतम्, गतानुगतिक, गतान्त, गतार्थ, गतासु, गतजीवित, गतप्राण, गतागतम्, गताधि, गतायुस्, गतार्तवा, गतोत्साह, गतौजस्, गतकल्मष, गतक्लम, गतचेतन, गतत्रप, गतदिनम्, गतदिवसः, गतदिनम्, गतप्रत्यागत, गतप्रभ, गतप्राण, गतप्राय, गतभर्तृका, गतमनस्क, गतलक्ष्मीक, गतवयस्, गतवयस्क, गतवर्षः, गतवर्षम्, गतवैर, गतव्यथ, गतशैशव, गतश्रम, गतसङ्ग, गतसत्त्व, गतसन्नकः, गतस्पृह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गताक्ष
गत + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> sightless, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गताध्वन्
गत + -अध्वन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has accomplished or finished a journey; बलैरध्युषितास्तस्य<BR> विजिगीषोर्गताध्वनः R. 4. 46, 11. 33.<BR>—2 conversant, familiar (with anything); त्रिविधे मोक्षधर्मेऽस्मिन्गताध्वा<BR> छिन्नसंशयः Mb. 12. 320. 25. ━(<i>f.</i>) the time immediately preceding<BR> new moon when a small streak of the moon is still visible; (चतुर्दशीयुक्ताऽमावास्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतानुगतम्
गत + -अनुगतम् following custom or precedent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतानुगतिक
गत + -अनुगतिक <i>a.</i> doing as others do, a blind follower; गतानुगतिको<BR> लोको न लोकः पारमार्थिकः Pt. 1. 342 ‘people are blind followers or servile imitators’<BR>; Mu. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतान्त|गतांत
गत + -अन्त <i>a.</i> one whose end has arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्थ
गत + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 poor.<BR>—2 meaningless (the meaning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">Page0649-1</a>]<BR> being already expressed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0648-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतासु
गत + -असु, -जीवित, -प्राण <i>a.</i> expired, dead; गतासूनगतासूंश्च<BR> नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः Bg. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतजीवित
गत + -असु, -जीवित, -प्राण <i>a.</i> expired, dead; गतासूनगतासूंश्च<BR> नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः Bg. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्राण
गत + -असु, -जीवित, -प्राण <i>a.</i> expired, dead; गतासूनगतासूंश्च<BR> नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः Bg. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतागतम्
गत + -आगतम्<BR>—1 going and coming, frequent visits; आदित्यस्य गतागतैरहरहः संक्षीयते<BR> जीवितम् Bh. 3. 7; Bg. 9. 21; Mu. 2. 3, 4. 1.<BR>—2 interchange of place; कष्टं स्मरामि तव तानि गतागतानि Māl. 9. 47.<BR>—3 the flight of a bird backward and forward.<BR>—4 irregular course of the stars (in astronomy).<BR>—5 Narration of past and future; स सर्वमखिलं राज्ञो वंशस्याह गतागतम्<BR> Rām. 7. 51. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गताधि
गत + -आधि <i>a.</i> free from anxiety, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतायुस्
गत + -आयुस् <i>a.</i> decrepit, infirm, very old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्तवा|गतार्त्तवा
गत + -आर्तवा<BR>—1 a woman past her child-bearing.<BR>—2 a barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतोत्साह
गत + -उत्साह <i>a.</i> disspirited, dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतौजस्
गत + -ओजस् <i>a.</i> bereft of strength or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतकल्मष
गत + -कल्मष <i>a.</i> freed from crime or sin, purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतक्लम
गत + -क्लम <i>a.</i> refreshed; संविशेत्तु यथाकालमुत्तिष्ठेच्च गतक्लमः Ms. 7. 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतचेतन
गत + -चेतन <i>a.</i> deprived of sense or consciousness, insensible, senseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतत्रप
गत + -त्रप <i>a.</i> bold, without fear or shame; Bhāg. 8. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतदिनम्
गत + -दिनम्, -दिवसः the past day, yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतदिवसः|गतदिवस
गत + -दिनम्, -दिवसः the past day, yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतदिनम्
गत + -दिनम् <i>ind.</i> yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्रत्यागत
गत + -प्रत्यागत <i>a.</i> returned after having gone away; Ms. 7. 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्रभ
गत + -प्रभ <i>a.</i> bereft of splendour, dim, obscured, faded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्राण
गत + -प्राण <i>a.</i> lifeless, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्राय
गत + -प्राय <i>a.</i> almost gone, nearly passed away; गतप्राया रजनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतभर्तृका|गतभर्त्तृका
गत + -भर्तृका<BR>—1 a widow.<BR>—2 (rarely) a woman whose husband has gone abroad (= प्रोषितभर्तृका);<BR> किमु मुहुर्मुहुर्गतभर्तृकाः Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतमनस्क
गत + -मनस्क <i>a.</i> thinking of (loc.); सपदि गतमनस्कः (प्रियायाः<BR> केशपाशे) R. 9. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतलक्ष्मीक
गत + -लक्ष्मीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bereft of lustre or splendour, faded.<BR>—2 deprived of wealth, impoverished, suffering losses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवयस्
गत + -वयस्, -वयस्क <i>a.</i> advanced in years, aged, old; गतवयसामपि<BR> पुंसां येषामर्था भवन्ति ते तरुणाः Pt. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवयस्क
गत + -वयस्, -वयस्क <i>a.</i> advanced in years, aged, old; गतवयसामपि<BR> पुंसां येषामर्था भवन्ति ते तरुणाः Pt. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवर्षः|गतवर्ष
गत + -वर्षः, -वर्षम् the past year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवर्षम्
गत + -वर्षः, -वर्षम् the past year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवैर
गत + -वैर <i>a.</i> at peace (with), reconciled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतव्यथ
गत + -व्यथ <i>a.</i> free from pain; प्रत्तां दुहितरं सम्राट् सदृक्षाय<BR> गतव्यथः Bhāg. 3. 22. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतशैशव
गत + -शैशव <i>a.</i> past child-hood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतश्रम
गत + -श्रम <i>a.</i> unmindful of troubles; आदित्यपथमाश्रित्य जगाम<BR> स गतश्रमः Rām. 6. 74. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसङ्ग
गत + -सङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from attachment; गतसङ्गस्य युक्तस्य Bg. 4. 23.<BR>—2 adverse or indifferent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसत्त्व
गत + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dead, annihilated, lifeless.<BR>—2 base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसन्नकः|गतसन्नक
गत + -सन्नकः an elephant out of rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतस्पृह
गत + -स्पृह <i>a.</i> indifferent to worldly attachments; गतस्पृहो<BR> धैर्यधरः कृपालुः Vaidyajīvanam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतकम्
गतकम् Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिः|गति
गतिः <i>f.</i> [गम्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Motion, going, moving, gait; गतिर्विगलिता Pt. 4. 78; अभिन्नगतयः<BR> Ś. 1. 14; (न) भिन्दन्ति मन्दां गतिमश्वमुख्यः Ku. 1. 11 do not<BR> mend their slow gait (do not mend their pace); so गगनगतिः Pt. 1;<BR> लघुगतिः Me. 16; U. 6. 23.<BR>—2 Access, entrance; मणौ वज्रसमुत्कीर्णे सूत्रस्येवास्ति मे गतिः R. 1. 4.<BR>—3 Scope, room; अस्त्रगतिः Ku. 3. 19; मनोरथानामगतिर्न विद्यते<BR> Ku. 5. 64; नास्त्यगतिर्मनोरथानाम् V. 2.<BR>—4 Turn, course; दैवगतिर्हि चित्रा, Mu. 7. 16.<BR>—5 Going to, reaching, obtaining; वैकुण्ठीया गतिः Pt. 1 obtaining Heaven.<BR>—6 Fate, issue; भर्तुर्गतिर्गन्तव्या Dk. 103.<BR>—7 State, condition; दानं भोगो नाशस्तिस्रो गतयो भवन्ति वित्तस्य<BR> Bh. 2. 43; Pt. 1. 106.<BR>—8 Position, station, situation, mode of existence; परार्ध्यगतेः पितुः<BR> R. 8. 27; कुसुमस्तबकस्येव द्वे गती<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">Page0649-2</a>]<BR> स्तो मनस्विनाम् Bh. 2. 104; Pt. 1. 41, 420.<BR>—9 A means, expedient, course, alternative; अनुपेक्षणे द्वयी गतिः<BR> Mu. 3; का गतिः what help is there, canʼt help (often used in dramas)<BR> Pt. 1. 319; अन्या गतिर्नास्ति K. 158; cf. also अगतिका हि एषा गतिः<BR> यत् कृत्स्नसंयोगे सति विकल्पसमुच्चयौ स्याताम् ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 47.<BR>—10 Recourse, shelter, refuge, asylum, resort; विद्यमाना गतिर्येषाम्<BR> Pt. 1. 320, 322; आसयत् सलिले पृथ्वीं यः स मे श्रीहरिर्गतिः Sk.<BR>—11 Source, origin, acquisition; क्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं<BR> प्रति Bg. 2. 43; Ms. 1. 50.<BR>—12 A way, path.<BR>—13 A march, procession.<BR>—14 An event, issue, result.<BR>—15 The course of events, fate, fortune.<BR>—16 Course of asterisms.<BR>—17 The diurnal motion of a planet in its orbit.<BR>—18 A running wound or sore, fistula.<BR>—19 Knowing; अनेन पूर्वं न मयेति का गतिः Ki. 14. 15; knowledge, wisdom.<BR>—20 Transmigration, metempsychosis; Ms. 6. 73, 12. 3, 23, 40-45; त्यज<BR> बुद्धिमिमां गतिप्रवृत्ताम् Bu. C. 5. 36; Bhāg. 1. 17. 10.<BR>—21 A stage or period of life (as शैशव, यौवन, वार्धक).<BR>—22 (In gram.) A term for prepositions and some other adverbial prefixes<BR> (such as अलम्, तिरस् &c.) when immediately connected with the tenses<BR> of a verb or verbal derivatives.<BR>—23 Position of a child at birth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गत्यनुसरः, गत्यून, गतिभङ्गः, गतिहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्यनुसरः|गत्यनुसर
गतिः + -अनुसरः following the course of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्यून
गतिः + -ऊन <i>a.</i> impassable, desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिभङ्गः|गतिभङ्ग
गतिः + -भङ्गः stoppage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिहीन
गतिः + -हीन <i>a.</i> without refuge, helpless, forlorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिकम्
गतिकम्<BR>—1 Going, motion.<BR>—2 Course.<BR>—3 Condition,<BR>—4 Refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिमत्|गतिमन्त्
गतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 In motion, moving; गिरिरिव गतिमानपक्षलोपात् V. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Having running sores, fistulous.<BR>—3 Possessing means (such as wealth, books &c.); अगाधाश्चाप्रतिष्ठाश्च<BR> गतिमन्तश्च नारद Mb. 12. 286. 7. com.<BR>—4 Learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिला
गतिला<BR>—1 A series, succession.<BR>—2 A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्वर|गत्वरः
गत्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Going, movable, locomotive; विग्रहायाग्रतः पश्चाद्गत्वरोरभ्रविभ्रमम् N. 17. 71.<BR>—2 Transient, perishable; गत्वरैरसुभिः Ki. 2. 19; गत्वर्यो यौवनश्रियः 11. 12.<BR>—3 A kind of horse; गत्वरा साध्यवासाश्च सिन्धुदाराः कनीयसः Śālihotra, ▪ Appendix II, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तव्य|गंतव्य
गन्तव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be gone, to be gone to or attained.<BR>—2 To be accomplished (as a way), to be approached, accessible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तुः|गन्तु|गंतुः
गन्तुः [गम-तुन्]<BR>—1 A way, course; मा नो मध्या रीरिषतायुर्गन्तोः Rv. 1. 89. 9; Bhāg. 11. 18. 43.<BR>—2 A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तृ|गंतृ
गन्तृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 One that goes or moves.<BR>—2 Having sexual intercourse with a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्त्री|गंत्री
गन्त्री A car drawn by oxen; (गन्त्रीरथ in the same sense); गन्त्र्यश्च<BR> चामीकररूप्यचित्राः Bu. C. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम|गमः
गम <i>a.</i> [गम् भावादौ अप्] (At the end of comp.) Going, moving,<BR> going to, reaching, attaining, getting &c.; खगम,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">Page0650-1</a>]<BR> पुरोगम, हृदयंगम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमः|गम
गम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Going, moving.<BR>—2 March; आदरेण गमं चक्रुर्विषमेष्वप्यसङ्घसाः Bk. 7. 56; अश्वस्यैकाहगमः.<BR>—3 The march of an assailant.<BR>—4 A road.<BR>—5 Inconsiderateness, thoughtlessness.<BR>—6 Superficiality, careless perusal.<BR>—7 (Sexual) intercourse with a woman, cohabitation; गुर्वङ्गनागमः<BR> Ms. 11. 55; Y. 2. 293.<BR>—8 A game played with dice and men.<BR>—9 Removal (as of fraction in math.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गमागमः, गमकारित्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0649-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमागमः|गमागम
गम + -आगमः going and coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमकारित्वम्
गम + -कारित्वम् inconsiderateness, rashness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमक|गमकः
गमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [गम्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Indicative or suggestive, a proof or index of; तदेव गमकं पाण्डित्यवैदग्ध्ययोः Māl. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Convincing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमकः|गमक
गमक + .{@-कः@} A kind of musical note (of which there are seven cf. स्वरोत्थानप्रकारस्तु<BR> गमकः परिकीर्तितः । स कम्पितादिभेदेन स्मृतः सप्तविधो बुधैः ॥ स्थानप्राप्त्या<BR> दधानं प्रकटितगमकां मन्द्रतारव्यवस्थाम् Nāg. 1. 12).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमथः|गमथ
गमथः<BR>—1 A traveller.<BR>—2 A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनम्
गमनम् [गम्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Going, motion, gait; श्रोणीभारादलसगमना Me. 84; so गजेन्द्रगमने Ś. Til. 7.<BR>—2 Going, motion; considered as one of the five <i>karmans</i> by the Vaiśeṣikas.<BR>—3 Approaching, going to.<BR>—4 March of an assailant.<BR>—5 Undergoing, suffering.<BR>—6 Obtaining, attaining.<BR>—7 Cohabitation.<BR>—8 Knowledge, understanding; नाञ्जः स्वरूपगमने प्रभवन्ति भूम्नः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 7. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनीय
गमनीय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Accessible, approachable; विकारस्य गमनीयास्मि संवृत्ता Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Intelligible, easy to be comprehended.<BR>—3 Fit to be practised or observed.<BR>—4 Relating to sexual intercourse; गुरुस्त्री˚ Ms. 11. 103 (पापम्);<BR> for other senses see गम्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमिन्
गमिन् <i>a.</i> Intending to go; as in ग्रामंगमी. ━<i>m.</i> A passenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्य|गम्यं|गम्यः
गम्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 Accessible, approachable, obtainable; या गम्याः सत्सहायानाम् Ki. 11. 22.<BR>—2 Intelligible, or easy to be comprehended.<BR>—3 Intended, implied, meant.<BR>—4 Suitable, desirable, fit; गम्यं त्वभावे दातॄणां कन्या कुर्यात्स्वयंवरम् Y. 1. 64.<BR>—5 Fit for cohabitation; दुर्जनगम्या नार्यः Pt. 1. 278; अभिकामां<BR> स्त्रियं यश्च गम्यां रहसि याचितः । नोपैति Mb.<BR>—6 Curable (by a drug &c.); न गम्यो मन्त्राणाम् Bh. 1. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्यः|गम्य|गम्यं
गम्य + .{@-म्यः@} A man with whom a woman may have intercourse, a libidinous<BR> or voluptuous man, lover, paramour; Dk. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भारिका
गम्भारिका, गम्भारी N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भारी|गंभारी
गम्भारिका, गम्भारी N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीर|गंभीर|गम्भीरं|गम्भीरः
गम्भीर <i>a.</i> [गच्छति जलमत्र; गम्-ईरन् नि˚ भुगागमः] =<BR> गभीर q. v.; स्निग्धगम्भीरनिर्घोषमेकं स्यन्दनमास्थितौ R. 1. 36; Me. 66, 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरः|गम्भीर|गंभीर|गम्भीरं
गम्भीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A lotus.<BR>—2 A citron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गम्भीरवेदिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरवेदिन्|गंभीरवेदिन्
गम्भीर + -वेदिन् <i>a.</i> restive (as an elephant); not minding the goad;<BR> sensitive only to harsh stimuli. cf. Mātaṅga L. 8. 21. अङ्कुशं द्विरदस्येव<BR> यन्ता गम्भीरवेदिनः R. 4. 39; Śi. 5. 49 (see Malli. <i>ad loc.</i>);<BR> गम्भीरवेदिभिर्भद्रकरिभिर्गिरिसंनिभैः Śiva B. 25. 58; cf. also चिरकालेन<BR> यो वेत्ति शिक्षां परिचितामपि । गम्भीरवेदी विज्ञेयः स गजो गजवेदिभिः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">Page0650-2</a>]<BR> also त्वग्भेदाच्छोणितस्रावान्मांसस्य क्रथनादपि । आत्मानं यो न जानाति<BR> तस्य गम्भीरवेदिता ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरक|गंभीरक
गम्भीरक <i>a.</i> Lying deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरा
गम्भीरा, गम्भीरिका N. of a river; गम्भीरायाः पयसि Me. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरिका
गम्भीरा, गम्भीरिका N. of a river; गम्भीरायाः पयसि Me. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गयः|गय
गयः<BR>—1 N. of the people living round Gayā and the district inhabited by them.<BR>—2 N. of an Asura.<BR>—3 Wealth.<BR>—4 House, household, family.<BR>—5 Offspring, progeny.<BR>—6 The sky.<BR>—7 Oneʼs own place or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गया
गयः + .{@-या@} N. of a city in Behār which is a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गयस्फान
गयस्फान <i>a.</i> Ved. Promoting domestic wealth; गयस्फानो अमीवहा Rv. 1. 91. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर|गरं|गरः
गर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) [गीर्यते गॄ-कर्मादौ अच्] Swallowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरः|गर|गरं
गर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Any drink or fluid, beverage.<BR>—2 Sickness, disease.<BR>—3 Swallowing (गरा also in this sense).<BR>—4 A factitious poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरः|गर|गरं
गर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Poison.<BR>—2 An antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरम्
गर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 Poison.<BR>—2 An antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरम्
गर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>—2 The fifth of the eleven Karaṇas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गराधिका, गरघ्न, गरश्रीः, गरद, गरव्रतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गराधिका
गर + -अधिका<BR>—1 the insect called Lākṣā.<BR>—2 the red dye obtained from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0650-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरघ्न|गरघ्नः
