गर्भिणी A pregnant female (whether of men or animals); गोगर्भिणीप्रियनवोलपमालभारिसेव्योपकण्ठविपिनावलयो<BR> भवन्ति Māl. 9. 2; Y. 1. 105; Ms. 3. 114.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गर्भिण्यवेक्षणम्, गर्भिणीदौहदम्, गर्भिणीव्याकरणम्, गर्भिणीव्याकृतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिण्यवेक्षणम्
गर्भिणी + -अवेक्षणम् mid-wifery, care and attendance of pregnant women<BR> and new-born infants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणीदौहदम्
गर्भिणी + -दौहदम् the longings of a pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणीव्याकरणम्
गर्भिणी + -व्याकरणम्, -व्याकृतिः <i>f.</i> ‘science of the progress of pregnancy’<BR> (a particular head in medical works.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणीव्याकृतिः|गर्भिणीव्याकृति
गर्भिणी + -व्याकरणम्, -व्याकृतिः <i>f.</i> ‘science of the progress of pregnancy’<BR> (a particular head in medical works.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भेतृप्त
गर्भेतृप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ‘Contented in the womb’, as a child.<BR>—2 Contented as to food or issue.<BR>—3 Indolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भेदृप्त
गर्भेदृप्त, गर्भेशूर <i>a.</i> Spiritless, coward, dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भेशूर
गर्भेदृप्त, गर्भेशूर <i>a.</i> Spiritless, coward, dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्मुत्|गर्म्मुत्
गर्मुत् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of grass.<BR>—2 A kind of reed.<BR>—3 Gold.<BR>—4 A kind of bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्
गर्व् €1 P. €10 Ā. (गर्वति, गर्वयते, गर्वित) To be proud or<BR> haughty (used only in <i>p. p.</i> which is also supposed to be an adjective<BR> derived from गर्व); कोऽर्थान्प्राप्य न गर्वितः Pt. 1. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्वः|गर्व|गर्व्व|गर्व्वः
गर्वः<BR>—1 Pride, arrogance; मा कुरु धनजनयौवनगर्वं हरति निमेषात्कालः<BR> सर्वम् Moha. M. 4; मुधेदानीं यौवनगर्वं वहसि M. 4.<BR>—2 Pride considered as one of the 33 subordinate feelings in rhetoric;<BR> रूपधनविद्यादिप्रयुक्तात्मोत्कर्षज्ञानाधीनपरावहेलनम् R. G.; or,<BR> according to S. D. गर्वो मदः प्रभावश्रीविद्यासत्कुलतादिजः । अवज्ञासविलासाङ्गदर्शनाविनयादिकृत् ॥ 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्वित|गर्व्वित|गर्व्वितः
गर्वित <i>a.</i> [गर्व् कर्त्तरि क्त, गर्वो जातोऽस्य तार˚ इतच् वा]<BR>—1 Proud, haughty.<BR>—2 Conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्वितम्
गर्वित + .{@-म्@} Pride (same as गर्व); न मे गर्वितमायस्तं सहिष्यति<BR> दुरात्मवान् Rām. 4. 16. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्वाटः|गर्वाट|गर्व्वाट|गर्व्वाटः
गर्वाटः A watch-man, door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्
गर्ह् €1. €10 Ā. (sometimes P. also) (गर्हते, गर्हयते, गर्हित)<BR>—1 To blame, censure, reproach; विषमां हि दशां प्राप्य दैवं गर्हयते<BR> नरः H. 4. 3; Ms. 4. 199.<BR>—2 To accuse, charge with.<BR>—3 To be sorry for; यथा यथा मनस्तस्य दुष्कृतं कर्म गर्हति Ms. 11. 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हणम्
गर्हणम्, -णा<BR> [गर्ह्-ल्युट्] Censure, blame, reproach, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हणा
गर्हणम्, -णा<BR> [गर्ह्-ल्युट्] Censure, blame, reproach, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हा
गर्हा [गर्ह्-अ] Abuse, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हित|गर्हितं
गर्हित <i>p. p.</i> [गर्ह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Blamed, censured.<BR>—2 Contemned, despised.<BR>—3 Contemptible.<BR>—4 Forbidden, bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हितम्
गर्हित + .{@-तम्@} A blamable or sinful act; एकस्य कर्म संवीक्ष्य करोत्यन्योऽपि<BR> गर्हितम् Pt. 1. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्य|गर्ह्यः
गर्ह्य <i>a.</i> [गर्ह्-ण्यत्] Deserving censure, censurable, blamable;<BR> गर्ह्ये कुर्यादुभे कुले Ms. 5. 149.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गर्ह्यवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्यवादिन्
गर्ह्य + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking ill, speaking vilely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्
गल् €1 P. (गलति, जगाल, अगालीत्, गलितुम्, गलित)<BR>—1 To drop, drip, ooze, trickle; जलमिव गलत्युपदिष्टम् K. 103;<BR> अच्छकपोलमूलगलितैः (अश्रुभिः) Amaru. 29, 96; Bv. 2. 21; R. 19. 22.<BR>—2 To drop or fall down; शरदमच्छगलद्वसनोपमा Śi. 6. 42, 9. 75;<BR> प्रतोदा जगलुः Bk. 14. 99, 17. 87. गलद्धम्मिल्ल Gīt. 2;<BR> R. 7. 10; Me. 46.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear, pass away, be removed; गलति मध्यरात्रे<BR> Dk.; शैशवेन सह गलति गुरुजनस्नेहः K. 289; विद्यां प्रमादगलितामिव<BR> चिन्तयामि C. P. 1; Bh. 2. 44; Bk. 5. 43; R. 3. 70.<BR>—4 To eat, swallow (connected with गॄ). ━<i>Caus.</i> or €10 U. (<i>p. p.</i><BR> गलित)<BR>—1 To pour out.<BR>—2 To filter, strain.<BR>—3 To flow (Ā.). —4 To fuse, liquefy, dissolve, melt. ━<i>With</i> {@निस्@} to<BR> ooze or flow out, trickle down; निर्गलिताम्बुगर्भं शरद्घनं नार्दति<BR> चातकोऽपि R. 5. 17.<BR>━{@पर्या@} to drop down; Bk. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलः|गल
गलः [गल्-भक्षणे बा˚ करणे अच्]<BR>—1 The throat, neck; शितिना गलेन विलसन्मरीचिना Ki. 12. 23; न<BR> गरलं गले कस्तूरीयम्; cf. अजागलस्तन; Bh. 1. 64; Amaru. 88.<BR>—2 The resin of the Śāla tree.<BR>—3 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>—4 A rope.<BR>—5 A kind of fish.<BR>—6 A large kind of grass (बृहत्काश).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गलाङ्कुरः, गलोद्भवः, गलौघः, गलकम्बलः, गलगण्डः, गलग्रहः, गलग्रहणम्, गलचर्मन्, गलद्वारम्, गलमेखला, गलवार्त, गलविद्रधिः, गलव्रतः, गलशुण्डिका, गलशुण्डी, गलस्तनी, गलहस्तः, गलहस्तित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाङ्कुरः|गलाङ्कुर|गलांकुर
गलः + -अङ्कुरः a particular disease of the throat (inflammation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलोद्भवः|गलोद्भव
गलः + -उद्भवः the tuft of hair on the neck of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलौघः|गलौघ
गलः + -ओघः tumor in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलकम्बलः|गलकम्बल|गलकंबल
गलः + -कम्बलः a bullʼs dewlap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलगण्डः|गलगण्ड|गलगंड
गलः + -गण्डः<BR>—1 enlargement of the glands of the neck.<BR>—2 goitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलग्रहः|गलग्रह
गलः + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम्<BR>—1 seizing by the throat, throttling, smothering.<BR>—2 a kind of disease; Mb. 12. 303. 5.<BR>—3 N. of certain days in the dark fortnight of a month:− <i>i. e.</i> the<BR> 4th, 7th, 8th, 9th, 13th and the three following days.<BR>—4 a day on which a course of study is commenced, but immediately preceding<BR> a day on which it is prohibited.<BR>—5 study, begun but immediately interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलग्रहणम्
गलः + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम्<BR>—1 seizing by the throat, throttling, smothering.<BR>—2 a kind of disease; Mb. 12. 303. 5.<BR>—3 N. of certain days in the dark fortnight of a month:− <i>i. e.</i> the<BR> 4th, 7th, 8th, 9th, 13th and the three following days.<BR>—4 a day on which a course of study is commenced, but immediately preceding<BR> a day on which it is prohibited.<BR>—5 study, begun but immediately interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलचर्मन्
गलः + -चर्मन् <i>n.</i> the gullet, throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलद्वारम्
गलः + -द्वारम् the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलमेखला
गलः + -मेखला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलवार्त|गलवार्त्त
गलः + -वार्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 safe in the work of the throat, able to eat much and digest it, healthy,<BR> sound; दृश्यन्ते चैव तीर्थेषु गलवार्तास्तपस्विनः Pt. 3, v. l.<BR>—2 a parasite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलविद्रधिः|गलविद्रधि
गलः + -विद्रधिः tumor and abscess in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलव्रतः|गलव्रत
गलः + -व्रतः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डिका|गलशुंडिका
गलः + -शुण्डिका the uvula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डी|गलशुंडी
गलः + -शुण्डी swelling of the glands of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलस्तनी
गलः + -स्तनी (also गलेस्तनी) a she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्तः|गलहस्त
गलः + -हस्तः<BR>—1 seizing by the throat, throttling, collaring; अनिच्छन्गलहस्तेन<BR> ताभिर्निर्वासितस्ततः Ks. 4. 68.<BR>—2 an arrow with a crescent-shaped head; cf. अर्धचन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्तित
गलः + -हस्तित <i>a.</i> seized by the throat, throttled, strangled; अर्धेन्दुलीलैर्गलहस्तितेव N. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलकः|गलक
गलकः [गल् बा˚ वुन्]<BR>—1 The throat, the neck.<BR>—2 A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलनम्
गलनम् [गल् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Oozing, trickling, dripping.<BR>—2 Leaking.<BR>—3 Melting, fusing.<BR>—4 Falling down or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन्तिका|गलंतिका
गलन्तिका, गलन्ती<BR>—1 A small pitcher.<BR>—2 A small water-jar with a hole in the bottom from which the water drops<BR> upon the object of worship (an image, Liṅga, Tulasī &c.) placed below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन्ती
गलन्तिका, गलन्ती<BR>—1 A small pitcher.<BR>—2 A small water-jar with a hole in the bottom from which the water drops<BR> upon the object of worship (an image, Liṅga, Tulasī &c.) placed below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलित|गलितः
गलित <i>p. p.</i> [गल्-क्त]<BR>—1 Dropped or fallen down.<BR>—2 Melted.<BR>—3 Oozed, flowing.<BR>—4 Lost, vanished, deprived.<BR>—5 Untied, got loose.<BR>—6 Emptied, leaked away.<BR>—7 Filtered.<BR>—8 Decayed, impaired.<BR>—9 Decreased, exhausted; गलितविभवाश्चार्थिषु नृपाः Bh. 2. 44.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गलितकुष्ठम्, गलितनखदन्त, गलितदन्त, गलितनयन, गलितयौवन, गलितवयस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितकुष्ठम्
गलित + -कुष्ठम् advanced or incurable leprosy when the fingers and toes<BR> fall off; also गुलत्कुष्ठम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनखदन्त
गलित + -नखदन्त <i>a.</i> one who has lost his claws and teeth; वृद्धो<BR> गलितनखदन्तो न कथं विश्वासभूमिः H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितदन्त
गलित + -दन्त <i>a.</i> toothless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनयन
गलित + -नयन <i>a.</i> one who has lost his eyes, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितयौवन
गलित + -यौवन <i>a.</i> one who has lost the bloom or charm of youth, grown<BR> old; गलितयौवना कामिनी Bh. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितवयस्
गलित + -वयस् <i>a.</i> being in the decline of age, in declining years;<BR> गलितवयसामिक्ष्वाकूणामिदं हि कुलव्रतम् R. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितकः|गलितक
गलितकः A kind of dance, gesticulation; V. 4. 56, 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्या
गल्या<BR>—1 A multitude of throats.<BR>—2 A quantity of a particular kind of grass or of ropes made of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेगण्डः|गलेगण्ड|गलेगंड|गलेगंडः
गलेगण्डः A kind of bird, (so called from the pendulous fleshy purse<BR> hanging from its throat); Adjutant bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलानिलः|गलानिल
गलानिलः A prawn or shrimp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलिः|गलि
गलिः [गडि, डस्य लः] A strong but lazy bull; see गडि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलुः|गलु
गलुः <i>m.</i> A kind of gem (चन्द्रकान्त); मसारगल्वर्कमयैर्विभङ्गैर्विभूषितं<BR> हेमनिबद्धचकम् Mb. 12. 46. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्दः|गल्द
गल्दः, -ल्दा Ved.<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 Straining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्दा
गल्दः, -ल्दा Ved.<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 Straining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ्
गल्भ् €1 Ā. (गल्भते, गल्भित) To be bold or confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bold, confident, audacious.<BR>—2 Proud, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लः|गल्ल
गल्लः The cheek; especially, the part of the cheek near the corners<BR> of the mouth; Pt. 1. 123. (Rhetoricians consider this word to be ग्राम्य<BR> or vulgar; cf. the instance given in K. P. 7:− ताम्बूलभृतगल्लोऽयं<BR> भल्लं जल्पति मानुषः; but cf. Bhavabhūtiʼs use:− पातालप्रतिमल्लगल्लविवरप्रक्षिप्तसप्तार्णवम् Māl. 5. 22).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गल्लचातुरी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लचातुरी
गल्लः + -चातुरी a small round pillow to put underneath the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लकः|गल्लक
गल्लकः<BR>—1 A wine-glass.<BR>—2 Sapphire; see गल्वर्क below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लर्कः|गल्लर्क
गल्लर्कः A vessel for drinking spirituous liquor; एवं बृहत्तरे<BR> गल्लर्कप्रमाणे कुले जातः Mk. 8; गल्लर्कशतपरिवृतः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्वर्कः|गल्वर्क
गल्वर्कः<BR>—1 Crystal.<BR>—2 Lapis lazuli; see गलुः; Mb. 7. 16. 54.<BR>—3 A goblet, a vessel for drinking spirituous liquor; मसारगल्वर्कमुखः<BR> Rām. 3. 43. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ह्
गल्ह् €1 Ā. (गल्हते, गल्हित) To blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव
गव (A substitute for गो at the beginning of certain compounds,<BR> especially before words beginning with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">Page0654-2</a>]<BR> vowels or as the second member of Dvigu comp.; पञ्चगवम् five cows;<BR> गवाकृति cow-shaped).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गवाक्षः, गवाक्षकः, गवाक्षित, गवाग्रम्, गवादनम्, गवादनी, गवाधिका, गवानृतम्, गवामृतम्, गवार्ह, गवाविकम्, गवाशनः, गवाश्वम्, गवाकृति, गवालम्भः, गवाह्निकम्, गवेन्द्रः, गवेशः, गवेश्वरः, गवोद्धः, गवराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षः|गवाक्ष
गव + -अक्षः<BR>—1 an air hole, a round window; विलोलनेत्रभ्रमरैर्गवाक्षाः सहस्रपत्राभरणा<BR> इवासन् R. 7. 11; कुवलयितगवाक्षां लोचनैरङ्गनानाम् 11. 93; Ku. 7. 58;<BR> Me. 100. ˚जालम् a lattice.<BR>—2 the mesh of a shirt of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षकः|गवाक्षक
गव + -अक्षकः an air-hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षित
गव + -अक्षित <i>a.</i> furnished with windows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाग्रम्
गव + -अग्रम् a multitude of cows; (written as गोऽग्रम्, गोअग्रम् and गवाग्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवादनम्
गव + -अदनम् pasture or meadow grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवादनी
गव + -अदनी<BR>—1 a pasture.<BR>—2 a manger, a trough for holding grass &c. for feeding cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाधिका
गव + -अधिका lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवानृतम्
गव + -अनृतम् a lie on cowʼs oath (अनृतगोशपथस्य पापम्); तस्याधर्मो<BR> गवानृतम् Mb. 13. 23. 33; Ms. 8. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवामृतम्
गव + -अमृतम्<BR>—1 the beverage or nectar consisting of rays of light.<BR>—2 cowʼs milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवार्ह
गव + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> of the value of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाविकम्
गव + -अविकम् cattle and sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाशनः|गवाशन
गव + -अशनः<BR>—1 a shoe-maker.<BR>—2 an out-cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाश्वम्
