गान्दी The mother of Akrūra^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्व|गांधर्व|गान्धर्वः|गान्धर्व्वं|गान्धर्व्वः
गान्धर्व <i>a.</i> (-र्वी <i>f.</i>) [गन्धर्वस्येदम्-अण्] Relating<BR> to the Gandharvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वः|गान्धर्व|गांधर्व|गान्धर्व्वं|गान्धर्व्वः
गान्धर्व + .{@-र्वः@}<BR>—1 A singer, celestial chorister; Rām. 7. 94. 6.<BR>—2 One of the eight forms of marriage;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">Page0657-1</a>]<BR> गान्धर्वः समयान्मिथः Y. 1. 61; (for explanation, see गन्धर्वविवाह);<BR> cf. अग्निर्गान्धर्वी पथ्यामृतस्या Rv. 10. 80. 6.<BR>—3 A subordinate Veda treating of music attached to the Sāmaveda; see उपवेद.<BR>—4 A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वम्
गान्धर्व + .{@-र्वम्@} The art of the Gandharvas; <i>i. e.</i> music, singing; कापि<BR> वेला चारुदत्तस्य गान्धर्वं श्रोतुं गतस्य Mk. 3; अये गान्धर्वध्वनिरिव<BR> श्रूयते Avimārakam 3; Ks. 12. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वी|गांधर्वी
गान्धर्व + .{@-र्वी@}<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गान्धर्वकला, गान्धर्वविद्या, गान्धर्वशिक्षा, गान्धर्वशास्त्रम्, गान्धर्वचित्त, गान्धर्ववेदः, गान्धर्वशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वकला
गान्धर्व + -कला, -विद्या, -शिक्षा, -शास्त्रम् song, music; यद्गान्धर्वकलासु<BR> कौशलम् Gīt. 12. 28; Ks. 12. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वविद्या
गान्धर्व + -कला, -विद्या, -शिक्षा, -शास्त्रम् song, music; यद्गान्धर्वकलासु<BR> कौशलम् Gīt. 12. 28; Ks. 12. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वशिक्षा
गान्धर्व + -कला, -विद्या, -शिक्षा, -शास्त्रम् song, music; यद्गान्धर्वकलासु<BR> कौशलम् Gīt. 12. 28; Ks. 12. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वशास्त्रम्
गान्धर्व + -कला, -विद्या, -शिक्षा, -शास्त्रम् song, music; यद्गान्धर्वकलासु<BR> कौशलम् Gīt. 12. 28; Ks. 12. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वचित्त|गांधर्वचित्त
गान्धर्व + -चित्त <i>a.</i> one whose mind is possessed by a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्ववेदः|गान्धर्ववेद
गान्धर्व + -वेदः the Veda of music (considered as an appendix to Sāmaveda<BR> and ascribed to Bharata).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वशाला|गांधर्वशाला
गान्धर्व + -शाला a music saloon, concert-hall; तत्र गान्धर्वशालायां वत्सराज<BR> उवास सः Ks. 12. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्वकः|गान्धर्वक|गांधर्वक|गांधर्वकः
गान्धर्व(र्वि)कः A singer; Ks. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्विकः|गान्धर्विक|गांधर्विक|गांधर्विकः
गान्धर्व(र्वि)कः A singer; Ks. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारः|गान्धार|गांधार|गान्धारं|गांधारः
गान्धारः<BR>—1 The third of the seven primary notes of the Indian Gamut; (commonly<BR> denoted by ग in musical notation).<BR>—2 Red lead.<BR>—3 N. of a country between India and Persia, the modern Kandahāra.<BR>—5 A native or a ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारम्
गान्धारः + .{@-रम्@} Gum myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारिः|गान्धारि|गांधारि|गांधारिः
गान्धारिः<BR>—1 An epithet of Śakuni, Duryodhanaʼs maternal uncle.<BR>—2 An epithet of Duryodhana; Mb. 1. 202. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारी
गान्धारी [गान्धारस्यापत्यम् इञ्]<BR>—1 N. of the daughter of Subala, king of the Gāndhāras and wife of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR> [She bore to her husband 100 sons━ Duryodhana and his 99 brothers. As<BR> her husband was blind she always wore a scarf over her face (probably<BR> to reduce herself to his state). After the destruction of all the Kauravas,<BR> she and her husband lived with their nephew Yudhiṣṭhira].<BR>—2 A kind of intoxicant; L. D. B.<BR>—3 A particular vein in the left eye; Gorakṣa Śataka 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गान्धारीग्रामः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारीग्रामः
गान्धारी + -ग्रामः a kind of musical scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारेयः|गान्धारेय|गांधारेय|गांधारेयः
गान्धारेयः [गान्धार्या अपत्यं ढक्] An epithet of Duryodhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिकः|गान्धिक|गांधिक|गांधिकः
गान्धिकः [गन्धो गन्धद्रव्यं पण्यमस्य ठक्]<BR>—1 A vendor of perfumes, a perfumer,<BR>—2 A scribe, clerk.<BR>—3 A kind of insect; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिकम्
गान्धिकः + .{@-कम्@} Fragrant wares, perfumes; पण्यानां गान्धिकं पण्यं किमन्यैः<BR> काञ्चनादिकैः Pt. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामिक
गामिक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Going, leading to (as a way);<BR> परत्रगामिकस्य ते कृताकृतस्य कर्मणः । न साक्षि आत्मना समो नृणामिहास्ति<BR> कश्चन ॥ Mb. 12. 321. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामिन्
गामिन् <i>a.</i> [गम्-णिनि] (Only at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Going, moving, walking; वैदिशगामी M. 5; मृगेन्द्रगामी R. 2. 30<BR> having the gait of a lion; कुब्ज˚ Pt. 2. 5; अलस˚ Amaru. 51.<BR>—2 Riding; द्विरद˚ R. 4. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">Page0657-2</a>]<BR>—3 Going or reaching to, extending or applying to, relating to; ननु सखीगामी<BR> दोषः Ś. 4; द्वितीयगामी न हि शब्द एष नः R. 3. 49.<BR>—4 Leading or going to, accruing to; चित्रकूटगामी मार्गः; कर्तृगामि क्रियाफलम्.<BR>—5 United with; सदृशभर्तृगामिनी M. 5.<BR>—6 Passing over to, devolving on; Ś. 6; शेषेषु पितृगामि तत् Y. 2. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामुक|गामुकः
गामुक <i>a.</i> Going, locomotive; गामुको ध्रुवमध्वानं सुग्रीवो वालिना<BR> गतम् Bk. 7. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाम्भीर्यम्
गाम्भीर्यम् [गम्भीरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Deepness, depth (of water, sound &c.).<BR>—2 Depth, profundity (of meaning, character &c.); cf. भीशोकक्रोधहर्षाद्यैः<BR> गाम्भीर्यं निर्विकारता । समुद्र इव गाम्भीर्ये Rām.; Śi. 1. 55; R. 3. 32.<BR>—3 Dignity; गाम्भीर्यात्सोऽप्युवाच तम् Ks. 86. 32.<BR>—4 Generosity; गाम्भीर्यगरिमा चित्रमपूर्वस्तस्य च प्रभोः । ददाति<BR> यद्ग्राममिति ब्रुवन्राज्यमपीदृशम् ॥ Ks. 124. 83.<BR>—5 Calmness, composure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायः|गाय
गायः [गै भावे घञ्] Singing, a song; यथाविधानेन पठन् सामगायमविच्युतम्<BR> Y. 3. 112; Bhāg. 10. 90. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायकः|गायक
गायकः [गै-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A singer, musician; न नटा न विटा न गायकाः Bh. 3. 27.<BR>—2 An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्र|गायत्रं|गायत्रः
गायत्र <i>a.</i> Consisting in or connected with गायत्री; गर्गाद्यदुकुलाचार्याद्गायत्रं<BR> व्रतमास्थितौ Bhāg. 10. 45. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रम्
गायत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} A song or hymn; एतद्गायत्रं प्राणेषु प्रोतम् Ch. Up. 2. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्री
गायत्री<BR>—1 A Vedic metre of 24 syllables; गायत्री छन्दसामहम् Bg. 10. 35.<BR>—2 N. of a very sacred verse repeated by every Brāhmaṇa at his Sandhyā<BR> (morning and evening devotions) and on other occasions also. Great sins<BR> even are said to be expiated by a pious repetition of this verse, which<BR> is as follows:− तत्सवितुर्वरेण्यं भर्गो देवस्य धीमहि धियो यो नः<BR> प्रचोदयात् Rv. 3. 62. 10.<BR>—3 A number of mystical verses in Tantra literature.<BR>—4 N. of Durgā, Ks. 53. 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रम्
गायत्री + .{@-त्रम्@} A hymn composed and recited in the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गायत्रीमन्त्रः, गायत्रीवल्लभः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रीमन्त्रः|गायत्रीमन्त्र
गायत्री + -मन्त्रः prayers connected with the गायत्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रीवल्लभः|गायत्रीवल्लभ
गायत्री + -वल्लभः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रिन्
गायत्रिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>) One who sings hymns, especially<BR> of the Sāmaveda; गायन्ति त्वा गायत्रिणो Rv. 1. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायनः|गायन
गायनः (नी <i>f.</i>) [गै-ल्युट्] A singer; गायनैश्च विरोविण्यो<BR> वादनैश्च तथापरैः । विरेजुर्विपुलास्तत्र सर्वरत्नसमन्विताः ॥ Rām. 1. 18. 19;<BR> तथैव तत्पौरुषगायनीकृताः N. 1. 103; Bh. 3. 27 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायनम्
गायनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Singing a song.<BR>—2 Practising singing as a means of subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारित्रम्
गारित्रम् Rice, corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुड|गारुडं|गारुडः
गारुड <i>a.</i> (-डी <i>f.</i>) [गरुडस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Shaped like Garuḍa.<BR>—2 Coming from or relating to Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडः|गारुड|गारुडं
गारुड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 An emerald; राशिर्मणीनामिव गारुडानां सपद्मरागः फलितो विभाति R. 13. 53.<BR>—2 A charm against (snake) poison; संगृहीतगारुडेन K. 51 (where<BR> it has sense 1 also).<BR>—3 A missile presided over by Garuḍa.<BR>—4 A military array (व्यूह) of the shape of Garuḍa.<BR>—5 Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडम्
गारुड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 An emerald; राशिर्मणीनामिव गारुडानां सपद्मरागः फलितो विभाति R. 13. 53.<BR>—2 A charm against (snake) poison; संगृहीतगारुडेन K. 51 (where<BR> it has sense 1 also).<BR>—3 A missile presided over by Garuḍa.<BR>—4 A military array (व्यूह) of the shape of Garuḍa.<BR>—5 Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडिकः|गारुडिक
गारुडिकः A charmer, dealer in antidotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुत्मत|गारुत्मतं
गारुत्मत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>) [गरुत्मान् अस्त्यस्य अण्]<BR>—1 Shaped like Garuḍa.<BR>—2 Sacred or presided over by Garuḍa (as a missile); गारुत्मतं तीरगतस्तरस्वी<BR> भुजङ्गनाशाय समाददेऽस्त्रम् R. 16. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुत्मतम्
