गार्ध्रवासस्
गार्ध्र + -पक्षः, -वासस् <i>m.</i> an arrow furnished with a vultureʼs feathers;<BR> न हि गाण्डीवमुक्तानां शराणां गार्ध्रवाससाम् Mb. 3. 33. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भ
गार्भ <i>a.</i> (-र्भी <i>f.</i>) [गर्भे साधु अण्], गार्भिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uterine, fetal; Bhāg. 3. 7. 27.<BR>—2 Relating to gestation; Ms. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भी
गार्भ <i>a.</i> (-र्भी <i>f.</i>) [गर्भे साधु अण्], गार्भिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uterine, fetal; Bhāg. 3. 7. 27.<BR>—2 Relating to gestation; Ms. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिक
गार्भ <i>a.</i> (-र्भी <i>f.</i>) [गर्भे साधु अण्], गार्भिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uterine, fetal; Bhāg. 3. 7. 27.<BR>—2 Relating to gestation; Ms. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिकी
गार्भ <i>a.</i> (-र्भी <i>f.</i>) [गर्भे साधु अण्], गार्भिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uterine, fetal; Bhāg. 3. 7. 27.<BR>—2 Relating to gestation; Ms. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिणम्
गार्भिणम्, -ण्यम्<BR> [गर्भिणीनां समूहः भिक्षा˚ अण्] A number of pregnant women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण्यम्
गार्भिणम्, -ण्यम्<BR> [गर्भिणीनां समूहः भिक्षा˚ अण्] A number of pregnant women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ह
गार्ह <i>a.</i> Domestic, pertaining to household. See गार्हमेध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हकमेधिकः|गार्हकमेधिक
गार्हकमेधिकः (in pl.) The duties of a householder; रेमे रमाभिर्निजकामसम्प्लुतो<BR> यथेतरो गार्हकमेधिकांश्चरन् Bhāg. 10. 59. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपतम्
गार्हपतम् [गृहपतेरिदम् अण्] The position and dignity of a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्यः|गार्हपत्य
गार्हपत्यः [गृहपतिना नित्यं संयुक्तः, संज्ञायां ञ्य]<BR>—1 One of the three sacred fires perpetually maintained by a householder,<BR> which he receives from his father and transmits to his descendants, and<BR> from which fires for sacrificial purposes are lighted; अथ हैनं गार्हपत्योऽनुशशास<BR> Ch. Up. 4. 11. 1; cf. Ms. 2. 231.<BR>—2 The place where this sacred fire is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्यम्
गार्हपत्यः + .{@-त्यम्@} The government of a family; position and dignity of a householder;<BR> गार्हपत्येन सन्त्य ऋतुना यज्ञनीरसि Rv. 1. 15. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गार्हपत्यन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्यन्यायः
गार्हपत्यः + -न्यायः A rule of interpretation according to which a direct statement<BR> (श्रुति) is stronger than an indirect one (लिङ्ग). This rule is<BR> discussed and established by जैमिनि and शबर at MS. 3. 2. 3 and 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हमेध|गार्हमेधः
गार्हमेध <i>a.</i> (-धी <i>f.</i>) [गृहमेधस्येदम् अण्] Fit<BR> or proper for a householder; Bhāg. 5. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हमेधः|गार्हमेध
गार्हमेध + .{@-धः@} The five Yajn~as to be performed by a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हस्थ्यम्
गार्हस्थ्यम् [गृहस्थस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 The order or stage of life of a householder (गृहस्थ); गार्हस्थ्यं<BR> चैव याज्याश्च सर्वा गृह्याश्च देवताः Mb. 14. 7. 10.<BR>—2 Domestic affairs, household.<BR>—3 The five Yajñas to be daily performed by a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ह्य
गार्ह्य <i>a.</i> Domestic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालः|गाल
गालः<BR>—1 Flowing, liquefying.<BR>—2 Dropping.<BR>—3 A flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालनम्
गालनम् [गल् णिच्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Straining (fluids).<BR>—2 Fusing, liquefying, melting.<BR>—3 Reviling; cf. com. on Mb. 12. 68. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालवः|गालव
गालवः<BR>—1 The Lodhra tree.<BR>—2 A kind of ebony.<BR>—3 N. of a sage, a pupil of Viśvāmitra (said in Hariv. to be his son).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिः|गालि
गालिः <i>f.</i> [गल्-इन्] Abuse, abusive or foul language; ददतु<BR> ददतु गालीर्गालिमन्तो भवन्तो वयमपि तदभावाद्गालिदानेऽसमर्थाः Bh. 3. 133;<BR> Rāj. T. 6. 157.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गालिदानम्, गालिप्रदानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिदानम्
गालिः + -दानम्, -प्रदानम् Reviling; Rāj. T. 7. 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिप्रदानम्
गालिः + -दानम्, -प्रदानम् Reviling; Rāj. T. 7. 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालित|गालितः
गालित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strained.<BR>—2 Distilled.<BR>—3 Melted, fused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिनी
गालिनी A particular position of the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोडित|गालोडितः
गालोडित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>—2 Sick, diseased.<BR>—3 Foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोडितम्
गालोडित + .{@-तम्@} Examination; investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोड्यम्
गालोड्यम् The seed of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गावल्गणिः|गावल्गणि
गावल्गणिः An epithet of Sañjaya, son of Gavalgaṇa; गावल्गणे<BR> क्व नस्तातो वृद्धो हीनश्च नेत्रयोः Bhāg. 1. 13. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह्
गाह् €1 Ā. [गाहते, जगाहे, अगाहिष्ट, अगाढ, गाहितुम्, गाढुम्, गाढ or गाहित]<BR>—1 To dive or plunge into, bathe, immerse oneself into (as water); गाहन्तां<BR> महिषा निपानसलिलं शृङ्गैर्मुहुस्ताडितम् Ś. 2. 6; गाहितासेऽथ पुण्यस्य<BR> गङ्गामूर्तिमिव द्रुताम् Bk. 22. 11, 14. 67; (fig. also); मनस्तु मे<BR> संशयमेव गाहते Ku. 5. 46 is plunged into or entertains doubt.<BR>—2 To enter deeply into, penetrate, roam or range over; गाहितमखिलं<BR> गहनम् Bv. 1. 21; कदाचित्काननं जगाहे K. 58; ऊनं न सत्त्वेष्वधिको<BR> बबाधे तस्मिन्वनं गोप्तरि गाहमाने R. 2. 14; Me. 50; H. 1. 150; Ki. 13. 24.<BR>—3 To stir up, agitate, shake, churn.<BR>—4 To be absorbed in (with loc.).<BR>—5 To hide oneself in.<BR>—6 To destroy. ━<i>With</i> {@सम्@} to enter, go to or into, penetrate into; समगाहिष्ट<BR> चाम्बरम् Bk. 15. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढ|गाढं
गाढ <i>p. p.</i> [गाह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Dived or plunged into, bathed in, deeply entered.<BR>—2 Frequently plunged into, resorted to, thickly crowded or inhabited;<BR> तपस्विगाढां तमसां प्राप नदीं तुरङ्गमेण R. 9. 72.<BR>—3 Closely pressed together, tightly drawn, fast, close, tight; गाढाङ्गदैर्बाहुभिः<BR> R. 16. 60; गाढालिङ्गन Amaru. 40, a close embrace; C. P. 6.<BR>—4 Thick, dense.<BR>—5 Deep, impervious.<BR>—6 Strong, vehement, excessive, intense; गाढनिद्रामवाप fell fast<BR> asleep; 20. ˚उद्वेग excessively tormented; U. 3. 31; Māl. 9. 12;<BR> गाढोत्कण्ठाललितलुलितैरङ्ग-कैस्ताम्यतीति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">Page0659-1</a>]<BR> Māl. 1. 15; Me. 85; प्राप्तगाढप्रकम्पा Ś. Til. 12; Amaru. 74; so<BR> also गाढतप्तेन तप्तम् Me. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढम्
गाढ + .{@-ढम्@} <i>ind.</i> Closely, fast, much, excessively, heavily, vehemently, powerfully.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गाढाङ्गद, गाढालिङ्गनम्, गाढकर्णः, गाढतरम्, गाढमुष्टि, गाढवचस्, गाढवर्चस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढाङ्गद
गाढ + -अङ्गद <i>a.</i> having closely fitting armlets; R. 16. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढालिङ्गनम्
गाढ + -आलिङ्गनम् a close embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढकर्णः|गाढकर्ण
गाढ + -कर्णः an attentive ear; ता ये पिबन्त्यवितृषो नृप गाढकर्णैः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 29. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढतरम्
गाढ + -तरम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 more tightly, closely.<BR>—2 more intensely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढमुष्टि|गाढमुष्टिः
गाढ + -मुष्टि <i>a.</i> close-fisted, avaricious, miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढमुष्टिः|गाढमुष्टि
गाढ + -मुष्टि + ({@-ष्टिः@}) a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढवचस्
गाढ + -वचस् <i>m.</i> a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढवर्चस्
गाढ + -वर्चस् <i>a.</i> costive, constipated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह|गाहः
गाह <i>a.</i> [गाह्-घञ्] Diving into, bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहः|गाह
गाह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 Diving into, plunging, bathing; रामाणामनवरतोद्गाहभाजाम् Śi. 8. 45.<BR>—2 Depth, interior; महो गाहाद्दिव आ निरधुक्षत Rv. 9. 110. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहनम्
गाहनम् [गाह्-ल्युट्] The act of diving into, plunging, bathing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहित
गाहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bathed in, plunged into.<BR>—2 Penetrated, entered into; see गाह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहितृ
गाहितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who plunges into water, a bather, diver.<BR>—2 One who penetrates.<BR>—3 Shaking or agitating.<BR>—4 Destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिन्दुकः|गिन्दुक|गिंदुक|गिंदुकः
गिन्दुकः<BR>—1 A ball for playing with.<BR>—2 N. of a tree; see गेन्दुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर्
गिर् <i>a.</i> [गॄ-क्विप् वा टाप्] Ved. Addressing, invoking. ━<i>f.</i><BR> (nom. sing. गीः; instr. dual गीर्भ्याम् &c.)<BR>—1 Speech, words, language; वचस्यवसिते तस्मिन् ससर्ज गिरमात्मभूः<BR> Ku. 2. 53, 3. 72; भवतीनां सूनृतयैव गिरा कृतमातिथ्यम् Ś. 1; प्रवृत्तिसाराः<BR> खलु मादृशां गिरः Ki. 1. 25; Śi. 2. 15; Y. 1. 71.<BR>—2 Invocation, praise, song.<BR>—3 N. of Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech and learning.<BR>—4 Intellect; cf. गिर्धीः Enm.<BR>—5 Knowledge from hearing (श्रवणजज्ञान); प्रपूर्वगौ पूर्वजौ चित्रभानू गिरा वाऽऽशंसामि तपसा ह्यनन्तौ Mb. 1. 3. 57. com.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गीर्देवी, गीष्पतिः, गीरथः, गीर्वाणः, गीर्बाणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्देवी
गिर् + -देवी (गीर्देवी) Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिष्पतिः
गिर् + -पतिः (written as गीःपतिः, गीष्पतिः and गीर्पतिः)<BR>—1 N. of Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>—2 a learned man; so गिरीशः,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीरथः|गीरथ
गिर् + -रथः (गीरथः) N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्वाणः|गीर्वाण|गीर्व्वाण|गीर्व्वाणः
गिर् + -वाणः, -बाणः (गीर्वाण) a god, deity; परिमलो गीर्वाणचेतोहरः Bv. 1. 63, 84. ˚कुसुमम् cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्बाणः|गीर्बाण|गीर्ब्बाणः
गिर् + -वाणः, -बाणः (गीर्वाण) a god, deity; परिमलो गीर्वाणचेतोहरः Bv. 1. 63, 84. ˚कुसुमम् cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरा
गिरा<BR>—1 Speech, speaking, language, voice.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गिरावृध्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरावृध्
गिरा + -वृध् delighting in praise; पवमान गिरावृधम् Rv. 9. 26. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरि|गिरिः
गिरि <i>a.</i> [गॄ-इ किच्च Uṇ. 4. 142] Venerable, respectable, worshipful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिः|गिरि
गिरि + .{@-रिः@}<BR>—1 A hill, mountain, an elevation; पश्याधः खनने मूढ गिरयो न पतन्ति<BR> किम् Subhāṣ.; ननु प्रवातेऽपि निष्कम्पा गिरयः Ś. 6.<BR>—2 A huge rock.<BR>—3 A disease of the eyes.<BR>—4 An honorific title given to Saṃnyāsins; <i>e. g.</i> आनन्दगिरिः<BR>—5 (In math.) The number ‘eight’.<BR>—6 A ball with which children play (गेन्दुक).<BR>—7 A cloud.<BR>—8 A peculiar defect in quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिः|गिरि
गिरि + .{@-रिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Swallowing.<BR>—2 A rat; mouse (written also गिरी in this sense).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गिरीन्द्रः, गिरीशः, गिरिकच्छपः, गिरिकण्टकः, गिरिकन्दरः, गिरिकर्णिका, गिरिकाणः, गिरिकाननम्, गिरिकूटम्, गिरिगङ्गा, गिरिगुडः, गिरिगुहा, गिरिचर, गिरिज, गिरितनयः, गिरिनन्दनः, गिरिसुतः, गिरिजालम्, गिरिज्वरः, गिरित्रः, गिरिदुर्गम्, गिरिद्वारम्, गिरिधातुः, गिरिध्वजम्, गिरिनगरम्, गिरिणदी, गिरिणद्ध, गिरिनन्दिनी, गिरिणितम्बः, गिरिपीलुः, गिरिपुष्पकम्, गिरिपृष्ठः, गिरिप्रपातः, गिरिप्रस्थः, गिरिप्रिया, गिरिबान्धवः, गिरिभिद्, गिरिभू, गिरिमल्लिका, गिरिमानः, गिरिमृद्, गिरिराज्, गिरिराजः, गिरिव्रजम्, गिरिशालः, गिरिशृङ्गः, गिरिषद्, गिरिसानु, गिरिसारः, गिरिसुतः, गिरिसुता, गिरिस्रवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरीन्द्रः|गिरीन्द्र|गिरींद्र
गिरि + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 a high mountain.<BR>—2 an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-2" target="_blank">Page0659-2</a>]<BR> epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 the Himālaya mountain.<BR>—4 a term for the number ‘eight’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

