गीता
गीता [गै कर्मणि क्त] A name given to certain sacred writings<BR> in verse (often in the form of a dialogue) which are devoted to the exposition<BR> of particular religious and theosophical doctrines; <i>e. g.</i> शिवगीता,<BR> रामगीता, भगवद्गीता. But the name appears to be especially confined<BR> to the last, the Bhagavadgītā; गीतासुगीता कर्तव्या किमन्यैः शास्त्रविस्तरैः ।<BR> या स्वयं पद्मनाभस्य मुखपद्माद्विनिःसृता ॥ quoted by Śrīdharasvāmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतिः|गीति
गीतिः <i>f.</i> [गै-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 A song; अहोरागपरिवाहिणी गीतिः Ś. 5; श्रुताप्सरोगीतिरपि क्षणेऽस्मिन्<BR> हरः प्रसंख्यानपरो बभूव Ku. 3. 40.<BR>—2 N. of a metre; see App.<BR>—3 A Sāma mantra; गीतिभिर्मधुरैः स्निग्धैर्मन्त्राह्वानैर्यथार्हतः Rām. 1. 14. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गीत्यार्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीत्यार्या
गीतिः + -आर्या <i>a.</i> a^1<BR>metre of 4 × 16 short syllables.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतिका
गीतिका<BR>—1 A short song.<BR>—2 Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतिन्
गीतिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) One who recites in a singing manner;<BR> गीती शीघ्री शिरःकम्पी तथा लिखितपाठकः Śik. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

