गुच्छः|गुच्छ|गुछ
गुच्छः —1 A bundle, bunch (in general); गुच्छगुल्मं तु विविधम् Ms. 1. 48.<BR>—2 A bunch of flowers, a cluster of blossoms, a clump (of trees &c.);<BR> अक्ष्णोर्निक्षिपदञ्जनं श्रवणयोस्तापिच्छगुच्छावलिम् Gīt. 11; Ms. 1. 48;<BR> Śi. 6. 50; Y. 2. 229.<BR>—3 The plumage of a peacock.<BR>—4 A necklace of pearls (in general).<BR>—5 A pearl necklace of 32 (or, according to some, of 70) strings; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गुच्छार्धः, गुच्छकणिशः, गुच्छपत्रः, गुच्छफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

