गुप्
गुप् I. €1 P. (गोपायति, गोपायित or गुप्त)<BR>—1 To guard, protect, defend, watch over; गोपायन्ति कुलस्त्रिय आत्मानम्<BR> Mb.; जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21; जुगोप गोरूपधरामिवोर्वीम् 2. 3;<BR> Bk. 17. 80.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal; किं वक्षश्चरणानतिव्यतिकरव्याजेन गोपाय्यते<BR> Amaru. 26; see गुप्त. ━II. €1 Ā.<BR> (जुगुप्सते strictly desid. of गुप्) —1 To despise, shun,<BR> abhor, detest, censure; (with abl. sometimes acc. also); पापाज्जुगुप्सते<BR> Sk.; किं त्वं मामजुगुप्सिष्ठाः Bk. 15. 19; Y. 3. 296.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal (गोपते in this sense). ━III. €4 P. (गुप्यति)<BR> To be confused or disturbed. ━IV. €10 U. (गोपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR>—3 To conceal; तव गोप्यते किमिव Śi. 9. 59, 11. 34; (the following<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">Page0664-2</a>]<BR> stanza from कविरहस्य illustrates the root in its different conjugations:− गोपायति<BR> क्षितिमिमां चतुरब्धिसीमां पापाज्जुगुप्सत उदारमतिः सदैव । वित्तं न<BR> गोपयति यस्तु वणीयकेभ्यो धीरो न गुप्यति महत्यपि कार्यजाते ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुपित
गुपित <i>a.</i> Protected, guarded; आच्छद्विधानैर्गुपितो बार्हतैः सोम<BR> रक्षितः Rv. 10. 85. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुपिलः|गुपिल
गुपिलः<BR>—1 A king.<BR>—2 A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्त|गुप्तं|गुप्तः
गुप्त <i>p. p.</i> [गुप् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Protected, preserved, guarded; गुप्तं ददृशुरात्मानं सर्वाः स्वप्नेषु<BR> वामनैः R. 10. 60.<BR>—2 Hidden, concealed, kept secret; Ms. 2. 160, 7. 76, 8. 374.<BR>—3 Secret, private.<BR>—4 Invisible, withdrawn from sight.<BR>—5 Joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तः|गुप्त|गुप्तं
गुप्त + .{@-प्तः@}<BR>—1 An appellation usually (though not necessarily) added to the name of<BR> a Vaiśya; as चन्द्रगुप्तः, समुद्रगुप्तः &c. (Usually शर्मन्<BR> or देव is added to the name of a Brāhmaṇa; गुप्त, भूति or दत्त<BR> to that of a Vaiśya; and दास to that of a Śūdra; cf. शर्मा देवश्च<BR> विप्रस्य वर्मा त्राता च भूभुजः । भूतिर्दत्तश्च वैश्यस्य दासः शूद्रस्य कारयेत्).<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तम्
गुप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Secretly, privately, apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्ता
गुप्त + .{@-प्ता@} One of the principal female characters in a poetical composition,<BR> a lady married to another (परकीया) who conceals her loverʼs caresses<BR> and endearments past, present or future; वृत्तसुरतगोपना, वर्तिष्यमाणसुरतगोपना<BR> and वर्तमानसुरतगोपना; see Ras. M. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गुप्तकथा, गुप्तगतिः, गुप्तगृहम्, गुप्तचर, गुप्तदानम्, गुप्तधनम्, गुप्तवेशः, गुप्तस्नेहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तकथा
गुप्त + -कथा a secret or confidential communication, a secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तगतिः|गुप्तगति
गुप्त + -गतिः a spy, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तगृहम्
गुप्त + -गृहम् bed-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तचर|गुप्तचरः
गुप्त + -चर <i>a.</i> going secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तचरः|गुप्तचर
गुप्त + -चर + ({@-रः@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Balarāma.<BR>—2 a spy, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तदानम्
गुप्त + -दानम् a secret gift or present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तधनम्
गुप्त + -धनम् money kept secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तवेशः|गुप्तवेश
गुप्त + -वेशः a disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तस्नेहा
गुप्त + -स्नेहा N. of the plant Alangium Hexapetalum (Mar. पिस्ता ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तकः|गुप्तक
गुप्तकः A preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तिः|गुप्ति
गुप्तिः <i>f.</i> [गुप्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Preserving, protection; सर्वस्यास्य तु सर्गस्य गुप्त्यर्थम् Ms. 1. 87, 94, 99;<BR> Y. 1. 198.<BR>—2 Concealing, hiding.<BR>—3 Covering, sheathing; असिधारासु कोषगुप्तिः K. 11.<BR>—4 A hole in the ground, a cavern, sink, cellar.<BR>—5 Digging a hole in the ground.<BR>—6 A means of protection, fortification, rampart; गुप्तावपि मनोहरम् Ku. 6. 38.<BR>—7 Confinement, prison; सरभस इव गुप्तिस्फोटमर्कः करोति Śi. 11. 60.<BR>—8 The lower deck of a boat.<BR>—9 A leak in a ship.<BR>—10 Check, stoppage; तथाऽस्य स्याज्जाठरी द्वारगुप्तिः Mb. 12. 269. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपः|गोप
गोपः (-पी <i>f.</i>) [गुप्-अच्]<BR>—1 One who guards or protects; शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR>—2 Hiding. concealment.<BR>—3 Reviling, abuse.<BR>—4 Flurry, agitation.<BR>—5 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनम्
गोपनम् [गुप् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Guarding, protecting; तदाहुः स्वस्य गोपनम् Av. 12. 4. 10.<BR>—2 Hiding, concealing; उचितं गोपनमनयोः कुचयोः कनकाद्रिकान्तितस्करयोः Udb.<BR>—3 Reviling, abuse.<BR>—4 Flurry, hurry, alarm.<BR>—5 Light, lustre.<BR>—6 Envy, jealousy.<BR>—7 Perplexity, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपना
गोपनम् + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 Protection.<BR>—2 Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनीय|गोपनीयं
गोपनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be preserved or protected.<BR>—2 To be prevented.<BR>—3 To be concealed or hidden.<BR>—4 Secret, mysterious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायक
गोपायक <i>a.</i> A preserver, defender, one who guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायनम्
गोपायनम् Protecting, guarding, defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायित|गोपायितं
गोपायित <i>a.</i> Protected, defended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायितृ
गोपायितृ <i>m.</i> A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपित
गोपित <i>a.</i> Concealed, kept secret; विपत्तिं चिरगोपितम् Rāj. T. 5. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिन्
गोपिन्, -गोपिल <i>a.</i><BR> Protecting, preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिल|गोपिलः
गोपिन्, -गोपिल <i>a.</i><BR> Protecting, preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्तृ
गोप्तृ <i>a.</i> (-प्त्री <i>f.</i>) [गुप् तृच्]<BR>—1 A protector, preserver, guardian; तस्मिन्वनं गोप्तरि गाहमाने<BR> R. 2. 14, 1. 55; M. 5. 20; Bg. 11. 18.<BR>—2 One who hides or conceals; स्वरन्ध्रगोप्ता Y. 1. 311. ━<i>m.</i> An<BR> epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्य|गोप्यः
गोप्य <i>a.</i> [गुप् कर्मणि यत्]<BR>—1 To be protected.<BR>—2 To be kept secret or hidden; दारेषु किंचित्स्वजनेषु किंचिद्गोप्यं<BR> वयस्येषु सुतेषु किंचित् Pt. 1. 100.<BR>—3 To be kept, to be taken care of.<BR>—4 To be cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्यः|गोप्य
गोप्य + .{@-प्यः@}<BR>—1 A servant, slave.<BR>—2 A son of a female slave.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गोप्याधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्याधिः|गोप्याधि
गोप्य + -आधिः a pledge to be carefully preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्यकः|गोप्यक
गोप्यकः A slave, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफ्
गुफ् or गुम्फ् €6 P. [गु-गुम्फति, गुम्फित]<BR>—1 To put string or weave together, tie, wind round; गुम्फिताः शिरसि<BR> वेणयोऽभवन् Śi. 14. 30; विश्वाभिरामगुणगौरवगुम्फितानाम् Bv. 1. 71;<BR> Bk. 7. 105.<BR>—2 (fig.) To write, compose. ━<i>Caus.</i> To string together; गुम्फयन्तीव<BR> सुश्लक्ष्णपदरत्नमयीं स्रजम् Ks. 72. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फ्
गुफ् or गुम्फ् €6 P. [गु-गुम्फति, गुम्फित]<BR>—1 To put string or weave together, tie, wind round; गुम्फिताः शिरसि<BR> वेणयोऽभवन् Śi. 14. 30; विश्वाभिरामगुणगौरवगुम्फितानाम् Bv. 1. 71;<BR> Bk. 7. 105.<BR>—2 (fig.) To write, compose. ━<i>Caus.</i> To string together; गुम्फयन्तीव<BR> सुश्लक्ष्णपदरत्नमयीं स्रजम् Ks. 72. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफित|गुफितः
गुफित, गुम्फित <i>p. p.</i> Strung together, tied, woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फित|गुंफित|गुम्फितः
गुफित, गुम्फित <i>p. p.</i> Strung together, tied, woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फः|गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुंफः
गुम्फः [गुम्फ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Tying, stringing together; गुम्फो वाणीनाम् B. R. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Putting together, composing, arrangement.<BR>—3 A bracelet.<BR>—4 A whisker, a mustachio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फना
गुम्फना [गुम्फ्-युच्]<BR>—1 Stringing together.<BR>—2 Arranging, composing.<BR>—3 Good adjustment (of words and their senses), good composition; वाक्ये<BR> शब्दार्थयोः सम्यग्रचना गुम्फना मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुमटी
गुमटी A woman with her face covered with a veil. L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्
गुर् I. €6 Ā. [गुरते, गूर्त-गूर्ण] To make an effort or exertion.<BR>━II. €4 Ā. (<i>p. p.</i> गूर्ण)<BR>—1 To hurt, kill, injure.<BR>—2 To go. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To raise, lift up.<BR>—2 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरणम्
गुरणम् [गुर् भावे ल्युट्] Effort, perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरु|गुरुः
गुरु <i>a.</i> (-रु, -र्वी <i>f.</i>) [ग कु उच्च Uṇ. 1. 24.]<BR> (compar. गरीयस्; superl. गरिष्ठ)<BR>—1 Heavy, weighty (opp. लघु); (fig. also); तेन धृर्जगतो गुर्वी<BR> सचिवेषु निचिक्षिपे R. 1. 34, 3. 35, 12. 102; विमुच्य वासांसि गुरूणि<BR> साम्प्रतम् Ṛs. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Great, large, long, extended.<BR>—3 Long (in duration or length);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">Page0665-2</a>]<BR> आरम्भगुर्वी Bh. 2. 60; गुरुषु दिवसेष्वेषु गच्छत्सु Me. 85.<BR>—4 Important, momentous, great; विभवगुरुभिः कृत्यैः Ś. 4. 19; स्वार्थात्सतां<BR> गुरुतरा प्रणयिक्रियैव V. 4. 31; Ku. 3. 13; Bh. 3. 7; R. 14. 35.<BR>—5 Arduous, difficult (to bear); कान्ताविरहगुरुणा शापेन Me. 1.<BR>—6 Great, excessive, violent, intense; गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव नात्मनि<BR> R. 3. 17; गुर्वपि विरहदुःखम् Ś. 4. 16; Bg. 6. 22.<BR>—7 Venerable, respectable.<BR>—8 Heavy, hard of digestion (as food).<BR>—9 Best, excellent.<BR>—10 Dear, beloved.<BR>—11 Haughty, proud (as a speech).<BR>—12 (In prosody) Long, as a syllable, either in itself, or being short,<BR> followed by a conjunct consonant &c.; <i>e. g.</i> ई in ईड् or त<BR> in तस्कर (It is usually represented by ग in works on prosody;<BR> मात्तौ गौ चेच्छालिनी वेदलोकैः &c.).<BR>—13 Irresistible, unassailable; जागर्ति दंशाय … गुरुर्भुजङ्गी Māl. 6. 1.<BR>—14 Mighty; powerful.<BR>—15 Valuable, highly prized; पूर्वं पूर्वं गुरु ज्ञेयम् Y. 2. 30.<BR>—16 Grievous; Me. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुः|गुरु
गुरु + .{@-रुः@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A father; न केवलं तद्गुरुरेकपार्थिवः क्षितावभूदेकधनुर्धरोऽपि<BR> सः R. 3. 31, 48, 4. 1, 8. 29.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Fore-father, ancestor; त्वां मैत्रावरुणोऽभिनन्दतु गुरुर्यस्ते<BR> गुरूणामपि U. 5. 27.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Father-in-law; त्वं हि मे गुरुः (तद्धर्मतः स्नुषा तेऽहम्)<BR> Rām. 7. 26. 28-29.<BR>—2 Any venerable or respectable person, an elderly personage or relative,<BR> the elders (pl.) शुश्रूषस्व गुरून् Ś. 4. 18; Bg. 2. 5; Bv. 2. 7, 18, 19, 49;<BR> आज्ञा गुरूणां ह्यविचारणीया R. 14. 46.<BR>—3 A teacher, preceptor; गुरुशिष्यौ.<BR>—4 Particularly, a religious teacher, spiritual preceptor; तौ गुरुर्गुरुपत्नी<BR> च प्रीत्या प्रतिननन्दतुः R. 1. 57; (technically a <i>Guru</i> is one<BR> who performs the purificatory ceremonies over a boy and instructs him<BR> in the Vedas; स गुरुर्यः क्रियाः कृत्वा वेदमस्मै प्रयच्छति Y. 1. 34).<BR>—5 A lord, head, superintendent, ruler; सर्वे गुरुहिते स्थिताः Rām. 4. 40. 6;<BR> वर्णाश्रमाणां गुरवे स वर्णी R. 5. 19 the head of the castes<BR> or orders; गुरुर्नृपाणां गुरवे निवेद्य 2. 68.<BR>—6 N. of Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods; गुरुं नेत्रसहस्रेण<BR> चोदयामास वासवः Ku. 2. 29; Pt. 1. 230.<BR>—7 The planet Jupiter; गुरुकाव्यानुगां बिभ्रच्चान्द्रीमभिनभः श्रियम् Śi. 2. 2.<BR>—8 The propounder of a new doctrine.<BR>—9 The lunar asterism called पुष्य.<BR>—10 N. of Droṇa, teacher of the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—11 N. of Prabhākara, the leader of a school of the Mīmāṃsakas (called<BR> after him Prābhākara).<BR>—12 The supreme spirit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गुर्वक्षरम्, गुर्वङ्गना, गुर्वर्थ, गुरूत्तम, गुरूपदेशः, गुरुकण्ठः, गुरुकारः, गुरुकार्यम्, गुरुकुलम्, गुरुकृत, गुरुक्रमः, गुरुगृहम्, गुरुघ्नः, गुरुचर्या, गुरुजनः, गुरुतल्पः, गुरुतल्पगः, गुरुतल्पिन्, गुरुदक्षिणा, गुरुदानम्, गुरुदैवतम्, गुरुपत्रा, गुरुपत्रम्, गुरुपाक, गुरुपूजा, गुरुप्रसादः, गुरुभम्, गुरुभावः, गुरुमर्दलः, गुरुरत्नम्, गुरुलाघवम्, गुरुवर्चोघ्नः, गुरुवर्तिन्, गुरुवासिन्, गुरुवर्ति, गुरुवर्तिता, गुरुवारः, गुरुवासरः, गुरुवृत्तिः, गुरुव्यथ, गुरुशिखरिन्, गुरुश्रुतिः, गुरुस्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्वक्षरम्
गुरु + -अक्षरम् a long syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्वङ्गना|गुर्व्वङ्गना
गुरु + -अङ्गना<BR>—1 the wife of a Guru.<BR>—2 a woman entitled to great respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्वर्थ|गुर्वर्थः|गुर्व्वर्थ
गुरु + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> important; सतीं व्यादाय शृण्वन्तो लघ्वीं गुर्वर्थगह्वराम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्वर्थः|गुर्वर्थ|गुर्व्वर्थ
गुरु + -अर्थ + ({@-र्थः@}) a preceptorʼs fee for instructing a<BR> pupil; गुर्वर्थमाहर्तुमहं यतिष्ये R. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरूत्तम|गुरूत्तमः
गुरु + -उत्तम <i>a.</i> highly revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरूत्तमः|गुरूत्तम
गुरु + -उत्तम + ({@-मः@}) the Supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरूपदेशः
गुरु + -उपदेशः<BR>—1 Consultation of the experts; एषु स्थानेषु गुरूपदेशात् सम्यङ् नाडीं<BR> परीक्ष्य शिरामोचनं कुर्यात् Śālihotra of Bhoja, 82.<BR>—2 advice by the elders or by the preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकण्ठः|गुरुकण्ठ
गुरु + -कण्ठः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकारः|गुरुकार
गुरु + -कारः worship, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकार्यम्
गुरु + -कार्यम्<BR>—1 a serious or weighty affair.<BR>—2 the office of a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकुलम्
गुरु + -कुलम् the residence of a Guru (गुरुगृह), academy; वसन्<BR> गुरुकुले नित्यं नित्यमध्ययने रतः Mb. 9. 40. 3; आवृत्तानां गुरुकुलाद्विप्राणां<BR> पूजको भवेत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">Page0666-1</a>]<BR> Ms. 7. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकृत
गुरु + -कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 worshipped.<BR>—2 made much of; अहो निन्द्यं रूपं कविजनविशेषैर्गुरु कृतम् Bh. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुक्रमः|गुरुक्रम
गुरु + -क्रमः instruction handed down through a series of teachers,<BR> traditional instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुगृहम्
गुरु + -गृहम् signs (राशिs) Sagittarius (धनु) and Pisces (मीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुघ्नः|गुरुघ्न
गुरु + -घ्नः white mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुचर्या
गुरु + -चर्या attendance upon a preceptor; Māl. 9. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुजनः|गुरुजन
गुरु + -जनः any venerable person, an elderly relative, the elders collectively;<BR> नापेक्षितो गुरुजनः K. 158; Bv. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पः|गुरुतल्प
गुरु + -तल्पः<BR>—1 the bed (wife) of a teacher.<BR>—2 violation or violator of a teacherʼs bed; Mb. 12. 56. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पगः|गुरुतल्पग
गुरु + -तल्पगः, -तल्पिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 one who violates his teacherʼs bed (wife), (ranked in Hindu law as<BR> a sinner of the worst kind, committer of an अतिपातक; cf. Ms. 11. 103);<BR> Mb. 3. 43. 6.<BR>—2 one who defiles his step-mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पिन्
गुरु + -तल्पगः, -तल्पिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 one who violates his teacherʼs bed (wife), (ranked in Hindu law as<BR> a sinner of the worst kind, committer of an अतिपातक; cf. Ms. 11. 103);<BR> Mb. 3. 43. 6.<BR>—2 one who defiles his step-mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुदक्षिणा
गुरु + -दक्षिणा fee given to a spiritual preceptor; उपात्तविद्यो गुरुदक्षिणार्थी R. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुदानम्
गुरु + -दानम् a Guruʼs gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुदैवतम्
गुरु + -दैवतम् the constellation पुष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपत्रा
गुरु + -पत्रा the tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपत्रम्
गुरु + -पत्रम् tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपाक
गुरु + -पाक <i>a.</i> difficult of digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपूजा
गुरु + -पूजा<BR>—1 the ceremonies in propitiation of Bṛhaspati when a work is to be<BR> performed or undertaken.<BR>—2 the worship of oneʼs spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

