गोमय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयम्
गोमय + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयम्
गोमय + .{@-यम्@} Cowdung cake; उपलशकलमेतद्भेदकं गोमयानाम् Mu. 3. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: गोमयोत्था, गोमयच्छत्रम्, गोमयप्रियम्, गोमयपायसीयन्यायवत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयोत्था
गोमय + -उत्था<BR>—1 a kind of beetle found in cow-dung<BR>—2 a gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयच्छत्रम्
गोमय + -छत्रम्, -प्रियम् a mushroom, a fungus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयप्रियम्
गोमय + -छत्रम्, -प्रियम् a mushroom, a fungus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयपायसीयन्यायवत्
गोमय + -पायसीय-न्याय-वत् <i>ind.</i> (in the manner of cowdung and milky<BR> food) i. e. Very different in nature though having the same origin, Sarva. S. 2. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिन्
गोमिन् <i>a.</i> Rich in herds. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An owner of cattle; Ms. 9. 50.<BR>—2 A jackal.<BR>—3 A worshipper.<BR>—4 An attendant on a Buddha.<BR>—5 A vaishya (चारण); योगक्षेमं च संप्रेक्ष्य गोमिनः कारयेत्करम्<BR> Mb. 12. 87. 35-40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठः|गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं
गोष्ठः, -ष्ठम्<BR> [गावस्तिष्ठन्त्यत्र घञ्र्थे क षत्वम्] (Usually गोष्ठम् only)<BR>—1 A cow-pen, cow-house, cow-station.<BR>—2 A station of cowherds.<BR>—3 An abode, place of living; गोष्ठान् हरीणां गिरिसेतुमालाः Mb. 3. 177. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठम्
गोष्ठः, -ष्ठम्<BR> [गावस्तिष्ठन्त्यत्र घञ्र्थे क षत्वम्] (Usually गोष्ठम् only)<BR>—1 A cow-pen, cow-house, cow-station.<BR>—2 A station of cowherds.<BR>—3 An abode, place of living; गोष्ठान् हरीणां गिरिसेतुमालाः Mb. 3. 177. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठः|गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं
गोष्ठः, -ष्ठम् + .{@-ष्ठः@}<BR>—1 An assembly or meeting.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठम्
गोष्ठः, -ष्ठम् + .{@-ष्ठम्@} A purificatory श्राद्ध ceremony; वाच्यं गोष्ठे तु सुश्रुतम्<BR> Ms. 3. 254. ˚पतिः a chief herdsman. ˚वेदिका a mound or altar<BR> in a cow-pen. ˚श्वः a dog in a cow-pen which barks at every one; applied<BR> figuratively to a slanderous person, one who stays idly at home and slanders<BR> his neighbours. गोष्ठेपण्डितः ‘wise in a cow-pen’, a braggart, vain<BR> boaster. गोष्ठेक्ष्वेडिन् <i>m.</i> a boasting coward; also गोष्ठपटु,<BR> गोष्ठेप्रगल्भः, -शूरः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्पदम्
गोष्पदम्<BR>—1 A cowʼs foot.<BR>—2 The mark or impression of a cowʼs foot in the soil.<BR>—3 The quantity of water sufficient to fill such an impression; <i>i. e.</i><BR> a very small puddle; गोष्पदे संप्लुतोदके Mb. 1. 31. 9. ˚प्रम्<BR> (णमुल्) in such a manner that a cowʼs footprint be filled; ददाल<BR> भूर्नभो रक्तं गोष्पदप्रं ववर्ष च Bk. 14. 20.<BR>—4 As much as a cows foot-step will hold.<BR>—5 A spot frequented by cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0674-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजिकाणः
गोजिकाणः A horse belonging to a particular locality; गोजिकाणाश्च<BR> केकाणाः प्रौढाहाराश्च मध्यमाः Śālihotra. Appendix II. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजी
