ग्रामघातः|ग्रामघात
ग्रामः + -घातः plundering a village; Ms. 9. 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामघोषिन्
ग्रामः + -घोषिन् <i>a.</i> sounding among men or armies (as a drum); प्रवेदकृद्<BR> बहुधा ग्रामघोषी Av. 5. 20. 9. ━<i>m.</i> an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामचर्या|ग्रामचर्य्या
ग्रामः + -चर्या sexual intercourse; (स्त्रीसंभोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामचैत्यः|ग्रामचैत्य
ग्रामः + -चैत्यः a sacred fig-tree of a village; नीडारम्भैर्गृहबलिभुजामाकुलग्रामचैत्याः Me. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामज
ग्रामः + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 village-born, rustic.<BR>—2 grown in cultivated ground; Ms. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामजात
ग्रामः + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 village-born, rustic.<BR>—2 grown in cultivated ground; Ms. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामजालम्
ग्रामः + -जालम् a number of villages, a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामणीः
ग्रामः + -णीः<BR>—1 the leader or chief of a village or community; तयोर्युद्धं समभवद्रक्षोग्रामणिमुख्ययोः Mb. 7. 109. 3.<BR>—2 a leader or chief in general.<BR>—3 a barber.<BR>—4 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 a libidinous man.<BR>—6 a yakṣa; उन्नह्यन्ति रथं नागा ग्रामण्यो रथयोजकाः Mb. 12. 11. 48. ━(<i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a whore, harlot.<BR>—2 the indigo plant. ˚पुत्रः a bastard, the son of a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामतक्षः|ग्रामतक्ष
ग्रामः + -तक्षः a village-carpenter; P. V. 4. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामदेवता
ग्रामः + -देवता the tutelary deity of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामद्रुमः|ग्रामद्रुम
ग्रामः + -द्रुमः a sacred tree in a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामधर्मः|ग्रामधर्म|ग्रामधर्म्म
ग्रामः + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the observances or customs of a village.<BR>—2 sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामधान्यम्
ग्रामः + -धान्यम् a cultivated grain (like rice); ग्रामधान्यं यथा शून्यं<BR> यथा कूपश्च निर्जलः Mb. 12. 36. 48. See ग्राम्यधान्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामपालः|ग्रामपाल
ग्रामः + -पालः<BR>—1 the guardian of a village.<BR>—2 army for the protection of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामपुरुषः|ग्रामपुरुष
ग्रामः + -पुरुषः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">Page0681-1</a>]<BR> the chief of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामप्रेष्यः|ग्रामप्रेष्य
ग्रामः + -प्रेष्यः the messenger or servant of a community or village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममद्गुरिका
ग्रामः + -मद्गुरिका<BR>—1 a riot, fray, village tumult.<BR>—2 N. of a fish (or a plant)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममुखम्
ग्रामः + -मुखम् a market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममृगः|ग्राममृग
ग्रामः + -मृगः a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजकः|ग्रामयाजक
ग्रामः + -याजकः, -याजिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 ‘the village priest’, a priest who conducts the religious ceremonies<BR> for all classes and is consequently considered as a degraded Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 4. 205.<BR>—2 the attendant of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजिन्
ग्रामः + -याजकः, -याजिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 ‘the village priest’, a priest who conducts the religious ceremonies<BR> for all classes and is consequently considered as a degraded Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 4. 205.<BR>—2 the attendant of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयुद्धम्
ग्रामः + -युद्धम् a riot, fray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामलुण्ठनम्
ग्रामः + -लुण्ठनम् plundering a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवासः|ग्रामवास
ग्रामः + -वासः (ग्रामेवासः also)<BR>—1 a villager.<BR>—2 residence in a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामविशेषः|ग्रामविशेष
ग्रामः + -विशेषः a variety of scales in music; स्फुटीभवद्ग्रामविशेषमूर्च्छना Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवृद्धः|ग्रामवृद्ध
ग्रामः + -वृद्धः an old villager; प्राप्यावन्तीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामषण्डः|ग्रामषण्ड|ग्रामषंड
ग्रामः + -षण्डः an impotent man (क्लीब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसंकरः|ग्रामसङ्कर|ग्रामसंकर
ग्रामः + -संकरः the common sewer or drain of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसंघः|ग्रामसङ्घ|ग्रामसंघ
ग्रामः + -संघः a village-corporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसिंहः|ग्रामसिंह
ग्रामः + -सिंहः a dog; व्यमुञ्चन्विविधा वाचो ग्रामसिंहास्ततस्ततः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 17. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामस्थ|ग्रामस्थः
ग्रामः + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 a villager.<BR>—2 a co-villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामहासकः|ग्रामहासक
ग्रामः + -हासकः a sisterʼs husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामकः|ग्रामक
ग्रामकः<BR>—1 A villager.<BR>—2 The collective department of celestial pleasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामटिका
ग्रामटिका A wretched or miserable village; कतिपयग्रामटिकापर्यटनदुर्विदग्ध P. R. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयति
ग्रामयति Den. P. To invite or call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिक|ग्रामिकः
ग्रामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Rural, rustic.<BR>—2 (In music) Chromatic.<BR>—3 Rude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिकः|ग्रामिक
ग्रामिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The headman of a village; Ms. 7. 116, 118.<BR>—2 A villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिन्
ग्रामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rustic, rural.<BR>—2 Libidinous. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A villager, peasant.<BR>—2 The head of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिणी
ग्रामिन् + .{@-णी@} The indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीण|ग्रामीणः
ग्रामीण <i>a.</i> [ग्रामे भवः खञ्]<BR>—1 Vulgar, rude.<BR>—2 Chromatic.<BR>—3 Belonging to a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीणः|ग्रामीण
ग्रामीण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A villager; ग्रामीणवध्वस्तमलक्षिता जनैश्चिरं वृतीनामुपरि व्यलोकयन्<BR> Śi. 12. 37; Amaru. 13.<BR>—2 A dog.<BR>—3 A crow.<BR>—4 A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीय|ग्रामीयः
ग्रामीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीयः|ग्रामीय
ग्रामीय + .{@-यः@} A villager, boor, churl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीयकः|ग्रामीयक
ग्रामीयकः A villager; ग्रामीयककुलानां च समक्षं सीम्नि साक्षिणः Ms. 8. 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेय
ग्रामेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>) Village-born, rustic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेयी
ग्रामेय + .{@-यी@} A harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्य|ग्राम्यः
ग्राम्य <i>a.</i> [ग्राम-यत्]<BR>—1 Relating to or used in a village; संत्यज्य ग्राम्यमाहारम् Ms. 6. 3, 7. 120.<BR>—2 Living in a village, rural, rustic; अल्पव्ययेन सुन्दरि ग्राम्यजनो<BR> मिष्टमश्नाति Chand. M. 1.<BR>—3 Domesticated, tame (as an animal).<BR>—4 Cultivated (opp. वन्य ‘growing wild’).<BR>—5 Low, vulgar, used only by low people (as a word); चुम्बनं देहि मे<BR> भार्ये कामचाण्डालतृप्तये R. G., or कटिस्ते हरते मनः S. D. 574,<BR> are instances of ग्राम्य expressions; तस्मात्संप्रतिपत्तिरेव हि<BR> वरं न ग्राम्यमत्रोत्तरम् Mu. 5. 18; Bhāg. 5. 2. 17.<BR>—6 Indecent, obscene.<BR>—7 Relating to sexual pleasures.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">Page0681-2</a>]<BR>—8 Relating to a musical scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यः|ग्राम्य
ग्राम्य + .{@-म्यः@}<BR>—1 A villager; Y. 2. 166.<BR>—2 A tame hog.<BR>—3 The first two signs of the zodiac, <i>Aries</i> and <i>Taurus</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्या
ग्राम्य + .{@-म्या@} The Indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यम्
ग्राम्य + .{@-म्यम्@}<BR>—1 A rustic speech.<BR>—2 Food prepared in a village.<BR>—3 Sexual intercourse.<BR>—4 Acceptance.<BR>—5 The Prakṛt and other dialects.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ग्राम्याश्वः, ग्राम्यकर्मन्, ग्राम्यकुङ्कुमम्, ग्राम्यधर्मः, ग्राम्यधान्यम्, ग्राम्यपशुः, ग्राम्यबुद्धि, ग्राम्यमृगः, ग्राम्यवल्लभा, ग्राम्यवादिन्, ग्राम्यसुखम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्याश्वः|ग्राम्याश्व
ग्राम्य + -अश्वः an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकर्मन्|ग्राम्यकर्म्मन्
ग्राम्य + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the occupation of a villager<BR>—2 sexual pleasure; ग्राम्यकर्मणैव विस्मृतकालावधिः Bhāg. 5. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकुङ्कुमम्
ग्राम्य + -कुङ्कुमम् safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यधर्मः|ग्राम्यधर्म|ग्राम्यधर्म्म|ग्राम्यधर्म्मः
ग्राम्य + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the duty of a villager.<BR>—2 sexual intercourse, copulation.<BR>—3 the right of a villager (as opp. to that of a ‘recluse’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यधान्यम्
ग्राम्य + -धान्यम् crops growing in a village; दश ग्राम्याणि धान्यानि भवन्ति<BR> व्रीहियवास्तिलमाषा अणुप्रियङ्गवो गोधूमाश्च मसूराश्च खल्वाश्च खलकुलाश्च … ।<BR> Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यपशुः|ग्राम्यपशु
ग्राम्य + -पशुः a domestic animal; Bhāg. 6. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यबुद्धि
ग्राम्य + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> boorish, clownish, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमृगः|ग्राम्यमृग
ग्राम्य + -मृगः a dog; ग्राम्यमृग इव हविस्तदयं (न भजते) Śi. 15. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यवल्लभा
ग्राम्य + -वल्लभा a harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यवादिन्
ग्राम्य + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a village bailiff; Ts. 2. 3. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यसुखम्
ग्राम्य + -सुखम् sexual intercourse, copulation; cf. अविदित्वा सुखं ग्राम्यं<BR> वैतृष्ण्यं नैति पूरुषः Bhāg. 9. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेरुकम्
ग्रामेरुकम् A variety of sandal; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रावन्
ग्रावन् <i>a.</i> Hard, solid. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A stone or rock; किं हि नामैतदम्बुनि मज्जन्त्यलाबूनि ग्रावाणः संप्लवन्त<BR> इति Mv. 1; अपि ग्रावा रोदित्यपि दलति वज्रस्य हृदयम् U. 1. 28; Śi. 4. 23.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवा
ग्रीवा [गिरत्यनया, गॄ-वनिप् नि˚ Uṇ. 1. 152] The neck, the back<BR> part of the neck; ग्रीवाभङ्गाभिरामं मुहुरनुपतति स्यन्दने दत्तदृष्टिः Ś. 1. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ग्रीवाङ्कुशः, ग्रीवाघण्टा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवाङ्कुशः
ग्रीवा + -अङ्कुशः a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवाघण्टा|ग्रीवाघंटा
ग्रीवा + -घण्टा a bell hanging down from the neck of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवालिका
ग्रीवालिका See ग्रीवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीविन्
ग्रीविन् <i>a.</i> Long-necked, handsome-necked. ━<i>m.</i> A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्म|ग्रीष्मः
ग्रीष्म <i>a.</i> [ग्रसते रसान्; ग्रस्-मनिन् Uṇ. 1. 147] Hot, warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मः|ग्रीष्म
ग्रीष्म + .{@-ष्मः@}<BR>—1 The summer, the hot season, corresponding to the months of Jyeṣṭha<BR> and Āṣāḍha; ग्रीष्मसमयमधिकृत्य गीयताम् Ś. 1; R. 16. 54; Bv. 1. 35.<BR>—2 Heat, warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मी
ग्रीष्म + .{@-ष्मी@} The नवमल्लिका plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ग्रीष्मकालीन, ग्रीष्मोद्भवा, ग्रीष्मजा, ग्रीष्मभवा, ग्रीष्मवनम्, ग्रीष्महासम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मकालीन
ग्रीष्म + -कालीन <i>a.</i> pertaining to summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मोद्भवा
ग्रीष्म + -उद्भवा, -जा, -भवा the Navamallikā creeper, (double jasmine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मजा
ग्रीष्म + -उद्भवा, -जा, -भवा the Navamallikā creeper, (double jasmine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मभवा
ग्रीष्म + -उद्भवा, -जा, -भवा the Navamallikā creeper, (double jasmine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मवनम्
ग्रीष्म + -वनम् a grove frequented in summer; अत्रान्तरे ग्रीष्मवनं मल्लिकामोदि<BR> मारुतम् Ks. 122. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्महासम्
ग्रीष्म + -हासम् The flocculent seeds, down &c. blown about in the air in summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रुच्
ग्रुच् €1 P. (ग्रोचति)<BR>—1 To steal, rob.<BR>—2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव|ग्रैवं
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [ग्रीवायां भवः; अण् ढञ् वा] Being on or<BR> belonging to the neck; ग्रैवेयाणामारवो बृंहितानि Śi. 18. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवी
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [ग्रीवायां भवः; अण् ढञ् वा] Being on or<BR> belonging to the neck; ग्रैवेयाणामारवो बृंहितानि Śi. 18. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेय|ग्रैवेयं
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [ग्रीवायां भवः; अण् ढञ् वा] Being on or<BR> belonging to the neck; ग्रैवेयाणामारवो बृंहितानि Śi. 18. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेयी
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> [ग्रीवायां भवः; अण् ढञ् वा] Being on or<BR> belonging to the neck; ग्रैवेयाणामारवो बृंहितानि Śi. 18. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवम्
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) + .{@-वम्, -यम्@}<BR>—1 A collar or necklace; Mb. 6. 96. 70.<BR>—2 A chain worn round the neck of an elephant; नास्रसत् करिणां ग्रैवं<BR> त्रिपदीच्छेदिनामपि R. 4. 48, 75; तूर्णवर्माण्यथो कक्षान् ग्रैवेयाण्यथ कम्बलान् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव्यम्
ग्रैव (-वी <i>f.</i>), ग्रैवेय (-यी <i>f.</i>) + .{@-वम्, -यम्@}<BR>—1 A collar or necklace; Mb. 6. 96. 70.<BR>—2 A chain worn round the neck of an elephant; नास्रसत् करिणां ग्रैवं<BR> त्रिपदीच्छेदिनामपि R. 4. 48, 75; तूर्णवर्माण्यथो कक्षान् ग्रैवेयाण्यथ कम्बलान् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेयकम्
ग्रैवेयकम् [ग्रीवायां बद्धोऽलंकारः, ढकञ्]<BR>—1 A neck-ornament; <i>e. g.</i> अस्माकं सखि वाससी न रुचिरे ग्रैवेयकं नोज्ज्वलम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">Page0682-1</a>]<BR> S. D. 3; सा हि चन्दनवर्णाभा ग्रीवा ग्रैवेयकोचिता Rām. 3. 60. 32.<BR>—2 A chain worn round the neck of an elephant. ━<i>m.</i> (pl.) a class of<BR> deities (9 in number) sitting on the neck of Loka-puruṣa (Jaina.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्म
ग्रैष्म, ग्रैष्मिक <i>a.</i> Relating to summer; ग्रैष्मौ मासौ<BR> गोप्तारावकुर्वन् Av. 15. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्मिक
ग्रैष्म, ग्रैष्मिक <i>a.</i> Relating to summer; ग्रैष्मौ मासौ<BR> गोप्तारावकुर्वन् Av. 15. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्मक
ग्रैष्मक <i>a.</i> (-ष्मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Sown in summer.<BR>—2 To be paid in summer (as a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपनम्
ग्लपनम्<BR>—1 Relaxation.<BR>—2 Fading; सान्द्रोद्यानद्रुमाग्रग्लपनपिशुनितात्यन्ततीव्राभितापः Ratn. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपित
ग्लपित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Exhausted, dissipated, heated; रविकरग्लपितैरिव वासिभिः Ki. 14. 64;<BR> R. 16. 38.<BR>—2 Taken off, cut; लाङ्गलग्लपितग्रीवा मुसलैर्भिन्नमस्तकाः Rām. 7. 7. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस्
ग्लस् €1 Ā. (ग्लसते, ग्लस्त) To eat, devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह्
ग्लह् €1 U., €10 U. (ग्लहति-ते, ग्लाहयति-ते)<BR>—1 To gamble, to win by gambling.<BR>—2 To take, receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लहः|ग्लह
ग्लहः [cf. P. III. 3. 70]<BR>—1 A dice-player; तावकानां जये भीष्मो ग्लह आसीद्विशांपते Mb. 6. 114. 44.<BR>—2 A stake, wager, bet; प्राणग्लहोऽयं समरः Bhāg. 6. 12. 17; व्यात्युक्षीमभिसरणग्लहामदीव्यन् Śi. 8. 32.<BR>—3 A die.<BR>—4 Gambling, playing.<BR>—5 A dice-box.<BR>—6 Cast of the dice, game at dice; ग्लहे शतिकवृद्धेस्तु Y. 2. 199.<BR>—7 A chessman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुच्
ग्लुच् €1 P. (ग्लोचति, ग्लुक्त)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To steal, rob.<BR>—3 To take away, deprive of; बहूनामग्लुचत् प्राणानग्लोचीच्च रणे यशः Bk. 15. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुञ्च्|ग्लुंच्
ग्लुञ्च् €1 P. (ग्लुञ्चति)<BR>—1 To rob.<BR>—2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेप्
ग्लेप् €1 Ā. (ग्लेपते)<BR>—1 To be poor or miserable.<BR>—2 To shake, tremble.<BR>—3 To move or go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेव्
ग्लेव् €1 Ā. (ग्लेवते) To serve, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेष्
ग्लेष् €1 Ā. (ग्लेषते) To seek, search, investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लै
ग्लै €1 P. (ग्लायति, ग्लान)<BR>—1 To feel aversion or dislike, be unwilling or disinclined to do anything (with inf.).<BR>—2 To be fatigued or wearied, feel tired or exhausted.<BR>—3 To despond, sink in spirit, be dejected; नाऽवकल्प्यमिदं ग्लायेद्<BR> यत् कृच्छ्रेषु भवानपि Bk. 19. 17, 6. 12.<BR>—4 To wane, fade, faint away. ━<i>Caus.</i> (ग्ल-ग्लपयति, but प्रग्लापयति)<BR>—1 To cause to fade away, wither up; ग्लपयति यथा शशाङ्कं न तथा<BR> हि कुमुद्वतीं दिवसः Ś. 3. 16; Ku. 3. 49.<BR>—2 To tire out, exhaust.<BR>—3 To injure, trouble, hurt.<BR>—4 To emaciate, waste; व्रतैः स्वमङ्गं ग्लपयन्त्यहर्निशम् Ku. 5. 29; U. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपनम्
ग्लपनम्<BR>—1 Withering, drying up.<BR>—2 Exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान|ग्लानः
ग्लान <i>p. p.</i> [ग्लै कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Weary, languid, tired, fatigued, exhausted.<BR>—2 Sick, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लानम्
ग्लान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Exhaustion; बुद्ध्वा पुम्प्रकृतिं च यानुचरति ग्लानेतरैश्चेष्टितैः<BR> Bṛ. S. 78. 12.<BR>—2 Disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लानिः|ग्लानि
ग्लानिः <i>f.</i> [ग्लै भावे नि]<BR>—1 Exhaustion, languor, fatigue; मनश्च ग्लानिमृच्छति Ms. 1. 53;<BR> अङ्गग्लानिं सुरतजनिताम् Me. 72, 31; Śānti. 4. 4.<BR>—2 Decay, decline; आत्मोदयः परग्लानिर्द्वयं नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30;<BR> यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत Bg. 4. 7.<BR>—3 Debility, weakness.<BR>—4 Displeasure, unwillingness, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लास्नु|ग्लास्नुः
ग्लास्नु <i>a.</i> [ग्लै-स्नु] Languid, wearied; वसन् माल्यवति ग्लास्नू<BR> रामो जिष्णुरधृष्णुवत् Bk. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौ
ग्लौ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>—3 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौतृ
ग्लौतृ <i>a.</i> Exhausted, fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ <i>a.</i>^1 (Used only as the last member of comp.) Striking, killing,<BR> destroying; as in पाणिघ, राजघ &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घः|घ
घ + .{@-घः@}<BR>—1 A bell.<BR>—2 Rattling, gurgling or tinkling noise; ‘घः सूनुर्वह्निः पूषा नृपो गजः ।’ Enm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घम्
घ + .{@-घम्@} Sin; घं पापमुच्यते <i>ibid.</i> The एकार्थनाममाला<BR> of राघव says: मेघे निदाघे किंकिण्यां घण्टायां घट्टने च घः ।<BR> घं वाद्यामृतयोर्घा भूवार्ताघोरेषु च त्रिषु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घा
घ + .{@-घा@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A blow.<BR>—2 A tinkling ornament worn by women round the waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घंष्
घंष् €1 Ā. (घंषते)<BR>—1 To shed or diffuse lustre.<BR>—2 To flow, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घग्घ्
घग्घ् €1 P. (घग्घते)<BR>—1 To laugh.<BR>—2 To laught at, deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्
घट् I. €1 Ā. (घटते, जघटे, अघटिष्ट, घटितुम्, घटित)<BR>—1 To be busy with, strive after, exert oneself for, be intently occupied<BR> with anything (with inf. loc., or dat.); घटस्व ज्ञातिभिः सह Bhāg. 8. 71. 6;<BR> दयितां त्रातुमलं घटस्व Bk. 10. 40; अङ्गदेन समं<BR> योद्धुमघटिष्ट 15. 77, 12. 26, 16. 23, 20. 24, 22. 31.<BR>—2 To happen, take place, be possible; प्राणैस्तपोभिरथवाऽभिमतं मदीयैः<BR> कृत्यं घटेत सुहृदो यदि तत्कृतं स्यात् Māl. 1. 9 if it can be effected;<BR> कस्यापरस्योडुमयैः प्रसूनैर्वादित्रसृष्टिर्घटते भटस्य N. 22. 22;<BR> उभयथापि घटते Ve. 3; प्रसीदेति ब्रूयामिदमसति कोपे न घटते<BR> Ratn. 2. 19 is not proper &c.<BR>—3 To be united with; दुर्दर्शनेन घटतामियमप्यनेन Māl. 2. 8.<BR>—4 To come to, reach. ━<i>Caus.</i> (घटयति)<BR>—1 To unite, join, bring together; इत्थं नारीर्घटयितुमलं कामिभिः Śi. 9. 87;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">Page0683-1</a>]<BR> अनेन भैमीं घटयिष्यतस्तथा N. 1. 46; क्रुधा संधिं भीमो विघटयति<BR> यूयं घटयत Ve. 1. 10; Bk. 11. 11.<BR>—2 To bring or place near to, bring in contact with, put on; घटयति<BR> घनं कण्ठाश्लेषे रसान्न पयोधरौ Ratn. 3. 9; घटय जघने काञ्चीम् Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 To accomplish, bring about, effect; तटस्थः स्वानर्थान् घटयति च<BR> मौनं च भजते Māl. 1. 14; (अभिमतं) आनीय झटिति घटयति<BR> Ratn. 1. 7; Bh. 2. 120.<BR>—4 To form, fashion, shape, work out, make; एवमभिधाय वैनतेयं …<BR> अघटयत् Pt. 1; कान्ते कथं घटितवानुपलेन चेतः Ś. Til. 3; घटय<BR> भुजबन्धनम् Gīt. 10.<BR>—5 To prompt, impel; स्नेहौघो घटयति मां तथापि वक्तुम् Bk. 10. 73.<BR>—6 To rub, touch.<BR>—7 To exert oneself for.<BR>—8 To move, agitate. ━II. €10 U. (घाटयति, घाटित)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>—2 To unite, join, bring or collect together.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0682-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटः|घट
घटः [घट-अच्]<BR>—1 A large earthen water-jar, pitcher, jar, watering-pot; आकाशमेकं<BR> हि यथा घटादिषु पृथग्भवेत् Y. 3. 144; कूपे पश्य पयोनिधावपि घटो<BR> गृह्णाति तुल्यं जलम् Bh. 2. 49.<BR>—2 The sign Aquarius of the zodiac (also called कुम्भ).<BR>—3 An elephantʼs frontal sinus.<BR>—4 Suspending the breath as a religious exercise.<BR>—5 A measure equal to 20 droṇas.<BR>—6 A part of a column; स्तम्भं विभज्य नवधा वहनं भागो घटोऽस्य<BR> भागोऽन्यः Bṛ. S. 53. 29.<BR>—7 A border.<BR>—8 A peculiar form of a temple; Bṛ. S. 56. 18, 26.<BR>—9 The head; ‘घटः समाधिभेदे ना शिरः कूटकटेषु च’ Med.; Mb. 1. 155. 38.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घटाटोपः, घटोदरः, घटोद्भवः, घटजः, घटयोनिः, घटसंभवः, घटोधस्, घटकञ्चुकि, घटकर्परः, घटकारः, घटकृत्, घटग्रहः, घटदासी, घटपर्यसनम्, घटभवः, घटयोनिः, घटभेदनकम्, घटराजः, घटस्थापनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटाटोपः|घटाटोप
घटः + -आटोपः covering for a carriage or any article of furniture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोदरः|घटोदर
घटः + -उदरः N. of Gaṇeśa; घटोदरः शूर्पकर्णो गणाध्यक्षो मदोत्कटः Ks. 55. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोद्भवः|घटोद्भव
घटः + -उद्भवः, -जः, -योनिः, -संभवः epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटजः|घटज
घटः + -उद्भवः, -जः, -योनिः, -संभवः epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटयोनिः|घटयोनि
घटः + -उद्भवः, -जः, -योनिः, -संभवः epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटसंभवः|घटसम्भव
घटः + -उद्भवः, -जः, -योनिः, -संभवः epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोधस्
घटः + -ऊधस् <i>f.</i> (forming {@घटोध्नी@}) a cow with a full udder;<BR> गाः कोटिशः स्पर्शयता घटोध्नीः R. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटकञ्चुकि
घटः + -कञ्चुकि <i>n.</i> a rite practised by Tāntrikas and Śāktas (in<BR> which the bodices of different women are placed in a receptacle (घट)<BR> and the men present at the ceremony are allowed to take them out one by<BR> one and then cohabit with the woman to whom each bodice belongs); Āgamapr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटकर्परः|घटकर्पर
घटः + -कर्परः<BR>—1 N. of a poet.<BR>—2 a piece of a broken jar, pot-sherd; जीयेय येन कविना यमकैः परेण<BR> तस्मै वहेयमुदकं घटकर्परेण Ghaṭ. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटकारः|घटकार
घटः + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> a potter; Bṛ. S. 15. 1, 16. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटकृत्
घटः + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> a potter; Bṛ. S. 15. 1, 16. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटग्रहः|घटग्रह
घटः + -ग्रहः a water-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटदासी
घटः + -दासी a procuress; cf. कुम्भदासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटपर्यसनम्
घटः + -पर्यसनम् the ceremony of performing the funeral rites of a<BR> <i>patita</i> or apostate (who is unwilling to go back to his caste &c.)<BR> during his very life-time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटभवः|घटभव
घटः + -भवः, -योनिः Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटयोनिः|घटयोनि
घटः + -भवः, -योनिः Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटभेदनकम्
घटः + -भेदनकम् an instrument used in making pots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटराजः|घटराज
घटः + -राजः a water-jar of baked clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटस्थापनम्
घटः + -स्थापनम् placing a water-pot as a type of Durgā for nine days<BR> (नवरात्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटक|घटकः
घटक <i>a.</i> [घटयति घट्-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Exerting oneself, striving for; एते सत्पुरुषाः परार्थघटकाः स्वार्थं<BR> परित्यज्य ये Bh. 2. 74.<BR>—2 Bringing about, accomplishing.<BR>—3 Forming a constituent part, constituent, component.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटकः|घटक
घटक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A tree that produces fruit without apparent flowers.<BR>—2 A match-maker, an agent who ascertains genealogies and negotiates matrimonial alliances.<BR>—3 A genealogist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटनम्
घटनम्, -ना<BR> [घट्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Effort, exertion.<BR>—2 Happening, occurring; तदेषा दैवघटना Ks. 122. 33.<BR>—3 Accomplishment, bringing about, effecting; as in अघटितघटना; यन्माहात्म्यवशेन<BR> यान्ति घटनां कार्याणि निर्यन्त्रणाम् Rāj. T. 4. 365.<BR>—4 Joining, union, mixing or bringing together, combination; तप्तेन<BR> तप्तमयसा घटनाय योग्यं V. 2. 16; देहद्वयार्धघटना रचितम्<BR> K. 239; U. 3. 13.<BR>—5 Making, forming, shaping.<BR>—6 Motion.<BR>—7 Strife, hostility; इत्थं यत्र परिग्रहस्य घटना शम्भोरपि स्याद्गृहे Pt. 1. 159.<BR>—8<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटना
घटनम्, -ना + ({@-ना@}) A troop of elephants.<BR>—9 A literary composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटना
घटनम्, -ना<BR> [घट्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Effort, exertion.<BR>—2 Happening, occurring; तदेषा दैवघटना Ks. 122. 33.<BR>—3 Accomplishment, bringing about, effecting; as in अघटितघटना; यन्माहात्म्यवशेन<BR> यान्ति घटनां कार्याणि निर्यन्त्रणाम् Rāj. T. 4. 365.<BR>—4 Joining, union, mixing or bringing together, combination; तप्तेन<BR> तप्तमयसा घटनाय योग्यं V. 2. 16; देहद्वयार्धघटना रचितम्<BR> K. 239; U. 3. 13.<BR>—5 Making, forming, shaping.<BR>—6 Motion.<BR>—7 Strife, hostility; इत्थं यत्र परिग्रहस्य घटना शम्भोरपि स्याद्गृहे Pt. 1. 159.<BR>—8<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटा
घटा [घट् भावे अड्]<BR>—1 An endeavour, effort, exertion.<BR>—2 A number, troop, assemblage; प्रलयघनघटा K. 111; कौशिकघटा<BR> U. 2. 29, 5. 6; Māl. 5. 19; Bhāg. 3. 17. 6.<BR>—3 A troop of elephants assembled for martial purposes; मातङ्गघटा Śi. 1. 64.<BR>—4 An assembly.<BR>—5 A plate of iron or mixed metal struck as a clock.<BR>—6 लम्बिनी, one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; स्त्रियां तु<BR> घण्टालम्बिन्योः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिकः|घटिक|घटिकं
घटिकः [घटेन तरति ठन्] A water-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिकम्
घटिकः + .{@-कम्@} The hip, the posteriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिका
घटिका<BR>—1 A small water-jar, bucket, a small earthen vessel; नार्यः श्मशानघटिका<BR> इव वर्जनीयाः Pt. 1. 192; एष क्रीडति कूपयन्त्रघटिकान्यायप्रसक्तो<BR> विधिः Mk. 10. 59.<BR>—2 A measure of time equal to 24 minutes.<BR>—3 A water-pot used in calculating the Ghaṭikās of the day;<BR>—4 The ankle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घटिकामण्डलम्, घटिकायन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिकामण्डलम्
घटिका + -मण्डलम् the equatorial circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिकायन्त्रम्
घटिका + -यन्त्रम् See घटीयन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटित
घटित <i>p. p.</i> [घट् णिच् क्त]<BR>—1 United, joined, connected; प्रथमानुरागघटिता Māl. 10. 23.<BR>—2 Planned, devised.<BR>—3 Happened.<BR>—4 Effected, produced.<BR>—5 Made or composed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्
घटिन् <i>m.</i> The sign Aquarius of the zodiac (also called कुम्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिंधम|घटिन्धम|घटिंधमः
घटिंधम <i>a.</i> One who blows into a water-jar or pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिंधमः|घटिन्धम|घटिंधम
घटिंधम + .{@-मः@} A potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिंधय|घटिन्धय
घटिंधय <i>a.</i> One who drinks a pitcherful (of water &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटी
घटी<BR>—1 A small jar.<BR>—2 A measure of time equal to 24 minutes.<BR>—3 A small water-pot used in calculating the Ghaṭikās or time of the<BR> day; घटी चेटी विटः किं स्विज्जानात्यमरकामिनीम् Udb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घटीकारः, घटीग्रह, घटीग्राह, घटीयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीकारः|घटीकार
घटी + -कारः a potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीग्रह
घटी + -ग्रह, -ग्राह <i>a.</i> See घटग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीग्राह
घटी + -ग्रह, -ग्राह <i>a.</i> See घटग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीयन्त्रम्
घटी + -यन्त्रम्<BR>—1 a machine for raising water (largely used in India), the rope and bucket<BR> of a well; see अरघट्ट; घटीयन्त्रगुणोपमः (हारः) Vikr. 8. 33.<BR>—2 a contrivance (like a clepsydra) to ascertain the ghaṭikās or time of the day.<BR>—3 Diarrhoea; Bhāva P. 7. 16. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिघटः|घटिघट
घटिघटः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोत्कचः|घटोत्कच
घटोत्कचः N. of a son of Bhīma by a female demon named हिडिम्बा;<BR> Bhāg. 9. 22. 30-31. He was a very powerful person and fought valiantly<BR> in the great war<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">Page0684-1</a>]<BR> between the Pāṇḍavas and Kauravas on the side of the former, but was<BR> slain by Karṇa with the Śakti or missile he had received from Indra;<BR> cf. Mu. 2. 15. The derivation of the name is given in the आदिपर्व<BR> of महाभारत as follows: घटो हास्योत्कच इति माता तं प्रत्यभाषत ।<BR> अब्रवीत्तेन नामास्य घटोत्कच इति स्म ह ॥ Mb. 1. 155. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट्
घट्ट् €1 Ā. (घट्टते), usually €10 U. (घट्टयति-ते, घट्टित)<BR>—1 To shake, stir about; as in वायुघट्टिता लताः<BR>—2 To touch, rub, rub the hands over; विटजननखघट्टितेव वीणा Mk. 1. 24;<BR> Bk. 14. 2.<BR>—3 To smooth, stroke.<BR>—4 To speak spitefully or malignantly.<BR>—5 To disturb; प्रावर्तयेतां संग्रामं घट्टिताविव पन्नगौ Mb. 7. 172. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टः|घट्ट
घट्टः [घट्ट्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A landing place, steps on the side of a river leading to the waters<BR> (Mar. घाट); श्रीवत्सराजघट्टोऽयं नूनं तेनात्र कारितः । ब्रह्माण्डमुज्ज्वलां<BR> कीर्तिमारोहयितुमात्मनः ॥ Deogaḍh Rock Inscription of Kīrtivarman, V. 7; Ind. Ant. Vol. XVIII pp. 238-9.<BR>—2 Stirring, agitating.<BR>—3 A toll station.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घट्टकुटी, घट्टजीविन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टकुटी
घट्टः + -कुटी a toll station. ˚प्रभातन्याय see under न्याय;<BR> Sarva. S. 13. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टजीविन्
घट्टः + -जीविन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a ferry-man.<BR>—2 a man of a mixed tribe; (वैश्यायां रजकाज्जातः).<BR>—3 attendant at a landing place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टनम्
घट्टनम्<BR>—1 Shaking, moving; सुप्तसर्प इव दण्डघट्टनाद्रोषितोऽस्मि R. 11. 71.<BR>—2 Effecting, forming; प्रणयविघटनार्थं किं नु तद् घट्टनार्थम् Parṇāl. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टना
घट्टना [घट्ट्-युञ्]<BR>—1 Shaking, moving, stirring round, agitating.<BR>—2 Rubbing.<BR>—3 A means of livelihood, practice, business, profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टित
घट्टित <i>a.</i> [घट्ट्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Shaken.<BR>—2 Produced.<BR>—3 Starched (thus thickened); Pañcadaśī 6. 3.<BR>—4 Pressed down, smoothed; Mb. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टिता
घट्टित + .{@-ता@} A particular way of beating a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्
घण् €8 U. (घणोति, घणुते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट्|घंट्
घण्ट् €1. €10. P. (घण्टति, घण्टयति)<BR>—1 To speak.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट|घंट|घण्टः
घण्ट <i>a.</i> Shining, splendid<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टः|घण्ट|घंट
घण्ट + .{@-ण्टः@}<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 A kind of sauce, a kind of dish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घण्टफलकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टफलकः|घण्टफलक
घण्ट + -फलकः a shield with a ringing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टा
घण्टा [घण्ट्-अच्]<BR>—1 A bell.<BR>—2 A plate of iron or mixed metal struck as a clock.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घण्टागारम्, घण्टाकर्णः, घण्टार्णी, घण्टाफलकः, घण्टाफलकम्, घण्टाताडः, घण्टानादः, घण्टापथः, घण्टामुद्रा, घण्टारवः, घण्टावाद्यम्, घण्टाशब्दः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टागारम्
घण्टा + -अगारम् a belfry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाकर्णः|घण्टाकर्ण|घण्टाकर्ण्ण
घण्टा + -कर्णः<BR>—1 N. of a demigod under Śiva, (of Skanda or of Kuber) worshipped in<BR> the month of Chaitra (also -ईश्वरः).<BR>—2 a fabulous demon, Rākṣasa; H. 2; Kathā. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टार्णी
घण्टा + -र्णी N. of a goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाफलकः|घण्टाफलक
घण्टा + -फलकः, -फलकम् a shield furnished with small bells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाफलकम्
घण्टा + -फलकः, -फलकम् a shield furnished with small bells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाताडः|घण्टाताड|घंटाताड
घण्टा + -ताडः a bellman; नॄन्प्रशंसत्यजस्रं यो घण्टाताडोरुणोदये Ms. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टानादः|घण्टानाद|घंटानाद
घण्टा + -नादः the sound of a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टापथः|घण्टापथ|घंटापथ
घण्टा + -पथः<BR>—1 the chief road through a village, a highway, main road; (दशधन्वन्तरो<BR> राजमार्गो घण्टापथः स्मृतः Kau. A.).<BR>—2 N. of Mallināthaʼs commentary on the Kirātārjunīyam; कर्तुं प्रवेशमिह<BR> भारविकाव्यमध्ये घण्टापथं कमपि नूतनमातनिष्ये<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">Page0684-2</a>]<BR> Malli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टामुद्रा
घण्टा + -मुद्रा a particular way of intertwining fingers (before ringing a bell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टारवः|घण्टारव
घण्टा + -रवः<BR>—1 a species of hemp (Mar. तुरी, शणपुष्पिका, लघुताग इ).<BR>—2 sound of a bell; घण्टारवः शणसुमे घण्टानादे च पुंसि वा Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टावाद्यम्
घण्टा + -वाद्यम् the sound of a clock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाशब्दः|घण्टाशब्द|घंटाशब्द|घण्टाशब्दं
घण्टा + -शब्दः<BR>—1 bell-metal.<BR>—2 the sound of a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिका|घंटिका
घण्टिका<BR>—1 A small bell.<BR>—2 The uvula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिन्|घंटिन्
घण्टिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Furnished with bells.<BR>—2 Sounding like a bell. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टुः|घण्टु|घंटुः
घण्टुः<BR>—1 A string of bells tied on an elephantʼs chest by way of ornament.<BR>—2 Heat, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टालः
घण्टालः An elephant; स्वर्धुनीपूरशुण्डः घण्टालः … … Sūkti. 5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिकः|घण्टिक
घण्टिकः The alligator; Bhāva P. 5. 10. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्डः|घण्ड|घंडः
घण्डः A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घन|घनं|घनः
घन <i>a.</i> [हन् मूर्तौ अप् घनादेशश्च Tv.]<BR>—1 Compact, firm, hard, solid; संजातश्च घनाघनः Māl. 9. 39; नासा<BR> घनास्थिका Y. 3. 89; R. 11. 18.<BR>—2 Thick, close, dense; घनविरलभावः U. 2. 27; R. 8. 91; Amaru. 59.<BR>—3 Thick-set, full, fully developed (as breasts); घटयति सुघने कुचयुगगगने<BR> मृगमदरुचि रूषिते Gīt. 7; अगुरु-चतुष्कं भवति गुरू द्वौ घनकुचयुग्मे<BR> शशिवदनाऽसौ Śrut. 8; Bh. 1. 8; Amaru. 31.<BR>—4 Deep (as sound); दधानः सौधानामलघुषु निकुञ्जेषु घनताम् Māl. 2. 12;<BR> Mu. 1. 21.<BR>—5 Uninterrupted, permanent.<BR>—6 Impenetrable.<BR>—7 Great, excessive, violent.<BR>—8 Complete; अभ्यङ्गभङ्ग्या पापस्य न्यस्तं घनमपश्यतः Ks. 4. 53.<BR>—9 Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>—10 Coarse, gross.<BR>—11 Engrossed by, full or replete with; मा ते मलीमसविकारघना मतिर्भूत्<BR> Māl. 1. 32; निर्वृति˚ U. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनः|घन|घनं
घन + .{@-नः@} A cloud; घनोदयः प्राक् तदनन्तरं पयः Ś. 7. 30;<BR> घनरुचिरकलापो निःसपत्नोऽस्य जातः V. 4. 22.<BR>—2 An iron club, a mace; प्रतिजघान घनैरिव मुष्टिभिः Ki. 18. 1.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>—4 The cube of a number (in math.).<BR>—5 Extension, diffusion.<BR>—6 A collection, multitude, quantity, mass, assemblage.<BR>—7 Talc.<BR>—8 Phlegm.<BR>—9 Any compact mass or substance.<BR>—10 Hardness, firmness.<BR>—11 A particular manner of reciting Vedic texts: thus the padas नमः<BR> रुद्रेभ्यः ये repeated in this manner would stand thus:− नमो रुद्रेभ्यो<BR> रुद्रेभ्यो नमो नमो रुद्रेभ्यो ये ये रुद्रेभ्यो नमो नमो रुद्रेभ्यो ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनम्
घन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A cymbal, a bell, a gong.<BR>—2 Iron.<BR>—3 Tin.<BR>—4 Skin, rind, bark.<BR>—5 A mode of dancing; (neither quick nor slow). <i>ind.</i> closely; घटयति<BR> घनं कण्ठाश्लेषे रसान्न पयोधरौ Ratn. 3. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घनात्ययः, घनान्तः, घनाझानी, घनाम्बु, घनाकरः, घनागमः, घनोदयः, घनामयः, घनाश्रयः, घनोत्तमः, घनोदधिः, घनोपलः, घनोरू, घनौघः, घनकफः, घनकालः, घनक्षम, घनगर्जितम्, घनगोलकः, घनघनः, घनजम्बाल, घनज्वाला, घनतालः, घनतोलः, घनधातुः, घनध्वनि, घननाभिः, घननीहारः, घनपदम्, घनपदवी, घनपाषण्डः, घनफलम्, घनमानम्, घनमूलम्, घनरसः, घनरूपा, घनवरम्, घनवर्गः, घनवर्त्मन्, घनवल्लिका, घनवल्ली, घनवाच्, घनवातः, घनवीथिः, घनशब्दः, घनवासः, घनवाहनः, घनश्याम, घनसंवृत्तिः, घनसमयः, घनसारः, घनस्वनः, घनशब्दः, घनरवः, घनहस्तसंख्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनात्ययः|घनात्यय
घन + -अत्ययः, -अन्तः ‘disappearance of the cloud’, the season succeeding<BR> the rains, autumn (शरद्); घनव्यपायेन गभस्तिमानिव R. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनान्तः|घनान्त
घन + -अत्ययः, -अन्तः ‘disappearance of the cloud’, the season succeeding<BR> the rains, autumn (शरद्); घनव्यपायेन गभस्तिमानिव R. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाझानी
