घोण(न)सः A sort of reptile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणा
घोणा<BR>—1 The nose; घोणोन्नतं मुखम् Mk. 9. 16.<BR>—2 The nose of a horse, snout (of a hog); घुर्घुरायमाणघोरघोणन K. 78.<BR>—3 The beak (of an owl); Mb. 10.<BR>—4 The nave of a wheel (रथचक्रपिण्डिका); तदेव स्थगु यद्दीर्घं<BR> रथघोणमिवायतम् Rām. 2. 10. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणिन्
घोणिन् <i>m.</i> A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोण्टा|घोंटा
घोण्टा<BR>—1 The jujube tree.<BR>—2 The betel-nut tree, a timber tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर <i>a.</i> [घर्-अच् Uṇ. 5. 64]<BR>—1 Terrific, frightful, horrible, awful; शिवाघोरस्वनां पश्चाद्बुबुधे<BR> विकृतेति ताम् R. 12. 39;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">Page0689-1</a>]<BR> or तत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव Mb.; घोरं लोके विततमयशः<BR> U. 7. 6; Ms. 1. 50, 12. 54.<BR>—2 Violent, vehement.<BR>—3 Ved. Venerable, awful, sublime.<BR>—4 Unsteady, displeasing; शान्ता घोराश्च मूढाश्च Sāṅ. K. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरः|घोर|घोरं
घोर + .{@-रः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरा
घोर + .{@-रा@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरम्
घोर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Horror, awfulness; अथापि मेऽविनीतस्य क्षात्रं घोरमुपेयुषः Bhāg. 4. 8. 36.<BR>—2 Poison.<BR>—3 Venerableness; Vāj. 2. 32.<BR>—4 Magic formulae and charms; मा नो घोरेण चरताभि घृष्णु Rv. 10. 34. 14.<BR>—5 Saffron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घोराकृति, घोरदर्शन, घोरघुष्यम्, घोरघोरतरः, घोरपुष्पम्, घोररासनः, घोररासिन्, घोरवाशनः, घोरवाशिन्, घोररूपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0688-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोराकृति
घोर + -आकृति, -दर्शन <i>a.</i> frightful in appearance, terrific, hideous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरदर्शनः
घोर + -आकृति, -दर्शन + ({@-नः@})<BR>—1 an owl.<BR>—2 a hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरदर्शन|घोरदर्शनः
घोर + -आकृति, -दर्शन <i>a.</i> frightful in appearance, terrific, hideous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरघुष्यम्
घोर + -घुष्यम् bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरघोरतरः|घोरघोरतर
घोर + -घोरतरः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरपुष्पम्
घोर + -पुष्पम् brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासनः|घोररासन
घोर + -रासनः, -रासिन्, -वाशनः, -वाशिन् <i>m.</i> a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासिन्
घोर + -रासनः, -रासिन्, -वाशनः, -वाशिन् <i>m.</i> a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरवाशनः|घोरवाशन
घोर + -रासनः, -रासिन्, -वाशनः, -वाशिन् <i>m.</i> a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरवाशिन्
घोर + -रासनः, -रासिन्, -वाशनः, -वाशिन् <i>m.</i> a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररूपः|घोररूप
घोर + -रूपः an epithet of Śiva. ━<i>a.</i> of a frightful appearance; Ms. 7. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोलः|घोल|घोलं
घोलः, -लम्<BR> Butter-milk having no water in it; (तत्तु सस्नेहमजलं<BR> मथितं घोलमुच्यते Suśr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोलम्
घोलः, -लम्<BR> Butter-milk having no water in it; (तत्तु सस्नेहमजलं<BR> मथितं घोलमुच्यते Suśr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्न
घ्न <i>a.</i> (-घ्नी <i>f.</i>) (Used only at the end of comp.)<BR> Killing, destroying, removing, curing; ब्राह्मणघ्नः, बालघ्नः, वातघ्नः,<BR> पित्तघ्नः; depriving one of, taking away; पुण्यघ्न, धर्मघ्न &c.<BR> Ms. 9. 232, 8. 127, 7. 218; Y. 1. 138 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रंस्
घ्रंस्, घ्रंसः Ved.<BR>—1 A day.<BR>—2 Sunʼs heat; हिमेनाग्निं घ्रंसमवारयेथाम् Rv. 1. 116. 8.<BR>—3 Sunshine, brightness; यो अस्मै घ्रंस उत वा य ऊधनि Rv. 5. 34. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रंसः|घ्रंस
घ्रंस्, घ्रंसः Ved.<BR>—1 A day.<BR>—2 Sunʼs heat; हिमेनाग्निं घ्रंसमवारयेथाम् Rv. 1. 116. 8.<BR>—3 Sunshine, brightness; यो अस्मै घ्रंस उत वा य ऊधनि Rv. 5. 34. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रा
घ्रा €1 P. (जिघ्रति, जघ्नौ, अघ्रात्-अघ्रासीत्, घ्रात-घ्राण)<BR>—1 To smell, smell at, perceive by smell; स्पृशन्नपि गजो हन्ति जिघ्नन्नपि<BR> भुजङ्गमः H. 3. 14; Bv. 1. 99; Ms. 2. 98.<BR>—2 To kiss. ━<i>Caus.</i> (घ्रापयति) To cause to kill, to smell;<BR> अजिघ्रपंस्तथैवाऽन्यानोषधीरालिपंस्तथा Bk. 15. 109. (Prepositions<BR> like अव, आ, उप, वि, सम् &c. are added to this root without any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">Page0689-2</a>]<BR> material change of meaning; गन्धमाघ्राय चोर्व्याः Me. 21; आमोदमुपजिघ्रन्तौ<BR> R. 1. 43; see Bk. 2. 10, 14. 12; R. 3. 3, 13. 70; Ms. 4. 209 also.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण <i>p. p.</i> [घ्रा कर्मणि-क्त] Smelt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणः|घ्राण|घ्राणं
घ्राण + .{@-णः, -णम्@}<BR>—1 Smell.<BR>—2 Smelling.<BR>—3 The nose (also <i>n.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणम्
घ्राण + .{@-णः, -णम्@}<BR>—1 Smell.<BR>—2 Smelling.<BR>—3 The nose (also <i>n.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणम्
घ्राण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of smelling; घ्राणेन सूकरा हन्ति Ms. 3. 241.<BR>—2 Odour, scent.<BR>—3 The nose; गन्धाय घ्राणमथ यो वेद Ch. Up. 8. 12. 4; बुद्धीन्द्रियाणि<BR> चक्षुः श्रोत्रघ्नाणरसनात्वगाख्यानि Sāṅ. K. 26; Ku. 3. 47; Ṛs. 6. 27; Ms. 5. 135.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: घ्राणेन्द्रियम्, घ्राणचक्षुस्, घ्राणतर्पण, घ्राणपाकः, घ्राणपुटका, घ्राणस्कन्दः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणेन्द्रियम्
घ्राण + -इन्द्रियम् the organ or sense of smell; नासाग्रवर्ति घ्राणम् T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणचक्षुस्
घ्राण + -चक्षुस् <i>a.</i> ‘having nose for the eyes’, blind (who smells out his way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पण|घ्राणतर्पणः
घ्राण + -तर्पण <i>a.</i> grateful or pleasant to the nose, fragrant, odorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पणम्
घ्राण + -तर्पण + .({@-णम्@}) fragrance, odour; प्रदोषपवनैश्चक्रे शिशिरैर्घ्नाणतर्पणम्<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणपाकः|घ्राणपाक
घ्राण + -पाकः a disease of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणपुटका
घ्राण + -पुटका nostril; Mārk. P. 65. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणस्कन्दः|घ्राणस्कन्द
घ्राण + -स्कन्दः blowing oneʼs nose; घ्रास्कन्दादिवाद्यज्ञाः Rāj. T. 5. 418.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात|घ्रातः
घ्रात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Smelled, smelled at; Vāj. 22. 7.<BR>—2 Perceiving, witnessing, feeling; अशनाहं क्रियाघ्रातो लोको लक्ष्मीकटाक्षितः<BR> Rāj. T. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रातव्य
घ्रातव्य <i>a.</i>^1 To be smelled at.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रातव्यम्
घ्रातव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} Odour; घ्नाणं च घ्रातव्यम् Praśna. Up. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रातिः|घ्राति
घ्रातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The act of smelling; न हि घ्रातुर्घ्रातेर्विपरिलोपो विद्यते Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 24;<BR> घ्रातिरघ्रेयमद्ययोः Ms. 11. 68.<BR>—2 Smell<BR>—3 The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रेय
घ्रेय <i>a.</i> To be smelled at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रेयम्
घ्रेय + .{@-यम्@} What may be smelled; smell, odour; घ्रेयैर्घ्राणं क्षितौ न्यस्येत्<BR> Bhāg. 7. 12. 28; घ्रेयं घ्राणं शरीरं च एते भूमिगुणास्त्रयः Mb. 12. 194. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ No word in general use begins with this letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङः|ङ
ङः<BR>—1 An object of sense.<BR>—2 Desire, wish.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva; {@ङः@} प्राणस्तुरगो ङा घरा रमा and {@ङं@} वितानं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-a2" target="_blank">Page0689-a2</a>]<BR> सुखं ब्रह्म सर्पिस्तोयं विषं पयः Enm.; ङं क्लीबमञ्जने,<BR> ना तु, भैरेव, विषये जने Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङु
ङु €1 Ā. (ङवते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Seedless. —2 Bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-b1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चः|च
च + .{@-चः@} —1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 Chewing, eating.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR>—4 A tortoise.<BR>—5 A thief. चश्चञ्चुश्चरणोऽर्चिर्मुखो रविः । चा कद्रूरदितिः कन्या … …<BR> and चं चरित्रं सुखं दुःखं कश्मलं भ्रमणं पयः । Enm. ━<i>ind.</i><BR> A particle expressing<BR>—1 Copulation (and, also as well as, moreover) used to join words or assertions<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-b2" target="_blank">Page0689-b2</a>]<BR> together; (in this sense it is used with each of the words or assertions<BR> which it joins together; or it is used after the last of the words or<BR> assertions so joined but it never stands first in a sentence); मनो निष्ठाशून्यं<BR> भ्रमति च किमप्यालिखति च Māl. 1. 31; तौ गुरुर्गुरुपत्नी च प्रीत्या<BR> प्रतिननन्दतुः R. 1. 57; Ms. 1. 64, 3. 5; कुलेन कान्त्या वयसा नवेन<BR> गुणैश्च तैस्तैर्विनयप्रधानैः R. 6. 79; Ms. 1. 105, 3. 116.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">Page0690-1</a>]<BR>—2 Disjunction (but, still, yet); शान्तमिदमाश्रमपदं स्फुरति च बाहुः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—3 Certainly, determination, (indeed certainly, exactly, quite, having<BR> the force of एव); अतीतः पन्थानं तव च महिमा वाङ्मनसयोः<BR> G. M.; ते तु यावन्त एवाजौ तावांश्च ददृशे स तैः R. 12. 45.<BR>—4 Condition (if = चेत्); जीवितुं चेच्छसे (= इच्छसे चेद्) मूढ<BR> हेतुं मे गदतः शृणु Mb.; लोभश्चास्ति (अस्ति चेद्) गुणेन किम्<BR> Bh. 2. 45 v. l.<BR>—5 It is often used expletively (पादपूरणार्थे); भीमः पार्थस्तथैव<BR> च G. M. (Lexicographers give, besides the above, the following senses<BR> of च which are included in the general idea of <i>copulation</i>;<BR>—1 अन्वाचय joining a subordinate fact with a principal one; भो<BR> भिक्षामट गां चानय; see अन्वाचय.<BR>—2 समाहार collective combination; as पाणी च पादौ च पाणिपादम्<BR>—3 इतरेतरयोग or mutual connection; as प्लक्षश्च न्यग्रोधश्च<BR> प्लक्षन्यग्रोधौ.<BR>—4 समुच्चय aggregation; as पचति च पठति च). च is frequently<BR> repeated with two assertions (1) in the sense of ‘on the one hand━on the other hand’,<BR> ‘though━yet’, to denote antithesis; न सुलभा सफलेन्दुमुखी<BR> च सा किमपि चेदमनङ्गविचेष्टितम् V. 2. 9, 4. 3; R. 16. 7; or (2)<BR> to express simultaneous or undelayed occurrence of two events (no sooner<BR> than, as soon as); ते च प्रापुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R. 10. 6, 3. 40, 11. 50, 81;<BR> Ku. 3. 58, 66; Ś. 6. 7; Māl. 9. 39.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: चादि, चकारः, चसमासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0689-b1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चादि
च + -आदि a Gaṇa of Pāṇini (including the indeclinable particles, P. I. 4. 57).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकारः|चकार
च + -कारः the particle च; P. II. 3. 72; Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चसमासः|चसमास
च + -समासः a Dvandva compound; Vop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्
चक् €1 U. (चकति-ते, चकित)<BR>—1 To be satiated, be contented or satisfied.<BR>—2 To repel, resist.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकित|चकितं
चकित <i>a.</i> [चक्-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Shaking, trembling (through fear); भय˚, साध्वस˚ Me. 27.<BR>—2 Frightened, made to tremble, startled; व्याधानुसारचकिता हरिणीव<BR> यासि Mk. 1. 17; Amaru. 46; Me. 14; R. 10. 73; Śivamahimna 2.<BR>—3 Afraid, timid, apprehensive; चकितविलोकितसकलदिशा Gīt. 2;<BR> पौलस्त्यचकितेश्वराः (दिशः) R. 10. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकितम्
चकित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Trembling.<BR>—2 Alarm, fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकितम्
चकित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> With fear, in a startled manner, alarmingly, with<BR> awe; चकितमुपैमि तथापि पार्श्वमस्य M. 1. 11; सभयचकितम् Gīt. 5;<BR> Śānti. 4. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: चकितचकित, चकितहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकितचकित
चकित + -चकित <i>a.</i> greatly alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकितहृदय
चकित + -हृदय <i>a.</i> faint-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास्
चकास् €2 P. (Rarely Ā.) (चकास्ति-स्ते, चकासाञ्चकार, अचकासीत्, चकासित)<BR>—1 To shine, be bright; गण्डश्चण्डि चकास्ति नीलनलिनश्रीमोचनं लोचनम्<BR> Gīt. 10; चकासतं चारुचमूरुचर्मणा Śi. 1. 8; Bk. 3. 37.<BR>—2 (Fig.) To be happy or prosperous; वितन्वति क्षेममदेवमातृकाश्चिराय<BR> तस्मिन् कुरवश्चकासते Ki. 1. 17. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to shine,<BR> illuminate; Śi. 3. 6. ━<i>With</i> {@वि@} to shine, be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासित
चकासित <i>a.</i> Shining, splendid, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरः|चकोर
चकोरः [चक्-तृप्तौ ओरन् Uṇ. 1. 64] A kind of bird, the Greek<BR> partridge (said to feed on moonbeams); ज्योत्स्नापानमदालसेन वपुषा<BR> मत्ताश्चकोराङ्गनाः Vb. 1. 11; इतश्चकोराक्षि विलोकयेति R. 6. 59, 7. 25;<BR> स्फुरदधरसीधवे तव वदनचन्द्रमा रोचयति लोचनचकोरम्<BR> Gīt. 10. (चकोरकः also.) (विषाभ्याशे)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">Page0690-2</a>]<BR> चकारस्ये अक्षिणी विरज्येते Kau. A. 1. 20. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: चकोराक्ष, चकोरदृश्, चकोरनेत्र, चकोरव्रतम्, चकोराय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोराक्ष
चकोरः + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> (= -दृश्);<BR> इतश्चकोराक्षि विलोकयेति R. 6. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरदृश्
चकोरः + -दृश् <i>a.</i> having (eyes like those of a Chakora bird) beautiful<BR> eyes; अनुचकार चकोरदृशां यतः Śi. 6. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरनेत्र
चकोरः + -नेत्र <i>a.</i> (= -दृश्);<BR> द्विरदेन्द्रगतिश्चकोरनेत्रः Mk. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरव्रतम्
चकोरः + -व्रतम् The vow <i>i. e.</i> the habit of a Chakora bird of drinking<BR> nectar from the moon; चकोरव्रतमालम्ब्य तत्रैवासन् दिवानिशम् Ks. 76. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोराय
चकोरः + -चकोराय To act like a Chakora bird; चकोरायितुमेते च प्रवृत्ते<BR> यावदुन्मुखे Ks. 89. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्क्
चक्क् €10 P. (चक्कयति)<BR>—1 To suffer.<BR>—2 To give or inflict pain, trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्कल
चक्कल <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 1. 108.] Round, circular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्नसः|चक्नस
चक्नसः Dishonesty, crookedness, fraud; Vop. 26. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रम्
चक्रम् [क्रियते अनेन, कृ घञर्थे क नि˚ द्वित्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 The wheel of a carriage; चक्रवत्परिवर्तन्ते दुःखानि च सुखानि च H. 1. 173.<BR>—2 A potterʼs wheel.<BR>—3 A sharp circular missile, weapon, a disc (especially applied to the<BR> weapon of Viṣṇu).<BR>—4 An oil-mill; दशसूनासमं चक्रं दशचक्रसमो ध्वजः Mb. 13. 125. 9.<BR>—5 A circle, ring; कलापचक्रेषु निवेशिताननम् Ṛs. 2. 14.<BR>—6 A troop, multitude, collection, Śi. 20. 17.<BR>—7 A realm, sovereignty; स्वस्थं स्वंचक्रं परचक्रमुक्तम् Bu. C. 2. 15;<BR> cf. चक्रं सैन्यरथाङ्गयोः । राष्ट्रे दम्भान्तरे … । Med.<BR>—8 A province, district, a group of villages.<BR>—9 A form of military array in a circle.<BR>—10 A circle or depression of the body.<BR>—11 A cycle, cycle of years.<BR>—12 The horizon; यावदावर्तते चक्रं तावती मे वसुन्धरा Rām. 2. 10. 36.<BR>—13 An army, a host.<BR>—14 Section of a book.<BR>—15 A whirlpool.<BR>—16 The winding of a river.<BR>—17 An astronomical circle; राशि˚ the zodiac.<BR>—18 Circular flight (of birds &c.).<BR>—19 A particular constellation in the form of a hexagon.<BR>—20 Range, department in general.<BR>—21 The convolutions or spiral marks of the शालिग्राम.<BR>—22 A crooked or fraudulent contrivance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रः|चक्र|चक्रं
चक्रम् + .{@-क्रः@}<BR>—1 The ruddy goose (also called चक्रवाक); पद्मोल्लासविधायिनि सत्पथदीप्तिकृति<BR> चक्रभव्यकरे Viś. Guṇā. 274.<BR>—2 A multitude, troop, group.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: चक्राङ्गः, चक्राटः, चक्राधिवासिन्, चक्रारः, चक्राश्मन्, चक्राकार, चक्राकृति, चक्रायुधः, चक्रावर्तः, चक्राह्वः, चक्राह्वयः, चक्रेश्वरः, चक्रेश्वरी, चक्रोपजीविन्, चक्रकारकम्, चक्रगजः, चक्रगण्डुः, चक्रगतिः, चक्रगुच्छः, चक्रग्रहणम्, चक्रग्रहणी, चक्रचक्रम्, चक्रचर, चक्रचारिन्, चक्रचूडामणिः, चक्रजीवकः, चक्रजीविन्, चक्रतीर्थम्, चक्रतुण्डः, चक्रदंष्ट्रः, चक्रघनः, चक्रधर, चक्रधारा, चक्रनदी, चक्रनाभिः, चक्रनामन्, चक्रनायकः, चक्रनेमिः, चक्रपाणिः, चक्रपादः, चक्रपादकः, चक्रपालः, चक्रफलम्, चक्रबन्धुः, चक्रबान्धवः, चक्रबालः, चक्रबाडः, चक्रवालः, चक्रवालम्, चक्रवाडम्, चक्रबालधिः, चक्रभृत्, चक्रभेदिनी, चक्रभ्रमः, चक्रभ्रमिः, चक्रभ्रान्तिः, चक्रमण्डलिन्, चक्रमुखः, चक्रमुषलः, चक्रयानम्, चक्ररदः, चक्रवर्तिन्, चक्रवर्मन्, चक्रवाकः, चक्रवाटः, चक्रवातः, चक्रवृद्धिः, चक्रव्यूहः, चक्रसंज्ञम्, चक्रसाह्वयः, चक्रहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्गः|चक्राङ्ग|चक्रांग
चक्रम् + -अङ्गः<BR>—1 a gander having a curved neck.<BR>—2 a carriage.<BR>—3 the ruddy goose (चक्रवाक); चक्राङ्गान् स च नित्यं वै सर्वतो<BR> वनगोचरान् Mb. 12. 268. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्गी
चक्रम् + -अङ्गः + ({@-ङ्गी@}) a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्गम्
चक्रम् + -अङ्गः + .({@-ङ्गम्@}) a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राटः|चक्राट
चक्रम् + -अटः<BR>—1 a juggler, snake-catcher.<BR>—2 a rogue, knave, cheat.<BR>—3 a particular coin, a <i>dināra</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राधिवासिन्
चक्रम् + -अधिवासिन् <i>m.</i> the orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रारः
चक्रम् + -अरः,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रारम्
चक्रम् + -अरः + .({@-रम्@}) the spoke of a wheel; चक्रारपङ्क्तिरिव गच्छति भाग्यपङ्क्तिः ।<BR> Svapna. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राश्मन्
चक्रम् + -अश्मन् <i>n.</i> a machine to hurl stones at a distance; अयःकणपचक्राश्मभुशुण्डपुद्यतबाहवः<BR> Mb. 1. 227. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राकार
चक्रम् + -आकार, -आकृति <i>a.</i> circular, round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राकृति
चक्रम् + -आकार, -आकृति <i>a.</i> circular, round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0690-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

