चतुर् + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> having 4 members, quadripartite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गम्
चतुर् + -अङ्ग + ({@-ङ्गम्@})<BR>—1 a complete army consisting of elephants, chariots, cavalry and infantry;<BR> चतुरङ्गसमायुक्तं मया सह च तं नय Rām. 1. 20. 10; एको हि<BR> खञ्जनवरो नलिनीदलस्थो दृष्टः करोति चतुरङ्गबलाधिपत्यम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0694-1" target="_blank">Page0694-1</a>]<BR> Ś. Til. 4; चतुरङ्गबलो राजा जगतीं वशमानयेत् । अहं पञ्चाङ्गबलवानाकाशं<BR> वशमानये ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 a sort of chess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गिकः
चतुर् + -अङ्गिकः A kind of horse, having four curls on the forehead; यस्य<BR> ललाटे भ्रमरचतुष्टयं स चतुरङ्गिको नाम । Śālihotra of Bhoj. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0694-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गिन्
