चीव्
चीव् I. €1 U. (चीवति-ते)<BR>—1 To wear, cover.<BR>—2 To take or receive.<BR>—3 To seize. ━II. €10 U. (चीवयति-ते)<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरम्
चीवरम् [चि-ष्वरच् नि˚ दीर्घः; चीव्-अरच् वा; cf. Uṇ. 3. 1]<BR>—1 A garment (in general); a tatter, rag; प्रेतचीवरवसा स्वनोग्रया R. 11. 16.<BR>—2 The dress of any mendicant, particularly of a Buddhist mendicant; चीवराणि<BR> परिधत्ते Sk.; चीरचीवरपरिच्छदाम् Māl. 1; प्रक्षालितमेतन्मया<BR> चीवरखण्डम् Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरिन्
