चौर्यकम् Theft, stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु I. €1 Ā. (च्यवते, च्युत)<BR>—1 To fall or drop down, slip, sink (fig. also); Ś. 2. 8.<BR>—2 To come out of, flow or issue from, drop, trickle or stream forth from;<BR> स्वतश्च्युतं वह्निमिवाद्भिरम्बुदः R. 3. 58; Bk. 9. 71.<BR>—3 To deviate or swerve from, fall off or away from, leave (duty &c.);<BR> (with abl.) अस्माद्धर्मान्न च्यवेत Ms. 7. 98, 12. 71-72.<BR>—4 To lose, be deprived of; अच्योष्ट सत्त्वान्नृपतिः Bk. 3. 20, 7. 92.<BR>—5 To vanish, disappear, perish, be at an end; R. 8. 66; Ms. 12. 96.<BR>—6 To decrease.<BR>—7 To bring about, make, form, create.<BR>—8 To cause to go away, cause to forget. ━<i>Caus.</i> (च्यावयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to move, excite, agitate.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To move oneself, be shaken or moved.<BR>—3 To remove, drive away, expel.<BR>—4 To deprive, take away; Pt. 1. 240.<BR>—5 To cause to fall. ━II. €10 P. (च्यावयति)<BR>—1 To suffer, bear.<BR>—2 To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवनः|च्यवन|च्यवनं
च्यवनः N. of a Ṛṣi (son of Bhṛgu, author of Rv. 10. 19.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवनम्
च्यवनम्<BR>—1 Moving, motion.<BR>—2 Being deprived of, loss; deprivation.<BR>—3 Dying, perishing.<BR>—4 Sinking, falling.<BR>—5 Departure, deviation.<BR>—6 Flowing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवान
च्यवान <i>a.</i> Moving, active; च्यवाना सुमतिं भुरण्यू Rv. 6. 62. 7.<BR>━<i>m.</i> N. of a Ṛṣi restored to youth by the Aśvins; युवं<BR> च्यवानमश्विना जरन्तं पुनर्युवानं चक्रथुः शचीभिः Rv. 1. 117. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावन
च्यावन <i>a.</i> Causing to fall; अच्युतच्यावनोऽरीणां संस्कृतो विकृतिर्वृषः Mb. 12. 43. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावनम्
च्यावन + .{@-नम्@} Expulsion, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत <i>p. p.</i> [च्यु-क्त च्युत्-क वा]<BR>—1 Fallen down, slipped, fallen.<BR>—2 Removed, expelled.<BR>—3 Strayed, erred, deviated from.<BR>—4 Deprived.<BR>—5 Broken, disordered.<BR>—6 Dropped, oozed out.<BR>—7 Lost, gone, perished; R. 3. 45.<BR>—8 Moved, shaken.<BR>—9 (also -त्री) Free quarters in connection with temples.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: च्युताधिकार, च्युतात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युताधिकार
च्युत + -अधिकार <i>a.</i> dismissed from office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युतात्मन्
च्युत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> of a depraved soul, evil-minded; Ku. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युतिः|च्युति
च्युतिः <i>f.</i> [च्यु-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Falling down, a fall.<BR>—2 Deviation from.<BR>—3 Dropping, oozing.<BR>—4 Losing, deprivation; धैर्यच्युतिं कुर्याम् Ku. 3. 10.<BR>—5 Vanishing, perishing.<BR>—6 The vulva.<BR>—7 The anus.<BR>—8 Quick motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत्
च्युत् €1 P. (च्योतति)<BR>—1 To drop, flow, ooze, trickle, stream forth; इदं शोणितमभ्यग्रं<BR> संप्रहारेऽच्युतत्तयोः Bk. 6. 28.<BR>—2 To drop or fall down, slip; इदं कवचमच्योतति Bk. 6. 29.<BR>—3 To cause to drop or steam forth.<BR>—4 To wet thoroughly, moisten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योतम्
च्योतम्<BR>—1 Sprinkling, pouring.<BR>—2 Dropping, falling.<BR>—3 Trickling, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युपः|च्युप
च्युपः The face, mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस्
च्युस् €10 P. (च्योसयति)<BR>—1 To laugh.<BR>—2 To suffer.<BR>—3 To leave.<BR>—4 To hurt, kill.<BR>—5 To loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यूतः|च्यूत
च्यूतः The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यौत्न|च्यौत्नः
च्यौत्न <i>a.</i> [च्यु गतौ करणे त्नण्]<BR>—1 Animating, enlivening. भुवो नॄँश्च्यौत्नो विश्वस्मिन् भरे Rv. 10. 50. 4.<BR>—2 A goer.<BR>—3 Oviparous.<BR>—4 Abandoned; wicked, void of virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यौत्नम्
च्यौत्न + .{@-त्नम्@}<BR>—1 Shaking, concussion; पुरां च्यौत्नाय शयथाय नू चित् Rv. 6. 18. 8.<BR>—2 Enterprise; प्र च्यौत्नानि देवयन्तो भरन्ते Rv. 1. 173. 4.<BR>—3 Management.<BR>—4 Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pure, clean.<BR>—2 Trembling, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छः|छ|छं
छ + .{@-छः@}<BR>—1 A part, fragment.<BR>—2 Cutting, dividing. Enm. says: छः सोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छा
छ + .{@-छा@}<BR>—1 Covering, concealing.<BR>—2 An infant, a child.<BR>—3 Quick-silver.<BR>—4 The number seven; छा च रुट् <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्
छ + .{@-छम्@} A house; छमर्चिर्भूतलं स्वः स्यात् कूटं कूलं मुखं कुलम् ।<BR> <i>ibid.</i> Nm. says: ‘छ इत्याच्छादनेऽब्जे च छं क्लीबे संवृतौ पुमान् । त्रिष्वयं निर्मले नित्ये मलिने भेदकेऽपि च ॥’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगः|छग
छगः (-गी <i>f.</i>) A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगणः|छगण|छगणं
छगणः, -णम्<BR> Dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगणम्
छगणः, -णम्<BR> Dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलः|छगल|छगलं
छगलः<BR>—1 A goat.<BR>—2 N. of the sage Atri.<BR>—3 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगला
छगलः + .{@-ला, -ली@} A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगली
छगलः + .{@-ला, -ली@} A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलम्
छगलः + .{@-लम्@} A blue cloth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छगलान्त्रिका, छगलान्त्रिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलान्त्रिका
छगलः + -अन्त्रिका, -अन्त्रिः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलान्त्रिः
छगलः + -अन्त्रिका, -अन्त्रिः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलकः|छगलक
छगलकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा<BR>—1 Mass, lump, number, assemblage; सटाच्छटाभिन्नघनेन Śi. 1. 74; Māl. 10. 10.<BR>—2 A collection of rays of light, lustre, splendour, light; भ्रमतः<BR> समरे बभ्रुर्वीरपट्टाञ्चलच्छटाः Rāj. T. 5. 333; Śi. 8. 38; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>—3 A continuous line, streak; छातेतराम्बुच्छटा K. P. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छटाभा, छटाफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाभा
छटा + -आभा lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाफलः|छटाफल
छटा + -फलः the betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रः|छत्र|छत्त्रं|छत्त्रः|छत्रं
छत्रः A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रम्
छत्रः + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 A parasol, an umbrella; अदेयमासीत् त्रयमेव भूपतेः शशिप्रभं छत्रमुभे<BR> च चामरे R. 3. 16; Ms. 7. 96.<BR>—2 Concealing the fault of oneʼs teacher.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छत्रधरः, छत्रधारः, छत्रधारण, छत्रपतिः, छत्रभङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधरः|छत्रधर
छत्रः + -धरः, -धारः the bearer of an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधारः|छत्रधार|छत्त्रधारः
छत्रः + -धरः, -धारः the bearer of an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधारण
छत्रः + -धारण<BR>—1 carrying<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">Page0717-a2</a>]<BR> or bearing an umbrella; Ms. 2. 178.<BR>—2 carrying an umbrella as a type of royal authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रपतिः|छत्रपति
छत्रः + -पतिः<BR>—1 a king over whom an umbrella is carried as a mark of dignity, a sovereign, emperor.<BR>—2 N. of an ancient king in जम्बुद्वीप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रभङ्गः|छत्रभङ्ग|छत्त्रभङ्गः|छत्रभंग
छत्रः + -भङ्गः<BR>—1 ‘destruction of the royal parasol’, loss of dominion, deposition.<BR>—2 dependence.<BR>—3 wilfulness.<BR>—4 a forlorn condition, widowhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रकः|छत्रक|छत्त्रकः
छत्रकः<BR>—1 A temple in honour of Śiva.<BR>—2 A bee-hive of a conical form.<BR>—3 A king-fisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिका
छत्रकः + .{@-त्रिका@} Mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रकम्
छत्रकः + .{@-कम्@} A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रा
छत्रा, छत्राकः A mushroom; Ms. 5. 19; Y. 1. 176; also छत्राकी-कम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्राकः|छत्राक|छत्त्राकं|छत्त्राकः
छत्रा, छत्राकः A mushroom; Ms. 5. 19; Y. 1. 176; also छत्राकी-कम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिकः|छत्रिक
छत्रिकः The bearer of an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिन्
छत्रिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>) Having or bearing an umbrella.<BR>━<i>m.</i> A barber.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छत्रिन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिन्यायः|छत्रिन्याय
छत्रिन् + -न्यायः ‘the manner of applying the term छत्रिन् to a king’,<BR> permitted synonym; Mbh. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रीकृ
छत्रीकृ To use as a parasol; छत्रीकृत्यैकमम्बुजम् Ks. 69. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्वरः|छत्वर
छत्वरः<BR>—1 A house.<BR>—2 A bower, arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् €10 U. (छदति-ते, छादयति-ते, छन्न, छादित)<BR>—1 To cover, cover over, veil; हैमैश्छन्ना Me. 76; चक्षुः खेदात्सलिलगुरुभिः<BR> पक्ष्मभिश्छादयन्तीम् Me. 90; छन्नोपान्तः … काननाम्रैः Me. 18.<BR>—2 To spread anything (as a cover), cover oneself.<BR>—3 To hide,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">Page0718-1</a>]<BR> conceal; Pt. 1. 287; (fig.); keep secret; ज्ञानपूर्वं कृतं कर्म छादयन्ते<BR> ह्यसाधवः Mb.; छन्नं दोषमुदाहरन्ति Mk. 9. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0717-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदः|छद
छदः, -छदनम्<BR>—1 A covering, cover; अल्पच्छद, उत्तरच्छद &c.<BR>—2 A wing; अन्यभृतच्छदच्छवेः Śi. 16. 50; च्छदहेम कषन्निवालसत् N. 2. 69.<BR>—3 A leaf.<BR>—4 A sheath, case; षण्णेम्यनन्तच्छदि यत्त्रिणाभि Bhāg. 3. 21. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छदपत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदनम्
छदः, -छदनम्<BR>—1 A covering, cover; अल्पच्छद, उत्तरच्छद &c.<BR>—2 A wing; अन्यभृतच्छदच्छवेः Śi. 16. 50; च्छदहेम कषन्निवालसत् N. 2. 69.<BR>—3 A leaf.<BR>—4 A sheath, case; षण्णेम्यनन्तच्छदि यत्त्रिणाभि Bhāg. 3. 21. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छदपत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदपत्रः|छदपत्र|छदपत्त्रः
छदः + -पत्रः the Bhūrja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिः|छदि
छदिः <i>f.</i>, छदिस् <i>n.</i><BR> [छद्-कि-इस् वा]<BR>—1 The roof of a carriage.<BR>—2 The roof or thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिस्
छदिः <i>f.</i>, छदिस् <i>n.</i><BR> [छद्-कि-इस् वा]<BR>—1 The roof of a carriage.<BR>—2 The roof or thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन् <i>n.</i> [छाद्यते स्वरूपमनेन; छद्-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 144]<BR>—1 A deceptive dress, a disguise.<BR>—2 A plea, pretext, guise; ब्रह्मछद्मा सामर्थ्यसारः Mv. 2. 25; पलितछद्मना<BR> जरा R. 12. 2; Śi. 2. 21; कुतोऽन्यथा स्रवत्येष स्वेदच्छद्मामृतद्रवः Ratn. 2. 17.<BR>—3 Fraud, dishonesty, trick; छद्मना परिददामि मृत्यवे U. 1. 46;<BR> Ms. 4. 199, 9. 72.<BR>—4 The thatch or roof of a house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छद्मतापसः, छद्मरूपेण, छद्मवेशिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मतापसः|छद्मतापस
छद्मन् + -तापसः a religious hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मरूपेण
छद्मन् + -रूपेण <i>ind.</i> incognito, in disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मवेशिन्
छद्मन् + -वेशिन् <i>m.</i> a player, a cheat, one dressed in disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मिन्
छद्मिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [छद्मन्-इनि]<BR>—1 Fraudulent, deceitful.<BR>—2 Disguised (at the end of comp.); <i>e. g.</i> ब्राह्मणछद्मिन् disguised<BR> as a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न <i>a.</i> [छद्-क्त नि˚]<BR>—1 Covered.<BR>—2 Hidden, concealed, secret &c.; see छद्.<BR>—3 Desolate, solitary.<BR>—4 Private.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्नम्
छन्न + .{@-न्नम्@} A secret; वागुराच्छन्नमाश्रित्य मृगाणामिष्यते वधः । भवाञ्छन्नेन<BR> दण्डितः Abhiṣeka. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्नवीरम्
छन्नवीरम् A kind of necklace; Māna. 50. 35-36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छनच्छन्
छनच्छन् <i>ind.</i> An imitative sound, expressive of the noise of<BR> falling drops &c.; छनच्छनिति बाष्पकणाः पतन्ति Amaru. 86. (छमच्छमिति v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द्|छंद्
छन्द् €10 U. (छन्दयति-ते, छन्दित)<BR>—1 To please, gratify.<BR>—2 To persuade, coax.<BR>—3 To cover.<BR>—4 To be delighted in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द|छंद|छन्दः
छन्द <i>a.</i> [छन्द्-अच्]<BR>—1 Pleasing, fascinating, inviting, alluring.<BR>—2 Private, solitary, secret. —3 Praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दः|छन्द|छंद
छन्द + .{@-दः@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Wish, desire, fancy, liking, will; विज्ञाप्यतां देवी यस्ते छन्द इति<BR> V. 3 just as you like; Pt. 1. 69. एते ते मृत्युना ये चिरमनवसिता<BR> … श्छन्दं मृगयता Pratimā 3. 7.<BR>—2 Free will, oneʼs own choice, whim, free or wilful conduct; षष्ठे<BR> काले त्वमपि दिवसस्यात्मनश्छन्दवतीं V. 2. 1; Gīt. 1; Y. 2. 195; स्वच्छन्दम्<BR> according to oneʼs free will, independently.<BR>—3 (Hence) subjection, control.<BR>—4 Meaning, intention, purport.<BR>—5 Poison.<BR>—6 Appearance, look, shape.<BR>—7 Pleasure, delight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छन्दानुवृत्तम्, छन्दानुवृत्तिः, छन्दपातनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दानुवृत्तम्
छन्द + -अनुवृत्तम्, -अनुवृत्तिः indulgence of whims, humouring, compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दानुवृत्तिः
छन्द + -अनुवृत्तम्, -अनुवृत्तिः indulgence of whims, humouring, compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दपातनः|छन्दपातन
छन्द + -पातनः A religious hypocrite. L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दकः|छन्दक|छंदकः
छन्दकः<BR>—1 An epithet of Vāsudeva.<BR>—2 A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दन|छंदन
छन्दन <i>a.</i> Pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्|छंदस्
छन्दस् <i>n.</i> [छन्दयति असुन्]<BR>—1 Wish, desire, fancy, will, pleasure; (गृह्णीयात्) मूर्खं छन्दोऽनुवृत्तेन<BR> याथातथ्येन पण्डितम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">Page0718-2</a>]<BR> Cāṇ. 33.<BR>—2 Free will, free or wilful conduct.<BR>—3 Meaning, intention.<BR>—4 Fraud, trick, deceit.<BR>—5 The Vedas, the sacred text of the Vedic hymns; स च कुलपतिराद्यश्छन्दसां<BR> यः प्रयोक्ता U. 3. 48; बहुलं छन्दसि frequently used by Pāṇini;<BR> प्रणवश्छन्दसामिव R. 1. 11; Y. 1. 143; Ms. 4. 95.<BR>—6 A metre; ऋक्छन्दसा आशास्ते Ś. 4; गायत्री छन्दसामहम् Bg. 10. 35, 13. 4.<BR>—7 Metrical science prosody; (regarded as one of the six Vedāṅgas or<BR> auxiliaries to the Vedas, the other five being शिक्षा, कल्प, व्याकरण,<BR> निरुक्त and ज्योतिष).<BR>—8 A metrical composition. … मया काव्यानि तन्वता छन्दो विनिर्मितं<BR> तस्मिन् कृतः सर्वस्य संग्रहः Parṇāl. 1. 23.<BR>—9 A festival; वेदे वाक्ये वृत्तभेदे उत्सवेऽपि नपुंसकम् । Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छन्दःकृतम्, छन्दोगः, छन्दोभङ्गः, छन्दोविचितिः, छन्दोवृत्तम्, छन्दःस्तुभ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दःकृतम्
छन्दस् + -कृतम् any metrical part of the Vedas or other sacred compositions;<BR> यथोदितेन विधिना नित्यं छन्दस्कृतं पठेत् Ms. 4. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोगः|छन्दोग|छंदोग
छन्दस् + -गः (छन्दोगः)<BR>—1 a reciter in metre.<BR>—2 a student or chanter of the Sāmaveda; Ms. 3. 145; (छन्दोगः सामवेदाध्यायी)<BR>—3 The Sāmaveda; साम्नां जैमिनये प्राह तथा छन्दोगसंहिताम् Bhāg. 12. 6. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोभङ्गः|छन्दोभङ्ग
छन्दस् + -भङ्गः a violation of the laws of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोविचितिः|छन्दोविचिति|छंदोविचिति
छन्दस् + -विचितिः <i>f.</i> ‘examination of metres’, N. of a work on metres,<BR> sometimes ascribed to Daṇḍin; छन्दोविचित्या सकलस्तत्प्रपञ्चो निदर्शितः Kāv. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोवृत्तम्
छन्दस् + -वृत्तम् a metre in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दःस्तुभ्
छन्दस् + -स्तुभ् <i>m.</i> N. of Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्य|छंदस्य
छन्दस्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Fit for hymns, metrical.<BR>—2 Made at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दित|छंदित
छन्दित <i>a.</i> Gratified, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दु|छंदु
छन्दु <i>a.</i> Ved. Pleasing, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्
छम् €1 P. (छमति) To eat, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमच्छमित
