छर्दिस्
छर्दिस् <i>f.</i> [छर्द्-भावे इति]<BR>—1 Vomiting.<BR>—2 A secure place or residence; प्र नो यच्छतादवृकं पृथु च्छर्दिः Rv. 1. 48. 15.<BR>—3 A house; यातं छर्दिष्पा उत नः परस्पा Rv. 8. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलः|छल|छलं
छलः, -लम्<BR> [छल्-अच्]<BR>—1 Fraud, trick, deceit, deception; विद्महे शठ पलायनच्छलानि R. 19. 31;<BR> छलमत्र न गृह्यते Mk. 9. 18; Y. 1. 61; Ms. 8. 49, 187;<BR> Amaru. 16; Śi. 13. 11.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">Page0719-1</a>]<BR>—2 Roguery, knavery.<BR>—3 A plea, pretext, guise, semblance (often used in this sense to denote<BR> an उत्प्रेक्षा); असुरक्षाहि बहुच्छलाः श्रियः Ki. 2. 39; परिखावलयच्छलेन<BR> या न परेषां ग्रहणस्य गोचरा N. 2. 95; प्रत्यर्प्य पूजामुपदाच्छलेन<BR> R. 7. 30, 6. 54, 16. 28; Bk. 1. 1; Amaru. 15; Māl. 9. 1.<BR>—4 Intention.<BR>—5 Wickedness.<BR>—6 A family.<BR>—7 Design, device.<BR>—8 Fiction, circumvention.<BR>—9 Deceitful disputation, perverting the sense of words; विधर्मः परधर्मश्च<BR> आभास उपमा छलः । अधर्मशाखाः पञ्चेमा धर्मज्ञोऽधर्मवत् त्यजेत् Bhāg. 7. 15. 12.<BR>—10 Difficult subject; ब्रह्म हि प्रचुरच्छलम् Mb. 12. 328. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलम्
छलः, -लम्<BR> [छल्-अच्]<BR>—1 Fraud, trick, deceit, deception; विद्महे शठ पलायनच्छलानि R. 19. 31;<BR> छलमत्र न गृह्यते Mk. 9. 18; Y. 1. 61; Ms. 8. 49, 187;<BR> Amaru. 16; Śi. 13. 11.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">Page0719-1</a>]<BR>—2 Roguery, knavery.<BR>—3 A plea, pretext, guise, semblance (often used in this sense to denote<BR> an उत्प्रेक्षा); असुरक्षाहि बहुच्छलाः श्रियः Ki. 2. 39; परिखावलयच्छलेन<BR> या न परेषां ग्रहणस्य गोचरा N. 2. 95; प्रत्यर्प्य पूजामुपदाच्छलेन<BR> R. 7. 30, 6. 54, 16. 28; Bk. 1. 1; Amaru. 15; Māl. 9. 1.<BR>—4 Intention.<BR>—5 Wickedness.<BR>—6 A family.<BR>—7 Design, device.<BR>—8 Fiction, circumvention.<BR>—9 Deceitful disputation, perverting the sense of words; विधर्मः परधर्मश्च<BR> आभास उपमा छलः । अधर्मशाखाः पञ्चेमा धर्मज्ञोऽधर्मवत् त्यजेत् Bhāg. 7. 15. 12.<BR>—10 Difficult subject; ब्रह्म हि प्रचुरच्छलम् Mb. 12. 328. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलक
छलक <i>a.</i> Delusive, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलयति
छलयति Den. P. To outwit, deceive, cheat; बलिं छलयते Gīt. 1;<BR> शैवाललोलांश्छलयन्ति मीनान् R. 16. 61; Bg. 10. 36; Amaru. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिकम्
छलिकम् A kind of drama or dancing, a song consisting of four parts<BR> and recited with gesticulation; छलिकं दुष्प्रयोज्यमुदाहरन्ति M. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलनम्
छलनम्, -ना<BR> [छल् णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Deceiving, cheating, outwitting; अथोपपत्तिं छलनापरोऽपराम् Śi. 1. 69.<BR>—2 Fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलना
छलनम्, -ना<BR> [छल् णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Deceiving, cheating, outwitting; अथोपपत्तिं छलनापरोऽपराम् Śi. 1. 69.<BR>—2 Fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलित
छलित <i>a.</i> Cheated, deceived &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलितम्
छलित + .{@-तम्@} Deceiving, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिन्
छलिन् <i>m.</i> A cheat, swindler, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लिः|छल्लि
छल्लिः, -ल्ली <i>f.</i><BR> [छद्-क्विप् तां लाति ला-क गौरा˚ ङीष्]<BR>—1 Bark, rind.<BR>—2 A spreading creeper.<BR>—3 Offspring, progeny, posterity; छल्ली वीरुधि सन्ताने वल्कले कुसुमान्तरे Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्ली
छल्लिः, -ल्ली <i>f.</i><BR> [छद्-क्विप् तां लाति ला-क गौरा˚ ङीष्]<BR>—1 Bark, rind.<BR>—2 A spreading creeper.<BR>—3 Offspring, progeny, posterity; छल्ली वीरुधि सन्ताने वल्कले कुसुमान्तरे Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छविः|छवि
छविः <i>f.</i> [छपति असारं छिनत्ति तमो वा छो-वि किच्च वा ङीप्;<BR> cf. Uṇ. 4. 56]<BR>—1 Hue, colour of the skin, complexion; हिमकरोदयपाण्डुमुखच्छविः<BR> R. 9. 38; छविः पाण्डुरा Ś. 3. 10; Me. 33; U. 6. 27.<BR>—2 Colour in general.<BR>—3 Beauty, splendour, brilliance; छविकरं मुखचूर्णमृतुश्रियः R. 9. 45.<BR>—4 Light, lustre.<BR>—5 Skin, hide; लोहितार्द्रीकृतच्छविः Mb. 12. 149. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छविल्लाकरः|छविल्लाकर
छविल्लाकरः N. of a historian of Kashmir; येऽप्यशोकादयः पञ्च<BR> श्रीछविल्लाकरोऽब्रवीत् Rāj. T. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छष्
छष् €1 U. (छषति-ते) To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग <i>a.</i> (-गी <i>f.</i>) Relating to a goat or she-goat; Y. 1. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागः|छाग
छाग + .{@-गः@} (-गी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A goat; ब्राह्मणश्छागतो यथा (वञ्चितः) H. 4. 53; Ms. 3. 269;<BR> छागो वा मन्त्रवर्णात् Ms. 6. 8. 31.<BR>—2 The sign Aries of the zodiac.<BR>—3 A horse whose movements have been cut off: यश्छिन्नगमनोऽश्वः स<BR> छागः । छिदेर्गमेश्च छागशब्दः ग्रसिद्धः । ŚB. on MS. 6. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागम्
छाग + .{@-गम्@}<BR>—1 The milk of a she-goat.<BR>—2 An oblation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छागभोजिन्, छागमुखः, छागरयः, छागवाहनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागभोजिन्
छाग + -भोजिन् <i>m.</i> a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागमुखः|छागमुख
छाग + -मुखः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागरयः
छाग + -रयः, -वाहनः an epithet of Agni, the god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागवाहनः|छागवाहन
छाग + -रयः, -वाहनः an epithet of Agni, the god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागणः|छागण
छागणः A fire of dried cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>) Coming from or relating to a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलः|छागल
छागल + .{@-लः@} A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागिका
छागिका A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Cut, divided.<BR>—2 Feeble, thin, emaciated (<i>p. p.</i> of छो q. v.). स्वच्छन्दो च्छलदच्छकच्छकुहरच्छातेतराम्बुच्छटा K. P. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रः|छात्र|छात्त्रः|छात्रं
छात्रः [छत्रं गुरोर्वैगुण्यावरणं शीलमस्य Sk.; छत्रा˚ ण]<BR> A pupil, disciple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रम्
छात्रः + .{@-त्रम्@} A kind of honey.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छात्रगण्डः, छात्रदर्शनम्, छात्रव्यंसकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रगण्डः|छात्रगण्ड|छात्रगंड
छात्रः + -गण्डः an indifferent poetical scholar, knowing only the beginnings of stanzas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रदर्शनम्
छात्रः + -दर्शनम् fresh butter prepared from milk one day old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रव्यंसकः|छात्रव्यंसक
छात्रः + -व्यंसकः a roguish or dull-witted pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रकम्
छात्रकम् Honey in the comb or hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादम्
छादम् [छद्-अच्] A thatch, roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादनम्
छादनम् [छद्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A cover, screen (fig. also); विनिर्मितं छादनमज्ञतायाः Bh. 2. 7.<BR>—2 Concealing.<BR>—3 A leaf.<BR>—4 Clothing.<BR>—5 Darkening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादनी
छादनम् + .{@-नी@} Hide, skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादित|छादितः
छादित <i>a.</i> See छन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक <i>a.</i> [छद्मना चरति व्यवहरति ठक्] Fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिकः|छाद्मिक
छाद्मिक + .{@-कः@} A rogue; Ms. 4. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दस|छांदस|छान्दसः
छान्दस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>) [छन्दः अधीते वेत्ति वा पक्षे अण्]<BR>—1 Vedic, peculiar to the Vedas; as छान्दसः प्रयोगः.<BR>—2 Studying or familiar with the Vedas.<BR>—3 Metrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दसः|छान्दस|छांदस
छान्दस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas.<BR>—2 The Vedas; मन्ये त्वां विषये वाचां स्नातमन्यत्र छान्दसात् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दसीय|छांदसीय
छान्दसीय <i>a.</i> Metrical, familiar with metres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोमिक|छांदोमिक
छान्दोमिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the छन्दोमस् (as a day or सूक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाया
छाया [छो-ण Uṇ. 4. 109]<BR>—1 Shade, shadow (changed at the end of Tat. comp. into छायम् when<BR> बाहुल्य or thickness of shade is meant; <i>e. g.</i> इक्षुच्छायनिषादिन्यः<BR> R. 4. 20; so 7. 4, 12. 50; Mu. 4. 21); छायामधः सानुगतां निषेव्य<BR> Ku. 1. 5, 6. 46; अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णं शमयति परितापं<BR> छायया संश्रितानाम् Ś. 5. 7; R. 1. 75, 2. 6, 3. 70; Me. 67.<BR>—2 A reflected image, a reflection; छाया न मूर्छति मलोपहतप्रसादे<BR> शुद्धे तु दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32.<BR>—3 Resemblance, likeness; क्षित्यादीनामिहार्थानां छाया न कतमापि हि<BR> Bhāg. 7. 15. 59.<BR>—4 A shadowy fancy, hallucination; असता छाययोक्ताय सदाभासाय ते नमः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 3. 14.<BR>—5 Blending of colours.<BR>—6 Lustre, light; भ्रष्टश्च स्वरयोगो मे छाया चापगता मम Rām. 2. 69. 20.<BR> छायामण्डललक्ष्येण R. 4. 5; रत्नच्छायाव्यतिकरः Me. 15, 35.<BR>—7 Colour; Māl. 6. 5.<BR>—8 Colour of the face, complexion; केवलं लावण्यमयी छाया त्वां न<BR> मुञ्चति Ś. 3; मेघैरन्तरितः प्रिये तव मुखच्छायानुकारी शशी S. D.; Pt. 5. 88.<BR>—9 Beauty क्षामच्छायं भवनम् Me. 80, 104.<BR>—10 Protection.<BR>—11 A row, line.<BR>—12 Darkness; (metaphorically) Avidyā; छायातपौ यत्र न गृध्रपक्षौ<BR> Bhāg. 8. 5. 27.<BR>—13 A bribe.<BR>—14 N. of Durgā.<BR>—15 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">Page0720-1</a>]<BR> shadow of a gnomon as indicating the sunʼs position.<BR>—16 The Sun.<BR>—17 Nightmare.<BR>—18 N. of a wife of the sun (she was but a shadow or likeness of संज्ञा,<BR> the wife of the sun; consequently when संज्ञा went to her fatherʼs<BR> house without the knowledge of her husband, she put छाया in her own<BR> place. छाया bore to the sun three children:− two sons Sāvarṇi and<BR> Śani, and one daughter Tapanī).<BR>—19 A Sanskrit version of a Prākṛt text.<BR>—20 The Ganges; L. D. B.<BR>—21 Method; L. D. B.<BR>—22 A servantʼs chit; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायः|छाय
छाया + .{@-यः@} One who grants shade.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छायाङ्कः, छायात्मन्, छायाकरः, छायाग्रहः, छायातनयः, छायासुतः, छायात्मजः, छायातरुः, छायाद्रुमः, छायाद्वितीय, छायापथः, छायाभृत्, छायामानः, छायामित्रम्, छायामृगधरः, छायायन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाङ्कः|छायाङ्क|छायांक
छाया + -अङ्कः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायात्मन्
छाया + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> a reflected image or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाकरः|छायाकर
छाया + -करः the bearer of an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाग्रहः|छायाग्रह
छाया + -ग्रहः a mirror, or a sun-dial; प्रसन्नालापसंप्राप्तौ छायाग्रह<BR> इवापरः Rāj. T. 3. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातनयः|छायातनय
छाया + -तनयः, -सुतः, -आत्मजः Saturn, son of छाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायासुतः|छायासुत
छाया + -तनयः, -सुतः, -आत्मजः Saturn, son of छाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायात्मजः|छायात्मज
छाया + -तनयः, -सुतः, -आत्मजः Saturn, son of छाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातरुः|छायातरु
छाया + -तरुः, -द्रुमः<BR>—1 a large umbrageous tree; स्निग्धच्छायातरुषु वसतिं रामगिर्याश्रमेषु<BR> Me. 1; Ś. 4. 11.<BR>—2 The Nameru tree; छायावृक्षो नमेरौ स्यात् । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाद्रुमः|छायाद्रुम
छाया + -तरुः, -द्रुमः<BR>—1 a large umbrageous tree; स्निग्धच्छायातरुषु वसतिं रामगिर्याश्रमेषु<BR> Me. 1; Ś. 4. 11.<BR>—2 The Nameru tree; छायावृक्षो नमेरौ स्यात् । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाद्वितीय
छाया + -द्वितीय <i>a.</i> ‘accompanied only by oneʼs shadow’, alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायापथः|छायापथ
छाया + -पथः the galaxy, the atmosphere; R. 13. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाभृत्
छाया + -भृत् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामानः|छायामान
छाया + -मानः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामानम्
छाया + -मानः + .({@-नम्@}) a measure of shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामित्रम्
छाया + -मित्रम् a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामृगधरः|छायामृगधर
छाया + -मृगधरः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायायन्त्रम्
छाया + -यन्त्रम् a sun-dial; छायाम्बुयन्त्रसंविदिते Bṛ. S. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायक
छायक <i>a.</i> Causing nightmare, dark like shadow; पवीनसात् तङ्गल्वा<BR> ३ च्छायकादुत नग्नकात् Av. 8. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामय
छायामय <i>a.</i> Reflected, shadowy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालः|छाल|छालं
छालः, -लम्<BR> Bark; a bark-garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालम्
छालः, -लम्<BR> Bark; a bark-garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिः|छि
छिः <i>f.</i> [छो-बा˚ कि] Abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्का
छिक्का Sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित|छितं
छित <i>a.</i> See छात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् €7 U. (छिनत्ति, छिन्ते, चिच्छेद, अच्छिदत्, अच्छैत्सीत्, अच्छित्त,<BR> छेत्तुम्, छिन्न)<BR>—1 To cut, cut or lop off, hew, mow, tear, pierce, break asunder, rend,<BR> split, divide; नैनं छिन्दन्ति शस्त्राणि Bg. 2. 23; R. 12. 80; Ms. 4. 69, 70, 9. 276;<BR> Y. 2. 302.<BR>—2 To disturb, interrupt (as sleep).<BR>—3 To remove, drive off, destroy, quell, annihilate; तृष्णां छिन्द्धि<BR> Bh. 2. 77; एतन्मे संशयं छिन्द्धि मतिर्मे संप्रमुह्यति Mb.; राघवो<BR> रथमप्राप्तां तामाशां च सुरद्विषाम् । अर्धचन्द्रमुखैर्बाणैश्चिच्छेद कदलीमुखम् ॥<BR> R. 12. 96; Ku. 7. 16.<BR>—4 To take away, remove, deprive of; न नः किंचिद् छिद्यते Ś. B.<BR> we do not lose anything [cf. L. <i>scindo</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्तिः|छित्ति
छित्तिः <i>f.</i> [छिद्-क्तिन्] Cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्वर|छित्वरः
छित्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [छिद्-ष्वर प् पृषो˚ दस्य तः]<BR>—1 Fit for cutting.<BR>—2 Hostile, fraudulent, roguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Cutting, dividing, destroying, removing,<BR> splitting &c.; श्रमच्छिदामाश्रमपादपानाम् R. 5. 6; पङ्कच्छिदः<BR> फलस्य M. 2. 8. ━<i>m.</i> The divisor, denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदकम्
छिदकम् [छिद्-क्वुन्]<BR>—1 Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR>—2 A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदा
छिदा Cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिः|छिदि
छिदिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An axe.<BR>—2 Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR>—3 Cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिरः|छिदिर
छिदिरः [छिद्-किरच् Uṇ. 1. 51]<BR>—1 An axe.<BR>—2 A sword.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR>—4 A rope, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर <i>a.</i> [छिद्-कुरच्]<BR>—1 Cutting, dividing, removing; Śi. 6. 8.<BR>—2 Easily breaking.<BR>—3 Broken, disordered, deranged; संलक्ष्यते न च्छिदुरोऽपि हारः R. 16. 62.<BR>—4 Hostile.<BR>—5 Roguish, knavish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र <i>a.</i> [छिद्-रक्, छिद्र-अच् वा] Pierced, containing holes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रम्
छिद्र + .{@-द्रम्@}<BR>—1 A hole, slit, cleft, fissure, rent, pit, opening, crack; नव छिद्राणि<BR> तान्येव प्राणस्यायतनानि तु Y. 3. 99; Ms. 8. 239; अयं पटश्छिद्रशतैरलङ्कृतः<BR> Mk. 2. 9; so काष्ठ˚, भूमि˚ &c.<BR>—2 A defect, flaw, blemish; त्वं हि सर्षपमात्राणि परच्छिद्राणि पश्यसि ।<BR> आत्मनो बिल्वमात्राणि पश्यन्नपि न पश्यसि ॥ Mb.; सुग्रीवेण समं<BR> त्वस्य अद्वैधं छिद्रवर्जितम् Rām. 7. 36. 39.<BR>—3 A vulnerable or weak point, weak side, imperfection, foible; नास्य<BR> छिद्रं परो विद्याद्विद्याच्छिद्रं परस्य तु । गूहेत् कूर्म इवाङ्गानि रक्षेद्विवरमात्मनः ॥<BR> Ms. 7. 105, 102; छिद्रं निरूप्य सहसा प्रविशत्यशङ्कः H. 1. 81.<BR> (where छिद्र means a hole also); Pt. 3. 39; Pt. 2. 38; <i>Proverb</i>:−<BR> छिद्रेष्वनर्था बहुलीभवन्ति ‘misfortunes never come single’.<BR>—4 (Astr.) N. of the eighth house.<BR>—5 Division; भूमिच्छिद्रविधानम् Kau. A. 2. 2;<BR>—6 Space; भूतानां छिद्रदातृत्वं बहिरन्तरमेव च Bhāg. 3. 26. 34.<BR>—7 Sky; नानात्वं छिद्रयोर्यद्वज्ज्योतिषोर्वातयोरिव Bhāg. 12. 4. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छिद्रानुजीविन्, छिद्रानुसंधानिन्, छिद्रानुसारिन्, छिद्रान्वेषिन्, छिद्रान्तर्, छिद्रात्मन्, छिद्रकर्ण, छिद्रदर्शन, छिद्रदर्शिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रानुजीविन्
छिद्र + -अनुजीविन्, -अनुसंधानिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -अन्वेषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking out for faults or flaws.<BR>—2 seeking the weak points of another, picking holes, censorious; सर्पाणां<BR> दुर्जनानां च परच्छिद्रानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रानुसंधानिन्
छिद्र + -अनुजीविन्, -अनुसंधानिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -अन्वेषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking out for faults or flaws.<BR>—2 seeking the weak points of another, picking holes, censorious; सर्पाणां<BR> दुर्जनानां च परच्छिद्रानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रानुसारिन्
छिद्र + -अनुजीविन्, -अनुसंधानिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -अन्वेषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking out for faults or flaws.<BR>—2 seeking the weak points of another, picking holes, censorious; सर्पाणां<BR> दुर्जनानां च परच्छिद्रानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्वेषिन्
छिद्र + -अनुजीविन्, -अनुसंधानिन्, -अनुसारिन्, -अन्वेषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking out for faults or flaws.<BR>—2 seeking the weak points of another, picking holes, censorious; सर्पाणां<BR> दुर्जनानां च परच्छिद्रानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्तर्|छिद्रांतर्
छिद्र + -अन्तर् <i>m.</i> a cane, reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रात्मन्
छिद्र + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> one who exposes his weak points to the attack of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रकर्ण
छिद्र + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> having the ear pierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रदर्शन
छिद्र + -दर्शन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 exhibiting faults.<BR>—2 seeking the weak points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रदर्शिन्
छिद्र + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> observing faults, a captious critic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रयति
छिद्रयति Den. P. To perforate, bore, pierce through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रित|छिद्रितः
छिद्रित <i>a.</i> [छिद्र् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 having holes.<BR>—2 Bored, perforated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्वर
छिद्वर = छित्वर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्न|छिन्नं
छिन्न <i>p. p.</i> [छिद्-क्त]<BR>—1 Cut, divided, rent, chopped, riven, torn, broken.<BR>—2 Destroyed, removed; see छिद्<BR>—3 Decaying, declining.<BR>—4 Exhausted, tired, fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ना
छिन्न + .{@-न्ना@} A whore, harlot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: छिन्नकेश, छिन्नद्रुमः, छिन्नद्वैध, छिन्ननासिक, छिन्नभिन्न, छिन्नमस्त, छिन्नमस्तक, छिन्नमूल, छिन्नश्वासः, छिन्नसंशय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

