जङ्गलम्
जङ्गल + .{@-लः, -लम्@} Flesh, meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गलम्
जङ्गल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A desert, dreary ground, waste land.<BR>—2 A thicket, forest.<BR>—3 A secluded or unfrequented place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गालः|जङ्गाल|जंगाल|जंगालः
जङ्गालः A ridge of earth running along the edge of a field to collect<BR> water and to form a passage over it, land-mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गिडः|जङ्गिड
जङ्गिडः N. of a plant or a gem worn as an amulet; मणिं विष्कन्धदूषणं<BR> जङ्गिडं बिभृमो वयम् Av. 2. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गुलम्
जङ्गुलम् Poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घा|जंघा
जङ्घा [जङ्घन्यते कुटिलं गच्छति हन् यङ्-लुकि अच् पृषो˚; cf. Uṇ. 5. 31]<BR>—1 Leg from the ankle to the knee, the shank.<BR>—2 The upper part of the leg, the part about the loins.<BR>—3 A part of a bed-stead.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जङ्घाकरः, जङ्घाकरिकः, जङ्घाकारः, जङ्घाकारिकः, जङ्घात्राणम्, जङ्घापथः, जङ्घाबलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाकरः|जङ्घाकर
जङ्घा + -करः, -करिकः, -कारः, -कारिकः a runner, courier, an express. Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0723-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाकरिकः|जङ्घाकरिक
