जन्
जन् €4 Ā. (जायते, जज्ञे, अजनि-अजनिष्ट, जनितुम्, जात; <i>pass.</i><BR> जन्यते or जायते)<BR>—1 To be born or produced (with abl. of source of birth); अजाने ते वै<BR> पुत्रः Ait. Br.; Ms. 1. 9, 3. 39, 41; प्राणाद्वायुरजायत Rv. 10. 90. 12;<BR> Ms. 10. 8, 3. 76, 1. 75.<BR>—2 To rise, spring up, grow (as a plant &c.)<BR>—3 To be, become, happen, take place, occur; अनिष्टादिष्टलाभेऽपि न गतिर्जायते<BR> शुभा H. 1. 6; रक्तनेत्रोऽजनि क्षणात Bk. 6. 32; Y. 3. 226; Ms. 1. 99.<BR>—4 To be possible, applicable &c.<BR>—5 To be born or destined for anything. ━<i>Caus.</i> (जनयति)<BR>—1 To give birth, beget, cause, produce.<BR>—2 To cause, occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनः|जन
जनः [जन्-अच्]<BR>—1 A creature, living being, man.<BR>—2 An individual or person (whether male or female); क्व वयं क्व परोक्षमन्मथो<BR> मृगशावैः सममेधितो जनः Ś. 2. 18; तत्तस्य किमपि द्रव्यं यो हि<BR> यस्य प्रियो जनः U. 2. 19; so सखीजनः a female friend; दासजनः<BR> a slave, अबलाजनः &c. (In this sense जनः or अयं जनः<BR> is often used by the speaker whether male or female, in the sing. or pl.<BR> −instead of the first personal pronoun to speak of himself in the third<BR> person); अयं जनः प्रष्टुमनास्तपोधने Ku. 5. 40 (male); भगवन्<BR> परवानयं जनः प्रतिकूलाचरितं क्षमख मे R. 8. 81 (female); पश्यानङ्गशरातुरं<BR> जनमिमं त्रातापि नो रक्षसि Nāg. 1. 1 (female and pl.).<BR>—3 Men collectively, the people, the world (in sing. or pl.); एवं जनो<BR> गृह्णाति M. 1; सतीमपि ज्ञातिकुलैकसंश्रयां जनोऽन्यथा भर्तृमतीं<BR> विशङ्कते Ś. 5. 17.<BR>—4 Race, nation, tribe.<BR>—5 The world beyond Maharloka, the heaven of deified mortals.<BR>—6 A low man, the mob; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जना
जनः + .{@-ना@} Birth, production.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जनातिग, जनाधिपः, जनाधिनाथः, जनान्तः, जनान्तिकम्, जनार्णवः, जनार्थशब्दः, जनार्दनः, जनाशनः, जनाकीर्ण, जनाचारः, जनाश्रमः, जनाश्रयः, जनेन्द्रः, जनेशः, जनेश्वरः, जनेष्ट, जनोदाहरणम्, जनौघः, जनकारिन्, जनचक्षुस्, जनजन्मादिः, जनजल्पः, जनत्रा, जनदेवः, जनपदः, जनपदिन्, जनप्रवादः, जनप्रिय, जनमरकः, जनमर्यादा, जनमारः, जनयोपन, जनरञ्जनम्, जनरवः, जनलोकः, जनवादः, जनव्यवहारः, जनश्रुत, जनश्रुतिः, जनंसह, जनसंबाध, जनस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनातिग
जनः + -अतिग <i>a.</i> extraordinary, uncommon, superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाधिपः|जनाधिप
जनः + -अधिपः, -अधिनाथः<BR>—1 a king<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाधिनाथः|जनाधिनाथ
जनः + -अधिपः, -अधिनाथः<BR>—1 a king<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तः|जनान्त|जनांत
जनः + -अन्तः<BR>—1 a place removed from men, an uninhabited place.<BR>—2 a region.<BR>—3 an epithet of Yama.<BR>—4 personal proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तिकम्|जनांतिकम्
जनः + -अन्तिकम् secret communication, whispering or speaking aside (to<BR> another). ━(<i>ind.</i>) aside to another (in dramas); the S. D. thus defines<BR> this stage direction:− त्रिपताककरेणान्यानपवार्यान्तरा कथाम् । अन्योन्यामन्त्रणं<BR> यत् स्याज्जनान्ते तज्जनान्तिकम् ॥ 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनार्णवः|जनार्णव
जनः + -अर्णवः a large concourse of people, caravan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनार्थशब्दः|जनार्थशब्द
जनः + -अर्थशब्दः a family appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनार्दनः|जनार्दन|जनार्द्दन|जनार्द्दनः
जनः + -अर्दनः an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाशनः|जनाशन
जनः + -अशनः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाकीर्ण
जनः + -आकीर्ण <i>a.</i> thronged or crowded with people; Ś. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाचारः|जनाचार
जनः + -आचारः<BR>—1 a popular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">Page0725-2</a>]<BR> usage or custom. —2 propriety, decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाश्रमः|जनाश्रम
जनः + -आश्रमः an asylum for people, an inn, caravansary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाश्रयः|जनाश्रय
जनः + -आश्रयः a pavilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेन्द्रः|जनेन्द्र|जनेंद्र
जनः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः, -ईश्वरः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेशः|जनेश
जनः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः, -ईश्वरः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेश्वरः|जनेश्वर
जनः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः, -ईश्वरः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेष्ट|जनेष्टः
जनः + -इष्ट <i>a.</i> desired or liked by the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेष्टः|जनेष्ट
जनः + -इष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@}) a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेष्टा
जनः + -इष्ट + .({@-ष्टा@}) turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनोदाहरणम्
जनः + -उदाहरणम् glory, fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनौघः|जनौघ
जनः + -ओघः a concourse of people, crowd, mob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकारिन्
जनः + -कारिन् <i>m.</i> lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनचक्षुस्
जनः + -चक्षुस् <i>n.</i> ‘the peopleʼs eye’, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनजन्मादिः|जनजन्मादि
जनः + -जन्मादिः the the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनजल्पः
जनः + -जल्पः A rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनत्रा
जनः + -त्रा an umbrella, a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनदेवः|जनदेव
जनः + -देवः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनपदः|जनपद
जनः + -पदः —1 a community, race, nation; Y. 1. 361 v. l.<BR>—2 a kingdom, an empire, an inhabited country; जनपदे न गदः पदमादधौ<BR> R. 9. 4; दाक्षिणात्ये जनपदे Pt. 1; Me. 48.<BR>—3 the country (opp. the town पुर, नगर); जनपदवधूलोचनैः<BR> पीयमानः Me. 16.<BR>—4 the people, subjects (opp. the sovereign); जनपदहितकर्ता त्यज्यते<BR> पार्थिवेन Pt. 1. 131.<BR>—5 mankind.<BR>—6 <i>a.</i> considering his subjects as authority; आपौरप्रकृतिजनपदो<BR> राजा Bhāg. 5. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनपदिन्
जनः + -पदिन् <i>m.</i> the ruler of a country or community.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रवादः|जनप्रवाद
जनः + -प्रवादः<BR>—1 rumour, report.<BR>—2 scandal, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रिय|जनप्रियः
जनः + -प्रिय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 philanthropic.<BR>—2 liked by the people, popular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रियः|जनप्रिय
जनः + -प्रिय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 coriander-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमरकः|जनमरक
जनः + -मरकः an epidemic disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमर्यादा
जनः + -मर्यादा established custom or usage, popular custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमारः|जनमार
जनः + -मारः an epidemic; Av. Pariś. 72. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयोपन
जनः + -योपन <i>a.</i> perplexing or vexing men; कमगञ्जनयोपनः<BR> Rv. 10. 86. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनरञ्जनम्
जनः + -रञ्जनम् gratifying the people, courting popular favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनरवः|जनरव
जनः + -रवः<BR>—1 rumour.<BR>—2 calumny, scandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनलोकः|जनलोक
जनः + -लोकः one (<i>i. e.</i> the fifth) of the seven divisions of the<BR> universe situated above Maharloka; यो ब्रह्मवादः पूर्वेषां जनलोकनिवासिनाम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 87. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनवादः|जनवाद
जनः + -वादः (also जनेवादः)<BR>—1 news, rumour.<BR>—2 a scandal; द्यूतं च जनवादं च Ms. 2. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनव्यवहारः|जनव्यवहार
जनः + -व्यवहारः popular usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनश्रुत
जनः + -श्रुत <i>a.</i> well-known among people, famous<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनश्रुतिः|जनश्रुति
जनः + -श्रुतिः <i>f.</i> a rumour, report; अभिचारं चकारास्येत्यविगाना<BR> जनश्रुतिः Rāj. T. 7. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनंसह
जनः + जनंसह <i>a.</i> subduing men; सत्रासाहो जनभक्षो<BR> जनंसहः Rv. 2. 21. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनसंबाध|जनसम्बाध
जनः + -संबाध <i>a.</i> densely crowded with people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्थानम्
जनः + -स्थानम् N. of a part of the Daṇḍakā forest; R. 12. 42, 13. 22;<BR> U. 1. 28, 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनंगमः|जनङ्गम|जनंगम
जनंगमः A Cāṇḍāla; … … जालिकाश्च जनंगमाः Śiva B. 31. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक <i>a.</i> (निका <i>f.</i>) [जन्-णिच् ण्वुल्] Generating,<BR> producing, causing; क्लेशजनक, दुःखजनक &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकः|जनक
जनक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A father, progenitor.<BR>—2 N. of a famous king of Videha or Mithilā, foster-father of Sītā.<BR> He was remarkable for his great knowledge, good works, and holiness. After<BR> the abandonment of Sītā by Rāma, he became an anchorite━indifferent<BR> to pleasure or pain━ and spent his time in philosophical discussions.<BR> The sage याज्ञवल्क्य was his priest and adviser.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जनकात्मजा, जनकतनया, जनकनन्दिनी, जनकसुता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकात्मजा
जनक + -आत्मजा, -तनया, -नन्दिनी, -सुता epithets of Sītā, daughter<BR> of king Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकतनया
जनक + -आत्मजा, -तनया, -नन्दिनी, -सुता epithets of Sītā, daughter<BR> of king Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकनन्दिनी|जनकनंदिनी
जनक + -आत्मजा, -तनया, -नन्दिनी, -सुता epithets of Sītā, daughter<BR> of king Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकसुता
जनक + -आत्मजा, -तनया, -नन्दिनी, -सुता epithets of Sītā, daughter<BR> of king Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनता
जनता [जनानां समूहः तल्]<BR>—1 Birth.<BR>—2 A number or assemblage of people, mankind, community; एकशतं ता<BR> जनता या भूमिर्व्यऽधूनुत Av. 5. 18. 12; आमन्त्रितो जनतायाश्च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">Page0726-1</a>]<BR> पालः Bhāg. 4. 17. 9; पश्यति स्म जनता दिनात्यये पार्वणौ शशिदिवाकराविव<BR> R. 11. 82, 15. 67; Pt. 1. 301; Śi. 5. 14, 12. 29, 16. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0725-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन <i>a.</i> [जन्-भावे ल्युट्] Producing, causing &c.; भुजगानां<BR> जननीं जजाप विद्याम् Śi. 20. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननः|जनन|जननं
जनन + .{@-नः@} The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननम्
जनन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Birth, being born; यावज्जननं तावन्मरणम् Moha M. 13.<BR>—2 Causing, production, creation; शोभाजननात् Ku. 1. 42.<BR>—3 Appearance, manifestation, rise.<BR>—4 Life, existence; यदैव पूर्वे जनने शरीरं सा दक्षरोषात्सुदती<BR> ससर्ज Ku. 1. 53; भावस्थिराणि जननान्तरसौहृदानि Ś. 5. 2.<BR>—5 Race, family, lineage.<BR>—6 Preparation for a religious ceremony (दीक्षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननिः|जननि
जननिः <i>f.</i> [जन्-अनि]<BR>—1 A mother.<BR>—2 Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननी
जननी [जन्-णिच् अनि ङीप्]<BR>—1 A mother.<BR>—2 Mercy, tenderness, compassion; जननी तु दयामात्रोः Med.; न<BR> संररञ्जे विषमं जनन्याम् Bu. C. 2. 34.<BR>—3 A bat.<BR>—4 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमेजयः|जनमेजय
जनमेजयः N. of a celebrated king of Hastināpura, son of Parīkṣit,<BR> the grandson of Arjuna. [His father died, being bitten by a serpent; and<BR> Janamejaya, determined to avenge the injury, resolved to exterminate the<BR> whole serpent-race. He accordingly instituted a serpent sacrifice, and<BR> burnt down all serpents except Takṣaka, who was saved only by the intercession<BR> of the sage Astika, at whose request the sacrifice was closed. It was<BR> to this king that Vaiśampāyana related the Mahābhārata, and the king<BR> is said to have listened to it to expiate the sin of killing a Brāhmaṇa.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयतिः|जनयति
जनयतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Production, generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयन्त|जनयंत
जनयन्त <i>a.</i> Generating, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Producing, begetting, creator. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A father; Pt. 1. 9.<BR>—2 Brahmadeva; प्रजावांस्तेन भवति यथा जनयिता तथा Mb. 13. 61. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयित्री
जनयित्री A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयिष्णुः|जनयिष्णु
जनयिष्णुः A progenitor, producer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनर्
जनर्, -ननस् <i>n.</i><BR> See जन 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननस्
जनर्, -ननस् <i>n.</i><BR> See जन 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिः|जनि
जनिः, जनिका, जनी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Birth, creation, production; अम्भोजन्मजनिस्तदन्तरगतः Bhāg. 10. 13. 15.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR>—3 A mother.<BR>—4 A wife; जन्युः पतिस्तन्वं १ मा विविश्याः Rv. 10. 10. 3.<BR>—5 A daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिका
जनिः, जनिका, जनी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Birth, creation, production; अम्भोजन्मजनिस्तदन्तरगतः Bhāg. 10. 13. 15.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR>—3 A mother.<BR>—4 A wife; जन्युः पतिस्तन्वं १ मा विविश्याः Rv. 10. 10. 3.<BR>—5 A daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनी
जनिः, जनिका, जनी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Birth, creation, production; अम्भोजन्मजनिस्तदन्तरगतः Bhāg. 10. 13. 15.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR>—3 A mother.<BR>—4 A wife; जन्युः पतिस्तन्वं १ मा विविश्याः Rv. 10. 10. 3.<BR>—5 A daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित|जनितं
जनित <i>a.</i> [जन्-णिच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Given birth to.<BR>—2 Produced, created.<BR>—3 Occasioned, occurred, happened &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितृ
जनितृ <i>m.</i> A father; यस्य हेतोर्जनितारं समेष्ये Mb. 3. 134. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्रम्
जनित्रम् Ved.<BR>—1 A birth-place, home.<BR>—2 Origin, source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्री
जनित्री A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्वः|जनित्व
जनित्वः A father^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्वा
जनित्वः + .{@-त्वा@} A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्वौ
जनित्वः + .{@-त्वौ@} (<i>dual</i>) Parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिमन्
जनिमन् <i>m.</i> or <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Birth, production.<BR>—2 Offspring, descendants.<BR>—3 A creature, being.<BR>—4 Gender, sex,<BR>—5 Genus, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनीयति
जनीयति Den. P. To long for a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनु|जनुः
जनु (-नू) <i>f.</i><BR> Birth, production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुस्
जनुस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Birth; धिग्वारिधीनां जनुः Bv. 1. 16.<BR>—2 Creation, production.<BR>—3 Life, existence; जनुः सर्वश्लाघ्यं जयति ललितोत्तंस भवतः Bv. 2. 55.<BR>—4 Nativity.<BR>—5 Birthplace.<BR>—6 A creature, being.<BR>—7 Genus, kind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जनुर्भवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुर्भवनम्
जनुस् + -भवनम्<BR>—1 lying in chamber.<BR>—2 (= सूतिकागृहम्); शाहेन्द्रविलास 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुषान्धः|जनुषान्ध
जनुषान्धः Blind from birth, born blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुः|जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः
जन्तुः [जन्-तुन्]<BR>—1 A creature, a living being, man; Ś. 5. 2; Ms. 3. 77.<BR>—2 The (individual) soul.<BR>—3 An animal of the lowest organization.<BR>—4 People, mankind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जन्तुकम्बुः, जन्तुघ्नः, जन्तुफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुकम्बुः|जन्तुकम्बु|जंतुकंबु
जन्तुः + -कम्बुः<BR>—1 a snailʼs shell.<BR>—2 a snail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुघ्नः|जन्तुघ्न|जन्तुघ्नं
जन्तुः + -घ्नः<BR>—1 the citron.<BR>—2 a snail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुफलः|जन्तुफल|जंतुफल
जन्तुः + -फलः the Udumbara tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुका|जंतुका
जन्तुका Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुमती
जन्तुमती The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मम्
जन्मम् Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन् <i>n.</i> [जन् भावे मनिन्]<BR>—1 Birth; तां जन्मने शैलवधूं प्रपेदे Ku. 1. 21.<BR>—2 Origin, rise, production, creation; आकरे पद्मरागाणां जन्म काचमणेः<BR> कुतः H. Pr. 44; Ku. 5. 60; (at the end of comp.) arising or born from;<BR> सरलस्कन्धसंघट्ठजन्मा दवाग्निः Me. 53.<BR>—3 Life, existence; पूर्वेष्वपि हि जन्मसु Ms. 9. 100, 5. 38; Bg. 4. 5.<BR>—4 Birthplace.<BR>—5 Nativity.<BR>—6 A father, giver of birth, progenitor; Ś. 7. 18.<BR>—7 Natal star.<BR>—8 (In astr.) N. of the first mansion or Nakṣatra.<BR>—9 A creature, being.<BR>—10 People.<BR>—11 The people of a household.<BR>—12 Kind, race.<BR>—13 Nature; property, quality.<BR>—14 Custom, manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्माधिपः|जन्माधिप
जन्मन् + .{@-अधिपः@}<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 the regent of a constellation under which a person is born (in astrology);<BR> होराजन्माधिपयोर्जन्मर्क्षे वाशुभो राज्ञः Bṛ. S. 34. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तरम्
जन्मन् + .{@-अन्तरम्@}<BR>—1 another life.<BR>—2 the preceding life, former birth; मनो हि जन्मान्तरसंगतिज्ञम् R. 7. 15.<BR>—3 regeneration.<BR>—4 the other world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तरीय|जन्मांतरीय
जन्मन् + .{@-अन्तरीय@} <i>a.</i> belonging to or done in another life; जन्मान्तरीयैः<BR> साम्राज्यं मया प्रापीति चिन्तयन् Rāj. T. 6. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्धः|जन्मान्ध|जन्मांध
जन्मन् + .{@-अन्धः@} <i>a.</i> born blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्माष्टमी
जन्मन् + .{@-अष्टमी@} the eighth day of the dark fortnight of Srāvaṇa, the<BR> birth-day of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मास्पदम्
जन्मन् + .{@-आस्पदम्@} birthplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मेशः|जन्मेश
जन्मन् + .{@-ईशः@} = 2 जन्माधिप;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकीलः|जन्मकील
जन्मन् + .{@-कीलः@} an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकुण्डली|जन्मकुंडली
जन्मन् + .{@-कुण्डली@} a diagram in a horoscope in which the positions of different<BR> planets at the time of oneʼs birth are marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकृत्
जन्मन् + .{@-कृत्@} <i>m.</i> a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मक्षेत्रम्
जन्मन् + .{@-क्षेत्रम्@} birth-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मतिथिः|जन्मतिथि
जन्मन् + .{@-तिथिः@} <i>m., f.</i>, {@-दिनम्, -दिवसः@}<BR> birth-day; सुखाय तज्जन्मदिनं बभूव Ku. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मदः|जन्मद
जन्मन् + .{@-दः@} a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मनक्षत्रम्
जन्मन् + .{@-नक्षत्रम्, -भम्@} the natal star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभम्
जन्मन् + .{@-नक्षत्रम्, -भम्@} the natal star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मनामन्
जन्मन् + .{@-नामन्@} <i>n.</i> the name<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">Page0727-1</a>]<BR> received on the 12th day after birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मपः|जन्मप
