जन्मपत्रम्
जन्मन् + .{@-पत्रम्, -पत्रिका@} a horoscope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मपत्रिका
जन्मन् + .{@-पत्रम्, -पत्रिका@} a horoscope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मपादपः|जन्मपादप
जन्मन् + .{@-पादपः@} a family-tree; उत्तराः कुरवोऽविक्षंस्तद्भयाज्जन्मपादपान्<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मप्रतिष्ठा
जन्मन् + .{@-प्रतिष्ठा@}<BR>—1 a birth-place.<BR>—2 a mother; Ś. 6 (between verses 9th and 10th).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभाज्
जन्मन् + .{@-भाज्, -भृत्@} <i>m.</i> a creature, living being; मोदन्तां जन्मभाजः<BR> सततम् Mk. 10. 60. ━<i>a.</i> one whose life is fruitful; अहो भोजपते<BR> यूयं जन्मभाजो नृणामिह Bhāg. 10. 82. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभृत्
जन्मन् + .{@-भाज्, -भृत्@} <i>m.</i> a creature, living being; मोदन्तां जन्मभाजः<BR> सततम् Mk. 10. 60. ━<i>a.</i> one whose life is fruitful; अहो भोजपते<BR> यूयं जन्मभाजो नृणामिह Bhāg. 10. 82. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभाषा
जन्मन् + .{@-भाषा@} a mother-tongue; यत्र स्त्रीणामपि किमपरं जन्मभाषावदेव<BR> प्रत्यावासं विलसति वचः संस्कृतं प्राकृतं च Vikr. 18. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभूमिः|जन्मभूमि
जन्मन् + .{@-भूमिः@} <i>f.</i> birth-place, native country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मयोगः|जन्मयोग
जन्मन् + .{@-योगः@} a horoscope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मरोगिन्
जन्मन् + .{@-रोगिन्@} <i>a.</i> sickly from birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मलग्नम्
जन्मन् + .{@-लग्नम्, -राशिः@} the sign of the zodiac under which a person is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मराशिः|जन्मराशि
जन्मन् + .{@-लग्नम्, -राशिः@} the sign of the zodiac under which a person is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवर्त्मन्
जन्मन् + .{@-वर्त्मन्@} <i>n.</i> the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवसुधा
जन्मन् + .{@-वसुधा@} native country; पश्यद्भिर्जन्मवसुधाम् Rāj. T. 4. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मशोधनम्
जन्मन् + .{@-शोधनम्@} discharging the obligations derived from birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मसाफल्यम्
जन्मन् + .{@-साफल्यम्@} attainment of the ends of existence; एतद्धि जन्मसाफल्यं<BR> ब्राह्मणस्य विशेषतः Ms. 12. 93; Pt. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मस्थानम्
जन्मन् + .{@-स्थानम्@}<BR>—1 birth-place, native country, home.<BR>—2 the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्महेतुः
जन्मन् + .{@-हेतुः@} cause of birth, author of oneʼs being; पितरस्तासां केवलं<BR> जन्महेतवः R. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन् <i>m.</i> A creature, a living being; Pt. 1. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य <i>a.</i> [जन् कर्तरि यत्]<BR>—1 To be born or produced.<BR>—2 Born, produced.<BR>—3 (At the end of comp.) Born from, occasioned by.<BR>—4 Belonging to a race or family<BR>—5 Vulgar, common.<BR>—6 National.<BR>—7 Relating to, or fit for men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यः|जन्य|जन्यं
जन्य + .{@-न्यः@}<BR>—1 A father.<BR>—2 A friend, attendant or relative of a bridegroom; Māl. 6. 2.<BR>—3 A common man.<BR>—4 A report, rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्या
जन्य + .{@-न्या@}<BR>—1 Motherʼs friend,<BR>—2 The relation of a bride, a brideʼs maid; याहीति जन्यामवदत् कुमारी R. 6. 30.<BR>—3 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>—4 Affection.<BR>—5 a market.<BR>—6 The world; जन्या तु मातृसख्यां च मदे हट्टे जनेऽपि च । लोके जन्तौ … Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यम्
जन्य + .{@-न्यम्@}<BR>—1 Birth, production, creation.<BR>—2 That which is born or created, a created thing, an effect (opp. जनक)<BR> जन्यानां जनकः कालः Bhāṣā P. 45; जनकस्य स्वभावो हि जन्ये<BR> तिष्ठति निश्चितम् Śabdak.<BR>—3 The body; तुष्टाव जन्यं विसृजञ्जनार्दनम् Bhāg. 1. 9. 31.<BR>—4 A portent occurring at birth.<BR>—5 A market, a fair.<BR>—6 War, battle; तत्र जन्यं रघोर्घोरं पर्वतीयैर्गणरभूत् R. 4. 77;<BR> चारुणा रमते जन्ये कोऽभीतो रसिताशिनि Ki. 15. 23.<BR>—7 Censure, abuse.<BR>—8 A community, nation.<BR>—9 People.<BR>—10 Report, rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्युः|जन्यु
जन्युः [जन्-युच् बा˚ न अनादेशः]<BR>—1 Birth.<BR>—2 A creature, living being.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR>—4 The creator or Brahmā; जन्युः पतिस्तन्वं ꣲ मा विविश्याः Rv. 10. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्
जप् €1 P. (जपति, जपित or जप्त)<BR>—1 To utter in a low voice, repeat internally, mutter; जपन्नपि तवैवालापमन्त्रावलिम्<BR> Gīt. 5; हरिरिति हरिरिति जपति सकामम् 4; N. 11. 26.<BR>—2 To mutter prayers or spells; Ms. 11. 194, 251, 260.<BR>—3 To pray to one or invoke in a low voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप <i>a.</i> [जप्-कर्तरि अच्] Muttering, whispering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपः|जप
जप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Muttering prayers, repeating prayers &c. in an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">Page0727-2</a>]<BR> under-tone.<BR>—2 Repeating passages of the Veda or names of deities &c.; Ms. 3. 74; Y. 1. 22.<BR>—3 A muttered prayer.<BR>—4 Counting silently the beads of a rosary &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जपपरायण, जपमाला, जपयज्ञः, जपहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपपरायण|जपपरायणः
जप + -परायण <i>a.</i> engaged in muttering prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपमाला
जप + -माला a rosary of beads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपयज्ञः|जपयज्ञ
जप + -यज्ञः, -होमः muttering prayers as a sacrifice; विधियज्ञाज्जपयज्ञो<BR> विशिष्टो दशभिर्गुणैः Ms. 2. 85; Y. 1. 101; Ms. 10. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपहोमः|जपहोम
जप + -यज्ञः, -होमः muttering prayers as a sacrifice; विधियज्ञाज्जपयज्ञो<BR> विशिष्टो दशभिर्गुणैः Ms. 2. 85; Y. 1. 101; Ms. 10. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपत्
जपत् <i>m.</i> An ascetic; प्रणतो विनयाद्वीरो वसिष्ठं जपतां वरम्<BR> Rām. 1. 52. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपनम्
जपनम् [जप्-भावे ल्युट्] The muttering of prayers; संन्यास<BR> एव वेदान्ते वर्तते जपनं प्रति । वेदवादाश्च निर्वृत्ताः शान्ता ब्रह्मण्यवस्थिताः<BR> Mb. 12. 196. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपा
जपा [जप्-अच् टाप्] The China rose (the plant or its flower); सान्ध्यं<BR> तेजः प्रतिनवजपापुष्परक्तं दधानः Me. 36; निजदृशा सनिपीय<BR> जपावलिम् Rām. Ch. 4. 73; जपापुष्पमिव रक्तलोचनः Pratijñā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्य|जप्यः
जप्य <i>a.</i> [जप् कर्मणि यत्] To be repeated in a low voice,<BR> muttered, or whispered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्यः|जप्य
जप्य + .{@-प्यः, -प्यम्@} A muttered prayer; कृतजप्यमङ्गलाः Mb. 12. 58. 30;<BR> जप्यश्च परमो गुह्यः श्रूयतां मे नृपात्मज Bhāg. 4. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्यम्
जप्य + .{@-प्यः, -प्यम्@} A muttered prayer; कृतजप्यमङ्गलाः Mb. 12. 58. 30;<BR> जप्यश्च परमो गुह्यः श्रूयतां मे नृपात्मज Bhāg. 4. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ्, जम्भ् I. €1 P. (जभति, जम्भति) To copulate; cf.<BR> यभ् ━II. €1 Ā. (जभते, जम्भते)<BR>—1 To yawn, gape.<BR>—2 To snap at; seize with the mouth. ━<i>Caus.</i> (जम्भयति) To<BR> crush, destroy, dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ्|जंभ्
जभ्, जम्भ् I. €1 P. (जभति, जम्भति) To copulate; cf.<BR> यभ् ━II. €1 Ā. (जभते, जम्भते)<BR>—1 To yawn, gape.<BR>—2 To snap at; seize with the mouth. ━<i>Caus.</i> (जम्भयति) To<BR> crush, destroy, dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्
जम् €1 P. (जमति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमनम्
जमनम् = जेमन q. v. eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्निः|जमदग्नि
जमदग्निः A Brāhmaṇa and descendant of Bhṛgu and father of Paraśurāma.<BR> [Jamadagni was the son of Ṛchika and Satyavatī. He was a pious sage,<BR> deeply engaged in study, and is said to have obtained entire possession<BR> of the Vedas. His wife was Reṇukā who bore him five sons. One day when<BR> she had gone out to bathe, she beheld a loving pair of Gandharvas (according<BR> to some Citraratha and his queen) sporting and playing in the water.<BR> The lovely sight made her feel envious of their pleasure, and she returned<BR> defiled by unworthy thoughts, ‘wetted but not purified by the stream’.<BR> Her husband, who was anger incarnate, seeing her shorn of the lustre of<BR> her sanctity, furiously scolded her, and ordered his sons, as they came<BR> in, to cut off her head. But the first four sons shrank from that cruel<BR> deed. It was only Paraśurāma, the youngest, that with characteristic<BR> obedience to his fatherʼs command, struck off her head with his axe. The<BR> deed pacified the fatherʼs anger, and he desired Paraśurāma to ask a<BR> boon. The kind-hearted son begged that his mother might be restored to<BR> life which the father readily granted.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्पती|जंपती
जम्पती <i>m.</i> (du.) [जाया च पतिश्च] Husband and wife; cf.<BR> दम्पती and जायापती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0727-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

