जयद्रथः|जयद्रथ
जयद्रथः A king of the Sindhu district and brother-in-law of Duryodhana,<BR> having married Duhśalā, daughter of Dhṛtarāṣṭra. [Once while out<BR> on hunting, he chanced to see Draupadī in the forest, and asked of her<BR> food for himself and his retinue. Draupadī, by virtue of her magical<BR> sthālī, was able to supply him with materials sufficient for their break-fast.<BR> Jayadratha was so much struck with this act, as well as her personal charms,<BR> that he asked her to elope with him. She, of course, indignantly refused,<BR> but he succeeded in carrying her off, as her husbands were out on hunting.<BR> When they returned they pursued and captured the ravisher and released<BR> Draupadī; and he himself was allowed to go after having been subjected<BR> to many humiliations. He took a leading part in compassing the death of<BR> Abhimanyu, and met his doom at the hands of Arjuna in the great war.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जया
जया <i>f.</i> The name of a magical lore (often mentioned with विजया)<BR> taught by Viśvāmitra to Rāma, विद्यामथैनं विजयां जयां च Bk. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर|जरः
