जरः|जर
जर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Wearing out, wasting.<BR>—2 Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ <i>a.</i> [जॄ बा˚ अठ]<BR>—1 Hard, solid.<BR>—2 old, aged; अयमतिजरठाः प्रकामगुर्वीः परिणतदिक्करिकास्तटीर्बिभर्ति<BR> Śi. 4. 29 (where जरठ means ‘hard’ also).<BR>—3 Decayed, decrepit, infirm.<BR>—4 Bent, bowed down, drooping.<BR>—5 Pale, yellowish-white.<BR>—6 Full-grown, ripe, matured; जरठकमल Śi. 11. 14.<BR>—7 Hard-hearted, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठः|जरठ
जरठ + .{@-ठः@}<BR>—1 N. of Paṇdu, father of the five Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—2 Old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण <i>a.</i> [जॄ-ल्यु]<BR>—1 Old, decayed, infirm.<BR>—2 Promoting digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणः|जरण|जरणं
जरण + .{@-णः, -णम्@} Cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणम्
जरण + .{@-णः, -णम्@} Cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणा
जरण + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 Old age.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणम्
जरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Old age.<BR>—2 One of the ten ways in which an eclipse is supposed to end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0728-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्ड|जरंड|जरण्डः
जरण्ड <i>a.</i> Decayed, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्या
जरण्या Ved. Old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्|जरन्त्
जरत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Old, aged, decayed.<BR>—2 Infirm, decrepit. ━<i>m.</i> An old man.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जरत्कारुः, जरद्गवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारुः|जरत्कारु
जरत् + -कारुः N. of a great sage who married a sister of the serpent<BR> Vāsuki. [One day as he was fallen asleep on the lap of his wife, the sun<BR> was about to set. His wife, perceiving that the time of offering his evening<BR> prayers was passing away, gently roused him. But he became angry with<BR> her for having disturbed his sleep, and left her never to return. He, however,<BR> told her, as he went, that she was pregnant and would give birth to a<BR> son who would be her support, and at the same time the saviour of the serpent-race.<BR> This son was Astika].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरद्गवः|जरद्गव
जरत् + -गवः an old ox; दारिद्र्यस्य परा मूर्तिर्यन्मानद्रविणाल्पता ।<BR> जरद्गवधनः शर्वस्तथापि परमेश्वरः ॥ Pt. 2. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरतिका
जरतिका, -जरती<BR> An old woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरती
जरतिका, -जरती<BR> An old woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरतः
जरतः<BR>—1 An old man.<BR>—2 A buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरसानः|जरसान
जरसानः Man; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
जरा [जॄ-अङ् गुणः] (The word जरस् is optionally substituted<BR> for जरा before vowel terminations after acc. dual.)<BR>—1 Old age; कैकेयीशङ्कयेवाह पलितच्छद्मना जरा R. 12. 2; तस्य<BR> धर्मरतेरासीद् वृद्धत्वं जरया (जरसा) विना 1. 23.<BR>—2 Decrepitude, infirmity, general debility consequent on old age.<BR>—3 Praise.<BR>—4 Digestion.<BR>—5 N. of a female demon; see जरासन्ध below.<BR>—6 Invoking, greeting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जरावस्था, जरातुर, जराजीर्ण, जरापुष्ट, जरासन्धः, जरासुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरावस्था
जरा + -अवस्था decrepitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरातुर|जरातुरः
जरा + -आतुर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 infirm.<BR>—2 old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जराजीर्ण
जरा + -जीर्ण <i>a.</i> old through age, debilitated, infirm; Bh. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापुष्ट|जरापुष्टः
जरा + -पुष्ट = जरासन्ध. {@-भीरुः@} the god of love, Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासन्धः|जरासन्ध|जरासंध
जरा + -सन्धः N. of a celebrated king and warrior, son of Bṛhadratha.<BR> [According to a legend, he was born divided in two halves which were put<BR> together by a Rākṣasī called Jarā, whence the boy was called Jarāsandha.<BR> He became king of Magadha and Chedi after his fatherʼs death. When he<BR> heard that Kṛṣṇa had slain his son-in-law Kaṃsa, he gathered a large<BR> army and besieged Mathurā eighteen times, but was as often repulsed.<BR> When Yudhiṣṭhira performed the great Rājasūya sacrifice, Kṛṣṇa,<BR> Arjuna and Bhīma went to the capital of Jarāsandha disguised as Brāhmaṇas,<BR> chiefly with the object of slaying their enemy and liberating the kings<BR> imprisoned by him. He, however, refused to release the kings, whereupon<BR> Bhīma challenged him to a single combat. The challenge was accepted;<BR> a hard fight ensued, but Jarāsandha was at last overpowered and slain by Bhīma.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासुतः
जरा + -सुतः Jarāsandha; जरासुतस्तावभिसृत्य माधवौ Bhāg. 10. 50. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायणिः|जरायणि
जरायणिः N. of Jarāsandha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायु|जरायुः
जरायु <i>n.</i> [जरामेति इ-ञुण्]<BR>—1 The slough or cast-off skin of a serpent.<BR>—2 The outer skin of the embryo.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">Page0729-2</a>]<BR>—3 After-birth.<BR>—4 Secundines.<BR>—5 The uterus, womb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जरायुज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायुज|जरायुजः
जरायु + -ज <i>a.</i> born from the womb, viviparous; Ms. 1. 43 and Malli. on Ku. 3. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरित
जरित <i>a.</i> [जरा-इतच्]<BR>—1 Old, aged.<BR>—2 Decayed, infirm; पाण्डुरस्यातपत्रस्य च्छायायां जरितं मया Rām. 2. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिन्
जरिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जरा अस्त्यस्य इनि] Old, aged. ━<i>m.</i> An old man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिमन्
जरिमन् <i>m.</i> Ved. Decrepitude, old age; नभो न रूपं जरिमा<BR> मिनाति Rv. 1. 71. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथ|जरूथं|जरूथः
जरूथ <i>a.</i> [जॄ-ऊथन्] Speaking harshly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथः|जरूथ|जरूथं
जरूथ + .{@-थः@} N. of a demon conquered by Agni; येभिस्तपोभिरदहो जरूथम् Rv. 7. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथम्
जरूथ + .{@-थम्@} Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च्
जर्च् (-र्छ्, -र्ज्) €1. €6. P.<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To blame, reprove, censure.<BR>—3 To threaten or menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्छ्
जर्च् (-र्छ्, -र्ज्) €1. €6. P.<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To blame, reprove, censure.<BR>—3 To threaten or menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज्
जर्च् (-र्छ्, -र्ज्) €1. €6. P.<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To blame, reprove, censure.<BR>—3 To threaten or menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर <i>a.</i> [जर्ज्-बा˚ अर]<BR>—1 Old, infirm, decayed.<BR>—2 Worn out, torn, shattered, broken to pieces, divided in parts, split<BR> up into thin particles; जराजर्जरितविषाणकोटयो मृगाः K. 21; गात्रं<BR> जराजर्जरितं विहाय Mv. 7. 18; विसर्पन् धाराभिर्लुठति धरणीं जर्जरकणः<BR> U. 1. 29; Śi. 4. 23; Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—3 Wounded, hurt.<BR>—4 Pained, tormented; Māl. 9. 53. —5 Dull, hollow (as the sound of a broken vessel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरम्
जर्जर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The banner of Indra.<BR>—2 Moss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरित
जर्जरित <i>a.</i> [जर्ज्-णिच् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Old, decayed, infirm.<BR>—2 Worn out, torn to pieces, shattered, splintered &c.<BR>—3 Completely overpowered, disabled; स्मरशरजर्जरितापि सा प्रभाते Gīt. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीक|जर्ज्जरीकः
जर्जरीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Old, decayed.<BR>—2 Ragged, full of holes, perforated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीकृ
जर्जरीकृ €8 U. To wound, disable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्झ्
जर्झ् €9. €6. P. (जर्झति)<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To blame.<BR>—3 To threaten, menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ण|जर्णः
जर्ण <i>a.</i> [जॄ-नन्] Old, aged, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्णः|जर्ण
जर्ण + .{@-र्णः@}<BR>—1 The (waning) moon.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्तिलः|जर्तिल|जर्त्तिल|जर्त्तिलः
जर्तिलः Wild sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्तुः|जर्तु|जर्त्तु|जर्त्तुः
जर्तुः<BR>—1 The vulva.<BR>—2 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्स्
जर्त्स् €1 P. (जर्त्सति)<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To blame, censure, abuse,<BR>—3 To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्भरि
जर्भरि <i>a.</i> Supporting; सृण्येव जर्भरी तुर्फरीतू Rv. 10. 106. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्हिलः|जर्हिल
जर्हिलः = जर्तिल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्
जल् I. €1 P. (जलति)<BR>—1 To be rich or wealthy.<BR>—2 To cover, hide, screen.<BR>—3 To cover (as with a net), encircle, entangle.<BR>—4 To be sharp.<BR>—5 To be cold, stiff, dull, or dumb. ━II. €10 P. (जालयति) To cover, screen &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल <i>a.</i> [जल् अच् डस्य लो वा]<BR>—1 Dull, cold, frigid = जड q. v. —2 Stupid, idiotic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0729-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलम्
जल + .{@-लम्@} —1 Water; तातस्य कूपोऽ-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0730-1" target="_blank">Page0730-1</a>]<BR> -यमिति ब्रुवाणाः क्षारं जलं कापुरुषाः पिबन्ति । Pt. 1. 322.<BR>—2 A kind of fragrant medicinal plant or perfume (ह्रीवेर).<BR>—3 The embryo or uterus of a cow.<BR>—5 The constellation called पूर्वाषाढा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जलाञ्चलम्, जलाञ्जलिः, जलाटनः, जलाटनी, जलाणुकम्, जलाण्डकम्, जलाण्टकः, जलात्ययः, जलाधिदैवतः, जलाधिदैवतम्, जलाधिपः, जलाम्बिका, जलार्कः, जलार्णवः, जलार्थिन्, जलावतारः, जलाष्ठीला, जलासुका, जलाकरः, जलाकाङ्क्षः, जलकाङ्क्षः, जलकाङ्क्षिन्, जलाखुः, जलागमः, जलाढ्य, जलात्मिका, जलाधारः, जलायुका, जलार्द्र, जलालोका, जलावर्तः, जलाशय, जलाश्रयः, जलाह्वयम्, जलेन्द्रः, जलेन्धनः, जलेभः, जलेशः, जलेश्वरः, जलोच्छ्वासः, जलोदरम्, जलोद्भव, जलोरगा, जलौकस्, जलकण्टकः, जलकपिः, जलकपोतः, जलकर, जलकरङ्कः, जलकल्कः, जलकल्मषः, जलकाकः, जलकान्तः, जलकान्तारः, जलकिराटः, जलकुक्कुटः, जलकुन्तलः, जलकोशः, जलकूपी, जलकूर्मः, जलकृत्, जलकेलिः, जलकेशः, जलक्रिया, जलगुल्मः, जलचर, जलचत्वरम्, जलचारिन्, जलज, जलजन्तुः, जलजन्तुका, जलजन्मन्, जलजिह्वः, जलजीविन्, जलडिम्बः, जलतरङ्गः, जलताडनम्, जलतापिकः, जलतापिन्, जलतालः, जलत्रा, जलत्रासः, जलदः, जलागमः, जलदर्दुरः, जलदेवः, जलदेवता, जलद्रोणी, जलद्वारम्, जलधरः, जलधारा, जलधिः, जलनकुलः, जलनरः, जलनाडी, जलनाली, जलनिधिः, जलनिर्गमः, जलनीलिः, जलपक्षिन्, जलपटलम्, जलपतिः, जलपथः, जलपद्धतिः, जलपात्रम्, जलपारावतः, जलपित्तम्, जलपुष्पम्, जलपूरः, जलपृष्ठजा, जलप्रदानम्, जलप्रपातः, जलप्रलयः, जलप्रान्तः, जलप्रायम्, जलप्रियः, जलप्लवः, जलप्लावनम्, जलबन्धः, जलबन्धकः, जलबन्धुः, जलबालकः, जलवालकः, जलबालिका, जलबिडालः, जलबिम्बः, जलबिम्बम्, जलबिल्वः, जलभीतिः, जलभू, जलभूः, जलभूषणः, जलभृत्, जलमक्षिका, जलमण्डूकम्, जलमद्गुः, जलमसिः, जलमार्गः, जलमार्जारः, जलमुच्, जलमूर्तिः, जलमूर्तिका, जलमोदम्, जलयन्त्रम्, जलयात्रा, जलयानम्, जलरङ्कुः, जलरण्डः, जलरुण्डः, जलरसः, जलराशिः, जलरुह्, जलहम्, जलरूपः, जललता, जलवरण्टः, जलवाद्यम्, जलवायसः, जलवासः, जलवाहः, जलवाहकः, जलवाहनः, जलवाहनी, जलविषुवम्, जलवृश्चिकः, जलवैकृतम्, जलव्यधः, जलव्यालः, जलशयः, जलशयनः, जलशायिन्, जलशय्या, जलशर्करा, जलशुक्