जवा
जवा The China rose; see जपा. जवापुष्पश्रेणीरुचिरुचिरपादाम्बुजतलम्<BR> Haṃsadūtam; बहलरागजवाधरचारुणि Śi. 6. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष्
जष् €1 U. (जषति-ते) To injure, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्
जस् I. €4 P. (जस्यति)<BR>—1 To set free, release.<BR>—2 To be exhausted or tired.<BR>—3 To go. ━II. €1. €10 P. (जसति जासयति)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure, strike.<BR>—2 To disregard, slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुः|जसु
जसुः<BR>—1 A weapon (आयुध).<BR>—2 Weakness, exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुरि|जसुरिः
