जाङ्गलिः|जाङ्गलि|जांगलिः
जाङ्गलिः, जाङ्गलिकः A snake-charmer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गलिकः|जाङ्गलिक|जांगलिकः
जाङ्गलिः, जाङ्गलिकः A snake-charmer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलम्
जाङ्गुलम् Poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुली
जाङ्गुलम् + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 Knowledge of poisons, possession of charms or drugs as antidotes;<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जाङ्गुलविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलविद्
जाङ्गुलम् + -विद् <i>m.</i> —1 A snake-doctor; तस्मादस्य जाङ्गुलीविदो भिषजश्च<BR> आसन्नाः स्युः Kau. A. 1. 21.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलिः|जाङ्गुलि|जांगुलि|जांगुलिः
जाङ्गुलिः, जाङ्गुलिकः A snake-doctor, a dealer in antidotes<BR> (विषवैद्य); मां जाङ्गुलिकमालोक्य महतीं शान्तिमागताः Śiva B. 13. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलिकः|जाङ्गुलिक|जांगुलिक|जांगुलिकः
जाङ्गुलिः, जाङ्गुलिकः A snake-doctor, a dealer in antidotes<BR> (विषवैद्य); मां जाङ्गुलिकमालोक्य महतीं शान्तिमागताः Śiva B. 13. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घिक|जांघिक|जाङ्घिकः
जाङ्घिक <i>a.</i> [जङ्घाभ्यां जीवति वेतना˚ ठञ्] Running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घिकः|जाङ्घिक|जांघिक
जाङ्घिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A courier, an express; अथोच्चबले भग्ने विदद्रुः केऽपि जाङ्घिकाः<BR> Rāj. T. 7. 1335.<BR>—2 A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजिन्
जाजिन् <i>m.</i> A warrior, combatant; जजौजोजाजिजिज्जाजी Śi. 19. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटासुरिः|जाटासुरि
जाटासुरिः N. of the demon Alaṃbuṣa; जाटासुरिर्भैमसेनिं नानाशस्त्रैरवाकिरत्<BR> Mb. 7. 174. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठर|जाठरः
जाठर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जठरे भवः अण्] Belonging to or being in the<BR> stomach, stomachic, abdominal; धनक्षये वर्धति जाठराग्निः Pt. 2. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठरः|जाठर
जाठर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The digestive faculty, gastric fluid.<BR>—2 ‘Offspring of the womb’, a child; भविष्यतस्तवाभद्रावभद्रे जाठराधमौ<BR> Bhāg. 3. 14. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्यम्
जाड्यम् [जडस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Coldness, frigidity.<BR>—2 Apathy, sluggishness, inactivity.<BR>—3 Dulness of intellect, folly, stupidity; तज्जाड्यं वसुधाधिपस्य<BR> Bh. 2. 15; जाड्यं धियो हरति 2. 23; जाड्यं ह्रीमति गण्यते 54.<BR>—4 Tastelessness of the tongue.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जाड्यारिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्यारिः|जाड्यारि
जाड्यम् + -अरिः the citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात <i>p. p.</i> [जन् कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Brought into existence, engendered, produced.<BR>—2 Grown, arisen.<BR>—3 Caused, occasioned.<BR>—4 Felt, affected by, oft. in comp.; ˚दुःख &c.<BR>—5 Apparent, clear.<BR>—6 Become, present.<BR>—7 Happened.<BR>—8 Ready at hand, collected; see जन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातः|जात|जातं
जात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A son, male offspring (in dramas often used as a term of endearment;<BR> अयि जात कययितव्यं कथय U. 4 ‘dear boy’, ‘oh my darling &c.’).<BR>—2 A living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाता
जात + .{@-ता@} A daughter, mostly used in addressing; जाते ‘dear child’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातम्
जात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A creature, living being.<BR>—2 Production, origin; धन्यः कुन्तीमुतो राजा सुजातं चास्य धीमतः Mb. 7. 12. 12.<BR>—3 Kind, sort, class, species.<BR>—4 A collection of things forming a class; निःशेषविश्राणितकोशजातम्<BR> R. 5. 1 all that goes to form wealth, <i>i. e.</i> every kind of property;<BR> so कर्मजातम् the whole aggregate of actions; सुख˚ everything<BR> included under the name of सुख or pleasure; अपत्यजातम् ‘the brood of young ones’<BR>; Ś. 5. 22.<BR>—5 A child, a young one.<BR>—6 Individuality, specific condition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जातापत्या, जातामर्ष, जाताश्रु, जातेष्टिः, जातोक्षः, जातकर्मन्, जातकलाप, जातकाम, जातकौतूहल, जातदन्त, जातपक्ष, जातपाश, जातपुत्रा, जातप्रत्यय, जातप्रेत, जातमन्मथ, जातमात्र, जातरूप, जातविद्या, जातविभ्रम, जातवेदस्, जातवेदसी, जातवासगृहम्, जातवेश्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातापत्या
जात + -अपत्या a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातामर्ष
जात + -अमर्ष <i>a.</i> vexed, enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाताश्रु
जात + -अश्रु <i>a.</i> shedding tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातेष्टिः|जातेष्टि
जात + -इष्टिः <i>f.</i> a sacrifice performed at the birth of a child. ˚न्यायः<BR> A rule of interpretation according to which the fruit of an act shall<BR> accrue to some one else than the performer if it is so directly declared<BR> by श्रुति (even against the general rule <i>viz.</i> शास्त्रफलं प्रयोक्तरि).<BR> From this it follows that such an act must be performed so as not to cause<BR> destruction of one to whom the fruit is to accrue. This is discussed by<BR> जैमिनि and शबर in connection with the वैश्वानरेष्टि, whose<BR> fruit accrues to the son and which has to be performed only after the<BR> performance of the birth-rite to avoid the sonʼs starvation to death. Read<BR> MS. 4. 3. 38-39 and शबरʼs भाष्य thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातोक्षः|जातोक्ष
जात + -उक्षः a young bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकर्मन्|जातकर्म्मन्
जात + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> a ceremony performed at the birth of a child; Ms. 2. 27, 29;<BR> R. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकलाप
जात + -कलाप <i>a.</i> having a tail (as a peacock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकाम
जात + -काम <i>a.</i> enamoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकौतूहल
जात + -कौतूहल <i>a.</i> being eagerly desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातदन्त
जात + -दन्त <i>a.</i> having teeth growing; जातदन्तस्य वा कुर्युर्नाम्नि<BR> वापि कृते सति Ms. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातपक्ष
जात + -पक्ष <i>a.</i> having wings; अजातपक्ष unfledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातपाश
जात + -पाश<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">Page0733-2</a>]<BR> <i>a.</i> fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातपुत्रा
जात + -पुत्रा a woman who has borne a son or sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातप्रत्यय
जात + -प्रत्यय <i>a.</i> inspired with confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातप्रेत
जात + -प्रेत <i>a.</i> born and dead, Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमन्मथ
जात + -मन्मथ <i>a.</i> fallen in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमात्र
जात + -मात्र <i>a.</i> just born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूप|जातरूपं
जात + -रूप <i>a.</i> beautiful, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूपम्
जात + -रूप + .({@-पम्@})<BR>—1 gold; पुनश्च याचमानाय जातरूपमदात् प्रभुः Bhāg. 1. 17. 39;<BR> अप्याकरसमुत्पन्ना मणिजातिरसंस्कृता । जातरूपेण कल्याणि न हि संयोगमर्हति ॥<BR> M. 5. 18; N. 1. 129.<BR>—2 the form in which a person is born, <i>i. e.</i> nakedness.<BR>—3 the thorn apple. ˚धर <i>a.</i> naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातविद्या
जात + -विद्या Ved. knowledge of the origin and nature of all things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातविभ्रम
जात + -विभ्रम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 confounded.<BR>—2 precipitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदस्
जात + -वेदस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of fire (or of the sun); विप्रेभिरस्तोष्ट<BR> जातवेदाः Rv. 1. 77. 5; Ku. 2. 46; Śi. 2. 51; R. 12. 104, 15. 72; Ki. 13. 11;<BR> the word is variously explained; cf. Nir.:− जातवेदाः कस्मात्<BR> जातानि वेद, जातानि वै नं विदुः, जाते जाते विद्यते इति वा, जातवित्तो<BR> वा जातधनो, जातविद्यो वा जातप्रज्ञानो यत्तज्जातः पशूनविन्दतेति तज्जातवेदसो<BR> जातवेदस्त्वमिति ब्राह्मणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदसी
जात + -वेदसी an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवासगृहम्
जात + -वासगृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>m.</i> the lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेश्मन्
जात + -वासगृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>m.</i> the lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक <i>a.</i> [जात-स्वार्थे क] Born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकः|जातक|जातकं
जातक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A new-born infant.<BR>—2 A mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकम्
जातक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A ceremony performed after the birth of a child (जातकर्मन्); जातकाद्याः<BR> क्रियाश्चास्या विधिपूर्वं यथाक्रमम् Mb. 1. 8. 12; जातकं कारयामास<BR> वर्तयित्वा च मङ्गलम् Bhāg. 1. 12. 13.<BR>—2 Astrological calculation of a nativity.<BR>—3 An aggregate of similar things.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जातकवक्रम्, जातकध्वनिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकवक्रम्
जातक + -वक्रम् A circle foreboding good or evil in a manʼs life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकध्वनिः|जातकध्वनि
जातक + -ध्वनिः a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिः|जाति
जातिः <i>f.</i> [जन्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Birth, production, सङ्कुलं जलजातिभिः Rām. 3. 11. 6; Pt. 1. 38;<BR> Ms. 2. 148; also ‘the time of birth’; cf. जातौ बाल्ये च कौमारे यौवने<BR> चापि मानवाः Mb. 12. 158. 11.<BR>—2 The form of existence fixed by birth.<BR>—3 Race, family, lineage, rank.<BR>—4 A caste, tribe or class (of men); अरे मूढ जात्या चेदवध्योऽहम् एषा<BR> सा जातिः परित्यक्ता Ve. 3; (the primary castes of the Hindus are only<BR> four:− ब्राह्मण, क्षत्रिय, वैश्य and शूद्र).<BR>—5 A class, genus, kind, species; पशुजातिः, पुष्पजातिः &c.<BR>—6 The properties which are peculiar to a class and distinguish it from<BR> all others, the essential characteristics of a species; as गोत्व, अश्वत्व<BR> of cows, horses &c.; see गुण, क्रिया and द्रव्य; जातिक्रियागुणैः<BR> Śi. 2. 47; and cf. K. P. 2.<BR>—7 A fire-place.<BR>—8 Nutmeg.<BR>—9 The Jasmine plant or its flower; नागपुन्नागजातिभिः Bhāg. 8. 2. 18;<BR> पुष्पाणां प्रकरः स्मितेन रचितो नो कुन्दजात्यादिभिः Amaru. 40<BR> (written also as जाती in the last two senses).<BR>—10 (In Nyāya) Futile answer.<BR>—11 (In music) The seven primary notes of the Indian gamut; जातिभिः<BR> सप्तभिर्युक्तं तन्त्रीलयसमन्वितम् Rām. 1. 4. 8.<BR>—12 Reduction of fractions to a common denominator.<BR>—13 False generalization.<BR>—14 A figure of speech (in rhetoric) which consists in so arranging words<BR> that they may read the same in Sanskṛt as well as in Prākṛta (संस्कृतप्राकृतयोः<BR> समा जातिः); cf. Vb. 1. 30.<BR>—15 A class of metres; see App.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जात्यन्ध, जातिकोशः, जातिकोषः, जातिकोषम्, जातिकोशी, जातिकोषी, जातिक्षयः, जातिगृद्धिः, जातिजानपद, जातिधर्मः, जातिध्वंसः, जातिपत्री, जातिफलम्, जातिब्राह्मणः, जातिभ्रंशः, जातिभ्रष्ट, जातिमहः, जातिमात्रम्, जातिलक्षणम्, जातिवाचक, जातिवैरम्, जातिवैरिन्, जातिवैलक्षण्यम्, जातिशब्दः, जातिसंकरः, जातिसंपन्न, जातिसारम्, जातिस्मर, जातिस्वभावः, जातिहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्यन्ध|जात्यंध|जात्यन्धः
जातिः + -अन्ध <i>a.</i> born blind; Bh. 1. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोशः|जातिकोश|जातिकोशं
जातिः + -कोशः, -कोषः, -कोषम् nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोषः|जातिकोष|जातिकोषं
जातिः + -कोशः, -कोषः, -कोषम् nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोषम्
जातिः + -कोशः, -कोषः, -कोषम् nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोशी
जातिः + -कोशी, -कोषी the outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोषी
जातिः + -कोशी, -कोषी the outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिक्षयः
जातिः + -क्षयः (= जन्मोच्छेदः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">Page0734-1</a>]<BR> the end of birth, spiritual release. जातिक्षयस्यासुलभस्य बोद्धा Bu. C. 1. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिगृद्धिः
जातिः + -गृद्धिः <i>f.</i> to take birth; जातिगृद्धयाभिपन्नाः Mb. 5. 60. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिजानपद
जातिः + -जानपद <i>a.</i> belonging to the castes and to the country; जातिजानपदान्<BR> धर्मान् Ms. 8. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिधर्मः|जातिधर्म|जातिधर्म्म
जातिः + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the duties of a caste.<BR>—2 a generic property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिध्वंसः|जातिध्वंस
जातिः + -ध्वंसः loss of caste or its privileges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिपत्री
जातिः + -पत्री the outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिफलम्
जातिः + -फलम् (sometimes जातीफलम् also) a nutmeg; जातीफलं मातुलानीमहिफेनं<BR> च पत्रकम् Śiva B. 30. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिब्राह्मणः|जातिब्राह्मण
जातिः + -ब्राह्मणः a Brāhmaṇa only by birth, but not by knowledge or<BR> religious austerities, an ignorant Brāhmaṇa; (तपः श्रुतं च योनिश्च<BR> त्रयं ब्राह्मण्यकारणम् । तपःश्रुताभ्यां यो हीनो जातिब्राह्मण एव सः ॥<BR> −शब्दार्थचिन्तामणि)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंशः|जातिभ्रंश
जातिः + -भ्रंशः loss of caste; Ms. 11. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रष्ट
जातिः + -भ्रष्ट <i>a.</i> outcaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमहः|जातिमह
जातिः + -महः birth-day festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमात्रम्
जातिः + -मात्रम्<BR>—1 ‘mere birth’, position in life obtained by mere birth.<BR>—2 caste only (but not the performance of duties pertaining to it); Ms. 8. 20, 12. 114.<BR>—3 species, genus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिलक्षणम्
जातिः + -लक्षणम् generic distinction, a characteristic of a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवाचक
जातिः + -वाचक <i>a.</i> expressing a genus, generic (as a word); गौरश्वः<BR> पुरुषो हस्ती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैरम्
जातिः + -वैरम् instinctive or natural hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैरिन्
जातिः + -वैरिन् <i>m.</i> a born enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैलक्षण्यम्
जातिः + -वैलक्षण्यम् inconsistency, incompatibility in kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिशब्दः|जातिशब्द
जातिः + -शब्दः a name conveying the idea of a genus, a generic word,<BR> common noun; गौः, अश्वः, पुरुषः, हस्ती &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिसंकरः|जातिसङ्कर
जातिः + -संकरः admixture of castes; mixed blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिसंपन्न
जातिः + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> belonging to a noble family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिसारम्
जातिः + -सारम् nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मर
जातिः + -स्मर <i>a.</i> remembering oneʼs condition in a former life; जातिस्मरो<BR> मुनिरस्मि जात्या K. 355.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्वभावः|जातिस्वभाव
जातिः + -स्वभावः generic character or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिहीन
जातिः + -हीन <i>a.</i> of low birth, outcaste; रूपद्रव्यविहीनांश्च जातिहीनांश्च<BR> नाक्षिपेत् Ms. 4. 141, 10. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमत्|जातिमन्त्
जातिमत् <i>a.</i> Nobly born, of high rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाती
जाती The jasmine plant (मालती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
जातीय, -क <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to a tribe, race, kind &c. <i>n.</i> a collection<BR> of utensils of a particular kind; तथा जातीयमादाय राजपुत्राभिषचेनम्<BR> Rām. 2. 15. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीक
जातीय, -क <i>a.</i><BR> Belonging to a tribe, race, kind &c. <i>n.</i> a collection<BR> of utensils of a particular kind; तथा जातीयमादाय राजपुत्राभिषचेनम्<BR> Rām. 2. 15. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य <i>a.</i> [जातौ भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Of the same family, related.<BR>—2 Noble, well-born, sprung from a noble family; जात्यस्तेनाभिजातेन<BR> शूरः शौर्यवता कुशः R. 17. 4; किं वा जात्याः स्वामिनो ह्रेपयन्ति Śi. 18. 23.<BR>—3 Lovely, beautiful, pleasing.<BR>—4 Best, excellent.<BR>—5 (Math.) Rectangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु <i>ind.</i> A particle meaning:−<BR>—1 At all, ever, at any time, possibly; नान्तरज्ञाः श्रियो जातुः प्रियैरासां<BR> न भूयते Ki. 11. 24; किं तेन जातु जातेन मातुर्यौवनहारिणा Pt. 1. 26;<BR> न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति Ms. 2. 94; Ku. 5. 55.<BR>—2 Perhaps, sometimes; गौरवाद्यदपि जातु मन्त्रिणां दर्शनं … ददौ R. 19. 7.<BR>—3 Once, once upon a time, sometime, at some day.<BR>—4 Used with the potential mood जातु has the sense of ‘not allowing or putting up with’<BR>; जातु तत्रभवान् वृषलं याजयेन्नावकल्पयामि<BR> (न मर्षयामि) Sk.<BR>—5 Used with a present indicative it denotes censure (गर्हा); जातु<BR> तत्रभवान् वृषलं याजयति <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुधानः|जातुधान
जातुधानः A demon, imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जतुनो विकारः अण्-षुक् च P. IV. 3. 138.]<BR>—1 Made of, or covered with, lac; यदाश्रौषं जातुषाद्वेश्मनस्तान् Mb. 1. 1. 153.<BR>—2 Sticky, adhesive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूः
जातूः <i>m.</i> A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूकर्णः|जातूकर्ण
जातूकर्णः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूभर्मन्
जातूभर्मन् Ved. <i>a.</i> Ever-nourishing or protecting; स जातूभर्मा<BR> श्रद्दधान ओजः Rv. 1. 103. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूष्ठिर
जातूष्ठिर Ved. <i>a.</i> ever solid, never yielding; जातष्ठिरस्य<BR> प्र वयः सहस्वतः Rv. 2. 13. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानम्
जानम् Ved. Birth, production, origin; स्थिरं हि जानमेषां वयो<BR> मातुर्निरेतवे Rv. 1. 37. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकी
जानकी [जनकस्यापत्यं स्त्री, अण्] N. of Sītā, wife of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानंतपिः|जानन्तपि|जानंतपि
जानंतपिः Patronymic of Atyarati; Ait. Br. 8. 23. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदः|जानपद
जानपदः [जानेन उत्पत्त्या पच्चते पद् अप्; जनपदे भवः, अण् वा]<BR>—1 An inhabitant of the country, a rustic, boor, peasant (opp. पौर);<BR> ततः कतिपयाहःसु वृद्धो जानपदो युवा Rām. 7. 73. 2.<BR>—2 A country.<BR>—3 A tax &c. from peasants.<BR>—4 subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदा
जानपदः + .{@-दा@} A popular expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदी
जानपदः + .{@-दी@} Profession, business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदिक
जानपदिक <i>a.</i> Relating to a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानराज्यम्
जानराज्यम् Sovereignty; इमं देवा असपत्नं … … महते जानराज्यायेन्द्रस्येन्द्रियाय Vāj. 9. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानश्रुतिः|जानश्रुति
जानश्रुतिः N. of a king; जानश्रुतिर्ह पौत्रायणो बहुदायी, बहुपाक्य<BR> आस Ch. Up. 4. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानान
जानान <i>a.</i> Knowing, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानि
जानि A substitute for जाया at the end of Bah. comp. अनन्यजानेः<BR> सैवासीद्यस्माज्जाया हिरण्मयी R. 15. 61; हृतजानिररातिभिः सलज्जः Mv. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु <i>n.</i> [जन्-ञुण्] The knee; जानुभ्यामवनिं गत्वा kneeling<BR> (or falling on oneʼs knees) on the ground.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जानुदघ्न, जानुप्रकृतिकम्, जानुफलकम्, जानुमण्डलम्, जानुविजानु, जानुसन्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुदघ्न
जानु + -दघ्न <i>a.</i> reaching to, as high as the knees, knee-deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुप्रकृतिकम्
जानु + -प्रकृतिकम् A variety of wrestling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुफलकम्
जानु + -फलकम्, -मण्डलम् the knee-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुमण्डलम्
जानु + -फलकम्, -मण्डलम् the knee-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुविजानु
जानु + -विजानु <i>n.</i> a peculiar position in fighting (contracting and<BR> extending the knees).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुसन्धिः|जानुसन्धि|जानुसंधि
जानु + -सन्धिः the knee-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापः|जाप
जापः [जप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Muttering prayers, whispering, murmuring.<BR>—2 A muttered prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Muttering prayers.<BR>—2 belonging to the muttering of prayers; अथवा सर्वमेवेह मामकं<BR> जापकं फलम् Mb. 12. 199. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापकः|जापक
जापक + .{@-कः@} A mutterer of prayers; जापकानां फलावाप्तिं श्रोतुमिच्छामि<BR> भारत । किं फलं जपतामुक्तं क्व वा तिष्ठन्ति जापकाः Mb. 12. 196. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापकम्
जापक + .{@-कम्@} A kind of fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्य
जाप्य <i>a.</i> To be muttered; जजाप परमं जाप्यं प्राग्जन्ममनुशिक्षितम्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्यम्
जाप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} A prayer to be muttered in a low voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापनम्
जापनम्<BR>—1 Declining, rejection.<BR>—2 Dismissing, sending away.<BR>—3 Completing, finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालः|जाबाल
जाबालः A goat-herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालिः|जाबालि
जाबालिः<BR>—1 N. of the author of a law-book.<BR>—2 N. of an infidel Brāhmaṇa, a priest of king Daśaratha who tried<BR> to dissuade Rāma from his resolution of going to the forest and to induce<BR> him to accept the throne offered by Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्यः|जामदग्न्य
जामदग्न्यः N. of Paraśurāma q. v.; जामदग्न्यमपहाय गीयते<BR> तापसेषु चरितार्थमायुधम् Ki. 13. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामलः|जामल
जामलः A variety in Āgamic Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामा
जामा [जम्-अदने वा. अण् स्त्रीत्वम्]<BR>—1 A daughter; अन्यत्र जामया सार्धं प्रजानां पुत्र ईहते Mb. 13. 45. 14.<BR>—2 A daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ <i>m.</i> [जायां माति मिनोति मिमीते वा नि˚; cf. Uṇ. 2. 94]<BR>—1 A son-in-law; जामातृयज्ञेन वयं निरुद्धाः U. 1. 11; जामाता दशमो<BR> ग्रहः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 A lord, master.<BR>—3 The sunflower.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जामातृबन्धकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृबन्धकम्
जामातृ + -बन्धकम् Dowry; शुल्कं घट्टादिदेये स्यात् जामातुर्बन्धकेऽपि च । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृकः|जामातृक
जामातृकः A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि <i>a.</i> [जम्-इन् नि˚ वृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Customary, usual.<BR>—2 Peculiar, or belonging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामिः|जामि
जामि + .{@-मिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A sister; तद् गदतु मे जामि देवदत्तोऽन्निकामिमाम् Gaṇeśa P.<BR>—2 A daughter.<BR>—3 A daughter-in-law.<BR>—4 A near female relative (सन्निहितसपिण्डस्त्री Kull.); Ms. 3. 57-58.<BR>—5 A virtuous and respectable woman.<BR>—6 Ved. A finger.<BR>—7 Water. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 Blood-relationship, relation of sister and brother.<BR>—2 Relation (in general), descent.<BR>—3 Tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्रम्
जामित्रम् The seventh zodiacal sign from the natal sign (लग्न);<BR> तिथौ च जामित्रगुणान्वितायाम् Ku. 7. 1 (जामित्रं लग्नात् सप्तमं स्थानम्<BR> Malli.). <i>Note</i>:− Some derive the word from जाया, because in<BR> astrology, the {@जामित्र@} sign indicates the future good-luck of oneʼs<BR> wife (जायामित्रम् ?); but the word is obviously connected with the<BR> Greek <i>diametron</i>.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जामित्रवेधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्रवेधः|जामित्रवेध
जामित्रम् + -वेधः A variety of योग (Astronomical) when the moon is in the 7th house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेयः|जामेय
जामेयः [जाम्या भगिन्या अपत्यं ढञ्] A sisterʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवम्
जाम्बवम् [जम्ब्वाः फलम् अण् तस्य बा˚ न लुप् Tv.]<BR>—1 Gold.<BR>—2 The fruit of the Jambu tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जाम्बवौष्ठम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवौष्ठम्
जाम्बवम् + -ओष्ठम् a cauterizing needle or probe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवत्|जांबवत्|जाम्बवन्त्
जाम्बवत् <i>m.</i> N. of a king of bears who was of signal service to<BR> Rāma at the siege of Laṅkā. He was also noted for his medical skill.<BR> [This same Jāmbavat appears to have lived up to the time of Kṛṣṇa,<BR> or perhaps he was another being of that time; for there was a fight between<BR> Kṛṣṇa and Jāmbavat for the <i>Syamantaka</i> jewel which the latter<BR> had got from Prasena, brother of Satrājit. Kṛṣṇa vanquished Jāmbavat,<BR> who placed the jewel, along with his daughter Jāmbavatī, at his entire disposal.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बीरम्
जाम्बीरम् (-लम्)<BR> A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बीलम्
जाम्बीरम् (-लम्)<BR> A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बीलम्
जाम्बीरम् (-लम्) + .{@-लम्@} Ved. The knee-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बीलम्
जाम्बीलम् The knee-joint; बाहुभ्यां जाम्बीलेनारण्यमग्निम् Vāj. 25. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनदम्
जाम्बूनदम् [जम्बूनद्यां भवम् अण्]<BR>—1 Gold, R. 18. 44.<BR>—2 A golden ornament; कृतरुचश्च जाम्बूनदैः Śi. 4. 66.<BR>—3 The Dhattūra plant. ━<i>a.</i> golden; ततो जाम्बूनदीः पात्रीर्वज्राङ्का<BR> विमलाः शुभाः Mb. 12. 171. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जाम्बूनदपर्वतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनदपर्वतः|जाम्बूनदपर्वत
जाम्बूनदम् + -पर्वतः the Meru mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूलमालिका
जाम्बूलमालिका Procession of the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्भवाभः
जाम्भवाभः A gem having the colour of a Jambu fruit; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायकम्
जायकम् A kind of yellow fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायन्तेयः|जायन्तेय
जायन्तेयः The son of Jayantī; जायन्तेयान् मुनीन् प्रीतः सोपाध्यायो<BR> ह्यपूजयत् Bhāg. 11. 5. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया A wife. (The word is thus derived━ पतिर्भार्यां संप्रविश्य<BR> गर्भो भूत्वेह जायते । जायायास्तद्धिः जायात्वं यदस्यां जायते पुनः ॥<BR> Ms. 9. 8; see also Malli. on R. 2. 1.) As last member of Bah. comp. जाया<BR> is changed to जानि; सीताजानिः ‘one who has Sītā for his wife’; so<BR> युवजानिः, वामार्धजानिः<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जायानुजीविन्, जायाघ्नः, जायापती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायानुजीविन्
जाया + -अनुजीविन् <i>m.</i>, {@-आजीवः@}<BR>—1 an actor, a dancer.<BR>—2 the husband of a harlot.<BR>—3 a needy man, pauper.<BR>—4 a kind of crane (बक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाघ्नः|जायाघ्न
जाया + -घ्नः<BR>—1 a murderer of his wife.<BR>—2 a mole or mark on the body indicative of the death of oneʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायापती
जाया + -पती (dual) husband and wife. (The other forms of the comp. are<BR> दम्पती and जम्पती q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायिन्
जायिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जि-णिनि] Conquering, subduing. ━<i>m.</i> The burden<BR> of a song (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायु|जायुः
जायु <i>a.</i> Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायुः|जायु
जायु + .{@-युः@}<BR>—1 Medicine.<BR>—2 A physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारः|जार
जारः [जीर्यत्यनेन जॄ करणे घञ्; जरयतीति जारः Nir.]<BR>—1 A paramour, gallant, lover; रथकारः स्वकां भार्यां सजारां शिरसावहत् Pt. 4. 54.<BR>—2 A confidential friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारी
जारः + .{@-री@} N. of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जारजः, जारजन्मन्, जारजातः, जारभरा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारजः|जारज
जारः + -जः, -जन्मन्, -जातः a bastard; न जारजातस्य ललाटशृङ्गम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारजन्मन्
जारः + -जः, -जन्मन्, -जातः a bastard; न जारजातस्य ललाटशृङ्गम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारजातः|जारजात
जारः + -जः, -जन्मन्, -जातः a bastard; न जारजातस्य ललाटशृङ्गम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारभरा
जारः + -भरा an adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारणम्
जारणम्<BR>—1 Causing decay.<BR>—2 Oxydizing of metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारिणी
जारिणी An adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारूथ्य
जारूथ्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praiseworthy; निर्गलान् सजारूथ्यान् सर्वान् विविधदक्षिणान् Mb. 9. 49. 3.<BR>—2 In which three kinds of Dakṣiṇā are given; जारूथ्यान् त्रिगुणदक्षिणानित्यर्जुनमिश्रः<BR> Mb. 3. 291. 70 (com.)<BR>—3 Rich in meat or donations of meat; मांसादिदानप्रधानान् पुष्टानित्यर्थः <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालम्
जालम्<BR>—1 A net, snare.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A web, cob-web.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Any woven texture.<BR>—3 A coat of mail, a helmet made of wire.<BR>—4 An eye-hole, lattice, window; जालान्तरप्रेषितदृष्टिरन्या R. 7. 9;<BR> धूपैर्जालविनिःसृतैर्वलभयः संदिग्धपारावताः V. 3. 2; Ku. 7. 60.<BR>—5 A collection, an assemblage, number, mass; गभस्तिजालैः प्रदिशो दिशश्च<BR> Mb. 3. 164. 10; चिन्तासन्ततितन्तुजालनिबिडस्यूतेव Māl. 5. 10; Ku. 7. 89;<BR> Śi. 4. 56; Amaru. 58.<BR>—6 Magic.<BR>—7 Illusion, deception.<BR>—8 An unblown flower.<BR>—9 The membrane which unites the toes of many water-birds.<BR>—10 A disease of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">Page0736-1</a>]<BR> eyes.<BR>—11 Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालः|जाल|जालं
जालम् + .{@-लः@} The Kadamba tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जालाक्षः, जालकर्मन्, जालकारकः, जालगर्दभः, जालगोणिका, जालग्रथित, जालपाद्, जालपादः, जालप्राया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालाक्षः|जालाक्ष
जालम् + -अक्षः a loop-hole, window; हेमजालाक्षनिर्गच्छद्धूमेन Bhāg. 8. 15. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकर्मन्
जालम् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> the occupation of catching fish, fishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकारकः|जालकारक
जालम् + -कारकः<BR>—1 a net-maker.<BR>—2 a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगर्दभः|जालगर्दभ|जालगर्द्दभ|जालगर्द्दभः
जालम् + -गर्दभः a kind of pimple or boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगोणिका
जालम् + -गोणिका a kind of churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालग्रथित
जालम् + -ग्रथित <i>a.</i> connected by a web; Ś. 7. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपाद्
जालम् + -पाद्, -पादः a goose; जालपादभुजौ तौ तु पादयोश्चक्रलक्षणौ<BR> Mb. 12. 343. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपादः|जालपाद
जालम् + -पाद्, -पादः a goose; जालपादभुजौ तौ तु पादयोश्चक्रलक्षणौ<BR> Mb. 12. 343. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालप्राया
जालम् + -प्राया mail, armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकम्
जालकम् [जालमिव कायति कै-क]<BR>—1 A net.<BR>—2 A multitude, collection; बद्धं कर्णशिरीषरोधि वदने घर्माम्भसां<BR> जालकम् Ś. 1. 30; R. 9. 68.<BR>—3 A lattice, window; जालकमुखोपगतान् Śi. 9. 39; आननविलग्नजालकम् R. 9. 68.<BR>—4 A bud, an unblown flower; अभिनवैर्जालकैर्मालतीनाम् Me. 98; so यूथिकाजालकानि 26.<BR>—5 A kind of ornament (worn in the hair); तिलकजालकजालकमौक्तिकैः<BR> R. 9. 44 (आभरणविशेषः).<BR>—6 A nest.<BR>—7 Illusion, deception.<BR>—8 A plantain or the fruit.<BR>—9 Pride.<BR>—10 A kind of tree; माधवीजालकादिभिः Bhāg. 8. 2. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकः|जालक|जालकं
जालकम् + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A window, lattice.<BR>—2 A fowler.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जालकमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकमालिन्
जालकम् + -मालिन् <i>a.</i> veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिन्
जालकिन् <i>m.</i> A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी A ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालवत्|जालवन्त्
जालवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Furnished with a net, reticulated.<BR>—2 Covered with iron network.<BR>—3 Cunning, deceptive (मायाविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिकः|जालिक
जालिकः [जालेन चरति पर्पा˚ ष्ठन्]<BR>—1 A fisherman.<BR>—2 A fowler, bird-catcher.<BR>—3 A spider.<BR>—4 The governor or chief ruler of a province.<BR>—5 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—6 A conjurer, juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिका
जालिकः + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 A net.<BR>—2 A chain-armour.<BR>—3 A spider.<BR>—4 A leech.<BR>—5 A widow.<BR>—6 Iron.<BR>—7 Plantain.<BR>—8 A veil, woollen cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिनी
जालिनी<BR>—1 A room ornamented with pictures.<BR>—2 A kind of melon (कोषातकी).<BR>—3 Certain boils or pustules which appear in the disease called प्रमेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धरः|जालन्धर|जालंधर|जालंधरः
जालन्धरः N. of a country in the north-west of India, the territory<BR> between the rivers Beas and Sutlej.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालाषम्
जालाषम् Ved. A kind of drug with healing properties; जालाषेणाभिषिञ्चत<BR> जालाषणोप सिञ्चत Av. 6. 57. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालोरः|जालोर
जालोरः N. of an Agra-hāra in Kashmir; विहारमग्रहारं च जालोराख्यं<BR> च निर्ममे Rāj. T. 1. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म <i>a.</i> (-ल्मी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Cruel, severe, harsh.<BR>—2 Rash, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मः|जाल्म
जाल्म + .{@-ल्मः@} (-ल्मी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A rogue, rascal, villain, wretch, miscreant; आस्तां जाल्म उदरं स्रंसयित्वा<BR> Av. 4. 16. 7; अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन गतः स जाल्म इति V. 1.<BR>—2 A poor man, a low or degraded man.<BR>—3 One who reads or recites badly; cf. P. VI. 2. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मक
जाल्मक <i>a.</i> (-ल्मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Despised, low, mean, contemptible; मित्रब्रह्मगुरुद्रोही<BR> जाल्मकः सुविगर्हितः Bhāg. 7. 195. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावन्यम्
जावन्यम्<BR>—1 Speed, swiftness.<BR>—2 Haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाष्कमदः|जाष्कमद
जाष्कमदः A kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जास्पतिः|जास्पति
जास्पतिः Ved. A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहम्
जाहम् A termination added to nouns expressive of the parts of the<BR> body in the sense of ‘the root of’; कर्णजाहम् the root of the ear;<BR> so अक्षि˚, ओष्ठ˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहकः|जाहक
जाहकः<BR>—1 A pole-cat; जाहकाहिशशक्रोडगोधानाम् Bṛ. S. 86. 42.<BR>—2 A leech.<BR>—3 A bed, a cot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहुषः|जाहुष
जाहुषः N. of a man protected by the Aśvins; परिविष्टं जाहुषं<BR> विश्वतः सीम् Rv. 1. 116. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवी
जाह्नवी [जह्नोः अपत्यं स्त्री अण् ङीप्] An epithet of the river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि €1 P. (Ātm. when preceded, by परा and वि) (जयति,<BR> जिगाय, जिग्ये, अजैषीत्-अजेष्ट, जेतुम्, जित)<BR>—1 To conquer, defeat, overcome, vanquish, subjugate; जयति तुलामधिरूढो<BR> भास्वानपि जलदपटलानि Pt. 1. 330; Bk. 15. 76, 19. 2.<BR>—2 To surpass, excel; गर्जितानन्तरां वृष्टिं सौभाग्येन जिगाय सा Ku. 2. 53;<BR> R. 3. 34; Ghaṭ. 22; Śi. 1. 19.<BR>—3 To win (by conquest, in gambling or in a law-suit), acquire by conquest;<BR> प्रागजीयत घृणा ततो मही R. 11. 65; (where जि means ‘to conquer’<BR> also); Ms. 7. 96.<BR>—4 To curb, restrain, control, conquer (as passions).<BR>—5 To be victorious, be supreme or pre-eminent (generally used in benedictory<BR> stanzas or salutations); जयतु जयतु महाराजः (in dramas); स<BR> जयति परिणद्धः शक्तिभिः शक्तिनाथः Māl. 5. 1; जितमुडुपतिना नमः<BR> सुरेभ्यः Ratn. 1. 5; Bh. 2. 24; Gīt. 1. 1.<BR>—6 To convict.<BR>—7 To overcome or get the better of (as a disease &c.).<BR>—8 To expect from (with abl.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (जापयति) To cause<BR> to win or conquer. ━<i>Desid.</i> (जिगीषति) To wish to win, acquire<BR> or excel, to vie with, emulate, to seek for; चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां<BR> हि चेतः Ki. 10. 29. ━<i>With</i> {@अधि@} to conquer defeat, vanquish; Bk. 19. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयः|जय
जयः [जि भावे अच्]<BR>—1 Conquest, triumph, victory, success, winning (in battle, game or a<BR> law-suit); सप्त वित्तागमा धर्म्या दायो लाभः क्रयो जयः Mb. 10. 115.<BR>—2 Restraint, curbing, conquest as in इन्द्रियजय.<BR>—3 N. of the sun.<BR>—4 N. of Jayanta, son of Indra; जगृहे च धनुर्धाता मुसलं तु जयस्तया<BR> Mb. 1. 227. 34.<BR>—5 N. of Yudhiṣṭhira, the first Pāṇḍava prince.<BR>—6 N. of an attendant of Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 An epithet of Arjuna; संस्मरन् भ्रातरं जयम् Mb. 3. 158. 2.<BR>—8 N. of the Mahābhārata; देवीं सरस्वतीं चैव ततो जयमुदीरयेत्<BR> Mb. 1. 1. 1; Bhāg. 1. 2. 4;<BR>—9 The heroic sentiment; सहजेतरौ जयशमौ दधती Ki. 6. 22.<BR>—10 Words of victory; जयेन वर्धयित्वा च मारीचप्रमुखास्ततः Rām. 7. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जया
जयः + .{@-या@}<BR>—1 N. of Durgā.<BR>—2 N. of an attendant of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—3 A kind of banner.<BR>—4 The third, eighth or thirteenth lunar days of any of the two lunar fortnights.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जयाजयौ, जयावह, जयाशिस्, जयोदधुर, जयकुञ्जरः, जयकोलाहलः, जयगत,^1 जयघोषः, जयघोषणम्, जयघोषणा, जयढक्का, जयदम्, जयदत्तः, जयदेवः, जयपत्रम्, जयपालः, जयपुत्रकः, जयमङ्गलः, जययज्ञः, जयलक्ष्मीः, जयश्रीः, जयलेखम्, जयवाहिनी, जयशब्दः, जयशृङ्गम्, जयस्तम्भः, जयस्थलम्, जयस्वामिन्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयाजयौ
जयः + -अजयौ Victory and defeat; सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ Bg. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयावह
जयः + -आवह <i>a.</i> conferring victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयाशिस्
जयः + -आशिस् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a prayer for victory.<BR>—2 congratulations after victory; a cheer<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">Page0737-1</a>]<BR> of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयोदधुर
जयः + -उदधुर <i>a.</i> exulting in victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयकुञ्जरः|जयकुञ्जर
जयः + -कुञ्जरः a victorious elephant; आक्षिप्तो जयकुञ्जरेण Ratn. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयकोलाहलः|जयकोलाहल
जयः + -कोलाहलः<BR>—1 a shout of victory.<BR>—2 a kind of game with dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयगत
जयः + -गत^1 <i>a.</i> Conquering, victorious; उक्तविपरीतलक्षणसंपन्नो<BR> जयगतो विनिर्दिष्टः Bṛ. S. 17. 10.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयघोषः|जयघोष
जयः + -घोषः, -घोषणम्, -घोषणा a proclamation of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयघोषणम्
जयः + -घोषः, -घोषणम्, -घोषणा a proclamation of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयघोषणा
जयः + -घोषः, -घोषणम्, -घोषणा a proclamation of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयढक्का
जयः + -ढक्का a kind of drum beaten as a sign of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदम्
जयः + -दम् A height which is 1½ of the breadth; Māna. 35. 22-26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदत्तः|जयदत्त
जयः + -दत्तः N. of Jayanta, Indraʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदेवः|जयदेव
जयः + -देवः N. of the author of Gītagovinda; यावच्छृङ्गारसारस्वतमिह<BR> जयदेवस्य विष्वग्वचांसि Gīt. last stanza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपत्रम्
जयः + -पत्रम् a record of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपालः|जयपाल
जयः + -पालः<BR>—1 a king.<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—3 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपुत्रकः|जयपुत्रक
जयः + -पुत्रकः a kind of dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयमङ्गलः|जयमङ्गल|जयमंगल
जयः + -मङ्गलः<BR>—1 a royal elephant.<BR>—2 a remedy for fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयमङ्गलम्
जयः + -मङ्गलः + .({@-लम्@}) a cheer of victory; ततो ऽब्धिवीचिनिर्घोषैरुद्गीतजयमङ्गलः<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जययज्ञः|जययज्ञ
जयः + -यज्ञः the अश्वमेध sacrifice<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयलक्ष्मीः
जयः + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः the goddess of victory; जयलक्ष्म्या बबन्धास्थां<BR> श्वश्रूः Rāj. T. 5. 246; बभार यद्भुजस्तम्भो जयश्रीसालभञ्जिकाम्<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 2. 64; Ku. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयश्रीः
जयः + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः the goddess of victory; जयलक्ष्म्या बबन्धास्थां<BR> श्वश्रूः Rāj. T. 5. 246; बभार यद्भुजस्तम्भो जयश्रीसालभञ्जिकाम्<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 2. 64; Ku. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयलेखम्
जयः + -लेखम् record of victory; … … रतिजयलेखम् Gīt. 8. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवाहिनी
जयः + -वाहिनी an epithet of Śachī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशब्दः|जयशब्द
जयः + -शब्दः<BR>—1 a shout of victory.<BR>—2 the exclamation <i>‘jaya’</i> (hail! glory!) uttered by bards &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशृङ्गम्
जयः + -शृङ्गम् a horn blown to announce a victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयस्तम्भः|जयस्तम्भ|जयस्तंभ
जयः + -स्तम्भः a trophy, a column erected to commemorate a victory,<BR> a triumphal column; निचखान जयस्तम्भान् गङ्गास्रोतोऽन्तरेषु सः R. 4. 36;<BR> यस्याद्यापि जयस्तम्भाः सन्ति ते पूर्ववारिधौ Rāj. T. 3. 479.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयस्थलम्
जयः + -स्थलम् N. of a village, <i>ibid.</i> 5. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयस्वामिन्
जयः + -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयक
जयक <i>a.</i> Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्सेनः|जयत्सेन
जयत्सेनः A name assumed by Nakula while living at Virāṭa King.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयद्वलः
जयद्वलः A name assumed by Sahadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनम्
जयनम् [जि करणे ल्युट्] Conquering, subduing.<BR>—2 Armour for cavalry, elephants &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जयनयुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनयुज्
जयनम् + -युज्<BR>—1 caparisoned.<BR>—2 victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन् <i>a.</i> [जि शीलार्थे इनि]<BR>—1 Conquering, vanquishing; विरूपाक्षस्य जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे वामलोचनाः Vb. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Successful, winning a law-suit, Y. 2. 79.<BR>—3 Fascinating, captivating, subduing the heart; जगति जयिनस्ते ते<BR> भावा नवेन्दुकलादयः Māl. 1. 36. ━<i>m.</i> A victor, a conqueror; पौरस्त्यानेवमाक्रामंस्तांस्ताञ्जनपदाञ्जयी R. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य <i>a.</i> [जि-यत्] Conquerable, vulnerable, that can be conquered<BR> (opp. जेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा [जि-सन् भावे अ]<BR>—1 Desire of conquering, subduing or overcoming; यानं सस्मार कौबेरं<BR> वैवस्वत जिगीषया R. 15. 45.<BR>—2 Emulation, rivalry.<BR>—3 Eminence.<BR>—4 Exertion, profession, habit of life.<BR>—5 Eminence.<BR>—6 Military ardour, warlike spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirous of conquering.<BR>—2 Vying or contending with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित <i>p. p.</i> [जि-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Conquered, subdued, curbed, restrained, (as enemies, passions &c.).<BR>—2 Won, got, obtained (by conquest).<BR>—3 Surpassed, excelled. —4 Subject to, enslaved or influenced by; कामजित; स्त्रीजित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितम्
जित + .{@-तम्@} Victory.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जिताक्षर, जितामित्र, जितारि, जितात्मन्, जिताहव, जितेन्द्रिय, जितकाशिः, जितकाशिन्, जितकोप, जितक्रोध, जितमन्यु, जितनेमिः, जितलोक, जितशत्रु, जितशिश्नोदर, जितश्रम, जितस्वर्ग, जितहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताक्षर|जिताक्षरः
जित + -अक्षर <i>a.</i> reading well or readily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितामित्र|जितामित्रः
जित + -अमित्र <i>a.</i> one who has conquered his foes, triumphant, victorious.<BR>—2 one who has subdued his passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितामित्रः|जितामित्र
जित + -अमित्र + .({@-त्रः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितारि|जितारिः
जित + -अरि <i>a.</i> one who has conquered his enemies or passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितारिः|जितारि
जित + -अरि + .({@-रिः@}) an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितात्मन्
जित + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> self-subdued, void of passion; जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य Bg. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताहव|जिताहवः
जित + -आहव <i>a.</i> victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रिय|जितेंद्रिय|जितेन्द्रियः
जित + -इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> one who has conquered his passions or subdued<BR> the senses (रूप, रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श & शब्द); श्रुत्वा स्पृष्ट्वाऽथ<BR> दृष्ट्वा च भुक्त्वा घ्रात्वा च यो नरः । न हृष्यति ग्लायति वा स विज्ञेयो<BR> जितेन्द्रियः Ms. 2. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशिः|जितकाशि
जित + -काशिः the fist doubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशिन्
जित + -काशिन् <i>a.</i> appearing victorious, proud of victory, assuming<BR> the airs of a victor; जितकाशिनश्च खचराः Mb. 3. 244. 6; भीष्मः<BR> पुरुषमानी च जितकाशी तथैव च <i>ibid.</i> 5. 177. 12; चाणक्योऽपि<BR> जितकाशितया Mu. 2; जितकाशी राजसेवकः <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकोप
जित + -कोप, -क्रोध, -मन्यु <i>a.</i> imperturbable, not excitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

