जिनेश्वरः|जिनेश्वर
जिन + -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a chief Bauddha saint.<BR>—2 an Arhat of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनयोनिः|जिनयोनि
जिन + -योनिः A deer (cf. अजिनयोनि); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनसद्मन्
जिन + -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> a Jaina temple or monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्दुराजः|जिन्दुराज
जिन्दुराजः N. of a person; तदानीं जिन्दुराजाख्यो … साचिव्यं<BR> ग्राहितोऽभवत् Rāj. T. 7. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रि|जिव्रिः
जिव्रि <i>a.</i> Ved. Old, decayed; अवासृजन्त जिव्रयो न देवाः Rv. 4. 19. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रिः|जिव्रि
जिव्रि + .{@-व्रिः@}<BR>—1 Time.<BR>—2 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम्
जिम् €1 P. (जेमति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
जिरि €5 P. (जिरिणोति) To kill, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिल्लिकः|जिल्लिक
जिल्लिकः (pl.) N. of people; (see झिल्लिक) जिल्लिकाः कुन्तलाश्चैव Mb. 6. 9. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्व्
जिन्व् €1 P. (जिन्वति)<BR>—1 To be active or lively, busy oneself.<BR>—2 To urge on, impel, excite.<BR>—3 To refresh,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">Page0738-2</a>]<BR> animate.<BR>—4 To promote.<BR>—5 To grant, confer.<BR>—6 To please, satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्
जिष् €1 P. (जेषति) To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवाजिवः|जिवाजिव
जिवाजिवः The Chakora bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going, going to.<BR>—2 Getting, obtaining, see हा ‘to go’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहानकः|जिहानक
जिहानकः Destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म <i>a.</i> [जहाति सरलमार्गम्; हा-मन् सन्वत् आलोपश्च Uṇ. 1. 138]<BR>—1 Sloping, athwart, oblique.<BR>—2 Crooked, awry, squint; Ṛs. 1. 12.<BR>—3 Tortuous, curved, going irregularly.<BR>—4 Curved, bent.<BR>—5 Morally crooked, deceitful, dishonest, wicked, unfair; धृतहेतिरप्यधृतजिह्ममतिः<BR> Ki. 6. 24; सुहृदर्थमीहितमजिह्मधियाम् Śi. 9. 62.<BR>—5 Dim, dark, pale-coloured; विधिसमयनियोगाद्दीप्तिसंहारजिह्मम् Ki. 1. 46.<BR>—6 Slow, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मम्
जिह्म + .{@-ह्मम्@}<BR>—1 Dishonesty; falsehood; जिह्मप्रायं व्यवहृतम् Bhāg. 1. 14. 4;<BR> समर्थस्त्वं रणे हन्तुं विक्रमे जिह्मकारिणम् Rām. 4. 27. 36.<BR>—2 The Tagara tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जिह्माक्ष, जिह्मेतर, जिह्मग, जिह्मगति, जिह्ममेहनः, जिह्मयोधिन्, जिह्मशल्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्माक्ष
जिह्म + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> crooked-eyed, squinting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मेतर
जिह्म + -इतर <i>a.</i> ‘other than lazy’, not dull; जिह्मेतरैर्ब्रह्म<BR> तदप्यवाप्यम् N. 3. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मग|जिह्मगः
जिह्म + -ग <i>a.</i> moving slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मगः|जिह्मग
जिह्म + -ग + .({@-गः@}) a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मगति
जिह्म + -गति <i>a.</i> meandering, going tortuously; Ṛs. 1. 13; निहन्ति<BR> यो जिह्मगतीन् परान् पतगराडिव Śiva B. 19. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्ममेहनः|जिह्ममेहन
जिह्म + -मेहनः a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मयोधिन्
जिह्म + -योधिन् <i>a.</i> fighting unfairly. ━<i>m.</i> an epithet of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मशल्यः|जिह्मशल्य
जिह्म + -शल्यः the Khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मायति
जिह्मायति Den. P. To go crookedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मित
जिह्मित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bewildered; परिश्रमजिह्मितेक्षणम् Ki. 10. 60.<BR>—2 made crooked, bent; जिह्मिताध्मातकुक्षिः Mb. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वः|जिह्व|जिह्वं
जिह्वः The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वल|जिह्वलः
जिह्वल <i>a.</i> Voracious, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वा
जिह्वा<BR>—1 The tongue.<BR>—2 The tongue of fire <i>i. e.</i> a flame.<BR>—3 A sentence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जिह्वास्वादः, जिह्वोल्लेखनी, जिह्वोल्लेखनिका, जिह्वानिर्लेखनम्, जिह्वापः, जिह्वामलम्, जिह्वामूलम्, जिह्वामूलीय, जिह्वारदः, जिह्वालिह्, जिह्वालौल्यम्, जिह्वाशल्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वास्वादः|जिह्वास्वाद
जिह्वा + -आस्वादः licking lapping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वोल्लेखनी
जिह्वा + -उल्लेखनी, -उल्लेखनिका, -निर्लेखनम् a tongue-scraper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वोल्लेखनिका
जिह्वा + -उल्लेखनी, -उल्लेखनिका, -निर्लेखनम् a tongue-scraper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वानिर्लेखनम्
जिह्वा + -उल्लेखनी, -उल्लेखनिका, -निर्लेखनम् a tongue-scraper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वापः|जिह्वाप
जिह्वा + -पः<BR>—1 a dog.<BR>—2 a cat.<BR>—3 a tiger.<BR>—4 a leopard.<BR>—5 a bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामलम्
जिह्वा + -मलम् the fur of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूलम्
जिह्वा + -मूलम् the root of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूलीय|जिह्वामूलीयः
जिह्वा + -मूलीय <i>a.</i> a term particularly applied to the Visarga before<BR> क् and ख् and also to ऋ and ऌ and the guttural class of<BR> consonants (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वारदः|जिह्वारद
जिह्वा + -रदः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वालिह्
जिह्वा + -लिह् <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वालौल्यम्
जिह्वा + -लौल्यम् greediness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाशल्यः|जिह्वाशल्य
जिह्वा + -शल्यः the Khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीतिः|जीति
जीतिः <i>f.</i> [जि-क्तिन् वेदे दीर्घः]<BR>—1 Victory.<BR>—2 Decrease, loss.<BR>—3 Fading away, growing old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन <i>a.</i> [ज्या-क्त संप्रसा˚ दीर्घः] Old, aged, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीनः|जीन
जीन + .{@-नः@} A leather bag; जीनकार्मुकबस्तावीन् पृथग् दद्याद्विशुद्धये Ms. 11. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतः|जीमूत
जीमूतः [जयति नभः, जीयते अनिलेन जीवनस्योदकस्य मूतं बन्धो<BR> यत्र, जीवनं जलं मूतं बद्धम् अनेन, जीवनं मुञ्चतीति वा पृषो˚<BR> Tv. cf. Uṇ. 3. 91]<BR>—1 cloud; जीमूतेन स्वकुशलमयीं हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिम् Me. 4.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 A nourisher, sustainer.<BR>—4 An epithet of Indra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीमूतकूटः, जीमूतकेतुः, जीमूतप्रभः, जीमूतवाहनः, जीमूतवाहिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतकूटः|जीमूतकूट
जीमूतः + -कूटः a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतकेतुः|जीमूतकेतु
जीमूतः + -केतुः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">Page0739-1</a>]<BR> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतप्रभः|जीमूतप्रभ
जीमूतः + -प्रभः A variety of gems; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहनः|जीमूतवाहन
जीमूतः + -वाहनः<BR>—1 N. of Indra.<BR>—2 N. of a king of the Vidyādharas, hero of the play called Nāgānanda;<BR> (mentioned also in कथासरित्सागर). [He was the son of Jīmūtaketu<BR> and renowned for his benevolent and charitable disposition. When his fatherʼs<BR> kingdom was invaded by his kinsmen, he scorned the idea of fighting with<BR> them and induced his father to leave it to those who sought for it and<BR> to repair with him to the Malaya mountain to lead a holy life. It is related<BR> that there he one day took the place of a young serpent who was, by virtue<BR> of an agreement, to be offered to Garuḍa as his daily meal, and induced,<BR> by his generous and touching behaviour, the enemy of serpents to give<BR> up his practice of devouring them. The story is very pathetically told in the play].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहिन्
जीमूतः + -वाहिन् Smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर <i>a.</i> [ज्या रक् संप्रसा˚ दीर्घः] Ved. Swift, quick; कनिक्रदद्<BR> वृषभो जीरदानू रेतो दधात्योषधीषु गर्भम् Rv. 5. 83. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरः|जीर
जीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A sword.<BR>—2 Cumin-seed.<BR>—3 An atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरकः|जीरक
जीरकः, -जीरणः<BR> Cumin-seed; अजमोदां च बाह्लीकं जीरकं लोध्रकं तथा<BR> Śiva B. 30. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरणः|जीरण
जीरकः, -जीरणः<BR> Cumin-seed; अजमोदां च बाह्लीकं जीरकं लोध्रकं तथा<BR> Śiva B. 30. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरिः|जीरि
जीरिः [जीर्यति जॄ-बा˚ रिक्] Ved. A man. ━<i>f.</i> Quick or flowing<BR> water; प्र जीरयः सिस्रते सध्प्य १ क् पृथक् Rv. 2. 17. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण <i>p. p.</i> [जॄ-क्त]<BR>—1 Old, ancient.<BR>—2 Worn out, ruined, wasted, decayed, tattered (as clothes); वासांसि<BR> जीर्णानि यथा विहाय Bg. 2. 22; U. 6. 38; Māl. 5. 30.<BR>—3 Digested; सुजीर्णमन्नं सुविचक्षणः सुतः H. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णः|जीर्ण|जीर्णं
जीर्ण + .{@-र्णः@}<BR>—1 An old man.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR>—3 Cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णा
जीर्ण + .{@-णा@} Large cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णम्
जीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@}<BR>—1 Benzoin.<BR>—2 Old age, decrepitude.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीर्णोद्धारः, जीर्णोद्यानम्, जीर्णज्वरः, जीर्णपर्णः, जीर्णवज्रम्, जीर्णवस्त्र, जीर्णवाटिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्धारः|जीर्णोद्धार
जीर्ण + -उद्धारः ‘renewing the old’, repairs, especially of a temple or<BR> any charitable or religious institution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्यानम्
जीर्ण + -उद्यानम् ruined or neglected garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णज्वरः|जीर्णज्वर
जीर्ण + -ज्वरः lingering fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णपर्णः|जीर्णपर्ण|जीर्णपर्ण्ण
जीर्ण + -पर्णः the Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवज्रम्
जीर्ण + -वज्रम् a particular gem (वैक्रान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवस्त्र|जीर्णवस्त्रं
जीर्ण + -वस्त्र <i>a.</i> wearing old clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवाटिका
जीर्ण + -वाटिका a ruined house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णक
जीर्णक <i>a.</i> Almost dried up or withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णिः|जीर्णि
जीर्णिः<BR>—1 Old age, decrepitude, decay, infirmity.<BR>—2 Digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्विः|जीर्वि
जीर्विः [जॄ-क्विन्]<BR>—1 An axe.<BR>—2 The body.<BR>—3 A cart. —4 An animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्
जीव् €1 P. (जीवति, जीवित)<BR>—1 To live, be alive; यस्मिञ् जीवति जीवन्ति बहवः सोऽत्र जीवति<BR> Pt. 1. 23; मा जीवन् यः परावज्ञादुःखदग्धोऽपि जीवति Śi. 2. 45; Ms. 2. 235.<BR>—2 To revive, come to life.<BR>—3 To live by, subsist on, make a livelihood by (with instr.); सत्यानृतं<BR> तु वाणिज्यं तेन चैवापि जीव्यते Ms. 4. 6; विपणेन च जीवन्तः 3. 152, 162, 11. 26;<BR> sometimes used with a cognate accusative in this sense;<BR> अजिह्मामशठां शुद्धां जीवेद् ब्राह्मणजीविकाम् Ms. 4. 11.<BR>—4 (Fig.) To live or prey upon, depend<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">Page0739-2</a>]<BR> upon as oneʼs source of existence (with loc.); चौराः प्रमत्ते जीवन्ति<BR> व्याधितेषु चिकित्सकाः । प्रमदाः कामयानेषु यजमानेषु याचकाः ॥ राजा<BR> विवदमानेषु नित्यं मूर्खेषु पण्डिताः Mb. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To restore to life.<BR>—2 To nourish, nurture, bring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव <i>a.</i> [जीव्-कर्तरि क] Living, existing; जीवपुत्रे निवर्तस्व<BR> Rām. 4. 19. 11; असच्च सज्जीवमजीवमन्यत् Bhāg. 5. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवः|जीव
जीव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 The principle of life, the vital breath, life, soul; गतजीव, जीवत्याग, जीवाशा &c.<BR>—2 The individual or personal soul enshrined in the human body and imparting<BR> to it life, motion and sensation (called जीवात्मन् as opposed to परमात्मन्<BR> the Supreme Soul); Y. 3. 131; Ms. 12. 22-23; सम्पद्यते गुणैर्मुक्तो जीवो<BR> जीवं विहाय माम् । जीवो जीवविनिर्मुक्तो गुणैश्चाशयसंभवैः ॥ Bhāg. 11. 25. 36.<BR> (here जीव = लिङ्गशरीर).<BR>—3 Life, existence.<BR>—4 A creature, living being.<BR>—5 Livelihood, profession.<BR>—6 N. of Karṇa.<BR>—7 N. of one of the Maruts.<BR>—8 The constellation पुष्य.<BR>—9 N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—10 The third lustrum in the cycle of Jupiter.<BR>—11 Association of cause and effect.<BR>—12 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीवान्तकः, जीवाजीवाधारः, जीवात्मन्, जीवादानम्, जीवाधानम्, जीवाधारः, जीवेन्धनम्, जीवोत्सर्गः, जीवोपाधिः, जीवोर्णा, जीवकोशः, जीवगृहम्, जीवमन्दिरम्, जीवग्राहः, जीवग्राहम्, जीवघनः, जीवज, जीवजीवः, जीवजीवकः, जीवतोका, जीवदः, जीवदशा, जीवधनम्, जीवधानी, जीवनिकायः, जीवपतिः, जीवपत्रम्, जीवपितृ, जीवपितृक, जीवपुत्रा, जीववत्सा, जीवमन्दिरम्, जीवमरणम्, जीवमातृका, जीवयोनिः, जीवरक्तम्, जीवलोकः, जीववृत्तिः, जीवशेष, जीवशोणितम्, जीवसंक्रमणम्, जीवसाधनम्, जीवसाफल्यम्, जीवसूः, जीवस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवान्तकः|जीवान्तक|जीवांतक
जीव + -अन्तकः<BR>—1 a bird-catcher, fowler.<BR>—2 a murderer, slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाजीवाधारः|जीवाजीवाधार
जीव + -अजीवाधारः the world of organic and inorganic creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवात्मन्
जीव + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the individual soul enshrined in the human body<BR> (as opposed to परमात्मन् ‘the Supreme soul’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवादानम्
जीव + -आदानम् abstracting healthy blood, bleeding (in medic.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाधानम्
जीव + -आधानम् preservation of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाधारः|जीवाधार
जीव + -आधारः the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवेन्धनम्
जीव + -इन्धनम् glowing fire-wood, burning wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवोत्सर्गः|जीवोत्सर्ग
जीव + -उत्सर्गः ‘casting off life’, voluntary death, suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवोपाधिः|जीवोपाधि
जीव + -उपाधिः the three states, <i>i. e.</i> waking, dreaming and sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवोर्णा
जीव + -ऊर्णा the wool of a living animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवकोशः|जीवकोश
जीव + -कोशः The subtle body (लिङ्गशरीर); तदनुस्मरणध्वस्तजीवकोशास्तमध्ययन्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 82. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवगृहम्
जीव + -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् ‘the abode of the soul’, the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमन्दिरम्
जीव + -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् ‘the abode of the soul’, the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवग्राहः|जीवग्राह
जीव + -ग्राहः a prisoner taken alive;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवग्राहम्
जीव + -ग्राहम् <i>ind.</i> in an alive condition; जीवग्राहं निगृह्णीमो<BR> वयमेनं नराधिपाः Mb. 6. 77. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवघनः|जीवघन
जीव + -घनः Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवज
जीव + -ज <i>a.</i> born alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवजीवः|जीवजीव
जीव + -जीवः, -जीवकः (also जीवंजीवः) the Chakora bird; रक्तानि<BR> हृत्वा वासांसि जायते जीवजीवकः Ms. 12. 66. According to Arthaśāstra,<BR> however, it means a pheasant; विषाभ्याशे ग्लायति जीवंजीवकः । चकोरस्याक्षिणी<BR> विरज्येते Kau. A. 1. 20. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवजीवकः|जीवजीवक
जीव + -जीवः, -जीवकः (also जीवंजीवः) the Chakora bird; रक्तानि<BR> हृत्वा वासांसि जायते जीवजीवकः Ms. 12. 66. According to Arthaśāstra,<BR> however, it means a pheasant; विषाभ्याशे ग्लायति जीवंजीवकः । चकोरस्याक्षिणी<BR> विरज्येते Kau. A. 1. 20. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवतोका
जीव + -तोका a woman whose children are living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवदः|जीवद
जीव + -दः<BR>—1 a physician.<BR>—2 an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवदशा
जीव + -दशा mortal existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवधनम्
जीव + -धनम् ‘living wealth’, property in the shape of living creatures, live-stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवधानी
जीव + -धानी the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनिकायः|जीवनिकाय
जीव + -निकायः a being endowed with life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपतिः|जीवपति
जीव + -पतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-पत्नी@}<BR> a woman whose husband is alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपत्रम्
जीव + -पत्रम् a fresh leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपितृ
जीव + -पितृ, -पितृक <i>a.</i> (a son or daughter) whose father is still alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपितृक
जीव + -पितृ, -पितृक <i>a.</i> (a son or daughter) whose father is still alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपुत्रा
जीव + -पुत्रा, -वत्सा a woman whose son is living; जीवपुत्रे निवर्तस्व<BR> पुत्रं रक्षस्व चाङ्गदम् Rām. 4. 19. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीववत्सा
जीव + -पुत्रा, -वत्सा a woman whose son is living; जीवपुत्रे निवर्तस्व<BR> पुत्रं रक्षस्व चाङ्गदम् Rām. 4. 19. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमन्दिरम्
जीव + -मन्दिरम् The body; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमरणम्
जीव + -मरणम् Death in life; जीवन्मरणमेतद् इति कौटिल्यः Kau. A. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमातृका
जीव + -मातृका the seven mothers or female divinities; (कुमारी धनदा<BR> नन्दा विमला मङ्गला बला । पद्मा चेति च विख्याताः सप्तैता जीवमातृकाः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवयोनिः|जीवयोनि
जीव + -योनिः a sentient being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवरक्तम्
जीव + -रक्तम् menstrual blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवलोकः|जीवलोक
जीव + -लोकः<BR>—1 the world of living beings, the world of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">Page0740-1</a>]<BR> mortals, the world or worldly existence; आलोकमर्कादिव जीवलोकः<BR> R. 5. 35; त्वत्प्रयाणे शान्तालोकः सर्वतो जीवलोकः Māl. 9. 37; जीवलोकतिलकः<BR> प्रलीयते 21; so स्वप्नेन्द्रजालसदृशः खलु जीवलोकः Śānti. 2. 2;<BR> Bg. 11. 7; U. 4. 17.<BR>—2 living beings; दिवस इवाभ्रश्यामस्तपात्यये जीवलोकस्य Ś. 3. 12;<BR> or आलोकमर्कादिव जीवलोकः R. 5. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीववृत्तिः|जीववृत्ति
जीव + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> breeding or keeping cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवशेष
जीव + -शेष <i>a.</i> one to whom only life is left, escaping only with<BR> life and nothing more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवशोणितम्
जीव + -शोणितम् living, <i>i. e.</i> healthy blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसंक्रमणम्
जीव + -संक्रमणम् transmigration of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाधनम्
जीव + -साधनम् grain, corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाफल्यम्
जीव + -साफल्यम् realization or attainment of the chief end of human existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसूः
जीव + -सूः ‘the mother of living beings’, a woman whose children are living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवस्थानम्
जीव + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a joint, an articulation.<BR>—2 the vital parts, heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक <i>a.</i> [जीव्-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Living, making a livelihood by, generating &c.<BR>—2 One who lives a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवकः|जीवक
जीवक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A living being.<BR>—2 A servant.<BR>—3 A Buddhist mendicant, any mendicant who lives by begging.<BR>—4 A usurer.<BR>—5 A snake-catcher.<BR>—6 A tree.<BR>—7 A medicinal plant of that name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्|जीवन्त्
जीवत् <i>a.</i> (-न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Living, alive.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीवत्तोका, जीवत्पतिः, जीवत्पितृकः, जीवन्मुक्त, जीवन्मुक्तिः, जीवन्मृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्तोका
जीवत् + -तोका a woman whose children are living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्पतिः|जीवत्पति
जीवत् + -पतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-पत्नी@} <i>f.</i><BR> a woman whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्पितृकः|जीवत्पितृक
जीवत् + -पितृकः one whose father is alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्त|जीवन्मुक्तः
जीवत् + -मुक्त <i>a.</i> ‘liberated while living’, a man who, being purified<BR> by a true knowledge of the Supreme Spirit, is freed from the future birth<BR> and all ceremonial rites while yet living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्तिः|जीवन्मुक्ति
जीवत् + -मुक्तिः <i>f.</i> final liberation in the present state of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मृत
जीवत् + -मृत <i>a.</i> ‘dead while alive’, one who, though alive, is as<BR> good as dead and useless to the world (said of a mad man or one whose character is lost).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ <i>a.</i> [जीव्-अथ]<BR>—1 Long-lived.<BR>—2 Virtuous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथः|जीवथ
जीवथ + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 Life, existence.<BR>—2 A tortoise.<BR>—3 A peacock.<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR>—5 Virtue, piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जीव् भावे ल्युट्] Enlivening, giving life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनः|जीवन|जीवनं
जीवन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A living being.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 A son.<BR>—4 The Supreme Being; बीजानां प्रभव नमोऽस्तु जीवनाय Ki. 18. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनम्
जीवन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Life, existence; (fig. also) त्वमसि मम भूषणं त्वमसि मम जीवनम् Gīt. 10.<BR>—2 The principle of life, vital energy; Bg. 7. 9.<BR>—3 Water; बीजानां प्रभव नमोऽस्तु जीवनाय Ki. 18. 39; or जीवनं<BR> जीवनं (life) हन्ति प्राणान् हन्ति समीरणः Udb.<BR>—4 Livelihood, profession, means of existence (fig. also); Ms. 11. 77;<BR> विदुषां जीवनं मूर्खः H. 3. 33.<BR>—5 Butter made from milk one day old.<BR>—6 Marrow.<BR>—7 Enlivening, making alive.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीवनान्तः, जीवनाघातम्, जीवनावासः, जीवनोपायः, जीवनौषधम्, जीवनपञ्चमूलानि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनान्तः|जीवनान्त|जीवनांत
जीवन + -अन्तः death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनाघातम्
जीवन + -आघातम् poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनावासः|जीवनावास
जीवन + -आवासः<BR>—1 ‘residing in water’, epithet of Varuṇa, the regent of water.<BR>—2 the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनोपायः|जीवनोपाय
जीवन + -उपायः livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनौषधम्
जीवन + -ओषधम्<BR>—1 elixir of life.<BR>—2 a life-giving medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनपञ्चमूलानि
जीवन + -पञ्चमूलानि (Āyurveda) The five medicinal herbs called वीरा,<BR> जीवन्ती, गुरुशतावरी, जीवक and ऋषभक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनक|जीवनकं
जीवनक <i>a.</i> [जीवन-कन्] Enlivening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनकम्
जीवनक + .{@-कम्@} Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीय|जीवनीयं
जीवनीय <i>a.</i> [जीव्-बा˚ करणे अनीयर्]<BR>—1 To be lived.<BR>—2 Supporting life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीयम्
जीवनीय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Fresh milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्त|जीवंत|जीवन्तः
जीवन्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living, existing.<BR>—2 Long-lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तः|जीवन्त|जीवंत
जीवन्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Life, existence.<BR>—2 A drug, medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तिकः|जीवन्तिक|जीवंतिक|जीवंतिकः
जीवन्तिकः A fowler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तिका
जीवन्तिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A goddess looking after the welfare of a child (Mar. जिवती); गणेशं<BR> जन्मदां षष्टीं देवीं जीवन्तिकामपि Śiva B. 6. 48.<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्ती
जीवन्ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A species of plant.<BR>—2 A kind of sweet dish; कृसरेणाथ जीवन्त्या हविष्येण च सर्वशः Mb. 2. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवल
जीवल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Full of life.<BR>—2 Animating, inspiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवा
जीवा <i>f.^1</i> [जीव्-अच्]<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR>—3 A bow-string; मुहुर्जीवाघोषैर्बधिरयति Mv. 6. 30.<BR>—4 The chord of an arc.<BR>—5 Means of living.<BR>—6 The tinkling of metallic ornaments.<BR>—7 N. of a plant (वचा).<BR>—8 Life, existence.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवातु|जीवातुः
जीवातु <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 Life, existence (fig. also); स खलु प्राज्ञजीवातुः सर्वशास्त्रविशारदः J. N. V.<BR>—3 Restoration to life, revival; रे हस्त दक्षिण मृतस्य शिशोर्द्विजस्य<BR> जीवातवे विसृज शूद्रमुनौ कृपाणम् U. 2. 10.<BR>—4 Medicine for restoring life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविका
जीविका [जीव्-अकन् अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 Means of living, livelihood; कुदेशे नास्ति जीविका Mb. 12. 139. 94.<BR>—2 The life-giving element, <i>i. e.</i> water.<BR>—3 life; कृपणा वर्तयिष्यामि कथं कृपणजीविका Rām. 2. 20. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवित|जीवितं
जीवित <i>p. p.</i> [जीव् कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Living, existent, alive; R. 12. 75.<BR>—2 Returned to life, revived.<BR>—3 Animated, enlivened.<BR>—4 Lived through (as a period).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितम्
जीवित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Life, existence; त्वं जीवितं त्वमसि मे हृदयं द्वितीयम् U. 3. 26;<BR> कन्येयं कुलजीवितम् Ku. 6. 63; Me. 83; नाभिनन्देत मरणं<BR> नाभिनन्देत जीवितम् Ms. 6. 45, 7. 111.<BR>—2 Duration of life.<BR>—3 Livelihood.<BR>—4 A living being.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जीवितान्तकः, जीविताशा, जीवितेशः, जीवितेश्वरः, जीवितकालः, जीवितज्ञा, जीवितनाथः, जीवितव्ययः, जीवितसंशयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितान्तकः|जीवितान्तक|जीवितांतक
जीवित + -अन्तकः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविताशा
जीवित + -आशा hope of life, love of life. नहि नहि तत्र धनाशा जीवित<BR> आशाऽपि दुस्सहो भवति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितेशः|जीवितेश
जीवित + -ईशः<BR>—1 a lover, husband.<BR>—2 an epithet of Yama; जीवितेशवसतिं जगाम सा R. 11. 20 (where<BR> the word is used in sense 1 also).<BR>—3 the sun.<BR>—4 the moon.<BR>—5 a drug which is said to revive the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितेश्वरः|जीवितेश्वर
जीवित + -ईश्वरः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितकालः|जीवितकाल
जीवित + -कालः duration of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितज्ञा
जीवित + -ज्ञा an artery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितनाथः|जीवितनाथ
जीवित + -नाथः a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्ययः|जीवितव्यय
जीवित + -व्ययः sacrifice of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितसंशयः|जीवितसंशय
जीवित + -संशयः risk of life, jeopardy, danger to life; स आतुरो जीवितसंशये<BR> वर्तते ‘he is dangerously ill’; Bv. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be lived, kept alive &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्यम्
जीवितव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} The possibility of living.<BR>—2 Life.<BR>—3 Possible return to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविन्
जीविन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जीव्-णिनि, जीव-इनि वा] (Generally at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Living, alive, existing; R. 1. 63.<BR>—2 Living upon or by; शस्त्रजीविन्, आयुधजीविन् &c. ━<i>m.</i> A living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्यम्
जीव्यम् Life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्या
जीव्यम् + .{@-व्या@} A means of livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जु
जु €1 Ā. (जवते) To go; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुटः|जुकुट
जुकुटः<BR>—1 A dog.<BR>—2 The Malaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुटम्
जुकुटः + .{@-टम्@} The egg-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सनम्
जुगुप्सनम्, जुगुप्सा<BR>—1 Censure, reproach.<BR>—2 Dislike, aversion, disgust, abhorrence.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Disgust considered as the feeling which gives rise to the<BR> Bībhatsa sentiment, thus defined:− दोषेक्षणादिभिर्गर्हा जुगुप्सा विषयोद्भवा S. D. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सा
जुगुप्सनम्, जुगुप्सा<BR>—1 Censure, reproach.<BR>—2 Dislike, aversion, disgust, abhorrence.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Disgust considered as the feeling which gives rise to the<BR> Bībhatsa sentiment, thus defined:− दोषेक्षणादिभिर्गर्हा जुगुप्सा विषयोद्भवा S. D. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सितम्
जुगुप्सितम् A disgusting or horrible deed; जुगुप्सितं धर्मकृतेऽनुशासतः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 15. कर्मजुगुप्सितेन <i>ibid.</i> 1. 7. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्ग्|जुंग्
जुङ्ग् €1 P. (जुङ्गति)<BR>—1 To abandon, quit.<BR>—2 To exclude, set aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्गित|जुंगित|जुङ्गितः
जुङ्गित <i>a.</i> Deserted, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्गितः|जुङ्गित|जुंगित
जुङ्गित + .{@-तः@} A man of a degraded caste, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटकम्
जुटकम् A braid of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटिका
जुटिका A tuft of hair on the top of the head; cf. चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुड्
जुड् I. €6 P. (जुडति)<BR>—1 To bind.<BR>—2 To go. ━II. €10 P.<BR>—1 To send, throw or cast, direct.<BR>—2 To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुत्
जुत् €1 Ā. (जोतते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुन्
जुन् €6 P. (जुनति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुम्बकः|जुम्बक|जुंबकः
जुम्बकः Ved. An epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर् €6. €4. P. (जुरति, जूर्यति) Ved. —1 To decay, become or grow<BR> old, waste away, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर्, -जूर् <i>m.</i><BR> An old man; इन्द्रं सोमैरोर्णुत जूर्न वस्त्रैः Rv. 2. 14. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्
जुर्, -जूर् <i>m.</i><BR> An old man; इन्द्रं सोमैरोर्णुत जूर्न वस्त्रैः Rv. 2. 14. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ण
जूर्ण <i>a.</i> Decayed, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्य|जूर्य्य
जूर्य <i>a.</i> Old; रण्वः पुरीव जूर्यः सूनुर्न त्रययाय्यः Rv. 6. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुल्
जुल् €10 P. (जोलयति) To reduce to powder, grind, pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुवस्
जुवस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Speed, quickness; आ नः सोम सहो जुवो रूपं<BR> न वर्चसे भर Rv. 6. 65. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् I. €6 Ā. (जुषते-जुष्ट)<BR>—1 To be pleased or satisfied.<BR>—2 To be favourable or propitious.<BR>—3 To like, be fond of, take pleasure or delight in, enjoy; सत्त्वं<BR> जुषाणस्य भवाय देहिनाम् Bhāg.<BR>—4 To devote or attach oneself to, practise, undergo, suffer; पौलस्त्योऽजुषत<BR> शुचं विपन्नबन्धुः Bk. 17. 112.<BR>—5 To frequent, visit, inhabit; जुषन्ते पर्वतश्रेष्ठमृषयः पर्वसन्धिषु Mb.<BR>—6 To enter, seat oneself, resort to; रथं च जुजुषे शुभम् Bk. 14. 95.<BR>—7 To choose.<BR>—8 To enjoy, possess, have; Māl. 5. 18.<BR>—9 To happen to.<BR>—10 To delight in granting or performing.<BR>—11 To show oneself favourable towards. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To like, be fond of.<BR>—2 To fondle, cherish.<BR>—3 To delight in, approve of, rejoice at. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (जोषति, जोषयति-ते)<BR>—1 To reason, think.<BR>—2 To investigate, examine.<BR>—3 To hurt.<BR>—4 To be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Liking, enjoying, taking delight in; Bh. 3. 103.<BR>—2 Visiting, approaching, going to, taking, amusing, resorting to &c.;<BR> परलोकजुषाम् R. 8. 85; रजोजुषे जन्मनि K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्य|जुष्यः
जुष्य <i>a.</i> To be served, worshipped &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्यम्
जुष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} Service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [जुष्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Pleased, gratified.<BR>—2 Practised, resorted to, visited, suffered &c.; अनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यमकीर्तिकरमर्जुन Bg. 2. 2.<BR>—3 Furnished or endowed with, possessed of; राजप्रभावजुष्टां च दुर्वहामजितेन्द्रियैः Rām. 2. 2. 9.<BR>—4 Liked, loved, agreeable.<BR>—5 Served, worshipped; सम्बन्धस्पृहणीयताप्रमुदितैर्जुष्टे वसिष्टादिभिः U. 6. 40.<BR>—6 Propitious, favourable.<BR>—7 Shared, partaken in; U. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्टम्
जुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} The remnants of meal (उच्छिष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषः|जोष|जोषं
जोषः [जुष्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Satisfaction, enjoyment, happiness, pleasure.<BR>—2 Silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषम्
जोषः + .{@-षम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to oneʼs wish, with ease.<BR>—2 Silently; किमिति जोषमास्यते Ś. 5; Bv. 2. 17; जोषमास न विशिष्य<BR> बभाषे N. 5. 78.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जोषवाकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषवाकः|जोषवाक
जोषः + -वाकः chattering nonsense; जोषवाकं वदतः Rv. 6. 59. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषणम्
जोषणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Liking.<BR>—2 Satisfaction, approval.<BR>—3 Choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषणा
जोषणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Liking.<BR>—2 Satisfaction, approval.<BR>—3 Choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्कः|जुष्क
जुष्कः N. of one of the three Kashmirian Turuṣka kings; हुष्कजुष्ककनिष्काख्यास्त्रयस्तत्रैव<BR> पार्थिवाः Rāj. T. 1. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ककः|जुष्कक
जुष्ककः Soup of boiled rice; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुराण|जुहुराणः
जुहुराण <i>a.</i> Making crooked or acting crookedly; युयोध्यस्मज्जुहुराणमेनः Īśop. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुराणः|जुहुराण
जुहुराण + .{@-णः@} The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवानः|जुहुवान
जुहुवानः [हु कर्मणि कानच्]<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR>—3 A hard-hearted man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूः
जुहूः <i>f.</i> [हु क्विप् नि˚ द्वित्वं दीर्घश्च Tv.]<BR>—1 A crescent-shaped wooden ladle used for pouring the sacrificial ghee into the fire.<BR>—2 A tongue, especially of Agni <i>i. e.</i> a flame.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जुह्वास्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वास्यः|जुह्वास्य
जुहूः + -आस्यः fire; हव्यवाड् जुह्वास्यः Rv. 1. 12. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूराणः|जुहूराण
जुहूरा(वा)णः<BR>—1 A sacrificial priest.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवाणः|जुहूवाण
जुहूरा(वा)णः<BR>—1 A sacrificial priest.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवत्|जुहूवन्त्
जुहूवत् <i>m.</i> Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहोतिः|जुहोति
जुहोतिः A technical name for those sacrificial ceremonies to which<BR> the verb जुहोति is applied as distinguished from those to which यजति<BR> is applied; क्षरन्ति सर्वा वैदिक्यो जुहोतियजतिक्रियाः Ms. 2. 84. (See<BR> Medhātithi and other commentators; सर्वज्ञनारायण shortly renders<BR> जुहोति by उपविष्टहोम and यजति by तिष्ठद्धोम. See Āśval. 1. 2. 5<BR> also); cf. also जुहोतिरासेचनाधिकः स्यात् MS. 4. 2. 28. यजतिरेवासेचनाधिको<BR> जुहोतिः । ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू €1 U., €9 P. (जवति-ते, जुनाति)<BR>—1 To press or hurry on, move on quickly.<BR>—2 To impel quickly, urge or drive on.<BR>—3 To excite, animate, inspire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू <i>a.</i> Ved. Quick, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूः
जूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Speed.<BR>—2 Atmosphere.<BR>—3 A female demon.<BR>—4 An epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—5 Going speedily, quick motion.<BR>—6 A mark on the forehead of horses and oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूत
जूत <i>a.</i> [जू-क्त] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Impelled, urged, pressed.<BR>—2 Ved. Gone.<BR>—3 Drawn.<BR>—4 Given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूतिः|जूति
जूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going on, proceeding, moving; जूतिमिच्छथ चेत्तूर्णम् … … Bk. 7. 69.<BR>—2 Quickness, speed.<BR>—3 Uninterrupted flow or motion.<BR>—4 Impulse, incitement, instigation.<BR>—5 Inclination, propensity, tendency.<BR>—6 N. of the author of Rv. 10. 136. 1.<BR>—7 Concentration of mind … … जूतिः स्मृतिः संकल्पः क्रतुरसुः कामो<BR> वश इति Ait. Up. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूकः|जूक
जूकः The sign Libra of the zodiac (a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूटः|जूट
जूटः The mass of twisted or matted hair; भूतेशस्य भुजङ्गवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटाजटाः Māl. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूटकम्
जूटकम् Matted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्
जूर् €4 Ā. (जूर्यते, जूर्ण)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>—2 To be angry with (with dat.); भर्त्रे नखेभ्यश्च चिरं जुजूरे Bk. 11. 8.<BR>—3 To grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
जूर्णि <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Swift, speedy, quick.<BR>—2 Running, proceeding quickly.<BR>—3 Praising, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णिः|जूर्णि
जूर्णि + .{@-र्णिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Speed.<BR>—2 An epithet of Āditya or sun.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>—4 The Brahman (<i>n.</i>).<BR>—5 Anger.<BR>—6 A fiery weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्तिः|जूर्ति|जूर्त्ति|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्तिः <i>f.</i> [ज्वर् भावे क्तिन् ऊठ्]<BR>—1 Fever.<BR>—2 Feverish or morbid heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्व्
जूर्व् €1 P. (जूर्वति) Ved.<BR>—1 To burn; उपप्तदसौ सूर्यः पुरु विश्वानि जूर्वन् Rv. 1. 191. 9.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष्
जूष् €1 U. (जूषति-ते) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषः|जूष|जूषं
जूषः, -षम्<BR> The water of boiled pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषम्
जूषः, -षम्<BR> The water of boiled pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ €1 P. (जरति)<BR>—1 To make low or humiliate.<BR>—2 To excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृङ्गः|जृङ्ग
जृङ्गः^1 <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a people; पञ्चनद-रमठ-पारत-तारक्षितिजृङ्ग-वैश्य-कनक-शकाः<BR> Bṛ. S. 14. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भ्|जृंभ्
जृम्भ् €1 Ā. (जृम्भते, जृम्भित, जृब्ध)<BR>—1 To gape, yawn; Ms. 4. 43.<BR>—2 To open, expand, burst open (as a flower &c.); वरयुवतिमुखाभं<BR> पङ्कजं जृम्भतेऽद्य Ṛs. 3. 22.<BR>—3 To increase, spread or extend everywhere; जृम्भतां जृम्भतामप्रतिहतप्रसरं<BR> क्रोधज्योतिः Ve. 1; तृष्णे जृम्भसि (Paras. is irregular) Bh. 3. 5;<BR> भोगः कोऽपि स एक एव परमो नित्योदितो जृम्भते 3. 80.<BR>—4 To appear, rise, show oneself, become visible or manifest; संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतमात्मानमाधाय<BR> मधूर्जजृम्भे Ku. 3. 24; U. 5. 13.<BR>—5 To be at ease.<BR>—6 To recoil or fly back (as a bow). ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to yawn or expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भः|जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभं|जृंभः
जृम्भः, -भा, -भम्<BR> [जृम्भ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Yawning, gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Opening, blossoming, expanding; कलिकाश्रयी जृम्भा प्रभवति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">Page0742-2</a>]<BR> K. 257; जृम्भारम्भप्रविततदलोपान्तजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7; Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—3 Expansion.<BR>—4 Bursting open.<BR>—5 A kind of bird; ततो जृम्भस्य शयने Rām. 2. 35. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भा
जृम्भः, -भा, -भम्<BR> [जृम्भ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Yawning, gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Opening, blossoming, expanding; कलिकाश्रयी जृम्भा प्रभवति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">Page0742-2</a>]<BR> K. 257; जृम्भारम्भप्रविततदलोपान्तजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7; Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—3 Expansion.<BR>—4 Bursting open.<BR>—5 A kind of bird; ततो जृम्भस्य शयने Rām. 2. 35. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भम्
जृम्भः, -भा, -भम्<BR> [जृम्भ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Yawning, gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>—2 Opening, blossoming, expanding; कलिकाश्रयी जृम्भा प्रभवति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">Page0742-2</a>]<BR> K. 257; जृम्भारम्भप्रविततदलोपान्तजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7; Māl. 9. 16.<BR>—3 Expansion.<BR>—4 Bursting open.<BR>—5 A kind of bird; ततो जृम्भस्य शयने Rām. 2. 35. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भकः|जृम्भक|जृंभकः
जृम्भकः [जृम्भ्-ण्वुल्] ‘A yawner’, a sort of demon; जृम्भकैर्यक्षरक्षोभिः<BR> स्रग्विभिः समलङ्कृतः Mb. 3. 231. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भकम्
जृम्भकः + .{@-कम्@} Swelling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जृम्भकास्त्रम्, जृम्भिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भकास्त्रम्
जृम्भकः + -अस्त्रम् A kind of missile causing yawning and sleepiness; नियतममितवीर्यं<BR> जृम्भते जृम्भकास्त्रम् U. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिका|जृंभिका
जृम्भकः + जृम्भिका Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भण|जृंभण|जृम्भणं
जृम्भण <i>a.</i> [जृम्भ्-भावे ल्युट्] Causing to gape or yawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भणम्
जृम्भण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>—2 Stretching (the limbs); (अङ्गानि) मुहुर्मुहुर्जृम्भणतत्पराणि Ṛs. 6. 9.<BR>—3 Blossoming, blooming; मालती शिरसि जृम्भणोन्मुखी Bh. 1. 25.<BR>—4 Causing unconsciousness; हरस्य जृम्भणं युद्धे Bhāg. 12. 12. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भित|जृंभित|जृम्भितं
जृम्भित <i>p. p.</i> [जृम्भ्-क्त]<BR>—1 Yawned, gaped.<BR>—2 Opened, expanded, displayed; Māl. 1. 32.<BR>—3 Opened, blown (as a flower).<BR>—4 Done, exerted.<BR>—5 Enlarged, increased.<BR>—6 Unstrung (a bow); जृम्भितं तद्धनुर्दृष्ट्वा शैवं विष्णुपराक्रमैः<BR> Rām. 1. 75. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भितम्
जृम्भित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Gaping.<BR>—2 Expansion, opening, blooming.<BR>—3 Developing, coming into view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ I. €1. €4. €9 P., €10 U. (जरति, जीर्यति, जृणाति, जारयतिते,<BR> जजार, जारयामास, अजरत्, अजारीत्, अजीजरत्, जरि(री)तुम्, जीर्ण or जारित)<BR>—1 To grow old, wear out, wither away, decay; जीर्यन्ते जीर्यतः केशा<BR> दन्ता जीर्यन्ति जीर्यतः । जीर्यतश्चक्षुषी श्रोत्रे तृष्णैका तरुणायते<BR> Pt. 5. 16; Bk. 9. 41.<BR>—2 To perish, be consumed (fig. also); अजारीदिव च प्रज्ञा बलं शोकात्तथाऽजरत्<BR> Bk. 6. 30; जेरुराशा दशास्यस्य 14. 112.<BR>—3 To be dissolved or digested; जीर्णमन्नं प्रशंसीयात् Cāṇ. 79;<BR> उदरे चाजरन्नन्ये Bk. 15. 150.<BR>—4 To break up or fall to pieces. ━<i>Caus.</i> (ज-जा-रयति)<BR>—1 To make old, wear out, consume.<BR>—2 To cause to be digested; to digest. ━II. €1 Ā. (जरते) Ved.<BR>—1 To move, approach, come near.<BR>—2 To crackle (as fire).<BR>—3 To roar.<BR>—4 To call out to, invoke, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारक
जारक <i>a.</i> [जॄ-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Causing to decay.<BR>—2 Promoting digestion, digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारणम्
जारणम् [जॄ-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Causing to decay.<BR>—2 Stimulating digestion.<BR>—3 Calcining or oxidizing metals.<BR>—4 A condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारद्गव
जारद्गव <i>a.</i> (वीथिः) The portion of the moonʼs path occupied<BR> by the constellations श्रवण, धनिष्ठा and शततारका (according<BR> to वराहमिहिर); according to others, by विशाखा, अनुराधा and ज्येष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेज्जटः|जेज्जट
जेज्जटः N. of an author on medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतृ
जेतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of a son of Madhucchandas (author of Rv. 1. 11.)<BR>—2 N. of prince who had a grove near Śrāvasti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्ताकः|जेन्ताक|जेंताक|जेंताकः
जेन्ताकः A heated chamber for inducing perspiration, a dry hot bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्य
जेन्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Of noble origin, well-born.<BR>—2 Genuine, true; प्रयक्षञ्जेन्यं वसु Rv. 2. 5. 1.<BR>—3 Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेपालः
जेपालः A kind of medicinal plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमनम्
जेमनम् [जिम्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Eating.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष्
जेष् €1 Ā. (जेषते) To move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेह्
जेह् €1 Ā. (जेहते) Ved.<BR>—1 To reach, go towards.<BR>—2 To strive after, exert.<BR>—3 To open the mouth, pant, gasp; अरेणुभिर्जेहमानं पतत्रि Rv. 1. 163. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जै
जै €1 P. (जायति) To wane, decline, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैगीषव्यः|जैगीषव्य
जैगीषव्यः N. of an ancient ṛṣi named along with Asita Devala;<BR> सनातनश्च दक्षश्च जैगीषव्यो भगन्दरः Bṛ. S. 48. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैज्जटः|जैज्जट
जैज्जटः (See जेज्जटः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्र|जैत्रं|जैत्रः
जैत्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [जेतृ-अण्]<BR>—1 Victorious, successful, leading to victory; जैत्रं यं ते अनुमदाम<BR> सङ्गमे Rv. 1. 102. 3; इदमिह मदनस्य जैत्रमस्त्रं विफलगुणातिशयं<BR> भविष्यतीति Māl. 2. 6; धनुर्जैत्रं रघुर्दधौ R. 4. 16, 16. 72;<BR> आकारयज्जयीजैत्रप्रयाणपटहस्वनम् Śiva B. 29. 64.<BR>—2 Superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्रः|जैत्र|जैत्रं
जैत्र + .{@-त्रः@}<BR>—1 A victor, conqueror.<BR>—2 Quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्रम्
जैत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} A Victory, triumph; जैत्रयात्रापरैः सद्यः परैः स परिभूयते<BR> Śiva B. 16. 41.<BR>—3 Superiority.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जैत्ररथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्ररथः|जैत्ररथ
जैत्र + -रथः a victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैनः|जैन
जैनः <i>m.</i>^1<BR>—1 A Jaina, a follower of Jaina doctrines.<BR>—2 A Buddha.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनिः|जैमिनि
जैमिनिः N. of a celebrated sage and philosopher, founder of the Mīmāṃsā<BR> school of philosophy (properly पूर्वमीमांसा); मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ<BR> सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनिम् Pt. 2. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: जैमिनिभागवतम्, जैमिनिभारतम्, जैमिनिसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनिभागवतम्
