जैव
जैव <i>a.</i> [जीवस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to जीव or the soul.<BR>—2 Belonging to Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Long-lived, one for whom long life is desired; जैवातृक ननु श्रूयते<BR> पतिरस्याः Dk.<BR>—2 Thin, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृकः|जैवातृक
जैवातृक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The moon; राजानं जनयांबभूव सहसा जैवातृक त्वां तु यः Bv. 2. 78.<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>—3 A son.<BR>—4 A drug, medicament.<BR>—5 A peasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवेयः|जैवेय
जैवेयः An epithet of Kacha, son of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्यम्
जैह्म्यम् Crookedness, deceit, falsehood; जैह्म्यं च मैथुनं पुंसि<BR> जातिभ्रंशकरं स्मृतम् Ms. 11. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्व्यम्
जैह्व्यम् The pleasure of taste; औपस्थ्यजैह्व्यं बहु मन्यमानः Bhāg. 7. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गम्
जोङ्गम्, -ङ्गकम्<BR> Aloe-wood, having variegated spots; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गकम्
जोङ्गम्, -ङ्गकम्<BR> Aloe-wood, having variegated spots; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गटः|जोङ्गट|जोंगट|जोंगटः
जोङ्गटः The longings of a pregnant woman (दोहद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोटिङ्गः|जोटिङ्ग|जोटिंग|जोटिंगः
जोटिङ्गः<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 A devotee who practises the most rigid austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोडः|जोड
जोडः Binding, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोनराजः|जोनराज
जोनराजः N. of the author of Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोन्ताला
जोन्ताला, जोन्नाला <i>f.</i> Barley (Mar. जोंधळा; according<BR> to others देवभात ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोन्नाला
जोन्ताला, जोन्नाला <i>f.</i> Barley (Mar. जोंधळा; according<BR> to others देवभात ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषम्
जोषम् <i>ind.</i> [see under जुष्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष्य
जोष्य <i>a.</i> Lovable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषा
जोषा, जोषित् <i>f.</i> A woman; cf. योषा, योषित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषित्
जोषा, जोषित् <i>f.</i> A woman; cf. योषा, योषित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिका
जोषिका<BR>—1 A cluster of young buds.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जौमरम्
जौमरम् Jumaraʼs grammar. ━<i>m.</i> (<i>pl.</i>) the followers of Jumara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
ज्ञा €9 U. (जानाति, जानीते, जज्ञौ, जज्ञे, अज्ञासीत्-अज्ञास्त, ज्ञातुम्, ज्ञात)<BR>—1 To know (in all senses), to learn, become acquainted with; मा ज्ञासीस्त्वं<BR> सुखी रामो यदकाषींत् स रक्षसाम् Bk. 15. 9.<BR>—2 To know, be aware of, be familiar or conversant with; जाने तपसो<BR> वीर्यम् Ś. 3. 1; जानन्नपि हि मेधावी जडवल्लोक आचरेत् Ms. 2. 110, 123, 7. 148.<BR>—3 To find out, ascertain, investigate; ज्ञायतां कः कः कार्याथींति Mk. 9.<BR>—4 To comprehend, apprehend, understand, feel, experience; as in दुःखज्ञ, सुखज्ञ &c.<BR>—5 To test, try, know the true character of; आपत्सु मित्रं जानीयात्<BR> H. 1. 72; Cāṇ. 21.<BR>—6 To recognise; न त्वं दृष्ट्वा न पुनरलकां ज्ञास्यसे कामचारिन् Me. 63.<BR>—7 To regard, consider, know to be; जानामि त्वां प्रकृतिपुरुषं कामरूपं<BR> मघोनः Me. 6.<BR>—8 To act, engage in (with gen. of the instrument); सर्पिषो जानीते<BR> Sk. he engages in sacrifice with clarified butter (सर्पिषः = सर्पिषा).<BR>—9 Ved. To acknowledge, approve, allow.<BR>—10 To recognise as oneʼs own, take possession of. ━<i>Caus.</i> (ज्ञापयति, ज्ञपयति)<BR>—1 To announce, inform, make acquainted with, make known, notify.<BR>—2 To request, ask (Ātm.).<BR>—3 To sharpen.<BR>—4 To satisfy.<BR>—5 To praise.<BR>—6 To immolate, kill (as an animal). ━<i>Desid.</i> (जिज्ञासते)<BR>—1 To desire to know, investigate, ascertain; R. 2. 26; Bk. 8. 33, 14. 91.<BR>—2 To conjecture, suppose, guess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ <i>a.</i> [ज्ञा-क] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Knowing, familiar with; कार्यज्ञ, निमित्तज्ञ, शास्त्रज्ञ, सर्वज्ञ &c.<BR>—2 Wise; as in ज्ञंमन्य thinking oneself to be wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञः|ज्ञ
ज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञः@}<BR>—1 A wise and learned man.<BR>—2 The sentient soul.<BR>—3 The planet Mercury.<BR>—4 The planet Mars.<BR>—5 An epithet of Brahmā; cf. ज्ञः प्राज्ञे चन्द्रतनये विषये चात्मगर्वयोः Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्ञशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञशक्तिः|ज्ञशक्ति
ज्ञ + -शक्तिः the intellectual faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञपित|ज्ञपितः
ज्ञपित, ज्ञप्त <i>a.</i> Made known, informed, expounded, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्त|ज्ञप्तः
ज्ञपित, ज्ञप्त <i>a.</i> Made known, informed, expounded, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्तिः|ज्ञप्ति
ज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Understanding.<BR>—2 Intellect.<BR>—3 Promulgating.<BR>—4 Satisfaction.<BR>—5 Sharpening.<BR>—6 Praise.<BR>—7 Immolating, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञंमन्य
ज्ञंमन्य <i>a.</i> Thinking oneself to be wise; निश्चिन्वते हि ज्ञंमन्या<BR> यमेवायोग्यमाग्रहात् Rāj. T. 3. 491.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात|ज्ञातं
ज्ञात <i>a.</i> [ज्ञा-कर्मणि-क्त] Known, ascertained, understood,<BR> learnt, comprehended &c.; आज्ञापय ज्ञातविशेष पुंसां Ku. 3. 3; see ज्ञा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातम्
ज्ञात + .{@-तम्@} Knowledge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्ञातान्वयः, ज्ञातसिद्धान्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातान्वयः|ज्ञातान्वय
ज्ञात + -अन्वयः son of a known family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातसिद्धान्तः|ज्ञातसिद्धान्त|ज्ञातसिद्धांत
ज्ञात + -सिद्धान्तः a man completely versed in any Śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातव्य|ज्ञातव्यं
ज्ञातव्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be known or understood.<BR>—2 Conceivable, comprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिः|ज्ञाति
ज्ञातिः [ज्ञा-क्तिच्]<BR>—1 A paternal relation, a father, brother &c.; agnate relatives collectively.<BR>—2 A kinsman or kindred in general.<BR>—3 A distant kinsman who is not entitled to the oblations offered to deceased ancestors.<BR>—4 A father.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्ञातिकर्मन्, ज्ञातिचेलम्, ज्ञातिप्रायः, ज्ञातिभावः, ज्ञातिभेदः, ज्ञातिविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिकर्मन्|ज्ञातिकर्म्मन्
ज्ञातिः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-कार्यम्@}<BR> the duty of a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिचेलम्
ज्ञातिः + -चेलम् A low-born person; विभिन्नकर्माशयवाक् कुले नो मा ज्ञातिचेलं<BR> भुवि करयचिद् भूत् । Bk. 12. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिप्रायः|ज्ञातिप्राय
ज्ञातिः + -प्रायः A meal for kinsmen (Mar. जातिभोजन); प्रक्षाल्य<BR> हस्तावाचम्य ज्ञातिप्रायं प्रकल्पयेत् Ms. 3. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिभावः|ज्ञातिभाव
ज्ञातिः + -भावः kin, relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिभेदः|ज्ञातिभेद
ज्ञातिः + -भेदः dissension among relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिविद्
ज्ञातिः + -विद् <i>a.</i> one who has or makes near relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातेयम्
ज्ञातेयम् Relationship, an act befitting a relative; ज्ञातेयं कुरु<BR> सौमित्रे भयात् त्रायस्व राघवम् । Bk. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातृ
ज्ञातृ <i>a.</i> [ज्ञा-तृच्] Knowing, intelligent, wise. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A wise man.<BR>—2 An acquaintance. —3 A bail, surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानम्
ज्ञानम् [ज्ञा-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Knowing, understanding, becoming acquainted with, proficiency; सांख्यस्य<BR> योगस्य चज्ञानम् Māl. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Knowledge, learning; तथेन्द्रियाकुलीभावे ज्ञेयं ज्ञानेन शुध्यति<BR> Mb. 12. 204. 2; बुद्धिर्ज्ञानेन शुध्यति Ms. 5. 109; ज्ञाने मौनं क्षमा<BR> शत्रौ R. 1. 22.<BR>—3 Consciousness, cognizance, knowledge; ज्ञानतोऽज्ञानतो वापि Ms. 8. 288<BR> knowingly or unknowingly, consciously or unconsciously.<BR>—4 Sacred knowledge; especially, knowledge derived form meditation on<BR> the higher truths of religion and philosophy which teaches man how to understand<BR> his own nature and how he may be reunited to the Supreme Spirit (opp.<BR> कर्मन्); cf. ज्ञानयोग and कर्मयोग in Bg. 3. 3.<BR>—5 The organ of intelligence, sense, intellect; कच्चिज्ज्ञानानि सर्वाणि<BR> प्रसन्नानि तवाच्युत Mb. 12. 45. 18.<BR>—6 Conscience.<BR>—7 The Supreme spirit.<BR>—8 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—9 The Vedas taken collectively.<BR>—10 Means of knowing; औत्पत्तिकस्तु शब्दस्यार्थेन सम्बन्धस्तस्य ज्ञानम्˚ ।<BR> MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR>—11 An opinion, a view; बलदेवस्य वाक्यं तु मम ज्ञाने न युज्यते Mb. 5. 4. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्ञानाग्निः, ज्ञानानुत्पादः, ज्ञानापोहः, ज्ञानाभ्यासः, ज्ञानात्मन्, ज्ञानेन्द्रियम्, ज्ञानकाण्डम्, ज्ञानकृत, ज्ञानगम्य, ज्ञानघन, ज्ञानचक्षुस्, ज्ञानतत्त्वम्, ज्ञानतपस्, ज्ञानदः, ज्ञानदा, ज्ञानदुर्बल, ज्ञाननिश्चयः, ज्ञाननिष्ठ, ज्ञानपतिः, ज्ञानपूर्व, ज्ञानबोधिनी, ज्ञानमुद्र, ज्ञानमूल, ज्ञानयज्ञः, ज्ञानयोगः, ज्ञानलक्षणम्, ज्ञानलक्षणा, ज्ञानविज्ञानम्, ज्ञानवृद्ध, ज्ञानशास्त्रम्, ज्ञानसाधनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानाग्निः|ज्ञानाग्नि
ज्ञानम् + -अग्निः knowledge-fire; ज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन Bg. 4. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानानुत्पादः|ज्ञानानुत्पाद
ज्ञानम् + -अनुत्पादः ignorance, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानापोहः|ज्ञानापोह
ज्ञानम् + -अपोहः forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानाभ्यासः|ज्ञानाभ्यास
ज्ञानम् + -अभ्यासः<BR>—1 study.<BR>—2 thinking,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">Page0744-2</a>]<BR> reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानात्मन्
ज्ञानम् + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> all-wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानेन्द्रियम्
ज्ञानम् + -इन्द्रियम् an organ of perception; (these are five त्वच्, रसना,<BR> चक्षुस्, कर्ण and घ्राण-the skin, tongue, eye, ear and nose; see<BR> बुद्धीन्द्रिय under इन्द्रिय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानकाण्डम्
ज्ञानम् + -काण्डम् that inner or esoteric portion of Veda which refers to<BR> true spiritual knowledge, or knowledge of the Supreme spirit, as distinguished<BR> from the knowledge of ceremonial rites (opp. कर्मकाण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानकृत
ज्ञानम् + -कृत <i>a.</i> done knowingly or intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानगम्य
ज्ञानम् + -गम्य <i>a.</i> attainable by the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानघन
ज्ञानम् + -घन <i>a.^1</i> pure or mere knowledge; निर्विशेषाय साम्याय नमो<BR> ज्ञानघनाय च Bhāg. 8. 3. 12; तं त्वामहं ज्ञानघनं … कथं … परिभावयामि<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 9. 8. 24.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानचक्षुस्
ज्ञानम् + -चक्षुस् <i>n.</i> the eye of intelligence, the mindʼs eye, intellectual<BR> vision (opp. चर्मचक्षुस्); सर्वं तु समवेक्ष्येदं निखिलं ज्ञानचक्षुषा<BR> Ms. 2. 8, 4. 24. ━(<i>m.</i>) a wise and learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतत्त्वम्
ज्ञानम् + -तत्त्वम् true knowledge, knowledge of God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतपस्
ज्ञानम् + -तपस् <i>n.</i> penance consisting in the acquisition of true knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदः|ज्ञानद
ज्ञानम् + -दः a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदा
ज्ञानम् + -दा an epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदुर्बल
ज्ञानम् + -दुर्बल <i>a.</i> wanting in knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाननिश्चयः|ज्ञाननिश्चय
ज्ञानम् + -निश्चयः certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाननिष्ठ
ज्ञानम् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> intent on acquiring true (spiritual) knowledge;<BR> ज्ञाननिष्ठा द्विजाः केचित् Ms. 3. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपतिः|ज्ञानपति
ज्ञानम् + -पतिः<BR>—1 the Supreme spirit.<BR>—2 a teacher, preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपूर्व|ज्ञानपूर्व्व
ज्ञानम् + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> preceded by knowledge, well-considered; निष्कामं<BR> ज्ञानपूर्वं तु निवृत्तमुपदिश्यते Ms. 12. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानबोधिनी
ज्ञानम् + -बोधिनी <i>f.</i> N. of a Vedāntic treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमुद्र
ज्ञानम् + -मुद्र <i>a.</i> ‘having the impress of wisdom’, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमूल
ज्ञानम् + -मूल <i>a.</i> founded on spiritual knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानयज्ञः|ज्ञानयज्ञ
ज्ञानम् + -यज्ञः a man possessed of true or spiritual knowledge, philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानयोगः|ज्ञानयोग
ज्ञानम् + -योगः contemplation as the principal means of, attaining the<BR> Supreme spirit or acquiring true or spiritual knowledge; ज्ञानयोगेन<BR> सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेण योगिनाम् Bg. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलक्षणम्
ज्ञानम् + -लक्षणम्, -लक्षणा<BR>—1 indication, sign, a means of knowing or inferring.<BR>—2 (in logic) sign or proof of knowledge; subsequent derived from antecedent knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलक्षणा
ज्ञानम् + -लक्षणम्, -लक्षणा<BR>—1 indication, sign, a means of knowing or inferring.<BR>—2 (in logic) sign or proof of knowledge; subsequent derived from antecedent knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानविज्ञानम्
ज्ञानम् + -विज्ञानम्<BR>—1 sacred and miscellaneous knowledge; तत्प्राज्ञेन विनीतेन ज्ञानविज्ञानवेदिना Ms. 18. 41.<BR>—2 the Vedas with the supplementary branches of knowledge, such as medicine, arms &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानवृद्ध
ज्ञानम् + -वृद्ध advanced in knowledge; ज्ञानवृद्धो वयोबालो मृदुवीर्यगुणान्वितः<BR> Rām. 2. 45. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानशास्त्रम्
ज्ञानम् + -शास्त्रम् the science of fortune-telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानसाधनम्
ज्ञानम् + -साधनम्<BR>—1 a means of acquiring true or spiritual knowledge.<BR>—2 an organ of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतः
ज्ञानतः <i>ind.</i> Consciously, knowingly, intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमय|ज्ञानमयः
ज्ञानमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Consisting of knowledge, spiritual; इतरो दहने स्वकर्मणां ववृते<BR> ज्ञानमयेन वह्निना R. 8. 20.<BR>—2 Containing knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमयः|ज्ञानमय
ज्ञानमय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 The Supreme spirit.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिन्
ज्ञानिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ज्ञानमस्त्यस्य इनि] Intelligent, wise. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An astrologer, fortune-teller; यदुवाचाग्निदाहादि स ज्ञानी भावि पृच्छताम् Ks. 19. 77.<BR>—2 A sage, one possessed of spiritual knowledge; आर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थाथीं<BR> ज्ञानी च भरतर्षभ Bg. 7. 16.<BR>—3 Planet mercury; ज्ञानी सर्वज्ञसौम्ययोः । Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानित्वम्
ज्ञानित्वम् Fortune-telling; तेषां च कुहकाभिज्ञो ज्ञानित्वमुपदर्शयन् Ks. 19. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानीयति
ज्ञानीयति Den. P. To wish for knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापक|ज्ञापकः
ज्ञापक <i>a.</i> [ज्ञा-णिच् ल्यु] Making known, teaching, informing, indicating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापकः|ज्ञापक
ज्ञापक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A teacher.<BR>—2 A commander, a master.<BR>—3 A master of requests, an officer of the court of an Indian prince; Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापकम्
ज्ञापक + .{@-कम्@} (In phil.) A significant expression, a suggestive rule or<BR> precept, said of such rules as imply something more than what is actually<BR> expressed by the words of those rules themselves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापनम्
ज्ञापनम् [ज्ञा णिच्-ल्युट्] Making known, informing, teaching, announcing,<BR> indicating; क्षितिभृद्दाक्षिणात्यानां तिर्यक्त्वज्ञापनाय सः Rāj. T. 4. 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापित
ज्ञापित <i>a.</i> Made known, informed, announced, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञीप्सा
ज्ञीप्सा [ज्ञा-सन-भावे अ] The desire of knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञेय|ज्ञेयं
ज्ञेय <i>pot. p.</i> [ज्ञा कर्मणि यत्]<BR>—1 To be investigated, or learnt or understood.<BR>—2 To be regarded as.<BR>—3 Perceptible, cognizable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्मन्
ज्मन् (only loc.) On the earth; अभि क्रत्वेन्द्र भूरध ज्मन् Rv. 7. 21. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या €9 P. (जिनाति)<BR>—1 To overpower, oppress.<BR>—2 To grow old.<BR>—3 Ā. (जीयते) To be oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीत
जीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Oppressed, overpowered.<BR>—2 Become old; also जीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानम्
ज्यानम् Ved. Oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येय
ज्येय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be oppressed.<BR>—2 First, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या<BR>—1 A bow-string; विश्रामं लभतामिदं च शियिलज्याबन्धमस्मद्धनुः<BR> Ś. 2. 6; R. 3. 59, 11. 15, 12. 104.<BR>—2 The chord of an arc.<BR>—3 The earth.<BR>—4 A mother.<BR>—5 Overpowering force or strength.<BR>—6 Excessive demand, importunity.<BR>—7 A kind of wooden stick (शम्या).<BR>—8 The rear of the army; ज्या भूमिमौर्व्योः शम्यायां वाहिन्याः पृष्ठभागके ।<BR> Nm. Hence ˚घातवारणम् A hand-guard used by the archers and ˚घोषः<BR> The twanging of the bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानिः|ज्यानि
ज्यानिः <i>f.</i> [ज्या-नि]<BR>—1 Old age, decay; तस्माद् यद्यपि सर्वज्यानिं जीयत आत्मना चेज्जीवति<BR> प्रधिनागादित्येबाहुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 15; दानज्यानिविषाद … etc. Māl. 9. 33.<BR>—2 Quitting, abandoning.<BR>—3 A river, stream.<BR>—4 Oppression.<BR>—5 Deprivation, loss; Māl. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस्
ज्यायस् <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>; Compar. of प्रशस्य, वृद्ध)<BR>—1 Elder, senior; प्रसवक्रमेण स किल ज्यायान् U. 6.<BR>—2 Superior, more excellent or worthy; Ms. 4. 8, 3. 137; Bg. 3. 1, 8.<BR>—3 Larger, greater.<BR>—4 (In law) One not a minor, <i>i. e.</i> come of age and responsible for<BR> his own action.<BR>—5 Aged, old.<BR>—6 Decayed, worn out.<BR>—7 Better, stronger, preferable; यद्यप्यपूर्वत्वादन्यत्र विधिर्ज्यायान्<BR> अनुवादात् तथाप्यत्रानुवाद एव बहुत्वस्य भवितुमर्हति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायिष्ठ
ज्यायिष्ठ <i>a.</i> (irreg.)<BR>—1 The most excellent.<BR>—2 First, noblest, best; यत्त्वेव राज्ञो ज्यायिष्ठं कार्याणां तद् ब्रवीमि<BR> ते Mb. 12. 152. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठ|ज्येष्ठः
ज्येष्ठ <i>a.</i> (Superl. of प्रशस्य or वृद्ध)<BR>—1 Eldest, most senior.<BR>—2 Most excellent, best.<BR>—3 Pre-eminent, first, chief, highest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठः|ज्येष्ठ
ज्येष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@}<BR>—1 An elder brother; R. 12. 19, 35.<BR>—2 An epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR>—3 Life.<BR>—4 N. a lunar month (= ज्यैष्ठ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठा
ज्येष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठा@}<BR>—1 An eldest sister.<BR>—2 N. of the eighteenth lunar mansion (consisting of the three stars).<BR>—3 The middle finger.<BR>—4 A small house-lizard.<BR>—5 An epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—6 The goddess of misfortune, elder sister of Lakṣmī; ज्येष्ठा च माया<BR> कलहश्च दम्भः Bhāg. 1. 17. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठी
ज्येष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठी@} A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठम्
ज्येष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@}<BR>—1 The most excellent, the first or head.<BR>—2 Tin.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्येष्ठांशः, ज्येष्ठाम्बु, ज्येष्ठाश्रमः, ज्येष्ठकलशः, ज्येष्ठतातः, ज्येष्ठतातिः, ज्येष्ठराज्, ज्येष्ठललिता, ज्येष्ठवर्णः, ज्येष्ठवृत्तिः, ज्येष्ठश्वश्रूः, ज्येष्ठसामन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठांशः|ज्येष्ठांश
ज्येष्ठ + -अंशः<BR>—1 eldest brotherʼs share.<BR>—2 the right of the eldest brother to a larger share of the patrimonial property.<BR>—3 the best share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाम्बु|ज्येष्ठांबु
ज्येष्ठ + -अम्बु <i>n.</i><BR>—1 water in which grain has been washed.<BR>—2 the scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाश्रमः|ज्येष्ठाश्रम
ज्येष्ठ + -आश्रमः<BR>—1 the highest or most excellent order in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> that of a householder; तस्माज्ज्येष्ठाश्रमो गृही Ms. 3. 78.<BR>—2 a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठकलशः|ज्येष्ठकलश
ज्येष्ठ + -कलशः N. of Bilhaṇaʼs father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठतातः|ज्येष्ठतात
ज्येष्ठ + -तातः a fatherʼs eldest brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठतातिः|ज्येष्ठताति
ज्येष्ठ + -तातिः <i>f.</i> Ved. superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठराज्
ज्येष्ठ + -राज् <i>m.</i> a Sovereign; ज्येष्ठराजं ब्रह्मणां ब्रह्मणस्पते Rv. 2. 23. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठललिता
ज्येष्ठ + -ललिता A particular vow to be observed in the month of Jyeṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवर्णः|ज्येष्ठवर्ण
ज्येष्ठ + -वर्णः<BR>—1 the highest caste (that of Brāhmaṇas).<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवृत्तिः|ज्येष्ठवृत्ति
ज्येष्ठ + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> the duties of seniority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठश्वश्रूः
ज्येष्ठ + -श्वश्रूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a wifeʼs eldest sister.<BR>—2 the eldest mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठसामन्
ज्येष्ठ + -सामन् <i>n.</i> N. of a particular Sāman; ब्रह्मदेयात्मसंतानो<BR> ज्येष्ठसामग एव च Ms. 3. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूल
ज्येष्ठामूल, -मूलीयः<BR> The month ज्यैष्ठ q. v.; ततो मध्याह्नमारूढे ज्येष्ठामूले<BR> दिवाकरे Mb. 13. 95. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूलीयः|ज्येष्ठामूलीय
ज्येष्ठामूल, -मूलीयः<BR> The month ज्यैष्ठ q. v.; ततो मध्याह्नमारूढे ज्येष्ठामूले<BR> दिवाकरे Mb. 13. 95. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठः|ज्यैष्ठ
ज्यैष्ठः N. of a lunar month in which the full moon stands in the<BR> constellation {@ज्येष्ठा@} (corresponding to May-June).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठी
ज्यैष्ठः + .{@-ष्ठी@}<BR>—1 The full-moon day in the month of ज्यैष्ठ.<BR>—2 A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठिनेय
ज्यैष्ठिनेय <i>a.</i> Born from the eldest or principal wife; कृते<BR> कनिष्ठिनेयस्य ज्यैष्ठिनेयं विवासितम् Bk. 5. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ्यम्
ज्यैष्ठ्यम्<BR>—1 Precedence, priority of birth, primogeniture, seniority.<BR>—2 Pre-eminence, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यु
ज्यु €1 Ā. (ज्यवते) To go near, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युत्
ज्युत् €1 U. (ज्योतति-ते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युतिः|ज्युति
ज्युतिः <i>f.</i> Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यो
ज्यो €1 Ā. (ज्यवते)<BR>—1 To advise, instruct.<BR>—2 To observe any religious obligation (such as a vow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योक्
ज्योक् <i>ind.</i> Long, for a long time; ज्योक् च सूर्यं दृशे Rv. 1. 23. 21;<BR> ज्योग्जीवति Ch. Up. 2. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योग्जीवनम्
ज्योग्जीवनम् A longer life; स्वरवर्णप्रसादादिदर्शनादेव ज्योग्जीवनमप्यनुमास्यते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस् <i>n.</i> [द्युत्-इसुन् आदेर्दस्य जः. ज्युत्-इसुन् वा]<BR>—1 Light, lustre, brightness, flash; ज्योतिरेकं जगाम Ś. 5. 30;<BR> R. 2. 75; Me. 5.<BR>—2 Light of Brahman, light regarded as the Supreme spirit; Bg. 5. 24, 13. 17;<BR> अथ यदतः परो दिवो ज्योतिदींप्यते Ch. Up. 3. 13. 7; U. 4. 18.<BR>—3 Lightning.<BR>—4 A heavenly body.<BR>—5 A heavenly body, a luminary (planet, star &c.); ज्योतिर्भिरुद्यद्भिरिव<BR> त्रियामा Ku. 7. 21; Bg. 10. 21; H. 1. 21; Ku. 2. 19; Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—6 Brightness of the sky, day-light (opp. तमस्).<BR>—7 The sun and moon (dual).<BR>—8 Light as the divine principle of life, intelligence.<BR>—9 The science of the course of heavenly bodies; astronomy. See ज्योतिष.<BR>—10 The faculty of seeing.<BR>—11 The celestial world.<BR>—12 A Cow; ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 Fire; ज्योतिष्कल्पोरुकेशरः (मारुतिः) Bk. 9. 60.<BR>—8 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्योतिरिङ्गः, ज्योतिरिङ्गणः, ज्योतिष्कणः, ज्योतिर्गणः, ज्योतिश्चक्रम्, ज्योतिर्ज्ञः, ज्योतिर्मण्डलम्, ज्योतिर्मिलिन्, ज्योतीरथः, ज्योतिर्लोकः, ज्योतिर्विद्, ज्योतिर्विद्या, ज्योतिःशास्त्रम्, ज्योतिःस्तोमः, ज्योतिर्हस्ता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिरिङ्गः|ज्योतिरिङ्ग|ज्योतिरिंग
ज्योतिस् + -इङ्गः, -इङ्गणः the fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिरिङ्गणः|ज्योतिरिङ्गण|ज्योतिरिंगण
ज्योतिस् + -इङ्गः, -इङ्गणः the fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कणः|ज्योतिष्कण
ज्योतिस् + -कणः a spark of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्गणः|ज्योतिर्गण
ज्योतिस् + -गणः the heavenly bodies collectively;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिश्चक्रम्
ज्योतिस् + -चक्रम् the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्ज्ञः|ज्योतिर्ज्ञ
ज्योतिस् + -ज्ञः an astronomer or astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्मण्डलम्
ज्योतिस् + -मण्डलम् the stellar sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्मिलिन्
ज्योतिस् + -मिलिन् <i>m.</i>,<BR> {@-वी(बी)जम्@} a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतीरथः|ज्योतीरथ
ज्योतिस् + -रथः (ज्योतीरथः) the polar star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्लोकः|ज्योतिर्लोक
ज्योतिस् + -लोकः the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्
ज्योतिस् + -विद् <i>m.</i> an astronomer or astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्या
ज्योतिस् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् (ज्योतिःशास्त्रम्) astronomy or astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिःशास्त्रम्
ज्योतिस् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् (ज्योतिःशास्त्रम्) astronomy or astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिःस्तोमः
ज्योतिस् + -स्तोमः (ज्योतिष्टोमः) a Soma sacrifice considered as the<BR> type of a whole class of sacrificial ceremonies. {@ज्योतिष्टोमः@} A<BR> kind of soma sacrifice requiring sixteen priests for its performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्हस्ता
ज्योतिस् + -हस्ता N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्मय
ज्योतिर्मय <i>a.</i> Consisting of stars, starry; R. 15. 59; ऋषीञ्ज्योतिर्मयान्<BR> सप्त सस्मार स्मरशासनः Ku. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं|ज्योतिषः
ज्योतिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ज्योतिः सूर्यादिगत्यादिकं प्रतिपाद्यतया ऽस्त्यस्य<BR> अच्] —1 Astronomical or astrological.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषः|ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं
ज्योतिष + .{@-षः@} An astronomer or astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषम्
ज्योतिष + .{@-षम्@}<BR>—1 Astronomy, astrology, the science of the course of the heavenly bodies<BR> and divisions of time resting thereon; कलामात्राविशेषज्ञाञ् ज्योतिषे<BR> च परं गतान् Rām. 7. 94. 7.<BR>—2 One of the six Vedāṅgas (being a short tract on astronomy).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्योतिषविद्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषविद्या
ज्योतिष + -विद्या astronomical or astrological science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषिकः|ज्योतिषिक
ज्योतिषिकः One who studies or knows astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषी
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः A planet, star, luminary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कः|ज्योतिष्क
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः A planet, star, luminary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कम्
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः + .{@-ष्कम्@} N. of the shining peak of Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कः|ज्योतिष्क
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः + .{@-ष्कः@} The चित्रक tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्मत्|ज्योतिष्मन्त्
ज्योतिष्मत् <i>a.</i> [ज्योतिरस्त्यस्य मतुप्]<BR>—1 Luminous, bright, shining, possessed of luminous bodies; नक्षत्रताराग्रहसङ्कुलापि<BR> ज्योतिष्मती चन्द्रमसैव रात्रिः R. 6. 22.<BR>—2 Celestial. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 N. of the third foot of Brahmā.<BR>—3 N. of one of the seven suns appearing at the destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्मती
ज्योतिष्मत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 The night (as illuminated by the stars).<BR>—2 (In phil.) A state of mind pervaded by सत्त्वगुण <i>i. e.</i> a tranquil state of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्ना
ज्योत्स्ना [ज्योतिरस्त्यस्यां ज्योतिष उपधालोपो नश्च प्रत्ययः P. V. 2. 114. Sk.]<BR>—1 Moonlight; स्फुरत्स्फारज्योत्स्नाधवलिततले क्वापि पुलिने Bh. 3. 42;<BR> ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति प्रदोषान्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-2" target="_blank">Page0746-2</a>]<BR> R. 6. 34.<BR>—2 Light (in general).<BR>—3 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—4 A moonlight-night.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ज्योत्स्नेशः, ज्योत्स्नाप्रियः, ज्योत्स्नावृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नेशः|ज्योत्स्नेश
ज्योत्स्ना + -ईशः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0746-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

