तण्डुलः + -उत्थम्, -उदकम् rice-gruel.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">Page0754-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलौघः|तण्डुलौघ
तण्डुलः + -ओघः<BR>—1 a prickly sort of bamboo.<BR>—2 a heap of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलकणः|तण्डुलकण
तण्डुलः + -कणः a rice-grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलकण्डनम्
तण्डुलः + -कण्डनम् bran.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलफला
तण्डुलः + -फला long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत See under तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम|ततमः
ततम <i>a.</i> That one (of many).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततर|ततरः
ततर <i>a.</i> That one (of two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्
ततस् (ततः) <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From that (person or place &c.), thence; न च निम्नादिव हृदयं<BR> निवर्तते मे ततो हृदयम् Ś. 3. 2 (v. l.); Māl. 2. 10; Ms. 6. 7, 12. 85.<BR>—2 There, thither.<BR>—3 Then, thereupon, afterwards; ततः कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 110;<BR> Amaru. 69; Ki. 1. 27; Ms. 2. 93, 7. 59.<BR>—4 Therefore, consequently, for that reason.<BR>—5 Then, in that case (as a corr. of यदि); यदि गृहीतमिदं ततः<BR> किम् K. 120; अमोच्यमश्वं यदि मन्यसे प्र भो ततः समाप्ते &c. R. 3. 65.<BR>—6 Beyond that (in place), further, further more, moreover; ततः परतो<BR> निर्मानुषमरण्यम् K. 121.<BR>—7 Than that, other than that; यं लब्ध्वा चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं<BR> ततः Bg. 6. 22, 2. 36.<BR>—8 Sometimes used for the ablative forms of तद् such as तस्माद्तस्याः;<BR> ततोऽन्यत्रापि दृश्यते Sk.; यतः━ततः means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) where━there; यतः कृष्णस्ततः सर्वे यतः कृष्णस्ततो जयः<BR> Mb.; Ms. 7. 188.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) since━therefore; यतो यतः━ततस्ततः wherever-there;<BR> यतोयतः षट्चरणोऽभिवर्तते ततस्ततः प्रेरितवामलोचना Ś. 1. 23<BR> (v. l.). ततः किम् ‘what then’, ‘of what use is it’, ‘what avails it’<BR>; प्राप्ताः श्रियः सकलकामदुघास्ततः किम् Bh. 3. 73, 74; Śānti. 4. 2.<BR> ततस्ततः<BR>——(<i>a</i>) ‘here and there’, ‘to and fro’; ततो दिव्यानि माल्यानि प्रादुरासंस्ततस्ततः Mb.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) ‘what next’, ‘what further’, well proceed (occurring in dramas);<BR> ततः प्रभृति thenceforward, (corr. of यतः प्रभृति); तृष्णा<BR> ततः प्रभृति मे द्विगुणत्वमेति Amaru. (after 56, प्रक्षेपक श्लोकः);<BR> Ms. 9. 68. Some other compounds−<BR>.-ततः कथम् but how is it then that.<BR>.-ततः क्षणम्, -क्षणात् immediately afterwards.<BR>.-ततः पर beyond that.<BR>.-ततः परम् <i>ind.</i> besides that, further.<BR>.-ततस्ततः (in drama) what then ?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्त्य|ततस्त्यं
ततस्त्य <i>a.</i> Coming or proceeding from thence; निशम्य सिद्धिं<BR> द्विषतामपाकृतीस्ततस्ततस्त्या विनियन्तुमक्षमा Ki. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततामहः|ततामह
ततामहः A grandfather (पितामहः); Bhāg. 6. 9. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति <i>pron. a.</i> (Declined only in plural, nom. and acc. तति)<BR> So many; <i>e. g.</i> तति पुरुषाः सन्ति &c. (for other senses see the<BR> word under तन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिथ
ततिथ <i>a.</i> (Correlative of यतिथ) That one of a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततुरि|ततुरिः
ततुरि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Preserving, cherishing.<BR>—2 Conquering; ददथुर्मित्रावरुणा ततुरिम् Rv. 4. 39. 2. —3 Killing, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततुरिः|ततुरि
ततुरि + .{@-रिः@} An epithet of Agni and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्प्रख्यन्यायः
तत्प्रख्यन्यायः A मीमांसा rule of interpretation according to<BR> which an expression is to be considered as नामधेय (name of the याग)<BR> if the गुण implied or stated by that expression is found to be stated by another<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">Page0755-1</a>]<BR> statement. This rule is discussed by जैमिनि and शबर at MS. I. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वम्
तत्त्वम् (Sometimes written as तत्वम्)<BR>—1 True state or condition, fact; वयं तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हतास्त्वं<BR> खलु कृती Ś. 1. 23.<BR>—2 Truth, reality; न तु मामभिजानन्ति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवन्ति ते Bg. 9. 24.<BR>—3 True or essential nature; संन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम्<BR> Bg. 18. 1, 3. 28; Ms. 1. 3, 3. 96, 5. 42.<BR>—4 The real nature of the human soul or the material world as being identical<BR> with the Supreme Spirit pervading the universe.<BR>—5 A true or first principle.<BR>—6 An element, a primary substance; तत्त्वान्यबुद्धाः प्रतनूनि येन,<BR> ध्यानं नृपस्तच्छिवमित्यवादीत् Bk. 1. 18.<BR>—7 The mind.<BR>—8 Sum and substance.<BR>—9 Slow time in music.<BR>—10 An element or elementary property.<BR>—11 The Supreme Being.<BR>—12 A kind of dance.<BR>—13 The three qualities or constituents of every thing in nature (सत्त्व,<BR> रजस् and तमस्).<BR>—14 The body; तत्त्वाभेदेन यच्छास्त्रं तत्कार्यं नान्यथाविधम् Mb. 12. 267. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तत्त्वाभियोगः, तत्त्वाभ्यासः, तत्त्वार्थः, तत्त्वज्ञ, तत्त्वविद्, तत्त्वज्ञानम्, तत्त्वदर्शिन्, तत्त्वदृश्, तत्त्वनिकषग्रावन्, तत्त्वन्यासः, तत्त्वभावः, तत्त्वशुद्धिः, तत्त्वसंख्यानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वाभियोगः|तत्त्वाभियोग
तत्त्वम् + -अभियोगः a positive charge or declaration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वाभ्यासः
तत्त्वम् + -अभ्यासः The study of the reality; एवं तत्त्वाभ्यासात् Sāṅ. K. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वार्थः|तत्त्वार्थ
तत्त्वम् + -अर्थः truth, reality, the exact truth, real nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वज्ञ|तत्त्वज्ञः
तत्त्वम् + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 a philosopher.<BR>—2 knowing the true nature of Brahman.<BR>—3 knowing the true nature of anything; Ms. 12. 102.<BR>—4 acquainted with the true principles of science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वज्ञः|तत्त्वज्ञ
तत्त्वम् + -ज्ञ, -विद् + .({@-ज्ञः@}) a Brāmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वविद्
तत्त्वम् + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 a philosopher.<BR>—2 knowing the true nature of Brahman.<BR>—3 knowing the true nature of anything; Ms. 12. 102.<BR>—4 acquainted with the true principles of science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वज्ञानम्
तत्त्वम् + -ज्ञानम्<BR>—1 knowledge of the truth.<BR>—2 a thorough knowledge of the principles of a science.<BR>—3 philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वदर्शिन्
तत्त्वम् + -दर्शिन्, -दृश् perceiving truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वदृश्
तत्त्वम् + -दर्शिन्, -दृश् perceiving truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वनिकषग्रावन्
तत्त्वम् + -निकषग्रावन् <i>m.</i> the touch-stone of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वन्यासः|तत्त्वन्यास
तत्त्वम् + -न्यासः N. of a ceremony performed in honour of Viṣṇu consisting<BR> in the application of mystical letters or other marks to different parts<BR> of the body while certain prayers are repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वभावः|तत्त्वभाव
तत्त्वम् + -भावः true being or nature; Kaṭh. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वशुद्धिः|तत्त्वशुद्धि
तत्त्वम् + -शुद्धिः ascertainment of truth; Ks. 75. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वसंख्यानम्
तत्त्वम् + -संख्यानम् Sāṅkhya philosophy; तत्त्वसंख्यानविज्ञप्त्यै जातं<BR> विद्वानजः स्वराट् Bhāg. 3. 24. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वतः
तत्त्वतः, -तत्त्वेन <i>ind.</i><BR> Truly, really, accurately; तत्त्वत एनामुपलप्स्ये<BR> Ś. 1; Ms. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वेन
तत्त्वतः, -तत्त्वेन <i>ind.</i><BR> Truly, really, accurately; तत्त्वत एनामुपलप्स्ये<BR> Ś. 1; Ms. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In that place, there, yonder, thither.<BR>—2 On that occasion, under those circumstances, then, in that case; दातुं<BR> दुहितरं तस्मै रोचयामास तत्र वै Rām. 7. 12. 17.<BR>—3 For that, in that; निरीतयः । यन्मदीयाः प्रजास्तत्र हेतुस्त्वद्ब्रह्मवर्चसम्<BR> R. 1. 63. —4 Often used for the loc. case of तद्; Ms. 2. 112, 3. 60, 4. 186;<BR> Y. 1. 263. तत्रापि ‘even then’, ‘nevertheless’ (corr.<BR> of यद्यपि). तत्र तत्र ‘in various places or cases’ ‘here and there’<BR>, ‘to every place’; अध्यक्षान्विविधान्कुर्यात् तत्र तत्र विपश्चितः Ms. 7. 81.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तत्रचक्षुर्मनस्, तत्रभवत्, तत्रस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रचक्षुर्मनस्
तत्र + -चक्षुर्मनस् <i>a.</i> directing oneʼs eyes and mind on him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रभवत्|तत्रभवन्त्
तत्र + -भवत् <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> his honour, his reverence, revered, respectable,<BR> worthy, a respectful title given in dramas to persons not near the speaker;<BR> (पूज्ये तत्रभवानत्रभवांश्च भगवानपि); आदिष्टोऽस्मि तत्रभवता<BR> काश्यपेन Ś. 4; तत्रभवान् काश्यपः Ś. 1 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रस्थ
तत्र + -स्थ <i>a.</i> standing or being there, belonging to that place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रत्य|तत्रत्यः
तत्रत्य <i>a.</i> (तत्र भवः अव्ययात् त्यप्) Born or produced there,<BR> belonging to that place; जित्वोर्वी कन्यकुब्जादौ तत्रत्यं स न्यवेशयत्<BR> Rāj. T. 1. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा [तद् प्रकारे थाल् विभक्तित्वात्] <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 So, thus, in that manner; तथा मां वञ्चयित्वा Ś. 5; सूतस्तथा<BR> करोति V. 1.<BR>—2 And also, so also, as well as; अनागतविधाता च प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिस्तथा<BR> Pt. 1. 318; R. 3. 21.<BR>—3 True, just so, exactly so; यदात्थ राजन्यकुमार तत्तथा R. 3. 48; Ms. 1. 42.<BR>—4 (In forms of adjuration) As surely as (preceded by यथा); see यथा.<BR> (For some of the meanings of तथा as a correlative of यथा, see<BR> under यथा). तथापि (oft. corr. of यद्यपि) ‘even then’, ‘still’,<BR> ‘yet’, ‘never-the-less’, प्रथितं दुष्यन्तस्य चरितं तथापीदं न लक्षये<BR> Ś. 5; वरं महत्या म्रियते पिपासया तथापि नान्यस्य करोत्युपासनां<BR> Cāt. 2. 6; वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद्गुरुं रघुस्तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत<BR> R. 3. 34, 62. तथेति shows ‘assent’ or ‘promise’; तथेति शेषामिव<BR> भर्तुराज्ञामादाय मूर्ध्ना मदनः प्रतस्थे Ku. 3. 22; R. 1. 92, 3. 67;<BR> Ku. 6. 3; तथेति निष्क्रान्तः (in dramas). तथैव; ‘even so’, ‘just so’<BR>; ‘exactly so’; तथैव च ‘in like manner; तथा च ‘and also’,<BR> ‘and likewise’, ‘in like manner’, ‘so it has been said’; तथा च श्रुतयो<BR> बह्व्यो निगीता निगमेष्वपि Ms. 9. 19; तथाहि ‘for so’, ‘as for instance’,<BR> ‘for this (it has been said)’; तं वेधा विदधे नूनं महाभूतसमाधिना ।<BR> तथाहि सर्वे तस्यासन् परार्थैकफला गुणाः ॥ R. 1. 29; Ś. 1. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तथाकृत, तथागत, तथागुण, तथाभावः, तथाभूत, तथाराजः, तथारूप, तथारूपिन्, तथावादिन्, तथाविध, तथाविधम्, तथाविधान, तथाव्रत, तथाविधेय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाकृत
तथा + -कृत <i>a.</i> thus done, or made; made true; Bṛ. S. 32. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथागत|तथागतः
तथा + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being in such a state or condition; तथागतायां परिहासपूर्वम् R. 6. 82.<BR>—2 of such a quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथागतः|तथागत
तथा + -गत + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 Buddha; काले मितं वाक्यमुदर्कपश्यं तथागतस्येव जनः सुचेताः Śi. 20. 81.<BR>—2 a Jina; स्थिता तथागतमुखे श्रुतिं श्रुतिविदो यथा Śiva B. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथागुण
तथा + -गुण <i>a.</i> endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाभावः|तथाभाव
तथा + -भावः<BR>—1 that state or condition.<BR>—2 reality; Māl. 1. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाभूत
तथा + -भूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of such qualities or nature.<BR>—2 so circumstanced, in that condition; तथाभूतां दृष्ट्वा नृपसदसि<BR> पाञ्चालतनयाम् Ve. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाराजः|तथाराज
तथा + -राजः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथारूप
तथा + -रूप, -रूपिन् <i>a.</i> thus shaped, looking thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथारूपिन्
तथा + -रूप, -रूपिन् <i>a.</i> thus shaped, looking thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथावादिन्
तथा + -वादिन्<BR>—1 telling the exact truth; एवं निराकृतो देवो वैरिणा तथ्यवादिना<BR> Bhāg. 8. 11. 11.<BR>—2 professing to be so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविध
तथा + -विध <i>a.</i> of such a sort, of such qualities or nature; तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु<BR> सः Ku. 5. 82; R. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविधम्
तथा + -विधम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 thus, in this manner.<BR>—2 likewise, equally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविधान
तथा + -विधान, -व्रत <i>a.</i> following this practice; H. 3; Ms. 4. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाव्रत
तथा + -विधान, -व्रत <i>a.</i> following this practice; H. 3; Ms. 4. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविधेय
तथा + -विधेय <i>a.</i> of such a sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथात्वम्
तथात्वम्, -तथाता<BR>—1 Such a state, being so.<BR>—2 True state or nature, truth.<BR>—3 The case being admitted to be as stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाता
तथात्वम्, -तथाता<BR>—1 Such a state, being so.<BR>—2 True state or nature, truth.<BR>—3 The case being admitted to be as stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य <i>a.</i> [तथा साधु यत्] True, real, genuine; प्रियमपि<BR> तथ्यमाह प्रियंवदा Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्यम्
तथ्य + .{@-थ्यम्@} Truth, reality; सा तथ्यमेवाभिहिता भवेन Ku. 3. 63; Ms. 8. 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्येन
तथ्य + .{@-तथ्येन, -तथ्यतः@} <i>ind.</i> According to truth; Ms. 8. 274; इयं<BR> चान्यमते ख्यातिः प्रथते तथ्यतः पुनः Rāj. T. 1. 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्यतः
तथ्य + .{@-तथ्येन, -तथ्यतः@} <i>ind.</i> According to truth; Ms. 8. 274; इयं<BR> चान्यमते ख्यातिः प्रथते तथ्यतः पुनः Rāj. T. 1. 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् <i>pron. a.</i> (Nom. sing. सः <i>m.</i>, सा <i>f.</i>, तत् <i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 That referring to something not present; (तदिति परोक्षे विजानीयात्).<BR>—2 He, she, it; (oft. as corr. of यद्); यस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">Page0756-1</a>]<BR> बुद्धिर्बलं तस्य Pt. 1.<BR>—3 That, <i>i. e.</i> well-known; सा रम्या नगरी महान्स नृपतिः सामन्तचक्रं<BR> च तत् Bh. 3. 37; Ku. 5. 71.<BR>—4 That (referring to something seen or experienced before, अनुभूतार्थः);<BR> उत्कम्पिनी भयपरिस्खलितांशुकान्ता ते लोचने प्रतिदिशं विधुरे क्षिपन्ती<BR> K. P. 7; Bv. 2. 5.<BR>—5 The same, identical, that, very; usually with एव; तानीन्द्रियाणि सकलानि<BR> तदेव नाम Bh. 2. 40. Sometimes the forms of तद् are used with<BR> the first and second personal pronouns, as well as with demonstratives<BR> and relatives, for the sake of emphasis; (often translatable by ‘therefore’,<BR> ‘then’); सोऽहमिज्याविशुद्धात्मा R. 1. 69; ‘I that very person’, ‘I therefore’;<BR> (I who am so and so); स त्वं निवर्तस्व विहाय लज्जाम् 2. 40 ‘thou, therefore, shouldst return’<BR>, &c. When repeated तद् has the sense of<BR> ‘several’, ‘various’; तेषु तेषु स्थानेषु K. 369; Bg. 7. 20; Māl. 1. 36;<BR> ते ते भावाः 1. 17. तेन the instr. of तद् is often used<BR> with adverbial force in the sense of ‘therefore’, ‘on that account’, ‘in that case’<BR>, ‘for that reason’. तेन हि if so, well then. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 There, thither.<BR>—2 Then, in that case, at that time.<BR>—3 For that reason, therefore, consequently; तदेहि विमर्दक्षमां भूमिमवतरावः<BR> U. 5; Me. 7, 109; R. 3. 46.<BR>—4 Then (corr. of यदि); तथापि यदि महत्कुतूहलं तत्कथयामि<BR> K. 136; Bg. 1. 46. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 The Supreme Spirit or Brahman; तद्भावभावी तद्बुद्धिः Mb. 12. 323. 29;<BR> Bg. 17. 23.<BR>—2 This world.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तदतिपात, तदनन्तर, तदनुसरणम्, तदन्त, तदन्य, तदपेक्ष, तदर्थ, तदर्थीय, तदर्थम्, तदर्ह, तदवधि, तदवस्थ, तदेकचित्त, तत्कर, तत्काल, तत्कालम्, तत्कालीन, तत्क्षणः, तत्क्षणम्, तत्क्षणात्, तत्क्रिय, तद्गत, तद्गुण, तज्ज, तज्ज्ञः, तत्तृतीय, तद्देश्य, तद्धन, तद्धर्मिन्, तद्धर्म्य, तत्पदार्थः, तत्पर, तत्परायण, तत्पुरुषः, तत्पूर्व, तत्पूर्वम्, तत्प्रथम, तत्फल, तद्बलः, तद्भव, तद्भावः, तन्मात्रम्, तन्मात्रिक, तद्राजः, तद्रूप, तद्वाचक, तद्विद्, तद्विद्य, तद्विध, तत्संख्याक, तत्समनन्तरम्, तत्स्थ, तद्धित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदतिपात
तद् + -अतिपात <i>a.</i> going beyond the bounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदनन्तर
तद् + -अनन्तर <i>a.</i> next to that. ━(<i>ind.</i>) immediately after that, thereupon.<BR> ━{@अनु@} <i>ind.</i> after that, afterwards; संदेशं मे तदनु जलद<BR> श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयम् Me. 13; R. 16. 87; Māl. 9. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदनुसरणम्
तद् + -अनुसरणम् going after that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदन्त|तदंत
तद् + -अन्त <i>a.</i> perishing in that, ending thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदन्य
तद् + -अन्य <i>a.</i> other than that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदपेक्ष
तद् + -अपेक्ष <i>a.</i> having regard to that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थ
तद् + -अर्थ, -अर्थीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 intended for that.<BR>—2 having that meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थीय
तद् + -अर्थ, -अर्थीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 intended for that.<BR>—2 having that meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थम्
तद् + -अर्थम् on that account, with that object, therefore; स्वस्रीयं<BR> मम राजेन्द्र द्रष्टुकामो महीपतिः । तदर्थमुपयातोऽहमयोध्यां रघुनन्दन ॥<BR> Rām. 1. 73. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्ह
तद् + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> meriting that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदवधि
तद् + -अवधि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 so far; upto that period, till then; तदवधि कुशली पुराणशास्त्रस्मृतिशतचारुविचारजो<BR> विवेकः Bv. 2. 14.<BR>—2 from that time, since then; श्वासो दीर्धस्तदवधि मुखे पाण्डिमा Bv. 2. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदवस्थ
तद् + -अवस्थ <i>a.</i> so circumstanced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदेकचित्त
तद् + -एकचित्त <i>a.</i> having the mind solely fixed on that; H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कर
तद् + -कर <i>a.</i> serving, obeying as servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्काल|तत्कालः
तद् + -काल<BR>—1 the current moment, present time.<BR>—2 that time. ˚धी <i>a.</i> having presence of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कालम्
तद् + -कालम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 instantly, immediately.<BR>—2 at that time, at a certain time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कालीन
तद् + -कालीन <i>a.</i> simultaneous; ब्रह्मन्कालान्तरकृतं तत्कालीनं<BR> कथं भवेत् Bhāg. 10. 12. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्षणः|तत्क्षण
तद् + -क्षणः<BR>—1 present, time being, present or current moment; R. 1. 51.<BR>—2 the same moment. —3 a measure of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्षणम्
तद् + -क्षणम्, -क्षणात् <i>ind.</i> immediately, directly, instantly; सेकान्ते<BR> मुनिकन्याभिस्तत्क्षणोज्झितवृक्षकम् R. 3. 14; Śi. 9. 5; Y. 2. 14; Amaru. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्षणात्
तद् + -क्षणम्, -क्षणात् <i>ind.</i> immediately, directly, instantly; सेकान्ते<BR> मुनिकन्याभिस्तत्क्षणोज्झितवृक्षकम् R. 3. 14; Śi. 9. 5; Y. 2. 14; Amaru. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्रिय|तत्क्रियः
तद् + -क्रिय <i>a.</i> working without wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्गत|तद्गतः
तद् + -गत <i>a.</i> gone or directed to that, intent on that, devoted<BR> to that, belonging to that; तद्गतेनैव चेतसा Ks. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्गतः|तद्गत
तद् + -गत + .({@-तः@}) the continued multiplication of four or more like quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्गुण|तद्गुणः
तद् + -गुण <i>a.</i> possessing those qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्गुणः|तद्गुण
तद् + -गुण + .({@-णः@})<BR>—1 the quality or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">Page0756-2</a>]<BR> virtue of anything; R. 1. 9.<BR>—2 a figure of speech (in Rhet.); स्वमुत्सृज्य गुणं योगादत्युज्ज्वलगुणस्य<BR> यत् । वस्तु तद्गुणतामेति भण्यते स तु तद्गुणः ॥ K. P. 10. 137;<BR> see Candr. 5. 141. ˚संविज्ञानः a term applied to those Bahuvrīhi<BR> compounds in which the qualities denoted by the name are perceived along<BR> with the thing itself; as लंबकर्ण; cf. अतद्गुणसंविज्ञान also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्ज
तद् + -ज <i>a.</i> immediate, instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्ज्ञः|तज्ज्ञ
तद् + -ज्ञः a knowing or intelligent man, wise man, philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्तृतीय
तद् + -तृतीय <i>a.</i> doing that for the third time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्देश्य
तद् + -देश्य <i>a.</i> coming from the same country. {@देश्यः@} a fellow countryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धन|तद्धनः
तद् + -धन <i>a.</i> miserly, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धर्मिन्
तद् + -धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> obeying his laws; तद्धर्मिणां निवसतां विषमः<BR> स्वभावः Bhāg. 3. 15. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धर्म्य
तद् + -धर्म्य <i>a.</i> of that kind; Bhāg. 5. 14. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पदार्थः
तद् + -पदार्थः the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पर|तत्परः
तद् + -पर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 following that, coming after that, inferior.<BR>—2 having that as the highest object, closely intent on, exclusively devoted<BR> to, eagerly engaged in (usually in comp.); सम्राट् समाराधनतत्परोऽभूत्<BR> R. 2. 5, 1. 66; Me. 10; Y. 1. 83; Ms. 3. 262.<BR>—3 diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्परः|तत्पर
तद् + -पर + .({@-रः@}) the thirtieth part of a twinkling of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्परा
तद् + -पर + .({@-रा@}) one sixtieth of a second of a circle. ˚ता, ˚त्वम्<BR>—1 intentness, entire devotion or addiction to a thing.<BR>—2 inferiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्परायण|तत्परायणः
तद् + -परायण <i>a.</i> solely devoted or attached to anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पुरुषः|तत्पुरुष
तद् + -पुरुषः<BR>—1 the original or Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 N. of a class of compounds in which the first member determines the<BR> sense of the other member, or in which the last member is defined or qualified<BR> by the first, without losing its original independence; as तत्पुरुषः;<BR> तत्पुरुष कर्मधारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः Udb. उत्तरपदप्रधानस्तत्पुरुषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पूर्व|तत्पूर्व्व
तद् + -पूर्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 happening or occurring for the first time; अकारि तत्पूर्वनिबद्धया<BR> तया Ku. 5. 10, 7. 30; R. 2. 42, 14. 38.<BR>—2 prior, former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पूर्वम्
तद् + -पूर्वम् <i>ind.</i> that for the first time; Ki. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्प्रथम
तद् + -प्रथम <i>a.</i> doing that for the first time; Ku. 5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्फल|तत्फलः
तद् + -फल <i>a.</i> having that as a fruit or result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्फलः|तत्फल
तद् + -फल + .({@-लः@})<BR>—1 the white water-lily.<BR>—2 a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्बलः|तद्बल
तद् + -बलः a kind of arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्भव
तद् + -भव <i>a.</i> sprung from Sanskṛt &c. (as Prākṛt or other words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्भावः|तद्भाव
तद् + -भावः becoming that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्रम्
तद् + -मात्रम्<BR>—1 merely that, only a trifle, a very small quantity; तन्मात्रादेव कुपितो<BR> राजा Ks. 6. 15.<BR>—2 (in phil.) a subtle and primary element (such as शब्द, स्पर्श, रूप,<BR> रस and गन्ध) तन्मात्राण्यविशेषाः Sāṅ. K. 38; गणस्तन्मात्रपञ्चकश्चैव<BR> Sāṅ. K. 24; Bhāg. 11. 24. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्रिक
तद् + -मात्रिक <i>a.</i> consisting of rudimentary atoms; अर्थस्तन्मात्रिकाज्जज्ञे<BR> Bhāg. 11. 24. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्राजः|तद्राज
तद् + -राजः an affix added to some proper names to form from them the<BR> names of the ‘king’ or ‘chief’; as from अङ्ग is formed आङ्ग ‘king of the Aṅgas’<BR> by the affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्रूप
तद् + -रूप <i>a.</i> thus shaped, so formed; of the same quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वाचक
तद् + -वाचक <i>a.</i> denoting or signifying that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्विद्
तद् + -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing that.<BR>—2 knowing the truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्विद्य
तद् + -विद्य <i>a.</i> a Connoisseur, expert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्विध
तद् + -विध <i>a.</i> of that kind or sort; भक्त्योपपन्नेषु हि तद्विधानां<BR> प्रसादचिह्नानि पुरः फलानि R. 2. 22; Ku. 5. 73; Ms. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्संख्याक
तद् + -संख्याक <i>a.</i> of that number; Y. 2. 6. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्समनन्तरम्
तद् + -समनन्तरम् <i>ind.</i> immediately upon that; Ks. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्स्थ|तत्स्थः
तद् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being on or in that, connected with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">Page0757-1</a>]<BR> it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्स्थः|तत्स्थ
तद् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः@}) a particular mode of multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धित|तद्धितः
तद् + -हित <i>a.</i> good for that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धितः|तद्धित
तद् + -हित + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 an affix added to primary bases to form derivative or secondary bases from them.<BR>—2 a noun formed by a Taddhita affix, a derivative noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदा
तदा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Then, at that time.<BR>—2 Then, in that case; (corr. of यदा); Bg. 2. 52-53; Ms. 1. 52, 54-56;<BR>—3 Therefore, hence; अनुभूय तदा कामं ततः प्राप्स्याम्यहं जराम्<BR> Rām. 7. 50. 3; यदा यदा-तदा तदा ‘whenever’; तदाप्रभृति ‘since then’<BR>, ‘thenceforward’; तदाप्रभृत्येव विमुक्तसङ्गः पतिः पशूनामपरिग्रहोऽभूत् Ku. 1. 53.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तदामुख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदामुख|तदामुखं
तदा + -मुख <i>a.</i> begun, commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदामुखम्
तदा + -मुख + .({@-खम्@}) beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदात्वम्
तदात्वम् The time being, present time; आयत्यां च तदात्वे च Mb. 12. 16. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदादितदन्तन्यायः|तदादितदन्तन्याय
तदादितदन्तन्यायः The rule according to which when an उत्कर्ष<BR> of a detail is laid down what is meant is that one should have उत्कर्ष<BR> not of that particular detail alone but of all the details beginning with<BR> that detail. In the case of अपकर्ष, however, there will be अपकर्ष<BR> not of that particular detail alone, but of all the details ending with<BR> it; तदादि उत्कर्षे तदन्तमपकर्षे गम्येत । ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानीम्
तदानीम् <i>ind.</i> Then, at that time; नासदासीन्नो सदासीत् तदानीम्<BR> Rv. 10. 129. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानींतन
तदानींतन <i>a.</i> Belonging to that time, contemporary of that time;<BR> एषोऽस्मि कार्यवशादायोध्यिकस्तदानींतनश्च संवृत्तः U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीय
तदीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to that, his, hers, its, theirs; सुतां<BR> तदीयां सुरभेः कृत्वा प्रतिनिधिं शुचिः R. 1. 81, 2. 28, 3. 8, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वत्|तद्वन्त्
तद्वत् <i>a.</i> Containing or possessed of that; as in तद्वानपोहः<BR> K. P. 2. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Like that, in that manner.<BR>—2 Equally, in like manner, so also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वथपदेशन्यायः
तद्वथपदेशन्यायः A मीमांसा rule of interpretation according<BR> to which an expression is to be considered as a नामधेय (name of<BR> a याग) if in the sequel is found a statement comparing the याग<BR> with the idea or thing expressed by that term. This rule is discussed<BR> by जैमिनि and शबर at MS. 1. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Made up of that.<BR>—2 Wholly absorbed in that; ज्वलति हृदयमन्तस्तन्मयत्वं च धत्ते<BR> Māl. 1. 41; Ś. 6. 21; M. 2. 9.<BR>—3 Identical with, or become one with that; ततस्तन्मयतां ययौ Rāj. T. 3. 498.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् I. €8 U. (तनोति, तनुते, ततान, तेने, अत(ता)नीत्, तनितुम्,<BR> ततः <i>pass.</i> तन्यते or तायते; <i>desid.</i> तितंसति, तितांसति तितनिषति)<BR>—1 To stretch, extend, lengthen, lengthen out; बाह्वोः सकरयोस्ततयोः Ak.<BR>—2 To spread, shed, diffuse; कूलानि साऽऽमर्षतयेव तेनुः सरोजलक्ष्मीं<BR> स्थलपद्महासैः Bk. 2. 3, 10. 32, 15. 91; Ku. 2. 33.<BR>—3 To cover, fill; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य तताम् Śi. 9. 23; Ki. 5. 11.<BR>—4 To cause, produce, form, give, grant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">Page0757-2</a>]<BR> bestow; त्वयि विमुखे मयि सपदि सुधानिधिरपि तनुते तनुदाहम् Gīt. 4;<BR> पितुर्मुदं तेन ततान सोऽर्भकः R. 3. 25, 7. 7; U. 3. 39; Māl. 9. 43;<BR> यो दुर्जनं वशयितुं तनुते मनीषाम् Bv. 1. 95, 10.<BR>—5 To perform, do, accomplish (as a sacrifice); इति क्षितीशो नवतिं<BR> नवाधिकां महाक्रतूनां महनीयशासनः । समारुरुक्षुर्दिवमायुषः क्षये<BR> ततान सोपानपरंपरामिव ॥ R. 3. 69; Ms. 4. 205.<BR>—6 To compose, write (as a work &c.); as in नाम्रां मालां तनोम्यहम्<BR> or तनुते टीकाम्.<BR>—7 To stretch or bend (as a bow).<BR>—8 To spin out, weave.<BR>—9 To propagate, or be propagated; धमार्थ उत्तमश्लोकं तन्तुं तन्वन्पितॄन्यजेत्<BR> Bhāg. 2. 3. 8.<BR>—10 To continue, last.<BR>—11 To protract, prolong, augment; मुदितस्तं चिरमुत्सवं ततान<BR> Ks. 51. 226; पितुर्मुदं तेन ततान सोऽर्भकः R. 3. 25.<BR>—12 To emboss.<BR>—13 To prepare (a way for); यज्ञैरथर्वा प्रथमः पथस्तते Rv. 1. 83. 5.<BR>—14 To direct oneʼs way towards.<BR>—15 To compose (a literary work). [cf. L. <i>tendo</i>]. ━II. €1 P., €10 U.<BR> (तनति, तानयतिते)<BR>—1 To confide, trust, place confidence in.<BR>—2 To help, assist, aid.<BR>—3 To pain or afflict with disease.<BR>—4 To be harmless.<BR>—5 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत <i>p. p.</i> [तन्-क्त]<BR>—1 Extended, spread; तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य तताम् Śi. 9. 23, 6. 50; Ki. 5. 11.<BR>—2 Spreading or reaching over, extending to.<BR>—3 Covered over, concealed.<BR>—4 Protracted, continued.<BR>—5 Bent (as a bow); ततायुधकलापवान् Mb. 1. 49. 25.<BR>—6 Spreading wide &c.; see तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततः|तत|ततं
तत + .{@-तः@} Ved.<BR>—1 A father; पितरं तत कस्मै मां दास्यसि Kaṭh. 1. 1. 4; Bhāg. 1. 18. 37.<BR>—2 Wind, air.<BR>—3 Extent.<BR>—4 Offspring, a child (<i>n.</i> also).<BR>—5 A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम्
तत + .{@-तम्@} Any stringed musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततत्वम्
ततत्वम् Slow time (in music); protractedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिः|तति
ततिः <i>f.</i> [तन्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 A series, row, line.<BR>—2 A troop, group, multitude; विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः<BR> पल्वले Ś. 2. 6; बलाहकततीः Śi. 4. 54, 1. 5.<BR>—3 A sacrificial act, a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Continuation, diffusion.<BR>—2 Offspring, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनः|तन
तनः Ved. A descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तना
तनः + .{@-ना, -नम्@} Offspring, posterity; आ वो मक्षू तनाय कम् Rv. 1. 39. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनम्
तनः + .{@-ना, -नम्@} Offspring, posterity; आ वो मक्षू तनाय कम् Rv. 1. 39. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयः|तनय
तनयः [तनोति कुलं, तन्-कयन्]<BR>—1 A son; Ms. 3. 16; सुदक्षिणायां तनयं ययाचे R. 2. 64.<BR>—2 A male descendant.<BR>—3 (In astrol.) N. of the fifth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनया
तनयः + .{@-या@} A daughter; Ms. 11. 171. ˚भवनम् The 5th lunar mansion;<BR> Bṛ. S. 104. 27. गिरि˚, कलिन्द˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयौ
तनयः + .{@-यौ@} (dual) A son and a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयम्
तनयः + .{@-यम्@} Posterity, family, offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयीकृत
तनयः + .{@-तनयीकृत@} <i>a.</i> made a son; मातामहस्य यो मात्रा दौहित्रस्तनयीकृतः Rāj. T. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयित्नु
तनयित्नु <i>a.</i> Ved. Roaring, thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनस्
तनस् <i>m.</i> Ved. Offspring, posterity; मा शेषसा मा तनसा Rv. 5. 70. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिका
तनिका A rope for fastening anything; त्रुट्यद्वितानतनिकाव्यतिषङ्गभाजः Śi. 5. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिमन्
तनिमन् <i>m.</i> [तनु-इमनि च्] Thinness, slenderness, minuteness<BR> &c.; नितान्तदीर्घं तनिमानमागताः Vikr. 13. 6. ━<i>n.</i> The liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिष्ठ|तनिष्ठः
तनिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thinnest; least.<BR>—2 Very minute, or delicate (superl. of तनु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनीयस्
तनीयस् <i>a.</i> Thinner, more minute, very thin (compar. of तनु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु <i>a.</i> (-नु, -न्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [तन्-उन्]<BR>—1 Thin, lean, emaciated; वीतप्रभावतनुरप्यतनुप्रभावः Ki. 16. 64.<BR>—2 Delicate, slender, slim (as a limb, as a mark of beauty); तनुवृत्तमध्यः<BR> R. 6. 32; cf. तन्वङ्गी<BR>—3 Fine, delicate (as cloth); स्तनेषु तन्वंशुकमुन्नतस्तना Ṛs. 1. 7.<BR>—4 Small, little, tiny, scanty, few, limited; तनुवाग्विभवोऽपि सन्<BR> R. 1. 9, 3. 2; तनुत्यागो बहुग्रहः H. 2. 89 ‘giving little’ &c.<BR>—5 Trifling, unimportant, little; Amaru. 28.<BR>—6 Shallow (as a river). ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 The body, the person.<BR>—2 Outward form, manifestation; प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः<BR> Ś. 1. 1; M. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Nature, the form or character of anything; तीक्ष्णां तनुं यः प्रथमं<BR> जहाति सोऽनन्त्यमाप्नोत्यभयं प्रजाभ्यः Mb. 12. 245. 26.<BR>—4 Skin. [cf. L. <i>tenuis</i>, Eng. <i>thin</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्वङ्ग, तनूनः, तनुकूपः, तनुगृहम्, तनुस्थानम्, तनुच्छद्, तनुच्छदः, तनुज, तनुजा, तनुत्यज्, तनुत्याग, तनुत्रम्, तनुत्राणम्, तनुदानम्, तनुधी, तनुप्रकाश, तनुबीजः, तनुभवः, तनुभस्त्रा, तनुभृत्, तनुमध्य, तनुरसः, तनुरुह्, तनुलता, तनुवातः, तनुवारम्, तनुव्रणः, तनुसंचारिणी, तनुसरः, तनुह्रदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वङ्ग|तन्वंग
तनु + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> having slender limbs, delicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वङ्गी|तन्वंगी
तनु + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गी@}) a delicate woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनः|तनून
तनु + -ऊनः the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुकूपः|तनुकूप
तनु + -कूपः a pore of the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुगृहम्
तनु + -गृहम्, -स्थानम् The first lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्थानम्
तनु + -गृहम्, -स्थानम् The first lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छद्
तनु + -छद् + ({@-द@})<BR> <i>a.</i> protecting, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छद|तनुच्छदः
तनु + -छद् + ({@-द@})<BR> <i>a.</i> protecting, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छदः|तनुच्छद
तनु + -छदः an armour; ततस्तु द्रुपदानीकं शरैश्छिन्नतनुच्छदम्<BR> Mb. 7. 168. 26; तरुपलाशसवर्णतनुच्छदः R. 9. 51, 12. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुज|तनुजः
तनु + -ज <i>a.</i> born from the body; वाञ्छैव सूचयति पूर्वतरं भविष्यं<BR> पुंसां यदन्यतनुजं त्वशुभं शुभं वा Pt. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुजः|तनुज
तनु + -ज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a son; Bhāg. 5. 9. 6.<BR>—2 the hair on the body; स्निग्धहर्यक्षतनुजश्मश्रुप्रवरमूर्द्धजम्<BR> Rām. 1. 16. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुजा
तनु + -जा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्यज्
तनु + -त्यज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 risking oneʼs life.<BR>—2 giving up oneʼs person, dying; योगेनान्ते तनुत्यजाम् R. 1. 8.<BR>—3 rash, desperate, fool-hardy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्याग
तनु + -त्याग <i>a.</i> spending little, sparing, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्रम्
तनु + -त्रम्, -त्राणम्, an armour; रक्षन् विप्रांस्तनुत्रवान् Bk.; Bhāg. 8. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्राणम्
तनु + -त्रम्, -त्राणम्, an armour; रक्षन् विप्रांस्तनुत्रवान् Bk.; Bhāg. 8. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुदानम्
तनु + -दानम्<BR>—1 offering the body (for sexual intercourse).<BR>—2 <i>a.</i> scanty gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुधी
तनु + -धी <i>a.</i> little-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुप्रकाश
तनु + -प्रकाश <i>a.</i> of dim lustre; तनुप्रकाशेन विचेयतारका; R. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुबीजः|तनुबीज
तनु + -बीजः the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभवः|तनुभव
तनु + -भवः a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभवा
तनु + -भवः + .({@-वा@}) a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभस्त्रा
तनु + -भस्त्रा the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभृत्
तनु + -भृत् <i>m.</i> any being furnished with a body, a living being; particularly<BR> a human being; कल्पं स्थितं तनुभृतां तनुभिस्ततः किम् Bh. 3. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्य
तनु + -मध्य <i>a.</i> having a slender waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्यम्
तनु + -मध्य + .({@-ध्यम्@}) the waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्या
तनु + -मध्य + .({@-ध्या@}) a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरसः|तनुरस
तनु + -रसः perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरुह्
तनु + -रुह् <i>n.</i>, {@-रुहम्@}<BR>—1 the hair of the body.<BR>—2 <i>a.</i> feather; तनुरुहाणि पुरो विजितध्वनेः Śi. 6. 45; Mv. 6. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुलता
तनु + -लता <i>f.</i> a^1 slender body; एणीदृशस्तनुलता तनुते मुदं नः P. R. 2. 19.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवातः|तनुवात
तनु + -वातः a kind of hell; Jain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवारम्
तनु + -वारम् an armour; तनुवारभसो भास्वानधीरोऽविनतोरसा Ki. 15. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुव्रणः|तनुव्रण
तनु + -व्रणः a pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुसंचारिणी|तनुसञ्चारिणी
तनु + -संचारिणी a young woman, a girl ten years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुसरः|तनुसर
तनु + -सरः perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुह्रदः|तनुह्रद
तनु + -ह्रदः the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुक
तनुक <i>a.</i> Thin, small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुता
तनुता Thinness, littleness, waning; बहुलेऽपि गते निशाकरस्तनुतां<BR> दुःखमनङ्ग मोक्ष्यति Ku. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुल|तनुलः
तनुल <i>a.</i> Spread, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्
तनुस् <i>n.</i> The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनू
तनू <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The body, person, self.<BR>—2 A limb, member of the body; तं दृष्ट्वा वृष्णयो हृष्टास्तन्वः प्राणमिवोत्थिताः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 82. 33.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तनूद्भवः, तनूजः, तनूद्भवा, तनूजा, तनूजानिः, तनूजन्मन्, तनूतलम्, तनूतापः, तनूनपम्, तनूनपात्, तनूनप्तृ, तनूरुहम्, तनूह्रदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूद्भवः|तनूद्भव
तनू + -उद्भवः, -जः<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 a feather; अथ भ्रष्टतनूजाङ्गमात्मानं ददृशे खगः Mb. 5. 113. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजः|तनूज
तनू + -उद्भवः, -जः<BR>—1 a son.<BR>—2 a feather; अथ भ्रष्टतनूजाङ्गमात्मानं ददृशे खगः Mb. 5. 113. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूद्भवा
तनू + -उद्भवा, -जा a daughter<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजा
तनू + -उद्भवा, -जा a daughter<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजानिः
तनू + -जानिः, -जन्मन् a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजन्मन्
तनू + -जानिः, -जन्मन् a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूतलम्
तनू + -तलम् a measure of length equal to the arms extended, a fathom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूतापः
तनू + -तापः fatigues or troubles of the body; अगणिततनूतापं तप्त्वा<BR> तपांसि भगीरथः U. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनपम्
तनू + -नपम् clarified, butter, ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनपात्
तनू + -नपात् <i>m.</i> fire; तनूनपाद्धूमवितानमाधिजैः Śi. 1. 62;<BR> अधःकृतस्यापि तनूनपातो नाधः शिखा याति कदाचिदेव H. 2. 66. ━(<i>n.</i>) ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनप्तृ
तनू + -नप्तृ <i>m.</i> wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूरुहम्
तनू + -रुहम्<BR>—1 the hair of the body. ━(<i>m.</i> also); रवितुरङ्गतनूरुहतुल्यतां<BR> दधति यत्र शिरीषरजोरुचः Śi. 6. 22; चन्द्रांशुगौरैश्छुरितं तनूरुहैः Bhāg.<BR>—2 the wing of a bird, a feather; चित्रतनूरुहः (विहङ्गः) Mb. 12. 144. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूरुहः|तनूरुह|तनूरुहं
तनू + -रुहम् + .({@-हः@}) a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूह्रदः|तनूह्रद
तनू + -ह्रदः the anus, the rectum; cf. तनुह्रद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकृ
तनूकृ €8 U. To make thin or fine, diminish, lessen; as in लज्जां<BR> तनूकृत्य; मध्यं तनूकृत्य यदीदमीयं वेधाः N. 7. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकरणम्
तनूकरणम् making thin, attenuation; Yoga S. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वी
तन्वी A delicate or slender woman; इयमधिकमनोज्ञा वल्कलेनापि<BR> तन्वी Ś. 1. 20; तव तन्वि कुचावेतौ नियतं चक्रवर्तिनौ Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तिः|तन्ति|तंतिः
तन्तिः <i>f.</i> [तन्-कर्मणि क्तिच्]<BR>—1 A cord, line, string; सासज्जत शिचस्तन्त्यां महिषी कालयन्त्रिता<BR> Bhāg. 7. 2. 52.<BR>—2 A row, series, (Mar. दावण); वत्सानां न तन्तयस्त इन्द्र<BR> Rv. 6. 24. 4; यथा गावो नसि प्रोतास्तन्त्र्यां बद्धाः स्वदामभिः Bhāg. 1. 13. 42.<BR>—3 Extension, expansion.<BR>—4 A cow.<BR>—5 A weaver.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्तिपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तिपालः|तन्तिपाल|तंतिपाल
तन्तिः + -पालः<BR>—1 a guardian of (the rows of) cows.<BR>—2 N. assumed by Sahadeva when living at the house of Virāṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुः|तन्तु|तंतु|तंतुः
तन्तुः [तन्-तुन्]<BR>—1 A thread, cord, wire, string, line; चिन्तासंततितन्तु Māl. 5. 10; Me. 70.<BR>—2 A cob-web R. 16. 20.<BR>—3 filament; बिसतन्तुगुणस्य कारितम् Ku. 4. 29.<BR>—4 An offspring, issue, race; स्वमाययाऽवृणोद्गर्भं वैराट्याः कुरुतन्तवे<BR> Bhāg. 1. 8. 14; Mb. 6. 43. 98.<BR>—5 A shark.<BR>—6 The Supreme Being; Bhāg. 8. 16. 31.<BR>—7 A snare, fetter (पाश); ते तानावारयिष्यन्ति ऐणेयानिव तन्तुना Mb. 5. 57. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्तुकरणम्, तन्तुकार्यम्, तन्तुकाष्ठम्, तन्तुकीटः, तन्तुकृन्तनम्, तन्तुनागः, तन्तुनिर्यासः, तन्तुनाभः, तन्तुपर्वन्, तन्तुभः, तन्तुवर्धनः, तन्तुवाद्यम्, तन्तुवानम्, तन्तुवापः, तन्तुवायः, तन्तुविग्रहा, तन्तुशाला, तन्तुसंतत, तन्तुसंततिः, तन्तुसारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकरणम्
तन्तुः + -करणम् spinning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकार्यम्
तन्तुः + -कार्यम् a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकाष्ठम्
तन्तुः + -काष्ठम् a piece of wood or brush used by weavers for cleaning threads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकीटः|तन्तुकीट|तंतुकीट
तन्तुः + -कीटः a silk-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकृन्तनम्
तन्तुः + -कृन्तनम् cutting off the propagation of a family; तन्तुकृन्तन<BR> यन्नस्त्वमभद्रमचरः पुनः Bhāg. 6. 5. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनागः|तन्तुनाग|तंतुनाग
तन्तुः + -नागः a (large) shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनिर्यासः|तन्तुनिर्यास|तंतुनिर्यास|तन्तुनिर्य्यास
तन्तुः + -निर्यासः the palmyra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनाभः|तन्तुनाभ|तंतुनाभ
तन्तुः + -नाभः a spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुपर्वन्|तन्तुपर्व्वन्
तन्तुः + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> the anniversary of the day of full-moon in the<BR> month of Srāvaṇa when Kṛṣṇa was invested with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुभः|तन्तुभ|तंतुभ
तन्तुः + -भः<BR>—1 the mustard seed.<BR>—2 a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवर्धनः|तन्तुवर्धन
तन्तुः + -वर्धनः ‘increasing the race’, N. of Viṣṇu, also of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाद्यम्
तन्तुः + -वाद्यम् any stringed musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवानम्
तन्तुः + -वानम् weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवापः|तन्तुवाप|तंतुवाप
तन्तुः + -वापः<BR>—1 a weaver.<BR>—2 a loom.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">Page0759-1</a>]<BR>—3 weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवायः|तन्तुवाय|तंतुवाय
तन्तुः + -वायः<BR>—1 a spider.<BR>—2 a weaver; तन्तुवायो दशपलं दद्यादेकपलाधिकम् Ms. 8. 397; तन्तुवायास्तुन्नवायाः …<BR> Śiva B. 31. 19.<BR>—3 weaving. ˚दण्डः a loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुविग्रहा|तंतुविग्रहा
तन्तुः + -विग्रहा a plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुशाला|तंतुशाला
तन्तुः + -शाला a weaverʼs workshop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसंतत|तन्तुसन्तत|तंतुसंतत|तन्तुसन्ततं
तन्तुः + -संतत <i>a.</i> woven, sewn. ({@तम्@}) woven cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसंततिः|तन्तुसन्तति
तन्तुः + -संततिः <i>f.</i>, {@-संतानः@}<BR> weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसारः|तन्तुसार|तंतुसार
तन्तुः + -सारः the betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकः|तन्तुक|तंतुक|तंतुकः
तन्तुकः<BR>—1 The mustard seed.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) A thread, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकी
तन्तुकः + .{@-की@} A vein or any tubular vessel of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनः|तन्तुन|तंतुनः
तन्तुनः, -णः<BR> A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुणः|तन्तुण|तंतुणः
तन्तुनः, -णः<BR> A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुरम्
तन्तुरम्, -लम्<BR> The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुलम्
तन्तुरम्, -लम्<BR> The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्र्|तंत्र्
तन्त्र् €10 U. (तन्त्रयति-ते, तन्त्रित)<BR>—1 To rule, control, govern; प्रजाः प्रजाः स्वा इव तन्त्रयित्वा Ś. 5. 5.<BR>—2 To perform or go through in order; तेन तन्त्रयतस्तन्त्रं वृत्तिः<BR> स्यात्तत्तदाचरेत् Mb. 12. 215. 21.<BR>—3 To maintain by discipline, keep in order.<BR>—4 (Ā.) To support, maintain (as a family).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रम्
तन्त्रम्<BR>—1 A loom; तदाऽपश्यत् स्त्रियौ तन्त्रे अधिरोप्य सुवेमे पटं वयन्त्यौ Mb. 1. 3. 144.<BR>—2 A thread.<BR>—3 The warp or threads extended lengthwise in a loom; सिरीस्तन्त्रं तन्वते<BR> अप्रजज्ञयः Rv. 10. 71. 9.<BR>—4 Posterity.<BR>—5 An uninterrupted series.<BR>—6 The regular order of ceremonies and rites, system, framework, ritual;<BR> कर्मणां युगपद्भावस्तन्त्रम् Kāty.; अशक्यं हि उत्तरं तन्त्रं<BR> कर्तुम् । ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 57.<BR>—7 Main point; प्रकर्षतन्त्रा हि रणे जयश्रीः Ki. 3. 17.<BR>—8 Principal doctrine, rule, theory, science; विधिनोपचरेद्देवं तन्त्रोक्तेन<BR> च केशवम् Bhāg. 11. 3. 47; जितमनसिजतन्त्रविचारम् Gīt. 2.<BR>—9 Subservience, dependence; as in स्वतन्त्र, परतन्त्र; दैवतन्त्रं<BR> दुःखम् Dk. 5.<BR>—10 A scientific work.<BR>—11 A chapter, section, as of a work; तन्त्रैः पञ्चभिरेतच्चकार सुमनोहरं<BR> शास्त्रम् Pt. 1.<BR>—12 A religious treatise teaching magical and mystical formularies for<BR> the worship of the deities or the attainment of superhuman power; Ks. 23. 63;<BR> Bṛ. S. 16. 19.<BR>—13 The cause of more than one effect.<BR>—14 A spell.<BR>—15 A chief remedy or charm; जानन्ति तन्त्रयुक्तिम् Ms. 2. 1.<BR>—16 A drug, medicament.<BR>—17 An oath, ordeal.<BR>—18 Raiment.<BR>—19 The right way of doing anything.<BR>—20 Royal retinue, train, court.<BR>—21 A realm, country, authority.<BR>—22<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Government, ruling, administration; लोकतन्त्रविधानम् Mb. 3. 162. 1, 13. 63. 5;<BR> लोकतन्त्राधिकारः Ś. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Arrangement or machinery of government; सर्वमेव तन्त्रमाकुलीभूतम् Mu. 1, 2. 1.<BR>—23 An army; पराजिताः फल्गुतन्त्रैः Bhāg. 10. 54. 15.<BR>—24 A heap, multitude.<BR>—25 A house.<BR>—26 Decoration.<BR>—27 Wealth.<BR>—28 Happiness.<BR>—29 Model.<BR>—30 Supporting a family; Mv. 2. 17.<BR>—31 Providing for the security and prosperity of a kingdom; Mb. 1. 103. 26.<BR>—32 A group of acts or subsidiaries common to several प्रधानकर्मs<BR> or things; यत् सकृत्कृतं बहूनामुपकरोति तत् तन्त्रमित्युच्यते । तथा<BR> बहूनां ब्राह्मणानां मध्ये कृतः प्रदीपः ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 1; तन्त्रं<BR> साधारणो धर्मग्रामः । ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">Page0759-2</a>]<BR> (Opp. आवापः)<BR>—33 The order of the world; यतः प्रवर्तते तन्त्रं यत्र च प्रतितिष्ठति<BR> Mb. 14. 20. 14.<BR>—34 A detail (matter or thing) which is subservient to (<i>i. e.</i> serves<BR> the purpose of) several things simultaneously; साधारणं भवेत् तन्त्रम्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्त्रकाष्ठम्, तन्त्रज्ञः, तन्त्रभावः, तन्त्रयुक्तिः, तन्त्रवापः, तन्त्रवापम्, तन्त्रवायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रकाष्ठम्
तन्त्रम् + -काष्ठम् = तन्तुकाष्ठ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रज्ञः
तन्त्रम् + -ज्ञः an expert, scientist; Bhāg. 10. 36. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रभावः
तन्त्रम् + -भावः Simultaneity; यथा एकैकस्य सत्त्वस्य हस्तिनोऽश्वस्य<BR> वा दर्शनमेकैकेन कृत्स्नमभिनिर्वर्त्यते एवमेव सत्रे तन्त्रभावो भवेत् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रयुक्तिः|तन्त्रयुक्ति
तन्त्रम् + -युक्तिः The plan of a treatise; Kau. A. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवापः|तन्त्रवाप|तंत्रवाप
तन्त्रम् + -वापः, -वापम्<BR>—1 weaving.<BR>—2 a loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवापम्
तन्त्रम् + -वापः, -वापम्<BR>—1 weaving.<BR>—2 a loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवायः|तन्त्रवाय|तंत्रवाय
तन्त्रम् + -वायः<BR>—1 a spider.<BR>—2 a weaver; (तन्त्रवापः also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रकः|तन्त्रक|तंत्रक|तन्त्रकं|तंत्रकः
तन्त्रकः A new garment (unbleached cloth); वसानस्तन्त्रकनिभे<BR> सर्वाङ्गीणे तरुत्वचौ Bk. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रणम्
तन्त्रणम् Maintenance of order, discipline, government; न जीवत्यधनः<BR> पापः कुतः पापस्य तन्त्रणम् Mb. 5. 107. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रता|तंत्रता
तन्त्रता<BR>—1 Arranging into a system.<BR>—2 Dependence, subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रा|तंत्रा
तन्त्रा Sleepiness; cf. तन्द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रायिन्|तंत्रायिन्
तन्त्रायिन् <i>m.</i> The sun; तन्त्रायिणे नमो द्यावापृथिवीभ्याम् Vāj. 38. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिन्|तंत्रिन्
तन्त्रिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having threads, made of threads.<BR>—2 Having chords or wires (as a lute).<BR>—3 Having a Tantra, or following one. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A musician.<BR>—2 A soldier. ━<i>n.</i> An act having a group of subsidiaries common with<BR> some other act, a main act (प्रधानकर्म); तन्त्रीणि प्रधानानि ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्त्रिसमवायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिसमवायः
तन्त्रिन् + -समवायः Simultaneity of (several) main acts; तन्त्रिसमवाये<BR> चोदनातः समानानामैकतन्त्र्यम्˚ MS. 12. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिः|तन्त्रि|तंत्रि|तंत्रिः
तन्त्रिः, -न्त्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A string, cord; न लङ्घयेद्वत्सतन्त्रीम् Ms. 4. 38.<BR>—2 A bow-string.<BR>—3 The wire of a lute; इमास्तन्त्रीः सुमधुराः Rām. 7. 93. 13; तन्त्रीमार्द्रां<BR> नयनसलिलैः सारयित्वा कथंचित् Me. 88.<BR>—4 A sinew.<BR>—5 A tail.<BR>—6 A young woman having peculiar qualities.<BR>—7 A lute.<BR>—8 N. of the plant Amṛtā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्त्रिभाण्डम्, तन्त्रिमुखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्री|तंत्री
तन्त्रिः, -न्त्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A string, cord; न लङ्घयेद्वत्सतन्त्रीम् Ms. 4. 38.<BR>—2 A bow-string.<BR>—3 The wire of a lute; इमास्तन्त्रीः सुमधुराः Rām. 7. 93. 13; तन्त्रीमार्द्रां<BR> नयनसलिलैः सारयित्वा कथंचित् Me. 88.<BR>—4 A sinew.<BR>—5 A tail.<BR>—6 A young woman having peculiar qualities.<BR>—7 A lute.<BR>—8 N. of the plant Amṛtā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तन्त्रिभाण्डम्, तन्त्रिमुखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिभाण्डम्
तन्त्रिः + -भाण्डम् the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिमुखः
तन्त्रिः + -मुखः peculiar position of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिल
तन्त्रिल <i>a.</i> Occupied with the affairs of government; त्वं तन्त्रिलः<BR> सेनापती राज्ञः प्रत्ययितः Mk. 6. 16/17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रेण
तन्त्रेण (Instr. used adv.) Simultaneously. (Opp. पर्याण); द्वितीया<BR> च विभक्तिस्तन्त्रेणोभाभ्यां संबध्यते । ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 51; पर्यायेण<BR> क्रियायामेवं दोषः । तन्त्रेण तु क्रियायां भवति क्वचित् संभवः । ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्र|तंद्र
तन्द्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tired, fatigued.<BR>—2 Lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रम्
तन्द्र + .{@-न्द्रम्@} Ved. A series or row; Vāj. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रा|तंद्रा
तन्द्रा<BR>—1 Lassitude, weariness, fatigue, exhaustion.<BR>—2 Sleepiness, sluggishness; तन्द्रालस्यविवर्जनम् Y. 3. 158; Mv. 7. 42;<BR> H. 1. 33; Bhāg. 12. 3. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रालु|तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तन्द्रालु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tired, exhausted.<BR>—2 Sleepy, slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिः|तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तंद्रिः
तन्द्रिः, -न्द्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Sleepiness, drowsiness; विभज्य नक्तंदिवमस्ततन्द्रिणा Ki. 1. 9;<BR> विहाय तन्द्रीं शोकं च Rām. 4. 49. 5.<BR>—2 Exhaustion, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्री|तंद्री
तन्द्रिः, -न्द्री <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Sleepiness, drowsiness; विभज्य नक्तंदिवमस्ततन्द्रिणा Ki. 1. 9;<BR> विहाय तन्द्रीं शोकं च Rām. 4. 49. 5.<BR>—2 Exhaustion, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिका|तंद्रिका
तन्द्रिका Sloth, sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रित|तंद्रित
तन्द्रित <i>a.</i> Lazy; as in अतन्द्रित ‘unremitting’; Ku. 5. 14;<BR> यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः Bg. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिन्|तंद्रिन्
तन्द्रिन् <i>a.</i> Weary, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्युतः
तन्युतः [तन्-युतच्]<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 Night.<BR>—3 Roaring, thundering.<BR>—4 A thunderbolt.<BR>—5 Cloud; तन्यतुर्न वृष्टिं दध्यङ् ह Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय See under तद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
तप् I. €1 P. rarely Ā., €4. P. (तपति, तप्यति; तप्त)<BR>—1 (Intransitively used)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To shine, blaze (as fire or sun); तमस्तपति घर्मांशौ कथमाविर्भविष्यति<BR> Ś. 5. 14; R. 5. 13; U. 6. 14; Bg. 9. 19.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To be hot or warm, give out heat.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To suffer pain; तपति न सा किसलयशयनेन Gīt. 7.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To mortify the body, undergo penance (with तपस्); अगणिततनूतापं<BR> तप्त्वा तपांसि भगीरथः U. 1. 23.<BR>—2 (Transitively used)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To make hot, heat, warm; Bk. 9. 2; पश्यामि त्वां दीप्तहुताशवक्त्रं<BR> स्वतेजसा विश्वमिदं तपन्तम् Bg. 11. 19.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To inflame, burn, consume by heat; तपति तनुगात्रि मदनस्त्वामनिशं<BR> मां पुनर्दहत्येव Ś. 3. 16; अङ्गैरनङ्गतप्तैः 3. 6.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To hurt, injure, damage, spoil; यास्यन् सुतस्तप्यति मां समन्युम्<BR> Bk. 1. 23; Ms. 7. 6.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) To pain, distress.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) mortify the body, undergo penance (with तपस्). ━<i>Pass.</i><BR> (तप्यते) (regarded by some as a root of the 4th conjugation)<BR>—1 To be heated, suffer pain.<BR>—2 To undergo severe penance (oft. with तपस्); शम्बूको नाम वृषलः<BR> पृथिव्यां तप्यते तपः U. 2. 8. ━II. €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i> (तापयति-ते, तापित)<BR>—1 To heat, make warm; गगनं तापितपायितासिलक्ष्मीम् Śi. 20. 75;<BR> न हि तापयितुं शक्यं सागराम्भस्तृणोल्कया H. 1. 83.<BR>—2 To torment, pain, distress; भृशं तापितः कन्दर्पेण Gīt. 11;<BR> Bk. 8. 13. ━<i>With</i> {@निस्@}<BR>—1 to heat.<BR>—2 to purify.<BR>—3 to burnish.<BR>━{@वि@}<BR>—1 to shine (Ātm. like उत्तप् q. v.); रविर्वितपतेऽत्यर्थम् Bk. 8. 14.<BR>—2 to warm, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप <i>a.</i> [तप्-अच्]<BR>—1 Burning, warming, consuming by heat.<BR>—2 Causing pain or trouble, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपः|तप
तप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Heat, fire, warmth.<BR>—2 The sun; तपतपनसहस्रद्योतवद्दुर्निरीक्ष्यम् (तेजः) Rām. Ch. 2. 85.<BR>—3 The hot season; Śi. 1. 66.<BR>—4 Penance, religious austerities.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तपात्ययः, तपान्तः, तपात्मक, तपर्तुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्ययः|तपात्यय
तप + -अत्ययः, -अन्तः the end of the hot season and the beginning of<BR> the rainy season; रविपीतजला तपात्यये पुनरोघेन हि युज्यते नदी<BR> Ku. 4. 44, 5. 23; Ś. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपान्तः|तपान्त|तपांत
तप + -अत्ययः, -अन्तः the end of the hot season and the beginning of<BR> the rainy season; रविपीतजला तपात्यये पुनरोघेन हि युज्यते नदी<BR> Ku. 4. 44, 5. 23; Ś. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्मक
तप + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> practising austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपर्तुः|तपर्तु
तप + -ऋतुः the hot season; तपर्तुपूर्तावपि मेदसां भरा N. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपती
तपती<BR>—1 The river Tāptī.<BR>—2 N. of a daughter of the sun, married to Samvarṇa and mother of Kuru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन <i>a.</i> [तप्-ल्यु]<BR>—1 Warming, heating, burning, shining &c.<BR>—2 Causing distress, paining; ब्रह्मद्विषस्तपनो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">Page0760-2</a>]<BR> मनुमीरसि Rv. 2. 23. 4.<BR>—3 The sun; प्रतापात्तपनो यथा R. 4. 12; ललाटंतपस्तपति तपनः U. 6; Māl. 1.<BR>—4 The hot season.<BR>—5 The sun-stone.<BR>—6 N. of a hell; Ms. 4. 89.<BR>—7 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—8 The Arka plant.<BR>—9 N. of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनम्
तपन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Heat, burning.<BR>—2 Paining, grieving.<BR>—3 Mental agony, anguish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तपनांशुः, तपनकरः, तपनदीधितिः, तपनात्मजः, तपनतनयः, तपनात्मजा, तपनतनया, तपनेष्टम्, तपनोपलः, तपनमणिः, तपनच्छदः, तपनद्युतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनांशुः|तपनांशु
तपन + -अंशुः, -करः, -दीधितिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनकरः|तपनकर
तपन + -अंशुः, -करः, -दीधितिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनदीधितिः
तपन + -अंशुः, -करः, -दीधितिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनात्मजः|तपनात्मज
तपन + -आत्मजः, -तनयः an epithet (1) of Yama. (2) of Karṇa. (3) of Sugrīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनतनयः|तपनतनय
तपन + -आत्मजः, -तनयः an epithet (1) of Yama. (2) of Karṇa. (3) of Sugrīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनात्मजा
तपन + -आत्मजा, -तनया an epithet of the Yamunā and of the Godāvarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनतनया
तपन + -आत्मजा, -तनया an epithet of the Yamunā and of the Godāvarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनेष्टम्
तपन + -इष्टम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनोपलः|तपनोपल
तपन + -उपलः, -मणिः the sun-stone; निर्वाणमनु निर्वाति तपनं तपनोपलः<BR> Rāj. T. 3. 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनमणिः|तपनमणि
तपन + -उपलः, -मणिः the sun-stone; निर्वाणमनु निर्वाति तपनं तपनोपलः<BR> Rāj. T. 3. 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनच्छदः|तपनच्छद
तपन + -च्छदः the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनद्युतिः|तपनद्युति
तपन + -द्युतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the heat of the sun; Śi. 1. 42.<BR>—2 the sun-shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनी
तपनी<BR>—1 The river Godāvarī or the river Tāptī.<BR>—2 Heat; तेजिष्ठया तपनी रक्षसस्तप Rv. 2. 23. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीय|तपनीयं
तपनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be heated.<BR>—2 To be suffered or practised (as a penance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीयम्
तपनीय + .{@-यम्@} Gold; especially gold purified with fire; तपनीयाशोकः<BR> M. 3; तपनीयोपानद्युगलमार्यः प्रसादीकरोतु Mv. 4; असंस्पृशन्तौ<BR> तपनीयपीठम् R. 18. 41; तपनीयोज्ज्वलसङ्गताङ्गदाभ्याम् Bu. C. 5. 50.<BR> (Also तपनीयकम् in this sense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस् <i>n.</i> [तप्-असुन्]<BR>—1 Warmth, heat, fire, light; एकः सूर्यस्तंपसो योनिरेका Mb. 12. 351. 10.<BR>—2 Pain, suffering; न तपः कुतश्चन Rv. 7. 82. 7.<BR>—3 Penance, religious austerity, mortification; तपः किलेदं तदवाप्तिसाधनम् Ku. 5. 64.<BR>—4 Meditation connected with the practice of personal self-denial or bodily<BR> mortification; गिरा वाऽऽशंसामि तपसा ह्यनन्तौ Mb. 1. 3. 57; Bhāg. 12. 11. 24.<BR>—5 Moral virtue, merit.<BR>—6 Special duty or observance (of any particular caste); यत्सप्तान्नानि<BR> मेधया तपसाजनयत्पिता Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 1.<BR>—7 One of the seven worlds; <i>i. e.</i> the region above the world called जनस्.<BR>—8 The month of religious austerities.<BR>—9 A long period of time, Kalpa.<BR>—10 (In astrol.) The ninth lunar mansion.<BR>—11 Chastisement (दण्ड); आयुः शक्तिं च कालं च निर्दिश्य तप<BR> आदिशेत् Mb. 12. 267. 35. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The month of Māgha; तपसि मन्दगभस्तिरभीषुमान् Śi. 6. 63.<BR>—2 An epithet of Agni. ━<i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 The cold season; (शिशिर).<BR>—2 The winter (हेमन्त).<BR>—3 The hot season (ग्रीष्म).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तपोनुभावः, तपोर्थीय, तपोवटः, तपःकर, तपःकरः, तपःकृश, तपःक्लेशः, तपोगच्छः, तपश्चरणम्, तपश्चर्या, तपोधन, तपोनिधिः, तपोनिष्ठ, तपःपतिः, तपःप्रभावः, तपोबलम्, तपोभृत्, तपोमूर्तिः, तपोमूल, तपोयज्ञः, तपोराजः, तपोराशिः, तपोलोकः, तपोवनम्, तपोवासः, तपोविशेषः, तपोवृद्ध, तपःशील, तपःसमाधिः, तपःसुतः, तपःस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनुभावः|तपोनुभाव
तपस् + -अनुभावः the influence of religious penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोर्थीय
तपस् + -अर्थीय <i>a.</i> destined for austerities; तपोर्थीयं ब्राह्मणी<BR> धत्त गर्भम् Mb. 11. 26. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवटः|तपोवट
तपस् + -अवटः the Brahmāvarta country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकर|तपःकरः
तपस् + -कर <i>a.</i> undergoing penance; also तपस्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकरः|तपःकर
तपस् + -करः the mango-fish (Polynemus Risua).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकृश
तपस् + -कृश <i>a.</i> emaciated by austerities<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःक्लेशः|तपःक्लेश
तपस् + -क्लेशः the pain of religious austerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोगच्छः|तपोगच्छ
तपस् + -गच्छः (also तपागच्छः) the 6th गच्छ of the Śvetāmbara Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपश्चरणम्
तपस् + -चरणम्, -चर्या the practice of penance. {@तक्षः, -तङ्कः@}<BR> an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपश्चर्या
तपस् + -चरणम्, -चर्या the practice of penance. {@तक्षः, -तङ्कः@}<BR> an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोधन|तपोधनः
तपस् + -धन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 rich in religious penance.<BR>—2 pious, ascetic.<BR>—3 consisting in penance,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोधनः|तपोधन
तपस् + -धन + .({@-नः@}) ‘rich in penance’, an ascetic, devotee; रम्यास्तपोधनाना<BR> क्रियाः Ś. 1. 13; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु 2. 7, 4. 1; Śi. 1. 23;<BR> R. 14. 19; Ms. 11. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनिधिः|तपोनिधि
तपस् + -निधिः an eminently pious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">Page0761-1</a>]<BR> man, an ascetic; R. 1. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनिष्ठ
तपस् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> performing penance; Ms. 3. 134; Y. 1. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःपतिः
तपस् + -पतिः N. of Viṣṇu; Bhāg. 4. 24. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःप्रभावः|तपःप्रभाव
तपस् + -प्रभावः, -बलम् the power acquired by religious austerities;<BR> efficacy or potency of devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोबलम्
तपस् + -प्रभावः, -बलम् the power acquired by religious austerities;<BR> efficacy or potency of devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोभृत्
तपस् + -भृत् <i>a.</i> ascetic, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूर्तिः|तपोमूर्ति|तपोमूर्त्ति
तपस् + -मूर्तिः<BR>—1 an ascetic.<BR>—2 the Supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूल
तपस् + -मूल <i>a.</i> founded on religious austerity; तपोमूलमिदं सर्वं<BR> दैवमानुषकं सुखम् Ms. 11. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोयज्ञः|तपोयज्ञ
तपस् + -यज्ञः sacrificing by austerities; Bg. 4. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोराजः|तपोराज
तपस् + -राजः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोराशिः|तपोराशि
तपस् + -राशिः<BR>—1 an ascetic.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu (पुरुषोत्तम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोलोकः|तपोलोक
तपस् + -लोकः the region above the world called जनस्; Bhāg. 2. 5. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवनम्
तपस् + -वनम् a penance-grove, a sacred grove in which ascetics practise<BR> penance; कृतं त्वयोपवनं तपोवनमिति प्रेक्षे Ś. 1; R. 1. 90, 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवासः|तपोवास
तपस् + -वासः a place of penance or religious austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोविशेषः|तपोविशेष
तपस् + -विशेषः excellence of devotion, pre-eminent religious austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवृद्ध
तपस् + -वृद्ध <i>a.</i> very ascetic or devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःशील
तपस् + -शील <i>a.</i> inclined to practise penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःसमाधिः|तपःसमाधि
तपस् + -समाधिः the practice of penance or religious austerities; तपःसमाधेः<BR> प्रतिकूलवर्ती Ku. 3. 24, 5. 6, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःसुतः|तपःसुत
तपस् + -सुतः N. of Yudhiṣṭhira; Mb. 3. 313. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःस्थली
तपस् + -स्थली<BR>—1 a seat of religious austerity.<BR>—2 N. of Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपसः|तपस
तपसः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
तपस्य <i>a.</i> Produced by heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्यः|तपस्य|तपस्यं
तपस्य + .{@-स्यः@}<BR>—1 The month of Phālguna; Bhāg. 12. 11. 40.<BR>—2 An epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्या
तपस्य + .{@-स्या@} Religious austerity, penance; (also <i>m.</i> and <i>n.</i>); अथास्य<BR> बुद्धिरभवत्तपस्ये भरतर्षभ Mb. 13. 10. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्यति
तपस्यति Den. P. To practise penance; सुरासुरगुरुः सोऽत्र सपत्नीकस्तपस्यति<BR> Ś. 7. 9, 12; R. 13. 41, 15. 49; Bk. 18. 21; स्थाणुं तपस्यन्तमधित्यकायाम् Ku. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्वत्|तपस्वन्त्
तपस्वत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Burning, hot; तपा तपिष्ठ तपसा तपस्वान् Rv. 6. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Ascetic, devout, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विता
तपस्विता<BR>—1 Religious penance.<BR>—2 Piety, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विन्
तपस्विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Practising penance, devout.<BR>—2 Poor, miserable, helpless, pitiable; सा तपस्विनी निर्वृता भवतु<BR> Ś. 4; Māl. 3; N. 1. 135. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An ascetic; तपस्विसामान्यमवेक्षणीया R. 14. 67.<BR>—2 A mendicant, pauper.<BR>—3 An epithet of Nārada.<BR>—4 A sparrow.<BR>—5 A mango-fish; (see तपस्कर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विनी
तपस्विन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 female ascetic.<BR>—2 A poor or wretched woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तपस्विपत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विपत्रः|तपस्विपत्र
तपस्विन् + -पत्रः the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपित|तपितं
तपित <i>a.</i> Heated, burnt &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपिष्णु
तपिष्णु <i>a.</i> Warming, heating, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपु|तपुः
तपु <i>a.</i> Ved. Burning hot; कृष्णाध्वा तपू रण्वश्चिकेत Rv. 2. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुषी
तपुषी The heat of anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुस्
तपुस् <i>a.</i> [तप्-उसि; cf. Uṇ. 2. 116] Burning hot; तपूंषि<BR> तस्मै वृजिनानि सन्तु Rv. 6. 52. 2. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 An enemy; ━<i>n.</i> Heat; नमस्ते हेतये तपुषे च कृण्मः Av. 1. 13. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमय|तपोमयः
तपोमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Consisting in religious penance; एतान्यदर्शन्गुरवः पुराणाः स्वान्येव<BR> तेजांसि तपोमयानि Mv. 1. 42.<BR>—2 Practising penace, devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमयः|तपोमय
तपोमय + .{@-यः@} The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त|तप्तः
तप्त <i>p. p.</i> [तप्-क्त]<BR>—1 Heated, burnt.<BR>—2 Red-hot.<BR>—3 Melted, fused.<BR>—4 Distressed, pained, afflicted,<BR>—5 Practised (as penance).<BR>—6 (in Astr.) Opposed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तम्
तप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} Hot water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तप्तकाञ्चनम्, तप्तकुम्भः, तप्तकूपः, तप्तकृच्छ्रम्, तप्ततप्त, तप्तताम्रम्, तप्तपाषाणकुण्डम्, तप्तमुद्रा, तप्तरूपम्, तप्तरूपकम्, तप्तलोमशः, तप्तलोहम्, तप्तवालुकः, तप्तशूर्मिकुण्डम्, तप्तसुराकुण्डम्, तप्तसूर्मिः, तप्तवालुकाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकाञ्चनम्
तप्त + -काञ्चनम् gold purified with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकुम्भः|तप्तकुम्भ
तप्त + -कुम्भः, -कूपः N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकूपः|तप्तकूप
तप्त + -कुम्भः, -कूपः N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकृच्छ्रम्
तप्त + -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of penance consisting in drinking hot water, milk<BR> and ghee for three days each, and inhaling hot air for three days; Ms. 11. 214;<BR> Y. 3. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्ततप्त
तप्त + -तप्त made hot repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तताम्रम्
तप्त + -ताम्रम् red hot or melted copper; Bhāg. 6. 9. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तपाषाणकुण्डम्
तप्त + -पाषाणकुण्डम् N. of a hell; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तमुद्रा
तप्त + -मुद्रा Mark of divine weapons stamped on the body by devotees<BR> with heated metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तरूपम्
तप्त + -रूपम्, -रूपकम् purified silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तरूपकम्
तप्त + -रूपम्, -रूपकम् purified silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तलोमशः|तप्तलोमश
तप्त + -लोमशः green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तलोहम्
तप्त + -लोहम्, -वालुकः, -शूर्मिकुण्डम्, -सुराकुण्डम्, -सूर्मिः N. of different hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तवालुकः|तप्तवालुक
तप्त + -लोहम्, -वालुकः, -शूर्मिकुण्डम्, -सुराकुण्डम्, -सूर्मिः N. of different hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तशूर्मिकुण्डम्
तप्त + -लोहम्, -वालुकः, -शूर्मिकुण्डम्, -सुराकुण्डम्, -सूर्मिः N. of different hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तसुराकुण्डम्
तप्त + -लोहम्, -वालुकः, -शूर्मिकुण्डम्, -सुराकुण्डम्, -सूर्मिः N. of different hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तसूर्मिः|तप्तसूर्मि
तप्त + -लोहम्, -वालुकः, -शूर्मिकुण्डम्, -सुराकुण्डम्, -सूर्मिः N. of different hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तवालुकाः
तप्त + -वालुकाः hot gravel; भुङ्क्ष्वैता भूयसी राजन्नर्जितास्तप्तवालुकाः Ks. 72. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापः|ताप
तापः [तप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Heat, glow; अर्कमयूखतापः Ś. 4. 11; M. 2. 13; Ms. 12. 76; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>—2 Torment, pain, affliction, misery, agony; इतरतापशतानि तवेच्छया<BR> वितर तानि सहे चतुरानन Udb.; समस्तापः कामं मनसिजनिदाघप्रसरयोः<BR> Ś. 3. 8; Bh. 1. 16.<BR>—3 Sorrow, distress.<BR>—4 A circle or heap of rays; प्रतिरूपं यथैवाप्सु तापः सूर्यस्य लक्ष्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 253. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापी
तापः + .{@-पी@} The Tāptī river (also Yamunā); Bhāg. 5. 19. 18, 10. 79. 20.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तापत्रयम्, तापहर, तापहरी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्रयम्
तापः + -त्रयम् the three kinds of miseries which human beings have to<BR> suffer in this world <i>i. e.</i> आध्यात्मिक, आधिदैविक and आधिभौतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापहर
तापः + -हर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 removing heat, cooling<BR>—2 consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापहरी
तापः + -हरी A sort of soup of pulse and grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक <i>a.</i> [तप्-ण्वुल्] Heating, burning, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापकः|तापक
तापक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Fever, morbid heat.<BR>—2 A cooking stove or frying pan.<BR>—3 A boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन <i>a.</i> [तप्-णिच् भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Heating, inflaming.<BR>—2 Distressing.<BR>—3 Illuminating; अतप्यत स्माखिललोकतापनम् Bhāg. 2. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनः|तापन
तापन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The hot season.<BR>—3 The sun-stone.<BR>—4 N. of one of the arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनम्
तापन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Burning.<BR>—2 Distressing.<BR>—3 Chastising.<BR>—4 A division of hell.<BR>—5 Gold.<BR>—6 (in drama) Helplessness, perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापना
तापन + .{@-ना@} Austerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनी
तापन + .{@-नी@} N. of several Upaniṣads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय <i>a.</i> Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीयम्
तापनीय + .{@-यम्@} Gold of the weight of a निष्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापयान
तापयान <i>a.</i> Warming, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापित
तापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Warmed Heated; Bṛ. S. 54. 115.<BR>—2 Distressed, pained; नातितृप्यति मे चित्तं सुचिरं तापतापितम् Bhāg. 8. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिन्
तापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Suffering from a disease (moral or physical.).<BR>—2 Heating.<BR>—3 Hot.<BR>—4 Causing pain, exciting; Ki. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप्यम्
ताप्यम् Sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्
तम् €4 P. (ताम्यति, तान्त)<BR>—1 To choke, be suffocated.<BR>—2 To be exhausted or fatigued; ललितशिरीषपुष्पहननैरपि ताम्यति<BR> यत् Māl. 5. 31.<BR>—3 To be distressed (in body or mind), be uneasy or pained, pine, waste<BR> away; प्रविशति मुहुः कुञ्जं गुञ्जन्मुहुर्बहु ताम्यति Gīt. 5; गाढोत्कण्ठा<BR> ललितलुलितैरङ्गकैस्ताम्यतीति Māl. 1. 15, 9. 33; तृष्णे मुधा ताम्यसि Mu. 3. 1;<BR> नार्यो मुग्धशठा हरन्ति रमणं तिष्ठन्ति नो वारितास्तत्किं ताम्यसि … Amaru. 8.<BR>—4 To stop, become immovable; Rāj. T. 5. 345.<BR>—5 To wish, desire. ━<i>Caus.</i> (तमयति) To suffocate, choke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमम्
तमम् Darkness.<BR>—2 The tip of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमः|तम|तमं
तमम् + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>—2 The Tamāla tree.<BR>—3 Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमकः|तमक
तमकः A kind of asthma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमका
तमकः + .{@-का@} The plant Phyllanthus Emblica (Mar. भुईआंवळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमत|तमतः
तमत <i>a.</i> [तम्-अतच् Uṇ. 3. 110]<BR>—1 Desirous, longing for.<BR>—2 Wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमनम्
तमनम् Becoming suffocated or breathless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त|तांत|तान्तः
तान्त <i>p. p.</i> [तम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Wearied, languid, fatigued; सविलासरतान्ततान्तमूर्वोर्विवरे कान्तमिवाभिनीय<BR> शिश्ये Bu. C. 5. 56.<BR>—2 Troubled, afflicted. —3 Faded, withered; मृदुलतान्तलता तमलोकयत्<BR> Śi.; see तम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस् <i>n.</i> [तम्-असुन्]<BR>—1 Darkness; किं वाऽभविष्यदरुणस्तमसां विभेत्ता तं चेत्सहस्रकिरणो<BR> धुरि नाकरिष्यत् Ś. 7. 4; V. 1. 7; Me. 39.<BR>—2 The gloom or darkness of hell; धर्मेण हि सहायेन तमस्तरति दुस्तरम् Ms. 4. 242.<BR>—3 Mental darkness, ignorance, illusion, error; मुनिसुताप्रणयस्मृतिरोधिना<BR> मम च मुक्तमिदं तमसा मनः Ś. 6. 8.<BR>—4 (In Sāṅ. phil.) Darkness or ignorance, as one of the three qualities<BR> or constitutents of every thing in nature (the other two being सत्त्व<BR> and रजस्); अन्तर्गतमपास्तं मे रजसोऽपि परं तमः Ku. 6. 60; Ms. 12. 24.<BR>—5 Grief, sorrow; Bhāg. 5. 14. 33.<BR>—6 Sin; Bhāg. 10. 15. 5.<BR>—7 Stupefaction, swoon; तया भिन्नतनुत्राणः प्राविशद्विपुलं तमः<BR> Rām. 7. 8. 14.<BR>—8 Anger; Bhāg. 10. 59. 42. ━<i>m., n.</i> An epithet of Rāhu; तमश्चन्द्रमसीवेदमुपरज्यावभासते<BR> Bhāg. 4. 29. 70.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तमोपह, तमोरिः, तमःकाण्डः, तमःकाण्डम्, तमोगुः, तमोगुणः, तमोघ्नः, तमोज्योतिस्, तमस्ततिः, तमोनिष्ठ, तमोनुद्, तमोनुदः, तमःप्रभा, तमःप्रवेशः, तमोभिद्, तमोमणिः, तमोराजः, तमोविकारः, तमोविशाल, तमोवृत, तमोहन्, तमोहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोपह|तमोपहः
तमस् + -अपह <i>a.</i> removing darkness or ignorance, illumining, enlightening;<BR> आगमादिव तमोपहादितः संभवन्ति मतयो भवच्छिदः Ki. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोपहः|तमोपह
तमस् + -अपह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोरिः|तमोरि
तमस् + -अरिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःकाण्डः
तमस् + -काण्डः, -काण्डम् great or spreading darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःकाण्डम्
तमस् + -काण्डः, -काण्डम् great or spreading darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोगुः|तमोगु
तमस् + -गुः an epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोगुणः|तमोगुण
तमस् + -गुणः see तमस् above (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोघ्नः|तमोघ्न
तमस् + -घ्नः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 Śiva.<BR>—6 Knowledge.<BR>—7 a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोज्योतिस्
तमस् + -ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i> a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्ततिः|तमस्तति
तमस् + -ततिः spreading darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनिष्ठ
तमस् + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> taking to hell (नरकप्रद); Ms. 12. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद्
तमस् + -नुद् <i>m.</i> ‘तमोनुदोऽग्निचन्द्रार्का’ इति विश्वः;<BR>—1 a shining body.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR>—3 the moon; नरेन्द्रकन्यास्तमवाप्य सत्पतिं तमोनुदं दक्षसुता इवाबभुः R. 3. 33.<BR>—4 fire.<BR>—5 a lamp, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुदः|तमोनुद
तमस् + -नुदः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःप्रभा
तमस् + -प्रभा a sort of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःप्रवेशः|तमःप्रवेश
तमस् + -प्रवेशः<BR>—1 groping in the dark.<BR>—2 mental gloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभिद्
तमस् + -भिद्, -मणिः<BR>—1 a fire-fly.<BR>—2 a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">Page0762-2</a>]<BR> sapphire.<BR>—3 a star.<BR>—4 the moon; तमोमणिस्तु खद्योते नीलमण्यामुडौ शशौ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमणिः|तमोमणि
तमस् + -भिद्, -मणिः<BR>—1 a fire-fly.<BR>—2 a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">Page0762-2</a>]<BR> sapphire.<BR>—3 a star.<BR>—4 the moon; तमोमणिस्तु खद्योते नीलमण्यामुडौ शशौ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोराजः
तमस् + -राजः a kind of sugar; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोविकारः|तमोविकार
तमस् + -विकारः sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोविशाल
तमस् + -विशाल <i>a.</i> abounding in gloom; तमोविशालश्च मूलतः सर्गः Sāṅ. K. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोवृत
तमस् + -वृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 obscured, clouded.<BR>—2 affected with anger, fear &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोहन्
तमस् + -हन्, -हर <i>a.</i> dispersing darkness. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोहर|तमोहरः
तमस् + -हन्, -हर <i>a.</i> dispersing darkness. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस <i>a.</i> Dark-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमसः|तमस|तमसं
तमस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 Darkness.<BR>—2 A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमसा
तमस + .{@-सा@} N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमसम्
तमस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Darkness.<BR>—2 A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्क
तमस्क (At the end of a compound)<BR>—1 Darkness; स तेजस्वतो लोकान् भास्वतोऽपहततमस्कानभिसिध्यति Ch. Up. 7. 11. 2.<BR>—2 Mental darkness; तत्प्रत्यनीकानसुरान्सुरप्रियो रजस्तमस्कान्प्रमिणोत्युरुश्रवाः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 7. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्वत्|तमस्वन्त्
तमस्वत् <i>a.</i> Dark, gloomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्वती
तमस्वत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्विनी
तमस्विनी, तमा A night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमा
तमस्विनी, तमा A night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालः|तमाल|तमालं
तमालः —1 N. of a tree with a very dark bark; तरुणतमालनीलबहलोन्नमदम्बुधराः<BR> Māl. 9. 18; R. 13. 15, 49; Gīt. 11.<BR>—2 A sectarial mark of sandal upon the forehead made with the juice of<BR> the Tamāla fruit.<BR>—3 A sword, scimitar.<BR>—4 The bark of the bamboo.<BR>—4 Tobacco.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तमालपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालपत्रम्
तमालः + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 a sectarial mark upon the forehead.<BR>—2 a Tamāla leaf; R. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालकः|तमालक|तमालकं
तमालकः<BR>—1 The Tamāla tree.<BR>—2 The bark of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालिनी
तमालिनी A place over-grown with Tamāla trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमि|तमिः
तमि, -मी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Night, especially a dark night; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य तताम्<BR> Śi. 9. 23; Bhāg. 10. 13. 45.<BR>—2 A swoon, faint.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमी
तमि, -मी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Night, especially a dark night; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य तताम्<BR> Śi. 9. 23; Bhāg. 10. 13. 45.<BR>—2 A swoon, faint.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र <i>a.</i> Dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रम्
तमिस्र + .{@-स्रम्@}<BR>—1 Darkness; एतत्तमालदलनीलतमं तमिस्रम् Gīt. 11; करचरणोरसि<BR> मणिगणभूषणकिरणविभिन्नतमिस्रम् 2; Ki. 5. 2.<BR>—2 Mental darkness, illusion.<BR>—3 Anger, wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रः|तमिस्र|तमिस्रं
तमिस्र + .{@-स्रः@} The dark half of the month.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तमिस्रपक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रपक्षः|तमिस्रपक्ष
तमिस्र + -पक्षः the dark fortnight (of a lunar month); R. 6. 34; तमिस्रपक्षत्रुटिकूटभक्षितम् N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रा
तमिस्रा<BR>—1 A dark night; सूर्ये तपत्यावरणाय दृष्टेः कल्पेत लोकस्य कथं<BR> तमिस्रा R. 5. 13; Śi. 6. 70; Ki. 9. 18; Ku. 6. 43.<BR>—2 Extensive darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमय|तमोमयः
तमोमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Covered with darkness.<BR>—2 Ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमयः|तमोमय
तमोमय + .{@-यः@} N. of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम A Taddhita affix of the superlative degree applied to nouns,<BR> adjectives and also to verbs and indeclinables in which latter case it<BR> is changed to तमाम्; अश्व˚ Pt. 5 ‘the best horse’; सुहृत्तम<BR> Mu. 1; so पचतितमाम्. It is also added to pronouns in the sense of<BR> ‘one of many’ <i>e. g.</i> कतम, यतम, ततम &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्गः|तमङ्ग|तमंगः
तमङ्गः A platform, a stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्गकः|तमङ्गक|तमंगकः
तमङ्गकः The projecting roof of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमरम्
तमरम्<BR>—1 Tin.<BR>—2 Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्पा
तम्पा, तम्बा, तम्बिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बा|तंबा
तम्पा, तम्बा, तम्बिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बिका
तम्पा, तम्बा, तम्बिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय्
तय् €1 Ā. (तयते)<BR>—1 To go, move; अध्युवास रथं तेये पुरात् Bk. 14. 75; धरित्रीं मुसली<BR> तेये प्रहस्तश्चिखिदे न च 14. 108.<BR>—2 To guard, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तयः|तय
तयः<BR>—1 Protection.<BR>—2 A protector; Ki. 15. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर A Taddhita affix of the comparative degree, added to adjectives,<BR> nouns, and also to verbs and indeclinables in which latter case it is<BR> changed to तराम्. It is added, like तम, to pronouns in the sense<BR> of ‘one of two’ <i>e. g.</i> कतर, ततर, यतर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरण्ड, तरि-री, तरीष &c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरण्ड, तरि-री, तरीष &c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0763-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

