तलप्रहारः|तलप्रहार
तलः + -प्रहारः a slap with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलबद्ध
तलः + -बद्ध <i>a.</i> having fastened round oneʼs arm the तल (त्र); Mb. 6. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलयुद्धम्
तलः + -युद्धम् a fight with the palms of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तललोकः|तललोक
तलः + -लोकः nether world (पाताल); Bhāg. 2. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलसारकम्
तलः + -सारकम्<BR>—1 a martingale.<BR>—2 a horseʼs food-receptacle; MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलसारणम्
तलः + -सारणम्, -सारिका <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलसारिका
तलः + -सारणम्, -सारिका <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलहृदयम्
तलः + -हृदयम् the centre of the sole of foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलकम्
तलकम् A large pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलकः|तलक|तलकं
तलकम् + .{@-कः@} A small cart with burning coals (Mar. शेगडी); Hc. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलतः
तलतः <i>ind.</i> From the bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलाची
तलाची A mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिका
तलिका A martingale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
तलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fixed, having a bottom.<BR>—2 Fried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलितम्
तलित + .{@-तम्@} Fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवः|तलव
तलवः A musician (playing with palms on the instrument); Vāj. 30. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवकारः|तलवकार
तलवः + .{@-कारः@} (pl.) N. of a school of the सामवेद. ˚प्राह्मणम्,<BR> ˚उपनिषद् other names for जैमिनीय ब्राह्मण and उपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवारणम्
तलवारणम् A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित्
तलित् <i>f.</i> Lightning; cf. तडित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन|तलिनं|तलिनः
तलिन <i>a.</i> [तल्-इनन् Uṇ. 2. 53]<BR>—1 Thin, meagre, spare.<BR>—2 Small, little.<BR>—3 Clear, clean.<BR>—4 Situated under or beneath.<BR>—5 Weak.<BR>—6 Separate.<BR>—7 Fine, very thin; क्षोणीकान्तमृणालतन्तुतलिनास्ताम्यन्ति तारापतेः Vikr. 11. 80.<BR>—8 Covered with; Vikr. 14. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिनम्
तलिन + .{@-नम्@} A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिनोदरी
तलिन + .{@-उदरी@} <i>a.</i> a slender-waisted woman; स्नानावसाने तलिनोदरीणामकृत्रिमं<BR> मण्डनमाविरासीत् Vikr. 10. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिमम्
तलिमम्<BR>—1 Paved ground, a pavement.<BR>—2 A bed, cot, couch.<BR>—3 An awning.<BR>—4 A large sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुन|तलुनः
तलुन <i>a.</i> [तल्-उनन्] Young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुनः|तलुन
तलुन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A youth.<BR>—2 Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुनी
तलुन + .{@-नी@} A girl, young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्कम्
तल्कम् A forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पः|तल्प|तल्पं
तल्पः, -ल्पम्<BR> [तल्-पक् Uṇ. 3. 28]<BR>—1 A couch, bed, sofa; सपदि विगतनिद्रस्तल्पमुज्झाञ्चकार R. 5. 75<BR> ‘left the bed’, ‘rose’.<BR>—2 (Fig.) A wife (as in गुरुतल्पग q. v.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">Page0766-1</a>]<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 10. 9.<BR>—3 The seat of a carriage.<BR>—4 An upper storey, a turret, tower; विशीर्णतल्पादृशतो निवेशः पर्यस्तशालः<BR> प्रभुणा विना मे R. 16. 11.<BR>—5 A guard, one who protects; तल्पैश्चाभ्यासिकैर्युक्तं शुशुभे योधरक्षितम्<BR> Mb. 1. 207. 34 (तल्पैः रक्षिभिः पुरुषैः com.)<BR>—6 (with अधिगम्) Sexual intercourse; श्राद्धभुग् वृषलीतल्पं तदहर्योऽधिगच्छति Ms. 3. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पम्
तल्पः, -ल्पम्<BR> [तल्-पक् Uṇ. 3. 28]<BR>—1 A couch, bed, sofa; सपदि विगतनिद्रस्तल्पमुज्झाञ्चकार R. 5. 75<BR> ‘left the bed’, ‘rose’.<BR>—2 (Fig.) A wife (as in गुरुतल्पग q. v.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">Page0766-1</a>]<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 10. 9.<BR>—3 The seat of a carriage.<BR>—4 An upper storey, a turret, tower; विशीर्णतल्पादृशतो निवेशः पर्यस्तशालः<BR> प्रभुणा विना मे R. 16. 11.<BR>—5 A guard, one who protects; तल्पैश्चाभ्यासिकैर्युक्तं शुशुभे योधरक्षितम्<BR> Mb. 1. 207. 34 (तल्पैः रक्षिभिः पुरुषैः com.)<BR>—6 (with अधिगम्) Sexual intercourse; श्राद्धभुग् वृषलीतल्पं तदहर्योऽधिगच्छति Ms. 3. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पा
तल्पः, -ल्पम् + .{@-ल्पा@} A couch bed; तल्पा नः सुशेवा Av. 13. 1. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तल्पकीटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0765-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पकीटः|तल्पकीट
तल्पः + -कीटः a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पकः|तल्पक
तल्पकः One whose business is to make or prepare beds (as a servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पनम्
तल्पनम्<BR>—1 The exterior muscles of an elephantʼs back.<BR>—2 The flesh on the back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पलम्
तल्पलम् The back-bone of an elephant (पृष्ठवंश); सान्द्रत्वक्कास्तल्पलाश्लिष्टकक्षाः Śi. 18. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लः|तल्ल|तल्लं
तल्लः A reservoir, tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्ली
तल्लः + .{@-ल्ली@}<BR>—1 A youthful woman.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Varuṇa.<BR>—3 A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लम्
तल्लः + .{@-ल्लम्@} A pit, hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लजः|तल्लज
तल्लजः<BR>—1 Excellence, superiority, happiness.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Excellent (in this sense the word is always masculine,<BR> whatever be the gender of the first member of the compound); गोतल्लजः<BR> ‘an excellent cow’; so कुमारीतल्लजः ‘an excellent maiden’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लिका
तल्लिका A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्वम्
तल्वम् Scent produced from the rubbing of fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवकः|तवक
तवकः Fraud, deceit; तवकः कपटेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक्षीरम्
तवक्षीरम्<BR>—1 Manna of bamboo (Mar. वंशलोचन).<BR>—2 A kind of extract of wheat, rice &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवराजः|तवराज
तवराजः A sort of sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्
तवस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Old.<BR>—2 strong, great. ━<i>n.</i> Strength, power (बल); सोमस्य मा तवसं<BR> वक्ष्यग्ने Rv. 3. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्य
तवस्य <i>a.</i> Increasing strength (as an oblation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्यम्
तवस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} strength; तस्मै तवस्यमनु दायि सत्रा Rv. 2. 20. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष|तविषः
तविष <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Old.<BR>—2 strong, powerful, bold, courageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविषः|तविष
तविष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR>—3 Strength; युधेव शक्रास्तविषाणि कर्तन Rv. 1. 166. 1.<BR>—4 Business (व्यवसाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविषी
तविष + .{@-षी@}<BR>—1 Power.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR>—3 A river.<BR>—4 N. of a daughter of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष्या
तविष्या Violence, force; रुवति भीमो वृषभस्तविष्याय Rv. 9. 70. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीषः|तवीष
तवीषः<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR>—3 Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तव्य
तव्य A Kṛt affix by means of which potential passive participles<BR> are formed from roots, <i>e. g.</i> कर्तव्य from कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्ट|तष्टः
तष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hewn, cut, chiselled, split.<BR>—2 Fashioned; see तक्ष्; formed in mind, produced; ऋतेन तष्टा मनसा<BR> हिता Av. 11. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्टृ
तष्टृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A carpenter in general; रथं न तष्टेव तत्सिनाय Rv. 1. 61. 4.<BR>—2 The architect of gods (विश्वकर्मन्)<BR>—3 One of the 12 Ādityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्
तस् €4 P. (तस्यति)<BR>—1 To fade away, become exhausted.<BR>—2 To throw down.<BR>—3 To wane, decay, perish.<BR>—4 To reject, cast. [cf. Eng. <i>toss</i>.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसरम्
तसरम् A shuttle; सामानि चक्रुस्तसराण्योतवे Rv. 10. 130. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसरिका
तसरिका Weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करः|तस्कर
तस्करः<BR>—1 A thief, robber; मा संचर मनःपान्थ तत्रास्ते स्मरतस्करः Bh. 1. 86;<BR> Ms. 4. 135, 8. 67.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Anything bad or contemptible; अकस्मात् तावदुत्तस्थौ<BR> गर्जञ्जलदतस्करः Ks. 101. 140.<BR>—3 The ear; cf. व्यावृत्ता यत्परस्वेभ्यः श्रुतौ तस्करता स्थिता R. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करी
तस्करः + .{@-री@} A passionate woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करता
तस्करता<BR>—1 Theft; R. 1. 27.<BR>—2 Hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्थु
तस्थु <i>a.</i> Stationary, immovable, stable; देहस्तु सर्वसङ्घातो<BR> जगत्तस्थुरिति द्विधा Bhāg. 7. 7. 23; त्वमीशिषे जगतस्तस्थुषश्च<BR> Bhāg. 7. 3. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्दी
तस्दी (in Astr.) Hexagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्षण्यः|ताक्षण्य
ताक्षण्यः, ताक्ष्णः The son of a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्ष्णः|ताक्ष्ण
ताक्षण्यः, ताक्ष्णः The son of a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छीलिकः|ताच्छीलिक
ताच्छीलिकः N. of an affix used to denote a particular inclination,<BR> tendency, or habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छील्यम्
ताच्छील्यम् [ताच्छील्ये णिनिः] The act of being accustomed to that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजत्
ताजत् <i>a.</i> Quick, speedy. ━<i>ind.</i> Suddenly, abruptly; (opp. चिरम्);<BR> ताजद्भङ्ग इव भज्यन्ताम् Av. 8. 8. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजिकः|ताजिक
ताजिकः(तः)<BR>—1 A Persian (म्लेच्छविशेषः); Ks. 37. 36.<BR>—2 N. of a breed of an excellent horse; ताजिकाः खुरशालाश्च तुषाराश्चोत्तमा<BR> हयाः Aśvachikitsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजितः
ताजिकः(तः)<BR>—1 A Persian (म्लेच्छविशेषः); Ks. 37. 36.<BR>—2 N. of a breed of an excellent horse; ताजिकाः खुरशालाश्च तुषाराश्चोत्तमा<BR> हयाः Aśvachikitsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटङ्कः|ताटङ्क|ताटंक|ताटंकः
ताटङ्कः An ornament for the ear, a large ear-ring; तेन मुनिना<BR> पारितोषिकं ताटङ्कयुगलमर्पितं तस्य राज्ञः P. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटस्थ्यम्
ताटस्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Proximity.<BR>—2 Indifference, disregard neutrality; see तटस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड, ताडनम् &c. See under तड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडनम्
ताड, ताडनम् &c. See under तड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडजः
ताडजः N. of an excellent breed of horses; ताडजा -उत्तमाशाश्च<BR> Aśvachikitsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडका
ता(ट)डका<BR>—1 N. of a female fiend, daughter of Suketu, wife of Sunda and mother<BR> of Mārīcha. [She was changed into a fiend by the sage Agastya whose devotions<BR> she had disturbed. She was killed by Rāma when she began to disturb,<BR> the sacrificial rites of Viśvāmitra. Rāma was first unwilling to bend<BR> his bow, against a <i>woman</i>, but the sage overcame his scruples. See R. 11. 20].<BR>—2 The large dark-green pumpkin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टडका
ता(ट)डका<BR>—1 N. of a female fiend, daughter of Suketu, wife of Sunda and mother<BR> of Mārīcha. [She was changed into a fiend by the sage Agastya whose devotions<BR> she had disturbed. She was killed by Rāma when she began to disturb,<BR> the sacrificial rites of Viśvāmitra. Rāma was first unwilling to bend<BR> his bow, against a <i>woman</i>, but the sage overcame his scruples. See R. 11. 20].<BR>—2 The large dark-green pumpkin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडकेयः|ताडकेय
ताडकेयः [ताडकाया अपत्यं ढक्] An epithet of the demon Mārīcha,<BR> son of Tāḍakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0766-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडङ्कः|ताडङ्क|ताडंक|ताडंकः
ताडङ्कः, ताडपत्रम् See ताटङ्कम्; विश्वासाय स्वताडङ्कपाणिं<BR> कृत्वा प्रयागकम् Rāj. T. 7. 749.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडपत्रम्
ताडङ्कः, ताडपत्रम् See ताटङ्कम्; विश्वासाय स्वताडङ्कपाणिं<BR> कृत्वा प्रयागकम् Rāj. T. 7. 749.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडाग
ताडाग <i>a.</i> (-गी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Being in or coming from tanks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडिः|ताडि
ताडिः, -डी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of palm.<BR>—2 A kind of ornament (also ताडि(डी)दल); ताडीदलेन<BR> श्रवणान्निपत्य Vikr. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडी
ताडिः, -डी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of palm.<BR>—2 A kind of ornament (also ताडि(डी)दल); ताडीदलेन<BR> श्रवणान्निपत्य Vikr. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवः|ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|तांडवः
ताण्डवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Dancing in general; मदताण्डवोत्सवान्ते U. 3. 18; भ्रू˚ dance<BR> or playful movement of the eyebrows; 3. 19.<BR>—2 Particularly, the frantic or violent dance of Śiva; त्र्यम्बकानन्दि<BR> वस्ताण्डव देवि भूयादभीष्टपै च हृष्टपै च नः Māl. 5. 23, 1. 1.<BR>—3 The art of dancing.<BR>—4 A sort of grass.<BR>—5 (In prosody) A foot of three short syllables.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ताण्डवतालिकः, ताण्डवप्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवम्
ताण्डवः, -वम्<BR>—1 Dancing in general; मदताण्डवोत्सवान्ते U. 3. 18; भ्रू˚ dance<BR> or playful movement of the eyebrows; 3. 19.<BR>—2 Particularly, the frantic or violent dance of Śiva; त्र्यम्बकानन्दि<BR> वस्ताण्डव देवि भूयादभीष्टपै च हृष्टपै च नः Māl. 5. 23, 1. 1.<BR>—3 The art of dancing.<BR>—4 A sort of grass.<BR>—5 (In prosody) A foot of three short syllables.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ताण्डवतालिकः, ताण्डवप्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवतालिकः|ताण्डवतालिक
ताण्डवः + -तालिकः an epithet of Nandin, the door-keeper of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवप्रियः|ताण्डवप्रिय|तांडवप्रिय
ताण्डवः + -प्रियः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवित|तांडवित
ताण्डवित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dancing, made to dance; Māl. 2.<BR>—2 Moving round in a wild dance; U. 5. 36.<BR>—3 Fluttering; P. R. 1. 3-4.<BR>—4 Frowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डिः|ताण्डि|तांडिः
ताण्डिः The science of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्ड्यब्राह्मणम्
ताण्ड्यब्राह्मणम् N. of a ब्राह्मण of Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातः|तात
तातः [तन्-क्त दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 3. 90]<BR>—1 A father; मृष्यन्तु लवस्य बालिशतां तातपादाः U. 6; हा तातेति<BR> क्रन्दितमाकर्ण्य विषण्णः R. 9. 75.<BR>—2 A term of affection, endearment or pity, applied to any person, but<BR> usually to inferiors or juniors, pupils, children &c.; तात चन्द्रापीड<BR> K. 106; Māl. 6. 16; रक्षसा भक्षितस्तात तव तातो वनान्तरे Mb.<BR>—3 A term of respect applied to elders or other venerable personages;<BR> ह्रेपिता हि बहवो नरेश्वरास्तेन तात धनुषा धनुर्भृतः R. 11. 40;<BR> तस्मान्मुच्ये यथा तात संविधातुं तथार्हसि 1. 72.<BR>—4 Any person for whom one feels pity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तातगु, ताततुल्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगु|तातगुः
तातः + -गु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 agreeable to a father.<BR>—2 paternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगुः|तातगु
तातः + -गु + .({@-गुः@}) a paternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताततुल्यः|ताततुल्य
तातः + -तुल्यः a paternal uncle, or the most respectable of a manʼs male relations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातनः|तातन
तातनः The Khañjana or wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातल|तातलः
तातल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Paternal.<BR>—2 Hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातलः|तातल
तातल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A disease.<BR>—2 An iron club or spike.<BR>—3 Cooking, maturing.<BR>—4 Heat.<BR>—5 A relative who may be regarded as a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातिः|ताति
तातिः Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातिः|ताति
तातिः + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Continuity, succession, as in अरिष्टताति or शिवताति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कर्म्यम्
तात्कर्म्यम् Sameness of occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Simultaneous; equally long; Y. 1. 151.<BR>—2 Immediate.<BR>—3 Relating to any particular time; हयान् संदृश्य मां सूतः प्राह<BR> तात्कालिकं वचः Mb. 3. 22. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्काल्यम्
तात्काल्यम् Simultaneity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यम्
तात्पर्यम् [तत्परस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Purport, meaning, scope, अत्रेदं तात्पर्यम् &c.<BR>—2 Purport of propositions; K. P. 2.<BR>—3 Aim, object, intended reference to any object,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">Page0767-2</a>]<BR> purpose, intention (with loc.); इह यथार्थकथने तात्पर्यम् P. II. 3. 43 com.<BR>—4 The object or intention of the speaker (in using particular words in<BR> a sentence); वक्तुरिच्छा तु तात्पर्यं परिकीर्तितम् Bhāṣā P. 84;<BR> तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः 82.<BR>—5 Explanation.<BR>—6 Entire devotion to, absorption in any object.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तात्पर्यार्थः, तात्पर्यनिर्णयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यार्थः|तात्पर्यार्थ|तात्पर्य्यार्थ
तात्पर्यम् + -अर्थः the meaning of a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यनिर्णयः|तात्पर्यनिर्णय
तात्पर्यम् + -निर्णयः ascertainment of meaning or purport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यक
तात्पर्यक <i>a.</i> Aiming at, meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यतः
तात्पर्यतः <i>ind.</i> With this intention; त्यक्तश्रीर्नगरान्तरात्<BR> स नृपतिस्तात्पर्यतो निर्ययौ Rāj. T. 1. 367.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्त्विक
तात्त्विक <i>a.</i> True, real, essential; किं चासीदमृतस्य भेदविगमः<BR> साचिस्मिते तात्त्विकः Bv. 2. 81; तात्त्विकः संबन्धः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थिक
तादर्थिक <i>a.</i> Intended for that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थ्यम्
तादर्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Identity of aim, object.<BR>—2 Relation to.<BR>—3 Sameness of meaning.<BR>—4 Purpose, aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्यम्
तादात्म्यम् Sameness of nature, identity, unity; नयनयोस्तादात्म्यमम्भोरुहाम्<BR> Bv. 2. 81; भगवत्यात्मनस्तादात्म्यम् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्विकः|तादात्विक
तादात्विकः A spendthrift; यो यद् यद् उत्पद्यते तत्तद् भक्षयति<BR> स तादात्विकः Kau. A. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृक्ष|तादृक्षः
तादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), तादृश् <i>a.</i>, तादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Such-like, like him, her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR> Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 51; यादृशस्तादृशः any body whoever, common<BR> or ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृक्षी
तादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), तादृश् <i>a.</i>, तादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Such-like, like him, her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR> Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 51; यादृशस्तादृशः any body whoever, common<BR> or ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश्
तादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), तादृश् <i>a.</i>, तादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Such-like, like him, her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR> Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 51; यादृशस्तादृशः any body whoever, common<BR> or ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश|तादृशः
तादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), तादृश् <i>a.</i>, तादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Such-like, like him, her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR> Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 51; यादृशस्तादृशः any body whoever, common<BR> or ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृशी
तादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), तादृश् <i>a.</i>, तादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Such-like, like him, her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR> Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 51; यादृशस्तादृशः any body whoever, common<BR> or ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताद्धर्म्यम्
ताद्धर्म्यम् Sameness of law, analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताद्रूप्यम्
ताद्रूप्यम् Sameness of form, identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानः|तान|तानं
तानः [तन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A thread, fibre.<BR>—2 (In music) A protracted tone, a key-note; यथा तानं विना रागः<BR> Bv. 1. 119; तानप्रदायित्वमिवोपगन्तुम् Ku. 1. 8 (the number of tānas<BR> is said to be 49).<BR>—3 A monotonous tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानम्
तानः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Expanse, extension.<BR>—2 An object of sense.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तानकर्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानकर्मन्
तानः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 tuning the voice as a preparatory step to singing.<BR>—2 running over the notes to catch the key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानवम्
तानवम् Thinness, smallness; हास्यप्रभा तानवमाससाद Vikr. 1. 106;<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूरः|तानूर
तानूरः A whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त|तांत|तान्तः
तान्त See under तम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव|तांतव
तान्तव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [तन्तोर्विकारः अञ्] Made of threads; चर्मजैस्तान्तवैः<BR> पाशैर्बद्ध्वा पतितमर्भकाः Bhāg. 10. 64. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तवम्
तान्तव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Spinning, weaving.<BR>—2 A web.<BR>—3 A woven cloth; Ms. 10. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तुवायिः|तान्तुवायि|तांतुवायिः
तान्तुवायिः, तान्तुवाय्यः The son of a weaver; P. IV. 1. 152. Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तुवाय्यः|तान्तुवाय्य
तान्तुवायिः, तान्तुवाय्यः The son of a weaver; P. IV. 1. 152. Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तान्त्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Well-versed in any science or doctrine<BR>—2 Relating to the Tantras.<BR>—3 Taught or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">Page0768-1</a>]<BR> contained in them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिकः|तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक
तान्त्रिक + .{@-कः@} A follower of Tantra doctrines; तान्त्रिकाः परिचर्यायां<BR> केवलस्य श्रियः पतेः । अङ्गोपाङ्गायुधाकल्पं कल्पयन्ति यथा च यैः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 12. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0767-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप, तापन &c. See under तप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
ताप, तापन &c. See under तप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्यः|तापत्य
तापत्यः An epithet of Kuru; also of Arjuna; सोऽहं त्वयेह विजितः<BR> संख्ये तापत्यवर्धन Mb. 1. 170. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to religious penance or to an ascetic; तापसेष्वेव विप्रेषु<BR> यात्रिकं भैक्षमाहरेत् Ms. 6. 27.<BR>—2 Devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसः|तापस|तापसं
तापस + .{@-सः@} (-सी <i>f.</i>) A hermit, devotee, an ascetic.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तापसेष्टा, तापसप्रिया, तापसतरुः, तापसद्रुमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसेष्टा
तापस + -इष्टा, -प्रिया a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसप्रिया
तापस + -इष्टा, -प्रिया a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसतरुः|तापसतरु
तापस + -तरुः, -द्रुमः the tree of ascetics, also called इङ्गुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसद्रुमः|तापसद्रुम
तापस + -तरुः, -द्रुमः the tree of ascetics, also called इङ्गुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसकः|तापसक
तापसकः (= कुतापसः) The wretch of an ascetic; अयं तापसकान्<BR> ध्वंसः Bk. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस्यम्
तापस्यम् Asceticism; तापस्ये मे मनस्तात वर्तते कुरुनन्दन Mb. 15. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छः|तापिच्छ
तापिच्छः The Tamāla tree or its flower (<i>n.</i>); प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः<BR> Śi. 1. 22; व्योम्नस्तापिच्छगुच्छावलिभिरिव तमोवल्लरीभिर्व्रियन्ते Māl. 5. 6<BR> (तापिञ्ज used in the same sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापीजम्
तापीजम् Sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापी
तापी<BR>—1 N. of the river Tāptī, which joins the sea near Surat.<BR>—2 The river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामः|ताम
तामः [तम्-करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 An object of terror.<BR>—2 A fault, defect.<BR>—3 Anxiety, distress.<BR>—4 Desire.<BR>—5 Exhaustion, fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरम्
तामरम्<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरसम्
तामरसम् [तामरे जले सस्ति सस् ड Tv.]<BR>—1 The red lotus; पङ्कात्तामरसम् Pt. 1. 94; R. 6. 37, 9. 12, 37;<BR> लीलातामरसाहतोऽन्यवनितानिःशङ्कदष्टाधरः Amaru. 72, 88.<BR>—2 Gold.<BR>—3 Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरसी
तामरसम् + .{@-सी@} A lotus-pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [तमोऽस्त्यस्य अण्]<BR>—1 Dark, consisting of darkness; व्यतिकर इव भीमस्तामसो वैद्युतश्च<BR> Māl. 9. 52; U. 5. 12.<BR>—2 Affected by or relating to तमस् or the quality of darkness (the<BR> third of the three qualities of nature); ये चैव सात्त्विका भावा राजसास्तामसाश्च<BR> ये Bg. 7. 12, 17. 2; M. 1. 1; Ms. 12. 33-34.<BR>—3 Ignorant.<BR>—4 Vicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसः|तामस|तामसं
तामस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 A malignant person, an incendiary, a villain.<BR>—2 A snake.<BR>—3 An owl.<BR>—4 N. of a son of Rāhu.<BR>—5 A kind of horse possessing the quality of तमस्; सात्त्विका राजसाश्चेति<BR> तामसाश्चेति ते हयाः Yuktikalpataru.<BR>—6 The 4th Manu; चतुर्थ उत्तमभ्राता मनुर्नाम्ना च तामसः Bhāg. 8. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसम्
तामस + .{@-सम्@} Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसी
तामस + .{@-सी@}<BR>—1 Night, a dark night.<BR>—2 Sleep.<BR>—3 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तामसलीना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसलीना
तामस + -लीना (in Sāṅ. phil.) One of the forms of dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसिक|तामसिकं
तामसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [तमसा निर्वृत्तं ठञ्]<BR>—1 Dark.<BR>—2 Belonging to, derived from, or connected with तमस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्रः|तामिस्र|तामिस्रं
तामिस्रः<BR>—1 A division of hell; Ms. 4. 88; Bhāg. 3. 12. 2.<BR>—2 The dark fortnight of a month.<BR>—3 Hatred.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">Page0768-2</a>]<BR>—4 Anger; तामिस्रं क्रोध उच्यते Mb. 12. 313. 25.<BR>—5 A demon, Rākṣasa (going about in the dark).<BR>—6 (Phil.) Dislike; तामिस्रोष्टादशधा Sāṅ. K. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिः|तामि
तामिः, -मी<BR> Restraining the breath until exhaustion is produced; Kauś. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामी
तामिः, -मी<BR> Restraining the breath until exhaustion is produced; Kauś. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलम्
ताम्बूलम्<BR>—1 The areca-nut.<BR>—2 The leaf of piper-betel, which together with the areca-nut, catechu,<BR> chunam, and spices is usually chewed after meals; ताम्बूलभृतगल्लोऽयं<BR> भल्लं जल्पति मानुषः K. P. 7; रागो न स्खलितस्तवाधरपुटे ताम्बूलसंवर्धितः Ś. Til. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ताम्बूलाधिकारः, ताम्बूलकरङ्कः, ताम्बूलपेटिका, ताम्बूलदः, ताम्बूलधरः, ताम्बूलवाहकः, ताम्बूलवल्ली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलाधिकारः|ताम्बूलाधिकार
ताम्बूलम् + -अधिकारः the office of carrying the betel-box; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलकरङ्कः|ताम्बूलकरङ्क|तांबूलकरंक
ताम्बूलम् + -करङ्कः, -पेटिका a betel-box (Mar. पानदान, पानपुडा);<BR> आकृष्य ताम्बूलकरङ्कमध्यात्कर्पूरदानं विदधे बहुभ्यः Vikr. 9. 82.<BR> ˚वाह, ˚हिनी see next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलपेटिका|तांबूलपेटिका
ताम्बूलम् + -करङ्कः, -पेटिका a betel-box (Mar. पानदान, पानपुडा);<BR> आकृष्य ताम्बूलकरङ्कमध्यात्कर्पूरदानं विदधे बहुभ्यः Vikr. 9. 82.<BR> ˚वाह, ˚हिनी see next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलदः|ताम्बूलद|तांबूलद
ताम्बूलम् + -दः, -धरः, -वाहकः a servant attached to men of rank to carry<BR> the betel-box and to provide them with ताम्बूल whenever necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलधरः|ताम्बूलधर|तांबूलधर
ताम्बूलम् + -दः, -धरः, -वाहकः a servant attached to men of rank to carry<BR> the betel-box and to provide them with ताम्बूल whenever necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवाहकः|ताम्बूलवाहक|तांबूलवाहक
ताम्बूलम् + -दः, -धरः, -वाहकः a servant attached to men of rank to carry<BR> the betel-box and to provide them with ताम्बूल whenever necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवल्ली|तांबूलवल्ली
ताम्बूलम् + -वल्ली the betel-plant; ताम्बूलवल्लीपरिणद्धपूगाः R. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिकः|ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः
ताम्बूलिकः A seller of betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिन्|तांबूलिन्
ताम्बूलिन् <i>a.</i> Relating to betel. ━<i>m.</i> A servant who prepares<BR> the Tāmbūla and gives it to his master when wanted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूली
ताम्बूली The betel-plant; ताम्बूलीनां दलैस्तत्र रचितापानभूमयः<BR> R. 4. 42; Māl. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र <i>a.</i> [तम्-रक् दीर्घः Uṇ. 2. 16]<BR>—1 Made of copper.<BR>—2 Of a coppery red colour, red; ततोऽनुकुर्याद्विशदस्य तस्यास्ताम्रौष्ठपर्यस्तरुचः<BR> स्मितस्य Ku. 1. 44; उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति च Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रः|ताम्र|ताम्रं
ताम्र + .{@-म्रः@} A kind of leprosy with red spots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रम्
ताम्र + .{@-म्रम्@}<BR>—1 Copper.<BR>—2 A dark or coppery red.<BR>—3 A coppery receptacle; ताम्रलोहैः परिवृता निधयो ये चतुः शताः Mb. 2. 61. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्री
ताम्र + .{@-म्री@} A copper pot having a small hole at the botton used in measuring<BR> time by placing it in a water-vessel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ताम्राक्षः, ताम्रार्धः, ताम्राश्मन्, ताम्राभम्, ताम्रोपजीविन्, ताम्रौष्ठः, ताम्रकारः, ताम्रकुट्टः, ताम्रकृमिः, ताम्रगर्भम्, ताम्रचूडः, ताम्रचूडकः, ताम्रत्रपुजम्, ताम्रद्रुः, ताम्रद्वीपः, ताम्रधातुः, ताम्रपट्टः, ताम्रपत्रम्, ताम्रपर्णी, ताम्रपलः, ताम्रपल्लवः, ताम्रपाकिन्, ताम्रपुष्पः, ताम्रपुष्पी, ताम्रमुख, ताम्रवदनः, ताम्रवर्णी, ताम्रलिप्तः, ताम्रलिप्ताः, ताम्रवृक्षः, ताम्रशिखिन्, ताम्रसारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राक्षः|ताम्राक्ष
ताम्र + -अक्षः<BR>—1 a crow.<BR>—2 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रार्धः|ताम्रार्ध
ताम्र + -अर्धः bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राश्मन्
ताम्र + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i> a kind of jewel (पद्मराग); ताम्राश्मरश्मिच्छुरितैर्नखाग्रैः Śi. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0768-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

