तिलपर्णकम्
तिलः + -पर्णिका, -पर्णिकम्, -पर्णकम् sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिच्चटम्
तिलः + -पिच्चटम् Sweetmeat of sesamum powder and sugar; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिञ्जः|तिलपिञ्ज
तिलः + -पिञ्जः, -पेजः barren sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपेजः|तिलपेज
तिलः + -पिञ्जः, -पेजः barren sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपीडः|तिलपीड
तिलः + -पीडः an oilman; स्नेहेन तिलवत्सर्वं सर्गचक्रे निपीड्यते ।<BR> तिलपीडैरिव Mb. 12. 174. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलभाविनी
तिलः + -भाविनी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलमयूरः|तिलमयूर
तिलः + -मयूरः a species of peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलरसः|तिलरस
तिलः + -रसः, -स्नेहः sesamum oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलस्नेहः|तिलस्नेह
तिलः + -रसः, -स्नेहः sesamum oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलहोमः|तिलहोम
तिलः + -होमः a burnt offering of sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकः|तिलक|तिलकं
तिलकः [तिल्-क्वुन्, तिल इवार्थे स्वल्पे वा कन् वा]<BR>—1 A species of tree with beautiful flowers; Rām. 2. 94. 9; आक्रान्ता<BR> तिलकक्रियापि तिलकैलींनद्विरेफाञ्जनैः M. 3, 5; न खलु शोभयति स्म<BR> वनस्थलीं न तिलकस्तिलकः प्रमदामिव R. 9. 41. Kālidāsa describes<BR> the beauty of this tree as being akin to that of the saffron-mark on the<BR> forehead of a woman. The name suggests a relation to <i>tila</i>, the<BR> sesame plant, Sesamum indicum Linn. Now this plant has got flowers that<BR> have got a very pretty appearance. It is a shrub and not a tree. It grows<BR> four to five feet in height. Its flower has five petals. The lower petal<BR> is the longest. In wild variety there is a promiment spot on the longest<BR> petal which is highly suggestive of the saffron-mark on the forehead of a woman.<BR>—2 A freckle or natural mark under the skin.<BR>—3 The sesamum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकः|तिलक|तिलकं
तिलकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A mark made with sandalwood or unguents &c.; मुखे मधुश्रीस्तिलकं<BR> प्रकाश्य Ku. 3. 30; कस्तूरिकातिलकमालि विधाय सायम् Bv. 2. 4, 1. 121.<BR>—2 The ornament of anything (used at the end of comp. in the sense of<BR> ‘best’, ‘chief’ or ‘distinguished’); कुल˚; जीवलोक˚ Māl. 9. 21;<BR> यस्य न विपदि विषादः संपदि हर्षो रणे न भीरुत्वम् । तं भुवनत्रयतिलकं<BR> जनयति जननी सुतं विरलम् ॥ Pt. 1. 105.<BR>—3 The burden of a song (ध्रुवक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकम्
तिलकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A mark made with sandalwood or unguents &c.; मुखे मधुश्रीस्तिलकं<BR> प्रकाश्य Ku. 3. 30; कस्तूरिकातिलकमालि विधाय सायम् Bv. 2. 4, 1. 121.<BR>—2 The ornament of anything (used at the end of comp. in the sense of<BR> ‘best’, ‘chief’ or ‘distinguished’); कुल˚; जीवलोक˚ Māl. 9. 21;<BR> यस्य न विपदि विषादः संपदि हर्षो रणे न भीरुत्वम् । तं भुवनत्रयतिलकं<BR> जनयति जननी सुतं विरलम् ॥ Pt. 1. 105.<BR>—3 The burden of a song (ध्रुवक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलका
तिलकः + .{@-का@} A kind of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकम्
तिलकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The bladder.<BR>—2 The right lung.<BR>—3 A kind of salt.<BR>—4 A kind of disease, the appearance of dark spots on the skin without<BR> any inflammation.<BR>—5 Alliteration.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तिलकाश्रयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकाश्रयः|तिलकाश्रय
तिलकः + -आश्रयः the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकायते
तिलकायते Den. Ā. To serve as a <i>Tilaka</i>-mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकित
तिलकित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Marked with a <i>Tilaka</i>.<BR>—2 Adorned; तावत्तिलकितं प्राच्या मुखमुद्भासितेन्दुना Ks. 93. 17; Rāj. T. 2. 40.<BR>—3 Freckled, spotted; also तिलकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलंतुदः|तिलन्तुद
तिलंतुदः An oilman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलशः
तिलशः <i>ind.</i> In pieces as small as sesamum-seed, in very small quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्य|तिल्यं
तिल्य <i>a.</i> Fit for the cultivation of sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्यम्
तिल्य + .{@-ल्यम्@} A field of sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0774-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्वः|तिल्व
तिल्वः The <i>lodhra</i> tree, Symplocos racemosa; Mātaṅga L. 9. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलित्सः|तिलित्स
तिलित्सः A large snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठद्गु|तिष्ठद्गुः
तिष्ठद्गु <i>ind.</i> At the time when cows stand to be milked (<i>i. e.</i><BR> after an hour or an hour and a half after evening); आतिष्ठद्गु जपन्<BR> संध्याम् Bk. 4. 14 (तिष्ठद्गु = रात्रैः प्रथमनाडिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठद्धोमः|तिष्ठद्धोम
तिष्ठद्धोमः A sacrifice at which the oblation is offered by a priest standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्य|तिष्यः
तिष्य <i>a.</i> [तुष्यन्त्यस्मिन् तुष्-क्यप् नि˚]<BR>—1 Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>—2 Born under the asterism पुष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यः|तिष्य
तिष्य + .{@-ष्यः@}<BR>—1 The eighth of the 27 constellations, (also called पुष्य); यदा<BR> चन्द्रश्च सूर्यश्च तथा तिष्यबृहस्पतीं । एकराशौ समेष्यन्ति तदा भवति<BR> तत्कृतम् ॥ Bhāg. 12. 2. 24.<BR>—2 The lunar month Pauṣa.<BR>—3 The Kali Yuga; तिष्यः पुष्ये कलियुगौ Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्या
तिष्य + .{@-ष्या@}<BR>—1 Lustre.<BR>—2 Emblic myrobalan; दीप्त्यामलकयोः स्त्रियाम् Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यम्
तिष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} The Kali Yuga; चत्वारि भारते वर्षे युगानि भरतर्षभ ।<BR> कृतं त्रेता द्वापरं च तिष्यं च कुरुवर्धन ॥ Mb. 6. 10. 3; तथापि<BR> तिष्यस्य बलाद् भृशं ववृधिरे श्रियः Śiva B. 5. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तिष्यकेतुः, तिष्यरक्षिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यकेतुः|तिष्यकेतु
तिष्य + -केतुः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यरक्षिता
तिष्य + -रक्षिता N. of the Aśokaʼs second wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यकः|तिष्यक
तिष्यकः The month पौष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिहन्
तिहन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Disease.<BR>—2 Grain (rice).<BR>—3 Bow.<BR>—4 Goodness; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्
तीक् €1 Ā. (तीकते) To go, move; cf. टीक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> [तिज्-क्स्न Uṇ. 3. 18.]<BR>—1 Sharp (in all senses), pungent; तीक्ष्णा नारुंतुदा बुद्धिः Śi. 2. 109.<BR>—2 Hot, warm (as rays); विवस्वता तीक्ष्णतरांशुमालिना Ṛs. 1. 18.<BR>—3 Fiery, passionate.<BR>—4 Hard, forcible, strong (as उपाय); आश्रयो धार्तराष्ट्राणां मानी<BR> तीक्ष्णपराक्रमः Mb. 12. 1. 20.<BR>—5 Rude, cross.<BR>—6 Severe, harsh, rough, strict; तीक्ष्णश्चैव मृदुश्च स्यात्कार्यं वीक्ष्य<BR> महीपतिः Ms. 7. 140.<BR>—7 Injurious, inauspicious.<BR>—8 Keen.<BR>—9 Intelligent, clever.<BR>—10 Zealous, vehement, energetic.<BR>—11 Devoted, self-abandoning.<BR>—12 Unfriendly, unfavourable.<BR>—13 Devout, ascetic, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णः|तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं
तीक्ष्ण + .{@-क्ष्णः@}<BR>—1 Nitre.<BR>—2 Long pepper.<BR>—3 Black pepper.<BR>—4 Black mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णम्
तीक्ष्ण + .{@-क्ष्णम्@}<BR>—1 Iron.<BR>—2 Steel.<BR>—3 Heat, pungency.<BR>—4 War, battle.<BR>—5 Poison.<BR>—6 Death.<BR>—7 A weapon.<BR>—8 Sea-salt.<BR>—9 Haste.<BR>—10 Anything sharp (as words &c.).<BR>—11 Plague, pestilence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तीक्ष्णांशुः, तीक्ष्णाग्निः, तीक्ष्णायसम्, तीक्ष्णोपायः, तीक्ष्णकण्टकः, तीक्ष्णकन्दः, तीक्ष्णकर्मन्, तीक्ष्णकल्कः, तीक्ष्णतण्डुला, तीक्ष्णतैलम्, तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रः, तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रकः, तीक्ष्णधारः, तीक्ष्णपुष्पम्, तीक्ष्णपुष्पा, तीक्ष्णफलम्, तीक्ष्णबुद्धि, तीक्ष्णमञ्जरी, तीक्ष्णमार्गः, तीक्ष्णरश्मिः, तीक्ष्णरसः, तीक्ष्णलौहम्, तीक्ष्णशूकः, तीक्ष्णसारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णांशुः|तीक्ष्णांशु
तीक्ष्ण + -अंशुः<BR>—1 the sun; श्वेताभ्र इव तीक्ष्णांशुं ददृशुः कुरुपाण्डवाः Mb. 6. 16. 23.<BR>—2 fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णाग्निः|तीक्ष्णाग्नि
तीक्ष्ण + -आग्निः dyspepsia, heartburn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णायसम्
