तीरान्तरम्
तीरम् + -अन्तरम् the opposite bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरजः|तीरज
तीरम् + -जः a tree near a shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरभुक्तिः|तीरभुक्ति
तीरम् + -भुक्तिः N. of a country in middle India (Tirhut).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरित|तीरितं
तीरित <i>a.</i> Settled, adjusted, decided according to evidence; Ms. 9. 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरितम्
तीरित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Completion of any affair.<BR>—2 Non-infliction of a sentence owing to bribery or other unfair means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरुः|तीरु
तीरुः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्ण|तीर्णः
तीर्ण See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थम्
तीर्थम् [तॄ-थक् Uṇ. 2. 7] ‘तीर्थं शास्त्राध्वरक्षेत्रोपायोपाध्यायमन्त्रिषु’ इति विश्वः.<BR>—1 A passage, road, way, ford; सुप्रतारां दृढां तीर्थे शीघ्रं नावमुपाहर<BR> Rām. 2. 52. 6; Bhāg. 9. 19. 4.<BR>—2 A descent into a river, the stairs of a landing-place (Mar. घाट);<BR> विषमोऽपि विगाह्यते नयः कृततीर्थः पयसामिवाशयः Ki. 2. 3 (where<BR> तीर्थ means ‘a remedy’ or ‘means’ also); तीर्थं सर्वविद्यावताराणाम् K. 44.<BR>—3 A place of water.<BR>—4 A holy place, place of pilgrimage, a shrine &c. dedicated to some holy<BR> object (especially on or near the bank of a sacred river &c.); तीर्थोदकं<BR> च वह्निश्च नान्यतः शुद्धिमर्हतः U. 1. 13; शुचि मनो यद्यस्ति तीर्थेन<BR> किम् Bh. 2. 55; R. 1. 85.<BR>—5 A channel, medium, means; तदनेन तीर्थेन घटेत &c. Māl. 1.<BR>—6 A remedy, expedient; नाध्यगच्छद्बलिर्लोके तीर्थमन्यत्र वै द्विजात् Mb. 3. 26. 12.<BR>—7 A sacred or holy personage, worthy person, an object of veneration,<BR> a fit recipient; क्व पुनस्तादृशस्य तीर्थस्य साधोः संभवः U. 1;<BR> Ms. 3. 136; H. 2. 8; R. 5. 15; वृद्धस्य तीर्थेषु प्रतिपादिनी Kau. A. 1.<BR>—8 A sacred preceptor, a teacher; मया तीर्थादभिनयविद्या शिक्षिता M. 1.<BR>—9 Source, origin.<BR>—10 A sacrifice.<BR>—11 A minister; Rām. 2. 100. 36; Pt. 3. 68.<BR>—12 Advice, instruction; विषमोऽपि विगाह्यते नयः कृततीर्थः पयसामिवाशयः Ki. 2. 3.<BR>—13 Right place or moment; प्रादात्स्वन्नं च विप्रेभ्यः प्रजातीर्थे स<BR> तीर्थवित् Bhāg. 1. 12. 14.<BR>—14 The right or usual manner; गौतम तीर्थेनेच्छासा इत्युपैम्यहं भवन्तम्<BR> Bṛ. Up. 6. 2. 7.<BR>—15 Certain parts of the hand sacred to deities, manes &c.<BR>—16 A school of philosophy.<BR>—17 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>—18 Menstrual courses of a woman.<BR>—19 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—20 (In liturgical language) The path to the altar between the चात्वाल<BR> q. v. and उत्कर q. v.<BR>—21 Fire.<BR>—22 Ascertainment of a disease.<BR>—23 A science<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">Page0776-1</a>]<BR> (शास्त्र).<BR>—24 An auxiliary, a help; a person or official connected with the king<BR> and being in close attendance on him; (the number being 15 on oneʼs side<BR> and 18 on the enemyʼs side); cf. Pt. 3. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थः|तीर्थ|तीर्थं
तीर्थम् + .{@-र्थः@} One of the ten orders of ascetics founded by शंकराचार्य,<BR> An honorary affix added to the names of ascetics, saints &c.; <i>e. g.</i><BR> आनन्दतीर्थ. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sacred.<BR>—2 Liberator, saviour; वार्तां सखे कीर्तय तीर्थकीर्तेः Bhāg. 3. 1. 45.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तीर्थोदकम्, तीर्थकमण्डलु, तीर्थकरः, तीर्थकाकः, तीर्थकाकः, तीर्थध्वाङ्क्षः, तीर्थवायसः, तीर्थचर्या, तीर्थदेवः, तीर्थपाद्, तीर्थभूत, तीर्थयात्रा, तीर्थराजः, तीर्थराजिः, तीर्थराजी, तीर्थवाकः, तीर्थविधिः, तीर्थशिला, तीर्थसेविन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0775-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थोदकम्
तीर्थम् + -उदकम् holy water; तीर्थोदकं च वह्निश्च नान्यतः शुद्धिमर्हतः U. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकमण्डलु
तीर्थम् + -कमण्डलु ━<i>m., n.</i> a pot filled with water from a holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकरः|तीर्थकर
तीर्थम् + -करः<BR>—1 a Jaina <i>Arhat</i>, sanctified teacher or saint of the Jainas; (also<BR> तर्थिंकर in this sense).<BR>—2 an ascetic.<BR>—3 the founder of a new religious or philosophical school.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकाकः|तीर्थकाक
तीर्थम् + -काकः an unsteady pupil; P. II. 1. 42. Vārt.;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकाकः|तीर्थकाक
तीर्थम् + -काकः, -ध्वाङ्क्षः, -वायसः ‘a crow at a sacred bathing-place’,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> a very greedy person (लोलुप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थध्वाङ्क्षः|तीर्थध्वाङ्क्ष|तीर्थध्वांक्ष
तीर्थम् + -काकः, -ध्वाङ्क्षः, -वायसः ‘a crow at a sacred bathing-place’,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> a very greedy person (लोलुप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थवायसः|तीर्थवायस
तीर्थम् + -काकः, -ध्वाङ्क्षः, -वायसः ‘a crow at a sacred bathing-place’,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> a very greedy person (लोलुप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थचर्या
तीर्थम् + -चर्या pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थदेवः|तीर्थदेव
तीर्थम् + -देवः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थपाद्
तीर्थम् + -पाद् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; Bhāg. 1. 7. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थभूत
तीर्थम् + -भूत <i>a.</i> sacred, holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थयात्रा
तीर्थम् + -यात्रा a visit to a holy place, a pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थराजः|तीर्थराज
तीर्थम् + -राजः N. of Prayāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थराजिः|तीर्थराजि
तीर्थम् + -राजिः, -राजी <i>f.</i> an epithet of Benaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थराजी
तीर्थम् + -राजिः, -राजी <i>f.</i> an epithet of Benaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थवाकः|तीर्थवाक
तीर्थम् + -वाकः the hair of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थविधिः|तीर्थविधि
तीर्थम् + -विधिः rites observed at a place of pilgrimage (such as क्षौर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थशिला
तीर्थम् + -शिला the stone-steps leading to a bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थसेविन्
तीर्थम् + -सेविन् <i>a.</i> a pilgrim. ━(<i>m.</i>) a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थक|तीर्थकः
तीर्थक <i>a.</i> Holy, sacred, venerable; कृपयातिथिरूपेण भवद्भिस्तीर्थकाः<BR> कृताः Bhāg. 1. 19. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकः|तीर्थक
तीर्थक + .{@-कः@} An ascetic, a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थिकः|तीर्थिक
तीर्थिकः<BR>—1 A pilgrim, an ascetic Brāhmaṇa (visiting holy places).<BR>—2 An adherent or head of any other than oneʼs own creed; Buddha, Jaina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थीकृ
तीर्थीकृ €8 U. To make sacred, sanctify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थीभूत
तीर्थीभूत <i>a.</i> Become sacred, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ्य|तीर्थ्यः
तीर्थ्य <i>a.</i> Relating to a sacred place; Vāj. 16. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ्यः|तीर्थ्य
तीर्थ्य + .{@-र्थ्यः@} An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्
तीव् €1 P. (तीवति)<BR>—1 To be large or strong.<BR>—2 To be fat or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीवरः|तीवर
तीवरः<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 A hunter. —3 The adulterine offspring of a Rājaputrī by a Kṣatriya<BR> (one of the mixed tribes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्र|तीव्रं|तीव्रः
तीव्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Severe, intense, sharp, acute, violent, poignant, pungent, impetuous;<BR> विलङ्घिताधोरणतीव्रयत्नाः R. 5. 48 ‘strong or violent efforts’ &c.;<BR> U. 3. 35; Ś. 1. 32, 5. 7.<BR>—2 Hot, warm.<BR>—3 Flashing.<BR>—4 Pervading.<BR>—5 Endless, unlimited.<BR>—6 Horrible, dreadful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रः|तीव्र|तीव्रं
तीव्र + .{@-व्रः@}<BR>—1 Sharpness.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रम्
तीव्र + .{@-व्रम्@}<BR>—1 Heat, pungency.<BR>—2 A shore.<BR>—3 Iron, steel.<BR>—4 Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रम्
तीव्र + .{@-व्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Violently, sharply, excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रा
तीव्र + .{@-व्रा@}<BR>—1 Black mustard.<BR>—2 Basil.<BR>—3 Helleborus niger (Mar. कुटकी).<BR>—4 (in music) N. of a श्रुति.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: तीव्रानन्दः, तीव्रगति, तीव्रगन्धा, तीव्रद्युतिः, तीव्रपौरुषम्, तीव्रवेदना, तीव्रसंवेग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रानन्दः|तीव्रानन्द|तीव्रानंद
तीव्र + -आनन्दः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रगति
तीव्र + -गति <i>a.</i> quick, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रगन्धा
तीव्र + -गन्धा cumin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रद्युतिः|तीव्रद्युति
तीव्र + -द्युतिः the sun;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">Page0776-2</a>]<BR> P. R. 7. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रपौरुषम्
तीव्र + -पौरुषम्<BR>—1 daring heroism.<BR>—2 heroism (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रवेदना
तीव्र + -वेदना acute or sharp pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रसंवेग
तीव्र + -संवेग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of strong impulse, resolute.<BR>—2 very poignant or sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रयति
तीव्रयति Den. P. To make sharp, strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रीभू
तीव्रीभू To become stronger, increase; अथाभिषिच्य संग्रामदेवं<BR> तीव्रीभवद्व्यथः Rāj. T. 6. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु €2 P. (तौति and तवीति)<BR>—1 To have authority or power, to be strong; स तूताव नैनमश्नोत्यंहतिः Rv. 1. 94. 2.<BR>—2 To get, attain.<BR>—3 To thrive, increase, become full.<BR>—4 To go, move.<BR>—5 To injure, hurt, strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु <i>ind.</i> (Never used at the beginning of a sentence, but usually<BR> after the first word)<BR>—1 An adversative particle meaning ‘but’, ‘on the contrary’, ‘on the other hand’<BR>, ‘nevertheless’; स सर्वेषां सुखानामन्त ययौ । एकं तु सुतमुखदर्शनसुखं<BR> न लेभे K. 59; विपर्यये तु पितुरस्याः समीपनयनमवस्थितमेव<BR> Ś. 5 (in this sense तु is often added to किं and परम्, and<BR> किंतु and परंतु are, unlike तु, always used at the beginning<BR> of a sentence).<BR>—2 And now, on oneʼs part, and; एकदा तु प्रतीहारी समुपसृत्याब्रवीत्<BR> Ks. 8; राजा तु तामार्यां श्रुत्वाऽब्रवीत् 12.<BR>—3 As to as regards, as for; प्रवर्त्यतां ब्राह्मणानुद्दिश्य पाकः ।,<BR> चन्द्रोपरागं प्रति तु केनापि विप्रलब्धासि Mu. 1; Māl. 8. 4.<BR>—4 It sometimes marks a difference (भेद) or superior quality; मृष्टं<BR> पयो मृष्टतरं तु दुग्धम् G. M.<BR>—5 Sometimes it is used as an emphatic particle; बालानां तु शुभं वाक्यं<BR> ग्राह्मम् Rām. 7. 83. 20. भीमस्तु पाण्डवानां रौद्रः G. M.<BR>—6 And sometimes it is used as a mere expletive; निरर्थकं तु हीत्यादि<BR> पूरणैकप्रयोजनम् Candr. 2. 6.<BR>—7 when used as an indeclinable it means, ‘undoubtedly’; तुशब्दः संशयव्याबृत्त्यर्थः ।<BR> न खलु संशयोऽस्ति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुक्खारः|तुक्खार
तुक्खारः, तुखारः, तुषारः<BR>—1 N. of a people inhabiting the in Vindhya mountain;<BR> cf. Vikr. 18. 93.<BR>—2 Tukhar horse; निशम्य तुक्खारखुरक्षतायाः क्षितेस्तनुत्वादिव यस्य<BR> कीर्तिम् Vikr. 9. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुखारः|तुखार
तुक्खारः, तुखारः, तुषारः<BR>—1 N. of a people inhabiting the in Vindhya mountain;<BR> cf. Vikr. 18. 93.<BR>—2 Tukhar horse; निशम्य तुक्खारखुरक्षतायाः क्षितेस्तनुत्वादिव यस्य<BR> कीर्तिम् Vikr. 9. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारः|तुषार
तुक्खारः, तुखारः, तुषारः<BR>—1 N. of a people inhabiting the in Vindhya mountain;<BR> cf. Vikr. 18. 93.<BR>—2 Tukhar horse; निशम्य तुक्खारखुरक्षतायाः क्षितेस्तनुत्वादिव यस्य<BR> कीर्तिम् Vikr. 9. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुग्र्या|तुग्र्य्या
