तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 High, elevated, tall, lofty, prominent; जलनिधिमिव विधुमण्डलदर्शनतरलिततुङ्गतरङ्गम्<BR> Gīt. 11; तुङ्गं नगोत्सङ्गमिवारुरोह R. 6. 3, 4. 70; Śi. 2. 48; Me. 12, 66.<BR>—2 Long<BR>—3 Vaulted.<BR>—4 Chief, principal.<BR>—5 Strong, passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गः|तुङ्ग|तुंग
तुङ्ग + .{@-गः@}<BR>—1 A height, elevation.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 Top, summit.<BR>—4 The planet Mercury.<BR>—5 A rhinoceros<BR>—6 The coco-nut tree; Mb. 12. 262. 7.<BR>—7 The aphelion of a planet.<BR>—8 (fig.) A throne; निपात्य तुङ्गाद्रिपुयूथनाथम् Bhāg. 3. 3. 1.<BR>—9 A wise man.<BR>—10 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—11 The Punnāga tree; तुङ्गस्तु शैलपुन्नागयोस्त्रिषु Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0776-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गम्
