त्र्यंशः|त्र्यंश
त्रि + -अंशः<BR>—1 a three-fold share; त्र्यंशं दायाद्धरेद्विप्रः Ms. 9. 151.<BR>—2 a third part.<BR>—3 three-fourths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्ष|त्र्यक्षः
त्रि + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> triocular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षः|त्र्यक्ष
त्रि + -अक्षः, -अक्षकः an epithet of Śiva; शुष्कस्रायुस्वराह्लादात्त्र्यक्षं<BR> जग्राह रावणः Pt. 5. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षकः|त्र्यक्षक
त्रि + -अक्षः, -अक्षकः an epithet of Śiva; शुष्कस्रायुस्वराह्लादात्त्र्यक्षं<BR> जग्राह रावणः Pt. 5. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षरः|त्र्यक्षर
त्रि + -अक्षरः<BR>—1 the mystic syllable ओम् consisting of three letters; see under अ.<BR> आद्यं यत्त्र्यक्षरं ब्रह्म Ms. 11. 265.<BR>—2 a match-maker or घटक (that word consisting of three syllables).<BR>—3 a genealogist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षरी
त्रि + -अक्षरः + .({@-री@}) knowledge, learning; see विद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्कटम्
त्रि + -अङ्कटम्, -अङ्गटम्<BR>—1 three strings suspended to either end of a pole for carrying burdens.<BR>—2 a sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्कटः|त्र्यङ्कट|त्र्यंकट
त्रि + -अङ्कटम्, -अङ्गटम् + .({@-टः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्गटम्
त्रि + -अङ्कटम्, -अङ्गटम्<BR>—1 three strings suspended to either end of a pole for carrying burdens.<BR>—2 a sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्गम्
त्रि + -अङ्गम् (pl.) a tripartite army (chariots, cavalry and infantry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्गुलम्
त्रि + -अङ्गुलम् three fingersʼ breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यञ्जनम्
त्रि + -अञ्जनम् the three kinds of collyrium; <i>i. e.</i> कालाञ्जन,<BR> रसाञ्जन and पुष्पाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यञ्जलम्
त्रि + -अञ्जलम्, -अञ्जलिः three handfuls taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यञ्जलिः|त्र्यञ्जलि|त्र्यंजलि
त्रि + -अञ्जलम्, -अञ्जलिः three handfuls taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यधिपतिः|त्र्यधिपति
त्रि + -अधिपतिः (the lord of the 3 guṇas or worlds), an epithet of<BR> Viṣṇu; Bhāg. 3. 16. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यधिष्ठानः|त्र्यधिष्ठान
त्रि + -अधिष्ठानः the soul. ({@नम्@}) spirit, life (चैतन्य).<BR>━<i>a.</i> having three stations; Ms. 12. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यध्वगा
त्रि + -अध्वगा, -मार्गगा, -वर्त्मगा epithets of the river Ganges (flowing<BR> through the three worlds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमार्गगा
त्रि + -अध्वगा, -मार्गगा, -वर्त्मगा epithets of the river Ganges (flowing<BR> through the three worlds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्त्मगा
त्रि + -अध्वगा, -मार्गगा, -वर्त्मगा epithets of the river Ganges (flowing<BR> through the three worlds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यनीक
त्रि + -अनीक <i>a.</i> having the three properties of heat, rain and cold;<BR> त्र्यनीकः पत्यते माहिनावान् Rv. 3. 56. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यनीका
त्रि + -अनीक + .({@-का@}) an army consisting of horses, elephants and chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्द
त्रि + -अब्द <i>a.</i> three years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्दम्
त्रि + -अब्दम् three years taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बकः|त्र्यम्बक|त्र्यंबक
त्रि + -अम्बकः (also त्रियम्बक in the same sense though rarely<BR> used in classical literature) ‘having three eyes’, N. of Śiva; त्रियम्बकं<BR> संयमिनं ददर्श Ku. 3. 44; जडीकृतस्त्र्यम्बकवीक्षणेन R. 2. 42, 3. 49.<BR> ˚सखः an epithet of Kubera; कुबेरस्त्र्यम्बकसखः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बका|त्र्यंबका
त्रि + -अम्बका an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यशीत
त्रि + -अशीत <i>a.</i> eighty-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यशीतिः|त्र्यशीति
त्रि + -अशीतिः <i>f.</i> eighty-three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यष्टन्
त्रि + -अष्टन् <i>a.</i> twenty-four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यश्र
त्रि + -अश्र, -अस्र <i>a.</i> triangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यस्रम्
त्रि + -अश्र, -अस्र + .({@-स्रम्@}) a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यस्र
त्रि + -अश्र, -अस्र <i>a.</i> triangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यहः|त्र्यह
त्रि + -अहः<BR>—1 a period of three days.<BR>—2 a festival lasting three days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यार्षेयाः
त्रि + -आर्षेयाः deaf, dumb and blind persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्याहिक|त्र्याहिकः
त्रि + -आहिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 performed or produced in three days.<BR>—2 recurring after the third day, tertian (as fever).<BR>—3 having provision for three days कुशूलकुम्भीधान्यो वा त्र्याहिकोऽश्वस्तनोऽपि<BR> वा Y. 1. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यृचम्
त्रि + -ऋचम् + ({@-तृचम्@} also) three <i>Ṛks</i> taken collectively; Ms. 8. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृचम्
त्रि + -ऋचम् + ({@-तृचम्@} also) three <i>Ṛks</i> taken collectively; Ms. 8. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यैहिक
त्रि + -ऐहिक <i>a.</i> having provision for three days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुद्
त्रि + -ककुद् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of the mountain Trikūṭa.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—3 the highest, chief.<BR>—4 a sacrifice lasting for ten nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुभ्
त्रि + -ककुभ् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Indra.<BR>—2 Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकटु
त्रि + -कटु dry ginger, black pepper and long pepper taken together<BR> as a drug; शिरामोक्षं विधायास्य दद्यात् त्रिकटुकं गुडम् Śālihotra 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्टः|त्रिकण्ट|त्रिकण्टं
त्रि + -कण्टः, -कण्टकः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्टकः|त्रिकण्टक
त्रि + -कण्टः, -कण्टकः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकरणी
त्रि + -करणी the side of a square 3 times as great as another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकर्मन्|त्रिकर्म्मन्
त्रि + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> the chief three duties of a Brāhmaṇa <i>i. e.</i><BR> sacrifice, study of the Vedas, and making gifts or charity. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR> one who engages in these three duties (as a Brāhmaṇa).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">Page0789-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकाण्डम्
त्रि + -काण्डम् N. of Amarsiṃhaʼs dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकायः|त्रिकाय
त्रि + -कायः N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालम्
त्रि + -कालम्<BR>—1 the three times; the past, the present, and the future; or morning,<BR> noon and evening.<BR>—2 the three tenses (the past, present, and future) of a verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालम्
त्रि + -कालम् + .({@-लम्@}) <i>ind.</i> three times, thrice; ˚ज्ञ, ˚दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> omniscient. (<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a divine sage, seer.<BR>—2 a deity.<BR>—3 N. of Buddha. ˚विद् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a Buddha.<BR>—2 an Arhat (with the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकूटः|त्रिकूट|त्रिकूटं
त्रि + -कूटः N. of a mountain in Ceylon on the top of which was situated<BR> Laṅkā, the capital of Rāvaṇa; Śi. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकूटम्
त्रि + -कूटम् sea-salt. {@कूर्चकम्@} a knife with three edges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकोण|त्रिकोणं|त्रिकोणः
त्रि + -कोण <i>a.</i> triangular, forming a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकोणः|त्रिकोण|त्रिकोणं
त्रि + -कोण + .({@-णः@})<BR>—1 a triangle.<BR>—2 the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिखम्
त्रि + -खम्<BR>—1 tin.<BR>—2 a cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिखट्वम्
त्रि + -खट्वम्, -खट्वी three bed-steads taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिखट्वी
त्रि + -खट्वम्, -खट्वी three bed-steads taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिक्षाराणि
त्रि + -क्षाराणि <i>n.</i> (pl.) salt-petre, natron and borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगणः|त्रिगण
त्रि + -गणः an aggregate of the three objects of worldly existence;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> धर्म, अर्थ and का; न बाधतेऽस्य त्रिगणः परस्परम्<BR> Ki. 1. 11; see त्रिवर्ग below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगत
त्रि + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 tripled.<BR>—2 done in three days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्ताः
त्रि + -गर्ताः (pl.)<BR>—1 N. of a country, also called जलन्धर, in the north-west of India.<BR>—2 the people or rulers of that country.<BR>—3 a particular mode of calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्ता|त्रिगर्त्ता
त्रि + -गर्ता<BR>—1 a lascivious woman, wanton.<BR>—2 a woman in general.<BR>—3 a pearl.<BR>—4 a kind of cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुण|त्रिगुणं
त्रि + -गुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 consisting of three threads; व्रताय मौञ्जीं त्रिगुणां वभार याम् Ku. 5. 10.<BR>—2 three-times repeated, thrice, treble, threefold, triple; सप्त व्यतीयुस्त्रिगुणानि<BR> तस्य (दिनानि) R. 2. 25.<BR>—3 containing the three Guṇas सत्त्व, रजस् and तमस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणम्
त्रि + -गुण + .({@-णम्@}) the Pradhāna (in Sāṅ. phil.); ━(<i>ind.</i>) three times; in three ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणाः
त्रि + -गुण + -णाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the three qualities or constituents of nature;<BR> त्रयीमयाय त्रिगुणात्मने नमः K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणा
त्रि + -गुण + -णाः + .({@-णा@})<BR>—1 Māyā or illusion (in Vedānta phil.).<BR>—2 an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणाकृतम्
त्रि + -गुणाकृतम् ploughed thrice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचक्षुस्
त्रि + -चक्षुस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचतुर
त्रि + -चतुर <i>a.</i> (pl.) three or four; गत्वा जवात्त्रिचतुराणि पदानि<BR> सीता B. R. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचत्वारिंश
त्रि + -चत्वारिंश <i>a.</i> forty-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचत्वारिंशत्
त्रि + -चत्वारिंशत् <i>f</i>, forty-three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजगत्
त्रि + -जगत् <i>n.</i>, {@-जगती@}<BR> the three worlds, (1) the heaven, the atmosphere and the<BR> earth; or (2) the heaven, the earth, and the lower world; त्वत्कीर्तिः … … त्रिजगति<BR> विहरत्येवमुवींश गुर्वी Sūkti. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजटः|त्रिजट
त्रि + -जटः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजटा
त्रि + -जटा N. of a female demon, one of the Rākṣasa attendants kept<BR> by Rāvaṇa to watch over Sītā, when she was retained as a captive in<BR> the Aśoka-vanikā. She acted very kindly towards Sītā and induced her<BR> companions to do the same; सीतां मायेति शंसन्ती त्रिजटा समजीवयत् R. 12. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजातम्
त्रि + -जातम्, -जातकम् The three spices (mace, cardamoms, cinnamon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजातकम्
त्रि + -जातम्, -जातकम् The three spices (mace, cardamoms, cinnamon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजीवा
त्रि + -जीवा, -ज्या the sine of three signs or 90°, a radius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिज्या
त्रि + -जीवा, -ज्या the sine of three signs or 90°, a radius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणता
त्रि + -णता a bow; कामुकानिव नालीकांस्त्रिणताः सहसामुचन् Śi. 19. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणव
त्रि + -णव, -णवन् <i>a.</i> (pl.) three times nine; <i>i. e.</i> 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणवन्
त्रि + -णव, -णवन् <i>a.</i> (pl.) three times nine; <i>i. e.</i> 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाकः|त्रिणाक
त्रि + -णाकः the heaven; तावत्त्रिणाकं नहुषः शशास Bhāg. 6. 13. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाचिकेतः|त्रिणाचिकेत
त्रि + -णाचिकेतः<BR>—1 a part of the Adhvaryu-sacrifice or Yajurveda, or one who performs<BR> a vow connected therewith (according to Kull. on Ms. 3. 185); Mb. 13. 90. 26.<BR>—2 one who has thrice kindled the Nāchiketa fire or studied the Nāchiketa<BR> section of Kāṭhaka; त्रिणाचिकेत-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">Page0790-1</a>]<BR> -स्त्रिभिरेत्य सन्धिम् Kaṭh. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0789-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणीता
त्रि + -णीता a wife (‘thrice married’; it being supposed that a girl<BR> belongs to <i>Soma, Gandharva</i> and <i>Agni</i> before she obtains a human husband).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणेमि
त्रि + -णेमि <i>a.</i> with three fellies; विचिन्वतोऽभूत् सुमहांस्त्रिणेमिः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितक्षम्
त्रि + -तक्षम्, -तक्षी three carpenters taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितक्षी
त्रि + -तक्षम्, -तक्षी three carpenters taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डम्
त्रि + -दण्डम्<BR>—1 the three staves of a <i>Saṃnyāsin</i> (who has resigned the world)<BR> tied together so as to form one.<BR>—2 the triple subjection of thought, word, and deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डः|त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदंड
त्रि + -दण्डम् + .({@-ण्डः@}) the state of a religious ascetic; ज्ञानवैराग्यरहितस्त्रिदण्डमुपजीवति<BR> Bhāg. 11. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डिन्|त्रिदंडिन्
त्रि + -दण्डिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a religious mendicant or <i>Saṃnyāsin</i> who has renounced all worldly<BR> attachments, and who carries three long staves tied together so as to<BR> form one in his right hand; तल्लिप्सुः स यतिर्भूत्वा त्रिदण्डी द्वारकामगात्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 86. 3.<BR>—2 one who has obtained command over his mind, speech, and body (or thought,<BR> word, and deed); cf. वाग्दण्डोऽथ मनोदण्डः कायदण्डस्तथैव च । यस्यैते<BR> निहिता बुद्धौ त्रिदण्डीति स उच्यते ॥ Ms. 12. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाः
त्रि + -दशाः (pl.)<BR>—1 thirty.<BR>—2 the thirty-three gods:−<BR> 12 Ādityas, 8 Vasus, 11 Rudras and 2 Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशः|त्रिदश
त्रि + -दशाः + .({@-शः@}) a god, an immortal; तस्मिन्मघोनस्त्रिदशान्विहाय सहस्रमक्ष्णां<BR> युगपत्पपात Ku. 3. 1. ˚अङ्कुशः (-शम्) the heaven. ˚आयुधम्<BR> Indraʼs thunderbolt; R. 9. 54. ˚आयुधम् rainbow; अथ नभस्य इव<BR> त्रिदशायुधम् R. 9. 54. ˚अधिपः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚पतिः epithets of Indra.<BR> ˚अधिपतिः N. of Śiva. ˚अध्यक्षः, ˚अयनः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> ˚अरिः a demon. ˚आचार्यः an epithet of Bṛhaspati. ˚आधार<BR> Nectar. ˚आलयः, ˚आवासः<BR>—1 heaven.<BR>—2 the mountain Meru.<BR>—3 a god. ˚आहारः ‘the food of the gods’, nectar. ˚इन्द्रः<BR>—1 Indra.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR>—3 Brahman. ˚गुरुः an epithet of Bṛhaspati, ˚गोपः a kind of<BR> insect; (cf. इन्द्रगोप) श्रद्दधे त्रिदशगोपमात्रके दाहशक्तिमिव<BR> कृष्णवर्त्मनि R. 11. 42. ˚दीर्घिका an epithet of the Ganges. ˚पतिः<BR> Indra; एषोऽप्यैरावतस्थस्त्रिदशपतिः Ratn. 4. 11. ˚पुङ्गवः Viṣṇu;<BR> Rām. 1. ˚मञ्जरी the holy basil. ˚वधू, ˚वनिता, an Apsaras or<BR> heavenly damsel; कैलासस्य त्रिदशवनितादर्पणस्यातिथिः स्याः Me. 60.<BR> ˚वर्त्मन् the sky. ˚श्रेष्ठः<BR>—1 Agni.<BR>—2 Brahman. ˚दशीभूत Become divine; त्रिदशीभूतपौराणां स्वर्गान्तरमकल्पयत् R. 15. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिनम्
त्रि + -दिनम् three days collectively. ˚स्पृश् <i>m.</i> concurrence of<BR> three lunations with one solar day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवम्
त्रि + -दिवम्<BR>—1 the heaven; त्रिमार्गयेव त्रिदिवस्य मार्गः Ku. 1. 28; Ś. 7. 3.<BR>—2 sky, atmosphere.<BR>—3 paradise.<BR>—4 happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवा
त्रि + -दिवम् + .({@-वा@}) cardamoms. ˚अधीशः, ˚ईशः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 a god. ˚आलयः the heaven; अश्वमेधजिताँल्लोकानाप्नोति त्रिदिवालये<BR> Mb. 13. 141. 53. ˚उद्भवा<BR>—1 the Ganges.<BR>—2 small cardamoms. ˚ओकस् <i>m.</i> a god; वपुषि त्रिदिवौकसां परं<BR> सह पुष्पैरपतञ्छिलीमुखाः Vikr. 15. 72. ˚गत dead; त्रिदिवगतः<BR> किमु वक्ष्यते पिता मे Vikr. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदृश्
त्रि + -दृश् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषम्
त्रि + -दोषम् vitiation or derangement of the three humours of the body,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> वात, पित्त and कफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधा
त्रि + -धा <i>ind.</i> in 3 parts, ways or places; triply. ˚त्वम् tripartition; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातुः|त्रिधातु
त्रि + -धातुः an epithet of Gaṇeśa;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातुम्
त्रि + -धातुम्<BR>—1 the triple world.<BR>—2 the aggregate of the 3 minerals or humours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधामन्
त्रि + -धामन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Vyāsa;<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR>—4 of Agni.<BR>—5 death. ━<i>n.</i> the heaven; हंसो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">Page0790-2</a>]<BR> हंसेन यानेन त्रिधाम परमं ययौ Bhāg. 3. 24. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधारा
त्रि + -धारा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनयन|त्रिनयनः
त्रि + -नयन, -नेत्रः, -लोचनः epithets of Śiva; R. 3. 66; Ku. 3. 66, 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्रः|त्रिनेत्र
त्रि + -नयन, -नेत्रः, -लोचनः epithets of Śiva; R. 3. 66; Ku. 3. 66, 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचनः|त्रिलोचन
त्रि + -नयन, -नेत्रः, -लोचनः epithets of Śiva; R. 3. 66; Ku. 3. 66, 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनवत
त्रि + -नवत <i>a.</i> ninety-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनवतिः|त्रिनवति
त्रि + -नवतिः <i>f.</i> ninety three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनयना
त्रि + -नयना Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनाभः|त्रिनाभ
त्रि + -नाभः Viṣṇu; Bhāg. 8. 17. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्रचूडामणिः|त्रिनेत्रचूडामणि
त्रि + -नेत्रचूडामणिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्रफलः|त्रिनेत्रफल
त्रि + -नेत्रफलः the cocoa-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपञ्च|त्रिपंच
त्रि + -पञ्च <i>a.</i> three-fold five, <i>i. e.</i> fifteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपञ्चाश|त्रिपंचाश
त्रि + -पञ्चाश <i>a.</i> fifty-third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपञ्चाशत्|त्रिपंचाशत्
त्रि + -पञ्चाशत् <i>f.</i> fifty-three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपटुः|त्रिपटु
त्रि + -पटुः glass (काच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपताकः|त्रिपताक|त्रिपताकं
त्रि + -पताकः<BR>—1 the hand with three fingers stretched out or erect.<BR>—2 the forehead marked naturally with three horizontal lines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपत्रकः|त्रिपत्रक
त्रि + -पत्रकः the Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथम्
त्रि + -पथम्<BR>—1 the three paths taken collectively, <i>i. e.</i> the sky, atmosphere,<BR> and the earth, or the sky, earth and the lower world.<BR>—2 a place where three roads meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथा
त्रि + -पथम् + .({@-था@}) an epithet of Mathura. ˚गा, ˚गामिनी an epithet of the<BR> Ganges; गङ्गा त्रिपथगामिनी; धृतसत्पथस्त्रिपथगामभितः स तमारुरोह<BR> पुरुहूतसुतः Ki. 6. 1; Amaru. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपद्
त्रि + -पद्, -पाद्, -पात् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 fever (personified).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाद्
त्रि + -पद्, -पाद्, -पात् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 fever (personified).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपात्
त्रि + -पद्, -पाद्, -पात् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 fever (personified).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपद
त्रि + -पद <i>a.</i> three-footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपदम्
त्रि + -पद + .({@-दम्@}) a tripod; त्रिपदैः करकैः स्थालैः … …<BR> Śiva B. 22. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपदिका
त्रि + -पदिका<BR>—1 a tripod.<BR>—2 a stand with three feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपदी
त्रि + -पदी<BR>—1 the girth of an elephant; नास्रसत्करिणां ग्रैवं त्रिपदीच्छेदिनामपि R. 4. 48.<BR>—2 the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>—3 a tripod.<BR>—4 the plant गोधापदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपरिक्रान्त
त्रि + -परिक्रान्त <i>a.</i> one who walks thrice round a sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपर्णः|त्रिपर्ण
त्रि + -पर्णः Kiṃśuka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाटः|त्रिपाट
त्रि + -पाटः<BR>—1 intersection of a prolonged side and perpendicular (in a quadrangular figure).<BR>—2 the figure formed by such intersection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाटिका
त्रि + -पाटिका a beak. पाठिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 familiar with Saṃhitā, Pada, and Krama.<BR>—2 one who learns a thing after three repetitions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपादः|त्रिपाद
त्रि + -पादः<BR>—1 the Supreme Being.<BR>—2 fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाद्
त्रि + -पाद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having three feet.<BR>—2 consisting of three parts, having three fourths; राघवः शिथिलं<BR> तस्थौ भुवि धर्मस्त्रिपादिव R. 15. 96.<BR>—3 trinomial. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu in his dwarf incarnation.<BR>—2 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिटकम्
त्रि + -पिटकम् the 3 collections of Buddhistic sacred writings (सुत्त,<BR> विनय and अभिधम्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुट|त्रिपुटः
त्रि + -पुट <i>a.</i> triangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटः|त्रिपुट
त्रि + -पुट + .({@-टः@})<BR>—1 an arrow.<BR>—2 the palm of the hand.<BR>—3 a cubit.<BR>—4 a bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटकः|त्रिपुटक
त्रि + -पुटकः a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटा
त्रि + -पुटा an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटिन्
