त्रिपुण्ड्रम्
त्रि + -पुण्ड्रम्, -पुण्ड्रक a mark on the forehead consisting of three<BR> lines made with cowdung ashes<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्रक|त्रिपुण्ड्रकं
त्रि + -पुण्ड्रम्, -पुण्ड्रक a mark on the forehead consisting of three<BR> lines made with cowdung ashes<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरम्
त्रि + -पुरम्<BR>—1 a collection of three cities.<BR>—2 the three cities of gold, silver, and iron in the sky, air and earth<BR> built for demons by Maya; (these cities were burnt down, along the demons<BR> inhabiting them, by Śiva at the request of the gods); Ku. 7. 48; Amaru. 2;<BR> संरक्ताभिस्त्रिपुरविजयो गीयते किन्नरीभिः Me. 56; Bh. 3. 123;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरः|त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं
त्रि + -पुरम् + .({@-रः@}) N. of a demon or demons presiding over these cities. ˚अधिपतिः<BR> N. of Maya, ˚अन्तकः, ˚अरिः, ˚घ्नः, ˚दहनः, ˚द्विष् <i>m.</i>, हरः<BR> &c. epithets of Śiva; अये गौरीनाथ त्रिपुरहर शम्भो त्रिनयन Bh. 3. 123;<BR> R. 17. 14. ˚दाहः burning of the three cities; मुहुरनुस्मरयन्तमनुक्षपं<BR> त्रिपुरदाहमुमापतिसेविनः Ki. 5. 14. ˚सुन्दरी Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरी
त्रि + -पुरम् + .({@-री@})<BR>—1 N. of a place near Jabalpura, formerly capital of the kings of Chedi.<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुष
त्रि + -पुरुष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the length of three men.<BR>—2 having three assistants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुषम्
त्रि + -पुरुष + .({@-षम्@}) the three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">Page0791-1</a>]<BR> ancestors-father, grand-father and great-grand-father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0790-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपृष्ठम्
त्रि + -पृष्ठम् the highest heaven; Bhāg. 1. 19. 23. ({@ष्ठः@}) Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपौरुष
त्रि + -पौरुष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to, or extending over, three generations of men.<BR>—2 offered to three (as oblations). —3 inherited from three (as an estate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिप्रस्रुतः|त्रिप्रस्रुत
त्रि + -प्रस्रुतः an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिफला
त्रि + -फला (1) the three myrobalans taken collectively, namely, Terminalia<BR> Chebula, T. Bellerica, and Phyllanthus (Mar. हिरडा, बेहडा and आंवळकाठी).<BR> Also (2) the three sweet fruits (grape, pomegranate, and date); (3) the<BR> three fragrant fruits (nutmeg, areca-nut, and cloves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबन्धनः|त्रिबन्धन|त्रिबंधन
त्रि + -बन्धनः the individual soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबलिः|त्रिबलि
त्रि + -बलिः, -बली, -वलिः, -वली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the three folds or wrinkles of skin above the navel of a woman (regarded<BR> as a mark of beauty); क्षामोदरोपरिलसत्त्रिवलीलतानाम् Bh. 1. 93, 81;<BR> cf. Ku. 1. 39.<BR>—2 the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबली
त्रि + -बलिः, -बली, -वलिः, -वली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the three folds or wrinkles of skin above the navel of a woman (regarded<BR> as a mark of beauty); क्षामोदरोपरिलसत्त्रिवलीलतानाम् Bh. 1. 93, 81;<BR> cf. Ku. 1. 39.<BR>—2 the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबलीकम्
त्रि + -बलीकम् the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबाहुः|त्रिबाहु
त्रि + -बाहुः a kind of fighting with swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिब्रह्मन्
त्रि + -ब्रह्मन् <i>a.</i> with ब्रह्मा, विष्णु and महेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभम्
त्रि + -भम् three signs of the zodiac, or ninety degrees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभङ्गम्
त्रि + -भङ्गम् a pose in which the image is bent at three parts of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभद्रम्
त्रि + -भद्रम् copulation, sexual union, cohabitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभागः|त्रिभाग
त्रि + -भागः<BR>—1 the third part; त्रिभागं ब्रह्महत्यायाः कन्या प्राप्नोति दुष्यती<BR> Mb. 12. 165. 42.<BR>—2 the third part of a sign of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुक्ल
त्रि + -भुक्ल <i>a.</i> one possessed of learning, good conduct and good<BR> family-descent (Dānasāgara, Bibliotheca Indica, 274, Fasc. 1, p. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुजम्
त्रि + -भुजम् a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुवनम्
त्रि + -भुवनम् the three worlds; पुण्यं यायास्त्रिभुवनगुरोर्धाम चण्डीश्वरस्य<BR> Me. 35; Bh. 1. 99. ˚गुरु Śiva. ˚कीर्तिरसः a patent medicine<BR> in Āyurveda. ˚पतिः Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभूमः|त्रिभूम
त्रि + -भूमः a palace with three floors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमद|त्रिमदः
त्रि + -मद the three narcotic plants; the three-fold haughtiness; Bhāg. 3. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमधु|त्रिमधुः
त्रि + -मधु <i>n.</i>, {@-मधुरम्@}<BR>—1 sugar, honey, and ghee.<BR>—2 three verses of the Ṛgveda (1. 90. 6-8; मधु वाता ऋतायते˚).<BR>—3 a ceremony based on the same; L. D. B.<BR>—4 threefold utterance of a vedic stanza ˚मधु वाता ━<i>m.</i> a reciter<BR> and performer of the above ceremony; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमार्गा
त्रि + -मार्गा the Ganges; त्रिमार्गयेव त्रिदिवस्य मार्गः Ku. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुकुटः|त्रिमुकुट
त्रि + -मुकुटः the Trikūṭa mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुखः|त्रिमुख
त्रि + -मुखः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुनि
त्रि + -मुनि <i>ind.</i> having the three sages पाणिनि, कात्यायन and<BR> पतञ्जलि; त्रिमुनि व्याकरणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्तिः|त्रिमूर्ति|त्रिमूर्त्ति|त्रिमूर्त्तिः
त्रि + -मूर्तिः<BR>—1 the united form of Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and Maheśa, the Hindu triad;<BR> नमस्त्रिमूर्तये तुभ्यं प्राक्सृष्टेः केवलात्मने । गुणत्रयविभागाय पश्चाद्भेदमुपेयुषे ॥ Ku. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Buddha, or Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्धन्
त्रि + -मूर्धन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a demon; त्रयश्च दूषणखरस्त्रिमूर्धानो रणे हताः U. 2. 15.<BR>—2 a world called महर्लोक; Gīrvāṇa.; cf. अमृतं क्षेममभयं<BR> त्रिमूर्ध्नोऽधायि मूर्धसु Bhāg. 2. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियव
त्रि + -यव <i>a.</i> weighing 3 barley corns; Ms. 8. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियष्टिः|त्रियष्टि
त्रि + -यष्टिः a necklace of three strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामकम्
त्रि + -यामकम् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामा
त्रि + -यामा<BR>—1 night (consisting of 3 watches or <i>praharas</i>, the first and last<BR> half <i>prahara</i> being excluded); संक्षिप्येत क्षण इव कथं दीर्घयामा<BR> त्रियामा Me. 110; Ku. 7. 21, 26; R. 9. 70; V. 3. 22.<BR>—2 turmeric.<BR>—3 the Indigo plant.<BR>—4 the river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियुगः|त्रियुग
त्रि + -युगः an epithet of Viṣṇu; धर्मं महापुरुष पासि युगानुवृत्तं<BR> छन्नः कलौ यदभवस्त्रियुगोऽथ सत्त्वम् Bhāg. 7. 9. 38; the god in<BR> the form of यज्ञपुरुष; Bhāg. 5. 18. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियोनिः|त्रियोनि
त्रि + -योनिः a law-suit (in which a person engages from anger, covetousness,<BR> or infatuation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरसकम्
त्रि + -रसकम् spirituous liquor;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">Page0791-2</a>]<BR> see त्रिसरकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरात्र|त्रिरात्रं|त्रिरात्रः
त्रि + -रात्र <i>a.</i> lasting for three nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरात्रः|त्रिरात्र|त्रिरात्रं
त्रि + -रात्र + .({@-त्रः@}) a festival lasting for three nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरात्रम्
त्रि + -रात्र + .({@-त्रम्@}) a period of three nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरेखः|त्रिरेख
त्रि + -रेखः a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलिङ्ग|त्रिलिंग
त्रि + -लिङ्ग <i>a.</i> having three genders, <i>i. e.</i> an adjective.<BR>—2 possessing the three Guṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलिङ्गाः
त्रि + -लिङ्ग + .({@-गाः@}) the country called Telaṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलिङ्गी|त्रिलिंगी
त्रि + -लिङ्ग + .({@-गी@}) the three genders taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकम्
त्रि + -लोकम् the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकः|त्रिलोक
त्रि + -लोकम् + .({@-कः@}) an inhabitant of the three worlds; यद्धर्मसूनोर्बत<BR> राजसूये निरीक्ष्य दृक्स्वस्त्ययनं त्रिलोकः Bhāg. 3. 2. 13. ˚आत्मन्<BR> <i>m.</i> the Supreme Being. ˚ईशः the sun. ˚नाथः ‘lord of the three worlds’<BR>, an epithet of<BR>—1 Indra; त्रिलोकनाथेन सदा मखद्विषस्त्वया नियम्या ननु दिव्यचक्षुषा R. 3. 45.<BR>—2 of Śiva; Ku. 5. 77. ˚रक्षिन् <i>a.</i> protecting the 3 worlds; त्रिलोकरक्षी<BR> महिमा हि वज्रिणः V. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकी
त्रि + -लोकी the three worlds taken collectively, the universe; सत्यामेव<BR> त्रिलोकीसरिति हरशिरश्चुम्बिनीविच्छटायाम् Bh. 3. 95; Śānti. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचनः|त्रिलोचन
त्रि + -लोचनः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचना
त्रि + -लोचनः + .({@-ना@})<BR>—1 an unchaste woman.<BR>—2 an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोहकम्
त्रि + -लोहकम् the three metals:− gold, silver, and copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्गः|त्रिवर्ग
त्रि + -वर्गः<BR>—1 the three objects of wordly existence, <i>i. e.</i> धर्म, अर्थ, and<BR> काम; अनेन धर्मः सविशेषमद्य मे त्रिवर्गसारः प्रतिभाति भाविनि<BR> Ku. 5. 38; अन्योन्यानुबन्धम् (त्रिवर्गम्) Kau. A. 1. 7; प्राप<BR> त्रिवर्गं बुबुधेऽत्रिवर्गम् (मोक्षम्) Bu. C. 2. 41.<BR>—2 the three states of loss, stability, and increase; क्षयः स्थानं<BR> च वृद्धिश्च त्रिवर्गो नीतिवेदिनाम् Ak.<BR>—3 the three qualities of nature, <i>i. e.</i> सत्त्व, रजस्, and तमस्.<BR>—4 the three higher castes.<BR>—5 the three myrobalans.<BR>—6 propriety, decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्णकम्
त्रि + -वर्णकम् the first three of the four castes of Hindus taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्ष
त्रि + -वर्ष <i>a.</i> three years old; Ms. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवलिः|त्रिवलि
त्रि + -वलिः, -वली <i>f.</i> (in comp.) three folds over a womanʼs navel<BR> (regarded as a mark of beauty)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवली
त्रि + -वलिः, -वली <i>f.</i> (in comp.) three folds over a womanʼs navel<BR> (regarded as a mark of beauty)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवली
त्रि + -वली the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवारम्
त्रि + -वारम् <i>ind.</i> three times, thrice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविक्रमः|त्रिविक्रम
त्रि + -विक्रमः Viṣṇu in his fifth or dwarf incarnation. ˚रसः<BR> a patent medicine in Āyurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविद्यः|त्रिविद्य
त्रि + -विद्यः a Brāhmaṇa versed in the three Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविध
त्रि + -विध <i>a.</i> of three kinds, three-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टपम्
त्रि + -विष्टपम्, -पिष्टपम्<BR>—1 the world of Indra, heaven; त्रिविष्टपस्येव पतिं जयन्तः R. 6. 78.<BR>—2 the three worlds. ˚सद् <i>m.</i> a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टपम्
त्रि + -विष्टपम्, -पिष्टपम्<BR>—1 the world of Indra, heaven; त्रिविष्टपस्येव पतिं जयन्तः R. 6. 78.<BR>—2 the three worlds. ˚सद् <i>m.</i> a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्
त्रि + -वृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 threefold; मौञ्जी त्रिवृत्समा श्लक्ष्णा कार्या विप्रस्य मेखला Ms. 2. 42.<BR>—2 consisting of three parts (as three गुणs, विद्याs); Bhāg. 3. 24. 33, 10. 23. 39;<BR> (consisting of three letters -ओङ्कार); हिरण्यगर्भो<BR> वेदानां मन्त्राणां प्रणवस्त्रिवृत् Bhāg. 11. 16. 12. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a sacrifice.<BR>—2 a girdle of three strings; Mb. 12. 47. 44.<BR>—3 an amulet of three strings. ━(<i>f.</i>) a plant possessing valuable purgative<BR> properties. ˚करण combining three things, <i>i. e.</i> earth, water, and fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्तिः|त्रिवृत्ति
त्रि + -वृत्तिः livelihood through 3 things (sacrifice, study and alms).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणिः|त्रिवेणि
त्रि + -वेणिः, -वेणी <i>f.</i> the place near Prayāga where the Ganges joins<BR> the Yamunā and receives under ground the Sarasvatī; the place called<BR> दक्षिणप्रयाग where the three sacred rivers separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणी
त्रि + -वेणिः, -वेणी <i>f.</i> the place near Prayāga where the Ganges joins<BR> the Yamunā and receives under ground the Sarasvatī; the place called<BR> दक्षिणप्रयाग where the three sacred rivers separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणुः|त्रिवेणु
त्रि + -वेणुः<BR>—1 The staff (त्रिदण्ड) of a Saṃnyāsin; केचित् त्रिवेणुं जगृहुरेके<BR> पात्रं कमण्डलुम् Bhāg. 11. 23. 34.<BR>—2 The pole of a chariot; अथ त्रिवेणुसंपन्नं … … बभञ्ज च महारथम्<BR> Rām. 3. 51. 16; Mb. 7. 156. 83; a three bannered (chariot); Bhāg. 4. 26. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेदः|त्रिवेद
त्रि + -वेदः a Brāhmaṇa versed in the three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">Page0792-1</a>]<BR> Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0791-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशक्तिः|त्रिशक्ति
त्रि + -शक्तिः a deity (त्रिकला), Māyā; Bhāg. 2. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुः|त्रिशङ्कु|त्रिशंकु
त्रि + -शङ्कुः<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated king of the Solar race, king of Ayodhyā and father<BR> of Hariśchandra. [He was a wise, pious, and just king, but his chief<BR> fault was that he loved his person to an inordinate degree. Desiring to<BR> celebrate a sacrifice by virtue of which he could go up to heaven in his<BR> mortal body, he requested his family-priest Vasiṣṭha to officiate for<BR> him; but being refused he next requested his hundred sons who also rejected<BR> his absurd proposal. He, therefore, called them cowardly and impotent,<BR> and was, in return for these insults, cursed and degraded by them to be<BR> a Cāṇḍāla. While he was in this wretched condition, Viśvāmitra,<BR> whose family Triśaṅku had in times of famine laid under deep obligations,<BR> undertook to celebrate the sacrifice, and invited all the gods to be present.<BR> They, however, declined; whereupon the enraged Viśvāmitra by his own<BR> power lifted up Triśaṅku to the skies with his cherished mortal body.<BR> He began to soar higher and higher till his head struck against the vault<BR> of the heaven, when he was hurled down head-foremost by Indra and the<BR> other gods. The mighty Viśvāmitra, however, arrested him in his downward<BR> course, saying ‘Stay Triśaṅku’, and the unfortunate monarch remained<BR> suspended with his head towards the earth as a constellation in the southern<BR> hemisphere. Hence the well-known proverb:− त्रिशङ्कुरिवान्तरा तिष्ठ Ś. 2.]<BR>—2 the Chātaka bird.<BR>—3 a cat.<BR>—4 a grass-hopper.<BR>—5 a fire-fly. ˚जः an epithet of Hariśchandra. ˚याजिन् <i>m.</i><BR> an epithet of Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशत
त्रि + -शत <i>a.</i> three hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशतम्
त्रि + -शत + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 one hundred and three.<BR>—2 three hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशरणः|त्रिशरण
त्रि + -शरणः a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशर्करा
त्रि + -शर्करा three kinds of sugar (गुडोत्पन्ना, हिमोत्था, and मधुरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशाख
त्रि + -शाख <i>a.</i> three-wrinkled; भ्रुकुट्या भीषणमुखः प्रकृत्यैव<BR> त्रिशाखया Ks. 102. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशालम्
त्रि + -शालम् a house with three halls or chambers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिखम्
त्रि + -शिखम्<BR>—1 a trident; तदापतद्वै त्रिशिखं गरुत्मते Bhāg. 10. 59. 9.<BR>—2 a crown or crest (with three points).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिरस्
त्रि + -शिरस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of a demon killed by Rāma.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR>—3 fever. त्रिशिरस्ते प्रसन्नोऽस्मि व्येतु ते मज्ज्वराद्भयम् Bhāg. 10. 63. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्षः|त्रिशीर्ष
त्रि + -शीर्षः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्षकम्
त्रि + -शीर्षकम्, -शूलम् a trident. ˚अङ्कः, ˚धारिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet<BR> of Śiva. शुक्लम् the holy combination of ‘three days’ <i>viz.</i> Uttarāyaṇa<BR> (day of the gods), the bright half of the moon (day of the manes) and<BR> day-time; त्रिशुक्ले मरणं यस्य, L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूलम्
त्रि + -शीर्षकम्, -शूलम् a trident. ˚अङ्कः, ˚धारिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet<BR> of Śiva. शुक्लम् the holy combination of ‘three days’ <i>viz.</i> Uttarāyaṇa<BR> (day of the gods), the bright half of the moon (day of the manes) and<BR> day-time; त्रिशुक्ले मरणं यस्य, L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

