त्रिसरः|त्रिसर
त्रि + -सरः milk, sesamum and rice boiled together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसरकम्
त्रि + -सरकम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">Page0792-2</a>]<BR> drinking wine thrice (‘सरकं शीधुपात्रे स्यात् शीधुपाने च शीधुनि’ इति<BR> विश्वः); प्रातिभं त्रिसरकेण गतानाम् Śi. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसर्गः|त्रिसर्ग
त्रि + -सर्गः the creation of the 3 Guṇas; Bhāg. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसाघन
त्रि + -साघन <i>a.</i> having a threefold causality; R. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसामन्
त्रि + -सामन् <i>a.</i> singing 3 Sāmans (an उद्गातृ); उद्राता तत्र<BR> संग्रामे त्रिसामा दुन्दुभिर्नृप Mb. 12. 98. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसाम्यम्
त्रि + -साम्यम् an equilibrium of the three (qualities); Bhāg. 2. 7. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्णः|त्रिसुपर्ण
त्रि + -सुपर्णः, -सुपर्णम्<BR>—1 N. of the three Ṛgvedic verses (Rv. 10. 114. 3-5).<BR>—2 N. of T. Ār. 10. 48-50. ━<i>a.</i> familiar with or reciting these verses; Ms. 3. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्णम्
त्रि + -सुपर्णः, -सुपर्णम्<BR>—1 N. of the three Ṛgvedic verses (Rv. 10. 114. 3-5).<BR>—2 N. of T. Ār. 10. 48-50. ━<i>a.</i> familiar with or reciting these verses; Ms. 3. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्थली
त्रि + -स्थली the three sacred places: काशी, प्रयाग, and गया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्थानम्
त्रि + -स्थानम् the head, neck and chest together; तन्त्रीलयसमायुक्तं<BR> त्रिस्थानकरणान्वितम् Rām. 7. 71. 15. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 having 3 dwelling places.<BR>—2 extending through the 3 worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रोतस्
त्रि + -स्रोतस् <i>f.</i> an epithet of the Ganges; त्रिस्रोतसं वहति<BR> यो गगनप्रतिष्ठाम् Ś. 7. 6; R. 10. 63; Ku. 7. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसीत्य|त्रिसीत्यं
त्रि + -सीत्य, -हल्य <i>a.</i> ploughed thrice (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहल्य|त्रिहल्यं
त्रि + -सीत्य, -हल्य <i>a.</i> ploughed thrice (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहायण
त्रि + -हायण <i>a.</i> three years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंश|त्रिंशः
त्रिंश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Thirtieth.<BR>—2 Joined with thirty; <i>e. g.</i> त्रिंशं शतम् one hundred and thirty.<BR>—3 Consisting of thirty.<BR>—4 ¹⁄₃₀ of a sign of the zodiac, a degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशक|त्रिंशकः
त्रिंशक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Consisting of thirty.<BR>—2 Bought for or worth thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्
त्रिंशत् <i>f.</i> Thirty.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: त्रिंशत्पत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्पत्रम्
त्रिंशत् + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 A lotus opening at moonrise.<BR>—2 a kind of lotus (the blossom of Nymphaea Esenlalenta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्कम्
त्रिंशत्कम् An aggregate of thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशतिः|त्रिंशति
त्रिंशतिः <i>f.</i> Thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिक|त्रिकं
त्रिक <i>a.</i> [त्रयाणां संघः कन्]<BR>—1 Triple, three-fold.<BR>—2 Forming a triad; अव द्वके अव त्रिका दिवश्चरन्ति भेषजा Rv. 10. 59. 9.<BR>—3 Three per cent; cf. Ms. 8. 152. Kull.<BR>—4 Happening the third time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकम्
त्रिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A triad; भक्तिः परेशानुभवो विरक्तिरन्यत्र चैष त्रिक एककालः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 42.<BR>—2 A place where three roads meet.<BR>—3 The lower part of the spine, the part about the hips; पृष्ठवंशाधरे<BR> त्रिकम् Ak. (Mar. माकडहाड); त्रिके स्थूलता Pt. 1. 190; कश्चिद्विवृत्तत्रिकभिन्नहारः<BR> R. 6. 16; छिन्नत्रिकास्तथा केचित् … Śiva B. 13. 126.<BR>—4 The part between the shoulderblades.<BR>—5 The three spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिका
त्रिक + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 A contrivance for raising water (like a wheel) over which passes the<BR> rope of the bucket.<BR>—2 The cover of a well.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: त्रिकत्रयम्, त्रिकस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकत्रयम्
त्रिक + -त्रयम् the 3 triads (त्रिफला, त्रिकटु and त्रिमद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकस्थानम्
त्रिक + -स्थानम् the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितय|त्रितयं
त्रितय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Consisting of three parts, three-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितयम्
त्रितय + .{@-यम्@} A triad, a group of three; श्रद्धा वित्तं विधिश्चेति त्रितयं<BR> तत्समागतम् Ś. 7. 29; R. 8. 78; Y. 3. 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधा
त्रिधा <i>ind.</i> In three ways, or in three parts; एकैव मूर्तिर्बिभिदे<BR> त्रिधा सा Ku. 7. 44; ज्ञानं कर्म च कर्ता च त्रिधैव गुणभेदतः Bg. 18. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्
त्रिस् <i>ind.</i> Thrice, three times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0792-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुट्
त्रुट् €4. €6 P. (त्रुट्यति, त्रुटति, त्रुटित) To tear, break, fall<BR> asunder, snap, be split (fig. also); गद्गदगलत्त्रुट्यद्विलीनाक्षरम्<BR> Bh. 3. 8, 1. 96; अयं ते बाष्पौघस्त्रुटित इव मुक्तामणिसरः U. 1. 29 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटिः|त्रुटि
त्रुटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [त्रुट्-इन् वा डीप्]<BR>—1 Cutting, tearing.<BR>—2 A small part, an atom.<BR>—3 A very minute space of time equal to ¼ of a <i>Kṣaṇa</i>; or ½ of a<BR> <i>Lava</i>; Mb. 1. 25. 14; Bhāg. 10. 13. 40.<BR>—4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>—5 Loss, destruction.<BR>—6 Small cardamoms (the plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटी
त्रुटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> [त्रुट्-इन् वा डीप्]<BR>—1 Cutting, tearing.<BR>—2 A small part, an atom.<BR>—3 A very minute space of time equal to ¼ of a <i>Kṣaṇa</i>; or ½ of a<BR> <i>Lava</i>; Mb. 1. 25. 14; Bhāg. 10. 13. 40.<BR>—4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>—5 Loss, destruction.<BR>—6 Small cardamoms (the plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटित
त्रुटित <i>p. p.</i> Cut, broken, divided, split &c. अयं तावद् वाष्पस्त्रुटित<BR> इव मुक्तामणिसरः U. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटिः|त्रोटि
त्रोटिः <i>f.</i>, -टी<BR> A bill, beak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: त्रोटिहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटी
त्रोटिः <i>f.</i>, -टी<BR> A bill, beak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: त्रोटिहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटिहस्तः|त्रोटिहस्त
त्रोटिः + -हस्तः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुप्
त्रुप्(फ्), त्रुम्प्(म्फ्) €1 P. (त्रोपति &c.) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्प्|त्रुंप्
त्रुप्(फ्), त्रुम्प्(म्फ्) €1 P. (त्रोपति &c.) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्फ्|त्रुंफ्
त्रुप्(फ्), त्रुम्प्(म्फ्) €1 P. (त्रोपति &c.) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेता
त्रेता<BR>—1 A triad, triplet.<BR>—2 The three sacred fires taken collectively (गार्हपत्य, दक्षिण<BR> and आहवनीय); cf. Ms. 2. 231; Bhāg. 9. 14. 44; त्रेताग्निधूमाग्रमनिन्द्यकीर्तेस्तस्येदमाक्रान्तविमानमार्गम् R. 13. 37.<BR>—3 A particular throw at dice, a cast of three or trey; त्रेताहृतसर्वस्वः Mk. 2. 8.<BR>—4 The second of the four Yugas of the Hindus; see युग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेधा
त्रेधा <i>ind.</i> Trebly, in three ways or parts; तदेकं सत्त्रेधाख्यायते<BR> Śat. Br.; Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 3; (नमः) तुभ्यं त्रेधा स्थितात्मने R. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रै
त्रै €1 Ā. (त्रायते, त्रात or त्राण) To protect, preserve,<BR> rescue or save from, defend from (usually with abl.); क्षतात्किल त्रायत<BR> इत्युदग्रः क्षत्रस्य शब्दो भुवनेषु रूढः R. 2. 53; Bg. 2. 40; Ms. 9. 138;<BR> Bk. 5. 54, 15. 120. ━<i>With</i> {@परि@} to save &c.; परित्रायस्व, परित्रायस्व (in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राण|त्राणं
त्राण <i>p. p.</i> [त्रै कर्मणि क्त, भावे ल्युट् वा] Protected, guarded,<BR> preserved, saved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राणम्
त्राण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Protection, defence, preservation; आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR> Ś. 1. 11; R. 15. 3; Māl. 9. 26.<BR>—2 Shelter, help, refuge.<BR>—3 Protecting, preserving.<BR>—4 An armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात|त्रातं
त्रात <i>p. p.</i> Preserved, saved, protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रातम्
त्रात + .{@-तम्@} Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रातृ
त्रातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A guardian, defender, protector.<BR>—2 Protecting, defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकालिक
त्रैकालिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to the three times, <i>i. e.</i> past, present, and future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकाल्यम्
त्रैकाल्यम्<BR>—1 The three times, past, present, and future, or sunrise, noon and sunset;<BR> कुर्यात्परिचयं योगे त्रैकाल्ये नियतो मुनिः Mb. 12. 240. 25.<BR>—2 Tripartition.<BR>—3 A triad.<BR>—4 The three states (growth, maintenance and decay); Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुणिक
त्रैगुणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Triple, three-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्यम्
त्रैगुण्यम्<BR>—1 The state of consisting of three threads, qualities &c.<BR>—2 Triplicity.<BR>—3 The three Guṇas or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">Page0793-2</a>]<BR> properties (सत्त्व, रजस् and तमस्) taken collectively; त्रैगुण्योद्भवमत्र<BR> लोकचरितं नानारसं दृश्यते M. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैतम्
त्रैतम् Ved. A triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिक
त्रैदशिक <i>a.</i> Divine; relating to the gods; Ms. 2. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिकम्
त्रैदशिक + .{@-कम्@} The part of the hand sacred to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैध|त्रैधं
त्रैध <i>a.</i> Three-fold, triple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैनिष्किक
त्रैनिष्किक <i>a.</i> Worth three niṣkas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुरः|त्रैपुर
त्रैपुरः<BR>—1 The Tripura country.<BR>—2 A ruler or inhabitant of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुरुष
त्रैपुरुष^1 <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Extending to the three male generations.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमातुरः|त्रैमातुर
त्रैमातुरः An epithet of Lakṣmaṇa; त्रैमातुरः कृत्स्नजितास्त्रशस्त्रःसध्प्यङ्<BR> रतः श्रेयसि लक्ष्मणोऽभूत् Bk. 1. 25. Lakṣmaṇa is so called because<BR> he was born to his mother Sumitrā on her eating the sacrificial oblation<BR> given to her by her two co-wives, Kausalyā and Kaikeyī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमासिक
त्रैमासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Three months old; तोकेन जीवहरणं यदुलूकिकायास्त्रैमासिकस्य च<BR> पदा शकटोऽप्रवृत्तः Bhāg. 2. 7. 27.<BR>—2 Lasting for or occurring every three months.<BR>—3 Quarterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमास्यम्
त्रैमास्यम् A period of three months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0793-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

