दक्षिणात्ययः|दक्षिणात्यय
दक्षिण + -अत्ययः a dweller in the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापर
दक्षिण + -अपर <i>a.</i> south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाभिमुख
दक्षिण + -अभिमुख <i>a.</i> facing the south, directed towards the south; Ms. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायनम्
दक्षिण + -अयनम् the sunʼs progress south of the equator, the half year<BR> in which the sun moves from the north to the south, the winter solstice;<BR> सर्वेऽश्वमेधैरीजानास्तेऽन्वयुर्दक्षिणायनम् Mb. 12. 29. 103. रात्रिः<BR> स्याद्दक्षिणायनम् Ms. 1. 67; Bhāg. 5. 21. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणारण्यम्
दक्षिण + -अरण्यम् Daṇḍakāraṇya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणार्धः|दक्षिणार्ध
दक्षिण + -अर्धः<BR>—1 the right hand.<BR>—2 the right or southern side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचार|दक्षिणाचारः
दक्षिण + -आचार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 honest, well-behaved.<BR>—2 a worshipper of Śakti according to the right hand (or purer) ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाम्नायः
दक्षिण + -आम्नायः the southern sacred text (of the Tāntrikas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः|दक्षिणावर्त्त
दक्षिण + -आवर्त <i>a.</i> turning to the right (from the left), (a conch-shell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशा
दक्षिण + -आशा the south. ˚पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Yama.<BR>—2 the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेतर
दक्षिण + -इतर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 left (as hand or foot); तमिमं कुरु दक्षिणेतरं चरणं निर्मितरागमेहि<BR> मे Ku. 4. 19.<BR>—2 northern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेतरा
दक्षिण + -इतर + .({@-रा@}) the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेर्मन्|दक्षिणेर्म्मन्
दक्षिण + -ईर्मन् <i>a.</i> (a deer) wounded on the right side मृगयुमिव<BR> मृगोऽथ दक्षिणेर्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणोत्तर
दक्षिण + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> turned or lying to the south and the north. ˚वृत्तम्<BR> the meridian line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणकालिका
दक्षिण + -कालिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A Tāntrika Deity.<BR>—2 Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपश्चात्
दक्षिण + -पश्चात् <i>ind.</i> to the south-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपश्चिम
दक्षिण + -पश्चिम <i>a.</i> south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपश्चिमा
दक्षिण + -पश्चिम + .({@-मा@}) the south-west; जग्मुर्भरतशार्दूल दिशं दक्षिणपश्चिमाम् Mb. 17. 1. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्व
दक्षिण + -पूर्व, -प्राच् <i>a.</i> south-east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणप्राच्
दक्षिण + -पूर्व, -प्राच् <i>a.</i> south-east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्वा|दक्षिणपूर्व्वा
दक्षिण + -पूर्वा, -प्राची the south-eastern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणप्राची
दक्षिण + -पूर्वा, -प्राची the south-eastern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणभागः|दक्षिणभाग
दक्षिण + -भागः the southern hemisphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणसमुद्रः|दक्षिणसमुद्र
दक्षिण + -समुद्रः, -सागरः the southern ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणसागरः
दक्षिण + -समुद्रः, -सागरः the southern ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणस्थः|दक्षिणस्थ
दक्षिण + -स्थः a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतः
दक्षिणतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the right or south.<BR>—2 To the right hand.<BR>—3 To the south or southward (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 On the right or south of.<BR>—2 In the southern direction (with abl.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 A present or gift to Brāhmaṇas (at the completion of a religious<BR> rite, such as a sacrifice).<BR>—2 Dakṣiṇā regarded as a daughter of Prajāpati and as the wife of<BR> Sacrifice personified; पत्नी सुदक्षिणेत्यासीदध्वरस्येव दक्षिणा R. 1. 31.<BR>—3 A gift, offering or donation in general, fee, remuneration; प्राणदक्षिणा,<BR> गुरुदक्षिणा &c.; cf. also दक्षिणाशब्दश्च परिक्रयार्थो भवति Ś. B. on MS. 10. 2. 38<BR> परिक्रयार्थे हि दक्षिणाशब्दो भवति ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 48.<BR> Etymologically दक्षिणा is so called because it imparts<BR> power or strength to the receiver; दक्षकरणी हि दक्षिणा । दक्षश्च<BR> बलम् । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 45; दक्षिणा नाम दक्षतेरुत्साहकर्मणः ।<BR> दक्षिणा उत्साहिका इति । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 57.<BR>—4 A good milch-cow, prolific cow.<BR>—5 The south.<BR>—6 The southern country, the Deccan.<BR>—7 Fame.<BR>—8 A kind of heroine thus defined:− या गौरवं भयं प्रेम सद्भावं<BR> पूर्वनायके । न मुञ्चत्यन्यसक्तापि सा ज्ञेया दक्षिणा बुधैः ॥.<BR>—9 Completion of any rite.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दक्षिणार्ह, दक्षिणावर्त, दक्षिणाकालः, दक्षिणापथः, दक्षिणाप्रत्यच्, दक्षिणाप्रतीची, दक्षिणापथिक, दक्षिणाप्रवण, दक्षिणाबन्धः, दक्षिणामूर्तिः, दक्षिणायुग्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणार्ह|दक्षिणार्हः
दक्षिणा + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> deserving or worthy of a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः|दक्षिणावर्त्त
दक्षिणा + -आवर्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 curved to the right (a conch-shell &c.); Bhāg. 5. 23. 5.<BR>—2 turned towards the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्तः|दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्त्त
दक्षिणा + -आवर्त + .({@-र्तः@})<BR>—1 the Deccan.<BR>—2 a conch-shell opening to the right; Divyāvadāna 56. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाकालः|दक्षिणाकाल
दक्षिणा + -कालः the time of receiving <i>Dakṣiṇā</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथः|दक्षिणापथ
दक्षिणा + -पथः<BR>—1 the southern part of India, the south or Deccan; अस्ति दक्षिणापथ<BR> विदर्भेषु पद्मपुरं नाम नगरम् Māl. 1.<BR>—2 ‘the path of the दक्षिणा’, <i>i. e.</i> the cow, constituting the sacrificial cow.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">Page0798-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0797-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रत्यच्
दक्षिणा + -प्रत्यच् <i>a.</i> south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रतीची
दक्षिणा + -प्रतीची south-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथिक
दक्षिणा + -पथिक <i>a.</i> belonging to the Deccan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणा + -प्रवण <i>a.</i> inclining to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाबन्धः|दक्षिणाबन्ध
दक्षिणा + -बन्धः (in Sāṅ. phil.) the bondage of ritual or cermonial observances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणामूर्तिः|दक्षिणामूर्ति|दक्षिणामूर्त्ति
दक्षिणा + -मूर्तिः <i>m.</i> a Tāntric form of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायुग्यः|दक्षिणायुग्य
दक्षिणा + -युग्यः the right yoke-horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्
दक्षिणात् <i>ind.</i> On the right, from the south, south ward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाहि
दक्षिणाहि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Far on the right.<BR>—2 Far in the south, to the south of (with abl.); दक्षिणाहि ग्रामात् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीकृ
दक्षिणीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To place on the right side.<BR>—2 To keep the right side towards any one (as a mark of respect); cf. प्रदक्षिण.<BR>—3 To give anything as a sacrificial fee; दक्षिणीकृत्य तं प्रीतो वनमेव<BR> जगाम ह Bhāg. 3. 24. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय, दक्षिण्य <i>a.</i> Worthy of or deserving a sacrificial<BR> gift, such as a Brāhmaṇa or a sage; दक्षिणां देवी दक्षिण्यैः प्रतिग्राहयति<BR> M. 5; दक्षिण्यदिष्टं कृतमार्त्विजीनैः Bk. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण्य|दक्षिण्यः
दक्षिणीय, दक्षिण्य <i>a.</i> Worthy of or deserving a sacrificial<BR> gift, such as a Brāhmaṇa or a sage; दक्षिणां देवी दक्षिण्यैः प्रतिग्राहयति<BR> M. 5; दक्षिण्यदिष्टं कृतमार्त्विजीनैः Bk. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेन
दक्षिणेन <i>ind.</i> On the right side of (with acc. or gen.); दक्षिणेन<BR> वृक्षवाटिकामालाप इव श्रूयते Ś. 1; दक्षिणेन ग्रामस्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दगार्गलम्
दगा(का)र्गलम् Examining the ground in searching for water, or rules<BR> for ascertaining the places of waters; धर्म्यं यशस्यं च वदाम्यतोऽहं<BR> दगार्गलं येन जलोपलब्धिः Bṛ. S. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दकार्गलम्
दगा(का)र्गलम् Examining the ground in searching for water, or rules<BR> for ascertaining the places of waters; धर्म्यं यशस्यं च वदाम्यतोऽहं<BR> दगार्गलं येन जलोपलब्धिः Bṛ. S. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध, -दग्धिका<BR> See under दह्. ˚रथः (= चित्ररथः) N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्ध, -दग्धिका<BR> See under दह्. ˚रथः (= चित्ररथः) N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्
दघ् I. €5 P. (दघ्नोति)<BR>—1 To kill, hurt.<BR>—2 To go, leap.<BR>—3 To protect. ━II. €4 P. (दध्यति) Ved.<BR>—1 To go, flow.<BR>—2 To reach, attain.<BR>—3 To go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्न
दघ्न <i>a.</i> (-घ्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> A termination added to nouns in the sense of ‘reaching to’<BR>, ‘as high or deep as’; ऊरुदघ्नेन पयसोत्तीर्य K.; कीलालव्यतिकरगुल्फदध्नपङ्कः<BR> (मार्गः) Māl. 3. 17, 5. 14; Y. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दङ्घ्|दंघ्
दङ्घ् €1 P. (दङ्घति)<BR>—1 To abandon, leave.<BR>—2 To protect, cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्|दंड्
दण्ड् €10 U. (दण्डयति-ते, दण्डित) To punish, fine, chastise;<BR> (this is one of the 16 roots that govern two accusatives); तान् सहस्रं<BR> च दण्डयेत् Ms. 9. 234, 8. 123; Y. 2. 269; स्थित्यै दण्डयतो दण्डपान् R. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डः|दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः
दण्डः, -ण्डम्<BR> [दण्ड्-अच्]<BR>—1 A stick, staff, rod, mace, club, cudgel; पततु शिरस्यकाण्डयमदण्ड<BR> इवैष भुजः Māl. 5. 31; काष्ठदण्डः.<BR>—2 The sceptre of a king, the rod as a symbol of authority and punishment;<BR> आत्तदण्डः Ś. 5. 8.<BR>—3 The staff given to a twice-born man at the time of investiture with<BR> the sacred thread; cf Ms. 2. 45-48.<BR>—4 The staff of a संन्यासिन् or ascetic.<BR>—5 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>—6 The stem or stalk as of a lotus, tree &c.; U. 1. 31; Māl. 9. 14; the<BR> handle as of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-2" target="_blank">Page0798-2</a>]<BR> umbrella; ब्रह्माण्डच्छत्रदण्डः &c. Dk. 1 (opening verse); राज्यं<BR> स्वहस्तधृतदण्डमिवातपत्रम् Ś. 5. 6; Ku. 7. 89; so कमलदण्ड &c.<BR>—7 The oar of a boat.<BR>—8 An arm or leg (at the end of comp.)<BR>—9 The staff or pole of a banner, a tent &c.<BR>—10 The beam of a plough.<BR>—11 The cross-bar of a lute or a stringed instrument.<BR>—12 The stick with which an instrument is played.<BR>—13 A churning-stick.<BR>—14 Fine; Ms. 8. 341, 9. 229; Y. 2. 237.<BR>—15 Chastisement, corporal punishment, punishment in general; यथापराधदण्डानाम्<BR> R. 1. 6; एवं राजापथ्यकारिषु तीक्ष्णदण्डो राजा Mu. 1; दण्डं दण्डपेषु<BR> पातयेत् Ms. 8. 126; कृतदण्ड स्वयं राज्ञा लेभे शूद्रः सतां गतिम्<BR> R. 15. 23. यथार्हदण्डो (राजा) पूज्यः Kau. A. 1. 4; सुविज्ञातप्रणीतो<BR> हि दण्डः प्रजां धर्मार्थकामैर्योजयति Kau. A. 1. 4<BR>—16 Imprisonment.<BR>—17 Attack, assault, violence, punishment, the last of the four expedients;<BR> see उपाय; सामादीनामुपायानां चतुर्णामपि पण्डिताः । सामदण्डौ प्रशंसन्ति<BR> नित्यं राष्ट्राभिवृद्धये ॥ Ms. 7. 109; cf. Śi. 2. 54.<BR>—18 An army; तस्य दण्डवतो दण्डः स्वदेहान्न व्यशिष्यत R. 17. 62;<BR> Ms. 7. 65, 9. 294; Ki. 2. 15.<BR>—19 A form of military array; Mb. 12. 59. 40.<BR>—20 Subjection, control, restraint; वाग्दण्डोऽथ मनोदण्डः कायदण्डस्तथैव<BR> च । यस्यैते निहिता बुद्धौ त्रिदण्डीति स उच्यते ॥ Ms. 12. 10.<BR>—21 A measure of length equal to 4 Hastas; Bṛ. S. 24. 9.<BR>—22 The penis.<BR>—23 Pride; या चापि न्यस्तदण्डानां तां गतिं व्रज पुत्रक Mb. 7. 78. 25.<BR>—24 The body.<BR>—25 An epithet of Yama.<BR>—26 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—27 N. of Śiva.<BR>—28 An attendant on the sun.<BR>—29 A horse (said to be <i>m.</i> only in this and the preceding four senses).<BR>—30 A particular appearance in the sky (similar to a stick).<BR>—31 An uninterrupted row or series, a line.<BR>—32 Standing upright or erect.<BR>—33 A corner, an angle.<BR>—34 The Science of Govt. विनयमूलो दण्डः, दण्डमूलास्तिस्रो विद्याः Kau. A. 1. 5.<BR>—35 Harm, injury; न्यासो दण्डस्य भूतेषु मनोवाक्कायजस्य यः Bhāg. 7. 15. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दण्डाजिनम्, दण्डाधिपः, दण्डानीकम्, दण्डापतानकः, दण्डावतानकः, दण्डापूपन्यायः, दण्डार्ह, दण्डालसिका, दण्डाख्यम्, दण्डाघातः, दण्डाज्ञा, दण्डाश्रमः, दण्डाश्रमिन्, दण्डासनम्, दण्डकासनम्, दण्डाहतम्, दण्डोद्यमः, दण्डकर्मन्, दण्डकलितम्, दण्डकल्पः, दण्डकाकः, दण्डकाष्ठम्, दण्डग्रहणम्, दण्डघ्न, दण्डचक्रः, दण्डच्छदनम्, दण्डढक्का, दण्डदासः, दण्डदेवकुलम्, दण्डधर, दण्डधार, दण्डधारणम्, दण्डनायकः, दण्डनिधानम्, दण्डनिपातनम्, दण्डनीतिः, दण्डनेतृ, दण्डपः, दण्डपांशुलः, दण्डपाणिः, दण्डपातः, दण्डपातनम्, दण्डपारुष्यम्, दण्डपालः, दण्डपालकः, दण्डपाशकः, दण्डपाशिकः, दण्डपोणम्, दण्डप्रणामः, दण्डबालधिः, दण्डभङ्गः, दण्डभृत्, दण्डमाणवः, दण्डमानवः, दण्डमाथः, दण्डमुखः, दण्डयात्रा, दण्डयामः, दण्डलेशम्, दण्डवधः, दण्डवाचिक, दण्डवादिन्, दण्डवारित, दण्डवासिकः, दण्डवासिन्, दण्डवाहिन्, दण्डविकल्पः, दण्डविधिः, दण्डविष्कम्भः, दण्डव्यूहः, दण्डशास्त्रम्, दण्डहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0798-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डम्
