दन्तुर|दंतुर|दन्तुरः
दन्तुर <i>a.</i> [दन्त-उरच्]<BR>—1 Having long or projecting teeth; शूकरे निहते चैव दन्तुरो जायते<BR> नरः Tv.; Śi. 6. 54.<BR>—2 Jagged, dentated, notched, serrated, uneven (fig. also); अखर्वगर्वस्मितदन्तुरेण Vikr. 1. 50.<BR>—3 Undulatory.<BR>—4 Rising, bristling (as hair).<BR>—5 Overspread, covered with; U. 6. 27.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दन्तुरच्छदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुरच्छदः|दन्तुरच्छद|दंतुरच्छद
दन्तुर + -छदः the lime tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुरित|दंतुरित
दन्तुरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having long or projecting teeth.<BR>—2 Notched, serrated, bristling; केतकिदन्तुरिताशे Gīt. 1; पुलकभर˚ 11; K. 216.<BR>—3 Besmeared, covered with; Māl. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुल
दन्तुल <i>a.</i> Having or furnished with teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्य|दंत्य|दन्त्यः
दन्त्य <i>a.</i> [दन्ते दन्तमूले वा भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Dental.<BR>—2 Suitable to the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्यः|दन्त्य|दंत्य
