दन्ध्वनः|दन्ध्वन
दन्ध्वनः A kind of whistling cane; Mb. 12. 86. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्
दभ्, दम्भ् I. €1. €5 P. (दभति or दभ्नोति, दब्ध; <i>desid.</i><BR> धिप्सति, धीप्सति, दिदभिषति)<BR>—1 To injure, hurt.<BR>—2 To deceive, cheat.<BR>—3 To go. ━II. €10 U. (दम्भयति-ते) To impel, propel, drive onward.<BR> अस्मान् कदा चना दभन् Rv. 1. 84. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ्|दंभ्
दभ्, दम्भ् I. €1. €5 P. (दभति or दभ्नोति, दब्ध; <i>desid.</i><BR> धिप्सति, धीप्सति, दिदभिषति)<BR>—1 To injure, hurt.<BR>—2 To deceive, cheat.<BR>—3 To go. ━II. €10 U. (दम्भयति-ते) To impel, propel, drive onward.<BR> अस्मान् कदा चना दभन् Rv. 1. 84. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दब्धिः|दब्धि
दब्धिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Injury, hurt, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभः|दभ
दभः Ved. Deception, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Little, small; अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य स स्थलीम् Ki. 1. 38; see अदभ्र.<BR>—2 Dull, not sharp; अहो बत मयाऽसाधु कृतं वै दभ्रबुद्धिना Bhāg. 6. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्रः|दभ्र|दभ्रं
दभ्र + .{@-भ्रः@} The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्रम्
दभ्र + .{@-भ्रम्@} Distress; रिपुः स्तेनः स्तेयकृद् दभ्रमेतु Rv. 7. 104. 10<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्रम्
दभ्र + .{@-भ्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> A little, slightly, to some extent; दभ्रं पश्यद्भप<BR> उर्विया विचक्ष Rv. 1. 113. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम् €4 P. (दाम्यति, दमित, दान्त)<BR>—1 To be tamed.<BR>—2 To be calm or tranquil; Ms. 4. 35, 6. 8, 7. 141.<BR>—3 To tame, subdue, conquer, restrain; यमो दाम्यति राक्षसान् Bk. 18. 29;<BR> दमित्वाप्यरिसंघातान् 9. 42, 19, 15. 37.<BR>—4 To pacify. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दमयति-ते)<BR>—1 To tame.<BR>—2 To subdue, conquer, overpower; अस्त्वयं सर्वदमनः सर्वं हि दमयत्यसौ Mb. 1. 74. 8.<BR>—3 To afflict, crush down; अतिभारेण दमयति Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0801-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमः|दम
दमः [दम् भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Taming, subduing.<BR>—2 Self-command, subduing or curbing the passions, self-restraint; Mb. 1. 100. 2;<BR> Bg. 10. 4; (निग्रहो बाह्यवृत्तीनां दम इत्यभिधीयते).<BR>—3 Drawing the mind away from evil deeds or curbing its evil propensities;<BR> (कुत्सितात्कर्मणो विप्र यच्च चित्तनिवारणं स कीर्तितो दमः).<BR>—4 Firmness of mind,<BR>—5 Punishment, fine; चिकित्सकानां सर्वेषां मिथ्या प्रचरतां दमः<BR> Ms. 9. 284, 290, 8. 293; Y. 2. 4; Bhāg. 1. 18. 41.<BR>—6 Mire, mud.<BR>—7 Viṣṇu.<BR>—8 N. of a brother of Damayantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमक|दमकः
दमक <i>a.</i> Taming, subduing, conquering; हस्तिगोश्वोष्ट्रदमकः Ms. 3. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथः|दमथ
दमथः, -थुः<BR> [दम्-भावे-अथच्]<BR>—1 Subduing or curbing the passions, self-restraint. —2 Punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथुः|दमथु
दमथः, -थुः<BR> [दम्-भावे-अथच्]<BR>—1 Subduing or curbing the passions, self-restraint. —2 Punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दम् भावे ल्युट्] Taming, subduing, overpowering,<BR> conquering, defeating; जामदग्न्यस्य दमने नैवं निर्वक्तुमर्हसि<BR> U. 5. 32; Bh. 3. 89; so सर्वदमन, अरिदमन &c.<BR>—2 Tranquil, passionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनः|दमन|दमनं
दमन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A charioteer; Bhāg. 4. 26. 2.<BR>—2 A warrior.<BR>—3 The <i>Kunda</i> plant.<BR>—4 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनम्
दमन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Taming, subjugation, curbing, restraint.<BR>—2 Punishing, chastising, दुर्दान्तानां दमनविधयः क्षत्रियेष्वायतन्ते Mv. 3. 34.<BR>—3 Self-restraint.<BR>—4 Slaying, killing; जामदग्न्यस्य दमने न हि निर्बन्धमर्हसि U. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनकः|दमनक
दमनकः N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयन्ती|दमयंती
दमयन्ती<BR>—1 N. of the daughter of Bhīma, king of the Vidarbhas. [She was so called<BR> because by her matchless beauty she subdued the pride of all lovely women;<BR> cf. N. 2. 18:− भुवनत्रयसुभ्रुवामसौ दमयन्ती कमनीयतामदम् । उदियाय<BR> यतस्तनुश्रिया दमयन्तीति ततोऽभिधां दधौ ॥ A golden swan first described<BR> to her the beauty and virtues of king Nala, and through him she communicated<BR> her love to Nala. Afterwards at the Svayaṃvara she chose Nala for her<BR> husband from out of a host of competitors among whom were the four gods<BR> Indra, Agni, Yama, and Varuṇa themselves, and the lovely pair spent some<BR> years very happily. But their happiness was not destined to last long.<BR> Kali, envious of the good fortune of Nala, entered his body, and induced<BR> him to play at dice with his brother Puṣkara. In the heat of the play<BR> the infatuated monarch staked and lost everything except himself and his<BR> wife. Nala and Damayantī were, therefore, driven out of the kingdom,<BR> ‘clad in a single garment’. While wandering through the wilderness, Damayantī<BR> had to pass through several trying adventures, but her devotion to her<BR> husband remained entirely unshaken. One day while she was asleep, Nala<BR> in the frenzy of despair abandoned her, and she was obliged to go to her<BR> fatherʼs house. After some time she was united with her husband, and they<BR> passed the rest of their lives in the undisturbed enjoyment<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">Page0802-2</a>]<BR> of happiness. See Nala and Ṛtuparṇa also.]<BR>—2 N. of a flowering plant (Mar. मोगरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयितृ
दमयितृ <i>a.</i> [दम्-णिच्-तृच्]<BR>—1 Taming, subduing.<BR>—2 A punisher, chastiser.<BR>—3 An epithet of Viṣṇu, or Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित|दमितः
दमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tamed, calmed, tranquillized.<BR>—2 Conquered, curbed, subdued, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिन्
दमिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tamed, subdued.<BR>—2 Taming, subduing, overpoweing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be trained or tamed; of the age of training; दम्यस्येवार्वतो मुहुः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 20. 21.<BR>—2 To be punished, punishable<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्यः|दम्य
दम्य + .{@-म्यः@}<BR>—1 A young bullock (requiring training and experience); नार्हति तातः<BR> पुङ्गवधारितायां धुरि दम्यं नियोजयितुम् V. 5; गुर्वी धुरं यो भुवनस्य<BR> पित्रा धुर्येण दम्यः सदृशं बिभर्ति R. 6. 78; Mu. 3. 3.<BR>—2 A steer that has to be tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त <i>p. p.</i> [दम्-कर्तरि-क्त]<BR>—1 Tamed, subdued, overpowered, curbed, restrained, bridled; see दम्.<BR>—2 Docile; tame, mild.<BR>—3 Self-possessed, self-controlled; U. 5.<BR>—4 Subdued, conquered, vanquished; तस्मिन्दान्ते कास्तुतिस्तस्य राज्ञः U. 5. 32.<BR>—5 Resigned.<BR>—6 Liberal.<BR>—7 Dental.<BR>—8 Patient of bodily mortifications or austerities &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्तः|दान्त|दांत
दान्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A tamed ox.<BR>—2 A donor.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (दमनक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्तिः|दान्ति|दांति|दांतिः
दान्तिः <i>f.</i> [दम्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Self-restraint, subjection, control.<BR>—2 The patient endurance of bodily mortifications, religious austerities &c.<BR>—3 Humiliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमः|दम
दमः, -मम् Ved.<BR>—1 A house, home; दमेदमे समिधम् Vāj. 8. 24.<BR>—2 The inmates of a house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दमकर्तृ, दमघोषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमम्
दमः, -मम् Ved.<BR>—1 A house, home; दमेदमे समिधम् Vāj. 8. 24.<BR>—2 The inmates of a house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दमकर्तृ, दमघोषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमकर्तृ
दमः + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a lord, ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमघोषः|दमघोष
दमः + -घोषः N. of a king, father of शिशुपाल. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमुनस्
दमु(मू)नस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire; ददौ पुनस्तां दमुनस्यतस्ते (चक्रवाकाः) | तपन्ति<BR> नक्तं न च तस्य भेदाः ॥ Rām. Ch. 6. 20.<BR>—2 N. of Śukra; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमूनस्
दमु(मू)नस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire; ददौ पुनस्तां दमुनस्यतस्ते (चक्रवाकाः) | तपन्ति<BR> नक्तं न च तस्य भेदाः ॥ Rām. Ch. 6. 20.<BR>—2 N. of Śukra; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्पती
दम्पती <i>m.</i> (du.)<BR>—1 The lord of the house (Agni, Indra, the Aśvins); दम्पतीव क्रतुविदा<BR> जनेषु Rv. 2. 39. 2.<BR>—2 (comp. of जाया and पति) Husband and wife; तौ दम्पती वसिष्ठस्य<BR> गुरोर्जग्मतुराश्रमम् R. 1. 35, 2. 70; Ms. 3. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ्|दंभ्
दम्भ् I. €5 P. See दभ्. ━II. <i>Caus.</i> or €10 U. (दम्भयतिते)<BR>—1 To kill, destroy, strike down.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To collect, arrange, string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भः|दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः
दम्भः [दम्भ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Deceit, fraud, trickery; Ms. 4. 163.<BR>—2 Religious hypocrisy; Bg. 16. 4.<BR>—3 Arrogance. pride, ostentation.<BR>—4 Sin, wickedness.<BR>—5 The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—6 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दम्भचर्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भचर्या
दम्भः + -चर्या deceit, hypocrisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भक|दंभक
दम्भक <i>a.</i> Cheating, deceiving; लोकदम्भकः Ms. 4. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भनम्
दम्भनम् [दम्भ्-भावे ल्युट्] Cheating, deceiving, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0802-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भिन्|दंभिन्
दम्भिन् <i>a.</i> [दम्भ्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Wicked, proud.<BR>—2 Hypocritical. ━<i>m.</i> A hypocrite, an impostor; दम्भिहैतुकपाखण्डिवकवृत्तींश्च<BR> वर्जयेत् Y. 1. 130; Bg. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भोलिः|दम्भोलि|दंभोलि|दंभोलिः
दम्भोलिः<BR>—1 Indraʼs thunderbolt; दन्तावलानां दन्तेषु दम्भोलिदृढमूर्तिषु Śiva B. 4. 44;<BR> दम्भोलिप्रकृतिभृतां बतायुधानाम् 24. 66; B. R. 4. 51.<BR>—2 A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय्
दय् €1 Ā. (दयते, दयित)<BR>—1 To feel pity or compassion for, pity, sympathise with (with gen.);<BR> रामस्य दयमानो ऽसावध्येति तव लक्ष्मणः Bk. 8. 119; तेषां दयसे<BR> न कस्मात् 2. 33, 15. 63.<BR>—2 To love, like, be fond of; दयमानाः प्रमदाः Ś. 1. 4; Bk. 10. 9.<BR>—3 To protect; नगजा न गजा दयिता दयिताः Bk. 10. 9.<BR>—4 To go, move.<BR>—5 To grant, give, divide or allot.<BR>—6 To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दया
दया [दय् भिदा-भावे अङ्] Pity, tenderness, compassion, mercy,<BR> sympathy; निर्गुणेष्वपि सत्त्वेषु दयां कुर्वन्ति साधवः H. 1. 60; R. 2. 11;<BR> यत्नादपि परक्लेशं हर्तुं या हृदि जायते । इच्छा भूमिसुरश्रेष्ठ<BR> सा दया परिकीर्तिता ॥.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दयाकर, दयाकूटः, दयाकूर्चः, दयावीरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकर|दयाकरः
दया + -कर <i>a.</i> kind, sympathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकरः|दयाकर
दया + -कर + .({@-रः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकूटः|दयाकूट
दया + -कूटः, -कूर्चः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकूर्चः|दयाकूर्च|दयाकूर्च्च
दया + -कूटः, -कूर्चः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयावीरः|दयावीर
दया + -वीरः<BR>—1 (in Rhet.) the sentiment of heroic compassion; the sentiment of heroism<BR> arising out of compassion; <i>e. g.</i> Jīmūtavāhanaʼs remark to Garuḍa<BR> in Nāg.:− शिरामुखैः स्यन्दत एव रक्तमद्यापि देहे मम मांसमस्ति ।<BR> तृप्तिं न पश्यामि तथापि तावत् किं भक्षणात्त्वं विरतो गरुत्मन् ॥<BR> cf. also R. G. under दयावीर<BR>—2 <i>a.</i> Very merciful man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
दयालु [दय्-आलुच्] Kind, tender, merciful, compassionate; यशःशरीरे<BR> भव मे दयालुः R. 2. 57, 3. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित|दयितं|दयितः
दयित <i>p. p.</i> [दय्-क्त] Beloved, desired, liked; Bk. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयितः|दयित|दयितं
दयित + .{@-तः@} A husband, lover, a beloved person; V. 3. 5; दयिता दयिताननाम्बुजं<BR> दरमीलन्नयना निरीक्षते Bv. 2. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयिता
दयित + .{@-ता@} A wife, oneʼs beloved woman; दयिताजीवितालम्बनाथीं Me. 4;<BR> R. 2. 3; Bv. 2. 182; Ki. 6. 13; दयिताजितः ‘a hen-pecked husband’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित्नु
दयित्नु <i>a.</i> Kind, compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर|दरं|दरः
दर <i>a.</i> [दॄ-अप्] Tearing, rending, &c. (at the end of comp.)<BR>—2 Little, small; दरदलदरविन्दसुन्दरं हा हरिणदृशो नयनं न<BR> विस्मरामि Bv. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरः|दर|दरं
दर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 A cave, cavity, hole.<BR>—2 A conch-shell; दध्मौ दरवरम् Bhāg. 1. 11. 1. —3 Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरम्
दर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 A cave, cavity, hole.<BR>—2 A conch-shell; दध्मौ दरवरम् Bhāg. 1. 11. 1. —3 Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरः|दर|दरं
दर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Fear, terror, dread; सा दरं पृतना निन्ये हीयमाना रसादरम् Śi. 19. 23;<BR> न जातहार्देन न विद्विषा दरः Ki. 1. 33.<BR>—2 A stream.<BR>—3 The navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरा
दर + .{@-रा@} A hole in the ground, cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरम्
दर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> A little, slightly (in comp.); दरमीलन्नयना<BR> निरीक्षते Bv. 2. 182, 7; दरविगलितमल्लीवल्लिचञ्चत्पराग &c.<BR> Gīt. 1; so दरदलित-विकसित U. 4; Māl. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दरकरः, दरतिमिरम्, दरद, दरदः, दरदम्, दरमन्थर, दरवरः, दरेन्द्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरकरः|दरकर
दर + -करः a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरतिमिरम्
दर + -तिमिरम् the darkness of fear; हरति दरतिमिरमतिघोरम् Gīt. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद|दरदं|दरदः
दर + -द <i>a.</i> causing fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरदः|दरद|दरदं
दर + -दः, -दम् vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरदम्
दर + -दः, -दम् vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरमन्थर
दर + -मन्थर <i>a.</i> a little slow; दरमन्थरचरणविहारम् Gīt. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरवरः|दरवर
दर + -वरः, -इन्द्रः Viṣṇuʼs conch (पाञ्चजन्य); Bhāg. 1. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरेन्द्रः|दरेन्द्र
दर + -वरः, -इन्द्रः Viṣṇuʼs conch (पाञ्चजन्य); Bhāg. 1. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरक
दरक <i>a.</i> Timid, cowardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणम्
दरणम् Breaking, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणि|दरणिः
दरणि <i>m., f.</i>, दरणी [दॄ-अण्]<BR>—1 An eddy.<BR>—2 current.<BR>—3 Surf.<BR>—4 Breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणी
दरणि <i>m., f.</i>, दरणी [दॄ-अण्]<BR>—1 An eddy.<BR>—2 current.<BR>—3 Surf.<BR>—4 Breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरथः|दरथ
दरथः<BR>—1 A cavity, hollow cave.<BR>—2 Fleeing away, taking flight.<BR>—3 Over-running the country for forage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद्
दरद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The heart.<BR>—2 Terror, fear.<BR>—3 A mountain.<BR>—4 A precipice.<BR>—5 A bank or mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरदाः
दरदाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) A country bordering on Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरदः|दरद|दरदं
दरदाः + .{@-दः@} Fear, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरदम्
दरदाः + .{@-दम्@} Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिः|दरि
दरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> A cave, cavern, valley; दरीगृह Ku. 1. 10; एका<BR> भार्या सुन्दरी वा दरी वा Bh. 3. 120.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दरिभृत्, दरिमुखम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरी
दरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> A cave, cavern, valley; दरीगृह Ku. 1. 10; एका<BR> भार्या सुन्दरी वा दरी वा Bh. 3. 120.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दरिभृत्, दरिमुखम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिभृत्
दरिः + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a mountain; प्रतिननाद दरीषु दरीभृतः Ki. 18. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिमुखम्
दरिः + -मुखम्<BR>—1 a mouth like a cave.<BR>—2 the opening of a cave.<BR>—3 cave representing a mouth; दुरीमुखोत्थेन समीरणेन Ku. 1. 8; R. 13. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरित|दरितः
दरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Frightened, terrified.<BR>—2 Timid.<BR>—3 Torn, rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रा
दरिद्रा €2 P. (दरिद्रति, दरिद्रित; <i>Caus.</i> दरिद्रयति<BR> <i>desid.</i> दिदरिद्रासति, दिदरिद्रिषति)<BR>—1 To be poor or needy; अधो ऽध पश्यतः कस्य महिमा नोपजायते । उपर्युपरि<BR> पश्यन्तः सर्व एव दरिद्रति ॥ H. 2. 2; Bk. 18. 31.<BR>—2 To be in distress; युक्तं ममैव किं वक्तुं दरिद्रति यथा हरिः Bk. 5. 86.<BR>—3 To become thin or sparse; दरिद्रति वियद्द्रुमे कुसुमकान्तयस्तारकाः Vikr. 11. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्र|दरिद्रः
दरिद्र <i>a.</i>^1 [दरिद्रा-क] Poor, needy, indigent, in distressed<BR> circumstances; स तु भवतु दरिद्रो यस्य तृष्णा विशाला मनसि च परितुष्टे<BR> कोऽर्थवान् को दरिद्रः Bh. 3. 50. ˚ताम् Poverty; शङ्कनीया हि लोकेऽस्मिन्निष्प्रतापा<BR> दरिद्रता Mk. 3. 24.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0803-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

