दशचतुष्कम्
दशन् + -चतुष्कम् N. of a sport; Sinhās. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशधर्मः
दशन् + -धर्मः unfavourable condition, distress; अभ्यस्तो बहुभिर्बाणैर्दशधर्मगतेन<BR> वै Mb. 7. 147. 20. (see com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपारमिताध्वरः|दशपारमिताध्वर
दशन् + -पारमिताध्वरः ‘possessing the ten perfections’, an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुरम्
दशन् + -पुरम् N. of an ancient city, capital of king Rantideva; पात्रीकुर्वन्दशपुरवधूनेत्रकौतूहलानाम् Me. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबन्धः|दशबन्ध
दशन् + -बन्धः a tenth part; Ms. 8. 107; also ˚बन्धक; Y. 2. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबलः|दशबल
दशन् + -बलः, -भूमिगः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशभूमिगः|दशभूमिग
दशन् + -बलः, -भूमिगः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबाहुः|दशबाहु
दशन् + -बाहुः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशभुजा
दशन् + -भुजा, -महाविद्या N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमहाविद्या
दशन् + -भुजा, -महाविद्या N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमालिकाः
दशन् + -मालिकाः (pl.)<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 the people or rulers of this country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमास्य
दशन् + -मास्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ten months old; एवा ते गर्भ एजतु निरैतु दशमास्यः Rv. 5. 78. 7-8.<BR>—2 ten months in the womb (as a child before birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुखः|दशमुख
दशन् + -मुखः an epithet of Rāvaṇa. ˚रिपुः an epithet of Rāma;<BR> सीतां हित्वा दशमुखरिपुर्नोपयेमे यदन्याम् R. 14. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमूत्रकम्
दशन् + -मूत्रकम् The urine of 10 (elephant, buffalo, camel, cow, goat,<BR> sheep, horse, donkey, man and woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमूलम्
दशन् + -मूलम् a tonic medicine prepared from the roots of ten plants;<BR> (Mar. सालवण, पिटवण (पृष्टिपर्णो), रिंगणी, डोरली, गोखरूं,<BR> बेल, ऐरण, टेंटू, पहाडमूळ, शिवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशयोजनम्
दशन् + -योजनम् a distance of 10 Yojanas; पादाङ्गुष्ठेन चिक्षेप संपूर्णं<BR> दशयोजनम् Rām. 1. 1. 65; also दशयोजनी; मोहितेन्द्रियवृत्तिं तं<BR> व्यतीत्य दशयोजनीम् Ks. 94. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरथः|दशरथ
दशन् + -रथः N. of a celebrated king of Ayodhyā, son of Aja, and father<BR> of Rāma and his three brothers. [He had three wives Kausalyā, Sumitrā,<BR> and Kaikeyī, but was for several years without issue. He was therefore<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">Page0805-2</a>]<BR> recommended by Vasiṣṭha to perform a sacrifice which he successfully<BR> did with the assistance of Ṛṣyaśṛṅga. On the completion of this<BR> sacrifice Kausalyā bore to him Rāma, Sumitrā Lakṣmaṇa and Śatrughna,<BR> and Kaikeyī Bharata. Daśaratha was extremely fond of his sons, but Rāma<BR> was his greatest favourite −‘his life, his very soul’. Thus when Kaikeyī<BR> at the instigation of Mantharā demanded the fulfilment of the two boons<BR> he had previously promised to her, the king tried to dissuade her mind<BR> from her wicked resolve by threats, and, failing these, by the most servile<BR> supplications. But Kaikeyī remained inexorable, and the poor monarch<BR> was obliged to send his beloved son into exile. He soon afterwards died<BR> of a broken heart]. Bhāg. 9. 10. 1 ˚ललिता The fourth day of the<BR> dark fortnight of Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरशिमशतः
दशन् + -रशिमशतः the sun; दशरशिमशतोपमद्युतिम् R. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरात्रम्
दशन् + -रात्रम् a period of ten nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरात्रः|दशरात्र
दशन् + -रात्रम् + .({@-त्रः@}) a particular sacrifice lasting for ten days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरूपकम्
दशन् + -रूपकम् the 10 kinds of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरूपभृत्
दशन् + -रूपभृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशलक्षण
दशन् + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> relating to 10 objects; इदं भागवतं पुराणं<BR> दक्षलक्षणम् Bhāg. 2. 9. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशणम्
दशन् + -णम् ten marks or attributes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशलक्षणकः|दशलक्षणक
दशन् + -लक्षणकः religion; cf. धृतिः क्षमा दमोऽस्तेयं शौचमिन्द्रियनिग्रहः ।<BR> धीर्विद्या सत्यमक्रोधो दशकं धर्मलक्षणम् ॥ Ms. 7. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवक्त्रः|दशवक्त्र
दशन् + -वक्त्रः, -वदनः see दशमुख; Bk. 9. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवदनः|दशवदन
दशन् + -वक्त्रः, -वदनः see दशमुख; Bk. 9. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवर्गः|दशवर्ग
दशन् + -वर्गः the double five classes of अमात्य, राष्ट्र, दुर्ग, कोश<BR> and दण्ड; वेत्ता च दशवर्गस्य स्थानवृद्धिक्षयात्मनः Mb. 12. 57. 18<BR> (com. ‘अमात्यराष्ट्रदुर्गाणि कोशो दण्डश्च पञ्चमः’ इति प्रकृतिपञ्चकं<BR> स्वपक्षे परपक्षे चेति दशको वर्गः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवाजिन्
दशन् + -वाजिन् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवार्षिक
दशन् + -वार्षिक <i>a.</i> happening after, or lasting for, ten years; Y. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशविध
दशन् + -विध <i>a.</i> of ten kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशतम्
दशन् + -शतम्<BR>—1 a thousand; ये सहस्रमराजन्नासन् दशशता उत Av. 5. 18. 10.<BR>—2 one hundred and ten. ˚रश्मिः the sun. ˚अक्षः, ˚नयनः Indra;<BR> दशशताक्षककुब्दरिनिःसृतः Mb. 7. 184. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशती
दशन् + -शती a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशसहस्रम्
दशन् + -सहस्रम्, -साहस्रम् ten thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशसाहस्रम्
दशन् + -सहस्रम्, -साहस्रम् ten thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशहरा
दशन् + -हरा<BR>—1 an epithet of the Ganges (taking away the 10 sins).<BR>—2 a festival in honour of the Ganges held on the 10th day of Jyeṣṭha.<BR>—3 a festival in honour of Durgā held on the tenth of Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशक
दशक <i>a.</i> Consisting of ten, tenfold; कामजो दशको गणः Ms. 7. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकम्
दशक + .{@-कम्@} A group of ten; decad; पदातिलक्षदशकम् Ks. 102. 108.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दशकमासिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकमासिक
दशक + -मासिक <i>a.</i> hired for ten months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशत्
दशत् <i>f.</i>, दशतिः <i>f.</i> A group of ten, decad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशतिः|दशति
दशत् <i>f.</i>, दशतिः <i>f.</i> A group of ten, decad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशतय
दशतय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Consisting of ten parts, ten-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशधा
दशधा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In ten ways.<BR>—2 In ten parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम <i>a.</i> Tenth.^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: definition added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमी
दशम + .({@-मी@} <i>f.</i>) Tenth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमम्
दशम + .{@-मम्@} A tenth part<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दशमभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमभावः|दशमभाव
दशम + -भावः the culminating point, the point in which the meridian<BR> crosses a given circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमिन्
दशमिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Very old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमी
दशमी<BR>—1 The tenth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR>—2 The tenth decade of the human life; यत्र स्युः सोऽत्र मानार्हः शूद्रोऽपि<BR> दशमीं गतः Ms. 2. 137.<BR>—3 The last ten years of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">Page0806-1</a>]<BR> a century.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दशमीस्थ, दशमींगत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0805-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीस्थ|दशमीस्थः
दशमी + -स्थ, दशमींगत <i>a.</i> above ninety years old; दशमीस्थः<BR> क्षीणरागे वृद्धे मरणसंशये Nm.; Ms. 2. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमींगत|दशमीङ्गत
दशमी + -स्थ, दशमींगत <i>a.</i> above ninety years old; दशमीस्थः<BR> क्षीणरागे वृद्धे मरणसंशये Nm.; Ms. 2. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशिन्
दशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Divided into ten parts.<BR>—2 Having ten. ━<i>m.</i> A superintendent of ten villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन|दशनं|दशनः
दशन, दष्ट See under दंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दशन, दष्ट See under दंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशा
दशा<BR>—1 The threads at the end of a piece of woven cloth, the fringe of a garment,<BR> the skirt, edge or hem of a garment; रक्तांशुकं पवनलोलदशं वहन्ती<BR> Mk. 1. 20; छिन्नाम् इवाम्बरपटस्य दशाः पतन्ति 5. 4.<BR>—2 The wick of a lamp; श्रेयोदशाग्रे स्फुरन् Bh. 3. 129; Ku. 4. 30.<BR>—3 Age or time of life; see दशान्त below.<BR>—4 A period or stage of life; as बाल्य, यौवन, &c.; दारक्रियायोग्यदशं<BR> च पुत्रम् R. 5. 40.<BR>—5 A period in general.<BR>—6 State, condition, circumstances; नीचैर्गच्छत्युपरि च दशा चक्रनेमिक्रमेण;<BR> Me. 111; विषमां हि दशां प्राप्य दैवं गर्हयते नरः H. 4. 3.<BR>—7 State or condition of mind.<BR>—8 The result of actions, fate.<BR>—9 The aspect or position of planets (at birth).<BR>—10 The mind, understanding.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दशांशः, दशाभागः, दशाधिपतिः, दशेशः, दशान्तः, दशान्तरम्, दशान्तरः, दशेन्धनः, दशाकर्षः, दशाकर्षिन्, दशापाकः, दशाविपाकः, दशाफलम्, दशाविपर्यासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशांशः|दशांश
दशा + -अंशः, -भागः bad days, straitened condition; परिमृष्टो दशान्तेन<BR> दशभागेन सेव्यते Rām. 3. 72. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाभागः
दशा + -अंशः, -भागः bad days, straitened condition; परिमृष्टो दशान्तेन<BR> दशभागेन सेव्यते Rām. 3. 72. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाधिपतिः|दशाधिपति
दशा + -अधिपतिः, -ईशः the sun; (for other meanings see under दशन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेशः|दशेश
दशा + -अधिपतिः, -ईशः the sun; (for other meanings see under दशन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशान्तः|दशान्त|दशांत
दशा + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the end of a wick.<BR>—2 the end of life; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः स दशान्तमुपेयिवान् R. 12. 1.<BR> (where the word is used in both senses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशान्तरम्
दशा + -अन्तरम् different states, vicissitudes of life; Ś. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशान्तरः|दशान्तर
दशा + -अन्तरः, -इन्धनः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेन्धनः|दशेन्धन|दशेंधन
दशा + -अन्तरः, -इन्धनः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्षः|दशाकर्ष
दशा + -कर्षः, -कर्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the end of garment.<BR>—2 a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्षिन्
दशा + -कर्षः, -कर्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the end of garment.<BR>—2 a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशापाकः|दशापाक
दशा + -पाकः, -विपाकः<BR>—1 the fulfilment of fate; शुभं दशापाकम् Bṛ. S. 95. 61.<BR>—2 a changed condition of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविपाकः|दशाविपाक
दशा + -पाकः, -विपाकः<BR>—1 the fulfilment of fate; शुभं दशापाकम् Bṛ. S. 95. 61.<BR>—2 a changed condition of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाफलम्
दशा + -फलम् future fate of a man; अशुभेष्वशुभं दशाफलम् Bṛ. S. 70. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविपर्यासः
दशा + -विपर्यासः ill-luck, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्णाः
दशार्णाः <i>m.</i> (pl.)<BR>—1 N. of country; संपत्स्यन्ते कतिपयदिन स्थायिहंसा दशार्णाः Me. 23.<BR>—2 The people of this country<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेर|दशेरः
दशेर See under दंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेरकः|दशेरक
दशे(से)रकः<BR>—1 A young camel; see under दशन.<BR>—2 N. of a country; Bṛ. S. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसेरकः|दसेरक
दशे(से)रकः<BR>—1 A young camel; see under दशन.<BR>—2 N. of a country; Bṛ. S. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्
दस् I. €4 P. (दस्यति)<BR>—1 To throw up, toss.<BR>—2 To decay, waste away, perish. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (दंसति, दंसयति-ते)<BR>—1 To bite, destroy, overpower.<BR>—2 To see.<BR>—3 To shine. ━<i>Caus.</i> To exhaust, weary; आविवासन्तो दसयन्त<BR> भूम Rv. 5. 45. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसनम्
दसनम्<BR>—1 Wasting, perishing.<BR>—2 Throwing.<BR>—3 Dismissing, sending away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्त
दस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wasted, perished.<BR>—2 Thrown, tossed.<BR>—3 Dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म|दस्मः
दस्म <i>a.</i> [दस्-मक्] Ved.<BR>—1 Destroying, destructive.<BR>—2 Beautiful.<BR>—3 Wonderful, extraordinary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्मः|दस्म
दस्म + .{@-स्मः@}<BR>—1 A sacrificer.<BR>—2 A thief, rogue.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्मत्|दस्मन्त्
दस्मत् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Desirable, acceptable.<BR>—2 Wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म्य
दस्म्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Beautiful.<BR>—2 Wonderful; द्युक्षाय दस्म्यं वचः Rv. 8. 24. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्युः|दस्यु
दस्युः [दस्-युच्]<BR>—1 N. of a class of evil beings or demons, enemies of gods and men, and<BR> slain by Indra, (mostly Vedic in this sense).<BR>—2 An outcast, a Hindu who has become an outcast by neglect of the essential<BR> rites; cf. Ms. 5. 131, 10. 45; दस्यूनां दीयतामेष साध्वद्य पुरुषाधमः<BR> Mb. 12. 173. 20.<BR>—3 A thief, robber, bandit; नीत्वोत्पथं विषयदस्युषु निक्षिपन्ति Bhāg. 7. 15. 46;<BR> पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20; R. 9. 53; Ms. 7 143.<BR>—4 A villain, miscreant; दस्योरस्य कृपाणपातविषयादाच्छिन्दतः प्रेयसीम् Māl. 5. 28.<BR>—5 A desperado, violator, oppressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्र|दस्रं|दस्रः
दस्र <i>a.</i> [दस्यति पांसून् दस्-रक्] Savage, fierce, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रौ
दस्र + .{@-स्रौ@} <i>m.</i> (du.)<BR>—1 The two Asvins, the physicians of the gods; Mb. 1. 3. 58; Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 17.<BR>—2 The number ‘two’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रः|दस्र|दस्रं
दस्र + .{@-स्रः@}<BR>—1 An ass.<BR>—2 A robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रम्
दस्र + .{@-स्रम्@}<BR>—1 The cold season.<BR>—2 The lunar mansion Aśvinī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दस्रदेवता, दस्रसूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रदेवता
दस्र + -देवता the constellation Aśvinī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रसूः
दस्र + -सूः <i>f.</i> wife of the sun and mother of the Aśvins, = संज्ञा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्
दह् €1 P. (दहति, ददाह, अधाक्षीत्, धक्ष्यति, दग्धुम्, दग्ध, <i>desid.</i> दिधक्षति)<BR>—1 To burn, scorch (fig. also); दग्धुं विश्वं दहनकिरणैर्नोदिता द्वादशार्काः<BR> Ve. 3. 6, 5. 20; सपदि मदनानलो दहति मम मानसं देहि मुखकमलमधुपानम्<BR> Gīt. 10; Ś. 3. 16.<BR>—2 To consume, destroy completely; एकमेव दहत्यग्निर्नरं दुरुपसर्पिणम् Ms. 7. 9.<BR>—3 To pain, torment, afflict, distress, grieve; इत्थमात्मकृतमप्रतिहतं<BR> चापलं दहति Ś. 5; तत् सविषमिव शल्यं दहति माम् 6. 9; एतत्तु<BR> मां दहति यद् गृहमस्मदीयं क्षीणार्थमित्यतिथयः परिवर्जयन्ति Mk. 1. 12;<BR> R. 8. 86; U. 4. 14.<BR>—4 To cauterize (in medicine). ━<i>With</i> {@निस्@}<BR>—1 to burn, consume.<BR>—2 to torment, distress, pain.<BR>━{@परि@} to burn, scorch; दिशि दिशि परिदग्धा भूमयः पावकेन<BR> Ṛs. 1. 24; Bg. 1. 30.<BR>━{@प्र@}<BR>—1 to burn.<BR>—2 to burn completely.<BR>—3 to pain, torment. —4 to trouble, tease.<BR>━{@सम्@} to burn; अभिजनः संदह्यतां वह्निना Bh. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहन|दहनं|दहनः
दहन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दह्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Burning, consuming by fire; Bh. 1. 71.<BR>—2 Destructive, injurious; दहनं धाम विलोकनक्षमम् Ki. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनः|दहन|दहनं
दहन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 Fire; Mb. 13. 2. 28.<BR>—2 A pigeon.<BR>—3 The number ‘three’.<BR>—4 A bad man.<BR>—5 The <i>Bhallātaka</i> plant.<BR>—6 Lead-wort. (चित्रक).<BR>—7 The constellation कृत्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनम्
दहन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Burning, consuming by fire (fig. also); अपरो दहने स्वकर्मणां ववृते ज्ञानमयेन वह्निना R. 8. 20.<BR>—2 Cauterizing.<BR>—3 Sour gruel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दहनारातिः, दहनोपलः, दहनोल्का, दहनर्क्षम्, दहनकेतनः, दहनप्रिया, दहनसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनारातिः|दहनाराति
दहन + -अरातिः water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनोपलः|दहनोपल
दहन + -उपलः the sun-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनोल्का
दहन + -उल्का a fire-brand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनर्क्षम्
दहन + -ऋक्षम् (दहनर्क्षम्) the constellation कृत्तिका; Bṛ. S. 10. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनकेतनः|दहनकेतन|दहनकेतनं
दहन + -केतनः smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनप्रिया
दहन + -प्रिया Svāhā, wife of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनसारथिः|दहनसारथि
दहन + -सारथिः wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनीय|दहनीयः
दहनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be burnt.<BR>—2 Combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनीयता
दहनीयता, दहनत्वम् Combustibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनत्वम्
दहनीयता, दहनत्वम् Combustibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध <i>p. p.</i> [दह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Burnt, consumed by fire.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Consumed by grief, tormented, distressed; (मही) न शक्यते<BR> द्रष्टुमपि प्रवासिभिः प्रियावियोगानलदग्धमानसैः Ṛs. 1. 10.<BR>—3 Famished.<BR>—4 Inauspicious, as in दग्धयोग.<BR>—5 Dry, tasteless, insipid<BR>—6 Wretched, accursed, vile, (used<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">Page0807-1</a>]<BR> as a term of abuse before a word); नाद्यापि मे दग्धदेहः पतति U. 4;<BR> अस्य दग्धोदरस्यार्थे कः कुर्यात् पातकं महत् H. 1. 68; so दग्धजठरस्यार्थे Bh. 3. 8.<BR>—7 Cunning (विदग्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धा
दग्ध + .{@-ग्धा@}<BR>—1 The quarter where the sun remains overhead.<BR>—2 A lunar day or तिथि on which it is considered inauspicious or unlucky to do any act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धम्
दग्ध + .{@-ग्धम्@}<BR>—1 Burning; Mb. 12. 303. 6.<BR>—2 Cauterizing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दग्धकाकः, दग्धजठरम्, दग्धव्रणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0806-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धकाकः|दग्धकाक
दग्ध + -काकः a raven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धजठरम्
दग्ध + -जठरम् the hungry stomach; Bh. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धव्रणः|दग्धव्रण
दग्ध + -व्रणः a burn, singe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्धिका Scorched rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहः|दाह
दाहः [दह्-भावे-घञ्]<BR>—1 Burning, conflagration; दाहशक्तिमिव कृष्णवर्त्मनि R. 11. 42;<BR> छेदो दंशस्य दाहो वा M. 4. 4; Ki. 5. 14.<BR>—2 Glowing redness (as of the sky).<BR>—3 The sensation of burning, internal heat.<BR>—4 Feverish or morbid heat.<BR>—5 A place of cremation; Vās. 19. 26.<BR>—6 Cauterizing; M. 4. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दाहागुरुः, दाहात्मक, दाहज्वरः, दाहसरः, दाहसरस्, दाहर, दाहरण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहागुरुः|दाहागुरु
दाहः + -अगुरुः <i>n.</i>, {@-काष्ठम्@}<BR> a kind of agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहात्मक
दाहः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> destructive, having power to burn, combustible;<BR> शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु गूढं हि दाहात्मकमस्ति तेजः Ś. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहज्वरः|दाहज्वर
दाहः + -ज्वरः inflammatory fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहसरः|दाहसर
दाहः + -सरः, -सरस् <i>n.</i>, {@-स्थलम्@}<BR> a place where dead bodies are burnt, cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहसरस्
दाहः + -सरः, -सरस् <i>n.</i>, {@-स्थलम्@}<BR> a place where dead bodies are burnt, cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहर
दाहः + दाहर, दाहरण <i>a.</i> allaying heat.<BR>.({@दाहरम्, -दाहरणम्@}) the Uśīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहरण
दाहः + दाहर, दाहरण <i>a.</i> allaying heat.<BR>.({@दाहरम्, -दाहरणम्@}) the Uśīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहर
दाहः + दाहर, दाहरण + .({@दाहरम्, -दाहरणम्@}) the Uśīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहर
दाहः + दाहर, दाहरण + .({@दाहरम्, -दाहरणम्@}) the Uśīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहक|दाहकः
दाहक <i>a.</i> (-हिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दह्-ण्वुल]<BR>—1 Burning, kindling; यथाग्निर्दारुणो दाह्याद्दाहकोऽन्यः प्रकाशकः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 10. 8.<BR>—2 Incendiary, inflammatory.<BR>—3 Cauterizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहकः|दाहक
दाहक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Fire<BR>—2 The Chitraka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहनम्
दाहनम्<BR>—1 Burning, reducing to ashes; वाराणस्याश्च दाहनम् Bhāg. 12. 12. 40.<BR>—2 Cauterizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहिन्
दाहिन् <i>a.</i> [दह्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Burning, setting on fire.<BR>—2 Tormenting, paining, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहुक
दाहुक <i>a.</i> Burning &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह्य
दाह्य <i>a.</i> [दह्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be burnt. —2 Combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहर|दहरं|दहरः
दहर <i>a.</i> [दह्-अर्] Small, subtle, fine, thin; अस्मिन् ब्रह्मपुरे<BR> दहरं पुण्डरीकं वेश्म Ch. Up. 8. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Young in age.<BR>—3 Unintelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहरः|दहर|दहरं
दहर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A child, an infant.<BR>—2 Any young animal.<BR>—3 A younger brother.<BR>—4 The cavity of the heart, or the heart itself; परिसरपद्धतिं हृदयमारुणयो<BR> दहरम् Bhāg. 10. 87. 18; दहरकुहरवर्ती देवता चक्रवर्ती Viś. Guṇā. 459.<BR>—5 A mouse or rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्र|दह्रः
दह्र <i>a.</i> Small, fine, thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्रः|दह्र
दह्र + .{@-ह्रः@}<BR>—1 cavity of the heart, or the heart itself; एवं व्याहृतयश्चासन् प्रणवो<BR> ह्यस्य दह्रतः Bhāg. 3. 12. 44.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 A forest-conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा I. €1 P. (यच्छति, दत्त) To give, grant.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@प्रति@} to exchange; तिलेभ्यः प्रतियच्छति माषान् Sk. ━II. €2 P. (दाति) To<BR> cut; ददाति द्रविणं भूरि दाति दारिद्र्यमर्थिनाम् K. R. ━III. €4 P. (दायति)<BR> To bind (?). ━IV. €3 U. (ददाति, दत्ते; ददौ-ददे, अदात्-अदित, दास्यति-ते,<BR> दातुम्, दत्त; but with आ the <i>p. p.</i> is आत्त; with उप,<BR> उपात्त; with नि, निदत्त or नीत्त, and with प्र, प्रदत्त or प्रत्त)<BR>—1 To give,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">Page0807-2</a>]<BR> grant, bestow, offer, yield, impart, present (usually with acc. of the<BR> thing and dat., sometimes gen. or loc. also, of the person); अवकाशं<BR> किलोदन्वान् रामायाभ्यर्थितो ददौ R. 4. 58; सेचनघटैः बालपादपेभ्यः<BR> पयो दातुमित एवाभिवर्तते Ś. 1; Ms. 3. 31, 9. 271; कथमस्य स्तनं दास्ये Hariv.<BR>—2 To pay (as debt, fine &c.).<BR>—3 To hand or deliver over.<BR>—4 To restore, return.<BR>—5 To give up, sacrifice, surrender; प्राणान् दा to sacrifice oneʼs<BR> life; so आत्मानं दा to sacrifice oneself.<BR>—6 To put, place, apply, plant; कर्णे करं ददाति &c.<BR>—7 To give in marriage; यस्मै दद्यात् पिता त्वेनाम् Ms. 5. 151; Y. 2. 146, 3. 24.<BR>—8 To allow, permit (usually with inf.); बाष्पस्तु न ददात्येनां द्रष्टुं<BR> चित्रगतामपि Ś. 6. 22. (The meanings of this root may be variously<BR> modified or extended according to the noun with which it is connected;<BR> मनो दा to think, direct the mind to anything; नीतौ मनो दीयते)<BR> Mu. 2. 5; अवकाशं दा to give place to, make room; (see अवकाश);<BR> कर्णं दा to give ear to or listen; दर्शनं दा to show oneself<BR> to, grant audience to; शब्दं दा to make a noise; तालं दा to<BR> clap the hands; आत्मानं खेदाय दा to expose oneself to trouble; आतपे<BR> दा to expose to the sunʼs heat; आज्ञाम्, निदेशं दा to issue orders,<BR> command; आशिषं दा to pronounce a blessing; चक्षुः, दृष्टिं दा<BR> to cast a glance, see; वाचं दा to address a speech to; प्रतिवचः,<BR> -वचनं or प्रत्युत्तरं दा to give reply; शोकं दा to cause<BR> grief; श्राद्धं दा to perform a Śrāddha; मार्गं दा to make way<BR> for, allow to pass, stand out of the way; वरं दा to grant a boon;<BR> संग्रामं दा to fight; अर्गलं दा to bolt, fasten or secure with<BR> a latch; निगडं दा to put in chains, fetter; संकेतं दा to make<BR> an appointment; शापं दा to curse; वृत्तिं दा to enclose, fence<BR> in; अग्निं, पावकं दा to set on fire, &c. &c. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दापयति-ते)<BR> To cause to give, grant, &c. ━<i>Desid.</i> (दित्सति-ते) To wish to give, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त <i>p. p.</i> [दा कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Given, given away, presented.<BR>—2 Made over, delivered, assigned.<BR>—3 Placed, stretched forth.<BR>—4 Preserved, guarded; see दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तः|दत्त|दत्तं
दत्त + .{@-त्तः@}<BR>—1 One of the twelve kinds of sons in Hindu law; (also called दत्त्रिम);<BR> माता पिता वा दद्यातां यमद्भिः पुत्रमापदि । सदृशं प्रीतिसंयुक्तं<BR> स ज्ञेयो दत्रिमः सुतः ॥ Ms. 9. 168.<BR>—2 A title added to the names of Vaiśyas; cf. the quotation under गुप्त.<BR>—3 N. of a son of Atri and Anasūyā; see दत्तात्रेय below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तम्
दत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} Gift, donation; य इमे ग्राम इष्टापूर्ते दत्तमित्युपासते<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 10. 3; स्वदत्तकृतसाक्षी यो द्वितीय इव पावकः Rām. 7. 20. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दत्तानपकर्मन्, दत्तानपाकर्मन्, दत्ताप्रदानिकम्, दत्तावधान, दत्तात्मन्, दत्तात्रेयः, दत्तादत्त, दत्तादर, दत्तक्षण, दत्तदृष्टि, दत्तनृत्योपहार, दत्तशुल्का, दत्तहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तानपकर्मन्|दत्तानपकर्म्मन्
दत्त + -अनपकर्मन्, -अनपाकर्मन्, -अप्रदानिकम् non-delivery<BR> or resumption of gifts, one of the 18 titles of Hindu law; Ms. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तानपाकर्मन्
दत्त + -अनपकर्मन्, -अनपाकर्मन्, -अप्रदानिकम् non-delivery<BR> or resumption of gifts, one of the 18 titles of Hindu law; Ms. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ताप्रदानिकम्
दत्त + -अनपकर्मन्, -अनपाकर्मन्, -अप्रदानिकम् non-delivery<BR> or resumption of gifts, one of the 18 titles of Hindu law; Ms. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तावधान
दत्त + -अवधान <i>a.</i> attentive; दत्तावधानः कुसृतिष्विव ध्यानं ततान<BR> सः Ks. 24. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्मन्
दत्त + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> an orphan or a son who being deserted by his parents,<BR> offers himself to persons disposed to adopt him; दत्तात्मा तु स्वयं<BR> दत्तः Y. 2. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्रेयः|दत्तात्रेय
दत्त + -आत्रेयः N. of a sage, son of Atri and Anasūyā, considered as<BR> an incarnation of Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Maheśa; Bhāg. 9. 23. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादत्त
दत्त + -आदत्त <i>a.</i> given and received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादर
दत्त + -आदर <i>a.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">Page0808-1</a>]<BR>—1 showing respect, respectful.<BR>—2 treated with respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0807-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक्षण
दत्त + -क्षण <i>a.</i> to whom occasion or a festival has been given; रेमे<BR> क्षणदया दत्तक्षणस्त्रीक्षणसौहृदः Bhāg. 3. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तदृष्टि
दत्त + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> looking at; Ś. 1. 7 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तनृत्योपहार
दत्त + -नृत्योपहार <i>a.</i> presented with the offering of a dance, <i>i. e.</i><BR> complimented with a dance; बन्धुप्रीत्या भवनशिखिभिर्दत्तनृत्योपहारः Me. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तशुल्का
दत्त + -शुल्का a bride for whom a dowry has been paid; Ms. 9. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तहस्त
दत्त + -हस्त <i>a.</i> having a hand given for support, supported by the<BR> hand of; शंभुना दत्तहस्ता Me. 60 ‘leaning on Śambhuʼs arm’; स<BR> कामरूपेश्वरदत्तहस्तः R. 7. 17; (fig.) being given a helping hand,<BR> supported, aided, assisted; दैवेनेत्थं दत्तहस्तावलम्बे Ratn. 1. 8;<BR> वात्या स्वेदं कृशाङ्ग्याः सुचिरमवयवैर्दत्तहस्ता करोति Ve. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तकः|दत्तक
दत्तकः An adopted son; अक्षतायां क्षतायां वा जातः पौनर्भवः<BR> सुतः । दद्यान्माता पिता वायं स पुत्रो दत्तको भवेत् ॥ Y. 2. 130; see<BR> दत्त above.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दत्तकवन्द्रिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तकवन्द्रिका
दत्तकः + -वन्द्रिका N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तिः|दत्ति
दत्तिः A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्रम्
दत्रम् Ved. A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्रिम
दत्त्रिम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Received by gift.<BR>—2 Belonging to a gift; निष्ठां गते दत्त्रिमसभ्यतोषे Bk. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्रिमः|दत्रिम
दत्त्रिम + .{@-मः@} One of the twelve kinds of sons; see दत्त; Ms. 8. 415, 9. 141.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददातिः|ददाति
ददातिः The act of removing oneʼs ownership of something and bringing<BR> it under the ownership of some one else; अथ ददातिः किंलक्षणकः इति ।<BR> आत्मनः स्वत्वव्यावृत्तिः परस्य स्वत्वेन संबन्धः । ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा<BR>—1 Protection, defence.<BR>—2 Cleaning, purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाकः|दाक
दाकः<BR>—1 A giver, donor.<BR>—2 An institutor of a sacrifice (who employs and pays the priests).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
दात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Divided, cut.<BR>—2 Washed, purified; तयदातवदा भीमा Ki. 15. 20.<BR>—3 Reaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातव्य
दातव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be given.<BR>—2 Payable.<BR>—3 To be restored or returned<BR>—4 To be given in marriage &c., see दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातव्यम्
दातव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} The act of giving, gift, giving away; दातव्यस्य एव तद्रूपं<BR> यत् स्वत्वपरित्यागेन परस्वत्वापादनम् । ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातिः|दाति
दातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Giving.<BR>—2 Cutting, destroying.<BR>—3 Distribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
दातृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दा-तृच्]<BR>—1 Giving, offering, granting, presenting, bestowing, imparting, &c.<BR>—2 Liberal. ━<i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृता
दातृ + .({@-ता@}) —11 A giver (in general); दाता मे भूभृतां नाथः Ku. 6. 1.<BR>—2 A donor; एवं दातृगुरोर्गुणाः सुरतरोः सर्वेऽपि लोकोत्तराः Bv. 1. 66.<BR>—3 A lender, creditor.<BR>—4 A teacher.<BR>—5 A cutter.<BR>—6 A guardian; अदत्तमेवाददीत दातुर्वित्तं ममेति च Mb. 12. 132. 5.<BR>—7 One who gives daughter or sister in marriage; Ms. 3. 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्रम्
दात्रम्<BR>—1 An instrument of cutting, a sort of sickle or knife; दात्रौश्छिन्दन्<BR> क्वचित् क्वचित् Rām. 2. 80. 7; Mb. 12. 228. 60.<BR>—2 Ved. A share, possession.<BR>—3 A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्वः|दात्व
दात्वः A donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्वम्
दात्वः + .{@-त्वम्@}<BR>—1 The performance of a sacrifice.<BR>—2 A sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानम्
दानम् [दा-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Giving, granting, teaching, &c. (in general); giving in marriage (cf.<BR> कन्यादान).<BR>—2 Delivering, handing over.<BR>—3 A gift, donation, present; Ms. 2. 158; दातव्यमिति यद्दानं दीयतेऽनुपकारिणे<BR> Bg. 17. 20; Y. 3. 274.<BR>—4 Liberality, charity, giving away as charity, munificence; R. 1. 69;<BR> दानं भोगो नाशस्तिस्रो गतयो भवन्ति वित्तस्य Bh. 2. 43; दानं हि<BR> उत्सर्गपूर्वकः परस्य स्वत्वसम्बन्धः ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 30; ननु<BR> दानमित्युच्यते स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः परस्वत्वापादनम् च । ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 1.<BR>—5 Ichor or the juice that exudes from the temples of an elephant in rut;<BR> स दानतोयेन विषाणि नागः Śi. 4. 63; Ki. 5. 9; V. 4. 25; Pt. 2. 75<BR> (where the word has sense 4 also); R. 2. 7, 4. 45, 5. 43.<BR>—6 Bribery, as one of the four Upāyas or expedients of overcoming oneʼs<BR> enemy; see उपाय.<BR>—7 Cutting, dividing<BR>—8 Purification, cleaning.<BR>—9 Protection.<BR>—10 Pasture.<BR>—11 Adding; addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानः|दान|दानं
दानम् + .{@-नः@} Ved.<BR>—1 Distribution (of food), meal, especially a sacrificial meal.<BR>—2 Part, possession, share.<BR>—3 A distributor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दानकाम, दानकुल्या, दानतोयम्, दानधर्मः, दानपतिः, दानपत्रम्, दानपात्रम्, दानपारमिता, दानप्रातिभाव्यम्, दानभिन्न, दानवज्रः, दानवर्षिन्, दानवार्, दानवारि, दानवीरः, दानव्यत्यासः, दानशाला, दानशील, दानशूर, दानशौण्ड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकाम
दानम् + -काम <i>a.</i> liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकुल्या
दानम् + -कुल्या the flow of rut from an elephantʼs temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानतोयम्
दानम् + -तोयम् दानवारि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानधर्मः|दानधर्म|दानधर्म्म|दानधर्म्मः
दानम् + -धर्मः alms-giving, charity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपतिः|दानपति
दानम् + -पतिः<BR>—1 an exceedingly liberal man.<BR>—2 Akrūra, a friend of Kṛṣṇa; Bhāg. 10. 36. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपत्रम्
दानम् + -पत्रम् a deed of gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपात्रम्
दानम् + -पात्रम् ‘a worthy recipient’, a Brāhmaṇa fit to receive gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपारमिता
दानम् + -पारमिता perfection of liberality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानप्रातिभाव्यम्
दानम् + -प्रातिभाव्यम् security for payment of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानभिन्न
दानम् + -भिन्न <i>a.</i> made hostile by bribes; लुब्धानुजीविकैरेष दानभिन्नैर्निहन्यते H. 4. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवज्रः|दानवज्र
दानम् + -वज्रः an epithet of the Vaiśyas or men of the third tribe;<BR> वैश्या वै दानवज्राश्च Mb. 1. 170. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवर्षिन्
दानम् + -वर्षिन् an elephant in rut, infatuated elephant; दानवर्षी कृताशंसो<BR> नागराज इवावभौ Ki. 15. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवार्
दानम् + -वार् <i>n.</i> libation of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवारि|दानवारिः
दानम् + -वारि <i>n.</i>, ichor flowing from the temples of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवीरः|दानवीर
दानम् + -वीरः<BR>—1 a very liberal man.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) the sentiment of heroism arising out of liberality, the<BR> sentiment of chivalrous liberality, <i>e. g.</i> Paraśurāma who gave away<BR> the earth with its seven continents; cf. the instance given in R. G. under<BR> दानवीरः- कियदिदमधिकं मे यद् द्विजायार्थयित्रे कवचमरमणीयं<BR> कुण्डलं चार्पयामि । अकरुणमवकृत्य द्राक्कृपाणेन निर्यद् बहलरुधिरधारं<BR> मौलिमावेदयामि ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव्यत्यासः|दानव्यत्यास
दानम् + -व्यत्यासः giving to a wrong person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशाला
दानम् + -शाला hall for alms-giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशील|दानशीलः
दानम् + -शील, -शूर, -शौण्ड <i>a.</i> exceedingly liberal or munificent;<BR> निर्गुणोऽपि विमुखो न भूपतेर्दानशौण्डमनसः पुरोऽभवत् Śi. 14. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशूर
दानम् + -शील, -शूर, -शौण्ड <i>a.</i> exceedingly liberal or munificent;<BR> निर्गुणोऽपि विमुखो न भूपतेर्दानशौण्डमनसः पुरोऽभवत् Śi. 14. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशौण्ड|दानशौंड|दानशौण्डः
दानम् + -शील, -शूर, -शौण्ड <i>a.</i> exceedingly liberal or munificent;<BR> निर्गुणोऽपि विमुखो न भूपतेर्दानशौण्डमनसः पुरोऽभवत् Śi. 14. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकम्
दानकम् A mean or unworthy gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिन्
दानिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Liberal, munificent; दानिष्वाख्यायमानेषु Bhāg. 10. 64. 10.<BR>—2 Having gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानीय|दानीयः
दानीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Due, bestowable, fit to be given.<BR>—2 Receiving gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानीयम्
दानीय + .{@-यम्@} A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानु|दानुः
दानु <i>a.</i> [दा-नु]<BR>—1 Valiant.<BR>—2 Conquering, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानुः|दानु
दानु + .{@-नुः@}<BR>—1 A donor.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR>—3 Satisfaction.<BR>—4 Air, wind.<BR>—5 A demon. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 A gift.<BR>—2 A fluid, drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0808-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापनम्
दापनम् Causing or obliging (one) to pay or give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापित|दापितः
दापित <i>p. p.</i> [दा-णिच् कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Caused to be given.<BR>—2 Condemned to pay fine, fined.<BR>—3 Adjudged.<BR>—4 Assigned, awarded.<BR>—5 Got, procured; obtained; मह्यं दापितवित्ताय किं ददासि Rāj. T. 6. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
दामन् <i>a.</i> Liberal, donor; Mb. 12. 92. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सा
दित्सा <i>n.</i> Desire of giving; दित्सां न सूचयसि Rāj. T. 3. 252;<BR> मृतस्य लिप्सा कृपणस्य दित्सा (न हि दृष्टपूर्वा) Bv. 1. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सु
दित्सु <i>a.</i> Wishing to give &c., यत् ते दित्सु प्रराध्यम् Rv. 5. 39. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देय|देयं
देय <i>a.</i> [दा कर्मणि यत्]<BR>—1 To be given, offered or presented; R. 3. 16; (see अदेय).<BR>—2 Fit to be given, proper for a gift.<BR>—3 To be returned; or restored; विभावितैकदेशेन देयं यदभियुज्यते<BR> V. 4. 33; Ms. 8. 139, 185.<BR>—4 To be shown.<BR>—5 To be given in marriage.<BR>—6 To be paid (as a debt &c.).<BR>—7 To be placed, put, applied, laid, &c.; see दा above.<BR>—8 To be ceded (road); पन्था देयो वरस्य च Ms. 2. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देयम्
देय + .{@-यम्@} A gift, donation,<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देयधर्मः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देयधर्मः|देयधर्म
देय + -धर्मः Charity; Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष
दाक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षम्
दाक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} The south; Ms. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण|दाक्षायणः
दाक्षायण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Coming from the Dakṣa family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणः|दाक्षायण
दाक्षायण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A son of Dakṣa.<BR>—2 A particular sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणम्
दाक्षायण + .{@-णम्@} Gold or a golden ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणिन्
दाक्षायणिन् <i>m.</i> A Brāhmaṇa student wearing gold ear-rings. दाक्षायणी<BR> ब्रह्मसूत्री वेणुमान् सकमण्डलुः Y. 1. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणी
दाक्षायणी [दक्षस्यापत्यं स्त्री इञि फक्-ङीप्]<BR>—1 Any one of the 27 lunar mansions (they being mythologically regarded<BR> as so many daughters of Dakṣa).<BR>—2 N. of Diti, wife of Kaśyapa and mother of the demons. Bhāg. 8. 4. 22.<BR>—3 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—4 The lunar constellation called Revatī.<BR>—5 N. of Kadru or Vinatā.<BR>—6 N. of Aditi, mother of the gods.<BR>—7 The Dantī plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दाक्षायणीपतिः, दाक्षायणीपुत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणीपतिः|दाक्षायणीपति
दाक्षायणी + -पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणीपुत्रः|दाक्षायणीपुत्र
दाक्षायणी + -पुत्रः a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण्यः|दाक्षायण्य
दाक्षायण्यः The sun; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षाय्यः|दाक्षाय्य
दाक्षाय्यः A vulture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिः|दाक्षि
दाक्षिः A son of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण
दाक्षिण <i>a.</i> (-र्णा <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दक्षिणा प्रयोजनमस्य-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a sacrificial gift or to a gift in general.<BR>—2 Relating to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणा
दाक्षिण + .{@-णा@} The southern country <i>i. e.</i> the Deccan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणम्
दाक्षिण + .{@-णम्@} A collection of sacrificial gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्य|दाक्षिणात्यः
दाक्षिणात्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to or living in the south, southern; अस्ति दाक्षिणात्ये जनपदे<BR> महिलारोप्यं नाम नगरम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्यः|दाक्षिणात्य
दाक्षिणात्य + .{@-त्यः@} A southerner, a native of the Deccan; आरम्भशूराः खलु दाक्षिणात्याः.<BR>—2 The cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणिक
दाक्षिणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Connected with a sacrificial gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
दाक्षिण्य <i>a.</i> [दक्षिणस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Relating to a sacrificial gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्यम्
दाक्षिण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Politeness, civility, courtesy; तस्य दाक्षिण्यरूढेन नाम्ना<BR> मगधवंशजा R. 1. 31.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Kindness; V. 1. 2; दाक्षिण्यं स्वजने Bh. 2. 22; Māl. 1. 8.<BR>—2 Insincere or overcourteous conduct of a lover (towards his beloved);<BR> दाक्षिण्येन ददाति वाचमुचिताम् Ś. 6. 4; it is thus defined:− दाक्षिण्यं<BR> चेष्टया वाचा परचित्तानुवर्तनम्.<BR>—3 The state of relating to or coming from the south; स्नेहदाक्षिण्ययोर्योगात्<BR> कामीव प्रतिभाति मे V. 2. 4 (where the word has sense 1 or 2 also).<BR>—4 Concord, harmony, agreement.<BR>—5 Honesty, candour.<BR>—6 Talent, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षी
दाक्षी<BR>—1 A daughter of दक्ष.<BR>—2 N. of the mother of Pāṇini.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दाक्षीपुत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षीपुत्रः|दाक्षीपुत्र|दाक्षीपुत्त्रः
दाक्षी + -पुत्रः N. of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षेयः|दाक्षेय
दाक्षेयः A metronymic of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष्यम्
दाक्ष्यम् [दक्षस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Cleverness, skill, fitness, dexterity, ability; Bg. 18. 43.<BR>—2 Probity, integrity, honesty.<BR>—3 Industry, activity; दाक्ष्येण हीनो धर्मयुक्तो न दान्तः Mb. 12. 292. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिकन्था
दाक्षिकन्था N. of a place in the Bālhīka country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाघः|दाघ
दाघः Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडकः|दाडक
दाडकः A tooth, tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमः|दाडिम
दाडि(लि)मः, -मा<BR>—1 The pomegranate tree; व्रीडार्ता प्रकरोति दाडिमफलव्याजेन वाग्बन्धनम् Amaru. 16.<BR>—2 Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिमः|दालिम
दाडि(लि)मः, -मा<BR>—1 The pomegranate tree; व्रीडार्ता प्रकरोति दाडिमफलव्याजेन वाग्बन्धनम् Amaru. 16.<BR>—2 Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमा
दाडि(लि)मः, -मा<BR>—1 The pomegranate tree; व्रीडार्ता प्रकरोति दाडिमफलव्याजेन वाग्बन्धनम् Amaru. 16.<BR>—2 Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमम्
दाडि(लि)मः, -मा + .{@-मम्@} The fruit of the pomegranate tree; पाकारुणस्फुटितदाडिमकान्ति<BR> वक्त्रम् Māl. 9. 31.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दाडिमप्रियः, दाडिमभक्षणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमप्रियः|दाडिमप्रिय
दाडिमः + -प्रियः, -भक्षणः a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमभक्षणः|दाडिमभक्षण
दाडिमः + -प्रियः, -भक्षणः a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम्बः|दाडिम्ब|दाडिंब|दाडिंबः
दाडिम्बः The pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढा
दाढा<BR>—1 A large tooth or tusk.<BR>—2 A multitude.<BR>—3 Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढिका
दाढिका The beard; Ms. 8. 283 (Kull. श्मश्रु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्ड|दांड
दाण्ड <i>a.</i> (-ण्डी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to a stick or punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डा
दाण्ड + .{@-ण्डा@} A kind of game with sticks.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दाण्डपाता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डपाता
दाण्ड + -पाता a particular festival (फाल्गुन पौर्णिमा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डक्यः|दाण्डक्य
दाण्डक्यः N. of a king who had no control over his senses; दाण्डक्यो<BR> भोजः, करालश्च वैदेहः Kau. A. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डाजिनिक|दांडाजिनिक|दाण्डाजिनिकः
दाण्डाजिनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Carrying a staff and hide (as mere outward signs<BR> of religious devotion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डाजिनिकः|दाण्डाजिनिक|दांडाजिनिक
दाण्डाजिनिक + .{@-कः@} A cheat, hypocrite, impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिकः|दाण्डिक|दांडिक|दांडिकः
दाण्डिकः A chastiser, punisher; न च दण्डो न दाण्डिकः Mb. 12. 59. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0809-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक|दाकः
