दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण <i>a.</i> [दॄ-णिच्-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 53]<BR>—1 Hard, rough; शोकदारुणाः (वाचः) U. 3. 34.<BR>—2 Harsh, cruel, ruthless, pitiless; मग्येव विस्मरणदारुणचित्तवृत्तौ<BR> Ś. 5. 23; पशुमारणकर्मदारुणः 6. 1; दारुणरसः ‘of cruel resolve or nature’<BR>; U. 5. 19; Ms. 8. 270.<BR>—3 Fierce, terrible, frightful; प्रसादसौम्यानि सतां सुहृज्जने पतन्ति<BR> चक्षूंषि न दारुणाः शराः Ś. 6. 28.<BR>—4 Heavy, violent, intense, poignant, agonizing (grief, pain &c.); हृदयकुसुमशोषी<BR> दारुणो दीर्घशोकः U. 3. 5.<BR>—5 Sharp, severe (as words).<BR>—6 Atrocious, shocking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0811-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुणः|दारुण
दारुण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 The sentiment of horror (भयानक).<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0811-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुणम्
दारुण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Severity, cruelty, horror, &c.<BR>—2 The harsh, unfavourable constellations मृग, पुष्य, ज्येष्ठा and<BR> मूल; Mb. 13. 104. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दारुणाध्यापकः, दारुणकर्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0811-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुणाध्यापकः|दारुणाध्यापक
