दाशग्रामः|दाशग्राम
दाशः + -ग्रामः a village mostly inhabited by fishermen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशनन्दिनी|दाशनंदिनी
दाशः + -नन्दिनी an epithet of Satyavatī, mother of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेयः|दाशेय
दाशे(से)यः The son of a fishermanʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेयः|दासेय
दाशे(से)यः The son of a fishermanʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेयी
दाशे(से)यः + .{@-यी@} An epithet of Satyavatī, mother of Vyāsa; समीक्ष्य राजा<BR> दाशेयीं कामयामास शान्तनुः Mb. 1. 100. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशतयी
दाशतयी <i>f.</i> Collection of 10 मण्डलs of the Rv. Saṃhitā;<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथ|दाशरथः
दाशरथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to sacrifice [‘एकः पशुः, द्वौ पत्नीयजमानौ, त्रयो वेदाः, चत्वार ऋत्विजः इति दशरथाश्च प्रचरन्ति यस्मिन्’ com. on Mb. 12. 8. 37. -महान् दाशरथः पन्थाः].<BR>—2 A road affording space for ten waggons (according to MW.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथः|दाशरथ
दाशरथः, -दाशरथिः<BR>—1 A son of Daśaratha in general R. 10. 44; अजीगणद्दाशरथं न वाक्यम् Bk.<BR>—2 N. of Rāma and his three brothers, but especially of Rāma; R. 12. 45;<BR> प्रदीयतां दाशरथाय मैथिली Mahānāṭaka; यथा यथा दाशरथिर्धर्ममेवाश्रितोऽभवत् ।<BR> तथा तथा प्रकृतयो रामं पतिमकामयन् ॥ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथिः|दाशरथि
दाशरथः, -दाशरथिः<BR>—1 A son of Daśaratha in general R. 10. 44; अजीगणद्दाशरथं न वाक्यम् Bk.<BR>—2 N. of Rāma and his three brothers, but especially of Rāma; R. 12. 45;<BR> प्रदीयतां दाशरथाय मैथिली Mahānāṭaka; यथा यथा दाशरथिर्धर्ममेवाश्रितोऽभवत् ।<BR> तथा तथा प्रकृतयो रामं पतिमकामयन् ॥ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशराज्ञ
दाशराज्ञ <i>a.</i> Belonging to ten kings. The battle of ten kings<BR> against king Sudāsa is often referred to in the Ṛgveda and is known<BR> as दाशराज्ञयुद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशापराधिकः|दाशापराधिक
दाशापराधिकः Probably an officer who collected fines for ten specified<BR> kinds of criminal offences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्हाः
दाशार्हाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) The descendants of Daśārha, the Yādavas; Śi. 2. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्हः|दाशार्ह
दाशार्हाः + .{@-र्हः@} An epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरः|दाशेर
दाशेरः<BR>—1 The son of a fisherman.<BR>—2 A fisherman.<BR>—3 A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरकः|दाशेरक
दाशेरकः<BR>—1 A fisherman; Ks. 124. 204.<BR>—2 The Mālava country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरकाः
दाशेरकः + .{@-काः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) The rulers or inhabitants of that country; see<BR> दाशेर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्वस्
दाश्वस् <i>a.</i> Liberal, giving, a donor; अप्युत्तमां गतिमसौ भजते<BR> त्रिलोकीं दाश्वानविक्लवमनाः कथमार्तिमृच्छेत् Bhāg. 8. 22. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्
दास् €1 U., €5 P. = दाश् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासः|दास
दासः<BR>—1 Slave, servant in general; गृहकर्मदासाः Bh. 1. 1; गृह˚, कर्म˚ &c.<BR>—2 A fisherman; निषादो मार्गवं सूते दासं नौकर्मजीविनम् Ms. 10. 34.<BR>—3 A Śūdra, a man of the fourth caste.<BR>—4 A knowing man, one who knows the universal spirit.<BR>—5 N. of Vṛtrāsura.<BR>—6 A demon.<BR>—7 A savage, barbarian (opp. आर्य).<BR>—8 A worthy recipient (दानपात्र).<BR>—9 A word added to the name of Śūdra; cf. गुप्त.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दासानुदासः, दासजनः, दासभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासानुदासः|दासानुदास
दासः + -अनुदासः ‘a slave of a slave’, the humblest of the servants;<BR> (sometimes used by the speaker as a mark of humility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासजनः|दासजन
दासः + -जनः a servant or slave; कमपराधलवं मयि पश्यसि त्यजसि<BR> मानिनि दासजनं यतः V. 4. 29; (दासस्यकुलम् is used as a compound<BR> in the sense of ‘the mob or the common people’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासभावः|दासभाव
दासः + -भावः servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासता
दासता, -दासत्वम्<BR> Slavery, servitude; यास्यसि त्वं रिपोः पाप जितः<BR> सन् दासतामिति Ks. 72. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासत्वम्
दासता, -दासत्वम्<BR> Slavery, servitude; यास्यसि त्वं रिपोः पाप जितः<BR> सन् दासतामिति Ks. 72. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासमीयाः
दासमीयाः N. of people; cf. Mb. 8. 44. 33 com. [दासमीय = दसमदेशोद्भव<BR> or दासं गृहशूद्रं मिमते मानयन्ति मैथुनार्थिन्यस्ताः दासभ्यः तज्ज]<BR> a son born of a woman of higher caste from Śudra father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासिका
दासिका A female servant or slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासी
दासी<BR>—1 A female servant or slave.<BR>—2 The wife of a fisherman.<BR>—3 The wife of a Śūdra.<BR>—4 An altar.<BR>—5 A harlot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दासीपुत्रः, दासीसुतः, दासीश्रोत्रियः, दासीसभम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीपुत्रः|दासीपुत्र
दासी + -पुत्रः, -सुतः the son of a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीसुतः|दासीसुत
दासी + -पुत्रः, -सुतः the son of a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीश्रोत्रियः|दासीश्रोत्रिय
दासी + -श्रोत्रियः a Brāhmaṇa (knowing the Vedas) attached to a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीसभम्
दासी + -सभम् a collection of female slaves. (The gen. sing. दास्याः<BR> enters into some compounds, but loses its literal sense; <i>e. g.</i> दास्याःपुत्रः,<BR> सुतः ‘a whore-son’, used as a term of abuse; Bhāg. 3. 1. 15; Rāj. T. 5. 398;<BR> दास्याःपुत्रैः शकुनिलुब्धकैः Ś. 2; but दास्याः सदृशी<BR> ‘like a female slave’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेयः|दासेय
दासेयः The son of a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेरः|दासेर
दासेरः, -रकः<BR>—1 The son of a female slave.<BR>—2 A Śūdra.<BR>—3 A fisherman.<BR>—4 A camel; चखाद दासेरयुवा वनावलीः Śi. 12. 32, 5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेरकः|दासेरक
दासेरः, -रकः<BR>—1 The son of a female slave.<BR>—2 A Śūdra.<BR>—3 A fisherman.<BR>—4 A camel; चखाद दासेरयुवा वनावलीः Śi. 12. 32, 5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्यम्
दास्यम् Servitude, slavery, service, bondage; पतिकुले तव दास्यमपि<BR> क्षमम् Ś. 5. 27; Ms. 8. 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0812-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

