दिवा + -करः<BR>—1 the sun; Ku. 1. 12, 5. 48.<BR>—2 a crow.<BR>—3 the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकीर्तिः|दिवाकीर्ति|दिवाकीर्त्ति|दिवाकीर्त्तिः
दिवा + -कीर्तिः<BR>—1 a Cāṇḍāla. —2 a man of low caste; Ms. 5. 85.<BR>—2 a barber. दिनमिव दिवाकीर्तिस्तीक्ष्णैः क्षुरैः सवितुः करैः N. 19. 55.<BR>—3 an owl; तस्मिन् कालेऽपि च भवान् दिवाकीर्तिभयार्दितः Mb. 12. 138. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाचरः|दिवाचर
दिवा + -चरः<BR>—1 a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>—2 a kind of bird (श्यामा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवानक्तम्
दिवा + -नक्तम् Day and night; Bhāg. 5. 22. 5. ━<i>ind.</i> by day and night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवानिशम्
दिवा + -निशम् <i>ind.</i> day and night; चकोरव्रतमालम्ब्य तत्रैवासन्<BR> दिवानिशम् Ks. 76. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवापुष्टः|दिवापुष्ट
दिवा + -पुष्टः, -मणिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामणिः|दिवामणि
दिवा + -पुष्टः, -मणिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाप्रदीपः|दिवाप्रदीप
दिवा + -प्रदीपः ‘a lamp by day’, an obscure man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीतः|दिवाभीत
दिवा + -भीतः, -भीतिः<BR>—1 an owl; दिवाकराद्रक्षति यो गुहासु लीनं दिवाभीतमिवान्धकारम् Ku. 1. 12.<BR>—2 a white lotus (opening at night).<BR>—3 a thief, house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीतिः|दिवाभीति
दिवा + -भीतः, -भीतिः<BR>—1 an owl; दिवाकराद्रक्षति यो गुहासु लीनं दिवाभीतमिवान्धकारम् Ku. 1. 12.<BR>—2 a white lotus (opening at night).<BR>—3 a thief, house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामध्यम्
दिवा + -मध्यम् mid-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवारात्रम्
दिवा + -रात्रम् <i>ind.</i> day and night; Ms. 5. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवावसुः|दिवावसु
दिवा + -वसुः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाशय
दिवा + -शय <i>a.</i> sleeping by day; आरुरोह कुमुदाकरोपमां रात्रिजागरपरो<BR> दिवाशयः R. 19. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाशयता
दिवा + -शयता sleep by day; रात्रौ दिवाशयतया योऽप्यनुत्थानदूषितः<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 253.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वप्नः|दिवास्वप्न
दिवा + -स्वप्नः, -स्वापः sleep during day-time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वापः|दिवास्वाप
दिवा + -स्वप्नः, -स्वापः + .({@-पः@}) an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवास्वापः|दिवास्वाप
दिवा + -स्वप्नः, -स्वापः sleep during day-time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवातन|दिवातनः
दिवातन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दिवा भवः टपु तुद् च] Of or belonging to the<BR> day; शशिन इव दिवातनस्य लेखा Ku. 4. 46; Bk. 5. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविः|दिवि
दिविः The Chāṣa bird (also दिवः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोदासः|दिवोदास
दिवोदासः N. of a reputed Vedic king, father of सुदास; Rv. 7. 18. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्य|दिव्यं|दिव्यः
दिव्य <i>a.</i> [दिवि भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Divine, heavenly, celestial; दिव्यस्त्वं हि न मानुषः Mb. 3. 252. 8.<BR>—2 Supernatural, wonderful; परदोषेक्षणदिव्यचक्षुषः Śi. 16. 29;<BR> दिव्यं ददामि ते चक्षुः Bg. 11. 8.<BR>—3 Brilliant, splendid.<BR>—4 Charming, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यः|दिव्य|दिव्यं
दिव्य + .{@-व्यः@}<BR>—1 A superhuman or celestial being; दिव्यानामपि कृतविस्मयां पुरस्तात् Śi. 8. 64.<BR>—2 Barley.<BR>—3 An epithet of Yama.<BR>—4 A fragrant resin, bdellium.<BR>—5 A philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यम्
दिव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 Celestial nature, divinity.<BR>—2 The sky.<BR>—3 An ordeal (of which 10 kinds are enumerated); cf. Y. 2. 22, 95.<BR>—4 An oath, a solemn declaration.<BR>—5 Cloves.<BR>—6 A kind of sandal.<BR>—7 A kind of water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दिव्यांशुः, दिव्याङ्गना, दिव्यनारी, दिव्यस्त्री, दिव्यादिव्य, दिव्यावदानम्, दिव्योदकम्, दिव्योपपादुकः, दिव्यौषधिः, दिव्यकारिन्, दिव्यक्रिया, दिव्यगन्धः, दिव्यगायनः, दिव्यचक्षुस्, दिव्यज्ञानम्, दिव्यदृश्, दिव्यदोहदम्, दिव्यधुनी, दिव्यपुष्पः, दिव्यप्रश्नः, दिव्यमन्त्रः, दिव्यमानम्, दिव्यमानुषः, दिव्यरत्नम्, दिव्यरथः, दिव्यरसः, दिव्यवस्त्र, दिव्यवाक्यम्, दिव्यश्रोत्रम्, दिव्यसरित्, दिव्यसानुः, दिव्यसारः, दिव्यस्त्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यांशुः|दिव्यांशु
दिव्य + -अंशुः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्याङ्गना|दिव्यांगना
दिव्य + -अङ्गना, -नारी, -स्त्री a heavenly nymph, celestial damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यनारी
दिव्य + -अङ्गना, -नारी, -स्त्री a heavenly nymph, celestial damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यस्त्री
दिव्य + -अङ्गना, -नारी, -स्त्री a heavenly nymph, celestial damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यादिव्य|दिव्यादिव्यः
दिव्य + -अदिव्य <i>a.</i> partly human and partly divine (as a hero, such as Arjuna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यावदानम्
दिव्य + -अवदानम् N. of Buddhistic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">Page0814-2</a>]<BR> work from Nepal (written in Sanskrit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योदकम्
दिव्य + -उदकम् rainwater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योपपादुकः|दिव्योपपादुक
दिव्य + -उपपादुकः a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यौषधिः|दिव्यौषधि
दिव्य + -ओषधिः <i>f.</i> a herb of great supernatural efficacy, <i>i. e.</i><BR> curing snake-poison; हिमवति दिव्यौषधयः Mu. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यकारिन्
दिव्य + -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 taking an oath.<BR>—2 undergoing an ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यक्रिया
दिव्य + -क्रिया the application of an ordeal; निःसंभ्रमः स्तम्भयितुं<BR> देव दिव्यक्रियामयम् Rāj. T. 4. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगन्धः|दिव्यगन्ध|दिव्यगन्धं
दिव्य + -गन्धः sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगन्धा
दिव्य + -गन्धः + .({@-न्धा@}) large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगन्धम्
दिव्य + -गन्धः + .({@-न्धम्@}) cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगायनः|दिव्यगायन
दिव्य + -गायनः a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यचक्षुस्
दिव्य + -चक्षुस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having divine vision, heavenly-eyed; त्वया नियम्या ननु दिव्यचक्षुषा R. 3. 45.<BR>—2 blind. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a monkey.<BR>—2 an Astrologer.<BR>—3 Arjuna.<BR>—4 one who has prophetic vision; दिव्यचक्षुर्ज्योतिषिके पार्थात्मज्ञानिनोरपि<BR> Nm. ━(<i>n.</i>) a divine or prophetic eye, supernatural vision, the power<BR> of seeing what is invisible by the human eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यज्ञानम्
दिव्य + -ज्ञानम् supernatural knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यदृश्
दिव्य + -दृश् <i>m.</i> an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यदोहदम्
दिव्य + -दोहदम् a present offered to a deity for the accomplishment of<BR> oneʼs desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यधुनी
दिव्य + -धुनी N. of Bhāgīrathī; दिव्यधुनि मकरन्दे˚ Stotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यपुष्पः|दिव्यपुष्प
दिव्य + -पुष्पः the Karavīra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यप्रश्नः|दिव्यप्रश्न
दिव्य + -प्रश्नः inquiry into celestial phenomena or future course of events, augury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यमन्त्रः|दिव्यमन्त्र
दिव्य + -मन्त्रः Om (ओम्); Amṛt. Up. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यमानम्
दिव्य + -मानम् measuring the time according to the days and years of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यमानुषः|दिव्यमानुष
दिव्य + -मानुषः a demi-god; दिव्यमानुषचेष्टा तु परभागे न हारिणी Ks. 1. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरत्नम्
दिव्य + -रत्नम् a fabulous gem said to grant all desires of its possessor,<BR> the philosopherʼs stone; cf. चिन्तामणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरथः|दिव्यरथ
दिव्य + -रथः a celestial car moving through the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरसः|दिव्यरस
दिव्य + -रसः —1 quicksilver. —2 heavenly water or love; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यवस्त्र|दिव्यवस्त्रः
दिव्य + -वस्त्र <i>a.</i> divinely dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यवस्त्रः|दिव्यवस्त्र
दिव्य + -वस्त्र + .({@-स्त्रः@})<BR>—1 sunshine.<BR>—2 a kind of sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यवाक्यम्
दिव्य + -वाक्यम् a celestial word or voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यश्रोत्रम्
दिव्य + -श्रोत्रम् an ear which hears everything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यसरित्
दिव्य + -सरित् <i>f.</i> the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यसानुः|दिव्यसानु
दिव्य + -सानुः N. of one of the Viśvedevas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यसारः|दिव्यसार
दिव्य + -सारः the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यस्त्री
दिव्य + -स्त्री an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
दिश् €6 U. (दिशति-ते, दिष्ट; <i>desid.</i> दिदिक्षति-ते)<BR>—1 To point out, show, exhibit, produce (as a witness); साक्षिणः सन्ति<BR> मेत्युक्त्वा दिशेत्युक्तो दिशेन्न यः Ms. 8. 57, 52, 53.<BR>—2 To assign, allot; इष्टां गतिं तस्य सुरा दिशन्ति Mb.<BR>—3 To give, grant, bestow upon, deliver or make over to; बाणमत्रभवते<BR> निजं दिशन् Ki. 13. 68; R. 5. 30, 11. 2, 16. 72.<BR>—4 To pay (as tribute).<BR>—5 To consent to; मृत्यभाविं दुहितुः परिग्रहाद्दिश्यतां कुलमिदं निमेरिति R. 11. 49.<BR>—6 To direct, order, command.<BR>—7 To allow, permit; स्मर्तुं दिशन्ति न दिवः सुरसुन्दरीभ्यः Ki. 5. 28.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> (देशयति-ते)<BR>—1 To show, point out, allot, assign.<BR>—2 To teach, communicate, tell, inform.<BR>—3 To direct, order.<BR>—4 To confer, bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
दिश् <i>f.</i> [दिशति ददात्यवकाशं दिश्-क्विप्] (Nom. sing. दिक्ग्)<BR>—1 A direction, cardinal point, point of the compass, quarter of the sky;<BR> दिशः प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः सुखाः R. 3. 14; दिशि दिशि किरति सजलकणजालम् Gīt. 4.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The mere direction of a thing, hint, indication (of the general<BR> lines); इति दिक् (often used by commentators &c.); इत्थं लौकिकशब्दानां<BR> दिङ्मात्रमिह दर्शितम् Sk.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) (Hence) Mode, manner, method; मुनेः पाठोक्तदिशा S. D.; दिगियं<BR> सूत्रकृता प्रदर्शितादासीसभं नृपसभं रक्षःसभमिमा दिशः Ak.<BR>—3 Region, space,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">Page0815-1</a>]<BR> place in general.<BR>—4 A foreign or distant region.<BR>—5 A point of view, manner of considering a subject.<BR>—6 A precept, order.<BR>—7 The number ‘ten’.<BR>—8 A side or party.<BR>—9 The mark of a bite. ‘दिग्दष्टे वर्तुलाकारे करिका नखरेखिका’ इति<BR> वैजयन्ती; परिणतदिक्करिकास्तटीर्बिभर्ति Śi. 4. 29. [N. B. In comp.<BR> दिश् becomes दिग् before words beginning with vowels and soft consonants,<BR> and दिक् before words beginning with hard consonants; <i>e. g.</i> दिगम्बर,<BR> दिग्गज, दिक्पथ, दिक्करिन्, &c.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दिगन्तः, दिगन्तरम्, दिगम्बर, दिग्वासस्, दिगम्बरकः, दिगवस्थानम्, दिगागत, दिगिभः, दिगीशः, दिगीश्वरः, दिक्कन्या, दिक्कान्ता, दिक्कामिनी, दिग्वधू, दिक्करः, दिक्करिका, दिक्करी, दिक्करिन्, दिग्गज, दिग्दन्तिन्, दिग्वारणः, दिग्ग्रहणम्, दिग्बन्धः, दिक्चक्रम्, दिग्जयः, दिग्विजयः, दिक्तटम्, दिग्दर्शनम्, दिग्दर्शिन्, दिग्दाहः, दिग्देशः, दिङ्नागः, दिक्पतिः, दिक्पालः, दिक्पथः, दिग्भागः, दिग्भ्रमः, दिङ्मण्डलम्, दिङ्मात्रम्, दिङ्मुखम्, दिङ्मोहः, दिग्यात्रा, दिग्वसन, दिग्वस्त्र, दिग्विभावित, दिक्छूलम्, दिक्साधनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0814-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तः|दिगन्त|दिगंत
दिश् + -अन्तः end of the direction or horizon, remote distance, remote<BR> place; दिगन्ते श्रूयन्ते मदमलिनगण्डाः करटिनः Bv. 1. 2; Māl. 2. 9;<BR> R. 3. 4, 5. 67, 16. 87. नानादिगन्तागता राजानः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तरम्
दिश् + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 another direction.<BR>—2 the intermediate space, atmosphere, space.<BR>—3 a distant quarter, another or foreign country; संचारपूतानि दिगन्तराणि<BR> कृत्वा दिनान्ते निलयाय गन्तुम् R. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बर|दिगंबर|दिगम्बरः
दिश् + -अम्बर, -वासस् <i>a.</i> having only the directions for his clothing,<BR> stark naked, unclothed; दिगम्बरत्वेन निवेदितं वसु Ku. 5. 72; एकाकी<BR> गृहसंत्यक्तः पाणिपात्रो दिगम्बरः Pt. 5. 15; Ms. 11. 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वासस्
दिश् + -अम्बर, -वासस् <i>a.</i> having only the directions for his clothing,<BR> stark naked, unclothed; दिगम्बरत्वेन निवेदितं वसु Ku. 5. 72; एकाकी<BR> गृहसंत्यक्तः पाणिपात्रो दिगम्बरः Pt. 5. 15; Ms. 11. 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बरः|दिगम्बर|दिगंबर
दिश् + -अम्बर, -वासस् + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a naked mendicant (of the Jaina or Buddha sect.)<BR>—2 a mendicant, an ascetic.<BR>—3 an epithet of (1) Śiva; (2) Skanda.<BR>—4 darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बरी
दिश् + -अम्बर, -वासस् + .({@-री@}) an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बरकः|दिगम्बरक
दिश् + -अम्बरकः a naked mendicant (of the Jaina sect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगवस्थानम्
दिश् + -अवस्थानम् the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगागत
दिश् + -आगत <i>a.</i> Come from a distance; Y. 2. 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगिभः|दिगिभ
दिश् + -इभः See दिक्करिन् &c. दिगिभाः पूर्णकलशैः Bhāg. 8. 8. 14, 5. 14. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगीशः|दिगीश
दिश् + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः regent of a quarter; चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी<BR> Ku. 5. 53; see अष्टदिक्पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगीश्वरः|दिगीश्वर
दिश् + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः regent of a quarter; चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी<BR> Ku. 5. 53; see अष्टदिक्पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

