दिक्करी
दिश् + -करिका, -करी a young girl or woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्करिन्
दिश् + -करिन्, -गज, -दन्तिन्, -वारणः <i>m.</i> one of the eight elephants<BR> said to guard and preside over the eight cardinal points; (see अष्टदिग्गज);<BR> दिग्दन्तिशेषाः ककुभश्चकार Vikr. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्गज|दिग्गजः
दिश् + -करिन्, -गज, -दन्तिन्, -वारणः <i>m.</i> one of the eight elephants<BR> said to guard and preside over the eight cardinal points; (see अष्टदिग्गज);<BR> दिग्दन्तिशेषाः ककुभश्चकार Vikr. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दन्तिन्|दिग्दंतिन्
दिश् + -करिन्, -गज, -दन्तिन्, -वारणः <i>m.</i> one of the eight elephants<BR> said to guard and preside over the eight cardinal points; (see अष्टदिग्गज);<BR> दिग्दन्तिशेषाः ककुभश्चकार Vikr. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वारणः|दिग्वारण
दिश् + -करिन्, -गज, -दन्तिन्, -वारणः <i>m.</i> one of the eight elephants<BR> said to guard and preside over the eight cardinal points; (see अष्टदिग्गज);<BR> दिग्दन्तिशेषाः ककुभश्चकार Vikr. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्ग्रहणम्
दिश् + -ग्रहणम्, -बन्धः observation of the quarters of the compass;<BR> Bṛ. S. 24. 9. संपूज्य शारिकांदेवीं दिग्बन्धादिपुरःसरम् Ks. 73. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्बन्धः|दिग्बन्ध
दिश् + -ग्रहणम्, -बन्धः observation of the quarters of the compass;<BR> Bṛ. S. 24. 9. संपूज्य शारिकांदेवीं दिग्बन्धादिपुरःसरम् Ks. 73. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्चक्रम्
दिश् + -चक्रम्<BR>—1 the horizon; Ratn. 3. 5.<BR>—2 the whole world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्जयः|दिग्जय
दिश् + -जयः, -विजयः ‘conquest of the directions’, the conquest of<BR> various countries in all directions, conquest of the world; सुनिश्चितपुरं<BR> चक्रे दिग्जये कृतनिश्चयः Rāj. T. 4. 183; स दिग्विजयमव्याजवीरः<BR> स्मरः इवाकरोत् Vikr. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजयः|दिग्विजय
दिश् + -जयः, -विजयः ‘conquest of the directions’, the conquest of<BR> various countries in all directions, conquest of the world; सुनिश्चितपुरं<BR> चक्रे दिग्जये कृतनिश्चयः Rāj. T. 4. 183; स दिग्विजयमव्याजवीरः<BR> स्मरः इवाकरोत् Vikr. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्तटम्
दिश् + -तटम् the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दर्शनम्
दिश् + -दर्शनम्<BR>—1 showing merely the direction, pointing out only the general mode or manner.<BR>—2 a general outline or survey.<BR>—3 a compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दर्शिन्
दिश् + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> looking on all sides, having a general view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दाहः|दिग्दाह
दिश् + -दाहः preternatural redness of the horizon; दैग्दाहः ‘a conflagration of the regions of the sky’<BR> (regarded as an evil omen) N. 12. 92; cf. Ms. 4. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्देशः|दिग्देश
दिश् + -देशः<BR>—1 a distant region or country; दृश्यन्ते कुलनिम्नगा अपि परं दिग्देशकालाविमौ<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 308, 417.<BR>—2 region, country; H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्नागः|दिङ्नाग
दिश् + -नागः<BR>—1 an elephant of the quarter of the compass; see दिग्गज.<BR>—2 N. of a poet said to be a contemporary of Kālidāsa. (This interpretation<BR> is based on Mallināthaʼs gloss on दिङ्नागानां पथि परिहरन् स्थूलहस्तावलेपान्<BR> Me. 14; which is, however, very doubtful.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">Page0815-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पतिः|दिक्पति
दिश् + -पतिः, -पालः the regent or guardian of a quarter; Rāj. T. 4. 225<BR> (for the names of the several regents, see अष्टदिक्पाल; cf. Ms. 5. 96, 7. 303<BR> also); सूर्यः शुक्रः क्षमापुत्रः सैंहिकेयः शनिः शशी ।<BR> सौम्यस्त्रिदशमन्त्री च प्राच्यादिदिगधीश्वराः ॥ -Jyotistattvam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पालः|दिक्पाल
दिश् + -पतिः, -पालः the regent or guardian of a quarter; Rāj. T. 4. 225<BR> (for the names of the several regents, see अष्टदिक्पाल; cf. Ms. 5. 96, 7. 303<BR> also); सूर्यः शुक्रः क्षमापुत्रः सैंहिकेयः शनिः शशी ।<BR> सौम्यस्त्रिदशमन्त्री च प्राच्यादिदिगधीश्वराः ॥ -Jyotistattvam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पथः|दिक्पथ
दिश् + -पथः the surrounding region; सैन्यैर्नानापथायातैर्नदद्भिर्व्याप्तदिक्पथः<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्भागः|दिग्भाग
दिश् + -भागः a point of the compass, direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्भ्रमः|दिग्भ्रम
दिश् + -भ्रमः perplexity about points of the compass, mistaking the<BR> way or direction; Vikr. 5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मण्डलम्
दिश् + -मण्डलम् = दिक्चक्रम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मात्रम्
दिश् + -मात्रम् the mere direction or indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मुखम्
दिश् + -मुखम् any quarter or part of the sky; हरति मे हरिवाहनदिङ्मुखम्<BR> V. 3. 6; Amaru. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मोहः|दिङ्मोह
दिश् + -मोहः mistaking the way or direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्यात्रा
दिश् + -यात्रा a procession in different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वसन
दिश् + -वसन, -वस्त्र <i>a.</i> stark naked, unclothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वस्त्रः|दिग्वस्त्र
दिश् + -वसन, -वस्त्र + .({@-स्त्रः@})<BR>—1 a Jaina or Buddhist mendicant of the दिगम्बर class.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वस्त्र|दिग्वस्त्रः
दिश् + -वसन, -वस्त्र <i>a.</i> stark naked, unclothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभावित
दिश् + -विभावित <i>a.</i> renowned or celebrated in all quarters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्छूलम्
दिश् + -शूलम् a bad yoga in Astronomy; cf. शुक्रादित्यदिने न वारुणदिशं<BR> न ज्ञे कुजे चोत्तरां मन्देन्दोश्च दिने न शक्रककुभं याम्यां गुरौ न व्रजेत् ।<BR> शूलानीति विलङ्घ्य यान्ति मनुजा ये वित्तलाभाशया भ्रष्टाशाः पुनरापतन्ति<BR> यदि ते शुक्रेण तुल्या अपि ॥ Jyotissārasaṅgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्साधनम्
दिश् + -साधनम् a means to make the journey in various quarters successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशस्
दिशस् <i>f.</i> (= दिश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशा
दिशा Direction, quarter of the compass, region, &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दिशागजः, दिशापालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशागजः|दिशागज
दिशा + -गजः, -पालः see दिग्गज, दिक्पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशापालः|दिशापाल
दिशा + -गजः, -पालः see दिग्गज, दिक्पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशोभाज्
दिशोभाज् <i>m.</i> One who runs in all directions, a fugitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्य|दिश्यं
दिश्य <i>a.</i> [दिशि भवः दिगा˚ यत्]<BR>—1 Belonging to or situated towards any quarter of the compass.<BR>—2 Foreign, outlandish; Śi. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [दिश्-कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Shown, indicated, assigned, pointed out.<BR>—2 Described, referred to.<BR>—3 Fixed, settled.<BR>—4 Directed, ordered &c.<BR>—5 Destined (दैवविहित); न दिष्टमर्थमत्येतुमीशो मर्त्यः कथंचन<BR> Mb. 3. 135. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टः|दिष्ट|दिष्टं
दिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टम्
दिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Assignment, allotment<BR>—2 Fate, destiny, good or ill-luck; भो दिष्टम् Ś. 2. यश्च दिष्टपरो<BR> लोके यश्चापि हठवादिकः । उभावपि शठावेतौ कर्मबुद्धिः प्रशस्यते ॥ Mb. 3. 32. 13.<BR>—3 Order, direction, command; सैनिका भयनाम्नो ये बर्हिष्मन् दिष्टकारिणः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 28. 1.<BR>—4 Aim, object.<BR>—5 An appointed place; तं प्रेतं दिष्टमितोऽग्नय एव हरन्ति Ch. Up. 5. 9. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दिष्टान्तः, दिष्टगतिः, दिष्टदृश्, दिष्टभाज्, दिष्टभावः, दिष्टभुक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टान्तः|दिष्टान्त|दिष्टांत
दिष्ट + -अन्तः ‘the end of oneʼs appointed time’, death; दिष्टान्तमाप्स्यति<BR> भवानपि पुत्रशोकात् R. 9. 79; Rām. 2. 65. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टगतिः
दिष्ट + -गतिः <i>f.</i> death; याजमानासम्भवादशक्यं हि दिष्टगतौ उत्तरं<BR> तन्त्रं कर्तुम् ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 57. Hence दिष्टां गतिं गम् = To<BR> die. तस्मिंश्च दिष्टां गतिं गते फलं दर्शयति यो दीक्षितानां प्रमीयेत<BR> अपि तस्य फलमिति । ŚB. on MS. 6. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टदृश्
दिष्ट + -दृश् <i>m.</i> the god; यस्य तुष्यति दिष्टदृक् Bhāg. 4. 21. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टभाज्
दिष्ट + -भाज् God. N. 11. 129. Chaṇḍū Paṇḍita com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टभावः|दिष्टभाव
दिष्ट + -भावः death; दिष्टभावं गतस्यापि विषये मोदते प्रजा Mb. 5. 133. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टभुक्
दिष्ट + -भुक् <i>a.</i> reaping the fruit as destined or ordained by god;<BR> वसेऽन्यदपि संप्राप्तं दिष्टभुक् तुष्टधीरहम् Bhāg. 7. 13. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0815-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टिः|दिष्टि
दिष्टिः <i>f.</i> [दिश भावे क्तिन्, संज्ञायां कर्तरि क्तिच् वा]<BR>—1 Assignment, allotment.<BR>—2 Direction, command, instruction, rule, precept.<BR>—3 Fate, fortune, destiny.<BR>—4 Good fortune, happiness, any auspicious event (such as the birth of<BR> a son); दिष्टिवृद्धिमिव शुश्राव K. 55; दिष्टिवृद्धिसंभ्रमो महानभूत् K. 70.<BR>—5 A sort of measure of length.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दिष्टिवृद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टिवृद्धिः|दिष्टिवृद्धि
दिष्टिः + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> congratulation; see दृष्टिः (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट्या
दिष्ट्या <i>ind.</i> (Strictly the instr. sing. of दिष्टि) Fortunately,<BR> luckily, thank God, how glad I am, how fortunate, bravo; (an exclamation<BR> of joy or gratulation); दिष्टपा प्रतिहतं दुर्जातम् Māl. 4; दिष्टपा<BR> सोयं महाबाहुरञ्जनानन्दवर्धनः U. 1. 32; Ve. 2. 12. (दिष्टपा वृध्<BR> means ‘to be congratulated upon’; as in दिष्टपा धर्मपत्नीसमागमेन<BR> पुत्रमुखदर्शनेन चायुष्मान् वर्धते Ś. 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशना
देशना <i>f.</i> Direction, injunction, laying down; सर्वास्वेव वैकृतीषु<BR> देशनासु प्राकृतं धर्मजातमपेक्ष्यते वाक्यशेषत्वेन । ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्णुः|दिष्णु
दिष्णुः A giver, donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह्
दिह् €2 U. (देग्धि, दिग्धे, दिग्ध; <i>desid.</i> दिधिक्षति)<BR>—1 To anoint, smear, plaster, spread over; स चन्दनोशीरमृणालदिग्धः<BR> Bk. 3. 21, अदिहंश्चन्दनैः शुभैः 17. 54.<BR>—2 To soil, defile, pollute; अस्रदिग्धं पदम् R. 16. 15.<BR>—3 To increase, augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह्
दिह् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Anointing, smearing.<BR>—2 Pollution, soiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्ध|दिग्धः
दिग्ध <i>p. p.</i> [दिह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Smeared, anointed, daubed; हस्तावसृग्दिग्धौ Ms. 3. 132; R. 16. 15.<BR> दिग्धोऽमृतेन च विषेण च पक्ष्मलाक्ष्या गाढं निखात इव मे हृदये कटाक्षः Māl. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Soiled, defiled, polluted.<BR>—3 Poisoned, envenomed; अथ तैः परिदेविताक्षरैर्हृदये दिग्धशरैरिवाहतः Ku. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्धः|दिग्ध
दिग्ध + .{@-ग्धः@}<BR>—1 Oil, ointment.<BR>—2 Any oily substance or unguent.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR>—4 A poisoned arrow; ‘दिग्धो विषाक्तबाणे स्यात्’ Med. करेणुमिव<BR> दिग्धेन विद्धां मृगयुना वने Rām. 2. 10. 26; Mb. 12. 69. 57.<BR>—5 A story (true or fictitious.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी I. €4 Ā. (दीयते, दीन)<BR>—1 To perish, die.<BR>—2 To waste, decay, diminish. ━II. €4 P. (दीयति) Ved. soar, fly. ━III. €3 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To please, be admired, appear good.<BR>—3 To bestow upon by shining; संददस्वान् रयिमस्मासु दीदिहि Rv. 2. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीः
दीः <i>f.</i> Decay, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीतिः|दीति
दीतिः, दीदितिः <i>f.</i> Splendour, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीदितिः|दीदिति
दीतिः, दीदितिः <i>f.</i> Splendour, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीन|दीनं|दीनः
दीन <i>a.</i> [दी-क्त तस्य न]<BR>—1 Poor, indigent.<BR>—2 Distressed, ruined, afflicted, miserable, wretched.<BR>—3 Sorry, dejected, melancholy, sad; सा विरहे तव दीना Gīt. 4.<BR>—4 Timid, frightened.<BR>—5 Mean, piteous; यं यं पश्यसि तस्य तस्य पुरतो मा ब्रूहि दीनं<BR> वचः Bh. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनः|दीन|दीनं
दीन + .{@-नः@} A poor person, one in distress or misery; दीनानां कल्पवृक्षः<BR> Mk. 1. 48; दिनानि दीनोद्धरणोचितस्य R. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनम्
दीन + .{@-नम्@} Distress, wretchedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीना
दीन + .{@-ना@} The female of a mouse or shrew.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीनदयालु, दीनवत्सल, दीनबन्धुः, दीनलोचनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनदयालु
दीन + -दयालु, -वत्सल <i>a.</i> kind to the poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनवत्सल
दीन + -दयालु, -वत्सल <i>a.</i> kind to the poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनबन्धुः|दीनबन्धु
दीन + -बन्धुः a friend of the poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनलोचनः|दीनलोचन
दीन + -लोचनः a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनक
दीनक <i>a.</i> Distressed, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनता
दीनता Scarcity, weakness; क्रत्वः समह दीनता प्रतीपं जगमा<BR> शुचे Rv. 7. 89. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्ष्
दीक्ष् €1 Ā. (दीक्षते, दीक्षित)<BR>—1 To consecrate or prepare oneself for the<BR> performance of a sacred rite; दीक्षयस्व त्वमात्मानम् Mb. 14. 71. 21;<BR> see दीक्षित below.<BR>—2 To dedicate oneself to.<BR>—3 To initiate or introduce a pupil.<BR>—4 To invest with the sacred thread.<BR>—5 To sacrifice.<BR>—6 To practise self-restraint.<BR>—7 To shave oneʼs head, to be shaved.<BR>—8 <i>caus.</i> impel; induce तत्कलमस्तमदिदीक्षत क्षणं तालवृन्तचलनाय<BR> नायकम् N. 18. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षकः|दीक्षक
दीक्षकः A spiritual guide, priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षणम्
दीक्षणम् [दीक्षभावे ल्युट्] Initiation, consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षणीया
दीक्षणीया, दीक्षणीयेष्टि <i>f.</i> A sacrificial yāga before<BR> initiation; the sacrifice of consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षणीयेष्टि|दीक्षणीयेष्टिः
दीक्षणीया, दीक्षणीयेष्टि <i>f.</i> A sacrificial yāga before<BR> initiation; the sacrifice of consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षा
दीक्षा [दीक्ष्-भावे-अ]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Consecration for a religious ceremony, initiation in general;<BR> अजस्रदीक्षाप्रयतस्य मद्गुरोः क्रियाविघाताय कथं प्रवर्तसे R. 3. 44, 65.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Receiving the initiatory <i>mantra</i>.<BR>—2 A ceremony preliminary to a sacrifice; Bhāg. 3. 13. 37.<BR>—3 A ceremony or religious rite in general; विवाहदीक्षाम्, R. 3. 33;<BR> Ku. 7. 1, 8, 24.<BR>—4 Investiture with the sacred thread. —5 Dedicating oneself to a particular<BR> object, self-devotion; विश्वत्राणैकदीक्षाः; विष्णुपादादिकेशान्तवर्णनस्तोत्रम् 33.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीक्षान्तः, दीक्षाश्रमः, दीक्षापतिः, दीक्षायूपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षान्तः|दीक्षान्त|दीक्षांत
दीक्षा + -अन्तः a supplementary sacrifice made to atone for the defects<BR> in a preceding one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षाश्रमः
दीक्षा + -आश्रमः (अवमृथ) (वैखानसः) the third stage of life<BR> (वानप्रस्थाश्रम); Mb. 12. 66. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षापतिः|दीक्षापति
दीक्षा + -पतिः the Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षायूपः|दीक्षायूप
दीक्षा + -यूपः A sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षित|दीक्षितः
दीक्षित <i>p. p.</i> [दीक्ष् कर्तरि क्त, दीक्षा जाताऽस्य तार˚ इतच् वा]<BR>—1 Consecrated, initiated (as for a religious ceremony); एते विवाहदीक्षिता<BR> यूयम् U. 1; Pt. 1. 167; आपन्ना भयसत्रेषु दीक्षिताः खलु पौरवाः<BR> Ś. 2. 17; R. 8. 75, 11. 24; Ve. 1. 25.<BR>—2 Prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>—3 Prepared for having taken a vow of; तं पितुर्वधभवेन मन्युना राजवंशनिधनाय<BR> दीक्षितम् R. 11. 67.<BR>—4 Crowned; पद्मा पद्मातपत्रेण भेजे साम्राज्यदीक्षितम् R. 4. 5.<BR>—5 Performed (as the दीक्षा ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षितः|दीक्षित
दीक्षित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A priest engaged in a Dīkṣā; नालं ते विप्रियं कर्तुं दीक्षितस्येव<BR> साधवः Rām. 3. 65. 12.<BR>—2 A pupil. —3 A person who or whose ancestors may have performed a grand<BR> sacrificial ceremony, such as ज्योतिष्टोम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षितृ
दीक्षितृ <i>m.</i> A consecrator, spiritual father; P. III. 2. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीदिवि|दीदिविः
दीदिवि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 shining; राजन्तमध्वराणां गोपामृतस्य दीदिविम् Rv. 1. 1. 8.<BR>—2 Risen (as a star).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीदिविः|दीदिवि
दीदिवि + .{@-विः@}<BR>—1 Boiled rice.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR>—3 An epithet of (1) Agni; (2) Bṛhaspati.<BR>—4 Final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधितिः|दीधिति
दीधितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light; तैरेव प्रतियुवतेरकारि दूरात्कालुष्यं शशधरदीधितिच्छटाच्छैः<BR> Śi. 8. 38; R. 3. 22, 17. 48; N. 2. 69; U. 6. 18.<BR>—2 Splendour, brightness.<BR>—3 Bodily<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">Page0817-1</a>]<BR> lustre, energy; विपन्नदीधितिरपि Bh. 2. 29.<BR>—4 A finger.<BR>—5 Ved. A religious prayer or devotion; इयं सा वो अस्मे दीधितिर्यजत्रा<BR> Rv. 1. 186. 11.<BR>—6 A son-in-law.<BR>—7 Divine inspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0816-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधितिमत्|दीधितिमन्त्
दीधितिमत् <i>a.</i> Brilliant. ━<i>m.</i> The sun; (प्रातर्दीधितिमानिव<BR> आविरभूत्) Ku. 2. 2, 7. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधी
दीधी €2 Ā. (दीधीते)<BR>—1 To shine,<BR>—2 To seem, appear; अक्षेत्रविद् यथा मुग्धो भुवनान्यदीधयुः Rv. 5. 40. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनारः|दीनार
दीनारः<BR>—1 A particular gold; जितश्चासौ मया षोडशसहस्त्राणि दीनाराणाम् Dk.<BR>—2 A coin in general.<BR>—3 A gold ornament.<BR>—4 A seal.<BR>—5 A weight of gold (cf. Gr. <i>denarius</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्
दीप् €4 Ā. (दीप्यते, दीप्त; <i>freq.</i> देदीप्यते)<BR>—1 To shine, blaze, (fig. also); सर्वैरुस्रैः समग्रैस्त्वमिव नृपगुणैर्दीप्यते<BR> सप्तसप्तिः M. 2. 12; तरुणीस्तन एव दीप्यते मणिहारावलिरामणीयकम्<BR> N. 2. 44; Bk. 2. 2; R. 14. 64; H. Pr. 46.<BR>—2 To burn, be lighted; सोऽयमग्निः परेण मृत्युमतिक्रान्तो दीप्यते<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 12. यथा यथा चेयं चपला दीप्यते K. 105.<BR>—3 To glow, be inflamed or excited, increase (fig. also); वन्येतरानेकपदर्शनेन<BR> पुनर्दिदीपे मददुर्दिनश्रीः R. 5. 47; Bk. 15. 88; Śi. 20. 71.<BR>—4 To be fired with anger; आसाद्य वाचं स भृशं दिदीपे Ki. 3. 55.<BR>—5 To be illustrious. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दीपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To kindle, set on fire, inflame; अयं हि मां दीपयतेऽद्य वह्निः<BR> Rām. 2. 43. 21.<BR>—2 To illuminate, light, irradiate; वृन्दावनान्तरमदीपयदंशुजालैः<BR> (इन्दुः) Gīt. 7; U. 1. 42.<BR>—3 To excite, raise.<BR>—4 To adorn, grace; अवयवदीपितमण्डनश्रियस्ताः Ki. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपः|दीप
दीपः-ली [दीप्-णिच् अच्] —1 A lamp, light; नृपदीपो धनस्नेहं प्रजाभ्यः<BR> संहरन्नपि । अन्तरस्थैर्गुणैः शुभ्रैर्लक्ष्यते नैव केनचित् ॥ Pt. 1. 221;<BR> न हि दीपौ परस्परस्योपकुरुतः Ś. B.; so ज्ञानदीपः &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीपाङ्कुर, दीपान्विता, दीपाराधनम्, दीपालिः, दीपाली, दीपावली, दीपोत्सवः, दीपोच्छिष्टम्, दीपकलिका, दीपकिट्टम्, दीपकूपी, दीपखोरी, दीपद, दीपदण्डः, दीपध्वजः, दीपपुष्पः, दीपभाजनम्, दीपमाला, दीपवर्तिः, दीपवृक्षः, दीपशत्रुः, दीपशिखा, दीपशृङ्खला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपाङ्कुर
दीपः + -अङ्कुर the flame or light of a lamp; दीपाङ्कुरच्छायाचञ्चलमाकलग्य Bh. 3. 68. कुरण्टकविपाण्डुरं दधति धाम दीपाङ्कुराः Vb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपान्विता
दीपः + -अन्विता<BR>—1 the day of new moon (अमा).<BR>—2 = दीपाली q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपाराधनम्
दीपः + -आराधनम् worshipping an idol by waving a light before it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपालिः|दीपालि
दीपः + -आलिः, -आली, -आवली, -उत्सवः<BR>—1 a row of lights, nocturnal illumination.<BR>—2 particularly, the festival called <i>Diwali</i> held on the night of new<BR> moon in आश्विन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपाली
दीपः + -आलिः, -आली, -आवली, -उत्सवः<BR>—1 a row of lights, nocturnal illumination.<BR>—2 particularly, the festival called <i>Diwali</i> held on the night of new<BR> moon in आश्विन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपावली
दीपः + -आलिः, -आली, -आवली, -उत्सवः<BR>—1 a row of lights, nocturnal illumination.<BR>—2 particularly, the festival called <i>Diwali</i> held on the night of new<BR> moon in आश्विन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपोत्सवः|दीपोत्सव
दीपः + -आलिः, -आली, -आवली, -उत्सवः<BR>—1 a row of lights, nocturnal illumination.<BR>—2 particularly, the festival called <i>Diwali</i> held on the night of new<BR> moon in आश्विन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपोच्छिष्टम्
दीपः + -उच्छिष्टम् soot, lamp-black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकलिका
दीपः + -कलिका<BR>—1 the flame of a lamp.<BR>—2 N. of a com. on Yajñavalkya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकिट्टम्
दीपः + -किट्टम् lamp-black, soot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकूपी
दीपः + -कूपी, -खोरी the wick of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपखोरी
दीपः + -कूपी, -खोरी the wick of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपद
दीपः + -द <i>a.</i> one who gives a lamp; दीपदश्चक्षुरुत्तमम् Ms. 4. 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपदण्डः
दीपः + -दण्डः A lamp-post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपध्वजः|दीपध्वज
दीपः + -ध्वजः<BR>—1 lamp-black.<BR>—2 lamp-stand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपपुष्पः|दीपपुष्प
दीपः + -पुष्पः the Champaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपभाजनम्
दीपः + -भाजनम् a lamp; वामनार्चिरिव दीपभाजनम् (अभूत्) R. 19. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपमाला
दीपः + -माला lighting, illumination; अद्यापि तां धवलवेश्मनि रत्नदीपमालामयूखपटलैर्दलितान्धकारे C. P. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपवर्तिः|दीपवर्ति
दीपः + -वर्तिः the wick of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपवृक्षः|दीपवृक्ष
दीपः + -वृक्षः<BR>—1 a lampstand. कनकोज्ज्वलदीप्तदीपवृक्षम् (आसनम्) Bu. C. 5. 44.<BR> तथेह पञ्चेन्द्रियदीपवृक्षा ज्ञानप्रदीप्ताः परवन्त एव Mb. 12. 202. 9.<BR> A treelike column of building (Mar. दीपमाळ); Rām. 2. 6. 18;<BR> also दीपपादप (a candle-stick).<BR>—2 a light.<BR>—3 a lantern.<BR>—4 the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">Page0817-2</a>]<BR> tree called <i>devadāru</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशत्रुः|दीपशत्रु
दीपः + -शत्रुः a moth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशिखा
दीपः + -शिखा<BR>—1 the flame of a lamp. अनङ्गमङ्गलावासरत्नदीपशिखामिव Ks. 18. 77.<BR>—2 lamp-black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशृङ्खला|दीपशृंखला
दीपः + -शृङ्खला a row of lights, illumination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपक|दीपकं|दीपकः
दीपक <i>a.</i> (-पिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दीप्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Kindling, inflaming.<BR>—2 Illuminating, making bright.<BR>—3 Illustrating, beautifying, making illustrious.<BR>—4 Exciting, making intense; सामवादाः सकोपस्य तस्य प्रत्युत दीपकाः<BR> Śi. 2. 55; Pt. 3. 28.<BR>—5 Tonic, stimulating digestion, digestive. —6 Skilful in managing a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकः|दीपक|दीपकं
दीपक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A light, lamp; तावदेव कृतिनामपि स्फुरत्येष निर्मलविवेकदीपकः Bh. 1. 70.<BR>—2 A falcon.<BR>—3 An epithet of Kāmadeva (also दीप्यक).<BR>—4 N. of several plants (Mar. ओंवा, जिरें, चित्रक, कांदा, मोरशेंडा)<BR>—5 N. of a Rāga.<BR>—6 A kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकम्
दीपक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Saffron.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech in which two or more objects (some प्रकृत<BR> ‘relevant’ and some अप्रकृत ‘irrelevant’) having the same attribute<BR> are associated together, or in which several attributes (some relevant<BR> and some irrelevant) are predicated of the same object; सकृद्वृत्तिस्तु<BR> धर्मस्य प्रकृताप्रकृतात्मनाम् । सैव क्रिंयासु बह्वीषु कारकस्येति दीपकम् ॥<BR> K. P. 10; cf. वदन्ति वर्ण्यावर्ण्यानाम् धर्मैक्यं दीपकं बुधाः ।<BR> मदेन भाति कलभः प्रतापेन महीपतिः ॥ Candr. 5. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपन|दीपनं|दीपनः
दीपन <i>a.</i> [दीप् णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Kindling, inflaming, &c.<BR>—2 Digestive, tonic.<BR>—3 Exciting, animating, stimulating; आनन्दमिश्रमदनज्वरदीपनानि Māl. 9. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनम्
दीपन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Kindling, inflaming.<BR>—2 A tonic stimulating digestion.<BR>—3 Exciting, stimulating,<BR>—4 Lighting, illuminating.<BR>—5 Promoting digestion.<BR>—6 Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनः|दीपन|दीपनं
दीपन + .{@-नः@} see दीपकः (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनी
दीपन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 N. of several plants (Mar. काकडी, मेथी, पहाडमूळ, ओंवा).<BR>—2 A mystical Tāntrika formula.<BR>—3 (In Music) A kind of composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीय|दीपनीयः
दीपनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be lighted or set on fire.<BR>—2 Combustible, inflammable.<BR>—3 To be excited or stimulated.<BR>—4 Relating to tonic medicines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीयः|दीपनीय
दीपनीय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 An aromatic seed (यवानी).<BR>—2 N. of some medicinal or aromatic substances (Mar. सुंठ, मिरी, पिंपळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीयम्
दीपनीय + .{@-यम्@} A tonic medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपिका
दीपिका<BR>—1 A light, torch; आसन्नोषधयो नेतुर्नक्तमस्नेहदीपिका, R. 4. 75, 9. 70.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Illustrator. elucidator as in तर्कदीपिका.<BR>—3 Moonlight.<BR>—4 N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR>—5 N. of some plants (Mar. वेखंड, मेथी, ओंवा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीपिकातैलम्, दीपिकाधारिणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपिकातैलम्
दीपिका + -तैलम् the oil of ptychotis Ajowan (Mar. ओंव्याचें तेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपिकाधारिणी
दीपिका + -धारिणी a female lamp-carrier; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपित
दीपित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set on fire.<BR>—2 Inflamed.<BR>—3 Illuminated.<BR>—4 Manifested.<BR>—5 Excited, stimulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपितृ
दीपितृ <i>m.</i> An illuminator, enlightener, P. III. 2. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपिन्
दीपिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Inflaming, kindling; राकानिशेव पूर्णेन्दुमुखी कन्दर्पदीपिनी Ks. 82. 29.<BR>—2 Illuminating. —3 Shining, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्त|दीप्तं|दीप्तः
दीप्त <i>p. p.</i> [दीप् क्त]<BR>—1 Lighted, inflamed, kindled; यथा सुदीप्तात्पावकाद्विस्फुलिङ्गाः सहस्रशः<BR> प्रभवन्ते सरूपाः Muṇḍ. 2. 1. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">Page0818-1</a>]<BR>—2 Glowing, hot, flashing, radiant.<BR>—3 Illuminated.<BR>—4 Excited, stimulated.<BR>—5 Luminous, bright; ततः शकुनयो दीप्ता मृगाश्च क्रूरभाषिणः । दीप्तायां<BR> दिशि भाषन्तो भयमावेदयन्ति मे ॥ Hariv.<BR>—6 Heated by the sun, exposed to sunshine.<BR>—7 Inauspicious (in general); Bṛ. S. 91. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तः|दीप्त|दीप्तं
दीप्त + .{@-प्तः@}<BR>—1 A lion.<BR>—2 The citron tree,<BR>—3 Inflammation of the nose.<BR>—4 Red arsenic.<BR>—5 (In Music) A particular tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तम्
दीप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} Gold.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीप्तांशुः, दीप्ताक्षः, दीप्ताग्नि, दीप्ताङ्गः, दीप्तात्मन्, दीप्तास्य, दीप्तोपलः, दीप्तकिरणः, दीप्तकीर्तिः, दीप्तवर्णः, दीप्तशक्तिः, दीप्तजिह्वा, दीप्ततपस्, दीप्तनिर्णयः, दीप्तपिङ्गलः, दीप्तमूर्तिः, दीप्तरसः, दीप्तलोचनः, दीप्तलोहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0817-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तांशुः|दीप्तांशु
दीप्त + -अंशुः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताक्षः|दीप्ताक्ष
दीप्त + -अक्षः<BR>—1 a cat.<BR>—2 a peacock<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताग्नि|दीप्ताग्निः
दीप्त + -अग्नि <i>a.</i> kindled (as fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताग्निः|दीप्ताग्नि
दीप्त + -अग्नि + .({@-ग्निः@})<BR>—1 blazing fire.<BR>—2 N. of अगस्त्य. ━(<i>a.</i>) digesting well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताङ्गः|दीप्ताङ्ग|दीप्तांग
दीप्त + -अङ्गः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तात्मन्
दीप्त + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> having a fiery nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तास्य
दीप्त + -आस्य a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तोपलः|दीप्तोपल
दीप्त + -उपलः<BR>—1 the sun-stone.<BR>—2 a crystalline lens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तकिरणः|दीप्तकिरण
दीप्त + -किरणः the sun; दीप्तकिरणश्च दिवाकरोऽयम् Mk. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तकीर्तिः|दीप्तकीर्ति|दीप्तकीर्त्ति
दीप्त + -कीर्तिः, -वर्णः, -शक्तिः epithets of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तवर्णः|दीप्तवर्ण
दीप्त + -कीर्तिः, -वर्णः, -शक्तिः epithets of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तशक्तिः|दीप्तशक्ति
दीप्त + -कीर्तिः, -वर्णः, -शक्तिः epithets of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तजिह्वा
दीप्त + -जिह्वा a vixen; (used figuratively for an ill-tempered, quarrelsome woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ततपस्
दीप्त + -तपस् <i>a.</i> of glowing piety, fervent in devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तनिर्णयः
दीप्त + -निर्णयः definite, actual result; वाहुवीर्याश्रिते मार्गे वर्तसे<BR> दीप्तनिर्णये Mb. 3. 292. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तपिङ्गलः|दीप्तपिङ्गल
दीप्त + -पिङ्गलः a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तमूर्तिः|दीप्तमूर्ति|दीप्तमूर्त्ति
दीप्त + -मूर्तिः Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तरसः|दीप्तरस
दीप्त + -रसः an earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोचनः|दीप्तलोचन
दीप्त + -लोचनः a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोहम्
दीप्त + -लोहम् brass, bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तकः|दीप्तक|दीप्तकं
दीप्तकः A kind of disease of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तकम्
दीप्तकः + .{@-कम्@} Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिः|दीप्ति
दीप्तिः <i>f.</i> [दीप्-भावे-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Brightness, splendour, brilliance, lustre.<BR>—2 Brilliancy of beauty, extreme loveliness; (for the difference between<BR> दीप्ति and कान्ति see under कान्ति).<BR>—3 Lac.<BR>—4 Brass.<BR>—5 The flash-like flight of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिमत्|दीप्तिमन्त्
दीप्तिमत् <i>a.</i> Splendid, brilliant, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिमती
दीप्तिमत् + .{@-ती@} (in music) N. of a Śruti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्य|दीप्यः
दीप्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be kindled, inflammable.<BR>—2 Tonic, digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्यम्
दीप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} White cumin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्यकम्
दीप्यकम्<BR>—1 A peacockʼs crest.<BR>—2 A figure of speech (दीपक)<BR>—3 N. of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्र|दीप्रः
दीप्र <i>a.</i> Shining, brilliant, radiant, resplendent; दीप्रास्त्रस्फुरदुग्रदीधितिशिखानीराजितज्यं<BR> धनुः U. 6. 18 (v. l.); क्वचित्क्वचिच्चिताज्योतिदींप्रदीपप्रकाशितम् Ks. 25. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्रः|दीप्र
दीप्र + .{@-प्रः@} Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घ|दीर्घं|दीर्घः
दीर्घ <i>a.</i> (Compar. द्राधीयस्, Superl. द्राघिष्ठ)<BR>—1 Long (in time or space), reaching far; दीर्घाक्षं शरदिन्दुकान्ति वदनम्<BR> M. 2. 3; दीर्घान् कटाक्षान् Me. 37; दीर्घापाङ्ग &c.<BR>—2 Of long duration, lasting long, tedious; दीर्घयामा त्रियामा Me. 110;<BR> V. 3. 4; Ś. 4. 15.<BR>—3 Deep (as a sigh); Amaru. 13; दीर्घमुष्णं च निश्वस्य.<BR>—4 Long (as a vowel), as the आ in काम.<BR>—5 Lofty, high, tall.<BR>—6 Dilated, expanded; तृष्णादीर्घस्य चक्षुषः U. 3. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घः|दीर्घ|दीर्घं
दीर्घ + .{@-र्घः@}<BR>—1 A camel.<BR>—2 A long vowel.<BR>—3 The fifth, sixth, seventh, and eighth signs of the zodiac.<BR>—4 A kind of grass or reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घा
दीर्घ + .{@-र्घा@} A long lake or oblong tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घम्
दीर्घ + .{@-र्घम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Long, for a long time.<BR>—2 Deeply.<BR>—3 Far.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दीर्घाध्वगः, दीर्घापेक्षिन्, दीर्घाहन्, दीर्घाकार, दीर्घायु, दीर्घायुस्, दीर्घायुष्य, दीर्घायुधः, दीर्घास्यः, दीर्घकणा, दीर्घकण्ठः, दीर्घकण्ठकः, दीर्घकन्धरः, दीर्घकाय, दीर्घकाष्ठम्, दीर्घकेशः, दीर्घकोशा, दीर्घकोशी, दीर्घकोशिका, दीर्घगतिः, दीर्घग्रीवः, दीर्घघाटिकः, दीर्घवतुरस्रः, दीर्घच्छदः, दीर्घजङ्गलः, दीर्घजङ्घः, दीर्घजिह्वः, दीर्घतपस्, दीर्घतमस्, दीर्घतरुः, दीर्घद्रुः, दीर्घतुण्डी, दीर्घदण्डः, दीर्घदर्शन, दीर्घदर्शिन्, दीर्घदृष्टि, दीर्घद्वेषिन्, दीर्घनाद, दीर्घनिद्रा, दीर्घपक्षः, दीर्घपत्नः, दीर्घपत्रकः, दीर्घपर्वन्, दीर्घपवनः, दीर्घपादः, दीर्घपद्, दीर्घपाद्, दीर्घपादपः, दीर्घपुच्छः, दीर्घपुच्छिका, दीर्घपृष्ठः, दीर्घप्रज्ञ, दीर्घबाला, दीर्घबाहु,^1 दीर्घमारुतः, दीर्घमुखी, दीर्घमूलः, दीर्घयज्ञ, दीर्घरङ्गा, दीर्घरतः, दीर्घरदः, दीर्घरसनः, दीर्घरोमन्, दीर्घलोहितयष्टिका, दीर्घवक्त्रः, दीर्घवच्छिका, दीर्घसक्थ, दीर्घसत्रम्, दीर्घसुरतः, दीर्घसूत्र, दीर्घसूत्रिन्, दीर्घस्कन्धः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घाध्वगः|दीर्घाध्वग
दीर्घ + -अध्वगः<BR>—1 a messenger, an express.<BR>—2 a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0818-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घापेक्षिन्
