दुरक्ष|दुरक्षः
दुर् + -अक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 weak-eyed.<BR>—2 evil-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरक्षः|दुरक्ष
दुर् + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षः@})<BR>—1 a loaded or false die. —2 dishonest gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरक्षरम्
दुर् + -अक्षरम् an evil word; श्रुतिं ममाविश्य भवद्दुरक्षरं सृजत्यदः<BR> कीटकवदुत्कटा रुजः N. 9. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरतिक्रम|दुरतिक्रमः
दुर् + -अतिक्रम <i>a.</i> difficult to be overcome or conquered, unconquerable;<BR> सर्वं तु तपसा साध्यं तपो हि दुरतिक्रमम् Ms. 11. 2. 38; स्वभावो<BR> दुरतिक्रमः ‘nature cannot be changed’; स्वजातिर्दुरतिक्रमा Pt. 1.<BR>—2 insurmountable, impassable; B. R. 6. 18-19.<BR>—3 inevitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरतिक्रमः|दुरतिक्रम
दुर् + -अतिक्रम + .({@-मः@}) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरत्यय
दुर् + -अत्यय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be overcome; स्वर्गमार्गपरिघो दुरत्ययः R. 11. 88.<BR>—2 hard to be attained or fathomed; स एष आत्मा स्वपरेत्यबुद्धिभिर्दुरत्ययानुक्रमणो<BR> निरूप्यते Bhāg. 7. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरदृष्टम्
दुर् + -अदृष्टम् ill-luck, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिग
दुर् + -अधिग, -अधिगम <i>a.</i> —1 hard to reach or attain, unattainable;<BR> Bhāg. 3. 23. 8; दुरधिगमः परभागो यावत्पुरुषेण पौरुषं न कृतम् Pt. 1. 330.<BR>—2 insurmountable.<BR>—3 hard to be studied or understood; इह दुरधिगमैः किञ्चिदेवागमैः Ki. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिगम
दुर् + -अधिग, -अधिगम <i>a.</i> —1 hard to reach or attain, unattainable;<BR> Bhāg. 3. 23. 8; दुरधिगमः परभागो यावत्पुरुषेण पौरुषं न कृतम् Pt. 1. 330.<BR>—2 insurmountable.<BR>—3 hard to be studied or understood; इह दुरधिगमैः किञ्चिदेवागमैः Ki. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिष्ठित
दुर् + -अधिष्ठित <i>a.</i> badly performed, managed, or executed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिष्ठितम्
दुर् + -अधिष्ठित + .({@-तम्@}) improper stay at a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधीत
दुर् + -अधीत <i>a.</i> badly learnt or read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्यय
दुर् + -अध्यय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult of attainment; सहस्रवर्त्मा चपलैर्दुरध्ययः Śi. 12. 11.<BR>—2 hard to be studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्यवसायः|दुरध्यवसाय
दुर् + -अध्यवसायः a foolish undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्वः|दुरध्व
दुर् + -अध्वः a bad road; स्वयं दुरध्वार्णवनाविकाः कथं स्पृशन्तु<BR> विज्ञाय हृदापि तादृशीम् N. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्त|दुरंत
दुर् + -अन्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 whose end is difficult to be reached, endless, infinite; संकर्षणाय<BR> सूक्ष्माय दुरन्तायान्तकाय च Bhāg.<BR>—2 ending ill or in misery, unhappy; अहो दुरन्ता बलवद्विरोधिता Ki. 1. 23;<BR> नृत्यति युवतिजनेन समं सखि विरहिजनस्य दुरन्ते (वसन्ते)<BR> Gīt. 1; इयमुदरदरीदुरन्तधारा यदि न भवेदभिमानभङ्गभूमिः Udb.<BR>—3 hard to be understood or known.<BR>—4 insurmountable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्तक|दुरन्तकः
दुर् + -अन्तक <i>a.</i> = दुरन्त q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्तकः|दुरन्तक
दुर् + -अन्तक + .({@-कः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्वय|दुरन्वयः
दुर् + -अन्वय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be passed along; Mb. 14. 51. 17.<BR>—2 hard to be carried out or followed.<BR>—3 difficult to be attained. or understood; बुद्धिश्च ते महाप्राज्ञ देवैरपि<BR> दुरन्वया Rām. 3. 66. 18.<BR>—4 not suitable, improper; वचो दुरन्वयं विप्रास्तूष्णीमासन्भ्रमद्धियः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">Page0820-2</a>]<BR> Bhāg. 10. 84. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्वयः|दुरन्वय
दुर् + -अन्वय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 a wrong conclusion, one wrongly inferred from given premisses.<BR>—2 (in gram.) a false agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरपवादः|दुरपवाद
दुर् + -अपवादः ill report, slander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरभिग्रह|दुरभिग्रहः
दुर् + -अभिग्रह <i>a.</i> difficult to be caught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरभिमानिन्
दुर् + -अभिमानिन् <i>a.</i> vain-glorious, disagreeably proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवगम
दुर् + -अवगम <i>a.</i> incomprehensible; Bhāg. 5. 13. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवग्रह
दुर् + -अवग्रह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be restrained or subjugated; भक्ता भजस्व दुरवग्रह<BR> मा त्यजास्मान् Bhāg. 10. 29. 31.<BR>—2 disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवग्राह
दुर् + -अवग्राह <i>a.</i> difficult to be attained; Bhāg. 7. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवच्छद
दुर् + -अवच्छद <i>a.</i> difficult to be hidden; हेतुभिर्लक्षयांचक्रुराप्रीतां<BR> दुरवच्छदैः Bhāg. 10. 62. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवबोध
दुर् + -अवबोध <i>a.</i> unintelligible. Bhāg. 10. 49. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवसित
दुर् + -अवसित <i>a.</i> unfathomed, difficult to be ascertained; द्युपतिभिरजशक्रशंकराद्यैर्दुरवसितस्तवमच्युतं<BR> नतोऽस्मि Bhāg. 12. 12. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवस्थ
दुर् + -अवस्थ <i>a.</i> ill off, badly or poorly circumstanced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवस्था
दुर् + -अवस्था, -अवस्थानम् a wretched or miserable state; Bhāg. 5. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवस्थानम्
दुर् + -अवस्था, -अवस्थानम् a wretched or miserable state; Bhāg. 5. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवाप
दुर् + -अवाप <i>a.</i> difficult to be gained or fulfilled; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरवेक्षितम्
दुर् + -अवेक्षितम् an improper look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरह्नः|दुरह्न
दुर् + -अह्नः a bad day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराकृति
दुर् + -आकृति <i>a.</i> ugly, mis-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रन्द
दुर् + -आक्रन्द <i>a.</i> crying bitterly or miserably; किं क्रन्दसि दुराक्रन्द<BR> स्वपक्षक्षयकारक Pt. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रम
दुर् + -आक्रम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 invincible, unconquerable.<BR>—2 difficult to be passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्रमणम्
दुर् + -आक्रमणम्<BR>—1 unfair attack.<BR>—2 difficult approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरागमः|दुरागम
दुर् + -आगमः improper or illegal acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराग्रहः|दुराग्रह
दुर् + -आग्रहः foolish obstinacy, headstrongness, pertinacity; ममाहमित्यूढदुराग्रहाणां<BR> पुंसाम् Bhāg. 3. 5. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचर
दुर् + -आचर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 hard to be performed.<BR>—2 incurable (as a disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचार|दुराचारः
दुर् + -आचार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ill-conducted, badly behaved. —2 following bad practices, wicked, depraved;<BR> अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक् Bg. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचारः|दुराचार
दुर् + -आचार + .({@-रः@}) bad practice, ill-conduct, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्य
दुर् + -आढ्य <i>a.</i> not rich, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरात्मता
दुर् + -आत्मता vileness, baseness, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरात्मन्
दुर् + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> evil-natured, low, wicked, vile, base, mean; ये<BR> च प्राहुर्दुरात्मानो दुराराध्या महीभुजः Pt. 1. 39. ━(<i>m.</i>) a rascal,<BR> villain, scoundrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधर
दुर् + -आधर <i>a.</i> difficult to be withstood or overpowered, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधर्ष|दुराधर्षः
दुर् + -आधर्ष <i>a.</i> hard to be approached or assailed, unassailable<BR> जगन्नाथो दुराधर्षो गङ्गां भागीरथीं प्रति Mb.<BR>—2 not to be attacked with impunity.<BR>—3 haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधर्षः|दुराधर्ष
दुर् + -आधर्ष + .({@-र्षः@}) white mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधारः|दुराधार
दुर् + -आधारः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधिः|दुराधि
दुर् + -आधिः (<i>m.</i>) —1 distress or anxiety of mind; निरस्तनारीसमया दुराधयः Ki. 1. 28.<BR>—2 indignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधी
दुर् + -आधी <i>a.</i> Ved. malignant, thinking ill of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरानम
दुर् + -आनम <i>a.</i> difficult to bend or draw; स विचिन्त्य धनुर्दुरानमम् R. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराप
दुर् + -आप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be obtained; श्रिया दुरापः कथमीप्सितो भवेत् Ś. 3. 13;<BR> R. 1. 72, 6. 62.<BR>—2 difficult to be approached; Pt. 1. 67.<BR>—3 hard to be overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरापादन
दुर् + -आपादन <i>a.</i> difficult to be brought about; किं दुरापादनं<BR> तेषाम् Bhāg. 3. 23. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरापूर
दुर् + -आपूर <i>a.</i> difficult to be filled or satisfied; Bhāg. 7. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराबाध|दुराबाधः
दुर् + -आबाध <i>a.</i> hard to be molested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराबाधः|दुराबाध
दुर् + -आबाध + .({@-धः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरामोदः|दुरामोद
दुर् + -आमोदः bad scent, stench; शवधूमदुरामोदः शालिभक्तेऽत्र विद्यते Ks. 82. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराराध्य
दुर् + -आराध्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be propitiated, hard to be won over<BR> or conciliated; दुराराध्याः श्रियो राज्ञां दुरापा दुष्परिग्रहाः Pt. 1. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारुह|दुरारुहः
दुर् + -आरुह <i>a.</i> difficult to be mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारुहः|दुरारुह
दुर् + -आरुह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 the Bilva tree.<BR>—2 the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—3 the date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारोप
दुर् + -आरोप <i>a.</i> difficult to be strung (bow); दुरारोपमैन्दुशेखरं<BR> धनुर्दुर्निवारा रावणभुजदण्डाः B. R. 1. 46-47.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">Page0821-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0820-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारोह|दुरारोहः
दुर् + -आरोह <i>a.</i> difficult of ascent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारोहः|दुरारोह
दुर् + -आरोह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 The cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—2 the palm tree.<BR>—3 the date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालापः|दुरालाप
दुर् + -आलापः<BR>—1 a curse, imprecation.<BR>—2 foul or abusive language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालोक|दुरालोकः
दुर् + -आलोक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be seen or perceived.<BR>—2 painfully bright, dazzling; दुरालोकः स समरे निदाघाम्बररत्नवत् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालोकः|दुरालोक
दुर् + -आलोक + .({@-कः@}) dazzling splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरावर
दुर् + -आवर, -आवार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be covered or filled up; दुरावरं त्वदन्येन राज्यखण्डमिदं<BR> महत् Rām. 2. 105. 5.<BR>—2 difficult to be restrained, shut in, kept back or stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरावार
दुर् + -आवर, -आवार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be covered or filled up; दुरावरं त्वदन्येन राज्यखण्डमिदं<BR> महत् Rām. 2. 105. 5.<BR>—2 difficult to be restrained, shut in, kept back or stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरावर्त
दुर् + -आवर्त <i>a.</i> difficult to be convinced or set up; भवन्ति<BR> सुदुरावर्ता हेतुमन्तोऽपि पण्डिताः Mb. 12. 19. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराशय
दुर् + -आशय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 evil-minded, wicked, malicious, स्फुटनिर्भिन्नो दुराशयोऽधमः Śi.<BR> उपेयिवान् मूलमशेषमूलं दुराशयः कामदुघाङ्घ्निपस्य Bhāg. 3. 21. 15.<BR>—2 having a bad place of rest. ━(<i>m.</i>) the subtle body which is not<BR> destroyed by death (लिङ्गदेह); एतन्मे जन्म लोकेऽस्मिन्मुमुक्षूणां<BR> दुराशयात् Bhāg. 3. 24. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराशा
दुर् + -आशा<BR>—1 a bad or wicked desire.<BR>—2 hoping against hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरास
दुर् + -आस <i>a.</i> difficult to be abided or associated with; संघर्षिणा<BR> सह गुणाभ्यधिकैर्दुरासम् Śi. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरासद|दुरासदः
दुर् + -आसद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be approached or overtaken; स सभूव दुरासदः परैः<BR> R. 3. 66, 8. 4; Mv. 2. 5, 4. 15.<BR>—2 difficult to be found or met with.<BR>—3 unequalled, unparalleled.<BR>—4 hard to be borne, insupportable.<BR>—5 difficult to be conquered, unassailable, unconquerable; जहि शत्रुं<BR> महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम् Bg. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरासदः|दुरासद
दुर् + -आसद + .({@-दः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरित|दुरितं
दुर् + -इत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult.<BR>—2 sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरितम्
दुर् + -इत + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 a bad course, evil, sin; दरिद्राणां दैन्यं दुरितमथ दुर्वासनहृदां<BR> द्रुतं दूरीकुर्वन् G. L. 2; R. 8. 2; Amaru. 2; Mv. 3. 43.<BR>—2 a difficulty, danger.<BR>—3 a calamity, evil; अपत्ये यत्तादृग्दुरितमभवत् U. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरितिः|दुरिति
दुर् + -इतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 a bad course.<BR>—2 difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरिष्टम्
दुर् + -इष्टम्<BR>—1 a curse, imprecation.<BR>—2 a spell or sacrificial rite performed to injure another person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरीशः|दुरीश
दुर् + -ईशः a bad lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरीषणा
दुर् + -ईषणा, -एषणा<BR>—1 a curse, an imprecation.<BR>—2 an evil eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरेषणा
दुर् + -ईषणा, -एषणा<BR>—1 a curse, an imprecation.<BR>—2 an evil eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुक्त
दुर् + -उक्त <i>a.</i> harshly uttered; Pt. 1. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुक्तम्
दुर् + -उक्तम्, -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> offensive speech, reproach, abuse, censure;<BR> लक्ष्मि क्षमस्व वचनीयमिदं दुरुक्तम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुक्तिः|दुरुक्ति
दुर् + -उक्तम्, -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> offensive speech, reproach, abuse, censure;<BR> लक्ष्मि क्षमस्व वचनीयमिदं दुरुक्तम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुच्छेद
दुर् + -उच्छेद <i>a.</i> difficult to be destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुत्तर
दुर् + -उत्तर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 unanswerable.<BR>—2 difficult to be crossed; दुरुत्तरे पङ्क इवान्धकारे Bk. 11. 20;<BR> प्राप्तः पङ्को दुरुत्तरः Ki. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुदय
दुर् + -उदय <i>a.</i> appearing with difficulty, not easily manifested;<BR> यो ऽनात्मनां दुरुदयो भगवान्प्रतीतः Bhāg. 3. 16. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुदर्क
दुर् + -उदर्क <i>a.</i> having bad or no consequences; N. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुदाहर
दुर् + -उदाहर <i>a.</i> difficult to be pronounced or composed; अनुज्झितार्थसंबन्धः<BR> प्रबन्धो दुरुदाहरः Śi. 2. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुद्वह
दुर् + -उद्वह <i>a.</i> burdensome, unbearable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपसद
दुर् + -उपसद <i>a.</i> difficult of approach; Ki. 7. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपसर्पिन्
दुर् + -उपसर्पिन् <i>a.</i> approaching incautiously; एकमेव दहत्यग्निर्नरं<BR> दुरुपसर्पिणम् Ms. 7. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरूह|दुरूहः
दुर् + -ऊह <i>a.</i> abstruse; जानीते जयदेव एव शरणः श्लाघ्ये दुरूहद्रुते Gīt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरेव|दुरेवः
दुर् + -एव <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 having evil ways.<BR>—2 irresistible, unassailable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरेवः|दुरेव
दुर् + -एव + .({@-वः@}) a wicked person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरोषस्
दुर् + -ओषस् <i>a.</i> Ved. slow, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग|दुर्गं|दुर्गः
दुर् + -ग<BR>—1 difficult of access, inaccessible, impervious, impassable; दुर्गस्त्वेष<BR> महापन्थाः Mb. 12. 300. 50; दुर्गं पथस्तत्कवयो वदन्ति Kaṭh. 1. 3. 14.<BR>—2 unattainable.<BR>—3 incomprehensible.<BR>—4 following wicked path, vicious; Rām. 2. 39. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गः|दुर्ग|दुर्गं
दुर् + -ग + .({@-गः, -गम्@})<BR>—1 a difficult or narrow passage through a wood or over a stream,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">Page0821-2</a>]<BR> mountain &c., a defile, narrow pass.<BR>—2 a citadel, fortress, castle; न दुर्गं दुर्गमित्येव दुर्गमं मन्यते<BR> जनः । तस्य दुर्गमता सैव यत्प्रभुस्तस्य दुर्गमः ॥ Śiva B. 16. 61.<BR>—3 rough ground.<BR>—4 difficulty, adversity, calamity, distress, danger; निस्तारयति दुर्गाच्च<BR> Ms. 3. 98, 11. 43; मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि; Bg. 18. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गम्
दुर् + -ग + .({@-गः, -गम्@})<BR>—1 a difficult or narrow passage through a wood or over a stream,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">Page0821-2</a>]<BR> mountain &c., a defile, narrow pass.<BR>—2 a citadel, fortress, castle; न दुर्गं दुर्गमित्येव दुर्गमं मन्यते<BR> जनः । तस्य दुर्गमता सैव यत्प्रभुस्तस्य दुर्गमः ॥ Śiva B. 16. 61.<BR>—3 rough ground.<BR>—4 difficulty, adversity, calamity, distress, danger; निस्तारयति दुर्गाच्च<BR> Ms. 3. 98, 11. 43; मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि; Bg. 18. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गः|दुर्ग|दुर्गं
दुर् + -ग + .({@-गः@})<BR>—1 bdellium.<BR>—2 the Supreme Being.<BR>—3 N. of an <i>Asura</i> slain by Durgā (thus receiving her name from him).<BR> ˚अध्यक्षः, ˚पतिः, ˚पालः the commandant or governor of a castle.<BR> ˚अन्तः The suburb of a fort; दुर्गान्ते सिद्धतापसाः Kau. A. 1. 12.<BR> ˚कर्मन् <i>n.</i> fortification. ˚कारक <i>a.</i> making difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गकः
दुर् + -ग + .({@-कः@}) the birch tree. ˚ध्नी N. of Durgā. ˚तरणी an epithet<BR> of Sāvitrī. सावित्री दुर्गतरणी वीणा सप्तविधा तथा Mb. ˚मार्गः<BR> a defile, gorge. ˚लङ्घनम् surmounting difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्गलङ्घनः
दुर् + -ग + .({@-नः@}) a camel. ˚संचरः<BR>—1 a difficult passage as to a fort &c., a bridge &c. over a defile. ˚संस्कारः<BR> Repairs to the old forts; अतो दुर्गसंस्कार आरब्धव्ये किं कौमुदीमहोत्सवेन<BR> Mu. ˚सिंहः N. of the author of कलापपरिशिष्ट. ˚व्यसनम्<BR> a defect or weak point in a fortress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गा
दुर् + -ग + .({@-र्गा@}) an epithet of Pārvatī, wife of Śiva.<BR>—2 The female cuckoo<BR>—3 N. of several plants. ˚नवमी the 9th day of the bright half of<BR> कार्तिक. ˚पूजा the chief festival in honour of दुर्गा in Bengal<BR> in the month of Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गत|दुर्गतः
दुर् + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 unfortunate, in bad circumstances; समाश्वसिमि केनाहं कथं प्राणिमि<BR> दुर्गतः Bk. 18. 10.<BR>—2 indigent, poor.<BR>—3 distressed, in trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गतता
दुर् + -गतता ill-luck, poverty, misery; तावज्जन्मातिदुःखाय ततो<BR> दुर्गतता सदा Pt. 1. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गतिः|दुर्गति
दुर् + -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 misfortune, poverty, want, trouble, indigence; न हि कल्याणकृत्कश्चिद्<BR> दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति Bg. 6. 40.<BR>—2 a difficult situation or path.<BR>—3 hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्ध|दुर्गंध|दुर्गन्धं|दुर्गन्धः
दुर् + -गन्ध <i>a.</i> ill-smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धः|दुर्गन्ध|दुर्गंध|दुर्गन्धं
दुर् + -गन्ध + .({@-न्धः@})<BR>—1 bad odour, stink<BR>—2 any ill-smelling substance.<BR>—3 an onion.<BR>—4 the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धम्
दुर् + -गन्ध + .({@-न्धम्@}) sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धि|दुर्गंधि
दुर् + -गन्धि, -गन्धिन् <i>a.</i> ill-smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धिन्|दुर्गंधिन्
दुर् + -गन्धि, -गन्धिन् <i>a.</i> ill-smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गम|दुर्गमः
दुर् + -गम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 impassable, inaccessible, impervious; कामिनीकायकान्तारे कुचपर्वतदुर्गमे<BR> Bh. 1. 86; Śi. 12. 49.<BR>—2 unattainable, difficult of attainment.<BR>—3 hard to be understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गमम्
दुर् + -गम + .({@-मम्@}) a difficult place like hill etc; भ्राम्यन्ते दुर्गमेष्वपि Pt. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाढ
दुर् + -गाढ, -गाध, -गाह्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be fathomed or investigated, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाध
दुर् + -गम + .({@-मम्@}) a difficult place like hill etc; भ्राम्यन्ते दुर्गमेष्वपि Pt. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाह्य
दुर् + -गम + .({@-मम्@}) a difficult place like hill etc; भ्राम्यन्ते दुर्गमेष्वपि Pt. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गुणितम्
दुर् + -गुणितम् not properly studied; चिराभ्यस्तपथं याति शास्त्रं<BR> दुर्गुणितं यथा Avimārakam 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गोष्ठी
दुर् + -गोष्ठी evil association; conspiracy. वृद्धो रक्कः कम्पनेशो<BR> दुर्गोष्ठीमध्यगोऽभवत् Rāj. T. 6. 170.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग्रह|दुर्ग्रहः
दुर् + -ग्रह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be gained or accomplished.<BR>—2 difficult to be conquered or subjugated; दुर्गाणि दुर्ग्रहाण्यासन् तस्य<BR> रोद्धुरपि द्विषाम् R. 17. 52.<BR>—3 hard to be understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग्रहः|दुर्ग्रह
दुर् + -ग्रह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 a cramp, spasm.<BR>—2 obstinacy.<BR>—3 whim, monomania; कथं न वा दुर्ग्रहदोष एष ते हितेन सम्यग्गुरुणापि<BR> शम्यते N. 9. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घट
दुर् + -घट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult. कार्याणि घटयन्नासीद् दुर्घटान्यपि हेलया Rāj. T. 4. 364.<BR>—2 impossible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घण
दुर् + -घण <i>a.</i> —1 closely packed together, very compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घुरुटः
दुर् + -घुरुटः An unbeliever; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घोषः|दुर्घोष
दुर् + -घोषः<BR>—1 a harsh cry.<BR>—2 a bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जन|दुर्जनः
दुर् + -जन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 wicked, bad, vile.<BR>—2 slanderous, malicious, mischievous; यथा स्त्रीणां तथा वाचां साधुत्वे<BR> दुर्जनो जनः U. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जनः|दुर्जन
दुर् + -जन + .({@-नः@}) a bad or wicked person, a malicious or mischievous man,<BR> villain; दुर्जनः प्रियवादी च नैतद्विश्वास-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">Page0822-1</a>]<BR> -कारणम् Cāṇ. 24, 25; शाम्येत्प्रत्यपकारेण नोपकारेण दुर्जनः<BR> Ku. 2. 40. (दुर्जनायते Den. Ā. to become wicked; स्वजनोऽपि दरिद्राणां<BR> तत्क्षणाद् दुर्जनायते Pt. 1. 5.). (दुर्जनीकृ [चिव] to make blameworthy;<BR> दुर्जनीकृतास्मि अनेन मां चित्रगतां दर्शयता Nāg. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0821-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जय|दुर्जयः|दुर्ज्जय
दुर् + -जय <i>a.</i> invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जयः|दुर्जय|दुर्ज्जय
दुर् + -जय + .({@-यः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जर|दुर्ज्जर
दुर् + -जर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ever youthful; तस्मिन्स्तनं दुर्जरवीर्यमुल्वणं घोराङ्कमादाय शिशोर्दधावथ<BR> Bhāg. 10. 6. 10.<BR>—2 hard (as food), indigestible.<BR>—3 difficult to be enjoyed; राजश्रीर्दुर्जरा तस्य नवत्वे भूभुजोऽभवत्<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जात|दुर्जातं|दुर्ज्जात
दुर् + -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 unhappy, wretched.<BR>—2 bad-tempered, bad, wicked; Rāj. T. 3. 142.<BR>—3 false, not genuine. ˚जायिन् <i>a.</i> one who is born in vain; यो<BR> न यातयते वैरमल्पसत्त्वोद्यमः पुमान् । अफलं जन्म तस्याहं मन्ये<BR> दुर्जातजायिनः ॥ Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जातम्
दुर् + -जात + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 a misfortune, calamity, difficulty; त्वं तावद् दुर्जाते मेऽत्यन्तसाहाय्यकारिणी<BR> भव M. 3; दुर्जातबन्धुः R. 13. 72 ‘a friend in need or adversity’.<BR>—2 impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जाति|दुर्जातिः|दुर्ज्जाति
दुर् + -जाति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bad natured, vile, wicked; रुदितशरणा दुर्जातीनां सहस्व रुषां<BR> फलम् Amaru. 96.<BR>—2 outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जातिः|दुर्जाति|दुर्ज्जाति
दुर् + -जाति + .({@-तिः@} <i>f.</i>) misfortune, ill condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्ञान
दुर् + -ज्ञान, -ज्ञेय <i>a.</i> difficult to be known, incomprehensible.<BR> उच्चावचेषु भुतेषु दुर्ज्ञेयामकृतात्मभिः Ms. 6. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्ञेयः|दुर्ज्ञेय
दुर् + -ज्ञान, -ज्ञेय + .({@-यः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्ञेय|दुर्ज्ञेयः
दुर् + -ज्ञान, -ज्ञेय <i>a.</i> difficult to be known, incomprehensible.<BR> उच्चावचेषु भुतेषु दुर्ज्ञेयामकृतात्मभिः Ms. 6. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णयः|दुर्णय
दुर् + -णयः, -नयः, -नीतिः<BR>—1 bad conduct.<BR>—2 impropriety<BR>—3 injustice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नयः|दुर्नय
दुर् + -णयः, -नयः, -नीतिः<BR>—1 bad conduct.<BR>—2 impropriety<BR>—3 injustice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नीतिः|दुर्नीति
दुर् + -णयः, -नयः, -नीतिः<BR>—1 bad conduct.<BR>—2 impropriety<BR>—3 injustice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णामन्
दुर् + -णामन्, -नामन् <i>a.</i> having a bad name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुर् + -णामन्, -नामन् <i>a.</i> having a bad name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीत
दुर् + -णीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ill-behaved.<BR>—2 impolitic.<BR>—3 forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीतम्
दुर् + -णीत + .({@-तम्@}) misconduct; दुर्णीतं किमिहास्ति किं सुचरितं कः स्थानलाभे गुणः H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दम
दुर् + -दम, -दमन, -दम्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be subdued, untamable, indomitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दमन
दुर् + -दम, -दमन, -दम्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be subdued, untamable, indomitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दम्य
दुर् + -दम, -दमन, -दम्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be subdued, untamable, indomitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर्श|दुर्द्दर्श
दुर् + -दर्श <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be seen.<BR>—2 dazzling; सुदुर्दर्शमिदं रूपं दृष्टवानसि यन्मन Bg. 11. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर्शन
दुर् + -दर्शन <i>a.</i> ugly, ill-looking; दुर्दर्शनेन घटतामियमप्यनेन Māl. 2. 8<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दशा
दुर् + -दशा a misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्दान्तः|दुर्द्दान्त
दुर् + -दान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 hard to be tamed or subdued, untamable; Śi. 12. 22.<BR>—2 intractable, proud, insolent; दुर्दान्तानां दमनविधयः क्षत्रियेष्वायतन्ते Mv. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दान्तः|दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्द्दान्त
दुर् + -दान्त + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 a calf.<BR>—2 a strife, quarrel.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिन|दुर्द्दिनं
दुर् + -दिन <i>a.</i> cloudy, rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिनम्
दुर् + -दिन + .({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 a bad day in general; तद्दिनं दुर्दिनं मन्ये यत्र मित्रागमो हि न Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 a rainy or cloudy day, stormy or rainy weather; उन्नमत्यकालदुर्दिनम्<BR> Mk. 5; Ku. 6. 43; Mv. 4. 57.<BR>—3 a shower (of anything); द्विषां विषह्य काकुत्स्थस्तत्र नाराचदुर्दिनम्<BR> ॥ सन्मङ्गलस्नात इव R. 4. 41, 82, 5. 47; U. 5. 5.<BR>—4 thick darkness; जीमूतैश्च दिशः सर्वाश्चक्रे तिमिरदुर्दिनाः Mb.<BR> (दुर्दिनायते Den. Ā. to become cloudy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिवसः|दुर्दिवस
दुर् + -दिवसः a dark or rainy day; Pt. 1. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुरूटः|दुर्दुरूट
दुर् + -दुरूटः, -दुरूढः<BR>—1 an unbeliever 2 an abusive word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुरूढः
दुर् + -दुरूटः, -दुरूढः<BR>—1 an unbeliever 2 an abusive word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दृश
दुर् + -दृश <i>a.</i> —1 disagreeable to the sight, disgusting; दुर्दृशं<BR> तत्र राक्षसं घोररूपमपश्यत्सः Mb. 1. 2. 298.<BR>—2 difficult to be seen; पादचारमिवादित्यं निष्पतन्तं सुदुर्दृशम्<BR> Rām. 7. 33. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दृष्ट
दुर् + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i> ill-judged or seen, wrongly decided; Y. 2. 305.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दैवम्
दुर् + -दैवम् ill-luck, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्यूतम्
दुर् + -द्यूतम् an unfair game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रुमः|दुर्द्रुम
दुर् + -द्रुमः onion (green).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः|दुर्धरः
दुर् + -धर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 irresistible, difficult to be stopped.<BR>—2 difficult to be borne or suffered; दुर्धरेण मदनेन साद्यते Ghaṭ. 11; Ms. 7. 28.<BR>—3 difficult to be accomplished.<BR>—4 difficult to be kept in memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धरः|दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः
दुर् + -धर + .({@-रः@}) quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर्ष
दुर् + -धर्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inviolable, unassailable.<BR>—2 inaccessible; संयोजयति विद्यैव नीचगापि नरं सरित् । समुद्रमिव<BR> दुर्धर्षं नृपं भाग्यमतः परम् ॥ H. Pr. 5.<BR>—3 fearful, dreadful.<BR>—4 haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धी
दुर् + -धी <i>a.</i> stupid, silly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नयः|दुर्नय
दुर् + -नयः<BR>—1 arrogance.<BR>—2 immorality.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">Page0822-2</a>]<BR>—3 evil strategy; उन्मूलयितुमीशोऽहं त्रिवर्गमिव दुर्नयः Mu. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामकः|दुर्नामक|दुर्नामकं
दुर् + -नामकः piles. ˚अरिः a kind of bulbous root (Mar. सुरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुर् + -नामन् <i>m. f.</i> a cockle. ━(<i>n.</i>) piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निग्रह
दुर् + -निग्रह <i>a.</i> irrepressible, unruly; मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलम् Bg. 6. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निमित
दुर् + -निमित <i>a.</i> carelessly put or placed on the ground; पदे<BR> पदे दुर्निमिते गलन्ती R. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निमित्तम्
दुर् + -निमित्तम् —1 a bad omen; R. 14. 50.<BR>—2 a bad pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निवार
दुर् + -निवार, -निवार्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be checked or warded off,<BR> irresistible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निवार्य
दुर् + -निवार, -निवार्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be checked or warded off,<BR> irresistible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नीतम्
दुर् + -नीतम् —1 misconduct, bad policy, demerit, misbehaviour; दुर्णीतं<BR> किमिहास्ति Pt. 2. 21; H. 1. 49.<BR>—2 ill-luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नीतिः|दुर्नीति
दुर् + -नीतिः <i>f.</i> maladministration; दुर्नींतिं तव वीक्ष्य कोपदहनज्वालाजटालोऽपि<BR> सन्; Bv. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नृपः|दुर्नृप
दुर् + -नृपः a bad king; आसीत् पितृकुलं तस्य भक्ष्यं दुर्नृपरक्षसः<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्न्यस्त
दुर् + -न्यस्त <i>a.</i> badly arranged; दुर्न्यस्तपुष्परचितोऽपि Māl. 9. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बल|दुर्ब्बल|दुर्ब्बलः
दुर् + -बल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 weak, feeble.<BR>—2 enfeebled, spiritless; दुर्बलान्यङ्गकानि U. 1. 24.<BR>—3 thin, lean, emaciated; U. 3.<BR>—4 small, scanty, little; स्वार्थोपपत्तिं प्रति दुर्बलाशः R. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बाध
दुर् + -बाध <i>a.</i> Unrestrained (अनीवार); दुर्बाधो जनिदिवमान्मम<BR> प्रवृद्धः (आधिः); Mv. 6. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बाल
दुर् + -बाल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bald-headed.<BR>—2 void of prepuce.<BR>—3 having crooked hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुद्धि
दुर् + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 silly, foolish, stupid. —2 perverse, evil-minded, wicked; धार्तराष्ट्रस्य<BR> दुर्बुद्धेर्युद्धे प्रियचिकीर्षवः (समागताः) Bg. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुध
दुर् + -बुध <i>a.</i> wicked-minded, silly; Mb. 11. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बोध
दुर् + -बोध <i>a.</i> unintelligible, unfathomable, inscrutable; निसर्गदुर्बोधमबोधविक्लवाः<BR> क्व भूपतीनां चरितं क्व जन्तवः Ki. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भग
दुर् + -भग <i>a.</i> —1 unfortunate, unlucky; श्रीवल्लभं दुर्भगाः (निन्दन्ति) Pt. 1. 415.<BR>—2 not possessed of good features, ill-looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भगा
दुर् + -भगा<BR>—1 a wife disliked by her husband; दुर्भगाभरणप्रायो ज्ञानं भारः क्रियां<BR> विना H. 1. 17.<BR>—2 an ill-tempered woman, a shrew.<BR>—3 a widow;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भर
दुर् + -भर <i>a.</i> insupportable, burdensome, heavily laden with (comp.);<BR> ततो राजाब्रवीदेतं बहुव्यसनदुर्भरः Ks. 112. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भाग्य
दुर् + -भाग्य <i>a.</i> unfortunate, unlucky. ({@ग्यम्@}) ill-luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भावना
दुर् + -भावना<BR>—1 an evil thought. —2 a bad tendency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0822-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भिक्षम्
