दुर्मल्ली
दुर् + -मल्लिका, -मल्ली a minor drama, comedy, farce; S. D. 553.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मित्रः|दुर्मित्र
दुर् + -मित्रः<BR>—1 a bad friend. —2 an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मुख|दुर्मुखः|दुर्म्मुख|दुर्म्मुखः
दुर् + -मुख <i>a.</i> —1 having a bad face, hideous, ugly; Bh. 1. 90.<BR>—2 foul-mouthed, abusive, scurrilous; Bh. 2. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मुखः|दुर्मुख|दुर्म्मुख|दुर्म्मुखः
दुर् + -मुख + .({@-खः@})<BR>—1 a horse.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 N. of a serpent king (Nm.)<BR>—4 N. of a monkey (Nm.)<BR>—5 N. of a year (29th year out of 60 years cycle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मूल्य|दुर्म्मूल्य|दुर्म्मूल्यं
दुर् + -मूल्य <i>a.</i> highly priced, dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मेधस्|दुर्म्मेधस्
दुर् + -मेधस् <i>a.</i> silly, foolish, dull-headed, dull; Pt. 1. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR> a dunce, dull-headed man, blockhead; ग्रन्थानधीत्य व्याकर्तुमिति दुर्मेधसोऽप्यलम् Śi. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मैत्र
दुर् + -मैत्र <i>a.</i> unfriendly, hostile; Bhāg. 7. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्यशस्
दुर् + -यशस् <i>n.</i> ill-repute, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योगः|दुर्योग
दुर् + -योगः<BR>—1 bad or clumsy contrivance.<BR>—2 a bad combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योध
दुर् + -योध, -योधन <i>a.</i> invincible, unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योधनः|दुर्योधन|दुर्य्योधन|दुर्य्योधनः
दुर् + -योध, -योधन + .({@-नः@}) the eldest of the 101 sons of Dhṛtarāṣṭra and Gāndhārī.<BR> [From his early years he conceived a deep hatred for his cousins the Pāṇḍavas,<BR> but particularly Bhīma, and made every effort he could to compass their<BR> destruction. When his father proposed to make Yudhiṣṭhira heir-apparent,<BR> Duryodhana did not like the idea, as his father was the reigning sovereign,<BR> and prevailed upon his blind father to send the Pāṇḍavas away into<BR> exile. Vāraṇāvata was fixed upon as their abode, and under pretext of<BR> constructing a palatial building for their residence, Duryodhana caused<BR> a palace to be built mostly of lac, resin and other combustible materials,<BR> thereby hoping to see them all destroyed when they should enter it. But<BR> the Pāṇḍavas were forewarned and they safely escaped. They then lived<BR> at Indraprastha, and Yudhiṣṭhira performed the Rājasūya sacrifice<BR> with great pomp and splendour. This event further excited the anger and<BR> jealousy of Duryodhana, who was already vexed to find that his plot for<BR> burning them up had signally failed, and he induced his father to invite<BR> the Pāṇḍavas to Hastināpura to play with dice (of which Yudhiṣṭhira<BR> was particularly fond). In that gambling-match, Duryodhana, who was ably<BR> assisted by his maternal uncle Śakuni, won from Yudhiṣṭhira everything<BR> that he staked, till the infatuated gambler staked himself, his brothers,<BR> and Draupadī herself, all of whom shared the same fate. Yudhiṣṭhira,<BR> as a condition of the wager, was forced to go to the forest with his wife<BR> and brothers, and to remain there for twelve years and to pass one additional<BR> year <i>incognito</i>. But even this period, long as it was, expired, and<BR> after their return from exile both the Pāṇḍavas and Kauravas made great<BR> preparations for the inevitable struggle and the great Bhāratī war commenced.<BR> It lasted for eighteen days during which all the Kauravas, with most of<BR> their allies, were slain. It was on the last day of the war that<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">Page0823-2</a>]<BR> Bhīma fought a duel with Duryodhana and smashed his thigh with his club.]<BR> मोघं तवेदं भुवि नामधेयं दुर्योधनेतीह कृतं पुरस्तात् न हीह दुर्योधनता<BR> तवास्ति पलायमानस्य रणं विहाय Mb. 4. 65. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योधन|दुर्योधनः|दुर्य्योधन|दुर्य्योधनः
दुर् + -योध, -योधन <i>a.</i> invincible, unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योनि
दुर् + -योनि <i>a.</i> of a low birth, न कथंचन दुर्योनिः प्रकृतिं<BR> स्वां नियच्छति Ms. 10. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लक्ष्य
दुर् + -लक्ष्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be seen or perceived, hardly visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्ष्यम्
दुर् + -क्ष्यम् bad aim; मनः प्रकृत्यैव चलं दुर्लक्ष्यं च तथापि<BR> मे Ratn. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लभ|दुर्लभः|दुर्ल्लभ
दुर् + -लभ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be attained, or accomplished; R. 1. 67, 17. 70; Ku. 4. 40, 5. 46, 61;<BR> दुर्लभं भारते जन्म मानुष्यं तत्र दुर्लभम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 difficult to be found or met with, scarce, rare; शुद्धान्तदुर्लभम् Ś. 1. 17.<BR>—3 best, excellent, eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग्रामः
दुर् + -ग्रामः a village situated close to a large village and inhabited<BR> by the free-holders (अग्रहारोपजीविनः); Māna. 10. 79-80.<BR>—4 dear, beloved.<BR>—5 costly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ललित
दुर् + -ललित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 spoilt by fondling, fondled too much, hard to please; हा मदङ्कदुर्ललित<BR> Ve. 4; V. 2. 8; Māl. 9.<BR>—2 (hence) wayward, naughty, ill-bred, unruly; स्पृहयामि खलु दुर्ललितायास्मै Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ललितम्
दुर् + -ललित + .({@-तम्@}) waywardness, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्लेख्यम्
दुर् + -लेख्यम् a forged document. Y. 2. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वच|दुर्व्वच|दुर्व्वचं|दुर्व्वचः
दुर् + -वच <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be described, indescribable. अपि वागधिपस्य दुर्वचं<BR> वचनं तद् विदधीत विस्मयम् Ki. 2. 2.<BR>—2 not to be talked about.<BR>—3 speaking improperly, abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वचम्
दुर् + -वच + .({@-चम्@}) abuse, censure, foul language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वचस्|दुर्व्वचस्
दुर् + -वचस् <i>n.</i> abuse, censure; असह्यं दुर्वचो ज्ञातेर्मेघान्तरितरौद्रवत् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्ण|दुर्वर्णः|दुर्व्वर्ण|दुर्व्वर्णं
दुर् + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> bad-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्णः|दुर्वर्ण|दुर्व्वर्ण|दुर्व्वर्णं
दुर् + -वर्णः<BR>—1 bad colour.<BR>—2 impurity; यथा हेम्नि स्थितो वह्निर्दुवणं हन्ति धातुजम् Bhāg. 12. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वर्णम्
दुर् + -वर्णः + .({@-र्णम्@})<BR>—1 silver. दुर्वर्णभित्तिरिह सान्द्रसुधासुवर्णा Śi. 4. 28.<BR>—2 a kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वस
दुर् + -वस <i>a.</i> difficult to be resided in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वसतिः|दुर्वसति
दुर् + -वसतिः <i>f.</i> painful residence; R. 8. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वह|दुर्व्वह
दुर् + -वह <i>a.</i> heavy, difficult to be borne; दुर्वहगर्भखिन्नसीता<BR> U. 2. 10; Ku. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्|दुर्व्वाच्
दुर् + -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking ill. ━(<i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 evil words, abuse.<BR>—2 inelegant language or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्य|दुर्व्वाच्य
दुर् + -वाच्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be spoken or uttered.<BR>—2 abusive, scurrilous.<BR>—3 harsh, cruel (as words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाच्यम्
दुर् + -वाच्य + .({@-च्यम्@})<BR>—1 censure, abuse. —2 scandal, ill-repute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वातः|दुर्वात
दुर् + -वातः a fart. ˚वातय Den. P. to break wind or fart; इत्येके<BR> विहसन्त्येनमेके दुर्वातयन्ति च Bhāg. 11. 23. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वादः|दुर्वाद|दुर्व्वाद|दुर्व्वादः
दुर् + -वादः slander, defamation, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वार|दुर्व्वार
दुर् + -वार, -वारण <i>a.</i> irresistible, unbearable; R. 14. 87; किं<BR> चायमरिदुर्वारः पाणौ पाशः प्रचेतसः Ku. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वारण
दुर् + -वार, -वारण <i>a.</i> irresistible, unbearable; R. 14. 87; किं<BR> चायमरिदुर्वारः पाणौ पाशः प्रचेतसः Ku. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वासना
दुर् + -वासना —1 evil propensity, wicked desire; कः शत्रुर्वद खेददानकुशलो<BR> दुर्वासनासंचयः Bv. 1. 86.<BR>—2 a chimera.//<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वासस्|दुर्व्वासस्
दुर् + -वासस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ill-dressed.<BR>—2 naked. ━(<i>m.</i>) N. of a very irascible saint or Ṛṣi, son of Atri<BR> and Anasūyā. (He was very hard to please, and he cursed many a male<BR> and female to suffer misery and degradation. His anger, like that of Jamadagni,<BR> has become almost proverbial.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वाहितम्
दुर् + -वाहितम् a heavy burden; उरोजपूर्णकुम्भाङ्का सदुर्वाहितविभ्रमा<BR> Rāj. T. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विगाह
दुर् + -विगाह, -विगाह्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be penetrated or fathomed, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विगाह्य
दुर् + -विगाह, -विगाह्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be penetrated or fathomed, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विचिन्त्य|दुर्विचिंत्य
दुर् + -विचिन्त्य inconceivable, inscrutable<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विद
दुर् + -विद <i>a.</i> difficult to be known or discovered; नूनं गतिः<BR> कृतान्तस्य प्राज्ञैरपि सुदुर्विदा Mb. 7. 78. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विदग्ध
दुर् + -विदग्ध<BR>—1 unskilled, raw, foolish, stupid, silly.<BR>—2 wholly ignorant.<BR>—3 foolishly puffed up, elated,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">Page0824-1</a>]<BR> vainly proud; वृथाशस्त्रग्रहणदुर्विदग्ध Ve. 3; ज्ञानलवदुर्विदग्धं<BR> ब्रह्मापि नरं न रञ्जयति Bh. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0823-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विद्ध
दुर् + -विद्ध <i>a.</i> Badly perforated (a pearl); Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विद्य
दुर् + -विद्य <i>a.</i> uneducated; Rāj. T. 1. 354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विध|दुर्व्विध|दुर्व्विधः
दुर् + -विध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 mean, base, low.<BR>—2 wicked, vile.<BR>—3 poor, indigent; विदधाते रुचिगर्वदुर्विधम् N. 2. 23. 4 stupid,<BR> foolish, silly; विविनक्ति न बुद्धिदुर्विधः Śi. 16. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

