दुर्व् €1 P. (दु-दूर्वति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुल्
दुल् €10 U. (दोलयति-ते, दोलित)<BR>—1 To swing, shake to and fro, cause to oscillate or move about; कटिं<BR> चेद्दोलयेदाशु Ratimañjarī; दोलयन्द्वाविवाक्षौ Bh. 3. 39.<BR>—2 To move or shake upwards, throw up; दोलयति धूलिं वायुः Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुलिः|दुलि
दुलिः <i>f.</i> A small or female tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुवस्
दुवस् <i>a.</i> Active. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 Wealth.<BR>—2 An offering.<BR>—3 Worship, honour; ऐभिरग्ने दुवो गिरो विश्वोभिः सोमपीतये Rv. 1. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुवस्यति
दुवस्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To honour, worship.<BR>—2 To reward; दुवस्यत दम्यं जातवेदसम् Rv. 3. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुवसन
दुवसन <i>a.</i> Adorable, to be worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुवस्वन्
दुवस्वन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Worshipping.<BR>—2 Enjoying worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुवोयु
दुवोयु <i>a.</i> Honouring, worshipping; स तु श्रुधि श्रुत्या यो दुवोयुः Rv. 6. 36. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्
दुष् €4 P. (दुष्यति, दुष्ट)<BR>—1 To be bad or corrupted, be spoiled or suffer damage.<BR>—2 To be defiled or violated (as a woman &c.), be stained, be or become<BR> impure or contaminated; स्वल्पेनाप्यपकारेण ब्राह्मण्यमिव दुष्यति<BR> Pt. 1. 66; Ms. 7. 24, 9. 318, 10. 102.<BR>—3 To sin, commit a mistake, be wrong.<BR>—4 To be unchaste or faithless. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दूषयति-ते, but दूषयति-ते<BR> or दोषयति-ते in the sense of ‘making depraved’ or ‘corrupting’)<BR>—1 To corrupt, spoil, cause to perish, hurt, destroy, defile, taint, contaminate,<BR> vitiate, pollute (lit. and fig.); न भीतो मरणादस्मि केवलं दूषितं<BR> यशः Mk. 10. 27; पूरा दूषयति स्थलीम् R. 12. 30, 8. 68, 10. 47, 12. 4;<BR> Ms. 5. 1, 104, 7. 195; Y. 1. 189; Amaru. 72; न त्वेवं दूषयिष्यामि<BR> शस्त्रग्रहमहाव्रतम् Mv. 3. 8 ‘shall not sully, violate or break &c.’<BR>—2 To corrupt the morals, demoralize.<BR>—3 To violate or dishonour (as a girl or anotherʼs wife); योऽकामां दूषयेत्कन्यां<BR> स सद्यो वधमर्हति Ms. 8. 364, 368.<BR>—4 To abrogate, rescind, annul.<BR>—5 To blame, censure, find fault with, speak ill of, accuse; दूषितः<BR> सर्वलोकेषु निषादत्वं गमिष्यति Rām.; Y. 1. 66.<BR>—6 To adulterate.<BR>—7 To falsify.<BR>—8 To refute, disprove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ट|दुष्टं|दुष्टः
दुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [दुष्-क्त]<BR>—1 Spoiled, damaged, injured, ruined.<BR>—2 Defiled, tainted, violated, sullied.<BR>—3 Depraved, corrupted.<BR>—4 Vicious, wicked; as दुष्टवृषः; वरं शून्या शाला न च खलु वरो<BR> दुष्टवृषभः H. 1. 117.<BR>—5 Guilty, culpable.<BR>—6 Low, vile.<BR>—7 Faulty or defective, as a हेतु in logic.<BR>—8 Painful.<BR>—9 Worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टा
दुष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@}<BR>—1 A bad or unchaste woman.<BR>—2 A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टम्
दुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Sin, crime, guilt.<BR>—2 A kind of leprosy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दुष्टात्मन्, दुष्टाशय, दुष्टगजः, दुष्टचारिन्, दुष्टचेतस्, दुष्टधी, दुष्टबुद्धि, दुष्टलाङ्गलम्, दुष्टवृषः, दुष्टव्रणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टात्मन्
दुष्ट + -आत्मन्, -आशय <i>a.</i> evil-minded, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टाशय
दुष्ट + -आत्मन्, -आशय <i>a.</i> evil-minded, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टगजः|दुष्टगज
दुष्ट + -गजः a vicious elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचारिन्
दुष्ट + -चारिन् <i>a.</i> wicked, sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचेतस्
दुष्ट + -चेतस्, -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> evil-minded, malevolent, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टधी
दुष्ट + -चेतस्, -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> evil-minded, malevolent, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टबुद्धि
दुष्ट + -चेतस्, -धी, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> evil-minded, malevolent, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टलाङ्गलम्
दुष्ट + -लाङ्गलम् N. of a particular form of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टवृषः|दुष्टवृष
दुष्ट + -वृषः a strong but stubborn ox which refuses to draw, a vicious ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टव्रणः|दुष्टव्रण
दुष्ट + -व्रणः<BR>—1 a dull boil or sore.<BR>—2 a sinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टिः|दुष्टि
दुष्टिः <i>f.</i> Corruption, depravity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष
दूष <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Defiling, polluting; <i>e. g.</i><BR> पङ्क्तिदूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0824-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषक|दूषकः
दूषक <i>a.</i> (-षिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दुष्-णिच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Corrupting, polluting, vitiating, defiling, spoiling; कौ युवां मुनिदूषकौ<BR> Rām. 3. 2. 12.<BR>—2 Violating, dishonouring, seducing; राज्ञः शासनदूषकैः Mk. 9. 41.<BR>—3 Offending, trespassing, guilty.<BR>—4 Disfiguring.<BR>—5 Sinful, wicked (as an action).<BR>—6 Irreligious; यः पुरुषाणां हि दूषकः Rām. 4. 38. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषकः|दूषक
दूषक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A seducer, a corrupter.<BR>—2 Any infamous or wicked person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषण|दूषणः
दूषण <i>a.</i> [दुष्-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Corrupting, spoiling, destroying, &c.; आपदेत्युभयलोकदूषणी Ki. 13. 64;<BR> see दुष्.<BR>—2 Dishonouring, violating.<BR>—3 Offending against.<BR>—4 Opposing, counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणम्
दूषण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Spoiling, corrupting, vitiating, ruining, polluting &c.<BR>—2 Violating, breaking (as an agreement).<BR>—3 Seducing, violating, dishonouring (as a woman).<BR>—4 Abuse, censure, blame; न चक्षमे शुभाचारः स दूषणामिवात्मनः R. 12. 46.<BR>—5 Detraction, disparagement.<BR>—6 Adverse argument or criticism, objection.<BR>—7 Refutation.<BR>—8 A fault, offence, defect, sin, crime; नोलूकोऽप्यवलोकते यदि दिवा<BR> सूर्यस्य किं दूषणम् Bh. 2. 93; हाहा धिक् परगृहवासदूषणम् U. 1. 40;<BR> Ms. 2. 213; H. 1. 94, 115, 2. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणः|दूषण
दूषण + .{@-णः@} N. of a demon, one of the generals of Rāvaṇa, slain by<BR> Rāma; R. 12. 46.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दूषणारिः, दूषणावह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणारिः|दूषणारि
दूषण + -अरिः an epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणावह
दूषण + -आवह <i>a.</i> involving (one) in blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणीय
दूषणीय <i>a.</i> Liable to be blamed, corrupted, vitiated &c.; see दूष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषयितृ
दूषयितृ <i>m.</i> A corrupter, violator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिः|दूषि
दूषिः, -षी <i>f.</i><BR> The rheum of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषी
दूषिः, -षी <i>f.</i><BR> The rheum of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिका
दूषिका<BR>—1 A pencil, paint-brush.<BR>—2 A kind of rice.<BR>—3 Rheum of the eyes [one of the 12 impurities (मल) of man]; Ms. 5. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषित|दूषितः
दूषित <i>a.</i> [दुष्-णिच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Corrupted. defiled, spoiled.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Hurt, injured.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Marred, spoiled, frustrated; किं तावद् व्रतिनामुपोढतपसां<BR> विध्नैस्तपो दूषितम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Blinded, obscured, injured; च्युतकेशरदूषितेक्षणानि Ku. 4. 8.<BR>—3 Damaged, demoralized.<BR>—4 Blamed, censured.<BR>—5 Falsely accused, traduced, vilified.<BR>—6 Affected; touched; एतावदुक्त्वा वचनं बाष्पदूषितलोचनः । बाष्पदूषितया<BR> वाचा नोच्चैः शक्नोति भाषितुम् ॥ Rām. 4. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिता
दूषित + .{@-ता@} A girl who has been violated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषितम्
दूषित + .{@-तम्@} A fault, offence; यदस्याः पत्युर्वा रहसि परमं दूषितमभूत् U. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीका
दूषीका = दूषि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष्य|दूष्यं|दूष्यः
दूष्य <i>a.</i> [दुष्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 Corruptible.<BR>—2 Condemnable, Culpable, blamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष्यम्
दूष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@}<BR>—1 Matter, pus.<BR>—2 Poison.<BR>—3 Cotton.<BR>—4 A garment, clothes.<BR>—5 A tent; दूष्यैर्जितोदग्रगृहाणि सा चमूरतीत्य भूयांसि पुराण्यवर्तत Śi. 12. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष्या
दूष्य + .{@-ष्या@} Leathern girth of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषः|दोष
दोषः [दुष् भावे करणे वा घञ्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A fault, blame, censure, defect, blemish, weak point; पत्रं<BR> नैव यदा करीरविटपे दोषो वसन्तस्य किम् Bh. 2. 93; Pt. 1. 242; नात्र<BR> कुलपतिर्दोषं ग्रहीष्यति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">Page0825-2</a>]<BR> Ś. 3 ‘will not find fault or take exception’; so पुनरुक्तदोषा R. 14. 9.<BR> विसृज्य शूर्पवद्दोषान् गुणान् गृह्णन्ति साधवः । दोषग्राही गुणत्यागी<BR> चालनीव हि दुर्जनः ॥ Udb.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) An error, a mistake.<BR>—2 A crime, sin, guilt, offence; जायामदोषामुत संत्यजामि R. 14. 34;<BR> Ms. 8. 205; Y. 3. 79; also अधर्मदोष; cf. Rām. 3. 66. 16.<BR>—3 Noxious quality, badness, injurious nature or quality; as in आहारदोष;<BR> cf. Ms. 10. 14.<BR>—4 Harm, evil, danger, injury; बहुदोषा हि शर्वरी Mk. 1. 58; अनुसरति<BR> हि शशाङ्कं राहु-दोषेऽपि तारा Pratimā 1. 25. को दोषः ‘what harm is there’.<BR>—5 Bad or injurious consequence, detrimental effect; तत्किमयमातपदोषः<BR> स्यात् Ś. 3; अदाता वंशदोषेण कर्मदोषाद्दरिद्रता Cāṇ. 49; Ms. 10. 14.<BR>—6 Morbid affection, disease.<BR>—7 Disorder of the three humours of the body, or the three humours when<BR> in a disordered state.<BR>—8 (In Nyāya &c.) A fault of a definition: (<i>i. e.</i> अव्याप्ति, अतिव्याप्ति<BR> and असंभव).<BR>—9 (In Rhet.) A fault or defect of composition (such as पददोष, पदांशदोष,<BR> वाक्यदोष, रसदोष, and अर्थदोष which are defined and illustrated<BR> in the 7th Ullāsa of K. P.).<BR>—10 A calf.<BR>—11 Refutation.<BR>—12 Evening, dusk; cf. दोषा; दोषे हृषीकेश उतार्धरात्रे निशीथ एकोऽवतु<BR> पद्मनाभः Bhāg. 6. 8. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोषाक्षरम्, दोषाकर, दोषारोपः, दोषैकदृश्, दोषकर, दोषकारिन्, दोषकृत्, दोषगुणम्, दोषग्रस्त, दोषग्राहिन्, दोषज्ञ, दोषत्रयम्, दोषदृष्टि, दोषप्रसंगः, दोषभक्तिः, दोषभाज्, दोषभेदः, दोषस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषाक्षरम्
दोषः + -अक्षरम् accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषाकर|दोषाकरः
दोषः + -आकर <i>a.</i> faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषारोपः|दोषारोप
दोषः + -आरोपः charge, accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

