दोषः + -एकदृश् <i>a.</i> fault-finding, censorious, picking holes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकर
दोषः + -कर, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> causing evil, hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकारिन्
दोषः + -कर, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> causing evil, hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकृत्
दोषः + -कर, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> causing evil, hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषगुणम्
दोषः + -गुणम् bad and good qualities; बीजानामुप्तिविच्च स्यात्क्षेत्रदोषगुणस्य<BR> च (जानीयात्) Ms. 9. 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषग्रस्त
दोषः + -ग्रस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 convicted, guilty.<BR>—2 full of faults or defects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषग्राहिन्
दोषः + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 malicious, malignant.<BR>—2 censorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषज्ञ|दोषज्ञः
दोषः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing faults &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषज्ञः|दोषज्ञ
दोषः + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञः@})<BR>—1 a wise or learned man; R. 1. 93.<BR>—2 a physician.<BR>—3 a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषत्रयम्
दोषः + -त्रयम् disorder or vitiation of the three humours of the body;<BR> (<i>i. e.</i> वात, पित्त and कफ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषदृष्टि
दोषः + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> looking at faults, censorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषप्रसंगः|दोषप्रसङ्ग|दोषप्रसंग
दोषः + -प्रसंगः attaching blame, condemnation, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषभक्तिः|दोषभक्ति
दोषः + -भक्तिः <i>f.</i> tendency to a disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषभाज्
दोषः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> faulty, guilty, wrong, a villain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषभेदः|दोषभेद
दोषः + -भेदः a peculiar modification of the vitiation of three humours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषस्थानम्
दोषः + -स्थानम् the seat of disorder of the humours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकः|दोषक
दोषकः A calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषणम्
दोषणम् A charge, an accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषल
दोषल <i>a.</i> Faulty, defective, corrupt, sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिक|दोषिकः
दोषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Faulty, defective, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिकः|दोषिक
दोषिक + .{@-कः@} Sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिन्
दोषिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दुष्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Impure, corrupt, defiled, contaminated.<BR>—2 Faulty, defective.<BR>—3 Criminal, wicked, sinful, guilty, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ठु|दुष्ठुः
दुष्ठु <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Ill, bad.<BR>—2 Improperly, incorrectly, wrongly. निन्दायां दुष्ठु, सुष्ठु प्रशंसने<BR> Ak. यतो मां दुष्ठु मन्यसे Bu. C. 4. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्यन्तः|दुष्यन्त|दुष्यंतः
दुष्यन्तः N. of a king of the lunar race, descendant of Puru, husband<BR> of Śakuntalā and father of Bharata. [Once upon a time Duṣyanta, while<BR> hunting in the forest, went to the hermitage of the sage Kaṇva,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">Page0826-1</a>]<BR> while pursuing a deer. There he was hospitably received by Śakuntalā,<BR> the adopted daughter of the sage, and her transcendent beauty made so<BR> great an impression on his mind that he prevailed on her to become his<BR> queen, and married her according to the <i>Gāndharva</i> form of marriage.<BR> Having passed some time in her company the king returned to his capital.<BR> After some months Śakuntalā was delivered of a son, and her father thought<BR> it advisable to send her with the boy to her husband. But when they went<BR> and stood before Duṣyanta, he (for fear of public scandal) denied all<BR> knowledge of having ever before seen or married her. But a heavenly voice<BR> told him that she was his lawful wife, and he thereupon admitted her,<BR> along with the boy, into his harem, and made her first queen. The happy<BR> pair lived to a good old age and committing the realm to the care of Bharata,<BR> retired to the woods. Such is the account of Duṣyanta and Śakuntalā<BR> given in the Mahābhārata; the story told by Kālidāsa differs in several<BR> important respects; see “Śakuntalā”.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0825-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्
दुस् A prefix to nouns and sometimes to verbs meaning ‘bad, evil, wicked, inferior, hard or difficult, &c.’<BR> (<i>N. B.</i> The स् of दुस्<BR> is changed to र् before vowels and soft consonants, see दुर्; to<BR> a Visarga before sibilants, to श् before च् and छ्, and to ष्<BR> before क् and प्.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दुरुपस्थान, दुष्कर, दुष्कर्मन्, दुष्कालः, दुष्कुलम्, दुष्कुलीन, दुष्कुह, दुष्कृत्, दुष्कृतिन्, दुष्कृतम्, दुष्कृतिः, दुष्क्रम, दुष्क्रिया, दुष्क्रीत, दुश्चर, दुश्चरित, दुश्चर्मन्, दुश्चिकित्स्य, दुश्चिक्यम्, दुश्चित्त, दुश्चेष्टितम्, दुश्च्यवनः, दुश्च्यावः, दुश्च्छद, दुस्तर, दुस्तर्कः, दुष्पच, दुष्पतनम्, दुष्परिग्रह, दुष्पान, दुष्पार, दुष्पूर, दुष्प्रकाश, दुष्प्रक्रिया, दुष्प्रकृति, दुष्प्रजस्, दुष्प्रज्ञ, दुष्प्रज्ञानम्, दुष्प्रणीत, दुष्प्रतर, दुष्प्रतीक, दुष्प्रद, दुष्प्रधर्ष, दुष्प्रधृष्य, दुष्प्रमेय, दुष्प्रवादः, दुष्प्रवृतिः, दुष्प्रसह, दुष्प्राप, दुष्प्रापण, दुष्प्रीतिः, दुर्मरम्, दुःशंस, दुःशक, दुःशक्त, दुःशकुनम्, दुःशला, दुःशासन, दुःशील, दुःशृङ्गी, दुःष्ठु, दुःसंचार, दुःषम, दुःषमम्, दुःसमम्, दुःसत्त्वम्, दुःसथः, दुःसंधान, दुःसंधेय, दुःसंस्थित, दुःसह, दुःसाक्षिन्, दुःसाध, दुःसाध्य, दुःसाधिन्, दुःसुप्त, दुःस्थ, दुःस्थित, दुःस्थम्, दुःस्थितिः, दुःस्पृष्टम्, दुःस्फाटः, दुःस्मर, दुःस्वप्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपस्थान
दुस् + -उपस्थान <i>a.</i> difficult to be approached; यो रणे दुरुपस्थानो<BR> हस्तरोधं दधद् धनुः Bk. 5. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर|दुष्करं
दुस् + -कर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 wicked, acting badly; काँल्लोकांस्तु गमिष्यामि कृत्वा कर्म सुदुष्करम्<BR> Mb. 12. 27. 18.<BR>—2 hard to be done or accomplished, arduous, difficult; वक्तुं सुकरं<BR> कर्तुं दुष्करम् ‘sooner said than done’; Amaru. 46; Mk. 3. 1; Ms. 7. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्करम्
दुस् + -कर + .({@-रम्@})<BR>—1 a difficult or painful task or act, difficulty.<BR>—2 atmosphere, ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर्मन्|दुष्कर्म्मन्
दुस् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 any bad act, sin, crime.<BR>—2 any difficult or painful act.<BR>—3 A wicked man; ततो वसति दुष्कर्मा नरके शाश्वतीः समाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कालः|दुष्काल
दुस् + -कालः<BR>—1 bad times; दुष्कालेऽपि कलावसज्जनरुचौ प्राणैः परं रक्षता Mu. 7. 5.<BR>—2 the time of universal destruction.<BR>—3 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुलम्
दुस् + -कुलम् a bad or low family; (आददीत) स्त्रीरत्नं दुष्कुलादपि Ms. 2. 238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुलीन|दुष्कुलीनः
दुस् + -कुलीन <i>a.</i> low-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुह
दुस् + -कुह <i>a.</i> hypocritical; अतीन्द्रियेणात्मनि दुष्कुहोऽयं मया<BR> जनो योजयितुं न शक्यः Bu. C. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृत्
दुस् + -कृत्, -कृतिन् <i>m.</i> a wicked person; विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम्<BR> Bg. 4. 8; पुनः पुनर्दुष्कृतिनं निनिन्द R. 14. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतिन्
दुस् + -कृत्, -कृतिन् <i>m.</i> a wicked person; विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम्<BR> Bg. 4. 8; पुनः पुनर्दुष्कृतिनं निनिन्द R. 14. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतम्
दुस् + -कृतम्, -कृतिः <i>f.</i> a sin, misdeed; उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते Bg. 2. 50;<BR> (ददर्श) ततस्तान् भिद्यमानांश्च कर्मभिः दुष्कृतैः स्वकैः<BR> Rām. 7. 21. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतिः|दुष्कृति
दुस् + -कृतम्, -कृतिः <i>f.</i> a sin, misdeed; उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते Bg. 2. 50;<BR> (ददर्श) ततस्तान् भिद्यमानांश्च कर्मभिः दुष्कृतैः स्वकैः<BR> Rām. 7. 21. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रम
दुस् + -क्रम <i>a.</i> ill-arranged, unmethodical, unsystematic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रिया
दुस् + -क्रिया a misdemeanour, bad act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रीत|दुष्क्रीतं
दुस् + -क्रीत <i>a.</i> not properly purchased; क्रीत्वा मूल्येन यो द्रव्यं<BR> दुष्क्रीतं मन्यते क्रयी Nārada Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर|दुश्चरः
दुस् + -चर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 hard to be performed or accomplished, arduous, difficult; चरतः<BR> किल दुश्चरं तपस्तृणबिन्दोः परिशङ्कितः पुरा R. 8. 79; Ku. 7. 65.<BR>—2 inaccessible, unapproachable.<BR>—3 acting ill, behaving wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चरः|दुश्चर
दुस् + -चर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a bear.<BR>—2 a bi-valve shell. ˚चारिन् <i>a.</i> practising very austere penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चरित
दुस् + -चरित <i>a.</i> wicked, ill-behaved,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">Page0826-2</a>]<BR> abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चरितम्
दुस् + -चरित + .({@-तम्@}) misbehaviour, ill-conduct; तथा दुश्चरितं सर्वं वेदे<BR> त्रिवृति मज्जति Ms. 11. 263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर्मन्|दुश्चर्म्मन्
दुस् + -चर्मन् <i>a.</i> affected with a disease of the skin, leprous. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a circumcised man, or one whose prepuce is naturally wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चिकित्स्य
दुस् + -चिकित्स्य <i>a.</i> difficult to be cured, incurable. सुदुश्चिकित्स्यस्य<BR> भवस्य मृत्योर्भिषक्तमं त्वाद्य गतिं गताः स्म Bhāg. 4. 30. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चिक्यम्
दुस् + -चिक्यम् the third लग्नराशि; दुश्चिक्यं स्यात्तृतीयकम् Jyotistattvam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चित्त
दुस् + -चित्त <i>a.</i> melancholy, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चेष्टितम्
दुस् + -चेष्टितम् misconduct, error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्च्यवनः|दुश्च्यवन
दुस् + -च्यवनः an epithet of Indra; अत्तुं महेन्द्रियं भागमेति दुश्च्यवनोऽधुना Bk. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्च्यावः|दुश्च्याव
दुस् + -च्यावः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्च्छद
दुस् + -च्छद <i>a.</i> difficult to be clothed, tattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तर
दुस् + -तर <i>a.</i> (दुष्टर or दुस्तर)<BR>—1 difficult to be crossed; तितीर्षुर्दुस्तरं मोहदुडुपेनास्मि सागरम्<BR> R. 1. 2; Ms. 4. 242; प्रविशेन्मुखमाहेयं दुस्तरं वा महार्णवम् Pt. 1. 111.<BR>—2 difficult to be subdued, insuperable, invincible.<BR>—3 not to be surpassed or excelled.<BR>—4 difficult to be borne or endured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तर्कः|दुस्तर्क
दुस् + -तर्कः false reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पच
दुस् + -पच (दुष्पच) <i>a.</i> difficult to be digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पतनम्
दुस् + -पतनम्<BR>—1 falling badly.<BR>—2 a word of abuse, abusive epithet (अपशब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्परिग्रह|दुष्परिग्रहः
दुस् + -परिग्रह <i>a.</i> difficult to be seized, taken, or kept; Pt. 1. 67.<BR> लोकाधाराः श्रियो राज्ञां दुरापा दुष्परिग्रहाः Kām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्परिग्रहः|दुष्परिग्रह
दुस् + -परिग्रह + .({@-हः@}) a bad wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पान
दुस् + -पान <i>a.</i> difficult to be drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पार
दुस् + -पार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be crossed.<BR>—2 difficult to be accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पूर
दुस् + -पूर <i>a.</i> difficult to be filled or satisfied; दुष्पूरोदरपूरणाय<BR> पिबति स्रोतःपतिं वाडवः Bh.; Bg. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रकाश
दुस् + -प्रकाश <i>a.</i> obscure, dark, dim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रक्रिया
दुस् + -प्रक्रिया little authority; Rāj. T. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रकृति
दुस् + -प्रकृति <i>a.</i> ill-tempered. evil-natured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रजस्
दुस् + -प्रजस् <i>a.</i> having bad progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रज्ञ
दुस् + -प्रज्ञ (दुष्प्रज्ञ) <i>a.</i> weak-minded, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रज्ञानम्
दुस् + -प्रज्ञानम् bad intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रणीत
दुस् + -प्रणीत <i>a.</i> ill-arranged or managed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रणीतम्
दुस् + -प्रणीत + .({@-तम्@}) impolitic conduct; Mb. 8. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रतर
दुस् + -प्रतर <i>a.</i> difficult to be overcome or understood; धर्मं<BR> सूक्ष्मतरं वाच्यं तत्र दुष्प्रतरं त्वया Mb. 12. 19. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रतीक
दुस् + -प्रतीक <i>a.</i> difficult to know or recognise; दुष्प्रतीकमरण्येऽस्मिन्किं<BR> तात वनमागतः Rām. 2. 100. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रद
दुस् + -प्रद <i>a.</i> causing pain or sorrow; अद्य भीताः पलायन्तु दुष्प्रदास्ते<BR> दिशो दश Rām. 2. 106. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्ष
दुस् + -प्रधर्ष, -प्रधृष्य<BR>—1 un assailable; see दुर्धर्ष; सा दुष्प्रधर्षा मनसापि हिंस्रैः R. 2. 27.<BR>—2 secure from assault, intangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधृष्य
दुस् + -प्रधर्ष, -प्रधृष्य<BR>—1 un assailable; see दुर्धर्ष; सा दुष्प्रधर्षा मनसापि हिंस्रैः R. 2. 27.<BR>—2 secure from assault, intangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रमेय
दुस् + -प्रमेय <i>a.</i> immeasurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रवादः|दुष्प्रवाद
दुस् + -प्रवादः slander, calumnious report, scandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रवृतिः
दुस् + -प्रवृतिः <i>f.</i> bad news, evil report; तेषां शूर्पणखैवैका<BR> दुष्प्रवृत्तिहराभवत् R. 12. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रसह
दुस् + -प्रसह (दुष्प्रसह) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 irresistible, terrible,<BR>—2 hard to bear or endure; M. 5. 10; R. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप
दुस् + -प्राप, -प्रापण <i>a.</i> unattainable, hard to get; R. 1. 48; असंयता<BR> त्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः Bg. 6. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रापण
दुस् + -प्राप, -प्रापण <i>a.</i> unattainable, hard to get; R. 1. 48; असंयता<BR> त्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः Bg. 6. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रीतिः|दुष्प्रीति
दुस् + -प्रीतिः <i>f.</i> displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्मरम्
दुस् + -मरम् a sad demise; अकाले दुर्मरमहो यज्जीवामस्तया विना Bk. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशंस
दुस् + -शंस <i>a.</i> Ved. evil-minded, malevolent, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशक
दुस् + -शक, -शक्त <i>a.</i> powerless, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशक्त
दुस् + -शक, -शक्त <i>a.</i> powerless, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशकुनम्
दुस् + -शकुनम् a bad omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशला
दुस् + -शला N. of the only daughter of धृतराष्ट्र given in marriage to Jayadratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशासन|दुःशासनः
दुस् + -शासन <i>a.</i> difficult to be managed or governed, intractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशासनः|दुःशासन
दुस् + -शासन + .({@-नः@}) N. of one of the 100 sons of धृतराष्ट्र. [He was brave<BR> and warlike, but wicked and intractable. When Yudhiṣṭhira staked and<BR> lost even Draupadī, Duhśāsana dragged her into the assembly by her<BR> hair and began to strip her of every clothing; but Kṛṣṇa, ever ready<BR> to help the distressed, covered her from shame and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">Page0827-1</a>]<BR> ignominy. Bhīma was so much exasperated at this dastardly act of Duhśāsana<BR> that he vowed in the assembly that he would not rest till he had drunk<BR> the villainʼs blood. On the 16th day of the great war Bhīma encountered<BR> Duhśāsana in a single combat, killed him with ease, and drank, according<BR> to his resolution, his blood to his heartʼs content.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0826-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशील
दुस् + -शील (दुश्शील) <i>a.</i> ill-mannered or ill behaved, reprobate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशृङ्गी
दुस् + -शृङ्गी a disloyal wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःष्ठु
दुस् + -ष्ठु see दुस्थ <i>a.</i> unsettled, in calamity; कथं दुष्ठुः<BR> स्वयं धर्मे प्रजास्त्वं पालयिष्यसि Bk. 6. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंचार
दुस् + -संचार <i>a.</i> difficult to be passed; दुःसंचारासु नगरवीथीषु; Pt. 1. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषम
दुस् + -षम (दुःषम or दुष्षम), {@-सम@} (दुःसम or दुस्सम) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 uneven, unlike, unequal.<BR>—2 adverse, unfortunate.<BR>—3 evil, improper, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषमम्
दुस् + -षमम्, -समम् <i>ind.</i> ill, wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसमम्
दुस् + -षमम्, -समम् <i>ind.</i> ill, wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसत्त्वम्
दुस् + -सत्त्वम् an evil being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसथः
दुस् + -सथः<BR>—1 a dog.<BR>—2 a cock; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंधान|दुःसन्धान
दुस् + -संधान, -संधेय <i>a.</i> difficult to be united or reconciled.<BR> -मृद्घटवत् सुखभेद्यो दुःसन्धानश्च दुर्जनो भवति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंधेय
दुस् + -संधान, -संधेय <i>a.</i> difficult to be united or reconciled.<BR> -मृद्घटवत् सुखभेद्यो दुःसन्धानश्च दुर्जनो भवति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसंस्थित
दुस् + -संस्थित <i>a.</i> very sinful or ugly to look at; Rām. 2. 9. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसह
दुस् + -सह (दुस्सह) <i>a.</i> unbearable, irresistible, insupportable.<BR> भवत्यनिष्टादपि नाम दुःसहात् Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाक्षिन्
दुस् + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a false witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाध
दुस् + -साध, -साध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be accomplished or managed.<BR>—2 difficult to be cured.<BR>—3 difficult to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाध्य|दुःसाध्यः
दुस् + -साध, -साध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 difficult to be accomplished or managed.<BR>—2 difficult to be cured.<BR>—3 difficult to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाधिन्
दुस् + -साधिन् <i>m.</i> door-keeper; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसुप्त
दुस् + -सुप्त <i>a.</i> having bad dreams (in oneʼs sleep).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थ|दुःस्थः
दुस् + -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> (written also दुस्थ and दुस्थित)<BR>—1 ill-conditioned, poor, miserable.<BR>—2 suffering pain, unhappy, distressed; कल्पान्तदुःस्था वसुधा तथोहे Bk.<BR>—3 unwell, ill.<BR>—4 unsteady, disquieted.<BR>—5 foolish, unwise, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थित
दुस् + -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> (written also दुस्थ and दुस्थित)<BR>—1 ill-conditioned, poor, miserable.<BR>—2 suffering pain, unhappy, distressed; कल्पान्तदुःस्था वसुधा तथोहे Bk.<BR>—3 unwell, ill.<BR>—4 unsteady, disquieted.<BR>—5 foolish, unwise, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थम्
दुस् + -स्थम् <i>ind.</i> badly, ill, unwell; दुःस्थं तिष्ठसि यच्च पथ्यमधुना<BR> कर्तास्मि तच्छ्रोष्यसि; Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थितिः|दुःस्थिति
दुस् + -स्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 bad condition or situation, unhappiness, misery.<BR>—2 instability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्पृष्टम्
दुस् + -स्पृष्टम् (दुः, दुस्पृष्टम्)<BR>—1 slight touch or contact.<BR>—2 slight touch or action of the tongue which produces the sounds य्,<BR> र्, ल् and व्; दुस्पृष्टश्चेति विज्ञेयो ऌकारः प्लुत एव च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्फाटः
दुस् + -स्फाटः a kind of weapon; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्मर
दुस् + -स्मर <i>a.</i> hard or painful to remember; U. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्वप्नः|दुःस्वप्न
दुस् + -स्वप्नः a bad dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्
दुह् I. €2 U. (दोग्धि, दुग्धे, दुदोह-दुदुहे. अधुक्षत्-त or अदुग्ध,<BR> धोक्ष्यति-ते, दोग्धुम्, दुग्ध)<BR>—1 To milk or squeeze out, extract (with two acc.); भास्वन्ति रत्नानि<BR> महौषधीश्च पृथूपदिष्टां दुदुहुर्धरित्रीम् Ku. 1. 2; यः पयो दोग्धि<BR> पाषाणं स रामाद्भूतिमाप्नुयात् Bk. 8. 82; पयो घटोध्नीरपि गा दुहन्ति 12. 73;<BR> R. 5. 33.<BR>—2 To draw anything out of another (with two acc.); प्राणान्दुहन्निवात्मानं<BR> शोकं चित्तमवारुधत् Bk. 6. 9.<BR>—3 To drain a thing of its contents, to make profit out of; दुदोह गां<BR> स यज्ञाय शस्याय मघवा दिवम् R. 1. 26.<BR>—4 To yield or grant (any desired object); कामान्दुग्धे विप्रकर्षत्यलक्ष्मीम् U. 5. 31.<BR>—5 To enjoy. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दोहयति-ते) To cause to milk. ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> (दुधुक्षति-ते) To wish to milk; राजन् दुधुक्षसि यदि क्षितिधेनुमेताम्<BR> Bh. 2. 46. ━II. €1 P. (दोहति) To hurt. pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्ध|दुग्धः
दुग्ध <i>p. p.</i> [दुह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Milked, milked out.<BR>—2 Extracted, drawn out &c.<BR>—3 Collected, filled, full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धम्
दुग्ध + .{@-ग्धम्@}<BR>—1 Milk.<BR>—2 The milky juice of plants.<BR>—3 Milking.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-2" target="_blank">Page0827-2</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दुग्धाक्षः, दुग्धकूपिका, दुग्धाग्रम्, दुग्धाम्रम्, दुग्धतालीयम्, दुग्धाङ्कः, दुग्धदा, दुग्धपाचनम्, दुग्धपाषाणम्, दुग्धपोष्य, दुग्धफेनः, दुग्धबन्धः, दुग्धबन्धकः, दुग्धबीजा, दुग्धसमुद्रः, दुग्धाब्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाक्षः|दुग्धाक्ष
दुग्ध + -अक्षः a kind of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धकूपिका
दुग्ध + -कूपिका a kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0827-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

