दृप्
दृप् I. €1 P., €10 U. (दर्पति, दर्पयति-ते) To light, inflame,<BR> kindle. ━II. €4 P. (दृप्यति, दृप्त)<BR>—1 To be proud, be arrogant or insolent; स किल नात्मना दृप्यति U. 5;<BR> दृप्यद्दानवदूयमानदिविषद्दुर्वारदुःखापदाम् Gīt. 9.<BR>—2 To be greatly delighted.<BR>—3 To be wild or extravagant.<BR>—4 To be mad or foolish. ━III. €6 P. (दृपति) To pain, torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्प|दर्पः
दर्प [दृप् भावे घञ् कर्तरि अच् वा]<BR>—1 Pride, arrogance, insolence, haughtiness; भृतो नार्तो न कुर्याद्यो<BR> दर्पात्कर्म यथोदितम् (स दण्ड्यः) Ms. 8. 215; Bg. 16. 4.<BR>—2 Rashness.<BR>—3 Vanity, conceit.<BR>—4 Sullenness, sulkiness.<BR>—5 Heat.<BR>—6 Musk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दर्पाध्मात, दर्पोपशान्तिः, दर्पकल, दर्पच्छिद्, दर्पहर, दर्पदः, दर्पहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पाध्मात
दर्प + -आध्मात <i>a.</i> inflated or puffed up with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पोपशान्तिः|दर्पोपशान्ति
दर्प + -उपशान्तिः allaying pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पकल
दर्प + -कल <i>a.</i> uttering a proud and agreeable sound; तुषारसंघातशिलाः<BR> खुराग्रैः समुल्लिखन्दर्पकलः ककुद्मान् Ku. 1. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पच्छिद्
दर्प + -छिद्, -हर <i>a.</i> humbling, humiliating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पहर
दर्प + -छिद्, -हर <i>a.</i> humbling, humiliating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पदः|दर्पद
दर्प + -दः, -हन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पहन्
दर्प + -दः, -हन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पक|दर्पकः
दर्पक <i>a.</i> Making proud, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पकः|दर्पक
दर्पक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR>—2 pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पणः|दर्पण|दर्पणं
दर्पणः [दृप्-ल्यु]<BR>—1 A looking-glass, mirror; लोचनाभ्यां विहीनस्य दर्पणः किं करिष्यति<BR> Cāṇ. 109; Ku. 7. 26; R. 10. 10, 14. 37.<BR>—2 N. of a mountain inhabited by Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पणम्
दर्पणः + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The eye.<BR>—2 Kindling, inflaming, making proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पित
दर्पित, दर्पिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पिन्
दर्पित, दर्पिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्त|दृप्तः
दृप्त <i>a.</i> [दृप्-क्त]<BR>—1 Proud, arrogant; योधाभ्यामधिकं दृप्तः शूराभ्यामधिको जयी Bm. 2. 45;<BR> -दृप्तबालाकिर्हानूचानो गार्ग्य आस Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Mad, wild, frantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्तः|दृप्त
दृप्त + .{@-प्तः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्र|दृप्रः
दृप्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proud, arrogant.<BR>—2 Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृभ्
दृभ् I. €1. €6 P., €10 U. (दर्भति, दृभति, दर्भयति-ते) To tie,<BR> fasten, string together, arrange. ━II. €10 U. (दर्भयति-ते) To fear, be afraid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृब्ध|दृब्धः
दृब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Tied, strung.<BR>—2 Afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृब्धम्
दृब्ध + .{@-ब्धम्@}<BR>—1 A string.<BR>—2 Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृब्धिः|दृब्धि
दृब्धिः <i>f.</i> Stringing together, arranging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्प्|दृंप्
दृम्प् (-म्फ्) €6 P. (दृम्प-म्फ-ति)<BR> To afflict, torture, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फ्|दृंफ्
दृम्प् (-म्फ्) €6 P. (दृम्प-म्फ-ति)<BR> To afflict, torture, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फू|दृंफू
दृम्फू <i>f.</i> A snake in general; cf. दृन्फू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् €1 P. (पश्यति, ददर्श, अदर्शत्, अद्राक्षीत्, द्रक्ष्यति, दृष्टुम्, दृष्ट)<BR>—1 To see, look at, observe, view, behold, perceive; द्रक्ष्यसि भ्रातृजायाम्<BR> Me. 10, 19; R. 3. 42.<BR>—2 To look upon, regard, consider; आत्मवत्सर्वभूतेषु यः पश्यति स<BR> पण्डितः Cāṇ. 5; Pt. 1. 58.<BR>—3 To visit, wait or call upon; प्रत्युद्ययौ मुनिं द्रष्टुं ब्रह्माणमिव<BR> वासवः Rām.<BR>—4 To perceive with the mind, learn, know, understand; एवमाचरतो दृष्ट्वा<BR> धर्मस्य मुनयो गतिम् Ms. 1. 110, 12. 23.<BR>—5 To inspect,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">Page0830-2</a>]<BR> discover.<BR>—6 To search, investigate, examine, decide; कृतरक्षः समुत्थाय पश्येदायव्ययौ<BR> स्वयम् Y. 1. 327, 2. 305.<BR>—7 To see by divine intuition; ऋषिर्दर्शनात्स्तोमान् ददर्श Nir.<BR>—8 To look helplessly on (without power to prevent what is taking place).<BR>━<i>Pass.</i> (दृश्यते)<BR>—1 To be seen or perceived, become visible or manifested; तव तच्चारु<BR> वपुर्न दृश्यते Ku. 4. 18, 3; R. 3. 40; Bk. 3. 19; दृष्टः स्वप्ने कितव<BR> रमयन्कामपि त्वं मयेति Me. 113.<BR>—2 To appear or look like, seem, look; तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत R. 3. 34.<BR>—3 To be found or seen, occur (as in a book &c.); द्वितीयाम्रेडितान्तेषु<BR> ततोऽन्यत्रापि दृश्यते Sk.; इति प्रयोगो भाष्ये दृश्यते.<BR>—4 To be considered or regarded; सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकमियं दारेषु<BR> दृश्या त्वया Ś. 4. 17. ━<i>Caus.</i> (दर्शयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause any one (acc., dat. or gen.) to see anything (acc.), to show,<BR> point out; दर्शय तं चौरसिंहम् Pt. 1; दर्शयति भक्तान् हरिम्<BR> Sk.; प्रत्यभिज्ञानरत्नं च रामायादर्शयत्कृती R. 12. 64, 1. 47, 13. 24; Ms. 4. 59.<BR>—2 To prove, demonstrate; वीर्यं मा न ददर्शस्त्वम् Bk. 15. 12.<BR>—3 To exhibit, display, make visible; तदेव मे दर्शय देव रूपम् Bg. 11. 45.<BR>—4 To produce (as in a court of justice); Ms. 8. 158.<BR>—5 To adduce (as evidence); अत्र श्रुतिं दर्शयति.<BR>—6 (Ā.) To show oneself, appear, show oneself or anything belonging to<BR> oneself; भवो भक्तान् दर्शयते Sk. (<i>i. e.</i> स्वयमेव); स्वां<BR> गृहेऽपि वनितां कथमास्यं ह्रीनिमीलि खलु दर्शयिताहे N. 5. 71; स<BR> संततं दर्शयते गतस्मयः कृताधिपत्यामिव साधु बन्धुताम् Ki. 1. 10;<BR> Ku. 4. 25. ━<i>Desid.</i> (दिदृक्षते) To wish or desire to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्वर
दृश्वर <i>a.</i> one who has seen; यमास्यदृश्वरी तस्य ताडका वेत्ति<BR> विक्रमम् Bk. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श <i>a.</i> [दृश्-भावे घञ्] Seeing, looking<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शः|दर्श
दर्श + .{@-र्शः@}<BR>—1 Sight, view, appearance (usually in comp.); दुर्दर्शः, प्रियदर्शः<BR> &c. दुर्दर्शा केचिदाभान्ति नराः काष्ठमया इव । प्रियदर्शास्तथा चान्ये<BR> दर्शनादेव मानवाः ॥ Mb. 13. 144. 45.<BR>—2 Ocular evidence or proof.<BR>—3 The day of the new moon (अमावास्या); एकत्रस्थितचन्दार्कदर्शनाद्<BR> दर्श उच्यते; शक्यते च चन्द्रस्यादर्शनेन अमावास्या दर्श इति लक्षयितुम् ।<BR> यथा चक्षुषोरभावे सति चक्षुष्मान् इति चक्षुर्भ्यां लक्ष्यते । ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 36.<BR>—4 The new moon.<BR>—5 The half-monthly sacrifice, a sacrificial rite performed on the day<BR> of the new moon. It comprises of the आग्नेय, ऐन्द्राग्न and सांनाग्य यागs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श + .{@-दर्श, -दर्शम्@} <i>ind.</i> At every sight; Ks.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दर्शपः, दर्शपूर्णमासन्यायः, दर्शयामिनी, दर्शविपद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शम्
दर्श + .{@-दर्श, -दर्शम्@} <i>ind.</i> At every sight; Ks.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दर्शपः, दर्शपूर्णमासन्यायः, दर्शयामिनी, दर्शविपद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शपः|दर्शप
दर्श + -पः a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शपूर्णमासन्यायः
दर्श + -पूर्णमासन्यायः The rule according to which the same act can<BR> be said to yield all desired objects but only one at a time (and not simultaneously).<BR> This is established by जैमिनि and शबर in MS. 4. 3. 25-28 (see<BR> योगसिद्धिन्याय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयामिनी
दर्श + -यामिनी the night of the new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शविपद्
दर्श + -विपद् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शक|दर्शकः
दर्शक <i>a.</i> (-का or -र्शिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दृश्-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Seeing, observing &c.<BR>—2 Showing, pointing out; विधिप्रयुक्तसत्कारैः स्वयं मार्गस्य दर्शकः Ku. 6. 52.<BR>—3 Examining, looking out for.<BR>—4 Explaining, making clear, elucidating<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शकः|दर्शक
दर्शक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 One who shows or exhibits.<BR>—2 A door-keeper, warder.<BR>—3 A skilful man, one proficient in any art or science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0830-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शत|दर्शतः
दर्शत <i>a.</i> [दृश् कर्मणि अतच्] Ved.<BR>—1 Visible. यद्वै चतुर्थं तत्तुरीयं दर्शतं पदमिति Bṛ. Up. 5. 14. 3.<BR>—2 Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शतः|दर्शत
दर्शत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शन|दर्शनं
दर्शन <i>a.</i> [दृश्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at (at the end of comp.); देव˚, धर्म˚, &c.<BR>—2 Showing, exhibiting.<BR>—3 Demonstrating, teaching; भागवतधर्मदर्शना नव महाभागवताः<BR> Bhāg. 5. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनम्
दर्शन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Looking at, seeing, observing; अतीन्द्रियेष्वप्युपपन्नदर्शनो बभूव<BR> भावेषु दिलीपनन्दनः R. 3. 41.<BR>—2 Knowing, understanding, perceiving, foreseeing; प्रमदामनु संस्थितः<BR> शुचा नृपतिः सन्निति वाच्यदर्शनात् R. 8. 72.<BR>—3 Sight, vision; चिन्ताजडं दर्शनम् Ś. 4. 6.<BR>—4 The eye.<BR>—5 Inspection, examination; बलानां दर्शनं कृत्वा सेनान्या सह चिन्तयेत् Y. 1. 329.<BR>—6 Showing, displaying, exhibition.<BR>—7 Becoming visible; रावणिः पितरं युद्धे दर्शनस्थोऽब्रवीदिदम् Rām. 7. 29. 32.<BR>—8 Visiting, paying a visit, a visit; देवदर्शनम् Y. 1. 84.<BR>—9 (Hence) Going into the presence of, audience; मारीचस्ते दर्शनं<BR> वितरति Ś. 7; राजदर्शनं मे कारय &c.<BR>—10 Colour, aspect, appearance, semblance, अनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम् Bg. 11. 10;<BR> R. 3. 57.<BR>—11 Appearance, producing (in court); यो यस्य प्रतिभूस्तिष्ठेद्दर्शनायेह<BR> मानवः Ms. 8. 158, 160.<BR>—12 A vision, dream, dream.<BR>—13 Discernment, understanding, intellect; सम्यग्दर्शनसंपन्नः कर्मभिर्न<BR> निबध्यते Ms. 6. 74.<BR>—14 Judgment, apprehension.<BR>—15 Religious knowledge.<BR>—16 A doctrine or theory prescribed in a system.<BR>—17 A system of philosophy; as in सर्वदर्शनसंग्रह.<BR>—18 A mirror.<BR>—19 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>—20 Opinion; अथानुजं भृशमनुशास्य दर्शनम् Rām. 2. 21. 64.<BR>—21 Intention.<BR>—22 Demonstration.<BR>—23 A sacrifice.<BR>—24 Mention, assertion; दर्शनादर्शनयोश्च दर्शनं प्रमाणम् ŚB. on MS. 10. 7. 36.<BR>—25 Experiencing; भवतो दर्शनं यत्स्यादपुनर्भवदर्शनम् Bhāg. 1. 8. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दर्शनेप्सु, दर्शनोज्ज्वला, दर्शनगृहम्, दर्शनपथः, दर्शनप्रतिभूः, दर्शनप्रातिभाव्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनेप्सु
दर्शन + -ईप्सु <i>a.</i> anxious to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनोज्ज्वला
दर्शन + -उज्ज्वला the great white jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनगृहम्
दर्शन + -गृहम् an audience chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनपथः|दर्शनपथ
दर्शन + -पथः the range of sight or vision, horizon; मम दर्शनपथमवतीर्णः<BR> Ś. 3 ‘crossed my sight’; क्रमेण तस्मिन्नवतीर्णदृक्पथे N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रतिभूः
दर्शन + -प्रतिभूः, -प्रातिभाव्यम् a bail or surety for appearance; Y. 2. 54;<BR> Ms. 8. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रातिभाव्यम्
दर्शन + -प्रतिभूः, -प्रातिभाव्यम् a bail or surety for appearance; Y. 2. 54;<BR> Ms. 8. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीय|दर्शनीयः
दर्शनीय <i>pot. p.</i> [दृश्-अनीयर्]<BR>—1 To be seen, visible, observable, perceptible.<BR>—2 Fit to be seen, good-looking, handsome, beautiful; अहो दर्शनीयान्यक्षराणि<BR> Mu. 1; Pt. 4. 38.<BR>—3 To be produced in a court of justice; cf. Ms. 8. 158; Kull.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दर्शनीयमानिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीयमानिन्
दर्शनीय + -मानिन् <i>a.</i> conceited, proud, vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितृ
दर्शयितृ <i>a.</i> [दृश्-णिच्-तृच्]<BR>—1 Showing, exhibiting.<BR>—2 Directing, guiding; पथः श्रुतेर्दर्शयितार ईश्वराः R. 3. 46. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A warder, door-keeper.<BR>—2 A guide (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शित|दर्शितः
दर्शित <i>p. p.</i> [दृश्-णिच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Shown, displayed, manifested, exhibited.<BR>—2 Explained, demonstrated, proved.<BR>—3 Apparent, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शिन्
दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> [दृश्-णिनि] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Seeing, perceiving, viewing, observing, knowing, understanding, showing,<BR> exhibiting; तद्दर्शिनमुदासीनं त्वामेव पुरुषं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">Page0831-2</a>]<BR> विदुः Ku. 2. 13.<BR>—2 Receiving, securing; नृपतिरिव निकाममायदर्शी Mk. 2. 7.<BR>—3 Experiencing; Rām. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षा
दिदृक्षा <i>f.</i> A desire to see; एकस्थसौन्दर्यदिदृक्षयेव Ku. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षु
दिदृक्षु <i>a.</i> Desirous to see; व्यवहारान् दिदृक्षस्तु ब्राह्मणैः<BR> सह पार्थिवः Ms. 8. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Seeing, superintending, surveying, viewing.<BR>—2 Discerning, knowing.<BR>—3 Looking like, appearing. ━(<i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Seeing, viewing, perceiving.<BR>—2 The eye, sight; स दधे दृशमुदग्रतारकाम् R. 11. 69.<BR>—3 Knowledge.<BR>—4 The number ‘two’.<BR>—5 The aspect of a planet.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृगञ्चलः, दृगध्यक्षः, दृक्कर्णः, दृक्कर्मन्, दृक्क्षयः, दृक्क्षेपः, दृग्गविः, दृग्गोचर, दृक्छत्रम्, दृग्जलम्, दृग्ज्या, दृक्तुल्य, दृङ्निमीलनम्, दृक्पथः, दृक्पातः, दृक्प्रसादा, दृक्प्रिया, दृग्भक्तिः, दृग्रुध, दृग्लम्बनम्, दृग्विषः, दृग्वृत्तम्, दृक्छक्तिः, दृक्छ्रुतिः, दृक्संगमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृगञ्चलः|दृगञ्चल
दृश् + -अञ्चलः a side-long glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृगध्यक्षः|दृगध्यक्ष
दृश् + -अध्यक्षः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्कर्णः|दृक्कर्ण
दृश् + -कर्णः a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्कर्मन्|दृक्कर्म्मन्
दृश् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> an operation by which any planet of a certain latitude<BR> is referred to the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्क्षयः|दृक्क्षय
दृश् + -क्षयः decay or loss of sight, becoming dimsighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्क्षेपः|दृक्क्षेप
दृश् + -क्षेपः the sine of the zenith distance of the highest or central<BR> point of the ecliptic at a given time; cf. दृग्ज्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्गविः
दृश् + -गविः the cosine of the zenith distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्गोचर|दृग्गोचरः
दृश् + -गोचर <i>a.</i> visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्गोचरः|दृग्गोचर
दृश् + -गोचर + .({@-रः@}) the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्छत्रम्
दृश् + -छत्रम् an eye-lid; Rāj. T. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्जलम्
दृश् + -जलम् tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्ज्या
दृश् + -ज्या the sine of the zenith-distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्तुल्य
दृश् + -तुल्य <i>a.</i> coincident with observation, or an observed place (in Astr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृङ्निमीलनम्
दृश् + -निमीलनम् a kind of game in which children play hide and seek<BR> (Mar. आंधळी कोशिंवीर)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्पथः|दृक्पथ
दृश् + -पथः the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्पातः|दृक्पात
दृश् + -पातः a look, glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्प्रसादा
दृश् + -प्रसादा a blue stone used for a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्प्रिया
दृश् + -प्रिया beauty, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्भक्तिः|दृग्भक्ति
दृश् + -भक्तिः <i>f.</i> a look of love, an amorous glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्रुध
दृश् + -रुध <i>a.</i> obstructing the sight; Śi. 19. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्लम्बनम्
दृश् + -लम्बनम् vertical parallax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्विषः|दृग्विष
दृश् + -विषः a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्वृत्तम्
दृश् + -वृत्तम् a vertical circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्छक्तिः
दृश् + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> the faculty of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्छ्रुतिः
दृश् + -श्रुतिः a snake, serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्संगमः|दृक्सङ्गम
दृश् + -संगमः the sight of and meeting with; यासां नाम्नापि कामः<BR> स्यात्संगमं दर्शनं विना । तासां दृक्संगमं प्राप्य यन्न द्रवति कौतुकम् ॥<BR> Pt. 4. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशतिः|दृशति
दृशतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Looking, seeing; सूरो न यस्य दृशतिररेपा Rv. 6. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशा
दृशा The eye.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृशाकाङ्क्ष्यम्, दृशोपमम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशाकाङ्क्ष्यम्
दृशा + -आकाङ्क्ष्यम् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशोपमम्
दृशा + -उपमम् a white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशानः|दृशान|दृशानं
दृशानः [दृश्-आनच् किच्च]<BR>—1 A spiritual teacher.<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 A guardian of the world (लोकपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशानम्
दृशानः + .{@-नम्@} Light, brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशालुः|दृशालु
दृशालुः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशिः|दृशि
दृशिः, -शी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The eye; मम दृशिगोचर एष आविरात्मा Bhāg. 1. 9. 41.<BR>—2 A Śāstra.<BR>—3 Light. द्रष्टा दृशिमात्रः शुद्धोऽपि प्रत्ययानुपश्यः Yogadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशी
दृशिः, -शी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The eye; मम दृशिगोचर एष आविरात्मा Bhāg. 1. 9. 41.<BR>—2 A Śāstra.<BR>—3 Light. द्रष्टा दृशिमात्रः शुद्धोऽपि प्रत्ययानुपश्यः Yogadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशिः|दृशि
दृशिः, -शी + .{@-शिः@} <i>f.</i> Seeing, viewing. गोपीदृगुत्सवदृशिः प्रविवेश गोष्ठम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 14. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशीक
दृशीक <i>a.</i> [दृश्-कर्मणि बा˚ ईकक्]<BR>—1 Worthy of regard, fit to be seen, conspicuous.<BR>—2 Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशीका
दृशीक + .{@-का, -कम्@} Appearance, becoming manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशीकम्
दृशीक + .{@-का, -कम्@} Appearance, becoming manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्य|दृश्यं|दृश्यः
दृश्य <i>pot. p.</i> [दृश् कर्मणि क्यप्]<BR>—1 To be seen, visible.<BR>—2 To be looked at.<BR>—3 Beautiful, pleasing to the sight, lovely: निदर्शयामास विशेषदृश्यम्<BR> R. 6. 31; तमेकदृश्यं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">Page0832-1</a>]<BR> नयनैः पिबन्त्यः (नार्यः) Ku. 7. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यः|दृश्य|दृश्यं
दृश्य + .{@-श्यः@} (Arith.) A given quantity or number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यम्
दृश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} A visible object; the visible world; दृश्यं तमसि न<BR> पश्यति दीपेन विना सचक्षुरपि M. 1. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृश्येतर, दृश्यजाति, दृश्यस्थापित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0831-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्येतर
दृश्य + -इतर <i>a.</i> invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यजाति
दृश्य + -जाति (Arith.) reduction of a given quantity with fractions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यस्थापित
दृश्य + -स्थापित <i>a.</i> placed conspicuously; दृश्यस्थापितमृद्दर्भभिक्षाभाण्डमृगाजिनाम् Ks. 24. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्वन्
दृश्वन् <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दृश् क्वनिप्] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Seeing, perceiving.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Familiar or conversant with; as in श्रुतपारदृश्वा R. 5. 24;<BR> विद्यानां पारदृश्वनः 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्ट|दृष्टं
दृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [दृश्-कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Seen, looked, perceived, observed, beheld; उभयोरपि दृष्टोऽन्तः Bg. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Visible, observable.<BR>—3 Regarded, considered; दृष्टो विवृत्य बहुशोऽप्यनया सतृष्णम् Ś. 3. 10.<BR>—4 Occurring, found.<BR>—5 Appearing, manifested.<BR>—6 Known, learned, understood.<BR>—7 Determined, decided, fixed; तदहं यष्टुमिच्छामि शास्त्रदृष्टेन कर्मणा Rām. 1. 8. 9.<BR>—8 Valid.<BR>—9 Allotted.<BR>—10 Experienced, suffered, endured, felt.<BR>—11 Treated of; see दृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टम्
दृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Perception, observation.<BR>—2 Danger from dacoits.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृष्टादृष्ट, दृष्टान्तः, दृष्टान्तम्, दृष्टार्थ, दृष्टकष्ट, दृष्टदुःख, दृष्टकूटम्, दृष्टदोष, दृष्टपृष्ठ, दृष्टप्रत्यय, दृष्टरजस्, दृष्टव्यतिकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टादृष्ट
दृष्ट + -अदृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 seen for the first time.<BR>—2 scarcely or hardly seen.<BR>—3 relating to the present and future life; दृष्टादृष्टक्रियासिद्धिर्न<BR> भवेत्तादृगन्यथा Rāj. T. 1. 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्तः|दृष्टान्त|दृष्टांत
दृष्ट + -अन्तः, -अन्तम्<BR>—1 an example, illustration, parable; पूर्णश्चन्द्रोदयाकाङ्क्षी दृष्टान्तोऽत्र<BR> महार्णवः Śi. 2. 31; साध्यसाधर्म्यात् तद्धर्मभावो दृष्टान्त उदाहरणम् Gautamasūtra.<BR>—2 (in Rhet.) a figure of speech in which an assertion or statement is<BR> illustrated by an example (distinguished from उपमा and प्रतिवस्तूपमा;<BR> see K. P. 10 and R. G. <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR>—3 a Śāstra or science; शोभार्थं विहितास्तत्र न तु दृष्टान्तः कृताः Mb. 2. 3. 13.<BR>—4 death (cf. दिष्टान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्तम्
दृष्ट + -अन्तः, -अन्तम्<BR>—1 an example, illustration, parable; पूर्णश्चन्द्रोदयाकाङ्क्षी दृष्टान्तोऽत्र<BR> महार्णवः Śi. 2. 31; साध्यसाधर्म्यात् तद्धर्मभावो दृष्टान्त उदाहरणम् Gautamasūtra.<BR>—2 (in Rhet.) a figure of speech in which an assertion or statement is<BR> illustrated by an example (distinguished from उपमा and प्रतिवस्तूपमा;<BR> see K. P. 10 and R. G. <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR>—3 a Śāstra or science; शोभार्थं विहितास्तत्र न तु दृष्टान्तः कृताः Mb. 2. 3. 13.<BR>—4 death (cf. दिष्टान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टार्थ
दृष्ट + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the object or meaning obvious or quite apparent.<BR>—2 practical.<BR>—3 having a clear idea about anything. {@˚आपत्तिः@} (see अर्थापत्तिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टकष्ट
दृष्ट + -कष्ट, -दुःख &c. <i>a.</i> one who has experienced or suffered<BR> misery, inured to hardships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टदुःख
दृष्ट + -कष्ट, -दुःख &c. <i>a.</i> one who has experienced or suffered<BR> misery, inured to hardships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टकूटम्
दृष्ट + -कूटम् a riddle, an enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टदोष
दृष्ट + -दोष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 found fault with, considered to be faulty; Ś. 2.<BR>—2 vicious.<BR>—3 exposed, detected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टपृष्ठ
दृष्ट + -पृष्ठ <i>a.</i> running from a battlefield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टप्रत्यय
दृष्ट + -प्रत्यय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having confidence manifested.<BR>—2 convinced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टरजस्
दृष्ट + -रजस् <i>f.</i> a girl arrived at puberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टव्यतिकर
दृष्ट + -व्यतिकर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has experienced a misfortune.<BR>—2 one who foresees evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिः|दृष्टि
दृष्टिः <i>f.</i> [दृश्-भावे-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Seeing, viewing.<BR>—2 Seeing with the mental eye.<BR>—3 Knowing, knowledge; सम्यग्दृष्टिस्तस्य परं पश्यति यस्त्वाम् Ki. 18. 28.<BR>—4 The eye, the faculty of seeing, sight; केनेदानीं दृष्टिं विलोभयामि<BR> V. 2; चलापाङ्गां दृष्टिं स्पृशसि Ś. 1. 23; दृष्टिस्तृणीकृतजगत्त्रयसत्त्वसारा<BR> U. 6. 19; R. 2. 28; Ś. 4. 2; देव दृष्टिप्रसादं कुरु H. 1.<BR>—5 A look, glance.<BR>—6 View, notion; क्षुद्रदृष्टिरेषा K. 173; एतां दृष्टिमवष्टभ्य Bg. 16. 9.<BR>—7 Consideration, regard.<BR>—8 Intellect, wisdom; तुभ्यं नमस्तेऽस्त्वविषक्तदृष्टये Bhāg. 10. 40. 12.<BR>—9 (In Astrol.) Aspect of the stars.<BR>—10 Light (प्रकाश).<BR>—11 A theory, doctrine, notion; याश्च काश्च कृदृष्टयः (सर्वास्ता<BR> निष्फलाः) Ms. 12. 95.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृष्टिकृत्, दृष्टिक्षम, दृष्टिक्षेपः, दृष्टिगतम्, दृष्टिगुणः, दृष्टिगोचर, दृष्टिदानम्, दृष्टिदोषः, दृष्टिपातः, दृष्टिपथः, दृष्टिपूत, दृष्टिप्रसादः, दृष्टिबन्धुः, दृष्टिमण्डलम्, दृष्टिरागः, दृष्टिवादः, दृष्टिविक्षेपः, दृष्टिविद्या, दृष्टिविभ्रमः, दृष्टिविषः, दृष्टिसंभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिकृत्
दृष्टिः + -कृत् <i>n.</i>, {@-कृतम्@}<BR> a kind of lily (स्थलपद्म).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">Page0832-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिक्षम
दृष्टिः + -क्षम worth-seeing; V. 4. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिक्षेपः|दृष्टिक्षेप
दृष्टिः + -क्षेपः a glance, look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगतम्
दृष्टिः + -गतम् a theory, doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगुणः|दृष्टिगुण
दृष्टिः + -गुणः a mark for archers, butt, target.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगोचर|दृष्टिगोचरः
दृष्टिः + -गोचर <i>a.</i> within the range of sight, in sight, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगोचरः|दृष्टिगोचर
दृष्टिः + -गोचर + .({@-रः@}) the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिदानम्
दृष्टिः + -दानम् appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिदोषः|दृष्टिदोष
दृष्टिः + -दोषः the evil influence of the human eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपातः|दृष्टिपात
दृष्टिः + -पातः<BR>—1 a look, glance; मार्गे मृगप्रोक्षिणि दृष्टिपातं कुरुष्व R. 13. 18;<BR> Bh. 1. 11, 94, 3. 66.<BR>—2 act of seeing, function of the eye; रजःकणैर्विध्नितदृष्टिपाताः<BR> Ku. 3. 31 (Malli. interprets −unnecessarily in our opinion− पात by प्रभा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपथः|दृष्टिपथ
दृष्टिः + -पथः the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपूत
दृष्टिः + -पूत <i>a.</i> ‘kept pure by the sight’, watched that no impurity<BR> is contracted; दृष्टिपूतं न्यसेत्पादम् Ms. 6. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिप्रसादः|दृष्टिप्रसाद
दृष्टिः + -प्रसादः the favour of a look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिबन्धुः|दृष्टिबन्धु|दृष्टिबंधु
दृष्टिः + -बन्धुः a firefly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिमण्डलम्
दृष्टिः + -मण्डलम्<BR>—1 the pupil of the eye.<BR>—2 the circle of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिरागः|दृष्टिराग
दृष्टिः + -रागः the expression of the eyes; भवन्तमन्तरेण कीदृशोऽस्या<BR> दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2. 11-12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिवादः|दृष्टिवाद
दृष्टिः + -वादः<BR>—1 a Buddhist canon dealing with discussion on other religious views;<BR> दृष्टिवादो द्वादशाङ्गी स्याद्गणिपिटकाह्वया । प्रतिकर्मसूत्रपूर्वानुयोगो<BR> पूर्वगतचूलिकाः । पञ्च स्युर्दृष्टिवादभेदाः पूर्वाणि चतुर्दशापि पूर्वगते । Hem.<BR>—2 N. of the 12th Aṅga of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविक्षेपः|दृष्टिविक्षेप
दृष्टिः + -विक्षेपः a side-glance, leer, oblique look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविद्या
दृष्टिः + -विद्या optics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविभ्रमः|दृष्टिविभ्रम
दृष्टिः + -विभ्रमः an amorous glance, a coquettish look; Ś. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविषः|दृष्टिविष
दृष्टिः + -विषः a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिसंभेदः|दृष्टिसम्भेद
दृष्टिः + -संभेदः mutual glance; त्वयापि न निरूपिता अनयोर्दृष्टिसंभेदाः Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिन्
दृष्टिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an insight into, or familiar with anything.<BR>—2 Having the looks or thoughts directed upon anything, absorbed in the<BR> contemplation of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशद्
दृशद् <i>f.</i> A stone; see दृषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्
दृषद् <i>f.</i> [दॄ अदि षुक् ह्रस्वश्च; cf. Uṇ. 1. 128]<BR>—1 A rock, large stone, or stone in general; तत्र व्यक्तं दृषदि चरणन्यासमर्धेन्दुमौलेः<BR> Me. 55; R. 4. 74; Bh. 1. 38.<BR>—2 A mill-stone, a flat stone for grinding condiments upon; भित्वा मृषाश्रुर्दृषदश्मना<BR> रहः Bhāg. 10. 9. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दृषदश्मन्, दृषदुपलः, दृषत्सारम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषदश्मन्
दृषद् + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i>, {@-पुत्रः@}<BR> the upper and smaller mill-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषदुपलः|दृषदुपल
दृषद् + -उपलः a grind-stone for grinding condiments upon. (दृषदिमाषकः<BR> a tax raised from mill stones).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषत्सारम्
दृषद् + -सारम् iron; दृषत्सारस्तत्त्वामृतमपि भवाम्भोनिधिगतः Mv. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्वत्|दृषद्वन्त्
दृषद्वत् <i>a.</i> Stony, rocky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्वती
दृषद्वत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 N. of a river flowing into the Sarasvatī and forming the eastern boundary<BR> of the Aryāvarta; cf. Ms. 2. 17.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृह्
दृह्, दृंह् €1 P. (दर्हति, दृंहति)<BR>—1 To be fixed or firm.<BR>—2 To grow, increase.<BR>—3 To prosper.<BR>—4 To fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृंह्
दृह्, दृंह् €1 P. (दर्हति, दृंहति)<BR>—1 To be fixed or firm.<BR>—2 To grow, increase.<BR>—3 To prosper.<BR>—4 To fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दॄ
दॄ I. €4. €9 P. (दीर्यति, दॄणाति, दीर्ण)<BR>—1 To burst or break asunder, split open.<BR>—2 To cause to burst, tear, divide, rend, sunder, pull to pieces. ━<i>Pass.</i> (दीर्यते)<BR>—1 To burst, break open, be sundered; कथमेवं प्रलपतां वः सहस्रधा<BR> न दीर्णमनया जिह्वया Ve. 3.<BR>—2 To separate.<BR>—3 To be afraid, to fear. ━<i>Caus.</i> (द(दा)रयति-ते)<BR>—1 To split, tear asunder, divide by digging.<BR>—2 To disperse, scatter. ━II. €1 P. (दरति) To fear, be afraid of.<BR> (With prepositions like अव, आ, प्र, &c. the root does not change its meaning.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0832-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्ण|दीर्णः
दीर्ण <i>p. p.</i> [दॄ-क्त]<BR>—1 Torn, rent, split &c.<BR>—2 Frightened, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्णम्
दीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@}<BR>—1 Cutting, a rent.<BR>—2 Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दे
दे €1 Ā. (दयते, दात, <i>desid.</i> दित्सते) To protect, cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देदीप्यमान|देदीप्यमानः
देदीप्यमान <i>a.</i> Shining intensely, bright, blazing, resplendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देय|देयं
देय See under दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव्
देव् €1 Ā. (देवते)<BR>—1 To sport, play, gamble.<BR>—2 To lament.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR>—4 To throw, cast. ━<i>With</i> {@परि@} to lament, mourn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव|देवं|देवः
देव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दिव्-अच्]<BR>—1 Divine, celestial; Bg. 11. 11; Ms. 12. 117.<BR>—2 Shining; यज्ञस्य देवमृत्विजम् Rv. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Fit to be worshipped or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवः|देव|देवं
देव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A god, deity; एको देवः केशवो वा शिवो वा Bh. 3. 120.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The god of rain, an epithet of Indra; as in द्वादश वर्षाणि<BR> देवो न ववर्ष; अवर्षयदेवः Rām. 1. 9. 18; काले च देशे च प्रबवर्ष<BR> देवः Bu. C. 2. 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A cloud.<BR>—3 A divine man, Brāhmaṇa, as in भूदेव.<BR>—4 A king, ruler, as in मनुष्यदेव; तां देवसमितिं (अभ्यागच्छत्)<BR> Mb. 3. 130. 22.<BR>—5 A title affixed to the names of Bārhmaṇas; as in गोविन्ददेव, पुरुषोत्तमदेव &c.<BR>—6 (In dramas) A title of honour used in addressing a king, (‘My lord’,<BR> ‘Your majesty’); ततश्च देव Ve. 4; यथाज्ञापयति देवः &c.<BR>—7 Quicksilver.<BR>—8 The Supreme Spirit; हित्वा च देहं प्रविशन्ति देवं दिवौकसो द्यामिव<BR> पार्थ सांख्याः Mb. 12. 301. 112.<BR>—9 A fool<BR>—10 A child.<BR>—11 A man following any particular business.<BR>—12 A lover.<BR>—13 Emulation.<BR>—14 Sport, play.<BR>—15 A husbandʼs brother (cf. देवृ, देवर).<BR>—16 A lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवम्
देव + .{@-वम्@} An organ of sense; देवानां प्रभवो देवो मनसश्च त्रिलोककृत्<BR> Mb. 14. 41. 3. [cf. L. <i>deus</i>; Gr. <i>deos</i>].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देवांशः, देवागारः, देवरम्, देवाङ्गना, देवातिदेवः, देवाधिदेवः, देवाधिपः, देवानीकम्, देवानुचरः, देवानुयायिन्, देवान्धस्, देवाभीष्ट, देवारण्यम्, देवारिः, देवार्चनम्, देवना, देवार्पणम्, देवावसथः, देवाश्वः, देवाक्रीडः, देवाजीवः, देवाजीविन्, देवात्मन्, देवायतनम्, देवायुधम्, देवायुषम्, देवालयः, देवावासः, देवाहारः, देवेज्, देवेज्यः, देवेन्द्रः, देवेष्ट, देवेशः, देवेश्वरः, देवोद्यानम्, देवर्षिः, देवौकस्, देवकन्या, देवकर्दमाः, देवकर्मन्, देवकाष्ठम्, देवकिरी, देवकुटम्, देवकुण्डम्, देवकुलम्, देवकुल्या, देवकुसुमम्, देवखातम्, देवखातकम्, देवगणः, देवगणिका, देवगतिः, देवगन्धर्वः, देवगर्जनम्, देवगर्भः, देवगायनः, देवगान्धारी, देवगिरिः, देवगिरी, देवगुरुः, देवगुही, देवगुह्यम्, देवगृहम्, देवग्रहः, देवचरितम्, देवचर्या, देवचिकित्सकौ, देवच्छन्दः, देवजनः, देवजातम्, देवजामिः, देवतरुः, देवतर्पणम्, देवताडः, देवतातः, देवतातिः, देवतीर्थम्, देवदत्त, देवदर्शन, देवदारु, देवदासः, देवदीपः, देवदुन्दुभिः, देवदूतः, देवदेवः, देवदैवत्य, देवद्रोणी, देवधर्मः, देवधानी, देवधान्यम्, देवधिष्ण्यम्, देवनक्षत्रम्, देवनदी, देवनन्दिन्, देवनागरी, देवनाथः, देवनिकायः, देवनिन्दकः, देवनिन्दा, देवनिर्माल्यम्, देवनिर्मित, देवपतिः, देवपादाः, देवपथः, देवपशुः, देवपात्रम्, देवपुर, देवपुरी, देवपुरोहितः, देवपुष्पम्, देवपूज्यः, देवप्रतिकृतिः, देवप्रश्नः, देवप्रसूत, देवप्रियः, देवबलिः, देवबाहुः, देवब्रह्मन्, देवब्राह्मणः, देवभक्तिः, देवभवनम्, देवभागः, देवभू, देवभूमिः, देवभूतिः, देवभूयम्, देवभृत्, देवभोगः, देवभोज्यम्, देवमणिः, देवमधु, देवमातृ, देवमातृक, देवमानकः, देवमाया, देवमार्गः, देवमासः, देवमुनिः, देवयजनम्, देवयजि, देवयज्ञः, देवयज्यम्, देवयज्या, देवयात्रा, देवयान, देवनः, देवयानम्, देवयुगम्, देवयोनिः, देवयोषा, देवरथः, देवरथम्, देवरहस्यम्, देवराज्, देवराजः, देवरातः, देवराष्ट्रम्, देवलक्ष्मम्, देवलता, देवलिङ्गम्, देवलोकः, देववक्त्रम्, देववर्त्मन्, देववर्धकिः, देवशिल्पिन्, देववाणी, देववाहनः, देवविद्या, देवविभागः, देवविश्, देववीतिः, देववृक्षः, देवव्यचस्, देवव्रतम्, देवव्रतत्वम्, देवशत्रुः, देवशुनी, देवशेखर, देवशेषम्, देवश्रीः, देवश्रुतः, देवसंसद्, देवसत्यम्, देवसंध, देवसभा, देवसभ्यः, देवसहा, देवसायुज्यम्, देवसिंह, देवसुषिः, देवसू, देवसृष्टा, देवसेना, देवस्वम्, देवसावर्णिः, देवहविस्, देवहिंसकः, देवहूः, देवहूतिः, देवहेडनम्, देवहेतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवांशः|देवांश
देव + -अंशः a partial incarnation of god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवागारः|देवागार
देव + -अगारः, -रम् a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरम्
देव + -अगारः, -रम् a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाङ्गना|देवांगना
देव + -अङ्गना a celestial damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवातिदेवः|देवातिदेव
देव + -अतिदेवः, -अधिदेवः<BR>—1 the highest god.<BR>—2 an epithet of (1) Śiva. (2) Buddha. (3) Viṣṇu. देवातिदेवो भगवान्<BR> प्रसूतिरंशे हरिर्यस्य जगत्प्रणेता Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाधिदेवः|देवाधिदेव
देव + -अतिदेवः, -अधिदेवः<BR>—1 the highest god.<BR>—2 an epithet of (1) Śiva. (2) Buddha. (3) Viṣṇu. देवातिदेवो भगवान्<BR> प्रसूतिरंशे हरिर्यस्य जगत्प्रणेता Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाधिपः|देवाधिप
देव + -अधिपः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 the supreme god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवानीकम्
देव + -अनीकम् an army of celestials.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवानुचरः|देवानुचर
देव + -अनुचरः, -अनुयायिन् <i>m.</i> an attendant or follower of a god;<BR> निशम्य देवानुचरस्य वाचं मनुष्यदेवः पुनरप्युवाच R. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवानुयायिन्
देव + -अनुचरः, -अनुयायिन् <i>m.</i> an attendant or follower of a god;<BR> निशम्य देवानुचरस्य वाचं मनुष्यदेवः पुनरप्युवाच R. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवान्धस्|देवांधस्
देव + -अन्धस् <i>n.</i>, {@अन्नम्@}<BR>—1 the food of gods, divine food, ambrosia.<BR>—2 food that has been first offered to an idol; see Ms. 5. 7 and Kull. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाभीष्ट
देव + -अभीष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 liked by or dear to gods.<BR>—2 sacred or dedicated to a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाभीष्टा
देव + -अभीष्ट + .({@-ष्टा@}) piper betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवारण्यम्
देव + -अरण्यम् the garden of gods, the Nandana garden; अलमुद्द्योतयामासुर्देवारण्यमिवर्तवः R. 10. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवारिः|देवारि
देव + -अरिः a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवार्चनम्
देव + -अर्चनम्, -ना<BR>—1 the worship of gods.<BR>—2 idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवना
देव + -अर्चनम्, -ना<BR>—1 the worship of gods.<BR>—2 idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवार्पणम्
देव + -अर्पणम्<BR>—1 an offering to the god.<BR>—2 the Veda; पृथग्भूतानि चान्यानि यानि देवार्पणानि च Mb. 13. 86. 17 (see com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवावसथः|देवावसथ
देव + -आवसथः a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाश्वः|देवाश्व
देव + -अश्वः an epithet of उच्चैः श्रवस्, the horse of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाक्रीडः|देवाक्रीड
देव + -आक्रीडः ‘the garden of the gods’, Nandana garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाजीवः|देवाजीव
देव + -आजीवः, -आजीविन् <i>m.</i> an attendant upon an idol.<BR>—2 a low Brāhmaṇa subsisting by attendance upon an idol and upon the<BR> offerings made to it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाजीविन्
देव + -आजीवः, -आजीविन् <i>m.</i> an attendant upon an idol.<BR>—2 a low Brāhmaṇa subsisting by attendance upon an idol and upon the<BR> offerings made to it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवात्मन्
देव + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 consecrated, holy, sacred.<BR>—2 of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">Page0833-2</a>]<BR> divine nature. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the divine soul; ते ध्यानयोगानुगता ऽपश्यन् देवात्मशक्तिं स्वगुणैर्निगूढाम्<BR> Śvet. Up. 1. 3.<BR>—2 the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायतनम्
देव + -आयतनम् a temple; Ms. 4. 46; न देवायतनं गच्छेत् कदाचिद्<BR> वाऽप्रदक्षिणम् । न पीडयेद् वा वस्त्राणि न देवायतनेष्वपि ॥ Kūrma P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायुधम्
देव + -आयुधम्<BR>—1 a divine weapon.<BR>—2 rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायुषम्
देव + -आयुषम् the life-time of a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवालयः|देवालय
देव + -आलयः<BR>—1 heaven.<BR>—2 a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवावासः|देवावास
देव + -आवासः<BR>—1 heaven.<BR>—2 the holy fig-tree (अश्वत्थ).<BR>—3 a temple.<BR>—4 the Sumeru mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाहारः|देवाहार
देव + -आहारः nectar, ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेज्
देव + -इज् <i>a.</i> (nom. sing. देवेट्-ड्) worshipping the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेज्यः|देवेज्य
देव + -इज्यः an epithet of Bṛhaspati, preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेन्द्रः|देवेन्द्र|देवेंद्र
देव + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेष्ट|देवेष्टः
देव + -इष्ट <i>a.</i> dear to gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेष्टः|देवेष्ट
देव + -इष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@}) bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेष्टा
देव + -इष्ट + .({@-ष्टा@}) the wild lime tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेशः|देवेश
देव + -ईशः an epithet of (1) Indra. (2) Śiva. (3) Viṣṇu. (4) Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेशी
देव + -ईशः + .({@-शी@}) N. of Durgā; also of Devakī, mother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेश्वरः|देवेश्वर
देव + -ईश्वरः N. of (1) Śiva. (2) Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवोद्यानम्
देव + -उद्यानम्<BR>—1 divine garden.<BR>—2 the Nandana garden.<BR>—3 a garden near a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर्षिः|देवर्षि
देव + -ऋषिः (देवर्षिः)<BR>—1 a deified saint, divine sage such as अत्रि, भृगु, पुलस्त्य, अङ्गिरस्<BR> &c.; एवंवादिनि देवर्षौ Ku. 6. 84 (<i>i. e.</i> अङ्गिरस्); अथ देवऋषी<BR> राजन् संपरेतं नृपात्मजम् Bhāg.; आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोका देवर्षिपितृमानवाः ।<BR> तृप्यन्तु पितरः सर्वे मातृमातामहादयाः Tarpaṇamantra.<BR>—2 an epithet of Narada; देवर्षीणां च नारदः Bg. 10. 13, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवौकस्
देव + -ओकस् <i>n.</i> the mountain Meru or Sumeru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकन्या
देव + -कन्या a celestial damsel, a nymph; also देवकन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकर्दमाः
देव + -कर्दमाः sandal, aloe wood, camphor, saffron pounded together<BR> and made into a paste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकर्मन्
देव + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-कार्यम्@}<BR>—1 a religious act or rite, divine command; अनुष्ठितदेवकार्यम् R. 12. 103.<BR>—2 the worship of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकाष्ठम्
देव + -काष्ठम् the Devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकिरी
देव + -किरी N. of a Rāgiṇi; ललिता मालती गौरी नाटी देवकिरी तथा ।<BR> मेघरागस्य रागिण्यो भवन्तीमाः सुमध्यमाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुटम्
देव + -कुटम् a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुण्डम्
देव + -कुण्डम् a natural spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुलम्
देव + -कुलम्<BR>—1 a temple.<BR>—2 a race of gods.<BR>—3 a group of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुल्या
देव + -कुल्या the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुसुमम्
देव + -कुसुमम् cloves; एलां च देवकुसुमं त्वक्पत्रं देवदारु च<BR> Śiva B. 30. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातम्
देव + -खातम्, -खातकम्<BR>—1 a natural hollow among mountains.<BR>—2 a natural pond or reservoir; Ms. 4. 203.<BR>—3 a pond near a temple. ˚बिल a cavern, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातकम्
देव + -खातम्, -खातकम्<BR>—1 a natural hollow among mountains.<BR>—2 a natural pond or reservoir; Ms. 4. 203.<BR>—3 a pond near a temple. ˚बिल a cavern, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगणः|देवगण
देव + -गणः a class of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगणिका
देव + -गणिका an <i>apsaras</i>; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगतिः
देव + -गतिः the path of देवलोक; अनुज्ञातश्च रामेण ययौ देवगतिं<BR> मुनिः A. Rām. 2. 1. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगन्धर्वः|देवगन्धर्व
देव + -गन्धर्वः an epithet of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगन्धर्वम्
देव + -गन्धर्वः + .({@-र्वम्@}) a particular mode of singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगर्जनम्
देव + -गर्जनम् thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगर्भः|देवगर्भ
देव + -गर्भः see हिरण्यगर्भ; Rām. 2. 40. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगायनः|देवगायन
देव + -गायनः a celestial chorister, a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगान्धारी
देव + -गान्धारी N. of a Rāgiṇī; गान्धारी देवगान्धारी मालवी श्रीश्च<BR> सारवी । रामकीर्यपि रागिण्यः श्रीरागस्य प्रिया इमाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगिरिः|देवगिरि
देव + -गिरिः<BR>—1 N. of a mountain; cf. Me. 44.<BR>—2 N. of a town (Daulatabad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगिरी
देव + -गिरी <i>f.</i> N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगुरुः|देवगुरु
देव + -गुरुः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kaśyapa (the father of gods).<BR>—2 of Bṛhaspati (the preceptor of gods).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगुही
देव + -गुही an epithet of Sarasvatī or of a place situated on it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगुह्यम्
देव + -गुह्यम्<BR>—1 a secret only known by gods.<BR>—2 death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगृहम्
देव + -गृहम्<BR>—1 a temple.<BR>—2 the place of a king.<BR>—3 a planetary sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवग्रहः|देवग्रह
देव + -ग्रहः a class of demons who causes harmless madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवचरितम्
देव + -चरितम् the course of action or practices of the gods; न देवचरितं चरेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवचर्या|देवचर्य्या
देव + -चर्या the worship or service of gods.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">Page0834-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0833-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवचिकित्सकौ
देव + -चिकित्सकौ (du.) Aśvins, the twin physicians of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवच्छन्दः|देवच्छन्द|देवच्छंद
देव + -छन्दः a pearl-necklace having 81, 100 or 108 strings; शतमष्टयुतं<BR> हारो देवच्छन्दो ह्यशीतिरेकयुता Bṛ. S. 81. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजनः|देवजन
देव + -जनः the gods collectively. ˚विद्या the science of music,<BR> dance, other arts &c.; Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजातम्
देव + -जातम् a class of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजामिः|देवजामि
देव + -जामिः <i>f.</i> a sister of the gods; देवजामीनां पुत्रोऽसि Av. 6. 46. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतरुः|देवतरु
देव + -तरुः<BR>—1 the holy fig-tree.<BR>—2 one of the trees of paradise. (<i>i. e.</i> मन्दार, पारिजात, सन्तान,<BR> कल्प and हरिचन्दन); पञ्चैते देवतरवो मन्दारः पारिजातकः ।<BR> सन्तानः कल्पवृक्षश्च पुंसि वा हरिचन्दनम् ॥ Ak.<BR>—3 the tree in a village (चैत्यवृक्ष) where the villagers usually<BR> meet (Mar. पार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतर्पणम्
देव + -तर्पणम् offerings of water, part of the सन्ध्या ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताडः|देवताड
देव + -ताडः<BR>—1 fire.<BR>—2 an epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतातः|देवतात
देव + -तातः<BR>—1 a sacrifice.<BR>—2 N. of Kaśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतातिः|देवताति
देव + -तातिः<BR>—1 a god.<BR>—2 divine service; स नो यक्षद् देवताता यजीयान् Rv. 3. 19. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतीर्थम्
देव + -तीर्थम्<BR>—1 the right moment for the worship of gods.<BR>—2 the tips of the fingers sacred to gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्त|देवदत्तः
देव + -दत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 god-given, granted by the gods.<BR>—2 given to the gods (as a village, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्तः|देवदत्त
देव + -दत्त + .({@-त्तः@})<BR>—1 N. of the conch-shell of Arjuna; देवदत्तं धनञ्जयः (दध्मौ) Bg. 1. 15.<BR>—2 a certain person (used in speaking of men indefinitely); मुक्तस्ततो<BR> यदि बन्धाद्देवदत्त उपाच्छिनत्ति Bhāg. 5. 14. 24; देवदत्तः पचति,<BR> पीनो देवदत्तो दिवा न भुङ्क्ते &c.<BR>—3 one of the vital airs exhaled in yawning; देवदत्तो विजृम्भणे.<BR> ˚अग्रजः N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदर्शन|देवदर्शनः
देव + -दर्शन <i>a.</i> visiting the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदर्शनः|देवदर्शन
देव + -दर्शन + .({@-नः@}) N. of Nārada; यथा प्राह नारदो देवदर्शनः Bhāg. 2. 8. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदारु|देवदारुः
देव + -दारु <i>m., n.</i> a species of pine; गङ्गाप्रवाहोक्षितदेवदारु<BR> Ku. 1. 54; R. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदासः|देवदास
देव + -दासः a servant or attendant upon a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदासी
देव + -दासः + .({@-सी@})<BR>—1 a female in the service of gods or a temple.<BR>—2 a courtezan (employed as a dancer in a temple).<BR>—3 the wild citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदीपः|देवदीप
देव + -दीपः the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदुन्दुभिः|देवदुन्दुभि|देवदुंदुभि
देव + -दुन्दुभिः<BR>—1 divine drum; देवदुन्दुभिनिर्घोषो पुष्पवृष्टिश्च खात् पतन् Rām.<BR>—2 the holy basil with red flowers. —3 an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदूतः|देवदूत
देव + -दूतः a divine envoy or messenger, an angel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदेवः|देवदेव
देव + -देवः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman; Rām. 1. 43. 1.<BR>—2 of Śiva; अयाचितारं न हि देवदेवमद्रिः सुतां ग्राहयितुं शशाक Ku. 1. 52.<BR>—3 of Viṣṇu; Bg. 10. 15.<BR>—4 of Gaṇeśa; दृष्टप्रभावो वरदो देवदेवो विनायकः Ks. 20. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदैवत्य
देव + -दैवत्य <i>a.</i> destined for the god; Ms. 2. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवद्रोणी
देव + -द्रोणी a procession with idols.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधर्मः|देवधर्म
देव + -धर्मः a religious duty or office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधानी
देव + -धानी the city of Indra; तां देवधानीं स वरुथिनीपतिर्बहिः<BR> समन्ताद्रुरुधे पृतन्यया Bhāg. 8. 15. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधान्यम्
देव + -धान्यम् a kind of grass-grain (Mar. देवभात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधिष्ण्यम्
देव + -धिष्ण्यम् a chariot of the gods (विमान); Bhāg. 10. 82. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनक्षत्रम्
देव + -नक्षत्रम् N. of the first 14 नक्षत्रs in the southern quarter<BR> (opp. to यमनक्षत्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनदी
देव + -नदी<BR>—1 the Ganges.<BR>—2 any holy river; Ms. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनन्दिन्|देवनंदिन्
देव + -नन्दिन् <i>m.</i> N. of the door-keeper of Indra.<BR>—2 N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनागरी
देव + -नागरी N. of the character in which Sanskrit is usually written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनाथः|देवनाथ
देव + -नाथः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिकायः|देवनिकाय
देव + -निकायः<BR>—1 ‘residence of gods’, paradise, heaven; तं तुष्टुवुर्देवनिकायकेतवः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 27. 25.<BR>—2 a host or assembly of gods; Ms. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दकः|देवनिन्दक|देवनिंदक
देव + -निन्दकः a blasphemer, unbeliever, heretic, atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दा
देव + -निन्दा heresy, atheism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिर्माल्यम्
देव + -निर्माल्यम् —1 a garland remaining from a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिर्मित|देवनिर्म्मित
देव + -निर्मित <i>a.</i> ‘god-created’, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपतिः|देवपति
देव + -पतिः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपादाः
देव + -पादाः ‘the royal feet or presence’, an honorific<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">Page0834-2</a>]<BR> term for a king; देवपादाः प्रमाणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपथः|देवपथ
देव + -पथः<BR>—1 ‘heavenly passage’, heaven, firmament दिव्यो देवपथो ह्येष नात्र<BR> गच्छन्ति मानुषाः Mb.<BR>—2 the milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपशुः|देवपशु
देव + -पशुः any animal consecrated to a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपात्रम्
देव + -पात्रम् an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुर
देव + -पुर, -पुरी <i>f.</i> an epithet of Amarāvatī, the city of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुरी
देव + -पुर, -पुरी <i>f.</i> an epithet of Amarāvatī, the city of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुरोहितः|देवपुरोहित
देव + -पुरोहितः<BR>—1 a domestic priest of the gods.<BR>—2 the planet Jupiter (बृहस्पति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुष्पम्
देव + -पुष्पम् cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपूज्यः|देवपूज्य
देव + -पूज्यः an epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रतिकृतिः|देवप्रतिकृति
देव + -प्रतिकृतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-प्रतिमा@}<BR> an idol, the image of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रश्नः|देवप्रश्न
देव + -प्रश्नः ‘consulting deities’, astrology, fortune-telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रसूत
देव + -प्रसूत <i>a.</i> good-produced (water); Av. 6. 100. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रियः|देवप्रिय
देव + -प्रियः ‘dear to the gods’, an epithet of Śiva; (देवानांप्रियः<BR> an irreg. comp. meaning<BR>—1 a goat.<BR>—2 a fool, idiot like a brute breast, as in तेऽप्यतात्पर्यज्ञा देवानांप्रियाः K. P.<BR>—3 an ascetic, who renounces the world).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवबलिः|देवबलि
देव + -बलिः an oblation to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवबाहुः|देवबाहु
देव + -बाहुः<BR>—1 N. of a king in the Yadu race.<BR>—2 N. of a sage; देवबाहुः शतधनुः कृतवर्मेति तत्सुताः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्रह्मन्
देव + -ब्रह्मन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्राह्मणः|देवब्राह्मण
देव + -ब्राह्मणः<BR>—1 a Brāhmaṇa who lives on the proceeds of a temple.<BR>—2 a venerable Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभक्तिः|देवभक्ति
देव + -भक्तिः worship or service of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभवनम्
देव + -भवनम्<BR>—1 the heaven.<BR>—2 a temple.<BR>—3 the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभागः|देवभाग
देव + -भागः the northern hemisphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभू
देव + -भू <i>m.</i> a god. ━(<i>f.</i>) heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूमिः|देवभूमि
देव + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> heaven; पितुः प्रदेशास्तव देवभूमयः Ku. 5. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूतिः|देवभूति
देव + -भूतिः <i>f.</i> an epithet of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूयम्
देव + -भूयम् divinity, godhead; विदितमेव भवतां … … परां<BR> निर्वृतिमुपेत्य देवभूयं गताः सर्वे न पूर्वपुरुषा इति Rāmāyaṇachampū<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभृत्
देव + -भृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभोगः|देवभोग
देव + -भोगः pleasure of the gods, heavenly joy; अश्रन्ति दिव्यान् दिवि<BR> देवभोगान् Bg. 9. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभोज्यम्
देव + -भोज्यम् nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमणिः|देवमणि
देव + -मणिः<BR>—1 the jewel of Viṣṇu called कौस्तुभ.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR>—3 a curl of hair on a horseʼs neck; आवर्तिनः शुभफलप्रदशुक्तियुक्ताः<BR> संपन्नदेवमणयो भृतरन्ध्रभागाः (अश्वाः) Śi. 5. 4; N. 1. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमधु
देव + -मधु <i>n.</i> divine honey; असौ वा आदित्यो देवमधु Ch. Up. 3. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृ
देव + -मातृ <i>f.</i> N. of Aditi, mother of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृक|देवमातृकः
देव + -मातृक <i>a.</i> ‘having the god of rain or clouds as foster-mother’,<BR> watered only by the clouds, depending on rain-water and not on irrigation,<BR> deprived of every other kind of water (as a country); देशो नद्यम्बुवृष्टपम्बुसंपन्नव्रीहिपालितः ।<BR> स्यान्नदीमातृको देवमातृकश्च यथाकमम् ॥ Ak.; cf. also वितन्वति<BR> क्षेममदेवमातृकाः (<i>i. e.</i> नदीमातृकाः) चिराय तस्मिन् कुरवश्चकासते Ki. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमानकः|देवमानक
देव + -मानकः the jewel of Viṣṇu called कौस्तुभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमाया
देव + -माया the Māyā of gods; ते दुस्तरामतितरन्ति च देवमायाम् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमार्गः|देवमार्ग
देव + -मार्गः the air or sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमासः|देवमास
देव + -मासः the eighth month of pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमुनिः|देवमुनि
देव + -मुनिः a divine sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजनम्
देव + -यजनम्<BR>—1 a sacrificial place, a place where a sacrifice is performed; ततस्ते<BR> देवयजनं ब्राह्मणाः स्वर्णलाङ्गलैः (कृष्ट्वा) Bhāg. 10. 74. 12.<BR> देवयजनसंभवे सीते U. 4.<BR>—2 a place of worship; मण्डलं देवयजनं दीक्षासंस्कार आत्मनः<BR> Bhāg. 12. 11. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजि|देवयजिः
देव + -यजि <i>a.</i> making oblations to gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्ञः|देवयज्ञ
देव + -यज्ञः a sacrifice to the superior gods made by oblations to<BR> fire, or through fire to the gods; (one of the five daily sacrifices of<BR> a Brāhmaṇa; see Ms. 3. 81, 85 and पञ्चयज्ञ also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्यम्
देव + -यज्यम्, -यज्या a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्या
देव + -यज्यम्, -यज्या a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयात्रा
देव + -यात्रा ‘an idol-procession’, any sacred festival when the idols<BR> are carried in procession; केनापि देवयात्रागतेन सिद्धादेशेन साधुना<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">Page0835-1</a>]<BR> मत्समक्षमादिष्टा M. 5. 12-13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0834-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयान|देवयानं
देव + -यान bestowing मोक्ष; यज्ञस्य देवयानस्य मेध्याय हविषे नृप<BR> Bhāg. 8. 8. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनः|देवन|देवनं
देव + -नः the path leading to मोक्ष; सत्येन पन्था विततो देवयानः<BR> Muṇḍ. 3. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयानम्
देव + -यानम् a celestial car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयुगम्
देव + -युगम्<BR>—1 the first of the four ages of the world; also called कृतयुग, सनत्कुमारो<BR> भगवान् पुरा देवयुगे प्रभुः Rām. 1. 11. 11.<BR>—2 an age of the gods comprising four ages of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोनिः|देवयोनि
देव + -योनिः<BR>—1 a superhuman being, a demigod; विद्याधरोऽप्सरोयक्षरक्षोगन्धर्वकिन्नराः ।<BR> पिशाचो गुह्यकः सिद्धो भूतोऽमी देवयोनयः ॥ Ak.<BR>—2 a being of divine origin.<BR>—3 fuel used in kindling fire (<i>f.</i> also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोषा
देव + -योषा an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरथः|देवरथ
देव + -रथः a car for carrying the image of god in procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरथम्
देव + -रथम् a dayʼs journey for the sunʼs chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरहस्यम्
देव + -रहस्यम् a divine mystery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज्
देव + -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra; Rām. 7. 6. 6.<BR>—2 a king.<BR>—3 N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराजः|देवराज
देव + -राज्, -राजः<BR>—1 an epithet of Indra; Rām. 7. 6. 6.<BR>—2 a king.<BR>—3 N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरातः|देवरात
देव + -रातः<BR>—1 an epithet of Parīkṣit. —2 a kind of swan or crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराष्ट्रम्
देव + -राष्ट्रम् N. of an empire in the Deccan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलक्ष्मम्
देव + -लक्ष्मम् the Brāhmanical cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलता
देव + -लता the Navamallikā or double jasmine plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलिङ्गम्
देव + -लिङ्गम् the image or statue of a deity; Bhāg. 3. 17. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलोकः|देवलोक
देव + -लोकः heaven, paradise; देवलोकस्य चर्त्विजः (प्रभुः) Ms. 4. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववक्त्रम्
देव + -वक्त्रम् an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर्त्मन्
देव + -वर्त्मन् <i>n.</i> the sky or atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर्धकिः|देववर्धकि|देववर्द्धकिः
देव + -वर्धकिः, -शिल्पिन् <i>m.</i> Viśvakarman, the architect of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशिल्पिन्
देव + -वर्धकिः, -शिल्पिन् <i>m.</i> Viśvakarman, the architect of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववाणी
देव + -वाणी ‘divine voice’, a voice from heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववाहनः|देववाहन
देव + -वाहनः an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवविद्या
देव + -विद्या —1 divine science; Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR>—2 the science of Nirukta or etymology; <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवविभागः|देवविभाग
देव + -विभागः the northern hemisphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवविश्
देव + -विश् <i>f.</i>, {@-विशा@}<BR> a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववीतिः|देववीति
देव + -वीतिः food of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववृक्षः|देववृक्ष
देव + -वृक्षः the Mandāra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्यचस्
देव + -व्यचस् <i>a.</i> Ved. occupied by the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रतम्
देव + -व्रतम्<BR>—1 a religious observance, any religious vow. —2 the favourite food of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रतः|देवव्रत
देव + -व्रतम् + .({@-तः@}) an epithet of 1 Bhīṣma; ततो विनशनं प्रागाद्यत्र<BR> देवव्रतोऽपतत् Bhāg. 1. 9. 1.<BR>—2 Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रतत्वम्
देव + -व्रतत्वम् celibacy (ब्रह्मचारिव्रत); देवव्रतत्वं विज्ञाप्य<BR> Mb. 5. 172. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशत्रुः|देवशत्रु
देव + -शत्रुः a demon; स देवशत्रूनिव देवराजः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशुनी
देव + -शुनी an epithet of Saramā, the bitch of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशेखर|देवशेखरः
देव + -शेखर the <i>damanaka</i> tree (Mar. दवणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवशेषम्
देव + -शेषम् the remnants of a sacrifice offered to gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रीः
देव + -श्रीः <i>m.</i> a sacrifice. (<i>f.</i>) Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रुतः|देवश्रुत
देव + -श्रुतः an epithet of<BR>—1 Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Nārada.<BR>—3 a sacred treatise.<BR>—4 a god in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसंसद्
देव + -संसद् <i>f.</i> देवसभा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसत्यम्
देव + -सत्यम् divine truth, established order of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसंध|देवसन्ध
देव + -संध <i>a.</i> divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभा
देव + -सभा<BR>—1 an assembly of the gods (सुधर्मन्).<BR>—2 a council of a king, council-chamber.<BR>—3 a gambling-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभ्यः|देवसभ्य
देव + -सभ्यः<BR>—1 a gambler.<BR>—2 a frequenter of gaming-houses.<BR>—3 an attendant on a deity.<BR>—4 the keeper of a gambling-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसहा
देव + -सहा<BR>—1 rules of begging alms (? भिक्षासूत्र); L. D. B.<BR>—2 N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसायुज्यम्
देव + -सायुज्यम् identification or unification with a deity, conjunction<BR> with the gods, deification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसिंह
देव + -सिंह an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसुषिः|देवसुषि
देव + -सुषिः a tube or cavity (in the heart) leading to the gods; cf.<BR> उदान; तस्य ह वा एतस्य हृदयस्य पञ्च देवसुषयः Ch. Up. 3. 13. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसू
देव + -सू N. of 8 deities (अग्नि, सोम, सवितृ, रुद्र, बृहस्पति, इन्द्र,<BR> मित्र and वरुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसृष्टा
देव + -सृष्टा an intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेना
देव + -सेना<BR>—1 the army of gods.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Skanda; स्कन्देन साक्षादिव देवसेनाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">Page0835-2</a>]<BR> R. 7. 1 (Malli.:− देवसेना = स्कन्दपत्नी; perhaps it merely means<BR> ‘the army of the gods’ personified as Skandaʼs wife). ˚पतिः, ˚प्रियः<BR> an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवस्वम्
देव + -स्वम् ‘property of gods’, property applicable to religious purposes<BR> or endowments; यद्धनं यज्ञशीलानां देवस्वं तद्विदुर्बुधाः Ms. 11. 20, 26.<BR> ˚अपहरणम् sacrilege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसावर्णिः|देवसावर्णि
देव + -सावर्णिः the 13th Manu; मनुस्त्रयोदशो भाव्यो देवसावर्णिरात्मवान्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 13. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवहविस्
देव + -हविस् <i>n.</i> an animal offered to gods at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

