देवद्र्यञ्च्|देवद्र्यंच्
देवद्र्यञ्च्^1 <i>a.</i> (-द्रीची <i>f.</i>)<BR> Adoring a deity.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: virama missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन्
देवन् <i>m.</i> The younger brother of a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनः|देवन|देवनं
देवनः [दीव्यत्यनेन दिव् करणे ल्युट्] A die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनम्
देवनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Beauty, splendour, lustre.<BR>—2 Gaming, gambling, a game at dice; प्रकाशमेतत्तास्कर्यं यद्देवनसमाह्वयौ Ms. 9. 222.<BR>—3 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>—4 A pleasure-ground, a garden.<BR>—5 A lotus.<BR>—6 Emulation, desire to excel.<BR>—7 Affair, business.<BR>—8 Praise.<BR>—9 Going, motion.<BR>—10 Grief, lamentation, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवना
देवनः + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 Gambling, a game at dice.<BR>—2 Sport, pastime.<BR>—3 Lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयानी
देवयानी N. of the daughter of Śukra, preceptor of the <i>Asuras</i>.<BR> [She fell in love with Kacha, her fatherʼs pupil, but he rejected her<BR> advances. On this she cursed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">Page0836-1</a>]<BR> the youth, who in return cursed her that she should become the wife of<BR> a Kṣatriya (See कच.) Once upon a time Devayānī and her companion<BR> Śarmiṣṭhā, the daughter of Vṛṣaparvan, the king of the Daityas,<BR> went to bathe keeping their clothes on the shore. But the god Wind changed<BR> their clothes, and when they were dressed they began to quarrel about<BR> the change until Śarmiṣṭhā, so far lost her temper that she, slapped<BR> Devayānīʼs face, and threw her into a well. There she remained until<BR> she was seen and rescued by Yayāti, who, with the consent of her father,<BR> married her, and Śarmiṣṭhā became her servant as a recompense for<BR> her insulting conduct towards her. Devayānī lived happily with Yayāti<BR> for some years and bore him two sons, Yadu and Turvasu. Subsequently her<BR> husband became enamoured of Śarmiṣṭhā, and Devayānī, feeling herself<BR> aggrieved, abruptly left her husband and went home to her father, who<BR> at her request condemned Yayāti with the infirmity of old age; see Yayāti also.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0835-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयु|देवयुः
देवयु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pious, holy, virtuous.<BR>—2 Attending sacred festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयुः|देवयु
देवयु + .{@-युः@} A god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरः|देवर
देवरः<BR>—1 A husbandʼs brother (elder or younger); Ms. 3. 55, 9. 59; अपुत्रां<BR> गुर्वनुज्ञातो देवरः पुत्रकाम्यया (इयात्) Y. 1. 68.<BR>—2 husband; का देवरं वशगतं कुसुमास्त्रवेगविस्रस्तपौस्नमुशती<BR> न भजेत कृत्ये Bhāg. 4. 26. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलः|देवल
देवलः<BR>—1 An attendant upon an idol, a low Brāhmaṇa who subsists upon the offerings<BR> made to an idol; … … देवलाश्च कृषीवलाः Śiva B. 31. 20.<BR>—2 A virtuous man.<BR>—3 N. of Nārada.<BR>—4 A husbandʼs brother.<BR>—5 N. of a law-giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलकः|देवलक
देवलकः An attendant upon an idol; see the preceding word; द्रव्यं<BR> देवलका हरन्त्यचकिताः Viś. Guṇā. 466.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाटः|देवाट
देवाटः N. of a sacred place called Harihara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाला
देवाला <i>f.</i> N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसात्
देवसात् <i>ind.</i> To the nature of a god or gods. (˚भू to be changed<BR> into a god; हता वा देवसाद्भूत्वा लोकान् प्राप्स्यथ पुष्कलान् Mb.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविक
देविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), देविल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Divine, godly.<BR>—2 Derived from a god.<BR>—3 Virtuous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविकी
देविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), देविल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Divine, godly.<BR>—2 Derived from a god.<BR>—3 Virtuous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविल|देविलः
देविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), देविल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Divine, godly.<BR>—2 Derived from a god.<BR>—3 Virtuous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवितव्य
देवितव्य <i>a.</i> To be gambled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवितव्यम्
देवितव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} Gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवितृ
देवितृ, देविन् <i>m.</i> A gamester; Mb. 3. 252. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविन्
देवितृ, देविन् <i>m.</i> A gamester; Mb. 3. 252. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविल|देविलः
देविल <i>a.</i> Righteous, virtuous, divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवी
देवी<BR>—1 A female deity, a goddess.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR>—3 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>—4 N. of Sāvitrī.<BR>—5 A queen, especially a crowned queen (अग्रमहिषी who has undergone<BR> the consecration along with her husband); प्रेष्यभावेन नामेयं देवीशब्दक्षमा<BR> सती । स्नायीयवस्त्रक्रियया पत्त्रोर्णं वोपयुज्यते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">Page0836-2</a>]<BR> M. 5. 12; देवीभावं गमिता परिवारपदं कथं भजत्येषा K. P. 10.<BR>—6 A respectful title applied to a lady of the first rank.<BR>—7 A kind of bird (श्यामा).<BR>—8 A particular supernatural power (कुण्डलिनी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देवीकोटः, देवीगृहम्, देवीपुराणम्, देवीभागवतम्, देवीभावः, देवीसूक्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीकोटः|देवीकोट
देवी + -कोटः<BR>—1 the city of Bāṇa (शोणितपुर).<BR>—2 Devikotta (on the Coromandel coast).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीगृहम्
देवी + -गृहम्<BR>—1 the temple of a goddess.<BR>—2 the apartment of a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीपुराणम्
देवी + -पुराणम् N. of an Upapurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीभागवतम्
देवी + -भागवतम् N. of an Upapurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीभावः|देवीभाव
देवी + -भावः the dignity of a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीसूक्तम्
देवी + -सूक्तम् a Sūkta addressed to Devī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवृ
देवृ <i>m.</i> [दिव्-ऋ]<BR>—1 A husbandʼs brother (especially younger).<BR>—2 The husband of a woman previously married (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेशयः|देवेशय
देवेशयः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव्यम्
देव्यम् Divine dignity, god-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवटः|देवट
देवटः An artisan, a mechanic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशः|देश
देशः [दिश्-अच्]<BR>—1 A place or spot in general; देशः को नु जलावसेकशिथिलः Mk. 3. 12<BR> (often used after words like कपोल, स्कन्ध, अंस, नितम्ब &c.,<BR> without any meaning; स्कन्धदेशे Ś. 1. 19 ‘on the shoulder’).<BR>—2 A region, country, province, land, territory; यं देशं श्रयते तमेव<BR> कुरुते बाहुप्रतापार्जितम् H. 1. 150.<BR>—3 A department, part, side, portion (as of a whole); as in एकदेश,<BR> एकदेशीय q. v.<BR>—4 An institute, an ordinance.<BR>—5 Range, compass; दृष्टिदेशः Pt. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देशाटनम्, देशातिथिः, देशान्तरम्, देशान्तरिन्, देशाचारः, देशधर्मः, देशकण्टकः, देशकारी, देशकालौ, देशकालज्ञ, देशच्युतिः, देशज, देशजात, देशदृष्ट, देशभाषा, देशरूपम्, देशविद्ध, देशवृत्तम्, देशव्यवहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशाटनम्
देशः + -अटनम् roaming through a country, travelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशातिथिः|देशातिथि
देशः + -अतिथिः a foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशान्तरम्
देशः + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 another country, foreign parts; Ms. 5. 78.<BR>—2 longitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशान्तरिन्
देशः + -अन्तरिन् <i>m.</i> a foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशाचारः|देशाचार
देशः + -आचारः, -धर्मः a local law or custom, the usage or custom of<BR> any country; देशधर्मान् जातिधर्मान् कुलधर्मांश्च शाश्वतान् Ms. 1. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशधर्मः|देशधर्म|देशधर्म्म
देशः + -आचारः, -धर्मः a local law or custom, the usage or custom of<BR> any country; देशधर्मान् जातिधर्मान् कुलधर्मांश्च शाश्वतान् Ms. 1. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकण्टकः|देशकण्टक
देशः + -कण्टकः a public calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकारी
देशः + -कारी N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालौ
देशः + -कालौ <i>m.</i> (du.) time and place; न देशकालौ हि यथार्थधर्माववेक्षते<BR> कामरतिर्मनुष्यः Rām. 4. 33. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालम्
देशः + -कालौ + .({@-लम्@}) <i>ind.</i> according to time and place; सत्पात्रं महती<BR> श्रद्धा देशकालं यथोचितम् Pt. 2. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालज्ञ
देशः + -कालज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the proper place and time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशच्युतिः|देशच्युति
देशः + -च्युतिः banishment or flight from oneʼs country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशज
देशः + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 native, indigenous.<BR>—2 produced in the right country.<BR>—3 genuine, of genuine descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशजात
देशः + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 native, indigenous.<BR>—2 produced in the right country.<BR>—3 genuine, of genuine descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशदृष्ट
देशः + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 seen in a country.<BR>—2 customary in a place; Ms. 8. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशभाषा
देशः + -भाषा the dialect of a country; आलोच्य लक्ष्यमधिगम्य च देशभाषाः<BR> Kāvyāl. 4. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशरूपम्
देशः + -रूपम् propriety, fitness; Mb. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशविद्ध
देशः + -विद्ध <i>a.</i> properly perforated (pearl); Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशवृत्तम्
देशः + -वृत्तम् a circle depending upon its relative position to the place<BR> of the observer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशव्यवहारः|देशव्यवहार
देशः + -व्यवहारः a local usage, custom of the country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकः|देशक
देशकः [दिश्-कर्तरि ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A ruler, governor.<BR>—2 An instructor, a preceptor.<BR>—3 A guide in general.<BR>—4 A shower.<BR>—5 An indicator.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देशकपटुम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकपटुम्
देशकः + -पटुम् a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशना
देशना [दिश्-णिच् युच्] Direction, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0836-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिक|देशिकः
देशिक <i>a.</i> [देशे प्रसितः ठन्] Local, pertaining to a particular<BR> place, native, अदेशिका महारण्ये ग्रीष्मे शत्रुवशं गताः Mb. 4. 47. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिकः|देशिक
देशिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A spiritual teacher (गुरुः) धर्माणां देशिकः साक्षात् स भविष्यति धर्मभाक् Mb.<BR>—2 A traveller.<BR>—3 A guide<BR>—4 One familiar with places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशित
देशित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Told, directed, ordered.<BR>—2 Advised, instructed.<BR>—3 Pointed out, shown, indicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिनी
देशिनी<BR>—1 The fore-finger; वत्स मा रोदीरितीन्द्रो देशिनीमदात् Bhāg. 9. 6. 31.<BR>—2 an index, contents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशी
देशी<BR>—1 The dialect of a country, one of the varieties of the Prākṛta dialect;<BR> see Kāv. 1. 33.<BR>—2 N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: देशीकट्टरिः, देशीनाममाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशीकट्टरिः|देशीकट्टरि
देशी + -कट्टरिः a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशीनाममाला
देशी + -नाममाला N. of a dictionary of provincialism by Hemacandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशीय
देशीय <i>a.</i> [देशे भवः -छ]<BR>—1 Belonging to a province, provincial.<BR>—2 Native, local.<BR>—3 Inhabiting any country (at the end of comp.); as in मगधदेशीय,<BR> तद्देशीय, वङ्गदेशीय &c.<BR>—4 Not far or distant from, almost, bordering on (used as affix at the<BR> end of words); अष्टादशवर्षदेशीयां कन्यां ददर्श K. 131; ‘a girl about 18 years old (whose age bordered on 18)’<BR>; षङ्वर्षदेशीयमपि प्रभुत्वात्<BR> प्रैक्षन्त पौराः पितृगौरवेण R. 18. 39; so पटुदेशीय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्य|देश्यं|देश्यः
देश्य <i>a.</i> [दिश्-कर्मणि ण्यत् देश-यत् वा]<BR>—1 To be pointed out or proved.<BR>—2 Local, provincial.<BR>—3 Born in a country, native.<BR>—4 Genuine, of genuine descent.<BR>—5 Being on the spot or place (where anything is due).<BR>—6 Not far from, almost; see देशीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्यः|देश्य|देश्यं
देश्य + .{@-श्यः@}<BR>—1 An eyewitness of anything अभियोक्ता दिशेद्देश्यम् Ms. 8. 52-53.<BR>—2 The inhabitant of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्यम्
देश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} The statement of a question or argument, the thing to be<BR> proved or substantiated (पूर्वपक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देष्टव्य
देष्टव्य <i>a.</i> To be pointed, shown or declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0837-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देष्टृ
