दैव + -कोविद, -चिन्तकः, -ज्ञः an astrologer, a fortune-teller; पुरोहितं<BR> प्रकुर्वीत दैवज्ञमुदितोदितम् Y. 1. 313; Kām. 9. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवज्ञः|दैवज्ञ
दैव + -कोविद, -चिन्तकः, -ज्ञः an astrologer, a fortune-teller; पुरोहितं<BR> प्रकुर्वीत दैवज्ञमुदितोदितम् Y. 1. 313; Kām. 9. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवगतिः|दैवगति
दैव + -गतिः <i>f.</i> turn or course of fate; मुक्ताजालं चिरपरिचितं<BR> त्याजितो दैवगत्या Me. 96; Pt. 3. 174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवचिन्ता
दैव + -चिन्ता fatalism; astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवज्ञ|दैवज्ञः
दैव + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing fate or menʼs destinies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवतन्त्र|दैवतंत्र
दैव + -तन्त्र <i>a.</i> dependent on fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदत्त
दैव + -दत्त <i>a.</i> innate, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदीपः|दैवदीप
दैव + -दीपः the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदुर्विपाकः|दैवदुर्विपाक
दैव + -दुर्विपाकः hardness of fortune, adverseness or unpropitiousness<BR> of fate, an evil turn of fate; U. 1. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदोषः|दैवदोष
दैव + -दोषः badness of fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवपर|दैवपरः
दैव + -पर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 trusting to fate, a fatalist.<BR>—2 fated, predestined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवप्रश्नः|दैवप्रश्न
दैव + -प्रश्नः<BR>—1 fortune-telling, astrology.<BR>—2 a voice from heaven. नक्तं निर्गत्य यत्किञ्चिच्छुभाशुभकरं वचः ।<BR> श्रूयते तद्विदुर्धीरा दैवप्रश्नमुपश्रुतिम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयुगम्
दैव + -युगम् ‘a Yuga of the gods’ said to consist of 12000 divine years,<BR> but see Kull. on एतद् द्वादशसाहस्रं देवानां युगमुच्यते Ms. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयोगः|दैवयोग
दैव + -योगः a lucky coincidence, fortuitous combination, fortune, chance.<BR> (दैवयोगेन, दैवयोगात् fortunately, accidentally.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवरक्षित
दैव + -रक्षित <i>a.</i> guarded by the gods; अरक्षितं तिष्ठति दैवरक्षितम् Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलेखकः|दैवलेखक
दैव + -लेखकः a fortune-teller, an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववशः|दैववश
दैव + -वशः, -वशम् the power of destiny, subjection to fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववशम्
दैव + -वशः, -वशम् the power of destiny, subjection to fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववाणी
दैव + -वाणी<BR>—1 a voice from heaven.<BR>—2 the Sanskrit language; cf. Kāv. 1. 33 quoted above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवविद्
दैव + -विद् <i>m.</i> an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवसभेयम्
दैव + -सभेयम् a variety of sandal-wood red and smelling like a lotus-flower; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवहत
दैव + -हत <i>a.</i> ill-fated; सुरक्षितं दैवहतं विनश्यति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवहीन
दैव + -हीन <i>a.</i> ill-fated, unfortunate, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकः|दैवक
दैवकः A god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवत|दैवतः
दैवत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [देवता-अण्]<BR>—1 Divine.<BR>—2 (At the end of an adj. comp.) Honouring or worshipping as oneʼs deity,<BR> as in सूर्यदैवता जनाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवतम्
दैवत + .{@-तम्@} A god, deity, divinity; मृदं गां दैवतं विप्रं घृतं<BR> मधु चतुष्पथं प्रदक्षिणानि कुर्वीत Ms. 4. 39, 153; U. 4. 4; Amaru. 3;<BR> हन्त प्रिया दैवतमस्य देवी Bhāg. 4. 4. 28.<BR>—2 A number of gods, the whole class of gods; Ve. 2.<BR>—3 An idol. (The word is said to be <i>m.</i> also, but is rarely used in<BR> that gender. Mammaṭa notices it as a fault called अप्रयुक्तत्व; see<BR> अप्रयुक्त).<BR>—4 N. of the third Kāṇḍa of Yāskas Nirukta.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दैवतपतिः, दैवतसरित्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवतपतिः|दैवतपति
दैवत + -पतिः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवतसरित्
दैवत + -सरित् <i>f.</i> the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवतस्
दैवतस् <i>ind.</i> By chance, fortunately, luckily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0838-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवत्य
दैवत्य <i>a.</i> Addressed or sacred to a deity; हुत्वाग्नीन् सूर्यदैवत्यान्<BR> जपेन् मन्त्रान् समाहितः Y. 1. 99; Ms. 2. 189, 4. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवत्यम्
दैवत्य + .{@-त्यम्@} A deity; Ms. 4. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैविक|दैविकः
दैविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [देव-ठक्] Relating to the gods, divine; अहोरात्रे<BR> विभजते सूर्यो मानुषदैविके Ms. 1. 65, 8. 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैविकम्
दैविक + .{@-कम्@} An inevitable accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैविन्
दैविन् <i>m.</i> An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव्य|दैव्यं
दैव्य <i>a.</i> (-व्या, -व्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव्यम्
दैव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 Fortune, fate.<BR>—2 Divine power; यदि देवा दैव्येनेदृगार Av. 4. 27. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलः|दैवल
दैवलः, -लकः<BR> The servant of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलकः|दैवलक
दैवलः, -लकः<BR> The servant of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवसिक
दैवसिक <i>a.</i> Happening in one day; इत्युक्त्वा ब्राह्मणाय दैवसिकामुत्पत्तिं<BR> प्रादात् Mb. 3. 196. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवाकरिः|दैवाकरि
दैवाकरिः<BR>—1 The planet Saturn.<BR>—2 An epithet of Yama.<BR>—3 The river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवारिपः|दैवारिप
दैवारिपः A conch-shell (शङ्ख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवासुरम्
दैवासुरम् The natural enmity subsisting between the gods and the demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैशिक|दैशिकं|दैशिकः
दैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [देशेन निर्वृत्तं तस्येदं वा-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Local, provincial.<BR>—2 National, belonging to the whole country.<BR>—3 Belonging or having reference to space; Bhāṣā P. 120.<BR>—4 Acquainted with any place.<BR>—5 Teaching, pointing, directing, showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैशिकः|दैशिक|दैशिकं
दैशिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A teacher, preceptor; शुको गतः परित्यज्य पितरं मोक्षदैशिकम्<BR> Mb. 12. 321. 94.<BR>—2 A guide.<BR>—3 One instructed by the preceptor; Bhāg. 11. 27. 22.<BR>—4 Local people; हस्तिनोऽश्वा रथाः पत्तिर्नावो विष्टिस्तथैव च । दैशिकाश्चाविकाश्चैव<BR> तदष्टाङ्गं बलं स्मृतम् Mb. 12. 121. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैशिकम्
दैशिक + .{@-कम्@} a kind of dance; cf. Me. 37; Malli. Com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिक|दैष्टिकः
दैष्टिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [दिष्टमिति मतिर्यस्य, ठक्] Fated, predestined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिकः|दैष्टिक
दैष्टिक + .{@-कः@} A fatalist; नालम्बते दैष्टिकतां न निषीदति पौरुषे । शब्दार्थौ<BR> सत्कविरिव द्वयं विद्वानपेक्षते ॥ Śi. 2. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैहिक|दैहिकं
दैहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [देहे भवः, तस्येदं वा ठक्] Bodily, corporeal;<BR> कर्ताऽस्य सर्गादिषु यो न बध्यते न हन्यते देहगतोऽपि दैहिकैः Bhāg. 5. 19. 12.<BR> प्रजाः ससर्ज कतिधा दैहिकीर्मानसीर्विभुः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैह्य|दैह्यः
दैह्य <i>a.</i> [देहे भवः ष्यञ्] Bodily; तथापि वत मे दैह्यो<BR> ह्यात्मा चैवात्मना विभुः Bhāg. 1. 4. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैह्यः|दैह्य
दैह्य + .{@-ह्यः@} The soul (enshrined in the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दो
दो €4 P. (द्यति, दित; ━<i>caus.</i> दापयति; ━<i>desid.</i> दित्सति)<BR>—1 To cut, divide.<BR>—2 To mow, reap. ━<i>With</i> {@अव@} to cut or lop off; यदन्यस्मिन् यज्ञे<BR> स्रुच्यवद्यति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोग्धृ
दोग्धृ See under दुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोघः|दोघ
दोघः A calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोङ्गकम्
दोङ्गकम् A variety of the resin of aloe (अगुरु), black in colour;<BR> Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोधकम्
दोधकम् N. of a metre consisting of three भगणs and one गुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोमन्
दोमन् <i>n.</i> Pain, inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोरः|दोर
दोरः A rope (रज्जु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोरकम्
दोरकम् A string for fastening the wires of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलः|दोल
दोलः [दुल्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Swinging, rocking, oscillating; वेलादोलानिलचलम् Mb. 1. 21. 10.<BR>—2 A swing, litter.<BR>—3 A festival held on the fourteenth or full-moon day of the month of<BR> Phālguna when figures of ‘young Kṛṣṇa’ (बालकृष्ण) are swung in a swing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोलमण्डपः, दोलमण्डपम्, दोलयानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलमण्डपः|दोलमण्डप
दोलः + -मण्डपः, -मण्डपम्, -यानम् a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलमण्डपम्
दोलः + -मण्डपः, -मण्डपम्, -यानम् a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलयानम्
दोलः + -मण्डपः, -मण्डपम्, -यानम् a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोला
दोला, दोलिका<BR>—1 A litter, palanquin.<BR>—2 A swing, hammock (fig. also); आसीत् स दोलाचलचित्तवृत्तिः R. 14. 34, 9. 46, 19. 44;<BR> संदेहदोलामारोप्यते K. 207.<BR>—3 Swinging, fluctuation.<BR>—4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>—5 The Indigo plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोलाधिरूढ, दोलारूढ, दोलाचलचित्तवृत्ति, दोलायन्त्रम्, दोलायुद्धम्, दोलालोल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलिका
दोला, दोलिका<BR>—1 A litter, palanquin.<BR>—2 A swing, hammock (fig. also); आसीत् स दोलाचलचित्तवृत्तिः R. 14. 34, 9. 46, 19. 44;<BR> संदेहदोलामारोप्यते K. 207.<BR>—3 Swinging, fluctuation.<BR>—4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>—5 The Indigo plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोलाधिरूढ, दोलारूढ, दोलाचलचित्तवृत्ति, दोलायन्त्रम्, दोलायुद्धम्, दोलालोल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलाधिरूढ
दोला + -अधिरूढ, -आरूढ <i>a.</i> (lit.) mounted on a swing; (fig.) uncertain,<BR> irresolute, disquieted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलारूढ
दोला + -अधिरूढ, -आरूढ <i>a.</i> (lit.) mounted on a swing; (fig.) uncertain,<BR> irresolute, disquieted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलाचलचित्तवृत्ति
दोला + -चलचित्तवृत्ति <i>a.</i> One whose mind is agitated like a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायन्त्रम्
दोला + -यन्त्रम् drugs tied up in a cloth and boiled out over a fire; Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायुद्धम्
दोला + -युद्धम् uncertainty of success, a fight with varying success;<BR> दोलायुद्धं कृतगुरुतरध्वानमौद्धत्यभाजाम् Śi. 18. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलालोल
दोला + -लोल <i>a.</i> uncertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायते
दोलायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To swing, rock to and fro, oscillate, fluctuate, vacillate (fig. also).<BR>—2 To be restless or uneasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायमान|दोलायमानः
दोलायमान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Swinging, oscillating.<BR>—2 Wavering, vacillating.<BR>—3 Perplexed, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायित
दोलायित, -दोलित <i>a.</i><BR> Swung, shaken, oscillating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलित
दोलायित, -दोलित <i>a.</i><BR> Swung, shaken, oscillating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलिका
दोलिका, -दोली<BR>—1 A cradle.<BR>—2 A swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोली
दोलिका, -दोली<BR>—1 A cradle.<BR>—2 A swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोष|दोषः
दोष, दोषिक, दोषिन्<BR> See under दुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिक|दोषिकः
दोष, दोषिक, दोषिन्<BR> See under दुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिन्
दोष, दोषिक, दोषिन्<BR> See under दुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषन्
दोषन् <i>m., n.</i> (This word has no forms for the first five inflections,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> before acc. pl.) An arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषस्
दोषस् <i>f.</i> Night. ━<i>n.</i> Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषा
दोषा <i>ind.</i> At night; दोषाऽपि नूनमहिमांशुरसौ किलेति Śi. 4. 46, 62.<BR>━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 The arm.<BR>—2 The darkness of night, night; घर्मकालदिवस इव क्षपितदोषः<BR> K. 37 (where the word means ‘a fault or sin’ also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोषास्यः, दोषातिलकः, दोषाकरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषास्यः|दोषास्य
दोषा + -आस्यः, -तिलकः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातिलकः|दोषातिलक
दोषा + -आस्यः, -तिलकः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषाकरः|दोषाकर
दोषा + -करः<BR>—1 The moon; यामित्रवेधविहितानपहृत्य दोषान् । दोषाकरः सुखमनेकविधं<BR> विधत्ते ॥ Jyotistattvam.<BR>—2 a mine of faults; दोषाकरोऽपि कुटिलोऽपि कलङ्कितोऽपि Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातन|दोषातनः
दोषातन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Nightly, nocturnal; दोषातनं बुधबृहस्पतियोगदृश्यः<BR> (तारापतिः) R. 13. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्
दोस् <i>m., n.</i> [दम्यते अनेन दम् दोऽसि अर्धर्चा˚; Uṇ. 2. 69]<BR> (दोषन् is optionally substituted for this word after acc. dual.)<BR>—1 The forearm, the arm; तमुपाद्रवदुद्यम्य दक्षिणं दोर्निशाचरः<BR> R. 15. 23; हेमपात्रगतं दोर्भ्यामादधानं पयश्चरुम् 10. 51; Ku. 3. 76.<BR>—2 The part of an arc defining its sine.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">Page0840-1</a>]<BR>—3 The side of a triangle or square.<BR>—4 A measure of eighteen inches; Mātaṅga L. 10. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोर्गडु, दोर्ग्रह, दोर्ज्या, दोर्दण्डः, दोर्निकर्तनम्, दोर्मूलम्, दोर्युद्धम्, दोःशालिन्, दोःशिखरम्, दोःसहस्रभृत्, दोःस्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0839-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्गडु|दोर्गडुः
दोस् + -गडु (दोर्गडु) <i>a.</i> crooked-armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्ग्रह|दोर्ग्रहः
दोस् + -ग्रह (दोर्ग्रह) <i>a.</i> strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्ग्रहः|दोर्ग्रह
दोस् + -ग्रह + .({@-हः@}) pain in the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्ज्या
दोस् + -ज्या (दोर्ज्या) the sine of the base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्दण्डः|दोर्दण्ड|दोर्दंड
दोस् + -दण्डः (दोर्दण्डः) a stick-like arm, strong arm; दोर्दण्डाञ्चितमहिमा<BR> Mv. 7. 8; Bv. 1. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्निकर्तनम्
दोस् + -निकर्तनम् (दोर्निकर्तनम्) amputation of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्मूलम्
दोस् + -मूलम् (दोर्मूलम्) the armpit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्युद्धम्
दोस् + -युद्धम् (दोर्युद्धम्) a duel; (अभ्युद्यतं) दोर्युद्धाय<BR> दशास्यमिन्द्रतनयः प्रक्षिप्य कक्षान्तरे Mv. 5. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःशालिन्
दोस् + -शालिन् (दोःशालिन्) possessed of strong arms, warlike, brave;<BR> इयं परिसमाप्यते रणकथाद्य दोःशालिनाम् Ve. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःशिखरम्
दोस् + -शिखरम् (दोःशिखरम्) the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःसहस्रभृत्
दोस् + -सहस्रभृत् (दोःसहस्रभृत्) <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of the demon Bāṇa.<BR>—2 an epithet of Sahasrārjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःस्थः|दोःस्थ
दोस् + -स्थः (दोःस्थः)<BR>—1 a servant.<BR>—2 service.<BR>—3 a player.<BR>—4 play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह|दोहः
दोह, दोहन, दोह्य &c. See under दुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहन|दोहनं
दोह, दोहन, दोह्य &c. See under दुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह्य|दोह्यं
दोह, दोहन, दोह्य &c. See under दुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदः|दोहद|दोहदं
दोहदः, -दम्<BR> [दोहमाकर्षं ददाति दा-क]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The longing of a pregnant woman; प्रजावती दोहदशंसिनी ते<BR> R. 14. 45; उपेत्य सा दोहददुःखशीलतां यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम् 3. 6, 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The desired object itself.<BR>—2 Pregnancy.<BR>—3 The desire of plants at budding time (as, for instance, of the Aśoka<BR> to be kicked by young ladies, of the Bakula to be sprinkled by mouthfuls<BR> of liquor &c.); महीरुहा दोहदसेकशक्तेराकालिकं कोरकमुद्गिरन्ति<BR> N. 3. 21; R. 8. 63; Me. 78; see अशोक.<BR>—4 Vehement desire; प्रवर्तितमहासमरदोहदा नरपतयः Ve. 4.<BR>—5 Wish or desire in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोहददुःखशीलता, दोहदधूपः, दोहदलक्षणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदम्
दोहदः, -दम्<BR> [दोहमाकर्षं ददाति दा-क]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The longing of a pregnant woman; प्रजावती दोहदशंसिनी ते<BR> R. 14. 45; उपेत्य सा दोहददुःखशीलतां यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम् 3. 6, 7.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The desired object itself.<BR>—2 Pregnancy.<BR>—3 The desire of plants at budding time (as, for instance, of the Aśoka<BR> to be kicked by young ladies, of the Bakula to be sprinkled by mouthfuls<BR> of liquor &c.); महीरुहा दोहदसेकशक्तेराकालिकं कोरकमुद्गिरन्ति<BR> N. 3. 21; R. 8. 63; Me. 78; see अशोक.<BR>—4 Vehement desire; प्रवर्तितमहासमरदोहदा नरपतयः Ve. 4.<BR>—5 Wish or desire in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: दोहददुःखशीलता, दोहदधूपः, दोहदलक्षणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहददुःखशीलता
दोहदः + -दुःखशीलता pregnancy; उपेत्य सा दोहददुःखशीलताम् R. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदधूपः
दोहदः + -धूपः a kind of fragrant substance used as manure; दाडिमे दोहदधूपिनि<BR> द्रुमे N. 1. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदलक्षणम्
दोहदः + -लक्षणम्<BR>—1 the foetus, the embryo (= दौर्हृदलक्षण q. v.).<BR>—2 the period of passing from one stage of life to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदवती
दोहदवती A pregnant woman longing for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदिन्
दोहदिन् <i>a.</i> Eagerly longing for, ardently desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0840-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहलः|दोहल
