द्युत्
द्युत् €1 Ā. [द्योतते, द्युतित or द्योतित. ━<i>desid.</i><BR> दिद्युतिषते, दिद्योतिषते] To shine, be bright or brilliant; दिद्युते<BR> च यथा रविः Bk. 14. 104, 6. 26, 7. 107, 8. 89. ━<i>Caus.</i> (द्योतयति-ते)<BR>—1 To illuminate, irradiate; Bk. 8. 46; ते प्रभामण्डलैर्व्योम द्योतयन्तस्तपोधनाः Ku. 6. 4.<BR>—2 To make clear, explain, elucidate.<BR>—3 To express, mean. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि@} (<i>Caus.</i>) to illuminate;<BR> तस्मिन्नभिद्योतितबन्धुपद्मे (भावं न बबन्ध) R. 6. 36. ━{@वि@}<BR> to shine, be bright; व्यद्योतिष्ट सभावेद्यामसौ नरशिखित्रयी Śi. 2. 3, 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0841-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत्
द्युत् <i>m.</i> A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0841-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिः|द्युति
द्युतिः <i>f.</i> [द्युत्-इन्]<BR>—1 Splendour, brightness, lustre, beauty; काचः काञ्चनसंसर्गाद् धत्ते<BR> मारकतीं द्युतिम् H. Pr. 35; Māl. 2. 10; R. 3. 64.<BR>—2 Light, a ray of light; Bh. 1. 61.<BR>—3 Majesty, dignity; Ms. 1. 87.<BR>—4 (in drama) A threatening attitude.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: द्युतिकरः, द्युतिधरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0841-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

