द्वि + -अष्टम् copper. ˚सहस्रम् 16000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यहः|द्व्यह
द्वि + -अहः a period of two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यात्मक|द्व्यात्मकः
द्वि + -आत्मक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having a double nature.<BR>—2 being two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यात्मकाः
द्वि + -आत्मकाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the signs of the zodiac Gemini, Virgo, Sagittarius and Pisces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यामुष्यायणः|द्व्यामुष्यायण
द्वि + -आमुष्यायणः ‘a son of two persons or fathers’, an adopted son<BR> who remains heir to his natural father though adopted by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्याम्नात
द्वि + -आम्नात <i>a.</i> twice mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्याहिक|द्व्याहिकः
द्वि + -आहिक <i>a.</i> recurring every other day (fever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यृचम्
द्वि + -ऋचम् (द्वृचम् or द्व्यर्चम्) a colletion of two verses or <i>ṛks</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्येकान्तर
द्वि + -एकान्तर <i>a.</i> separated by two or by one (degree); द्व्येकान्तरासु<BR> जातानां धर्म्यं विद्यादिमं विधिम् Ms. 10. 7.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">Page0848-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0847-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकः|द्विक|द्विकं
द्वि + -कः, -ककारः<BR>—1 crow (there being two <i>‘Ka’s</i> in the word काक).<BR>—2 the ruddy goose (there being two <i>‘Ka’s</i> in the word कोक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककारः|द्विककार
द्वि + -कः, -ककारः<BR>—1 crow (there being two <i>‘Ka’s</i> in the word काक).<BR>—2 the ruddy goose (there being two <i>‘Ka’s</i> in the word कोक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककुद्
द्वि + -ककुद् <i>m.</i> a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकर
द्वि + -कर <i>a.</i> Yielding two senses, serving two purposes; तत्र<BR> द्विकरः शब्दः स्यात् । न च सकृदुच्चरितः शक्तो ह्यर्थद्वयं विधातुम् ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकार्षापणिक
द्वि + -कार्षापणिक <i>a.</i> worth two कार्षापणs<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकौडविक
द्वि + -कौडविक <i>a.</i> containing or worth two कुडवs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगत
द्वि + -गत <i>a.</i> ambiguous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगु|द्विगुः
द्वि + -गु <i>a.</i> exchanged or bartered for two cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुः|द्विगु
द्वि + -गु + .({@-गुः@}) a subdivision of the Tatpuruṣa compound in which the first<BR> member is a numeral; द्वन्द्वो द्विगुरपि चाहम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुण|द्विगुणं
द्वि + -गुण <i>a.</i> double, twofold; पितुर्वधव्यसनमिदं हि येन<BR> मे चिरादपि द्विगुणमिवाद्य वर्धते Mu. 5. 6 (द्विगुणाकृ to plough<BR> twice; द्विगुणीकृ to double, increase; द्विगुणीभूत <i>a.</i> double, augmented).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणित
द्वि + -गुणित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doubled, multiplied by two; वैरोचनैर्द्विगुणिताः सहसा मयूखैः Ki. 5. 46.<BR>—2 folded double.<BR>—3 enveloped. —4 doubly increased, doubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विचरण
द्वि + -चरण <i>a.</i> having two legs, two-legged; द्विचरणपशूनां<BR> क्षितिभुजाम् Śānti. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विचत्वारिंश
द्वि + -चत्वारिंश <i>a.</i> (द्वि(द्वा)चत्वारिंश) forty-second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विचत्वारिंशत्
द्वि + -चत्वारिंशत् <i>f.</i> (द्वि(द्वा)चत्वारिंशत्) forty-two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विचन्द्रधी
द्वि + -चन्द्रधी, -मतिः The illusion of seeing two moons due to an eye<BR> disease called Timira; N. 13. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमतिः
द्वि + -चन्द्रधी, -मतिः The illusion of seeing two moons due to an eye<BR> disease called Timira; N. 13. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजः|द्विज
द्वि + -जः ‘twice-born’<BR>—1 a man of any of the first three castes of the Hindus (a Brāhmaṇa,<BR> Kṣatriya or Vaiśya); मातुर्यदग्रे जायन्ते द्वितीयं मौञ्जिबन्धनात् ।<BR> ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशस्तस्मादेते द्विजाः स्मृताः Y. 1. 39.<BR>—2 Brāhmaṇa (over whom the Saṃskāras or purificatory rites are performed);<BR> जन्मना ब्राह्मणो ज्ञेयः संस्कारैर्द्विज उच्यते.<BR>—3 any oviparous animal, such as a bird, snake, fish &c.; Mb. 12. 361. 5.<BR> (द्विजश्रेष्ठ = द्विजानामण्डजानां सर्पाणां श्रेष्ठ); स तमानन्दमविन्दत<BR> द्विजः N. 2. 1; Ś. 5. 22; R. 12. 22; Mu. 1. 11; Ms. 5. 17.<BR>—4 a tooth; कीर्णं द्विजानां गणैः Bh. 1. 13 (where द्विज means<BR> ‘a Brāhmaṇa’ also).<BR>—5 A star; L. D. B.<BR>—6 A kind of horse; जलोद्भवा द्विजा ज्ञेयाः Aśvachikitsā.<BR>—7 A Brahmachārī; Bhāg. 11. 18. 42. ˚अग्र्य a Brāhmaṇa. ˚अयनी<BR> the sacred thread worn by the first three castes of the Hindus. ˚आलयः<BR>—1 the house of a <i>dvija</i>.<BR>—2 a nest. ˚इन्द्रः, ˚ईशः<BR>—1 the moon; द्विजेन्द्रकान्तं श्रितवक्षसं श्रिया Śi. 12. 3.<BR>—2 an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—3 camphor. ˚दासः a Śūdra. ˚देवः<BR>—1 a Brāhmaṇa; Bhāg. 8. 15. 37.<BR>—2 a sage; Bhāg. 3. 1. 23.<BR>—3 N. of Brahmadeva; Bhāg. 5. 2. 16. ˚पतिः, ˚राजः an epithet of<BR>—1 the moon; इत्थं द्विजेन द्विजराजकान्तिः R. 5. 23.<BR>—2 Garuḍa.<BR>—3 camphor. ˚प्रपा<BR>—1 a trench or basin round the root of a tree for holding water.<BR>—2 a trough near a well for watering birds, cattle. &c. ˚प्रियः kind<BR> of khadira. ˚प्रिया the Soma plant. ˚बन्धुः, ˚ब्रुवः<BR>—1 a man who pretends to be a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—2 one who is ‘twice-born’ or a Brāhmaṇa by name and birth only and<BR> not by acts; cf. ब्रह्मबन्धु. ˚मुख्यः a Brāhmaṇa. ˚लिङ्गिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a Kṣatriya.<BR>—2 a pseudo-Brāhmaṇa, one disguised as a Brāhmaṇa. ˚वाहनः an<BR> epithet of Viṣṇu (having Garuḍa for his vehicle). ˚सेवकः a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजन्मन्
द्वि + -जन्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having two natures.<BR>—2 regenerated.<BR>—3 oviparous. ━(<i>m.</i>), {@-जातिः@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a man of any of the first three castes of the Hindus; एतान्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">Page0848-2</a>]<BR> द्विजातयो देशान् संश्रयेरन् प्रयत्नतः Ms. 2. 24.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa Ki. 1. 39; Ku. 5. 40. गुरुरग्निर्द्विजातीनां वर्णानां<BR> ब्राह्मणो गुरुः H.<BR>—3 a bird.<BR>—4 a tooth.<BR>—5 A kind of horse; लक्षणद्वयसम्बन्धाद् द्विजातिः स्यात् तुरङ्गमः<BR> Yuktikalpataru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजातीय|द्विजातीयः
द्वि + -जातीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 belonging to the first three castes of the Hindus.<BR>—2 of a twofold nature.<BR>—3 of mixed origin, mongrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजातीयः|द्विजातीय
द्वि + -जातीय + .({@-यः@}) a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजानि
द्वि + -जानि a having two wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्व|द्विजिह्वः
द्वि + -जिह्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 double-tongued (fig. also).<BR>—2 insincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्वः|द्विजिह्व
द्वि + -जिह्व + .({@-ह्वः@})<BR>—1 a snake; परस्य मर्माविधमुज्झतां निजं द्विजिह्वतादोषमजिह्मगामिभिः<BR> Śi. 1. 63; R. 11. 64, 14. 41; Bv. 1. 20.<BR>—2 an informer, a slanderer, tale-bearer.<BR>—3 an insincere person<BR>—4 a thief.<BR>—5 particular disease of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज्या
द्वि + -ज्या the sine of an arc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विठः|द्विठ
द्वि + -ठः<BR>—1 the sign <i>visarga</i> consisting of two dots.<BR>—2 N. of Svāhā, wife of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वित्र
द्वि + -त्र <i>a.</i> (pl.) two or three; द्वित्राण्यहान्यर्हसि सोढुमर्हन्<BR> R. 5. 25; सूक्ष्मा एव पतन्ति चातकमुखे द्वित्राः पयोबिन्दवः Bh. 2. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वित्रिंश
द्वि + -त्रिंश (द्वात्रिंश) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 thirty second.<BR>—2 consisting of thirty two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वित्रिंशत्
द्वि + -त्रिंशत् (द्वात्रिंशत्) <i>f.</i> thirty-two. ˚लक्षण<BR> <i>a.</i> having thirty-two auspicious marks upon the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदण्डि|द्विदंडि
द्वि + -दण्डि <i>ind.</i> stick against stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदत्|द्विदन्त्
द्वि + -दत् <i>a.</i> having two teeth (as a mark of age).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदन्तः|द्विदन्त
द्वि + -दन्तः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदल
द्वि + -दल <i>a.</i> having two parts, two-leafed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदश
द्वि + -दश <i>a.</i> (pl.) twenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदश
द्वि + -दश <i>a.</i> (द्वादश)<BR>—1 twelfth; गर्भात् तु द्वादशे विशः Ms. 2. 36.<BR>—2 consisting of twelve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदशन्
द्वि + -दशन् (द्वादशन्) <i>a.</i> (pl.) twelve. ˚अंशुः, ˚अर्चिस्<BR> <i>m.</i> an epithet of<BR>—1 the planet Jupiter.<BR>—2 Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods. ˚अक्षः, ˚करः, ˚लोचनः<BR> epithets of Kārtikeya ˚अक्षरमन्त्रःविद्या the mantra अँ नमो भगवते<BR> वासुदेवाय; गन्धघूपादिभिश्चार्चेद्वादशाक्षरविद्यया Bhāg. 8. 16. 39.<BR> ˚अङ्गुल a measure of twelve fingers. ˚अध्यायी N. of Jaiminiʼs Mimāṃsā<BR> in twelve Adhyāyas. ˚अन्यिक <i>a.</i> committing twelve mistakes in<BR> reading. ˚अस्र a dodecagon. ˚अहः<BR>—1 a period of twelve days; शुध्येद् विप्रो दशाहेन द्वादशाहेन भूमिपः<BR> Ms. 5. 83, 11. 168.<BR>—2 a sacrifice lasting for or completed in twelve days. ˚अक्षः, ˚आख्यः<BR> a Buddha. ˚आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the sun; N. 10. 52. ˚आदित्याः (pl.) the<BR> twelve suns; see आदित्य. ˚आयुस् <i>m.</i> a dog. ˚लक्षणी <i>f.</i><BR> the मीमांसासूत्र of जैमिनि (so called because it comprises twelve<BR> chapters); धर्मो द्वादशलक्षण्या व्युत्पाद्यः ŚB. on MS. ˚वार्षिक<BR> <i>a.</i> —1 twelve years old, lasting for twelve years; Pt. 1. ˚विध<BR> <i>a.</i> twelve-fold. ˚सहस्र <i>a.</i> consisting of 12000.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदशी
द्वि + -दशी (द्वादशी) the twelfth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विद्वादशान्यिक
द्वि + -द्वादशान्यिक (द्वादशापपाठा यस्य जाताः द्वादशान्यिकः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदशम्
द्वि + -दशम् (द्वादशम्) a collection of twelve, ˚आदित्याः<BR> Twelve Ādityas:− विवस्वान्, अर्यमा, पूषन्, त्वष्टा, सविता, भग, धाता,<BR> विधाता, वरुण, मित्र, रुद्र, विष्णु. ˚पुत्रा Twelve types of sons<BR> according to Dharmaśāstra:− औरस, क्षेत्रज, दत्तक, कृत्रिम, गूढोत्पन्न,<BR> अपविद्ध, कानीन, सहोढ, क्रीत, पौनर्भव, स्वयंदत्त, पारशव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदाम्नी
द्वि + -दाम्नी a cow tied with two ropes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदिवः|द्विदिव
द्वि + -दिवः a ceremony lasting for two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदेवतम्
द्वि + -देवतम् the constellation विशाखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदेहः|द्विदेह
द्वि + -देहः an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधातुः|द्विधातु
द्वि + -धातुः an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनग्नकः|द्विनग्नक
द्वि + -नग्नकः a circumcised man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनवत
द्वि + -नवत (द्वि(द्वा)नवत) <i>a.</i> ninety-second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनवतिः|द्विनवति
द्वि + -नवतिः (द्वि(द्वा)नवतिः) <i>f.</i> ninety-two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपः|द्विप
द्वि + -पः an elephant; यदा किञ्चिज्ज्ञोऽहं द्विप इव मदान्धः समभवम्<BR> Bh. 3. 31; विपूर्यमाणश्रवणोदरं द्विपाः Śi. ˚अधिपः Indraʼs<BR> elephant. ˚आस्य an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0848-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

