द्वैगुण्यम्<BR>—1 Double amount, value or measure.<BR>—2 Duality.<BR>—3 The possession of two out of the three qualities सत्त्व, रजस् and तमस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतम्
द्वैतम् [द्विधा इतं द्वितं तस्य भावः स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 Duality.<BR>—2 Dualism in philosophy, the assertion of two distinct principles, such<BR> as the maintenance of the doctrine that, spirit and matter, Brahman and<BR> the Universe, or the Individual and the Supreme Soul, are different from<BR> each other; cf. अद्वैत; किं शास्त्रं श्रवणेन यस्य गलति द्वैतान्धकारोत्करः Bv. 1. 86.<BR>—3 N. of a forest.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: द्वैताद्वैतमार्गः, द्वैतवनम्, द्वैतवादः, द्वैतवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैताद्वैतमार्गः|द्वैताद्वैतमार्ग
द्वैतम् + -अद्वैतमार्गः the path of dualism and non-dualism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवनम्
द्वैतम् + -वनम् N. of a forest; भीमं प्रशस्याथ गुणैरनेकैर्हृष्टास्ततो<BR> द्वैतवनाय जग्मुः Mb. 3. 11. 68; Ki. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवादः|द्वैतवाद
द्वैतम् + -वादः the doctrine of dualism; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवादिन्
द्वैतम् + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a philosopher who maintains the <i>dvaita</i> doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतिन्
द्वैतिन् <i>m.</i> A philosopher who maintains the <i>dvaita</i> doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0850-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतीयीक|द्वैतीयीकः
द्वैतीयीक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Second; द्वैतीयीकतया मितोऽयमगमत् तस्य प्रबन्धे<BR> महाकाव्ये चारुणि नैषधीयचरिते सर्गो निसर्गोज्ज्वलः N. 2. 110; cf. तार्तींयीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध|द्वैधं
द्वैध <i>a.</i> (-धी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Two-fold, double.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधम्
द्वैध + .{@-धम्@}<BR>—1 Duality, two-fold nature or state.<BR>—2 Separation into two parts.<BR>—3 Double resource, secondary reserve; कार्यं वीक्ष्य प्रयुञ्जीत द्वैधं<BR> संश्रयमेव च Ms. 7. 161.<BR>—4 Diversity, difference, conflict, contest, variance; श्रुतिद्वैधं तु<BR> यत्र स्यात् तत्र धर्मावुभौ स्मृतौ Ms. 2. 14, 9. 32; Y. 2. 78.<BR>—5 Doubt, uncertainty; छिन्नद्वैधाः (ऋषयः) Bg. 5. 25; Ve. 6. 44.<BR>—6 Double-dealing, duplicity, one of the six modes of foreign policy;<BR> see द्वैधीभाव below and गुण.<BR>—7 Contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधम्
द्वैध + .{@-धम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In two parts.<BR>—2 In two ways, doubly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकृ
द्वैधीकृ €8 U. To separate, divide (into two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकरणम्
द्वैधीकरणम् Making into two, separating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकृत
द्वैधीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Separated, made two-fold.<BR>—2 Brought into a dilemma, embarrassed, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभू
द्वैधीभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To become divided into two parts, be disunited.<BR>—2 To vacillate, be divided or uncertain, be in suspense (as mind); कृत्ययोर्भिन्नदेशत्वाद्<BR> द्वैधीभवति मे मनः Ś. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभावः|द्वैधीभाव
द्वैधीभावः<BR>—1 Duality, double state or nature.<BR>—2 Separation into two, difference, diversity.<BR>—3 Doubt, uncertainty, vacillation, suspense; धृतद्वैधीभावकातरं मे मनः Ś. 1.<BR>—4 A dilemma.<BR>—5 One of the six Guṇas or modes of foreign policy. (According to some<BR> authorities it means ‘double dealing’, or ‘duplicity’ ‘keeping apparently friendly relations with the enemy’<BR>; द्वैधीभाविकाः सन्धिविग्रहाः Kau. A. 7;<BR> बलिनोर्द्विषतोर्मध्ये वाचात्मानं समर्पयन् । द्वैधीभावेन तिष्ठेत्तु<BR> काकाक्षिवदलक्षितः ॥ According to others it means ‘dividing oneʼs army and encountering a superior enemy in detachments’<BR>, ‘harassing the enemy by attacking them in small bands’<BR>; द्वैधीभावः स्वबलस्य द्विधाकरणम्<BR> Mit. on Y. 1. 347; cf. also Ms. 7. 173 and 160.)<BR>—6 A contest, dispute.<BR>—7 Falsehood, duplicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध्यम्
द्वैध्यम्<BR>—1 Duplicity.<BR>—2 Diversity, difference.<BR>—3 Falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप|द्वैपः
द्वैप <i>a.</i> (-पी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [द्वीपिनो विकारः अञ् द्वीपादागतः अण् वा]<BR>—1 Relating to or living on an island.<BR>—2 Belonging to a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">Page0851-2</a>]<BR> tiger, made of or covered with a tigerʼs skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपः|द्वैप
द्वैप + .{@-पः@} A car covered with a tigerʼs skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपम्
द्वैप + .{@-पम्@} The skin of a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपक्षम्
द्वैपक्षम् Two parties; also द्वैपक्ष्यम्; द्वैपक्ष्यमासीद् देवानामसुराणां<BR> च भारत Mb. 8. 87. 60<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपायनः|द्वैपायन
द्वैपायनः [द्वीपः अयनं जन्मभूमिर्यस्य स द्वीपायनः, स्वार्थे-अण्]<BR>—1 ‘The island-born’, N. of Vyāsa; उदारचेता गिरमित्युदारां द्वैपायनेनाभिदधे<BR> नरेन्द्रः Ki. 3. 10.<BR>—2 N. of the sage Durvāsas; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप्य|द्वैप्यं
द्वैप्य <i>a.</i> (-प्या, -प्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Living on or relating to an island; विक्रीय<BR> दिश्यानि धनान्युरूणि द्वैप्यानसावुत्तमलाभभाजः Śi. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातुर|द्वैमातुरः
द्वैमातुर <i>a.</i> Having two mothers, <i>i. e.</i> a natural mother and a stepmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातुरः|द्वैमातुर
द्वैमातुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—2 N. of Jarāsandha; हते हिडिम्बरिपुणा राज्ञि द्वैमातुरे युधि Śi. 2. 60<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातृक|द्वैमातृकः
द्वैमातृक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Nourished by rain and rivers (as a country); cf. देवमातृक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरथम्
द्वैरथम्<BR>—1 A single combat in chariots; एकः सुभद्रामारोप्य द्वैरथे कृष्णमाह्वयत् Mb. 4. 49. 6.<BR>—2 A single combat in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरथः|द्वैरथ|द्वैरथं
द्वैरथम् + .{@-थः@} An adversary; अलक्षितद्वैरथमत्यमर्षणं प्रचण्डवक्त्रं<BR> न बभाज कश्चन Bhāg. 7. 8. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैराज्यम्
द्वैराज्यम्<BR>—1 A dominion divided between two kings. तत्रभवतोर्भ्रात्रोः … द्वैराज्यमवस्थापयितुकामोऽस्मि M. 5. 12/13.<BR>—2 A frontier. चरच्चिरं शैशवयौवनीयद्वैराज्यभाजि त्वयि खेदमेति N. 8. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैवार्षिक
द्वैवार्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Biennial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैविध्यम्
द्वैविध्यम्<BR>—1 Duality, two-fold nature.<BR>—2 Variance, diversity, difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैसमिक
द्वैसमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Two years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैहकाल्यम्
द्वैहकाल्यम् (opp. सद्यस्कालता or ऐककाल्य) The characteristic<BR> of being performed in (or spread over) a period of two days; द्वैहकाल्यं<BR> हि चोदकप्राप्तमानुमानिकं प्रत्यक्षरूपया सद्यस्कालतया बाध्येत ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 20; द्वैहकाल्ये तु यथान्यायम् Ms. 5. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैहायनम्
द्वैहायनम् The period of two years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यहकाल
द्व्यहकाल <i>a.</i> To be performed in two days; कितमो द्व्यहकाला<BR> इष्टयः उत सद्यस्काला इति । ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Placing, holding, containing, causing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धः|ध|धं
ध + .{@-धः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—2 N. of Kubera.<BR>—3 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>—4 (in music) The 6th note of the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्
ध + .{@-धम्@} Wealth, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्
धक् An exclamation of anger; U. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्क्
धक्क् €10 U. (धक्कयति-ते) To destroy or annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धगिति
धगिति <i>ind.</i> In a moment, at once; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटः|धट
धटः<BR>—1 A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>—2 Ordeal by the balance.<BR>—3 The sign Libra of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0851-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटकः|धटक
धटकः A kind of weight equal to 42 Guñjās or Raktikas; तुल्या<BR> यवाभ्यां कथितात्र गुञ्जा वल्लस्त्रिगुञ्जो धरणं च तेऽष्टौ । गद्यानकस्तद्द्वयमिन्द्रतुल्यैर्वल्लैस्तथैवं<BR> धटकः प्रदिष्टः ॥ Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिका
धटिका, धटी<BR>—1 Old cloth or raiment.<BR>—2 A strip of cloth fastened round the loins or over the privities.<BR>—3 A kind of garment worn by a woman after Garbhādhāna.<BR>—4 A kind of measure equal to five <i>shers</i>; द्व्यक्षेन्दुसंख्यैर्धटकैस्तु<BR> सैरस्तैः पञ्चभिः स्याद् धटिका च ताभिः Līlā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धटिकादानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटी
धटिका, धटी<BR>—1 Old cloth or raiment.<BR>—2 A strip of cloth fastened round the loins or over the privities.<BR>—3 A kind of garment worn by a woman after Garbhādhāna.<BR>—4 A kind of measure equal to five <i>shers</i>; द्व्यक्षेन्दुसंख्यैर्धटकैस्तु<BR> सैरस्तैः पञ्चभिः स्याद् धटिका च ताभिः Līlā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धटिकादानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिकादानम्
धटिका + -दानम् (धटीदानम्) giving an old cloth to a woman after impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिन्
धटिन् <i>m.</i> [धटोऽस्त्यस्य-इनि]<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 The sign Libra of the zodiac.<BR>—3 A dealer, trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिनी
धटिन् + .{@-नी@} = धटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धण्
धण् €1 P. (धणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूरः|धत्तूर
धत्तूरः, धत्तूरकः, -का<BR> The white thorn-apple (Mar. धोतरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूरकः|धत्तूरक
धत्तूरः, धत्तूरकः, -का<BR> The white thorn-apple (Mar. धोतरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूरका
धत्तूरः, धत्तूरकः, -का<BR> The white thorn-apple (Mar. धोतरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्
धन् I. €1 P. (धनति) To sound. ━II. €3 P. (दधन्ति) Ved. To bear fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनम्
धनम् [धन्-अच्]<BR>—1 Property, wealth, riches, treasure, money (gold, chattels &c.); धनं<BR> तावदसुलभम् H. 1; (fig. also) as in तपोधन, विद्याधन, &c.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Any valued possession, an object of affection or endearment,<BR> dearest treasure; कष्टं जनः कुलधनैरनुरञ्जनीयः U. 1. 14; गुरोरपीदं<BR> धनमाहिताग्नेः R. 2. 44; मानधन, अभिमान˚ &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A valuable article; Ms. 8. 201, 202.<BR>—3 Capital (opp. वृद्धि or interest).<BR>—4 A booty, prey, spoil.<BR>—5 The reward given to a victor in a combat, the prize won in a game.<BR>—6 A contest for prizes, a match.<BR>—7 The lunar mansion called धनिष्ठा.<BR>—8 Surplus, residue.<BR>—9 (In math.) The affirmative quantity or plus (opp. ऋण).<BR>—10 A sound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धनाधिकारः, धनाधिकारिन्, धनाधिगोप्तृ, धनापहारः, धनार्चित, धनार्थिन्, धनाढद्य, धनादानम्, धनाधारः, धनाशा, धनेशः, धनेश्वरः, धनोष्मन्, धनैषिन्, धनकाम, धनकाम्य, धनकेलिः, धनक्षयः, धनगर्व, धनगर्वित, धनच्छूः, धनजातम्, धनद, धनदण्डः, धनदायिन्, धनधानी, धनधान्यम्, धनपतिः, धनपालः, धनपिशाचिका, धनपिशाची, धनप्रयोगः, धनमद, धनमूलम्, धनलोभः, धनव्ययः, धनसूः, धनस्थानम्, धनहरः, धनहार्य, धनहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकारः|धनाधिकार
धनम् + -अधिकारः right to property, right of inheriting property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकारिन्
धनम् + -अधिकारिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-अधिकृतः@}<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 an heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिगोप्तृ
धनम् + -अधिगोप्तृ <i>m.</i>, {@-अधिपः, -अधिपतिः, -अध्यक्षः@}<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera; अनुचरेण धनाधिपते रथो नगविलोकनविस्मितमानसः<BR> (स जगदे) Ki. 5. 16. धनाधिपेन विद्धस्य अनुह्रादस्य संयुगे<BR> Hariv.; यदस्माकं धनाध्यक्षः प्रभूतं धनमाहरत् Mb. 179. 18.<BR>—2 a treasurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनापहारः|धनापहार
धनम् + -अपहारः<BR>—1 fine.<BR>—2 plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्चित|धनार्च्चित
धनम् + -अर्चित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 honoured with gifts of wealth, kept contented by valuable presents;<BR> मानधना धनार्चिताः Ki. 1. 19.<BR>—2 wealthy, opulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्थिन्
धनम् + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> desiring or seeking for wealth, covetous, miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाढद्य
धनम् + -आढद्य <i>a.</i> opulent, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनादानम्
धनम् + -आदानम् acceptance of money; Ms. 11. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधारः|धनाधार
धनम् + -आधारः a treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाशा
धनम् + -आशा <i>f.</i> Desire for wealth; धनाशा जीविताशा च जीर्यतोऽपि<BR> न जीर्यति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेशः|धनेश
धनम् + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेश्वरः|धनेश्वर
धनम् + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनोष्मन्
धनम् + -उष्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 warmth of wealth; cf. अर्थोष्मन्;<BR>—2 burning desire for wealth; Ms. 9. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनैषिन्
धनम् + -एषिन् <i>m.</i> a creditor who claims his money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकाम
धनम् + -काम, -काम्य <i>a.</i> covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकाम्य
धनम् + -काम, -काम्य <i>a.</i> covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकेलिः|धनकेलि
धनम् + -केलिः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनक्षयः|धनक्षय
धनम् + -क्षयः loss of wealth; धनक्षये वर्धति जाठराग्निः Pt. 2. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनगर्व
धनम् + -गर्व, -गर्वित <i>a.</i> purse-proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनगर्वित|धनगर्व्वित
धनम् + -गर्व, -गर्वित <i>a.</i> purse-proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनच्छूः
धनम् + -छूः the numidian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनजातम्
धनम् + -जातम् all kinds of valuable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">Page0852-2</a>]<BR> possessions, aggregate property; सर्वेषां धनजातानामाददीताग्र्यमग्रजः Ms. 9. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनद|धनदः
धनम् + -द <i>a.</i> liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदः|धनद
धनम् + -द + .({@-दः@})<BR>—1 a liberal or munificent man.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera; जिगमिषुर्धनदाध्युषितां दिशम् R. 9. 25, 17. 80.<BR>—3 N. of fire.<BR>—4 = धनञ्जय (4) q. v. ˚अनुजः an epithet of Rāvaṇa; R. 12. 52, 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदण्डः|धनदण्ड|धनदंड
धनम् + -दण्डः punishment in the shape of a fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदायिन्
धनम् + -दायिन् <i>m.</i> fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनधानी
धनम् + -धानी treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनधान्यम्
धनम् + -धान्यम्<BR>—1 money and grain.<BR>—2 a spell for restraining certain magical weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपतिः|धनपति
धनम् + -पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera; तत्रागारं धनपतिगृहानुत्तरेणास्मदीयम् Me. 77, 7.<BR>—2 a treasurer.<BR>—3 = धनञ्जय (4) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपालः|धनपाल
धनम् + -पालः<BR>—1 a treasurer.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिशाचिका
धनम् + -पिशाचिका, -पिशाची ‘the demon of wealth’, an avaricious desire<BR> of wealth, greed, avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिशाची
धनम् + -पिशाचिका, -पिशाची ‘the demon of wealth’, an avaricious desire<BR> of wealth, greed, avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनप्रयोगः|धनप्रयोग
धनम् + -प्रयोगः usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमद|धनमदः
धनम् + -मद <i>a.</i> purse-proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमदः|धनमद
धनम् + -मद + .({@-दः@}) pride of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमूलम्
धनम् + -मूलम् principal, capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनलोभः|धनलोभ
धनम् + -लोभः avarice, cupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनव्ययः|धनव्यय
धनम् + -व्ययः<BR>—1 expenditure.<BR>—2 extravagance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसूः
धनम् + -सूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 mother of daughters; L. D. B.<BR>—2 <i>m.</i> the fork-tailed shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्थानम्
धनम् + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a treasury.<BR>—2 the second mansion from लग्न in a horoscope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहरः|धनहर
धनम् + -हरः<BR>—1 an heir.<BR>—2 a thief.<BR>—3 a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहार्य
धनम् + -हार्य <i>a.</i> to be won over by wealth; वहसि हि धनहार्यं<BR> पण्यभूतं शरीरम् Mk. 1. 31, 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहीन
धनम् + -हीन <i>a.</i> deprived of wealth, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकः|धनक
धनकः, -धनाया<BR> Avarice, greed, covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाया
धनकः, -धनाया<BR> Avarice, greed, covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनंजयः|धनञ्जय|धनंजय|धनञ्जयः
धनंजयः<BR>—1 N. of Arjuna (the name is thus derived in Mb. 4. 44. 13:− सर्वान्<BR> जनपदान् जित्वा वित्तमादाय केवलं । मध्ये धनस्य तिष्ठामि तेनाहुर्मां<BR> धनंजयम् ॥).<BR>—2 An epithet of fire.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 A kind of vital air nourishing the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनवत्|धनवन्त्
धनवत् <i>a.</i> Rich, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनवती
धनवत् + .{@-ती@} N. of the constellation धनिष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनायति
धनायति Den. P. To wish for wealth; अर्थितस्तु न महान् समीहते<BR> जीवितं किमु धनं धनायितुम् Ki. 13. 56; Mv. 4. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाश्री
धनाश्री N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिक|धनिकः
धनिक <i>a.</i> [धनमादेयत्वेनास्त्यस्य-ठन्]<BR>—1 Rich, wealthy.<BR>—2 Virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिकः|धनिक
धनिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A rich or wealthy man.<BR>—2 A moneylender, creditor; दापयेद्धनिकस्यार्थम् Ms. 8. 51; Y. 2. 55.<BR>—3 A husband.<BR>—4 The Vaiśya class; मुखजा ब्राह्मणास्तात बाहुजाः क्षत्रियाः स्मृताः ।<BR> ऊरुजा धनिनो राजन् पादजाः परिचारकाः ॥ Mb. 12. 296. 6.<BR>—5 An honest trader.<BR>—6 The प्रियङ्गु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिकः|धनिक
धनिक + .{@-कः, -कम्@} coriander (Mar. धणे, कोथिंबीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिकम्
धनिक + .{@-कः, -कम्@} coriander (Mar. धणे, कोथिंबीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिका
धनिक + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 A virtuous woman.<BR>—2 A wife, young woman.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (प्रियङ्गु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिन्
धनिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Rich, opulent, wealthy. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A wealthy man; धनिनः श्रोत्रियो राजा नदी वैद्यश्च पञ्चमः Cāṇ.<BR>—2 A creditor; Y. 2. 18; गृहीतानुक्रमाद् दाप्यो धनिनामधमर्णिकः 41; Ms. 8. 61.<BR>—3 The possessor of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठ
धनिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Very rich; (Superl. of धनिन् or धनवत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठा
धनिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठा@} N. of the twenty-third lunar mansion (consisting of four stars).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनी
धनी, धनीका A young girl or woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीका
धनी, धनीका A young girl or woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0852-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीयती
धनीयती Den. P. To wish for wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाश्री
धनाश्री <i>f.</i> N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीयकम्
धनी(ने)यकम् Coriander seed; see धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेयकम्
धनी(ने)यकम् Coriander seed; see धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुः|धनु
धनुः<BR>—1 A bow (perhaps for धनुस् q. v.).<BR>—2 N. of the प्रियङ्गु tree.<BR>—3 A measure of four <i>hastas</i>.<BR>—4 The sign Sagittarius of the zodiac.<BR>—5 An archer. ━<i>f.</i> A sandy shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस् <i>a.</i> [धन् शब्दे-उसि] Armed with a bow. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 A bow; धनुर्वंशविशुद्धोऽपि निर्गुणः किं करिष्यति Subhāṣ. धनुष्यमोघं<BR> समधत्त बाणम् Ku. 3. 66; so इन्द्रधनुः &c. (At the end of Bah. comp.<BR> धनुस् is changed to धन्वन्; अधिज्यधन्वा विचचार दावम् R. 2. 8).<BR>—2 A measure of length equal to four <i>hastas</i>; धनुःशतं परीणाहो<BR> ग्रामे क्षेत्रान्तरं भवेत् Y. 2. 167; Ms. 8. 237.<BR>—3 An arc of a circle.<BR>—4 The sign Sagittarius of the zodiac.<BR>—5 A desert; cf. धन्वन्. ━<i>m.</i> N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धनुराकार, धनुरासनम्, धनुष्कर, धनुष्काण्डम्, धनुष्खण्डम्, धनुर्गुणः, धनुर्ग्रहः, धनुर्ग्रहम्, धनुर्ज्या, धनुर्दुर्गम्, धनुर्द्रुमः, धनुर्धरः, धनुर्भृत्, धनुर्धारिन्, धनुष्पाणि, धनुर्मार्गः, धनुर्मासः, धनुर्मुष्टिः, धनुर्लता, धनुर्वातः, धनुर्विद्या, धनुर्वृक्षः, धनुर्वेदः, धनुर्वेदिन्, धनुःस्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुराकार
धनुस् + -आकार <i>a.</i> (धनुराकार) bow-shaped, curved, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुरासनम्
धनुस् + -आसनम् (धनुरासनम्) a particular mode of sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्कर|धनुष्करः
धनुस् + -कर (धनुष्कर) <i>a.</i> having or armed with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्करः|धनुष्कर
धनुस् + -कर + .({@-रः@}) a bow-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्काण्डम्
धनुस् + -काण्डम् (धनुष्काण्डम्) a bow and arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्खण्डम्
धनुस् + -खण्डम् (धनुष्खण्डम्) part of a bow; Me. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्गुणः|धनुर्गुण
धनुस् + -गुणः (धनुर्गुणः) a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्ग्रहः|धनुर्ग्रह
धनुस् + -ग्रहः (धनुर्ग्रहः), {@-ग्राहः@}<BR> an archer. धनुर्ग्रहवरो यस्य बाणखड्गास्त्रभृत्स्वयम्<BR> Rām. 2. 44. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्ग्रहम्
धनुस् + -ग्रहम् a measure, a cubit of 27 aṅgulas; Māna. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्ज्या
धनुस् + -ज्या (धनुर्ज्या) a bow-string; अनवरतधनुर्ज्यास्फालनक्रूरपूर्वम् Ś. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्दुर्गम्
धनुस् + -दुर्गम् (धनुर्दुर्गम्) a place protected by a desert; Ms. 7. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्द्रुमः|धनुर्द्रुम
धनुस् + -द्रुमः (धनुर्द्रुमः) a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धरः|धनुर्धर
धनुस् + -धरः, -भृत् <i>m.</i> (धनुर्धरः &c.)<BR>—1 an archer; धनुर्भृतोऽप्यस्य दयार्द्रभावम् R. 2. 11; धनुर्धरः<BR> केसरिणं ददर्श 29, 3. 31, 38, 39, 9. 11, 12. 97, 16. 77.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 the sign Sagittarius of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्भृत्
धनुस् + -धरः, -भृत् <i>m.</i> (धनुर्धरः &c.)<BR>—1 an archer; धनुर्भृतोऽप्यस्य दयार्द्रभावम् R. 2. 11; धनुर्धरः<BR> केसरिणं ददर्श 29, 3. 31, 38, 39, 9. 11, 12. 97, 16. 77.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 the sign Sagittarius of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धारिन्
धनुस् + -धारिन् (धनुर्धारिन्) <i>m.</i> an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्पाणि
धनुस् + -पाणि <i>a.</i> (धनुष्पाणि) armed with a bow, with a bow in hand;<BR> अहमेव धनुष्पाणिर्योद्धा समरमूर्धनि Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मार्गः|धनुर्मार्ग|धनुर्म्मार्ग
धनुस् + -मार्गः (धनुर्मार्गः) a line curved like a bow, a curve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मासः
धनुस् + -मासः (धनुर्मासः) The period during which the sun is<BR> in Sagittarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्मुष्टिः|धनुर्मुष्टि
धनुस् + -मुष्टिः (धनुर्मुष्टिः) a measure, a cubit of 26 aṅgulas; Māna. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्लता
धनुस् + -लता<BR>—1 bow.<BR>—2 Soma creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वातः|धनुर्वात
धनुस् + -वातः (धनुर्वातः) a kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्विद्या
धनुस् + -विद्या (धनुर्विद्या) the science of archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वृक्षः|धनुर्वृक्ष
धनुस् + -वृक्षः (धनुर्वृक्षः)<BR>—1 a bamboo.<BR>—2 the अश्वत्थ tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वेदः|धनुर्वेद|धनुर्व्वेदः
धनुस् + -वेदः (धनुर्वेदः) the science of archery, one of the<BR> four <i>Upavedas</i> q. v. चतुष्पादं धनुर्वेदं वेद पञ्चविधं द्विज ।<BR> रथनागाश्वपत्तीनां योधांश्चाश्रित्य कीर्तितम् ॥ यन्त्रमुक्तं पाणिमुक्तं<BR> मुक्तसन्धारितं तथा । अमुक्तं बाहुयुद्धं च पञ्चधा तत् प्रकीर्तितम् ॥ Agni P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वेदिन्
धनुस् + -वेदिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःस्तम्भः|धनुःस्तम्भ
धनुस् + -स्तम्भः Tetanus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्मत्|धनुष्मन्त्
धनुष्मत् <i>m.</i> An archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनू
धनू <i>f.</i> A bow. ━<i>m.</i> A store of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य <i>a.</i> [धनं लब्धा-यत्]<BR>—1 Bestowing or conferring wealth; धन्यं यशस्यं पुत्रीयमायुष्यं विजयावहम्<BR> Mb. 1. 67; Ms. 3. 106; धन्यानि शास्त्राण्यवेक्षेत 4. 19.<BR>—2 Wealthy, rich,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">Page0853-2</a>]<BR> opulent.<BR>—3 Blessed, fortunate, lucky, happy; धन्यं जीवनमस्य मार्गसरसः<BR> Bv. 1. 16, 4. 37; धन्या केयं स्थिता ते शिरसि M. 1. 1.<BR>—4 Excellent, good, virtuous; धन्योऽसि कृतकृत्योऽसि पावितं ते कुलं<BR> त्वया । यदविद्याबन्धमुक्त्या ब्रह्मीभवितुमिच्छसि ॥ Vivekacūḍāmaṇi. 5<BR> Wholesome, healthy; (इदं पायसं) प्रजाकरं गृहाण त्वं धन्यमारोग्यवर्धनम्<BR> Rām. 1. 16. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यः|धन्य
धन्य + .{@-न्यः@}<BR>—1 A lucky or blessed man, a fortunate being; धन्यास्तदङ्गरजसा मलिनीभवन्ति<BR> Ś. 7. 17; Bh. 1. 41; धन्यः कोऽपि न विक्रियां कलयते प्राप्ते नवे<BR> यौवने 1. 72.<BR>—2 An infidel, an atheist.<BR>—3 N. of a spell.<BR>—4 A source of wealth; धन्यानामुत्तमं दाक्ष्यं धनानामुत्तमं श्रुतम्<BR> Mb. 3. 313. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्या
धन्य + .{@-न्या@}<BR>—1 A nurse.<BR>—2 Coriander.<BR>—3 Myrobalan; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यम्
धन्य + .{@-न्यम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth, treasure.<BR>—2 Coriander.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धन्यवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यवादः|धन्यवाद
धन्य + -वादः<BR>—1 an expression of thanks, thanksgiving.<BR>—2 praise, applause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यंमन्य
धन्यंमन्य <i>a.</i> Considering oneself to be blessed or fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्याकम्
धन्याकम्<BR>—1 A plant bearing a small pungent seed used as a condiment.<BR>—2 The seed of this plant (coriander).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वम्
धन्वम् A bow (rarely used in classical literature); धन्वान्यादुधुवुस्तमाम्<BR> Śiva B. 13. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वः|धन्व|धन्वं
धन्वम् + .{@-न्वः@} A desert; मरुधन्वमतिक्रम्य Bhāg. 1. 10. 35.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धन्वचर, धन्वधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वचर
धन्वम् + -चर <i>a.</i> going in a desert-land; धन्वचरो न वंसगस्तृषाणः Rv. 5. 36. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वधिः|धन्वधि
धन्वम् + -धिः a bow-case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 A dry soil, desert, waste; एवं धन्वनि चम्पकस्य सकले संहारहेतावपि<BR> Bv. 1. 31; Mb. 1. 175. 5.<BR>—2 Shore, firm land.<BR>—3 The sky.<BR>—4 A bow; किमात्मभवधन्वना यदि सुसंयुताः कुन्तलाः Mv. 6. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धन्वदुर्गम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वदुर्गम्
धन्वन् + -दुर्गम् a fort inaccessible on account of a surrounding desert; cf. Ms. 7. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वनः|धन्वन
धन्वनः Alhagi Maurorum (Mar. धमासा); Mb. 12. 155. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वनम्
धन्वनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A bow.<BR>—2 A rain-bow.<BR>—3 the sign of the zodiac Sagittarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरम्
धन्वन्तरम् A measure of distance or length equal to four <i>hastas</i>;<BR> cf. दण्ड; वितस्तिः स्यादतो द्वाभ्यां हस्तः स्यात् तच्चतुष्टयम् । दण्डो<BR> धन्वन्तरम् …<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरिः|धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः
धन्वन्तरिः<BR>—1 N. of the physician of the gods, said to have been produced at the<BR> churning of the ocean with a cup of nectar in his hand; cf. चतुर्दशरत्न.<BR>—2 N. of the nine Ratnas at the court of Vikramāditya.<BR>—3 N. of a deity to whom oblations were offered to the North-east quarter; Ms. 3. 85.<BR>—4 N. of the sun; Mb. 3. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धन्वं चापोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Armed with a bow.<BR>—2 Cunning, shrewd. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An archer; के मम धन्विनोऽन्ये Ku. 3. 10; उत्कर्षः स च धन्विनां<BR> यदिषवः सिध्यन्ति लक्ष्ये चले Ś. 2. 5; यस्य तृणसमा बाणा यस्येन्धनसमं<BR> धनुः । यस्य प्राणसमा मौर्वी स धन्वी धन्विनां वरः ॥ Dhanur. 147.<BR>—2 An epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 The sign Sagittarius of the zodiac.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धन्विस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विस्थानम्
धन्विन् + -स्थानम् A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">Page0854-1</a>]<BR> posture of an archer; वैक्लवं समपादं च वैशाखं मण्डलं तथा ।<BR> प्रत्यालीढं तथा लीढं स्थानान्येतानि धन्विनाम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0853-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विनः|धन्विन
धन्विनः A hog (शूकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्
धम् €1 P. See ध्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम|धमः
धम <i>a.</i> (-मा, -मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धम् ध्माने-अच्] (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Blowing; अग्निंधम, नाडिंधम.<BR>—2 Melting, fusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमः|धम
धम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 An epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—3 Of Yama, the god of death.<BR>—4 Of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमकः|धमक
धमकः A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमधमा
धमधमा An onomatopoetic word expressive of the sound made by blowing<BR> with a bellows or a trumpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमधमाय्
धमधमाय् <i>Denom.</i> To blaze; मे उदराग्निर्धमधमायते Nāg. 1. 19, 20.<BR> Māl. 7. 1/2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमन|धमनः
धमन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A Blowing.<BR>—2 Cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनः|धमन
धमन + .{@-नः@} A kind of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनम्
धमन + .{@-नम्@} Melting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनिः|धमनि
धमनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A reed, blow-pipe; वेणुधमन्या प्रबोध्य Vaiśvadeva.<BR>—2 A tube or canal of the human body, tubular vessel, as a vein, a nerve, &c.<BR>—3 Throat, neck.<BR>—4 A speech.<BR>—5 Turmeric.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धमनिसंतत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनी
धमनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A reed, blow-pipe; वेणुधमन्या प्रबोध्य Vaiśvadeva.<BR>—2 A tube or canal of the human body, tubular vessel, as a vein, a nerve, &c.<BR>—3 Throat, neck.<BR>—4 A speech.<BR>—5 Turmeric.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धमनिसंतत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनिसंतत
धमनिः + -संतत <i>a.</i> emaciated, lank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनील
धमनील <i>a.</i> Full veined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमिः|धमि
धमिः <i>f.</i> The act of blowing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धमित्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमित्रम्
धमिः + -त्रम् an implement for kindling fire; see धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्ब्
धम्ब् €1 P. To go; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मलः|धम्मल
धम्मलः, धम्मिलः, धम्मिल्लः The braided and ornamented<BR> hair of a woman tied over the head and inter mixed with flowers, pearls<BR> &c.; आकुलाकुलगलद्धम्मिल्लम् Gīt. 2; उरसि निपतितानां स्रस्तधम्मिल्लकानाम्<BR> (वधूनाम्) Bh. 1. 49; Ś. Til. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिलः|धम्मिल
धम्मलः, धम्मिलः, धम्मिल्लः The braided and ornamented<BR> hair of a woman tied over the head and inter mixed with flowers, pearls<BR> &c.; आकुलाकुलगलद्धम्मिल्लम् Gīt. 2; उरसि निपतितानां स्रस्तधम्मिल्लकानाम्<BR> (वधूनाम्) Bh. 1. 49; Ś. Til. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्लः|धम्मिल्ल
धम्मलः, धम्मिलः, धम्मिल्लः The braided and ornamented<BR> hair of a woman tied over the head and inter mixed with flowers, pearls<BR> &c.; आकुलाकुलगलद्धम्मिल्लम् Gīt. 2; उरसि निपतितानां स्रस्तधम्मिल्लकानाम्<BR> (वधूनाम्) Bh. 1. 49; Ś. Til. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धय
धय <i>a.</i> (Usually at the end of comp.) Drinking, sucking; as in<BR> स्तनन्धय; फलानि धूमस्य धयानधोमुखान् N. 1. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर|धरः
धर <i>a.</i> (-रा, -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धृ-अच्] (Usually at the end of comp.) Holding,<BR> carrying, bearing, wearing, containing, possessing, endowed with, preserving,<BR> observing, &c.; as in अक्षधर, अंशुधर, गदाधर, गङ्गाधर, महीधर,<BR> असृग्धर, दिव्याम्बरधर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरः|धर
धर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A mountain; a hill-fort. शिवस्य यस्य हस्तेऽद्य धरौ सिंहपुरंदरौ<BR> Śiva B. 15. 17. उत्कं धरं द्रष्टुमवेक्ष्य शौरिमुत्कन्धरं दारुक<BR> इत्युवाच Śi. 4. 18; धरसंस्थः Ki. 15. 12.<BR>—2 A flock of cotton.<BR>—3 A frivolous or dissolute man (विट).<BR>—4 The king of the tortoises, <i>i. e.</i> Viṣṇu in his Kūrma incarnation.<BR>—5 N. of one of the Vasus.<BR>—6 A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरम्
धर + .{@-रम्@} poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरण|धरणं|धरणः
धरण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धृ-युच्] Bearing, preserving, holding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणः|धरण|धरणं
धरण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A ridge of land serving the purpose of a bridge; the side of a mountain.<BR>—2 The world.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR>—4 The female breast.<BR>—5 Rice, corn.<BR>—6 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">Page0854-2</a>]<BR> Himālaya (as king of mountains). —7 A dike, bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणम्
धरण + .{@-णम@}<BR>—1 Supporting, sustaining, upholding; सारं धरित्रीधरणक्षमं च<BR> Ku. 1. 17; धरणिधरणकिणचक्रगरिष्ठे Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 Possessing, bringing, procuring, &c.<BR>—3 Prop, stay, support.<BR>—4 Security.<BR>—5 A measure of weight equal to ten <i>palas</i>; पलं सुवर्णाश्चत्वारः<BR> पलानि धरणं दश Ms. 8. 135.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धरणप्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणप्रिया
धरण + -प्रिया N. of a Jaina deity executing the commands of the 19th Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिः|धरणि
धरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [धृ-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 The earth; लुठति धरणिशयने बहु विलपति तव नाम Gīt. 5.<BR>—2 Ground, soil.<BR>—3 A beam for a roof.<BR>—4 A vein.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धरणीश्वरः, धरणिकीलकः, धरणिकोश, धरणिजः, धरणिपुत्रः, धरणिसुतः, धरणिजा, धरणिपुत्री, धरणिसुता, धरणितलम्, धरणिधरः, धरणिधृतः,^1 धरणिपतिः, धरणिपूरः, धरणिप्लवः, धरणिबिडौजस्, धरणिभृत्, धरणिमण्डलम्, धरणिरुहः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणी
धरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [धृ-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 The earth; लुठति धरणिशयने बहु विलपति तव नाम Gīt. 5.<BR>—2 Ground, soil.<BR>—3 A beam for a roof.<BR>—4 A vein.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धरणीश्वरः, धरणिकीलकः, धरणिकोश, धरणिजः, धरणिपुत्रः, धरणिसुतः, धरणिजा, धरणिपुत्री, धरणिसुता, धरणितलम्, धरणिधरः, धरणिधृतः,^1 धरणिपतिः, धरणिपूरः, धरणिप्लवः, धरणिबिडौजस्, धरणिभृत्, धरणिमण्डलम्, धरणिरुहः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीश्वरः|धरणीश्वर
धरणिः + -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a king.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिकीलकः|धरणिकीलक
धरणिः + -कीलकः a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिकोश
धरणिः + -कोश N. of the Dictionary of धरणीदास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0854-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिजः|धरणिज
