धर्त्रम्
धर्त्रम् [धृ-त्र]<BR>—1 A house.<BR>—2 A prop, stay.<BR>—3 A sacrifice.<BR>—4 Virtue, moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मः|धर्म|धर्म्म|धर्म्मः
धर्मः [ध्रियते लोकोऽनेन, धरति लोकं वा धृ-मन्; cf. Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>—1 Religion; the customary observances of a caste, sect, &c.<BR>—2 Law, usage, practice, custom, ordinance, statute.<BR>—3 Religious or moral merit, virtue, righteousness, good works (regarded<BR> as one of the four ends of human existence); अनेन धर्मः सविशेषमद्य<BR> मे त्रिवर्गसारः प्रतिभाति भाविनि Ku. 5. 38, and see त्रिवर्ग also;<BR> एक एव सुहृद्धर्मो निधनेऽप्यनुयाति यः H. 1. 63.<BR>—4 Duty, prescribed course of conduct; षष्ठांशवृत्तेरपि धर्म एषः<BR> Ś. 5. 4; Ms. 1. 114.<BR>—5 Right, justice, equity, impartiality.<BR>—6 Piety, propriety, decorum.<BR>—7 Morality, ethics<BR>—8 Nature. disposition, character; उत्पत्स्यतेऽस्ति मम कोऽपि समानधर्मा<BR> Māl. 1. 6; प्राणि˚, जीव˚.<BR>—9 An essential quality, peculiarity, characteristic property, (peculiar)<BR> attribute; वदन्ति वर्ण्यावर्ण्यानां धर्मैक्यं दीपकं बुधाः Candr. 5. 45;<BR> Pt. 1. 304.<BR>—10 Manner, resemblance, likeness.<BR>—11 A sacrifice.<BR>—12 Good company, associating with the virtuous<BR>—13 Devotion, religious abstraction.<BR>—14 Manner, mode.<BR>—15 An <i>Upaniṣad</i> q. v.<BR>—16 N. of Yudhiṣṭhira, the eldest Pāṇḍava.<BR>—17 N. of Yama, the god of death.<BR>—18 A bow.<BR>—19 A drinker of <i>Soma</i> juice.<BR>—20 (In astrol.) N. of the ninth lunar mansion.<BR>—21 An <i>Arhat</i> of the Jainas.<BR>—22 The soul.<BR>—23 Mastery, great skill; दिव्यास्त्रगुणसंपन्नः परं धर्मं गतो युधि<BR> Rām. 3. 31. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मम्
धर्मः + .{@-र्मम्@} A virtuous deed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धर्माक्षरम्, धर्माङ्गः, धर्माधर्मौ, धर्माधिकरणम्, धर्माधिकरणिकः, धर्माधिकारिन्, धर्माधिकरणिन्, धर्माधिकारः, धर्माधिष्ठानम्, धर्माध्यक्षः, धर्मानुष्ठानम्, धर्मानुसारः, धर्मापेत, धर्मायनम्, धर्मारण्यम्, धर्मार्थौः, धर्मार्थम्, धर्मालीक, धर्मास्तिकायः, धर्माहन्, धर्मागमः, धर्माचार्यः, धर्मात्मजः, धर्मात्मता, धर्मात्मन्, धर्माश्रय, धर्माश्रित, धर्मासनम्, धर्मेन्द्रः, धर्मेशः, धर्मेप्सु, धर्मोत्तर, धर्मोपचायिन्, धर्मोपदेशः, धर्मोपदेशकः, धर्मकथकः, धर्मकर्मन्, धर्मकथादरिद्रः, धर्मकाम, धर्मकायः, धर्मकारणम्, धर्मकीलः, धर्मकृत्, धर्मकेतुः, धर्मकोशः, धर्मकोषः, धर्मक्रिया, धर्मकृत्यम्, धर्मक्षेत्रम्, धर्मगुप्त, धर्मग्रन्थः, धर्मघटः, धर्मघ्न, धर्मचक्रः, धर्मचरणम्, धर्मचर्या, धर्मचारिन्, धर्मचारिणी, धर्मचिन्तक, धर्मचिन्तनम्, धर्मचिन्ता, धर्मच्छलः, धर्मजः, धर्मजन्मन्, धर्मजिज्ञासा, धर्मजीवन, धर्मज्ञ, धर्मत्यागः, धर्मदक्षिणा, धर्मदानम्, धर्मदुघा, धर्मद्रवी, धर्मदाराः, धर्मद्रुह्, धर्मद्रोहिन्, धर्मधातुः, धर्मध्वजः, धर्मध्वजिन्, धर्मनन्दनः, धर्मनाथः, धर्मनाभः, धर्मनिबन्धिन्, धर्मनिवेशः, धर्मनिष्ठ, धर्मनिष्पत्तिः, धर्मपत्नी, धर्मपथः, धर्मपर, धर्मपरिणामः, धर्मपाठकः, धर्मपालः, धर्मपीडा, धर्मपुत्रः, धर्मप्रचारः, धर्मप्रतिरूपकः, धर्मप्रधान, धर्मप्रवक्तृ, धर्मप्रवचनम्, धर्मप्रेक्ष्य, धर्मबाणिजिकः, धर्मवाणिजिकः, धर्मबाह्य,^1 धर्मभगिनी, धर्मभागिनी, धर्मभाणकः, धर्मभिक्षुकः, धर्मभृत्, धर्मभ्रातृ, धर्ममहामात्रः, धर्ममूलम्, धर्ममेघः, धर्मयुगम्, धर्मयूपः, धर्मयोनिः, धर्मरति, धर्मरत्नम्, धर्मराज्, धर्मराज, धर्मराजः, धर्मराजन्, धर्मराजिका, धर्मरोधिन्, धर्मलक्षणम्, धर्मलोपः, धर्मवत्सल, धर्मवर्तिन्, धर्मवर्धनः, धर्मवादः, धर्मवासरः, धर्मवाहनः, धर्मविद्, धर्मविद्या, धर्मविधिः, धर्मविप्लवः, धर्मवीरः, धर्मवृद्ध, धर्मवैतंसिकः, धर्मव्यवस्था, धर्मशाला, धर्मशासनम्, धर्मशास्त्रम्, धर्मशील, धर्मशुद्धिः, धर्मसंहिता, धर्मसंगः, धर्मसंगीतिः, धर्मसभा, धर्मसमयः, धर्मसहायः, धर्मसूः, धर्मसूत्रम्, धर्मसेतुः, धर्मसेवनम्, धर्मस्थः, धर्मस्थीय, धर्मस्वामिन्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माक्षरम्
धर्मः + -अक्षरम् (pl.) holy mantras; a formula of faith; धर्माक्षराण्युदाहरामि Mk. 8. 45-46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माङ्गः|धर्माङ्ग|धर्मांग
धर्मः + -अङ्गः + ({@-ङ्गा@} <i>f.</i>)<BR> the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माङ्गा
धर्मः + -अङ्गः + ({@-ङ्गा@} <i>f.</i>)<BR> the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधर्मौ
धर्मः + -अधर्मौ <i>m.</i> (du.) right and wrong, religion and irreligion;<BR> धर्माधर्मौ सपदि गलितौ पुण्यपापे विशीर्णे. ˚विद् <i>m.</i> a Mīmāṃsaka<BR> who knows the right and wrong course of action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणम्
धर्मः + -अधिकरणम्<BR>—1 administration of the laws. —2 a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणः|धर्माधिकरण|धर्म्माधिकरण|धर्म्माधिकरणं|धर्म्माधिकरणः
धर्मः + -अधिकरणम् + .({@-णः@}) a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणिकः|धर्माधिकरणिक
धर्मः + -अधिकरणिकः, -अधिकारिन् <i>m.</i> a judge, magistrate, any judicial functionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकारिन्|धर्म्माधिकारिन्
धर्मः + -अधिकरणिकः, -अधिकारिन् <i>m.</i> a judge, magistrate, any judicial functionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकरणिन्|धर्म्माधिकरणिन्
धर्मः + -अधिकरणिन् <i>m.</i> a judge, magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिकारः|धर्माधिकार|धर्म्माधिकार
धर्मः + -अधिकारः —1 superintendence of religious affairs; Ś. 1.<BR>—2 administration of justice.<BR>—3 the office of a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माधिष्ठानम्
धर्मः + -अधिष्ठानम् a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माध्यक्षः|धर्माध्यक्ष|धर्म्माध्यक्ष|धर्म्माध्यक्षः
धर्मः + -अध्यक्षः<BR>—1 a judge.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मानुष्ठानम्
धर्मः + -अनुष्ठानम् acting according to religion, virtuous or moral conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मानुसारः|धर्मानुसार|धर्म्मानुसार
धर्मः + -अनुसारः conformity to virtue or justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मापेत|धर्म्मापेत
धर्मः + -अपेत <i>a.</i> deviating from virtue, wicked, immoral, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मापेतम्
धर्मः + -अपेत + .({@-तम्@}) vice, immorality,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">Page0855-2</a>]<BR> injustice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मायनम्
धर्मः + -अयनम् course of law, law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मारण्यम्
धर्मः + -अरण्यम् a sacred or penance grove, a wood inhabited by ascetics;<BR> धर्मारण्यं प्रविशति गजः Śi. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मार्थौः
धर्मः + -अर्थौः religious merit and wealth; धर्मार्थौ यत्र न स्याताम् Ms. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मार्थम्
धर्मः + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 for religious purposes.<BR>—2 justly, according to justice or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मालीक
धर्मः + -अलीक <i>a.</i> having a false character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मास्तिकायः|धर्मास्तिकाय
धर्मः + -अस्तिकायः (with Jainas) the category or predicament of virtue;<BR> cf. अस्तिकाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माहन्
धर्मः + -अहन् Yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मागमः|धर्मागम
धर्मः + -आगमः a religious statute, lawbook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माचार्यः|धर्माचार्य|धर्माचार्य्य
धर्मः + -आचार्यः<BR>—1 a religious teacher.<BR>—2 a teacher of law or customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मजः|धर्मात्मज
धर्मः + -आत्मजः an epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मता
धर्मः + -आत्मता religious-mindedness; justice, virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मात्मन्|धर्म्मात्मन्
धर्मः + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> just, righteous, pious, virtuous. ━(<i>m.</i>) a saint, a pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माश्रय
धर्मः + -आश्रय, -आश्रित <i>a.</i> righteous, virtuous; धर्माश्रयं पापिनः<BR> (निन्दन्ति) Pt. 1. 415.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माश्रित
धर्मः + -आश्रय, -आश्रित <i>a.</i> righteous, virtuous; धर्माश्रयं पापिनः<BR> (निन्दन्ति) Pt. 1. 415.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मासनम्
धर्मः + -आसनम् the throne of justice, judgment-seat, tribunal; न संभावितमद्य<BR> धर्मासनमध्यासितुम् Ś. 6; धर्मासनाद्विशति वासगृहं नरेन्द्रः U. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मेन्द्रः|धर्मेन्द्र|धर्मेंद्र
धर्मः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः an epithet of Yama; पितॄणामिव धर्मेन्द्रः Mb. 7. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मेशः|धर्मेश
धर्मः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः an epithet of Yama; पितॄणामिव धर्मेन्द्रः Mb. 7. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मेप्सु
धर्मः + -ईप्सु <i>a.</i> wishing to gain religious merit; Ms. 10. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोत्तर
धर्मः + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> ‘rich in virtue’, chiefly characterized by justice,<BR> eminently just and impartial; धर्मोत्तरं मध्यममाश्रयन्ते R. 13. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपचायिन्
धर्मः + -उपचायिन् <i>a.</i> religious; यच्च वः प्रेक्षमाणानां सर्वधर्मोपचायिनाम्<BR> Mb. 5. 137. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपदेशः|धर्मोपदेश|धर्म्मोपदेश
धर्मः + -उपदेशः<BR>—1 instruction in law or duty, religious or moral instruction. आर्षं<BR> धर्मोपदेशं च वेदशास्त्राविरोधिना । यस्तर्केणानुसंधत्ते स धर्मं वेद<BR> नेतरः ॥ Ms. 12. 106.<BR>—2 the collective body of laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मोपदेशकः|धर्मोपदेशक|धर्म्मोपदेशक|धर्म्मोपदेशकः
धर्मः + -उपदेशकः<BR>—1 a teacher of the law.<BR>—2 a spiritual teacher, a Guru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकथकः|धर्मकथक
धर्मः + -कथकः an expounder of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकर्मन्|धर्म्मकर्म्मन्
धर्मः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-कार्यम्, -क्रिया@}<BR>—1 any act of duty or religion, any moral or religious observance, a religious act or rite.<BR>—2 virtuous conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकथादरिद्रः|धर्मकथादरिद्र|धर्म्मकथादरिद्र
धर्मः + -कथादरिद्रः the <i>Kali</i> age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकाम|धर्म्मकाम
धर्मः + -काम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devoted to virtue.<BR>—2 observing duty or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकायः|धर्मकाय|धर्म्मकाय|धर्म्मकायः
धर्मः + -कायः<BR>—1 an epithet of Buddha.<BR>—2 a Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकारणम्
धर्मः + -कारणम् Cause of virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकीलः|धर्मकील|धर्म्मकील|धर्म्मकीलः
धर्मः + -कीलः<BR>—1 a grant, royal edict or decree.<BR>—2 husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकृत्|धर्म्मकृत्
धर्मः + -कृत् <i>a.</i> observing duty, acting justly. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a pious man; धर्माधर्मविहीनोऽपि धर्ममर्यादास्थापनार्थं धर्ममेव<BR> करोतीति धर्मकृत् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकेतुः|धर्मकेतु|धर्म्मकेतु|धर्म्मकेतुः
धर्मः + -केतुः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकोशः|धर्मकोश
धर्मः + -कोशः, -कोषः the collective body of laws or duties; धर्मकोषस्य<BR> गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकोषः|धर्मकोष|धर्म्मकोष
धर्मः + -कोशः, -कोषः the collective body of laws or duties; धर्मकोषस्य<BR> गुप्तये Ms. 1. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मक्रिया|धर्म्मक्रिया
धर्मः + -क्रिया, -कृत्यम् any act of religion, any moral or religious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मकृत्यम्
धर्मः + -क्रिया, -कृत्यम् any act of religion, any moral or religious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मक्षेत्रम्
धर्मः + -क्षेत्रम्<BR>—1 Bhāratavarṣa (the land of religion).<BR>—2 N. of a plain near Delhi, the scene of the great battle between the<BR> Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas; धर्मक्षेत्रे कुरुक्षेत्रे समवेता युयुत्सवः Bg. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मक्षेत्रः|धर्मक्षेत्र|धर्म्मक्षेत्र|धर्म्मक्षेत्रं
धर्मः + -क्षेत्रम् + .({@-त्रः@}) a virtuous or pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मगुप्त|धर्मगुप्तः
धर्मः + -गुप्त <i>a.</i> observing and protecting religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मगुप्तः|धर्मगुप्त
धर्मः + -गुप्त + .({@-प्तः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मग्रन्थः
धर्मः + -ग्रन्थः a sacred work or scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मघटः|धर्मघट|धर्म्मघटः
धर्मः + -घटः a jar of fragrant water offered daily (to a Brāhmaṇa)<BR> in the month of Vaiśākha; एष धर्मघटो दत्तो ब्रह्माविष्णुशिवात्मकः ।<BR> अस्य प्रदानात् सफला मम सन्तु मनोरथाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मघ्न|धर्म्मघ्न
धर्मः + -घ्न <i>a.</i> immoral, unlawful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचक्रः|धर्मचक्र|धर्म्मचक्र|धर्म्मचक्रः
धर्मः + -चक्रः<BR>—1 The wheel or range of the law; Buddh. Jain.<BR>—2 a Buddha. ˚भृत् <i>m.</i> a Buddha or Jaina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचरणम्
धर्मः + -चरणम्, -चर्या observance of the law, performance of religious<BR> duties; शिवेन भर्त्रा सह धर्मचर्या कार्या त्वया मुक्तविचारयेति<BR> Ku. 7. 83; वयसि प्रथमे, मतौ चलायां बहुदोषां हि वदन्ति धर्मचर्याम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">Page0856-1</a>]<BR> Bu. C. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचर्या
धर्मः + -चरणम्, -चर्या observance of the law, performance of religious<BR> duties; शिवेन भर्त्रा सह धर्मचर्या कार्या त्वया मुक्तविचारयेति<BR> Ku. 7. 83; वयसि प्रथमे, मतौ चलायां बहुदोषां हि वदन्ति धर्मचर्याम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">Page0856-1</a>]<BR> Bu. C. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0855-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचारिन्|धर्म्मचारिन्
धर्मः + -चारिन् <i>a.</i> practising virtue, observing the law, virtuous,<BR> righteous; स चेत्स्वयं कर्मसु धर्मचारिणां त्वमन्तरायो भवसि R. 3. 45.<BR>━(<i>m.</i>) an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचारिणी|धर्म्मचारिणी
धर्मः + -चारिणी<BR>—1 a wife.<BR>—2 a chaste or virtuous wife. cf. सह˚; इयं चोर्वशी यावदायुस्तव<BR> सहधर्मचारिणी भवत्विति V. 5. 19/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचिन्तक
धर्मः + -चिन्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 studying or familiar with duty.<BR>—2 reflecting on the law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचिन्तनम्
धर्मः + -चिन्तनम्, -चिन्ता study of virtue, consideration of moral duties,<BR> moral reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिंता|धर्म्मचिन्ता
धर्मः + -चिन्तनम्, -चिन्ता study of virtue, consideration of moral duties,<BR> moral reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मच्छलः|धर्मच्छल
धर्मः + -च्छलः fraudulent transgression of law or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजः|धर्मज
धर्मः + -जः<BR>—1 ‘duly or lawfully born’, a legitimate son; cf. Ms. 9. 107.<BR>—2 N. of युधिष्ठिर; Mb. 15. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजन्मन्
धर्मः + -जन्मन् <i>m.</i> N. of युधिष्ठिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजिज्ञासा
धर्मः + -जिज्ञासा inquiry into religion or the proper course of conduct;<BR> अथातो धर्मजिज्ञासा Jaiminiʼs Sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजीवन|धर्मजीवनः|धर्म्मजीवन
धर्मः + -जीवन <i>a.</i> one who acts according to the rules of his caste<BR> or fulfils prescribed duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मजीवनः|धर्मजीवन|धर्म्मजीवन
धर्मः + -जीवन + .({@-नः@}) a Brāhmaṇa who maintains himself by assisting other men<BR> in the performance of their religious rites; यश्चापि धर्मसमयात्प्रच्युतो<BR> धर्मजीवनः Ms. 9. 273.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मज्ञ|धर्म्मज्ञ|धर्म्मज्ञः
धर्मः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing what is right, conversant with civil or religious law; Ms. 7. 141, 8. 179, 10. 127.<BR>—2 just, righteous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मत्यागः|धर्मत्याग
धर्मः + -त्यागः abandoning oneʼs religion, apostacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मदक्षिणा
धर्मः + -दक्षिणा a fee for instruction in the law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मदानम्
धर्मः + -दानम् a charitable gift (made without any self-interest.) पात्रेभ्यो<BR> दीयते नित्यमनपेक्ष्य प्रयोजनम् । केवलं धर्मबुद्धपा यद् धर्मदानं<BR> प्रचक्षते ॥ Ms. 3. 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मदुघा
धर्मः + -दुघा a cow milked for religious purposes only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मद्रवी|धर्म्मद्रवी
धर्मः + -द्रवी N. of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मदाराः
धर्मः + -दाराः <i>m.</i> (pl.) a lawful wife; स्त्रीणां भर्ता धर्मदाराश्च<BR> पुंसाम् Māl. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मद्रुह्
धर्मः + -द्रुह् <i>a.</i> violating the law or right; निसर्गेण स धर्मस्य<BR> गोप्ता धर्मद्रुहो वयम् Mv. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मद्रोहिन्|धर्म्मद्रोहिन्
धर्मः + -द्रोहिन् <i>m.</i> a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मधातुः|धर्मधातु|धर्म्मधातु|धर्म्मधातुः
धर्मः + -धातुः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मध्वजः|धर्मध्वज
धर्मः + -ध्वजः, -ध्वजिन् <i>m.</i> a religious hypocrite, an impostor; Bhāg. 3. 32. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मध्वजिन्|धर्म्मध्वजिन्
धर्मः + -ध्वजः, -ध्वजिन् <i>m.</i> a religious hypocrite, an impostor; Bhāg. 3. 32. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनन्दनः|धर्मनन्दन|धर्मनंदन|धर्म्मनन्दन
धर्मः + -नन्दनः an epithet of युधिष्ठिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनाथः|धर्मनाथ
धर्मः + -नाथः a legal protector, rightful master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनाभः|धर्मनाभ|धर्म्मनाभ
धर्मः + -नाभः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनिबन्धिन्|धर्म्मनिबन्धिन्
धर्मः + -निबन्धिन् <i>a.</i> pious, holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनिवेशः|धर्मनिवेश
धर्मः + -निवेशः religious devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनिष्ठ
धर्मः + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> devoted to religion or virtue; श्रीमन्तः पान्तु<BR> पृथ्वीं प्रशमितरिपवो धर्मनिष्ठाश्च भूपाः Mk. 10. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मनिष्पत्तिः|धर्मनिष्पत्ति|धर्म्मनिष्पत्ति
धर्मः + -निष्पत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 discharge or fulfilment of duty.<BR>—2 moral or religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपत्नी|धर्म्मपत्नी
धर्मः + -पत्नी a lawful wife; R. 2. 2, 20, 72, 8. 7; Y. 2. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपथः|धर्मपथ
धर्मः + -पथः the way of virtue, a virtuous course of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपर|धर्म्मपर
धर्मः + -पर <i>a.</i> religious-minded, pious, righteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपरिणामः|धर्मपरिणाम
धर्मः + -परिणामः rise of righteous conduct in the heart (Jainism); cf.<BR> also एतेन भूतेन्द्रियेषु धर्मलक्षणावस्थापरिणामा व्याख्याताः Yogadarśana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपाठकः|धर्मपाठक|धर्म्मपाठक
धर्मः + -पाठकः a teacher of civil or religious law; Ms. 12. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपालः|धर्मपाल
धर्मः + -पालः ‘protector of the law’, said metaphorically of (दण्ड)<BR> ‘punishment or chastisement’, or ‘sword’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपीडा
धर्मः + -पीडा transgressing the law, an offence against law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मपुत्रः|धर्मपुत्र|धर्म्मपुत्त्र|धर्म्मपुत्त्रः|धर्म्मपुत्र
धर्मः + -पुत्रः<BR>—1 a lawful son, a son begotten from a sense of duty and not from mere<BR> lust or sensual pleasure.<BR>—2 an epithet of युधिष्ठिर.<BR>—3 any one regarded as a son for religious purposes, a spiritual son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रचारः|धर्मप्रचार
धर्मः + -प्रचारः (fig.) sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रतिरूपकः|धर्मप्रतिरूपक
धर्मः + -प्रतिरूपकः a counterfeit of virtue; Ms. 11. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रधान|धर्म्मप्रधान
धर्मः + -प्रधान <i>a.</i> eminent in piety; धर्मप्रधानं पुरुषं तपसा<BR> हतकिल्बिषम् Ms. 4. 243.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रवक्तृ|धर्म्मप्रवक्तृ
धर्मः + -प्रवक्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an expounder of the law, a legal adviser.<BR>—2 a religious teacher, preacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रवचनम्
धर्मः + -प्रवचनम्<BR>—1 the science of duty; U. 5. 23.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">Page0856-2</a>]<BR>—2 expounding the law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रवचनः|धर्मप्रवचन
धर्मः + -प्रवचनम् + .({@-नः@}) an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रेक्ष्य
धर्मः + -प्रेक्ष्य <i>a.</i> religious or virtuous (धर्मदृष्टि); Rām. 2. 85. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबाणिजिकः|धर्मबाणिजिक|धर्म्मबाणिजिकः
धर्मः + -बाणिजिकः, -वाणिजिकः<BR>—1 one who tries to make profit out of his virtue like a merchant.<BR>—2 one who performs religious rites with a view to reward, like a merchant<BR> dealing in transactions for profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवाणिजिकः|धर्मवाणिजिक
धर्मः + -बाणिजिकः, -वाणिजिकः<BR>—1 one who tries to make profit out of his virtue like a merchant.<BR>—2 one who performs religious rites with a view to reward, like a merchant<BR> dealing in transactions for profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबाह्य
धर्मः + -बाह्य^1 <i>a.</i> contrary to religion or what is right.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभगिनी
धर्मः + -भगिनी<BR>—1 a lawful sister.<BR>—2 a daughter of the spiritual preceptor.<BR>—3 a spiritual sister, any one regarded as a sister or discharging the<BR> same religious duties एतस्मिन्विहारे मम धर्मभगिनी तिष्ठति Mk. 8. 46/47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभागिनी|धर्म्मभागिनी
धर्मः + -भागिनी a virtuous wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभाणकः|धर्मभाणक|धर्म्मभाणक|धर्म्मभाणकः
धर्मः + -भाणकः a lecturer or public reader who reads and explains to<BR> audiences sacred books like the Bhārata, Bhāgavata, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभिक्षुकः|धर्मभिक्षुक|धर्म्मभिक्षुक
धर्मः + -भिक्षुकः a mendicant from virtuous motives; Ms. 11. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभृत्
धर्मः + -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 ‘a preserver or defender of justice’, a king.<BR>—2 a virtuous person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभ्रातृ|धर्म्मभ्रातृ
धर्मः + -भ्रातृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a fellow religious student, a spiritual brother.<BR>—2 any one regarded as a brother from discharging the same religious duties.<BR> वानप्रस्थयतिब्रह्मचारिणां रिक्थभागिनः । क्रमेणाचार्यसच्छिष्यधर्मभ्रात्रेकतीर्थिनः ॥<BR> Y. 2. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममहामात्रः|धर्ममहामात्र
धर्मः + -महामात्रः a minister of religion, a minister in charge of religious affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममूलम्
धर्मः + -मूलम् the foundation of civil or religious law, the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघः|धर्ममेघ
धर्मः + -मेघः a particular Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयुगम्
धर्मः + -युगम् the Kṛta age; अथ धर्मयुगे तस्मिन्योगधर्ममनुष्ठिता ।<BR> महीमनुचचारैका सुलभा नाम भिक्षुकी Mb. 12. 320. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयूपः|धर्मयूप|धर्म्मयूप
धर्मः + -यूपः, -योनिः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयोनिः|धर्मयोनि
धर्मः + -यूपः, -योनिः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरति
धर्मः + -रति <i>a.</i> ‘delighting in virtue or justice’, righteous, pious,<BR> just; तस्य धर्मरतेरासीद् वृद्धत्वं जरसा विना. R. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरत्नम्
धर्मः + -रत्नम् N. of a Jaina स्मृतिग्रन्थ prepared by Jīmūtavāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज्|धर्म्मराज्
धर्मः + -राज् ━<i>m.</i> an epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज|धर्मराजः|धर्म्मराज|धर्म्मराजः
धर्मः + -राज <i>a.</i> धर्मशील q. v.; धर्मराजेन जनकेन महात्मना<BR> (विदेहान् रक्षितान्) Mb. 12. 325. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराजः|धर्मराज|धर्म्मराज|धर्म्मराजः
धर्मः + -राजः an epithet of<BR>—1 Yama.<BR>—2 Jina.<BR>—3 युधिष्ठिर.<BR>—4 a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराजन्
धर्मः + -राजन् <i>m.</i> N. of युधिष्ठिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराजिका
धर्मः + -राजिका a monument, a stūpa (Sārnāth Inscrip. of Mahīpāla; Ind. Ant. Vol. 14, p. 140.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरोधिन्|धर्म्मरोधिन्
धर्मः + -रोधिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 opposed to law, illegal, unlawful.<BR>—2 immoral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मलक्षणम्
धर्मः + -लक्षणम्<BR>—1 the essential mark of law.<BR>—2 the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मलक्षणा
धर्मः + -लक्षणम् + .({@-णा@}) the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मलोपः|धर्मलोप
धर्मः + -लोपः<BR>—1 irreligion, immorality.<BR>—2 violation of duty; धर्मलोपभयाद्राज्ञीमृतुस्नातामिमां स्मरन् R. 1. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवत्सल
धर्मः + -वत्सल <i>a.</i> loving piety or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवर्तिन्
धर्मः + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> just, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवर्धनः|धर्मवर्धन
धर्मः + -वर्धनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवादः|धर्मवाद
धर्मः + -वादः discussion about law or duty, religious controversy; अनुकल्पः<BR> परो धर्मो धर्मवादैस्तु केवलम् Mb. 12. 165. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवासरः|धर्मवासर|धर्म्मवासर|धर्म्मवासरः
धर्मः + -वासरः<BR>—1 the day of full moon.<BR>—2 yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवाहनः|धर्मवाहन|धर्म्मवाहन|धर्म्मवाहनः
धर्मः + -वाहनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a buffalo (being the vehicle of Yama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविद्|धर्म्मविद्
धर्मः + -विद् <i>a.</i> familiar with the law (civil or religous). ˚उत्तमः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविद्या|धर्म्मविद्या
धर्मः + -विद्या knowledge of the law or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविधिः|धर्मविधि|धर्म्मविधि
धर्मः + -विधिः a legal precept or injunction; एष धर्मविधिः कृत्स्नश्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य<BR> कीर्तितः Ms. 10. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविप्लवः|धर्मविप्लव|धर्म्मविप्लव
धर्मः + -विप्लवः violation of duty, immorality. विवेचनम्<BR>—1 judicial investigation; यस्य शूद्रस्तु कुरुते राज्ञो धर्मविवेचनम् ।<BR> तस्य सीदति तद्राष्ट्रं पङ्के गौरिव पश्यतः ॥ Ms. 8. 21.<BR>—2 dissertation on duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवीरः|धर्मवीर|धर्म्मवीर
धर्मः + -वीरः (in Rhet.) the sentiment of heroism arising out of virtue<BR> or piety, the sentiment of chivalrous piety; the following instance is<BR> given in R. G.:− सपदि विलयमेतु राज्यलक्ष्मीरुपरि पतन्त्वथवा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">Page0857-1</a>]<BR> कृपाणधाराः । अपहरतुतरां शिरः कृतान्तो मम तु मतिर्न मनागपैतु<BR> धर्मात् ॥ स च दानधर्मयुद्धैर्दयया च समन्वितश्चतुर्धा स्यात् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0856-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवृद्ध|धर्म्मवृद्ध
धर्मः + -वृद्ध <i>a.</i> advanced in virtue or piety; न धर्मवृद्धेषु वयः<BR> समीक्ष्यते Ku. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवैतंसिकः|धर्मवैतंसिक|धर्म्मवैतंसिकः
धर्मः + -वैतंसिकः one who gives away money unlawfully acquired in the<BR> hope of appearing generous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मव्यवस्था
धर्मः + -व्यवस्था <i>m.</i> judicial decision, decisive sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशाला|धर्म्मशाला
धर्मः + -शाला<BR>—1 a court of justice, tribunal.<BR>—2 any charitable institution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशासनम्
धर्मः + -शासनम्, -शास्त्रम् a code of laws, jurisprudence; न धर्मशास्त्रं<BR> पठतीति कारणम् H. 1. 17; Y. 1. 5. [मनुर्यमो वसिष्ठोऽत्रिः दक्षो<BR> विष्णुस्तथाङ्गिराः । उशना वाक्पतिर्व्यास आपस्तम्बो ऽथ गौतमः ॥ कात्यायनो<BR> नारदश्च याज्ञवल्क्यः पराशरः । संवर्तश्चैव शङ्खश्च हारीतो लिखितस्तथा<BR> ॥ एतैर्यानि प्रणीतानि धर्मशास्त्राणि वै पुरा । तान्येवातिप्रमाणानि न हन्तव्यानि हेतुभिः ॥]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशास्त्रम्
धर्मः + -शासनम्, -शास्त्रम् a code of laws, jurisprudence; न धर्मशास्त्रं<BR> पठतीति कारणम् H. 1. 17; Y. 1. 5. [मनुर्यमो वसिष्ठोऽत्रिः दक्षो<BR> विष्णुस्तथाङ्गिराः । उशना वाक्पतिर्व्यास आपस्तम्बो ऽथ गौतमः ॥ कात्यायनो<BR> नारदश्च याज्ञवल्क्यः पराशरः । संवर्तश्चैव शङ्खश्च हारीतो लिखितस्तथा<BR> ॥ एतैर्यानि प्रणीतानि धर्मशास्त्राणि वै पुरा । तान्येवातिप्रमाणानि न हन्तव्यानि हेतुभिः ॥]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशील|धर्म्मशील|धर्म्मशीलः
धर्मः + -शील <i>a.</i> just, pious, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशुद्धिः|धर्मशुद्धि
धर्मः + -शुद्धिः a correct knowledge of the law; प्रत्यक्षं चानुमानं<BR> च शास्त्रं च विविधागमम् । त्रयं सुविदितं कार्यं धर्मशुद्धिमभीप्सता ॥<BR> Ms. 12. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसंहिता|धर्म्मसंहिता
धर्मः + -संहिता a code of laws (especially compiled by sages like Manu,<BR> Yājñavalkya, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसंगः|धर्मसङ्ग|धर्मसंग|धर्म्मसङ्ग
धर्मः + -संगः<BR>—1 attachment to justice or virtue.<BR>—2 hypocrisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसंगीतिः|धर्मसङ्गीति
धर्मः + -संगीतिः<BR>—1 discussion about law.<BR>—2 (with Buddhists) a council.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसभा|धर्म्मसभा
धर्मः + -सभा a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसमयः|धर्मसमय
धर्मः + -समयः a legal obligation; यश्चापि धर्मसमयात्प्रच्युतो धर्मजीवनः Ms. 9. 273.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसहायः|धर्मसहाय
धर्मः + -सहायः a partner or companion in the discharge of religious duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसूः|धर्म्मसूः
धर्मः + -सूः <i>m.</i> the fork-tailed shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसूत्रम्
धर्मः + -सूत्रम् a book on पूर्वमीमांसा written by Jaimini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसेतुः|धर्मसेतु
धर्मः + -सेतुः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मसेवनम्
धर्मः + -सेवनम् fulfilment of duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मस्थः|धर्मस्थ
धर्मः + -स्थः a judge; धर्मस्थः कारणैरेतैहींनं तमिति निदिंशेत् Ms. 8. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मस्थीय
धर्मः + -स्थीय <i>a.</i> Concerning law; धर्मस्थीयं तृतीयं प्रकरणम् Kau. A. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मस्वामिन्
धर्मः + -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मतः|धर्मत
धर्मतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to law or rule, rightly, religiously, justly.<BR>—2 Virtuously, righteously.<BR>—3 From a virtuous or religious motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मत्वम्
धर्मत्वम्<BR>—1 Morality, virtue, righteousness.<BR>—2 Inherent property or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मन्|धर्म्मन्
धर्मन् <i>m.</i> [धृ-मनिन्] —1 A preserver, maintainer, supporter. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 A religious rite.<BR>—2 Support, stay.<BR>—3 Religion, duty.<BR>—4 Law, custom.<BR>—5 A mode, manner.<BR>—6 Characteristic quality or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममय|धर्म्ममय
धर्ममय <i>a.</i> Virtuous, righteous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयु|धर्म्मयु|धर्म्मयुः
धर्मयु <i>a.</i> Virtuous, just, pious, righteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवत्|धर्मवन्त्|धर्म्मवत्
धर्मवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Holy, virtuous.<BR>—2 Upright, just.<BR>—3 Lawful, legal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिन्|धर्म्मिन्
धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> [धर्मोऽस्त्यस्य-इनि]<BR>—1 Virtuous, just, pious.<BR>—2 Knowing oneʼs duties.<BR>—3 Obeying the law.<BR>—4 Having the properties of, having the nature, peculiar properties or<BR> characteristics of anything (at the end of comp.); षट् सुता द्विजधर्मिणः<BR> Ms. 10. 41; कल्पवृक्षफलधर्मि काङ्क्षितम् R. 11. 50.<BR>—5 Following the habits of any person. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठः|धर्म्मिष्ठ
धर्मिष्ठ <i>a.</i> (Superl. of धर्मिन्) Very pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठः|धर्मिष्ठ|धर्म्मिष्ठ
धर्मिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मीपुत्रः|धर्मीपुत्र
धर्मीपुत्रः An actor, player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्य|धर्म्म्यः
धर्म्य <i>a.</i> [धर्मादनपेतः-यत्]<BR>—1 Consistent with law, duty or religon, lawful, legal; यो यस्य धर्म्यो<BR> वर्णस्य Ms. 3. 22, 25-26.<BR>—2 Religious (as an act); क्रियाणां खलु धर्म्याणां सत्पत्न्यो मूलकारणम् Ku. 6. 13.<BR>—3 Just, righteous, fair; धर्म्याद्धि युद्धाच्छ्रेयोऽन्यत्क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते<BR> Bg. 2. 31, 9. 2; Y. 3. 44; धर्म्यासु कामार्थयशस्करीषु Bk. 1. 9.<BR>—4 Legitimate.<BR>—5 Usual.<BR>—6 Endowed with particular qualities, as तद्धर्म्य; धर्म्यमणुमेतमाप्य<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 2. 13.<BR>—7 Relating to Dharma; अध्येष्यते च य इमं धर्म्यं संवादमावयोः Bg. 18. 70.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धर्म्यविवाहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्यविवाहः|धर्म्यविवाह|धर्म्म्यविवाहः
धर्म्य + -विवाहः a legal marriage; cf. Ms. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षः|धर्ष
धर्षः [धृष्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Boldness, insolence, haughtiness, impudence.<BR>—2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>—3 Impatience.<BR>—4 Restraint.<BR>—5 Violation, seduction (of a woman).<BR>—6 Injury, wrong, insult.<BR>—7 A eunuch.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धर्षकारिणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षकारिणी
धर्षः + -कारिणी a violated woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षक|धर्षकः
धर्षक <i>a.</i> [धृष्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Assailing, attacking, assaulting.<BR>—2 Violating, seducing.<BR>—3 Impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षकः|धर्षक
धर्षक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A seducer, an adulterer, a violator.<BR>—2 An actor, dancer.<BR>—3 Mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणम्
धर्षणम्, -णा<BR> [धृष् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Boldness, insolence.<BR>—2 Insult, affront; धर्षणां कृतवानेतां पश्यतस्ते धनेश्वर Mb. 3. 161. 60.<BR>—3 An assault, outrage, seduction, violation; as in नारी˚; माऽत्र प्राप्स्यति<BR> शापं वा धर्षणां वेति पाण्डवः Mb. 3. 146. 68.<BR>—4 Copulation.<BR>—5 Contempt, disrespect.<BR>—6 Abuse.<BR>—7 arrogance.<BR>—8 An offence.<BR>—9 Overpowering, defeat; धर्षणं यत्र न प्राप्तो रावणो राक्षसेश्वरः<BR> Rām. 7. 31. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धर्षणात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणा
धर्षणम्, -णा<BR> [धृष् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Boldness, insolence.<BR>—2 Insult, affront; धर्षणां कृतवानेतां पश्यतस्ते धनेश्वर Mb. 3. 161. 60.<BR>—3 An assault, outrage, seduction, violation; as in नारी˚; माऽत्र प्राप्स्यति<BR> शापं वा धर्षणां वेति पाण्डवः Mb. 3. 146. 68.<BR>—4 Copulation.<BR>—5 Contempt, disrespect.<BR>—6 Abuse.<BR>—7 arrogance.<BR>—8 An offence.<BR>—9 Overpowering, defeat; धर्षणं यत्र न प्राप्तो रावणो राक्षसेश्वरः<BR> Rām. 7. 31. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धर्षणात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणात्मन्
धर्षणम् + -आत्मन् (धर्षणात्मन्) having a violent nature (N. of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणिः|धर्षणि
धर्षणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> A disloyal or wanton woman, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणी
धर्षणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> A disloyal or wanton woman, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षित|धर्षितं
धर्षित <i>a.</i> [धृष्-कर्मणि क्त -इट् गुणश्च]<BR>—1 Seduced, outraged, violated.<BR>—2 Overpowered, overcome, defeated; यत्काव्यं मधुवर्षि धर्षितपरास्तर्केषु<BR> यस्योक्तयः N. 22. 155.<BR>—3 Ill-treated, abused, insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षितम्
धर्षित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Contumely, pride.<BR>—2 Cohabitation, copulation.<BR>—3 Impatience, intolerance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिता
धर्षित + .{@-ता@} A harlot, a disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिन्
धर्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proud, arrogant, overbearing.<BR>—2 Assaulting, seducing, outraging.<BR>—3 Insulting, ill-treating.<BR>—4 Audacious, impudent.<BR>—5 Cohabiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिणी
धर्षिन् + .{@-णी@} A harlot, an unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवः|धव
धवः<BR>—1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>—2 A man.<BR>—3 A husband, as in विधवा.<BR>—4 A master, lord.<BR>—5 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—6 A kind of tree; Anogeissus latifolia; (Mar. धावडा); Rām. 1. 24. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवल|धवलः
धवल <i>a.</i> [धवं कम्पं लाति ला-क; Tv.]<BR>—1 White; धवलातपत्र, धवलगृहम्, धवलवस्त्रम् &c. नीता येन<BR> निशा शशाङ्कधवला Ujjvalamaṇi.<BR>—2 Handsome.<BR>—3 Clear, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलः|धवल
धवल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 An excellent bull.<BR>—3 China camphor<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">Page0858-1</a>]<BR> (चीनकर्पूर).<BR>—4 N. of a tree (धव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलम्
धवल + .{@-लम्@} White-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवला
धवल + .{@-ला@} A woman with a white complexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवली
धवल + .{@-ली@} A white cow; (धवला also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धवलोत्पलम्, धवलगिरिः, धवलगृहम्, धवलपक्षः, धवलमृत्तिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0857-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलोत्पलम्
धवल + -उत्पलम् the white water-lily (said to open at moonrise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलगिरिः|धवलगिरि
धवल + -गिरिः N. of the highest peak of the Himālaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलगृहम्
धवल + -गृहम् a house whitened with chunam, a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलपक्षः|धवलपक्ष
धवल + -पक्षः<BR>—1 a goose; धवलपक्षविहंगमकूजितैः Śi. 6. 45.<BR>—2 the bright half of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलमृत्तिका
धवल + -मृत्तिका chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलित
धवलित <i>a.</i> Whitened, made white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलिमन्
धवलिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Whiteness, white colour; अधिगतधवलिम्नः शूलपाणेरभिख्याम् Śi. 4. 65.<BR>—2 Paleness; इयं भूतिर्नाङ्गे प्रियविरहजन्मा धवलिमा Subhāṣ.; धवलिमा<BR> जातो मणीनां गणे Sūkti. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवाणकः|धवाणक
धवाणकः Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवित्रम्
धवित्रम् A fan made of the deerʼs skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धस्
धस् <i>a.</i> [धा-कसुन्] Holding; रेतोधस्, पुरोधस् &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Brahman.<BR>—2 Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा €3 U. (दधाति, धत्ते, दधौ-दधे, अधात्-अधित, धास्यति-ते, धातुम्,<BR> हित)<i>pass.</i> धीयते; <i>caus.</i> धापयति-ते; <i>desid.</i> धित्सति-ते<BR>—1 To put, place, set, lay, put in, lay on or upon; विज्ञातदोषेषु दधाति<BR> दण्डम् Mb.; निःशङ्कं धीयते (v. l. for दीयते) लोकैः पश्य<BR> भस्मचये पदम् H. 2. 132.<BR>—2 To fix upon, direct (the mind or thoughts &c.) towards (with dat. or<BR> loc.); धत्ते चक्षुर्मुकुलिनि रणत्कोकिले बालचूते Māl. 3. 12; दधुः<BR> कुमारानुगमे मनांसि Bk. 3. 11, 2. 7; Ms. 12. 23.<BR>—3 To bestow anything upon one, grant, give, confer, present (with dat.,<BR> gen., or loc.); धुर्यां लक्ष्मीमथ मयि भृशं धेहि देव प्रसीद Māl. 1. 3;<BR> यद्यस्य सोऽदधात्सर्गे तत्तस्य स्वयमाविशत् Ms. 1. 29.<BR>—4 To hold, contain; तानपि दधासि मातः Bv. 1. 68; Ś. 4. 4.<BR>—5 To seize, take hold of (as in the hand); धनुररिभिरसह्यं मृष्टिपीडं<BR> दधाने Bk. 1. 26, 4. 26.<BR>—6 To wear, put on, bear; गुरूणि वासांसि विहाय तूर्णं तनूनि … … धत्ते<BR> जनः काममदालसाङ्गः Ṛs. 6. 13, 16; धत्ते भरं कुसुमपत्रफलावलीनाम्<BR> Bv. 1. 94; दधतो मङ्गलक्षौमे R. 12. 8, 9. 40; Bk. 17. 54.<BR>—7 To assume, take, have, show, exhibit, possess; (usually Ātm.); काचः<BR> काञ्चनसंसर्गाद्धत्ते मारकतीं द्युतिम् H. Pr. 35; शिरसि मसीपटलं<BR> दधाति दीपः Bv. 1. 74; R. 2. 7; Amaru. 27. 70; Me. 38; Bh. 3. 46; R. 3. 1;<BR> Bk. 2. 1, 4. 16, 18; Śi. 9. 3, 10. 86; Ki. 5. 5.<BR>—8 To hold up, sustain, bear up; गामधास्यत्कथं नागो मृणालमृदुभिः<BR> फणैः Ku. 6. 68.<BR>—9 To support, maintain संपद्विनिमयेनोभौ दधतुर्भुवनद्वयम् R. 1. 26.<BR>—10 To cause, create, produce, generate, make; मुग्धा कुड्मलिताननेन<BR> दधती वायुं स्थिता तत्र सा Amaru. 72.<BR>—11 To suffer, undergo, incur; दधती रतेन भृशमुत्सुकताम् Śi. 9. 2, 32, 66.<BR>—12 To perform, do.<BR>—13 Ved. To bring, convey.<BR>—14 To appoint, fix. [The meanings of this root, like those of दा,<BR> are variously modified according to the word with which it is connected;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> मनः, मतिम्, धियम्, &c. धा to fix the mind or thoughts<BR> upon, resolve upon; पदं धा to set foot on, to enter; कर्णे करं<BR> धा to place the hand on the ear &c.]. ━<i>With</i> {@अपि@} (the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">Page0858-2</a>]<BR> अ being sometimes dropped).<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) to close, shut; ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे श्रवणमपिदधाति Gīt. 5;<BR> so कर्णौ-नयने-पिदधाति<BR>——(<i>b</i>) to cover, hide, conceal; प्रायो मूर्खः परिभवविधौ नाभिमानं<BR> पिधत्ते Ś. Til. 17 (v. l.); प्रभावपिहिता V. 4. 2; Śi. 9. 76; Bk. 7. 69.<BR>—2 to hinder, obstruct, bar; भुजंगपिहितद्वारं पातालमधितिष्ठति<BR> R. 1. 80. (The following verse illustrates the use of धा with some<BR> prepositions:− अधित कापि मुखे सलिलं सखी प्यधित कापि सरोजदलैः<BR> स्तनौ । व्यधित कापि हृदि व्यजनानिलं न्यधित कापि हिमं सुतनोस्तनौ<BR> N. 4. 111; or, better still, the following verse of Jagannātha:−<BR> निधानं धर्माणां किमपि च विधानं नवमुदां प्रधानं तीर्थानाममलपरिधानं<BR> त्रिजगतः । समाधानं बुद्धेरथ खलु तिरोधानमधियां श्रियामाधानं नः<BR> परिहरतु तापं तव वपुः ॥ G. L. 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाकः|धाक
धाकः [धा-उणा˚क तस्य नेत्वम्]<BR>—1 An ox.<BR>—2 A receptacle, reservoir.<BR>—3 Food, boiled rice.<BR>—4 A post, pillar, column.<BR>—5 Brahman.<BR>—6 A supporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुः|धातु
धातुः [धा-आधारे तुन्]<BR>—1 A constituent or essential part, an ingredient.<BR>—2 An element, primary or elementary substance, <i>i. e.</i> पृथिवी, अप्,<BR> तेजस्, वायु and आकाश; Bhāg. 7. 15. 60.<BR>—3 A secretion, primary fluid or juice, essential ingredients of the body<BR> (which are considered to be 7:− रसासृङ्मांसमेदोऽस्थिमज्जाशुक्राणि धातवः,<BR> or sometimes ten if केश, त्वच् and स्नायु be added); Mb. 3. 213. 10.<BR>—4 A humour or affection of the body, (<i>i. e.</i> वात, पित्त and कफ);<BR> यस्यात्मबुद्धिः कुणपे त्रिधातुके Bhāg. 10. 84. 13.<BR>—5 A mineral, metal, metallic ore; न्यस्ताक्षरा धातुरसेन यत्र Ku. 1. 7;<BR> त्वामालिख्य प्रणयकुपितां धातुरागैः शिलायाम् Me. 107; R. 4. 71; Ku. 6. 51.<BR>—6 A verbal root; भूवादयो धातवः P. I. 3. 1; पश्चादध्ययनार्थस्य<BR> धातोरधिरिवाभवत् R. 15. 9.<BR>—7 The soul.<BR>—8 The Supreme Spirit; धातुप्रसादान्महिमानमात्मनः Kaṭh.<BR>—9 An organ of sense.<BR>—10 Any one of the properties of the five elements, <i>i. e.</i> रूप,<BR> रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श and शब्द; तत्र तत्र हि दृश्यन्ते धातवः पाञ्चभौतिकाः ।<BR> तेषां मनुष्यास्तर्केण प्रमाणानि प्रचक्षते ॥ Mb. 6. 5. 11.<BR>—11 A bone.<BR>—12 A part, portion.<BR>—13 A fluid mineral of a red colour.<BR>—14 Ved. A supporter.<BR>—15 Anything to be drunk, as milk &c. ━<i>f.</i> A milch cow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धातूपलः, धातुकाशीशम्, धातुकासीसम्, धातुकुशल, धातुक्रिया, धातुक्षयः, धातुगर्भः, धातुस्तपः, धातुग्राहिन्, धातुघ्नम्, धातुनाशनम्, धातुचूर्णम्, धातुजम्, धातुद्रावकः, धातुपः, धातुपाठः, धातुपुष्टिः, धातुप्रसक्त, धातुभृत्, धातुमलम्, धातुमाक्षिकम्, धातुमारिणी, धातुमारिन्, धातुरसः, धातुराजकः, धातुराजकम्, धातुवल्लभम्, धातुवादः, धातुवादिन्, धातुविष्, धातुवैरिन्, धातुशेखरम्, धातुशोधनम्, धातुसंभवम्, धातुसाम्यम्, धातुहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातूपलः|धातूपल
धातुः + -उपलः chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुकाशीशम्
धातुः + -काशीशम्, -कासीसम् red sulphate of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुकासीसम्
धातुः + -काशीशम्, -कासीसम् red sulphate of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुकुशल
धातुः + -कुशल <i>a.</i> skilful in working in metals, metallurgist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुक्रिया
धातुः + -क्रिया metallurgy, mineralogy<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुक्षयः|धातुक्षय
धातुः + -क्षयः waste of the bodily humours, a wasting disease, a kind<BR> of consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुगर्भः|धातुगर्भ
धातुः + -गर्भः, -स्तपः a receptacle for ashes, Dagoba; Buddh. ˚कुम्भः a relic urn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुस्तपः
धातुः + -गर्भः, -स्तपः a receptacle for ashes, Dagoba; Buddh. ˚कुम्भः a relic urn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुग्राहिन्
धातुः + -ग्राहिन् <i>m.</i> calamine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुघ्नम्
धातुः + -घ्नम्, -नाशनम् sour gruel (prepared from the fermentation of rice-water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुनाशनम्
धातुः + -घ्नम्, -नाशनम् sour gruel (prepared from the fermentation of rice-water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुचूर्णम्
धातुः + -चूर्णम् mineral powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुजम्
धातुः + -जम् bitumen<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0858-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

