धान्धा Cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यम्
धान्यम् [धाने पोषणे साधु यत्]<BR>—1 Grain, corn, rice (for the distinction between सस्य, धान्य, तण्डुल<BR> and अन्न see under तण्डुल). सस्यं क्षेत्रगतं प्रोक्तं सतुषं<BR> धान्यमुच्यते.<BR>—2 Coriander.<BR>—3 A measure equal to four sesamum seeds.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धान्याचलः, धान्यारिः, धान्यार्थः, धान्याम्लम्, धान्यास्थि, धान्योत्तमः, धान्यकल्कम्, धान्यकोशः, धान्यकोष्ठकम्, धान्यकः, धान्यक्षेत्रम्, धान्यखलः, धान्यचमसः, धान्यचौरः, धान्यत्वच्, धान्यधेनु, धान्यपञ्चकम्, धान्यमायः, धान्यमानम्, धान्यमुष्टिः, धान्यराजः, धान्यवर्धनम्, धान्यवीजम्, धान्यवीरः, धान्यशीर्षकम्, धान्यशूकम्, धान्यसारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याचलः|धान्याचल
धान्यम् + -अचलः a pile of grain presented to Brhāmaṇas as a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यारिः|धान्यारि
धान्यम् + -अरिः a mouse, rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यार्थः|धान्यार्थ
धान्यम् + -अर्थः wealth in rice or grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याम्लम्
धान्यम् + -अम्लम् sour gruel made of the fermentation of rice-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यास्थि
धान्यम् + -अस्थि <i>n.</i> husk, chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्योत्तमः|धान्योत्तम
धान्यम् + -उत्तमः the best of grain, <i>i. e.</i> rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकल्कम्
धान्यम् + -कल्कम्<BR>—1 bran.<BR>—2 chaff, straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकोशः|धान्यकोश
धान्यम् + -कोशः, -कोष्ठकम्, -कः a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकोष्ठकम्
धान्यम् + -कोशः, -कोष्ठकम्, -कः a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकः|धान्यक|धान्यकं
धान्यम् + -कोशः, -कोष्ठकम्, -कः a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यक्षेत्रम्
धान्यम् + -क्षेत्रम् a corn-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यखलः|धान्यखल
धान्यम् + -खलः threshing floor (Mar. खळें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यचमसः|धान्यचमस
धान्यम् + -चमसः rice flattened by threshing after it has been steeped<BR> and fried in the husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यचौरः|धान्यचौर
धान्यम् + -चौरः a stealer of corn; धान्यचौरोऽङ्गहीनत्वम् Ms. 11. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यत्वच्
धान्यम् + -त्वच् <i>f.</i> the husk of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यधेनु|धान्यधेनुः
धान्यम् + -धेनु <i>f.</i> a heap of corn (like a cow, to be presented to a<BR> Brāhmaṇa); तमिदानीं प्रवक्ष्यामि धान्यधेनुविधिं परम् । यां दत्त्वा<BR> सर्वपापेभ्यः शशाङ्क इव राहुणा ॥ … … मुच्यते … … Varāha P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यपञ्चकम्
धान्यम् + -पञ्चकम् the following grains; शालि, व्रीहि, शूक, शिखि and<BR> क्षुद्र धान्यs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यमायः|धान्यमाय
धान्यम् + -मायः a corn-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यमानम्
धान्यम् + -मानम् a measure of corn (as much corn as a man can eat at once).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यमुष्टिः
धान्यम् + -मुष्टिः a handful of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यराजः|धान्यराज
धान्यम् + -राजः barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवर्धनम्
धान्यम् + -वर्धनम् lending grain at interest, usury with grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीजम्
धान्यम् + -वीजम् ({@बीजम्@}) coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीरः|धान्यवीर
धान्यम् + -वीरः a sort of pulse (माष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यशीर्षकम्
धान्यम् + -शीर्षकम् the ear of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यशूकम्
धान्यम् + -शूकम् the beard or awn of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यसारः|धान्यसार
धान्यम् + -सारः threshed corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्या
धान्या, धान्याकम् Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याकम्
धान्या, धान्याकम् Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन
धान्वन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Situated in a desert (धन्वन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन्तर्यम्
धान्वन्तर्यम् A <i>Homa</i> in which Dhanvantari is the Devatā; अग्नीषोमं<BR> वैश्वदेवं धान्वन्तर्यमनन्तरम् । प्रजानां पतये चैव पृथग् होमो विधीयते<BR> Mb. 13. 97. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामकः|धामक
धामकः A sort of weight (माष q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0859-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन् <i>n.</i> [धा-मनिन्]<BR>—1 A dwelling-place, abode, residence, house; तुरासाहं पुरोधाय धाम<BR> स्वायंभुवं ययुः Ku. 2. 1, 44; पुण्यं यायास्त्रिभुवनगुरोर्धाम चण्डीश्वरस्य<BR> Me. 33; Bg. 8. 21; Bh. 1. 35; पतत्यधो धाम विसारि सर्वतः किमेतदित्याकुलमीक्षितं<BR> जनैः Śi. 1. 2.<BR>—2 A place, site, resort; श्रियो धाम; भूतैः स्वधामभिः पश्येदप्रविष्टं<BR> प्रविष्टवत् Bhāg. 7. 12. 15.<BR>—3 The inmates of a house, members of a family.<BR>—4 A ray of light; धाम्नातिशाययति धाम सहस्रधाम्नः Mu. 3. 17; Śi. 9. 53.<BR>—5 Light, lustre, splendour; Mu. 3. 17; Ki. 2. 20, 55, 59, 10. 6; Amaru. 86;<BR> R. 6. 6, 18. 22.<BR>—6 Majestic lustre, majesty, glory, dignity; गां गतस्य तव धाम वैष्णवं<BR> कोपितो ह्यसि मया दिदृक्षुणा R. 11. 85.<BR>—7 Power, strength, energy (प्रताप); सहते न जनोऽप्यधःक्रियां<BR> किमु लोकाधिकधाम राजकम् Ki. 2. 47.<BR>—8 Birth.<BR>—9 The body.<BR>—10 A troop, host.<BR>—11 State, condition; Prab. 1. 30.<BR>—12 A class.<BR>—13 Ved. Law, rule.<BR>—14 Ved. Property, wealth.<BR>—15 A fetter.<BR>—16 Fashion, mode, manner, form, appearance; स बिभ्रत्पौरुषं धाम भ्राजमानो<BR> यथा रविः Bhāg. 10. 2. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धामकेशिन्, धामच्छद्, धाममानिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामकेशिन्
धामन् + -केशिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-निधिः@}<BR> the sun; Mb. 3. 3. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामच्छद्
धामन् + -छद् <i>m.</i> Ved. N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाममानिन्
धामन् + -मानिन् <i>a.</i> believing in a material existence; नैवेशितुं प्रभुर्भूम्न<BR> ईश्वरो धाममानिनाम् Bhāg. 3. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनिका
धामनिका, धामनी See धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनी
धामनिका, धामनी See धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामवत्|धामवन्त्
धामवत् <i>a.</i> powerful, strong; पुरःसरा धामवतां यशोधनाः Ki. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय|धायः
धाय, धायक <i>a.</i> Having, possessing, holding, sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायक
धाय, धायक <i>a.</i> Having, possessing, holding, sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
धायस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Sustaining, supporting.<BR>—2 Nourishing.<BR>—3 Drinking. ━<i>n.</i> The act of drinking or sucking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायु
धायु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sustaining, supporting; इन्द्र प्रिया सुरथा शूर धायू Rv. 7. 36. 4.<BR>—2 Liberal.<BR>—3 Feeding, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्यः|धाय्य
धाय्यः A <i>Purohita</i> or family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्या
धाय्या <i>f.</i> (सामिधेनी ऋग् या समिदाधाने पठ्यते)<BR>—1 A kind of prayer recited while the sacrificial fire is being kindled;<BR> यासु धाय्याशब्दः श्रूयते तास्तावद् धाय्याः ŚB. on MS. 5. 3. 5.<BR>—2 Fuel; क्रोधाग्नौ निजतातनिग्रहकथाधाय्यासमुद्दीपिते Rām. Ch. 2. 86; N. 1. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार <i>a.</i> [धृ-णिच्-अच्]<BR>—1 Holding, bearing, supporting; नमः स्त्रीरूपधाराय Mb. 13. 14. 13.<BR>—2 Streaming, dripping, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारः|धार|धारं
धार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 A sudden and violent shower of rain, sharp-driving shower.<BR>—3 Snow, hail.<BR>—4 A deep place.<BR>—5 Debt.<BR>—6 A boundary, limit.<BR>—7 A sort of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक <i>a.</i> Holding, possessing, bearing &c.; नाम˚, देह˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारकः|धारक
धारक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A vessel of any kind (box, trunk, &c.), a water-pot.<BR>—2 A debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारका
धारक + .{@-का@} The vulva of a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिका
धारक + .{@-धारिका@}<BR>—1 A prop, pillar.<BR>—2 A division of time (= ½ Muhūrta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धृ-णिच्-ल्युट्] Holding, bearing, carrying, preserving,<BR> sustaining, protecting, having,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">Page0860-2</a>]<BR> assuming, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणौ
धारण + .{@-णौ@} (du.) The two female breasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणम्
धारण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of holding, bearing, supporting, preserving or keeping back.<BR>—2 Possessing, possession.<BR>—3 Observing; holding fast.<BR>—4 Retaining in the memory; ग्रहणधारणपटुर्बालकः.<BR>—5 Being indebted (to any one).<BR>—6 Steady abstraction of the mind.<BR>—7 Keeping, maintaining.<BR>—8 Restraining.<BR>—9 (In gram.) Pronouncing imperfectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणी
धारण + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A row or line.<BR>—2 A vein or tubular vessel.<BR>—3 Steadiness.<BR>—4 A mystical verse or charm to assuage pain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धारणाध्ययनम्, धारणमातृका, धारणयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणाध्ययनम्
धारण + -अध्ययनम् The conservative method of reading (opp. to ग्रहणाध्ययन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणमातृका
धारण + -मातृका One of the 64 arts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणयन्त्रम्
धारण + -यन्त्रम् a kind of amulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणकः|धारणक
धारणकः A debtor; विना धारणकाद्वापि विक्रीणीत ससाक्षिकम् Y. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणा
धारणा<BR>—1 The act of holding, bearing, supporting, preserving, &c.<BR>—2 The faculty of retaining in the mind, a good or retentive memory; धीर्धारणावती मेधा Ak.<BR>—3 Memory in general.<BR>—4 Keeping the mind collected, holding the breath suspended, steady abstraction<BR> of mind; परिचेतुमुपांशु धारणाम् R. 8. 18; Ms. 6. 72; Y. 3. 201 (धारणेत्युच्यते<BR> चेयं धार्यते यन्मनो तया).<BR>—5 Fortitude, firmness, steadiness.<BR>—6 A fixed precept or injunction, a settled rule, conclusion; इति धर्मस्य<BR> धारणा Ms. 8. 184, 4. 38, 9. 124.<BR>—7 Understanding, intellect; Y. 3. 73.<BR>—8 Continuance in rectitude, propriety, decorum.<BR>—9 Conviction or abstraction.<BR>—10 A kind of योगाङ्ग; देशबन्धश्चित्तस्य धारणा Yogadarśana.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धारणात्मक, धारणायोगः, धारणाशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणात्मक
धारणा + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> one who easily composes himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणायोगः|धारणायोग
धारणा + -योगः deep devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणाशक्तिः
धारणा + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> a retentive memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयिष्णु
धारयिष्णु <i>a.</i> Capable of holding, sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयिष्णुता
धारयिष्णुता Patience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयित्री
धारयित्री The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारा
धारा —1 A stream or current of water, a line of descending fluid,<BR> stream, current; धारा नैव पतन्ति चातकमुखे मेघस्य किं दूषणम्<BR> Bh. 2. 93; Me. 55; R. 16. 66; आबद्धधारमश्रु प्रावर्तत Dk. 74.<BR>—2 A shower, a hard or sharp-driving shower.<BR>—3 A continuous line or series; प्रणतौ हन्त निरन्तराश्रुधाराः Bv. 2. 20.<BR>—4 A leak or hole in a pitcher.<BR>—5 The pace of a horse; धाराः प्रसाधयितुमव्यतिकीर्णरूपाः Śi. 5. 60; N. 1. 72.<BR>—6 The margin, edge or border of anything; ध्रुवं स नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया<BR> शमीलतां छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यवस्यति Ś. 1. 18.<BR>—7 The sharp edge of a sword, axe, or of any cutting instrument; तर्जितः<BR> परशुधारया मम R. 11. 78, 6. 42, 10. 86, 41; Bh. 2. 28.<BR>—8 The edge of a mountain or precipice.<BR>—9 A wheel or the periphery of a wheel; धारानिबद्धेव कलङ्करेखा R. 13. 15.<BR>—10 A garden-wall, fence, hedge.<BR>—11 The van or front line of an army.<BR>—12 The highest point, excellence.<BR>—13 A multitude.<BR>—14 Fame.<BR>—15 Night.<BR>—16 Turmeric.<BR>—17 Likeness.<BR>—18 The tip of the ear.<BR>—19 Speech.<BR>—20 Rumour, report.<BR>—21 N. of an ancient town in Mālvā, capital<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">Page0861-1</a>]<BR> of king Bhoja.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धाराग्रम्, धाराङ्कुरः, धाराङ्गः, धाराटः, धाराधिरूढ, धारावनिः, धाराश्रु, धारावर्तः, धारासारः, धारेश्वरः, धारोष्ण, धारागिरिः, धारागृहम्, धाराधरः, धारानिपातः, धारापातः, धारायन्त्रम्, धारावर्षः, धारावर्षम्, धारासंपातः, धारावाहिन्, धाराविषः, धाराशीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0860-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराग्रम्
धारा + -अग्रम् the broad-edged head of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्कुरः|धाराङ्कुर|धारांकुर
धारा + -अङ्कुरः<BR>—1 a drop of rain.<BR>—2 hail; धाराङ्कुरवर्षिणो जलदाः Bṛ. S. 32. 21.<BR>—3 advancing before the line of an army (to defy the enemy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्गः|धाराङ्ग|धारांग
धारा + -अङ्गः a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराटः|धाराट
धारा + -अटः<BR>—1 the Chātaka bird.<BR>—2 a horse.<BR>—3 a cloud. —4 a furious elephant, one in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराधिरूढ
धारा + -अधिरूढ <i>a.</i> raised to the highest pitch; किं वा धाराधिरूढं<BR> हि जाड्यं वेदजडे जने Ks. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावनिः|धारावनि
धारा + -अवनिः <i>f.</i> wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराश्रु
धारा + -अश्रु <i>n.</i> a flood of tears; Amaru. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावर्तः|धारावर्त
धारा + -आवर्तः a whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासारः|धारासार
धारा + -आसारः a heavy down-fall of rain, a hard or sharp driving shower;<BR> धारासारैर्महती वृष्टिर्बभूव H. 3; V. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारेश्वरः|धारेश्वर
धारा + -ईश्वरः king Bhoja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारोष्ण|धारोष्णं
धारा + -उष्ण <i>a.</i> warm from a cow (as milk); धारोष्णं त्वमृतं पयो<BR> भ्रमहरं निद्राकरं कान्तिदम् । वृष्यं बृंहणमग्निवर्धनमतिस्वादु<BR> त्रिदोषापहम् ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारागिरिः
धारा + -गिरिः The fort of Devagiri or Daulatabad; स हि शैलो निजामस्य<BR> प्रियकारी महायशाः । प्रतापी प्रथितो लोके धारागिरिरिवापरः ॥ Śiva B. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारागृहम्
धारा + -गृहम् a bath-room with water-jets, a shower-bath or a house furnished<BR> with artificial jets or fountains of water; शिलाविशेषानधिशय्य निन्युर्धारागृहेष्वातपमृद्धिमन्तः R. 16. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराधरः|धाराधर
धारा + -धरः<BR>—1 holder of streams, a cloud; धातः किं नु विधौ विधातुमुचितो धाराधराडम्बरः Bv. 1. 4.<BR>—2 a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारानिपातः|धारानिपात
धारा + -निपातः, -पातः<BR>—1 a fall of rain, a hard or pelting shower; Me. 48.<BR>—2 a stream of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारापातः|धारापात
धारा + -निपातः, -पातः<BR>—1 a fall of rain, a hard or pelting shower; Me. 48.<BR>—2 a stream of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारायन्त्रम्
धारा + -यन्त्रम् a fountain, jet (of water); धारायन्त्रजलाभिषेककलुषे<BR> धौताञ्जने लोचने Amaru. 124; धारायन्त्रविमुक्तसंततपयः पूरप्लुते<BR> सर्वतः Ratn. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावर्षः|धारावर्ष
धारा + -वर्षः, -वर्षम्, -संपातः a hard, sharp-driving or incessant shower;<BR> न प्रसेहे स रुद्धार्कमधारावर्षदुर्दिनम् R. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावर्षम्
धारा + -वर्षः, -वर्षम्, -संपातः a hard, sharp-driving or incessant shower;<BR> न प्रसेहे स रुद्धार्कमधारावर्षदुर्दिनम् R. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासंपातः|धारासम्पात|धारासंपात|धारासम्पातः
धारा + -वर्षः, -वर्षम्, -संपातः a hard, sharp-driving or incessant shower;<BR> न प्रसेहे स रुद्धार्कमधारावर्षदुर्दिनम् R. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावाहिन्
धारा + -वाहिन् <i>a.</i> incessant, continuous; पटुर्धारावाही नव इव<BR> चिरेणापि (मन्युः) U. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराविषः|धाराविष
धारा + -विषः a crooked sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराशीत
धारा + -शीत <i>a.</i> (milk) cooled after having been milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराल
धाराल, धारावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an edge, edged (as a sword &c.).<BR>—2 Flowing in streams; Mātaṅga L. 9. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावत्|धारावन्त्
धाराल, धारावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an edge, edged (as a sword &c.).<BR>—2 Flowing in streams; Mātaṅga L. 9. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिणी
धारिणी The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारित
धारित <i>a.</i> Held, supported, maintained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारितम्
धारित + .{@-तम्@} A horseʼs trot; also धारितकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धृ-णिनि]<BR>—1 Carrying, bearing, sustaining, preserving, having, holding, supporting;<BR> पादाम्भोरुहधारि Gīt. 12; कर˚ &c.<BR>—2 Keeping in oneʼs memory, possessed of retentive memory; अज्ञेभ्यो ग्रन्थिनः<BR> श्रेष्ठा ग्रन्थिभ्यो धारिणो वराः Ms. 12. 103.<BR>—3 Edged, observing, doing; यज्ञधारी च सततम् Mb. 12. 340. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारु|धारुः
धारु <i>a.</i> Drinker (?); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य|धार्य्य|धार्य्यं
धार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be held or maintained; धार्यः कथंकारमहं भवत्या वियद्विहारी<BR> वसुधैकगत्या N.<BR>—2 Bearable.<BR>—3 To be worn.<BR>—4 To be suffered, supportable.<BR>—5 To be borne in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्यम्
धार्य + .{@-र्यम्@} Clothes, garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्तराष्ट्रः [धृतराष्ट्रस्यापत्यं पुमान्-अण्]<BR>—1 A son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR>—2 A sort of goose with black legs and bill; निपतन्ति धार्तराष्ट्राः<BR> कालवशान्मेदिनीपृष्ठे Ve. 1. 6 (where the word is used in both the senses);<BR> cf. धार्तराष्ट्रो हंसभेदे दुर्योधनकुलेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म|धार्म्म
धार्म <i>a.</i> [धर्मस्येदम् अण्] Belonging to justice or <i>Dharma</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धर्मम् अधीते चरति वा ठक्]<BR>—1 Righteous, pious, just, virtuous; काकुत्स्थं करुणार्णवं गुणनिधिं<BR> विप्रप्रियं धार्मिकम् (वन्दे) Rāmarakṣā 26.<BR>—2 Resting on right, conformable to justice, equitable.<BR>—3 Religious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिकः|धार्मिक|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A judge.<BR>—2 A bigot.<BR>—3 A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिणम्
धार्मिणम् An assemblage of virtuous men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट्यम्
धार्ष्ट्यम् [धृष्टस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Arrogance, insolence, audacity, impudence, rudeness; अहो धाष्टर्पमहो<BR> धाष्टर्पं तयोः क्षत्रियवीरयोः Hariv.<BR>—2 Boldness; सखीषु निर्वाच्यमधाष्टर्पदूषितं प्रियाङ्गसंश्लेषमवाप<BR> मानिनी Ki. 8. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् I. €1 P. (धावति, धावित)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To run, advance; अद्यापि धावति मनः C. P. 36; धावन्त्यमी<BR> मृगजवाक्षमयेव रथ्याः Ś. 1. 8; गच्छति पुरः शरीरं धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं<BR> चेतः 1. 33.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To move, glide.<BR>—2 To run towards, advance against, assault, encounter; अधावीच्चारिसंमुखम् Bk. 15. 67.<BR>—3 To flow, stream or flow forth; धावत्यम्भसि तैलवत् Suśr.<BR>—4 To run or flee away.<BR>—5 To give milk (as a cow). ━II. €1 U. (धावति-ते, धौत or धावित)<BR>—1 To wash, clean, cleanse, purify, rub off; दधावाद्भिस्ततश्चक्षुः सुग्रीवस्य<BR> विभीषणः । विदांचकार धौताक्षः स रिपुं खे ननर्द च ॥ Bk. 14. 50;<BR> Ś. 6. 25; Śi. 17. 8.<BR>—2 To brighten, polish.<BR>—3 To rub into oneʼs person (Ātm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव
धाव <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Washing, cleaning &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक <i>a.</i> [धाव्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Running, flowing.<BR>—2 Quick, swift.<BR>—3 Washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावकः|धावक
धावक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A washerman.<BR>—2 N. of a poet (said to have composed the Ratnāvalī for King Śrīharṣa);<BR> श्रीहर्षादेर्धावकादीनामिव यशः K. P. 1. (v. l.); प्रथितयशसां<BR> धावकसौमिल्लकविपुत्रादीनां प्रबन्धानतिक्रम्य M. 1 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनम्
धावनम् [धाव्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Running, galloping.<BR>—2 Flowing.<BR>—3 Attacking.<BR>—4 Cleansing, purifying, rubbing, washing off.<BR>—5 Rubbing with anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
धावित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Purified, cleansed.<BR>—2 Running towards, or against.<BR>—3 Running, going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावितृ
धावितृ <i>m.</i> a runner, courser; तपोर्थीयं ब्राह्मणी धत्त गर्भं<BR> गौर्वोढारं धावितारं तुरङ्गी Mb. 11. 26. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावल्यम्
धावल्यम्<BR>—1 Whiteness.<BR>—2 Paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस् <i>m.</i> Ved. A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासिः|धासि
धासिः Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि I. €6 P. (धियति) To hold, have, possess.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@सम्@} to make peace, treat with; cf. संधा. ━II. (or धिन्व्) €5 P. (धिनोति)<BR> To please, delight; satisfy; पश्यन्ती चात्मरूपं तदपि विलुलितस्रग्धरेयं<BR> धिनोति Gīt. 12; धिनोति नास्माञ्जलजेन पूजा त्वयान्वहं तन्वि वितन्यमाना<BR> N. 8. 97; U. 5. 27; Ki. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिः|धि
धिः (At the end of comp. only) A receptacle, store, reservoir &c.;<BR> as in उदधि, इषुधि, वारिधि, जलधि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0861-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धित
धित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Placed, bestowed.<BR>—2 Satisfied, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् <i>ind.</i> An interjection of censure, menace or displeasure (‘fie’,<BR> ‘shame’, ‘out upon’, ‘what a pity’ &c. usually with acc.); धिक् तां च<BR> तं च मदनं च इमां च मां च Bh. 2. 2; धिगिमां देहभृतामसारताम्<BR> R. 8. 50; धिक् तान् धिक् तान् धिगेतान् कथयति सततं कीर्तनस्थो मृदङ्गः;<BR> धिक् सानुजं कुरुपतिं धिगजातशत्रुम् Ve. 3. 11; sometimes with nom.,<BR> voc. and gen. also; धिङ् मूर्ख, धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1; धिगस्तु<BR> हृदयस्यास्य &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धिग्दण्डः, धिक्पारुष्यम्, धिग्वादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दण्डः|धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दंड
धिक् + -दण्डः reprimand, censure; वाग्दण्डं प्रथमं कुर्याद् धिग्दण्डं<BR> तदनन्तरम् Ms. 8. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्पारुष्यम्
धिक् + -पारुष्यम् abuse, reproach, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वादः|धिग्वाद
धिक् + -वादः a reproachful speech, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृ
धिक्कृ €8 U. To despise, disregard, contemn, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कारः|धिक्कार
धिक्कारः, -धिक्क्रिया<BR> Reproach, contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्क्रिया
धिक्कारः, -धिक्क्रिया<BR> Reproach, contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृत|धिक्कृतः
धिक्कृत <i>a.</i> Censured, reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृतम्
धिक्कृत + .{@-तम्@} Reproach, censure, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष्
धिक्ष् €1 Ā. (धिक्षते)<BR>—1 To kindle.<BR>—2 To live.<BR>—3 To be harassed.<BR>—4 To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वणः|धिग्वण
धिग्वणः A man of a mixed tribe (sprung from a Brāhmaṇa and a female<BR> of the Āyogava tribe); (ब्राह्मणात्) आयोगव्यां तु धिग्वणः Ms. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु <i>a.</i> Wishing to deceive, deceptive; भूयस्तं धिप्सुमाहूय Bk. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिन्व्
धिन्व् See धि II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
धिष् €3 P. (दिधेष्टि) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
धिष् <i>f.</i> = धिषणा q. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषणः|धिषण
धिषणः N. of Bṛhaspati, preceptor of the gods; बुद्ध्या यो धिषणाधिकः<BR> Parṇāl. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषणम्
धिषणः + .{@-णम्@} A dwelling-place, an abode, residence; यत्रात्मयोनिधिषणाखिललोकपद्मम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 28. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषणा
धिषणः + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 Praise, hymn.<BR>—3 Intellect, understanding; विशुद्धैवोत्पत्त्या पतति न च तत्पापधिषणा<BR> Mv. 6. 8; आर्यपुत्रार्यधिषण, प्राणनाथ, शुभव्रत Kāśīkhaṇḍa.<BR>—4 Earth.<BR>—5 A cup, bowl.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धिषणाधिपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषणाधिपः|धिषणाधिप
धिषणः + -अधिपः N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठित
धिष्ठित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Well-placed; शाल्वो वैहायसं चापि तत्पुरं व्यूह्य धिष्ठितः Mb. 3. 15. 3.<BR>—2 Lodged, fixed; अथ तं बालकं वीक्ष्य नेत्राभ्यां धिष्ठितं हृदि Bhāg. 12. 10. 32.<BR>—3 Taking a bold stand, stood boldly; अथ दानवसंघास्ते विकृताननमूर्धजाः ।<BR> उदक्रोशन्महाराज धिष्ठिते मयि भारत । Mb. 3. 22. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 To be praised or meditated upon.<BR>—2 Worthy of a high place.<BR>—3 Mindful, attentive.<BR>—4 Benevolent, liberal; धिष्ण्या वनतं गिरः Rv. 1. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्यः|धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं
धिष्ण्य + .{@-ष्ण्यः@}<BR>—1 A place for the sacrificial fire; अमी वेदिं परितः कॢप्तधिष्ण्याः Ś. 4. 8.<BR>—2 N. of Śukra, preceptor of the demons.<BR>—3 The planet Venus.<BR>—4 Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्यम्
धिष्ण्य + .{@-ष्ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 A seat, an abode, site, place, house; न भौमान्येव धिष्ण्यानि हित्वा<BR> ज्योतिर्मयान्यपि R. 15. 59; उदग्रधिष्ण्यं गगनेऽवगाढम् Bu. C. 1. 2;<BR> विवेश धिष्ण्यं क्षितिपालकात्मजः 4. 102.<BR>—2 A meteor.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">Page0862-2</a>]<BR>—3 Fire (<i>m.</i> also).<BR>—4 A star, an asterism; धिष्ण्यमाकाशगं यथा Mb. 5. 184. 6.<BR>—5 A quarter of the sky (मण्डल); य एष दिवि धिष्ण्येन नाकं व्याप्नोति<BR> तेजसा Mb. 1. 171. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धिष्ण्याधिपतिः, धिष्ण्यपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्याधिपतिः|धिष्ण्याधिपति
धिष्ण्य + -अधिपतिः, -पः The guardian of a quarter of the sky; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्यपः|धिष्ण्यप
धिष्ण्य + -अधिपतिः, -पः The guardian of a quarter of the sky; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी €4 Ā. (धीयते)<BR>—1 To disregard, disrespect.<BR>—2 To propitiate.<BR>—3 To hold, contain.<BR>—4 To accomplish, fulfil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीः
धीः [ध्यै भावे क्विप् संप्रसारणं च]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Intellect, understanding; धियः समग्रैः स गुणैरुदारधीः<BR> R. 3. 30; cf. कुधी, सुधी &c. धियो यो नः प्रचोदयात् Gāyatrīmantra;<BR> तत्राज्ञानं धिया नश्येदाभासात्तु घटः स्फुरेत् Vedāntasāra.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Mind; दुष्टधी wicked-minded; स्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत Bg. 2. 54;<BR> R. 3. 30.<BR>—2 Idea, imagination, fancy, conception; न धियां पथि वर्तसे Ku. 6. 22;<BR> ध्यायन्ति चान्यं धिया Pt. 136.<BR>—3 A thought, intention, purpose, propensity; इमामहं वेद न तावकीं<BR> धियम् Ki. 1. 37.<BR>—4 Devotion, prayer.<BR>—5 A sacrifice.<BR>—6 Knowledge, science.<BR>—7 (in Horoscope) The fifth house from the लग्न.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धीन्द्रियम्, धीगुणाः, धीपतिः, धीमन्त्रिन्, धीविभ्रमः, धीशक्तिः, धीसखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीन्द्रियम्
धीः + -इन्द्रियम् an organ of perception (= ज्ञानेन्द्रिय q. v.; मनः<BR> कर्णस्तथा नेत्रं रसना च त्वचा सह । नासिका चेति षट् तानि धीन्द्रियाणि<BR> प्रचक्षते ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीगुणाः
धीः + -गुणाः (pl.) intellectual qualities: they are:− शुश्रूषा श्रवणं<BR> चैव ग्रहणं धारणं तथा । ऊहापोहोऽर्थविज्ञानं तत्त्वज्ञानं च धीगुणाः ॥<BR> Kām. (sing.) (नमो) अखिलधीगुणाय Bhāg. 8. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीपतिः
धीः + -पतिः (धियांपतिः) Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमन्त्रिन्|धीमंत्रिन्
धीः + -मन्त्रिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-सचिवः@}<BR>—1 a minister for counsel (opp. कर्मसचिव ‘a minister for action or execution’<BR>).<BR>—2 a wise or prudent adviser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीविभ्रमः|धीविभ्रम
धीः + -विभ्रमः hallucination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीशक्तिः|धीशक्ति
धीः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> intelletual quality or faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसखः|धीसख
धीः + -सखः a counsellor, adviser, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धीमत्^1 <i>a.</i> Wise, intelligent, learned. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Bṛshaspati.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीक्ष्
धीक्ष् = दीक्ष्. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sucked, drunk; see धे.<BR>—2 Reflected upon, thought about.<BR>—3 Propitiated. ━<i>n.</i> (pl.) thoughts, meditations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीतिः|धीति
धीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Drinking, sucking.<BR>—2 Thirst.<BR>—3 Ved. The fingers.<BR>—4 Thought, notion.<BR>—5 Devotion.<BR>—6 Disrespect, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा<BR>—1 Intellect.<BR>—2 A daughter, virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर <i>a.</i> [धियं राति रा-क, धियमीरयति ईर-अण् वा उप˚ स˚<BR> Tv.] Brave, bold, courageous; धीरोद्धता गतिः U. 6. 19.<BR>—2 Steady, steadfast, firm, durable, lasting, constant; निषेदुषीमासनबन्धधीरः R. 2. 6.<BR>—3 Strong-minded, persevering, self-possessed, resolute, of firm resolve<BR> or purpose; धीरा हि तरन्त्यापदम् K. 175; विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियन्ते<BR> येषां न चेतांसि त एव धीराः Ku. 1. 59.<BR>—4 Composed, calm, collected.<BR>—5 Sedate, sober, grave, solemn; सागरधीरचेताः R. 18. 4.<BR>—6 Strong, energetic.<BR>—7 Wise, prudent, intelligent, sensible, learned, clever; तमेव धीरो<BR> विज्ञाय प्रज्ञां कुर्वीत ब्राह्मणः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 21. धृतेश्च धीरः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">Page0863-1</a>]<BR> सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R. 3. 10, 5. 38, 16. 74; U. 5. 31.<BR>—8 Deep, grave, loud, hollow (as sound); स्वरेण धीरेण निवर्तयन्निव<BR> R. 3. 43, 59; U. 6. 17.<BR>—9 Well-conducted, well-behaved.<BR>—10 Gentle, soft, agreeable, pleasing (as a breeze); धीरसमीरे यमुनातीरे<BR> वसति वने वनमाली Gīt. 5.<BR>—11 Lazy, dull.<BR>—12 Daring.<BR>—13 Headstrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरः|धीर|धीरं
धीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 An epithet of Buddha.<BR>—3 The thinking principle, the soul (चिदात्मन्).<BR>—4 An epithet of king Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरम्
धीर + .{@-रम्@} Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरम्
धीर + .{@-रम्@} ━<i>ind.</i> Boldly, firmly, steadfastly, steadily; धीरं<BR> विलोकयति Bh. 2. 31; Amaru. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धीरोदात्तः, धीरोद्धतः, धीरचेतस्, धीरप्रशान्तः, धीरललितः, धीरललिता, धीरस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0862-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोदात्तः|धीरोदात्त
धीर + -उदात्तः the hero of a poetic composition (<i>i. e.</i> a play or<BR> poem) who is brave and noble-minded; अविकत्थनः क्षमावानतिगम्भीरो<BR> महासत्त्वः । स्थेयान्निगूढमानो धीरोदात्तो दृढव्रतः कथितः ॥ S. D. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोद्धतः|धीरोद्धत
धीर + -उद्धतः the hero of a poetic composition who is brave but haughty;<BR> मायापरः प्रचण्डश्चपलोऽहंकारदर्पभूयिष्ठः । आत्मश्लाधानिरतो धीरैर्धीरोद्धतः<BR> कथितः S. D. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरचेतस्
धीर + -चेतस् <i>a.</i> firm, resolute, strong-minded, courageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरप्रशान्तः|धीरप्रशान्त|धीरप्रशांत
धीर + -प्रशान्तः the hero of a poetic composition who is brave and calm;<BR> सामान्यगुणैर्भूयान् द्विजातिको धीरप्रशान्तः स्यात् S. D. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललितः|धीरललित
धीर + -ललितः hero of a poetic composition who is firm and brave, but<BR> sportive and reckless; निश्चिन्तो मृदुरनिशं कलापरो धीरललितः स्यात् S. D. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललिता
धीर + -ललिता <i>f.</i> N. of a metre with the गणs as भरनरनग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरस्कन्धः|धीरस्कन्ध|धीरस्कंध
धीर + -स्कन्धः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरता
धीरता, -धीरत्वम्<BR>—1 Fortitude, courage, strength of mind; विपत्तौ च महाँल्लोके धीरतामनुगच्छति<BR> H. 3. 37; V. 2.<BR>—2 Suppression of jealousy &c.<BR>—3 Gravity, solemnity (as shown by silence &c.); प्रत्यादेशान्न खलु<BR> भवतो धीरतां कल्पयामि Me. 116.<BR>—4 Steadiness, firmness.<BR>—5 Wisdom, cleverness.<BR>—6 Refusal. (For other meanings see धैर्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरत्वम्
धीरता, -धीरत्वम्<BR>—1 Fortitude, courage, strength of mind; विपत्तौ च महाँल्लोके धीरतामनुगच्छति<BR> H. 3. 37; V. 2.<BR>—2 Suppression of jealousy &c.<BR>—3 Gravity, solemnity (as shown by silence &c.); प्रत्यादेशान्न खलु<BR> भवतो धीरतां कल्पयामि Me. 116.<BR>—4 Steadiness, firmness.<BR>—5 Wisdom, cleverness.<BR>—6 Refusal. (For other meanings see धैर्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरा
धीरा The heroine of a poetic composition who, though jealous of her<BR> husband or lover, suppresses all outward manifestation or expression of<BR> her resentment in his presence or as the Rasamañjarī puts it, व्यङ्ग्यकोपप्रकाशिका<BR> धीरा; see S. D. 102-105 also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धीराधीरा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीराधीरा
धीरा + -अधीरा the heroine of a poetic composition who, being jealous<BR> of her husband or lover, alternately expresses and conceals her jealousy;<BR> धीराधीरा तु सोल्लुण्ठभाषितैः खेदयेदमुम् S. D.; (व्यङ्ग्याव्यङ्ग्यकोपप्रकाशिका<BR> धीराधीरा Ras. M..)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटिः|धीलटि
धीलटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटी
धीलटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन् <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Clever, skilful. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An artist.<BR>—2 A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरः|धीवर
धीवरः A fisherman; मृगमीनसज्जनानां तृणजलसंतोषविहितवृत्तीनाम् ।<BR> लुब्धकधीवरपिशुना निष्कारणवैरिणो जगति ॥ Bh. 2. 61, 1. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरम्
धीवरः + .{@-रम्@} Iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरी
धीवरः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A fishermanʼs wife.<BR>—2 A kind of harpoon for catching fish.<BR>—3 A fish-basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरकः|धीवरक
धीवरकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु €5 U. (धुनोति धुनुते, धुत) See धू. धूनोति चम्पकवनानि<BR> धुनोत्यशोकम् K. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुः|धु
धुः <i>f.</i> Shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shaken; तीव्रवेगधुतमार्गवृक्षया (ताडकया) R. 11. 16.<BR>—2 Left, abandoned.<BR>—3 Chastened; आत्मानं चेद्विजानीयात्परं ज्ञानधुताशयः Bhāg. 7. 15. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुति
धुत + .{@-ति@} <i>f.</i> Shaking, flapping; श्येनेयस्य बृहत्पतत्रधुतयः<BR> प्रख्यापयन्त्यागमम् Mv. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन
धुन <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Sounding.<BR>—2 Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनयति
धुनयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To sound, roar.<BR>—2 To flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् €1 Ā. (धुक्षते, धुक्षित)<BR>—1 To be kindled; स्वैरेवोत्पातवातप्रसरपटुतरैर्धुक्षिते पक्षवातैः Nāg. 5. 21.<BR>—2 To live.<BR>—3 To be weary. ━<i>Caus.</i> (धुक्षयति-ते) To kindle, inflame.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@सम्@} to be kindled or excited (fig. also); संदुधुक्षे तयोः<BR> कोपः Bk. 14. 109. ━(<i>Caus.</i>) to kindle, inflame, excite; निवार्णभूयिष्ठमथास्य<BR> वीर्यं संधुक्षयन्तीव वपुर्गुणेन Ku. 3. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनिः|धुनि
धुनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> A river; पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G. L. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धुनिनाथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR> A river; पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G. L. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धुनिनाथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनिनाथः|धुनिनाथ
धुनिः + -नाथः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुकम्
धुन्धुकम् A particular defect in wood (a hole); कालकधुन्धुकसंज्ञं<BR> कीटैर्विद्धं च न शुभदं छिद्रम् Bṛ. S. 19. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुमारः|धुन्धुमार|धुंधुमारः
धुन्धुमारः<BR>—1 A kind of insect (इन्द्रगोप).<BR>—2 The smoke of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुरिः|धुन्धुरि
धुन्धुरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> A particular musical instrument; Bhāg. 1. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुरी
धुन्धुरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> A particular musical instrument; Bhāg. 1. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् <i>f.</i> (Nom. sing. धूः)<BR>—1 A yoke (lit.); न गर्दभा वाजिधुरं वहन्ति Mk. 4. 17; अत्रस्नुभिर्युक्तधुरं<BR> तुरङ्गैः R. 14. 47.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) That part of a yoke which rests on the shoulder.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The foremost part of the pole where the yoke is fixed.<BR>—3 The pin at both ends of an axle for fastening the nave of the wheel.<BR>—4 The shaft or pole of a carriage.<BR>—5 A load, burden (fig. also); responsibility, duty, task; तेन धूर्जगतो<BR> गुर्वी सचिवेषु निचिक्षिपे R. 1. 34, 2. 74, 3. 35, 5. 66; Ku. 6. 30; कार्यधुरं<BR> वहन्ति Mu. 1. 14; आप्तैरप्यनवाप्तपौरुषफलैः कार्यस्य धूरुज्झिता<BR> Mu. 6. 5, 4. 6; Ki. 3. 50, 14. 6.<BR>—6 The foremost or highest place, van, front, top, head; अपांसुलानां<BR> धुरि कीर्तनीया R. 2. 2; धुरि स्थिता त्वं पतिदेवतानाम् 14. 74; अविघ्नमस्तु<BR> ते स्थेयाः पितेव धुरि पुत्रिणाम् 1. 91; धुरि प्रतिष्ठापयितव्य एव<BR> M. 1. 16, 5. 16.<BR>—7 A finger.<BR>—8 Agitation, trembling.<BR>—9 Reflection.<BR>—10 A spark of fire.<BR>—11 Distress, affliction.<BR>—12 A part, portion, share.<BR>—13 Wealth.<BR>—14 N. of the Ganges. (धुरि कृ ‘to place at the head or in front of’;<BR> किंवाभविष्यदरुणस्तमसां विभेत्ता तं चेत्सहस्रकिरणो धुरि नाकरिष्यत् Ś. 7. 4)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धूर्गत, धूर्जटिः, धूर्धर, धूर्वह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्गत
धुर् + -गत (धूर्गत) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 standing on the pole of a chariot.<BR>—2 standing at the head, chief, head, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्जटिः|धूर्जटि|धूर्ज्जटि
धुर् + -जटिः (धूर्जटिः) an epithet of Śiva; धूर्जटिः पातु युष्मान् Ve. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्धर|धूर्धरः
धुर् + -धर (धूर्धर also धुरंधर) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bearing the yoke.<BR>—2 fit to be harnessed.<BR>—3 laden with good qualities or important duties.<BR>—4 chief, head, foremost, pre-eminent; कुलधुरंधरो भव V. 5; गजानां<BR> पङ्कमग्नानां गजा एव धुरंधराः H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्धरः|धूर्धर
धुर् + -धर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a beast of burden.<BR>—2 a man of business.<BR>—3 a chief, head, leader.<BR>—4 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वह|धूर्वहः|धूर्व्वह|धूर्व्वहः
धुर् + -वह (धूर्वह) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 carrying or bearing a burden.<BR>—2 managing affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वहः|धूर्वह|धूर्व्वह|धूर्व्वहः
धुर् + -वह + .({@-हः@}) a beast of burden; so धूर्वोढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0863-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरः|धुर
धुरः (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 A yoke, pole.<BR>—2 Burden.<BR>—3 A pin at the end of an axle &c.; see धुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरंधर|धुरन्धर|धुरन्धरः
धुरंधर See धूर्धर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा A burden, load; रणधुरा Ve. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण, धुरीय <i>a.</i> [धुरं वहति, अर्हति वा, धुर् ख छ वा]<BR>—1 Able to bear or carry a burden.<BR>—2 Fit to be harnessed.<BR>—3 Charged with important duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीण, धुरीय <i>a.</i> [धुरं वहति, अर्हति वा, धुर् ख छ वा]<BR>—1 Able to bear or carry a burden.<BR>—2 Fit to be harnessed.<BR>—3 Charged with important duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीणः|धुरीण
धुरीण, धुरीय + .{@-णः, -यः@}<BR>—1 A beast of burden.<BR>—2 A man of business, or one charged with important duties.<BR>—3 A chief, head, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्यः|धुर्य|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुरीण, धुरीय + .{@-णः, -यः@}<BR>—1 A beast of burden.<BR>—2 A man of business, or one charged with important duties.<BR>—3 A chief, head, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य <i>a.</i> [धुरं वहति, यत्]<BR>—1 Fit for a burden, able to bear a burden &c.<BR>—2 Fit to be entrusted with important duties.<BR>—3 Standing at the head, chief, foremost; see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्यः|धुर्य|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य + .{@-र्यः@}<BR>—1 A beast of burden.<BR>—2 A horse or bullock yoked to the pole of a carriage; नाविनीतैर्व्रजेद्<BR> धुर्यैः Ms. 4. 67; येनेदं ध्रियते विश्वं धुर्यैर्यानमिवाध्वनि Ku. 6. 76;<BR> धुर्यान् विश्रामयेति R. 1. 54, 6. 78, 17. 19.<BR>—3 One who carries a burden (of responsibility); तस्या भवानपरधुर्यपदावलम्बी R. 5. 66.<BR>—4 A chief, leader, head; न हि सति कुलधुर्ये सूर्यवंश्या गृहाय R. 7. 71.<BR>—5 A minister, one charged with important duties; ततो युगंधराख्यस्य<BR> हस्ते धुर्यस्य मन्त्रिणः Ks. 9. 14.<BR>—6 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्यम्
धुर्य + .{@-र्यम्@} The forepart of a pole.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धुर्यवाहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्यवाहः|धुर्यवाह
धुर्य + -वाहः a beast for draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्यता
धुर्यता Leadership; समस्तकार्येषु गतेन धुर्यताम् Śi. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्
धुर्व् €1 P. (धुर्वति) To hurt, injure; kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवका
धुवका The introductory stanza of a song; cf. ध्रुवका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवित्रम्
धुवित्रम् A sort of fan (made of deer-skin) used in kindling the sacred<BR> fire; cf. धवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवनः|धुवन
धुवनः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुरः|धुस्तुर
धुस्तु(स्तू)रः N. of a plant (= धत्तूर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तूरः|धुस्तूर
धुस्तु(स्तू)रः N. of a plant (= धत्तूर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू €6 P., €1. €5. €9. €10. U. (धुवति, धवति-ते, धूनोति, धूनुते, धुनाति,<BR> धुनीत, धूनयति-ते, also धावयति-ते, धूत-धून)<BR>—1 To shake, agitate, cause to move or tremble; धुन्वन्ति पक्षपवनैर्न<BR> नभो वलाकाः Ṛs. 3. 12; धुन्वन् कल्पद्रुमकिसलयानि Me. 64; Ku. 7. 49;<BR> R. 4. 67; Bk. 5. 101, 9. 7, 10. 22.<BR>—2 To shake off, remove, throw off; स्रजमपि शिरस्यन्धः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्यहिशङ्कया Ś. 7. 24.<BR>—3 To blow away, destroy,<BR>—4 To kindle, excite, fan (as fire); वायुना धूयमानो हि वनं दहति<BR> पावकः Mb.; पवनधूतः … अग्निः Ṛs. 1. 26.<BR>—5 To treat roughly, hurt, injure; मा न धावीररिं रणे Bk. 9. 50, 15. 61.<BR>—6 To shake off from oneself, free oneself from; (सेवकाः) आरोहन्ति<BR> शनैः पश्चाद् धुन्वन्तमपि पार्थिवम् Pt. 1. 36.<BR>—7 To strive against, resist, oppose. (The following stanza from Kavirahasya<BR> illustrates the root in its different conjugations:− धूनोति चम्पकवनानि<BR> धुनोत्यशोकं चूतं धुनाति धुवति स्फुटितातिमुक्तं । वायुर्विधूनयति चम्पकपुष्परेणून्<BR> यत्कानने धवति चन्दनमञ्जरीश्च ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूः
धूः <i>f.</i> Shaking, trembling, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूकः|धूक
धूकः<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—3 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूणकः
धूण(न)कः Resin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनकः|धूनक
धूण(न)कः Resin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत <i>p. p.</i> [धू-क्त]<BR>—1 Shaken.<BR>—2 Shaken off, removed.<BR>—3 Fanned.<BR>—4 Abandoned, deserted.<BR>—5 Reviled.<BR>—6 Judged.<BR>—7 Disregarded, treated with contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूता
धूत + .{@-ता@} A wife.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धूतकल्मष, धूतपाप, धूतगुणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतकल्मष
धूत + -कल्मष, -पाप <i>a.</i> who has shaken off his sins, free from sin, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतपाप
धूत + -कल्मष, -पाप <i>a.</i> who has shaken off his sins, free from sin, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतगुणः|धूतगुण
धूत + -गुणः an ascetic practice, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतिः|धूति
धूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Shaking, moving.<BR>—2 Fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken, agitated &c.<BR>—2 Afflicted by heat or thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूननः|धूनन|धूननं
धूननः Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूननम्
धूननः + .{@-नम्@} Shaking, agitation; निशान्तनारीपरिधानधूननम् Śi. 1. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनिः|धूनि
धूनिः <i>f.</i> Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् I. €1 P. (धूपायति, धूपायित) To heat or to be heated.<BR>━II. €10 U. (धूपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To fumigate, perfume, incense, to make fragrant.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR>—3 To speak.<BR>—4 (In Astr.) To obscure with mist, eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपः|धूप
धूपः [धूप्-अच्]<BR>—1 Incense, frankincense, perfume, any fragrant substance.<BR>—2 The vapour issuing from any fragrant substance (like gum, resin &c.),<BR> aromatic vapour or smoke; धूपोष्मणा त्याजितमार्द्रभावम् Ku. 7. 14;<BR> Me. 34; V. 3. 2; R. 16. 50.<BR>—3 A fragrant powder.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धूपागुरु, धूपाङ्गः, धूपार्हम्, धूपग्रहः, धूपनेत्रम्, धूपपात्रम्, धूपवर्तिः, धूपवासः, धूपवृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपागुरु
धूपः + -अगुरु <i>n.</i> a kind of agallochum used for incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपाङ्गः|धूपाङ्ग|धूपांग
धूपः + -अङ्गः<BR>—1 turpentine.<BR>—2 the Sarala tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपार्हम्
धूपः + -अर्हम् a black kind of agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपग्रहः
धूपः + -ग्रहः a censer; N. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपनेत्रम्
धूपः + -नेत्रम् a pipe for smoking; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपपात्रम्
धूपः + -पात्रम् a vessel for incense, censer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपवर्तिः|धूपवर्ति
धूपः + -वर्तिः a kind of cigarette; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपवासः|धूपवास
धूपः + -वासः fumigating, perfuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपवृक्षः|धूपवृक्ष
धूपः + -वृक्षः a kind of pine, the Sarala tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपकः|धूपक
धूप(पि)कः A perfumer; Rām. 2. 83. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिकः|धूपिक
धूप(पि)कः A perfumer; Rām. 2. 83. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपनम्
धूपनम्<BR>—1 Fumigation, perfuming; बलयश्चान्नलाजाभिर्धूपनं दीपकर्म च Mb. 13. 99. 7.<BR>—2 Incense; लाज्यैश्च गन्धैश्च तथा वितानैरभ्यर्चितं धूपनधूपितं च<BR> Mb. 5. 192. 35; Ms. 7. 219.<BR>—3 (astrol.) The obscuration of a comet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपित|धूपितः
धूपित, धूपायित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fumigated, heated, perfumed, incensed.<BR>—2 Suffering pain or fatigue, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपायित|धूपायितः
धूपित, धूपायित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fumigated, heated, perfumed, incensed.<BR>—2 Suffering pain or fatigue, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमः|धूम
धूमः [धू-कम्पे मक्]<BR>—1 Smoke, vapour; शिरांस्यपातयत्त्रीणि वेगवद्भिस्त्रिभिः शरैः । सधूमशोणितोद्गारी<BR> रामबाणाभिपीडितः ॥ Rām. 3. 27. 18. धूमज्योतिःसलिलमरुतां सन्निपातः<BR> क्व मेघः Me. 5.<BR>—2 Mist, haze.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A meteor.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) The fall of a meteor.<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR>—5 Smoke inhaled (as a sternutatory).<BR>—6 Belch, eructation.<BR>—7 A place prepared for the building of a house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धूमाभ, धूमावलिः, धूमोत्थम्, धूमोद्गारः, धूमोपहत, धूमोर्णा, धूमकेतनः, धूमकेतुः, धूमग्रहः, धूमजः, धूमध्वजः, धूमनिर्गमनम्, धूमप, धूमपथः, धूमपानम्, धूमप्राश, धूममहिषी, धूमलता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाभ|धूमाभः
धूमः + -आभ <i>a.</i> of a smoky appearance, smoke-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाभः|धूमाभ
धूमः + -आभ + .({@-भः@}) purple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमावलिः|धूमावलि
धूमः + -आवलिः <i>f.</i> a wreath or cloud of smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोत्थम्
धूमः + -उत्थम् ammoniac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोद्गारः|धूमोद्गार
धूमः + -उद्गारः<BR>—1 issuing of smoke or vapour; धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणा जर्जरा निष्पतन्ति Me. 71.<BR>—2 eructation, belch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोपहत
धूमः + -उपहत a suffocated by smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोर्णा
धूमः + -ऊर्णा N. of the wife of Yama. ˚पतिः an epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतनः|धूमकेतन
धूमः + -केतनः, -केतुः<BR>—1 fire; कोपस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">Page0865-1</a>]<BR> नन्दकुलकाननधूमकेतोः Mu. 1. 10; R. 11. 81.<BR>—2 a meteor, comet, falling star; धूमकेतुमिव किमपि करालम् Gīt. 1;<BR> धूमकेतुरिवोत्थितः Ku. 2. 32.<BR>—3 Ketu.<BR>—4 a kind of horse; पृष्ठवंशे यदावर्त एकः संपरिलक्ष्यते । धूमकेतुरिति<BR> ख्यातः स त्याज्यो दूस्तो नृपैः ॥ Aśvachikitsā.<BR>—5 N. of the sun; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतुः|धूमकेतु
धूमः + -केतनः, -केतुः<BR>—1 fire; कोपस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">Page0865-1</a>]<BR> नन्दकुलकाननधूमकेतोः Mu. 1. 10; R. 11. 81.<BR>—2 a meteor, comet, falling star; धूमकेतुमिव किमपि करालम् Gīt. 1;<BR> धूमकेतुरिवोत्थितः Ku. 2. 32.<BR>—3 Ketu.<BR>—4 a kind of horse; पृष्ठवंशे यदावर्त एकः संपरिलक्ष्यते । धूमकेतुरिति<BR> ख्यातः स त्याज्यो दूस्तो नृपैः ॥ Aśvachikitsā.<BR>—5 N. of the sun; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0864-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमग्रहः|धूमग्रह
धूमः + -ग्रहः Rāhu; दुर्दर्शनेन घटतामियमप्यनेन धूमग्रहेण<BR> विमला शशिनः कलेव Māl. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमजः|धूमज
धूमः + -जः a cloud. ˚अङ्गजम् ammoniac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमध्वजः|धूमध्वज
धूमः + -ध्वजः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमनिर्गमनम्
धूमः + -निर्गमनम् a chimney.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमप
धूमः + -प <i>a.</i> inhaling only smoke as a sort of penance; इन्द्रेण<BR> सहिताः सर्वे आगता यज्ञभागिनः । ऊष्मपाः सोमपाश्चैव धूमपा आज्यपास्तथा<BR> Mb. 12. 284. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमपथः|धूमपथ
धूमः + -पथः<BR>—1 a sacrifice.<BR>—2 seeking salvation by religious works; (कर्ममार्ग); जगर्ह सामर्षविपन्नया<BR> गिरा शिवद्विषं धूमपथश्रमस्मयम् Bhāg. 4. 4. 10.<BR>—3 an air-hole, a window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमपानम्
धूमः + -पानम् inhaling smoke or vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमप्राश
धूमः + -प्राश <i>a.</i> feeding only on smoke (as a hermit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूममहिषी
धूमः + -महिषी fog, mist. योनिः a cloud; cf. Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमलता
धूमः + -लता a mass of curling smoke; कोपानलबहुललोलधूमलताम्<BR> (शिखाम्) Mu. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमनम्
धूमनम् (in astrol.) The obscuration (of a comet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमयति
धूमयति Den. P. To cover with smoke, obscure with mist, darken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमरी
धूमरी mist, fog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमल|धूमलः
धूमल <i>a.</i> Smoke-coloured, brownish-red, purple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमलः|धूमल
धूमल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 Purple.<BR>—2 A kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमवत्|धूमवन्त्
धूमवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Smoky.<BR>—2 Smoking, steaming. पर्वतो वह्निमान् धूमवत्त्वात् Tarkasaṃgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायति
धूमायति, -ते Den. P.<BR>—1 To cover or fill with smoke, vapour &c., darken; धूमायिता दश दिशो<BR> दलितारविन्दाः Bv. 1. 104; Mk. 5. 27.<BR>—2 To smoke, or be covered with smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायते
धूमायति, -ते Den. P.<BR>—1 To cover or fill with smoke, vapour &c., darken; धूमायिता दश दिशो<BR> दलितारविन्दाः Bv. 1. 104; Mk. 5. 27.<BR>—2 To smoke, or be covered with smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमावती
धूमावती <i>f.</i> One of the ten great goddesses of learning; विद्या<BR> धूमावती तथा Tantrasāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायनम्
धूमायनम्<BR>—1 Smoking, steaming.<BR>—2 Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिका
धूमिका Vapour, fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमित
धूमित <i>a.</i> Obscured with smoke, darkened; अहमस्य दशेव पश्य<BR> मामविषह्यव्यसनेन धूमिताम् Ku. 4. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिता
धूमित + .{@-ता@} (<i>i. e.</i> दिक्) The quarter towards which the sun turns<BR> first; धूमिताभिमुखी हन्ति स्वरदीप्ता दिगीश्वरान् Bṛ. S. 90. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिन्
धूमिन् <i>a.</i> Smoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिनी
धूमिन् + .{@-नी@} N. of one of the tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्या
धूम्या [धूमानां समूहः य] A volume or cloud of smoke, thick<BR> smoke; ‘धूम्या धूमसमूहेऽपि नीहारेऽपि निगद्यते’ इति धरणिः; स्फीतधूम्याप्रकाशम्<BR> Māl. 5. 6; देहच्छायोद्गमाभारिपुवपुरगुरुप्लोषरोषाग्निधूम्याः; विष्णुपादादिकेशान्तवर्णनस्तोत्रम् 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र <i>a.</i> [धूमं तद्वर्णं राति रा-क]<BR>—1 Smoke-coloured, smoky, grey; हुतभुग्धूमधूम्रोपकण्ठम् Bh. 3. 55; R. 15. 16.<BR>—2 Dark-red.<BR>—3 Dark, obscured.<BR>—4 Purple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0865-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रः|धूम्र
