धृ
धृ I. €6 Ā. (Supposed by some to be a passive form of धृ); (ध्रियते, धृत)<BR>—1 To be or exist, live, continue to live, survive; आर्यपुत्र ध्रिये<BR> एषा ध्रिये U. 3; ध्रियते यावदेकोऽपि रिपुस्तावत्कुतः सुखम् Śi. 2. 35, 15. 89;<BR> नष्टा शरीरैः क्रतुभिर्धरन्ते Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To be maintained or preserved, remain, continue; सुरतश्रमसंभृतो<BR> मुखे ध्रियते स्वेदलवोद्गमोऽपि ते R. 8. 51; Ku. 4. 18.<BR>—3 To resolve upon. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (धरति, usually धारयति-ते,<BR> धृत, धारित)<BR>—1 To hold, bear, carry; भुजङ्गमपि कोपितं शिरसि पुष्पवद्धारयेत्<BR> Bh. 2. 4; वैणवीं धारयेद्यष्टिं सोदकं च कमण्डलुम् Ms. 4. 36; Bk. 17. 54;<BR> V. 4. 36.<BR>—2 To hold or bear up, maintain, support, sustain; अभिनवजलधरसुन्दर<BR> धृतमन्दर … … Gīt. 1. 2. 7; यथा सर्वाणि भूतानि धरा धारयते<BR> समम् Ms. 9. 311; Pt. 1. 126; प्रातःकुन्दप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं धारयेथाः<BR> Me. 115; चिरमात्मना धृताम् R. 3. 35; U. 3. 29.<BR>—3 To hold in oneʼs possession, possess, have, keep; या संस्कृता धार्यते Bh. 2. 19.<BR>—4 To assume, take (as a form, disguise &c.); केशव धृतसूकररूप<BR> Gīt. 1. 1. 4; धारयति कोकनदरूपम् 10. 4.<BR>—5 To wear, put on, use (clothes, ornaments &c.); श्रितकमलाकुचमण्डल<BR> धृतकुण्डल ए Gīt. 1. 2. 1.<BR>—6 To hold in check, curb, restrain, stop, detain; त्वया हि धर्मो विधृतः<BR> कृत्स्नं धारयते जगत् Mb. 1. 63. 5; दधार द्रोणमायान्तं वेलेव सरितां<BR> पतिम् Mb. 7. 16. 21.<BR>—7 To fix upon, direct towards; (with dat. or loc.) ब्राह्मण्ये धृतमानसः,<BR> मनो दध्रे राजसूयाय &c.<BR>—8 To suffer, undergo.<BR>—9 To assign anything to any person, allot, assign.<BR>—10 To owe anything to a person (with dat.; rarely gen. of person, 10<BR> only in this sense); वृक्षसेचने द्वे धारयसि मे Ś. 1; तस्मै तस्य<BR> वा धनं धारयति &c.<BR>—11 To hold, contain.<BR>—12 To observe, practise.<BR>—13 To cite, quote.<BR>—14 To keep, retain (in oneʼs service).<BR>—15 To preserve, maintain.<BR>—16 To seize, lay hold of.<BR>—17 To hold out or on, endure.<BR>—18 To fix, place, deposit.<BR>—19 To intend in mind; स यद्यदेवासृजत तत्तदत्तुमाध्रियत Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 5.<BR> (The senses of this root may be variously modified according<BR> to the noun with which it is connected; <i>e. g.</i> मनसा धृ to bear<BR> in mind, remember; शिरसा, मूर्ध्नि धृ to bear on the head, respect<BR> highly; अन्तरे धृ to pledge, deposit anything as surety; समये धृ<BR> to bring to terms or agreement; दण्डं धृ to punish, chastise, use<BR> force; जीवितम्, प्राणान्, गात्रम्, शरीरम्, देहम् &c. धृ to continue<BR> to live, maintain the soul &c.; preserve the vital spirits; व्रतं धृ<BR> to observe a vow; इत्थं व्रतं धारयतः प्रजार्थम् R. 2. 25; तुलया<BR> धृ to hold in a balance, weigh &c.; मनः, मतिम्, चित्तम्, बुद्धिम् धृ<BR> to bend the mind to a thing, fix the mind upon, think of, resolve upon;<BR> गर्भं धृ to become pregnant, conceive; धारणां धृ to practise<BR> concentration or self-control &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयः|धारय
धारयः [अनुपसर्गात् लिम्प विन्दधारि इति शः P. III. 1. 138]<BR> One that owes something, a debtor; N. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृक्
धृक् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Bearing, carrying, supporting &c.;<BR> कालरूप˚, शाक्ति˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
धृत्^1 <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Possessing, bearing, holder, bearer &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: missing virAma. Dfta is next entry..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत <i>p. p.</i> [धृ-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Held, carried, borne, supported.<BR>—2 Possessed.<BR>—3 Kept, preserved, retained.<BR>—4 Seized, grasped, laid, hold of.<BR>—5 Worn, used, put on; किमित्यपास्याभरणानि यौवने धृतं त्वया वार्धकशोभि<BR> वल्कलम् Ku. 5. 44.<BR>—6 Placed, deposited.<BR>—7 Practised, observed.<BR>—8 Weighed.<BR>—9 (Actively used) Holding, bearing.<BR>—10 Intent upon.<BR>—11 Prepared, ready.<BR>—12 Resolved, firm; रिपुनिग्रहे धृतः Rām. 4. 27. 47; see धृ also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतम्
धृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Falling.<BR>—2 State, existence.<BR>—3 Taking, seizing.<BR>—4 Wearing, putting on.<BR>—5 A particular manner of fighting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धृतात्मन्, धृतोत्सेक, धृतैकवेणि, धृतगर्भ, धृतदण्ड, धृतदीधितिः, धृतपट, धृतमानस, धृतराजन्, धृतराष्ट्रः, धृतवर्मन्, धृतव्रत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतात्मन्
धृत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> firm minded, steady, calm, collected. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतोत्सेक
धृत + -उत्सेक <i>a.</i> haughty, arrogant; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतैकवेणि
धृत + -एकवेणि <i>a.</i> bearing a single braid of hair (as a sign of mourning);<BR> नियमक्षाममुखी धृतैकवेणिः Ś. 7. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतगर्भ
धृत + -गर्भ <i>a.</i> pregnant; Ks. 7. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतदण्ड
धृत + -दण्ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inflicting punishment.<BR>—2 one on whom punishment is inflicted; राजभिर्धृतदण्डास्तु कृत्वा पापानि<BR> मानवाः । निर्मलाः खर्गमायान्ति सन्तः सुकृतिनो यथा ॥ Ms. 8. 318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतदीधितिः|धृतदीधिति
धृत + -दीधितिः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतपट
धृत + -पट <i>a.</i> covered with a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतमानस
धृत + -मानस <i>a.</i> firm-minded, bent upon; तपसे धृतमानसः Rām. 7. 9. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराजन्
धृत + -राजन् <i>a.</i> ruled by a good king (as a country).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराष्ट्रः|धृतराष्ट्र
धृत + -राष्ट्रः<BR>—1 a good king.<BR>—2 a country ruled by a good king.<BR>—3 N. of the eldest son of Vyāsa by a widow of विचित्रवीर्य. [As<BR> the eldest son he was entitled to the throne, but being blind from birth,<BR> he renounced the sovereignty in favour of Pāṇḍu; but on his retirement<BR> to the woods, he undertook it himself, making Duryodhana, his eldest son,<BR> the virtual ruler. When Duryodhana was killed by Bhīma, the old king<BR> thirsted for revenge, and expressed his desire to embrace Yudhiṣṭhira<BR> and Bhīma. Kṛṣṇa readily discovered his object, and convinced that<BR> Bhīma was marked out by the king as his prey, he caused an iron image<BR> of Bhīma to be made. And when the blind king rushed forward to embrace<BR> Bhīma, Kṛṣṇa substituted the iron image which the revengeful old<BR> man pressed with so much force that it was crushed to pieces, and Bhīma<BR> escaped. Thus discomfited, he, with his wife, repaired to the Himālaya<BR> and there died after some years.]<BR>—4 N. of a bird; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतवर्मन्|धृतवर्म्मन्
धृत + -वर्मन् <i>a.</i> clad in armour, mailed. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a reputed king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतव्रत|धृतव्रतः
धृत + -व्रत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 observing vows, performing religious rites.<BR>—2 devoted, attached.<BR>—3 of a fixed law or order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतव्रतः|धृतव्रत
धृत + -व्रत + .({@-तः@}) an epithet of (1) Indra. (2) Varuṇa. (3) Agni. (4) A king<BR> in the Puru dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिः|धृति
धृतिः <i>f.</i> [धृ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Taking, holding, seizing.<BR>—2 Having, possessing.<BR>—3 Maintaining, supporting.<BR>—4 Firmness; steadiness, constancy.<BR>—5 Fortitude, energy, resolution, courage, self-command; भज धृतिं<BR> त्यज भीतिमहेतुकाम् N. 4. 105; Bg. 16. 3; Ki. 6. 11; R. 8. 66.<BR>—6 Satisfaction, contentment, pleasure, happiness, delight, joy; धृतेश्च<BR> धीरः सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R. 3. 10, 16. 82; न चक्षुर्बध्नाति धृतिम्<BR> V. 2. 8; Śi. 7. 10, 14.<BR>—7 Satisfaction considered as one of the 33 subordinate feelings (in Rhetoric);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">Page0867-1</a>]<BR> ज्ञानाभीष्टागमाद्यैस्तु संपूर्णस्पृहता धृतिः । सौहित्यवचनोल्लाससहासप्रतिभादिकृत्<BR> S. D. 198, 168; cf. Ki. 1. 36; R. 3. 10; Ms. 10. 116.<BR>—8 A sacrifice.<BR>—9 N. of a metre; Nm.<BR>—10 consideration, care for; अनादृतस्यामरसायकेष्वपि स्थिता कथं शैलजनाशुगे<BR> धृतिः Ki. 14. 10.<BR>—11 N. of the numeral 18.<BR>—12 N. of one of the 16 kalās of the moon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धृतिगृहीत, धृतिमुष्, धृतिहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0866-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिगृहीत
धृतिः + -गृहीत <i>a.</i> armed with constancy and resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमुष्
धृतिः + -मुष् <i>a.</i> destroying all composure, discomposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिहोमः|धृतिहोम
धृतिः + -होमः a sacrifice included in the marriage-rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिंकृ
धृतिं कृ<BR>—1 To keep ground, to stand still; इतश्चेतश्च धावन्तो नैव चक्रुर्धृतिं<BR> रणे Mb. 7. 114. 101.<BR>—2 To find pleasure or satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिंबन्ध्
धृतिं बन्ध्<BR>—1 To show firmness; मानं धत्स्व धृतिं बधान ऋजुतां दूरे कुरु प्रेयसि Ak. 70.<BR>—2 To fix the mind on; यद्ध्यायति यत्कुरुते धृतिं बध्नाति यत्र च Ms. 5. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमत्|धृतिमन्त्
धृतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Firm, steady, steadfast, resolute.<BR>—2 Satisfied, happy, glad, content; रामेण मैथिलसुतां दशकण्ठकृच्छ्रात्प्रत्युद्धृतां<BR> धृतिमतीं भरतो ववन्दे R. 13. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Of Brahmā.<BR>—3 Virtue, morality.<BR>—4 The sky.<BR>—5 The sea.<BR>—6 A clever man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वरी
धृत्वरी The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज्
धृज्, धृञ्ज् €1 P. (धर्जति, धृञ्जति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृञ्ज्
धृज्, धृञ्ज् €1 P. (धर्जति, धृञ्जति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् I. €1 P. (धर्षति, धर्षित)<BR>—1 To come together, be compact.<BR>—2 To hurt or injure. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (धर्षति, धर्षयति-ते)<BR>—1 To offend, hurt, injure.<BR>—2 To insult, treat with indignity.<BR>—3 To assail, overcome, overpower, conquer, destroy.<BR>—4 To dare to attack, challenge, defy. —5 To violate or outrage (as a woman).<BR>━III. €5 P. (धृष्णोति, धृष्ट)<BR>—1 To be bold or courageous; ते ह ब्राह्मणा न दधृषुः Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 2.<BR>—2 To be confident.<BR>—3 To be proud or overbearing.<BR>—4 To be impudent or impatient.<BR>—5 To dare, venture (with inf.)<BR>—6 To brave, challenge; प्रहस्तस्य पुरोमात्यान् जिहिंसुर्दधृषुस्तथा<BR> (वानराः) Bk. 14. 102.<BR>—7 To insult, treat with contumely. ━IV. €10 Ā. (धर्षयते) To assail,<BR> attack, outrage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषित
धृषित <i>a.</i> Brave, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषु|धृषुः
धृषु <i>a.</i> [धृष्-कु]<BR>—1 Bold, brave.<BR>—2 Clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषुः|धृषु
धृषु + .{@-षुः@} A heap, group, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [धृष्-क्त]<BR>—1 Bold, courageous, confident.<BR>—2 Impudent, rude, shameless, saucy, insolent; स्तुवञ्जिह्रेमि त्वां न<BR> खलु ननु धृष्टा मुखरता Śivamahimna 9; धृष्टः पार्श्वे वसति H. 2. 26.<BR>—3 Forward, presumptuous.<BR>—4 Profligate, abandoned.<BR>—5 Cruel, unkind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टः|धृष्ट
धृष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} A faithless husband or lover; कृतागा अपि निःशङ्कस्तर्जितोऽपि<BR> न लज्जितः । दृष्टदोषोऽपि मिथ्यावाक् कथितो धृष्टनायकः S. D. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टा
धृष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@} A disloyal woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धृष्टकेतुः, धृष्टद्युम्नः, धृष्टधी, धृष्टमानिन्, धृष्टवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टकेतुः|धृष्टकेतु
धृष्ट + -केतुः N. of the son of धृष्टद्युम्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टद्युम्नः|धृष्टद्युम्न
धृष्ट + -द्युम्नः N. of a son of Drupada and brother of Draupadī. [He<BR> with his father fought on the side<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">Page0867-2</a>]<BR> of the Pāṇḍavas, and for some days he acted as commander-in-chief of<BR> their forces. When Droṇa had killed Drupada after a hard struggle, Dhṛṣṭadyumna<BR> vowed that he would be revenged for the death of his father. And he was<BR> able to fulfil this vow on the morning of the 16th day of the battle,<BR> when he unfairly cut off the head of Droṇa (see Droṇa). He was afterwards<BR> surprised by Aṣvatthāman while lying asleep in the camp of the Pāṇḍavas,<BR> and was stamped to death.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टधी
धृष्ट + -धी <i>a.</i> bold, presumptuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टमानिन्
धृष्ट + -मानिन् <i>a.</i> having too high an opinion of oneself, presumptuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टवादिन्
धृष्ट + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking boldly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टि
धृष्टि <i>a.</i> Ved. Bold; धृष्टिरसि Vāj. 1. 17. ━<i>m.</i> —1 A pair<BR> of tongs. ━<i>f.</i> Boldness, bravery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bold, confident.<BR>—2 Impudent, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णिः|धृष्णि
धृष्णिः A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु <i>a.</i> [धृष्-क्नु]<BR>—1 Bold, confident, courageous, valiant, powerful (in a good sense); विष्णुः<BR> सहिष्णुर्धृष्णुश्च स एनं पालयिष्यति Mb. 14. 72. 15; रामस्य रोचिष्णुमुखस्य<BR> धृष्णुः Bk. 1. 25.<BR>—2 Shameless, impudent.<BR>—3 Ved. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्य
धृष्य <i>a.</i> To be attacked, assailable, conquerable; as in अधृष्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे €1 P. (धयति, धीत; <i>caus.</i> धापयति; <i>desid.</i> धित्सति)<BR>—1 To suck, drink, drink in, absorb (fig. also); अधाद्वसामधासीच्च<BR> रुधिरं वनवासिनाम् Bk. 15. 29, 6. 18; Ms. 4. 59; Y. 1. 140.<BR>—2 To kiss; धन्यो धयत्याननम् Gīt. 12.<BR>—3 To suck out, draw or take away.<BR>—4 To appropriate. ━<i>Caus.</i> To suckle, nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनः|धेन
धेनः [धयन्ति एनं धे-नन् इच्च]<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 A male river (नद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेना
धेनः + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 A river.<BR>—2 Speech.<BR>—3 A milch cow (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुः|धेनु
धेनुः <i>f.</i> [धयति सुतान्, धीयते वत्सैर्वा, धे-नु इच्च Tv.]<BR>—1 A cow, milch-cow; धेनुं धीराः सूनृतां वाचमाहुः U. 5. 31.<BR>—2 The female of a species (affixed to the names of other animals in this<BR> sense); as खड्गधेनुः, वडवधेनुः &c.<BR>—3 The earth. (Sometimes at the end of comp. धेनु forms a diminutive;<BR> as आसिधेनुः, खड्गधेनुः).<BR>—4 Any offering or present to Brāhmaṇa instead of or in the shape of<BR> a cow such as गुडधेनु, घृतधेनु, तिलधेनु, जलधेनु, क्षीरधेनु, मधुधेनु,<BR> शर्कराधेनु, दधिधेनु, रसधेनु, स्वरूपधेनु; Matsya P.<BR>—5 A mare; यथा धेनुः किशोरेण MS. 7. 4. 7. (तद्यथा कृष्णकिशोरा<BR> धेनुरिति । यद्यपि धेनुशब्दो गोधेन्वां दृष्टप्रवृत्तिस्तथाप्यभिधानसामान्यादश्वधेन्वामपि<BR> भागीति किशोरेण लिङ्गेन अश्वधेन्वां विज्ञायते । ŚB. on MS.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धेनुदक्षिण, धेनुदुग्धम्, धेनुमक्षिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुदक्षिण
धेनुः + -दक्षिण <i>a.</i> (a sacrifice) whereat a cow is given as a fee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुदुग्धम्
धेनुः + -दुग्धम्<BR>—1 cowʼs milk.<BR>—2 a kind of gourd (Mar. चिबुड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुमक्षिका
धेनुः + -मक्षिका a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकः|धेनुक
धेनुकः<BR>—1 N. of a demon killed by Balarāma. दारुणो धेनुको नाम दैत्यो गर्दभरूपवान् Hariv.<BR>—2 A mode of sexual enjoyment; see धैनुक.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धेनुकसूदनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकसूदनः|धेनुकसूदन
धेनुकः + -सूदनः an epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0867-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुका
धेनुका<BR>—1 A female elephant.<BR>—2 A milch-cow.<BR>—3 A gift, an offering.<BR>—4 A female animal in general.<BR>—5 A dagger; L. D. B.<BR>—6 Pārvatī; स्त्रियां स्याद्धेनुका वाजियोषित्यपि पशौ गवि । भवान्यां<BR> च कृपाण्यां च प्रसूताकरियोषितोः ॥ Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्टरी
धेनुष्टरी A milch-cow ceasing to give milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या A cow who or whose milk has been pledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेय
धेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be held or taken.<BR>—2 To be produced.<BR>—3 To be fed or nourished.<BR>—4 To be drunk.<BR>—5 An affix as in नाम˚, भाग˚, q. v.<BR>—6 To be applied or put in practice; अव्याकुलं प्रकृतमुत्तरधेयकर्म Śi. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेयम्
धेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Nourishing.<BR>—2 Drinking.<BR>—3 Holding, taking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुकम्
धैनुकम्<BR>—1 A herd of cows.<BR>—2 A particular mode of sexual enjoyment (रतिबन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यम्
धैर्यम् [धीरस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Firmness, durability, strength, constancy, steadiness, stability, fortitude,<BR> courage; धैर्यमवष्टभ्य Pt. 1; विपदि धैर्यम् Bh. 2. 63;<BR>—2 Calmness, composure.<BR>—3 Gravity, patience.<BR>—4 Inflexibility. उदस्य धैर्यं दयितेन सादरम् Ki. 8. 50.<BR>—5 Boldness, forwardness; तस्मादस्याः कुमुदविशदार्न्यहसि त्वं न धैर्यान्मोघीकर्तुं<BR> चटुलशफरोद्वर्तनप्रेक्षितानि Me. 40 (धाष्टर्प Malli.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धैर्यकलित, धैर्यवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यकलित|धैर्य्यकलित
धैर्यम् + -कलित <i>a.</i> steady, calm; अवधीर्य धैर्यकलिता दयितम् Śi. 9. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यवृत्तिः|धैर्यवृत्ति
धैर्यम् + -वृत्तिः Steady conduct, composure; संजातवेपथुभिरुज्झितधैर्यवृत्तिरिच्छामि<BR> चैनमदयं परिरब्धुमङ्गैः V. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवतः|धैवत
धैवतः The sixth of the seven primary notes of the Indian gamut.<BR> गत्वा नाभेरधो भागं वस्तिं प्राप्योर्ध्वगः पुनः । धावन्निव च यो याति<BR> कण्ठदेशं स धैवतः ॥ Saṅgītadāmodara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत्यम्
धैवत्यम् Cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोडः|धोड
धोडः = डुण्डुभः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर्
धोर् P.<BR>—1 (धोरति) To go quickly, have good paces, run, trot.<BR>—2 To be skilful (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणम्
धोरणम् [धोर् करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A vehicle in general (as a horse, elephant &c.); दृष्ट्वा त्वरेण निजधोरणतोऽवतीर्य<BR> Bhāg. 10. 13. 62.<BR>—2 Going well or quickly.<BR>—3 A horseʼs trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणिः|धोरणि
धोरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [धोर्-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 An uninterrupted series or continutity; यैर्माकन्दवने मनोज्ञपवने<BR> सद्यः स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधौतधामनि धराधीशत्वमालम्ब्यते । तेषां<BR> नित्यविनोदिनां सुकृतिनां माध्वीकपानां पुनः कालः किं न करोति केतकि<BR> यतस्त्वं चापि केलिस्थली Udb.; N. 15. 49.<BR>—2 Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणी
धोरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [धोर्-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 An uninterrupted series or continutity; यैर्माकन्दवने मनोज्ञपवने<BR> सद्यः स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधौतधामनि धराधीशत्वमालम्ब्यते । तेषां<BR> नित्यविनोदिनां सुकृतिनां माध्वीकपानां पुनः कालः किं न करोति केतकि<BR> यतस्त्वं चापि केलिस्थली Udb.; N. 15. 49.<BR>—2 Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरितम्
धोरितम् [धोर्-भावे क्त]<BR>—1 Injuring, hurting, striking.<BR>—2 Going, motion.<BR>—3 A horseʼs trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत <i>p. p.</i> [धाव्-क्त ऊठ्]<BR>—1 Washed, washed off, cleaned, purified, laved; कुल्याम्भोभिः पवनचपलैः<BR> शाखिनो धौतमूलाः Ś. 1. 15; Śik. 58; Ku. 1. 6, 6, 57; R. 16. 49, 19. 10.<BR>—2 Polished, brightened; षष्ठपा शरैः संयति तैलधौतैर्जघान तानप्यथ<BR> पृष्ठगोपान् Mb. 6. 85. 7.<BR>—3 Bright, white, shining, brightened, glistening; हरशिरश्चन्द्रिकाधौतहर्म्या<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">Page0868-2</a>]<BR> Me. 7, 46; विकसदृन्ताशुधौताधरम् Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतम्
धौत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Silver.<BR>—2 Cleaning, washing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: धौतापाङ्ग, धौतात्मन्, धौतकट, धौतकोषजम्, धौतकौःषेयम्, धौतखण्डी, धौतमूल, धौतशिलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतापाङ्ग
धौत + -अपाङ्ग <i>a.</i> having the corners of the eyes illumined; Me. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतात्मन्
धौत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> pure-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकट|धौतकटः
धौत + -कट a bag of coarse cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकोषजम्
धौत + -कोषजम्, -कौःषेयम् bleached or purified silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकौःषेयम्
धौत + -कोषजम्, -कौःषेयम् bleached or purified silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतखण्डी
धौत + -खण्डी sugar-candy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतमूल
धौत + -मूल <i>a.</i> (a tree) having its roots washed; शाखिनो धौतमूलाः Ś. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतशिलम्
धौत + -शिलम् rock-crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतेयः|धौतेय|धौतेयं
धौतेयः A kind of salt (सैन्धव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतेयम्
धौतेयम् Rock-salt (सैन्धव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतरि
धौतरि <i>a.</i> Ved. Shaking, trembling; ससवान् त्स्तौलाभिर्धौतरीभिः Rv. 6. 44. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौति
धौति, -ती <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A spring.<BR>—2 A river; यो धौतीनामहिहन्नारिणक् पथः Rv. 2. 13. 5.<BR>—3 One of the ways of practising Yoga; धौती बस्ती तथा नौती नौलिकी त्रोटकस्तथा ।<BR> कपालभाती चैतानि षट् कर्माणि समाचरेत् ॥ Haṭhayogapradīpikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौती
धौति, -ती <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A spring.<BR>—2 A river; यो धौतीनामहिहन्नारिणक् पथः Rv. 2. 13. 5.<BR>—3 One of the ways of practising Yoga; धौती बस्ती तथा नौती नौलिकी त्रोटकस्तथा ।<BR> कपालभाती चैतानि षट् कर्माणि समाचरेत् ॥ Haṭhayogapradīpikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्यः|धौम्य
धौम्यः N. of an ancient Ṛṣi; the family priest of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्रः|धौम्र
धौम्रः<BR>—1 Greyness.<BR>—2 A place for building (prepared in a particular way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरितकम्
धौरितकम् A horseʼs trot; cf. धौरित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेय|धौरेयः
धौरेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [धुरं वहति ढक्] Fit for a burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेयः|धौरेय
धौरेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 A beast of burden.<BR>—2 A horse.<BR>—3 A chief, leader; वयं वसिष्ठधौरेयाः सर्वे प्रतिभुवोऽत्र वः Mv. 3. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तकम्
धौर्तकम्, धौर्तिंकम्, धौर्त्यम्<BR> Fraud, dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तिंकम्
धौर्तकम्, धौर्तिंकम्, धौर्त्यम्<BR> Fraud, dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्त्यम्
धौर्तकम्, धौर्तिंकम्, धौर्त्यम्<BR> Fraud, dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्यम्
धौर्यम् A horseʼs trot, cf. धोरणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा €1 P. (धमति, ध्मात; <i>Caus.</i> ध्मापयति)<BR>—1 To blow, breathe out, exhale.<BR>—2 To blow (as a wind-instrument), produce sound by blowing; शङ्खं<BR> दध्मौ प्रतापवान् Bg. 1. 12, 18; R. 7. 63; Bk. 3. 34, 17. 7.<BR>—3 To blow a fire, excite fire by blowing, excite sparks; को धमेच्छान्तं<BR> च पावकम् Mb.<BR>—4 To manufacture by blowing.<BR>—5 To cast, blow, or throw away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माकारः|ध्माकार
ध्माकारः A blacksmith, smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मात
ध्मात <i>p. p.</i> [ध्मा-क्त]<BR>—1 Blown (as a wind-instrument). ध्माता गिरेर्धातवः Bh.<BR>—2 Blown up or into, inflamed, blown, fanned, excited.<BR>—3 Inflated, puffed, puffed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मानम्
ध्मानम् Blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मापनम्
ध्मापनम् Inflating, swelling by blowing into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मापित
ध्मापित <i>a.</i> Reduced to ashes, burnt to cinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माङ्क्ष्|ध्मांक्ष्
ध्माङ्(ध्वाङ्)क्ष् €1 P. (ध्माङ्क्षति)<BR>—1 To crow, or caw.<BR>—2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष्|ध्वांक्ष्
ध्माङ्(ध्वाङ्)क्ष् €1 P. (ध्माङ्क्षति)<BR>—1 To crow, or caw.<BR>—2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याङ्क्षः|ध्याङ्क्ष
ध्याङ्क्षः see ध्वाङ्क्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c.<BR> See under ध्यै; ध्यातं वित्तमहर्निशं<BR> नियमितप्राणैर्न शम्भोः पदम् Bh. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c.<BR> See under ध्यै; ध्यातं वित्तमहर्निशं<BR> नियमितप्राणैर्न शम्भोः पदम् Bh. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c.<BR> See under ध्यै; ध्यातं वित्तमहर्निशं<BR> नियमितप्राणैर्न शम्भोः पदम् Bh. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0868-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम <i>a.</i> Unclean, dirty, black, soiled; Bk. 8. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामम्
ध्याम + .{@-मम्@} A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामन्
ध्यामन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Measure.<BR>—2 Light. ━<i>n.</i> Meditation (less correctly ध्मामन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै €1 P. (ध्यायति, ध्यात; <i>desid.</i> दिध्यासति; <i>pass.</i><BR> ध्यायते) To think of, meditate upon, ponder over, contemplate, reflect<BR> upon, imagine, call to mind; ध्यायतो विषयान् पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते<BR> Bg. 2. 62; न ध्यातं पदमीश्वरस्य Bh. 3. 11; पितॄन् ध्यायन् Ms. 3. 224;<BR> ध्यायन्ति चान्यं धिया Pt. 1. 136; Me. 3; Ms. 5. 47, 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्या
ध्या Thought, meditation, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात <i>p. p.</i> [ध्यै-क्त] Thought of, meditated or reflected upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातव्य
ध्यातव्य, ध्येय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be meditated upon, to be contemplated.<BR>—2 Fit for meditation; ध्येयः सदा सवितृमण्डलमध्यवर्ती Viṣṇudhyānam.<BR>—3 To be imagined or conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्येय|ध्येयः
ध्यातव्य, ध्येय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be meditated upon, to be contemplated.<BR>—2 Fit for meditation; ध्येयः सदा सवितृमण्डलमध्यवर्ती Viṣṇudhyānam.<BR>—3 To be imagined or conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात्वम्
ध्यात्वम् Thought, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान [ध्यै-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Meditation, reflection, thought; contemplation; ज्ञानाद् ध्यानं विशिष्यते<BR> Bg. 12. 12; Ms. 1. 12, 6. 72.<BR>—2 Especially, abstract contemplation, religious meditation; तदैव<BR> ध्यानादवगतोऽस्मि Ś. 7; ध्यानस्तिमितलोचनः R. 1. 73.<BR>—3 Divine intuition or discernment.<BR>—4 Mental representation of the personal attributes of a deity; इति ध्यानम्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्यानगम्य, ध्यानतत्पर, ध्याननिष्ठ, ध्यानपर, ध्यानधिष्ण्य, ध्यानमात्रम्, ध्यानमुद्रा, ध्यानयोगः, ध्यानस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानगम्य
ध्यान + -गम्य <i>a.</i> attainable by meditation only; योगिभिर्ध्यानगम्यम् Viṣṇustotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानतत्पर
ध्यान + -तत्पर, -निष्ठ, -पर <i>a.</i> lost in thought, absorbed in meditation, contemplative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याननिष्ठ
ध्यान + -तत्पर, -निष्ठ, -पर <i>a.</i> lost in thought, absorbed in meditation, contemplative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानपर
ध्यान + -तत्पर, -निष्ठ, -पर <i>a.</i> lost in thought, absorbed in meditation, contemplative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानधिष्ण्य
ध्यान + -धिष्ण्य <i>a.</i> suitable for ध्यान; रूपं चेदं पौरुषं ध्यानधिष्ण्यम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानमात्रम्
ध्यान + -मात्रम् mere thought or reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानमुद्रा
ध्यान + -मुद्रा a prescribed attitude in which to meditate on a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानयोगः|ध्यानयोग
ध्यान + -योगः profound meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानस्थ
ध्यान + -स्थ <i>a.</i> absorbed in meditation; lost in thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यानिक <i>a.</i> Sought or obtained by pious contemplation or abstract<BR> meditation; ध्यानिकं सर्वमेवैतद्यदेतदभिशब्दितम् Ms. 7. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिन्
ध्यानिन् <i>a.</i> contemplative, engaged in religious meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिबुद्धः|ध्यानिबुद्ध
ध्यानिन् + .{@-बुद्धः, -बोधिसत्त्वः@} a spiritual Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिबोधिसत्त्वः|ध्यानिबोधिसत्त्व
ध्यानिन् + .{@-बुद्धः, -बोधिसत्त्वः@} a spiritual Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्र
ध्र <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Holding, supporting; as in महीध्रः, कुध्रः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज्
ध्रज्, ध्रञ्ज् €1 P. (ध्रजति &c.) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रञ्ज्
ध्रज्, ध्रञ्ज् €1 P. (ध्रजति &c.) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रजि
ध्रजि <i>f.</i> Gliding motion (of wind) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राजिः|ध्राजि
ध्राजिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 = ध्रजिः.<BR>—2 Impulse.<BR>—3 Strong wind, storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण्
ध्रण् €1 P. (ध्रणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस्
ध्रस् €9 P., €10 U. (ध्रस्नाति, ध्रासयति-ते) To throw or toss up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रा
ध्रा €1 P. (ध्राति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख्
ध्राख् €1 P.<BR>—1 To be dry or arid.<BR>—2 To clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ्
ध्राघ् €1 Ā. —1 To be able or competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राङ्क्ष्|ध्रांक्ष्
ध्राङ्क्ष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To crow, caw.<BR>—2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड्
ध्राड् €1 Ā. To divide, split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राडिः|ध्राडि
ध्राडिः Gathering flowers (पुष्पचय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज्
ध्रिज् €1 P. To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु €1. €6 P. (ध्रवति, ध्रुवति)<BR>—1 To be firm or fixed.<BR>—2 To go, move (ध्रु गतिस्थैर्ययोः) बुद्धिपूर्वं ध्रुवन् … Bk. 6. 130.<BR>—3 To ascertain, know definitely.<BR>—4 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुतिः|ध्रुति
ध्रुतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Fixed destiny.<BR>—2 Misleading, corrupting, seduction; न स स्वो दक्षो वरुण ध्रुतिः<BR> सा Rv. 7. 86. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Fixed, firm, immovable, stable, permanent, constant, unchangeable;<BR> इति ध्रुवेच्छामनुशासती सुताम् Ku. 5. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Perpetual, everlasting, eternal; ध्रुवेण भर्त्रा Ku. 7. 85; Ms. 7. 208.<BR>—2 Fixed (in astrology).<BR>—3 Certain, sure, inevitable; जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य<BR> च Bg. 2. 27; यो ध्रुवाणि परित्यज्य अध्रुवं परिषेवते Cāṇ. 63; Pt. 1. 419.<BR>—4 Retentive, tenacious; as in ध्रुवा स्मृति Ch. Up. 7. 26. 2.<BR>—5 Strong, fixed, settled (as a day).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf. quotation and other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवः|ध्रुव|ध्रुवं
ध्रुव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 The polar star; शरत्प्रसन्नैर्ज्योतिर्भिर्विभावर्य इव ध्रुवम् (अन्वयुः)<BR> R. 17. 35, 18. 34; ध्रुवेण भर्त्रा ध्रुवदर्शनाय प्रयुज्यमाना प्रियदर्शनेन<BR> (सा दृष्टा) Ku. 7. 85.<BR>—2 The pole of any great circle.<BR>—3 The distance of a planet from the beginning of the sidereal zodiac,<BR> polar longitude.<BR>—4 The Indian figtree.<BR>—5 A post, stake.<BR>—6 The stem or trunk (of a tree lopped off).<BR>—7 The introductory stanza of a song (repeated as a kind of chorus; see Gīt.).<BR>—8 Time, epoch, era.<BR>—9 An epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—10 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—11 Of Śiva.<BR>—12 A constant arc.<BR>—13 The tip of the nose.<BR>—14 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>—15 N. of the son of Uttānapāda and grandson of Manu. [Dhruva is the<BR> polar star, but personified in mythology as the son of Uttānapāda. The<BR> account of the elevation of an ordinary mortal to the position of the<BR> polar star runs thus: Uttānapāda had two wives, Suruchi and Sunīti,<BR> but the latter was disliked by him. Suruchi had a son named Uttama, and<BR> Sunīti gave birth to Dhruva. One day the boy tried, like his elder brother,<BR> to take a seat in his fatherʼs lap, but he was contemptuously treated<BR> both by the King and his favourite wife. The poor child went sobbing to<BR> its mother who told him in consolatory terms that fortune and favour were<BR> not attainable without hard exertions. At these words the youth left the<BR> paternal roof, retired to the woods, and, though quite a lad, performed<BR> such rigorous austerities that he was at last raised by Viṣṇu to the<BR> position of the Polar Star.]<BR>—16 Peg Nm.<BR>—17 N. of an astrological yoga (Nm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवम्
ध्रुव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 The sky, atmosphere.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR>—3 The fixed point (from which a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">Page0870-1</a>]<BR> departure takes place); P. I. 4. 24.<BR>—4 A certain Yoga (अमृतसिद्धि); सेनामाज्ञापयामासुर्नक्षत्रेऽहनि<BR> च ध्रुवे Mb. 14. 63. 18. (Com. रोहिण्यामुत्तररात्रये च अहनि वारे<BR> ध्रुवे रविवारे उत्तरार्केऽमृतसिद्धियोगे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवा
ध्रुव + .{@-वा@}<BR>—1 A sacrificial ladle (made of wood); साधारण्यान्न ध्रुवायां स्यात् Jaimini S.<BR>—2 A virtuous woman.<BR>—3 A cow who stands still when being milked; सहस्रं धारा द्रविणस्य<BR> मे दुहां ध्रुवेव धेनुरनपस्फुरन्ती Av. 12. 1. 45.<BR>—4 A bow-string.<BR>—5 clapping the hands together to show a particular measure of time in<BR> music; स्रुचि मौर्व्यां तालभेदे स्त्रियाम् Nm.<BR>—6 The upper quarter (ऊर्ध्व); किंदेवतोऽस्यां ध्रुवायां दिशि Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 24.<BR> (MWʼs meaning is अधरदिशा ?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवम्
ध्रुव + .{@-वम्@} <i>ind.</i> Certainly, surely, verily; R. 8. 49; ध्रुवं स<BR> नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया समिल्लतां छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यवस्यति Ś. 1. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्रुवाक्षरः, ध्रुवायर्तः, ध्रुवकेतुः, ध्रुवगतिः, ध्रुवतारा, ध्रुवतारकम्, ध्रुवभागः, ध्रुवमण्डलम्, ध्रुवयष्टिः, ध्रुवयोनि, ध्रुवरत्ना, ध्रुवशील^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0869-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवाक्षरः|ध्रुवाक्षर
ध्रुव + -अक्षरः an epithet of Viṣṇu (ओम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवायर्तः
ध्रुव + -आयर्तः the point on the crown of the head from which the hair radiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवकेतुः|ध्रुवकेतु
ध्रुव + -केतुः a kind of meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवगतिः|ध्रुवगति
ध्रुव + -गतिः a firm position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवतारा
ध्रुव + -तारा, -तारकम् the Polar star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवतारकम्
ध्रुव + -तारा, -तारकम् the Polar star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवभागः|ध्रुवभाग
ध्रुव + -भागः the unchangeable longitude of fixed stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवमण्डलम्
ध्रुव + -मण्डलम् the polar region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवयष्टिः|ध्रुवयष्टि
ध्रुव + -यष्टिः the axis of the poles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवयोनि
ध्रुव + -योनि <i>a.</i> having a firm resting place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवरत्ना
ध्रुव + -रत्ना N. of one of the मातृकाs (attending on Skanda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवशील
ध्रुव + -शील^1 <i>a.</i> having a fixed residence.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवकः|ध्रुवक
ध्रुवकः<BR>—1 The introductory stanza of a song (repeated as a sort of chorus); see ध्रुव.<BR>—2 A trunk, stem.<BR>—3 A post.<BR>—4 Polar longitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवि
ध्रुवि <i>a.</i> Ved. Firm, stable; शं नः पर्वता ध्रुवयो भवन्तु Rv. 7. 35. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक्
ध्रेक् €1 Ā. (ध्रेकते)<BR>—1 To sound.<BR>—2 To grow, increase.<BR>—3 To be filled with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
ध्रै €1 P. (ध्रायति) To be pleased or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव्यम्
ध्रौव्यम्<BR>—1 Fixedness, firmness, stability; परो ध्रौव्याध्रौव्ये जगति गदति<BR> व्यस्तविषये Śivamahimna 9.<BR>—2 Duration.<BR>—3 Certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस्
ध्वंस् €1 Ā. (ध्वंसते, ध्वस्त)<BR>—1 To fall down, fall to pieces, be reduced<BR> to dust or powder; प्राणा दध्वंसिरे गात्रं तस्तम्भे च प्रिये हते<BR> Bk. 14. 55, 15. 93;<BR>—2 To drop, sink, despond; प्रयान्तीव प्राणाः सुतनु हृदयं ध्वंसत<BR> इव Māl. 9. 45.<BR>—3 To perish, be ruined or decayed.<BR>—4 To be eclipsed धूमैर्ध्वस्तार्कभासां सघनमिव दिशां मण्डलं दर्शयन्तः Mu. 3. 28.<BR>—5 To be covered with dust.<BR>—6 To scatter or sprinkle over.<BR>—7 To go. ━<i>Caus.</i> (ध्वंसयति) To destroy, ruin, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसः|ध्वंस
ध्वंसः [ध्वंस्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Falling down, sinking, falling to pieces.<BR>—2 Vanishing, disappearance; ध्रुवं ध्वंसो भावी जलनिधिमहीशैलसरिताम्.<BR>—3 Loss, destruction, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसी
ध्वंसः + .{@-सी@} A mote in the sun-beam.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वंसकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसकारिन्
ध्वंसः + -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 destroying; स हि गगनविहारी कल्मषध्वंसकारी H. 1. 19.<BR>—2 violating; मर्त्योऽप्यन्तःपुरध्वंसकारी Ks. 106. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसकः|ध्वंसक
ध्वंसकः A kind of disease (caused by over-drinking).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन <i>a.</i> [ध्वंस्-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>—1 Destroying, ruining; ‘पाता विश्वस्य शश्वत्सकलसुररिपुध्वंसनः’<BR> -विष्णुपादादिकेशान्तवर्णनस्तोत्रम् 7.<BR>—2 Scattering, dispersing.<BR>—3 Sprinkling, covering.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">Page0870-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसनम्
ध्वंसन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Perishing, dying.<BR>—2 Loss, destruction.<BR>—3 Falling.<BR>—4 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिः|ध्वंसि
ध्वंसिः The hundredth part of a Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसित
ध्वंसित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Destroyed, demolished, ruined.<BR>—2 Removed, driven away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Destroying, demolishing, removing.<BR>—2 Falling, perishing, as in क्षणध्वांसिन्. ━<i>m.</i> The Pīlu tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen.<BR>—2 Destroyed, removed.<BR>—3 Lost, perished; वरं कृतध्वस्तगुणादत्यन्तमगुणः पुमान् Ki. 15. 15; Amaru. 15.<BR>—4 Covered (with dust or anything); काञ्चनं रजसा ध्वस्तम् Rām. 7. 104. 25.<BR>—5 Eclipsed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वस्ताक्ष<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्ताक्ष
ध्वस्त + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> Whose eyes are sunk (as in death); प्रकीर्णकेशं<BR> ध्वस्ताक्षम् Bhāg. 7. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्तिः|ध्वस्ति
ध्वस्तिः <i>f.</i> Destruction, ruin, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज्
ध्वज् €1 P. (ध्वजति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजः|ध्वज
ध्वजः [ध्वज्-अच्]<BR>—1 A flag, banner, standard, ensign; R. 7. 40, 17. 32; आरोहति न यः<BR> स्वस्य वंशस्याग्रे ध्वजो यथा Pt. 1. 26; ध्वजं चक्रे च भगवानुपरि<BR> स्थास्यतीति तम् Mb.<BR>—2 A distinguished or eminent person, the flag or ornament (at the end<BR> of comp.); as in कुलध्वजः ‘the head, ornament, or distinguished person of a family’<BR>.<BR>—8 A flagstaff.<BR>—4 A mark, emblem, sign, a symbol; वृषभ˚, मकर˚ &c.<BR>—5 the attribute of a deity.<BR>—6 The sign of a tavern.<BR>—7 The sign of a trade, any trademark.<BR>—8 The organ of generation (of any animal, male or female).<BR>—9 One who prepares and sells liquors; Ms. 4. 85; सुरापाने सुराध्वजः Ms.<BR>—10 A house situated to the east of any object.<BR>—11 Pride.<BR>—12 Hypocrisy.<BR>—13 A skull carried on a staff (as a mark of ascetics) or as a penance<BR> for the murder of a Brāhmaṇa; see खट्वाङ्ग.<BR>—14 (In prosody) An iambic foot. (ध्वजीकृ to hoist a flag; (fig.)<BR> to use as a plea or pretext.)<BR>—15 part of a sword; श्रेष्ठखड्गाङ्गयोरपि Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वजांशुकम्, ध्वजपटः, ध्वजपटम्, ध्वजारोपणम्, ध्वजारोहणम्, ध्वजारोहः, ध्वजाहृत, ध्वजोच्छ्रयः, ध्वजोत्थानम्, ध्वजगृहम्, ध्वजद्रुमः, ध्वजप्रहरणः, ध्वजभङ्गः, ध्वजपातः, ध्वजयन्त्रम्, ध्वजयष्टिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजांशुकम्
ध्वजः + -अंशुकम्, -पटः, -पटम् a flag; तमाधूतध्वजपटं व्योमगङ्गोर्मिवायुभिः R. 12. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजपटः|ध्वजपट
ध्वजः + -अंशुकम्, -पटः, -पटम् a flag; तमाधूतध्वजपटं व्योमगङ्गोर्मिवायुभिः R. 12. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजपटम्
ध्वजः + -अंशुकम्, -पटः, -पटम् a flag; तमाधूतध्वजपटं व्योमगङ्गोर्मिवायुभिः R. 12. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजारोपणम्
ध्वजः + -आरोपणम्, -आरोहणम् raising a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजारोहणम्
ध्वजः + -आरोपणम्, -आरोहणम् raising a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजारोहः|ध्वजारोह
ध्वजः + -आरोहः a kind of ornament on a flag; काञ्चना मणिचित्राङ्गा ज्वलन्त<BR> इव पावकाः । अर्चिष्मन्तो व्यरोचन्त ध्वजारोहा सहस्रशः ॥ Mb. 6. 16. 12. (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजाहृत
ध्वजः + -आहृत <i>a.</i> seized on the battle-field; Ms. 8. 415.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजोच्छ्रयः
ध्वजः + -उच्छ्रयः hypocrisy; Mb. 3. 3/3. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजोत्थानम्
ध्वजः + -उत्थानम् a festival in honour of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजगृहम्
ध्वजः + -गृहम् a room in which banners are kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजद्रुमः|ध्वजद्रुम
ध्वजः + -द्रुमः the palm tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजप्रहरणः|ध्वजप्रहरण
ध्वजः + -प्रहरणः air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजभङ्गः|ध्वजभङ्ग
ध्वजः + -भङ्गः, -पातः inability to beget children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजपातः
ध्वजः + -भङ्गः, -पातः inability to beget children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजयन्त्रम्
ध्वजः + -यन्त्रम् any contrivance to which a flag-staff is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजयष्टिः|ध्वजयष्टि
ध्वजः + -यष्टिः a flag-staff; संक्रमध्वजयष्टीनां प्रतिमानां च भेदकः Ms. 9. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजवत्|ध्वजवन्त्
ध्वजवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Adorned with flags.<BR>—2 Having a mark.<BR>—3 Having the mark of a criminal, branded; शिरःकपाली ध्वजवान्भिक्षाशी<BR> कर्म वेदयन् Y. 3. 243. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A standard-bearer.<BR>—2 A vendor of spirituous liquors, distiller; Ms. 4. 84.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa who carries with him the skull of the man murdered by<BR> him to places of pilgrimage by way of penance; cf. com. on Y. 3. 243.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0870-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिकः|ध्वजिक
ध्वजिकः A hypocrite (who only makes a pretence of religion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ध्वजोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Bearing or carrying a flag.<BR>—2 Having as a mark.<BR>—3 Having the mark of a liquor-vessel (सुराभाजनचिह्न); सुरापानापनुत्यर्थं<BR> वालवासा जटी ध्वजी Ms. 11. 93. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A standard-bearer.<BR>—2 A distiller or vendor of spirituous liquors; Y. 1. 141.<BR>—3 A car, carriage, chariot.<BR>—4 A mountain.<BR>—5 A snake.<BR>—6 A peacock.<BR>—7 A horse.<BR>—8 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—9 A hypocrite; धर्मवैतंसिकाः क्षुद्रा मुष्णन्ति ध्वजिनो जगत् M. 12. 158. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिनी
ध्वजिन् + .{@-नी@} An army; R. 7. 40; Śi. 12. 66; पृथुभिर्ध्वजिनीरवैरकार्षीच्चकितोद्भ्रान्तमृगानि<BR> काननानि Ki. 13. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजीकरणम्
ध्वजीकरणम्<BR>—1 Raising a standard, hoisting a flag.<BR>—2 Setting up as a pretext of claim, making anything a plea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण्
ध्वण् €1 P. (ध्वणति) To sound; cf. ध्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
ध्वन् €1 P. also €10 P. (ध्वनति, ध्वनयति, ध्वनित) To sound,<BR> produce or utter sounds, buzz, hum, echo, reverberate, thunder, roar; विभिद्यमाना<BR> इव दध्वनुर्दिशः Ki. 14. 46; अयं धीरं धीरं ध्वनति नवनीलो जलधरः<BR> Bv. 1. 60; कपिर्दध्वान भेघवत् Bk. 9. 5, 14. 3; ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे<BR> श्रवणमपिदधाति Gīt. 5. ━<i>Caus.</i> (ध्वनयति)<BR>—1 To cause to sound, ring (as a bell); but ध्वानयति ‘to cause to articulate indistinctly’<BR>.<BR>—2 To allude, hint at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनः|ध्वन
ध्वनः<BR>—1 Sound, tune.<BR>—2 Hum, buzz.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वनमोदिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनमोदिन्
ध्वनः + -मोदिन् <i>m.</i> a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वननम्
ध्वननम् [ध्वन्-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sounding.<BR>—2 Hinting at, suggesting or implying (as a meaning).<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) The same as व्यञ्जना q. v., or that power of a word<BR> or sentence by virtue of which it conveys a sense different from its primary<BR> or secondary meaning, suggestive power; cf. अञ्जन also वृत्तिर्व्यञ्जनध्वननगमनप्रत्यायनादिव्यपदेशविषया<BR> व्यञ्जना नाम S. D.<BR>—4 Humming, indistinct utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिः|ध्वनि
ध्वनिः [ध्वन्-इन्]<BR>—1 Sound, echo, noise in general; मृदङ्गधीरध्वनिमन्वगच्छत् R. 16. 13, 2. 72, 4. 72;<BR> U. 6. 17. शब्दो ध्वनिश्च वर्णश्च मृदङ्गादिभवो ध्वनिः<BR> Bhāṣā P.; स्फोटस्य ग्रहणे हेतुः प्राकृतो ध्वनिरिष्यते Vāk. P.<BR>—2 Tune, note, tone; Śi. 6. 48.<BR>—3 The sound of a musical instrument;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">Page0871-2</a>]<BR> पटुपटहध्वनिभिर्विनीतनिद्रः R. 9. 71.<BR>—4 The roar or thunder of a cloud.<BR>—5 A mere empty sound.<BR>—6 A word.<BR>—7 Hint, implied meaning.<BR>—8 (In Rhet.) The first and best of the three main divisions of काव्य<BR> or poetry, in which the implied or <i>suggested</i> sense of a passage is<BR> more striking than the <i>expressed</i> sense; or where the <i>expressed</i><BR> sense is made subordinate to the <i>suggested</i> sense; इदमुत्तममतिशयिनि<BR> व्यङ्ग्ये वाच्याद् ध्वनिर्बुधैः कथितः K. P. 1 (R. G. gives 5 kinds of ध्वनि;<BR> see under ध्वनि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वनिग्रहः, ध्वनिनाला, ध्वनिविकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिग्रहः|ध्वनिग्रह
ध्वनिः + -ग्रहः<BR>—1 the ear.<BR>—2 hearing.<BR>—3 a fife, pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिनाला
ध्वनिः + -नाला<BR>—1 A lute.<BR>—2 a flute.<BR>—3 a kind of drum; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिविकारः|ध्वनिविकार
ध्वनिः + -विकारः a change of voice caused by fear, grief &c.; see काकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनित|ध्वनितः
ध्वनित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sounded.<BR>—2 Implied, suggested, hinted at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनितम्
ध्वनित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A sound.<BR>—2 The roar or thunder of a cloud; ध्वनितसूचितमम्बुमुचां चयम् Ki. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वानः|ध्वान
ध्वानः [ध्वन्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Sound (in general); मन्दरध्वानधीरः (दुन्दुभिः) Ve. 1. 22;<BR> रामाकर्षणभग्नकार्मकभुवा ध्वानेन रोदोरुधा Rāmāyaṇachampū.<BR>—2 Buzzing, humming, murmuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त, ध्वस्ति &c. See under ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्ति|ध्वस्तिः
ध्वस्त, ध्वस्ति &c. See under ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसिर
ध्वसिर <i>a.</i> Ved. Destroyed; also ध्वस्मन्, ध्वस्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षः|ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वांक्षः
ध्वाङ्क्षः<BR>—1 A crow; (sometimes used at the end of comp. to show contempt; <i>e. g.</i><BR> तीर्थध्वाङ्क्षः q. v.).<BR>—2 A beggar.<BR>—3 An impudent fellow.<BR>—4 A gull, crane; यस्य दस्युगणा राष्ट्रे ध्वाङ्क्षा मत्स्यान् जलादिव ।<BR> विहरन्ति परस्वानि स वै क्षत्रियपांसनः ॥ Mb. 12. 142. 29.<BR>—5 A carpenter.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वाङ्क्षारातिः, ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्टः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षारातिः|ध्वाङ्क्षाराति|ध्वांक्षाराति
ध्वाङ्क्षः + -अरातिः an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्टः|ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्ट|ध्वांक्षपुष्ट
ध्वाङ्क्षः + -पुष्टः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तम्
ध्वान्तम् Darkness; ध्वान्तं नीलनिचोलचारु सुदृशां प्रत्यङ्गमालिङ्गति<BR> Gīt. 11; N. 19. 42; Śi. 4. 62.<BR>—2 Hell (नरक) ध्वान्तं न याह्यकरुणेन यमेन दूरम् Bhāg. 6. 14. 55.<BR>—3 the quality of darkness or ignorance (तमोगुण).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ध्वान्तोन्मेषः, ध्वान्तवित्तः, ध्वान्तजालम्, ध्वान्तशात्रवः, ध्वान्तारातिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तोन्मेषः|ध्वान्तोन्मेष|ध्वांतोन्मेष
ध्वान्तम् + -उन्मेषः, -वित्तः a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तवित्तः|ध्वान्तवित्त|ध्वांतवित्त
ध्वान्तम् + -उन्मेषः, -वित्तः a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तजालम्
ध्वान्तम् + -जालम् the cover of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तशात्रवः|ध्वान्तशात्रव|ध्वांतशात्रव
ध्वान्तम् + -शात्रवः, -अरातिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 the white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तारातिः|ध्वान्ताराति
ध्वान्तम् + -शात्रवः, -अरातिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 the white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ €1 P. (ध्वरति)<BR>—1 to bend. —2 To kill [ध्वृ हूर्च्छने । हूर्च्छा कौटिल्ये]; ध्वृषीष्ठा<BR> युधि मायाभिः … … Bk. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न <i>a.</i> Thin, spare.<BR>—2 Vacant, empty.<BR>—3 Same, identical.<BR>—4 Unwearied.<BR>—5 Praised.<BR>—6 Undivided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नः|न|नं
न + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A pearl.<BR>—2 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—3 Wealth, prosperity.<BR>—4 A band, tie.<BR>—5 War.<BR>—6 N. of Buddha.<BR>—7 A gift. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>——(<i>a</i>) A particle of negation equivalent to ‘not’, ‘no’, ‘nor’, ‘neither’,<BR> and used in wishing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-a2" target="_blank">Page0871-a2</a>]<BR> requesting, or commanding, but not in prohibition before the imperative mood.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Used with the potential mood न may sometimes have the force<BR> of ‘lest’, ‘for fear lest’, ‘that not’; क्षत्रियैर्धार्यते शस्त्रं नार्तशब्दो<BR> भवेदिति Rām.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) In argumentative writings न often comes after इति चेत्<BR> and means ‘not so’.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) When a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">Page0872-1</a>]<BR> negative has to be repeated in successive clauses of the same sentence<BR> or in different sentences, न may be simply repeated or may be used<BR> with particles like उत, च, अपि, चापि, वा &c.; नाधीयीताश्वमारूढो<BR> न वृक्षं न च हस्तिनम् । न नावं न खरं नोष्ट्रं नेरिणत्थो न यानगः ॥<BR> Ms. 4. 120; प्रविशन्तं न मां कश्चिदपश्यन्नाप्यवारयत् Mb.;<BR> Ms. 2. 195, 3. 8, 9, 4. 15; न वा शरच्चन्द्रमरीचिकोमलं मृणालसूत्रं<BR> रचितं स्तनान्तरे Ś. 6. 17. Sometimes न may not be expressed<BR> in the second and other clauses, but represented only by च, वा, अपि<BR> वा; संपदि यस्य न हर्षो विपदि विषादो रणे च धीरत्वम् Pt. 2. 175.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) न is frequently joined with a second न or any other<BR> negative particle to intensify or emphasize an assertion; प्रत्युवाच<BR> तमृषिर्न तत्त्वतस्त्वां न वेद्मि पुरुषं पुरातनम् R. 11. 85; न च<BR> न परिचितो न चाप्यगम्यः M. 1. 11; न पुनरलंकारश्रियं न पुष्यति<BR> Ś. 1. 19/20; नादण्ड्यो नाम राज्ञोऽस्ति Ms. 8. 335; Me. 65, 108; नासौ<BR> न काम्यो न च वेद सम्यग् द्रष्टुं न सा R. 6. 30; Śi. 1. 55; Ve. 2. 10.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) In a few cases न is retained at the beginning of a negative<BR> Tatpuruṣa compound; as नाक, नासत्य, नकुल; see P. VI. 3. 75.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) न is often joined with other particles; नच, नवा, नैव,<BR> नतु, न चेद्, न खलु &c.<BR>——(<i>h</i>) It is also used, especially in early Vedic literature, in the<BR> sense of ‘like’, ‘as’, ‘as it were’; यद्वां नरा सनये दंस उग्रमाविष्कृणोमि<BR> तन्यतुर्न वृष्टिम् Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 16; गावो न गव्यूतीरनुः Śi. 20. 4. (v. l.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाधीत, नानुरक्त, नादरः, नैकः, नमाय, नकिंचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0871-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाधीत
न + -अधीत <i>a.</i> unread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानुरक्त
न + -अनुरक्त <i>a.</i> unkind, not loving; Pt. 2. 46 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादरः|नादर
न + -आदरः disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
न + -एक^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ‘not one’, more than one, several, various; नैकः सुप्तेषु जागृयात् Viduranīti.<BR>—2 Not anyone, nobody; नैको मुनिर्यस्य वचः प्रमाणम् Pt.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकः|नैक
न + -एकः + .({@-कः@}) an epithet of Viṣṇu. ˚आत्मन् <i>a.</i> of a manifold<BR> or diverse nature. ━(<i>m.</i>) N. of the Supreme Being. ˚चर <i>a.</i><BR> ‘not living alone’, gregarious, living in society. ˚जः the Supreme<BR> Being. ˚धा <i>ind.</i> in many ways, diversely. ˚भेद, ˚रूप <i>a.</i><BR> various, multiform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमाय
न + -माय <i>a.</i> using many artifices or stratagems. ˚शस् <i>ind.</i><BR> repeatedly, often.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिंचन
न + -किंचन <i>a.</i> very poor, beggarly. सर्वकामरसैर्हीनाः स्थानभ्रष्टा<BR> नकिंचनाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशुक|नंशुकः
नंशुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Injurious, destructive.<BR>—2 Going astray, being lost.<BR>—3 Small, minute, thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंष्टृ
नंष्टृ <i>a.</i> Injurious, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंहसः|नंहस
नंहसः A god very kind to his worshippers (हसन्ति विकसन्ति<BR> ते हसाः । नमन्तो हसाः येषां ते नंहसाः । भक्तानुग्राहका देवाः । Mb. 1. 170. 15.<BR> com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुटम्
नकुटम् The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलः|नकुल
नकुलः<BR>—1 The mungoose, an ichneumon; यदयं नकुलद्वेषी सकुलद्वेषी पुनः<BR> पिशुनः Vās.<BR>—2 N. of the fourth Pāṇḍava prince; the twin-brother of Sahadeva and<BR> a son of Mādrī. अहं तस्य अतिशयितदिव्यरूपिणो नकुलस्य दर्शनेनोत्सुका<BR> जाता Ve. 2 (where नकुल has really sense 1, but is taken in sense 2<BR> by Duryodhana).<BR>—3 A son.<BR>—4 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—5 Born of a base family; नकुलः पाण्डुतनये सर्पभुक् कुलहीनयोः Nm.<BR>—6 N. of a physician (author of a work on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">Page0872-2</a>]<BR> horses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुली
नकुलः + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 A female mungoose.<BR>—2 Saffron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नकुलेष्टा, नकुलेष्टका, नकुलेशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेष्टा
नकुलः + -इष्टा, -इष्टका a kind of medicinal plant (Mar. मुंगुसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेष्टका
नकुलः + -इष्टा, -इष्टका a kind of medicinal plant (Mar. मुंगुसवेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेशः|नकुलेश
नकुलः + -ईशः (नकुलीश)<BR>—1 N. of a Bhairava living in the temple of Kālī.<BR>—2 A mode of worship in Tantraśāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क्
नक्क् €10 U. (नक्कयति-ते) To destroy completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त <i>a.</i> [नज्-क्त] Ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तम्
नक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 Eating only at night, as a sort of religious vow or penance<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नक्तान्ध, नक्तचर्या, नक्तचारिन्, नक्तभोजनम्, नक्तमालः, नक्तमुखा, नक्तव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तान्ध|नक्तांध
नक्त + -अन्ध <i>a.</i> blind at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचर्या
नक्त + -चर्या wandering at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचारिन्
नक्त + -चारिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an owl.<BR>—2 a cat.<BR>—3 a thief.<BR>—4 a demon, goblin, evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तभोजनम्
नक्त + -भोजनम् supper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमालः|नक्तमाल
नक्त + -मालः N. of a tree; स नर्मदारोधसि सीकरार्द्रैर्मरुद्भिरानर्तितनक्तमाले R. 5. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमुखा
नक्त + -मुखा evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तव्रतम्
नक्त + -व्रतम्<BR>—1 fasting by day and eating at night.<BR>—2 any penance or religious rite observed at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तम्
नक्तम् <i>ind.</i> At night, by night; गच्छन्तीनां रमणवसतिं योषितां<BR> तत्र नक्तम् Me. 39; Ms. 6. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नक्तचरः, नक्तचर्या, नक्तचारिन्, नक्ततन, नक्तदिनम्, नक्तदिनम्, नक्तदिवम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचरः
नक्तम् + -चरः<BR>—1 any animal that goes about at night.<BR>—2 a fiend, demon, goblin. सासितूणधनुर्बाणपाणिं नक्तंचरान्तकम्<BR> Rāmarakṣā 3.<BR>—3 a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचर्या
नक्तम् + -चर्या wandering by night. नक्तंचर्यां दिवास्वप्नम् आलस्यं<BR> पैशुनं मदम् । अतियोगमयोगं च श्रेयसोऽथीं परित्यजेत् ॥ Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचारिन्
नक्तम् + -चारिन् <i>m.</i> = नक्तचारिन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ततन
नक्तम् + -तन <i>a.</i> nocturnal; इदं नक्तंतनं दाम पौष्पमेतद् दिवातनम् Bk. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तदिनम्
नक्तम् + -दिनम् night and day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0872-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तदिनम्
