नना Ved.<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 Mother.<BR>—3 A daughter; कारुरहं ततो भिषगुपलप्रक्षिणी नना Rv. 9. 112. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु <i>ind.</i> (Originally a combination of न and नु, now<BR> used as a separate word) A particle implying:−<BR>—1 Inquiry or interrogation; ननु समाप्तकृत्यो गौतमः M. 4.<BR>—2 Surely, certainly, indeed, is it not indeed (with an interrogative<BR> force); यदाऽमेधाविनी शिष्योपदेशं मलिनयति तदाचार्यस्य दोषो ननु M. 1.<BR>—3 Of course, indeed, certainly (अवधारणम्); उपपन्नं ननु शिवं<BR> सप्तस्वङ्गेषु R. 1. 60; त्रिलोकनाथेन सदा मखद्विषस्त्वया नियम्या<BR> ननु दिव्यचक्षुषा 3. 45.<BR>—4 It is used as a vocative particle meaning ‘O’, ‘Oh’; ननु मानव<BR> Dk.; ननु मूर्खाः पठितमेव युष्माभिस्तत्काण्डे U. 4.<BR>—5 It is used in propitiatory expressions in the sense of ‘pray’, ‘be pleased’<BR>; ननु मां प्रापय पत्युरन्तिकम् Ku. 4. 32.<BR>—6 It is sometimes used as a corrective word like the English ‘why’ or<BR> ‘I say’; ननु पदे परिवृत्य भण Mk. 5; ननु भणामि चिन्तित उपाय<BR> इति V. 2; ननु भवानग्रतो मे वर्तते Ś. 2; ननु विचिनोतु भवान् V. 2.<BR>—7 In argumentative discussions ननु is frequently used to head an<BR> objection or advance a contrary proposition (generally followed by उच्यते);<BR> नन्वचेतनान्येव वृश्चिकादिशरीराणि अचेतनानां च गोमयादीनां कार्याणीति<BR> उच्यते Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्|नंद्
नन्द् €1 P. (नन्दति, नन्दित)<BR>—1 To be glad, be pleased, delighted or satisfied, rejoice at (anything);<BR> ननन्दतुस्तत्सदृशेन तत्समौ R. 3. 23, 11, 2. 22, 4. 3; Bk. 15. 28.<BR>—2 To be propitious; be gracious; दैवतानि न नन्दन्ति धर्मयुक्तेन<BR> केनचित् Rām. 7. 15. 20. ━<i>Caus.</i> (नन्दयति-ते) To please,<BR> delight, gladden, make happy; अन्तर्हिते शशिनि सैव कुमुद्वती मे दृष्टिं<BR> न नन्दयति संस्मरणीयशोभा Ś. 4. 3; Bk. 2. 16; R. 9. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दः|नन्द|नंद|नंदः
नन्दः [नन्द्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Happiness, pleasure, joy.<BR>—2 A kind of lute (11 inches long). (MW. 7 inches).<BR>—3 A frog.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 N. of a cowherd, husband of Yaśodā and foster-father of Kṛṣṇa<BR> (to whose care the child was committed when Kaṃsa wanted to destroy it).<BR>—6 N. of the founder of the Nanda dynasty; or of nine brother-kings of<BR> Pāṭaliputra killed by the machinations of Cāṇakya, the minister of<BR> Chandragupta; समुत्खाता नन्दा नव हृदयरोगा इव भुवः Mu. 1. 13;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">Page0876-2</a>]<BR> अगृहीते राक्षसे किमुत्खातं नन्दवंशस्य Mu. 1. 27, 3. 28.<BR>—7 One of the nine treasures of Kubera.<BR>—8 Number ‘nine’ (from the nine Nandas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दी
नन्दः + .{@-दी@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्दात्मजः, नन्दनन्दनः, नन्दपालः, नन्दप्रयागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दात्मजः|नन्दात्मज|नंदात्मज
नन्दः + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनन्दनः|नन्दनन्दन|नंदनंदन
नन्दः + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपालः|नन्दपाल|नंदपाल
नन्दः + -पालः an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दप्रयागः|नन्दप्रयाग
नन्दः + -प्रयागः N. of a sacred place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक <i>a.</i> [नन्द्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Rejoicing, making happy, gladdening.<BR>—2 Delighting or rejoicing in.<BR>—3 Gladdening a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकः|नन्दक|नंदक
नन्दक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A frog.<BR>—2 N. of the sword of Viṣṇu; नित्यानन्दाय भूयान्मधुमथनमनोनन्दको<BR> नन्दको नः । विष्णुपादादिकेशान्तवर्णनस्तोत्रम् 4.<BR>—3 A sword in general.<BR>—4 Happiness.<BR>—5 Nanda, the foster-father of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—6 N. of a gem; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिः|नन्दकि|नंदकिः
नन्दकिः Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिन्|नंदकिन्
नन्दकिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दथुः|नन्दथु|नंदथु|नंदथुः
नन्दथुः Happiness, pleasure, delight. यस्यासौ तस्य नन्दथुः Bk. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नन्दन <i>a.</i> [नन्द्-ल्यु] Delighting, pleasing, gladdening; Ś. 7;<BR> सोऽयमद्य मकरन्दनन्दनो जीवलोकतिलकः प्रलीयते Māl. 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनः|नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं
नन्दन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A son; Y. 1. 174; R. 3. 41.<BR>—2 A frog.<BR>—3 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 N. of Śiva. —5 N. of twenty-sixth year (संवत्सर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दना|नंदना
नन्दन + .{@-ना@} A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनम्
नन्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 N. of the garden of Indra, the Elysium; हन्त गच्छत भद्रं वो नन्दने<BR> पश्यत स्थितम् Mb. 3. 142. 59; R. 8. 95; पुरीमवस्कन्द लुनीहि नन्दनं<BR> मुषाण रत्नानि हरामराङ्गनाः Śi. 1. 51.<BR>—2 Rejoicing, being glad.<BR>—3 Joy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्दनजम्, नन्दनद्रुमः, नन्दनवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनजम्
नन्दन + -जम् yellow sandal-wood (हरिचन्दन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनद्रुमः|नन्दनद्रुम
नन्दन + -द्रुमः a tree of the divine garden; अभिज्ञाश्छेदपातानां क्रियन्ते<BR> नन्दनद्रुमाः Ku. 2. 41;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनवनम्
नन्दन + -वनम् the divine grove (of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनकः|नन्दनक|नंदनकः
नन्दनकः A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्त|नंदंत|नन्दन्तः
नन्दन्त <i>a.</i> Delighting, making happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्तः|नन्दन्त|नंदंत
नन्दन्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 A son.<BR>—2 A friend.<BR>—3 A king or prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्ती
नन्दन्त + .{@-ती@} A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दा
नन्दा [नन्दयति नन्द्-अच्]<BR>—1 Delight, joy, happiness.<BR>—2 Affluence, wealth, prosperity.<BR>—3 A small earthen water-jar.<BR>—4 A husbandʼs sister.<BR>—5 The first, sixth and eleventh days of a lunar fortnight (considered<BR> as auspicious <i>tithis</i>); नन्दा भद्रा जया रिक्ता पूर्णा च प्रतिपत्<BR> क्रमात् Jyotistattvam.<BR>—6 An epithet of Gaurī.<BR>—7 N. of a cave; नन्दागुहायामिव नागराजः Bu. C. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिः|नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः
नन्दिः <i>m., f.</i> [नन्द्-इन्] Joy, pleasure, delight; प्रातिष्ठन्नन्दिमापन्नाः<BR> स्वं स्वमाश्रममण्डलम् Bhāg. 3. 24. 25. कौसल्यानन्दिवर्धनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिः|नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः
नन्दिः + .{@-दिः@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Of Śiva.<BR>—3 N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR>—4 Gambling, gaming; (<i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>—5 The speaker of a prelude or benediction (in a drama.)<BR>—6 Prosperity; मानहा भव शत्रूणां सुहृदां नन्दिवर्धनः Mb. 3. 162. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्द्यावर्तः, नन्दीशः, नन्दीश्वरः, नन्दिग्रामः, नन्दिघोषः, नन्दितूर्यम्, नन्दिदेवी, नन्दिनागरी, नन्दिपटहः, नन्दिपुराणम्, नन्दिवर्धनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्यावर्तः|नन्द्यावर्त|नन्द्यावर्त्त|नन्द्यावर्त्तः
नन्दिः + -आवर्तः<BR>—1 a sort of building in the form of a quadrangle without a western gate; (<i>n.</i> also).<BR>—2 Anything so formed (as dish, vessel संपुटिताद्यर्घपात्राणि); Mb. 7. 82. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीशः|नन्दीश|नंदीश
नन्दिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः —1 an epithet of Śiva; चतुर्थं शिवधर्माख्यं<BR> साक्षान्नन्दीशभाषितम् Kūrma P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीश्वरः|नन्दीश्वर|नंदीश्वर
नन्दिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः —1 an epithet of Śiva; चतुर्थं शिवधर्माख्यं<BR> साक्षान्नन्दीशभाषितम् Kūrma P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिग्रामः|नन्दिग्राम|नंदिग्राम
नन्दिः + -ग्रामः N. of a village<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">Page0877-1</a>]<BR> near Daulatabad where Bharata lived during Rāmaʼs banishment; नन्दिग्रामगतस्तस्य<BR> राज्यं न्यासमिवाभुनक् R. 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0876-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिघोषः|नन्दिघोष|नंदिघोष
नन्दिः + -घोषः<BR>—1 N. of the chariot of Arjuna.<BR>—2 a sound of joy; सनन्दिघोषां कल्याणीं गुहो नावमुपाहरत् । Rām. 2. 89. 12.<BR>—3 the proclamation of a herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दितूर्यम्
नन्दिः + -तूर्यम् a musical instrument played on festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिदेवी
नन्दिः + -देवी also नन्दादेवी N. of one of the loftiest Himalayan peaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिनागरी
नन्दिः + -नागरी N. of a written character, script.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिपटहः
नन्दिः + -पटहः (see तूर्यम् above); छत्रं सव्यजनं सनन्दिपटहं<BR> भद्रासनं कल्पितम् Pratimā 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिपुराणम्
नन्दिः + -पुराणम् N. of an उपपुराण of देवीपुराण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवर्धनः|नन्दिवर्धन|नन्दिवर्द्धनः|नंदिवर्धन
नन्दिः + -वर्धनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a friend.<BR>—3 the end of a lunar fortnight, <i>i. e.</i> the day of new or full moon.<BR>—4 a son.<BR>—5 a friend.<BR>—6 a particular form of temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिकः|नन्दिक|नंदिक|नंदिकः
नन्दिकः<BR>—1 Joy, pleasure.<BR>—2 A small water-jar.<BR>—3 An attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिका
नन्दिकः + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 A small water-jar.<BR>—2 = नन्दा (5) above.<BR>—3 N. of Indraʼs pleasure-ground<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्दिकेशः, नन्दिकेश्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिकेशः|नन्दिकेश|नंदिकेश
नन्दिकः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 N. of one of Śivaʼs chief attendants.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिकेश्वरः|नन्दिकेश्वर|नंदिकेश्वर
नन्दिकः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 N. of one of Śivaʼs chief attendants.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन् <i>a.</i> [नन्द्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Happy, pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>—2 Making happy, gladdening, giving delight; अद्याप्यानन्दयति मां त्वं<BR> पुनः क्वासि नन्दिनी U. 3. 14.<BR>—3 Delighting in, liking. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A son.<BR>—2 The speaker of a prelude or benediction in a drama.<BR>—3 N. of the door-keeper of Śiva, his chief attendant, or of the bull<BR> which he rides; लतागृहद्वारगतोऽथ नन्दी Ku. 3. 41; Māl. 1. 1.<BR>—4 An epithet of Viṣṇu. —5 The Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिनी|नंदिनी
नन्दिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A daughter; तेषां कुले त्वमसि नन्दिनि पार्थिवानाम् U. 1. 9.<BR>—2 A husbandʼs sister.<BR>—3 A fabulous cow, daughter of <i>Surabhi</i>, yielding all desires (कामधेनु)<BR> and in the possession of the sage Vasisṭha; अनिन्द्या नन्दिनी नाम धेनुराववृते<BR> वनात् R. 1. 82, 2. 69.<BR>—4 An epithet of the Ganges; नन्दिनी नलिनी सीता मालती च मलापहा ।<BR> विष्णुपादाब्जसंभूता गङ्गा त्रिपथगामिनी ॥<BR>—5 The holy basil.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्दितनयः, नन्दिसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दितनयः
नन्दिन् + -तनयः, -सुतः the sage Vyāḍi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिसुतः
नन्दिन् + -तनयः, -सुतः the sage Vyāḍi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दी
नन्दी <i>f.</i> N. of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नन्दीमुखी, नन्दीसरस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीमुखी
नन्दी + -मुखी sleepiness, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीसरस्
नन्दी + -सरस् Indraʼs lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपराजित्
नपराजित् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपात्
नपात् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A grandson (usually restricted to the Vedas), as in तनूनपात्.<BR>—2 A descendant, son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपातः|नपात
नपातः The Devayāna Mārga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंस्
नपुंस् <i>m.</i>, नपुंसः Not a man, a eunuch; हतास्म्यहं<BR> कुनाथेन नपुंसा वीरमानिना Bhāg. 9. 14. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसः|नपुंस
नपुंस् <i>m.</i>, नपुंसः Not a man, a eunuch; हतास्म्यहं<BR> कुनाथेन नपुंसा वीरमानिना Bhāg. 9. 14. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसकः|नपुंसक|नपुंसकं
नपुंसकः, -कम्<BR> [न पुमान् न स्त्री]<BR>—1 A hermaphrodite (neither man, nor woman).<BR>—2 An impotent man, a eunuch.<BR>—3 A coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसकम्
नपुंसकः, -कम्<BR> [न पुमान् न स्त्री]<BR>—1 A hermaphrodite (neither man, nor woman).<BR>—2 An impotent man, a eunuch.<BR>—3 A coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसकम्
नपुंसकः, -कम् + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A word in the neuter gender.<BR>—2 The neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृ
नप्तृ <i>m.</i> A grandson (a sonʼs or daughterʼs son); स्वे स्वे किल<BR> कुले जाते पुत्रे नप्तरि वा पुनः Mb. 3. 159. 12. ━<i>f.</i> {@नप्त्री@}.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् €1 Ā. (नभते)<BR>—1 To hurt, injure; सुग्रीवः प्रघसं नेभे Bk. 14. 33.<BR>—2 To be torn or rent, to burst; नभन्तामन्यकेषां ज्याका अधि धन्वसु<BR> Rv. 10. 133. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् <i>f.</i> Ved. Hurt, injury; सहो नभोऽविरणाय पूर्वीः Rv. 1. 174. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ <i>a.</i> Killing, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभः|नभ
नभ + .{@-भः@} The month Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभम्
नभ + .{@-भम्@} The sky, atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभा
नभ + .{@-भा@} A spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभनु
नभनु <i>a.</i> Ved. Hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभनु
नभनु + .{@-नु@} <i>f.</i> A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभन्यु
नभन्यु <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Injuring, destroying.<BR>—2 Ethereal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस् <i>n.</i> [नह्यते मेघैः नह्-असुन् भश्चान्तादेशः; cf. Uṇ. 4. 210]<BR>—1 The sky, atmosphere; R. 5. 29; नभश्च पृथिवीं चैव तुमुलो व्यनुनादयन्<BR> Bg. 1. 19; वनान्तरे तोयमिति प्रधाविता निरीक्ष्य भिन्नाञ्जनसंनिभं<BR> नभः Ṛs. 1. 11.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 Fog, vapour.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 Period of life, age. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The rains or rainy season.<BR>—2 The nose, smell.<BR>—3 N. of the month of Śrāvaṇa (corresponding to July-August), (said<BR> to be <i>n.</i> also in this sense); प्रत्यासन्ने नभसि दयिताजीवितालम्बनार्थी<BR> Me. 4; R. 12. 29, 17. 41, 18. 6; N. 9. 84; श्रावणे तु स्यान्नभाः श्रावणिकश्च<BR> सः Ak.; पञ्चमोऽयं तु संप्राप्तः नभाः श्यामनभाः शुभः Śiva B. 26. 57.<BR>—4 The fibres in the root of the lotus.<BR>—5 A spitting-pot. ━(du.) Both the worlds, heaven and earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नभोम्बुपः, नभःकेतनः, नभःपान्थः, नभःक्रान्तिन्, नभोग, नभोगजः, नभोगति, नभश्चक्षुस्, नभश्चमसः, नभश्चर, नभस्तलम्, नभोदुहः, नभोदृष्टि, नभोद्वीपः, नभोधूमः, नभोनदी, नभःप्राणः, नभोमणिः, नभोमण्डलम्, नभोयोनिः, नभोरजस्, नभोरूप, नभोरेणुः, नभोलयः, नभोलिह्, नभोवटः, नभोवीथी, नभःश्वासः, नभःसद्, नभःसरित्, नभःस्थलः, नभःस्थली, नभःस्पृश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोम्बुपः|नभोम्बुप|नभोंबुप
नभस् + -अम्बुपः the Chātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःकेतनः|नभःकेतन
नभस् + -केतनः, -पान्थः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःपान्थः|नभःपान्थ
नभस् + -केतनः, -पान्थः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःक्रान्तिन्|नभःक्रांतिन्
नभस् + -क्रान्तिन् <i>m.</i> a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोग
नभस् + -ग <i>a.</i> going in the sky (as a star, god, bird &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगजः|नभोगज
नभस् + -गजः a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगति|नभोगतिः
नभस् + -गति <i>f.</i> soaring, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चक्षुस्
नभस् + -चक्षुस् <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चमसः|नभश्चमस
नभस् + -चमसः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चर|नभश्चरः
नभस् + -चर <i>a.</i> moving in the sky; निकामतप्ता विविधेन वह्निना<BR> नभश्चरेणेन्धनसंभृतेन सा Ku. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चरः|नभश्चर
नभस् + -चर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a god or demi-god; नभश्चरैर्गीतयशाः स लेभे R. 18. 6.<BR>—2 a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्तलम्
