नभोरेणुः|नभोरेणु
नभस् + -रेणुः <i>f.</i> fog-mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलयः|नभोलय
नभस् + -लयः smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलिह्
नभस् + -लिह् <i>a.</i> licking the sky, lofty, very high; cf. अभ्रंलिह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोवटः|नभोवट
नभस् + -वटः atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोवीथी
नभस् + -वीथी the sunʼs path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःश्वासः|नभःश्वास
नभस् + -श्वासः wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसद्
नभस् + -सद् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a bird.<BR>—2 a star.<BR>—3 a god; अतीन्द्रियज्ञाननिधिर्नभःसदः Śi. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसरित्
नभस् + -सरित् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the milky way.<BR>—2 the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थलः|नभःस्थल
नभस् + -स्थलः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थली
नभस् + -स्थली the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्पृश्
नभस् + -स्पृश् <i>a.</i> reaching the sky, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस|नभसं|नभसः
नभस <i>a.</i> Vapoury, misty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभसः|नभस|नभसं
नभस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 The sky.<BR>—2 The rainy season.<BR>—3 The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभसंगमः|नभसङ्गम|नभसंगम|नभसङ्गमः
नभसंगमः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य <i>a.</i> Vapoury, foggy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्यः|नभस्य
नभस्य + .{@-स्यः@}<BR>—1 N. of the month Bhādrapada (corresponding to August-September); अथ<BR> नभस्य इव त्रिदशायुधम् R. 9. 54, 12. 29, 17. 41; Bhāg. 12. 11. 38.<BR>—2 N. of one of the sons of स्वारोचिष मनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0877-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्वत्|नभस्वन्त्
नभस्वत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vaporous, misty, cloudy.<BR>—2 Young. ━<i>m.</i> The wind, air; नभस्वतस्तं कुसुमेषु केलयः N. 1. 97;<BR> R. 4. 8, 10. 73; Śi. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
नभ्य <i>a.</i> Cloudy, misty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्यम्
नभ्य + .{@-भ्यम्@} The central part of a wheel; cf. नाभि. तदेतन्नभ्यम्<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाकः|नभाक|नभाकं
नभाकः<BR>—1 Darkness.<BR>—2 An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>—3 A cloud.<BR>—4 The sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभिः|नभि
नभिः A wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्राज्
नभ्राज् <i>m.</i> A dark cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्
नम् €1 P., sometimes Ā. (नमति-ते, ननाम, अनंसीत्, नंस्यति,<BR> नत, <i>caus.</i> नमयति-ते or नामयति-ते, but with a preposition<BR> नमयति only; <i>desid.</i> निनंसति) also €9 P. (नम्नाति), €4. P.<BR> (नम्यति)<BR>—1 To bow to, make obeisance to, salute (as a mark of respect) (with acc.<BR> or dat.); इयं नमति वः सर्वान् त्रिलोचनवधूरिति Ku. 6. 89; Bg. 11. 37;<BR> Bk. 9. 51, 10. 31, 12. 99; Śi. 4. 57.<BR>—2 To submit or subject oneself, bow down; अशक्तः सन्धिमान् नमेत् Kām. 8. 55.<BR>—3 To bend, sink; go down; अनंसीद्भूर्भरेणास्य Bk. 15. 25; नेमुः<BR> सर्वदिशः K. 55; उन्नमति नमति वर्षति … … मेघः Mk. 5. 26.<BR>—4 To stoop, be inclined.<BR>—5 To be bent or curved.<BR>—6 To sound.<BR>—7 To change a dental to a lingual letter. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bend, make curved.<BR>—2 To bend (as a bow); न नमयितुमधिज्यमस्मि शक्तः Ś. 2. 3.<BR>—3 To cause to sink.<BR>—4 To prevent, ward off.<BR>—5 To subdue, make subordinate; स पुरस्कृतमध्यमक्रमो नमयामास<BR> नृपाननुद्धरन् R. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत|नमतः
नमत <i>a.</i> [नम्-अतच्] Bent, bowed, crooked, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमतः|नमत
नमत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 An actor.<BR>—2 Smoke.<BR>—3 A master, lord.<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमतम्
नमत + .{@-तम्@} Woollen stuff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमनम्
नमनम् [नम्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Bowing down, bending, stooping.<BR>—2 Sinking. —3 A bow, salutation, obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमनः|नमन|नमनं
नमनम् + .{@-नः@} One who causes to bend or bow; नमयति स्म वनानि मनस्विनीजनमनो<BR> नमनो घनमारुतः Śi. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A bow, salutation, obeisance, adoration; (this word is, by itself,<BR> invariably used with dat.; तस्मै वदान्यगुरवे तरवे नमोऽस्तु Bv. 1. 94;<BR> नमस्त्रिमूर्तये तुभ्यम् Ku. 2. 4; but with कृ, generally<BR> with acc.; मुनित्रयं नमस्कृत्य Sk.; but sometimes with dat. also;<BR> नमस्कुर्मो नृसिंहाय <i>ibid.</i> The word has the sense of a noun, but<BR> is treated as an indeclinable.)<BR>—2 Ved. Food.<BR>—3 A thunderbolt.<BR>—4 A gift, present.<BR>—5 A sacrifice.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नमःकारः, नमःकृतिः, नमःकारी, नमःकृत, नमोगुरुः, नमश्चमसः, नमोवाकम्, नमोवृध्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमःकारः
नमस् + -कारः, -कृतिः <i>f.</i>,<BR> {@-करणम्@} bowing, respectful or reverential salutation, respectful<BR> obeisance (made by uttering the word नमस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमःकृतिः
नमस् + -कारः, -कृतिः <i>f.</i>,<BR> {@-करणम्@} bowing, respectful or reverential salutation, respectful<BR> obeisance (made by uttering the word नमस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमःकारी
नमस् + -कारी a kind of plant (Mar. लाजाळू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमःकृत
नमस् + -कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bowed down to, saluted.<BR>—2 revered, adored, worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमोगुरुः|नमोगुरु
नमस् + -गुरुः<BR>—1 a spiritual teacher.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमश्चमसः
नमस् + -चमसः<BR>—1 a kind of cake.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमोवाकम्
नमस् + -वाकम् <i>ind.</i> uttering the word नमस् <i>i. e.</i> making a<BR> low obeisance; इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे U. 1. 1;<BR>━<i>m.</i> नाथायाभिरुपासिताय च नमोवाकानधीयीमहि Viś. Guṇā. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमोवृध्
नमस् + -वृध् <i>m.</i> a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस|नमसः
नमस <i>a.</i> Favourable, kindly disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसित|नमसितः
नमसित, नमस्यित <i>a.</i> Revered, respected, saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यित|नमस्यितः
नमसित, नमस्यित <i>a.</i> Revered, respected, saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यति
नमस्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To bow down to, pay homage to, worship; नमस्यामो देवान् ननु हतविधेस्तेऽपि<BR> वशगाः Bh. 2. 94.<BR>—2 To act humbly towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Entitled to obeisance, revered, respectable, adorable; ब्रह्मन्नतिथिनर्मस्यः<BR> Kaṭh.; ब्राह्मणा मे महाभागा नमस्याः पुरुषर्षभाः Mb. 12. 59. 109.<BR>—2 Respectful, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्या
नमस्य + .{@-स्या@} Worship, adoration, reverence, obeisance; प्रियायास्मै धाम्ने<BR> प्रविहितनमस्योऽस्मि भवते Śivamahimna 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यु
नमस्यु <i>a.</i> Ved. Worshipping, saluting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमित|नमितः
नमित <i>a.</i> Bowed, bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्य
नम्य, also नमनीय <i>a.</i> Venerable, respectable; त्वमर्थानां<BR> मूलं धनदनमनीयाङ्घ्निकमले Ā. L. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमनीय
नम्य, also नमनीय <i>a.</i> Venerable, respectable; त्वमर्थानां<BR> मूलं धनदनमनीयाङ्घ्निकमले Ā. L. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र <i>a.</i> [नम्-र]<BR>—1 Bowing, bowing down, bent, inclined, hanging down; भवन्ति नम्रास्तरवः<BR> फलागमैः Ś. 5. 12. स्तोकनम्रा स्तनाभ्याम् Me. 84; Pt. 1. 106; Ratn. 1. 19.<BR>—2 Bowing down, making a low obeisance; अभूत् च नम्रः प्रणिपातशिक्षया<BR> R. 3. 25; इत्युच्यते ताभिरुमा स्म नम्रा Ku. 7. 28.<BR>—3 Lowly, submissive, humble, reverential; as in भक्तिनम्रः Me. 57.<BR>—4 Crooked, curved.<BR>—5 Worshipping.<BR>—6 Devoted or attached to.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नम्राङ्ग, नम्रमूर्ति, नम्रनासिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्राङ्ग
नम्र + -अङ्ग, -मूर्ति <i>a.</i> bent, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रमूर्ति|नम्रमूर्त्ति
नम्र + -अङ्ग, -मूर्ति <i>a.</i> bent, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रनासिक
नम्र + -नासिक <i>a.</i> flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रक|नम्रकः
नम्रक <i>a.</i> Bent, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रकः|नम्रक
नम्रक + .{@-कः@} kind of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रता
नम्रता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Obeisance, respect.<BR>—2 Submissiveness, humility.<BR>—3 Condescension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रत्वम्
नम्रता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Obeisance, respect.<BR>—2 Submissiveness, humility.<BR>—3 Condescension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रित
नम्रित <i>a.</i> Bent or bowed down, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिः|नमुचि
नमुचिः [न मुञ्चति]<BR>—1 N. of a demon slain by Indra; वनमुचे नमुचेररये शिरः R. 9. 22.<BR> [When Indra conquered the Asuras, there was only one called Namuchi<BR> who strongly resisted and at last captured him. He offered to let Indra<BR> go provided he promised ‘not to kill by day or by night, with wet or dry’.<BR> Indra promised to do so and was released, but he cut off Namuchiʼs head<BR> at twilight and with foam of water (which is neither wet nor day). According<BR> to another version Namuchi was a friend of Indra, and once drank up his<BR> strength and made him quite imbecile. The Aśvins (and Sarasvatī also,<BR> as the story goes) then supplied Indra with a <i>Vajra</i> with which he<BR> cut off the demonʼs head].<BR>—2 N. of the god of love.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नमुचिसूदनः, नमुचिद्विष्, नमुचिहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिसूदनः|नमुचिसूदन
नमुचिः + -सूदनः, -द्विष्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; विगृह्य चक्रे<BR> नमुचिद्विषा बली य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्निशं दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिद्विष्
नमुचिः + -सूदनः, -द्विष्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; विगृह्य चक्रे<BR> नमुचिद्विषा बली य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्निशं दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिहन्
नमुचिः + -सूदनः, -द्विष्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; विगृह्य चक्रे<BR> नमुचिद्विषा बली य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्निशं दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमेरुः|नमेरु
नमेरुः N. of a tree (रुद्राक्ष or सुरपुन्नाग); गणा नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः<BR> Ku. 1. 55, 3. 43; R. 4. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय्
नय् €1 Ā. (नयते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय <i>a.</i> [नी भावे अच्]<BR>—1 Leading, conducting.<BR>—2 A guide.<BR>—3 Suitable, right, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयः|नय
नय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Guiding,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">Page0879-1</a>]<BR> leading, managing.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Behaviour, course of conduct, conduct, way of life as in दुर्नय.<BR> सितोन्नतेनैव नयेन हृत्वा कैलासशैलस्य यदग्रशोभाम् Bu. C. 1. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Prudent or righteous conduct, virtue. नयानयौ दण्डनीत्याम् Kau. A. 1. 2.<BR>—3 Prudence, foresight, circumspection; तत् तासामुपशान्तये सुमतिभिः<BR> कार्यो विशेषान्नयः Pt. 1. 371, 3. 176.<BR>—4 Policy, political wisdom, statesmanship, civil administration, state-policy;<BR> नयप्रचारं व्यवहारदुष्टताम् Mk. 1. 7; नयगुणोपचितामिव भूपतेः<BR> सदुपकारफलां श्रियमर्थिनः R. 9. 27; नयशालिभिः Mu. 1. 22.<BR>—5 Morality, justice, rectitude, equity; चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां हि<BR> चेतः Ki. 10. 29, 2. 3, 6. 38, 16. 42.<BR>—6 A plan, design, scheme; हितैः साधुसमाचारैः शास्त्रज्ञैर्मतिशालिभिः ।<BR> कथंचिन्न विकल्पन्ते विद्वद्भिश्चिन्तिता नयाः ॥ Pt. 1. 339, 377; Mu. 6. 11, 7. 9.<BR>—7 A maxim, principle.<BR>—8 Course, method, manner.<BR>—9 A system, doctrine, opinion.<BR>—10 A philosophical system; वैशेषिके नये Bhāṣā P. 105.<BR>—11 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—12 A kind of game.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नयकोविद, नयग, नयचक्षुस्, नयनेतृ, नयपीठी, नयप्रयोगः, नयवादिन्, नयविद्, नयशास्त्रम्, नयशालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0878-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयकोविद
नय + -कोविद, -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> skilled in policy, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयग
नय + -ग <i>a.</i> behaving properly or prudently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयचक्षुस्
नय + -चक्षुस् <i>a.</i> having political foresight, wise, prudent; अर्हणामर्हते<BR> चक्रुर्मुनयो नयचक्षुषे R. 1. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनेतृ
नय + -नेतृ <i>m.</i> a master in politics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयपीठी
नय + -पीठी the board or cloth on which men are moved in play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयप्रयोगः|नयप्रयोग
नय + -प्रयोगः political wisdom, statesmanship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयवादिन्
नय + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a politician; Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयविद्
नय + -विद् <i>m.</i>, {@-विशारदः@}<BR> a politician, statesman; सन्धिविग्रहिको कार्यो राज्ञा<BR> नयविशारदः Matsya P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयशास्त्रम्
नय + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 the science of politics.<BR>—2 any work on politics or political economy.<BR>—3 a work on morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयशालिन्
नय + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> just, righteous; नयशालिनि श्रिय इवाधिपतौ विरमन्ति<BR> न ज्वलितुमौषधयः Ki. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयकः|नयक
नयकः<BR>—1 A skilful manager.<BR>—2 One versed in policy, a statesman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनम्
नयनम् [नी-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Leading, guiding, conducting managing.<BR>—2 Taking, bringing to or near, drawing; पापापहं स्वर्नयनं दुस्तरं<BR> पार्थिवर्षभैः Rām. 1. 14. 58.<BR>—3 Ruling, governing, polity; वाक्यैः पवित्रार्थपदैर्नयनैः प्राकृतैरपि<BR> Bhāg. 10. 50. 34.<BR>—4 Obtaining.<BR>—5 The eye.<BR>—6 Passing, spending (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयना
नयनम् + .{@-ना, -नी@} The pupil of the eye.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नयनाञ्चलः, नयनान्तः, नयनाभिराम, नयनामोषिन्, नयनोत्सवः, नयनोपान्तः, नयनगोचर, नयनचरितम्, नयनच्छदः, नयनजम्, नयनजलम्, नयनवारि, नयनपथः, नयनपुटम्, नयनप्रबन्धः, नयनप्रीतिः, नयनप्लवः, नयनबुद्बुदम्, नयनविषयः, नयनसलिलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनी
नयनम् + .{@-ना, -नी@} The pupil of the eye.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नयनाञ्चलः, नयनान्तः, नयनाभिराम, नयनामोषिन्, नयनोत्सवः, नयनोपान्तः, नयनगोचर, नयनचरितम्, नयनच्छदः, नयनजम्, नयनजलम्, नयनवारि, नयनपथः, नयनपुटम्, नयनप्रबन्धः, नयनप्रीतिः, नयनप्लवः, नयनबुद्बुदम्, नयनविषयः, नयनसलिलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनाञ्चलः|नयनाञ्चल
नयनम् + -अञ्चलः, -अन्तः<BR>—1 the eye-corner.<BR>—2 a side-glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनान्तः|नयनान्त
नयनम् + -अञ्चलः, -अन्तः<BR>—1 the eye-corner.<BR>—2 a side-glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनाभिराम|नयनाभिरामः
नयनम् + -अभिराम <i>a.</i> gladdening the sight, lovely to behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनाभिरामः|नयनाभिराम
नयनम् + -अभिराम + .({@-मः@}) the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनामोषिन्
नयनम् + -आमोषिन् <i>a.</i> blinding the sight, obscuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोत्सवः|नयनोत्सव
नयनम् + -उत्सवः<BR>—1 a lamp.<BR>—2 delight of the eyes. —3 any lovely object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोपान्तः|नयनोपान्त|नयनोपांत
नयनम् + -उपान्तः the corner of the eye; नयनोपान्तविलोकितं च यत्<BR> (स्मरामि) Ku. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनगोचर
नयनम् + -गोचर <i>a.</i> visible, within the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनचरितम्
नयनम् + -चरितम् the play of the eyes, ogling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनच्छदः|नयनच्छद
नयनम् + -छदः an eyelid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनजम्
नयनम् + -जम्, -जलम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> tears; देव त्वद्वैरिनारीनयननयनजैर्निर्ममे<BR> नीरधिर्न Sūkti. 5. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनजलम्
नयनम् + -जम्, -जलम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> tears; देव त्वद्वैरिनारीनयननयनजैर्निर्ममे<BR> नीरधिर्न Sūkti. 5. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनवारि
नयनम् + -जम्, -जलम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> tears; देव त्वद्वैरिनारीनयननयनजैर्निर्ममे<BR> नीरधिर्न Sūkti. 5. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनपथः|नयनपथ
नयनम् + -पथः the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनपुटम्
नयनम् + -पुटम् the cavity of the eye, eye-lid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनप्रबन्धः|नयनप्रबन्ध
नयनम् + -प्रबन्धः the outer corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनप्रीतिः|नयनप्रीति
नयनम् + -प्रीतिः lovely sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनप्लवः|नयनप्लव
नयनम् + -प्लवः the swimming of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनबुद्बुदम्
नयनम् + -बुद्बुदम् an eye-ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनविषयः|नयनविषय
नयनम् + -विषयः<BR>—1 any visible object; नयनविषयं जन्मन्येकः स एव महोत्सवः Māl. 1. 36.<BR>—2 the horizon. —3 the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनसलिलम्
नयनम् + -सलिलम् tears; तस्मिन् काले नयनसलिलं योषितां खण्डितानाम्<BR> (शान्ति नेयम्) Me. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनत्वम्
नयनत्वम् The condition of the eyes; बाष्पजलान्तरितनयनत्वान्न<BR> पश्यामि ते मुखचन्द्रम् Ve. 6. 39/40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरः|नर|नरं
नरः [नॄ-नये-अच्]<BR>—1 A man, male person; संयोजयति विद्यैव नीचगापि नरं सरित् । समुद्रमिव<BR> दुर्धर्षं नृपं भाग्यमतः परम् ॥ H. Pr. 5; Ms. 1. 96, 2. 213.<BR>—2 A man or piece at chess.<BR>—3 The pin of a sun-dial.<BR>—4 The Supreme Spirit, the original or eternal man.<BR>—5 Manʼs length (= पुरुष. q. v.).<BR>—6 N. of a primitive sage.<BR>—7 N. of Arjuna; see नरनारायण below.<BR>—8 A horse.<BR>—9 (In gram.) A personal termination.<BR>—10 The individual soul (जीवात्मा); Mb. 12. 280. 50.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नराङ्गः, नराधमः, नराधिपः, नराधिपतिः, नरेशः, नरेश्वरः, नरदेवः, नरपतिः, नरपालः, नरान्तकः, नरायनः, नराशः, नराधारः, नरेतरः, नरेन्द्रः, नरोत्तमः, नरर्षभः, नरकपालः, नरकीलकः, नरकेशरिन्, नरकेसरिन्, नरचिह्नम्, नरदेवः, नरधिः, नरद्विष्, नरनारायणः, नरपशुः, नरपुङ्गवः, नरबलिः, नरभुज्, नरभूः, नरमानिका, नरमानिनी, नरमालिनी, नरमाला, नरमेधः, नरयन्त्रम्, नरयानम्, नररथः, नरवाहनम्, नरलोकः, नरवाहनः, नरविष्वणः, नरवीरः, नरव्याघ्रः, नरशार्दूलः, नरशृङ्गम्, नरसंसर्गः, नरसखः, नरसिंहः, नरहरिः, नरसिंहद्वादशी, नरस्कन्धः, नरहयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराङ्गः|नराङ्ग|नरांग
नरः + -अङ्गः<BR>—1 the penis.<BR>—2 eruption on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधमः|नराधम
नरः + -अधमः a wretch, miscreant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधिपः|नराधिप
नरः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः, -ईशः, -ईश्वरः, -देवः, -पतिः, -पालः a<BR> king; नरपतिहितकर्ता द्वेष्यतां याति लोके Pt. नराणां च नराधिपम्<BR> Bg. 10. 27; Ms. 7. 13; R. 2. 75, 3. 42, 7. 62; Me. 39; Y. 1. 311.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

