नराधारा
नरः + -आधारः + .({@-रा@}) the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेतरः|नरेतर
नरः + -इतरः<BR>—1 a being higher than a man, a god; Bhāg. 4. 6. 9.<BR>—2 an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेन्द्रः|नरेन्द्र|नरेंद्र
नरः + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 a king; R. 2. 18. नरेन्द्रकन्यास्तमवाप्य सत्पतिं तमोनुदं दक्षसुता<BR> इवाबभुः 3. 33, 6. 80; Ms. 9. 253.<BR>—2 a physician, dealer in antidotes, curer of poisons; तेषु कश्चिन्नरेन्द्राभिमानी<BR> तां निर्वर्ण्य Dk. 51; सुनिग्रहा नरेन्द्रेण फणीन्द्रा इव शत्रवः<BR> Śi. 2. 88 (where the word is used in both senses). ˚मार्गः a high<BR> street, main road.<BR>—3 a mineralogist; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरोत्तमः|नरोत्तम
नरः + -उत्तमः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरर्षभः|नरर्षभ
नरः + -ऋषभः ‘the chief of men’, a prince, king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकपालः|नरकपाल
नरः + -कपालः a manʼs skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकीलकः|नरकीलक
नरः + -कीलकः the murderer of a spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकेशरिन्
नरः + -केशरिन्, -केसरिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Viṣṇu in his fourth incarnation; cf. नरसिंह below.<BR>—2 the chief of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकेसरिन्
नरः + -केशरिन्, -केसरिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Viṣṇu in his fourth incarnation; cf. नरसिंह below.<BR>—2 the chief of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरचिह्नम्
नरः + -चिह्नम् the moustaches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरदेवः|नरदेव
नरः + -देवः<BR>—1 the warrior class (क्षत्रिय); शिष्ट्वा वा भूमिदेवानां नरदेवसमागमे Ms. 11. 82.<BR>—2 a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरधिः
नरः + -धिः the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरद्विष्
नरः + -द्विष् <i>m.</i> a demon, goblin; तेन मूर्धानमध्वंसन्नरद्विषः Bk. 15. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0879-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरनारायणः|नरनारायण
