नर्मः|नर्म|नर्म्म
नर्मः Ved. Sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0880-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मटः|नर्मट|नर्म्मट|नर्म्मटः
नर्मटः<BR>—1 A pot-sherd.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0880-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मठः|नर्मठ|नर्म्मठ|नर्म्मठः
नर्मठः [नर्मन्-अठन्]<BR>—1 jester.<BR>—2 A lecher, rake, libertine.<BR>—3 Sport, pastime, amusement.<BR>—4 Copulation, coition.<BR>—5 The chin.<BR>—6 The nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मन्|नर्म्मन्
नर्मन् <i>n.</i> [नॄ-मनिन्]<BR>—1 Sport, amusement, diversion, merriment, pleasure, amorous pastime or<BR> sport; जितकमले विमले परिकर्मय नर्मजनकमलकं मुखे Gīt. 12<BR> (कौतुकजनक); R. 19. 28.<BR>—2 Jest, joke, humour, wit; सुहृत्प्रयुक्ता इव नर्मवादाः Ki. 17. 33.<BR> नर्मप्रायाभिः कथाभिः K. 70; ‘jocular, humorous’.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नर्मालापः, नर्मोक्तिः, नर्मकीलः, नर्मगर्भ, नर्मद, नर्मदा, नर्मद्युति, नर्मसचिवः, नर्मसुहृद्, नर्मसाचिव्यम्, नर्मस्फूर्जः, नर्मस्फोटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मालापः|नर्मालाप
नर्मन् + -आलापः a jocular conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मोक्तिः|नर्मोक्ति
नर्मन् + -उक्तिः a facetious expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मकीलः|नर्मकील|नर्म्मकील|नर्म्मकीलः
नर्मन् + -कीलः a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मगर्भ|नर्मगर्भः|नर्म्मगर्भ
नर्मन् + -गर्भ <i>a.</i> humorous, full of humour, witty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मगर्भः|नर्मगर्भ|नर्म्मगर्भ
नर्मन् + -गर्भ + .({@-र्भः@})<BR>—1 a secret lover.<BR>—2 an action of the hero in an unrecognizable form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मद|नर्मदः|नर्म्मद|नर्म्मदः
नर्मन् + -द <i>a.</i> delighting, making happy; नन्दसूनुरनघे तव वत्सो<BR> नर्मदः प्रणयिनां विजहार Bhāg. 10. 35. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मदः|नर्मद|नर्म्मद|नर्म्मदः
नर्मन् + -द + .({@-दः@}) a jester (= नर्मसचिव q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मदा|नर्म्मदा
नर्मन् + -दा N. of a river which rises in the Vindhya mountain, and falls<BR> into the gulf of Cambay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मद्युति|नर्मद्युतिः|नर्म्मद्युति
नर्मन् + -द्युति <i>a.</i> bright with joy, cheerful, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मद्युतिः|नर्मद्युति|नर्म्मद्युति
नर्मन् + -द्युति + .({@-तिः@} <i>f.</i>) enjoyment of a joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मसचिवः|नर्मसचिव|नर्म्मसचिव
नर्मन् + -सचिवः, -सुहृद् <i>m.</i> ‘a pleasure-companion’, an associate of<BR> the amusements of a prince or a man of rank; न नर्मसचिवैः सार्धं<BR> किञ्चिदप्यप्रियं वदेत् Kām. इदं त्वैदंपर्यं यदुत नृपतेर्नर्मसचिवः<BR> सुतादानान्मित्रं भवतु Māl. 2. 7; तां याचते नरपतेर्नर्मसुहृन्नन्दनो<BR> नृपमुखेन 1. 11; Śi. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मसुहृद्
नर्मन् + -सचिवः, -सुहृद् <i>m.</i> ‘a pleasure-companion’, an associate of<BR> the amusements of a prince or a man of rank; न नर्मसचिवैः सार्धं<BR> किञ्चिदप्यप्रियं वदेत् Kām. इदं त्वैदंपर्यं यदुत नृपतेर्नर्मसचिवः<BR> सुतादानान्मित्रं भवतु Māl. 2. 7; तां याचते नरपतेर्नर्मसुहृन्नन्दनो<BR> नृपमुखेन 1. 11; Śi. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मसाचिव्यम्
नर्मन् + -साचिव्यम्<BR>—1 amusement; flattery.<BR>—2 Superintendence of a princeʼs amusements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मस्फूर्जः|नर्मस्फूर्ज|नर्म्मस्फूर्ज्ज
नर्मन् + -स्फूर्जः (in drama) the first meeting of lovers beginning with<BR> joy but ending in alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मस्फोटः|नर्मस्फोट|नर्म्मस्फोट
नर्मन् + -स्फोटः the first symptoms of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मय्
नर्मय् Den. To entertain; Kau. A. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मवत्
नर्मवत् <i>a.</i> Humorous, witty. ━<i>n.</i> A kind of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मायितम्
नर्मायितम् Sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मरा
नर्मरा<BR>—1 A valley, cavity.<BR>—2 A bellows.<BR>—3 An old woman past menstruation.<BR>—4 The plant <i>Saralā</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य See under नर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्
नल् €1 P. (नलति)<BR>—1 To smell.<BR>—2 To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलः|नल|नलं
नलः<BR>—1 A kind of reed; Bhāg. 1. 6. 13; एरण्डभिण्डार्कनलैः प्रभूतैरपि<BR> संचितैः । दारुकृत्यं यथा नास्ति तथैवाज्ञैः प्रयोजनम् ॥ Pt. 1. 96.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated king of the Niṣadhas and hero of the poem called<BR> ‘Naiṣadhacharita’. [Nala was a very noble-minded and virtuous king. He<BR> was chosen by Damayantī in spite of the opposition of gods, and they<BR> lived happily for some years. But Kali −who was disappointed in securing<BR> her hand− resolved to persecute Nala, and entered into his person. Thus<BR> affected he played at dice with his brother, and having lost everything,<BR> he, with his wife, was banished from the kingdom. One day, while wandering<BR> through the wilderness, he abandoned his wife, almost naked, and went<BR> away. Subsequently he was deformed by the serpent Karkoṭaka, and so deformed<BR> he entered the service of king Ṛtuparṇa of Ayodhyā as a horse-groom<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">Page0881-2</a>]<BR> under the name of Bāhuka. Subsequently with the assistance of the king<BR> he regained his beloved and they led a happy life; see ऋतुपर्ण and<BR> दमयन्ती also.]<BR>—3 N. of a monkey-chief, son of Viśvakarman, who, it is said, built the<BR> bridge of stones called Nalasetu or ‘Adamʼs bridge’ over which Rāma passed<BR> to Laṅkā with his army.<BR>—4 N. of a year (Nm.)<BR>—5 A measure of length (equal to 4 हस्तs); वेदीमष्टनलोत्सेधाम् Mb. 7. 70. 16.<BR>—6 N. of divine being (पितृदेव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलम्
नलः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A blue lotus; नलनीलमूर्तेः Śrīkaṇṭhacharita 1. 33.<BR>—2 Smell, odour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नलकीलः, नलकूबरः, नलकूवरः, नलतूला, नलदम्, नलपट्टिका, नलमीनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकीलः|नलकील
नलः + -कीलः the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकूबरः|नलकूबर
नलः + -कूबरः, -कूवरः N. of a son of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकूवरः|नलकूवर
नलः + -कूबरः, -कूवरः N. of a son of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलतूला
नलः + -तूला a variety of the hides of aquatic animals; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलदम्
नलः + -दम्<BR>—1 a fragrant root (उशीर); Ki. 12. 50; N. 4. 116. कतकं नक्रनखरं<BR> नलदं नागकेसरम् Śiva B. 30. 14.<BR>—2 the honey of a flower.<BR>—3 the flower of Hibiscus Rosa Sinensis (Mar. जास्वंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलपट्टिका
नलः + -पट्टिका a sort of mat made of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलमीनः|नलमीन
नलः + -मीनः a shrimp or prawn; Rām. 3. 73. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकम्
नलकम्<BR>—1 Any long bone of the body; Mv. 1. 35; जङ्घानलकमुदयिनीर्मज्जधाराः<BR> पिबन्ति Māl. 5. 17.<BR>—2 The radius of the arm.<BR>—3 A particular ornament for the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकिनी
नलकिनी<BR>—1 The knee-pan.<BR>—2 The leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिका
नलिका<BR>—1 A tube.<BR>—2 A tubular organ of the body (नाडी).<BR>—3 A quiver.<BR>—4 A kind of fragrant substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनः|नलिन|नलिनं
नलिनः The (Indian) crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनम्
नलिनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A lotus-flower, water-lily.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 The Indigo plant. (नलिनेशयः an epithet of Viṣṇu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनी
नलिनी<BR>—1 A lotus-plant; न पर्वताग्रे नलिनी प्ररोहति Mk. 4. 17; नलिनीदलगतजलमतितरलम्<BR> Moha M. 5; Ku. 4. 6.<BR>—2 An assemblage of lotuses.<BR>—3 A pond or place abounding in lotuses; राजन्तीं राजराजस्य नलिनीमिव<BR> सर्वतः Rām. 2. 95. 4; नलिन्यो यत्र क्रीडन्ति प्रमदाः सुरसेविताः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 13.<BR>—4 A lotus or the stalk of it.<BR>—5 The celestial Ganges.<BR>—6 The intoxicating juice of the cocoa-nut.<BR>—7 A myst.<BR>—8 N. of one of the nostrils. —9 the city of Indra (शक्रपुरी); ‘वस्वौकसारा श्रीदस्य शक्रस्य नलिनी पुरी’ इति हरिः; Rām. 2. 94. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नलिनीखण्डम्, नलिनीषण्डम्, नलिनीदलम्, नलिनीपत्रम्, नलिनीरुहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीखण्डम्
नलिनी + -खण्डम्, -षण्डम् a group or assemblage of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीषण्डम्
नलिनी + -खण्डम्, -षण्डम् a group or assemblage of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीदलम्
नलिनी + -दलम्, -पत्रम् a leaf of the lotus plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीपत्रम्
नलिनी + -दलम्, -पत्रम् a leaf of the lotus plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीरुहः|नलिनीरुह|नलिनीरुहं
नलिनी + -रुहः an epithet of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीरुहम्
नलिनी + -रुहः + .({@-हम्@}) a lotus-stalk, the fibres of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नली
नली <i>f.</i> A kind of perfume or red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्वः|नल्व
नल्वः A measure of distance equal to 400 <i>hastas</i> or cubits.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नल्ववर्त्मगा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्ववर्त्मगा
नल्वः + -वर्त्मगा the orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 New, fresh, young, recent; चित्तयोनिरभवत्पुनर्नवः R. 19. 46;<BR> एते वयं पुनर्नवीकृताः स्मः Ś. 5; क्लेशः फलेन हि पुनर्नवतां<BR> विधत्ते Ku. 5. 86; U. 1. 19; R. 1. 83, 2. 47, 3. 53, 4. 3, 11; Śi. 1. 4;<BR> नववयसि Mu. 3. 3; Śi. 3. 31; Ki. 9. 43.<BR>—2 Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवः|नव
नव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A crow.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR>—3 A young monk, novice; Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम्
नव + .{@-वम्@} ━<i>ind.</i> Recently, newly, lately, not long ago.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नवाङ्गी, नवान्नम्, नवाम्बु, नवाहः, नवेतर, नवोद्धृतम्, नवोढा, नवपाणिग्रहणा, नवकारिका, नवकालिका, नवफलिका, नवच्छात्रः, नवद्वीपः, नवनी, नवनीतकम्, नवनीतजम्, नवपाठकः, नवप्रसूता, नवप्राशनम्, नवमल्लिका, नवमालिका, नवयज्ञः, नवयौवनम्, नवरजस्, नववधूः, नववरिका, नववल्लभम्, नववस्त्रम्, नवशस्यम्, नवशशिभृत्, नवश्राद्धम्, नवसारः, नवसूतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाङ्गी
नव + -अङ्गी a woman. नवाङ्गी कुरङ्गी दृगङ्गीकरोतु Jag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवान्नम्
नव + -अन्नम्<BR>—1 new rice or grain.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">Page0882-1</a>]<BR>—2 a ceremony performed on first eating the new rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0881-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाम्बु|नवांबु
नव + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> fresh water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाहः|नवाह
नव + -अहः the first day of a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवेतर
नव + -इतर <i>a.</i> old; न च योगविधेर्नवेतरः स्थिरधीरा परमात्मदर्शनात्<BR> (विरराम); R. 8. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोद्धृतम्
नव + -उद्धृतम् fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोढा
नव + -ऊढा, -पाणिग्रहणा —1 a newly married woman, a bride; आस्तां मानसतुष्टये<BR> सुकृतिनां नीतिर्नवोढेव वः H. 1. 185; Bh. 1. 4; नवपाणिग्रहणां<BR> वधूमिव (सदयं बुभुजे) R. 8. 7.<BR>—2 a kind of heroine (in dramas); “लज्जाभरपराधीनरतिर्नवोढा”;<BR> बलान्नीता पार्श्वं मुखमनुमुखं नैव कुरुते, धुनाना मूर्धानं क्षिपति<BR> वदनं चुम्बनविधौ । हृदि न्यस्तं हस्तं क्षिपति गमनारोपितमना, नवोढा<BR> बोढारं रमयति च सन्तापयति च ॥ Ras. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपाणिग्रहणा
नव + -ऊढा, -पाणिग्रहणा —1 a newly married woman, a bride; आस्तां मानसतुष्टये<BR> सुकृतिनां नीतिर्नवोढेव वः H. 1. 185; Bh. 1. 4; नवपाणिग्रहणां<BR> वधूमिव (सदयं बुभुजे) R. 8. 7.<BR>—2 a kind of heroine (in dramas); “लज्जाभरपराधीनरतिर्नवोढा”;<BR> बलान्नीता पार्श्वं मुखमनुमुखं नैव कुरुते, धुनाना मूर्धानं क्षिपति<BR> वदनं चुम्बनविधौ । हृदि न्यस्तं हस्तं क्षिपति गमनारोपितमना, नवोढा<BR> बोढारं रमयति च सन्तापयति च ॥ Ras. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकारिका
नव + -कारिका, -कालिका, -फलिका<BR>—1 a woman newly married.<BR>—2 a woman in whom menstruation has recently commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकालिका
नव + -कारिका, -कालिका, -फलिका<BR>—1 a woman newly married.<BR>—2 a woman in whom menstruation has recently commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवफलिका
नव + -कारिका, -कालिका, -फलिका<BR>—1 a woman newly married.<BR>—2 a woman in whom menstruation has recently commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवच्छात्रः|नवच्छात्र|नवछात्र
नव + -छात्रः a fresh student, novice, tyro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवद्वीपः|नवद्वीप
नव + -द्वीपः N. of a place (modern Nuddea, at the confluence of भागीरथी<BR> and जलङ्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनी
नव + -नी <i>f.</i>, {@-नीतम्@}<BR> fresh butter; अहो नवनीतकल्पहृदय आर्यपुत्रः M. 3.<BR> दुग्धोत्थं नवनीतं तु चक्षुष्यं रक्तपित्तनुत् Āyurveda. ˚धेनुः<BR> A cow made of butter, fit to be offered to a Brahmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतकम्
नव + -नीतकम्, -नीतजम्<BR>—1 clarified butter.<BR>—2 fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतजम्
नव + -नीतकम्, -नीतजम्<BR>—1 clarified butter.<BR>—2 fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपाठकः|नवपाठक
नव + -पाठकः a new teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवप्रसूता
नव + -प्रसूता a woman who has lately brought forth (a child).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवप्राशनम्
नव + -प्राशनम् eating of new rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमल्लिका
नव + -मल्लिका, -मालिका a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमालिका
नव + -मल्लिका, -मालिका a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयज्ञः|नवयज्ञ
नव + -यज्ञः an offering of the first fruits of the harvest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयौवनम्
नव + -यौवनम् fresh youth, bloom or prime of youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयौवना
नव + -यौवनम् + .({@-ना@}) a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरजस्
नव + -रजस् <i>f.</i> a girl who has recently menstruated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववधूः
नव + -वधूः, -वरिका<BR>—1 a newly-married girl.<BR>—2 a daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववरिका
नव + -वधूः, -वरिका<BR>—1 a newly-married girl.<BR>—2 a daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववल्लभम्
नव + -वल्लभम् a kind of sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववस्त्रम्
नव + -वस्त्रम् new cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्यम्
नव + -शस्यम् the first fruits of the yearʼs harvest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशशिभृत्
नव + -शशिभृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva; रक्षाहेतोर्नवशशिभृता<BR> वासवीनां चमूनामत्यादित्यं हुतवहमुखे संभृतं तद्धि तेजः Me. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवश्राद्धम्
नव + -श्राद्धम् a श्राद्ध performed on odd days after death <i>i. e.</i><BR> on the third, fifth, seventh, ninth, eleventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवसारः|नवसार
नव + -सारः a kind of Āyurvedic decoction; नवसारो भवेच्छुद्धश्चूर्णतोयैर्विपाचितः ।<BR> दोलायन्त्रेण यत्नेन भिषग्भिर्योगसिद्धये ॥ Vaidyacandrikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवसूतिः|नवसूति
नव + -सूतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-सूतिका@}<BR>—1 a milch-cow.<BR>—2 a woman recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवता
नवता, -त्वम्<BR> Freshness, novelty; क्षणे क्षणे यन्नवतामुपैति तदेव<BR> रूपं रमणीयतायाः Śi. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत्वम्
नवता, -त्वम्<BR> Freshness, novelty; क्षणे क्षणे यन्नवतामुपैति तदेव<BR> रूपं रमणीयतायाः Śi. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनम्
नवनम् The act of praising or extolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकृ
नवीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To make new, renew, revive.<BR>—2 To refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन, नव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 New, fresh, recent नवीननीरदश्यामं रक्तपङ्कजलोचनम् Brav. P. 2. 16, 3. 36.<BR>—2 Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0882-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
