नवम|नवमः
नवम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमी
नवम + .{@-मी@} The ninth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशः
नवशः <i>ind.</i> By nines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् I. €4 P. (नश्यति, ननाश, अनशत्, नङ्क्ष्यति, नशिष्यति नष्ट;<BR> <i>caus.</i> नाशयति; <i>desid.</i> निनङ्क्षति, निनशिषति)<BR>—1 To be lost, to disappear, vanish, become invisible; ध्रुवाणि तस्य<BR> नश्यन्ति H. 1; तथा सीमा न नश्यति Ms. 8. 247; Y. 2. 58; क्षणनष्टदृष्टतिमिरम् Mk. 5. 24.<BR>—2 To be destroyed, to perish, die, be ruined; जीवनाशं ननाश च<BR> Bk. 14. 31; Ms. 8. 166, 7. 40; Mu. 6. 8.<BR>—3 To run away, fly away, escape; नश्यन्ति वृन्दानि ददर्श कपीन्द्रः<BR> Bk. 10. 12; नेशुश्चित्रा निशाचराः 14. 112; Ratn. 2. 3.<BR>—4 To be frustrated, become unsuccessful. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to disappear.<BR>—2 To destroy, remove, efface, drive away, cause to fly away.<BR>—3 To violate (as a virgin).<BR>—4 To cause to be lost, lose.<BR>—5 To forget.<BR>—6 To extinguish, put out (as fire). ━II. €1 U. (नशति-ते) Ved.<BR>—1 To reach, attain.<BR>—2 To meet with, find.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् <i>f.</i>, नशः, नशनम् Destruction, perishing, loss,<BR> disappearing; प्रतीक्षन्गिरिशादेशं स्ववीर्यनशनं कुधीः Bhāg. 10. 62. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशः|नश
नश् <i>f.</i>, नशः, नशनम् Destruction, perishing, loss,<BR> disappearing; प्रतीक्षन्गिरिशादेशं स्ववीर्यनशनं कुधीः Bhāg. 10. 62. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशनम्
नश् <i>f.</i>, नशः, नशनम् Destruction, perishing, loss,<BR> disappearing; प्रतीक्षन्गिरिशादेशं स्ववीर्यनशनं कुधीः Bhāg. 10. 62. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्प्रसूतिका
नश्यत्प्रसूतिका A woman who brings forth a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [नश्-क्वरप्]<BR>—1 Perishable, transitory, evanescent, transient, frail; निखिलं जगदेव<BR> नश्वरम् R. G.<BR>—2 Destructive, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [नश्-क्त]<BR>—1 Lost, disappeared, vanished, invisible; गगनमिव नष्टतारम् Pt. 5. 6, 2. 167.<BR>—2 Dead, perished, destroyed.<BR>—3 Spoiled, wasted.<BR>—4 Fled or run away; नष्टं वर्षधरैर्मनुष्यगणनाभावादकृत्वा त्रपाम् Ratn. 2. 3.<BR>—5 Deprived of, free from (in comp.)<BR>—6 Depraved, corrupted, debauched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टम्
नष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Destruction, loss.<BR>—2 Disappearance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नष्टाग्निः, नष्टार्थ, नष्टातङ्कम्, नष्टात्मन्, नष्टाप्तिसूत्रम्, नष्टाशङ्क, नष्टेन्दुकला, नष्टेन्द्रिय, नष्टक्रिय, नष्टकोण, नष्टचन्द्रः, नष्टचर्या, नष्टचेतन, नष्टचेष्ट, नष्टसंज्ञ, नष्टचेष्टता, नष्टजन्मन्, नष्टदृष्टि, नष्टधी, नष्टबीज, नष्टरूप, नष्टस्मृति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाग्निः|नष्टाग्नि
नष्ट + -अग्निः a householder who has lost his consecrated fire (it being extinguished).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टार्थ
नष्ट + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> reduced to poverty (having lost oneʼs wealth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टातङ्कम्|नष्टातंकम्
नष्ट + -आतङ्कम् <i>ind.</i> without anxiety or fear; नष्टातङ्कं हरिणशिशवो<BR> मन्दमन्दं चरन्ति Ś. 1. 15 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0883-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टात्मन्
