नागसंभूतम्
नाग + -संभवम्, -संभूतम् red lead … … मञ्जिष्ठां नागसंभवम्<BR> Śiva B. 30. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागसाह्वयम्
नाग + -साह्वयम् Hastināpura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागिन्
नागिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [नगरे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Town-born, town-bred.<BR>—2 Relating to a town, civic.<BR>—3 Spoken in a town.<BR>—4 Polite, civil.<BR>—5 Clever, sharp.<BR>—6 Bad, vile, one who has contracted the vices of a town. नागनागरयोर्मध्ये<BR> वरं नागो न नागरः । नागो दशति कालेन नागरस्तु पुनः पुनः ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—7 Nameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरः|नागर|नागरं
नागर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A citizen (पौर); यः पण्यस्त्रीरतिपरिमलोद्गारिभिर्नागराणामुद्दामानि<BR> प्रथयति शिलावेश्मभिर्यौवनानि Me. 25; Śānti. 4. 19; Bhāg. 10. 56. 17.<BR>—2 A husbandʼs brother.<BR>—3 A lecturer.<BR>—4 An orange.<BR>—5 Fatigue; hardship, toil.<BR>—6 Desire of final beatitude.<BR>—7 A term applied to a prince engaged in war under certain circumstances<BR> and also to a planet when in opposition to other planets (in astrol.)<BR>—8 Denial of knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरम्
नागर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Dry ginger; खर्बूरं मरिचं पूर्णं देवदारु च नागरम् Śiva B. 30. 16.<BR> पिप्पली सैन्धवं चैव नागरं च गुडान्वितम् । प्रातर्दत्तं तुरङ्गाणां<BR> नस्यं श्लेष्मविनाशनम् ॥ Śālihotra.<BR>—2 A kind of coitus.<BR>—3 One of the three styles of architecture; it is quadrangular in shape;<BR> चतुरस्राकृतिं यत्तु नागरं तत् प्रकीर्तितम् Māna. 18. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरी
नागर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 The character in which Sanskrit is generally written; cf. देवनागरी.<BR>—2 A clever, intriguing or shrewd woman; हन्ताभीरीः स्मरतु स कथं<BR> संवृतो नागरीभिः Ud. D. 16.<BR>—3 The plant स्नुही.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नागराह्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराह्वम्
नागर + -आह्वम् dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक, नागरिक <i>a.</i> [नगरे भवः वुञ्]<BR>—1 Town-bred, town-born.<BR>—2 Polite, courteous, courtly; नागरिकवृत्त्या संज्ञापयैनाम् Ś. 5;<BR> साधु आर्य नागरिकोऽसि V. 2.<BR>—3 Clever,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">Page0885-2</a>]<BR> shrewd, cunning (विदग्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरिक
नागरक, नागरिक <i>a.</i> [नगरे भवः वुञ्]<BR>—1 Town-bred, town-born.<BR>—2 Polite, courteous, courtly; नागरिकवृत्त्या संज्ञापयैनाम् Ś. 5;<BR> साधु आर्य नागरिकोऽसि V. 2.<BR>—3 Clever,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">Page0885-2</a>]<BR> shrewd, cunning (विदग्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरकः|नागरक
नागरक, नागरिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A citizen.<BR>—2 A polite or courteous man, a gallant, one who shows exaggerated attention<BR> to his first mistress while he is courting some one else.<BR>—3 One who has contracted the vices of a town.<BR>—4 A thief.<BR>—5 An artist.<BR>—6 The chief of the police; V. 5; Ś. 6.<BR>—7 A city-superintendent; cf. नागरिकप्रणिधिः Kau. A.<BR>—8 A kind of coitus; ऊरुमूलोपरि स्थित्वा योषिदूरुद्वयं रमेत् । ग्रीवां<BR> धृत्वा कराभ्यां च बन्धो नागरको मतः ॥ Ratimañjarī.<BR>—9 (pl.) planets opposite to each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरकम्
नागरक, नागरिक + .{@-कम्@} —1 Dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरिकम्
नागरक, नागरिक + .{@-कम्@} + .({@-रिकम्@}) The toll levied from a town.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नागरकवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरकवृत्तिः
नागरक + -वृत्तिः a courtly manner or style; नागरिकवृत्त्या संज्ञापयैनाम् Ś. 5. 1/2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरता
नागरता Cleverness, dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेयक|नागरेयकः
नागरेयक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [नगर्यां भवः ठकञ्] Belonging to a town, civic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरीटः|नागरीट
नागरीटः, -नागवीटः<BR>—1 A libertine, rake.<BR>—2 A paramour.<BR>—3 A match-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीटः|नागवीट
नागरीटः, -नागवीटः<BR>—1 A libertine, rake.<BR>—2 A paramour.<BR>—3 A match-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरुकः|नागरुक
नागरुकः Orange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर्यम्
नागर्यम् Shrewdness, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागार्जुनः|नागार्जुन
नागार्जुनः N. of an ancient Buddhist teacher of the rank of बोधिसत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोजीभट्टः|नागोजीभट्ट
नागोजीभट्टः N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेतः|नाचिकेत
नाचिकेतः —1 Fire; ततो मया नाचिकेतश्चितोऽग्निरनित्यैर्द्रव्यैः<BR> Kaṭh. 1. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेतम्
नाचिकेतः + .{@-तम्@} N. of an उपाख्यान; नाचिकेतमुपाख्यानं मृत्युप्रोक्तं सनातनम् ।<BR> उक्त्वा श्रुत्वा च मेधावी ब्रह्मलोके महीयते ॥ Kaṭh. 1. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटः|नाट
नाटः [नट्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Dancing, acting.<BR>—2 N. of the Karnāṭaka country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकम्
नाटकम् [नट्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A play, drama (in general).<BR>—2 The first of the 10 principal kinds of dramatic composition; for definition<BR> and other information see S. D. 277, where 36 लक्षणs of a नाटक are given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकः|नाटक|नाटकं
नाटकम् + .{@-कः@} An actor, a dancer; वधूनाटकसंघैश्च संयुक्तां सर्वतः<BR> पुरीम् Rām. 1. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकी
नाटकम् + .{@-की@} The court of Indra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाटकप्रपञ्चः, नाटकविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकप्रपञ्चः|नाटकप्रपञ्च
नाटकम् + -प्रपञ्चः the arrangement of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकविधिः|नाटकविधि
नाटकम् + -विधिः dramatic action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीय
नाटकीय <i>a.</i> [नाटक-छ] Pertaining to a drama, dramatic;<BR> पूर्वरङ्गः प्रसंगाय नाटकीयस्य वस्तुना Śi. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीया
नाटकीय + .{@-या@} An actress or dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटारः|नाटार
नाटारः [नटपा अपत्यम् आरक्] The son of an actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटिका
नाटिका A short or light comedy, one of the Uparūpakas, q. v.; <i>e. g.</i><BR> the Ratnāvalī, Priyadarśikā or Viddhaśālabañjikā. The S. D.<BR> thus defines it:− नाटिका कॢप्तवृत्ता स्यात् स्त्रीप्राया चतुरङ्किका ।<BR> प्रख्यातो धीरललितस्तत्र स्यान्नायको नृपः ॥ स्यादन्तःपुरसंबन्धा संगीतव्यापृताऽथवा ।<BR> नवानुरागा कन्याऽत्र नायिका नृपवंशजा ॥ संप्रवर्तेत नेतास्यां देव्यास्त्रासेन<BR> शङ्कितः । देवी पुनर्भवेज्ज्येष्ठा प्रगल्भा नृपवंशजा ॥ पदे पदे मानवती<BR> तद्वशः संगमो द्वयोः । वृत्तिः स्यात् कौशिकी स्वल्पविमर्शाः संधयः पुनः ॥ 539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0885-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटितकम्
नाटितकम् A mimic representation, a gesture, gesticulation; भीतिनाटितकेन Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेयः|नाटेय
नाटेयः, -रः<BR> [नटपा अपत्यं ढक् ढ्रक् वा] The son of an actress or dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेरः|नाटेर
नाटेयः, -रः<BR> [नटपा अपत्यं ढक् ढ्रक् वा] The son of an actress or dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यम्
नाट्यम् [नटस्येदं कृत्यं ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Dancing.<BR>—2 Dramatic representation, gesticulation, acting; नाट्ये च दक्षा वयम्<BR> Ratn. 1. 6; नूनं नाटपे भवति च चिरं नोर्वशी गर्वशीला Vikr. 18. 29.<BR>—3 The science or art of dancing or acting, scenic art; नाट्यं भिन्नरुचेर्जनस्य<BR> बहुधाप्येकं समाराधनम् M. 1. 4.<BR>—4 The costume of an actor; न लक्ष्यसे मूढदृशा नटो नाट्यधरो यथा<BR> Bhāg. 1. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यः|नाट्य|नाट्यं
नाट्यम् + .{@-ट्यः@} An actor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाट्याङ्गानि, नाट्यागारम्, नाट्याचार्यः, नाट्योक्तिः, नाट्यधर्मिका, नाट्यधर्मी, नाट्यप्रियः, नाट्यरासकम्, नाट्यवेदः, नाट्यवेदी, नाट्यशाला, नाट्यशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्याङ्गानि
नाट्यम् + -अङ्गानि <i>n.</i> (pl.) ten अङ्गs of नाट्य <i>i. e.</i> गेयपद,<BR> स्थितपाद्य, आसीन, पुष्पगण्डिका, प्रच्छेदक, त्रिगूढक, सैन्धव, द्विगूढक,<BR> उत्तमोत्तमक, उक्तप्रत्युक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यागारम्
नाट्यम् + -आगारम् a dancing room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्याचार्यः|नाट्याचार्य
नाट्यम् + -आचार्यः a dancing preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्योक्तिः|नाट्योक्ति
नाट्यम् + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> dramatic phraseology (as: स्वगत, प्रकाश, अपवाहित, जनान्तिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यधर्मिका|नाट्यधर्म्मिका
नाट्यम् + -धर्मिका, -धर्मी the rules of dramatic representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यधर्मी
नाट्यम् + -धर्मिका, -धर्मी the rules of dramatic representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यप्रियः|नाट्यप्रिय
नाट्यम् + -प्रियः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यरासकम्
नाट्यम् + -रासकम् a kind of play consisting of one act; S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यवेदः|नाट्यवेद
नाट्यम् + -वेदः the science of drama and dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यवेदी
नाट्यम् + -वेदी a stage, scene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यशाला
नाट्यम् + -शाला<BR>—1 a dancing-hall.<BR>—2 a theatre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यशास्त्रम्
नाट्यम् + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 the dramatic science, dramaturgy.<BR>—2 a work on dramatic representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाड
नाड = नाल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिः|नाडि
नाडिः, -डी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The tubular stalk of any plant.<BR>—2 The hollow stalk of a lotus &c.; स इत्थमुद्वीक्ष्य तदब्दनालनाडीभिरन्तर्जलमाविवेश<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 19.<BR>—3 Any tubular organ of the body (such as an artery, vein); षडधिकदशनाडीचक्रमध्यस्थितात्मा Māl. 5. 1, 2.<BR>—4 A pipe, flute.<BR>—5 A fistulous sore, fistula, sinus.<BR>—6 The pulse at the hand or foot.<BR>—7 A measure of time equal to twenty-four minutes.<BR>—8 A period of time = ½ Muhūrta.<BR>—9 A sort of bent grass.<BR>—10 A juggling trick.<BR>—11 A leather-string; L. D. B.<BR>—12 A weaverʼs implement; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाडिचक्रम्, नाडिचरणः, नाडिचीरम्, नाडिजङ्घः, नाडितरङ्गः, नाडिनक्षत्रम्, नाडिपरीक्षा, नाडिपात्रम्, नाडिमण्डलम्, नाडियन्त्रम्, नाडिवलयम्, नाडिव्रणः, नाडिखेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडी
नाडिः, -डी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The tubular stalk of any plant.<BR>—2 The hollow stalk of a lotus &c.; स इत्थमुद्वीक्ष्य तदब्दनालनाडीभिरन्तर्जलमाविवेश<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 19.<BR>—3 Any tubular organ of the body (such as an artery, vein); षडधिकदशनाडीचक्रमध्यस्थितात्मा Māl. 5. 1, 2.<BR>—4 A pipe, flute.<BR>—5 A fistulous sore, fistula, sinus.<BR>—6 The pulse at the hand or foot.<BR>—7 A measure of time equal to twenty-four minutes.<BR>—8 A period of time = ½ Muhūrta.<BR>—9 A sort of bent grass.<BR>—10 A juggling trick.<BR>—11 A leather-string; L. D. B.<BR>—12 A weaverʼs implement; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाडिचक्रम्, नाडिचरणः, नाडिचीरम्, नाडिजङ्घः, नाडितरङ्गः, नाडिनक्षत्रम्, नाडिपरीक्षा, नाडिपात्रम्, नाडिमण्डलम्, नाडियन्त्रम्, नाडिवलयम्, नाडिव्रणः, नाडिखेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिचक्रम्
नाडिः + -चक्रम् a group of tubular organs of the body such as: मूलाधार,<BR> स्वाधिष्ठान, मणिपुर, अनाहत, विशुद्धि, आज्ञाचक्र, सहस्राधार; Pātañjala S.;<BR> षडधिकदशनाडीचक्रमध्यस्थितात्मा Māl. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिचरणः
नाडिः + -चरणः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिचीरम्
नाडिः + -चीरम्<BR>—1 a small reed.<BR>—2 a tube round which the woof is wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिजङ्घः
नाडिः + -जङ्घः<BR>—1 a crow.<BR>—2 a kind of crane; नाडीजङ्घो निजघ्ने कृततदुपकृतिर्यत्कृते गौतमेन Nāg. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडितरङ्गः
नाडिः + -तरङ्गः<BR>—1 an astrologer.<BR>—2 a debaucher, ravisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिनक्षत्रम्
नाडिः + -नक्षत्रम् = जन्मनक्षत्र q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिपरीक्षा
नाडिः + -परीक्षा feeling the pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिपात्रम्
नाडिः + -पात्रम् a kind of water-clock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिमण्डलम्
नाडिः + -मण्डलम् the celestial equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडियन्त्रम्
नाडिः + -यन्त्रम् any tubular instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिवलयम्
नाडिः + -वलयम् equinoctical circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिव्रणः|नाडिव्रण
नाडिः + -व्रणः sinus, an ulcer, a fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिखेदः
नाडिः + -खेदः steam-bath through tubes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिका
नाडिका<BR>—1 A tubular organ &c.; see नाडि.<BR>—2 A Ghaṭikā or 24 minutes; नाडिकाविच्छेदपटहः Māl. 7; Bhāg. 3. 11. 8;<BR> K. 13, 70; दशनाडिकाः पूर्णाः । अतिक्रामति स्नानवेला । Abhiṣeka. 1.<BR>—3 A hollow stalk in general.<BR>—4 A fistulous sore.<BR>—5 A ray of the sun.<BR>—6 A gong (on which the hours are struck).<BR>—7 A measure of length = ½ Daṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिंधम|नाडिन्धम|नाडिंधमः|नाडिन्धमः
नाडिं(डीं)धम <i>a.</i> Causing a movement of the tubular organs (as<BR> fright &c.); नाडिंधमेन श्वासेन K. 353; कथं नाडिंधमान् मार्गानागतौ<BR> विषमोपलान् Bk. 6. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडींधम
नाडिं(डीं)धम <i>a.</i> Causing a movement of the tubular organs (as<BR> fright &c.); नाडिंधमेन श्वासेन K. 353; कथं नाडिंधमान् मार्गानागतौ<BR> विषमोपलान् Bk. 6. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिंधमः|नाडिन्धम|नाडिंधम|नाडिन्धमः
नाडिं(डीं)धम + .{@-मः@} A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिंधय|नाडिन्धय|नाडिन्धयः
नाडिंधय <i>a.</i> Drinking or sucking through a tube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीका
नाडीका The wind-pipe or throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिकेलः|नाडिकेल
नाडिकेलः = नारिकेल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकम्
नाणकम् A coin, anything stamped with an impression; एषा नाणकमोषिका<BR> मकशिका Mk. 1. 23; Y. 2. 240.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाणकपरीक्षा, नाणकपरीक्षिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षा
नाणकम् + -परीक्षा the testing of coin, assaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षिन्
नाणकम् + -परीक्षिन् an assayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिचिर
नातिचिर <i>a.</i> Of no long duration, not very long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिदूर
नातिदूर <i>a.</i> Not very far or distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिवादः|नातिवाद
नातिवादः Avoiding abusive language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्रः|नात्र|नात्रं
नात्रः<BR>—1 Śiva.<BR>—2 A sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्रम्
नात्रः + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 Praise.<BR>—2 Surprise, wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ्
नाथ् €1 P. (नाथति, but sometimes Ā. also)<BR>—1 To ask, beg, solicit for anything (with dat. or two acc.); मोक्षाय<BR> नाथते मुनिः Vop.; नाथसे किमु पतिं न भूभृतः Ki. 13. 59; संतुष्टमिष्टानि<BR> तमिष्टदेवं नाथन्ति के नाम न लोकनाथम् N. 3. 25; वनं न यायादिति<BR> नाथमानः Bu. C. 2. 54.<BR>—2 To have power, be master, prevail.<BR>—3 To harass, trouble.<BR>—4 To bless, wish well to, give blessings to; (said to be Ātm. only in<BR> this sense); धृत्या नाथस्व वैदेहि … Bk. 8. 120; नाथितशमे Mv. 1. 11;<BR> (Mammaṭa quotes the line दीनं त्वामनुनाथते कुचयुगं पत्रावृतं<BR> मा कृथाः to show that नाथ् here only means ‘to ask or beg’, and says<BR> that नाथते should, therefore, be नाथति); सर्पिषो नाथते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथः|नाथ
नाथः [नाथ्-अच्]<BR>—1 A lord, master, leader; नाथे कुतस्त्वय्यशुभं प्रजानाम् R. 5. 13, 2. 73, 3. 45;<BR> त्रिलोक˚, कैलास˚ &c. भर्तृनाथा हि नार्यः Pratimā 1. 25;<BR> विजनेऽपि च नाथवानिवास्मि Bu. C. 5. 69.<BR>—2 A husband.<BR>—3 A rope passed through the nose of a draft-ox.<BR>—4 A possessor.<BR>—5 A protector; अनाथाया हि नाथस्त्वं कौसल्याया भविष्यसि Rām. 2. 53. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाथहरिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथहरिः|नाथहरि
नाथः + -हरिः a beast (पशु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवत्|नाथवन्त्
नाथवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of a lord or protector; नाथवन्तस्त्वया लोकास्त्वमनाथा<BR> विपत्स्यसे U. 1. 43.<BR>—2 Dependent, subject; ब्राह्मणा भुञ्जते नित्यं नाथवन्तश्च भुञ्जते<BR> Rām. 1. 14. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथितम्
नाथितम् Supplication, demand, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादः|नाद
नादः [नद्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A loud roar, cry, shout, sounding, roaring; सिंहनादः, घन˚ &c.<BR>—2 A sound in general; Māl. 5. 20; न नादेन विना गीतं न नादेन विना<BR> स्वरः । न नादेन विना रागस्तस्मान्नादात्मकं जगत् ॥ Saṅgītadāmodara.<BR>—3 (In Yoga phil.) The nasal sound represented by a semicircle.<BR>—4 One who praises.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नादमुद्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादमुद्रा
नादः + -मुद्रा <i>f.</i> A kind of Tāntrika Mudrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादवत्|नादवन्त्
नादवत् <i>a.</i> Sonant, resounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादि
नादि <i>a.</i> Sounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0886-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sounding, resonant; अम्बुदवृन्दनादी रथः Mb.; R. 3. 59, 19. 5.<BR>—2 Bellowing, roaring; खर˚, सिंह˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय [नद्या नदस्य वा ठक्] River-born, aquatic, marine; Rām. 4. 39. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेयम्
नादेय + .{@-यम्@} Rock-salt; नादेयं नादेयं शरदि वसन्ते च नादेयम् Vaidyaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेयी
नादेय + .{@-यी@} N. of several plants (Mar. भुइजांभळी, टाहाकळ, बोरू etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद्य
नाद्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to a river, river-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद्यम्
नाद्य + .{@-द्यम्@} A lotus; (नमो) नाद्योपहारलुब्धाय Mb. 12. 284. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध्
नाध् = नाथ् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानर्दमान
नानर्दमान <i>a.</i> Sounding loudly, roaring lustily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In different places, in different ways, manifoldly, variously; मृत्योः<BR> स मृत्युमाप्नोति य इह नानेव पश्यति ।<BR>—2 Distinctly, separately.<BR>—3 Without (= विना; with acc., instr. or abl.); नाना नारीं निष्फला<BR> लोकयात्रा Vop.; (विश्वं) न नाना शंभुना रामात् वर्षेणाधोक्षजोवर; <i>ibid.</i><BR>—4 (Used as an adjective at the beginning of comp.) Manifold, various,<BR> sundry, different, diverse; नानाफलैः फलति कल्पलतेव भूमिः Bh. 2. 46;<BR> नानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः Bg. 1. 9; Ms. 9. 148.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नानात्यय^1, नानार्थ, नानात्मवादिन्, नानाश्रय, नानाकारम्, नानाग्रहः, नानाजातीय, नानाधर्मन्, नानाध्वनिः, नानाभाव, नानारस, नानारूप, नानावर्ण, नानाविध, नानाविधम्, नानावीर्य<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानात्यय
नाना + -अत्यय^1 <i>a.</i> of different kinds, manifold, diverse.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानार्थ
नाना + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having different aims or objects.<BR>—2 having different meanings, homonymous (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानात्मवादिन्
नाना + -आत्मवादिन् <i>a.</i> maintaining the Sāṅkhya doctrine that each<BR> individual has a soul distinct from the universal spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाश्रय
नाना + -आश्रय <i>a.</i> of many abodes; नानाश्रया प्रकृतिः Sāṅ. K. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाकारम्
नाना + -कारम् <i>ind.</i> having done variously; P. III. 4. 62; Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाग्रहः|नानाग्रह
नाना + -ग्रहः taking separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाजातीय
नाना + -जातीय <i>a.</i> of diverse kinds or sorts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाधर्मन्
नाना + -धर्मन् <i>a.</i> having different customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाध्वनिः|नानाध्वनि
नाना + -ध्वनिः a musical instrument producing more than one sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाभाव
नाना + -भाव <i>a.</i> various, manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारस
नाना + -रस <i>a.</i> of different or varying tastes; त्रैगुण्योद्भवमत्र<BR> लोकचरितं नानारसं दृश्यते M. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारूप|नानारूपः
नाना + -रूप <i>a.</i> of different forms, diverse, multiform, various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानावर्ण|नानावर्णः
नाना + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> of different colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाविध|नानाविधः
नाना + -विध <i>a.</i> of various sorts, diverse, manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाविधम्
नाना + -विधम् <i>ind.</i> in various ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानावीर्य
नाना + -वीर्य <i>a.</i> having manifold energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानात्वम्
नानात्वम् The state of diversity or plurality; नानात्वं वाह्यभेदाश्च Sāṅ. K. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानानम्
नानानम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Differently, separately &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानान्द्रः|नानान्द्र|नानांद्र|नानांद्रः
नानान्द्रः A husbandʼs sisterʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्त|नांत
नान्त <i>a.</i> Endless, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्तरीयक|नांतरीयक
नान्तरीयक <i>a.</i> Inseparable, invariably connected; अविनाभावः<BR> संबन्धमात्रं न तु नान्तरीयकत्वम् K. P. 2. (नान्तरीयकत्वम् =<BR> तदभावे तदभावरूपा व्याप्तिः); cf. also यत्र च संबन्धो विधीयते<BR> तत्रान्यतरस्यान्यत्र विधानम्, संबन्धो नान्तरीयकः यद् वा संबन्धस्य<BR> विधानं नान्तरीयकौ संबन्धिनौ ŚB. on MS. 3. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्त्रम्
नान्त्रम् Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दन
नान्दन <i>a.</i> Gladdening, pleasing; सैषा विदृतिर्नाम द्वास्तदेतन्नान्दनम्<BR> Ait. Up. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दनम्
नान्दन + .{@-नम्@} A pleasure-garden, paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दिकरः|नान्दिकर|नांदिकर|नांदिकरः
नान्दिकरः, नान्दिन् <i>m.</i> The speaker of the नान्दी or benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दिन्|नांदिन्
नान्दिकरः, नान्दिन् <i>m.</i> The speaker of the नान्दी or benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दी|नांदी
नान्दी [नन्दन्ति देवा अत्र नन्द्-घञ् पृषो˚ वृद्धिः ङीप्]<BR>—1 Joy, satisfaction, delight.<BR>—2 Prosperity; ततो राजकुले नान्दी संजज्ञे भूयसा पुनः Mb. 12. 82. 66.<BR>—3 Praise of a deity at the commencement of a religious rite or observance.<BR>—4 Particularly, the benedictory verse or verses recited as a sort of<BR> prologue at the beginning of a drama, benediction; आशीर्वचनसंयुक्ता<BR> नित्यं यस्मात् प्रयुज्यते । देवद्विजनृपादीनां तस्मान्नान्दीति संज्ञिता ।<BR> or देवद्विजनृपादीनामाशीर्वचनपूर्विका । नन्दन्ति देवता यस्यां<BR> तस्मान्नान्दीति कीर्तिता ॥<BR>—5 Loud noise of a dozen drums; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नान्दीकरः, नान्दीपटः, नान्दीमुख, नान्दीवादिन्, नान्दीश्राद्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीकरः|नान्दीकर|नांदीकर
नान्दी + -करः see नान्दिन्. {@-निनादः, -नादः, -रवः@} a shout<BR> of joy or rejoicing; नान्दीनादप्रभृति हि कृतं मङ्गलं तैस्तदानीम्<BR> Mv. 2. 4. (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीपटः|नान्दीपट|नांदीपट
नान्दी + -पटः the lid or cover of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुख|नांदीमुख|नान्दीमुखः
नान्दी + -मुख <i>a.</i> (the class of manes or deceased ancestors) to whom<BR> the नान्दीमुखश्राद्ध is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुखम्
नान्दी + -मुख + .({@-खम्@}), ˚श्राद्धम् a Śrāddha ceremony performed in memory<BR> of the manes, preliminary to any festive occasion such as marriage &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुखः|नान्दीमुख|नांदीमुख
नान्दी + -मुख + .({@-खः@}) the cover or lid of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुखी
नान्दी + -मुख + .({@-खी@}) a female ancestor entitled to a share in the above Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीवादिन्|नांदीवादिन्
नान्दी + -वादिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the speaker of a prologue to a drama.<BR>—2 a drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीश्राद्धम्
नान्दी + -श्राद्धम् see नान्दीमुखम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीकः|नान्दीक|नांदीकः
नान्दीकः<BR>—1 A post in a door-way set up for good luck.<BR>—2 = नान्दीश्राद्ध see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितः|नापित
नापितः A barber, shaver.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नापितोच्छिष्टता, नापितगृहम्, नापितशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितोच्छिष्टता
नापितः + -उच्छिष्टता the act of not bathing after the shave; पारदार्यमनायुष्यं<BR> नापितोच्छिष्टता तथा Mb. 13. 104. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितगृहम्
नापितः + -गृहम्, -शाला a barberʼs shop, shaving-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितशाला
नापितः + -गृहम्, -शाला a barberʼs shop, shaving-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितायनिः|नापितायनि
नापितायनिः The son of a barber; P. IV. 1. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्यम्
नापित्यम् The trade of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्यः|नापित्य|नापित्यं
नापित्यम् + .{@-त्यः@} The son of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभकः|नाभक
नाभकः A myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभागः|नाभाग
नाभागः N. of the son of Vaivasvata Manu. ˚अरिष्टः N. of the<BR> son of Vaivasvata Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभस
नाभस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Heavenly, celestial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभस्वत
नाभस्वत <i>a.</i> Relating to the wind; अहो यत्र वने घोरे नैव<BR> नाभस्वती कथा Śiva B. 19. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि, -भी <i>m., f.</i><BR> [नह्-इञ् भश्चान्तादेशः cf. Uṇ. 4. 125]<BR>—1 The navel; गङ्गावर्तसनाभिर्नाभिः Dk. 2 &c.; निम्ननाभिः Me. 84, 28;<BR> R. 6. 52; अरा इव रथनाभौ प्राणे सर्वं प्रतिष्ठितम् Praśna. Up.<BR>—2 Any navel-like cavity. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The nave of a wheel; अरैः संधार्यते नाभिर्नाभौ चाराः प्रतिष्ठिताः ।<BR> स्वामिसेवकयोरेवं वृत्तिचक्रं प्रवर्तते ॥ Pt. 1. 81.<BR>—2 The centre, focus, chief point; समुद्रनाभ्यां शाल्वोऽभूत् सौभमास्थाय<BR> शत्रुहन् Mb. 3. 20. 17.<BR>—3 Chief, leader, head; कृत्स्नस्य नाभिर्नृपमण्डलस्य R. 18. 20.<BR>—4 Near relationship, community (of race &c.); as in सनाभि q. v.<BR>—5 A paramount sovereign or lord; उपगतोऽपि च मण्डलनाभिताम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">Page0888-1</a>]<BR> R. 9. 15.<BR>—6 A near relation.<BR>—7 A Kṣatriya<BR>—8 Home.<BR>—9 A field; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभी
नाभि, -भी <i>m., f.</i><BR> [नह्-इञ् भश्चान्तादेशः cf. Uṇ. 4. 125]<BR>—1 The navel; गङ्गावर्तसनाभिर्नाभिः Dk. 2 &c.; निम्ननाभिः Me. 84, 28;<BR> R. 6. 52; अरा इव रथनाभौ प्राणे सर्वं प्रतिष्ठितम् Praśna. Up.<BR>—2 Any navel-like cavity. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The nave of a wheel; अरैः संधार्यते नाभिर्नाभौ चाराः प्रतिष्ठिताः ।<BR> स्वामिसेवकयोरेवं वृत्तिचक्रं प्रवर्तते ॥ Pt. 1. 81.<BR>—2 The centre, focus, chief point; समुद्रनाभ्यां शाल्वोऽभूत् सौभमास्थाय<BR> शत्रुहन् Mb. 3. 20. 17.<BR>—3 Chief, leader, head; कृत्स्नस्य नाभिर्नृपमण्डलस्य R. 18. 20.<BR>—4 Near relationship, community (of race &c.); as in सनाभि q. v.<BR>—5 A paramount sovereign or lord; उपगतोऽपि च मण्डलनाभिताम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">Page0888-1</a>]<BR> R. 9. 15.<BR>—6 A near relation.<BR>—7 A Kṣatriya<BR>—8 Home.<BR>—9 A field; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिः|नाभि
नाभि, -भी + .{@-भिः@} <i>f.</i> Musk (<i>i. e.</i> मृगनाभि). [<i>N. B.</i> नाभि<BR> at the end of Bah. comp. becomes नाभ when the comp. is used as epithet;<BR> as पद्मनाभः.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नाभ्यावर्तः, नाभिकण्टकः, नाभिकूपिका, नाभिगुलकः, नाभिगोलकः, नाभिगन्धः, नाभिजः, नाभिजन्मन्, नाभिनाडी, नाभिनालम्, नाभिमूलम्, नाभिवर्धनम्, नाभिवर्षम्, नाभिवीथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0887-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्यावर्तः|नाभ्यावर्त|नाभ्यावर्त्त
नाभि + -आवर्तः the cavity of the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिकण्टकः|नाभिकण्टक
नाभि + -कण्टकः, -कूपिका, -गुलकः, -गोलकः ruptured navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिकूपिका
नाभि + -कण्टकः, -कूपिका, -गुलकः, -गोलकः ruptured navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगुलकः|नाभिगुलक
नाभि + -कण्टकः, -कूपिका, -गुलकः, -गोलकः ruptured navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगोलकः|नाभिगोलक
नाभि + -कण्टकः, -कूपिका, -गुलकः, -गोलकः ruptured navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगन्धः|नाभिगन्ध
नाभि + -गन्धः the odour of the musk; नाभिगन्धैर्मृगाणाम् Me. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिजः|नाभिज
नाभि + -जः, -जन्मन् <i>m.</i>, {@-भूः@}<BR> epithets of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिजन्मन्
नाभि + -जः, -जन्मन् <i>m.</i>, {@-भूः@}<BR> epithets of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाडी
नाभि + -नाडी, -नालम्<BR>—1 the umbilical cord; तदङ्कशय्याच्युतनाभिनाला R. 5. 7.<BR>—2 rupture of the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनालम्
नाभि + -नाडी, -नालम्<BR>—1 the umbilical cord; तदङ्कशय्याच्युतनाभिनाला R. 5. 7.<BR>—2 rupture of the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिमूलम्
नाभि + -मूलम् the part of the body immediately under the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवर्धनम्
नाभि + -वर्धनम्<BR>—1 cutting or division of the umbilical cord. प्राङ् नाभिवर्धनात् पुंसो<BR> जातकर्म विधीयते Ms. 2. 29.<BR>—2 rupture of the navel.<BR>—3 corpulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवर्षम्
नाभि + -वर्षम् N. of one of the nine वर्षs belonging to Jambudvīpa<BR> and named after Nābhi, the son of Agnīdhra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवीथिः
नाभि + -वीथिः a road proceeding from the central part of a village or<BR> town; Kāmikāgama 25. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिका
नाभिका A cavity shaped like a navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिल
नाभिल <i>a.</i> [नाभिरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्] Relating to or coming from a navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभीलम्
नाभीलम्<BR>—1 The cavity of the navel.<BR>—2 Pain.<BR>—3 A ruptured navel.<BR>—4 The groin of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य <i>a.</i> [नाभि-यत्] Relating to, proceeding from, being in,<BR> the navel, umbilical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्यः|नाभ्य|नाभ्यं
नाभ्य + .{@-भ्यः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभोगः
नाभोगः<BR>—1 A god.<BR>—2 A snake; नाभोगभोज्यो हरिणाधिरूढः सोऽयं गरुत्मानिव राजतीन्दुः<BR> Rām. Ch. 6. 84. (Mark the paranomasia in the words नाभोगभोज्य and<BR> हरिणाधिरूढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम <i>ind.</i> A particle used in the following senses:−<BR>—1 Named, called, by name; हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; तन्नन्दिनीं<BR> सुवृत्तां नाम Dk. 7.<BR>—2 Indeed, certainly, truly, forsooth, verily, to be sure; मया नाम<BR> जितम् V. 2. 17; विनीतवेषेण प्रवेष्टव्यानि तपोवनानि नाम Ś. 1;<BR> आश्वासितस्य मम नाम V. 5. 16 ‘when I was just consoled’; तन्नाम<BR> निष्ठुराः पुरुषाः Mk. 5. 32 ‘that means men are cruel’.<BR>—3 Probably, perhaps; oft. with मा; अये पदशब्द इव मा नाम रक्षिणः<BR> Mk. 3 ‘perhaps (but I hope not) that of guards’; मा नाम अकार्यं कुर्यात् Mk. 4.<BR>—4 possibility; तवैव नामास्त्रगतिः Ku. 3. 19; त्वया नाम मुनिर्विमान्यः<BR> Ś. 5. 20 ‘is it possible &c.’ (implying censure); frequently used with<BR> अपि in the sense of ‘I wish’, ‘would that’, ‘is it likely that &c.’;<BR> see under अपि.<BR>—5 A feigned or pretended action, pretence (अलीक); कार्न्तान्तिको<BR> नाम भूत्वा Dk. 130; so भीतो नामावप्लुत्य 104 ‘as if afraid’, परिश्रमं<BR> नाम विनीय च क्षणम् Ku. 5. 32.<BR>—6 (With imperatives) Granted, though, it may be, well, it may be; तद्<BR> भवतु नाम शोकावेगाय K. 328; अतनुषु विभवेषु ज्ञातयः सन्तु नाम<BR> Ś. 5. 8; Bh. 1. 16; एवं नामास्तु ‘be it so, if you like’; करोतु<BR> नाम नीतिज्ञो व्यवसायमितस्ततः H. 2. 14 ‘though he may exert himself’; Māl. 10. 7.<BR>—7 Anger or censure; ममापि नाम दशाननस्य परैः परिभवः G. M.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">Page0888-2</a>]<BR> (the sentence may imply ‘censure’ also); किं नाम विस्फुरन्ति शस्त्राणि<BR> U. 4; ममापि नाम सत्त्वैरभिभूयन्ते गृहाः Ś. 6.<BR>—8 Wonder; आश्चर्यमन्धो नाम पुत्रं द्रक्ष्यति Sk.<BR>—9 Recollection. नाम is often used with the interrogative pronoun<BR> and its derivatives कथम्, कदा &c. in the sense of ‘possibly’, ‘indeed’,<BR> ‘I should like to know’; अयि कथं नामैतत् U. 6; R. 16. 82; Bh. 2. 44;<BR> H. 1. 104; को नाम राज्ञां प्रियः Pt. 1. 146; को नाम पाकाभिमुखस्य<BR> जन्तुर्द्वाराणि दैवस्य पिधातुमीष्टे U. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन् <i>n.</i> [म्नायते अभ्यस्यते नम्यते अभिधीयते अर्थोऽनेन वा]<BR>—1 A name, appellation, personal name (opp. गोत्र); किं नु नामैतदस्याः<BR> Mu. 1. 1; नाम ग्रह् ‘to address or call upon by name’, नामग्राहमरोदीत्<BR> सा Bk. 5. 5; नाम कृ or दा, नाम्ना or नामतः कृ ‘to give a name, call, name’<BR>; चकार नाम्ना रघुमात्मसंभवम् R. 3. 31, 5. 36;<BR> तौ कुशलवौ चकार किल नामतः 15. 32; चन्द्रापीड इति नाम चक्रे<BR> K. 74; मातरं नामतः पृच्छेयम् Ś. 7.<BR>—2 The mere name; संतप्तायसि संस्थितस्य पयसो नामापि न ज्ञायते<BR> Bh. 2. 67 ‘not even the name, <i>i. e.</i> no trace or mark is seen’ &c.; Pt. 1. 250.<BR>—3 (In gram.) A noun, substantive (opp. आख्यात); तन्नाम येनाभिदधाति<BR> सत्त्वम्; सत्त्वप्रधानानि नामानि Nir.<BR>—4 A word, name, synonymous word; इति वृक्षनामानि.<BR>—5 Substance (opp. गुण).<BR>—6 Water.<BR>—7 Ved. Mark, sign, token.<BR>—8 Form, mode, manner.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नामाङ्क, नामानुशासनम्, नामाभिधानम्, नामापराधः, नामाख्यातिक, नामावली, नामकरणम्, नामकर्मन्, नामग्रहः, नामग्रहणम्, नामग्राहम्, नामत्यागः, नामद्वादशी, नामधातुः, नामधारक, नामधारिन्, नामधेयम्, नामनाभिकः, नामनिर्देशः, नाममात्र, नाममाला, नामसंग्रहः, नाममुद्रा, नामलिङ्गम्, नामवर्जित, नामवाचक, नामशेष, नामशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामाङ्क|नामांक
नामन् + -अङ्क <i>a.</i> marked with a name; नामाङ्करावणशराङ्कितकेतुयाष्टिम्<BR> (रथम्) R. 12. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामानुशासनम्
नामन् + -अनुशासनम्, -अभिधानम्<BR>—1 declaring oneʼs name.<BR>—2 a dictionary, lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामाभिधानम्
नामन् + -अनुशासनम्, -अभिधानम्<BR>—1 declaring oneʼs name.<BR>—2 a dictionary, lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामापराधः|नामापराध
नामन् + -अपराधः abusing (a respectable man) by name, calling names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामाख्यातिक
नामन् + -आख्यातिक <i>a.</i> relating to nouns and verbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामावली
नामन् + -आवली a list of names (of a god).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामकरणम्
नामन् + -करणम्, -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the ceremony of naming a child after birth.<BR>—2 a nominal affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामकर्मन्
नामन् + -करणम्, -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the ceremony of naming a child after birth.<BR>—2 a nominal affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामग्रहः|नामग्रह
नामन् + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम् addressing or mentioning by name, utterance<BR> of the name, calling to mind the name; पुण्यानि नामग्रहणान्यपि महामुनीनाम्<BR> K. 43; Ms. 8. 271; R. 7. 41, 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामग्रहणम्
नामन् + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम् addressing or mentioning by name, utterance<BR> of the name, calling to mind the name; पुण्यानि नामग्रहणान्यपि महामुनीनाम्<BR> K. 43; Ms. 8. 271; R. 7. 41, 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामग्राहम्
नामन् + -ग्राहम् <i>ind.</i> by naming, by mentioning the name; नामग्राहमरोदीत्<BR> सा भ्रातरौ रावणान्तिके Bk. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामत्यागः
नामन् + -त्यागः abandonment of name; स्वनामत्यागं करोमि Pt. 1 ‘I shall forego my name’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामद्वादशी
नामन् + -द्वादशी a kind of religious ceremony, the worship of Durgā daily<BR> under one of her 12 names, <i>i. e.</i> गौरी, काली, उमा, भद्रा, दुर्गा,<BR> कान्ति, सरस्वती, मङ्गला, वैष्णवी, लक्ष्मी, शिवा and नारायणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधातुः|नामधातु
नामन् + -धातुः a nominal verb, denominative base (as पार्थायते, वृषस्यति &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधारक
नामन् + -धारक, -धारिन् <i>a.</i> bearing only the name, in name only, nominal;<BR> (तथा) अर्थेन विहीनोऽत्र पुरुषो नामधारकः Pt. 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधारिन्
नामन् + -धारक, -धारिन् <i>a.</i> bearing only the name, in name only, nominal;<BR> (तथा) अर्थेन विहीनोऽत्र पुरुषो नामधारकः Pt. 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेयम्
नामन् + -धेयम्<BR>—1 a name, appellation; वनज्योत्स्नेति कृतनामधेया Ś. 1; किं नामधेया<BR> सा M. 4; R. 1. 45, 10. 67, 11. 8; नामधेयस्य ये केचिदभिवादं न<BR> जानते Ms. 2. 123.<BR>—2 the ceremony of naming a child. ˚शब्दः a word or an expression<BR> which forms the name of a thing or an act; चोदकाच्च नामधेयशब्दो बलवत्तरः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामनाभिकः
नामन् + -नाभिकः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामनिर्देशः|नामनिर्देश
नामन् + -निर्देशः indication by name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममात्र
नामन् + -मात्र <i>a.</i> having only the name, nominal, in name; काचे मणिर्मणौ<BR> काचो येषां बुद्धिः प्रवर्तते । न तेषां सन्निधौ भृत्यो नाममात्रोऽपि तिष्ठति ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 77, 2. 86.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">Page0889-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममात्रम्
नामन् + -मात्र + .({@-त्रम्@}) the mere name or mention (of a thing); नाममात्रप्रस्तावो<BR> मे विषादाय कल्पते Ś. 7; Pt. 3. 81; H. 1. 128; नाममात्रावशेषिताः<BR> शत्रवः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0888-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममाला
नामन् + -माला, -संग्रहः a list of names, glossary (of nouns).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामसंग्रहः|नामसङ्ग्रह
नामन् + -माला, -संग्रहः a list of names, glossary (of nouns).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममुद्रा
नामन् + -मुद्रा a seal-ring, signet-ring; उभे नाममुद्राक्षराण्यनुवाच्य<BR> परस्परमवलोकयतः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामलिङ्गम्
नामन् + -लिङ्गम् gender of nouns. ˚अनुशासनम् rules on the gender of nouns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामवर्जित
नामन् + -वर्जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 nameless.<BR>—2 stupid, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामवाचक
नामन् + -वाचक <i>a.</i> expressing a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामवाचकम्
नामन् + -वाचक + .({@-कम्@}) a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामशेष|नामशेषः
नामन् + -शेष <i>a.</i> having only the name left, remaining in name only,<BR> dead, deceased; त्वां नामशेषामपि दृश्यमानः U. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामशेषः|नामशेष
नामन् + -शेषः death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामक
नामक (At the end of adj. comp.) = नामन्; as कृतनामक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामतः
नामतः <i>ind.</i> By name, namely; तन्नामतोऽन्यद्वपवहारमूलम्<BR> Bhāg. 5. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधः|नामध
नामधः, -धा <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR> A name-giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधा
नामधः, -धा <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR> A name-giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधा
नामधा <i>ind.</i> By name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिक
नामिक <i>a.</i> Relating to a name or a noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिः|नामि
नामिः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामित
नामित <i>a.</i> Bent, bowed down &c.; नामितं नु गगनं स्थगितं<BR> नु Ki. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम्य
नाम्य <i>a.</i> Pliable, flexible, pliant; क्षत्रियेण धनुर्नाम्यम् Mb. 8. 55. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायः|नाय
नायः [नी-कर्तरि ण]<BR>—1 A leader, guide.<BR>—2 Guiding, directing.<BR>—3 Policy, prudence; यात यूयं यमश्रायं दिशं नायेन दक्षिणाम् Bk. 7. 36.<BR>—4 Means, expedient; नायः कोऽत्र स येन स्यां बताहं विगतज्वरः Bk. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक <i>a.</i> [नी-ण्वुल्] Guiding, leading, conducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकः|नायक
नायक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A guide, leader, conductor.<BR>—2 A chief, master, head, lord.<BR>—3 A pre-eminent or principal person, distinguished personage; सैन्यनायकः &c.<BR>—4 A general, commander.<BR>—5 (In Rhet.) The hero of a poetic composition (a play or drama); (according<BR> to S. D. there are four main kinds of नायक:− धीरोदात्त, धीरोद्धत,<BR> धीरललित, and धीरप्रशान्त, q. v.; these are again subdivided,<BR> the total number of kinds being 48; see S. D. 64-75. The Rasamañjarī<BR> mentions 3 classes पति, उपपति and वैशिक; 95. 110).<BR>—6 The central gem of a necklace; ‘नायको नेतरि श्रेष्ठे हारमध्यमणावपि’ इति विश्वः.<BR>—7 A paradigm or leading example; दशैते स्त्रीषु नायकाः.<BR>—8 An epithet of Śākyamuni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नायकाधिपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकाधिपः|नायकाधिप
नायक + -अधिपः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकायते
नायकायते Denom. Ā.<BR>—1 To play the part of a leader.<BR>—2 To act the part of the central gem of a necklace; एकार्थतनुप्रोतायां<BR> नायको नायकायते Śi. 2. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायिका
नायिका<BR>—1 A mistress.<BR>—2 A wife.<BR>—3 The heroine of a poetic composition. (According to S. D. a नायिका<BR> is of three kinds स्वा or स्वीया, अन्या or परकीया, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">Page0889-2</a>]<BR> साधारणस्त्री. For further classification, see S. D. 97-112, and Rasamañjarī 3-94;<BR> cf. अन्यस्त्री also).<BR>—4 A kind of musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [नरस्येदम्-अण्]<BR>—1 Human, mortal.<BR>—2 Spiritual; आपो नारा इति प्रोक्ताः Ms. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारः|नार|नारं
नार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A calf.<BR>—2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारा
नार + .{@-रा@} Water; cf. Ms. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारम्
नार + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A multitude or assemblage of men.<BR>—2 Dry ginger.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नारकीटः, नारजीवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीटः|नारकीट
नार + -कीटः a deceiver (disappointing expectations raised by himself).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारजीवनम्
नार + -जीवनम् gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [नरक एव प्रज्ञा˚ अण् नरकस्येदम् अण् वा] Hellish,<BR> relating to hell, infernal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकः|नारक
नारक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The infernal regions, hell; कुभ्मीपाकं गुरुमपि हरे नारकं नापनेतुम्<BR> Mukunda-mālā 6.<BR>—2 An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिक
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय <i>a.</i> Hellish. ━<i>m.</i> An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय <i>a.</i> Hellish. ━<i>m.</i> An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीय
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय <i>a.</i> Hellish. ━<i>m.</i> An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्गः|नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारंगः
नारङ्गः<BR>—1 The orange tree.<BR>—2 A lecher, libertine.<BR>—3 A living being.<BR>—4 A twin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्गम्
नारङ्गः + .{@-ङ्गम्, -ङ्गकम्@}<BR>—1 The fruit of the orange tree; सद्योमुण्डितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि नारङ्गकम्.<BR>—2 A carrot.<BR>—3 The juice of the pepper plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरङ्गकम्
नारङ्गः + .{@-ङ्गम्, -ङ्गकम्@}<BR>—1 The fruit of the orange tree; सद्योमुण्डितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि नारङ्गकम्.<BR>—2 A carrot.<BR>—3 The juice of the pepper plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदः|नारद
नारदः [नरस्य धर्मो नारं, तत् ददाति दा-क] N. of a celebrated<BR> <i>Devarṣi</i> (deified saint or divine sage). [He is one of the ten mind-born<BR> sons of Brahmā, being supposed to have sprung from his thigh (Ms. 1. 35).<BR> He is represented as a messenger from the gods to men and <i>vice versa</i><BR> and as being very fond of promoting discords among gods and men; hence<BR> his epithet of <i>Kalipriya</i>. He is said to have been the inventor of<BR> the lute or Vīṇā. He is also the author of a code of laws which goes by his name.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नारदोपनिषद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदोपनिषद्
नारदः + -उपनिषद् N. of a Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंह|नारसिंहः
नारसिंह <i>a.</i> (-ही <i>f.</i>)<BR> Pertaining to Narasimha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंहः|नारसिंह
नारसिंह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 The 16th period of the world (कल्प).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नारसिंहचूर्णम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंहचूर्णम्
नारसिंह + -चूर्णम् N. of a particular aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराचः|नाराच
नाराचः [नरान् आचामति आ-चम्-ड स्वार्थे अण्, नारम् आचामति वा Tv.]<BR>—1 An iron arrow; तत्र नाराचदुर्दिनम् R. 4. 41.<BR>—2 An arrow in general; सर्वलोहास्तु ये बाणाः नाराचास्ते प्रकीर्तिताः ।<BR> पञ्चभिः पृथुलैः पक्षैर्युक्ताः सिध्यन्ति कस्यचित् ॥ Dhanur. 73; Rām. 3. 25. 25;<BR> कनकनाराचपरंपराभिरिव K. 57.<BR>—3 Water-elephant.<BR>—4 A road running towards the east; Kāmikāgama 25. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराचिका
नाराचिका, नाराची A goldsmithʼs scales (assay balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराची
नाराचिका, नाराची A goldsmithʼs scales (assay balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणः|नारायण
नारायणः —1 An epithet of Viṣṇu; (the word is thus derived in Ms. 1. 10;<BR> आपो नारा इति प्रोक्ता आपो वै नरसूनवः । ता यदस्यायनं पूर्वं<BR> तेन नारायणः स्मृतः ॥) नारायणं नमस्कृत्य … … ततो जयमुदीरयेत्<BR> Mb. 1. 1. 1; नीरे नीरचरैः समं स भगवान् निद्राति नारायणः Jag.<BR>—2 N. of an ancient sage said to be a companion of <i>Nara</i> and to have<BR> produced Urvaśī from his thigh; cf. ऊरूद्भवा नरसखस्य मुनेः सुरस्त्री<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">Page0890-1</a>]<BR> V. 1. 3; see नरनारायण under नर also.<BR>—3 N. of the second month (reckoning from मार्गशीर्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणी
नारायणः + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Lakṣmī the goddess of wealth.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—3 An epithet of Gaṅgā and Gaṇḍakī.<BR>—4 N. of a plant (Mar. शतावरी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नारायणास्त्रम्, नारायणोपनिषद्, नारायणप्रियः, नारायणबलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0889-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणास्त्रम्
नारायणः + -अस्त्रम् N. of a missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणोपनिषद्
नारायणः + -उपनिषद् N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणप्रियः|नारायणप्रिय
नारायणः + -प्रियः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 yellow sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणबलिः|नारायणबलि
नारायणः + -बलिः an oblation given to five deities including नारायण<BR> in performing the funeral rites of a person dying a sinful death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिक
नारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Watery, aqueous.<BR>—2 Spiritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेरः|नारिकेर
नारिकेरः, -लः<BR> The cocoa-nut; नारिकेलसमाकारा दृश्यन्ते हि सुहृज्जनाः<BR> H. 1. 90. [The word is also written नारिकेलि, -ली, नारिकेर, -ल, नारीकेलि, -ली,<BR> नाडि(डी)केर, नालिकेर (Bhāg. 8. 2. 11), नालिकेलि, -ली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेलः|नारिकेल
नारिकेरः, -लः<BR> The cocoa-nut; नारिकेलसमाकारा दृश्यन्ते हि सुहृज्जनाः<BR> H. 1. 90. [The word is also written नारिकेलि, -ली, नारिकेर, -ल, नारीकेलि, -ली,<BR> नाडि(डी)केर, नालिकेर (Bhāg. 8. 2. 11), नालिकेलि, -ली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङरिकेली
नारिकेरः, -लः + .{@-ली@} Fermented liquor made from the water of the cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी [नॄ-नर-वा जातौ ङीष् नि˚]<BR>—1 A woman; अर्थतः पुरुषो नारी या नारी सार्थतः पुमान् Mk. 3. 27.<BR>—2 Any female or feminine object.<BR>—3 Sacrifice.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नारीष्टा, नारीतरङ्गकः, नारीदूषणम्, नारीनाथ, नारीपरायण, नारीपुरम्, नारीप्रसंगः, नारीरत्नम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीष्टा
नारी + -इष्टा Arabian Jasmin (Mar. मोगरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीतरङ्गकः|नारीतरङ्गक|नारीतरंगक
नारी + -तरङ्गकः<BR>—1 a paramour.<BR>—2 a libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीदूषणम्
नारी + -दूषणम् a womanʼs vice: (they are:− पानं दुर्जनसंसर्गः<BR> पत्या च विरहोऽटनम् । स्वप्नोऽन्यगृहवासश्च नारीणां दूषणानि षट् Ms. 9. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीनाथ
नारी + -नाथ <i>a.</i> having a woman for possessor or owner; क्वचिदपि<BR> गृहं नारीनाथं निरीक्ष्य विवर्जिंतम् Mk. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीपरायण
नारी + -परायण <i>a.</i> devoted to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीपुरम्
नारी + -पुरम् womenʼs apartment in house, gynaeceum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीप्रसंगः|नारीप्रसङ्ग|नारीप्रसंग
नारी + -प्रसंगः lechery, libertinism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीरत्नम्
नारी + -रत्नम् a jewel of a woman, an excellent woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकम्
नारीकम् (in Sāṅkhya) One of the 9 kinds of तुष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्पत्य
नार्पत्य <i>a.</i> Kingly, relating to royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्पयति
नार्पयति [न + अर्पयति] To surrender to the king (<i>i. e.</i><BR> property); N. 5. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मद
नार्मद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to the river Narmadā.<BR>—2 A class of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0890-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

