नासिरम्
नासिरम्, -नासीरम्<BR> [नासाय ईर्ते ईर्-क Tv.] Advancing or fighting in<BR> front of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासीरम्
नासिरम्, -नासीरम्<BR> [नासाय ईर्ते ईर्-क Tv.] Advancing or fighting in<BR> front of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिरः|नासिर
नासिरम्, -नासीरम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The van or front (of an army &c.); नासीरचरयोर्भटयोः Mv. 6;<BR> N. 1. 68. नासीरस्थानपि तया पताकाभिरलङ्कृतान् Parṇāl.<BR>—2 A champion who advances before the line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्ति
नास्ति <i>ind.</i> ‘It is not’, non-existence, as in नास्तिक्षीरा &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नास्तिवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिवादः|नास्तिवाद
नास्ति + -वादः assertion of the non-existence of God or a Supreme Ruler,<BR> atheism, infidelity; बौद्धेनेव सर्वदा नास्तिवादशूरेण K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक|नास्तिकः
नास्तिक <i>a.</i> (-कः)<BR> [नास्ति परलोकस्तत्साधनमदृष्टं तत्साक्षीश्वरो वा इति<BR> मतिरस्य ठन्] An atheist, unbeliever, one who denies the authority<BR> of the Vedas and a future life or the existence of a Supreme Ruler or Creator<BR> of the Universe; अतिमात्रोज्झितभीरनास्तिकः Śi. 16. 7; Ms. 2. 11, 8. 22.<BR> नासाचूर्णे नास्ति कस्याभिलाषः नासाचूर्णे नास्तिकस्याभिलाषः Subhāṣ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नास्तिकमतम्, नास्तिकवृत्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिकमतम्
नास्तिक + -मतम् an atheistical opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिकवृत्ति
नास्तिक + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> leading the life of an atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक्यम्
नास्तिक्यम् Atheism, infidelity, heresy; नास्तिक्यं तु प्रभाषसे Mb. 3. 31. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिदः|नास्तिद
नास्तिदः The mango-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0891-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहः|नाह
