निःसीमन्
निःसीमन् <i>a.</i> Unbounded, immeasurable, grand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0892-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृ
निःसृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To come forth, slip away from, go out, issue from; बाणैः खरकार्मुकनिःसृतैः<BR> Rām.; Śi. 9. 25.<BR>—2 To depart, set out for; ग्रामादरण्यं निःसृत्य निवसेन्नियतेन्द्रियः Ms. 6. 4.<BR>—3 To flow forth, ooze out, exude; यो हेमकुम्भस्तननिःसृतानाम् R. 2. 36.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To turn out, expel, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0892-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरणम्
निःसरणम्<BR>—1 Going out, exit.<BR>—2 An egress or outlet from a house, a gate.<BR>—3 Final departure, death.<BR>—4 A means, expedient, remedy.<BR>—5 Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0892-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारः|निःसार
