निकाम + .{@-मः, -मम्@} Wish, desire; हातुं प्रचक्रमे राजा तां पुरीमनिकामतः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 28. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामम्
निकाम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to oneʼs wish or desire, agreeably to desire.<BR>—2 To oneʼs satisfaction, to the heartʼs content; रात्रौ निकामं शयितव्यमपि<BR> नास्ति Ś. 2 ‘I cannot even sleep at ease or comfortably at night’.<BR>—3 Very much, exceedingly; निकामं क्षामाङ्गी Māl. 2. 3; often used<BR> as the first member of comp. when it loses its final म्; निकामनिरङ्कुशः<BR> Gīt. 7; Ku. 5. 23; Śi. 4. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामनम्
निकामनम् Desire, longing after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकरः|निकर
निकरः [निकॄ भावादौ अप्]<BR>—1 A heap, pile.<BR>—2 A flock, multitude, collection; पपात स्वेदाम्बुप्रसर इव हर्षाश्रुनिकरः<BR> Gīt. 11; Śi. 4. 58; Ṛs. 6. 18.<BR>—3 A bundle.<BR>—4 Sap, pith, essence.<BR>—5 A suitable gift, honorarium.<BR>—6 A treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्तनम्
निकर्तनम् See under निकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षण|निकर्षणं
निकर्षण See under निकृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषः|निकष
निकषः (-सः)<BR>—1 A touch-stone, whet-stone; निकषे हेमरेखेव R. 17. 46; Mv. 1. 4.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Anything serving as a touch-stone, a test; नन्वेष दर्पनिकषस्तव<BR> चन्द्रकेतुः U. 5. 10; आदर्शः शिक्षितानां सुचरितनिकषः Mk. 1. 48;<BR> Dk. 1; K. 44.<BR>—3 A streak or line of gold made on a touchstone; कनकनिकषरुचिशुचिवसनेन<BR> श्वसिति न सा परिजनहसनेन Gīt. 7. 6; कनकनिकषस्निग्धा विद्युत् प्रिया न ममोर्वशी V. 4. 1, 5. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकषोपलः, निकषग्रावन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकसः|निकस
निकषः (-सः)<BR>—1 A touch-stone, whet-stone; निकषे हेमरेखेव R. 17. 46; Mv. 1. 4.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Anything serving as a touch-stone, a test; नन्वेष दर्पनिकषस्तव<BR> चन्द्रकेतुः U. 5. 10; आदर्शः शिक्षितानां सुचरितनिकषः Mk. 1. 48;<BR> Dk. 1; K. 44.<BR>—3 A streak or line of gold made on a touchstone; कनकनिकषरुचिशुचिवसनेन<BR> श्वसिति न सा परिजनहसनेन Gīt. 7. 6; कनकनिकषस्निग्धा विद्युत् प्रिया न ममोर्वशी V. 4. 1, 5. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकषोपलः, निकषग्रावन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषोपलः|निकषोपल
निकषः + -उपलः, -ग्रावन् <i>m.</i>, {@-पाषाणः@}<BR> a touch-stone, whetstone; तत्प्रेमहेमनिकषोपलतां<BR> तनोति Gīt. 11; तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु तेषां विपद् H. 1. 183, 2. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषग्रावन्
निकषः + -उपलः, -ग्रावन् <i>m.</i>, {@-पाषाणः@}<BR> a touch-stone, whetstone; तत्प्रेमहेमनिकषोपलतां<BR> तनोति Gīt. 11; तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु तेषां विपद् H. 1. 183, 2. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषणः|निकषण
निकषणः (-णम्)<BR>—1 the touch-stone; य एकः शूराणां गुरुसमरकण्डूनिकषणः Ve. 3. 16.<BR>—2 Rubbing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषणम्
निकषणः (-णम्)<BR>—1 the touch-stone; य एकः शूराणां गुरुसमरकण्डूनिकषणः Ve. 3. 16.<BR>—2 Rubbing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषा
निकषा N. of the mother of Rāvaṇa or of imps in general. ━<i>ind.</i><BR> Near, hard, close by, at hand (with acc.); निकषा सौधभित्तिम् Dk.;<BR> विलङ्घ्य लङ्कां निकषा हनिष्यति Śi. 1. 68.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकषात्मजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषात्मजः|निकषात्मज
निकषा + -आत्मजः a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकायः|निकाय
निकायः [नि-चि-घञ् कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 A heap, an assemblage, a class, multitude, flock, group in general;<BR> Mv. 1. निकाय इति सङ्घात् औत्तराधर्येणावस्थित उच्यते । ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 19;<BR> तप्तहेमनिकायाभं शितिकण्ठं त्रिलोचनम् (वीक्ष्य) Bhāg. 4. 24. 25.<BR>—2 A congregation, school, an association of persons who perform like duties.<BR>—3 A house, habitation dwelling-place; Ms. 1. 36; काशीनिकायः &c.<BR>—4 The body.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">Page0893-2</a>]<BR>—5 Aim, butt, mark.<BR>—6 The Supreme Being.<BR>—7 Ved. Air, wind; Vāj. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकायिन्
निकायिन् <i>m.</i> (pl.) Serial sacrifices; निकायः एषां ते निकायिनः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 19; निकायिनां च पूर्वस्योत्तरेषु प्रवृत्तिः स्यात् MS. 8. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय्यः|निकाय्य
निकाय्यः [cf. P. III. 1. 129] A dwelling, habitation, house; न<BR> प्रणाय्यो जनः कच्चिन्निकाय्यं तेऽधितिष्ठति Bk. 6. 66; cf. पाय्यसान्नाय्यनिकाय्यधाय्याः<BR> मानहविर्निवाससामिधेनीषु P. III. 1. 29 quoted in ŚB. on MS. 5. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
निकार &c. See under निकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाशः|निकाश
निकाशः, -सः<BR> [नि-काश्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Appearance, sight.<BR>—2 Horizon.<BR>—3 Proximity, vicinity; प्रत्येष्यतं निकाशं मे कालेनाल्पीयसा पुनः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 16. 31.<BR>—4 Likeness, resemblance (at the end of comp.); क्वचिन्मणिनिकाशोदाम्<BR> (नदीम्) Rām. 2. 95. 10; Māl. 5. 13.<BR>—5 light.<BR>—6 secret; निकाशस्तु प्रकाशे स्यात् सदृशे रहसि स्मृतः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकासः|निकास
निकाशः, -सः<BR> [नि-काश्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Appearance, sight.<BR>—2 Horizon.<BR>—3 Proximity, vicinity; प्रत्येष्यतं निकाशं मे कालेनाल्पीयसा पुनः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 16. 31.<BR>—4 Likeness, resemblance (at the end of comp.); क्वचिन्मणिनिकाशोदाम्<BR> (नदीम्) Rām. 2. 95. 10; Māl. 5. 13.<BR>—5 light.<BR>—6 secret; निकाशस्तु प्रकाशे स्यात् सदृशे रहसि स्मृतः Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाषः|निकाष
निकाषः Scratching, rubbing; कनकनिकाषराजिगौरैः Ki. 7. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चनः|निकुञ्चन|निकुंचन|निकुंचनः
निकुञ्चनः A measure of capacity equal to ¼ of a <i>Kudava</i> (also<BR> निकुञ्चक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्जः|निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुंजं|निकुञ्जं|निकुंजः
निकुञ्जः, -जम्<BR>—1 A bower, an arbour, a place overgrown with shrubs and creepers; यमुनातीरवानीरनिकुञ्जे<BR> मन्दमास्थितम् Gīt. 4. 2, 11; Ṛs. 1. 23.<BR>—2 A vault; दधानः सौधानामलघुषु निकुञ्जेषु घनताम् Māl. 2. 12.<BR>—3 A cavern; पर्यन्तभूधरनिकुञ्जविजृम्भमाणः Māl. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्जम्
निकुञ्जः, -जम्<BR>—1 A bower, an arbour, a place overgrown with shrubs and creepers; यमुनातीरवानीरनिकुञ्जे<BR> मन्दमास्थितम् Gīt. 4. 2, 11; Ṛs. 1. 23.<BR>—2 A vault; दधानः सौधानामलघुषु निकुञ्जेषु घनताम् Māl. 2. 12.<BR>—3 A cavern; पर्यन्तभूधरनिकुञ्जविजृम्भमाणः Māl. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भः|निकुम्भ|निकुंभ|निकुंभः
निकुम्भः<BR>—1 N. of an attendant of Śiva; R. 2. 35.<BR>—2 N. of the father of Sunda and Upasunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भिला|निकुंभिला
निकुम्भिला<BR>—1 A cave or grove at the western gate of Laṅkā.<BR>—2 An image of Bhadrakālī on the west side of Laṅkā.<BR>—3 A place where oblations are offered; ध्रुवं स मोहयित्वाऽस्मान् पापोऽगच्छन्निकुम्भिलाम् Bk. 17. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरम्बम्
निकुर(रु)म्बम् A flock, collection, mass, multitude; लतानिकुरुम्बम्<BR> Gīt. 11. किरण˚ Ā. L. 20; चिकुर˚ 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरुम्बम्
निकुर(रु)म्बम् A flock, collection, mass, multitude; लतानिकुरुम्बम्<BR> Gīt. 11. किरण˚ Ā. L. 20; चिकुर˚ 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुलीनिका
निकुलीनिका A family art, one inherited by birth, any skill or art<BR> peculiar to a race. See निपात; Mb. 8. 41. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृ
निकृ €8 U. Ved.<BR>—1 To humiliate, subdue, overcome.<BR>—2 To maltreat, act or treat ill.<BR>—3 To injure, wrong, offend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारः|निकार
निकारः<BR>—1 Winnowing corn.<BR>—2 Lifting up.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—4 Humiliation, subjugation.<BR>—5 Insult, injury, wrong, offence; तीर्णो निकारार्णवः Ve. 6. 43; Mv. 3. 41, 5. 14, 7. 8;<BR> Ki. 1. 43, 3. 44.<BR>—6 Abuse, reproach, disrespect.<BR>—7 Wickedness, malice; अलमङ्ग निकारोऽयम् Mb. 5. 129. 47.<BR>—8 Opposition, contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारणम्
निकारणम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0893-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत|निकृतः
निकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Humbled, cast down, humiliated; अस्माभिर्ह्येष निकृतः Mb. 4. 49. 18.<BR>—2 Insulted, offended; किमाग्नेयो ग्रावा निकृत इव तेजांसि वमति U. 6. 14.<BR>—3 Deceived, cheated; एकदाऽसत्प्रसङ्गगान्निकृतमतिः Bhāg. 5. 14. 13.<BR>—4 Removed.<BR>—5 Afflicted, injured.<BR>—6 Wicked, dishonest.<BR>—7 Base, low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतम्
निकृत + .{@-तम्@} Humiliation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकृतप्रज्ञ, निकृतमति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतप्रज्ञ
निकृत + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> evil-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतमति
निकृत + -मति <i>a.</i> depraved in mind, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृति|निकृतिः
निकृति <i>a.</i> Base, dishonest, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतिः|निकृति
निकृति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Baseness, wickedness.<BR>—2 Dishonesty, fraud, deception; अनिकृतिनिपुणं ते चेष्टितं मानशौण्ड<BR> Ve. 5. 21; Ki. 1. 45. अयं कौमारमारभ्य निकृतिप्रकृतिः स्वयम् Śiva B. 17. 21;<BR> अन्तर्गतगुरुनिकृतिः 17. 26.<BR>—3 Insult, offence, humiliation; स्वाग्रासनापनयनान्निकृतिर्न सोढा Mu. 4. 11.<BR>—4 A buse, reproach.<BR>—5 Rejection, removal.<BR>—6 Poverty, indigence.<BR>—7 The earth.<BR>—8 N. of one of the eight Vasus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकृतिप्रज्ञ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतिप्रज्ञ
निकृति + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> evil minded, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतिन्
निकृतिन् <i>a.</i> Base, dishonest, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्
निकृत् €6 P.<BR>—1 To cut down, cut to pieces, cut or tear off, tear up; विश्वासाद्भयमुत्पन्नं<BR> मूलान्यपि निकृन्तति Pt. 2. 39; निकृन्तन्निव मानसम् Bk. 7. 11; भल्लनिकृत्तकण्ठैः R. 7. 58.<BR>—2 To cut oneself (Ā.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्तनम्
निकर्तनम्<BR>—1 Cutting down or off, tearing; निकर्तनमिवात्युग्रं लाङ्गूलस्य महाहरिः<BR> Mb. 7. 170. 25.<BR>—2 Annihilation, wiping out completely; उत्सादनममित्राणां परसेनानिकर्तनम्<BR> Mb. 3. 167. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृन्तन|निकृंतन
निकृन्तन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Cutting down, destroying; विरहिनिकृन्तनकुन्तमुखाकृतिकेतकिदन्तुरिताशे<BR> (वसन्ते) Gīt. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृन्तनम्
निकृन्तन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Cutting, cutting off, destruction.<BR>—2 An instrument for cutting; एकेन नखनिकृन्तनेन सर्वं कार्ष्णायसं<BR> विज्ञातं स्यात् Ś. B.<BR>—3 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्
निकृष् €1. €6 P.<BR>—1 To lessen, diminish.<BR>—2 To draw or drag down, pull down; (मौर्यनृपस्य लक्ष्मीं) निकृष्यमाणामिव<BR> लक्षयामि Mu. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षणम्
निकर्षणम्<BR>—1 An open space for recreation, or a playground in or near a town.<BR>—2 A court at the entrance of a house.<BR>—3 Neighbourhood.<BR>—4 An uncultivated or unploughed plot of ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्ट|निकृष्टः
निकृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Low, base, vile.<BR>—2 Out-cast, despised.<BR>—3 Vulgar.<BR>—4 Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्टम्
निकृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Proximity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निकृष्टयुद्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्टयुद्धम्
निकृष्ट + -युद्धम् Hand to hand fight, close fight; निकृष्टयुद्धं संसक्तं<BR> महदासीत्सुदारुणम् Mb. 7. 187. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेचायः|निकेचाय
निकेचायः Piling or collecting repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतः|निकेत
निकेतः, -तकः<BR>—1 A house, habitation, mansion, abode; श्रितगोकर्णनिकेतमीश्वरम्<BR> R. 8. 33, 14. 58; Bg. 12. 19; Ku. 5. 25; Ms. 6. 26; Śi. 5. 26.<BR>—2 A mark, counter-sign.<BR>—3 A stage in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतकः|निकेतक
निकेतः, -तकः<BR>—1 A house, habitation, mansion, abode; श्रितगोकर्णनिकेतमीश्वरम्<BR> R. 8. 33, 14. 58; Bg. 12. 19; Ku. 5. 25; Ms. 6. 26; Śi. 5. 26.<BR>—2 A mark, counter-sign.<BR>—3 A stage in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतनः|निकेतन|निकेतनं
निकेतनः An onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतनम्
निकेतनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A mansion, house, abode; सिञ्जाना मञ्जुमञ्जीरं प्रविवेश निकेतनम्<BR> Gīt. 11: Ms. 6. 26, 11. 129; Ki. 1. 16.<BR>—2 A temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोचनम्
निकोचनम् Contraction, compression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रन्दित
निक्रन्दित <i>a.</i> Cried, roared (said of a faulty recitation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रमणम्
निक्रमणम् Ved.<BR>—1 Trampling down.<BR>—2 A foot-step, foot-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वणः|निक्वण
निक्वणः, निक्वाणः<BR>—1 A musical tone or sound.<BR>—2 A sound in general. विहितालिनिक्वणजयध्वनयः Ki. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वाणः|निक्वाण
निक्वणः, निक्वाणः<BR>—1 A musical tone or sound.<BR>—2 A sound in general. विहितालिनिक्वणजयध्वनयः Ki. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्ष्
निक्ष् €1 P. (निक्षति) Ved.<BR>—1 To pierce.<BR>—2 To kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षणम्
निक्षणम् Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षा
निक्षा A nit (a wrong form for लिक्षा q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्
निक्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To throw or cast down, put or place down; अन्नं भूमौ श्वचाण्डालवायसेभ्यश्च<BR> निक्षिपेत् Y. 1. 103; Amaru. 80.<BR>—2 To entrust, commit, consign to the care of; देवीहस्ते निक्षिपता<BR> Ratn. 1; Ms. 6. 3, 8. 179; R. 1. 34.<BR>—3 To deposit, place as deposit.<BR>—4 To encamp.<BR>—5 To cast off, reject.<BR>—6 To give or hand over, grant, bestow (on).<BR>—7 To install, appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्त|निक्षिप्तं
निक्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or put down, thrown into.<BR>—2 Deposited, pledged, pawned.<BR>—3 Sent, sent off.<BR>—4 Rejected, abandoned.<BR>—5 Appointed, installed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपः|निक्षेप
निक्षेपः<BR>—1 Throwing or casting on (with acc.); अलं मान्यानां व्याख्यानेषु कटाक्षनिक्षेपेण S. D. 2.<BR>—2 A deposit, pledge, pawn in general; निक्षेपे पतिते हर्म्ये श्रेष्ठी<BR> स्तौति स्वदेवताम् । निक्षेपी म्रियते तुभ्यं प्रदास्याम्युपयाचितम् ॥ Pt. 1. 14;<BR> Ms. 8. 4.<BR>—3 Anything deposited without a seal in trust or as a compensation, an<BR> open deposit; समक्षं तु निक्षेपणं निक्षेपः Mit. on Y. 2. 67.<BR>—4 Sending away.<BR>—5 Throwing away, abandoning.<BR>—6 Wiping, drying.<BR>—7 Treasure-trove; निक्षेपस्वर्णसंपूर्णकटाहजठरां धराम् Śiva B. 30. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निक्षेपलिपिः, निक्षेपवणिक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपलिपिः|निक्षेपलिपि
निक्षेपः + -लिपिः A particular mode of writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपवणिक्
निक्षेपः + -वणिक् a merchant with whom goods are left in deposit N. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपणम्
निक्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Putting down, placing down (the feet); Ku. 1. 33.<BR>—2 A means by which anything is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपित
निक्षेपित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Caused to be put down in writing, inscribed.<BR>—2 Caused to be deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्तृ
निक्षेप्तृ <i>m.</i> A depositor, pawner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षुभा
निक्षुभा<BR>—1 The wife of the sun.<BR>—2 A female Brāhmaṇa (ब्राह्मणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखन्
निखन् €1 P.<BR>—1 To dig, dig up.<BR>—2 To bury, inter; ऊनद्विवर्षं निखनेत् Y. 3. 1; वसुधायां निचख्नतुः<BR> R. 12. 30; Bk. 4. 3, 16. 22.<BR>—3 To erect (as a column); निचखान जयस्तम्भान् R. 4. 36.<BR>—4 To implant, infix, pierce into; निचखान शरं भुजे R. 12. 90, 3. 55;<BR> Bk. 3. 8; H. 4. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखननम्
निखननम् Digging in, burying; as in स्थूणानिखननन्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखात
निखात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dug up, excavated.<BR>—2 Fixed, planted (as a stake), infixed; शल्यं निखातमुदहारयतामुरस्तः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">Page0895-1</a>]<BR> R. 9. 78, 13. 61; अष्टादशद्वीपनिखातयूपः 6. 38; गाढं निखात इव<BR> मे हृदये कटाक्षः Māl. 1. 29.<BR>—3 Dug in, buried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0894-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्व|निखर्व्व
निखर्व <i>a.</i> Dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्वम्
निखर्व + .{@-र्वम्@} A trillion (अब्ज); तत्राङ्गुष्ठेन राजेन्द्र निखर्वमपरं<BR> ततः Mb. 12. 258. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिल|निखिलं
निखिल <i>a.</i> [निवृत्तं खिलं शेषो यस्मात्] Complete, whole, entire,<BR> all; प्रत्यक्षं ते निखिलमचिराद् भ्रातरुक्तं मया यत् Me. 96; सूर्यांशुभिर्जगदिदं<BR> निखिलार्थमेति Bil. C. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिलेन
निखिल + .{@-लेन@} <i>ind.</i> completely, totally; निखिलेन विचिन्वन्तौ सीतां<BR> दशरथात्मजौ Rām. 3. 61. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगड|निगडः
निगड <i>a.</i> [नि-गल्-अच् लस्य डः] Fettered, chained; बद्धस्य<BR> निगडस्य च Ms. 4. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडः|निगड
निगड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 An iron chain for the feet of an elephant; बद्धापराणिं परितो निगडान्यलावीत्<BR> Śi. 5. 48; Bv. 4. 20; निबद्धनिगडालाननियन्त्रितमदद्विपम् Śiva B. 20. 52.<BR>—2 A fetter, chain or shackle in general; देवकीं वसुदेवं च निगृह्य<BR> निगडैर्गृहे Bhāg. 10. 1. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडम्
निगड + .{@-डः, -डम्@}<BR>—1 An iron chain for the feet of an elephant; बद्धापराणिं परितो निगडान्यलावीत्<BR> Śi. 5. 48; Bv. 4. 20; निबद्धनिगडालाननियन्त्रितमदद्विपम् Śiva B. 20. 52.<BR>—2 A fetter, chain or shackle in general; देवकीं वसुदेवं च निगृह्य<BR> निगडैर्गृहे Bhāg. 10. 1. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडनम्
निगडनम् Chaining, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडयति
निगडयति Den. P. To put in chains, fetter; (fig. also); निद्रानिगडितजनदृशि Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडित|निगडितः
निगडित <i>a.</i> Fettered, put in irons, chained, bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगणः|निगण
निगणः The smoke of a sacrificial fire or burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद्
निगद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To proclaim, declare, announce; पुलकैः प्रियं नववधूर्न्यगदत् Śi. 9. 76.<BR>—2 To declare, say, speak; सिंहोरुसत्त्वं निजगाद सिंहः R. 2. 33.<BR>—3 To speak to, address (any one).<BR>—4 To enumerate.<BR>—5 To call, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदः|निगद
निगदः, निगादः<BR>—1 Recitation, audible recitation of prayers.<BR>—2 A prayer repeated aloud.<BR>—3 Speech, discourse.<BR>—4 Learning anything without knowing the meaning; यदधीतमविज्ञातं<BR> निगदेनैव शब्द्यते Nir.<BR>—5 Mention, mentioning; इति निगदेनैव व्याख्यातम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगादः|निगाद
निगदः, निगादः<BR>—1 Recitation, audible recitation of prayers.<BR>—2 A prayer repeated aloud.<BR>—3 Speech, discourse.<BR>—4 Learning anything without knowing the meaning; यदधीतमविज्ञातं<BR> निगदेनैव शब्द्यते Nir.<BR>—5 Mention, mentioning; इति निगदेनैव व्याख्यातम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदित
निगदित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Told, said, spoken.<BR>—2 Incited, urged, directed; धर्मे निगदितश्चैव पितुर्निर्देशकारकः Rām. 4. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदितम्
निगदित + .{@-तम्@} A discourse, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगादः|निगाद
निगादः Recitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम्
निगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go to, attain, acquire, obtain; यत्र दुःखान्तं च निगच्छति<BR> Bg. 18. 36, 9. 31.<BR>—2 To get knowledge, learn.<BR>—3 To be inserted. —4 To enter (with acc. or loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमः|निगम
निगमः<BR>—1 The Veda or Vedic text; साढ्यै साढ्वा साढेति निगमे P. VI. 3. 113, VII. 2. 64;<BR> निगमकल्पतरोर्गलितं फलम् Bhāg. 1. 1. 3; Māl. 9. 4;<BR> निगमशब्दो वेदवाची Sāyaṇa Bhāṣya.<BR>—2 Any passage or word quoted from the Vedas, a Vedic sentence; तथापि<BR> च निगमो भवति (often found in Nirukta).<BR>—3 A work auxiliary to, and explanatory of the Vedas; नित्यं शास्त्राण्यवेक्षेत<BR> निगमांश्चैव वैदिकान् Ms. 4. 19 and Kull. thereon.<BR>—4 A sacred precept, the words of a god or holy man.<BR>—5 A root (as the source of a word).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">Page0895-2</a>]<BR>—6 Certainty, assurance.<BR>—7 Logic or science of ethics; सर्वे च येऽन्ये धृतराष्ट्रपुत्रा बलप्रधाना<BR> निगमप्रधानाः Mb. 5. 2. 6.<BR>—8 Trade, traffic.<BR>—9 A market, fair.<BR>—10 A caravan of wandering merchants; Rām. 2. 15. 2.<BR>—11 A road, market-road.<BR>—12 A city.<BR>—13 Insertion of the name of a deity into a liturgical formula.<BR>—14 Resolution; स्वनिगममपहाय मत्प्रतिज्ञाम् Bhāg. 1. 9. 37.<BR>—15 Precept, advice; इमं स्वनिगमं ब्रह्मन्नवेत्य मदनुष्ठितम् Bhāg. 1. 5. 39.<BR>—16 Obtainment (प्राप्ति); पन्था मन्निगमः स्मृतः Bhāg. 11. 19. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमनम्
निगमनम्<BR>—1 Quotation of a word from the Veda or the word so quoted.<BR>—2 (In logic) The conclusion in a syllogism, a deduction (the fifth member<BR> of the five-membered Indian syllogism); निगमनं च प्रतिज्ञाया हेतोश्च<BR> पुनर्वचनम् ŚB. on MS. 7. 1. 12.<BR>—3 Going in or into.<BR>—4 End, conclusion; इत्येवमुपक्रम्य निगमने इदं श्रूयते । ŚB. on MS. 3. 3. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निगमनसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमनसूत्रम्
निगमनम् + -सूत्रम् The aphorism which forms the निगमन; इदं निगमनसूत्रम्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 7. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमात्
निगमात् <i>ind.</i> In short, in brief; सर्वं पृथक्त्वं निगमात्कथं<BR> वदेत् Bhāg. 10. 13. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमिन्
निगमिन् <i>a.</i> Knowing the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरः|निगर
निगरः, -रणम् &c.<BR> See under निगॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरणम्
निगरः, -रणम् &c.<BR> See under निगॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगर्ह्
निगर्ह् €10 P. To despise, disdain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगु|निगुः
निगु <i>a.</i> Pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगुः|निगु
निगु + .{@-गुः@}<BR>—1 The mind.<BR>—2 Dirt, excrement.<BR>—3 A root.<BR>—4 Painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगुप्
निगुप् To conceal. See गुप्; इच्छतीशश्च्युताचारान् दारानिव निगोपितुम् Ki. 15. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगॄ
निगॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To swallow, eat up, devour; सर्वानेव गुणानियं (द्विजिह्वावली)<BR> निगिरति श्रीखण्ड ते सुन्दरान् Bv. 1. 38.<BR>—2 To conceal, hide (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरः|निगर
निगरः, निगारः Swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगारः|निगार
निगरः, निगारः Swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरणम्
निगरणम्<BR>—1 Swallowing, devouring.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Taking up, completely absorbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरणः|निगरण|निगरणं
निगरणम् + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 The throat.<BR>—2 The smoke of a sacrificial fire or burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगलः|निगल
निग(गा)लः<BR>—1 Swallowing, devouring.<BR>—2 The throat or neck of a horse; N. 1. 58;<BR>—3 A chain; दैवप्रणामचलिता निगलाः स्वनन्ति Pratijñā. 3. 4;<BR> मया एकिकना निगलगुरुचरणेन … । Bālacharitam 1. ˚वत् <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालः|निगाल
निग(गा)लः<BR>—1 Swallowing, devouring.<BR>—2 The throat or neck of a horse; N. 1. 58;<BR>—3 A chain; दैवप्रणामचलिता निगलाः स्वनन्ति Pratijñā. 3. 4;<BR> मया एकिकना निगलगुरुचरणेन … । Bālacharitam 1. ˚वत् <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगारक
निगार(ल)क <i>a.</i> Swallowing, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालक
निगार(ल)क <i>a.</i> Swallowing, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीर्ण
निगीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Swallowed, devoured.<BR>—2 (Fig.) Completely swallowed or absorbed, hidden, concealed and hence<BR> to be supplied; उपमानेनान्तर्निगीर्णस्योपमेयस्य यदध्यवसानं सैका K. P. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निगीर्णचारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीर्णचारिन्
निगीर्ण + -चारिन् <i>a.</i> walking concealed or in disguise; Ms. 9. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढ|निगूढः
निगूढ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hidden, concealed; नलिनी निगूढसलिला च यत्र सा Śi. 13. 59.<BR>—2 Secret, private; पुरा न केनाप्यभिचोदितोऽहं वक्तुं रहस्यं परमं<BR> निगूढम् A. Rām. 1. 1. 16.<BR>—3 Mysterious, obscure.<BR>—4 Inscrutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढम्
निगूढ + .{@-ढम्@} <i>ind.</i> Secretly, privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0895-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहनम्
निगूहनम् Concealing, hiding; नाज्ञातचर्यां पश्यामि मेरोरिव निगूहनम् Mb. 3. 35. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगोजाहकः
निगोजाहकः A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रन्थनम्
निग्रन्थनम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रन्थिः|निग्रन्थि
निग्रन्थिः <i>m.</i> The cover of a book; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह्
निग्रह् €9 P.<BR>—1 To keep or hold down, keep in check.<BR>—2 To curb, restrain, suppress, control; निगृह्य शोकम् K. 25; स्वकं<BR> तेजो निगृह्य Pt. 3. 174; Bg. 2. 68; R. 5. 59, 14. 85.<BR>—3 To stop, obstruct; निगृहीतो बलाद् द्वारि Mb.<BR>—4 To punish, chastise; अधार्मिकं त्रिभिर्न्यायैर्निगृह्णीयात् प्रयत्नतः<BR> Ms. 8. 310, 9. 308.<BR>—5 To seize, catch, apprehend, lay hold of; तमार्यगृह्यं निगृहीतधेनुः R. 2. 33.<BR>—6 To close or contract (as eyes); माथुरोऽक्षिणी निगृह्य Mk. 2.<BR>—7 To subdue, conquer, overpower; प्रज्ञया निग्रहीतुं शक्यः Mu. 1, 1. 28.<BR>—8 To draw in, restrain; निगृह्यन्तामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seized, arrested.<BR>—2 Restrained, curbed, checked, subdued.<BR>—3 Attacked.<BR>—4 Defeated in argument, caught; भो निगृहीतोऽसि U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीतिः|निगृहीति
निगृहीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Restraint, check<BR>—2 Overpowering, subjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहः|निग्रह
निग्रहः<BR>—1 Keeping in check, restraint, curbing, subjection; as in इन्द्रियानिग्रह<BR> Ms. 6. 92; Y. 1. 222; Bh. 1. 66; चञ्चलं मनः … तस्याहं निग्रहं<BR> मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम् Bg. 6. 34; तस्य ता वपुषाक्षिप्ता निग्रहार्थं<BR> जजृम्भिरे Bu. C. 4. 6.<BR>—2 Suppression, obstruction, putting down; तथेन्द्रियाणां दह्यन्ते दोषाः<BR> प्राणस्य निग्रहात् Ms. 6. 71.<BR>—3 Overtaking, capturing, arresting; त्वन्निग्रहे तु वरगात्रि न मे<BR> प्रयत्नः Mk. 1. 22; Śi. 2. 88.<BR>—4 Confinement, imprisonment.<BR>—5 Defeat, overthrow, vanquishing.<BR>—6 Dispelling, destruction, removing; दिनमुखानि रविर्हिमनिग्रहैर्विमलयन्<BR> मलयं नगमत्यजत् R. 9. 25, 15. 6; Ku. 5. 53.<BR>—7 Arresting of disease, cure.<BR>—8 Punishment (opp. अनुग्रह) निग्राहानुग्रहस्य कर्ता Pt. 1; निग्रहोऽप्ययमनुग्रहीकृतः<BR> R. 11. 90, 55, 12. 52, 63.<BR>—9 Rebuke, reprimand, blame.<BR>—10 Aversion, dislike, disgust.<BR>—11 (In Nyāya phil.) A flaw in an argument, a fault in a syllogism (by<BR> which a disputant is put down in argument); cf. Mu. 5. 10.<BR>—12 A handle.<BR>—13 A limit, boundary.<BR>—14 The Supreme Being.<BR>—15 Transgressing (अतिलङ्घन); निग्रहाद्धर्मशास्त्राणामनुरुद्धपन्नपेतभीः<BR> Mb. 12. 24. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निग्रहस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहस्थानम्
निग्रहः + -स्थानम् the reason of defeat, unfitness to be argued with, one<BR> of the 16 categories of the Naiyāyikas; एवमपि प्रकृतं दूषयितुमशक्नुवतस्तत्सिद्धान्तान्तरदूषणे<BR> निग्रहस्थानमापद्यते । ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहण
निग्रहण <i>a.</i> Holding back or down, suppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहणम्
निग्रहण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Subduing, suppression.<BR>—2 Capture, confinement.<BR>—3 Chastisement, punishment in general.<BR>—4 Defeat.<BR>—5 War, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राभः|निग्राभ
निग्राभः Pressing down, letting sink, suppressing (the voice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राहः|निग्राह
निग्राहः<BR>—1 Punishment.<BR>—2 An imprecation; as in निग्राहस्ते भूयात् ‘confusion seize thee!’; Bk. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ|निघः
निघ <i>a.</i> As high as broad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघः|निघ
निघ + .{@-घः@}<BR>—1 A ball.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निघानिघ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघानिघ
निघ + -अनिघ <i>a.</i> of different forms or sizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टः|निघण्ट
निघण्टः, निघण्टुः<BR>—1 A vocabulary or glossary of words.<BR>—2 Particularly the glossary of Vedic words explained by Yāska, in his Nirukta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टुः|निघण्टु|निघंटु|निघंटुः
निघण्टः, निघण्टुः<BR>—1 A vocabulary or glossary of words.<BR>—2 Particularly the glossary of Vedic words explained by Yāska, in his Nirukta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघसः|निघस
निघ(घा)सः<BR>—1 Eating, dining.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघासः
निघ(घा)सः<BR>—1 Eating, dining.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातः|निघात
निघातः<BR>—1 A blow, stroke; ज्यानिघातकठिनाङ्गुलिर्वृथा बध्यतामभययाचनाञ्जलिः<BR> R. 11. 78; मयि तु कृतनिघाते किं विदध्यात्परेण Mv. 2. 49.<BR>—2 Suppression or absense of accent.<BR>—3 A vowel having a grave accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातिः|निघाति
निघातिः <i>f.</i> An iron club, hammer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्टम्
निघुष्टम् Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्
निघृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To rub, pound, grind.<BR>—2 To graze, wear away by rubbing or grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षः|निघर्ष
निघर्षः, निघर्षणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, friction; तरुशाखां न निघर्षजोऽनलः Ki. 2. 51; यथा<BR> चतुर्भिः कनकं परीक्ष्यते निघर्षणच्छेदनतापताडनैः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षणम्
निघर्षः, निघर्षणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing, friction; तरुशाखां न निघर्षजोऽनलः Ki. 2. 51; यथा<BR> चतुर्भिः कनकं परीक्ष्यते निघर्षणच्छेदनतापताडनैः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्ट
निघृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rubbed, ground.<BR>—2 Chafed, grazed.<BR>—3 Subdued, overpowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्व|निघृष्वः
निघृष्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rubbed off, excoriated.<BR>—2 Small, trifling, insignificant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्वः|निघृष्व
निघृष्व + .{@-ष्वः@}<BR>—1 A hoof.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 An ass or mule.<BR>—4 A boar.<BR>—5 A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्वम्
निघृष्व + .{@-ष्वम्@} The mark of a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्न|निघ्नः
निघ्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dependent, subservient, obedient (as a servant); तथापि निघ्नं नृप<BR> तावकीनैः प्रह्वीकृतं मे हृदयं गुणौघैः Ki. 3. 12; निघ्नस्य मे भर्तृनिदेशरौक्ष्यं<BR> देवि क्षमस्वेति बभूव नम्रः R. 14. 58.<BR>—2 Docile, tractable.<BR>—3 Dependent on (<i>i. e.</i> following the gender &c. of) a substantive;<BR> इति विशेष्यनिध्नवर्गः.<BR>—4 (After a numeral) Multiplied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नान
निघ्नान <i>a.</i> One who destroys (see निहन्); निध्नानं शात्रवान्<BR> रामं कथं त्वं नावगच्छसि Bk. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचि
निचि €5 U.<BR>—1 To pile up, heap up.<BR>—2 To cover or fill with, strew, overspread (chiefly in <i>p. p.</i>); निचितं<BR> खमुपेत्य नीरदैः Ghaṭ. 1; शकुन्तनीडनिचितं बिभ्रज्जटामण्डलम्<BR> Ś. 7. 11; Bk. 10. 4.<BR>—3 To accumulate, store; निचीयते त्वया साधो यशोऽपि सुहृदा विना Mu. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयः|निचय
निचयः<BR>—1 A collection, heap, multitude; निचय इवाम्बुमुचां नगाधिराजः<BR> (ददृशे) Ki. 4. 37.<BR>—2 Store, stock, provisions; as षण्मासनिचयः Ms. 6. 18; सर्वे<BR> क्षयान्ता निचयाः Rām. 7. 52. 11.<BR>—3 An assemblage of parts consisting a whole; as in शरीरनिचयः<BR>—4 Certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयिन्
निचयिन् <i>a.</i> Full of, abounding in; निचयिनि लवलीलताविकासे<BR> जनयति लोध्रसमीरणे च हर्षम् Ki. 10. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचायः|निचाय
निचायः A heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0896-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचित|निचितं
निचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Covered, overcast, overspread; बभौ चिरं निचित इवासृजां लवैः Śi. 17. 14.<BR>—2 Full of, filled.<BR>—3 Raised up.<BR>—4 Piled or heaped up.<BR>—5 Constipated (as the bowels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिकी
निचिकी, -नैचिकी<BR> An excellent cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचिकी
निचिकी, -नैचिकी<BR> An excellent cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुम्पुणः|निचुम्पुण|निचुंपुणः
निचुम्पुणः Ved.<BR>—1 The sea, a gush, flood; अपां जग्मिर्निचुम्पुणः Rv. 8. 93. 22.<BR>—2 An epithet of Soma.<BR>—3 N. of an <i>avabhṛtha</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलः|निचुल
निचुलः<BR>—1 A kind of reed.<BR>—2 N. of a poet and friend of Kālidāsa; स्थानादस्मात् सरसनिचुलादुत्पतोदङ्मुखः<BR> खम् Me. 14 (where Malli. observes:− निचुलो नाम महाकविः कालिदासस्य<BR> सहाध्यायः; but this explanation is very doubtful).<BR>—3 An upper garment, cover; cf. निचोल.<BR>—4 The tree called हिज्जल, (Barringtonia Acutangula).<BR>—5 A lotus.<BR>—6 A cocoa-nut tree; निचुलो हिज्जले पद्मेऽप्यस्त्री मधुफले ऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलकम्
निचुलकम्<BR>—1 A breast-plate, cuirass.<BR>—2 An outer garment.<BR>—3 A case box; कृत्वा धनुर्निचुलके मृगयानिवृत्तौ B. R. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलित
निचुलित <i>a.</i> Being in a case; cased; निर्मोकेन च वासुकेर्निचुलितम्<BR> (धनुः) B. R. 4. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलः|निचोल
निचोलः<BR>—1 A cover, veil, wrapper; ध्वान्तं नीलनिचोलचारु Gīt. 11; शीलय<BR> नीलनिचोलम् 5; तमोमयं नीलनिचोलचेलम् Rām. Ch. 6. 28.<BR>—2 A bed-cover.<BR>—3 The cover of a litter (दोलिकावरणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलकः|निचोलक
निचोलकः<BR>—1 A jacket, bodice.<BR>—2 A soldierʼs jacket serving as a breast-plate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छविः|निच्छवि|निछवि
निच्छविः N. of a district, the modern Tirhut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिविः|निच्छिवि|निछिवि
निच्छिविः N. of one of the degraded castes (sprung from outcast Kṣatriyas);<BR> see Ms. 10. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छेदः|निच्छेद
निच्छेदः<BR>—1 Cutting off.<BR>—2 (In arith.) Leaving no common measure, reducing by the common divisor,<BR> to the least term, so as to be capable of no further reduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज्
निज् €3 U. (नेनेक्ति, नेनिंक्ते, प्रणेनेक्ति, निक्त)<BR>—1 To wash, cleanse, purify; सस्नुः पयः पपुरनेनिजुरम्बराणि Śi. 5. 28.<BR>—2 To wash or clean oneself, to be purified (Ā.).<BR>—3 To nourish. ━<i>With</i> {@निस्@} to wash, clean, purify; तोयनिर्णिक्तपाणयः<BR> R. 17. 22; Y. 1. 191; Ms. 5. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्त
निक्त <i>p. p.</i> Washed, cleansed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज|निजं
निज <i>a.</i> [नितरां जायते निजन्-ड]<BR>—1 Innate, indigenous, native, inborn, congenial.<BR>—2 Own, oneʼs own, relating to one-self, of oneʼs own party or country;<BR> निजं वपुः पुनरनयन्निजां रुचिम् Śi. 17. 4; R. 3. 15, 18. 27; Ms. 2. 50.<BR>—3 Peculiar.<BR>—4 Continual, perpetual. ━<i>m.</i> (pl.) Oneʼs own people.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निजबोधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजबोधः
निज + -बोधः Self-knowledge, spiritual knowledge; भिक्षुर्न चाहं निजबोधरूपः<BR> Hastāmalaka Stotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निञ्ज्|निंज्
निञ्ज् €2 Ā. (निंक्ते) To wash.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@प्र@} to wash (प्रणिङ्क्ते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलम्
निटलम् (Sometimes written निटिल) The forehead; निटिलतटचुम्बित Dk. 4. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निटलाक्षः, निटलेक्षणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलाक्षः|निटलाक्ष
निटलम् + -अक्षः, -ईक्षणः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलेक्षणः
निटलम् + -अक्षः, -ईक्षणः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडीनम्
निडीनम् The downward flight or swoop of birds; Mb. 8. 4. 26; see डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्य
निण्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Hidden, concealed.<BR>—2 Secret, mysterious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्यम्
निण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@} A secret or mystery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितप्
नितप् €1 P. To emit heat downwards, to sweat; तदाहुर्निशोचति नितपति<BR> वर्षिष्यति वा Ch. Up. 7. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बः|नितम्ब|नितंब|नितंबः
नितम्बः [निभृतं तम्यते कामुकैः, तमु काङ्क्षायाम्]<BR>—1 The buttocks, posteriors (of a woman), (the circumference of the hip<BR> and loins); यातं यच्च नितम्बयोर्गुरुतया मन्दं विलासादिव Ś. 2. 2;<BR> R. 4. 52, 6. 17; Me. 43; Bh. 1. 5; M. 2. 7.<BR>—2 The slope, ridge, side, flank of a mountain; सनाकवनितं नितम्बरुचिरम्<BR> (गिरिम्) Ki. 5. 27; सेव्या नितम्बाः किमु भूधराणामुत स्मरस्मेरविलासिनीनाम्<BR> Bh. 1. 19; V. 4. 26; Bk. 2. 8, 7. 58.<BR>—3 A precipice.<BR>—4 The sloping bank of a river; Mb. 1. 120. 12.<BR>—5 The shoulder.<BR>—6 The sounding-board of the Vīṇā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नितम्बबिम्बम्, नितम्बस्थलम्, नितम्बस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बबिम्बम्
नितम्बः + -बिम्बम् round or circular hips; Ṛs. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बस्थलम्
नितम्बः + -स्थलम्, -स्थली The region of the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बस्थली
नितम्बः + -स्थलम्, -स्थली The region of the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बवत्|नितम्बवन्त्
नितम्बवत् <i>a.</i> Having beautiful hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बवती|नितंबवती
नितम्बवत् + .{@-ती@} A woman; चारु चुचुम्ब नितम्बवती दयितम् Gīt. 1; V. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बिन्|नितंबिन्
नितम्बिन् <i>a.</i> [नितम्ब-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 Having beautiful hips, having well-sloped buttocks (often applied to<BR> जघन); cf. M. 2. 3; Ki. 8. 16; R. 19. 26.<BR>—2 Having beautiful sides (as a mountain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बिनी|नितंबिनी
नितम्बिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A woman with large and handsome hips; नितम्बिनीनां भृशमादधे धृतिम्<BR> Ki. 8. 3; Śi. 7. 68; Ku. 3. 7.<BR>—2 A woman in general; नामृतं न विषं किंचिदेकां मुक्त्वा नितम्बिनीम् ।<BR> यस्याः सङ्गेन जीव्येत म्रियेत च वियोगतः ॥ Pt. 4. 32, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितराम्
नितराम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Wholly, entirely, completely; प्राणांस्त्यजामि नितरां तदवाप्तिहेतोः<BR> C. P. 41; Bh. 1. 96.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, excessively, very much; तुदन्ति चेतो नितरां प्रवासिनाम्<BR> Ṛs. 2. 4; Amaru. 10; Bh. 2. 18; शोषितसरसि निदाधे नितरामेवोद्धतः<BR> सिन्धुः Pt. 1. 104; नितरां नीचोऽस्मीति Bv. 1. 8.<BR>—3 Continually, always, eternally.<BR>—4 At all events.<BR>—5 Certainly.<BR>—6 Ved. In a low tone. —7 Downward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितलम्
नितलम् One of the seven divisions of the lower regions; see पाताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्त|नितांत|नितान्तं
नितान्त <i>a.</i> Extraordinary, excessive, very much, intense; नितान्तकठिनां<BR> रुजं मम न वेद यो मानसीम् V. 2. 11; R. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्तम्
नितान्त + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Excessively, very much, exceedingly, in a high degree;<BR> मित्रं कोऽपि न कस्याऽपि नितान्तं न च वैरकृत् Pt. 2. 116.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नितान्तकठिण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्तकठिण
नितान्त + -कठिण ({@न@}) <i>a.</i> Very hard, severe; नितान्तकठिनां<BR> रुजं मम न वेद यो मानसीम् V. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0897-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य <i>a.</i> [नियमेन नियतं वा भवं नि-त्य-प्; cf. P. IV. 2. 104; Vārt.]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Continual, perpetual, constant, everlasting, eternal, uninterrupted;<BR> यथा त्वमसि दुर्धर्षो धर्मनित्यः प्रजाहितः Rām. 7. 37. 8; यदि<BR> नित्यमनित्येन लभ्यते H. 1. 48; नित्यज्योत्स्नाः प्रतिहततमोवृत्तिरम्याः<BR> प्रदोषाः Me. (regarded by Malli. as an interpolation); Ms. 2. 206.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Imperishable, indestructible; पृथिवी द्विविधा नित्याऽनित्या च Tarka K.<BR>—2 Invariable, regular, fixed, not optional, regularly prescribed (opp. काम्य).<BR>—3 Necessary, obligatory, essential.<BR>—4 Ordinary, usual (opp. नौमित्तिक).<BR>—5 (At the end of comp.) Constantly dwelling in, perpetually engaged in<BR> or busy with; जाह्नवीतीर˚, अरण्य˚, आदान˚, ध्यान˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यः|नित्य|नित्यं
नित्य + .{@-त्यः@} The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्या
नित्य + .{@-त्या@}<BR>—1 An epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—2 A plough-share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यम्
नित्य + .{@-त्यम्@} An indispensable or inevitable act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यम्
नित्य + .{@-त्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Daily, constantly, always, ever, perpetually, eternally.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नित्यानध्यायः, नित्यानित्य, नित्यानुबद्ध, नित्यानुवादः, नित्याभियुक्त, नित्यर्तु, नित्यकर्मन्, नित्यकालम्, नित्यगतिः, नित्यजात, नित्यदानम्, नित्यनियमः, नित्यनैमित्तिकम्, नित्यपुष्ट, नित्यप्रलयः, नित्यबुद्धि,^1 नित्यभावः, नित्यमुक्तः, नित्ययुक्त, नित्ययुज्, नित्ययौवना, नित्यव्रतम्, नित्यशङ्कित, नित्यसमः, नित्यसमासः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानध्यायः|नित्यानध्याय
नित्य + -अनध्यायः invariable suspension of Vedic studies; नित्यानध्याय<BR> एव स्याद् ग्रामेषु नगरेषु च Ms. 4. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानित्य
नित्य + -अनित्य <i>a.</i> eternal and perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानुबद्ध
नित्य + -अनुबद्ध <i>a.</i> always approached or resorted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानुवादः
नित्य + -अनुवादः a bare statement of fact; स्याज्जुह्वप्रतिषेधान्नित्यानुवादः MS. 4. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्याभियुक्त
नित्य + -अभियुक्त <i>a.</i> One who is completely absorbed in yogic practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यर्तु
नित्य + -ऋतु <i>a.</i> regularly recurring at the seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकर्मन्|नित्यकर्म्मन्
नित्य + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-कृत्यम्, -क्रिया@}<BR> any daily and necessary rite, a constant act or<BR> duty, as the five daily Yajñas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकालम्
नित्य + -कालम् <i>ind.</i> always, at all times; ब्राह्मेण विप्रस्तीर्थेन<BR> नित्यकालमुपस्पृशेत् Ms. 2. 58, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यगतिः|नित्यगति
नित्य + -गतिः air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यजात
नित्य + -जात <i>a.</i> constantly born; अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा<BR> मन्यसे मृतम् Bg. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदानम्
नित्य + -दानम् daily alms-giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यनियमः
नित्य + -नियमः an invariable rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यनैमित्तिकम्
नित्य + -नैमित्तिकम् an occasional act regularly recurring, or any ceremony<BR> constantly performed to accomplish a particular object, <i>e. g.</i> (a पर्वश्राद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यपुष्ट
नित्य + -पुष्ट <i>a.</i> always well-supplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यप्रलयः|नित्यप्रलय
नित्य + -प्रलयः<BR>—1 the constant dissolution of living beings.<BR>—2 sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यबुद्धि
नित्य + -बुद्धि^1 <i>a.</i> considering anything as constant or eternal.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यभावः|नित्यभाव
नित्य + -भावः eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यमुक्तः|नित्यमुक्त
नित्य + -मुक्तः the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययुक्त
नित्य + -युक्त <i>a.</i> always busy or intent upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययुज्
नित्य + -युज् <i>a.</i> having the mind always fixed upon one object; दृग्भिर्हृदीकृतमलं<BR> परिरभ्य सर्वास्तद्भावमापुरपि नित्ययुजां दुरापम् Bhāg. 10. 82. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययौवना
नित्य + -यौवना (ever youthful) an epithet of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यव्रतम्
नित्य + -व्रतम् a perpetual observance (lasting for life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशङ्कित|नित्यशंकित
नित्य + -शङ्कित <i>a.</i> perpetually alarmed, ever suspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यसमः|नित्यसम
नित्य + -समः the assertion that all things remain the same; Sarva. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यसमासः|नित्यसमास
नित्य + -समासः ‘a necessary compound’, a compund the meaning of which<BR> cannot be expressed by its constituent members used separately (the separate<BR> ideas having merged in one); <i>e. g.</i> जमदग्नि, जयद्रथ &c.; इवेन<BR> नित्यसमासः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यता
नित्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Invariableness, constancy, continuance, eternity, perpetuity.<BR>—2 Necessity.<BR>—3 Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यत्वम्
नित्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Invariableness, constancy, continuance, eternity, perpetuity.<BR>—2 Necessity.<BR>—3 Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदा
नित्यदा <i>ind.</i> Perpetually, always, constantly, eternally; स<BR> नित्यदोद्विग्नधिया तमीश्वरम् (ददर्श) Bhāg. 10. 44. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशस्
नित्यशस् <i>ind.</i> Constantly, always, eternally; अनन्यचेताः सततं<BR> यो मां स्मरति नित्यशः Bg. 8. 14; Ms. 2. 96, 4. 150<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
निद् €1 U. (नेदति-ते)<BR>—1 To be near.<BR>—2 To blame, censure, approach; cf. निन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
निद् <i>f.</i> Ved. Mocking, despising, censuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद <i>a.</i> Censuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदम्
निद + .{@-दम्@} Poison; (also निदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदद्रुः|निदद्रु
निदद्रुः<BR>—1 A man.<BR>—2 One without herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
निदर्शक, -नम् &c.<BR> See under निदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्
निदर्शक, -नम् &c.<BR> See under निदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघः|निदाघ
निदाघः [नि-दह् आधारे घञ् न्यङ्क्वादि कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 Heat, warmth; आर्द्राङ्गुलीदलमनङ्गनिदाघतप्तः<BR>—2 The hot season, summer (the months of ज्येष्ठ and आषाढ); निदाघमिहिरज्वालाशतैः<BR> Bv. 1. 16; निदाघकालः समुपागतः प्रिये Ṛs. 1. 1; Pt. 1. 104; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>—3 Sweat, perspiration. प्रस्नापयामास मुखं निदाघः Ki. 17. 8.<BR>—4 The internal heat; स्त्रियो निदाघं शमयन्ति कामिनाम् Ṛs. 1. 4.<BR>—5 The water of perspiration.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निदाघकरः, निदाघकालः, निदाघधामन्, निदाघवार्षिक, निदाघसिन्धुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकरः|निदाघकर
निदाघः + -करः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकालः|निदाघकाल
निदाघः + -कालः summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघधामन्
निदाघः + -धामन् the sun; निदाघधामानमिवाधिदीधितिम् Śi. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघवार्षिक
निदाघः + -वार्षिक <i>a.</i> (months) belonging to the hot and rainy season;<BR> निदाघवार्षिकौ मासौ लोकं घर्मांशुभिर्यथा Mb. 7. 30. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघसिन्धुः|निदाघसिन्धु
निदाघः + -सिन्धुः a river in hot season (nearly dry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदानम्
निदानम्<BR>—1 A band, rope, halter; उदुस्रियाणामसृजन्निदानम् Rv. 6. 32. 2.<BR>—2 A rope for tying up a calf; बालजेन निदानेन कांस्यं भवतु दोहनम्<BR> Mb. 13. 94. 41.<BR>—3 A primary cause, the first or essential cause; निदानमिक्ष्वाकुकुलस्य<BR> सन्ततेः R. 3. 1; अथवा बलमारम्भो निदानं क्षयसम्पदः Śi. 2. 94.<BR>—4 A cause in general; मुञ्च मयि मानमनिदानम् Gīt. 5.<BR>—5 (in medicine) Inquiry into the causes of a disease, pathology.<BR>—6 Diagnosis of a disease.<BR>—7 End, termination.<BR>—8 Purity, purification, correctness.<BR>—9 Claiming the reward of penitential acts.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निदानस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदानस्थानम्
निदानम् + -स्थानम् one of the departments of medical science, Pathology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्ध|निदिग्धं
निदिग्ध <i>p. p.</i> [नि-दिह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Smeared, annointed.<BR>—2 Increased, accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धा
निदिग्ध + .{@-ग्धा@} Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धिकादिक्काथः
निदिग्धिकादिक्काथः A kind of Āyurvedic decoction; निदिग्धिकानागरकामृतानां<BR> क्वाथं पिबेन्मिश्रितपिपप्लीकम् । जीर्णज्वरारोचककासशूलश्वासाग्निमान्द्यार्दितपीनसेषु ॥<BR> Com. of Cakradatta on Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासः|निदिध्यास
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनम् See under निध्यै; निरन्तरं विचारो<BR> यः श्रुतार्थस्य गुरोर्मुखात् । तन्निदिध्यासनं प्रोक्तं तच्चैकाग्र्येण लभ्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासनम्
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनम् See under निध्यै; निरन्तरं विचारो<BR> यः श्रुतार्थस्य गुरोर्मुखात् । तन्निदिध्यासनं प्रोक्तं तच्चैकाग्र्येण लभ्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिश्
निदिश् €6 P. To order, point out &c.; see निर्दिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिष्ट
निदिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pointed out.<BR>—2 Ordered, directed.<BR>—3 Advised, enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशः|निदेश
निदेशः<BR>—1 Order, command, direction, instruction; वाक्येनेयं स्थापिता स्वे निदेशे<BR> M. 3. 14; स्थितं निदेशे पृथगादिदेश R. 14. 58; Ku. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Speech, narration, conversation.<BR>—3 Vicinity, neighbourhood; निदेशे चैव तिष्ठतः Ms. 2. 197.<BR>—4 A vessel, vase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0898-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिन्
निदेशिन् <i>a.</i> Pointing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिनी
निदेशिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A quarter, point of the compass.<BR>—2 A region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदृश्
निदृश् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To show, point out; निदर्शयामास विशेषदृश्यमिन्दुं नवोत्थानमिवेन्दुमत्यै R. 6. 31.<BR>—2 To prove, establish, demonstrate.<BR>—3 To consider, treat of, discuss (as in a book).<BR>—4 To teach, explain.<BR>—5 To illustrate by an example; cf. निदर्शना.<BR>—6 To introduce, cause to enter.<BR>—7 To show oneself to (a person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
निदर्शक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Seeing.<BR>—2 Seeing into, perceiving.<BR>—3 Pointing out, proclaiming, indicating, showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pointing, showing.<BR>—2 Proclaiming, declaring announcing.<BR>—3 Teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शनम्
निदर्शन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 View, insight, looking into, sight, vision; शुद्धात्मा ब्राह्मणो रात्रौ<BR> निदर्शनमपश्यत Mb. 12. 271. 14.<BR>—2 Pointing to, showing.<BR>—3 Proof, evidence; बलिना सह योद्धव्यमिति नास्ति निदर्शनम् Pt. 3. 23.<BR>—4 An instance, example, illustration; ननु प्रभुरेव निदर्शनम् Ś. 2;<BR> निदर्शनसाराणां लघुर्बहुतृणं नरः Śi. 2. 50; R. 8. 45; जनकस्य<BR> नृपेन्द्रस्य तपसः सन्निदर्शनम् Pratimā 4. 14.<BR>—5 Injunction.<BR>—6 Authority, text.<BR>—7 A scheme, system.<BR>—8 A precept, scriptural authority, an injunction.<BR>—9 The third member of an Indian syllogism (usually called उदाहरण q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शना
निदर्शन + .{@-ना@} A figure of speech (in Rhetoric) thus defined:− निदर्शना ।<BR> अभवन्वस्तुसंबन्ध उपमापरिकल्पकः K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> R. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शित
निदर्शित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shown, presented.<BR>—2 Offered (as a seat).<BR>—3 Illustrated, exemplified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शिन्
निदर्शिन् <i>a.</i> Suiting, pleasing; सतां बुद्धिं पुरस्कृत्य सर्वलोकनिदर्शिनीम् ।<BR> राज्यं स त्वं निगृह्णीष्व भरतेन प्रसादितः ॥ Rām. 2. 108. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा €2 P. To fall asleep, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा<BR>—1 Sleep, sleepiness; प्रच्छायसुलभनिद्रा दिवसाः Ś. 1. 3; निद्रामुद्रां<BR> क्षिपन् Māl. 2. 12.<BR>—2 Sloth; निद्रां च प्रतिभां चैव ज्ञानाभ्यासेन तत्त्ववित् (निवर्तयेत्)<BR> Mb. 12. 274. 7.<BR>—3 Shutting, budding state.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निद्रान्ध, निद्रालस, निद्रादारिद्र, निद्राभङ्गः, निद्रावृक्षः, निद्रासजननम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रान्ध
निद्रा + -अन्ध <i>a.</i> dead, fast asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालस
निद्रा + -अलस <i>a.</i> dull or languid with drowsiness, fast asleep; निद्रालसा<BR> बर्हिणः V. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रादारिद्र
निद्रा + -दारिद्र <i>a.</i> suffering from want of sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राभङ्गः|निद्राभङ्ग
निद्रा + -भङ्गः awaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रावृक्षः|निद्रावृक्ष
निद्रा + -वृक्षः darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रासजननम्
निद्रा + -सजननम् phlegm, phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राण|निद्राणः
निद्राण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sleeping, asleep.<BR>—2 Shut, closed (as a bud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालु|निद्रालुः
निद्रालु <i>a.</i> Sleeping, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालुः|निद्रालु
निद्रालु + .{@-लुः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu; निद्रालोः कमठाकृतेर्भगवतः श्वासानिलाः<BR> पान्तु वः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रित
निद्रित <i>a.</i> Asleep, slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधन|निधनं|निधनः
निधन <i>a.</i> [निवृत्तं धनं यस्मात्; Uṇ. 2. 81] Poor, indigent;<BR> अहो निधनता सर्वापदामास्पदम् Mk. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनः|निधन|निधनं
निधन + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 Destruction, annihilation, death, loss; स्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः<BR> Bg. 3. 35; म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालम् Gīt. 1; कल्पान्तेष्वपि<BR> न प्रयाति निधनं विद्याख्यमन्तर्धनम् Bh. 2. 16; Pt. 1. 21, 5. 95.<BR>—2 The concluding passage at the end of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">Page0899-2</a>]<BR> Sāman sung in chorus, the fifth of the five parts of Sāman; लोकेषु<BR> पञ्चविधं सामोपासीत … … द्यौर्निधनम् Ch. Up. 2. 2. 1.<BR>—3 The <i>finale</i> (in music).<BR>—4 N. of the eighth lunar mansion.<BR>—5 Conclusion, end, termination; अस्य वाक्यस्य निधने प्रादुरासीच्छिवोऽनिलः<BR> Mb. 6. 119. 38.<BR>—6 Ved. Residence; receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनम्
निधन + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 Destruction, annihilation, death, loss; स्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः<BR> Bg. 3. 35; म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालम् Gīt. 1; कल्पान्तेष्वपि<BR> न प्रयाति निधनं विद्याख्यमन्तर्धनम् Bh. 2. 16; Pt. 1. 21, 5. 95.<BR>—2 The concluding passage at the end of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">Page0899-2</a>]<BR> Sāman sung in chorus, the fifth of the five parts of Sāman; लोकेषु<BR> पञ्चविधं सामोपासीत … … द्यौर्निधनम् Ch. Up. 2. 2. 1.<BR>—3 The <i>finale</i> (in music).<BR>—4 N. of the eighth lunar mansion.<BR>—5 Conclusion, end, termination; अस्य वाक्यस्य निधने प्रादुरासीच्छिवोऽनिलः<BR> Mb. 6. 119. 38.<BR>—6 Ved. Residence; receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनः|निधन|निधनं
निधन + .{@-नः@} The head of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनम्
निधन + .{@-नम्@} Family, race.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निधनकारिन्, निधनक्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनकारिन्
निधन + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> fatal, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनक्रिया
निधन + -क्रिया a funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनता
निधनता Indigence, poverty; अहो निधनता सर्वापदामास्पदम् Mk. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
निधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place, put, put or set down; शिरसि निदधानोऽञ्जलिपुटम् Bh. 3. 123;<BR> R. 3. 50, 62, 12. 52; Śi. 1. 13.<BR>—2 To confide, or entrust, commit to the care of; निदधे विजयाशंसां<BR> चापे सीतां च लक्ष्मणे R. 12. 44, 15. 36.<BR>—3 To give, impart to, deposit with; दिनान्ते निहितं तेजः सवित्रेव<BR> हुताशनः R. 4. 1.<BR>—4 To put down, lay, allay, restrain; सलिलैर्निहितं रजः क्षितौ Ghaṭ. 1<BR>—5 To bury, conceal or hide (as under ground); ऊनद्विवार्षिकं प्रेतं<BR> निदध्युर्बान्धवा बहिः Ms. 5. 68.<BR>—6 To fix or direct the thoughts upon; cf. निध्यै.<BR>—7 To determine, resolve.<BR>—8 To direct oneʼs labours, endeavour.<BR>—9 To appoint.<BR>—10 To remove, relinquish.<BR>—11 To lay up, treasure up.<BR>—12 To remember, keep or bear in mind.<BR>—13 To end, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
निधा Ved.<BR>—1 Laying snares.<BR>—2 A net or snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधानम्
निधानम्<BR>—1 Putting down, laying down, depositing.<BR>—2 Keeping, preserving.<BR>—3 Place where anything is placed, a receptacle, reservoir; निधानं<BR> धर्माणाम् G. L. 18.<BR>—4 Treasure; निधानगर्भामिव सागराम्बराम् R. 3. 9; Bg. 9. 18; विद्यैव<BR> लोकस्य परं निधानम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—5 Hoard, store, property, wealth.<BR>—6 A place of cessation or rest.<BR>—7 A deposit; Ms. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिः|निधि
निधिः [नि-धा-आधारे कि]<BR>—1 Abode, receptacle, reservoir; जल˚, तोय˚, तपोनिधि &c.<BR>—2 A store-house, treasury.<BR>—3 A treasure, store, hoard (for the nine treasures of Kubera, see नवनिधि).<BR>—4 The ocean.<BR>—5 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 A man endowed with many good qualities.<BR>—7 the science of chronology; Ch. Up. 7. 2. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निधीशः, निधिनाथः, निधिवादः, निधिवासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीशः|निधीश
निधिः + -ईशः, -नाथः an epithet of Kubera; Bhāg. 10. 50. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिनाथः|निधिनाथ
निधिः + -ईशः, -नाथः an epithet of Kubera; Bhāg. 10. 50. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिवादः|निधिवाद
निधिः + -वादः the art of finding treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिवासः|निधिवास
निधिः + -वासः the town of Newāsā on the Pravarā river in the Ahmednagar<BR> District; Cf. निधिवासकर-परमानन्द-प्रकाशितायां … संहितायां … … ।<BR> Colophon of Śiva B. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवनम्
निधुवनम् [नितरां धुवनं हस्तपादादिचालनमत्र]<BR>—1 Agitation, trembling;<BR>—2 Sexual enjoyment, coition; अतिशयमधुरिपुनिधुवनशीलम् Gīt. 2;<BR> Śi. 11. 18; C. P. 4, 8, 25.<BR>—3 Pleasure, enjoyment, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यै
निध्यै €1 P.<BR>—1 To think of, meditate upon, remember; विभीषणादिति श्रुत्वा तं निदध्यौ<BR> रघूत्तमः Bk. 14. 65.<BR>—2 To meditate deeply upon, look steadfastly or intently at; अङ्गुलीयकं<BR> निध्यायन्ती M. 1; Śi. 8. 69, 12. 40; Ki. 10. 46, 14. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0899-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासः|निदिध्यास
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनम् Profound and repeated meditation,<BR> constant musing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासनम्
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनम् Profound and repeated meditation,<BR> constant musing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यात
निध्यात <i>a.</i> Meditated or thought on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यानम्
निध्यानम् Seeing, beholding, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्वानः|निध्वान
निध्वानः Sound; निध्वानैनीरदौघध्वनिपरिभवदैरम्बरं कम्बुराजः<BR> Viṣṇupāda. S. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनङ्क्षु|निनंक्षु
निनङ्क्षु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing to die.<BR>—2 Wishing to escape or fly away; अपिस्फवच्च बन्धूनां निनङ्क्षुर्विक्रमं<BR> मुहुः Bk. 4. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद्
निनद् €1 P. —1 To sound, shout; मधुपटनिनदद्भिर्बोधितो राजहंसैः<BR> R. 5. 75; M. 5. 10; Bk. 6. 117.<BR>—3 To resound, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनदः|निनद
निन(ना)दः<BR>—1 Sound, noise; U. 3. 7 (v. l.); उच्चचार निनदोऽम्भसि तस्याः R. 9. 73, 11. 15;<BR> Ṛs. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Buzzing, humming (of bees &c.).<BR>—3 A sound like that of a chariot; कर्णावपिगृह्य निनदमिव नदथुः<BR> Ch. Up. 3. 13. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादः|निनाद
निन(ना)दः<BR>—1 Sound, noise; U. 3. 7 (v. l.); उच्चचार निनदोऽम्भसि तस्याः R. 9. 73, 11. 15;<BR> Ṛs. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Buzzing, humming (of bees &c.).<BR>—3 A sound like that of a chariot; कर्णावपिगृह्य निनदमिव नदथुः<BR> Ch. Up. 3. 13. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादित
निनादित <i>a.</i> Filled with noise, resounding, made to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादितम्
निनादित + .{@-तम्@} A sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादिन्
निनादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sounding, ringing.<BR>—2 Causing to sound, playing (as a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयनम्
निनयनम् See under निनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्द्
निनर्द् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sound.<BR>—2 To prolong a note (in chanting).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्दः|निनर्द
निनर्दः Prolonging a note in chanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनाह्यः|निनाह्य
निनाह्यः A water-jar to be put into the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनी
निनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To take near or towards, carry near, bring, fetch; चरितव्रत आयाते<BR> निनयेरन्नवं घटम् Y. 3. 295.<BR>—2 To bend, incline; वक्त्रं निनीय.<BR>—3 To pour down.<BR>—4 To bring about, accomplish, perform.<BR>—5 To spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयनम्
निनयनम्<BR>—1 Performance.<BR>—2 Performing, accomplishing.<BR>—3 Pouring out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनृत्त
निनृत्त <i>a.</i> Repeated (as a portion of a verse.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनृत्तिः|निनृत्ति
निनृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्|निंद्
निन्द् €1 P. (निन्दति, निन्दित; प्रणिन्दति) To blame, censure, find<BR> fault with, revile, reproach, condemn; निनिन्द रूपं हृदयेन पार्वती<BR> Ku. 5. 1; सा निन्दन्ती स्वानि भाग्यानि बाला Ś. 5. 30; Bg. 2. 36; Ms. 3. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दक|निंदक|निन्दकः
निन्दक <i>a.</i> [निन्द्-वुञ्] Blaming, censuring, abusing, defaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दनम्
निन्दनम्, निन्दा [निन्द्-भावे-ल्युट् अ वा]<BR>—1 Blame, censure, reproof, reproach, abuse, reviling, defamation; व्याजस्तुतिर्मुखे<BR> निन्दा K. P. 10; पर˚, वेद˚.<BR>—2 Injury, wickedness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निन्दनोपमा, निन्दनस्तुतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दा|निंदा
निन्दनम्, निन्दा [निन्द्-भावे-ल्युट् अ वा]<BR>—1 Blame, censure, reproof, reproach, abuse, reviling, defamation; व्याजस्तुतिर्मुखे<BR> निन्दा K. P. 10; पर˚, वेद˚.<BR>—2 Injury, wickedness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निन्दनोपमा, निन्दनस्तुतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दनोपमा
निन्दनम् + -उपमा a comparison which involves reproofs; Kāv. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दनस्तुतिः
निन्दनम् + -स्तुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 ironical praise, irony.<BR>—2 overt praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दित|निंदित|निन्दितः
निन्दित <i>p. p.</i> [निन्द्-क्त]<BR>—1 Blamed, censured, abused, defamed &c.<BR>—2 Low, despicable.<BR>—3 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्य|निंद्य
निन्द्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blamable, censurable, reprehensible, bad, vile.<BR>—2 Forbidden, prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दतल|निन्दतलः
निन्दतल <i>a.</i> Having a maimed hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दुः|निन्दु|निंदु|निंदुः
निन्दुः <i>f.</i> A woman bearing a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपः|निप|निपं
निपः, -पम्<BR> A water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपम्
निपः, -पम्<BR> A water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपः|निप|निपं
निपः, -पम् + .{@-पः@} The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठः|निपठ
निप(पा)ठः, निपठनम्, निपठितिः <i>f.</i> Reading, reciting, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाठः|निपाठ
निप(पा)ठः, निपठनम्, निपठितिः <i>f.</i> Reading, reciting, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठनम्
निप(पा)ठः, निपठनम्, निपठितिः <i>f.</i> Reading, reciting, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठितिः|निपठिति
निप(पा)ठः, निपठनम्, निपठितिः <i>f.</i> Reading, reciting, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्
निपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fall or come down, descend, alight, sink down; निपतन्ती पतिमप्यपातयत्<BR> R. 8. 38; Bk. 15. 27.<BR>—2 To be cast at, be directed towards; निपेतुरन्तःकरणैर्नरेन्द्राः R. 6. 11.<BR>—3 To throw oneself down (as at the feet), fall prostrate; देवास्तदन्ते<BR> हरमूढभार्यं किरीटबद्धाञ्जलयो निपत्य Ku. 7. 92; R. 4. 50; Bh. 2. 31.<BR>—4 To fall or descend into, meet in; त्वय्येव निपतन्त्योघा जाह्नवीया<BR> इवार्णवे R. 10. 26.<BR>—5 To fall upon, attack, rush at or upon; सिंहो शिशुरपि निपतति मदमलिनकपोलभित्तिषु<BR> गजेषु Bh. 2. 38.<BR>—6 To happen, occur, take place, fall to oneʼs lot; सकृदंशो निपतति Ms. 9. 47.<BR>—7 To be placed, occupy a place; अभ्यर्हितं पूर्वं निपतति.<BR>—8 To flow in, discharge into.<BR>—9 To fall into ruin.<BR>—10 To fall into (any state).<BR>—11 To be miscarried (as the foetus). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to fall down, throw or hurl down.<BR>—2 To kill, destroy; तातं निपात्य सह बन्धुजनाक्षितोयैः Mu. 5. 7; Pt. 3. 63.<BR>—3 To inlay, emboss.<BR>—4 To direct (the eyes) upon.<BR>—5 To spit out.<BR>—6 To raise or levy (as a tribute).<BR>—7 (In gram.) To put down as a special or irregular form, to mention as<BR> an irregular formation; एते पञ्चविंशतिरजन्ता निपात्यन्ते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतनम्
निपतनम्<BR>—1 Falling down, descending, alighting.<BR>—2 Flying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्या
निपत्या<BR>—1 Slippery ground.<BR>—2 A battle-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातः|निपात
निपातः<BR>—1 Falling or coming down, descending, alighting; पयोधरोत्सेधनिपातचूर्णिताः<BR> Ku. 5. 24; Ṛs. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Attacking, falling upon, a spring, leap; उत्पश्यतः सिंहनिपातमुग्रम् R. 2. 60.<BR>—3 Casting, hurling, discharging; स च त्वदेकेषुनिपातसाध्यः Ku. 3. 15.<BR>—4 Descent, fall; निशितनिपाताः शराः Ś. 1. 10.<BR>—5 Dying, death; आनिपाताच्छरीरस्य युक्तो वार्यनिलाशनः Ms. 6. 31.<BR>—6 Accidental occurrence or mention; Mb. 12. 59. 46.<BR>—7 An irregular form, irregularity, putting down as irregular or exceptional;<BR> एते निपाताः, निपातोऽयम् &c.<BR>—8 A particle, an indeclinable; see P. I. 4. 56.<BR>—9 The opposite extremity, the lower end.<BR>—10 Mixing, coming together; बिन्दुन्यासादयोऽवस्थाः शुक्रशोणितसंभवाः ।<BR> यासामेव निपातेन कललं नाम जायते ॥ Mb. 12. 320. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातकः|निपातक
निपातकः, -कम्<BR> Sin, a bad act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातकम्
निपातकः, -कम्<BR> Sin, a bad act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0900-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातन|निपातनं
निपातन <i>a.</i> Killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातनम्
निपातन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Throwing down, beating or knocking down; अवगूर्य चरेत् कृच्छ्रमतिकृच्छ्रं<BR> निपातने Ms. 11. 209.<BR>—2 Overthrowing, destroying, killing; माषकस्तु भवेद्दण्डः श्वसूकरनिपातने Ms. 8. 298.<BR>—3 Touching with.<BR>—4 Putting down as irregular or exceptional.<BR>—5 An irregular form of a word, irregularity, exception; यल्लक्षणेनानुत्पन्नं<BR> तत् सर्वं निपातनात् सिद्धम् Mbh.<BR>—6 Falling or flying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातित
निपातित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or put down, felled.<BR>—2 Killed, destroyed.<BR>—3 Beaten down.<BR>—4 Irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातिन्
निपातिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Falling down, alighting; कुसुमपङ्क्तिनिपातिभिरङ्कितः R. 9. 41.<BR>—2 Destroyed, decayed.<BR>—3 Destroying; ज्योतिरिन्धननिपाति भास्करात् R. 11. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपलाशम्
निपलाशम् <i>ind.</i> Ved. Without speaking (like a tree without foliage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपा
निपा €2 P.<BR>—1 To drink or suck in, imbibe.<BR>—2 To absorb, dry up.<BR>—3 To drink, kiss; अत एव निपीयतेऽधरः Pt. 1. 189; दन्तच्छदं<BR> प्रियतमेन निपीतसारम् Ṛs. 4. 13.<BR>—4 To feast on (with the eyes or ears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपानम्
निपानम्<BR>—1 Drinking.<BR>—2 Any reservoir of water, pool, puddle; गाहन्तां महिषा निपानसलिलं<BR> शृङ्गैर्मुहुस्ताडितम् Ś. 2. 6; H. 1. 172; R. 9. 53; निपानवत् स कमलचारुदीर्घिकं<BR> ददर्श तद् वनमिव नन्दनं वनम् Bu. C. 3. 64.<BR>—3 A place or trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR>—4 A well; जह्युः स्वराडिव निपानखनित्रमिन्द्रः Bhāg. 2. 7. 48.<BR>—5 A milkpail.<BR>—6 A resort, place of shelter; निपानं सर्वभूतानाम् Mb. 12. 18. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीत
निपीत <i>p. p.</i> Drunk in, absorbed, dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीतिः|निपीति
निपीतिः <i>f.</i> Drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाकः|निपाक
निपाकः<BR>—1 Maturing, ripening.<BR>—2 Cooking.<BR>—3 Perspiration.<BR>—4 The result of a bad action; निपाकः पचने स्वेदेऽप्यसत्कर्मफलेऽपि च Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपादः|निपाद
निपादः Ved.<BR>—1 Low ground.<BR>—2 High and low ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीड्
निपीड् €10 U.<BR>—1 To harass, pain, molest, injure, punish, trouble; तेऽपि भोगाय कल्पन्ते<BR> दण्डेनैव निपीडिताः Ms. 7. 23.<BR>—2 To press together, squeeze.<BR>—3 To seize, grasp, hold fast, embrace; गुरोः सदारस्य निपीड्य पादौ<BR> R. 2. 23, 5. 65.<BR>—4 To impress.<BR>—5 To eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडनम्
निपीडनम्<BR>—1 Squeezing, pressing; घनपुलकपुलोमजाकुचाग्रद्रुतपरिरम्भनिपीडनक्षमत्वम्<BR> (दधातु) Śi. 1. 74, 13. 11.<BR>—2 Hurting, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडना
निपीडनम् + .{@-ना@} Oppression, hurt, injury; कृत्वा दीननिपीडनां निजजने<BR> बद्ध्वा वचोविग्रहम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडित
निपीडित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Squeezed, pressed.<BR>—2 Pained, hurt.<BR>—3 Embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुण|निपुणः
निपुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clever, sharp, shrewd, skilful; वयस्य निसर्गनिपुणाः स्त्रियः M. 3.<BR>—2 Proficient or skilled in, conversant or familiar with (with loc. or<BR> instr.); वाचि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">Page0901-2</a>]<BR> निपुणः; वाचा निपुणः.<BR>—3 Experienced.<BR>—4 Kindly or friendly towards.<BR>—5 Acute, fine, delicate, minute, sharp.<BR>—6 Complete, perfect, accurate.<BR>—7 Absolute; प्रसन्ननिपुणेन Bhāg. 5. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुणम्
निपुण + .{@-णम्@} Skill, proficiency; न चास्य कश्चिन्निपुणेन धातुरवैति<BR> जन्तुः कुमनीष ऊतीः Bhāg. 1. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुणम्
निपुण + .{@-णम्@} <i>ind.</i> or निपुणेन<BR>—1 Skilfully, cleverly.<BR>—2 Perfectly, completely, totally,<BR>—3 Exactly, carefully, accurately, minutely; निपुणमन्विष्यन्नुपलब्धवान्<BR> Dk. 59; निपुणमनुपाल्या हि शिशवः Mv. 5. 14.<BR>—4 In a delicate manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुणता
निपुणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Skilfulness, cleverness.<BR>—2 Carefulness, accuracy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुणत्वम्
निपुणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Skilfulness, cleverness.<BR>—2 Carefulness, accuracy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफला
निफला Cardiospermum Halicacabum (Mar. मालकांगोणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफेनम्
निफेनम् Opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्ध्|निबंध्
निबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind, tie, fasten, chain, fetter; आत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति<BR> धनंजय Bg. 4. 41, 9. 9, 14. 7, 18. 17; Ms. 6. 14; Ku. 5. 10.<BR>—2 To fix upon, rivet; त्वयि निबद्धरतेः V. 4. 29; Bh. 3. 87.<BR>—3 To join, unite, connect; आभाति वेला लवणाम्बुराशेर्धारानिबद्धेव कलङ्करेखा R. 13. 15.<BR>—4 To form, build, construct, arrange; हेमनिबद्धं चक्रम्, पाषाणचयबद्धः कूपः &c.<BR>—5 To write, compose; मया निबद्धेयमतिद्वयी कथा K. 5.<BR>—6 To restrain, obstruct.<BR>—7 To fix upon, impose.<BR>—8 To appoint.<BR>—9 To place, locate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबद्ध
निबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied, fettered, stopped, closed &c.<BR>—2 Connected with, relating to.<BR>—3 Formed of.<BR>—4 Set or inlaid with.<BR>—5 Called as a witness; Ms. 8. 76.<BR>—6 Restricted, checked.<BR>—7 Composed, written; धर्मद्रुहो दमयितुश्चरितं निबद्धम् Mv. 1. 6.<BR>—8 Covered with, enveloped.<BR>—9 Furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्द्धृ|निबंद्धृ
निबन्द्धृ^1 <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A writer, author; निबन्द्धा यस्त्वेषां स खलु निखिलेऽस्मिन् कविवृषा B. R. 1. 11.<BR>—2 A commentator.<BR>—3 A binder.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: vowel 'f' missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धः|निबन्ध|निबंध|निबन्धं|निबंधः
निबन्धः<BR>—1 Binding, tying, fastening.<BR>—2 Attachment, intentness; दैवी संपद्विमोक्षाय निबन्धायासुरी मता Bg. 16. 5.<BR>—3 Composing, writing down.<BR>—4 Literary composition or treatise, work; प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबन्धविन्यासवैदग्ध्यनिधिर्निबन्धं चक्रे Vās.<BR>—5 A compendium.<BR>—6 Restraint, obstruction, confinement.<BR>—7 Suppression of urine.<BR>—8 A bond, fetter.<BR>—9 A grant of property, an assignment of cattle, money &c. for support;<BR> भूर्या पितामहोपात्ता निबन्धो द्रव्यमेव वा Y. 2. 121.<BR>—10 Fixed property.<BR>—11 Foundation, origin.<BR>—12 Cause, reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धम्
निबन्धः + .{@-धम्@} Song, singing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निबन्धपुस्तकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धपुस्तकम्
निबन्धः + -पुस्तकम् a register; निबन्धपुस्तकस्थानं च कारयेत् Kau. A. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धनम्
निबन्धनम्<BR>—1 The act of fastening, binding together; तं ददर्श यवक्रीतो यन्त्रवन्तं<BR> निबन्धने Mb. 3. 135. 34.<BR>—2 Constructing, building.<BR>—3 Restraining, checking, confining.<BR>—4 A bond, fetter.<BR>—5 A tie, band, support, stay; आशानिबन्धनं जाता जीवलोकस्य U. 3;<BR> यस्त्वमिव मामकीनस्य मनसो द्वितीयं निबन्धनम् Māl. 3.<BR>—6 Dependence, connection;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">Page0902-1</a>]<BR> ते त्वदाशानिबन्धनाः M. 4. 14; परस्परनिबन्धनः Pt. 1. 79 ‘interdependent’.<BR>—7 Cause, origin, ground, motive, basis, foundation; वाक्प्रतिष्ठानिबन्धनानि<BR> देहिनां व्यवहारतन्त्राणि Māl. 4 based on, &c.; प्रत्याशा˚ 3; अनिबन्धन<BR> causeless, accidental; U. 5, 7.<BR>—8 Abode, seat, receptacle; सहजविलासनिबन्धनं शरीरम् Māl. 2. 6.<BR>—9 Composing, arrangement (रचना); संस्कारपूतेन वरं वरेण्यं<BR> वधूं सुखग्राह्यनिबन्धनेन Ku. 7. 90.<BR>—10 A literary composition or work, a treatise; Śi. 2. 112.<BR>—11 A grant (of land), an assignment; सद्वृत्तिः सन्निबन्धना Śi. 2. 112<BR> (where निबन्धन means ‘a treatise’ also).<BR>—12 The peg of a lute.<BR>—13 (In gram.) Syntax.<BR>—14 A commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0901-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धनी
निबन्धनी A bond, fetter, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धिन्|निबंधिन्
निबन्धिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Binding, fastening, confining.<BR>—2 Connected with.<BR>—3 Causing, being the origin of, producing,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबर्हण|निबर्हणं
निब(व)र्हण <i>a.</i> Destroying, destroyer, enemy (in comp.); अनपायि<BR> निबर्हणं द्विषां न तितिक्षासममस्ति साधनम् Ki. 2. 43; Mv. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हण
निब(व)र्हण <i>a.</i> Destroying, destroyer, enemy (in comp.); अनपायि<BR> निबर्हणं द्विषां न तितिक्षासममस्ति साधनम् Ki. 2. 43; Mv. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबर्हणम्
निब(व)र्हण + .{@-नम्@} Killing, destruction, annihilation, slaughter; निबर्हणं<BR> धर्मधनैर्विगर्हितं विशिष्य विश्वासजुषां द्विषामपि N. 1. 131; इहैव<BR> तु त्वया स्थेयं ताम्रानननिबर्हणे Śiva B. 29. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबर्हित
निबर्हित <i>a.</i> Destroyed, removed (अपहृत); कृतः कृतार्थोऽस्मि<BR> निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबिड
निबिड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dense, thick; कालिकेव निबिडा बलाकिनी R. 11. 15.<BR>—2 Hard, difficult; R. 9. 58; पर्यङ्कबन्धं निबिडं बिभेद Ku. 3. 59.<BR> See निबिड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबिडित
निबिडित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Become thick, heavy; जलनिबिडितवस्त्रव्यक्तनिम्नोन्नताभिः Māl. 4. 10.<BR>—2 Pressed close to; (देहि मे) लङ्काभर्तुर्निबिडितकुचामादरादङ्कपालीम् B. R. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबिरीस
निबिरीस <i>a.</i> See निबिड; ‘निबिडं निबिरीसं च दृढं गाढं प्रचक्षते’,<BR> इति वैजयन्ती; उरुनिबिरीसनितम्बभारखेदि Śi. 7. 20; निबिरीसगुणस्तोमः<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 438.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबुध्
निबुध् €1 P.<BR>—1 To know, understand, learn; निबोध साधो तव चेत् कुतूहलम्<BR> Ku. 5. 52, 3. 14; Ms. 1. 68; Y. 1. 2.<BR>—2 To regard or consider as, deem.<BR>—3 To listen or attend to. ━<i>Caus.</i> To explain, inform, acquaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबोधः|निबोध
निबोधः, -धनम्<BR>—1 Understanding, learning.<BR>—2 Acquainting, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबोधनम्
निबोधः, -धनम्<BR>—1 Understanding, learning.<BR>—2 Acquainting, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभ|निभः
निभ [नि-भा-क] (At the end of comp. only) Like, similar, resembling;<BR> उद्बुद्धमुग्धकनकाब्जनिभं वहन्ती Māl. 1. 40; Me. 83; so चन्द्रनिभानना &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभः|निभ
निभ + .{@-भः, -भम्@}<BR>—1 appearance, light, manifestation.<BR>—2 Pretence, disguise, pretext,<BR>—3 A trick, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभम्
निभ + .{@-भः, -भम्@}<BR>—1 appearance, light, manifestation.<BR>—2 Pretence, disguise, pretext,<BR>—3 A trick, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभल्
निभल् €10 U. To see, behold, perceive, look at; निभाल्य भूयो निजगौरिमाणं<BR> मा नाम मानं सहसैव यासीः Bv. 2. 176; or यन्मां न भामिनि निभालयसि<BR> प्रभातनीलारविन्दमदभङ्गिपदैः कटाक्षैः 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभालनम्
निभालनम् Seeing, sight, perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभालित
निभालित <i>a.</i> Seen; कति नो विषया निभालिताः Sūkti. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभूत|निभूतं
निभूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Quite frightened (अत्यन्तभीत).<BR>—2 Gone, past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृत|निभृतः
निभृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Placed down, deposited, lowered.<BR>—2 Filled with, full of; चिन्तया निभृतः Bhāg. 10. 32. 20.<BR>—3 Concealed, hidden, out of sight, unperceived, unobserved; निभृतो<BR> भूत्वा Pt. 1; नभसा निभृतेन्दुना R. 8. 15 ‘with the moon become invisible, about to set or go down’<BR>; Ve. 6. 2; Śi. 6. 20.<BR>—4 Secret, covert; अणुदीर्णवर्णनिभृतार्थमाह्वयत् Śi. 13. 42.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Still, silent; निभृतद्विरेफम् (काननम्) Ku. 3. 42, 6. 2.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Steady, fixed, immovable, motionless; निष्कम्पचामरशिखा निभृतोर्ध्वकर्णाः Ś. 1. 8.<BR>—6 Mild, gentle; अनिभृता वायवः Ki. 13. 66 ‘not gentle, violent or strong’<BR>; Māl. 2. 12; Mv. 3. 14; स्वजननिभृतः सर्वोऽप्येवं मृदुः परिभूयते<BR> Pratimā 1. 18.<BR>—7 Modest, humble; अनिमृतकरेषु प्रियेषु Me. 70; प्रणामनिभृता<BR> कुलवधूरिव Mu. 1; वधनिमृतसिंहाश्च गिरयः Pañc. 1. 3; अद्यप्रभृति<BR> निभृता भवन्ति 2; युक्तं चतुर्भिर्निभृतैस्तुरङ्गैः (रथम्) Bu. C. 3. 8.<BR>—8 Firm, resolute.<BR>—9 Lonely, solitary; (निभृतनिकुञ्जगृहं गतया) Gīt. 2.<BR>—10 Shut, closed (as a door).<BR>—11 True, faithful, firmly attached.<BR>—12 Inactive (निष्क्रिय, त्यक्तोद्योग); निभृता नरेन्द्राः Rām. 4. 28. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृता
निभृत + .{@-ता@} A kind of riddle; Kāv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतम्
निभृत + .{@-तम्@} Modesty, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतम्
निभृत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Secretly, covertly, privately, unperceived; Ś. 3; Śi. 3. 74; Ms. 9. 263.<BR>—2 Silently, quietly; K. 134.<BR>—3 Out of sight, in a corner.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निभृताचार, निभृतात्मन्, निभृतस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृताचार
निभृत + -आचार <i>a.</i> of resolute conduct, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतात्मन्
निभृत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> firm, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतस्थित
निभृत + -स्थित <i>a.</i> standing unperceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमः|निम
निमः A (wooden) pin, stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमदः|निमद
निमदः A distinct but slow pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्र्|निमंत्र्
निमन्त्र् €10 Ā. To invite, call, summon; दिग्भ्यो निमन्त्रिताश्चैनमभिजग्मुर्महर्षयः<BR> R. 15. 59, 11. 32; Y. 1. 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रणम्
निमन्त्रणम्<BR>—1 Invitation. —2 Summoning, calling; निमन्त्रणार्थं दूतांश्च प्रेषयामास<BR> शीघ्रगान् Mb. 3. 256. 6.<BR>—2 A summons.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निमन्त्रणपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रणपत्रम्
निमन्त्रणम् + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 an invitation card or note.<BR>—2 a summons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमयः|निमय
निमयः Barter, exchange; पक्वेनामस्य निमयं न प्रशंसन्ति साधवः Mb. 12. 78. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमस्ज्
निमस्ज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To sink, sink down or under, sink into (fig. also); यथा प्लवेनौपलेन<BR> निमज्जत्युदके तरन् । तथा निमज्जतोऽधस्तादज्ञौ दातृप्रतीच्छकौ Ms. 4. 194, 5. 73;<BR> शोके मुहुश्चाविरतं न्यमाङ्क्षीत् Bk. 3. 30, 15. 31; Śi. 9. 74;<BR> Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 To be merged into, merge, disappear, escape observation; एको हि दोषो<BR> गुणसंनिपाते निमज्जतीन्दोः किरणेष्विवाङ्कः Ku. 1. 3.<BR>—3 To immerse in water, cause to sink down. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to dive under water; अप्सु चैनं निमज्जयेत् Ms. 8. 114.<BR>—2 To cause to penetrate; ततो मर्मसु मर्मज्ञो मज्जयन्निशिताञ्शरान्<BR> Rām. 6. 45. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0902-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्न
निमग्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Plunged, dipped into, immersed, submerged, sunk (fig. also); वल्मीकार्धनिमग्नमूर्तिः<BR> Ś. 7. 11; निमग्नस्य पयोराशौ, चिन्तानिमग्न &c.<BR>—2 Gone down, set (as the sun).<BR>—3 Overwhelmed, covered.<BR>—4 Depressed, not prominent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निमग्ननाभिः, निमग्नमध्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्ननाभिः|निमग्ननाभि
निमग्न + -नाभिः, -मध्या (a woman) having a depressed navel or a slender waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्नमध्या
निमग्न + -नाभिः, -मध्या (a woman) having a depressed navel or a slender waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जथुः|निमज्जथु
निमज्जथुः<BR>—1 The act of diving or entering into, plunging.<BR>—2 Plunging into the bed, sleeping, going to bed; तल्पे कान्तान्तरैः<BR> सार्धं मन्येऽहं धिङ् निमज्जथुम् Bk. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जनम्
निमज्जनम् Bathing, diving, plunging, sinking (lit. and fig.); दृङ्<BR> निमज्जनमुपैति सुधायाम् N. 5. 94; एवं संसारगहने उन्मज्जननिमज्जने Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमा
निमा €3 Ā. To measure; see मा; शक्तिं श्रेष्ठां कुण्डलाभ्यां निमाय<BR> Mb. 7. 179. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमानम्
निमानम् [संख्याया गुणस्य निमाने मयट्; P. V. 2. 47]<BR>—1 Measure.<BR>—2 Price (निमानं = मूल्यम् Sk.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिः|निमि
निमिः<BR>—1 Winking, twinkling (of the eyes).<BR>—2 N. of one of the descendants of Ikṣvāku, and ancestor of the line<BR> of kings who ruled in Mithilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित
निमित<BR>—1 See निर्मित; caused; शापो मयैव निमितस्तदवैत विप्राः Bhāg. 3. 16. 26.<BR>—2 Measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तम्
निमित्तम् [नि-मिद्-क्त Tv.]<BR>—1 A cause, motive, ground reason; निमित्तनैमित्तिकयोरयं क्रमः Ś. 7. 30.<BR>—2 The instrumental or efficient cause (opp. उपादान); धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणां<BR> निमित्तान्यविरोधतः Bhāg. 3. 7. 32.<BR>—3 Any apparent cause, pretext; निमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन् Bg. 11. 33;<BR> निमित्तमात्रेण पाण्डवक्रोधेन भवितव्यम् Ve. 1.<BR>—4 A mark, sign, token.<BR>—5 A butt, mark, target; निमित्ते दूरपातित्वे लघुत्वे दृढवेधने Mb. 7. 74. 23;<BR> निमित्तादपराद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येव वल्गितम् Śi. 2. 27.<BR>—6 An omen, prognostic (good or bad); निमित्तं सूचयित्वा Ś. 1; निमित्तानि<BR> च पश्यामि विपरीतानि केशव Bg. 1. 31; R. 1. 86; Ms. 6. 50; Y. 1. 203, 3. 171.<BR>—7 Means of knowledge; तस्य निमित्तपरीष्टिः MS. 1. 1. 3.<BR>—8 Function, ceremony; एतान्येव निमित्तानि मुनीनामूर्ध्वरेतसाम् (कर्तव्यानि);<BR> Mb. 12. 61. 6. (निमित्त is used at the end of comp. in the sense of<BR> ‘caused or occasioned by’; किन्निमित्तोऽयमातङ्कः Ś. 3. निमित्तम्,<BR> निमित्तेन, निमित्तान् ‘because of’, ‘on account of’.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निमित्तार्थः, निमित्तावृत्तिः, निमित्तकालः, निमित्तकृत्, निमित्तज्ञ, निमित्तधर्मः, निमित्तनैमित्तिकम्, निमित्तपरीष्टि, निमित्तमात्रम्, निमित्तविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तार्थः|निमित्तार्थ
निमित्तम् + -अर्थः the infinitive mood (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तावृत्तिः|निमित्तावृत्ति
निमित्तम् + -आवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> dependence on a special cause. {@-कारणम्, -हेतुः@}<BR> an instrumental or efficient cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकालः|निमित्तकाल
निमित्तम् + -कालः a specific time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकृत्
निमित्तम् + -कृत् <i>m.</i> a crow<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तज्ञ
निमित्तम् + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> acquainted with omens (as an astrologer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0903-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

