नियन्त्रणम्
नियन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Checking, reserve, restraint; अनियन्त्रणानुयोगो नाम तपस्विजनः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Restricting, confining (to a particular sense); अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्यैकार्थनियन्त्रणम् S. D. 2.<BR>—3 Guiding, governing.<BR>—4 Defining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रणा
नियन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Checking, reserve, restraint; अनियन्त्रणानुयोगो नाम तपस्विजनः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Restricting, confining (to a particular sense); अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्यैकार्थनियन्त्रणम् S. D. 2.<BR>—3 Guiding, governing.<BR>—4 Defining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रित|नियंत्रित|नियन्त्रितः
नियन्त्रित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Curbed, restrained, checked.<BR>—2 Guided, governed.<BR>—3 Restricted, confined to (a particular sense, as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्
नियम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To restrain, curb, check, control, govern; प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया<BR> Bg. 7. 20; (सुतां) शशाक मेना न नियन्तुमुद्यमात् Ku. 5. 5; ‘could not dissuade her’<BR>, &c.<BR>—2 To suppress, suspend, hold in (as breath, &c.); Ms. 2. 192; न कथंचन<BR> दुर्योनिः प्रकृतिं स्वां नियच्छति Ms. 10. 59 ‘does not suppress or conceal’, &c.<BR>—3 To offer, give; को नः कुले निवपनानि नियच्छतीति Ś. 6. 25.<BR>—4 To punish, chastise; नियन्तव्यश्च राजभिः Ms. 9. 213.<BR>—5 To regulate or direct in general; लोको नियम्यत इवात्मदशान्तरेषु Ś. 4. 2.<BR>—6 To attain, obtain; तालज्ञश्चाप्रयासेन मोक्षमार्गं नियच्छति Y. 3. 115;<BR> Ms. 2. 93.<BR>—7 To put on, assume.<BR>—8 To place upon. ━<i>Caus.</i> (नियमयति)<BR>—1 To restrain, control, regulate, check, punish; नियमयसि विमार्गप्रस्थितानात्तदण्डः Ś. 5. 8.<BR>—2 To bind, fasten; Śi. 7. 56; R. 5. 73.<BR>—3 To moderate, lessen, mitigate, relieve; छायाद्रुमैर्नियमितार्कमयूखतापः<BR> Ś. 4. 11; Ku. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियत|नियतः
नियत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Curbed, restrained; तं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया Bg. 7. 20.<BR>—2 Subdued, controlled, self-possessed, self-governed.<BR>—3 Abstemious, temperate.<BR>—4 Attentive, intent.<BR>—5 Fixed, permanent, constant, steady; अन्यथासिद्धिशून्यस्य नियता पूर्ववर्तिता Bhāṣā P.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Certain, settled, sure; Pt. 1. 284.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Fixed; प्रकृतिनियतत्वादकृतकः U. 6. 14; fixed in number,<BR> limited; बाणाः पञ्च मनोभवस्य नियतास्तेषामसंख्यो जनः (लक्ष्यः) Ratn. 3. 3.<BR>—7 Inevitable.<BR>—8 Positive, definite.<BR>—9 Forming the subject of consideration, relevant or irrelevant; see तुल्ययोगिता.<BR>—10 Maintained, observed (as a vow &c.); नियतैकपतिव्रतानि पश्चात्तरुमूलानि<BR> गृहीभवन्ति तेषाम् Ś. 7. 20.<BR>—11 Held back, fastened, tied; पशूनां त्रिशतं तत्र यूपेषु नियतं<BR> तदा Rām. 1. 14. 32.<BR>—12 Connected with, dependent on; वाच्यर्था नियताः सर्वे Ms. 4. 256.<BR>—13 (in gram.) Pronounced with अनुदात्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतम्
नियत + .{@-तम्@} (pl.) (in Sāṅkhya) the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतम्
नियत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Always, constantly.<BR>—2 Positively, certainly, invariably, inevitably, surely.<BR>—3 Forcibly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नियतकाल, नियतमानस, नियतवाच, नियतव्रत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतकाल
नियत + -काल <i>a.</i> Limited in time, temporary; Kāśi. on P. I. 4. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतमानस
नियत + -मानस <i>a.</i> of subdued mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतवाच
नियत + -वाच <i>a.</i> limited as to the use of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतव्रत
नियत + -व्रत <i>a.</i> pious, religious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतिः|नियति
नियतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Restraint, restriction.<BR>—2 Destiny, fate, luck, fortune (good or bad); (sometimes personified<BR> as a goddess, the sister of Āyati, both being daughters of Meru and wives<BR> of Dhātṛ and Vidhātṛ); नियतिबलान्नु Dk.; नियतेर्नियोगात्<BR> Śi. 4. 34; Ki. 2. 12, 4. 21.<BR>—3 A religious duty or obligation; नियतिः कारणं लोके नियतिः कर्मसाधनम् ।<BR> नियतिः सर्वभूतानां नियोगेष्विह कारणम् ॥ Rām. 4. 25. 4.<BR>—4 Self-command, self-restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तृ|नियंतृ
नियन्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A charioteer, driver; नियन्तरि व्याकुलमुक्तरज्जुके Śi. 12. 24.<BR>—2 A governor, ruler, master, regulator; न व्यतीयुः प्रजास्तस्य नियन्तुर्नेमिवृत्तयः<BR> R. 1. 17, 15. 51.<BR>—3 A punisher, chastiser.<BR>—4 The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमः|नियम
नियमः<BR>—1 Restraining, checking.<BR>—2 Taming, subduing.<BR>—3 Confining, preventing.<BR>—4 A restraint, check; वाचि नियमः U. 2. 2; अधर्मानियमः Ms. 8. 122.<BR>—5 Restriction, limitation; Mb. 14. 13. 11.<BR>—6 A rule or precept, law (in general), usage; नायमेकान्ततो नियमः Ś. B.<BR>—7 Regularity; कुसुमसुकुमारमूर्तिर्दधती नियमेन तनुतरं मध्यम् Ratn. 1. 20.<BR>—8 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>—9 An agreement, promise, vow, engagement.<BR>—10 Necessity, obligation.<BR>—11 Any voluntary or self-imposed religious observance (dependent on external<BR> conditions); [The earliest explanation of this expression is the one found<BR> in the ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 24. cf. कोऽयं नियमः । अनियतस्य नियतता ।<BR> प्रयोगाङ्गतया सर्वे देशाः प्राप्नुवन्ति, न तु समच्चयेन । यदा समो<BR> न तदा विषमः । यदा विषमो न तदा समः । स एष समः प्राप्तश्चाप्राप्तश्च ।<BR> यदा न प्राप्तः स पक्षो विधिं प्रयोजयति. This is very nicely stated<BR> in the Vārttika━ ‘नियमः पाक्षिके सति’]; R. 1. 94; Ki. 5. 40; (see<BR> Malli. on Śi. 13. 23).<BR>—12 Any minor observance or lesser vow, a duty prescribed to be done,<BR> but which is not so obligatory as a यम q. v. शौचमिज्या तपो दानं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">Page0905-1</a>]<BR> स्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहः । व्रतमौनोपवासं च स्नानं च नियमा दश ॥ Atri.<BR>—13 Penance, devotion, religious austerities; नियमविध्नकारिणी Ś. 1; R. 15. 74.<BR>—14 (In Mīm. phil.) A rule or precept which lays down or <i>specifies</i><BR> something which, in the absence of that rule, would be <i>optional</i>;<BR> विधिरत्यन्तमप्राप्तौ नियमः पाक्षिके सति.<BR>—15 (In Yoga phil.) Restraint of the mind, the second of the 8 principal<BR> steps of meditation in <i>Yoga</i>; दशैते नियमाः प्रोक्ता योगशास्त्रविशारदैः Tantrasāra.<BR>—16 (In Rhet.) A poetical common place or convention, as the description<BR> of the cuckoo in spring, peacocks in the rains &c.<BR>—17 Defining, definition.<BR>—18 Keeping down, lowering (as the voice).<BR>—19 Keeping secret; मन्त्रस्य नियमं कुर्याः Mb. 5. 141. 20.<BR>—20 Effort (यत्न); यथैते नियमं पौराः कुर्वन्त्यस्मिन्निवर्तने<BR> Mb. 2. 46. 20. (नियमेन as a rule, invariably).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नियमोपमा, नियमनिष्ठा, नियमपत्रम्, नियमविधिः, नियमस्थ, नियमस्थितिः, नियमहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0904-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमोपमा
नियमः + -उपमा a simile which expressly states that something can be compared<BR> only with something else. {@-धर्मः@} a law prescribing restraints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमनिष्ठा
नियमः + -निष्ठा rigid observance of prescribed rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमपत्रम्
नियमः + -पत्रम् a written agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमविधिः
नियमः + -विधिः a religious rite, daily ritual; नियमविधिजलानां बर्हिषां<BR> चोपनेत्री Ku. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमस्थ
नियमः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> observing penance; Ku. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमस्थितिः|नियमस्थिति
नियमः + -स्थितिः <i>f.</i> steady observance of religious obligations, asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमहेतुः|नियमहेतु
नियमः + -हेतुः a regulating cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमनम्
नियमनम्<BR>—1 Checking, punishing, restraining, subduing; नियमनादसतां च नराधिपः R. 9. 6.<BR>—2 Restriction, limitation.<BR>—3 Humiliation.<BR>—4 A precept, fixed rule.<BR>—5 Binding, tying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमवती
नियमवती A woman having the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमित|नियमितः
नियमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Checked, curbed, restrained.<BR>—2 Moderated, tempered.<BR>—3 Removed, lessened; नियमितपरिखेदा Ku. 1. 60.<BR>—4 Governed, guided.<BR>—5 Regulated, prescribed, laid down.<BR>—6 Fixed, agreed upon, stipulated.<BR>—7 Bound, confined; ब्रह्मा येन कुलालवन्नियमितो ब्रह्माण्डभाण्डोदरे. Bh.<BR>—8 Observed (as a vow or penance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामः|नियाम
नियामः<BR>—1 Restraint.<BR>—2 A religious vow.<BR>—3 A boatman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामक|नियामकः
नियामक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Restraining, checking.<BR>—2 Subduing, overpowering.<BR>—3 Limiting, restricting, defining more closely.<BR>—4 Guiding, governing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामकः|नियामक
नियामक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A master, ruler.<BR>—2 A charioteer.<BR>—3 A boatman, sailor.<BR>—4 A pilot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामकता
नियामकता<BR>—1 Controlling.<BR>—2 Exact definition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियवः|नियव
नियवः Ved.<BR>—1 Mixing, mixture.<BR>—2 A continuous line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियानम्
नियानम् Ved. A cow-pen; यन्नियानं न्ययनम् Rv. 10. 19. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियातन|नियातनं
नियातन See निपातन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्
नियुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To appoint, depute, order (with loc.) यन्मां विधेयविषये स भवान्नियुङ्क्ते<BR> Māl. 1. 9; असाधुदर्शी तत्रभवान् काश्यपः य इमामाश्रमधर्मे नियुङ्क्ते<BR> Ś. 1; Ku. 3. 13; R. 5. 29.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">Page0905-2</a>]<BR>—2 To join, unite, fasten to.<BR>—3 To prescribe, ordain.<BR>—4 To yoke, harness (as horses).<BR>—5 To employ, engage.<BR>—6 To authorize.<BR>—7 To commit, consign, entrust.<BR>—8 To urge, incite, constrain.<BR>—9 To trouble, harass. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To join, unite, provide, or endow with, give to; (स्मरं) वपुषा<BR> खेन नियोजयिष्यति Ku. 4. 42.<BR>—2 To yoke, harness.<BR>—3 To incite, urge; तत् किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव Bg. 3. 1;<BR> प्रश्नकर्मणि मां नियोजयति K.; Pt. 5. 81.<BR>—4 To appoint, employ; ईदृशेषु नियोगेषु नियोजिता Mu. 6.<BR>—5 To use, employ; स्थानेष्वेव नियोक्तव्या भृत्याश्चाभरणानि च Pt. 1. 72; Ku. 4. 15.<BR>—6 To devote, apply.<BR>—7 To expose, put to; श्रमाय मां नियोजयसि Pt. 2.<BR>—8 To accomplish, perform (a rite); पूर्वं दैवं नियोजयेत् Ms. 3. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्त|नियुक्तः
नियुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Directed, ordered, instructed, commanded.<BR>—2 Authorised, appointed; नियुक्तः क्षत्रियो द्रव्ये खड्गं दर्शयते<BR> ध्रुवम् H. 2. 95.<BR>—3 Permitted to raise issue; see नियोग (7) below.<BR>—4 Attached to.<BR>—5 Fastened to.<BR>—6 Ascertained.<BR>—7 Prompted, incited.<BR>—8 Used, employed; नियुक्तौ हव्यकव्ययोः Ms. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्तः|नियुक्त
नियुक्त + .{@-क्तः@} A functionary, an officer, any one charged with some business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्तम्
नियुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> By all means, necessarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्तिः|नियुक्ति
नियुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Injunction, order, command.<BR>—2 Appointment, commission, office, charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तव्य
नियोक्तव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be placed in or put to.<BR>—2 To be appointed, intrusted, charged.<BR>—3 To be harassed, prosecuted; न स राज्ञा नियोक्तव्यः Ms. 8. 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तृ
नियोक्तृ <i>m.</i> An employer, a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगः|नियोग
नियोगः<BR>—1 Employment, use, application.<BR>—2 An injunction, order, command, direction, commission, charge, appointed<BR> task or duty, any business committed to oneʼs care; यः सावज्ञो माधवश्रीनियोगे<BR> M. 5. 8; मनो नियोगक्रिययोत्सुकं मे R. 5. 11; अथवा नियोगः खल्वीदृशो<BR> मन्दभाग्यस्य U. 1; आज्ञापयतु को नियोगोऽनुष्ठीयतामिति Ś. 1; त्वमपि<BR> स्वनियोगमशून्यं कुरु ‘go about your own business’, ‘do your appointed duty’<BR>, (frequently occurring in plays, and used as a courteous way of<BR> asking servants to withdraw).<BR>—3 Fastening or attaching to.<BR>—4 Necessity, obligation; तत् सिषेवे नियोगेन स विकल्पपराङ्मुखः R. 17. 49.<BR>—5 Effort, exertion.<BR>—6 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>—7 An invariable rule; न चैष नियोगो वृत्तिपक्षे नित्यः; समास इति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 5.<BR>—8 Commission, act; न कर्ता कस्यचित् कश्चिन्नियोगेनापि चेश्वरः Rām. 4. 25. 5.<BR>—9 Right (अधिकार); अलघुनि बहु मेनिरे च ताः स्वं कुलिशभृता विहितं<BR> पदे नियोगम् Ki. 10. 16.<BR>—10 A practice prevalent in ancient times which permitted a childless<BR> widow to have intercourse with the brother or any near kinsman of her deceased<BR> husband to raise up issue to him, the son so born being called क्षेत्रज;<BR> cf. Ms. 9. 59:− देवराद्वा सपिण्डाद्वा स्त्रिया सम्यङ् नियुक्तया । प्रजेप्सिताधिगन्तव्या<BR> सन्तानस्य परिक्षये ॥; see 60, 65 also. (Vyāsa begot पाण्डु and<BR> धृतराष्ट्र on the widows of विचित्रवीर्य in this way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0905-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगिन्
नियोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Appointed, employed.<BR>—2 Authorized. ━<i>m.</i> An officer, dependent, minister, functionary; अपराधेऽपि<BR> निःशङ्को नियोगी चिरसेवकः H. 2. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग्यः|नियोग्य
नियोग्यः A lord, master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजनम्
नियोजनम्<BR>—1 Fastening, attaching.<BR>—2 Ordering, prescribing.<BR>—3 Urging, impelling.<BR>—4 Appointing.<BR>—5 Ved. That with which anything is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजनी
नियोजनम् + .{@-नी@} A halter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजित
नियोजित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Directed, ordered.<BR>—2 Appointed.<BR>—3 Joined to.<BR>—4 Instigated, incited.<BR>—5 Used, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोज्यः|नियोज्य
नियोज्यः One charged with any duty, a functionary, an officer, a<BR> servant, employee; सिध्यन्ति कर्मसु महत्स्वपि यन्नियोज्याः Ś. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत्
नियुत् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A horse, particularly of Vāyu.<BR>—2 A praiser. ━<i>f.</i> A line, row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुतम्
नियुतम्<BR>—1 A million.<BR>—2 A hundred thousand.<BR>—3 Ten thousand crores or 100 Ayutas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुद्धम्
नियुद्धम् Fighting on foot, close fight, personal struggle, wrestling;<BR> तिष्ठेदानीं सुसन्नद्धो नियुद्धे नास्ति मत्समः Madhyamavyāyoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोद्धृ
नियोद्धृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A combatant, wrestler.<BR>—2 A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोधकः|नियोधक
नियोधकः A combatant, wrestler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0906-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्
निर् <i>ind.</i> A substitute for निस् before vowels and soft consonants<BR> conveying the senses of ‘out of’, ‘away from’, ‘without’, ‘free from’,<BR> and be frequently expressed by ‘less’, ‘un’, used with the noun; see the<BR> compounds given below; see निस् and cf. अ also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निरंश, निरक्षः, निरक्षर, निरग्नि, निरग्र, निरग्रक, निरङ्कुश, निरघ, निरङ्ग, निरजिन, निरञ्जन, निरतिशय, निरत्यय, निरधिष्ठान, निरध्व, निरनुक्रोश, निरनुग, निरनुग्रह, निरनुनासिक, निरनुमान, निरनुयोज्य, निरनुरोध, निरन्तर, निरन्तराल, निरन्धस्, निरन्वय, निरपत्रप, निरपराध, निरपवर्त, निरपवाद, निरपाय, निरपेक्ष, निरपेक्षित, निरपेक्षिन्, निरभिभव, निरभिमान, निरभिलाष, निरभिसंधानम्, निरभ्र, निरमर्ष, निरम्बर, निरम्बु, निरर्गल, निरर्थ, निरर्थक, निरलंकृतिः, निरवकाश, निरवग्रह, निरवद्य, निरवधि, निरवयव, निरवलम्ब, निरवशेष, निरवसाद, निरव्यय, निरशन, निरश्रि, निरष्ट, निरस्त्र, निरस्थि, निरहंकार, निरहंकृति, निरहंकृत, निरहम्, निराकाङ्क्ष, निराकार, निराकृति, निराकाश, निराकुल, निराक्रन्द, निराक्रोश, निरागम, निरागस्, निराचार, निराडम्बर, निरातङ्क, निरातप, निरादर, निरादान, निराधार, निराधि, निरानन्द, निरान्त्र, निरापद्, निराबाध, निरामय, निरामिष, निराय, निरायः, निरायत, निरायतत्वम्, निरायति, निरायास, निरायुध, निरारम्भ, निरालम्ब, निरालोक, निरावर्ण, निराश, निराशक, निराशिन्, निराशङ्क, निराशा, निराशिस्, निराश्रय, निरास्वाद, निराहार, निरिङ्ग, निरिच्छ, निरिन्द्रिय, निरिन्धन, निरीति, निरीश्वर, निरीषम्, निरीह, निरुच्छ्वास, निरुत्तर, निरुत्थ, निरुद्धति, निरुत्सव, निरुत्साह, निरुत्सुक, निरुदक, निरुदर, निरुद्यम, निरुद्योग, निरुद्विग्न, निरुद्वेग, निरुपक्रम, निरुपद्रव, निरुपधि, निरुपपत्ति, निरुपपद, निरुपप्लव, निरुपभोग, निरुपम, निरुपसर्ग, निरुपस्कृत, निरुपहत, निरुपाख्य, निरुपाधि, निरुपाधिक, निरुपाय, निरुपेक्ष, निरुष्मन्, निर्गन्ध, निर्गर्व, निर्गवाक्ष, निर्गुण, निर्गृह,^1 निर्गौरव, निर्ग्रन्थ, निर्ग्रन्थक, निर्ग्रन्थिक, निर्घटम्, निर्घण्टः, निर्घृण, निर्घृणा, निर्घोष, निर्जन, निर्जन्तु, निर्जर, निर्जरायु, निर्जल, निर्जाड्य, निर्जिह्वः, निर्जीव, निर्ज्ञाति, निर्ज्वर, निर्दण्डः, निर्दय, निर्दयम्, निर्दश, निर्दशन, निर्दाक्षिण्य, नि