निर्वासनम्
निर्वासः, -निर्वासनम्<BR>—1 Expulsion, banishment.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—3 Leaving oneʼs home, living abroad (निर्वास only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0918-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासित|निर्व्वासित
निर्वासित <i>a.</i> Expelled, banished; spent (as time), driven out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0918-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वास्य|निर्व्वास्य
निर्वास्य <i>a.</i> Fit to be expelled; निर्वास्या व्यभिचारिण्यः प्रतिकूलास्तथैव च Y. 2. 142<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0918-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वह्
निर्वह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To carry out, extricate oneself.<BR>—2 To be finished.<BR>—3 To live upon, live by the aid of. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To take to the end of, complete, finish, manage; यथा प्रियसखी बन्धुजनशोचनीया<BR> न भवति तथा निर्वाहय Ś. 3.<BR>—2 To carry out, accomplish, effect.<BR>—3 To pass, spend (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0918-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वहणम्
निर्वहणम्<BR>—1 End, completion; यान्ति निर्वहणमस्य संसृतिक्लेशनाटकविडम्बनाविधेः Ś. 14. 63.<BR>—2 Maintaining, carrying to the end, sustaining; मानस्य निर्वहणम् Amaru. 24.<BR>—3 Destruction, annihilation.<BR>—4 (In dramas) The catastrophe, the last stage in which the action of the play<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">Page0919-1</a>]<BR> is brought to a head, the denouement; तत्किंनिमित्तं कुकविकृतनाटकस्येव<BR> अन्यन्मुखेऽन्यन्निर्वहणे Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0918-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहितृ
निर्वाहितृ <i>a.</i> Accomplisher, producer; आकाशो वै नाम नामरूपयोर्निर्वहिता<BR> Ch. Up. 8. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहः|निर्वाह|निर्व्वाह|निर्व्वाहः
निर्वाहः<BR>—1 Carrying on, accomplishing, performing.<BR>—2 Completion, end.<BR>—3 Carrying to the end, supporting, steadfast adherence, perseverance;<BR> निर्वाहः प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु सतामेतद्धि गोत्रव्रतम् Mu. 2. 18.<BR>—4 Subsisting on.<BR>—5 Sufficiency, competent provision, competency.<BR>—6 Describing, narrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहण|निर्व्वाहण|निर्व्वाहणं
निर्वाहण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Carrying out, effecting.<BR>—2 Removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहणम्
निर्वाहण + .{@-णम्@} Accomplishment, completion; see निर्वहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहिन्
निर्वाहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Effecting.<BR>—2 Discharging (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वा|निर्व्वा
निर्वा €2 P.<BR>—1 To blow.<BR>—2 To be cooled, be cool or assuaged (fig. also); वपुर्जलार्द्रापवनैर्न<BR> निर्ववौ Śi. 1. 65; त्वयि दृष्ट एव तस्या निर्वाति मनो मनोभवज्वलितम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 To blow out, be extinguished, be extinct; निर्वाणदीपे किमु तैलदानम्<BR> Subhāṣ.; निर्वाणभूयिष्ठमथास्य वीर्यं संधुक्षयन्तीव वपुर्गुणेन<BR> Ku. 3. 52; Śi. 14. 85; Mu. 3. 28. ━<i>Caus.</i> (निर्वापयति)<BR>—1 To blow or put out, extinguish, destroy, kill; शशाक निर्वापयितुं<BR> न वासवः R. 3. 58.<BR>—2 To cool, alleviate the heat of, act as a refrigerant; सखि अन्यादृश<BR> एव तेऽद्य निर्वापयति शरीरस्पर्शः Māl. 6; Ratn. 3. 11; R. 19. 56, 3<BR> To gratify, soothe, comfort; निर्वाप्य प्रियसंदेशैः सीतामक्षबधोद्धतः R. 12. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाण|निर्व्वाण|निर्व्वाणं|निर्व्वाणः
निर्वाण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Blown or put out, extinguished (as a lamp or fire); निर्वाणवैरदहनाः<BR> प्रशमादरीणाम् Ve. 1. 7; Ku. 2. 23.<BR>—2 Lost, disappeared.<BR>—3 Dead, deceased.<BR>—4 Liberated from existence.<BR>—5 Set (as the sun).<BR>—6 Calmed, quieted.<BR>—7 Plunged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणम्
निर्वाण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Extinction; अपि निर्वाणमायाति नानलो याति शीतताम् H. 1. 131; शनैर्निर्वाणमाप्नोति<BR> निरिन्धन इवानलः Mb.<BR>—2 Vanishing from sight, disappearance.<BR>—3 Dissolution, death.<BR>—4 Final liberation or emancipation from matter and reunion with the Supreme<BR> Spirit, eternal bliss; निर्वाणं नाधिगच्छेयुर्जीवेयुः पशुजीविकाम् Mb. 3. 31, 26;<BR> निर्वाणमपि मन्येऽहमन्तरायं जयश्रियः Ki. 11. 69; R. 12. 1.<BR>—5 (With Buddhists) Absolute extinction or annihilation, complete extinction<BR> of individual or worldly existence.<BR>—6 Perfect and perpetual calm, repose; निर्वाणं समुपगमेन यच्छते<BR> ते (नमः) Ki. 18. 39.<BR>—7 Complete satisfaction or pleasure, supreme bliss, highest felicity;<BR> स योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति Bg. 5. 24; अये लब्धं<BR> नेत्रनिर्वाणम् Ś. 3; M. 3. 1; Śi. 4. 23; V. 3. 21.<BR>—8 Cessation, desisting.<BR>—9 Vacuity.<BR>—10 Union, association, confluence.<BR>—11 The bathing of an elephant; as in अनिर्वाण R. 1. 71.<BR>—12 Instruction in sciences.<BR>—13 Finis, completion; प्राप्य संकल्पनिर्वाणं नातिप्रीतोऽभ्यगात् पुरम्<BR> Bhāg. 4. 9. 27.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निर्वाणपुराणम्, निर्वाणभूयिष्ठ, निर्वाणमस्तकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणपुराणम्
निर्वाण + -पुराणम् offering oblations to the dead (?); Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणभूयिष्ठ
निर्वाण + -भूयिष्ठ <i>a.</i> almost vanished or departed; see under निर्वा (3) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणमस्तकः|निर्वाणमस्तक|निर्व्वाणमस्तक
निर्वाण + -मस्तकः final emancipation or deliverance, final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापः|निर्वाप|निर्व्वाप|निर्व्वापः
निर्वापः<BR>—1 See निर्वपण and निर्वाप.<BR>—2 Putting out, extinguishing (as fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापणम्
निर्वापणम्<BR>—1 An offering, oblation, a funeral oblation.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR>—3 Putting out, extinguishing.<BR>—4 Pouring out, scattering, sowing (as seed).<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Offering, giving.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Offering oblations (especially funeral).<BR>—6 Allaying, alleviation, pacification; कर्तव्यानि दुःखितैर्दुःखनिर्वापणानि U. 3.<BR>—7 Annihilation.<BR>—8 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—9 Cooling, refreshing; शरीरनिर्वापणाय Ś. 3.<BR>—10 A refrigerant or cooling application; तप्तायःपिण्डसिकतानां वा<BR> निर्वापणं प्रसाधनं च कर्तव्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापयितृ
निर्वापयितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Extinguishing, blowing, blowing out.<BR>—2 Allaying the heat of, cooling; स्मर एव तापहेतुर्निर्वापयिता स<BR> एव मे जातः Ś. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापित|निर्व्वापित
निर्वापित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Extinguished, quenched.<BR>—2 Cooled.<BR>—3 Killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वादः|निर्वाद|निर्व्वाद|निर्व्वादः
निर्वादः<BR>—1 Blame, reproach.<BR>—2 Scandal, bad rumour, obloquy; किमात्मनिर्वादकथामुपेक्षे R. 14. 34; Ki. 2. 10.<BR>—3 Decision of a controversy.<BR>—4 Absence of dispute (वादाभाव); निर्वादैर्निर्वदेदेनम् Mb. 5. 135. 37.<BR>—5 Rumour, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विद्|निर्व्विद्
निर्विद् €4 Ā. To be dissatisfied or disgusted with (with instr.);<BR> निर्विण्णस्य पदं करोति हृदये तस्य स्वतन्त्रस्पृहा Pt. 1. 240. ━<i>f.</i><BR> Despondency, despair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्णः
निर्विण्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Despondent, depressed; निर्विण्णः शुचमेति Mk. 1. 14.<BR>—2 Overcome with fear or sorrow.<BR>—3 Emaciated with grief.<BR>—4 Abused, degraded.<BR>—5 Disgusted with anything; मत्स्याशनस्य निर्विण्णः Pt. 1.<BR>—6 Impaired, decayed.<BR>—7 Humble, modest.<BR>—8 Known, certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेदः|निर्वेद|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेदः<BR>—1 Disgust, loathing.<BR>—2 Satiety, cloy.<BR>—3 Depression of spirits, despair, despondency; निर्वेदो नात्र कर्तव्यः<BR> Mb. 3. 32. 50; परिभवान्निर्वेदमापद्यते Mk. 1. 14.<BR>—4 Humiliation.<BR>—5 Grief.<BR>—6 Complete indifference to wordly objects; तदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य<BR> श्रुतस्य च Bg. 2. 52 (regarded as the feeling which gives rise to the<BR> sentiment called शान्त) (quietude); निर्वेदस्थायिभावोऽस्ति शान्तोऽपि<BR> नवमो रसः K. P. 4; (see R. G. under निर्वेद).<BR>—7 Self-disparagement or humiliation (regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR> feelings); cf. the definition in R. G. under निर्वेद; (the following<BR> is there given as an instance; यदि लक्ष्मण सा मृगेक्षणा न मदीक्षासरणिं<BR> समेष्यति । अमुना जडजीवितेन मे जगता वा विफलेन किं फलम् ॥). —8 Shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विश्
निर्विश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To enjoy; ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति प्रदोषान् R. 6. 34; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः<BR> स दशान्तमुपेयिवान् R. 12. 1, 4. 51, 6. 50, 9. 35, 13. 60, 14. 80, 18. 3, 19. 47;<BR> Me. 112; Ku. 1. 29.<BR>—2 To adorn, embellish.<BR>—3 To settle in a home, become a householder.<BR>—4 To marry; निर्वेष्टुकामस्तु पुरा अष्टावक्रो महातपाः Mb. 13. 19. 11.<BR> निर्वेष्टुकामोऽस्मि नरेन्द्र V. P.<BR>—6 To feel, experience.<BR>—6 To reward, recompense.<BR>—7 To enter into.<BR>—8 To go forth.<BR>—9 To repay<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">Page0920-1</a>]<BR> (a debt); निर्वेष्टव्यं मया तत्र प्राणानपरिरक्षता Mb. 5. 146. 15.<BR>—10 To live together; निरूपितो बालक एव योगिनां शुश्रूषणे प्रावृषि<BR> निर्विविक्षताम् Bhāg. 1. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0919-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्टः
निर्विष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Enjoyed, attained, experienced.<BR>—2 Fully enjoyed or used.<BR>—3 Obtained as wages; निर्विष्टं वैश्यशूद्रयोः Gaut. S.<BR>—4 Married.<BR>—5 Engaged in.<BR>—6 Arrived at, attained to.<BR>—7 One who has maintained the sacred fire.<BR>—8 Entered, sticking in.<BR>—9 Sitting, encamping; निर्विष्टमुदधेः कूले तं प्रपेदे विभीषणः R. 12. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेशः|निर्वेश|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेशः<BR>—1 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>—2 Wages, hire, employment.<BR>—3 Eating, enjoyment, use.<BR>—4 Return of payment; सर्वार्थसम्भवो देहो जनितः पोषितो यतः । न<BR> तयोर्याति निर्वेशं पित्रोर्मर्त्यः शतायुषा ॥ Bhāg. 10. 45. 5.<BR>—5 Expiation, atonement; Bhāg. 5. 26. 18.<BR>—6 Marriage.<BR>—7 Fainting, swooning.<BR>—8 Spreading; L. D. B.<BR>—9 Entering; आत्मनिर्वेशमात्रेण तिर्यग्गतमुलूखलम् (ययौ) Bhāg. 10. 10. 26.<BR>—10 Revenging; अभ्यधावन्नभिक्रुद्धा भ्रातुनिर्वेशकरिणः Bhāg. 10. 44. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृ
निर्वृ €5 U. (usually in <i>p. p.</i> only) To feel happy, be pleased<BR> or satisfied; निर्ववार मधुनीन्द्रियवर्गः Śi. 10. 3. See निर्वृत below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वारित
निर्वारित <i>a.</i> Warded off; Prab. 4. 30/31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Satisfied, contented, happy; निर्वृतौ स्वः Ś. 2, 4, 5. 1.<BR>—2 Free from care or anxiety, secure, at ease.<BR>—3 Ceased, ended. तीर्णे भीष्ममहोदधौ कथमपि द्रोणानले निर्वृते Ve. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृतम्
निर्वृत + .{@-तम्@} A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृतिः|निर्वृति
निर्वृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Satisfaction, happiness, pleasure, bliss; व्रजति निर्वृतिमेकपदे<BR> मनः V. 2. 9; R. 9. 38, 12. 65; Ś. 7. 19; Śi. 4. 64, 10. 28; Ki. 3. 8.<BR>—2 Tranquillity, rest, repose; न जातु बाला लभते स्म निर्वृतिं तुषारसंघातशिलातलेष्वपि<BR> Ku. 5. 55; Pt. 1. 201.<BR>—3 Final emancipation or liberation from worldly existence; द्वारं निर्वृतिसद्मनो<BR> विजयते कृष्णेति वर्णद्वयम् Bv. 4. 14.<BR>—4 Completion, accomplishment.<BR>—5 Freedom.<BR>—6 Disappearance; death, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्
निर्वृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To cease, come to an end; निरवर्त्स्यन् न चेद्वार्ता सीताया वितथैव<BR> नः Bk. 8. 69.<BR>—2 To be got or accomplished; निर्वर्तेतास्य यावद्भिरितिकर्तव्यता नृभिः Ms. 7. 61.<BR>—3 To be with-held, not to happen; निर्वर्त्स्यत्यृतुसंघातः Bk. 16. 6.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> —1 To perform; accomplish, finish, complete; आहारं<BR> निर्वर्तयामास K. 16; R. 2. 45, 3. 33, 11. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तक
निर्वर्तक <i>a.</i> (-र्तिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Completing, accomplishing, executing, performing &c.<BR>—2 Desisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तनम्
निर्वर्तनम्<BR>—1 Accomplishment, completion, execution.<BR>—2 Desisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तिन्
निर्वर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Completing, accomplishing &c.<BR>—2 Acting rudely, uncivil, impolitic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्वृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Accomplished, attained, performed &c.; निर्वृत्तपर्जन्यजलाभिषेका<BR> प्रफुल्लकाशा वसुधेव रेजे Ku. 7. 11.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">Page0920-2</a>]<BR> सा तस्य कर्मनिर्वृतैर्दूरं पश्चात्कृता फलैः R. 17. 18.<BR>—2 Finished, ended; निर्वृत्ते तु क्रतौ तस्मिन् हयमेधे महात्मनः Rām. 1. 18. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निर्वृत्तचूडक^1, निर्वृत्तमात्र<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्तचूडक
निर्वृत्त + -चूडक^1 <i>a.</i> One on whom tonsure has been performed; निर्वृत्तचूडकानां<BR> तु त्रिरात्रात् शुद्धिरिष्यते Ms. 5. 67.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्तमात्र
निर्वृत्त + -मात्र <i>a.</i> just finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्तिः|निर्वृत्ति
निर्वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> (See also under निर्)<BR>—1 Accomplishment, fulfilment; यस्येयं फलनिर्वृत्तिः Mb. 1. 108. 10;<BR> कर्मणां फलनिर्वृत्तिं शंस नस्तत्त्वतः पराम् Ms. 12. 1.<BR>—2 Completion, end.<BR>—3 (In gram.) Discontinuance of the influence of one rule over another<BR> (opp. अनुवृत्ति).<BR>—4 Result, fruit.<BR>—5 Ceasing, desisting, abstaining from.<BR>—6 Inactivity.<BR>—7 Impropriety.<BR>—8 Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टनम्
निर्वेष्टनम् A weaverʼs shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यञ्जक
निर्व्यञ्जक <i>a.</i> Indicating, betraying; प्राप्तः संप्रति रामरावणरणः<BR> स्नेहस्य निर्व्यञ्जकः Mv. 5. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथनम्
निर्व्यथनम्<BR>—1 Extreme pain, paining, afflicting.<BR>—2 Freedom from pain.<BR>—3 A hole, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यध्
निर्व्यध् €4 P. To pierce through, wound, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विद्ध
निर्विद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wounded, killed.<BR>—2 Separated from each other, isolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेध
निर्वेध<BR>—1 Penetration.<BR>—2 Insight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्युषित
निर्व्युषित <i>a.</i> Spent, passed away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्व्यूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Completed, finished; निर्व्यूढं प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु सतामेतद्धि गोत्रव्रतम्<BR> Mu. 2. 18 (v. l.).<BR>—2 Grown, increased, developed; मुहूर्तनिर्व्यूढविस्मय Māl. 7; निर्व्यूढसौहृदभरेति 6. 17<BR> (उपचित Jagaddhara).<BR>—3 Vindicated, fully shown, proved true, carried out faithfully or to<BR> the end; हा तात जटायो निर्व्यूढस्तेऽपत्यस्नेहः U. 3; निर्व्यूढः संभावनाभारो<BR> बुद्धरक्षितया Māl. 8; निर्व्यूढं तातस्य कापालिकत्वम् Māl. 4, 9. 10;<BR> Mv. 7. 8.<BR>—4 Deserted, abandoned; निर्व्यूढा रणसाहसव्यंसनिता Priy. D. 1. 6.<BR>—5 Arrayed in order of battle.<BR>—6 Successful, lucky.<BR>—7 Pushed out, expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढिः|निर्व्यूढि
निर्व्यूढिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 End, completion.<BR>—2 A helmet, crest.<BR>—3 A door, gate.<BR>—4 A peg or bracket projecting from a wall.<BR>—5 Highest point or degree.<BR>—6 Decoction; cf. निर्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूहः|निर्व्यूह
निर्व्यूहः See निर्यूहः<BR>—1 A peg (नागदन्त); द्वारतोरणनिर्व्यूहः Mb. 3. 160. 39.<BR>—2 A particular weapon (यूपिका) Mb. 7. 89. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हादः|निर्हाद
निर्हादः Evacuation, voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृ
निर्हृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To take or draw out from, extract; यद्यर्थिता निर्हृतवाच्यशल्यान्<BR> प्राणान् मया धारयितुं चिरं वः R. 14. 42.<BR>—2 To carry out the dead body; निर्हृत्य तु व्रती प्रेतान्न व्रतेन वियुज्यते<BR> Ms. 5. 91; Y. 3. 15.<BR>—3 To remove (as a fault &c.).<BR>—4 To carry or take away.<BR>—5 To export (goods)<BR>—6 To change or mix together (clothes &c.); न च वासांसि वासोभिर्निर्हरेष्न<BR> च वासयेत् Ms. 8. 396.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0920-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरणम्
निर्हरणम्<BR>—1 Carrying out dead bodies to be burnt, carrying corpses to the funeral<BR> pile; तस्य निर्हरणादीनि … … युधिष्ठिरः कारायित्वा Bhāg. 1. 9. 46.<BR>—2 Taking forth, carrying or drawing out, extracting, removal.<BR>—3 Rooting up, extirpation, destruction.<BR>—4 An antidote (Mar. विषाचा उतारा); तांस्तान् विषविशेषांश्च तत्तन्निर्हरणानि<BR> च Śiva B. 30. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारः|निर्हार
निर्हारः<BR>—1 Taking away, removing, removal.<BR>—2 Drawing out, extracting.<BR>—3 Rooting up, destruction; कर्मणा कर्मनिर्हारो न ह्यात्यन्तिक इष्यते<BR> Bhāg. 6. 1. 11.<BR>—4 Carrying out a dead body to be burnt; एवं विलपतीनां वै परिगृह्य<BR> मृतं पतिम् । अनिच्छतीनां निर्हारमर्कोऽस्तं संन्यवर्तत ॥ Bhāg. 7. 2. 35.<BR>—5 Accumulation of a private store of wealth, private hoard; न निर्हारं<BR> स्त्रियः कुर्युः कुटुम्बाद्बहुमध्यगात् Ms. 9. 199.<BR>—6 Evacuation of the natural excrements of the body (opp. आहार).<BR>—7 Putting forth or out.<BR>—8 Setting aside, excluding, leaving.<BR>—9 Deduction.<BR>—10 Diffusive fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्हारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Carrying out.<BR>—2 Diffusive, spreading wide (as fragrance).<BR>—3 Fragrant.<BR>—4 A kind of fragrance surpassing all others (सर्वगन्धाभिभावको हिङ्ग्वादौ<BR> com. on Mb. 12. 184. 28).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृतिः|निर्हृति
निर्हृतिः <i>f.</i> Taking out of oneʼs way, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रादः|निर्ह्राद
निर्ह्रादः A sound in general; निर्घाता रथनिर्ह्नादा विवरेभ्यः प्रजज्ञिरे<BR> Bhāg. 3. 17. 8; R. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रासः|निर्ह्रास
निर्ह्रासः Shortening, abbreviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निल्
निल् €6 P.<BR>—1 To understand slowly.<BR>—2 To be impassable, or impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पः|निलिम्प|निलिंप|निलिंपः
निलिम्पः<BR>—1 A god; निलिम्पैर्निर्मुक्तानपि च निरयान्तर्निपतितान् G. L. 15.<BR>—2 A troop of Maruts.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निलिम्पाधिपः, निलिम्पनिर्झरी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पाधिपः
निलिम्पः + -अधिपः Lord of the gods, Indra; निलिम्पाधिपबलं शाहम् Śiva B. 12. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पनिर्झरी|निलिंपनिर्झरी
निलिम्पः + -निर्झरी the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पा
निलिम्पा, निलिम्पिका<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 (निलिम्पा) A milk-pail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पिका|निलिंपिका
निलिम्पा, निलिम्पिका<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 (निलिम्पा) A milk-pail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निली
निली €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To stick or adhere to, lie or rest upon, settle down or alight upon;<BR> निलिल्ये मूर्ध्नि गृध्रोऽस्य Bk. 14. 76, 2. 5.<BR>—2 To lurk or hide, hide oneself in; गुहास्वन्ये न्यलेषत Bk. 15. 32;<BR> निशि रहसि निलीय Gīt. 2.<BR>—3 To hide or conceal oneself from (with abl.); मातुर्निलीयते कृष्णः Sk.<BR>—4 To die, perish.<BR>—5 To become settled or fixed; पूर्वमेव हि जन्तूनां योधिवासो निलीयते<BR> Rāj. T. 3. 426.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयः|निलय
निलयः<BR>—1 A hiding place, the lair or den of animals, a nest (of birds); निलयाय<BR> शाखिन इवाह्वयते Śi. 9. 4.<BR>—2 A cellar; अम्बराख्याननिलयौ कण्ठदध्नं समन्ततः Parṇāl. (Two<BR> cellars known as Ambarakhānā.)<BR>—3 An abode, residence, house, dwelling; oft. at the end of comp. in the<BR> sense of ‘living or residing in’; नित्यं निर्मूलयेयुर्निचिततरममी<BR> भक्तिनिध्नात्मनां नः पद्माक्षस्याङ्घ्रिपद्मद्वयतलनिलयाः पांसवः पापपङ्कम् ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">Page0921-2</a>]<BR> -विष्णुपादादि स्तोत्रम् १०.<BR>—4 Hiding oneself; तस्मान्निलयमुत्सृज्य यूयं सर्वे त्रिविष्टपम् । यात<BR> कालं प्रतीक्षन्तो यतः शत्रोर्विपर्ययः ॥ Bhāg. 8. 15. 31.<BR>—5 Total destruction.<BR>—6 Setting, disappearance; दिनान्ते निलयाय गन्तुम् R. 2. 15 (where<BR> the word is used in sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयनम्
निलयनम्<BR>—1 Settling in a place, alighting.<BR>—2 A place of refuge; निलयनं चानिलयनं च T. Up. 2. 6; Bhāg. 5. 19. 20.<BR>—3 A house, dwelling, habitation; नदीनिलयनाः सर्पा नदीकुटिलगामिनः ।<BR> तिष्ठन्त्यावृत्य पन्थानमतो दुःखतरं वनम् ॥ Rām. 2. 28. 20; Ki. 7. 20.<BR>—4 The act of going out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायनम्
निलायनम् Playing at hide and seek; Bhāg. 10. 11. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीन|निलीनं
निलीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Melted or fused into.<BR>—2 Shut or wrapt up, hidden into.<BR>—3 Involved, surrounded, encompassed.<BR>—4 Destroyed, perished.<BR>—5 Changed, transformed.<BR>—6 Full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवचने
निवचने <i>ind.</i> Not speaking, ceasing to speak, holding the tongue<BR> (regarded as a गति or preposition, or a separate word, when used<BR> with कृ; <i>e. g.</i> निवचनेकृत्य, निवचने कृत्वा; P. I. 4. 76; Kāśi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवत्
निवत् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A valley.<BR>—2 Depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवत्ता
निवत् + .{@-ता@} <i>ind.</i> Downwards (also निवना in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवप्
निवप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To scatter about, sow (as seed).<BR>—2 To offer (as oblations), especially to the manes; स्तोतव्या चेह पृथिवी<BR> निवापस्येह धारिणी Mb. 13. 91. 25; न्युप्य पिण्डांस्ततः Ms. 3. 216;<BR> (स्मरमुद्दिश्य) निवपेः सहकारमञ्जरीः Ku. 4. 38.<BR>—3 To immolate, kill (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवपनम्
निवपनम्<BR>—1 Scattering down, pouring out, throwing down.<BR>—2 Sowing.<BR>—3 An offering to the manes, an oblation in honour of oneʼs deceased ancestors;<BR> को नः कुले निवपनानि नियच्छतीति Ś. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापः|निवाप
निवापः<BR>—1 Seed, grain, seed-corn.<BR>—2 An offering to the manes of deceased parents or other relatives, a<BR> libation of water &c. at the Śrāddha ceremony; एको निवापसलिलं पिबसीत्ययुक्तम्<BR> Māl. 9. 40; निवापदत्तिभिः R. 8. 86; निवापञ्जलयः पितॄणाम् 5. 8, 15. 91;<BR> Mu. 4. 5.<BR>—3 A gift or offering in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निवापाञ्जलिः, निवापान्नम्, निवापोदकम्, निवापमाल्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापाञ्जलिः|निवापाञ्जलि
निवापः + -अञ्जलिः two handfuls of water as a libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापान्नम्
निवापः + -अन्नम् sacrificial food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापोदकम्
निवापः + -उदकम् a libation of water; अत्यल्पमिदमस्माकं निवापोदकभोजनम् Mk. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापमाल्यम्
निवापः + -माल्यम् funeral wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापकः|निवापक
निवापकः A sower, scatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर|निवरः
निवर <i>a.</i> Preventing, warding off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवरः|निवर
निवर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 One who prevents.<BR>—2 Protection, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवरा
निवरा A virgin, an unmarried girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवस्
निवस् I. €1 P.<BR>—1 To live, dwell, stay; आहो निवत्स्यति समं हरिणाङ्गनाभिः Ś. 1. 26;<BR> निवसिष्यसि मय्येव Bg. 12. 8.<BR>—2 To be, exist, निवसन्नन्तर्दारुणि लङ्घ्यो वह्निर्न तु ज्वलितः Pt. 1. 31.<BR>—3 To occupy, settle in, take possession of.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">Page0922-1</a>]<BR>—4 To sojourn, pass the night.<BR>—5 To cohabit; Mb. 9. ━II. €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To dress, wear or put on clothes.<BR>—2 To change oneʼs clothes.<BR>—3 To gird round (as a sword).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0921-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसतिः|निवसति
निवसतिः <i>f.</i> A house, habitation, abode, residence, dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसथः|निवसथ
निवसथः A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसनम्
निवसनम्<BR>—1 A house, habitation, dwelling; निवसनं श्मशानम् Ā. L. 16.<BR>—2 A garment, cloth, an undergarment; प्रस्थितं निवसनग्रहणाय Śi. 10. 60; R. 19. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासः|निवास
निवासः<BR>—1 Living, dwelling, residing.<BR>—2 A house, abode, habitation, resting-place; निवासश्चिन्तायाः Mk. 1. 15;<BR> Śi. 4. 63, 5. 21; Bg. 9. 18; Mk. 3. 23.<BR>—3 Passing the night.<BR>—4 A dress, garment.<BR>—5 Nightquarters.<BR>—6 Refuge, receptacle, asylum; जगन्निवासो वसुदेवसद्मनि Śi. 1. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निवासभवनम्, निवासरचना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासभवनम्
निवासः + -भवनम् sleeping-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासरचना
निवासः + -रचना an edifice; दृष्ट्वा प्राङ्भवतीं निवासरचनामस्माकमाशान्वितः Mk. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासनम्
निवासनम्<BR>—1 Residence.<BR>—2 Sojourn.<BR>—3 Spending time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
निवासिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dwelling, residing.<BR>—2 Wearing, dressed or clothed in; नवं नवक्षौमनिवासिनी सा Ku. 7. 26.<BR>━<i>m.</i> A resident, an inhabitant; अथानाथाः प्रकृतयो मातृबन्धुनिवासिनम् R. 12. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह्
निवह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To bring or lead near.<BR>—2 To bear up, sustain, support; वेदानुद्धरते जगन्निवहते Gīt. 1.<BR>—3 To flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवहः|निवह
निवहः<BR>—1 A multitude, collection, quantity, heap; भुजगनिवहो भूषणनिधिः<BR> Ā. L. 16; राजपुत्रनिवहः Bh. 3. 37; so घन˚, दैत्य˚, कपोत˚ &c.<BR>—2 N. of one of the seven winds.<BR>—3 N. of one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>—4 Killing, slaughter. ━<i>a.</i> Bringing, causing; कर्माणि पुण्यनिवहानि<BR> सुमङ्गलानि Bhāg. 11. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात <i>a.</i> [निवृत्तो निरुद्धो वा वातोऽस्मात्]<BR>—1 Sheltered from the wind, not windy, calm; निवातपद्मस्तिमितेन चक्षुषा<BR> नृपस्य कान्तं पिबतः सुताननम् R. 3. 17, 19. 42.<BR>—2 Unhurt, uninjured, unobstructed.<BR>—3 Safe, secure.<BR>—4 Well-armed, accoutred in strong mail; निवातकवचैर्युद्धं पर्व चाजगरं<BR> ततः Mb. 1. 2. 53.<BR>—5 Closely woven, without holes; निवातो दृढसंनाहे निर्वाते चाश्रयेऽपि<BR> च Viśva.; उपाहितैर्वपुषि निवातवर्मभिः Śi. 17. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातः|निवात
निवात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A refuge, dwelling, an asylum<BR>—2 An impenetrable coat of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातम्
निवात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A place sheltered from the wind; निवातनिष्कम्पमिव प्रदीपम् Ku. 3. 48;<BR> Ki. 14. 37; R. 13. 52, 3. 17; यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते Bg. 6. 19.<BR>—2 Absence of wind, calm, stillness; निवातस्तिमितां वेलां चन्द्रोदय<BR> इवोदधेः (संरम्भं निनाय) R. 12. 36.<BR>—3 A secure spot.<BR>—4 A strong armour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निवातकवचाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातकवचाः
निवात + -कवचाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाकु
निवाकु <i>a.</i> Not speaking, silent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवान्या
निवान्या A cow whose calf is dead and who is milked by means of another calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवास्
निवास् €10 P. To clothe, to put on clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविड|निविडं
निवि(बि)ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without space or interstices, close, compact.<BR>—2 Firm, tight, fast; निबिडो मुष्टिः R. 9. 58, 19. 44; गुरुनिबिडनितम्बबिम्बभाराः Śi.<BR>—3 Thick, impervious, dense, impenetrable; कालिकेव निबिडा बलाकिनी R. 11. 15.<BR>—4 Gross, coarse.<BR>—5 Bulky, large.<BR>—6 Crooked-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबिड
निवि(बि)ड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without space or interstices, close, compact.<BR>—2 Firm, tight, fast; निबिडो मुष्टिः R. 9. 58, 19. 44; गुरुनिबिडनितम्बबिम्बभाराः Śi.<BR>—3 Thick, impervious, dense, impenetrable; कालिकेव निबिडा बलाकिनी R. 11. 15.<BR>—4 Gross, coarse.<BR>—5 Bulky, large.<BR>—6 Crooked-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
निविद् €2 P. (generally in the <i>Caus.</i>)<BR>—1 To tell, communicate, inform (with dat.); उपस्थितां होमवेलां गुरवे<BR> निवेदयामि Ś. 4; काश्यपाय वनस्पतिसेवां निवेदयावः <i>ibid.</i>; R. 2. 68.<BR>—2 To declare or announce oneself; कथमात्मानं निवेदयामि Ś. 1.<BR>—3 To indicate, betray, show; शङ्कापरिग्रहनिवेदयिता Mu. 1; दिगम्बरत्वेन<BR> निवेदितं वसु Ku. 5. 72; R. 17. 40.<BR>—4 To offer, present, give, make an offer of; स्वराज्यं चन्द्रापीडाय<BR> न्यवेदयत् K. 367; राज्यमस्मै न्यवेदयत् R. 15. 70, 11. 47; Ms. 2. 51;<BR> Y. 1. 27.<BR>—5 To entrust to the care of, make or deliver over to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
निविद् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Speech, a short Vedic text; स हैतयैव निविदा प्रतिपेदे यावन्तो<BR> वैश्वदेवस्य निविद्युच्यन्ते Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 1.<BR>—2 Instruction, precept, direction.<BR>—3 Invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदक
निवेदक <i>a.</i> Informing, communicating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदनम्
निवेदनम्<BR>—1 Making known, relating, proclaiming; a communication, announcement.<BR>—2 Delivering, entrusting.<BR>—3 Dedication.<BR>—4 Representation.<BR>—5 An offering or oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदनः|निवेदन|निवेदनं
निवेदनम् + .{@-नः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदित|निवेदितं
निवेदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Made known, announced, told, communicated.<BR>—2 Delivered, given, entrusted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेद्यम्
निवेद्यम् <i>n.</i> Offering of food to an idol; cf. नैवेद्य. ━<i>a.</i><BR> To be communicated, related or presented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीश
निविरी(डी)श, -स <i>a.</i> See निबिरीस.<BR>—1 Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितम्बभारखेदि Śi. 7. 20.<BR>—2 Coarse, gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडीश
निविरी(डी)श, -स <i>a.</i> See निबिरीस.<BR>—1 Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितम्बभारखेदि Śi. 7. 20.<BR>—2 Coarse, gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीस|निविरीसं
निविरी(डी)श, -स <i>a.</i> See निबिरीस.<BR>—1 Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितम्बभारखेदि Śi. 7. 20.<BR>—2 Coarse, gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीसा
निविरी(डी)श, -स + .{@-सा@} A crooked nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविश्
निविश् €6 Ā.<BR>—1 To sit down, take a seat; नवाम्बुदश्यामवपुर्न्यविक्षत (आसने) Śi. 1. 19.<BR>—2 To halt, encamp; R. 12. 68.<BR>—3 To enter; रामशालां न्यविक्षत Bk. 4. 28, 6. 143, 8. 7; R. 9. 82, 12. 38.<BR>—4 To be fixed on, be directed towards; सूर्यनिविष्टदृष्टिः R. 14. 66.<BR>—5 To be devoted or attached to, be intent on, to practise; श्रुतिप्रामाण्यतो<BR> विद्वान् स्वधर्मे निविशेत वै Ms. 2. 8.<BR>—6 To marry (for निर्विश् q. v.).<BR>—7 To alight, descend. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fix or direct upon, apply to (as thought, mind &c.); मयि बुद्धिं<BR> निवेशय Bg. 12. 8.<BR>—2 To put, place, keep; मनोगतं वाचि निवेशयन्ति Ki. 14. 4; R. 4. 39, 7. 63, 6. 16.<BR>—3 To seat, install; स निवेश्य कुशावत्यां रिपुनागाङ्कुशं कुशम् R. 15. 97.<BR>—4 To cause to settle in life, get married; दौष्यन्तिमप्रतिरथं तनयं<BR> निवेश्य Ś. 4. 20; R. 11. 57.<BR>—5 To encamp (as an army); निवेशयामास विलङ्घिताध्वा क्लान्तं रजोधूसरकेतु<BR> सैन्यम् R. 5. 42, 16. 37.<BR>—6 To draw, paint, portray; चित्रे निवेश्य परिकल्पितसत्त्वयोगा Ś. 2. 10;<BR> M. 3. 11.<BR>—7 To commit to writing, inscribe on; पत्रे निवेशितमुदाहरणं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">Page0923-1</a>]<BR> प्रियायाः V. 2. 14.<BR>—8 To intrust or commit to; मित्रं ममायमिति निर्वृतचित्तवृत्तिं विश्रम्भतस्त्वयि<BR> निवेशितसर्वकार्यम् Mu. 5. 7; R. 19. 4.<BR>—9 To introduce.<BR>—10 To found (a city).<BR>—11 To throw, hurl upon, shoot at.<BR>—12 To impress (on mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0922-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्टः|निविष्ट|निविष्टं
निविष्टः <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seated, sitting upon.<BR>—2 Encamped; निविष्टमुदधेः कूले तं प्रपेदे विभीषणः R. 12. 68.<BR>—3 Fixed or intent upon.<BR>—4 Concentrated, subdued, controlled; भवन्ति साम्येऽपि निविष्टचेतसां<BR> वपुर्विशेषेष्वतिगौरवाः क्रियाः Ku. 5. 31.<BR>—5 Initiated.<BR>—6 Arranged.<BR>—7 Entered, gone into.<BR>—8 Appointed (guardians).<BR>—9 Cultivated (a country).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्टिः|निविष्टि
निविष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Copulation, coition (Ved.).<BR>—2 Coming to rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशः|निवेश
निवेशः<BR>—1 Entering, entrance.<BR>—2 Encamping, halting.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A halting place, camp, encampment; सेनानिवेशं तुमुलं चकार<BR> R. 5. 49, 7. 2; Śi. 17. 40; Ki. 7. 27.<BR>—4 A house, an abode, a dwelling; निवेशपरिवेशनम् Mb. 14. 45. 1;<BR> भृशं ददर्श … स निवेशवीरुधः Ki. 4. 19.<BR>—5 Expanse, contour (of the breast); नवातपालोहितमाहितं मुहुर्महानिवेशौ<BR> परितः पयोधरौ Ki. 4. 8.<BR>—6 Depositing, delivering,<BR>—7 Marrying, marriage, settling in life; ततो निवेशाय तदा स विप्रः<BR> संशितव्रतः । महीं चचार दारार्थी न च दारानविन्दत ॥ Mb. 1. 14. 1.<BR>—8 Impression, copy.<BR>—9 Military array.<BR>—10 Ornament. decoration.<BR>—11 Founding (a town), निवेशं चक्रिरे सर्वे पुराणां नृवरास्तदा Rām. 1. 32. 5.<BR>—12 Settling in a place; वास्तुकर्मानिवेशं च भरतागमनं तथा Rām. 1. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनम्
निवेशनम्<BR>—1 Entering, entrance.<BR>—2 Halting, encamping.<BR>—3 Marrying, marriage; प्रतिलोमनिवेशनम् Bhāg. 3. 7. 31.<BR>—4 Entering in writing, inscribing.<BR>—5 An abode, a dwelling, house, habitation.<BR>—6 A camp; निवेशयामास मुदा कल्पितान्यनिवेशने Bhāg. 10. 53. 16; Mb. 3. 240. 1.<BR>—7 A town or city; पार्थिवस्य निवेशने Rām. 7. 62. 18.<BR>—8 A nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनी
निवेशनम् + .{@-नी@} The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेष|निविशेषः
निविशेष <i>a.</i> Not different, alike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेषः|निविशेष
निविशेष + .{@-षः@} Want of difference, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतम्
निवीतम्<BR>—1 Wearing the sacred thread round the neck (making it hang down like<BR> a garland); निवीतं मनुष्याणां प्राचीनावीतं पितॄणामुपवीतं देवानाम्<BR> J. N. V.; निवीतं हि मनुष्याः प्रायशः स्वार्थं कुर्वन्ति ŚB. on MS. 3. 4. 2.<BR>—2 The thread so worn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतः|निवीत|निवीतं
निवीतम् + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A veil, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतम्
निवीतम् + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A veil, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतिन्
निवीतिन् <i>a.</i> Wearing the sacred thread round the neck (like a garland);<BR> उद्धृते दक्षिणे पाणावुपवीत्युच्यते द्विजः । सव्ये तु प्राचीनावीती निवीती<BR> कण्ठसज्जने ॥ Ms. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृ
निवृ €5. €9. €1 U. To surround, enclose; षट्त्रिंशद्धरिकोट्यश्च निवव्रुर्वानराऽधिपम्<BR> Bk. 14. 29. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To ward off, keep away from, avert from (with abl.); पापान्निवारयति<BR> योजयते हिताय Bh. 2. 72; निवारयन्ती महतो मुनिव्रतात् Ku. 5. 3.<BR>—2 To surround, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारः|निवार
निवारः, निवारणम्<BR>—1 Keeping off, preventing, warding off; दंशनिवारणैश्च R. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Prohibition, impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारणम्
निवारः, निवारणम्<BR>—1 Keeping off, preventing, warding off; दंशनिवारणैश्च R. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Prohibition, impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारकः|निवारक
निवारकः Defender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत|निवृतं|निवृतः
निवृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Surrounded, enclosed.<BR>—2 Held back, withheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृतः|निवृत|निवृतं
निवृत + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A veil, mantle, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृतम्
निवृत + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A veil, mantle, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृतिः|निवृति
निवृतिः <i>f.</i> Covering, enclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्
निवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To come back, return; न च निम्नादिव सलिलं निवर्तते मे ततो हृदयम्<BR> Śi. 3. 2; Ku. 4. 30; R. 2. 40; Bg. 8. 21, 15. 4.<BR>—2 To flee from, retreat; रणान्निववृते न च Bk. 5. 102.<BR>—3 To turn away from; be averse to; R. 5. 23, 7. 61.<BR>—4 To cease, desist or abstain from; प्रसमीक्ष्य निवर्तेत सर्वमांसस्य<BR> भक्षणात् Ms. 5. 49, 1. 53; Bk. 1. 18; निवृत्तमांसस्तु जनकः U. 4.<BR>—5 To be freed or absolved from, to escape; कथं न ज्ञेयमस्माभिः पापादस्मान्निवर्तितुम् Bg. 1. 39.<BR>—6 To leave off speaking, cease, stop.<BR>—7 To be removed, come to an end, cease, disappear; विषया विनिवर्तन्ते<BR> निराहारस्य देहिनः Bg. 2. 59, 14. 22; Ms. 11. 185, 186.<BR>—8 To be accomplished or finished, come to an end.<BR>—9 To be withheld or withdrawn from.<BR>—10 To refuse, decline.<BR>—11 To be engaged in.<BR>—12 To be reversed.<BR>—13 To set (as the sun).<BR>—14 To be forbidden.<BR>—15 To be wanting; यतो वाचो निवर्तन्ते. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to return, send back; निवर्त्य राजा दयितां दयालुः R. 2. 3, 3. 47, 7. 44.<BR>—2 To withdraw, keep away from; turn away, divert; रश्मिष्विवादाय नगेन्द्रसक्तां<BR> निवर्तयामास नृपस्य दृष्टिम् R. 2. 28; Ku. 5. 11.<BR>—3 To accomplish, perform, finish, complete.<BR>—4 To shorten (the hair).<BR>—5 To Annul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तक
निवर्तक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Returning, coming or turning back.<BR>—2 Stopping, ceasing.<BR>—3 Abolishing, expelling, removing.<BR>—4 Bringing back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तन|निवर्त्तन
निवर्तन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing to return.<BR>—2 Turning back, ceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तनम्
निवर्तन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Returning, turning or coming back, return; इह हि पततां नास्त्यालम्बो<BR> न चापि निवर्तनम् Śānti. 3. 2.<BR>—2 Not happening, ceasing.<BR>—3 Desisting or abstaining from (with abl.)<BR>—4 Desisting from work, inactivity (opp. प्रवर्तन); Kām. 1. 28.<BR>—5 Bringing back; Amaru. 84.<BR>—6 Repenting, a desire to improve.<BR>—7 A measure of land (20 rods).<BR>—8 Averting, keeping back from (with abl.) विनिपातनिवर्तनक्षमम् Ki. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तित
निवर्तित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Turned or brought back.<BR>—2 Averted.<BR>—3 Removed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निवर्तिताखिलाधार^1, निवर्तितपूर्व<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तिताखिलाधार
निवर्तित + -अखिलाधार^1 <i>a.</i> One who has abstained from all food.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तितपूर्व
निवर्तित + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> one who has turned away before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तिन्
निवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Turning back, flying from, returning.<BR>—2 Desisting or abstaining from.<BR>—3 Allowing to return or turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्त|निवृत्तः
निवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Returned, turned back.<BR>—2 Gone, departed, vanished, disappeared.<BR>—3 Ceased, refrained or abstained from, stopped, desisted; तस्थौ निवृत्तान्यवराभिलाषः Ku. 1. 51.<BR>—4 Abstaining from worldly acts, abstracted from this world, quiet; प्रवृत्तं<BR> च निवृत्तं च द्विविधं कर्म वैदिकम् Ms. 12. 88.<BR>—5 Repenting of improper<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">Page0924-1</a>]<BR> conduct.<BR>—6 Finished, completed, whole;<BR>—7 Set (as the sun); see वृत् with नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तम्
निवृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@}<BR>—1 Return.<BR>—2 A mind free from the influence of passions.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निवृत्तात्मन्, निवृत्तेन्द्रिय, निवृत्तकारण, निवृत्तमांस, निवृत्तयौवन, निवृत्तराग, निवृत्तलौल्य, निवृत्तवृत्ति, निवृत्तहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0923-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तात्मन्
निवृत्त + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a sage.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तेन्द्रिय
निवृत्त + -इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> one whose senses or desires are averted from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तकारण|निवृत्तकारणः
निवृत्त + -कारण <i>a.</i> without further cause or motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तकारणः|निवृत्तकारण
निवृत्त + -कारण + .({@-णः@}) a virtuous man, a man uninfluenced by worldly desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तमांस
निवृत्त + -मांस <i>a.</i> one who abstains from eating meat; निवृत्तमांसस्तु<BR> जनकः U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तयौवन
निवृत्त + -यौवन <i>a.</i> one whose youth has returned, restored to youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तराग
निवृत्त + -राग <i>a.</i> of subdued passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तलौल्य
निवृत्त + -लौल्य <i>a.</i> not desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तवृत्ति
निवृत्त + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> quitting any practice or occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तहृदय
निवृत्त + -हृदय <i>a.</i> with relenting heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तिः|निवृत्ति
निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Returning or coming back, return; दुर्गमेकमपुनर्निवृत्तये यं विशन्ति<BR> वशिनं मुमुक्षवः Śi. 14. 64; R. 4. 87.<BR>—2 Disappearance, cessation, termination, suspension; शापनिवृत्तौ<BR> Ś. 7; R. 8. 82.<BR>—3 Abstaining from work, inactivity (opp. प्रवृत्ति); प्रवृत्तिं च<BR> निवृत्तिं च जना न विदुरासुराः Bg. 16. 7.<BR>—4 Abstaining from, aversion; प्राणाघातान्निवृत्तिः Bh. 3. 63.<BR>—5 Leaving off, desisting from.<BR>—6 Resignation, discontinuance of worldly acts or emotions, quietism,<BR> separation from the world.<BR>—7 Repose, rest.<BR>—8 Felicity, beatitude.<BR>—9 Denial, refusal.<BR>—10 Abolition, prevention.<BR>—11 Ceasing to be valid or binding (as a rule.).<BR>—12 Completion.<BR>—13 (In drama.) Citation of an example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टः|निवेष्ट
निवेष्टः A cover, an envelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टनम्
निवेष्टनम् Covering, enveloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्य|निवेष्यः
निवेष्य <i>a.</i> Whirling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्यः|निवेष्य
निवेष्य + .{@-ष्यः@}<BR>—1 An eddy, a whirlpool,<BR>—2 A whirlwind or a similar phenomenon.<BR>—3 Hoarfrost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्यम्
निवेष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} Extent (व्याप्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्यूढम्
निव्यूढम् Perseverance, energy; cf. निर्व्यूढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्ये
निव्ये €1 U. To put on (round the neck); see निवीत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् €1 P. (नेशति) To lose oneself in abstract meditation, meditate upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् <i>f.</i> (This word is optionally substituted for निशा in all<BR> cases after acc. dual; it has no forms for the first five inflections).<BR>—1 Night.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ <i>a.</i> Honest, candid; प्रसादयिष्ये निशठः शीर्ष्णा तच्चरणं स्पृशन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशब्द
निशब्द <i>a.</i> Silent, not speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्
निशम् €4 P., €10 U.<BR>—1 To hear, listen to, come to know; निशम्य चैनां तपसे कृतोद्यमाम्<BR> Ku. 5. 3; Ś. 5. 2; R. 2. 41, 52, 61, 3. 47, 4. 2, 5. 12; Bk. 2. 9; निशामय<BR> प्रियसखि Māl. 7.<BR>—2 To see, observe; निशामयन् दीप्तमिवाग्निना जगत् Bu. C. 4. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमनम्
निशमनम्<BR>—1 Looking at, beholding.<BR>—2 Seeing, sight<BR>—3 Hearing.<BR>—4 Becoming aware of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्त|निशांत|निशान्तं|निशान्तः
निशान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Tranquil, calmed, quiet, patient.<BR>—2 Customary, traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्तम्
निशान्त + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A house, habitation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">Page0924-2</a>]<BR> dwelling; तस्याः स राजोपपदं निशान्तं कामीव कान्ताहृदयं विवेश R. 16. 40.<BR>—2 A harem, seraglio; Kau. A. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निशान्तनारी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्तनारी
निशान्त + -नारी a housewife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामः|निशाम
निशामः Observing, perceiving, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामनम्
निशामनम्<BR>—1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>—2 Sight.<BR>—3 Hearing.<BR>—4 Repeated observation.<BR>—5 A shadow, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामित
निशामित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Perceived.<BR>—2 Heard, learnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशरणम्
निश(शा)रणम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारणम्
निश(शा)रणम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा [नितरां श्यति तनूकरोति व्यापारान् शो-क Tv.]<BR>—1 Night या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी Bg. 2. 69.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR>—3 A dream.<BR>—4 A collective name for the zodiacal signs Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer,<BR> Sagittarius, and Capricorn.<BR>—5 A species of plant (Mar. कचरा or उपळसरी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निशाटः, निशाटनः, निशाटकः, निशातिक्रमः, निशात्ययः, निशान्तः, निशावसानम्, निशादः, निशान्ध, निशाधीशः, निशेशः, निशानाथः, निशापतिः, निशामणिः, निशारत्नम्, निशार्धकालः, निशाख्या, निशाह्वा, निशादिः, निशात्सर्गः, निशोषित, निशैतः, निशाकरः, निशाकेतुः, निशागृह, निशाक्षयः, निशाचर, निशाचर्मन्, निशाजलम्, निशादर्शिन्, निशानिशम्, निशापुष्पम्, निशाबलम्, निशामुखम्, निशामृगः, निशारत्नम्, निशावनः, निशाविहारः, निशावेदिन्, निशाहसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाटः|निशाट
निशा + -अटः, -अटनः<BR>—1 an owl.<BR>—2 a demon, ghost, goblin; ईश्वरस्य निशाटानां विलोक्य निखिलां पुरीम्<BR> Bk. 8. 115; Rām. Ch. 1. 34<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाटनः|निशाटन
निशा + -अटः, -अटनः<BR>—1 an owl.<BR>—2 a demon, ghost, goblin; ईश्वरस्य निशाटानां विलोक्य निखिलां पुरीम्<BR> Bk. 8. 115; Rām. Ch. 1. 34<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाटकः|निशाटक
निशा + -अटकः bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशातिक्रमः|निशातिक्रम
निशा + -अतिक्रमः, -अत्ययः, -अन्तः, -अवसानम्<BR>—1 the passing away of night.<BR>—2 day-break; ये मां स्तुवन्त्यनेनाङ्ग प्रतिबुध्य निशात्यये Bhāg. 8. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात्ययः|निशात्यय
निशा + -अतिक्रमः, -अत्ययः, -अन्तः, -अवसानम्<BR>—1 the passing away of night.<BR>—2 day-break; ये मां स्तुवन्त्यनेनाङ्ग प्रतिबुध्य निशात्यये Bhāg. 8. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

