निशा + -चर <i>a.</i> (-रा, -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> moving about by night, night stalker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचरः|निशाचर
निशा + -चर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a fiend, goblin, an evil spirit; तस्मै निशाचरैश्वर्यं प्रतिशुश्राव<BR> राघवः R. 12. 69.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 a jackal.<BR>—4 an owl.<BR>—5 a snake.<BR>—6 the ruddy goose.<BR>—7 a thief. ˚पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of (1) Śiva;<BR>—2 an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचरी
निशा + -चर + .({@-री@})<BR>—1 a female fiend.<BR>—2 a woman going to meet her lover at night by appointment; राममन्मथशरेण<BR> ताडिता दुःसहेन हृदये निशाचरी R. 11. 20 (where the word is used in sense 1 also).<BR>—3 a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचर्मन्|निशाचर्म्मन्
निशा + -चर्मन् <i>m.</i> darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाजलम्
निशा + -जलम् dew, frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादर्शिन्
निशा + -दर्शिन् <i>m.</i> an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशानिशम्
निशा + -निशम् <i>ind.</i> every night, always; ऋषेस्तस्योटजस्थस्य कालोऽगच्छन्निशानिशम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापुष्पम्
निशा + -पुष्पम्<BR>—1 the white water-lily (opening at night).<BR>—2 hoar-frost, dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाबलम्
निशा + -बलम् see निशा (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामुखम्
निशा + -मुखम् the beginning of night, cf. प्रदोषो रजनीमुखम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामृगः|निशामृग
निशा + -मृगः a jackal<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारत्नम्
निशा + -रत्नम्<BR>—1 the moon<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावनः|निशावन
निशा + -वनः hemp (शण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाविहारः|निशाविहार
निशा + -विहारः a demon. goblin, a Rākṣasa; प्रचक्रतू रामनिशाविहारौ Bk. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावेदिन्
निशा + -वेदिन् <i>m.</i> a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाहसः|निशाहस
निशा + -हसः the white water-lily (opening at night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
निशात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sharpened, whetted, sharp; निशातरौद्रेषु विकासतां गतैः Ki. 14. 30.<BR>—2 Polished, burnished, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशानम्
निशानम् Sharpening, whetting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निशानपट्टः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशानपट्टः|निशानपट्ट
निशानम् + -पट्टः a whet stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0924-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशित|निशितं|निशितः
निशित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sharpened, whetted, sharp; धनुर्गृहीत्वौपनिषदं महास्त्रं शरं<BR> ह्युपासा निशितं संधयीत Muṇḍ. 2. 2. 3; निशितनिपाताः शराः Ś. 1. 10;<BR> नागेन्द्रो निशिताङ्कुशेन Bh.<BR>—2 Stimulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशितम्
निशित + .{@-तम्@} Iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिता
निशित + .{@-ता@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशितिः|निशिति
निशितिः <i>f.</i> Excitement, agitation (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादः|निशाद
निशादः A man of low caste; see निषाद. (निशादापुत्रः A pestle;<BR> so ˚शिला a mortar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुकः|निशारुक
निशारुकः One of the seven Rūpakas in music; दृढः प्रौढोऽथ खचरो<BR> विभवश्चतुरक्रमः । निशारुकः प्रतीतालः कथिताः सप्त रूपकाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुकम्
निशारुकः + .{@-कम्@} An air, a sort of musical compositon played as an accompaniment to dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिचारः
निशिचारः (= निशाचरः) A fiend, a goblin; स घोररूपो निशिचारवीरः (रावणः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथः|निशीथ
निशीथः [निशेरते जना अस्मिन्; निशी आधारे थक् Tv.]<BR>—1 Midnight; निशीथदीपाः सहसा हतत्विषः R. 3. 15; Me. 90; Māl. 8. 10.<BR>—2 The time of sleep, night in general; शुचौ निशीथेऽनुभवन्ति कामिनः<BR> Ṛs. 1. 3; श्रुत्वा निशीथे ध्वनिम् Amaru. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनी
निशीथिनी, निशीथ्या Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ्या
निशीथिनी, निशीथ्या Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुभ्
निशुभ् (-म्भ्) €6 P.<BR> To tread down; पद्भ्यां निशुम्भति B. R. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भ्
निशुभ् (-म्भ्) €6 P.<BR> To tread down; पद्भ्यां निशुम्भति B. R. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भः|निशुम्भ|निशुंभ|निशुंभः
निशुम्भः<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter. उद्दर्पदुन्दुभिनिशुम्भपटुप्रचण्ड Mv. 5. 61;<BR> सावष्टम्भनिशुम्भसंभ्रमनमत् Māl. 5. 22.<BR>—2 Breaking, bending (as of a bow); प्रागप्राप्तनिशुम्भशाम्भवधनुर्द्वेधाक्रियाविर्भवत् Mv. 2. 33.<BR>—3 N. of a demon killed by Durgā. शक्तिः शुम्भनिशुम्भदैत्यदलनी Devī-stotram.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निशुम्भमथनी, निशुम्भमर्दनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भमथनी|निशुंभमथनी
निशुम्भः + -मथनी, -मर्दनी epithets of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भमर्दनी
निशुम्भः + -मथनी, -मर्दनी epithets of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भनम्
निशुम्भनम् Killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चक्रम्
निश्चक्रम् <i>ind.</i> See निःशेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चल
निश्चल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Immovable, steady, fixed, still.<BR>—2 Invariable, unchangeable; श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला Bg. 2. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चला
निश्चल + .{@-ला@} The earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निश्चलाङ्ग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चलाङ्ग|निश्चलांग|निश्चलाङ्गः
निश्चल + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चलाङ्गः|निश्चलाङ्ग|निश्चलांग
निश्चल + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गः@})<BR>—1 a species of crane.<BR>—2 a rock or mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चर्
निश्चर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To issue, go out; शिखाभिरिव निश्चरन् Mv. 5. 26.<BR>—2 To arise, be produced, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चारकम्
निश्चारकम्<BR>—1 Evacuation by stools.<BR>—2 Air, wind.<BR>—3 Obstinacy, wilful nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चवनः
निश्चवनः<BR>—1 N. of a sage.<BR>—2 N. of a kind of Fire; अग्निर्निश्चवनो नाम पृथिवीं स्तौति केवलम् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चि
निश्चि €5 U. To determine, resolve, ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चयः|निश्चय
निश्चयः<BR>—1 Ascertainment, investigation, inquiry.<BR>—2 A fixed opinion, settled or firm conviction, firm belief.<BR>—3 A determination, resolution, resolve; एष मे स्थिरो निश्चयः Mu. 1.<BR>—4 Certainty, positiveness, positive conclusion.<BR>—5 Fixed intention, design, purpose, aim; कैकेयी क्रूरनिश्चया R. 12. 4; Ku. 5. 5.<BR>—6 N. of a figure in Rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायः
निश्चायः Congregation; ततः कपिसमाहारमेकनिश्चायमागतम् Bk. 7. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायक|निश्चायकः
निश्चायक <i>a.</i> Who or what ascertains or determines, decisive, conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित
निश्चित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ascertained, determined, decided, settled, concluded (used actively<BR> also); राक्षसानां सहस्राणि राक्षसाधिपनिश्चिताः Rām. 6. 8. 13; अरावणमरामं<BR> वा जगदद्येति निश्चितः R. 12. 83.<BR>—2 Sentenced, pronounced (as a sentence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितम्
निश्चित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Certainty, decision.<BR>—2 Design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितम्
निश्चित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Decidedly, positively, certainly; यच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं<BR> तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्चितम् Bg. 5. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निश्चितार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितार्थ
निश्चित + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who has formed a certain opinion about.<BR>—2 judging rightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितिः|निश्चिति
निश्चितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Ascertainment, settling.<BR>—2 A determination, resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चुक्कणम्
निश्चुक्कणम् A powder for clearing the teeth, a kind of tooth-powder<BR> (Mar. दांतवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रमः|निश्रम
निश्रमः Labour bestowed upon anything, continued practice or labour;<BR> स चापि वीरः कृतशस्त्रनिश्रमः Mb. 1. 137. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रयणी
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder, a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी<BR> &c. कुम्भद्रोणीनिश्रेणीपरशु … Kau. A.; निश्रेणिरिव वीराणां सद्यो<BR> द्यामारुरुक्षताम् Śiva B. 4. 37; निश्रेणीरधिरुह्यान्ये तद्भित्तीः परिरेभिरे<BR> Śiva B. 13. 92; सम्भूय सम्यक् तैः सर्वैः मालानिःश्रेणिसाधकान् Parṇāl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेणि
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder, a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी<BR> &c. कुम्भद्रोणीनिश्रेणीपरशु … Kau. A.; निश्रेणिरिव वीराणां सद्यो<BR> द्यामारुरुक्षताम् Śiva B. 4. 37; निश्रेणीरधिरुह्यान्ये तद्भित्तीः परिरेभिरे<BR> Śiva B. 13. 92; सम्भूय सम्यक् तैः सर्वैः मालानिःश्रेणिसाधकान् Parṇāl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेणी
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder, a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी<BR> &c. कुम्भद्रोणीनिश्रेणीपरशु … Kau. A.; निश्रेणिरिव वीराणां सद्यो<BR> द्यामारुरुक्षताम् Śiva B. 4. 37; निश्रेणीरधिरुह्यान्ये तद्भित्तीः परिरेभिरे<BR> Śiva B. 13. 92; सम्भूय सम्यक् तैः सर्वैः मालानिःश्रेणिसाधकान् Parṇāl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्राणः|निश्राण
निश्राणः<BR>—1 A whet-stone.<BR>—2 A weapon (sword); विद्युत्कृत्वाऽथ निश्राणम् Mb. 7. 202. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वस्
निश्वस् €2 P.<BR>—1 To sigh, heave.<BR>—2 To draw in the breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वासः|निश्वास
निश्वासः Inspiration, inhaling, sighing; cf. निःश्वास.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निश्वाससंहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वाससंहिता
निश्वासः + -संहिता N. of a Śaiva Pāśupataśāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्
निष् €1 Ā. (नेषते) To moisten, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषञ्ज्
निषञ्ज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To adhere or stick, to be thrown round or placed on; कण्ठे स्वयंग्राहनिषक्तबाहुम्<BR> Ku. 3. 7; U. 4. 18; R. 9. 50, 11. 70, 19. 45.<BR>—2 To be reflected; दरीगृहोत्सङ्गनिषक्तभासः Ku. 1. 10, 7. 36.<BR>—3 To be attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गः|निषङ्ग|निषंग|निषंगः
निषङ्गः<BR>—1 Attachment, clinging to.<BR>—2 Union, association.<BR>—3 A quiver; अग्रहीन्नु सशरं धनुरुज्झामास नूज्झितनिषङ्गमनङ्गः<BR> Śi. 10. 34; Ki. 17. 36; R. 2. 30, 3. 64.<BR>—4 A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गथिः|निषङ्गथि|निषंगथि|निषंगथिः
निषङ्गथिः<BR>—1 An embrace.<BR>—2 A bowman.<BR>—3 A charioteer.<BR>—4 A car.<BR>—5 Grass.<BR>—6 The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गिन्|निषंगिन्
निषङ्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attached or clinging to; स्थाणौ निषङ्गिण्यनसि क्षणं पुरः Śi. 12. 26.<BR>—2 Having a quiver.<BR>—3 Bearing a sword. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An archer, a bowman.<BR>—2 A quiver.<BR>—3 A sword-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
निषद् €1 P. (निषीदति &c.)<BR>—1 To sit down, lie, recline; उष्णालुः शिशिरे निषीदति तरोर्मूलालवाले<BR> शिखी V. 2. 23.<BR>—2 To sink down, fail, be disappointed.<BR>—3 To dwell.<BR>—4 To suffer pain, be afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0925-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
निषद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Consecration for a sacrifice (यज्ञदीक्षा).<BR>—2 A kind of literary composition (कर्माङ्गाद्यवबद्धदेवतादिज्ञानवाक्यम्<BR> com. on Mb. 12. 47. 26.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्ण|निषण्णः
निषण्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seated; sitting on or in, rested, reclined, resting or reclining on;<BR> पृष्टान्वयः स जलकुम्भनिषण्णदेहः R. 9. 76; Ku. 4. 23.<BR>—2 Supported.<BR>—3 Gone to.<BR>—4 Dejected, afflicted, down-cast; cf. विषण्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्णकम्
निषण्णकम्<BR>—1 A seat.<BR>—2 A kind of pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषत्तिः|निषत्ति
निषत्तिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Sitting down idly, dulness, inactivity; का<BR> ते निषत्तिः किमु नो ममत्सि Rv. 4. 21. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषदनम्
निषदनम् Ved.<BR>—1 Sitting.<BR>—2 Dwelling; क्वचिच्चाशेषदोषनिषदनम् Bhāg. 5. 14. 7.<BR>—3 A seat.<BR>—4 A house, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषदनः|निषदन|निषदनं
निषदनम् + .{@-नः@} = निषाद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्या
निषद्या<BR>—1 A small bed or couch.<BR>—2 The hall of a merchant, a traderʼs shop.<BR>—3 A market-place, market; आपणस्तु निषद्यायाम् । Ak. केचिद् गुर्वीमेत्य<BR> संयन्निषद्यां क्रीणन्ति स्म प्राणमूल्यैर्यशांसि Śi. 18. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वरः|निषद्वर
निषद्वरः<BR>—1 Mud, mire; सक्थिदध्ननिषद्वरम् (अध्वानम्) Śiva B. 26. 74.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वरा
निषद्वरः + .{@-रा, -री@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वरी
निषद्वरः + .{@-रा, -री@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादित
निषादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Made to sit down.<BR>—2 Afflicted, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादिन्
निषादिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sitting or lying down, resting, reclining; आतपात्ययसंक्षिप्तनीवारासु<BR> निषादिभिः R. 1. 52, 4. 20. ━<i>m.</i> An elephant-driver; Śi. 5. 41. निषादिनुन्नाः<BR> करिणः Śiva B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध <i>a.</i> Hard, solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषधाः
निषध + .{@-धाः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a people and their country governed by Nala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषधः|निषध
निषध + .{@-धः@}<BR>—1 A ruler of the Niṣadhas.<BR>—2 N. of a mountain.<BR>—3 A musical note; cf. निषाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषधा
निषध + .{@-धा@} N. of Nalaʼs capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादः|निषाद
निषादः<BR>—1 N. of one of the wild aboriginal tribes in India, such as hunters,<BR> fishermen &c.; a mountaineer; मा निषाद प्रतिष्ठां त्वमगमः शाश्वतीः<BR> समा Rām. 1. 2. 15; R. 14. 52, 70; U. 2. 5.<BR>—2 A man of a degraded tribe in general, an outcast, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>—3 Especially, the son of a Brāhmaṇa by a Śūdra woman; cf. ब्राह्मणाद्वैश्यकन्यायामम्बष्ठो<BR> नाम जायते । निषादः शूद्रकन्यायां यः पारशव उच्यते ॥ Ms. 10. 8.<BR>—4 (In music) The first (more properly the last or seventh) note of the<BR> Hindu gamut; गीतकलाविन्यासमिव निषादानुगतम् K. 31 (where it has sense 1 also).<BR>—5 N. of a Kalpa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निषादवत्, निषादस्थपतिन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादवत्|निषादवन्त्
निषादः + -वत् <i>m.</i> the निषाद note; Mb. 12. 184. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादस्थपतिन्यायः
निषादः + -स्थपतिन्यायः The rule according to which when a compound expression<BR> is capable of being dissolved as a कर्मधारय or a तत्पुरुष,<BR> the former is to be preferred to the latter. This is discussed and established<BR> by जैमिनि and शबर in MS. 6. 1. 51-52 in connection with the<BR> expression निषादस्थपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिच्
निषिच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To pour upon or down, sprinkle, pour in; सुखैर्निषिञ्चन्तमिवामृतं<BR> त्वचि R. 3. 26; Ś. 4. 14;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">Page0926-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 2. 57.<BR>—2 To inpregnate; निषिञ्चन् माधवीमेतां लतां कौन्दीं च नर्तयन् V. 2. 4<BR> (where the word also means ‘to fill with honey-drops’).<BR>—3 To wet, irrigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिक्त
निषिक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sprinkled upon.<BR>—2 Infused, instilled, poured into, impregnated. —3 Irrigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेकः|निषेक
निषेकः<BR>—1 Sprinking, infusion; सुखसलिलनिषेकः Ṛs. 1. 28.<BR>—2 Dripping, trickling, distilling; तैलनिषेकबिन्दुना R. 8. 38, ‘a drop of dripping oil’<BR>.<BR>—3 Effusion, discharge,<BR>—4 Seminal effusion or discharge, infusion of semen, impregnation, seed;<BR> योषित्सु तद्वीर्यनिषेकभूमिः (सैव) Ku. 3. 16; प्रजानिषेकं मयि<BR> वर्तमानम् R. 14. 60.<BR>—5 The ceremony performed upon impregnation; निषेकादिश्मशानान्तो मन्त्रैर्यस्योदितो<BR> विधिः । तस्य शास्त्रेऽधिकारोऽस्मिन् ज्ञेयो नान्यस्य कस्यचित् ॥ Ms. 2. 16;<BR> Bhāg. 7. 15. 52.<BR>—6 Irrigation.<BR>—7 Water for washing.<BR>—8 Seminal impurity; Ms. 4. 151.<BR>—9 Dirty water.<BR>—10 Drawing essence by distillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेक्तृ
निषेक्तृ <i>m.</i> Impregnator, begetter, father; देहः किमन्नदातुः<BR> स्वं निषेक्तुर्मातुरेव च Bhāg. 10. 10. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेचनम्
निषेचनम्<BR>—1 Sprinkling, pouring out.<BR>—2 Watering, irrigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिध्
निषिध् €1 P.<BR>—1 To ward off, prevent, restrain, keep back; न्यषेधि शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः<BR> R. 2. 4, 3. 42, 5. 18.<BR>—2 To oppose, contradict, object to; न कश्चन भ्रातृषु तेषु शक्तो निषेद्धुमासीदनुवर्तितुं<BR> वा R. 14. 43.<BR>—3 To prohibit, forbid; निषिद्धो भाषमाणस्तु सुवर्णं दण्डमर्हति Ms. 8. 361.<BR>—4 To defeat, conquer; निषिद्धशत्रुः R. 18. 1.<BR>—5 To remove, drive off, counteract; न्यषेधत् पावकास्त्रेण रामस्तद्राक्षसस्ततः<BR> Bk. 17. 87, 1. 15.<BR>—6 To out-do, surpass; Kāv. 2. 64. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To prohibit, keep off or ward off.<BR>—2 To deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्ध|निषिद्धं
निषिद्ध <i>p. p.</i> Forbidden, prohibited, warded off, prevented; निषिद्धैरप्येभिर्लुलितमकरन्दो<BR> मधुकरैः Ve. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्धिः|निषिद्धि
निषिद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Prohibition, warding or keeping off,<BR>—2 Defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधः|निषेध
निषेधः<BR>—1 Prohibition, warding or keeping off, stopping, prevention.<BR>—2 Negation, denial.<BR>—3 The particle of negation; द्वौ निषेधौ प्रकृतार्थं गमयतः<BR>—4 A prohibitive rule (opp. विधि).<BR>—5 Deviation from a rule, exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधिन्
निषेधिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Defending, keeping back or down.<BR>—2 Excelling, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूद्
निषूद् €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i> To kill, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूदनम्
निषूदनम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूदनः|निषूदन|निषूदनं
निषूदनम् + .{@-नः@} A killer; as in बलवृत्रनिषूदनः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव्
निषेव् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To pursue, follow, attach oneself to, practise; वैखानसं किमनया<BR> व्रतमा प्रदानाद् व्यापाररोधि मदनस्य निषेवितव्यम् Ś. 1. 27.<BR>—2 To enjoy; निषेवते श्रान्तमना विविक्तम् Ś. 5. 5; Ku. 1. 5.<BR>—3 To enjoy carnally; यथा यथा तामरसेक्षणा मया पुनः सरागं नितरां<BR> निषेविता Bv. 2. 155; कौलिको विष्णुरूपेण राजकन्यां निषेवते Pt. 1. 202.<BR>—4 To resort to,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">Page0927-1</a>]<BR> inhabit, frequent; विपत्प्रतीकारपरेण मङ्गलं निषेव्यते भूतिसमुत्सुकेन<BR> वा Ku. 5. 76.<BR>—5 To use, employ; विषतां निषेवितमपक्रियया समुपैति सर्वमिति सत्यमदः Śi. 9. 68.<BR>—6 To wait upon, attend.<BR>—7 To adore, worship.<BR>—8 To draw near, approach.<BR>—9 To suffer, experience; स दुःखे लभते दुःखं द्वावनर्थौ निषेवते<BR> Pt. 1. 334. ━<i>Caus.</i> To fall into (hell &c.); ते रौरवादीनि निषेवयन्ति Pt. 3. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0926-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव
निषेव, निषेवक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Practising, following, devoted to, fond of.<BR>—2 Frequenting, inhabiting, resorting to.<BR>—3 Enjoying. यत्पादपङ्कजपरागनिषेवतृप्ताः Bhāg. 10. 33. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवक
निषेव, निषेवक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Practising, following, devoted to, fond of.<BR>—2 Frequenting, inhabiting, resorting to.<BR>—3 Enjoying. यत्पादपङ्कजपरागनिषेवतृप्ताः Bhāg. 10. 33. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवणम्
निषेवणम्, -निषेवा<BR>—1 Serving, service, attending, waiting upon.<BR>—2 Worship, adoration.<BR>—3 Practice, performance.<BR>—4 Attachment or adherence to.<BR>—5 Living in, inhabiting, enjoying, using.<BR>—6 Familiarity with, use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवा
निषेवणम्, -निषेवा<BR>—1 Serving, service, attending, waiting upon.<BR>—2 Worship, adoration.<BR>—3 Practice, performance.<BR>—4 Attachment or adherence to.<BR>—5 Living in, inhabiting, enjoying, using.<BR>—6 Familiarity with, use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवित
निषेवित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Served, waited upon, worshipped, honoured.<BR>—2 Visited, resorted to, haunted, frequented<BR>—3 Practised, observed (as a vow &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्
निष्क् €10 Ā. (निष्कयते) To weigh, measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कः|निष्क|निष्कं
निष्कः, -कम्<BR>—1 A golden coin (of different values, but generally taken to be equal<BR> to one <i>Karṣa</i> or Suvarṇa of 16 Māṣas); वराटकानां दशकद्वयं<BR> यत् सा काकिणी ताश्च पणश्चतस्रः । ते षोडश द्रम्म इहावगम्यो द्रम्मैस्तथा<BR> षोडशभिश्च निष्कः ॥ मांसभेत्ता तु षष्णिष्कान् (दण्डः) Ms. 8. 284.<BR>—2 A weight of gold equal to 108 or 150 Suvarṇas q. v.<BR>—3 A golden ornament for the neck or the breast; हरिचक्रेण तेनास्य<BR> कण्ठे निष्कमिवार्पितम् Ku. 2. 49; निष्ककण्ठीः (उपदेववरस्त्रियः)<BR> Bhāg. 4. 3. 6.<BR>—4 Gold in general.<BR>—5 A golden vessel.<BR>—6 A die or dice; L. D. B.<BR>—7 Departure, going away; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कम्
निष्कः, -कम्<BR>—1 A golden coin (of different values, but generally taken to be equal<BR> to one <i>Karṣa</i> or Suvarṇa of 16 Māṣas); वराटकानां दशकद्वयं<BR> यत् सा काकिणी ताश्च पणश्चतस्रः । ते षोडश द्रम्म इहावगम्यो द्रम्मैस्तथा<BR> षोडशभिश्च निष्कः ॥ मांसभेत्ता तु षष्णिष्कान् (दण्डः) Ms. 8. 284.<BR>—2 A weight of gold equal to 108 or 150 Suvarṇas q. v.<BR>—3 A golden ornament for the neck or the breast; हरिचक्रेण तेनास्य<BR> कण्ठे निष्कमिवार्पितम् Ku. 2. 49; निष्ककण्ठीः (उपदेववरस्त्रियः)<BR> Bhāg. 4. 3. 6.<BR>—4 Gold in general.<BR>—5 A golden vessel.<BR>—6 A die or dice; L. D. B.<BR>—7 Departure, going away; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कः|निष्क|निष्कं
निष्कः, -कम् + .{@-ष्कः@} A Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल्
निष्कल् €10 P. To drive out, or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निष्कल <i>a.</i> inarticulate (a musical term); N. 21. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालनम्
निष्कालनम्<BR>—1 Driving away (cattle &c.)<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter (मारण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कस्
निष्कस् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To take or draw out.<BR>—2 To turn or drive out, banish, expel; निरकासयद्रविमपेतवसुं वियदालयादपरदिग्गणिका<BR> Śi. 9. 10; येनाहं जीवलोकान्निष्कासयिष्ये Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासः|निष्कास
निष्कासः(शः)<BR>—1 Exit, egress, issue.<BR>—2 A portico.<BR>—3 Day-break.<BR>—4 Disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काशः|निष्काश
निष्कासः(शः)<BR>—1 Exit, egress, issue.<BR>—2 A portico.<BR>—3 Day-break.<BR>—4 Disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासित|निष्कासितः
निष्कासित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Expelled, turned out, driven out.<BR>—2 Gone forth or out, issued.<BR>—3 Placed, deposited.<BR>—4 Stationed, appointed.<BR>—5 Opened, blown, expanded.<BR>—6 Reviled, reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासिनी
निष्कासिनी A female slave not restrained by her master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटः|निष्कुट
निष्कुटः<BR>—1 A pleasure-grove near a house; निष्कुटश्चैव देशोऽयम् Rām. 2. 85. 16.<BR>—2 A field.<BR>—3 The female apartments, the harem of a king.<BR>—4 A door, gate.<BR>—5 The hollow of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटिः|निष्कुटि
निष्कुटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> Large cardamoms (एला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटी
निष्कुटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> Large cardamoms (एला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुलाकृ
निष्कुलाकृ €8 U. To peel off; तन्निष्कुलाकृत्य रविं त्वगेषा सन्ध्योज्झिता<BR> पाकिमदाडिमं वा N. 22. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुष्
निष्कुष् €9 P.<BR>—1 To extract, tear, draw out; उपान्तयोर्निष्कुषितं विहङ्गैः R. 7. 50;<BR> Bk. 9. 30, 5. 42; so काकैर्निष्कुषितं श्वभिः कवलितं गोमायुभिर्लुण्ठितम्<BR> Gaṅgāṣṭaka; Māl. 5. 17.<BR>—2 To husk, shell.<BR>—3 To injure or hurt by tearing; अयस्मयैरग्निपिण्डैः संदंशैस्त्वचि<BR> निष्कुषन्ति Bhāg. 5. 26. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुषित
निष्कुषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Torn off, forced or drawn out, lacerated; उपान्तयोर्निष्कुषितं विहङ्गैः R. 7. 50.<BR>—2 Expelled.<BR>—3 Eaten up; कीटनिष्कुषितं धनुः Bk. 5. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषः|निष्कोष
निष्कोषः, निष्कोषणम्<BR>—1 Tearing, drawing off or out, extracting, extirpating.<BR>—2 Husking, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषणम्
निष्कोषः, निष्कोषणम्<BR>—1 Tearing, drawing off or out, extracting, extirpating.<BR>—2 Husking, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषणकम्
निष्कोषणकम् A tooth-pick; दन्तस्य निष्कोषणकेन नित्यं …<BR> तृणेन कार्यं भवतीश्वराणाम् Pt. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुहः|निष्कुह
निष्कुहः The hollow of a tree; cf. निष्कुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृ
निष्कृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To remove, drive away, expel;<BR>—2 To break, frustrate; Bk. 15. 51.<BR>—3 To break into pieces, destroy.<BR>—4 To prepare, fit up, equip.<BR>—5 To accomplish, finish.<BR>—6 To absolve, free from (blame, sin &c.), acquit.<BR>—7 To cure, heal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारणम्
निष्कारणम्<BR>—1 Removing, taking away.<BR>—2 Killing; cf. निकारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत
निष्कृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Taken away, removed.<BR>—2 Expiated, absolved, pardoned. निन्द्यैर्हि लक्षणैर्युक्ता जायन्तेऽनिष्कृतैनसः Ms. 11. 53.<BR>—3 Disregarded, overlooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृतम्
निष्कृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Expiation or atonement; न ते यमं पाशभृतश्च तद्भटान् खप्नेऽपि<BR> पश्यन्ति हि चीर्णनिष्कृताः Bhāg. 6. 1. 19.<BR>—2 A place of rendezvous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृतिः|निष्कृति
निष्कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Expiation, atonement; ब्रह्मघ्ने च सुरापे च चौरे भग्नव्रते शठे ।<BR> निष्कृतिर्विहिता सद्भिः कृतघ्ने नास्ति निष्कृतिः ॥ Pt. 3. 157.<BR>—2 Acquittance, requital, discharge of a debt or obligation; न तस्य<BR> निष्कृतिः शक्या कर्तुं वर्षशतैरपि Ms. 2. 227, 3. 19, 8. 105, 9. 19, 11. 27.<BR>—3 Removal.<BR>—4 Restoration, cure.<BR>—5 Avoiding, escaping from.<BR>—6 Neglecting.<BR>—7 Bad conduct, roguery.<BR>—8 Reproach, scoffing (धिक्कार); स्त्रियास्तथाऽपचारिण्या निष्कृतिः<BR> स्याददूषिका Mb. 12. 34. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत्
निष्कृत् €6 P.<BR>—1 To cut, cut off, divide, tear asunder, cut in pieces.<BR>—2 To loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्तनम्
निष्कर्तनम् Cutting off, tearing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्
निष्कृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw or pull out, extract.<BR>—2 To extort, exact, snatch or take by force; निष्क्रष्टुमर्थं चकमे<BR> कुबेरात् R. 5. 26.<BR>—3 To tear asunder, cut in pieces. ━<i>Caus.</i> To destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षः|निष्कर्ष
निष्कर्षः<BR>—1 Drawing out, extraction.<BR>—2 The essence, the chief or main point, pith; इति निष्कर्षः (often<BR> used by commentators); एतद्विदन्तो विद्वांसस्त्रयीनिष्कर्षमन्वहम् Ms. 4. 125;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">Page0928-1</a>]<BR> Bhāṣā P. 138.<BR>—3 Measuring.<BR>—4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षम्
निष्कर्षः + .{@-षम्@} Oppressing subjects by taxes; विशेषात् सर्वमेवैतत् संजज्ञे<BR> राजकर्मणा । अनुकर्षं च निष्कर्षं व्याधिपावकमूर्छनम् ॥ Mb. 2. 13. 13.<BR> (com. निष्कर्षं करार्थं प्रजापीडनम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0927-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षणम्
निष्कर्षणम्<BR>—1 Drawing out, extracting, pulling off; ब्राह्ममस्त्रं प्रियाशोकशल्यनिष्कर्षणौषधम् R. 12. 97.<BR>—2 Deducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्ट
निष्कृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pulled or drawn out, extracted.<BR>—2 Summed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम्
निष्क्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To go away or from, leave, depart.<BR>—2 To issue from, come out of; निष्कम्य शिक्षया तस्यास्त्रपान्वतो रसातलात् Bk. 7. 71.<BR>—3 To make an exit from the stage; इति निष्कान्ताः सर्वे<BR>—4 To stop, cease; नैतावतापि पीडा निष्क्रामति Ś. 2; ‘the evil does not stop here’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमः|निष्क्रम
निष्क्रमः<BR>—1 Going out, coming forth; अविभावितनिष्क्रमप्रयाणः Ki. 13. 27.<BR>—2 Departure from, exit.<BR>—3 One of the Saṃskāras or religious rites; <i>i. e.</i> taking out a child<BR> for the first time into the open air (which is usually performed in the<BR> fourth month of its age); चतुर्थे मासि निष्क्रमः Y. 1. 12; cf. उपनिष्क्रमण also.<BR>—4 Degradation, loss of caste, inferiority of tribe.<BR>—5 Intellectual faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमणम्
निष्क्रमणम्<BR>—1 Going forth or out.<BR>—2 = निष्क्रम (3) above; चतुर्थे मासि कर्तव्यं शिशोर्निष्क्रमणं<BR> गृहात् Ms. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमणिका
निष्क्रमणिका See निष्क्रम (3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रान्त|निष्क्रान्तः
निष्क्रान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gone out, departed.<BR>—2 Come forth; ददर्श भूमौ निष्क्रान्तं राक्षसस्य पदं महत् Rām. 3. 64. 36.<BR>—3 (in drama) Exit, exeunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्री
निष्क्री €9 U. To buy off, redeem, ransom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रयः|निष्क्रय
निष्क्रयः<BR>—1 Redemption, ransom; ददौ दत्तं समुद्रेण पीतेनेवात्मनिष्क्रयम्<BR> R. 15. 55, 2. 55, 5. 22; Mu. 6. 20.<BR>—2 Reward; सम्यक्संपादितो वत्स भवद्भ्यां गुरुनिष्कयः Bhāg. 10. 45. 47.<BR>—3 Hire, wages.<BR>—4 Return, aquittance; त्रसत्तुषाराद्रिसुताससंभ्रमस्वयंग्रहाश्लेषसुखेन<BR> निष्क्रयम् Śi. 1. 50.<BR>—5 Exchange, barter.<BR>—6 Sale; न निष्क्रयविसर्गाभ्यां भर्तुर्भार्या विमुच्यते Ms. 9. 46.<BR>—7 Purchase; cf. निष्क्रयो बुद्धियोगे स्यात् सामर्थ्ये निर्गतावपि; Vaijayantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रयणम्
निष्क्रयणम् Redemption, ransom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रीतिः|निष्क्रीति
निष्क्रीतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Redemption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्वाथः|निष्क्वाथ
निष्क्वाथः<BR>—1 Decoction.<BR>—2 Broth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टनः|निष्टन
निष्टनः Groan, sigh; ददर्श बध्यमानांश्च क्लिश्यमानांश्च देहिनः ।<BR> क्रोशतश्च महानादं तीव्रनिष्टनतत्परान् ॥ Rām. 7. 21. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्
निष्टप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To heat, scorch.<BR>—2 To purify.<BR>—3 To burnish.<BR>—4 To roast, fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टपनम्
निष्टपनम् Burning, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्त
निष्टप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Burnished.<BR>—2 Well-dressed or cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टापः|निष्टाप
निष्टापः Burning, slight heating; निष्टापस्विद्यदस्थ्नः Māl. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टानकः|निष्टानक
निष्टानकः<BR>—1 Roar, murmur.<BR>—2 Groan; निष्टानको महानासीत् सैन्यानां तव भारत Mb. 7. 151. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टुर्
निष्टुर् <i>m.</i> Ved. A conqueror of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्य|निष्ट्यः
निष्ट्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Foreign, exotic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्यः|निष्ट्य
निष्ट्य + .{@-ष्ट्यः@} An outcast, a Chānḍāla or Mleccha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्या
निष्ट्य + .{@-ष्ट्या@} N. of a lunar mansion (स्वाति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ|निष्ठः
निष्ठ <i>a.</i> [नि-स्था-क षत्वटुत्वे] (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Being in or on, situated on; तन्निष्ठे फेने.<BR>—2 Depending or resting on, referring or relating to; तमोनिष्ठाः Ms. 12. 95.<BR>—3 Devoted or attached to, practising, intent on; सत्यनिष्ठ.<BR>—4 Skilled in.<BR>—5 Believing in; धर्मनिष्ठ. 6 Conducive to, effecting; हेमाम्भोज<BR> स्रजस्ते विशद सुमहते प्लोषपोषाय निष्ठाः B. R. 5. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठा
निष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठा@}<BR>—1 Position, condition, state; तेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण Bg. 17. 1;<BR> तेषामशान्तकामानां का निष्ठाऽविजितात्मनाम् Bhāg. 11. 5. 1.<BR>—2 Basis, foundation.<BR>—3 Fixity, fixedness, steadiness; मनो निष्ठाशून्यं भ्रमति च किमप्यालिखति<BR> च Māl. 1. 31.<BR>—4 Devotion or application, close attachment.<BR>—5 Belief, firm adherence, faith; शास्त्रेषु निष्ठा Māl. 3. 11; लोकेऽस्मिन्<BR> द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयाऽनघ Bg. 3. 3.<BR>—6 Excellence, skill, proficiency, perfection.<BR>—7 Conclusion, end, termination; (शृणु) चरितं पार्थिवेन्द्रस्य यथा<BR> निष्ठां गतश्च सः Mb. 1. 49. 6; अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा<BR> Ś. 4. 3 (v. l.).<BR>—8 The catastrophe or end of a drama.<BR>—9 Accomplishment, completion (समाप्ति); पाणिग्रहणिका मन्त्रा नियतं<BR> दारलक्षणम् । तेषां निष्ठा तु विज्ञेया विद्वद्भिः सप्तमे पदे ॥ Ms. 8. 227.<BR>—10 The culminating point; इयं च निष्ठा नियतं प्रजानाम् Bu. C. 3. 61.<BR>—11 Death, destruction, disappearance from the world at the fixed time.<BR>—12 Fixed or certain knowledge, certainty.<BR>—13 Begging.<BR>—14 Suffering, trouble, distress, anxiety.<BR>—15 (In gram.) A technical term for the past participial terminations<BR> क्त, क्तवतु (<i>i. e.</i> त and तवत.)<BR>—16 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठापित
निष्ठापित <i>a.</i> Accomplished; Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठाव
निष्ठाव <i>a.</i> Ved. Concluding, deciding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठित|निष्ठितं
निष्ठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Being in or on.<BR>—2 Devoted to.<BR>—3 Versed or skilled in.<BR>—4 Firm, fixed.<BR>—5 Certain, ascertained.<BR>—6 Fulfilled, complete; अनिष्ठिताशः स चकार मार्गणे पुनः प्रियायाः<BR> परमं परिश्रमम् Rām. 3. 60. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठानम्
निष्ठानम्<BR>—1 Sauce, condiment; ‘निष्ठानं व्यञ्जनं ज्ञेयम्’ इति हलायुधः; Rām. 2. 91. 67.<BR>—2 See अधिष्ठान; देवनिष्ठानभूतं तद्विमानम् पुष्पकं मृधे Rām. 7. 21. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठानित
निष्ठानित <i>a.</i> (= दध्यादिव्यञ्जनसंयुक्त, तेमनयुक्त) Seasoned<BR> with condiments; निर्यातय एतानि मोदकानि … निष्ठानिता सुरा इव<BR> मधुराणि Pratijñā. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठिव्
निष्ठिव् €1. €4 P.<BR>—1 To eject, emit, send forth; निष्ठपूतश्चरणोपभोगसुलभो लाक्षारसः<BR> केनचित् Ś. 4. 5; R. 2. 75; Bk. 14. 100, 17. 10, 18. 14; Kāv. 1. 95.<BR>—2 To eject saliva from the mouth, spit; Ms. 4. 132; अमेध्यपार्ष्णिनिष्ठपूतस्पर्शने<BR> द्विगुणस्ततः (दण्डः) Y. 2. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0928-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठित|निष्ठितं
निष्ठित <i>a.</i> Spit upon; निष्ठितो मूत्रितो वाज्ञैर्बहुधैव प्रकम्पितः ।<BR> श्रेयस्कामः कृच्छ्रगत आत्मनात्मानमुद्धरेत् ॥ Bhāg. 11. 22. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवः|निष्ठीव|निष्ठीवं
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेवः|निष्ठेव|निष्ठेवं
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवम्
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवनम्
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेवनम्
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवितम्
निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वः, -वम्, निष्ठी(ष्ठे)वनम्, निष्ठीवितम्<BR> Spitting out, spitting; Bh. 1. 92.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्ठीवशरावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवशरावः
निष्ठीवः + -शरावः spittoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूत|निष्ठ्यूतं
निष्ठ्यूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spit out, exuded, cast or thrown out; Ś. 4. 5; सुरसरिदिव तेजो<BR> वह्निनिष्ठपूतमैशम् R. 2. 75; अङ्गुष्ठनिष्ठपूत मिवोर्ध्वमुच्चैस्त्रिस्रोतसः<BR> संततधारमम्भः Śi. 3. 10.<BR>—2 Uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूतम्
निष्ठ्यूत + .{@-तम्@} Spitting out, spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूतिः|निष्ठ्यूति
निष्ठ्यूतिः <i>f.</i> Spitting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुर|निष्ठुरं
निष्ठुर <i>a.</i> [नि-स्था-उरच् षत्वटुत्वे]<BR>—1 Hard, rugged, coarse, rough.<BR>—2 Severe, sharp, smart (as a bow); जज्ञे जनैर्मुकुलिताक्षमनाददाने<BR> संरब्धहस्तिपकनिष्टुरचोदनाभिः Śi. 5. 49.<BR>—3 Cruel, harsh, hard-hearted (said of persons or things); व्यवसायः<BR> प्रतिपत्तिनिष्ठुरः R. 8. 65, 3. 62.<BR>—4 Motionless, stiff.<BR>—5 Contumelious.<BR>—6 Harsh, jarring; प्रक्षिप्य व्यनदन्नादं वज्रनिष्पेषनिष्टुरम् Bhāg. 10. 55. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुरम्
निष्ठुर + .{@-रम्@} A harsh speech, abusive language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ण
निष्ण, निष्णात <i>a.</i> [नि-स्ना-क षत्वं टुत्वम्]<BR>—1 Clever, skilful, versed, skilled, conversant, expert; निष्णातोऽपि<BR> च वेदान्ते साधुत्वं नैति दुर्जनः Bv. 1. 87; Bk. 2. 26; Śi. 8. 63; Y. 1. 321;<BR> कुतोऽपत्यस्नेहः कुटिलनयनिष्णातमनसाम् Māl. 2. 7.<BR>—2 Brought about, completed, fully accomplished; निष्णातश्च समागमोऽपि<BR> विहितस्त्वत्प्रेयसः कान्तया Māl. 10. 24; (निःशङ्कं विहितः Jagaddhara).<BR>—3 Superior, perfect.<BR>—4 Agreed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्णात|निष्णातः
निष्ण, निष्णात <i>a.</i> [नि-स्ना-क षत्वं टुत्वम्]<BR>—1 Clever, skilful, versed, skilled, conversant, expert; निष्णातोऽपि<BR> च वेदान्ते साधुत्वं नैति दुर्जनः Bv. 1. 87; Bk. 2. 26; Śi. 8. 63; Y. 1. 321;<BR> कुतोऽपत्यस्नेहः कुटिलनयनिष्णातमनसाम् Māl. 2. 7.<BR>—2 Brought about, completed, fully accomplished; निष्णातश्च समागमोऽपि<BR> विहितस्त्वत्प्रेयसः कान्तया Māl. 10. 24; (निःशङ्कं विहितः Jagaddhara).<BR>—3 Superior, perfect.<BR>—4 Agreed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पक्व|निष्पक्वं
निष्पक्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Decocted, infused.<BR>—2 Well-cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्
निष्पत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To issue or come out of, issue from, fly out of; अयमरविवरेभ्यश्चातकैर्निष्पतद्भिः<BR> Ś. 7. 7; एषा विदूरीभवतः समुद्रात् सकानना निष्पततीव भूमिः R. 13. 18;<BR> Ms. 8. 55; Y. 2. 16; Ku. 3. 71; Me. 71.<BR>—2 To fall away. ━<i>Caus.</i> To annihilate, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतनम्
निष्पतनम् Rushing out, issuing quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पातः|निष्पात
निष्पातः Throbbing, any short or quick motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्राकृतिः|निष्पत्राकृति
निष्पत्राकृतिः <i>f.</i> Excessive pain as experienced by a person pierced<BR> through with an arrow. See under निस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पद्
निष्पद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To issue out of, spring from.<BR>—2 To be produced, be brought about, arise, to be effected; निष्पद्यन्ते<BR> च सस्यानि Ms. 9. 247.<BR>—3 To be got ready or prepared.<BR>—4 To become ripe, ripen. ━<i>Caus.</i> To produce, bring about, cause,<BR> effect, prepare; द्रव्यक्षित्यात्मलिङ्गानि निष्पाद्य प्रोक्ष चासनम् Bhāg. 11. 3. 50;<BR> त्वं नित्यमेकमेव पटं निष्पादयसि Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्तिः|निष्पत्ति
निष्पत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Birth, production; शस्यनिष्पत्तिः.<BR>—2 Ripeness, maturity (परिपाक); कथमप्यम्भसामन्तरा निष्पत्तेः<BR> प्रतीयते Ku. 2. 37.<BR>—3 Perfection, consummation; मोदकेनापि किं तेन निष्पत्तिर्यस्य सेवया Pt. 1. 271.<BR>—4 Completion, accomplishment, termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्न|निष्पन्नः
निष्पन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Born, arisen, sprung up, produced.<BR>—2 Effected, completed, accomplished.<BR>—3 Ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पादनम्
निष्पादनम्<BR>—1 Effecting, accomplishing.<BR>—2 Concluding.<BR>—3 Producing, causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्द|निष्पंद|निष्पन्दः
निष्पन्द <i>a.</i> Motionless, immovable, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्दः|निष्पन्द|निष्पंद
निष्पन्द + .{@-न्दः@}<BR>—1 The tie or bond of friendship; आर्षोऽयं देवि निष्पन्दो यस्त्वामभिभविष्यति<BR> Rām. 3. 55. 35.<BR>—2 Multitude (समूह); नानाद्रुमविकीर्णेषु धातुनिष्पन्दशोभिषु Rām. 4. 67. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पिष्
निष्पिष् €7 P.<BR>—1 To pound, powder, pulverize, reduce to atoms; (तं) निष्पिपेष<BR> क्षितौ क्षिप्रं पूर्णं कुम्भमिवाम्भसि Mb.; शिलानिष्पिष्टमुद्गरः R. 12. 73.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, bruise; ऋष्यमूकमगात् क्लान्तः … निष्पिष्टः<BR> कोष्णमुच्छवसन् Bk. 6. 120.<BR>—3 To rub the hands.<BR>—4 To gnash the teeth. ━<i>Caus.</i> To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पिष्टः|निष्पिष्ट
निष्पिष्टः <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pounded.<BR>—2 Beaten, harassed, oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पीडनम्
निष्पीडनम् Pressing, squeezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पीडित
निष्पीडित <i>p. p.</i> Squeezed, pressed together or out; निष्पीडितेन्दुकरकन्दलजो<BR> नु सेकः U. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पू
निष्पू €9 U.<BR>—1 To purify.<BR>—2 To winnow, faṇ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पवनम्
निष्पवनम् Winnowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाव|निष्पावः
निष्पाव <i>a.</i> Certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पावः|निष्पाव
निष्पाव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Winnowing, cleaning corn &c.<BR>—2 The wind caused by the winnowing sieve or basket.<BR>—3 Wind.<BR>—4 A legume, pod.<BR>—5 A kind of pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पूर्तम्
निष्पूर्तम् Building well, resting place as charity; हव्यं कव्यं<BR> च विविधं निष्पूर्तं हुतमेव च Mb. 7. 59. 16. (See com.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पेषः|निष्पेष
निष्पेषः, -निष्पेषणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing together, grinding, bruising, pulverizing; भुजान्तरनिष्पेष Ve. 3; Māl. 8. 9. 3.<BR>—2 Striking, clashing, hitting against, friction;<BR> प्रक्षिप्य व्यनदन्नादं वज्रनिष्पेषनिष्ठुरम् Bhāg. 10. 55. 19; R. 4. 77;<BR> Mv. 1. 34; K. 56.<BR>—3 The sound produced by striking or clashing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पेषणम्
निष्पेषः, -निष्पेषणम्<BR>—1 Rubbing together, grinding, bruising, pulverizing; भुजान्तरनिष्पेष Ve. 3; Māl. 8. 9. 3.<BR>—2 Striking, clashing, hitting against, friction;<BR> प्रक्षिप्य व्यनदन्नादं वज्रनिष्पेषनिष्ठुरम् Bhāg. 10. 55. 19; R. 4. 77;<BR> Mv. 1. 34; K. 56.<BR>—3 The sound produced by striking or clashing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाणम्
निष्प्रवाणम्, -णि <i>n.</i><BR> New unbleached cloth; ˚युगलम् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाणि
निष्प्रवाणम्, -णि <i>n.</i><BR> New unbleached cloth; ˚युगलम् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्
निस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a prefix to verbs it implies separation (away from, outside of),<BR> certainty, completeness or fulness, enjoyment, crossing over, transgressing<BR> &c.; (for examples see under (निर्).<BR>—2 As a prefix to nouns, not directly derived from verbs, it forms nouns<BR> or adjectives), and has the sense of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) ‘out of’, ‘away from’; as in निर्वन, निष्कौशाम्बि; or<BR>——(<i>b</i>) more usually, ‘not’, ‘without’, ‘devoid of’ (having a privative<BR> force); निःशेष ‘without a remainder’; निष्फल, निर्जल, &c.<BR> <i>N. B.</i> In compound the स् of निस् is changed to र् before vowels<BR> and soft consonants (see निर्), to a visarga before sibilants, to श्<BR> before च् and छ्, and to ष् before क् and प्; cf. दुस्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निष्कण्टक, निष्कन्द, निष्कपट, निष्कम्प, निष्करुण, निष्करूष, निष्कर्मन्, निष्कल, निष्कलङ्क, निष्कषाय, निष्कान्त, निष्काम, निष्कारण, निष्कालकः, निष्कालिक, निष्किञ्चन, निष्किल्विष, निष्कुल, निष्कुलीन, निष्कूज, निष्कूट, निष्कैवल्य, निष्कोश, निष्कौशाम्बि, निष्क्रिय, निर्यम्, निष्क्षत्र, निष्क्षेपः, निश्चक्रम्, निश्चक्रिक, निश्चक्षुस्, निश्चत्वारिंशः, निश्चिन्त, निश्चेतन, निश्चेतस्, निश्चेष्ट, निश्चेष्टाकरण, निश्छन्दस्, निश्छिद्र, निस्तन्तु, निस्तन्द्र, निस्तन्द्रि, निस्तमस्क, निस्तिमिर, निस्तर्क्य, निस्तल, निस्तुल, निस्तुष, निस्तुषत्वम्, निस्तुषित, निस्तेजस्, निस्त्रप, निस्त्रिंश, निस्त्रैगुण्य, निष्पक्व, निष्पङ्क, निष्पताक, निष्पतिसुता, निष्पत्र, निष्पथ्य, निष्पद, निष्पराक्रम, निष्परामर्श, निष्परिकर, निष्परिग्रह, निष्परिच्छद, निष्परिदाह, निष्परिहार्य, निष्परीक्ष, निष्परीहार, निष्परुष, निष्पर्यन्त, निष्पर्याय, निष्पाप, निष्पुत्र, निष्पुराण, निष्पुरुष, निष्पुरुषः, निष्पुलाक, निष्पौरुष, निष्प्रकम्प, निष्प्रकारक, निष्प्रकाश, निष्प्रचार, निष्प्रज्ञ, निष्प्रणय, निष्प्रताप, निष्प्रतिकार, निष्प्रतीकार, निष्प्रतिग्रह, निष्प्रतिघ, निष्प्रतिद्वन्द्व, निष्प्रतिभ, निष्प्रतिभान, निष्प्रतीप, निष्प्रत्याश, निष्प्रत्यूह, निष्प्रपञ्च, निष्प्रभ, निष्प्रमाणक, निष्प्रयत्न, निष्प्रयोजन, निष्प्रवणि, निष्प्रवाण, निष्प्रवाणि, निष्प्राण, निष्फल, निष्फेन, निःशङ्क, निःशब्द, निःशमः, निःशरण, निःशर्कर, निःशलाक, निःशल्य, निःशूक, निःशेष, निःशोध्य, निःश्रीक,^1 निःश्रेयस, निःसंशय, निःसंस्कार, निःसंख्य, निःसंग, निःसंचारः, निःसंज्ञ, निःसत्त्व, निःसंतति, निःसंदिग्ध, निःसंधि, निःसपत्न, निःसमम्, निःसंपात, निःसंबाध, निःसंभ्रम, निःसरणि, निःसह, निःसार, निःसीम, निःस्तम्भ, निःसूत्र, निःस्नेह, निःस्पन्द, निःस्पर्श, निःस्पृह, निःस्व, निःस्वन, निःस्वभावः, निःस्वादु<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक|निष्कण्टकः
निस् + -कण्टक (निष्कण्टक) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 thornless.<BR>—2 free from thorns or enemies, free from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">Page0930-1</a>]<BR> danger or nuisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टकः|निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक
निस् + -कण्टक + .({@-कः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0929-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कन्द|निष्कंद
निस् + -कन्द (निष्कन्द) <i>a.</i> without edible roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कपट
निस् + -कपट (निष्कपट) <i>a.</i> guileless, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कम्प|निष्कंप
निस् + -कम्प (निष्कम्प) <i>a.</i> motionless, steady, immovable;<BR> निष्कम्पचामरशिखाः Ś. 1. 8; Ku. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करुण
निस् + -करुण (निष्करुण) <i>a.</i> merciless, pitiless, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करूष
निस् + -करूष (निष्करूष) <i>a.</i> free from dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्मन्|निष्कर्म्मन्
निस् + -कर्मन् (निष्कर्मन्) <i>a.</i> inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निस् + -कल (निष्कल) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 without parts, undivided, whole.<BR>—2 waned, decayed, diminished.<BR>—3 impotent, barren.<BR>—4 maimed.<BR>—5 inarticulate (a musical term); N. 21. 16.<BR>—6 Without attributes, or qualities; निष्कलं निष्क्रियं शान्तं निरवद्यं<BR> निरञ्जनम् Śvet. Up.; Bhāg. 1. 9. 44; तद् ब्रह्म निष्कलमहं (स्मरामि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कलः|निष्कल|निष्कलं
निस् + -कल + .({@-लः@})<BR>—1 a receptacle.<BR>—2 the pudendum muliebre.<BR>—3 N. of Brahmā. ({@ला, -ली@}) an elderly woman, one who is past<BR> child-bearing, or one in whom menstruation has ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कलङ्क|निष्कलंक
निस् + -कलङ्क, (निष्कलङ्क)<BR> {@-कल्मष@} <i>a.</i> stainless, spotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कषाय
निस् + -कषाय (निष्कषाय) <i>a.</i> free from dirt or impure passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कान्त
निस् + -कान्त (निष्कान्त) <i>a.</i> not lovely, ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काम
निस् + -काम (निष्काम) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from wish or desire, desireless, disinterested, unselfish.<BR>—2 free from all worldly desires; विशिष्टफलदाः पुंषां निष्कामाणां विमुक्तिदाः V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कामम्
निस् + -काम + .({@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i>)<BR>—1 without wish or desire.<BR>—2 unwillingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारण|निष्कारणं
निस् + -कारण (निष्कारण) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 causeless, unnecessary.<BR>—2 disinterested, free from any motive; निष्कारणो बन्धुः.<BR>—3 groundless, not proceeding from any cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारणम्
निस् + -कारण + .({@-णम्@} <i>ind.</i>) without any cause or reason, causelessly, needlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालकः|निष्कालक
निस् + -कालकः (निष्कालकः) a penitent shaven and smeared with<BR> clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालिक
निस् + -कालिक (निष्कालिक) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one whose term of life is over or elapsed, whose days are numbered.<BR>—2 one who has no conqueror, invincible (अजय्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किञ्चन|निष्किंचन
निस् + -किञ्चन (निष्किञ्चन) <i>a.</i> penniless, poor, indigent;<BR> प्रज्ञानं शौचमेवात्र शरीरस्य विशेषतः । तथा निष्किञ्चनत्वं च<BR> मनसश्च प्रसन्नता ॥ Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किल्विष
निस् + -किल्विष (निष्किल्विष) <i>a.</i> sinless, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुल
निस् + -कुल (निष्कुल) <i>a.</i> having no kindred, left alone in<BR> the world. (निष्कुलं कृ ‘to cut off completely, exterminate’; निष्कुला कृ<BR>—1 to exterminate oneʼs family<BR>—2 to shell, strip off the husk; निष्कुलाकरोति दाडिमम् Sk.; N. 22. 15.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुलीन
निस् + -कुलीन (निष्कुलीन) <i>a.</i> of low family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कूज
निस् + -कूज (निष्कूज) <i>a.</i> still, silent; U. 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कूट
निस् + -कूट (निष्कूट) <i>a.</i> pitiless, merciless, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कैवल्य
निस् + -कैवल्य (निष्कैवल्य) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 mere, pure, absolute.<BR>—2 deprived of final beatitude (मोक्षहीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोश
निस् + -कोश (निष्कोश) <i>a.</i> unsheathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कौशाम्बि|निष्कौशांबि
निस् + -कौशाम्बि (निष्कौशाम्बि) <i>a.</i> who has gone out of Kauśāmbī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रिय|निष्क्रियं
निस् + -क्रिय (निष्क्रिय) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inactive.<BR>—2 not performing ceremonial rites; Ms. 10. 58.<BR>—3 knowing higher know. ledge as a sage, Saṃnyāsin; न्यासे कुटीचकः<BR> पूर्वं बह्वोदो हंसनिष्क्रियौ Bhāg. 3. 12. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यम्
निस् + -यम् the Supreme Spirit (ब्रह्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्षत्र
निस् + -क्षत्र (निःक्षत्र), {@-क्षत्रिय@} (निःक्षत्रिय)<BR> <i>a.</i> destitute of the military tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्षेपः
निस् + -क्षेपः (निःक्षेप) = निक्षेप q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चक्रम्
निस् + -चक्रम् (निश्चकम्) <i>ind.</i> completely; निश्चकं हतराक्षसः<BR> पुनरगाद्ब्रह्मत्वमाद्यं स्थिराम् A. Rām. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चक्रिक
निस् + -चक्रिक (निश्चक्रिक) <i>a.</i> without tricks, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चक्षुस्
निस् + -चक्षुस् (निश्चक्षुस्) <i>a.</i> blind, eyeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चत्वारिंशः|निश्चत्वारिंश
निस् + -चत्वारिंशः (निश्चत्वारिंश) <i>a.</i> past forty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चिन्त|निश्चिंत|निश्चिन्तः
निस् + -चिन्त (निश्चिन्त) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from anxiety, unconcerned, secure.<BR>—2 thoughtless, unthinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेतन
निस् + -चेतन (निश्चेतन)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">Page0930-2</a>]<BR> <i>a.</i> unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेतस्
निस् + -चेतस् (निश्चेतस्) <i>a.</i> not in oneʼs right senses, mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्ट|निश्चेष्टः
निस् + -चेष्ट (निश्चेष्ट) <i>a.</i> motionless, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्टाकरण
निस् + -चेष्टाकरण (निश्चेष्टाकरण) <i>a.</i> depriving (one) of<BR> motion, causing motionlessness (said of one the arrows of Cupid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छन्दस्|निश्छंदस्
निस् + -छन्दस् (निश्छन्दस्) <i>a.</i> not studying the Vedas (छन्दस्) Ms. 3. 7^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छिद्र
निस् + -छिद्र (निश्छिद्र) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 without holes.<BR>—2 without defects or weak points.<BR>—3 uninterrupted, unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तन्तु|निस्तंतु
निस् + -तन्तु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having no offspring, childless.<BR>—2 a Brahmachārin; मुण्डा निस्तन्तवश्चापि वसत्यर्थार्थिनः पृथक्<BR> Mb. 12. 167. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तन्द्र|निस्तंद्र
निस् + -तन्द्र, -तन्द्रि <i>a.</i> not lazy, fresh, healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तन्द्रि
निस् + -तन्द्र, -तन्द्रि <i>a.</i> not lazy, fresh, healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तमस्क
निस् + -तमस्क, -तिमिर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from darkness, bright; तस्य द्वितीयहरिविक्रमनिस्तमस्कं वायोरिमं<BR> परिवहस्य वदन्ति मार्गम् Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—2 freed from sin or moral impurities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तिमिर
निस् + -तमस्क, -तिमिर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from darkness, bright; तस्य द्वितीयहरिविक्रमनिस्तमस्कं वायोरिमं<BR> परिवहस्य वदन्ति मार्गम् Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—2 freed from sin or moral impurities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्क्य
निस् + -तर्क्य <i>a.</i> unimaginable, inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तल|निस्तलं
निस् + -तल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 round, globular; मुक्ताकलापस्य च निस्तलस्य Ku. 1. 42; Kau. A. 2. 9.<BR>—2 moving, trembling, shaking.<BR>—3 bottomless.<BR>—4 down, below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तला
निस् + -तल + .({@-ला@}) a pill, round ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुल
निस् + -तुल <i>a.</i> matchless, incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुष
निस् + -तुष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 freed from chaff.<BR>—2 purified, cleansed.<BR>—3 simplified. ˚क्षीरः wheat. ˚रत्नम् a crystal.<BR>—4 faultless, pure; शशंस गुणैररीणैरुदयास्तनिस्तुषम् N. 15. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषत्वम्
निस् + -तुषत्वम् faultlessness; कवेः पुष्यति निस्तुषत्वम् Maṅkhaka 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषित|निस्तुषितं
निस् + -तुषित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 husked.<BR>—2 made thin. —3 abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तेजस्
निस् + -तेजस् <i>a.</i> destitute of fire, heat or energy, powerless, impotent;<BR> न भेतव्यं भृशं चैते मात्रा निस्तेजसः कृताः Mārk. P.<BR>—2 spiritless, dull.<BR>—3 obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रप
निस् + -त्रप <i>a.</i> impudent, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंश|निस्त्रिंशः
निस् + -त्रिंश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 more than thirty; निस्त्रिंशानि वर्षाणि चैत्रस्य P. V. 4. 73; Sk.<BR>—2 pitiless, merciless, cruel; हे निस्त्रिंश विमुक्तकण्ठकरुणं तावत्<BR> सखी रोदितु Amaru. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंशः|निस्त्रिंश
निस् + -त्रिंश + .({@-शः@}) a sword; निजध्नुः शरनिस्त्रिंशकुन्ततोमरशक्तिभिः<BR> Śiva B. 3. 19; शूरौर्निस्त्रिंशपाणिभिः Parṇāl. 1. 5. ˚भृत् <i>m.</i><BR> a sword-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रैगुण्य
निस् + -त्रैगुण्य <i>a.</i> destitute of the three qualities (सत्त्व, रजस्<BR> and तमस्); निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन Bg. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पक्व|निष्पक्वं
निस् + -पक्व (निष्पक्व) well cooked, boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पङ्क|निष्पंक
निस् + -पङ्क (निष्पङ्क) <i>a.</i> free from mud, clear, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पताक
निस् + -पताक (निष्पताक) <i>a.</i> having no flag or banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतिसुता
निस् + -पतिसुता (निष्पतिसुता) a woman having no husband and no sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्र
निस् + -पत्र (निष्पत्र) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 leafless.<BR>—2 unfeathered, featherless. [निष्पत्राकृ ‘to pierce with an arrow so that the feathers come through on the other side’<BR>; to cause excessive<BR> bodily pain (fig.); निष्पत्राकरोति मृगं व्याधः (सपुङ्खस्य शरस्य<BR> अपरपार्श्वे निर्गमनान्निष्पत्रं करोति Sk.); एकश्च मृगः सपत्राकृतोऽन्यश्च<BR> निष्पत्राकृतोऽपतत् Dk. 165; so यान्ती गुरुजनैः साकं स्मयमानाननाम्बुजा ।<BR> तिर्यगग्रीवं यदद्राक्षीत्तन्निष्पत्राकरोज्जगत् Bv. 2. 132.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पथ्य
निस् + -पथ्य (निष्पथ्य) <i>a.</i> unwell, ill<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पद
निस् + -पद (निष्पद) <i>a.</i> having no foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पदम्
निस् + -पद + .({@-दम्@}) a vehicle moving without feet (as a ship).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पराक्रम
निस् + -पराक्रम (निष्पराक्रम) <i>a.</i> weak, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परामर्श
निस् + -परामर्श (निष्परामर्श) <i>a.</i> without advice, helpless; M. 4. 2/3<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिकर
निस् + -परिकर (निष्परिकर) <i>a.</i> without preparations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिग्रह|निष्परिग्रहः
निस् + -परिग्रह (निष्परिग्रह) <i>a.</i> having no property or<BR> possessions; Mu. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिग्रहः|निष्परिग्रह
निस् + -परिग्रह + .({@-हः@}) an ascetic without family, dependents, or other belongings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिच्छद
निस् + -परिच्छद (निष्परिच्छद) <i>a.</i> having no retinue or train.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिदाह
निस् + -परिदाह (निष्परिदाह) <i>a.</i> incombustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिहार्य
निस् + -परिहार्य (निष्परिहार्यं) <i>a.</i> To be applied by all means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परीक्ष
निस् + -परीक्ष (निष्परीक्ष) <i>a.</i> not examining or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">Page0931-1</a>]<BR> testing accurately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0930-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परीहार
निस् + -परीहार (निष्परीहार) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not avoiding.<BR>—2 not observing caution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परुष
निस् + -परुष (निष्परुष) <i>a.</i> (in music) soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पर्यन्त|निष्पर्यंत
निस् + -पर्यन्त (निष्पर्यन्त), {@-पार@} (निष्पार)<BR> <i>a.</i> boundless, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पर्याय
निस् + -पर्याय (निष्पर्याय) <i>a.</i> out of order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाप
निस् + -पाप (निष्पाप) sinless, guiltless, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुत्र
निस् + -पुत्र (निष्पुत्र) <i>a.</i> sonless, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुराण
निस् + -पुराण (निष्पुराण) <i>a.</i> not existing before, unheard of, new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुष|निष्पुरुषः
निस् + -पुरुष (निष्पुरुष)<BR>—1 unpeopled, tenantless, desolate. —2 without male issue; Ms. 3. 7.<BR>—2 not male, feminine, neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुषः|निष्पुरुष
निस् + -पुरुषः<BR>—1 a eunuch.<BR>—2 a coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुलाक
निस् + -पुलाक (निष्पुलाक) <i>a.</i> freed from chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पौरुष
निस् + -पौरुष (निष्पौरुष) <i>a.</i> unmanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकम्प|निष्प्रकंप
निस् + -प्रकम्प (निष्प्रकम्प) <i>a.</i> steady, immovable, motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकारक
निस् + -प्रकारक (निष्प्रकारक)<BR>—1 <i>a.</i> without ditinction of species, without specification, absolute.<BR>—2 without the relation of the qualifier and the qualified, see निर्विकल्प<BR> (7); निष्प्रकारकं ज्ञानं निर्विकल्पकम् T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकाश
निस् + -प्रकाश (निष्प्रकाश) <i>a.</i> not transparent, not clear, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रचार
निस् + -प्रचार (निष्प्रचार) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not moving away, remaining in one place.<BR>—2 concentrated, intently fixed; निष्प्रचारेण मनसा परं तदधिगच्छति<BR> Mb. 12. 215. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रज्ञ
निस् + -प्रज्ञ (निष्प्रज्ञ) <i>a.</i> ignorant, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रणय
निस् + -प्रणय (निष्प्रणय) <i>a.</i> cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रताप
निस् + -प्रताप (निष्प्रताप) <i>a.</i> destitute of glory, mean,<BR> base; शङ्कनीया हि सर्वत्र निष्प्रतापा दरिद्रता Pt. 2. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिकार
निस् + -प्रतिकार, -प्रतीकार (निष्प्रति(ती)कार), {@-प्रतिक्रिय@}, ({@निष्प्रतिक्रिय@}) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 incurable, irremediable; सर्वथा निष्प्रतीकारेयमापदुपस्थिता K. 151.<BR>—2 unobstructed, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिकारम्
निस् + -प्रतिकार, -प्रतीकार + .({@-रम्@}) <i>ind.</i> uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतीकार
निस् + -प्रतिकार, -प्रतीकार (निष्प्रति(ती)कार), {@-प्रतिक्रिय@}, ({@निष्प्रतिक्रिय@}) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 incurable, irremediable; सर्वथा निष्प्रतीकारेयमापदुपस्थिता K. 151.<BR>—2 unobstructed, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिग्रह
निस् + -प्रतिग्रह (निष्प्रतिग्रह) <i>a.</i> not accepting gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिघ
निस् + -प्रतिघ (निष्प्रतिघ) <i>a.</i> unhindered, unobstructed,<BR> unimpeded; स हि निष्प्रतिघेन चक्षुषा त्रितयं ज्ञानमयेन पश्यति R. 8. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिद्वन्द्व|निष्प्रतिद्वंद्व
निस् + -प्रतिद्वन्द्व (निष्प्रतिद्वन्द्व) <i>a.</i> without enemies, unopposed.<BR>—2 matchless, unrivalled, unequalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभ|निष्प्रतिभः
निस् + -प्रतिभ (निष्प्रतिभ) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devoid of splendour.<BR>—2 having no intelligence, not ready-witted, dull, stupid.<BR>—3 apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभान
निस् + -प्रतिभान (निष्प्रतिभान) <i>a.</i> cowardly, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतीप
निस् + -प्रतीप (निष्प्रतीप) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 looking straightforward, not turned backwards.<BR>—2 unconcerned (as a look).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रत्याश
निस् + -प्रत्याश (निष्प्रत्याश) <i>a.</i> hopeless, despondent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रत्यूह|निष्प्रत्यूहः
निस् + -प्रत्यूह (निष्प्रत्यूह) <i>a.</i> unobstructed, unimpeded;<BR> निष्प्रत्यूहाः प्रियसखि यदा दुःसहाः संबभूवुः Māl. 9. 45; निष्प्रत्यूहमुपास्महे<BR> भगवतः कौमोदकीलक्ष्मणः Murārināṭakam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रपञ्च|निष्प्रपंच
निस् + -प्रपञ्च (निष्प्रपञ्च) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 without extension.<BR>—2 without deceit, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभ|निष्प्रभः
निस् + -प्रभ (निःप्रभ or निष्प्रभ) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 lustreless, pale-looking; निष्प्रभश्च रिपुरास भूभृताम् R. 11. 81.<BR>—2 powerless. —3 gloomy, obscure, dim, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रमाणक
निस् + -प्रमाणक (निष्प्रमाणक) <i>a.</i> without authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयत्न
निस् + -प्रयत्न (निष्प्रयत्न) <i>a.</i> inactive, dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयोजन|निष्प्रयोजनं
निस् + -प्रयोजन (निष्प्रयोजन) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 without motive, not influenced by any motive.<BR>—2 causeless, groundless,<BR>—3 useless.<BR>—4 needless, unnecessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयोजनम्
निस् + -प्रयोजन + .({@-नम्@}) <i>ind.</i> causelessly, without reason, without any object; Mu. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवणि
निस् + -प्रवणि, -प्रवाण, -प्रवाणि (निष्प्रवणि, -ष्प्रवाण, -ष्प्रवाणि)<BR> <i>a.</i> fresh from loom, quite new (cloth, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाण|निष्प्रवाणं
निस् + -प्रवणि, -प्रवाण, -प्रवाणि (निष्प्रवणि, -ष्प्रवाण, -ष्प्रवाणि)<BR> <i>a.</i> fresh from loom, quite new (cloth, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाणि
निस् + -प्रवणि, -प्रवाण, -प्रवाणि (निष्प्रवणि, -ष्प्रवाण, -ष्प्रवाणि)<BR> <i>a.</i> fresh from loom, quite new (cloth, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्राण
निस् + -प्राण (निष्पाण) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 lifeless, dead.<BR>—2 Weak (निर्बल); निष्प्राणो नाभिहन्तव्यः Mb. 12. 95. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फल|निष्फलः
निस् + -फल (निष्फल) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bearing no fruit, fruitless (fig. also), unsuccessful,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">Page0931-2</a>]<BR> futile; निष्फलारम्भयत्नाः Me. 56.<BR>—2 useless, profitless, vain; Ku. 4. 13.<BR>—3 barren (as a tree).<BR>—4 meaningless (as a word).<BR>—5 seedless, impotent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फला
निस् + -फल + .({@-ला, -ली@}) a woman past child-bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फली
निस् + -फल + .({@-ला, -ली@}) a woman past child-bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फेन
निस् + -फेन (निष्फेन) <i>a.</i> foamless. ━<i>n.</i> opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्क
निस् + -शङ्क (निःशङ्क) <i>a.</i> free from fear or risk, secure, fearless.<BR> ({@निःशङ्कः@}) (in music) a kind of dance. ━<i>f.</i> (निःशङ्का)<BR> absence of fear. ━<i>ind.</i> fearlessly, securely, easily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्द|निःशब्दः
निस् + -शब्द (निःशब्द) <i>a.</i> not expressed in words, inaudible;<BR> निःशब्दं रोदितुमारेभे K. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्दः|निःशब्द
निस् + -शब्द + .({@-ब्दः, -ब्दम्@}) silence, a calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्दम्
निस् + -शब्द + .({@-ब्दः, -ब्दम्@}) silence, a calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशमः|निःशम
निस् + -शमः (निःशमः) uneasiness, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशरण
निस् + -शरण <i>a.</i> (निःशरण) helpless, forlorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशर्कर
निस् + -शर्कर (निःशर्कर) <i>a.</i> free from pebbles (as a bathing place).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाक|निःशलाकः
निस् + -शलाक (निःशलाक) <i>a.</i> lonely, solitary, retired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाकम्
निस् + -शलाक + .({@-कम्@}) a retired place, solitude; अरण्ये निःशलाके वा मन्त्रयेदविभावितः Ms. 7. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशल्य
निस् + -शल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from arrows.<BR>—2 free from thorns or darts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशूक|निःशूकः
निस् + -शूक (निःशूक) <i>a.</i> merciless, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशूकः|निःशूक
निस् + -शूक + .({@-कः@}) beardless rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निस् + -शेष (निःशेष) <i>a.</i> without remainder (either finished<BR> or passed away).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोध्य|निःशोध्यं
निस् + -शोध्य (निःशोध्य) <i>a.</i> washed, pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रीक
निस् + -श्रीक^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deprived of lustre, beauty.<BR>—2 unhappy.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयस|निःश्रेयसं|निःश्रेयसः
निस् + -श्रेयस <i>a.</i> the best, most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयसः|निःश्रेयस|निःश्रेयसं
निस् + -श्रेयस + .({@-सः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयसम्
निस् + -श्रेयस + .({@-सम्@}) final beatitude, absolution; यः करोति वधोदर्का निःश्रेयसकरीः<BR> क्रियाः Ki. 11. 19; see निःश्रेयस also.<BR>—2 devotion, faith, belief.<BR>—3 apprehension, conception.<BR>—4 happiness (in general), welfare; इदं निःश्रेयसं परम् Ms. 1. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंशय
निस् + -संशय (निःसंशय) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 undoubted, certain.<BR>—2 not doubtful, not suspecting or doubting; कुरु निःसंशयं वत्से<BR> स्ववृत्ते लोकमित्यशात् R. 15. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंशयम्
निस् + -संशय + .({@-यम्@}) <i>ind.</i> doubtlessly, undoubtedly, surely, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंस्कार
निस् + -संस्कार (निःसंस्कार) <i>a.</i> uneducated, ill-mannered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंख्य|निःसङ्ख्य
निस् + -संख्य (निःसंख्य) <i>a.</i> innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंग|निःसङ्ग|निःसंगः|निःसङ्गः
निस् + -संग (निःसंग) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not attached or devoted to, regardless of, indifferent to; यन्निःसंगस्त्वं<BR> फलस्यानतेभ्यः Ki. 18. 24.<BR>—2 one who has renounced all worldly attachments; भर्तुर्ये प्रलयेऽपि<BR> पूर्वसुकृतासङ्गेन निःसङ्गया भक्त्या कार्यधुरं वहन्ति कृतिनस्ते दुर्लभास्त्वादृशाः Mu. 1. 14.<BR>—3 unconnected, separated, detached.<BR>—4 unobstructed; निःसङ्गं प्रतिभिरुपाददे विवृत्तिः Ki. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंगम्|निःसङ्गम्
निस् + -संग + .({@-गम्@}) <i>ind.</i> unselfishly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंचारः|निःसञ्चार
निस् + -संचारः (निःसंचारः) not taking a walk; Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंज्ञ
निस् + -संज्ञ (निःसंज्ञ) <i>a.</i> unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्त्व
निस् + -सत्त्व (निःसत्त्व) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 unenergetic, weak, impotent.<BR>—2 mean, insignificant, low.<BR>—3 non-existent, unsubstantial.<BR>—4 deprived of living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्त्वम्
निस् + -सत्त्व + .({@-त्त्वम्@})<BR>—1 absence of power or energy.<BR>—2 non-existence.<BR>—3 insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंतति|निःसन्तति
निस् + -संतति (निःसंतति), {@-संतान@} ({@निःसंतान@})<BR> <i>a.</i> childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंदिग्ध|निःसन्दिग्ध
निस् + -संदिग्ध (निःसंदिग्ध), {@-संदेह@}, (निःसंदेह)<BR> <i>a.</i> see निःसंशय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंधि|निःसन्धि|निःसन्धिः
निस् + -संधि (निस्संधि, निःसंधि) <i>a.</i> having no joints perceptible,<BR> compact, firm, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसपत्न
निस् + -सपत्न (निःसपत्न) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having no rival or enemy; घनरुचिरकलापो निःसपत्नोऽद्य जातः V. 4. 10.<BR>—2 not claimed by another, belonging exclusively to one possessor.<BR>—3 having no foes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसमम्
निस् + -समम् (निःसमम्) <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 unseasonably, at a wrong time.<BR>—2 wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंपात|निःसम्पात|निःसंपातः|निःसम्पातः
निस् + -संपात (निःसंपात) <i>a.</i> affording no passage, blocked up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंपातः|निःसम्पात|निःसंपात|निःसम्पातः
निस् + -संपात + .({@-तः@}) the darkness of midnight, thick darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंबाध
निस् + -संबाध (निःसंबाध) <i>a.</i> not contracted, spacious, large.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">Page0932-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0931-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंभ्रम|निःसम्भ्रम
निस् + -संभ्रम (निःसंभ्रम) <i>a.</i> not perplexed, unembarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरणि
निस् + -सरणि (निःसरणि) <i>a.</i> pathless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निस् + -सह (निःसह) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Exhausted, powerless; कुसुमावचयपरिश्रमनिःसहं मे शरीरम् Nāg. 2.<BR>—2 intolerable, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
निस् + -सार (निःसार) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 sapless, pithless.<BR>—2 worthless, vain, unsubstantial. ˚ता<BR>—1 sapless, pithlessness; निःसारत्वाल्लघीयसः (तृणस्य च समा<BR> गतिः) Pt. 1. 106.<BR>—2 worthlessness. —3 vanity, unsubstantial or transitory nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसीम
निस् + -सीम (निःसीम), {@-सीमन्@} (निःसीमन्)<BR> <i>a.</i> immeasurable, boundless; अहह<BR> महतां निःसीमानश्चरित्रविभूतयः Bh. 2. 35; निःसीमशर्मप्रदम् 3. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्तम्भ
निस् + -स्तम्भ (निःस्तम्भ) <i>a.</i> having no pillars.<BR>—2 having no support.<BR>—3 not proud; निःस्तम्भो भ्रष्टसंकल्पः स्वान् मेघान् स न्यवारयत् Bhāg. 10. 25. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसूत्र
निस् + -सूत्र <i>a.</i> helpless; निःसूत्रमास्ते घनपङ्कमृत्सु N. 7. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्नेह|निःस्नेहः
निस् + -स्नेह (निःस्नेह) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not unctuous or greasy, without unction or oil, dry.<BR>—2 not showing affection, unfeeling, unkind, indifferent.<BR>—3 not loved, not cared for; केशा अपि विरज्यन्तो निःस्नेहाः किं न सेवकाः Pt. 1. 82.<BR>—4 not longing for, indifferent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्नेहा
निस् + -स्नेह + .({@-हा@}) lin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पन्द|निःस्पंद
निस् + -स्पन्द (निःस्पन्द or निस्स्पन्द) <i>a.</i> motionless,<BR> steady; ज्याबन्धनिस्स्पन्दभुजेन यस्य R. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पर्श
निस् + -स्पर्श (निःस्पर्श) <i>a.</i> hard, rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पृह
निस् + -स्पृह (निःस्पृह) <i>a.</i> free from desire; निःस्पृहस्य तृणं जगत्.<BR>—2 regardless of, indifferent to; ननु वक्तृविशेषनिःस्पृहाः Ki. 2. 5;<BR> R. 8. 10; भोगेभ्यः स्पृहयालवो न हि वयं का निःस्पृहाणामसि Bh.<BR>—3 content, unenvious.<BR>—4 free from any worldly ties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्व|निःस्वः
निस् + -स्व (निःस्व) <i>a.</i> poor, indigent; निस्वो वष्टि शतम्<BR> Śānti. 2. 6; त्यक्त्वा जनयितारं स्वं निःस्वं गच्छति दूरतः Pt. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वन|निःस्वनः
निस् + -स्वन (निःस्वन) <i>a.</i> soundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वभावः|निःस्वभाव
निस् + -स्वभावः (निःस्वभावः) poverty. ━<i>a.</i> void of peculiarities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वादु
निस् + -स्वादु (निःस्वादु) <i>a.</i> tasteless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसंपात|निसम्पात|निसम्पातः
निसंपात See निःसंपात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसानः|निःसान
निःसानः A drum ? (Mar. नगारा); तं श्रुत्वा कारतलवः शिवनिःसाननिःस्वनम्<BR> Śiva B. 28. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारः|निःसार
निःसारः A multitude (समूह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदन|निसूदनं
निसूदन <i>p. p.</i> Killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदनम्
निसूदन + .{@-नम्@} Killing, slaughter; cf. निषूदन. यमिन्द्रशब्दार्थनिसूदनं हरेः Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृज्
निसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To set free, release; न स्वामिना निसृष्टोऽपि शूद्रो दास्याद्विमुच्यते Ms. 8. 414.<BR>—2 To deliver over, consign, entrust.<BR>—3 To give away, offer, present; see निसृष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गः|निसर्ग
निसर्गः —1 Bestowing, granting. presenting, giving away; न चाधेः<BR> कालसंरोधान्निसर्गोऽस्ति न विक्रयः Ms. 8. 143.<BR>—2 A grant.<BR>—3 Evacuation, voiding excrement.<BR>—4 Abandoning, relinquishing.<BR>—5 Creation; प्रजा निसर्गाद् विप्रान् वै क्षत्रियाः पूजयन्ति ह Mb. 14. 58. 5.<BR>—6 Nature, natural character, natural state or condition; निसर्गदुर्बोधम्<BR> Ki. 1. 6, 18. 31; R. 3. 35; Ku. 4. 16; निसर्गतः, निसर्गेण ‘by nature’,<BR> or ‘naturally’.<BR>—7 Exchange, barter.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निसर्गज, निसर्गसिद्ध, निसर्गनिपुण, निसर्गभिन्न, निसर्गविनीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गज
निसर्गः + -ज, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> innate, inborn, natural; निसर्गजं तु तत्तस्य<BR> कस्तस्मात्तदपोहति Ms. 8. 414.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गसिद्ध
निसर्गः + -ज, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> innate, inborn, natural; निसर्गजं तु तत्तस्य<BR> कस्तस्मात्तदपोहति Ms. 8. 414.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गनिपुण
निसर्गः + -निपुण <i>a.</i> naturally clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गभिन्न
निसर्गः + -भिन्न <i>a.</i> different by nature; निसर्गभिन्नास्पदमेकसंस्थम् R. 6. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गविनीत
निसर्गः + -विनीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 naturally discreet.<BR>—2 naturally well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्ट|निसृष्टं
निसृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Delivered, given, bestowed.<BR>—2 Abandoned, left.<BR>—3 Dismissed.<BR>—4 Permitted, allowed.<BR>—5 Central, middle.<BR>—6 Kindled (as fire).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निसृष्टार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्टार्थ|निसृष्टार्थः
निसृष्ट + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> to whom the management of an affair is entrusted;<BR> उभयोर्भावमुन्नीय स्वयं वदति चोत्तरम् । संदिष्टः कुरुते कर्म निसृष्टार्थः स उच्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्टार्थः|निसृष्टार्थ
निसृष्ट + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@})<BR>—1 an envoy, ambassador.<BR>—2 a messenger, an agent; see S. D. 86, 87. ˚दूती a female who, having<BR> discovered the love of a youth and maiden for each other, brings about<BR> their union of her own accord; तन्निपुणं निसृष्टार्थदूतीकल्पः सूत्रयितव्यः<BR> Māl. 1; (where Jagaddhara explains निसृष्टार्थदूती by नायिकाया नायकस्य<BR> वा मनोरथं ज्ञात्वा स्वमत्या कार्यं साधयति या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तनी
निस्तनी A pill, bolus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तब्ध
निस्तब्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Paralysed.<BR>—2 Stopped, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्हणम्
निस्तर्हणम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुद्
निस्तुद् €1 P. To pierce, prick, sting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तोदः|निस्तोद
निस्तोदः, निस्तोदनम् Piercing, pricking, stinging; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तोदनम्
निस्तोदः, निस्तोदनम् Piercing, pricking, stinging; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तॄ
निस्तॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To pass through, cross over (fig. also); निस्तीर्णा प्रतिज्ञासरित्<BR> Mu. 1; Bh. 3. 4; Ve. 6. 36.<BR>—2 To fulfil, accomplish.<BR>—3 To pass or get over, surmount, overcome; धनैरापदं मानवा निस्तरन्ति<BR> Subhāṣ.; R. 3. 7.<BR>—4 To complete, go to the end of; पितुर्नियोगाद्वनवासमेवं निस्तीर्य<BR> रामः प्रतिपन्नराज्यः R. 14. 21.<BR>—5 To pass or spend (as a time).<BR>—6 To expiate, atone for.<BR>—7 To get out of, escape, be saved from. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To deliver, rescue; save; निस्तारयति दुर्गाच्च महतश्चैव किल्बिषात् Ms. 3. 98.<BR>—2 To overcome, surmount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तरणम्
निस्तरणम्<BR>—1 Going out or forth, coming out of.<BR>—2 Crossing over.<BR>—3 Rescue, deliverance, getting rid of.<BR>—4 An expedient, a means, plan.<BR>—5 Accomplishing, mastering (पारगमन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारः|निस्तार
निस्तारः<BR>—1 Crossing or passing over; संसार तव निस्तारपदवी न दवीयसी Bh. 1. 69.<BR>—2 Getting rid of, release, escape, rescue.<BR>—3 Final emancipation.<BR>—4 Discharge or payment of a debt, acquittance, requital; वेतनस्य<BR> निस्तारः कृतः H. 3.<BR>—5 A means, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारणम्
निस्तारणम्<BR>—1 Passing or conveying across.<BR>—2 Conquering, overcoming.<BR>—3 Delivering, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तीर्ण
निस्तीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rescued, delivered, saved.<BR>—2 Crossed (fig. also).<BR>—3 Fulfilled, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रुटी
निस्त्रुटी Cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्नावः|निस्नाव
निस्नावः Residue of articles after a sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्द|निस्पंद|निस्पन्दः
निस्पन्द <i>a.</i> Immovable, steady; अतो निस्पन्दमभवद्धनाध्यक्षविनाकृतम् Rām. 7. 16. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्दः|निस्पन्द|निस्पंद
निस्पन्द + .{@-दः@} Trembling, throbbing motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्दः|निस्यन्द|निस्यंदः
निस्य(ष्य)न्दः<BR>—1 Flowing forth or down, trickling down, dropping, dripping, streaming,<BR> oozing; वल्कलशिखा-निस्यन्दरेखाङ्किताः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">Page0933-1</a>]<BR> Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—2 A discharge, flux, sap, juice; इभदलितविकीर्णग्रन्थिनिष्यन्दगन्धः<BR> U. 2. 21; Māl. 9. 6.<BR>—3 A flow, stream, fluid that trickles down; हिमाद्रिनिस्यन्द इवावतीर्णः<BR> R. 14. 3, 3. 41, 16. 70; मदनिस्यन्दरेखयोः 10. 57; Me. 44.<BR>—4 Necessary consequence or result.<BR>—5 Uttering, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्यन्दः|निष्यन्द|निष्यंद|निष्यंदः
निस्य(ष्य)न्दः<BR>—1 Flowing forth or down, trickling down, dropping, dripping, streaming,<BR> oozing; वल्कलशिखा-निस्यन्दरेखाङ्किताः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">Page0933-1</a>]<BR> Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—2 A discharge, flux, sap, juice; इभदलितविकीर्णग्रन्थिनिष्यन्दगन्धः<BR> U. 2. 21; Māl. 9. 6.<BR>—3 A flow, stream, fluid that trickles down; हिमाद्रिनिस्यन्द इवावतीर्णः<BR> R. 14. 3, 3. 41, 16. 70; मदनिस्यन्दरेखयोः 10. 57; Me. 44.<BR>—4 Necessary consequence or result.<BR>—5 Uttering, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0932-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्दिन्|निस्यंदिन्
निस्यन्दिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Trickling or flowing down, oozing.<BR>—2 Dropping or pouring down; कनकरसनिस्यन्दी सानुमानालोक्यते Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्रवः|निस्रव
निस्रवः, निस्रावः<BR>—1 A stream, torrent.<BR>—2 The scum of boiled rice.<BR>—3 Flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्रावः|निस्राव
निस्रवः, निस्रावः<BR>—1 A stream, torrent.<BR>—2 The scum of boiled rice.<BR>—3 Flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वनः|निस्वन
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितम्<BR>—1 Noise, voice; सुखश्रवा मङ्गलतूर्यनिस्वनाः R. 3. 19; Ṛs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>—2 The whistling sound of an arrow (only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वानः|निस्वान
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितम्<BR>—1 Noise, voice; सुखश्रवा मङ्गलतूर्यनिस्वनाः R. 3. 19; Ṛs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>—2 The whistling sound of an arrow (only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वनितम्
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितम्<BR>—1 Noise, voice; सुखश्रवा मङ्गलतूर्यनिस्वनाः R. 3. 19; Ṛs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>—2 The whistling sound of an arrow (only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्
निहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To kill, destroy; देवयजीन् निहन्मः Bk. 2. 34, 6. 10; R. 11. 71; Y. 3. 262.<BR>—2 To strike, hit; तानेव सामर्षतया निजध्नुः R. 7. 44; Ms. 7. 27.<BR>—3 To conquer, overcome; दैवं निहत्य कुरु पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या Pt. 1. 361.<BR>—4 To beat, strike (as a drum); कोणैर्भेर्यो निजघ्निरे Bk. 14. 2.<BR>—5 To counteract, oppose, render void, frustrate; वचसेव तयोर्वाक्यमस्त्रमस्त्रेण<BR> निध्नतोः R. 12. 92.<BR>—6 To cure (as a disease).<BR>—7 To disregard.<BR>—8 To remove, dispel; बद्धां बद्धां भित्तिशङ्काममुष्मिन्नावानावान्मातरिश्वा<BR> निहन्ति Ki. 5. 36.<BR>—9 To strike in, infix.<BR>—10 (In gram.) To cut off, separate; अतिङन्तात् पदात् पदं तिङन्तं<BR> निहन्यते Sk. on P. VIII. 1. 28, 29, 30. ━<i>Caus.</i> To kill, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहत
निहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck down, smitten, killed, slain.<BR>—2 Struck into, infixed.<BR>—3 Attached or devoted.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निहतार्थता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहतार्थता
निहत + -अर्थता a kind of fault in poetry; ग्राम्योऽप्रतीतसन्दिग्धनेयार्थनिहतार्थता S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहननम्
निहननम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्तृ|निहंतृ
निहन्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A killer.<BR>—2 Destructive, murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहवः|निहव
निहवः Invocation, summoning, calling; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहिंसनम्
निहिंसनम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहाका
निहाका<BR>—1 The Gangetic alligator.<BR>—2 A storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहार|निहारः
निहार See नीहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
निहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed, laid, lodged, situated, deposited; उत्तीरं निहितविवृत्तलोचनेन Ki. 7. 34.<BR>—2 Delivered, entrusted.<BR>—3 Bestowed upon; applied to.<BR>—4 Inserted infixed.<BR>—5 Treasured up.<BR>—6 Held.<BR>—7 Laid (as dust).<BR>—8 Uttered in a deep tone.<BR>—9 Encamped (as an army).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निहितदण्ड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहितदण्ड
निहित + -दण्ड <i>a.</i> One showing clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
निहीन <i>a.</i> Low, vile; निहीनमुपतिष्ठेयं शार्दूली क्रोष्टुकं यथा<BR> Mb. 3. 278. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीनः|निहीन
निहीन + .{@-नः@} A low man, one of vile origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नु
निह्नु €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To hide, conceal; देव्या निह्नोतुमिच्छोरिति सुरसरितम् Mu. 1. 1; Bk. 10. 36.<BR>—2 To deny or dissimulate before any one, to hide from (with dat.); अशप्त<BR> निह्नुवानोऽसो सीतायै स्मरमोहितः Bk. 8. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवः|निह्नव
निह्नवः<BR>—1 Denial, concealment of knowledge; कार्यः स्वमतिनिह्नवः Māl. 1. 12;<BR> Candr. 5. 27.<BR>—2 Secrecy, concealment in general; निह्नवे याचितो दद्याद्धनं राज्ञे<BR> च तत्समम् Y. 2. 11, 267.<BR>—3 A secret.<BR>—4 Mistrust; doubt, suspicion.<BR>—5 Wickedness.<BR>—6 Atonement, expiation; तस्यैष व्यभिचारस्य निह्नवः सम्यगुच्यते Ms. 9. 21.<BR>—7 Contradiction.<BR>—8 Obscuring, surpassing.<BR>—9 Excuse, exculpation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: निह्नवोत्तरम्, निह्नववादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवोत्तरम्
निह्नवः + -उत्तरम् an evasive reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नववादिन्
निह्नवः + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a defendant or witness who prevaricates or gives<BR> evasive replies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवनम्
निह्नवनम्<BR>—1 Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>—2 Excuse, exculpation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुत
निह्नुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Denied, disowned.<BR>—2 Concealed, dissembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुति|निह्नुतिः
निह्नुति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Denial, concealment of knowledge; धन्यो हन्यत एव निह्नुतिपरः<BR> प्रेयान् रुदत्या हसन् Amaru. 9.<BR>—2 Dissimulation, reserve.<BR>—3 Secrecy, concealment in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्रादः|निह्राद
निह्रादः A sound; cf. निर्ह्राद. प्रोवाच निह्रादवता स्वरेण<BR> Bu. C. 3. 60; सारसैः कलनिह्रादैः क्वचिदुन्नमिताननौ R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी €1 U. (नयति-ते, निनाय-निन्ये, अनैषीत्-अनेष्ट, नेष्यति-ते, नेतुम्,<BR> नीत) (One of the roots that govern two accusatives, see examples below)<BR>—1 To carry, lead, bring, convey, take, conduct; अजां ग्रामं नयति<BR> Sk.; नय मां नवेन वसतिं पयोमुचा V. 4. 43.<BR>—2 To guide, direct, govern; मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयबुद्धिः M. 1. 2.<BR>—3 To lead away to, carry or bring away; सीता लङ्कां नीता सुरारिणा<BR> Bk. 6. 49; R. 12. 103; Ms. 6. 88.<BR>—4 To carry off; Śānti. 3. 5.<BR>—5 To carry off for oneself (Ātm.).<BR>—6 To spend, or pass (as time); येनामन्दमरन्दे दलदरविन्दे दिनान्यनायिषत<BR> Bv. 1. 10; नीत्वा मासान् कतिचित् Me. 2; संविष्टः कुशशयने निशां<BR> निनाय R. 1. 95.<BR>—7 To bring or reduce any person to any state or condition; तमपि तरलतामनयदनङ्गः<BR> K. 143; नीतस्त्वया पञ्चताम् Ratn. 3. 3; R. 8. 19. (In this sense the<BR> root is used with substantives much in the same way as कृ q. v.);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> दुःखं नी to reduce to misery; वशं नी to reduce to<BR> subjection, win over; अस्तं नी to cause to set; विनाशं नी to destroy;<BR> परितोषं नी to gratify, please; शूद्रतां-दासत्वं &c. नी<BR> to reduce to the state of a Śūdra, slave &c.; साक्ष्यं नी to admit<BR> as a witness; दण्डं नी to inflict punishment upon, to punish; पुनरुक्ततां<BR> नी to render superfluous; विक्रयं नी to sell; भस्मतां-भस्मसात्<BR> नी to reduce to ashes &c.<BR>—8 To ascertain, investigate, inquire into, settle, decide; छलं निरस्य<BR> भूतेन व्यवहारान्नयेन्नृपः Y. 2. 19; एवं शास्त्रेषु भिन्नेषु बहुधा<BR> नीयते क्रिया Mb.<BR>—9 To trace, track, find out; एतैर्लिङ्गैर्नयेत् सीमाम् Ms. 8. 252, 256;<BR> यथा नयत्यसृक्पातैर्मृगस्य मृगयुः पदम् 8. 44; Y. 2. 151.<BR>—10 To marry.<BR>—11 To exclude from.<BR>—12 (Ātm.) To instruct, give instruction in; शास्त्रे नयते Sk. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (नाययति-ते) To cause to lead, carry &c. (with instr. of agent);<BR> तेन मां सरस्तीरमनाययत् K. 38. ━<i>Desid.</i> (निनीषति-ते)<BR> To wish to carry &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0933-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी <i>m.</i> (Used at the end of comp.) A leader, guide; as in ग्रामणी,<BR> सेनानी, अग्रणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
नीत <i>p. p.</i> [नी-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Carried, conducted, led.<BR>—2 Gained, obtained.<BR>—3 Brought or reduced to<BR>—4 Spent, passed away; नीतं जन्म नवीननीरजवने पीतं मधु स्वेच्छया<BR> Bhramarāṣṭakam<BR>—5 Well-behaved, correct; see नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतम्
नीत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth<BR>—2 Corn, grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिः|नीति
नीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Guidance, direction, management.<BR>—2 Conduct, manner of conducting oneself, behaviour, course of action.<BR>—3 propriety, decorum.<BR>—4 Policy, prudence, wisdom, right course; आर्जवं हि कुटिलेषु न नीतिः<BR> N. 5. 103; R. 13. 69; Ku. 1. 22.<BR>—5 A plan, contrivance, scheme; भूयः स्नेहविचेष्टितैर्मृगदृशो नीतस्य<BR> कोटिं पराम् Māl. 6. 3.<BR>—6 Politics, political science, statesmanship, political wisdom; आत्मोदयः<BR> परग्लानिर्द्वयं नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30; दण्डो दमयतामस्मि नीतिरस्मि<BR> जिगीषताम् Bg. 10. 38.<BR>—7 Righteousness, moral conduct, morality.<BR>—8 The science of morality, morals, ethics, moral philosophy; निन्दन्तु<BR> नीतिनिपुणा यदि वा स्तुवन्तु Bh. 2. 83.<BR>—9 Acquirement, acquisition.<BR>—10 Giving, offering, presenting.<BR>—11 Relation, support.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नीतिकुशल, नीतिज्ञ, नीतिनिपुण, नीतिनिष्ण, नीतिविद्, नीतिघोषः, नीतिदोषः, नीतिबीजम्, नीतिविद्या, नीतिविषयः, नीतिव्यतिक्रमः, नीतिशतकम्, नीतिशास्त्रम्, नीतिसन्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिकुशल
नीतिः + -कुशल, -ज्ञ, -निपुण, -निष्ण, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one versed in politics, a statesman, politician.<BR>—2 prudent, wise; किं चित्रं यदि राजनीतिकुशलो राजा भवेद्धार्मिकः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिज्ञ
नीतिः + -कुशल, -ज्ञ, -निपुण, -निष्ण, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one versed in politics, a statesman, politician.<BR>—2 prudent, wise; किं चित्रं यदि राजनीतिकुशलो राजा भवेद्धार्मिकः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0934-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

