नैपुण See निपुण; तथैव तेऽस्तूपमा जीवलोके यथा धर्मो नैपुणेनोपदिष्टः<BR> Mb. 13. 113. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुणम्
नैपुणम् (-ण्यम्)<BR>—1 Dexterity, skill, cleverness, proficiency; चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य धर्मं<BR> वै नैपुण्येन प्रकीर्तय Mb. 13. 141. 34; नैपुणोन्नेयमन्ति U. 6. 26; Śi. 16. 30.<BR>—2 Strictness, exactness.<BR>—3 Anything that requires skill, a delicate matter.<BR>—4 Totality, completeness; इदं तु वृत्तिवैकल्यात्त्यजतो धर्मनैपुणम् Ms. 10. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण्यम्
नैपुणम् (-ण्यम्)<BR>—1 Dexterity, skill, cleverness, proficiency; चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य धर्मं<BR> वै नैपुण्येन प्रकीर्तय Mb. 13. 141. 34; नैपुणोन्नेयमन्ति U. 6. 26; Śi. 16. 30.<BR>—2 Strictness, exactness.<BR>—3 Anything that requires skill, a delicate matter.<BR>—4 Totality, completeness; इदं तु वृत्तिवैकल्यात्त्यजतो धर्मनैपुणम् Ms. 10. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैभृत्यम्
नैभृत्यम्<BR>—1 Modesty, humility.<BR>—2 Secrecy; नैभृत्यमवलम्बितम् M. 5; Mb. 5. 53. 10.<BR>—3 Stillness, silentness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमन्त्रणकम्
नैमन्त्रणकम् A banquet, feast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमयः|नैमय
नैमयः A trader, merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्त|नैमित्तः
नैमित्त <i>a.</i> (-त्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to signs, marks &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तः|नैमित्त
नैमित्त + .{@-त्तः@} An astrologer, fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं|नैमित्तिकः
नैमित्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Produced by, connected with, or dependent on, any particular cause.<BR>—2 Unusual, occasional, accidental, produced by some cause (opp. नित्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिकः|नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं
नैमित्तिक + .{@-कः@} An astrologer, prophet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिकम्
नैमित्तिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 An effect (opp. निमित्त ‘cause’); निमित्तनैमित्तिकयोरयं क्रमः Ś. 7. 30.<BR>—2 An occasional rite, a periodical ceremony, a conditional act, an act<BR> which is to be performed on the occurrence of a निमित्त; निमित्तप्राप्तौ<BR> च नैमित्तिकं कर्तव्यम् ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नैमित्तिककर्मन्, नैमित्तिकलयः, नैमित्तिकश्राद्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिककर्मन्|नैमित्तिककर्म्मन्
नैमित्तिक + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-क्रिया@}<BR> an occasional or periodical ceremony or rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिकलयः|नैमित्तिकलय
नैमित्तिक + -लयः N. of a ब्राह्मलय occurring at the end of four thousand years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिकश्राद्धम्
नैमित्तिक + -श्राद्धम् a special funeral rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिष
नैमिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Lasting for a ‘nimiṣa’ or twinkling, momentary, transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषम्
नैमिष + .{@-षम्@} N. of a sacred forest celebrated as the residence of certain<BR> sages to whom Sauti related the Mahābhārata; शिश्रिये श्रुतवतामपश्चिमः<BR> पश्चिमे वयसि नैमिषं वशी R. 19. 1; (the name is thus derived:− यतस्तु<BR> निमिषेणेदं निहतं दानवं बलम् । अरण्येऽस्मिंस्ततस्तेन नैमिषारण्यसंज्ञितम् ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषीयः|नैमिषीय
नैमिषीयः, -नैमिषेयः<BR> An inhabitant of the forest, called Naimiṣa; सह<BR> नैमिषीयाणामुद्गाता बभूव Ch. Up. 1. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषेयः|नैमिषेय
नैमिषीयः, -नैमिषेयः<BR> An inhabitant of the forest, called Naimiṣa; सह<BR> नैमिषीयाणामुद्गाता बभूव Ch. Up. 1. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमेयः|नैमेय
नैमेयः Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयग्रोधम्
नैयग्रोधम् The fruit of न्यग्रोध, the Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयत्यम्
नैयत्यम्<BR>—1 Restraint, self-command.<BR>—2 Necessity, obligation.<BR>—3 The being settled or established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिक
नैयमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Conformable to rule or precept, regular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिकम्
नैयमिक + .{@-कम्@} Regularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयाय
नैयाय <i>a.</i> Treating of, or explaining the Nyāya philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0940-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयायिकः|नैयायिक
नैयायिकः A logician, a follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy;<BR> नैयायिकानां तु नये द्व्यणुकादावपीष्यते Bhāṣā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरन्तर्यम्
नैरन्तर्यम्<BR>—1 Uninterruptedness, close succession, continuity; स तु दीर्घकालनैरन्तर्यसत्कारासेवितो<BR> दृढभूमिः Yoga S. 1. 14; नभो नैरन्तर्यप्रचलिततडित्पिञ्जरमिव Mv. 1. 43.<BR>—2 Closeness, contiguity (in space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरपेक्ष्यम्
नैरपेक्ष्यम् Disregard, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरयिकः|नैरयिक
नैरयिकः An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरर्थ्यम्
नैरर्थ्यम् Senselessness, nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैराश्यम्
नैराश्यम्<BR>—1 Hopelessness, despair, despondency; आशा हि परमं दुःखं नैराश्यं<BR> परमं सुखम् Bhāg. 11. 8. 44; तटस्थं नैराश्यात् U. 3. 13.<BR>—2 Absence of wish or expectation; येनाशाः पृष्ठतः कृत्वा नैराश्यमवलम्बितम्<BR> H. 1. 124; Bv. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्तः|नैरुक्त|नैरुक्तं
नैरुक्तः, -नैरुक्तिकः<BR> One who knows the etymology of words, an etymologist; Ms. 12. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्तिकः|नैरुक्तिक
नैरुक्तः, -नैरुक्तिकः<BR> One who knows the etymology of words, an etymologist; Ms. 12. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुज्यम्
नैरुज्यम् Health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृतः|नैरृत
नैरृतः<BR>—1 A demon; भयमप्रलयोद्वेगादाचख्युर्नैरृतोदधेः R. 10. 34, 11. 21, 12. 43, 14. 4, 15. 20.<BR>—2 The regent of the south-western direction; निर्घृणं नैरृतादुच्चैर्वलिनं<BR> मारुतादपि Śiva B. 29. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृतम्
नैरृतः + .{@-तम्@} The lunar mansion called Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृती
नैरृती<BR>—1 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—2 The south-western direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत्य
नैरृत्य <i>a.</i> South-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गुण्यम्
नैर्गुण्यम्<BR>—1 Absence of qualities or properties; गुणानुरक्तं व्यसनाय जन्तोः<BR> क्षेमाय नैर्गुण्यमथो मनः स्यात् Bhāg. 5. 11. 8.<BR>—2 Want of excellence, absence of good qualities; नैर्गुण्यमेव साधीयो<BR> धिगस्तु गुणगौरवम् Bv. 1. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्घृण्यम्
नैर्घृण्यम् Pitilessness, cruelty; वैषम्यनैर्धृण्ये न सापेक्षत्वात्<BR> तथा हि दर्शयति Br. Sūt. 2. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्दश्य
नैर्दश्य <i>a.</i> Getting over dangerous or critical times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्देशिकः|नैर्देशिक
नैर्देशिकः A servant; नैर्देशिकैर्यस्य वशे जनोऽयम् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्मल्यम्
नैर्मल्यम् Cleanness, purity, spotlessness (physical as well as moral).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्लज्ज्यम्
नैर्लज्ज्यम्^1 Shamelessness, impudence.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf other dictionaries..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैल्यम्
नैल्यम् Blueness, dark-blue colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्वाहिक
नैर्वाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Conducting or leading out, carrying (as water &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्वाहिकम्
नैर्वाहिक + .{@-कम्@} A sluice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्वेधिक
नैर्वेधिक <i>a.</i> Piercing, penetrating. ˚प्रज्ञा <i>a.</i> Sagacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैविड्यम्
नैवि(बि)ड्यम्<BR>—1 Compactness, closeness, thickness, denseness.<BR>—2 Substance.<BR>—3 A continuous sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैबिड्यम्
नैवि(बि)ड्यम्<BR>—1 Compactness, closeness, thickness, denseness.<BR>—2 Substance.<BR>—3 A continuous sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेद्यम्
नैवेद्यम् An offering of eatables presented to a deity or idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेशिकम्
नैवेशिकम्<BR>—1 Any vessel or implement forming part of domestic furniture; नैवेशिकं<BR> सर्वगुणोपपन्नं ददाति वै यस्तु नरो द्विजाय Mb. 13. 57. 33.<BR>—2 A present to a Brāhmaṇa householder, <i>e. g.</i> a girl or ornaments<BR> given with her.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश|नैशं
नैश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), नैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nocturnal, belonging to the night, nightly; तन्नैशं तिमिरमपाकरोति<BR> चन्द्रः Ś. 6. 30; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 8;<BR> Ki. 5. 2; जगति नैशमशीतकरः करैर्वियति वारिदवृन्दमयं तमः Śi. 6. 43.<BR>—2 To be observed at night. ˚आत्मक <i>a.</i> darkish; नैशात्मकं तमो<BR> विद्यात् त्रिगुणं मोहसंज्ञितम् Mb. 14. 36. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशी
नैश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), नैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nocturnal, belonging to the night, nightly; तन्नैशं तिमिरमपाकरोति<BR> चन्द्रः Ś. 6. 30; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 8;<BR> Ki. 5. 2; जगति नैशमशीतकरः करैर्वियति वारिदवृन्दमयं तमः Śi. 6. 43.<BR>—2 To be observed at night. ˚आत्मक <i>a.</i> darkish; नैशात्मकं तमो<BR> विद्यात् त्रिगुणं मोहसंज्ञितम् Mb. 14. 36. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशिक|नैशिकं
नैश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), नैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nocturnal, belonging to the night, nightly; तन्नैशं तिमिरमपाकरोति<BR> चन्द्रः Ś. 6. 30; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 8;<BR> Ki. 5. 2; जगति नैशमशीतकरः करैर्वियति वारिदवृन्दमयं तमः Śi. 6. 43.<BR>—2 To be observed at night. ˚आत्मक <i>a.</i> darkish; नैशात्मकं तमो<BR> विद्यात् त्रिगुणं मोहसंज्ञितम् Mb. 14. 36. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशिकी
नैश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), नैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nocturnal, belonging to the night, nightly; तन्नैशं तिमिरमपाकरोति<BR> चन्द्रः Ś. 6. 30; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 8;<BR> Ki. 5. 2; जगति नैशमशीतकरः करैर्वियति वारिदवृन्दमयं तमः Śi. 6. 43.<BR>—2 To be observed at night. ˚आत्मक <i>a.</i> darkish; नैशात्मकं तमो<BR> विद्यात् त्रिगुणं मोहसंज्ञितम् Mb. 14. 36. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चल्यम्
नैश्चल्यम् Fixedness, immovableness, fixity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चित्यम्
नैश्चित्यम्<BR>—1 Determination, certainty.<BR>—2 A fixed ceremony or festival (such as a birth, marriage &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चिन्त्यम्
नैश्चिन्त्यम् Absence of care or anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध|नैषधः
नैषध<BR>—1 A king of the Niṣadhas.<BR>—2 Especially, an epithet of king Nala, q. v.; स नैषधस्यार्थपतेः सुतायाम् R.<BR>—3 A native or inhabitant of Niṣadha.<BR>—4 N. of a Mahākāvya by Śrīharṣa (treating of the adventures of Nala,<BR> king of the Niṣadhas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषधीय
नैषधीय <i>a.</i> Relating to Nala; काव्ये चारुणि नैषधीयचरिते सर्गोयमादिर्गतः N. 1. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्म्यम्
नैष्कर्म्यम्<BR>—1 Idleness, inactivity.<BR>—2 Exemption from acts or their consequences; न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं<BR> पुरुषोऽश्नुते Bg. 3. 4, 18. 49.<BR>—3 The salvation obtained by abstraction (as opposed to the salvation<BR> obtained by कर्ममार्ग q. v.).<BR>—4 Self-knowledge (आत्मज्ञान); नैष्कर्म्यभावेन विवर्जितागमस्वयंप्रकाशाय<BR> नमस्करोमि Bhāg. 8. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्तृक
नैष्कर्तृक <i>a.</i> Employed on wages for cutting wood; यथा वै दारुहारो<BR> नैष्कर्तृको निष्कर्तनभृतो कर्मयोगे वर्तते एवं वा एते यज्ञस्य ऋत्विज<BR> इति ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कशतिक
नैष्कशतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Worth a hundred <i>Niṣkas</i>; (so also नैष्कसहस्रिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्काम्यम्
नैष्काम्यम्<BR>—1 Suppression of desire.<BR>—2 Profound contemplation; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किक|नैष्किकः
नैष्किक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Bought with or made of a Niṣka q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किकः|नैष्किक
नैष्किक + .{@-कः@} A mint-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किंचन्यम्
नैष्किंचन्यम् Indigence, absolute poverty or want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्क्रमणम्
नैष्क्रमणम् Any oblation or rite performed when a new-born child<BR> is taken out of the house for the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्क्रम्यम्
नैष्क्रम्यम् Indifference (to worldly pleasures); Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Final, last, concluding; विदधे विधिमस्य नैष्ठिकम् R. 8. 25.<BR>—2 Decided, definitive, conclusive (as a reply.); एषा नो नैष्ठिकी बुद्धिः Mb. 1. 37. 29.<BR>—3 Fixed, firm, constant; शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् Bg. 5. 12; भक्तिर्भवति<BR> नैष्ठिकी Bhāg. 1. 2. 18.<BR>—4 Highest, perfect; मोदेन वां कामसुखैर्मदाद् वा यो नैष्ठिकं श्रोष्यति<BR> नास्य धर्मम् Bu. C. 1. 82.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">Page0942-1</a>]<BR>—5 Completely familiar with or versed in.<BR>—6 Vowing perpetual abstinence and chastity.<BR>—7 Obligatory; न चैतन्नैष्ठिकं कर्म त्रयाणां भूरिदक्षिण Mb. 12. 63. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिकः|नैष्ठिक
नैष्ठिक + .{@-कः@} [निष्ठा मरणं तत्पर्यन्तं ब्रह्मचर्येण तिष्ठति निष्ठा-ठक्]<BR> A perpetual religious student who continues with his spiritual precept<BR> or even after the prescribed period, and vows life-long abstinence and<BR> chastity; निवेदितो नैष्ठिकसुन्दरस्तया Ku. 5. 62; cf. नैष्ठिको ब्रह्मचारी<BR> तु वसेदाचार्यसंनिधौ Y. 1. 49 and उपकुर्वाण also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0941-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठ्यम्
नैष्ठ्यम् Constancy, steady adherence to rule, firm belief, steadfastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठुर्यम्
नैष्ठुर्यम् Cruelty, harshnesss, severity; जनकृपानैष्ठुर्यमुत्सृज्यताम्<BR> Sādhanapañcaka Stotra 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्गिक|नैसर्गिकः
नैसर्गिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Natural, inborn, innate, inherent; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः<BR> कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि स्थितिर्न मुसलैरवताडनानि Māl. 9. 49; R. 5. 37, 6. 46.<BR> अहं ममेदमिति नैसर्गिकोऽयं लोकव्यवहारः Śāṅkarabhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्त्रिंशिकः|नैस्त्रिंशिक
नैस्त्रिंशिकः A swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैहार
नैहार^1 <i>a.</i> Produced by mist or fog; तम्यां तमोवन्नैहारम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 13. 45.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नो
नो <i>ind.</i> (न + उ) No, not; often used like न q. v.; न<BR> च तत् प्रेत्य नो इह Bg. 17. 28; Pt. 5. 24; Amaru. 6, 8, 10, 62; गोप्याधिभागे<BR> नो वृद्धिः सोपकारेऽथ हापिते Y. 2. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोचेत्
नोचेत् If noxt, otherwise; नो चेत्त्वामिह को जानीते काककदम्बकळिहिते द्यूते Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदनम्
नोदनम् [नुद्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Impelling, driving, urging onward.<BR>—2 Removing, driving away, dispelling. —3 Cutting, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदयितृ
नोदयितृ <i>a.</i> One who urges forward or propels; समीरणो नोदयिता<BR> भवेति व्यादिश्यते केन हुताशनस्य Ku. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधा
नोधा <i>ind.</i> Ninefold, in nine parts; नोधा विधाय रूपं स्वं सर्वसंकल्पविद्विभुः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 23. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A ship, boat, vessel; महता पुण्यपण्येन क्रीतेयं कायनौस्त्वया<BR> Śānti. 3. 1.<BR>—2 N. of a constellation.<BR>—3 Time; नौः काले तरणावपि Nm.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नावारोहः, नौकर्णधारः, नौकर्मन्, नौक्रमः, नौचरः, नावुपजीवकः, नौजीविकः, नौतार्य, नौदण्डः, नौयानम्, नौयायिन्, नौवाहः, नौव्यसनम्, नौसाधनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावारोहः|नावारोह
नौ + -आरोहः (नावारोहः)<BR>—1 a passenger on board a ship.<BR>—2 a sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौकर्णधारः|नौकर्णधार
नौ + -कर्णधारः a helmsman, pilot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौकर्मन्|नौकर्म्मन्
नौ + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> the occupation of a sailor; निषादो मार्गवं सूते<BR> दासं नौकर्मजीविनम् Ms. 10. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौक्रमः|नौक्रम
नौ + -क्रमः a bridge of boats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौचरः|नौचर
नौ + -चरः, -उपजीवकः, -जीविकः a sailor, boatman; यादोनाथः शिवजलपथः<BR> कर्मणे नौचराणाम् R. 17. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावुपजीवकः
नौ + -चरः, -उपजीवकः, -जीविकः a sailor, boatman; यादोनाथः शिवजलपथः<BR> कर्मणे नौचराणाम् R. 17. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौजीविकः|नौजीविक
नौ + -चरः, -उपजीवकः, -जीविकः a sailor, boatman; यादोनाथः शिवजलपथः<BR> कर्मणे नौचराणाम् R. 17. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौतार्य|नौतार्य्य|नौतार्य्यं
नौ + -तार्य <i>a.</i> navigable, to be traversed in a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौदण्डः|नौदण्ड|नौदंड
नौ + -दण्डः an oar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौयानम्
नौ + -यानम् navigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौयायिन्
नौ + -यायिन् <i>a.</i> going in a boat, a passenger; एष नौयायिनामुक्तो<BR> व्यवहारस्य निर्णयः Ms. 8. 409.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौवाहः|नौवाह
नौ + -वाहः a steersman, pilot, captain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौव्यसनम्
नौ + -व्यसनम् shipwreck, naufrage; नौव्यसने विपन्नः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौसाधनम्
नौ + -साधनम् fleet, navy; वङ्गानुत्खाय तरसा नेता नौसाधनोद्यतान् R. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौका
नौका A small boat, a boat in general; क्षणमिह सज्जनसंगतिरेका<BR> भवति भवार्णवतरणे नौका Moha M. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: नौकादण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौकादण्डः|नौकादण्ड|नौकादंड
नौका + -दण्डः an oar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्
न्यक् <i>ind.</i> An adverb, prefixed to कृ or भू, to imply ‘contempt’,<BR> ‘degradation’ or ‘humiliation’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यकाक्नका
न्यकाक्नका <i>f.</i> A worm of ordure; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कृ
न्यक्कृ €8 U. To insult, contemn, slight, degrade, humiliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्करणम्
न्यक्करणम्, न्यक्कारः Humiliation, degradation, disrespect,<BR> contempt, insult; न्यक्कारो हृदि वज्रकील इव मे तीव्रं परिस्पन्दते<BR> Mv. 5. 22, 3. 40; अयं हि न्यक्कारो जननि मनुजस्य श्रवणयो G. L. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कारः|न्यक्कार
न्यक्करणम्, न्यक्कारः Humiliation, degradation, disrespect,<BR> contempt, insult; न्यक्कारो हृदि वज्रकील इव मे तीव्रं परिस्पन्दते<BR> Mv. 5. 22, 3. 40; अयं हि न्यक्कारो जननि मनुजस्य श्रवणयो G. L. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भू
न्यग्भू €1 P. To become low or humble. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To despise, contemn.<BR>—2 To humiliate, subdue, overcome; न्यग्भावयिता शत्रून् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावः|न्यग्भाव
न्यग्भावः<BR>—1 Humiliation, degradation.<BR>—2 Making inferior, subordination.<BR>—3 Being brought or come down; न्यग्भावं परमं वायोः शाल्मले त्वमुपागतः<BR> Mb. 12. 155. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावित
न्यग्भावित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Humiliated, degraded, slighted.<BR>—2 Surpassed, excelled, made inferior or secondary (अप्रधानीकृत);<BR> न्यग्भावितवाच्यव्यङ्गपव्यञ्जनक्षमस्य शब्दार्थयुगलस्य K. P. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्ष|न्यक्षं|न्यक्षः
न्यक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Low, inferior, vile, mean.<BR>—2 Whole, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्षः|न्यक्ष|न्यक्षं
न्यक्ष + .{@-क्षः@}<BR>—1 A buffalo.<BR>—2 An epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्षम्
न्यक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@}<BR>—1 The whole.<BR>—2 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधः|न्यग्रोध
न्यग्रोधः<BR>—1 The (Indian) fig tree; जटाः कृत्वा गमिष्यामि न्यग्रोधक्षीरमानय<BR> Rām. 2. 52. 68.<BR>—2 A fathom (measured by the arms extended).<BR>—3 The Śamī tree.<BR>—4 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधी
न्यग्रोधः + .{@-धी@} + ({@-धिका@})<BR> N. of a plant (Mar. उंदीरकानी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डलः, न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधिका
न्यग्रोधः + .{@-धी@} + ({@-धिका@})<BR> N. of a plant (Mar. उंदीरकानी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डलः, न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डलः|न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डल
न्यग्रोधः + -परिमण्डलः a man being a fathom in circumference; (thus described:− महाधनुर्धराश्चैव<BR> त्रेतायां चक्रवर्तिनः । सर्वलक्षणसंपन्ना न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डलाः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला|न्यग्रोधपरिमंडला
न्यग्रोधः + -परिमण्डला an excellent woman; (she is thus described:− स्तनौ<BR> सुकठिनौ यस्या नितम्बे च विशालता । मध्ये क्षीणा भवेद्या सा न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला)<BR> (Śabdak.); दूर्वाकाण्डमिव श्यामा न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला Bk. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कुः|न्यङ्कु|न्यंकु|न्यंकुः
न्यङ्कुः<BR>—1 A kind of antelope; सद्यो हतन्यङ्कुभिरस्रदिग्धं व्याघ्रैः पदं तेषु<BR> निधीयतेऽद्य R. 16. 15.<BR>—2 N. of the sage ऋष्यशृङ्ग.<BR>—3 A student staying with his Guru. Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यच्छम्
न्यच्छम् A mole upon the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
न्यञ्च् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go down, bend down; Māl. 5. 22.<BR>—2 To incline.<BR>—3 To diminish, pass away; न्यञ्चति वयसि प्रथमे Bv. 2. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
न्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> (-नीची <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Going or turned downwards, turned or bent down.<BR>—2 Lying on the face.<BR>—3 Low, contemptible, base, mean, vile; Śi. 15. 21 (where it also means<BR> निम्न or downward). न्यञ्चस्तं प्राप्य मद्विधाः Bk. 5. 36.<BR>—4 Slow, lazy.<BR>—5 Whole, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चनम्
न्यञ्चनम्<BR>—1 A curve.<BR>—2 A hiding place.<BR>—3 A hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चनी
न्यञ्चनम् + .{@-नी@} The lap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0942-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चित|न्यंचित|न्यञ्चितं
न्यञ्चित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or cast down.<BR>—2 Bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्ज्|न्यंज्
न्यञ्ज् €7 P.<BR>—1 To anoint, besmear.<BR>—2 To conceal oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्त
न्यक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Anointed, smeared.<BR>—2 Mixed up, blended together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्गः|न्यङ्ग|न्यंगः
न्यङ्गः<BR>—1 A mark, sign.<BR>—2 A kind, sort.<BR>—3 Disgrace ? एतत्तन्न्यङ्गमस्माकमेष सोऽतिमनोरथः Pratijñā. 1. 10.<BR> इक्ष्वाकुकुलन्यङ्गभूतो भरतः Pratimā 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यन्तः|न्यन्त
न्यन्तः<BR>—1 Proximity.<BR>—2 Western side; न्यन्तेनापरतालस्य Rām. 2. 68. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्ययः|न्यय
न्ययः Loss, destruction; decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्बुदम्
न्यर्बुदम् Ved. One hundred millions (दशगुणम् अर्बुदम्); विमानैर्न्यर्बुदैर्युताम्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यवग्रहः|न्यवग्रह
न्यवग्रहः The accentless vowel at the end of the first member of a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यवेक्ष्
न्यवेक्ष् €1 Ā. To consider; deliberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्
न्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To set or put down, place, throw down; शिखरिषु पदं न्यस्य Me. 13;<BR> दृष्टिपूतं न्यसेत् पादम् Ms. 6. 46.<BR>—2 To lay or throw aside, abandon, give up, resign, relinquish; स न्यस्तचिह्नामपि<BR> राजलक्ष्मीम् R. 2. 7; न्यस्तशस्त्रस्य Ve. 3. 18; so प्राणान् न्यस्यति &c.<BR>—3 To put in, place within, place or put down upon anything (with loc.);<BR> शिरस्याज्ञा न्यस्ता Amaru. 82; चित्रन्यस्त ‘committed to picture’,<BR> V. 1. 4; स्तनन्यस्तोशीरं Ś. 3. 8 ‘applied’; अयोग्ये न मद्विधो<BR> न्यस्यति भारमग्र्यम् Bk. 1. 22; Me. 61.<BR>—4 To entrust, consign, commit to the care of, deliver; अहमपि तव<BR> सूनौ न्यस्तराज्यः V. 5. 17; भ्रातरि न्यस्य माम् Bk. 5. 82.<BR>—5 To give to, confer or bestow upon; रामे श्रीर्न्यस्यतामिति R. 12. 2.<BR>—6 To state, bring forward, adduce, propound (as an argument); अर्थान्तरं<BR> न्यस्यति Malli. on Śi. 1. 17.<BR>—7 To settle, fix, appoint.<BR>—8 To support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यसनम्
न्यसनम्<BR>—1 Depositing, lying down.<BR>—2 Delivering, giving up.<BR>—3 Bringing forward, mentioning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्त|न्यस्तं
न्यस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cast down, thrown or laid down, deposited.<BR>—2 Put in, inserted, applied; न्यस्ताक्षराः Ku. 1. 7.<BR>—3 Depicted, drawn; चित्रन्यस्त.<BR>—4 Consigned, delivered or transferred to; अहमपि तव सूनावायुषि न्यस्तराज्यः V. 5. 17.<BR>—5 Leaning, resting on.<BR>—6 Given up, set aside, resigned.<BR>—7 Mystically touched; नित्यं न्यस्तषडङ्गचक्रनिहितं हृत्पद्ममध्योदितम् Māl. 5. 2.<BR>—8 Exposed (for sale; क्रयाय न्यस्त).<BR>—9 Put on, donned; न्यस्तालक्तकरक्तमाल्यवसना Māl. 5. 24.<BR>—10 Having the low tone (as a vowel).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यस्तास्तव्य, न्यस्तचिह्न, न्यस्तदण्ड, न्यस्तदेह, न्यस्तशस्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तास्तव्य
न्यस्त + -अस्तव्य <i>a.</i> To be placed, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तचिह्न
न्यस्त + -चिह्न <i>a.</i> destitute of external signs (as royal marks &c.);<BR> स न्यस्तचिह्नामपि राजलक्ष्मीं तेजोविशेषानुमितां दधानः R. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तदण्ड
न्यस्त + -दण्ड <i>a.</i> giving up the rod, <i>i. e.</i> punishment, meek, harmless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तदेह
न्यस्त + -देह <i>a.</i> one who lays down the body, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तशस्त्र|न्यस्तशस्त्रः
न्यस्त + -शस्त्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has resigned or laid down his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">Page0943-2</a>]<BR> arms; आचार्यस्य त्रिभुवनगुरोर्न्यस्तशस्त्रस्य शोकात् Ve. 3. 18; Ms. 3. 192.<BR>—2 unarmed, defenceless.<BR>—3 harmless.<BR>—4 epithet of the manes, or deified progenitors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासः|न्यास
न्यासः<BR>—1 Placing, putting down or upon, planting, तस्या खुरन्यासपवित्रपांसुम्<BR> R. 2. 2; Ku. 6. 50; M. 2. 9; Māl. 5. 5; चरणन्यास, अङ्गन्यास &c.;<BR> सैन्दूरं क्रियते जनेन चरणन्यासैः पुनः कुट्टिमम् Ratn. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Hence, any impression, mark, stamp, print; अतिशस्त्रनखन्यासः<BR> R. 12. 73; ‘where the nail-marks surpassed those of weapons’; दन्तन्यासः.<BR>—3 Depositing.<BR>—4 A pledge, deposit; प्रत्यर्पितन्यास इवान्तरात्मा Ś. 4. 22; R. 12. 18;<BR> Y. 2. 67.<BR>—5 Entrusting, committing, giving over, delivering, consigning.<BR>—6 Painting, writing down.<BR>—7 Giving up, resigning, abandoning, relinquishing; शस्त्र˚; न्यासो दण्डस्य<BR> भूतेषु Bhāg. 7. 15. 8; काम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो<BR> विदुः Bg. 18. 2.<BR>—8 Bringing forward, adducing.<BR>—9 Digging in, seizing (as with claws).<BR>—10 Assignment of the various parts of the body to different deities,<BR> which is usually accompanied with prayers and corresponding gesticulations.<BR>—11 Lowering the tone or voice.<BR>—12 संन्यास q. v.; एवं वसन् गृहे कालं विरक्तो न्यासमास्थितः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 6. 53.<BR>—13 Written or literal text (यथान्यासम्).<BR>—14 Bringing forward, introducing (cf. अर्थान्तरन्यास).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यासापह्नवः, न्यासधारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासापह्नवः|न्यासापह्नव
न्यासः + -अपह्नवः repudiation of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासधारिन्
न्यासः + -धारिन् <i>m.</i> the holder of a deposit, a mortgagee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासिन्
न्यासिन् <i>m.</i> One who has renounced all worldly ties, a Saṃnyāsin;<BR> गृहस्थो येन पदवीमञ्जसा न्यासिनामियात् Bhāg. 7. 15. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासीकृ
न्यासीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To place as deposit; न्यासीकृता स्थानविदा स्मरेण Ku. 3. 55.<BR>—2 To entrust to, give in charge of; न राक्षसोऽनात्मसदृशेषु कलत्रं<BR> न्यासीकरिष्यति Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याक्यम्
न्याक्यम् Fried rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यादः|न्याद
न्यादः Eating, feeding; P. III. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायः|न्याय
न्यायः [नियन्ति अनेन; नि-इ घञ्]<BR>—1 Method, manner, way, rule, system, plan; अधार्मिकं त्रिभिर्न्यायैर्निगृह्णीयात्<BR> प्रयत्नतः Ms. 8. 310; अनुक्ते हि न्याये न प्रतीमोऽर्थान्तरम् ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 5;<BR> तस्मान्नावस्थितो न्यायः प्रत्युद्ध्रियेत ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 10.<BR> ननु लिङ्गमसाधकं, न्याय उच्यतां यस्यैतद् द्योतकमिति ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 30.<BR>—2 Fitness, propriety, decorum; न्यायाधारा हि साधवः Ki. 11. 30.<BR>—3 Law, justice, virtue, equity, righteousness, honesty; यान्ति न्यायप्रवृत्तस्य<BR> तिर्यञ्चोऽपि सहायताम् A. R. 1. 4.<BR>—4 A law-suit, legal proceeding.<BR>—5 Judicial sentence, judgment.<BR>—6 Policy, good government.<BR>—7 Likeness, analogy.<BR>—8 A popular maxim, an apposite illustration, illustration, as दण्डापूपन्याय,<BR> काकतालीयन्याय, घुणाक्षरन्याय &c.; see Appendix.<BR>—9 A Vedic accent; न्यायैस्त्रिभिरुदीर्णम् Ku. 2. 12. (Malli. takes न्याय<BR> to mean स्वर; but it is quite open, in our opinion, to take न्याय<BR> in the sense of ‘a system’ or ‘way’; ‘which are manifested in three systems, <i>i. e.</i> ऋक्, यजुस् and सामन्’<BR>); न्यायगर्भद्विजाः Bh. 3. 55.<BR>—10 (In gram.) A universal rule.<BR>—11 A system of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">Page0944-1</a>]<BR> Hindu philosophy founded by the sage Gautama.<BR>—12 The science of logic, logical philosophy.<BR>—13 A complete argument or syllogism (consisting of five members; <i>i. e.</i><BR> प्रतिज्ञा, हेतु, उदाहरण, उपनय and निगमन).<BR>—14 An epithet of Viṣṇu. (न्यायेन <i>ind.</i> in the way of, after<BR> the manner or analogy of; बधिरान्मन्दकर्णः श्रेयानिति न्यायेन &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यायागत, न्यायाचार, न्यायाधारः, न्यायाभासः, न्यायोपेत, न्यायनिर्वपण, न्यायणः, न्यायपथः, न्यायवर्तिन्, न्यायवादिन्, न्यायविद्या, न्यायशिक्षा, न्यायवृत्तम्, न्यायशास्त्रम्, न्यायसंबद्ध, न्यायसारिणी, न्यायसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0943-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायागत
न्यायः + -आगत <i>a.</i> rightly got, acquired (money).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाचार
न्यायः + -आचार <i>a.</i> virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाधारः|न्यायाधार
न्यायः + -आधारः an example of virtue or propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाभासः|न्यायाभास
न्यायः + -आभासः semblance of reason, sophism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायोपेत
न्यायः + -उपेत rightly admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायनिर्वपण
न्यायः + -निर्वपण <i>a.</i> bestowing justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायणः
न्यायः + -णः N. of Śiva; Mb. 13. 17. 126 (com. न्याययुक्तं निर्वपणं<BR> दानं यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायपथः|न्यायपथ
न्यायः + -पथः the Mīmāmsā philosophy; (pl.) the different philosophical<BR> systems; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायवर्तिन्
न्यायः + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> well behaved, acting justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायवादिन्
न्यायः + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> one who speaks what is right or just.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायविद्या
न्यायः + -विद्या, -शिक्षा see न्यायशास्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायशिक्षा
न्यायः + -विद्या, -शिक्षा see न्यायशास्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायवृत्तम्
न्यायः + -वृत्तम् good conduct, virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायशास्त्रम्
न्यायः + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 the philosophical system of the Nyāya school.<BR>—2 the science of logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायसंबद्ध|न्यायसम्बद्ध
न्यायः + -संबद्ध <i>a.</i> rational, logical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायसारिणी
न्यायः + -सारिणी proper or suitable behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायसूत्रम्
न्यायः + -सूत्रम् the aphorisms of Nyāya philosophy by Gautama. [<i>NOTE</i>:−<BR> A few of the common Nyāyas or popular maxims that were given under this<BR> word by Prin. Apte are taken in the Appendix along with many others.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायतः
न्यायतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In a fitting manner, suitably, fitly; क्रतुं समाप्य तु तदा न्यायतः<BR> पुरुषर्षभः Rām. 1. 14. 45.<BR>—2 Justly, rightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायिन्
न्यायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Right, fit, proper, just.<BR>—2 Logical, rational.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय्य|न्याय्यं
न्याय्य <i>a.</i> [न्यायादनपेतः यत्]<BR>—1 Just, proper, right, equitable, suitable, fit; न्याय्यात्पथः प्रविचलन्ति<BR> पदं न धीराः Bh. 2. 83; शरीरवाङ्मनोभिर्यत् कर्म प्रारभते नरः ।<BR> न्याय्यं वा विपरीतं वा पञ्चैते तस्य हेतवः ॥ Bg. 18. 15; Ms. 2. 152^1, 9. 202;<BR> R. 2. 55; Ki. 14. 7; Ku. 6. 87; श्रुतिलक्षणाविषये च श्रुतिर्न्याय्या<BR> न लक्षणा ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 51, 6. 2. 20.<BR>—2 Usual, customary.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्यास, न्यासिन् &c. See under न्यस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासिन्
न्यास, न्यासिन् &c. See under न्यस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युङ्ख|न्युंख|न्युङ्खः
न्यु(न्यू)ङ्ख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Charming, beautiful, lovely.<BR>—2 Proper, right.<BR>—3 A particular sound of ॐ in the recitation of Sāmans; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूङ्ख|न्यूंख
न्यु(न्यू)ङ्ख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Charming, beautiful, lovely.<BR>—2 Proper, right.<BR>—3 A particular sound of ॐ in the recitation of Sāmans; Nm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युच्
न्युच् €4 P.<BR>—1 To assent or agree to.<BR>—2 To rejoice, delight in, be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योचनी
न्योचनी<BR>—1 A female servant (according to Sāyaṇa).<BR>—2 A kind of womanʼs ornament; MW.; रैभ्यासीदनुदेयी नाराशंसी न्योचनी Rv. 10. 85. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज्
न्युब्ज् €6 P. To bend or press down, throw down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं|न्युब्जः
न्युब्ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Turned or bent downwards, lying on the face; ऊर्ध्वार्पितन्युब्जकटाहकल्पे<BR> (व्योम्नि) N. 22. 32; न्युब्जीकृतेषुधिस्तत्र शरसन्धानतत्परः Śiva B. 28. 83.<BR>—2 Bent, crooked.<BR>—3 Convex.<BR>—4 Hump-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्जः|न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं
न्युब्ज + .{@-ब्जः@}<BR>—1 The Nyagrodha tree.<BR>—2 A kind of ladle made of Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्जम्
न्युब्ज + .{@-ब्जम्@} A vessel used in Śrāddhas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्युब्जखड्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्जखड्गः|न्युब्जखड्ग
न्युब्ज + -खड्गः a crooked sword, sabre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यून|न्यूनं
न्यून <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lessened, diminished, shortened.<BR>—2 Defective, inferior, deficient, wanting, destitute of; as in अर्थन्यून;<BR> अथ कस्मादेतानि वैकृतानि वाक्यानि न्यूनान्येव नानुमन्यन्ते । किमेभिः पूरितैः ।<BR> न्यूनानि अनेकार्थानि भवन्ति ŚB. on MS. 7. 4. 12.<BR>—3 Less (opp. अधिक); न्यूनाधिकविभक्तानां धर्म्यः पितृकृतः स्मृतः Y. 2. 116.<BR>—4 Defective (in some organ); पाद˚.<BR>—5 Low, wicked, vile, despicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनम्
न्यून + .{@-नम्@} Want or omission of one of the five members in a Nyāya argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनम्
न्यून + .{@-नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Less, in a less degree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: न्यूनाङ्ग, न्यूनाधिक, न्यूनधी, न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भावः, न्यूनभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाङ्ग|न्यूनांग
न्यून + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> maimed, mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाधिक
न्यून + -अधिक <i>a.</i> more or less, unequal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनधी
न्यून + -धी <i>a.</i> deficient in intellect, ignorant, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भावः|न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भाव
न्यून + -पञ्चाशद्भावः an idiot (having no full 50 properties of human nature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनभावः|न्यूनभाव
न्यून + -भावः inferiority, deficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनता
न्यूनता<BR>—1 Inferiority (to).<BR>—2 Want, deficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनयति
न्यूनयति Den. P., न्यूनीकृ €8 U. To lessen, diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनीकृ
न्यूनयति Den. P., न्यूनीकृ €8 U. To lessen, diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्येज्
न्येज् (नि + एज्)<BR>—1 To tremble; निशितासिरतोऽभीको न्येजते ऽमरणा रुचा Ki. 15. 22.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्येर्
न्येर् (नि + आ + ईर्)<BR>—1 Direct or address (a wish or desire) to.<BR>—2 To appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योकस्
न्योकस् <i>a.</i> Ved. Having an eternal abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योजस्
न्योजस् <i>a.</i> Crooked (fig. also), wicked, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Drinking; as in द्विप, अनेकप.<BR>—2 Guarding, protecting, ruling; as in गोप. नृप, क्षितिप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पः|प|पं
प + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Air, wind.<BR>—2 A leaf.<BR>—3 An egg,<BR>—4 The act of drinking; also पा.<BR>—5 (in music) The fifth note of the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंश्
पंश्, -स् €1. €10. P.<BR> To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंस्
पंश्, -स् €1. €10. P.<BR> To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कणः|पक्कण
पक्कणः<BR>—1 The hut of a Cāṇḍāla or barbarian; (विश्वामित्रस्य संवादं चाण्डालस्य<BR> च पक्कणे) Mb. 12. 141. 12.<BR>—2 A village of the barbarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति, पक्तृ, पक्व &c. See under पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तृ
पक्ति, पक्तृ, पक्व &c. See under पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्व|पक्वं
पक्ति, पक्तृ, पक्व &c. See under पच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0944-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वशः|पक्वश
पक्वशः^1 N. of a barbarous tribe, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: Not sure.  pakvaSaH agrees with other dictionaries..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्
पक्ष् €1 P., €10 U. (पक्षति, पक्षयति-ते)<BR>—1 To take, seize.<BR>—2 To accept.<BR>—3 To side with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षः|पक्ष
पक्षः [पक्ष्-अच्]<BR>—1 A wing, pinion; अद्यापि पक्षावपि नोद्भिद्येते K. 347; so उद्भिन्नपक्षः<BR> fledged; पक्षच्छेदोद्यतं शक्रम् R. 4. 40, 3. 42.<BR>—2 The feather or feathers on each side of an arrow; अनुसंततिपातिनः<BR> पटुत्वं दधतः शुद्धिभृतो गृहीतपक्षाः (शराः) Śi. 20. 11.<BR>—3 The flank or side of a man or animal, the shoulder; स्तम्बेरमा उभयपक्षविनीतनिद्राः R. 5. 72.<BR>—4 The side of anything, a flank; वितत्य पक्षद्वयमायतम् Ki. 14. 31.<BR>—5 The wing or flank of an army; सुपर्णपक्षानिलनुन्नपक्षम् (राक्षसराजसैन्यम्)<BR> Rām. 7. 6. 69.<BR>—6 The half of anything.<BR>—7 The half of a lunar month, a fortnight (comprising 15 days; there are<BR> two such <i>pakṣas</i>, शुक्लपक्षः the bright or light half, and कृष्ण-तमिस्र-पक्षः<BR> the dark half); तमिस्रपक्षेऽपि सह प्रियाभिर्ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति<BR> प्रदोषान् R. 6. 34; Ms. 1. 66; Y. 3. 50; सीमा वृद्धिं समायाति शुक्लपक्ष<BR> इवोडुराट् Pt. 1. 92; Mb. 3. 260. 5.<BR>—8<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A party in general, faction, side; प्रमुदितवरपक्षम् R. 6. 86;<BR> Śi. 2. 117; तुल्यो मित्रारिपक्षयोः Bg. 14. 25; R. 6. 53, 18. 17.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A family, race; रूपान्वितां पक्षवतीं मनोज्ञां भार्यामयत्नोपगतां<BR> लभेत् सः Mb. 13. 57. 40; किं क्रन्दसि दुराक्रन्द स्वपक्षक्षयकारक Pt. 4. 29.<BR>—9 One belonging to any party, a follower, partisan; विष्णुपक्षैः प्रतिच्छन्नैर्न<BR> भिद्येतास्य धीर्यथा Bhāg. 7. 5. 7; शत्रुपक्षो भवान् H. 1.<BR>—10 A class, multitude, host, any number of adherents; as अरि˚, मित्र˚.<BR>—11 One side of an argument, an alternative, one of two cases; पक्षे<BR> ‘in the other case, on the other hand’, पूर्व एवाभवत् पक्षस्तस्मिन्नाभवदुत्तरः<BR> R. 4. 10, 14. 34; cf. पूर्वपक्ष and उत्तरपक्ष.<BR>—12 A case or supposition in general; as in पक्षान्तरे.<BR>—13 A point under discussion, a thesis, an argument to be maintained.<BR>—14 The subject of a syllogism or conclusion (the minor term); संदिग्धसाध्यवान्<BR> पक्षः T. S., दधतः शुद्धिभृतो गृहीतपक्षाः Śi. 20. 11<BR> (where it means ‘a feather’ also).<BR>—15 A symbolical expression for the number ‘two’.<BR>—16 A bird.<BR>—17 A state, condition.<BR>—18 The body.<BR>—19 A limb of the body.<BR>—20 A royal elephant.<BR>—21 An army; Mb. 2. 16. 7.<BR>—22 A wall.<BR>—23 Opposition.<BR>—24 Rejoinder, reply.<BR>—25 A mass, quantity (when in composition with words meaning ‘hair’);<BR> केशपक्षः; cf. हस्त.<BR>—26 Place, position.<BR>—27 A view, notion, idea.<BR>—28 The side of an equation in a primary division.<BR>—29 The ash-pit of a fire-place.<BR>—30 Proximity, neighbourhood.<BR>—31 A bracket.<BR>—32 Purity, perfection.<BR>—33 A house.<BR>—34 The sun (according to Sāyaṇa); सा पक्ष्या नव्यमायुर्दधाना Rv. 3. 53. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पक्षाध्यायः, पक्षान्तः, पक्षान्तरम्, पक्षावसरः, पक्षाघातः, पक्षाभासः, पक्षाहारः, पक्षोद्ग्राहिन्, पक्षगम, पक्षग्रहणम्, पक्षघातः, पक्षघ्न, पक्षचरः, पक्षच्छिद्, पक्षजः, पक्षद्वयम्, पक्षद्वारम्, पक्षधर, पक्षनाडी, पक्षनिक्षेपः, पक्षपातः, पक्षपातिता, पक्षत्वम्, पक्षपातिन्, पक्षपालिः, पक्षपुटः, पक्षपोषण, पक्षप्राप्तानुवादः, पक्षबिन्दुः, पक्षभागः, पक्षभुक्ति, पक्षभेदः, पक्षरात्रिः, पक्षवञ्चितकम्, पक्षवधः, पक्षमूलम्, पक्षरचना, पक्षवादः, पक्षवाहनः, पक्षव्यापिन्, पक्षहत, पक्षहरः, पक्षहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाध्यायः|पक्षाध्याय
पक्षः + -अध्यायः logic, casuistry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्तः|पक्षान्त|पक्षांत
पक्षः + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the 15th day of either half month, <i>i. e.</i> the day of new or full moon.<BR>—2 the end of the wings of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्तरम्
पक्षः + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 another side.<BR>—2 a different side or view of an argument.<BR>—3 another supposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षावसरः|पक्षावसर
पक्षः + -अवसरः = पक्षान्त q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाघातः|पक्षाघात
पक्षः + -आघातः<BR>—1 palsy or paralysis of one side, hemiplegia.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">Page0945-2</a>]<BR>—2 refutation of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाभासः|पक्षाभास
पक्षः + -आभासः<BR>—1 a fallacious argument.<BR>—2 a false plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाहारः|पक्षाहार
पक्षः + -आहारः eating food only once in a fortnight; सपुत्रदारो हि<BR> मुनिः पक्षाहारो बभूव ह Mb. 3. 26. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षोद्ग्राहिन्
पक्षः + -उद्ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> showing partiality, adopting a side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षगम
पक्षः + -गम <i>a.</i> flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षग्रहणम्
पक्षः + -ग्रहणम् choosing a party; taking the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षघातः|पक्षघात
पक्षः + -घातः = पक्षाघातः see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षघ्न
पक्षः + -घ्न <i>a.</i> (a house) wanting a side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षचरः|पक्षचर
पक्षः + -चरः<BR>—1 an elephant strayed from the herd.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षच्छिद्
पक्षः + -छिद् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Indra (clipper of the wings of mountains);<BR> क्रुद्धेऽपि पक्षच्छिदि वृत्रशत्रौ Ku. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षजः|पक्षज
पक्षः + -जः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वयम्
पक्षः + -द्वयम्<BR>—1 both sides of an argument.<BR>—2 ‘a couple of fortnights’, <i>i. e.</i> a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वारम्
पक्षः + -द्वारम् a side-door, private entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षधर|पक्षधरः
पक्षः + -धर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 winged.<BR>—2 adhering to the party of one, siding with any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षधरः|पक्षधर
पक्षः + -धर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a bird.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 a partisan.<BR>—4 an elephant strayed from the herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षनाडी
पक्षः + -नाडी a quill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षनिक्षेपः|पक्षनिक्षेप
पक्षः + -निक्षेपः the placing on the side of, counting among.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातः|पक्षपात
पक्षः + -पातः<BR>—1 siding with any one; यद् दुर्योधनपक्षपातसदृशं कर्म Ve. 3. 5.<BR>—2 liking, desire, love, affection (for a thing); भवन्ति भव्येषु हि<BR> पक्षपाताः Ki. 3. 12; U. 5. 17; रिपुपक्षे बद्धः पक्षपातः Mu. 1.<BR>—3 attachment to a party, partisanship, partiality; पक्षपातमत्र देवी<BR> मन्यते M. 1; सत्यं जना वच्मि न पक्षपातात् Bh. 1. 47.<BR>—4 falling of wings, the moulting of birds.<BR>—5 a partisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिता
पक्षः + -पातिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 partisanship, adherence to a side or party.<BR>—2 friendship, fellowship.<BR>—3 movement of the wings; न परं पथि पक्षपातिताऽनवलम्बे किमु मादृशेऽपि सा N. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षत्वम्
पक्षः + -पातिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 partisanship, adherence to a side or party.<BR>—2 friendship, fellowship.<BR>—3 movement of the wings; न परं पथि पक्षपातिताऽनवलम्बे किमु मादृशेऽपि सा N. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिन्
पक्षः + -पातिन् <i>a.</i> or <i>subst.</i><BR>—1 siding with, adhering to, a party, attached or partial (to a particular<BR> cause); पक्षपातिनो देवा अपि पाण्डवानाम् Ve. 3.<BR>—2 sympathizing; Ve. 3.<BR>—3 a follower, partisan, friend; यः सुरपक्षपाती V. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपालिः|पक्षपालि
पक्षः + -पालिः a private door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपुटः|पक्षपुट
पक्षः + -पुटः a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपोषण
पक्षः + -पोषण <i>a.</i> factious, promoting quarrels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षप्राप्तानुवादः
पक्षः + -प्राप्तानुवादः a case of the description of a thing which admits<BR> of two alternatives (cf. Daṇḍaviveka, G. O. S. 52, p. 21).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षबिन्दुः|पक्षबिन्दु|पक्षबिंदु
पक्षः + -बिन्दुः a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षभागः|पक्षभाग
पक्षः + -भागः<BR>—1 the side or flank.<BR>—2 especially, the flank of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षभुक्ति
पक्षः + -भुक्ति <i>f.</i> the course traversed by the sun in a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षभेदः|पक्षभेद
पक्षः + -भेदः a distinction between two sides of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षरात्रिः|पक्षरात्रि
पक्षः + -रात्रिः a kind of play or sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवञ्चितकम्
पक्षः + -वञ्चितकम् a particular position of hands in dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवधः|पक्षवध
पक्षः + -वधः paralysis of one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षमूलम्
पक्षः + -मूलम् the root of a wing; उल्लासपल्लवितकोमलपक्षमूलाः<BR> (चकोराः) Bv. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षरचना
पक्षः + -रचना forming a party or faction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवादः|पक्षवाद
पक्षः + -वादः<BR>—1 an exparte statement.<BR>—2 stating a case, expression of opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवाहनः|पक्षवाहन
पक्षः + -वाहनः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षव्यापिन्
पक्षः + -व्यापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 embracing the whole of an argument.<BR>—2 pervading the minor term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षहत
पक्षः + -हत <i>a.</i> paralysed on one side; दृष्ट्वा कुणीन् पक्षहतान्<BR> Mb. 12. 180. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षहरः|पक्षहर
पक्षः + -हरः<BR>—1 a bird.<BR>—2 a recreant, traitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षहोमः|पक्षहोम
पक्षः + -होमः<BR>—1 a sacrificial rite lasting for a fortnight.<BR>—2 a rite to be performed every fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षकः|पक्षक
पक्षकः<BR>—1 A side-door.<BR>—2 A side; गजपतिमधिरोहः पक्षकव्यत्ययेन Śi. 11. 7.<BR>—3 An associate, a partisan (at the end of comp.).<BR>—4 A fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0945-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षता
पक्षता<BR>—1 Alliance, partisanship.<BR>—2 Adherence to a party.<BR>—3 Taking up a side or argument.<BR>—4 Forming a part of.<BR>—5 Maintaining or defending a thesis.<BR>—6 The essential nature of a proposition.<BR>—7 Being the minor term or subject of a syllogism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षतिः|पक्षति
पक्षतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The root of a wing; अलिखच्चञ्चुपुटेन पक्षती N. 2. 2; खड्गच्छिन्नजटायुपक्षतिः<BR> U. 3. 43; Śi. 11. 26; पार्श्वद्वितयसंसक्तनिषङ्गद्वयपक्षतौ Śiva B. 29. 16.<BR>—2 The first day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवत्|पक्षवन्त्
पक्षवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Winged.<BR>—2 Belonging to a party.<BR>—3 Of good family, well-born; रूपान्वितां पक्षवतीं मनोज्ञां भार्यामयत्नोपगतां<BR> लभेत् सः Mb. 13. 57. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षस्
पक्षस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 A wing.<BR>—2 The side-part of a carriage.<BR>—3 The leaf of a door.<BR>—4 The wing of an army.<BR>—5 A half or division.<BR>—6 A half month.<BR>—7 The side or shore of a river.<BR>—8 A side in general.<BR>—9 Part, view, alternative; पूर्वस्मिन् पक्षसि त्र्यनीका विपरिवर्तते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षालुः|पक्षालु
पक्षालुः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिणी
पक्षिणी [पक्षतुल्यौ दिवसौ अस्याः इनि ङीप्]<BR>—1 A female bird.<BR>—2 A night with the two days enclosing it; (द्वावह्नावेकरात्रिश्च पक्षिणीत्यभिधीयते).<BR>—3 The day of full moon.<BR>—4 A childrenʼs malady (पूतना); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिन्
पक्षिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पक्ष अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 Winged; ये पक्षिणः प्रथममम्बुनिधिं गतास्ते Śi. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Furnished with wings.<BR>—3 Siding with, adhering to the party of. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A bird.<BR>—2 An arrow. —3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पक्षीन्द्रः, पक्षिप्रवरः, पक्षिराज्, पक्षिकीटः, पक्षितीर्थम्, पक्षिपतिः, पक्षिपानीयशालिका, पक्षिपुङ्गवः, पक्षिबालकः, पक्षिशावकः, पक्षिमार्गः, पक्षिशार्दूलः, पक्षिशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षीन्द्रः|पक्षीन्द्र|पक्षींद्र
पक्षिन् + -इन्द्रः, -प्रवरः, -राज् <i>m.</i>, {@-राजः, -सिंहः, -स्वामिन्@} <i>m.</i><BR> epithets of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0946-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

