पञ्चष, पञ्चषष्ट, पञ्चषष्टिः, पञ्चसटः, पञ्चसप्तत, पञ्चसप्ततिः, पञ्चसस्यम्, पञ्चसिद्धान्ती, पञ्चसिद्धौषधयः, पञ्चसुगन्धकम्, पञ्चसूनाः, पञ्चसूरणाः, पञ्चस्रोतम्, पञ्चहायन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चांशः|पञ्चांश|पंचांश
पञ्चन् + -अंशः the fifth part, a fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाग्निः|पञ्चाग्नि|पंचाग्नि
पञ्चन् + -अग्निः<BR>—1 an aggregate of five sacred fires; <i>i. e.</i> (अन्वाहार्यपचन or<BR> दक्षिण, गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय, सभ्य, and आवसथ्य).<BR>—2 a householder who maintains the five sacred fires; पञ्चाग्नयो धृतव्रताः<BR> Māl. 1; Ms. 3. 185.<BR>—3 five mystic fires supposed to exist in the body; तेजो ह्यग्निस्तथा<BR> क्रोधश्चक्षुरूष्मा तथैव च । अग्निर्जरयते यच्च पञ्चाग्नेयाः शरीरिणः ॥<BR> Mb. 12. 184. 21.<BR>—4 one who is acquainted with the doctrine of these fires. ˚साधनम्<BR> four fires on four sides and the sun above the head. This is a form of penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्ग|पंचांग|पञ्चाङ्गं|पञ्चाङ्गः
पञ्चन् + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> five-membered, having five parts or divisions as<BR> in पञ्चाङ्गः प्रणामः (<i>i. e.</i> बाहुभ्यां चैव जानुभ्यां शिरसा वक्षसा<BR> दृशा); कृतपत्र्चाङ्गविनिर्णयो नयः Ki. 2. 12 (see Malli. and Kām.<BR> quoted by him); पञ्चाङ्गमभिनयमुपदिश्य M. 1; चित्ताक्षिभ्रूहस्तपादैरङ्गैश्चेष्टादिसाम्यतः ।<BR> पात्राद्यवस्थाकरणं पञ्चाङ्गोऽभिनयो मतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गः|पञ्चाङ्ग|पंचांग|पञ्चाङ्गं
पञ्चन् + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गः@})<BR>—1 a tortoise or turtle.<BR>—2 a kind of horse with five spots in different parts of his body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गी|पंचांगी
पञ्चन् + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गी@}) a bit for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गम्
पञ्चन् + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गम्@})<BR>—1 collection or aggregate of five parts.<BR>—2 five modes of devotion (silent prayer, oblations, libations, bathing<BR> idols and feeding Brāhmaṇas)<BR>—3 the five parts of a tree; त्वक्पत्रकुसुमं मूलफलमेकस्य शाखिनः ।<BR> एकत्र मिलितं चैतत् पञ्चाङ्गमिति संज्ञितम् ॥<BR>—4 a calendar or almanac, so called because it treats of five things:−<BR> (तिथिर्वारश्च नक्षत्रं योगः करणमेव च); चतुरङ्गबलो राजा<BR> जगतीं वशमानयेत् । अहं पञ्चाङ्गबलवानाकाशं वशमानये ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR> ˚गुप्तः a turtle. ˚पत्रम् a calendar. ˚विनिर्णयः the five<BR> rules are as follows; सहायाः साधनोपाया विभागो देशकालयोः । विनिपातप्रतीकारः<BR> सिद्धिः पञ्चाङ्गमिष्यते ॥ Kām.; cf. Ki. 2. 12. ˚शुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR> the propitiousness or favourable state of five important points; <i>i. e.</i><BR> तिथि, वार, नक्षत्र, योग, and करण (in astrology).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गिक
पञ्चन् + -अङ्गिक <i>a.</i> five-membered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुल|पंचांगुल|पञ्चाङ्गुलः
पञ्चन् + -अङ्गुल <i>a.</i> (-ला or -ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> measuring five fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुलः|पञ्चाङ्गुल|पंचांगुल
पञ्चन् + -अङ्गुल + .({@-लः@}) the castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाजम्
पञ्चन् + -अजम्, -आजम् the five products of the goat; cf. पञ्चगव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाजम्
पञ्चन् + -अजम्, -आजम् the five products of the goat; cf. पञ्चगव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चातिग
पञ्चन् + -अतिग <i>a.</i> liberated (मुक्त); सोऽपि पञ्चातिगोऽभवत्<BR> Mb. 12. 59. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाप्सरस्
पञ्चन् + -अप्सरस् <i>n.</i> N. of a lake, said to have been created by the<BR> sage Maṇḍakarṇi; cf. R. 13. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चामरा
पञ्चन् + -अमरा The five plants <i>i. e.</i> (Mar. भांग, दूर्वा, बेल, निर्गुडी<BR> and तुळस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चामृत|पंचामृत|पञ्चामृतं
पञ्चन् + -अमृत) <i>a.</i> consisting of 5 ingredients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चामृतम्
पञ्चन् + -अमृत + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 the aggregate of five drugs: dry ginger, a species of Moon-seed (Cocculus<BR> cordifolius, Mar. गुळवेल), Asparagus racemosus (Mar. शतावरी),<BR> Hypoxis brevifolia<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">Page0949-1</a>]<BR> (Mar. मुसळी), गोक्षुरक (Mar. गोखरूं).<BR>—2 the collection of five sweet things used in worshipping deities; (दुग्धं<BR> च शर्करा चैव घृतं दधि तथा मधु).<BR>—3 the five elements; Māl. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0948-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्लम्
पञ्चन् + -अम्लम् the aggregate of five acid plants (the jujube, pomegranate,<BR> sorrel, spondias and citron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चार्चिस्|पंचार्चिस्|पञ्चार्च्चिस्
पञ्चन् + -अर्चिस् <i>m.</i> the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावयव|पंचावयव
पञ्चन् + -अवयव <i>a.</i> five-membered (as a syllogism, the five members<BR> being, प्रतिज्ञा, हेतु, उदाहरण, उपनय and निगमन q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावस्थः|पञ्चावस्थ|पंचावस्थ
पञ्चन् + -अवस्थः a corpse (so called because it is resolved into the five<BR> elements) cf. पञ्चत्व below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाविकम्
पञ्चन् + -अविकम् the five products of the sheep; cf. पञ्चगव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशीतिः|पञ्चाशीति|पंचाशीति
पञ्चन् + -अशीतिः <i>f.</i> eighty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाहः|पञ्चाह|पंचाह
पञ्चन् + -अहः a period of five days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चातप|पंचातप
पञ्चन् + -आतप <i>a.</i> doing penance with five fires (<i>i. e.</i> with four<BR> fires and the sun); cf. R. 13. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चात्मक
पञ्चन् + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> consisting of five elements (as body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाननः|पञ्चानन|पंचानन
पञ्चन् + -आननः, -आस्यः, -मुखः, -वक्त्रः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a lion (so called because its mouth is generally wide open; पञ्चम्<BR> आननं यस्य), (often used at the end of names of learned men to express<BR> great learning or respect; न्याय˚, तर्क˚ &c. <i>e. g.</i> जगन्नाथतर्कपञ्चानन);<BR> see पञ्च <i>a.</i><BR>—3 the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाननी
पञ्चन् + -आननः, -आस्यः, -मुखः, -वक्त्रः + .({@-नी@}) an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चास्यः|पञ्चास्य|पंचास्य
पञ्चन् + -आननः, -आस्यः, -मुखः, -वक्त्रः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a lion (so called because its mouth is generally wide open; पञ्चम्<BR> आननं यस्य), (often used at the end of names of learned men to express<BR> great learning or respect; न्याय˚, तर्क˚ &c. <i>e. g.</i> जगन्नाथतर्कपञ्चानन);<BR> see पञ्च <i>a.</i><BR>—3 the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुखः|पञ्चमुख|पंचमुख
पञ्चन् + -आननः, -आस्यः, -मुखः, -वक्त्रः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a lion (so called because its mouth is generally wide open; पञ्चम्<BR> आननं यस्य), (often used at the end of names of learned men to express<BR> great learning or respect; न्याय˚, तर्क˚ &c. <i>e. g.</i> जगन्नाथतर्कपञ्चानन);<BR> see पञ्च <i>a.</i><BR>—3 the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवक्त्रः|पञ्चवक्त्र|पंचवक्त्र
पञ्चन् + -आननः, -आस्यः, -मुखः, -वक्त्रः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a lion (so called because its mouth is generally wide open; पञ्चम्<BR> आननं यस्य), (often used at the end of names of learned men to express<BR> great learning or respect; न्याय˚, तर्क˚ &c. <i>e. g.</i> जगन्नाथतर्कपञ्चानन);<BR> see पञ्च <i>a.</i><BR>—3 the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्नायाः
पञ्चन् + -आम्नायाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) five Śāstras supposed to have proceeded<BR> from the five mouths of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चायतनी
पञ्चन् + -आयतनी, -आयतनम् a group of five deities like गणपति, विष्णु,<BR> शंकर, देवी and सूर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चायतनम्
पञ्चन् + -आयतनी, -आयतनम् a group of five deities like गणपति, विष्णु,<BR> शंकर, देवी and सूर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेन्द्रियम्
पञ्चन् + -इन्द्रियम् an aggregate of the five organs (of sense or actions;<BR> see इन्द्रियम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेषुः|पञ्चेषु|पंचेषु
पञ्चन् + -इषुः, -बाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; (so called<BR> because he has five arrows: their names are:− अरविन्दमशोकं च चूतं<BR> च नवमल्लिका । नीलोत्पलं च पञ्चैते पञ्चबाणस्य सायकाः ॥ the five<BR> arrows are also thus named:− संमोहनोन्मादनौ च शोषणस्तापनस्तथा ।<BR> स्तम्भनश्चेति कामस्य पञ्चबाणाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबाणः|पञ्चबाण|पंचबाण
पञ्चन् + -इषुः, -बाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; (so called<BR> because he has five arrows: their names are:− अरविन्दमशोकं च चूतं<BR> च नवमल्लिका । नीलोत्पलं च पञ्चैते पञ्चबाणस्य सायकाः ॥ the five<BR> arrows are also thus named:− संमोहनोन्मादनौ च शोषणस्तापनस्तथा ।<BR> स्तम्भनश्चेति कामस्य पञ्चबाणाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशरः|पञ्चशर|पंचशर
पञ्चन् + -इषुः, -बाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; (so called<BR> because he has five arrows: their names are:− अरविन्दमशोकं च चूतं<BR> च नवमल्लिका । नीलोत्पलं च पञ्चैते पञ्चबाणस्य सायकाः ॥ the five<BR> arrows are also thus named:− संमोहनोन्मादनौ च शोषणस्तापनस्तथा ।<BR> स्तम्भनश्चेति कामस्य पञ्चबाणाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चोपचारः|पञ्चोपचार
पञ्चन् + -उपचारः the five articles of worship <i>i. e.</i> (गन्ध, पुष्प,<BR> धूप, दीप and नैवेद्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चोष्मन्|पंचोष्मन्
पञ्चन् + -उष्मन् <i>m.</i> (pl.) the five digestive fires supposed to be in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकपाल|पञ्चकपालः
पञ्चन् + -कपाल <i>a.</i> prepared or offered in five cups.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकर्ण
पञ्चन् + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> branded in the ear with the number ‘five’ (as cattle<BR> &c.); cf. P. VI. 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकर्मन्|पंचकर्मन्|पञ्चकर्म्मन्
पञ्चन् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> (in medicine) the five kinds of treatment; <i>i. e.</i><BR> 1 वमन ‘giving emetics’; 2 रेचन ‘purging’; 3 नस्य<BR> ‘giving strenutatories’; 4 अनुवासन ‘administering an enema which is oily’<BR>, and 5 निरूह ‘administering an enema which is not oily’.<BR> वमनं रेचनं नस्यं निरूहश्चानुवासनम् । पञ्चकर्मेदमन्यच्च ज्ञेयमुत्क्षेपणादिकम् ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकल्याणकः|पञ्चकल्याणक
पञ्चन् + -कल्याणकः a horse with white feet and a white mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकषाय|पञ्चकषायः
पञ्चन् + -कषाय a decoction from the fruits of five plants (जम्बु, शाल्मलि,<BR> वाट्याल, बकुल and बदर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृत्यम्
पञ्चन् + -कृत्यम् the five actions by which the Supreme Power manifests<BR> itself (सृष्टि, स्थिति, संहार, तिरोभाव and अनुग्रहकरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृत्वस्|पंचकृत्वस्
पञ्चन् + -कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> five times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृष्णः|पञ्चकृष्ण
पञ्चन् + -कृष्णः A kind of game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृष्ष्णाः
पञ्चन् + -कृष्णः + .({@-ष्णाः@}) The five deities of Mahānubhāva sect namely चक्रवर्ती<BR> कृष्ण, Datta of Mātāpura, Gundam Raul of ऋद्धिपुर, चांगदेव राऊळ<BR> of द्वारावती and चांगदेव राऊळ of प्रतिष्ठान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोणः|पञ्चकोण|पंचकोण
पञ्चन् + -कोणः a pentagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोलम्
पञ्चन् + -कोलम् the five spices taken collectively; पिप्पली पिप्पलीमूलं<BR> चव्यचित्रकनागरम् । पञ्चकोलं … … … (Mar. पिंपळी, पिंपळमूळ,<BR> चवक, चित्रक ब सुंठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोषाः
पञ्चन् + -कोषाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the five vestures or wrappers supposed to<BR> invest the soul; they are:− अन्नमयकोष or the earthly body<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">Page0949-2</a>]<BR> (स्थूलशरीर); प्राणमयकोष the vesture of the vital airs; मनोमयकोष<BR> the sensorial vesture; विज्ञानमयकोष the cognitional vesture (these<BR> three form the लिङ्गशरीर); and आनन्दमयकोष the last vesture,<BR> that of beatitude. कोषैरन्नमयाद्यैः पञ्चभिरात्मा न संवृतो भाति ।<BR> निजशक्तिसमुत्पन्नैः शैवालपटलैरिवाम्बु वापीस्थम् ॥ Vivekacūḍāmaṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोशी
पञ्चन् + -कोशी<BR>—1 a distance of five Krośas.<BR>—2 N. of the city, Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चखट्वम्
पञ्चन् + -खट्वम्, -खट्वी a collection of five beds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चखट्वी|पंचखट्वी
पञ्चन् + -खट्वम्, -खट्वी a collection of five beds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगत
पञ्चन् + -गत <i>a.</i> (in alg.) raised to the fifth power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगवम्
पञ्चन् + -गवम् a collection of five cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगव्यम्
पञ्चन् + -गव्यम् the five products of the cow taken collectively; <i>i. e.</i><BR> milk, curds, clarified butter or ghee, urine, and cowdung (क्षीरं<BR> दधि तथा चाज्यं मूत्रं गोमयमेव च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगु|पंचगु|पञ्चगुः
पञ्चन् + -गु <i>a.</i> bought with five cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुण|पंचगुण
पञ्चन् + -गुण <i>a.</i> five-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुणाः
पञ्चन् + -गुण + .({@-णाः@}) the five objects of sense (रूप, रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श<BR> and शब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुणी
पञ्चन् + -गुण + .({@-णी@}) the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुप्तः|पञ्चगुप्त|पंचगुप्त
पञ्चन् + -गुप्तः<BR>—1 a tortoise (as drawing in its 4 feet and head).<BR>—2 the materialistic system of philosophy, the doctrines of the Cārvākas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चघातः|पञ्चघात
पञ्चन् + -घातः (in music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचत्वारिंश|पंचचत्वारिंश
पञ्चन् + -चत्वारिंश <i>a.</i> forty-fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचत्वारिंशत्|पंचचत्वारिंशत्
पञ्चन् + -चत्वारिंशत् <i>f.</i> forty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचामरम्
पञ्चन् + -चामरम् N. of 2 kinds of metre; प्रमाणिकापदद्वयं वदन्ति<BR> पञ्चचामरम् Vṛttaratnākara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनः|पञ्चजन|पंचजन
पञ्चन् + -जनः<BR>—1 a man, mankind.<BR>—2 N. of a demon who had assumed the form of a conch-shell, and was slain<BR> by Kṛṣṇa; तस्मै प्रादाद्वरं पुत्रं मृतं पञ्चजनोदरात् Bhāg. 3. 3. 2.<BR>—3 the soul.<BR>—4 the five classes of beings; <i>i. e.</i> gods, men, Gandharvas, serpents<BR> and pitṛs; यस्मिन् पञ्च पञ्चजना आकाशश्च प्रतिष्ठितः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 17.<BR>—5 the four primary castes of the Hindus (ब्राह्मण, क्षत्रिय, वैश्य<BR> and शूद्र) with the Niṣādas or barbarians as the fifth (pl. in these<BR> two senses); (for a full exposition see Śārīrabhāṣya on Br. Sūtras 1. 4. 11-13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनी
पञ्चन् + -जनः + .({@-नी@}) an assemblage of five persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनीन|पंचजनीन|पञ्चजनीनः
पञ्चन् + -जनीन <i>a.</i> devoted to the five races.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनीनः|पञ्चजनीन|पंचजनीन
पञ्चन् + -जनीन + .({@-नः@}) an actor, a mimic, buffoon, one who is devoted to the pentad<BR> <i>viz.</i> singer, musician, dancer, harlot and a jester; गायकवादकनर्तकदासीभण्डरतः<BR> खलु पञ्चजनीनः Bhāṣāvṛtti on P. V. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चज्ञानः|पञ्चज्ञान|पंचज्ञान
पञ्चन् + -ज्ञानः<BR>—1 an epithet of Buddha as possessing the five kinds of knowledge.<BR>—2 a man familiar with the doctrines of the Pāśupatas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतक्षम्
पञ्चन् + -तक्षम्, -तक्षी a collection of five carpenters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतक्षी|पंचतक्षी
पञ्चन् + -तक्षम्, -तक्षी a collection of five carpenters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतत्त्वम्
पञ्चन् + -तत्त्वम्<BR>—1 the five elements taken collectively; <i>i. e.</i> पृथ्वी, अप्, तेजस्,<BR> वायु and आकाश.<BR>—2 (in the Tantras) the five essentials of the Tāntrikas, also called<BR> पञ्चमकार because they all begin with म; <i>i. e.</i> मद्य,<BR> मांस, मत्स्य, मुद्रा and मैथुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतन्त्रम्
पञ्चन् + -तन्त्रम् N. of a well-known collection in five books containing<BR> moral stories and fables by Viṣṇugupta; पञ्चतन्त्रात्तथान्यस्माद् ग्रन्थादाकृष्य<BR> लिख्यते H. Pr. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतन्मात्रम्
पञ्चन् + -तन्मात्रम् the five subtle and primary elements (such as शब्द,<BR> रस, स्पर्श, रूप and गन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतपस्|पंचतपस्
पञ्चन् + -तपस् <i>m.</i> an ascetic who in summer practises penance sitting<BR> in the middle of four fires with the sun burning right over his head;<BR> cf. हविर्भुजामेधवतां चतुर्णां मध्ये ललाटंतपसप्तसप्तिः R. 13. 41;<BR> Ku. 5. 23; Ms. 6. 23 and Śi. 2. 51 also; ग्रीष्मे पञ्चतपा वीरो<BR> वर्षास्वासारषाण्मुनिः Bhāg. 4. 23. 6; Rām. 3. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतय|पंचतय|पञ्चतयं|पञ्चतयः
पञ्चन् + -तय <i>a.</i> five-fold; वृत्तयः पञ्चतय्यः क्लिष्टा अक्लिष्टाः Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतयः|पञ्चतय|पंचतय|पञ्चतयं
पञ्चन् + -तय + .({@-यः@}) a pentad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतिक्तम्
पञ्चन् + -तिक्तम् the five bitter things:− निंबामृतावृषपटोलनिदिग्धिकाश्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्रिंश|पंचत्रिंश
पञ्चन् + -त्रिंश <i>a.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">Page0950-1</a>]<BR> thirty-fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0949-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्रिंशत्|पंचत्रिंशत्
पञ्चन् + -त्रिंशत्, -त्रिंशतिः <i>f.</i> thirty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्रिंशतिः|पञ्चत्रिंशति|पंचत्रिंशति
पञ्चन् + -त्रिंशत्, -त्रिंशतिः <i>f.</i> thirty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदश|पंचदश|पञ्चदशः
पञ्चन् + -दश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fifteenth.<BR>—2 increased by fifteen; as in पञ्चदशं शतम् ‘one hundred and fifteen’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशन्|पंचदशन्
पञ्चन् + -दशन् <i>a.</i> (pl.) fifteen. {@˚अहः@} a period of fifteen days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशिन्|पंचदशिन्
पञ्चन् + -दशिन् <i>a.</i> made or consisting of fifteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशी|पंचदशी
पञ्चन् + -दशी<BR>—1 the fifteenth day of a lunar fortnight (the full or new moon day); Y. 1. 146.<BR>—2 N. of a philosophical work (प्रकरणग्रन्थ) by माधवाचार्य<BR> (विद्यारण्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदीर्घम्
पञ्चन् + -दीर्घम् the five long parts of the body; the arms, eyes, belly,<BR> nose and breast; बाहू नेत्रद्वयं कुक्षिर्द्वे तु नासे तथैव च । स्तनयोरन्तरं<BR> चैव पञ्चदीर्घं प्रचक्षते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदेवताः
पञ्चन् + -देवताः the five deities:− आदित्यं गणनाथं च देवीं रुद्रं<BR> च केशवम् । पञ्चदैवतमित्युक्तं सर्वकर्मसु पूजयेत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चधारणक
पञ्चन् + -धारणक <i>a.</i> upheld by the five elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनखः|पञ्चनख|पंचनख
पञ्चन् + -नखः<BR>—1 any animal with five claws; such as the hare, alligator, tortoise,<BR> porcupine, rhinoceros शशकः शल्लकी गोधा खड्गी कूर्मश्च पञ्चमः ।<BR> पञ्च पञ्चनखा भक्ष्या ये प्रोक्ताः कृतजैर्द्विजैः Bk. 6. 131; Ms. 5. 17, 18; Y. 1. 177.<BR>—2 an elephant.<BR>—3 a turtle.<BR>—4 a lion or tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनखी
पञ्चन् + -नखी, -नखराज an iguana (Mar. घोरपड); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनखराज
पञ्चन् + -नखी, -नखराज an iguana (Mar. घोरपड); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनदः|पञ्चनद|पंचनद
पञ्चन् + -नदः ‘the country of five rivers’, the modern Panjab (the five<BR> rivers being शतद्रु, विपाशा, इरावती, चन्द्रभागा and वितस्ता,<BR> or the modern names Sutlej, Beas, Ravee, Chenab and Jhelum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनदाः
पञ्चन् + -नदाः (pl.) the people of this country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनवतिः|पञ्चनवति|पंचनवति
पञ्चन् + -नवतिः <i>f.</i> ninety-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनिम्बम्
पञ्चन् + -निम्बम् the five products of निम्ब <i>viz.</i> (the flowers,<BR> fruit, leaves, bark and root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनीराजनम्
पञ्चन् + -नीराजनम् waving five things before an idol and then falling<BR> prostrate before it; (the five things being:− a lamp, lotus, cloth, mango<BR> and betel-leaf).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चाश|पंचपंचाश
पञ्चन् + -पञ्चाश <i>a.</i> fifty-fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चाशत्|पंचपंचाशत्
पञ्चन् + -पञ्चाशत् <i>f.</i> fifty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपदी
पञ्चन् + -पदी<BR>—1 five steps; पुंसो यमान्तं व्रजतोऽपि निष्ठुरैरेतैर्धनैः पञ्चपदी<BR> न दीयते Pt. 2. 115.<BR>—2 the five strong cases, <i>i. e.</i> the first five inflections<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपर्वन्
पञ्चन् + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> (pl.) the five <i>parvans</i> q. v.; they are चतुर्दश्यष्टमी<BR> चैव अमावास्या च पूर्णिमा । पर्वाण्येतानि राजेन्द्र रविसंक्रान्तिरेव च ।<BR>━<i>a.</i> five-knotted (an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपल्लवम्
पञ्चन् + -पल्लवम् The leaves of the mango, fig, banyan, ficus religiosa<BR> (Mar. पिंपळ) and Genus Ficus (Mar. पायरी). There are other<BR> variations such as पनस, आम्र, पिप्पल, वट and बकुल. The<BR> first group is for the Vedic ritual only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपात्रम्
पञ्चन् + -पात्रम्<BR>—1 five vessels taken collectively.<BR>—2 a Srāddha in which offerings are made in five vessels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपाद्
पञ्चन् + -पाद् <i>a.</i> consisting of five feet, steps, or parts; पञ्चपादं<BR> पितरम् Praśna. Up. 1. 11. ━(<i>m.</i>) a year (संवत्सर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपादिका
पञ्चन् + -पादिका N. of a commentary on शारीरकभाष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपितृ
पञ्चन् + -पितृ <i>m.</i> (pl.) the five fathers:− जनकश्वोपनेता च यश्च<BR> कन्यां प्रयच्छति । अन्नदाता भयत्राता पञ्चैते पितरः स्मृताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपित्तम्
पञ्चन् + -पित्तम् the bile of five animals <i>viz.</i> (the boar, goat, buffalo,<BR> fish and peacock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्रस्थ
पञ्चन् + -प्रस्थ <i>a.</i> having five elevations (a forest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्राणाः
पञ्चन् + -प्राणाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the five life-winds or vital airs; प्राण,<BR> अपान, व्यान, उदान and समान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्रासादः|पञ्चप्रासाद
पञ्चन् + -प्रासादः a temple of a particular size with four pinnacles and a steeple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबन्ध|पञ्चबन्धः
पञ्चन् + -बन्ध a fine equal to the fifth part of anything lost or stolen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबलाः
पञ्चन् + -बलाः five medicinal herbs, namely बला, नागबला, महाबला,<BR> अतिबला and राजबला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबाणः|पञ्चबाण|पंचबाण
पञ्चन् + -बाणः, -वाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; see पञ्चेषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवाणः|पञ्चवाण|पंचवाण
पञ्चन् + -बाणः, -वाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; see पञ्चेषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशरः|पञ्चशर|पंचशर
पञ्चन् + -बाणः, -वाणः, -शरः epithets of the god of love; see पञ्चेषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबाहुः|पञ्चबाहु
पञ्चन् + -बाहुः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबिन्दुप्रसृतम्
पञ्चन् + -बिन्दुप्रसृतम् N. of a particular movement in dancing; Dk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबीजानि
पञ्चन् + -बीजानि the five seeds:− कर्कटी, त्रपुस, दाडिम, पद्मबीज,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">Page0950-2</a>]<BR> and वानरीबीज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभद्र|पञ्चभद्रः
पञ्चन् + -भद्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having five good qualities.<BR>—2 consisting of five good ingredients (as a sauce &c.).<BR>—3 having five auspicious marks (as a horse) in the chest, back, face and flanks.<BR>—4 vicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभद्रः|पञ्चभद्र
पञ्चन् + -भद्रः a kind of pavilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभागिन्
पञ्चन् + -भागिन् <i>m.</i> the five deities of पञ्चमहा. यज्ञ; धर्मकामविहीनस्य<BR> चुक्रुधुः पञ्चभागिनः Bhāg. 11. 23. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभुज|पञ्चभुजः
पञ्चन् + -भुज <i>a.</i> pentagonal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभुजः|पञ्चभुज
पञ्चन् + -भुज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a pentagon; cf. पञ्चकोण.<BR>—2 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभूतम्
पञ्चन् + -भूतम् the five elements; पृथ्वी, अप्, तेजस्, वायु and आकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभृङ्गाः
पञ्चन् + -भृङ्गाः the five trees, <i>viz.</i> देवदाली (Mar. देवडंगरी),<BR> शमी, भङ्गा (Mar. भांग), निर्गुण्डी and तमालपत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमकारम्
पञ्चन् + -मकारम् the five essentials of the left-hand Tantra ritual of<BR> which the first letter is म; see पञ्चतत्त्व (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमहापातकम्
पञ्चन् + -महापातकम् the five great sins; see महापातक; Ms. 11. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमहायज्ञाः
पञ्चन् + -महायज्ञाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the five daily sacrifices enjoined to<BR> be performed by a Brāhmaṇa; अध्यापनं ब्रह्मयज्ञः पितृयज्ञस्तु तर्पणम् ।<BR> होमो दैवो बलिर्भौतो नृयज्ञोऽतिथिपूजनम् ॥ Ms. 3. 70. अहुतं च<BR> हुतं चैव तथा प्रहुतमेव च । ब्राह्मं हुतं प्राशितं च पञ्च यज्ञान्<BR> प्रचक्षते ॥ Ms. 3. 73; see महायज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमारः|पञ्चमार
पञ्चन् + -मारः son of Baladeva; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाशक
पञ्चन् + -माशक, -माषिक <i>a.</i> consisting of five Māṣas<BR> (as a fine &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाषिक
पञ्चन् + -माशक, -माषिक <i>a.</i> consisting of five Māṣas<BR> (as a fine &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाषक
पञ्चन् + -माषक, -माषिक <i>a.</i> amounting to five māṣas;<BR> गर्दभाजाविकानां तु दण्डः स्यात्पञ्चमाषिकः Ms. 8. 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाषिक
पञ्चन् + -माषक, -माषिक <i>a.</i> amounting to five māṣas;<BR> गर्दभाजाविकानां तु दण्डः स्यात्पञ्चमाषिकः Ms. 8. 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमास्य|पंचमास्य|पञ्चमास्यः
पञ्चन् + -मास्य <i>a.</i> happening every five months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुखः|पञ्चमुख|पंचमुख
पञ्चन् + -मुखः an arrow with five points; (for other senses see पञ्चानन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुद्रा
पञ्चन् + -मुद्रा five gestures to be made in presenting offerings to an<BR> idol; <i>viz.</i> आवाहनी, स्थापनी, संनिधापनी, संबोधनी and संमुखीकरणी; see मुद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूत्रम्
पञ्चन् + -मूत्रम् (the urine of five female animals; the cow, goat, she-buffalo,<BR> sheep, and she-ass.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूलम्
पञ्चन् + -मूलम् there are nine varieties of the pentad combinations of<BR> roots; लघुपञ्चमूल, बृहत्पञ्चमूल, शतावर्यादि, तृणपञ्चमूल, जीवकादिपञ्चमूल,<BR> पुनर्नवादिपञ्चमूल, गोक्षुरादि˚, वल्ली˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरत्नम्
पञ्चन् + -रत्नम् a collection of five gems; (they are variously enumerated:−<BR> (1) नीलकं वज्रकं चेति पद्मरागश्च मौक्तिकम् । प्रवालं चेति विज्ञेयं<BR> पंचरत्नं मनीषिभिः ॥ (2) सुवर्णं रजतं मुक्ता राजावर्तं प्रवालकम् ।<BR> रत्नपञ्चकमाख्यातम् … ॥ (3) कनकं हीरकं नीलं पद्मरागश्च<BR> मौक्तिकम् । पञ्चरत्नमिदं प्रोक्तमृषिभिः पूर्वदर्शिभिः ॥<BR>—2 the five most admired episodes of the Mahābhārata; गीता, विष्णुसहस्रनाम,<BR> भीष्मस्तवराज, अनुस्मृति and गजेन्द्रमोक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरसा
पञ्चन् + -रसा the आमलकी tree (Mar. आंवळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरात्रम्
पञ्चन् + -रात्रम्<BR>—1 a period of five nights; इत्यर्थं वयमानीताः पञ्चरात्रोऽपि विद्यते Pañc. 3. 24.<BR>—2 N. of one of Bhāsaʼs dramas.<BR>—3 N. of a philosophical treatise attributed to Nārada.<BR>—4 N. of an अहीन (sacrifice) lasting for 5 days; स एतं पञ्चरात्रं<BR> पुरुषमेधं यज्ञक्रतुमपश्यत् Śat. Br.; cf. Mb. 12. 218. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चराशिकम्
पञ्चन् + -राशिकम् the rule of five (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलक्षणम्
पञ्चन् + -लक्षणम् a Purāṇa; so called because it deals with five important<BR> topics:− सर्गश्च प्रतिसर्गश्च वंशो मन्वन्तराणि च । वंशानुचरितं<BR> चैव पुराणं पञ्चलक्षणम् ॥ see पुराण also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलवणम्
पञ्चन् + -लवणम् five kinds of salt; <i>i. e.</i> काचक, सैन्धव, सामुद्र,<BR> बिड and सौवर्चल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलाङ्गलकम्
पञ्चन् + -लाङ्गलकम् a gift (महादान) of as much land as can be cultivated<BR> with five ploughs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोकपालः|पञ्चलोकपाल
पञ्चन् + -लोकपालः the five guardian deities <i>viz.</i> Vināyaka, Durgā,<BR> Vāyu, Ākāśa and Aśvinīkumāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोहम्
पञ्चन् + -लोहम् a metallic alloy containing five metals (<i>i. e.</i> copper,<BR> brass, tin, lead and iron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोहकम्
पञ्चन् + -लोहकम् the five metals <i>i. e.</i> gold, silver, copper, tin and lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवटः|पञ्चवट
पञ्चन् + -वटः the sacred or sacrificial thread worn across the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">Page0951-1</a>]<BR> breast (यज्ञोपवीत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0950-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवटी
पञ्चन् + -वटी<BR>—1 the five fig-trees: <i>i. e.</i> अश्वत्थ, बिल्व, वट, धात्री and अशोक.<BR>—2 N. of a part of the Daṇḍakā forest where the Godāvarī rises and<BR> where Rāma dwelt for a considerable time with his beloved; it is two<BR> miles from Nasik; परिहरन्तमपि मामितः पञ्चवटीस्नेहो बलादाकर्षतीव<BR> U. 2. 27/28; R. 13. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्गः|पञ्चवर्ग
पञ्चन् + -वर्गः<BR>—1 an aggregate of five.<BR>—2 the five essential elements of the body.<BR>—3 the five organs of sense; संतुष्टपञ्चवर्गोऽहं लोकयात्रां प्रवाहये<BR> Rām. 2. 109. 27.<BR>—4 the five daily sacrifices enjoined to be performed by a Brāhmaṇa;<BR> cf. महायज्ञ.<BR>—5 the five classes of spies (कापटिक, उदास्थित, गृहपतिव्यञ्जन,<BR> वैदेहिकव्यञ्जन and तापसव्यञ्जन); cf. Kull. on Ms. 7. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्षदेशीय|पंचवर्षदेशीय
पञ्चन् + -वर्षदेशीय <i>a.</i> about five years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्षीय|पंचवर्षीय
पञ्चन् + -वर्षीय <i>a.</i> five years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवल्कलम्
पञ्चन् + -वल्कलम् a collection of the barks of five kinds of trees; namely<BR> न्यग्रोध, उदुम्बर, अश्वत्थ, प्लक्ष and वेतस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवल्लभा
पञ्चन् + -वल्लभा N. of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवार्षिक
पञ्चन् + -वार्षिक <i>a.</i> recurring every five years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवाहिन्
पञ्चन् + -वाहिन् <i>a.</i> drawn by five (as a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंश|पंचविंश|पञ्चविंशः
पञ्चन् + -विंश <i>a.</i> twenty-fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंशः|पञ्चविंश|पंचविंश
पञ्चन् + -विंशः<BR>—1 a Stoma consisting of 25 parts.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu (regarded as the 25th तत्त्व); स तु जनपरितापं<BR> तत्कृतं जानता ते नरहर उपनीतः पञ्चतां पञ्चविंश Bhāg. 7. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंशतिः|पञ्चविंशति|पंचविंशति
पञ्चन् + -विंशतिः <i>f.</i> twenty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविंशतिका|पंचविंशतिका
पञ्चन् + -विंशतिका a collection of twenty-five; as in वेतालपञ्चविंशतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चविध|पंचविध
पञ्चन् + -विध <i>a.</i> fivefold, of five kinds. ˚प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i> the<BR> five departments of a government; अमात्यराष्ट्रदुर्गार्थदण्डाख्याः पञ्च<BR> चापराः Ms. 7. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0951-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

