पट्टः + -देवी, -महिषी, -राज्ञी the principal queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टबन्धः|पट्टबन्ध
पट्टः + -बन्धः, -बन्धनम्<BR>—1 wearing dress.<BR>—2 binding the head with a crown or turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टबन्धनम्
पट्टः + -बन्धः, -बन्धनम्<BR>—1 wearing dress.<BR>—2 binding the head with a crown or turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टरागः|पट्टराग
पट्टः + -रागः sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टवस्त्र
पट्टः + -वस्त्र, -वासस् <i>a.</i> attired in woven silk or coloured cloth;<BR> जीर्णा कन्था ततः किं सितममलवरं पट्टवस्त्रं ततः किम् Bh. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टवासस्
पट्टः + -वस्त्र, -वासस् <i>a.</i> attired in woven silk or coloured cloth;<BR> जीर्णा कन्था ततः किं सितममलवरं पट्टवस्त्रं ततः किम् Bh. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टशाला
पट्टः + -शाला a tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टसूत्रकारः|पट्टसूत्रकार
पट्टः + -सूत्रकारः a silk-weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टकः|पट्टक
पट्टकः<BR>—1 A plate of metal used for inscriptions or royal edicts.<BR>—2 A bandage.<BR>—3 A document; (also <i>n.</i>)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टकिलः|पट्टकिल
पट्टकिलः The tenant of a piece of land (by royal edict).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टनम्
पट्टनम्, -नी<BR> A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टनी
पट्टनम्, -नी<BR> A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिका
पट्टिका<BR>—1 A tablet, plate; as in हृतपट्टिका.<BR>—2 A document.<BR>—3 A piece or fragment of cloth: वल्कलैकदेशाद्विपाट्य पट्टिकाम् K. 149.<BR>—4 A piece of silken cloth.<BR>—5 A ligature, bandage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पट्टिकावायकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिकावायकः|पट्टिकावायक
पट्टिका + -वायकः a silk-weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टलम्
पट्टलम् A coating, multitude; वाजिराजिमुखोत्खातधूलीपट्टलपाटलाम्<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टला
पट्टला A district, community.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिशः|पट्टिश
पट्टि(ट्टी)शः (सः) A kind of spear with a sharp edge (Mar.<BR> पट्टा); कणपप्रासपट्टिश &c. Dk.; (पट्टिशो लौहदण्डो यस्तीक्ष्णधारः<BR> क्षुरोपमः Vaijayantī); भुशुण्डिभिश्चकगदर्ष्टिपट्टिशैः … … शिरांसि<BR> चिच्छिदुः Bhāg. 8. 10. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टीशः|पट्टीश
पट्टि(ट्टी)शः (सः) A kind of spear with a sharp edge (Mar.<BR> पट्टा); कणपप्रासपट्टिश &c. Dk.; (पट्टिशो लौहदण्डो यस्तीक्ष्णधारः<BR> क्षुरोपमः Vaijayantī); भुशुण्डिभिश्चकगदर्ष्टिपट्टिशैः … … शिरांसि<BR> चिच्छिदुः Bhāg. 8. 10. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टीसः|पट्टीस
पट्टि(ट्टी)शः (सः) A kind of spear with a sharp edge (Mar.<BR> पट्टा); कणपप्रासपट्टिश &c. Dk.; (पट्टिशो लौहदण्डो यस्तीक्ष्णधारः<BR> क्षुरोपमः Vaijayantī); भुशुण्डिभिश्चकगदर्ष्टिपट्टिशैः … … शिरांसि<BR> चिच्छिदुः Bhāg. 8. 10. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टोलिका
पट्टोलिका<BR>—1 A kind of bond or lease (भूमिकरग्रहणव्यवस्थापकः पत्रभेदः Tv.).<BR>—2 A written legal opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठ्
पठ् €1 P. (पठति, पठित)<BR>—1 To read or repeat aloud, recite, rehearse; यः पठेच्छृणुयादपि.<BR>—2 To read or recite<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">Page0954-1</a>]<BR> to oneself; study, peruse; इत्येतन्मानवं शास्त्रं भृगुप्रोक्तं पठन्<BR> द्विजः Ms. 15. 126, 4. 98; नाक्षराणि पठता किमपाठि N. 5. 121.<BR>—3 To invoke (as a deity).<BR>—4 To cite, quote, mention (as in a book); एतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं पुराणे<BR> यदि पठ्यते Mb.<BR>—5 To declare, describe, express; भार्या च परमो ह्यर्थः पुरुषस्येह<BR> पठपते; Mb.<BR>—6 To teach.<BR>—7 To learn from (with abl.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (पाठयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to read aloud.<BR>—2 To teach, instruct; राजन् राजसुता न पाठयति माम् K. P. 10. ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> (पिपठिषति) To wish to recite &c. ━<i>With</i> {@परि@} to mention,<BR> declare. ━(<i>Caus.</i>) to teach; तौ सर्वविद्याः परिपाठितौ U. 2.<BR>━{@सम्@} to read, learn; वेदाङ्गानि च सर्वाणि कृष्णपक्षेषु संपठेत् Ms. 4. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0953-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठः|पठ
पठः Reading, reciting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पठमञ्जरी, पठसमञ्जरी, पठहंसिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठमञ्जरी
पठः + -मञ्जरी, -समञ्जरी N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठसमञ्जरी
पठः + -मञ्जरी, -समञ्जरी N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठहंसिका
पठः + -हंसिका N. of a Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठकः|पठक
पठकः A reader, reciter; a student; पठकाः पाठकाश्चैव ये चान्ये<BR> शास्त्रचिन्तकाः । सर्वे व्यसनिनो मूर्खा यः क्रियावान् स पण्डितः ॥ Mb. 3. 313. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठनम्
पठनम् [पठ्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Reading, reciting.<BR>—2 Mentioning.<BR>—3 Studying, perusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठनीय
पठनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit to be read or studied.<BR>—2 Legible, readable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठिः|पठि
पठिः <i>f.</i> Reading, studying, perusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठित|पठितः
पठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Recited, repeated.<BR>—2 Studied, perused; प्रस्मृतः किमथवा पठितोऽपि N. 5. 121.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पठितसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितसिद्ध
पठित + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> effective on being merely recited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितिः|पठिति
पठितिः <i>f.</i> N. of a figure of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितृ
पठितृ <i>a.</i> A Reader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पड्वीशम्
पड्वीशम्, पड्विंशम् A fetter (पादबन्धन); महासुहयः<BR> सैन्धवः पङ्वीशशङ्कून् संवृहेत् Bṛ. Up. 6. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पड्विंशम्
पड्वीशम्, पड्विंशम् A fetter (पादबन्धन); महासुहयः<BR> सैन्धवः पङ्वीशशङ्कून् संवृहेत् Bṛ. Up. 6. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्
पण् I. €1 Ā. (पणते, पणित)<BR>—1 To deal in, barter, purchase, buy; विततं वणिजापणेऽखिलं पणितुं<BR> यत्र जनेन वीक्ष्यते N. 2. 91.<BR>—2 To bargain, transact business.<BR>—3 To bet or stake at play (usually with gen. of the thing staked, but<BR> sometimes with acc.); प्राणानामपणिष्टासौ Bk. 8. 121; पणस्व कृष्णां पाञ्चालीम् Mb.<BR>—4 To risk or hazard (a battle).<BR>—5 To win anything at play. ━II. €1 Ā., €10 U. (पणते, पणायति-ते)<BR> कोटिभिः पणते नित्यं तस्य राष्ट्रे वणिग्जनः.<BR>—1 To praise.<BR>—2 To honour; यक्षाश्चापि पणायन्ति तद्विभूतिं गृहे गृहे. ━<i>With</i><BR> {@वि@} to sell, barter; आभीरदेशे किल चन्द्रकान्तं त्रिभिर्वराटैर्विपणन्ति<BR> गोपाः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणः|पण
पणः<BR>—1 Playing with dice or for a stake.<BR>—2 A game played for a stake, bet, wager; सपणश्चेद्विवादः स्यात्तत्र<BR> हीनं तु दापयेत् Y. 2. 18; दमयन्त्याः पणः साधुर्वर्तताम् Mb.<BR>—3 The thing staked.<BR>—4 A condition, compact, agreement; संधिं करोतु भवतां नृपतिः पणेन<BR> Ve. 1. 15; ‘a stipulation, treaty’; H. 4. 118, 119.<BR>—5 Wages, hire.<BR>—6 Reward.<BR>—7 A sum in coins or shells.<BR>—8 A particular coin equal in value to 80 <i>cowries</i>; अशीतिभिर्वराटकैः<BR> पण इत्यभिधीयते; ततोऽरिसैन्या -दानीतान् सौवर्णान् राजतान् पणान्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">Page0954-2</a>]<BR> Śiva B. 23. 3.<BR>—9 Price.<BR>—10 Wealth, property; आरोपणेन पणमप्रतिकार्यमार्यस्त्रैयम्बकस्य<BR> धनुषो यदि नाकरिष्यत् Mv. 1. 27.<BR>—11 A commodity for sale.<BR>—12 Business, transaction; निरस्य समयं सर्वे पणोऽस्माकं भविष्यति Mb. 3. 7. 9.<BR>—13 A shop.<BR>—14 A seller, vendor.<BR>—15 A distiller.<BR>—16 A house.<BR>—17 Expense of an expedition.<BR>—18 A handful of anything.<BR>—19 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पणाङ्गना, पणस्त्री, पणायः, पणार्पणम्, पणकर्मन्, पणक्रिया, पणग्रन्थिः, पणबन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाङ्गना|पणांगना
पणः + -अङ्गना, -स्त्री a prostitute, harlot; शोभा हि पणस्त्रीणां सदृशजनसमाश्रयः<BR> कामः Mk. 8. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणस्त्री
पणः + -अङ्गना, -स्त्री a prostitute, harlot; शोभा हि पणस्त्रीणां सदृशजनसमाश्रयः<BR> कामः Mk. 8. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणायः|पणाय
पणः + -अयः Acquisition of profit; न चोपलेभे वणिजां पणायान् Bk. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणार्पणम्
पणः + -अर्पणम् making an agreement, a contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणकर्मन्
पणः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> A solemn contract; पणकर्मणा संहितान् अपसर्पान् Kau. A. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणक्रिया
पणः + -क्रिया Putting in a stake, contest for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणग्रन्थिः|पणग्रन्थि|पणग्रंथि
पणः + -ग्रन्थिः a market, fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणबन्धः|पणबन्ध|पणबंध
पणः + -बन्धः —1 making a treaty of peace (संधि); पणबन्धमुखान्<BR> गुणानजः षडुपायुङ्क्त समीक्ष्य तत्फलम् R. 8. 21, 10. 86.<BR>—2 an agreement, stipulation (यदि भवानिदं कुर्यात्तर्हीदमहं भवते<BR> दास्यामीति समयकरणं पणबन्धः Manoramā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणता
पणता, -त्वम्<BR> Price, value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणत्वम्
पणता, -त्वम्<BR> Price, value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणनम्
पणनम् [पण्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Bartering, purchasing.<BR>—2 Betting.<BR>—3 Sale.<BR>—4 Traffic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणसः|पणस
पणसः An article of sale, a commodity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाया
पणाया<BR>—1 Transaction, business, dealing.<BR>—2 A market-place.<BR>—3 Profits of a trade.<BR>—4 Gambling.<BR>—5 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणायित|पणायितः
पणायित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praised.<BR>—2 Bought, sold, transacted &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणायितृ
पणायितृ <i>m.</i> A seller; Māl. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणिः|पणि
पणिः <i>f.</i> A market. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A miser, niggard.<BR>—2 An impious man, a thief (appearing as a Purohita); Bhāg. 5. 9. 15.<BR>—3 A bargainer; धरां रजःस्वभावेन पणयो ये च ताननु Bhāg. 3. 6. 28.<BR>—4 N. of a class of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणिक
पणिक <i>a.</i> Consisting of 50 Paṇas (as fine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणित|पणितं
पणित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Transacted (as business).<BR>—2 Betted; see पण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणितम्
पणित + .{@-तम्@} A bet, wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणितृ
पणितृ <i>m.</i> A trader, dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्य|पण्यं|पण्यः
पण्य <i>a.</i> [पण्-कर्मणि यत्]<BR>—1 Saleable, vendible.<BR>—2 To be transacted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यः|पण्य|पण्यं
पण्य + .{@-ण्यः@}<BR>—1 A ware, an article, a commodity; पूराबभासे विपणिस्थपण्या R. 16. 41;<BR> पण्यानां गान्धिकं पण्यम् Pt. 1. 13; सौभाग्यपण्याकरः Mk. 8. 38;<BR> Ms. 5. 129; M. 1. 17; Y. 2. 245.<BR>—2 Trade, business.<BR>—3 Price; महता पुण्यपण्येन क्रीतेयं कायनौस्त्वया Śānti. 3. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पण्याङ्गना, पण्ययोषित्, पण्याजिरम्, पण्याजीवः, पण्याजीवकम्, पण्यजनः, पण्यदासी, पण्यपतिः, पण्यपत्तनम्, पण्यपरिणीता, पण्यफलत्वम्, पण्यबाहुल्यम्, पण्यभूमिः, पण्यवीथिका, पण्यवीथी, पण्यशाला, पण्यसंस्था, पण्यहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याङ्गना|पण्यांगना
पण्य + -अङ्गना, -योषित् <i>f.</i>, {@-विलासिनी, -स्त्री@} <i>f.</i><BR> a harlot, a courtezan; पण्यस्त्रीषु विवेककल्पलतिकाशस्त्रीषु<BR> रज्येत कः Bh. 1. 90; Me. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ययोषित्
पण्य + -अङ्गना, -योषित् <i>f.</i>, {@-विलासिनी, -स्त्री@} <i>f.</i><BR> a harlot, a courtezan; पण्यस्त्रीषु विवेककल्पलतिकाशस्त्रीषु<BR> रज्येत कः Bh. 1. 90; Me. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजिरम्
पण्य + -अजिरम् a market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजीवः|पण्याजीव
पण्य + -आजीवः a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजीवकम्
पण्य + -आजीवकम् a market, fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यजनः|पण्यजन
पण्य + -जनः a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यदासी
पण्य + -दासी a hired female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यपतिः|पण्यपति
पण्य + -पतिः a great merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यपत्तनम्
पण्य + -पत्तनम् a market town; पण्यपत्तनानि च निवेशयेत् Kau. A. 2. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यपरिणीता
पण्य + -परिणीता a concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यफलत्वम्
पण्य + -फलत्वम् prosperity or profit in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">Page0955-1</a>]<BR> trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0954-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यबाहुल्यम्
पण्य + -बाहुल्यम् prosperity of commerce; सस्यसंपत्पण्यबाहुल्यमुपसर्गप्रमोक्षः … इति<BR> कोशवृद्धिः Kau. A. 2. 7. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यभूमिः|पण्यभूमि
पण्य + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> a ware-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथिका
पण्य + -वीथिका, -वीथी, -शाला<BR>—1 a market.<BR>—2 a stall, shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथी
पण्य + -वीथिका, -वीथी, -शाला<BR>—1 a market.<BR>—2 a stall, shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यशाला
पण्य + -वीथिका, -वीथी, -शाला<BR>—1 a market.<BR>—2 a stall, shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यसंस्था
पण्य + -संस्था the ware-house of merchandise; Kau. A. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यहोमः|पण्यहोम
पण्य + -होमः a sacrifice consisting of wares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणफरम्
पणफरम् The second, eighth, fifth or eleventh house (in a horoscope)<BR> from the लग्नराशि; पणफरं द्वितीयाष्टपञ्चमैकादशं स्मृतम् Jyotistattvam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणवः|पणव
पणवः A kind of musical instrument, a small drum or tabor; Bg. 1. 13;<BR> Śi. 13. 5; गुरु-पणव-वेणु-गुञ्जभेरी … … Bk. 18. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणविन्
पणविन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ड्|पंड्
पण्ड् I. €1 Ā. (पण्डते, पण्डित) To go or move. ━II. €10 U. (पण्डयति-ते)<BR> To collect, pile up, heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डः|पण्ड|पंड|पंडः
पण्डः A eunuch; weakling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डा
पण्डा<BR>—1 Wisdom, understanding.<BR>—2 Learning, science.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पण्डापूर्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डापूर्वम्
पण्डा + -अपूर्वम् non-occurrence of the results of fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डावत्
पण्डावत् <i>a.</i> Wise; पण्डावदग्रिम Aśvad. 6. ━<i>m.</i> A learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डित|पंडित|पण्डितः
पण्डित <i>a.</i> [पण्डा तारका˚ इतच्]<BR>—1 Learned, wise; स्वस्थे को वा न पण्डितः.<BR>—2 Shrewd, clever.<BR>—3 Skilled in, proficient, skilful (generally with loc. or in comp.);<BR> मधुरालापनिसर्गपण्डिताम् Ku. 4. 16; so रतिपण्डित 4. 18; नयपण्डित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितः|पण्डित|पंडित
पण्डित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A scholar, learned man, <i>Paṇdita</i>.<BR>—2 Incense.<BR>—3 An adept, expert.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पण्डितजातीय, पण्डितमण्डलम्, पण्डितसभा, पण्डितमानिक, पण्डितमानिन्, पण्डितवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितजातीय
पण्डित + -जातीय <i>a.</i> somewhat clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमण्डलम्
पण्डित + -मण्डलम्, -सभा an assembly of learned men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितसभा
पण्डित + -मण्डलम्, -सभा an assembly of learned men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमानिक
पण्डित + -मानिक, -मानिन्, also {@पण्डितंमन्य@} <i>a.</i> fancying oneself<BR> to be learned, a conceited person, a pedant who fancies himself to be<BR> a <i>Paṇdita</i>; रण्डे पण्डितमानिनि तूष्णीं भव Pt. 4. 100; अविद्यायामन्तरे<BR> वर्तमाना वयं धीराः पण्डितंमन्यमानाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमानिन्
पण्डित + -मानिक, -मानिन्, also {@पण्डितंमन्य@} <i>a.</i> fancying oneself<BR> to be learned, a conceited person, a pedant who fancies himself to be<BR> a <i>Paṇdita</i>; रण्डे पण्डितमानिनि तूष्णीं भव Pt. 4. 100; अविद्यायामन्तरे<BR> वर्तमाना वयं धीराः पण्डितंमन्यमानाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितवादिन्
पण्डित + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> pretending to be wise; रे रे पण्डितवादिनि नाशङ्कसे<BR> प्रजल्पन्ती Pt. 1. 392.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितक|पंडितक|पण्डितकः
पण्डितक <i>a.</i> Learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितकः|पण्डितक|पंडितक
पण्डितक + .{@-कः@} A learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितिमन्|पंडितिमन्
पण्डितिमन् <i>m.</i> Learning, scholarship, wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डिती
पण्डिती <i>f.</i> Learning; प्रतिपत्तुमियत्तया जनो न किलासीदलमस्य<BR> पण्डितीम् Śāhendra. 2. 51; Ms. 12. 28.<BR>—4 Obtaining, securing.<BR>—5 A ttracting, captivating,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ड्रः|पण्ड्र
पण्ड्रः (-कः)<BR>—1 An eunuch; Mārk. P.<BR>—2 One affected by वात disease; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ड्रक
पण्ड्रः (-कः)<BR>—1 An eunuch; Mārk. P.<BR>—2 One affected by वात disease; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्
पत् I. €1 P. (पतति, पतित)<BR>—1 To fall, fall down, come down, descend, drop down, alight; अवाङ्मुखस्योपरि<BR> पुष्पवृष्टिः पपात विद्याधरहस्तमुक्ता R. 2. 60; वृष्टिर्भवने चास्य<BR> पेतुषी 10. 77; (रेणुः) पतति परिणतारुणप्रकाशः शलभसमूह<BR> इवाश्रमद्रुमेषु Ś. 1. 31; Me. 107; Bk. 7. 9, 21. 6.<BR>—2 To fly, move through the air, soar; हन्तुं कलहकारोऽसौ शब्दकारः<BR> पपात खम् Bk. 5. 100; see पतत् below.<BR>—3 To set, sink (below the horizon); सोऽयं सोमः पतति गगनादल्पशेषमैर्यूखैः<BR> Ś. 4. 2 v. l.; पतत्पतङ्गप्रतिमस्तपोनिधिः Śi. 1. 12.<BR>—4 To cast oneself at, throw oneself down,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">Page0955-2</a>]<BR> मयि ते पादपतिते किंकरत्वमुपागते Pt. 4. 7; so चरणपतितम् Me. 105;<BR>—5 To fall (in a moral sense), lose oneʼs caste, forfeit oneʼs rank or<BR> position, fall off; परधर्मेण जीवन् हि सद्यः पतति जातितः Ms. 10. 97, 3. 16, 5. 19, 9. 200;<BR> Y. 1. 38.<BR>—6 To come down (as from heaven); पतन्ति पितरो ह्येषां लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रियाः Bg. 1. 42.<BR>—7 To fall, be reduced to wretchedness or misery; प्रायः कन्दुकपातेनोत्पतत्यार्यः<BR> पतन्नपि Bh. 2. 123.<BR>—8 To go down into hell, go to perdition; Ms. 11. 37; प्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु<BR> पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ Bg. 16. 16.<BR>—9 To fall, occur, come to pass, take place; लक्ष्मीर्यत्र पतन्ति तत्र<BR> विवृतद्वारा इव व्यापदः Subhāṣ.<BR>—10 To be directed to, light or fall upon (with loc.); प्रसादसौम्यानि<BR> सतां सुहृज्जने पतन्ति चक्षूंषि न दारुणाः शराः Ś. 6. 29.<BR>—11 To fall to oneʼs lot or share.<BR>—12 To be in, fall in or into. ━<i>Caus.</i> (पातयति-ते, पतयति rarely)<BR>—1 To cause to fall down, descend or sink &c.; निपतन्ती पतिमप्यपातयत्<BR> R. 8. 38, 9. 61, 11. 76.<BR>—2 To let fall, throw or drop down, fell down (as trees &c.).<BR>—3 To ruin, overthrow; व्यपदेशमाविलयितुं किमीहसे जनमिमं च पातयितुम् Ś. 5. 21.<BR>—4 To shed (as tears).<BR>—5 To cast, direct (as the sight).<BR>—6 To dash or strike out.<BR>—7 To throw or put in, cause to enter.<BR>—8 To bring to ruin or misfortune.<BR>—9 To depreciate, lower the value of anything; अर्घतः पातिताः Bh. 2. 15.<BR>—10 (In arith.) To subtract, deduct.<BR>—11 To set in motion, set on foot. ━<i>Desid.</i> (पिपतिषति or<BR> पित्सति) To wish to fall. ━II. €4 Ā. (पत्यते) Ved.<BR>—1 To be master of.<BR>—2 To rule, control.<BR>—3 To possess.<BR>—4 To be fit for, serve for (with dat.). ━III. €10 U. (पतयति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be master of (intransitive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत|पतं|पतः
पत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Cherished, well-fed, protected (पुष्ट).<BR>—2 Flying, falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतः|पत|पतं
पत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Flying, flight.<BR>—2 Going, falling, alighting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतगः|पतग
पत + -गः<BR>—1 a bird; Ms. 7. 23.<BR>—2 the sun; पतगोऽसौ विभावसुः Mb. 6. 12. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतक|पतकः
पतक <i>a.</i> Falling, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतकः|पतक
पतक + .{@-कः@} An astronomical table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गः|पतङ्ग|पतंग|पतङ्गं|पतंगः
पतङ्गः [पतन् उत्प्लवन् गच्छति गम्-ड नि˚]<BR>—1 A bird; नृपः पतङ्गं समधत्त पाणिना N. 1. 124; Bv. 1. 17.<BR>—2 The sun; विकसति हि पतङ्गस्योदये पुण्डरीकम् U. 6. 12; Māl. 1. 24;<BR> Śi. 1. 12; R. 2. 15.<BR>—3 A moth, locust, or grass-hopper; पतङ्गवद्वह्निमुखं विविक्षुः<BR> Ku. 3. 64, 4. 20; Pt. 3. 126.<BR>—4 A bee.<BR>—5 A ball for playing with; योऽसौ त्वया करसरोजहतः पतङ्गः Bhāg. 5. 2. 14.<BR>—6 Ved. A spark.<BR>—7 A devil.<BR>—8 Quicksilver.<BR>—9 N. of Kṛṣṇa<BR>—10 A horse.<BR>—11 A species of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गम्
पतङ्गः + .{@-ङ्गम्@}<BR>—1 Quicksilver.<BR>—2 A kind of sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गमः|पतङ्गम|पतंगम|पतंगमः
पतङ्गमः<BR>—1 A bird.<BR>—2 A moth; अलक्षितोऽग्नौ पतितः पतङ्गमः Bhāg. 7. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गिका|पतंगिका
पतङ्गिका<BR>—1 A small bird.<BR>—2 A kind of small bee; पतङ्गिकानां पुच्छेषु त्वयेषीका प्रवेशिता । कर्मणस्तस्य<BR> ते प्राप्तं फलमेतत्तपोधन ॥ Mb. 1. 108. 11.<BR>—3 A bow-string; L. D. B.; also पतञ्चिका; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0955-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गिन्
पतङ्गिन् <i>m.</i> A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्जलिः|पतञ्जलि|पतंजलि|पतंजलिः
पतञ्जलिः N. of the celebrated author of the Mahābhāṣya, the<BR> great commentary on Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras; also of a philosopher, the propounder<BR> of the Yoga philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्|पतन्त्
पतत् (-न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Flying, descending, alighting, coming down &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR> A bird; परमः पुमानिव पतिं पतताम् Ki. 6. 1; क्वचित् पथा संचरते<BR> सुराणां क्वचिद्धनानां पततां क्वचिच्च R. 13. 19; Śi. 9. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतद्ग्रहः, पतत्प्रकर्ष, पतद्भीरुः, पतद्वहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्ग्रहः|पतद्ग्रह
पतत् + -ग्रहः<BR>—1 the reserve of an army.<BR>—2 a spitting pot, spittoon; तमेकमाणिक्यमयं महोन्नतं पतद्ग्रहं<BR> ग्राहितवान्नलेन सः N. 16. 27; रौप्यान् रौक्माँश्च पर्यङ्कान् करङ्काँश्च<BR> पतद्ग्रहान् Śiva B. 17. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्प्रकर्ष
पतत् + -प्रकर्ष <i>a.</i> (in rhet.) illogical; prosaical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्भीरुः|पतद्भीरु
पतत् + -भीरुः a hawk, falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्वहः
पतत् + -वहः (= पतद्ग्रहः) पतद्वहत्वेन कृतात्पतङ्गः पत्न्या<BR> जलेशस्य दिशा वहस्य Rām. Ch. 6. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रम्
पतत्रम् [पत्-करणे अत्रन्]<BR>—1 A wing, pinion; Śvet. Up. 3. 3; येन मे पूर्वमद्रीणां पक्षच्छेदः<BR> प्रजात्यये । कृतो निविशतां भारैः पतत्त्रैः पततां भुवि ॥ Bhāg. 8. 11. 34.<BR>—2 A feather.<BR>—3 A vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिः|पतत्रि
पतत्रिः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिन्
पतत्रिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A bird; दयिता द्वन्द्वचरं पतत्रिणम् (पुनरेति) R. 8. 56, 9. 27, 11. 11, 12. 48;<BR> Ku. 5. 4.<BR>—2 An arrow; अभिजग्राह सौमित्रिर्विनद्योभौ पतत्रिभिः Mb. 3. 287. 22.<BR>—3 A horse; esp. in Aśvamedha sacrifice; पतत्रिणा तदा सार्धम् Rām. 1. 14. 34;<BR> पतत्रिणस्तस्य वपामुद्धृत्य नियतेन्द्रियः 36. ━<i>n.</i><BR> (dual) Ved. Day and night; मामिमे पतत्रिणी वि दुग्धाम् Rv. 1. 158. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतत्रिकेतनः, पतत्रिराजः, पतत्रिवरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिकेतनः|पतत्रिकेतन
पतत्रिन् + -केतनः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिराजः|पतत्रिराज
पतत्रिन् + -राजः, -वरः N. of Garuḍa; Mb. 7. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिवरः|पतत्रिवर
पतत्रिन् + -राजः, -वरः N. of Garuḍa; Mb. 7. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतनम्
पतनम् [पत्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of flying or coming down, alighting, descending, throwing oneself down at.<BR>—2 Setting (as of the sun).<BR>—3 Going down to hell; निरये चैव पतनम् Ms. 6. 61.<BR>—4 Apostacy.<BR>—5 Falling from dignity, virtue &c. अनिग्रहाच्चेन्द्रियाणां नरः पतनमृच्छति Y. 3. 219.<BR>—6 Fall, decline, ruin, adversity (opp. उदय or उच्छ्राय); ग्रहाधीना<BR> नरेन्द्राणामुच्छ्रायाः पतनानि च Y. 1. 308.<BR>—7 Death.<BR>—8 Hanging down, becoming flaccid (as breasts).<BR>—9 Miscarriage.<BR>—10 (In arith.) Subtraction.<BR>—11 The latitude of a planet.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतनधर्मिन्, पतनशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतनधर्मिन्
पतनम् + -धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> subject to the law of decay, perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतनशील
पतनम् + -शील <i>a.</i> accustomed to fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतनीय
पतनीय <i>a.</i> Causing a fall, causing the loss of caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतनीयम्
पतनीय + .{@-यम्@} A degrading crime or sin; लाक्षालवणमांसानि पतनीयानि<BR> विक्रये Y. 3. 40. नीचाभिगमनं गर्भपातनं भर्तृहिंसनम् । विशेषपतनीयानि<BR> स्त्रीणामेतान्यपि ध्रुवम् ॥ 297; Mb. 7. 156. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतमः|पतम
पतमः, पतसः<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 A bird.<BR>—3 A grasshopper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतसः|पतस
पतमः, पतसः<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 A bird.<BR>—3 A grasshopper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतयालु|पतयालुः
पतयालु <i>a.</i> Tending or prone to fall, liable to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतापत
पतापत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going, or inclined to fall.<BR>—2 Going much or frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित|पतितः
पतित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen, descended, alighted.<BR>—2 Dropped.<BR>—3 Fallen (in a moral sense), abandoned, wicked; नष्टे मृते प्रव्रजिते<BR> क्लीबे च पतिते पतौ ।<BR>—4 Apostate.<BR>—5 Degraded, outcast.<BR>—6 Fallen in battle, defeated or overthrown.<BR>—7 Being in, fallen into; as in अवंशपतित.<BR>—8 Placed, kept; निक्षेपे पतिते हर्म्ये श्रेष्ठी स्तौति स्वदेवताम् Pt. 1. 14.<BR>—9 (with पादयोः or पाद-) Having thrown oneself at (a personʼs feet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितम्
पतित + .{@-तम्@} Flying.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतितोत्पन्न, पतितगर्भा, पतितमूर्धज, पतितवृत्त, पतितसावित्रीकः, पतितस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितोत्पन्न
पतित + -उत्पन्न <i>a.</i> sprung from an outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितगर्भा
पतित + -गर्भा a woman who miscarries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितमूर्धज
पतित + -मूर्धज <i>a.</i> one whose hair has fallen out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितवृत्त
पतित + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> one leading a life of an out-cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितसावित्रीकः|पतितसावित्रीक
पतित + -सावित्रीकः a man of the first three classes whose thread-ceremony<BR> has been improperly performed, or not performed at all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितस्थित
पतित + -स्थित <i>a.</i> lying on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतेर|पतेरः
पतेर <i>a.</i> [पत्-एर]<BR>—1 Flying, falling.<BR>—2 Going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतेरः|पतेर
पतेर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A bird.<BR>—2 A hole or pit.<BR>—3 A kind of measure (आढक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्मन्
पत्मन् <i>n.</i> Ved. Flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्वन्
पत्वन् <i>n.</i> Ved. Flying, flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्चिका|पतंचिका
पतञ्चिका A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकः|पताक
पताकः<BR>—1 पताका q. v.<BR>—2 A particular position of the hands or fingers in shooting of an arrow;<BR> cf. त्रिपताक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताका
पताका<BR>—1 A flag, banner (fig. also); पताकाभिर्वरार्हाभिर्ध्वजैश्च समलंकृताम्<BR> Rām. 2. 7. 3; यं काममञ्जरी कामयते स हरतु सुभगपताकाम् Dk. 47<BR> ‘let him carry the palm of beauty or good fortune’.<BR>—2 A flag-staff.<BR>—3 A sign, emblem, mark, symbol.<BR>—4 An episode or episodical incident in a drama; see पताकास्थानक below.<BR>—5 Auspiciousness, good fortune or luck.<BR>—6 Celebrity, publicity; रम्या इति प्राप्तवतीः पताकाः Śi. 3. 53<BR> (com. ‘अन्यत्र रम्या इत्येवं पताकाः प्राप्तवतीः । प्रसिद्धिं गता इत्यर्थः ।’).<BR>—7 A particular high number; तत्र शङ्कुपताके द्वे युगान्तं कल्पमेव<BR> च Mb. 13. 107. 63.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पताकांशुकम्, पताकादण्डः, पताकास्थानकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकांशुकम्
पताका + -अंशुकम् a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकादण्डः|पताकादण्ड
पताका + -दण्डः a flag-staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकास्थानकम्
पताका + -स्थानकम् (in dramaturgy) intimation of an episodical incident,<BR> when instead of the thing thought of or expected, another of the same<BR> character is brought in by some unexpected circumstance (यत्रार्थे चिन्तितेऽन्यस्मिंस्तल्लिङ्गोऽन्यः<BR> प्रयुज्यते । आगन्तुकेन भावेन पताकास्थानकं तु तत् ॥ S. D. 299; for<BR> its different kinds, see 300-304).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकिक
पताकिक <i>a.</i> Having or carrying a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकिन्
पताकिन् <i>a.</i> Having or carrying a banner, adorned with flags. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An ensign, standard-bearer.<BR>—2 A flag.<BR>—3 A scheme or figure for casting a nativity.<BR>—4 A chariot; क्षितिरेणुकेतुवसनाः पताकिनः Śi. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकिनी
पताकिन् + .{@-नी@} An army; (न प्रसेहे) रथवर्त्मरजोऽप्यस्य कुत एव<BR> पताकिनीम् R. 4. 82; Ki. 14. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिः|पति
पतिः [पा-डति]<BR>—1 A master, lord; as in गृहपतिः.<BR>—2 An owner, possessor, proprietor; क्षेत्रपतिः.<BR>—3 Governor, ruler, one who presides over; ओषधीपतिः, वनस्पतिः, कुलपतिः &c.<BR>—4 A husband; प्रमदाः पतिवर्त्मगा इति प्रतिपन्नं हि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">Page0957-1</a>]<BR> विचेतनैरपि Ku. 4. 33.<BR>—5 A root.<BR>—6 Going, motion, fight. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 A female possessor, a mistress.<BR>—2 A wife.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पतिघातिनी, पतिघ्नी, पतिदेवता, पतिदेवा, पतिधर्मः, पतिप्राणा, पतिलङ्घनम्, पतिवेदनः, पतिलोकः, पतिव्रता, पतिसेवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0956-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघातिनी
पतिः + -घातिनी, -घ्नी<BR>—1 a woman who murders her husband.<BR>—2 a line on the hand showing that a woman will be faithless to her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघ्नी
पतिः + -घातिनी, -घ्नी<BR>—1 a woman who murders her husband.<BR>—2 a line on the hand showing that a woman will be faithless to her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिदेवता
पतिः + -देवता, -देवा one who regards her husband as a divinity, a woman<BR> loyally devoted to her husband, a chaste woman; कः पतिदेवतामन्यः<BR> परिमार्ष्टुमुत्सहते Ś. 6; तमलभन्त पतिं पतिदेवताः शिखरिणामिव<BR> सागरमापगाः R. 9. 17; धुरिस्थिता त्वं पतिदेवतानाम् 14. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिदेवा
पतिः + -देवता, -देवा one who regards her husband as a divinity, a woman<BR> loyally devoted to her husband, a chaste woman; कः पतिदेवतामन्यः<BR> परिमार्ष्टुमुत्सहते Ś. 6; तमलभन्त पतिं पतिदेवताः शिखरिणामिव<BR> सागरमापगाः R. 9. 17; धुरिस्थिता त्वं पतिदेवतानाम् 14. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिधर्मः|पतिधर्म
पतिः + -धर्मः duty (of a wife) towards a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिप्राणा
पतिः + -प्राणा a chaste wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिलङ्घनम्
पतिः + -लङ्घनम् disregarding a former husband by marrying another; cf. Ms. 5. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवेदनः|पतिवेदन
पतिः + -वेदनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवेदनम्
पतिः + -वेदनः + .({@-नम्@}) procuring a husband (by magical means); धातुर्देवस्य<BR> सत्येन कृणोमि पतिवेदनम् Av. 2. 36. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिलोकः|पतिलोक
पतिः + -लोकः the world of husbands in a future life; पतिलोकमभीप्सन्ती<BR> नाचरेत् किंचिदप्रियम् Ms. 5. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिव्रता
पतिः + -व्रता a devoted, faithful and loyal wife, a chaste and virtuous<BR> wife; ˚त्वम् fidelity to a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिसेवा
पतिः + -सेवा devotion to a husband; वैवाहिको विधिः स्त्रीणां संस्कारो<BR> वैदिकः स्मृतः । पतिसेवा गुरौ वासो गृहार्थोऽग्निपरिक्रिया ॥ Ms. 2. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिंवरा
पतिंवरा A woman who is about to choose a husband; विवेश मञ्चान्तरराजमार्गं<BR> पतिंवरा कॢप्तविवाहवेषा R. 6. 10, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्वम्
पतित्वम्, -पतित्वनम् Ved.<BR>—1 Lordship.<BR>—2 The conjugal state, wedlock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्वनम्
पतित्वम्, -पतित्वनम् Ved.<BR>—1 Lordship.<BR>—2 The conjugal state, wedlock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिमती
पतिमती, -वती<BR> A woman having a husband; उदीर्ष्वातः पतिवती ह्येषा Rv.<BR>—10 85. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवती
पतिमती, -वती<BR> A woman having a husband; उदीर्ष्वातः पतिवती ह्येषा Rv.<BR>—10 85. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवत्नी
पतिवत्नी A wife whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतीयति
पतीयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To wish for a husband.<BR>—2 To become a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतीयन्ती|पतीयंती
पतीयन्ती A woman wishing or fit for a husband. प्राप्य चञ्चूर्यमाणासौ<BR> पतीयन्ती रघूत्तमम् Bk. 4. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्काषिन्
पत्काषिन् <i>m.</i> A foot-soldier; पत्काषिणस्तीर्थजलार्थमाशु Bk. 3. 4;<BR> मानुषो नाम पत्काषी राजानं पुरुषाशिनाम् Bk. 16. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नी
पत्नी —1 A wife; वृषेव पत्नीरभ्येति रोरुवत् Rv. 1. 140. 6; पत्नीमूलं<BR> गृहं पुंसां यदि छन्दोनुवर्तिनी, गृहाश्रमसमं नास्ति यदि भार्या वशानुगा ॥<BR> Dakṣasaṃhitā.<BR>—2 Ved. A mistress; पत्नी इति हि यज्ञस्य स्वामिनीति उच्यते, न कीता<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 17.<BR>—3 (in Astro.) N. of the 7th mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पत्न्याटः, पत्नीशाला, पत्नीसंनहनम्, पत्नीसंयाजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्न्याटः|पत्न्याट
पत्नी + -आटः seraglio, womenʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीशाला
पत्नी + -शाला a hut tent, room for wives and domestic purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीसंनहनम्
पत्नी + -संनहनम्<BR>—1 girdling a wife.<BR>—2 the girdle of a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीसंयाजः|पत्नीसंयाज
पत्नी + -संयाजः a particular sacrifice; पत्नीसंयाजावभृथ्यैश्चरित्वा<BR> ते तमृत्विजः Bhāg. 10. 75. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नीत्वम्
पत्नीत्वम्<BR>—1 Wifehood.<BR>—2 matrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित|पतितः
पतित See under पत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तनम्
पत्तनम् —1 A town, city (opp. ग्राम); पत्तने विद्यमानेऽपि<BR> ग्रामे रत्नपरीक्षा M. 1; एको वासः पत्तने वा वने वा Bh. 3. 120.<BR>—2 A musical instrument, मृदङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिः|पत्ति
पत्तिः [पद्-तिन्]<BR>—1 A footman, a foot-soldier; पत्तिः पदातिम् (अभ्यपतत्) R. 7. 37;<BR> Ve. 1. 27.<BR>—2 A pedestrian.<BR>—3 A hero. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 The smallest division of an army, consisting of one chariot, one elephant,<BR> three horsemen and five foot-soldiers; एको रथो गजश्चैको नराः पञ्च<BR> पदातयः । त्रयश्च तुरगास्तज्ज्ञैः पत्तिरित्यभिधीयते ॥ Mb. 1. 2. 19.<BR>—2 Going, walking.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पत्त्यध्यक्षः, पत्तिकायः, पत्तिगणकः, पत्तिसंहतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्त्यध्यक्षः
पत्तिः + -अध्यक्षः the superintendent of infantry; Kau. A. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिकायः|पत्तिकाय
पत्तिः + -कायः infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिगणकः|पत्तिगणक
पत्तिः + -गणकः an officer whose business it is to muster the infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिसंहतिः|पत्तिसंहति
पत्तिः + -संहतिः <i>f.</i> a body of infantry, infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिक
पत्तिक <i>a.</i> Going on foot, pedestrian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिन्
पत्तिन् <i>m.</i> A foot-soldier, foot-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रम्
पत्रम् [पत्-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 A leaf (of a tree); पत्रं पुष्पं फलं तोयं यो मे भक्त्या प्रयच्छति<BR> Bg. 9. 26; धत्ते भरं कुसुमपत्रफलावलीनाम् Bv. 1. 94.<BR>—2 The leaf of a flower, lotus &c.; नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया Ś. 1. 18.<BR>—3 A leaf for writing upon, a paper, a leaf written upon; सुरवरतरुशाखा<BR> लेखनी पत्रमुर्वी Śivamahimna 32. पत्रमारोप्य दीयताम् Ś. 6 ‘commit to writing’<BR>, V. 2. 14.<BR>—4 A letter, document; विवादेऽन्विष्यते पत्रं पत्राभावे तु साक्षिणः Pt. 1. 403.<BR>—5 A challenge; आत्मनः पूजाख्यात्यर्थं गुणोत्कर्षप्रतिपादको लेखो यद्विपक्षोपरि<BR> दीयते तत्पत्रम् N. 7. 93; विद्याधर com.<BR>—6 Any thin leaf or plate of metal, a gold-leaf.<BR>—7 The wing of a bird, a pinion, feather of an arrow; यावद्वा मक्षिकायाः<BR> पत्रम् Bṛ. Up. 3. 3. 2; R. 2. 31; सद्यः प्रवालोद्गमचारुपत्रे नीते<BR> समाप्तिं नवचूतबाणे Ku. 3. 27.<BR>—8 A vehicle in general (car, horse, camel &c.); दिशः पपात पत्रेण<BR> वेगनिष्कम्पकेतुना R. 15. 84; N. 3. 16; Mb. 12. 67. 25; Śi. 12. 2.<BR>—9 Painting the person (particularly the face) with musk, sandal-juice<BR> or other fragrant substances; रचय कुचयोः पत्रं चित्रं कुरुष्व कपोलयोः<BR> Gīt. 12; R. 13. 55.<BR>—10 The blade of a sword, knife &c.<BR>—11 A knife, dagger.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पत्राङ्गम्, पत्राङ्गुलिः, पत्राञ्जनम्, पत्राढ्यम्, पत्रालम्बनम्, पत्रारूढ, पत्रावलिः, पत्रावली, पत्राहारः, पत्रोर्णम्, पत्रोल्लासः, पत्रकाहला, पत्रकृच्छ्रम्, पत्रगर्भा, पत्रघना, पत्रझङ्कारः, पत्रतण्डुला, पत्रदारकः, पत्रनाडिका, पत्रन्यासः, पत्रपरशुः, पत्रपालः, पत्रपाश्या, पत्रपिशाचिका, पत्रपुटम्, पत्रपुष्पा, पत्रबन्धः, पत्रबालः, पत्रवालः, पत्रभङ्गः, पत्रभङ्गिः, पत्रभङ्गी, पत्रमालः, पत्रयौवनम्, पत्ररञ्जनम्, पत्ररथः, पत्रलता, पत्ररेखा, पत्रलेखा, पत्रवल्लरी, पत्रवल्लिः, पत्रवल्ली, पत्रवाज, पत्रवाहः, पत्रविशेषकः, पत्रवेष्टः, पत्रशाकः, पत्रशिरा, पत्रश्रेष्ठः, पत्रसूचिः, पत्रहिमम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्गम्
पत्रम् + -अङ्गम्<BR>—1 the Bhūrja tree.<BR>—2 red sanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्गुलिः|पत्राङ्गुलि|पत्रांगुलि
पत्रम् + -अङ्गुलिः drawing lines of painting with the finger on the person<BR> (throat, forehead &c.) with coloured sandal, saffron, or any other fragrant substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राञ्जनम्
पत्रम् + -अञ्जनम्<BR>—1 ink.<BR>—2 blacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राढ्यम्
पत्रम् + -आढ्यम् the root of long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रालम्बनम्
पत्रम् + -आलम्बनम् a challenge; cf. पत्रालम्बनं करोति ‘to challenge to a controversy’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रारूढ
पत्रम् + -आरूढ <i>a.</i> written down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावलिः|पत्रावलि
पत्रम् + -आवलिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 red chalk.<BR>—2 a row of leaves.<BR>—3 the lines of painting drawn on the body with cosmetics as a decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावली
पत्रम् + -आवली<BR>—1 a row of leaves.<BR>—2 = ˚आवलि (3).<BR>—3 mixture of young Aśvattha leaves with barley and honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राहारः|पत्राहार
पत्रम् + -आहारः feeding on leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोर्णम्
पत्रम् + -ऊर्णम् wove-silk, a sik-garment; स्नानीयवस्त्रक्रियया पत्रोर्णं<BR> वोपयुज्यते M. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोल्लासः|पत्रोल्लास
पत्रम् + -उल्लासः the bud or eye of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकाहला
पत्रम् + -काहला the noise or sound made by the flapping of wings or rustling of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकृच्छ्रम्
पत्रम् + -कृच्छ्रम् a sort of penance, drinking the infusion of leaves of<BR> various plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगर्भा
पत्रम् + -गर्भा a small cake with very thin layers inside (Mar. चिरोटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रघना
पत्रम् + -घना a plant with full leaves (सातल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रझङ्कारः|पत्रझङ्कार|पत्त्रझङ्कार
पत्रम् + -झङ्कारः the current of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रतण्डुला
पत्रम् + -तण्डुला a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रदारकः|पत्रदारक
पत्रम् + -दारकः a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रनाडिका
पत्रम् + -नाडिका the fibre of a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रन्यासः|पत्रन्यास
पत्रम् + -न्यासः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">Page0958-1</a>]<BR> inserting feathers (into an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0957-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपरशुः|पत्रपरशु
पत्रम् + -परशुः a file.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपालः|पत्रपाल
पत्रम् + -पालः a long dagger, large knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाली
पत्रम् + -पालः + .({@-ली@})<BR>—1 the feathered part of an arrow.<BR>—2 a pair or scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाश्या
पत्रम् + -पाश्या an ornament (a gold-leaf) on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपिशाचिका
