पत्रम् + -भङ्गः, -भङ्गिः, -भङ्गी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 drawing lines or figures of painting on the face and person with fragrant<BR> and coloured substances, such as musk, saffron, sandal-juice, yellow pigment<BR> &c., as a mark of decoration; कस्तूरीवरपत्रभङ्गनिकरो मृष्टो न गण्डस्थले<BR> Ś. Til. 7 (used frequently in K.).<BR>—2 leaves or leafy branches fed to elephants; Mātaṅga L. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0958-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

