पद्म + -लाञ्छनः + .({@-ना@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Lakṣmī, the goddess of wealth.<BR>—2 or of Sarasvatī, the goddess of learning.<BR>—3 N. of Tārā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवनबान्धवः|पद्मवनबान्धव
पद्म + -वनबान्धवः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवर्चस्
पद्म + -वर्चस् <i>a.</i> lotus-hued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवासा
पद्म + -वासा an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मसमासनः|पद्मसमासन
पद्म + -समासनः an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मस्नुषा
पद्म + -स्नुषा<BR>—1 an epithet of Gaṅgā.<BR>—2 of Lakṣmī.<BR>—3 of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्महस्तः|पद्महस्त
पद्म + -हस्तः a particular measure of length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्महासः|पद्महास
पद्म + -हासः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकम्
पद्मकम्<BR>—1 An army arrayed in the form of a lotus-flower.<BR>—2 The coloured spots on the trunk and face of an elephant.<BR>—3 A particular posture in sitting.<BR>—4 A kind of wood (of Cerasus Puddum); Rām. 2. 76. 16; Mb. 4.<BR>—5 N. of a particular constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकिन्
पद्मकिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An elephant.<BR>—2 The <i>Bhūrja</i> or birch tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मशः
पद्मशः <i>ind.</i> By thousands of trillions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावती
पद्मावती<BR>—1 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 N. of a river; Māl. 9. 1.<BR>—3 The goddess Manasā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिन्
पद्मिन् <i>a.</i> [पद्म-इनि]<BR>—1 Possessing lotuses.<BR>—2 Spotted; शतं गजानामपि पद्मिनां तथा Mb. 1. 198. 16. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An elephant; पद्मीशनाथैः परिशीलनीया लक्ष्मीव संभाति नरेन्द्र<BR> ते सभा Sūkti. 5. 30.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0961-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनी
पद्मिनी<BR>—1 The lotus plant; पद्मिनी नक्तमुन्निद्रा Kāv. 4. 45; सुरगज<BR> इव बिभ्रत् पद्मिनीं दन्तलग्नाम् Ku. 3. 76; R. 16. 68; Me. 83; M. 2. 13;<BR> निरास भृङ्गं कुपितेव पद्मिनी Bk. 2. 6.<BR>—2 An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>—3 A pond or lake abounding in lotuses; पुष्पैश्चान्यैः परिक्षिप्तं पद्मिन्या<BR> च सपद्मया Rām. 3. 1. 6; क्षीणतोयानिलार्काभ्यां हतत्विडिव पद्मिनी ।<BR> बभूव पाण्डवी सेना तव पुत्रस्य तेजसा ॥ Mb. 7. 153. 20.<BR>—4 The fibrous stalk of a lotus.<BR>—5 A female elephant.<BR>—6 A woman of the first of the four classes into which writers on erotical<BR> science divide women; the रतिमञ्जरी thus defines her:− भवति<BR> कमलनेत्रा नासिकाक्षुद्ररन्ध्रा अविरलकुचयुग्मा चारुकेशी कृशाङ्गी । मृदुवचनसुशीला<BR> गीतवाद्यानुरक्ता सकलतनुसुवेशा पद्मिनी पद्मगन्धा ॥<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पद्मिनीशः, पद्मिनीकान्तः, पद्मिनीवल्लभः, पद्मिनीकण्टकः, पद्मिनीखण्डम्, पद्मिनीषण्डम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीशः|पद्मिनीश
पद्मिनी + -ईशः, -कान्तः, -वल्लभः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीकान्तः|पद्मिनीकान्त|पद्मिनीकांत
पद्मिनी + -ईशः, -कान्तः, -वल्लभः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीवल्लभः|पद्मिनीवल्लभ
पद्मिनी + -ईशः, -कान्तः, -वल्लभः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीकण्टकः|पद्मिनीकण्टक
पद्मिनी + -कण्टकः a^1 kind of leprosy.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीखण्डम्
पद्मिनी + -खण्डम्, -षण्डम् a multitude of lotuses; a place abounding in lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीषण्डम्
पद्मिनी + -खण्डम्, -षण्डम् a multitude of lotuses; a place abounding in lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मेशयः|पद्मेशय
पद्मेशयः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्य|पद्यं|पद्यः
पद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Consisting of Padas or lines.<BR>—2 Measuring a <i>pada</i>.<BR>—3 Belonging to the foot; श्रीविष्णुपद्या मनुजस्तुलस्याः श्वसन् शवो<BR> यस्तु न वेद गन्धम् Bhāg. 2. 3. 23.<BR>—4 Marked with footsteps.<BR>—5 Belonging to a word.<BR>—6 Final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्यः|पद्य|पद्यं
पद्य + .{@-द्यः@}<BR>—1 A Śūdra.<BR>—2 A part of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्या
पद्य + .{@-द्या@}<BR>—1 A footpath, path, way.<BR>—2 Sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्यम्
पद्य + .{@-द्यम्@}<BR>—1 A stanza or verse (consisting of four lines); मदीयपद्यरत्नानां<BR> मञ्जूषैषा मया कृता Bv. 4. 45; पद्यं चतुष्पदी तच्च वृत्तं जातिरिति<BR> द्विधा Chand. M. 2.<BR>—2 Praise, panegyric (स्तुति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्रः|पद्र
पद्रः<BR>—1 A village.<BR>—2 A village road.<BR>—3 The earth.<BR>—4 N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्वः|पद्व
पद्वः, -द्वम्<BR>—1 The world of human beings (भूलोक).<BR>—2 A car.<BR>—3 A road; (also पद्वन् in this sense).<BR>—4 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्वम्
पद्वः, -द्वम्<BR>—1 The world of human beings (भूलोक).<BR>—2 A car.<BR>—3 A road; (also पद्वन् in this sense).<BR>—4 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्
पन् €1 U. (पनायति-ते, पनायित or पनित)<BR>—1 To praise, extol; cf. पण्.<BR>—2 (Ātm.) To rejoice at, be glad of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनस्यति
पनस्यति Den. P. To be admirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनस्यु
पनस्यु <i>a.</i> Showing oneʼs self worthy of admiration; glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनायित
पनायित, -पनित <i>a.</i><BR> Praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनित
पनायित, -पनित <i>a.</i><BR> Praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनुः|पनु
पनुः (-नूः Ved.)<BR> Admiration, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनूः
पनुः (-नूः Ved.)<BR> Admiration, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसः|पनस
पनसः<BR>—1 The bread-fruit or jack tree.<BR>—2 A thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसा
पनसः + .{@-सा, -सी@}<BR>—1 A kind of malady, pustular and phlegmonoid inflammation of the skin<BR> or external organs.<BR>—2 A female monkey.<BR>—3 A female demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसी
पनसः + .{@-सा, -सी@}<BR>—1 A kind of malady, pustular and phlegmonoid inflammation of the skin<BR> or external organs.<BR>—2 A female monkey.<BR>—3 A female demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसम्
पनसः + .{@-सम्@} The fruit of the bread-fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसिका
पनसिका Pustules on the ears and neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्थ्
पन्थ् €1. €10 P. To go, to travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्थक|पंथक
पन्थक <i>a.</i> Produced in or on the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्न|पन्नं|पन्नः
पन्न, पन्नग See under पद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नग|पन्नगः
पन्न, पन्नग See under पद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपिः|पपि
पपिः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपी
पपी <i>m.</i> [cf. Uṇ. 3. 159]<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपु|पपुः
पपु <i>a.</i> Fostering, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपुः|पपु
पपु + .{@-पुः@} <i>f.</i> A foster-mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पम्पा|पंपा
पम्पा<BR>—1 N. of a lake in the Daṇḍakā forest; इदं च पम्पाभिधानं सरः<BR> U. 1; R. 13. 30; Bk. 6. 73.<BR>—2 N. of a river in the south of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पय्
पय् €1 Ā. (पयते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्
पयस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Water; Bhāg. 8. 2. 4; पयसा कमलं कमलेन पयः पयसा कमलेन<BR> विभाति सरः.<BR>—2 Milk; पयःपानं भुजङ्गानां केवलं विषवर्धनम् H. 3. 4; R. 2. 36, 63, 14. 78<BR> (where both senses are intended).<BR>—3 Semen virile.<BR>—4 Food.<BR>—5 Ved. Night.<BR>—6 Vital spirit, power, strength (Ved.). (पयस् is changed to पयो<BR> before soft consonants).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पयोगलः, पयोगडः, पयोघनम्, पयश्चयः, पयोजम्, पयोजन्मन्, पयोदः, पयोधरः, पयोधस्, पयोधारागृहम्, पयोधिः, पयोनिधिः, पयःपूरः, पयोभृत्, पयोमानुषी, पयोरयः, पयोराशिः, पयोवाहः, पयोव्रतः, पयोव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोगलः|पयोगल
पयस् + -गलः, -गडः<BR>—1 hail.<BR>—2 an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोगडः|पयोगड
पयस् + -गलः, -गडः<BR>—1 hail.<BR>—2 an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोघनम्
पयस् + -घनम् hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयश्चयः|पयश्चय
पयस् + -चयः (पयश्चयः) a reservoir or lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोजम्
पयस् + -जम् a lotus; पातामेतौ पयोजोदरललिततलौ पङ्कजाक्षस्य पादौ ।<BR> विष्णुपादादि स्तोत्रम् 12. ˚योनिः (same as पद्मयोनि = Brahmadeva);<BR> पयोजयोनिः प्रणिधाय मानसं व्यधत्त यस्यामरविन्दलोचनः Śāhendra. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोजन्मन्
पयस् + -जन्मन् <i>m.</i> a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोदः|पयोद
पयस् + -दः a cloud; Me. 7; मत्तः सदाचारशुचे कलङ्कः पयोदवातादिव<BR> दर्पणस्य R. 14. 37. ˚सुहृद् <i>m.</i> a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधरः|पयोधर
पयस् + -धरः<BR>—1 a cloud; पयोधरघनीभावस्तावदम्बरमध्यगः । आश्लेषोपगमस्तत्र<BR> यावन्नेव प्रवर्तते ॥ Subh. Ratn. (this refers both to a cloud and<BR> a womanʼs breast).<BR>—2 a womanʼs breast; पद्मापयोधरतटी Gīt. 1; विपाण्डुभिर्म्लानतया<BR> पयोधरैः Ki. 4. 24. (where the word means ‘a cloud’ also); R. 14. 22.<BR>—3 an udder; पयोधरीभूतचतुःसमुद्रां जुगोप गोरूपधरामिवोर्वीम् R. 2. 3.<BR>—4 the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—5 the backbone or spine (कशेरुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधस्
पयस् + -धस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the ocean.<BR>—2 a pond, lake, a piece of water.<BR>—3 a rain-cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधारागृहम्
पयस् + -धारागृहम् a bath-room with flowing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधिः|पयोधि
पयस् + -धिः, -निधिः the ocean; प्रयान्ति नद्यस्त्वरितं पयोनिधिम्<BR> Ṛs. 2. 7; N. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोनिधिः|पयोनिधि
पयस् + -धिः, -निधिः the ocean; प्रयान्ति नद्यस्त्वरितं पयोनिधिम्<BR> Ṛs. 2. 7; N. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयःपूरः|पयःपूर
पयस् + -पूरः a pool, lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोभृत्
पयस् + -भृत् <i>m.</i>, {@-मुच्@} <i>m.</i><BR> a cloud; यदि नासारभृतः पयोभृतः Śi. 16. 61;<BR> करीव सिक्तं पृषतैः पयोमुचाम् R. 3. 3, 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोमानुषी
पयस् + -मानुषी a water-nymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोरयः|पयोरय
पयस् + -रयः the current of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोराशिः|पयोराशि
पयस् + -राशिः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोवाहः|पयोवाह
पयस् + -वाहः a cloud; प्रावृषेण्यं पयोवाहं विद्युदैरावताविव R. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोव्रतः|पयोव्रत
पयस् + -व्रतः, -व्रतम् subsisting on mere milk (as a vow); दिनमेकं<BR> पयोव्रतः Ms. 11. 144. cf. अदितिपयोव्रतम् Bhāg. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोव्रतम्
पयस् + -व्रतः, -व्रतम् subsisting on mere milk (as a vow); दिनमेकं<BR> पयोव्रतः Ms. 11. 144. cf. अदितिपयोव्रतम् Bhāg. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्य|पयस्यं|पयस्यः
पयस्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Milky, made of milk.<BR>—2 Watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्यः|पयस्य|पयस्यं
पयस्य + .{@-स्यः@} A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्या
पयस्य + .{@-स्या@} Curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्यति
पयस्यति, पयायते Den. P. To flow, to act like milk; कामं<BR> मदीक्षामयकामधेनोः पयायतामभ्युदयस्त्वदीयः N. 14. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयायते
पयस्यति, पयायते Den. P. To flow, to act like milk; कामं<BR> मदीक्षामयकामधेनोः पयायतामभ्युदयस्त्वदीयः N. 14. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्वल|पयस्वलः
पयस्वल <i>a.</i> Rich in milk, yielding copious milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्वलः|पयस्वल
पयस्वल + .{@-लः@} A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्विन्
पयस्विन् <i>a.</i> Milky, juicy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्विनी
पयस्विन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A milch-cow; प्रदक्षिणीकृत्य पयस्विनीं ताम् R. 2. 21, 54, 65.<BR>—2 A river.<BR>—3 A she-goat.<BR>—4 Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधिकम्
पयोधिकम् The cuttle-fish bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोरः|पयोर
पयोरः The Khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0962-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोष्णी
पयोष्णी N. of a river rising in the Vindhya mountain (identified<BR> by some with the modern Tāptī river, but more correctly with Purṇā,<BR> a feeder of that river).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पयोष्णीजाता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोष्णीजाता
पयोष्णी + -जाता (पयोष्णी जाता यस्याः सा) an epithet of the river Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर|परं|परः
पर <i>a.</i> [पॄ-भावे-अप्, कर्तरि अच्-वा] (Declined optionally<BR> like a pronoun in nom. voc. pl., and abl. and loc. sing. when it denotes<BR> relative position)<BR>—1 Other, different, another; see पर <i>m.</i> also.<BR>—2 Distant, removed, remote; अपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः Bg. 4. 4.<BR>—3 Beyond, further, on the other side of; म्लेच्छदेशस्ततः परः Ms. 2. 23, 7 158.<BR>—4 Subsequent, following, next to, future, after (usually with abl.);<BR> बाल्यात् परामिव दशां मदनोऽध्युवास R. 5. 63; Ku. 1. 31.<BR>—5 Higher, superior; सिकतात्वादपि परां प्रपेदे परमाणुताम् R. 15. 22;<BR> इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः । मनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो<BR> बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः ॥ Bg. 3. 42.<BR>—9 Highest, greatest, most distinguished, pre-eminent, chief, best, principal;<BR> क्षत्रात् परं नास्ति Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11. न त्वया द्रष्टव्यानां परं<BR> दृष्टम् Ś. 2; Ki. 5. 18; परतोऽपि परः Ku. 2. 14<BR> ‘higher than the highest’; 6. 19; Ś. 7. 27.<BR>—7 Having as a following letter or sound, followed by (in comp.).<BR>—8 Alien, estranged, stranger.<BR>—9 Hostile, inimical, adverse,<BR>—10 Exceeding, having a surplus or remainder, left over; as in परं<BR> शतम् exceeding or more than a hundred.<BR>—11 Final, last.<BR>—12 (At the end of comp.) Having anything as the highest<BR> object, absorbed or engrossed in, intent on, solely devoted to, wholly<BR> engaged or occupied in; परिचर्यापरः R. 1. 91; so ध्यानपर, शोकपर,<BR> दैवपर, चिन्तापर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परः|पर|परं
पर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Another person, a stranger, foreigner; oft. in pl. in this sense; यतः<BR> परेषां गुणग्रहीतासि Bv. 1. 9; Śi. 20. 74; see एक, अन्य also.<BR>—2 A foe, an enemy, adversary; उत्तिष्ठमानस्तु परो नोपेक्ष्यः पथ्यमिच्छता<BR> Śi. 2. 10; Pt. 2. 158; R. 3. 21.<BR>—3 The Almighty; तावदध्यासते लोकं परस्य परचिन्तकाः Bhāg. 3. 32. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्
पर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The highest point or pitch, culminating point.<BR>—2 The Supreme Spirit; तेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत् परम् Bg. 5. 16.<BR>—3 Final beatitude; असक्तो ह्याचरन् कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः Bg. 3. 19.<BR>—4 The secondary meaning of a word.<BR>—5 (In logic) One of the two kinds of सामान्य or generality of notion;<BR> more extensive kind, (comprehending more objects); <i>e. g.</i> (पृथ्वी<BR> is पर with respect to a घट).<BR>—6 The other or future world; परासक्ते च वस्तस्मिन् कथमासीन्मनस्तदा<BR> Mb. 6. 14. 55. <i>Note</i>:− The acc., instr. and loc. singulars of पर<BR> are used adverbially; <i>e. g.</i><BR>——(<i>a</i>) परम्<BR>—1 beyond, over, out of (with abl.); वर्त्मनः परम् R. 1. 17.<BR>—2 after (with abl.); अस्मात् परम् Ś. 6. 24; R. 1. 66, 3. 39; Me. 102;<BR> भाग्यायत्तमतः परम् Ś. 4. 17; ततः परम् &c.<BR>—3 thereupon, thereafter.<BR>—4 but, however.<BR>—5 otherwise.<BR>—6 in a high degree, excessively, very much, completely, quite; परं<BR> दुःखितोऽस्मि &c.<BR>—7 most willingly.<BR>—8 only.<BR>—9 at the utmost.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) परेण<BR>—1 farther, beyond, more than; किं वा मृत्योः परेण विधास्यति Māl. 2. 2.<BR>—2 afterwards; मयि तु कृतनिधाने किं विदध्याः परेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">Page0963-2</a>]<BR> Mv. 2. 49.<BR>—3 after (with abl.) स्तन्यत्यागात् परेण U. 2. 7.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) परे<BR>—1 afterwards, thereupon; अथ तेन दशाहतः परे R. 8. 73.<BR>—2 in future.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पराङ्गम्, पराङ्गदः, पराणुः, परादनः, पराधिकारचर्चा, पराधीन, परान्तः, परान्तकः, परान्तकालः, परान्न, परापर, पराभिध्यानम्, परामृतम्, परायण, परार्थ, परार्थिन्, परार्धम्, परार्धक, परार्ध्य, परावर, परावसथशायिन्, पराहः, पराह्णः, परागमः, पराचित, परात्मन्, परायत्त, परायुस्, पराविद्धः, पराश्रय, परासङ्गः, परास्कन्दिन्, परेतर, परेशः, परेष्टिः, परेष्टुका, परोत्कर्षः, परोद्वहः, परोपकारः, परोपकारिन्, परोपजापः, परोपदेशः, परोपरुद्ध, परोपसर्पणम्, परोढा, परैधित, परकर्मन्, परकलत्रम्, परकायप्रवेशनम्, परकारः, परकार्यम्, परकाल, परकृतिः, परक्रमः, परक्रान्तिः, परक्षेत्रम्, परगामिन्, परगुण, परग्रन्थिः, परग्लानिः, परचक्रम्, परच्छन्द, परच्छिद्रम्, परज, परजनः, परजन्मन्, परजात, परजित, परतन्त्र, परतन्त्रम्, परतर्ककः, परतल्पगामिन्, परतीर्थिकः, परदाराः, परदारिन्, परदुःखम्, परदेवता, परदेशः, परदेशिन्, परद्रोहिन्, परद्वेषिन्, परधनम्, परधर्मः, परध्यानम्, परनिपातः, परनिर्वाणम्, परपक्षः, परपदम्, परपरिग्रह, परपरिग्रहः, परपरिभवः, परपाकनिवृत्त, परपाकरत, परपाकरुचिः, परपिण्डः, परपुरञ्जयः, परपुरुषः, परपुष्ट, परपुष्टा, परपूर्वा, परप्रतिनप्तृ, परप्रपौत्रः, परप्रेष्यः, परब्रह्मन्, परभागः, परभाव, परभावः, परभाषा, परभुक्त, परभूत, परभृत्, परभृत, परभृतः, परता, परमतम्, परमर्मज्ञ, परमृत्युः, पररमणः, परलोकः, परवश, परवश्य, परवाच्यम्, परवाणिः, परवादः, परवादिन्, परवेश्मन्, परव्रतः, परशब्दः, परश्वस्, परसंगत, परसंज्ञकः, परसवर्ण, परसात्, परसेवा, परस्त्री, परस्वम्, परहन्, परहित, परतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गम्
पर + -अङ्गम् the hinder part of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गदः|पराङ्गद|परांगद
पर + -अङ्गदः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराणुः
पर + -अणुः See परमाणु; Bhāg. 10. 14. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादनः|परादन
पर + -अदनः a horse found in the country of Persia or Arabia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिकारचर्चा|पराधिकारचर्च्चा
पर + -अधिकारचर्चा officiousness, meddlesomeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीन|पराधीनः
पर + -अधीन <i>a.</i> dependent on another, subject, subservient; अन्नमेषां<BR> पराधीनं देयं स्याद्भिन्नभाजने Ms. 10. 54, 83; H. 1. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्तः|परान्त|परांत
पर + -अन्तः final death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्ताः
पर + -अन्तः + .({@-ताः@}) <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्तकः|परान्तक|परांतक
पर + -अन्तकः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a frontier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्तकालः|परान्तकाल
पर + -अन्तकालः the time of death; ते ब्रह्मलोकेषु परान्तकाले परामृताः<BR> परिमुच्यन्ति सर्वे Muṇḍ. 3. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्न|परान्नं|परान्नः
पर + -अन्न <i>a.</i> living or subsisting on anotherʼs food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्नम्
पर + -अन्न + .({@-न्नम्@}) the food of another; परगृहललिताः परान्नपुष्टाः<BR> Mk. 4. 28. ˚परिपुष्टता being fed with the food of others; Y. 3. 241.<BR> ˚भोजिन् <i>a.</i> subsisting on the food of others; रोगी चिरप्रवासी<BR> परान्नभोजी परावसथशायी । यज्जीवति तन्मरणं यन्मरणं सोऽस्य विश्रामः ॥<BR> H. 1. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापर|परापरं|परापरः
पर + -अपर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 far and near, remote and proximate.<BR>—2 prior and posterior.<BR>—3 before and beyond, earlier and later.<BR>—4 higher and lower, best and worst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापरः|परापर|परापरं
पर + -अपर + .({@-रः@}) a <i>Guru</i> of an intermediate class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापरम्
पर + -अपर + .({@-रम्@}) (in logic) a property intermediate between the greatest<BR> and smallest numbers, a species (as existing between the genus and individual);<BR> <i>e. g.</i> पृथ्वी which is पर with respect to a घट is अपर<BR> with respect to द्रव्य; द्रव्यत्वादिकजातिस्तु परापरतयोच्यते Bhāṣā P. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभिध्यानम्
पर + -अभिध्यानम् self-conceit; high opinion for self or body (देहाभिमान);<BR> स्वयं पराभिध्यानेन विभ्रंशितस्मृतिः Bhāg. 5. 14. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृतम्
पर + -अमृतम् rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायण|परायणं
पर + -अयण ({@अयन@}) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 attached or devoted to, adhering to.<BR>—2 depending on, subject to.<BR>—3 intent on, solely devoted to or absorbed in (at the end of comp.);<BR> प्रभुर्धनपरायणः Bh. 2. 56; so मोह˚; अथ मोहपरायणा सती विवशा<BR> कामवधूर्विबोधिता Ku. 4. 1; अग्निहोत्र˚ &c.<BR>—4 connected with.<BR>—5 being a protector (त्राता); अबर्हाश्चरणैर्हीनाः पूर्वेषां वः परायणाः Mb. 1. 230. 4.<BR>—6 leading or conducive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायणम्
पर + -अयण + .({@-णम्@})<BR>—1 the principal or highest object, chief aim, best or last resort; एतत्<BR> परायणम् Praśna. Up. 1. 10; तपसश्च परायणम् Rām. 1. 21. 10;<BR> Mb. 12. 179. 12.<BR>—2 essence, sum.<BR>—3 Ved. going away, departure, exit.<BR>—4 firm devotion.<BR>—5 a universal medicine, panacea.<BR>—6 a religious order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
पर + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having another aim or meaning.<BR>—2 intended or designed for another, done for another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थः|परार्थ
पर + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@})<BR>—1 the highest interest or advantage.<BR>—2 the interest of another (opp. स्वार्थ); स्वार्थो यस्य परार्थ एव<BR> स पुमानेकः सतामग्रणीः Subhāṣ.; R. 1. 29.<BR>—3 the chief or highest meaning.<BR>—4 the highest object (<i>i. e.</i> sexual intercourse).<BR>—5 the supreme good (मोक्ष); ज्ञात्वा प्रजहि कालेन परार्थमनुदृश्य<BR> च Mb. 12. 288. 9.<BR>—6 Something else. Hence परार्थता or परार्थत्व means ‘being subsidiary to something else’<BR>; परार्थता हि गुणभावः ŚB. on MS. 4. 3.<BR>—7 an object which is meant for anotherʼs use (Sāṅ. Phil.); सङ्घातपरार्थत्वात्<BR> त्रिगुणादिविपर्ययादधिष्ठानात् Sāṅ. K. 17. ˚वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking<BR> for another; mediator, substitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थिन्
पर + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> striving for the supreme good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थम्
पर + -अर्थिन् + .({@-र्थम्, -र्थे@})<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">Page0964-1</a>]<BR> <i>ind.</i> for the sake of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थे
पर + -अर्थिन् + .({@-र्थम्, -र्थे@})<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">Page0964-1</a>]<BR> <i>ind.</i> for the sake of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0963-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्धम्
पर + -अर्धम्<BR>—1 the other part (opp. पूर्वार्ध); the latter half; दिनस्य पूर्वार्धपरार्धभिन्ना<BR> छायेव मैत्री खलसज्जनानाम् Bh. 2. 60.<BR>—2 a particular high number; <i>i. e.</i> 100,000,000,000,000,000; एकत्वादिपरार्धपर्यन्ता संख्या T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्धक
पर + -अर्धक <i>a.</i> One half of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्ध्य
पर + -अर्ध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being on the farther side or half.<BR>—2 most distant in number; हेमन्तो वसन्तात् परार्ध्यः Śat. Br.<BR>—3 most excellent, best, most exalted, highly esteemed, highest, supreme;<BR> R. 3. 27, 8. 27, 10. 64, 16. 39; आबद्धप्रचुरपरार्ध्यकिंकिणीकः Śi. 8. 45.<BR>—4 most costly; Śi. 4. 11; श्रियं परार्ध्यां विदधद् विधातृभिः Bu. C. 1. 1.<BR>—5 most beautiful or lovely, finest; R. 6. 4; परस्परस्पर्धिपरार्ध्यरूपाः<BR> पौरस्त्रियो यत्र विधाय वेधाः Śi. 3. 58.<BR>—6 Divine: असावाटीत् सङ्ख्ये परार्ध्यवत् Bk. 9. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्ध्यम्
पर + -अर्ध्य + .({@-र्ध्यम्@})<BR>—1 a maximum.<BR>—2 an infinite number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर
पर + -अवर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 far and near; परावराणां स्रष्टारं पुराणं परमव्ययम् Mb. 1. 1. 23.<BR>—2 earlier and later.<BR>—3 prior and posterior or subsequent.<BR>—4 higher and lower.<BR>—5 traditional; पुनाति पङ्क्तिं वंश्यांश्च सप्त सप्त परावरान् Ms. 1. 105.<BR>—6 all-including; परावरज्ञोऽसि परावरस्त्वम् Mb. 3. 232. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावरा
पर + -अवर + .({@-रा@}) descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावरम्
पर + -अवर + .({@-रम्@})<BR>—1 cause and effect.<BR>—2 the whole extent of an idea.<BR>—3 the universe.<BR>—4 totality. ˚ज्ञ, ˚दृश् <i>a.</i> knowing both the past and the future;<BR> परावरज्ञो ब्रह्मर्षिः Mb. 1. 60. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावसथशायिन्
पर + -अवसथशायिन् <i>a.</i> sleeping in anotherʼs house; H. 1. 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहः|पराह
पर + -अहः the next day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह्णः|पराह्ण
पर + -अह्णः the afternoon, the latter part of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागमः|परागम
पर + -आगमः attack of an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचित|पराचितः
पर + -आचित <i>a.</i> fostered or brought up by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचितः|पराचित
पर + -आचित + .({@-तः@}) a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्मन्
पर + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायत्त|परायत्तं
पर + -आयत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dependent on another, subject, subservient; परायत्तः प्रीतेः कथमिव<BR> रसं वेत्तु पुरुषः Mu. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Wholly subdued or overwhelmed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायुस्
पर + -आयुस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman; नाहं परायुरृषयो न मरीचिमुख्या<BR> जानन्ति यद्विरचितं खलु सत्त्वसर्गाः Bhāg. 8. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराविद्धः|पराविद्ध
पर + -आविद्धः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रय|पराश्रयः
पर + -आश्रय <i>a.</i> dependent upon another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रयः|पराश्रय
पर + -आश्रय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 dependence upon another.<BR>—2 the retreat of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रया
पर + -आश्रय + .({@-या@}) a plant growing on another tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासङ्गः|परासङ्ग|परासंग
पर + -आसङ्गः dependence upon another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्कन्दिन्|परास्कंदिन्
पर + -आस्कन्दिन् <i>m.</i> a thief, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेतर
पर + -इतर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 other than inimical, <i>i. e.</i> friendly, kind.<BR>—2 oneʼs own; विधाय रक्षान् परितः परेतरान् Ki. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेशः|परेश
पर + -ईशः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टिः|परेष्टि
पर + -इष्टिः N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टुका
पर + -इष्टुका a cow which has often calved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोत्कर्षः|परोत्कर्ष
पर + -उत्कर्षः anotherʼs prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोद्वहः|परोद्वह
पर + -उद्वहः the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकारः|परोपकार
पर + -उपकारः doing good to others, benevolence, beneficence, charity;<BR> परोपकारः पुण्याय पापाय परपीडनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकारिन्
पर + -उपकारिन् <i>a.</i> benevolent, kind to others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपजापः|परोपजाप
पर + -उपजापः causing dissension among enemies; परोपजापात् संरक्षेत्<BR> प्रधानान् क्षुद्रकान् अपि Kau. A. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपदेशः|परोपदेश
पर + -उपदेशः advising others; परोपदेशे पाण्डित्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपरुद्ध
पर + -उपरुद्ध <i>a.</i> besieged by an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपसर्पणम्
पर + -उपसर्पणम् approaching another; begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोढा
पर + -ऊढा anotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परैधित|परैधितः
पर + -एधित <i>a.</i> fostered or brought up by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परैधितः|परैधित
पर + -एधित + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 a servant.<BR>—2 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकर्मन्
पर + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> service for another. ˚निरतः a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकलत्रम्
पर + -कलत्रम् anotherʼs wife. ˚अभिगमनम् adultery; वरं क्लैब्यं<BR> पुसां न च परकलत्राभिगमनम् H. 1. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकायप्रवेशनम्
पर + -कायप्रवेशनम् entering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">Page0964-2</a>]<BR> anotherʼs body (a supernatural art).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकारः|परकार
पर + -कारः The deeds of the enemy; राज्ञः समीपे परकारमाह प्रज्ञापनैषा<BR> विविधोपदिष्टा Kau. A. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकार्यम्
पर + -कार्यम् anotherʼs business or work. ˚निरतः<BR>—1 a benevolent man.<BR>—2 a slave, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकाल
पर + -काल <i>a.</i> relating to a later time, mentioned later.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकृतिः|परकृति
पर + -कृतिः an example or precedent, a passage descriptive of the doings<BR> of men; MS. 6. 7. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परक्रमः|परक्रम
पर + -क्रमः doubling the second letter of a conjunction of consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परक्रान्तिः|परक्रान्ति
पर + -क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> inclination of the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परक्षेत्रम्
पर + -क्षेत्रम्<BR>—1 anotherʼs body.<BR>—2 anotherʼs field; येऽक्षेत्रिणो बीजवन्तः परक्षेत्रप्रवापिणः । ते<BR> वै सस्यस्य जातस्य न लभन्ते फलं क्वचित् ॥ Ms. 9. 49.<BR>—3 anotherʼs wife; तौ तु जातौ परक्षेत्रे Ms. 3. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परगामिन्
पर + -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being with another.<BR>—2 relating to another.<BR>—3 beneficial to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परगुण|परगुणः
पर + -गुण <i>a.</i> beneficial to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परगुणः|परगुण
पर + -गुण + .({@-णः@}) the virtue of another; परगुणपरमाणून् पर्वतीकृत्य<BR> नित्यम् Bh. 2. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्रन्थिः|परग्रन्थि|परग्रंथि
पर + -ग्रन्थिः joint (as of a finger); an articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्लानिः|परग्लानि
पर + -ग्लानिः <i>f.</i> subjugation of an enemy; आत्मोदयः परग्लानिर्द्वयं<BR> नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परचक्रम्
पर + -चक्रम्<BR>—1 the army of an enemy.<BR>—2 invasion by an enemy, one of the six <i>itis</i> q. v.<BR>—3 a hostile prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परच्छन्द|परच्छंद|परच्छन्दः|परछन्द
पर + -छन्द <i>a.</i> dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परच्छन्दः|परच्छन्द|परच्छंद|परछन्द
पर + -छन्द + .({@-दः@})<BR>—1 the will of another.<BR>—2 dependence. ˚अनुवर्तनम् following the will of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परच्छिद्रम्
पर + -छिद्रम् a weak or vulnerable point of another, a defect in another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परज
पर + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 stranger.<BR>—2 coming from a foe.<BR>—3 inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजनः|परजन
पर + -जनः a stranger (opp. स्वजन); शक्तः परजने दाता Ms. 11. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजन्मन्
पर + -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> a future birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजात|परजातः
पर + -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 born of another.<BR>—2 dependent on another for livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजातः|परजात
पर + -जात + .({@-तः@}) a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजित|परजितः
पर + -जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 conquered by another.<BR>—2 maintained by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजितः|परजित
पर + -जित + .({@-तः@}) the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतन्त्र|परतंत्र|परतन्त्रः
पर + -तन्त्र <i>a.</i> dependent on another, dependent, subservient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतन्त्रम्
पर + -तन्त्रम् (a common group of) subsidiaries belonging to another;<BR> जैमिनेः परतन्त्रापत्तेः स्वतन्त्रप्रतिषेधः स्यात् MS. 12. 1. 8 (see तन्त्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतर्ककः|परतर्कक
पर + -तर्ककः a suppliant, beggar; Dānasāgara, Bibliotheca Indica, 274, Fascicule 1, p. 15;<BR> also परतर्कुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतल्पगामिन्
पर + -तल्पगामिन् <i>m.</i> One who approaches another manʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतीर्थिकः|परतीर्थिक
पर + -तीर्थिकः The adherent of another sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदाराः
पर + -दाराः <i>m.</i> (pl.) anotherʼs wife; ˚अभिगमनम्, ˚अभिमर्षः Adultery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदारिन्
पर + -दारिन् <i>m.</i> an adulterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदुःखम्
पर + -दुःखम् the sorrow or grief of another; विरलः परदुःखदुःखितो<BR> जनः; महदपि परदुःखं शीतलं सम्यगाहुः V. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेवता
पर + -देवता the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशः|परदेश
पर + -देशः a hostile or foreign country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशिन्
पर + -देशिन् <i>m.</i> a foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्रोहिन्
पर + -द्रोहिन्, -द्वेषिन् <i>a.</i> hating others, hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्वेषिन्
पर + -द्रोहिन्, -द्वेषिन् <i>a.</i> hating others, hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधनम्
पर + -धनम् anotherʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधर्मः|परधर्म|परधर्म्म
पर + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the religion of another; स्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः Bg. 3. 35.<BR>—2 anotherʼs duty or business.<BR>—3 the duties of another caste; परधर्मेण जीवन् हि सद्यः पतति जातितः Ms. 10. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परध्यानम्
पर + -ध्यानम् absolute meditation or contemplation; ध्येये मनो निश्चलतां<BR> याति ध्येयं विचिन्तयत् । यत् तद् ध्यानं परं प्रोक्तं मुनिभिर्ध्यानचिन्तकैः ॥<BR> Garuḍa P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परनिपातः|परनिपात
पर + -निपातः the irregular posteriority of a word in a compound; <i>i. e.</i><BR> भूतपूर्वः where the sense is पूर्वं भूतः; so राजदन्तः,<BR> अग्न्याहितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परनिर्वाणम्
पर + -निर्वाणम् the highest निर्वाण; (Buddh.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपक्षः|परपक्ष
पर + -पक्षः the side or party of an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपदम्
पर + -पदम्<BR>—1 the highest position, eminence.<BR>—2 final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपरिग्रह|परपरिग्रहः
पर + -परिग्रह <i>a.</i> see पराधीन; स्ववीर्यविजये युक्ता नैते पर-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">Page0965-1</a>]<BR> -परिग्रहाः Mb. 7. 144. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0964-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपरिग्रहः|परपरिग्रह
पर + -परिग्रहः anotherʼs property (as wife &c.); यथा बीजं न वप्तव्यं<BR> पुंसा परपरिग्रहे Ms. 9. 42-3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपरिभवः|परपरिभव
पर + -परिभवः humiliation or injury suffered from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकनिवृत्त|परपाकनिवृत्तः
पर + -पाकनिवृत्त <i>a.</i> One who does not depend on others for his<BR> sustenance and performs the पञ्चयज्ञs faultlessly and takes food<BR> in his own house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरत|परपाकरतः
पर + -पाकरत <i>a.</i> one who depends upon others for his sustenance<BR> but performs the usual ceremonies before cooking; पञ्चयज्ञान् स्वयं<BR> कृत्वा परान्नमुपजीवति । सततं प्रातरुत्थाय परपाकरतस्तु सः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरुचिः|परपाकरुचि
पर + -पाकरुचिः having a liking for othersʼ food; परपाकरुचिर्न<BR> स्यादनिन्द्यामन्त्रणादृते Y. 1. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपिण्डः|परपिण्ड|परपिंड
पर + -पिण्डः anotherʼs food, food given by another. ˚अद् <i>a.</i>,<BR> ˚भक्षक <i>a.</i> one who eats anotherʼs food or one who feeds at the<BR> cost of another; यादृशोऽहं परपिण्डभक्षको भूतः Mk. 8. 25/26. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR> a servant. ˚रत <i>a.</i> feeding upon anotherʼs food; परपिण्डरता मनुष्याः Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुरञ्जयः|परपुरञ्जय
पर + -पुरञ्जयः a conqueror, hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुरुषः|परपुरुष
पर + -पुरुषः<BR>—1 another man, a stranger.<BR>—2 the Supreme Spirit, Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 the husband of another woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्ट|परपुष्टः
पर + -पुष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fed or nourished by another.<BR>—2 Stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्टः|परपुष्ट
पर + -पुष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@}) the (Indian) cuckoo. ˚महोत्सवः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्टा
पर + -पुष्टा<BR>—1 the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>—2 a parasitical plant.<BR>—3 a harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्वा|परपूर्व्वा
पर + -पूर्वा a woman who has or had a former husband; Ms. 3. 166; पतिं<BR> हित्वाऽपकृष्टं स्वमुत्कृष्टं या निषेवते । निन्द्यैव सा भवेल्लोके परपूर्वेति<BR> चोच्यते Ms. 5. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रतिनप्तृ
पर + -प्रतिनप्तृ <i>m.</i> son of the great grand son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रपौत्रः|परप्रपौत्र
पर + -प्रपौत्रः (see प्रतिनप्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रेष्यः|परप्रेष्य
पर + -प्रेष्यः a servant, menial, slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परब्रह्मन्
पर + -ब्रह्मन् <i>n.</i> the Supreme Spirit; cf. लीने परे ब्रह्मणि<BR> Bh. परे ब्रह्मणि कोऽपि न लग्नः Śaṅkara. (चर्पटपञ्जरिका 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभागः|परभाग
पर + -भागः<BR>—1 anotherʼs share.<BR>—2 superior merit.<BR>—3 good fortune, prosperity.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) excellence, superiority, supremacy; दुरधिगमः परभागो यावत्<BR> पुरुषेण पौरुषं न कृतम् Pt. 1. 330, 5. 34.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) excess, abundance, height; स्थलकमलगञ्जनं मम हृदयरञ्जनम्<BR> जनितरतिरङ्गपरभागम् Gīt. 10; आभाति लब्धपरभागतयाधरोष्ठे<BR> R. 5. 70; Ku. 7. 17; Ki. 5. 30, 8. 42; Śi. 7. 33, 8. 51, 10. 86, 12. 15.<BR>—5 the last part, remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाव|परभावः
पर + -भाव <i>a.</i> loving another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभावः|परभाव
पर + -भावः the being second member in a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाषा
पर + -भाषा a foreign tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभुक्त
पर + -भुक्त <i>a.</i> enjoyed or used by another; परभुक्तां च कान्तां<BR> च यो भुङ्क्ते स नराधमः । स पच्यते कालसूत्रे यावच्चन्द्रदिवाकरौ ॥ Brav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूत
पर + -भूत <i>a.</i> following, subsequent (as words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत्
पर + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a crow (said to nourish the cuckoo).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत|परभृतः
पर + -भृत <i>a.</i> nourished by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृतः|परभृत
पर + -भृतः, -ता the (Indian) cuckoo; (so called because she is nourished<BR> by another <i>i. e.</i> by a crow); प्रागन्तरिक्षगमनात्स्वमपत्यजातमन्यैर्द्विजैः<BR> परभृताः खलु पोषयन्ति Ś. 5. 22; Ku. 6. 2; R. 9. 43; Ś. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परता
पर + -भृतः, -ता the (Indian) cuckoo; (so called because she is nourished<BR> by another <i>i. e.</i> by a crow); प्रागन्तरिक्षगमनात्स्वमपत्यजातमन्यैर्द्विजैः<BR> परभृताः खलु पोषयन्ति Ś. 5. 22; Ku. 6. 2; R. 9. 43; Ś. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमतम्
पर + -मतम्<BR>—1 anotherʼs opinion.<BR>—2 different opinion or doctrine; heterodoxy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्मज्ञ|परमर्म्मज्ञ
पर + -मर्मज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the secrets of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमृत्युः|परमृत्यु
पर + -मृत्युः a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पररमणः|पररमण
पर + -रमणः a married womanʼs gallant or paramour; स्वाधीने पररमणे<BR> धन्यास्तारुण्यफलभाजः Pt. 1. 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोकः|परलोक|परलोकं
पर + -लोकः the next (or future) world; परलोकनवप्रवासिनः प्रतिपत्स्ये<BR> पदवीमहं तव Ku. 4. 10. ˚गमः, ˚यानम् death. ˚विधि funeral<BR> rites; परलोकविधौ च माधव स्मरमुद्दिश्य (निवपेः सहकारमञ्जरीः) Ku. 4. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश|परवशः
पर + -वश, -वश्य <i>a.</i> subject to another, dependent, dependent<BR> on others; सर्वं परवशं दुःखं सर्वमात्मवशं सुखम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश्य
पर + -वश, -वश्य <i>a.</i> subject to another, dependent, dependent<BR> on others; सर्वं परवशं दुःखं सर्वमात्मवशं सुखम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाच्यम्
पर + -वाच्यम् a fault or a defect of another; प्रकटान्यपि नैपुणं महत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">Page0965-2</a>]<BR> परवाच्यानि चिराय गोपितुम् Śi. 16. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाणिः|परवाणि
पर + -वाणिः<BR>—1 a judge.<BR>—2 a year.<BR>—3 N. of the peacock of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवादः|परवाद
पर + -वादः<BR>—1 rumour, report.<BR>—2 objection, controversy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवादिन्
पर + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a disputant, controversialist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवेश्मन्
पर + -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> the abode of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परव्रतः|परव्रत
पर + -व्रतः an epithet of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशब्दः
पर + -शब्दः a word expressive of something else; परशब्दस्य परत्र<BR> वृत्तौ तद्वद् भावो गम्यते ŚB. on MS. 7. 2 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वस्
पर + -श्वस् <i>ind.</i> the day after tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसंगत|परसङ्गत
पर + -संगत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 associated with another.<BR>—2 fighting with another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसंज्ञकः|परसञ्ज्ञक
पर + -संज्ञकः the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसवर्ण
पर + -सवर्ण <i>a.</i> homogeneous with a following letter (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसात्
पर + -सात् <i>ind.</i> into the hands of another. ˚कृता a woman given in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसेवा
पर + -सेवा service of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्त्री
पर + -स्त्री anotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वम्
पर + -स्वम् anotherʼs property; व्यावृता यत् परस्वेभ्यः श्रुतौ तस्करता<BR> स्थिता R. 1. 27; Ms. 7. 123. ˚हरणम् seizing anotherʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परहन्
पर + -हन् <i>a.</i> killing enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परहित
पर + -हित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 benevolent.<BR>—2 profitable to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतम्
पर + -तम् the welfare of another; सन्तः स्वयं परहिताभिहिताभियोगाः Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकीय|परकीयं
परकीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to another; अर्थो हि कन्या परकीय एव Ś. 4. 22; Ms. 4. 201.<BR>—2 Stranger, hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकीया
परकीय + .{@-या@} Anotherʼs wife, a woman not oneʼs own, one of the three main<BR> kinds of heroines; see अन्यस्त्री and S. D. 108 <i>et seq.</i>; cf. also<BR> अप्रकटपरपुरुषानुरागा परकीया । सा च द्विधा । परोढा कन्यका च ।<BR> कन्यकायाः पित्राद्यधीनतया परकीयता । Ras. M..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंजनः|परञ्जन|परंजन|परञ्जनः
परंजनः, परंजयः An epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंजयः|परञ्जय|परंजय|परञ्जयः
परंजनः, परंजयः An epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतस्
परतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From another; सन्तः स्वतः प्रकाशन्ते गुणा न परतो नृणाम् Bv. 1. 120.<BR>—2 From an enemy; यशस्तु रक्ष्यं परतो यशोधनैः R. 3. 48.<BR>—3 Further, more (than), beyond, after, over (often with abl.); यो बुद्धेः<BR> परतस्तु सः Bg. 3. 42.<BR>—4 Otherwise.<BR>—5 Differently.<BR>—6 Further, afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्वम्
परत्वम्<BR>—1 The following of another letter, posteriority.<BR>—2 Distinction, difference.<BR>—3 Remoteness.<BR>—4 Consequence, result.<BR>—5 Enmity, hostility.<BR>—6 Priority of place or time, proximity, one of the 24 guṇas of the Vaiśeṣikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्र|परत्रं
परत्र <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In another world, in a future birth; परत्रेह च शर्मणे R. 1. 69;<BR> Ku. 4. 37; Ms. 3. 275, 5. 166, 8. 127.<BR>—2 In the sequel, further or later on.<BR>—3 Hereafter, in future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्रम्
परत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} Future world.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परत्रभीरुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्रभीरुः|परत्रभीरु
परत्र + -भीरुः one who stands in awe of the future world, a pious or religious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परथा
परथा <i>ind.</i> (like अन्यथा) Otherwise; Colacampūkāvya 5. 5; p. 4; p. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंतप|परन्तप|परंतपः|परन्तपः
परंतप <i>a.</i> [cf. P. III. 2. 39] Annoying or vexing others, subduing<BR> oneʼs enemy; Bg. 4. 2; यः कश्चन रघूणां हि परमेकः परंतपः R. 15. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंतपः|परन्तप|परंतप|परन्तपः
परंतप + .{@-पः@} A hero, conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम|परमः
परम <i>a.</i> [परं परत्वं माति-क Tv.]<BR>—1 Most distant, last.<BR>—2 Highest, best, most excellent, greatest; प्राप्नोति परमां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">Page0966-1</a>]<BR> गतिम् Ms. 4. 14, 7. 1, 2. 13.<BR>—3 Chief, principal, primary, supreme; सर्वथा ब्राह्मणाः पूज्याः परमं<BR> दैवतं हि तत् Ms. 9. 319.<BR>—4 Exceeding, extreme.<BR>—5 Adequate, sufficient; परमं यत्नमातिष्ठेत् स्तेनानां निग्रहे नृपः Ms. 8. 302.<BR>—6 Worst.<BR>—7 Higher than, superior to; न मन्ये वाणिज्यात् किमपि परमं वर्तनमिह Pt. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमम्
परम + .{@-मम्@} The utmost or highest; the chief or prominent part; (at the<BR> end of comp.) consisting principally of, solely occupied with; कामोपभोगपरमा<BR> एतावदिति निश्चिताः Bg. 16. 11; Ms. 6. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमम्
परम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A particle of assent, acceptance or agreement (well, very well, yes,<BR> be it so); ततः परममित्युक्त्वा प्रतस्थे मुनिमण्डलम् Ku. 6. 35.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, very much; परमक्रुद्धः &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परमाक्षरम्, परमाङ्गना, परमाणुः, परमाद्वैतम्, परमान्नम्, परमापमः, परमार्थः, परमार्थतः, परमाहः, परमात्मन्, परमानन्दः, परमापद्, परमायुधम्, परमार्यः, परमेष्वासः, परमेशः, परमेश्वरः, परमर्षिः, परमैश्वर्यम्, परमकाण्डः, परमकाण्डम्, परमक्रान्तिः, परमगतिः, परमगवः, परमगहन, परमतत्त्वम्, परमधर्मात्मन्, परमपदम्, परमपरम, परमपुंस्, परमपुरुषः, परमपूरुषः, परमप्रख्य, परमब्रह्मन्, परममुद्रा, परमरसः, परमराजः, परमसमुदय, परमसम्मत, परमहंसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0965-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाक्षरम्
परम + -अक्षरम् the sacred syllable ‘om’ or Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाङ्गना|परमांगना
परम + -अङ्गना an excellent woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाणुः|परमाणु
परम + -अणुः an infinitesimal particle, an atom; सिकतात्वादपि परां<BR> प्रपेदे परमाणुताम् R. 15. 22; परगुणपरमाणून् पर्वतीकृत्य नित्यम्<BR> Bh. 2. 78; पृथ्वी नित्या परमाणुरूपा T. S.; (a परमाणु is thus<BR> defined:− जालान्तरस्थसूर्यांशौ यत् सूक्ष्मं दृश्यते रजः । भागस्तस्य<BR> च षष्ठो यः परमाणुः स उच्यते ॥ Tarka K., or less accurately:−<BR> जालान्तरगते रश्मौ यत् सूक्ष्मं दृश्यते रजः । तस्य त्रिंशत्तमो भागः<BR> परमाणुः स उच्यते ॥) ˚अङ्गकः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाद्वैतम्
परम + -अद्वैतम्<BR>—1 the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 pure unitarianism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमान्नम्
परम + -अन्नम् rice boiled in milk with sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमापमः|परमापम
परम + -अपमः the inclination of a planetʼs orbit to the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थः|परमार्थ
परम + -अर्थः<BR>—1 the highest or most sublime truth, true spiritual knowledge, knowledge<BR> about Brahman or the Supreme Spirit; इदं हि तत्त्वं परमार्थभाजाम् Mv. 7. 2.<BR>—2 truth, reality, earnestness; परिहासविजल्पितं सखे परमार्थेन<BR> न गृह्यतां वचः Ś. 2. 19; oft. in comp. in the sense of ‘true’ or ‘real’.<BR> ˚मत्स्याः R. 7. 40; Mv. 4. 30.<BR>—3 any excellent or important object.<BR>—4 the best sense.<BR>—5 the best kind of wealth. ˚दरिद्र really poor; Mk. ˚भाज <i>a.</i><BR> partaking of the highest truth; Mv. ˚विद् a philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थतः
परम + -अर्थतः <i>ind.</i> truly, really, exactly, accurately; विकारं<BR> खलु परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वाऽनारम्भः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 4; उवाच चैनं परमार्थतो<BR> हरं न वेत्सि नूनं यत एवमात्थ माम् Ku. 5. 75; Pt. 1. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाहः|परमाह
परम + -अहः an excellent day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमात्मन्
परम + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the Supreme Spirit or Brahman; न च योगविधेर्नवेतरः<BR> स्थिरधीरा परमात्मदर्शनात् R. 8. 22; स्वर्गापवर्गयोर्मार्गमामनन्ति<BR> मनीषिणः । यदुपास्तिमसावत्र परमात्मा निरूप्यते ॥ Kusum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमानन्दः|परमानन्द
परम + -आनन्दः ‘supreme felicity’, Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमापद्
परम + -आपद् <i>f.</i> the greatest calamity or misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमायुधम्
परम + -आयुधम् the wheel (चक्र); शूलैः प्रमथिताः केचित् केचित्तु<BR> परमायुधैः Rām. 6. 58. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्यः|परमार्य
परम + -आर्यः a Bodhisattva (q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्वासः|परमेष्वास
परम + -इष्वासः an excellent archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेशः|परमेश
परम + -ईशः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेश्वरः|परमेश्वर
परम + -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Indra.<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR>—4 the Almighty god, the Supreme Being.<BR>—5 N. of Brahman.<BR>—6 a universal monarch, sovereign of the world; see चक्रवर्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्षिः|परमर्षि
परम + -ऋषिः a great sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमैश्वर्यम्
परम + -ऐश्वर्यम् supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमकाण्डः|परमकाण्ड
परम + -काण्डः, -काण्डम् a very auspicious moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमकाण्डम्
परम + -काण्डः, -काण्डम् a very auspicious moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमक्रान्तिः|परमक्रान्ति
परम + -क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> the sine of the greatest declination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगतिः|परमगति
परम + -गतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 any chief object or refuge (as a god).<BR>—2 final beatitude, emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगवः|परमगव
परम + -गवः an excellent bull or cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगहन
परम + -गहन <i>a.</i> very myserious, profound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमतत्त्वम्
परम + -तत्त्वम् the highest truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमधर्मात्मन्
परम + -धर्मात्मन् <i>a.</i> very dutiful, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपदम्
परम + -पदम्<BR>—1 the best<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">Page0966-2</a>]<BR> position, highest rank.<BR>—2 final beatitude; विष्णोः पदे परमे मध्व उत्सः Rv. 1. 154. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपरम
परम + -परम <i>a.</i> most excellent of all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपुंस्
परम + -पुंस् the Supreme Spirit; N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपुरुषः|परमपुरुष
परम + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपूरुषः|परमपूरुष
परम + -पुरुषः, -पूरुषः the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमप्रख्य
परम + -प्रख्य <i>a.</i> celebrated, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमब्रह्मन्
परम + -ब्रह्मन् <i>n.</i> the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परममुद्रा
परम + -मुद्रा <i>f.</i> One of the poses of goddess त्रिपुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमरसः|परमरस
परम + -रसः butter-milk mixed with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमराजः|परमराज
परम + -राजः a supreme monarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमसमुदय
परम + -समुदय <i>a.</i> very auspicious or successful; परमसमुदयेनाश्वमेधेन<BR> चेष्ट्वा Mk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमसम्मत
परम + -सम्मत <i>a.</i> highly esteemed; much revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमहंसः|परमहंस
परम + -हंसः an ascetic of the highest order, one who has controlled<BR> and subdued all his senses by abstract meditation; cf. कुटीचक; कुटीचको<BR> बहूदकः हंसश्चैव तृतीयकः । चतुर्थः परमो हंसो यो यः पश्चात् स<BR> उत्तमः ॥ Hārītāsmṛti. ˚परिव्राजकाचार्यः N. of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमक
परमक <i>a.</i> Highest, most excellent, best &c.; also परमिक;<BR> चतुर्णामात्मजानां हि प्रीतिः परमिका मम Rām. 1. 20. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमतः|परमत
परमतः <i>ind.</i> In the highest degree, exceedingly, very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमता
परमता<BR>—1 Highest rank, position; यद्यपि राजा परमतां गच्छति ब्रह्मैवान्तत<BR> उपनिश्रयति Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11.<BR>—2 Highest aim or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंतप|परन्तप|परंतपः|परन्तपः
परंतप <i>a.</i> Destroying foes (a hero).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपदम्
परंपदम्<BR>—1 The abode of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Eternal felicity.<BR>—3 A high position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठ|परमेष्ठः
परमेष्ठ <i>a.</i> Superior, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठः|परमेष्ठ
परमेष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठिन्
परमेष्ठिन् <i>a.</i> Standing at the head, highest, chief; परमेष्ठिनां<BR> प्रभुः Bhāg. 10. 89. 58. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 Of Garuḍa.<BR>—5 Of Agni.<BR>—6 A ny spiritual teacher. —7 (with Jainas) An Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपर|परम्पर|परंपरः|परम्परः
परंपर <i>a.</i> One following the other; परंपराणां भक्षिष्ये<BR> वानराणां मृतं मृतम् Rām. 4. 56. 5.<BR>—2 Successive, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरः|परम्पर|परंपर|परम्परः
परंपर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A great-grandson.<BR>—2 A kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरा|परम्परा
परंपर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 An uninterrupted series, regular series, succession; महतीयं खल्वनर्थपरंपरा<BR> K. 103; कर्णपरंपरया ‘from ear to ear, by hear-say’; परंपरया<BR> आगम् ‘to be handed down in regular succession’.<BR>—2 A row, line, collection, assemblage (of regular things); तोयान्तर्भास्करालीव<BR> रेजे मुनिपरंपरा Ku. 6. 49; R. 6. 5, 35, 40, 12. 100.<BR>—3 Method, order, due arrangement; एवं परंपराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो<BR> विदुः Bg. 1. 2.<BR>—4 Race, family, lineage.<BR>—5 Injury, hurting, killing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परंपरयात, परंपरवाहनम्, परंपरसम्बन्धः, परंपररम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरयात
परंपर + -यात <i>a.</i> received by tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरवाहनम्
परंपर + -वाहनम् an indirect means of conveyance (such as horse which<BR> draws the carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरसम्बन्धः
परंपर + -सम्बन्धः an indirect conjunction; cf. P. VIII. 1. 24 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपररम्
परंपर + -रम् <i>ind.</i> Successively, one after the other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपराक|परम्पराक|परम्पराकं
परंपराक <i>a.</i> Immolating an animal at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरित
परंपरित <i>a.</i> Continuous, forming a series,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0966-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परंपरीण|परम्परीण|परम्परीणं
परंपरीण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obtained by succession or descent, hereditary; लक्ष्मीं परंपरीणां<BR> त्वं पुत्रपौत्रीणतां नय Bk. 5. 15.<BR>—2 Traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवत्|परवन्त्
परवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dependent upon or subject to another, ready to obey; सा बाला परवतीति<BR> मे विदितम् Ś. 3. 2; भगवन्परवानयं जनः R. 8. 81, 2. 56;<BR> oft. with instr. or loc. of person; भ्रात्रा यदित्थं परवानसि त्वम् R. 14. 59.<BR>—2 Deprived of strength, rendered powerless; परवानिव शरीरोपतापेन Māl. 3.<BR>—3 Completely under the influence of (another), not master of oneself,<BR> overpowered or overcome; विस्मयेन परवानस्मि U. 5; आनन्देन परवानस्मि<BR> U. 3; साध्वसेन Māl. 6.<BR>—4 Devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवत्ता
परवत्ता Subjection to another, dependence; न हि सुलभवियोगा<BR> कर्तुमात्मप्रियाणि प्रभवति परवत्ता V. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जः|परञ्ज|परंज|परंजः
परञ्जः<BR>—1 An oil-mill.<BR>—2 The blade of a sword.<BR>—3 Foam.<BR>—4 A scymitar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जा
परञ्जः + .{@-जा@} The sounds of instruments at festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जम्
परञ्जः + .{@-जम्@} Indraʼs sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशः|परश|परशं
परशः A kind of stone or gem, the touch of which is said to turn<BR> other metals, such as iron, into gold; perhaps the philosopherʼs stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुः|परशु
परशुः [परं-शृणाति, शॄ-कु डिच्च; cf. Uṇ. 1. 34]<BR>—1 An axe, a hatchet, a battle-axe; तर्जितः परशुधारया मम R. 11. 78.<BR>—2 A weapon in general.<BR>—3 A thunderbolt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परशुधरः, परशुमुद्रा, परशुरामः, परशुवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुधरः|परशुधर
परशुः + -धरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR>—2 of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—3 a soldier armed with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुमुद्रा
परशुः + -मुद्रा a kind of pose in Tantraśāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुरामः|परशुराम
परशुः + -रामः ‘Rāma with the axe’, N. of a celebrated Brāhmaṇa warrior,<BR> son of Jamadagni and the sixth incarnation of Viṣṇu. [While young he<BR> cut off with his axe the head of his mother Reṇukā at the command of<BR> his father when none of his other brothers was willing to do so; (see<BR> जमदग्नि). Some time after this, king Kārtavīrya went to the hermitage<BR> of his father, and carried off his cow. But Paraśurāma, when he returned<BR> home, fought with the king and killed him. When his sons heard this they<BR> became very angry, and repaired to the hermitage, and on finding Jamadagni<BR> alone, they shot him dead. When Paraśurāma, who was not then also at<BR> home, returned, he became very much exasperated, and made the dreadful<BR> vow of exterminating the whole Kṣatriya race. He succeeded in fulfilling<BR> this vow, and is said to have ‘rid the earth thrice seven times of the royal race’<BR>. He was afterwards, destroyer of the Kṣatriyas as he was,<BR> defeated by Rāma, son of Daśaratha, though quite a boy of sixteen (see<BR> R. 11. 68-91). He is said to have at one time pierced through the Krauñca<BR> mountain, being jealous of the might of Kārtikeya; cf. Me. 57. He is<BR> one of the seven <i>chirajivins</i>, and is believed to be still practising<BR> penance on the Mahendra mountain; cf. Gīt. 1.:− क्षत्रियरुधिरमये जगदपगतपापं<BR> स्नपयसि पयिसि शामतभवतापम् । केशव धृतभृगुपतिरूप जय जगदीश हरे ।].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुवनम्
परशुः + -वनम् N. of a certain part of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वधः|परश्वध
परश्व(स्व)धः A hatchet, a battle-axe; धारां शितां रामपरश्वधस्य<BR> संभावयत्युत्पलपत्रसाराम् R. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वधः|परस्वध
परश्व(स्व)धः A hatchet, a battle-axe; धारां शितां रामपरश्वधस्य<BR> संभावयत्युत्पलपत्रसाराम् R. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्
परस् <i>ind.</i> (Rarely used by itself in classical Sanskrit)<BR>—1 Beyond, further, more than; परोरजः सवितुर्जातवेदः Bhāg. 5. 7. 14.<BR>—2 On the other side of.<BR>—3 Far away, at a distance<BR>—4 With the exception of.<BR>—5 Ved. In future, afterwards.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परःकृष्ण, परःपुंसा, परःपुरुष, परःशत, परःश्वस्, परःसहस्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःकृष्ण
परस् + -कृष्ण <i>a.</i> very black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःपुंसा
परस् + -पुंसा Ved. a woman not satisfied with her husband (and therefore<BR> seeking for a paramour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःपुरुष
परस् + -पुरुष <i>a.</i> higher than a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परस् + -शत <i>a.</i> more than a hundred; स जवेन पतन् परःशतानां<BR> पततां व्रात इवारवं वितेने Ki. 13. 26; Śi. 12. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःश्वस्
परस् + -श्वस् <i>ind.</i> the day after tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परस् + -सहस्र <i>a.</i> more than a thousand; परःसहस्राः शरदस्तपांसि<BR> तप्त्वा U. 1. 15; परःसहस्रैः पिशाचैः Mv. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तात्
परस्तात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Beyond, on the other side of, further than (with gen.); आदित्यवर्णं<BR> तमसः परस्तात् Bg. 8. 9.<BR>—2 Hereafter, afterwards; परस्तादवगम्यते Ś. 1.<BR>—3 Higher than.<BR>—4 Ved. From above.<BR>—5 Aside, apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पर|परस्परं
परस्पर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mutual; परस्परस्य मर्माणि ये न रक्षन्ति जन्तवः । त एव निधनं<BR> यान्ति वल्मीकोदरसर्पवत् ॥ Pt. 3. 186; परस्परां विस्मयवन्ति<BR> लक्ष्मीमालोकयांचक्रुरिवादरेण Bk. 2. 5.<BR>—2 (pl.) Like one another; Mb. 12. ━<i>pron. a.</i> Each other, one another<BR> (used in the sing. only; often in comp.); परस्परस्योपरि पर्यचीयत<BR> R. 3. 24, 7. 38; अविज्ञातपरस्परैः अपसर्पैः 17. 51; परस्पराक्षिसादृक्ष्यम् 1. 40, 3. 24.<BR> <i>Note</i>:− The acc. and abl. singulars are often used<BR> adverbially in the sense of ‘mutually’, ‘reciprocally’, ‘one another’,<BR> ‘by, from’ or ‘to one another’, ‘against one another’ &c.; see परस्परं<BR> भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ Bg. 3. 11, 10. 9; R. 4. 79, 6. 46, 7. 14, 53, 12. 94.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परस्परादिन्, परस्परज्ञः, परस्परविलक्षण, परस्परव्यावृत्तिः, परस्परस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परादिन्
परस्पर + -अदिन् <i>a.</i> consuming one another; परस्परादिनस्स्तेनाः (भवन्ति) Ms. 12. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परज्ञः|परस्परज्ञ
परस्पर + -ज्ञः a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परविलक्षण
परस्पर + -विलक्षण <i>a.</i> mutually opposing; परस्परविलक्षणा गुणविशेषाः Sāṅ. K. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परव्यावृत्तिः|परस्परव्यावृत्ति
परस्पर + -व्यावृत्तिः <i>f.</i> mutual exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परस्थित
परस्पर + -स्थित <i>a.</i> standing opposite to one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्मैपदम्
परस्मैपदम्, -परस्मैभाषा<BR> ‘A voice for another’, one of the two voices in which<BR> verbs in Sanskrit are conjugated; आत्मनेपदनिमित्तहीनाद् धातोः परस्मैपदं स्यात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्मैभाषा
परस्मैपदम्, -परस्मैभाषा<BR> ‘A voice for another’, one of the two voices in which<BR> verbs in Sanskrit are conjugated; आत्मनेपदनिमित्तहीनाद् धातोः परस्मैपदं स्यात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परा
परा <i>ind.</i> A prefix to verbs and nouns in the sense of ‘away, back, in an inverted order, aside, towards’<BR>. According to G. M. the senses<BR> of परा are:−<BR>—1 killing, injuring & (पराहत).<BR>—2 going (परागत).<BR>—3 seeing, encountering (परादृष्ट).<BR>—4 prowess (पराक्रान्त).<BR>—5 direction towards (परावृत्त).<BR>—6 excess (पराजित).<BR>—7 dependence (पराधीन).<BR>—8 liberation (पराकृत).<BR>—9 inverted order, backwards (पराङ्मुख).<BR>—10 setting aside, disregarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्
पराक् See पराच्; पुनरासाद्य संरब्ध उपक्रोष्टा पराक् स्थितः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 15. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक|पराकः
पराक <i>a.</i> Small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकः|पराक
पराक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A sacrificial sword.<BR>—2 A kind of penance; यतात्मनोऽप्रमत्तस्य द्वादशाहमभोजनम् । पराको<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">Page0968-1</a>]<BR> नाम कृच्छ्रोऽयं सर्वपापापनोदनः Ms. 11. 215; N. 17. 193. द्वादशाहोपवासेन<BR> पराकः परिकीर्तितः; U. 4.<BR>—3 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0967-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकाशः|पराकाश
पराकाशः<BR>—1 Remote expectation or hope.<BR>—2 Distant view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकृ
पराकृ €8 U. To reject, disregard, slight, take no notice of; तां<BR> हनूमान् पराकुर्वन्नगमत् पुष्पकं प्रति Bk. 8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकरणम्
पराकरणम् The act of setting aside, rejecting, disregarding, disdaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकृष्ट
पराकृष्ट <i>a.</i> Disparaged, reviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराके
पराके <i>ind.</i> At a distance (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रम्
पराक्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To display courage, strength or heroism, act bravely; बकवच्चिन्तयेदर्थान्<BR> सिंहवच्च पराक्रमेत् Ms. 7. 106; इत्युक्त्वा खे पराक्रंस्त Bk. 8. 22, 94.<BR>—2 To turn back.<BR>—3 To march against, attack.<BR>—4 To march forward, advance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रमः|पराक्रम
पराक्रमः<BR>—1 Heroism, prowess, courage, valour; पराक्रमः परिभवे Śi. 2. 44.<BR>—2 Marching againt, attack.<BR>—3 Attempt, endeavour, enterprise.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रमिन्
पराक्रमिन् <i>a.</i> Heroic, spirited, courageous, valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रान्त|पराक्रांत
पराक्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Strong, valiant, bold, energetic; शक्रतुल्यपराक्रान्तम् Rām. 4. 19. 23;<BR> Mb. 7. 65. 3.<BR>—2 Attacked.<BR>—3 Turned back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्षिप्त
पराक्षिप्त <i>a.</i> Upset, wrested away.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पराक्षिप्तमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्षिप्तमनस्
पराक्षिप्त + -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind carried away, enraptured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागः|पराग
परागः<BR>—1 The pollen of a flower; स्फुटपरागपरागतपङ्कजम् Śi. 6. 2; Amaru. 54.<BR>—2 Dust in general; प्रतापोऽग्रे ततः शब्दः परागस्तदनन्तरम् R. 4. 30.<BR>—3 Fragrant powder used after bathing.<BR>—4 Sandal.<BR>—5 An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>—6 Fame, celebrity.<BR>—7 Independence, self-will.<BR>—8 Medicinal powder; Mātaṅga L. 11. 28.<BR>—9 Powder; कायेऽपि कर्पूरपरागपूरः Mv. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागम्
परागम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To return; तदयं परागत एवास्मि U. 5.<BR>—2 To surround, encompass, pervade; स्फुटपरागपरागतपङ्कजम् Śi. 6. 2.<BR>—3 Ved. To go away, depart.<BR>—4 To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागत
परागत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dead.<BR>—2 Covered with, surrounded.<BR>—3 Spread, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागमः|परागम
परागमः Invasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गवः|पराङ्गव|परांगव|परांगवः
पराङ्गवः The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराच्
पराच्, पराञ्च् <i>a.</i> (-ची <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Situated beyond or on the other side; ये चामुष्मात् पराञ्चो लोकाः<BR> Ch. Up.; दिग्देशकालवचनो हि पराक्शब्दो भवति ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 47.<BR>—2 Having the face turned away; आत्मीयास्ते ये पराञ्चः पुरस्तात् (पराङ्मुख); Śi. 18. 18.<BR>—3 Unfavourable, adverse; दैवे पराचि Bv. 1. 105; or दैवे पराग्वदनशालिनि<BR> हन्त जाते 3. 1.<BR>—4 Distant.<BR>—5 Directed outwards; पराङ् पश्यति नान्तरात्मन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">Page0968-2</a>]<BR> Kaṭh. 2. 1. 1; Bhāg. 8. 19. 9.<BR>—6 Turned away, averted.<BR>—7 Departing or returning from.<BR>—8 Inverted, reversed.<BR>—9 Not repeated; अनभ्यासे पराक्शब्दस्य तादर्थ्यात् MS. 10. 5. 45; अनभ्यासे<BR> पराक्शब्दो वर्तते ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 45. ━<i>n.</i> The body; यदात्मानं<BR> पराग्गृह्य पशुवद्भूतवैशसम् Bhāg. 4. 11. 10. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Away, off.<BR>—2 Outwards.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पराग्दृश्, पराक्पुष्पः, पराक्पुष्पी, पराङ्मुख, पराक्खम्, पराङ्मुखता, पराङ्मुखत्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्च्|परांच्
पराच्, पराञ्च् <i>a.</i> (-ची <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Situated beyond or on the other side; ये चामुष्मात् पराञ्चो लोकाः<BR> Ch. Up.; दिग्देशकालवचनो हि पराक्शब्दो भवति ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 47.<BR>—2 Having the face turned away; आत्मीयास्ते ये पराञ्चः पुरस्तात् (पराङ्मुख); Śi. 18. 18.<BR>—3 Unfavourable, adverse; दैवे पराचि Bv. 1. 105; or दैवे पराग्वदनशालिनि<BR> हन्त जाते 3. 1.<BR>—4 Distant.<BR>—5 Directed outwards; पराङ् पश्यति नान्तरात्मन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">Page0968-2</a>]<BR> Kaṭh. 2. 1. 1; Bhāg. 8. 19. 9.<BR>—6 Turned away, averted.<BR>—7 Departing or returning from.<BR>—8 Inverted, reversed.<BR>—9 Not repeated; अनभ्यासे पराक्शब्दस्य तादर्थ्यात् MS. 10. 5. 45; अनभ्यासे<BR> पराक्शब्दो वर्तते ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 45. ━<i>n.</i> The body; यदात्मानं<BR> पराग्गृह्य पशुवद्भूतवैशसम् Bhāg. 4. 11. 10. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Away, off.<BR>—2 Outwards.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पराग्दृश्, पराक्पुष्पः, पराक्पुष्पी, पराङ्मुख, पराक्खम्, पराङ्मुखता, पराङ्मुखत्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग्दृश्
पराच् + -दृश् <i>a.</i> having the eyes turned towards the outer world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्पुष्पः
पराच् + -पुष्पः The कदम्ब tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्पुष्पी
पराच् + -पुष्पी The अपामार्ग. tree (Mar. आघाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुख|पराङ्मुखः
पराच् + -मुख <i>a.</i> (पराङ्मुख)<BR>—1 having the face turned away or averted, turning the back upon; विग्रहाच्च<BR> शयने पराङ्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स तत्वरे R. 19. 38; Amaru. 90; Ms. 2. 195, 10. 119.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) averse from; मातुर्न केवलं स्वस्याः श्रियोऽप्यासीत् पराङ्मुखः R. 12. 13.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) not disposed towards, shunning, avoiding; प्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुखो<BR> भावः V. 4. 20; Ś. 5. 28.<BR>—3 adverse, unfavourable; तनुरपि न ते दोषोऽस्माकं विधिस्तु पराङ्मुखः Amaru. 30.<BR>—4 not caring about, regardless of; मर्त्येष्वास्थापराङ्मुखः R. 10. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखः|पराङ्मुख
पराच् + -मुख + .({@-खः@}) a magical formula pronounced over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्खम्
पराच् + -खम्, -मुखता, -मुखत्वम् Turning away, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखता
पराच् + -खम्, -मुखता, -मुखत्वम् Turning away, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखत्वम्
पराच् + -खम्, -मुखता, -मुखत्वम् Turning away, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीन|पराचीनः
पराचीन <i>a.</i> [पराच्-ख]<BR>—1 Turned in an opposite direction, averted; पराचीनोऽभवत्तेभ्यः<BR> Śiva B. 27. 42.<BR>—2 Averse from, disinclined to.<BR>—3 Not minding, not caring about.<BR>—4 Happening subsequently or afterwards (उत्तरकालभव).<BR>—5 Situated on the other side, being beyond; न कदाचित् पराचीना भवितुमुत्सहन्ते<BR> Bhāg. 5. 20. 37.<BR>—6 Unfit, improper.<BR>—7 Outward (वहिर्मुख); ज्ञानमेकं पराचीनैरिन्द्रियैर्ब्रह्म निर्गुणम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 32. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीनम्
पराचीन + .{@-नम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Away from, beyond.<BR>—2 More than.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पराचीनरात्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीनरात्रम्
पराचीन + -रात्रम् the second half of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजि
पराजि €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To defeat, conquer, overcome, subdue; यं पराजयसे मृषा Y. 2. 75;<BR> Bk. 8. 9; Śi. 19. 82.<BR>—2 To lose, be deprived of.<BR>—3 To be conquered or overcome by, find (something) unbearable; अध्ययनात्<BR> पराजयते Sk. ‘finds it unbearable or difficult to study’; तां पराजयमानां<BR> स प्रीते रक्ष्यां दशाननात् Bk. 8. 71.<BR>—4 To submit or yield to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजयः|पराजय
पराजयः<BR>—1 Overpowering, conquest, conquering, subjugating, defeat; विष्टपत्रयपराजयस्थिरां<BR> रावणश्रियमपि व्यकम्पयत् R. 11. 19; Ms. 7. 199.<BR>—2 Being overcome by, not being able to suffer (with abl.); as in अध्ययनात् पराजयः<BR>—3 Losing, loss, failure (as in a law-suit); अन्यथावादिनो (साक्षिणः)<BR> यस्य ध्रुवस्तस्य पराजयः Y. 2. 79.<BR>—4 Deprivation.<BR>—5 Desertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजित|पराजितः
पराजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Conquered, subjugated, defeated.<BR>—2 Condemned by law, cast or defeated (as in a lawsuit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजिष्णु
पराजिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Victorious.<BR>—2 Conquered, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्जः|पराञ्ज|परांजः
पराञ्जः<BR>—1 An oil-mill.<BR>—2 Foam.<BR>—3 The blade of a sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0968-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराडीनम्
पराडीनम् Flying backward ‘पश्चाद्गतिः पराडीनम्’; Mb. 8. 41. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराणुत्तिः|पराणुत्ति
पराणुत्तिः <i>f.</i> Driving away, expelling, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परातंसः|परातंस
परातंसः The being thrushed or pushed aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्परः|परात्पर
परात्परः The Supreme Being. ━<i>a.</i> Supreme; परात्परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादा
परादा €3 U. Ved.<BR>—1 To give or hand over, deliver.<BR>—2 To throw away, squander.<BR>—3 To give away or exchange for (with dat.).<BR>—4 To exclude from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादानम्
परादानम्<BR>—1 Giving up or away.<BR>—2 Exchanging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिः|पराधि
पराधिः<BR>—1 Hunting, chase.<BR>—2 Extreme mental pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परानसा
परान(ण)सा Medical treatment, practice of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराणसा
परान(ण)सा Medical treatment, practice of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापत्
परापत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To arrive, draw near, approach.<BR>—2 To return.<BR>—3 To escape.<BR>—4 To depart.<BR>—5 To fall out.<BR>—6 To fail. ━<i>Caus.</i> To chase or drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभू
पराभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To defeat, vanquish, overcome.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, tease.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear.<BR>—4 To perish, be lost.<BR>—5 To submit, yield. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To defeat, overcome.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To vanish, disappear.<BR>—3 To suffer a loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभवः|पराभव
पराभवः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Defeat, discomfiture, overthrow; पराभवोऽप्युत्सव एव मानिनाम् Ki. 1. 41.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Mortification, humiliation; कुबेरस्य मनःशल्यं शंसतीव<BR> पराभवम् Ku. 2. 22; तव पदपल्लववैरिपराभवमिदमनुभवतु सुवेशम् Gīt. 12.<BR>—2 Contempt, disregard, disrespect.<BR>—3 Destruction.<BR>—4 Disappearance, separation (sometimes written पराभाव).<BR>—5 N. of the 40th year in the cycle of 60 years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभावः|पराभाव
पराभावः Same as पराभव; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभावनम्
पराभावनम् Suppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभावुक
पराभावुक <i>a.</i> About to decline, going to pass away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभूत|पराभूतः
पराभूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Defeated, overcome.<BR>—2 Treated with contempt, degraded, dishonoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभूतिः|पराभूति
पराभूतिः <i>f.</i> See पराभव; दैन्यस्य पात्रतामेति पराभूतेः परं<BR> पदम् Pt. 2. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृत|परामृतं
परामृत <i>a.</i> One who has overcome death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृश्
परामृश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To touch, rub or stroke gently; परामृशन् हर्षजडेन पाणिना तदीयमङ्गं<BR> कुलिशव्रणाङ्कितम् R. 3. 68; Śi. 17. 11; Mk. 5. 28.<BR>—2 To lay hands on, attack, assail, seize; Mk. 1. 39.<BR>—3 To defile, pollute, outrage (a woman or a temple).<BR>—4 To reflect, think, consider किं भवितेति सशङ्कं पङ्कजनयना<BR> परामृशति Bv. 2. 53.<BR>—5 To think mentally of, praise (स्तु); ग्रन्थारम्भे विध्नविघाताय<BR> समुचितेष्टदेवतां ग्रन्थकृत् परामृशति K. P. 1.<BR>—6 To have reference to, point to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्शः|परामर्श
परामर्शः<BR>—1 Seizing, pulling; as in केशपरामर्शः. —2 Bending or drawing (as a bow).<BR>—2 Violence, attack, assault; याज्ञसेन्याः परामर्शः Mb.<BR>—4 Disturbance, hindrance; तपःपरामर्शविवृद्धमन्योः Ku. 3. 71.<BR>—5 Calling to mind, recollection.<BR>—6 Consideration, reflection, thought.<BR>—7 Judgment.<BR>—8 (In logic) Deduction, ascertaining that the पक्ष or subject possesses<BR> the हेतु; व्याप्तिविशिष्टपक्षधर्मताज्ञानं परामर्शः T. S.; or व्याप्तस्य<BR> पक्षधर्मत्वधीः परामर्श उच्यते Bhāṣā P. 66.<BR>—9 Touching, striking gently.<BR>—10 Affection (by disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्शनम्
परामर्शनम्<BR>—1 Remembrance.<BR>—2 Consideration, reflection, thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृष्ट|परामृष्टः
परामृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Touched, handled, seized, grasped.<BR>—2 Roughly treated, violated.<BR>—3 Weighed, considered, judged.<BR>—4 Endured.<BR>—5 Connected with.<BR>—6 Afflicted by (as a disease); see परामृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारि
परारि <i>ind.</i> The year before last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायण|परायणं
परायण See under पर (पर-अयन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारुः|परारु
परारुः The tree called कारवेल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारुकः|परारुक
परारुकः A stone or rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावसुः|परावसु
परावसुः N. of the 40th year in the cycle of 60 year; cf. पराभव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावाकः|परावाक
परावाकः Contradiction (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराविद्धः|पराविद्ध
पराविद्धः N. of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावत्|परावन्त्
परावत्^1 <i>ind.</i> Ved. At a distance.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: Based on sense acc. to MW AP90 and VCP..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्
परावृत् €1 Ā. To return, turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्तः|परावर्त|परावर्त्त|परावर्त्तः
परावर्तः<BR>—1 Turning back, return, retreat.<BR>—2 Exchange, barter.<BR>—3 Restoration.<BR>—4 Reversal of a sentence (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्य
परावर्त्य <i>a.</i> To be turned back or exchanged or reversed or restored.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परावर्त्यव्यवहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्यव्यवहारः|परावर्त्यव्यवहार
परावर्त्य + -व्यवहारः (in law) an appeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्त
परावृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Returned, turned back.<BR>—2 Revolved.<BR>—3 Exchanged.<BR>—4 Reversed (as a judgment).<BR>—5 Restored, given back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्तिः|परावृत्ति
परावृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 = परावर्तः above.<BR>—2 Recoiling.<BR>—3 Not taking effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावहः|परावह
परावहः N. of one of the seven winds (the other six are:− आवह,<BR> उद्वह, परिवह, प्रवह, विवह and संवह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराव्याधः|पराव्याध
पराव्याधः<BR>—1 A stoneʼs throw.<BR>—2 The range of any missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशरः|पराशर
पराशरः N. of a celebrated sage, father of Vyāsa and the author of a Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशरिन्
पराशरिन् <i>m.</i> A beggar, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0969-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्
परास् €4 P.<BR>—1 To leave, give up, quit, abandon; परास्तवसुधा सुधाधिवसति Ki. 5. 27.<BR>—2 To expel.<BR>—3 To reject, repudiate; इति यदुक्तं तदपि परास्तम् S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासिसिषु
परासिसिषु <i>a.</i> Wishing to drive away; द्विषतः परासिसिषुरेषः Ki. 12. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासः|परास
परासः The range of anything thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासम्
परासः + .{@-सम्@} Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासनम्
परासनम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्त|परास्तं
परास्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or cast away.<BR>—2 Expelled, turned out.<BR>—3 Repudiated.<BR>—4 Refuted, rejected.<BR>—5 Defeated, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासिक्त
परासिक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thrown away.<BR>—2 Set aside, rendered useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासु|परासुः
परासु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lifeless, dead; प्राक् परासुर्द्विजात्मजः R. 15. 56, 9. 78.<BR>—2 One whose vital spirit is departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासुता
परासु + .{@-परासुता, -परासुत्वम्@}<BR>—1 Exhaustion, death; व्रजति पुरा हि परासुतां त्वदर्थे Ki. 10. 50.<BR>—2 A dependent life (पराधीनप्राणत्व); लोभान्मोहश्च माया च मानस्तम्भः<BR> परासुता Mb. 12. 158. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासुत्वम्
परासु + .{@-परासुता, -परासुत्वम्@}<BR>—1 Exhaustion, death; व्रजति पुरा हि परासुतां त्वदर्थे Ki. 10. 50.<BR>—2 A dependent life (पराधीनप्राणत्व); लोभान्मोहश्च माया च मानस्तम्भः<BR> परासुता Mb. 12. 158. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासेधः|परासेध
परासेधः Arrest, imprisonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्कन्दिन्|परास्कंदिन्
परास्कन्दिन् <i>m.</i> A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहन्
पराहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike or beat back, strike down, repulse, repel, overthrow, drive<BR> back; दैवं मत्पौरुषपराहतम् Rām.<BR>—2 To attack, assail; कटाक्षपराहतं वदनपङ्कजम् Māl. 7.<BR>—3 To dash against, strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहत
पराहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck down or back.<BR>—2 Driven back, repelled, repulsed.<BR>—3 Assailed, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहतम्
पराहत + .{@-तम्@} A stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहतिः|पराहति
पराहत + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i> Contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि <i>ind.</i> (Sometimes changed to परी, as परिवाह or परीवाह, परिहास or परीहास)<BR>—1 As a prefix to verbs and nouns derived from them, it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) round, round about, about;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) in addition to, further;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) opposite to, against;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) much, excessively.<BR>—2 As a separable preposition it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) towards, in the direction of, to, opposite to (with an acc.);<BR> वृक्षं परि विद्योतते विद्युत्;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) successively, severally (with an acc.); वृक्षं वृक्षं परि<BR> सिञ्चति ‘he waters tree after tree’;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) to the share or lot of (showing भाग or participation) (with<BR> acc.); यदत्र मां परि स्यात् ‘what may fall to my lot’; or लक्ष्मीर्हरिं परि Sk.;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) from, out of;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) except, outside of, with the exception of (with abl.); परि<BR> त्रिगर्तेभ्यो वृष्टो देवः or पर्यनन्तात् त्रयस्तापाः Vop.;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) after the lapse of; परि संवत्सरात्;<BR>——(<i>g</i>) in consequence of;<BR>——(<i>h</i>) beyond, more than; भृत्याः परि चतुर्दश Mb. 3. 1. 11 (com.<BR> अधिकचतुर्दशाः पञ्चदशेत्यर्थः);<BR>——(<i>i</i>) according to, in accordance with;<BR>——(<i>j</i>) above, over.<BR>—3 As an adverbial prefix to nouns not directly connected with verbs,<BR> it means ‘very’, ‘very much’, ‘excessively’; as in पर्यश्रु ‘bursting into tears’<BR>; so परिचतुर्दशन्, परिदौर्बल्य.<BR>—4 At the beginning of adverbial compounds परि means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) without,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">Page0970-2</a>]<BR> except, outside, with the exception of; as in परित्रिगर्तं वृष्टो दिवः<BR> P. II. 1. 12, VI. 2. 33. (According to P. II. 1. 10 परि may be used<BR> at the end of adverbial comp. after अक्ष, शलाका), and a numeral to<BR> denote loss or defeat in a game by an unlucky or adverse cast of dice<BR> (द्यूतव्यवहारे पराजये एवायं समासः) <i>e. g.</i> अक्षपरि, शलाकापरि,<BR> एकपरि; cf. अक्षपरि;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) round about, all round, surrounded by; as in पर्यग्नि ‘in the midst of flames’<BR>.<BR>—5 At the end of an adjectival comp. परि has the sense of ‘exhausted by’<BR>, or ‘feeling repugnance for’; as in पर्यध्ययनः = परिग्लानोऽध्ययनाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकथा
परिकथा<BR>—1 A religious tale or narrative; Buddh. Divyāvadāna.<BR>—2 A work giving the history and adventures of a fabulous person, a work of fiction.<BR>—3 A fairy tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकन्दल
परिकन्दल <i>a.</i> Full of, teeming with (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकम्पः|परिकम्प|परिकंप|परिकंपः
परिकम्पः<BR>—1 A great terror.<BR>—2 Violent tremour or trembling; विरमतु परिकम्पः कातरे क्षत्रियासि Mv. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकरः|परिकर
परिकरः<BR>—1 Retinue, train, attendants, followers.<BR>—2 A multitude, collection, crowd; संध्याकृष्टावशिष्टस्वकरपरिकरस्पृष्टहेमारपङ्क्तिः Ratn. 3. 5.<BR>—3 A beginning, commencement; गतानामारम्भः किसलयितलीलापरिकरः Bh. 1. 6.<BR>—4 A girth, waist-band, cloth worn round the loins; अहिपरिकरभाजः<BR> Śi. 4. 65; परिकरं बन्ध् or कृ ‘to gird up oneʼs loins, to make oneself ready, prepare oneself for any action’<BR>; बध्नन् सवेगं परिकरम्<BR> K. 170; कृतपरिकरः कर्मसु जनः Śivamahimna 20; कृतपरिकरस्य<BR> भवादृशस्य त्रैलोक्यमपि न क्षमं परिपन्थीभवितुम् Ve. 3; G. L. 47;<BR> बद्धो मानपरिग्रहे परिकरः सिद्धिस्तु दैवे स्थिता Amaru. 97; U. 5. 12.<BR>—5 A sofa.<BR>—6 (in Rhet.) N. of a figure of speech which consists in the use of significant<BR> epithets; विशेषणैर्यत् साकूतैरुक्तिः परिकरस्तु सः K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i><BR> सुधांशुकलितोत्तंसस्तापं हरतु वः शिवः Candr. 5. 59.<BR>—7 (In dramaturgy) Covet or indirect intimation of coming events in the<BR> plot or a drama, the germ or the बीज q. v.; see S. D. 340.<BR>—8 Judgment.<BR>—9 A helper, colleague, co-worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्तनम्
परिकर्तनम्<BR>—1 Cutting, cutting off.<BR>—2 A circular incision.<BR>—3 Cutting out.<BR>—4 A shooting pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्तिका|परिकर्त्तिका
परिकर्तिका A sharp shooting pain, especially in the rectum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्तृ|परिकर्त्तृ
परिकर्तृ <i>m.</i> A priest who performs the marriage ceremony of a<BR> younger brother whose elder brother is not yet married; परिकर्ता याजकः<BR> Hārīta; cf. परिवेत्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्मन्|परिकर्म्मन्
परिकर्मन् <i>m.</i> A servant. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 Painting or perfuming the body, personal decoration, dressing, toilet;<BR> कृताचारपरिकर्माणम् Ś. 2.<BR>—2 Painting or dyeing the foot; असमाप्ते परिकर्मणि स्मृतः Ku. 4. 19.<BR>—3 Preparation.<BR>—4 Worship, adoration; अविक्लमस्ते परिकर्मणि स्थितः Bhāg. 2. 9. 29.<BR>—5 (In Yoga phil.) Purifying, a means of purifying the mind; मैत्र्यादिचित्तपरिकर्मविदो<BR> विधाय क्लेशप्रहाण-मिह लब्धसबीजयोगाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">Page0971-1</a>]<BR> Śi. 4. 55 (see Malli. thereon).<BR>—6 An arithmetical operation (of which there are 8 divisions).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिकर्माष्टकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0970-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्माष्टकम्
परिकर्मन् + -अष्टकम् the eight fundamental rules of arithmetic <i>viz.</i> (addition,<BR> subtraction, multiplication, division, finding the square, extracting<BR> the square root, finding the cube, extracting the cube root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्मयति
परिकर्मयति Den. P. To decorate, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्मित
परिकर्मित <i>a.</i> Decorated, adorned; त्रिस्रोतसा परिकर्मितशिखरे<BR> इव हिमवान् Colacampūkāvya, p. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्मिन्|परिकर्म्मिन्
परिकर्मिन् <i>m.</i> An assistant, a servant, slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्
परिकल् €10 U.<BR>—1 To know, consider, regard.<BR>—2 To be aware of, remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकलयितृ
परिकलयितृ <i>a.</i> Surrounding, encircling; Mv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकलितम्
परिकलितम् Comprehending, knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्कनम्
परिकल्कनम् Deceit, cheating, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकाङ्क्षितः|परिकाङ्क्षित|परिकांक्षित|परिकांक्षितः
परिकाङ्क्षितः A religious mendicant or ascetic, a devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकूटम्
परिकूटम् A barrier, a trench before the gate of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकृश
परिकृश <i>a.</i> Very thin, emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकृष्
परिकृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw, pull, drag.<BR>—2 To lead (as an army).<BR>—3 To ponder, reflect constantly upon. ━<i>Caus.</i> To torment, trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्षः|परिकर्ष
परिकर्षः, -कर्षणम्<BR>—1 Dragging out, extraction.<BR>—2 A circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्षणम्
परिकर्षः, -कर्षणम्<BR>—1 Dragging out, extraction.<BR>—2 A circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्षित
परिकर्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dragged about.<BR>—2 Harassed, tortured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॄ
परिकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To surround; परिकीर्णा परिवादिनी मुनेः R. 8. 35.<BR>—2 To hand or give over, deliver; महीं महेच्छः परिकीर्य सूनौ R. 18. 33.<BR>—3 To scatter about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्ण
परिकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread, diffused, scattered about; स्फुरन्नीलाब्जानां प्रकरपरिकीर्णा<BR> इव दिशः Bh. 1. 4.<BR>—2 Surrounded, crowded with, filled; नगरेषु भवन्तु वीथयः परिकीर्णा<BR> वनजैर्मृगादिभिः Śi. 16. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॄत्
परिकॄत् €10 U.<BR>—1 To relate, narrate, proclaim, announce.<BR>—2 To praise, extol.<BR>—3 To name, call.<BR>—4 To propound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्तनम्
परिकीर्तनम्<BR>—1 Proclaiming, saying, talking of.<BR>—2 Boasting.<BR>—3 Naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्तित|परिकीर्त्तित
परिकीर्तित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Proclaimed, announced.<BR>—2 Boasted of.<BR>—3 Said, declared to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॢप्
परिकॢप् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To tend to.<BR>—2 To give, grant, vouchsafe; श्रेयसे शाश्वतो देवो वराहः परिकल्पताम्<BR> U. 5. 27 (v. l.).<BR>—3 To think. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To decide, determine.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">Page0971-2</a>]<BR>—2 To fix upon, design, make or turn into; यं सर्वशैलाः परिकल्प्य<BR> वत्सम् Ku. 1. 2.<BR>—3 To prepare, get ready.<BR>—4 To endow with; चित्रे निवेश्य परिकल्पितसत्त्वयोगा Ś. 2. 10.<BR>—5 To destine for.<BR>—6 To perform, effect, accomplish.<BR>—7 To contrive, invent, devise.<BR>—8 To distribute.<BR>—9 To invite.<BR>—10 To choose; अन्यत्र वासं परिकल्पयन्तु Bṛ. S. 59. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पनम्
परिकल्पनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Settling, fixing, deciding, determining.<BR>—2 Contriving, inventing, forming, arranging; पश्यैतान् परिकल्पनाव्यतिकरप्रोच्छूनवंशान्<BR> गजान् Mu. 7. 15.<BR>—3 Providing, furnishing.<BR>—4 Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पना
परिकल्पनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Settling, fixing, deciding, determining.<BR>—2 Contriving, inventing, forming, arranging; पश्यैतान् परिकल्पनाव्यतिकरप्रोच्छूनवंशान्<BR> गजान् Mu. 7. 15.<BR>—3 Providing, furnishing.<BR>—4 Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पित
परिकल्पित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Settled, decided.<BR>—2 Made, invented.<BR>—3 Got ready, prepared.<BR>—4 Contrived, arranged.<BR>—5 Distributed.<BR>—6 Divided.<BR>—7 Provided, furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॢप्त
परिकॢप्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distributed.<BR>—2 Scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकोपः|परिकोप
परिकोपः Great anger, fury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रम्
परिक्रम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To walk about, walk around; परिक्रम्यावलोक्य च (in dramas).<BR>—2 To overtake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रमः|परिक्रम
परिक्रमः<BR>—1 Roaming about, moving about; द्रुतपदमभियातुमिच्छितानां गगनपरिक्रमलाघवेन<BR> तासाम् Ki. 10. 2.<BR>—2 Roaming, walking or passing over.<BR>—3 Circumambulating.<BR>—4 Walking for pleasure.<BR>—5 Series, order.<BR>—6 Succession.<BR>—7 Penetrating.<BR>—8 Following the course of a river down from its source to its mouth and<BR> then on the other bank upto its source again; MW.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिक्रमसहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रमसहः|परिक्रमसह
परिक्रमः + -सहः a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रान्त|परिक्रांत
परिक्रान्त <i>p. p.</i> Walked round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रान्तम्
परिक्रान्त + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The place on which any one has walked about.<BR>—2 A foot-step, foot-print.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रान्तिः|परिक्रान्ति|परिक्रांतिः
परिक्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> Revolution, perambulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रिया
परिक्रिया<BR>—1 Enclosing with a fence or ditch, intrenching.<BR>—2 Encircling or surrounding in general.<BR>—3 (In dramaturgy) = परिकर (7) q. v.<BR>—4 Attention, attending to; गृहार्थोऽग्निपरिक्रिया Ms. 2. 67.<BR>—5 Exercise, enjoyment; राज्यपरिक्रिया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्री
परिक्री €9 Ā.<BR>—1 To buy; संभोगाय परिक्रीतः कर्तास्मि तव नाप्रियम् Bk. 8. 78.<BR>—2 To hire, purchase for a time (with instr. or dat. of the price at which<BR> one is employed on stipulated wages); शतेन शताय वा परिक्रीतः Sk.<BR>—3 To return, requite, repay; कृतेनोपकृतं वायोः परिक्रीणानमुत्थितम् Bk. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रयः|परिक्रय
परिक्रयः, -क्रयणम्<BR>—1 Wages, hire.<BR>—2 Employing on wages.<BR>—3 Purchasing or buying of.<BR>—4 Barter, exchange.<BR>—5 A peace purchased with the payment of money; कोषान् रक्षार्धकोषेण<BR> सर्वकोषेण वा पुनः । शेषप्रकृतिरक्षार्थं परिक्रय उदाहृतः ॥ Kām.; cf. H. 4. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रयणम्
परिक्रयः, -क्रयणम्<BR>—1 Wages, hire.<BR>—2 Employing on wages.<BR>—3 Purchasing or buying of.<BR>—4 Barter, exchange.<BR>—5 A peace purchased with the payment of money; कोषान् रक्षार्धकोषेण<BR> सर्वकोषेण वा पुनः । शेषप्रकृतिरक्षार्थं परिक्रय उदाहृतः ॥ Kām.; cf. H. 4. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लान्त|परिक्लांत
परिक्लान्त <i>a.</i> Fatigued, exhausted, tired out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0971-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिश्
परिक्लिश् I. €9 P. To torment, trouble, harass. ━II. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To feel pain, suffer.<BR>—2 To be vexed or troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिष्ट
परिक्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Vexed. troubled.<BR>—2 Exhausted, fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिष्टम्
परिक्लिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Pain, vexation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लेशः|परिक्लेश
परिक्लेशः Fatigue, trouble, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लेदः|परिक्लेद
परिक्लेदः Wetness, dampness, moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्वणन|परिक्वणनः
परिक्वणन <i>a.</i> Loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्वणनः|परिक्वणन
परिक्वणन + .{@-नः@} Ved. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षत
परिक्षत <i>a.</i> Wounded, hurt, injured; परिक्षते वक्षसि दन्तिदन्तैः Ki. 16. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षतिः|परिक्षति
परिक्षतिः <i>f.</i> Injury, hurt, harm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षा
परिक्षा Clay, mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षवः|परिक्षव
परिक्षवः Ill-omened sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षाम
परिक्षाम <i>a.</i> Emaciated, wasted away, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षालनम्
परिक्षालनम्<BR>—1 Washing, cleansing.<BR>—2 Water for washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षि
परिक्षि €5. €9 P.<BR>—1 To decay, wane.<BR>—2 To be emaciated or lean.<BR>—3 To destroy, put an end to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षयः|परिक्षय
परिक्षयः<BR>—1 Decay, waste, destruction; परिक्षयोऽपि अधिकं रमणीयः Mk. 1;<BR> किरण˚ Ku. 4. 46.<BR>—2 Disappearing, ceasing.<BR>—3 Ruin, loss, failure; व्रजाद्भिरार्द्रेन्धनवत्परिक्षयम् Ki. 16. 57; Ms. 9. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीण
परिक्षीण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>—2 Wasted, decayed.<BR>—3 Emaciated, worn away, exhausted; सदादानः परिक्षीणः शस्त एव करीश्वरः Pt. 2. 75.<BR>—4 Impoverished, entirely ruined; परिक्षीणः कश्चित् स्पृहयति यवानां<BR> प्रसृतये Bh. 2. 45.<BR>—5 Lost, destroyed.<BR>—6 Diminished, decreased; प्राण˚ Pt. 4. 23.<BR>—7 (In law) Insolvent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षित्
परिक्षित् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of a king, son of Abhimanyu and father of Janamejaya.<BR>—2 An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्
परिक्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To surround; गङ्गास्रोतःपरिक्षिप्तम् Ku. 6. 38.<BR>—2 To embrace.<BR>—3 To put or lay round.<BR>—4 To survey round, measure, range over.<BR>—5 To throw over or beyond.<BR>—6 To throw or put into.<BR>—7 To fetter, chain.<BR>—8 To deride; प्रणयाच्चाभिमानाच्च परिचिक्षेप राघवम् Rām. 2. 30. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्त|परिक्षिप्तं
परिक्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered, diffused.<BR>—2 Encircled, surrounded; कुशचीरपरिक्षिप्तम् Rām. 3. 1. 2. वेतसपरिक्षिप्ते<BR> मण्डपे Ś. 3.<BR>—3 Intrenched.<BR>—4 Overspread, overlaid.<BR>—5 Left, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेपः|परिक्षेप
परिक्षेपः<BR>—1 Moving about, walking to and fro.<BR>—2 Scattering, spreading.<BR>—3 Surrounding, encircling, circumfluence; circuit; अहोरात्रपरिक्षेपम् Mb. 14. 45. 3.<BR>—2 An enclosing belt or boundary, that by which anything is surrounded;<BR> महार्णवपरिक्षेपं लङ्कायाः परिखालघुम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">Page0972-2</a>]<BR> (मेने) R. 12. 66.<BR>—5 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>—6 An organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीव
परिक्षीव <i>a.</i> Quite intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखण्डयति
परिखण्डयति Den. P. To humiliate, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखा
परिखा<BR>—1 A moat, ditch, trench round a fort or town; Mb. 5. 243. 23; स वेलावप्रवलयां<BR> परिखीकृतसागराम् (उवी शशास) R. 1. 30, 12. 66; तस्य परिखास्तिस्रो<BR> दण्डान्तराः कारयेत् Kau. A. 2. 2. 21.<BR>—2 The bottom, depth; (fig.) root; बुद्धिर्ममैषा परिखास्थितस्य माभूद्विचारस्तव<BR> धर्मपुत्र Mb. 12. 167. 39 (परिखास्थित impregnable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखातम्
परिखातम्<BR>—1 A moat, ditch.<BR>—2 A rut, furrow.<BR>—3 Digging round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखिद्
परिखिद् €4 P. To suffer pain or misery, be distressed or wearied.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To injure, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखिन्न
परिखिन्न <i>p. p.</i> Afflicted, troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखेदः|परिखेद
परिखेदः Fatigue, exhaustion, lassitude; नियमितपरिखेदा तच्छिरश्चन्द्रपादैः<BR> Ku. 1. 60; हुतवहपरिखेदादाशु निर्गत्य कक्षात् Ṛs. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्या
परिख्या €2 P. Ved.<BR>—1 To look at, perceive.<BR>—2 To regard, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्यात|परिख्यातः
परिख्यात <i>a.</i> Celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्यातिः|परिख्याति
परिख्यातिः <i>f.</i> Fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगण्
परिगण् €10 U.<BR>—1 To enumerate, count.<BR>—2 consider, regard, think; अपरिगणयन् Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणनम्
परिगणनम्, -ना<BR> Complete enumeration, accurate statement or calculation; श्रेणीभूताः<BR> परिगणनया निर्दिशन्तो बलाकाः Me. (considered as an interpolation<BR> or क्षेपक by Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणना
परिगणनम्, -ना<BR> Complete enumeration, accurate statement or calculation; श्रेणीभूताः<BR> परिगणनया निर्दिशन्तो बलाकाः Me. (considered as an interpolation<BR> or क्षेपक by Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगम्
परिगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go or walk round; तं हयं तत्र परिगम्य Rām.; यथा हि<BR> मेरुः सूर्येण नित्यशः परिगम्यते Mb.<BR>—2 To surround; विशदप्रभापरिगतम् Śi. 9. 26; Bk. 10. 1; सेनापरिगत &c.<BR>—3 To spread everywhere, pervade all directions.<BR>—4 To attain to, obtain; वृषलताम् &c.<BR>—5 To know, understand, learn; प्रथमपरिगतार्थस्तं रघुः संनिवृत्तम् R. 7. 71.<BR>—6 To die, go forth (from this world); वयं येभ्यो जाताश्चिरपरिगता<BR> एव खलु ते Bh. 3. 38.<BR>—7 To overpower, affect; as in क्षुधया परिगतः. ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> pass or spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगत|परिगतः
परिगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Surrounded, enclosed, encircled; परिगततटभूमिः स्नानमात्रोत्थिताभिः<BR> (वधूभिः) Māl. 4. 10.<BR>—2 Diffused, spread around; ममापि च क्षपयतु नीललोहितः पुनर्भवं<BR> परिगतशक्तिरात्मभूः Ś. 7. 35.<BR>—3 Known, understood; R. 7. 71; परिगतपरिगन्तव्य एव भवान् Ve. 3; Mv. 3. 47.<BR>—4 Filled or covered with, possessed of (usually in comp.); Śi. 9. 26.<BR>—5 Got, obtained; भ्रमणपरिगतं भैक्षमक्षय्यमन्नम् Bh. 3. 52.<BR>—6 Remembered.<BR>—7 Overcome, over-whelmed.<BR>—8 Affected by, afflicted with; अपि स्थाणुवदासीनः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">Page0973-1</a>]<BR> शुष्यन् परिगतः क्षुधा । न त्वेवानात्मसंपन्नाद् वृत्तिमीहेत पण्डितः ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 49.<BR>—9 Performed.<BR>—10 Forgotten.<BR>—11 Obstructed, hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0972-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमः|परिगम
परिगमः, परिगमनम्<BR>—1 round, surrounding.<BR>—2 Spreading, diffusing.<BR>—3 Obtaining.<BR>—4 Knowing, determining, ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमनम्
परिगमः, परिगमनम्<BR>—1 round, surrounding.<BR>—2 Spreading, diffusing.<BR>—3 Obtaining.<BR>—4 Knowing, determining, ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगर्हणम्
परिगर्हणम् Excessive blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलित
परिगलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sunk.<BR>—2 Tumbled or dropped down.<BR>—3 Vanished.<BR>—4 Melted.<BR>—5 Flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगाढ
परिगाढ <i>a.</i> Very much; परिगाढकृशः Ki. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगुणित
परिगुणित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Reiterated, repeated.<BR>—2 Augmented by addition; Bhāg. 5. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगूढ
परिगूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Quite secret.<BR>—2 Incomprehensible, very difficult to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगै
परिगै €1 P. To sing, relate, describe, celebrate, or proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगीति
परिगीति <i>f.</i> A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रह्
परिग्रह् €9 P.<BR>—1 To clasp round, embrace.<BR>—2 To encircle; surround, fence or hedge round; न्यविशन्त ततः सर्वे<BR> परिगृह्य सरस्वतीम् Mb. 5. 178. 23.<BR>—3 To lay hold of, seize.<BR>—4 To take, assume.<BR>—5 To accept.<BR>—6 To favour, patronize; देवेन च परिगृहीतः M. 1, 1. 13.<BR>—7 To support, assist, guide; राक्षसमतिपरिगृहीतः Mu. 1.<BR>—8 To put on (a dress).<BR>—9 To take possession of, master, overpower.<BR>—10 To conceive, comprehend.<BR>—11 To undertake.<BR>—12 To receive hospitably; परिग्रहेण ब्राह्मेण परिगृह्य महाद्युतिः Mb. 1. 195. 1.<BR>—13 To take (a wife), marry; प्रथमपरिगृहीतं स्यान्न वेत्यव्यवस्यन् Ś. 5. 19.<BR>—14 To conform to, follow.<BR>—15 To surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीत
परिगृहीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Grasped, seized, clutched.<BR>—2 Embraced, surrounded.<BR>—3 Accepted, taken, received.<BR>—4 Assented or consented to, admitted.<BR>—5 Patronized, favoured.<BR>—6 Followed, obeyed, observed.<BR>—7 Married,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीतिः|परिगृहीति
परिगृहीतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Grasping, comprehension.<BR>—2 Summing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृह्या
परिगृह्या A married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहः|परिग्रह
परिग्रहः —1 Seizing, holding, taking, grasping; आसनरज्जुपरिग्रहे<BR> R. 9. 46; शङ्कापरिग्रहः Mu. 1<BR> ‘taking or entertaining a doubt’.<BR>—2 Surrounding, enclosing, encircling, fencing round.<BR>—3 Putting on, wrapping round (as a dress); मौलिपरिग्रहः R. 18. 38.<BR>—4 Assuming, taking; मानपरिग्रहः Amaru. 97; विवाहलक्ष्मी˚ U. 4.<BR>—5 Receiving, taking, accepting, acceptance; भौमो मुनेः स्थानपरिग्रहोऽयम्<BR> R. 13. 36; अर्घ्यपरिग्रहान्ते 70, 12. 16; Ku. 6. 53; विद्यापरिग्रहाय<BR> Māl. 1; so आसनपरिग्रहं करोतु देवः U. 3 ‘your majesty will be pleased to take a seat or sit down’<BR>.<BR>—6 Possessions, property, belongings; त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः Bg. 4. 21;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">Page0973-2</a>]<BR> R. 15. 55; V. 4. 26.<BR>—7 Taking in marriage, marriage; नवे दारपरिग्रहे U. 1. 19; Māl. 5. 27;<BR> असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा Ś. 1. 22; न हि गणयति<BR> क्षुद्रो जन्तुः परिग्रहफल्गुताम् Bh. 1. 9.<BR>—8 A wife, queen; प्रयतपरिग्रहद्वितीयः R. 1. 95, 92, 9. 14, 11. 33, 16. 8;<BR> Ś. 5. 28, 31; परिग्रहबहुत्वेऽपि Ś. 3. 19; प्राप श्रियं<BR> मुनिवरस्य परिग्रहोऽसौ Rām. Ch.<BR>—9 Taking under oneʼs protection, favouring; धन्याः स्मो वः परिग्रहात्<BR> U. 7. 11; M. 1. 13; कुर्वन्ति पाण्डवपरिग्रहमेव पौराः Pañc. 1. 20.<BR>—10 Attendants, followers, train, retinue, suite; परिग्रहेण सर्वेण<BR> कोषेण च महीयसा Śiva B. 8. 40.<BR>—11 A household, family, members of a family.<BR>—12 The seraglio or household of a king, harem.<BR>—13 Anything received, a present; राजपरिग्रहोऽयम् Ś. 1.<BR>—14 Assent, consent.<BR>—15 Taking possession of, acquiring.<BR>—16 A claim.<BR>—17 Entertaining, honouring, receiving (a guest &c.). Mb. 1. 195. 1.<BR>—18 An entertainer.<BR>—19 Assistance.<BR>—20 A husband.<BR>—21 Respect, reverence.<BR>—22 Grace, favour.<BR>—23 Comprehension, understanding.<BR>—24 Undertaking, performing.<BR>—25 Subjugation; धर्षितो मत्परिग्रहः Mb. 12. 320. 55.<BR>—26 Dominion.<BR>—27 Punishment.<BR>—28 Connection, relation.<BR>—29 Summing up, totality.<BR>—30 A house, residence.<BR>—31 Removing, taking away.<BR>—32 A curse; निर्मुक्तनिष्ठुरपरिग्रहपाशबन्धः Rām. Ch. (cf. पत्नीपरिजनादानमूलशापाः<BR> परिग्रहाः Ak.).<BR>—33 (In Ved. gram.) The double mention of a word both before and after इति.<BR>—34 The form which precedes इति.<BR>—35 Root, origin.<BR>—36 The eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>—37 An oath.<BR>—38 The rear of an army.<BR>—39 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—40 The body; आश्रयन्त्याः स्वभावेन मम पूर्वपरिग्रहम् Mb. 12. 320. 57<BR> (com. स्वभावेन चित्तेन मम परिग्रहं शरीरम् आश्रयन्त्याः).<BR>—41 Administration; राज्यपरिग्रहः Mb. 12. 320. 51.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिग्रहार्थीय, परिग्रहद्वितीय, परिग्रहबहुत्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहार्थीय
परिग्रहः + -अर्थीय <i>a.</i> generalizing; having the sense of comprehension; Nir. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहद्वितीय
परिग्रहः + -द्वितीय <i>a.</i> accompanied by oneʼs wife or family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहबहुत्वम्
परिग्रहः + -बहुत्वम् multitude of wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहणम्
परिग्रहणम् Wrapping round, putting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहीतृ
परिग्रहीतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A husband; तामद्य संप्रेष्य परिग्रहीतुः Ś. 4. 22.<BR>—2 An assistant.<BR>—3 An adoptive father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राहः|परिग्राह
परिग्राहः The fencing round of the sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राहक
परिग्राहक <i>a.</i> Favouring, befriending; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राह्य
परिग्राह्य <i>a.</i> To be treated or addressed kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्लान
परिग्लान <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Languid, exhausted.<BR>—2 Averse from, disinclined to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघः|परिघ
परिघः<BR>—1 An iron (or wooden) beam or bar used for locking or shutting a gate<BR> (अर्गल); एकः कृत्स्नां नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Ś. 2. 16;<BR> R. 16. 84; Śi. 19. 32; M. 5. 2.<BR>—2 (Hence) A bar, barrier, hindrance, obstacle; भार्गवस्य सुकृतोऽपि<BR> सोऽभवत् स्वर्गमार्गपरिघो दुरत्ययः R. 11. 88.<BR>—3 A stick or club studded or tipped with iron; पादपाविद्धपरिघः R. 12. 73.<BR>—4 An iron club in general. It is a kind of weapon (परितो हन्तीती-सर्वतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">Page0974-1</a>]<BR> कण्टकितो लोहदण्डः com. on Mb. 1. 19. 17); … … हन्तुं घोरं<BR> परिघमाददे Śiva B. 14. 99.<BR>—5 A water-jar, pitcher.<BR>—6 A glass-pitcher.<BR>—7 A house, dwelling.<BR>—8 Killing, destroying.<BR>—9 Striking, a stroke or blow.<BR>—10 A child which assumes a peculiar cross position in birth.<BR>—11 A line of clouds crossing the sun at sunrise or sunset.<BR>—12 The gate of a palace, town or house. Hence perhaps it means ‘Gate-duty’;<BR> मूलं भागो व्याजी परिघः कॢप्तं रूपिकमत्ययश्चाय-मुखम् Kau. A. 2. 6. 24.<BR>—13 (In astrol.) N. of the 19th Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघौ
परिघः + .{@-घौ@} <i>m.</i> (du.) Two birds flying on each side of a traveller<BR> (regarded as an omen).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिघगुरु, परिघस्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0973-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघगुरु
परिघः + -गुरु <i>a.</i> as heavy as an iron bar; M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघस्तम्भः|परिघस्तम्भ
परिघः + -स्तम्भः a door-post; M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्ट्
परिघट्ट् €10 U.<BR>—1 To strike; तव सा कथासु परिघट्टयति श्रवणं यदङ्गुलिमुखेन<BR> मुहुः Śi. 9. 64.<BR>—2 To stir up.<BR>—3 To touch or press on all sides.<BR>—4 To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्टनम्
परिघट्टनम् Stirring up, stirring round; अस्मिन् महामोहमये कटाहे<BR> सूर्याग्निना रात्रिदिवेन्धनेन । मासर्तुदर्वीपरिघट्टनेन भूतानि कालः पचतीति<BR> वार्ता ॥ Mb. 3. 313. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघर्मः|परिघर्म
परिघर्मः, -र्म्यः<BR> A vessel for preparing the hot sacrificial beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघर्म्यः|परिघर्म्य
परिघर्मः, -र्म्यः<BR> A vessel for preparing the hot sacrificial beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातः|परिघात
परिघातः, -घातनम्<BR>—1 Killing, striking, removing, getting rid of.<BR>—2 A club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातनम्
परिघातः, -घातनम्<BR>—1 Killing, striking, removing, getting rid of.<BR>—2 A club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघोषः|परिघोष
परिघोषः<BR>—1 Noise.<BR>—2 Improper speech.<BR>—3 Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघ्रा
परिघ्रा See घ्रा. To kiss passionately, cover with kisses; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचक्ष्
परिचक्ष् €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To declare, relate, tell.<BR>—2 To enumerate.<BR>—3 To mention.<BR>—4 To name, call; वेदप्रदानादाचार्यं पितरं परिचक्षते Ms. 2. 171;<BR> श्रद्धाविरहितं यज्ञं तामसं परिचक्षते Bg. 17. 13, 17.<BR>—5 To disregard, overlook, pass over; revile; को वैनं परिचक्षीत<BR> Bhāg. 4. 14. 33.<BR>—6 To disapprove, reject.<BR>—7 To acknowledge, admit.<BR>—8 To address (with acc.).<BR>—9 To answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचक्षा
परिचक्षा Ved. Rejection, disapproval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचतुर्दशन्
परिचतुर्दशन् <i>a.</i> Fully fourteen; more than fourteen; भृत्याः<BR> परिचतुर्दश Mb. 3. 1. 11; so also परिदश; क्वचित् परिदशान् मासान्<BR> Rām. 3. 11. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचपल
परिचपल <i>a.</i> Always moving about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्
परिचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go or walk about.<BR>—2 To serve, wait or attend upon; Ms. 2. 243; गुणोदारान् दारानुत परिचरामः<BR> सविनयम् Bh. 3. 40.<BR>—3 To worship, adore, reverence; अनुत्पन्नं ज्ञानं यदि यदि च संदेहविधुरं<BR> विपर्यस्तं वा स्यात् परिचर वसिष्ठस्य चरणौ Mv. 3. 36.<BR>—4 To take care of, nurse, tend. ━<i>Caus.</i> To enclose, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर|परिचरः
परिचर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Roaming or moving about.<BR>—2 Flowing.<BR>—3 Movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरः|परिचर
परिचर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A servant, follower, an attendant.<BR>—2 A body-guard.<BR>—3 A guard or patrol in general.<BR>—4 Homage, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरणः|परिचरण
परिचरणः A servant, an attendant, assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरणम्
परिचरणः + .{@-णम्@} (also परिचारणम्)<BR>—1 Serving, attending or waiting upon; शूद्रधर्मः समाख्यातस्त्रिवर्गपरिचारणम्<BR> Mb. 13. 141. 75.<BR>—2 Going about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरितृ
परिचरितृ <i>m.</i> A servant, an attendant; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्या|परिचर्य्या
परिचर्या<BR>—1 Service, attendance; R. 1. 91; कृषिगोरक्ष्यवाणिज्यं वैश्यकर्म स्वभावजम् ।<BR> परिचर्यात्मकं कर्म शूद्रस्यापि स्वभावजम् ॥ Bg. 18. 44.<BR>—2 Adoration, worship; ग्रहीतुमार्यान् परिचर्यया मुहुः Śi. 1. 17.<BR>—3 Conduct (आचार); Mb. 5. 39. 44.<BR>—4 Circumambulation (प्रदक्षिणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारः|परिचार
परिचारः<BR>—1 Service, attendance; शुश्रूषां परिचारं च देववद्या करोति च<BR> Mb. 13. 146. 37.<BR>—2 A servant.<BR>—3 A place for walking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारकः|परिचारक
परिचारकः, परिचारिकः, परिचारिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A servant, an attendant.<BR>—2 A Śūdra; मुखजा ब्राह्मणास्तात … पादजाः परिचारकाः Mb. 12. 296. 6.<BR>—3 An executor (of an order).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिकः|परिचारिक
परिचारकः, परिचारिकः, परिचारिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A servant, an attendant.<BR>—2 A Śūdra; मुखजा ब्राह्मणास्तात … पादजाः परिचारकाः Mb. 12. 296. 6.<BR>—3 An executor (of an order).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिन्
परिचारकः, परिचारिकः, परिचारिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A servant, an attendant.<BR>—2 A Śūdra; मुखजा ब्राह्मणास्तात … पादजाः परिचारकाः Mb. 12. 296. 6.<BR>—3 An executor (of an order).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिका
परिचारिका<BR>—1 A female servant; भुञ्जते रुक्मपात्रीभिर्यत्राहं परिचारिका Mb. 3. 30. 13.<BR>—2 (pl.) Fried grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचार्य|परिचार्य्य|परिचार्य्यः
परिचार्य <i>a.</i> To be served, obeyed or worshipped; एष तस्यापि<BR> ते मार्गः परिचार्यस्य गालव Mb. 5. 109. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारितम्
परिचारितम् Amusement, sport; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचीर्ण
परिचीर्ण <i>a.</i> Worshipped; भवेयुरग्नयस्तस्य परिचीर्णास्तु नित्यशः<BR> Mb. 3. 214. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्मण्यम्
परिचर्मण्यम् A strip of leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचाय्यः|परिचाय्य
परिचाय्यः Sacrificial fire (arranged in a circle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचि
परिचि I. €5 U.<BR>—1 To heap up, accumulate.<BR>—2 To know; एता भुवः परिचिनोषि Mv. 7. 11.<BR>—3 To get, acquire.<BR>—4 To increase.<BR>—5 To cover or fill with. ━II. €3 P.<BR>—1 To practise, familiarize oneself with<BR>—2 To become acquainted with.<BR>—3 Ved. To examine, investigate. ━<i>Caus.</i> To search, seek for. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR> To grow, be developed; (यत्प्रेम परस्पराश्रयम्) विभक्तमप्येकसुतेन<BR> तत्तयोः परस्परस्योपरि पर्यचीयत R. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयः|परिचय
परिचयः<BR>—1 Heaping up, accumulation.<BR>—2 Acquaintance; familiarity, intimacy; पुरुषपरिचयेन Mk. 1. 56;<BR> अतिपरिचयादवज्ञा ‘familiarity breeds contempt’; परिचयं चललक्ष्यनिपातने<BR> R. 9. 49; सकलकलापरिचयः K. 76.<BR>—3 Trial, study, practice, frequent repetition; हेतुः परिचयेस्थैर्ये<BR> वक्तुर्गुणनिकैव सा Śi. 2. 75, 11. 5; वर्णपरिचयं करोति Ś. 5.<BR>—4 Recognition; Me. 9.<BR>—5 Stay; चिरं मातुलपरिचयादविज्ञातवृत्तान्तोऽस्मि Pratimā 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिचयकरुणा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयकरुणा
परिचयः + -करुणा increasing love or tenderness; तदिह सुवदनायां तात<BR> मत्तः परस्तात् परिचयकरुणायां सर्वथा मा विरंसीः Māl. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयवत्|परिचयवन्त्
परिचयवत् <i>a.</i> Being at its height, complete; शठ इति मयि<BR> तावदस्तु ते परिचयवत्यवधीरणा प्रिये M. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचित|परिचितः
परिचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heaped up, accumulated; निजरमणारुणचरणारविन्दानुध्यानपरिचितभक्तियोगेन<BR> Bhāg. 5. 7. 12.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">Page0975-1</a>]<BR>—2 Familiar, intimate or acquainted with; परिचितपरिक्लेशकृपया Mu. 6. 12;<BR> शश्वत् परिचितविविक्तेन मनसा Ś. 5. 10.<BR>—3 Learnt, practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0974-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचितिः|परिचिति
परिचितिः <i>f.</i> Acquaintance, familiarity, intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिन्त्|परिचिंत्
परिचिन्त् €10 U.<BR>—1 To think, consider, judge; त्वमेव तावत् परिचिन्तय स्वयं कदाचिदेते<BR> यदि योगमर्हतः Ku. 5. 67; कथं विद्यामहं योगिंस्त्वां सदा परिचिन्तयन् Bg. 10. 17.<BR>—2 To think of, remember, call to mind.<BR>—3 To devise, find out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिन्तनम्
परिचिन्तनम् Thinking of, remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचुद्
परिचुद् €10 P. To urge, impel, exhort; गुणैश्च परिचोदयेत् Ms. 3. 233.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचुम्ब्|परिचुंब्
परिचुम्ब् €1 P. To kiss passionately; परिचुम्ब्य चूतमञ्जरीम् Ś. 5. 1;<BR> Ṛs. 6. 17; विस्रब्धं परिचुम्ब्य जातपुलकामालोक्य गण्डस्थलीम् Amaru. 82<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचुम्बनम्
परिचुम्बनम् Kissing passionately; परिचितपरिचुम्बनाभियोगादपगतकुङ्कुमरेणुभिः<BR> कपोलैः Śi. 7. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद्
परिच्छद् €10 U.<BR>—1 To cover, clothe; दर्भैस्तं परिच्छाद्य Pt. 2; द्वीपिचर्मपरिच्छन्नः<BR> (गर्दभः) H. 3. 9.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal.<BR>—3 To surround with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद्
परिच्छद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Retinue, train.<BR>—2 Paraphernalia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छदः|परिच्छद|परिछद
परिच्छदः<BR>—1 A covering, cover, canopy, awning; विद्यालयं सितगृहं सपरिच्छदं<BR> तत् Bil. C. 20; पयःफेननिभा शय्या दान्ता रुक्मपरिच्छदा Bhāg.;<BR> दर्शनीयास्तु काम्बोजाः शुकपत्रपरिच्छदाः Mb. 7. 23. 7 (com. शुकपत्रपरिच्छदाः<BR> शुकपत्राभरोमाणः).<BR>—2 A garment, clothes, dress; शाखावसक्तकमनीयपरिच्छदानाम् Ki. 7. 40.<BR>—3 Train, retinue, attendants, circle of dependants; नरपतिरतिवाहयांबभूव<BR> क्वचिदसमेतपरिच्छदस्त्रियामाम्; R. 9. 70.<BR>—4 Paraphernalia, external appendage, (as छत्र, चामर); सेना परिच्छदस्तस्य R. 1. 19.<BR>—5 Goods and chattels, personal property, all oneʼs possessions or belongings<BR> (utensils, implements &c.); विवास्यो वा भवेद्राष्ट्रात् सद्रव्यः सपरिच्छदः<BR> Ms. 9. 241, 7. 40, 8. 405, 9. 78, 11. 76; अभिषेकाय रामस्य यत्कर्म<BR> सपरिच्छदम् Rām.; स्रुग्भाण्डमरणीं दर्भानुपभुङ्क्ते हुताशनः । व्यसनित्वान्नरः<BR> क्षीणः परिच्छदमिवात्मनः ॥<BR>—6 Necessaries for travelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्दः|परिच्छन्द|परिच्छंद|परिच्छंदः
परिच्छन्दः Train, retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्न|परिच्छन्नः|परिछन्न
परिच्छन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Enveloped, covered, clothed, clad.<BR>—2 Overspread or overlaid.<BR>—3 Surrounded with (a retinue).<BR>—4 Concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिद्
परिच्छिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To tear, cut off, tear to pieces.<BR>—2 To wound, mutilate.<BR>—3 To separate, divide, part; शतेन परिच्छिद्य Sk.<BR>—4 To fix accurately, set limits to, define, decide, distinguish or discriminate;<BR> मध्यस्था भगवती नौ गुणदोषतः परिच्छेत्तुमर्हति M. 1; (न)<BR> यशः परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालम् R. 6. 77, 17. 59; Ku. 2. 58.<BR>—5 To avert, obviate, remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छित्तिः|परिच्छित्ति|परिछित्ति
परिच्छित्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Accurate definition, limiting.<BR>—2 Partition, separation, division.<BR>—3 Limit, measure; P. III. 3. 20. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिन्न|परिच्छिन्नः|परिछिन्न
परिच्छिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cut off, divided.<BR>—2 Accurately defined, determined, ascertained; परिच्छिन्नप्रभावर्धिर्न<BR> मया न च विष्णुना Ku. 2. 58.<BR>—3 Limited, circumscribed, confined.<BR>—4 Remedied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदः|परिच्छेद|परिछेद
परिच्छेदः<BR>—1 Cutting, separating, dividing, discriminating (between right and wrong).<BR>—2 Accurate, definition or distinction, decision, accurate determination,<BR> ascertainment; परिच्छेदव्यक्तिर्भवति न पुरःस्थेऽपि विषये Māl. 1. 31;<BR> परिच्छेदातीतः सकलवचनानामविषयः 1. 30 ‘transcending all definition or determination’<BR>; इत्यारूढबहुप्रतर्कमपरिच्छेदाकुलं<BR> मे मनः Ś. 5. 9.<BR>—3 Discrimination, judgment, discernment; परिच्छेदो हि पाण्डित्यं यदापन्ना<BR> विपत्तयः । अपरिच्छेदकर्तॄणां विपदः स्युः पदे पदे H. 1. 128; किं<BR> पाण्डित्यं परिच्छेदः 1. 127.<BR>—4 A limit, boundary, setting limits to, circumscribing; अलमलं परिच्छेदेन M. 2.<BR>—5 A section, chapter or division of a work (for the other names for section<BR> &c. see under अध्याय).<BR>—6 A segment.<BR>—7 Remedying.<BR>—8 A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदकम्
परिच्छेदकम् Limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदनम्
परिच्छेदनम्<BR>—1 Discriminating.<BR>—2 Dividing.<BR>—3 A division of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद्य
परिच्छेद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be accurately defined, definable; प्रत्यक्षोऽप्यपरिच्छेद्यो मह्यादिर्महिमा<BR> तव R. 10. 28.<BR>—2 To be weighed or estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्यु
परिच्यु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go away or fly off from, escape.<BR>—2 To proceed from.<BR>—3 To swerve, fall off from, deviate, leave.<BR>—4 To lose, be deprived of.<BR>—5 To drop or fall down.<BR>—6 To be displaced or ejected from.<BR>—7 To be freed from.<BR>—8 To come down, descend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्यवनम्
परिच्यवनम्<BR>—1 Descending from heaven.<BR>—2 Loss, deprivation of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्युतिः|परिच्युति
परिच्युतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Falling down.<BR>—2 Swerving, deviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजनः|परिजन
परिजनः<BR>—1 Attendants, followers, servants taken collectively; परिजनो राजानमभितः<BR> स्थितः M. 1.<BR>—2 Especially, the retinue, suite, or train of females, the maids of a<BR> lady; अन्वभूत् परिजनाङ्गनारतम् R. 19. 23.<BR>—3 A single servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजनता
परिजनता Service; the condition of a servant; परिजनताऽपि गुणाय<BR> सद्गुणानाम् Ki. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजन्मन्
परिजन्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजल्पितम्
परिजल्पितम् A covert indication (as by a servant) of oneʼs own skill,<BR> superiority &c. by pointing out the cruelty, deceitfulness and such other<BR> faults of his master; Ujjvalamaṇi thus defines it:− प्रभोर्निर्दयताशाठ्यचापलाद्युपपादनात् ।<BR> स्वविचक्षणताव्यक्तिर्भङ्ग्या स्यात् परिजल्पितम् ॥ (Wilson renders the<BR> word by ‘the covert reproaches of a mistress neglected or ill-used by her lover’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0975-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजीर्ण
परिजीर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Worn out, faded.<BR>—2 Digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञा
परिज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To be aware of; know, be acquainted with; वृषभोऽयमिति परिज्ञाय<BR> Pt. 1; Ms. 8. 126.<BR>—2 To find out, ascertain; सम्यक् परिज्ञाय Pt. 1.<BR>—3 To recognise; तपस्विभिः कैशिचत् परिज्ञातोऽस्मि Ś. 2.<BR>—4 To observe, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञप्तिः|परिज्ञप्ति
परिज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Conversation, discourse.<BR>—2 Recognition; जातायां च परिज्ञप्तौ ज्ञातबन्धुक्षयोऽथ सः Ks. 21. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञा
परिज्ञा, परिज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Thorough knowledge, complete acquaintance; यत्ते मम परिज्ञाने कौतुहलमरिंदम<BR> Mb. 3. 147. 26.<BR>—2 Recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञानम्
परिज्ञा, परिज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Thorough knowledge, complete acquaintance; यत्ते मम परिज्ञाने कौतुहलमरिंदम<BR> Mb. 3. 147. 26.<BR>—2 Recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञातृ
परिज्ञातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A knower, observer.<BR>—2 Wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञेय
परिज्ञेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be recognised or ascertained.<BR>—2 Comprehensible, conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्मन्
परिज्मन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Running or walking round.<BR>—2 Omnipresent. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्रि
परिज्रि <i>a.</i> Running round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्वन्
परिज्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिडीनम्
परिडीनम् The flight of a bird in circles; see डीन; Mb. 8. 41. 27<BR> (com. परिडीनं तु सर्वतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणम्
परिणम् €1 U.<BR>—1 To stoop, bend down (as an elephant to strike with his tusks); विष्के<BR> नागः पर्यणंसीत् स्व एव Śi. 18. 27.<BR>—2 To bend or bow down, be inclined; लज्जापरिणतैः (वदनकमलैः) Bh. 1. 4.<BR>—3 To be changed or transformed into, assume the form of (with instr.);<BR> लताभावेन परिणतमस्या रूपम् V. 4, 4. 28; क्षीरं जलं वा स्वयमेव<BR> दधिहिमभावेन परिणमते Ś. B.; स्रोतोमूर्त्या भुवि परिणतां रन्तिदेवस्य<BR> कीर्तिम् Me. 47.<BR>—4 To result; happen; सर्वं विपरीतं परिणमति Mk. 1.<BR>—5 To be developed or matured, be ripe; छन्नोपान्तः परिणतफलद्योतिभिः<BR> काननाम्रैः Me. 18; शाखाभृतां परिणमन्ति न पल्लवानि Ki. 5. 37;<BR> M. 3. 8; परिणतदलशाखाः (वृक्षाः) Ṛs. 1. 26; Mv. 1. 12; see<BR> परिणत below.<BR>—6 To be advanced (in age), grow old, be aged, decay; परिणतशरच्चन्द्रिकासु<BR> क्षपासु Me. 112; so जरापरिणत &c.<BR>—7 To set, decline in the west (as the sun); अनेन समयेन परिणतो<BR> दिवसः K. 47.<BR>—8 To be digested; ग्रस्तं परिणमेच्च यत् Mb.<BR>—9 To be cooked or roasted; निष्टापस्विद्यदस्थ्नः क्वथनपरिणमन्मेदसः<BR> प्रेतकायान् Māl. 5. 17.<BR>—10 To elapse (as time). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To make ripe, mature, develop, perfect.<BR>—2 To pass (as the night); परिणाम्य निशां तत्र Rām. 3. 8. 1; तत्र<BR> काकसहस्राणि तां निशां पर्यणामयन् Mb. 10. 1. 36.<BR>—3 To stoop, bend oneself down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bent or bowed down, stooping; वप्रक्रीडापरिणतगजप्रेक्षणीयं ददर्श Me. 2;<BR>—2 Declining, old (as age); परिणते वयसि K. 35, 62, 63.<BR>—3 Ripe, matured, ripened, fully developed or formed; शब्दब्रह्मविदः<BR> कवेः परिणतप्रज्ञस्य वाणीमिमाम् U. 7. 21, 1. 39, 6. 13; Me. 23; परिणतमकरन्दमार्मिकास्ते<BR> Bv. 1. 8; Śi. 11. 39.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">Page0976-2</a>]<BR>—4 Full-grown, advanced, perfected; परिणतशरच्चन्द्रकिरणैः Bh. 3. 49;<BR> Me. 112; परिच्छिन्नामेवं त्वयि परिणता विभ्रतु गिरम् Śivamahimna 26.<BR>—5 Digested (as food).<BR>—6 Transformed or changed into (with instr.); V. 4. 28.<BR>—7 Ended, come to a close, terminated; संप्रति परिणतमहः Nāg. 3.<BR>—8 Set (as the sun); पतति परिणतारुणप्रकाशः Ś. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतः|परिणत|परिणतं
परिणत + .{@-तः@} An elephant stooping to strike with his tusks, or giving<BR> a side-blow with his tusks; (तिर्यग्दन्तप्रहारश्च गजः परिणतो मतः<BR> Halāy.); परिणतदिक्करिकास्तटीर्बिभर्ति Śi. 4. 29; Ki. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतम्
परिणत + .{@-तम्@} Capital, wealth accumulated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिणतप्रज्ञ, परिणतप्रत्यय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतप्रज्ञ
परिणत + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> of mature understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतप्रत्यय
परिणत + -प्रत्यय whose results are matured (an action).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतिः|परिणति
परिणतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bending or stooping down, bowing.<BR>—2 Ripeness, maturity, development; कृशपरिणति चेतः Śivamahimna 31;<BR> प्रभुत्वस्योत्कर्षात् परिणतिविशुद्धेश्च तपसामसौ दृष्टः सत्त्वं प्रबलयति Mv. 2. 15.<BR>—3 Change, transformation, transmutation.<BR>—4 Fulfilment.<BR>—5 Result, consequence, issue; परिणतिरवधार्या यत्नतः पण्डितेन<BR> Bh. 2. 99, 1. 20, 3. 17; Mv. 6. 28; विधौ वामारम्भे मम समुचितैषा परिणतिः Māl. 4. 4.<BR>—6 End, conclusion, close, termination; परिणतिरमणीयाः प्रीतयस्त्वद्विधानाम्<BR> Māl. 6. 7, 16; Śi. 11. 1.<BR>—7 Close of life, old age; सेवाकारा परिणतिरभूत् V. 3. 1; अभवद्गतः<BR> परिणतिं शिथिलः परिमन्दसूर्यनयनो दिवसः Śi. 9. 3. (where प˚<BR> means ‘end or conclusion’ also).<BR>—8 Digestion (of food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणमनम्
परिणमनम् Change, transformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामक
परिणामक <i>a.</i> Causing a change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामः|परिणाम
परि(री)णामः<BR>—1 Alteration, change, transformation.<BR>—2 Digestion; अन्नं न सम्यक् परिणाममेति Suśr.; भुक्तस्य परिणामहेतुरौदर्यम्<BR> T. S.; Pt. 4. 22.<BR>—3 Result, consequence, issue, effect; अप्रियस्यापि पथ्यस्य परिणामः<BR> सुखावहः H. 2. 124; Mk. 3. 1; परिणामसुखे गरीयसि (वचसि औषधे<BR> च) Ki. 2. 4; Bg. 18. 37, 38.<BR>—4 Ripening, maturity, full development; उपैति शस्यं परिणामरम्यताम्<BR> Ki. 4. 22; फलभरपरिणामश्यामजम्बू &c. U. 2. 20; Māl. 9. 24.<BR>—5 End, termination, conclusion, close, decline; दिवसाः परिणामरमणीयाः<BR> Ś. 1. 3; वयःपरिणामपाण्डुरशिरसम् K. 10; परिणाममुपैति दिवसः<BR> K. 254 ‘the day is drawing to a close’.<BR>—6 Old age; परिणामे हि दिलीपवंशजाः R. 8. 11.<BR>—7 Lapse (of time).<BR>—8 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech allied to रूपक, by which the properties<BR> of any object are transferred to that with which it is compared. (The<BR> Chandrāloka thus defines and illustrates it:− परिणामः क्रियार्थश्चेद्विषयी<BR> विषयात्मना । प्रसन्नेन दृगब्जेन वीक्षते मदिरेक्षणा ॥ 5. 18; see R. G. also under परिणाम).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिणामजम्, परिणामदर्शिन्, परिणामदृष्टि, परिणामपथ्य, परिणाममुख, परिणामवादः, परिणामशूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणामः|परीणाम
परि(री)णामः<BR>—1 Alteration, change, transformation.<BR>—2 Digestion; अन्नं न सम्यक् परिणाममेति Suśr.; भुक्तस्य परिणामहेतुरौदर्यम्<BR> T. S.; Pt. 4. 22.<BR>—3 Result, consequence, issue, effect; अप्रियस्यापि पथ्यस्य परिणामः<BR> सुखावहः H. 2. 124; Mk. 3. 1; परिणामसुखे गरीयसि (वचसि औषधे<BR> च) Ki. 2. 4; Bg. 18. 37, 38.<BR>—4 Ripening, maturity, full development; उपैति शस्यं परिणामरम्यताम्<BR> Ki. 4. 22; फलभरपरिणामश्यामजम्बू &c. U. 2. 20; Māl. 9. 24.<BR>—5 End, termination, conclusion, close, decline; दिवसाः परिणामरमणीयाः<BR> Ś. 1. 3; वयःपरिणामपाण्डुरशिरसम् K. 10; परिणाममुपैति दिवसः<BR> K. 254 ‘the day is drawing to a close’.<BR>—6 Old age; परिणामे हि दिलीपवंशजाः R. 8. 11.<BR>—7 Lapse (of time).<BR>—8 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech allied to रूपक, by which the properties<BR> of any object are transferred to that with which it is compared. (The<BR> Chandrāloka thus defines and illustrates it:− परिणामः क्रियार्थश्चेद्विषयी<BR> विषयात्मना । प्रसन्नेन दृगब्जेन वीक्षते मदिरेक्षणा ॥ 5. 18; see R. G. also under परिणाम).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिणामजम्, परिणामदर्शिन्, परिणामदृष्टि, परिणामपथ्य, परिणाममुख, परिणामवादः, परिणामशूलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामजम्
परिणामः + -जम् Violent or painful indigestion (see शूलम् below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामदर्शिन्
परिणामः + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> prudent, fore-sighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामदृष्टि|परिणामदृष्टिः
परिणामः + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामदृष्टिः|परिणामदृष्टि
परिणामः + -दृष्टि + .({@-ष्टिः@} <i>f.</i>) prudence, providence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामपथ्य
परिणामः + -पथ्य <i>a.</i> salutary in the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाममुख
परिणामः + -मुख <i>a.</i> about to terminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामवादः|परिणामवाद
परिणामः + -वादः the Sāṅkhya doctrine of evolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामशूलम्
परिणामः + -शूलम् violent or painful indigestion, colic, flatulence with pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणह्
परिणह् €4 U.<BR>—1 To surround, intertwine, encircle; स जयति परिणद्धः शक्तिभिः<BR> शक्तिनाथः Māl. 5. 1; R. 6. 64; M. 5. 10; Ṛs. 6. 25.<BR>—2 To bind or tie round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0976-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणद्ध
परिणद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound or wrapped round.<BR>—2 Broad, large; परिणद्धकन्धरः R. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणहनम्
परिणहनम् Girding on, wrapping round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहः|परिणाह
परि(री)णाहः<BR>—1 Circumference, compass, expanse, extent, breadth, width; स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छदिना<BR> वल्कलेन Ś. 1. 19; स्तनपरिणाहविलासवैजयन्ती Māl. 3. 15 ‘large or expansive breasts’<BR>; ककुदे वृषस्य कृतबाहुमकृशपरिणाहशालिनि<BR> Ki. 12. 20; Mk. 3. 9; Ratn. 2. 13; Mv. 7. 24; नल्वमात्रपरीणाहो घनच्छायो<BR> वनस्पतिः Mb. 12. 154. 7.<BR>—2 Periphery or circumference of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणाहः|परीणाह
परि(री)णाहः<BR>—1 Circumference, compass, expanse, extent, breadth, width; स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छदिना<BR> वल्कलेन Ś. 1. 19; स्तनपरिणाहविलासवैजयन्ती Māl. 3. 15 ‘large or expansive breasts’<BR>; ककुदे वृषस्य कृतबाहुमकृशपरिणाहशालिनि<BR> Ki. 12. 20; Mk. 3. 9; Ratn. 2. 13; Mv. 7. 24; नल्वमात्रपरीणाहो घनच्छायो<BR> वनस्पतिः Mb. 12. 154. 7.<BR>—2 Periphery or circumference of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहवत्|परिणाहवन्त्
परिणाहवत् <i>a.</i> Large, big, expansive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहिन्
परिणाहिन् <i>a.</i> large, big; लब्ध्वापि लोके परिणाहि रूपम् Ku. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसक
परिणिंसक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tasting, eating; फलानां परिणिंसकः Bk. 9. 106.<BR>—2 Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिष्ठा
परिणिष्ठा Perfect skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणी
परिणी €1 P.<BR>—1 To lead or carry round (the fire); तौ दम्पती त्रिः परिणीय वह्निम्<BR> (पुरोधाः) Ku. 7. 80; अग्निं पर्यणयं च यत् Rām.<BR>—2 To marry, espouse; परिणेष्यति पार्वतीं यदा तपसा तत्प्रवणीकृतो<BR> हरः Ku. 4. 42.<BR>—3 To ascertain, investigate; तेषां वृत्तं परिणयेत् सम्यग् राष्ट्रेषु<BR> तच्चरैः Ms. 7. 122.<BR>—4 To lead forward. ━<i>Caus.</i> To pass, spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणयः|परिणय
परिणयः, -नम्<BR> Marriage; नवपरिणया वधूः शयने K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणयनम्
परिणयः, -नम्<BR> Marriage; नवपरिणया वधूः शयने K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायः|परिणाय
परि(री)णायः<BR>—1 Moving a piece at chess, draughts &c.<BR>—2 A move (at chess).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणायः|परीणाय
परि(री)णायः<BR>—1 Moving a piece at chess, draughts &c.<BR>—2 A move (at chess).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायकः|परिणायक
परिणायकः<BR>—1 A leader, a guide; तत्राहं दुर्बलावन्धौ वृद्धावपरिणायकौ (अपश्यम्)<BR> Rām. 2. 64. 4.<BR>—2 A husband; अनुदेहमागतवतः प्रतिमां परिणायकस्य गुरुमुद्वहता Śi. 9. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणी
परिणी (= पतिः ?) चिरं परिण्या परिशीलिताप्यसौ, जहाति न<BR> ह्रीभरमस्य केलिषु Rām. Ch. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीत
परिणीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Married.<BR>—2 completed, executed; सर्वान् सुपरिणीतेन कर्मणा तोषयाम्यहम् Mb. 3. 207. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीतिः
परिणीतिः <i>f.</i> A marriage; परिणीतिमहोत्सवे विभोः Śāhendra. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणुत
परिणुत <i>a.</i> Praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणेतव्य
परिणेतव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be married.<BR>—2 To be exchanged or bartered against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणेतृ
परिणेतृ <i>m.</i> A husband; Ś. 5. 17; R. 1. 25, 14. 26; Ku. 7. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीवित
परिणीवित <i>a.</i> Covered; पीताङ्गदैः परिगतैः परिणीवितांसः<BR> Pratijñā. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितक्म्य
परितक्म्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Dangerous, risky, unsafe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितक्म्या
परितक्म्य + .{@-क्म्या@}<BR>—1 Error.<BR>—2 Night, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्
परितप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To heat, burn, consume.<BR>—2 To inflame, set on fire.<BR>—3 To suffer pain.<BR>—4 To practise penance. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To scorch.<BR>—2 To torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्त
परितप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated, burnt.<BR>—2 Tormented, pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्तिः|परितप्ति
परितप्तिः <i>f.</i> Excessive pain, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितापः|परिताप
परितापः<BR>—1 Extreme or scorching heat; (पादपः) शमयति परितापं छायया<BR> संश्रितानाम् Ś. 5. 7; गुरुपरितापानि गात्राणि 3. 18; Ṛs. 1. 22.<BR>—2 Pain, agony, anguish, grief; प्रसक्ते निर्वाणे हृदय परितापं वहसि किम् M. 3. 1.<BR>—3 Lamentation, wailing; विरचितविविधविलापं सा परितापं चकारोच्चैः Gīt. 7.<BR>—4 Trembling, fear.<BR>—5 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितापिन्
परितापिन् <i>a.</i> Harassing, agonising; आपातरम्या विषयाः पर्यन्तपरितापिनः Ki. 11. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्क्
परितर्क् €10 P.<BR>—1 To reflect, consider.<BR>—2 To examine (judicially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्कणम्
परितर्कणम् Consideration, reflection; जिज्ञासा न तु कर्तव्या<BR> धर्मस्य परितर्कणात् Mb. 13. 162. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्कित
परितर्कित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Expected<BR>—2 Examined (judicially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितस्
परितस् <i>ind.</i> (Usually with a noun in the acc., sometimes by itself)<BR>—1 All around, on all sides, round about, in all directions, everywhere,<BR> on every side; रक्षांसि वेदीं परितो निरास्थत् Bk. 1. 12; Śi. 5. 26, 9. 36;<BR> Ś. 4. 8, 3. 26; Ki. 1. 14; गाहितमखिलं गहनं परितो दृष्टाश्च<BR> विटपिनः सर्वे Bv. 1. 21, 29.<BR>—2 Towards, in the direction of, आपेदिरेऽम्बरपथं परितः पतङ्गाः<BR> Bv. 1. 17; R. 9. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्
परितुष् €4 P. To be satisfied, be delighted or contented; अस्मत्कृते<BR> च परितुष्यति काचिदन्या Bh. 2. 2 (v. l.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To satisfy or please completely.<BR>—2 To appease.<BR>—3 To flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्ट|परितुष्टः
परितुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Completely satisfied; वयमिह परितुष्टा वल्कलैस्त्वं च लक्ष्म्या<BR> Bh. 3. 50; so मनसि च परितुष्टे कोऽर्थवान् को दरिद्रः <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 Pleased, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्टिः|परितुष्टि
परितुष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Contentment, complete satisfaction.<BR>—2 Delight, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोषः|परितोष
परितोषः<BR>—1 Contentment, absence of desire (opp. लोभ); सम इह परितोषो<BR> निर्विशेषो विशेषः Bh. 3. 50.<BR>—2 Complete satisfaction, gratification; आपरितोषाद्विदुषां न साधु मन्ये<BR> प्रयोगविज्ञानम् Ś. 1. 2.<BR>—3 Pleasure, delight, delight in, liking for (with loc.); Ku. 6. 59; R. 11. 92;<BR> गुणिनि परितोषः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोषण
परितोषण <i>a.</i> Satisfying, gratifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोषणम्
परितोषण + .{@-णम्@} Satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितृप्
परितृप् €4 P. To be pleased or contented. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To satisfy, please, gratify.<BR>—2 To refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्पणम्
परितर्पणम्<BR>—1 Gratifying.<BR>—2 A restorative; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितृप्तिः|परितृप्ति
परितृप्तिः <i>f.</i> Complete satisfation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0977-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितृषित
परितृषित <i>a.</i> Anxiously longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यज्
परित्यज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To leave, quit, abandon.<BR>—2 To resign, give up, discard, renounce; प्रारब्धमुत्तमगुणा न परित्यजन्ति Mu. 2. 17.<BR>—3 To except; तृणमप्यपरित्यज्य सतृणम् Sk.<BR>—4 To leave over, leave as a remainder.<BR>—5 To neglect, disregard.<BR>—6 To forsake (the body), die.<BR>—7 To disembark (with नावम्). ━<i>Caus.</i> To deprive a person of,<BR> rob any one of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यक्त
परित्यक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, quitted, abandoned.<BR>—2 Deprived or bereft of (with instr.).<BR>—3 Let go, discharged (as an arrow).<BR>—4 Wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यक्तम्
परित्यक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>n.</i> Anything to spare. ━<i>ind.</i> Without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यजनम्
परित्यजनम् Abandoning, giving up, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यागः|परित्याग
परित्यागः<BR>—1 Leaving, quitting, abandonment, desertion, repudiation (as a wife &c.);<BR> अपरित्यागमयाचतात्मनः R. 8. 12; कृतसीतापरित्यागः 15. 1.<BR>—2 Giving up, renouncing, discarding, renunciation, abdication &c.; स्वनामपरित्यागं<BR> करोमि Pt. 1 ‘I shall forego my name’; प्रापणात् सर्वकामानां परित्यागो<BR> विशिष्यते Ms. 2. 95.<BR>—3 Neglect, omission; मोहात्तस्य (कर्मणः) परित्यागस्तामसः<BR> परिकीर्तितः Bg. 18. 7.<BR>—4 Giving away, liberality.<BR>—5 Loss, privation.<BR>—6 A sacrifice.<BR>—7 Separation from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यागिन्
परित्यागिन् <i>a.</i> Renouncing (a Saṃnyāsin); गच्छत्येव परित्यागी<BR> वानप्रस्थश्च गच्छति Mb. 12. 268. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्याज्य
परित्याज्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be abandoned, left.<BR>—2 To be omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रस्त
परित्रस्त <i>a.</i> Frightened, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रासः|परित्रास
परित्रासः Fear, terror, fright; न परित्रासः कर्तव्यः Rām. 7. 27. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रै
परित्रै €1 Ā. To rescue, save, protect; परित्रायस्व परित्रायस्व<BR> (in dramas); परित्रायध्वम् Help! to the rescue! Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्राणम्
परित्राणम्<BR>—1 Preservation, protection, rescue, defence, deliverance; परित्राणाय<BR> साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम् Bg. 4. 8; रामापरित्राणविहस्तयोधं सेनानिवेशं<BR> तुमुलं चकार R. 5. 49.<BR>—2 Self-defence.<BR>—3 Abstaining from.<BR>—4 The hair of the body; moustaches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदरः|परिदर
परिदरः A disease of the gums in which the skin peels off and bleeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदंशित
परिदंशित <i>a.</i> Covered with mail, armed cap-a-pie (completely<BR> or from head to foot); ततः प्रत्यागतप्राणा तावुभौ परिदंशितौ Mb. 1. 136. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदह्
परिदह् €1 P. To burn completely, dry up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदहनम्
परिदहनम् Burning, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदाहः|परिदाह
परि(री)दाहः<BR>—1 Burning.<BR>—2 Anguish, pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीदाहः|परीदाह
परि(री)दाहः<BR>—1 Burning.<BR>—2 Anguish, pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदष्ट
परिदष्ट^1 <i>a.</i> Bitten.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिदष्टदच्छद<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदष्टदच्छद
परिदष्टः + -दच्छद <i>a.</i> biting the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदा
परिदा €3 U.<BR>—1 To hand or deliver over, consign; छद्मना परिददामि मृत्यवे U. 1. 46;<BR> Ms. 9. 327.<BR>—2 To entrust or deposit with.<BR>—3 To present.<BR>—4 To lend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदा
परिदा Ved.<BR>—1 Giving oneself up to the favour of another.<BR>—2 Surrender.<BR>—3 Devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदानम्
परिदानम्<BR>—1 Barter, exchange.<BR>—2 Devotion.<BR>—3 Restitution or restoration of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदायिन्
परिदायिन् <i>m.</i> A father who gives his daughter in marriage to a<BR> man whose elder brother is not yet married; cf. परिवेत्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदिव्
परिदिव्, -देव् I. €1. €10 P.<BR> To lament, moan, suffer pain; खरदूषणयोर्भ्रात्रोः<BR> पर्यदोविष्ट सा पुरः Bk. 4. 34. ━II. €4 P. To sell, deal in (with acc.<BR> or gen.); शतं शतस्य वा परिदीव्यति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेव्
परिदिव्, -देव् I. €1. €10 P.<BR> To lament, moan, suffer pain; खरदूषणयोर्भ्रात्रोः<BR> पर्यदोविष्ट सा पुरः Bk. 4. 34. ━II. €4 P. To sell, deal in (with acc.<BR> or gen.); शतं शतस्य वा परिदीव्यति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवः|परिदेव
परिदेवः Wailing, lamentation; परिदेवो महानद्य Mb. 7. 85. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवनम्
परिदेवनम्, -ना, परिदेवितम्<BR>—1 Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25;<BR> R. 14. 83; तत्र का परिदेवना Bg. 2. 28; H. 4. 71; तस्यास्तत्परिदेवितं<BR> श्रुत्वा पृथा सुदुःखार्ता Mb. 14. 61. 32; Y. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवना
परिदेवनम्, -ना, परिदेवितम्<BR>—1 Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25;<BR> R. 14. 83; तत्र का परिदेवना Bg. 2. 28; H. 4. 71; तस्यास्तत्परिदेवितं<BR> श्रुत्वा पृथा सुदुःखार्ता Mb. 14. 61. 32; Y. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवितम्
परिदेवनम्, -ना, परिदेवितम्<BR>—1 Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25;<BR> R. 14. 83; तत्र का परिदेवना Bg. 2. 28; H. 4. 71; तस्यास्तत्परिदेवितं<BR> श्रुत्वा पृथा सुदुःखार्ता Mb. 14. 61. 32; Y. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिद्यून
परिद्यून <i>a.</i> Sorrowful, sad, miserable; परिद्यूनान् वृतवती<BR> किमुताद्य मृजावतः Mb. 1. 202. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदिष्ट
परिदिष्ट <i>a.</i> Made known, pointed out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदृश्
परिदृश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To see, view, behold.<BR>—2 To consider, investigate, find out.<BR>—3 To know.<BR>—4 To frequent. ━<i>Pass.</i>. To appear, become visible. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To show.<BR>—2 To explain, expound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिद्रष्टृ
परिद्रष्टृ <i>m.</i> A spectator, looker on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधर्षणम्
परिधर्षणम्<BR>—1 An assault, attack, outrage.<BR>—2 Insult, affront, abuse.<BR>—3 Ill-treatment, rough usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधा
परिधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To put or wear (as a garment); त्वचं स मेध्यां परिधाय रौरवीम् R. 3. 31.<BR>—2 To surround, enclose.<BR>—3 To direct towards.<BR>—4 To put or place round.<BR>—5 To cast round the eyes, turn the glance upon.<BR>—6 To conclude, close (as the recitation of a hymn). ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> cause to put on, clothe with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानम्
परि(री)धानम्<BR>—1 Putting on a garment, dressing.<BR>—2 A garment, especially an under-garment, clothes in general; आत्तचित्रपरिधानविभूषाः<BR> Ki. 9. 1; Śi. 1. 61, 4. 68; Pt. 5. 23 (fig.). A sword-sheath; समुल्लसत्तनुपरिधानसंपदः<BR> (सदसिलताः) Śi. 17. 25.<BR>—3 Closing or concluding.<BR>—4 Ved. Putting round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीधानम्
परि(री)धानम्<BR>—1 Putting on a garment, dressing.<BR>—2 A garment, especially an under-garment, clothes in general; आत्तचित्रपरिधानविभूषाः<BR> Ki. 9. 1; Śi. 1. 61, 4. 68; Pt. 5. 23 (fig.). A sword-sheath; समुल्लसत्तनुपरिधानसंपदः<BR> (सदसिलताः) Śi. 17. 25.<BR>—3 Closing or concluding.<BR>—4 Ved. Putting round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानीयम्
परिधानीयम् An under-garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानीया
परिधानीयम् + .{@-या@} A concluding hymn; न पुरा परिधानीयाया ब्रह्मा व्यववदत<BR> Ch. Up. 4. 16. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0978-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधायः|परिधाय
परिधायः<BR>—1 Train, retinue, attendants collectively.<BR>—2 A receptacle, a reservoir.<BR>—3 The posteriors.<BR>—4 A garment to be worn.<BR>—5 The region of buttocks.<BR>—6 (= परिच्छेद q. v.) परिधायो जनस्थाने परिच्छेदनितम्बयोः Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधायकः|परिधायक
परिधायकः A hedge, fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिः|परिधि
परिधिः<BR>—1 A wall, fence, hedge, anything surrounding or enclosing another; नैनं<BR> परिधिमेतेषामीषत् क्षपयितुं क्षमाः Śiva B. 26. 59; बर्बरान् परिधीभूतान्<BR> परिभूय स्वतेजसा 28. 27.<BR>—2 A misty halo round the sun or moon; परिधेर्मुक्त इवोष्णदीधितिः<BR> R. 8. 30; शशिपरिधिरिवोच्चेर्मण्डलस्तेन तेने N. 2. 108.<BR>—3 A circle of light; मेघश्यामः कनकपरिधिः कर्णविद्योतविद्युत् Bhāg.<BR>—4 The horizon; the quarter; पिबद्भिरिव खं दृग्भिर्दहद्भिः परिधीनिव<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 10.<BR>—5 The circumference or compass in general.<BR>—6 The circumference of a circle.<BR>—7 The periphery of a wheel.<BR>—8 A stick (of a sacred tree like पलाश) laid round the sacrificial<BR> fire; सप्तास्यासन् परिधयः त्रिःसप्त समिधः कृताः Rv. 10. 90. 15;<BR> धूम्रा दिशः परिधयः कम्पते भूः सहाद्रिभिः Bhāg.1. 14. 15.<BR>—9 A circle surrounding the globe.<BR>—10 Epicycle.<BR>—11 A covering.<BR>—12 A branch of a sacred tree to which the sacrificial victim is tied.<BR>—13 A cover, garment; श्यामं हिरण्यपरिधिं नवमाल्यबर्हधातुप्रवालनटवेषमनुव्रतांसे<BR> Bhāg. 10. 23. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिध्युपान्त, परिधिपतिखेचरः, परिधिस्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्युपान्त
परिधिः + -उपान्त <i>a.</i> bordered by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिपतिखेचरः|परिधिपतिखेचर
परिधिः + -पतिखेचरः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिस्थः|परिधिस्थ
परिधिः + -स्थः<BR>—1 a guard.<BR>—2 an officer attendant on a king or general (modern ‘aide-de-camp’).<BR>—3 A number of sentinels posted in a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधारणम्
परिधारणम् Suffering, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधारणा
परिधारणा Patience, perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाव्
परिधाव् €1 P.<BR>—1 To flow or stream round.<BR>—2 To go about.<BR>—3 To run after, pursue. ━<i>Caus.</i> To surround, encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाविन्
परिधाविन् <i>a.</i> Running round. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a year (संवत्सर),<BR> the 46th of the 60 years cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधीर
परिधीर <i>a.</i> Very deep (as a tone or sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूपित
परिधूपित <i>a.</i> Richly perfumed or scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूसर
परिधूसर <i>a.</i> Quite grey; वसने परिधूसरे वसाना Ś. 7. 21; R. 11. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधेयम्
परिधेयम् An under garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्वंसः|परिध्वंस
परिध्वंसः<BR>—1 Distress, disaster, ruin, trouble.<BR>—2 Failure.<BR>—3 Destruction.<BR>—4 Loss of caste.<BR>—5 Mixture of caste (वर्णसंकर); यत्र त्वेते परिध्वंसा जायन्ते<BR> वर्णदूषकाः Ms. 10. 61.<BR>—6 Eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्वंसिन्
परिध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i> Ruining, destroying; राजकार्यपरिध्वंसी मन्त्री<BR> दोषेण लिप्यते H. 2. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वपणम्
परिनिर्वपणम् Distributing, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वाण
परिनिर्वाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Completely extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वाणम्
परिनिर्वाण + .{@-णम्@} Final extinction (of the individual); entire cessation of rebirths.<BR>—2 N. of a place where Buddha disappeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्विण्ण
परिनिर्विण्ण <i>a.</i> Extremely disgusted with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वृत्तिः
परिनिर्वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> Final liberation or complete emancipation of<BR> the soul from the body and exemption from future transmigration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठा
परिनिष्ठा<BR>—1 Complete knowledge or acquaintance (of anything).<BR>—2 Complete accomplishment.<BR>—3 Extreme limit.<BR>—4 Final emancipation (मोक्ष); बुद्धिश्च परिनैष्ठिकी Mb. 1. 62. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठित
परिनिष्ठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Completely skilled in; औत्पातिके च विविधे सर्वतः परिनिष्ठिता<BR> Rām. 4. 22. 13.<BR>—2 Well fixed; अपरिनिष्ठितस्योपदेशस्यान्याय्यं प्रकाशन् M. 1.<BR>—3 Quite perfect.<BR>—4 Acquainted, accomplished; परिनिष्ठितकार्यो हि स्वाध्यायेन द्विजो भवेत्<BR> Mb. 12. 238. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्पत्तिः|परिनिष्पत्ति
परिनिष्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> Perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिन्यासः|परिन्यास
परिन्यासः<BR>—1 Completing the sense of a passage.<BR>—2 Alluding to the development of the origin of the dramatic plot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्व
परिपक्व <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Completely cooked.<BR>—2 Completely baked or burnt.<BR>—3 Quite ripe, mature, perfected (fig. also); प्रफुल्ललोध्रः परिपक्वशालिः<BR> Ṛs. 4. 1; so परिपक्वबुद्धिः<BR>—4 Highly cultivated, very sharp or shrewd.<BR>—5 Fully digested.<BR>—6 Decaying, on the point of decay or death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणम्
परिपणम् (-नम्)<BR> Capital, principal, stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपनम्
परिपणम् (-नम्)<BR> Capital, principal, stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणनम्
परिपणनम्<BR>—1 Plighting, promising; Mu. 1.<BR>—2 Playing for, wagering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणित
परिपणित <i>p. p.</i> Plighted, pledged, promised; Śi. 7. 9; परिपणितापरिपणितापसृताश्च<BR> सन्धयः Kau. A. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपण्डिमन्
परिपण्डिमन् <i>m.</i> Complete whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपत्
परिपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly round or about, wheel or whirl round, hover about; बिन्दूत्क्षेपान्<BR> पिपासुः परिपतति शिखी भ्रान्तिमद्वारियन्त्रम् M. 2. 13; Amaru. after 56<BR> (प्रक्षिप्त).<BR>—2 To spring down upon, attack, fall upon (as in battle).<BR>—3 To run in all directions; (हयाः) परिपेतुर्दिशो दश Mb.<BR>—4 To go to or fall into; Śi. 11. 41. ━<i>Caus.</i> To shoot off or down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपतनम्
परिपतनम् Flying round or about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपतिः|परिपति
परिपतिः (Ved.) A protector, the lord of all around.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपद्
परिपद् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A snare, trap.<BR>—2 A living being.<BR>—3 Walking about.<BR>—4 A bird. ━<i>Caus. verb</i> To change into Anusvāra; Rv. Pr. [परिपन्नम्<BR> the change of <i>m</i> into Anusvāra].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थः|परिपन्थ|परिपंथः
परिपन्थः An antagonist, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपथक
परिपथक An antagonist, adversary, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थिन्|परिपंथिन्
परिपन्थिन् <i>a.</i> Standing in the way, obstructing, opposing, hindering<BR> (said by Pānini to be admissible<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">Page0980-1</a>]<BR> only in the Veda, but see the quotations given below); अर्थपरिपन्थी<BR> महानरातिः Mu. 5; नाभविष्यमहं तत्र यदि तत्परिपन्थिनी Māl. 9. 50;<BR> so Bv. 1. 62; Ms. 7. 107, 1. 10. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An enemy, antagonist, opponent, a foe.<BR>—2 A robber, thief, highwayman; इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ ।<BR> तयोर्न वशमागच्छेत् तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ Bg. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0979-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपरः|परिपर
परिपरः A tortuous or round-about way; see अपरिपर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपरिन्
परिपरिन् <i>m.</i> Ved. An antagonist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपवनः|परिपवन
परिपवनः<BR>—1 Winnowing corn.<BR>—2 A winnowing basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपा
परिपा I. €1 P. To drink; उपनिषदः परिपीताः Bv. 2. 40. ━II. €2 P.<BR>—1 To protect, preserve, guard, defend against; पुण्यात्षड्भागमादत्ते<BR> न्यायेन परिपालयन् । सर्वदानाधिकं यस्मात्प्रजानां परिपालनम् ॥ Y. 1. 335<BR> Ms. 9. 251.<BR>—2 To rule, govern; Māl. 10. 25.<BR>—3 To bring up, nourish, support.<BR>—4 To keep to, observe, adhere to, persevere in; अङ्गीकृतं सुकृतिनः<BR> परिपालयन्ति C. P. 50.<BR>—5 To wait for, await; अथ मदनवधूरुपप्लवान्तं व्यसनकृशा परिपालयांबभूव<BR> Ku. 4. 46. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To protect.<BR>—2 To keep, maintain.<BR>—3 To wait for, expect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाकः|परिपाक
परि(री)पाकः<BR>—1 Being completely cooked or dressed.<BR>—2 Digestion, as in अन्नपरिपाक.<BR>—3 Ripening, maturing, development, perfection; परिपाकपिशङ्गलतारजसा<BR> रोधश्चकास्ति कपिशं गलता Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 10.<BR>—4 Fruit, result, consequence; प्रपन्नानां मूर्तः सुकृतपरिपाको जनिमताम्<BR> Mv. 4. 31; Bh. 2. 132, 3. 135.<BR>—5 Cleverness, shrewdness, skilfulness; वीक्ष्य तस्य विनये परिपाकं<BR> पाकशासनपदं स्पृशतोऽपि N. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीपाकः|परीपाक
परि(री)पाकः<BR>—1 Being completely cooked or dressed.<BR>—2 Digestion, as in अन्नपरिपाक.<BR>—3 Ripening, maturing, development, perfection; परिपाकपिशङ्गलतारजसा<BR> रोधश्चकास्ति कपिशं गलता Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 10.<BR>—4 Fruit, result, consequence; प्रपन्नानां मूर्तः सुकृतपरिपाको जनिमताम्<BR> Mv. 4. 31; Bh. 2. 132, 3. 135.<BR>—5 Cleverness, shrewdness, skilfulness; वीक्ष्य तस्य विनये परिपाकं<BR> पाकशासनपदं स्पृशतोऽपि N. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटल
परिपाटल <i>a.</i> Pale red; धौतरागपरिपाटलाधरैः (मुखैः)<BR> R. 19. 10; Śi. 13. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटिः|परिपाटि
परिपाटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Method, manner, course; पाटीर तव पटीयान् कः परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुम्<BR> Bv. 1. 12; कदम्बानां वाटी रसिकपरिपाटीं स्फुटयति H. D. 24;<BR> ‘भवानि त्वत्पाणिग्रहणपरिपाटीफलमिदम् ।’ -देव्यपराधक्षमापणस्तोत्रम् 7.<BR>—2 Arrangement, order, succession.<BR>—3 Arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटी
परिपाटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Method, manner, course; पाटीर तव पटीयान् कः परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुम्<BR> Bv. 1. 12; कदम्बानां वाटी रसिकपरिपाटीं स्फुटयति H. D. 24;<BR> ‘भवानि त्वत्पाणिग्रहणपरिपाटीफलमिदम् ।’ -देव्यपराधक्षमापणस्तोत्रम् 7.<BR>—2 Arrangement, order, succession.<BR>—3 Arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाठः|परिपाठ
परिपाठः<BR>—1 Complete enumeration, detail.<BR>—2 The repetition (of the Vedas); न धर्मः परिपाठेन शक्यो भारत<BR> वेदितुम् Mb. 12. 260. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपार्श्व
परिपार्श्व <i>a.</i> Near, at the side, close or hard by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालनम्
परिपालनम्<BR>—1 Protecting, defending, maintaining, keeping, sustaining; क्लिश्नाति<BR> लब्धपरिपालनवृत्तिरेव Ś. 5. 6.<BR>—2 Nourishment, nurture; जातस्य परिपालनम् Ms. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपिच्छम्
परिपिच्छम् A peacockʼs feather; an ornament made of it; गुञ्जावतंसपरिपिच्छलसन्मुखाय<BR> (नौमि) Bhāg. 10. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपिष्टकम्
परिपिष्टकम् Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपीड्
परिपीड् €10 U.<BR>—1 To pain, trouble, molest.<BR>—2 To press, squeeze.<BR>—3 To hug, embrace.<BR>—4 (In augury) To cover, cover up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपीडनम्
परिपीडनम्, परिपीडा<BR>—1 Squeezing, peeling out.<BR>—2 Injuring, hurting, doing harm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपीडा
परिपीडनम्, परिपीडा<BR>—1 Squeezing, peeling out.<BR>—2 Injuring, hurting, doing harm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपीवर
परिपीवर <i>a.</i> Very fat or plump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपुटनम्
परिपुटनम्<BR>—1 Removing the bark, peeling off.<BR>—2 Losing the bark or skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपू
परिपू €9 U.<BR>—1 To purify completely.<BR>—2 To lustrate.<BR>—3 To become purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूत|परिपूतं
परिपूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Purified, quite pure; उत्पत्तिपरिपूतायाः किमस्याः पावनान्तरैः<BR> U. 1. 13; Śi. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Completely winnowed or threshed, freed from chaff; परिपूतेषु धान्येषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजनम्
परिपूजनम्, परिपूजा Honouring, worshipping, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजा
परिपूजनम्, परिपूजा Honouring, worshipping, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूरणम्
परिपूरणम्<BR>—1 Filling; त्वक्साररन्ध्रपरिपूरणलब्धगीतिः Śi. 4. 61.<BR>—2 Perfecting, making complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्ण
परिपूर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Quite full; ˚इन्दुः the full moon; entire, complete, completely filled.<BR>—2 Self-satisfied, content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्तिः|परिपूर्ति
परिपूर्तिः <i>f.</i> Completion, fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपृच्छिक
परिपृच्छि(ष्टि)क <i>a.</i> One who receives anything only when asked<BR> for; Mb. 14. 92. 7. (Com. परिपृष्टं चेदेव गृह्णन्ति नान्यथा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपृष्टिक
परिपृच्छि(ष्टि)क <i>a.</i> One who receives anything only when asked<BR> for; Mb. 14. 92. 7. (Com. परिपृष्टं चेदेव गृह्णन्ति नान्यथा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेलव|परिपेलवं
परिपेलव <i>a.</i> Very delicate or fine, excessively tender; स्फीतमध्यपरिपेलवं<BR> कलम् Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेलवम्
परिपेलव + .{@-वम्@} A kind of fragrant grass (Mar. नागरमोथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपोटः|परिपोट
परिपोटः, -पोटकः<BR> A particular disease of the ear (in medicine) (by which<BR> the ear loses its skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपोटकः|परिपोटक
परिपोटः, -पोटकः<BR> A particular disease of the ear (in medicine) (by which<BR> the ear loses its skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपोषणम्
परिपोषणम्<BR>—1 Feeding, nourishing.<BR>—2 Furthering, promoting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रच्छ्|परिप्रछ्
परिप्रच्छ् €6 P. To ask, question, inquire about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपृच्छा
परिपृच्छा Question, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रश्नः|परिप्रश्न
परिप्रश्नः Inquiry, interrogation, question; कतरकतमौ जातिपरिप्रश्ने<BR> P. II. 1. 63, III. 3. 110; तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया Bg. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रवच्
परिप्रवच् To tell anything earlier than another person; मा त्वाग्नयः<BR> परिप्रवोचन् Ch. Up. 4. 10. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्राप्तिः|परिप्राप्ति
परिप्राप्तिः <i>f.</i> Acquisition, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेषणम्
परिप्रेषणम्<BR>—1 Sending away.<BR>—2 Banishing, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेष्यः|परिप्रेष्य
परिप्रेष्यः A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लु
परिप्लु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To swim, float.<BR>—2 To bathe, plunge into.<BR>—3 To jump, spring.<BR>—4 To deluge, inundate, flood.<BR>—5 To cover with.<BR>—6 To overwhelm.<BR>—7 To fly or hover about.<BR>—8 To revolve, move in a circle.<BR>—9 To go astray.<BR>—10 To hasten forward. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bathe, water.<BR>—2 To flood, deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0980-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लव|परिप्लवं|परिप्लवः
परिप्लव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Floating.<BR>—2 Shaking, trembling, oscillating, undulating, tremulous.<BR>—4 Unsteady, restless; मत्कुणाविव पुरा परिप्लवौ Śi. 14. 68; चञ्चलं<BR> चपलं तूर्णं पारिप्लवपरिप्लवे Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लवः|परिप्लव|परिप्लवं
परिप्लव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Inundation.<BR>—2 Immersing, wetting.<BR>—3 A boat.<BR>—4 Oppression, tyranny.<BR>—5 Floating, swimming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुत|परिप्लुतः
परिप्लुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Flooded, inundated.<BR>—2 Overwhelmed; as in शोक˚.<BR>—3 Wetted, bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुतम्
परिप्लुत + .{@-तम्@} A spring, jump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुता
परिप्लुत + .{@-ता@} Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुति
परिप्लुत + .{@-ति@} <i>f.</i> Over-abundance पुरभिदा गमितस्त्वमदृश्यतां त्रिनयनत्वपरिप्लुतिशङ्कया N. 4. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुष्ट
परिप्लुष्ट Burnt, scorched, singed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लोषः|परिप्लोष
परिप्लोषः Internal heat; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबन्ध्|परिबंध्
परिबन्ध् €9 Ā.<BR>—1 To tie, bind.<BR>—2 To put on.<BR>—3 To encircle, fasten round.<BR>—4 To arrest, stop.<BR>—5 To hinder, interrupt. ━<i>Caus.</i> To tie round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबन्धनम्
परिबन्धनम् Tying round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबाध्
परिबाध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To trouble, afflict; Ś. 7. 25.<BR>—2 Ved. To hinder, obstruct.<BR>—3 Ved. To protect from or defend against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबाधा
परिबाधा<BR>—1 Trouble, pain, annoyance.<BR>—2 Fatigue, hardship; कथमातपे गमिष्यसि परिबाधापेलवैरङ्गैः Ś. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंह्
परिबृं(वृं)ह् €6 U.<BR>—1 To strengthen, fortify.<BR>—2 To increase.<BR>—3 Ved. To encircle, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंह्
परिबृं(वृं)ह् €6 U.<BR>—1 To strengthen, fortify.<BR>—2 To increase.<BR>—3 Ved. To encircle, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्हः|परिबर्ह
परिब(व)र्हः<BR>—1 Retinue, train, attendants; इयं प्रचुरपरिबर्हया भवत्या संवर्ध्यताम्<BR> Dk. 108; महता परिबर्हेण राजयोग्येन संवृतः Mb. 3. 264. 7.<BR>—2 Furniture; (निवेश्य) चमूं विधानैः परिबर्हशोभिनीम् Rām. 2. 83. 26.<BR> परिबर्हवन्ति वेश्मानि R. 14. 15 ‘rooms properly furnished or provided with furniture’<BR>; अर्हेण परिबर्हेण संस्तवेन स्तवेन च<BR> Śiva B. 11. 27.<BR>—3 Royal insignia.<BR>—4 The necessaries of life.<BR>—5 Property, wealth.<BR>—6 A present, presentation; अहं च तस्मिन् भवताभिकामये सहोपनीतं<BR> परिबर्हमर्हितुम् Bhāg. 4. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्हः|परिवर्ह
परिब(व)र्हः<BR>—1 Retinue, train, attendants; इयं प्रचुरपरिबर्हया भवत्या संवर्ध्यताम्<BR> Dk. 108; महता परिबर्हेण राजयोग्येन संवृतः Mb. 3. 264. 7.<BR>—2 Furniture; (निवेश्य) चमूं विधानैः परिबर्हशोभिनीम् Rām. 2. 83. 26.<BR> परिबर्हवन्ति वेश्मानि R. 14. 15 ‘rooms properly furnished or provided with furniture’<BR>; अर्हेण परिबर्हेण संस्तवेन स्तवेन च<BR> Śiva B. 11. 27.<BR>—3 Royal insignia.<BR>—4 The necessaries of life.<BR>—5 Property, wealth.<BR>—6 A present, presentation; अहं च तस्मिन् भवताभिकामये सहोपनीतं<BR> परिबर्हमर्हितुम् Bhāg. 4. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्हणम्
परिब(व)र्हणम्<BR>—1 Retinue, train.<BR>—2 Attire, trim; Mb. 12. 192. 3.<BR>—3 Growth.<BR>—4 Worship; मनोवचोदृक्करणे हितस्य साक्षात्कृतं मे परिबर्हणं हि<BR> Bhāg. 5. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्हणम्
परिब(व)र्हणम्<BR>—1 Retinue, train.<BR>—2 Attire, trim; Mb. 12. 192. 3.<BR>—3 Growth.<BR>—4 Worship; मनोवचोदृक्करणे हितस्य साक्षात्कृतं मे परिबर्हणं हि<BR> Bhāg. 5. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहणम्
परिबृं(वृं)हणम्<BR>—1 Prosperity, welfare.<BR>—2 Appendix, supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहणम्
परिबृं(वृं)हणम्<BR>—1 Prosperity, welfare.<BR>—2 Appendix, supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहित
परिबृं(वृं)हित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Increased, augmented; फलन्त्युपायाः परिबृंहितायतीः Ki. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Thriven, grown prosperous.<BR>—3 Accompanied by, furnished with; कृतवान् भारतं यस्त्वं सर्वार्थपरिबृंहितम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहित
परिबृं(वृं)हित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Increased, augmented; फलन्त्युपायाः परिबृंहितायतीः Ki. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Thriven, grown prosperous.<BR>—3 Accompanied by, furnished with; कृतवान् भारतं यस्त्वं सर्वार्थपरिबृंहितम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहितम्
परिबृं(वृं)हित + .{@-तम्@} The roar of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबोधः|परिबोध
परिबोधः Reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबोधनम्
परिबोधनम्, परिबोधा Admonition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबोधा
परिबोधनम्, परिबोधा Admonition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभङ्गः|परिभङ्ग|परिभंग|परिभंगः
परिभङ्गः Shattering, breaking to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभर्त्सनम्
परिभर्त्सनम् Threatening, menacing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाण्डम्
परिभाण्डम् Furniture, utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाष्
परिभाष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To lay down a convention, speak conventionally.<BR>—2 To speak to, address.<BR>—3 To teach, explain, interpret, expound.<BR>—4 To exhort, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषणम्
परिभाषणम्<BR>—1 Speaking, discourse, talking, chatting, gossiping.<BR>—2 Expression of censure, admonition, reproof, abuse; आपद्गतोऽथवा<BR> वृद्धो गर्भिणी बाल एव वा परिभाषणमर्हन्ति Ms. 9. 283.<BR>—3 Rule, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषा
परिभाषा<BR>—1 Speech, discourse; ग्राम्यवैदग्ध्यया परिभाषया Bhāg. 5. 2. 17.<BR>—2 Censure, reproof, blame, abuse.<BR>—3 An explanation.<BR>—4 Terminology, technical phraseology, technical terms (used in a work);<BR> इति परिभाषाप्रकरणम् Sk.; इको गुणवृद्धीत्यादिका परिभाषा Mbh;<BR> cf. also अधिकारशब्देन पारार्थ्यात् परिभाषाप्युच्यते । कश्चित् परिभाषारूप<BR> इति Kaiyaṭa.<BR>—5 (Hence) Any general rule, precept, or definition which is applicable<BR> throughout (अनियमनिवारको न्यायविशेषः); परितः प्रमिताक्षरापि<BR> सर्वं विषयं प्राप्तवती गता प्रतिष्ठाम् । न खलु प्रतिहन्यते कदाचित्<BR> परिभाषेव गरीयसी यदाज्ञा Śi. 16. 80.<BR>—6 A list of abbreviations or signs used in any work.<BR>—7 (In gram.) An explanatory Sūtra mixed up with the other Sūtras of<BR> Pāṇini, which teaches the method of applying them.<BR>—8 (In medicine) Prognosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभिन्न
परिभिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Split open, cracked.<BR>—2 Deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुग्न
परिभुग्न <i>a.</i> Bowed, curved, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुज्
परिभुज् €7 U.<BR>—1 To eat.<BR>—2 To use, enjoy; न खलु च परिभोक्तुं नैव शक्नोमि हातुम् Ś. 5. 19;<BR> Ki. 5. 5, 8. 57.<BR>—3 To neglect to feed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुक्त
परिभुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Eaten.<BR>—2 Used, enjoyed.<BR>—3 Possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोक्तृ
परिभोक्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eating, enjoying, possessing.<BR>—2 Living at anotherʼs cost, using anotherʼs property illegally; Ms. 2. 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोगः|परिभोग
परिभोगः<BR>—1 Enjoyment; R. 4. 45.<BR>—2 Especially, sexual enjoyment; प्रीतिरोधमसहिष्ट सा पुरी स्त्रीव कान्तपरिभोगमायतम्<BR> R. 11. 52, 19. 21, 28, 30.<BR>—3 Illegal use of anotherʼs goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभू
परिभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To defeat, subdue, conquer, overcome; (hence) to surpass, excel; लग्नद्विरेफं<BR> परिभूय पद्मम् Ku. 7. 16; R. 10. 35.<BR>—2 To despise, slight, treat with contempt, disrespect, insult; नित्यं<BR> परिभवेच्छ्वश्रूम् Mb. 13. 93. 33; मा मां महात्मन् परिभूः Bk. 1. 22, 4. 37.<BR>—3 To injure, destroy, ruin.<BR>—4 To afflict, grieve.<BR>—5 To humiliate, disgrace.<BR>—6 To disappear.<BR>—7 Ved. To surround, encircle.<BR>—8 To go or fly round.<BR>—9 To accompany.<BR>—10 To take care of.<BR>—11 To guide, govern. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To think of, reflect on, meditate, contemplate; तामेतां परिभावयन्त्वभिनयैर्विन्यस्तरूपां<BR> बुधाः U. 7. 20. मुक्तात्मभिः स्वहृदये परिभाविताय ज्ञानात्मने भगवते<BR> नम ईश्वराय Bhāg. 8. 3. 18.<BR>—2 To contain, include.<BR>—3 To make known.<BR>—4 To surpass, exceed.<BR>—5 To soak,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">Page0982-1</a>]<BR> saturate.<BR>—6 To concentrate, to make cohesive; एवमेवेन्द्रियग्रामं शनैः संपरिभावयेत्<BR> Mb. 12. 195. 19. See परिभावन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0981-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवः|परिभव
परि(री)भवः<BR>—1 Insult, injury, humiliation, disrespect, degradation, disgrace; पराक्रमः<BR> परिभवे वैयात्यं सुरतेष्विव (भूषणम्) Śi. 2. 44; R. 12. 37;<BR> Ve. 1. 25; U. 4. 23; Mu. 3. 4; Mv. 1. 40, 3. 17.<BR>—2 Defeat, discomfiture.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिभवास्पदम्, परिभवपदम्, परिभवविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीभवः|परीभव
परि(री)भवः<BR>—1 Insult, injury, humiliation, disrespect, degradation, disgrace; पराक्रमः<BR> परिभवे वैयात्यं सुरतेष्विव (भूषणम्) Śi. 2. 44; R. 12. 37;<BR> Ve. 1. 25; U. 4. 23; Mu. 3. 4; Mv. 1. 40, 3. 17.<BR>—2 Defeat, discomfiture.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिभवास्पदम्, परिभवपदम्, परिभवविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवास्पदम्
परिभवः + -आस्पदम्, -पदम्<BR>—1 an object of contempt; अदुर्गो विषयः कस्य नारेः परिभवास्पदम् H. 3. 51.<BR>—2 a disgrace or disgraceful situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवपदम्
परिभवः + -आस्पदम्, -पदम्<BR>—1 an object of contempt; अदुर्गो विषयः कस्य नारेः परिभवास्पदम् H. 3. 51.<BR>—2 a disgrace or disgraceful situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवविधिः|परिभवविधि
परिभवः + -विधिः humiliation; प्रायो मूर्खः परिभवविधौ नाभिमानं तनोति Ś. Til. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभविन्
परिभविन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Humiliating, treating with disrespect or contempt.<BR>—2 Suffering disrespect.<BR>—3 conquering; भुवनपरिभवी Ki. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावः|परिभाव
परिभावः See परिभव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावनम्
परिभावनम्<BR>—1 Union, cohesion; पांसुभस्मकरीषाणां यथा वै राशयश्चिताः । सहसा<BR> वारिणा सिक्ता न यान्ति परिभावनम् ॥ Mb. 12. 195. 17, 18.<BR>—2 Contemplation, meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावना
परिभावना<BR>—1 Contempt.<BR>—2 Thought, contemplation.<BR>—3 (In dram.) Words exciting curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावित
परिभावित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Contained, included.<BR>—2 Pervaded.<BR>—3 Penetrated.<BR>—4 Conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाविन्
परिभाविन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Humiliating, despising, treating with contempt; आ अतिथिपरिभाविनी Ś. 4.<BR>—2 Putting to shame, surpassing, excelling.<BR>—3 Setting at naught, defying; वैद्ययत्नपरिभाविनं गदम् R. 19. 53<BR> ‘defying medical remedies’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावुक
परिभावुक <i>a.</i> Contemning, shaming &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूत|परिभूतं
परिभूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Overpowered, conquered.<BR>—2 Disregarded, slighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूतिः|परिभूति
परिभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Contempt, insult, disrespect, humiliation; मौर्यात् कथं नु परिभूतिमिमां<BR> सहेत Mu. 4. 11.<BR>—2 Defeat (परपराभव); परिभूत्या विचेतसः Mb. 12. 174. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूष्
परिभूष् €10 U.<BR>—1 To decorate, adorn.<BR>—2 To serve, wait upon.<BR>—3 To honour, worship.<BR>—4 To take care of.<BR>—5 To observe, follow.<BR>—6 To prepare, equip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूषणः|परिभूषण
परिभूषणः (<i>scil.</i> संधि) Peace obtained by the cession of<BR> the whole revenue of a land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभेदः|परिभेद
परिभेदः Hurt, injury; विपत्तिः परिभेदो वा न भवेच्च तथा कुरु<BR> Rām. 7. 75. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंश्
परिभ्रंश् €1 Ā., €4 P.<BR>—1 To fall or drop down, tumble, slip.<BR>—2 To stray from, go astray.<BR>—3 To fall away from, swerve, deviate.<BR>—4 To lose, be deprived of; Ms. 10. 20.<BR>—5 To escape.<BR>—6 To neglect, omit.<BR>—7 To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंशः|परिभ्रंश
परिभ्रंशः<BR>—1 Escape.<BR>—2 Falling from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंशनम्
परिभ्रंशनम्<BR>—1 Falling from.<BR>—2 Loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रष्ट
परिभ्रष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen or dropped off.<BR>—2 Escaped.<BR>—3 Cast down, degraded.<BR>—4 Deprived of, devoid of (with abl. or instr.); मत्स्यमांसपरिभ्रष्टे<BR> किं निरीक्षसि जम्बुके Pt. 4. 93.<BR>—5 Neglecting.<BR>—6 Vanished.<BR>—7 Lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभृष्ट
परिभृष्ट <i>a.</i> Fried, roasted, parched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रम्
परिभ्रम् €1. €4 P.<BR>—1 To rove, wander about, ramble, move to and fro; परिभ्रमसि किं वृथा<BR> क्वचन चित्त विश्रम्यताम् Bh. 3. 137.<BR>—2 To hover, whirl round; परिभ्रमन्मूर्धजषट्पदाकुलैः Ki. 5. 14.<BR>—3 To revolve, rotate, move or turn round.<BR>—4 To wander or roam over (with acc.); भुवं परिबभ्राम.<BR>—5 To turn round (anything), circumambulate.<BR>—6 To encircle. ━<i>Caus.</i> To bewilder, overwhelm, overpower; चिरपरिचितास्ते<BR> ते भावाः परिभ्रमयन्ति माम् U. 3. 32 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रमः|परिभ्रम
परिभ्रमः<BR>—1 Wandering, going about.<BR>—2 Rambling discourse, circumlocution, periphrasis; अलमनेन परिषत्कुतूहलविमर्दकारिणा<BR> परिभ्रमेण Mk. 1. 2/3. (v. l.).<BR>—3 Error, delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रमणम्
परिभ्रमणम्<BR>—1 Going about, roaming, wandering.<BR>—2 Revolving, turning round.<BR>—3 Circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डल|परिमंडल|परिमण्डलं|परिमण्डलः
परिमण्डल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Globular, round, circular.<BR>—2 Of the measure of an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलम्
परिमण्डल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A globe, sphere.<BR>—2 A ball.<BR>—3 A circle.<BR>—4 An orb.<BR>—5 The felly of a wheel (नेमि); अव्यक्तनाभं व्यक्तारं विकारपरिमण्डलम् ।<BR> क्षेत्रज्ञाधिष्ठितं चक्रं स्निग्धाक्षं वर्तते ध्रुवम् ॥ Mb. 12. 211. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलः|परिमण्डल|परिमंडल|परिमण्डलं
परिमण्डल + .{@-लः@} A species of venomous gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलय्
परिमण्डलय् denom. To besiege; ततस्तु तस्य सैन्यानि परसैन्येन<BR> पालितौ । पर्यमण्डलयंश्छैलावुभौ चन्दनवन्दनौ ॥ Śiva B. 23. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डित
परिमण्डित <i>a.</i> Adorned, decorated all around.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमन्थर|परिमंथर
परिमन्थर <i>a.</i> Extremely slow; Śi. 9. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमन्द|परिमंद
परिमन्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very dull or dim, quite faint; परिमन्दसूर्यनयनो दिवसः Śi. 9. 3.<BR>—2 Very slow.<BR>—3 Very thin or weak; भवनोदरेषु परिमन्दतया शयितोऽलसः (मदनः) Śi. 9. 39.<BR>—4 very litle; परिमन्दभिन्नतिमिरौघजटम् Śi. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमरः|परिमर
परिमरः<BR>—1 Destruction; चिरात् क्षत्रस्यास्तु प्रलय इव घोरः परिमरः Mv. 3. 41.<BR>—2 The wind.<BR>—3 A magical rite for the destruction of enemies; तद्ब्रह्मणः परिमर<BR> इत्युपासीत T. Up. 3. 10. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलः|परिमल
परिमलः<BR>—1 Fragrance, perfume, scent; परिमलो गीर्वाणचेतोहरः Bv. 1. 63, 66, 70, 71;<BR> यः पण्यस्त्रीरतिपरिमलोद्गारिभिर्नागराणामुद्दामानि प्रथयति<BR> शिलावेश्मभिर्यौवनानि Me. 25.<BR>—2 Pounding or trituration of fragrant substances.<BR>—3 A fragrant substance.<BR>—4 Copulation; ‘संभोगः स्यात् परिमले’ इति वैजयन्ती; अथ परिमलजामवाप्य<BR> लक्ष्मीम् Ki. 10. 1.<BR>—4 A meeting of learned men<BR>—5 A stain, spot, dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलनम्
परिमलनम् Rubbing (मर्दन); श्रीमत्यौ चारुवृत्ते करपरिमलनानन्दहृष्टे<BR> रमायाः; (विष्णुपादा॰ वर्णनस्तोत्रम् 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0982-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलित
परिमलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Perfumed; परिमलितमपि प्रियैः प्रकामं कुचयुगम्.<BR>—2 Soiled, despoiled of beauty; <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमा
परिमा €2 P., €3. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To measure.<BR>—2 To measure off, limit.<BR>—3 To estimate, determine.<BR>—4 To fulfil (a period or course).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाणम्
परि(री)माणम्<BR>—1 Measuring, measure (of strength, power &c.); सद्यः परात्मपरिमाणविवेकमूढः<BR> Mu. 1. 10; Ku. 2. 8; Ms. 3. 133; सदा पान्थः पूषा गगनपरिमाणं कलयति Bh.<BR>—2 Weight, number, value; प्रतिग्रहपरीमाणं … शासनं कारयेत्<BR> स्थिरम् Y. 1. 320.<BR>—3 Size, dimension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीमाणम्
परि(री)माणम्<BR>—1 Measuring, measure (of strength, power &c.); सद्यः परात्मपरिमाणविवेकमूढः<BR> Mu. 1. 10; Ku. 2. 8; Ms. 3. 133; सदा पान्थः पूषा गगनपरिमाणं कलयति Bh.<BR>—2 Weight, number, value; प्रतिग्रहपरीमाणं … शासनं कारयेत्<BR> स्थिरम् Y. 1. 320.<BR>—3 Size, dimension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाणकम्
परिमाणकम् Weight, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमित|परिमितं
परिमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Moderate, sparing.<BR>—2 Limited.<BR>—3 Measured, meted out.<BR>—4 Regulated, adjusted.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: परिमिताभरण, परिमितायुस्, परिमिताहार, परिमितभोजन, परिमितकथ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिताभरण
परिमित + -आभरण <i>a.</i> wearing a few ornaments, moderately adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितायुस्
परिमित + -आयुस् short-lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिताहार
परिमित + -आहार, -भोजन <i>a.</i> abstemious, eating little food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितभोजन
परिमित + -आहार, -भोजन <i>a.</i> abstemious, eating little food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितकथ
परिमित + -कथ <i>a.</i> saying or speaking little, using measured words;<BR> तां जानीयाः परिमितकथां जीवितं मे द्वितीयम् Me. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितिः|परिमिति
परिमितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Measure, quantity.<BR>—2 Limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमेय|परिमेयं
परिमेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Few, limited; परिमेयपुरःसरौ R. 1. 37.<BR>—2 Measurable, calculable.<BR>—3 Finite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाथिन्
परिमाथिन् <i>a.</i> Torturing; प्रसरति परिमाथी कोऽप्ययं देहदाहः Māl. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ग्
परिमार्ग् €10 U. To search, seek, look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्गः|परिमार्ग
परिमार्गः, -मार्गणम्<BR>—1 Searching or looking for, seeking out, tracing, tracking.<BR>—2 Touch, contact; प्रियकरपरिमार्गदङ्गनानां यदाभूत् पुनरधिकतरैव<BR> स्वेदतोयोदयश्रीः Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—3 Cleaning, wiping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्गणम्
परिमार्गः, -मार्गणम्<BR>—1 Searching or looking for, seeking out, tracing, tracking.<BR>—2 Touch, contact; प्रियकरपरिमार्गदङ्गनानां यदाभूत् पुनरधिकतरैव<BR> स्वेदतोयोदयश्रीः Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—3 Cleaning, wiping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिलनम्
परिमिलनम्<BR>—1 Touch, contact; तनोर्मध्यस्यान्तः परिमिलनमप्राप्य हरितम् Ratn. 2. 11;<BR> चन्दनवनोत्संगपरिमिलनवहलपरिमलः Nāg. 1.<BR>—2 Combination, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिलित
परिमिलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mixed with.<BR>—2 Filled, penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमुखम्
परिमुखम् <i>ind.</i> About the face, round or about (a person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमुच्
परिमुच् €6 U.<BR>—1 To free, release, liberate; मेघोपरोधपरिमुक्तशशाङ्कवक्त्रा Ṛs. 3. 7;<BR> C. P. 9.<BR>—2 To leave, quit, abandon.<BR>—3 To discharge, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

