परिमुह्
परिमुह् €4 U. To be bewildered or perplexed. ━<i>Caus.</i> (Ātm.)<BR>—1 To entice, beguile, allure; परिमोहयमाणाभी राक्षसीभिः समावृताः<BR> (बन्धाः) Bk. 8. 63.<BR>—2 (P.) To perplex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमुग्ध
परिमुग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Artlessly lovely, lovely yet simple.<BR>—2 Fascinating but foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमूढ
परिमूढ <i>p. p.</i> Bewildered, perplexed, troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोहनम्
परिमोहनम्<BR>—1 Beguiling, alluring, enticing, fascinating.<BR>—2 Bewildering, infatuating; स्पर्शः पुरा परिचितो नियतं स एव संजीवनश्च<BR> मनसः परिमोहनश्च U. 3. 12. (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=0983-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृज्
