पांसुः + -क्षारम्, -जम् a kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुजम्
पांसुः + -क्षारम्, -जम् a kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुगुण्ठित
पांसुः + -गुण्ठित <i>a.</i> covered with dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुचत्वरम्
पांसुः + -चत्वरम् hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुचन्दनः|पांसुचन्दन|पांसुचंदन
पांसुः + -चन्दनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुचामरः|पांसुचामर
पांसुः + -चामरः<BR>—1 a heap of dust.<BR>—2 a tent.<BR>—3 a bank covered with Dūrvā grass.<BR>—4 praise.<BR>—5 bushes (?) carried by the current of the river; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुजालिकः|पांसुजालिक
पांसुः + -जालिकः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुनिपातः|पांसुनिपात
पांसुः + -निपातः a shower of dust; also -वर्षः Ms. 4. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुपटलम्
पांसुः + -पटलम् a mass or coating of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुपिशाचः|पांसुपिशाच
पांसुः + -पिशाचः a class of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुमर्दनः|पांसुमर्दन
पांसुः + -मर्दनः an excavation for water round the root of a tree, a<BR> trench or basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुलवणम्
पांसुः + -लवणम् a kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसक
पांसक <i>a.</i> Vitiating, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांस(श)न <i>a.</i> (-ना, -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Disgracing, dishonouring, defiling; सदस्पतीनतिक्रम्य गोपालः<BR> कुलपांसनः Bhāg. 10. 74. 34; पौलस्त्यकुलपांसन Mv. 5.<BR>—2 Vitiating, spoiling.<BR>—3 Wicked, contemptible.<BR>—4 Infamous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशन
पांस(श)न <i>a.</i> (-ना, -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Disgracing, dishonouring, defiling; सदस्पतीनतिक्रम्य गोपालः<BR> कुलपांसनः Bhāg. 10. 74. 34; पौलस्त्यकुलपांसन Mv. 5.<BR>—2 Vitiating, spoiling.<BR>—3 Wicked, contemptible.<BR>—4 Infamous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसनम्
पांस(श)न + .{@-नम्@} Contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसव
पांस(श)व <i>a.</i> Consisting of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशव|पांशवः
पांस(श)व <i>a.</i> Consisting of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुका
पांसुका A menstruous woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुरः|पांसुर
पांसु(शु)रः<BR>—1 A gad-fly.<BR>—2 A cripple moved about in a wheel-chair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुरः|पांशुर
पांसु(शु)रः<BR>—1 A gad-fly.<BR>—2 A cripple moved about in a wheel-chair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुल|पांसुलः
पांसु(शु)ल <i>a.</i> [पांसुरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्]<BR>—1 Dusty, covered with dust; परिपाण्डु पांसुलकपोलमाननम् Māl. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Polluted, defiled, sullied, stained; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांशुलः Ś. 5. 29.<BR>—3 Defiling, disgracing, dishonouring; as in कुलपांसुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुल|पांशुलः
पांसु(शु)ल <i>a.</i> [पांसुरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्]<BR>—1 Dusty, covered with dust; परिपाण्डु पांसुलकपोलमाननम् Māl. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Polluted, defiled, sullied, stained; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांशुलः Ś. 5. 29.<BR>—3 Defiling, disgracing, dishonouring; as in कुलपांसुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुलः|पांसुल
पांसु(शु)ल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A profligate or licentious person, libertine, gallant.<BR>—2 One of the weapons of Śiva.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुलः|पांसुल
पांसु(शु)ल + .{@-लः, -लम्@} A dusty place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुलम्
पांसु(शु)ल + .{@-लः, -लम्@} A dusty place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुला
पांसु(शु)ल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 A menstruous woman.<BR>—2 An unchaste or licentious woman; अ˚ a chaste woman, अपांसुलानां<BR> धुरि कीर्तनीया R. 2. 2.<BR>—3 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुवः|पांसुव
पांसुवः A cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Small.<BR>—2 Praiseworthy.<BR>—3 Of perfected or matured intellect.<BR>—4 Ved. Very young.<BR>—5 Simple, genuine.<BR>—6 Honest, sincere.<BR>—7 Ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकः|पाक
पाक + .{@-कः@} [पच्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Cooking, dressing, baking, boiling.<BR>—2 Burning, (as bricks), baking; पुनः पाकेन मृन्मयम् (शुद्धयति)<BR> Ms. 5. 122; Y. 1. 187; एक एवायमर्थः पाको नाम । तस्यार्थान्तरे वैरूप्यं<BR> भवति । अन्यथालक्षण ओदनस्य पाकः अन्यथालक्षणो गुडस्य । ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Digestion (as of food); रूपं चक्षुस्तथा पाकस्त्रिविधं तेज उच्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 194. 10.<BR>—4 Ripeness; ओषध्यः फलपाकान्ताः Ms. 1. 46; फलमभिमुखपाकं राजजम्बूद्रुमस्य<BR> V. 4. 27; Māl. 9. 31.<BR>—5 Maturity, full or perfect development; धी˚, मति˚.<BR>—6 Completion, accomplishment, fulfilment; युयोज पाकाभिमुखैर्भृत्यान्<BR> विज्ञापनाफलैः R. 17. 40.<BR>—7 Result, consequence, fruit, fruition<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">Page1001-2</a>]<BR> (fig. also); आशीर्भिरेधयामासुः पुरः पाकाभिरम्बिकाम् Ku. 6. 90; पाकाभिमुखस्य<BR> दैवस्य U. 7. 4; Mv. 4. 14.<BR>—8 Development of the consequences of acts done.<BR>—9 Grain, corn, नीवारपाकादि R. 5. 9. (पच्यते इति पाकः धान्यम्).<BR>—10 Ripeness; suppuration (as of a boil).<BR>—11 Greyness of hair caused by old age.<BR>—12 A domestic fire.<BR>—13 An owl.<BR>—14 A child, young one.<BR>—15 N. of a demon killed by Indra.<BR>—16 An abscess, ulcer.<BR>—17 A vessel, cooking-utensil.<BR>—18 General fear and panic such as causes a revolution or some national calamity.<BR>—19 The subversion of a country.<BR>—20 Inflammation, suppuration.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाकागारः, पाकागारम्, पाकागारः, पाकागारम्, पाकशाला, पाकस्थानम्, पाकातीसारः, पाकात्ययः, पाकाभिमुख, पाककुटी, पाकक्रिया, पाकज, पाकपण्डितः, पाकपात्रम्, पाकभाण्डम्, पाकपुटी, पाकभेदकः, पाकयज्ञः, पाकशासनः, पाकद्विष्, पाकहन्तृ, पाकशासनिः, पाकशास्त्रम्, पाकशुक्ला, पाकस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकागारः|पाकागार
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकागारम्
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकागारः|पाकागार
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकागारम्
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशाला
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकस्थानम्
पाक + -अगारः, -अगारम्, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -शाला, -स्थानम् a kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकातीसारः|पाकातीसार
पाक + -अतीसारः chronic dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकात्ययः|पाकात्यय
पाक + -अत्ययः obscuration of the cornea after inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकाभिमुख
पाक + -अभिमुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 ready for ripeness or development; युयोज पाकाभिमुखैर्भृत्यान् विज्ञापनाफलैः R. 17. 40.<BR>—2 inclined to favour;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाककुटी
पाक + -कुटी a potterʼs kiln, pottery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकक्रिया
पाक + -क्रिया the act of cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकज|पाकजं
पाक + -ज <i>a.</i> produced by heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकजम्
पाक + -ज + .({@-जम्@})<BR>—1 black salt.<BR>—2 flatulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपण्डितः|पाकपण्डित
पाक + -पण्डितः a master in the art of cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपात्रम्
पाक + -पात्रम्, -भाण्डम् a cooking-utensil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकभाण्डम्
पाक + -पात्रम्, -भाण्डम् a cooking-utensil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपुटी
पाक + -पुटी a potterʼs kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकभेदकः|पाकभेदक
पाक + -भेदकः a particular class of criminals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञः|पाकयज्ञ
पाक + -यज्ञः a simple or domestic sacrifice (for some varieties of<BR> it −हुत, प्रहुत, ब्रह्मयज्ञ− see Kull. on Ms. 2. 143); वर्तन्ते<BR> पाकयज्ञाश्च यज्ञकर्म च नित्यदा Mb. 3. 30. 15 (com. पाकयज्ञाः<BR> गृह्याग्निसाध्या इष्टयः); Bhāg. 6. 19. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासनः|पाकशासन
पाक + -शासनः, -द्विष्, -हन्तृ <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; तत्र निश्चित्य<BR> कन्दर्पमगमत् पाकशासनः Ku. 2. 63; Ki. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकद्विष्
पाक + -शासनः, -द्विष्, -हन्तृ <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; तत्र निश्चित्य<BR> कन्दर्पमगमत् पाकशासनः Ku. 2. 63; Ki. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकहन्तृ
पाक + -शासनः, -द्विष्, -हन्तृ <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra; तत्र निश्चित्य<BR> कन्दर्पमगमत् पाकशासनः Ku. 2. 63; Ki. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासनिः|पाकशासनि
पाक + -शासनिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Jayanta, son of Indra.<BR>—2 of Vāli.<BR>—3 of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशास्त्रम्
पाक + -शास्त्रम् the science of cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशुक्ला
पाक + -शुक्ला chalk; पाकशुक्ला शिलाधातुः कडिनी करवटी खडी Śabdachandrikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकस्थानम्
पाक + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a kitchen.<BR>—2 a potterʼs kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकलः|पाकल|पाकलं
पाकलः<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 A fever to which elephants are subject; cf. कूटपाकल; पाकलाख्यज्वरं<BR> मर्त्यज्वरोक्तैरेव लक्षणैः । लक्षयेन्मतिमांस्तस्मात् तदेव च चिकित्सितम् ॥<BR> Mātaṅga L. 11. 50. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bringing to ripeness.<BR>—2 Quite black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकवती
पाकवती A pause of ¾ of an instance between two short syllables;<BR> Maṇḍūkī Śikṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिन्
पाकिन् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Becoming ripe, ripening.<BR>—2 Being digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Cooked, dressed.<BR>—2 Ripened (naturally or artificially).<BR>—3 Got by boiling (as salt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुः|पाकु
पाकुः, पाकुकः A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुकः|पाकुक
पाकुः, पाकुकः A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य <i>a.</i> To be cooked, dressed, matured &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्यः|पाक्य|पाक्यं
पाक्य + .{@-क्यः@} Salt-petre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्ष
पाक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पक्षे भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a lunar fortnight, fortnightly.<BR>—2 Relating to a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षपातिक
पाक्षपातिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Partial, factious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a fortnight, fortnightly.<BR>—2 Belonging to a bird.<BR>—3 Favouring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">Page1002-1</a>]<BR> a party or faction.<BR>—4 Belonging to an argument.<BR>—5 Optional, subject to an alternative, allowed but not specifically laid<BR> down; नियमः पाक्षिके सति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिकः|पाक्षिक
पाक्षिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A fowler.<BR>—2 An alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1001-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाखण्डः|पाखण्ड|पाखंड|पाखंडः
पाखण्डः<BR>—1 A heretic; पाखण्डचण्डालयोः पापारम्भकयोर्मृगीव वृकयोर्भीरुर्गता<BR> गोचरम् Māl. 5. 24; दुरात्मन् पाखण्डचण्डाल Māl. 5; पाखण्डाः<BR> पण्डितंमन्या न ते किमपि जानते Aman. Up. 2. 102.<BR>—2 The Jainas or Bauddhas; अस्वधर्मो ममैष पाखण्डावतारः Dk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पागल|पागलः
पागल <i>a.</i> Mad, demented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्त
पाङ्क्त <i>a.</i> (-क्ती <i>f.</i>) Ved.<BR>—1 Consisting of five parts, fivefold; स एष पाङ्क्तो यज्ञः Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 17.<BR>—2 Having ten limbs (as a man or beast).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्तेय|पांक्तेय
पाङ्क्तेय, -पाङ्क्त्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit to sit in the same row at a dinner-party; Mb. 13. 90. 5.<BR>—2 Fit to be associated with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्त्य|पांक्त्य
पाङ्क्तेय, -पाङ्क्त्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit to sit in the same row at a dinner-party; Mb. 13. 90. 5.<BR>—2 Fit to be associated with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्गुल्यम्
पाङ्गुल्यम् Limping, halting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक <i>a.</i> [पच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Cooking, baking.<BR>—2 Maturing, bringing to maturity.<BR>—3 Digestive, tonic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचकः|पाचक|पाचकं
पाचक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A cook.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचकम्
पाचक + .{@-कम्@} Gall, bile.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाचकस्त्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचकस्त्री
पाचक + -स्त्री a female cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पाचयति कर्तरि ल्युः पाच्यतेऽनेन करणे ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Cooking.<BR>—2 Ripening.<BR>—3 Digestive.<BR>—4 Softening, relaxing.<BR>—5 Suppurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनः|पाचन|पाचनं
पाचन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 Sourness, acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनम्
पाचन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The act of cooking.<BR>—2 The act of ripening.<BR>—3 A dissolvent, digestive medicine.<BR>—4 Causing a wound to close.<BR>—5 Penance, expiation (प्रायश्चित्त).<BR>—6 Infusion.<BR>—7 Decoction.<BR>—8 Extracting extraneous substances from a wound.<BR>—9 A cataplasm.<BR>—10 A substance used in closing wounds or restraining bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनकः|पाचनक
पाचनकः Borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनकम्
पाचनकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A sort of diet-drink; digestive.<BR>—2 Causing a wound to close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनिका
पाचनिका Cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचल|पाचलं|पाचलः
पाचल <i>a.</i> Cooking, ripening, causing digestion &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचलः|पाचल|पाचलं
पाचल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A cook.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 Wind.<BR>—4 A thing dressed without the aid of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचा
पाचा, -चिः <i>f.</i><BR> Cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचिः|पाचि
पाचा, -चिः <i>f.</i><BR> Cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्
पाजस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्यम्
पाजस्यम्<BR>—1 The region of the belly (of an animal); पृथिवी पाजस्यम् Bṛ. Up. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—2 The flanks, side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजिकः|पाजिक
पाजिकः A falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चकपाल|पांचकपाल|पाञ्चकपालः
पाञ्चकपाल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to an oblation offered in five cups (कपाल);<BR> P. IV. 1. 88; Patañ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पांचजन्यः
पाञ्चजन्यः<BR>—1 N. of the conch of Kṛṣṇa; स तु पञ्चजनं हत्वा शङ्खं लेभे<BR> जनार्दनः । स च देवमनुष्येषु पाञ्चजन्य इति श्रुतः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">Page1002-2</a>]<BR> Hariv.; (दधानो) निध्वानमश्रूयत पाञ्चजन्यः Śi. 3. 21; Bg. 1. 15.<BR>—2 Kāśyapa, Vasiṣṭha, Prāṇa, Aṅgirasa, and Cyavana.<BR>—3 अग्नि produced from the five fires; Śabda C.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाञ्चजन्यधरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्यधरः|पाञ्चजन्यधर|पांचजन्यधर
पाञ्चजन्यः + -धरः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश|पांचदश
पाञ्चदश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), पाञ्चदश्य (-श्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the fifteenth day of a month.<BR>—2 Being kindled by fifteen Sāmidhenī mantras; वह्निं यथा दारुणि<BR> पाञ्चदश्यं मनीषया निष्कर्षन्ति गूढम् Bhāg. 6. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदशी|पांचदशी
पाञ्चदश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), पाञ्चदश्य (-श्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the fifteenth day of a month.<BR>—2 Being kindled by fifteen Sāmidhenī mantras; वह्निं यथा दारुणि<BR> पाञ्चदश्यं मनीषया निष्कर्षन्ति गूढम् Bhāg. 6. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश्य|पांचदश्यं
पाञ्चदश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), पाञ्चदश्य (-श्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the fifteenth day of a month.<BR>—2 Being kindled by fifteen Sāmidhenī mantras; वह्निं यथा दारुणि<BR> पाञ्चदश्यं मनीषया निष्कर्षन्ति गूढम् Bhāg. 6. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश्यी
पाञ्चदश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>), पाञ्चदश्य (-श्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the fifteenth day of a month.<BR>—2 Being kindled by fifteen Sāmidhenī mantras; वह्निं यथा दारुणि<BR> पाञ्चदश्यं मनीषया निष्कर्षन्ति गूढम् Bhāg. 6. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश्यम्
पाञ्चदश्यम् A collection of fifteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनद|पांचनद|पाञ्चनदः
पाञ्चनद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Prevalent in the पञ्चनद or Punjab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनदः|पाञ्चनद|पांचनद
पाञ्चनद + .{@-दः@} A prince of the Punjab.<BR>—2 (pl.) Its inhabitants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चभौतिक|पांचभौतिक
पाञ्चभौतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Composed of the five elements or containing them;<BR> पाञ्चभौतिकी सृष्टिः Mv. 6; Y. 3. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयज्ञिक|पांचयज्ञिक
पाञ्चयज्ञिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to the five great sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयज्ञिकम्
पाञ्चयज्ञिक + .{@-कम्@} Any one of the five great sacrifices; एकमप्याशयेद् विप्रं<BR> पित्रर्थे पाञ्चयज्ञिके Ms. 3. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चरात्रम्
पाञ्चरात्रम् N. of a Vaiṣṇava sect and its doctrine; भक्तिमार्ग;<BR> परस्पराङ्गान्येतानि पाञ्चरात्रं च कथ्यते । एष एकान्तिनां धर्मो नारायणपरात्मकः ॥<BR> Mb. 12. 348. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चवर्षिक|पांचवर्षिक
पाञ्चवर्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Five years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चशब्दिकम्
पाञ्चशब्दिकम्<BR>—1 Music of five kinds; अङ्गजं कर्मजं चैव तन्त्रजं कांस्यजं तथा ।<BR> फूत्कृतं चेति मुनिभिः कथितं पाञ्चशब्दिकम् ॥ Skanda P.<BR>—2 Musical instruments in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चार्थिकः|पाञ्चार्थिक|पांचार्थिकः
पाञ्चार्थिकः A follower or votary of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पाञ्चाल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to or ruling over the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालः|पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं
पाञ्चाल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 The country of the Pañcālas.<BR>—2 A prince of the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालाः
पाञ्चाल + .{@-लाः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.)<BR>—1 The people of the Pañcālas.<BR>—2 An association of five guilds (<i>i. e.</i> of a carpenter, weaver, barber,<BR> washerman, and shoe-maker).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालक|पांचालक|पाञ्चालकः
पाञ्चालक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the people of the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालकः|पाञ्चालक|पांचालक
पाञ्चालक + .{@-कः@} A king of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाली|पांचाली
पाञ्चाली<BR>—1 A woman or princess of the Pañcālas.<BR>—2 N. of Draupadī, the wife of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—3 A doll, puppet.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.) One of the four styles of composition. The S. D. thus defines<BR> it:− वर्णैः शेषैः (<i>i. e.</i> माधुर्यव्यञ्जकौजःप्रकाशकाभ्यां<BR> भिन्नैः) पुनर्द्वयोः समस्तपञ्चषपदो बन्धः पाञ्चालिको मतः ॥ 628.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालिका|पांचालिका
पाञ्चालिका A doll, puppet; स्तन्यत्यागात् प्रभृति सुमुखी दन्तपाञ्चालिकेव<BR> क्रीडायोगं तदनु विनयं प्रापिता वर्धिता च Māl. 10. 5; चतुःषष्टिपाञ्चालिका<BR> the 64 arts collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालेयः|पाञ्चालेय
पाञ्चालेयः A son of Pāñcālī; समार्पयत् कर्णपुत्रश्च शूरः<BR> पाञ्चालेयं शरवर्षैरनेकैः Mb. 8. 75. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल्यः|पाञ्चाल्य
पाञ्चाल्यः The prince of the Pāñcālas (द्रुपद); पाञ्चाल्यो द्विपदां<BR> वरः Mb. 3. 91. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1002-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्
पाट् <i>ind.</i> An interjection used in calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटः|पाट
पाटः<BR>—1 Extension, breadth.<BR>—2 (In geometry) The intersection of a prolonged side and perpendicular,<BR> or the figure formed by such intersection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटा
पाटः + .{@-टा@}<BR>—1 A series, order.<BR>—2 A species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटकः|पाटक
पाटकः [पट् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A splitter, divider.<BR>—2 Part of a village.<BR>—3 The half of a village.<BR>—4 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>—5 A bank, shore.<BR>—6 A flight of steps leading to the water.<BR>—7 Loss of capital or stock.<BR>—8 A long span.<BR>—9 Throwing dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटच्चरः|पाटच्चर
पाटच्चरः A thief, robber, pilferer; कुसुमरसपाटच्चर Ś. 6;<BR> पद्मिनीपरिमलालिपाटच्चरै; Bv. 2. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटनम्
पाटनम् [पट् भावे ल्युट्] Splitting, breaking, cleaving, destroying;<BR> स्वर्गद्वारकपाटपाटनपटुर्धर्मोऽपि नोपार्जितः<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाटनक्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटनक्रिया
पाटनम् + -क्रिया lancing an ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Torn, cleft, split, broken.<BR>—2 Pierced, pricked; आशिषामनुपदं समस्पृशद् दर्भपाटिततलेन पाणिना R. 11. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल <i>a.</i> [पट् णिच् कलच्] Pale-red, of a pink or pale-red<BR> colour; अग्रे स्त्रीनखपाटलं कुरबकम् V. 2. 7; R. 1. 83, 2. 29, 7. 27;<BR> पाटलपाणिजाङ्कितमुरः Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलः|पाटल|पाटलं
पाटल + .{@-लः@} —1 The pale-red or pink colour; कपोलपाटलादेशि बभूव रघुचेष्टितम् R. 4. 68.<BR>—2 The trumpet-flower, Bignonia Suaveolens; पाटलसंसर्गसुरभिवनवाताः Ś. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलम्
पाटल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 The flower of this tree; R. 16. 52; यत् स भग्नसहकारमासवं रक्तपाटलसमागमं पपौ 19. 46.<BR>—2 A kind of rice ripening in the rains.<BR>—3 Saffron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाटलोपलः, पाटलकीटः, पाटलद्रुमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलोपलः|पाटलोपल
पाटल + -उपलः a ruby; समुल्लसच्छकलितपाटलोपलः Śi. 17. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलकीटः|पाटलकीट
पाटल + -कीटः a kind of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलद्रुमः|पाटलद्रुम
पाटल + -द्रुमः the trumpet-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलक
पाटलक <i>a.</i> Of a pale-red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटला
पाटला<BR>—1 The red <i>Lodhra</i>.<BR>—2 The trumpet-flower (the tree or its blossom).<BR>—3 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलावती
पाटलावती An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिः|पाटलि
पाटलिः <i>f.</i> The trumpet-flower.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाटलिपुत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्रम्
पाटलिः + -पुत्रम् N. of an ancient city, the capital of Magadha, situated<BR> near the confluence of the Śoṇa and the Ganges, and identified by some<BR> with the modern Pātṇā. It is also known by the names of पुष्पपुर,<BR> कुसुमपुर; see Mu. 2, 3, and 4. 16, and R. 6. 24 also; तदिदं दिव्यं<BR> नगरं मायारचितं सपौरमत एव । नाम्ना पाटलिपुत्रं क्षेत्रं लक्ष्मीसरस्वत्योः<BR> Ks. 3. 78. अस्ति भागीरथीतीरे पाटलिपुत्रं नाम नगरम् H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलित
पाटलित <i>a.</i> Made red, reddened; त्विषां ततिः पाटलिताम्बुवाहा Ki. 16. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिमन्
पाटलिमन् <i>m.</i> Pale-red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल्या
पाटल्या A multitude of Pāṭala flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिक|पाटलिकः
पाटलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Knowing the secrets of others.<BR>—2 Knowing time and place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिकः|पाटलिक
पाटलिक + .{@-कः@} A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटवम्
पाटवम् [पटोर्भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Sharpness, acuteness.<BR>—2 Cleverness, skill, dexterity, proficiency; पाटवं संस्कृतोक्तिषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">Page1003-2</a>]<BR> H. 1; ह्रीविमोहविरहादुपलेभे पाटवं नु हृदयं नु वधूभिः Ki. 9. 54.<BR>—3 Energy.<BR>—4 Quickness, rashness.<BR>—5 Health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Clever, sharp, skilful; रणे रभसनिर्भिन्नद्विपपाटविकासिनि । न<BR> तत्र गतभीः कश्चिद् विपपाट विकासिनि ॥ Śi. 19. 56.<BR>—2 Cunning, fraudulent, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटी
पाटी Arithmetic; अस्ति त्रैराशिकं बीजं पाटी च विमला मतिः Līlā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाट्युपरिकः, पाटीगणितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्युपरिकः|पाट्युपरिक
पाटी + -उपरिकः the chief officer of the Accounts departments; IHQ. VI, 53 ff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीगणितम्
पाटी + -गणितम् arithmetic; the science of Arithmetic; पाटी नाम संकलितव्यवकलितगुणनभाजनादीनां<BR> क्रमः तया युक्तं गणितं पाटीगणितम् Līlāvatī-ṭīkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीरः|पाटीर
पाटीरः<BR>—1 Sandal; पाटीर तव पटीयान् कः परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुम् Bv. 1. 12.<BR>—2 A field.<BR>—3 Tin.<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR>—5 A sieve.<BR>—6 A pungent root.<BR>—7 The manna of the bamboo.<BR>—8 Catarrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठः|पाठ
पाठः [पठ्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Reciting, recitation, repeating.<BR>—2 Reading, perusal, study.<BR>—3 Studying or reciting the Vedas (ब्रह्मयज्ञ), one of the five daily<BR> Yajñas or sacrifices to be performed by Brāhmaṇas.<BR>—4 A particular method of reciting the text of the Veda (of which there<BR> are five:− संहिता, पद, क्रम, जटा and घन).<BR>—5 The text of a book, a reading, variant; अत्र गन्धवद् गन्धमादनम्<BR> इति आगन्तुकः पाठः । प्राचीनपाठस्तु सुगन्धिर्गन्धमादनः इति पुल्लिङ्गान्तः<BR> Malli. on Ku. 6. 46.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाठान्तरम्, पाठक्रमः, पाठच्छेदः, पाठदोषः, पाठनिश्चयः, पाठभूः, पाठमञ्जरी, पाठशालिनी, पाठशाला, पाठशालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठान्तरम्
पाठः + -अन्तरम् another reading, a variant (v. l.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक्रमः
पाठः + -क्रमः the order determined or expressed by the recitation or<BR> the statement; यः पाठक्रमः स एव नियम्येत ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठच्छेदः|पाठच्छेद
पाठः + -छेदः a pause, caesura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठदोषः|पाठदोष
पाठः + -दोषः a false reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठनिश्चयः|पाठनिश्चय
पाठः + -निश्चयः determining the text of a passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठभूः
पाठः + -भूः <i>f.</i> a place where the Vedas are learnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठमञ्जरी
पाठः + -मञ्जरी, -शालिनी the Sārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशालिनी
पाठः + -मञ्जरी, -शालिनी the Sārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशाला
पाठः + -शाला a school, college, seminary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशालिन्
पाठः + -शालिन् <i>m.</i> a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठकः|पाठक
पाठकः [पठ्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A teacher, lecturer, preceptor. पठकाः पाठकाश्चैव ये चान्ये शास्त्रचिन्तकाः ।<BR> सर्वे व्यसनिनो मूर्खा यः क्रियावान् स पण्डितः Mb. 3. 313. 110.<BR>—2 A public reader of the Purāṇas or other sacred books.<BR>—3 A spiritual teacher.<BR>—4 A pupil, student, scholar.<BR>—5 The text of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठनम्
पाठनम् Teaching, lecturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित <i>p. p.</i> Taught, instructed; पाठितोऽपि खलु विस्मृत एव N. 5. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिक
पाठिक <i>a.</i> Conformable to the text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिन्
पाठिन् <i>a.</i> [पठ्-णिनि]<BR>—1 One who has read or studied any subject.<BR>—2 Knowing or familiar with. ━<i>m.</i> A Brāhmaṇa who has finished his studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीनः|पाठीन
पाठीनः<BR>—1 A public reader of the Purāṇas or other mythological books.<BR>—2 A kind of fish; विवृत्तपाठीनपराहतं पयः Ki. 4. 5; Ms. 5. 16.<BR>—3 N. of a tree (Moringa with red blossoms).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1003-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठद्व्य
पाठद्व्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be recited.<BR>—2 To be taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठद्व्यम्
पाठद्व्य + .{@-म्@} See पठण; पाठ्ये गेये च मधुरम् (काव्यं रामायणम्) Rām. 1. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाडिनी
पाडिनी<BR>—1 An earthen pot.<BR>—2 A boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणः|पाण
पाणः [पण् भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Trade, traffic; समीक्ष्य च बहून् दोषान् संवासाद् विद्धि पाणयोः Mb. 13. 44. 37.<BR>—2 A trader.<BR>—3 A game; a turn in game (Mar. डाव); एकपाणेन भद्रं ते प्राणयोश्च<BR> पणावहे Mb. 3. 78. 6.<BR>—4 A stake at play; दीव्यामहे पार्थिव मा विशङ्कां कुरुष्व पाणं च चिरं<BR> च मा कृथाः Mb. 2. 59. 8.<BR>—5 An agreement.<BR>—6 Praise.<BR>—7 The hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिः|पाणि
पाणिः [पण्-इण् आयाभावः, cf. Uṇ. 4. 132]<BR>—1 The hand; दानेन पाणिर्न तु कङ्कणेन (विभाति) Bh. 2. 71; often<BR> at the end of comp. in the sense of ‘carrying in the hand’; as चक्र˚,<BR> खड्ग˚ &c.; पाणिं ग्रह् or पीड् ‘to take the hand of, lead to the altar, marry’<BR>. पाणौ कृ to hold by the hand, marry; पाणौकरणम्<BR> ‘marriage’. —2 Ved. A hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिः|पाणि
पाणिः + .{@-णिः@} <i>f.</i> A market.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाणिकच्छपिका, पाणिकर्मन्, पाणिगत, पाणिगृहीती, पाणिग्रहः, पाणिग्रहणम्, पाणिग्राहः, पाणिग्रहणिक, पाणिग्रहणीय, पाणिग्रहीतृ, पाणिघः, पाणिघातः, पाणिचापल्यम्, पाणिजः, पाणितलम्, पाणितालः, पाणिदाक्ष्यम्, पाणिधर्मः, पाणिपल्लवः, पाणिपात्र, पाणिपीडनम्, पाणिप्रणयिनी, पाणिबन्धः, पाणिभुज्, पाणिमुक्तम्, पाणिमुखाः, पाणिरुह्, पाणिवादः, पाणिसर्ग्या, पाणिस्वनिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिकच्छपिका
पाणिः + -कच्छपिका <i>f.</i> A kind of मुद्रा (= कूर्ममुद्रा); Kālikā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिकर्मन्|पाणिकर्म्मन्
पाणिः + -कर्मन् <i>m.</i> —1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 one playing on a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिगत
पाणिः + -गत <i>a.</i> ready, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिगृहीती
पाणिः + -गृहीती ‘espoused by the hand’, a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहः|पाणिग्रह
पाणिः + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम्, -ग्राहः marrying, marriage; इति स्वसुर्भोजकुलप्रदीपः<BR> संपाद्य पाणिग्रहणं स राजा R. 7. 29, 8. 7; Ku. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणम्
पाणिः + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम्, -ग्राहः marrying, marriage; इति स्वसुर्भोजकुलप्रदीपः<BR> संपाद्य पाणिग्रहणं स राजा R. 7. 29, 8. 7; Ku. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्राहः|पाणिग्राह
पाणिः + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम्, -ग्राहः marrying, marriage; इति स्वसुर्भोजकुलप्रदीपः<BR> संपाद्य पाणिग्रहणं स राजा R. 7. 29, 8. 7; Ku. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणिक
पाणिः + -ग्रहणिक, -ग्रहणीय <i>a.</i> matrimoinal, nuptial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणीयम्
पाणिः + -ग्रहणिक, -ग्रहणीय + .({@-यम्@}) a nuptial gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणीय
पाणिः + -ग्रहणिक, -ग्रहणीय <i>a.</i> matrimoinal, nuptial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहीतृ
पाणिः + -ग्रहीतृ <i>m.</i>, {@-ग्राहः@}<BR> a bridegroom, husband; ध्यायत्यनिष्टं यत्किंचित् पाणिग्राहस्य<BR> चेतसा Ms. 9. 21; बाल्ये पितुर्वशे तिष्ठेत् पाणिग्राहस्य यौवने 5. 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघः|पाणिघ
पाणिः + -घः<BR>—1 a drummer; शिल्पिभिः पाणिघैः क्रुद्धः Bk. 6. 113.<BR>—2 a workman, handicrafts-man; cf. P. III. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघातः|पाणिघात
पाणिः + -घातः<BR>—1 a blow with the hand.<BR>—2 boxing.<BR>—3 a boxer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिचापल्यम्
पाणिः + -चापल्यम् snapping the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिजः|पाणिज
पाणिः + -जः a fingernail; तस्याः पाटलपाणिजाङ्कितमुरः Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणितलम्
पाणिः + -तलम् the palm of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणितालः|पाणिताल
पाणिः + -तालः (in music) a particular measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिदाक्ष्यम्
पाणिः + -दाक्ष्यम् trickery (Mar. हातचलाखी); दीक्षा विपत्सु दिश दर्शय<BR> पाणिदाक्ष्यम् Bm. 2. 323.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिधर्मः|पाणिधर्म|पाणिधर्म्म
पाणिः + -धर्मः due form of marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपल्लवः|पाणिपल्लव
पाणिः + -पल्लवः<BR>—1 a sprout-like hand.<BR>—2 the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपात्र
पाणिः + -पात्र <i>a.</i> drinking by means of the hand; cf. पाणिः पात्रं<BR> पवित्रम् Bh. 3. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपीडनम्
पाणिः + -पीडनम् marriage; पाणिपीडनमहं दमयन्त्याः कामयेमहि महीमिहिकांशो<BR> N. 5. 99; पाणिपीडनविधेरनन्तरम् Ku. 8. 1; Māl. 8. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिप्रणयिनी
पाणिः + -प्रणयिनी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिबन्धः|पाणिबन्ध|पाणिबंध
पाणिः + -बन्धः ‘union of the hands’, marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिभुज्
पाणिः + -भुज् <i>m.</i> the sacred figtree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिमुक्तम्
पाणिः + -मुक्तम् a missile thrown with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिमुखाः
पाणिः + -मुखाः <i>m.</i> (pl.) the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिरुह्
पाणिः + -रुह् <i>m.</i>, {@-रुहः@}<BR> a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिवादः|पाणिवाद
पाणिः + -वादः<BR>—1 clapping the hands together.<BR>—2 playing on a drum, a clapper; … पाणिवादाश्च वैणिकाः Śiva B. 31. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिसर्ग्या
पाणिः + -सर्ग्या a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिस्वनिक
पाणिः + -स्वनिक <i>a.</i> playing musical instruments with the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिंधम|पाणिन्धम|पाणिन्धमः
पाणिंधम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blowing through the hands; cf. Kāśi. on P. III. 2. 37.<BR>—2 Chilly, as a road or journey.<BR>—3 Obscure, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिंधय|पाणिन्धय|पाणिन्धयः
पाणिंधय <i>a.</i> Drinking out of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिक|पाणिकः
पाणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Got by playing at stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिकः|पाणिक
पाणिक + .{@-कः@} A merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिका
पाणिका<BR>—1 A kind of song; Y.<BR>—2 A kind of spoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनिः|पाणिनि
पाणिनिः N. of a celebrated grammarian who is considered as an inspired<BR> <i>muni</i>, and is said to have derived the knowledge of his grammar from<BR> Śiva; येनाक्षरसमाम्नायमधिगम्य महेश्वरात् । कृत्स्नं व्याकरणं चक्रे<BR> तस्मै पाणिनये नमः ॥ Śekhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं|पाणिनीयः
पाणिनीय <i>a.</i> Relating to or composed by Pāṇini; पाणिनीयमिवालोकि<BR> धीरैस्तत्समराजिरम् Śi. 19. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीयः|पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं
पाणिनीय + .{@-यः@} A follower of Pāṇini; अकृतव्यूहाः पाणिनीयाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीयम्
पाणिनीय + .{@-यम्@} The grammar of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डर|पांडर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पाण्डर <i>a.</i> Whitish, pale-white; यत् कङ्कालमकालपाण्डुरघनप्रस्पर्धि<BR> रुन्धन्नभः Mv. 5. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डरम्
पाण्डर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Red-chalk.<BR>—2 The blossom of the jasmine.<BR>—3 Semen virile; पाण्डरं शुक्रमित्याहुः Dhyān. Up. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवः|पाण्डव|पांडव|पांडवः
पाण्डवः [पाण्डोरपत्यं पुमान् ओरञ्] ‘A son or descendant of Pāṇḍu’,<BR> N. of any one of the five sons of Pāṇḍu; <i>i. e.</i> युधिष्ठिर, भीम,<BR> अर्जुन, नकुल and सहदेव; मामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत सञ्जय<BR> Bg. 1. 1; हंसाः संप्रति पाण्डवा इव वनादज्ञातचर्यां गताः Mk. 5. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाण्डवाभीलः, पाण्डवश्रेष्ठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवाभीलः|पाण्डवाभील|पांडवाभील
पाण्डवः + -आभीलः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवश्रेष्ठः|पाण्डवश्रेष्ठ
पाण्डवः + -श्रेष्ठः N. of Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवायनः|पाण्डवायन|पांडवायनः
पाण्डवायनः An epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवीय|पांडवीय
पाण्डवीय^1 <i>a.</i> Belonging to the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवेयः|पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पांडवेयः
पाण्डवेयः = पाण्डव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डित्यम्
पाण्डित्यम्<BR>—1 Scholarship, profound learning, erudition; तदेव गमकं पाण्डित्यवैदग्ध्ययोः Māl. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Cleverness, skill, dexterity, sharpness; नखानां पाण्डित्यं प्रकटयतु<BR> कस्मिन् मृगपतिः Bv. 1. 2; परोपदेशे पाण्डित्यं सर्वेषां सुकरं नृणाम्.<BR>—3 Prudence; न स्वल्पस्य कृते भूरि नाशयेन्मतिमान्नरः । एतदेव हि<BR> पाण्डित्यं यत् स्वल्पाद् भूरिरक्षणम् ॥ Pt. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डिमन्
पाण्डिमन् <i>m.</i> Whiteness (पाण्डुत्व); पाण्डिमा गण्डमूले Bv. 2. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डु|पांडु|पाण्डुः
पाण्डु <i>a.</i> Pale-white, whitish, pale, yellowish; यथा पाण्ड्वाविकम्<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 3. 6; विकलकरणः पाण्डुच्छायः शुचा परिदुर्बलः U. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुः|पाण्डु|पांडु
पाण्डु + .{@-ण्डुः@}<BR>—1 The pale-white or yellowish-white colour.<BR>—2 Jaundice.<BR>—3 A white elephant.<BR>—4 N. of the father of the Pāṇḍavas. [He was begotten by Vyāsa on<BR> Ambālikā, one of the widows of Vicitravīrya. He was called Pāṇḍu,<BR> because he was born pale (पाण्डु) by reason of his mother having become<BR> quite pale with fear when in private with the sage Vyāsa; (यस्मात् पाण्डुत्वमापन्ना<BR> विरूपं प्रेक्ष्य मामिह । तस्मादेव सुतस्ते वै पाण्डुरेव भविष्यति Mb.)<BR> He was prevented by a curse from having progeny himself; so he allowed<BR> his first wife Kuntī to make use of a charm she had acquired from Durvāsas<BR> for the birth of sons. She gave birth to Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma and Arjuna;<BR> and Mādrī, his other wife, by the use of the same charm, gave birth<BR> to Nakula and Sahadeva. One day Pāṇdu forgot the curse under which he<BR> was labouring, and made bold<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">Page1005-1</a>]<BR> to embrace Mādrī, but he fell immediately dead in her arms.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाण्ड्वामयः, पाण्डुकम्बलः, पाण्डुकम्बलिन्, पाण्डुपुत्रः, पाण्डुपृष्ठ, पाण्डुभावः, पाण्डुभूमः, पाण्डुमृत्तिका, पाण्डुमृद्, पाण्डुरङ्गः, पाण्डुरागः, पाण्डुरोगः, पाण्डुलेखः, पाण्डुलोहम्, पाण्डुवर्ण, पाण्डुशर्करा, पाण्डुशर्मिला, पाण्डुसोपाकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1004-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्वामयः|पाण्ड्वामय|पांड्वामय
पाण्डु + -आमयः jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बलः|पाण्डुकम्बल|पांडुकंबल
पाण्डु + -कम्बलः<BR>—1 a white blanket.<BR>—2 a warm upper garment.<BR>—3 the housing of a royal elephant.<BR>—4 A kind of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बलिन्
पाण्डु + -कम्बलिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a carriage covered with a woollen blanket.<BR>—2 the housings of a royal elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपुत्रः|पाण्डुपुत्र|पांडुपुत्र
पाण्डु + -पुत्रः a son of Pāṇḍu, any one of the five Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपृष्ठ|पाण्डुपृष्ठः
पाण्डु + -पृष्ठ <i>a.</i> ‘white-backed’, having no auspicious marks on the<BR> body, one from whom nothing great is to be expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुभावः|पाण्डुभाव
पाण्डु + -भावः Becoming yellowish white, pale; न कलङ्कानुगमो न पाण्डुभावः Bv. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुभूमः|पाण्डुभूम
पाण्डु + -भूमः a region full of chalky soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्तिका|पांडुमृत्तिका
पाण्डु + -मृत्तिका<BR>—1 white or pale soil.<BR>—2 the opal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृद्
पाण्डु + -मृद् <i>f.</i> chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरङ्गः|पाण्डुरङ्ग
पाण्डु + -रङ्गः N. of a god (at Pandharpur), Viṭṭhala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरागः|पाण्डुराग|पांडुराग
पाण्डु + -रागः whiteness, pallor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरोगः|पाण्डुरोग|पांडुरोग
पाण्डु + -रोगः jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुलेखः|पाण्डुलेख|पांडुलेख
पाण्डु + -लेखः a sketch made with chalk; a rough draft or sketch made<BR> on the ground, board &c.; पाण्डुलेखेन फलके भूमौ वा प्रथमं लिखेत् ।<BR> न्यूनाधिकं तु संशोध्य पश्चात् पत्रे निवेशयेत् ॥ Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुलोहम्
पाण्डु + -लोहम् silver; पाण्डुलोहशृङ्खलात्मना मया पादपद्मयोर्युगलं<BR> तव निगडयित्वा Dk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुवर्ण
पाण्डु + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुशर्करा|पाण्डुशर्क्करा
पाण्डु + -शर्करा light-coloured gravel (प्रमेहभेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुशर्मिला|पांडुशर्मिला|पाण्डुशर्म्मिला
पाण्डु + -शर्मिला an epithet of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुसोपाकः|पाण्डुसोपाक|पांडुसोपाक
पाण्डु + -सोपाकः N. of a mixed tribe; चाण्डालात् पाण्डुसोपाकस्त्वक्सारव्यवहारवान्<BR> Ms. 10. 37; Mb. 13. 48. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकः|पाण्डुक|पांडुकः
पाण्डुकः<BR>—1 The yellowish-white colour.<BR>—2 Jaundice<BR>—3 N. of Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकिन्|पांडुकिन्
पाण्डुकिन् <i>a.</i> Suffering from jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुर|पांडुर
पाण्डुर <i>a.</i> [पाण्डुवर्णोऽस्यास्ति र] Whitish, pale, pale-white,<BR> yellowish-white; पाण्डुरेणातपत्रेण ध्रियमाणेन मूर्धनि । शुशुभे तारकाराजः<BR> सितमभ्रमिव स्थितः Mb. 3. 41. 14. छविः पाण्डुरा Ś. 3. 9; R. 14. 26; Ku. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरम्
पाण्डुर + .{@-रम्@} The white leprosy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाण्डुरेक्षुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरेक्षुः|पाण्डुरेक्षु|पांडुरेक्षु
पाण्डुर + -इक्षुः a species of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरिमन्|पांडुरिमन्
पाण्डुरिमन् <i>m.</i> Paleness, white or pale colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्यकवाटकम्
पाण्ड्यकवाटकम् A gem from the country of पाण्ड्यकवाटक; Kau. A. 2. 10. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्याः
पाण्ड्याः <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants; तस्यामेव<BR> रघोः पाण्ड्याः प्रतापं न विषेहिरे R. 4. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्यः|पाण्ड्य|पांड्य
पाण्ड्याः + .{@-ण्ड्यः@} A king of that country; पाण्ड्योऽयमंसार्पितलम्बहारः R. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्वम्
पाण्ड्वम् An uncoloured woollen garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
पाण्य <i>a.</i> Praiseworthy, commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात् <i>a.</i> Protecting, guarding. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Falling.<BR>—2 Sin.<BR>—3 A guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
पात <i>p. p.</i> Protected, guarded &c.; see पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातः|पात
पातः [पत्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Flying, flight.<BR>—2 Alighting, descending, descent.<BR>—3 Falling down, fall, downfall (fig. also); द्रुम˚, गृह˚; &c. चरणपातः<BR> ‘falling down at the feet’; तस्याभवत् क्षणशुचः परितोषलाभः कक्षाग्निलङ्घिततरोरिव<BR> वृष्टिपातः R. 11. 92; पातोत्पातौ ‘rise and fall’.<BR>—4 Destruction, dissolution, ruin; आसीनमासन्नशरीरपातस्त्रियम्बकं<BR> संयमिनं ददर्श<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">Page1005-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 3. 44.<BR>—5 A blow, stroke; as in खड्गपातः.<BR>—6 Shedding, discharging, emitting; असृक्पातैः Ms. 8. 44.<BR>—7 A cast, throw, shot; कुरुष्व तावत् करभोरु पश्चान्मार्गे मृगप्रोक्षिणि<BR> दृष्टिपातम् R. 13. 18.<BR>—8 An attack, inroad.<BR>—9 Happening, coming to pass, occurrence.<BR>—10 A failing, defect.<BR>—11 An epithet of Rāhu; दक्षिणोत्तरतोऽप्येवं पातु राहुः स्वरंहसा ।<BR> विक्षिपत्येष विक्षेपं चन्द्रादीनामपक्रमात् ॥ Sūrya S.<BR>—12 (In astr.) An inauspicious or malignant position or aspect.<BR>—13 The node in a planetʼs orbit.<BR>—14 Application (of ointment, of a knife &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन <i>a.</i> [पत्-णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Felling, cutting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातनम्
पातन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Causing to fall down, bringing or throwing down, knocking down.<BR>—2 Throwing, casting.<BR>—3 Humbling, lowering.<BR>—4 Removing.<BR>—5 N. of a particular process to which minerals (esp. quicksilver) are<BR> subjected. <i>N. B.</i> पातनम् may have different meanings according<BR> to the noun with which it is used; <i>e. g.</i> दण्डस्य पातनम् ‘causing the rod to fall’<BR>, <i>i. e.</i> chastising; गर्भस्य पातनम् ‘causing the foetus to fall’<BR>, causing an abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातनिका
पातनिका Fitness, correspondence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित
पातित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cast down, struck down.<BR>—2 Overthrown, humbled.<BR>—3 Lowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिन्
पातिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पत्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Going to, descending, alighting on.<BR>—2 Falling, sinking.<BR>—3 Being contained in.<BR>—4 Felling or throwing down.<BR>—5 Pouring forth, discharging, emitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पत्-उकञ्]<BR>—1 Falling habitually or frequently; संयच्छन् भवति प्राणानसंयच्छंस्तु<BR> पातुकः Mb. 12. 91. 42; Śi. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Apt or disposed to fall.<BR>—3 Losing oneʼs caste.<BR>—4 Going to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुकः|पातुक
पातुक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The declivity of a mountain, a precipice.<BR>—2 The water-elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
पात्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be caused to fall, to be felled or cut down.<BR>—2 To be imposed (as a fine); see पत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकः|पातक|पातकं
पातकः, -कम्<BR> [पातयति नरं, पत्-ण्वुल्] Sin, crime; (Hindu law-givers<BR> enumerate five great sins:− ब्रह्महत्या सुरापानं स्तेयं गुर्वङ्गनागमः ।<BR> महान्ति पातकान्याहुः संसर्गश्चापि तैः सह Ms. 11. 54).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकम्
पातकः, -कम्<BR> [पातयति नरं, पत्-ण्वुल्] Sin, crime; (Hindu law-givers<BR> enumerate five great sins:− ब्रह्महत्या सुरापानं स्तेयं गुर्वङ्गनागमः ।<BR> महान्ति पातकान्याहुः संसर्गश्चापि तैः सह Ms. 11. 54).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन् <i>a.</i> Sinful, guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्ग|पातंग
पातङ्ग <i>a.</i> Brown; Mb. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्गिः|पातङ्गि|पातंगि|पातंगिः
पातङ्गिः^1<BR>—1 An epithet of Saturn.<BR>—2 Of Yama.<BR>—3 Of Karṇa.<BR>—4 Of Sugrīva.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. note: diacritic misplaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जल|पातंजल|पातञ्जलं
पातञ्जल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Composed by Patañjali; पातञ्जले महाभाष्ये कृतभूरिपरिश्रमः<BR> Pari. Śekh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जलम्
पातञ्जल + .{@-लम्@} The Yoga system of philosophy taught by Patañjali. (It is<BR> generally believed that Patañjali, the author of the Mahābhāṣya, is<BR> the same as the author of the Yoga system; but it is a dubious point.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1005-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालम्
पातालम् [पतत्यस्मिन्नधर्मेण पत्-आलञ्; cf. Uṇ. 1. 114]<BR>—1 The last of the seven regions or worlds under the earth said to be<BR> peopled by Nāgas; the seven regions are:− अतल, वितल, सुतल, रसातल,<BR> तलातल, महातल and पाताल.<BR>—2 The lower regions or world in general; मा मेति व्याहरत्येव तस्मिन्<BR> पातालमभ्यगात् R. 15. 84, 1. 80; पातालान्न विमोचितो बत बली नीतो<BR> न मृत्युः क्षयम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 An excavation, a hole.<BR>—4 Submarine fire.<BR>—5 (In astrol.) The fourth house or sign from that in which the sun is present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालः|पाताल|पातालं
पातालम् + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A kind of instrument for distillation or the calcination and sublimation of metals.<BR>—2 N. of Jupiterʼs year (of 361 days).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पातालगङ्गा, पातालौकस्, पातालतलम्, पातालमूलम्, पातालमुखम्, पातालमूलम्, पातालयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालगङ्गा|पातालगंगा
पातालम् + -गङ्गा the Ganges of the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालौकस्
पातालम् + -ओकस् <i>m.</i>, {@-निलयः, -निवासः, -वासिन्@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a demon.<BR>—2 a Nāga or a serpent-demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालतलम्
पातालम् + -तलम्, -मूलम् the bottom of Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालमूलम्
पातालम् + -तलम्, -मूलम् the bottom of Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालमुखम्
पातालम् + -मुखम् a great hollow (महागर्त); यस्त्वद्य पातालमुखे<BR> पतन्तं पाणौ गृहीत्वा प्रतिसंहरेत Mb. 3. 268. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालमूलम्
पातालम् + -मूलम् the centre of gravity; आस्ते पातालमूलस्थः शोषोऽशेषसुतर्चितः<BR> V. P. 2. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालयन्त्रम्
पातालम् + -यन्त्रम् See पातालः (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिः|पाति
पातिः<BR>—1 A master.<BR>—2 A bird.<BR>—3 A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिकः|पातिक
पातिकः The Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित्यम्
पातित्यम् Loss of caste or position; एतत् पातित्यदान्नो जघनमतिघनादेनसो<BR> माननीयम् Viṣṇupāda. S. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिली
पातिली<BR>—1 A snare, trap.<BR>—2 A small earthen vessel (Mar. पातेलें).<BR>—3 A woman of a particular class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिव्रती
पातिव्रती, पातिव्रत्यम् Fidelity to a husband, chastity; Śāhendra. 1. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिव्रत्यम्
पातिव्रती, पातिव्रत्यम् Fidelity to a husband, chastity; Śāhendra. 1. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्त्र
पात्त्र <i>a.</i> Releasing from sins; सर्वेषामेव पात्त्राणां परं<BR> पात्त्रं महेश्वरः Nandī P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रम्
पात्रम् [पाति रक्षत्याधेयं, पिबत्यनेन वा पा-ष्ट्रन् Tv.]<BR>—1 A drinking-vessel, cup, jar.<BR>—2 A vessel or pot in general; पात्रे निधायार्ध्यम् R. 5. 2, 12; any<BR> sacrificial vessel or utensil.<BR>—3 A receptacle of any kind, recipient; दैन्यस्य पात्रतामेति Pt. 2. 101.<BR>—4 A reservoir.<BR>—5 A fit or worthy person, a person fit or worthy to receive gifts; वित्तस्य<BR> पात्रे व्ययः Bh. 2. 82; अदेशकाले यद् दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते Bg. 17. 22;<BR> Y. 1. 201; R. 11. 86.<BR>—6 An actor, a <i>dramatis persona</i>; तत् प्रतिपात्रमाधीयतां यत्नः<BR> Ś. 1; उच्यतां पात्रवर्गः v. l. <i>dramatis personae</i>.<BR>—7 A kingʼs minister.<BR>—8 The channel or bed of a river. सुरस्रवन्त्या इव पात्रमागतम् N. 16. 11, 15. 86.<BR>—9 Fitness, propriety.<BR>—10 An order, command.<BR>—11 A leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रः|पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं
पात्रम् + .{@-त्रः@}<BR>—1 A kind of measure (आढक).<BR>—2 A preservative from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्री
पात्रम् + .{@-त्री@}<BR>—1 A vessel, plate, dish; भुञ्जन्ते रुक्मपात्रीभिर्यत्राहं परिचारिका<BR> Mb. 3. 30. 13, 233. 49.<BR>—2 A small furnace.<BR>—3 N. of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पात्रासादनम्, पात्रोपकरणम्, पात्रपालः, पात्रभृत्, पात्रमेलनम्, पात्रशेषः, पात्रसंस्कारः, पात्रसंचारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रासादनम्
पात्रम् + -आसादनम् the placing of sacrificial utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रोपकरणम्
पात्रम् + -उपकरणम् ornaments of a secondary kind (as bells, chowries &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रपालः|पात्रपाल
पात्रम् + -पालः<BR>—1 a large paddle used as a rudder.<BR>—2 the rod of a balance (तुलाघट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रभृत्
पात्रम् + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a servant;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रमेलनम्
पात्रम् + -मेलनम् (In dram.) the bringing together of the characters of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रशेषः|पात्रशेष
पात्रम् + -शेषः scraps of food.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">Page1006-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंस्कारः|पात्रसंस्कार
पात्रम् + -संस्कारः<BR>—1 the cleaning or purification of a vessel.<BR>—2 the current of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंचारः|पात्रसञ्चार
पात्रम् + -संचारः the handing round of vessels at a meal; Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रकम्
पात्रकम् A vessel, pot &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रट|पात्रटः
पात्रट <i>a.</i> Lean, emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटः|पात्रट
पात्रट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A cup, pot<BR>—2 Rugged garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटीरः|पात्रटीर
पात्रटीरः<BR>—1 A competent minister.<BR>—2 A vessel of iron, brass or silver.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR>—4 A crow.<BR>—5 A heron.<BR>—6 Rust of iron.<BR>—7 Mucus running from the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रता
पात्रता, पात्रत्वम्<BR>—1 Capacity, worthiness.<BR>—2 Dignity, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रत्वम्
पात्रता, पात्रत्वम्<BR>—1 Capacity, worthiness.<BR>—2 Dignity, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रयति
पात्रयति Den. P. To use as a drinking-vessel; पाणिं पात्रयताम् Bh. 3. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसात्
पात्रसात् <i>ind.</i> In the possession of worthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Measured out with any vessel or a measure called आढकं.<BR>—2 Fit, adequate, appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिकम्
पात्रिक + .{@-कम्, -की@} A vessel, cup, dish; तस्मा इत्युपनीताय यक्षराट् पात्रिकामदात्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 18. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिकी
पात्रिक + .{@-कम्, -की@} A vessel, cup, dish; तस्मा इत्युपनीताय यक्षराट् पात्रिकामदात्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 18. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिका
पात्रिक + .{@-का@} An alms-bowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having or provided with a drinking-vessel; Ms. 6. 52.<BR>—2 Having fit or worthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीकृ
पात्रीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To make worthy; पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20.<BR>—2 To honour, dignify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीण
पात्रीण <i>a.</i> Measured, sown, or cooked with a Pātra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीय|पात्रीयं
पात्रीय, पात्र्य <i>a.</i> Worthy to partake of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र्य
पात्रीय, पात्र्य <i>a.</i> Worthy to partake of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीयम्
पात्रीयम् A sacrificial vessel or utensil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीरः|पात्रीर|पात्रीरं
पात्रीरः, -रम्<BR> An oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीरम्
पात्रीरः, -रम्<BR> An oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेबहुलः|पात्रेबहुल
पात्रेबहुलः, -पात्रेसमितः<BR>—1 ‘Constant at meals or dinner-time’, a parasite;<BR> वृतस्त्वं पात्रेसमितैः Bk. 5. 10.<BR>—3 A treacherous or hypocritical fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेसमितः|पात्रेसमित
पात्रेबहुलः, -पात्रेसमितः<BR>—1 ‘Constant at meals or dinner-time’, a parasite;<BR> वृतस्त्वं पात्रेसमितैः Bk. 5. 10.<BR>—3 A treacherous or hypocritical fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रौकरणम्
पात्रौकरणम् Marriage ममैव पात्रौकरणेऽग्निसाक्षिकमङ्गसङ्गतम् N. 6. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथः|पाथ|पाथं
पाथः [पीयतेऽदः पा-कर्मणि थ]<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथम्
पाथः + .{@-थम्@} Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस् <i>n.</i> [पा-असुन् थुक् च]<BR>—1 Water; हरन्तां संतापं कमपि मरुदुल्लासलहरीछटाश्चञ्चत्पाथः<BR> कणसरणयो दिव्यसरितः G. L. 26; Mv. 6. 12.<BR>—2 Air, wind.<BR>—3 Food.<BR>—4 The sky.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाथोजम्, पाथोदः, पाथोधरः, पाथोधिः, पाथोनिधिः, पाथःपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोजम्
पाथस् + -जम्<BR>—1 a lotus.<BR>—2 a conch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोदः|पाथोद
पाथस् + -दः, -धरः a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधरः|पाथोधर
पाथस् + -दः, -धरः a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधिः|पाथोधि
पाथस् + -धिः, -निधिः, -पतिः the ocean; N. 13. 20; पाथोधिमध्ये पतितः<BR> पतङ्गः Rām. Ch. 6. 7; पाथोधिर्जलधिः पयोधिरुदधिर्बारांनिधिर्वारिधिः Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोनिधिः|पाथोनिधि
पाथस् + -धिः, -निधिः, -पतिः the ocean; N. 13. 20; पाथोधिमध्ये पतितः<BR> पतङ्गः Rām. Ch. 6. 7; पाथोधिर्जलधिः पयोधिरुदधिर्बारांनिधिर्वारिधिः Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथःपतिः
पाथस् + -धिः, -निधिः, -पतिः the ocean; N. 13. 20; पाथोधिमध्ये पतितः<BR> पतङ्गः Rām. Ch. 6. 7; पाथोधिर्जलधिः पयोधिरुदधिर्बारांनिधिर्वारिधिः Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथिस्
पाथिस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sea.<BR>—2 The eye. ━<i>n.</i> Scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेयम्
पाथेयम् [पथि तद्व्यहारे वा साधु ढञ्]<BR>—1 Provender or provisions for a journey, viaticum; जग्राह पाथेयमिवेन्द्रसूनुः<BR> Ki. 3. 37; बिसकिसलयच्छेदपाथेयवन्तः Me. 11; V. 4. 15.<BR>—2 The sign <i>virgo</i> of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1006-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादः|पाद
पादः [पद्यते गम्यतेऽनेन करणे कर्मणि वा घञ्]<BR>—1 The foot (whether of men or animals); तयोर्जगृहतुः पादान् R. 1. 57;<BR> पादयोर्निपत्य, पादपतित &c. (The word पाद at the end of<BR> comp). is changed to पाद् after सु and numerals; <i>i. e.</i> सुपाद्,<BR> द्विपाद्, त्रिपाद् &c.; and also when the first member is used as a standard<BR> of comparison, but is a word other than हस्ति &c.; see P. V. 4. 138-140;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> व्याघ्रपाद्. The nom. pl. of पाद is often added to names<BR> of persons or titles of address to show great respect or veneration; मृष्यन्तु<BR> लवस्य बालिशतां तातपादाः U. 6; जीवत्सु तातपादेषु 1. 19; देवपादानां<BR> नास्माभिः प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1; so एवमाराध्यपादा आज्ञापयन्ति Prab. 1;<BR> so कुमारिलपादाः &c.<BR>—2 A ray of light; बालस्यापि रबेः पादाः पतन्त्युपरि भूभृताम् Pt. 1. 328;<BR> Śi. 9. 34; R. 16. 53 (where the word has sense 1 also).<BR>—3 The foot or leg of an inanimate object, as of a bed-stead; चतुष्पदी<BR> हि निःश्रेणी ब्रह्मण्येव प्रतिष्ठिता Mb. 12. 20. 4.<BR>—4 The foot or root of a tree; as in पादप.<BR>—5 The foot of a mountain, a hill at the foot of a mountain (पादाः प्रत्यन्तपर्वताः);<BR> रेवां द्रक्ष्यस्युपलविषमे विन्ध्यपादे विशीर्णाम् Me. 19; Ś. 6. 17.<BR>—6 A quarter, fourth part; as in सपादो रूपकः ‘one and one fourth rupee’<BR>; Ms. 8. 241; Y. 2. 174; कार्षापणे दीयमाने पादोऽपि दत्तो भवति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 20.<BR>—7 The fourth part of a stanza, a line.<BR>—8 The fourth part of a chapter or book, as of the Adhyāyas of Pāṇini,<BR> or of the Brahma-sūtras.<BR>—9 A part in general.<BR>—10 A column, pillar; सहस्रपादं प्रासादं … अधिरोहन्मया दृष्टः<BR> Mb. 5. 143. 30.<BR>—11 A foot as a measure equal to twelve Aṅgulis.<BR>—12 The quadrant of a circle.<BR>—13 The foot-hole or bottom of a water-skin; इन्द्रियाणां तु सर्वेषां<BR> यद्येकं क्षरतीन्द्रियम् । तेनास्य क्षरति प्रज्ञा दृतेः पादादिवोदकम् ॥ Ms. 2. 99.<BR>—14 A wheel; गिरिकूबरपादाक्षं शुभवेणु त्रिवेणुमत् Mb. 3. 175. 4; Ki. 12. 21.<BR>—15 A golden coin (weighing one tola); स ह गवां सहस्रमवरुरोध<BR> दश दश पादा एकैकस्याः शृङ्गयोराबद्धा बभुवुः Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पादाग्रम्, पादाङ्कः, पादाङ्गदम्, पादाङ्गदी, पादाङ्गुलिः, पादाङ्गुली, पादाङ्गुष्ठः, पादाङ्गुष्ठिका, पादान्तः, पादान्तरम्, पादान्तिकम्, पादाम्बु, पादाम्भस्, पादारविन्दम्, पादकमलम्, पादपङ्कजम्, पादपद्मम्, पादार्घ्यम्, पादार्धम्, पादालिन्दी, पादावनामः, पादावनेजः, पादावसेचनम्, पादाष्ठीलः, पादाघातः, पादानत, पादावर्तः, पादासनम्, पादास्फालनम्, पादाहत,^1 पादाहति, पादोदकम्, पादजलम्, पादोदरः, पादोद्धूतम्, पादकटकः, पादकम्, पादकीलिका, पादकृच्छ्रम्, पादक्षेपः, पादगण्डीरः, पादग्रन्थिः, पादग्रहणम्, पादचतुरः, पादचत्वरः, पादचापल्यम्, पादचारः, पादचारिन्, पादच्छेदनम्, पादजः, पादजलम्, पादजाहम्, पादतलम्, पादत्रः, पादत्रा, पादत्राणम्, पाददारी, पाददारिका, पाददाहः, पादधावनिका, पादनालिका, पादनिकेतः, पादन्यासः, पादपः, पादपद्धतिः, पादपरिचारकः, पादपालिका, पादपाशः, पादपीठः, पादपीठम्, पादपीठिका, पादपूरणम्, पादप्रक्षालनम्, पादप्रणामः, पादप्रतिष्ठानम्, पादप्रधारणम्, पादप्रसारणम्, पादप्रहारः, पादबद्ध, पादबन्धनम्, पादभटः, पादभागः, पादमुद्रा, पादमूलम्, पादयमकः, पादरक्षः, पादरक्षणम्, पादरजस्, पादरज्जुः, पादरथी, पादरोहः, पादरोहणः, पादलग्न,^2 पादलेपः, पादवन्दनम्, पादवल्मीकः, पादविरजस्, पादवेष्टनिकः, पादकम्, पादशाखा, पादशैलः, पादशोथः, पादशौचम्, पादसंहिता, पादसेवनम्, पादसेवा, पादस्तम्भः, पादस्फोटः, पादहत, पादहर्षः, पादहीनजलम्, पादहीनात्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाग्रम्
पादः + -अग्रम् the point or extremity of the foot; पादाग्रस्थितया मुहुः<BR> स्तनभरेणानीतया नम्रताम् Ratn. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्कः|पादाङ्क
पादः + -अङ्कः a foot-mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गदम्
पादः + -अङ्गदम्, -अङ्गदी an ornament for the foot, an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गदी|पादांगदी
पादः + -अङ्गदम्, -अङ्गदी an ornament for the foot, an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुलिः|पादाङ्गुलि
पादः + -अङ्गुलिः, -अङ्गुली <i>f.</i> a toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुली
पादः + -अङ्गुलिः, -अङ्गुली <i>f.</i> a toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्ठः|पादाङ्गुष्ठ|पादांगुष्ठ
पादः + -अङ्गुष्ठः the great toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्ठिका
पादः + -अङ्गुष्ठिका a ring worn on the great toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्तः|पादान्त|पादांत
पादः + -अन्तः the point or extremity of the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्तरम्
पादः + -अन्तरम् the interval of a step, distance of a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्तरे|पादांतरे
पादः + -अन्तरम् + .({@-रे@}) <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 after the interval of a step.<BR>—2 close or near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादान्तिकम्
पादः + -अन्तिकम् <i>ind.</i> near to, towards any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाम्बु|पादांबु
पादः + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> butter-milk containing a fourth part of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाम्भस्|पादांभस्
पादः + -अम्भस् <i>n.</i> water in which the feet (of revered persons) have been washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादारविन्दम्
पादः + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -पङ्कजम्, -पद्मम् a lotus-like foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकमलम्
पादः + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -पङ्कजम्, -पद्मम् a lotus-like foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपङ्कजम्
पादः + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -पङ्कजम्, -पद्मम् a lotus-like foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपद्मम्
पादः + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -पङ्कजम्, -पद्मम् a lotus-like foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्घ्यम्
पादः + -अर्घ्यम् a gift to a Brāhmāṇa or a venerable person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्धम्
पादः + -अर्धम्<BR>—1 half a quarter, an eighth; पादं पशुश्च योषिच्च पादार्धं रिक्तकः<BR> पुमान् Ms. 8. 404.<BR>—2 half a line of a stanza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्दी
पादः + -अलिन्दी a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावनामः|पादावनाम
पादः + -अवनामः bowing to a personʼs feet; इति कृतवचनायाः कश्चिदभ्येत्य<BR> बिभ्यद्गलितनयनवारेर्याति पादावनामम् Śi. 11. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावनेजः|पादावनेज
पादः + -अवनेजः washing anotherʼs feet; विभ्व्यस्तवामृतकथोदवहास्त्रिलोक्याः<BR> पादावनेजसरितः शमलानि हन्तुम् Bhāg. 11. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावसेचनम्
पादः + -अवसेचनम्<BR>—1 washing the feet.<BR>—2 the water used for washing the feet; दूरात् पादावसेचनम् Ms. 4. 151.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">Page1007-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाष्ठीलः|पादाष्ठील
पादः + -अष्ठीलः the ankle; मर्मस्वभ्यवधीत् क्रुद्धः पादाष्ठालैः सुदारुणैः Mb. 10. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाघातः|पादाघात
पादः + -आघातः a kick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादानत
पादः + -आनत <i>a.</i> prostrate, fallen at the feet of; कयासि कामिन्<BR> सुरतापराधात् पादानतः कोपनयावधूतः Ku. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावर्तः|पादावर्त|पादावर्त्त|पादावर्त्तः
पादः + -आवर्तः<BR>—1 a wheel worked by the feet for raising up water from a well.<BR>—2 a square foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादासनम्
पादः + -आसनम् a foot-stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादास्फालनम्
पादः + -आस्फालनम् trampling or motion of the feet, floundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाहत
पादः + -आहत^1 <i>a.</i> kicked.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाहति
पादः + -आहति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 treading or trampling.<BR>—2 a kick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादोदकम्
पादः + -उदकम्, -जलम्<BR>—1 water for washing the feet.<BR>—2 water in which the feet of sacred and revered persons are washed, and<BR> which is thus considered holy; विष्णुपादोदकं तीर्थं जठरे धारयाम्यहम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादजलम्
पादः + -उदकम्, -जलम्<BR>—1 water for washing the feet.<BR>—2 water in which the feet of sacred and revered persons are washed, and<BR> which is thus considered holy; विष्णुपादोदकं तीर्थं जठरे धारयाम्यहम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादोदरः|पादोदर
पादः + -उदरः a serpent; यथा पादोदरस्त्वचा विनिर्मुच्यते Praśna. Up. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादोद्धूतम्
पादः + -उद्धूतम् stamping the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकटकः|पादकटक
पादः + -कटकः, -कम्, -कीलिका an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकम्
पादः + -कटकः, -कम्, -कीलिका an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकीलिका
पादः + -कटकः, -कम्, -कीलिका an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकृच्छ्रम्
पादः + -कृच्छ्रम् a vow in which taking of meals and observing a fast are<BR> done on alternate days; Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादक्षेपः|पादक्षेप
पादः + -क्षेपः<BR>—1 a footstep.<BR>—2 a kick with the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादगण्डीरः|पादगण्डीर
पादः + -गण्डीरः a morbid swelling of the legs and feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादग्रन्थिः|पादग्रन्थि|पादग्रंथि
पादः + -ग्रन्थिः the ankle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादग्रहणम्
पादः + -ग्रहणम् seizing or clasping the feet (as a mark of respectful<BR> salutation); अकारयत् कारयितव्यदक्षा क्रमेण पादग्रहणं सतीनाम् Ku. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचतुरः|पादचतुर
पादः + -चतुरः, -चत्वरः<BR>—1 a slanderer.<BR>—2 a goat.<BR>—3 the fig-tree.<BR>—4 a sand-bank.<BR>—5 hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचत्वरः|पादचत्वर
पादः + -चतुरः, -चत्वरः<BR>—1 a slanderer.<BR>—2 a goat.<BR>—3 the fig-tree.<BR>—4 a sand-bank.<BR>—5 hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचापल्यम्
पादः + -चापल्यम् shuffling of the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचारः|पादचार
पादः + -चारः<BR>—1 going on foot, walking; यदि च विहरेत् पादचारेण गौरी Me. 62 ‘if Gaurī should walk on foot’; R. 11. 10.<BR>—2 the daily position of the planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचारिन्
पादः + -चारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 walking or going on foot.<BR>—2 fighting on foot. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a pedestrian.<BR>—2 a foot-soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादच्छेदनम्
पादः + -च्छेदनम् cutting off a foot; पादेन प्रहरन् कोपात् पादच्छेदनमर्हति Ms. 8. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादजः|पादज
पादः + -जः a sūdra; पादजोच्छिष्टकांस्यं यत् … … विशुद्धेद् दशभिस्तु<BR> तत् Mb. 12. 35. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादजलम्
पादः + -जलम्<BR>—1 butter-milk mixed with one-fourth of water. —2 water for the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादजाहम्
पादः + -जाहम् the tarsus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतलम्
पादः + -तलम् the sole of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादत्रः|पादत्र
पादः + -त्रः, -त्रा, -त्राणम् a boot or shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादत्रा
पादः + -त्रः, -त्रा, -त्राणम् a boot or shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादत्राणम्
पादः + -त्रः, -त्रा, -त्राणम् a boot or shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाददारी
पादः + -दारी, -दारिका a chap in the feet, chilblain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाददारिका
पादः + -दारी, -दारिका a chap in the feet, chilblain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाददाहः|पाददाह
पादः + -दाहः a burning sensation in the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादधावनिका
पादः + -धावनिका sand used for rubbing the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादनालिका
पादः + -नालिका an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादनिकेतः|पादनिकेत
पादः + -निकेतः a foot-stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादन्यासः|पादन्यास
पादः + -न्यासः movement of the feet; पादन्यासो लयमनुगतः M. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपः|पादप
पादः + -पः —1 a tree; निरस्तपादपे देशे एरण्डोऽपि द्रुमायते H. 1. 67;<BR> अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णम् Ś. 5. 7.<BR>—2 a foot-stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपा
पादः + -पः + .({@-पा@}) a shoe. ˚खण्डः, -ण्डम् a grove of trees. ˚रुहा a<BR> climbing plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपद्धतिः|पादपद्धति
पादः + -पद्धतिः <i>f.</i> a track.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपरिचारकः|पादपरिचारक
पादः + -परिचारकः a humble servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपालिका
पादः + -पालिका an anklet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपाशः|पादपाश
पादः + -पाशः<BR>—1 a foot-rope for cattle.<BR>—2 an anklet of small bells &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपाशिकः|पादपाशिक
पादः + -पाशः + .({@-शिकः, -शी@})<BR>—1 a fetter; हस्तिपक-पादपाशिक-सैमिक-वनचर-पारिकर्मिकसखः Kau. A.<BR>—2 a mat.<BR>—3 a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपाशी
पादः + -पाशः + .({@-शिकः, -शी@})<BR>—1 a fetter; हस्तिपक-पादपाशिक-सैमिक-वनचर-पारिकर्मिकसखः Kau. A.<BR>—2 a mat.<BR>—3 a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठः|पादपीठ|पादपीठं
पादः + -पीठः, -पीठम् a foot-stool; चूडामाणिभिरुद्घृष्टपादपीठं महीक्षिताम्<BR> R. 17. 28; Ku. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठम्
पादः + -पीठः, -पीठम् a foot-stool; चूडामाणिभिरुद्घृष्टपादपीठं महीक्षिताम्<BR> R. 17. 28; Ku. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठिका
पादः + -पीठिका<BR>—1 a vulgar trade (as that of a barber).<BR>—2 white stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपूरणम्
पादः + -पूरणम्<BR>—1 filling out a line; P. VI. 1. 134.<BR>—2 an expletive; तु पादपूरणे भेदे सभुच्चयेऽवधारणे Viśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रक्षालनम्
पादः + -प्रक्षालनम् washing the feet; पादप्रक्षालने वज्री Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रणामः|पादप्रणाम
पादः + -प्रणामः prostration (at the feet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रतिष्ठानम्
पादः + -प्रतिष्ठानम् a foot-stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रधारणम्
पादः + -प्रधारणम् a shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रसारणम्
पादः + -प्रसारणम् stretching out the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रहारः|पादप्रहार
पादः + -प्रहारः a kick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादबद्ध
पादः + -बद्ध <i>a.</i> consisting of verses (as a metre).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादबन्धनम्
पादः + -बन्धनम्<BR>—1 a chain, fetter.<BR>—2 a stock of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">Page1008-1</a>]<BR> cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1007-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादभटः|पादभट
पादः + -भटः a foot soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादभागः|पादभाग
पादः + -भागः a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमुद्रा
पादः + -मुद्रा a footprint. ˚पङ्क्तिः a track, trail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमूलम्
पादः + -मूलम्<BR>—1 the tarsus.<BR>—2 the sole of the foot.<BR>—3 the heel.<BR>—4 the foot of a mountain.<BR>—5 a polite way of speaking of a person; देवपादमूलमागताहम् K. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादयमकः|पादयमक
पादः + -यमकः paronomasia within the Pādas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरक्षः|पादरक्ष
पादः + -रक्षः<BR>—1 a shoe.<BR>—2 a foot-guard; (pl.) armed men protecting the feet of an elephant in<BR> battle; शिरांसि पादरक्षाणां बीजवत् प्रवपन् मुहुः Mb. 3. 271. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरक्षणम्
पादः + -रक्षणम्<BR>—1 a cover for the feet.<BR>—2 a leather boot or shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरजस्
पादः + -रजस् <i>n.</i> the dust of the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरज्जुः|पादरज्जु
पादः + -रज्जुः <i>f.</i> a tether for the foot of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरथी
पादः + -रथी a shoe, boot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरोहः|पादरोह
पादः + -रोहः, -रोहणः the (Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरोहणः|पादरोहण
पादः + -रोहः, -रोहणः the (Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादलग्न
पादः + -लग्न^1 <i>a.</i> lying at a personʼs feet.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादलेपः|पादलेप
पादः + -लेपः an unguent for the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवन्दनम्
पादः + -वन्दनम् saluting the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवल्मीकः|पादवल्मीक
पादः + -वल्मीकः elephantiasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविरजस्
पादः + -विरजस् <i>f.</i> a shoe, boot. ━(<i>m.</i>) a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवेष्टनिकः|पादवेष्टनिक
पादः + -वेष्टनिकः, -कम् a stocking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकम्
पादः + -वेष्टनिकः, -कम् a stocking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशाखा
पादः + -शाखा a toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशैलः|पादशैल
पादः + -शैलः a hill at the foot of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशोथः|पादशोथ
पादः + -शोथः swelling of the foot; अन्योन्योपद्रवकृतः शोथः पादसमुत्थितः ।<BR> पुरुषं हन्ति नारीं तु मुखजो गुह्यजो ह्ययम् ॥ Mādhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशौचम्
पादः + -शौचम् cleaning the feet by washing, washing the feet; पादशौचेन<BR> गोविन्दः (तृप्तः) Pt. 1. 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादसंहिता
पादः + -संहिता the junction of words in a quarter of a stanza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादसेवनम्
पादः + -सेवनम्, -सेवा<BR>—1 showing respect by touching the feet.<BR>—2 service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादसेवा
पादः + -सेवनम्, -सेवा<BR>—1 showing respect by touching the feet.<BR>—2 service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादस्तम्भः|पादस्तम्भ
पादः + -स्तम्भः a supporting beam, pillar, post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादस्फोटः|पादस्फोट
पादः + -स्फोटः ‘cracking of the feet’, chilblain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहत
पादः + -हत <i>a.</i> kicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहर्षः|पादहर्ष
पादः + -हर्षः numbness of the feet after pressure upon the crural nerves;<BR> हृष्यतः चरणौ यस्य भवतश्च प्रसुप्तवत् । पादहर्षः सः विज्ञेयः<BR> कफवातप्रकोपजः ॥ Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहीनजलम्
पादः + -हीनजलम् Water with a portion boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहीनात्
पादः + -हीनात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 without division or transition.<BR>—2 all at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादयति
पादयति Den. P. To stretch out the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविकः|पादविक
पादविकः A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात्
पादात् <i>m.</i> A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादातः|पादात|पादातं
पादातः A foot-soldier; पादातानां भ्रेजिरे खड्गलेखः Śi. 18. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादातम्
पादातः + .{@-तम्@} Infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादातिः|पादाति
पादातिः, पादातिकः, पादाविकः A foot-soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादातिकः|पादातिक
पादातिः, पादातिकः, पादाविकः A foot-soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाविकः|पादाविक
पादातिः, पादातिकः, पादाविकः A foot-soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिक
पादिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Amounting to a quarter or fourth; पादिकं शतम्, 25 per cent.<BR>—2 Lasting for a quarter of the time; Ms. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन्
पादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Footed, having feet.<BR>—2 Having four parts, as a stanza.<BR>—3 Receiving or entitled to a fourth part; चतुर्थांशाश्च पादिनः Ms. 8. 210.<BR>━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An amphibious animal.<BR>—2 A heir to a fourth part of an estate; ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिनः|पादिन
पादिनः A fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुक|पादुकः
पादुक <i>a.</i> (-का, -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Going on foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुका
पादुक + .{@-का@} A wooden shoe, sandal; व्रज भरत गृहीत्वा पादुके त्वं<BR> मदीये Bk. 3. 56; R. 12. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकम्
पादुक + .{@-कम्@} the plinth, the pedestal, the base.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पादुकाकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकाकारः|पादुकाकार
पादुक + -आकारः a shoemaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादू
पादू <i>f.</i> A shoe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पादूकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादूकृत्
पादू + -कृत् <i>m.</i> a shoe-maker; पादूकृतः पुलिन्दाश्च … … … Śiva B. 31. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्मः|पाद्म
पाद्मः N. of Brahmā; इति तस्य वचः पाद्मो भगवान् परिपालयन्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्य|पाद्यं
पाद्य <i>a.</i> [पादार्थं पाद-यत्] Belonging to the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्यम्
पाद्य + .{@-द्यम्@} Water for washing the feet; पादयोः पाद्यं समर्पयामि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादक्रमिकः|पादक्रमिक
पादक्रमिकः One knowing or reading the पदक्रम q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाकुलकम्
पादाकुलकम् N. of a metre; यदतीतकृतविविधलक्ष्मयुतैर्मात्रासमदिपादैः<BR> कलितम् । अनियतवृत्तपरिमाणसहितं प्रथितं जगत्सु पादाकुलमम् ॥<BR> Vṛttaratnākara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादारकः|पादारक
पादारकः The rib of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्दः|पादालिन्द|पादालिंदः
पादालिन्दः, -न्दा, -न्दी<BR> A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्दा
पादालिन्दः, -न्दा, -न्दी<BR> A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्दी
पादालिन्दः, -न्दा, -न्दी<BR> A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानम्
पानम् [पा-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Drinking, quaffing, kissing (a lip); पयःपानम्; देहि मुखकमलमधुपानम् Gīt. 10.<BR>—2 Drinking spirituous liquors; नहि धर्मार्थसिद्ध्यर्थं पानमेव प्रशस्यते<BR> Rām. 4. 33. 46; Ms. 7. 50, 9. 13; द्यूतपानप्रसक्ताश्च जघन्या राजसी<BR> गतिः 12. 45.<BR>—3 A drink, beverage in general; Ms. 3. 227; पयःपानं भुजङ्गानां केवलं<BR> विषवर्धनम् Pt. 1. 389.<BR>—4 A drinking vessel.<BR>—5 Sharpening; whetting.<BR>—6 Protection, defence.<BR>—7 A canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानः|पान|पानं
पानम् + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A distiller.<BR>—2 Breath, expiration. ━<i>a.</i> (in comp.) Drinking, one who drinks; विश्वं<BR> युगान्ते वटपत्र एकः शेते स्म मायाशिशुरङ्घ्रिपानः Bhāg. 3. 33. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पानागारः, पानागारः, पानागारम्, पानात्ययः, पानगोष्ठिका, पानगोष्ठी, पानप,^1 पानपात्रम्, पानभाजनम्, पानभाण्डम्, पानभूः, पानभूमिः, पानभूमी, पानमण्डलम्, पानरत, पानवणिज्, पानविभ्रमः, पानशौण्डः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानागारः|पानागार
पानम् + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a tavern; Mb. 12. 88. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानागारः|पानागार
पानम् + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a tavern; Mb. 12. 88. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानागारम्
पानम् + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a tavern; Mb. 12. 88. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1008-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

