पापिन्
पापिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sinful, wicked, bad. ━<i>m.</i> A sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिष्ठ
पापिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Most sinful, worst, very wicked (superl. of पाप q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीयस्
पापीयस् <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Worse, more vile or wicked (compar. of पाप q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप्मन्
पाप्मन् <i>a.</i> Hurtful, injurious.<BR>—2 Sinful. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Sin, crime, wickedness, guilt; यदेवेदमप्रतिरूपं वदति स एव<BR> स पाप्मा Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 2. मया गृहीतनामानः स्पृश्यन्त इव पाप्मना<BR> U. 1. 48, 7. 20; Māl. 5. 26; Ms. 6. 85.<BR>—2 Evil, bad fortune or state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1009-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन्
