पार्
पार् €10 P.<BR>—1 To complete, finish.<BR>—2 To cross over.<BR>—3 To be able, competent.<BR>—4 To win; समरं पारयिष्यति Śiva B. 24. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारः|पार|पारं
पारः, -रम्<BR> [परं तीरं परमेव अण्, पॄ-घञ् वा]<BR>—1 The further or opposite bank of a river or ocean: पारं दुःखोदधेर्गन्तुं<BR> तर यावन्न भिद्यते Śānti. 3. 1; विरहजलधेः पारमासादयिष्ये<BR> Pad. D. 13; H. 1. 177.<BR>—2 The further or opposite side of anything; स हि देवः परं ज्योतिस्तमःपारे<BR> व्यवस्थितम् Ku. 2. 58.<BR>—3 The end or extremity of anything; furtherest or concluding limit; तेजस्वी<BR> रिपुहतबन्धुदुःखपारम् (व्रजति) Ve. 3. 25.<BR>—4 The fullest extent, the totality of anything; स पूर्वजन्मान्तरदृष्टपाराः<BR> स्मरन्निव R. 18. 50. (पारं गम्, -इ, -या<BR>—1 to cross over, surmount, get over; व्यसनेष्वेव सर्वेषु यस्य बुद्धिर्न<BR> हीयते । स तेषां पारमभ्येति Pt. 2. 6.<BR>—2 to accomplish, fulfil; as in प्रतिज्ञायाः पारं गतः<BR>—3 To master fully, become proficient in; सकलशास्त्रपारं गतः<BR> Pt. 1; पारं नी ‘to bring to a close’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्
पारः, -रम्<BR> [परं तीरं परमेव अण्, पॄ-घञ् वा]<BR>—1 The further or opposite bank of a river or ocean: पारं दुःखोदधेर्गन्तुं<BR> तर यावन्न भिद्यते Śānti. 3. 1; विरहजलधेः पारमासादयिष्ये<BR> Pad. D. 13; H. 1. 177.<BR>—2 The further or opposite side of anything; स हि देवः परं ज्योतिस्तमःपारे<BR> व्यवस्थितम् Ku. 2. 58.<BR>—3 The end or extremity of anything; furtherest or concluding limit; तेजस्वी<BR> रिपुहतबन्धुदुःखपारम् (व्रजति) Ve. 3. 25.<BR>—4 The fullest extent, the totality of anything; स पूर्वजन्मान्तरदृष्टपाराः<BR> स्मरन्निव R. 18. 50. (पारं गम्, -इ, -या<BR>—1 to cross over, surmount, get over; व्यसनेष्वेव सर्वेषु यस्य बुद्धिर्न<BR> हीयते । स तेषां पारमभ्येति Pt. 2. 6.<BR>—2 to accomplish, fulfil; as in प्रतिज्ञायाः पारं गतः<BR>—3 To master fully, become proficient in; सकलशास्त्रपारं गतः<BR> Pt. 1; पारं नी ‘to bring to a close’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारः|पार|पारं
पारः, -रम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Quick-silver.<BR>—2 Guardian; तस्माद् भयाद् येन स नोऽस्तु पारः Bhāg. 6. 9. 24.<BR>—3 The end; महिम्नः पारं ते Śivamahimna 1. (पारे meaning ‘on the other side of’<BR>, ‘beyond’ sometimes enters into comp.; <i>e. g.</i> पारेगङ्गम्,<BR> पारेसमुद्रम् beyond the Ganges or the ocean; मम लङ्कापुरी नाम्ना<BR> रम्या पारे महोदधेः Mb. 3. 274. 35.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पारापारम्, पारावारम्, पारायणम्, पारायणी, पारकाम, पारग, पारगत, पारगामिन्, पारचर, पारदर्शक, पारदृश्वन्, पारनेतृ, पारसमुद्रकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापारम्
पारः + -अपारम्, -अवारम् both banks, the nearer and further bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापारः|पारापार
पारः + -अपारम्, -अवारम् + .({@-रः@}) the sea, ocean; शोकपारावारमुत्तर्तुमशक्नुवती Dk. 4; Bv. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावारम्
पारः + -अपारम्, -अवारम् both banks, the nearer and further bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायणम्
पारः + -अयणम्<BR>—1 going across.<BR>—2 reading through, perusal, thorough study.<BR>—3 the whole, completeness, or totality of anything; as in ब्रह्मपारायणम्,<BR> मन्त्रपारायणम् &c. याज्ञवल्क्यो मुनिर्यस्मै ब्रह्मपारायणं जगौ Mv. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायणी
पारः + -अयणी<BR>—1 N. of the goddess Sarasvatī.<BR>—2 considering, meditation.<BR>—3 an act, action.<BR>—4 light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारकाम
पारः + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of going to the other end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग|पारगः
पारः + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 crossing over, ferrying across.<BR>—2 one who has gone to the end of, one who has completely mastered anything, completely<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">Page1010-2</a>]<BR> familiar or conversant with (with gen. or in comp.); वेदपारगः Ms. 2. 148;<BR> Y. 1. 111.<BR>—3 profoundly learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगम्
पारः + -ग + .({@-गम्@}) keeping, fulfilling (of a promise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगत|पारगतः
पारः + -गत, -गामिन् <i>a.</i> one who has gone to the other side or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगतः|पारगत
पारः + -गत, -गामिन् + .({@-तः@}) an Arhat or deified saint with Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगामिन्
पारः + -गत, -गामिन् <i>a.</i> one who has gone to the other side or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारचर
पारः + -चर <i>a.</i> emancipated forever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदर्शक
पारः + -दर्शक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 showing the opposite bank.<BR>—2 transparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदृश्वन्
पारः + -दृश्वन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 far-seeing, wise, prudent.<BR>—2 one who has seen the other side of anything, one who has completely<BR> mastered or has become familiar with anything; (cf. P. III. 2. 94); श्रुतिपारदृश्वा R. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारनेतृ
पारः + -नेतृ <i>a.</i> making a person conversant with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसमुद्रकः|पारसमुद्रक
पारः + -समुद्रकः A variety of gems; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक|पारकः
पारक <i>a.</i> (-की)<BR> [पॄ-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Enabling to cross.<BR>—2 Carrying over, saving, delivering.<BR>—3 Pleasing, satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्य|पार्य्य
पार्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Being on the other bank or side.<BR>—2 Last, final.<BR>—3 Upper.<BR>—4 Decisive.<BR>—5 Effectual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्यम्
पार्य + .{@-र्यम्@}<BR>—1 End.<BR>—2 Decision.<BR>—3 The means of crossing over (पारप्रदम्); सहि पार्यं महानासीत् पुत्राणां<BR> मम संजय Mb. 8. 9. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारे
पारे <i>ind.</i> On the other side of; पारेश्मशानं सरित् Māl. 5. 19;<BR> पारेसमुद्रं लङ्कायां वसन्तं रावणं पतिम् Bk. 5. 4; see पार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्य|पारक्यं|पारक्यः
पारक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Alien, belonging to another; वरं स्वधर्मो विगुणो न पारक्यः स्वनुष्ठितः<BR> Ms. 10. 97; पारक्यस्यैव देहस्य बह्वपो मेऽक्षौहिणीर्हताः Bhāg. 1. 8. 48.<BR>—2 Intended for others.<BR>—3 Hostile, inimical.<BR>—4 Useful in the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्यः|पारक्य|पारक्यं
पारक्य + .{@-क्यः@} An enemy, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्यम्
पारक्य + .{@-क्यम्@} Doing anything for future happiness (परलोकसाधन); pious conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग्रामिक
पारग्रामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Alien, hostile, inimical; यावदरिः पारग्रामिकं<BR> विधिमाचिकीर्षति Dk. 2. 2. ˚योगः Measures which are employed to<BR> capture the villages of a foreign king; Kau. A. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारज्
पारज् <i>m.</i> Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारजायिकः|पारजायिक
पारजायिकः An adulterer. See पारदारिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारटीटः|पारटीट
पारटीटः, -नः<BR> A stone or rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारटीनः|पारटीन
पारटीटः, -नः<BR> A stone or rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
पारण <i>a.</i> [पॄ भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Carrying across, bringing over.<BR>—2 Saving, delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणः|पारण|पारणं
पारण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A cloud.<BR>—2 Satisfaction<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणम्
पारण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Accomplishing, fulfilling; व्यवसितपारणमाशशंसिरेऽस्मै Bu. C. 5. 85;<BR> व्याघ्रस्य चोपवासेन पारणं पशुमारणम् Udb.<BR>—2 Reading through, perusal.<BR>—3 Eating after a fast, concluding a fast.<BR>—4 The complete text of a book.<BR>—5 Swallowing; स्वर्भानुप्रतिवारपारणमिलद्दन्तौघ … … द्युतिः N. 22. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणा
पारण + .{@-णा@}<BR>—1 Eating after a fast, concluding a fast; कारय चक्षुषी पारणाम्<BR> Vb. 1; R. 2. 39, 55, 70.<BR>—2 Eating (in general); बभूव तस्याः किल पारणाविधिः Ku. 5. 22 (अभ्यवहारकर्म Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणीय
पारणीय <i>a.</i> Capable of being completed or finished; प्रायोऽधुना<BR> तेऽसुरयूथनाथा अपारणीया इति देवि मे मतिः Bhāg. 8. 17. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1010-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
पारय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Adequate, fit for, appropriate.<BR>—2 Satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयति
पारयति, -ते Den. U.<BR>—1 To be able.<BR>—2 To bring or fead over; see पॄ <i>caus.</i> also; cf. वक्तुं<BR> न पार्यत इति व्यथते मनो मे Bil. C. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयते
पारयति, -ते Den. U.<BR>—1 To be able.<BR>—2 To bring or fead over; see पॄ <i>caus.</i> also; cf. वक्तुं<BR> न पार्यत इति व्यथते मनो मे Bil. C. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतः|पारत
पारतः Quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्रिक|पारतंत्रिक
पारतन्त्रिक <i>a.</i> Enjoined by the religious treatises of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्र्यम्
पारतन्त्र्यम् Dependence, subjection, subservience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्रिक|पारत्रिकं
पारत्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to the next world.<BR>—2 Useful in the future life; तद् वै पारत्रिकं तात ब्राह्मणानामकुप्यताम्<BR> Mb. 12. 151. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्र्य|पारत्र्यं
पारत्र्य <i>a.</i> Useful in the future life (परलोकहित); निधिं<BR> निदध्यात् पारत्र्यं यात्रार्थं दानशब्दितम् Mb. 13. 162. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्र्यम्
पारत्र्य + .{@-त्र्यम्@} Reward in a future life (परलोकफल); तेषामनुपरोधेन<BR> पारत्र्यं यद् यदाचरेत् Ms. 2. 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतल्पिकम्
पारतल्पिकम् Adultery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदः|पारद
पारदः Quick-silver; पारदः पारतः सूतो हरबीजं रसश्चलः<BR> Abh. Cin. 1050; निदर्शनं पारदोऽत्र रसः Bv. 1. 82; पारदं<BR> हरितालं च Śiva B. 30. 19; संसारस्य परं पारं दत्तेऽसौ पारदः<BR> स्मृतः Raseśvaradarśanam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदाः
पारदः + .{@-दाः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) N. of a barbarous tribe; see Ms. 10. 44; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिकः|पारदारिक
पारदारिकः An adulterer (intriguing with the wife of another); Y. 2. 295;<BR> पारदारिकविलाससाहसम् N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदार्यम्
पारदार्यम् Adultery, intriguing with anotherʼs wife; Ms. 11. 59;<BR> Y. 3. 235; Dk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेशिक|पारदेशिकः
पारदेशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Foreign, out-landish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेशिकः|पारदेशिक
पारदेशिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A foreigner.<BR>—2 A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्य|पारदेश्यः
पारदेश्य <i>a.</i> (-श्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to a foreign country, foreign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्यः|पारदेश्य
पारदेश्य + .{@-श्यः@}<BR>—1 A foreigner.<BR>—2 A traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारधेनुः|पारधेनु
पारधेनुः, -नुकः<BR> N. of a low mixed caste; an Āyogava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारधेनुकः|पारधेनुक
पारधेनुः, -नुकः<BR> N. of a low mixed caste; an Āyogava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृतम्
पारभृतम् A present (perhaps a misreading for प्राभृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्य|पारमहंस्यं
पारमहंस्य <i>a.</i> Relating to a ‘Paramahaṃsa’ or a religious man<BR> who has subdued all his senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्यम्
पारमहंस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} Most sublime asceticism or meditation; साङ्ख्यायनः पारमहंस्यमुख्यः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 8; न वै तथा चेतनया बहिष्कृते हुताशने पारमहंस्य<BR> पर्यगुः Bhāg. 4. 21. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पारमहंस्यपरि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्यपरि
पारमहंस्य + -परि <i>ind.</i> relating to such asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमार्थिक|पारमार्थिकः
पारमार्थिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [परमाथीय हितं ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to परमार्थ or the highest truth or spiritual knowledge.<BR>—2 Real, essential, truly or really existent; सत्ता त्रिविधा पारमार्थिकी,<BR> व्यावहारिकी, प्रातीतिकी च Vedānta.<BR>—3 Caring for truth, loving truth or right; न लोकः पारमार्थिकः Pt. 1. 342.<BR>—4 Excellent, supremely good, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमिक
पारमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Supreme, best, chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमित
पारमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Gone to the opposite bank or side.<BR>—2 Crossed, traversed.<BR>—3 Transcendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमिता
पारमित + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 Complete attainment, perfection. Ks. Taraṅga 72. 362 illustrates<BR> six Pāramitas दान, शील, क्षमा, धैर्य, ध्यान and प्रज्ञा by suitable<BR> stories; Bṛ. Kath. 9. 1. 496; cf. दानपारमिता ‘perfection in charity’<BR> दानपारमितयैव वदान्यान् N. 5. 11; नूनमेवं बुद्धेनापि दानपारमिता<BR> पूरिता (मत्तविलास प्रहसन).<BR>—2 Transcendental virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेश्वर
पारमेश्वर <i>a.</i> Relating, belonging or coming from the supreme god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेष्ठ्यम्
पारमेष्ठ्यम्<BR>—1 Supremacy, highest position; Deve Mantra.<BR>—2 Royal insignia; पारमेष्ठपानुपादाय पण्यान्युच्चावचानि च । पादयोर्न्यपतत्<BR> प्रेम्णा प्रक्लिन्नहृदयेक्षणः ॥ Bhāg. 9. 10. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपर
पारंपर <i>a.</i> Further, future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपरी|पारम्परी
पारंपर + .{@-री@} Regular succession, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपरिण
पारंपरि(री)ण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [परंपरायाः आगतः खञ्] Handed down from father<BR> to son, hereditary, ancestral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपरीण|पारम्परीण
पारंपरि(री)ण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [परंपरायाः आगतः खञ्] Handed down from father<BR> to son, hereditary, ancestral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपरीय|पारम्परीय
पारंपरीय <i>a.</i> Handed down, traditional, hereditary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपर्यम्
पारंपर्यम् [परंपरैव स्वार्थे ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Hereditary succession, continuous order; तस्मिन् देशे य आचारः पारंपर्यकमागतः ।<BR> वर्णानां सान्तरालानां स सदाचार उच्यते Ms. 2. 18.<BR>—2 Traditional instruction, tradition.<BR>—3 Intermediation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपर्येण|पारम्पर्येण
पारंपर्यम् + .{@-पारंपर्येण@} <i>ind.</i> Successively, by degrees; निवृत्तेषु<BR> च सैन्येषु पारंपर्येण सर्वशः । निमुर्क्तकवचाः सर्वे भीष्ममीयुर्नराधिपाः ॥<BR> Mb. 6. 120. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पारंपर्योपदेशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारंपर्योपदेशः|पारम्पर्योपदेश|पारंपर्योपदेश|पारम्पर्य्योपदेश|पारम्पर्य्योपदेशः
पारंपर्यम् + -उपदेशः traditional instruction, tradition, regarded by the<BR> Paurāṇikas as a प्रमाण or proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
पारयिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>—2 Able to go to the end of or accomplish anything.<BR>—3 Successful, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलोक्य
पारलोक्य <i>a.</i> Relating to the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिक
पारलौकिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [परलोकाय हितं ठक् द्विपदवृद्धिः] Relating<BR> to or useful in the next world; धर्म एको मनुष्याणां सहायः पारलौकिकः<BR> Mb.; Mk. 1; साधुरेति सुकृतैर्यदि कर्तुं पारलौकिककुसीदमसीदत् N. 5. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिकम्
पारलौकिक + .{@-कम्@} Obsequies, funeral rites; इच्छामि … … पर्वतेश्वरस्य<BR> पारलौकिकं कर्तुम् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवतः|पारवत
पारवतः A pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवर्ग्य
पारवर्ग्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to another party, inimical; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवश्यम्
पारवश्यम् Dependence, subjection, subservience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारश(स)व <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Made of iron.<BR>—2 Relating to or derived from an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसव
पारश(स)व <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Made of iron.<BR>—2 Relating to or derived from an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशवः|पारशव
पारश(स)व + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Iron.<BR>—2 The son of a Brāhmaṇa by a Śūdra woman; यं ब्राह्मणस्तु शूद्रायां<BR> कामादुत्पादयेत् सुतम् । स पारयन्नेव शवस्तस्मात् पारशवः स्मृतः Ms. 9. 178;<BR> or परं शवात् ब्राह्मणस्यैष पुत्रः शूद्रापुत्रं पारशवं तमाहुः Mb.<BR>—3 An adulterine, a bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशवी
पारश(स)व + .{@-वी@} A daughter of a Brāhmaṇa by a Śūdra woman; भीष्मः पारशवीं<BR> कन्यां देवकस्य महीपतेः । विदुराय समानीय ददौ वंशविवृद्धये ॥ Bm. 1. 519.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1011-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधः|पारश्वध
पारश्वधः, पारश्वधिकः A man armed with an axe, halbert-man;<BR> cf. P. IV. 4. 58.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पारश्वधिकरामः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधिकः|पारश्वधिक
पारश्वधः, पारश्वधिकः A man armed with an axe, halbert-man;<BR> cf. P. IV. 4. 58.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पारश्वधिकरामः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधिकरामः
पारश्वधः + पारश्वधिकरामः<BR> (= परशुरामः); पारश्वधिकरामस्य शक्तेरन्तकरो<BR> रणे Bk. 5. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारषदम्
पारषदम् membership (सभापतित्व); सारथ्यपारषदसेवनसख्यदौत्यवीरासनानुगमनस्तवनप्रणामम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 16. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस
पारस (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Persian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिकः|पारसिक
पारसिकः<BR>—1 Persia.<BR>—2 = पारसीक 2 q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसी
पारसी The Persian language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीकः|पारसीक
पारसीकः<BR>—1 Persia.<BR>—2 Persian horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीकाः
पारसीकः + .{@-काः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) The Persians; पारसीकांस्ततो जेतुं प्रतस्थे<BR> स्थलवर्त्मना R. 4. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसव
पारसव See पारशव; पारसवत्त्वाद्विदुरः (राज्यं न प्रत्यपद्यत)<BR> Mb. 1. 109. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्करः|पारस्कर
पारस्करः<BR>—1 N. of a certain district.<BR>—2 N. of a sage, the author of the Gṛhya Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेयः|पारस्त्रैणेय
पारस्त्रैणेयः An adulterine, a bastard (born from anotherʼs wife, परस्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्यकुलीन
पारस्यकुलीन <i>a.</i> Born in the family of another (as an adopted son).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारहंस्य
पारहंस्य <i>a.</i> Relating to an ascetic who has subdued all his senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1012-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारा
