पारिप्लाव्यः A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लाव्यम्
पारिप्लाव्यः + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 Perplexity, uneasiness, agitation.<BR>—2 Tremour, tremulousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिबर्हः|पारिबर्ह
पारिबर्हः<BR>—1 A wedding present; शतरूपा महाराज्ञी पारिबर्हान् महाधनान् । दम्पत्योः<BR> पर्यदात् प्रीत्या भूषावासः परिच्छदान् ॥ Bhāg. 3. 22. 23.<BR>—2 Retinue; Mb. 3. 140. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभद्रः|पारिभद्र
पारिभद्रः<BR>—1 The coral tree.<BR>—2 The <i>Devadāru</i> tree; Mb. 1. 125. 3.<BR>—3 The <i>Saralā</i> tree.<BR>—4 The <i>Nimba</i> tree.<BR>—5 The <i>Mandāra</i> tree; also पारिभद्रक; Rām. 4. 1. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाव्यम्
पारिभाव्यम्<BR>—1 Bail, security, surety.<BR>—2 A kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाषिक|पारिभाषिकं
पारिभाषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Current, common, universally received; उभयावृत्तिधर्मेण संज्ञा स्यात्<BR> पारिभाषिकी Nyāya-śāstra.<BR>—2 Technical (as a word &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्डल्यम्
पारिमाण्डल्यम्<BR>—1 An atom, a mote in a sun-beam; the measure of an atom; Bhāṣa P. 14.<BR>—2 Spherical shape, globularness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्यम्
पारिमाण्यम् Circumference, compass; प्रजाविसर्गस्य च पारिमाण्यं<BR> वापीसहस्राणि बहूनि दैत्य Mb. 12. 280. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमित्यम्
पारिमित्यम् Limit, limited extent or number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुखिक|पारिमुखिकः
पारिमुखिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Being before the face, being near or present; P. IV. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुख्यम्
पारिमुख्यम् Presence; P. IV. 3. 58; Vārt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्रः|पारियात्र
पारिया(पा)त्रः N. of one of the seven principal mountain ranges;<BR> उच्चैः शिरस्त्वाज्जितपारियात्रं लक्ष्मीः सिषेवे किल पारियात्रम् R. 18. 16;<BR> see कुलाचल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रः|पारिपात्र|पारिपात्रं
पारिया(पा)त्रः N. of one of the seven principal mountain ranges;<BR> उच्चैः शिरस्त्वाज्जितपारियात्रं लक्ष्मीः सिषेवे किल पारियात्रम् R. 18. 16;<BR> see कुलाचल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्रिकः|पारियात्रिक
पारिया(पा)त्रिकः<BR>—1 An inhabitant of the Pāriyātra mountain.<BR>—2 The Pāriyātra mountain itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रिकः|पारिपात्रिक
पारिया(पा)त्रिकः<BR>—1 An inhabitant of the Pāriyātra mountain.<BR>—2 The Pāriyātra mountain itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियानिकः|पारियानिक
पारियानिकः A travelling carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिरक्षकः|पारिरक्षक
पारिरक्षकः A religious mendicant, an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवित्त्यम्
पारिवित्त्यम्, -पारिवेत्र्यम्<BR> Being unmarried while a younger brother is married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवेत्र्यम्
पारिवित्त्यम्, -पारिवेत्र्यम्<BR> Being unmarried while a younger brother is married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिव्राजकम्
पारिव्राजकम्, -पारिव्राज्यम्<BR> The wandering life of a religious mendicant, asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिव्राज्यम्
पारिव्राजकम्, -पारिव्राज्यम्<BR> The wandering life of a religious mendicant, asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशीलः|पारिशील
पारिशीलः A cake (अपूप q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशेष्यम्
पारिशेष्यम् That which is left over, remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशेष्यात्
पारिशेष्यम् + .{@-ष्यात्@} <i>ind.</i> Consequently, ergo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद|पारिषदः
पारिषद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to an assembly or council.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषदः|पारिषद
पारिषद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 A person present at an assembly, a member of an assembly, such as an assessor.<BR>—2 A kingʼs companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषदाः
पारिषद + .{@-दाः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) The retinue of a god; तिथिष्विव महादेवो वृतः<BR> पारिषदां गणैः Rām. 3. 25. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषदम्
पारिषद + .{@-दम्@} Taking part in an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद्यः|पारिषद्य
पारिषद्यः One present at an assembly, a spectator; cf. P. IV. 4. 44, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिसीर्य|पारिसीर्य्य
पारिसीर्य <i>a.</i> That which is prepared without the help of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहारिक|पारिहारिकः
पारिहारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Taking, seizing.<BR>—2 Surrounding.<BR>—3 Privileged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहारिकः|पारिहारिक
पारिहारिक + .{@-कः@} A maker of garlands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहारिकी
पारिहारिक + .{@-की@} A kind of enigma or riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहार्यः|पारिहार्य|पारिहार्य्य|पारिहार्य्यः
पारिहार्यः A bracelet (आवापकः पारिहार्यः कटको वलयो ऽस्त्रियाम्<BR> Ak.); Mb. 5. 162. 16; भुजपाशैस्तपनीयपारिहार्यैः Bu. C. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहार्यम्
पारिहार्यः + .{@-र्यम्@} Taking, seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहास्यम्
पारिहास्यम् Jest, joke, fun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारी
पारी<BR>—1 A rope for tying an elephantʼs feet.<BR>—2 A quantity of water.<BR>—3 A drinking vessel, waterjar, cup.<BR>—4 A milk-pail; निगृह्य पारीमुभयेन जानुनोः Śi. 12. 40.<BR>—5 Pollen (of flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीक्षितः|पारीक्षित
पारीक्षितः = परीक्षित् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीण|पारीणः
पारीण <i>a.</i> [पारं गच्छति, पार-खञ्]<BR>—1 Being on or going over to the other or opposite side.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Thoroughly versed in, well acquainted with; त्रिवर्गपारीणमसौ<BR> भवन्तमध्यासयन्नासनमेकमिन्द्रः Bk. 2. 46.<BR>—3 Fulfilling, completing, accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीय
पारीय <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Completely versed in or conversant with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीणह्यम्
पारीणह्यम् Household furniture or utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीन्द्रः|पारीन्द्र|पारींद्र|पारींद्रः
पारीन्द्रः<BR>—1 A lion.<BR>—2 A large serpent, boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीरणः|पारीरण
पारीरणः<BR>—1 A tortoise.<BR>—2 A stick, staff.<BR>—3 A garment (पट्टशाटक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुः|पारु
पारुः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 A Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुषिक
पारुषिक <i>a.</i> Harsh, violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्यम्
पारुष्यम् [परुषस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Roughness, ruggedness, hardness.<BR>—2 Harshness, cruelty, unkindness (as of disposition).<BR>—3 Abusive language, abuse, reproach, scurrilous language, insult; Bg. 16. 4;<BR> Y. 2. 12, 72; हिंसा तदभिमानेन दण्ड्यपारुष्ययोर्यथा । वैषम्यमिह<BR> भूतानां ममाहमिति पार्थिव ॥ Bhāg. 7. 1. 23.<BR>—4 Violence (in word or deed); Ms. 7. 48, 51, 8. 6, 72.<BR>—5 The garden of Indra.<BR>—6 Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्यः|पारुष्य|पारुष्यं
पारुष्यम् + .{@-ष्यः@} An epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1013-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेरकः|पारेरक
पारेरकः A sword (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेवतः|पारेवत
पारेवतः A kind of date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारोक्ष
पारोक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Unintelligible, mysterious, secret, obscure; also<BR> पारोक्ष्य; त्वं नूनमसुराणां नः पारोक्ष्यः परमो गुरुः Bhāg. 8. 22. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारोक्ष्यम्
पारोक्ष्यम् Mystery, secrecy; भरतोपाख्याने पारोक्ष्यवर्णनम् Bhāg. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारोवर्यम्
पारोवर्यम् Tradition; Nir. 13. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्घटम्
पार्घटम् Dust or ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्जन्य
पार्जन्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ण|पार्णः
पार्ण <i>a.</i> (-र्णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to or made of leaves, leafy.<BR>—2 Raised from leaves (as a tax).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्णः|पार्ण
पार्ण + .{@-र्णः@} A hut made of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थः|पार्थ
पार्थः [पृथायाः अपत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 A metronymic of all Pāṇḍavas; सर्वेषामेव पार्थानां फाल्गुनो बलवत्तरः<BR> Mb. 7. 158. 8; but especially of Arjuna; उवाच पार्थ पश्यैतान् समवेतान्<BR> कुरूनिति Bg. 1. 25 and several other places.<BR>—2 A king.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पार्थसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थसारथिः|पार्थसारथि
पार्थः + -सारथिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—2 N. of a famous writer on Mīmāṃsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थक्यम्
पार्थक्यम् Severalty, separateness, separation, singleness, variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थव|पार्थवं
पार्थव <i>a.</i> Belonging to पृथु; अस्मिन् कृतमतिर्मर्त्यः पार्थवीं<BR> गतिमाप्नुयात् Bhāg. 4. 23. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थवम्
पार्थवम् Greatness, immensity, width.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिव|पार्थिवं|पार्थिवः
पार्थिव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पृथिव्याः ईश्वरः इदं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Earthen, earthy, terrestrial, relating to the earth; यतो रजः पार्थिवमुज्जिहीते R. 13. 64.<BR>—2 Ruling the earth.<BR>—3 Princely, royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवः|पार्थिव|पार्थिवं
पार्थिव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 An inhabitant of the earth.<BR>—2 A king, sovereign; अथ तस्य विवाहकौतुकं ललितं बिभ्रत एव पार्थिवः R. 8. 1.<BR>—3 An earthen vessel.<BR>—4 The body.<BR>—5 The विकार of the earth; अयं जनो नाम चलन् पृथिव्यां यः पार्थिवः<BR> पार्थिव कस्य हेतोः Bhāg. 5. 12. 5.<BR>—6 A गृह्याग्नि of the naming ceremony (नामकरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवम्
पार्थिव + .{@-वम्@} An earthy substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवा
पार्थिव + .{@-वा@}<BR>—1 A royal concubine.<BR>—2 Arsenic (see निघण्टरत्नाकर).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पार्थिवनन्दिनी, पार्थिवसुता, पार्थिवकन्या, पार्थिवात्मजः, पार्थिवनन्दनः, पार्थिवसुतः, पार्थिवपुत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवनन्दिनी|पार्थिवनंदिनी
पार्थिव + -नन्दिनी, -सुता, -कन्या the daughter of a king, princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवसुता
पार्थिव + -नन्दिनी, -सुता, -कन्या the daughter of a king, princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवकन्या
पार्थिव + -नन्दिनी, -सुता, -कन्या the daughter of a king, princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवात्मजः
पार्थिव + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -पुत्रः the sun. ˚पौत्रः ‘Yamaʼs son’<BR>, Yudhiṣṭhira; स वृत्तवांस्तेषु कृताभिषेकः सहानुजः पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रः Mb. 3. 118. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवनन्दनः|पार्थिवनन्दन
पार्थिव + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -पुत्रः the sun. ˚पौत्रः ‘Yamaʼs son’<BR>, Yudhiṣṭhira; स वृत्तवांस्तेषु कृताभिषेकः सहानुजः पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रः Mb. 3. 118. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवसुतः|पार्थिवसुत
पार्थिव + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -पुत्रः the sun. ˚पौत्रः ‘Yamaʼs son’<BR>, Yudhiṣṭhira; स वृत्तवांस्तेषु कृताभिषेकः सहानुजः पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रः Mb. 3. 118. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवपुत्रः
पार्थिव + -आत्मजः, -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -पुत्रः the sun. ˚पौत्रः ‘Yamaʼs son’<BR>, Yudhiṣṭhira; स वृत्तवांस्तेषु कृताभिषेकः सहानुजः पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रः Mb. 3. 118. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवी
पार्थिवी —1 An epithet of Sītā, daughter of the earth; पार्थिवीमुदवहद् रघूद्वहः R. 11. 54.<BR>—2 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्परः|पार्पर
पार्परः<BR>—1 A handful of rice.<BR>—2 Consumption (क्षयरोग).<BR>—3 Ashes.<BR>—4 A filament of Kadamba.<BR>—5 N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्यन्तिक|पार्यंतिक|पार्य्यन्तिक
पार्यन्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Final, last, conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्यवसानिक
पार्यवसानिक <i>a.</i> Coming to a close; द्वापरस्य कलेश्चैव सन्धौ<BR> पार्यवसानिके Mb. 12. 339. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वण|पार्व्वण|पार्व्वणः
पार्वण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पर्वणि भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging or relating to a <i>Parvan</i>, falling on a Parva day, such<BR> as the full-moon, new-moon &c.; पश्यति स्म जनता दिनात्यये पार्वणौ<BR> शशिदिवाकराविव R. 11. 82; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>—2 Waxing, increasing (as the moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वणम्
पार्वण + .{@-णम्@} The ceremony of offering oblations to all the manes at a<BR> <i>Parvan</i>; अमावास्यां यत् क्रियते तत् पार्वणमुदाहृतम् । क्रियते वा पर्वणि<BR> यत् तत् पार्वणमिति स्मृतिः ॥ B. P.; also पार्वणश्राद्धम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वत|पार्व्वत|पार्व्वतः
पार्वत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पर्वते भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Being or living on a mountain.<BR>—2 Growing on or coming from a mountain. —3 Mountainous; प्रतिश्रयार्थं<BR> सेवेत पार्वतीं वा पुनर्गुहाम् Mb. 14. 46. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतिकम्
पार्वतिकम् A multitude of mountains, a mountain-range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वती|पार्व्वती
पार्वती [पर्वतस्यापत्यं स्त्री अण्]<BR>—1 N. of Durgā, born as the daughter of the Himālaya mountain (she was<BR> Satī in her former birth; cf Ku. 1. 21); तां पार्वतीत्याभिजनेन नाम्ना<BR> बन्धुप्रियां बन्धुजनो जुहाव Ku. 1. 26.<BR>—2 A female cowherd.<BR>—3 An epithet of Draupadī.<BR>—4 A mountain stream.<BR>—5 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पार्वतीनन्दनः, पार्वतीनेत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीनन्दनः|पार्वतीनन्दन|पार्वतीनंदन|पार्व्वतीनन्दन|पार्व्वतीनन्दनः
पार्वती + -नन्दनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीनेत्रः|पार्वतीनेत्र
पार्वती + -नेत्रः (In music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीय|पार्वतीयः|पार्व्वतीय
पार्वतीय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Dwelling in a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीयः|पार्वतीय|पार्व्वतीय
पार्वतीय + .{@-यः@} A mountaineer.<BR>—2 N. of a particular mountain tribe (pl.); तत्र जन्यं रघोर्घोरं<BR> पार्वतीयैर्गणैरभूत् R. 4. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतेय|पार्व्वतेय|पार्व्वतेयं|पार्व्वतेयः
पार्वतेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पर्वते भवं ढक्] Mountain-born; Rām. 4. 39. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतेयम्
पार्वतेय + .{@-यम्@} Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वायनान्तिया
पार्वायनान्तिया <i>f.</i> N. of an Iṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शवः|पार्शव
पार्शवः A warrior armed with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शुका
पार्शुका A rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व <i>a.</i> Near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वः|पार्श्व|पार्श्वं
पार्श्व + .{@-र्श्वः, -र्श्वम्@} [पर्शूनां समूहः]<BR>—1 The part of the body below the arm-pit, the region of the ribs; वामं<BR> पार्श्वं विनिर्भिद्य सुतः सूर्य इव स्थितः Mb. 3. 126. 27; शयने सन्निषण्णैकपार्श्वाम् Me. 91.<BR>—2 The side, flank (in general) (of animate or inanimate objects), पिठरं<BR> क्वथदतिमात्रं निजपार्श्वानेव दहतितराम् Pt. 1. 324.<BR>—3 Vicinity.<BR>—4 Ved. A curved knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वम्
पार्श्व + .{@-र्श्वः, -र्श्वम्@} [पर्शूनां समूहः]<BR>—1 The part of the body below the arm-pit, the region of the ribs; वामं<BR> पार्श्वं विनिर्भिद्य सुतः सूर्य इव स्थितः Mb. 3. 126. 27; शयने सन्निषण्णैकपार्श्वाम् Me. 91.<BR>—2 The side, flank (in general) (of animate or inanimate objects), पिठरं<BR> क्वथदतिमात्रं निजपार्श्वानेव दहतितराम् Pt. 1. 324.<BR>—3 Vicinity.<BR>—4 Ved. A curved knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वः|पार्श्व|पार्श्वं
पार्श्व + .{@-र्श्वः@} An epithet of the twenty-third Tīrthaṅkar of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वम्
पार्श्व + .{@-र्श्वम्@}<BR>—1 A multitude of ribs.<BR>—2 A fraudulent expedient, a dishonourable means.<BR>—3 The extremity of the fore-axle of a wheel. (पार्श्वम् is used adverbially<BR> in the sense of ‘near to’, ‘by the side of’, ‘towards’; केनाप्युत्क्षिपतेव<BR> पश्य भुवनं मत्पार्श्वमानीयते Ś. 7. 8; so पार्श्वात् ‘from the side of, away, from’<BR>; पार्श्वे ‘near’, ‘at hand’, ‘at the side’; नमे दूरे<BR> किंचित् क्षणमपि न पार्श्वे रथजवात् Ś. 1. 9; Bh. 3. 37.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पार्श्वानुचरः, पार्श्वापवृत्त, पार्श्वास्थिः, पार्श्वायात, पार्श्वार्तिः, पार्श्वासन्न, पार्श्वोदरप्रियः, पार्श्वोपपीडम्, पार्श्वग, पार्श्वगम, पार्श्वचर, पार्श्वस्थित, पार्श्वगः, पार्श्वगत,^1 पार्श्वचरः, पार्श्वदः, पार्श्वदेशः, पार्श्वनाथः, पार्श्वपरिवर्तनम्, पार्श्वभागः, पार्श्वमण्डलिन्, पार्श्वमानी, पार्श्ववक्त्रः, पार्श्ववर्तिन्, पार्श्वशय, पार्श्वशूलः, पार्श्वलम्, पार्श्वसूत्रकः, पार्श्वस्थ<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वानुचरः|पार्श्वानुचर
पार्श्व + -अनुचरः an attendant, a servant; विसृष्टपार्श्वानुचरस्य तस्य R. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वापवृत्त
पार्श्व + -अपवृत्त <i>a.</i> bent on one side (one of the defects of diamonds);<BR> Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वास्थिः|पार्श्वास्थि
पार्श्व + -अस्थिः <i>n.</i> a rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वायात
पार्श्व + -आयात <i>a.</i> one who has come very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वार्तिः|पार्श्वार्ति
पार्श्व + -आर्तिः <i>f.</i> pain in the side, pleurisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वासन्न
पार्श्व + -आसन्न <i>a.</i> sitting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">Page1015-1</a>]<BR> or standing by the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1014-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वोदरप्रियः|पार्श्वोदरप्रिय
पार्श्व + -उदरप्रियः a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वोपपीडम्
पार्श्व + -उपपीडम् <i>ind.</i> (to laugh) so as to hold oneʼs sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वग|पार्श्वगः
पार्श्व + -ग, -गम, -चर, -स्थित <i>a.</i> being close to, standing by the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वगम
पार्श्व + -ग, -गम, -चर, -स्थित <i>a.</i> being close to, standing by the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वचर|पार्श्वचरः
पार्श्व + -ग, -गम, -चर, -स्थित <i>a.</i> being close to, standing by the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वस्थित
पार्श्व + -ग, -गम, -चर, -स्थित <i>a.</i> being close to, standing by the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वगः|पार्श्वग
पार्श्व + -गः an attendant, a servant; व्यादिदेश गणशोऽथ पार्श्वगान्<BR> कार्मुकाभिहरणाय मैथिलः R. 11. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वगत
पार्श्व + -गत^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being at the side, being near or close to, attending upon.<BR>—2 sheltered.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वचरः|पार्श्वचर
पार्श्व + -चरः a servant, an attendant; विपिने पार्श्वचरैरलक्ष्यमाणः<BR> R. 9. 72, 14. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वदः|पार्श्वद
पार्श्व + -दः an attendant, a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वदेशः|पार्श्वदेश
पार्श्व + -देशः the side (of the human body), the ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वनाथः|पार्श्वनाथ
पार्श्व + -नाथः the Jaina pontiff, the 23rd Tīrthaṅkara (Mar. पारसनाथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वपरिवर्तनम्
पार्श्व + -परिवर्तनम्<BR>—1 turning round from one side to the other in a bed.<BR>—2 N. of a festival on the twelfth day of the first half of Bhādrapada<BR> (when Viṣṇu is supposed to turn upon the other side in his sleep).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वभागः|पार्श्वभाग
पार्श्व + -भागः the side or flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वमण्डलिन्
पार्श्व + -मण्डलिन् <i>m.</i> N. of a particular posture in dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वमानी
पार्श्व + -मानी the longer side of an oblong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्ववक्त्रः|पार्श्ववक्त्र
पार्श्व + -वक्त्रः an epithet of Mahādeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्ववर्तिन्
पार्श्व + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being by the side, attending, waiting upon.<BR>—2 adjacent. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 an attendant; भूयः स भूतेश्वरपार्श्ववतीं किंचिद् विहस्यार्थपतिं<BR> बभाषे R. 2. 46.<BR>—2 a companion, associate; अमुना ननु पार्श्ववर्तिना Ku. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशय
पार्श्व + -शय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 sleeping on the side.<BR>—2 sleeping by the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशूलः|पार्श्वशूल
पार्श्व + -शूलः, -लम्<BR>—1 a shooting pain in the side.<BR>—2 pleurisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वलम्
पार्श्व + -शूलः, -लम्<BR>—1 a shooting pain in the side.<BR>—2 pleurisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वसूत्रकः|पार्श्वसूत्रक
पार्श्व + -सूत्रकः a kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वस्थ|पार्श्वस्थः
पार्श्व + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being at the side, near, close, proximate; सुरपतिमपि<BR> श्वा पार्श्वस्थं विलोक्य न शङ्कते Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वस्थः|पार्श्वस्थ
पार्श्व + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः@})<BR>—1 a companion.<BR>—2 an assistant of a stage-manager; cf. पारिपार्श्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वकः|पार्श्वक
पार्श्वकः (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> A swindler, pilferer, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतस्
पार्श्वतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Near, at hand, by the side, close to; पार्श्वतः प्रस्थितं तमनवस्थितं<BR> प्रियाः R. 19. 31; प्रायेण भूमिपतयः प्रमदा लताश्च यत् पार्श्वतो<BR> भवति तत् परिवेष्टयन्ति Pt. 1. 35.<BR>—2 (= पश्चात् q. v.); पार्श्वतः करणं प्राज्ञः Mb. 12. 142. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतीय|पार्श्वतीयः
पार्श्वतीय <i>a.</i> Being on or situated at the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं|पार्श्विकः
पार्श्विक^1 <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पार्श्वे भवः ठक्] Belonging to the side.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विकः|पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं
पार्श्विकः + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A sides-man, partisan.<BR>—2 A companion, an associate.<BR>—3 A juggler.<BR>—4 One who seeks money by fraudulent means, a thief.<BR>—5 One who earns money through the instrumentality of oneʼs own kinsmen<BR> after knowing their needs by means of staying by the side (पार्श्व)<BR> of the king; Dānasāgara, Bibliotheca Indica 274, Fasc. 1, p. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षत|पार्षतः
पार्षत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to the spotted antelope; Ms. 3. 269; Y. 1. 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षतः|पार्षत
पार्षत + .{@-तः@} A patronymic of king Drupada, and of his son Dhṛṣṭadyumna;<BR> Mb. 1. 138. 20, 7. 7. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षती
पार्षत + .{@-ती@} A patronymic of Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षती
पार्षती<BR>—1 An epithet of Draupadī; सूतस्येति वचः श्रुत्वा पार्षती दुःखिताऽवदत् Bm. 2. 369.<BR>—2 Of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्
पार्षद् <i>f.</i> An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षदः|पार्षद
पार्षदः [पार्षदमर्हति अण्]<BR>—1 A companion, an associate, attendant.<BR>—2 A train, retinue (of a god); शर्वस्य सह<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">Page1015-2</a>]<BR> पार्षदैः Mb. 3. 130. 14.<BR>—3 One present at an assembly, a spectator, an assessor.<BR>—4 A text-book received by any particular grammatical school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्यः|पार्षद्य
पार्षद्यः A member of an assembly, an assessor; सभ्याः सदस्याः<BR> पार्षद्याः सभास्ताराः सभासदः Abh. Cin. 480.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिः|पार्ष्णि
पार्ष्णिः <i>m. f.</i> [पृष्-नि नि˚ वृद्धिः; Uṇ. 4. 52]<BR>—1 The heel; Bhāg. 7. 8. 31; उद्वेजयत्यङ्गुलिपार्ष्णिभागान् Ku. 1. 11;<BR> पार्ष्णिप्रहार K. 119; प्रतनत्रिकपुच्छमूलपार्ष्णिम् Bu. C. 5. 73.<BR>—2 The rear of an army.<BR>—3 The back or rear in general; शुद्धपार्ष्णिरयान्वितः R. 4. 26 ‘with his rear cleared of foes’<BR>.<BR>—4 A kick.<BR>—5 Desire of conquering.<BR>—6 Inquiry. ━(<i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A licentious woman.<BR>—2 An epithet of Kuntī.<BR>—3 The extremity of the fore-axle of a four-horse chariot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पार्ष्णिग्रहः, पार्ष्णिग्रहणम्, पार्ष्णिग्राहः, पार्ष्णिघातः, पार्ष्णित्रम्, पार्ष्णिवाहः, पार्ष्णिविग्रहः, पार्ष्णिसारथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्रहः|पार्ष्णिग्रह
पार्ष्णिः + -ग्रहः a follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्रहणम्
पार्ष्णिः + -ग्रहणम् attacking or threatening an enemy in the rear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्राहः|पार्ष्णिग्राह
पार्ष्णिः + -ग्राहः<BR>—1 an enemy in the rear; ˚चिन्ता N. of a chapter in Kau. A. (7. 13).<BR> बलिनोऽफजलस्यैते पार्ष्णिग्राहाः प्रमाथिनः Śiva B. 21. 60, 24. 44; also 12. 15.<BR>—2 a general commanding the rear of an army.<BR>—3 an ally who supports a prince; Bhāg. 7. 2. 6; पार्ष्णिग्राहं च संप्रेक्ष्य<BR> तथाक्रन्दं च मण्डले Ms. 7. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिघातः|पार्ष्णिघात
पार्ष्णिः + -घातः a kick; क्षितिं विधुन्वन्निव पार्ष्णिघातैः Ki. 17. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णित्रम्
पार्ष्णिः + -त्रम् a rear-guard, a body of forces in the rear, reserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिवाहः|पार्ष्णिवाह
पार्ष्णिः + -वाहः an outside horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिविग्रहः
पार्ष्णिः + -विग्रहः an attack by an enmy in the rear; मा विधान्मुधा कृतानुतापस्त्वयि<BR> पार्ष्णिविग्रहम् N. 9. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिसारथिः|पार्ष्णिसारथि
पार्ष्णिः + -सारथिः a charioteer who drives one of the outside horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्
पाल् €10 P.<BR>—1 To watch, guard, protect; पितेव पालयेत् पुत्रान् Ms. 9. 108,<BR>—2 To observe (a promise); अद्धा श्रियं पालितसंगराय R. 13. 65.<BR>—3 To wait; Ve. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालः|पाल
पालः<BR>—1 [पाल्-अच्] A protector, guardian, keeper; as in गोपालः, वृष्णिपालः, &c.<BR>—2 A herdsman; विवादः स्वामिपालयोः Ms. 8. 5, 229, 240.<BR>—3 A king; अहो अधर्मः पालानाम् Bhāg. 1. 18. 33.<BR>—4 A spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाली
पालः + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 A herdsmanʼs wife; Mb. 5.<BR>—2 An oblong pond.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पालघ्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालघ्नः|पालघ्न
पालः + -घ्नः a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकः|पालक
पालकः [पाल्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A guardian, protector.<BR>—2 A prince, king, ruler, sovereign.<BR>—3 A groom, horse-keeper.<BR>—4 A horse.<BR>—5 The Chitraka tree.<BR>—6 A foster-father.<BR>—7 Protection.<BR>—8 One who maintains or observes (as a promise &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकम्
पालकः + .{@-कम्@} A spittoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन <i>a.</i> [पाल्-भावे ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Protecting, guarding &c.; Ki. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालनम्
पालन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Protecting, guarding, nourishing, cherishing, fostering; लब्ध˚<BR> R. 19. 3; so प्रजा˚, क्षिति˚, &c.<BR>—2 Maintaining, observing, keeping (as a promise, vow &c.)<BR>—3 The milk of a cow that has recently calved.<BR>—4 the sharpening (of arms); शस्त्राणां पालनं ज्ञानं Mb. 12. 59. 46<BR> (com. शस्त्राणां पालनं तीक्ष्णीकरणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालनीय
पालनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be protected or guarded.<BR>—2 Fit to be protected, preserved or maintained.<BR>—3 To be kept or observed (as a promise, vow &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1015-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्य
पाल्य <i>a.</i> See पालनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्यम्
पाल्य + .{@-ल्यम्@} See पालनम्; उर्ध्वं वर्षसहस्रान्ते प्रजापाल्यमनन्तरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ <i>m.</i> A protector, guardian; शचीसखो मरुतां पालयितेव<BR> नन्दने (विजहार) R. 8. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित|पालितः
पालित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Protected, guarded, preserved.<BR>—2 Observed, fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपालयिषुः
पिपालयिषुः (Desiderative from पाल्) Desirous to protect; प्राज्यं<BR> प्रभावलीराज्यं पिपालयिषुरात्मनः Śiva B. 31. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाप्यः|पालकाप्य
पालकाप्यः N. of a sage, son of Kareṇu (who first taught the science of elephants).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाप्यम्
पालकाप्यः + .{@-प्यम्@} The science of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्कः|पालङ्क|पालंकः
पालङ्कः<BR>—1 The olibanum tree.<BR>—2 A hawk<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्की
पालङ्कः + .{@-ङ्की@} Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्यः
पालक्यः, -क्या<BR> Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्या
पालक्यः, -क्या<BR> Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालल
पालल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of the powdered sesamum-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालवी
पालवी A kind of vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पलाश-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to or coming from the Palāśa tree.<BR>—2 Made of the wood of the Palāśa tree; Ms. 2. 45.<BR>—3 Green; पालाश-ताम्रासित-कर्बुराणाम् Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशः|पालाश|पालाशं
पालाश + .{@-शः@} The green colour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पालाशखण्डः, पालाशषण्डः, पालाशविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशखण्डः|पालाशखण्ड|पालाशखंड
पालाश + -खण्डः, -षण्डः an epithet of the Magadha country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशषण्डः|पालाशषण्ड|पालाशषंड
पालाश + -खण्डः, -षण्डः an epithet of the Magadha country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशविधिः|पालाशविधि
पालाश + -विधिः Burning a human corpse with Pālāśa wood in case it is<BR> not burnt in the normal course. Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिः|पालि
पालिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The tip of the ear; श्रवणपालिः Gīt. 3.<BR>—2 The edge, skirt, margin; तिष्ठतो युगपालीषु Mb. 7. 191. 30; महति<BR> सितपटच्छन्नपालीं कपालीम् Bh. 3. 55.<BR>—3 The sharp side, edge or point of anything (अश्रि); कपोलपालिं<BR> तव तन्वि मन्ये लावण्यधन्ये दिशमुत्तराख्याम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR>—4 Boundary, limit.<BR>—5 A line, row; विपुलपुलकपाली Gīt. 6; Śi. 3. 51; रजनीचरपालिरागमिष्यत्यविलम्बं<BR> प्रतिपाल्यतां कुमारौ Rām. Ch. 2. 52.<BR>—6 A spot, mark.<BR>—7 A causeway, bridge.<BR>—8 The lap or bosom.<BR>—9 An oblong pond.<BR>—10 Maintenance of a pupil by his teacher during the period of his studies.<BR>—11 A louse.<BR>—12 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—13 A woman with a beard.<BR>—14 The hip.<BR>—15 A measure of capacity (प्रस्थ).<BR>—16 A circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाली
पालिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The tip of the ear; श्रवणपालिः Gīt. 3.<BR>—2 The edge, skirt, margin; तिष्ठतो युगपालीषु Mb. 7. 191. 30; महति<BR> सितपटच्छन्नपालीं कपालीम् Bh. 3. 55.<BR>—3 The sharp side, edge or point of anything (अश्रि); कपोलपालिं<BR> तव तन्वि मन्ये लावण्यधन्ये दिशमुत्तराख्याम् Bv. 2. 9.<BR>—4 Boundary, limit.<BR>—5 A line, row; विपुलपुलकपाली Gīt. 6; Śi. 3. 51; रजनीचरपालिरागमिष्यत्यविलम्बं<BR> प्रतिपाल्यतां कुमारौ Rām. Ch. 2. 52.<BR>—6 A spot, mark.<BR>—7 A causeway, bridge.<BR>—8 The lap or bosom.<BR>—9 An oblong pond.<BR>—10 Maintenance of a pupil by his teacher during the period of his studies.<BR>—11 A louse.<BR>—12 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—13 A woman with a beard.<BR>—14 The hip.<BR>—15 A measure of capacity (प्रस्थ).<BR>—16 A circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाली
पालिः, -ली + .{@-ली@} A pot, boiler.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाल्यामयः, पालिज्वरः, पालिभङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्यामयः|पाल्यामय
पालिः + -आमयः a disease of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिज्वरः|पालिज्वर
पालिः + -ज्वरः a kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिभङ्गः|पालिभङ्ग
पालिः + -भङ्गः the bursting of a dike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिका
पालिका<BR>—1 The tip of the ear.<BR>—2 The sharp edge of a sword or of any cutting instrument.<BR>—3 A butter-knife; Rām. 1. 73. 21.<BR>—4 A pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित्यम्
पालित्यम् Greyness of hair caused by old age, hoariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्दः|पालिन्द|पालिंदः
पालिन्दः Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्लवा
पाल्लवा A game with twigs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्लविक
पाल्लविक <i>a.</i> Diffusive, digressive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्वल
पाल्वल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Coming from a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावः|पाव
पावः A particular wind-instrument; (Mar. पावा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक <i>a.</i> [पू-ण्वुल्] Purifying; पन्थानं पावकं हित्वा जनको<BR> मौढ्यमास्थितः Mb. 12. 18. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकः|पावक
पावक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Fire; पावकस्य महिमा स गण्यते कक्षवज्ज्वलति सागरेऽपि यः<BR> R. 11. 75, 3. 9, 16. 87.<BR>—2 Agni or the god of fire.<BR>—3 The fire of lightning.<BR>—4 The Chitraka tree.<BR>—5 The number ‘three’.<BR>—6 A person purified by religious abstraction, saint, sage.<BR>—7 Good conduct or behaviour.<BR>—8 N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकी
पावक + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 The wife of Agni.<BR>—2 Ved. N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पावकारणिः, पावकार्चिस्, पावकास्त्रम्, पावकात्मजः, पावकमणिः, पावकशिखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकारणिः|पावकारणि
पावक + -अरणिः an epithet of a plant called अग्निमन्थ (Mar. थोर ऐरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकार्चिस्
पावक + -अर्चिस् <i>f.</i> a flash of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकास्त्रम्
पावक + -अस्त्रम् a fiery weapon; प्रशान्तमेव पावकास्त्रम् U. 6. 5/6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकात्मजः|पावकात्मज
पावक + -आत्मजः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 N. of a sage called सुदर्शन who married the daughter of Duryodhana<BR> of the Ikṣvāku family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकमणिः
पावक + -मणिः <i>m.</i> The Sūryakānta Maṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकशिखः
पावक + -शिखः (= अग्निशिखः) Saffron; Śiva B. 30. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकिः|पावकि
पावकिः<BR>—1 An epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 Of the sage सुदर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकीय
पावकीय <i>a.</i> Fiery (as a weapon); सर्वत्रावर्तमुद्रां विदधति<BR> जलधौ सायकैः पावकीयैः B. R. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पू-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>—1 Purifying, freeing from sin, purificatory, sanctifying; पादास्तामभितो<BR> निषण्णहरिणा गौरीगुरोः पावनाः Ś. 6. 17; R. 15. 101, 19. 53; यज्ञो<BR> दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम् Bg. 18. 5; Ms. 2. 26; Y. 3. 307.<BR>—2 Sacred, holy, pure, purified; तपोवनं तच्च बभूव पावनम् Ku. 5. 17.<BR>—3 One living on wind (a Sādhu); कुतः क्षीरं वनस्थानां मुनीनां गिरिवासिनाम् ।<BR> पावनानां वनाशानां वनाश्रमनिवासिनाम् ॥ Mb. 13. 14. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनः|पावन|पावनं
पावन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 Incense.<BR>—3 A kind of demi-god or Siddha.<BR>—4 N. of the poet Vyāsa.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनम्
पावन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Purifying, purification; विष्णोर्भूतानि लोकानां पावनाय चरन्ति हि<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 28; पदनखनीरजनितजनपावन Gīt. 1; Mv. 1. 26; Ms. 11. 85.<BR>—2 Penance.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 Cow-dung.<BR>—5 A sectarial mark.<BR>—6 Any means of purification; उत्पत्तिपरिपूतायाः किमस्याः पावनान्तरैः U. 1. 13.<BR>—7 Atonement, expiation.<BR>—8 Incense (सिह्वक).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पावनध्वनिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनध्वनिः|पावनध्वनि
पावन + -ध्वनिः a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनी
पावनी<BR>—1 The holy basil.<BR>—2 A cow. —3 The river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमानी
पावमानी An epithet of particular Vedic hymns (especially those of<BR> Rv. 9 and Av. 19. 71 &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित
पावित <i>a.</i> cleansed, purified, sanctified, made holy; धन्योऽसि<BR> कृतकृत्योऽसि पावितं ते कुलं त्वया । Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित्र्यम्
पावित्र्यम् Purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाविन्
पाविन् <i>a.</i> Purificatory; पाविन्याः शरणगतार्तिहारिणे तन्माहात्म्यं<BR> भव भवते नमस्क्रियायाः Ki. 18. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाव्य
पाव्य <i>a.</i> To be cleansed or purified; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1016-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावरः|पावर
पावरः The side of a die which is marked with two points; or a particular<BR> throw of this die; पावरपतनाच्च शोषितशरीरः Mk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशः|पाश
पाशः [पश्यते बध्यतेऽनेन, पश्-करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 A cord, chain, fetter, noose; पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः<BR> Ś. 1. 32; बाहुपाशेन व्यापादिता Mk. 9; R. 6. 84.<BR>—2 A snare, trap or net for catching birds and beasts.<BR>—3 A noose used as a weapon (as by Varuṇa); किं चायमरिदुर्वारः पाणौ<BR> पाशः प्रचेतसः Ku. 2. 21.<BR>—4 A die, dice; Malli. on R. 6. 18.<BR>—5 The edge or border of anything woven.<BR>—6 (With Jainas) The outer world, nature.<BR>—7 (At the end of comp.) पाश expresses<BR>——(<i>a</i>) contempt or depreciation; as in छात्रपाशः a bad pupil; वैयाकरण˚, भिषक्˚ &c.;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) beauty or admiration; as in सैवोष्ठमुद्रा स च कर्णपाशः U. 6. 27;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) abundance, mass, or quantity (after a word signifying ‘hair’);<BR> as in केशपाश q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशी
पाशः + .{@-शी@} A rope, fetter; पाशीकल्पामायतामाचकर्ष Śi. 18. 57.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाशान्तः, पाशक्रीडा, पाशजालम्, पाशधरः, पाशपाणिः, पाशबद्ध, पाशबन्धः, पाशबन्धकः, पाशबन्धनम्, पाशभृत्, पाशरज्जुः, पाशहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशान्तः|पाशान्त|पाशांत
पाशः + -अन्तः the back of a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशक्रीडा
पाशः + -क्रीडा gambling, playing with dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशजालम्
पाशः + -जालम् the outer world (conceived as a net).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशधरः|पाशधर
पाशः + -धरः, -पाणिः an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशपाणिः|पाशपाणि
पाशः + -धरः, -पाणिः an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबद्ध
पाशः + -बद्ध <i>a.</i> entrapped, caught in a snare or net, noosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्धः|पाशबन्ध|पाशबंध
पाशः + -बन्धः a noose, snare, halter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्धकः|पाशबन्धक|पाशबंधक
पाशः + -बन्धकः a bird-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्धनम्
पाशः + -बन्धनम् a snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशभृत्
पाशः + -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Varuṇa; R. 2. 9.<BR>—2 one armed with a noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशरज्जुः|पाशरज्जु
पाशः + -रज्जुः <i>f.</i> a fetter, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशहस्तः|पाशहस्त
पाशः + -हस्तः ‘holding a noose in hand’, an epithet of Varuṇa and of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशकः|पाशक
पाशकः<BR>—1 A die, dice.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) A snare, trap; as in कण्ठ˚ &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाशकपीठम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशकपीठम्
पाशकः + -पीठम् a gambling house or table; अर्धवाचितं पाशकपीठे तिष्ठति<BR> पुस्तकम् Mk. 4. 27/28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशनम्
पाशनम्^1<BR>—1 A noose, snare, net, sling.<BR>—2 A cord, lash.<BR>—3 Ensnaring, entrapping.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: virAma missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशयति
पाशयति Den. P. To bind, fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिकः|पाशिक
पाशिकः A bird-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिक्यम्
पाशिक्यम् A pearl from the river Pāśā; Kau. A. 2. 11. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशित|पाशितः
पाशित <i>a.</i> Bound, ensnared, fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशीकृत|पाशीकृतः
पाशीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Chained, fettered.<BR>—2 Snared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन् <i>m.</i> [पाशोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 An epithet of Varuṇa; ‘प्रचेता वरुणः पाशी’ Ak.<BR>—2 Yama.<BR>—3 A deer-catcher, fowler, trapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या<BR>—1 A net.<BR>—2 A collection of snares or ropes (पाशानां समूहः); P. IV. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पशोरिदम् अण्] Relating to or derived from animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशवम्
पाशव + .{@-वम्@} A flock, herd.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाशवपालनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशवपालनम्
पाशव + -पालनम् pasturage or meadow grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुक
पाशुक <i>a.</i> Ved. Belonging to cattle or a sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पशुपतेरिदम् अण्] Coming from or relating or<BR> sacred to Paśupati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतः|पाशुपत
पाशुपत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A follower and worshipper of Śiva.<BR>—2 A follower of the doctrines of Paśupati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतम्
पाशुपत + .{@-तम्@} The Pāśupata doctrines; (for the Pāśupata doctrines,<BR> see Sarva. S.); मया पाशुपतं दक्ष शुभमुत्पादितं पुरा Mb. 12. 284. 195;<BR> (com. ‘अग्निरिति भस्म˚’ इत्यादिना भस्म गृहीत्वा निमृज्याङ्गानि संस्पृशेत् ।<BR> तस्माद् व्रतमेतत् पाशुपतम् ।)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पाशुपतास्त्रम्, पाशुपतयोगः, पाशुपतव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतास्त्रम्
पाशुपत + -अस्त्रम् N. of a missile presided over by पशुपति or Śiva<BR> (which Arjuna acquired from Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतयोगः|पाशुपतयोग
पाशुपत + -योगः, -व्रतम् The system of पाशुपत. See पाशुपतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतव्रतम्
पाशुपत + -योगः, -व्रतम् The system of पाशुपत. See पाशुपतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्यम्
पाशुपाल्यम् The breeding or rearing of cattle, a herdsmanʼs occupation;<BR> वैश्यस्य सततं धर्मः पाशुपाल्यं कृषिस्तथा Mb. 13. 141. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुबन्धकः|पाशुबन्धक|पाशुबंधकः
पाशुबन्धकः A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुबन्धका
पाशुबन्धकः + .{@-का@} The sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्य|पाश्चात्यः
पाश्चात्य <i>a.</i> [पश्चाद्भवः त्यक्]<BR>—1 Hinder.<BR>—2 Western; सङ्ग्रामस्तुमुलस्तस्य पाश्चात्यैरश्वसाधनैः R. 4. 62; जित्वावाच्यांश्च<BR> पाश्चात्यान् प्राच्यांश्च भुजतेजसा Śiva B. 6. 65.<BR>—3 Posterior, later.<BR>—4 Subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्यम्
पाश्चात्य + .{@-त्यम्@} The hinder part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्ड|पाषंड|पाषण्डः
पाषण्ड <i>a.</i> Impious, heretical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डः|पाषण्ड|पाषंड
पाषण्ड + .{@-ण्डः@} A heretic, an unbeliver, a hypocrite; पाषण्डमाश्रितानां … … … योषिताम्<BR> (निवर्तेतोदकक्रिया) Ms. 5. 90, 9. 225; पाषण्डसङ्घद्रव्यमश्रोत्रियभोग्यम्; … चिकित्सकवाग्जीवनपाषण्डछद्मभिर्वा … … Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डः|पाषण्ड|पाषंड
पाषण्ड + .{@-ण्डः, -ण्डम्@} Heresy; also पाषाण्ड्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डम्
पाषण्ड + .{@-ण्डः, -ण्डम्@} Heresy; also पाषाण्ड्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1017-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डकः|पाषण्डक|पाषंडक|पाषंडकः
