पिल्ल|पिल्लः
पिल्ल <i>a.</i> Blear-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्लम्
पिल्ल + .{@-ल्लम्@} A bleared eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्लका
पिल्लका A female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश्
पिश् €6 U. (पिंशति-ते)<BR>—1 To shape, fashion, form; त्वष्टा रूपाणि पिंशतु Rv. 10. 184. 1.<BR>—2 To be organised.<BR>—3 To light, irradiate.<BR>—4 To be reduced to oneʼs constituent parts.<BR>—5 Ved. To adorn, decorate.<BR>—6 To make ready, prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from sin.<BR>—2 Multiform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्ग|पिशंग|पिशङ्गः
पिशङ्ग <i>a.</i> [पिंश्-अङ्गच् किच्च] Reddish-brown, reddish, of<BR> a tawny colour; मध्येसमुद्रं ककुभः पिशङ्गीः Śi. 3. 33, 1. 6; Ki. 4. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गः|पिशङ्ग|पिशंग
पिशङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः@} The tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गकः|पिशङ्गक|पिशंगक|पिशंगकः
पिशङ्गकः An epithet of Viṣṇu or his attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिन्|पिशंगिन्
पिशङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> Brown, tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिला
पिशङ्गिला Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचः|पिशाच
पिशाचः [पिशितमाचामति, आ + चम् बा˚ ड पृषो˚] A fiend, goblin,<BR> devil, spirit, malevolent being; नन्वाश्वासितः पिशाचोऽपि भोजनेन<BR> V. 2; Ms. 1. 37, 12. 44.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पिशाचालयः, पिशाचचर्या, पिशाचद्रुः, पिशाचबाधा, पिशाचसंचारः, पिशाचभाषा, पिशाचसभम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचालयः|पिशाचालय
पिशाचः + -आलयः phosphorescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचचर्या
पिशाचः + -चर्या the practice of पिशाचs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचद्रुः|पिशाचद्रु
पिशाचः + -द्रुः a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचबाधा
पिशाचः + -बाधा, -संचारः demoniacal possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचसंचारः|पिशाचसञ्चार
पिशाचः + -बाधा, -संचारः demoniacal possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचभाषा
पिशाचः + -भाषा ‘the language of devils’, a gibberish or corruption of Sanskrit,<BR> one of the lowest Prākṛta dialects used in plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचसभम्
पिशाचः + -सभम्<BR>—1 an assemblage of fiends.<BR>—2 pandemonium, the hall of their assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचकिन्
पिशाचकिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Kubera, the god of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचिः|पिशाचि
पिशाचिः Ved. = पिशाच q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचिका
पिशाचिका<BR>—1 A she-demon, a female imp.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Devilish or diabolical fondness for a thing;<BR> किमनया आयुधपिशाचिकया Mv. 3 ‘devilish fondness for fighting’; (पिशाची<BR> is used in the same sense; तस्य खल्वियं यावज्जीवमायुधपिशाची न हृदयादपक्रामति<BR> B. R. 4; or कियच्चिरमियमतिनाटयिष्यति भवन्तमायुधपिशाची A. R. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशितम्
पिशितम् [पिश्-क्त; Uṇ. 3. 95]<BR>—1 Flesh; कुत्रापि नापि खलु हा पिशितस्य लेशः Bv. 1. 105; R. 7. 50.<BR>—2 A small piece or part.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पिशिताशनः, पिशिताशः, पिशिताशिन्, पिशितभुज्, पिशितपिण्डः, पिशितप्ररोहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशनः|पिशिताशन
पिशितम् + -अशनः, -आशः, -आशिन्, -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 flesh-eater, a demon, goblin; (छायाः) संध्यापयोदकपिशाः पिशिताशनानां<BR> चरन्ति Ś. 3. 26; Mb. 3. 142. 37.<BR>—2 a man-eater, cannibal. —3 a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशः|पिशिताश
पिशितम् + -अशनः, -आशः, -आशिन्, -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 flesh-eater, a demon, goblin; (छायाः) संध्यापयोदकपिशाः पिशिताशनानां<BR> चरन्ति Ś. 3. 26; Mb. 3. 142. 37.<BR>—2 a man-eater, cannibal. —3 a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशिन्
पिशितम् + -अशनः, -आशः, -आशिन्, -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 flesh-eater, a demon, goblin; (छायाः) संध्यापयोदकपिशाः पिशिताशनानां<BR> चरन्ति Ś. 3. 26; Mb. 3. 142. 37.<BR>—2 a man-eater, cannibal. —3 a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशितभुज्
पिशितम् + -अशनः, -आशः, -आशिन्, -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 flesh-eater, a demon, goblin; (छायाः) संध्यापयोदकपिशाः पिशिताशनानां<BR> चरन्ति Ś. 3. 26; Mb. 3. 142. 37.<BR>—2 a man-eater, cannibal. —3 a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशितपिण्डः|पिशितपिण्ड
पिशितम् + -पिण्डः a piece of flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशितप्ररोहः|पिशितप्ररोह
पिशितम् + -प्ररोहः a fleshy excrescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन <i>a.</i> [पिश्-उनच् किच्च; Uṇ. 3. 55]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Indicating, manifesting, evincing, displaying, indicative of;<BR> शत्रूनामनिशं विनाशपिशुनः Śi. 1. 75; तुल्यानुरागपिशुनम् V. 2. 14;<BR> R. 1. 53; Amaru. 97.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Memorable for, commemorating; क्षेत्रं क्षत्रप्रधनपिशुनं<BR> कौरवं तद् भजेथाः Me. 48.<BR>—2 Slanderous, back-biting, calumniating; पिशुनजनं खलु बिभ्रति क्षितीन्द्राः Bv. 1. 74.<BR>—3 Betraying, treacherous.<BR>—4 Harsh, cruel, unkind.<BR>—5 Wicked, malicious; malignant.<BR>—6 Low, vile, contemptible; of a wicked person; पिशुनं भोजनं भुङ्क्ते<BR> ब्रह्महत्यासमं विदुः Mb. 13. 136. 16.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">Page1024-1</a>]<BR>—7 Foolish, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनः|पिशुन|पिशुनं
पिशुन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A slanderer, back-biter, tale-bearer, base informer, traitor, calumniator;<BR> वरं प्राणत्यागो न च पिशुनवाक्येष्वभिरुचिः H. 1. 116; Pt. 1. 304;<BR> Ms. 3. 161; पिशुनता यद्यस्ति किं पातकैः Bh. 1. 55.<BR>—2 Cotton.<BR>—3 An epithet of Nārada.<BR>—4 A crow.<BR>—5 N. of a goblin (said to be dangerous to pregnant women).<BR>—6 N. of a writer on अर्थशास्त्र mentioned by Kauṭilya in connection<BR> with राजपुत्ररक्षण; Kau. A. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनम्
पिशुन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Betraying.<BR>—2 Saffron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पिशुनवचनम्, पिशुनवाक्यम्, पिशुनवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1023-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवचनम्
पिशुन + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः slander, detraction, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवाक्यम्
पिशुन + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः slander, detraction, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवादः|पिशुनवाद
पिशुन + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः slander, detraction, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनयति
पिशुनयति Den. P. To indicate, show; पिशुनयति रथस्ते शीकरक्लिन्ननेमिः Ś. 7. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनित
पिशुनित <i>p. p.</i> Betrayed, shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशीलम्
पिशीलम्, -लकम् Ved.<BR> An earthen vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशीलकम्
पिशीलम्, -लकम् Ved.<BR> An earthen vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्
पिष् I. €7 P. (पिनष्टि, पिष्ट)<BR>—1 To pound, grind, pulverize, crush; अथवा भवतः प्रवर्तना न कथं<BR> पिष्टमियं पिनष्टि नः N. 2. 61, 13. 19; माषपेषं पिपेष Mv. 6. 45;<BR> Bk. 6. 37, 12. 18; Bv. 1. 12.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, destroy, kill (with gen.); क्रमेण पेष्टुं भुवनद्विषामसि<BR> Śi. 1. 40. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To grind, pound.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure.<BR>—3 To give.<BR>—4 To be strong.<BR>—5 To dwell. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (पेषति, पेषयति-ते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [पिष-क्त]<BR>—1 Ground, powdered, crushed; यत् पिषतामपि नॄणां पिष्टोऽपि तनोषि परिमलैः<BR> पुष्टिम् Bv. 1. 12.<BR>—2 Rubbed together, squeezed or clasped (as the hands).<BR>—3 Kneaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टम्
पिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 Anything ground, a ground substance.<BR>—2 Flour, meal; पिष्टं पिनष्टि he ‘grinds flour’; <i>i. e.</i> does a<BR> useless work or a profitless repetition.<BR>—3 Lead.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पिष्टाद, पिष्टोदकम्, पिष्टपचनम्, पिष्टपशुः, पिष्टपाकभृत्, पिष्टपाकः, पिष्टपाचकम्, पिष्टपिण्डः, पिष्टपूर, पिष्टपेषः, पिष्टपेषणम्, पिष्टमेहः, पिष्टवर्तिः, पिष्टसौरभम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टाद
पिष्ट + -अद <i>a.</i> eating flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टोदकम्
पिष्ट + -उदकम् water mixed with flour; पिष्टोदकं सुतो यस्य पीत्वा<BR> क्षीरस्य तृष्णया Mb. 1. 131. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपचनम्
पिष्ट + -पचनम् a pan for parching flour, a boiler &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपशुः|पिष्टपशु
पिष्ट + -पशुः an effigy of a beast made with flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाकभृत्
पिष्ट + -पाकभृत् <i>m.</i> a boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाकः|पिष्टपाक
पिष्ट + -पाकः a quantity of baked flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाचकम्
पिष्ट + -पाचकम् a boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपिण्डः|पिष्टपिण्ड|पिष्टपिंड
पिष्ट + -पिण्डः a cake or a ball of flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपूर|पिष्टपूरः
पिष्ट + -पूर see घृतपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपेषः|पिष्टपेष
पिष्ट + -पेषः, -पेषणम् ‘grinding flour’ <i>i. e.</i> doing any useless<BR> work or vain or profitless repetition. ˚न्यायः see under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपेषणम्
पिष्ट + -पेषः, -पेषणम् ‘grinding flour’ <i>i. e.</i> doing any useless<BR> work or vain or profitless repetition. ˚न्यायः see under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टमेहः|पिष्टमेह
पिष्ट + -मेहः a variety of diabetes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टवर्तिः|पिष्टवर्ति|पिष्टवर्त्ति|पिष्टवर्त्तिः
पिष्ट + -वर्तिः a kind of small ball made of the flour of barley, pulse or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टसौरभम्
पिष्ट + -सौरभम् (pounded) sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टकः|पिष्टक|पिष्टकं
पिष्टकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A cake made of the flour of any grain.<BR>—2 A baked cake, bread.<BR>—3 A disease of the eye, opacity of the cornea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टकम्
पिष्टकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A cake made of the flour of any grain.<BR>—2 A baked cake, bread.<BR>—3 A disease of the eye, opacity of the cornea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टकम्
पिष्टकः, -कम् + .{@-कम्@} Pounded sesamum-seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपः|पिष्टप|पिष्टपं
पिष्टपः, -पम्<BR> A division of the universe; cf. विष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपम्
पिष्टपः, -पम्<BR> A division of the universe; cf. विष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टातः|पिष्टात
पिष्टातः, पिष्टातकः Fragrant powder (पिष्टातः पटवासकः<BR> Ak.); वृष्टपा पिष्टातकस्य द्युतिमिह मलये मेरुतुल्यां दधानः Nāg. 2. 13.<BR> (This powder is sprinkled over each other at Holi festival).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टातकः|पिष्टातक
पिष्टातः, पिष्टातकः Fragrant powder (पिष्टातः पटवासकः<BR> Ak.); वृष्टपा पिष्टातकस्य द्युतिमिह मलये मेरुतुल्यां दधानः Nāg. 2. 13.<BR> (This powder is sprinkled over each other at Holi festival).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टापः
पिष्टापः Scented or perfumed powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टिकम्
पिष्टिकम् A cake made of rice-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टिका
पिष्टिका Thin paste of raw rice or pulse; दालिः संस्थापिता तोये<BR> ततोऽपहृतकञ्चुका । शिलायां साधु संपिष्टा पिष्टिका कथिता बुधैः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्
पिस् I. €1 P. (पेसति) To go, move. ━II. €10 U. (पेसयति-ते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To be strong.<BR>—3 To dwell.<BR>—4 To hurt, injure.<BR>—5 To give or take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्पृक्षु
पिस्पृक्षु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing to touch.<BR>—2 (with जलम् or सलिलम्) Being about to rinse the mouth or to<BR> perform ablution; कदाचित् प्रातरुत्थाय पिस्पृक्षुः सलिलं शुचि Mb. 12. 228. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
पिहित See under पिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी €4 Ā. (पीयते) To drink; तव वदनभवामृतं निपीय Mk. 10. 13;<BR> N. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीचम्
पीचम् The chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठम्
पीठम्<BR>—1 A seat (a stool, chair, bench, sofa &c.); जवेन पीठादुदतिष्ठदच्युतः<BR> Śi. 1. 12; R. 4. 84, 6. 15.<BR>—2 The seat of a religious student made of Kuśa grass.<BR>—3 The seat of a deity, an altar.<BR>—4 A pedestal in general, basis.<BR>—5 A particular posture in sitting.<BR>—6 (In geometry) The complement of a segment.<BR>—7 N. of various temples; पीठं जालंधरं नाम तिष्ठत्यत्र चतुर्मुख<BR> Yogaśikhopaniṣad 5. 11.<BR>—8 A royal seat, throne.<BR>—9 A district, province.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पीठाधिकारः, पीठकेलिः, पीठग, पीठगर्भः, पीठचक्रम्, पीठनायिका, पीठभूः, पीठमर्द, पीठमर्दः, पीठसर्प<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठाधिकारः|पीठाधिकार
पीठम् + -अधिकारः appointment to an office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठकेलिः|पीठकेलि
पीठम् + -केलिः a male confidant, a parasite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठग
पीठम् + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 lame, crippled.<BR>—2 seated in oneʼs seat (not a warrior); योऽपि स्यात् पीठगः कश्चित् किं<BR> पुनः समरे स्थितः Mb. 3. 22. 24 (com. पीठगः स्वासनस्थः अयुद्धमानोऽपीत्यर्थः ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठगर्भः|पीठगर्भ
पीठम् + -गर्भः the cavity in the pedestal of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठचक्रम्
पीठम् + -चक्रम् a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठनायिका
पीठम् + -नायिका a girl of fourteen (before menstruation) who represents<BR> Durgā at the festival of that goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठभूः
पीठम् + -भूः <i>f.</i> basis, basement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठमर्द|पीठमर्दः|पीठमर्द्द|पीठमर्द्दः
पीठम् + -मर्द <i>a.</i> very impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठमर्दः|पीठमर्द|पीठमर्द्द|पीठमर्द्दः
पीठम् + -मर्दः<BR>—1 a companion, parasite, one who assists the hero of a drama in great<BR> undertakings, <i>e. g.</i> in securing his mistress; Dk. 2. 2; so पीठमर्दिका<BR> ‘a lady who assists the heroine in securing her lover’; उपस्थिता पीठमर्दिकां<BR> पण्डितकौशिकीं पुरस्कृत्य देवी M. 1. 13/14.<BR>—2 a dancing master who instructs courtezans in the art of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठसर्प
पीठम् + -सर्प <i>a.</i> lame, crippled; Ms. 8. 394; कर्तव्ये पुरुषव्याघ्र<BR> किमास्से पीठसर्पवत् Mb. 3. 35. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठकः|पीठक|पीठकं
पीठकः, -कम्<BR> A seat; हस्तिनां पीठकानां च गर्दभानां तथैव च Mb. 1. 84. 21<BR> (com. पीठकानां राजयोग्यानां नरयानविशेषाणां ‘तरबतरावा’<BR> इति म्लेच्छेषु प्रसिद्धानाम् ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठकम्
पीठकः, -कम्<BR> A seat; हस्तिनां पीठकानां च गर्दभानां तथैव च Mb. 1. 84. 21<BR> (com. पीठकानां राजयोग्यानां नरयानविशेषाणां ‘तरबतरावा’<BR> इति म्लेच्छेषु प्रसिद्धानाम् ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठिका
पीठिका<BR>—1 A seat (bench, stool).<BR>—2 A pedestal, base. —3 A section or division of a book, as the पूर्वपीठिका<BR> and उत्तरपीठिका of दशकुमारचरित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठी
पीठी A wooden seat; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्
पीड् €10 U. [पीडयति-ते, पीडित]<BR>—1 To pain, torment, harm, hurt, injure, harass, annoy, molest; नीलं<BR> चापीपिडच्छरैः Bk. 15. 82; Pt. 1. 343; Ms. 4. 67, 238, 7. 29.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">Page1025-1</a>]<BR>—2 To oppose, resist.<BR>—3 To besiege (as a city).<BR>—4 To press or squeeze together, compress, pinch; कण्ठे पीडयन् Mk. 9;<BR> लभेत सिकतासु तैलमपि यत्नतः पीडयन् Bh. 2. 5; दशनपीडिताधरा R. 19. 35.<BR>—5 To suppress, destroy; आत्मन्यन्तर्दधे भूयः कालं कालेन पीडयन् Ms. 1. 51.<BR>—6 To neglect.<BR>—7 To cover with anything inauspicious.<BR>—8 To eclipse.<BR>—9 To overpower.<BR>—10 To break, violate.<BR>—11 To take away, remove.<BR>—12 To stir, agitate.<BR>—13 To cover, wrap.<BR>—14 To leave away, give up; श्रुतिसमधिकमुच्चैः पञ्चमं पीडयन्तः Śi. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1024-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडकः|पीडक
पीडकः An oppressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडनम्
पीडनम् [पीड् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Paining, distressing, oppressing, inflicting pain; Ms. 9. 299; प्रजापीडनसंतापात्<BR> समुद्भूतो हुताशनः । राज्ञः श्रियं कुलं प्राणान्नादग्ध्वा विनिवर्तते ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 345; पीडनवर्गः N. of a chapter in Kau. A. (8. 4).<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Squeezing; pressing; Rām. 7. 16. 29; दोर्वल्लिबन्धनिबिडस्तनपीडनानि<BR> Gīt. 10; दन्तोष्ठपीडननखक्षतरक्तसिक्ताम् C. P. 44.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Pressure; ममातिदृढपीडनैरपि न तृप्तिरालिङ्गनैः Māl. 9. 38.<BR>—3 An instrument for pressing.<BR>—4 Taking, holding, seizing, as in करपीडन or पाणिपीडन q. v.<BR>—5 Laying waste, devastation.<BR>—6 Threshing corn.<BR>—7 An eclipse; as in ग्रहपीडन q. v. शशिदिवाकरयोर्ग्रहपीडनम् Bh. 2. 91.<BR>—8 Suppressing sounds, a fault in the pronunciation of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडा
पीडा [पीड् भावे भिदा˚ अङ्]<BR>—1 Pain, trouble, suffering, annoyance, molestation, agony; आश्रमपीडा<BR> R. 1. 37 ‘disturbance’, 71; मदन˚, दारिद्र्य˚ &c.<BR>—2 Injury, damage, harm; मूढग्राहेणात्मनो यत् पीडया क्रियते तपः<BR> Bg. 17. 19; Ms. 7. 169.<BR>—3 Devastation, laying waste.<BR>—4 Violation, infringement.<BR>—5 Restriction.<BR>—6 Pity, compassion.<BR>—7 Eclipse.<BR>—8 A chaplet, garland for the head.<BR>—9 The <i>Saralā</i> tree.<BR>—10 A basket.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पीडाकर, पीडाकरणम्, पीडागृहम्, पीडाभाज्, पीडास्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकर
पीडा + -कर <i>a.</i> troublesome, painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकरणम्
पीडा + -करणम् torturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडागृहम्
पीडा + -गृहम् house of correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाभाज्
पीडा + -भाज् <i>a.</i> showing wavy marks of pressure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडास्थानम्
पीडा + -स्थानम् (In astrol.) inauspicious distance (of a planet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडित|पीडितं
पीडित <i>p. p.</i> [पीङ्-क्त]<BR>—1 Pained, harassed, tormented, oppressed, pinched.<BR>—2 Squeezed, pressed; गाढालिङ्गनसङ्गपीडितमुखम् (स्तनम्) Mu. 2. 12.<BR>—3 Espoused, held, seized; न प्रमाणीकृतः पाणिर्बाल्ये बालेन पीडितः U. 7. 5.<BR>—4 Violated, broken.<BR>—5 Laid waste, devastated.<BR>—6 Eclipsed.<BR>—7 Bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडितम्
पीडित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Paining, injuring, harassing.<BR>—2 A particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडितम्
पीडित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Fast, closely, firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत <i>a.</i> [पा-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Drunk, quaffed; वनाय पीतप्रतिबद्धवत्सां (गां मुमोच) R. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Steeped, soaked in, filled or saturated with.<BR>—3 Absorbed, drunk up, evaporated; रविपीतजला तपात्यये पुनरोघेन<BR> हि युज्यते नदी Ku. 4. 44.<BR>—4 Watered, sprinkled with water; पातुं न प्रथमं व्यवस्यति जलं<BR> युष्मास्वपीतेषु या Ś. 4. 9.<BR>—5 Yellow; विद्युत्प्रभारचितपीतपटोत्तरीयः Mk. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतः|पीत|पीतं
पीत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Yellow colour.<BR>—2 Topaz.<BR>—3 Safflower.<BR>—4 A yellow pigment prepared<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">Page1025-2</a>]<BR> from cowʼs urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतम्
पीत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Gold.<BR>—2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पीताब्धिः, पीताम्बरः, पीतारुण, पीताश्मन्, पीतकदली, पीतकन्दम्, पीतकावेरम्, पीतकाष्ठम्, पीतकीलका, पीतकुष्ठः, पीतकोश,^1 पीतगन्धम्, पीतचन्दनम्, पीतचम्पकः, पीततुण्डः, पीतदारु, पीतदुग्धा, पीतद्रुः, पीतनिद्र, पीतनील, पीतपादा, पीतपुष्पः, पीतमणिः, पीतमाक्षिकम्, पीतमारुतः, पीतमूलकम्, पीतयूथी, पीतरक्त, पीतरागः, पीतलोहम्, पीतवालुका, पीतवासस्, पीतशोणित, पीतसारः, पीतसारि, पीतस्कन्धः, पीतस्फटिकः, पीतस्फोटः, पीतहरित<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताब्धिः|पीताब्धि
पीत + -अब्धिः an epithet of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताम्बरः|पीताम्बर|पीतांबर
पीत + -अम्बरः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu; इति निगदितः प्रीतः पीताम्बरोपि तथाऽकरोत् Gīt. 12.<BR>—2 an actor.<BR>—3 a religious mendicant wearing yellow garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतारुण|पीतारुणः
पीत + -अरुण <i>a.</i> yellowish-red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतारुणः|पीतारुण
पीत + -अरुण + .({@-णः@}) the middle of day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताश्मन्
पीत + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i> topaz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकदली
पीत + -कदली a species of banana (स्वर्णकदली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकन्दम्
पीत + -कन्दम् the carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकावेरम्
पीत + -कावेरम्<BR>—1 saffron.<BR>—2 brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकाष्ठम्
पीत + -काष्ठम् yellow sanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकीलका
पीत + -कीलका The N. of a tree (senna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकुष्ठः|पीतकुष्ठ
पीत + -कुष्ठः yellow leprosy; भगिनीगमने चैव पीतकुष्ठः प्रजायते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकोश
पीत + -कोश^1 <i>a.</i> one who has ratified a treaty by drinking from a cup; Rāj. T.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतगन्धम्
पीत + -गन्धम् yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचन्दनम्
पीत + -चन्दनम्<BR>—1 a species of sandal-wood.<BR>—2 saffron.<BR>—3 turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचम्पकः|पीतचम्पक|पीतचंपक
पीत + -चम्पकः a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीततुण्डः|पीततुण्ड|पीततुंड
पीत + -तुण्डः a Kāraṇḍava bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदारु
पीत + -दारु <i>n.</i> a kind of pine or <i>Saralā</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदुग्धा
पीत + -दुग्धा<BR>—1 a milch cow.<BR>—2 a cow whose milk has been pledged.<BR>—3 a cow tied up to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतद्रुः|पीतद्रु
पीत + -द्रुः the <i>Saralā</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतनिद्र
पीत + -निद्र <i>a.</i> immersed in slumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतनील|पीतनीलः
पीत + -नील <i>a.</i> green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतनीलः|पीतनील
पीत + -नील + .({@-लः@}) the green colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपादा
पीत + -पादा a kind of bird (Mar. मैमा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपुष्पः|पीतपुष्प|पीतपुष्पं
पीत + -पुष्पः N. of several plants, चम्पक, कर्णिकार &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमणिः|पीतमणि
पीत + -मणिः a topaz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमाक्षिकम्
पीत + -माक्षिकम् a kind of mineral substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमारुतः|पीतमारुत
पीत + -मारुतः a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमूलकम्
पीत + -मूलकम् the carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1025-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतयूथी
