पुटित + .{@-तम्@} The hollow of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटी
पुटी A small piece of cloth worn over the privities; (for other senses see पुट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटीकृ
पुटीकृ To make into a funnel-shaped vessel; B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट्ट्
पुट्ट् €10 U. (पुट्टयति-ते)<BR>—1 To become small, decrease, diminish.<BR>—2 To be low or shallow.<BR>—3 To disregard, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुड्
पुड् €6 P.<BR>—1 To leave, quit, abandon.<BR>—2 To dismiss.<BR>—3 To emit, send forth.<BR>—4 To discover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्
पुण् €6 P. (पुणति) To be virtuous or holy, act in a virtuous manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ट्|पुंट्
पुण्ट् €10 U. (पुण्टयति-ते)<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्|पुंड्
पुण्ड् €1 P. (पुण्डति) To grind, reduce to powder, pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डः|पुण्ड|पुंड|पुंडः
पुण्डः A sign, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकम्
पुण्डरीकम्<BR>—1 A lotus-flower, especially a white lotus; Nelumbium Speciosum; हृत्पुण्डरीकान्तरसंनिविष्टं<BR> स्वतेजसा व्याप्तनभोऽवकाशम् Śivakavacha; U. 6. 12, 29; Māl. 9. 14.<BR>—2 A white parasol.<BR>—3 A medicine, drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकः|पुण्डरीक|पुंडरीक|पुंडरीकं|पुण्डरीकं
पुण्डरीकम् + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 N. of the elephant presiding over the south-east direction; तेन<BR> द्विपानामिव पुण्डरीको राज्ञामजग्योऽजनि पुण्डरीकः R. 18. 8.<BR>—3 A tiger.<BR>—4 A kind of serpent.<BR>—5 A species of rice.<BR>—6 A kind of leprosy.<BR>—7 A fever in an elephant.<BR>—8 A kind of mango tree.<BR>—9 A pitcher, water-pot.<BR>—10 Fire.<BR>—11 A (sectarial) mark on the fore-head.<BR>—12 A kind of sacrifice; पुण्डरीकसहस्रेण वाजपेयशतैस्तथा Mb. 7. 63. 2.<BR>—13 N. of an ancient and renowned devotee of the god Viṭhobā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुण्डरीकाक्षः, पुण्डरीकप्लवः, पुण्डरीकमुखी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकाक्षः|पुण्डरीकाक्ष|पुंडरीकाक्ष|पुण्डरीकाक्षं
पुण्डरीकम् + -अक्षः an epithet of Viṣṇu; यं पुण्डरीकाक्षमिव श्रिता श्रीः R. 18. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकप्लवः|पुण्डरीकप्लव|पुंडरीकप्लव
पुण्डरीकम् + -प्लवः a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकमुखी|पुंडरीकमुखी
पुण्डरीकम् + -मुखी a kind of leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीयकम्
पुण्डरीयकम्<BR>—1 Land lotus.<BR>—2 A kind of plant (= पुण्डर्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डर्यम्
पुण्डर्यम्<BR>—1 A plant, creeper.<BR>—2 A kind of medicinal plant (used as a remedy for diseased eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रः|पुण्ड्र|पुंड्र|पुंड्रः
पुण्ड्रः [पुण्ड्-भेदने रक् Uṇ. 2. 13]<BR>—1 A kind of sugarcane (red variety).<BR>—2 A lotus in general.<BR>—3 A white lotus<BR>—4 A mark or line (on the fore-head) made with sandal &c., sectarial mark;<BR> उत्थं तत् पुण्ड्रमूर्ध्वं जनिमरणतमःखण्डनं मण्डनं च Viṣṇupāda. S. 43.<BR>—5 A worm.<BR>—6 The <i>Atimukta</i> creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्ण्ड्राः
पुण्ड्रः + .{@-ण्ड्राः@} (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुण्ड्रकेलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रकेलिः|पुण्ड्रकेलि|पुंड्रकेलि
पुण्ड्रः + -केलिः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रकः|पुण्ड्रक|पुंड्रक|पुंड्रकः
पुण्ड्रकः<BR>—1 A variety of sugar-cane (red-variety); (Mar. पुंड्या ऊंस); कृष्टे<BR> रोहति दोहदेन पयसां पिण्डेन चेत् पुण्ड्रकः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">Page1028-2</a>]<BR> N. 21. 153.<BR>—2 A sectarial mark.<BR>—3 One who lives by breeding silk-worms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्य|पुण्यं
पुण्य <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 5. 15]<BR>—1 Holy, sacred, pure; जनकतनयास्नानपुण्योदकेषु आश्रमेषु Me. 1;<BR> पुण्यं धाम चण्डीश्वरस्य Me. 35; पुण्यानि हि नामग्रहणान्यपि<BR> महामुनीनां किं पुनर्दर्शनानि K. 41; Ś. 2. 14; Ms. 2. 68.<BR>—2 Good, meritorious, virtuous, righteous, just.<BR>—3 Auspicious, propitious, lucky, favourable (as a day); Ms. 2. 26, 30.<BR>—4 Agreeable, pleasing, lovely, beautiful; प्रकृत्या पुण्यलक्ष्मीकौ<BR> Mv. 1. 16, 24; U. 4. 19; Ku. 5. 73; so पुण्यदर्शनः &c.<BR>—5 Sweet, fragrant (as odour). —6 Solemn, festive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यम्
पुण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 Virtue, religious or moral merit; अत्युत्कटैः पापपुण्यैरिहैव फलमश्नुते<BR> H. 1. 80; महतः पुण्यपण्येन कीतेयं कायनौस्त्वया Śānti. 3. 1;<BR> R. 1. 69; N. 3. 87.<BR>—2 A virtuous or meritorious act, good or virtuous works.<BR>—3 Purity, purification.<BR>—4 A trough for watering cattle.<BR>—5 A religious ceremony, especially one performed by a wife to retain<BR> her husbandʼs affection and to obtain a son.<BR>—6 (Astrol.) the seventh mansion from जन्मलग्न.<BR>—7 the union of मेष, कर्क, तुला and मकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्या
पुण्य + .{@-ण्या@}<BR>—1 The holy basil.<BR>—2 The Ganges.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुण्यानुभावः, पुण्याहम्, पुण्यात्मन्, पुण्योदयः, पुण्योद्यान, पुण्यकर्तृ, पुण्यकर्मन्, पुण्यकालः, पुण्यकीर्तनः, पुण्यश्रवणः, पुण्यकीर्ति, पुण्यकृत्, पुण्यकृत्यम्, पुण्यक्षेत्रम्, पुण्यगन्ध, पुण्यगन्धि, पुण्यगृह, पुण्यजनः, पुण्यजित, पुण्यतीर्थम्, पुण्यदर्शन, पुण्यदुह्, पुण्यनिवह, पुण्यपुरुषः, पुण्यप्रतापः, पुण्यफलम्, पुण्यभाज्, पुण्यभूः, पुण्यभूमिः, पुण्ययोगः, पुण्यरात्रः, पुण्यलक्ष्मीक, पुण्यलोकः, पुण्यशकुनम्, पुण्यशाला, पुण्यशील, पुण्यश्लोक, पुण्यसंचयः, पुण्यस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यानुभावः|पुण्यानुभाव
पुण्य + -अनुभावः pleasing majesty or dignity; U. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याहम्
पुण्य + -अहम् (for अहन्) a happy or auspicious day; पुण्याहं भवन्तो<BR> ब्रुवन्तु । अस्तुपुण्याहम्; पुण्याहं व्रज मङ्गलं सुदिवसं प्रातः प्रयातस्य<BR> ते Amaru. 61. ˚वाचन repeating ‘this is an auspicious day’ three<BR> times at the commencement of most religious ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यात्मन्
पुण्य + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> pious, righteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्योदयः|पुण्योदय
पुण्य + -उदयः the dawn or resulting of good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्योद्यान
पुण्य + -उद्यान <i>a.</i> having lovely gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकर्तृ
पुण्य + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a meritorious or virtuous man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकर्मन्|पुण्यकर्म्मन्
पुण्य + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> doing meritorious acts, upright, righteous. ━(<i>n.</i>)<BR> a meritorious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकालः|पुण्यकाल
पुण्य + -कालः an auspicious time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकीर्तनः
पुण्य + -कीर्तनः, -श्रवणः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकीर्तनम्
पुण्य + -कीर्तनः, -श्रवणः + .({@-नम्@}) narrating or reading Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्रवणः
पुण्य + -कीर्तनः, -श्रवणः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकीर्ति|पुण्यकीर्त्ति
पुण्य + -कीर्ति <i>a.</i> bearing a good or holy name, of auspicious fame,<BR> celebrated; स पुण्यकीर्तिः शतमन्युकल्पो महेन्द्रलोकप्रतिमां समृद्धपा<BR> (अध्यास्त) Bk. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकृत्
पुण्य + -कृत् <i>a.</i> virtuous, meritorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकृत्यम्
पुण्य + -कृत्यम् a meritorious work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यक्षेत्रम्
पुण्य + -क्षेत्रम्<BR>—1 a holy place, place of pilgrimage; अन्यक्षेत्रे कृतं पापं पुण्यक्षेत्रे<BR> विनश्यति । पुण्यक्षेत्रे कृतं पापं वज्रलेपो भविष्यति ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 ‘The holy land’, N. of Āryāvarta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगन्ध|पुण्यगंध|पुण्यगन्धः
पुण्य + -गन्ध <i>a.</i> sweet-scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगन्धः|पुण्यगन्ध|पुण्यगंध
पुण्य + -गन्ध + .({@-न्धः@}) the Champaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगन्धि|पुण्यगंधि
पुण्य + -गन्धि <i>a.</i> fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगृह
पुण्य + -गृह<BR>—1 an alms-house.<BR>—2 a temple; उद्यानानि च रम्याणि हृष्टाः पुण्यगृहाणि च Rām. 2. 67. 12<BR> (com. पुण्यगृहाणि पुण्यसंपादकगृहाणि विप्राद्यर्थानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजनः|पुण्यजन
पुण्य + -जनः<BR>—1 a virtuous man.<BR>—2 a demon, goblin; वियति प्रसमीक्ष्य कालमेघमप्रतिमं पुण्यजनौघमुन्नदन्तम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 2. 56.<BR>—3 a Yakṣa; Bhāg. 4. 10. 3; पयोधरैः पुण्यजनाङ्गनानाम् R. 13. 60.<BR> ˚ईश्वरः an epithet of Kubera; अनुययौ यमपुण्यजनेश्वरौ R. 9. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजित
पुण्य + -जित <i>a.</i> won by merit or good works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यतीर्थम्
पुण्य + -तीर्थम् a holy place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शन|पुण्यदर्शनः
पुण्य + -दर्शन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 beautiful.<BR>—2 of sacred appearance; तां पुण्यदर्शनां दृष्ट्वा R. 1. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शनः|पुण्यदर्शन
पुण्य + -दर्शन + .({@-नः@}) the blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शनम्
पुण्य + -दर्शन + .({@-नम्@}) visiting holy shrines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदुह्
पुण्य + -दुह् <i>a.</i> granting happiness or beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यनिवह
पुण्य + -निवह <i>a.</i> meritorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यपुरुषः|पुण्यपुरुष
पुण्य + -पुरुषः a man rich in moral merit, a pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यप्रतापः|पुण्यप्रताप
पुण्य + -प्रतापः the efficacy of virtue or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">Page1029-1</a>]<BR> moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1028-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यफलम्
पुण्य + -फलम् the reward of good works; यत् पुण्यफलमाप्नोति गां दत्त्वा<BR> विधिवद् गुरोः । तत् पुण्यफलमाप्नोति भिक्षां दत्त्वा द्विजो गृही ॥ Ms. 3. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यफलः|पुण्यफल
पुण्य + -फलम् + .({@-लः@}) a grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभाज्
पुण्य + -भाज् <i>a.</i> blessed, virtuous, meritorious; पुभ्यभाजः खल्वमी<BR> मुनयः K. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभूः
पुण्य + -भूः, -भूमिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 ‘the holy land’, <i>i. e.</i> Āryāvarta.<BR>—2 The son-bearing mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभूमिः|पुण्यभूमि
पुण्य + -भूः, -भूमिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 ‘the holy land’, <i>i. e.</i> Āryāvarta.<BR>—2 The son-bearing mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ययोगः|पुण्ययोग
पुण्य + -योगः the result of virtuous deeds done in a former life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यरात्रः|पुण्यरात्र
पुण्य + -रात्रः<BR>—1 an auspicious night.<BR>—2 a night on which any religious ceremony is held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यलक्ष्मीक
पुण्य + -लक्ष्मीक <i>a.</i> auspicious, prosperous; प्रकृत्या पुण्यलक्ष्मीकौ<BR> कावेतौ ज्ञायते त्विदम् Mv. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यलोकः|पुण्यलोक
पुण्य + -लोकः heaven, paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशकुनम्
पुण्य + -शकुनम् an auspicious omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशकुनः|पुण्यशकुन
पुण्य + -शकुनम् + .({@-नः@}) a bird of good omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशाला
पुण्य + -शाला alms-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशील
पुण्य + -शील <i>a.</i> of a virtuous disposition, inclined to pious acts,<BR> virtuous, pious, righteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोक|पुण्यश्लोकः
पुण्य + -श्लोक <i>a.</i> ‘well-spoken of’, or ‘auspicious to repeat or utter the name of’<BR>, of good fame; Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोकः|पुण्यश्लोक
पुण्य + -श्लोक + .({@-कः@}) an epithet of Nala (of Niṣadha); Yudhiṣṭhira and Janārdana;<BR> पुण्यश्लोको नलो राजा पुण्यश्लोको युधिष्ठिरः । पुण्यश्लोका च वैदेही पुण्यश्लोको<BR> जनार्दनः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोका
पुण्य + -श्लोक + .({@-का@}) an epithet of Śītā and Draupadī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यसंचयः|पुण्यसञ्चय
पुण्य + -संचयः a store of virtue or religious merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यस्थानम्
पुण्य + -स्थानम् a sacred or holy place, a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकम्
पुण्यकम्<BR>—1 A religious or virtuous act (such as fasting &c.).<BR>—2 A religious rite or ceremony, a festival &c.<BR>—3 = पुण्यम् 5; Mb. 1. 3. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकः|पुण्यक|पुण्यकं
पुण्यकम् + .{@-कः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुण्यकव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकव्रतम्
पुण्यकम् + -व्रतम् the worship of Kṛṣṇa for a year, performed by a woman<BR> desirous of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यवत्|पुण्यवन्त्
पुण्यवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Meritorious, virtuous.<BR>—2 Lucky, auspicious, fortunate.<BR>—3 Happy, blessed.<BR>—4 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्
पुत् <i>n.</i> A particular division of Hell or the infernal regions<BR> to which childless persons are said to be condemned; see पुत्र below.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुन्नामन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नामन्|पुंनामन्
पुत् + -नामन् <i>a.</i> (hell) called पुत्; पुन्नाम्नो नरकाद् यस्मात् त्रायते<BR> पितरं सुतः । तस्मात् पुत्र इति प्रोक्तः … … Ms. 9. 138; Mb. 1. 74. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलः|पुत्तल
पुत्तलः, -ली<BR>—1 An image, idol, a statue, effigy.<BR>—2 A doll, puppet.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुत्तलदहनम्, पुत्तलविधिः, पुत्तलपूजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तली
पुत्तलः, -ली<BR>—1 An image, idol, a statue, effigy.<BR>—2 A doll, puppet.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुत्तलदहनम्, पुत्तलविधिः, पुत्तलपूजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलदहनम्
पुत्तलः + -दहनम्, -विधिः burning an effigy in place of the body of one<BR> who has died abroad or whose corpse is lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलविधिः|पुत्तलविधि
पुत्तलः + -दहनम्, -विधिः burning an effigy in place of the body of one<BR> who has died abroad or whose corpse is lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलपूजा
पुत्तलः + -पूजा idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलकः|पुत्तलक
पुत्तलकः, पुत्तलिका A doll &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तलिका
पुत्तलकः, पुत्तलिका A doll &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तिका
पुत्तिका<BR>—1 A small kind of bee; पुलाका इव धान्येषु पुत्तिका इव पक्षिषु । तद्विधास्ते<BR> मनुष्याणां येषां धर्मो न कारणम् ॥ Mb. 12. 181. 7.<BR>—2 The white ant.<BR>—3 A doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रः|पुत्र|पुत्त्रः
पुत्रः —1 A son; (the word is thus derived:− पुन्नाम्नो नरकाद् यस्मात्<BR> त्रायते पितरं सुतः । तस्मात् पुत्र इति प्रोक्तः स्वयमेव स्वयंभुवा ।<BR> Ms. 9. 138; the word, therefore, should be strictly written पुत्त्रः).<BR>—2 A child, young one of an animal.<BR>—3 A dear child (a term of endearment in addressing young persons).<BR>—4 (At the end of comp.) Anything little or small of its kind; as in असिपुत्रः,<BR> शिलापुत्रः &c.<BR>—5 (Astrol.) The fifth mansion from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">Page1029-2</a>]<BR> जन्मलग्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रौ
पुत्रः + .{@-त्रौ@} (du.) A son and daughter.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुत्रान्नादः, पुत्रार्थिन्, पुत्राचार्य, पुत्रादिनी, पुत्रेष्टिः, पुत्रेष्टिका, पुत्रैश्वर्यम्, पुत्रकर्मन्, पुत्रकाम, पुत्रकाम्या, पुत्रकार्यम्, पुत्रकृत्, पुत्रकृतकः, पुत्रजग्धी, पुत्रजात, पुत्रदारम्, पुत्रधर्मः, पुत्रपौत्रम्, पुत्रपौत्राः, पुत्रपौत्रीण, पुत्रप्रतिनिधिः, पुत्रप्रवरः, पुत्रलाभः, पुत्रवधः, पुत्रसखः, पुत्रसूः, पुत्रहीन, पुत्रसंकरिन्, पुत्रहतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रान्नादः|पुत्रान्नाद|पुत्त्रान्नादः
पुत्रः + -अन्नादः<BR>—1 one who lives at a sonʼs expense, one who is maintained by his son.<BR>—2 a mendicant of a particular order; see कुटीचक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रार्थिन्
पुत्रः + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> wishing for a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्राचार्य|पुत्राचार्य्य
पुत्रः + -आचार्य <i>a.</i> one having a son for his teacher; Ms. 3. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रादिनी
पुत्रः + -आदिनी<BR>—1 an unnatural mother.<BR>—2 a tigress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रेष्टिः|पुत्रेष्टि|पुत्त्रेष्टिः
पुत्रः + -इष्टिः, -इष्टिका <i>f.</i> a sacrifice performed to obtain male issue;<BR> गृहीत्वा पञ्चवर्षीयं पुत्रेष्टिं प्रथमं चरेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रेष्टिका
पुत्रः + -इष्टिः, -इष्टिका <i>f.</i> a sacrifice performed to obtain male issue;<BR> गृहीत्वा पञ्चवर्षीयं पुत्रेष्टिं प्रथमं चरेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रैश्वर्यम्
पुत्रः + -ऐश्वर्यम् a resignation of property or power by a father to his son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकर्मन्
पुत्रः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> a ceremony on the birth of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकाम
पुत्रः + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकाम्या
पुत्रः + -काम्या a wish for sons; अथाभ्यर्च्य विधातारं प्रयतौ पुत्रकाम्यया R. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकार्यम्
पुत्रः + -कार्यम् a ceremony relating to a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकृत्
पुत्रः + -कृत् <i>m.</i> an adopted son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकृतकः|पुत्रकृतक
पुत्रः + -कृतकः one who is adopted as a son, an adopted son; श्यामाकमुष्टिपरिवर्धितको<BR> जहाति सोऽयं न पुत्रकृतकः पदवीं मृगस्ते Ś. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रजग्धी
पुत्रः + -जग्धी an unnatural mother (who eats her own children.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रजात
पुत्रः + -जात <i>a.</i> one to whom a son is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रदारम्
पुत्रः + -दारम् son and wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रधर्मः|पुत्रधर्म
पुत्रः + -धर्मः filial duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रपौत्रम्
पुत्रः + -पौत्रम्, -पौत्राः sons and grandsons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रपौत्राः
पुत्रः + -पौत्रम्, -पौत्राः sons and grandsons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रपौत्रीण
पुत्रः + -पौत्रीण <i>a.</i> transmitted from son to son, hereditary; लक्ष्मीं<BR> परंपरीणां त्वं पुत्रपौत्रीणतां नय Bk. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रप्रतिनिधिः|पुत्रप्रतिनिधि
पुत्रः + -प्रतिनिधिः a substitute for a son (<i>e. g.</i> an adopted son).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रप्रवरः|पुत्रप्रवर
पुत्रः + -प्रवरः the eldest son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रलाभः|पुत्रलाभ
पुत्रः + -लाभः obtaining a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रवधः
पुत्रः + -वधः <i>f.</i> a daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रसखः|पुत्रसख
पुत्रः + -सखः ‘a friend of children’, one who is fond of children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रसूः
पुत्रः + -सूः a mother of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रहीन
पुत्रः + -हीन <i>a.</i> sonless, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रसंकरिन्
पुत्रः + -संकरिन् <i>a.</i> mixing or confusing sons by mixed marriages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रहतः|पुत्रहत
पुत्रः + -हतः an epithet of Vasiṣṭha (whose hundred sons were killed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रहती
पुत्रः + -हतः + .({@-ती@}) an unnatural mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकः|पुत्रक|पुत्त्रकः
पुत्रकः [पुत्र अनुकम्पायां संज्ञायां वा कन् स्वार्थे क वा]<BR>—1 A little son or boy, boy, chap, lad (often used as a term of endearment);<BR> हा हा पुत्रक नाधीतं सुगतैतासु रात्रिषु.<BR>—2 A doll, puppet; सा कन्दुकैः कृत्रिमपुत्रकैश्च रेमे Ku. 1. 29.<BR>—3 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—4 A locust, grass-hopper.<BR>—5 A fabulous animal with eight feet (शरभ).<BR>—6 Hair.<BR>—7 A pitiable person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रका
पुत्रका, -पुत्रिका<BR>—1 A daughter.<BR>—2 A doll, puppet.<BR>—3 A daughter appointed to raise male issue for a father who has no sons;<BR> अपुत्राऽनेन विधिना सुतां कुर्वीत पुत्रिकाम् । यदपत्यं भवेदस्यां तन्मम<BR> स्यात् स्वधाकरम् ॥ Ms. 9. 127.<BR>—4 The cotton or down of the tamarisk.<BR>—5 A small statue; तद्धाम्नाऽभूदजस्तूष्णीं पूर्देव्यन्तीव पुत्रिका Bhāg. 10. 13. 56.<BR>—6 (At the end of comp.) Anything little or small of its kind; as in असिपुत्रिका,<BR> खड्गपुत्रिका &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुत्रकाधर्मः, पुत्रकापुत्रः, पुत्रकासुतः, पुत्रकाप्रसूः, पुत्रकाभर्तृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिका
पुत्रका, -पुत्रिका<BR>—1 A daughter.<BR>—2 A doll, puppet.<BR>—3 A daughter appointed to raise male issue for a father who has no sons;<BR> अपुत्राऽनेन विधिना सुतां कुर्वीत पुत्रिकाम् । यदपत्यं भवेदस्यां तन्मम<BR> स्यात् स्वधाकरम् ॥ Ms. 9. 127.<BR>—4 The cotton or down of the tamarisk.<BR>—5 A small statue; तद्धाम्नाऽभूदजस्तूष्णीं पूर्देव्यन्तीव पुत्रिका Bhāg. 10. 13. 56.<BR>—6 (At the end of comp.) Anything little or small of its kind; as in असिपुत्रिका,<BR> खड्गपुत्रिका &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुत्रकाधर्मः, पुत्रकापुत्रः, पुत्रकासुतः, पुत्रकाप्रसूः, पुत्रकाभर्तृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकाधर्मः
पुत्रका + -धर्मः bestowing a daughter in marriage so as to raise issue<BR> for her father (see पुत्रिका 3); आकूतिं रुचये प्रादादपि भ्रातृमतीं<BR> नृपः । पुत्रिकाधर्ममाश्रित्य Bhāg. 4. 1. 2. See next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकापुत्रः|पुत्रकापुत्र
पुत्रका + -पुत्रः, -सुतः<BR>—1 a daughterʼs son who by agreement becomes the son of her father; see<BR> Ms. 9. 127; अभ्रातृकां प्रदास्यामि तुभ्यं कन्यामलंकृताम् । अस्यां यो जायते<BR> पुत्रः स मे पुत्रो भवेदिति ॥ Vasiṣṭhasmṛti.<BR>—2 a daughter who, being regarded as a son, returns to her fatherʼs house;<BR> (पुत्रिकैव पुत्रः; अथवा पुत्रिकैव सुतः पुत्रिकासुतः सोऽप्यौरससम<BR> एव Mit. on Y. 2. 128).<BR>—3 a grandson<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकासुतः|पुत्रकासुत
पुत्रका + -पुत्रः, -सुतः<BR>—1 a daughterʼs son who by agreement becomes the son of her father; see<BR> Ms. 9. 127; अभ्रातृकां प्रदास्यामि तुभ्यं कन्यामलंकृताम् । अस्यां यो जायते<BR> पुत्रः स मे पुत्रो भवेदिति ॥ Vasiṣṭhasmṛti.<BR>—2 a daughter who, being regarded as a son, returns to her fatherʼs house;<BR> (पुत्रिकैव पुत्रः; अथवा पुत्रिकैव सुतः पुत्रिकासुतः सोऽप्यौरससम<BR> एव Mit. on Y. 2. 128).<BR>—3 a grandson<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकाप्रसूः
पुत्रका + -प्रसूः a mother<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">Page1030-1</a>]<BR> of daughters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1029-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रकाभर्तृ
पुत्रका + -भर्तृ <i>m.</i> ‘a daughterʼs husband’, a son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रंचारिन्
पुत्रंचारिन् N. of some plant; Mātaṅga L. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रंजीवः|पुत्रञ्जीव
पुत्रंजीवः, -वकः<BR> N. of a plant (from its seeds or flowers are made garlands<BR> and worn to keep children in good health).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रंजीवकः|पुत्रञ्जीवक|पुत्त्रञ्जीवकः|पुत्रंजीवक
पुत्रंजीवः, -वकः<BR> N. of a plant (from its seeds or flowers are made garlands<BR> and worn to keep children in good health).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिन्
पुत्रिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Having a son or sons; अविध्नमस्तु ते स्थेयाः पितेव<BR> धुरि पुत्रिणाम् R. 1. 91; V. 5. 14. ━<i>m.</i> The father of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिणी
पुत्रिन् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 The mother of a son.<BR>—2 A parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रिय
पुत्रिय, पुत्रीय, पुत्र्य <i>a.</i> Relating to a son, filial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रीय|पुत्त्रीयं
पुत्रिय, पुत्रीय, पुत्र्य <i>a.</i> Relating to a son, filial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्र्य|पुत्त्र्यं
पुत्रिय, पुत्रीय, पुत्र्य <i>a.</i> Relating to a son, filial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्री
पुत्री<BR>—1 A daughter.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā; see पुत्रिका also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रीकृ
पुत्रीकृ €8 U. To adopt as a son; अमुं पुरः पश्यसि देवदारुं पुत्रीकृतोऽसौ<BR> वृषभध्वजेन R. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रीय|पुत्त्रीयं
पुत्रीय <i>a.</i> Relating to a son; ततः प्राकमदिष्टिं तां पुत्रीयां<BR> पुत्रकारणात् Rām. 1. 15. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्रीया
पुत्रीया The desire of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ्
पुथ् I. €4 P. (पुथ्यति) To injure, hurt. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To destroy completely, annihilate.<BR>—2 To overpower, drown (as a sound).<BR>—3 To speak.<BR>—4 To shine. ━II. €10 U. (पोथयति-ते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोथित
पोथित <i>p. p.</i> Hurt, killed, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गल|पुद्गलः
पुद्गल <i>a.</i> Beautiful, lovely, handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गलः|पुद्गल
पुद्गल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 Atom (परमाणुः) पुद्गलाः परमाणवः Śrīdhara.<BR>—2 The body, matter; A. Rām. 3. 2. 28.<BR>—3 The soul.<BR>—4 The Ego or individual.<BR>—5 Man.<BR>—6 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्थ्
पुन्थ् €1 P.<BR>—1 To kill, to hurt.<BR>—2 To suffer; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्
पुनर् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Again, once more, anew; न पुनरेवं प्रवर्तितव्यम् Ś. 6; किमप्ययं<BR> बटुः पुनर्विवक्षुः स्फुरितोत्तराधरः Ku. 5. 83; so पुर्नभू ‘to become a wife again’<BR>.<BR>—2 Back, in an opposite direction (mostly with verbs); पुनर्दा ‘to give back, restore’<BR>; पुनर्या-इ-गम् &c. ‘to go back, return’ &c.<BR>—3 On the other hand, on the contrary, but, however, nevertheless, still<BR> (with an adversative force); प्रसाद इव मूर्तस्ते स्पर्शः स्नेहार्द्रशीतलः ।<BR> अद्याप्यानन्दयति मां त्वं पुनः क्वासि नन्दिनि U. 3. 14; मम पुनः<BR> सर्वमेव तन्नास्ति U. 3.<BR>—4 Further, furthermore, besides; पुनः पुनः ‘again and again’, ‘repeatedly’,<BR> ‘frequently’; पुनः पुनः सुतनिषिद्धचापलम् R. 3. 42; किं पुनः<BR> ‘how much more’, or ‘how much less’; see under किम्. पुनरपि again,<BR> once more, and also; on the other hand.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुनरन्वयः, पुनरपगमः, पुनरर्थिता, पुनरागत, पुनरागमः, पुनरागमनम्, पुनराधानम्, पुनराधेयम्, पुनरावर्तः, पुनरावर्तिन्, पुनरावृत्, पुनरुक्त, पुनरुक्तिः, पुनरुत्थानम्, पुनरुत्पत्ति, पुनरुत्पादनम्, पुनरुपगमः, पुनरुपोढा, पुनरूढा, पुनःक्रिया, पुनर्गमनम्, पुनर्जन्मन्, पुनर्जात, पुनर्डीनम्, पुनर्णवः, पुनर्नवः, पुनर्दारक्रिया, पुनर्नवा, पुनःपुना, पुनःप्रत्युपकारः, पुनःप्रसवः, पुनर्भव, पुनर्भविन्, पुनर्भावः, पुनर्भूः, पुनर्भोगः, पुनर्वचनम्, पुनर्वत्सः, पुनर्वसुः, पुनर्विवाहः, पुनःसंस्कारः, पुनःसंगमः, पुनःसंधानम्, पुनःसंभवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरन्वयः
पुनर् + -अन्वयः returning; किंवा गतोऽस्य पुनरन्वयमन्यलोकम् Bhāg. 6. 14. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरपगमः|पुनरपगम
पुनर् + -अपगमः going away again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरर्थिता
पुनर् + -अर्थिता a repeated request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागत
पुनर् + -आगत <i>a.</i> come back, returned; गोव्रजात् पुनरागतम् Ms. 11. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागमः|पुनरागम
पुनर् + -आगमः, -आगमनम् coming back, return; भस्मीभूतस्य देहस्य पुनरागमनं<BR> कुतः Sarva. S.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">Page1030-2</a>]<BR> इष्टकामप्रसिद्धयर्थं पुनरागमनाय च Pūjāmantram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागमनम्
पुनर् + -आगमः, -आगमनम् coming back, return; भस्मीभूतस्य देहस्य पुनरागमनं<BR> कुतः Sarva. S.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">Page1030-2</a>]<BR> इष्टकामप्रसिद्धयर्थं पुनरागमनाय च Pūjāmantram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनराधानम्
पुनर् + -आधानम्, -आधेयम् renewing the consecrated fire; पुनर्दारक्रियां<BR> कुर्यात् पुनराधानमेव च Ms. 5. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनराधेयम्
पुनर् + -आधानम्, -आधेयम् renewing the consecrated fire; पुनर्दारक्रियां<BR> कुर्यात् पुनराधानमेव च Ms. 5. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्तः|पुनरावर्त|पुनरावर्त्त
पुनर् + -आवर्तः<BR>—1 return.<BR>—2 repeated birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्तिन्|पुनरावर्त्तिन्
पुनर् + -आवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> returning to mundane existence; आ ब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः<BR> पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन Bg. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावृत्
पुनर् + -आवृत् <i>f.</i><BR> {@-आवृत्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 repetition.<BR>—2 return to worldly existence, repetition of birth; करोति पुनरावृत्तिस्तेषामिह<BR> न विद्यते Y. 3. 194.<BR>—3 revision, another edition (of a book &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्त|पुनरुक्तं
पुनर् + -उक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 said again, repeated, reiterated.<BR>—2 superfluous, unnecessary; शशंस वाचा पुनरुक्तयेव R. 2. 68; Śi. 7. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्तम्
पुनर् + -उक्त + .({@-क्तम्@}), {@पुनरुक्तता@}<BR>—1 repetition.<BR>—2 superfluity, redundancy, uselessness, tautology; V. 5. 15; व्यापारैः<BR> पुनरुक्तभुक्तविषयैरेवंविधेनामुना संसारेण कदर्थिताः Bh. 3. 78.<BR> ˚जन्मन् <i>m.</i> a Brāhmaṇa (द्विजन्मन्). {@पुनरुक्तवदाभासः@}<BR> seeming tautology, appearance of repetition, regarded as a figure of speech;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> भुजंगकुण्डलीव्यक्तशशिशुभ्रांशुशीतगुः । जगन्त्यपि सदापायादव्याच्चेतोहरः<BR> शिवः S. D. 632; (here the first impression of the tautology is removed<BR> when the passage is rightly understood; cf. also K. P. 9 under पुनरुक्तवदाभास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्तिः|पुनरुक्ति
पुनर् + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 repetition.<BR>—2 superfluity, uselessness, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुत्थानम्
पुनर् + -उत्थानम् rising again, resurrection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुत्पत्ति
पुनर् + -उत्पत्ति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 reproduction. —2 return of birth, metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुत्पादनम्
पुनर् + -उत्पादनम् reproduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुपगमः|पुनरुपगम
पुनर् + -उपगमः return; क्वायोध्यायाः पुनरुपगमो दण्डकायां वने वः U. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुपोढा
पुनर् + -उपोढा, -ऊढा a woman married again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरूढा
पुनर् + -उपोढा, -ऊढा a woman married again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःक्रिया
पुनर् + -क्रिया <i>f.</i> repetition, doing again; न च कृतस्य क्रमानुग्रहार्थं<BR> पुनःक्रिया न्याय्या । ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्गमनम्
पुनर् + -गमनम् return, going again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मन्
पुनर् + -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> repeated birth, metempsychosis; मामुपेत्य तु<BR> कौन्तेय पुनर्जन्म न विद्यते Bg. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जात
पुनर् + -जात <i>a.</i> born again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्डीनम्
पुनर् + -डीनम् a particular manner of flying; Mb. 8. 41. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्णवः|पुनर्णव|पुनर्ण्णव
पुनर् + -णवः, -नवः ‘growing again and again’, a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्नवः|पुनर्नव
पुनर् + -णवः, -नवः ‘growing again and again’, a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्दारक्रिया
पुनर् + -दारक्रिया marrying again, taking a second wife; Ms. 5. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्नवा
पुनर् + -नवा hog-weed, Boerhavia Procumbens (Mar. घेटुळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुना
पुनर् + -पुना (पुनःपुना) N. of a river in Behār; कीकटेषु<BR> गया रम्या नदी पुण्या पुनःपुना Vāyu P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःप्रत्युपकारः|पुनःप्रत्युपकार
पुनर् + -प्रत्युपकारः returning oneʼs obligations, requital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःप्रसवः
पुनर् + -प्रसवः (See प्रतिप्रसवः) प्रतिषिद्धस्य पत्न्या अध्ययनस्य<BR> पुनःप्रसवे न किंचिदस्ति प्रमाणम् ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भव|पुनर्भवः
पुनर् + -भव <i>a.</i> born again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भवः|पुनर्भव
पुनर् + -भव + .({@-वः@}) —1 transmigration, repeated or recurring birth; metempsychosis;<BR> अदृष्टाश्रुतवस्तुत्वात् स जीवो यत् पुनर्भवः Bhāg. 1. 3. 32; ममापि<BR> च क्षपयतु नीललोहितः पुनर्भवं परिगतशक्तिरात्मभूः Ś. 7. 35; Ku. 3. 5.<BR>—2 a finger nail, hair; Mb. 13. 111. 98;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भविन्
पुनर् + -भविन् <i>m.</i> the sentient soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भावः|पुनर्भाव
पुनर् + -भावः new birth, repeated birth; न गच्छन्ति पुनर्भावं मुनयः<BR> संशितव्रताः Mb. 12. 279. 5; मेने पुनर्भावमिवात्मनश्च Bu. C. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भूः
पुनर् + -भूः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a (virgin) widow remarried.<BR>—2 re-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भोगः|पुनर्भोग
पुनर् + -भोगः<BR>—1 repeated enjoyment.<BR>—2 return of fruition.<BR>—3 repeated possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वचनम्
पुनर् + -वचनम्<BR>—1 repetition.<BR>—2 repeated scriptural injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वत्सः|पुनर्वत्स
पुनर् + -वत्सः a weaned calf that begins to suck again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसुः|पुनर्वसु|पुनर्व्वसुः
पुनर् + -वसुः (usually dual)<BR>—1 the seventh lunar mansion (consisting of two or four stars); गां<BR> गताविव दिवः पुनर्वसू R. 11. 36.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्विवाहः|पुनर्विवाह
पुनर् + -विवाहः remarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंस्कारः|पुनःसंस्कार
पुनर् + -संस्कारः (पुनःसंस्कारः) repetition of any Saṃskāra<BR> or purificatory ceremony.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">Page1031-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1030-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंगमः|पुनःसङ्गम
पुनर् + -संगमः, -संधानम् (पुनःसंधानम् &c.)<BR>—1 reunion.<BR>—2 rekindling the sacred fire when it has been extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंधानम्
पुनर् + -संगमः, -संधानम् (पुनःसंधानम् &c.)<BR>—1 reunion.<BR>—2 rekindling the sacred fire when it has been extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंभवः|पुनःसम्भव
पुनर् + -संभवः (पुनःसंभवः) being born again (into the world), metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुपूषा
पुपूषा The desire to cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुटः
पुप्फुटः N. of a disease of the palate and gums.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुलः|पुप्फुल
पुप्फुलः Flatulency or wind (in the stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुसः|पुप्फुस
पुप्फुसः<BR>—1 The lungs.<BR>—2 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
पुर् €6 P. (पुरति) To go before, precede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
पुर् <i>f.</i> (Nom. sing. पूः; instr. du. पूर्भ्याम्)<BR>—1 A town, fortified town; पूरप्यभिव्यक्तमुखप्रसादा R. 16. 23.<BR>—2 A fortress, castle, strong-hold.<BR>—3 A wall, rampart.<BR>—4 The body; पुरश्चक्रे द्विपदः पुरश्चक्रे चतुष्पदः Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 18. 5<BR> Intellect.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूर्द्वार्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्द्वार्
पुर् + -द्वार् <i>f.</i>, {@-द्वारम्@} (पूर्द्वार्)<BR> the gate of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर <i>a.</i> [पृ-क] Full of, filled with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरम्
पुर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A town, city (containing large buildings, surrounded by a ditch, and<BR> not less than one Krośa in extent); पुरे तावन्तमेवास्य तनोति रविरातपम्<BR> Ku. 2. 33; R. 1. 59.<BR>—2 A castle, fortress, stronghold.<BR>—3 A house, residence, abode.<BR>—4 The body; नवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन् न कारयन् Bg. 5. 13.<BR>—5 The female apartments.<BR>—6 N. of the town पाटलिपुत्र; q. v.<BR>—7 The calyx of a flower, or any cup formed of leaves.<BR>—8 A brothel.<BR>—9 The skin.<BR>—10 Bdellium.<BR>—11 An upper story.<BR>—12 A store-house.<BR>—13 A fragrant grass (नागरमुस्ता).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुराट्टः, पुराधिपः, पुराध्यक्षः, पुरारातिः, पुरारिः, पुरासुहृद्, पुरार्धाविस्तारः, पुरोत्सवः, पुरोद्यानम्, पुरौकस्, पुरकोट्टम्, पुरग, पुरजित्, पुरद्विष्, पुरभिद्, पुरज्योतिस्, पुरतटी, पुरतोरणम्, पुरदेवता, पुरद्वारम्, पुरनारी, पुरनिवेशः, पुरपालः, पुरमथनः, पुरमार्गः, पुररक्षः, पुररक्षकः, पुररक्षिन्, पुररोधः, पुरवासिन्, पुरवास्तु, पुरशासनः, पुरहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराट्टः|पुराट्ट
पुर + -अट्टः a turret on a city-wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराधिपः|पुराधिप
पुर + -अधिपः, -अध्यक्षः the governor of a town; Mb. 13. 135. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराध्यक्षः|पुराध्यक्ष
पुर + -अधिपः, -अध्यक्षः the governor of a town; Mb. 13. 135. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरारातिः|पुराराति
पुर + -अरातिः, -अरिः, -असुहृद् <i>m.</i>, {@-रिपुः@}<BR> epithets of Śiva; Bhāg. 5. 24. 28; पुरारातिभ्रान्त्या<BR> कुसुमशर किं मां प्रहरसि Subhāṣ.; see त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरारिः|पुरारि
पुर + -अरातिः, -अरिः, -असुहृद् <i>m.</i>, {@-रिपुः@}<BR> epithets of Śiva; Bhāg. 5. 24. 28; पुरारातिभ्रान्त्या<BR> कुसुमशर किं मां प्रहरसि Subhāṣ.; see त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरासुहृद्
पुर + -अरातिः, -अरिः, -असुहृद् <i>m.</i>, {@-रिपुः@}<BR> epithets of Śiva; Bhāg. 5. 24. 28; पुरारातिभ्रान्त्या<BR> कुसुमशर किं मां प्रहरसि Subhāṣ.; see त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरार्धाविस्तारः
पुर + -अर्धाविस्तारः<BR>—1 a small village, hamlet.<BR>—2 a suburb, ward, division of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोत्सवः|पुरोत्सव
पुर + -उत्सवः a festival celebrated in a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोद्यानम्
पुर + -उद्यानम् a city-garden, park.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरौकस्
पुर + -ओकस् <i>m.</i> an inhabitant of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरकोट्टम्
पुर + -कोट्टम् a citadel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरग
पुर + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going to a town.<BR>—2 favourably inclined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरजित्
पुर + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद् <i>m.</i> epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्विष्
पुर + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद् <i>m.</i> epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरभिद्
पुर + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद् <i>m.</i> epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरज्योतिस्
पुर + -ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of fire.<BR>—2 the world of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतटी
पुर + -तटी a small market-town, small village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतोरणम्
पुर + -तोरणम् the outer gate of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरदेवता
पुर + -देवता the tutelary deity of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्वारम्
पुर + -द्वारम् a city-gate; कोट्या कोट्या पुरद्वारमेकैकं रुरुधे द्विषाम् Bk. 14. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरनारी
पुर + -नारी a courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरनिवेशः|पुरनिवेश
पुर + -निवेशः the founding of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरपालः|पुरपाल
पुर + -पालः<BR>—1 ‘city-governor’, the commandant of a fortress.<BR>—2 the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरमथनः|पुरमथन
पुर + -मथनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरमार्गः|पुरमार्ग
पुर + -मार्गः the street of a town; पुरमार्गे घनशब्दविक्लवाः<BR> Ku. 4. 11; R. 11. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररक्षः|पुररक्ष
पुर + -रक्षः, -रक्षकः, -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a constable, police-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररक्षकः|पुररक्षक
पुर + -रक्षः, -रक्षकः, -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a constable, police-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररक्षिन्
पुर + -रक्षः, -रक्षकः, -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a constable, police-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुररोधः|पुररोध
पुर + -रोधः the siege of a fortress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवासिन्
पुर + -वासिन् <i>m.</i> a citizen, a townsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवास्तु
पुर + -वास्तु <i>n.</i> ground fit for the foundation of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरशासनः|पुरशासन
पुर + -शासनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Śiva; प्रसाधनं मातृभिरादृताभिर्न्यस्तं पुरस्तात् पुरशासनस्य Ku. 7. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरहन्
पुर + -हन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जनः|पुरञ्जन|पुरंजन|पुरंजनः
पुरञ्जनः<BR>—1 The soul.<BR>—2 N. of Hari; जपयज्ञेन तपसा पुरञ्जनमतोषयन् Bhāg. 4. 30. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जनी
पुरञ्जनः + .{@-नी@} Intellect, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंदरः|पुरन्दर|पुरंदर|पुरन्दरं|पुरन्दरः
पुरंदरः [पुरः शत्रूणां नगराणि दारयति खच्]<BR>—1 N. of Indra; पुरन्दरश्रीः पुरमुत्पताकं प्रविश्य पौरैरभिनन्द्यमानः R. 2. 74.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Agni.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 N. of the eighteenth lunar mansion (ज्येष्ठा).<BR>—6 A thief, house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंदरा
पुरंदरः + .{@-रा@} An epithet of the Ganges.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरंदरक्ष्माधरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंदरक्ष्माधरः
पुरंदरः + -क्ष्माधरः (= महेन्द्रपर्वतः); तया समेतः सपुरं पुरन्दरः<BR> पुरन्दरक्ष्माधरसुन्दरं भुवः Rām. Ch. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंजरः|पुरञ्जर
पुरंजरः The arm-pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरटम्
पुरटम् Gold; अङ्गुष्ठमात्रममलं स्फुरत् पुरटमौलिनम् Bhāg. 1. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरणः|पुरण
पुरणः The sea, ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतस्
पुरतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Before, in front (opp. पश्चात्); पश्यामि तामित इतः पुरतश्च<BR> पश्चात् Māl. 1. 40; in the presence of; यं यं पश्यसि तस्य तस्य<BR> पुरतो मा ब्रूहि दीनं वचः Bh. 2. 51.<BR>—2 Afterwards; इयं च तेऽन्या पुरतो विडम्बना Ku. 5. 70 (आदावेव<BR> Malli.); Amaru. 43.<BR>—3 Before (in time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंध्रिः|पुरन्ध्रि|पुरंध्रि|पुरन्ध्रिः
पुरंध्रिः, -ध्री <i>f.</i><BR> [पुरं गेहस्थजनं धारयति धृ-खच् ङीप् पृषो˚ वा ह्रस्वः Tv.]<BR>—1 An elderly married woman, a respectable matron; पुरंध्रीणां चित्तं<BR> कुसुमसुकुमारं हि भवति U. 4. 12; Mu. 2. 7; Ku. 6. 32, 7. 2.<BR>—2 A woman whose husband and children are living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंध्री
पुरंध्रिः, -ध्री <i>f.</i><BR> [पुरं गेहस्थजनं धारयति धृ-खच् ङीप् पृषो˚ वा ह्रस्वः Tv.]<BR>—1 An elderly married woman, a respectable matron; पुरंध्रीणां चित्तं<BR> कुसुमसुकुमारं हि भवति U. 4. 12; Mu. 2. 7; Ku. 6. 32, 7. 2.<BR>—2 A woman whose husband and children are living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरंध्रिका
पुरंध्रिका <i>f.</i> wife; एकोजि-भूमीपतिशेखरस्य पुरंध्रिका गर्भमधत्त<BR> भव्यम् Śāhendra. 1. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरला
पुरला An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्
पुरस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Before (in time or space), in front, in the presence of, before the<BR> eyes of (by itself or with gen.); अमुं पुरः पश्यसि देवदारुम् R. 2. 36;<BR> तव प्रसादस्य पुरस्तु संपदः Ś. 7. 30; तस्य स्थित्वा कथमपि<BR> पुरः Me. 3; Ku. 4. 3; Amaru. 43; often used with कृ, गम्, धा, भू (see below).<BR>—2 In the east, from the east.<BR>—3 Eastward.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरोनुवाक्या, पुरःकरणम्, पुरःकारः, पुरोग, पुरोगम, पुरोगत, पुरोगतिः, पुरोगन्तृ, पुरोगामिन्, पुरश्चरणम्, पुरश्छदः, पुरोजन्मन्, पुरोजव, पुरोवः, पुरोडाश्, पुरःपाक, पुरःप्रहर्तृ, पुरःफल, पुरोभाग, पुरोभागिन्, पुरोमारुतः, पुरोवातः, पुरोवर्तिन्, पुरस्सर,^1 पुरःस्थायिन्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोनुवाक्या
पुरस् + -अनुवाक्या (पुरोऽनुवाक्या) an introductory verse or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःकरणम्
पुरस् + -करणम्, -कारः see under पुरस्कृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःकारः
पुरस् + -करणम्, -कारः see under पुरस्कृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोग|पुरोगः
पुरस् + -ग, -गम (पुरोग, -गम) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 chief, leading, foremost, pre-eminent, oft. with the force of a noun;<BR> स किंवदन्तीं वदतां पुरोगः R. 14. 31, 6. 55; Ku. 7. 40.<BR>—2 led or presided over by (at the end of comp.); इन्द्रपुरोगमा देवाः<BR> ‘the gods with Indra at the head’; अतुलाः प्रीतयो राजन् संबन्धकपुरोगमाः<BR> Rām. 7. 38. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगम|पुरोगमः
पुरस् + -ग, -गम (पुरोग, -गम) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 chief, leading, foremost, pre-eminent, oft. with the force of a noun;<BR> स किंवदन्तीं वदतां पुरोगः R. 14. 31, 6. 55; Ku. 7. 40.<BR>—2 led or presided over by (at the end of comp.); इन्द्रपुरोगमा देवाः<BR> ‘the gods with Indra at the head’; अतुलाः प्रीतयो राजन् संबन्धकपुरोगमाः<BR> Rām. 7. 38. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगत
पुरस् + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 standing in front of.<BR>—2 preceded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगतिः|पुरोगति
पुरस् + -गतिः <i>f.</i> precedence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगतिः|पुरोगति
पुरस् + -गतिः + .({@-तिः@}) a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगन्तृ
पुरस् + -गन्तृ, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going before or in front.<BR>—2 chief, leading, a leader. ━(<i>m.</i>) a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगामिन्
पुरस् + -गन्तृ, -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going before or in front.<BR>—2 chief, leading, a leader. ━(<i>m.</i>) a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्चरणम्
पुरस् + -चरणम् (पुरश्चरणम्)<BR>—1 a preparatory or initiatory rite.<BR>—2 preparation, initiation.<BR>—3 repetition of the name of a deity accompanied with burnt offerings;<BR> जीवहीनो यथा देही सर्वकर्मसु न क्षमः । पुरश्चरणहीनोऽपि तथा<BR> मन्त्रः प्रकीर्तितः ॥ Tantrasāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्छदः|पुरश्छद
पुरस् + -छदः (पुरश्छदः) a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोजन्मन्
पुरस् + -जन्मन् (पुरोजन्मन्) <i>a.</i> born before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोजव
पुरस् + -जव <i>a.</i> (पुरोजव)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">Page1032-1</a>]<BR> surpassing in speed, swifter than.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1031-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवः
पुरस् + -वः a servant, attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश्
पुरस् + -डाश् <i>m.</i>, {@-डाशः@} (पुरोडाश्, -शः)<BR>—1 a sacrificial oblation made of ground rice and offered in <i>kapālas</i><BR> or vessels; पुरोडाशांश्चरूंश्चैव विधिवन्निर्वपेत् पृथक् Ms. 6. 11.<BR>—2 an oblation in general; Ms. 7. 21.<BR>—3 an oblation of ghee with cakes of ground meal.<BR>—4 a kind of sacrificial ladle.<BR>—5 the leavings of an oblation (हुतशेष).<BR>—6 the Soma juice.<BR>—7 a prayer (मन्त्र) recited in offering oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःपाक
पुरस् + -पाक <i>a.</i> near fulfilment, about to be fulfilled; आशीर्भिरेधयामासुः<BR> पुरःपाकाभिरम्बिकाम् Ku. 6. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःप्रहर्तृ
पुरस् + -प्रहर्तृ <i>m.</i> one who fights in the van or frontline; पौलस्त्य<BR> एष समरेषु पुरःप्रहर्ता R. 13. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःफल
पुरस् + -फल <i>a.</i> having the fruit near or at hand, promising fruit<BR> (in the near future); भक्त्योपपन्नेषु हि तद्विधानां प्रसादचिह्नानि पुरःफलानि R. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभाग|पुरोभागः
पुरस् + -भाग (पुरोभाग) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 obtrusive, officious; किमिदानीं पुरोभागामद्य त्वं नाभिभाषसे Rām. 4. 20. 4.<BR>—2 fault-finding.<BR>—3 envious or jealous of; प्रायः समानविद्याः परस्परयशःपुरोभागाः<BR> M. 1. 20 (पुरोभाग may here mean ‘envy’ also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभागः|पुरोभाग
पुरस् + -भाग + .({@-गः@})<BR>—1 the front part, forepart, van.<BR>—2 obtrusiveness, officiousness.<BR>—3 jealousy, envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभागिन्
पुरस् + -भागिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 forward, self-willed, naughty; किं पुरोभागिनि स्वातन्त्र्यमवलम्बसे Ś. 5.<BR>—2 obtrusive, officious; V. 3.<BR>—3 fault-finding.<BR>—4 envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोमारुतः|पुरोमारुत
पुरस् + -मारुतः, -वातः (पुरोमारुतः, -वातः) a fore-wind, wind<BR> blowing in front; कोटरमकालवृष्टपा प्रबलपुरोवातया गमिते M. 4. 2;<BR> R. 18. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवातः|पुरोवात
पुरस् + -मारुतः, -वातः (पुरोमारुतः, -वातः) a fore-wind, wind<BR> blowing in front; कोटरमकालवृष्टपा प्रबलपुरोवातया गमिते M. 4. 2;<BR> R. 18. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोवर्तिन्
पुरस् + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i> being in front or in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्सर
पुरस् + -सर^1 <i>a.</i> going or moving in front.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःसरः|पुरःसर
पुरस् + -सरः + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a forerunner, harbinger; आविष्कृतोऽरुणपुरःसर एकतोऽर्कः Ś. 4. 2.<BR>—2 a follower, attendant; servant; ऊचुर्निषोधितास्तांस्ते वैवस्वतपुरःसराः<BR> Bhāg. 6. 1. 32; परिमेयपुरःसरौ R. 1. 37.<BR>—3 a leader, one who leads the way, foremost, pre-eminent; गगनादवतीर्णा<BR> सा यथावृद्धपुरःसरा Ku. 6. 49.<BR>—4 (at the end of comp.) attended or preceded by, with; as मानपुरःसरम्,<BR> प्रणामपुरःसरम्, वृकपुरःसराः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःसरम्
पुरस् + -सरः + .({@-रम्@}) <i>ind.</i> with or after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःस्थायिन्
पुरस् + -स्थायिन् <i>a.</i> standing in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कृ
पुरस्कृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To place before or in front, make oneʼs leader, put at the head; हते<BR> जरति गाङ्गेये पुरस्कृत्य शिखण्डिनम् Ve. 2. 4; U. 1. 3; Ku. 2. 52.<BR>—2 To introduce, present; मद्वचनात् स राजा शकुन्तलां पुरस्कृत्य वक्तव्यः Ś. 4, 7.<BR>—3 To honour, respect, esteem, hospitably receive or entertain; दर्शनेनैव<BR> भवतीनां पुरस्कृतोऽस्मि Ś. 1.<BR>—4 To adopt, choose, follow; स पुरस्कृतमध्यमक्रमः R. 8. 9.<BR>—5 To appoint.<BR>—6 To show, indicate, evince.<BR>—7 To lead.<BR>—8 To use as a pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करणम्
पुरस्करणम् The act of placing in front, honouring &c.; see पुरस्कार below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करणीय
पुरस्करणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be honoured.<BR>—2 To be placed at the head.<BR>—3 To be made complete &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कारः|पुरस्कार
पुरस्कारः<BR>—1 Placing before or in front.<BR>—2 Preference.<BR>—3 Treating with honour, showing respect, deference.<BR>—4 Worshipping.<BR>—5 Accompanying, attending.<BR>—6 Preparing.<BR>—7 Arranging, making complete<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">Page1032-2</a>]<BR> or perfect.<BR>—8 Attacking.<BR>—9 Accusation.<BR>—10 Consecrating<BR>—11 Anticipating, expecting.<BR>—12 (At the end of comp.) Preceded or accompanied by.<BR>—13 Sprinkling with holy water.<BR>—14 Acceptance.<BR>—15 Manifesting oneself; कर्महेतुपुरस्कारं भूतेषु परिवर्तते Mb. 12. 19. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कृत|पुरस्कृतः
पुरस्कृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed in front; पुरस्कृता वर्त्मनि पार्थिवेन R. 2. 20.<BR>—2 Honoured, treated with respect, distinguished.<BR>—3 Chosen, adopted, followed.<BR>—4 Adored, worshipped.<BR>—5 Attended or accompanied, provided with, possessing, having.<BR>—6 Prepared, got ready.<BR>—7 Consecrated.<BR>—8 Accused, calumniated.<BR>—9 Made perfect or complete, finished.<BR>—10 Anticipated, expected.<BR>—11 Appointed.<BR>—12 Harassed or attacked (by an enemy).<BR>—13 Sprinkled with holy water.<BR>—14 Initiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कृत्य
पुरस्कृत्य <i>ind.</i> Regarding, concerning, on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्क्रिया
पुरस्क्रिया<BR>—1 Showing respect, honouring, hospitable reception.<BR>—2 A preparatory or initiatory rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्तात्
पुरस्तात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Before, in front of (oft. with gen. or abl.); गुरोरपीदं धनमाहिताग्नेर्नश्यत्<BR> पुरस्तादनुपेक्षणीयम् R. 2. 44; Ku. 7. 30; Me. 15; or used by itself;<BR> अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तात् Ś. 3. 7.<BR>—2 At the head of, foremost; यः पुरस्ताद् यतीनाम् M. 1. 1.<BR>—3 In the first place, at the beginning; पुरस्ताद् दारुणो भूत्वा Mb. 12. 152. 2.<BR>—4 Formerly, previously.<BR>—5 Eastward, in or towards the east; द्यां निरुन्धदतिनीलघनाभं ध्वान्तमुद्यतकरेण<BR> पुरस्तात् Ki. 9. 20.<BR>—6 Later or further on, in the sequel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधा
पुरोधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place or put in the front or at the head, make as a leader; तुरासाहं<BR> पुरोधाय धाम स्वायंभुवं ययुः Ku. 2. 1; R. 12. 43.<BR>—2 To make a family-priest of any one.<BR>—3 To appoint, place in office.<BR>—4 To entrust or charge with.<BR>—5 To place or set before or in front to.<BR>—6 To honour, esteem, respect.<BR>—7 To devote or apply oneself to.<BR>—8 To think, ponder over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधस्
पुरोधस् <i>m.</i> A family-priest (particularly that of a king.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधा
पुरोधा<BR>—1 The office of a <i>purohita</i>.<BR>—2 Charge, commission.<BR>—3 Representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधानम्
पुरोधानम्<BR>—1 Placing in front.<BR>—2 Ministration by a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधिका
पुरोधिका, पुरोहितिका A favourite wife (preferred to all others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहितिका
पुरोधिका, पुरोहितिका A favourite wife (preferred to all others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभक्तका
पुरोभक्तका Breakfast; Divyāvadāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहित|पुरोहितः
पुरोहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed in front.<BR>—2 Appointed, charged, entrusted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहितः|पुरोहित
पुरोहित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 One charged with a business, an agent.<BR>—2 A family-priest, one who conducts all the ceremonial rites of the family.<BR> मन्त्रिपुरोहितसखः (राजा); … … … अमात्यानुपधाभिः शौचयेत्<BR> Kau. A. 1. 10; पुरोहितो हितो वेदस्मृतिज्ञः सत्यवाक् शुचिः Kavikalpalatā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1032-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरा
पुरा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In former times, formerly, of yore, in the olden time; पुरा शक्रमुपस्थाय<BR> R. 1. 75; पुरा सरसि मानसे … यस्य यातं वयः Bv. 1. 3; Ms. 1. 119, 5. 22.<BR>—2 Before, hitherto, upto the present time<BR>—3 At first, in the first place; रामं दर्शय मे शीघ्रं पुरा मेऽर्थोऽतिवर्तते<BR> Rām. 7. 105. 2.<BR>—4 In a short time, soon, ere-long, shortly (in this sense usually with<BR> a present tense to which it gives a future sense); पुरा सप्तद्वीपां<BR> जयति वसुधामप्रतिरथः Ś. 7. 33; पुरा दूषयति स्थलीम् R. 12. 30;<BR> आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला वा Me. 87; N. 1. 18; Śi. 10. 56;<BR> Ki. 10. 50, 11. 36.<BR>—5 Ved. For the defence of.<BR>—6 Securely from.<BR>—7 Except, besides.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरोपनीत, पुराकथा, पुराकल्पः, पुराकृत्, पुरायोनि, पुरावसुः, पुराविद्, पुरावृत्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोपनीत
पुरा + -उपनीत <i>a.</i> formerly possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकथा
पुरा + -कथा an old legend; को नाम लोके पुरुषार्थसारवित् पुराकथानां<BR> भगवत्कथासुधाम् Bhāg. 3. 13. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकल्पः|पुराकल्प
पुरा + -कल्पः<BR>—1 a former creation; सिद्धसंघपरिज्ञातं पुराकल्पं सनातनम् Mb. 14. 35. 23.<BR>—2 a story of the past.<BR>—3 a former age; द्यूतमेतत् पुराकल्पे दृष्टं वैरकरं महत् Ms. 9. 227;<BR> Mb. 3. 41. 35.<BR>—4 A passage descriptive of past events; MS. 6. 7. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकृत्
पुरा + -कृत् <i>a.</i> done formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरात्कृतम्
पुरा + -कृत् + .({@-तम्@}) actions done in a former life; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरायोनि|पुरायोनिः
पुरा + -योनि <i>a.</i> of ancient origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरायोनिः|पुरायोनि
पुरा + -योनि + .({@-निः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावसुः|पुरावसु
पुरा + -वसुः an epithot of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराविद्
पुरा + -विद् <i>a.</i> acquainted with the past, knowing the events of former<BR> times, conversant with former times or events; वदन्त्यपर्णेति च तां<BR> पुराविदः Ku. 5. 28, 6. 9; R. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्त|पुरावृत्तं
पुरा + -वृत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 occurring in, or relating to, ancient times.<BR>—2 old, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्तम्
पुरा + -वृत्त + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 history.<BR>—2 an old or legendary event; पुरावृत्तोद्गारैरपि च कथिता कार्यपदवी<BR> Māl. 2. 13. ˚कथा an old legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातन|पुरातनः
पुरातन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Old, ancient; बहिर्विकारं प्रकृतेः परं विदुः पुरातनं त्वां पुरुषं<BR> पुराविदः Śi. 12. 60; स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः Bg. 4. 3.<BR>—2 Aged, primeval; त्वां न वेद्मि पुरुषं पुरातनम् R. 11. 85; Ku. 6. 9.<BR>—3 Worn out, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातनः|पुरातन
पुरातन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 (pl.) The ancients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातनम्
पुरातन + .{@-नः@} + .({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 An ancient story.<BR>—2 A Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरा
पुरा<BR>—1 An epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—2 A kind of perfume.<BR>—3 The east. —4 A castle. See पुरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण <i>a.</i> (-णा, -णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुरा नवम् Nir.]<BR>—1 Old, ancient, belonging to olden times; पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वं<BR> न चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम् M. 1. 2; पुराणपत्रापगमादनन्तरम् R. 3. 7<BR>—2 Aged, primeval; गृध्रराजः पुराणोऽसौ श्वशुरस्य सखा मम Rām. 3. 53. 5;<BR> अजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणः Bg. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Decayed, worn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणम्
पुराण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 A past event or occurrence.<BR>—2 tale of the past, legend, ancient or legendary history.<BR>—3 N. of certain well-known sacred works; these are 18; these are supposed<BR> to have been composed by Vyāsa, and contain the whole body of Hindu mythology.<BR> A Purāṇa treats of five topics (or लक्षणानि), and is hence often<BR> called पञ्चलक्षण; सर्गश्च प्रतिसर्गश्च वंशो मन्वन्तराणि च ।<BR> वंशानुचरितं चैव पुराणं पञ्चलक्षणम् ॥ For the names of the 18<BR> Purāṇas see under अष्टादशन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणः|पुराण|पुराणं
पुराण + .{@-णः@} A coin equal to 80 cowries; ते षोडश स्याद् धरणं पुराणश्चैव<BR> राजतः Ms. 8. 136.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुराणान्तः, पुराणोक्त, पुराणकल्पः, पुराणगः, पुराणपुरुषः, पुराणप्रोक्त, पुराणविद्या, पुराणवेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणान्तः|पुराणान्त|पुराणांत
पुराण + -अन्तः an epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणोक्त
पुराण + -उक्त <i>a.</i> enjoined by or laid down in the Purāṇas.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">Page1033-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणकल्पः|पुराणकल्प
पुराण + -कल्पः = पुराकल्प q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणगः|पुराणग
पुराण + -गः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 a reciter or reader of the Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणपुरुषः|पुराणपुरुष
पुराण + -पुरुषः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 an old man; यद् वदन्ति चपलेत्यपवादं तन्न दूषणमहो चपलायाः ।<BR> दोष एष जलधेः पितुरस्या यत् पुराणपुरुषाय ददौ ताम् Subhāṣ.;<BR> (where both senses are intended).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणप्रोक्त
पुराण + -प्रोक्त <i>a.</i> proclaimed by ancient sages; P. IV. 3. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणविद्या
पुराण + -विद्या, -वेदः knowledge of the past events.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणवेदः|पुराणवेद
पुराण + -विद्या, -वेदः knowledge of the past events.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराषाट्
पुराषाट् (Ved.) Vanquisher of many; यद्वावान पुरुतमं पुराषाळा<BR> वृत्रहेन्द्रो नामान्यप्राः Rv. 10. 74. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरिः|पुरि
पुरिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A town, city.<BR>—2 A river.<BR>—3 A king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरिशय
पुरिशय <i>a.</i> Reposing in the body; स वा अयं पुरुषः सर्वासु<BR> पूर्षु पुरिशयः Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 18; Praśna. Up. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरी
पुरी<BR>—1 A city, town; शशासैकपुरीमिव R. 1. 30; पुरीमवस्कन्द लुनीहि<BR> नन्दनम् Śi. 1. 51.<BR>—2 A stronghold.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरीमोहः, पुरीलोकाः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीमोहः|पुरीमोह
पुरी + -मोहः the Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीलोकाः
पुरी + -लोकाः townʼs folk, citizens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीतत्
पुरीतत् <i>m., n.</i> [पुरीं देहं तनोति तन् क्विप्]<BR>—1 A particular intestine near the heart; यदा मनः पुरीतति प्रविशति<BR> T. S.; यदा सुप्तो न कंचन वेद हिता नाम नाड्यो द्वासप्ततिः सहस्राणि<BR> हृदयात् पुरीततमभिप्रतिष्ठन्ते ताभिः प्रत्यवसृप्य पुरीतति शेते ŚB. on MS.;<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 19.<BR>—2 The entrails in general; (also पुरितत्, but it appears to be a wrong form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषम्
पुरीषम् [पॄ-ईषन् किच्च Uṇ. 4. 27]<BR>—1 Feces, excrement, ordure; तस्याः पुरीषे तन्मांसं पितरस्तस्य शेरते<BR> Ms. 3. 250, 4. 56, 5. 123, 6. 76.<BR>—2 Rubbish, dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीष्यम्
पुरीषम् + .{@-ष्यम्@} excremental dirt; द्रवत्पुरीष्याः पुलिनैः समन्ततः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 18. 6.<BR>—3 Ved. Water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरीषाधानम्, पुरीषोत्सर्गः, पुरीषनिग्रहणम्, पुरीषभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषाधानम्
पुरीषम् + -आधानम् the rectum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषोत्सर्गः|पुरीषोत्सर्ग
पुरीषम् + -उत्सर्गः voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषनिग्रहणम्
पुरीषम् + -निग्रहणम् obstruction of the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषभेदः|पुरीषभेद
पुरीषम् + -भेदः diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषणः|पुरीषण
पुरीषणः Feces, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषणम्
पुरीषणः + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Evacuation by stool, voiding of excrement.<BR>—2 The rectum or anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषयति
पुरीषयति Den. P. To void excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषित
पुरीषित <i>a.</i> Voided, evacuated (as the bowels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषमः|पुरीषम
पुरीषमः The black kidney-bean (Mar. उडीद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरु|पुरुः
पुरु <i>a.</i> (-रु, -र्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पृ-पालनपोषणयोः कु; Uṇ. 1. 24] Much,<BR> abundant, excessive, many; (in classical literature पुरु occurs usually<BR> at the beginning of proper names); इन्द्रो मायाभिः पुरुरूप ईयते Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 19;<BR> स्त्रीणां प्रियतमो नित्यं मत्तस्तु पुरुलम्पटः Bhāg. 7. 15. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुः|पुरु
पुरु + .{@-रुः@}<BR>—1 The pollen of flowers.<BR>—2 Heaven, the world of the immortals.<BR>—3 N. of a demon killed by Indra.<BR>—4 N. of a prince, the sixth monarch of the lunar race. [He was the youngest<BR> son of Yayāti and Śarmiṣṭhā. When Yayāti asked his five sons if<BR> any one of them would exchange his youth and beauty for his own decrepitude<BR> and infirmities, it was Puru alone who consented to make the exchange.<BR> After a thousand years Yayāti restored to Puru his youth and beauty<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">Page1034-1</a>]<BR> and made him successor to the throne. Puru was the ancestor of the Kauravas<BR> and Pāṇḍavas.] ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Much, exceedingly.<BR>—2 Repeatedly, often.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरुकृत, पुरुकृत्वन्, पुरुजित्, पुरुदम्, पुरुदंशकः, पुरुदंश, पुरुदंस, पुरुदंसस्, पुरुदत्रः, पुरुद्रुह्, पुरुनिष्ठ, पुरुप्रौढ, पुरुभोजस्, पुरुलम्पट, पुरुह, पुरुहु, पुरुहूत, पुरुहूतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1033-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुकृत
पुरु + -कृत, -कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुकृत्वन्
पुरु + -कृत, -कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुजित्
पुरु + -जित् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of king Kuntibhoja or his brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदम्
पुरु + -दम् gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंशकः|पुरुदंशक
पुरु + -दंशकः a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंश
पुरु + -दंश, -दंस, -दंसस्, -दत्रः, -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंस
पुरु + -दंश, -दंस, -दंसस्, -दत्रः, -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंसस्
पुरु + -दंश, -दंस, -दंसस्, -दत्रः, -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदत्रः|पुरुदत्र
पुरु + -दंश, -दंस, -दंसस्, -दत्रः, -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुद्रुह्
पुरु + -दंश, -दंस, -दंसस्, -दत्रः, -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> epithets of Indra (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुनिष्ठ
पुरु + -निष्ठ <i>a.</i> excelling among many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुप्रौढ
पुरु + -प्रौढ <i>a.</i> possessing much self-confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुभोजस्
पुरु + -भोजस् <i>m.</i> a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुलम्पट|पुरुलंपट
पुरु + -लम्पट <i>a.</i> very lustful or lascivious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुह|पुरुहं
पुरु + -ह, -हु much, many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहु
पुरु + -ह, -हु much, many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूत|पुरुहूतः
पुरु + -हूत <i>a.</i> invoked by many; प्रादुश्चकर्थ यदिदं पुरुहूतरूपम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 15. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूतः|पुरुहूत
पुरु + -हूत + .({@-तः@}) an epithet of Indra; पुरुहूतध्वजः R. 4. 3, 16. 5;<BR> पुरुहूतमुख्याः (लोकपालाः) Ku. 7. 45; Ms. 11. 122. ˚द्विष् <i>m.</i><BR> an epithet of Indrajit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूतिः|पुरुहूति
पुरु + -हूतिः <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu. ━<i>f.</i> manifold invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुवी
पुरुवी N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषः|पुरुष
पुरुषः [पुरि देहे शेते शी-ड पृषो˚ Tv.; पुर्-अग्रगमने कुषन् Uṇ. 4. 74]<BR>—1 A male being, man; अर्थतः पुरुषो नारी या नारी सार्थतः पुमान् Mk. 3. 27;<BR> Ms. 1. 32, 7. 17, 9. 2; R. 2. 41.<BR>—2 Men, mankind.<BR>—3 A member or representative of a generation.<BR>—4 An officer, functionary, agent, attendant, servant.<BR>—5 The height or measure of a man (considered as a measure of length);<BR> द्वौ पुरुषौ प्रमाणमस्य सा द्विपुरुषा-षी परिखा Sk.<BR>—6 The Soul; द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ लोके क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च Bg. 15. 16 &c.<BR>—7 The Supreme Being, God (soul of the universe); पुरातनं त्वां पुरुषं<BR> पुराविदः (विदुः) Śi. 1. 33; R. 13. 6.<BR>—8 A person (in grammar); प्रथमपुरुषः the third person, मध्यमपुरुषः<BR> the second person, and उत्तमपुरुषः the first person, (this is the<BR> strict order in Sk.).<BR>—9 The pupil of the eye.<BR>—10 (In Sāṅ. phil.) The soul (opp. प्रकृति); according to the Sāṅkhyas<BR> it is neither a production nor productive; it is passive and a looker-on<BR> of the Prakṛti; cf. त्वामामनन्ति प्रकृतिं पुरुषार्थप्रवर्तिनीम् Ku. 2. 13<BR> and the word सांख्य also.<BR>—11 The soul, the original source of the universe (described in the पुरुषसूक्त);<BR> सहस्रशीर्षः पुरुषः सहस्राक्षः सहस्रपात् &c.<BR>—12 The Punnāga tree.<BR>—13 N. of the first, third, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh signs of the zodiac.<BR>—14 The seven divine or active principles of which the universe was formed;<BR> तेषामिदं तु सप्तानां पुरुषाणां महौजसाम् Ms. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषी
पुरुषः + .{@-षी@} A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषम्
पुरुषः + .{@-षम्@} An epithet of the mountain Meru.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुरुषाङ्गम्, पुरुषादः, पुरुषाद्, पुरुषाधमः, पुरुषाधिकारः, पुरुषान्तरम्, पुरुषायणः, पुरुषार्थः, पुरुषास्थिमालिन्, पुरुषाद्यः, पुरुषायुषम्, पुरुषायुस्, पुरुषाशिन्, पुरुषेन्द्रः, पुरुषोत्तमः, पुरुषकारः, पुरुषकुणपः, पुरुषकुणपम्, पुरुषकेसरिन्, पुरुषज्ञानम्, पुरुषतन्त्र, पुरुषदध्न, पुरुषद्वयस्, पुरुषद्विष्, पुरुषद्वेषिणी, पुरुषनाथः, पुरुषनियमः, पुरुषपशुः, पुरुषपुङ्गवः, पुरुषपुण्डरीकः, पुरुषपुरम्, पुरुषबहुमानः, पुरुषमानिन्, पुरुषमेधः, पुरुषवरः, पुरुषवर्जित, पुरुषवाहः, पुरुषव्याघ्रः, पुरुषशार्दूलः, पुरुषसिंहः, पुरुषसमवायः, पुरुषशीर्षकः, पुरुषसारः, पुरुषसूक्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाङ्गम्
पुरुषः + -अङ्गम् the male organ of generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषादः|पुरुषाद
पुरुषः + -अदः, -अद् <i>m.</i> ‘a man-eater’, cannibal, goblin; अवमेने हि<BR> दुर्बुद्धिर्मनुष्यान् पुरुषादकः Mb. 3. 275. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाद्
पुरुषः + -अदः, -अद् <i>m.</i> ‘a man-eater’, cannibal, goblin; अवमेने हि<BR> दुर्बुद्धिर्मनुष्यान् पुरुषादकः Mb. 3. 275. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाधमः|पुरुषाधम
पुरुषः + -अधमः the vilest of men, a very low or despicable man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाधिकारः|पुरुषाधिकार
पुरुषः + -अधिकारः<BR>—1 a manly office or duty.<BR>—2 calculation or estimation of men; संसत्सु जाते पुरुषाधिकारे न पूरणी<BR> तं समुपैति संख्या Ki. 3. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषान्तरम्
पुरुषः + -अन्तरम् another man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायणः|पुरुषायण
पुरुषः + -अयणः, -अर्थः<BR>—1 any one of the four principal objects of human life; <i>i. e.</i> धर्म<BR> अर्थ, काम and मोक्ष.<BR>—2 human effort or exertion (पुरुषकार); धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाश्च पुरुषार्था<BR> उदाहृताः Agni P.; H. Pr. 35.<BR>—3 something which when done results in the satisfaction of the performer;<BR> यस्मिन् कृते पदार्थे पुरुषस्य प्रीतिर्भवति स पुरुषार्थः पदार्थः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">Page1034-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषार्थः|पुरुषार्थ
पुरुषः + -अयणः, -अर्थः<BR>—1 any one of the four principal objects of human life; <i>i. e.</i> धर्म<BR> अर्थ, काम and मोक्ष.<BR>—2 human effort or exertion (पुरुषकार); धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाश्च पुरुषार्था<BR> उदाहृताः Agni P.; H. Pr. 35.<BR>—3 something which when done results in the satisfaction of the performer;<BR> यस्मिन् कृते पदार्थे पुरुषस्य प्रीतिर्भवति स पुरुषार्थः पदार्थः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">Page1034-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषास्थिमालिन्
पुरुषः + -अस्थिमालिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाद्यः|पुरुषाद्य
पुरुषः + -आद्यः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायुषम्
पुरुषः + -आयुषम्, -आयुस् <i>n.</i> the duration of a manʼs life; अकृपणमतिः<BR> कामं जीव्याज्जनः पुरुषायुषम् Ve. 6. 44; पुरुषायुषजीविन्यो निरातङ्का<BR> निरीतयः R. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायुस्
पुरुषः + -आयुषम्, -आयुस् <i>n.</i> the duration of a manʼs life; अकृपणमतिः<BR> कामं जीव्याज्जनः पुरुषायुषम् Ve. 6. 44; पुरुषायुषजीविन्यो निरातङ्का<BR> निरीतयः R. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाशिन्
पुरुषः + -आशिन् <i>m.</i> ‘a man-eater’, a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषेन्द्रः|पुरुषेन्द्र|पुरुषेंद्र
पुरुषः + -इन्द्रः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोत्तमः|पुरुषोत्तम
पुरुषः + -उत्तमः<BR>—1 an excellent man.<BR>—2 the highest or Supreme Being, an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; यस्मात्<BR> क्षरमतीतोऽहमक्षरादपि चोत्तमः । अतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः ॥<BR> Bg. 15. 18.<BR>—3 a best attendant.<BR>—4 a Jaina. —5 N. of a district in Orissa sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकारः|पुरुषकार
पुरुषः + -कारः<BR>—1 human effort or exertion, manly act, manliness, prowess (opp. दैव);<BR> एवं पुरुषकारेण विना दैवं न सिध्यति H. Pr. 32; दैवे पुरुषकारे<BR> च कर्मसिद्धिर्व्यवस्थिता Y. 1. 349; cf. ‘god helps those who help themselves’;<BR> अभिमतसिद्धिरशेषा भवति हि पुरुषस्य पुरुषकारेण Pt. 5. 30; Ki. 5. 52.<BR>—2 manhood, virility.<BR>—3 haughtiness, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकुणपः|पुरुषकुणप
पुरुषः + -कुणपः, -कुणपम् a human corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकुणपम्
पुरुषः + -कुणपः, -कुणपम् a human corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकेसरिन्
पुरुषः + -केसरिन् <i>m.</i> man-lion, an epithet of Viṣṇu in his fourth<BR> incarnation; पुरुषकेसरिणश्च पुरा नखैः Ś. 7. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषज्ञानम्
पुरुषः + -ज्ञानम् knowledge of mankind; Ms. 7. 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषतन्त्र
पुरुषः + -तन्त्र <i>a.</i> subjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषदध्न
पुरुषः + -दध्न, -द्वयस् <i>a.</i> of the height of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्वयस्
पुरुषः + -दध्न, -द्वयस् <i>a.</i> of the height of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्विष्
पुरुषः + -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an enemy of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्वेषिणी
पुरुषः + -द्वेषिणी an ill-tempered woman (who hates her husband).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषनाथः|पुरुषनाथ
पुरुषः + -नाथः<BR>—1 a general, commander.<BR>—2 a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषनियमः|पुरुषनियम
पुरुषः + -नियमः (in gram.) a restriction to a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपशुः|पुरुषपशु
पुरुषः + -पशुः a beast of a man, brutish person; cf. नरपशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

