पुरुषः + -पुङ्गवः, -पुण्डरीकः a superior or eminent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुण्डरीकः|पुरुषपुण्डरीक|पुरुषपुंडरीक
पुरुषः + -पुङ्गवः, -पुण्डरीकः a superior or eminent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुरम्
पुरुषः + -पुरम् N. of the capital of Gāndhāra, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषबहुमानः|पुरुषबहुमान
पुरुषः + -बहुमानः the esteem of mankind; निवृत्ता भोगेच्छा पुरुषबहुमानो<BR> विगलितः Bh. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमानिन्
पुरुषः + -मानिन् <i>a.</i> fancying oneself a hero; कथं पुरुषमानी स्यात्<BR> पुरुषाणां मयि स्थिते Rām. 2. 24. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमेधः|पुरुषमेध
पुरुषः + -मेधः a human sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवरः|पुरुषवर
पुरुषः + -वरः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवर्जित
पुरुषः + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> desolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवाहः|पुरुषवाह
पुरुषः + -वाहः<BR>—1 an epithet of Garuḍa. —2 an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषव्याघ्रः|पुरुषव्याघ्र
पुरुषः + -व्याघ्रः, -शार्दूलः, -सिंहः ‘a tiger or lion among men’, a distinguished<BR> or eminent man. उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति लक्ष्मीः H.<BR>—2 a hero, brave man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषशार्दूलः|पुरुषशार्दूल|पुरुषशार्द्दूल
पुरुषः + -व्याघ्रः, -शार्दूलः, -सिंहः ‘a tiger or lion among men’, a distinguished<BR> or eminent man. उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति लक्ष्मीः H.<BR>—2 a hero, brave man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसिंहः|पुरुषसिंह
पुरुषः + -व्याघ्रः, -शार्दूलः, -सिंहः ‘a tiger or lion among men’, a distinguished<BR> or eminent man. उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति लक्ष्मीः H.<BR>—2 a hero, brave man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसमवायः|पुरुषसमवाय
पुरुषः + -समवायः a number of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषशीर्षकः|पुरुषशीर्षक
पुरुषः + -शीर्षकः A kind of weapon used by burglars (a sham head to be<BR> inserted into the hole made in a wall); Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसारः
पुरुषः + -सारः an eminent man; Bhāg. 10. 16. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसूक्तम्
पुरुषः + -सूक्तम् N. of the 90th hymn of the 10th Maṇḍala of the Ṛgveda<BR> (regarded as a very sacred hymn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकः|पुरुषक|पुरुषकं
पुरुषकः, -कम्<BR> Standing on two feet like a man, the rearing of a horse;<BR> श्रीवृक्षकी पुरुषकोन्नमिताग्रकायः Śi. 5. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकम्
पुरुषकः, -कम्<BR> Standing on two feet like a man, the rearing of a horse;<BR> श्रीवृक्षकी पुरुषकोन्नमिताग्रकायः Śi. 5. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषता
पुरुषता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Manhood, manliness, prowess.<BR>—2 Virility.<BR>—3 Manly nature or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषत्वम्
पुरुषता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Manhood, manliness, prowess.<BR>—2 Virility.<BR>—3 Manly nature or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायते
पुरुषायते Den. Ā. To act like a man, play the man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायित
पुरुषायित <i>a.</i> Acting like a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायितम्
पुरुषायित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Playing the man, acting a manly part, a manly conduct.<BR>—2 A kind of coitus or mode of sexual enjoyment, in which the woman plays<BR> the man; आकृतिमवलोक्य कयापि वितर्कितं पुरुषायितम् असिलतालेखनेन<BR> वैदग्ध्यादभिव्यक्तिमुपनीतम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुष्य
पुरुष्य <i>a.</i> Ved. Human, mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1034-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूरवस्
पुरूरवस् <i>m.</i> [cf. Uṇ. 4. 231] The son of Budha and Ilā and<BR> founder of the lunar race of kings. [He saw the nymph Urvaśī, while descending<BR> upon earth owing to the curse of Mitra and Varuṇa, and fell in love with<BR> her. Urvaśī, too, was enamoured of the king who was as renowned for<BR> personal beauty as for truthfulness, devotion, and generosity, and became<BR> his wife. They lived happily together for many days, and after she had<BR> borne him a son, she returned to the heaven. The king heavily mourned<BR> her loss, and she was pleased to repeat her visits five successive times<BR> and bore him five sons. But the king, who wanted her life-long company,<BR> was not evidently satisfied with this; and he obtained his desired object<BR> after he had offered oblations as directed by the Gandharvas. The story<BR> told in Vikramorvaśīya differs in many respects; so does the account<BR> given in the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa, based on a passage in the Ṛgveda,<BR> where it is said that Urvaśī agreed to live with Purūravas on two conditions:−<BR> namely that her two rams which she loved as children must be kept near<BR> her bed-side and never suffered to be carried away, and that he must take<BR> care never to be seen by her undressed. The Gandharvas, however, carried<BR> away the rams, and so Urvaśī disappeared.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोटिः|पुरोटि
पुरोटिः<BR>—1 The current of a river.<BR>—2 The rustling noise of leaves (पत्र-शब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश|पुरोडाशः
पुरोडाश, -पुरोधस् &c.<BR> See under पुरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधस्
पुरोडाश, -पुरोधस् &c.<BR> See under पुरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्व्
पुर्व् €1 P. (पुर्वति)<BR>—1 To fill.<BR>—2 To dwell, inhabit.<BR>—3 To invite (said to be €10 P. in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्
पुल् €1. €6 P., €10 U. (पोलति, पुलति, पोलयति-ते)<BR>—1 To draw or pull out.<BR>—2 To be great.<BR>—3 To be lofty.<BR>—4 To be collected together, be gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल <i>a.</i> Great, large, wide, extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलः|पुल
पुल + .{@-लः@} Horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलम्
पुल + .{@-लम्@} Size, extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुली
पुल + .{@-ली@} A bunch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकः|पुलक|पुलकं
पुलकः<BR>—1 Erection or bristling of the hairs of the body, a thrill (of joy or<BR> fear), horripilation; चारु चुचुम्ब नितम्बवती दयितं पुलकैरनुकूले<BR> Gīt. 1; मृगमदतिलकं लिखति सपुलकं मृगमिव रजनीकरे 7; Amaru. 59, 82.<BR>—2 A kind of stone or gem; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR>—3 A flaw or defect in a gem.<BR>—4 A kind of mineral.<BR>—5 A ball of food with which elephants are fed (गजान्नपिण्ड).<BR>—6 Yellow orpiment, a dot of the same; रक्तोज्ज्वलांशुकवृते द्विरदस्य<BR> कुम्भे जाम्बूनदेन रचितः पुलको यथैव Abhiṣeka. 4. 23.<BR>—7 A wine-glass.<BR>—8 A species of mustard.<BR>—9 See पुलाकः (1); अश्राद्धेयानि धान्यानि कोद्रवाः पुलकास्तथा Mb. 13. 91. 38<BR> (com. पुलकाः असंपूर्णतण्डुलयुक्तधान्यानि).<BR>—10 A bunch.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुलकाङ्गः, पुलकालयः, पुलकोद्गमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकाङ्गः|पुलकाङ्ग|पुलकांग
पुलकः + -अङ्गः the noose of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकालयः|पुलकालय
पुलकः + -आलयः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकोद्गमः|पुलकोद्गम
पुलकः + -उद्गमः erection of the hairs of the body, horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकयति
पुलकयति Den. P. To have the hairs of the body erect, thrill (with joy &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकित
पुलकित <i>a.</i> Having the hairs of the body erect, thrilled with<BR> joy; hence, rejoiced, enraptured; पुलकिता तन्वी तवेयं तनुः K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकिन्
पुलकिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Having the hairs of the body erect &c. ━<i>m.</i> A<BR> species of Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकीकृत
पुलकीकृत <i>a.</i> Thrilled with joy, rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्तिः|पुलस्ति
पुलस्तिः, -स्त्यः<BR> N. of a sage, one of the mind-born sons of Brahmā; Ms. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1035-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

