पुष्पवत्|पुष्पवन्त्
पुष्पवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Blooming, flowery<BR>—2 Set off with flowers. ━<i>m.</i> (du.) The sun and moon; तेजस्विनौ विराजेते<BR> पुष्पवन्ताविवोदितौ Śiva B. 2. 23; रवित्वचन्द्रत्वाभ्यामेकशक्तिमदेव<BR> नियतद्विवचनाकाङ्क्षम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवती
पुष्पवत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 A woman in her courses; पुष्पवत्यपि पवित्रा K.<BR>—2 A cow longing for the bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पा
पुष्पा N. of the town Champā, the modern Bhāgalpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिका
पुष्पिका<BR>—1 The tartar of the teeth.<BR>—2 The mucus of the penis.<BR>—3 The last words of a chapter, which state the subject treated therein.<BR> <i>e. g.</i> इति श्रीमहाभारते शतसाहस्त्यां संहितायां वनपर्वणि &c.<BR> … अमुकोऽध्यायः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिणी
पुष्पिणी A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पित|पुष्पितः
पुष्पित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Flowered, full of flowers, in bloom, blooming; चिरविरहेण विलोक्य<BR> पुष्पिताग्राम् Gīt. 4 (where पुष्पिताग्रा is also the name of a metre).<BR>—2 Florid, flowery (as speech).<BR>—3 A bounding or rich in; as in सुवर्णपुष्पितां पृथ्वीम् Pt. 1. 45.<BR>—4 Fully developed, completely manifested.<BR>—5 Spotted, variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिता
पुष्पित + .{@-ता@} A woman in her courses.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुष्पिताग्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिताग्रा
पुष्पित + -अग्रा N. of a metre; see App. II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिन्
पुष्पिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bearing flowers, blooming, blossoming.<BR>—2 Rich or abounding in flowers.<BR>—3 Flowery (as speech); गिरः श्रुतायाः पुष्पिण्या मधुगन्धेन भूरिणा<BR> Bhāg. 4. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलकः|पुष्पलक
पुष्पलकः A post, wedge, pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यः|पुष्य
पुष्यः<BR>—1 The Kali age.<BR>—2 The month called पौष.<BR>—3 The eighth lunar mansion (consisting of three stars), written also तिष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यम्
पुष्यः + .{@-ष्यम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 The blossom.<BR>—2 Foam, scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्या
पुष्यः + .{@-ष्या@} The asterism called पुष्य.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुष्याभिषेकः, पुष्यस्नानम्, पुष्यनेत्रा, पुष्ययोगः, पुष्यरथः, पुष्यरागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

