पुष्यरथः|पुष्यरथ
पुष्यः + -रथः = पुष्परथः q. v. युक्तः पुष्परथश्च Pratimā 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यरागः|पुष्यराग
पुष्यः + -रागः = पुष्परागः q. v.; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यलकः|पुष्यलक
पुष्यलकः See पुष्पलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्
पुस् €10 U. (पोसयति-ते)<BR>—1 To rub.<BR>—2 To decrease, lessen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त्
पुस्त् €10 U. (पुस्तयति-ते)<BR>—1 To bind, tie.<BR>—2 To disrespect, contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तम्
पुस्तम्<BR>—1 Plastering, painting, anointing.<BR>—2 Working in clay, modelling.<BR>—3 Anything made of clay, wood or metal.<BR>—4 A book, manuscript; also पुस्ता-स्ती.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पुस्तकर्मन्, पुस्तपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकर्मन्|पुस्तकर्म्मन्
पुस्तम् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> plastering, painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तपालः|पुस्तपाल
पुस्तम् + -पालः Keeper of land records; EI. XV. 130, XX. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकः|पुस्तक|पुस्तकं
पुस्तकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A book, manuscript.<BR>—2 A protuberant ornament, boss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकम्
पुस्तकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A book, manuscript.<BR>—2 A protuberant ornament, boss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकागारम्
पुस्तकः, -कम् + .{@-आगारम्@} a library.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकास्त्रणम्
पुस्तकः, -कम् + .{@-आस्तरणम्@} The wrapper of a manuscript; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकमुद्रा
पुस्तकः, -कम् + .{@-मुद्रा@} a kind of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">Page1038-2</a>]<BR> mudrā mentioned in Tantraśāstra; वाममुष्टिं स्वाभिमुखीं कृत्वा पुस्तकमुद्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तिकापूलिकः
पुस्तकः, -कम् + .{@-पुस्तिकापूलिकः@} a collection of manuscripts; Hc. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू €1, €4 Ā., €9 U. (पवते, पूयते, पुनाति, पुनीते, पूत; <i>caus.</i><BR> पावयति; <i>desid.</i> पुपूषति, पिपविषते)<BR>—1 To make pure, cleanse, purify (lit. and fig.); अवश्यपाव्यं पवसे<BR> Bk. 6. 64, 3. 18; पुण्याश्रमदर्शनेन तावदात्मानं पुनीमहे Ś. 1;<BR> Ms. 1. 105, 2. 62; Y. 1. 58; R. 1. 53; पवनः पवतामस्मि Bg. 10. 31.<BR>—2 To refine.<BR>—3 To clean from chaff, winnow; पूत्वा तृणमिषीकां वा ते लभन्ते न<BR> किञ्चन Mb. 12. 237. 4.<BR>—4 To expiate, atone for; दुर्मित्रासो हि क्षितयः पवन्ते Rv. 7. 28. 4.<BR>—5 To discern, discriminate.<BR>—6 To think out, devise, invent.<BR>—7 To become clear or pure (Ātm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनीत
पुनीत <i>p. p.</i> cleaned, purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Purifying, cleansing, refining; as<BR> in खलपू &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
पूत <i>p. p.</i> [पू-क्त]<BR>—1 Purified, cleansed, washed (fig. also); दृष्टिपूतं न्यसेत् पादं वस्त्रपूतं<BR> जलं पिबेत् । सत्यपूतां वदेद् वाचं मनःपूतं समाचरेत् ॥ Ms. 6. 46;<BR> त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा यज्ञैरिष्ट्वा स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते Bg. 9. 20.<BR>—2 Threshed, winnowed.<BR>—3 Expiated.<BR>—4 Contrived, invented.<BR>—5 Stinking, putrid, fetid, foul-smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतः|पूत|पूतं
पूत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A conch-shell.<BR>—2 White Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतम्
पूत + .{@-तम्@} Truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूता
पूत + .{@-ता@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूतात्मन्, पूतक्रतायी, पूतक्रतुः, पूततृणम्, पूतद्रुः, पूतधान्यम्, पूतपत्री, पूतपाप, पूतपाप्मन्, पूतफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतात्मन्
पूत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> pure-minded. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a purified man, saint, sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतायी
पूत + -क्रतायी Śachī, the wife of Indra; पूतक्रतायीमभ्येति सत्रपः<BR> किं न गोत्रभित् Bk. 5. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतुः|पूतक्रतु
पूत + -क्रतुः N. of Indra; घोषस्यान्ववदिष्टेव लङ्का पूतकतोः पुरः Bk. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूततृणम्
पूत + -तृणम् white Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतद्रुः|पूतद्रु
पूत + -द्रुः the tree called पलाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतधान्यम्
पूत + -धान्यम् sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपत्री
पूत + -पत्री holy basil (तुलसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप
पूत + -पाप, -पाप्मन् <i>a.</i> freed from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप्मन्
पूत + -पाप, -पाप्मन् <i>a.</i> freed from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतफलः|पूतफल
पूत + -फलः the bread fruit tree (पनस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्रिम
पूत्रिम <i>a.</i> Ved. Purified, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूनिः|पूनि
पूनिः <i>f.</i> Purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगः|पूग|पूगं
पूगः [पू गन् किच्च; Uṇ. 1. 121]<BR>—1 A multitude, heap, collection, quantity; केशवः शत्रुपूगहा Mb. 5. 131. 1;<BR> घनतां ध्रुवं नयति तेन भवद्गुणपूगपूरितम् (श्रवणं)<BR> अतृप्ततया Śi. 9. 64.<BR>—2 An association, corporation, union; नृपेणाधिकृताः पूगाः Y. 2. 30;<BR> Ms. 3. 151; सत्रिणः … … पूगजनसमवायेषु विवादं कुर्युः Kau. A. 1. 13.<BR>—3 The areca or betelnut-tree (पूगी also); R. 4. 44; ताम्बूलवल्लीपरिणद्धपूगाः 6. 64, 13. 17;<BR> धृष्यत् पूगवनीघनीकृततलैस्तुङ्गैर्जरच्छाखिभिः (लक्ष्यन्ते) Mv. 7. 13.<BR>—4 Nature, property, disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगम्
पूगः + .{@-गम्@} Areca-nut, betelnut.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूगकृत, पूगपात्रम्, पूगपीठः, पूगपीठम्, पूगपुष्पिका, पूगफलम्, पूगवैरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगकृत
पूगः + -कृत <i>a.</i> heaped, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपात्रम्
पूगः + -पात्रम्<BR>—1 a spitting-pot, spittoon.<BR>—2 a betel-box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपीठः|पूगपीठ|पूगपीठं
पूगः + -पीठः, -पीठम् a spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपीठम्
पूगः + -पीठः, -पीठम् a spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपुष्पिका
पूगः + -पुष्पिका betel-nut and flowers given to guests at a marriage ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगफलम्
पूगः + -फलम् the areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगवैरम्
पूगः + -वैरम् enmity against many men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगी
पूगी The betel-nut tree (पूग).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूगीफलम्, पूगीलता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगीफलम्
पूगी + -फलम् the areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगीलता
पूगी + -लता the areca palm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1038-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्
पूज् €10 U. (पूजयति-ते, पूजयांचकारं-चक्रे, अपूपुजत्-त, अपुपूजत्त,<BR> पूजयितुम्, पूजित)<BR>—1 To adore, worship, revere, honour, receive with respect; यदपूपुजस्त्वमिह<BR> पार्थ मुरजितमपूजितं सताम् Śi. 15. 14; Ms. 4. 31; Bk. 2. 26; Y. 2. 14.<BR>—2 To present or honour with; रत्नैश्च पूजयेदेनं प्रधानपुरुषैः सह Ms. 7. 203.<BR>—3 To regard, take notice of.<BR>—4 To initiate, consecrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजक|पूजकः
पूजक <i>a.</i> (-जिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पूज्-ण्वुल्] Honouring, adoring, worshipping, respecting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजनम्
पूजनम् [पूज् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Worshipping, honouring, adoring; देवद्विजगुरुप्राज्ञपूजनं … तप<BR> उच्यते Bg. 17. 14.<BR>—2 Treating with respect, entertaining, hospitality.<BR>—3 An object of reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजना
पूजनम् + .{@-ना@} same as पूजनम्; अहो देहप्रदानेन दर्शिताऽतिथिपूजना Mb. 12. 147. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजनी
पूजनम् + .{@-नी@} A hen-sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयान
पूजयान <i>a.</i> Worshipping, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजा
पूजा [पूज्-भावे-अ] Worship, honour, adoration, respect, homage;<BR> प्रतिबध्नाति हि श्रेयः पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R. 1. 79.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूजार्ह, पूजोपकरणम्, पूजागृहम्, पूजापट्टकम्, पूजासंभारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजार्ह|पूजार्हः
पूजा + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> venerable, respectable, worshipful, worthy of reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजोपकरणम्
पूजा + -उपकरणम् the requisites for the worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजागृहम्
पूजा + -गृहम् a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजापट्टकम्
पूजा + -पट्टकम् a document of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजासंभारः|पूजासम्भार
पूजा + -संभारः See पूजोपकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजित|पूजितः
पूजित <i>p. p.</i> [पूज्-क्त]<BR>—1 Honoured, respected.<BR>—2 Adored, revered.<BR>—3 Acknowledged.<BR>—4 Endowed.<BR>—5 Recommended.<BR>—6 Frequented.<BR>—7 Consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजिल|पूजिलः
पूजिल <i>a.</i> Venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजिलः|पूजिल
पूजिल + .{@-लः@} A god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्य|पूज्यः
पूज्य <i>a.</i> Deserving respect, worthy of honour, respectable, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्यः|पूज्य
पूज्य + .{@-ज्यः@} A father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूण्
पूण् €10 U. (पूणयति-ते) To heap together, accumulate, amass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्
पूत् <i>ind.</i> An imitative word expressive of hard breathing or blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्कृ
पूत्कृ €8 U. To blow, breathe hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्कारी
पूत्कारी<BR>—1 An epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR>—2 N. of the capital of the Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनः|पूतन
पूतनः A dead body in a cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतना
पूतनः + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 N. of a female demon who, while attempting to kill Kṛṣṇa, when<BR> but an infant, was herself crushed by him.<BR>—2 A demoness, or Rākṣasī in general; मा पूतनात्वमुपगाः शिवतातिरेधि Māl. 9. 50.<BR>—3 Terminalia chebula (हरीतकी); ‘पूतना राक्षसीभेदे हरीतक्यां च पूतना’ Viśva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पूतनारिः, पूतनसूदनः, पूतनहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1039-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

