पैत्त (-त्ती <i>f.</i>), पैत्तिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्ती
पैत्त (-त्ती <i>f.</i>), पैत्तिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिक|पैत्तिकः
पैत्त (-त्ती <i>f.</i>), पैत्तिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिकी
पैत्त (-त्ती <i>f.</i>), पैत्तिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तल
पैत्तल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of brass, brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पितुरिदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a father or ancestors generally, paternal, ancestral.<BR>—2 Sacred to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्रम्
पैत्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 The part of the hand between the forefinger and the thumb. (Also पैत्र्य<BR> in this sense.)<BR>—2 A year, month, or day sacred to the Pitṛs.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पैत्राहोरात्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्राहोरात्रः|पैत्राहोरात्र
पैत्र + -अहोरात्रः one month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पल
पैप्पल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of the wood of the holy fig-tree; दण्डोऽपरः<BR> पैप्पलः U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पलादाः
पैप्पलादाः N. of a school of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलः|पैल
पैलः N. of a sage and promulgator of the Ṛgveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलव
पैलव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of the wood of the Pīlu tree; Ms. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैल्ल्यम्
पैल्ल्यम् Blear-eyedness<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशल्यम्
पैशल्यम्<BR>—1 Mildness, affability, softness.<BR>—2 Skilfulness (कौशल्य); प्रहस्य मन्दं पैशल्यादभ्यभाषत वीर्यवान्<BR> Mb. 1. 131. 22 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच <i>a.</i> (-ची <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पिशाचेन निर्वृत्तः अण्] Demoniacal, infernal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचः|पैशाच
पैशाच + .{@-चः@}<BR>—1 The eighth or lowest of the eight forms<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">Page1048-2</a>]<BR> of marriage in Hindu law, in which a lover ravishes a maiden without her<BR> consent when she is sleeping, or intoxicated, or deranged in intellect;<BR> सुप्तां मत्तां प्रमत्तां वा रहो यत्रोपगच्छति । स पापिष्ठो विवाहानां<BR> पैशाचश्चाष्टमो ऽधमः Ms. 3. 34; Y. 1. 61.<BR>—2 A kind of demon or पिशाच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाची
पैशाच + .{@-ची@}<BR>—1 A present made at a religious ceremony.<BR>—2 Night.<BR>—3 A sort of gibberish spoken on the stage by demons.<BR>—4 One of the forms of Prākṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचिक
पैशाचिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Infernal, demoniacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच्यम्
पैशाच्यम् A demoniacal nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुनम्
पैशुनम्, -न्यम्<BR> [पिशुनस्य भावः अण् ष्यञ् वा]<BR>—1 Backbiting, slandering, tale-bearing, calumny; पैशुन्यं साहसं … … क्रोधजोऽपि<BR> गणोऽष्टकः Ms. 7. 48, 11. 56; Bg. 16. 2.<BR>—2 Roguery, depravity.<BR>—3 Wickdness, malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन्यम्
पैशुनम्, -न्यम्<BR> [पिशुनस्य भावः अण् ष्यञ् वा]<BR>—1 Backbiting, slandering, tale-bearing, calumny; पैशुन्यं साहसं … … क्रोधजोऽपि<BR> गणोऽष्टकः Ms. 7. 48, 11. 56; Bg. 16. 2.<BR>—2 Roguery, depravity.<BR>—3 Wickdness, malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुनिक
पैशुनिक <i>a.</i> Slanderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट <i>a.</i> (-ष्टी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पिष्टस्येदम् अण्] Made of flour or meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of flour or meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिकम्
पैष्टिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A number of cakes.<BR>—2 A spirituous liquor distilled from meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टी
पैष्टी A spirituous liquor distilled from meal; cf. गौडी; गौडी पैष्टी<BR> च माध्वी च विज्ञेया त्रिविधा सुरा Ms. 11. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पो
पो <i>a.</i> Pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगण्ड|पोगंड|पोगण्डः
पोगण्ड <i>a.</i> [पौः शुद्धो गण्ड एकदेशो यस्य Tv.]<BR>—1 Young, not adult or full-grown.<BR>—2 Having a deficient or redundant member.<BR>—3 Deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगण्डः|पोगण्ड|पोगंड
पोगण्ड + .{@-ण्डः@} A boy, one from his 5th to his 16th year; ‘बाल आ षोडशाद् वर्षात् पोगण्डश्चापि शब्दितः’ Nārada.; Ms. 8. 148; cf. अपोगण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटः|पोट
पोटः<BR>—1 The foundation of a house.<BR>—2 Putting together, uniting, mixing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पोटगलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटगलः|पोटगल
पोटः + -गलः<BR>—1 a kind of reed (नल).<BR>—2 a kind of grass (काश); पोटगलास्तु धमनो नडः Abh. Cin. 1193^1.<BR>—3 a kind of fish.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/44aba84e.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटकः|पोटक
पोटकः A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटलः|पोटल
पोटलः, पोटलकः, पोटलिका See पोट्टलः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटलकः|पोटलक
पोटलः, पोटलकः, पोटलिका See पोट्टलः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटलिका
पोटलः, पोटलकः, पोटलिका See पोट्टलः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटा
पोटा<BR>—1 A masculine woman, a woman with a beard or such other masculine features;<BR> पोटा तु स्त्री नृलक्षणा Abh. Cin.<BR>—2 A hermaphrodite.<BR>—3 A female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटिकः|पोटिक
पोटिकः A boil, pustule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1048-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटी
