पोषितृ
पोषितृ <i>a.</i> One who feeds, nourishes &c. ━<i>m.</i> A feeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषिन्
पोषिन्, पोष्टृ <i>a.</i> [पुष्-णिनि तृच् च] One who feeds,<BR> nourishes &c. ━<i>m.</i> A feeder, nourisher, protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृ
पोषिन्, पोष्टृ <i>a.</i> [पुष्-णिनि तृच् च] One who feeds,<BR> nourishes &c. ━<i>m.</i> A feeder, nourisher, protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्य|पोष्यः
पोष्य <i>a.</i> [पुष्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be fed, nourished or supported.<BR>—2 Well-fed, thriving.<BR>—3 Causing prosperity.<BR>—4 Abundant, copious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पोष्यपुत्रः, पोष्यसुतः, पोष्यवर्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यपुत्रः|पोष्यपुत्र|पोष्यपुत्त्रः
पोष्य + -पुत्रः, -सुतः an adopted son; अधुना कृत्तिकादीनां षण्णां यः<BR> पोष्यपुत्रकः । तन्नाम चक्रुस्ताः प्रेम्णा कार्तिकश्चेति कौतुकात् ॥ Brav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यसुतः
पोष्य + -पुत्रः, -सुतः an adopted son; अधुना कृत्तिकादीनां षण्णां यः<BR> पोष्यपुत्रकः । तन्नाम चक्रुस्ताः प्रेम्णा कार्तिकश्चेति कौतुकात् ॥ Brav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यवर्गः|पोष्यवर्ग
पोष्य + -वर्गः a class of relatives, who must be nourished and protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषधः|पोषध
पोषधः A fasting day, sacred day; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चलीय
पौंश्चलीय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चलेयः|पौंश्चलेय
पौंश्चलेयः The son of a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चल्यम्
पौंश्चल्यम् Harlotry, female incontinence; पौश्चल्याच्चलचित्ताच्च<BR> नैस्नेह्याच्च स्वभावतः । रक्षिता यत्नतोऽपीह भर्तृष्वेता विकुर्वते ॥ Ms. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंसवनम्
पौंसवनम् See पुंसवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्न|पौंस्नं
पौंस्न <i>a.</i> (-स्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fit for a man; संगच्छ पौंस्नि स्त्रैणं मां युवानं तरुणीशुभे Bk. 5. 91.<BR>—2 Manly, virile.<BR>—3 Human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्नम्
पौंस्न + .{@-स्नम्@} Manhood, virility; का देवरं वशगतं कुसुमास्त्रवेगविस्रस्तपौंस्नमुशती<BR> न भजेत कृत्ये Bhāg. 4. 26. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्यम्
पौंस्यम् Ved.<BR>—1 Manly courage, strength.<BR>—2 Manhood, virility.<BR>—3 A battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्ड|पौगंड|पौगण्डं
पौगण्ड <i>a.</i> (-डी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Boyish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्डम्
पौगण्ड + .{@-ण्डम्, पौगण्डकम्@} Boyhood (from the 5th to the 16th year); मृत्योः<BR> पौगण्डके बाला दृष्ट्वोचुर्विस्मिता व्रजे Bhāg. 10. 12. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्डकम्
पौगण्ड + .{@-ण्डम्, पौगण्डकम्@} Boyhood (from the 5th to the 16th year); मृत्योः<BR> पौगण्डके बाला दृष्ट्वोचुर्विस्मिता व्रजे Bhāg. 10. 12. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डरीक|पौंडरीक|पौण्डरीकं|पौण्डरीकः
पौण्डरीक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to or made of lotus-flowers; अविरलमिव<BR> दाम्ना पौण्डरीकेण नद्धः Māl. 3. 16; वातावधूता वरपौण्डरीकी लम्बेव<BR> माला रुचिराम्बरस्य Rām. 4. 28. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डरीकः|पौण्डरीक|पौंडरीक|पौण्डरीकं
पौण्डरीक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A kind of leprosy.<BR>—2 A Soma sacrifice of 11 days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डर्यम्
पौण्डर्यम् A kind of drug used as a remedy for diseased eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रः|पौण्ड्र|पौंड्र|पौंड्रः
पौण्ड्रः<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 A king or inhabitant of that country; पौण्ड्रश्च बलिनां वरः Hariv.<BR>—3 A kind of sugar-cane.<BR>—4 A sectarial mark.<BR>—5 N. of the conchshell of Bhīma; पौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा<BR> वृकोदरः Bg. 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पौण्ड्रवर्धनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रवर्धनः|पौण्ड्रवर्धन|पौण्ड्रवर्द्धनः
पौण्ड्रः + -वर्धनः (पौण्ड्रम् इक्षुविशेषं वर्धयति) N. of the country of Bihar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रकः|पौण्ड्रक|पौंड्रक|पौंड्रकः
पौण्ड्रकः<BR>—1 A kind of sugar-cane.<BR>—2 A mixed caste (of sugar-boilers); cf. Ms. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रिकः|पौण्ड्रिक|पौंड्रिक|पौंड्रिकः
पौण्ड्रिकः A kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्य
पौण्य <i>a.</i> Virtuous, holy, upright, righteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतवम्
पौतवम् A measure; शुल्कं दण्डः पौतवं नागरिको … च दुर्गम्<BR> Kau. A. 2. 6. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1049-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिनासिक्यम्
पौतिनासिक्यम् Fetor of the nostrils; Ms. 11. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्तिकम्
पौत्तिकम् A kind of honey (pale-coloured).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्र|पौत्त्रः|पौत्रः
पौत्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुत्रस्यापत्यम् अण्] Relating to or derived from a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रः|पौत्र|पौत्त्रः
पौत्र + .{@-त्रः@} A grandson, sonʼs son. पौत्रदौहित्रयोर्लोके न विशेषोऽस्ति<BR> धर्मतः Ms. 9. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्री
पौत्र + .{@-त्री@}<BR>—1 A grand-daughter.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रम्
पौत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} The office of a Potṛ, q. v.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पौत्रजीविकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रजीविकम्
पौत्र + -जीविकम् an amulet made of the seeds of पुत्रंजीव plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिक
पौत्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to a son or grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिकेयः|पौत्रिकेय
पौत्रिकेयः The son of a daughter appointed to raise issue for her father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिन्
पौत्रिन् <i>a.</i> Having a grandson; Ms. 9. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौद्गलिक
पौद्गलिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Substantial, material.<BR>—2 Selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुनिक|पौनःपुनिकः
पौनःपुनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Frequently repeated, recurring again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुन्यम्
पौनःपुन्यम् Frequent or constant repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्तम्
पौनरुक्तम्, पौनरुक्त्यम्<BR>—1 Repetition; अतिप्रियोऽसीति पौनरुक्त्यम् K. 237; R. 12. 40.<BR>—2 Superfluity, redundancy, uselessness; अभिव्यक्तायां चन्द्रिकायां किं<BR> दीपिकापौनरुक्त्येन V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त्यम्
पौनरुक्तम्, पौनरुक्त्यम्<BR>—1 Repetition; अतिप्रियोऽसीति पौनरुक्त्यम् K. 237; R. 12. 40.<BR>—2 Superfluity, redundancy, uselessness; अभिव्यक्तायां चन्द्रिकायां किं<BR> दीपिकापौनरुक्त्येन V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भव|पौनर्भवः
पौनर्भव <i>a.</i> [पुनर्भू विदा˚ अपत्ये अञ्]<BR>—1 Relating to a widow who has married a second husband.<BR>—2 Repeated, superfluous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भवः|पौनर्भव
पौनर्भव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 The son of a widow remarried, one of the twelve sons recognised by<BR> the old Hindu law; Y. 2. 130; या पत्या वा परित्यक्ता विधवा वा स्वयेच्छया ।<BR> उत्पादयेत् पुनर्भूत्वा स पौनर्भव उच्यते ॥ Ms. 9. 175. भस्मनीव<BR> हुतं हव्यं तथा पौनर्भवे द्विजे Mb. 13. 90. 15; Ms. 3. 1. 55.<BR>—2 The second husband of a woman; पौनर्भवेन भर्त्रा सा पुनः संस्कारमर्हति Ms. 9. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुरे वसति शौषिको अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a city or town, produced in a town, civic.<BR>—2 Ved. Filling oneʼs own belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरः|पौर|पौरं
पौर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A townsman, citizen, (opp. जानपद); Ku. 6. 41; R. 2. 10, 74, 12. 3, 16. 9.<BR>—2 A term applied to a prince engaged in war under particular circumstances.<BR>—3 A planet in a state of opposition to other planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरी
पौर + .{@-री@} The language of the servants in a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरम्
पौर + .{@-रम्@} A sort of grass (रोहिष).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: पौराङ्गना, पौरयोषित्, पौरकार्यम्, पौरजनः, पौरलोकः, पौरजानपद, पौरजानपदाः, पौरवृद्धः, पौरसख्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराङ्गना|पौरांगना
पौर + -अङ्गना, -योषित् <i>f.</i>, {@-स्त्री@}<BR> a woman living in a town; विद्युद्दामस्फुरितचकितैर्यत्र<BR> पौराङ्गनानां लोलापाङ्गैर्यदि न रमसे लोचनैर्वञ्चितोऽसि Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरयोषित्
पौर + -अङ्गना, -योषित् <i>f.</i>, {@-स्त्री@}<BR> a woman living in a town; विद्युद्दामस्फुरितचकितैर्यत्र<BR> पौराङ्गनानां लोलापाङ्गैर्यदि न रमसे लोचनैर्वञ्चितोऽसि Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरकार्यम्
पौर + -कार्यम् public business; अर्थजातस्य गणनाबहुलतयैकमेव<BR> पौरकार्यमवेक्षितम् Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजनः|पौरजन
पौर + -जनः, -लोकः<BR>—1 a citizen.<BR>—2 citizens, burghers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरलोकः|पौरलोक
पौर + -जनः, -लोकः<BR>—1 a citizen.<BR>—2 citizens, burghers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजानपद
पौर + -जानपद <i>a.</i> belonging to town and country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजानपदाः
पौर + -जानपदाः (pl.) citizens and rustics, townsmen and country people;<BR> कथं दुर्जनाः पौरजानपदाः U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवृद्धः|पौरवृद्ध
पौर + -वृद्धः an eminent citizen, an elder man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरसख्यम्
पौर + -सख्यम् fellow-citizenship; दशाब्दाख्यं पौरसख्यम् Ms. 2. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरकम्
पौरकम्<BR>—1 A garden near a house.<BR>—2 A garden near a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरिकः|पौरिक
पौरिकः<BR>—1 A citizen.<BR>—2 A governor of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरेय
पौरेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Civic, town-bred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरंदर
पौरंदर <i>a.</i> (-री)<BR> Derived from or sacred to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरंदरम्
पौरंदर + .{@-रम्@} The lunar mansion called ज्येष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरन्ध्र
पौरन्ध्र <i>a.</i> Feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरव|पौरवः
पौरव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुरोर्गोत्रापत्यम् अण्] Descended from Puru; पौरवेणाथ<BR> वयसा राजा यौवनमास्थितः Mb. 1. 75. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवः|पौरव
पौरव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Puru; Ś. 5. 2 N. of a country or people in the north of India.<BR>—2 An inhabitant or ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवीय
पौरवीय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Devoted to Paurava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्य|पौरस्त्यः
पौरस्त्य <i>a.</i> [पुरस्-भवार्थे त्यक् अण् च]<BR>—1 Eastern; पौरस्त्यो वा सुखयति मरुत् साधुसंवाहनाभिः Māl. 9. 25;<BR> पौरस्त्यझञ्झामरुत् 9. 17; R. 4. 34.<BR>—2 Foremost.<BR>—3 Prior, first, preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराण
पौराण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुराण-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the past, ancient, of the past, primeval.<BR>—2 Relating to the Purāṇas or derived from them.<BR>—3 Former, previous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिक|पौराणिकः
पौराणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुराण-ठक्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the past, ancient.<BR>—2 Belonging to the Purāṇas or derived from them.<BR>—3 Versed in the legends of the past.<BR>—4 Versed in the science of architecture (शिल्पशास्त्र); Mb. 1. 51. 15 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिकः|पौराणिक
पौराणिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa well-versed in the Purāṇas, a public reader of the Purāṇas.<BR>—2 A mythologist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरिकः|पौरिक
पौरिकः A country in the South.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष|पौरुषं|पौरुषः
पौरुष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुरुष अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a man or man in general, human.<BR>—2 Manly, virile. —3 Secred to <i>Puruṣa</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषः|पौरुष|पौरुषं
पौरुष + .{@-षः@} A weight which can be carried by one man; Ms. 8. 404.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषी
पौरुष + .{@-षी@} A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषम्
पौरुष + .{@-षम्@}<BR>—1 Human action, manʼs work, exertion, effort; धिग् धिग् वृथा पौरुषम्<BR> Bh. 2. 88; दैवं निहत्य कुरु पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या Pt. 1. 361, 2. 85.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Heroism, prowess, valour, manliness, courage; पौरुषभूषणः<BR> R. 15. 28, 8. 28.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Strength, power, vigour.<BR>—3 Virility; पौरुषं नृषु Bg. 7. 8; स्त्रीभूतश्च परं मासं न स्मरिष्यसि<BR> पौरुषम् Rām. 7. 87. 29.<BR>—4 Semen virile.<BR>—5 Penis.<BR>—6 The full height of a man, the height to which he reaches with both<BR> arms elevated and the fingers extended; जवेऽपि मानेऽपि च पौरुषाधिकम् N. 1. 57.<BR>—7 Sun-dial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषिकः|पौरुषिक
पौरुषिकः A worshipper of Puruṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेय|पौरुषेयः
पौरुषेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [पुरुष-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Derived from or belonging to man, human, incidental to man; made, established<BR> or propounded by man; as in अपौरुषेया वै वेदाः.<BR>—2 Manly, virile.<BR>—3 Spiritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेयः|पौरुषेय
पौरुषेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Manslaughter<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">Page1051-1</a>]<BR> (पुरुषवध).<BR>—2 A crowd of men.<BR>—3 A day-labourer, hireling.<BR>—4 Human action, manʼs work.<BR>—5 Law as affecting persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेयम्
पौरुषेय + .{@-यम्@} Human work, action of man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1050-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष्यम्
पौरुष्यम् Manliness, courage, heroism; किमार्य कामस्य वशंगतेन<BR> किमात्मपौरुष्यपराभवेन Rām. 4. 30. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुहूत
पौरुहूत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to Indra; अस्याधिज्ये धनुषि विजयं पौरुहूते<BR> च वज्रे Ś. 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोगवः|पौरोगव
पौरोगवः A superintendent of the royal household; especially, of<BR> the royal kitchen; पौरोगवः सूदाध्यक्षः Abh. Cin. 722.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशः|पौरोडाश
पौरोडाशः A Mantra recited upon making an oblation of ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशिकः|पौरोडाशिक
पौरोडाशिकः A priest who repeats the above Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोधसम्
पौरोधसम् The office of a family-priest; पौरोधसं हृष्यति येन<BR> दुर्मतिः Bhāg. 6. 7. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोभाग्यम्
पौरोभाग्यम्<BR>—1 Fault-finding, censoriousness; प्रियोपभोगचिह्नेषु पौरोभाग्यमिवाचरन् R. 12. 22.<BR>—2 Ill-will, envy, jealousy.<BR>—3 An ill-natured act, mischievous deed; किमिदमनुष्ठितं पौरोभाग्यम् Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Obtrusiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित्यम्
पौरोहित्यम् The office of a family-priest; नरकाय मतिस्ते चेत्<BR> पौरोहित्यं समाचर Pt. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास|पौर्णमासः
पौर्णमास <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासः|पौर्णमास
पौर्णमास + .{@-सः@} A ceremony performed on the full-moon day by one who maintains<BR> the sacred fire (अग्निहोत्रिन्); दर्शपौर्णमासाभ्यां यजेत ŚB. on MS. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासम्
पौर्णमास + .{@-सम्@} A day of full-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासी
पौर्णमासी, -पौर्णमी<BR> A day of full-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमी
पौर्णमासी, -पौर्णमी<BR> A day of full-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास्यम्
पौर्णमास्यम् A sacrifice performed on the full-moon day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिमः|पौर्णिम
पौर्णिमः An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिमा
पौर्णिमा A day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्त
पौर्त, पौर्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to acts of pious charity; आशीर्युक्तानि<BR> कर्माणि पौर्तानि विविधानि च Mb. 14. 37. 9; तावतां न भवेद् दातुः फलं<BR> दानस्य पौर्तिकम् Ms. 3. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्तिक|पौर्त्तिक
पौर्त, पौर्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to acts of pious charity; आशीर्युक्तानि<BR> कर्माणि पौर्तानि विविधानि च Mb. 14. 37. 9; तावतां न भवेद् दातुः फलं<BR> दानस्य पौर्तिकम् Ms. 3. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व|पौर्व्व
पौर्व, पौर्वक <i>a.</i> (-र्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the past.<BR>—2 Relating to the east, eastern.<BR>—3 Coming in succession (परंपरागत); एतैर्ब्रह्मर्षिभिर्नित्यमृत्विजस्तस्य<BR> पौर्वकाः Rām. 1. 7. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वक
पौर्व, पौर्वक <i>a.</i> (-र्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the past.<BR>—2 Relating to the east, eastern.<BR>—3 Coming in succession (परंपरागत); एतैर्ब्रह्मर्षिभिर्नित्यमृत्विजस्तस्य<BR> पौर्वकाः Rām. 1. 7. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वदेहिक|पौर्व्वदेहिक
पौर्वदे(दै)हिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to a former existence, done in a former<BR> life; तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम् Bg. 6. 43; Y. 1. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वदैहिक
पौर्वदे(दै)हिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to a former existence, done in a former<BR> life; तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम् Bg. 6. 43; Y. 1. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वपदिक|पौर्व्वपदिक
पौर्वपदिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to the first member of a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वापर्यम्
पौर्वापर्यम्<BR>—1 The relation of prior and posterior.<BR>—2 Due order, succession, continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1051-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिकः
