प्रचुरीकृत
प्रचुरीकृत <i>a.</i> Augmented, increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीभू
प्रचुरीभू €1 P. To become plentiful, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतस्
प्रचेतस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Varuṇa; Ku. 2. 21.<BR>—2 N. of an ancient sage and law-giver; Ms. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतृ
प्रचेतृ <i>m.</i> A charioteer, coach-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेलम्
प्रचेलम् Yellow sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेलकः|प्रचेलक
प्रचेलकः A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छ्|प्रछ्
प्रच्छ् €6 P. (पृच्छति, पप्रच्छ, अप्राक्षीत्, प्रक्ष्यति, प्रष्टुम्, पृष्ट;<BR> <i>caus.</i> प्रच्छयति; <i>pass.</i> पृच्छयते; <i>desid.</i><BR> पिप्रच्छिषति)<BR>—1 To ask, question, interrogate, inquire of (with two acc.); पप्रच्छ<BR> रामां रमणोऽभिलाषम् R. 14. 27; Bk. 6. 8; R. 3. 5; पृच्छामि त्वां धर्मसंमूढचेताः<BR> Bg. 2. 7; ब्राह्मणं कुशलं पृच्छेत् Ms. 2. 127; so महाश्वेता कादम्बरीमनामयं<BR> पप्रच्छ K. 192; कुशलमबले पृच्छति त्वां वियुक्तः Me. 103; R. 1. 58.<BR>—2 To ascertain, learn by inquiry.<BR>—3 To seek, seek for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छनम्
प्रच्छनम्, -ना<BR> A question, inquiry, interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छना
प्रच्छनम्, -ना<BR> A question, inquiry, interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद्
प्रच्छद् €10 U.<BR>—1 To cover, wrap up, veil, envelop (वनं) प्राच्छादयदमेयात्मा<BR> नीहारेणेव चन्द्रमाः Mb.<BR>—2 To hide, conceal, disguise, keep secret; प्रच्छादय स्वान् गुणान्<BR> Bh. 2. 77; प्रदानं प्रच्छन्नम् 2. 64; Ms. 4. 198, 10. 40; C. P. 4.<BR>—3 To clothe oneself, put on clothes.<BR>—4 To stand in the way, become an obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद्
प्रच्छद् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 A cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदः|प्रच्छद|प्रछद
प्रच्छदः A cover, wrapper, coverlet, bed-clothes, bed-cover; प्रच्छदान्तगलिताश्रुबिन्दुभिः R. 19. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रच्छदपटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदपटः|प्रच्छदपट
प्रच्छदः + -पटः bed-clothes, coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्न|प्रच्छन्नं
प्रच्छन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Covered, wrapped, enveloped.<BR>—2 Private, secret; विद्या नाम नरस्य रूपमधिकं प्रच्छन्नगुप्तं धनम् Bh. 2. 64.<BR>—3 Concealed, hidden; प्रच्छन्ना वा प्रकाशा वा वेदितव्याः स्वकर्मभिः<BR> Ms. 10. 40; Mb. 3. 35. 31.<BR>—4 Clothed, clad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्नम्
प्रच्छन्न + .{@-न्नम्@}<BR>—1 A private door.<BR>—2 A loop-hole, lattice, window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्नम्
प्रच्छन्न + .{@-न्नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Secretly, covertly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रच्छन्नतस्करः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्नतस्करः|प्रच्छन्नतस्कर
प्रच्छन्न + -तस्करः an unseen thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादक|प्रच्छादकः
प्रच्छादक <i>a.</i> Concealing, covering (at the end of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादकः|प्रच्छादक
प्रच्छादक + .{@-कः@} The song of a wife deserted by her husband (containing a<BR> covert description of her sorrows); also प्रच्छेदक in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादनम्
प्रच्छादनम्<BR>—1 Covering, concealing.<BR>—2 An upper garment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रच्छादनपटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादनपटः|प्रच्छादनपट
प्रच्छादनम् + -पटः a wrapper, cover, coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादित|प्रच्छादितं
प्रच्छादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Covered, enveloped, clothed &c.<BR>—2 Hidden, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दक
प्रच्छर्दक <i>a.</i> Anything (drug &c.) causing vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दनम्
प्रच्छर्दनम्<BR>—1 Vomiting.<BR>—2 Emitting, sending forth.<BR>—3 An emetic; प्रच्छर्दनविधारणाभ्यां वा प्राणस्य Pātañjala S. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दिका|प्रच्छर्द्दिका
प्रच्छर्दिका Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छानम्
प्रच्छानम्<BR>—1 Scarifying.<BR>—2 Making sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छायम्
प्रच्छायम् [प्रकृष्टा छाया यत्र] Thick or dense shade, a shadowy<BR> place; प्रच्छायसुलभनिद्रा दिवसाः परिणामरमणीयाः Ś. 1. 3; M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छिद्
प्रच्छिद् €7 U. To cut, cleave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छेदनम्
प्रच्छेदनम् Dividing into small pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छिल
प्रच्छिल <i>a.</i> Dry, waterless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यु
प्रच्यु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To move away, go away, withdraw, retreat.<BR>—2 To fall off from, drop down, fall down.<BR>—3 To forsake, abandon (as religion).<BR>—4 To be ejected or driven, be dislodged, be deprived of, lose (with abl.)<BR>—5 To flow out, stream forth.<BR>—6 To drive, urge on. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To move, shake.<BR>—2 To displace, dislodge, eject, expel.<BR>—3 To cause to fall, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यवः|प्रच्यव
प्रच्यवः<BR>—1 Fall, ruin.<BR>—2 Improvement, advancement, growth.<BR>—3 Withdrawal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यवनम्
प्रच्यवनम्<BR>—1 Departing, retreating, withdrawal.<BR>—2 Loss, deprivation.<BR>—3 Oozing, dropping (क्षरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यावनम्
प्रच्यावनम्<BR>—1 Causing to give up.<BR>—2 A means of removing, a sedative or palliative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यावित
प्रच्यावित <i>p. p.</i> Driven away; ततो निवातकवचैरितः प्रच्याविताः<BR> सुराः Mb. 3. 172. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यावुक
प्रच्यावुक <i>a.</i> Transitory, fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युत
प्रच्युत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen off or from.<BR>—2 Strayed, deviated.<BR>—3 Dislodged, displaced, degraded; अस्मादप्रच्युतो विप्रः प्राप्नोति परमां<BR> गतिम् Ms. 12. 116.<BR>—4 Displaced, ejected.<BR>—5 Banished, expelled.<BR>—6 Routed, put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युतिः|प्रच्युति
प्रच्युतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Departing, withdrawal.<BR>—2 Loss, deprivation, falling down from; नित्यं प्रच्युतिशङ्कया क्षणमपि<BR> स्वर्गे न मोदामहे Śānti. 4. 20.<BR>—3 Fall, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजन्
प्रजन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born or produced, come into existence.<BR>—2 To grow, arise, spring up.<BR>—3 To bring forth, be delivered of.<BR>—4 To beget, generate, produce in general; चरितब्रह्मचर्यो हि प्रजायेत<BR> यजेत च Mb. 12. 28. 55. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To beget, generate.<BR>—2 To cause, produce.<BR>—3 To bring forth, bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1061-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजः|प्रज
प्रजः A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनः|प्रजन
प्रजनः<BR>—1 Impregnating, begetting, generating, production; अप्रमोदात् पुनः<BR> पुंसः प्रजनं न प्रवर्तते Mb. 13. 46. 4; T. Up. 1. 9. 1; Ms. 3. 61, 9. 61.<BR>—2 The impregnation of cattle.<BR>—3 Bringing forth, bearing; प्रजनार्थं स्त्रियः सृष्टाः Ms. 9. 96.<BR>—4 A generator, progenitor; प्रजनश्चास्मि कन्दर्पः Bg. 10. 28.<BR>—5 The generative organ; प्रजने च प्रजापतिम् (सन्निवेशयेत्) Ms. 12. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनन|प्रजननं
प्रजनन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Producing, generating, procreative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजननम्
प्रजनन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Procreation, generation, conception in the womb.<BR>—2 Production, birth, delivery.<BR>—3 Semen.<BR>—4 The male or female organ of generation (penis or vulva); आत्मानमुभयोर्मध्ये<BR> यत्तत् प्रजननं विदुः Bhāg. 9. 14. 46.<BR>—5 Offspring.<BR>—6 Pregnancy of cattle (उपसर).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रजननकुशल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजननकुशल
प्रजनन + -कुशल <i>a.</i> skilled in midwifery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिका
प्रजनिका A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिष्णु
प्रजनिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Procreative, productive.<BR>—2 Growing, standing (as corn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनुकः|प्रजनुक
प्रजनुकः The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनूः
प्रजनूः <i>f.</i> The vulva (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजा
प्रजा (Changed to प्रजस् at the end of a Bah. compound, when<BR> the first member is अ, सु or दुस्; as अवेक्षितप्रजः R. 8. 32;<BR> सुप्रजस् 18. 29.)<BR>—1 Procreation, generation, propagation, birth, production.<BR>—2 Offspring, progeny, issue; children, brood (of animals); प्रजार्थव्रतकर्शिताङ्गम्<BR> R. 2. 73; प्रजायै गृहमेधिनाम् R. 1. 7; Ms. 3. 42; Y. 1. 269; so बकस्य<BR> प्रजा, सर्पप्रजा &c.<BR>—3 Posterity, descendants.<BR>—4 A creature.<BR>—6 Subjects, people, mankind; ननन्दुः सप्रजाः प्रजाः R. 4. 3; प्रजाः<BR> प्रजाः स्वा इव तन्त्रयित्वा Ś. 5. 5 and स्वाभ्यः प्रजाभ्यो हि यथा तथैव<BR> सर्वप्रजाभ्यः शिवमाशशंसे Bu. C. 2. 35 (where प्रजा has sense 2<BR> also); R. 1. 7, 2. 73; Ms. 1. 8.<BR>—6 Semen.<BR>—7 An era; Buddh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रजाध्यक्षः, प्रजान्तकः, प्रजेप्सु, प्रजेशः, प्रजेश्वरः, प्रजोत्पत्तिः, प्रजाकल्पः, प्रजाकाम, प्रजाकारः, प्रजातन्तुः, प्रजातीर्थम्, प्रजाद, प्रजादानम्, प्रजाद्वारम्, प्रजानाथः, प्रजानिषेकः, प्रजापः, प्रजापतिः, प्रजापरिपालनम्, प्रजापालनम्, प्रजापालः, प्रजापालकः, प्रजापालिः, प्रजापाल्यम्, प्रजावृद्धिः, प्रजाव्यापारः, प्रजासृज्, प्रजाहित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाध्यक्षः|प्रजाध्यक्ष
प्रजा + -अध्यक्षः<BR>—1 an epithet of the sun.<BR>—2 of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजान्तकः|प्रजान्तक|प्रजांतक
प्रजा + -अन्तकः Yama, the god of death; अथ वा मृदु वस्तु हिंसितुं<BR> मृदुनैवारभते प्रजान्तकः R. 8. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजेप्सु
प्रजा + -ईप्सु <i>a.</i> desirous of progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजेशः|प्रजेश
प्रजा + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः the lord of men, a king, sovereign; तमभ्यनन्दत्<BR> प्रथमं प्रबोधितः प्रजेश्वरः शासनहारिणा हरेः R. 3. 68, 5. 32;<BR> प्रजाश्चिरं सुप्रजसि प्रजेशे ननन्दुरानन्दजलाविलाक्ष्यः 18. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजेश्वरः|प्रजेश्वर
प्रजा + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः the lord of men, a king, sovereign; तमभ्यनन्दत्<BR> प्रथमं प्रबोधितः प्रजेश्वरः शासनहारिणा हरेः R. 3. 68, 5. 32;<BR> प्रजाश्चिरं सुप्रजसि प्रजेशे ननन्दुरानन्दजलाविलाक्ष्यः 18. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजोत्पत्तिः|प्रजोत्पत्ति
प्रजा + -उत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR> {@-उत्पादनम्@} the raising up of progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाकल्पः|प्रजाकल्प
प्रजा + -कल्पः the time of creation; Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाकाम
प्रजा + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाकारः|प्रजाकार
प्रजा + -कारः author of the creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजातन्तुः|प्रजातन्तु|प्रजातंतु
प्रजा + -तन्तुः a line of descendants, lineage, race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजातीर्थम्
प्रजा + -तीर्थम् the auspicious moment of birth; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाद
प्रजा + -द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 granting progeny.<BR>—2 removing barrenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजादानम्
प्रजा + -दानम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाद्वारम्
प्रजा + -द्वारम् N. of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानाथः|प्रजानाथ
प्रजा + -नाथः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—2 a king, sovereign, prince; प्रजाः प्रजानाथ पितेव पासि R. 2. 48, 10. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानिषेकः|प्रजानिषेक
प्रजा + -निषेकः<BR>—1 impregnation, seed (implanted in the womb); प्रजानिषेकं मयि वर्तमानं<BR> सूनोरनुध्यायत चेतसेति R. 14. 60.<BR>—2 offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापः|प्रजाप
प्रजा + -पः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापतिः|प्रजापति
प्रजा + -पतिः<BR>—1 the god presiding over creation; प्रजने च प्रजापतिम् Ms. 12. 121.<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahmā;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">Page1062-2</a>]<BR> अस्याः सर्गविधौ प्रजापतिरभूच्चन्द्रो नु कान्तिप्रदः V. 1. 9.<BR>—3 an epithet of the ten lords of created beings first created by Brahmā<BR> (see Ms. 1. 34).<BR>—4 an epithet of Viśvakarman, the architect of gods.<BR>—5 the sun.<BR>—6 a king.<BR>—7 a son-in-law.<BR>—8 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—9 a father, progenitor.<BR>—10 the penis.<BR>—11 a sacrifice; ˚हृदयम् A kind of सामगान.<BR>—12 N. of a संवत्सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापरिपालनम्
प्रजा + -परिपालनम्, -पालनम् the protection of subjects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापालनम्
प्रजा + -परिपालनम्, -पालनम् the protection of subjects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापालः|प्रजापाल
प्रजा + -पालः, -पालकः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापालकः|प्रजापालक
प्रजा + -पालः, -पालकः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापालिः|प्रजापालि
प्रजा + -पालिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापाल्यम्
प्रजा + -पाल्यम् royal office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावृद्धिः|प्रजावृद्धि
प्रजा + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> increase of progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाव्यापारः|प्रजाव्यापार
प्रजा + -व्यापारः care for or anxiety about the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजासृज्
प्रजा + -सृज् <i>m.</i> epithet of Brahmā; कृतः प्रजाक्षेमकृता प्रजासृजा Śi. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाहित|प्रजाहितं
प्रजा + -हित <i>a.</i> beneficial to children or people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाहितम्
प्रजा + -हित + .({@-तम्@}) water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजात
प्रजात <i>p. p.</i> Born, produced &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाता
प्रजात + .{@-ता@} A woman who has borne a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजातिः|प्रजाति
प्रजातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Procreation, production, propagation; प्रजातिश्च स्वाध्यायप्रवचने<BR> च T. Up. 1. 9. 1; अथापि काममेतं ते प्रजात्यै करवाण्यलम् Bhāg. 3. 14. 21.<BR>—2 Delivery.<BR>—3 Procreative power.<BR>—4 Travail, labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजायिन्
प्रजायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Being about to produce or bring forth.<BR>—2 Bearing, bringing forth (अभिरूप˚, वीर˚ &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावत्|प्रजावन्त्
प्रजावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having subjects or children.<BR>—2 Pregnant.<BR>—3 Abounding in progeny, prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावती
प्रजावत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 A brotherʼs wife (भ्रातृजाया); प्रजावती दोहदशंसिनी ते R. 14. 45, 15. 13.<BR>—2 A matron, mother.<BR>—3 An elder brotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्प्
प्रजल्प् €1 P.<BR>—1 To speak, say, talk; स्वरेण तस्याममृतस्रुतेव प्रजल्पितायामभिजातवाचि Ku. 1. 45.<BR>—2 To call.<BR>—3 To proclaim.<BR>—4 To prattle, chatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पः|प्रजल्प
प्रजल्पः Prattle, gossip, heedless or frivolous words (used in greeting<BR> a lover); असूयेर्ष्यामदयुजा योऽवधीरणमुद्रया । प्रियस्य कौशलोद्गारः<BR> प्रजल्पः स तु कथ्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पनम्
प्रजल्पनम्<BR>—1 Talking, speaking.<BR>—2 Prattle, gossip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पित
प्रजल्पित <i>a.</i> Talked, prattled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पितम्
प्रजल्पित + .{@-तम्@} Talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन् See under प्रजू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागृ
प्रजागृ €2 P.<BR>—1 To keep watch, be awake, wake.<BR>—2 To lie in wait for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागरः|प्रजागर
प्रजागरः<BR>—1 Lying awake at night, sleeplessness; स राजर्षिरिमानि दिवसानि प्रजागरकृशो<BR> लक्ष्यते Ś. 3; प्रजागरात् खिलीभूतस्तस्याः स्वप्ने समागमः Ś. 6. 22.<BR>—2 Vigilance, carefulness.<BR>—3 A guardian.<BR>—4 An epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu (नित्यं प्रबुद्धत्वात् प्रजागर्ति<BR> इति प्रजागरः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागरणम्
प्रजागरणम् Being awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागरूक
प्रजागरूक <i>a.</i> Wide awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजिनः|प्रजिन
प्रजिनः Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1062-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजीवनम्
प्रजीवनम् Livelihood, subsistence; शेषाणामानृशंस्यार्थं प्रदद्यात्तु<BR> प्रजीवनम् Ms. 9. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजुष्ट
प्रजुष्ट <i>a.</i> Attached or devoted to, intent on; विषयेषु प्रजुष्टानि Ms. 2. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजू
प्रजू €1 U.<BR>—1 To push or drive onward, impel, urge on.<BR>—2 To hasten forward. ━<i>Caus.</i> To shoot, dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजवः|प्रजव
प्रजवः Ved. Haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजवन
प्रजवन <i>a.</i> Swift, fleet; व्यावल्गत् प्रजवनवाजिना रथेन<BR> U. 5. 1 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन् <i>a.</i> Rapid, swift, speedy. ━<i>m.</i> An express, a courier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजृम्भ्
प्रजृम्भ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To begin to yawn.<BR>—2 To open the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्जटिका
प्रज्जटिका A kind of Prākṛta metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञा
प्रज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To know, know about, be acquainted with.<BR>—2 To be aware of, find out.<BR>—3 To discern, distinguish. ━<i>Caus.</i> (प्रज्ञपयति)<BR>—1 To show, point out (as way).<BR>—2 To discover.<BR>—3 To call, summon, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञ|प्रज्ञः
प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wise, intelligent, learned.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) conversant with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञः|प्रज्ञ
प्रज्ञ + .{@-ज्ञः@} A wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञप्त
प्रज्ञप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ordered, prescribed.<BR>—2 Arranged (as a seat); Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञप्तिः|प्रज्ञप्ति
प्रज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Agreement, engagement.<BR>—2 Teaching, informing, communicating.<BR>—3 A doctrine.<BR>—4 Intellect.<BR>—5 N. of a goddess, Vidyādevā (Jainism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञा
प्रज्ञा<BR>—1 Intelligence, understanding, intellect, wisdom; आकारसदृशप्रज्ञः<BR> प्रज्ञया सदृशागमः R. 1. 15; नाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा<BR> प्रतिष्ठिता Bg. 2. 57; शस्त्रं निहन्ति पुरुषस्य शरीरमेकं प्रज्ञा<BR> कुलं च विभवं यशश्च हन्ति ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Discernment, discrimination, judgment; इयं निष्ठा बहुविधा प्रज्ञया<BR> त्वध्यवस्यति Mb. 14. 30. 24.<BR>—3 Device or design.<BR>—4 A wise or learned woman.<BR>—5 Longing for (वासना); impression (संस्कार); तं विद्याकर्मणि<BR> समन्वारभेते पूर्वप्रज्ञा च Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 2.<BR>—6 N. of the goddess Sarasvatī.<BR>—7 A particular Śakti or energy.<BR>—8 A true or transcendental wisdom; Buddh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रज्ञास्त्रम्, प्रज्ञाघनः, प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्, प्रज्ञानयन, प्रज्ञापारमिता, प्रज्ञामात्रा, प्रज्ञावादः, प्रज्ञावृद्ध, प्रज्ञासहाय, प्रज्ञाहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञास्त्रम्
प्रज्ञा + -अस्त्रम् a missile, weapon; ततः प्रज्ञास्त्रमादाय मोहनास्त्रं<BR> व्यनाशयत् Mb. 6. 77. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाघनः|प्रज्ञाघन
प्रज्ञा + -घनः nothing but intelligence; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्
प्रज्ञा + -चक्षुस्, -नयन <i>a.</i> blind; (lit. having understanding as the<BR> only eyes); ततो ज्ञास्यसि मां सौते प्रज्ञाचक्षुषमित्युत Mb. 1. 1. 149;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 13. 28; Manodūta 115; N. 12. 106. ━(<i>m.</i>) an epithet<BR> of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; Mb. 3. 7. 24; Kāvyamālā, Part. 13. ━(<i>n.</i>) the<BR> mindʼs eye, mental eye, the mind; M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञानयन
प्रज्ञा + -चक्षुस्, -नयन <i>a.</i> blind; (lit. having understanding as the<BR> only eyes); ततो ज्ञास्यसि मां सौते प्रज्ञाचक्षुषमित्युत Mb. 1. 1. 149;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 13. 28; Manodūta 115; N. 12. 106. ━(<i>m.</i>) an epithet<BR> of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; Mb. 3. 7. 24; Kāvyamālā, Part. 13. ━(<i>n.</i>) the<BR> mindʼs eye, mental eye, the mind; M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञापारमिता
प्रज्ञा + -पारमिता one of the transcendent virtues; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञामात्रा
प्रज्ञा + -मात्रा an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावादः|प्रज्ञावाद
प्रज्ञा + -वादः a wise saying; अशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे Bg. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावृद्ध
प्रज्ञा + -वृद्ध <i>a.</i> old in wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञासहाय
प्रज्ञा + -सहाय <i>a.</i> intelligent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाहीन
प्रज्ञा + -हीन <i>a.</i> void of wisdom, silly, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञात
प्रज्ञात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Known, understood.<BR>—2 Distinguished, discerned.<BR>—3 Distinct, clear.<BR>—4 Famous, well-known, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञान|प्रज्ञानं
प्रज्ञान <i>a.</i> Prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञानम्
प्रज्ञान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Intelligence, knowledge, wisdom.<BR>—2 A mark, token, sign; ध्वजो रथस्य प्रज्ञानम् Rām. 2. 67. 30.<BR>—3 Discernment, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञापनम्
प्रज्ञापनम् Statement, assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञापित
प्रज्ञापित <i>p. p.</i> Betrayed, disclosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाल
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (-नी <i>f.</i>), प्रज्ञिल <i>a.</i><BR> Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिन्
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (-नी <i>f.</i>), प्रज्ञिल <i>a.</i><BR> Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिनी
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (-नी <i>f.</i>), प्रज्ञिल <i>a.</i><BR> Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिल
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (-नी <i>f.</i>), प्रज्ञिल <i>a.</i><BR> Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावत्|प्रज्ञावन्त्
प्रज्ञावत् <i>a.</i> Wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञु|प्रज्ञुः
प्रज्ञु <i>a.</i> Bow-legged, bandy-legged; (so प्रज्ञ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वल्
प्रज्वल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To burn brightly, blaze up, shine; रणाङ्गानि प्रजज्वलुः Bk. 14. 98.<BR>—2 To catch fire, be in flames, blaze up.<BR>—3 To be kindled (as anger), to be incensed or wrathful. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (प्रज्व(ज्वा)लयति)<BR>—1 To kindle, set on fire.<BR>—2 To brighten, illumine, irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलनम्
प्रज्वलनम्<BR>—1 Blazing up, flaming, burning.<BR>—2 Kindling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलित|प्रज्वलितः
प्रज्वलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Being in flames, burning, flaming, blazing.<BR>—2 Bright, shining.<BR>—3 Burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलितम्
प्रज्वलित + .{@-तम्@} Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वालनम्
प्रज्वालनम् Kindling, setting on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वारः|प्रज्वार
प्रज्वारः Fever; heat of fever; प्रज्वारोऽयं मम भ्राता त्वं च<BR> मे भगिनी भव Bhāg. 4. 27. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रडीनम्
प्रडीनम्<BR>—1 Flying in every direction; प्रडीनं सर्वतोयानम् Mb. 8. 41. 26 (com.).<BR>—2 Flying forward; see under डीन.<BR>—3 Taking flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रण|प्रणः
प्रण <i>a.</i> Old, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणखः|प्रणख
प्रणखः The point of a nail; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणद्
प्रणद् €1 P. To sound, resound, echo; क्रव्यादाः प्राणदन् घोराः<BR> Mb.; शिवाः प्रणदन्ति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदनम्
प्रणदनम् Sounding, a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदित
प्रणदित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sounding.<BR>—2 Humming, buzzing (as a bee).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणादः|प्रणाद
प्रणादः<BR>—1 A loud noise, shout, cry; यियासतस्तस्य महीध्ररन्ध्रभिदापटीयान्पटहप्रणादः Śi. 3. 24.<BR>—2 Roaring, a roar.<BR>—3 Neighing, braying.<BR>—4 A murmur of rapture; a burst of applause; huzza.<BR>—5 A cry for help.<BR>—6 A particular disease of the ear (a buzzing sound in the ear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणम्
प्रणम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bow down, salute, make a low obeisance to, be humble (with acc.<BR> or dative); न प्रणमन्ति देवताभ्यः K. 108; तां भक्तिप्रवणेन चेतसा<BR> प्रणनाम K. 228; Ku. 7. 27; तस्मात् प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायम् Bg. 11. 44;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">Page1064-1</a>]<BR> R. 2. 21. (साष्टाङ्गं प्रणम् ‘to fall down on the eight limbs’; see<BR> अष्टाङ्ग; दण्डवत् प्रणम् ‘to bow by throwing oneself down on the ground quite prostrate and flat like a stick placed horizontally, touching the ground at all points’<BR>; cf. दण्डप्रणाम). ━<i>Caus.</i> (प्रणमयति)<BR> To cause to bow down; तामर्चिताभ्यः कुलदेवताभ्यः कुलप्रतिष्ठां प्रणमग्य<BR> माता Ku. 7. 27.<BR>—2 To bend, incline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1063-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणत|प्रणतः
प्रणत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bending, inclined, stooping.<BR>—2 Bowing to, saluting; भृत्यार्तिहं प्रणतपालभवाब्धिपोतम् Bhāg.<BR>—3 Humble.<BR>—4 Skilful, clever.<BR>—5 Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणतिः|प्रणति
प्रणतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A bow, salutation, obeisance; तव सर्वविधेयवर्तिनः प्रणतिं<BR> बिभ्रति के न भूमृतः Śi. 16. 5; R. 4. 88.<BR>—2 Submissiveness, humility, courtesy; स ददर्श वेतसवनाचरितां<BR> प्रणतिं बलीयसि समृद्धिकरीम् Ki. 6. 5; निर्जितेषु तरसा तरस्विनां<BR> शत्रुषु प्रणतिरेव कीर्तये R. 11. 89.<BR>—3 Inclination, bending, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणमित
प्रणमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bent, bowed.<BR>—2 Offered or given respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणामः|प्रणाम
प्रणामः<BR>—1 Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR>—2 A reverential salutation, obeisance, prostration, bow (used with dat.);<BR> as in साष्टाङ्गप्रणाम; Ku. 6. 91; मूर्ध्ना प्रणामं वृषभध्वजाय<BR> चकार 3. 62; अस्मै प्रणाममकरवम् K. 142.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रणामाञ्जलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणामाञ्जलिः|प्रणामाञ्जलि
प्रणामः + -अञ्जलिः a respectful salutation with the hands folded together;<BR> Ku. 4. 35; for अष्टाङ्ग˚ see अष्टाङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणवः|प्रणव
प्रणवः<BR>—1 The sacred syllable <i>om</i>; आसीन्महीक्षितामाद्यः प्रणवश्छन्दसामिव<BR> R. 1. 11; Ms. 2. 74; Ku. 2. 12; प्रणवः सवेदेषु Bg. 7. 8; तस्य<BR> वाचकः प्रणवः, Pātañjala S. 27; प्राणदः प्रणवः प्रभुः V. Sah.<BR>—2 A kind of musical instrument (drum or tabor).<BR>—3 An epithet of Viṣṇu or the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणवकः|प्रणवक
प्रणवकः The Oṃkāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणश्
प्रणश् €4 P.<BR>—1 To perish, die; स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात् प्रणश्यति Bg. 2. 63;<BR> विद्युत् प्रणाशं स वरं प्रनष्टः Bk. 3. 14.<BR>—2 To vanish, disappear.<BR>—3 To escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशः|प्रणाश
प्रणाशः<BR>—1 Cessation, loss, disappearance; ज्ञात्वा प्रणाशं तु तदा जयन्तस्य<BR> Rām. 7. 28. 21; ध्रुवं प्रणाशः प्रहितस्य पत्रिणः Ki. 14. 9, 13. 33.<BR>—2 Death, destruction; भर्तुः प्रणाशादथ शोचनीयम् R. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशन|प्रणाशनं
प्रणाशन <i>a.</i> Destroying, annihilating, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशनम्
प्रणाशन + .{@-नम्@} Destruction, annihilation; प्रणाशनाय प्रबलस्य विद्विषः R. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्ट|प्रनष्टः
प्रनष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Disappeared, vanished, not to be seen.<BR>—2 Lost; Pt. 4. 35.<BR>—3 Perished, dead.<BR>—4 Ruined, destroyed, annihilated.<BR>—5 Escaped.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रनष्टस्वामिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्टस्वामिक
प्रनष्ट + -स्वामिक <i>a.</i> प्रनष्टस्वामिकं रिक्थं राजा त्र्यब्दं निधापयेत् Ms. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणस
प्रणस <i>a.</i> Having a prominent nose, large-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाडिका
प्रणाडिका, प्रणाडी<BR>—1 Intervention, interposition, medium.<BR>—2 Ved. A water-course, drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाडी
प्रणाडिका, प्रणाडी<BR>—1 Intervention, interposition, medium.<BR>—2 Ved. A water-course, drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाय्य|प्रणाय्यः
प्रणाय्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dear, beloved.<BR>—2 Upright, honest, straight-forward.<BR>—3 Disliked, disapproved; न प्रणाय्यो जनः कच्चिन् निकाय्यं तेऽधितिष्ठति Bk. 6. 66.<BR>—4 Free from passion, indifferent to worldly attachments (विरक्त).<BR>—5 Fit, worthy; प्रब्रूयात् प्रणाय्याय वान्तेवासिने Ch. Up. 3. 11. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणालः|प्रणाल
प्रणालः, -ली, प्रणालिका<BR>—1 A channel, water-course, drain; कौसल्या व्यसृजद् बाष्पं प्रणालीव<BR> नवोदकम् Rām. 2. 62. 10; कुर्वन् पूर्णा नयनपयसां चकवालैः प्रणालीः<BR> Ud. S. 2; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>—2 Succession, uninterrupted series.<BR>—3 Recension (of a text).<BR>—4 Intervention, interposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाली
प्रणालः, -ली, प्रणालिका<BR>—1 A channel, water-course, drain; कौसल्या व्यसृजद् बाष्पं प्रणालीव<BR> नवोदकम् Rām. 2. 62. 10; कुर्वन् पूर्णा नयनपयसां चकवालैः प्रणालीः<BR> Ud. S. 2; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>—2 Succession, uninterrupted series.<BR>—3 Recension (of a text).<BR>—4 Intervention, interposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणालिका
प्रणालः, -ली, प्रणालिका<BR>—1 A channel, water-course, drain; कौसल्या व्यसृजद् बाष्पं प्रणालीव<BR> नवोदकम् Rām. 2. 62. 10; कुर्वन् पूर्णा नयनपयसां चकवालैः प्रणालीः<BR> Ud. S. 2; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>—2 Succession, uninterrupted series.<BR>—3 Recension (of a text).<BR>—4 Intervention, interposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशः|प्रणाश
प्रणाशः, -शनम्<BR> s. v. प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशनम्
प्रणाशः, -शनम्<BR> s. v. प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिगद्
प्रणिगद् €1 P. To declare; समय एव करोति बलाबलं प्रणिगदन्त<BR> इतीव शरीरिणाम् Śi. 6. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसित
प्रणिंसित <i>a.</i> Kissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधा
प्रणिधा €2 U.<BR>—1 To place, put or lay down; prostrate; प्रणिहितशिरसं वा कान्तमार्द्रापराधम्<BR> M. 3. 12; तस्मात् प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायम् Bg. 11. 44.<BR>—2 To set, put in, inlay or incase; यदि मणिस्त्रपुणि प्रणिधीयते<BR> Pt. 1. 75 (v. l.).<BR>—3 To apply, fix upon, direct towards; भर्तृप्रणिहितेक्षणाम् R. 15. 84;<BR> Bk. 6. 142.<BR>—4 To stretch out, extend; मामाकाशप्रणिहितभुजं निर्दयाश्लेषहेतोः<BR> Me. 108; नीवीं प्रति प्रणिहिते तु करे प्रियेण सख्यः शपामि यदि किंचिदपि<BR> स्मरामि K. P. 4.<BR>—5 To send out (as spies).<BR>—6 To place or lay in the front.<BR>—7 To include, enclose.<BR>—8 To employ, use; प्रणिहितमपि चक्षुर्ग्रस्तमुक्तं हिनस्ति U. 5. 13.<BR>—9 To resolve.<BR>—10 To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधानम्
प्रणिधानम्<BR>—1 Applying, employing, application, use.<BR>—2 Great effort, energy.<BR>—3 Profound religious meditation, abstract contemplation; सोऽपश्यत्<BR> प्रणिधानेन संततेः स्तम्भकारणम् R. 1. 74, 8. 19; V. 2; तपःस्वाध्यायेश्वरप्रणिधानानि<BR> क्रियायोगः Pātañjala S.; ईश्वरप्रणिधानाद्वा Pātañjala S. 23.<BR>—4 Respectful behaviour towards (with loc.); जानामि प्रणिधानं ते बाल्यात्<BR> प्रभृति नन्दिनि । ब्राह्मणेष्विह सर्वेषु गुरुबन्धुषु चैव ह ॥ Mb. 3. 303. 19.<BR>—5 Renunciation of the fruit of actions (कर्मफलत्याग).<BR>—6 Entrance, access.<BR>—7 (With Buddhists) A prayer, an entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधिः|प्रणिधि
प्रणिधिः<BR>—1 Observing, spying out.<BR>—2 Sending out spies.<BR>—3 A spy, an emissary; अध्यापितस्योशनसापि नीतिं प्रयुक्तरागप्रणिधिर्द्विषस्ते<BR> Ku. 3. 6; R. 17. 48; Ms. 7. 153, 8. 182.<BR>—4 An attendant, a follower.<BR>—5 Care, attention.<BR>—6 Solicitation, entreaty, request; ‘प्रणिधिः प्रार्थने चरे’ Yādava.<BR>—7 A method of driving an elephant; Mātaṅga L. 12. 6. 8. (There are<BR> three kinds of प्रणिधिs: by speech, feet and look.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधेयम्
प्रणिधेयम्<BR>—1 Sending spies.<BR>—2 Employing, using.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिहित|प्रणिहितं
प्रणिहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Laid on, applied.<BR>—2 Deposited.<BR>—3 Outstretched, stretched forth; मामाकाशप्रणिहितभुजं निर्दयाश्लेषहेतोः Me. 108.<BR>—4 Consigned, delivered, entrusted.<BR>—5 Having the attention fixed upon one object, with the mind concentrated,<BR> intent; ऋजुः प्रणिहितो गच्छंस्त्रसस्थावर-वर्जकः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">Page1065-1</a>]<BR> Mb. 12. 9. 19.<BR>—6 Determined, decided.<BR>—7 Cautious, wary.<BR>—8 Obtained, attained.<BR>—9 Spied out.<BR>—10 Acknowledged, admitted, stated; सम्यक् प्रणिहितं चार्थं पृष्टः<BR> सन्नाभिनन्दति Ms. 8. 54.<BR>—11 Applied, directed; प्रियायास्मै धाम्ने प्रणिहितनमस्योऽस्मि भवते<BR> Śivamahimna 28 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1064-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनादः|प्रणिनाद
प्रणिनादः A deep sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपत्
प्रणिपत् €1 P. To bow down to, fall prostrate before, bow respectfully<BR> to, salute (with acc. or dat.); प्रणिपत्य सुरास्तस्मै शमयित्रे सुरद्विषाम्<BR> R. 10. 15; वागीशं वाग्भिरर्थ्याभिः प्रणिपत्योपतस्थिरे Ku. 2. 3, 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनम्
प्रणिपतनम्, प्रणिपातः<BR>—1 Falling at oneʼs feet, prostration, submission; प्रणिपातप्रतीकारः<BR> संरम्भो हि महात्मनाम्. R. 4. 64; तद् विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन<BR> सेवया Bg. 4. 34.<BR>—2 Obeisance, salutation, reverential bow; प्रणिपातपूर्वं स्वहस्तलूनः<BR> (पुष्पोच्चयः) Ku. 3. 61, 4. 35; R. 3. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रणिपतनपुरःसरम्, प्रणिपतनपूर्वकम्, प्रणिपतनप्रतीकार, प्रणिपतनरसः, प्रणिपतनशिक्षा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपातः|प्रणिपात
प्रणिपतनम्, प्रणिपातः<BR>—1 Falling at oneʼs feet, prostration, submission; प्रणिपातप्रतीकारः<BR> संरम्भो हि महात्मनाम्. R. 4. 64; तद् विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन<BR> सेवया Bg. 4. 34.<BR>—2 Obeisance, salutation, reverential bow; प्रणिपातपूर्वं स्वहस्तलूनः<BR> (पुष्पोच्चयः) Ku. 3. 61, 4. 35; R. 3. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रणिपतनपुरःसरम्, प्रणिपतनपूर्वकम्, प्रणिपतनप्रतीकार, प्रणिपतनरसः, प्रणिपतनशिक्षा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनपुरःसरम्
प्रणिपतनम् + -पुरःसरम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> with an obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनपूर्वकम्
प्रणिपतनम् + -पुरःसरम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> with an obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनप्रतीकार
प्रणिपतनम् + -प्रतीकार <i>a.</i> averted or counteracted by prostration; R. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनरसः
प्रणिपतनम् + -रसः a magical formula pronounced over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनशिक्षा
प्रणिपतनम् + -शिक्षा teaching (one) to salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिहन्
प्रणिहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To slay, kill.<BR>—2 To bend down, lower (the hand).<BR>—3 To pronounce lower (than अनुदात्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणी
प्रणी €1 P.<BR>—1 To lead out or forth (as an army), conduct; वानरेन्द्रेण प्रणीतेन<BR> (बलेन) Rām.<BR>—2 To offer, give, present; अर्ध्यं प्रणीय जनकात्मजा Bk. 5. 76.<BR>—3 To bring to, set (as fire); दग्धां गुहां पश्य उलूकपूर्णां काकप्रणीतेन<BR> हुताशनेन Pt. 3. 1.<BR>—4 To consecrate by reciting sacred Mantras, hallow, consecrate in general;<BR> त्रिधा प्रणीतो ज्वलनः Hariv.<BR>—5 To inflict (as punishment); यदि न प्रणयेद् राजा दण्डं दण्ड्येष्वतन्द्रितः<BR> Ms. 7. 20, 8. 238; Mb. 1. 64. 15.<BR>—6 To lay down, teach, promulgate, institute, prescribe; स एव धर्मो<BR> मनुना प्रणीतः R. 14. 67; भवत्प्रणीतमाचारमामनन्ति हि साधवः Ku. 6. 31.<BR>—7 To write, compose (as a work); प्रणीतः न तु प्रकाशितः U. 4;<BR> उत्तरं रामचरितं तत्प्रणीतं प्रयुज्यते U. 1. 3.<BR>—8 To accomplish, effect, perform, bring about; प्रणीय दारिद्र्यदरिद्रतां<BR> नृपः N. 1. 15, 19; कण्ठाश्लेषोपगूढं तदपि च न चिरं यत् प्रियाभिः<BR> प्रणीतम् Bh. 3. 82.<BR>—9 To lead or reduce to any condition.<BR>—10 To show, display; यद्यद्धिया त उरुगाय विभावयन्ति तत्तद्वपुः<BR> प्रणयसे सदनुग्रहाय Bhāg. 3. 9. 11.<BR>—11 To direct, fix or turn towards (as the eyes).<BR>—12 To show affection or love, love.<BR>—13 To throw, cast, discharge; अस्त्रं पुनः पाशभृतः प्रणिन्ये Ki. 16. 54.<BR>—14 To remove, destroy; द्रौपद्याश्च परिक्लेशं प्रणेष्यामि हते त्वयि Mb. 6. 79. 4.<BR>—15 To draw in the breath (Ātm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयः|प्रणय
प्रणयः<BR>—1 Espousing, seizing (as in marriage); आबद्धकङ्कणकरप्रणयप्रसादमासाद्य Māl. 6. 14.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Love, affection, fondness, attachment, liking, regard; साधारणोऽयमुभयोः<BR> प्रणयः स्मरस्य V. 2. 16; साधारणोऽयं प्रणयः Ś. 3; (where<BR> in both cases sense 6 may do as well); Ś. 6. 8, 5. 23; Me. 107; R. 6. 12; Bh. 2. 42.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A wish, desire, longing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">Page1065-2</a>]<BR> हरेरतुलविक्रमप्रणयलालसः साहसे Māl. 8. 7; Ś. 7. 16.<BR>—3 Friendly acquaintance or regard, friendship, intimacy; अजानता महिमानं<BR> तवेदं मया प्रमादात् प्रणयेन वापि Bg. 11. 41; स्नेहस्य तत् फलमसौ<BR> प्रणयस्य सारः Māl. 1. 9.<BR>—4 Familiarity, confidence, trust; मया गृहीते सलिलेऽनेन कृतःप्रणयः Ś. 5.<BR>—5 Favour, kindness, act of courtesy; अलंकृतोऽस्मि स्वयंग्राह प्रणयेन<BR> भवता Mk. 1, 1. 45.<BR>—6 An entreaty, request, solicitation; तद् भूतनाथानुग नार्हसि त्वं<BR> संबन्धिनो मे प्रणयं विहन्तुम् R. 2. 58; V. 4. 13.<BR>—7 Reverence, obeisance.<BR>—8 Final beatitude.<BR>—9 A leader.<BR>—10 Conduct, guidance. (प्रणयेन confidentially, candidly; without<BR> reserve or ceremony; प्रणयात् openly, frankly).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रणयापराधः, प्रणयोन्मुख, प्रणयोपेत, प्रणयकलहः, प्रणयकुपित, प्रणयकोपः, प्रणयपेशल, प्रणयप्रकर्षः, प्रणयभङ्गः, प्रणयमानः, प्रणयवचनम्, प्रणयविमुख, प्रणयविहतिः, प्रणयविघातः, प्रणयस्पृश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयापराधः|प्रणयापराध
प्रणयः + -अपराधः an offence against friendship or love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयोन्मुख
प्रणयः + -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> —1 disposed or about to declare oneʼs love; विसृज<BR> सुन्दरि संगमसाध्वसं तव चिरात् प्रभृति प्रणयोन्मुखे M. 4. 13.<BR>—2 impatient through love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयोपेत
प्रणयः + -उपेत <i>a.</i> candid, frank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयकलहः|प्रणयकलह
प्रणयः + -कलहः a loverʼs quarrel, a mock or feigned quarrel; नाप्यन्यस्मात्<BR> प्रणयकलहाद् विप्रयोगोपपत्तिः Me. (considered spurious by Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयकुपित
प्रणयः + -कुपित <i>a.</i> angry through love, feigning anger; त्वामालिख्य<BR> प्रणयकुपितां धातुरागैः शिलायाम् Me. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयकोपः|प्रणयकोप
प्रणयः + -कोपः feigned anger of a mistress towards her lover, coquettish anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयपेशल
प्रणयः + -पेशल <i>a.</i> soft through affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयप्रकर्षः|प्रणयप्रकर्ष
प्रणयः + -प्रकर्षः excessive love, intense attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयभङ्गः|प्रणयभङ्ग|प्रणयभंग
प्रणयः + -भङ्गः<BR>—1 breach of friendship.<BR>—2 faithlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयमानः|प्रणयमान
प्रणयः + -मानः the jealousy of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयवचनम्
प्रणयः + -वचनम् expression of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविमुख
प्रणयः + -विमुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 averse from love.<BR>—2 disinclined to friendship; सौधोत्सङ्गप्रणयविमुखो मा स्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविहतिः|प्रणयविहति
प्रणयः + -विहतिः, -विघातः non-compliance, refusal (of a request &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविघातः|प्रणयविघात
प्रणयः + -विहतिः, -विघातः non-compliance, refusal (of a request &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयस्पृश्
प्रणयः + -स्पृश् <i>a.</i> inspired by love; Māl. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयनम्
प्रणयनम्<BR>—1 Bringing, fetching.<BR>—2 Conducting, conveying.<BR>—3 Carrying out, executing, performing; सर्गशेषप्रणयनाद्विश्वयोनेरनन्तरम् Ku. 6. 9.<BR>—4 Writing, composing.<BR>—5 Decreeing, sentencing, awarding; as दण्डस्य प्रणयनम्.<BR>—6 Bringing forward, adducing.<BR>—7 Distributing.<BR>—8 Infliction of (punishment).<BR>—9 Founding (of a school).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयवत्|प्रणयवन्त्
प्रणयवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Loving, fond, affectionate; सापि प्रणयवत्यासीत् सपत्न्योरुभयोरपि R. 10. 57.<BR>—2 Candid, frank.<BR>—3 Earnestly desirous of, longing for; जातः सखे प्रणयवान्मृगतृष्णिकायाम् Ś. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिता
प्रणयिता Love, attachment; (श्रीः) मूर्खान् द्वेष्टि न गच्छति प्रणयितामत्यन्तविद्वत्स्वपि Mu. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिन्
प्रणयिन्<BR>—1 Loving, affectionate, kind, attached; यदिन्दावानन्दं प्रणयिनि जने<BR> वा न भजते Māl. 3. 9, 6. 30.<BR>—2 Beloved, dearly loved.<BR>—3 Desirous of, longing for, fondly solicitous of; अङ्काश्रयप्रणयिनस्तनयान्<BR> वहन्तः Ś. 7. 17; Me. 3; R. 9. 55, 11. 3.<BR>—4 Familiar, intimate. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A friend, companion, favourite; कृतोऽक्षसूत्रप्रणयी तया करः Ku. 5. 11.<BR>—2 A husband, lover.<BR>—3 A supplicant, humble petitioner, suitor; स्वार्थात् सतां गुरुतरा प्रणयिक्रियैव<BR> V. 4. 15, 1. 2.<BR>—4 A worshipper, devotee; प्रतिग्रहीतुं प्रणयिप्रियत्वात् त्रिलोचनस्तामुपचक्रमे च Ku. 3. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिनी
प्रणयिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A mistress, beloved, wife.<BR>—2 A female friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1065-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणायकः|प्रणायक
प्रणायकः<BR>—1 A leader or commander (of an army).<BR>—2 A guide, head, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणी
प्रणी <i>a.</i> maker, fashioner; सायंतनीं तिथिप्रण्यः Bk. 5. 65.<BR> (तिथिप्रणी the moon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीत|प्रणीतं|प्रणीतः
प्रणीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Put forward, advanced, presented.<BR>—2 Delivered, given, offered, presented.<BR>—3 Brought into, reduced to.<BR>—4 Executed, effected, performed.<BR>—5 Taught, prescribed.<BR>—6 Cast, sent, discharged.<BR>—7 Brought to, set.<BR>—8 Written, composed.<BR>—9 Set aside, removed.<BR>—10 Agreeable or pleasing.<BR>—11 Inflicted (as punishment); see प्रणी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीतः|प्रणीत|प्रणीतं
प्रणीत + .{@-तः@} Fire consecrated by prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीता
प्रणीत + .{@-ता@} A sacrificed vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीतम्
प्रणीत + .{@-तम्@} Anything cooked or dressed, such as a condiment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रणीताग्नि, प्रणीतापस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीताग्नि
प्रणीत + -अग्नि fire consecrated by prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीतापस्
प्रणीत + -आपस् (pl.) holy water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीतिः|प्रणीति
प्रणीतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Conduct, guidance.<BR>—2 Favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेतृ
प्रणेतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A leader.<BR>—2 A maker, creator.<BR>—3 The promulgator of a doctrine, expounder, teacher; कर्मतन्त्रपणेतार<BR> एकाशीतिर्द्विजातयः Bhāg. 11. 2. 19.<BR>—4 An author.<BR>—5 A performer or player of a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेय|प्रणेयः
प्रणेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be guided or led, tractable, yielding, submissive, obedient; अस्मत्प्रणेयो<BR> राजेति लोकांश्चैव वदन्त्युत Mb. 12. 56. 60.<BR>—2 To be executed or accomplished.<BR>—3 To be settled or fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणु
प्रणु €2. €6 P.<BR>—1 To praise.<BR>—2 To mutter the sacred syllable <i>om</i>.<BR>—3 To roar, bellow.<BR>—4 To resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत|प्रणुतं
प्रणुत <i>p. p.</i> Praised, lauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुद्
प्रणुद् €6 P.<BR>—1 To dispel, drive off, remove; दयितावलोकविकसन्नयनप्रणुन्नमिव<BR> वारिरुहम् Śi. 9. 71.<BR>—2 To push or thrust forward, push on.<BR>—3 To drive, stir, set in motion.<BR>—4 To scare away, frighten away. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To prompt, incite, urge forward.<BR>—2 To push away.<BR>—3 To request or ask any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत्त
प्रणुत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Driven away, repelled.<BR>—2 Scared away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुन्न
प्रणुन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Driven or sent away.<BR>—2 Set in motion; सदश्व इव स क्षिप्रः प्रणुन्नो वाक्यसायकैः Mb. 5. 136. 16.<BR>—3 Scared away.<BR>—4 Shaking, trembling.<BR>—5 Sent, despatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदः|प्रणोद
प्रणोदः<BR>—1 Driving.<BR>—2 Directing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदित
प्रणोदित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Set in motion.<BR>—2 Directed, ordered.<BR>—3 Driven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेजनम्
प्रणेजनम्<BR>—1 Washing or wiping away.<BR>—2 Bathing.<BR>—3 Water for washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन्
प्रतन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To spread abroad, diffuse; ख्यातस्त्वं विभवैर्यशांसि कवयो दिक्षु<BR> प्रतन्वन्ति नः Bh. 3. 24.<BR>—2 To spread, extend, stretch out.<BR>—3 To spread over, fill.<BR>—4 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">Page1066-2</a>]<BR> cause, produce, create.<BR>—5 To show, display, exhibit; तदूरीकृत्य कृतिभिर्वाचस्पत्यं प्रतायते Śi. 2. 30.<BR>—6 To perform, do (as a sacrifice).<BR>—7 To execute, complete, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतत
प्रतत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread over, covered.<BR>—2 Stretched out, diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रततम्
प्रतत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Continuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रततामहः|प्रततामह
प्रततामहः A great-grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रततिः|प्रतति
प्रततिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Extension, expansion, diffusion.<BR>—2 A creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानः|प्रतान
प्रतानः<BR>—1 A Shoot, tendril; लताप्रतानोद्ग्रथितैः स केशैः R. 2. 8; Ś. 7. 11;<BR> बीजकाण्डरुहाण्येव प्रताना बल्ल्य एव वा Ms. 1. 48.<BR>—2 A creeper, low spreading plant.<BR>—3 Branching out, ramification.<BR>—4 Tetanus or epilepsy.<BR>—5 Extension.<BR>—6 Diffuseness, prolixity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानिन्
प्रतानिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spreading.<BR>—2 Having shoots or tendrils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानिनी
प्रतानिन् + .{@-नी@} A spreading creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन|प्रतनः
प्रतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Old, ancient; प्रतनेनानुबन्धेन निजामोपचिकीर्षया<BR> Śiva B. 8. 8; … … नयवर्त्म प्रतनं प्रवर्तयन् Śiva B. 32. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतनहविस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतनहविस्
प्रतन + -हविस् Old ghee to be used as an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतनु
प्रतनु <i>a.</i> (-नु or -न्वी)<BR>—1 Very thin or minute, delicate; वेणीभूतप्रतनुसलिला Me. 29.<BR>—2 Very small, limited, narrow; प्रतनुतपसाम् K. 43; U. 1. 20; Me. 41.<BR>—3 Slender, emaciated; ततः सदर्पं प्रतनुं तपस्यया Ki. 14. 35.<BR>—4 Insignificant, trifling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतप्
प्रतप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To be hot, burn, glow.<BR>—2 To heat.<BR>—3 To kindle, illumine.<BR>—4 To bake, roast.<BR>—5 To feel pain, suffer.<BR>—6 To mortify the body, undergo penance.<BR>—7 To pain, distress, torment. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To warm, heat.<BR>—2 To set on fire, irradiate.<BR>—3 To torment, pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतपः|प्रतप
प्रतपः The heat of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतपत्रम्
प्रतपत्रम् Umbrella (छत्र); छायया च विदधत् प्रतपत्रम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 35. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतपनम्
प्रतपनम् Warming, making warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतप्त
प्रतप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated.<BR>—2 Hot, ardent.<BR>—3 Tormented, tortured, pained.<BR>—4 One who has tortured oneʼs body by penance; उपवासैः प्रतप्तानां<BR> दीर्घं सुखमनन्तकम् Mb. 12. 181. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापः|प्रताप
प्रतापः<BR>—1 Heat, warmth; अन्यप्रतापमासाद्य यो दृढत्वं न गच्छति (here प्रताप<BR> means ‘prowess’ also); Pt. 1. 107.<BR>—2 Radiance, glowing heat; अमी च कथमादित्याः प्रतापक्षतिशीतलाः Ku. 2. 24.<BR>—3 Splendour, brilliancy.<BR>—4 Dignity, majesty, glory; सर्वः प्रायो भजति विकृतिं भिद्यमाने प्रतापे Mv. 2. 4.<BR>—5 Courage, valour, heroism; प्रतापस्तस्य भानोश्च युगपद् व्यानशे दिशः<BR> R. 4. 15. (where प्रताप means ‘heat’ also); 4. 30; शत्रुश्रेणीपतङ्गाञ्ज्वलति<BR> रघुपते त्वत्प्रतापप्रदीपः Udb.; यं देशं श्रयते तमेव कुरुते<BR> बाहुप्रतापार्जितम् H.<BR>—6 Spirit, vigour, energy.<BR>—7 Ardour, zeal.<BR>—8 Issue of ultimatum; प्रेषणं सन्धिपालत्वं प्रतापो मित्रसंग्रहः<BR> Kau. A. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1066-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापन|प्रतापनं|प्रतापनः
प्रतापन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Warming.<BR>—2 Distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापनम्
प्रतापन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Burning, heating, warming.<BR>—2 Paining, tormenting, inflicting punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापनः|प्रतापन|प्रतापनं
प्रतापन + .{@-नः@} N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापवत्|प्रतापवन्त्
प्रतापवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Glorious, dignified.<BR>—2 Valorous, powerful, mighty. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापिन्
प्रतापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Burning, scorching.<BR>—2 Splendid, brilliant.<BR>—3 Paining, distressing.<BR>—4 Glorious, dignified.<BR>—5 Powerful, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतम्
प्रतम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To become exhausted or fatigued, faint.<BR>—2 To lose the breath, be beside oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतमकः|प्रतमक
प्रतमकः A kind of asthma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतमाम्
प्रतमाम् <i>ind.</i> Specially, particularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतरम्
प्रतरम्, प्रतराम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Further, more particularly.<BR>—2 In future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतराम्
प्रतरम्, प्रतराम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Further, more particularly.<BR>—2 In future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्क्
प्रतर्क् €10 U.<BR>—1 To conclude, infer, guess.<BR>—2 To reason, reflect.<BR>—3 To think, believe, consider, suppose; प्रतर्कयन्नन्यमृगेन्द्रनादान् Bk. 2. 9.<BR>—4 To search, investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कः|प्रतर्क
प्रतर्कः Conjecture, guess, supposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कणम्
प्रतर्कणम्<BR>—1 Reasoning, discussion.<BR>—2 Doubt.<BR>—3 Logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्दनः|प्रतर्दन|प्रतर्द्दन
प्रतर्दनः<BR>—1 N. of the son of Divodāsa.<BR>—2 N. of one of Indraʼs disciples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतलम्
प्रतलम् One of the seven divisions of the lower world; see पाताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतलः|प्रतल|प्रतलं
प्रतलम् + .{@-लः@} The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As a prefix to verbs it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) towards, in the direction of;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) back, in return, again; तिष्ठेदानीं न मे जीवन् प्रतियास्यसि<BR> दुर्मते Rām. 7. 18. 13;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) in opposition to, against, counter;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) upon, down upon; (see the several roots with this preposition).<BR>—2 As a prefix to nouns not directly derived from verbs it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) likeness, resemblance, equality;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) opposite, of the opposite side; प्रतिबल Ve. 3. 5 ‘the opposing force’<BR>; so प्रतिद्विपाः Mu. 2. 13;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) rivalry; as in प्रतिचन्द्रः ‘a rival moon’; प्रतिपुरुषः &c.<BR>—3 As a separable preposition (with acc.) it means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) towards, in the direction of, to; तौ दम्पती स्वां प्रति राजधानीं<BR> प्रस्थापयामास वशी वसिष्ठः R. 2. 70, 1. 75; प्रत्यनिलं विचेरु<BR> Ku. 3. 31; वृक्षं प्रति विद्योतते विद्युत् Sk.;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) against, counter, in opposition to, opposite; तदा यायाद् रिपुं<BR> प्रति Ms. 7. 171; प्रदुद्रुवुस्तं प्रति राक्षसेन्द्रम् Rām.; ययावजः<BR> प्रत्यरिसैन्यमेव R. 7. 55;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) in comparison with, on a par with, in proportion to, a match<BR> for; त्वं सहस्राणि प्रति Rv. 2. 1. 8;<BR>——(<i>d</i>) near, in the vicinity of, by, at, in, on; समासेदुस्ततो गङ्गां<BR> शृङ्गवेरपुरं प्रति Rām.; गङ्गां प्रति;<BR>——(<i>e</i>) at the time, about, during; आदित्यस्योदयं प्रति Mb.; फाल्गुनं<BR> वाथ चैत्रं वा मासौ प्रति Ms. 7. 182;<BR>——(<i>f</i>) on the side of, in favour of, to the lot of; यदत्र मां प्रति<BR> स्यात् Sk.; हरं प्रति हलाहलं (अभवत्) Vop.;<BR>——(<i>g</i>) in each, in or at every,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1067-2" target="_blank">Page1067-2</a>]<BR> severally (used in a distributive sense); वर्षं प्रति, प्रतिवर्षम्;<BR> यज्ञं प्रति Y. 1. 110; वृक्षं वृक्षं प्रति सिञ्चति Sk.;<BR>——(<i>h</i>) with regard or reference to, in relation to, regarding, concerning,<BR> about, as to; न हि मे संशीतिरस्या दिव्यतां प्रति K. 132; चन्द्रोपरागं<BR> प्रति तु केनापि विप्रलब्धासि Mu. 1; धर्मं प्रति Ś. 5. 18; मन्दौत्सुक्योऽस्मि<BR> नगरगमनं प्रति Ś. 1; Ku. 6. 27, 7. 83; त्वयैकमीशं प्रति साधु<BR> भाषितभ् 5. 81; Y. 1. 218; R. 6. 12, 10. 29, 12. 51;<BR>——(<i>i</i>) according to, in conformity with; मां प्रति in my opinion;<BR>——(<i>j</i>) before, in the presence of;<BR>——(<i>k</i>) for, on account of.<BR>—4 As a separable preposition (with abl.) it means either<BR>——(<i>a</i>) a representative of, in place of, instead of; प्रद्युम्नः कृष्णात्<BR> प्रति Sk.; संग्रामे यो नारायणतः प्रति Bk. 8. 89; or<BR>——(<i>b</i>) in exchange or return for; तिलेभ्यः प्रति यच्छति माषान् Sk.;<BR> भक्तेः प्रत्यमृतं शंभोः Vop.<BR>—5 As the first member of Avyayībhāva compound it usually means<BR>——(<i>a</i>) in or at every; as प्रतिसंवत्सरम् ‘every year’, प्रतिक्षणम्,<BR> प्रत्यहम् &c.;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) towards, in the direction of; प्रत्यग्नि शलभा डयन्ते.<BR>—6 प्रति is sometimes used as the last member of Avyayī. comp. in<BR> the sense of ‘a little’; सूपप्रति, शाकप्रति. [<i>Note</i>:− In the<BR> compounds given below all words the second members of which are words<BR> not immediately connected with verbs, are included; other words will be<BR> found in their proper places.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यंशम्, प्रत्यक्षरम्, प्रत्यग्नि, प्रत्यग्र, प्रत्यङ्गम्, प्रत्यधिदेवता, प्रत्यधिष्ठानम्, प्रत्याधानम्, प्रत्यनन्तर, प्रत्यनन्तरीभू, प्रत्यनिलम्, प्रत्यनीक, प्रत्यनुप्रासः, प्रत्यनुमानम्, प्रत्यन्त, प्रत्यन्धकार, प्रत्यपकारः, प्रत्यब्दम्, प्रत्यमित्र, प्रत्यरिः, प्रत्यर्कः, प्रत्यर्गलम्, प्रत्यवयवम्, प्रत्यवर, प्रत्यश्मन्, प्रत्यष्ठीला, प्रत्यहम्, प्रत्याकारः, प्रत्याघातः, प्रत्याचारः, प्रत्यात्मम्, प्रत्यात्मक, प्रत्यात्म्यम्, प्रत्यात्म्येन, प्रत्यादित्यः, प्रत्यारम्भः, प्रत्यार्द्र, प्रत्याशा, प्रत्यासङ्गः, प्रत्यास्वर, प्रत्याह्वयः, प्रत्युत्तरम्, प्रत्युलूकः, प्रत्यृचम्, प्रत्येक, प्रत्येनस्, प्रतिकञ्चुकः, प्रतिकण्ठम्, प्रतिकलम्, प्रतिकश, प्रतिकष्ट, प्रतिकामिनी, प्रतिकायः, प्रतिकितवः, प्रतिकुञ्जरः, प्रतिकूपः, प्रतिकूल, प्रतिकूल, प्रतिकूलय, प्रतिकूलिक, प्रतिक्ष