प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा €9 Ā.<BR>—1 To promise, declare solemnly, engage, agree, vow; हरचापारोपणेन<BR> कन्यादानं प्रतिजानीते P. R. 4.<BR>—2 To state, affirm, assert, maintain, allege.<BR>—3 To bring forward or introduce, adduce.<BR>—4 To admit, own, acknowledge.<BR>—5 To confirm.<BR>—6 To approve, consent.<BR>—7 To observe, learn, discern.<BR>—8 To propose.<BR>—9 To remember with regret.<BR>—10 To become aware of; कौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति Bg. 9. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा<BR>—1 Admission, acknowledgment.<BR>—2 A vow, promise, engagement, solemn declaration; दैवात् तीर्णप्रतिज्ञः<BR> Mu. 4. 12; तीर्त्वा जवेनैव नितान्तदुस्तरां नदीं प्रतिज्ञामिव तां गरीयसीम् Śi. 12. 74.<BR>—3 A statement, assertion, declaration, affirmation.<BR>—4 (In Nyāya phil.) A proposition, statement of the proposition to be<BR> proved, the first member of the five-membered Indian syllogism; साध्यनिर्देशः<BR> प्रतिज्ञा यथा पर्वतो वह्निमान् Gaut. S.; see under न्याय;<BR> (पर्वतो वह्निमान् is the usual instance).<BR>—5 (In Law) A plaint, an indictment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिज्ञान्तरम्, प्रतिज्ञापत्रम्, प्रतिज्ञापत्रकम्, प्रतिज्ञापरिपालनम्, प्रतिज्ञापालनम्, प्रतिज्ञापारणम्, प्रतिज्ञाभङ्गः, प्रतिज्ञाविरोधः, प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित, प्रतिज्ञासंन्यासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञान्तरम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -अन्तरम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">Page1073-1</a>]<BR> (in logic) a subsequent proposition on failure of the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1072-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापत्रम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -पत्रम्, -पत्रकम् a bond, written contract or document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापत्रकम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -पत्रम्, -पत्रकम् a bond, written contract or document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापरिपालनम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -परिपालनम्, -पालनम् keeping oneʼs word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापालनम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -परिपालनम्, -पालनम् keeping oneʼs word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापारणम्
प्रतिज्ञा + -पारणम् fulfilment of a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाभङ्गः|प्रतिज्ञाभङ्ग|प्रतिज्ञाभंग
प्रतिज्ञा + -भङ्गः breach of promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविरोधः|प्रतिज्ञाविरोध
प्रतिज्ञा + -विरोधः<BR>—1 breaking an agreement, acting contrary to promise.<BR>—2 denial of a logical proposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित
प्रतिज्ञा + -विवाहित <i>a.</i> betrothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञासंन्यासः|प्रतिज्ञासन्न्यास|प्रतिज्ञासंन्यास
प्रतिज्ञा + -संन्यासः<BR>—1 breaking a promise.<BR>—2 (in logic) abandonment of the original proposition; also प्रतिज्ञाहानि<BR> in this sense; प्रतिज्ञानार्थाय नयनं प्रतिज्ञासंन्यासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञात|प्रतिज्ञातं
प्रतिज्ञात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Declared, stated, asserted.<BR>—2 Promised, agreed.<BR>—3 Admitted, acknowledged.<BR>—4 Agreeable, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञातम्
प्रतिज्ञात + .{@-तम्@} A promise.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिज्ञातार्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञातार्थः|प्रतिज्ञातार्थ
प्रतिज्ञात + -अर्थः a statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञानम्
प्रतिज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Asserting, affirmation.<BR>—2 Agreement, promise.<BR>—3 Admission.<BR>—4 Bringing forward or adducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञेय|प्रतिज्ञेयः
प्रतिज्ञेय <i>a.</i> To be promised &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञेयः|प्रतिज्ञेय
प्रतिज्ञेय + .{@-यः@} A panegyrist, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितरः|प्रतितर
प्रतितरः An oarsman, a sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितालः|प्रतिताल
प्रतितालः A kind of <i>Tāla</i> in music; कान्तारः समराख्यश्च<BR> वकुण्ठो वाञ्छितस्तथा । कथिताः शङ्करेणैव चत्वारः प्रतितालकाः ॥ Saṃgītasāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिताली
प्रतिताली The key of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदर्शनम्
प्रतिदर्शनम् Seeing, perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदा
प्रतिदा €3 U.<BR>—1 To exchange, barter; तिलेभ्यः प्रतियच्छति माषान्.<BR>—2 To give back, return, restore; अद्यापि कोपविमुखीकृतगन्तुकामा नोक्तं<BR> वचः प्रतिददाति यदैव वक्त्रम् C. P. 36.<BR>—3 To recompensate.<BR>—4 To give as a reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदत्त
प्रतिदत्त <i>p. p.</i> Returned, restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदानम्
प्रतिदानम्<BR>—1 Restoration, giving back, restitution (as of a deposit).<BR>—2 Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदेय|प्रतिदेयं
प्रतिदेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be returned &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदेयम्
प्रतिदेय + .{@-यम्@} A pawn, pledge.<BR>—2 An article purchased and given back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदारणम्
प्रतिदारणम्<BR>—1 Fighting, battle.<BR>—2 Splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिवन्
प्रतिदिवन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A day.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदीप्त
प्रतिदीप्त <i>p. p.</i> Flaming against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदुह्
प्रतिदुह् <i>n.</i> Fresh milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदूषित
प्रतिदूषित <i>a.</i> Defiled, contaminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदृश्
प्रतिदृश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To see, behold.<BR>—2 To know, become aware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदृष्ट
प्रतिदृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Beheld.<BR>—2 Come in sight, become visible.<BR>—3 Famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिद्रुह्
प्रतिद्रुह् <i>m.</i> One who seeks to injure in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधा
प्रतिधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To place or lay on.<BR>—2 To return, restore.<BR>—3 To fix (as an arrow).<BR>—4 To offer, present<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">Page1073-2</a>]<BR>—5 To use, employ.<BR>—6 To begin, commence.<BR>—7 To draw near, approach (as the night); (mostly Vedic in these senses).<BR>—8 To restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधा
प्रतिधा A draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधानम्
प्रतिधानम्<BR>—1 Putting on.<BR>—2 Taking measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधिः|प्रतिधि
प्रतिधिः<BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 (Vedic) A cross-piece on the pole of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधावनम्
प्रतिधावनम् Assailing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वनिः|प्रतिध्वनि
प्रतिध्वनिः, -प्रतिध्वानः<BR> An echo, reverberation; श्रुतपदरवस्तेषामेव<BR> प्रतिध्वनिमध्वनि N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वानः|प्रतिध्वान|प्रतिध्वानं
प्रतिध्वनिः, -प्रतिध्वानः<BR> An echo, reverberation; श्रुतपदरवस्तेषामेव<BR> प्रतिध्वनिमध्वनि N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वस्त
प्रतिध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Down-cast.<BR>—2 Sunk, hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनद्
प्रतिनद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To resound, echo.<BR>—2 To answer with a shout. ━<i>Caus.</i> To fill with noise, make resonant;<BR> Śānti. 2. 17; स्वस्थस्थिताण्डजकुलप्रतिनादितानि (उपवनानि) Ṛs. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादः|प्रतिनाद
प्रतिनादः An echo, a reverberation (also प्रतिनिनदः in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादित
प्रतिनादित <i>a.</i> Resounding, echoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनन्द्|प्रतिनंद्
प्रतिनन्द् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bless; तौ गुरुर्गुरुपत्नी च प्रीत्या प्रतिननन्दतुः R. 1. 57;<BR> Ms. 7. 146; Ku. 7. 87.<BR>—2 To welcome, congratulate, hail with joy, receive gladly; प्रतिनन्द्य<BR> स तां पूजाम् Mb.; Ms. 2. 54.<BR>—3 To accept cheerfully; भर्तुः प्रसादं प्रतिनन्द्य मूर्ध्ना Ku. 3. 2.<BR>—4 To address kindly, show devotion. ━<i>Caus.</i> To delight, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनन्दनम्
प्रतिनन्दनम्<BR>—1 Congratulating, welcoming.<BR>—2 Thanks giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाहः|प्रतिनाह
प्रति(ती)नाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीनाहः|प्रतीनाह
प्रति(ती)नाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधा
प्रतिनिधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To substitute, put in the place of.<BR>—2 To slight, disregard.<BR>—3 To order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधिः|प्रतिनिधि
प्रतिनिधिः<BR>—1 A representative, substitute; सोऽभवत् प्रतिनिधिर्न कर्मणा R. 11. 13, 1. 81, 4. 54, 5. 63, 9. 40.<BR> अल्लीशाहात् प्रतिनिधिं तस्य शैलस्य<BR> सर्वथा Śiva B. 28. 4.<BR>—2 A deputy, vicegerent.<BR>—3 Substitution.<BR>—4 A surety.<BR>—5 An image, likeness, picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिपातः|प्रतिनिपात
प्रतिनिपातः Falling down, alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनियत
प्रतिनियत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Settled, predestined; विधिर्वन्द्यः सोऽपि प्रतिनियतकर्मैकफलदः Bh. 2. 94.<BR>—2 Firm, unshakable; विपक्षाणां हेतीः प्रतिनियतधैर्यानुभवतः Mv. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनियमः|प्रतिनियम
प्रतिनियमः<BR>—1 A general rule.<BR>—2 A separate allotment; जननमरणकरणानां प्रतिनियमादयुगपत्<BR> प्रवृत्तेश्च Sāṅ. K. 18.<BR>—3 A strict rule applying only to a particular case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्जित
प्रतिनिर्जित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Vanquished, subdued.<BR>—2 Rescinded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्देश्य
प्रतिनिर्देश्य <i>a.</i> That which, though before expressed, is repeated<BR> in order to state something more about it;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">Page1074-1</a>]<BR> cf. the instance given in K. P. 7; उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति<BR> च, where ताम्र is repeated to show that the sun that rises <i>red</i><BR> sets also <i>red</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1073-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्यातनम्
प्रतिनिर्यातनम्<BR>—1 Retribution, retaliation.<BR>—2 Returning, giving back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिविष्ट
प्रतिनिविष्ट <i>a.</i> Perverse, obstinate, hardened.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खः|प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्ख
प्रतिनिविष्ट + -मूर्खः a perverse fool, confirmed blockhead; न तु प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खजनचित्तमाराधयेत् Bh. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवेशः|प्रतिनिवेश
प्रतिनिवेशः Obstinacy, obdurateness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवर्तनम्
प्रतिनिवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Returning, return.<BR>—2 Turning away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिष्क्रयः|प्रतिनिष्क्रय
प्रतिनिष्क्रयः Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिष्पूत
प्रतिनिष्पूत <i>p. p.</i> Cleansed, winnowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनुद्
प्रतिनुद् €6 U. To ward off, repel, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनोदः|प्रतिनोद
प्रतिनोदः Repelling, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To step or go towards, approach, resort or betake oneself to; उमामुखं<BR> तु प्रतिपद्य लोलाद् द्विसंश्रयां प्रीतिमवाप लक्ष्मीः Ku. 1. 43.<BR>—2 To enter upon, step upon, take, follow (as a way &c.); इतः पन्थानं<BR> प्रतिपद्यस्व Ś. 4; प्रतिपत्स्ये पदवीमहं तवं Ku. 4. 10.<BR>—3 To arrive at, reach, attain: मरणमप्यपराः प्रतिपेदिरे Śi. 6. 16.<BR>—4 To get, gain, obtain, share, partake; स हि तस्य न केवलां श्रियं<BR> प्रतिपेदे सकलान् गुणानपि R. 8. 5, 13, 4. 1, 41, 11. 34, 12. 7, 19. 55;<BR> तदोत्तमविदां लोकानमलान् प्रतिपद्यते Bg. 14. 14; Śi. 10. 63.<BR>—5 To accept, take to; प्रतिपत्तुमङ्ग घटते च न तव नृपयोग्यमर्हणम्<BR> Śi. 15. 22, 16. 24.<BR>—6 To recover, re-obtain, regain, receive; प्रायः स्वं महिमानं क्षोभात्<BR> प्रतिपद्यते जन्तुः Ś. 6. 31; Ku. 4. 16, 7. 22.<BR>—7 To admit, acknowledge; न मासे प्रतिपत्तासे मां चेन्मर्तासि मैथिलि<BR> Bk. 8. 95; Ś. 5. 23; प्रमदाः पतिवर्त्मगा इति प्रतिपन्नं हि विचेतनैरपि Ku. 4. 33.<BR>—8 To hold, grasp, seize; सुमन्त्रप्रतिपन्नरश्मिभिः R. 14. 47;<BR>—9 To consider, regard, deem, look upon; तद्धनुर्ग्रहणमेव राघवः<BR> प्रत्यपद्यत समर्थमुत्तरम् R. 11. 79.<BR>—10 To undertake, promise to do, take in hand; निर्वाहः प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु<BR> सतामेतद् हि गोत्रव्रतम् Mu. 2. 18; कार्यं त्वया नः प्रतिपन्नकल्पम्<BR> Ku. 3. 14; R. 10. 40.<BR>—11 To assent or agree to, consent; तथेति प्रतिपन्नाय R. 15. 93.<BR>—12 To do, perform, practise, observe; आचार प्रतिपद्यस्व Ś. 4;<BR> V. 2 ‘do the formal obeisance’; शासनमर्हतां प्रतिपद्यध्वम् Mu. 4.<BR>—18 ‘act up to or obey’.<BR>—13 To act or behave towards, deal, do anything to any one (with gen.<BR> or loc.); स कालयवनश्चापि किं कृष्णे प्रत्यपद्यत Hariv.; स भवान्<BR> मातृपितृवदस्मासु प्रतिपद्यताम् Mb.; कथमहं प्रतिपत्स्ये Ś. 5;<BR> न युक्तं भवतास्मासु प्रतिपत्तुमसांप्रतम् Mb.<BR>—14 To give or return (as a reply); कथं प्रतिवचनमपि न प्रतिपद्यसे<BR> Mu. 6; न जाने किं तातः प्रतिपत्स्यत इति Ś. 4.<BR>—15 To perceive, become aware of.<BR>—16 To know, understand, become acquainted with, learn, discover.<BR>—17 To roam, wander.<BR>—18 To take place, occur.<BR>—19 To restore.<BR>—20 To permit, allow.<BR>—21 To take place, happen.<BR>—22 To go back, return. ━(<i>Caus.</i>)<BR>—1 To give, present, bestow,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">Page1074-2</a>]<BR> confer upon, impart; अर्थिभ्यः प्रतिपाद्यमानमनिशं प्राप्नोति वृद्धिं<BR> पराम् Bh. 2. 16; Ms. 11. 4; गुणवते कन्या प्रतिपादनीया Ś. 4.<BR>—2 To substantiate, prove, establish by proof; उक्तमेवार्थमुदाहरणेन<BR> प्रतिपादयति.<BR>—3 To explain, expound.<BR>—4 To bring or lead back, convey or transport (to a place)<BR>—5 To regard, consider.<BR>—6 To assert, declare to be represent.<BR>—7 To procure.<BR>—8 To effect, accomplish.<BR>—9 To communicate, teach.<BR>—10 To appoint to, install (loc.).<BR>—11 To prepare, get ready.<BR>—12 To dispose off; एष हि न्यायो यदन्यत्र कृतार्थमन्यत्र प्रतिपाद्यते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 21<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिः|प्रतिपत्ति
प्रतिपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Getting, acquirement, gain; चन्द्रलोकप्रतिपत्तिः; स्वर्ग˚ &c.<BR>—2 Perception, observation, consciousness, (right) knowledge; वागर्थप्रतिपत्तये<BR> R. 1. 1; तयोरभेदप्रतिपत्तिरस्ति मे Bh. 3. 99; गुणिनामपि निजरूपप्रतिपत्तिः<BR> परत एव संभवति Vās.<BR>—3 Assent, compliance, acceptance; प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुखी Bk. 8. 95 ‘averse from compliance, unyielding’<BR>.<BR>—4 Admission, acknowledgment.<BR>—5 Assertion, statement.<BR>—6 Undertaking, beginning, commencement.<BR>—7 Action, proceeding, course of action, procedure; वयस्य का प्रतिपत्तिरत्र<BR> M. 4; Ku. 5. 42; विषादलुप्तप्रतिपत्तिविस्मितं सैन्यम् R. 3. 40 ‘which did not know what course of action to follow through dismay’<BR>.<BR>—8 Performance, doing, proceeding with; प्रस्तुतप्रतिपत्तये R. 15. 75.<BR>—9 Resolution, determination; कैकेय्याः प्रतिपत्तिर्हि कथं स्यान्मम<BR> वेदने Rām. 2. 22. 16; व्यवसायः प्रतिपत्तिनिष्ठुरः R. 8. 65.<BR>—10 News, intelligence; कर्मसिद्धावाशु प्रतिपत्तिमानय Mu. 4; Ś. 6.<BR>—11 Honour, respect, mark of distinction, respectful behaviour; सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकमियं<BR> दारेषु दृश्या त्वया Ś. 4. 17, 7. 1; R. 14. 22, 15. 12; तत् कस्मादेतस्मिन्<BR> महानुभावे प्रतिपत्तिमूढा तिष्ठसि Nāg. 1;<BR> यत्स महानुभावो वाङ्मात्रेणापि अकृतप्रतिपत्तिः अदक्षिणेति मां संभावयिष्यति Nāg. 2.<BR>—12 A method, means.<BR>—13 Intellect, intelligence.<BR>—14 Use, application.<BR>—15 Promotion, preferment, exaltation.<BR>—16 Fame, renown, reputation.<BR>—17 Boldness, assurance, confidence.<BR>—18 Conviction, proof.<BR>—19 A rite from which no advantage accrues.<BR>—20 The concluding portion of an action. (In Daṇḍaviveka, G. O. S. 52, p. 259,<BR> it means punishment of an offence.)<BR>—21 Disposing of a matter or a thing which has served the purpose of something<BR> else; यद् येन प्रयोजनेन सम्बद्धमुत्पद्यते तत् तदर्थमेव न्याय्यम् ।<BR> तस्यान्यत्र गमने प्रतिपत्तिरित्येतदुपपद्यते ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 19.<BR> Also cf. एष हि न्यायो यदन्यत्र कृतार्थमन्यत्र प्रतिपाद्यत इति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 22; cf. also प्रतिपत्तिश्च विविक्तकरणेन उपकरोति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 3. Hence प्रतिपत्तिकर्मन् means ‘a mere disposal’<BR> (as opposed to अर्थकर्मन्); किं शाखाप्रहरणं प्रतिपत्तिकर्म उतार्थकर्मेति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 10.<BR>—22 giving (दान); अपात्रे प्रतिपत्तिः Mb. 12. 26. 31;<BR> दानवारिरसिकाय विभूतेर्वश्मि तेऽस्मि सुतरां प्रतिपत्तिम् N. 21. 63.<BR>—23 Remedy (प्रतिविधान); प्रतिपत्तिं कां प्रत्यपद्यन्त मामकाः Mb. 7. 46. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिपत्तिदक्ष, प्रतिपत्तिपटहः, प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख, प्रतिपत्तिप्रदानम्, प्रतिपत्तिभेदः, प्रतिपत्तिविशारद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिदक्ष
प्रतिपत्तिः + -दक्ष <i>a.</i> knowing how to act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपटहः|प्रतिपत्तिपटह
प्रतिपत्तिः + -पटहः a kind of kettle drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख
प्रतिपत्तिः + -पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> obstinate, unyielding; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिप्रदानम्
प्रतिपत्तिः + -प्रदानम् Conferring promotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिभेदः|प्रतिपत्तिभेद
प्रतिपत्तिः + -भेदः difference of view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिविशारद
प्रतिपत्तिः + -विशारद <i>a.</i> knowing how to act, skilful, clever; वायव्यमभिमन्त्र्याथ<BR> प्रतिपत्तिविशारदः Mb. 1. 227. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1074-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिमत्|प्रतिपत्तिमन्त्
प्रतिपत्तिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intelligent,<BR>—2 Active, prompt.<BR>—3 Celebrated, famous.<BR>—4 Noble, dignified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Access, entrance, way.<BR>—2 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—3 Intelligence, intellect.<BR>—4 The first day of a lunar fortnight.<BR>—5 A kettle-drum.<BR>—6 An introductory stanza.<BR>—7 Rank.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिपच्चन्द्रः, प्रतिपत्तूर्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपच्चन्द्रः|प्रतिपच्चन्द्र|प्रतिपच्चंद्र
प्रतिपद् + -चन्द्रः the new moon (the moon on the first day) particularly<BR> revered and saluted by people; प्रतिपच्चन्द्रनिभोऽयमात्मजः R. 8. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तूर्यम्
प्रतिपद् + -तूर्यम् a kind of kettle-drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदा
प्रतिपदा, -दी<BR> The first day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदी
प्रतिपदा, -दी<BR> The first day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपन्न|प्रतिपन्नं
प्रतिपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gained, obtained.<BR>—2 Done, performed, effected, accomplished.<BR>—3 Undertaken, commenced.<BR>—4 Promised, engaged.<BR>—5 Agreed to, assented to; admitted, acknowledged.<BR>—6 Known, learnt, understood.<BR>—7 Answered, replied.<BR>—8 Proved, demonstrated; प्रमदाः प्रतिवर्त्मगा इति प्रतिपन्नं हि विचेतनैरपि Ku. 4. 33.<BR>—9 Approached, reached.<BR>—10 Conquered, overcome.<BR>—11 Conversant with, proficient in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादक|प्रतिपादकः
प्रतिपादक <i>a.</i> (-दिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Giving, granting, bestowing, imparting.<BR>—2 Demonstrating, supporting, proving, establishing.<BR>—3 Treating of, explaining, illustrating.<BR>—4 Promoting, furthering, advancing.<BR>—5 Effective, accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादनम्
प्रतिपादनम्^1<BR>—1 Giving, granting bestowing.<BR>—2 Demonstrating, proving, establishing.<BR>—3 Treating of, explaining, expounding, illustrating<BR>—4 Effecting, accomplishing, fulfilment.<BR>—5 Causing, producing.<BR>—6 Repeated action, practice.<BR>—7 Commencement; त्रेताविमोक्षसमये द्वापरप्रतिपादने Mb. 12. 141. 14.<BR>—8 Giving back, restoring.<BR>—9 Entrusting, appointing.<BR>—10 Action, worldly conduct.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादयितृ
प्रतिपादयितृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A teacher, instructor.<BR>—2 A giver, bestower.<BR>—3 A demonstrator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादित
प्रतिपादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Given, bestowed, granted, presented; यस्याः पितेव प्रतिपादितायाः Śi. 3. 36.<BR>—2 Established, proved, demonstrated.<BR>—3 Explained, expounded.<BR>—4 Declared, asserted.<BR>—5 Caused, produced.<BR>—6 Suddenly appeared, manifested; स वै तदैव प्रतिपादितां गिरं दैवीं<BR> परिज्ञातपरात्मनिर्णयः Bhāg. 4. 9. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाद्य
प्रतिपाद्य <i>a.</i> To be treated, discussed, explained, propounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाद्यमान
प्रतिपाद्यमान <i>a.</i> Given, offered; ह्यर्थिभ्यः प्रतिपाद्यमानमनिशं<BR> प्राप्नोति वृद्धिं पराम् Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादुक
प्रतिपादुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Producing, causing.<BR>—2 Ascertaining.<BR>—3 Making manifest or clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपानम्
प्रतिपानम्<BR>—1 Water for drinking.<BR>—2 Drinking, giving a drink; अश्वानां प्रतिपानं च खादनं चैन सोऽन्वशात्<BR> Rām. 2. 50. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाल्
प्रतिपाल् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To protect, preserve, guard, defend.<BR>—2 To wait for, await; महाराज तत् किं प्रतिपाल्यते Nāg. 5.<BR>—3 To act up to, obey.<BR>—4 To nourish, foster, rear.<BR>—5 To keep, maintain, observe, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालकः|प्रतिपालक
प्रतिपालकः A protector, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालनम्
प्रतिपालनम्<BR>—1 Guarding, protecting, defending.<BR>—2 Observance, following, practising; शृणु सखि साधनमेकं न कुलप्रतिपालनं श्रेयः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालित
प्रतिपालित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Protected, cherished.<BR>—2 Observed, practised, followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपिष्ट
प्रतिपिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rubbed.<BR>—2 Struck against each other (as swords).<BR>—3 Bruised, crushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपीडनम्
प्रतिपीडनम् Oppressing, molesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूज्
प्रतिपूज् €10 U.<BR>—1 To salute in return.<BR>—2 To honour, salute respectfully, esteem; प्रतिपूज्य वचस्तेषाम् Bhāg. 1. 2. 1.<BR>—3 To commend, approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजनम्
प्रतिपूजनम्, -पूजा<BR>—1 Doing homage, showing respect.<BR>—2 Mutual salutation, exchange of courtesies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजा
प्रतिपूजनम्, -पूजा<BR>—1 Doing homage, showing respect.<BR>—2 Mutual salutation, exchange of courtesies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजित
प्रतिपूजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Saluted in return.<BR>—2 Honoured, respectfully treated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपॄ
प्रतिपॄ <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fill up, fill completely.<BR>—2 To satisfy, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूरणम्
प्रतिपूरणम्<BR>—1 Filling, filling up.<BR>—2 Injecting (a fluid &c.)<BR>—3 Congestion (of the head).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूर्ण
प्रतिपूर्ण <i>a.</i> Expanded, broad; प्रतिपूर्णं च जघनम् Rām. 2. 9. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रणामः|प्रतिप्रणाम
प्रतिप्रणामः An obeisance in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रदानम्
प्रतिप्रदानम्<BR>—1 Returning, restoring.<BR>—2 Giving in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रभा
प्रतिप्रभा Reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रयाणम्
प्रतिप्रयाणम् Return, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रश्नः|प्रतिप्रश्न
प्रतिप्रश्नः<BR>—1 A question asked in return.<BR>—2 An answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसवः|प्रतिप्रसव
प्रतिप्रसवः<BR>—1 A counter-exception, an exception to an exception (wherein the general<BR> rule is shown to be applicable to cases falling under the exception);<BR> तृजकाभ्यां कर्तरि इत्यस्य प्रतिप्रसवोऽयं (याजकादिभिश्च) Sk.<BR>—2 A contrary effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रस्थातृ
प्रतिप्रस्थातृ <i>m.</i> An epithet of a priest who assists the Adhvaryū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रस्थानम्
प्रतिप्रस्थानम्<BR>—1 Joining the opposite party, going over to the enemy.<BR>—2 The office of the प्रतिप्रस्थातृ. प्रतिप्रास्थानिक = relating<BR> to this office; प्रतिप्रास्थानिकं कर्म सात्यकिस्तु करिष्यति Mb. 5. 141, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1075-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रहारः|प्रतिप्रहार
प्रतिप्रहारः A counter-blow, a blow in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्लवनम्
प्रतिप्लवनम् Leaping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफल्
प्रतिफल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To be reflected.<BR>—2 To rebound, recoil.<BR>—3 To requite, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलः|प्रतिफल|प्रतिफलं
प्रतिफलः, -प्रतिफलनम्<BR>—1 A reflection, reflected image, an image or shadow. स्फुरन्नानारत्नस्फटिकमयभित्तिप्रतिफलम्<BR> Ā. L. 14; न बिम्ब त्वद्बिम्बप्रतिफलनलाभादरुणितम् Ā. L.<BR>—2 Remuneration, requital.<BR>—3 Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलनम्
प्रतिफलः, -प्रतिफलनम्<BR>—1 A reflection, reflected image, an image or shadow. स्फुरन्नानारत्नस्फटिकमयभित्तिप्रतिफलम्<BR> Ā. L. 14; न बिम्ब त्वद्बिम्बप्रतिफलनलाभादरुणितम् Ā. L.<BR>—2 Remuneration, requital.<BR>—3 Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलित|प्रतिफलितं
प्रतिफलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Reflected; शिष्टैः कृष्ट्वा स्वचेतःप्रतिफलितवृथारन्ध्रमात्रप्रविष्टान् Mv. 6. 25.<BR>—2 Returned, requited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफुल्लक|प्रतिफुल्लकः
प्रतिफुल्लक <i>a.</i> Blossoming, full-blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्ध्|प्रतिबंध्
प्रतिबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To tie, fasten, bind (to); पीतप्रतिबद्धवत्साम् (धेनुम्) R. 2. 1.<BR>—2 To fix upon, direct towards; रसान्तरेषु प्रतिबद्धरागम् Ku. 7. 91.<BR>—3 To inlay, set, incase; यदि मणिस्त्रपुणि प्रतिबध्यते Pt. 1. 75;<BR> बहलानुरागकुरुविन्ददलप्रतिबद्धमध्यमिवं दिग्वलयम् Śi. 9. 8.<BR>—4 To obstruct, hinder, keep off or back, exclude, shut out;<BR> प्रतिबध्नाति हि श्रेयः पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R. 1. 79.<BR>—5 To stop, interrupt; मैनमन्तरा प्रतिबध्नीतम् Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबद्ध|प्रतिबद्धः
प्रतिबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied, fastened to; वनाय पीतप्रतिबद्धवत्सां यशोधनो धेनुमृषेर्मुमोच R. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Connected with, harmonizing with; रसान्तरेषु प्रतिबद्धरागम् Ku. 7. 91.<BR>—3 Hindered, obstructed, impeded.<BR>—4 Set, inlaid; यस्याः पुरा परिचयप्रतिबद्धबीजम् Māl. 10. 21.<BR>—5 Furnished with, possessing.<BR>—6 Entangled, involved.<BR>—7 Kept at a distance.<BR>—8 Disappointed.<BR>—9 Fixed, directed.<BR>—10 Attached or hanging to.<BR>—11 Excluded, cut off.<BR>—12 (In phil.) Invariably and inseparably connected and implied (as fire in smoke).<BR>—13 Wreathed (as a garland); सखि एकपार्श्वविषमप्रतिबद्धा खल्वेषा<BR> रचना Māl. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्दी|प्रतिबंदी
प्रतिब(व)न्दी <i>f.</i> A retort; हृदाभिनन्द्य प्रतिबन्द्यनुत्तरः<BR> N. 9. 17. See प्रतिबन्धी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवन्दी
प्रतिब(व)न्दी <i>f.</i> A retort; हृदाभिनन्द्य प्रतिबन्द्यनुत्तरः<BR> N. 9. 17. See प्रतिबन्धी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धः|प्रतिबन्ध|प्रतिबंध|प्रतिबंधः
प्रतिबन्धः<BR>—1 Binding or tying to.<BR>—2 Obstruction, impediment, obstacle; स तपःप्रतिबन्धमन्युना R. 8. 80;<BR> Mv. 5. 4; सिद्धीनामसाधनमनवतारणमप्रवेशनं वा प्रतिबन्धः,<BR> also प्रतिबन्धः प्रयोगो … … कोशक्षयः Kau. A. 2. 7. 26.<BR>—3 Opposition, resistance.<BR>—4 Investment, blockade, siege.<BR>—5 Connection.<BR>—6 Cessation.<BR>—7 Disappointment.<BR>—8 (In phil.) Invariable and inseparable connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबंधक|प्रतिबन्धकः
प्रतिबन्धक <i>a.</i> (-न्धिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Binding, fastening.<BR>—2 Impeding, obstructing, hindering.<BR>—3 Resisting, opposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धकः|प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबंधक
प्रतिबन्धक + .{@-कः@} A branch, shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धनम्
प्रतिबन्धनम्<BR>—1 Binding, tying.<BR>—2 Confinement.<BR>—3 Obstructing, impeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धवत्|प्रतिबन्धवन्त्
प्रतिबन्धवत् <i>a.</i> Full of obstacles, beset with difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धिन्|प्रतिबंधिन्
प्रतिबन्धिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fastening.<BR>—2 Hindering, obstructing.<BR>—3 Impeded, obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धिः|प्रतिबन्धि|प्रतिबंधिः
प्रतिबन्धिः, -न्धी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An objection.<BR>—2 An argument which equally affects the other side. (प्रतिबन्धि <i>m.</i><BR> also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धी
प्रतिबन्धिः, -न्धी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An objection.<BR>—2 An argument which equally affects the other side. (प्रतिबन्धि <i>m.</i><BR> also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्द्धृता
प्रतिबन्द्धृता Opposition, refutation; प्रबन्द्धृतास्तु प्रतिबन्द्धृता<BR> न ते N. 9. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाध्
प्रतिबाध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To repel, ward or keep off.<BR>—2 To check, restrain.<BR>—3 To pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधक
प्रतिबाधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Repelling, keeping off.<BR>—2 Preventing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधनम्
प्रतिबाधनम् Repelling, keeping off, rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधिन्
प्रतिबाधिन् <i>a.</i> Obstructing. ━<i>m.</i> An adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बनम्
प्रतिबिम्बनम्<BR>—1 Reflection.<BR>—2 Comparison; दृष्टान्तः पुनरेतेषां सर्वेषां प्रतिबिम्बनम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बयति
प्रतिबिम्बयति Den. P. To reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बित|प्रतिबिंबित
प्रतिबिम्बित <i>a.</i> Reflected, mirrored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुध्
प्रतिबुध् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To wake, wake up, awaken; तस्य सोऽहर्निशस्यान्ते प्रसुप्तं प्रतिबुध्यते<BR> Ms. 1. 74; Y. 1. 330.<BR>—2 To perceive, be conscious, know. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To awaken, rouse from sleep; प्रियया प्रतिबोध्यमानमपि सुप्तम्<BR> (हतहृदयम्) Ś. 6. 7.<BR>—2 To inform, make known, acqaint with, communicate; भावितात्मा भुवो<BR> भर्तुरथैनं प्रत्यबोधयत् R. 1. 74; Śi. 6. 8.<BR>—3 To charge or entrust with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्ध
प्रतिबुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Awakened, roused, wide awake; प्रतिबुद्धापि किं करिष्यामि Ś. 4;<BR> Māl. 4; Ms. 1. 74.<BR>—2 Restored to consciousness.<BR>—3 Opened, blown; अप्रतिबुद्धोऽपि चूतप्रसवोऽत्र बन्धनभङ्गसुरभिर्भवति Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Illuminated, enlightened.<BR>—5 Great, exalted.<BR>—6 Recognized, observed.<BR>—7 Celebrated, known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्धिः|प्रतिबुद्धि
प्रतिबुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Awakening.<BR>—2 Hostile purpose or intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधः|प्रतिबोध
प्रतिबोधः<BR>—1 Waking, awaking, being awakened; तदपोहितुमर्हसि प्रिये प्रतिबोधेन<BR> विषादमाशु मे R. 8. 54; अप्रतिबोधशायिनी 58 ‘sleeping not to wake again’<BR>; Ki. 6. 12, 12. 48.<BR>—2 Perception, knowledge.<BR>—3 Instruction.<BR>—4 Reason, reasoning faculty; किमुत याः प्रतिबोधवत्यः Ś. 5. 22.<BR>—5 Recollection; संमोहः खलु विस्मयनीयो न प्रतिबोधः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधक|प्रतिबोधकः
प्रतिबोधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Awakening.<BR>—2 Instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधकः|प्रतिबोधक
प्रतिबोधक + .{@-कः@} A teacher, instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधन
प्रतिबोधन <i>a.</i> Awakening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधनम्
प्रतिबोधन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Awakening.<BR>—2 Instructing, informing.<BR>—3 Knowledge, refinement, enlightenment; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधना
प्रतिबोधन + .{@-ना@} Awakening, recovering consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधित
प्रतिबोधित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Awakened.<BR>—2 Instructed, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिब्रू
प्रतिब्रू €2 P.<BR>—1 To answer; प्रत्यब्रवीच्चैनमिषुप्रयोगे तत्पूर्वभङ्गे वितथप्रयत्नः R. 2. 42.<BR>—2 (Ā.) To refuse, deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1076-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभज्
प्रतिभज् €1 U.<BR>—1 To receive back (as a share).<BR>—2 To fall to oneʼs share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभागः|प्रतिभाग
प्रतिभागः<BR>—1 Division.<BR>—2 A share, portion (given to a king as a tax) of oneʼs income, generally<BR> a sixth part; cf. षष्ठांशवृत्तेरपि धर्म एषः Ś. 5. 4; अरक्षितारं<BR> राजानं बलिषङ्भागहारिणम् । तमाहुः सर्वलोकस्य समग्रमलहारकम् ।<BR> Ms. 8. 308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा €2 P.<BR>—1 To shine, appear bright or luminous; प्रतिभान्त्यद्य वनानि केतकीनाम् Ghaṭ. 15.<BR>—2 To show oneself, become manifest.<BR>—3 To seem, appear; स्त्रीरत्नसृष्टिरपरा प्रतिभाति सा मे Ś. 2. 10;<BR> R. 2. 47; Ku. 2. 38, 6. 54.<BR>—4 To occur to, come into the mind of; as in नोत्तरं प्रतिभाति मे,<BR> इति प्रतिभाति मे मनः.<BR>—5 To fall to the lot or share of.<BR>—6 To seem fit or proper; appear good, please to; सा भार्या प्रतिभाति<BR> मे Ks.; Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा<BR>—1 An appearance, a look. —2 Light, splendour.<BR>—2 Intellect, understanding; सभेव भीमा विदधे गणानां निद्रा निरासं<BR> प्रतिभागुणस्य Ki. 16. 27; Vikr. 1. 18, 23.<BR>—4 Genius, bright conception, vivid imagination; (प्रज्ञा नवनवोन्मेषशालिनी<BR> प्रतिभा मता Rudra.).<BR>—5 An image, reflection.<BR>—6 Audacity, impudence.<BR>—7 Suitableness, agreeableness;<BR>—8 Sudden appearance, manifestation (स्फूर्ति); प्रतिभा त्वस्ति मे<BR> काचित्तां ब्रूयामनुमानतः Mb. 12. 260. 1.<BR>—9 Distraction (विक्षेप); निद्रां च प्रतिभां चैव ज्ञानाभ्यासेन तत्त्ववित्<BR> (विनिवर्तयेत्); Mb. 12. 274. 7, 316. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिभान्वित, प्रतिभामुख, प्रतिभाहानिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान्वित|प्रतिभान्वितः
प्रतिभा + -अन्वित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 endowed with genius, intelligent,<BR>—2 audacious, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभामुख|प्रतिभामुखः
प्रतिभा + -मुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bold, confident.<BR>—2 quickwitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाहानिः|प्रतिभाहानि
प्रतिभा + -हानिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 darkness.<BR>—2 absence of intellect or genius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभात
प्रतिभात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bright, luminous.<BR>—2 Known, understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानम्
प्रतिभानम्<BR>—1 Light, splendour.<BR>—2 Intellect or understanding, brightness of conception; दूतः स्यात्<BR> प्रतिभानवान् H. 3. 19.<BR>—3 Readiness of wit, presence of mind; कालावबोधः प्रतिभानवत्त्वम्<BR> Māl. 3. 11; कथायोगेषु वाग्मित्वं प्रागल्भ्यं प्रतिभानवत्त्वं च Kau. A. 1. 9;<BR> दमघोषसुतेन कश्चन प्रतिशिष्टः प्रतिभानवानथ Śi. 16. 1.<BR>—4 Confidence, boldness, audacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानवत्|प्रतिभानवन्त्
प्रतिभानवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Splendid, bright.<BR>—2 Ready-witted, prompt.<BR>—3 Bold.<BR>—4 Intelligent; H. 3. 19; कच्चिज्जानपदो विद्वान् दक्षिणः प्रतिभानवान्<BR> Rām. 2. 100. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावत्|प्रतिभावन्त्
प्रतिभावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bright.<BR>—2 Intelligent, shrewd.<BR>—3 Confident, bold. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावः|प्रतिभाव
प्रतिभावः Corresponding disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाष्
प्रतिभाष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To speak in return, reply or answer; तं भीतंकारमाक्रुश्य रावणः<BR> प्रत्यभाषत Bk. 5. 39.<BR>—2 To tell, relate.<BR>—3 To say after one, speak after hearing.<BR>—4 To name, call; कामिनि तामुपगीतिं प्रतिभाषन्ते महाकवयः Śrut. 6.<BR>—5 To address or speak to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाषा
प्रतिभाषा An answer, a reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभास्
प्रतिभास् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To appear or look like.<BR>—3 To become clear, manifest oneself.<BR>—4 To be reflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासः|प्रतिभास
प्रतिभासः<BR>—1 Occurring to, or flashing across, the mind at once, (sudden) perception;<BR> वाच्यवैचित्र्यप्रतिभासादेव K. P. 10.<BR>—2 A look, appearance.<BR>—3 Illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासनम्
प्रतिभासनम् Look, appearance, semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिद्
प्रतिभिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To break through, pierce, penetrate.<BR>—2 To disclose, betray.<BR>—3 To reproach, abuse, censure; प्रतिभिद्य कान्तमपराधकृतम् Śi. 9. 58;<BR> R. 19. 22.<BR>—4 To reject, disown.<BR>—5 To touch, be in close contact with; चन्द्रेण नित्यं प्रतिभिन्नमौलेश्चूडामणेः<BR> किं ग्रहणं हरस्य Ku. 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिन्न
प्रतिभिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pierced through.<BR>—2 Closely connected with.<BR>—3 Divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदः|प्रतिभेद
प्रतिभेदः<BR>—1 Splitting, dividing.<BR>—2 Discovery.<BR>—3 Betrayal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदनम्
प्रतिभेदनम्<BR>—1 Piercing, penetrating.<BR>—2 Cutting, splitting, cleaving.<BR>—3 Putting out (as the eyes).<BR>—4 Dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभूः
प्रतिभूः A bail, surety, guarantee; सौभाग्यलाभप्रतिभूः पदानाम्<BR> Vikr. 1. 9; Y. 2. 10, 54; N. 14. 4; सहग्राहिणः प्रतिभुवः … … अस्य<BR> कर्मच्छेदं वहेयुः Kau. A. 2. 7. 25; यच्च प्रतिभ्वो विभवेऽपि शक्ये<BR> न प्रार्थयन्ति स्म नराः परेभ्यः Bu. C. 2. 10; यदि मे प्रतिभूश्चतुर्षु<BR> राजन् भवसि त्वं न तपोवनं श्रयिष्ये Bu. C. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावः|प्रतिभाव
प्रतिभावः Counter-part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभोगः|प्रतिभोग
प्रतिभोगः Enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभोजनम्
प्रतिभोजनम् Prescribed diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमन्त्रणम्
प्रतिमन्त्रणम् An answer, reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमर्शः|प्रतिमर्श
प्रतिमर्शः A powder used as a sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा €3. €4 Ā. To compare, liken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा <i>m.</i> Ved. A creator, maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 An image, a likeness, statue, figure, an idol; पुरः परार्ध्यप्रतिमागृहायाः R. 16. 39.<BR>—2 Resemblance, similitude; oft. in comp. in the sense of ‘like, similar, or equal to’<BR>; देवप्रतिम, अप्रतिम &c.; गुरोः कुशानुप्रतिमात्<BR> R. 2. 49; पतत्पतङ्गप्रतिमस्तपोनिधिः Śi. 1. 12.<BR>—3 A reflection, reflected image; मुखमिन्दुरुज्ज्वलकपोलमतः प्रतिमाच्छलेन<BR> सुदृशामविशत् Śi. 9. 48, 73; R. 7. 64, 12. 100.<BR>—4 A measure, extent.<BR>—5 The part of an elephantʼs head between the tusks.<BR>—6 A symbol.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिमागत, प्रतिमागृहम्, प्रतिमागेहम्, प्रतिमाचन्द्रः, प्रतिमापरिचारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमागत
प्रतिमा + -गत <i>a.</i> present in an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमागृहम्
प्रतिमा + -गृहम्, -गेहम् A statue-house; Pratimā 3; R. 16. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमागेहम्
प्रतिमा + -गृहम्, -गेहम् A statue-house; Pratimā 3; R. 16. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमाचन्द्रः|प्रतिमाचन्द्र
प्रतिमा + -चन्द्रः the reflected moon, reflection of the moon; उवास प्रतिमाचन्द्रः<BR> प्रसन्नानामपामिव R. 10. 65; so प्रतिमेन्दुः, प्रतिमाशशाङ्कः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमापरिचारकः|प्रतिमापरिचारक
प्रतिमा + -परिचारकः an attendant upon an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमानम्
प्रतिमानम्<BR>—1 A model, pattern; सोऽर्जुनेन हतः कर्णः प्रतिमानं धनुष्मताम् Mb. 8. 9. 18.<BR>—2 An image, idol.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">Page1078-1</a>]<BR>—3 Likeness, similitude, similarity; हेरम्बकण्ठरसितप्रतिमानमेति Māl. 9. 3.<BR>—4 A weight; रत्नसारफल्गुकुप्यानामर्घप्रतिवर्णकप्रतिमानमानोन्मानावमानभाण्डम्<BR> Kau. A. 2. 7. 25.<BR>—5 The part of an elephantʼs head between the tusks and below the वाहित्थ;<BR> Mb. 8. 28. 38; also 6. 46. 29; पृथुप्रतिमानभाग &c. Śi. 5. 36; Mātaṅga L. 5. 7, 6. 8.<BR>—6 A reflection.<BR>—7 A picture.<BR>—8 Ved. An adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1077-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमित
प्रतिमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Imitated, copied.<BR>—2 Compared.<BR>—3 Reflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमार्गकः|प्रतिमार्गक|प्रतिमार्ग्गक
प्रतिमार्गकः The city of Hariścandra <i>i. e.</i> the magical illusion<BR> of a city in the sky; हरिश्चन्द्रपुरं शोभमुद्रकः प्रतिमार्गकः<BR> Trik.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुच्
प्रतिमुच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To free, liberate, release, set free; गृहीतप्रतिमुक्तस्य R. 4. 43;<BR> अमुं तुरङ्गं प्रतिमोक्तुमर्हसि 3. 46.<BR>—2 To put on, wear, accoutre or arm oneself with; प्रतिमुञ्च शुभ्रं यज्ञोपवीतम्.<BR>—3 To quit, leave, abandon.<BR>—4 To throw, cast, or discharge at.<BR>—5 To pay off (a debt.).<BR>—6 To return, restore.<BR>—7 To fasten, bind; तमेकदा मणिं कण्ठे प्रतिमुच्य महाप्रभम् Bhāg. 10. 56. 13.<BR>—8 To assume a form. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To liberate, release.<BR>—2 To rescue, save, deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुक्त|प्रतिमुक्तः
प्रतिमुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Put on, worn, applied.<BR>—2 Tied, bound, fastened; Bhāg. 3. 18. 10.<BR>—3 Armed, accoutred.<BR>—4 Liberated, released.<BR>—5 Restored, returned.<BR>—6 Flung, hurled.<BR>—7 Thrown, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुहुः
प्रतिमुहुः (= emphatic for मुहुः) Often and often; प्रतिमुहुर्द्राङ्गितप्रेयसी N. 20. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोक्षः|प्रतिमोक्ष
प्रतिमोक्षः, प्रतिमोक्षणम् Liberation, deliverance; प्रतिमोक्षणम्<BR> remission (of taxes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोक्षणम्
प्रतिमोक्षः, प्रतिमोक्षणम् Liberation, deliverance; प्रतिमोक्षणम्<BR> remission (of taxes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोचनम्
प्रतिमोचनम्<BR>—1 Loosening.<BR>—2 Requital, retaliation, retribution; वैरप्रतिमोचनाय R. 14. 41.<BR>—3 Liberation, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्
प्रतियत् €1 Ā. To try; वयमप्याश्रमपीडा यथा न भविष्यति तथा<BR> प्रतियतिष्यामहे Ś. 1. 32/33 (v. l.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To restore, return.<BR>—2 To retaliate, requite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्न|प्रतियत्नः
प्रतियत्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Troubling about.<BR>—2 Active, vigorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्नः|प्रतियत्न
प्रतियत्न + .{@-त्नः@}<BR>—1 An effort, endeavour, exertion.<BR>—2 Preparation, elaboration; ‘प्रतियत्नस्तु संस्कारः’ Vaijayantī;<BR> सुगन्धितामप्रतियत्नपूर्वां बिभ्रन्ति यत्र प्रमदाय पुंसाम् Śi. 3. 54.<BR>—3 Making complete or perfect.<BR>—4 Imparting a new quality or virtue; सतो गुणान्तराधानं प्रतियत्नः<BR> Kāśi. on P. II. 3. 53.<BR>—5 Wish, desire.<BR>—6 Opposition, resistance.<BR>—7 Retaliation, retribution, revenge.<BR>—8 Making captive, taking prisoner.<BR>—9 Favour.<BR>—10 Acting well or properly.<BR>—11 Comprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातनम्
प्रतियातनम् Requital, retaliation; as in वैरप्रतियातनम्; अयं<BR> हि कालोऽस्य दुरात्मनो वै पार्थस्य वैरप्रतियातनाय Mb. 8. 90. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातना
प्रतियातना A picture, an image, statue; अनिर्विदा या विदधे विधात्रा<BR> पृथ्वी पृथिव्याः प्रतियातनेव Śi. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियम्
प्रतियम् €1 P. To restore, return; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिया
प्रतिया €2 P.<BR>—1 To go back, return; एतावदुक्त्वा प्रतियातुकामं शिष्यं महर्षेर्नृपतिर्निषिध्य<BR> R. 5. 18, 8. 91.<BR>—2 To equal, be a match for; अयं नृपः कः प्रतियाति कर्मभिः Bhāg. 5. 15. 9.<BR>—3 To be returned, requited; या माऽभजन्दुर्जरगेहशृङ्खलाः संवृश्च्य<BR> तद्वः प्रतियातु साधुना Bhāg. 10. 32. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियात
प्रतियात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Resisted, opposed.<BR>—2 Turned, returned.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतियातनिद्र, प्रतियातबुद्धि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातनिद्र
प्रतियात + -निद्र <i>a.</i> awakened, awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातबुद्धि
प्रतियात + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> one whose mind is turned towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियानम्
प्रतियानम् Return, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियुध्
प्रतियुध् €4 Ā. To encounter in fight, oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियुद्धम्
प्रतियुद्धम् Fighting against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधः|प्रतियोध
प्रतियोधः, प्रतियोधिन् <i>m.</i> An adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधिन्
प्रतियोधः, प्रतियोधिन् <i>m.</i> An adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगः|प्रतियोग
प्रतियोगः<BR>—1 Being or forming a counter-part of anything.<BR>—2 Opposition, resistance; यत्तः परेषां प्रतियोगशङ्कितः Bhāg. 4. 10. 22, 5. 14. 1.<BR>—3 Contradiction.<BR>—4 Cooperation.<BR>—5 An antidote, a remedy.<BR>—6 A rejoinder; प्रतियोगार्थिनी काचित् गृहीत्वा चूतवल्लरीम् Bu. C. 4. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिक
प्रतियोगिक <i>a.</i> Antithetical, correlative, relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिन्
प्रतियोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Opposing, counteracting, impeding.<BR>—2 Related or corresponding to, being or forming a counter-part of (anything);<BR> often used in works on Nyāya; as a घट is the प्रतियोगी of घटाभाव;<BR> (यस्याभावो विवक्ष्यते स प्रतियोगी).<BR>—3 Co-operating with.<BR>—4 Equally matched. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An adversary, opponent, enemy; आर्थो विरोधः शक्तेन जातो नः प्रतियोगिना<BR> Mv. 2. 7; दहत्यशेषं प्रतियोगिगर्वम् Vikr. 1. 117.<BR>—2 A counter-part, match.<BR>—3 A partner, an associate.<BR>—4 An object dependent upon another.<BR>—5 A counter-part, counter-entity; प्रतियोगिज्ञानाधीनज्ञानविषयत्वमभावलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिता
प्रतियोगिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Opposition.<BR>—2 Dependent existence.<BR>—3 Being a counter-part.<BR>—4 Partnership, co-operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगित्वम्
प्रतियोगिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Opposition.<BR>—2 Dependent existence.<BR>—3 Being a counter-part.<BR>—4 Partnership, co-operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोद्धृ
प्रतियोद्धृ<BR>—1 An opponent, adversary.<BR>—2 One who begins a battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधनम्
प्रतियोधनम् Assailing in turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षणम्
प्रतिरक्षणम्, -रक्षा<BR> Safety, preservation, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षा
प्रतिरक्षणम्, -रक्षा<BR> Safety, preservation, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरत
प्रतिरत <i>a.</i> Delighting in, zealous for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरम्भः|प्रतिरम्भ|प्रतिरंभ|प्रतिरंभः
प्रतिरम्भः Passion, rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुध्
प्रतिरुध् €7 U.<BR>—1 To obstruct, stop; oppose, resist.<BR>—2 To blockade, besiege.<BR>—3 To impair, disable.<BR>—4 To blame, accuse.<BR>—5 To hide, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुद्ध
प्रतिरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Impeded, obstructed, hindered.<BR>—2 Interrupted.<BR>—3 Impaired.<BR>—4 Disabled.<BR>—5 Invested, blockaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1078-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधः|प्रतिरोध
प्रतिरोधः<BR>—1 Impediment, obstruction, hindrance.<BR>—2 Siege, blockade.<BR>—3 An opponent.<BR>—4 Concealing.<BR>—5 Theft, robbery.<BR>—6 Censure, despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधक|प्रतिरोधकः
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्, -द्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstructing.<BR>—2 Besieging. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An opponent.<BR>—2 A robber, thief; कोदण्डपाणि निनदत्प्रतिरोधकानामापातदुष्प्रसहमाविरभूदनीकम्<BR> M. 5. 10; Śi. 1. 32.<BR>—3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधिन्
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्, -द्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstructing.<BR>—2 Besieging. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An opponent.<BR>—2 A robber, thief; कोदण्डपाणि निनदत्प्रतिरोधकानामापातदुष्प्रसहमाविरभूदनीकम्<BR> M. 5. 10; Śi. 1. 32.<BR>—3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोद्धृ
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्, -द्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obstructing.<BR>—2 Besieging. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An opponent.<BR>—2 A robber, thief; कोदण्डपाणि निनदत्प्रतिरोधकानामापातदुष्प्रसहमाविरभूदनीकम्<BR> M. 5. 10; Śi. 1. 32.<BR>—3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधनम्
प्रतिरोधनम् Opposing, obstructing; स हि स्वाम्यादतिक्रामेदृतूनां<BR> प्रतिरोधनात् Ms. 9. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरूढ
प्रतिरूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Entered, possessed.<BR>—2 Established again.<BR>—3 Imitated; गतिस्मितप्रेक्षणभाषणादिषु प्रियाः प्रियस्य प्रतिरूढमूर्तयः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 30. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलभ्
प्रतिलभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To recover, regain.<BR>—2 To get, obtain.<BR>—3 To learn, understand.<BR>—4 To expect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलम्भः|प्रतिलम्भ|प्रतिलंभः
प्रतिलम्भः<BR>—1 Getting, obtaining, receiving.<BR>—2 Censure, abuse, reviling; अन्यतः कथमदः प्रतिलम्भः N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलाभः|प्रतिलाभ
प्रतिलाभः Taking or obtaining back, taking, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलिखित
प्रतिलिखित <i>p. p.</i> Answered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलेखनम्
प्रतिलेखनम्, -ना<BR> The regular cleaning of all implements or objects for daily use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलेखना
प्रतिलेखनम्, -ना<BR> The regular cleaning of all implements or objects for daily use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवच्
प्रतिवच् €2 P. To speak in reply, answer, reply to; न चेद्रहस्यं<BR> प्रतिवक्तुमर्हसि Ku. 5. 40; R. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचनम्
प्रतिवचनम्<BR>—1 An answer, reply, परभृतविरुतं कलं यथा प्रतिवचनीकृतमेभिरीदृशम्<BR> Ś. 4. 9; न ददाति प्रतिवचनं विकयकाले शठो वणिङ् मौनी Kalāvilāsa.<BR>—2 An echo.<BR>—3 A dependent or final clause in a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवक्तव्य
प्रतिवक्तव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be replied, answered.<BR>—2 To be contradicted.<BR>—3 To be disputed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचस्
प्रतिवचस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 An answer.<BR>—2 An echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्य|प्रतिवाक्यं
प्रतिवाक्य <i>a.</i> Answerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्यम्
प्रतिवाक्य + .{@-क्यम्@} A reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाच्
प्रतिवाच् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An answer, reply; पतिवाचमदत्त केशवः शपमानाय न चेदिभूभुजे Śi. 16. 25.<BR>—2 Calling out to.<BR>—3 Barking in return (as a dog).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाचिकम्
प्रतिवाचिकम् An answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवद्
प्रतिवद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To speak in reply, answer; प्रियंवदः प्रत्यवदत् सुरेश्वरम् R. 3. 64.<BR>—2 To speak, utter.<BR>—3 To repeat.<BR>—4 To speak in opposition; किंचित् किंचित् प्रतिवदंस्तूष्णीमासं मुहुर्मुहुः<BR> Mb. 5. 136. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादः|प्रतिवाद
प्रतिवादः<BR>—1 An answer, a rejoinder, reply.<BR>—2 Refusal, rejection; उद्यतस्य हि कामस्य प्रतिवादो न शस्यते Bhāg. 3. 22. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादिन्
प्रतिवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Answering, replying.<BR>—2 Contradicting. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A defendant, respondent (in law); कारणे प्रतिवादिनि Y.<BR>—2 An opponent in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवध्
प्रतिवध् €1 P. To beat back, ward off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवन्द्
प्रतिवन्द् €1 Ā. To receive deferentially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवप्
प्रतिवप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sow.<BR>—2 Plant or fix in, implant; प्रत्युप्तस्येव दयिते U. 3. 46; Māl. 5. 10.<BR>—3 To set, stud (as with jewels); see प्रत्युप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवापः|प्रतिवाप
प्रतिवापः Addition of substances to medicines either during or after decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवर्णकम्
प्रतिवर्णकम् The rate of barter; रत्नसारफल्गुकुप्यानामर्घप्रतिवर्णकप्रतिमानमानोन्मानावामानभाण्डम्<BR> Kau. A. 2. 7. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवर्तनम्
प्रतिवर्तनम् Returning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवसथः|प्रतिवसथ
प्रतिवसथः A village, settlement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवहनम्
प्रतिवहनम् Leading back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाणिः|प्रतिवाणि
प्रतिवाणिः <i>f.</i> An answer, reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारः|प्रतिवार
प्रतिवारः, -प्रतिवारणम्<BR> Warding or keeping off, keeping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारणम्
प्रतिवारः, -प्रतिवारणम्<BR> Warding or keeping off, keeping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवार्ता|प्रतिवार्त्ता
प्रतिवार्ता Account, information, news, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासिन्
प्रतिवासिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Dwelling near, neighbouring. ━<i>m.</i> A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविघातः|प्रतिविघात
प्रतिविघातः Striking back, defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविज्ञा
प्रतिविज्ञा €9 P. To acknowledge gratefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविद्
प्रतिविद् I. €2 P. To acknowledge, receive. ━II. €6 P. To get, obtain. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To communicate, inform.<BR>—2 To deliver, give, grant.<BR>—3 restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधा
प्रतिविधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To counteract, correct, repair, retaliate, remedy, take steps against;<BR> अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं तु मे कंचित् कथय येन स प्रतिविधीयेत U. 1;<BR> क्षिप्रमेव कस्मान्न प्रतिविहितमार्येण Mu. 3.<BR>—2 To dispose, arrange, prepare.<BR>—3 To despatch, send.<BR>—4 To doom, condemn; U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधातव्यम्
प्रतिविधातव्यम् (impers.) Care should be taken; Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधानम्
प्रतिविधानम्<BR>—1 Counteracting, counter-working, taking steps against.<BR>—2 Arrangement, array.<BR>—3 Prevention.<BR>—4 Substituted ceremony, subsidiary rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधिः|प्रतिविधि
प्रतिविधिः<BR>—1 Retaliation.<BR>—2 A remedy, means of counteracting; तत्र प्रतिविधिं सम्यगात्मयोगेन<BR> साधये Bhāg. 10. 25. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविभागः|प्रतिविभाग
प्रतिविभागः Distribution, apportionment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविरुद्ध
प्रतिविरुद्ध <i>a.</i> Rebellious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविशिष्ट
प्रतिविशिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Most excellent.<BR>—2 Peculiar, better or worse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविशेषः|प्रतिविशेष
प्रतिविशेषः Peculiarity, singularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविशेषणम्
प्रतिविशेषणम् Detailed specification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशः|प्रतिवेश
प्रतिवेशः<BR>—1 A neighbour.<BR>—2 The residences of a neighbour, neighbourhood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिवेशवासिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशवासिन्
प्रतिवेशः + -वासिन् <i>a.</i> living in the neighbourhood. ━(<i>m.</i>) a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1079-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशिन्
प्रतिवेशिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> A neighbour; दृष्टिं हे प्रतिवेशिनि क्षणमिहाप्यस्मद्गृहे<BR> दास्यसि S. D.; Mk. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश्यः|प्रतिवेश्य
प्रतिवेश्यः A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेष्टित
प्रतिवेष्टित <i>p. p.</i> Rolled back, reverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्याहारः|प्रतिव्याहार
प्रतिव्याहारः An answer, reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूढ
प्रतिव्यूढ <i>p. p.</i> Drawn out in battle-array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूहः|प्रतिव्यूह
प्रतिव्यूहः<BR>—1 Arraying an army against an enemy.<BR>—2 A multitude, collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशक्
प्रतिशक् To be a match for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशमः|प्रतिशम
प्रतिशमः Cessation; प्रतिज्ञातो हि भवता दुःखप्रतिशमो मम<BR> Mb. 5. 191. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशयनम्
प्रतिशयनम् The act of lying down without food before a deity to<BR> secure some desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशयित
प्रतिशयित <i>a.</i> One who lies down without food before a deity<BR> to secure his desired object; अनया च किलास्मै प्रतिशयिताय स्वप्ने<BR> समादिष्टम् Dk. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशापः|प्रतिशाप
प्रतिशापः A curse for curse, a curse in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशासनम्
प्रतिशासनम्<BR>—1 Giving orders, sending on an errand, ordering.<BR>—2 Ordering or despatching an inferior after calling him to attend.<BR>—3 Counter-manding.<BR>—4 A rival command or authority; अप्रतिशासनं जगत् R. 8. 27 ‘completely under the sway of one ruler’<BR>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशास्तिः|प्रतिशास्ति
प्रतिशास्तिः <i>f.</i> Sending on an errand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशिष्ट|प्रतिशिष्टं
प्रतिशिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ordered, sent; दमधोषसुतेन कश्चन प्रतिशिष्टः प्रतिभानवानथ Śi. 16. 1.<BR>—2 Dismissed, rejected.<BR>—3 Famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशीन
प्रतिशीन <i>a.</i> Fluid, dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशीर्षकम्
प्रतिशीर्षकम् Redemption, ransom. (See Mallināthaʼs commentary on<BR> R. 2. 55 where he gives this word as a synonym of निष्क्रय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्या
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानम्, प्रतिश्यायः A catarrh or cold; नारीप्रसङ्गः<BR> शिरसोऽभितापो धूमो रजः शीतमतिप्रतापः । संधारणं मूत्रपुरीषयोश्च<BR> सद्यः प्रतिश्यायनिदानमुक्तम् ॥ Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्यानम्
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानम्, प्रतिश्यायः A catarrh or cold; नारीप्रसङ्गः<BR> शिरसोऽभितापो धूमो रजः शीतमतिप्रतापः । संधारणं मूत्रपुरीषयोश्च<BR> सद्यः प्रतिश्यायनिदानमुक्तम् ॥ Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्यायः|प्रतिश्याय
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानम्, प्रतिश्यायः A catarrh or cold; नारीप्रसङ्गः<BR> शिरसोऽभितापो धूमो रजः शीतमतिप्रतापः । संधारणं मूत्रपुरीषयोश्च<BR> सद्यः प्रतिश्यायनिदानमुक्तम् ॥ Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रयः|प्रतिश्रय
प्रतिश्रयः<BR>—1 A shelter, asylum; प्रतिश्रयार्थी तद्वेश्म ब्राह्मणस्य जगाम ह Mb. 1. 165. 3.<BR>—2 A house, dwelling, residence; प्रतिश्रयं प्राप्य समीक्ष्य शून्यम्<BR> Rām. 3. 58. 19; Y. 1. 210. चण्डालश्वपचानां तु बहिर्ग्रामात् प्रतिश्रयः Ms. 10. 51.<BR>—3 An assembly.<BR>—4 A sacrificial hall.<BR>—5 Help, assistance.<BR>—6 A promise.<BR>—7 A receptacle.<BR>—8 A Jain-monastery.<BR>—9 An alms-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रु
प्रतिश्रु €5 P. To promise (with dat. of person to whom the promise<BR> is made); तस्यै प्रतिश्रुत्य रघुप्रवीरस्तदीप्सितम् R. 14. 29, 2. 65, 3. 67, 15. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवः|प्रतिश्रव
प्रतिश्रवः<BR>—1 Assent, agreement, promise; नाम्ना दशरथो राजा श्रीमान्सत्यप्रतिश्रवः<BR> Rām. 1. 11. 2.<BR>—2 An echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवणम्
प्रतिश्रवणम्<BR>—1 Listening to; प्रतिश्रवणसंभाषे शयानो न समाचरेत् Ms. 2. 195.<BR>—2 Promising, assenting; agreeing.<BR>—3 A promise.<BR>—4 Maintaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत्
प्रतिश्रुत्, प्रतिश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A promise; इष्टं नः प्रति ते प्रतिश्रुतिरभूद्याद्य स्वराह्लादिनी N. 5. 135.<BR>—2 An answer.<BR>—3 An echo, reverberation; वियद्गतः पुष्पकचन्द्रशालाः क्षणं प्रतिश्रुन्मुखराः<BR> करोति R. 13. 40, 16. 31; Śi. 17. 42.<BR>—4 (Also प्रत्याश्रुत) The sacrificial formula “अस्ति श्रौषट्” spoken<BR> by the Āgnīdhra priest in reply to the Adhvaryu priest who addresses<BR> him by saying ओ श्रावय; cf. ‘अस्तु श्रौषडित्याग्नीध्रः प्रत्याश्रावयति’<BR> सत्याषाढसूत्र 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुतिः|प्रतिश्रुति
प्रतिश्रुत्, प्रतिश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A promise; इष्टं नः प्रति ते प्रतिश्रुतिरभूद्याद्य स्वराह्लादिनी N. 5. 135.<BR>—2 An answer.<BR>—3 An echo, reverberation; वियद्गतः पुष्पकचन्द्रशालाः क्षणं प्रतिश्रुन्मुखराः<BR> करोति R. 13. 40, 16. 31; Śi. 17. 42.<BR>—4 (Also प्रत्याश्रुत) The sacrificial formula “अस्ति श्रौषट्” spoken<BR> by the Āgnīdhra priest in reply to the Adhvaryu priest who addresses<BR> him by saying ओ श्रावय; cf. ‘अस्तु श्रौषडित्याग्नीध्रः प्रत्याश्रावयति’<BR> सत्याषाढसूत्र 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत|प्रतिश्रुतः
प्रतिश्रुत <i>p. p.</i> Promised, agreed, assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुतम्
प्रतिश्रुत + .{@-तम्@} A promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिध्
प्रतिषिध् €1 P. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To prevent, ward off, restrain; Ms. 2. 206; इति शत्रुषु चेन्द्रियेषु<BR> च प्रतिषिद्धप्रसरेषु जाग्रतौ R. 8. 23.<BR>—2 To forbid, prohibit; नृपतेः प्रतिषिद्धमेव तत् कृतवान् पङ्क्तिरथो<BR> विलङ्घ्य यत् R. 9. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्ध|प्रतिषिद्धः
प्रतिषिद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Forbidden, prohibited, disallowed, refused.<BR>—2 Contradicted.<BR>—3 Refractory, perverse; प्रतिषिद्धापि वामैषा जातिः Ś. 6. 19/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधः|प्रतिषेध
प्रतिषेधः<BR>—1 Keeping or warding off, driving away, expulsion; अशेषविध्नप्रतिषेधदक्षमन्त्राक्षतानांमिव<BR> दिङ्मुखेषु Vikr. 1. 8.<BR>—2 Prohibition; as in शास्त्रप्रतिषेधः; विधिप्रतिषेधयोः प्रतिषेधो बलीयान्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 2; प्राप्तिपूर्वो हि प्रतिषेधो भवति इति अवाक्यशेषता<BR> अध्यवसीयते ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 22.<BR>—3 Denial, refusal.<BR>—4 Negation, contradiction.<BR>—5 A negative particle.<BR>—6 An exception.<BR>—7 (In Rhet.). Enforcing or reminding of a prohibition.<BR>—8 (In Drama.) An obstacle to obtaining the desired object.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिषेधाक्षरम्, प्रतिषेधोक्तिः, प्रतिषेधोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधाक्षरम्
प्रतिषेधः + -अक्षरम्, -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> words of denial, refusal; प्रतिषेधाक्षरविक्लवाभिरामम् Ś. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधोक्तिः|प्रतिषेधोक्ति
प्रतिषेधः + -अक्षरम्, -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> words of denial, refusal; प्रतिषेधाक्षरविक्लवाभिरामम् Ś. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधोपमा
प्रतिषेधः + -उपमा one of the several kinds of Upamā mentioned by Daṇḍin.<BR> It is thus explained: न जातु शक्तिरिन्दोस्ते मुखेन प्रतिगर्जितुम् । कलङ्किनो<BR> जडस्येति प्रतिषेधोपमैव सा ॥ Kāv. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधक|प्रतिषेधकः
प्रतिषेधक, -प्रतिषेद्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Warding off, prohibiting, preventing.<BR>—2 Preventive. ━<i>m.</i> A hinderer, prohibitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेद्धृ
प्रतिषेधक, -प्रतिषेद्धृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Warding off, prohibiting, preventing.<BR>—2 Preventive. ━<i>m.</i> A hinderer, prohibitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधनम्
प्रतिषेधनम्<BR>—1 Keeping or warding off, preventing.<BR>—2 Prohibition.<BR>—3 Denial, refusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कः|प्रतिष्क
प्रतिष्कः, -प्रतिष्कसः<BR> A spy, messenger, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कसः|प्रतिष्कस
प्रतिष्कः, -प्रतिष्कसः<BR> A spy, messenger, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कशः|प्रतिष्कश
प्रतिष्कशः<BR>—1 A spy, emissary.<BR>—2 A whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कषः|प्रतिष्कष
प्रतिष्कषः A whip, leather-thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टब्ध
प्रतिष्टब्ध <i>p. p.</i> Obstruted, impeded, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टम्भः|प्रतिष्टम्भ|प्रतिष्टंभ|प्रतिष्टंभः
प्रतिष्टम्भः Obstruction, impediment, resistance, opposition, obstacle;<BR> बाहुप्रतिष्टम्भविवृद्धमन्युः R. 2. 32, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठा
प्रतिष्ठा €1 P.<BR>—1 To stand firm, be established.<BR>—2 To be supported.<BR>—3 To rest or depend upon.<BR>—4 To stay, abide, be situated.<BR>—5 To set (as the sun); उदेति च यतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">Page1081-1</a>]<BR> सूर्यो यत्र च प्रतितिष्ठति Mb. 7. 62. 11. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To place firmly on, station.<BR>—2 To set up, erect, establish; धुरि प्रतिष्ठापयितव्य एव; M. 1. 16.<BR>—3 To install, inaugurate (on a throne).<BR>—4 To entrust with, consign to.<BR>—5 To offer, present; पर्यङ्कमग्र्यास्तरणं नानारत्नविभूषितम् । तमपीच्छति<BR> वैदेही प्रतिष्ठापयितुं त्वयि Rām. 2. 22. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1080-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठ|प्रतिष्ठः
प्रतिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Famous.<BR>—2 Standing firmly (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठा
प्रतिष्ठा<BR>—1 Resting, remaining, situation, position; धर्मो विश्वस्य जगतः प्रतिष्ठा<BR> Mahānār. Up.; अलसचलिताङ्गुष्ठशिरसि प्रतिष्ठा त्वय्यासीत् Śivamahimna 12.<BR> अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठम् Māl. 9; Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—2 A house, residence, home, habitation; अगाधसत्त्वो मगधप्रतिष्ठः<BR> R. 6. 21, 14. 5.<BR>—3 Fixity, stability, strength, permanence, firm basis; अप्रतिष्ठे रघुज्येष्ठे<BR> का प्रतिष्ठा कुलस्य नः U. 5. 25; अत्र खलु मे वंशप्रतिष्ठा Ś. 7;<BR> वंशः प्रतिष्ठां नीतः K. 280; Śi. 2. 34; असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं<BR> ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम् Bg. 16. 8; अहिंसाप्रतिष्ठायां तत्संनिधौ वैरत्यागः Pātañjala S.<BR>—4 Basis, foundation, site; as in गृहप्रतिष्ठा; लोकस्य नाभिर्जगतः<BR> प्रतिष्ठा Mb. 12. 245. 27.<BR>—5 A prop, stay, support; (hence) an object of glory, a distinguished<BR> ornament; त्यक्ता मया नाम कुलप्रतिष्ठा Ś. 6. 24; द्वे प्रतिष्ठे कुलस्य<BR> नः 3. 19; Ku. 7. 27; Mv. 7. 21.<BR>—6 High position, pre-eminence, high authority; किंप्रमाणमिदं काव्यं<BR> का प्रतिष्ठा महात्मनः Rām. 7. 94. 23; मया नात्मप्रतिष्ठार्थिना Mu. 2. 5.<BR>—7 Fame, glory, renown, celebrity; मा निषाद प्रतिष्ठं त्वमगमः शाश्वतीः<BR> समाः Rām. 1. 2. 15. (= U. 2. 5.).<BR>—8 Installation, inauguration; तं गच्छन्त्यनु ये विपत्तिषु पुनस्ते<BR> तत्प्रतिष्ठाशया Mu. 1. 14.<BR>—9 Attainment of a desired object, accomplishment, fulfilment (of oneʼs<BR> desire); औत्सुक्यमात्रमवसादयति प्रतिष्ठा Ś. 5. 6.<BR>—10 Tranquillity, rest, repose.<BR>—11 A receptacle.<BR>—12 The earth.<BR>—13 The consecration of an idol or image; चलाचलेति द्विविधा प्रतिष्ठा<BR> जीवमन्दिरम् Bhāg. 11. 27. 13; cf. प्राणप्रतिष्ठा.<BR>—14 A limit, boundary.<BR>—15 The foot; अहोरात्राणि प्रतिष्ठा Bṛ. Up. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—16 Completion of a vow.<BR>—17 A ceremony for obtaining supernatural or magical powers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठानम्
प्रतिष्ठानम्<BR>—1 Basis, foundation.<BR>—2 Site, situation, position.<BR>—3 A resting place.<BR>—4 The foundation of a city.<BR>—5 A leg, foot.<BR>—6 Continuation; वंशप्रतिष्ठानकराः सर्वभूतेषु विश्रुताः (पुत्राः)<BR> Rām. 1. 11. 18.<BR>—7 N. of a town at the confluence of the Ganges and Yamunā and capital<BR> of the early kings of the lunar race; cf. V. 2.<BR>—8 N. of a town on the Godāvarī and capital of Śālivāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापनम्
प्रतिष्ठापनम्<BR>—1 Placing, locating.<BR>—2 Installation, inauguration.<BR>—3 Consecrating or setting up of an idol.<BR>—4 Establishment, corroboration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापना
प्रतिष्ठापनम् + .{@-ना@} Counter-assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठासु
प्रतिष्ठासु <i>a.</i> (<i>Desid.</i>) Desirous to stand firm; अभिचैद्यं<BR> प्रतिष्ठासुरासीत् कार्यद्वयाकुलः Śi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापयितृ
प्रतिष्ठापयितृ <i>m.</i> A founder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठिका
प्रतिष्ठिका A basis, foundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठित|प्रतिष्ठितः
प्रतिष्ठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set up, erected.<BR>—2 Fixed, established; तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता Bg. 2. 57-58.<BR>—3 Placed, situated; अरैः संधार्यते नाभिर्नाभौ चाराः प्रतिष्ठिताः Pt. 1. 81.<BR>—4 Installed, inaugurated, consecrated; दिलीपानन्तरं राज्ये तं निशम्य<BR> प्रतिष्ठितम् R. 4. 2.<BR>—5 Completed, effected; प्रतिष्ठितेऽहनि सन्ध्यामुपासीत Kau. A. 1. 19.<BR>—6 Prized, valued.<BR>—7 Famous, celebrated.<BR>—8 Settled, determined.<BR>—9 Comprised, included; त्वयि सर्वं प्रतिष्ठितम् Rām. 7. 76. 28.<BR>—10 Established in life, married.<BR>—11 Endowed; प्रतिष्ठितां द्वादशभिः Rām. 6. 48. 12 (com. पादद्वयवर्त्यङ्गुलिदशकं<BR> द्वे पादतले च एवं द्वादशभिः).<BR>—12 Applied, applicable; पाणिग्रहणिका मन्त्राः कन्यास्वेव प्रतिष्ठिताः Ms. 8. 226.<BR>—13 Conversant with.<BR>—14 Secured, got, acquired.<BR>—15 Decided, certain; यदि वा मन्यसे राजन् हतमेकं प्रतिष्ठितम् Mb. 12. 32. 19.<BR>—16 Complete, finished; एवमेषा महाभागा प्रतिष्ठाने प्रतिष्ठिता । तीर्थयात्रा<BR> महापुण्या सर्वपापप्रमोचिनी ॥ Mb. 3. 85. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठितः|प्रतिष्ठित
प्रतिष्ठित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Tortoise; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठितिः|प्रतिष्ठिति
प्रतिष्ठितिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Standing firmly.<BR>—2 A station, position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्णिका
प्रतिष्णिका A water-basin (for bath); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंयत्त
प्रतिसंयत्त <i>p. p.</i> Completely prepared, armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंयात
प्रतिसंयात <i>a.</i> Assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंरुद्ध
प्रतिसंरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i> Shrunk, contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंलयनम्
प्रतिसंलयनम्, -संलीनम्<BR> Complete retirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंलीनम्
प्रतिसंलयनम्, -संलीनम्<BR> Complete retirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंविद्
प्रतिसंविद् <i>f.</i> An accurate knowledge of the particulars of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंवेदक
प्रतिसंवेदक <i>a.</i> Giving detailed information about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंवेदनम्
प्रतिसंवेदनम् Experiment, enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंविधानम्
प्रतिसंविधानम् A counter-action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंस्तरम्
प्रतिसंस्तरम् Friendly reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंस्थानम्
प्रतिसंस्थानम् Setting in, entering into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृ
प्रतिसंहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw back, withdraw, draw in; तत् साधुकृतसंधानं प्रतिसंहर<BR> सायकम् Ś. 1. 11; R. 3. 64; प्रतिसंहर तात बुद्धिमेताम् Bu. C. 5. 30.<BR>—2 To retract, take back.<BR>—3 To compress, reduce in bulk.<BR>—4 To change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहारः|प्रतिसंहार
प्रतिसंहारः<BR>—1 Taking back, withdrawing.<BR>—2 Diminution, compression.<BR>—3 Comprehension, inclusion.<BR>—4 Yielding, giving up; रसानां प्रतिसंहारात् सौभाग्यमिह विन्दति Mb. 13. 57. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृत
प्रतिसंहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Taken back, withdrawn; एष प्रतिसंहृतः Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Comprehended, included.<BR>—3 Compressed.<BR>—4 Checked, restrained; युगान्तकालप्रतिसंहृतात्मनः Śi. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंकाशः|प्रतिसङ्काश|प्रतिसंकाश
प्रतिसंकाशः Resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंक्रमः|प्रतिसङ्क्रम|प्रतिसंक्रम
प्रतिसंक्रमः<BR>—1 Reabsorption.<BR>—2 Reflection (प्रतिच्छाया).<BR>—3 Dissolution (प्रलय); तत्त्वानां भगवंस्तेषां कतिधा प्रतिसंकमः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 7. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1081-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंख्या|प्रतिसङ्ख्या
प्रतिसंख्या Consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंख्यानम्
प्रतिसंख्यानम्<BR>—1 The tranquil consideration of a matter; युक्तो योगं प्रति सदा प्रतिसंख्यानमेव<BR> च Mb. 13. 141. 83.<BR>—2 The Sāṅkhya Philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंगक्षिका|प्रतिसङ्गक्षिका
प्रतिसंगक्षिका A cloak to keep off dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंगिन्|प्रतिसङ्गिन्
प्रतिसंगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clinging or adhering to, attached to.<BR>—2 Irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंचरः|प्रतिसञ्चर|प्रतिसंचर
प्रतिसंचरः<BR>—1 Moving backwards.<BR>—2 Reabsorption.<BR>—3 Especially, re-absorption (of the world) back into Prakṛti.<BR>—4 A place of resort, haunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंदेशः|प्रतिसन्देश|प्रतिसंदेश
प्रतिसंदेशः A message in return, an answer to a message.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधा|प्रतिसन्धा
प्रतिसंधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To re-adjust.<BR>—2 To aim at, direct.<BR>—3 To conceive, comprehend.<BR>—4 To be, fasten.<BR>—5 To put on, wear.<BR>—6 To restore, return.<BR>—7 To compose oneself.<BR>—8 To fit (as an arrow to the bow-string.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहित
प्रतिसंहित <i>p. p.</i> Aimed at, directed against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधानम्
प्रतिसंधानम्<BR>—1 Joining together, uniting again; नैकोऽपि (उपायः) च्छिन्नकण्ठप्रतिसंधानपूर्वस्य<BR> प्राणलाभस्य Dk. 2. 2.<BR>—2 The period of transition between two ages.<BR>—3 A means, remedy.<BR>—4 Self-command, restraint of feelings or passion.<BR>—5 Praise.<BR>—6 Memory, recollection.<BR>—7 Remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधिः|प्रतिसन्धि|प्रतिसंधि
प्रतिसंधिः<BR>—1 Reunion.<BR>—2 Entering into the womb.<BR>—3 The period of transition between two ages.<BR>—4 Stop, cessation (उपरम); अदृष्टतोऽनुपायाच्च प्रतिसन्धेश्च कर्मणः<BR> Mb. 12. 206. 20.<BR>—5 Rebirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधित
प्रतिसंधित <i>a.</i> Fastened, strengthened, confirmed; मनुरपि<BR> परेणैव प्रतिसंधितमनोरथः Bhāg. 5. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमाधानम्
प्रतिसमाधानम् Cure, remedy; दोषे प्रतिसमाधानमज्ञाते क्रियतां<BR> कथम् Bk. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमासनम्
प्रतिसमासनम्<BR>—1 Coping with, being a match for.<BR>—2 Resisting, opposing, withstanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमासित
प्रतिसमासित <i>a.</i> Equalled, opposed; भीष्मद्रोणादयो युद्धे शक्याः<BR> प्रतिसमासितुम् Mb. 3. 47. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर|प्रतिसरः
प्रतिसर <i>a.</i> Dependent, subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरः|प्रतिसर
प्रतिसर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 A cord or ribbon worn round the wrist or neck as an amulet.<BR>—2 An ornament.<BR>—3 A watch, guard.<BR>—4 Assailing, an attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरम्
प्रतिसर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 A cord or ribbon worn round the wrist or neck as an amulet.<BR>—2 An ornament.<BR>—3 A watch, guard.<BR>—4 Assailing, an attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरः|प्रतिसर
प्रतिसर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A servant, follower; विजये त्वर्यतां लेखः प्रतिसराय Pratijñā.<BR>—2 A bracelet, marriage-string; स्रस्तोरगप्रतिसरेण करेण पाणिः<BR> (अगृह्यत) Ki. 5. 33; (= कौतुकसूत्र); Māl. 5. 18.<BR>—3 A garland, wreath.<BR>—4 Day-break.<BR>—5 The rear of an army.<BR>—6 A form of incantation.<BR>—7 Healing or dressing a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरा
प्रतिसर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 A female servant.<BR>—2 A thread, fillet; प्रतिसरया तुरगाणां भल्लातकशालिकुण्ठसिद्धार्थं<BR> कण्ठेषु निवध्नीयात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर्गः|प्रतिसर्ग
प्रतिसर्गः<BR>—1 Secondary creation (as by the agents of one Supreme Being); संग्रहेण<BR> मया ख्यातः प्रतिसर्गस्तवानघ Bhāg. 4. 8. 5; आदिसर्गस्तु यः सूत<BR> कथितो विस्तरेण च । प्रतिसर्गश्च ये येषामधिपास्तान् वदस्व नः ॥ Kālikā P.<BR>—2 Dissolution.<BR>—3 Continued creation out of primitive matter.<BR>—4 The portion of a Purāṇa which treats of the destruction and renovation<BR> of the world; सर्गश्च प्रतिसर्गश्च वंशो मन्वन्तराणि च । वंशानुचरितं<BR> चैव पुराणं पञ्चलक्षणम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसांधानिकः|प्रतिसान्धानिक|प्रतिसांधानिक|प्रतिसान्धानिकः
प्रतिसांधानिकः A bard, panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृ
प्रतिसृ P.<BR>—1 To go back, return.<BR>—2 To go towards, rush upon, attack, assail; दैत्यः प्रत्यसरद्देवं<BR> मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् Hariv. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To push backwards, replace; कनकवलयं स्रस्तं स्रस्तं मया प्रतिसार्यते Ś. 3. 12.<BR>—2 To repel, drive away or back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरणम्
प्रतिसरणम् Leaning or resting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारणम्
प्रतिसारणम्<BR>—1 Dressing the edges of a wound.<BR>—2 An instrument used for anointing a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारित
प्रतिसारित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Repelled, removed.<BR>—2 Dressed (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसीरा
प्रतिसीरा A screen, curtain, wall of cloth; भावस्त्रपोर्मिप्रतिसीरया<BR> ते न दीयते N. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृष्ट|प्रतिसृष्टः
प्रतिसृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sent out, despatched.<BR>—2 Celebrated.<BR>—3 Repulsed, rejected.<BR>—4 Intoxicated (प्रमत्त according to धरणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्त्री
प्रतिस्त्री <i>a.</i> Lying on a woman; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नात
प्रतिस्नात <i>p. p.</i> Bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नेहः|प्रतिस्नेह
प्रतिस्नेहः Love in return, requital or reciprocation of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पन्दनम्
प्रतिस्पन्दनम् Throbbing, vibration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्धा
प्रतिस्पर्धा Rivalry, emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्धिन्
प्रतिस्पर्धिन् <i>a.</i> Rival, envious of. ━<i>m.</i> A rival, competitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वनः|प्रतिस्वन
प्रतिस्वनः, प्रतिस्वरः<BR>—1 An echo, reverberation; दधिरेऽधिभित्ति पटहप्रतिस्वनैः स्फुटमट्टहासमिव<BR> सौधपङ्क्तयः Śi. 13. 31.<BR>—2 A focus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वरः|प्रतिस्वर
प्रतिस्वनः, प्रतिस्वरः<BR>—1 An echo, reverberation; दधिरेऽधिभित्ति पटहप्रतिस्वनैः स्फुटमट्टहासमिव<BR> सौधपङ्क्तयः Śi. 13. 31.<BR>—2 A focus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वम्
प्रतिस्वम् <i>ind.</i> One by one, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहन्
प्रतिहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To strike back or in return; (तं) विध्यन्तमुद्धृतसटाः प्रतिहन्तुमीषुः R. 9. 60.<BR>—2 To ward off, keep off, prevent, oppose, resist; तोयस्येवाप्रतिहतरयः<BR> सैकतं सेतुमोघः U. 3. 36; प्रतिहतविध्नाः क्रियाः समवलोक्य Ś. 1. 13;<BR> Me. 20; Ku. 2. 48; V. 2. 1.<BR>—3 To repel, drive back, repulse; अग्निवेगवहः प्राणो गुदान्ते प्रतिहन्यते<BR> Mb. 3. 213. 14.<BR>—4 To remove, destroy; यद्यत् पापं प्रतिजहि जगन्नाथ नम्रस्य तन्मे Māl. 1. 3.<BR>—5 To counter-act, remedy.<BR>—6 To disown, disavow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1082-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहत|प्रतिहतः
प्रतिहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck or beaten back; knocked back; तस्मिन् प्रतिहते चास्त्रे विस्मयो<BR> मे महानभूत् Mb. 3. 167. 31.<BR>—2 Driven away, repelled, repulsed; शापादसि प्रतिहता Ś. 7. 32;<BR> सा बुद्धिरप्रतिहता वचनं तदेव Bh. 2. 40.<BR>—3 Opposed, obstructed.<BR>—4 Sent, despatched.<BR>—5 Hated, disliked.<BR>—6 Disappointed, frustrated.<BR>—7 Fallen, overthrown.<BR>—8 Tied, bound.<BR>—9 Impaired, lost; यावच्चेन्द्रियशक्तिरप्रतिहता Bh. 3. 88; इमास्ता<BR> मन्मथवतां हिताः प्रतिहता दिशः Rām. 4. 28. 13.<BR>—10 Dazzled (as eyes).<BR>—11 Dulled, blunted (as teeth by acid).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिहतधी, प्रतिहतमति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतधी
प्रतिहत + -धी, -मति <i>a.</i> hating, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतमति
प्रतिहत + -धी, -मति <i>a.</i> hating, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतिः|प्रतिहति
प्रतिहतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Striking or knocking back, repelling.<BR>—2 Rebound, recoil; प्रतिहतिं ययुरर्जुनमुष्टयः Ki. 18. 5; Śi. 9. 49.<BR>—3 Disappointment, frustration.<BR>—4 Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहननम्
प्रतिहननम् Striking or knocking back, returning a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहासः|प्रतिहास
प्रतिहासः<BR>—1 Returning a laugh.<BR>—2 Fragrant oleander (Mar. कण्हेर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहित
प्रतिहित <i>p. p.</i> —1 Fitted to, put close to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसा
प्रतिहिंसा Retaliation, revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसितम्
प्रतिहिंसितम् Requital of an injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहृ
प्रतिहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To beat back.<BR>—2 To avoid, shun.<BR>—3 To offer, present.<BR>—4 To disregard; आज्ञां प्रतिहरच्चापि कृतज्ञैः पुरुषैः सदा Mb. 15. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहरणम्
प्रतिहरणम्<BR>—1 Avoiding, shunning.<BR>—2 Striking back, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहर्तृ|प्रतिहर्त्तृ
प्रतिहर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who beats back or removes, repeller, remover, averter, destroyer<BR> &c.; सर्वे वियुक्ताः स्वविहारतन्त्रं न शक्नुमस्तत्प्रतिहर्तवे ते<BR> Bhāg. 3. 5. 47.<BR>—2 The assistant of the Udgātṛ; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारः|प्रतिहार
प्रति(ती)हारः<BR>—1 Striking back.<BR>—2 A door, gate.<BR>—3 A porter, door-keeper; आर्य अदेशकालः प्रतीहारस्य Svapna. 5, 6.<BR>—4 A juggler.<BR>—5 Juggling, a juggling trick.<BR>—6 (In gram.) The hard contact of the tongue with the edge of the teeth<BR> in pronouncing dental letters.<BR>—7 Intimating arrival (आगमननिवेदन); संप्राप्यैते महात्मानो राघवस्य<BR> निवेशनम् । विष्ठिताः प्रतिहारार्थम् Rām. 7. 1. 7; see प्रतिहारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहारः|प्रतीहार
प्रति(ती)हारः<BR>—1 Striking back.<BR>—2 A door, gate.<BR>—3 A porter, door-keeper; आर्य अदेशकालः प्रतीहारस्य Svapna. 5, 6.<BR>—4 A juggler.<BR>—5 Juggling, a juggling trick.<BR>—6 (In gram.) The hard contact of the tongue with the edge of the teeth<BR> in pronouncing dental letters.<BR>—7 Intimating arrival (आगमननिवेदन); संप्राप्यैते महात्मानो राघवस्य<BR> निवेशनम् । विष्ठिताः प्रतिहारार्थम् Rām. 7. 1. 7; see प्रतिहारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारी
प्रति(ती)हारः + .{@-री@} A female doorkeeper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतिहारभूमिः, प्रतिहाररक्षी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारभूमिः|प्रतिहारभूमि
प्रतिहारः + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> the threshold (of a house &c.); भविष्यतः पत्युरुमा<BR> च शंभोः समाससाद प्रतिहारभूमिम् Ku. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहाररक्षी
प्रतिहारः + -रक्षी a female doorkeeper; पुंवत्प्रगल्भा प्रतिहाररक्षी R. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारकः|प्रतिहारक
प्रतिहारकः A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारणम्
प्रतिहारणम् Entrance, permission to enter a door; व्यतिष्ठत प्रेक्ष्य<BR> तदा सुमन्त्रं पितुर्महात्मा प्रतिहारणार्थम् Rām. 2. 33. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहार्यम्
प्रतिहार्यम् Juggling, jugglery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहोमः|प्रतिहोम
प्रतिहोमः A supplementary sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रती
प्रती (प्रति-इ) €2 P.<BR>—1 To go back to, return; प्रतीयाय गुरोः सकाशम् R. 5. 35; Bk. 3. 19.<BR>—2 To go to, approach, turn to.<BR>—3 To fall to the lot of.<BR>—4 To reach, attain.<BR>—5 To believe, trust, be certain or sure of, rely on; कः प्रत्येति सैवेयमिति<BR> U. 4, 1. 44; ततः परशुरामस्य न प्रतीमः पराभवम् Mv. 2. 14.<BR>—6 To learn, understand, know, प्रतीयते धातुरिवेहितं फलैः Ki. 1. 20;<BR> Śi. 1. 69.<BR>—7 To be well-known or celebrated; सोऽयं वटः श्याम इति प्रतीतः R. 13. 53.<BR>—8 To be pleased or satisfied; प्रतिः प्रतीतः प्रसवोन्मुखीं प्रियाम्<BR> (ददर्श) R. 3. 12, 16. 23.<BR>—9 To face (an opponent); सहसैन्यानहं तांश्च प्रतीयां रणमूर्धनि<BR> Mb. 5. 172. 13. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be recognized or perceived.<BR>—2 To be proved, turn out to be true.<BR>—3 To follow from anything (as a necessary result). ━<i>Caus.</i> (प्रत्याययति)<BR>—1 To cause to believe; convince, inspire confidence; एष विवाद एव<BR> प्रत्याययति Ś. 7, 5. 31; ताः खचारित्र्यमुद्दिश्य प्रत्याययतु मैथिली R. 15. 73.<BR>—2 To cause to perceive, bring to mind.<BR>—3 To prove, demonstrate, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत|प्रतीतः
प्रतीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set forth, started.<BR>—2 Gone by, past, gone; एवं राजर्षयः सर्वे प्रतीता रघुनन्दन<BR> Rām. 2. 107. 14.<BR>—3 Believed, trusted.<BR>—4 Proved, established.<BR>—5 Acknowledged, recognised.<BR>—6 Called, known as, named.<BR>—7 Well-known, renowned, famous; ततः प्रतीतं प्लवतां वरिष्ठम्<BR> Rām. 4. 65. 35; स वासुदेवानुचरं प्रशान्तं बृहस्पतेः प्राक्तनयं<BR> प्रतीतम् Bhāg. 3. 1. 25.<BR>—8 Firmly resolved.<BR>—9<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Convinced, of a firm conviction.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Believing, trusting, confident.<BR>—10 Pleased, delighted; cf. प्रतीतः सादरे ज्ञाते हृष्टप्रख्यातयोः त्रिषु<BR> Med.; Rām. 2. 71. 19; R. 3. 12, 5. 26, 14. 47, 16. 23; भव इव<BR> षण्मुखजन्मना प्रतीतः Bu. C. 1. 94; अथेष्टपुत्रः परमप्रतीतः<BR> कुलस्य वृद्धिं प्रति भूमिपालः 2. 47.<BR>—11 Respectful.<BR>—12 Clever, learned, wise.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतीतात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीतात्मन्
प्रतीत + -आत्मन् confident, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीतिः|प्रतीति
प्रतीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Conviction, settled belief; पदानि दृष्ट्वा तु भवेत् प्रतीतिः Ś. 7. 31.<BR>—2 Belief.<BR>—3 Knowledge, ascertainment, clear or distinct perception or apprehension;<BR> अपि तु वाच्यवैचित्र्यप्रतिभासादेव चारुताप्रतीतिः K. P. 10.<BR>—4 Fame, renown; प्रतिव्रता प्रतीतिं लेभे Dk. 2. 6.<BR>—5 Respect.<BR>—6 Delight.<BR>—7 Going towards, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक|प्रतीकः
प्रतीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Directed or turned towards.<BR>—2 Inverted, reverse.<BR>—3 Contrary, unfavourable, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकः|प्रतीक
प्रतीक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A limb, member; अप्राणद्भिः प्राणभाजां प्रतीकैः Śi. 18. 79.<BR>—2 A part, portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकम्
प्रतीक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 An image.<BR>—2 Mouth, face.<BR>—3 The front (of anything).<BR>—4 The first word (of a verse, sentence &c.).<BR>—5 A lamp; L. D. B.<BR>—6 A symbol.<BR>—7 A copy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतीकदर्शनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकदर्शनम्
प्रतीक + -दर्शनम् a symbolic conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकार|प्रतीकारः
प्रतीकार = प्रतिकार q. v. अवश्यंभाविभावानां प्रतीकारो भवेद्यदि ।<BR> तदा दुःखैर्न लिप्येरन् नलरामयुधिष्ठिराः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकाश|प्रतीकाशः
प्रतीकाश = प्रतिकाश q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्
प्रतीक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To look at, observe, consider.<BR>—2 To look out for, expect.<BR>—3 To wait for, await; संपत्स्यते वः कामोऽयं कालः कश्चित् प्रतीक्ष्यताम्<BR> Ku. 2. 54, 2. 37; Ms. 9. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1083-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष
प्रतीक्ष, प्रतीक्षक, प्रतीक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Expectant, waiting for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षक
प्रतीक्ष, प्रतीक्षक, प्रतीक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Expectant, waiting for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षिन्
प्रतीक्ष, प्रतीक्षक, प्रतीक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Expectant, waiting for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षणम्
प्रतीक्षणम्, प्रतीक्षा<BR>—1 Waiting for; सत्यव्रतस्यागमनप्रतीक्षाः Mb. 3. 164. 11.<BR>—2 Expectation, hope.<BR>—3 Regard, consideration, attention; इत्यादृतोक्तः परमस्य पुंसः प्रतीक्षणानुग्रहभाजनोऽहम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 4. 14.<BR>—4 Looking at, considering.<BR>—5 Fulfilment, observance (of a vow, promise &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षा
प्रतीक्षणम्, प्रतीक्षा<BR>—1 Waiting for; सत्यव्रतस्यागमनप्रतीक्षाः Mb. 3. 164. 11.<BR>—2 Expectation, hope.<BR>—3 Regard, consideration, attention; इत्यादृतोक्तः परमस्य पुंसः प्रतीक्षणानुग्रहभाजनोऽहम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 4. 14.<BR>—4 Looking at, considering.<BR>—5 Fulfilment, observance (of a vow, promise &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षित
प्रतीक्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Waited for, expected.<BR>—2 Considered.<BR>—3 Respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्य|प्रतीक्ष्यः
प्रतीक्ष्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be waited for.<BR>—2 Worthy of consideration or regard.<BR>—3 Venerable, respectable; भक्तिः प्रतीक्ष्येषु कुलोचिता ते R. 5. 14; Śi. 2. 108.<BR>—4 To be adhered to or maintained, to be fulfilled; प्रतीक्ष्यं तत् प्रतीक्ष्यायै<BR> पितृष्वस्रे प्रतिश्रुतम् Śi. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघात|प्रतीघातः
प्रतीघात = प्रतिघात q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीची
प्रतीची The west.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतीचीशः, प्रतीचीपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीशः|प्रतीचीश
प्रतीची + -ईशः, -पतिः<BR>—1 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—2 Ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीपतिः|प्रतीचीपति
प्रतीची + -ईशः, -पतिः<BR>—1 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—2 Ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीन|प्रतीचीनं
प्रतीचीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Western, westerly.<BR>—2 Future, subsequent, following.<BR>—3 Ved. Turned or directed towards.<BR>—4 Turning back, turned away from.<BR>—5 Coming from behind.<BR>—6 Turned inwards (अभिमुख); सध्रीचीनं प्रतीचीनं परस्यानुपथं गताः<BR> Bhāg. 6. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्य|प्रतीच्यः
प्रतीच्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living in the west, western, westerly.<BR>—2 Ved. Disappeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्छकः|प्रतीच्छक
प्रतीच्छकः A receiver; तथा निमज्जतोऽधस्तादज्ञौ दातृप्रतीच्छकौ Ms. 4. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत्त
प्रतीत्त <i>a.</i> Given back, restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीन्धकः|प्रतीन्धक|प्रतींधक|प्रतींधकः
प्रतीन्धकः N. of a country called विदेह q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीनाहः|प्रतीनाह
प्रतीनाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीप|प्रतीपं|प्रतीपः
प्रतीप <i>a.</i> [प्रतिगताः आपो यत्र, प्रतिअप् अच्, अप ईप् च्]<BR>—1 Contrary, unfavourable, adverse, opposite; तत्प्रतीपपवनादि वैकृतम्<BR> R. 11. 62; Ki. 14. 60.<BR>—2 Reverse, inverted, out of order.<BR>—3 Backward, retrograde.<BR>—4 Disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>—5 Refractory, disobedient, obstinate, perverse; प्रेष्यः प्रतीपोऽधिकृतः<BR> प्रमादी (त्याज्याः) Pt. 1. 424.<BR>—6 Turned away, averted.<BR>—7 Meeting, encountering.<BR>—8 Hindering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपः|प्रतीप|प्रतीपं
प्रतीप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 N. of a king, father of Śantanu and grand-father of Bhīṣma.<BR>—2 An adversary, opponent; चरति मयि रणे यश्च यश्च प्रतीपः Ve. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपम्
प्रतीप + .{@-पम्@} N. of a figure of speech in which the usual form of comparison<BR> is inverted, the उपमान being compared with the उपमेय; प्रतीपमुपमानस्याप्युपमेयत्वकल्पनम् ।<BR> त्वल्लोचनसमं पद्मं त्वद्वक्त्रसदृशो विधुः ॥ Candr. 5. 9; (for<BR> fuller definitions and explanation see K. P. 10 under प्रतीप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपम्
प्रतीप + .{@-पम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 On the contrary.<BR>—2 In an inverted order.<BR>—3 Against, in opposition to; भर्तृर्विप्रकृतापि रोषणतया मा स्म प्रतीपं<BR> गमः Ś. 4. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रतीपोक्तिः, प्रतीपग, प्रतीपगमनम्, प्रतीपगतिः, प्रतीपतरणम्, प्रतीपदर्शिनी, प्रतीपदीपकम्, प्रतीपवचनम्, प्रतीपविपाकिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपोक्तिः|प्रतीपोक्ति
प्रतीप + -उक्तिः contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपग
प्रतीप + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going against.<BR>—2 adverse, unfavourable; तस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">Page1084-2</a>]<BR> जातु मरुतः प्रतीपगाः R. 11. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपगमनम्
प्रतीप + -गमनम्, -गतिः <i>f.</i> retrograde motion; अम्भसामोघसंरोधः<BR> प्रतीपगमनादिव Ku. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपगतिः|प्रतीपगति
प्रतीप + -गमनम्, -गतिः <i>f.</i> retrograde motion; अम्भसामोघसंरोधः<BR> प्रतीपगमनादिव Ku. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपतरणम्
प्रतीप + -तरणम् going or sailing against the stream; स्रोतोजवोह्यमानस्य<BR> प्रतीपतरणं हि तत् V. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपदर्शिनी
प्रतीप + -दर्शिनी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपदीपकम्
प्रतीप + -दीपकम् a particular figure of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपवचनम्
प्रतीप + -वचनम्<BR>—1 contradiction.<BR>—2 a perverse or evasive manner of speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपविपाकिन्
प्रतीप + -विपाकिन् <i>a.</i> producing the opposite result (recoiling on the<BR> doer); फलमनुभवत्युग्रं पापः प्रतीपविपाकिनः Māl. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपक
प्रतीपक <i>a.</i> Hostile, opposed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपयति
प्रतीपयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To cause to turn back, reverse, turn back; क ईप्सितार्थस्थिरनिश्चयं<BR> मनः पयश्च निम्नाभिमुखं प्रतीपयेत् Ku. 5. 5.<BR>—2 To be against or hostile to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपायते
प्रतीपायते Den. Ā. To be opposed or unfavourable, to dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीरम्
प्रतीरम् A shore, bank; प्रतीरदेशैः स्वकलत्रचारुभिर्विभूषिताः<BR> कुञ्जसमुद्रयोषितः Ki. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवापः|प्रतीवाप
प्रतीवापः<BR>—1 Adding to, inserting (as an ingredient); तत्र वीरतर्वादिसिद्धं<BR> जलमूषकादि प्रतीवापं पाययेत् Suśr.<BR>—2 Calcining or fluxing metals.<BR>—3 An epidemic disease, a plague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेश|प्रतीवेशः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहार|प्रतीहारः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहास|प्रतीहासः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेशिन्
प्रतीवेशिन् <i>a.</i> See प्रतिवेशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीष्
प्रतीष् €6 P.<BR>—1 To receive, accept; देवस्य शासनं प्रतीष्य Ś. 6.<BR>—2 To welcome, greet, receive, honour; एष माधवीमण्डपः स्वागतेनैव<BR> नौ प्रतीच्छति Ś. 6.<BR>—3 To obey (as an order).<BR>—4 To wait for, expect; हृदि प्रतीष्या कवयो मनीषा Rv. 10. 129. 4;<BR> एष खलु त्वां प्रतीच्छति V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीष्ट
प्रतीष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Accepted, received &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहासः|प्रतीहास
प्रतीहासः A fragrant oleander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहारी
प्रतीहारी<BR>—1 A female door-keeper.<BR>—2 A door-keeper in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुद्
प्रतुद् €6 P. To strike, hurt, wound. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To urge on, drive forward; (fig.) to press, urge repeatedly (to do<BR> a thing): प्रविश गृहमिति प्रतोद्यमाना न चलति भाग्यकृतां दशामवेक्ष्य Mk. 1. 56.<BR>—2 To pierce, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुदः|प्रतुद
प्रतुदः<BR>—1 An epithet of a class of birds (such as hawks, parrots, crows &c.);<BR> Ms. 5. 13; हारितो धवलः पाण्डुश्चित्रपक्षो बृहच्छुकः । पारावतः खञ्जरीटः<BR> पिकाद्याः प्रतुदाः स्मृताः ॥ प्रतुद्य भक्षयन्त्येते तुण्डेन प्रतुदास्ततः<BR>—2 An instrument for pricking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोदः|प्रतोद
प्रतोदः<BR>—1 A goad.<BR>—2 A long whip; शरः क्षत्रियया ग्राह्यः प्रतोदो वैश्यकन्यया Ms. 3. 44.<BR>—3 A pricking instrument; वाक्यप्रतोदाभिहतो यत्र कृष्णेन पाण्डवः Mb. 1. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टिः|प्रतुष्टि
प्रतुष्टिः <i>f.</i>, प्रतोषः Gratification, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोषः|प्रतोष
प्रतुष्टिः <i>f.</i>, प्रतोषः Gratification, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूणी
प्रतूणी A kind of disease (in the bowels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1084-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूर्ण
प्रतूर्ण <i>a.</i> Speedy, quick, fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूलिका
प्रतूलिका <i>f.</i> A kind of bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतृद्
प्रतृद् To thrust, pierce, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्दन|प्रतर्दनः|प्रतर्द्दन
प्रतर्दन <i>a.</i> Piercing, destroying (an epithet of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतॄ
प्रतॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To cross over.<BR>—2 To further, promote, advance.<BR>—3 To raise, elevate, enhance.<BR>—4 To lengthen, prolong (life). —5 To lead, conduct. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cheat, deceive, take in; मां तथा प्रतार्य Ś. 5; किंत्वेवं<BR> कविभिः प्रतारितमनास्तत्त्वं विजानन्नपि Bh. 1. 78.<BR>—2 To mislead, lead astray.<BR>—3 To spread, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतरः|प्रतर
प्रतरः<BR>—1 Crossing, crossing or going over.<BR>—2 N. of the joints on the neck and the spinal vertebrae; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतरणम्
प्रतरणम् Crossing, going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारः|प्रतार
प्रतारः<BR>—1 Carrying or bearing over, crossing.<BR>—2 Deceit, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारकः|प्रतारक
प्रतारकः, -प्रतारिन्<BR> A cheat, an impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारिन्
प्रतारकः, -प्रतारिन्<BR> A cheat, an impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारणम्
प्रतारणम्<BR>—1 Carrying over.<BR>—2 Deceiving, cheating, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारणा
प्रतारणम् + .{@-णा@} Fraud, deceit, knavery, trickery, roguery, deception, hypocrisy;<BR> यदीच्छसि वशीकर्तुं जगदेकेन कर्मणा । उपास्यतां कलौ कल्पलतादेवी<BR> प्रतारणा ॥; प्रतारणासमर्थस्य विद्यया किं प्रयोजनम् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारित|प्रतारितः
प्रतारित <i>a.</i> Deceived, defrauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोली
प्रतोली<BR>—1 A street, main road, principal street through a town; प्रापत् प्रतोलीमतुलप्रतापः<BR> Śi. 3. 64; सहर्म्यद्वितलां द्वयर्धायामां प्रतोलीं कारयेत् Kau. A. 2. 3. 21.<BR> स्वयमभवन् विवृताः पुरप्रतोल्यः Bu. C. 5. 82; N. 6. 58.<BR>—2 A kind of bandage; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्त|प्रत्तं
प्रत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Given, given away, presented, offered; अप्रत्तं नस्त्वया किं नु भगवन्<BR> भुवनेश्वर Bhāg. 9. 11. 6.<BR>—2 Given in marriage, married. See प्रदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्न|प्रत्नः
प्रत्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Old, ancient; आदित्प्रत्नस्य रेतसः Ch. Up. 3. 17. 7.<BR>—2 Former.<BR>—3 Traditional, customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्नम्
प्रत्न + .{@-त्नम्@} A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्
प्रत्यक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In an opposite direction, backwards.<BR>—2 Against.<BR>—3 Westward, to the west of (with abl.).<BR>—4 In the interior, inwardly. —5 Formerly, in former times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष <i>a.</i> [अक्ष्णःप्रति]<BR>—1 Perceptible (to the eye), visible; प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु<BR> वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Present, in sight, before the eye.<BR>—3 Cognizable by any organ of sense.<BR>—4 Distinct, evident, clear.<BR>—5 Direct, immediate.<BR>—6 Explicit, express.<BR>—7 Corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षम्
प्रत्यक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@}<BR>—1 Perception, ocular evidence, apprehension by the senses, considered<BR> as a प्रमाण or mode of proof; इन्द्रियार्थसंनिकर्षजन्यं ज्ञानं<BR> प्रत्यक्षम् T. S.<BR>—2 Explicitness, distinctness.<BR>—3 Superintendence, care for; प्रत्यहं लोकयात्रायाः प्रत्यक्षं स्त्रीनिबन्धनम् Ms. 9. 27.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">Page1085-2</a>]<BR> A kind of style descriptive of impressions derived from the senses. (The<BR> forms प्रत्यक्षम्, प्रत्यक्षेण, प्रत्यक्षतः, प्रत्यक्षात् are used adverbially<BR> in the sense of<BR>—1 Before, in the presence of, in the sight of.<BR>—2 Openly, publicly.<BR>—3 Directly, immediately. Hence; प्रत्यक्षतोदृष्टसम्बन्धम् is a variety<BR> of अनुमान where the connection between the लिङ्ग and the लिङ्गिन्<BR> or साध्य is directly perceived; प्रत्यक्षतो दृष्टसम्बन्धं यथा<BR> धूमाकृतिदर्शनादग्न्याकृतिविज्ञानम् ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR>—4 Personally.<BR>—5 At sight.<BR>—6 Explicitly.<BR>—7 Distinctly, clearly.<BR>—8 Literally. So प्रत्यक्षे in the sight of, before the eyes of.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यक्षकरणम्, प्रत्यक्षकृता, प्रत्यक्षज्ञानम्, प्रत्यक्षदर्शनम्, प्रत्यक्षदृष्ट, प्रत्यक्षपर, प्रत्यक्षपरीक्षणम्, प्रत्यक्षप्रमा, प्रत्यक्षप्रमाणम्, प्रत्यक्षफल, प्रत्यक्षभूत, प्रत्यक्षभोगः, प्रत्यक्षवादिन्, प्रत्यक्षविधानम्, प्रत्यक्षविषयीभू, प्रत्यक्षविहित, प्रत्यक्षवृत्तिः, प्रत्यक्षसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षकरणम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -करणम् oneʼs own perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षकृता
प्रत्यक्ष + -कृता (<i>i. e.</i> ऋक्) a hymn in which a deity is directly addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षज्ञानम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -ज्ञानम् ocular evidence, knowledge obtained by direct perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षदर्शनम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -दर्शनम् ocular evidence, direct proof. {@-दर्शनः, -दर्शिन्@}<BR> <i>m.</i> an eyewitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षदृष्ट
प्रत्यक्ष + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i> personally seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षपर
प्रत्यक्ष + -पर <i>a.</i> setting the highest value on the visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षपरीक्षणम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -परीक्षणम् personal examination, real observation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षप्रमा
प्रत्यक्ष + -प्रमा correct or certain knowledge, such as is obtained by direct<BR> perception through the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षप्रमाणम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -प्रमाणम्<BR>—1 ocular proof, evidence of the senses.<BR>—2 an organ of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षफल
प्रत्यक्ष + -फल <i>a.</i> having evident or visible consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभूत
प्रत्यक्ष + -भूत <i>a.</i> manifested, appeared personally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभोगः|प्रत्यक्षभोग
प्रत्यक्ष + -भोगः enjoyment of anything with the knowledge of the owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षवादिन्
प्रत्यक्ष + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a Buddhist who admits no other evidence than ocular<BR> proof or perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षविधानम्
प्रत्यक्ष + -विधानम् an express injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षविषयीभू
प्रत्यक्ष + -विषयीभू to move only within the range of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षविहित
प्रत्यक्ष + -विहित <i>a.</i> directly or explicitly enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षवृत्तिः|प्रत्यक्षवृत्ति
प्रत्यक्ष + -वृत्तिः composed clearly or intelligibly (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षसिद्ध
प्रत्यक्ष + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> determined by ocular proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षता
प्रत्यक्षता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Perceptibility, ocular proof.<BR>—2 Standing face to face.<BR>—3 Explicitness.<BR>—4 (In phil.) … … तत्तदिन्द्रिययोग्यवर्तमानविषयावच्छिन्नचैतन्याभिन्नत्वं<BR> तत्तदाकारवृत्त्यवच्छिन्नज्ञानस्य तत्तदंशे प्रत्यक्षत्वम् Vedānta P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षत्वम्
प्रत्यक्षता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Perceptibility, ocular proof.<BR>—2 Standing face to face.<BR>—3 Explicitness.<BR>—4 (In phil.) … … तत्तदिन्द्रिययोग्यवर्तमानविषयावच्छिन्नचैतन्याभिन्नत्वं<BR> तत्तदाकारवृत्त्यवच्छिन्नज्ञानस्य तत्तदंशे प्रत्यक्षत्वम् Vedānta P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षयति
प्रत्यक्षयति Den. P. To make visible, show, manifest, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षिन्
प्रत्यक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Witnessing in person. ━<i>m.</i> An eyewitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकृ
प्रत्यक्षीकृ €8 U. To witness or see in person, ascertain or see with<BR> oneʼs own eyes; राजर्षेरुदन्तं प्रत्यक्षीकरिष्यामि Ś. 6; तद्देवः<BR> पत्रारूढं प्रत्यक्षीकरोतु <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्र|प्रत्यग्रः
प्रत्यग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fresh, young, new, recent; प्रत्यग्रहतानां मांसम् Ve. 3; कुसुमशयनं<BR> न प्रत्यग्रम् V. 3. 10; Me. 4; R. 10. 54; Ratn. 1. 21.<BR>—2 Repeated.<BR>—3 Pure.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यग्रवयस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रवयस्
प्रत्यग्र + -वयस् <i>a.</i> young in age, in the prime of life, youthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्च्|प्रत्यंच्
प्रत्यञ्च्, -प्रत्यच् <i>a.</i><BR>.(-प्रतीची <i>f.</i> or according to Vopadeva प्रत्यञ्ची also)<BR>—1 Turned or directed towards; turned inward; मनः प्रत्यक् चित्ते सविधमवधायात्तमरुतः<BR> Śivamahimna 25.<BR>—2 Being behind.<BR>—3 Following, subsequent; समेत्य तरसा प्रत्यग्द्वाभ्यां पद्भ्यां बलं<BR> बली । निहत्य Bhāg. 10. 15. 30.<BR>—4 Averted, turned away, turning back;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">Page1086-1</a>]<BR> Pt. 3. 181.<BR>—5 Western, westerly.<BR>—6 Inner, interior.<BR>—7 Equal to, a match for. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The individual soul.<BR>—2 Future time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यञ्गक्षम्, प्रत्यञ्गात्मन्, प्रत्यञ्गानन्द, प्रत्यञ्गाशापतिः, प्रत्यञ्गुदच्, प्रत्यञ्क्चेतन, प्रत्यञ्ग्दक्षिणतः, प्रत्यञ्ग्दृश्, प्रत्यञ्ग्धामन्, प्रत्यञ्क्पुष्पा, प्रत्यञ्क्प्रवण, प्रत्यञ्ङ्मुख, प्रत्यञ्ग्रथाः, प्रत्यञ्क्स्रोतस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यच्
प्रत्यञ्च्, -प्रत्यच् <i>a.</i><BR>.(-प्रतीची <i>f.</i> or according to Vopadeva प्रत्यञ्ची also)<BR>—1 Turned or directed towards; turned inward; मनः प्रत्यक् चित्ते सविधमवधायात्तमरुतः<BR> Śivamahimna 25.<BR>—2 Being behind.<BR>—3 Following, subsequent; समेत्य तरसा प्रत्यग्द्वाभ्यां पद्भ्यां बलं<BR> बली । निहत्य Bhāg. 10. 15. 30.<BR>—4 Averted, turned away, turning back;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">Page1086-1</a>]<BR> Pt. 3. 181.<BR>—5 Western, westerly.<BR>—6 Inner, interior.<BR>—7 Equal to, a match for. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The individual soul.<BR>—2 Future time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यञ्गक्षम्, प्रत्यञ्गात्मन्, प्रत्यञ्गानन्द, प्रत्यञ्गाशापतिः, प्रत्यञ्गुदच्, प्रत्यञ्क्चेतन, प्रत्यञ्ग्दक्षिणतः, प्रत्यञ्ग्दृश्, प्रत्यञ्ग्धामन्, प्रत्यञ्क्पुष्पा, प्रत्यञ्क्प्रवण, प्रत्यञ्ङ्मुख, प्रत्यञ्ग्रथाः, प्रत्यञ्क्स्रोतस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1085-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्गक्षम्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -अक्षम् (प्रत्यगक्षम्) an inner organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्गात्मन्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> (प्रत्यगात्मन्) the individual soul; कश्चिद्धीरः<BR> प्रत्यगात्मानमैक्षदावृत्तचक्षुरमृतत्वामिच्छन् Kaṭh. 2. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्गानन्द
प्रत्यञ्च् + -आनन्द <i>a.</i> inwardly joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्गाशापतिः
प्रत्यञ्च् + -आशापतिः (प्रत्यगाशापतिः) ‘The lord of the western direction’,<BR> an epithet of Varuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्गुदच्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -उदच् <i>f.</i> (प्रत्यगुदच्) the north-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्क्चेतन|प्रत्यञ्क्चेतनः
प्रत्यञ्च् + -चेतन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 whose thoughts are turned upon himself.<BR>—2 intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्क्चेतनः|प्रत्यञ्क्चेतन
प्रत्यञ्च् + -चेतन + .({@-नः@})<BR>—1 the supreme soul; the Puruṣa in the Sāṅkhya philosophy.<BR>—2 the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्ग्दक्षिणतः
प्रत्यञ्च् + -दक्षिणतः (प्रत्यग्दक्षिणतः) <i>ind.</i> towards the south-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्ग्दृश्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -दृश् <i>f.</i> (प्रत्यग्दृश्) an inward glance, a glance directed<BR> inwards; स्वांशेन सर्वतनुभृन्मनसि प्रतीतप्रत्यग्दृशे भगवते बृहते<BR> नमस्ते Bhāg. 8. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्ग्धामन्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -धामन् <i>a.</i> internally illuminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्क्पुष्पा
प्रत्यञ्च् + -पुष्पा Achyranthes aspera (Mar. आघाडा); Mātaṅga L. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्क्प्रवण
प्रत्यञ्च् + -प्रवण <i>a.</i> devoted to the individual soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्ङ्मुख
प्रत्यञ्च् + -मुख <i>a.</i> (प्रत्यङ्मुख)<BR>—1 facing the west; श्रियं प्रत्यङ्मुखो भुङ्क्ते Ms. 2. 52.<BR>—2 having the face averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्ग्रथाः
प्रत्यञ्च् + -रथाः (Pl.) (प्रत्यग्रथाः) N. of the Ahicchatra country; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्क्स्रोतस्
प्रत्यञ्च् + -स्रोतस् (प्रत्यक्स्रोतस्) flowing towards the west; Malli.<BR> on Śi. 4. 66. ━(<i>f.</i>) an epithet of the river Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्चित|प्रत्यंचित
प्रत्यञ्चित <i>a.</i> Honoured, worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञा
प्रत्यभिज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To recognize; ततस्ते प्रत्यभिज्ञाय अर्जुनाय न्यवेदयन् Rām. 7. 33. 5.<BR>—2 To come to oneself, recover consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञा
प्रत्यभिज्ञा<BR>—1 Knowing, recognition; सप्रत्यभिज्ञमिव मामवलोक्य Māl. 1. 25.<BR>—2 (Phil.) A particular type of knowledge; ननु केयं प्रत्यभिज्ञा नाम<BR> न तावदेकस्यातीतवर्तमानकालद्वयसम्बन्धविषयं प्रत्यक्षज्ञानं प्रत्यभिज्ञा,<BR> प्रत्यक्षज्ञानस्य वर्तमानमात्रार्थग्राहित्वात् Vivaraṇaprameya-saṃgraha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यभिज्ञादर्शनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञादर्शनम्
प्रत्यभिज्ञा + -दर्शनम् Maheśvaraśāstra; a work on Śaiva philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञानम्
प्रत्यभिज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Recognition; see the word अभिज्ञान also.<BR>—2 A token of recognition (in return); प्रत्याभिज्ञानरत्नं च रामायादर्शयत्<BR> कृती R. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञात
प्रत्यभिज्ञात <i>p. p.</i> Recognised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिनन्द्
प्रत्यभिनन्द् P.<BR>—1 To greet in return.<BR>—2 To bid welcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिभाषिन्
प्रत्यभिभाषिन् <i>a.</i> Speaking to, addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिभूत
प्रत्यभिभूत <i>p. p.</i> Overcome, conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियुक्त
प्रत्यभियुक्त <i>p. p.</i> Accused in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियोगः|प्रत्यभियोग
प्रत्यभियोगः A counter-charge, an accusation in return; कुर्यात्<BR> प्रत्यभियोगं च कलहे साहसेषु च Y. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिलेख्यम्
प्रत्यभिलेख्यम् A counter-document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवद्
प्रत्यभिवद्^1 <i>Caus.</i> To salute or greet in return.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. note: root 'vad'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवादः|प्रत्यभिवाद
प्रत्यभिवादः, प्रत्यभिवादनम् Returning a salutation; यो<BR> न वेत्त्यभिवादस्य विप्रः प्रत्यभिवादनम् Ms. 2. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवादनम्
प्रत्यभिवादः, प्रत्यभिवादनम् Returning a salutation; यो<BR> न वेत्त्यभिवादस्य विप्रः प्रत्यभिवादनम् Ms. 2. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिस्कन्दनम्
प्रत्यभिस्कन्दनम् A counter-plaint or charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभ्युत्थानम्
प्रत्यभ्युत्थानम् Rising from a seat through politeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययः|प्रत्यय
प्रत्ययः<BR>—1 Conviction, settled belief; मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयबुद्धिः M. 1. 2;<BR> संजातप्रत्ययः Pt. 4.<BR>—2 Trust, reliance, faith, confidence; रक्षन् प्रत्ययमात्मनः Rām. 3. 9. 19;<BR> बलवदपि शिक्षितानामात्मन्यप्रत्ययं चेतः Ś. 1. 2; Ku. 6. 20;<BR> Śi. 18. 63; Bh. 3. 60; प्रत्ययार्थं हि लोकानामेवमेव मया कृतम्<BR> Abhiṣeka. 6. 29.<BR>—3 Conception, idea, notion, opinion.<BR>—4 Surety, certainty; प्रत्ययार्थं ततः सीता विवेश ज्वलनं तदा<BR> Rām. 7. 45. 7.<BR>—5 Knowledge, experience, cognition; स्थानप्रत्ययात् Ś. 7 ‘judging by the place’<BR>; so आकृतिप्रत्ययात् M. 1; Me. 8.<BR>—6 A cause, ground, means of action; स्वकर्मप्रत्ययाँल्लोकान् मत्वाऽर्जुनमब्रवीत्<BR> Mb. 13. 1. 77; अपेक्षते प्रत्ययमुत्तमं त्वाम् Ku. 3. 18.<BR>—7 Celebrity, fame, renown.<BR>—8 A termination, an affix or suffix; केवलं दधति कर्तृवाचिनः प्रत्ययानिह<BR> न जातु कर्मणि Śi. 14. 66.<BR>—9 An oath.<BR>—10 A dependant.<BR>—11 A usage, practice.<BR>—12 A hole.<BR>—13 Intellect, understanding (बुद्धि).<BR>—14 An assistant or associate.<BR>—15 An epithet of Viṣṇu; नामरूपे भगवती प्रत्ययस्त्वमपाश्रयः Bhāg. 6. 19. 14.<BR>—16 (With Buddhists) A co-operating cause.<BR>—17 An instrument, a means of agency.<BR>—18 Religious contemplation.<BR>—19 A householder who keeps a sacred fire.<BR>—20 Function of the organs (इन्द्रियवृत्ति); सर्वेन्द्रियगुणद्रष्ट्रे<BR> सर्वप्रत्ययहेतवे Bhāg. 8. 3. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्ययकारकः, प्रत्ययकारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययकारकः|प्रत्ययकारक
प्रत्ययः + -कारकः, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> producing assurance, convincing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययकारक्णी
प्रत्ययः + -कारकः, -कारिन् + .({@-णी@}) a seal, signet-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययकारिन्
प्रत्ययः + -कारकः, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> producing assurance, convincing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययित|प्रत्ययितः
प्रत्ययित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relied upon, confided in.<BR>—2 Trusty, confidential.<BR>—3 Trustworthy; यत्तु लौकिकं वचनं तच्चेत् प्रत्ययितात् पुरुषात् इन्द्रियविषयं<BR> वा अवितथमेव तत् ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययिन्
प्रत्ययिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relying upon, trusting, believing.<BR>—2 Trustworthy, confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्चनम्
प्रत्यर्चनम् Returning a salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ्
प्रत्यर्थ् €10 Ā.<BR>—1 To challenge (to combat), encounter, seek as an opponent; एते सीताद्रुहः<BR> संख्ये प्रत्यर्थयत राघवम् Bk. 6. 25.<BR>—2 To make an enemy of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ
प्रत्यर्थ <i>a.</i> Useful, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थम्
प्रत्यर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@}<BR>—1 A reply, an answer.<BR>—2 Hostility, opposition. ━<i>ind.</i> At every object, in every case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थवेदनः
प्रत्यर्थ + .{@-वेदनः@} Of contrary sensitivity; Mātaṅga L. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थकः|प्रत्यर्थक
प्रत्यर्थकः, प्रत्यर्थिकः An opponent; वहुप्रत्यर्थिकं<BR> ह्येतद्राज्यं नाम कुरूद्वह Mb. 15. 36. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिकः|प्रत्यर्थिक
प्रत्यर्थकः, प्रत्यर्थिकः An opponent; वहुप्रत्यर्थिकं<BR> ह्येतद्राज्यं नाम कुरूद्वह Mb. 15. 36. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिन्
प्रत्यर्थिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Hostile, opposing, inimical to; नास्मि भवत्योरीश्वरनियोगप्रत्यथीं V. 2.<BR>—2 Emulating.<BR>—3 Contradicting. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An opponent, adversary, enemy.<BR>—2 A rival, equal, match; चन्द्रो मुखस्य प्रत्यथीं.<BR>—3 (In law) A defendant; स धर्मस्थसखः शश्वदर्थिप्रत्यर्थिनां स्वयम्<BR> R. 17. 39; Ms. 8. 79; प्रत्यर्थिनोऽग्रतो लेख्यं यथावेदितमर्थिना Y. 2. 6.<BR>—4 An obstacle or impediment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यर्थिभूत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिभूत
प्रत्यर्थिन् + -भूत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">Page1087-1</a>]<BR> <i>a.</i> coming in the way, become an obstacle; प्रत्यर्थिभूतामपि तां<BR> समाधेः शुश्रूषमाणां गिरीशोऽनुमेने Ku. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1086-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पणम्
प्रत्यर्पणम् Giving back, restoring; सीताप्रत्यर्पणौषिणः R. 15. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पित|प्रत्यर्पितं
प्रत्यर्पित <i>p. p.</i> Restored, given back; जातो ममायं विशदः<BR> प्रकामं प्रत्यर्पितन्यास इवान्तरात्मा Ś. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवकर्शन
प्रत्यवकर्शन <i>a.</i> Baffling, annihilating; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्शः|प्रत्यवमर्श
प्रत्यवमर्शः, -र्षः<BR>—1 Profound meditation or reflection.<BR>—2 Counsel, advice.<BR>—3 A counter-conclusion.<BR>—4 Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्षः|प्रत्यवमर्ष
प्रत्यवमर्शः, -र्षः<BR>—1 Profound meditation or reflection.<BR>—2 Counsel, advice.<BR>—3 A counter-conclusion.<BR>—4 Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्शनम्
प्रत्यवमर्शनम् Contemplation, meditation; कृतशोकानुतापेन सद्यः<BR> प्रत्यवमर्शनात् Bhāg. 3. 14. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवरोधनम्
प्रत्यवरोधनम् Obstruction, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसानम्
प्रत्यवसानम् Eating, or drinking; P. I. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसित|प्रत्यवसितं
प्रत्यवसित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eaten, drunk.<BR>—2 Relapsed into the old (bad) way of life; ये प्रत्यवसिताश्चैव ते<BR> वै निरयगामिनः Mb. 13. 23. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कन्दः|प्रत्यवस्कन्द|प्रत्यवस्कंद|प्रत्यवस्कंदः
प्रत्यवस्कन्दः, -दनम्<BR> (In law) A special plea; admitting a fact, but qualifying<BR> it in such a manner that it may not appear as a count of accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कन्दनम्
प्रत्यवस्कन्दः, -दनम्<BR> (In law) A special plea; admitting a fact, but qualifying<BR> it in such a manner that it may not appear as a count of accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्था
प्रत्यवस्था €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To stand separately.<BR>—2 To oppose, act hostilely, object to (in argument); अत्र केचित् प्रत्यवतिष्ठन्ते<BR> Ś. B.; दुष्टः प्रत्यवतिष्ठते तदधुना कस्मै किमाचक्ष्महे Bv. 1. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थातृ
प्रत्यवस्थातृ <i>m.</i> An opponent, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थानम्
प्रत्यवस्थानम्<BR>—1 Removal.<BR>—2 Hostility, opposition.<BR>—3 <i>Status quo</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थापनम्
प्रत्यवस्थापनम् Refreshing, strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवहारः|प्रत्यवहार
प्रत्यवहारः<BR>—1 Withdrawal; ततः प्रत्यवहारोऽभूत् सैन्यानां राघवाज्ञया Mb. 3. 284. 41.<BR>—2 Universal destruction, dissolution (of the world); सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवायः|प्रत्यवाय
प्रत्यवायः<BR>—1 Decrease, diminution.<BR>—2 An obstacle, impediment; danger; कुमारेण बहुप्रत्यवायेऽस्मिन् प्रदेशे<BR> कुतूहलिना न स्थातव्यम् Nāg. 4; U. 1. 8.<BR>—3 A contrary or opposite course, contrariety; उत्तमानुत्तमान् गच्छन्<BR> हीनान् हीनांश्च वर्जयन् । ब्राह्मणः श्रेष्ठतामेति प्रत्यवायेन शूद्रताम् ॥<BR> Ms. 4. 245.<BR>—4 A sin, an offence, sinfulness; अनुत्पत्तिं तथा चान्ये प्रत्यवायस्य<BR> मन्वते Jābāli; नेहाभिकमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते Bg. 2. 40.<BR>—5 Disappointment.<BR>—6 Disappearance of an existing thing.<BR>—7 Non-production of what does not exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्ष्
प्रत्यवेक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To look into, inspect, examine; प्रत्यवेक्षिताः प्रमदवनभूमयः<BR> Ś. 6; प्रत्यहं प्रत्यवेक्षेत नरश्चरितमात्मनः<BR>—2 To investigate, inquire into, transact; प्रत्यवेक्षितं पौरकार्यमार्येण Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षणम्
प्रत्यवेक्षणम्, प्रत्यवेक्षा Taking care of, regard for, looking<BR> after; भव्यमुख्याः समारम्भाः प्रत्यवेक्ष्या निरत्ययाः R. 17. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षा
प्रत्यवेक्षणम्, प्रत्यवेक्षा Taking care of, regard for, looking<BR> after; भव्यमुख्याः समारम्भाः प्रत्यवेक्ष्या निरत्ययाः R. 17. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षणा
प्रत्यवेक्षणा (With Buddhists) One of the 5 kinds of knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षितृ
प्रत्यवेक्षितृ <i>m.</i> A superintendent of, one who looks after; Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यस्त
प्रत्यस्त <i>p. p.</i> Thrown off, given up; प्रत्यस्तव्यसने महीयसि<BR> परं प्रीतोऽस्मि जामातरि Māl. 10. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यस्तमयः|प्रत्यस्तमय
प्रत्यस्तमयः<BR>—1 Setting (of the sun).<BR>—2 End, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकलित
प्रत्याकलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Enumerated.<BR>—2 Interposed, inserted,<BR>—3 Introduced (as a step in legal proceedings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकलितम्
प्रत्याकलित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Judicial decision as to which of the litigants is to prove his case.<BR>—2 Supplement to the written deposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याक्षेपक
प्रत्याक्षेपक <i>a.</i> (-पिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Jeering, derisive, deriding, treating scornfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्या
प्रत्याख्या €2 P.<BR>—1 To deny (as a fact).<BR>—2 To decline, refuse, reject.<BR>—3 To forbid, prohibit.<BR>—4 To interdict.<BR>—5 To excel, surpass; प्रत्याख्यातविशेषकं कुरबकं श्यामावदातारुणम् M. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यात|प्रत्याख्यातः
प्रत्याख्यात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Refused, denied.<BR>—2 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>—3 Set aside, rejected.<BR>—4 Repulsed.<BR>—5 Excelled, surpassed.<BR>—6 Informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यानम्
प्रत्याख्यानम्<BR>—1 Repulse, rejection; प्रत्याख्यानाच्च भीतैस्त्वम् Rām. 7. 9. 8.<BR>—2 Denial, refusal, disavowal; निकृष्टजातिसंसर्गवैक्लव्यात् प्रत्याख्यानपारुष्यम् Dk. 2. 3.<BR>—3 Disregard.<BR>—4 Reproach.<BR>—5 Refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्येय
प्रत्याख्येय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be denied, refuted.<BR>—2 To be cured, curable (as a disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागम्
प्रत्यागम् €1 P. To come back, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागतिः|प्रत्यागति
प्रत्यागतिः <i>f.</i> Coming back, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागमः|प्रत्यागम
प्रत्यागमः, प्रत्यागमनम्<BR>—1 Return, coming back.<BR>—2 Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागमनम्
प्रत्यागमः, प्रत्यागमनम्<BR>—1 Return, coming back.<BR>—2 Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याचक्षाणक
प्रत्याचक्षाणक <i>a.</i> Desirous of refuting or objecting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादा
प्रत्यादा €3 U.<BR>—1 To take back.<BR>—2 To recall, revoke.<BR>—3 To draw forth from.<BR>—4 To repeat, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादानम्
प्रत्यादानम्<BR>—1 Receiving back, resumption.<BR>—2 Repetition, reiteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिश्
प्रत्यादिश् €6 P.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To reject, discard, shun; प्रत्यादिष्टविशेषमण्डनविधिः Ś. 6. 6.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To repulse; प्रत्यादिदेशैनमभाषमाणा R. 6. 25.<BR>—2 To cast off, repudiate (as a person); कामं प्रत्यादिष्टां स्मरामि<BR> न परिग्रहं मुनेस्तनयाम् Ś. 5. 31.<BR>—3 To obscure, eclipse, defeat, throw into the shade or background; प्रत्यादिश्यन्त<BR> इव मे दृष्टलक्षभिदः शराः R. 1. 61; रक्षागृहगता दीपाः प्रत्यादिष्टा इव 10. 68.<BR>—4 To order back, countermand.<BR>—5 To direct, prescribe, enjoin.<BR>—6 To warn, caution.<BR>—7 To report to.<BR>—8 To summon.<BR>—9 To conquer, overcome.<BR>—10 To remove, set aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1087-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिष्ट|प्रत्यादिष्टः
प्रत्यादिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Prescribed.<BR>—2 Informed.<BR>—3 Rejected, repulsed.<BR>—4 Removed, set aside.<BR>—5 Obscured, thrown into the shade.<BR>—6 Warned, cautioned.<BR>—7 Declared.<BR>—8 Overcome, conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादेशः|प्रत्यादेश
प्रत्यादेशः<BR>—1 An order, a command.<BR>—2 Information, declaration.<BR>—3 Refusal, denial, rejection, repulse, repudiation; प्रत्यादेशान्न खलु<BR> भवतो धीरतां कल्पयामि Me. 116, 97; Ś. 6. 9.<BR>—4 Obscuring, eclipsing, one that obscures, puts to shame or throws into<BR> shade; या प्रत्यादेशो रूपगर्वितायाः श्रियः V. 1; K. 5.<BR>—5 Caution, warning.<BR>—6 Particularly divine caution, supernatural warning.<BR>—7 Reproach; न्यूनभावात्तु पश्यामि प्रत्यादेशमिवात्मनः Mb. 3. 2. 12.<BR>—8 Prevention, defence (निवारण); तत्तदेव हरेत्तस्य प्रत्यादेशाय<BR> पार्थिवः Ms. 8. 334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याधानम्
प्रत्याधानम् A place where anything is deposited, repository. इदं<BR> प्रत्याधानम् Bṛ. Up. 2. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याध्मानम्
प्रत्याध्मानम् A particular nervous disease, wind dropsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानयनम्
प्रत्यानयनम् Bringing back, recovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानाहः|प्रत्यानाह
प्रत्यानाहः Pleuritis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यापत्तिः|प्रत्यापत्ति
प्रत्यापत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Return; प्रत्यापत्तिमपश्यन्ती द्विजस्याचिन्तयत्तदा Bhāg. 10. 53. 22.<BR>—2 Aversion from or indifference to worldly objects (वैराग्य); प्रत्यापत्तिश्च<BR> यस्येह बालिशस्य न जायते Mb. 12. 291. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यापन्न
प्रत्यापन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Returned, restored.<BR>—2 One having a perverted mind; किंकष्टमनुपश्यामि फलं पापस्य कर्मणः ।<BR> प्रत्यापन्नस्य हि ततः Mb. 12. 291. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याम्नान
प्रत्याम्नान <i>a.</i> Representative; यजमानकर्तृत्वेन विधीयन्ते<BR> प्रत्याम्नानाश्च ऋत्विजो निवर्तन्ते Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याम्नायः|प्रत्याम्नाय
प्रत्याम्नायः<BR>—1 The fifth member of a complete syllogism; <i>i. e.</i> निगमन (the<BR> repetition of the first proposition).<BR>—2 Contrary determination.<BR>—3 Ved. A substitute; see प्रत्याम्नान; प्रत्याम्नायं तु त्वं ह्येनं मा<BR> हिंसीः Mb. 3. 197. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायः|प्रत्याय
प्रत्यायः<BR>—1 A toll, tax.<BR>—2 Revenue, income.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायक
प्रत्यायक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proving, explaining.<BR>—2 Convincing, producing assurance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायनम्
प्रत्यायनम्<BR>—1 Leading home (a bride), marrying.<BR>—2 Setting (of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायनम्
प्रत्यायनम् + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Producing confidence.<BR>—2 Explaining.<BR>—3 Proving, demonstrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायना
प्रत्यायनम् + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Producing confidence.<BR>—2 Explaining.<BR>—3 Proving, demonstrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायितः|प्रत्यायित
प्रत्यायितः A confidential agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यालीढम्
प्रत्यालीढम् A particular attitude in shooting (opp. आलीढ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावर्तनम्
प्रत्यावर्तनम्, -प्रत्यावृत्तिः<BR> Returning, coming back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावृत्तिः|प्रत्यावृत्ति
प्रत्यावर्तनम्, -प्रत्यावृत्तिः<BR> Returning, coming back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वस्त
प्रत्याश्वस्त <i>p. p.</i> Consoled, revived, refreshed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वासः|प्रत्याश्वास
प्रत्याश्वासः Respiration, recovery (of breath); एकश्चाप्यगणः<BR> संख्ये प्रत्याश्वासमरोचयम् Mb. 9. 31. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वासनम्
प्रत्याश्वासनम् Consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासंकलितम्
प्रत्यासंकलितम् Consideration pro and con.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासत्तिः|प्रत्यासत्ति
प्रत्यासत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Close proximity or contiguity (in time or space); रिपुः प्रत्यासत्तेरहिरिव<BR> भयं नो जनयति Mv. 4. 7.<BR>—2 Close contact; दूरे प्रत्यासत्तिर्दर्शनमपि दुर्लभमधन्यैः Mu. 4. 4.<BR>—3 An analogy.<BR>—4 Good humour, cheerfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्न|प्रत्यासन्नः
प्रत्यासन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Proximate, near, contiguous.<BR>—2 Imminent; प्रत्यासन्ने नभसि Me. 4.<BR>—3 Feeling repentance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्यासन्नमरण, प्रत्यासन्नमृत्यु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्नमरण
प्रत्यासन्न + -मरण, -मृत्यु <i>a.</i> at the point of death, about to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्नमृत्यु
प्रत्यासन्न + -मरण, -मृत्यु <i>a.</i> at the point of death, about to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्नता
प्रत्यासन्नता Proximity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासरः|प्रत्यासर
प्रत्यास(सा)रः<BR>—1 The rear of an army.<BR>—2 A form of array, one array behind another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासारः|प्रत्यासार
प्रत्यास(सा)रः<BR>—1 The rear of an army.<BR>—2 A form of array, one array behind another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहत
प्रत्याहत <i>a.</i> Distracted, repelled; प्रत्याहतास्त्रो गिरिशप्रभावात् R. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृ
प्रत्याहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To take back again, bring back, recover.<BR>—2 To withdraw, draw back.<BR>—3 To utter (a speech).<BR>—4 To report.<BR>—5 To re-arrange, restore.<BR>—6 To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरणम्
प्रत्याहरणम्<BR>—1 Bringing or taking back recovery.<BR>—2 Withholding.<BR>—3 Restraining the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहारः|प्रत्याहार
प्रत्याहारः<BR>—1 Drawing back, marching back, retreat.<BR>—2 Keeping back, withholding.<BR>—3 Restraining the organs; स्वविषयाऽसंप्रयोगे चित्तस्य स्वरूपानुकार<BR> इवेन्द्रियाणां प्रत्याहारः Pātañjala S.<BR>—4 Dissolution of the world; प्रत्याहारं तु वक्ष्यामि शर्वर्यादौ गतेऽहनि<BR> Mb. 12. 233. 1.<BR>—6 (In gram.) The comprehension of several letters or affixes into one<BR> syllable, effected by combining the first letter of a Sūtra with its<BR> final indicatory letter, or in the case of several Sūtras, with the final<BR> letter of the last member; thus अण् is the प्रत्याहार of the Sūtra<BR> ऐउण्; अच् (vowels) of the four Sūtras ऐउण्, ऋलूक्, एओङ्, ऐऔच्; हल्<BR> of the consonants; अल् of all letters.<BR>—6 Abridgment.<BR>—7 (In drama) N. of a particular part of the पूर्वरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृत
प्रत्याहृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Got back, recovered.<BR>—2 Restrained, withheld, checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्त
प्रत्युक्त <i>p. p.</i> Answered, said in return, replied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्तिः|प्रत्युक्ति
प्रत्युक्तिः <i>f.</i> A reply, an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युच्चारः|प्रत्युच्चार
प्रत्युच्चारः, -च्चारणम्<BR>—1 Repetition.<BR>—2 Answering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युच्चारणम्
प्रत्युच्चारः, -च्चारणम्<BR>—1 Repetition.<BR>—2 Answering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युज्जीव्
प्रत्युज्जीव् €1 P. To revive, return to life. ━<i>Caus.</i> To restore<BR> or bring to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युज्जीवनम्
प्रत्युज्जीवनम्<BR>—1 Reviving, restoring to life, resuscitation (fig. also).<BR>—2 Coming to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत
प्रत्युत <i>ind.</i> —1 On the contrary; कृतमपि महोपकारं पय<BR> इव पीत्वा निरातङ्कः । प्रत्युत हन्तुं यतते काकोदरसोदरः खलो जगति<BR> Bv. 1. 76; विषादे कर्तव्ये विदधति जडाः प्रत्युत मुदम् Bh. 3. 25; Śi. 1. 39.<BR>—2 Rather, even.<BR>—3 On the other hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1088-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रमः|प्रत्युत्क्रम
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, -त्क्रमणम्, -त्क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An undertaking.<BR>—2 Preparations for war.<BR>—3 Marching out to attack an enemy.<BR>—4 A secondary act or effort tending to a main object.<BR>—5 The first step in any business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रमणम्
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, -त्क्रमणम्, -त्क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An undertaking.<BR>—2 Preparations for war.<BR>—3 Marching out to attack an enemy.<BR>—4 A secondary act or effort tending to a main object.<BR>—5 The first step in any business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रान्तिः|प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति|प्रत्युत्क्रांति|प्रत्युत्क्रांतिः
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, -त्क्रमणम्, -त्क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An undertaking.<BR>—2 Preparations for war.<BR>—3 Marching out to attack an enemy.<BR>—4 A secondary act or effort tending to a main object.<BR>—5 The first step in any business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थानम्
प्रत्युत्थानम्<BR>—1 Rising against; मङ्गलाद्यप्रयोगं च प्रत्युत्थानं च सर्वतः<BR> Rām. 2. 100. 67.<BR>—2 Making preparations for war.<BR>—3 Rising from oneʼs seat (as a mark of respect) to welcome a visitor;<BR> असवर्णास्तु संपूज्याः प्रत्युत्थानाभिवादनैः Ms. 2. 210.<BR>—4 Making preparations for, undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थित
प्रत्युत्थित <i>p. p.</i> Risen to meet or encounter (a friend, foe &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्न|प्रत्युत्पन्नः
प्रत्युत्पन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Reproduced, regenerated.<BR>—2 Prompt, ready, quick.<BR>—3 (In math.) Multiplied.<BR>—4 Present, existing at present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नम्
प्रत्युत्पन्न + .{@-न्नम्@} Multiplication.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रत्युत्पन्नबुद्धि, प्रत्युत्पन्नमति, प्रत्युत्पन्नजातिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नबुद्धि
प्रत्युत्पन्न + -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of presence of mind, ready-witted; इदं तत्प्रत्युत्पन्नमति<BR> स्त्रैणमिति यदुच्यते Ś. 5. 21/22.<BR>—2 bold, confident.<BR>—3 subtle, sharp; प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः प्राप्तां क्रियां कर्तुं व्यवस्यति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नमति|प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः
प्रत्युत्पन्न + -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of presence of mind, ready-witted; इदं तत्प्रत्युत्पन्नमति<BR> स्त्रैणमिति यदुच्यते Ś. 5. 21/22.<BR>—2 bold, confident.<BR>—3 subtle, sharp; प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः प्राप्तां क्रियां कर्तुं व्यवस्यति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नजातिः|प्रत्युत्पन्नजाति
प्रत्युत्पन्न + -जातिः (in math.) assimilation consisting in multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युदाहरणम्
प्रत्युदाहरणम् A counter-illustration, an example to the contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गम्
प्रत्युद्गम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go forth or advance towards to meet (as a mark of respect); प्रत्युज्जगामातिथिमातिथेयः<BR> R. 5. 2; प्रत्युद्गच्छति मूर्छति स्थिरतमः पुञ्जे निकुञ्जे प्रियः Gīt. 11; Bv. 3. 3.<BR>—2 To advance or march towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गत
प्रत्युद्गत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Risen from oneʼs seat as a mark of respect to greet or welcome a guest;<BR> प्रत्युद्गतो मां भरतः ससैन्यः R. 13. 64, 12. 62.<BR>—2 Gone forth against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गतिः|प्रत्युद्गति
प्रत्युद्गतिः <i>f.</i>, प्रत्युद्गमः, प्रत्युद्गमनम् Going out<BR> or rising from oneʼs seat to meet or greet a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमः|प्रत्युद्गम
प्रत्युद्गतिः <i>f.</i>, प्रत्युद्गमः, प्रत्युद्गमनम् Going out<BR> or rising from oneʼs seat to meet or greet a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमनम्
प्रत्युद्गतिः <i>f.</i>, प्रत्युद्गमः, प्रत्युद्गमनम् Going out<BR> or rising from oneʼs seat to meet or greet a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमनीयम्
प्रत्युद्गमनीयम् A clean pair of garments; गृहीतप्रत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा<BR> Ku. 7. 11. (v. l. for ˚पत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा); see उद्गमनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धरणम्
प्रत्युद्धरणम्<BR>—1 Recovering, re-obtaining.<BR>—2 Raising up again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धारः|प्रत्युद्धार
प्रत्युद्धारः Offering, tendering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यमः|प्रत्युद्यम
प्रत्युद्यमः<BR>—1 Counterbalance, counterpoise.<BR>—2 An effort or measure against, counteraction; संदीप्ते भवने तु कूपखननं<BR> प्रत्युद्यमः कीदृशः Bh. 3. 88, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यात
प्रत्युद्यात <i>a.</i> See प्रत्युद्गत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युन्नमनम्
प्रत्युन्नमनम् Rising or springing up again, rebounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकृ
प्रत्युपकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To requite a favour, render a service in return.<BR>—2 To repay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकारः|प्रत्युपकार
प्रत्युपकारः<BR>—1 Returning a service or kindness, requital of an obligation, service in return.<BR>—2 Mutual assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपक्रिया
प्रत्युपक्रिया Return of a service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपदेशः|प्रत्युपदेश
प्रत्युपदेशः Advice in return; व्यनीयत प्रत्युपदेशलुब्धैः Ku. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपपन्न
प्रत्युपपन्न <i>a.</i> See प्रत्युत्पन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपमानम्
प्रत्युपमानम्<BR>—1 A counterpart of a resemblance.<BR>—2 A pattern, model.<BR>—3 A counter-comparison; उपमानस्यापि सखे प्रत्युपमानं वपुस्तस्याः V. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपलब्ध
प्रत्युपलब्ध <i>p. p.</i> Got back, recovered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपवेशः|प्रत्युपवेश
प्रत्युपवेशः, -वेशनम्<BR> Besetting any one in order to bring him to compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपवेशनम्
प्रत्युपवेशः, -वेशनम्<BR> Besetting any one in order to bring him to compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्थानम्
प्रत्युपस्थानम् Viscinity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्थापनम्
प्रत्युपस्थापनम् Mental realization.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्थित
प्रत्युपस्थित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Approached, come near to.<BR>—2 Present.<BR>—3 Collecting, pressing (as urine).<BR>—4 Gone against, standing opposite to; श्रेयसा योजयत्याशु श्रेयसि प्रत्युपस्थिते<BR> Mb. 12. 287. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्पर्शनम्
प्रत्युपस्पर्शनम् Touching, sipping (water) again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपहारः|प्रत्युपहार
प्रत्युपहारः<BR>—1 A respectful offering.<BR>—2 Giving back, restoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपाकरणम्
प्रत्युपाकरणम् Recommencement of Vedic study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युप्त
प्रत्युप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Inlaid, set with, studded; Mv. 1. 34.<BR>—2 Sown.<BR>—3 Fixed, implanted, firmly fixed or lodged; Māl. 5. 10; यथा तिरश्चीनमलातशल्यं<BR> प्रत्युप्तमन्तः सविषश्च दंशः U. 3. 35, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषः|प्रत्युष
प्रत्युषः, -प्रत्युषस् <i>n.</i><BR> Morning, day-break, dawn; याति व्यक्तिं पुरस्तादरुणकिसलये<BR> प्रत्युषः पारिजातः Sūryaśatakam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषस्
प्रत्युषः, -प्रत्युषस् <i>n.</i><BR> Morning, day-break, dawn; याति व्यक्तिं पुरस्तादरुणकिसलये<BR> प्रत्युषः पारिजातः Sūryaśatakam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषः|प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषं
प्रत्यूषः, -षम्<BR> Day-break, morning, dawn; प्रत्यूषेषु स्फुटितकमलामोदमैत्रीकषायः<BR> Me. 31; महत्येव प्रत्यूषे Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषम्
प्रत्यूषः, -षम्<BR> Day-break, morning, dawn; प्रत्यूषेषु स्फुटितकमलामोदमैत्रीकषायः<BR> Me. 31; महत्येव प्रत्यूषे Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषः|प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषं
प्रत्यूषः, -षम् + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 N. of one of the eight Vasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषस्
प्रत्यूषस् <i>n.</i> Day-break, morning, dawn; स्नानमत्यधिकं कार्यं<BR> प्रत्यूषस्यात्मनो जले Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूह्
प्रत्यूह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To oppose, resist.<BR>—2 To disturb, interrupt, impede.<BR>—3 To reject, refuse.<BR>—4 To excel, surpass.<BR>—5 To offer, present; पशून् देवताभ्यः प्रत्यौहत Bṛ. Up. 1. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूढ
प्रत्यूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rejected, refused; प्रत्यूढकर्मकलिलप्रकृतिं प्रपद्ये Bhāg. 4. 22. 38.<BR>—2 Neglected.<BR>—3 Surpassed.<BR>—4 Covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूहः|प्रत्यूह
प्रत्यूहः Impediment, obstacle, hindrance; विस्मयः सर्वथा हेयः<BR> प्रत्यूहः सर्वकर्मणाम् H. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूहनम्
प्रत्यूहनम् Interruption, discontinuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथ्
प्रथ् I. €1 Ā. (प्रथते, प्रथित)<BR>—1 To increase (wealth &c.); तत्प्रथ्यमानवपुषा<BR> व्यथितात्मभोगः Bhāg. 10. 16. 24.<BR>—2 To spread abroad (as fame, rumour &c.); तथा यशोऽस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">Page1090-1</a>]<BR> प्रथते Ms. 11. 15.<BR>—3 To become famous or celebrated; अतस्तदाख्यया तीर्थं पावनं भुवि<BR> पप्रथे R. 15. 101; अतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः Bg. 15. 18;<BR> Śi. 9. 16, 15. 23; Ku. 5. 7; Me. 24; R. 5. 65, 9. 76.<BR>—4 To appear, arise, come to light; श्रमो नु तासां मदनो नु पप्रथे Ki. 8. 53.<BR>—5 To occur (to mind). ━II. €10 U. (प्रथयति-ते, प्रथित)<BR>—1 To spread abroad, proclaim; सज्जना एव साधूनां प्रथयन्ति गुणोत्करम्<BR> Dṛ. Ś. 12; Bk. 17. 107; जगद्भ्रमणकौतुकोच्चलितरामकीर्त्यङ्गनाप्रयाणपटहध्वनिं<BR> प्रथयति स्म ताराध्वनिः Rāmāyaṇachampū.<BR>—2 To show, manifest, display, evince, indicate; परमं वपुः प्रथयतीव<BR> जयम् Ki. 6. 35, 5. 3; Śi. 10. 25; Ratn. 4. 13; Ś. 3. 14.<BR>—3 To increase, enlarge, enhance, augment, stretch; अवस्था वस्तूनि प्रथयति<BR> च संकोचयति च Bh. 2. 45.<BR>—4 To disclose.<BR>—5 To spread, extend.<BR>—6 To throw, cast.<BR>—7 To celebrate (प्राथयति); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1089-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथनम्
प्रथनम् [प्रथ्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Spreading, extension.<BR>—2 Scattering.<BR>—3 Throwing, projecting.<BR>—4 Showing, evincing, displaying.<BR>—5 A place where anything is spread.<BR>—6 Celebrating, proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथस्
प्रथस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम [प्रथ्-अमच्] (Nom. pl. <i>m.</i> प्रथमे or प्रथमाः)<BR>—1 First, foremost; मखांशभाजां प्रथमो मनीषिभिस्त्वमेव देवेन्द्र सदा<BR> निगद्यसे R. 3. 44; H. 2. 39; Ki. 2. 44.<BR>—2 First, chief, principal, most excellent or eminent, matchless, incomparable;<BR> Śi. 15. 42; एष वै प्रथमः कल्पः प्रदाने हव्यकव्ययोः Ms. 3. 147.<BR>—3 Earliest, most ancient, primary.<BR>—4 Prior, previous, former, earlier; प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया Me. 17;<BR> नामधेयं गुरुश्चक्रे जगत्प्रथममङ्गलम् R. 10. 67.<BR>—5 (In gram.) The first person (= third person according to European phraseology).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमः|प्रथम
प्रथम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 The first (third) person.<BR>—2 The first consonant of a class.<BR>—3 (In math.) The sum of the products divided by the difference between<BR> the squares of the cosine of the azimuth and the sine of the amplitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमा
प्रथम + .{@-मा@} The nominative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमम्
प्रथम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 first, firstly, at first; उमास्तनोद्भेदमनुप्रवृद्धो मनोरथो यः<BR> प्रथमं बभूव Ku. 7. 24; R. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Already, previously, formerly; प्रथमोदितम् aforesaid; तमभ्यनन्दत्<BR> प्रथमं प्रबोधितः प्रजेश्वरः शासनहारिणा हरेः R. 3. 68.<BR>—3 At once, immediately.<BR>—4 Before; यात्रायै चोदयामास तं शक्तेः प्रथमं शरत् R. 4. 24;<BR> उत्तिष्ठेत् प्रथमं चास्य चरमं चैव संविशेत् Ms. 2. 194.<BR>—5 Newly, recently. प्रथमम्━अनन्तरम् or ततः or पश्रात्<BR> first━afterwards; प्रथमात् firstly, for the first time; प्रथमतः<BR>—1 At first, firstly.<BR>—2 previously.<BR>—3 immediately.<BR>—4 before, in preference to (gen.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रथमार्धः, प्रथमार्धम्, प्रथमागामिन्, प्रथमादेशः, प्रथमाश्रमः, प्रथमेतर, प्रथमोदित, प्रथमोत्पन्न, प्रथमकल्पः, प्रथमकल्पित, प्रथमकुसुमः, प्रथमगर्भ,^1 प्रथमगिरिः, प्रथमज, प्रथमदर्शनम्, प्रथमदिवसः, प्रथमनवनीतम्, प्रथमनिर्दिष्ट, प्रथमपुरुषः, प्रथममङ्गल, प्रथमयौवनम्, प्रथमवयस्, प्रथमवसतिः, प्रथमवित्ता, प्रथमविरहः, प्रथमवृत्तान्तः, प्रथमवैयाकरणः, प्रथमश्री, प्रथमश्रुत, प्रथमसाहसः, प्रथमसुकृतम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमार्धः|प्रथमार्ध
प्रथम + -अर्धः, -अर्धम् the first half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमार्धम्
प्रथम + -अर्धः, -अर्धम् the first half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमागामिन्
प्रथम + -आगामिन् <i>a.</i> first mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमादेशः|प्रथमादेश
प्रथम + -आदेशः placing at the beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमाश्रमः|प्रथमाश्रम
प्रथम + -आश्रमः the first of the four stages in the religious life of<BR> a Brāhmaṇa; <i>i. e.</i> Brahmacharya; शरीरबद्धः प्रथमाश्रमो यथा Ku. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमेतर
प्रथम + -इतर <i>a.</i> ‘other than first’, the second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमोदित
प्रथम + -उदित <i>a.</i> first uttered; उवाच धात्र्या प्रथमोदितं वचः R. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमोत्पन्न
प्रथम + -उत्पन्न <i>a.</i> first born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमकल्पः|प्रथमकल्प
प्रथम + -कल्पः<BR>—1 the best course to adopt.<BR>—2 an excellent suggestion or idea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमकल्पित
प्रथम + -कल्पित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 first<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">Page1090-2</a>]<BR> thought out.<BR>—2 first in rank or importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमकुसुमः|प्रथमकुसुम
प्रथम + -कुसुमः white marjoran.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमगर्भ
प्रथम + -गर्भ^1 <i>a.</i> pregnant for the first time.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमगिरिः
प्रथम + -गिरिः the Eastern mountain; द्वित्रेषु द्युमणिकरेषु शेखरत्वं<BR> प्राप्तेषु प्रथमगिरिः प्रयाति सोऽयम् Rām. Ch. 7. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमज
प्रथम + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 first-born.<BR>—2 original, primary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमदर्शनम्
प्रथम + -दर्शनम् first sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमदिवसः|प्रथमदिवस
प्रथम + -दिवसः the first day; आषाढस्य प्रथमदिवसे Me. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमनवनीतम्
प्रथम + -नवनीतम्<BR>—1 the butter which appears first after churning.<BR>—2 the milk of a cow at the time when hundred days have elapsed after her delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमनिर्दिष्ट
प्रथम + -निर्दिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> first mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमपुरुषः|प्रथमपुरुष
प्रथम + -पुरुषः the first person (= third person according to the English<BR> system of treating Sanskrit grammar); अथवा अस्तिर्भवतीतिपरः प्रथमपुरुषे<BR> प्रयुज्यमानोऽप्यस्तीति ŚB. on MS. 11. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथममङ्गल
प्रथम + -मङ्गल <i>a.</i> highly auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमयौवनम्
प्रथम + -यौवनम् early youth or age, youthful state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवयस्
प्रथम + -वयस् <i>n.</i> early age, youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवसतिः|प्रथमवसति
प्रथम + -वसतिः the original home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवित्ता
प्रथम + -वित्ता Ved. a first wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमविरहः|प्रथमविरह
प्रथम + -विरहः separation for the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवृत्तान्तः|प्रथमवृत्तान्त
प्रथम + -वृत्तान्तः antecedents, former circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमवैयाकरणः|प्रथमवैयाकरण
प्रथम + -वैयाकरणः<BR>—1 the most distinguished grammarian.<BR>—2 a beginner in grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमश्री
प्रथम + -श्री <i>a.</i> One who has just become rich or fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमश्रुत
प्रथम + -श्रुत <i>a.</i> heard for the first time; न हि प्रथमश्रुताच्छब्दात्<BR> कश्चिदर्थं प्रत्येति ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमसाहसः|प्रथमसाहस
प्रथम + -साहसः the first or lowest of the three degrees of punishment<BR> or fine; पणानां द्वे शते सार्धे प्रथमः साहसः स्मृतः Ms. 8. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमसुकृतम्
प्रथम + -सुकृतम् former kindness or service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमक
प्रथमक <i>a.</i> First, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथा
प्रथा Fame, celebrity; अतः श्रियः पतिरिति प्रथामगाः Śi. 15. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथित|प्रथितः
प्रथित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Increased, extended.<BR>—2 Published, proclaimed, spread, declared; प्रथितयशसां भासकविसोमिल्लकविमिआदीनाम्<BR> M. 1; तेनावतीर्य तुरगात् प्रथितान्वयेन R.<BR>—3 Shown, displayed, manifested, evinced; उवाच प्रथितं वचः Rām. 2. 2. 1.<BR>—4 Famous, celebrated, renowned, well known; यज्जीव्यते क्षणमपि प्रथितं<BR> मनुष्यैर्विज्ञानशौर्यविभवार्यंगुणैः समेतम् । तन्नाम जीवितम् … Pt. 1. 24;<BR> Ku. 5. 7.<BR>—5 Intent upon, engaged in, devoted to.<BR>—6 Spread, stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथितः|प्रथित
प्रथित + .{@-तः@} N. of Viṣṇu; अच्युतः प्रथितः प्राणः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथितिः|प्रथिति
प्रथितिः <i>f.</i> Celebrity, fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमन्
प्रथिमन् <i>m.</i> Breadth, greatness, extension, magnitude; प्रथिमानं<BR> दधानेन जघनेन घनेन सा Bk. 4. 17; (गुणाः) प्रारम्भसूक्ष्माः<BR> प्रथिमानमापुः R. 18. 49; Mv. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिविः|प्रथिवि
प्रथिविः <i>f.</i> The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिष्ठ|प्रथिष्ठः
प्रथिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Largest, widest, broadest; (superl. of पृथु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथीयस्
प्रथीयस् <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Larger, wider, broader.<BR>—2 More celebrated; कथा प्रथीयसी A. Rām. 1. 6. 3. (compar. of पृथु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथु|प्रथुः
प्रथु <i>a.</i> Wide, wide-spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुः|प्रथु
प्रथु + .{@-थुः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुकः|प्रथुक
प्रथुकः Rice parched and flattened (cf. पृथुक); (Mar. पोहे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1090-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम See under प्रथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं|प्रदक्षिणः
प्रदक्षिण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Being placed or standing on the right, moving to the right; प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14.<BR>—2 Respectful, reverential.<BR>—3 Auspicious, of good omen; सिध्यन्त्यर्था महाबाहो दैवं चात्र प्रदक्षिणम्<BR> Mb. 3. 36. 7; तदा वयं विजेष्यामो यदा कालः प्रदक्षिणः Bhāg. 10. 54. 16.<BR>—4 Clever, sharp; तानुवाच विनीतात्मा सूतपुत्रः प्रदक्षिणः Rām. 2. 16. 5.<BR>—5 Amenable, favourable; अभिवाद्याभ्यनुज्ञाता प्रदक्षिणमवर्तत Mb. 1. 122. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणः|प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं
प्रदक्षिण + .{@-णः, -णा, -णम्@} Circumambulation from left to right, so that the<BR> right side is always turned towards the person or object circumambulated,<BR> a reverential salutation made by walking in this manner; प्रदक्षिणप्रकमणात्<BR> कृशानोरुदर्चिषस्तन्मिथुनं चकासे Ku. 7. 79; Y. 1. 232; अष्टोत्तरशतं<BR> यस्तु देव्याः कुर्यात् प्रदक्षिणम् । सर्वान् कामान् समासाद्य पश्चान्मोक्षमवाप्नुयात् ॥<BR> Kālikā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणा
प्रदक्षिण + .{@-णः, -णा, -णम्@} Circumambulation from left to right, so that the<BR> right side is always turned towards the person or object circumambulated,<BR> a reverential salutation made by walking in this manner; प्रदक्षिणप्रकमणात्<BR> कृशानोरुदर्चिषस्तन्मिथुनं चकासे Ku. 7. 79; Y. 1. 232; अष्टोत्तरशतं<BR> यस्तु देव्याः कुर्यात् प्रदक्षिणम् । सर्वान् कामान् समासाद्य पश्चान्मोक्षमवाप्नुयात् ॥<BR> Kālikā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणम्
प्रदक्षिण + .{@-णः, -णा, -णम्@} Circumambulation from left to right, so that the<BR> right side is always turned towards the person or object circumambulated,<BR> a reverential salutation made by walking in this manner; प्रदक्षिणप्रकमणात्<BR> कृशानोरुदर्चिषस्तन्मिथुनं चकासे Ku. 7. 79; Y. 1. 232; अष्टोत्तरशतं<BR> यस्तु देव्याः कुर्यात् प्रदक्षिणम् । सर्वान् कामान् समासाद्य पश्चान्मोक्षमवाप्नुयात् ॥<BR> Kālikā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणम्
प्रदक्षिण + .{@-णम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From left to right; एवं सम्यग्घविर्हुत्वा सर्वदिक्षु प्रदक्षिणम् Ms. 3. 87.<BR>—2 Towards the right side, so that the right side is always turned towards<BR> the person or object circumambulated.<BR>—3 In a southern direction, towards the south.<BR>—4 All right, O. k.; श्रमो नाशमुपागच्छत् सर्वं चासीत् प्रदक्षिणम्<BR> Mb. 3. 151. 2. (प्रदक्षिणीकृ or प्रदक्षिणयति Den. P. means ‘to go round from left to right’<BR> as a mark of respect; प्रदक्षिणीकुरुष्व<BR> सद्योहुताग्नीन् Ś. 4; प्रदक्षिणीकृत्य हुतं हुताशनम् R. 2. 71).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रदक्षिणार्चिस्, प्रदक्षिणावर्त, प्रदक्षिणावृत्क, प्रदक्षिणक्रिया, प्रदक्षिणनम्, प्रदक्षिणपट्टिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणार्चिस्
प्रदक्षिण + -अर्चिस् <i>a.</i> flaming towards the right, having the flames turned<BR> towards the right; प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14. ━(<i>f.</i>)<BR> flames turned towards the right; प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्व्याजेन हस्तेनेव जयं<BR> ददौ R. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणावर्त
प्रदक्षिण + -आवर्त, -आवृत्क <i>a.</i> turned towards the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणावृत्क
प्रदक्षिण + -आवर्त, -आवृत्क <i>a.</i> turned towards the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणक्रिया
प्रदक्षिण + -क्रिया going round from left to right, keeping the right side<BR> towards one as a mark of respect; प्रदक्षिणक्रियार्हायां तस्यां त्वं साधु<BR> नाचरः R. 1. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणनम्
प्रदक्षिण + -नम् same as ˚क्रिया; किं प्रदक्षिणनकृद्भ्रमिपाशं जाम्बवानदित<BR> ते बलिबन्धे N. 21. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणपट्टिका
प्रदक्षिण + -पट्टिका a yard, court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदरः|प्रदर
प्रदरः<BR>—1 Rending, tearing.<BR>—2 (<i>a.</i>) A fracture, crack, cleft, crevice, chasm; इत्युक्त्वा लक्ष्मणं<BR> रामः प्रदरः खन्यतामिति Rām. 3. 4. 12; सीमानः प्रदरोदरेषु विरलस्वच्छाम्भसः U. 2. 16.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Breach, hole.<BR>—3 The dispersion of an army; न सन्निपाते प्रदरं वधं वा कुर्युरीदृशाः<BR> Mb. 12. 100. 34.<BR>—4 An arrow; त्रीण्येव च प्रदराणां स्म पार्थ Mb. 8. 76. 16.<BR>—5 A kind of disease of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्पः|प्रदर्प
प्रदर्पः, -प्रदृप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR> Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदृप्तिः|प्रदृप्ति
प्रदर्पः, -प्रदृप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR> Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदलः|प्रदल
प्रदलः An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदवः|प्रदव
प्रदवः Burning, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदव्यः|प्रदव्य
प्रदव्यः A forest conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदह्
प्रदह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To burn.<BR>—2 To consume, destroy completely.<BR>—3 To pain, torment.<BR>—4 To trouble, tease. ━<i>Pass.</i> To take or catch fire, be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदग्ध
प्रदग्ध <i>p. p.</i> Burnt up, consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदाहः|प्रदाह
प्रदाहः<BR>—1 Burning, heating.<BR>—2 Destruction; annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदा
प्रदा €3 U.<BR>—1 To grant, give, offer, present; स्वं प्रागहं प्रादिषि नामराय किं<BR> नाम तस्मै मनसा नराय N. 6. 95; Ms. 3. 99, 108, 273; Y. 2. 90.<BR>—2 To impart, teach (as learning); शिष्यप्रदेयागमाः (कवयः) Bh. 2. 15.<BR>—3 To give away; yield.<BR>—4 To give up, deliver.<BR>—5 To give away in marriage.<BR>—6 To sell; यत्रैकेन च यत् क्रीतं तच्छतेन प्रदीयते Pt. 1. 13.<BR>—7 To deliver up, restore.<BR>—8 To pay, discharge (a debt).<BR>—9 To put, place in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद|प्रदः
प्रद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 (At the end of comp.) Giving, bestowing, or conferring on, yielding;<BR> सुख˚, ताप˚, सस्य˚ &c.<BR>—2 Liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदा
प्रद + .{@-दा@} A gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदातृ
प्रदातृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A giver, donor.<BR>—2 A liberal man.<BR>—3 One who gives a daughter in marriage.<BR>—4 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानम्
प्रदानम्<BR>—1 Giving, granting, bestowing, offering; वर˚, अग्नि˚, काष्ठ˚ &c.;<BR> प्रदानं प्रच्छन्नं गृहमुपगते संभ्रमविधिः Bh. 1. 63.<BR>—2 Giving away in marriage; वैखानसं किमनया व्रतमा प्रदानाद् व्यापाररोधि<BR> मदनस्य निषेवितव्यम् Ś. 1. 26.<BR>—3 Imparting, instructing; विद्या˚.<BR>—4 A gift, donation, present.<BR>—5 A goad.<BR>—6 An oblation.<BR>—7 Refuting, frustrating (खण्डन); असदेव हि धर्मस्य प्रदानं<BR> धर्म आसुरः Mb. 13. 45. 8 (com.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रदानकृपण, प्रदानशूरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानकृपण
प्रदानम् + -कृपण <i>a.</i> illiberal; mean or niggardly in making presents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानशूरः|प्रदानशूर
प्रदानम् + -शूरः a very munificent man, donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानकम्
प्रदानकम् An offering, a gift, donation, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायम्
प्रदायम् A present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायिन्
प्रदायिन्, -प्रदायक <i>a.</i><BR> Granting, giving, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायक
प्रदायिन्, -प्रदायक <i>a.</i><BR> Granting, giving, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिः|प्रदि
प्रदिः, -प्रदेयः<BR> A present, gift; प्रदेयांश्च ददौ राजा सूतमागधवन्दिनाम्<BR> Rām. 1. 18. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेयः|प्रदेय
प्रदिः, -प्रदेयः<BR> A present, gift; प्रदेयांश्च ददौ राजा सूतमागधवन्दिनाम्<BR> Rām. 1. 18. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेय|प्रदेयः
प्रदेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be given, imparted, communicated &c.; किं वस्तु विद्वन् गुरवे<BR> प्रदेयम् R. 5. 18, 31.<BR>—2 To be given in marriage; इमे अपि प्रदेये Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिव्
प्रदिव् <i>a.</i> Ancient, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To point out, indicate, show, assign; तस्याधिकारपुरुषैः प्रणतैः<BR> प्रदिष्टाम् R. 5. 63, 2. 39.<BR>—2 To tell, mention, communicate; दानेषु यत् पुण्यफलं प्रदिष्टम्<BR> Bg. 8. 28; Bk. 4. 5.<BR>—3 To give, grant, offer, bestow or confer upon; विद्ययोः पथि मुनिप्रदिष्टयोः<BR> R. 11. 9, 7. 35; निःशब्दोऽपि प्रदिशसि जलं याचितश्चातकेभ्यः Me. 116;<BR> Ms. 8. 265; प्रदिशन् सर्वसत्त्वेष्वभीतिम् Nāg. 5. 24.<BR>—4 To direct, prescribe, ordain.<BR>—5 To signify, declare, make known.<BR>—6 To urge on, incite.<BR>—7 To advise; सायंप्रातश्च विप्राणां प्रदिष्टमभिवादनम् Mb. 12. 193. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Pointing out.<BR>—2 An order, direction, command.<BR>—3 A direction, quarter.<BR>—4 An intermediate point of the compass; such as नैरृती, आग्नेयी, ऐशानी<BR> and वायवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिष्ट
प्रदिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shown, pointed out.<BR>—2 Directed, ordered.<BR>—3 Fixed upon, ordained, appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1091-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशः|प्रदेश
प्रदेशः<BR>—1 Pointing out, indicating.<BR>—2 A place, region, spot, country, territory, district; पितुः प्रदेशास्तव<BR> देवभूमयः Ku. 5. 45; R. 5. 60; so कण्ठ˚, तालु˚, हृदय˚, &c.<BR>—3 A span measured from the tip of the thumb to that of the fore-finger.<BR>—4 Decision, determination.<BR>—5 A wall.<BR>—6 An example (in gram.).<BR>—7 (With Jainas) One of the obstacles to liberation. ━<i>a.</i> Commanding<BR> (ईशनशील); एते प्रदेशाः कथिता भुवनानां प्रभावनाः Mb. 12. 208. 10.<BR> (com. प्रदेशाः प्रदिशन्ति आज्ञापयन्तीति).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रदेशशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशशास्त्रम्
प्रदेशः + -शास्त्रम् a book containing examples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशनम्
प्रदेशनम्<BR>—1 Pointing out.<BR>—2 Advice, instruction.<BR>—3 A gift, present, an offering, especially to gods, superiors &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशनी
प्रदेश(शि)नी<BR>—1 The fore-finger, the index finger; अवमुच्य प्रदेशिन्या दंष्ट्रामादातुमिच्छसि<BR> Mb. 4. 49. 13; Śi. 17. 9.<BR>—2 The corresponding toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशिनी
प्रदेश(शि)नी<BR>—1 The fore-finger, the index finger; अवमुच्य प्रदेशिन्या दंष्ट्रामादातुमिच्छसि<BR> Mb. 4. 49. 13; Śi. 17. 9.<BR>—2 The corresponding toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिह्
प्रदिह् €2 U. To besmear, daub, anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिग्ध|प्रदिग्धं
प्रदिग्ध <i>p. p.</i> Besmeared, bedaubed, anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिग्धम्
प्रदिग्ध + .{@-ग्धम्@} Meat fried in a particular way; (मांसं) … … … तदेव<BR> घृततक्राढ्यं प्रदिग्धं सत्रिजातकम् Śabdachandrikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेहः|प्रदेह
प्रदेहः<BR>—1 Anointing, plastering, unction.<BR>—2 A plaster, thick ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेहनम्
प्रदेहनम् Smearing, anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्
प्रदीप् €4 Ā. To blaze, flame forth, shine brilliantly. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To kindle, inflame.<BR>—2 To excite, rouse, stimulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपः|प्रदीप
प्रदीपः<BR>—1 A lamp, light (fig. also); अतैलपूराः सुरतप्रदीपाः Ku. 1. 10;<BR> R. 2. 24, 16. 4; कुलप्रदीपो नृपतिर्दिलीपः R. 6. 74 ‘light or ornament of the family’<BR>; 7. 29; एते प्रदीपकल्पाः परस्परविलक्षणा गुणविशेषाः Sāṅ. K. 36.<BR>—2 That which enlightens or elucidates, elucidation; especially at the<BR> end of titles of works; as in महाभाष्यप्रदीपः, काव्यप्रदीपः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपक
प्रदीपक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Illuminating.<BR>—2 Explaining, illustrating. {@-कः, -प्रदीपिका@}<BR>—1 A small lamp.<BR>—2 Explanation, commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपन|प्रदीपनः
प्रदीपन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Kindling.<BR>—2 Illuminating.<BR>—3 Stimulating, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपनम्
प्रदीपन + .{@-नम्@} The act of kindling, lighting, stimulating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपनः|प्रदीपन
प्रदीपन + .{@-नः@} A kind of mineral poison; वर्णतो लोहितो यः स्याद्दीप्तिमान्<BR> दहनप्रभः । महादाहकरः पूर्वैः कथितः स प्रदीपनः ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्त
प्रदीप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Kindled, lighted, inflamed, illuminated.<BR>—2 Blazing, burning, shining.<BR>—3 Raised, expanded; प्रदीप्तशिरसमाशीविषम् Dk.<BR>—4 Stimulated, excited (hunger &c.); दीर्घकालं प्रदीप्तास्मि पापानां<BR> पापकर्मणाम् Mb. 3. 12. 119.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रदीप्तप्रज्ञ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्तप्रज्ञ
प्रदीप्त + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> of a bright intellect, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्तिः|प्रदीप्ति
प्रदीप्तिः <i>f.</i> Lustre, splendour, brilliancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुष्
प्रदुष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To grow worse, deteriorate.<BR>—2 To be corrupted or spoiled, be vitiated; तदहर्न प्रदुष्येत पूर्वेषां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">Page1092-2</a>]<BR> जन्मकारणात् Y. 3. 19.<BR>—3 To sin, err, commit an offence against, be faithless or unchaste; अधर्माभिभवात्<BR> कृष्ण प्रदुष्यन्ति कुलस्त्रियः Bg. 1. 41; Ms. 9. 74; यद्यस्य विहितं<BR> भोज्यं न तत्तस्य प्रदुष्यति Pt. 4. 57. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To spoil, corrupt, soil, taint.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To pollute, contaminate, defile.<BR>—2 To blame, censure, find fault with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुष्ट
प्रदुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spoiled, corrupted.<BR>—2 Wicked, bad, sinful.<BR>—3 Licentious, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदूषणम्
प्रदूषणम्<BR>—1 Corrupting, spoiling.<BR>—2 Polluting, defiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदूषित
प्रदूषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Corrupted, vitiated, spoiled, depraved.<BR>—2 Polluted, defiled, contaminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोष|प्रदोषः
प्रदोष <i>a.</i> Bad, corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषः|प्रदोष
प्रदोष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A fault, defect, sin, offence,<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Transgression, violation.<BR>—2 Disordered condition, such as mutiny, rebellion.<BR>—3 Evening, nightfall, the first part of the night; प्रदोषो रजनीमुखम्<BR> Ak.; ‘प्रदोषेऽध्ययनं धीमान्न करोति यथाक्रमम्’ Śabda C.; तमःस्वभावास्तेऽप्यन्ये<BR> प्रदोषमनुयायिनः Śi. 2. 98 (where प्रदोष primarily means ‘corrupt’<BR> or ‘bad’); व्रजसुन्दरीजनमनस्तोषप्रदोषः Gīt. 5; Ku. 5. 44;<BR> R. 1. 93; Ṛs. 1. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रदोषागमः, प्रदोषकालः, प्रदोषसमयः, प्रदोषवेला, प्रदोषतिमिरम्, प्रदोषरमणीय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषागमः|प्रदोषागम
प्रदोष + -आगमः nightfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषकालः|प्रदोषकाल
प्रदोष + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला evening-time, nightfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषसमयः|प्रदोषसमय
प्रदोष + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला evening-time, nightfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषवेला
प्रदोष + -कालः, -समयः, -वेला evening-time, nightfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषतिमिरम्
प्रदोष + -तिमिरम् evening darkness, the dusk of early night; कामं प्रदोषतिमिरेण<BR> न दृश्यसे त्वम् Mk. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषरमणीय
प्रदोष + -रमणीय <i>a.</i> delightful in the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषक|प्रदोषकः
प्रदोषक <i>a.</i> Born in the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषकः|प्रदोषक
प्रदोषक + .{@-कः@} Evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदृश्
प्रदृश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To see, behold.<BR>—2 To look at, regard.<BR>—3 To foresee.<BR>—4 To observe, perceive, discern.<BR>—5 To be intelligent.<BR>—6 To think, have an opinion.<BR>—7 To look at, look upon. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To become visible.<BR>—2 To look, appear. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To show, point out, discover, exhibit.<BR>—2 To make clear, prove, demonstrate, explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शः|प्रदर्श
प्रदर्शः<BR>—1 Look, appearance.<BR>—2 Direction, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शक|प्रदर्शकः
प्रदर्शक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Showing, manifesting, exhibiting.<BR>—2 Foretelling.<BR>—3 Presenting.<BR>—4 Proclaiming.<BR>—5 Teaching, informing, instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शकः|प्रदर्शक
प्रदर्शक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A prophet.<BR>—2 A teacher, instructor.<BR>—3 A doctrine, principle, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शनम्
प्रदर्शनम्<BR>—1 Look, appearance; as in घोरप्रदर्शनः.<BR>—2 Manifesting, displaying, show, exhibition.<BR>—3 Teaching, explaining.<BR>—4 An example.<BR>—5 Prophesying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शना
प्रदर्शनम् + .{@-ना@} Indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शित|प्रदर्शितः
प्रदर्शित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shown forth, exhibited, manifested, evinced, displayed.<BR>—2 Made known.<BR>—3 Taught.<BR>—4 Explained, declared.<BR>—5 Foretold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोहः|प्रदोह
प्रदोहः Milking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युत्
प्रद्युत् €1 Ā. To shine forth. ━<i>Caus.</i> To illumine, irradiate, light up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युतित
प्रद्युतित^1 <i>a.</i> Illuminated, lighted up.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1092-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतः|प्रद्योत
प्रद्योतः<BR>—1 Irradiating, lighting, illuminating.<BR>—2 Splendour, light, lustre.<BR>—3 A ray of light.<BR>—4 N. of a king of Ujjayinī, whose daughter Vatsa married; प्रद्योतस्य<BR> प्रियदुहितरं वत्सराजोऽत्र जह्ने Me. 32. (considered as an interpolation<BR> by Malli.); Ratn. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतनम्
प्रद्योतनम्<BR>—1 Blazing, shining.<BR>—2 Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतनः|प्रद्योतन|प्रद्योतनं
प्रद्योतनम् + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 N. of a prince of Ujjayinī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्नः|प्रद्युम्न
प्रद्युम्नः An epithet of Cupid, the god of love. [He was a son of<BR> Kṛṣṇa and Rukmiṇī. When only six years old, he was stolen away by<BR> the demon Śambara for he was foretold that Pradyumna would be his destroyer.<BR> Śambara cast the child into the roaring sea, and a large fish swallowed<BR> it. This fish was caught by a fisherman and taken to the demon; and when<BR> it was cut up, a beautiful child came out from the belly, and Māyāvatī,<BR> the mistress of Śambaraʼs household, at the desire of Nārada, carefully<BR> reared him from childhood. As he grew up, she was fascinated by the beauty<BR> of his person, but Pradyumna reproved her for entertaining towards himself<BR> feelings so unbecoming a mother as he considered her. But when he was<BR> told that he was not her son, but of Viṣṇu and was cast into the sea<BR> by Śambara, he became enraged, and, challenging him to fight, succeeded<BR> in killing him by the force of illusions. He and Māyāvatī afterwards<BR> repaired to the house of Kṛṣṇa, where Nārada told him and Rukmiṇī<BR> that the boy was their own and that Māyāvatī was his wife.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्नकः|प्रद्युम्नक
प्रद्युम्नकः N. of the god of love; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राणक
प्रद्राणक <i>a.</i> Sorely distressed, hard pressed, indigent, poor;<BR> चाक्रायण इभ्यग्रामे प्रद्राणक उवास Ch. Up. 1. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रु
प्रद्रु €1 P.<BR>—1 To run, run away, retreat or fly to (with acc. or abl.); रणात् प्रद्रवन्ति<BR> बलानि Ve. 4; Bk. 15. 79.<BR>—2 To hasten away, rush towards.<BR>—3 To assail, fall upon, attack.<BR>—4 To attain. ━<i>Caus.</i> To put to flight, rout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रव|प्रद्रवः
प्रद्रव <i>a.</i> Fluid, liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रवः|प्रद्रव
प्रद्रव + .{@-वः@} Running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रावः|प्रद्राव
प्रद्रावः<BR>—1 Running away, flight, retreat, escape.<BR>—2 Going quickly or fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राविन्
प्रद्राविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Running away; fugitive.<BR>—2 Retreating, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रेक्
प्रद्रेक् €1 Ā. To neigh, bellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वार्
प्रद्वार्, प्रद्वारम् A place before a door or gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वारम्
प्रद्वार्, प्रद्वारम् A place before a door or gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष् €2 U. To hate, dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष्, प्रद्विषत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hating, disliking.<BR>—2 Hostile or opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विषत्
प्रद्विष्, प्रद्विषत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hating, disliking.<BR>—2 Hostile or opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेषः|प्रद्वेष
प्रद्वेषः, -प्रद्वेषणम्<BR> Dislike, hatred, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेषणम्
प्रद्वेषः, -प्रद्वेषणम्<BR> Dislike, hatred, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधनम्
प्रधनम्<BR>—1 A battle, fight, war, contest; प्रहितः प्रधनाय माधवानहमाकारयितुं<BR> महीभृता Śi. 16. 52; क्षेत्रं क्षत्रप्रधनपिशुनं कौरवं तद्भजेथाः<BR> Me. 50; R. 11. 77; Mv. 6. 33; U. 5. 1.<BR>—2 Spoil taken in battle.<BR>—3 Destruction.<BR>—4 Tearing, rending.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रधनाङ्गणम्, प्रधनाघातक, प्रधनोत्तमम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधनाङ्गणम्
प्रधनम् + -अङ्गणम् a battle field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधनाघातक
प्रधनम् + -आघातक <i>a.</i> bringing about a contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधनोत्तमम्
प्रधनम् + -उत्तमम् great battle or contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधमनम्
प्रधमनम्<BR>—1 Blowing in or into.<BR>—2 A sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधान|प्रधानं|प्रधानः
प्रधान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Chief, principal, pre-eminent, main, best, most excellent; as in; प्रधानामात्य,<BR> प्रधानपुरुष &c.; रत्नैश्च पूजयेदेनं प्रधानपुरुषैः सह Ms. 7. 203;<BR> प्रधानफलं वा आनुषङ्गैकं वा सर्वमेव आधातरि समवेतुमर्हति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 10; ‘यस्मिन् कुले यः पुरुषः प्रधानः स सर्वयत्नेन हि रक्षणीयः’.<BR>—2 Principally inherent, prevalent, predominant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानम्
प्रधान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The chief thing or object, most important thing; head, chief; न<BR> परिचयो मलिनात्मनां प्रधानम् Śi. 7. 61; G. L. 18; प्रयोगप्रधानं<BR> हि नाट्यशास्त्रम् M. 1; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु Ś. 2. 7; गुणैश्च<BR> तैस्तैर्विनयप्रधानैः R. 6. 79.<BR>—2 The first evolver, originator, or source of the material world, the<BR> primary germ out of which all material appearances are evolved, according<BR> to Sāṅkhya philosophy; न पुनरपि प्रधानवादी अशब्दत्वं प्रधानस्या<BR> सिद्धमित्याह Ś. B.; see प्रकृति also; प्रधानक्षेत्रज्ञपतिर्गुणेशः<BR> Śvet. Up. 6. 16; एतस्याद्या प्रवृत्तिस्तु प्रधानात् संप्रवर्तते Mb. 12. 205. 25.<BR>—3 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>—4 Intellect, understanding; एको मयेह भगवान् विबुधप्रधानैश्चित्तीकृतः<BR> प्रजननाय कथं नु यूयम् Bhāg. 4. 1. 28.<BR>—5 The principal member of a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानः|प्रधान|प्रधानं
प्रधान + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 The principal attendant or companion of a king (his minister or confidant).<BR>—2 A noble, courtier.<BR>—3 An elephant-driver.<BR>—4 The commander-in-chief.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रधानाङ्गम्, प्रधानामात्यः, प्रधानात्मन्, प्रधानोत्तम, प्रधानकर्मन्, प्रधानकारणवादः, प्रधानधातुः, प्रधानपुरुषः, प्रधानभाज्, प्रधानमन्त्रिन्, प्रधानवादिन्, प्रधानवासस्, प्रधानवृष्टिः, प्रधानशिष्ट, प्रधानसभिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानम्
प्रधान + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 The principal attendant or companion of a king (his minister or confidant).<BR>—2 A noble, courtier.<BR>—3 An elephant-driver.<BR>—4 The commander-in-chief.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रधानाङ्गम्, प्रधानामात्यः, प्रधानात्मन्, प्रधानोत्तम, प्रधानकर्मन्, प्रधानकारणवादः, प्रधानधातुः, प्रधानपुरुषः, प्रधानभाज्, प्रधानमन्त्रिन्, प्रधानवादिन्, प्रधानवासस्, प्रधानवृष्टिः, प्रधानशिष्ट, प्रधानसभिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानाङ्गम्
प्रधान + -अङ्गम्<BR>—1 the principal branch or part of anything.<BR>—2 the chief member of the body.<BR>—3 the principal or most eminent person in a state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानामात्यः|प्रधानामात्य
प्रधान + -अमात्यः the prime-minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानात्मन्
प्रधान + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानोत्तम
प्रधान + -उत्तम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 eminent, most illustrious.<BR>—2 warlike, brave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानकर्मन्
प्रधान + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@कार्यम्@}<BR>—1 the chief business, the principal act; यस्यैव प्रधानकर्मफलं<BR> तस्यैवानुषङ्गिकमपि भवितुमर्हति ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 10.<BR>—2 (Medic.) the principal mode of treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानकारणवादः|प्रधानकारणवाद
प्रधान + -कारणवादः the doctrine that प्रधान is the original cause<BR> (according to Sāṅkhyas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानधातुः|प्रधानधातु
प्रधान + -धातुः the chief element of the body; <i>i. e.</i> semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानपुरुषः|प्रधानपुरुष
प्रधान + -पुरुषः<BR>—1 the principal or most eminent person (in a state &c.) Ms. 7. 203; Pt. 3. 138.<BR> ˚अतीतः transcending प्रधान and पुरुष (matter and spirit).<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानभाज्
प्रधान + -भाज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 most distinguished.<BR>—2 receiving the chief share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानमन्त्रिन्|प्रधानमंत्रिन्
प्रधान + -मन्त्रिन् <i>m.</i> the prime-minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानवादिन्
प्रधान + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> one who asserts the Sāṅkhya doctrine (of प्रधान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानवासस्
प्रधान + -वासस् <i>n.</i> a principal garment; (du.) the two chief garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानवृष्टिः|प्रधानवृष्टि
प्रधान + -वृष्टिः <i>f.</i> a heavy shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानशिष्ट
प्रधान + -शिष्ट <i>a.</i> taught or prescribed as of primary importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानसभिकः|प्रधानसभिक
प्रधान + -सभिकः the chief of a gambling house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानक
प्रधानक <i>a.</i> Chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानकम्
प्रधानक + .{@-कम्@} The original germ out of which the material universe is evolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1093-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानता
प्रधानता, -त्वम्<BR> = प्राधान्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानत्वम्
प्रधानता, -त्वम्<BR> = प्राधान्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानेन
प्रधानेन = प्राधान्येन chiefly; न हि शक्यं प्रधानेन श्रेयः<BR> संख्यातुमात्मनः Mb. 12. 287. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधाव्
प्रधाव् €1 U.<BR>—1 To run forward, run away.<BR>—2 To set out, start.<BR>—3 To become spread or diffused.<BR>—4 To wash, cleanse.<BR>—5 To rub off, wipe out.<BR>—6 To pervade, permeate. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to run away, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावनः|प्रधावन
प्रधावनः<BR>—1 Air, wind.<BR>—2 A runner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावनम्
प्रधावनः + .{@-नम्@} Rubbing, rubbing or washing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावितिका
प्रधावितिका A passage for flight; अग्राह्ये देशे प्रधावितिकां निष्कुरद्वारं<BR> च Kau. A. 2. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधिः|प्रधि
प्रधिः<BR>—1 The periphery of a wheel; चके प्रधिरिवासक्तः Mb. 5. 51. 58; Śi. 15. 79;<BR> मुहुर्युधि क्षतसुरशत्रुशोणितप्लुतप्रधिं रथमधिरोहति स्म<BR> सः Śi. 17. 27.<BR>—2 A well.<BR>—3 Orb, disc.<BR>—4 A segment. ˚अनीकम् centre of a segment; a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधी
प्रधी <i>a.</i> Pre-eminently intelligent. ━<i>f.</i> Great intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूपित
प्रधूपित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fumigated, perfumed.<BR>—2 Heated, burned.<BR>—3 Inflamed.<BR>—4 Afflicted, distressed; व्यसनप्रधूपिताम् Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूपिता
प्रधूपित + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 A woman in trouble.<BR>—2 The quarter to which the sun proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूमित
प्रधूमित <i>a.</i> Smothered with smoke, smouldering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृ
प्रधृ €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To place or fix upon.<BR>—2 To direct the mind towards, determine, resolve.<BR>—3 To bear or keep in mind.<BR>—4 To think, consider, reflect.<BR>—5 To chastise, punish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधारण
प्रधारण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Preserving, keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधारणा
प्रधारण + .{@-णा@} Constantly fixing oneʼs mind on a certain object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्
प्रधृष् €5 P.<BR>—1 To assail, lay hands on.<BR>—2 To injure, harass.<BR>—3 To overpower, overcome. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To assail, attack, overpower.<BR>—2 To outrage, violate (a woman).<BR>—3 To injure, hurt.<BR>—4 To devastate, lay waste, destroy completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षः|प्रधर्ष
प्रधर्षः<BR>—1 Assaulting, attacking; an attack, assault.<BR>—2 Violation, outrage.<BR>—3 Ill-treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षक
प्रधर्षक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attacking, assailing.<BR>—2 Troubling, harassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षणम्
प्रधर्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 An assault, attack.<BR>—2 An outrage, ill-treatment, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षणा
प्रधर्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 An assault, attack.<BR>—2 An outrage, ill-treatment, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षित
प्रधर्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Assaulted, attacked.<BR>—2 Hurt, injured.<BR>—3 Haughty, arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्ट
प्रधृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Treated with contumely.<BR>—2 Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मा
प्रध्मा €1 P.<BR>—1 To blow (as a conch); शङ्खौ प्रदध्मतुः Bg. 1. 14.<BR>—2 To blow away or into.<BR>—3 To destroy.<BR>—4 (Ā.) To cry out; प्रध्मायीताभिनद्धाक्ष आनीतोऽभिनद्धाक्षो विसृष्टः<BR> Ch. Up. 6. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मापनम्
प्रध्मापनम् A remedy for assisting respiration in any obstruction<BR> of the air-passages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्यै
प्रध्यै €1 P., Ā.<BR>—1 To meditate upon, think, reflect, consider<BR>—2 To devise, hit upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्यानम्
प्रध्यानम्<BR>—1 Deep thought or reflection.<BR>—2 Reflection or thought in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंस्
प्रध्वंस् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To fall in ruins, waste, decay.<BR>—2 To perish, be destroyed. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to perish, destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसः|प्रध्वंस
प्रध्वंसः Utter destruction, annihilation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रध्वंसाभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसाभावः|प्रध्वंसाभाव
प्रध्वंसः + -अभावः ‘non-existence caused by destruction’, one of the four<BR> kinds of अभाव or non-existence, in which the non-existence of a thing<BR> is caused by destruction, as of an effect subsequently to its production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसनः|प्रध्वंसन
प्रध्वंसनः Ved. A destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसिन्
प्रध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Transitory, perishable.<BR>—2 Destroying, annihilating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वस्त
प्रध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i> Annihilated, completely destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनप्तृ
प्रनप्तृ <i>m.</i> The son of a grandson, a great-grand-son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्ट|प्रनष्टः
प्रनष्ट See under प्रणश्; प्रनष्टस्वामिकं रिक्थं राजा त्र्यब्दं<BR> निधापयेत् Ms. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनायक
प्रनायक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One whose leader is away.<BR>—2 Destitute of a leader or guide; P. I. 4. 59, VIII. 4. 14 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनालः|प्रनाल
प्रनालः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> See प्रणाल and प्रणाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनाली
प्रनालः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> See प्रणाल and प्रणाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिघातनम्
प्रनिघातनम् Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्
प्रनृत् €4 P. To dance. ━<i>Caus.</i> To shake, cause to dance, set in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनर्तित|प्रनर्त्तित
प्रनर्तित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set in motion, shaken.<BR>—2 Dandled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्त
प्रनृत्त <i>a.</i> Dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्तम्
प्रनृत्त + .{@-त्तम्@} A dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपक्षः|प्रपक्ष
प्रपक्षः The extremity of a wing (as of an army); प्रपक्षः शकुनिस्तेषां<BR> प्रवरैर्हयसादिभिः (ययौ) Mb. 7. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चः|प्रपञ्च|प्रपंच|प्रपंचः
प्रपञ्चः<BR>—1 Display, manifestation; रागप्रायः प्रपञ्चः K. 151.<BR>—2 Development, expansion, extension; भरतज्ञकविप्रणीतकाव्यग्रथिताङ्का<BR> इव नाटकप्रपञ्चाः Śi. 20. 44.<BR>—3 Amplification, expatiation, explanation, elucidation.<BR>—4 Prolixity, diffuseness, copiousness; अलं प्रपञ्चेन.<BR>—5 Manifoldness, diversity.<BR>—6 Heap, abundance, quantity.<BR>—7 An appearance, phenomenon.<BR>—8 Illusion, fraud.<BR>—9 The visible world or universe, which is illusory and the scene of manifold action.<BR>—10 Reciprocal false praise.<BR>—11 Opposition, inversion.<BR>—12 Analysis.<BR>—13 (In dram.) Ludicrous dialogue.<BR>—14 (In gram.) The repetition of an obscure rule in a clearer form.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रपञ्चचतुर, प्रपञ्चबुद्धि, प्रपञ्चवचनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चचतुर
प्रपञ्चः + -चतुर <i>a.</i> skilful in assuming different forms; Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चबुद्धि|प्रपंचबुद्धि
प्रपञ्चः + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> cunning, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चवचनम्
प्रपञ्चः + -वचनम् a prolix discourse, diffuse talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1094-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चक|प्रपंचक
प्रपञ्चक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Displaying, showing.<BR>—2 Developing.<BR>—3 Explaining fully, amplifying, expounding in detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चनम्
प्रपञ्चनम्<BR>—1 Display, development; अरिमध्यस्थमित्राणां सम्यक् चोक्तं प्रपञ्चनम्<BR> Mb. 12. 59. 52.<BR>—2 Copious exposition, detailed explanation or amplification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चयति
प्रपञ्चयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To show forth, display; प्रपञ्चय पञ्चमम् Gīt. 10.<BR>—2 To expand, amplify, explain in detail, dwell or dilate upon, treat at length.<BR>—3 To cause to appear in a false light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चित|प्रपंचित|प्रपञ्चितं
प्रपञ्चित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Displayed.<BR>—2 Expanded, amplified.<BR>—3 Dilated upon, fully explained, expatiated upon.<BR>—4 Erring, mistaken.<BR>—5 Deceived, tricked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपठ्
प्रपठ् €1 P. To repeat aloud. ━<i>Caus.</i> To teach, explain, expound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाठकः|प्रपाठक
प्रपाठकः<BR>—1 A lesson, lecture.<BR>—2 A chapter or subdivision of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाठित
प्रपाठित <i>p. p.</i> Taught, expounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपणः|प्रपण
प्रपणः Ved. Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपत्
प्रपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly forth or away,<BR>—2 To fly, fly or move about.<BR>—3 To fall down or upon, throw oneself down.<BR>—4 To hasten towards.<BR>—5 To be deprived of, fall from, lose, fall off or away from.<BR>—6 To come down, fall down, descend. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To throw down.<BR>—2 To rout, put to flight.<BR>—3 To chase, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतनम्
प्रपतनम्<BR>—1 Flying forth or away.<BR>—2 Throwing oneself into, falling down.<BR>—3 Alighting.<BR>—4 Death, destruction.<BR>—5 A precipice, a steep crag.<BR>—6 Assault; लीयन्ते यत्र शत्रुप्रपतनविवशाः कोटिशः शूरकीटाः Mv. 6. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतित
प्रपतित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Flown away.<BR>—2 Fallen, come down.<BR>—3 Decayed, wasted.<BR>—4 Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातः|प्रपात
प्रपातः<BR>—1 Going forth or away, departure.<BR>—2 Falling down or into, a fall; मनोरथानामतटप्रप्रातः Ś. 6. 10; Ku. 6. 57.<BR>—3 A sudden attack.<BR>—4 A cascade, waterfall, the place over which water falls down; गङ्गाप्रपातान्तनिरूढशष्पं<BR> गौरीगुरोर्गह्वरमाविवेश R. 2. 26.<BR>—5 A bank, shore.<BR>—6 A precipice, steep rock; प्राप्ताः प्रपातनिकटं सङ्कटेन महीयसा<BR> Parṇāl. 3. 30.<BR>—7 Falling out or loss, as in केशप्रपात.<BR>—8 Emission, discharge, efflux, as in वीर्यप्रपात.<BR>—9 Throwing oneself down from a rock.<BR>—10 A particular mode of flight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रपाताम्बु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाताम्बु
प्रपातः + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> water falling from a rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातनम्
प्रपातनम् Causing to fall, throwing down (on the ground).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातिन्
प्रपातिन् <i>m.</i> A precipitous mountain, cliff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ|प्रपथः
प्रपथ <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Loose, relaxed. —2 Languid, enervated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथः|प्रपथ
प्रपथ + .{@-थः@} A long journey, a journey to a distant place.<BR>—2 A remote place.<BR>—3 A broad street; जुष्टां विभक्तप्रपथाम् Bhāg. 8. 15. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ्य
प्रपथ्य <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Being in or on the road.<BR>—2 An epithet of Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ्या
प्रपथ्या Yellow myrobalan (Mar. हिरडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपद्
प्रपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To enter upon, set forward, set foot in.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go to or towards, approach, resort or attain to, reach; तां<BR> जन्मने शैलवधूं प्रपेदे Ku. 1. 21; (क्षितीशं) कौत्सः प्रपेदे<BR> वरतन्तुशिष्यः R. 5. 1; Bk. 4. 1; Ki. 1. 9, 11. 16; R. 8. 11.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To take shelter or refuge with, flee to for safety, submit; शरणार्थमन्यां<BR> कथं प्रपत्स्ये त्वयि दीप्यमाने R. 14. 64.<BR>—3 To go or come to a particular state, arrive at, attain to, arrive at<BR> or be in a particular condition; रेणुः प्रपेदे पथि पङ्कभावम् R. 16. 30;<BR> मुहूर्तकर्णोत्पलतां प्रपेदे Ku. 7. 81; बाल्यात्परं साथ<BR> वयः प्रपेदे Ku. 1. 31, 5. 24; ईदृशीमवस्थां प्रपन्नोस्मि Ś. 5;<BR> ऋषिनिकरैरिति संशयः प्रपेदे Bv. 4. 33; Amaru. 30.<BR>—4 To get, find, secure, obtain, attain to; partake of, share in; सहकार<BR> न प्रपेदे मधुपेन भवत्समं जगति Bv. 1. 21; कान्तं वपुर्व्योमचरम्<BR> प्रपेदे R. 5. 51.<BR>—5 To behave or act towards, deal with; किं प्रपद्यते वैदर्भः M. 1<BR> ‘what does he propose to do’; पश्यामो मयि किं प्रपद्यते Amaru. 24.<BR>—6 To admit, allow, agree or consent to; प्रपन्नं साधयन्नर्थम् Y. 2. 40.<BR>—7 To draw near, come on, approach (as time &c.).<BR>—8 To be going on, to proceed.<BR>—9 To take effect, thrive, prosper.<BR>—10 To throw oneself down, fall down (at anotherʼs feet).<BR>—11 Ved. To attack, assault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदम्
प्रपदम्<BR>—1 The forepart of the foot; स तं गृहीत्वा प्रपदोर्भ्रामयित्वैकपाणिना<BR> Bhāg. 10. 15. 32.<BR>—2 Tip of the toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदनम्
प्रपदनम्<BR>—1 Entrance.<BR>—2 Access, approach; लोकद्वारं विदुषां प्रपदनं निरोधोऽविदुषाम्<BR> Ch. Up. 8. 6. 5.<BR>—3 Approaching for protection; प्रपदनधनतुष्टाः पञ्चसंस्कारदानात्<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदीन
प्रपदीन <i>a.</i> Relating or extending to the forepart of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्न|प्रपन्नः
प्रपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Arriving at, reaching or going to.<BR>—2 Resorting to, betaking oneself to; इयं प्रपन्ना तपसे तपोवनम्<BR> Ku. 5. 59, 3. 5.<BR>—3 Taking refuge with, seeking protection with, suppliant or submissive<BR> to; शिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम् Bg. 2. 7; पुनर्भवक्लेशभयात्<BR> प्रपन्नः Ku; प्रपन्नार्तिहरे! देवि! Caṇḍīpāṭha.<BR>—4 Adhering to.<BR>—5 Furnished or endowed with, possessed of; प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—6 Promised.<BR>—7 Got, obtained.<BR>—8 Poor, distressed.<BR>—9 Effecting, producing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रपन्नपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्नपालः|प्रपन्नपाल
प्रपन्न + -पालः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादः|प्रपाद
प्रपादः Ved. Miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्नाडः|प्रपन्नाड
प्रपन्नाडः See प्रपुनाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपर्ण
प्रपर्ण <i>a.</i> Devoid of leaves (as a tree; प्रपतितानि पर्णानि यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपर्णम्
प्रपर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} A fallen leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायनम्
प्रपलायनम् Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायित
प्रपलायित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Run away.<BR>—2 Routed, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1095-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायिन्
प्रपलायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Flying, escaping.<BR>—2 A fugitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपा
प्रपा<BR>—1 A place where water is distributed to travellers; भूतानामिह संवासः<BR> प्रपायामिव सुव्रते Bhāg. 7. 2. 21; व्याख्यास्थानान्यमलसलिला यस्य<BR> कूपाः प्रपाश्च Vikr. 18. 78.<BR>—2 A well, cistern; यस्तु रज्जुं घटं कूपाद्धरेद्भिद्याच्च यः प्रपाम् Ms. 8. 319.<BR>—3 A place for watering cattle.<BR>—4 A supply of water.<BR>—5 A draught.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रपापालिका, प्रपावनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपापालिका
प्रपा + -पालिका a woman who distributes water to travellers; भूपेषु<BR> कूपेष्विव रिक्तभावं कृत्वा प्रपापालिकयैव यस्य Vikr. 1. 89, 13. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपावनम्
प्रपा + -वनम् a cool grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाकः|प्रपाक
प्रपाकः<BR>—1 Ripening (of a boil &c.).<BR>—2 Inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणिः|प्रपाणि
प्रपाणिः<BR>—1 The forepart of the hand.<BR>—2 The palm of the extended hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाण्डु
प्रपाण्डु <i>a.</i> Very white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाथः|प्रपाथ
प्रपाथः A road, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादिकः|प्रपादिक
प्रपादिकः A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपानम्
प्रपानम्<BR>—1 Drinking.<BR>—2 The underpart of a horseʼs upper lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपानकम्
प्रपानकम् A kind of drink; प्रपानकरसन्यायाच्चर्व्यमाणो रसो भवेत् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपालनम्
प्रपालनम् Protecting, guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपालिन्
प्रपालिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामहः|प्रपितामह
प्रपितामहः<BR>—1 A paternal great-grandfather.<BR>—2 An epithet of Kṛṣṇa; प्रजापतिस्त्वं प्रपितामहश्च Bg. 11. 39.<BR>—3 Of Brahman.<BR>—4 Of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामही
प्रपितामहः + .{@-ही@} A paternal great-grandmother; पितामही च स्वेनैव स्वेनैव<BR> प्रपितामही Dāy. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितृव्यः|प्रपितृव्य
प्रपितृव्यः A paternal grand-uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीड्
प्रपीड् €10 U.<BR>—1 To press, squeeze.<BR>—2 To torture, torment, harass, afflict.<BR>—3 To check, suppress, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीडनम्
प्रपीडनम्<BR>—1 Pressing, squeezing.<BR>—2 An astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीत
प्रपीत (-न) <i>a.</i><BR> Swollen up, distended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीन
प्रपीत (-न) <i>a.</i><BR> Swollen up, distended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुत्रः|प्रपुत्र
प्रपुत्रः A grandson, descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाटः|प्रपुनाट
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः, -डः N. of a tree (चकमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाटः|प्रपुन्नाट
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः, -डः N. of a tree (चकमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाडः|प्रपुनाड
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः, -डः N. of a tree (चकमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुराण
प्रपुराण <i>a.</i> Very old, kept for a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूर्वगः|प्रपूर्वग
प्रपूर्वगः<BR>—1 The Supreme Being.<BR>—2 N. of the two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुष्पित
प्रपुष्पित <i>a.</i> Flowering, blooming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपृष्ठ
प्रपृष्ठ <i>a.</i> Having a prominent back; P. VI. 2. 177 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपॄ
प्रपॄ €9 P. To fill up, complete. ━<i>Pass.</i> To be filled or completed; be fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरक
प्रपूरक <i>a.</i> Fulfilling, satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरणम्
प्रपूरणम्<BR>—1 Filling, filling up, completing.<BR>—2 Inserting, injecting.<BR>—3 Satisfying; satiating.<BR>—4 Attaching to, affixing.<BR>—5 Bending (of a bow); क्व गतिर्मानुषाणां च धनुषोऽस्य प्रपूरणे<BR> Rām. 1. 67. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरित
प्रपूरित <i>p. p.</i> Filled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौण्डरीकः|प्रपौण्डरीक|प्रपौण्डरीकं
प्रपौण्डरीकः A kind of shrub (पौण्डर्य); प्रपौण्डरीकमधुकपिप्पलीचन्दनोत्पलैः … …<BR> Cakrapāṇidatta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्रः|प्रपौत्र
प्रपौत्रः A great-grandson; लोकानन्त्यं दिवः प्राप्तिः पुत्रपौत्रप्रपौत्रकैः Y. 1. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्री
प्रपौत्रः + .{@-त्री@} A great-grand-daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रप्यायनम्
प्रप्यायनम् Swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफर्वी
प्रफर्वी Ved. A woman having excellent hips or going in a graceful<BR> way; a lewd girl (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्त
प्रफुल्त <i>p. p.</i> Blooming, blossomed, full-blown; लोध्रद्रुमं<BR> सानुमतः प्रफुल्तम् R. 2. 29 (v. l. for प्रफुल्ल). cf. P. VII. 4. 89 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्तिः|प्रफुल्ति
प्रफुल्तिः <i>f.</i> Blooming, expansion, blossoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्ल|प्रफुल्लः
प्रफुल्ल <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Full-blown, blossoming, blooming; न हि प्रफुल्लं सहकारमेत्य वृक्षान्तरं<BR> काङ्क्षति षट्पदाली R. 6. 69, 2. 29; Ku. 3. 45, 7. 11.<BR>—2 Expanded or dilated like a full-blown flower (as eyes).<BR>—3 Smiling.<BR>—4 Shining.<BR>—5 Gay, cheerful, pleased.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रफुल्लनयन, प्रफुल्लनेत्र, प्रफुल्ललोचन, प्रफुल्लवदन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लनयन
प्रफुल्ल + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> with eyes expanded with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लनेत्र
प्रफुल्ल + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> with eyes expanded with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्ललोचन
प्रफुल्ल + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> with eyes expanded with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लवदन
प्रफुल्ल + -वदन <i>a.</i> having a beaming or cheerful countenance, looking cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्ध्|प्रबंध्
प्रबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind on, tie, fasten.<BR>—2 To stop, suppress, check.<BR>—3 To compose, put together, arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबद्ध
प्रबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied, fastened.<BR>—2 Stopped, obstructed, checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्द्धृ|प्रबंद्धृ
प्रबन्द्धृ <i>m.</i> An author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धः|प्रबन्ध|प्रबंध|प्रबंधः
प्रबन्धः<BR>—1 A bond, tie.<BR>—2 Uninterruptedness, continuance, continuity, uninterrupted series or<BR> succession; विच्छेदमाप भुवि यस्तु कथाप्रबन्धः K. 239; क्रियाप्रबन्धादयमध्वराणाम्<BR> R. 6. 23, 3. 58; Māl. 6. 3.<BR>—3 A continued or connected narrative or discourse; अनुज्झितार्थसंबन्धः<BR> प्रबन्धो दुरुदाहरः Śi. 2. 73.<BR>—4 Any literary work or composition; प्रथितयशसां भासकविसौमिल्लकविमिश्रादीनां<BR> प्रबन्धानतिक्रम्य M. 1; प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबन्ध &c. Vās.<BR>—6 Arrangement, plan, scheme; as in कपटप्रबन्धः<BR>—6 A commentary.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रबन्धार्थः, प्रबन्धकल्पना, प्रबन्धवर्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धार्थः|प्रबन्धार्थ
प्रबन्धः + -अर्थः the subject-matter of a composition or treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धकल्पना|प्रबंधकल्पना
प्रबन्धः + -कल्पना a feigned story, a work of imagination founded on a substratum<BR> of fact; प्रबन्धकल्पनां स्तोकसत्यां प्राज्ञाः कथां विदुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धवर्षः|प्रबन्धवर्ष
प्रबन्धः + -वर्षः continuous or incessant rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धनम्
प्रबन्धनम्<BR>—1 Bond, tie.<BR>—2 Binding, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबभ्रः|प्रबभ्र
प्रबभ्रः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबर्ह
प्रब(व)र्ह <i>a.</i> Most excellent, best; धृष्टद्युम्नः सोमकानां<BR> प्रबर्हः Mb. 1. 193. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ह|प्रवर्हः
प्रब(व)र्ह <i>a.</i> Most excellent, best; धृष्टद्युम्नः सोमकानां<BR> प्रबर्हः Mb. 1. 193. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबल|प्रबलः
प्रबल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very stong or powerful, mighty, valorous (as a man); प्रणाशनाय<BR> प्रबलस्य विद्विषः R. 3. 60; Ṛs. 3. 23.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">Page1097-1</a>]<BR>—2 Violent, strong, intense, excessive, very great; प्रबलतमसामेवंप्रायाः<BR> शुभेषु हि वृत्तयः Ś. 7. 24; प्रबलपुरोवातया वृष्टपा M. 4. 2;<BR> प्रबलां वेदनाम् R. 8. 50; अबला यत्र प्रबला, बालो राजा, निरक्षरो<BR> मन्त्री Udb.; Śivamahimna 30.<BR>—3 Important.<BR>—4 Abounding with.<BR>—5 Dangerous, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलः|प्रबल
प्रबल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 N. of a Daitya.<BR>—2 A sprout (पल्लव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलम्
प्रबल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Exceedingly, much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1096-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलता
प्रबलता, -त्वम्<BR> Strength, power, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलत्वम्
प्रबलता, -त्वम्<BR> Strength, power, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलति
प्रबलति Den. P. To become strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबली
प्रबली A class, division of a community (?); Inscrip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाध्
प्रबाध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To press hard upon, oppress.<BR>—2 To trouble, torment, harass, tease, hurt; समुच्छ्रितानेव तरून प्रबाधते<BR> (प्रभञ्जनः) H. 1; Bk. 12. 2.<BR>—3 To drive away, remove, get over; छायां ते दिनकरभाः प्रबाधमानं<BR> वर्षत्रं भरत करोतु मूर्ध्नि शीताम् Rām. 2. 107. 18; कथं च दैवं<BR> शक्येत पौरुषेण प्रबाधितुम् Mb.<BR>—4 To throw down, destroy; समुच्छ्रितानेव तरून् प्रबाधते Pt. 1. 122.<BR>—5 To repel, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधक
प्रबाधक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Repelling, repulsive.<BR>—2 Harassing, oppressive.<BR>—3 Keeping off or back.<BR>—4 Refusing, rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधनम्
प्रबाधनम्<BR>—1 Oppressing, tormenting.<BR>—2 Refusing, denying.<BR>—3 Keeping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधित
प्रबाधित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Molested, troubled, oppressed.<BR>—2 Pressed forward, driven onward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबह्लिका
प्रब(व)ह्लिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिका
प्रब(व)ह्लिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालः|प्रबाल|प्रबालं
प्रबा(वा)लः, -लम्<BR>—1 A sprout, shoot, new leaf; अपि … … प्रवालमासामनुबन्धि वीरुधाम्<BR> Ku. 5. 34, 1. 44, 3. 8; R. 6. 12, 13. 49.<BR>—2 Coral; शुद्धं दृढं घनं वृत्तं स्निग्धं पात्रसुरङ्गकम् । समं<BR> गुरु सिराहीनं प्रबालं धारयेच्छुभम् ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR>—3 The neck of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवालः|प्रवाल|प्रवालं
प्रबा(वा)लः, -लम्<BR>—1 A sprout, shoot, new leaf; अपि … … प्रवालमासामनुबन्धि वीरुधाम्<BR> Ku. 5. 34, 1. 44, 3. 8; R. 6. 12, 13. 49.<BR>—2 Coral; शुद्धं दृढं घनं वृत्तं स्निग्धं पात्रसुरङ्गकम् । समं<BR> गुरु सिराहीनं प्रबालं धारयेच्छुभम् ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR>—3 The neck of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालम्
प्रबा(वा)लः, -लम्<BR>—1 A sprout, shoot, new leaf; अपि … … प्रवालमासामनुबन्धि वीरुधाम्<BR> Ku. 5. 34, 1. 44, 3. 8; R. 6. 12, 13. 49.<BR>—2 Coral; शुद्धं दृढं घनं वृत्तं स्निग्धं पात्रसुरङ्गकम् । समं<BR> गुरु सिराहीनं प्रबालं धारयेच्छुभम् ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR>—3 The neck of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालः|प्रबाल|प्रबालं
प्रबा(वा)लः, -लम् + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A pupil.<BR>—2 An animal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रबालाश्मन्तकः, प्रबालपद्मम्, प्रबालफलम्, प्रबालभस्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालाश्मन्तकः|प्रबालाश्मन्तक|प्रबालाश्मंतक
प्रबालः + -अश्मन्तकः<BR>—1 the red Aśmantaka tree.<BR>—2 the coral tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालपद्मम्
प्रबालः + -पद्मम् a red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालफलम्
प्रबालः + -फलम् red sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालभस्मन्
प्रबालः + -भस्मन् <i>n.</i> calx of coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुः|प्रबाहु
प्रबाहुः The fore-arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुक्
प्रबाहुक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In an even line, to an equal height.<BR>—2 At the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुकम्
प्रबाहुकम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 On high.<BR>—2 At the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुध्
प्रबुध् €4 Ā., €1 P.<BR>—1 To awake, wake up, rise from sleep; प्रबुद्ध इव सुप्तम् Ś. 5. 11; Śi. 9. 30.<BR>—2 To blow, expand, bloom, be blown; साभ्रेऽह्नीव स्थलकमलिनीं नप्रबुद्धां<BR> नसुप्ताम् Me. 94.<BR>—3 To perceive, observe, be aware of. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To awaken, waken, rouse; प्राबोधयन्नुषसि वाग्भिरुदारवाचः R. 5. 65, 6. 56.<BR>—2 To acquaint with, inform, make known; तमभ्यनन्दत् प्रथमं प्रबोधितः R. 3. 68.<BR>—3 To cause to expand or open; (पद्मानि) प्रबोधवत्यूर्ध्वमुखैर्मयूखैः Ku. 1. 16.<BR>—4 To instruct, teach; explain.<BR>—5 To persuade, induce.<BR>—6 To stimulate, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुद्ध|प्रबुद्धः
प्रबुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Awakened, roused; तथा लिखितवान् प्रातः प्रबुद्धो बुधकौशिकः Rāmarakṣā 15.<BR>—2 Wise, learned, clever; Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Knowing, conversant with.<BR>—4 Full-blown, expanded; पुष्पैः समं निपातिता रजनीप्रबुद्धैः Ve. 2. 7.<BR>—5 Beginning to work or take effect (as a charm).<BR>—6 Enlivened, lively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुद्धता
प्रबुद्धता Intelligence, wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुधः|प्रबुध
प्रबुधः A great sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधः|प्रबोध
प्रबोधः<BR>—1 Awaking (fig. also), awakening; regaining oneʼs consciousness, consciousness;<BR> अप्रबोधाय सुष्वाप R. 12. 50; मोहादभूत् कष्टतरः प्रबोधः 14. 56.<BR>—2 Blowing, expanding (of flowers)<BR>—3 Wakefulness, sleeplessness; चिरप्रबोधान्न संभावितं धर्मासनमध्यासितुम् Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Vigilance, watchfulness.<BR>—5 Knowledge, understanding, wisdom, removal of delusion, real knowledge;<BR> as in प्रबोधचन्द्रोदय; सूतात्मजाः सवयसः प्रथितप्रबोधम् R. 5. 65.<BR>—6 Consolation.<BR>—7 Reviving the fragrance of a perfume.<BR>—8 Explaining.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रबोधोत्सवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधोत्सवः|प्रबोधोत्सव
प्रबोधः + -उत्सवः N. of a festival observed from the tenth to the day of<BR> full-moon in the month of Kārtika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधकः|प्रबोधक
प्रबोधकः A minstrel whose duty it is to wake the king, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधन|प्रबोधनं
प्रबोधन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Awakening, rousing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधनम्
प्रबोधन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Waking.<BR>—2 Awakening, rousing.<BR>—3 Regaining oneʼs consciousness; recovery of senses; प्रथमप्रमूढजनकप्रबोधनात् U. 6. 41.<BR>—4 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>—5 Instructing, advising.<BR>—6 Reviving the scent of a perfume.<BR>—7 Refinement, enlightenment; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधनी
प्रबोध(धि)नी The eleventh day of the bright half of Kārtika on<BR> which Viṣṇu awakes from his four monthsʼ sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधिनी
प्रबोध(धि)नी The eleventh day of the bright half of Kārtika on<BR> which Viṣṇu awakes from his four monthsʼ sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधित
प्रबोधित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Awakened, roused.<BR>—2 Instructed, informed, taught, acquainted with.<BR>—3 Convinced, persuaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रब्रू
प्रब्रू €2 P.<BR>—1 To proclaim, announce.<BR>—2 To exclaim, shout.<BR>—3 To say, speak, tell; पापाऽनुवासितं सीता रावणं प्राब्रवीद् वचः<BR> Bk. 8. 85; Pt. 1. 53.<BR>—4 To praise, laud.<BR>—5 To read before.<BR>—6 To describe.<BR>—7 To teach; प्रब्रूयाद् ब्राह्मणस्त्वेषाम् Ms. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्ज्|प्रभंज्
प्रभञ्ज् €7 P.<BR>—1 To break down, shatter.<BR>—2 To stop, arrest, suspend.<BR>—3 To frustrate, disappoint.<BR>—4 To defeat, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभग्न
प्रभग्न <i>p. p.</i> Crushed to pieces, defeated; ययौ लङ्काभिमुखं<BR> प्रभग्नं राक्षसं बलम् Rām. 7. 7. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभङ्गः|प्रभङ्ग|प्रभंगः
प्रभङ्गः<BR>—1 Breaking, crushing.<BR>—2 Destruction; complete defeat.<BR>—3 A breaker, crusher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्जनम्
प्रभञ्जनम् Breaking to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्जनः|प्रभञ्जन|प्रभंजन|प्रभंजनं
प्रभञ्जनम् + .{@-नः@} Wind, especially stormy wind, hurricane; प्रभञ्जनाध्येयजवेन<BR> वाजिना N. 1. 67;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">Page1098-1</a>]<BR> तृणानि नोन्मूलयति प्रभञ्जनः Pt. 1. 22. ━<i>a.</i> Destroying; … पुत्रं<BR> देहि सुरोत्तम । बलवन्तं महाकायं सर्वदर्पप्रभञ्जनम् Mb. 1. 123. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1097-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभद्रः|प्रभद्र
प्रभद्रः The Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभद्रक
प्रभद्रक <i>a.</i> Exceedingly handsome or beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभद्रकम्
प्रभद्रक + .{@-कम्@} A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा €2 P.<BR>—1 To appear, seem.<BR>—2 To shine forth, gleam.<BR>—3 To begin to become light, begin to dawn; ननु प्रभाता रजनी Ś. 4; प्रभातकल्पा शशिनेव शर्वरी R. 3. 2.<BR>—4 To illuminate, enlighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा<BR>—1 Light, splendour, lustre, effulgence, radiance; प्रभास्मि शशिसूर्ययोः<BR> Bg. 7. 8; प्रभा पतङ्गस्य R. 2. 15, 31, 6. 18; Ṛs. 1. 20; Me. 49;<BR> दृष्टस्त्वं प्रभया गोप्या युक्तो वृन्दावने वने Brahmavaivasvata P.<BR>—2 A ray of light.<BR>—3 The shadow of the sun on a sun-dial.<BR>—4 An epithet of Durgā; प्रभा प्रभानशीलत्वात् Devī. P.<BR>—5 N. of the city of Kubera.<BR>—6 N. of an Apsaras.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभाकरः, प्रभाकीटः, प्रभातरल, प्रभापल्लवित, प्रभाप्रभुः, प्रभाप्ररोहः, प्रभाभिद्, प्रभामण्डलम्, प्रभालेपिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकरः|प्रभाकर
प्रभा + -करः<BR>—1 the sun; प्रसन्नत्वात् प्रभाकरः R. 10. 74.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 the ocean.<BR>—5 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—6 N. of a learned writer, the founder of a school of Mīmāṃsā philosophy<BR> called after him.<BR>—7 A gem (पद्मराग); Rām. 2. 114. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकीटः|प्रभाकीट
प्रभा + -कीटः a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातरल
प्रभा + -तरल <i>a.</i> tremulously radiant; न प्रभातरलं ज्योतिरुदेति<BR> वसुधातलात् Ś. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभापल्लवित
प्रभा + -पल्लवित <i>a.</i> overspread or glowing with lustre; प्रभापल्लवितेनासौ<BR> करोति मणिना खगः (अवतंसकम्); V. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाप्रभुः
प्रभा + -प्रभुः the sun; दृष्टदृग्भिर्दुरालोकं प्रभयेव प्रभाप्रभुम्<BR> (व्यलोकत) N. 17. 205.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाप्ररोहः|प्रभाप्ररोह
प्रभा + -प्ररोहः a ray or flash of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाभिद्
प्रभा + -भिद् <i>a.</i> brilliant, shining; शक्रधनुः प्रभाभिदः Ki. 16. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभामण्डलम्
प्रभा + -मण्डलम् a circle or halo of light; स्फुरत्प्रभामण्डलया चकाशे<BR> Ku. 1. 24, 6. 4; R. 3. 60, 14. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभालेपिन्
प्रभा + -लेपिन् <i>a.</i> covered with lustre, emitting lustre; प्रभालेपी<BR> नायं हरिहतमृगस्यामिषलवः V. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभात|प्रभातं
प्रभात <i>p. p.</i> Begun to become clear or light; प्रभातायां रजन्यां<BR> वै इदं युद्धं भविष्यति Mb. 5. 168. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातम्
प्रभात + .{@-तम्@} Day-break, dawn; अक्ष्णोः प्रभातमासीत् Ś. 2; प्रभाते<BR> स्नातीनां नृपतिरमणीनां कुचतटे G. L.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभातकरणीयम्, प्रभातकल्प, प्रभातप्राय, प्रभातकालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातकरणीयम्
प्रभात + -करणीयम् a morning rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातकल्प
प्रभात + -कल्प, -प्राय approaching dawn (as night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातप्राय
प्रभात + -कल्प, -प्राय approaching dawn (as night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातकालः|प्रभातकाल
प्रभात + -कालः the time of day break; वैद्यः पुरोहितो मन्त्री दैवज्ञोऽथ<BR> चतुर्थकः । प्रभातकाले द्रष्टव्यो नित्यं स्वश्रियमिच्छता ॥ Rājavallabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभानम्
प्रभानम् Light, lustre, splendour, radiance; P. VIII. 4. 34 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावत्|प्रभावन्त्
प्रभावत् <i>a.</i> Luminous, radiant, splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावती
प्रभावती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of metre.<BR>—2 (In music) A particular श्रुति.<BR>—3 N. of the wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभागः|प्रभाग
प्रभागः<BR>—1 Division.<BR>—2 The fraction of a fraction (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाष्
प्रभाष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To speak to, address to; स्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत Bg. 2. 54.<BR>—2 To proclaim; publish.<BR>—3 To disclose, reveal.<BR>—4 To expound, explain.<BR>—5 To prate, prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषणम्
प्रभाषणम् Explanation, interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषित
प्रभाषित <i>p. p.</i> Spoken, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषितम्
प्रभाषित + .{@-तम्@} Speech, talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्
प्रभास् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine.<BR>—2 To appear. ━<i>Caus.</i> To illuminate, irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासः|प्रभास
प्रभासः Splendour, beauty, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासः|प्रभास
प्रभासः + .{@-सः, -सम्@}<BR>—1 N. of a well-known place of pilgrimage near Dvārakā.<BR>—2 N. of one of the eight Vasus.<BR>—3 N. of one of the Jaina Gaṇādhipa.<BR>—4 N. of one of the Devagaṇas in the eighth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासम्
प्रभासः + .{@-सः, -सम्@}<BR>—1 N. of a well-known place of pilgrimage near Dvārakā.<BR>—2 N. of one of the eight Vasus.<BR>—3 N. of one of the Jaina Gaṇādhipa.<BR>—4 N. of one of the Devagaṇas in the eighth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासनम्
प्रभासनम् Illumining, irradiating, brightening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्वर
प्रभास्वर <i>a.</i> Brilliant, bright, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिद्
प्रभिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To break, tear, break or tear asunder.<BR>—2 To exude (from the temples of an elephant); see प्रभिन्न. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be broken to pieces.<BR>—2 To bud forth, open, expand (as flowers).<BR>—3 To split, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्न|प्रभिन्नः
प्रभिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Severed, split, cleft, divided.<BR>—2 Broken to pieces.<BR>—3 Cut off, detached.<BR>—4 Budding, expanded, opened.<BR>—5 Changed, altered.<BR>—6 Deformed, disfigured.<BR>—7 Relaxed, loosened.<BR>—8 Intoxicated, in rut; वेगेनापततस्तांस्तु प्राभिन्नानिव वारणान् Mb. 1. 189. 14;<BR> प्रभिन्नदिग्वारणवाहनो वृषा Ku. 5. 80.<BR>—9 Pierced, bored.<BR>—10 Different, distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्नः|प्रभिन्न
प्रभिन्न + .{@-न्नः@} An elephant in rut.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभिन्नाञ्जनम्, प्रभिन्नकरट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्नाञ्जनम्
प्रभिन्न + -अञ्जनम् a kind of collyrium or eye-salve mixed with oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्नकरट
प्रभिन्न + -करट <i>a.</i> ‘having the cheeks cleft’, being in rut, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदः|प्रभेद
प्रभेदः<BR>—1 Splitting, cleaving, opening.<BR>—2 Division, separation.<BR>—3 The flowing of rut or ichor from the temples of an elephant; बभूव<BR> तेनातितरां सुदुःसहः कटप्रभेदेन करीव पार्थिवः R. 3. 37.<BR>—4 Difference, distinction.<BR>—5 A kind or sort.<BR>—6 The place of origin (as of a river); शोणस्य नर्मदायाश्च प्रभेदे<BR> कुरुनन्दन Mb. 3. 85. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदक
प्रभेदक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tearing asunder, piercing &c.<BR>—2 Distinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभू
प्रभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To arise, proceed, spring up, to be born or produced, originate (with<BR> abl.); लोभात् क्रोधः प्रभवति H. 1. 25; स्वायंभुवान्मरीचेर्यः प्रबभूव<BR> प्रजापतिः Ś. 7. 9; पुरुषः प्रबभूवाग्नेर्विस्मयेन सहर्त्विजाम्<BR> R. 10. 50; अव्यक्ताद् व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे Bg. 8. 18.<BR>—2 To appear, become visible; वनेऽपि दोषाः प्रभवन्ति रागिणाम् H. 4. 84.<BR>—3 To multiply, increase; see प्रभूत.<BR>—4 To be strong or powerful, prevail, predominate, show oneʼs power; प्रभवति<BR> हि महिम्ना स्वेन योगीश्वरीयम् Māl. 9. 52; प्रभवति भगवान् विधिः K.; Pt. 1. 44.<BR>—5 To be able or equal, have power for (with inf.) कुसुमान्यपि गात्रसंगमात्<BR> प्रभवन्त्यायुरपोहितुं यदि R. 8. 44; कोऽन्यो हुतवहाद्दग्धुं प्रभविष्यति<BR> Ś. 4; Ś. 6. 30; V. 1. 9; U. 2. 4; Pt. 1.<BR>—5 To have control or power over, prevail over, be master of (usually<BR> with gen., sometimes with dat. or loc.); यदि प्रभविष्याम्यात्मनः Ś. 1;<BR> प्रभवति निजस्य कन्यकाजनस्य महाराजः Māl. 4; तत् प्रभवति<BR> अनुशासने देवी Ve. 2. विधिरपि न<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">Page1099-1</a>]<BR> येभ्यः प्रभवति Bh. 2. 94; नृपतिकुलवतंसमात्मवंशं भुवमधिपल्लवितं<BR> प्रभूय मेने Śiva B. 1. 91.<BR>—7 To be a match for (with dat.); प्रभवति मल्लो मल्लाय Mbh.<BR>—8 To be sufficient for, be able to contain; अपि व्याप्तदिगन्तानि नाङ्गानि<BR> प्रभवन्ति मे Ku. 6. 59.<BR>—9 To be contained in (wit loc.); गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव नात्मनि R. 3. 17.<BR>—10 To be useful.<BR>—11 To implore, beseech.<BR>—12 To extend beyond, surpass (Ved.).<BR>—13 To profit, avail. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To increase, augment.<BR>—2 To provide more fully.<BR>—3 To recognize.<BR>—4 To gain power or strength.<BR>—5 To make powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1098-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्रभव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Excellent, distinguished.<BR>—2 Superior, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवः|प्रभव
प्रभव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Source, origin; अनन्तरत्नप्रभवस्य यस्य Ku. 1. 3; अकिंचनः<BR> सन् प्रभवः स संपदाम् 5. 77; R. 9. 75.<BR>—2 Birth, production.<BR>—3 The source of a river; तस्या एवं प्रभवमचलं प्राप्य गौरं तुषारैः Me. 54.<BR>—4 The operative cause, origin of being (as father, mother &c.); तमस्याः<BR> प्रभवमवगच्छ Ś. 1.<BR>—5 The author, creator; अतश्चराचरं विश्वं प्रभवस्तस्य गीयसे Ku. 2. 5.<BR>—6 Birthplace.<BR>—7 Power, strength, valour, majestic dignity (= प्रभाव q. v.).<BR>—8 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—9 Prosperity, happiness; प्रभवार्थाय भूतानां धर्मप्रवचनं कृतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 109. 10.<BR>—10 (At the end of comp.) Arising or originating from, derived from; सूर्यप्रभवो<BR> वंशः R. 1. 2; Ku. 3. 15; यथा नदीनां प्रभवः (meeting place)<BR> समुद्रः, यथाहुतीनां प्रभवो (growth) हुताशः । यथेन्द्रियाणां प्रभवं<BR> (one having mastery over) मनोऽपि तथा प्रभुर्नो भगवानुपेन्द्रः Madhyamavyāyoga 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवनम्
प्रभवनम्<BR>—1 Production.<BR>—2 Source, origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवितृ
प्रभवितृ <i>m.</i> A ruler, great lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्रभविष्णु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, mighty, powerful.<BR>—2 Pre-eminent, distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णुः|प्रभविष्णु
प्रभविष्णु + .{@-ष्णुः@}<BR>—1 A lord, master; यत् प्रभविष्णवे रोचते Ś. 2; Ku. 6. 62.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावः|प्रभाव
प्रभावः<BR>—1 Lustre, splendour, brilliance.<BR>—2 Dignity, glory, majesty, grandeur, majestic lustre; प्रभाववानिव<BR> लक्ष्यते Ś. 1; अहो प्रभावो महात्मनाम् K.<BR>—3 Strength, valour, power, efficacy; पूज्यते यदपूज्योपि यदगम्योपि<BR> गम्यते । वन्द्यते यदवन्द्योपि स प्रभावो धनस्य च ॥ Pt. 1. 7; जानपदः<BR> प्रतिपत्तिमानुत्साहप्रभावयुक्तः Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR>—4 Regal power (one of the three Śaktis, q. v.).<BR>—5 A superhuman power or faculty, miraculous power; अनुभावांश्च जानासि<BR> ब्राह्मणानां न संशयः । प्रभावांश्चैव वेत्थ त्वं सर्वेषामेव पार्थिव ॥<BR> Mb. 3. 24. 8 (‘अनुभावो निश्चये स्यात् प्रभावः शक्तितेजसोः’ Viśva.);<BR> प्रत्याहतास्त्रो गिरिशप्रभावात् R. 2. 41, 62, 3. 40.<BR>—6 Magnanimity.<BR>—7 Extension, circumference.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभावज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावज|प्रभावजः
प्रभावः + -ज <i>a.</i> proceeding from majesty or regal power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाववत्|प्रभाववन्त्
प्रभाववत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, powerful, mighty.<BR>—2 Majestic; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावक
प्रभावक <i>a.</i> Prominent, having power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावन|प्रभावनः
प्रभावन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Prominent, influential.<BR>—2 Creating, creative; एते प्रदेशाः कथिता भुवनानां प्रभावनाः Mb. 12. 208. 10.<BR>—3 Explaining, disclosing; तदस्त्रं तस्य वीरस्य स्वर्गमार्गप्रभावनम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">Page1099-2</a>]<BR> Rām. 4. 17. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावनः|प्रभावन
प्रभावन + .{@-नः@} Creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावना
प्रभावन + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 Promulgation (of a doctrine).<BR>—2 Disclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु <i>a.</i> (भु, -भ्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Mighty, strong, powerful.<BR>—2 Able, competent, having power to (with inf. or in comp.); ऋषिप्रभावान्मयि<BR> नान्तकोऽपि प्रभुः प्रहर्तुं किमुतान्यहिंस्राः R. 2. 62; समाधिभेदप्रभवो<BR> भवन्ति Ku. 3. 40.<BR>—3 A match for; प्रभुर्मल्लो मल्लाय Mbh.<BR>—4 Abundant. —5 Ever-lasting, eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुः|प्रभु
प्रभु + .{@-भुः@}<BR>—1 A lord, master; प्रभुर्बुभूषुर्भुवनत्रयस्य यः Śi. 1. 49.<BR>—2 A governor, ruler, supreme authority.<BR>—3 An owner, proprietor.<BR>—4 Quick-silver.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 Of Śiva.<BR>—7 Of Brahmā; cf. समीक्ष्य प्रभवस्त्रयः Bhāg. 4. 1. 21; (also<BR> applied to various gods as Indra, Sūrya, Agni).<BR>—8 Word, sound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभुभक्त, प्रभुभक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्त|प्रभुभक्तः
प्रभु + -भक्त <i>a.</i> attached or devoted to oneʼs lord, loyal; बह्वाशी,<BR> स्वल्पसंतुष्टः, सुनिद्रः, शीघ्रचेतनः । प्रभुभक्तश्च शूरश्च ज्ञातव्याः<BR> षड्गुणाः शुनः ॥ Cāṇakyanītidarpaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्तः|प्रभुभक्त
प्रभु + -भक्त + .({@-क्तः@}) a good horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्तिः|प्रभुभक्ति
प्रभु + -भक्तिः <i>f.</i> devotion to oneʼs lord, loyalty, faithfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुता
प्रभुता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Lordship, supremacy, mastery, ascendancy, authority; भर्तर्यपेततमसि<BR> प्रभुता तवैव Ś. 7. 32; ‘मा गा इत्यपमङ्गलं, व्रज पुनः स्नेहेन हीनं वचः, तिष्ठेति प्रभुता, थयारुचि कुरु ह्येषाप्युदासीनता ।’ Śabda C.<BR>—2 Ownership.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभुताक्षेपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुत्वम्
प्रभुता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Lordship, supremacy, mastery, ascendancy, authority; भर्तर्यपेततमसि<BR> प्रभुता तवैव Ś. 7. 32; ‘मा गा इत्यपमङ्गलं, व्रज पुनः स्नेहेन हीनं वचः, तिष्ठेति प्रभुता, थयारुचि कुरु ह्येषाप्युदासीनता ।’ Śabda C.<BR>—2 Ownership.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभुताक्षेपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुताक्षेपः
प्रभुता + -आक्षेपः (प्रभुत्वाक्षेपः) (in rhet.) an objection based<BR> on power (<i>i. e.</i> on a word of command); प्रभुत्वेनैव रुद्धत्वात् प्रभुत्वाक्षेप<BR> उच्यते Kāv. 2. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूत|प्रभूतं
प्रभूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sprung from, produced.<BR>—2 Much, abundant.<BR>—3 Numerous, many.<BR>—4 Mature, perfect.<BR>—5 High, lofty.<BR>—6 Long.<BR>—7 Presided over.<BR>—8 Abounding in.<BR>—9 Gone up or upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतम्
प्रभूत + .{@-तम्@} A great or primary element.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रभूतयवसेन्धन, प्रभूतवयस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतयवसेन्धन
प्रभूत + -यवसेन्धन <i>a.</i> abounding in fresh grass and fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतवयस्
प्रभूत + -वयस् <i>a.</i> advanced in age, old, aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतता
प्रभूतता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Abundance, plenty.<BR>—2 Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतत्वम्
प्रभूतता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Abundance, plenty.<BR>—2 Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतिः|प्रभूति
प्रभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Source, origin.<BR>—2 Power, strength.<BR>—3 Sufficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्रभूष्णु <i>a.</i> Able, powerful, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृतिः|प्रभृति
प्रभृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Beginning, commencement; generally used in this sense as the last member<BR> of Bah. compound; इन्द्रप्रभृतयो देवाः &c.<BR>—2 Ved. An oblation.<BR>—3 Throwing or casting (Ved.). ━<i>ind.</i> From, ever since, beginning with<BR> (with abl.); शैशवात् प्रभृति पोषितां प्रियाम् U. 1. 45; Ku. 3. 26; R. 2. 38;<BR> अद्यप्रभृति henceforward; ततः प्रभृति, अतः प्रभृति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंश्
प्रभ्रंश् €1 Ā., €4 P.<BR>—1 To fall or drop down, slip; प्रभ्रश्यमानाभरणप्रसूना R. 14. 54.<BR>—2 To lose, be deprived of; प्रभ्रश्यते तेजसः Mk. 1. 14.<BR>—3 To escape or free onself from. ━<i>Caus.</i> To throw or bring down<BR> from, cause to fall down from; प्रभ्रंशयां यो नहुषं चकार R. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशः|प्रभ्रंश
प्रभ्रंशः Fall, falling off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1099-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशथुः|प्रभ्रंशथु
प्रभ्रंशथुः A disease of the nose; प्रभ्रश्यते नासिकयैव यश्च<BR> सान्द्रो विदग्धो लवणः कफस्तु । प्राक् संचितो मूर्ध्नि च पित्ततप्तं प्रभ्रंशथुं<BR> व्याधिमुदाहरन्ति ॥ Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशित
प्रभ्रंशित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thrown or cast down.<BR>—2 Deprived of.<BR>—3 Expelled, driven out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशिन्
प्रभ्रंशिन् Falling off or down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्ट
प्रभ्रष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen off, fallen or dropped down.<BR>—2 Broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टम्
प्रभ्रष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} A garland of flowers suspended from the lock on the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टकम्
प्रभ्रष्टकम् See प्रभ्रष्टम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्रमग्न <i>p. p.</i> Drowned, immersed, dipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमणस्
प्रमण(न)स् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Happy, cheerful, delighted.<BR>—2 Good-natured.<BR>—3 Attentive.<BR>—4 Kind, amiable (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्रमण(न)स् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Happy, cheerful, delighted.<BR>—2 Good-natured.<BR>—3 Attentive.<BR>—4 Kind, amiable (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत
प्रमत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Thought out.<BR>—2 Wise, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्
प्रमथ्, -मन्थ् €1. €9 P.<BR>—1 To churn; प्रमथ्यमानो (समुद्रो) गिरिणेव भूयः R. 13. 14.<BR>—2 To harass, trouble excessively, annoy, torment.<BR>—3 To strike down, bruise, hurt.<BR>—4 To tear off or cut.<BR>—5 To lay waste, devastate.<BR>—6 To kill, destroy; प्रमथ्य क्रव्यादं मरणसमये रक्षितवतः<BR> Māl. 4. 9, 9. 27.<BR>—7 To agitate, stir about.<BR>—8 Ved. To rob. ━<i>Caus.</i> To harass, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्थ्|प्रमंथ्
प्रमथ्, -मन्थ् €1. €9 P.<BR>—1 To churn; प्रमथ्यमानो (समुद्रो) गिरिणेव भूयः R. 13. 14.<BR>—2 To harass, trouble excessively, annoy, torment.<BR>—3 To strike down, bruise, hurt.<BR>—4 To tear off or cut.<BR>—5 To lay waste, devastate.<BR>—6 To kill, destroy; प्रमथ्य क्रव्यादं मरणसमये रक्षितवतः<BR> Māl. 4. 9, 9. 27.<BR>—7 To agitate, stir about.<BR>—8 Ved. To rob. ━<i>Caus.</i> To harass, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथः|प्रमथ
प्रमथः<BR>—1 A horse.<BR>—2 N. of a class of Beings (said to be goblins) attending on Śiva; प्रमथमुखविकारैर्हासयामास<BR> गूढम् Ku. 7. 95.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमथाधिपः, प्रमथनाथः, प्रमथपतिः, प्रमथालयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथाधिपः|प्रमथाधिप
प्रमथः + -अधिपः, -नाथः, -पतिः an epithet of Śiva; तेनाहृताः प्रमथनाथमखाय<BR> भूपाः Bhāg. 1. 15. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथनाथः|प्रमथनाथ
प्रमथः + -अधिपः, -नाथः, -पतिः an epithet of Śiva; तेनाहृताः प्रमथनाथमखाय<BR> भूपाः Bhāg. 1. 15. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथपतिः|प्रमथपति
प्रमथः + -अधिपः, -नाथः, -पतिः an epithet of Śiva; तेनाहृताः प्रमथनाथमखाय<BR> भूपाः Bhāg. 1. 15. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथालयः|प्रमथालय
प्रमथः + -आलयः hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथनम्
प्रमथनम्<BR>—1 Hurting, injuring, tormenting.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—3 Churning, stirring about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथित|प्रमथितं
प्रमथित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Tormented, distressed.<BR>—2 Trampled down.<BR>—3 Slain, killed; प्रमथितश्च दंष्ट्रायुधः Māl. 3. 18.<BR>—4 Properly churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथितम्
प्रमथित + .{@-तम्@} Butter-milk without water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथिन्
प्रमथिन् <i>a.</i> Destroying; तल्लक्ष्मीमिव चेतनाप्रमथनीमूढ्वा<BR> च वध्यस्रजम् Mu. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्या
प्रमथ्या A kind of medicinal paste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्थः|प्रमन्थ
प्रमन्थः A stick used for producing fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथः|प्रमाथ
प्रमाथः<BR>—1 Excessive paining, tormenting, torturing.<BR>—2 Agitating, churning.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter, destruction, सैनिकानां प्रमाथेन सत्यमोजायितं<BR> त्वया U. 5. 31, 4.<BR>—4 Violence, outrage.<BR>—6 Rape, forcible abduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथाः
प्रमाथः + .{@-थाः@} <i>m.</i> (pl.) Epithet of the fiends attendant upon Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथित
प्रमाथित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Forcibly attacked, roughly handled<BR>—2 Ravished, seduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्रमाथिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tormenting, harassing, torturing, afflicting, harrowing; क्व रुजा<BR> हृदयप्रमाथिनी क्व च ते विश्वसनीयमायुधम् M. 3. 2; Māl. 2. 1; Ki. 3. 14.<BR>—2 Killing, destroying.<BR>—3 Agitating, setting in motion; इन्द्रियाणि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">Page1100-2</a>]<BR> प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः Bg. 2. 60, 6. 34.<BR>—4 Tearing or pulling down, striking down; वर्त्मसु ध्वजतरुप्रमाथिनः R. 11. 58.<BR>—5 Cutting down; प्रमाथिनस्तान् भवमार्गणानाम् (बाणान्) Ki. 17. 31.<BR>—6 (In medic.) Producing secretion of the vessels. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्
प्रमद् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be intoxicated or drunk.<BR>—2 To be careless about, to be negligent or heedless, be regardless of<BR> or indifferent to (with loc.); अतोऽर्थान्न प्रमाद्यन्ति प्रमदासु विपश्चितः Ms. 2. 213.<BR>—3 To omit to do, swerve or deviate from (with abl.); स्वाधिकारात् प्रमत्तः Me. 1.<BR>—4 To make a mistake, err, go astray; प्रमाद्यन् चारदुर्बलः Bk. 5. 8, 17. 39, 18. 8.<BR>—5 To spend or while away (time).<BR>—6 To be joyous; युक्तः प्रमाद्यसि हितादपेतः परितप्यसे Ki. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्रमत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Intoxicated, drunk; कथां प्रमत्तः प्रथमं कृतामिव (न स्मरिष्यति) Ś. 4. 1;<BR>—2 Mad, insane.<BR>—3 Careless, negligent, inattentive; heedless, regardless (generally with<BR> loc.); सुप्तां मत्तां प्रमत्तां वा रहो यत्रोपगच्छति Ms. 3. 34; मत्तं<BR> प्रमत्तमुन्मत्तं सुप्तं बालं स्त्रियं जडम् । प्रपन्नं विरथं भीतं<BR> न रिपुं हन्ति धर्मवित् ॥ Bhāg. 1. 7. 36.<BR>—4 Swerving from, failing to do (with abl.).<BR>—5 Blundering.<BR>—6 wanton, lascivious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमत्तगीत, प्रमत्तचित्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तगीत
प्रमत्त + -गीत <i>a.</i> sung carelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तचित्त
प्रमत्त + -चित्त <i>a.</i> negligent, heedless, careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तता
प्रमत्तता Inattention, carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तवत्|प्रमत्तवन्त्
प्रमत्तवत् <i>a.</i> Inattentive, careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्रमद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Drunk, intoxicated (fig. also).<BR>—2 Impassioned.<BR>—3 Careless.<BR>—4 Wanton, dissolute.<BR>—5 Violent, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदः|प्रमद
प्रमद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 Joy, pleasure, delight; बिभ्रन्ति यत्र प्रमदाय पुंसाम् Śi. 3. 54, 13. 2;<BR> Māl. 9; अप्यमुना न वचोविषयो यः स प्रमदः सहासालसमूहे<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 94.<BR>—2 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>—3 The ankle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमदकाननम्, प्रमदवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदकाननम्
प्रमद + -काननम्, -वनम् a pleasure garden attached to the royal harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदवनम्
प्रमद + -काननम्, -वनम् a pleasure garden attached to the royal harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदक
प्रमदक <i>a.</i> Licentious, sensual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदनम्
प्रमदनम् Amorous desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदा
प्रमदा —1 A young handsome woman; अतः समीपे परिणेतुरिष्यते तदप्रियापि<BR> प्रमदा स्वबन्धुभिः Ś. 5. 17.<BR>—2 A wife or woman in general; असति त्वयि वारुणीमदः प्रमदानामधुना<BR> विडम्बना Ku. 4. 12; R. 8. 72.<BR>—3 The sign <i>virgo</i> of the zodiac.<BR>—4 N. of a metre; नजसजला गुरुश्च भवति प्रमदा; V. Ratn.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमदाकाननम्, प्रमदावनम्, प्रमदाजनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदाकाननम्
प्रमदा + -काननम्, -वनम् a pleasure garden attached to the royal harem<BR> (for the use of the wives of a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदावनम्
प्रमदा + -काननम्, -वनम् a pleasure garden attached to the royal harem<BR> (for the use of the wives of a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदाजनः|प्रमदाजन
प्रमदा + -जनः<BR>—1 a young woman.<BR>—2 womankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्वर
प्रमद्वर <i>a.</i> Careless, inattentive; heedless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्वरा
प्रमद्वरा <i>f.</i> N. of the mother of sage Śunaka and wife of sage Ruru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादः|प्रमाद
प्रमादः<BR>—1 Carelessness, negligence, inattention, inadvertence, oversight; विजिगीषुमिवानयप्रमादौ<BR> Ki. 13. 29; ज्ञातुं प्रमादस्खलितं न शक्यम् Ś. 6. 25; विद्यां प्रमादगुणितामिव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">Page1101-1</a>]<BR> चिन्तयामि C. P. 1.<BR>—2 Intoxication, drunkenness.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Fainting, swoon.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Insanity, madness.<BR>—4 A mistake, blunder, mistaken judgment; Pt. 1. 39.<BR>—5 An accident, mishap, calamity, danger; अहो प्रमादः Māl. 3; U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1100-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादवत्|प्रमादवन्त्
प्रमादवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intoxicated.<BR>—2 Mad, insane.<BR>—3 Careless, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका<BR>—1 A careless woman.<BR>—2 A deflowered girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादित
प्रमादित <i>a.</i> Ridiculed, mocked, scoffed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Careless, inattentive, negligent; सर्वत्र प्रमादी वैधेयः V. 2;<BR> एकः प्रमादी स कथं न हन्यते Udb.<BR>—2 Insane, mad.<BR>—3 Intoxicated, drunk. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्रमनस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 (Vedic) Careful, tender.<BR>—2 Delighted, happy, cheerful, in good spirits; नृपस्य नातिप्रमनाः<BR> सदोगृहं सुदक्षिणासूनुरपि न्यवर्तत R. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्यु
प्रमन्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Enraged, irritated, incensed against (with loc.); प्रमन्यवः प्रागपि<BR> कोशलेन्द्रे R. 7. 34.<BR>—2 Distressed, sorrowful, sorely grieved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमयः|प्रमय
प्रमयः<BR>—1 Death.<BR>—2 Ruin, downfall.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दः|प्रमर्द
प्रमर्दः N. of a position of the moon in the नक्षत्रs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दनम्
प्रमर्दनम् Crushing, destroying, trampling down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दनः|प्रमर्दन|प्रमर्दनं
प्रमर्दनम् + .{@-नः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमहस्
प्रमहस् <i>a.</i> Of great might or splendour; प्रमहसि पदे निस्त्रैगुण्ये<BR> शिवाय नमो नमः Śivamahimna 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा €2 P., €3 Ā.<BR>—1 To measure; त्रीणि पदानि प्रमाय.<BR>—2 To form, make, build.<BR>—3 To prove, establish, demonstrate.<BR>—4 To arrange, place in order.<BR>—5 To know, understand, get a correct idea of; न परोपहितं न च<BR> स्वतः प्रमिमीतेऽनुभवादृतेऽल्पधीः Śi. 16. 40; अशक्योऽयमर्थः प्रमातुम् H. 3.<BR>—6 To conjecture. ━<i>Caus.</i> To afford or give proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा<BR>—1 Consciousness, perception.<BR>—2 (In logic) Correct notion or apprehension, true and certain knowledge,<BR> accurate conception; तद्वति तत्प्रकारकोऽनुभवः प्रमा यथा रजते<BR> इदं रजतमिति ज्ञानम् T. S.; दोषोऽप्रमाया जनकः प्रमायास्तु गुणो भवेत् ।<BR> प्रत्यक्षे तु विशेष्येण विशेषेणवता समम् ॥ Bhāṣā P.<BR>—3 Ved. Basis, foundation.<BR>—4 A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणम्
प्रमाणम् —1 A measure in general (of length, breadth &c.); न प्रमाणेन<BR> नोत्साहात् सत्त्वस्थो भव पाण्डब Mb. 3. 33. 63. (‘प्रमाणं नित्यमर्यादासंघवादिप्रमादिषु’<BR> Viśva.); Mb. 1. 222. 31; दृष्टो हि वृण्वन् कलभप्रमाणोऽप्याशाः पुरोवातमवाप्य<BR> मेघः R. 18. 38.<BR>—2 Size, extent, magnitude.<BR>—3 Scale, standard; पृथिव्यां स्वामिभक्तानां प्रमाणे परमे स्थितः Mu. 2. 21.<BR>—4 Limit, quantity; वञ्चयित्वा तु राजानं न प्रमाणेऽवतिष्ठसि Rām. 2. 37. 22.<BR>—5 Testimony, evidence, proof.<BR>—6 Authority, warrant; one who judges or decides, one whose word<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">Page1101-2</a>]<BR> is an authority; श्रुत्वा देवः प्रमाणम् Pt. 1 ‘having heard this your Majesty will decide (what to do)’<BR>; आर्यमिश्राः प्रमाणम् M. 1; Mu. 1. 1;<BR> सतां हि संदेहपदेषु वस्तुषु प्रमाणमन्तःकरणप्रवृत्तयः<BR> Ś. 1. 22; व्याकरणे पाणिनिः प्रमाणम्; Ms. 2. 13; Pt. 1. 240; sometimes<BR> in pl.; वेदाः प्रमाणाः.<BR>—7 A true or certain knowledge, accurate conception or notion.<BR>—8 A mode of proof, a means of arriving at correct knowledge; (the Naiyāyikas<BR> recognize only four kinds; प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान, उपमान and शब्द,<BR> the Vedāntins and Mimāṃsakas add two more, अनुपलब्धि and अर्थापत्ति;<BR> while the Sāṅkhyas admit प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान and शब्द only;<BR> cf. अनुभव also.).<BR>—9 Principal, capital.<BR>—10 Unity.<BR>—11 Scripture, sacred authority.<BR>—12 Cause, reason.<BR>—13 Rule, sanction, precept.<BR>—14 The first term in a rule of three.<BR>—15 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—16 Freedom from apprehension.<BR>—17 The prosodial length of a vowel.<BR>—18 An eternal matter; L. D. B.<BR>—19 (In music) A measure (such as द्रुत, मध्य, विलम्बित); Rām. 1. 4. 8.<BR>—20 The measure of a square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणः|प्रमाण|प्रमाणं
प्रमाणम् + .{@-णः, -णी@} A rule, standard, authority.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमाणाधिक, प्रमाणानुरूप, प्रमाणान्तरम्, प्रमाणाभावः, प्रमाणकुशल, प्रमाणप्रवीण, प्रमाणकोटिः, प्रमाणज्ञ, प्रमाणदृष्ट, प्रमाणपत्रम्, प्रमाणपथः, प्रमाणपुरुषः, प्रमाणबाधितार्थकः, प्रमाणभूत, प्रमाणराशिः, प्रमाणवचनम्, प्रमाणवाक्यम्, प्रमाणशास्त्रम्, प्रमाणसूत्रम्, प्रमाणस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणी
प्रमाणम् + .{@-णः, -णी@} A rule, standard, authority.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमाणाधिक, प्रमाणानुरूप, प्रमाणान्तरम्, प्रमाणाभावः, प्रमाणकुशल, प्रमाणप्रवीण, प्रमाणकोटिः, प्रमाणज्ञ, प्रमाणदृष्ट, प्रमाणपत्रम्, प्रमाणपथः, प्रमाणपुरुषः, प्रमाणबाधितार्थकः, प्रमाणभूत, प्रमाणराशिः, प्रमाणवचनम्, प्रमाणवाक्यम्, प्रमाणशास्त्रम्, प्रमाणसूत्रम्, प्रमाणस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणाधिक
प्रमाणम् + -अधिक <i>a.</i> more than ordinary, inordinate, excessive; श्वासः<BR> प्रमाणाधिकः Ś. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणानुरूप
प्रमाणम् + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i> corresponding to physical strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणान्तरम्
प्रमाणम् + -अन्तरम् another mode of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणाभावः|प्रमाणाभाव
प्रमाणम् + -अभावः absence of authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणकुशल
प्रमाणम् + -कुशल, -प्रवीण <i>a.</i> skilful in arguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणप्रवीण
प्रमाणम् + -कुशल, -प्रवीण <i>a.</i> skilful in arguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणकोटिः|प्रमाणकोटि
प्रमाणम् + -कोटिः the point in an argument which is regarded as actual proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणज्ञ|प्रमाणज्ञः
प्रमाणम् + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the modes of proof, (as a logician).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणज्ञः|प्रमाणज्ञ
प्रमाणम् + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणदृष्ट
प्रमाणम् + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i> sanctioned by authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपत्रम्
प्रमाणम् + -पत्रम् a written warrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपथः|प्रमाणपथ
प्रमाणम् + -पथः the way of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपुरुषः|प्रमाणपुरुष
प्रमाणम् + -पुरुषः an arbitrator, a judge, an umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणबाधितार्थकः|प्रमाणबाधितार्थक
प्रमाणम् + -बाधितार्थकः a kind of Tarka in Nyāyaśāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणभूत|प्रमाणभूतः
प्रमाणम् + -भूत (˚णीभूत) <i>a.</i> authoritative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणभूतः|प्रमाणभूत
प्रमाणम् + -भूत + .({@-तः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणराशिः|प्रमाणराशि
प्रमाणम् + -राशिः the quantity of the first term in a rule of three sums.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणवचनम्
प्रमाणम् + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् an authoritative statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणवाक्यम्
प्रमाणम् + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् an authoritative statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणशास्त्रम्
प्रमाणम् + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 scripture.<BR>—2 the science of logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणसूत्रम्
प्रमाणम् + -सूत्रम् a measuring cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणस्थ
प्रमाणम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of normal size.<BR>—2 unperturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणक|प्रमाणकः
प्रमाणक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Measuring, extending to, as far as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणकः|प्रमाणक
प्रमाणक + .{@-कः@} see प्रमाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणतः
प्रमाणतः <i>ind.</i> According to measure or weight; चतुःसौवर्णिको<BR> निष्को विज्ञेयस्तु प्रमाणतः Ms. 8. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणयति
प्रमाणयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To regard as an authority; दैवमविद्वांसः प्रमाणयन्ति Mu. 3;<BR> प्रमाणयति नो धर्मे H. 1. 10.<BR>—2 To hold up as a model.<BR>—3 To prove, demonstrate, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिक
प्रमाणिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Forming or being a measure.<BR>—2 Forming an authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिका
प्रमाणिक + .{@-का@} A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणित
प्रमाणित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Adjusted.<BR>—2 Proved, demonstrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकृ
प्रमाणीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To confide, believe.<BR>—2 To hold or regard as an authority; शासनं तरुभिरपि प्रमाणीकृतम् Ś. 6.<BR>—3 To fix upon, dispense, deal or meet out; दैवेन प्रभुणा स्वयं जगति<BR> यद्यस्य प्रमाणीकृतम् Bh. 2. 121.<BR>—4 To obey,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">Page1102-1</a>]<BR> conform to.<BR>—5 To prove, to establish.<BR>—6 To consult, take the consent of; दाता मे भूभृतां नाथः प्रमाणीक्रियतामिति Ku. 6. 1.<BR>—7 To take into account; न प्रमाणीकृतः पाणिर्बाल्ये बालेन पीडितः U. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1101-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्रमातृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a right notion, competent to judge or ascertain.<BR>—2 An authority, proof.<BR>—3 Demonstrating.<BR>—4 A civil judge; EI. XVII. 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमात्वम्
प्रमात्वम् Accuracy of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापक|प्रमापकः
प्रमापक <i>a.</i> Furnishing authority or proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापकः|प्रमापक
प्रमापक + .{@-कः@} An authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापणम्
प्रमापणम् Form, shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
प्रमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Measured.<BR>—2 Measured off, limited, few, little; प्रमितविषयां शक्तिं विन्दन्<BR> Mv. 1. 51; Śi. 16. 80.<BR>—3 Known, understood.<BR>—4 Proved, demonstrated.<BR>—5 (At the end of comp.) Of such and such extent or measure.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमिताक्षरा, प्रमिताक्षरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिताक्षरा
प्रमित + -अक्षरा <i>f.</i> N. of a metre having each quarter comprised of 12 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिताक्षरम्
प्रमित + -अक्षरम् few words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमितिः|प्रमिति
प्रमितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Measurement, a measure.<BR>—2 True or certain knowledge, accurate notion or conception. —3 Knowledge<BR> obtained by any one of the Pramāṇas or means of knowledge.<BR>—4 True inference or analogy.<BR>—5 Manifestation; इतीरेशेऽतक्र्ये निजमहिमनि स्वप्रमितिके Bhāg. 10. 13. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेय
प्रमेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Measurable, finite.<BR>—2 To be proved, demonstrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेयम्
प्रमेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 An object of certain knowledge, a demonstrated conclusion, theorem.<BR>—2 The thing to be proved, the topic to be proved or discussed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामहः|प्रमातामह
प्रमातामहः A maternal great-grand-father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामही
प्रमातामहः + .{@-ही@} A maternal great-grand-mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापणम्
प्रमापणम् Killing, slaughter; नभसि महसां ध्वान्तध्वाङ्क्षप्रमापणपत्रिणाम्<BR> N. 19. 12. cf. प्रमापणनिष्णातैः Haravijaya 43. 58; Dk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापयितृ
प्रमापयितृ <i>m.</i> A murderer, killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमायुक
प्रमायुक <i>a.</i> conducive to death; न चास्य प्रियं प्रमायुकं<BR> भवति Bṛ. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिद्
प्रमिद् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To grow fat.<BR>—2 To begin to show affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदित
प्रमेदित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unctuous, greasy.<BR>—2 Having begun to show affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमी
प्रमी €9 U.<BR>—1 To destroy, annihilate, kill, slay.<BR>—2 To diminish.<BR>—3 To surmount, get over.<BR>—4 To surpass, outstrip.<BR>—5 Ved. To transgress, infringe.<BR>—6 Ved. To lose or miss (oneʼs way).<BR>—7 To perish, die. ━<i>Caus.</i> To destroy, annihilate &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीत|प्रमीतः
प्रमीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dead, deceased; … यो मोहात् प्रमीतपतिकां स्त्रियम् । नियोजयत्यपत्यार्थं<BR> तं विगर्हन्ति साधवः ॥ Ms. 9. 68; Mb. 9. 53. 11.<BR>—2 Sacrificed (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीतः|प्रमीत
प्रमीत + .{@-तः@} An animal immolated or killed at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीतिः|प्रमीति
प्रमीतिः <i>f.</i> Death, destruction, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीढ|प्रमीढः
प्रमीढ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thick, dense, compact.<BR>—2 Passed as urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्रमीला<BR>—1 Sleepiness, lassitude, enervation of spirits; स्वदृशोर्जनयन्ति सान्त्वनां … उदयप्रत्मीलयोः<BR> N. 2. 21.<BR>—2 N. of a woman, sovereign of a kingdom of women. She fought with Arjuna<BR> when his horse entered her territory, but she was conquered and became his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलिका
प्रमीलिका Sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलित
प्रमीलित <i>p. p.</i> With closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुख|प्रमुखं|प्रमुखः
प्रमुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Facing, turning the face towards.<BR>—2 Chief, principal, foremost, first.<BR>—3 Respectable, honourable.<BR>—4 (At the end of comp.)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Headed by, having as chief or at the head; वासुकिप्रमुखाः Ku. 2. 38.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Accompanied with; प्रीतिप्रमुखवचनं स्वागतं व्याजहार Me. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुखः|प्रमुख|प्रमुखं
प्रमुख + .{@-खः@}<BR>—1 A respectable man.<BR>—2 A heap, multitude.<BR>—3 The tree called Punnāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुखम्
प्रमुख + .{@-खम्@}<BR>—1 The mouth.<BR>—2 The beginning of a chapter or section.<BR>—3 The time being, the present. (प्रमुखतस् and प्रमुखे are used<BR> adverbially in the sense of ‘in front of’, ‘before’, ‘opposite to’; भीष्मद्रोणप्रमुखतः<BR> सर्वेषां च महीक्षिताम् Bg. 1. 25; Ś. 7. 22.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुच्
प्रमुच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To set free, liberate, release.<BR>—2 To throw, cast, hurl.<BR>—3 To shed, emit, send forth.<BR>—4 To abandon, forsake, give up, renounce.<BR>—5 To loosen, untie, unbind.<BR>—6 To expel, drive away, banish.<BR>—7 To utter.<BR>—8 To put on, wear (as a garland &c.).<BR>—9 To give, bestow; अत्र तेऽहं प्रमोक्ष्यामि मालां कुब्जे हिरण्मयीम्<BR> Rām. 2. 9. 47. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be loose or detached.<BR>—2 To leave off, cease.<BR>—3 To free oneself from. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To loosen, unbind.<BR>—2 To liberate, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुक्त
प्रमुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Loosened.<BR>—2 Liberated, set free.<BR>—3 Resigned, renounced.<BR>—4 Cast, hurled.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमुक्तकण्ठम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुक्तकण्ठम्|प्रमुक्तकंठम्
प्रमुक्त + -कण्ठम् <i>ind.</i> bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुक्तिः|प्रमुक्ति
प्रमुक्तिः Liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोक्षः|प्रमोक्ष
प्रमोक्षः<BR>—1 Dropping, letting fall.<BR>—2 Discharging, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोचनम्
प्रमोचनम्<BR>—1 Liberating, setting free.<BR>—2 Emitting, shedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद् €1 Ā. To be extremely glad, be very much delighted; प्रमुदितवरपक्षमेकतस्तत्<BR> R. 6. 86; Māl. 5. 23. ━<i>Caus.</i> To gladden, delight, exhilarate;<BR> प्रमोदय चातकान् Māl. 9. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद् <i>f.</i> Extreme joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदित|प्रमुदितः
प्रमुदित <i>p. p.</i> Delighted, glad, pleased, happy; प्रमुदितकटपूतनोत्तालवेताल …<BR> Māl. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदितम्
प्रमुदित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Gladness, gaiety.<BR>—2 One of the 8 Sāṅkhya perfections.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रमुदितवदना, प्रमुदितहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदितवदना
प्रमुदित + -वदना <i>f.</i> N. of a metre with each line consisting of 12 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदितहृदय
प्रमुदित + -हृदय <i>a.</i> delighted at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1102-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदः|प्रमोद
प्रमोदः<BR>—1 Joy, delight, rejoicing, pleasure; प्रमोदनृत्यैः सह वारयोषिताम्<BR> R. 3. 19; Ms. 3. 61.<BR>—2 One of the eight perfections in the Sāṅkhya philosophy.<BR>—3 A strong perfume.<BR>—4 (With Jainas) joy as exhibited in the virtuous.<BR>—5 N. of a year.<BR>—6 A kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदनम्
प्रमोदनम्<BR>—1 Gladdening, delighting, making glad.<BR>—2 Gladness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदनः|प्रमोदन|प्रमोदनं
प्रमोदनम् + .{@-नः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu; जितामित्रः प्रमोदनः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदित|प्रमोदितः
प्रमोदित <i>p. p.</i> Pleased, delighted, joyful, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदितः|प्रमोदित
प्रमोदित + .{@-तः@} An epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदिन्
प्रमोदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Delighting, making happy.<BR>—2 Delighted, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुष्
प्रमुष् €9 P.<BR>—1 To take away, obscure; परा ऽऽत्मीयाविवेकं च प्रामुष्णात कपिरक्षसाम् Bk. 17. 60.<BR>—2 To steal away, rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुषित
प्रमुषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stolen, taken away; Bhāg. 5. 1. 29; (पाणिना) परामृशत् कठिनकठोरकामिनीकुचस्थलप्रमुषितचन्दनम् Śi. 17. 11.<BR>—2 Distracted, unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुषिता
प्रमुषित + .{@-ता@} A kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोषः|प्रमोष
प्रमोषः Stealing or taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुह्
प्रमुह् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be stupefied or infatuated.<BR>—2 To faint, swoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुग्ध
प्रमुग्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fainting, unconscious.<BR>—2 Very lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढ
प्रमूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Perplexed, bewildered, infatuated.<BR>—2 Stupid, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोहः|प्रमोह
प्रमोहः<BR>—1 Stupefaction, insensibility, stupor; तिरयति करणानां ग्राहकत्वं<BR> प्रमोहः Māl. 1. 41.<BR>—2 Infatuation, bewilderment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोहित
प्रमोहित <i>p. p.</i> Infatuated, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृत
प्रमृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dead, deceased.<BR>—2 Covered, concealed.<BR>—3 Withdrawn or gone out of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृतम्
प्रमृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Death.<BR>—2 Cultivation; ऋतामृताभ्यां जीवेत्तु मृतेन प्रमृतेन वा Ms. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृज्
प्रमृज् €2 P.<BR>—1 To wipe off or out, cleanse (fig. also); स्वभावलोलेत्ययशः प्रमृष्टम् R. 6. 41.<BR>—2 To wipe off, away or out, blow out, efface; नामान्येषां लिखामि ध्रुवमहमधुना<BR> चित्रगुप्तः प्रमार्ष्टु Mu. 1. 20.<BR>—3 To remove, rid oneself of.<BR>—4 To atone for, make amends for, expiate; प्रणिपातलङ्घनं प्रमार्ष्टुकामा<BR> V. 3; सर्वथा प्रमार्जितं त्वया प्रत्यादेशदुःखम् Ś. 6.<BR>—5 To stroke or rub gently.<BR>—6 To prepare.<BR>—7 To mark useless, frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमार्जनम्
प्रमार्जनम्<BR>—1 Wiping off, rubbing or washing off.<BR>—2 Removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृड
प्रमृड <i>a.</i> Making glad, happy; नमः शिवाय शान्ताय सत्त्वाय<BR> प्रमृडाय च Bhāg. 12. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृष्ट
प्रमृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rubbed off, washed or wiped off, cleared off; येन श्रियः संश्रयदोषरूढं<BR> स्वभावलोलेत्ययशः प्रमृष्टम् R. 6. 41, 44.<BR>—2 Polished, bright, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृष्टिः|प्रमृष्टि
प्रमृष्टिः <i>f.</i> Rubbing over with; Hc. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेहः|प्रमेह
प्रमेहः A general name for a urinary disease (such as gleet, diabetes<BR> &c.); आस्यामुखं स्वप्नसुखं दधीनि ग्राम्यौदनानूपरसः पयांसि । नवान्नपानं<BR> गुडवैकृतं च प्रमेहहेतुः कफकृच्च सर्वम् ॥ Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लै
प्रम्लै €1 P.<BR>—1 To fade, wither.<BR>—2 To be downcast, sad or dejected.<BR>—3 To be languid or wearied.<BR>—4 To be dirty; or foul, be soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लान
प्रम्लान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Faded, withered away.<BR>—2 Soiled, dirty; cf. परिम्लान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्
प्रयत् €1 Ā. To try, endeavour, strive, attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नः|प्रयत्न
प्रयत्नः<BR>—1 Effort, exertion, endeavour; तस्येदं विपुलं विधेर्विलसितं पुसां<BR> प्रयत्नच्छिदः Mu. 5. 20.<BR>—2 Persevering or continued effort; perseverance.<BR>—3 Labour, difficulty; प्रयत्नप्रेक्षणीयः संवृत्तः Ś. 1 ‘hardly visible’<BR>, ‘seen with difficulty’.<BR>—4 Great care, caution; कृतप्रयत्नोऽपि गृहे विनश्यति Pt. 1. 20.<BR>—5 (In gram.) Effort in uttering, effort of the mouth in the production<BR> of articulate sounds; see Sk. on P. VIII. 2. 1.<BR>—6 (In phil.) Active effort of three kinds; प्रवृत्तिश्च निवृत्तिश्च तथा<BR> जीवनकारणम् । एवं प्रयत्नत्र्यैविध्यं तान्त्रिकैः परिदर्शितम् ॥<BR>—7 Activity, action in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयत्नगौरवम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नगौरवम्
प्रयत्नः + -गौरवम् Elaborateness of effort; इतरथा वेदवाक्यानि व्याख्येयानि<BR> स्वपदार्थाश्च व्याख्येया इति प्रयत्नगौरवं प्रसज्येत ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नतः
प्रयत्नः + .({@प्रयत्नतः, प्रयत्नेन, -त्नात्@} &c. <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With great effort, diligently.<BR>—2 Assiduously.<BR>—3 Hardly, scarcely.<BR>—4 Particularly, specially.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नेन
प्रयत्नः + .({@प्रयत्नतः, प्रयत्नेन, -त्नात्@} &c. <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With great effort, diligently.<BR>—2 Assiduously.<BR>—3 Hardly, scarcely.<BR>—4 Particularly, specially.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नात्
प्रयत्नः + .({@प्रयत्नतः, प्रयत्नेन, -त्नात्@} &c. <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With great effort, diligently.<BR>—2 Assiduously.<BR>—3 Hardly, scarcely.<BR>—4 Particularly, specially.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नवत्|प्रयत्नवन्त्
प्रयत्नवत् <i>a.</i> Assiduous, diligent, persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयम्
प्रयम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To give, grant (with dat. of person).<BR>—2 To curb, check, restrain, control.<BR>—3 To deliver, restore.<BR>—4 To give in marriage.<BR>—5 To pay, discharge (as a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत|प्रयतः
प्रयत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Restrained, self-subdued, holy, pious, devout, purified by austerities<BR> or religious observances; keeping the organs of sense under restraint;<BR> प्रयतपरिग्रहद्वितीयः R. 1. 95, 8. 11, 13. 70; समादिदेश प्रयतां<BR> तनूजाम् Ku. 1. 58, 3. 16; शुचिः प्रयतवाक्चित्तः स्तुत्वा माद्रीसुतोऽथ<BR> तम् Bm. 2. 133; प्रयते केरलदेशे प्रथितं राराष्टि कोटिलिङ्गपुरम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Zealous, intent; प्रयतोपचराम्यहम् Mb. 3. 233. 19.<BR>—3 Submissive.<BR>—4 Careful, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतः|प्रयत
प्रयत + .{@-तः@} A holy or pious person.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयतात्मन्, प्रयतमानस, प्रयतपाणि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतात्मन्
प्रयत + -आत्मन्, -मानस pious-minded, devout, ascetic; प्रयतात्मनः Bg. 9. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतमानस
प्रयत + -आत्मन्, -मानस pious-minded, devout, ascetic; प्रयतात्मनः Bg. 9. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतपाणि
प्रयत + -पाणि folding palms together (in नमस्कार); यश्चिन्त्यते<BR> प्रयतपाणिभिः Bhāg. 11. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतत्वम्
प्रयतत्वम् Purity, holiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतनम्
प्रयतनम् Effort, endeavour; see प्रयत्न; तद्दैवस्यानुगुण्यात्<BR> प्रयतनविभवैश्चाद्य राज्येऽभिषिच्य Mv. 7. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतिः|प्रयति
प्रयतिः <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 An offering, oblation.<BR>—2 A gift, present.<BR>—3 Effort, endeavour.<BR>—4 Will, intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1103-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयन्तृ
प्रयन्तृ <i>m.</i> A guide, driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयामः|प्रयाम
प्रयामः<BR>—1 Restraining, checking.<BR>—2 Dearth, scarcity, dearness (of water, corn &c.).<BR>—3 Length; कुर्वन् प्रयामक्षयमायतीनाम् Ki. 3. 43.<BR>—4 Competition of buyers on account of dearth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To strive, endeavour.<BR>—2 To toil, labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयासः|प्रयास
प्रयासः<BR>—1 Effort, exertion, endeavour; जहार सीतां पक्षीन्द्रप्रयासक्षणविघ्नितः<BR> R. 12. 53, 14. 41.<BR>—2 Labour, difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 Pleasure, delight.<BR>—3 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्त|प्रयस्तं
प्रयस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seasoned, dressed with condiments.<BR>—2 Striving, eager.<BR>—3 Scattered; वेदीं हुताशनवतीं परितः प्रयस्ताः Ś. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रया
प्रया €2 P.<BR>—1 To walk, go; त्रस्ताद्भुतं नगरदैवतवत् प्रयासि Mk. 1. 27.<BR>—2 To walk on, set out.<BR>—3 To depart, go forth or out; यथा प्रयान्ति संयान्ति स्रोतोवेगेन वालुकाः<BR> Bhāg. 6. 15. 3.<BR>—4 To advance, progress; संख्यावन्तोऽपि भूम्ना परकृतिषु मुदं संप्रधार्य<BR> प्रयान्तु Mv. 7. 42.<BR>—5 To enter, undergo, incur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणम्
प्रयाणम्<BR>—1 Setting out, starting, departure.<BR>—2 A march, journey; मार्गं तावच्छृणु कथयतस्त्वत्प्रयाणानुरूपम्<BR> Me. 13; Mb. 7. 166. 1.<BR>—3 Progress, advance.<BR>—4 The march (of an enemy), an attack, invasion, expedition; कामं पुरः<BR> शुक्रमिव प्रयाणे Ku. 3. 43; R. 6. 33; प्रयाणपटहध्वनिं प्रथयति<BR> स्म ताराध्वनि Rāmāyaṇachampū.<BR>—5 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—6 Death, departure (from the world); प्रयाणकालेऽपि च मां ते विदुर्युक्तचेतसः Bg. 7. 30.<BR>—7 The back of a horse; Mb. 3. 71. 16.<BR>—8 The hinder part of any animal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयाणकालः, प्रयाणसमयः, प्रयाणभङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणकालः|प्रयाणकाल
प्रयाणम् + -कालः, -समयः time of departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणसमयः
प्रयाणम् + -कालः, -समयः time of departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणभङ्गः|प्रयाणभङ्ग|प्रयाणभंग
प्रयाणम् + -भङ्गः a break in a journey, halt; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणकम्
प्रयाणकम्<BR>—1 A journey, march; तेनैव क्रमेणानवरतप्रयाणकैः K. 118, 305.<BR>—2 Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयात|प्रयातः
प्रयात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Advanced, gone forth, departed.<BR>—2 Deceased, dead; तत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः Bg. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयातः|प्रयात
प्रयात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 An invasion.<BR>—2 A precipice, steep rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयातम्
प्रयात + .{@-तम्@} Going, gait; जितकलहंसवधूगति प्रयातम् Ki. 10. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापनम्
प्रयापनम् (-णम्)<BR>—1 Sending.<BR>—2 Expelling, driving away; cf. P. VIII. 4. 30 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापणम्
प्रयापनम् (-णम्)<BR>—1 Sending.<BR>—2 Expelling, driving away; cf. P. VIII. 4. 30 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापित
प्रयापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Made to advance or go forward.<BR>—2 Made to go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयागः|प्रयाग
प्रयागः<BR>—1 A sacrifice.<BR>—2 N. of Indra.<BR>—3 A horse.<BR>—4 N. of a celebrated place of pilgrimage at the confluence of the Gaṅgā<BR> and Yamunā near the modern Allahabad; प्रत्यगेव प्रयागाच्च मध्यदेशः<BR> प्रकीर्तितः Ms. 2. 21; (said to be <i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयागभयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयागभयः|प्रयागभय
प्रयागः + -भयः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाचनम्
प्रयाचनम् Begging, requesting, imploring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाजः|प्रयाज
प्रयाजः A principal sacrificial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To use, employ; अयमपि च गिरं नस्त्वत् प्रबोधयुक्ताम् R. 5. 74;<BR> सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते Bg. 17. 26.<BR>—2 To appoint, employ, direct, order; मा मां प्रयुक्थाः कुलकीर्तिलेपे<BR> Bk. 3. 54; प्रायुङ्क्त राज्ये बत दुष्करे त्वाम् 3. 51; Ku. 7. 85.<BR>—3 To give, bestow, confer; आशिषं प्रयुयुजे न वाहिनीम् R. 11. 6, 2. 70, 5. 35, 15. 8.<BR>—4 To move, set in motion; मरुत्प्रयुक्ताः (बाललताः) R. 2. 10.<BR>—5 To excite, urge, prompt, drive on; अथावमानेन पितुः प्रयुक्ता Ku. 1. 21;<BR> अथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः Bg. 3. 36.<BR>—6 To perform, do; प्रयुक्तपाणिग्रहणोपचारौ Ku. 7. 86, 17. 12.<BR>—7 To represent on the stage, act, perform; उत्तरं रामचरितं तत्प्रणीतं<BR> प्रयोक्ष्यते U. 1. 2; Ku. 5. 35; परिषदि प्रयुञ्जानस्य मम Mu. 1.<BR>—8 To lend for use, put to interest (as money &c.); धेनुरुष्ट्रो वहन्नश्वो<BR> यश्च दम्यः प्रयुज्यते Ms. 8. 146.<BR>—9 To harness, yoke.<BR>—10 To appoint, invest, instal (in an office).<BR>—11 To cast, hurl, throw (as a missile); direct; प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रमितो<BR> वृथा स्यात् R. 2. 34<BR>—12 To be fit, become.<BR>—13 To impose, inflict (with loc. or gen. of person). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To use, employ; भोजयेत् सह भृत्यैस्तावानृशंस्यं प्रयोजयन् Ms. 3. 112.<BR>—2 To exact (as interest).<BR>—3 To perform, practise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्त|प्रयुक्तं
प्रयुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Yoked, harnessed.<BR>—2 Used, employed (as a word &c.); सप्रयुक्तस्य दम्भस्य ब्रह्माप्यन्तं<BR> न गच्छति Pt. 1. 202.<BR>—3 Applied.<BR>—4 Appointed, nominated.<BR>—5 Acted, represented.<BR>—6 Arising or resulting from, produced by, consequent on; मेधाविनो नीतिगुणप्रयुक्तां<BR> पुरः स्फुरन्तीमिव दर्शयन्ति Pt. 1. 61.<BR>—7 Endowed with.<BR>—8 Lost in meditation, abstracted.<BR>—9 Lent or put to interest (as money).<BR>—10 Prompted, instigated, urged; गुणप्रयुक्ताः परमर्मभेदिनः Udb.;<BR> अथावमानेन प्रयुक्ता Ku. 1. 21.<BR>—11 Directed, hurled at.<BR>—12 Shaken, set in motion.<BR>—13 Inflicted upon.<BR>—14 Connected with.<BR>—15 Thick, compact, closely united.<BR>—16 Drawn (as a sword).<BR>—17 Contrived.<BR>—18 Suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्तम्
प्रयुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} A cause.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयुक्तसंस्कार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्तसंस्कार
प्रयुक्त + -संस्कार <i>a.</i> polished (as a gem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्तिः|प्रयुक्ति
प्रयुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Use, employment, application.<BR>—2 Incitement, instigation.<BR>—3 Motive, main object or end, occasion.<BR>—4 Consequence, result.<BR>—5 Activity, effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Impulse, motive, cause.<BR>—2 Acquisition, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तृ
प्रयोक्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who uses or employs (as a means, word &c.).<BR>—2 One who performs or directs, an executor.<BR>—3 One who prompts or instigates, an instigator.<BR>—4 An author, an agent; स च कुलपतिराद्यश्छन्दसां यः प्रयोक्ता U. 3. 48.<BR>—5 One who acts or represents (a drama).<BR>—6 One who lends money at interest, a money-lender.<BR>—7 One who shoots (an arrow).<BR>—8 The agent of an action.<BR>—9 A reciter.<BR>—10 A procurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1104-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्त्रम्
प्रयोक्त्रम् Harness; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगः|प्रयोग
प्रयोगः<BR>—1 Use, application, employment; as in शब्दप्रयोगः, अयं शब्दो भूरिप्रयोगः<BR> -अल्पप्रयोगः ‘this word is generally or rarely used’.<BR>—2 A usual form, general usage.<BR>—3 Hurling, throwing, discharging, (opp. संहारः); प्रयोगसंहारविभक्तमन्त्रम् R. 5. 57.<BR>—4 Exhibition, performance, representation (dramatic), acting; देव<BR> प्रयोगप्रधानं हि नाट्यशास्त्रम् M. 1; नाटिका न प्रयोगतो दृष्टा Ratn. 1<BR> ‘not seen acted on the stage’; आ परितोषाद्विदुषां न साधु मन्ये प्रयोगविज्ञानम् Ś. 1. 2.<BR>—5 Practice, experimental portion (of a subject); (opp. शास्त्र ‘theory’);<BR> तदत्रभवानिमं मां च शास्त्रे प्रयोगे च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>—6 Course of procedure, ceremonial form.<BR>—7 An act, action.<BR>—8 Recitation, delivery.<BR>—9 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—10 A plan, contrivance, device, scheme.<BR>—11 A means, instrument; नयप्रयोगाविव गां जिगीषोः Ki. 17. 38.<BR>—12 Consequence, result.<BR>—13 Combination, connection.<BR>—14 Addition.<BR>—15 (In gram.) A usual form.<BR>—16 Offering, presenting.<BR>—17<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Principal, loan bearing interest.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Lending money on usury; प्रतिबन्धः प्रयोगो व्यवहारोऽवस्तारः<BR> … … कोशक्षयः Kau. A. 2. 7. 26; also कोशद्रव्याणां वृद्धिप्रयोगः<BR>—18 Appointment.<BR>—19 A sacred text or authority. A text which brings together the various<BR> धर्मs of a विकृति. A प्रयोगवचन, however, does this only<BR> when धर्मs are made available by the चोदक which, therefore,<BR> is said to be the stronger of the two. चोदको हि प्रयोगवचनाद् बलवत्तरः ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 8.<BR>—20 A cause; motive.<BR>—21 An example.<BR>—22 Application of magic, magical rites.<BR>—23 A horse.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रयोगातिशयः, प्रयोगार्थः, प्रयोगग्रहणम्, प्रयोगचतुर, प्रयोगनिपुण, प्रयोगवीर्यम्, प्रयोगशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगातिशयः|प्रयोगातिशय
प्रयोगः + -अतिशयः One of the five kinds of प्रस्तावना or prologue,<BR> in which a part or performance is superseded by another in such a manner<BR> that a character is suddenly brought on the stage; <i>i. e.</i> where the<BR> Sūtradhāra goes out hinting the entrance of a character and thus performs<BR> a part superseding that which he has apparently intended for his own,<BR> <i>viz.</i> dancing; the S. D. thus defines it:− यदि प्रयोग एकस्मिन् प्रयोगोऽन्यः<BR> प्रयुज्यते । तेन पात्रप्रवेशश्चेत् प्रयोगातिशयस्तदा ॥ 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगार्थः|प्रयोगार्थ
प्रयोगः + -अर्थः (= प्रत्युत्कमः q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगग्रहणम्
प्रयोगः + -ग्रहणम् acquirement of practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगचतुर
प्रयोगः + -चतुर, -निपुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 skilled in practice; M. 3; चतुःषष्टिकलागमप्रयोगचतुरः Dk. 2. 5.<BR>—2 practically experienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगनिपुण
प्रयोगः + -चतुर, -निपुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 skilled in practice; M. 3; चतुःषष्टिकलागमप्रयोगचतुरः Dk. 2. 5.<BR>—2 practically experienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगवीर्यम्
प्रयोगः + -वीर्यम् (with Buddhists) energy in practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगशास्त्रम्
प्रयोगः + -शास्त्रम् the कल्पसूत्र, which lays down the प्रयोग of<BR> various sacrificial acts; प्रयोगशास्त्रमिति चेत् MS. 1. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगतः
प्रयोगतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 By the use of, through the employment of.<BR>—2 In consequence of.<BR>—3 According to.<BR>—4 In action, actually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगिन्
प्रयोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Using, employing.<BR>—2 Having an object in view.<BR>—3 Prompting, stimulating. ━<i>m.</i> Performer (rituals &c.); तत्र कर्मणि<BR> विपर्यणीनमन् मन्त्रमूहकुशलाः प्रयोगिणः Śi. 14. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोग्यः|प्रयोग्य
प्रयोग्यः A horse or any animal harnessed to a carriage, draught animal; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजक|प्रयोजकः
प्रयोजक <i>a.</i> Occasioning, causing, effecting, leading to, inciting,<BR> stimulating, deputing, appointing &c.; यस्मिन् कृते यन्निष्पद्यते प्रयोजनवत्<BR> तत् तस्य प्रयोजकमिति गम्यते । ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 22; तत्प्रयोजको<BR> हेतुश्च Pāṇini S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजकः|प्रयोजक
प्रयोजक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An employer, one who uses or employs.<BR>—2 An author.<BR>—3 A founder, an institutor.<BR>—4 A money-lender.<BR>—5 A law-giver, legislator.<BR>—6 An instigator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनम्
प्रयोजनम्<BR>—1 Use, employment, application.<BR>—2 Use, need, necessity (with instr. of that which is needed and gen.<BR> of the user); सर्वैरपि राज्ञां प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1; बाले किमनेन पृष्टेन<BR> प्रयोजनम् K. 144.<BR>—3 End, aim, object, purpose; प्रयोजनमनुद्दिश्य न मन्दोऽपि प्रवर्तते;<BR> पुत्रप्रयोजना दाराः पुत्रः पिण्डप्रयोजनः । हितप्रयोजनं मित्रं धनं<BR> सर्वप्रयोजनम् ॥ Subhāṣ; गुणवत्तापि परप्रयोजना R. 8. 31.<BR>—4 A means of attaining; एतच्चतुर्विधं विद्यात् पुरुषार्थप्रयोजनम् Ms. 7. 100.<BR>—5 A cause, motive, occasion; दुरधिगमा हि गतिः प्रयोजनानाम् Ki. 10. 40.<BR>—6 Profit, interest.<BR>—7 The signification, sense (of a word); नासमवायात् प्रयोजनेन स्यात् MS. 4. 3. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनवत्|प्रयोजनवन्त्
प्रयोजनवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having or done with a particular object.<BR>—2 Selfish.<BR>—3 Useful, serviceable.<BR>—4 Caused, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्य|प्रयोज्यं|प्रयोज्यः
प्रयोज्य <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be used or employed.<BR>—2 To be practised.<BR>—3 To be produced or caused.<BR>—4 To be appointed.<BR>—5 To be thrown or discharged (as a missile).<BR>—6 To be set to work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्यः|प्रयोज्य|प्रयोज्यं
प्रयोज्य + .{@-ज्यः@} A servant, an employee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्यम्
प्रयोज्य + .{@-ज्यम्@} Capital, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत|प्रयुतं
प्रयुत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Joined, united.<BR>—2 Separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुतम्
प्रयुत + .{@-तम्@} A million; लक्षप्रयुतकोटयः Līlā.; बहूनीह सह<BR> णि प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च Mb. 1. 35. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत्सुः|प्रयुत्सु
प्रयुत्सुः<BR>—1 A warrior.<BR>—2 A ram.<BR>—3 Wind, air.<BR>—4 An ascetic.<BR>—5 N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्धम्
प्रयुद्धम् A battle, fight. ━<i>a.</i> Fighting violently; Rām. 4. 16. 25;<BR> निर्मर्यादं प्रयुद्धानि Mb. 6. 46. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुवनम्
प्रयुवनम् Stirring, mingling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररक्षणम्
प्ररक्षणम् Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुच्
प्ररुच् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine very much.<BR>—2 To be liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोचन
प्ररोचन <i>a.</i> Exciting or enticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोचनम्
प्ररोचन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Exciting, or stimulating.<BR>—2 Illustration, explanation.<BR>—3 Seduction.<BR>—4 Exhibition (of a person) for being seen and liked (by the people);<BR> अलोकसामान्यगुणस्तनूजः प्ररोचनार्थं प्रकटीकृतश्च Māl. 1. 10 (where<BR> Jagaddhara interprets प्ररोचनार्थम् by प्रवृत्तिपाटवार्थम् ‘in order to be thoroughly acquainted with the world’<BR>).<BR>—5 Favourable description of that which is to follow in a play.<BR>—6 Representation of the end as all but accomplished; see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">Page1106-1</a>]<BR> S. D. 388 (प्ररोचना also in the last two senses; प्ररोचना तु विज्ञेया<BR> संहारार्थप्रदर्शिनी S. D. 396).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1105-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुदित
प्ररुदित <i>p. p.</i> Crying bitterly, weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुह्
प्ररुह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To grow, rise, shoot forth; न पर्वताग्रे नलिनी प्ररोहति Mk. 4. 17.<BR>—2 To heal up (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुह्
प्ररुह् <i>f.</i> Ved. A shoot, branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढ|प्ररूढः
प्ररूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Full-grown, developed.<BR>—2 Born, sprung, produced; यस्यायमङ्गात् कृतिनः प्ररूढः Ś. 7. 19.<BR>—3 Increased.<BR>—4 Gone deep, rooted; as in प्ररूढमूल.<BR>—5 Grown long; as in प्ररूढकेश, प्ररूढश्मश्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढिः|प्ररूढि
प्ररूढिः <i>f.</i> Growth, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहः|प्ररोह
प्ररोहः<BR>—1 Sprouting, shooting or growing up, germination; as in यवाङ्कुरप्ररोहः.<BR>—2 A bud, sprout, shoot (fig. also); प्लक्षप्ररोह इव सौधतलं बिभेद<BR> R. 8. 93; प्लक्षान् प्ररोहजटिलानिव मन्त्रिवृद्धान् 13. 71; Ku. 5. 60, 7. 17;<BR> U. 5. 3.<BR>—3 A scion, offspring; हा राधेयकुलप्ररोह Ve. 4; Mv. 6. 25; नन्दवंशप्ररोहः Mu. 1. 11.<BR>—4 A shoot of light; कुर्वन्ति सामन्तशिखामणीनां प्रभाप्ररोहास्तमयं<BR> रजांसि R. 6. 33.<BR>—5 A new leaf or branch, twig, spray.<BR>—8 An excrescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहणम्
प्ररोहणम्<BR>—1 Growing, shooting forth, germination.<BR>—2 Budding, sprouting.<BR>—3 A twig, sprout, shoot, spray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहिन्
प्ररोहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shooting up.<BR>—2 Growing, propagated; उद्भिज्जाः स्थावराः सर्वे बीजकाण्डप्ररोहिणः Ms. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलघु
प्रलघु <i>a.</i> Very small, inconsiderable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलप्
प्रलप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To speak, talk; वचो वै देहीति (वैदेहीति) प्रतिपदमुदश्रु<BR> प्रलपितम् S. D. 6.<BR>—2 To talk at random or incoherently, prate, chatter, talk wildly or nonsensically;<BR> प्रलपत्येष वैधेयः Ś. 2.<BR>—3 To lament, mourn, cry, bewail.<BR>—4 To call, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपनम्
प्रलपनम्<BR>—1 Talking, speaking, talk, words, conversation.<BR>—2 Prating, prattle, raving, incoherent or nonsensical talk; इदं कस्यापि प्रलपितम्.<BR>—3 Lamentation, wailing; U. 3. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपित|प्रलपितः
प्रलपित <i>p. p.</i> Talked, prated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपितम्
प्रलपित + .{@-तम्@} Talk; वचो वैदेहीति प्रतिपदमुदश्रु प्रलपितम्; see<BR> प्रलपन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापः|प्रलाप
प्रलापः<BR>—1 Talk, conversation, discourse.<BR>—2 Prating, prattling, an incoherent or nonsensical talk; Ms. 12. 6.<BR>—3 An unjustified statement, non-sensical statement; न शक्यं नित्येनोपकर्तुम् ।<BR> तेन नित्यमुपकुर्यादिति वचमं प्रलापः एव ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 12.<BR>—4 Lamentation, wailing; उत्तराप्रालापोपजनितकृपो भगवान् वासुदेवः<BR> K. 175; Ve. 5. 30; U. 3. 29; Rām. 1. 3. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रलापहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापहन्
प्रलापः + -हन् <i>m.</i> a sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापनम्
प्रलापनम् Causing or teaching to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिता
प्रलापिता Amorous conversation or prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिन्
प्रलापिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Talking, speaking; हा असंबद्धप्रलापिन् Ve. 3.<BR>—2 Prating, prattling.<BR>—3 (Fever) Attended with delirium; Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलभ्
प्रलभ् €1 Ā. To cheat, deceive; cf. विप्रलभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्भः|प्रलम्भ|प्रलंभ|प्रलंभः
प्रलम्भः<BR>—1 Obtaining, gaining, attaining.<BR>—2 Deceiving, imposing upon, cheating, overreaching; (न्यवेदयत्)<BR> प्रलम्भमात्मनश्चैव शूद्रायाः पुत्रजन्म च Mb. 1. 106. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्भनम्
प्रलम्भनम्<BR>—1 Deceiving, cheating.<BR>—2 Wonderful and delusive contrivances; परघातप्रयोगः; प्रलम्भनम् … … चतुर्दशमधिकरणम्<BR> Kau. A. 1. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Jest, joke; यन्नाम श्रुतमनुकीर्तयेदकस्मादार्तो वा यदि पतितः<BR> प्रलम्भनाद् वा Bhāg. 5. 25. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलब्ध
प्रलब्ध <i>p. p.</i> Deceived, cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्ब|प्रलंब|प्रलम्बः
प्रलम्ब <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pendulous, hanging down; as in प्रलम्बकेश.<BR>—2 Prominent; as in प्रलम्बनासिकः.<BR>—3 Slow, dilatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बः|प्रलम्ब|प्रलंब
प्रलम्ब + .{@-म्बः@}<BR>—1 Hanging on or from, depending.<BR>—2 Anything hanging down.<BR>—3 A branch.<BR>—4 A garland worn round the neck.<BR>—5 A kind of necklace.<BR>—6 The female breast.<BR>—7 Tin or lead.<BR>—8 N. of a demon killed by Balarāma.<BR>—9 A shoot of the vine-palm.<BR>—10 A cucumber.<BR>—11 A verse (गाथा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रलम्बाण्डः, प्रलम्बघ्नः, प्रलम्बमथनः, प्रलम्बहन्, प्रलम्बबाहु, प्रलम्बभुज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बाण्डः|प्रलम्बाण्ड|प्रलंबांड
प्रलम्ब + -अण्डः a man with hanging testicles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बघ्नः|प्रलम्बघ्न|प्रलंबघ्न
प्रलम्ब + -घ्नः, -मथनः, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बमथनः|प्रलम्बमथन|प्रलंबमथन
प्रलम्ब + -घ्नः, -मथनः, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बहन्|प्रलंबहन्
प्रलम्ब + -घ्नः, -मथनः, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बबाहु
प्रलम्ब + -बाहु, -भुज <i>a.</i> One whose arms hang down; Mb. 3. 284. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बभुज
प्रलम्ब + -बाहु, -भुज <i>a.</i> One whose arms hang down; Mb. 3. 284. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बनम्
प्रलम्बनम् Hanging down, depending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बित|प्रलंबित|प्रलम्बितः
प्रलम्बित <i>a.</i> Pendulous, hanging down, suspended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बीकृ|प्रलंबीकृ
प्रलम्बीकृ €8 U. To cause to hang down, suspend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रललाट
प्रललाट <i>a.</i> Having a prominent forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलवः|प्रलव
प्रलवः<BR>—1 A fragment, chip, bit.<BR>—2 The sheath of a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलवित्रम्
प्रलवित्रम् An instrument for cutting off; P. VI. 2. 144 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रली
प्रली €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To become dissolved, melt away.<BR>—2 To be a absorbed or dissolved in, be resolved into; आत्मना कृतिना<BR> च त्वमात्मन्येव प्रलीयसे Ku. 2. 10; रात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके<BR> Bg. 8. 18; Ms. 1. 54.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear; सह मेघेन तडित् प्रलीयते Ku. 4. 33.<BR>—4 To be destroyed, to perish, die; जीवलोकतिलकः प्रलीयते Māl. 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयः|प्रलय
प्रलयः<BR>—1 Destruction, annihilation, dissolution; स्थानानि किं हिमवतः प्रलयं<BR> गतानि Bh. 3. 70, 69; प्रलयं नीत्वा Śi. 11. 66 ‘causing to disappear’.<BR>—2 The destruction of the whole universe (at the end of a <i>kalpa</i>),<BR> universal destruction; Ku. 2. 8; अहं कृत्स्नस्य जगतः प्रभवः प्रलयस्तथा Bg. 7. 6.<BR>—3 Any extensive destruction or devastation.<BR>—4 Death, dying, destruction; प्रारब्धाः प्रलयाय मांसवदहो विक्रेतुमेते<BR> वयम् Mu. 5. 21, 1. 14; यदा सत्त्वे प्रवृद्धे तु प्रलयं याति देहभृत् Bg. 14. 14.<BR>—5 Swoon, fainting, loss of consciousness, syncope; प्रलयान्तोन्मिषिते<BR> विलोचने Ku. 4. 2.<BR>—6 (In Rhet.) Loss of consciousness, considered as one of the 33 subordinate<BR> feelings; प्रलयः सुखदुःखाद्यैर्गाढमिन्द्रियमूर्छनम् Pratāparudra.<BR>—7 The mystic syllable <i>om</i>.<BR>—8 Spiritual unification (लय); बुद्धिः कर्मगुणैहींना यदा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">Page1107-1</a>]<BR> मनसि वर्तते । तदा संपद्यते ब्रह्म तत्रैव प्रलयं गतम् ॥<BR> Mb. 12. 204. 17.<BR>—9 Sleepiness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रलयकालः, प्रलयघनः, प्रलयजलधरः, प्रलयदहनः, प्रलयपयोधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1106-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयकालः|प्रलयकाल
प्रलयः + -कालः the time of universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयघनः|प्रलयघन
प्रलयः + -घनः, -जलधरः a cloud at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयजलधरः|प्रलयजलधर
प्रलयः + -घनः, -जलधरः a cloud at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयदहनः|प्रलयदहन
प्रलयः + -दहनः the fire at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयपयोधिः|प्रलयपयोधि
प्रलयः + -पयोधिः the ocean at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीन
प्रलीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Melted, dissolved; तथा प्रलीनस्तमसि मूढयोनिषु जायते Bg. 14. 15.<BR>—2 Annihilated, destroyed.<BR>—3 Insensible, unconscious.<BR>—4 Concealed; hidden; इति प्रलीनां नलिनीवने सखीं विदांबभूवुः सुचिरेण<BR> योषितः Ki. 8. 36.<BR>—5 Lost, died.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुठ्
प्रलुठ् €1 P.<BR>—1 To roll along the ground, roll, wallow; प्रलुठितमवनौ विलोक्य कृत्तम् Bk. 5. 108.<BR>—2 To be agitated, heave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठनम्
प्रलोठनम्<BR>—1 Rolling (on the ground).<BR>—2 Heaving, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुप्त
प्रलुप्त <i>p. p.</i> Robbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुभ्
प्रलुभ् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be greedy or desirous, be lustful.<BR>—2 To allure, seduce, entice.<BR>—3 To pollute (through lust). ━<i>Caus.</i> To allure, attract, entice, seduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुब्ध
प्रलुब्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who deceives (वञ्चक); तं निहत्य प्रलुब्धोऽयं शिखण्डी<BR> पूर्णमानसः Mb. 7. 150. 13.<BR>—2 Seduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुब्धा
प्रलुब्ध + .{@-ब्धा@} One who has conceived an illicit affection for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभः|प्रलोभ
प्रलोभः<BR>—1 Cupidity, greediness, covetousness.<BR>—2 Allurement, seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभनम्
प्रलोभनम्<BR>—1 Attracting.<BR>—2 An allurement, seduction, temptation.<BR>—3 A lure, bait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभनी
प्रलोभनी Sand, gravel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभिन्
प्रलोभिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Greedy of, lusting after.<BR>—2 Alluring, enticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभ्य
प्रलोभ्य <i>a.</i> To be desired or coveted, attractive, alluring; प्रलोभ्य<BR> वस्तुप्रणयप्रसारितः Ś. 7. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलून
प्रलून <i>p. p.</i> Cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपः|प्रलेप
प्रलेपः<BR>—1 An unguent, an ointment, a salve; आलिम्पन्नमृतमयैरिव प्रलेपैः U. 3. 39.<BR>—2 Plaster.<BR>—3 A hectic or slow fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपक|प्रलेपकः
प्रलेपक <i>a.</i> Anointing, smearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपकः|प्रलेपक
प्रलेपक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An anointer, a plasterer.<BR>—2 A kind of slow fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेहः|प्रलेह
प्रलेहः A kind of broth; ‘सूरणादिदव्ययुक्त आद्रकादिसंस्कृततक्रादिनिर्मितो द्रवद्रव्यविशेषः’; N. 16. 86 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोपः|प्रलोप
प्रलोपः Destruction, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोल
प्रलोल <i>a.</i> Greatly agitated or tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवच्
प्रवच् €2 P.<BR>—1 To speak, say, address.<BR>—2 To tell, relate, announce.<BR>—3 To explain.<BR>—4 To recite.<BR>—5 To celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तव्य
प्रवक्तव्य <i>a.</i> To be announced, taught, explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तृ
प्रवक्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who declares or relates, a speaker, declarer.<BR>—2 A teacher, expounder; धर्मप्रवक्ता नृपतेर्न तु शूद्रः कथंचन<BR> Ms. 8. 20; Pt. 3. 73.<BR>—3 An orator, eloquent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनम्
प्रवचनम्<BR>—1 Speaking, declaration, announcement; प्रवचने मान्द्यम् Pt. 1. 190.<BR>—2 Teaching, expounding.<BR>—3 Exposition, explanation, interpretation; नायमात्मा प्रवचनेन लभ्यो<BR> न भेधया न बहुना श्रुतेन Kaṭh. 1. 2. 22; लब्ध्वा ज्ञानमनेकधा<BR> प्रवचनैर्मन्वादयः प्राणयन् Mv. 4. 25; Bhāg. 7. 15. 1.<BR>—4 Eloquence.<BR>—5 A sacred treatise or writing; Ms. 3. 184.<BR>—6 An expression, a term.<BR>—7 A system of doctrines (in the form of a treatise).<BR>—8 The fundamental doctrine of the Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनः|प्रवचन|प्रवचनं
प्रवचनम् + .{@-नः@} One who exposes, propounds; Bhāg. 10. 87. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवचनपटु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनपटु
प्रवचनम् + -पटु <i>a.</i> skilled in talking, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनीय|प्रवचनीयः
प्रवचनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be taught, propounded.<BR>—2 To be well spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनीयः|प्रवचनीय
प्रवचनीय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 A propounder, teacher. —2 An orator, speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवगः|प्रवग
प्रवगः, प्रवङ्गः, प्रवङ्गमः A monkey; see प्लवग,<BR> प्लवङ्ग, प्लवङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवङ्गः|प्रवङ्ग|प्रवंगः
प्रवगः, प्रवङ्गः, प्रवङ्गमः A monkey; see प्लवग,<BR> प्लवङ्ग, प्लवङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवङ्गमः|प्रवङ्गम|प्रवंगमः
प्रवगः, प्रवङ्गः, प्रवङ्गमः A monkey; see प्लवग,<BR> प्लवङ्ग, प्लवङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवटः|प्रवट
प्रवटः Wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवण|प्रवणः
प्रवण <i>a.</i> Sloping down, inclined, shelving, flowing downwards;<BR> प्रागुदक्प्रबणां वेदिं विशालां दीप्तपावकाम् (ददर्श) Rām. 2. 99. 24.<BR>—2 Steep, abrupt, precipitous.<BR>—3 Crooked, bent.<BR>—4 Inclined, disposed to, tending to (oft. at the end of comp.); भयेकप्रवणः<BR> Ki. 3. 19; श्वपचप्रवणो भवेत् Mb. 13. 136. 18.<BR>—5 Devoted or attached to, addicted to, intent on, prone to, full of;<BR> नृभिः प्राणत्राणप्रवणमतिभिः कैश्चिदधुना Bh. 3. 29; Śi. 8. 35;<BR> Mu. 5. 21; Ki. 2. 44.<BR>—6 Favourably inclined or disposed towards; Ku. 4. 42.<BR>—7 Eager, ready; प्रवणोऽस्मि वरं दातुम् Mb. 15. 29. 22. फलसंपत्प्रवणः Ki. 2. 8.<BR>—8 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>—9 Humbled, modestly humble, submissive.<BR>—10 Decayed, wasted, waning.<BR>—11 Generous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणः|प्रवण
प्रवण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A place where four roads meet.<BR>—2 A moment.<BR>—3 A whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणम्
प्रवण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 A descent, a steep descent, precipice; उदके भूरियं धार्या मर्तव्यं<BR> प्रवणे मया Mb. 5. 136. 13.<BR>—2 The side of a hill, slope, declivity.<BR>—3 The belly.<BR>—4 An access to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणता
प्रवणता<BR>—1 Slope, inclination, declivity.<BR>—2 Propensity, tendency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणायति
प्रवणायति Den. P. To feel inclined or disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणायितम्
प्रवणायितम् Inclination, propensity, bias.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणीकृ
प्रवणीकृ €8 U. To incline favourably towards, overcome, win over;<BR> तपसा तत्प्रवणीकृतो हरः Ku. 4. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्|प्रवन्त्
प्रवत् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A precipice, declivity.<BR>—2 Height, elevation.<BR>—3 A sloping path, easy passage; यथाप; प्रवतायन्ति T. Up. 1. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1107-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्स्यत्
प्रवत्स्यत् <i>a.</i> (-ती, -न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> About to go on a journey.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवत्स्यत्पतिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्स्यत्पतिका
प्रवत्स्यत् + -पतिका the wife of one who intends to go on a journey (one of<BR> the 8 Nāyikās in erotic poetry); यस्याः पतिरग्रिमक्षणे देशान्तरं<BR> यास्यत्येव सा प्रवत्स्यत्पतिका Ras. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवद्
प्रवद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To say, speak, utter.<BR>—2 To speak to, address; सुग्रीवः प्रावदन् नृपम् Bk. 7. 24.<BR>—3 To name, call.<BR>—4 To regard, consider.<BR>—5 To converse or talk with.<BR>—6 To proclaim, declare. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to speak.<BR>—2 To play on (a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवदनम्
प्रवदनम् Ved. A proclamation, announcement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादः|प्रवाद
प्रवादः<BR>—1 Uttering a word or sound.<BR>—2 Expressing, mentioning, declaring.<BR>—3 Discourse, conversation.<BR>—4 Talk, report, rumour, popular saying or belief; अनुरागप्रवादस्तु<BR> वत्सयोः सार्वलौकिकः Māl. 1. 13; व्याध्रो मानुषं खादतीति लोकप्रवादो<BR> दुर्निवारः H. 1; Ratn. 4. 15.<BR>—5 A fable or myth.<BR>—6 Litigious language.<BR>—7 Words of challenge, mutual defiance; इत्थं प्रवादं युधि संप्रहारं<BR> प्रचक्रतू रामनिशाविहारौ Bk. 2. 36.<BR>—8 A base or crude form (Ved.); (in gram.) any form or case.<BR>—9 Ill-rumour, slander, calumny; अवापुरारभ्य ततश्चला इति प्रवादमुच्चैरयशस्करं<BR> श्रियः Śi. 1. 44.<BR>—10 Pretext, excuse; शत्रुः पतिप्रवादेन … बाले परिधृतस्त्वया<BR> Rām. 2. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादक
प्रवादक <i>a.</i> Playing on (a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादिन्
प्रवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uttering a sound; speaking, reporting.<BR>—2 Being in some grammatical form or case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवप्
प्रवप् €1 U.<BR>—1 To throw, cast, offer; प्रबपाणि शिरौ भूमौ वानरस्य वनाच्छिदः Bk. 9. 98.<BR>—2 To scatter, strew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवप
प्रवप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very fat.<BR>—2 Having a thick membrane or omentum; P. VIII. 4. 16 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवपणम्
प्रवपणम् Ved.<BR>—1 Scattering forth.<BR>—2 Shaving or shearing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवापिन्
प्रवापिन् <i>a.</i> Scattering, sowing; तथैवाक्षेत्रिणो बीजं परक्षेत्रप्रवापिणः Ms. 9. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयणम्
प्रवयणम्<BR>—1 The upper part of a piece of woven cloth.<BR>—2 A goad, a whip; स्वयमादित प्रवयणं प्रजापतिः Śi. 13. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयस्
प्रवयस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Advanced in age, aged, old; केप्येते प्रवयसस्त्वां दिदृक्षवः U. 4; R. 8. 18.<BR>—2 Ancient, old.<BR>—3 Strong, vigorous (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर|प्रवरं|प्रवरः
प्रवर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Chief, principal, most excellent or distinguished, best, exalted; भीष्मः<BR> कुरूणां प्रवरः Mb. 3. 85. 116; संकेतके चिरयति प्रबरो विनोदः<BR> Mk. 3. 3; Ms. 10. 27; Ghaṭ. 16.<BR>—2 Eldest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरः|प्रवर|प्रवरं
प्रवर + .{@-रः@} A call, summons.<BR>—2 A particular invocation addressed to Agni by a Brāhmaṇa at the consecration of his fire.<BR>—3 A line of ancestors.<BR>—4 A race, family, lineage.<BR>—5 An ancestor.<BR>—6 A Muni or noble ancestor who contributes to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">Page1108-2</a>]<BR> credit of a particular <i>gotra</i> or family; said to be the friend of Indra;<BR> पुरश्चकार प्रवरं वरं यमायन् सखायं ददर्श तया सः N. 14. 62;<BR> cf. पञ्च˚, त्रि˚.<BR>—7 Offspring, descendants.<BR>—8 A cover, covering.<BR>—9 An upper garment.<BR>—10 One of the 42 Gotras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरा
प्रवर + .{@-रा@} N. of a river falling into the Godāvarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरम्
प्रवर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Aloe-wood<BR>—2 A particular high number; Buddh.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवरकल्याण, प्रवरजनः, प्रवरधातुः, प्रवरललितम्, प्रवरवाहनौ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरकल्याण
प्रवर + -कल्याण <i>a.</i> eminently beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरजनः|प्रवरजन
प्रवर + -जनः a person of quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरधातुः|प्रवरधातु
प्रवर + -धातुः precious metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरललितम्
प्रवर + -ललितम् N. of a metre with each line of sixteen syllables; V. Ratn.<BR> See appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरवाहनौ
प्रवर + -वाहनौ (du.) an epithet of the two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरणम्
प्रवरणम्<BR>—1 Call, summons &c.<BR>—2 (With Buddhists) Festivities at the end of the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्गः|प्रवर्ग
प्रवर्गः<BR>—1 The sacrificial fire.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग्यः|प्रवर्ग्य
प्रवर्ग्यः A ceremony preliminary to the Soma sacrifice; प्रबग्र्यं<BR> शास्त्रतः कृत्वा Rām. 1. 14. 4; Bhāg. 3. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्जनम्
प्रवर्जनम् The performance of the प्रवर्ग्य ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवलाकिन्
प्रवलाकिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A peacock.<BR>—2 A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवल्ग्
प्रवल्ग् €1 P., Ā. To move the limbs quickly, bound, leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवस्
प्रवस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To live, dwell.<BR>—2 To go abroad, sojourn, be absent from home, travel; विधाय वृत्तिं<BR> भार्यायाः प्रवसेत् कार्यवान्नरः Ms. 9. 74; R. 11. 4. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To banish, send into exile; एकस्थमथ संरुध्यात् पुत्रवान् वा प्रवासयेत् Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसनम्
प्रवसनम्<BR>—1 Going or journeying abroad, going on a journey.<BR>—2 Dying disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासः|प्रवास
प्रवासः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Going or journeying abroad, being absent from oneʼs home, foreign<BR> residence; कुशः प्रवासस्थकलत्रवेषाम् (वनितामपश्यत्) R. 16. 4;<BR> Ś. 4. 3; U. 6. 38; स्नेहः प्रवासाश्रयात् Pt. 1. 169; Bh. 3. 94.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A temporary sojourn; प्रवासादुपावृत्तेन काश्यपेनादिष्टोऽस्मि Ś. 4.<BR>—2 (In astr.) Heliacal setting of the planets.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवासगत, प्रवासस्थ, प्रवासस्थित, प्रवासपर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासगत
प्रवासः + -गत, -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> journeying abroad, being absent from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासस्थ
प्रवासः + -गत, -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> journeying abroad, being absent from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासस्थित
प्रवासः + -गत, -स्थ, -स्थित <i>a.</i> journeying abroad, being absent from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासपर
प्रवासः + -पर <i>a.</i> addicted to living abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासनम्
प्रवासनम्<BR>—1 Living abroad, temporary sojourn.<BR>—2 Exile, banishment; सीताविवासनपटोः करुणा कुतस्ते U. 2. 10.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—4 Going from a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासित
प्रवासित <i>a.</i> Banished, exiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासिन्
प्रवासिन् <i>m.</i> A traveller, wayfarer, sojourner; परलोकनवप्रवासिनः<BR> प्रतिपत्स्ये पदवीमहं तव Ku. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवास्य
प्रवास्य <i>a.</i> To be sent abroad, banished; Ms. 8. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्
प्रवह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bear, carry, draw along.<BR>—2 To waft, carry or bear along; प्रवहन्तं सदामोदम् Bk. 8. 52.<BR>—3 To support, bear up (as a burden).<BR>—4 To flow, stream forth.<BR>—5 To blow.<BR>—6 To have, possess, feel.<BR>—7 To breathe.<BR>—8 To exhibit, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1108-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहः|प्रवह
प्रवहः<BR>—1 Flowing or streaming forth.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 N. of one of the seven courses of wind (said to cause the motion of<BR> the planets); प्राणापानौ समानं च व्यानोदानौ च तत्त्वतः । अधश्चैवानिलं<BR> ज्ञात्वा प्रवहं चानिलं पुनः ॥ सप्त वातांस्तथा ज्ञात्वा Mb. 12. 301. 27-28;<BR> एकः पिपासुः प्रवहानिलस्य N. 22. 77.<BR>—4 A reservoir into which water is carried off.<BR>—5 Going forth, going from a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहणम्
प्रवहणम्<BR>—1 A covered carriage or litter (for women); आरुह प्रवहणम् Mk. 4. 23/24.<BR>—2 A carriage, conveyance, vehicle in general.<BR>—3 A ship; प्रवहणनिमित्तमेकोऽमात्यः सर्वानमात्यानावाहयेत् Kau. A. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहणी
प्रवहणी, -निकायः Corporation of workmen; Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहनिकायः
प्रवहणी, -निकायः Corporation of workmen; Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहः|प्रवाह
प्रवाहः<BR>—1 Flowing or streaming forth.<BR>—2 A stream, course, current; प्रवाहस्ते वारां श्रियमयमपारां दिशतु<BR> नः G. L. 2; R. 5. 46, 13. 10, 48; Ku. 1. 54; Me. 48.<BR>—3 Flow, running water.<BR>—4 Continuous flow, unbroken succession, continuity.<BR>—5 Course of events (rolling onward like a stream).<BR>—6 Activity, active occupation.<BR>—7 A pond, lake.<BR>—8 Course or direction towards.<BR>—9 An excellent horse. (प्रवाहेमूत्रितम् means (lit.) making water<BR> in a stream; (fig.) doing a useless action).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहक|प्रवाहकः
प्रवाहक <i>a.</i> Carrying off or forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहकः|प्रवाहक
प्रवाहक + .{@-कः@} A goblin, an imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहनम्
प्रवाहनम्<BR>—1 Driving forth.<BR>—2 Evacuation by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहणी
प्रवाहणी The sphincter muscle which ejects the faeces from the rectum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहिका
प्रवाहिका Diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहिन्
प्रवाहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Carrying forward, driving onward.<BR>—2 Carrying away.<BR>—3 Flowing, streaming forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाही
प्रवाही Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिः|प्रवह्लि
प्रवह्लिः, -ह्ली (also -ह्लिका and -ह्लीका)<BR> See प्रहेलिका. A riddle, enigma; विदग्धबालेङ्गितगुप्तिचातुरीप्रवह्लिकोत्पाटनपाटवे हृदः N. 16. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्ली
प्रवह्लिः, -ह्ली (also -ह्लिका and -ह्लीका)<BR> See प्रहेलिका. A riddle, enigma; विदग्धबालेङ्गितगुप्तिचातुरीप्रवह्लिकोत्पाटनपाटवे हृदः N. 16. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिका
प्रवह्लिः, -ह्ली (also -ह्लिका and -ह्लीका)<BR> See प्रहेलिका. A riddle, enigma; विदग्धबालेङ्गितगुप्तिचातुरीप्रवह्लिकोत्पाटनपाटवे हृदः N. 16. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लीका
प्रवह्लिः, -ह्ली (also -ह्लिका and -ह्लीका)<BR> See प्रहेलिका. A riddle, enigma; विदग्धबालेङ्गितगुप्तिचातुरीप्रवह्लिकोत्पाटनपाटवे हृदः N. 16. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाकः|प्रवाक
प्रवाकः A proclaimer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्
प्रवाच् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eloquent, oratorical; (कुर्वते) जडानप्यनुलोमार्थान् प्रवाचः<BR> कृतिनां गिरः Śi. 2. 25.<BR>—2 Talkative, garrulous; प्रवाचः कार्पण्यात् Mu. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचक|प्रवाचकः
प्रवाचक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Explanatory.<BR>—2 Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचनम्
प्रवाचनम्<BR>—1 Proclamation, promulgation, declaration.<BR>—2 A designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्यम्
प्रवाच्यम् A literary production or composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणम्
प्रवाणम् The trimming or edging of a piece of woven cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणिः|प्रवाणि
प्रवाणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> A weaverʼs shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणी
प्रवाणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> A weaverʼs shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवात
प्रवात <i>p. p.</i> Exposed to stormy wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवातम्
प्रवात + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A current of air, fresh or free air; प्रवातशयनस्था देवी M. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">Page1109-2</a>]<BR>—2 A strong or stormy wind; ननु प्रवातेऽपि निष्कम्पा गिरयः Ś. 6.<BR>—3 An airy place; प्रवातनीलोत्पलनिर्विशेषम् Ku. 1. 46.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवातशयनम्, प्रवातसुभग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवातशयनम्
प्रवात + -शयनम् a bed placed in the airy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवातसुभग
प्रवात + -सुभग <i>a.</i> delightful by a fresh breeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारः|प्रवार
प्रवारः, प्रवारकः A cover, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारकः|प्रवारक
प्रवारः, प्रवारकः A cover, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारणम्
प्रवारणम्<BR>—1 Satisfying (a desire).<BR>—2 Priority of choice.<BR>—3 Prohibition, opposition.<BR>—4 A free-will offering (काम्यदान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाल|प्रवालं|प्रवालः
प्रवाल See प्रबाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविकीर्ण
प्रविकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered or strewed about.<BR>—2 Dispersed, diffused.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रविकीर्णकामा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविकीर्णकामा
प्रविकीर्ण + -कामा a woman who has various lovers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्यात
प्रविख्यात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Named, called.<BR>—2 Famous, renowned, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्यातिः|प्रविख्याति
प्रविख्यातिः <i>f.</i> Fame, renown, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविघटित
प्रविघटित <i>p. p.</i> Hewn off, severed; झटिति विततवह्नपुद्गारभास्वत्कुठारप्रविघटितकठोरस्कन्धबन्धः<BR> कबन्धः Mv. 2. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचयः|प्रविचय
प्रविचयः Examination, investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचर्
प्रविचर् €1 P.<BR>—1 To roam about.<BR>—2 To move onward, advance.<BR>—3 To wander through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचरः
प्रविचरः Discernment, discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचारः|प्रविचार
प्रविचारः Distinction, division, species, kind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रविचारमार्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचारमार्गः|प्रविचारमार्ग
प्रविचारः + -मार्गः (pl.) springing from side to side (an artifice in fighting);<BR> चचार चित्रं प्रविचारमार्गैः Ki. 17. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचारित
प्रविचारित <i>p. p.</i> Examined, investigated accurately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचल्
प्रविचल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To shake, tremble.<BR>—2 To deviate, swerve from, go astray; न्याग्यात् पथः प्रविचलन्ति पदं<BR> न धीराः Bh. 2. 83.<BR>—3 To become confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचलित
प्रविचलित <i>a.</i> Moved, set in motion, shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचित
प्रविचित <i>a.</i> Tried, proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचेतनम्
प्रविचेतनम् Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवितत
प्रवितत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread out, expanded.<BR>—2 Dishevelled, disordered (hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारः|प्रविदार
प्रविदारः Bursting asunder, opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारणम्
प्रविदारणम्<BR>—1 Tearing, rending, breaking, bursting asunder.<BR>—2 Budding.<BR>—3 Conflict, war, battle.<BR>—4 Crowd, confusion, tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्ध
प्रविद्ध <i>p. p.</i> Cast away, thrown off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्रुत
प्रविद्रुत <i>p. p.</i> Dispersed, put to flight, scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविधा
प्रविधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To decide.<BR>—2 To do or make.<BR>—3 To meditate, think upon.<BR>—4 To place in front or at the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविधानम्
प्रविधानम्<BR>—1 Thinking upon.<BR>—2 Doing.<BR>—3 A means employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविध्वस्त
प्रविध्वस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thrown away.<BR>—2 Agitated, disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1109-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविपलः|प्रविपल|प्रविपलं
प्रविपलः, -लम्<BR> A small part of a <i>Vipala</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविपलम्
प्रविपलः, -लम्<BR> A small part of a <i>Vipala</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभज्
प्रविभज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sever, separate.<BR>—2 To divide, distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभक्त
प्रविभक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Severed, separated.<BR>—2 Apportioned, partitioned, divided, distributed; ज्योतींषि वर्तयति<BR> च प्रविभक्तरशिमः Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—3 One who has received his share; दातव्यं बान्धवैस्तत् स्यात् प्रविभक्तैरपि<BR> स्वतः Ms. 8. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभागः|प्रविभाग
प्रविभागः<BR>—1 Division, distribution.<BR>—2 A part, portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभागशः
प्रविभागशः <i>ind.</i> Separately, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभुज्
प्रविभुज् €6 P. To bend back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरः|प्रविर
प्रविरः Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरत
प्रविरत <i>a.</i> One who has desisted from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरल
प्रविरल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Separated by a great interval, isolated, separate.<BR>—2 Very few or rare, very scanty; प्रविरला इव मुग्धवधूकथाः R. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलयः|प्रविलय
प्रविलयः, -विलयनम्<BR>—1 Melting away.<BR>—2 Complete dissolution or absorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलयनम्
प्रविलयः, -विलयनम्<BR>—1 Melting away.<BR>—2 Complete dissolution or absorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलुप्त
प्रविलुप्त <i>p. p.</i> Cut off, fallen or rubbed off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवादः|प्रविवाद
प्रविवादः Dispute, quarrel, wrangling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविविक्त
प्रविविक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very solitary.<BR>—2 Separated, detached; प्रविविक्तभुक् तैजसः Māṇḍ. 1. 4. 3 Sharp, keen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवेकः|प्रविवेक
प्रविवेकः Complete solitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्
प्रविश् €6 P. To enter into; अनाहूतः प्रविशति Mb. 5. 33. 36;<BR> इति प्रविश्याभिहिता द्विजन्मना Ku. 5. 51.<BR>—2 To enter upon, commence.<BR>—3 To appear. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To admit, introduce, usher; त्वरितं प्रवेशय U. 1.<BR>—2 To lay or store up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्ट|प्रविष्टः
प्रविष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone or entered into; पञ्चार्धेन प्रविष्टः शरपतनभयाद्भूयसा<BR> पूर्वकायम् Ś. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Engaged in, occupied with.<BR>—3 Begun (as an age).<BR>—4 Sunk (as an eye); Suśr.<BR>—5 Agreeing with.<BR>—6 Invested (as money).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्टकम्
प्रविष्टकम्<BR>—1 Entrance on the stage.<BR>—2 Entering a room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशः|प्रवेश
प्रवेशः<BR>—1 Entrance, penetration; पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R. 7. 1; Ku. 3. 60.<BR>—2 Ingress, access, approach.<BR>—3 Entrance on the stage; तेन पात्रप्रवेशश्चेत् S. D. 6.<BR>—4 The entrance or door (of a house &c.).<BR>—5 Income, revenue.<BR>—6 Close application (to a pursuit), intentness of purpose.<BR>—7 The entrance of the sun into a sign of the zodiac.<BR>—8 Coming on, setting in (of night).<BR>—9 The syringe of a clyster-pipe.<BR>—10 Employment, use. (Proverb━ चञ्चुप्रवेशो मुसलप्रवेशः; cf.<BR> ‘the thin end of the wedge’).<BR>—11 Manner, method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशकः|प्रवेशक
प्रवेशकः ‘The introducer’, an interlude acted by inferior characters<BR> (such as servants, buffoon &c.) for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">Page1110-2</a>]<BR> the purpose of acquainting the audience with events not represented on<BR> the stage, but a knowledge of which is essential for the proper understanding<BR> of what follows; (like the Viṣkambhaka it connects the story of the drama<BR> and the subdivisions of the plot, by briefly referring to what has occurred<BR> in the intervals of the acts, or what is likely to happen at the end;<BR> it never occurs at the beginning of the first act or at the end of the<BR> last). S. D. thus defines it:− प्रवेशकोऽनुदात्तोक्त्या नीचपात्रप्रयोजितः ।<BR> अङ्कद्वयान्तर्विज्ञेयः शेषं विष्कम्भके यथा ॥ 309; see विष्कम्भक; cf. Ve. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशनम्
प्रवेशनम्<BR>—1 Entrance, penetration, going into.<BR>—2 Introducing, leading to, conducting.<BR>—3 An entrance to the main door of a house, gate.<BR>—4 Sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशित
प्रवेशित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Introduced, showed in, led or conducted to, brought in.<BR>—2 Thrown into (any condition).<BR>—3 Appointed, installed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशिता
प्रवेशित + .{@-ता@} Impregnated, pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be entered.<BR>—2 To be penetrated or pervaded.<BR>—3 To be played (as a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्लेषः|प्रविश्लेष
प्रविश्लेषः Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषण्ण
प्रविषण्ण <i>a.</i> Dejected, spiritless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषयः|प्रविषय
प्रविषयः Scope, range, reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषा
प्रविषा A birch tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविसृत
प्रविसृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spread, divulged.<BR>—2 Run away.<BR>—3 Violent, intensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविस्तरः|प्रविस्तर
प्रविस्त(स्ता)रः Extent, circumference, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविस्तारः|प्रविस्तार
प्रविस्त(स्ता)रः Extent, circumference, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविहत
प्रविहत <i>p. p.</i> Beaten back, put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीण|प्रवीणः
प्रवीण <i>a.</i> Clever, skilled or versed in, conversant with; आमोदानथ<BR> हरिदन्तराणि नेतुं नैवान्यो जगति समीरणात् प्रवीणः Bv. 1. 15; Ku. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीर|प्रवीरः
प्रवीर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Foremost, best, most excellent or distinguished; तस्यै प्रतिश्रुत्य<BR> रघुप्रवीरः R. 14. 29, 16. 1; कुरुप्रवीर Bg. 11. 48.<BR>—2 Strong, powerful, heroic; प्रवीरे वास्तुनि राजनिवेशाः Kau. A. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीरः|प्रवीर
प्रवीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A brave person, hero, warrior; प्रक्षपितप्रवीरम् … … जर्जरमकुर्वन् Dk. 2. 8.<BR>—2 A chief, distinguished personage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृ
प्रवृ €5 U.<BR>—1 To cover, envelop; प्रावारिषुरिव क्षोणीं क्षिप्ता वृक्षाः समन्ततः Bk. 9. 25.<BR>—2 To wear, put on.<BR>—3 To choose, select. —4 To keep or ward off (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत
प्रवृत <i>p. p.</i> Selected, picked, chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्
प्रवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To go forward, move on, proceed; स्वामिसेवकयोरेवं वृत्तिचकं प्रवर्तते Pt. 1. 81.<BR>—2 To arise, be produced, spring; प्रवर्तन्ते क्रियाः सर्वाः पर्वतेभ्य<BR> इवापगाः Pt. 1. 6.<BR>—3 To happen, come to pass, take place.<BR>—4 To begin, commence (usually with inf.); हन्त प्रवृत्तं संगीतकम्<BR> M. 1; Ś. 7. 34; Ku. 3. 25.<BR>—5 To strive, exert oneself;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">Page1111-1</a>]<BR> प्रवर्ततां प्रकृतिहिताय पार्थिवः Ś. 7. 35.<BR>—6 To act up to, follow; न कौलीन्यान्न सौहार्दान्नृपो वाक्ये प्रवर्तते Pt. 1. 116.<BR>—7 To engage in, be occupied with; अपि स्वशक्त्या तपसि प्रवर्तसे Ku. 5. 33.<BR>—8 To act, do; न पुनरेवं प्रवर्तितव्यम् Ś. 6.<BR>—9 To act or behave towards.<BR>—10 To prevail, exist; राजन् प्रजासु ते कश्चिदपचारः प्रवर्तते R. 15. 47.<BR>—11 To hold good.<BR>—12 To proceed uninterruptedly, thrive; तस्मादोमित्युदाहृत्य यज्ञदानतपःक्रियाः ।<BR> प्रवर्तन्ते ….<BR> Bg. 17. 24; Ms. 3. 61. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To proceed with, continue; Mu. 2.<BR>—2 To introduce.<BR>—3 To set on foot, establish, found.<BR>—4 To drive, propel, urge, stimulate.<BR>—5 To promote, advance.<BR>—6 To throw, cast.<BR>—7 To produce, create.<BR>—8 To invent, devise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1110-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तः|प्रवर्त|प्रवर्त्त
प्रवर्तः<BR>—1 Commencing, undertaking, engaging in.<BR>—2 Excitement, stimulus.<BR>—3 Ved. A round ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्तक <i>a.</i> (-र्तिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Setting on foot, founding.<BR>—2 Advancing, promoting, furthering.<BR>—3 Producing, causing,<BR> … कृतिसाध्यताज्ञानं वा प्रवर्तकमिति जरन्नैयायिकाः.<BR>—4 Prompting, urging, inducing, instigating (in a bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्तक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An originator, founder, author.<BR>—2 A prompter, instigator.<BR>—3 An arbiter, umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तकम्
प्रवर्तक + .{@-कम्@} The entrance of a character on the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तनम्
प्रवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Going on, moving forward.<BR>—2 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—3 Setting on foot, founding, establishing, instituting.<BR>—4 Prompting, urging, simulating, inciting.<BR>—5 Engaging in, applying oneself to.<BR>—6 Happening, coming to pass.<BR>—7 Activity, action.<BR>—8 Behaviour, conduct, procedure.<BR>—9 Directing, superintending.<BR>—10 Employment.<BR>—11 Exhortation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तना|प्रवर्त्तना
प्रवर्तनम् + .{@-ना@} Inciting or prompting to action; अस्ति प्रवर्तनारूपमनुरूपं<BR> चतुर्ष्वपि Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तयितृ
प्रवर्तयितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who sets in motion, urges, establishes, founds &c.<BR>—2 An employer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तित|प्रवर्त्तित|प्रवर्त्तितः
प्रवर्तित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Caused to turn, made to go or roll onwards, revolving; चमरान् परितः<BR> प्रवर्तिताश्वः R. 9. 66.<BR>—2 Founded, set up, established.<BR>—3 Prompted, incited, instigated.<BR>—4 Kindled; प्रवर्तितो दीप इव प्रदीपात् R. 5. 37.<BR>—5 Caused, made.<BR>—6 Purified, rendered pure; गोभिः प्रवर्तिते तीर्थे Ms. 11. 196.<BR>—7 Informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तिन्
प्रवर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proceeding, moving onward.<BR>—2 Being active.<BR>—3 Causing, effecting.<BR>—4 Using.<BR>—5 Arising from, flowing; Ś. 3. 14.<BR>—6 Spreading &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्त|प्रवृत्तः
प्रवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Begun, commenced, proceeded with.<BR>—2 Set in; अचिरप्रवृत्तं ग्रीष्मसमयमधिकृत्य Ś. 1.<BR>—3 Engaged in, occupied with.<BR>—4 Going to, bound for.<BR>—5 Fixed, settled, determined.<BR>—6 Unimpeded, undisputed.<BR>—7 Round.<BR>—8 Flowing, running; प्रवृत्तमुदकं वायुं सर्वं वानेयमाश्रयेत् Mb. 14. 46. 12.<BR>—9 Circulated (as a book).<BR>—10 Offending, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तः|प्रवृत्त
प्रवृत्त + .{@-त्तः@} A round ornament. {@त्तम्@} An action, undertaking.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवृत्तचक्रता, प्रवृत्तवाक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तचक्रता
प्रवृत्त + -चक्रता <i>f.</i> sovereign power;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">Page1111-2</a>]<BR> प्रवृत्तचकतां चैव वाणिज्यप्रभृतीनपि Y. 1. 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तवाक्
प्रवृत्त + -वाक् of fluent speech, eloquent; Mb. 5. 33. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तकम्
प्रवृत्तकम्<BR>—1 Entrance on the stage.<BR>—2 N. of a Mātrā-metre; यदा समावोजयुग्मकौ पूर्ग्ययौ भवति तत् प्रवृत्तकम् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिः|प्रवृत्ति
प्रवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Continued advance.<BR>—2 Rise, origin, source, flow (of words &c.); प्रवृत्तिरासीच्छब्दानां<BR> चरितार्था चतुष्टयी Ku. 2. 17.<BR>—3 Appearance, manifestation; कुसुमप्रवृत्तिसमये Ś. 4. 9. (v. l.);<BR> R. 11. 43, 14. 39, 15. 4.<BR>—4 Advent, setting in, commencement; आकालिकीं वीक्ष्य मधुप्रवृत्तिम् Ku. 3. 34.<BR>—5 Application or addiction to, tendency, inclination, predilection, propensity;<BR> न हि प्रजानामि तव प्रवृत्तिम् Bg. 11. 31; सतां हि संदेहपदेषु<BR> वस्तुषु प्रमाणमन्तःकरणप्रवृत्तयः Ś. 1. 22.<BR>—6 Conduct, behaviour; त्वां प्रत्यकस्मात् कलुषप्रवृत्तौ R. 14. 73.<BR>—7 Employment, occupation, activity; विदितं वो यथा स्वार्था न मे काश्चित्<BR> प्रवृत्तयः Ku. 6. 26.<BR>—8 Use, employment, currency (as of a word).<BR>—9 Continued effort, perseverance.<BR>—10 Signification, sense, acceptation (of a word).<BR>—11 Continuance, permanence, prevalence. —12 Active life, taking an active<BR> part in worldly affairs (opp. निवृत्ति); प्रवृत्तिः कुत्र कर्तव्या<BR> जीवितव्यं कथं नु वा H.<BR>—13 News, tidings, intelligence; ततः प्रवृत्तिः सीतायाः Mb. 3. 148. 5;<BR> प्रवृत्तिसाराः खलु मादृशां गिरः Ki. 1. 25; जीमूतेन स्वकुशलमयीं<BR> हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिम् Me. 4; V. 4. 20.<BR>—14 Applicability or validity of a rule.<BR>—15 Fate, destiny, luck.<BR>—16 Cognition, direct perception or apprehension.<BR>—17 Rutting juice, or ichor exuding from the temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>—18 N. of the city of उज्जयिनी q. v.<BR>—19 (In Arith.) The multiplier.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रवृत्तिज्ञः, प्रवृत्तिनिमित्तम्, प्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुख, प्रवृत्तिपुरुषः, प्रवृत्तिप्रत्ययः, प्रवृत्तिमार्गः, प्रवृत्तिलेखः, प्रवृत्तिविज्ञानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिज्ञः|प्रवृत्तिज्ञ
प्रवृत्तिः + -ज्ञः a spy, secret emissary or agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिनिमित्तम्
प्रवृत्तिः + -निमित्तम् a reason for the use of any term in a particular signification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुख
प्रवृत्तिः + -पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> averse to giving news; मयि च विधुरे भावः<BR> कान्ताप्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुखः V. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिपुरुषः
प्रवृत्तिः + -पुरुषः a news agent; प्रवृत्तिपुरुषाः कथयन्ति Pañc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिप्रत्ययः|प्रवृत्तिप्रत्यय
प्रवृत्तिः + -प्रत्ययः conception of the things relating to the external world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिमार्गः|प्रवृत्तिमार्ग
प्रवृत्तिः + -मार्गः active or worldly life, attachment to the business and<BR> pleasure of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिलेखः
प्रवृत्तिः + -लेखः a writ of guidance; प्रावृत्तिकश्च प्रतिलेख एव Kau. A. 2. 10. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिविज्ञानम्
प्रवृत्तिः + -विज्ञानम् cognition of the things belonging to the external world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृध्
प्रवृध् €1 Ā. To grow, increase, be augmented. ━<i>Caus.</i> To increase, augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्धनम्
प्रवर्धनम् Increasing, augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्ध|प्रवृद्धः
प्रवृद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Full-grown.<BR>—2 Increased, augmented, expanded, enlarged; प्रवृद्धं यद् वैरं मम<BR> खलु शिशोरेव कुरुभिः Ve. 1. 10.<BR>—3 Full, deep.<BR>—4 Haughty, arrogant.<BR>—5 Violent.<BR>—6 Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्धिः|प्रवृद्धि
प्रवृद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Increase, growth; श्मश्रुप्रवृद्धिः R. 13. 71; प्रवृद्धौ हीयते<BR> चन्द्रः 17. 71.<BR>—2 Rise, prosperity, preferment, promotion, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृष्
प्रवृष् €1 P. To begin to rain, rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1111-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षः|प्रवर्ष
प्रवर्षः Heavy rain, heavy down-pour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षणम्
प्रवर्षणम्<BR>—1 Raining.<BR>—2 The first rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षिन्
प्रवर्षिन् <i>a.</i> Raining; causing to rain, showering or pouring down, discharging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक|प्रवेकः
प्रवेक <i>a.</i> Best, chief, choicest, most excellent; अथ यानप्रबेकैस्तु<BR> कौसल्याप्रमुखाः स्त्रियः (प्रययुः) Rām. 2. 92. 36; Bhāg. 7. 8. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेगः|प्रवेग
प्रवेगः Great speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेटः|प्रवेट
प्रवेटः Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेण
प्रवेण <i>a.</i> Pertaining to a particular goat; न कादली, न प्रियकी,<BR> न प्रवेणी, न चाविकी Rām. 3. 43. 36 (com. प्रवेणी अजविशेषसंबन्धिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणिः|प्रवेणि
प्रवेणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A braid of hair (in general); हेमभक्तिमतीं भूमेः प्रवेणीमिव पिप्रिये R. 15. 30.<BR>—2 The hair twisted and unadorned (worn by wives in the absence of their husbands).<BR>—3 The housings of an elephant.<BR>—4 A piece of coloured woollen cloth; Mb. 15. 27. 13.<BR>—5 The current or stream (of a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्रवेणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A braid of hair (in general); हेमभक्तिमतीं भूमेः प्रवेणीमिव पिप्रिये R. 15. 30.<BR>—2 The hair twisted and unadorned (worn by wives in the absence of their husbands).<BR>—3 The housings of an elephant.<BR>—4 A piece of coloured woollen cloth; Mb. 15. 27. 13.<BR>—5 The current or stream (of a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेतृ
प्रवेतृ <i>m.</i> A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेदित
प्रवेदित <i>p. p.</i> made known; चारैः प्रबेदिते तत्र Mb. 7. 74. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेदनम्
प्रवेदनम् Making known, announcing, proclaiming; P. III. 3. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेधः|प्रवेध
प्रवेधः<BR>—1 A bow-shot.<BR>—2 A particular measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपः|प्रवेप
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनम् Trembling, quivering,<BR> shaking, tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपकः|प्रवेपक
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनम् Trembling, quivering,<BR> shaking, tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपथुः|प्रवेपथु
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनम् Trembling, quivering,<BR> shaking, tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपनम्
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनम् Trembling, quivering,<BR> shaking, tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेरित
प्रवेरित <i>a.</i> Cast hither and thither, thrown about; नानाशस्त्रास्त्रवर्षैस्तान्<BR> वीर्यामर्षप्रवेरितैः (सायकैः) Mb. 6. 108. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेलः|प्रवेल
प्रवेलः A kind of kidney-bean (Mar. पिवळा मूग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्टः|प्रवेष्ट
प्रवेष्टः<BR>—1 An arm.<BR>—2 The wrist or forearm.<BR>—3 The fleshy part of an elephantʼs back (where the rider sits).<BR>—4 An elephantʼs gums.<BR>—5 An elephantʼs housings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्त|प्रव्यक्तं
प्रव्यक्त <i>p. p.</i> Apparent, clear, manifest, evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्तिः|प्रव्यक्ति
प्रव्यक्तिः <i>f.</i> Manifestation, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्याहरणम्
प्रव्याहरणम् The faculty of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्याहारः|प्रव्याहार
प्रव्याहारः<BR>—1 Prolongation of discourse.<BR>—2 Speaking to, address.<BR>—3 Sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्
प्रव्रज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go into exile.<BR>—2 To renounce all worldly attachments, enter on the fourth stage in life,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> to become a <i>Samnyāsin</i>; आत्मन्यग्नीन् समारोप्य ब्राह्मणः<BR> प्रव्रजेद् गृहात् Ms. 6. 38, 8. 363. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To banish, send into exile.<BR>—2 To compel to become a monk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजनम्
प्रव्रजनम्<BR>—1 Going abroad, sojourning.<BR>—2 Going into exile.<BR>—3 Turning a recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजित|प्रव्रजितः
प्रव्रजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone abroad or into exile.<BR>—2 Turned a recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजितः|प्रव्रजित
प्रव्रजित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A religious mendicant or ascetic in general.<BR>—2 Especially, a Brāhmaṇa who has entered on the fourth (भिक्षु) order.<BR>—3 The pupil of a Jaina or Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजिता
प्रव्रजित + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 A female ascetic.<BR>—2 A spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजितम्
प्रव्रजित + .{@-तम्@} Turning a recluse, the life of a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्यम्
प्रव्रज्यम् Going abroad, migration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्या
प्रव्रज्या<BR>—1 Going abroad, migration.<BR>—2 Roaming, wandering about as a religious mendicant; अतश्च प्रव्रज्यासुलभसमयाचारविमुखः ।<BR> प्रसक्तस्ते यत्नः … Māl. 4. 6.<BR>—3 The order of a religious mendicant, a mendicantʼs life, the fourth<BR> (or भिक्षु) order in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa; प्रव्रज्यां<BR> कल्पवृक्षा इवाश्रिताः Ku. 6. 6. (where Malli. says प्रव्रज्या means<BR> the वानप्रस्थ or third order).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रव्रज्यावसितः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्यावसितः|प्रव्रज्यावसित
प्रव्रज्या + -अवसितः a religious mendicant who renounces his order; प्रव्रज्यावसिता<BR> यत्र त्रयो वर्णा द्विजोत्तमाः । निर्वासं कारयेद् विप्रं दासत्वं क्षत्रवैश्ययोः ॥<BR> Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राज्
प्रव्राज् <i>m.</i>, प्रव्राजकः A religious mendicant, recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजकः|प्रव्राजक
प्रव्राज् <i>m.</i>, प्रव्राजकः A religious mendicant, recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजिका
प्रव्राज् <i>m.</i>, प्रव्राजकः + .{@-जिका@} A female ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजनम्
प्रव्राजनम् Banishing, exile, sending into exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रश्चनः|प्रव्रश्चन
प्रव्रश्चनः A knife for cutting wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंस्
प्रशंस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To praise, extol, approve, speak approvingly of, commend; हरिणा<BR> युवतिः प्रशशंसे Gīt. 1; यच्च वाचा प्रशस्यते Ms. 5. 127; प्राशंसीत्तं<BR> निशाचरः Bk. 15. 65; R. 5. 25, 17. 36.<BR>—2 To esteem, value.<BR>—3 To declare.<BR>—4 To foretell, prophesy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसक
प्रशंसक, प्रशंसिन् Praising, laudatory, eulogistic. ━<i>m.</i> A panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसिन्
प्रशंसक, प्रशंसिन् Praising, laudatory, eulogistic. ━<i>m.</i> A panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसनम्
प्रशंसनम् Praising, extolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसनीय
प्रशंसनीय <i>a.</i> To be praised, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसा
प्रशंसा<BR>—1 Praise, eulogy, panegyric, applause; प्रशंसावचनम् ‘a complimentary or laudatory remark’<BR>.<BR>—2 Description, reference to; as in अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा q. v.<BR>—3 Glory, fame, reputation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रशंसालापः, प्रशंसोपमा, प्रशंसामुखर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसालापः|प्रशंसालाप
प्रशंसा + -आलापः Applause, acclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसोपमा
प्रशंसा + -उपमा one of the several kinds of उपमा mentioned by Daṇḍin;<BR> ब्रह्मणोऽप्युद्भवः पद्मश्चन्द्रः शंभुशिरोधृतः । तौ तुल्यौ त्वन्मुखेनेति<BR> सा प्रशंसोपमोच्यते ॥ Kāv. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसामुखर
प्रशंसा + -मुखर <i>a.</i> loudly praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसित
प्रशंसित <i>p. p.</i> Praised, extolled, applauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्त|प्रशस्तं
प्रशस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Praised, lauded, commended, eulogised.<BR>—2 Praiseworthy, commendable.<BR>—3 Best, excellent.<BR>—4 Blessed, happy, auspicious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रशस्ताद्रिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्ताद्रिः|प्रशस्ताद्रि
प्रशस्त + -अद्रिः N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्तिः|प्रशस्ति
प्रशस्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Praise, eulogy, laudation.<BR>—2 Description; U. 7.<BR>—3 A panegyric or small poem written in praise of any one (<i>e. g.</i> a patron).<BR>—4 Excellence, eminence.<BR>—5 Benediction.<BR>—6 Guidance, instruction, rule<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">Page1113-1</a>]<BR> for guidance; as in लेखप्रशस्तिः ‘a form of writing’.<BR>—7 Publicity, advertising; दशाननतिरस्कारप्रशस्तिमिव Mv. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1112-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्य|प्रशस्यः
प्रशस्य <i>a.</i> (Compar. श्रेयस् or ज्यायस्, superl. श्रेष्ठ<BR> or ज्येष्ठ) Praiseworthy, commendable, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्त्वन्
प्रशत्त्वन् <i>m.</i> The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्त्वरी
प्रशत्त्वरी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम्
प्रशम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To become calm or tranquil.<BR>—2 To be soothed or appeased.<BR>—3 To stop, cease, terminate.<BR>—4 To be allayed, be quenched or extinguished; प्रशान्तं पावकास्त्रम्<BR> U. 6; निर्वाते ज्वलितो वह्निः स्वयमेव प्रशाम्यति Pt. 3. 56.<BR>—5 To decay, wither away. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To soothe, appease, pacify; सान्त्वेन प्रशमय्यादौ स्वधर्मं प्रतिपादयेत् Ms. 8. 391.<BR>—2 To allay, extinguish, quench, put down; त्वामासारप्रशमितवनोपप्लवम् Me. 17.<BR>—3 To remove, put an end to; तम् (अपचारं) अन्विष्य प्रशमयेः R. 15. 47.<BR>—4 To conquer, vanquish, subdue; पान्तु पृथ्वीं प्रशमितरिपवो धर्मनिष्ठाश्च<BR> भूपाः Mk. 10. 60.<BR>—5 To settle, adjust, compose; प्रशमयसि विवादं कल्पसे रक्षणाय Ś. 5. 8.<BR>—6 To kill, destroy.<BR>—7 To cure, heal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमः|प्रशम
प्रशमः<BR>—1 Calmness, tranquillity, composure; प्रशमस्थितपूर्वपार्थिवम् R. 8. 15;<BR> Ki. 2. 32.<BR>—2 Peace, rest.<BR>—3 Extinction, abatement; प्रशमादर्चिषामेतत् Ku. 2. 20.<BR>—4 Cessation, end, destruction; निर्वाणवैरदहनाः प्रशमादरीणां<BR> Ve. 1. 7; प्रयतः प्रशमं हुताशनस्य Śi. 20. 73.<BR>—5 Pacification, appeasement; प्रशमोपन्यसनं वृथा मम Śi. 16. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Calming, tranquillizing, pacifying, removing &c.<BR>—2 Curing, healing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमनम्
प्रशमन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Calming, tranquillizing, pacifying.<BR>—2 Allaying, assuaging, soothing, mitigating; आपन्नार्तिप्रशमनफलाः<BR> संपदो ह्युत्तमानाम् Me. 55.<BR>—3 Curing, healing; as in व्याधिप्रशमनम्.<BR>—4 Quenching, extinguishing, suppressing, quelling; Mb. 5. 165. 9.<BR>—5 Cessation, abatement.<BR>—6 Bestowing fitly or on fit objects; लब्धप्रशमनं कृत्वा Mb. 12. 45. 10<BR> (com. लब्धस्य धनादेः यथोचितमंशतः पात्रे समर्पणेन शान्तिकम्)<BR> Ms. 7. 56; (सत्पात्रे प्रतिपादनम् Kull.; but others give it the next sense).<BR>—7 Securing, guarding, keeping safe; लब्धप्रशमनस्वस्थमथैनं समुपास्थिता R. 4. 14.<BR>—8 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—9 Restoration of peace; लब्धप्रशमनम् Kau. A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमित
प्रशमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pacified, soothed, composed, appeased, allayed.<BR>—2 Extinguished, quenched.<BR>—3 Atoned for, expiated; हा हा धिक् परगृहवासदूषणं यद् वैदेह्याः<BR> प्रशमितमद्भुतैरुपायैः U. 1. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्त|प्रशांत|प्रशान्तः
प्रशान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Calmed, tranquillized, composed; जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा<BR> समाहितः Bg. 6. 7.<BR>—2 Calm. serene, quiet, sedate, still; अहो प्रशान्तरमणीयतोद्यानस्य.<BR>—3 Tamed, subdued, quelled.<BR>—4 Ended, ceased, over; तत् सर्वमेकपद एव मम प्रशान्तम् Māl. 9. 36;<BR> प्रशान्तमस्त्रम् U. 6 ‘ceased to work or withdrawn’.<BR>—5 Dead, deceased; (see शम् with प्र).<BR>—6 Allayed, removed; त्यक्त्वा भयं सर्प इव प्रशान्तः Rām. 7. 69. 39.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रशान्तात्मन्, प्रशान्तोर्ज, प्रशान्तकाम, प्रशान्तचित्त, प्रशान्तचेष्ट, प्रशान्तबाध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तात्मन्|प्रशांतात्मन्
प्रशान्त + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> composed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">Page1113-2</a>]<BR> in mind, peaceful, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तोर्ज|प्रशांतोर्ज
प्रशान्त + -ऊर्ज <i>a.</i> weakened, enervated, prostrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तकाम
प्रशान्त + -काम <i>a.</i> content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तचित्त
प्रशान्त + -चित्त <i>a.</i> calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तचेष्ट|प्रशांतचेष्ट
प्रशान्त + -चेष्ट <i>a.</i> resting, ceased to work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तबाध|प्रशांतबाध
प्रशान्त + -बाध <i>a.</i> having all obstacles or calamities removed; प्रशान्तबाधं<BR> दिशतोऽभिरक्षया Ki. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तिः|प्रशान्ति|प्रशांति|प्रशांतिः
प्रशान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Calmness, tranquillity, composure, quiet, repose.<BR>—2 Rest, cessation, abatement.<BR>—3 Allaying, quenching, extinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशामः|प्रशाम
प्रशामः<BR>—1 Tranquillity, calm, composure.<BR>—2 Quenching, extinction, allaying.<BR>—3 Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाख
प्रशाख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having many or spreading branches.<BR>—2 Being in the 5th stage of formation (said of the embryo, when the hands<BR> and feet are formed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखा
प्रशाख + .{@-खा@} A small branch or twig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखिका
प्रशाखिका A small branch; Mb. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्
प्रशास् €2 P.<BR>—1 To teach, instruct, advise; अपि साक्षात् प्रशिष्यास्त्वं कृच्छ्रेष्विन्द्रपुरोहितम् Bk. 19. 19.<BR>—2 To order, command; प्रशाधि यन्मया कार्यम् Mārk. P.<BR>—3 To rule, govern, be lord of; द्यां प्रशाधि गलितावधिकांलम् N. 5. 24;<BR> R. 6. 76, 9. 1.<BR>—4 To punish, chastise.<BR>—5 To pray or ask for, seek for (Ātm.); इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं<BR> प्रशास्महे U. 1. 1 (used in the sense of शास् with आ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासकः|प्रशासक
प्रशासकः<BR>—1 A director, ruler.<BR>—2 A spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासनम्
प्रशासनम्<BR>—1 Governing, ruling; एतस्य वा अक्षरस्य प्रशासने गार्गि सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ<BR> विधृतौ तिष्ठत Bṛ. Up. 3. 8. 9.<BR>—2 Enjoining, exacting.<BR>—3 Government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासितृ
प्रशासितृ, प्रशास्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A king, ruler, governor; ततः सेनापतिः पश्चात् प्रशास्ता च न्यषीदत<BR> Rām. 2. 91. 40.<BR>—2 A director, adviser; बालो यत्र प्रशासिता Pt. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्तृ
प्रशासितृ, प्रशास्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A king, ruler, governor; ततः सेनापतिः पश्चात् प्रशास्ता च न्यषीदत<BR> Rām. 2. 91. 40.<BR>—2 A director, adviser; बालो यत्र प्रशासिता Pt. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्ट
प्रशिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Ruled over, governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्टिः|प्रशिष्टि
प्रशिष्टिः, प्रशिस् <i>f.</i> Ved. Command, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिस्
प्रशिष्टिः, प्रशिस् <i>f.</i> Ved. Command, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिथिल
प्रशिथिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very loose; प्रशिथिलमृणालैकवलयम् Ś. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Very feeble, hardly perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्यः|प्रशिष्य
प्रशिष्यः The pupil of a pupil, the disciple of a disciple; शिष्यप्रशिष्यैरुपगीयमानमवेहि<BR> तन्मण्डनमिश्रधाम Śāṅkaradigvijaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशुद्धिः|प्रशुद्धि
प्रशुद्धिः <i>f.</i> Clearness, purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशून
प्रशून <i>a.</i> Swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशोषः|प्रशोष
प्रशोषः Becoming dry, drying up, aridity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्चोतनम्
प्रश्चो(श्च्यो)तनम् Sprinkling, oozing; प्रश्च्योतनं नु हरिचन्दनपल्लवानाम्<BR> U. 3. 11 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्च्योतनम्
प्रश्चो(श्च्यो)तनम् Sprinkling, oozing; प्रश्च्योतनं नु हरिचन्दनपल्लवानाम्<BR> U. 3. 11 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नः|प्रश्न
प्रश्नः [प्रच्छ्-भावे नङ्]<BR>—1 A question, query; an inquiry, interrogation (अविज्ञातप्रवचनं<BR> प्रश्न इत्यभिधीयते); अनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकम् Ś. 5 ‘with an inquiry about (your) well-being or health’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">Page1114-1</a>]<BR>.<BR>—2 A judicial inquiry or investigation.<BR>—3 A point at issue, a subject of controversy, controverted or disputed<BR> point; इति प्रश्न उपस्थितः.<BR>—4 A problem for solution or calculation; अहं ते प्रश्नं दास्यामि Mk.<BR>—5 Inquiry into the future.<BR>—6 A short section of a work.<BR>—7 Basket-work.<BR>—8 A task or lesson (in Vedic recitation).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रश्नोपनिषद्, प्रश्नकथा, प्रश्नदूतिः, प्रश्नदूती, प्रश्नपूर्वकेन, प्रश्नवादिन्, प्रश्नविवाकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1113-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नोपनिषद्
प्रश्नः + -उपनिषद् <i>f.</i> N. of an Upaniṣad consisting of six questions<BR> and six answers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नकथा
प्रश्नः + -कथा a story containing a question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नदूतिः|प्रश्नदूति
प्रश्नः + -दूतिः, -दूती <i>f.</i> a riddle, an enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नदूती
प्रश्नः + -दूतिः, -दूती <i>f.</i> a riddle, an enigma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नपूर्वकेन
प्रश्नः + -पूर्वकेन <i>ind.</i> after examination; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नवादिन्
प्रश्नः + -वादिन् a fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नविवाकः|प्रश्नविवाक
प्रश्नः + -विवाकः an arbitrator, umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नयति
प्रश्नयति Den. P. To inquire after, ask about (with two acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्निन्
प्रश्निन् <i>m.</i> A questioner, interrogator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रथः|प्रश्रथ
प्रश्रथः Laxity, looseness, relaxation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रब्धिः|प्रश्रब्धि
प्रश्रब्धिः <i>f.</i> Trust, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयः|प्रश्रय
प्रश्रयः, प्रश्रयणम्<BR>—1 Respect, courtesy, civility, politeness, respectful or courteous behaviour,<BR> humility; वचः प्रश्रयगम्भीरमथोवाच कपिध्वजः Ki. 11. 37; समागतैः<BR> प्रश्रयनम्रमूर्तिभिः Śi. 12. 33; R. 10. 70, 83; U. 6. 23; सप्रश्रयम्<BR> respectfully, modestly.<BR>—2 Love, affection, regard.<BR>—3 Resort, recourse (आश्रय); कपिकुलैः स्कन्धे कृतप्रश्रयः Pt. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयणम्
प्रश्रयः, प्रश्रयणम्<BR>—1 Respect, courtesy, civility, politeness, respectful or courteous behaviour,<BR> humility; वचः प्रश्रयगम्भीरमथोवाच कपिध्वजः Ki. 11. 37; समागतैः<BR> प्रश्रयनम्रमूर्तिभिः Śi. 12. 33; R. 10. 70, 83; U. 6. 23; सप्रश्रयम्<BR> respectfully, modestly.<BR>—2 Love, affection, regard.<BR>—3 Resort, recourse (आश्रय); कपिकुलैः स्कन्धे कृतप्रश्रयः Pt. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयिन्
प्रश्रयिन्, प्रश्रित <i>a.</i> Civil, polite, courteous, humble,<BR> well-behaved; प्रोवाच चामितमतिः प्रश्रितं विनयान्वितः Mb. 1. 206. 15;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रित|प्रश्रितः
प्रश्रयिन्, प्रश्रित <i>a.</i> Civil, polite, courteous, humble,<BR> well-behaved; प्रोवाच चामितमतिः प्रश्रितं विनयान्वितः Mb. 1. 206. 15;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लथ|प्रश्लथः
प्रश्लथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very loose or flaccid.<BR>—2 Spiritless, unnerved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लिष्ट|प्रश्लिष्टः
प्रश्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Twisted, entwined.<BR>—2 Reasonable, well-argued or reasoned (युक्तियुत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लिष्टः|प्रश्लिष्ट
प्रश्लिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@}<BR>—1 A term applied to the Sandhi of the vowel अ with a following vowel<BR> and of other vowels with other homogeneous ones.<BR>—2 The vowel resulting from this Sandhi.<BR>—3 The accent with which such substituted vowel is pronounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लेषः|प्रश्लेष
प्रश्लेषः<BR>—1 Close contact, pressing hard against.<BR>—2 Euphonic coalition of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्वासः|प्रश्वास
प्रश्वासः Breath, respiration; श्वासप्रश्वासयोर्गतिविच्छेदः प्राणायामः Pātañjala S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टिः|प्रष्टि
प्रष्टिः Ved.<BR>—1 A side-horse.<BR>—2 A by-stander.<BR>—3 A tripod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठ|प्रष्ठः
प्रष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Standing or being in front; पुरोगाग्रेसरप्रष्ठाग्रतःसरपुरस्सराः<BR> Ak.; R. 15. 10; तं पृष्ठतः प्रष्ठमियाय नम्रः Bk. 1. 24.<BR>—2 Chief, principal, foremost, best; a leader; पुलस्त्यप्रष्ठः Mv. 1. 30, 6. 30;<BR> Śi. 19. 30; सर्वनारीगुणैः प्रष्ठाम् Bk. 9. 84.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रष्ठवाह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठवाह्
प्रष्ठ + -वाह् <i>m.</i> a young bull being trained for the plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठौही
प्रष्ठौही A cow for the first time with a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्
प्रस् €1. €4 Ā. (प्रस-स्य-ते)<BR>—1 To bring forth young.<BR>—2 To spread, diffuse, expand, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसकल
प्रसकल <i>a.</i> Very full (as a bosom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्या|प्रसङ्ख्या
प्रसंख्या €2 P. To count, enumerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्या|प्रसङ्ख्या
प्रसंख्या<BR>—1 Total number, sum.<BR>—2 Reflection, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्यानः|प्रसङ्ख्यान
प्रसंख्यानः Payment, liquidation; प्रसंख्यानानसंख्येयान् प्रत्यगृह्णन्<BR> द्विजातयः Mb. 3. 121. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्यानम्
प्रसंख्यानः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Enumeration.<BR>—2 Reflection, meditation; deep meditation, abstract contemplation; हरः<BR> प्रसंख्यानपरो बभूव Ku. 3. 40.<BR>—3 Fame, reputation; यो न याति प्रसंख्यानमस्पष्टो भूमिवर्धनः Mb. 3. 35. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्घः|प्रसङ्घ|प्रसंघ|प्रसंघः
प्रसङ्घः A great multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसञ्ज्|प्रसंज्
प्रसञ्ज् €1 P. To become attached to or fond of, feel affection for. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To cling to or adhere to.<BR>—2 To follow, apply or be applicable, hold good in the case of (active<BR> also in this sense); इतरेतराश्रयः प्रसज्येत, वैषम्यनैर्घृण्ये नेश्वरस्य<BR> प्रसज्येते Ś. B.<BR>—3 To be attached to; तस्यामसौ प्रासजत् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्त|प्रसक्तं
प्रसक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Attached to, connected with.<BR>—2 Excessively attached or fond; प्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ<BR> Bg. 16. 16; कुर्वन्ति तावत् प्रथमं प्रियाणि यावन्न जानन्ति नरं प्रसक्तम् Pt. 1. 193.<BR>—3 Adhering or sticking to.<BR>—4 Fixed or intent upon, devoted or addicted to, engaged in, applied to;<BR> यस्तदनुप्रसक्तहृदयेयमिति Śi. 9. 63; so द्यूत˚, निद्रा˚ &c.<BR>—5 Contiguous, near; प्रसक्तं हि प्रतिषिध्यते -मीमांसकका˚.<BR>—6 Constant, incessant, uninterrupted; प्रसक्तसंपातपृथक्कृतान् पथः<BR> (पपात) Ki. 4. 18; R. 13. 40; Māl. 4. 6; M. 3. 1.<BR>—7 Got, obtained, gained.<BR>—8 Expanded, opened.<BR>—9 Clinging to the world, mundane; Bhāg.<BR>—10 See प्रयुक्त; तन्माभूदिह वः पुरंदरपुरीबन्दीप्रसक्तो विधिः Mv. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्तम्
प्रसक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Incessantly, continuously; अपः प्रसक्तं मुमुचुः<BR> पयोमुचः Ki. 16. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्तिः|प्रसक्ति
प्रसक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Attachment, devotion, addiction, devotedness, adherence.<BR>—2 Connection, union, association; अङ्कप्रसक्तिरकलङ्कहृदां क्व तेषाम्<BR> Viś. Guṇā. 503.<BR>—3 Applicability, bearing, application; as in अतिप्रसक्ति (which is<BR> = अतिव्याप्ति q. v.).<BR>—4 Energy, perseverance; संतापे दिशतु शिवः शिवां प्रसक्तिम् Ki. 5. 50.<BR>—5 Conclusion, deduction.<BR>—6 A topic or subject of discourse.<BR>—7 Occurrence of a possibility.<BR>—8 Acquisition, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गः|प्रसङ्ग|प्रसंग|प्रसंगः
प्रसङ्गः —1 Attachment, devotion, addiction, devotedness; स्वरूपयोग्ये<BR> सुरतप्रसङ्गे Ku. 1. 19; तस्यात्यायतकोमलस्य सततं द्यूतप्रसङ्गेन<BR> किम् Mk. 2. 11; Śi. 11. 22.<BR>—2 Union, intercourse, association, connection; निवर्ततामस्माद्गणिकाप्रसंगात्<BR> Mk. 4; Pt. 1. 251.<BR>—3 Illicit intercourse.<BR>—4 Occupation, intentness, being engaged or occupied with; भ्रूविक्रियायां<BR> विरतप्रसङ्गैः Ku. 3. 47.<BR>—5 A subject or topic (of discourse or controversy).<BR>—6 An occasion, incident; दिग्विजयप्रसंगेन K. 191; यात्राप्रसंगेन Māl. 1.<BR>—7 Conjuncture, time, opportunity; सूक्ष्मेभ्योऽपि प्रसंगेभ्यः स्त्रियो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">Page1115-1</a>]<BR> रक्ष्या विशेषतः Ms. 9. 5.<BR>—8 A contingency, event, case, occurrence of a possibility; नेश्वरो<BR> जगतः कारणमुपपद्यते, कुतः, वैषम्यनैर्घृण्यप्रसंगात् Ś. B.; एवं<BR> चानवस्थाप्रसंगः <i>ibid.</i>; तस्याणुतरप्रसंगात् Tarka K.; Ku. 7. 16.<BR>—8 Connected reasoning or argument.<BR>—9 A conclusion, an inference.<BR>—10 Connected language.<BR>—11 Inseparable application or connection (= व्याप्ति q. v.).<BR>—12 Mention of parents.<BR>—13 Introduction, insertion.<BR>—14 Gain.<BR>—15 An extended application; अन्यत्र कृतस्यान्यत्रासक्तिः प्रसङ्गः ।<BR> यथा प्रदीपस्य प्रासादे कृतस्य राजमार्गेऽप्यालोककरणम् ŚB. on MS. 12. 1. 1.<BR>—16 (In drama) A second or subsidiary incident or plot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसङ्गनिवारणम्, प्रसङ्गवशात्, प्रसङ्गविनिवृत्तिः, प्रसङ्गसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गेन
प्रसङ्गः + .({@प्रसंगेन, प्रसंगतः, प्रसंगात्@} are used adverbially in the sense of:−<BR>—1 in relation to.<BR>—2 in consequence of, on account of, because of, by way of.<BR>—3 occasionally, incidentally.<BR>—4 in course of; as in कथाप्रसंगेन ‘in course of conversation’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गतः
प्रसङ्गः + .({@प्रसंगेन, प्रसंगतः, प्रसंगात्@} are used adverbially in the sense of:−<BR>—1 in relation to.<BR>—2 in consequence of, on account of, because of, by way of.<BR>—3 occasionally, incidentally.<BR>—4 in course of; as in कथाप्रसंगेन ‘in course of conversation’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गात्
प्रसङ्गः + .({@प्रसंगेन, प्रसंगतः, प्रसंगात्@} are used adverbially in the sense of:−<BR>—1 in relation to.<BR>—2 in consequence of, on account of, because of, by way of.<BR>—3 occasionally, incidentally.<BR>—4 in course of; as in कथाप्रसंगेन ‘in course of conversation’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1114-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गनिवारणम्
प्रसङ्गः + -निवारणम् prevention or obviation of similar contingencies in future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गवशात्|प्रसंगवशात्
प्रसङ्गः + -वशात् <i>ind.</i> according to the time, by the force of circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गविनिवृत्तिः|प्रसङ्गविनिवृत्ति
प्रसङ्गः + -विनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> non-recurrence of a contingency; द्विशतं<BR> तु दमं दाप्यः प्रसङ्गविनिवृत्तये Ms. 8. 368.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गसमः|प्रसङ्गसम
प्रसङ्गः + -समः (in न्याय) the sophism that the proof too must be proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गिता
प्रसङ्गिता Attachment, intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गिन्|प्रसंगिन्
प्रसङ्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fond of, attached or devoted to.<BR>—2 Dependent on, contingent on.<BR>—3 Occasional, incidental; नान्वेष्टव्या विशेषास्तु विशेषा हि प्रसङ्गिनः<BR> Mb. 12. 325. 9.<BR>—4 Secondary, subordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसज्य
प्रसज्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be attached to<BR>—2 Applicable, holding good.<BR>—3 Contingent, possible.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसज्यप्रतिषेधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसज्यप्रतिषेधः|प्रसज्यप्रतिषेध
प्रसज्य + -प्रतिषेधः<BR>—1 negation of a possible case or contingeny.<BR>—2 a simple prohibition of the particular matter specified without mentioning<BR> what is different (from it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसञ्जनम्
प्रसञ्जनम्<BR>—1 Act of connecting, combining, uniting.<BR>—2 Applying, bringing to bear upon, bringing into use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसञ्जित
प्रसञ्जित <i>a.</i> Made, brought into being; प्रसह्य वर्षासु ऋतौ<BR> प्रसञ्जिते N. 9. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसद्
प्रसद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To be pleased, be gracious or propitious (oft. with inf.); तमालपत्रास्तरणासु<BR> रन्तुं प्रसीद शश्वन्मलयस्थलीषु R. 6. 64.<BR>—2 To be appeased or soothed, be satisfied; निमित्तमुद्दिश्य हि यः प्रकुप्यति<BR> ध्रुवं स तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति Pt. 1. 283.<BR>—3 To be pure or clear, clear up, brighten up (lit. and fig.); दिशः<BR> प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः सुखाः R. 3. 14; Ki. 16. 35; प्रससादोदयादम्भः कुम्भयोनेर्महौजसः 4. 21.<BR>—4 To bear fruit, succeed, be successful;<BR> क्रिया हि वस्तूपहिता प्रसीदति R. 3. 29. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To propitiate, secure the favour of, pray, beseech; तस्मात् प्रणम्य<BR> प्रणिधाय कायं प्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम् Bg. 11. 44; R. 1. 88; Y. 3. 283.<BR>—2 To beg pardon, pray for grace.<BR>—3 To purify, make clear or pure; चेतः प्रसादयति Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्तिः|प्रसत्ति
प्रसत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Favour, graciousness, complacency; करिष्यसे यत्र सुदुश्चराणि प्रसत्तये<BR> गोत्रभिदस्तपांसि Ki. 3. 29.<BR>—2 Clearness, purity, transparency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्न|प्रसन्नः
प्रसन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pure, clear, bright, limpid, pellucid, transparent; प्रसन्नदिक्पांसुविविक्तवातम्<BR> Ku. 1. 23, 7. 74; कूलंकषेव सिन्धुः प्रसन्नमम्भस्तटतरुं च Ś. 5. 21.<BR>—2 Pleased, delighted, propitiated, soothed; मया प्रसन्नेन तवार्जुनेदं<BR> रूपं परं दर्शितमात्मयोगात् Bg. 11. 47; गङ्गां शरन्नयति सिन्धुपतिं<BR> प्रसन्नाम् Mu. 3. 9; गम्भीरायाः पयसि सरितश्चेतसीव प्रसन्ने Me. 42<BR> (where the first sense is also intended); Ku. 5. 35; R. 2. 68.<BR>—3 Kind, kindly disposed, gracious, propitious; अवेहि मां कामदुघां<BR> प्रसन्नाम् R. 2. 63.<BR>—4 Plain, open, clear, easily intelligible (as meaning).<BR>—5 True, correct; प्रसन्नस्ते तर्कः V. 2; प्रसन्नप्रायस्ते तर्कः Māl. 1.<BR>—6 Settled down, tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्ना
प्रसन्न + .{@-न्ना@}<BR>—1 Propitiation, pleasing.<BR>—2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसन्नात्मन्, प्रसन्नेरा, प्रसन्नकल्प, प्रसन्नमुख, प्रसन्नवदन, प्रसन्नरस, प्रसन्नसलिल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नात्मन्
प्रसन्न + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> gracious-minded, propitious. ━(<i>m.</i>) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नेरा
प्रसन्न + -ईरा spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नकल्प
प्रसन्न + -कल्प <i>a.</i><BR>—1 almost calm.<BR>—2 almost true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नमुख
प्रसन्न + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> gracious-looking, with a pleased countenance, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नवदन
प्रसन्न + -मुख, -वदन <i>a.</i> gracious-looking, with a pleased countenance, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नरस
प्रसन्न + -रस <i>a.</i> clear-juiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नसलिल
प्रसन्न + -सलिल <i>a.</i> having clear water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नता
प्रसन्नता<BR>—1 Brightness, clearness, purity.<BR>—2 Perspicuity. —3 Complacence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादः|प्रसाद
प्रसादः<BR>—1 Favour, kindness, condescension, propitiousness; कुरु दृष्टिप्रसादम्<BR> ‘be pleased to show yourself’; इत्या प्रसादादस्यास्त्वं परिचर्यापरो<BR> भव R. 1. 91, 2. 22; ध्रुवमत्र न वर्धयेत् प्रसादम् Bu. C. 5. 65.<BR>—2 Good temper, graciousness of disposition.<BR>—3 Calmness, tranquillity, composure, serenity, sedateness, absence of<BR> excitement; आत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति Bg. 2. 64.<BR>—4 Clearness, limpidness, brightness, transparency, purity (as of water,<BR> mind &c.); गङ्गा रोधःपतनकलुषा गृह्णतीव प्रसादम् V. 1. 9; Ś. 7. 32;<BR> प्राप्तबुद्धिप्रसादाः Śi. 11. 6; R. 17. 1; Ki. 9. 25.<BR>—5 Perspicuity, clearness of style, one of the three Guṇas according<BR> to Mammaṭa, who thus defines it:− शुष्केन्धनाग्निवत् स्वच्छजलवत् सहसैव<BR> यः । व्याप्नोत्यन्यत् प्रसादोऽसौ सर्वत्र विहितस्थितिः K. P. 8; यावदर्थकपदत्वरूपमर्थवैमल्यं<BR> प्रसादः or श्रुतमात्रा वाक्यार्थं करतलबदरमिव निवेदयन्ती घटना<BR> प्रसादस्य R. G.; see Kāv. 1. 44; चित्तं व्याप्नोति यः क्षिप्रं शुष्केन्धनमिवानलः ।<BR> स प्रसादः समस्तेषु रसेषु रचनासु च S. D. 611; प्रसादरम्यमोजस्वि<BR> गरीयो लाघवान्वितम् Ki. 11. 38.<BR>—6 Food offered to idols &c., or the remnants of such food.<BR>—7 A free gift, gratuity.<BR>—8 Any propitiatory offering.<BR>—9 Wellbeing, welfare.<BR>—10 An essence of the food etc. (at the completion of the stages of digestion);<BR> रसाद् रक्तं प्रसादजं, ततो रक्तान्मांसं प्रसादजं, मांसान्मेदः प्रसादज<BR> इत्यादि यावत् शुकाद् गर्भः प्रसादजः इति Āyurvedaśāstra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसादोन्मुख, प्रसाददानम्, प्रसादपट्टः, प्रसादपट्टकम्, प्रसादपराङ्मुख, प्रसादपात्रम्, प्रसादस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादोन्मुख
प्रसादः + -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> disposed to favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाददानम्
प्रसादः + -दानम् a propitiatory gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपट्टः|प्रसादपट्ट
प्रसादः + -पट्टः a turban of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपट्टकम्
प्रसादः + -पट्टकम् a written edict of favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपराङ्मुख
प्रसादः + -पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 withdrawing favour from any one.<BR>—2 not caring for any bodyʼs favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपात्रम्
प्रसादः + -पात्रम् an object of favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादस्थ
प्रसादः + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 kind, propitious.<BR>—2 serene, pleased, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादक
प्रसादक, प्रसादिन् <i>a.</i> (-दिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Purifying, clearing, making pellucid; फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यम्बुप्रसादकम् Ms. 6. 67.<BR>—2 Soothing, calming.<BR>—3 Gladdening, cheering.<BR>—4 Courting favour, propitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादिन्
प्रसादक, प्रसादिन् <i>a.</i> (-दिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Purifying, clearing, making pellucid; फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यम्बुप्रसादकम् Ms. 6. 67.<BR>—2 Soothing, calming.<BR>—3 Gladdening, cheering.<BR>—4 Courting favour, propitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1115-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादन|प्रसादनं|प्रसादनः
प्रसादन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Purifying, clearing, rendering pure or clear.<BR>—2 Soothing, calming.<BR>—3 Cheering, gladdening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादनः|प्रसादन|प्रसादनं
प्रसादन + .{@-नः@} A royal tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादनम्
प्रसादन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Clearing from impurities, purifying.<BR>—2 Soothing, calming, tranquillizing, composing.<BR>—3 Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>—4 Propitiating, courting favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादना
प्रसादन + .{@-ना, -नी@}<BR>—1 Service, worship.<BR>—2 Purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादनी
प्रसादन + .{@-ना, -नी@}<BR>—1 Service, worship.<BR>—2 Purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादित
प्रसादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Purified, cleared.<BR>—2 Appeased, propitiated.<BR>—3 Worshipped.<BR>—4 Calmed, soothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादीकृ
प्रसादीकृ €8 U. To bestow as a favour, give as a present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिवस्
प्रसेदिवस् <i>a.</i> One who has become pleased, favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्दानम्
प्रसन्दानम् A rope, a fetter; तद् दुर्गद्वितयीदानप्रसन्दानममन्यत<BR> Śiva B. 15. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंधानम्
प्रसंधानम् Combination, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभः|प्रसभ
प्रसभः Force, violence, impetuosity; प्रसभोद्धृतारिः R. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभम्
प्रसभः + .{@-भम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Violently, forcibly, perforce; इन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं<BR> मनः Bg. 2. 60; Ms. 8. 332.<BR>—2 Very much, exceedingly; तवास्मि गीतरागेण हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः<BR> Ś. 1. 5; नार्यो हरन्ति हृदयं प्रसभं नराणाम् Ṛs. 6. 25.<BR>—3 Importunately; सखेति मत्वा प्रसभं यदुक्तम् Bg. 11. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसभदमनम्, प्रसभहरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभदमनम्
प्रसभः + -दमनम् subduing by force; इहायं सत्त्वानां प्रसभदमनात्<BR> सर्वदमनः Ś. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभहरणम्
प्रसभः + -हरणम् forcible abduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षणम्
प्रसमीक्षणम्, प्रसमीक्षा Consideration, deliberation, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षा
प्रसमीक्षणम्, प्रसमीक्षा Consideration, deliberation, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसयनम्
प्रसयनम्<BR>—1 Binding, fastening.<BR>—2 A Net; प्रसितिः प्रसयनात् तन्तुर्वा जालं वा Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्गः|प्रसर्ग
प्रसर्गः Ved.<BR>—1 Pouring or flowing forth.<BR>—2 Emission, discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसलः|प्रसल
प्रस(श)लः The cold season (हेमन्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशलः|प्रशल
प्रस(श)लः The cold season (हेमन्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव्य|प्रसव्यं
प्रसव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Contrary, inverted, reverse.<BR>—2 Turned towards the left; प्रसव्यं चापि तं चकुरृत्विजोऽग्निचितं<BR> नृपम् Rām. 2. 76. 20.<BR>—3 Favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्
प्रसह् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To bear, endure; न तेजस्तेजस्वी प्रसृतमपरेषां प्रसहते U. 6. 14.<BR>—2 To withstand, resist, overpower; संयुगे सांयुगीनं तमुद्यतं प्रसहेत<BR> कः Ku. 2. 57.<BR>—3 To exert oneself, attempt.<BR>—4 To dare, venture, be able.<BR>—5 To have power or energy; see प्रसह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्
प्रस(सा)ह् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Force, violence.<BR>—2 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाह्
प्रस(सा)ह् <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Force, violence.<BR>—2 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह|प्रसहः
प्रसह <i>a.</i> Withstanding, enduring, bearing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहः|प्रसह
प्रसह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 A beast or bird of prey.<BR>—2 Resistance, endurance, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहनः|प्रसहन
प्रसहनः A beast or bird of prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहनम्
प्रसहनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Withstanding, resisting.<BR>—2 Enduring, bearing up.<BR>—3 Defeating, overcoming.<BR>—4 Embracing, an embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्य
प्रसह्य <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Forcibly, violently, by force; प्रसह्य मणिमुद्धरेन्मकरवक्त्रदंष्ट्राङ्कुरात्<BR> Bh. 2. 4; Śi. 1. 27.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, much.<BR>—3 Having conquered or won; नाहमिच्छामि भीष्मेण गृहीतां त्वां प्रसह्य<BR> वै Mb. 5. 175. 6; M. 1.<BR>—4 Instantly, at once; परस्य भूयान् विवरेऽभियोगः प्रसह्य संरक्षणमात्मरन्ध्रे Ki. 16. 23.<BR>—5 Necessarily, absolutely.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसह्यकारिन्, प्रसह्यचौरः, प्रसह्यहरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्यकारिन्
प्रसह्य + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> acting with violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्यचौरः|प्रसह्यचौर
प्रसह्य + -चौरः a plunderer, highwayman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्यहरणम्
प्रसह्य + -हरणम् violent or forcible seizure, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाहः|प्रसाह
प्रसाहः Overpowering, defeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसातिका
प्रसातिका A kind of rice (with small grains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाध्
प्रसाध् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To advance, promote.<BR>—2 To accomplish, effect; perfect, complete.<BR>—3 To gain, obtain; यत्नेन मतिमांस्तस्मादर्थमेकं प्रसाधयेत् Pt. 1. 2.<BR>—4 To overcome, subdue.<BR>—5 To dress, decorate, adorn, embellish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधक|प्रसाधकः
प्रसाधक <i>a.</i> (-धिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Accomplishing, or perfecting.<BR>—2 Purifying, cleansing.<BR>—3 Decorating, ornamenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधकः|प्रसाधक
प्रसाधक + .{@-कः@} A valet-de-chambre, an attendant who dresses his master;<BR> प्रसाधका भोजकाश्च गात्रसंवाहका अपि Kām.; आकल्पसाधनैस्तैस्तैरुपसेधुः<BR> प्रसाधकाः R. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनम्
प्रसाधनम्<BR>—1 Accomplishing, effecting, bringing about.<BR>—2 Setting in order, arranging.<BR>—3 Decorating, ornamenting, embellishing; toilet, dress; ध्रियते कुसुमप्रसाधनं<BR> तव तच्चारु वपुर्न दृश्यते Ku. 4. 18.<BR>—4 A decoration, ornament, means of decoration or ornament; भूतार्थशोभाह्रियमाणनेत्राः<BR> प्रसाधने संनिहितेऽपि नार्यः Ku. 7. 13, 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनः|प्रसाधन|प्रसाधनं
प्रसाधनम् + .{@-नः, -नम्, -नी@} A comb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसाधनविधिः, प्रसाधनविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनम्
प्रसाधनम् + .{@-नः, -नम्, -नी@} A comb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसाधनविधिः, प्रसाधनविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनी
प्रसाधनम् + .{@-नः, -नम्, -नी@} A comb.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसाधनविधिः, प्रसाधनविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविधिः|प्रसाधनविधि
प्रसाधनम् + -विधिः decoration, embellishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविशेषः|प्रसाधनविशेष
प्रसाधनम् + -विशेषः the highest decoration; प्रसाधनविधेः प्रसाधनविशेषः V. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधिका
प्रसाधिका<BR>—1 A ladyʼs maid, a female attendant who looks to the toilet of her mistress;<BR> प्रसाधिकालम्बितमग्रपादमाक्षिप्य R. 7. 7.<BR>—2 Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधित|प्रसाधितः
प्रसाधित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Accomplished, completed, perfected.<BR>—2 Ornamented, decorated.<BR>—3 Proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसित|प्रसितं
प्रसित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound, fastened.<BR>—2 Devoted to, engaged in, occupied with; प्रसितावुदयापवर्गयोरुभयीं<BR> सिद्धिमुभाववापतुः R. 8. 23.<BR>—3 Intent on, longing for, craving after (with instr. or loc.); क्षितिपतेः<BR> प्रसितो वरिवस्यया Rām. Ch. 4. 85; लक्ष्म्या लक्ष्म्यां वा प्रसितः Sk.; R. 8. 23.<BR>—4 Very clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसितम्
प्रसित + .{@-तम्@} Pus, matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसितिः|प्रसिति
प्रसितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A net.<BR>—2 A ligament.<BR>—3 A tie, fetter.<BR>—4 An attack, assault.<BR>—5 A throw, shot.<BR>—6 Reach, extent.<BR>—7 A series, succession.<BR>—8 Power, authority, influence.<BR>—9 Ved. A flame.<BR>—10 A track, path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिध्
प्रसिध् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be accomplished or effected; शरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिध्येदकर्मणः Bg. 3. 8.<BR>—2 To succeed.<BR>—3 To be made known.<BR>—4 To be got or obtained; तपसैव प्रसिद्धपन्ति तपस्तेषां हि साधनम् Ms. 11. 237.<BR>—5 To be established. —6 To be decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1116-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्ध|प्रसिद्धः
प्रसिद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Renowned, famous, celebrated.<BR>—2 Decorated, ornamented, adorned; सालक्तकौ भूपतयः प्रसिद्धैर्ववन्दिरे<BR> मौलिभिरस्य पादौ R. 18. 41; यथा प्रसिद्धैर्मधुरं शिरोरुहैः Ku. 5. 9, 7. 16.<BR>—3 Excellent; द्रव्यैः प्रसिद्धैर्मद्यागः प्रतिमादिष्वमायिनः । भक्तस्य<BR> च यथालब्धैर्हृदि भावेन चैव हि ॥ Bhāg. 11. 27. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धा
प्रसिद्ध + .{@-द्धा@} A particular measure in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धिः|प्रसिद्धि
प्रसिद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Fame, celebrity, publicity, renown.<BR>—2 Success, accomplishment, fulfilment; आधिद्विषामा तपसां प्रसिद्धेः<BR> Ki. 3. 39; Ms. 4. 3; Bhāg. 11. 3. 3.<BR>—3 Ornament, decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसीदिका
प्रसीदिका A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुत
प्रसुत <i>a.</i> Pressed or pressing continuously (as Soma juice);<BR> अहरहर्ह सुतः प्रसुतो भवति Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्त
प्रसुप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Asleep, sleepy.<BR>—2 Fast asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्तिः|प्रसुप्ति
प्रसुप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Sleepiness.<BR>—2 Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसु
प्रसु, -सू €1 P., €2. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To beget, generate, produce.<BR>—2 To bring forth, be delivered of; पुत्ररत्नं प्रासोष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसु, -सू €1 P., €2. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To beget, generate, produce.<BR>—2 To bring forth, be delivered of; पुत्ररत्नं प्रासोष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवः|प्रसव
प्रसवः<BR>—1 Begetting, generation, procreation, birth, production; प्रसवविकारो<BR> स्त्रीणां द्वित्रिचतुःप्रभृति संप्रसूतौ वा । हीनातिरिक्तकाले च देशकुलसंक्षयो<BR> भवति Bṛ. S.<BR>—2 Child-birth, delivery, confinement; an in आसन्नप्रसवा.<BR>—3 Offspring, progeny, young ones, children; oft. at the end of comp.;<BR> केवलं वीरप्रसवा भूयाः U. 1; Ku. 7. 87.<BR>—4 Source, origin, birth-place (fig. also); प्रसवः कर्मफलस्य भूरिणः Ki. 2. 43.<BR>—5 Flower, blossom; प्रसवविभूतिषु भूरुहां विरक्तः Śi. 7. 42; नीता<BR> लोध्रप्रसवरजसा पाण्डुतामानने श्रीः Me. 67; कुन्दप्रसवशिथिलं<BR> जीवितम् 113; R. 9. 28; Ku. 1. 55, 4. 14; Ś. 5. 9; Māl. 9. 27, 31; U. 2. 20.<BR>—6 A fruit, product; यज्ञप्रसववर्जिताः Mb. 12. 180. 46.<BR>—7 Ved. Extracting Soma juice; अपुत्रः प्रसवेनार्थी वनवासमुपावसत् Mb. 13. 4. 6.<BR>—7 Setting in motion.<BR>—9 A current, stream.<BR>—10 Excitement, animation.<BR>—11 Enjoining, ordering.<BR>—12 Assistance, help.<BR>—13 pursuit, acquisition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसवोन्मुख^1, प्रसवकालः, प्रसवगृहम्, प्रसवधर्मिन्, प्रसवबन्धनम्, प्रसववेदना, प्रसवव्यथा, प्रसवस्थली, प्रसवस्थानम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवोन्मुख
प्रसवः + -उन्मुख^1 <i>a.</i> about to be delivered or confined; पतिः प्रतीतः<BR> प्रसवोन्मुखीं प्रियां ददर्श R. 3. 12.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवकालः|प्रसवकाल
प्रसवः + -कालः the time of delivery or bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवगृहम्
प्रसवः + -गृहम् a lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवधर्मिन्
प्रसवः + -धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> productive, prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवबन्धनम्
प्रसवः + -बन्धनम् the foot-stalk of a leaf or flower, peduncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसववेदना
प्रसवः + -वेदना, -व्यथा pangs of child-birth, throes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवव्यथा
प्रसवः + -वेदना, -व्यथा pangs of child-birth, throes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थली
प्रसवः + -स्थली a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थानम्
प्रसवः + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a place for delivery.<BR>—2 a nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवकः|प्रसवक
प्रसवकः The Piyāla tree; Buchanania Latifolia (Mar. चारोळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवनम्
प्रसवनम्<BR>—1 Bringing forth.<BR>—2 Bearing children, fecundity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवन्ती
प्रसवन्ती <i>f.</i> A woman in labour; न पश्येत् प्रसवन्तीं च तेजस्कामो<BR> द्विजोत्तमः Ms. 4. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवितृ
प्रसवितृ <i>m.</i> A father, procreator; स्वयं वेदान् व्यस्यञ्छमितकुरुवंशप्रसविता Pt. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवित्री
प्रसवित्री A mother; bestowing progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू <i>a.</i> Bringing forth, bearing, giving birth to; स्त्रीप्रसूश्चाधिवेत्तव्या<BR> Y. 1. 73. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 A mother; मातरपितरौ प्रसूजनयितारौ Ak. ‘parents’; Śi. 9. 14.<BR>—2 A mare.<BR>—3 A spreading creeper.<BR>—4 A young shoot, tender grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूका
प्रसूका A mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूत|प्रसूतं|प्रसूतः
प्रसूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Begotten, engendered; तच्च भीष्मप्रसूतं (दुःखं) मे तं<BR> जहीश्वर Mb. 5. 178. 5.<BR>—2 Brought forth, born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतम्
प्रसूत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A flower.<BR>—2 Any productive source.<BR>—3 (In Sāṅkhya) The primordial essence or matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूता
प्रसूत + .{@-ता@} A woman recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिः|प्रसूति
प्रसूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Procreation, begetting, generation.<BR>—2 Bringing forth, bearing, delivering, giving birth to; ऊर्ध्वं प्रसूतेश्चरितुं<BR> यतिष्ये R. 14. 66.<BR>—3 Calving.<BR>—4 Laying eggs; नवप्रसूतिर्वरटा तपस्विनी N. 1. 135.<BR>—5 Birth, production, generation; प्रसूतिं चकमे तस्मिंस्त्रैलोक्यप्रभवोऽपि<BR> यत् R. 10. 53.<BR>—6 Appearance, coming forth, growth (of flowers &c.); आरण्यकोपात्तफलप्रसूतिः R. 5. 15.<BR>—7 A product, production.<BR>—8 Offspring, progeny, issue; R. 1. 25, 77, 2. 4, 5. 7; प्रसूतिभाजः<BR> सर्गस्य तावेव पितरौ स्मृतौ Ku. 2. 7; नूनं प्रसूतिविकलेन मया<BR> प्रसिक्तं धौताश्रुशेषमुदकं पितरः पिबन्ति Ś. 6. 24.<BR>—9 A producer, generator, procreator; न केवलानां पयसां प्रसूतिम् R. 2. 63.<BR>—10 A mother.<BR>—11 A cause (कारण); जगत्प्रसूतिः Ki. 4. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसूतिजम्, प्रसूतिवायुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिजम्
प्रसूतिः + -जम् pain resulting as a necessary consequence of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिवायुः|प्रसूतिवायु
प्रसूतिः + -वायुः wind produced in the womb during the pangs of travail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका A woman recently delivered; प्रसूतिकामस्नपयन् मिलिताः<BR> कुलयोषितः Śiva B. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसून|प्रसूनं
प्रसून <i>p. p.</i> Produced, born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनम्
प्रसून + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A flower; लतायां पूर्वलूनायां प्रसूनस्यागमः कुतः U. 5. 20; R. 2. 10.<BR>—2 A bud, blossom.<BR>—3 A fruit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसूनाञ्जलि, प्रसूनरससंभवा, प्रसूनवर्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनाञ्जलि
प्रसून + -अञ्जलि <i>a.</i> = पुष्पाञ्जलि. {@-इषुः, -बाणः, -वाणः@}<BR> epithets of the god of love; प्रसूनबाणाद्वयवादिनी सा कापि द्विजेनोपनिषतपिकेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनरससंभवा
प्रसून + -रससंभवा <i>f.</i> the sugar prepared from flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनवर्षः|प्रसूनवर्ष
प्रसून + -वर्षः a shower of flowers (rained from heaven).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनकम्
प्रसूनकम्<BR>—1 A flower.<BR>—2 A bud, blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनकः|प्रसूनक|प्रसूनकं
प्रसूनकम् + .{@-कः@} A kind of Kadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू €6 P.<BR>—1 To urge, impel, bid.<BR>—2 To hurl, throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृ
प्रसृ P.<BR>—1 To flow forth, spring, arise, proceed; लोहिताद्या महानद्यः प्रसस्रुस्तत्र चासकृत् Mb.<BR>—2 To go forth, advance; वेलानिलाय प्रमृता भुजङ्गाः R. 13. 12; अन्वेषणप्रसृते<BR> च मित्रगणे Dk.<BR>—3 To spread, spread round; कृशानुः किं साक्षात् प्रसरति दिशो नैष नियतम्<BR> K. P. 10; प्रसरति तृणमध्ये लब्धवृद्धिः क्षणेन (दवाग्निः) Ṛs. 1. 25.<BR>—4 To spread, prevail, pervade; प्रसरति परिमाथी कोऽप्ययं देहदाहः<BR> Māl. 1. 41; भित्त्वा भित्त्वा प्रसरति वलात् कोऽपि चेतोविकारः U. 3. 36.<BR>—5 To be stretched, to extend; न मे हस्तौ प्रसरतः Ś. 2.<BR>—6 To be disposed or inclined to (do a thing), move; न मे उचितेषु करणीयेषु<BR> हस्तपादं प्रसरति Ś. 4; प्रसरति मनः कायारम्भं Pt. 3. 181.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">Page1118-1</a>]<BR>—7 To prevail, begin, commence; प्रससार चोत्सवः Ks. 16. 85.<BR>—8 To be long, be lengthened; यदि तु तव समागमे तथैव प्रसरति<BR> सुभ्रु ततः कृती भवेयम् V. 3. 22.<BR>—9 To grow strong or intense; प्रसृततरं सख्यम् Dk.<BR>—10 To pass away (as time).<BR>—11 To break forth or out (as fire).<BR>—12 To be displaced (as the humours of the body). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To spread, stretch; जलनिधिवेगसहं प्रसार्य देहम् Bk. 10. 44.<BR>—2 To stretch forward, extend, hold out (as the hand); कालः सर्वजनान्<BR> प्रसारितकरो गृह्णाति दूरादपि Pt. 2. 20.<BR>—3 To spread out or expose for sale; क्रेतारः क्रीणीयुरिति बुद्धया आपणे<BR> प्रसारितं क्रय्यम् Sk.; Ms. 5. 129; वणिजो न प्रसारयन् Rām. 2. 48. 4.<BR>—4 To open wide, expand (as eyes).<BR>—5 To publish, promulgate.<BR>—6 To prosecute. —7 (In gram.) To change a semi-vowel into the corresponding vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1117-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरः|प्रसर
प्रसरः<BR>—1 Going forward, advancing; सहसा विनयेन वारितप्रसरः Ś. 1. 28.<BR>—2 Free or unimpeded motion, free scope; access or course; प्रतिषिद्धप्रसरेषु<BR> जाग्रतौ R. 8. 23, 16. 20; लब्धप्रसरा Mu. 3. 5; H. 1. 186.<BR>—3 Spreading, diffusion, extension, expansion, dilation; दयितावलोकविकसन्नयनप्रसरप्रणुन्नमिव<BR> वारिरुहम् Śi. 9. 71.<BR>—4 Extent, dimension, great quantity; त्वष्टुः सदाभ्यासगृहीतशिल्पविज्ञानसंपत्प्रसरस्य<BR> सीमा Śi. 3. 35.<BR>—5 Prevalence, influence; समस्तापः कामं मनसिजनिदाघप्रसरयोः Ś. 3. 8.<BR>—6 A stream, flow, torrent, flood; पपात स्वेदाम्बुप्रसर इव हर्षाश्रुनिकरः<BR> Gīt. 11; स्नेहप्रसरसम्प्लुतः Bhāg. 3. 2. 5.<BR>—7 A group, multitude.<BR>—8 War, battle.<BR>—9 An iron arrow.<BR>—10 Speed.<BR>—11 Affectionate solicitation.<BR>—12 (In medicine) Morbid displacement of the humours of the body.<BR>—13 Destruction, ruin.<BR>—14 Opportunity, room (अवकाश); यो हि विक्लवया बुद्ध्या प्रसरं<BR> शत्रवे दिशेत् Rām. 7. 68. 19.<BR>—15 Range (of the eye).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरम्
प्रसरः + .{@-रम्@} (In music) A kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणम्
प्रसरणम्<BR>—1 Going forth, running or streaming forth.<BR>—2 Escaping, running away.<BR>—3 Spreading forth or abroad.<BR>—4 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>—5 Amiability.<BR>—6 Morbid displacement of the humours of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणिः|प्रसरणि
प्रसरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> Surrounding an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणी
प्रसरणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> Surrounding an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारः|प्रसार
प्रसारः<BR>—1 Spreading, extending.<BR>—2 Spread, diffusion, extension, expansion.<BR>—3 Stretching out.<BR>—4 Spreading over the country to forage.<BR>—5 Opening (the mouth).<BR>—6 A traderʼs shop; Nalachampū.<BR>—7 Raising (dust); B. R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारणम्
प्रसारणम्<BR>—1 Spreading abroad, extending, increase, diffusing, expanding.<BR>—2 Stretching out; as in बाहुप्रसारणम्.<BR>—3 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>—4 Spreading over the country for fuel and grass.<BR>—5 The change of a semivowel (य् र् and व्) into a vowel; see संप्रसारण.<BR>—6 Displaying, unfolding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारिणी
प्रसारिणी Surrounding an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारित
प्रसारित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Expanded, spread, diffused, extended.<BR>—2 Stretched out (as hands.).<BR>—3 Exhibited, laid<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">Page1118-2</a>]<BR> out, exposed (for sale).<BR>—4 Published, promulgated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसारितगात्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारितगात्र
प्रसारित + -गात्र <i>a.</i> With out-stretched limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत|प्रसृतं|प्रसृतः
प्रसृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gone forward.<BR>—2 Stretched out, extended.<BR>—3 Spread, diffused.<BR>—4 Long, lengthened.<BR>—5 Engaged in, attached to; अष्टकापितृदेवत्यमित्ययं प्रसृतो जनः.<BR> Rām. 2. 108. 14.<BR>—6 Swift, or quick.<BR>—7 Manifested, displayed; न तेजस्तेजस्वी प्रसृतमपरेषां विषहते U. 6. 14.<BR>—8 Modest, humble.<BR>—9 Devoted (निष्ठावत्); त्यागिनः प्रसृतस्येह नोच्छित्तिर्विद्यते क्वचित्<BR> Mb. 12. 12. 19.<BR>—10 Knowing subtle meaning (सूक्ष्मार्थगामिन्); Mb. 12. 118. 14.<BR>—11 = पक्व; अतिथिः प्रसृताग्रभुक् Mb. 13. 35. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतः|प्रसृत|प्रसृतं
प्रसृत + .{@-तः@} The palm of the hand stretched out and hollowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतः|प्रसृत|प्रसृतं
प्रसृत + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A measure equal to two <i>palas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतम्
प्रसृत + .{@-तः, -तम्@} A measure equal to two <i>palas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतम्
प्रसृत + .{@-तम्@} Grass, plants etc; agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृता
प्रसृत + .{@-ता@} The leg.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रसृतजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतजः|प्रसृतज
प्रसृत + -जः a particular class of sons, an adulterine (कुण्डगोलकरूप);<BR> आत्मा पुत्रश्च विज्ञेयस्तस्यानन्तरजश्च यः । निरुक्तजश्च विज्ञेयः<BR> सुतः प्रसृतजस्तथा ॥ Mb. 13. 49. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतिः|प्रसृति
प्रसृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Advance, progress.<BR>—2 Flowing.<BR>—3 The plam of the hand stretched out and hollowed; निर्माय चक्षुःप्रसृतिचुलुकितम्<BR> N. 15. 82 ‘looking at him eagerly with their large eyes’; cf. 20. 11-12.<BR>—4 A handful (considered as a measure equal to two <i>palas</i>); परिक्षीणः<BR> कश्चित् स्पृहयति यवानां प्रसृतये Bh. 2. 45; Y. 2. 112; पृथुकप्रसृतिं<BR> राजन्न प्रायच्छदवाङ्मुखः Bhāg. 10. 81. 5.<BR>—5 Swiftness, haste; वर्धिताने प्रसृत्या वै विनताकुलकर्तृभिः Mb. 5. 101. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत्वर
प्रसृत्वर <i>a.</i> Spreading about; (दावानल) प्रसृत्वरशिखावलीविकलितं<BR> मदीयं मनः Bv. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृमर
प्रसृमर <i>a.</i> Flowing forth, dropping, distilling; क्रोधाग्निप्रसृमरधूमधूम्रधामा<BR> Śiva B. 24. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृज्
प्रसृज् €6 P.<BR>—1 To leave, abandon.<BR>—2 To let loose.<BR>—3 To sow, scatter.<BR>—4 To injure, hurt.<BR>—5 To dismiss, set aside, send back; त्वत्प्रसृष्टं माभिवदेत् प्रतीत Kaṭh. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृष्ट
प्रसृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Laid aside, dismissed.<BR>—2 Hurt, injured.<BR>—3 Uncontrolled.<BR>—4 Given up, renounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृष्टा
प्रसृष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@}<BR>—1 A finger stretched forth or extended; (अङ्गुल्यः प्रसृता यास्तु ताः<BR> प्रसृष्टा उदीरिताः)<BR>—2 A particular movement in fighting (Mar. चपेटा); Mb. 4. 13. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृप्
प्रसृप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go forth, proceed; मृगाः प्रससृपुर्वामम् Bk. 14. 20.<BR>—2 To spread, circulate (fig.); रुधिरेण प्रसर्पता Mb.; आलर्कं<BR> विषमिव सर्वतः प्रसृप्तम् U. 1. 40.<BR>—3 To creep or crawl forth or along.<BR>—4 To set in (as darkness).<BR>—5 To advance, progress; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पः|प्रसर्प
प्रसर्पः Going to the part of the sacrificial enclosure called सदस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पणम्
प्रसर्पणम्<BR>—1 Going or moving forward, advancing.<BR>—2 Pervading, spreading in all directions.<BR>—3 Entering the सदस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पित
प्रसर्पित <i>p. p.</i> Spread, diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पिन्
प्रसर्पिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going forth, progressing, advancing.<BR>—2 Creeping along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1118-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेकः|प्रसेक
प्रसेकः —1 Flowing forth, oozing, dropping —2 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>—3 Emission, discharge; मत्तद्विरेफपरिपीतमधुप्रसेकः Ṛs. 3. 6.<BR>—4 Vomiting.<BR>—5 Watering of the mouth or nose.<BR>—6 The bowl of a spoon or ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेकिन्
प्रसेकिन् <i>m.</i> A kind of disease; मांसपिण्डवदुद्रताः प्रसेकिनोऽन्तःपूयवेदनावन्तोऽश्वाऽपानवदुद्धृतौष्ठाः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिका
प्रसेदिका A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवः|प्रसेव
प्रसेवः, -प्रसेवकः<BR>—1 A sack, bag for grain.<BR>—2 A leathern bottle.<BR>—3 A small instrument of wood placed under the neck of the lute to make<BR> the sound deeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवकः|प्रसेवक
प्रसेवः, -प्रसेवकः<BR>—1 A sack, bag for grain.<BR>—2 A leathern bottle.<BR>—3 A small instrument of wood placed under the neck of the lute to make<BR> the sound deeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्द्|प्रस्कंद्
प्रस्कन्द् €1 P.<BR>—1 To leap forward, up or down; गदां प्रगृह्य वेगेन प्रचस्कन्द रथोत्तमात् Mb. 6. 95. 77.<BR>—2 To fall upon, attack.<BR>—3 To shed, spill; एते प्रस्कन्दन्ति Praśna. Up. 1. 13. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cross (a river &c.)<BR>—2 To pour out (as an oblation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दनम्
प्रस्कन्दनम्<BR>—1 Springing across or leaping over.<BR>—2 Evacuation by stool, diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दनः|प्रस्कन्दन|प्रस्कंदन|प्रस्कंदनं|प्रस्कन्दनं
प्रस्कन्दनम् + .{@-नः@} An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दिका|प्रस्कंदिका
प्रस्कन्दिका Dysentery; प्रस्कन्दिकामिव प्राप्तो ध्यात्वा ब्रूते स्म<BR> जाम्बवान् Bk. 7. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्न|प्रस्कन्नः
प्रस्कन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sprung forth.<BR>—2 Fallen, dropped, lost, gone; प्रस्कन्नं पिबतः प्राणैर्यत् किञ्चिज्जगृहुः<BR> स्म तत् Bhāg. 8. 7. 47.<BR>—3 Defeated.<BR>—4 Having attacked, assailed; एते विनिहताः सर्वे प्रस्कन्नाः पाण्डुवाहिनीम् Mb. 9. 18. 22.<BR>—5 Shed, spilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्नः|प्रस्कन्न
प्रस्कन्न + .{@-न्नः@}<BR>—1 An outcast.<BR>—2 A sinner, transgressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कुन्दः|प्रस्कुन्द|प्रस्कुंद|प्रस्कुंदः
प्रस्कुन्दः An altar of a circular shape; प्रस्कुन्देन प्रतिस्तब्धश्छिन्नमूल<BR> इव द्रुमः Mb. 5. 73. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्खल्
प्रस्खल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To jostle; रथाः प्रचस्खलुश्चाश्वाः Bk. 14. 98.<BR>—2 To stagger, stumble, reel, totter; सूतीगृहमगात्तूर्णं प्रस्खलन्मुक्तमूर्धजः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्खलनम्
प्रस्खलनम्<BR>—1 Staggering.<BR>—2 Stumbling, falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तब्ध
प्रस्तब्ध <i>p. p.</i> Stiff, rigid; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरः|प्रस्तर
प्रस्तरः<BR>—1 A couch of leaves and flowers.<BR>—2 A couch or bed in general; इष्टकाप्रस्तरे चैव कण्टकप्रस्तरे तथा<BR> (शयनम्) Mb. 12. 303. 10.<BR>—3 A flat surface or top, level, plain.<BR>—4 A stone, rock; पर्वतप्रतिमं भाति पर्वतप्रस्तराश्रितम् Mb. 3. 142. 16.<BR>—5 A precious stone, gem.<BR>—6 A paragraph, section of a work.<BR>—7 A handful of <i>darbha</i> grass.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्तरप्रहरणन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरप्रहरणन्यायः
प्रस्तरः + -प्रहरणन्यायः a rule of interpretation according to which the<BR> matter mentioned in the instrumental should be construed as being subsidiary<BR> to that which is mentioned in the accusative. This न्याय is mentioned<BR> by जौमिनि and शबर at MS. 3. 2. 11-14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरणम्
प्रस्तरणम्, -णा<BR>—1 A bed, couch.<BR>—2 A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरणा
प्रस्तरणम्, -णा<BR>—1 A bed, couch.<BR>—2 A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरिणी
प्रस्तरिणी Elephantopus Scaber (गोजिव्हा; Mar. पाथरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तारः|प्रस्तार
प्रस्तारः<BR>—1 Strewing, spreading out, covering with.<BR>—2 A bed of leaves and flowers.<BR>—3 A bed or couch<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">Page1119-2</a>]<BR> in general.<BR>—4 A flat surface, level, plain.<BR>—5 A thicket, wood.<BR>—6 (In prosody) A tabular representation of the long and short vowels<BR> of a metre with all possible varieties.<BR>—7 A process in preparing minerals.<BR>—8 A flight of steps (leading down to water; Mar. घाट); मणिप्रवालप्रस्तारम्<BR> Mb. 3. 145. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तार्यर्मम्
प्रस्तार्यर्मम् A kind of eye-disease; समन्ताद् विस्तृतः श्यावो, रक्तो<BR> वा मांससंचयः । संनिपातेन दोषाणां प्रस्तार्यर्मं तदुच्यते Vaidyaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तिरः|प्रस्तिर
प्रस्तिरः A bed of leaves and flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीत|प्रस्तीतः
प्रस्तीत, -म <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Making a noise, sounded.<BR>—2 Crowded together, swarming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीम
प्रस्तीत, -म <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Making a noise, sounded.<BR>—2 Crowded together, swarming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तु
प्रस्तु €2 U.<BR>—1 To praise.<BR>—2 To begin, commence; प्रापयन् मनसस्तुल्या यत्र तत् प्रस्तुतं रणम्<BR> Rām. 7. 22. 8; प्रस्तूयतां विवादवस्तु M. 1.<BR>—3 To cause, produce; यत्रालोकपथावतारिणि रतिं प्रस्तौति नेत्रोत्सवः Mv. 2. 45; also Māl. 5. 9.<BR>—4 To say, relate, propound. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To relate, allude to, tell; शाकुन्तलादीनितिहासवादान् प्रस्तावितानन्यपरैर्वचोभिः<BR> Māl. 3. 3; अथापृच्छदृषिस्तत्र कश्चित् प्रस्तावयन् कथाः Mb. 1. 1. 6.<BR>—2 To begin, commence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तवः|प्रस्तव
प्रस्तवः<BR>—1 A song or hymn of praise.<BR>—2 A fit time or opportunity; see प्रस्ताव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावः|प्रस्ताव
प्रस्तावः<BR>—1 Beginning, commencement.<BR>—2 An introduction.<BR>—3 Mention, allusion, reference; नाममात्रप्रस्तावः Ś. 7.<BR>—4 An occasion, opportunity, time, season; fit or proper time; त्वराप्रस्तावोयं<BR> न खलु परिहासस्य विषयः Māl. 9. 45; शिष्याय बृहतां पत्युः प्रस्तावमदिशद्<BR> दृशा Śi. 2. 68.<BR>—5 The occasion of a discourse, subject, topic.<BR>—6 The prologue of a drama; see प्रस्तावना below.<BR>—7 The prelude or introductory words of a <i>Sāman</i>; लोकेषु पञ्चविधं<BR> सामोपासीत पृथिवी हिंकारोऽग्निः प्रस्तावः˚ Ch. Up. 2. 2. 1.<BR>—8 An introductory praise. ({@प्रस्तावे@} <i>ind.</i> on a suitable occasion,<BR> seasonably. {@प्रस्तावेन@}<BR>—1 incidentally, occasionally.<BR>—2 suitably).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्तावयज्ञः, प्रस्तावसदृश<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावयज्ञः|प्रस्तावयज्ञ
प्रस्तावः + -यज्ञः a conversation in which each interlocutor takes a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावसदृश
प्रस्तावः + -सदृश <i>a.</i> suited to the occasion, appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावना
प्रस्तावना<BR>—1 Causing to be praised or mentioned, praising, praise.<BR>—2 Beginning, commencement; आर्य बालचरितप्रस्तावनाडिण्डिमः Mv. 1. 54.<BR>—3 An introduction, preface, exordium (in general); प्रस्तावना इयं<BR> कपटनाटकस्य Māl. 2.<BR>—4 Sounding forth.<BR>—5 An introductory dialogue (the prologue) at the beginning of a drama<BR> between the manager and one of the actors, which, after giving an account<BR> of the author and his qualifications &c., introduces the audience to the<BR> incidents of the drama; (for definition, see आमुख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावित
प्रस्तावित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Begun, commenced.<BR>—2 Mentioned, referred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुत|प्रस्तुतः
प्रस्तुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Praised, eulogized.<BR>—2 Begun, commenced.<BR>—3 Accomplished, done, effected.<BR>—4 Happened.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">Page1120-1</a>]<BR>—5 Approached.<BR>—6 Proposed, declared, under discussion, taken in hand.<BR>—7 Expected, desired.<BR>—8 Ready, prepared.<BR>—9 Executed with effort or energy.<BR>—10 Made or consisting of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुतम्
प्रस्तुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The matter in hand, the subject under discussion or consideration;<BR> अपि स्मरति नः साधो गोविन्दः प्रस्तुते क्वचित् Bhāg. 10. 47. 42; अधुना<BR> प्रस्तुतमनुस्रियताम्.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) Forming the subject of discussion, the उपमेय; see<BR> प्रकृत; अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव प्रस्तुताश्रया K. P. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्तुताङ्कुरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1119-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुताङ्कुरः|प्रस्तुताङ्कुर|प्रस्तुतांकुर
प्रस्तुत + -अङ्कुरः a figure of speech in which a reference is made to a<BR> passing circumstance to bring out something latent in the hearerʼs mind;<BR> see Candr. 5. 64 and Kuval. under प्रस्तुताङ्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुतिः|प्रस्तुति
प्रस्तुतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. Praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तोतृ
प्रस्तोतृ <i>m.</i> N. of the assistant of the उद्रातृ; स वै खलु प्रस्तोता<BR> साम प्रस्तौति Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तोभः|प्रस्तोभ
प्रस्तोभः Allusion, reference to; श्रुत्वा गाथां देवयानी मेने प्रस्तोभमात्मनः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 19. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्था
प्रस्था €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To set out, depart; पारसीकांस्ततो जेतुं प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना<BR> R. 4. 60; Ku. 3. 22.<BR>—2 To advance, march towards.<BR>—3 To walk, move; प्रस्थितायां प्रतिष्ठेथाः R. 1. 89.<BR>—4 To stand firmly.<BR>—5 To be established.<BR>—6 To approach, come near. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to retire. —2 To send away, dismiss, despatch; तौ दम्पती<BR> स्वां प्रति राजधानीं प्रस्थापयामास वशी वशिष्ठः R. 2. 70.<BR>—2 To drive away, banish, expel; अधः प्रस्थापिताश्वेन Ku. 6. 7.<BR>—4 To urge forward, push on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going to, visiting, abiding in; as in वानप्रस्थ.<BR>—2 Going on a journey.<BR>—3 Spreading, expanding.<BR>—4 Firm, stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थः|प्रस्थ
प्रस्थ + .{@-स्थः, -स्थम्@}<BR>—1 A level expanse, level plain; as in ओषधिप्रस्थ, इन्दप्रस्थ &c.<BR>—2 Table-land on the top of a mountain; प्रस्थं हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगन्धि<BR> किंचित् क्कणत्किन्नरमध्युवास Ku. 1. 54; Me. 60.<BR>—3 The top or peak of a mountain; Śi. 4. 11 (where it has sense 4 also).<BR>—4 A particular measure of capacity equal to thirty-two <i>palas</i>.<BR>—5 Anything measuring a <i>prastha</i> (a seer); प्रस्थभुग्देवदत्त इत्युच्यते ।<BR> यद्यपि सूपशाकादिभिरधिकः प्रस्थो भवति तथापि भुजौ प्रस्थो निर्दिश्यते ।<BR> व्यञ्जनानि ओदनार्थानि ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 29; प्रस्थं वाहसहस्रेषु<BR> यात्रार्थ चैव कोटिषु Mb. 12. 288. 30; (com. प्रस्थं पुरुषाहारपरिमितं धान्यम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्थपुष्पः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थम्
प्रस्थ + .{@-स्थः, -स्थम्@}<BR>—1 A level expanse, level plain; as in ओषधिप्रस्थ, इन्दप्रस्थ &c.<BR>—2 Table-land on the top of a mountain; प्रस्थं हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगन्धि<BR> किंचित् क्कणत्किन्नरमध्युवास Ku. 1. 54; Me. 60.<BR>—3 The top or peak of a mountain; Śi. 4. 11 (where it has sense 4 also).<BR>—4 A particular measure of capacity equal to thirty-two <i>palas</i>.<BR>—5 Anything measuring a <i>prastha</i> (a seer); प्रस्थभुग्देवदत्त इत्युच्यते ।<BR> यद्यपि सूपशाकादिभिरधिकः प्रस्थो भवति तथापि भुजौ प्रस्थो निर्दिश्यते ।<BR> व्यञ्जनानि ओदनार्थानि ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 29; प्रस्थं वाहसहस्रेषु<BR> यात्रार्थ चैव कोटिषु Mb. 12. 288. 30; (com. प्रस्थं पुरुषाहारपरिमितं धान्यम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्थपुष्पः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थपुष्पः|प्रस्थपुष्प
प्रस्थ + -पुष्पः a variety of holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थंपच
प्रस्थंपच <i>a.</i> Cooking a <i>Prastha</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानम्
प्रस्थानम्<BR>—1 Going or setting forth, departure, moving, walking; प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलम्बनार्थम्<BR> Ś. 5. 3; R. 4. 88; Me. 43; प्रस्थानं वलयैः कृतम् Amaru. 36.<BR>—2 Coming to; मन्ये मत्पावनायैव प्रस्थानं भवतामिह Ku. 6. 61.<BR>—3 Sending away, despatching.<BR>—4 Procession, march.<BR>—5 A march, the march of an army or assailant; प्रस्थाने भूमिपालो दशदिवमसभिव्याप्य<BR> नैकत्र तिष्ठेत.<BR>—6 A method, system.<BR>—7 Death, dying.<BR>—8 An inferior kind of drama; see S. D. 276, 544.<BR>—9 A religious school, sect; प्रभिन्ने प्रस्थाने परिमितमदः पथ्यमिति<BR> च Śivamahimna 7.<BR>—10 Religious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-2" target="_blank">Page1120-2</a>]<BR> mendicancy; सप्रस्थानाः क्षात्रधर्मा विशिष्टाः Mb. 12. 64. 22.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रस्थानत्रयी, प्रस्थानत्रयम्, प्रस्थानदुन्दुभिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानत्रयी
प्रस्थानम् + -त्रयी, -त्रयम् Bhagwadgītā, Upaniṣadas and Brahmasūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानत्रयम्
प्रस्थानम् + -त्रयी, -त्रयम् Bhagwadgītā, Upaniṣadas and Brahmasūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1120-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

