प्रस्वृ
प्रस्वृ €1 P. To lengthen or prolate a tone in uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहन्
प्रहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To kill, slay; प्राघानिषत रक्षांसि येनाप्तानि वने मम । न प्रहण्मः<BR> कथं पापं वद पूर्वापकारिणम् Bk. 9. 102.<BR>—2 To strike, beat, hit; गदाप्रहततनुः<BR>—3 To strike, beat (a drum &c.); see प्रहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणनम्
प्रहणनम्<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—2 A kind of amorous sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहत|प्रहतं
प्रहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Wounded, killed, slain.<BR>—2 Beaten, struck (as a drum); स स्वयं प्रहतपुष्करः कृती R. 19. 14; Me. 66.<BR>—3 Repulsed, overcome, defeated.<BR>—4 Spread, expanded.<BR>—5 Contiguous.<BR>—6 Beaten, frequented (as a track).<BR>—7 Accomplished, learned.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहतमुरज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहतमुरज
प्रहत + -मुरज <i>a.</i> having drums beaten; resounding with the beating<BR> of drums; संगीताय प्रहतमुरजाः स्निग्धपर्जन्यघोषम् Me. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहतिः|प्रहति
प्रहतिः <i>f.</i> A stroke, blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणेमिः|प्रहणेमि
प्रहणे(ने)मिः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहनेमिः|प्रहनेमि
प्रहणे(ने)मिः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्
प्रहस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To laugh, smile; ततः प्रहस्यापभयः पुरंदरम् R. 3. 51.<BR>—2 To deride, ridicule, mock; हसन्तं प्रहसन्त्येता रुदन्तं प्ररुदन्ति च Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 To brighten up, look splendid, cheer up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसनम्
प्रहसनम्<BR>—1 Loud or violent laughter, laughing, mirth.<BR>—2 Ridicule, mockery, irony, joke; धिक् प्रहसनम् U. 4.<BR>—3 Satire, satirical writing.<BR>—4 A farce, a kind of low comedy; S. D. thus defines it:− भाणवत्संधिसंध्यङ्गलास्याङ्गाङ्कैर्विनिर्मितम् ।<BR> भवेत् प्रहसनं वृत्तं निन्द्यानां कविकल्पितम् ॥ 533 <i>et seq.</i><BR> <i>e. g.</i> कन्दर्पकेलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसन्ती|प्रहसंती
प्रहसन्ती<BR>—1 A kind of jasmine (पृथिका or वासन्ती q. v.).<BR>—2 A large firepan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1121-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसित
प्रहसित <i>p. p.</i> Laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसितम्
प्रहसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Laughter, mirth.<BR>—2 Displaying bright gaudy colours; Jātak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासः|प्रहास
प्रहासः<BR>—1 Violent or loud laughter.<BR>—2 Ridicule, derision.<BR>—3 Irony, satire.<BR>—4 A dancer, an actor.<BR>—5 N. of Śiva.<BR>—6 Appearance, display; प्रालम्बद्विगुणितचामरप्रहासः Ve. 2. 29.<BR>—7 N. of a place of pilgrimage; cf. प्रभास.<BR>—8 Splendour of colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासकः|प्रहासक
प्रहासकः A jester, buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासिन्
प्रहासिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing laughter, amusing, diverting.<BR>—2 Joking, jesting,<BR>—3 Smiling with; उन्मीलत्कुटजप्रहासिषु गिरेरालम्ब्य सानूनितः Māl. 9. 15.<BR>—4 Shining, resplendent; विकीर्णसप्तर्षिबलिप्रहासिभिः Ku. 5. 37.<BR>—5 Satirical. ━<i>m.</i> A jester, buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्तः|प्रहस्त
प्रहस्तः<BR>—1 The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR>—2 N. of a general of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहा
प्रहा €3 P.<BR>—1 To give up, forsake, abandon, relinquish; प्रजहाति यदा कामान्<BR> Bg. 2. 55, 39; मोदमेतौ प्रहास्येते Rām.<BR>—2 To let go, cast, discharge; प्रजहुः शूलपट्टिशान् Bk. 14. 23.<BR>—3 To depart from. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be forsaken or neglected.<BR>—2 To be lost, to perish.<BR>—3 To vanish, cease, disappear.<BR>—4 To be vanquished, to succumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहा
प्रहा Ved.<BR>—1 A good throw at dice.<BR>—2 Gain, advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणम्
प्रहाणम्<BR>—1 Abandoning, omitting, quitting; क्लेशप्रहाणमिह लब्धसबीजयोगाः Śi. 4. 55.<BR>—2 Abstraction, speculation, meditation.<BR>—3 Exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणिः|प्रहाणि
प्रहाणिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Abandoning.<BR>—2 Deficiency, want.<BR>—3 Cessation, disappearance.<BR>—4 Destruction; स त्वं जगत्त्राणखलप्रहाणये Bhāg. 9. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहापणम्
प्रहापणम्<BR>—1 Abandonment; न्याग्याया अपि ते लक्ष्म्याः कुर्वन्त्याशु प्रहापणम् Bk. 9. 104.<BR>—2 Departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीण|प्रहीणः
प्रहीण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, quitted, abandoned; धनं प्रहीणमाजह्नुः Bhāg. 1. 12. 33.<BR>—2 Cast off, worn out (as a garment).<BR>—3 Ceased, vanquished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीणम्
प्रहीण + .{@-णम्@} Destruction, removal, loss.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहीणजीवित, प्रहीणदोष<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीणजीवित
प्रहीण + -जीवित <i>a.</i> dead, slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीणदोष
प्रहीण + -दोष <i>a.</i> sinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहि|प्रहिः
प्रहि €5 P.<BR>—1 To send forth, propel.<BR>—2 To throw, discharge, shoot; विनाशात्तस्य वृक्षस्य रक्षस्तस्मै महोपलं<BR> प्रजिघाय R. 15. 21; Bk. 15. 121.<BR>—3 To send, despatch; हरिरस्मै हरिणीं सुराङ्गनां प्रजिघाय R. 8. 79, 11. 49, 12. 84;<BR> Bk. 15. 104.<BR>—4 To turn the eyes towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाय्यः|प्रहाय्य
प्रहाय्यः Ved. A messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहिः|प्रहि
प्रहिः A well<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहित|प्रहितं
प्रहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed, put forth.<BR>—2 Extended, stretched out.<BR>—3 Sent, despatched, directed; विचारमार्गप्रहितेन चेतसा Ku. 5. 42.<BR>—4 Discharged, shot (as an arrow).<BR>—5 Appointed.<BR>—6 Appropriate, suitable.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">Page1122-2</a>]<BR>—7 Imbedded (as nails).<BR>—8 Turned towards, cast upon (as eyes, mind).<BR>—9 Sent away, expelled; इयमद्य निशा पूर्वा सौमित्रे प्रहिता वनम्<BR> Rām. 2. 46. 2 (com. gives प्रहिता = प्राप्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहितम्
प्रहित + .{@-तम्@} A sauce, condiment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहितात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहितात्मन्
प्रहित + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहितंगम
प्रहितंगम <i>a.</i> Going on an errand or mission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतः|प्रहुत|प्रहुतं
प्रहुतः, -तम्<BR> An offering of food to all created beings (भूतयज्ञ),<BR> one of the five daily Yajñas to be performed by a householder; cf. अहुतं<BR> च हुतं चैव तथा प्रहुतमेव च । ब्राह्मपं हुतं प्राशितं च पञ्चयज्ञान्<BR> प्रचक्षते Ms. 3. 73; Bhāg. 7. 15. 49. It also means दर्शोष्टि (बलिहरण);<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतम्
प्रहुतः, -तम्<BR> An offering of food to all created beings (भूतयज्ञ),<BR> one of the five daily Yajñas to be performed by a householder; cf. अहुतं<BR> च हुतं चैव तथा प्रहुतमेव च । ब्राह्मपं हुतं प्राशितं च पञ्चयज्ञान्<BR> प्रचक्षते Ms. 3. 73; Bhāg. 7. 15. 49. It also means दर्शोष्टि (बलिहरण);<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतिः|प्रहुति
प्रहुतिः <i>f.</i> Ved. An excellent oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृ
प्रहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To strike, strike at, beat; लत्तया प्रहरति ‘kicks’; दयापरोऽभूः<BR> प्रहरन्नपि त्वम् R. 5. 58; Ku. 3. 70; Bk. 9. 7.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, wound (with loc.); आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR> Ś. 1. 11; R. 2. 62, 7. 59, 11. 84, 15. 3.<BR>—3 To attack, assault.<BR>—4 To throw, cast, hurl (with loc. or dat.).<BR>—5 To seize upon.<BR>—6 To offer, present (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरः|प्रहर
प्रहरः The eighth part of a whole day, a watch (a period roughly<BR> reckoned at 3 hours); प्रहरे प्रहरेऽसहोच्चारितानि गामानयेत्यादिपदानि<BR> न प्रमाणम् T. S.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहरकुटुम्बी, प्रहरविरतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरकुटुम्बी
प्रहरः + -कुटुम्बी a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरविरतिः|प्रहरविरति
प्रहरः + -विरतिः the end of a watch (at 9 oʼclock in the forenoon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरकः|प्रहरक
प्रहरकः<BR>—1 A watch; प्रहरकमपनीय स्वं निदिद्रासतोच्चैः Śi. 11. 4.<BR>—2 Striking the hours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणम्
प्रहरणम्<BR>—1 Striking, beating.<BR>—2 Casting, throwing.<BR>—3 Assailing, attacking.<BR>—4 Hurting.<BR>—5 Removing, expelling.<BR>—6 A weapon, missile; या (उर्वशी) सुकुमारं प्रहरणं महेन्द्रस्य<BR> V. 1; Bhāg. 4. 26. 2; R. 13. 73; Mk. 5. 12; नानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः<BR> Bg. 1. 9; Māl. 8. 9.<BR>—7 War, battle, fight.<BR>—8 A covered litter or car.<BR>—9 The box of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणकलिका
प्रहरणकलिका <i>f.</i> N. of a metre with each quarter of fourteen<BR> syllables; ननभनलघुगैः प्रहरणकलिका V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणीयम्
प्रहरणीयम् A missile, weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरत्
प्रहरत् <i>m.</i> A warrior; रामः प्रहरतां वरः Mb. 3. 83. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिन्
प्रहरिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A watchman.<BR>—2 A bellman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्तृ|प्रहर्त्तृ
प्रहर्तृ <i>a.</i> or <i>s.</i><BR>—1 One who strikes or beats, an assailant.<BR>—2 Fighting, a combatant, fighter.<BR>—3 Shooting, a shooter, an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारः|प्रहार
प्रहारः<BR>—1 Striking, beating, hitting; मतकल्पः प्रहारार्तो जीवन्नपि विशुद्धपति Y. 3. 248.<BR>—2 Wounding, killing.<BR>—3 A stroke, blow, hit, knock, thump; प्रहारमूर्च्छपगमे रथस्थाः<BR> R. 7. 44; मुष्टिप्रहार, तलप्रहार &c.<BR>—4 A cut or thrust, as in खड्गप्रहार.<BR>—5 A kick; as in पादप्रहार; लत्ताप्रहार.<BR>—6 Shooting.<BR>—7 A battle (रण); प्रहारे च पराकान्तः शूरः पञ्चत्वमागतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">Page1123-1</a>]<BR> Rām. 4. 23. 12.<BR>—8 A Necklace.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहारार्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1122-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारार्त|प्रहारार्त्त
प्रहारः + -आर्त <i>a.</i> wounded by a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारार्तम्
प्रहारः + -आर्त + .({@-र्तम्@}) acute pain caused by a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारणम्
प्रहारणम् A desirable gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारिन्
प्रहारिन् <i>m.</i> A good fighter, champion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृत
प्रहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Beaten, struck, hit, wounded.<BR>—2 Seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृतम्
प्रहृत + .{@-तम्@} A blow, stroke, hit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्
प्रहृष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be glad, to rejoice; न प्रहृष्येत् प्रियं प्राप्य Bg. 5. 20, 11. 36.<BR>—2 To stand on end, bristle (as hair of the body).<BR>—3 To rejoice beforehand, anticipate pleasure. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To gladden, exhilarate, delight.<BR>—2 To encourage, inspirit; प्रहर्षयेद्वलं व्यूह्य तांश्च सम्यक् परीक्षयेत् Ms. 7. 194.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षः|प्रहर्ष
प्रहर्षः<BR>—1 Extreme joy, exultation, rapture; गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव नात्मनि R. 3. 17.<BR>—2 Erection of the male organ; तं विचिन्तयतः शापं प्रहर्षः समजायत<BR> Mb. 1. 125. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षणम्
प्रहर्षणम्<BR>—1 Enrapturing, making extremely glad.<BR>—2 The attainment of a desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षणः|प्रहर्षण|प्रहर्षणं
प्रहर्षणम् + .{@-णः@} The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षणी
प्रहर्ष(र्षि)णी<BR>—1 Turmeric.<BR>—2 N. of a metre; see App. म्नो ज्रौ गस्त्रिदशयतिः प्रहर्षणीयम् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षिणी
प्रहर्ष(र्षि)णी<BR>—1 Turmeric.<BR>—2 N. of a metre; see App. म्नो ज्रौ गस्त्रिदशयतिः प्रहर्षणीयम् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षित
प्रहर्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stiffened (as reed).<BR>—2 Made desirous of sexual intercourse.<BR>—3 Greatly delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षुलः|प्रहर्षुल
प्रहर्षुलः The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्ट
प्रहृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Delighted, pleased, glad, overjoyed. —2 Thrilling, bristling (as hair).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रहृष्टात्मन्, प्रहृष्टचित्त, प्रहृष्टमनस्, प्रहृष्टरूप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टात्मन्
प्रहृष्ट + -आत्मन्, -चित्त, -मनस् <i>a.</i> delighted in soul, rejoiced at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टचित्त
प्रहृष्ट + -आत्मन्, -चित्त, -मनस् <i>a.</i> delighted in soul, rejoiced at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टमनस्
प्रहृष्ट + -आत्मन्, -चित्त, -मनस् <i>a.</i> delighted in soul, rejoiced at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टरूप
प्रहृष्ट + -रूप <i>a.</i> looking pleased.<BR>—2 of a pleasing form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टकः|प्रहृष्टक
प्रहृष्टकः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेणकम्
प्रहेणकम्<BR>—1 A kind of pastry (पिष्टक).<BR>—2 Sweetmeats distributed at festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलकः|प्रहेलक|प्रहेलकं
प्रहेलकः<BR>—1 A kind of cake or sweetmeat.<BR>—2 A riddle; see प्रहेलिका below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेला
प्रहेला Free or unrestrained behaviour, loose conduct, playful dalliance;<BR> भूमौ प्रहेलया पश्चाज्जारहस्तोऽङ्गनास्विव Pt. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलिः|प्रहेलि
प्रहेलिः <i>f.</i>, प्रहेलिका A riddle, an enigma, a conundrum.<BR> It is thus defined in the विदग्धमुखमण्डन -व्यक्तीकृत्य कमप्यर्थं<BR> स्वरूपार्थस्य गोपनात् । यत्र बाह्यान्तरावर्थौ कथ्येते सा प्रहेलिका.<BR> It is आर्थी or शाब्दी; तरुण्यालिङ्गितः कण्ठे नितम्बस्थलमाश्रितः ।<BR> गुरूणां सन्निधानेऽपि कः कूजति मुहुर्मुहुः (where the answer is ईषदूनजलपूर्णकुम्भः)<BR> is an instance of the former kind; सदारिमध्यापि न वैरियुक्ता नितान्तरक्ताप्यसितैव<BR> नित्यम् । यथोक्तवादिन्यपि नैव दूती का नाम कान्तेति निवेदयाशु ॥ (where<BR> the answer is सारिका), of the latter. Daṇḍin, however, mentions 16<BR> different kinds of प्रहेलिका; see Kāv. 3. 96-124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलिका
प्रहेलिः <i>f.</i>, प्रहेलिका A riddle, an enigma, a conundrum.<BR> It is thus defined in the विदग्धमुखमण्डन -व्यक्तीकृत्य कमप्यर्थं<BR> स्वरूपार्थस्य गोपनात् । यत्र बाह्यान्तरावर्थौ कथ्येते सा प्रहेलिका.<BR> It is आर्थी or शाब्दी; तरुण्यालिङ्गितः कण्ठे नितम्बस्थलमाश्रितः ।<BR> गुरूणां सन्निधानेऽपि कः कूजति मुहुर्मुहुः (where the answer is ईषदूनजलपूर्णकुम्भः)<BR> is an instance of the former kind; सदारिमध्यापि न वैरियुक्ता नितान्तरक्ताप्यसितैव<BR> नित्यम् । यथोक्तवादिन्यपि नैव दूती का नाम कान्तेति निवेदयाशु ॥ (where<BR> the answer is सारिका), of the latter. Daṇḍin, however, mentions 16<BR> different kinds of प्रहेलिका; see Kāv. 3. 96-124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्रासः|प्रह्रास
प्रह्रासः<BR>—1 Diminution, decrease.<BR>—2 Languishing, fading away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लाद्
प्रह्लाद् €1 Ā. To be greatly delighted, rejoice. ━<i>Caus.</i> To<BR> delight, exhilarate, gladden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्न|प्रह्लन्नः
प्रह्लन्न <i>p. p.</i> Delighted, joyful, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्निः|प्रह्लन्नि
प्रह्लन्निः <i>f.</i> Pleasure, delight; also प्रह्लत्तिः P. VI. 4. 95 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्रादः|प्रह्राद
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दः<BR>—1 Great joy, pleasure, delight, happiness.<BR>—2 Sound.<BR>—3 A species of rice.<BR>—4 N. of a son of the demon Hiraṇya-Kaśipu. [According to the Padma<BR> Purāṇa, he was a Brāhmaṇa in his previous existence, and when born<BR> as son of Hiraṇya-Kaśipu, he still retained his ardent devotion to Viṣṇu.<BR> His father, of course, did not like that his own son should be such a<BR> devout worshipper of his mortal enemies, the gods, and with the object<BR> of getting rid of him, he subjected him to a variety of cruelties; but<BR> Prahlādā, by the favour of Viṣṇu, was quite unscathed, and began to<BR> preach with even greater earnestness than before the doctrine that Viṣṇu<BR> filled all space and was omni-present, omni-scient, omni-potent. HiraṇyaKaśipu<BR> in a fit of exasperation asked him “If Viṣṇu is omni-present how do<BR> I not see him in the pillar of this hall?” Whereupon Prahlāda struck the<BR> pillar with his fist (according to another account, HiraṇyaKaśipu himself<BR> angrily kicked the pillar to convince his son of the absurdity of his<BR> faith), when Viṣṇu came out half-man and half-lion, and tore HiraṇyaKaśipu<BR> to pieces. Prahlāda succeeded his father, and reigned wisely and righteously.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादः|प्रह्लाद
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दः<BR>—1 Great joy, pleasure, delight, happiness.<BR>—2 Sound.<BR>—3 A species of rice.<BR>—4 N. of a son of the demon Hiraṇya-Kaśipu. [According to the Padma<BR> Purāṇa, he was a Brāhmaṇa in his previous existence, and when born<BR> as son of Hiraṇya-Kaśipu, he still retained his ardent devotion to Viṣṇu.<BR> His father, of course, did not like that his own son should be such a<BR> devout worshipper of his mortal enemies, the gods, and with the object<BR> of getting rid of him, he subjected him to a variety of cruelties; but<BR> Prahlādā, by the favour of Viṣṇu, was quite unscathed, and began to<BR> preach with even greater earnestness than before the doctrine that Viṣṇu<BR> filled all space and was omni-present, omni-scient, omni-potent. HiraṇyaKaśipu<BR> in a fit of exasperation asked him “If Viṣṇu is omni-present how do<BR> I not see him in the pillar of this hall?” Whereupon Prahlāda struck the<BR> pillar with his fist (according to another account, HiraṇyaKaśipu himself<BR> angrily kicked the pillar to convince his son of the absurdity of his<BR> faith), when Viṣṇu came out half-man and half-lion, and tore HiraṇyaKaśipu<BR> to pieces. Prahlāda succeeded his father, and reigned wisely and righteously.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादक
प्रह्लादक <i>a.</i> Causing pleasure, refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्नादन
प्रह्ना(ह्ला)दन <i>a.</i> Gladdening, delighting; प्रह्लादनं ज्योतिरजन्यनेन R. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादन
प्रह्ना(ह्ला)दन <i>a.</i> Gladdening, delighting; प्रह्लादनं ज्योतिरजन्यनेन R. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्नादनम्
प्रह्ना(ह्ला)दन + .{@-नम्@} Causing joy or delight, gladdening, delighting; यथा प्रह्लादनाच्चन्द्रः R. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्व|प्रह्वः
प्रह्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sloping, slanting, inclined; प्रह्वानतीव क्वचिदुद्धतिश्रितः Śi. 12. 56.<BR>—2 Stooping, bent down; bowing humbly down; एष प्रह्वोऽस्मि भगवन् एषा<BR> विज्ञापना च नः Mv. 1. 47, 6. 37; तमाराध्य गुरुं भक्त्या प्रह्वप्रश्रयसेवनैः<BR> Vivekacūḍāmaṇi.<BR>—3 Submissive, humble, modestly submitting; प्रह्वेष्वनिर्बन्धरुषो हि<BR> सन्तः R. 16. 80; प्रह्वग्रीवः पुरोवर्ती Śiva B. 24. 6; शिवाय<BR> प्रेषयामास प्रह्वभावमुपाश्रयन् Śiva B. 29. 14.<BR>—4 Devoted or attached to, engaged in, engrossed by.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रह्वाञ्जलि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वाञ्जलि|प्रह्वांजलि
प्रह्व + -अञ्जलि <i>a.</i> bowing with the palms of the hand joined and put<BR> to the forehead as a mark of respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वणम्
प्रह्वणम् Bowing down in reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वयति
प्रह्वयति Den. P. To make humble, subdue; तदौद्धत्यं क्वापि व्रजति<BR> विनयः प्रह्वयति माम् U. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वल्
प्रह्वल् €1 P. To quake, tremble; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1123-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वलिका
प्रह्वलिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वायः|प्रह्वाय
प्रह्वायः A call, summons, invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रा
प्रा €2 P. (प्राति) To fill; अप्रासीदिषुभिर्मुखम् Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रा
प्रा <i>f.</i> Matted hair; Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशु|प्रांशुः
प्रांशु <i>a.</i> [प्रकृष्टाः अंशवोऽत्र]<BR>—1 High, tall, lofty, of lofty or great stature (as a man); शालप्रांशुर्महाभुजः<BR> R. 1. 13, 15. 19.<BR>—2 Long, extended; Ś. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशुः|प्रांशु
प्रांशु + .{@-शुः@} A tall man, a man of great stature; प्रांशुलभ्ये फले मोहादुद्बाहुरिव<BR> वामनः R. 1. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रांशुप्राकार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशुप्राकार
प्रांशु + -प्राकार <i>a.</i> having long walls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्
प्राक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Before (usually with abl.); सफलानि निमित्तानि प्राक्प्रभातात्ततो मम<BR> Bk. 8. 106; प्राक्सृष्टेः केवलात्मने Ku. 2. 4; R. 14. 78; Ś. 5. 22.<BR>—2 At first, already; प्रमन्यवः प्रागपि कोशलेन्द्रे R. 7. 34.<BR>—3 Before, previously, in a previous portion (as of a book); इति प्रागेव<BR> निर्दिष्टम्; Ms. 1. 71; प्राक्पादयोः पतति खादति पृष्ठमांसम् H.<BR>—4 In the east, to the east of; ग्रामात् प्राक्पर्वतः.<BR>—5 In front.<BR>—6 As far as, up to; प्राक्कडारात्.<BR>—7 At dawn or day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकट्यम्
प्राकट्यम् Manifestation, publicity, notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकरणिक
प्राकरणिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Pertaining to the subject of discussion, relevant<BR> to the matter in hand (often used in the sense of उपमेय in works<BR> on Rhetoric); अप्राकरणिकस्याभिधानेन प्राकरणिकस्याक्षेपोऽप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकर्षिक
प्राकर्षिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Entitled to preference or superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकषिकः|प्राकषिक
प्राकषिकः^1<BR>—1 A catamite.<BR>—2 A man supported by anotherʼs wife.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. note: the spelling changed in 1957; corrected back after ap90, MW, PWG;  see reference to Unadi-sutras in MW प्रा-कषिक [p= 701] ; m. (fr. -कष ; » Uṇ.  ii, 41 Sch.) a dancer employed by a woman or one supported by another's wives L.; in Unadi it is given प्राकषिकः नर्तकः।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाम्यम्
प्राकाम्यम्<BR>—1 Freedom of will; प्राकाम्यं ते विभूतिषु Ku. 2. 11.<BR>—2 Wilfulness.<BR>—3 Irresistible will, considered as one of the eight attributes or <i>siddhis</i><BR> of Śiva or the Supreme Being; see सिद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारः|प्राकार
प्राकारः<BR>—1 A fence, a wall, an enclosure.<BR>—2 An encircling or surrounding wall, rampart; द्वितीयं हेमप्राकारं<BR> कुर्वद्भिरिव वानरैः R. 12. 71; Pt. 1. 229.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्राकारधरणी, प्राकारस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारधरणी
प्राकारः + -धरणी the platform upon a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारस्थ
प्राकारः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> One who is stationed on the rampart; एकः शतं<BR> योधयति प्राकारस्थो धनुर्धरः Ms. 7. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारीय
प्राकारीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit for a wall.<BR>—2 Enclosed by a wall, walled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाशः|प्राकाश
प्राकाशः Ved.<BR>—1 A metallic mirror.<BR>—2 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाश्यम्
प्राकाश्यम्<BR>—1 Being known, evident or clear, publicity.<BR>—2 Fame, celebrity, renown; प्राकाश्यं चैव गच्छन्ति कृत्वा निष्कल्मषं<BR> तपः Mb. 12. 295. 28; प्राकाश्यं स्वगुणोदयेन गुणिनो गच्छन्ति किं<BR> जन्मना Pt. 1. 94.<BR>—3 Brightness; Mb. 12. 313. 17.<BR>—4 Seeing all things; प्राकाश्यं श्रुतदृष्टेषु Bhāg. 11. 15. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृत|प्राकृतः
प्राकृत <i>a.</i> (-ता, -ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [प्रकृतेरयं प्रकृत्या निर्वृत्तो वा अण्]<BR>—1 Original, natural, unaltered, unmodified; स्यातामामित्रौ मित्रे च सहजप्राकृतावपि<BR> Śi. 2. 36 (see Malli. thereon).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">Page1124-2</a>]<BR>—2 Usual, common, ordinary.<BR>—3 Uncultivated, vulgar, unrefined, illiterate; प्राकृत इव परिभूयमानमात्मानं<BR> न रुणत्सि K. 146; Bg. 18. 28.<BR>—4 Insignificant, unimportant; trifling; Mu. 1.<BR>—5 Derived from Prakṛti, q. v.; प्राकृतो लयः ‘re-absorption into Prakṛti’<BR>; विमुञ्चेत् प्राकृतान् ग्रामांस्तान् मुक्त्वाऽमृतमश्नुते Mb. 12. 204. 12.<BR>—6 Provincial, vernacular (as a dialect); see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतः|प्राकृत
प्राकृत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A low man, an ordinary or vulgar man. कार्षापणं भवेद्दण्डयो यत्रान्यः<BR> प्राकृतो जनः Ms. 8. 336.<BR>—2 A kind of fever; वर्षाशरद्वसन्तेषु वाताद्यैः प्राकृतः कमात् Mādhava; (see -ज्वरः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतम्
प्राकृत + .{@-तम्@} A vernacular or provincial dialect derived from and akin<BR> to Sanskrit; प्रकृतिः संस्कृतं तत्र भवं तत आगतं च प्राकृतम्<BR> Hem. (Many of these dialects are spoken by the female characters<BR> and inferior personages of Sanskrit plays and are usually divided into 4<BR> dialects:− शौरसेनी, माहाराष्ट्री, अपभ्रंश and पैशाची); तद्भवस्तत्समो<BR> देशीत्यनेकः प्राकृतक्रमः Kāv. 1. 33; also 34, 35; त्वमप्यस्मादृशजनयोग्ये<BR> प्राकृतमार्गे क्रमः Kāv. 1. 33; त्वमप्यस्मादृशजनयोग्ये प्राकृतमार्गे<BR> प्रकृति; the dissolution of the universe.<BR>—3 A particular ritual or यज्ञ; Bhāg. 10. 84. 52.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्राकृतारिः, प्राकृतोदासीनः, प्राकृतज्वरः, प्राकृतप्रलयः, प्राकृतमानुषः, प्राकृतमित्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतारिः|प्राकृतारि
प्राकृत + -अरिः a natural enemy, <i>i. e.</i> the ruler of an adjacent country;<BR> see Malli. on Śi. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतोदासीनः|प्राकृतोदासीन
प्राकृत + -उदासीनः a natural neutral <i>i. e.</i> a ruler whose dominions<BR> lie beyond those of the natural ally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतज्वरः|प्राकृतज्वर
प्राकृत + -ज्वरः a common or ordinary fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतप्रलयः|प्राकृतप्रलय
प्राकृत + -प्रलयः complete dissolution of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमानुषः|प्राकृतमानुष
प्राकृत + -मानुषः a common or ordinary man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमित्रम्
प्राकृत + -मित्रम् a natural ally; <i>i. e.</i> a ruler whose dominions lie<BR> immediately beyond those of the natural enemy (<i>i. e.</i> whose country<BR> is separated from the country with which he is allied by that of another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतत्वम्
प्राकृतत्वम्<BR>—1 Original or natural state.<BR>—2 Vulgarity (of speech).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतिक|प्राकृतिकः
प्राकृतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [प्रकृत्या निर्वृत्तः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Natural, derived from nature; क्षात्रं प्राकृतिकं तेजो ब्राह्मं यस्य<BR> विशिष्यते Mv. 7. 39.<BR>—2 Illusory.<BR>—3 Vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Former, previous, antecedent; प्रपेदिरे प्राक्तनजन्मविद्याः Ku. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Old, ancient, early.<BR>—3 Relating to a former life or acts in a former life; संस्काराः प्राक्तना<BR> इव R. 1. 20; Ku. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तनम्
प्राक्तन + .{@-नम्@} (or {@प्राक्तनकर्मन्@}) <i>n.</i> Fate, destiny.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्राक्तनकर्मन्, प्राक्तनजन्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तनकर्मन्|प्राक्तनकर्म्मन्
प्राक्तन + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> any act formerly done, or done in a former state of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तनजन्मन्
प्राक्तन + -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> a former birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्रमिक
प्राक्रमिक <i>a.</i> One who only commences a work (but does not carry<BR> it to completion); उपकम्य अपरिसमापयतस्तदनन्तरमेवैनं शिष्टा<BR> विगर्हेयुः प्राकमिकोऽयं कापुरुष इति वदन्तः ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 24;<BR> यो हि आरब्धमेवंजातीयकं समापयति न तं शिष्टा विगर्हन्ते प्राकमिकोऽयमसंव्यवहार्य<BR> इति ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राखर्यम्
प्राखर्यम्<BR>—1 Sharpness.<BR>—2 Pungency.<BR>—3 Wickedness.<BR>—4 Ardour, zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भी
प्रागल्भी<BR>—1 Boldness, confidence.<BR>—2 Resoluteness, determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1124-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्यम्
प्रागल्भ्यम्<BR>—1 Boldness, confidence; निःसाध्वसत्वं प्रागल्भ्यम् S. D.<BR>—2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>—3 Proficiency, skill.<BR>—4 Development, greatness, maturity; बुद्धिप्रागल्भ्य, तमःप्रागल्भ्य &c.<BR>—5 Manifestation, appearance; अवाप्तः प्रागल्भ्यं परिणतरुचः शैलतनये<BR> K. P. 10 ‘which has appeared’.<BR>—6 Eloquence; प्रागल्भ्यहीनस्य नरस्य विद्या शस्त्रं यथा कापुरुषस्य<BR> हस्ते (where प्रा˚ may mean ‘boldness’ also); प्रागल्भ्यमीधकमाप्तुं<BR> वाणी बाणो बभूवेति Subhāṣ.; प्रागल्भ्यमभ्यस्तगुणा च वाणी Māl. 3. 11.<BR>—7 Pomp, rank.<BR>—8 Resoluteness, determination.<BR>—9 Impudence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रागल्भ्यबुद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्यबुद्धिः|प्रागल्भ्यबुद्धि
प्रागल्भ्यम् + -बुद्धिः boldness of judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागारः|प्रागार
प्रागारः A house, building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागीत्यम्
प्रागीत्यम् Celebrity, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागुण्यम्
प्रागुण्यम् Right position or direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रम्
प्राग्रम् The highest point.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्राग्रसर, प्राग्रहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रसर
प्राग्रम् + -सर <i>a.</i> first, foremost; त्वमर्हतां प्राग्रसरः स्मृतोऽसि<BR> नः Ś. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रहर|प्राग्रहरः
प्राग्रम् + -हर <i>a.</i> chief, principal; विश्वावसुप्राग्रहरैः प्रवीणैः<BR> Ku. 7. 48; R. 16. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्राटः|प्राग्राट|प्राग्राटं
प्राग्राटः Thin coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्र्य|प्राग्र्यं
प्राग्र्य <i>a.</i> Chief, foremost, best, most excellent; यथा प्राग्र्यान्<BR> यथा ज्येष्ठान् Mb. 6. 64. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघातः|प्राघात
प्राघातः War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघारः|प्राघार
प्राघारः Trickling out, dropping, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1125-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुणः|प्राघुण
