प्रावृष्यम्
प्रावृष्यः + .{@-ष्यम्@} Lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेण्यम्
प्रावेण्यम् A fine woollen covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशन
प्रावेशन <i>a.</i> (-ना <i>f.</i>)<BR> To be given or done on entering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशनम्
प्रावेशन + .{@-नम्@} A workshop, manufactory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशिक
प्रावेशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to or connected with entrance (into a house or upon the stage).<BR>—2 In the habit of entering.<BR>—3 Auspicious for entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्रज्यम्
प्राव्रज्यम्, -प्राव्राज्यम्<BR>—1 The life of a religious mendicant or recluse.<BR>—2 Vagrancy, wandering habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्राज्यम्
प्राव्रज्यम्, -प्राव्राज्यम्<BR>—1 The life of a religious mendicant or recluse.<BR>—2 Vagrancy, wandering habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् €9 P.<BR>—1 To eat, consume, devour, feed upon.<BR>—2 To taste; वैश्योऽद्भिः प्राशिताभिस्तु Ms. 2. 62.<BR>—3 To enjoy, sport with.<BR>—4 To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् <i>f.</i> Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशः|प्राश
प्राशः<BR>—1 Eating, tasting, living or feeding on; घृतप्राशो विशोधनम् Ms. 11. 143;<BR> धूम˚ &c.<BR>—2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1134-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशकः|प्राशक
