प्रोथ्
प्रोथ् €1 U. (प्रोथति-ते)<BR>—1 To be equal to, be a match for, withstand (with dat.); पुप्रोथास्मै<BR> न कश्चन Bk. 14. 84, 15. 40.<BR>—2 To be able, adequate or competent.<BR>—3 To be full or complete.<BR>—4 To subdue, overpower.<BR>—5 To destroy, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Famous, well-known.<BR>—2 Placed, fixed.<BR>—3 Travelling, going out on a journey, wayfaring; वृक्षान्तमुदकान्तं<BR> च प्रियं प्रोथमनुव्रजेत् Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथः|प्रोथ
प्रोथ + .{@-थः, -थम्@}<BR>—1 The nose or nostrils of a horse; चलाचलप्रोथतया महीभृते स्ववेगदर्पानिव<BR> वक्तुमुत्सुकम् N. 1. 60; Śi. 11. 11, 12. 73; विपुलप्रोथललाटकटपुरस्कम् Bu. C. 5. 73.<BR>—2 The snout of a hog; निध्नन् प्रोथेन पृथिवीं विलिखंश्चरणैरपि Mb. 3. 167. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथम्
प्रोथ + .{@-थः, -थम्@}<BR>—1 The nose or nostrils of a horse; चलाचलप्रोथतया महीभृते स्ववेगदर्पानिव<BR> वक्तुमुत्सुकम् N. 1. 60; Śi. 11. 11, 12. 73; विपुलप्रोथललाटकटपुरस्कम् Bu. C. 5. 73.<BR>—2 The snout of a hog; निध्नन् प्रोथेन पृथिवीं विलिखंश्चरणैरपि Mb. 3. 167. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

