प्रोषधः Fasting; cf. पोषध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषित|प्रोषितः
प्रोषित <i>p. p.</i> Gone abroad, on a journey, living abroad, away<BR> from home, absent, living in a foreign country; जीवत्सु पाण्डुपुत्रेषु<BR> दूरमप्रोषितेषु च । पाञ्चालराजतनया वहते यदिमां दशाम् Ve. 1. 18;<BR> प्रोषिते मलिना कृशा Kāśīkhaṇḍa..<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रोषितभर्तृका, प्रोषितमरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितभर्तृका|प्रोषितभर्त्तृका
प्रोषित + -भर्तृका a woman whose husband is gone abroad; one of the eight<BR> Nāyikās in erotic poetry. She is thus defined in S. D.:− नानाकार्यवशाद्<BR> यस्या दूरदेशं गतः पतिः । सा मनोभवदुःखार्ता भवेत् प्रोषितभर्तृका ॥ 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितमरणम्
प्रोषित + -मरणम् dying in a foreign country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्यपापीयान्
प्रोष्य-पापीयान् <i>a.</i> Sinful on account of oneʼs living away from<BR> home; राघवः प्रोष्य-पापीयान्, जहीहि तमकिञ्चनम् Bk. 5. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

